window.EDMUND_IELTS_READING_PASSAGE_3_SEED = {"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 3":[{"front":"what’s in blood?","meaning":"血液內有甚麼？","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains what is contained in human blood.","zh":"文章解釋人類血液內含有甚麼。"},{"en":"“What’s in blood?” asks which liquids, cells, chemicals, and proteins make up blood.","zh":"“What’s in blood?” 是問血液由哪些液體、細胞、化學物質和蛋白質組成。"},{"en":"A biology teacher may ask, “What’s in blood?” before explaining plasma and blood cells.","zh":"生物老師在解釋血漿和血細胞前，可能會問：「血液內有甚麼？」"},{"en":"Understanding what is in blood helps doctors explain oxygen transport, immunity, and clotting.","zh":"理解血液內有甚麼，有助醫生解釋氧氣運送、免疫和凝血。"},{"en":"This question introduces the basic contents and functions of blood.","zh":"這個問題引出血液的基本內容和功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"specialised fluid","meaning":"特殊化液體","examples":[{"en":"Blood is the most specialised fluid within living animals.","zh":"血液是活體動物體內最特殊化的液體。"},{"en":"A specialised fluid is a liquid that has particular structures and functions.","zh":"specialised fluid 指具有特定結構和功能的液體。"},{"en":"Blood is not just red water; it carries oxygen, nutrients, hormones, and immune cells.","zh":"血液不只是紅色的水；它運送氧氣、養分、荷爾蒙和免疫細胞。"},{"en":"Because blood performs many exact jobs, it is more specialised than ordinary body fluid.","zh":"由於血液執行許多精確工作，它比普通體液更特殊化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a liquid adapted for important biological work.","zh":"這個短語描述一種適應重要生物工作的液體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"living animals","meaning":"活體動物","examples":[{"en":"Blood performs essential functions within living animals.","zh":"血液在活體動物體內執行必要功能。"},{"en":"Living animals are animals that are alive and whose bodies are still functioning.","zh":"living animals 指仍然活着、身體仍在運作的動物。"},{"en":"In living animals, blood moves through the body to support organs and tissues.","zh":"在活體動物中，血液在身體內流動，支援器官和組織。"},{"en":"If blood circulation stops in a living animal, cells quickly lose oxygen.","zh":"如果活體動物的血液循環停止，細胞很快會失去氧氣。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts living bodies with dead tissue or preserved specimens.","zh":"這個短語把活着的身體與死亡組織或保存標本作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"play a critical role","meaning":"發揮關鍵作用","examples":[{"en":"Blood plays an absolutely critical role in the body.","zh":"血液在身體內發揮絕對關鍵的作用。"},{"en":"To play a critical role means to be extremely important in making something work.","zh":"play a critical role 指對某事能否運作極其重要。"},{"en":"Nurses play a critical role in hospitals because they monitor patients closely every day.","zh":"護士在醫院發揮關鍵作用，因為他們每天密切監察病人。"},{"en":"Blood plays a critical role because many organs depend on it for oxygen and nutrients.","zh":"血液發揮關鍵作用，因為許多器官依賴它獲得氧氣和養分。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when something is not optional but essential.","zh":"這個短語用於某事並非可有可無，而是不可或缺的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"symbolise life","meaning":"象徵生命","examples":[{"en":"Blood is often used to symbolise life.","zh":"血液常被用來象徵生命。"},{"en":"To symbolise life means to represent the idea of being alive.","zh":"symbolise life 指代表「活着」這個概念。"},{"en":"In stories, blood may symbolise life because losing too much blood can mean death.","zh":"在故事中，血液可能象徵生命，因為失去太多血可能代表死亡。"},{"en":"People connect blood with life because it moves through the body and keeps organs working.","zh":"人們把血液與生命連繫起來，因為它在身體內流動並維持器官運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes symbolic meaning, not just physical function.","zh":"這個短語描述象徵意義，而不只是實際功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get your blood running","meaning":"令血液循環起來","examples":[{"en":"Exercise can help get your blood running.","zh":"運動可以幫助令血液循環起來。"},{"en":"To get your blood running means to make blood circulate faster through the body.","zh":"get your blood running 指令血液在身體內循環得更快。"},{"en":"A short walk in the morning can get your blood running before work or school.","zh":"早上一段短步行可以在上班或上學前令血液循環起來。"},{"en":"When your blood gets running, your muscles receive more oxygen and may feel warmer.","zh":"當血液循環起來，肌肉會獲得更多氧氣，並可能感到較暖。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for movement that wakes the body up.","zh":"這個短語常用於描述令身體醒過來的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"good or bad blood","meaning":"良好或惡劣關係；性格好壞","examples":[{"en":"The expression “good or bad blood” associates blood with personality or relationships.","zh":"“good or bad blood” 這個表達把血液與性格或關係連繫起來。"},{"en":"Good or bad blood refers to friendly or hostile feelings between people or families.","zh":"good or bad blood 指人與人或家庭之間友好或敵對的感情。"},{"en":"There was bad blood between the two neighbours after a long argument about noise.","zh":"兩名鄰居因噪音長期爭執後，彼此之間有了惡劣關係。"},{"en":"Good blood between colleagues makes cooperation easier because people trust one another.","zh":"同事之間關係良好會令合作更容易，因為人們互相信任。"},{"en":"This expression uses blood metaphorically to talk about relationships.","zh":"這個表達以血作比喻，談論人際關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"bloodline","meaning":"血統","examples":[{"en":"The word “bloodline” refers to family descent.","zh":"“bloodline” 一詞指家族血統。"},{"en":"A bloodline is the line of family relationship passed from parents to children.","zh":"bloodline 指由父母傳給子女的家族關係脈絡。"},{"en":"Some royal families trace their bloodline back through many generations.","zh":"有些王室家族會把血統追溯到許多代以前。"},{"en":"People may use bloodline when discussing ancestry, inheritance, or family history.","zh":"人們討論祖先、繼承或家族歷史時，可能使用 bloodline。"},{"en":"This word is about descent, not the physical movement of blood.","zh":"這個字關於血統傳承，而不是血液的實際流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"would rather not see","meaning":"寧願不看見","examples":[{"en":"Most people would rather not see blood.","zh":"大多數人寧願不看見血。"},{"en":"Would rather not see means would prefer to avoid looking at something unpleasant or upsetting.","zh":"would rather not see 指較希望避免看見令人不舒服或不安的東西。"},{"en":"Many children would rather not see a needle before an injection.","zh":"許多孩子在打針前寧願不看見針。"},{"en":"People may look away from blood because it reminds them of injury or pain.","zh":"人們可能避開血液，因為它令人想起受傷或痛楚。"},{"en":"This phrase politely expresses a preference to avoid seeing something.","zh":"這個短語禮貌地表達不想看見某物的偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a complex soup of","meaning":"複雜混合物","examples":[{"en":"Blood contains a complex soup of chemicals and cells.","zh":"血液含有由化學物質和細胞組成的複雜混合物。"},{"en":"A complex soup of something means a complicated mixture containing many different parts.","zh":"a complex soup of something 指由許多不同部分組成的複雜混合物。"},{"en":"A hospital report may show a complex soup of medical terms, numbers, and test results.","zh":"醫院報告可能包含醫學術語、數字和檢測結果的複雜混合物。"},{"en":"Blood is called a complex soup because plasma, cells, proteins, sugars, and ions are mixed together.","zh":"血液被稱為複雜混合物，因為血漿、細胞、蛋白質、糖分和離子混在一起。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a complicated mixture easier to imagine.","zh":"這個短語令複雜混合物更容易想像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"proteins and sugars","meaning":"蛋白質和糖分","examples":[{"en":"Blood contains proteins and sugars dissolved in plasma.","zh":"血液含有溶解在血漿中的蛋白質和糖分。"},{"en":"Proteins and sugars are important chemical substances that help the body build, repair, and use energy.","zh":"proteins and sugars 是幫助身體建造、修復和使用能量的重要化學物質。"},{"en":"A blood test may measure certain proteins and sugars to check a person’s health.","zh":"驗血可能量度某些蛋白質和糖分，以檢查一個人的健康。"},{"en":"Too much sugar in the blood can signal a problem with how the body controls energy.","zh":"血液中糖分過高，可能顯示身體控制能量的方式有問題。"},{"en":"This phrase names two kinds of substances carried in blood.","zh":"這個短語指出血液中攜帶的兩類物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ions","meaning":"離子","examples":[{"en":"Various ions circulate through the body in the blood.","zh":"各種離子透過血液在身體內循環。"},{"en":"Ions are charged particles that help cells, nerves, and muscles work properly.","zh":"ions 是帶電粒子，幫助細胞、神經和肌肉正常運作。"},{"en":"Sodium and potassium are ions that doctors may check in a blood test.","zh":"鈉和鉀是醫生可能在驗血中檢查的離子。"},{"en":"If ion levels become too high or too low, the heart and muscles may be affected.","zh":"如果離子水平過高或過低，心臟和肌肉可能受影響。"},{"en":"This word describes tiny charged substances moving in body fluids.","zh":"這個字描述在體液中移動的微小帶電物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hormones","meaning":"荷爾蒙","examples":[{"en":"Blood carries hormones to different parts of the body.","zh":"血液把荷爾蒙運送到身體不同部分。"},{"en":"Hormones are chemical messengers that tell organs and tissues what to do.","zh":"hormones 是化學信使，告訴器官和組織要做甚麼。"},{"en":"Insulin is a hormone that helps control the amount of sugar in the blood.","zh":"胰島素是一種幫助控制血糖量的荷爾蒙。"},{"en":"Hormones travel in blood, so they can affect distant parts of the body.","zh":"荷爾蒙在血液中運行，因此可以影響身體遠處部分。"},{"en":"This word describes chemicals that coordinate body functions.","zh":"這個字描述協調身體功能的化學物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cellular components","meaning":"細胞成分","examples":[{"en":"Blood contains several basic cellular components.","zh":"血液含有幾種基本細胞成分。"},{"en":"Cellular components are the cell-based parts of blood, such as red cells, white cells, and platelets.","zh":"cellular components 指血液中以細胞為基礎的部分，例如紅血球、白血球和血小板。"},{"en":"A blood test can count cellular components to check whether a patient is healthy.","zh":"驗血可以計算細胞成分，以檢查病人是否健康。"},{"en":"If a cellular component is too low, the body may struggle with oxygen transport or clotting.","zh":"如果某種細胞成分過低，身體可能難以運送氧氣或凝血。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the living or cell-like parts of blood.","zh":"這個短語指血液中活細胞或類似細胞的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be worth considering","meaning":"值得探討","examples":[{"en":"The composition of blood is worth considering in detail.","zh":"血液的組成值得詳細探討。"},{"en":"To be worth considering means to deserve attention, thought, or discussion.","zh":"be worth considering 指值得注意、思考或討論。"},{"en":"Before choosing a university course, the cost and career path are worth considering.","zh":"選擇大學課程前，費用和職業道路都值得考慮。"},{"en":"Blood is worth considering because it affects many systems in the body.","zh":"血液值得探討，因為它影響身體許多系統。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that a topic is important enough to study.","zh":"這個短語表示某主題重要到值得研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in some detail","meaning":"較詳細地","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines blood in some detail.","zh":"文章較詳細地探討血液。"},{"en":"In some detail means with more explanation than a brief mention, but not necessarily exhaustively.","zh":"in some detail 指比簡短提及有更多解釋，但不一定非常全面。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain exam marking in some detail before students write practice essays.","zh":"老師可能在學生寫練習作文前，較詳細地解釋考試評分。"},{"en":"Discussing blood in some detail helps readers understand its different parts and functions.","zh":"較詳細地討論血液，有助讀者理解其不同部分和功能。"},{"en":"This phrase indicates a moderately careful explanation.","zh":"這個短語表示一種中等程度仔細的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"by volume","meaning":"按體積計","examples":[{"en":"By volume, about half of blood consists of plasma.","zh":"按體積計，約一半血液由血漿組成。"},{"en":"By volume means measured according to how much space something takes up.","zh":"by volume 指按某物佔多少空間來量度。"},{"en":"By volume, a large box may contain more air than actual objects.","zh":"按體積計，一個大箱子可能含有的空氣比實際物件更多。"},{"en":"Saying blood is half plasma by volume describes its physical proportion.","zh":"說血液按體積計一半是血漿，是在描述其物理比例。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when comparing amounts by space, not weight.","zh":"這個短語用於按空間而不是重量比較數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"liquid part","meaning":"液體部分","examples":[{"en":"Plasma is the liquid part of blood.","zh":"血漿是血液的液體部分。"},{"en":"The liquid part is the fluid portion that carries dissolved substances and cells.","zh":"liquid part 指承載溶解物質和細胞的流體部分。"},{"en":"In soup, the broth is the liquid part that holds flavour and ingredients.","zh":"在湯中，湯底是承載味道和材料的液體部分。"},{"en":"The liquid part of blood allows cells and chemicals to move through vessels.","zh":"血液的液體部分讓細胞和化學物質能在血管中移動。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the fluid portion with solid or cellular parts.","zh":"這個短語把流體部分與固體或細胞部分作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be called plasma","meaning":"稱為血漿","examples":[{"en":"The liquid component of blood is called plasma.","zh":"血液的液體成分稱為血漿。"},{"en":"To be called plasma means to have the scientific name plasma.","zh":"be called plasma 指具有 plasma 這個科學名稱。"},{"en":"In biology class, students learn that the yellowish liquid in blood is called plasma.","zh":"在生物課中，學生會學到血液中帶黃色的液體稱為血漿。"},{"en":"Naming this liquid plasma helps separate it from red cells, white cells, and platelets.","zh":"把這種液體命名為血漿，有助把它與紅血球、白血球和血小板分開。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the correct term for the liquid part of blood.","zh":"這個短語引出血液液體部分的正確術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the rest comprises","meaning":"其餘部分包括","examples":[{"en":"The rest of the blood comprises specialised components.","zh":"血液其餘部分包括特殊化成分。"},{"en":"The rest comprises means the remaining part is made up of particular elements.","zh":"the rest comprises 指剩餘部分由某些特定元素組成。"},{"en":"In a lunch box, half may be rice, while the rest comprises vegetables, meat, and fruit.","zh":"在飯盒中，一半可能是飯，其餘部分包括蔬菜、肉和水果。"},{"en":"In blood, the rest after plasma includes cells and platelets.","zh":"在血液中，除血漿以外的其餘部分包括細胞和血小板。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe what remains after one part has been identified.","zh":"這個短語幫助描述某部分被指出後剩下的是甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"specialised components","meaning":"特殊化成分","examples":[{"en":"Blood contains several specialised components.","zh":"血液含有幾種特殊化成分。"},{"en":"Specialised components are parts designed for particular jobs.","zh":"specialised components 指為特定工作而設的部分。"},{"en":"A camera has specialised components for focusing, storing images, and controlling light.","zh":"相機有負責對焦、儲存影像和控制光線的特殊化成分。"},{"en":"Blood’s specialised components work together to carry oxygen, fight disease, and clot wounds.","zh":"血液的特殊化成分共同運作，以運送氧氣、對抗疾病和令傷口凝血。"},{"en":"This phrase describes parts with clear and specific functions.","zh":"這個短語描述具有清楚特定功能的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"red blood cells","meaning":"紅血球","examples":[{"en":"Red blood cells are the main cellular component of blood.","zh":"紅血球是血液中主要的細胞成分。"},{"en":"Red blood cells are blood cells that carry oxygen around the body.","zh":"red blood cells 指把氧氣運送到全身的血細胞。"},{"en":"A doctor may check red blood cells when a patient feels tired or weak.","zh":"當病人感到疲倦或虛弱時，醫生可能檢查紅血球。"},{"en":"If red blood cell numbers are too low, the body may not receive enough oxygen.","zh":"如果紅血球數量過低，身體可能得不到足夠氧氣。"},{"en":"This phrase names the blood cells most closely linked with oxygen transport.","zh":"這個短語指出最與氧氣運送相關的血細胞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"technically known as","meaning":"正式稱為","examples":[{"en":"Red blood cells are technically known as erythrocytes.","zh":"紅血球正式稱為 erythrocytes。"},{"en":"Technically known as means formally or scientifically called by a specific name.","zh":"technically known as 指在正式或科學上被稱為某個特定名稱。"},{"en":"The kneecap is technically known as the patella in medical language.","zh":"膝蓋骨在醫學語言中正式稱為 patella。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect an everyday name with a specialist term.","zh":"這個短語幫助把日常名稱與專門術語連接起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining scientific vocabulary to learners.","zh":"它適合用於向學習者解釋科學詞彙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"erythrocytes","meaning":"紅血球；紅細胞","examples":[{"en":"Erythrocytes transport oxygen throughout the body.","zh":"紅血球把氧氣運送到全身。"},{"en":"Erythrocytes are the scientific name for red blood cells.","zh":"erythrocytes 是紅血球的科學名稱。"},{"en":"A laboratory report may use “erythrocytes” instead of “red blood cells.”","zh":"化驗報告可能使用 erythrocytes，而不是 red blood cells。"},{"en":"If erythrocytes are damaged or too few, oxygen delivery can suffer.","zh":"如果紅血球受損或數量太少，氧氣輸送可能受影響。"},{"en":"This word is a formal medical term for oxygen-carrying blood cells.","zh":"這個字是運送氧氣的血細胞的正式醫學術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"transport oxygen molecules","meaning":"運送氧分子","examples":[{"en":"Red blood cells transport oxygen molecules throughout the body.","zh":"紅血球把氧分子運送到全身。"},{"en":"To transport oxygen molecules means to carry tiny oxygen units from the lungs to body tissues.","zh":"transport oxygen molecules 指把微小氧氣單位從肺部帶到身體組織。"},{"en":"Delivery workers transport parcels; red blood cells transport oxygen molecules.","zh":"送貨員運送包裹；紅血球運送氧分子。"},{"en":"If oxygen molecules are not transported well, muscles and organs cannot work properly.","zh":"如果氧分子未能良好運送，肌肉和器官就不能正常運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the carrying job of red blood cells.","zh":"這個短語描述紅血球的運輸工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"throughout the body","meaning":"遍及全身","examples":[{"en":"Oxygen is carried throughout the body by red blood cells.","zh":"氧氣由紅血球運送至全身。"},{"en":"Throughout the body means in all or many parts of the body.","zh":"throughout the body 指在身體所有或許多部分。"},{"en":"Medicine can travel throughout the body after it enters the bloodstream.","zh":"藥物進入血液後，可以遍及全身。"},{"en":"Oxygen must reach tissues throughout the body so cells can produce energy.","zh":"氧氣必須到達全身各組織，細胞才能產生能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wide distribution inside the body.","zh":"這個短語描述身體內部的廣泛分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"give blood its colour","meaning":"賦予血液顏色","examples":[{"en":"Red blood cells give blood its characteristic colour.","zh":"紅血球賦予血液其特有顏色。"},{"en":"To give blood its colour means to be the reason blood looks red.","zh":"give blood its colour 指成為血液看起來呈紅色的原因。"},{"en":"Paint gets its colour from pigments; blood gets its colour mainly from hemoglobin in red cells.","zh":"顏料令油漆有顏色；紅血球中的血紅蛋白主要令血液有顏色。"},{"en":"When hemoglobin carries oxygen, it helps make blood appear bright red.","zh":"當血紅蛋白攜帶氧氣時，它幫助血液顯得鮮紅。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the source of blood’s visible colour.","zh":"這個短語解釋血液可見顏色的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hemoglobin protein","meaning":"血紅蛋白","examples":[{"en":"Hemoglobin is the protein responsible for blood’s red colour.","zh":"血紅蛋白是負責血液紅色的蛋白質。"},{"en":"Hemoglobin protein is a protein in red blood cells that binds oxygen.","zh":"hemoglobin protein 指紅血球中能與氧結合的蛋白質。"},{"en":"Doctors may test hemoglobin levels when checking for anaemia.","zh":"醫生檢查貧血時，可能測試血紅蛋白水平。"},{"en":"Without enough hemoglobin protein, blood carries less oxygen than the body needs.","zh":"沒有足夠血紅蛋白，血液攜帶的氧氣會少於身體所需。"},{"en":"This phrase names the oxygen-binding protein that gives blood its colour.","zh":"這個短語指出令血液有顏色並能結合氧氣的蛋白質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"combine with oxygen","meaning":"與氧結合","examples":[{"en":"Hemoglobin turns red when it combines with oxygen.","zh":"血紅蛋白與氧結合時會變紅。"},{"en":"To combine with oxygen means to join or attach to oxygen chemically.","zh":"combine with oxygen 指在化學上與氧連接或附着。"},{"en":"Iron can combine with oxygen and form rust on a wet bicycle chain.","zh":"鐵可以與氧結合，在潮濕單車鏈上形成鏽。"},{"en":"In blood, hemoglobin combines with oxygen so red blood cells can carry it.","zh":"在血液中，血紅蛋白與氧結合，使紅血球能攜帶氧氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a chemical joining process.","zh":"這個短語描述化學結合過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have a limited operating life","meaning":"使用壽命有限","examples":[{"en":"Red blood cells have a limited operating life.","zh":"紅血球使用壽命有限。"},{"en":"To have a limited operating life means to work only for a certain period before wearing out.","zh":"have a limited operating life 指只在某段時間內有效運作，之後會耗損。"},{"en":"A phone battery has a limited operating life and eventually holds less charge.","zh":"手機電池使用壽命有限，最後會儲電較少。"},{"en":"Red blood cells must be replaced because they do not work forever.","zh":"紅血球必須被替換，因為它們不能永遠運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes useful function that ends after a period of time.","zh":"這個短語描述有用功能在一段時間後結束。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be produced within","meaning":"在……內產生","examples":[{"en":"Blood cells are produced within the marrow of bones.","zh":"血細胞在骨髓內產生。"},{"en":"To be produced within something means to be made inside it.","zh":"be produced within something 指在某物內部被製造出來。"},{"en":"New blood cells are produced within bone marrow rather than in the skin.","zh":"新血細胞在骨髓內產生，而不是在皮膚中產生。"},{"en":"A factory’s products are produced within its workshops before being sent out.","zh":"工廠產品在車間內生產，然後運出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where something is created.","zh":"這個短語描述某物在哪裡被創造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"bone marrow","meaning":"骨髓","examples":[{"en":"Red and white blood cells are produced in bone marrow.","zh":"紅血球和白血球在骨髓中產生。"},{"en":"Bone marrow is the soft tissue inside certain bones where blood cells are made.","zh":"bone marrow 指某些骨頭內部的軟組織，是血細胞產生的地方。"},{"en":"Doctors may examine bone marrow when investigating serious blood diseases.","zh":"醫生調查嚴重血液疾病時，可能檢查骨髓。"},{"en":"If bone marrow does not work properly, the body may not produce enough blood cells.","zh":"如果骨髓不能正常運作，身體可能無法產生足夠血細胞。"},{"en":"This phrase names the body’s blood-cell production site.","zh":"這個短語指出身體製造血細胞的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"principally the larger ones","meaning":"主要是較大的那些","examples":[{"en":"Blood cells are produced principally in the larger bones.","zh":"血細胞主要在較大的骨頭中產生。"},{"en":"Principally the larger ones means mainly the bigger examples in a group.","zh":"principally the larger ones 指主要是一組中較大的那些例子。"},{"en":"A city’s largest hospitals, principally the larger ones, may handle the most serious cases.","zh":"一個城市最大的醫院，主要是較大型那些，可能處理最嚴重個案。"},{"en":"In the body, larger bones provide important spaces for blood-cell production.","zh":"在身體中，較大的骨頭提供製造血細胞的重要空間。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows a general group to its main larger members.","zh":"這個短語把一般群組收窄至其中主要較大的成員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"live for about four months","meaning":"存活約四個月","examples":[{"en":"Red blood cells live for about four months.","zh":"紅血球存活約四個月。"},{"en":"To live for about four months means to remain active for roughly that period of time.","zh":"live for about four months 指大約在這段時間內保持活躍。"},{"en":"Some flowers live for only a few days, while red blood cells live for about four months.","zh":"有些花只存活幾天，而紅血球存活約四個月。"},{"en":"Because red blood cells do not last forever, the body must keep making new ones.","zh":"由於紅血球不能永久存在，身體必須持續製造新的紅血球。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the approximate lifespan of red blood cells.","zh":"這個短語描述紅血球的大約壽命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"become inactive","meaning":"失去活性","examples":[{"en":"Red blood cells eventually become inactive.","zh":"紅血球最終會失去活性。"},{"en":"To become inactive means to stop working effectively.","zh":"become inactive 指停止有效運作。"},{"en":"An old membership card may become inactive if it has not been used for years.","zh":"舊會員卡如果多年未使用，可能會失去有效狀態。"},{"en":"When red blood cells become inactive, the body removes and breaks them down.","zh":"當紅血球失去活性，身體會移除並分解它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something losing its ability to function.","zh":"這個短語描述某物失去功能能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be reabsorbed by","meaning":"被……重新吸收","examples":[{"en":"Old red blood cells are reabsorbed by the spleen and liver.","zh":"舊紅血球被脾臟和肝臟重新吸收。"},{"en":"To be reabsorbed by something means to be taken back into the body or system and processed.","zh":"be reabsorbed by something 指被身體或系統重新吸收並處理。"},{"en":"The body can reabsorb some useful materials instead of wasting them.","zh":"身體可以重新吸收一些有用物質，而不是把它們浪費掉。"},{"en":"When old red blood cells are reabsorbed, their materials can be broken down and reused or removed.","zh":"當舊紅血球被重新吸收，其材料可以被分解、再用或移除。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the body reclaiming or processing old material.","zh":"這個短語描述身體回收或處理舊物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"spleen and liver","meaning":"脾臟和肝臟","examples":[{"en":"The spleen and liver help remove old red blood cells.","zh":"脾臟和肝臟幫助移除舊紅血球。"},{"en":"The spleen and liver are organs that help process blood and remove waste or old cells.","zh":"spleen and liver 是幫助處理血液並移除廢物或舊細胞的器官。"},{"en":"Doctors may check the liver when blood tests show signs of abnormal breakdown.","zh":"當血液檢查顯示異常分解跡象時，醫生可能檢查肝臟。"},{"en":"If the spleen or liver is damaged, blood processing may be affected.","zh":"如果脾臟或肝臟受損，血液處理可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase names two organs involved in cleaning and processing blood.","zh":"這個短語指出兩個參與清理和處理血液的器官。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"waste products","meaning":"廢物","examples":[{"en":"The breakdown of blood cells produces waste products.","zh":"血細胞分解會產生廢物。"},{"en":"Waste products are unwanted materials left after the body uses or breaks down substances.","zh":"waste products 指身體使用或分解物質後留下的不需要材料。"},{"en":"After exercise, the body produces waste products that must be removed through blood and urine.","zh":"運動後，身體會產生必須透過血液和尿液移除的廢物。"},{"en":"If waste products build up, they can harm organs and make a person ill.","zh":"如果廢物累積，它們可以傷害器官並令人患病。"},{"en":"This phrase describes materials the body needs to get rid of.","zh":"這個短語描述身體需要排走的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be excreted in urine","meaning":"經尿液排出","examples":[{"en":"Some waste products are eventually excreted in urine.","zh":"有些廢物最終經尿液排出。"},{"en":"To be excreted in urine means to leave the body through urine.","zh":"be excreted in urine 指透過尿液離開身體。"},{"en":"Doctors may test urine to see what substances the body is excreting.","zh":"醫生可能檢驗尿液，看身體正在排出甚麼物質。"},{"en":"If waste cannot be excreted in urine properly, it may build up in the body.","zh":"如果廢物不能正常經尿液排出，可能在身體內累積。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one way the body removes waste.","zh":"這個短語描述身體移除廢物的一種方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"contrast with","meaning":"與……形成對比","examples":[{"en":"The lifespan of red blood cells contrasts with that of white blood cells.","zh":"紅血球的壽命與白血球的壽命形成對比。"},{"en":"To contrast with something means to be clearly different from it.","zh":"contrast with something 指與某事物有明顯不同。"},{"en":"A quiet library contrasts with a noisy shopping mall.","zh":"安靜的圖書館與嘈雜的商場形成對比。"},{"en":"Red blood cells last months, whereas some white blood cells last only days.","zh":"紅血球可維持數月，而有些白血球只維持數天。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare two things by showing difference.","zh":"這個短語透過展示差異來幫助比較兩件事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"white blood cells","meaning":"白血球","examples":[{"en":"White blood cells defend the body against infection.","zh":"白血球保護身體免受感染。"},{"en":"White blood cells are immune cells that identify and fight harmful invaders.","zh":"white blood cells 指識別並對抗有害入侵物的免疫細胞。"},{"en":"A high white blood cell count may show that the body is fighting an infection.","zh":"白血球數量偏高可能顯示身體正在對抗感染。"},{"en":"Without enough white blood cells, a person may become ill more easily.","zh":"沒有足夠白血球，人可能更容易生病。"},{"en":"This phrase names the blood cells most closely linked with immunity.","zh":"這個短語指出最與免疫有關的血細胞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"leukocytes","meaning":"白血球；白細胞","examples":[{"en":"White blood cells are technically known as leukocytes.","zh":"白血球正式稱為 leukocytes。"},{"en":"Leukocytes are the scientific name for white blood cells.","zh":"leukocytes 是白血球的科學名稱。"},{"en":"A medical report may list leukocytes when describing a patient’s immune response.","zh":"醫學報告描述病人免疫反應時，可能列出 leukocytes。"},{"en":"Leukocytes increase when the body needs more defence against infection.","zh":"當身體需要更多防禦來對抗感染時，白血球可能增加。"},{"en":"This formal term refers to the blood cells that protect the body.","zh":"這個正式術語指保護身體的血細胞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"similarly produced","meaning":"同樣地產生","examples":[{"en":"White blood cells are similarly produced in the bone marrow.","zh":"白血球同樣在骨髓中產生。"},{"en":"Similarly produced means made in the same or a very similar way or place.","zh":"similarly produced 指以相同或非常相似的方式或位置產生。"},{"en":"Two school worksheets may be similarly produced if both use the same template.","zh":"如果兩份學校工作紙使用同一模板，它們可能是同樣地製作出來。"},{"en":"Red and white blood cells are similarly produced because both come from bone marrow.","zh":"紅血球和白血球同樣地產生，因為兩者都來自骨髓。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a similarity between two production processes.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個產生過程之間的相似性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be active for","meaning":"活躍……時間","examples":[{"en":"Some white blood cells are active for only a few days.","zh":"有些白血球只活躍幾天。"},{"en":"To be active for a period means to function or work during that length of time.","zh":"be active for a period 指在某段時間內發揮功能或運作。"},{"en":"A discount code may be active for only one week.","zh":"優惠碼可能只有效一星期。"},{"en":"White blood cells may be active for a short time because they respond quickly to threats.","zh":"白血球可能只活躍短時間，因為它們快速回應威脅。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how long something continues to work.","zh":"這個短語描述某物持續運作多久。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be essential in doing something","meaning":"對做……不可或缺","examples":[{"en":"White blood cells are essential in defending the body against infection.","zh":"白血球對保護身體免受感染不可或缺。"},{"en":"To be essential in doing something means to be necessary for that action to happen successfully.","zh":"be essential in doing something 指對某行動成功發生是必需的。"},{"en":"Clear instructions are essential in helping students complete a difficult task.","zh":"清晰指示對幫助學生完成困難任務不可或缺。"},{"en":"White blood cells are essential because infections can spread without immune defence.","zh":"白血球不可或缺，因為沒有免疫防禦，感染可能擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something necessary, not merely helpful.","zh":"這個短語描述某事是必要的，而不只是有幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"defend the body against","meaning":"保護身體免受……侵害","examples":[{"en":"White blood cells defend the body against infections.","zh":"白血球保護身體免受感染侵害。"},{"en":"To defend the body against something means to protect it from harm or attack.","zh":"defend the body against something 指保護身體免受傷害或攻擊。"},{"en":"Vaccines help the body defend itself against certain diseases.","zh":"疫苗幫助身體保護自己免受某些疾病侵害。"},{"en":"If the body cannot defend itself against infection, even minor germs can become dangerous.","zh":"如果身體不能保護自己免受感染，即使小病菌也可能變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes biological protection.","zh":"這個短語描述生物防禦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"come in many different types","meaning":"有許多不同種類","examples":[{"en":"White blood cells come in many different types.","zh":"白血球有許多不同種類。"},{"en":"To come in many different types means to exist in several forms or categories.","zh":"come in many different types 指以幾種形式或類別存在。"},{"en":"Shoes come in many different types, such as trainers, boots, and sandals.","zh":"鞋有許多不同種類，例如運動鞋、靴和涼鞋。"},{"en":"White blood cells have different types because different threats need different defences.","zh":"白血球有不同種類，因為不同威脅需要不同防禦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes variety within one general group.","zh":"這個短語描述一個總類別內的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be designed to deal with","meaning":"為應付……而設","examples":[{"en":"Each type is designed to deal with a different invader.","zh":"每種類型都是為應付不同入侵物而設。"},{"en":"To be designed to deal with something means to be made for handling a particular problem.","zh":"be designed to deal with something 指被製造或形成來處理某特定問題。"},{"en":"A fire extinguisher is designed to deal with small fires, not medical emergencies.","zh":"滅火筒是為應付小型火警而設，不是為醫療緊急情況而設。"},{"en":"Different white blood cells are designed to deal with different germs or parasites.","zh":"不同白血球是為應付不同病菌或寄生蟲而設。"},{"en":"This phrase links a tool or body part with its specific job.","zh":"這個短語把工具或身體部分與其特定工作連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"invader","meaning":"入侵物","examples":[{"en":"A virus or bacterium can act as an invader in the body.","zh":"病毒或細菌可以在身體內成為入侵物。"},{"en":"An invader is something that enters a place where it does not belong and may cause harm.","zh":"invader 指進入不屬於它的地方並可能造成傷害的東西。"},{"en":"In a computer, a virus can be an invader that damages files.","zh":"在電腦中，病毒可以是破壞檔案的入侵物。"},{"en":"In the body, invaders such as bacteria can trigger an immune response.","zh":"在身體中，細菌等入侵物可以觸發免疫反應。"},{"en":"This word describes an outside threat entering a protected system.","zh":"這個字描述進入受保護系統的外來威脅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bacteria, viruses and fungi","meaning":"細菌、病毒和真菌","examples":[{"en":"White blood cells attack bacteria, viruses, and fungi.","zh":"白血球攻擊細菌、病毒和真菌。"},{"en":"Bacteria, viruses and fungi are different kinds of microorganisms that may cause disease.","zh":"bacteria, viruses and fungi 是可能引起疾病的不同微生物。"},{"en":"A doctor may need tests to know whether an illness is caused by bacteria, viruses, or fungi.","zh":"醫生可能需要檢測，才知道疾病是由細菌、病毒還是真菌造成。"},{"en":"Different microbes require different treatments, so identifying them matters.","zh":"不同微生物需要不同治療，因此識別它們很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase lists common biological threats to the body.","zh":"這個短語列出身體常見的生物威脅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"parasite","meaning":"寄生蟲","examples":[{"en":"Some white blood cells defend the body against parasites.","zh":"有些白血球保護身體免受寄生蟲侵害。"},{"en":"A parasite is an organism that lives on or inside another living thing and takes resources from it.","zh":"parasite 指生活在另一生物身上或體內，並從其取得資源的生物。"},{"en":"Some parasites enter the body through contaminated food or insect bites.","zh":"有些寄生蟲透過受污染食物或昆蟲叮咬進入身體。"},{"en":"Parasites can make people ill because they use the host’s nutrients or damage tissues.","zh":"寄生蟲會令人患病，因為它們使用宿主養分或傷害組織。"},{"en":"This word describes a living invader that depends on a host.","zh":"這個字描述依賴宿主生存的活入侵物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"enter the body","meaning":"進入身體","examples":[{"en":"White blood cells react when a harmful organism enters the body.","zh":"當有害生物進入身體時，白血球會作出反應。"},{"en":"To enter the body means to get inside the body through the mouth, skin, lungs, or another route.","zh":"enter the body 指透過口、皮膚、肺部或其他途徑進入身體內部。"},{"en":"Germs may enter the body when someone touches food with dirty hands.","zh":"當人用骯髒的手接觸食物，病菌可能進入身體。"},{"en":"Once harmful organisms enter the body, the immune system begins to respond.","zh":"一旦有害生物進入身體，免疫系統便開始回應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first stage of infection or exposure.","zh":"這個短語描述感染或接觸的第一階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"determine its nature","meaning":"判斷其性質","examples":[{"en":"The immune system quickly determines the nature of an invader.","zh":"免疫系統迅速判斷入侵物的性質。"},{"en":"To determine its nature means to identify what kind of thing it is and how it behaves.","zh":"determine its nature 指識別它是甚麼類型，以及它如何運作。"},{"en":"A doctor determines the nature of a rash before choosing treatment.","zh":"醫生在選擇治療前，會判斷皮疹的性質。"},{"en":"The body must determine an invader’s nature so it can choose the correct defence.","zh":"身體必須判斷入侵物的性質，才能選擇正確防禦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes identifying the type and character of something.","zh":"這個短語描述識別某物的類型和特性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"muster sufficient numbers","meaning":"集結足夠數量","examples":[{"en":"The body must muster sufficient numbers of the correct white blood cell.","zh":"身體必須集結足夠數量的正確白血球。"},{"en":"To muster sufficient numbers means to gather enough people, cells, or resources for a task.","zh":"muster sufficient numbers 指為某任務聚集足夠的人、細胞或資源。"},{"en":"A school must muster sufficient volunteers before running a large charity event.","zh":"學校舉辦大型慈善活動前，必須集結足夠志願者。"},{"en":"If the body cannot muster enough immune cells, infection may spread.","zh":"如果身體不能集結足夠免疫細胞，感染可能擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collecting enough of what is needed.","zh":"這個短語描述收集足夠所需之物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a specific type","meaning":"特定種類","examples":[{"en":"The body produces a specific type of white blood cell for each threat.","zh":"身體會為每種威脅產生特定種類的白血球。"},{"en":"A specific type is one particular kind, not just any general kind.","zh":"specific type 指某一特定種類，而不是任何一般種類。"},{"en":"A mechanic needs a specific type of tool to fix a particular engine part.","zh":"機械師需要特定種類的工具，才能修理某個引擎部件。"},{"en":"The immune system uses specific cells because different invaders require different responses.","zh":"免疫系統使用特定細胞，因為不同入侵物需要不同回應。"},{"en":"This phrase points to an exact category chosen for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語指出為某目的而選定的確切類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the period in which","meaning":"……發生的期間","examples":[{"en":"The period in which the body builds its defences is often when the person feels ill.","zh":"身體建立防禦的期間，通常就是人感到不適的時候。"},{"en":"The period in which something happens means the time during which that process takes place.","zh":"the period in which something happens 指某過程發生的那段時間。"},{"en":"The period in which students revise before exams can be stressful.","zh":"學生考試前溫習的期間可能令人有壓力。"},{"en":"During the period in which the immune system prepares, symptoms may appear.","zh":"在免疫系統準備的期間，症狀可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the time frame of an action or process.","zh":"這個短語指出某行動或過程的時間範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"launch into the fight","meaning":"投入戰鬥","examples":[{"en":"White blood cells launch themselves into the fight against infection.","zh":"白血球投入對抗感染的戰鬥。"},{"en":"To launch into the fight means to begin attacking or responding actively and forcefully.","zh":"launch into the fight 指開始積極而有力地攻擊或回應。"},{"en":"A debate team may launch into the fight once the opposing side makes a strong claim.","zh":"當對方提出強烈主張時，辯論隊可能投入戰鬥。"},{"en":"When enough white blood cells are ready, they begin attacking the invaders.","zh":"當足夠白血球準備好，它們便開始攻擊入侵物。"},{"en":"This phrase uses battle language to describe active defence.","zh":"這個短語用戰鬥語言描述主動防禦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"envelop each cell","meaning":"包圍每個細胞","examples":[{"en":"White blood cells may envelop each individual invasive cell.","zh":"白血球可能包圍每個單獨的入侵細胞。"},{"en":"To envelop each cell means to surround and cover each cell completely.","zh":"envelop each cell 指完全圍住並覆蓋每個細胞。"},{"en":"A blanket can envelop a child when it wraps fully around them.","zh":"當毛氈完全裹住孩子時，它可以包圍孩子全身。"},{"en":"Some white blood cells envelop harmful cells so they can digest or destroy them.","zh":"有些白血球包圍有害細胞，以便消化或消滅它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes surrounding something from all sides.","zh":"這個短語描述從四周包住某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"invasive cell","meaning":"入侵細胞","examples":[{"en":"An invasive cell may be broken down by the immune system.","zh":"入侵細胞可能被免疫系統分解。"},{"en":"An invasive cell is a harmful or foreign cell that has entered where it does not belong.","zh":"invasive cell 指進入不應出現位置的有害或外來細胞。"},{"en":"In the body, an invasive cell may be part of a bacterium or other threat.","zh":"在身體中，入侵細胞可能是細菌或其他威脅的一部分。"},{"en":"If invasive cells multiply, the immune system must respond quickly.","zh":"如果入侵細胞繁殖，免疫系統必須快速回應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a cell treated as an intruder.","zh":"這個短語描述被視為入侵者的細胞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"break something down","meaning":"分解……","examples":[{"en":"White blood cells break harmful cells down.","zh":"白血球分解有害細胞。"},{"en":"To break something down means to separate it into smaller parts or destroy its structure.","zh":"break something down 指把某物分成較小部分或破壞其結構。"},{"en":"The stomach breaks food down into smaller pieces the body can use.","zh":"胃把食物分解成身體可以使用的較小部分。"},{"en":"White blood cells break down harmful cells so the body can remove them.","zh":"白血球分解有害細胞，使身體能移除它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes destroying or reducing something into simpler parts.","zh":"這個短語描述破壞某物或把它簡化成較小部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lead to recovery","meaning":"促使康復","examples":[{"en":"The destruction of the invaders eventually leads to recovery.","zh":"入侵物被消滅最終促使康復。"},{"en":"To lead to recovery means to cause or help a person return to health.","zh":"lead to recovery 指造成或幫助一個人恢復健康。"},{"en":"Rest, medicine, and enough water can lead to recovery after a mild illness.","zh":"休息、藥物和足夠水分可以在輕微疾病後促使康復。"},{"en":"When the immune system removes the infection, symptoms usually improve.","zh":"當免疫系統清除感染，症狀通常會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a helpful process with becoming well again.","zh":"這個短語把有益過程與重新健康連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"that leaves","meaning":"這便剩下……","examples":[{"en":"That leaves platelets as the last main blood component.","zh":"這便剩下血小板作為最後一種主要血液成分。"},{"en":"That leaves means after discussing other items, the remaining item is this one.","zh":"that leaves 指討論完其他項目後，剩下的是這一項。"},{"en":"We have packed clothes and books; that leaves the laptop and charger.","zh":"我們已收拾衣服和書；這便剩下手提電腦和充電器。"},{"en":"In an explanation, “that leaves” helps move to the final remaining part.","zh":"在解釋中，that leaves 幫助轉到最後剩餘的部分。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what is left after other things have been covered.","zh":"這個短語引出其他東西處理後剩下的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"main component","meaning":"主要成分","examples":[{"en":"Platelets are another main component of blood.","zh":"血小板是血液的另一種主要成分。"},{"en":"A main component is an important part that helps make up a whole system.","zh":"main component 指組成整個系統的重要部分。"},{"en":"Flour is a main component of bread, while water and yeast are also important.","zh":"麵粉是麵包的主要成分，水和酵母也很重要。"},{"en":"Blood has several main components because it must perform several jobs.","zh":"血液有幾種主要成分，因為它必須執行幾種工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major building block of something.","zh":"這個短語描述某物的主要組成部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"platelets","meaning":"血小板","examples":[{"en":"Platelets help the blood to clot after an injury.","zh":"血小板幫助血液在受傷後凝固。"},{"en":"Platelets are small blood components that help stop bleeding.","zh":"platelets 指幫助止血的小型血液成分。"},{"en":"A doctor may check platelet levels before surgery to reduce bleeding risk.","zh":"醫生可能在手術前檢查血小板水平，以降低出血風險。"},{"en":"If platelets are too low, a small cut may bleed for longer than normal.","zh":"如果血小板過低，小傷口可能比正常流血更久。"},{"en":"This word names the blood component most closely linked with clotting.","zh":"這個字指出最與凝血相關的血液成分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"thrombocytes","meaning":"血小板","examples":[{"en":"Platelets are technically called thrombocytes.","zh":"血小板正式稱為 thrombocytes。"},{"en":"Thrombocytes are the scientific name for platelets.","zh":"thrombocytes 是血小板的科學名稱。"},{"en":"A laboratory report may mention thrombocytes when showing blood-clotting information.","zh":"化驗報告顯示凝血資料時，可能提到 thrombocytes。"},{"en":"If thrombocyte numbers are abnormal, doctors may worry about bleeding or clotting.","zh":"如果血小板數量異常，醫生可能擔心出血或凝血問題。"},{"en":"This formal word refers to the small blood components that help clot blood.","zh":"這個正式詞指幫助血液凝固的小型血液成分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"much smaller than","meaning":"比……小得多","examples":[{"en":"Platelets are much smaller than red and white blood cells.","zh":"血小板比紅血球和白血球小得多。"},{"en":"Much smaller than means far less large in size compared with something else.","zh":"much smaller than 指與某物相比，體積細小得多。"},{"en":"A phone screen is much smaller than a cinema screen.","zh":"手機螢幕比戲院銀幕小得多。"},{"en":"Platelets can circulate easily because they are much smaller than full blood cells.","zh":"血小板小得多，因此可以容易地在血液中循環。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a clear size comparison.","zh":"這個短語顯示清楚的大小比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"circulate freely","meaning":"自由循環","examples":[{"en":"Platelets circulate freely in the bloodstream.","zh":"血小板在血流中自由循環。"},{"en":"To circulate freely means to move around without being fixed in one place.","zh":"circulate freely 指不固定在一處，而是四處流動。"},{"en":"Air circulates freely in a well-ventilated classroom.","zh":"空氣在通風良好的課室中自由循環。"},{"en":"Platelets must circulate freely so they can reach an injury when needed.","zh":"血小板必須自由循環，才能在需要時到達傷口。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement through a system without obstruction.","zh":"這個短語描述在系統中不受阻礙地流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be responsible for","meaning":"負責……","examples":[{"en":"Platelets are responsible for blood clotting.","zh":"血小板負責血液凝固。"},{"en":"To be responsible for something means to have the duty or role of causing or managing it.","zh":"be responsible for something 指有責任或角色去造成或管理某事。"},{"en":"A class monitor may be responsible for collecting homework.","zh":"班長可能負責收功課。"},{"en":"Platelets are responsible for clotting because they help seal damaged blood vessels.","zh":"血小板負責凝血，因為它們幫助封住受損血管。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who or what performs a job.","zh":"這個短語指出誰或甚麼執行某項工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"clot the blood","meaning":"令血液凝固","examples":[{"en":"Platelets help clot the blood after an injury.","zh":"血小板幫助血液在受傷後凝固。"},{"en":"To clot the blood means to make liquid blood thicken and form a plug.","zh":"clot the blood 指令液態血液變稠並形成堵塞物。"},{"en":"When you cut your finger, the body clots the blood to stop bleeding.","zh":"當你割傷手指，身體會令血液凝固以止血。"},{"en":"If blood cannot clot properly, even a small wound may become dangerous.","zh":"如果血液不能正常凝固，即使小傷口也可能變危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process that stops bleeding.","zh":"這個短語描述止血的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"heal an injury","meaning":"治療傷口","examples":[{"en":"Blood clotting is necessary to heal an injury.","zh":"血液凝固對治療傷口是必要的。"},{"en":"To heal an injury means to repair damaged body tissue after harm.","zh":"heal an injury 指在受傷後修復受損身體組織。"},{"en":"A scraped knee needs time, cleaning, and protection to heal properly.","zh":"擦傷的膝蓋需要時間、清潔和保護才能妥善癒合。"},{"en":"Clotting helps heal an injury by stopping blood loss and starting repair.","zh":"凝血透過止血和啟動修復來幫助治療傷口。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the body returning damaged tissue to a healthier state.","zh":"這個短語描述身體把受損組織恢復至較健康狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"external and internal injuries","meaning":"外傷和內傷","examples":[{"en":"Clotting helps the body repair both external and internal injuries.","zh":"凝血幫助身體修復外傷和內傷。"},{"en":"External injuries are on the outside of the body, while internal injuries are inside the body.","zh":"external injuries 在身體外部，而 internal injuries 在身體內部。"},{"en":"A cut on the arm is external, but bleeding inside the stomach is internal.","zh":"手臂割傷是外傷，但胃內出血是內傷。"},{"en":"Blood clotting matters for both kinds because the body must stop blood loss wherever it occurs.","zh":"凝血對兩者都重要，因為身體必須在任何出血位置止血。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts visible injuries with hidden ones.","zh":"這個短語把可見傷害與隱藏傷害作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ability to change shape","meaning":"改變形狀的能力","examples":[{"en":"Platelets have the interesting ability to change shape.","zh":"血小板具有有趣的改變形狀能力。"},{"en":"Ability to change shape means the capacity to alter form when needed.","zh":"ability to change shape 指在需要時改變形態的能力。"},{"en":"Some toys have the ability to change shape from a car into a robot.","zh":"有些玩具具有從汽車變成機械人的改變形狀能力。"},{"en":"Platelets change shape so they can stick together and help form a clot.","zh":"血小板會改變形狀，以便互相黏附並幫助形成血塊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes flexibility in physical form.","zh":"這個短語描述物理形態上的靈活性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be related to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Several diseases are related to abnormal platelet numbers.","zh":"幾種疾病與血小板數量異常有關。"},{"en":"To be related to something means to have a connection with it.","zh":"be related to something 指與某事有連繫。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is related to lower concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足與課堂專注力下降有關。"},{"en":"Diseases may be related to platelet numbers because platelets affect bleeding and clotting.","zh":"疾病可能與血小板數量有關，因為血小板影響出血和凝血。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two things are connected in cause, effect, or association.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩件事在原因、結果或關聯上有連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a breakdown in regulation","meaning":"調節機制失靈","examples":[{"en":"Disease may result from a breakdown in the regulation of platelet numbers.","zh":"疾病可能源於血小板數量調節機制失靈。"},{"en":"A breakdown in regulation means the system that controls something stops working properly.","zh":"breakdown in regulation 指控制某事的系統停止正常運作。"},{"en":"A breakdown in school discipline may happen when rules are unclear and nobody enforces them.","zh":"當規則不清楚且無人執行，學校紀律調節可能失靈。"},{"en":"If platelet regulation breaks down, the body may have too many or too few platelets.","zh":"如果血小板調節失靈，身體可能有太多或太少血小板。"},{"en":"This phrase describes failure in a control system.","zh":"這個短語描述控制系統失效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"regulate their numbers","meaning":"調節其數量","examples":[{"en":"The body must carefully regulate the number of platelets.","zh":"身體必須小心調節血小板數量。"},{"en":"To regulate their numbers means to control how many of them exist.","zh":"regulate their numbers 指控制它們存在的數目。"},{"en":"A school regulates class numbers so each teacher can manage students properly.","zh":"學校會調節班級人數，讓每位老師能妥善管理學生。"},{"en":"The body regulates platelet numbers because both too many and too few can be dangerous.","zh":"身體調節血小板數量，因為太多或太少都可能危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping a quantity within a safe range.","zh":"這個短語描述把數量保持在安全範圍內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be too low","meaning":"過低","examples":[{"en":"If the platelet count is too low, excessive bleeding may occur.","zh":"如果血小板數量過低，可能出現大量出血。"},{"en":"To be too low means to fall below the level needed for safety or normal function.","zh":"be too low 指低於安全或正常功能所需水平。"},{"en":"If a student’s attendance is too low, they may miss important lessons.","zh":"如果學生出席率過低，可能錯過重要課堂。"},{"en":"A platelet count that is too low can make it hard for blood to clot.","zh":"血小板數量過低會令血液難以凝固。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an amount below a safe or useful level.","zh":"這個短語描述低於安全或有用水平的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"excessive bleeding","meaning":"大量出血","examples":[{"en":"A low platelet count can cause excessive bleeding.","zh":"血小板數量偏低可以造成大量出血。"},{"en":"Excessive bleeding is bleeding that is heavier or lasts longer than normal.","zh":"excessive bleeding 指比正常更多或持續更久的出血。"},{"en":"If a small cut keeps bleeding for a long time, it may be excessive bleeding.","zh":"如果小傷口長時間不停流血，可能是大量出血。"},{"en":"Excessive bleeding can be dangerous because the body loses too much blood.","zh":"大量出血很危險，因為身體會失去太多血液。"},{"en":"This phrase describes abnormal or serious blood loss.","zh":"這個短語描述異常或嚴重失血。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"internal clotting","meaning":"體內血液凝固","examples":[{"en":"Too many platelets may result in internal clotting.","zh":"血小板太多可能導致體內血液凝固。"},{"en":"Internal clotting means blood forms clots inside the body where they may block vessels.","zh":"internal clotting 指血液在體內形成血塊，可能阻塞血管。"},{"en":"A clot inside a leg vein is an example of internal clotting.","zh":"腿部靜脈內的血塊就是體內血液凝固的例子。"},{"en":"Internal clotting can be dangerous because the clot may stop blood from reaching an organ.","zh":"體內血液凝固可能危險，因為血塊可能阻止血液到達器官。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clotting that happens inside rather than on a visible wound.","zh":"這個短語描述發生在體內，而不是可見傷口上的凝血。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"potentially catastrophic","meaning":"可能造成災難性後果的","examples":[{"en":"Internal blood clots may cause potentially catastrophic damage.","zh":"體內血塊可能造成災難性損害。"},{"en":"Potentially catastrophic means possibly causing extremely serious harm.","zh":"potentially catastrophic 指可能造成極其嚴重的傷害。"},{"en":"A small fire in a kitchen can become potentially catastrophic if gas is leaking nearby.","zh":"如果附近有煤氣洩漏，廚房小火也可能造成災難性後果。"},{"en":"A blood clot can be potentially catastrophic if it blocks blood flow to the brain or heart.","zh":"如果血塊阻塞流向大腦或心臟的血液，可能造成災難性後果。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that the result could be disastrous.","zh":"這個短語警告結果可能是災難性的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"blockage","meaning":"阻塞","examples":[{"en":"A blood clot can create a blockage in a blood vessel.","zh":"血塊可以在血管中造成阻塞。"},{"en":"A blockage is something that stops or slows movement through a passage.","zh":"blockage 指阻止或拖慢物體通過通道的東西。"},{"en":"Hair in a drain can create a blockage that prevents water from flowing away.","zh":"排水口中的頭髮可以造成阻塞，使水無法流走。"},{"en":"In the body, a blockage in a vessel can stop oxygen-rich blood from reaching tissues.","zh":"在身體中，血管阻塞可以阻止富氧血液到達組織。"},{"en":"This word describes an obstruction in a pathway.","zh":"這個字描述通道中的障礙物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"medical ailment","meaning":"疾病","examples":[{"en":"Strokes and heart attacks are serious medical ailments.","zh":"中風和心臟病發是嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"A medical ailment is a disease, illness, or health problem.","zh":"medical ailment 指疾病、病症或健康問題。"},{"en":"A persistent cough may be a minor ailment, but chest pain may signal something serious.","zh":"持續咳嗽可能是輕微病症，但胸痛可能代表嚴重問題。"},{"en":"Some medical ailments develop suddenly, while others build up over time.","zh":"有些疾病突然發生，另一些則逐漸形成。"},{"en":"This phrase is a general way to describe health conditions.","zh":"這個短語是描述健康狀況的一般說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stroke","meaning":"中風","examples":[{"en":"A blockage in the brain can cause a stroke.","zh":"大腦中的阻塞可以導致中風。"},{"en":"A stroke is a serious medical event in which blood supply to part of the brain is blocked or reduced.","zh":"stroke 指腦部某部分血液供應被阻塞或減少的嚴重醫療事件。"},{"en":"Sudden weakness on one side of the body may be a warning sign of a stroke.","zh":"身體一側突然無力可能是中風警號。"},{"en":"A stroke can damage speech, movement, memory, or vision.","zh":"中風可以損害說話、活動、記憶或視力。"},{"en":"This word names a medical emergency involving the brain.","zh":"這個字指出涉及大腦的醫療急症。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"heart attack","meaning":"心臟病發","examples":[{"en":"A blockage in the heart can cause a heart attack.","zh":"心臟中的阻塞可以導致心臟病發。"},{"en":"A heart attack happens when blood flow to part of the heart is blocked.","zh":"heart attack 指流向心臟某部分的血液被阻塞時發生的情況。"},{"en":"Severe chest pain and shortness of breath can be signs of a heart attack.","zh":"嚴重胸痛和呼吸短促可以是心臟病發的跡象。"},{"en":"If heart muscle loses oxygen, it can be damaged quickly.","zh":"如果心肌失去氧氣，可能很快受損。"},{"en":"This phrase names a medical emergency involving the heart.","zh":"這個短語指出涉及心臟的醫療急症。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"embolism","meaning":"栓塞","examples":[{"en":"An embolism occurs when a clot blocks a blood vessel.","zh":"當血塊阻塞血管時，就會發生栓塞。"},{"en":"An embolism is a blockage caused by a clot or other material travelling through the bloodstream.","zh":"embolism 指由血塊或其他物質經血流移動而造成的阻塞。"},{"en":"A lung embolism can happen when a clot travels to the lungs.","zh":"當血塊移動到肺部時，可能發生肺栓塞。"},{"en":"An embolism is dangerous because it can suddenly stop blood flow.","zh":"栓塞很危險，因為它可以突然阻止血液流動。"},{"en":"This word describes a moving blockage inside the circulation system.","zh":"這個字描述循環系統內移動中的阻塞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"blood’s complexity","meaning":"血液的複雜性","examples":[{"en":"Blood’s complexity creates difficulties during transfusions.","zh":"血液的複雜性在輸血時造成困難。"},{"en":"Blood’s complexity means blood has many parts, groups, antigens, and reactions to consider.","zh":"blood’s complexity 指血液有許多部分、血型、抗原和反應需要考慮。"},{"en":"A doctor cannot treat blood as a simple liquid because its components behave differently.","zh":"醫生不能把血液當成簡單液體，因為其成分有不同行為。"},{"en":"Because blood is complex, matching donor blood with patient blood requires care.","zh":"由於血液複雜，把捐血者血液與病人血液配對需要小心。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why blood-related medical work can be difficult.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何血液相關醫療工作可以很困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"present particular difficulties","meaning":"帶來特殊困難","examples":[{"en":"Blood compatibility presents particular difficulties in emergencies.","zh":"血液相容性在緊急情況中帶來特殊困難。"},{"en":"To present particular difficulties means to create specific problems that need careful handling.","zh":"present particular difficulties 指造成需要小心處理的特定問題。"},{"en":"Teaching a large mixed-level class presents particular difficulties for a new teacher.","zh":"教導大型混合程度班級，會為新老師帶來特殊困難。"},{"en":"Emergency transfusions are difficult because doctors may have little time to test blood fully.","zh":"緊急輸血很困難，因為醫生可能沒有太多時間完整檢測血液。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights special challenges in a situation.","zh":"這個短語突出某情況中的特殊挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"emergency transfusion","meaning":"緊急輸血","examples":[{"en":"An emergency transfusion may be required after severe blood loss.","zh":"嚴重失血後，可能需要緊急輸血。"},{"en":"An emergency transfusion is a rapid transfer of blood to a patient in a life-threatening situation.","zh":"emergency transfusion 指在危及生命情況下快速把血液輸給病人。"},{"en":"A patient injured in a car accident may need an emergency transfusion.","zh":"車禍受傷的病人可能需要緊急輸血。"},{"en":"Emergency transfusions must balance speed with safety because incompatible blood can be dangerous.","zh":"緊急輸血必須在速度和安全之間取得平衡，因為不相容血液可能很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes urgent blood replacement.","zh":"這個短語描述緊急補充血液。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be avoided whenever possible","meaning":"在可行情況下盡量避免","examples":[{"en":"Transfusions are avoided whenever possible because of possible reactions.","zh":"由於可能出現反應，輸血在可行情況下會盡量避免。"},{"en":"To be avoided whenever possible means to be done only when necessary.","zh":"be avoided whenever possible 指只有在必要時才做某事。"},{"en":"Doctors avoid unnecessary antibiotics whenever possible to reduce resistance.","zh":"醫生在可行情況下盡量避免不必要使用抗生素，以減少抗藥性。"},{"en":"Blood transfusions may be avoided when other safer treatments are enough.","zh":"當其他較安全治療足夠時，可能會避免輸血。"},{"en":"This phrase shows caution because an action carries risk.","zh":"這個短語顯示因某行動有風險而採取謹慎態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lower the risk of","meaning":"降低……的風險","examples":[{"en":"Careful testing lowers the risk of a transfusion reaction.","zh":"仔細檢測會降低輸血反應的風險。"},{"en":"To lower the risk of something means to reduce the chance that it will happen.","zh":"lower the risk of something 指減少某事發生的機會。"},{"en":"Wearing a seat belt lowers the risk of serious injury in a car accident.","zh":"繫安全帶會降低車禍中嚴重受傷的風險。"},{"en":"Blood testing lowers risk by identifying possible incompatibility before transfusion.","zh":"血液檢測透過在輸血前識別可能的不相容來降低風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a bad outcome less likely.","zh":"這個短語描述令壞結果較不可能發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"transfusion reaction","meaning":"輸血反應","examples":[{"en":"Blood incompatibility can cause a serious transfusion reaction.","zh":"血液不相容可以引起嚴重輸血反應。"},{"en":"A transfusion reaction is a harmful response by the body to transfused blood.","zh":"transfusion reaction 指身體對輸入血液產生的有害反應。"},{"en":"Fever, chills, or breathing problems may warn doctors of a transfusion reaction.","zh":"發燒、發冷或呼吸困難可能提醒醫生出現輸血反應。"},{"en":"Transfusion reactions can occur when the immune system attacks donated blood.","zh":"當免疫系統攻擊捐贈血液時，可能出現輸血反應。"},{"en":"This phrase names a dangerous medical response to blood transfer.","zh":"這個短語指出對輸血產生的危險醫療反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"blood incompatibility","meaning":"血液不相容","examples":[{"en":"Blood incompatibility may produce potentially lethal results.","zh":"血液不相容可能產生致命後果。"},{"en":"Blood incompatibility means donor blood and patient blood do not match safely.","zh":"blood incompatibility 指捐血者血液與病人血液不能安全配對。"},{"en":"Before a transfusion, hospitals test for blood incompatibility.","zh":"輸血前，醫院會檢測血液不相容問題。"},{"en":"If blood is incompatible, the patient’s immune system may attack the transfused cells.","zh":"如果血液不相容，病人的免疫系統可能攻擊輸入的細胞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a dangerous mismatch between blood types or antigens.","zh":"這個短語描述血型或抗原之間的危險不匹配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"unexpected antigens","meaning":"未預期的抗原","examples":[{"en":"Unexpected antigens may trigger a dangerous immune response.","zh":"未預期的抗原可能觸發危險免疫反應。"},{"en":"Unexpected antigens are substances on cells that the immune system did not expect and may treat as foreign.","zh":"unexpected antigens 指細胞上免疫系統未預期並可能視為外來物的物質。"},{"en":"In a transfusion, unexpected antigens can make the patient’s body attack donated blood.","zh":"在輸血中，未預期的抗原可以令病人身體攻擊捐贈血液。"},{"en":"Careful testing helps find unexpected antigens before blood is given.","zh":"仔細檢測有助在輸血前找出未預期的抗原。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hidden immune markers that may cause danger.","zh":"這個短語描述可能造成危險的隱藏免疫標記。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"trigger antibodies to attack","meaning":"觸發抗體攻擊","examples":[{"en":"Some antigens trigger antibodies to attack blood components.","zh":"有些抗原會觸發抗體攻擊血液成分。"},{"en":"To trigger antibodies to attack means to cause immune proteins to target something as harmful.","zh":"trigger antibodies to attack 指令免疫蛋白把某物視為有害並進行攻擊。"},{"en":"An allergen can trigger antibodies to attack substances the body sees as a threat.","zh":"過敏原可以觸發抗體攻擊身體視為威脅的物質。"},{"en":"In transfusion, the wrong antigen may trigger antibodies to attack donor blood cells.","zh":"在輸血中，錯誤抗原可能觸發抗體攻擊捐血者血細胞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the start of an immune attack.","zh":"這個短語描述免疫攻擊的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"blood components","meaning":"血液成分","examples":[{"en":"Antibodies may mistakenly attack blood components.","zh":"抗體可能錯誤攻擊血液成分。"},{"en":"Blood components are the different parts of blood, such as plasma, cells, and platelets.","zh":"blood components 指血液的不同部分，例如血漿、細胞和血小板。"},{"en":"A hospital may separate blood components so different patients receive what they need.","zh":"醫院可能分離血液成分，讓不同病人得到所需部分。"},{"en":"If immune cells attack blood components, the transfusion can become dangerous.","zh":"如果免疫細胞攻擊血液成分，輸血可能變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the parts that together make up blood.","zh":"這個短語指共同組成血液的各部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"potentially lethal results","meaning":"可能致命的後果","examples":[{"en":"An incompatible transfusion may have potentially lethal results.","zh":"不相容輸血可能帶來致命後果。"},{"en":"Potentially lethal results are outcomes that could cause death.","zh":"potentially lethal results 指可能導致死亡的結果。"},{"en":"A severe allergic reaction can have potentially lethal results if treatment is delayed.","zh":"如果治療延誤，嚴重過敏反應可能造成致命後果。"},{"en":"Blood incompatibility can be lethal because the immune system may destroy transfused cells.","zh":"血液不相容可能致命，因為免疫系統可能破壞輸入的細胞。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that the danger may be life-threatening.","zh":"這個短語警告危險可能威脅生命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take place","meaning":"進行；發生","examples":[{"en":"If a transfusion is to take place, blood must be carefully classified.","zh":"如果要進行輸血，血液必須被仔細分類。"},{"en":"To take place means to happen or occur.","zh":"take place 指發生或進行。"},{"en":"A school meeting will take place after lunch in the hall.","zh":"學校會議將在午飯後於禮堂進行。"},{"en":"Before a transfusion takes place, doctors must check blood compatibility.","zh":"輸血進行前，醫生必須檢查血液相容性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an event happening.","zh":"這個短語描述事件發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"thorough knowledge of","meaning":"對……有全面認識","examples":[{"en":"A thorough knowledge of blood groups is essential for safe transfusions.","zh":"對血型有全面認識，對安全輸血至關重要。"},{"en":"Thorough knowledge of something means deep and careful understanding of it.","zh":"thorough knowledge of something 指對某事有深入而仔細的理解。"},{"en":"A pilot needs thorough knowledge of safety procedures before flying passengers.","zh":"機師載客飛行前需要對安全程序有全面認識。"},{"en":"Doctors need thorough blood-group knowledge because mistakes can harm patients.","zh":"醫生需要全面了解血型，因為錯誤可以傷害病人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes detailed understanding, not basic familiarity.","zh":"這個短語描述詳細理解，而不是基本熟悉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"classification of blood","meaning":"血液分類","examples":[{"en":"The classification of blood is essential before a transfusion.","zh":"輸血前，血液分類是必要的。"},{"en":"Classification of blood means sorting blood into groups according to markers such as antigens.","zh":"classification of blood 指按照抗原等標記把血液分成不同組別。"},{"en":"Blood classification tells doctors which blood can be safely given to which patient.","zh":"血液分類告訴醫生哪些血液可以安全輸給哪些病人。"},{"en":"Without blood classification, transfusion reactions would be more likely.","zh":"沒有血液分類，輸血反應會更可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organising blood into medical categories.","zh":"這個短語描述把血液組織成醫學類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be essential","meaning":"至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Accurate blood-group identification is essential in medical care.","zh":"準確識別血型在醫療護理中至關重要。"},{"en":"To be essential means to be absolutely necessary.","zh":"be essential 指絕對必要。"},{"en":"Clean water is essential for health and daily life.","zh":"清潔食水對健康和日常生活至關重要。"},{"en":"Blood-group identification is essential because wrong blood can trigger a dangerous reaction.","zh":"血型識別至關重要，因為錯誤血液可以觸發危險反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that cannot safely be left out.","zh":"這個短語描述不能安全省略的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"recognised blood-group systems","meaning":"獲認可的血型系統","examples":[{"en":"There are around 30 recognised blood-group systems.","zh":"約有三十個獲認可的血型系統。"},{"en":"Recognised blood-group systems are officially accepted ways of classifying blood.","zh":"recognised blood-group systems 指正式接受的血液分類方法。"},{"en":"The ABO system is one recognised blood-group system that many people know.","zh":"ABO 系統是許多人知道的一個獲認可血型系統。"},{"en":"Multiple recognised systems exist because blood has many different antigens.","zh":"存在多個獲認可系統，因為血液有許多不同抗原。"},{"en":"This phrase describes medically accepted blood-classification systems.","zh":"這個短語描述醫學上接受的血液分類系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"contain hundreds of antigens","meaning":"含有數百種抗原","examples":[{"en":"The recognised blood-group systems contain hundreds of antigens.","zh":"獲認可的血型系統含有數百種抗原。"},{"en":"To contain hundreds of antigens means to include a very large number of immune markers.","zh":"contain hundreds of antigens 指包括大量免疫標記。"},{"en":"A complex database may contain hundreds of labels for different user groups.","zh":"複雜數據庫可能含有數百個不同用戶群組標籤。"},{"en":"Blood matching is difficult because there are hundreds of antigens to consider.","zh":"血液配對很困難，因為有數百種抗原需要考慮。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why blood classification is complex.","zh":"這個短語解釋血液分類為何複雜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"present quite a challenge","meaning":"帶來相當大的挑戰","examples":[{"en":"The complexity of blood groups presents quite a challenge.","zh":"血型的複雜性帶來相當大的挑戰。"},{"en":"To present quite a challenge means to create a fairly difficult problem.","zh":"present quite a challenge 指造成相當困難的問題。"},{"en":"Teaching thirty students with very different levels presents quite a challenge.","zh":"教導三十名程度差異很大的學生，會帶來相當大的挑戰。"},{"en":"Blood groups present a challenge because many markers must be matched safely.","zh":"血型帶來挑戰，因為許多標記必須安全配對。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that is difficult but possible to handle.","zh":"這個短語描述困難但仍可處理的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ABO system","meaning":"ABO 血型系統","examples":[{"en":"The ABO system is the most important blood-group system.","zh":"ABO 血型系統是最重要的血型系統。"},{"en":"The ABO system classifies blood mainly into A, B, AB, and O groups.","zh":"ABO system 主要把血液分為 A、B、AB 和 O 型。"},{"en":"Hospitals check the ABO system carefully before most transfusions.","zh":"醫院在大多數輸血前會仔細檢查 ABO 血型系統。"},{"en":"If the wrong ABO blood is given, the patient may have a serious reaction.","zh":"如果輸入錯誤 ABO 血型，病人可能出現嚴重反應。"},{"en":"This phrase names the best-known blood-group classification system.","zh":"這個短語指出最廣為人知的血型分類系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"on top of this","meaning":"除此之外","examples":[{"en":"On top of this, doctors must consider the Rhesus factor.","zh":"除此之外，醫生還必須考慮 Rh 因子。"},{"en":"On top of this means in addition to what has already been mentioned.","zh":"on top of this 指除了已提及的事情之外。"},{"en":"The rent is expensive; on top of this, electricity costs have increased.","zh":"租金很貴；除此之外，電費也上升了。"},{"en":"Blood matching is already complex, and on top of this the Rhesus factor adds another layer.","zh":"血液配對本來已很複雜，除此之外 Rh 因子又增加另一層考量。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an extra point or burden.","zh":"這個短語引出額外觀點或負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Rhesus factor","meaning":"恒河猴因子；Rh 因子","examples":[{"en":"The Rhesus factor is another important part of blood classification.","zh":"Rh 因子是血液分類的另一個重要部分。"},{"en":"The Rhesus factor, or Rh factor, is an antigen system used in blood typing.","zh":"Rhesus factor 或 Rh factor 是血型分類中使用的抗原系統。"},{"en":"People often hear Rh described simply as positive or negative.","zh":"人們常聽到 Rh 被簡單描述為陽性或陰性。"},{"en":"Doctors consider the Rhesus factor because mismatches can affect transfusion safety.","zh":"醫生考慮 Rh 因子，因為不匹配可能影響輸血安全。"},{"en":"This phrase names an important blood-group marker beyond ABO.","zh":"這個短語指出 ABO 以外的重要血型標記。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not as simple as","meaning":"並非像……那麼簡單","examples":[{"en":"The Rhesus system is not as simple as positive or negative.","zh":"Rh 系統並非像陽性或陰性那麼簡單。"},{"en":"Not as simple as means more complicated than the basic description suggests.","zh":"not as simple as 指比基本描述所暗示的更複雜。"},{"en":"Healthy eating is not as simple as avoiding sugar; balance and portion size also matter.","zh":"健康飲食並非像避免糖分那麼簡單；均衡和份量也重要。"},{"en":"The Rhesus system includes many antigens, so it is not just one yes-or-no label.","zh":"Rh 系統包含許多抗原，所以不只是單一的是或否標籤。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a topic has hidden complexity.","zh":"這個短語提醒某主題有隱藏的複雜性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"comprise scores of","meaning":"包括數十種……","examples":[{"en":"The Rhesus system comprises scores of different antigens.","zh":"Rh 系統包括數十種不同抗原。"},{"en":"To comprise scores of something means to include many dozens of them.","zh":"comprise scores of something 指包括許多、數十個某物。"},{"en":"A large library may comprise scores of sections for different subjects.","zh":"大型圖書館可能包括數十個不同學科分區。"},{"en":"The Rhesus system is complex because it comprises many antigens, not just one marker.","zh":"Rh 系統很複雜，因為它包括許多抗原，而不只是一個標記。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a system made up of many parts.","zh":"這個短語描述由許多部分組成的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be clustered together","meaning":"被歸入同一組","examples":[{"en":"Related antigens can be clustered together into groups.","zh":"相關抗原可以被歸入同一組。"},{"en":"To be clustered together means to be grouped closely because of shared features.","zh":"be clustered together 指因共同特徵而被密切分組。"},{"en":"Students with similar reading levels may be clustered together for extra practice.","zh":"閱讀程度相近的學生可能被歸入同一組作額外練習。"},{"en":"Antigens are clustered together when they cause similar immune responses.","zh":"當抗原引起相似免疫反應時，它們會被歸入同一組。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organising similar things into groups.","zh":"這個短語描述把相似事物組織成群組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cause similar responses","meaning":"引起相似反應","examples":[{"en":"Some antigens cause similar immune responses.","zh":"有些抗原引起相似免疫反應。"},{"en":"To cause similar responses means to produce reactions that are alike.","zh":"cause similar responses 指產生相近的反應。"},{"en":"Two medicines may cause similar responses, such as sleepiness or dry mouth.","zh":"兩種藥物可能引起相似反應，例如嗜睡或口乾。"},{"en":"If antigens cause similar responses, scientists may group them together.","zh":"如果抗原引起相似反應，科學家可能把它們歸類在一起。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with reactions that look or act alike.","zh":"這個短語把原因與相似反應連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"create some order","meaning":"令系統較有條理","examples":[{"en":"Grouping related antigens creates some order within the system.","zh":"把相關抗原分組會令系統較有條理。"},{"en":"To create some order means to make a confusing situation more organised.","zh":"create some order 指令混亂情況變得較有組織。"},{"en":"Labelling books by subject creates some order in a messy shelf.","zh":"按科目標籤書本可以令凌亂書架較有條理。"},{"en":"Grouping antigens helps doctors understand a complex blood system more clearly.","zh":"把抗原分組幫助醫生更清楚理解複雜血型系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing confusion through organisation.","zh":"這個短語描述透過組織減少混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the simplest system","meaning":"最簡單的方法","examples":[{"en":"The simplest system is for patients to receive their own blood.","zh":"最簡單的方法是讓病人接受自己的血液。"},{"en":"The simplest system means the easiest or least risky method among available choices.","zh":"the simplest system 指可選方法中最容易或風險最低的一種。"},{"en":"The simplest system for collecting homework may be one labelled tray for each class.","zh":"收功課最簡單的方法可能是每班一個有標籤的收集盤。"},{"en":"Using a patient’s own blood is simplest because compatibility problems are reduced.","zh":"使用病人自己的血液最簡單，因為相容性問題會減少。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the most straightforward method.","zh":"這個短語引出最直接的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"avoid adverse reactions","meaning":"避免不良反應","examples":[{"en":"Using a patient’s own blood helps avoid adverse transfusion reactions.","zh":"使用病人自己的血液有助避免不良輸血反應。"},{"en":"To avoid adverse reactions means to prevent harmful or unwanted responses.","zh":"avoid adverse reactions 指防止有害或不想要的反應。"},{"en":"A doctor asks about allergies to avoid adverse reactions to medicine.","zh":"醫生詢問過敏史，以避免藥物不良反應。"},{"en":"Own-blood transfusion can avoid immune reactions caused by donor blood.","zh":"自體輸血可以避免由捐血者血液引起的免疫反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preventing negative medical effects.","zh":"這個短語描述防止負面醫療效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"receive one’s own blood","meaning":"接受自己的血液","examples":[{"en":"A patient may receive their own stored blood during an operation.","zh":"病人可能在手術期間接受自己儲存的血液。"},{"en":"To receive one’s own blood means to be given blood that was previously taken from the same person.","zh":"receive one’s own blood 指接受先前從同一人身上抽取的血液。"},{"en":"Before planned surgery, a patient may store blood so they can receive their own blood later.","zh":"在預定手術前，病人可能儲存血液，以便之後接受自己的血液。"},{"en":"Receiving one’s own blood reduces the risk of donor incompatibility.","zh":"接受自己的血液可以降低捐血者血液不相容的風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes autologous transfusion in simple terms.","zh":"這個短語用簡單方式描述自體輸血。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"blood donation","meaning":"捐血","examples":[{"en":"A patient may make a blood donation before a planned operation.","zh":"病人可能在計劃手術前捐血。"},{"en":"Blood donation is the act of giving blood so it can be stored or used medically.","zh":"blood donation 指捐出血液，以便儲存或作醫療用途。"},{"en":"Healthy adults may make a blood donation at a community blood drive.","zh":"健康成年人可能在社區捐血活動中捐血。"},{"en":"Blood donation helps hospitals maintain supplies for surgery and emergencies.","zh":"捐血幫助醫院維持手術和緊急情況所需供應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving blood for medical use.","zh":"這個短語描述為醫療用途提供血液。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in anticipation of","meaning":"預先為……作準備","examples":[{"en":"Blood may be donated in anticipation of an operation.","zh":"血液可能預先為手術作準備而捐出。"},{"en":"In anticipation of something means before it happens, because you expect it or prepare for it.","zh":"in anticipation of something 指在某事發生前，因預期或準備它而行動。"},{"en":"A family may buy extra food in anticipation of a typhoon.","zh":"家庭可能預先為颱風作準備而購買額外食物。"},{"en":"Patients may donate blood in anticipation of surgery so it is ready if needed.","zh":"病人可能預先為手術捐血，以便需要時已有血液可用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparation for an expected future event.","zh":"這個短語描述為預期中的未來事件作準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"scheduled in advance","meaning":"預早安排","examples":[{"en":"The operation may be scheduled several months in advance.","zh":"手術可能在數月前預早安排。"},{"en":"Scheduled in advance means arranged before the time when something will happen.","zh":"scheduled in advance 指在事情發生前已安排好。"},{"en":"A school trip is usually scheduled in advance so parents can prepare.","zh":"學校旅行通常會預早安排，讓家長可以準備。"},{"en":"When surgery is scheduled in advance, doctors have time to plan blood needs.","zh":"當手術預早安排，醫生有時間規劃血液需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planned timing rather than sudden action.","zh":"這個短語描述有計劃的時間安排，而不是突然行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the second-best system","meaning":"次佳方法","examples":[{"en":"The second-best system is to undertake cross-matching.","zh":"次佳方法是進行血液交叉配對。"},{"en":"The second-best system is the next most suitable method when the best method is not available.","zh":"second-best system 指最佳方法不可用時，下一個最合適的方法。"},{"en":"If direct tutoring is impossible, a recorded lesson may be the second-best system.","zh":"如果面授補習不可行，錄影課堂可能是次佳方法。"},{"en":"Cross-matching is second-best because it checks compatibility when own blood cannot be used.","zh":"血液交叉配對是次佳方法，因為當不能使用自身血液時，它可以檢查相容性。"},{"en":"This phrase ranks one method just below the ideal option.","zh":"這個短語把某方法排在理想選項之後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"undertake cross-matching","meaning":"進行血液交叉配對","examples":[{"en":"Laboratory staff undertake cross-matching before a transfusion.","zh":"化驗室人員在輸血前進行血液交叉配對。"},{"en":"To undertake cross-matching means to test whether patient blood and donor blood are compatible.","zh":"undertake cross-matching 指檢測病人血液與捐血者血液是否相容。"},{"en":"Before a transplant or transfusion, laboratory staff may undertake matching tests.","zh":"在移植或輸血前，化驗室人員可能進行配對測試。"},{"en":"Cross-matching helps prevent dangerous immune reactions during transfusion.","zh":"血液交叉配對有助防止輸血時出現危險免疫反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a safety test before blood is given.","zh":"這個短語描述輸血前的安全測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"involve doing something","meaning":"涉及做……","examples":[{"en":"Cross-matching involves mixing patient and donor blood samples.","zh":"血液交叉配對涉及混合病人和捐血者的血液樣本。"},{"en":"To involve doing something means to include that action as part of the process.","zh":"involve doing something 指把某行動包括在過程之中。"},{"en":"Applying for university may involve writing essays, submitting forms, and attending interviews.","zh":"申請大學可能涉及寫文章、提交表格和參加面試。"},{"en":"Cross-matching involves mixing samples because staff need to see whether they react badly.","zh":"血液交叉配對涉及混合樣本，因為人員需要看它們是否有不良反應。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what actions are part of a process.","zh":"這個短語解釋某過程包括哪些行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"blood sample","meaning":"血液樣本","examples":[{"en":"A small blood sample is used for compatibility testing.","zh":"一小份血液樣本用於相容性測試。"},{"en":"A blood sample is a small amount of blood taken for examination.","zh":"blood sample 指抽取少量血液作檢查之用。"},{"en":"A nurse may take a blood sample to test sugar, iron, or infection markers.","zh":"護士可能抽取血液樣本來測試糖分、鐵質或感染標記。"},{"en":"Blood samples allow doctors to check health without needing a large amount of blood.","zh":"血液樣本讓醫生不用大量血液也能檢查健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes blood taken for testing.","zh":"這個短語描述用於檢測的血液。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"donor’s blood","meaning":"捐血者的血液","examples":[{"en":"The patient’s blood is mixed with the donor’s blood.","zh":"病人的血液與捐血者的血液混合。"},{"en":"Donor’s blood is blood given by another person for medical use.","zh":"donor’s blood 指由另一個人捐出作醫療用途的血液。"},{"en":"Hospitals store donor’s blood so it can be used in emergencies.","zh":"醫院儲存捐血者的血液，以便緊急情況使用。"},{"en":"Donor’s blood must be tested because it may not match every patient.","zh":"捐血者的血液必須經過檢測，因為它未必與每位病人相容。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to blood supplied by a person who donates it.","zh":"這個短語指由捐血者提供的血液。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"check microscopically","meaning":"用顯微鏡檢查","examples":[{"en":"Laboratory staff check the mixture microscopically.","zh":"化驗室人員用顯微鏡檢查混合物。"},{"en":"To check microscopically means to examine something using a microscope.","zh":"check microscopically 指使用顯微鏡檢查某物。"},{"en":"A scientist may check water samples microscopically to look for tiny organisms.","zh":"科學家可能用顯微鏡檢查水樣本，尋找微小生物。"},{"en":"In cross-matching, staff check microscopically to see whether blood cells clump.","zh":"在交叉配對中，人員用顯微鏡檢查血細胞是否凝集。"},{"en":"This phrase describes close examination of things too small for the naked eye.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細檢查肉眼看不見的小東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"clumping","meaning":"凝集","examples":[{"en":"Clumping is a key sign that blood samples are incompatible.","zh":"凝集是血液樣本不相容的重要跡象。"},{"en":"Clumping means cells or particles stick together in groups.","zh":"clumping 指細胞或粒子黏在一起形成團塊。"},{"en":"Flour may form clumps if it is mixed into sauce too quickly.","zh":"如果麵粉太快加入醬汁，可能形成團塊。"},{"en":"In blood testing, clumping can show that antibodies are reacting against cells.","zh":"在血液測試中，凝集可以顯示抗體正在對細胞作出反應。"},{"en":"This word describes unwanted sticking together.","zh":"這個字描述不想要的黏結成團。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a key sign of","meaning":"……的重要跡象","examples":[{"en":"Clumping is a key sign of blood incompatibility.","zh":"凝集是血液不相容的重要跡象。"},{"en":"A key sign of something is an important clue that it is present.","zh":"a key sign of something 指顯示某事存在的重要線索。"},{"en":"A high fever can be a key sign of infection.","zh":"高燒可以是感染的重要跡象。"},{"en":"In blood testing, clumping is a key sign because it warns of unsafe mixing.","zh":"在血液測試中，凝集是重要跡象，因為它警告混合不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies an important indicator.","zh":"這個短語指出重要指標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"obviously impractical","meaning":"顯然不切實際","examples":[{"en":"Some testing methods are obviously impractical in a true emergency.","zh":"有些檢測方法在真正緊急情況中顯然不切實際。"},{"en":"Obviously impractical means clearly not realistic or usable in that situation.","zh":"obviously impractical 指在該情況下明顯不現實或不可用。"},{"en":"Asking students to write a full essay in five minutes is obviously impractical.","zh":"要求學生在五分鐘內寫完整作文，顯然不切實際。"},{"en":"Slow blood testing may be impractical when a patient is losing blood rapidly.","zh":"當病人快速失血時，緩慢血液檢測可能不切實際。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a method that cannot sensibly be used.","zh":"這個短語描述不能合理使用的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"emergency situation","meaning":"緊急情況","examples":[{"en":"Doctors may have little time for testing in an emergency situation.","zh":"醫生在緊急情況中可能沒有太多時間檢測。"},{"en":"An emergency situation is a sudden serious event that requires immediate action.","zh":"emergency situation 指需要立即行動的突然嚴重事件。"},{"en":"A fire in a building is an emergency situation that needs fast evacuation.","zh":"建築物火警是需要快速疏散的緊急情況。"},{"en":"In an emergency situation, speed may become as important as accuracy.","zh":"在緊急情況中，速度可能變得與準確性同樣重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a high-pressure situation where delay can be dangerous.","zh":"這個短語描述延誤可能危險的高壓情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"meticulous testing","meaning":"一絲不苟的檢測","examples":[{"en":"Blood banks require meticulous testing of every donation.","zh":"血庫需要對每份捐血作一絲不苟的檢測。"},{"en":"Meticulous testing is very careful and detailed testing.","zh":"meticulous testing 指非常仔細而詳細的檢測。"},{"en":"A food laboratory performs meticulous testing before approving drinking water.","zh":"食品實驗室在批准飲用水前會進行一絲不苟的檢測。"},{"en":"Blood requires meticulous testing because hidden diseases or incompatibility can harm patients.","zh":"血液需要一絲不苟地檢測，因為隱藏疾病或不相容可以傷害病人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes testing done with great care and precision.","zh":"這個短語描述極其仔細和精確的檢測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"documentation and labelling","meaning":"記錄及標籤","examples":[{"en":"Accurate documentation and labelling are essential for blood safety.","zh":"準確記錄及標籤對血液安全至關重要。"},{"en":"Documentation and labelling mean recording information clearly and marking items correctly.","zh":"documentation and labelling 指清楚記錄資料並正確標示物品。"},{"en":"In a pharmacy, documentation and labelling help ensure patients receive the right medicine.","zh":"在藥房中，記錄及標籤幫助確保病人收到正確藥物。"},{"en":"If blood bags are poorly labelled, a patient may receive the wrong blood.","zh":"如果血袋標籤不清，病人可能收到錯誤血液。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the paperwork and labels that keep medical systems safe.","zh":"這個短語描述維持醫療系統安全的文件和標示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"true emergency","meaning":"真正的緊急情況","examples":[{"en":"In a true emergency, doctors may need blood immediately.","zh":"在真正的緊急情況中，醫生可能立即需要血液。"},{"en":"A true emergency is a real urgent crisis, not just an inconvenience.","zh":"true emergency 指真正緊急的危機，而不只是麻煩。"},{"en":"Heavy traffic is annoying, but a serious accident with bleeding is a true emergency.","zh":"嚴重交通擠塞令人煩躁，但有出血的嚴重意外才是真正緊急情況。"},{"en":"In a true emergency, long testing procedures may not be possible.","zh":"在真正的緊急情況中，漫長檢測程序可能不可行。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses genuine urgency.","zh":"這個短語強調真正的迫切性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"blood bank","meaning":"血庫","examples":[{"en":"A blood bank stores different types of blood for emergencies.","zh":"血庫儲存不同類型血液以備緊急情況。"},{"en":"A blood bank is a medical facility that collects, tests, stores, and supplies blood.","zh":"blood bank 指收集、檢測、儲存和供應血液的醫療設施。"},{"en":"Hospitals rely on blood banks when patients need surgery or emergency transfusions.","zh":"當病人需要手術或緊急輸血，醫院依賴血庫。"},{"en":"If a blood bank lacks supplies, doctors may struggle to treat severe blood loss.","zh":"如果血庫供應不足，醫生可能難以治療嚴重失血。"},{"en":"This phrase names the system that keeps blood available for medical use.","zh":"這個短語指出讓血液可供醫療使用的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"an array of","meaning":"各式各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"A blood bank keeps an array of blood types on hand.","zh":"血庫隨時備有各式各樣的血型。"},{"en":"An array of something means a wide variety or collection of different items.","zh":"an array of something 指各種不同物品的集合。"},{"en":"A supermarket offers an array of fruits, snacks, and drinks.","zh":"超級市場提供各式各樣的水果、零食和飲品。"},{"en":"Blood banks need an array of blood types because patients do not all match the same blood.","zh":"血庫需要各式各樣的血型，因為病人不會全都配合同一種血。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a varied selection.","zh":"這個短語描述多樣的選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"on hand","meaning":"隨時可用","examples":[{"en":"Hospitals need several blood types on hand.","zh":"醫院需要隨時備有幾種血型。"},{"en":"On hand means available and ready to use when needed.","zh":"on hand 指可取得並準備好在需要時使用。"},{"en":"A teacher keeps extra pencils on hand for students who forget theirs.","zh":"老師會隨時備有額外鉛筆，給忘記帶筆的學生。"},{"en":"Hospitals keep blood on hand because emergencies cannot always wait.","zh":"醫院隨時備有血液，因為緊急情況不能總是等待。"},{"en":"This phrase describes supplies that are ready for immediate use.","zh":"這個短語描述可立即使用的供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"hence","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"Hence, blood donations must occur regularly.","zh":"因此，捐血必須定期發生。"},{"en":"Hence means therefore or for this reason.","zh":"hence 指因此或基於這個原因。"},{"en":"The road is flooded; hence, the school bus will be delayed.","zh":"道路被水淹浸；因此，校車會延誤。"},{"en":"Blood is used often and cannot be stored forever; hence, donations must continue.","zh":"血液經常被使用，而且不能永久儲存；因此，捐血必須持續。"},{"en":"This word connects a reason to a conclusion.","zh":"這個字把原因與結論連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"regular occurrence","meaning":"經常發生的事情","examples":[{"en":"Blood donation must be a regular occurrence within the community.","zh":"捐血必須成為社區中經常發生的事情。"},{"en":"A regular occurrence is something that happens repeatedly or often.","zh":"regular occurrence 指重複或經常發生的事情。"},{"en":"Weekly homework is a regular occurrence in most schools.","zh":"每週功課是大多數學校經常發生的事情。"},{"en":"Blood donation must happen regularly because hospitals constantly need fresh supplies.","zh":"捐血必須定期發生，因為醫院持續需要新供應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that is not rare or one-off.","zh":"這個短語描述並非罕見或一次性的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"significant segment of the population","meaning":"人口中的一大部分","examples":[{"en":"A significant segment of the population must donate blood regularly.","zh":"人口中的一大部分必須定期捐血。"},{"en":"A significant segment of the population means a large or important part of the people in a society.","zh":"significant segment of the population 指社會中很大或重要的一部分人。"},{"en":"A significant segment of the population uses public transport every day.","zh":"人口中的一大部分每天使用公共交通。"},{"en":"Blood supply is safer when a large enough group of people donate regularly.","zh":"當有足夠大的一群人定期捐血，血液供應會更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important portion of society.","zh":"這個短語描述社會中的重要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"developed world","meaning":"已發展國家","examples":[{"en":"In the developed world, unpaid volunteers provide most donated blood.","zh":"在已發展國家，大多數捐贈血液由無償志願者提供。"},{"en":"The developed world refers to wealthier countries with more advanced infrastructure and healthcare systems.","zh":"developed world 指較富裕、基建和醫療系統較先進的國家。"},{"en":"Hospitals in the developed world usually have organised blood banks and screening systems.","zh":"已發展國家的醫院通常有有組織的血庫和篩查系統。"},{"en":"In the developed world, voluntary donation may replace family-based donation more often.","zh":"在已發展國家，自願捐血較常取代家人捐血。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts richer countries with less developed nations.","zh":"這個短語把較富裕國家與較不發達國家作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unpaid volunteers","meaning":"無償志願捐血者","examples":[{"en":"Unpaid volunteers provide much of the community’s blood supply.","zh":"無償志願者提供社區大部分血液供應。"},{"en":"Unpaid volunteers are people who help without receiving money.","zh":"unpaid volunteers 指不收取金錢而提供幫助的人。"},{"en":"Unpaid volunteers may serve meals, teach children, or donate blood for the community.","zh":"無償志願者可能為社區派飯、教孩子或捐血。"},{"en":"Blood systems depend on unpaid volunteers because regular supply requires public participation.","zh":"血液系統依賴無償志願者，因為穩定供應需要公眾參與。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people who contribute freely.","zh":"這個短語描述自願無償貢獻的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"provide blood for the community","meaning":"為社區提供血液","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers provide blood for the wider community.","zh":"志願者為更廣泛社區提供血液。"},{"en":"To provide blood for the community means to donate blood so local people can receive it when needed.","zh":"provide blood for the community 指捐血，讓本地人在需要時可以使用。"},{"en":"A blood drive allows healthy adults to provide blood for patients they may never meet.","zh":"捐血活動讓健康成年人為他們可能從未見過的病人提供血液。"},{"en":"Community blood supply improves when more people donate safely and regularly.","zh":"當更多人安全而定期捐血，社區血液供應會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public service through blood donation.","zh":"這個短語描述透過捐血提供公共服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"whereas","meaning":"然而；相對地","examples":[{"en":"In wealthy countries volunteers donate blood, whereas families often donate elsewhere.","zh":"在富裕國家，志願者捐血；相對地，在其他地方則常由家人捐血。"},{"en":"Whereas introduces a contrast between two facts or situations.","zh":"whereas 引出兩個事實或情況之間的對比。"},{"en":"Some students prefer morning study, whereas others work better at night.","zh":"有些學生較喜歡早上學習，而另一些則晚上表現較好。"},{"en":"The sentence contrasts volunteer-based donation with family-based donation.","zh":"這句把志願捐血模式與家人捐血模式作對比。"},{"en":"This word is useful for comparing two different patterns.","zh":"這個字適合用來比較兩種不同模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"less developed nations","meaning":"較不發達國家","examples":[{"en":"Family members often provide blood in less developed nations.","zh":"在較不發達國家，家人常提供血液。"},{"en":"Less developed nations are countries with fewer economic resources and less developed infrastructure.","zh":"less developed nations 指經濟資源較少、基建較不完善的國家。"},{"en":"Hospitals in less developed nations may have fewer stored blood supplies.","zh":"較不發達國家的醫院可能儲存血液供應較少。"},{"en":"Family donation may be more common when national blood-bank systems are limited.","zh":"當全國血庫系統有限時，家人捐血可能較常見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes countries with lower levels of economic and institutional development.","zh":"這個短語描述經濟和制度發展水平較低的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be involved","meaning":"參與","examples":[{"en":"Families and friends are often involved in blood donation.","zh":"家人和朋友常參與捐血。"},{"en":"To be involved means to take part in an activity or process.","zh":"be involved 指參加某項活動或過程。"},{"en":"Parents may be involved in school events by helping teachers organise games.","zh":"家長可能透過幫老師組織遊戲來參與學校活動。"},{"en":"In some places, relatives are involved because hospitals need family blood donors.","zh":"在有些地方，親屬會參與，因為醫院需要家人捐血。"},{"en":"This phrase describes participation.","zh":"這個短語描述參加其中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in the era of","meaning":"在……的時代","examples":[{"en":"Blood screening is essential in the era of HIV.","zh":"在 HIV 的時代，血液篩查至關重要。"},{"en":"In the era of something means during a period strongly affected by that issue or development.","zh":"in the era of something 指在深受某問題或發展影響的時期。"},{"en":"In the era of smartphones, students can access information almost anywhere.","zh":"在智能手機的時代，學生幾乎可以在任何地方取得資訊。"},{"en":"In the era of HIV, blood safety requires careful screening for infection.","zh":"在 HIV 的時代，血液安全需要仔細篩查感染。"},{"en":"This phrase places an issue within a particular historical or social period.","zh":"這個短語把某問題放在特定歷史或社會時期中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"insidious disease","meaning":"隱伏而危險的疾病","examples":[{"en":"HIV is an insidious disease that may be transmitted through blood.","zh":"HIV 是一種可能透過血液傳播的隱伏而危險的疾病。"},{"en":"An insidious disease develops or spreads in a hidden, gradual, and dangerous way.","zh":"insidious disease 指以隱藏、逐漸且危險方式發展或傳播的疾病。"},{"en":"High blood pressure can be insidious because people may feel normal for years.","zh":"高血壓可以是隱伏而危險的，因為人們多年來可能感覺正常。"},{"en":"HIV is described as insidious because it may not show obvious signs at first.","zh":"HIV 被描述為隱伏而危險，是因為它起初可能沒有明顯跡象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a disease that is dangerous partly because it can be hidden.","zh":"這個短語描述一種因可被隱藏而部分變得危險的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"blood-borne disease","meaning":"血液傳播疾病","examples":[{"en":"Potential donors are screened for blood-borne diseases.","zh":"潛在捐血者會接受血液傳播疾病篩查。"},{"en":"A blood-borne disease is an illness that can be carried and spread through blood.","zh":"blood-borne disease 指可以由血液攜帶並傳播的疾病。"},{"en":"Hospitals screen blood to reduce the risk of passing on blood-borne diseases.","zh":"醫院篩查血液，以減少傳播血液傳播疾病的風險。"},{"en":"If infected blood is transfused, a blood-borne disease may spread to the patient.","zh":"如果受感染血液被輸入病人體內，血液傳播疾病可能傳給病人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes diseases transmitted through blood contact.","zh":"這個短語描述透過血液接觸傳播的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"potential donor","meaning":"潛在捐血者","examples":[{"en":"Every potential donor must be carefully screened.","zh":"每位潛在捐血者都必須接受仔細篩查。"},{"en":"A potential donor is a person who may give blood, organs, money, or other help.","zh":"potential donor 指可能捐出血液、器官、金錢或其他幫助的人。"},{"en":"A blood centre asks questions to decide whether a potential donor can donate safely.","zh":"血液中心會提問，以判斷潛在捐血者能否安全捐血。"},{"en":"Screening potential donors protects both the donor and the patient receiving blood.","zh":"篩查潛在捐血者可以保護捐血者和接受血液的病人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone who might donate but has not yet been accepted.","zh":"這個短語描述可能捐贈但尚未被接受的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be carefully screened and tested","meaning":"接受仔細篩查和檢測","examples":[{"en":"Potential donors are carefully screened and tested.","zh":"潛在捐血者會接受仔細篩查和檢測。"},{"en":"To be carefully screened and tested means to be checked in detail for safety and suitability.","zh":"be carefully screened and tested 指為安全和適合性接受詳細檢查。"},{"en":"Food workers may be carefully screened and tested during a disease outbreak.","zh":"疾病爆發期間，食品工作者可能接受仔細篩查和檢測。"},{"en":"Donors are screened and tested to reduce the risk of unsafe blood entering the supply.","zh":"捐血者接受篩查和檢測，以降低不安全血液進入供應的風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a thorough safety-checking process.","zh":"這個短語描述全面安全檢查過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"successive donations","meaning":"連續捐血","examples":[{"en":"Donors should wait between successive whole-blood donations.","zh":"捐血者在連續全血捐贈之間應等待一段時間。"},{"en":"Successive donations are donations that happen one after another over time.","zh":"successive donations 指隨時間一次接一次發生的捐贈。"},{"en":"A charity may record successive donations from the same supporter each year.","zh":"慈善機構可能記錄同一支持者每年的連續捐款。"},{"en":"Blood donors must wait between successive donations so the body can recover.","zh":"捐血者必須在連續捐血之間等待，讓身體恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated donations in sequence.","zh":"這個短語描述按次序重複發生的捐贈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"whole blood donation","meaning":"全血捐贈","examples":[{"en":"A whole blood donation removes several blood components together.","zh":"全血捐贈會同時抽走幾種血液成分。"},{"en":"Whole blood donation means donating blood with its main components still together.","zh":"whole blood donation 指捐出主要成分仍在一起的血液。"},{"en":"A blood centre may later separate a whole blood donation into plasma, red cells, and platelets.","zh":"血液中心之後可能把全血捐贈分離成血漿、紅血球和血小板。"},{"en":"Whole blood donation affects the body more than giving only one component.","zh":"全血捐贈對身體影響比只捐一種成分更大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes donating complete blood rather than a single part.","zh":"這個短語描述捐出完整血液，而不是單一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"given the vital role","meaning":"鑑於……的重要作用","examples":[{"en":"Given the vital role of blood, bloodletting seems surprising today.","zh":"鑑於血液的重要作用，放血療法今天看來令人驚訝。"},{"en":"Given the vital role means considering how important something is.","zh":"given the vital role 指考慮到某事有多重要。"},{"en":"Given the vital role of sleep, students should not stay up all night before exams.","zh":"鑑於睡眠的重要作用，學生不應在考試前通宵。"},{"en":"Bloodletting seems strange because blood is now known to be essential.","zh":"放血療法看來奇怪，因為今天我們知道血液不可或缺。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a reason that makes the next point understandable.","zh":"這個短語引出令下一點更易理解的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"bloodletting","meaning":"放血療法","examples":[{"en":"Bloodletting was once a widespread medical treatment.","zh":"放血療法曾是一種廣泛使用的醫療方法。"},{"en":"Bloodletting is the old practice of removing blood from a patient as treatment.","zh":"bloodletting 指舊時作為治療而從病人體內放出血液的做法。"},{"en":"In the past, doctors used bloodletting because they misunderstood illness and circulation.","zh":"過去醫生使用放血療法，因為他們誤解疾病和血液循環。"},{"en":"Bloodletting often harmed patients because it removed blood they needed.","zh":"放血療法常傷害病人，因為它移除了病人需要的血液。"},{"en":"This word names a historical treatment now seen as mostly ineffective.","zh":"這個字指出一種今天多被視為無效的歷史療法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"widespread medical practice","meaning":"廣泛使用的醫療做法","examples":[{"en":"For centuries, bloodletting was a widespread medical practice.","zh":"幾個世紀以來，放血療法是一種廣泛使用的醫療做法。"},{"en":"A widespread medical practice is a treatment commonly used by many doctors or communities.","zh":"widespread medical practice 指許多醫生或社群普遍使用的治療方法。"},{"en":"Vaccination is now a widespread medical practice in many countries.","zh":"疫苗接種現在是許多國家廣泛使用的醫療做法。"},{"en":"A practice can be widespread even if later science shows it was wrong.","zh":"即使後來科學顯示某做法錯誤，它也可能曾被廣泛使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes medical behaviour used widely over time or place.","zh":"這個短語描述在時間或地區上被廣泛使用的醫療行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be based on the belief that","meaning":"建基於……的信念","examples":[{"en":"Bloodletting was based on the belief that blood carried humours.","zh":"放血療法建基於血液承載體液的信念。"},{"en":"To be based on the belief that means to be built on an idea people accept as true.","zh":"be based on the belief that 指建立在被人們視為真實的想法之上。"},{"en":"A school rule may be based on the belief that uniforms reduce social comparison.","zh":"校服規定可能建基於校服能減少社交比較的信念。"},{"en":"Bloodletting was based on a belief that later medical science rejected.","zh":"放血療法建基於一個後來被醫學科學否定的信念。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the idea behind an action or system.","zh":"這個短語解釋行動或制度背後的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"carry humours","meaning":"承載體液","examples":[{"en":"Ancient doctors believed that blood carried bodily humours.","zh":"古代醫生相信血液承載身體體液。"},{"en":"To carry humours means, in old medicine, to transport substances thought to control health and temperament.","zh":"carry humours 在古代醫學中指運送被認為控制健康和氣質的物質。"},{"en":"Ancient medicine treated humours as body fluids linked to illness and personality.","zh":"古代醫學把體液視為與疾病和性格相關的身體液體。"},{"en":"Doctors practised bloodletting because they believed blood carried an excess humour.","zh":"醫生施行放血療法，因為他們相信血液承載過量體液。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to outdated medical theory.","zh":"這個短語屬於已過時的醫學理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"imbalance","meaning":"失衡","examples":[{"en":"An imbalance of the humours was believed to cause illness.","zh":"人們曾相信體液失衡會導致疾病。"},{"en":"An imbalance is a situation where the amounts or forces are not properly balanced.","zh":"imbalance 指數量或力量沒有適當平衡的情況。"},{"en":"An imbalance between study and rest can make students exhausted.","zh":"學習和休息之間失衡可以令學生疲憊不堪。"},{"en":"Ancient doctors believed illness came from imbalance inside the body.","zh":"古代醫生相信疾病來自身體內部失衡。"},{"en":"This word describes a lack of proper balance.","zh":"這個字描述缺乏適當平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"result in illness","meaning":"導致疾病","examples":[{"en":"Doctors believed that an imbalance of humours resulted in illness.","zh":"醫生曾相信體液失衡會導致疾病。"},{"en":"To result in illness means to cause sickness or poor health.","zh":"result in illness 指造成疾病或健康變差。"},{"en":"Poor food hygiene can result in illness among customers.","zh":"食物衛生差可以導致顧客生病。"},{"en":"In the old theory, internal imbalance was thought to result in illness.","zh":"在舊理論中，內部失衡被認為會導致疾病。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with becoming sick.","zh":"這個短語把原因與患病連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"bleed a patient","meaning":"為病人放血","examples":[{"en":"Doctors would bleed a patient to remove supposed harmful substances.","zh":"醫生會為病人放血，以移除據稱有害的物質。"},{"en":"To bleed a patient means to deliberately remove blood from them as treatment.","zh":"bleed a patient 指故意從病人體內放出血液作為治療。"},{"en":"Historical doctors might bleed a feverish patient because they believed it restored balance.","zh":"歷史上的醫生可能為發燒病人放血，因為他們相信這能恢復平衡。"},{"en":"Bleeding a patient could weaken them because it removed needed blood.","zh":"為病人放血可能令病人虛弱，因為它移除了所需血液。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an old medical procedure, not ordinary bleeding from injury.","zh":"這個短語描述舊醫療程序，而不是受傷造成的普通出血。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be supposed to","meaning":"據稱可以；理應","examples":[{"en":"The treatment was supposed to restore balance in the body.","zh":"這種治療據稱可以恢復身體平衡。"},{"en":"Be supposed to means be expected or claimed to do something.","zh":"be supposed to 指被期望或聲稱會做某事。"},{"en":"A fire alarm is supposed to warn people when there is danger.","zh":"火警鐘理應在有危險時警告人們。"},{"en":"Bloodletting was supposed to help, but in most cases it did not.","zh":"放血療法據稱可以有幫助，但在大多數情況下並沒有。"},{"en":"This phrase can show intended purpose, even if the result fails.","zh":"這個短語可以顯示預期目的，即使結果失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"undesirable excess","meaning":"不必要的過量部分","examples":[{"en":"Bloodletting was intended to remove an undesirable excess of a humour.","zh":"放血療法旨在移除某種體液不必要的過量部分。"},{"en":"An undesirable excess is too much of something unwanted or harmful.","zh":"undesirable excess 指某種不想要或有害東西太多。"},{"en":"Too much salt in soup is an undesirable excess because it ruins the taste.","zh":"湯中太多鹽是不必要的過量部分，因為它破壞味道。"},{"en":"Ancient doctors believed removing excess humours could restore health.","zh":"古代醫生相信移除過量體液可以恢復健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unwanted surplus.","zh":"這個短語描述不想要的過剩部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"furthermore","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"Furthermore, early doctors did not understand blood circulation.","zh":"此外，早期醫生並不了解血液循環。"},{"en":"Furthermore means in addition, especially when adding another important point.","zh":"furthermore 指此外，尤其用於加入另一個重要觀點。"},{"en":"The course is expensive; furthermore, it requires students to travel every week.","zh":"這課程很昂貴；此外，它要求學生每星期出行。"},{"en":"The writer uses furthermore to add a second reason bloodletting was mistaken.","zh":"作者用 furthermore 加入放血療法錯誤的第二個原因。"},{"en":"This word strengthens an argument by adding more information.","zh":"這個字透過加入更多資料來加強論點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"circulate around the body","meaning":"在全身循環","examples":[{"en":"People once did not know that blood circulated around the body.","zh":"人們曾經不知道血液會在全身循環。"},{"en":"To circulate around the body means to move continuously through the body’s vessels.","zh":"circulate around the body 指透過身體血管持續流動。"},{"en":"Medicine can circulate around the body after entering the bloodstream.","zh":"藥物進入血液後，可以在全身循環。"},{"en":"Blood circulation allows oxygen and nutrients to reach distant tissues.","zh":"血液循環讓氧氣和養分到達遠處組織。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the continuous movement of blood.","zh":"這個短語描述血液的持續流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be assumed to","meaning":"被假設為","examples":[{"en":"Blood was assumed to be created and exhausted very quickly.","zh":"血液曾被假設為很快被創造並耗盡。"},{"en":"To be assumed to means to be believed without full proof.","zh":"be assumed to 指在沒有充分證據下被相信為某情況。"},{"en":"A quiet student may be assumed to be shy, even if they are simply tired.","zh":"安靜學生可能被假設為害羞，即使他只是疲倦。"},{"en":"Early doctors assumed wrong ideas about blood because they lacked modern evidence.","zh":"早期醫生因缺乏現代證據，而對血液作出錯誤假設。"},{"en":"This phrase describes belief based on assumption rather than certainty.","zh":"這個短語描述基於假設而非確定性的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be exhausted of its value","meaning":"失去其價值","examples":[{"en":"People believed that old blood became exhausted of its value.","zh":"人們曾相信舊血會失去其價值。"},{"en":"To be exhausted of its value means to lose the usefulness people think it once had.","zh":"be exhausted of its value 指失去人們認為它曾經具有的用途。"},{"en":"An old voucher becomes exhausted of its value after it expires.","zh":"舊優惠券到期後便失去其價值。"},{"en":"Early doctors wrongly believed old blood lost its value inside the body.","zh":"早期醫生錯誤地相信舊血在身體內失去價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something being seen as used up or no longer useful.","zh":"這個短語描述某物被視為用盡或不再有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"stagnate unhealthily","meaning":"不健康地淤積","examples":[{"en":"Blood was thought to stagnate unhealthily in the extremities.","zh":"人們曾認為血液會在身體末端部位不健康地淤積。"},{"en":"To stagnate unhealthily means to stop moving properly and become harmful.","zh":"stagnate unhealthily 指不能正常流動並變得有害。"},{"en":"Water can stagnate unhealthily in a blocked drain and attract mosquitoes.","zh":"水可以在堵塞排水渠中不健康地淤積，並吸引蚊子。"},{"en":"Early doctors believed blood could sit still in body parts and cause illness.","zh":"早期醫生相信血液可以停留在身體部分並導致疾病。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harmful lack of movement.","zh":"這個短語描述有害的缺乏流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"bodily extremities","meaning":"身體末端部位","examples":[{"en":"Doctors believed that blood collected in the bodily extremities.","zh":"醫生曾相信血液會聚集在身體末端部位。"},{"en":"Bodily extremities are the body’s outer parts, especially the hands, feet, fingers, and toes.","zh":"bodily extremities 指身體外端部分，尤其是手、腳、手指和腳趾。"},{"en":"In cold weather, the bodily extremities often feel cold first.","zh":"在寒冷天氣中，身體末端部位通常最先感到寒冷。"},{"en":"Blood flow to the extremities matters because fingers and toes need oxygen too.","zh":"流向末端部位的血液很重要，因為手指和腳趾也需要氧氣。"},{"en":"This phrase names the far ends of the body.","zh":"這個短語指出身體最遠端的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"although the logic was there","meaning":"儘管理論看似有道理","examples":[{"en":"Although the logic was there, the treatment rarely helped patients.","zh":"儘管理論看似有道理，這種治療很少幫到病人。"},{"en":"Although the logic was there means the idea seemed reasonable, even if it was wrong or ineffective.","zh":"although the logic was there 指想法看似合理，即使它其實錯誤或無效。"},{"en":"Although the logic was there, studying all night made the student too tired to perform well.","zh":"儘管理論看似有道理，通宵溫習令學生太累而表現不好。"},{"en":"Bloodletting seemed logical under old beliefs, but the medical result was usually poor.","zh":"在舊信念下，放血療法看似合理，但醫療結果通常很差。"},{"en":"This phrase separates an apparently sensible theory from its real outcome.","zh":"這個短語把表面合理的理論與真實結果分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"it goes without saying that","meaning":"不用說也知道","examples":[{"en":"It goes without saying that bloodletting was usually ineffective.","zh":"不用說也知道，放血療法通常無效。"},{"en":"It goes without saying that means something is so obvious it hardly needs to be stated.","zh":"it goes without saying that 指某事明顯到幾乎不用說。"},{"en":"It goes without saying that students need to read the question before answering.","zh":"不用說也知道，學生答題前需要讀題。"},{"en":"After understanding blood’s importance, it becomes obvious that removing blood often harmed patients.","zh":"理解血液的重要性後，很明顯移除血液常傷害病人。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a point the writer treats as clear.","zh":"這個短語引出作者視為清楚的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"respond positively to","meaning":"對……有正面反應","examples":[{"en":"Very few patients responded positively to bloodletting.","zh":"很少病人對放血療法有正面反應。"},{"en":"To respond positively to a treatment means to improve after receiving it.","zh":"respond positively to a treatment 指接受治療後情況改善。"},{"en":"A patient may respond positively to medicine if their fever falls and pain decreases.","zh":"如果病人發燒下降、痛楚減少，就可能對藥物有正面反應。"},{"en":"If few patients respond positively, doctors should question whether the treatment works.","zh":"如果很少病人有正面反應，醫生應質疑治療是否有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a beneficial reaction to treatment or action.","zh":"這個短語描述對治療或行動的有益反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct heading for each paragraph.","zh":"考生為每段選出正確標題。"},{"en":"To choose the correct heading means to select the title that best matches the paragraph’s main idea.","zh":"choose the correct heading 指選擇最符合段落主旨的標題。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should read the whole paragraph before choosing the heading.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先讀完整段，再選標題。"},{"en":"A heading that matches only one small detail may be wrong.","zh":"只符合一個小細節的標題可能是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in matching-headings questions.","zh":"這個短語是標題配對題中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The task provides a list of possible paragraph headings.","zh":"題目提供可能的段落標題列表。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a set of possible titles for paragraphs or sections.","zh":"list of headings 指一組可供段落或部分選擇的標題。"},{"en":"Students compare each paragraph with the list of headings before choosing an answer.","zh":"學生選答案前，會把每段與標題列表比較。"},{"en":"Extra headings are often included to test whether students understand the main idea.","zh":"額外標題通常會被加入，以測試學生是否理解主旨。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the answer options in a heading-matching task.","zh":"這個短語描述標題配對題中的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"not as big, but needing just enough","meaning":"體積較小，但數量必須適中","examples":[{"en":"Platelets are small, but their numbers must remain within a safe range.","zh":"血小板體積較小，但其數量必須保持在安全範圍內。"},{"en":"“Not as big, but needing just enough” means something is small but still must exist in the right amount.","zh":"“not as big, but needing just enough” 指某物雖小，但仍必須以適當數量存在。"},{"en":"Salt is not the biggest ingredient in soup, but the amount must be just right.","zh":"鹽不是湯中最大的材料，但份量必須剛剛好。"},{"en":"Platelets are small, yet too many or too few can cause serious problems.","zh":"血小板雖小，但太多或太少都可以造成嚴重問題。"},{"en":"This heading captures the importance of balance in platelet numbers.","zh":"這個標題概括血小板數量平衡的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"some attitudes to blood","meaning":"對血液的一些觀念","examples":[{"en":"The opening paragraph describes several cultural attitudes to blood.","zh":"開首段落描述了對血液的一些文化觀念。"},{"en":"Some attitudes to blood means different ways people think or feel about blood.","zh":"some attitudes to blood 指人們對血液的不同想法或感受。"},{"en":"Some people connect blood with life, while others feel frightened when they see it.","zh":"有些人把血液與生命連繫起來，另一些人看見血會害怕。"},{"en":"Cultural attitudes to blood appear in sayings, family ideas, and reactions to injury.","zh":"對血液的文化觀念出現在俗語、家族概念和對受傷的反應中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes beliefs and feelings about blood.","zh":"這個短語描述關於血液的信念和感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"good, but not so quick","meaning":"雖然有效，但不夠快捷","examples":[{"en":"Safe blood matching is useful but may take too long in an emergency.","zh":"安全血液配對很有用，但在緊急情況中可能花太長時間。"},{"en":"“Good, but not so quick” describes a method that works well but is too slow for urgent situations.","zh":"“good, but not so quick” 描述某方法有效，但對緊急情況而言太慢。"},{"en":"A full medical report is good, but not so quick when a patient needs help immediately.","zh":"完整醫療報告很好，但當病人立即需要幫助時就不夠快捷。"},{"en":"Cross-matching is useful, but in true emergencies doctors may not have enough time.","zh":"血液交叉配對有用，但在真正緊急情況中，醫生可能沒有足夠時間。"},{"en":"This heading contrasts safety with speed.","zh":"這個標題對比安全與速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"two ideas lead to a wrong conclusion","meaning":"兩個觀念導致錯誤結論","examples":[{"en":"Two mistaken beliefs once led doctors to practise bloodletting.","zh":"兩個錯誤信念曾導致醫生施行放血療法。"},{"en":"“Two ideas lead to a wrong conclusion” means false assumptions can produce an incorrect decision.","zh":"“two ideas lead to a wrong conclusion” 指錯誤假設可以產生錯誤決定。"},{"en":"If a teacher assumes a student is lazy and uninterested, they may miss the real problem of anxiety.","zh":"如果老師假設學生懶惰又不感興趣，可能錯過焦慮這個真正問題。"},{"en":"Bloodletting came from wrong ideas about humours and blood circulation.","zh":"放血療法來自關於體液和血液循環的錯誤觀念。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how faulty reasoning can create harmful practice.","zh":"這個短語顯示錯誤推理如何造成有害做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complicated identification","meaning":"複雜的識別過程","examples":[{"en":"Blood-group identification is a complicated process.","zh":"血型識別是一個複雜過程。"},{"en":"Complicated identification means recognising something is difficult because many details must be checked.","zh":"complicated identification 指因需要檢查許多細節而難以識別某物。"},{"en":"Identifying a rare plant can be complicated if several species look similar.","zh":"如果幾種植物看起來相似，識別罕見植物可能很複雜。"},{"en":"Blood identification is complicated because many blood-group systems and antigens exist.","zh":"血液識別很複雜，因為存在許多血型系統和抗原。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a difficult process of correctly recognising something.","zh":"這個短語描述正確識別某物的困難過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"an interesting treatment","meaning":"一種有趣的治療方法","examples":[{"en":"Bloodletting was an unusual historical medical treatment.","zh":"放血療法是一種不尋常的歷史醫療方法。"},{"en":"An interesting treatment is a medical method that attracts attention because it is unusual, surprising, or historically important.","zh":"interesting treatment 指因不尋常、令人驚訝或具歷史重要性而引人注意的醫療方法。"},{"en":"Some old treatments are interesting to study even though they are not used today.","zh":"有些舊療法即使今天不再使用，也值得研究。"},{"en":"Bloodletting is interesting because it shows how medical beliefs can change over time.","zh":"放血療法有趣，因為它顯示醫學信念如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a treatment worth examining, not necessarily one that works.","zh":"這個短語描述值得探討的治療，而不一定代表有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a shorter life, but just as important","meaning":"壽命較短，但同樣重要","examples":[{"en":"White blood cells have a shorter life but are essential to immunity.","zh":"白血球壽命較短，但對免疫同樣重要。"},{"en":"“A shorter life, but just as important” means something lasts less time but still matters greatly.","zh":"“a shorter life, but just as important” 指某物維持時間較短，但仍非常重要。"},{"en":"A short warning message may last only seconds but can save lives in an emergency.","zh":"簡短警告訊息可能只持續數秒，但在緊急情況中可以救命。"},{"en":"White blood cells may live briefly, yet they protect the body from infection.","zh":"白血球可能存活短暫，但它們保護身體免受感染。"},{"en":"This heading stresses that short duration does not mean low importance.","zh":"這個標題強調持續時間短不代表重要性低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"principal part that adds colour","meaning":"賦予顏色的主要部分","examples":[{"en":"Red blood cells form a principal component and give blood its colour.","zh":"紅血球構成主要成分，並賦予血液顏色。"},{"en":"A principal part that adds colour is a main element that creates the visible colour of something.","zh":"principal part that adds colour 指令某物呈現可見顏色的主要元素。"},{"en":"Cocoa powder is a principal part that adds colour to chocolate cake.","zh":"可可粉是令朱古力蛋糕有顏色的主要部分。"},{"en":"Red blood cells add colour because they contain hemoglobin.","zh":"紅血球賦予顏色，因為它們含有血紅蛋白。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a main component linked with appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述與外觀相關的主要成分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"maintaining supplies","meaning":"維持血液供應","examples":[{"en":"Regular donations are needed for maintaining blood supplies.","zh":"維持血液供應需要定期捐血。"},{"en":"Maintaining supplies means keeping enough materials available for future use.","zh":"maintaining supplies 指保持足夠物資可供將來使用。"},{"en":"A school maintains emergency supplies such as water, masks, and first-aid items.","zh":"學校會維持緊急物資，例如水、口罩和急救用品。"},{"en":"Blood supplies need maintenance because hospitals use blood regularly and stored blood has limits.","zh":"血液供應需要維持，因為醫院經常使用血液，而儲存血液有期限。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping resources ready and sufficient.","zh":"這個短語描述保持資源準備好且足夠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete the table","meaning":"完成表格","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the table with words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成表格。"},{"en":"To complete the table means to fill empty spaces in a table with correct information.","zh":"complete the table 指用正確資料填滿表格中的空格。"},{"en":"Students may complete a table by matching each blood component with its function.","zh":"學生可能透過把每種血液成分與其功能配對來完成表格。"},{"en":"Table completion tests whether readers can locate details and fit them into categories.","zh":"表格填充測試讀者能否定位細節並放入類別中。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in reading tasks.","zh":"這個短語是閱讀任務中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不超過三個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer must contain no more than three words.","zh":"每個答案不得超過三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer may use one, two, or three words, but not four.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案可以用一、二或三個字，但不能用四個。"},{"en":"If the instruction says no more than three words, students must count carefully.","zh":"如果指示說不超過三個字，學生必須仔細計算字數。"},{"en":"Adding an unnecessary extra word can make an otherwise correct answer wrong.","zh":"加入不必要的額外字，可能令本來正確的答案變錯。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a strict answer length.","zh":"這個短語設定嚴格答案長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"blood component","meaning":"血液成分","examples":[{"en":"The table lists each major blood component.","zh":"表格列出每種主要血液成分。"},{"en":"A blood component is one part of blood, such as plasma, red cells, white cells, or platelets.","zh":"blood component 指血液的一部分，例如血漿、紅血球、白血球或血小板。"},{"en":"Doctors may give patients only the blood component they need.","zh":"醫生可能只給病人所需的血液成分。"},{"en":"Separating blood components helps one donation support different patients.","zh":"分離血液成分有助一份捐血支援不同病人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major part of blood.","zh":"這個短語描述血液的主要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"associated fact","meaning":"相關事實","examples":[{"en":"Each blood component is matched with an associated fact.","zh":"每種血液成分都配上一項相關事實。"},{"en":"An associated fact is a piece of information connected with a particular item.","zh":"associated fact 指與某特定項目有關的一項資料。"},{"en":"In a history table, a king may be matched with an associated fact about his reign.","zh":"在歷史表格中，某位國王可能配上一項與其統治相關的事實。"},{"en":"For platelets, an associated fact might be that they help blood clot.","zh":"對血小板而言，相關事實可能是它們幫助血液凝固。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information linked to a topic or category.","zh":"這個短語描述與主題或類別相連的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"upon dying","meaning":"死亡後","examples":[{"en":"Upon dying, red blood cells are removed by the spleen and liver.","zh":"死亡後，紅血球由脾臟和肝臟移除。"},{"en":"Upon dying means when they die or immediately after they die.","zh":"upon dying 指當它們死亡時或死亡後立即。"},{"en":"Upon finishing the exam, students should check that their answers are on the answer sheet.","zh":"完成考試後，學生應檢查答案是否在答題紙上。"},{"en":"When red blood cells die, the body removes them and processes their waste.","zh":"當紅血球死亡，身體會移除它們並處理其廢物。"},{"en":"This phrase marks what happens at or just after a moment.","zh":"這個短語標示某一刻或剛之後發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"deal with","meaning":"處理","examples":[{"en":"The spleen and liver deal with inactive red blood cells.","zh":"脾臟和肝臟處理失去活性的紅血球。"},{"en":"To deal with something means to handle, manage, or process it.","zh":"deal with something 指處理、管理或加工某事物。"},{"en":"A school counsellor helps students deal with stress before exams.","zh":"學校輔導員幫助學生處理考試前壓力。"},{"en":"The spleen and liver deal with old blood cells by removing and breaking them down.","zh":"脾臟和肝臟透過移除並分解舊血細胞來處理它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes handling a problem, task, or material.","zh":"這個短語描述處理問題、任務或材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"require sufficient numbers","meaning":"需要足夠數量","examples":[{"en":"White blood cells require sufficient numbers before attacking invaders.","zh":"白血球在攻擊入侵物前需要足夠數量。"},{"en":"To require sufficient numbers means to need enough people, cells, or items for a job.","zh":"require sufficient numbers 指需要足夠的人、細胞或物品來完成工作。"},{"en":"A rescue team requires sufficient numbers before searching a large area safely.","zh":"救援隊在安全搜索大片區域前，需要足夠人手。"},{"en":"The immune system needs enough white blood cells before it can fight strongly.","zh":"免疫系統需要足夠白血球，才能有力對抗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes needing an adequate quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述需要足夠數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"attack invaders","meaning":"攻擊入侵物","examples":[{"en":"White blood cells attack invaders after multiplying.","zh":"白血球繁殖後會攻擊入侵物。"},{"en":"To attack invaders means to fight harmful organisms or foreign cells that enter the body.","zh":"attack invaders 指對抗進入身體的有害生物或外來細胞。"},{"en":"Security guards attack invaders only in a metaphorical comparison; white blood cells do it biologically.","zh":"保安員攻擊入侵者只是比喻比較；白血球則是在生物上這樣做。"},{"en":"If white blood cells attack invaders effectively, infection may be controlled.","zh":"如果白血球有效攻擊入侵物，感染可能受控。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the immune system fighting threats.","zh":"這個短語描述免疫系統對抗威脅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"need careful regulation","meaning":"需要小心調節","examples":[{"en":"Platelet numbers need careful regulation.","zh":"血小板數量需要小心調節。"},{"en":"To need careful regulation means to require close control so the level stays safe.","zh":"need careful regulation 指需要密切控制，使水平保持安全。"},{"en":"Traffic lights need careful regulation to prevent accidents at busy junctions.","zh":"繁忙路口的交通燈需要小心調節，以防止意外。"},{"en":"Platelet numbers need regulation because both low and high counts can be harmful.","zh":"血小板數量需要調節，因為過低和過高都可能有害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a need for precise control.","zh":"這個短語描述對精確控制的需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"many varieties exist","meaning":"存在許多種類","examples":[{"en":"Many varieties of blood groups and antigens exist.","zh":"血型和抗原存在許多種類。"},{"en":"Many varieties exist means there are many different types or forms.","zh":"many varieties exist 指有許多不同類型或形式。"},{"en":"Many varieties of rice exist, each suited to different climates and dishes.","zh":"稻米存在許多種類，每種適合不同氣候和菜式。"},{"en":"Blood matching is complex because many varieties of antigens and blood systems exist.","zh":"血液配對很複雜，因為抗原和血型系統存在許多種類。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights diversity within a category.","zh":"這個短語突出一個類別內的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether statements agree with the information given.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與所給資料相符。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文章所說內容一致。"},{"en":"If the passage says platelets help clot blood, a statement saying the same thing agrees with it.","zh":"如果文章說血小板幫助血液凝固，而陳述說同樣內容，就與資料相符。"},{"en":"Students should answer from the text, not from outside knowledge.","zh":"學生應根據文本回答，而不是根據外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text states.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文本陳述相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says red blood cells last months, a statement saying they last minutes contradicts it.","zh":"如果文章說紅血球可維持數月，而陳述說只維持數分鐘，就與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"A statement is FALSE only when the contradiction is clear in the text.","zh":"只有當文本中清楚出現矛盾，陳述才是 FALSE。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct conflict with given information.","zh":"這個短語描述與所給資料直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students write “NOT GIVEN” when the passage provides no relevant information.","zh":"當文章沒有提供相關資料時，學生寫 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the text does not say enough to decide.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文本沒有說足夠內容去判斷。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions whether bloodletting was painful, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文章從未提及放血療法是否痛苦，就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from common sense when the passage is silent.","zh":"當文章沒有說明時，學生不應憑常識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the answer cannot be proven from the text.","zh":"這個短語表示答案不能由文本證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"cross-matching","meaning":"血液交叉配對","examples":[{"en":"Blood cross-matching checks whether two samples are compatible.","zh":"血液交叉配對檢查兩個樣本是否相容。"},{"en":"Cross-matching is a laboratory test that compares patient blood with donor blood.","zh":"cross-matching 是比較病人血液與捐血者血液的化驗測試。"},{"en":"Before a transfusion, cross-matching helps doctors avoid dangerous reactions.","zh":"輸血前，血液交叉配對幫助醫生避免危險反應。"},{"en":"If cross-matching shows clumping, the blood samples may be incompatible.","zh":"如果交叉配對顯示凝集，血液樣本可能不相容。"},{"en":"This word names an important blood-safety test.","zh":"這個字指出重要的血液安全測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"special equipment","meaning":"專門設備","examples":[{"en":"Microscopic examination requires special equipment.","zh":"顯微鏡檢查需要專門設備。"},{"en":"Special equipment is equipment designed for a particular task, not ordinary use.","zh":"special equipment 指為特定任務而設，而不是普通用途的設備。"},{"en":"A science lab needs special equipment such as microscopes, gloves, and test tubes.","zh":"科學實驗室需要顯微鏡、手套和試管等專門設備。"},{"en":"Cross-matching may require special equipment because tiny blood reactions cannot be seen easily.","zh":"血液交叉配對可能需要專門設備，因為微小血液反應不易看見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes tools needed for specialised work.","zh":"這個短語描述專門工作所需工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"poorer countries","meaning":"較貧窮國家","examples":[{"en":"In poorer countries, relatives often provide blood.","zh":"在較貧窮國家，親屬常提供血液。"},{"en":"Poorer countries are countries with fewer financial resources and weaker public systems.","zh":"poorer countries 指財政資源較少、公共系統較弱的國家。"},{"en":"Hospitals in poorer countries may have fewer stored blood supplies.","zh":"較貧窮國家的醫院可能儲存血液供應較少。"},{"en":"Relatives may provide blood when organised blood-bank systems are limited.","zh":"當有組織的血庫系統有限時，親屬可能提供血液。"},{"en":"This phrase describes countries with fewer economic resources.","zh":"這個短語描述經濟資源較少的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"family members donate blood","meaning":"家人捐血","examples":[{"en":"Family members often donate blood in less developed countries.","zh":"在較不發達國家，家人常捐血。"},{"en":"Family members donate blood means relatives give blood for a patient or community need.","zh":"family members donate blood 指親屬為病人或社區需要提供血液。"},{"en":"A brother may donate blood when his sister needs surgery.","zh":"當妹妹需要手術時，哥哥可能捐血。"},{"en":"Family donation may happen when hospitals do not have enough stored blood available.","zh":"當醫院沒有足夠儲存血液可用時，家人捐血可能會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes blood donation by relatives.","zh":"這個短語描述由親屬進行的捐血。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"painful process","meaning":"痛苦的過程","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether bloodletting was a painful process.","zh":"該陳述問放血療法是否是一個痛苦的過程。"},{"en":"A painful process is an action or experience that causes physical or emotional pain.","zh":"painful process 指造成身體或情感痛苦的行動或經歷。"},{"en":"Removing a tooth can be a painful process without proper anaesthetic.","zh":"如果沒有適當麻醉，拔牙可以是一個痛苦的過程。"},{"en":"A treatment may be called painful if it causes suffering while it is being done.","zh":"如果治療在進行時造成痛苦，就可稱為痛苦的過程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a process that hurts or causes distress.","zh":"這個短語描述會令人受痛或受困擾的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 3 - What’s in Blood?.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 4":[{"front":"criminal rehabilitation","meaning":"罪犯更生","examples":[{"en":"Criminal rehabilitation aims to help former offenders return successfully to society.","zh":"罪犯更生旨在幫助前罪犯成功重返社會。"},{"en":"Criminal rehabilitation means helping offenders change their behaviour and live law-abiding lives after punishment.","zh":"criminal rehabilitation 指幫助罪犯改變行為，並在受罰後過守法生活。"},{"en":"A prison education course can support criminal rehabilitation by giving inmates job skills.","zh":"監獄教育課程可以透過給予囚犯工作技能來支持罪犯更生。"},{"en":"If rehabilitation succeeds, former offenders are less likely to commit crimes again.","zh":"如果更生成功，前罪犯再次犯罪的可能性會較低。"},{"en":"Criminal rehabilitation focuses on change and reintegration, not only punishment.","zh":"罪犯更生著重改變和重新融入，而不只是懲罰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a difficult issue","meaning":"棘手的問題","examples":[{"en":"Accurately assessing whether an offender has changed is a difficult issue.","zh":"準確評估罪犯是否已改變是一個棘手的問題。"},{"en":"A difficult issue is a problem that is hard to judge, solve, or manage.","zh":"a difficult issue 指難以判斷、解決或處理的問題。"},{"en":"Deciding whether a student should repeat a year can be a difficult issue for teachers and parents.","zh":"決定學生是否應留級，對老師和家長來說可以是棘手的問題。"},{"en":"A difficult issue often involves risk, uncertainty, and competing values.","zh":"棘手的問題往往涉及風險、不確定性和互相衝突的價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when there is no simple or completely safe answer.","zh":"當沒有簡單或完全安全的答案時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"convicted criminals","meaning":"已定罪的罪犯","examples":[{"en":"Convicted criminals may serve lengthy prison sentences.","zh":"已定罪的罪犯可能服長期監禁刑期。"},{"en":"Convicted criminals are people who have been found guilty of crimes by a court.","zh":"convicted criminals 指已被法院裁定犯罪成立的人。"},{"en":"A convicted criminal may lose certain freedoms because the court has confirmed guilt.","zh":"已定罪的罪犯可能失去某些自由，因為法院已確認其罪責。"},{"en":"After conviction, punishment may include imprisonment, fines, or community-based orders.","zh":"定罪後，懲罰可能包括監禁、罰款或社區式命令。"},{"en":"This phrase describes legal status after guilt has been formally decided.","zh":"這個短語描述罪責正式被裁定後的法律身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"serve a long term of imprisonment","meaning":"服長期監禁刑期","examples":[{"en":"Some convicted criminals serve long terms of imprisonment.","zh":"有些已定罪的罪犯服長期監禁刑期。"},{"en":"To serve a long term of imprisonment means to spend many years in prison as punishment.","zh":"serve a long term of imprisonment 指作為懲罰在監獄中度過多年。"},{"en":"A person convicted of a serious violent crime may serve a long term of imprisonment.","zh":"被判嚴重暴力罪行的人可能服長期監禁刑期。"},{"en":"Long imprisonment removes offenders from society but may make reintegration harder later.","zh":"長期監禁把罪犯移離社會，但日後可能令重新融入更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on completing a lengthy prison sentence.","zh":"這個短語著重完成漫長的監禁刑期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"upon one’s release","meaning":"在某人獲釋後","examples":[{"en":"Upon their release, former prisoners may need considerable support.","zh":"在前囚犯獲釋後，他們可能需要大量支援。"},{"en":"Upon one’s release means at the time when someone is allowed to leave prison or custody.","zh":"upon one’s release 指某人被允許離開監獄或羈押時。"},{"en":"Upon his release, a prisoner may need a place to live and help finding work.","zh":"在某人獲釋後，他可能需要住所和找工作的協助。"},{"en":"If support is missing upon release, the person may return to old habits or unsafe networks.","zh":"如果獲釋後缺乏支援，該人可能回到舊習慣或不安全的人際網絡。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the moment when imprisonment ends and reintegration begins.","zh":"這個短語標記監禁結束和重新融入開始的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"not necessarily expect someone to","meaning":"不一定能期望某人……","examples":[{"en":"We cannot necessarily expect every released prisoner to be fully reformed.","zh":"我們不一定能期望每名獲釋囚犯都已完全改過自新。"},{"en":"To not necessarily expect someone to do something means we should not assume it will always happen.","zh":"not necessarily expect someone to do something 指不應假設某事一定會發生。"},{"en":"We cannot necessarily expect a new employee to understand every system on the first day.","zh":"我們不一定能期望新員工第一天就明白每個系統。"},{"en":"If a task is difficult, expecting instant success may be unrealistic.","zh":"如果任務困難，期望即時成功可能不切實際。"},{"en":"This phrase helps express caution about what people can reasonably achieve.","zh":"這個短語有助謹慎表達對他人能否做到某事的合理期望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be reformed","meaning":"得到改造；改過自新","examples":[{"en":"Prisoners are expected to be reformed before returning to society.","zh":"囚犯被期望在重返社會前得到改造。"},{"en":"To be reformed means to have changed one’s behaviour and attitudes for the better.","zh":"be reformed 指行為和態度已向好的方向改變。"},{"en":"A former bully may be considered reformed if he apologises and stops harming classmates.","zh":"如果前欺凌者道歉並停止傷害同學，他可能被視為已改過自新。"},{"en":"Real reform usually requires reflection, support, and repeated good choices.","zh":"真正改造通常需要反思、支援和反覆作出良好選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes genuine personal change, not merely pretending to behave well.","zh":"這個短語描述真誠的個人改變，而不只是裝作表現良好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"reintegrate into society","meaning":"重新融入社會","examples":[{"en":"Former inmates may struggle to reintegrate into society.","zh":"前囚犯可能難以重新融入社會。"},{"en":"To reintegrate into society means to return to ordinary community life after being separated from it.","zh":"reintegrate into society 指在與社會分隔後重返一般社區生活。"},{"en":"A released prisoner may need work, housing, family support, and counselling to reintegrate into society.","zh":"獲釋囚犯可能需要工作、住所、家庭支援和輔導，才能重新融入社會。"},{"en":"Without support, reintegration can fail and the person may feel rejected or isolated.","zh":"如果沒有支援，重新融入可能失敗，而當事人可能感到被排斥或孤立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes returning to a normal social role after exclusion or imprisonment.","zh":"這個短語描述在被排除或監禁後重新回到正常社會角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rough and violent prison environments","meaning":"惡劣而暴力的監獄環境","examples":[{"en":"Rough and violent prison environments may reinforce criminal behaviour.","zh":"惡劣而暴力的監獄環境可能強化犯罪行為。"},{"en":"Rough and violent prison environments are harsh places where inmates may face fear, aggression, and physical danger.","zh":"rough and violent prison environments 指囚犯可能面對恐懼、攻擊和人身危險的嚴苛場所。"},{"en":"A prison with frequent fights and intimidation can be a rough and violent environment.","zh":"經常發生打鬥和恐嚇的監獄，可以是惡劣而暴力的環境。"},{"en":"Such environments may make inmates more defensive, angry, or connected to criminal groups.","zh":"這類環境可能令囚犯更防衛、更憤怒，或與犯罪團體關係更深。"},{"en":"This phrase describes prison conditions that may damage rather than reform people.","zh":"這個短語描述可能傷害人而不是改造人的監獄條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"prison gang culture","meaning":"監獄幫派文化","examples":[{"en":"Prison gang culture may expose inmates to further violence and crime.","zh":"監獄幫派文化可能令囚犯接觸更多暴力和犯罪。"},{"en":"Prison gang culture refers to the power, loyalty, threats, and criminal networks formed by gangs inside prison.","zh":"prison gang culture 指監獄內幫派形成的權力、忠誠、威脅和犯罪網絡。"},{"en":"A new inmate may feel pressured to join a gang for protection.","zh":"新囚犯可能因尋求保護而感到被迫加入幫派。"},{"en":"Gang culture can make prison more dangerous and make rehabilitation harder.","zh":"幫派文化可以令監獄更危險，並令更生更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised criminal influence inside prisons.","zh":"這個短語描述監獄內有組織的犯罪影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"quite the opposite may occur","meaning":"結果可能恰恰相反","examples":[{"en":"Instead of rehabilitation, quite the opposite may occur in prison.","zh":"在監獄中，結果可能不是更生，而是恰恰相反。"},{"en":"Quite the opposite may occur means the result may be the reverse of what was intended.","zh":"quite the opposite may occur 指結果可能與原本意圖完全相反。"},{"en":"A strict school rule meant to improve behaviour may make students more rebellious; quite the opposite may occur.","zh":"本來為改善行為而設的嚴格校規，可能令學生更反叛；結果可能恰恰相反。"},{"en":"If prison increases violence instead of reducing it, the policy has failed in an important way.","zh":"如果監獄增加暴力而不是減少暴力，政策就在重要方面失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a plan may produce the opposite result.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們，計劃可能產生相反結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"raise a difficult dilemma","meaning":"帶來棘手的兩難局面","examples":[{"en":"The possibility of prisoners becoming more violent raises a difficult dilemma.","zh":"囚犯可能變得更暴力這種可能性帶來棘手的兩難局面。"},{"en":"To raise a difficult dilemma means to create a situation where every choice has serious problems.","zh":"raise a difficult dilemma 指造成一種每個選擇都有嚴重問題的情況。"},{"en":"A school may face a difficult dilemma if suspending a student protects others but harms that student’s education.","zh":"如果停學能保護其他人但會傷害該學生的教育，學校可能面對棘手的兩難局面。"},{"en":"When punishment may worsen behaviour, society must decide how to balance safety and reform.","zh":"當懲罰可能令行為更差，社會必須決定如何平衡安全和改造。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a hard choice with no perfect solution.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有完美解決方案的艱難選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"criminal justice system","meaning":"刑事司法制度","examples":[{"en":"The criminal justice system must balance punishment with rehabilitation.","zh":"刑事司法制度必須在懲罰和更生之間取得平衡。"},{"en":"The criminal justice system is the set of police, courts, prisons, and laws used to respond to crime.","zh":"criminal justice system 指用來處理犯罪的警察、法院、監獄和法律制度。"},{"en":"A fair criminal justice system should protect victims while respecting the rights of accused people.","zh":"公平的刑事司法制度應保護受害者，同時尊重被告權利。"},{"en":"If the system focuses only on punishment, it may fail to reduce future crime.","zh":"如果制度只集中於懲罰，它可能未能減少未來犯罪。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the whole legal structure for dealing with crime.","zh":"這個短語指處理犯罪的整套法律結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"maintain social order","meaning":"維持社會秩序","examples":[{"en":"Laws and punishments are intended to maintain social order.","zh":"法律和懲罰旨在維持社會秩序。"},{"en":"To maintain social order means to keep society stable, safe, and governed by accepted rules.","zh":"maintain social order 指保持社會穩定、安全，並受公認規則管理。"},{"en":"Traffic laws help maintain social order by preventing dangerous driving and confusion.","zh":"交通法例透過防止危險駕駛和混亂來維持社會秩序。"},{"en":"When people believe rules are fair, they are more likely to obey them.","zh":"當人們相信規則公平，他們較可能遵守。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping public life organised and peaceful.","zh":"這個短語描述保持公共生活有組織而和平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"break the law","meaning":"違法","examples":[{"en":"Those who break the law may face criminal punishment.","zh":"違法者可能面對刑事懲罰。"},{"en":"To break the law means to do something illegal.","zh":"break the law 指做違法的事情。"},{"en":"A driver breaks the law if he drives while drunk.","zh":"如果司機酒後駕駛，他就是違法。"},{"en":"Breaking the law can lead to fines, arrest, imprisonment, or a criminal record.","zh":"違法可能導致罰款、拘捕、監禁或刑事紀錄。"},{"en":"This phrase describes violating legal rules.","zh":"這個短語描述違反法律規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be expected to be punished","meaning":"理應受到懲罰","examples":[{"en":"People who commit serious offences are expected to be punished.","zh":"作出嚴重罪行的人理應受到懲罰。"},{"en":"To be expected to be punished means people generally believe punishment should follow wrongdoing.","zh":"be expected to be punished 指人們普遍認為錯誤行為之後應有懲罰。"},{"en":"A student who cheats in an exam may be expected to be punished by the school.","zh":"在考試中作弊的學生可能被認為理應受到學校懲罰。"},{"en":"Punishment is often seen as necessary for fairness, warning, and public safety.","zh":"懲罰常被視為對公平、警示和公共安全必要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a social or legal expectation after misconduct.","zh":"這個短語描述不當行為後的社會或法律期望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"place a high emphasis on","meaning":"高度重視……","examples":[{"en":"The justice system must place a high emphasis on rehabilitation.","zh":"司法制度必須高度重視更生。"},{"en":"To place a high emphasis on something means to treat it as very important.","zh":"place a high emphasis on something 指把某事視為非常重要。"},{"en":"A school may place a high emphasis on reading because it supports every subject.","zh":"學校可能高度重視閱讀，因為閱讀支援每個科目。"},{"en":"When a system places emphasis on rehabilitation, it invests in education, therapy, and support.","zh":"當制度重視更生，它會投資於教育、治療和支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving strong priority to something.","zh":"這個短語描述給予某事高度優先。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the principle of rehabilitation","meaning":"更生原則","examples":[{"en":"The principle of rehabilitation assumes that offenders can change.","zh":"更生原則假設罪犯可以改變。"},{"en":"The principle of rehabilitation is the idea that punishment should help offenders become safer and more responsible people.","zh":"principle of rehabilitation 指懲罰應幫助罪犯成為更安全、更負責任的人這一理念。"},{"en":"A prison programme based on this principle may teach work skills and emotional control.","zh":"以這原則為基礎的監獄計劃可能教授工作技能和情緒控制。"},{"en":"If society rejects this principle completely, prison becomes only a place of punishment.","zh":"如果社會完全拒絕這原則，監獄就只會成為懲罰場所。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the guiding belief behind offender reform.","zh":"這個短語描述罪犯改造背後的指導信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be based on the assumption that","meaning":"基於……的假設","examples":[{"en":"Rehabilitation is based on the assumption that criminal tendencies are not permanent.","zh":"更生基於犯罪傾向並非永久的假設。"},{"en":"To be based on the assumption that means to depend on a belief taken as the starting point.","zh":"be based on the assumption that 指依靠某個作為起點的信念。"},{"en":"A homework policy may be based on the assumption that students have quiet study space at home.","zh":"家課政策可能基於學生在家有安靜學習空間的假設。"},{"en":"If the assumption is wrong, the policy built on it may also fail.","zh":"如果假設錯誤，建基於它的政策也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the belief behind an argument, policy, or plan.","zh":"這個短語解釋論點、政策或計劃背後的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"criminal tendencies","meaning":"犯罪傾向","examples":[{"en":"Therapy may help some offenders control their criminal tendencies.","zh":"治療可能幫助某些罪犯控制其犯罪傾向。"},{"en":"Criminal tendencies are patterns of thought, desire, or behaviour that make someone more likely to commit crimes.","zh":"criminal tendencies 指令人較可能犯罪的思想、慾望或行為模式。"},{"en":"A person with violent tendencies may need therapy to manage anger before it becomes harmful.","zh":"有暴力傾向的人可能需要治療來管理憤怒，以免造成傷害。"},{"en":"Support can reduce criminal tendencies by changing habits, friends, and coping methods.","zh":"支援可以透過改變習慣、朋友和應對方法來減少犯罪傾向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes risk patterns, not a fixed identity.","zh":"這個短語描述風險模式，而不是固定身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not necessarily permanent","meaning":"不一定是永久的","examples":[{"en":"Antisocial behaviour is not necessarily permanent.","zh":"反社會行為不一定是永久的。"},{"en":"Not necessarily permanent means something may change, even if it seems stable now.","zh":"not necessarily permanent 指某事可能會改變，即使現在看似穩定。"},{"en":"A student’s poor attitude is not necessarily permanent if adults give guidance and support.","zh":"如果成年人給予指導和支援，學生的不良態度不一定是永久的。"},{"en":"Labelling a problem as permanent can make people stop trying to improve it.","zh":"把問題標籤為永久，可能令人停止嘗試改善。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses hope while remaining realistic.","zh":"這個短語在保持現實的同時表達希望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"former inmates","meaning":"前囚犯","examples":[{"en":"Former inmates often face difficulties finding housing and employment.","zh":"前囚犯經常面對找住所和工作方面的困難。"},{"en":"Former inmates are people who were once imprisoned but have now been released.","zh":"former inmates 指曾經被監禁但現在已獲釋的人。"},{"en":"A former inmate may struggle because employers or landlords do not trust people with prison records.","zh":"前囚犯可能因僱主或業主不信任有監獄紀錄的人而遇到困難。"},{"en":"Without housing and work, former inmates may find reintegration much harder.","zh":"沒有住所和工作，前囚犯可能覺得重新融入社會困難得多。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people after imprisonment, especially during re-entry into society.","zh":"這個短語指監禁後的人，尤其是在重返社會期間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lead a productive life","meaning":"過有貢獻的生活","examples":[{"en":"Many former offenders can lead productive lives after release.","zh":"許多前罪犯獲釋後可以過有貢獻的生活。"},{"en":"To lead a productive life means to live in a way that is useful, responsible, and meaningful.","zh":"lead a productive life 指以有用、負責任和有意義的方式生活。"},{"en":"A former offender may lead a productive life by working, caring for family, and obeying the law.","zh":"前罪犯可以透過工作、照顧家庭和守法過有貢獻的生活。"},{"en":"Stable work and social support can help people build productive lives after difficult periods.","zh":"穩定工作和社會支援可以幫助人在困難時期後建立有貢獻的生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes positive participation in ordinary life.","zh":"這個短語描述正面參與一般生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"contribute positively to society","meaning":"對社會作出正面貢獻","examples":[{"en":"Rehabilitated offenders may contribute positively to society.","zh":"已更生罪犯可能對社會作出正面貢獻。"},{"en":"To contribute positively to society means to help the community through useful, lawful, or caring actions.","zh":"contribute positively to society 指透過有用、守法或關懷的行動幫助社區。"},{"en":"A person contributes positively by working honestly, volunteering, or supporting family members.","zh":"一個人可以透過誠實工作、做義工或支援家庭成員來對社會作出正面貢獻。"},{"en":"When former offenders contribute positively, society gains safety and human potential.","zh":"當前罪犯作出正面貢獻，社會會獲得安全和人的潛能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving value back to the community.","zh":"這個短語描述把價值回饋社區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the ultimate goal","meaning":"最終目標","examples":[{"en":"The ultimate goal of rehabilitation is to prevent further offending.","zh":"更生的最終目標是防止進一步犯罪。"},{"en":"The ultimate goal is the final and most important aim behind an action or policy.","zh":"ultimate goal 指行動或政策背後最終且最重要的目標。"},{"en":"The ultimate goal of education is not only passing exams but helping students live well.","zh":"教育的最終目標不只是通過考試，而是幫助學生好好生活。"},{"en":"Clear ultimate goals help people judge whether a programme is truly successful.","zh":"清楚的最終目標幫助人判斷一個計劃是否真正成功。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the deepest purpose of an effort.","zh":"這個短語指出努力背後最深層的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prevent someone from reoffending","meaning":"防止某人再次犯罪","examples":[{"en":"Support services aim to prevent former inmates from reoffending.","zh":"支援服務旨在防止前囚犯再次犯罪。"},{"en":"To prevent someone from reoffending means to stop them from committing another crime after a previous offence.","zh":"prevent someone from reoffending 指防止某人在過往犯罪後再犯另一罪行。"},{"en":"Job training may prevent a former prisoner from reoffending by giving him legal income.","zh":"職業訓練可以透過給予合法收入，防止前囚犯再次犯罪。"},{"en":"Housing, counselling, and supervision can reduce the risk of returning to crime.","zh":"住所、輔導和監管可以降低重返犯罪的風險。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on stopping repeat crime.","zh":"這個短語著重阻止重複犯罪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reoffend","meaning":"再次犯罪","examples":[{"en":"Stable employment may reduce the likelihood that an offender will reoffend.","zh":"穩定就業可能降低罪犯再次犯罪的可能性。"},{"en":"To reoffend means to commit another crime after already being convicted or punished.","zh":"reoffend 指已被定罪或受罰後再次犯罪。"},{"en":"A person may be less likely to reoffend if they have work, housing, and supportive family members.","zh":"如果一個人有工作、住所和支持他的家人，他再次犯罪的可能性可能較低。"},{"en":"Reoffending can show that punishment alone did not solve the deeper problem.","zh":"再犯可以顯示單靠懲罰沒有解決更深層問題。"},{"en":"This word describes returning to crime after an earlier offence.","zh":"這個詞描述在早前罪行後重返犯罪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"criminal recidivism","meaning":"刑事再犯","examples":[{"en":"Criminal recidivism refers to committing another offence after release.","zh":"刑事再犯指獲釋後再犯另一罪行。"},{"en":"Criminal recidivism means repeated criminal behaviour after a person has already been punished or released.","zh":"criminal recidivism 指一個人在已受罰或獲釋後重複犯罪。"},{"en":"A justice department may measure criminal recidivism to see whether rehabilitation programmes work.","zh":"司法部門可能量度刑事再犯率，以了解更生計劃是否有效。"},{"en":"High recidivism can suggest that former offenders lack support, skills, or supervision.","zh":"高再犯率可能顯示前罪犯缺乏支援、技能或監管。"},{"en":"This phrase is the formal term for returning to crime.","zh":"這個短語是重返犯罪的正式用語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"systems of education and therapy","meaning":"教育及治療制度","examples":[{"en":"Prisons may provide systems of education and therapy.","zh":"監獄可能提供教育及治療制度。"},{"en":"Systems of education and therapy are organised programmes that teach skills and address emotional or behavioural problems.","zh":"systems of education and therapy 指教授技能並處理情緒或行為問題的有組織計劃。"},{"en":"A prison may offer reading classes, addiction counselling, and anger-management therapy.","zh":"監獄可能提供閱讀課、戒癮輔導和憤怒管理治療。"},{"en":"These systems can support rehabilitation if they are well designed and consistently delivered.","zh":"如果設計良好且持續提供，這些制度可以支持更生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes structured support for learning and psychological change.","zh":"這個短語描述支援學習和心理改變的結構化制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"inmate education","meaning":"囚犯教育","examples":[{"en":"Inmate education may improve employment opportunities after release.","zh":"囚犯教育可能改善獲釋後的就業機會。"},{"en":"Inmate education means classes or training provided to people in prison.","zh":"inmate education 指提供給監獄中人士的課堂或訓練。"},{"en":"An inmate may learn reading, computer skills, or a trade through prison education.","zh":"囚犯可能透過監獄教育學習閱讀、電腦技能或一門手藝。"},{"en":"Education can increase confidence and make lawful work more realistic after release.","zh":"教育可以增加信心，並令獲釋後合法工作更可行。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on learning opportunities for prisoners.","zh":"這個短語著重囚犯的學習機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"therapeutic programmes","meaning":"治療計劃","examples":[{"en":"Therapeutic programmes may address addiction or violent behaviour.","zh":"治療計劃可能處理成癮或暴力行為。"},{"en":"Therapeutic programmes are organised treatments designed to improve mental health, behaviour, or emotional control.","zh":"therapeutic programmes 指旨在改善心理健康、行為或情緒控制的有組織治療。"},{"en":"A programme for anger management may help inmates understand triggers and practise calmer responses.","zh":"憤怒管理計劃可能幫助囚犯理解觸發因素並練習更冷靜的回應。"},{"en":"Therapy can reduce risk when it helps people change the thoughts behind harmful behaviour.","zh":"當治療幫助人改變有害行為背後的思想，它可以降低風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes structured treatment, not casual advice.","zh":"這個短語描述結構化治療，而不是隨意建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"assessment procedures","meaning":"評估程序","examples":[{"en":"Assessment procedures are used to evaluate an inmate’s progress.","zh":"評估程序被用來評估囚犯的進展。"},{"en":"Assessment procedures are formal steps used to judge someone’s behaviour, risk, ability, or improvement.","zh":"assessment procedures 指用來判斷某人的行為、風險、能力或改善情況的正式步驟。"},{"en":"A school may use assessment procedures to decide whether a student needs extra support.","zh":"學校可能使用評估程序來決定學生是否需要額外支援。"},{"en":"Clear procedures help reduce guesswork, but they cannot remove all uncertainty.","zh":"清楚程序有助減少猜測，但不能消除所有不確定性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised methods for evaluation.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的評估方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"determine whether","meaning":"判斷是否……","examples":[{"en":"Officials try to determine whether the offender is ready for release.","zh":"官員嘗試判斷該罪犯是否已準備好獲釋。"},{"en":"To determine whether means to find out or decide if something is true.","zh":"determine whether 指查明或決定某事是否屬實。"},{"en":"A doctor may run tests to determine whether a patient needs surgery.","zh":"醫生可能進行檢查，以判斷病人是否需要手術。"},{"en":"Decisions become safer when people determine the facts before acting.","zh":"當人們在行動前判斷事實，決定會更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a careful judgement between yes and no.","zh":"這個短語引入是與否之間的謹慎判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"develop genuine remorse","meaning":"產生真誠悔意","examples":[{"en":"Prison authorities assess whether inmates have developed genuine remorse.","zh":"監獄當局評估囚犯是否已產生真誠悔意。"},{"en":"To develop genuine remorse means to feel sincere regret for harm one has caused.","zh":"develop genuine remorse 指對自己造成的傷害感到真誠後悔。"},{"en":"A student who truly understands how bullying hurt a classmate may develop genuine remorse.","zh":"真正明白欺凌如何傷害同學的學生，可能產生真誠悔意。"},{"en":"Genuine remorse can lead to apology, changed behaviour, and a desire to repair damage.","zh":"真誠悔意可以帶來道歉、行為改變和修補傷害的願望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes real regret, not a performance to avoid punishment.","zh":"這個短語描述真實後悔，而不是為避免懲罰而表演。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"remorse for past misdeeds","meaning":"對過往過失的悔意","examples":[{"en":"A parole board may look for remorse for past misdeeds.","zh":"假釋委員會可能尋找對過往過失的悔意。"},{"en":"Remorse for past misdeeds means sincere regret about wrong actions committed earlier.","zh":"remorse for past misdeeds 指對早前不當行為的真誠後悔。"},{"en":"A person may show remorse for past misdeeds by accepting responsibility and apologising.","zh":"一個人可以透過承擔責任和道歉來表現對過往過失的悔意。"},{"en":"Without remorse, officials may worry that the offender has not understood the harm caused.","zh":"如果沒有悔意，官員可能擔心罪犯未明白造成的傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on regret for earlier wrongdoing.","zh":"這個短語著重對早前錯事的後悔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"past misdeeds","meaning":"過往的不當行為","examples":[{"en":"The offender expressed regret for his past misdeeds.","zh":"該罪犯對自己的過往不當行為表示後悔。"},{"en":"Past misdeeds are wrong or harmful actions committed in the past.","zh":"past misdeeds 指過去作出的錯誤或有害行為。"},{"en":"A public figure may apologise for past misdeeds after old evidence is discovered.","zh":"當舊證據被發現，公眾人物可能為過往不當行為道歉。"},{"en":"Reflecting on past misdeeds can help a person understand who was hurt and why change is needed.","zh":"反思過往不當行為可以幫助人明白誰受到傷害以及為何需要改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to earlier wrongdoing, often with moral blame.","zh":"這個短語指早前的錯事，通常帶有道德責備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"an ability to reintegrate","meaning":"重新融入的能力","examples":[{"en":"Officials assess an inmate’s ability to reintegrate into society.","zh":"官員評估囚犯重新融入社會的能力。"},{"en":"An ability to reintegrate means the capacity to return to ordinary life and follow social rules.","zh":"ability to reintegrate 指回到一般生活並遵守社會規則的能力。"},{"en":"A person with stable housing, work skills, and family support may have a stronger ability to reintegrate.","zh":"有穩定住所、工作技能和家庭支援的人，可能有較強重新融入能力。"},{"en":"Reintegration becomes harder when someone lacks income, relationships, or emotional control.","zh":"當一個人缺乏收入、關係或情緒控制，重新融入會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes readiness to live safely in the community again.","zh":"這個短語描述再次安全地生活於社區中的準備程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"intentions to do so","meaning":"這樣做的意願","examples":[{"en":"The inmate must demonstrate both the ability and the intention to change.","zh":"囚犯必須展示改變的能力和意願。"},{"en":"Intentions to do so are plans or willingness to carry out the action already mentioned.","zh":"intentions to do so 指計劃或願意做前文已提及的事情。"},{"en":"A student may have the ability to apologise but no intention to do so.","zh":"學生可能有道歉能力，但沒有這樣做的意願。"},{"en":"Good intentions matter because ability alone does not guarantee action.","zh":"良好意願很重要，因為單有能力並不保證會行動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a person’s real willingness to follow through.","zh":"這個短語指某人真正付諸行動的意願。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"assess something accurately","meaning":"準確評估……","examples":[{"en":"It is difficult to assess a person’s future behaviour accurately.","zh":"準確評估一個人未來的行為是困難的。"},{"en":"To assess something accurately means to judge it correctly based on reliable evidence.","zh":"assess something accurately 指根據可靠證據正確判斷某事。"},{"en":"A teacher needs several assignments to assess a student’s writing accurately.","zh":"老師需要幾份功課才能準確評估學生的寫作。"},{"en":"If the evidence is incomplete, even experts may assess a situation wrongly.","zh":"如果證據不完整，即使專家也可能錯誤評估情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful and correct evaluation.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細而正確的評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"it must be accepted that","meaning":"必須承認","examples":[{"en":"It must be accepted that rehabilitation does not succeed in every case.","zh":"必須承認，更生並非在每個個案中都成功。"},{"en":"It must be accepted that means we need to recognise an unpleasant or difficult truth.","zh":"it must be accepted that 指我們需要承認一個不愉快或困難的事實。"},{"en":"It must be accepted that not every student improves at the same speed.","zh":"必須承認，並非每個學生都以相同速度進步。"},{"en":"Accepting reality helps people design better policies instead of pretending problems do not exist.","zh":"接受現實幫助人設計更好的政策，而不是假裝問題不存在。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a necessary but sometimes uncomfortable admission.","zh":"這個短語引入必要但有時令人不舒服的承認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"however much we try","meaning":"無論我們多麼努力","examples":[{"en":"Some individuals may remain dangerous however much we try to rehabilitate them.","zh":"有些人可能仍然危險，無論我們多麼努力改造他們。"},{"en":"However much we try means no matter how much effort we make.","zh":"however much we try 指無論我們付出多少努力。"},{"en":"However much we try, we cannot help a student improve if he refuses all feedback.","zh":"無論我們多麼努力，如果學生拒絕所有回饋，我們也不能幫助他進步。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that effort may not always produce the desired result.","zh":"這個短語顯示努力未必總能產生理想結果。"},{"en":"It is useful when acknowledging limits despite serious attempts.","zh":"它適合用於承認即使認真嘗試仍有局限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be incapable of rehabilitation","meaning":"無法得到改造","examples":[{"en":"A small number of offenders may be incapable of rehabilitation.","zh":"少數罪犯可能無法得到改造。"},{"en":"To be incapable of rehabilitation means to be unable to change safely or responsibly through reform programmes.","zh":"be incapable of rehabilitation 指無法透過更生計劃安全或負責任地改變。"},{"en":"A person who repeatedly manipulates therapy and refuses responsibility may be seen as difficult to rehabilitate.","zh":"反覆操控治療並拒絕承擔責任的人，可能被視為難以改造。"},{"en":"If someone is incapable of rehabilitation, public safety becomes a major concern.","zh":"如果某人無法得到改造，公共安全就會成為重大關注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious limit to reform.","zh":"這個短語描述改造上的嚴重限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the term psychopath","meaning":"「心理病態者」這個詞","examples":[{"en":"The term psychopath is often used when discussing persistent antisocial behaviour.","zh":"討論持續反社會行為時，常使用「心理病態者」這個詞。"},{"en":"The term psychopath refers to a person described as having severe traits such as lack of empathy, manipulation, and persistent antisocial behaviour.","zh":"psychopath 這個詞指被描述為具有缺乏同理心、操控他人和持續反社會行為等嚴重特徵的人。"},{"en":"In careful writing, this term should not be used casually to insult someone.","zh":"在謹慎寫作中，這個詞不應被隨便用來侮辱別人。"},{"en":"Misusing the term can create stigma and confusion about mental health and criminal risk.","zh":"誤用這個詞可能造成污名，並混淆心理健康和犯罪風險。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a specific and sensitive label used in psychology and criminal justice.","zh":"這個短語引入心理學和刑事司法中使用的一個具體而敏感的標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a key indicator of","meaning":"……的一個主要指標","examples":[{"en":"An inability to learn from mistakes may be a key indicator of psychopathy.","zh":"無法從錯誤中汲取教訓可能是心理病態的一個主要指標。"},{"en":"A key indicator of something is an important sign that suggests it may be present.","zh":"key indicator of something 指顯示某事可能存在的重要跡象。"},{"en":"Regular lateness may be a key indicator of poor time management.","zh":"經常遲到可能是時間管理差的一個主要指標。"},{"en":"Indicators do not prove everything by themselves, but they help guide assessment.","zh":"指標本身不能證明一切，但有助引導評估。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important warning sign or clue.","zh":"這個短語描述重要警號或線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an inability to learn from","meaning":"無法從……汲取教訓","examples":[{"en":"Some offenders display an inability to learn from past mistakes.","zh":"有些罪犯顯示出無法從過往錯誤中汲取教訓。"},{"en":"An inability to learn from something means a failure to change behaviour after experience or correction.","zh":"inability to learn from something 指經歷或糾正後仍未能改變行為。"},{"en":"A student shows an inability to learn from feedback if he repeats the same grammar error every week.","zh":"如果學生每週重複同一文法錯誤，他就顯示出無法從回饋中汲取教訓。"},{"en":"When people cannot learn from consequences, they may repeat harmful behaviour.","zh":"當人無法從後果中學習，他們可能重複有害行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes failure to improve after evidence or experience.","zh":"這個短語描述在證據或經驗後仍未改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"past mistakes","meaning":"過往錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Rehabilitation requires offenders to reflect on past mistakes.","zh":"更生要求罪犯反思過往錯誤。"},{"en":"Past mistakes are wrong choices or actions made earlier.","zh":"past mistakes 指早前作出的錯誤選擇或行動。"},{"en":"A student can learn from past mistakes by reviewing why previous answers were wrong.","zh":"學生可以透過檢視之前答案為何錯誤，從過往錯誤中學習。"},{"en":"Reflecting on past mistakes helps people avoid repeating the same harm.","zh":"反思過往錯誤幫助人避免重複相同傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes earlier errors that can become lessons.","zh":"這個短語描述可以成為教訓的早前錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"improve someone’s behaviour","meaning":"改善某人的行為","examples":[{"en":"Therapy is intended to improve an offender’s behaviour.","zh":"治療旨在改善罪犯的行為。"},{"en":"To improve someone’s behaviour means to help them act in a safer, kinder, or more responsible way.","zh":"improve someone’s behaviour 指幫助某人以更安全、更友善或更負責任的方式行動。"},{"en":"Clear classroom rules can improve students’ behaviour when they know the consequences.","zh":"當學生知道後果，清楚課堂規則可以改善他們的行為。"},{"en":"Behaviour improves when people understand harm, practise alternatives, and receive support.","zh":"當人理解傷害、練習替代做法並得到支援，行為會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on changing actions, not only changing words.","zh":"這個短語著重改變行動，而不只是改變說話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be unlikely to work","meaning":"不大可能奏效","examples":[{"en":"Conventional treatment may be unlikely to work with some individuals.","zh":"傳統治療對某些人不大可能奏效。"},{"en":"To be unlikely to work means to have a low chance of being successful.","zh":"be unlikely to work 指成功機會較低。"},{"en":"A short lecture is unlikely to work if students need practical speaking practice.","zh":"如果學生需要實際口語練習，短講座不大可能奏效。"},{"en":"If a method does not match the problem, it may fail even when people try hard.","zh":"如果方法不配合問題，即使人們努力，它也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses doubt about effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語表達對成效的懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be highly correlated with","meaning":"與……高度相關","examples":[{"en":"Psychopathy is highly correlated with criminal recidivism.","zh":"心理病態與刑事再犯高度相關。"},{"en":"To be highly correlated with something means two things often occur together in a strong statistical relationship.","zh":"be highly correlated with something 指兩件事常一起出現，並有強烈統計關係。"},{"en":"Poor sleep may be highly correlated with weak concentration in students.","zh":"睡眠不足可能與學生專注力弱高度相關。"},{"en":"Correlation suggests a strong link, but it does not always prove direct cause.","zh":"相關顯示強連繫，但不一定證明直接因果。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when research shows two factors are closely connected.","zh":"當研究顯示兩個因素緊密相連時，這個短語很常用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"psychopathic prisoners","meaning":"有心理病態特徵的囚犯","examples":[{"en":"Psychopathic prisoners may become skilled at disguising their intentions.","zh":"有心理病態特徵的囚犯可能變得擅長掩飾自己的意圖。"},{"en":"Psychopathic prisoners are inmates described as having psychopathic traits such as manipulation and lack of remorse.","zh":"psychopathic prisoners 指被描述為具有操控他人、缺乏悔意等心理病態特徵的囚犯。"},{"en":"Assessors may need special tools when evaluating prisoners with these traits.","zh":"評估具有這些特徵的囚犯時，評估人員可能需要特殊工具。"},{"en":"Such prisoners may appear cooperative while hiding harmful motives.","zh":"這類囚犯可能表面合作，同時隱藏有害動機。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific high-risk group in prison assessment.","zh":"這個短語描述監獄評估中的特定高風險群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be equally likely to","meaning":"有同等可能……","examples":[{"en":"Psychopathic prisoners may be equally likely to be released as other prisoners.","zh":"有心理病態特徵的囚犯可能與其他囚犯有同等可能獲釋。"},{"en":"To be equally likely to do something means to have the same chance of doing it as another group.","zh":"be equally likely to do something 指與另一組有相同機會做某事。"},{"en":"Two students may be equally likely to pass if they have similar preparation and support.","zh":"如果兩名學生有相似準備和支援，他們可能有同等可能合格。"},{"en":"If a high-risk group is equally likely to be released, assessment procedures may need review.","zh":"如果高風險群體有同等可能獲釋，評估程序可能需要檢討。"},{"en":"This phrase compares probability between groups.","zh":"這個短語比較組別之間的可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"non-psychopathic prisoners","meaning":"沒有心理病態特徵的囚犯","examples":[{"en":"The study compared psychopathic and non-psychopathic prisoners.","zh":"該研究比較了有心理病態特徵和沒有心理病態特徵的囚犯。"},{"en":"Non-psychopathic prisoners are inmates not identified as having psychopathic traits.","zh":"non-psychopathic prisoners 指未被識別為具有心理病態特徵的囚犯。"},{"en":"A study may compare two prisoner groups to see whether risk factors affect release decisions.","zh":"研究可能比較兩組囚犯，以了解風險因素是否影響釋放決定。"},{"en":"Comparing groups can reveal whether assessment systems treat different risk profiles differently.","zh":"比較組別可以揭示評估制度是否不同地處理不同風險特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase names the comparison group without psychopathic traits.","zh":"這個短語命名沒有心理病態特徵的比較組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be explained by the fact that","meaning":"可由……這一事實解釋","examples":[{"en":"This result may be explained by the fact that some offenders deceive assessors effectively.","zh":"這個結果可由某些罪犯能有效欺騙評估人員這一事實解釋。"},{"en":"To be explained by the fact that means a result can be understood because a particular fact is true.","zh":"be explained by the fact that 指某結果可以因某事實成立而被理解。"},{"en":"A student’s low mark may be explained by the fact that she missed several lessons.","zh":"學生低分可由她缺了幾堂課這一事實解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the reason behind an observed result.","zh":"這個短語引入觀察結果背後的原因。"},{"en":"It helps connect evidence with explanation.","zh":"它幫助把證據與解釋連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"develop better strategies for","meaning":"發展更有效的策略去……","examples":[{"en":"Some offenders develop better strategies for hiding their motives.","zh":"有些罪犯發展更有效的策略去隱藏自己的動機。"},{"en":"To develop better strategies for something means to create more effective methods to achieve that aim.","zh":"develop better strategies for something 指創造更有效的方法來達成該目的。"},{"en":"A student may develop better strategies for remembering vocabulary by using spaced revision.","zh":"學生可能透過間隔複習，發展更有效的策略去記憶詞彙。"},{"en":"Strategies improve when people learn from past failures and adapt their methods.","zh":"當人從過往失敗中學習並調整方法，策略會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improving methods for a particular purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述為特定目的改善方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"disguise one’s intentions","meaning":"掩飾自己的意圖","examples":[{"en":"A manipulative offender may disguise their true intentions.","zh":"操控型罪犯可能掩飾自己的真正意圖。"},{"en":"To disguise one’s intentions means to hide what one really plans or wants.","zh":"disguise one’s intentions 指隱藏自己真正計劃或想要的東西。"},{"en":"A student may disguise his intentions by saying he wants to help while actually trying to copy homework.","zh":"學生可能說自己想幫忙，實際上想抄功課，藉此掩飾自己的意圖。"},{"en":"When people disguise intentions, others may make decisions based on false trust.","zh":"當人掩飾意圖，其他人可能基於錯誤信任作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hiding real motives behind acceptable behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述把真正動機藏在可接受行為背後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"become more adept at","meaning":"變得更擅長……","examples":[{"en":"Some individuals become more adept at tricking authority figures.","zh":"有些人變得更擅長欺騙權威人物。"},{"en":"To become more adept at something means to become more skilled at doing it.","zh":"become more adept at something 指做某事變得更熟練。"},{"en":"A student can become more adept at essay writing after regular feedback and revision.","zh":"學生經過定期回饋和修改後，可以變得更擅長寫作文。"},{"en":"People become adept through practice, observation, and repeated attempts.","zh":"人們透過練習、觀察和反覆嘗試變得擅長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growing skill, whether the skill is good or harmful.","zh":"這個短語描述技能增長，不論該技能是好是壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"trick others","meaning":"欺騙他人","examples":[{"en":"Manipulative offenders may learn how to trick others.","zh":"操控型罪犯可能學會如何欺騙他人。"},{"en":"To trick others means to deceive people so they believe something false or act against their own interests.","zh":"trick others 指欺騙人，使他們相信錯誤事情或作出不利於自己的行動。"},{"en":"A scammer tricks others by pretending to be a bank officer.","zh":"騙徒會假扮銀行職員來欺騙他人。"},{"en":"People who trick others often use charm, lies, or pressure to gain advantage.","zh":"欺騙他人的人常使用魅力、謊言或壓力來取得好處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intentional deception.","zh":"這個短語描述有意欺騙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"penal procedures","meaning":"刑罰程序","examples":[{"en":"Treatment may teach offenders how penal procedures operate.","zh":"治療可能教會罪犯刑罰程序如何運作。"},{"en":"Penal procedures are rules and processes connected with punishment, prisons, and offender management.","zh":"penal procedures 指與懲罰、監獄和罪犯管理有關的規則和程序。"},{"en":"A prison’s disciplinary hearing is part of its penal procedures.","zh":"監獄紀律聆訊是其刑罰程序的一部分。"},{"en":"If offenders understand procedures only to manipulate them, rehabilitation may be weakened.","zh":"如果罪犯理解程序只是為了操控它們，更生可能被削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the formal processes of the punishment system.","zh":"這個短語指懲罰制度中的正式程序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"judicial procedures","meaning":"司法程序","examples":[{"en":"Offenders may learn about judicial procedures during rehabilitation programmes.","zh":"罪犯可能在更生計劃中學到司法程序。"},{"en":"Judicial procedures are formal court processes used to handle legal cases.","zh":"judicial procedures 指用來處理法律案件的正式法院程序。"},{"en":"A trial, appeal, or sentencing hearing follows judicial procedures.","zh":"審訊、上訴或判刑聆訊都遵循司法程序。"},{"en":"Understanding judicial procedures can help people know their rights and responsibilities.","zh":"理解司法程序可以幫助人知道自己的權利和責任。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to how courts operate according to law.","zh":"這個短語指法院如何依法運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"twist something to one’s advantage","meaning":"扭曲利用……為自己謀利","examples":[{"en":"A manipulative person may twist procedural knowledge to their advantage.","zh":"操控型的人可能扭曲利用程序知識為自己謀利。"},{"en":"To twist something to one’s advantage means to use it in a distorted or unfair way for personal benefit.","zh":"twist something to one’s advantage 指以扭曲或不公平方式利用某事來取得個人利益。"},{"en":"A student may twist a teacher’s flexible rule to his advantage by avoiding all deadlines.","zh":"學生可能扭曲利用老師彈性規則，為自己避開所有限期。"},{"en":"When rules are twisted for advantage, fairness and trust are damaged.","zh":"當規則被扭曲利用來謀利，公平和信任會受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exploiting something in a self-serving way.","zh":"這個短語描述以自利方式利用某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"system cracking","meaning":"操弄制度","examples":[{"en":"“System cracking” means manipulating prison officials and procedures.","zh":"“System cracking” 指操弄監獄官員和程序。"},{"en":"System cracking is the practice of learning how a system works in order to exploit its weaknesses.","zh":"system cracking 指了解制度如何運作，從而利用其弱點的做法。"},{"en":"An inmate may use system cracking by saying what assessors want to hear without truly changing.","zh":"囚犯可能透過說出評估人員想聽的話，而不真正改變，來操弄制度。"},{"en":"If system cracking succeeds, officials may mistake manipulation for rehabilitation.","zh":"如果操弄制度成功，官員可能把操控誤認為更生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gaming or exploiting an institution’s rules.","zh":"這個短語描述鑽空子或利用機構規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cases such as these","meaning":"這類個案","examples":[{"en":"Cases such as these illustrate the limitations of rehabilitation assessments.","zh":"這類個案說明更生評估的局限。"},{"en":"Cases such as these means examples of this kind.","zh":"cases such as these 指這種類型的例子。"},{"en":"Cases such as these show why teachers need to check both homework answers and how students reached them.","zh":"這類個案顯示為何老師需要同時檢查功課答案和學生如何得出答案。"},{"en":"When examples repeat the same problem, they reveal a wider pattern.","zh":"當例子重複同一問題，它們揭示更廣泛的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples that support a general point.","zh":"這個短語引入支持一般觀點的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reveal the biggest problem with","meaning":"揭示……最大的問題","examples":[{"en":"These cases reveal the biggest problem with predicting future behaviour.","zh":"這些個案揭示預測未來行為最大的問題。"},{"en":"To reveal the biggest problem with something means to show its most serious weakness.","zh":"reveal the biggest problem with something 指顯示某事最嚴重的弱點。"},{"en":"A failed online lesson may reveal the biggest problem with relying only on technology: not all students have stable internet.","zh":"失敗的網課可能揭示只依賴科技最大的問題：並非所有學生都有穩定網絡。"},{"en":"Revealing the main problem helps people improve a system rather than defend it blindly.","zh":"揭示主要問題有助人改善制度，而不是盲目維護它。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the central weakness in an approach.","zh":"這個短語指出某方法中的核心弱點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"deepest intentions","meaning":"內心最深層的意圖","examples":[{"en":"It is impossible to observe another person’s deepest intentions directly.","zh":"直接觀察另一個人內心最深層的意圖是不可能的。"},{"en":"Deepest intentions are the hidden motives or plans a person truly has inside.","zh":"deepest intentions 指一個人內心真正擁有的隱藏動機或計劃。"},{"en":"A person may smile politely while their deepest intentions remain unknown.","zh":"一個人可能禮貌地微笑，但其內心最深層的意圖仍然未知。"},{"en":"Because intentions are internal, outsiders must infer them from words, behaviour, and patterns.","zh":"因為意圖屬於內在，外人必須從說話、行為和模式推斷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes motives that are private and hard to judge.","zh":"這個短語描述私密而難以判斷的動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"read someone’s intentions","meaning":"看穿某人的意圖","examples":[{"en":"Even trained professionals may struggle to read an offender’s intentions.","zh":"即使受過訓練的專業人士，也可能難以看穿罪犯的意圖。"},{"en":"To read someone’s intentions means to understand what the person really plans or wants.","zh":"read someone’s intentions 指理解某人真正計劃或想要甚麼。"},{"en":"A teacher may try to read a student’s intentions when the student says he forgot homework again.","zh":"當學生再次說忘記功課，老師可能嘗試看穿他的意圖。"},{"en":"It is hard to read intentions because people can lie, hide feelings, or behave strategically.","zh":"看穿意圖很難，因為人可以說謊、隱藏感受或策略性行事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes judging hidden motives from visible clues.","zh":"這個短語描述從可見線索判斷隱藏動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"nevertheless","meaning":"儘管如此","examples":[{"en":"Nevertheless, most inmates will eventually be released.","zh":"儘管如此，大多數囚犯最終都會獲釋。"},{"en":"Nevertheless means however, despite what has just been said.","zh":"nevertheless 指然而；儘管剛才所說如此。"},{"en":"The exam is difficult; nevertheless, careful revision can improve performance.","zh":"考試很難；儘管如此，仔細溫習可以改善表現。"},{"en":"This word helps show contrast between a problem and what still remains true.","zh":"這個詞幫助顯示問題與仍然成立的事實之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when admitting a difficulty before continuing the argument.","zh":"當先承認困難再繼續論證時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"need assistance with","meaning":"在……方面需要協助","examples":[{"en":"Released inmates may need assistance with housing and employment.","zh":"獲釋囚犯可能在住所和就業方面需要協助。"},{"en":"To need assistance with something means to require help in that area.","zh":"need assistance with something 指在某方面需要幫助。"},{"en":"A new student may need assistance with choosing subjects and finding classrooms.","zh":"新學生可能在選科和找課室方面需要協助。"},{"en":"People leaving prison may need practical help because daily life outside has changed.","zh":"離開監獄的人可能需要實際幫助，因為外面的日常生活已經改變。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the specific area where support is needed.","zh":"這個短語指出需要支援的具體範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"social reintegration","meaning":"重新融入社會","examples":[{"en":"Parole officers support the social reintegration of released offenders.","zh":"假釋官支援獲釋罪犯重新融入社會。"},{"en":"Social reintegration means returning to normal relationships, work, rules, and community life after separation.","zh":"social reintegration 指在分離後回到正常關係、工作、規則和社區生活。"},{"en":"A person may need counselling and family support for successful social reintegration.","zh":"一個人可能需要輔導和家庭支援，才能成功重新融入社會。"},{"en":"Without social reintegration, release from prison may not lead to a stable life.","zh":"如果沒有社會重新融入，離開監獄未必能帶來穩定生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the social side of returning to society.","zh":"這個短語描述重返社會中的社會層面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be most commonly done through","meaning":"最常透過……進行","examples":[{"en":"Supervised reintegration is most commonly done through parole.","zh":"受監督的重新融入最常透過假釋進行。"},{"en":"To be most commonly done through something means that method is the usual way it is carried out.","zh":"be most commonly done through something 指某事通常透過某方法進行。"},{"en":"School notices are most commonly sent through email when parents check messages regularly.","zh":"如果家長定期查看訊息，學校通知最常透過電郵發出。"},{"en":"A common method is not always perfect, but it is the one most often used.","zh":"常用方法不一定完美，但它是最常被使用的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the usual channel or method.","zh":"這個短語指出通常的渠道或方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"parole","meaning":"假釋","examples":[{"en":"Parole allows an offender to serve part of a sentence in the community.","zh":"假釋容許罪犯在社區中服部分刑期。"},{"en":"Parole is conditional release from prison before the full sentence has ended.","zh":"parole 指在完整刑期結束前有條件地從監獄釋放。"},{"en":"A person on parole may live outside prison but must report to a parole officer.","zh":"假釋人士可以住在監獄外，但必須向假釋官報到。"},{"en":"If parole conditions are broken, the person may be returned to prison.","zh":"如果違反假釋條件，該人可能被送回監獄。"},{"en":"This word describes supervised early release, not complete freedom.","zh":"這個詞描述受監督的提早釋放，而不是完全自由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"serve the remainder of a sentence","meaning":"服完餘下刑期","examples":[{"en":"A prisoner on parole serves the remainder of the sentence outside prison.","zh":"假釋囚犯在監獄外服完餘下刑期。"},{"en":"To serve the remainder of a sentence means to complete the part of the punishment that is still left.","zh":"serve the remainder of a sentence 指完成仍然剩下的那部分懲罰。"},{"en":"If someone has two years left, parole may allow them to serve the remainder under supervision in the community.","zh":"如果某人還有兩年刑期，假釋可能容許他在社區監督下服完餘下刑期。"},{"en":"The sentence continues even though the person is no longer inside prison.","zh":"即使該人不再身處監獄，刑期仍然繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finishing the unused part of a legal punishment.","zh":"這個短語描述完成法律懲罰中未服完的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"outside prison","meaning":"在監獄以外","examples":[{"en":"Parole allows part of the sentence to be served outside prison.","zh":"假釋容許部分刑期在監獄以外服完。"},{"en":"Outside prison means in the community rather than inside a prison building.","zh":"outside prison 指在社區中，而不是在監獄建築內。"},{"en":"A person outside prison may still face strict rules if released on parole.","zh":"在監獄以外的人如果是假釋獲釋，仍可能面對嚴格規則。"},{"en":"Living outside prison can help reintegration, but it also requires responsibility.","zh":"在監獄以外生活可以幫助重新融入，但也需要責任感。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts community life with imprisonment.","zh":"這個短語把社區生活與監禁作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be different from","meaning":"與……不同","examples":[{"en":"Parole is different from probation.","zh":"假釋與感化令不同。"},{"en":"To be different from something means not to be the same as it.","zh":"be different from something 指與某事物並不相同。"},{"en":"Online learning is different from classroom learning because students need more self-discipline.","zh":"網上學習與課室學習不同，因為學生需要更多自律。"},{"en":"Explaining differences helps readers avoid confusing similar terms.","zh":"解釋差異有助讀者避免混淆相似詞語。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces contrast between two things.","zh":"這個短語引入兩件事之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"probation","meaning":"感化令；緩刑監管","examples":[{"en":"Probation is a community-based alternative to imprisonment.","zh":"感化令是以社區為本、代替監禁的安排。"},{"en":"Probation is a court order that allows an offender to remain in the community under conditions and supervision.","zh":"probation 指法院命令罪犯在條件和監督下留在社區。"},{"en":"A person on probation may have to meet an officer, attend treatment, and obey rules.","zh":"接受感化令的人可能必須見感化主任、接受治療並遵守規則。"},{"en":"If probation conditions are broken, the court may impose a stronger penalty.","zh":"如果違反感化令條件，法院可能施加更嚴厲懲罰。"},{"en":"This word describes supervised punishment in the community instead of prison.","zh":"這個詞描述在社區中受監督的懲罰，而不是監禁。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be used instead of","meaning":"被用來代替……","examples":[{"en":"Probation may be used instead of a prison sentence.","zh":"感化令可能被用來代替監禁刑罰。"},{"en":"To be used instead of something means to replace it with another option.","zh":"be used instead of something 指用另一選項取代某物。"},{"en":"A video call may be used instead of a face-to-face meeting when people live far apart.","zh":"當人們住得很遠，視像通話可能被用來代替面對面會議。"},{"en":"Alternatives are chosen when they may achieve the goal with fewer costs or harms.","zh":"當替代方案能以較少成本或傷害達成目標，人們會選擇它。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly shows replacement.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示取代關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"prison sentence","meaning":"監禁刑罰","examples":[{"en":"The judge imposed probation instead of a prison sentence.","zh":"法官判處感化令，而不是監禁刑罰。"},{"en":"A prison sentence is a punishment requiring someone to spend time in prison.","zh":"prison sentence 指要求某人在監獄中度過一段時間的懲罰。"},{"en":"A serious offence may lead to a prison sentence if the court decides community punishment is not enough.","zh":"如果法院認為社區懲罰不足，嚴重罪行可能導致監禁刑罰。"},{"en":"Prison sentences remove liberty and can affect family, employment, and future opportunities.","zh":"監禁刑罰剝奪自由，並可能影響家庭、就業和未來機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes imprisonment ordered by a court.","zh":"這個短語描述由法院命令的監禁。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"place greater restrictions on","meaning":"對……施加更多限制","examples":[{"en":"Probation may place greater restrictions on the offender than parole.","zh":"感化令可能比假釋對罪犯施加更多限制。"},{"en":"To place greater restrictions on someone means to set stricter rules controlling what they can do.","zh":"place greater restrictions on someone 指設定更嚴格規則來控制某人可以做甚麼。"},{"en":"A school may place greater restrictions on phone use after students misuse phones in class.","zh":"學生在課堂濫用手機後，學校可能對手機使用施加更多限制。"},{"en":"Greater restrictions can improve safety but may also limit freedom.","zh":"更多限制可以提高安全，但也可能限制自由。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stronger control over behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述對行為更強的控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the person concerned","meaning":"有關人士","examples":[{"en":"The person concerned must obey all conditions of the order.","zh":"有關人士必須遵守命令中的所有條件。"},{"en":"The person concerned means the specific person being discussed or affected.","zh":"person concerned 指正在被討論或受影響的特定人士。"},{"en":"If a complaint is made about a staff member, the person concerned should be allowed to respond.","zh":"如果有人投訴某員工，有關人士應被允許回應。"},{"en":"This phrase helps avoid repeating a name while keeping the focus clear.","zh":"這個短語有助避免重複姓名，同時保持焦點清楚。"},{"en":"It is often used in formal writing about rules, cases, or decisions.","zh":"它常用於關於規則、個案或決定的正式寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"supervised release","meaning":"監督釋放","examples":[{"en":"Supervised release begins after the full prison sentence has been served.","zh":"監督釋放在完整監禁刑期服完後開始。"},{"en":"Supervised release is a period after imprisonment when a person lives in the community under official monitoring.","zh":"supervised release 指監禁後某人在官方監察下生活於社區的一段時期。"},{"en":"Someone on supervised release may have to report regularly and avoid certain people or places.","zh":"接受監督釋放的人可能必須定期報到，並避開某些人或地方。"},{"en":"Supervision aims to reduce risk while helping the person adjust to ordinary life.","zh":"監督旨在降低風險，同時幫助該人適應一般生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes monitored freedom after prison.","zh":"這個短語描述監獄後受監察的自由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"face the same restrictions as","meaning":"面對與……相同的限制","examples":[{"en":"A person on supervised release may face the same restrictions as someone on probation.","zh":"接受監督釋放的人可能面對與感化令人士相同的限制。"},{"en":"To face the same restrictions as someone means to be subject to similar rules or limits.","zh":"face the same restrictions as someone 指受到類似規則或限制約束。"},{"en":"New drivers may face the same restrictions as learner drivers in some situations.","zh":"新手司機在某些情況下可能面對與學車人士相同的限制。"},{"en":"Similar restrictions can make different legal arrangements feel alike in daily life.","zh":"類似限制可以令不同法律安排在日常生活中感覺相似。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the limits placed on two people or groups.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個人或群體所受限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"serve the entire sentence","meaning":"服完整段刑期","examples":[{"en":"The offender served the entire prison sentence before supervised release began.","zh":"該罪犯在監督釋放開始前服完整段監禁刑期。"},{"en":"To serve the entire sentence means to complete the whole period of punishment ordered by the court.","zh":"serve the entire sentence 指完成法院命令的整段懲罰期限。"},{"en":"If a person receives a five-year sentence and serves all five years, they have served the entire sentence.","zh":"如果某人被判五年並服滿五年，他就是服完整段刑期。"},{"en":"Serving the whole sentence is different from early release on parole.","zh":"服完整段刑期與假釋提早釋放不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes completing the full legal punishment.","zh":"這個短語描述完成全部法律懲罰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"whatever the arrangement","meaning":"無論採用哪種安排","examples":[{"en":"Whatever the arrangement, the released offender will be monitored.","zh":"無論採用哪種安排，獲釋罪犯都會受到監察。"},{"en":"Whatever the arrangement means no matter which system or plan is used.","zh":"whatever the arrangement 指無論使用哪種制度或計劃。"},{"en":"Whatever the arrangement, students must still submit their work before the deadline.","zh":"無論採用哪種安排，學生仍必須在限期前交功課。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one result remains true across different options.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個結果在不同選項下仍然成立。"},{"en":"It is useful when the details vary but the main rule stays the same.","zh":"當細節不同但主要規則相同時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"parole officer","meaning":"假釋官","examples":[{"en":"A parole officer monitors and supports released inmates.","zh":"假釋官監察並支援獲釋囚犯。"},{"en":"A parole officer is an official who supervises people released from prison under parole conditions.","zh":"parole officer 指監督按假釋條件獲釋者的官員。"},{"en":"A parole officer may check whether a person has found work and is obeying curfew rules.","zh":"假釋官可能檢查某人是否找到工作並遵守宵禁規則。"},{"en":"Good parole officers combine monitoring with practical support.","zh":"好的假釋官會結合監察和實際支援。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the official responsible for supervising parolees.","zh":"這個短語指負責監督假釋人士的官員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"monitor a released inmate","meaning":"監察獲釋囚犯","examples":[{"en":"The parole officer regularly monitors the released inmate.","zh":"假釋官定期監察獲釋囚犯。"},{"en":"To monitor a released inmate means to watch, check, and record whether a former prisoner follows release conditions.","zh":"monitor a released inmate 指觀察、檢查並記錄前囚犯是否遵守釋放條件。"},{"en":"A parole officer may monitor a released inmate through meetings, home visits, and reports from employers.","zh":"假釋官可能透過會面、家訪和僱主報告來監察獲釋囚犯。"},{"en":"Monitoring can protect the public and help identify problems early.","zh":"監察可以保護公眾，並及早發現問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official supervision after release.","zh":"這個短語描述獲釋後的官方監督。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"offer support and assistance","meaning":"提供支援和協助","examples":[{"en":"Parole officers offer support and assistance wherever possible.","zh":"假釋官在可行情況下提供支援和協助。"},{"en":"To offer support and assistance means to provide help, guidance, or practical resources.","zh":"offer support and assistance 指提供幫助、指導或實際資源。"},{"en":"A school counsellor may offer support and assistance to students facing family problems.","zh":"學校輔導員可能向面對家庭問題的學生提供支援和協助。"},{"en":"Support can make rules easier to follow because people are not left to struggle alone.","zh":"支援可以令規則更容易遵守，因為人們不會被留下獨自掙扎。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active help, not only supervision.","zh":"這個短語描述主動幫助，而不只是監督。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"wherever possible","meaning":"在可行情況下","examples":[{"en":"Officials try to assist released offenders wherever possible.","zh":"官員在可行情況下嘗試協助獲釋罪犯。"},{"en":"Wherever possible means whenever and wherever it can reasonably be done.","zh":"wherever possible 指在合理可行的任何時間和地方。"},{"en":"Teachers give students extra examples wherever possible when a topic is difficult.","zh":"當主題困難，老師會在可行情況下給學生額外例子。"},{"en":"This phrase shows willingness to help within practical limits.","zh":"這個短語顯示願意在實際限制內提供幫助。"},{"en":"It is useful when support depends on available time, resources, or authority.","zh":"當支援取決於可用時間、資源或權限時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"grant parole","meaning":"批准假釋","examples":[{"en":"A parole board decides whether to grant parole.","zh":"假釋委員會決定是否批准假釋。"},{"en":"To grant parole means to officially allow a prisoner to be released under parole conditions.","zh":"grant parole 指正式容許囚犯按假釋條件獲釋。"},{"en":"A board may grant parole if the inmate has behaved well and has a stable release plan.","zh":"如果囚犯表現良好並有穩定釋放計劃，委員會可能批准假釋。"},{"en":"If parole is granted, the prisoner is not completely free but must follow conditions.","zh":"如果假釋獲批，囚犯並非完全自由，而是必須遵守條件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the official approval of conditional release.","zh":"這個短語描述有條件釋放的正式批准。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lie with","meaning":"由……負責決定","examples":[{"en":"The final decision usually lies with a parole board.","zh":"最終決定通常由假釋委員會負責。"},{"en":"To lie with someone means that responsibility or authority belongs to that person or group.","zh":"lie with someone 指責任或權力屬於某人或某群體。"},{"en":"In a school, the final decision on suspension may lie with the principal.","zh":"在學校，停學的最終決定可能由校長負責。"},{"en":"When responsibility lies with a board, its members must justify their decision carefully.","zh":"當責任由委員會承擔，其成員必須謹慎解釋決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where decision-making power rests.","zh":"這個短語描述決策權所在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"parole board","meaning":"假釋委員會","examples":[{"en":"A parole board reviews an inmate’s suitability for early release.","zh":"假釋委員會審視囚犯是否適合提早獲釋。"},{"en":"A parole board is a group that decides whether a prisoner should be released on parole.","zh":"parole board 指決定囚犯是否應獲假釋的團體。"},{"en":"The board may consider prison behaviour, risk, remorse, housing, and employment.","zh":"委員會可能考慮監獄行為、風險、悔意、住所和就業。"},{"en":"Its decision can affect both the offender’s future and public safety.","zh":"其決定可以影響罪犯未來和公共安全。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the official body that makes parole decisions.","zh":"這個短語指作出假釋決定的官方機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"appointed citizens","meaning":"獲委任的市民","examples":[{"en":"Some parole boards include appointed citizens from the local community.","zh":"有些假釋委員會包括來自本地社區的獲委任市民。"},{"en":"Appointed citizens are members of the public chosen officially to serve a role.","zh":"appointed citizens 指被正式選中擔任某角色的公眾成員。"},{"en":"A city committee may include appointed citizens who represent community concerns.","zh":"城市委員會可能包括代表社區關注的獲委任市民。"},{"en":"Appointing citizens can bring public values into official decision-making.","zh":"委任市民可以把公共價值帶入官方決策。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordinary people selected for formal responsibility.","zh":"這個短語描述被選中承擔正式責任的普通人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"local community","meaning":"本地社區","examples":[{"en":"Community representatives may serve on a parole board.","zh":"社區代表可能在假釋委員會服務。"},{"en":"The local community is the people living in a particular area.","zh":"local community 指生活在某特定地區的人。"},{"en":"A local community may include families, schools, shops, religious groups, and public services.","zh":"本地社區可能包括家庭、學校、商店、宗教團體和公共服務。"},{"en":"Community involvement can make decisions feel more connected to real public concerns.","zh":"社區參與可以令決定更連接真實公共關注。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people and organisations in a nearby area.","zh":"這個短語指附近地區的人和組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the common factor","meaning":"共同因素","examples":[{"en":"The common factor is that board members are well educated.","zh":"共同因素是委員會成員都受過良好教育。"},{"en":"The common factor is the shared feature found in several people, cases, or situations.","zh":"common factor 指多個人、個案或情況中共有的特徵。"},{"en":"In several successful students, the common factor may be regular practice rather than natural talent.","zh":"在幾名成功學生身上，共同因素可能是定期練習，而不是天生才能。"},{"en":"Finding the common factor helps people understand what different examples have in common.","zh":"找出共同因素幫助人理解不同例子有甚麼共同之處。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the shared element across a group.","zh":"這個短語指出一個群體中的共有元素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be well educated","meaning":"受過良好教育","examples":[{"en":"Parole-board members are generally expected to be well educated.","zh":"假釋委員會成員一般被期望受過良好教育。"},{"en":"To be well educated means to have received a good level of learning and knowledge.","zh":"be well educated 指接受過良好程度的學習並具備知識。"},{"en":"A well-educated person should be able to read evidence carefully and think critically.","zh":"受過良好教育的人應能仔細閱讀證據並批判思考。"},{"en":"Education may help board members understand reports, risks, and legal responsibilities.","zh":"教育可能幫助委員會成員理解報告、風險和法律責任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong educational background, not simply politeness.","zh":"這個短語描述良好教育背景，而不只是有禮貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be of high moral standing","meaning":"具有崇高品格","examples":[{"en":"Board members are expected to be of high moral standing.","zh":"委員會成員被期望具有崇高品格。"},{"en":"To be of high moral standing means to be widely trusted as honest, fair, and responsible.","zh":"be of high moral standing 指被廣泛信任為誠實、公平和負責任。"},{"en":"A community leader of high moral standing is trusted because people believe she acts fairly.","zh":"具有崇高品格的社區領袖受到信任，因為人們相信她行事公平。"},{"en":"Moral standing matters when a role involves judging other people’s behaviour.","zh":"當某角色涉及判斷他人行為，道德聲望就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes respected moral character.","zh":"這個短語描述受尊重的道德品格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"psychological state","meaning":"心理狀態","examples":[{"en":"The board attempts to assess the inmate’s psychological state.","zh":"委員會嘗試評估囚犯的心理狀態。"},{"en":"Psychological state means a person’s mental and emotional condition at a particular time.","zh":"psychological state 指某人在特定時間的心理和情緒狀況。"},{"en":"A counsellor may check a student’s psychological state after a serious family problem.","zh":"學生遇到嚴重家庭問題後，輔導員可能檢視他的心理狀態。"},{"en":"Stress, fear, remorse, anger, or calmness can all affect someone’s psychological state.","zh":"壓力、恐懼、悔意、憤怒或平靜都可以影響人的心理狀態。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inner mental condition.","zh":"這個短語描述內在心理狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"intentions that lie within","meaning":"隱藏在內心的意圖","examples":[{"en":"It is difficult to know what intentions lie within another person.","zh":"要知道另一個人內心隱藏着甚麼意圖是困難的。"},{"en":"Intentions that lie within are motives or plans hidden inside a person’s mind.","zh":"intentions that lie within 指藏在一個人心中的動機或計劃。"},{"en":"A quiet student may seem calm, but the intentions that lie within may be hard to know.","zh":"安靜的學生可能看似平靜，但隱藏在內心的意圖可能難以知道。"},{"en":"Because hidden intentions cannot be seen directly, decisions must rely on behaviour and evidence.","zh":"因為隱藏意圖不能被直接看見，決定必須依賴行為和證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes private motives that are not immediately visible.","zh":"這個短語描述不會立即可見的私人動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"problematic at best","meaning":"最樂觀地說也是有問題的","examples":[{"en":"Predicting an offender’s future conduct is problematic at best.","zh":"預測罪犯未來行為，最樂觀地說也是有問題的。"},{"en":"Problematic at best means that even in the most favourable view, something still has serious difficulties.","zh":"problematic at best 指即使從最有利角度看，某事仍有嚴重困難。"},{"en":"Judging a student’s whole ability from one test is problematic at best.","zh":"只用一次測驗判斷學生整體能力，最樂觀地說也是有問題的。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a method is uncertain, weak, or risky even when handled carefully.","zh":"這個短語提醒人，即使處理謹慎，某方法仍不確定、薄弱或有風險。"},{"en":"It is used when confidence should be limited.","zh":"當信心應受限制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"good conduct","meaning":"良好行為","examples":[{"en":"Good conduct in prison is an important condition for parole.","zh":"監獄中的良好行為是假釋的重要條件。"},{"en":"Good conduct means behaving responsibly, peacefully, and according to rules.","zh":"good conduct 指負責任、和平並按規則行事。"},{"en":"A student shows good conduct by respecting classmates and following classroom rules.","zh":"學生透過尊重同學和遵守課堂規則來表現良好行為。"},{"en":"Good conduct can build trust because it shows a pattern of self-control.","zh":"良好行為可以建立信任，因為它顯示自我控制的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes behaviour judged positively by an institution.","zh":"這個短語描述被機構正面評價的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the most obvious prerequisite","meaning":"最明顯的先決條件","examples":[{"en":"Good conduct is the most obvious prerequisite for early release.","zh":"良好行為是提早獲釋最明顯的先決條件。"},{"en":"The most obvious prerequisite is the clearest condition that must be met first.","zh":"most obvious prerequisite 指最清楚、必須先符合的條件。"},{"en":"Regular attendance is the most obvious prerequisite for doing well in a course.","zh":"定期出席是課程中表現良好最明顯的先決條件。"},{"en":"If a prerequisite is missing, later benefits may not be considered.","zh":"如果缺少先決條件，之後的好處可能不會被考慮。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the basic requirement that is hardest to ignore.","zh":"這個短語指出最基本且最難忽視的要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"support networks","meaning":"支援網絡","examples":[{"en":"Strong support networks can help an offender avoid reoffending.","zh":"強大的支援網絡可以幫助罪犯避免再犯。"},{"en":"Support networks are people, services, and organisations that provide help and guidance.","zh":"support networks 指提供幫助和指導的人、服務和組織。"},{"en":"A student’s support network may include family, teachers, friends, and counsellors.","zh":"學生的支援網絡可能包括家人、老師、朋友和輔導員。"},{"en":"Support networks reduce isolation and make it easier to handle problems safely.","zh":"支援網絡減少孤立，並令人更容易安全地處理問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the web of help around a person.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞一個人的幫助網絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"exist outside prison","meaning":"存在於監獄以外","examples":[{"en":"The board considers the support networks that exist outside prison.","zh":"委員會考慮存在於監獄以外的支援網絡。"},{"en":"To exist outside prison means to be available in the community rather than inside the prison system.","zh":"exist outside prison 指在社區中可取得，而不是在監獄制度內。"},{"en":"Family, employers, housing services, and counsellors may exist outside prison as support.","zh":"家人、僱主、房屋服務和輔導員都可能作為監獄以外的支援。"},{"en":"If no support exists outside prison, release may be riskier.","zh":"如果監獄以外沒有支援，釋放可能更有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts community resources with prison-based resources.","zh":"這個短語把社區資源與監獄內資源作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"play a role","meaning":"發揮作用","examples":[{"en":"Family support and employment also play a role in parole decisions.","zh":"家庭支援和就業也在假釋決定中發揮作用。"},{"en":"To play a role means to have some influence or part in a result.","zh":"play a role 指對結果有某種影響或參與其中。"},{"en":"Sleep, practice, and confidence all play a role in exam performance.","zh":"睡眠、練習和信心都在考試表現中發揮作用。"},{"en":"A factor may play a role even if it is not the only cause.","zh":"即使某因素不是唯一原因，它仍可能發揮作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes contribution to an outcome.","zh":"這個短語描述對結果的貢獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"establish a permanent residence","meaning":"確立固定住所","examples":[{"en":"An offender may need to establish a permanent residence before release.","zh":"罪犯可能需要在獲釋前確立固定住所。"},{"en":"To establish a permanent residence means to secure a stable place to live for the long term.","zh":"establish a permanent residence 指取得一個長期穩定居住的地方。"},{"en":"A person leaving prison may establish a permanent residence with family or in supported housing.","zh":"離開監獄的人可能與家人同住或住進支援房屋，以確立固定住所。"},{"en":"Stable housing can reduce stress and make supervision easier.","zh":"穩定住所可以減少壓力，並令監督更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes setting up a fixed home.","zh":"這個短語描述建立固定居所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"permanent residence","meaning":"固定住所","examples":[{"en":"A permanent residence provides stability after release.","zh":"固定住所為獲釋後提供穩定。"},{"en":"A permanent residence is a fixed and stable place where someone lives.","zh":"permanent residence 指某人居住的固定而穩定的地方。"},{"en":"A person without a permanent residence may find it harder to receive letters, attend appointments, or keep a job.","zh":"沒有固定住所的人可能較難收信、出席預約或保住工作。"},{"en":"Permanent residence matters because housing stability supports routine and responsibility.","zh":"固定住所重要，因為住屋穩定支援日常規律和責任感。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a lasting home address, not temporary shelter.","zh":"這個短語指長期住址，而不是臨時庇護所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"gain employment","meaning":"找到工作","examples":[{"en":"Having gained employment may improve an inmate’s chance of parole.","zh":"已找到工作可能改善囚犯獲假釋的機會。"},{"en":"To gain employment means to get a job.","zh":"gain employment 指找到工作。"},{"en":"A former prisoner may gain employment through a training programme and a supportive employer.","zh":"前囚犯可能透過訓練計劃和願意支援的僱主找到工作。"},{"en":"Employment can provide income, structure, and a reason to avoid criminal activity.","zh":"就業可以提供收入、規律和避免犯罪活動的理由。"},{"en":"This phrase describes successfully entering work.","zh":"這個短語描述成功進入工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be mandatory","meaning":"是強制要求","examples":[{"en":"Stable housing and employment may be mandatory conditions of parole.","zh":"穩定住所和就業可能是假釋的強制條件。"},{"en":"To be mandatory means to be required by rule or law.","zh":"be mandatory 指按規則或法律必須做。"},{"en":"Wearing a seat belt is mandatory in many places.","zh":"在許多地方，佩戴安全帶是強制要求。"},{"en":"If a condition is mandatory, ignoring it can lead to penalties or loss of permission.","zh":"如果某條件是強制的，無視它可能導致懲罰或失去許可。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that is not optional.","zh":"這個短語描述非選擇性的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be released on parole","meaning":"獲假釋","examples":[{"en":"The inmate was released on parole after serving most of the sentence.","zh":"該囚犯在服完大部分刑期後獲假釋。"},{"en":"To be released on parole means to leave prison early under official conditions and supervision.","zh":"be released on parole 指在官方條件和監督下提早離開監獄。"},{"en":"A prisoner released on parole may have to report weekly to a parole officer.","zh":"獲假釋的囚犯可能必須每週向假釋官報到。"},{"en":"If the person breaks parole conditions, release may be cancelled.","zh":"如果該人違反假釋條件，釋放可能被取消。"},{"en":"This phrase describes conditional freedom before the sentence is fully finished.","zh":"這個短語描述刑期完全結束前的有條件自由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"regulatory conditions","meaning":"監管條件","examples":[{"en":"A person on parole must meet a variety of regulatory conditions.","zh":"假釋人士必須符合多種監管條件。"},{"en":"Regulatory conditions are official rules that control what a person must or must not do.","zh":"regulatory conditions 指控制某人必須做或不得做甚麼的官方規則。"},{"en":"A licence may include regulatory conditions such as regular inspections and safety reports.","zh":"牌照可能包括定期檢查和安全報告等監管條件。"},{"en":"Conditions help authorities monitor behaviour and manage risk.","zh":"條件幫助當局監察行為和管理風險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal rules attached to permission or release.","zh":"這個短語指附加於許可或釋放的正式規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"conditions to be met","meaning":"必須符合的條件","examples":[{"en":"Several conditions must be met throughout the parole period.","zh":"整個假釋期內有幾項條件必須符合。"},{"en":"Conditions to be met are requirements that must be satisfied.","zh":"conditions to be met 指必須達成的要求。"},{"en":"A student scholarship may have conditions to be met, such as attendance and passing grades.","zh":"學生獎學金可能有必須符合的條件，例如出席率和合格成績。"},{"en":"If required conditions are not met, benefits or permission may be lost.","zh":"如果沒有符合必要條件，福利或許可可能會失去。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rules that must be fulfilled.","zh":"這個短語描述必須履行的規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"obey the law","meaning":"遵守法律","examples":[{"en":"A person on parole must continue to obey the law.","zh":"假釋人士必須繼續遵守法律。"},{"en":"To obey the law means to follow legal rules and avoid illegal actions.","zh":"obey the law 指遵循法律規則並避免違法行為。"},{"en":"Drivers obey the law when they stop at red lights and follow speed limits.","zh":"司機在紅燈停車並遵守速度限制時，就是遵守法律。"},{"en":"Obeying the law is especially important for people under supervision because violations may have serious consequences.","zh":"對受監督的人來說，守法尤其重要，因為違反可能有嚴重後果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lawful behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述合法行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at specified intervals","meaning":"按指定時間間隔","examples":[{"en":"The offender must contact the parole officer at specified intervals.","zh":"該罪犯必須按指定時間間隔聯絡假釋官。"},{"en":"At specified intervals means at clearly stated regular times or periods.","zh":"at specified intervals 指在清楚列明的定期時間或時段。"},{"en":"A patient may take medicine at specified intervals, such as every six hours.","zh":"病人可能按指定時間間隔服藥，例如每六小時一次。"},{"en":"Regular contact helps officers notice problems before they become serious.","zh":"定期聯絡幫助官員在問題變嚴重前發現它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fixed schedule for repeated action.","zh":"這個短語描述重複行動的固定時間表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"individual and specific","meaning":"因人而異且具體的","examples":[{"en":"Some parole conditions are individual and specific.","zh":"有些假釋條件是因人而異且具體的。"},{"en":"Individual and specific means tailored to one person’s particular situation rather than general for everyone.","zh":"individual and specific 指按某人的特定情況量身制定，而不是人人通用。"},{"en":"A student’s learning plan may be individual and specific if it targets her reading weakness.","zh":"如果學生的學習計劃針對她的閱讀弱點，它就是因人而異且具體的。"},{"en":"Specific conditions can address special risks, such as addiction, violent contacts, or curfew needs.","zh":"具體條件可以處理特殊風險，例如成癮、暴力接觸或宵禁需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rules designed for a particular case.","zh":"這個短語描述為特定個案設計的規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"non-use of drugs and alcohol","meaning":"禁止吸毒及飲酒","examples":[{"en":"The conditions may require the non-use of drugs and alcohol.","zh":"條件可能要求禁止吸毒及飲酒。"},{"en":"Non-use of drugs and alcohol means not taking illegal drugs and not drinking alcohol.","zh":"non-use of drugs and alcohol 指不吸食非法毒品，也不飲酒。"},{"en":"A person recovering from addiction may agree to the non-use of drugs and alcohol as part of treatment.","zh":"正在戒癮的人可能同意禁止吸毒及飲酒，作為治療的一部分。"},{"en":"This condition can reduce risk when substance use is linked to offending.","zh":"當物質使用與犯罪有關，這條件可以降低風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rule requiring complete avoidance of substances.","zh":"這個短語描述要求完全避免使用物質的規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"return home before a certain time","meaning":"在指定時間前回家","examples":[{"en":"The offender may be required to return home before a certain time.","zh":"該罪犯可能被要求在指定時間前回家。"},{"en":"To return home before a certain time means to be back at one’s residence by a set deadline.","zh":"return home before a certain time 指在設定限時前回到住所。"},{"en":"A teenager may have to return home before 10 p.m. on school nights.","zh":"青少年可能要在上學日晚上十時前回家。"},{"en":"Time limits help supervisors know where a person should be during risky hours.","zh":"時間限制幫助監督者知道某人在高風險時段應身處何處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a curfew-style requirement.","zh":"這個短語描述類似宵禁的要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"curfew","meaning":"宵禁；指定回家時間","examples":[{"en":"A curfew requires a person to be at home by a predetermined time.","zh":"宵禁要求一個人在預先指定時間前留在家中。"},{"en":"A curfew is a rule requiring someone to stay home or avoid being outside during certain hours.","zh":"curfew 指要求某人在某些時段留在家中或避免外出的規則。"},{"en":"Parents may set a curfew so a child returns home before it gets too late.","zh":"家長可能設定指定回家時間，讓孩子不要太晚回家。"},{"en":"In parole, curfews help monitor behaviour and reduce risky night-time activity.","zh":"在假釋中，宵禁幫助監察行為並減少夜間高風險活動。"},{"en":"This word describes a time-based restriction on movement.","zh":"這個詞描述基於時間的行動限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"breach a condition","meaning":"違反條件","examples":[{"en":"An offender may be arrested for breaching a parole condition.","zh":"罪犯可能因違反假釋條件而被拘捕。"},{"en":"To breach a condition means to break a rule or fail to meet a requirement.","zh":"breach a condition 指違反規則或未能符合要求。"},{"en":"A student breaches a scholarship condition if she stops attending required classes.","zh":"如果學生停止出席必修課，她就是違反獎學金條件。"},{"en":"Breaching conditions can lead to warnings, penalties, or loss of permission.","zh":"違反條件可能導致警告、懲罰或失去許可。"},{"en":"This phrase describes violation of an agreed or official rule.","zh":"這個短語描述違反已同意或官方規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ignore a condition","meaning":"無視；違反條件","examples":[{"en":"Ignoring any parole condition may lead to arrest.","zh":"無視任何假釋條件都可能導致拘捕。"},{"en":"To ignore a condition means to fail to follow a rule, either deliberately or carelessly.","zh":"ignore a condition 指有意或粗心地不遵守某條規則。"},{"en":"A worker ignores a safety condition if he removes protective equipment during work.","zh":"如果工人在工作期間移除防護裝備，他就是無視安全條件。"},{"en":"Ignoring conditions can make authorities think the person is not taking responsibility seriously.","zh":"無視條件可能令當局認為該人沒有認真承擔責任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disregarding a required rule.","zh":"這個短語描述漠視必須遵守的規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"arrest warrant","meaning":"拘捕令","examples":[{"en":"An arrest warrant may be issued after a serious parole violation.","zh":"嚴重違反假釋後，可能會發出拘捕令。"},{"en":"An arrest warrant is an official order allowing police to arrest a person.","zh":"arrest warrant 指容許警方拘捕某人的正式命令。"},{"en":"A court may issue an arrest warrant if someone fails to attend a required hearing.","zh":"如果某人未有出席指定聆訊，法院可能發出拘捕令。"},{"en":"Once a warrant exists, the person may be taken into custody by police.","zh":"一旦有拘捕令，該人可能被警方拘留。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal legal permission to arrest someone.","zh":"這個短語描述拘捕某人的正式法律許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be issued","meaning":"被發出","examples":[{"en":"An arrest warrant is issued when a parolee breaches certain conditions.","zh":"當假釋人士違反某些條件時，拘捕令會被發出。"},{"en":"To be issued means to be officially given, published, or authorised.","zh":"be issued 指被正式給予、公布或授權。"},{"en":"A school warning may be issued after repeated rule-breaking.","zh":"在反覆違規後，學校警告可能被發出。"},{"en":"Once an official document is issued, it usually has formal force.","zh":"一旦正式文件被發出，它通常具有正式效力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal release of an order, notice, or document.","zh":"這個短語描述命令、通知或文件的正式發布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"parole period","meaning":"假釋期","examples":[{"en":"The parole period may be suspended after an alleged violation.","zh":"據稱違規後，假釋期可能被暫停。"},{"en":"The parole period is the time during which a released prisoner remains under parole conditions.","zh":"parole period 指獲釋囚犯仍受假釋條件約束的一段時間。"},{"en":"During the parole period, a person may have to report regularly and obey restrictions.","zh":"在假釋期內，一個人可能必須定期報到並遵守限制。"},{"en":"If rules are broken, the parole period may be interrupted or reviewed.","zh":"如果違反規則，假釋期可能被中斷或檢討。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the supervised time after early release.","zh":"這個短語指提早獲釋後受監督的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be suspended","meaning":"被暫停","examples":[{"en":"Parole time may be suspended while the violation is investigated.","zh":"在違規被調查期間，假釋時間可能被暫停。"},{"en":"To be suspended means to be temporarily stopped.","zh":"be suspended 指被暫時停止。"},{"en":"A student may be suspended from school while a serious incident is investigated.","zh":"在嚴重事件被調查期間，學生可能被暫停上學。"},{"en":"Suspension does not always mean a final decision has been made.","zh":"暫停不一定代表已作出最終決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a pause while authorities review a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述當局檢視問題期間的暫停。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"parole violation hearing","meaning":"違反假釋條件聆訊","examples":[{"en":"A parole violation hearing determines whether the conditions were breached.","zh":"違反假釋條件聆訊判斷條件是否被違反。"},{"en":"A parole violation hearing is a formal meeting or legal process to decide if parole rules were broken.","zh":"parole violation hearing 指用來決定假釋規則是否被違反的正式會議或法律程序。"},{"en":"At the hearing, evidence may be presented about missed appointments, new offences, or curfew breaches.","zh":"在聆訊中，可能會提交關於缺席預約、新罪行或違反宵禁的證據。"},{"en":"The outcome can affect whether parole continues or is revoked.","zh":"結果可以影響假釋是否繼續或被撤銷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the official review after an alleged parole breach.","zh":"這個短語描述據稱違反假釋後的官方檢討。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make a decision about whether","meaning":"決定是否……","examples":[{"en":"The board makes a decision about whether to revoke parole.","zh":"委員會決定是否撤銷假釋。"},{"en":"To make a decision about whether means to choose between doing or not doing something.","zh":"make a decision about whether 指在做與不做某事之間作出選擇。"},{"en":"A teacher may make a decision about whether to give a student extra time.","zh":"老師可能決定是否給學生額外時間。"},{"en":"Such decisions require evidence because the result may seriously affect someone.","zh":"這類決定需要證據，因為結果可能嚴重影響某人。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a yes-or-no decision.","zh":"這個短語引入是與否的決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"revoke parole","meaning":"撤銷假釋","examples":[{"en":"The board may revoke parole after a serious breach.","zh":"委員會可能在嚴重違規後撤銷假釋。"},{"en":"To revoke parole means to officially cancel parole and remove the person’s conditional freedom.","zh":"revoke parole 指正式取消假釋並移除該人的有條件自由。"},{"en":"Parole may be revoked if a person commits a new serious offence.","zh":"如果一個人犯下新的嚴重罪行，假釋可能被撤銷。"},{"en":"Revocation can lead to the person being sent back to prison.","zh":"撤銷可能導致該人被送回監獄。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cancelling early release because conditions were broken.","zh":"這個短語描述因違反條件而取消提早釋放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be reincarcerated","meaning":"再次被監禁","examples":[{"en":"An offender whose parole is revoked may be reincarcerated.","zh":"假釋被撤銷的罪犯可能再次被監禁。"},{"en":"To be reincarcerated means to be put back in prison after release.","zh":"be reincarcerated 指獲釋後再次被送回監獄。"},{"en":"A parolee may be reincarcerated if he repeatedly ignores reporting requirements.","zh":"如果假釋人士反覆無視報到要求，他可能再次被監禁。"},{"en":"Reincarceration shows that conditional freedom has been removed.","zh":"再次監禁顯示有條件自由已被移除。"},{"en":"This phrase describes returning to custody after a failed release.","zh":"這個短語描述釋放失敗後重返羈押。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"allow parole to continue","meaning":"允許假釋繼續","examples":[{"en":"The board may instead allow parole to continue.","zh":"委員會也可能改為允許假釋繼續。"},{"en":"To allow parole to continue means to decide that the person can remain on parole despite a concern or allegation.","zh":"allow parole to continue 指儘管有疑慮或指稱，仍決定讓該人維持假釋狀態。"},{"en":"A board may allow parole to continue if the breach was minor and the person has otherwise complied.","zh":"如果違規輕微且該人其他方面一直遵守，委員會可能允許假釋繼續。"},{"en":"Continuing parole may come with warnings or stricter conditions.","zh":"假釋繼續可能伴隨警告或更嚴格條件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping conditional release in place.","zh":"這個短語描述維持有條件釋放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"not an exact science","meaning":"並非精確科學","examples":[{"en":"Assessing future criminal behaviour is not an exact science.","zh":"評估未來犯罪行為並非精確科學。"},{"en":"Not an exact science means something cannot be predicted or measured with complete certainty.","zh":"not an exact science 指某事不能以完全確定方式預測或量度。"},{"en":"Choosing the best teaching method is not an exact science because students respond differently.","zh":"選擇最佳教學方法並非精確科學，因為學生反應不同。"},{"en":"When something is not exact, judgement and evidence must be used carefully.","zh":"當某事不精確，就必須謹慎使用判斷和證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an area with uncertainty and imperfect prediction.","zh":"這個短語描述有不確定性和不完美預測的範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"mistakes can be made","meaning":"可能會犯錯","examples":[{"en":"Because prediction is uncertain, mistakes can be made.","zh":"由於預測不確定，可能會犯錯。"},{"en":"Mistakes can be made means errors are possible even when people try carefully.","zh":"mistakes can be made 指即使人們謹慎嘗試，也可能出現錯誤。"},{"en":"In medical diagnosis, mistakes can be made if symptoms are unclear.","zh":"在醫學診斷中，如果症狀不清楚，可能會犯錯。"},{"en":"Accepting that mistakes can happen encourages checks, reviews, and caution.","zh":"承認可能出錯會鼓勵檢查、覆核和謹慎。"},{"en":"This phrase admits human or system error.","zh":"這個短語承認人或制度可能出錯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"controversial and politically charged","meaning":"具爭議性並帶有政治色彩的","examples":[{"en":"Parole is a controversial and politically charged issue.","zh":"假釋是一個具爭議性並帶有政治色彩的議題。"},{"en":"Controversial and politically charged means strongly debated and connected to public opinion, elections, or government pressure.","zh":"controversial and politically charged 指被激烈爭論，並與公眾意見、選舉或政府壓力相連。"},{"en":"School admission policy can become controversial and politically charged when families feel treated unfairly.","zh":"當家庭感到被不公平對待，學校收生政策可以變得具爭議性並帶有政治色彩。"},{"en":"Political pressure may make calm evidence-based discussion harder.","zh":"政治壓力可能令冷靜、以證據為本的討論更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an issue that attracts conflict and political emotion.","zh":"這個短語描述吸引衝突和政治情緒的議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"highly publicised crime","meaning":"被廣泛報道的罪案","examples":[{"en":"One highly publicised crime can affect attitudes towards the whole parole system.","zh":"一宗被廣泛報道的罪案可以影響人們對整個假釋制度的態度。"},{"en":"A highly publicised crime is a crime widely reported by news media and discussed by the public.","zh":"highly publicised crime 指被新聞媒體廣泛報道並由公眾討論的罪案。"},{"en":"A violent case shown repeatedly on television can become a highly publicised crime.","zh":"在電視上反覆播放的暴力案件可以成為被廣泛報道的罪案。"},{"en":"Such cases can strongly shape public fear, even if they are rare.","zh":"這類案件即使罕見，也可以強烈塑造公眾恐懼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a crime made very visible by media attention.","zh":"這個短語描述因媒體關注而非常顯眼的罪案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a person on parole","meaning":"假釋人士","examples":[{"en":"The crime was committed by a person on parole.","zh":"該罪案由一名假釋人士犯下。"},{"en":"A person on parole is someone released from prison under official conditions before the full sentence ends.","zh":"person on parole 指在完整刑期結束前按官方條件從監獄獲釋的人。"},{"en":"A person on parole may have to report regularly, obey curfew, and avoid certain people.","zh":"假釋人士可能必須定期報到、遵守宵禁並避開某些人。"},{"en":"If a person on parole commits a new crime, public trust in parole may fall.","zh":"如果假釋人士犯新罪，公眾對假釋的信任可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies someone under conditional release.","zh":"這個短語指出受有條件釋放約束的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"sway public opinion against","meaning":"令公眾輿論轉為反對……","examples":[{"en":"A serious incident may sway public opinion strongly against parole.","zh":"嚴重事件可能令公眾輿論強烈轉為反對假釋。"},{"en":"To sway public opinion against something means to make many people turn against it.","zh":"sway public opinion against something 指令許多人轉為反對某事。"},{"en":"A school accident may sway public opinion against a popular sports programme.","zh":"學校意外可能令公眾輿論轉為反對一個受歡迎的體育計劃。"},{"en":"Emotional cases can shift public opinion quickly, even before all evidence is reviewed.","zh":"情緒化個案可以在所有證據被檢視前迅速改變公眾意見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing public attitudes in a negative direction.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾態度向負面方向改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"political will","meaning":"政治意願","examples":[{"en":"The political will to defend an unpopular policy may be lacking.","zh":"捍衛不受歡迎政策的政治意願可能欠缺。"},{"en":"Political will means the determination of leaders or governments to take action despite difficulty.","zh":"political will 指領袖或政府儘管困難仍採取行動的決心。"},{"en":"A city needs political will to reduce traffic if the policy will anger some drivers.","zh":"如果減少交通的政策會激怒某些司機，城市需要政治意願去推行它。"},{"en":"Without political will, even good ideas may remain only reports and promises.","zh":"沒有政治意願，即使好的想法也可能只停留在報告和承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the courage and commitment needed for public action.","zh":"這個短語描述公共行動所需的勇氣和承擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be lacking","meaning":"欠缺","examples":[{"en":"Support for rehabilitation may be lacking after a widely reported crime.","zh":"在一宗被廣泛報道的罪案後，對更生的支持可能欠缺。"},{"en":"To be lacking means to be missing or insufficient.","zh":"be lacking 指缺失或不足。"},{"en":"A student’s essay may be lacking if it has examples but no clear argument.","zh":"如果學生作文有例子但沒有清楚論點，它可能有所欠缺。"},{"en":"When support is lacking, people may fail even if they want to improve.","zh":"當支援欠缺，即使人們想改善也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes absence or shortage of something needed.","zh":"這個短語描述所需事物的缺乏或不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"abolish the parole system","meaning":"廢除假釋制度","examples":[{"en":"Some jurisdictions have abolished the parole system.","zh":"有些司法管轄區已廢除假釋制度。"},{"en":"To abolish the parole system means to officially end the system that allows conditional early release.","zh":"abolish the parole system 指正式終止容許有條件提早釋放的制度。"},{"en":"A government may abolish a policy if it believes the policy creates more harm than benefit.","zh":"如果政府認為某政策造成的害處多於好處，它可能廢除該政策。"},{"en":"Abolishing parole removes one route between prison and full freedom.","zh":"廢除假釋會移除監獄與完全自由之間的一條過渡路徑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ending parole by law or official decision.","zh":"這個短語描述以法律或官方決定終止假釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"specific offences","meaning":"特定罪行","examples":[{"en":"Parole may be unavailable for specific serious offences.","zh":"某些特定嚴重罪行可能不適用假釋。"},{"en":"Specific offences are particular crimes named or defined by law.","zh":"specific offences 指法律列明或界定的特定罪案。"},{"en":"A law may set different penalties for specific offences such as assault, theft, or fraud.","zh":"法律可能對襲擊、盜竊或詐騙等特定罪行設定不同刑罰。"},{"en":"Some policies treat specific offences more strictly because they involve greater harm or risk.","zh":"有些政策更嚴格處理特定罪行，因為它們涉及較大傷害或風險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to named categories of crime.","zh":"這個短語指被命名的犯罪類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in response to public pressure","meaning":"因應公眾壓力","examples":[{"en":"Policies are sometimes changed in response to public pressure.","zh":"政策有時因應公眾壓力而改變。"},{"en":"In response to public pressure means because many people demand action or change.","zh":"in response to public pressure 指因許多人要求行動或改變而作出回應。"},{"en":"A school may change its lunch policy in response to public pressure from parents.","zh":"學校可能因應家長的公眾壓力而改變午餐政策。"},{"en":"Public pressure can force action, but it may not always lead to the best evidence-based decision.","zh":"公眾壓力可以迫使行動，但不一定總能帶來最以證據為本的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase explains that public opinion caused a response.","zh":"這個短語解釋公眾意見造成了回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a considered assessment of","meaning":"對……經深思熟慮的評估","examples":[{"en":"Policy should follow a considered assessment of the evidence.","zh":"政策應建基於對證據經深思熟慮的評估。"},{"en":"A considered assessment of something is a careful judgement made after thinking about evidence and consequences.","zh":"considered assessment of something 指在考慮證據和後果後作出的謹慎判斷。"},{"en":"A doctor makes a considered assessment of test results before recommending treatment.","zh":"醫生在建議治療前，會對檢查結果作出深思熟慮的評估。"},{"en":"Careful assessment reduces the risk of decisions based only on fear or anger.","zh":"謹慎評估能降低只基於恐懼或憤怒作決定的風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes thoughtful evaluation before action.","zh":"這個短語描述行動前的深思熟慮評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the pros and cons","meaning":"利弊","examples":[{"en":"Governments should examine the pros and cons of parole.","zh":"政府應審視假釋的利弊。"},{"en":"The pros and cons are the advantages and disadvantages of an idea or choice.","zh":"pros and cons 指某想法或選擇的優點和缺點。"},{"en":"A family may discuss the pros and cons of moving to a new district.","zh":"家庭可能討論搬到新地區的利弊。"},{"en":"Looking at both sides helps people avoid one-sided decisions.","zh":"看雙方有助人避免片面決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when weighing benefits against risks.","zh":"當權衡好處與風險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the same argument applies","meaning":"同一道理亦適用","examples":[{"en":"The same argument applies to offenders released without supervision.","zh":"同一道理亦適用於沒有監督而獲釋的罪犯。"},{"en":"The same argument applies means the same reasoning is also relevant in another situation.","zh":"the same argument applies 指同樣推理也適用於另一情況。"},{"en":"If small classes help younger students, the same argument applies to students who need extra support.","zh":"如果小班教學有助年幼學生，同一道理亦適用於需要額外支援的學生。"},{"en":"This phrase extends a point from one case to another.","zh":"這個短語把一個觀點由一個個案延伸到另一個個案。"},{"en":"It is useful when two situations share the same logic.","zh":"當兩種情況共享相同邏輯時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"an intermediate step","meaning":"中間過渡階段","examples":[{"en":"Parole provides an intermediate step between prison and complete freedom.","zh":"假釋提供監獄與完全自由之間的中間過渡階段。"},{"en":"An intermediate step is a middle stage between two very different conditions.","zh":"intermediate step 指兩種非常不同狀態之間的中間階段。"},{"en":"A part-time job can be an intermediate step between school and full-time work.","zh":"兼職工作可以是學校與全職工作之間的中間過渡階段。"},{"en":"Intermediate steps can make big transitions safer and more manageable.","zh":"中間過渡階段可以令巨大轉變更安全和更容易處理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a bridge between one stage and the next.","zh":"這個短語描述一個階段通往下一階段之間的橋樑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"face an uphill battle","meaning":"面對艱苦的挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Released inmates may face an uphill battle to rebuild their lives.","zh":"獲釋囚犯可能面對重建生活的艱苦挑戰。"},{"en":"To face an uphill battle means to face a very difficult struggle that requires great effort.","zh":"face an uphill battle 指面對需要巨大努力的艱難奮鬥。"},{"en":"A student who has missed months of school may face an uphill battle to catch up.","zh":"缺課數月的學生可能面對追上進度的艱苦挑戰。"},{"en":"The battle is “uphill” because progress is slow and obstacles are heavy.","zh":"這場戰鬥是「上坡」的，因為進展緩慢且障礙沉重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a hard challenge, not an impossible one.","zh":"這個短語描述艱難挑戰，而不是不可能的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"avoid recidivism","meaning":"避免再犯","examples":[{"en":"Employment and stable housing can help offenders avoid recidivism.","zh":"就業和穩定住所可以幫助罪犯避免再犯。"},{"en":"To avoid recidivism means to stay away from committing crimes again after release or punishment.","zh":"avoid recidivism 指在獲釋或受罰後避免再次犯罪。"},{"en":"A former inmate may avoid recidivism by keeping a job and staying away from old criminal contacts.","zh":"前囚犯可以透過保住工作並遠離過往犯罪關係來避免再犯。"},{"en":"Support, routine, and accountability can reduce the chance of returning to crime.","zh":"支援、規律和責任追蹤可以降低重返犯罪的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preventing repeated offending.","zh":"這個短語描述防止重複犯罪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in the longer term","meaning":"從長遠而言","examples":[{"en":"Failed reintegration may cost society more in the longer term.","zh":"重新融入失敗從長遠而言可能令社會付出更大代價。"},{"en":"In the longer term means over a longer future period, not just immediately.","zh":"in the longer term 指在較長的未來時期，而不只是立即。"},{"en":"Skipping sleep may save time tonight, but in the longer term it can damage health and learning.","zh":"今晚少睡可能節省時間，但從長遠而言會損害健康和學習。"},{"en":"Policies should consider long-term costs, not only short-term reactions.","zh":"政策應考慮長期成本，而不只是短期反應。"},{"en":"This phrase shifts attention from immediate effects to future consequences.","zh":"這個短語把注意力由即時影響轉向未來後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"an innovative method","meaning":"創新的方法","examples":[{"en":"Time off for good behaviour is a more innovative rehabilitation method.","zh":"因表現良好而減刑是一種較創新的更生方法。"},{"en":"An innovative method is a new or creative way of solving a problem.","zh":"innovative method 指解決問題的新穎或具創意的方法。"},{"en":"A school may use peer mentoring as an innovative method to support younger students.","zh":"學校可能使用朋輩指導作為支援低年級學生的創新方法。"},{"en":"Innovative methods can motivate people when older approaches are not enough.","zh":"當舊方法不足，創新方法可以激勵人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fresh approach rather than a traditional one.","zh":"這個短語描述新鮮做法，而不是傳統方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"encourage rehabilitation","meaning":"鼓勵更生","examples":[{"en":"Sentence reductions may encourage rehabilitation and good conduct.","zh":"減刑可能鼓勵更生和良好行為。"},{"en":"To encourage rehabilitation means to give offenders reasons or support to change their behaviour.","zh":"encourage rehabilitation 指給予罪犯改變行為的理由或支援。"},{"en":"Education, counselling, and sentence incentives can encourage rehabilitation in prison.","zh":"教育、輔導和刑期獎勵可以在監獄中鼓勵更生。"},{"en":"If good behaviour leads to real benefits, inmates may be more willing to change.","zh":"如果良好行為帶來真實好處，囚犯可能更願意改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes promoting reform through support or motivation.","zh":"這個短語描述透過支援或動機推動改造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"time off for good behaviour","meaning":"因表現良好而減刑","examples":[{"en":"Some prison systems offer time off for good behaviour.","zh":"有些監獄制度提供因表現良好而減刑。"},{"en":"Time off for good behaviour means reducing a prisoner’s sentence because they follow rules and behave responsibly.","zh":"time off for good behaviour 指因囚犯遵守規則並表現負責而減少刑期。"},{"en":"An inmate who studies, works, and avoids trouble may earn time off for good behaviour.","zh":"學習、工作並避免惹麻煩的囚犯，可能因表現良好而獲減刑。"},{"en":"This reward can encourage discipline because good conduct has a clear benefit.","zh":"這種獎勵可以鼓勵紀律，因為良好行為有清楚好處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sentence reduction as an incentive.","zh":"這個短語描述把減刑作為誘因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"for each year of imprisonment","meaning":"每服刑一年","examples":[{"en":"Inmates may earn a sentence reduction for each year of imprisonment.","zh":"囚犯每服刑一年，可能獲得刑期扣減。"},{"en":"For each year of imprisonment means for every one-year period spent in prison.","zh":"for each year of imprisonment 指每在監獄中度過一年。"},{"en":"A rule may give a prisoner a fixed number of credit days for each year of imprisonment.","zh":"規則可能給予囚犯每服刑一年固定日數的減刑。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a benefit or calculation to each year served.","zh":"這個短語把好處或計算連接到每一年服刑。"},{"en":"It is used when sentence credits are counted year by year.","zh":"當減刑期按年計算時，這個短語會使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"automatically grant someone","meaning":"自動給予某人……","examples":[{"en":"The system automatically grants well-behaved inmates time off their sentences.","zh":"該制度自動給予表現良好的囚犯刑期扣減。"},{"en":"To automatically grant someone something means to give it without a separate special decision each time.","zh":"automatically grant someone something 指每次無需另作特別決定便給予某物。"},{"en":"A school system may automatically grant students access to online notes after enrolment.","zh":"學校系統可能在學生註冊後自動給予他們網上筆記使用權。"},{"en":"Automatic grants make rules predictable because people know what behaviour earns what benefit.","zh":"自動給予令規則可預測，因為人們知道甚麼行為可換來甚麼好處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a benefit given by rule rather than by personal favour.","zh":"這個短語描述按規則給予的好處，而不是私人恩惠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"exhibit good behaviour","meaning":"表現良好","examples":[{"en":"Inmates who exhibit good behaviour may earn early release.","zh":"表現良好的囚犯可能獲得提早釋放。"},{"en":"To exhibit good behaviour means to show responsible and rule-following conduct.","zh":"exhibit good behaviour 指展現負責任並遵守規則的行為。"},{"en":"A child exhibits good behaviour when she shares materials and listens to the teacher.","zh":"當孩子分享物資並聆聽老師，她就是表現良好。"},{"en":"Good behaviour shown repeatedly can build trust with those in authority.","zh":"反覆展現良好行為可以與權威人士建立信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visibly showing positive conduct.","zh":"這個短語描述可見地展現正面行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a certain number of days","meaning":"指定日數","examples":[{"en":"The system deducts a certain number of days from the sentence.","zh":"該制度從刑期中扣減指定日數。"},{"en":"A certain number of days means a specific but not yet named amount of time measured in days.","zh":"a certain number of days 指以日計算的某個特定但未說明的時間量。"},{"en":"A school may allow a certain number of days for students to submit late work.","zh":"學校可能容許學生在指定日數內補交遲交功課。"},{"en":"Setting a fixed number of days makes a rule clearer and easier to apply.","zh":"設定固定日數令規則更清楚並更容易執行。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a defined amount of time.","zh":"這個短語指一段已界定的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"good-time credit","meaning":"良好行為減刑期","examples":[{"en":"Good-time credit accumulates when an inmate follows prison rules.","zh":"當囚犯遵守監獄規則，良好行為減刑期會累積。"},{"en":"Good-time credit is sentence reduction earned through good behaviour in prison.","zh":"good-time credit 指透過在監獄中表現良好而賺取的減刑。"},{"en":"An inmate may earn good-time credit by working, studying, and avoiding disciplinary problems.","zh":"囚犯可能透過工作、學習和避免紀律問題賺取良好行為減刑期。"},{"en":"If rules are broken, earned credit may be reduced or lost.","zh":"如果違反規則，已賺取的減刑期可能被減少或失去。"},{"en":"This phrase describes time deducted from a sentence as a reward for good conduct.","zh":"這個短語描述因良好行為作為獎勵而從刑期中扣減的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"accrue over time","meaning":"隨時間累積","examples":[{"en":"Sentence-reduction credits accrue over time.","zh":"減刑期會隨時間累積。"},{"en":"To accrue over time means to gradually build up or increase as time passes.","zh":"accrue over time 指隨時間過去逐漸增加或累積。"},{"en":"Savings accrue over time when a person puts a small amount aside every month.","zh":"當一個人每月存下一小筆錢，儲蓄會隨時間累積。"},{"en":"Credits that accrue slowly can motivate consistent good behaviour.","zh":"慢慢累積的減刑期可以鼓勵持續良好行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual accumulation.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步累積。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"result in early release","meaning":"導致提早獲釋","examples":[{"en":"Good behaviour may result in early release.","zh":"良好行為可能導致提早獲釋。"},{"en":"To result in early release means to lead to someone being allowed to leave prison before the full sentence ends.","zh":"result in early release 指導致某人在完整刑期結束前被允許離開監獄。"},{"en":"In some systems, steady rule-following can result in early release.","zh":"在某些制度中，持續遵守規則可以導致提早獲釋。"},{"en":"Early release is usually conditional and may still involve supervision.","zh":"提早獲釋通常是有條件的，並可能仍涉及監督。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a consequence of good conduct or sentence credit.","zh":"這個短語描述良好行為或減刑期帶來的後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"one-third of the sentence earlier","meaning":"提早相當於刑期三分之一的時間","examples":[{"en":"An inmate may be released up to one-third of the sentence earlier.","zh":"囚犯可能提早相當於刑期三分之一的時間獲釋。"},{"en":"One-third of the sentence earlier means before the original release date by as much as one third of the total sentence.","zh":"one-third of the sentence earlier 指比原定釋放日期最多提早整段刑期的三分之一。"},{"en":"If a sentence is six years, one-third earlier could mean up to two years earlier.","zh":"如果刑期是六年，提早三分之一可以表示最多提早兩年。"},{"en":"This kind of reduction gives inmates a strong reason to follow rules.","zh":"這種扣減給囚犯強烈理由去遵守規則。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the maximum size of an early-release benefit.","zh":"這個短語描述提早釋放好處的最大幅度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"commit an infraction","meaning":"違反規則","examples":[{"en":"An inmate may lose privileges after committing an infraction.","zh":"囚犯違反規則後可能失去特權。"},{"en":"To commit an infraction means to break a rule, usually one within an institution or system.","zh":"commit an infraction 指違反規則，通常是某機構或制度內的規則。"},{"en":"A student commits an infraction if he uses a phone during an exam.","zh":"如果學生在考試中使用手機，他就是違反規則。"},{"en":"Infractions may be minor or serious, but they still show a rule has been broken.","zh":"違規可以輕微或嚴重，但仍顯示有規則被打破。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rule-breaking rather than necessarily a major crime.","zh":"這個短語描述違反規則，而不一定是重大犯罪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"serious infractions","meaning":"嚴重違規行為","examples":[{"en":"Serious infractions may result in the loss of earned sentence reductions.","zh":"嚴重違規行為可能導致已賺取的減刑被取消。"},{"en":"Serious infractions are major rule violations that can lead to strong penalties.","zh":"serious infractions 指可導致嚴厲懲罰的重大違規。"},{"en":"Fighting in prison or bringing in banned items may be treated as serious infractions.","zh":"在監獄中打鬥或帶入違禁物品，可能被視為嚴重違規行為。"},{"en":"Serious infractions damage trust and may cancel benefits previously earned.","zh":"嚴重違規會破壞信任，並可能取消先前獲得的好處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rule-breaking with important consequences.","zh":"這個短語描述有重大後果的違規。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"forfeit one’s accumulated time","meaning":"喪失累積的減刑期","examples":[{"en":"Prisoners who break the rules may forfeit their accumulated good-time credit.","zh":"違反規則的囚犯可能喪失累積的良好行為減刑期。"},{"en":"To forfeit one’s accumulated time means to lose time credits that have been earned because of misconduct.","zh":"forfeit one’s accumulated time 指因不當行為而失去已賺取的時間扣減。"},{"en":"A student may forfeit accumulated bonus points if he cheats in a class activity.","zh":"如果學生在課堂活動中作弊，他可能喪失累積的加分。"},{"en":"Losing accumulated time makes rule-breaking costly because past good behaviour no longer brings the same reward.","zh":"失去累積時間令違規代價高昂，因為過往良好行為不再帶來同樣獎勵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes losing earned benefits.","zh":"這個短語描述失去已獲得的好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"complete the full duration of","meaning":"服完整段……刑期","examples":[{"en":"The inmate may then have to complete the full duration of the sentence.","zh":"該囚犯之後可能必須服完整段刑期。"},{"en":"To complete the full duration of something means to finish the whole period without reduction.","zh":"complete the full duration of something 指不獲縮短地完成整段時間。"},{"en":"A student given detention may have to complete the full duration if she breaks the rules again.","zh":"被罰留堂的學生如果再次違規，可能必須完成整段留堂時間。"},{"en":"When sentence credits are lost, early release may no longer be possible.","zh":"當減刑期被失去，提早獲釋可能不再可能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serving or finishing the entire required time.","zh":"這個短語描述服完或完成整段要求時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether each statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"考生判斷每項陳述是否與文章一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information means to match what the text says.","zh":"agree with the information 指與文本所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the passage says parole is conditional, a statement saying the same thing agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說假釋是有條件的，而陳述說同一件事，它就是與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should check the exact wording before choosing TRUE.","zh":"學生在選 TRUE 前應檢查準確措辭。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading-comprehension questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀理解題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to state the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"contradict the information 指陳述與文章所說相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the text says probation is not prison, an answer saying it is imprisonment contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文本說感化令不是監禁，而答案說它是監禁，就是與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"Careful readers look for direct conflict, not just a small difference in wording.","zh":"細心讀者會尋找直接衝突，而不只是措辭上的細小差異。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a statement that clashes with the text.","zh":"這個短語描述與文本相衝突的陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"“Not Given” means that the passage provides no relevant information.","zh":"“Not Given” 表示文章沒有提供相關資料。"},{"en":"No information on this means the text does not give enough evidence to decide true or false.","zh":"no information on this 指文本沒有提供足夠證據來判斷真假。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions a parole officer’s age, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文章從未提及假釋官年齡，就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not answer from general knowledge when the passage is silent.","zh":"當文章沒有提及時，學生不應以常識作答。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a NOT GIVEN situation.","zh":"這個短語表示 NOT GIVEN 的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"become worse in prison","meaning":"在監獄中變得更差","examples":[{"en":"Some inmates may become more violent or criminally experienced in prison.","zh":"有些囚犯可能在監獄中變得更暴力或更有犯罪經驗。"},{"en":"To become worse in prison means to leave prison with more harmful behaviour or stronger criminal habits.","zh":"become worse in prison 指離開監獄時帶着更有害行為或更強犯罪習慣。"},{"en":"An inmate may become worse if he is surrounded by violence, fear, and gang pressure.","zh":"如果囚犯被暴力、恐懼和幫派壓力包圍，他可能在監獄中變得更差。"},{"en":"Prison can fail as rehabilitation if it teaches people new criminal methods.","zh":"如果監獄教會人新的犯罪方法，它作為更生場所就可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes negative change during imprisonment.","zh":"這個短語描述監禁期間的負面改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"provide effective education and therapy","meaning":"提供有效的教育及治療","examples":[{"en":"Prisons may provide education and therapy, although their quality can vary.","zh":"監獄可能提供教育及治療，雖然其質素可以不同。"},{"en":"To provide effective education and therapy means to offer learning and treatment that genuinely help people change.","zh":"provide effective education and therapy 指提供真正幫助人改變的學習和治療。"},{"en":"A prison provides effective education and therapy when inmates gain skills and learn to manage harmful behaviour.","zh":"當囚犯獲得技能並學會管理有害行為，監獄就是提供有效教育及治療。"},{"en":"If programmes are poorly taught or too short, they may not be effective.","zh":"如果計劃教得差或時間太短，它們可能沒有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaningful support, not just the existence of classes.","zh":"這個短語描述有意義的支援，而不只是有課程存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reoffend after release","meaning":"獲釋後再犯","examples":[{"en":"Some prisoners reoffend after release from custody.","zh":"有些囚犯在羈押獲釋後再犯。"},{"en":"To reoffend after release means to commit another crime after leaving prison or detention.","zh":"reoffend after release 指離開監獄或羈押後再次犯罪。"},{"en":"A person may reoffend after release if they return to the same criminal group and have no job.","zh":"如果一個人回到同一犯罪團體且沒有工作，他可能獲釋後再犯。"},{"en":"Reoffending after release suggests that reintegration support may have failed or been insufficient.","zh":"獲釋後再犯顯示重新融入支援可能失敗或不足。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeat crime after custody ends.","zh":"這個短語描述羈押結束後的重複犯罪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be stricter than","meaning":"比……更嚴格","examples":[{"en":"Supervised release may impose stricter conditions than parole.","zh":"監督釋放可能施加比假釋更嚴格的條件。"},{"en":"To be stricter than something means to have tougher rules or stronger limits.","zh":"be stricter than something 指有更嚴厲規則或更強限制。"},{"en":"A final exam may be stricter than a class quiz because it affects the whole grade.","zh":"期末考試可能比課堂小測更嚴格，因為它影響整體成績。"},{"en":"Stricter rules may reduce risk but can also make daily life harder.","zh":"更嚴格的規則可以降低風險，但也可能令日常生活更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the severity of two sets of rules.","zh":"這個短語比較兩套規則的嚴厲程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be abolished after careful consideration","meaning":"經慎重考慮後被廢除","examples":[{"en":"A parole system should not be abolished without careful consideration.","zh":"假釋制度不應在沒有慎重考慮下被廢除。"},{"en":"To be abolished after careful consideration means to be ended only after serious review of evidence and consequences.","zh":"be abolished after careful consideration 指只有在認真檢視證據和後果後才終止。"},{"en":"A school should not abolish exams after one complaint without careful consideration.","zh":"學校不應在一次投訴後，未經慎重考慮便廢除考試。"},{"en":"Ending a system too quickly may create new problems that were not expected.","zh":"太快終止制度可能產生未被預料的新問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cautious decision-making before removing a policy.","zh":"這個短語描述移除政策前的謹慎決策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the flow chart","meaning":"完成流程圖","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the flow chart using words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的詞語完成流程圖。"},{"en":"To complete the flow chart means to fill missing steps or labels in a process diagram.","zh":"complete the flow chart 指填寫流程圖中缺失的步驟或標籤。"},{"en":"In a science test, students may complete a flow chart showing how water is purified.","zh":"在科學測驗中，學生可能完成展示水如何被淨化的流程圖。"},{"en":"Flow charts help readers see order, cause, and sequence clearly.","zh":"流程圖幫助讀者清楚看見次序、原因和流程。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in IELTS-style reading tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於 IELTS 類閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個字","examples":[{"en":"Each flow-chart answer should contain no more than three words.","zh":"每個流程圖答案應不多於三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must use three words or fewer.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案必須使用三個或更少的英文詞。"},{"en":"If the correct answer is “parole officer,” it fits because it has two words.","zh":"如果正確答案是 “parole officer”，它符合要求，因為它有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing extra words may make an answer wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫多餘詞語也可能令答案錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語在考試指示中給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"write the specific term","meaning":"寫出具體術語","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the specific term that matches each definition.","zh":"考生寫出與每個定義相配的具體術語。"},{"en":"To write the specific term means to give the exact word or phrase required by the definition.","zh":"write the specific term 指給出定義所要求的準確詞語或短語。"},{"en":"If the definition says “conditional release from prison,” the specific term may be “parole.”","zh":"如果定義說「有條件地從監獄釋放」，具體術語可能是 “parole”。"},{"en":"This task tests vocabulary precision, not general explanation.","zh":"這項任務測試詞彙精準度，而不是一般解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase tells students to supply the correct technical term.","zh":"這個短語告訴學生提供正確專門術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Each specific term should contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個具體術語應不多於兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must use two words or fewer.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案必須使用兩個或更少的英文詞。"},{"en":"“Good-time credit” may count as two words if written with a hyphenated first part.","zh":"如果 “good-time credit” 的第一部分以連字符書寫，它可能算作兩個詞。"},{"en":"Students must follow the word limit exactly to avoid losing marks.","zh":"學生必須準確遵守字數限制，以免失分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a shorter and stricter answer limit.","zh":"這個短語給出更短、更嚴格的答案限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reoffending after release","meaning":"獲釋後再犯","examples":[{"en":"Criminal recidivism means reoffending after release from prison.","zh":"刑事再犯指從監獄獲釋後再犯。"},{"en":"Reoffending after release means committing another crime after leaving prison or custody.","zh":"reoffending after release 指離開監獄或羈押後再次犯罪。"},{"en":"A former prisoner may risk reoffending after release if he has no housing, work, or support.","zh":"如果前囚犯沒有住所、工作或支援，他可能有獲釋後再犯的風險。"},{"en":"Preventing reoffending after release is a major aim of rehabilitation and parole.","zh":"防止獲釋後再犯是更生和假釋的主要目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeat crime after a person returns to the community.","zh":"這個短語描述一個人回到社區後重複犯罪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"manipulate officials and procedures","meaning":"操弄官員和程序","examples":[{"en":"“System cracking” involves manipulating prison officials and procedures.","zh":"“System cracking” 涉及操弄監獄官員和程序。"},{"en":"To manipulate officials and procedures means to unfairly influence people and rules for personal advantage.","zh":"manipulate officials and procedures 指為個人利益而不公平地影響人員和規則。"},{"en":"A clever applicant may manipulate procedures by hiding information and saying only what officers want to hear.","zh":"狡猾的申請者可能透過隱藏資料並只說官員想聽的話來操弄程序。"},{"en":"When officials and procedures are manipulated, the system may make unsafe decisions.","zh":"當官員和程序被操弄，制度可能作出不安全的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exploiting both people and rules.","zh":"這個短語描述同時利用人和規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"an alternative to imprisonment","meaning":"監禁以外的替代刑罰","examples":[{"en":"Probation is an alternative to imprisonment.","zh":"感化令是監禁以外的替代刑罰。"},{"en":"An alternative to imprisonment is a punishment or arrangement used instead of sending someone to prison.","zh":"alternative to imprisonment 指用來代替送某人入獄的懲罰或安排。"},{"en":"Community service can be an alternative to imprisonment for some less serious offences.","zh":"對某些較輕罪行而言，社會服務令可以是監禁以外的替代刑罰。"},{"en":"Alternatives may punish wrongdoing while allowing people to keep work and family ties.","zh":"替代方案可以懲罰不當行為，同時讓人保留工作和家庭聯繫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a non-prison option.","zh":"這個短語描述非監禁選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a predetermined time","meaning":"預先指定的時間","examples":[{"en":"A curfew requires a person to return home by a predetermined time.","zh":"宵禁要求一個人在預先指定的時間前回家。"},{"en":"A predetermined time is a time decided in advance.","zh":"predetermined time 指事先決定的時間。"},{"en":"Students may have to submit online homework by a predetermined time, such as 11 p.m.","zh":"學生可能必須在預先指定的時間前提交網上功課，例如晚上十一時。"},{"en":"Predetermined times reduce confusion because everyone knows the deadline.","zh":"預先指定的時間減少混亂，因為每個人都知道限期。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fixed time set before the action happens.","zh":"這個短語描述行動發生前已設定的固定時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"time deducted from a sentence","meaning":"從刑期中扣減的時間","examples":[{"en":"Good-time credit is time deducted from a well-behaved prisoner’s sentence.","zh":"良好行為減刑期是從表現良好囚犯刑期中扣減的時間。"},{"en":"Time deducted from a sentence means days, months, or years taken away from the original prison term.","zh":"time deducted from a sentence 指從原本監禁刑期中扣走的日、月或年。"},{"en":"A prisoner may receive time deducted from a sentence after consistently following prison rules.","zh":"囚犯在持續遵守監獄規則後，可能獲得從刑期中扣減的時間。"},{"en":"Deducted time can lead to earlier release if the prisoner does not lose the credit.","zh":"如果囚犯沒有失去減刑期，被扣減的時間可以導致較早獲釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reduction of a prison sentence.","zh":"這個短語描述監禁刑期的減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 4 - Criminal Rehabilitation - A Difficult Issue.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 5":[{"front":"destination Mars","meaning":"目的地：火星","examples":[{"en":"Mars may eventually become a destination for human settlers.","zh":"火星最終可能成為人類定居者的目的地。"},{"en":"Destination Mars means the idea that Mars is a place humans may travel to, explore, or settle in the future.","zh":"destination Mars 指火星可能成為人類未來前往、探索或定居的地方這個想法。"},{"en":"In a school science project, students might design a poster called “Destination Mars” to explain how people could live there.","zh":"在學校科學項目中，學生可能設計一張名為「目的地：火星」的海報，解釋人類如何在那裏生活。"},{"en":"Mars becomes a possible destination because it has land, frozen water, and conditions that partly resemble Earth’s.","zh":"火星成為可能目的地，是因為它有陸地、冰封水源，以及部分與地球相似的條件。"},{"en":"The phrase presents Mars not just as a planet to observe, but as a possible place to reach.","zh":"這個短語把火星呈現為不只是被觀察的行星，而是可能抵達的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"potentially habitable planet","meaning":"可能適合居住的行星","examples":[{"en":"Mars is the closest potentially habitable planet to Earth.","zh":"火星是最接近地球、可能適合居住的行星。"},{"en":"A potentially habitable planet is a planet that may have conditions allowing life or human settlement, at least with technology.","zh":"potentially habitable planet 指可能具備讓生命或人類定居的條件的行星，至少在科技協助下如此。"},{"en":"Scientists look for potentially habitable planets by checking water, temperature, atmosphere, and surface conditions.","zh":"科學家透過檢查水、溫度、大氣和地表條件，尋找可能適合居住的行星。"},{"en":"A planet is only potentially habitable if its dangers can possibly be managed, not because it is already comfortable.","zh":"一顆行星只有在其危險可能被處理時，才算可能適合居住，而不是因為它已經舒適。"},{"en":"The phrase means “possibly suitable for living,” not “already safe to live on.”","zh":"這個短語意思是「可能適合生活」，不是「已經安全可居住」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"solid ground","meaning":"固體地面","examples":[{"en":"Mars has solid ground on which spacecraft can land.","zh":"火星有固體地面，太空船可以在上面降落。"},{"en":"Solid ground is a firm surface that people, vehicles, or spacecraft can stand or land on.","zh":"solid ground 指人、車輛或太空船可以站立或降落的堅實表面。"},{"en":"A rescue team needs solid ground before it can safely set up tents and equipment.","zh":"救援隊需要固體地面，才能安全搭建帳篷和設備。"},{"en":"Solid ground makes landing easier because a craft can touch down instead of floating or sinking.","zh":"固體地面令降落較容易，因為太空船可以着陸，而不是漂浮或下沉。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts a firm surface with water, gas, ice, or unstable material.","zh":"這個短語把堅實表面與水、氣體、冰或不穩定物料作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"protective surface features","meaning":"具保護作用的地表特徵","examples":[{"en":"Mars has some protective surface features, including possible caves.","zh":"火星有一些具保護作用的地表特徵，包括可能存在的洞穴。"},{"en":"Protective surface features are natural shapes or structures on the ground that can help shield people or equipment from danger.","zh":"protective surface features 指地面上能幫助保護人或設備免受危險的自然形狀或結構。"},{"en":"A deep valley can be a protective surface feature if it blocks strong wind from a campsite.","zh":"如果深谷能為營地阻擋強風，它就可以是具保護作用的地表特徵。"},{"en":"On Mars, caves may protect settlers from radiation, micrometeoroids, and extreme surface conditions.","zh":"在火星上，洞穴可能保護定居者免受輻射、微流星體和極端地表環境影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to useful landforms that offer physical protection.","zh":"這個短語指能提供物理保護的有用地貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"thin atmosphere","meaning":"稀薄的大氣層","examples":[{"en":"Mars has a thin atmosphere that offers little protection.","zh":"火星有稀薄的大氣層，幾乎不能提供保護。"},{"en":"A thin atmosphere is a weak layer of gases around a planet, with much lower density than Earth’s atmosphere.","zh":"thin atmosphere 指包圍行星的一層稀薄氣體，其密度遠低於地球大氣。"},{"en":"A planet with a thin atmosphere cannot easily block harmful radiation or burn up incoming objects.","zh":"大氣層稀薄的行星不容易阻擋有害輻射，也不容易令進入的物體燃燒殆盡。"},{"en":"Because Mars has a thin atmosphere, settlers would need artificial shelters and protective equipment.","zh":"因為火星有稀薄的大氣層，定居者需要人工庇護所和防護設備。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why the Martian surface remains dangerous despite having some air.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何火星表面即使有一些空氣，仍然危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"closely mimic","meaning":"與……非常相似","examples":[{"en":"Some conditions on Mars closely mimic those on Earth.","zh":"火星上的一些條件與地球上的條件非常相似。"},{"en":"To closely mimic something means to be very similar to it or copy its features closely.","zh":"closely mimic something 指與某事非常相似，或緊密模仿其特徵。"},{"en":"A training simulator can closely mimic a real driving test so learners feel prepared.","zh":"訓練模擬器可以與真實駕駛考試非常相似，讓學習者有準備。"},{"en":"Conditions that closely mimic Earth’s may make it easier for humans to adapt to another planet.","zh":"與地球非常相似的條件，可能令人在另一顆行星上較容易適應。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses strong similarity, not complete identity.","zh":"這個短語強調高度相似，而不是完全相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"gravitational conditions","meaning":"重力環境","examples":[{"en":"Mars partly resembles Earth in its gravitational conditions.","zh":"火星在重力環境方面部分類似地球。"},{"en":"Gravitational conditions are the way gravity affects weight, movement, muscles, bones, and daily activities in a place.","zh":"gravitational conditions 指某地的重力如何影響重量、移動、肌肉、骨骼和日常活動。"},{"en":"Astronauts must train for different gravitational conditions before working on the Moon or Mars.","zh":"太空人到月球或火星工作前，必須為不同重力環境接受訓練。"},{"en":"If gravitational conditions differ greatly from Earth’s, the human body may weaken or move awkwardly.","zh":"如果重力環境與地球差異很大，人體可能變弱或動作不自然。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the strength and effects of gravity in an environment.","zh":"這個短語指某環境中重力的強度和影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lighting conditions","meaning":"光照條件","examples":[{"en":"The lighting conditions on Mars are closer to Earth’s than those elsewhere.","zh":"火星的光照條件比其他地方更接近地球。"},{"en":"Lighting conditions are the amount, colour, timing, and quality of light in a place.","zh":"lighting conditions 指某地光線的多少、顏色、時間和質素。"},{"en":"A classroom needs good lighting conditions so students can read without straining their eyes.","zh":"課室需要良好光照條件，讓學生閱讀時不用太吃力。"},{"en":"On another planet, familiar lighting conditions may help people keep a more normal daily rhythm.","zh":"在另一顆行星上，熟悉的光照條件可能幫助人維持較正常的日常節律。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how light affects visibility, comfort, and activity.","zh":"這個短語描述光線如何影響可見度、舒適度和活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be reachable—just","meaning":"勉強可以到達","examples":[{"en":"With present technology, Mars is reachable—just.","zh":"以現有科技而言，火星勉強可以到達。"},{"en":"Reachable—just means possible to reach, but only with great difficulty and little margin for failure.","zh":"reachable—just 指可以到達，但非常困難，而且幾乎沒有出錯空間。"},{"en":"For a tired runner, the finish line may be reachable—just—if he keeps a slow pace.","zh":"對疲累跑手而言，如果保持慢速，終點可能勉強可以到達。"},{"en":"Mars is reachable because rockets can get there, but the distance, cost, and risks remain severe.","zh":"火星可以到達，是因為火箭能抵達那裏，但距離、成本和風險仍然嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests something is barely possible, not easy.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事只是勉強可能，而不是容易。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"most importantly","meaning":"最重要的是","examples":[{"en":"Most importantly, Mars has vast reserves of frozen water.","zh":"最重要的是，火星有大量冰封水源儲備。"},{"en":"Most importantly introduces the point that matters more than the others.","zh":"most importantly 引入比其他重點更重要的一點。"},{"en":"When choosing a flat, location matters; most importantly, it must be safe to live in.","zh":"選擇單位時，地點很重要；最重要的是，它必須適合安全居住。"},{"en":"The phrase helps readers recognise which reason should receive the greatest attention.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者看出哪個理由最值得注意。"},{"en":"It signals that the next point is central to the argument.","zh":"它表示下一點是論點的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"studies have found that","meaning":"研究發現","examples":[{"en":"Studies have found that Mars contains frozen water.","zh":"研究發現火星含有冰封水源。"},{"en":"Studies have found that means research has produced evidence supporting a conclusion.","zh":"studies have found that 指研究已產生支持某結論的證據。"},{"en":"Studies have found that regular sleep helps students remember information more effectively.","zh":"研究發現規律睡眠幫助學生更有效記住資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a claim is based on research rather than personal opinion.","zh":"當某主張建基於研究而不是個人意見，便會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It gives a statement more authority by linking it to investigation.","zh":"它透過連接調查，令陳述更具權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"vast reserves of","meaning":"大量儲備的……","examples":[{"en":"Mars appears to have vast reserves of frozen water.","zh":"火星似乎有大量儲備的冰封水源。"},{"en":"Vast reserves of something are very large stored amounts of a useful resource.","zh":"vast reserves of something 指非常大量儲存起來的有用資源。"},{"en":"A country with vast reserves of oil may rely heavily on energy exports.","zh":"擁有大量石油儲備的國家，可能高度依賴能源出口。"},{"en":"Vast reserves matter because they can support long-term use instead of only short visits.","zh":"大量儲備很重要，因為它們可以支持長期使用，而不只是短暫到訪。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both large quantity and potential usefulness.","zh":"這個短語同時強調數量巨大和潛在用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"frozen water","meaning":"冰封水源","examples":[{"en":"Frozen water could support a future Martian settlement.","zh":"冰封水源可以支持未來火星殖民地。"},{"en":"Frozen water is water in solid form, such as ice, that may be melted or processed for use.","zh":"frozen water 指固態形式的水，例如冰，可能被融化或處理後使用。"},{"en":"Campers may melt frozen water from snow if they have no other safe water source.","zh":"如果沒有其他安全水源，露營者可能融化雪中的冰封水源。"},{"en":"On Mars, frozen water could provide drinking water, oxygen, and fuel ingredients.","zh":"在火星上，冰封水源可以提供飲用水、氧氣和燃料原料。"},{"en":"The phrase is important because water is basic to survival and settlement.","zh":"這個短語很重要，因為水是生存和定居的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"basic minerals","meaning":"基本礦物","examples":[{"en":"Mars also contains basic minerals needed by settlers.","zh":"火星也含有定居者所需的基本礦物。"},{"en":"Basic minerals are simple natural substances in rock or soil that can be used for construction, chemistry, farming, or industry.","zh":"basic minerals 指岩石或土壤中的簡單天然物質，可用於建築、化學、農業或工業。"},{"en":"A village may need basic minerals such as sand, clay, and stone to build houses.","zh":"村莊可能需要沙、黏土和石材等基本礦物來建屋。"},{"en":"On Mars, basic minerals could reduce the need to bring every material from Earth.","zh":"在火星上，基本礦物可以減少從地球帶去所有材料的需要。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to useful raw materials found in the ground.","zh":"這個短語指地下找到的有用原材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"In contrast, the Moon is barren and has few useful resources.","zh":"相比之下，月球荒蕪，而且有用資源很少。"},{"en":"In contrast introduces a clear difference between two ideas, places, or situations.","zh":"in contrast 引入兩個想法、地方或情況之間的清楚差異。"},{"en":"One student enjoys speaking tasks; in contrast, another feels more comfortable with writing.","zh":"一名學生喜歡口語任務；相比之下，另一名學生更習慣寫作。"},{"en":"The phrase helps readers compare Mars and the Moon by showing opposite features.","zh":"這個短語透過展示相反特徵，幫助讀者比較火星和月球。"},{"en":"It signals that the next point differs from the previous one.","zh":"它表示下一點與前一點不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"closest heavenly body","meaning":"最近的天體","examples":[{"en":"The Moon is the closest heavenly body to Earth.","zh":"月球是最接近地球的天體。"},{"en":"A heavenly body is a natural object in space, such as a planet, moon, star, asteroid, or comet.","zh":"heavenly body 指太空中的天然物體，例如行星、月球、恆星、小行星或彗星。"},{"en":"Children often first learn about heavenly bodies by observing the Moon and bright planets in the night sky.","zh":"孩子通常透過觀察夜空中的月球和明亮行星，初步認識天體。"},{"en":"The closest heavenly body is easier to reach, but closeness does not automatically make it useful for settlement.","zh":"最近的天體較容易到達，但距離近不會自動表示它適合定居。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a space object in relation to Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述與地球相關的太空物體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"dusty and barren","meaning":"塵土滿佈而荒蕪的","examples":[{"en":"The Moon is dusty and barren.","zh":"月球塵土滿佈而荒蕪。"},{"en":"Dusty and barren means covered with dust and lacking plants, water, or obvious life-supporting resources.","zh":"dusty and barren 指滿佈塵埃，而且缺乏植物、水或明顯生命支持資源。"},{"en":"An abandoned construction site may look dusty and barren if no one has used it for years.","zh":"如果多年沒有人使用，廢棄建築地盤可能看起來塵土滿佈而荒蕪。"},{"en":"A dusty and barren environment is difficult for settlement because it offers little natural support.","zh":"塵土滿佈而荒蕪的環境難以定居，因為它幾乎不提供天然支持。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a dry, empty, and lifeless-looking place.","zh":"這個短語描述乾燥、空蕩和看似沒有生命的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hostile environment","meaning":"惡劣環境","examples":[{"en":"The Moon presents a hostile environment for permanent settlement.","zh":"月球為永久殖民提供的是惡劣環境。"},{"en":"A hostile environment is a place with conditions that are dangerous, uncomfortable, or difficult for life.","zh":"hostile environment 指條件危險、不舒適或不利於生命的地方。"},{"en":"A desert without water or shade can be a hostile environment for unprepared travellers.","zh":"沒有水或遮蔭的沙漠，對沒有準備的旅客而言可以是惡劣環境。"},{"en":"Hostile environments require special equipment because ordinary human bodies cannot cope with them safely.","zh":"惡劣環境需要特殊設備，因為普通人體不能安全應付。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a place that works against survival.","zh":"這個短語描述不利於生存的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"settlement of the Moon","meaning":"月球殖民","examples":[{"en":"Settlement of the Moon would be easier than settlement of Mars.","zh":"月球殖民會比火星殖民容易。"},{"en":"Settlement of the Moon means humans establishing a place to live and work on the Moon.","zh":"settlement of the Moon 指人類在月球建立居住和工作的地方。"},{"en":"A science club might debate whether settlement of the Moon should come before settlement of Mars.","zh":"科學學會可能辯論月球殖民是否應先於火星殖民。"},{"en":"Lunar settlement may be easier to reach, but it may still be hard to sustain without useful local resources.","zh":"月球殖民可能較容易抵達，但如果沒有有用本地資源，仍可能難以維持。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to creating a lasting human presence on the Moon.","zh":"這個短語指在月球建立持久的人類存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ultimately more costly","meaning":"最終成本更高","examples":[{"en":"Despite being closer, lunar settlement could ultimately be more costly.","zh":"儘管月球較近，月球殖民最終成本可能更高。"},{"en":"Ultimately more costly means more expensive in the end, after all long-term needs are considered.","zh":"ultimately more costly 指在考慮所有長期需要後，最終更昂貴。"},{"en":"A cheap printer may be ultimately more costly if its ink is very expensive.","zh":"如果墨水非常昂貴，便宜打印機最終成本可能更高。"},{"en":"A settlement can become more costly when every resource must be imported from elsewhere.","zh":"當每種資源都必須從其他地方輸入，殖民地成本可能變得更高。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds us to judge cost over the whole project, not only at the start.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們應按整個項目判斷成本，而不只是看開頭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"of little use","meaning":"用處不大","examples":[{"en":"A settlement without local resources might be of little use.","zh":"沒有本地資源的殖民地可能用處不大。"},{"en":"Of little use means not very helpful, valuable, or practical.","zh":"of little use 指幫助、價值或實際用途不大。"},{"en":"A phone without battery power is of little use during an emergency.","zh":"在緊急情況中，沒有電的手機用處不大。"},{"en":"A space base is of little use if it cannot support people, research, or resource production.","zh":"如果太空基地不能支持人員、研究或資源生產，它就用處不大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that exists but does not help much.","zh":"這個短語描述某物存在，但幫助不多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"extraterrestrial site","meaning":"地球以外的地點","examples":[{"en":"Mars may be the most suitable extraterrestrial site for settlement.","zh":"火星可能是最適合殖民的地球以外地點。"},{"en":"An extraterrestrial site is a place beyond Earth, such as a planet, moon, or asteroid.","zh":"extraterrestrial site 指地球以外的地方，例如行星、月球或小行星。"},{"en":"A space agency may compare each extraterrestrial site by distance, resources, safety, and scientific value.","zh":"太空機構可能按距離、資源、安全和科學價值比較每個地球以外的地點。"},{"en":"A good extraterrestrial site for settlement needs more than land; it needs usable resources and protection.","zh":"適合殖民的地球以外地點不只需要土地；還需要可用資源和保護。"},{"en":"The phrase means a location outside Earth.","zh":"這個短語意思是地球以外的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"humankind will ultimately settle","meaning":"人類最終會定居","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists believe humankind will ultimately settle on Mars.","zh":"有些科學家相信人類最終會定居火星。"},{"en":"Humankind will ultimately settle means human beings will eventually establish a lasting home or community somewhere.","zh":"humankind will ultimately settle 指人類最終會在某地建立持久家園或社群。"},{"en":"A science-fiction story may imagine that humankind will ultimately settle beyond Earth.","zh":"科幻故事可能想像人類最終會定居地球以外。"},{"en":"People support this idea because settling elsewhere could protect civilisation from disasters on Earth.","zh":"有人支持這個想法，因為在其他地方定居可能保護文明免受地球災難影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a long-term future vision for humanity.","zh":"這個短語描述人類的長遠未來願景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"must be Mars","meaning":"必然是火星","examples":[{"en":"If humans settle another planet, the destination may have to be Mars.","zh":"如果人類定居另一顆行星，目的地可能必然是火星。"},{"en":"Must be Mars means Mars appears to be the necessary or most logical choice.","zh":"must be Mars 指火星似乎是必要或最合邏輯的選擇。"},{"en":"If a school wants a quiet place for exams, the best room must be the library.","zh":"如果學校想找安靜地方考試，最佳房間必然是圖書館。"},{"en":"Mars may be the required choice because other nearby bodies lack enough useful resources.","zh":"火星可能成為必要選擇，因為其他附近天體缺乏足夠有用資源。"},{"en":"The phrase presents Mars as the strongest or unavoidable option.","zh":"這個短語把火星呈現為最強或無可避免的選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"much more distant than","meaning":"比……遠得多","examples":[{"en":"Mars is much more distant than the Moon.","zh":"火星比月球遠得多。"},{"en":"Much more distant than means far farther away than another place or object.","zh":"much more distant than 指比另一地方或物體遠得多。"},{"en":"A university overseas is much more distant than a college in the same city.","zh":"海外大學比同城學院遠得多。"},{"en":"Greater distance increases travel time, cost, communication delay, and emergency difficulty.","zh":"距離更遠會增加旅程時間、成本、通訊延遲和緊急處理難度。"},{"en":"The phrase makes a strong comparison in distance.","zh":"這個短語對距離作出強烈比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make the logistics daunting","meaning":"令後勤安排極為艱巨","examples":[{"en":"The planet’s distance makes the logistics daunting.","zh":"這顆行星的距離令後勤安排極為艱巨。"},{"en":"To make the logistics daunting means to make planning, transport, timing, and supply extremely difficult.","zh":"make the logistics daunting 指令規劃、運輸、時間安排和供應變得極其困難。"},{"en":"Organising a school trip for 300 students can make the logistics daunting if transport and meals are not planned early.","zh":"如果交通和膳食沒有早早規劃，組織三百名學生的學校旅行會令後勤安排極為艱巨。"},{"en":"Distance makes logistics harder because every mistake becomes expensive and difficult to fix.","zh":"距離令後勤更困難，因為每個錯誤都變得昂貴且難以修正。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical planning becoming intimidatingly complex.","zh":"這個短語描述實際規劃變得令人卻步地複雜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"logistics","meaning":"後勤安排","examples":[{"en":"A Mars mission involves extremely complex logistics.","zh":"火星任務涉及極其複雜的後勤安排。"},{"en":"Logistics are the practical arrangements for moving people, equipment, supplies, and information.","zh":"logistics 指移動人員、設備、物資和資訊的實際安排。"},{"en":"A hospital vaccination programme needs careful logistics, including storage, staffing, and appointments.","zh":"醫院疫苗接種計劃需要仔細後勤安排，包括儲存、人手和預約。"},{"en":"Poor logistics can cause delays even when the main idea is good.","zh":"即使主要想法很好，差劣後勤安排也可以造成延誤。"},{"en":"The word refers to practical planning and coordination.","zh":"這個詞指實際規劃和協調。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"life-support systems","meaning":"生命維持系統","examples":[{"en":"A long journey requires reliable life-support systems.","zh":"長途旅程需要可靠的生命維持系統。"},{"en":"Life-support systems are machines and systems that provide air, water, temperature control, and other conditions needed for survival.","zh":"life-support systems 指提供空氣、水、溫度控制和其他生存所需條件的機器和系統。"},{"en":"A submarine needs life-support systems because people inside cannot simply open a window for air.","zh":"潛艇需要生命維持系統，因為裏面的人不能簡單開窗透氣。"},{"en":"In space, life-support systems must work continuously because failure could quickly become fatal.","zh":"在太空中，生命維持系統必須持續運作，因為故障很快可能致命。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to technology that keeps people alive in hostile environments.","zh":"這個短語指在惡劣環境中維持人命的科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"too heavy for","meaning":"對……來說太重","examples":[{"en":"Current life-support equipment may be too heavy for existing rockets.","zh":"現有生命維持設備對現有火箭來說可能太重。"},{"en":"Too heavy for something means heavier than that thing can safely carry or support.","zh":"too heavy for something 指重量超過某物能安全承載或支撐的程度。"},{"en":"A large sofa may be too heavy for one person to move alone.","zh":"大型梳化對一個人來說可能太重，無法獨自搬動。"},{"en":"If equipment is too heavy for a rocket, engineers must reduce weight or improve launch power.","zh":"如果設備對火箭來說太重，工程師必須減重或提高發射能力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a mismatch between weight and carrying capacity.","zh":"這個短語描述重量與承載能力不匹配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"current rocket technology","meaning":"現有火箭技術","examples":[{"en":"Current rocket technology cannot easily carry all the necessary supplies.","zh":"現有火箭技術不能輕易運載所有必要物資。"},{"en":"Current rocket technology means the rocket systems and launch abilities available now.","zh":"current rocket technology 指目前可用的火箭系統和發射能力。"},{"en":"Current rocket technology can send probes to other planets, but carrying a whole human settlement is far harder.","zh":"現有火箭技術可以把探測器送往其他行星，但運載整個人類殖民地困難得多。"},{"en":"Technology limits matter because every kilogram launched into space adds cost and difficulty.","zh":"科技限制很重要，因為每一公斤被送上太空都增加成本和難度。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to present launch capability, not future breakthroughs.","zh":"這個短語指目前發射能力，而不是未來突破。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"technological innovations","meaning":"科技創新","examples":[{"en":"A Mars mission would require major technological innovations.","zh":"火星任務需要重大科技創新。"},{"en":"Technological innovations are new or improved tools, machines, systems, or methods.","zh":"technological innovations 指新的或改良的工具、機器、系統或方法。"},{"en":"Electric buses became more practical because of technological innovations in batteries.","zh":"電動巴士因電池方面的科技創新而變得更實用。"},{"en":"Space missions need innovation when existing technology cannot solve weight, safety, or distance problems.","zh":"當現有科技不能解決重量、安全或距離問題，太空任務就需要創新。"},{"en":"The phrase describes new technology created to meet difficult needs.","zh":"這個短語描述為應對困難需要而創造的新科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be absolutely critical","meaning":"極為關鍵","examples":[{"en":"The timing of a Mars launch would be absolutely critical.","zh":"火星發射的時間安排極為關鍵。"},{"en":"To be absolutely critical means to be extremely important and impossible to ignore.","zh":"be absolutely critical 指極其重要，而且不能忽視。"},{"en":"In surgery, clean equipment is absolutely critical because infection can be life-threatening.","zh":"在手術中，乾淨設備極為關鍵，因為感染可能危及生命。"},{"en":"If something is absolutely critical, failure in that area can endanger the whole plan.","zh":"如果某事極為關鍵，該方面失敗可能危及整個計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase means essential, not merely helpful.","zh":"這個短語意思是不可或缺，而不只是有幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"different orbits","meaning":"不同軌道","examples":[{"en":"Mars and Earth travel around the Sun in different orbits.","zh":"火星和地球沿不同軌道繞太陽運行。"},{"en":"Different orbits are different paths that objects follow as they move around another body in space.","zh":"different orbits 指物體在太空中繞另一個天體移動時所跟隨的不同路徑。"},{"en":"Satellites in different orbits pass over different parts of Earth at different times.","zh":"處於不同軌道的衛星會在不同時間經過地球不同地區上空。"},{"en":"Because Earth and Mars have different orbits, the distance between them keeps changing.","zh":"因為地球和火星有不同軌道，它們之間的距離會不斷改變。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why timing matters in space travel.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何太空旅行中時間安排很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"approach each other","meaning":"互相接近","examples":[{"en":"The two planets approach each other most closely at regular intervals.","zh":"這兩顆行星會定期最接近彼此。"},{"en":"To approach each other means to move nearer to one another.","zh":"approach each other 指彼此移動得更近。"},{"en":"Two trains approach each other as they travel toward the same station from opposite directions.","zh":"兩列火車從相反方向駛向同一車站時，會互相接近。"},{"en":"When Earth and Mars approach each other, a spacecraft needs less time and fuel to travel between them.","zh":"當地球和火星互相接近，太空船在兩者之間旅行需要較少時間和燃料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes distance becoming smaller.","zh":"這個短語描述距離變小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"every 26 months","meaning":"每二十六個月","examples":[{"en":"Mars and Earth approach each other closely every 26 months.","zh":"火星和地球每二十六個月會互相接近一次。"},{"en":"Every 26 months means once in each period of twenty-six months.","zh":"every 26 months 指每二十六個月這段時間出現一次。"},{"en":"A professional certificate may need renewal every 26 months if the rules require it.","zh":"如果規則要求，專業證書可能每二十六個月需要續期。"},{"en":"If launch chances come every 26 months, missing one opportunity can delay a mission for years.","zh":"如果發射機會每二十六個月才出現，錯過一次機會可能令任務延遲多年。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a repeated time interval.","zh":"這個短語描述重複出現的時間間隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fluctuate on a cycle","meaning":"按周期波動","examples":[{"en":"The distance between the planets fluctuates on a 15-year cycle.","zh":"兩顆行星之間的距離按十五年周期波動。"},{"en":"To fluctuate on a cycle means to rise and fall or change repeatedly according to a pattern.","zh":"fluctuate on a cycle 指按照某模式反覆上升、下降或改變。"},{"en":"A shop’s sales may fluctuate on a yearly cycle, rising during holidays and falling afterward.","zh":"小店銷售可能按年度周期波動，在假期上升，之後下降。"},{"en":"Cyclical fluctuation matters because planning depends on knowing when conditions are best.","zh":"周期性波動很重要，因為規劃取決於知道何時條件最佳。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated change over a regular or long-term pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述按規律或長期模式重複變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"launch window","meaning":"發射時機；發射窗口","examples":[{"en":"A suitable launch window opens only at particular times.","zh":"合適的發射窗口只在特定時間出現。"},{"en":"A launch window is the limited period when a spacecraft can be launched most efficiently or safely.","zh":"launch window 指太空船能最有效或最安全發射的有限時段。"},{"en":"An airport has a similar idea when planes must depart during an assigned time slot.","zh":"機場也有類似概念，飛機必須在指定時段出發。"},{"en":"Space missions depend on launch windows because planets move and distances change.","zh":"太空任務取決於發射窗口，因為行星會移動，距離會改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the correct timing for launching a mission.","zh":"這個短語指發射任務的正確時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"open once in that time","meaning":"在該段時間只出現一次","examples":[{"en":"The best launch window opens only once during the longer cycle.","zh":"最佳發射窗口在較長周期中只出現一次。"},{"en":"Open once in that time means become available only one time within a stated period.","zh":"open once in that time 指在指定時段內只變得可用一次。"},{"en":"A scholarship may open once in that time if applications are accepted only every two years.","zh":"如果獎學金每兩年才接受申請一次，它就在該段時間只出現一次。"},{"en":"When an opportunity opens only once, missing it creates a long delay.","zh":"當機會只出現一次，錯過它會造成長時間延誤。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses rarity within a specific time span.","zh":"這個短語強調某一時段內的罕有性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"few and far between","meaning":"十分罕有","examples":[{"en":"Ideal opportunities for launching are few and far between.","zh":"理想發射機會十分罕有。"},{"en":"Few and far between means rare and not happening often.","zh":"few and far between 指罕見而且不常發生。"},{"en":"Quiet seats in a crowded library are few and far between during exam season.","zh":"考試季節中，擁擠圖書館裏安靜座位十分罕有。"},{"en":"When opportunities are few and far between, careful preparation becomes even more important.","zh":"當機會十分罕有，仔細準備就變得更加重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something uncommon and widely spaced in time or place.","zh":"這個短語描述在時間或地點上不常出現、相隔很遠的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"missions must leave at these times","meaning":"任務必須在這些時段出發","examples":[{"en":"Mars missions must leave during the correct launch windows.","zh":"火星任務必須在正確發射窗口期間出發。"},{"en":"Missions must leave at these times means the departure must happen during the limited periods when travel is possible or efficient.","zh":"missions must leave at these times 指任務必須在旅行可行或有效的有限時段內出發。"},{"en":"A ferry trip must leave at the scheduled time because the tide may become unsafe later.","zh":"渡輪旅程必須在預定時間出發，因為稍後潮汐可能變得不安全。"},{"en":"Space missions follow strict timing because the planets will not stay in the same positions.","zh":"太空任務遵從嚴格時間安排，因為行星不會停留在相同位置。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that timing controls departure.","zh":"這個短語強調時間安排控制出發。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the trouble is","meaning":"問題是","examples":[{"en":"The trouble is that the return journey would take more than a year.","zh":"問題是回程旅程需要超過一年。"},{"en":"The trouble is introduces the main problem or difficulty in a situation.","zh":"the trouble is 引入某情況中的主要問題或困難。"},{"en":"The plan sounds simple; the trouble is that no one has enough time to organise it.","zh":"這個計劃聽起來簡單；問題是沒有人有足夠時間組織它。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when a positive idea has a serious hidden difficulty.","zh":"當一個正面想法背後有嚴重隱藏困難，作者會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It signals that an obstacle is about to be explained.","zh":"它表示接下來會解釋障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"journey to Mars and back","meaning":"往返火星的旅程","examples":[{"en":"A journey to Mars and back would be extremely lengthy.","zh":"往返火星的旅程會極其漫長。"},{"en":"A journey to Mars and back means travelling from Earth to Mars and then returning to Earth.","zh":"journey to Mars and back 指從地球前往火星，然後返回地球。"},{"en":"A school project might calculate how much food astronauts need for a journey to Mars and back.","zh":"學校項目可能計算太空人在往返火星的旅程中需要多少食物。"},{"en":"A return journey adds time, fuel, equipment, and health risks to the mission.","zh":"回程旅程會增加任務的時間、燃料、設備和健康風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the complete round trip, not just arrival on Mars.","zh":"這個短語描述完整來回旅程，而不只是到達火星。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take over a year","meaning":"需時超過一年","examples":[{"en":"The complete journey would take over a year.","zh":"完整旅程需時超過一年。"},{"en":"To take over a year means to require more than twelve months to finish.","zh":"take over a year 指需要超過十二個月才能完成。"},{"en":"Building a new school hall may take over a year if planning approval is slow.","zh":"如果規劃審批緩慢，興建新學校禮堂可能需時超過一年。"},{"en":"A journey that takes over a year creates problems with supplies, health, and morale.","zh":"需時超過一年的旅程會造成物資、健康和士氣問題。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a very long duration.","zh":"這個短語強調非常長的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"suffer profoundly","meaning":"受到嚴重影響","examples":[{"en":"The human body suffers profoundly during prolonged microgravity.","zh":"人體在長時間微重力下會受到嚴重影響。"},{"en":"To suffer profoundly means to be affected very seriously or deeply.","zh":"suffer profoundly 指受到非常嚴重或深刻影響。"},{"en":"A student’s concentration can suffer profoundly if she sleeps only four hours each night.","zh":"如果學生每晚只睡四小時，她的專注力可能受到嚴重影響。"},{"en":"The body suffers profoundly in space because muscles, bones, lungs, and immunity can all weaken.","zh":"人體在太空中受到嚴重影響，因為肌肉、骨骼、肺部和免疫力都可能變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes severe harm, not mild discomfort.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重傷害，而不是輕微不適。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"microgravity","meaning":"微重力","examples":[{"en":"Astronauts experience microgravity during long space missions.","zh":"太空人在長期太空任務中會經歷微重力。"},{"en":"Microgravity is a condition in space where people and objects feel almost weightless.","zh":"microgravity 指太空中人和物體感覺幾乎失重的狀態。"},{"en":"In microgravity, a pen can float instead of falling onto a desk.","zh":"在微重力下，筆可以漂浮，而不是跌到桌上。"},{"en":"Microgravity affects the body because muscles and bones no longer work against normal weight.","zh":"微重力影響人體，因為肌肉和骨骼不再對抗正常重量。"},{"en":"The word refers to near-weightlessness, not the complete absence of gravity.","zh":"這個詞指接近失重，而不是完全沒有重力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"for that length of time","meaning":"長達那段時間","examples":[{"en":"Humans are not well adapted to microgravity for that length of time.","zh":"人類並不適應長達那段時間的微重力。"},{"en":"For that length of time means for such a long period as the one being discussed.","zh":"for that length of time 指持續達到正在討論的那麼長時間。"},{"en":"A student may struggle to sit still for that length of time during a three-hour exam.","zh":"在三小時考試中，學生可能難以長達那段時間保持不動。"},{"en":"The longer a difficult condition lasts, the more serious its effects may become.","zh":"困難狀況持續越久，其影響可能越嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase points back to a previously mentioned duration.","zh":"這個短語指回之前提到的時間長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"without the need to stand","meaning":"無需站立時","examples":[{"en":"Without the need to stand, astronauts use their muscles less.","zh":"無需站立時，太空人較少使用肌肉。"},{"en":"Without the need to stand means when a person no longer has to support body weight upright.","zh":"without the need to stand 指某人不再需要直立支撐體重時。"},{"en":"A patient in bed for weeks uses leg muscles less without the need to stand.","zh":"長期臥床的病人在無需站立時，較少使用腿部肌肉。"},{"en":"Muscles weaken when they are not required to hold the body against gravity.","zh":"當肌肉不需要對抗重力支撐身體，它們就會變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why weight-bearing movement matters.","zh":"這個短語解釋承重活動為何重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"flexing or pressure on","meaning":"對……的屈曲活動或壓力","examples":[{"en":"There is little flexing or pressure on the back and leg muscles.","zh":"背部和腿部肌肉幾乎沒有屈曲活動或壓力。"},{"en":"Flexing or pressure on muscles means bending, using, or loading muscles so they work against force.","zh":"flexing or pressure on muscles 指彎曲、使用或讓肌肉承受負荷，使它們對抗力量。"},{"en":"Walking upstairs creates flexing and pressure on leg muscles.","zh":"上樓梯會對腿部肌肉造成屈曲活動和壓力。"},{"en":"Without flexing or pressure, muscles receive fewer signals to stay strong.","zh":"如果沒有屈曲活動或壓力，肌肉接收到維持強壯的訊號就會減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the physical use that keeps muscles active.","zh":"這個短語描述令肌肉保持活躍的身體使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"leg muscles","meaning":"腿部肌肉","examples":[{"en":"Leg muscles gradually weaken in microgravity.","zh":"腿部肌肉在微重力中會逐漸變弱。"},{"en":"Leg muscles are the muscles in the thighs, calves, and lower body used for standing, walking, and balance.","zh":"leg muscles 指大腿、小腿和下半身中用於站立、行走和平衡的肌肉。"},{"en":"A runner trains leg muscles by climbing stairs, squatting, and jogging regularly.","zh":"跑手透過爬樓梯、深蹲和定期慢跑訓練腿部肌肉。"},{"en":"Leg muscles weaken when people do not stand or walk for long periods.","zh":"當人們長時間不站立或行走，腿部肌肉會變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to muscles needed for movement and support.","zh":"這個短語指移動和支撐所需的肌肉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"gradually shrink and weaken","meaning":"逐漸萎縮和變弱","examples":[{"en":"Unused muscles gradually shrink and weaken.","zh":"沒有使用的肌肉會逐漸萎縮和變弱。"},{"en":"To gradually shrink and weaken means to become smaller and less powerful little by little.","zh":"gradually shrink and weaken 指一點一點變小和力量變弱。"},{"en":"A broken arm in a cast may gradually shrink and weaken if it is not used for weeks.","zh":"如果手臂骨折後打石膏數星期不用，它可能逐漸萎縮和變弱。"},{"en":"Muscles shrink and weaken when the body no longer needs them to work hard.","zh":"當身體不再需要肌肉努力工作，肌肉就會萎縮和變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow physical decline caused by lack of use.","zh":"這個短語描述由缺乏使用造成的緩慢身體衰退。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lose bone density","meaning":"流失骨質密度","examples":[{"en":"Astronauts can lose bone density during long missions.","zh":"太空人在長期任務中可能流失骨質密度。"},{"en":"To lose bone density means to have bones become less dense, weaker, and more fragile.","zh":"lose bone density 指骨骼變得較不密實、較弱和較脆。"},{"en":"Older adults may lose bone density if they lack exercise, calcium, or sunlight.","zh":"如果長者缺乏運動、鈣質或陽光，可能流失骨質密度。"},{"en":"Bone density falls when bones are not stressed by normal standing, walking, and lifting.","zh":"當骨骼沒有受到正常站立、行走和舉重造成的壓力，骨質密度會下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weakening of the skeleton.","zh":"這個短語描述骨骼系統變弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"aerobic capacity","meaning":"帶氧能力","examples":[{"en":"The lungs may lose some of their aerobic capacity.","zh":"肺部可能失去部分帶氧能力。"},{"en":"Aerobic capacity is the body’s ability to use oxygen during sustained physical activity.","zh":"aerobic capacity 指身體在持續體力活動中使用氧氣的能力。"},{"en":"A student improves aerobic capacity by swimming, running, or cycling regularly.","zh":"學生透過定期游泳、跑步或踩單車改善帶氧能力。"},{"en":"If aerobic capacity falls, a person becomes tired more quickly during demanding tasks.","zh":"如果帶氧能力下降，一個人在高強度任務中會更快疲倦。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to endurance linked to oxygen use.","zh":"這個短語指與氧氣使用相關的耐力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be left long enough in space","meaning":"長時間逗留太空","examples":[{"en":"People left long enough in space may struggle to function normally.","zh":"長時間逗留太空的人可能難以正常活動。"},{"en":"To be left long enough in space means to remain in space for a period long enough to cause serious effects.","zh":"be left long enough in space 指留在太空中足夠長時間，以致造成嚴重影響。"},{"en":"A worker left long enough in an unsafe environment may develop health problems.","zh":"長時間留在不安全環境中的工人，可能出現健康問題。"},{"en":"Long exposure matters because small stresses can become severe when they continue for months.","zh":"長時間暴露很重要，因為小壓力持續數月後可能變得嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the effect of extended time in space.","zh":"這個短語強調在太空中長時間停留的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be unable to function properly","meaning":"無法正常活動","examples":[{"en":"Astronauts may become unable to function properly.","zh":"太空人可能變得無法正常活動。"},{"en":"To be unable to function properly means to be unable to work, move, think, or perform tasks normally.","zh":"be unable to function properly 指不能正常工作、移動、思考或完成任務。"},{"en":"A student who has a high fever may be unable to function properly in class.","zh":"發高燒的學生可能在課堂上無法正常活動。"},{"en":"If astronauts cannot function properly on arrival, the mission may fail at its most dangerous stage.","zh":"如果太空人到達時不能正常活動，任務可能在最危險階段失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious loss of normal ability.","zh":"這個短語描述正常能力的嚴重喪失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"full physical strength","meaning":"完整體力","examples":[{"en":"Crew members will need their full physical strength on arrival.","zh":"機組人員到達時需要完整體力。"},{"en":"Full physical strength means the complete bodily power needed to move, work, lift, react, and survive.","zh":"full physical strength 指移動、工作、搬運、反應和生存所需的完整身體力量。"},{"en":"Firefighters need full physical strength when carrying equipment up many flights of stairs.","zh":"消防員把設備搬上多層樓梯時，需要完整體力。"},{"en":"A Mars crew needs strength because landing, repairs, and emergencies may be physically demanding.","zh":"火星團隊需要體力，因為降落、維修和緊急事故可能很耗體力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes maximum working condition of the body.","zh":"這個短語描述身體的最高工作狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"alertness","meaning":"警覺性","examples":[{"en":"Space operations require physical strength and mental alertness.","zh":"太空操作需要體力和精神警覺性。"},{"en":"Alertness is the ability to stay awake, focused, and ready to notice danger or respond quickly.","zh":"alertness 指保持清醒、專注，並準備好注意危險或快速回應的能力。"},{"en":"A bus driver needs alertness to react when a child suddenly crosses the road.","zh":"巴士司機需要警覺性，以便在小孩突然過馬路時作出反應。"},{"en":"Low alertness can lead to mistakes, especially during complex or risky tasks.","zh":"警覺性低可能導致錯誤，尤其是在複雜或高風險任務中。"},{"en":"The word refers to mental readiness and attention.","zh":"這個詞指心理準備和注意力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"operational duties","meaning":"操作職務","examples":[{"en":"Astronauts must perform many demanding operational duties.","zh":"太空人必須執行許多高要求的操作職務。"},{"en":"Operational duties are practical tasks needed to run, control, repair, or manage a system or mission.","zh":"operational duties 指運行、控制、維修或管理系統或任務所需的實際工作。"},{"en":"In a hospital, operational duties include checking equipment, recording data, and moving patients safely.","zh":"在醫院中，操作職務包括檢查設備、記錄數據和安全移動病人。"},{"en":"Space missions depend on operational duties because small practical tasks keep the whole mission working.","zh":"太空任務依賴操作職務，因為小型實際工作維持整個任務運作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to necessary hands-on work.","zh":"這個短語指必要的實際操作工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dock in space","meaning":"在太空對接","examples":[{"en":"The crew may need to dock in space before continuing the mission.","zh":"機組人員可能需要在繼續任務前在太空對接。"},{"en":"To dock in space means to connect one spacecraft with another spacecraft or station while in orbit.","zh":"dock in space 指在軌道上把一艘太空船與另一艘太空船或太空站連接。"},{"en":"Astronauts must dock in space carefully because even a small mistake can damage equipment.","zh":"太空人必須小心在太空對接，因為即使小錯誤也可能損壞設備。"},{"en":"Docking allows crews to transfer people, fuel, supplies, or modules between spacecraft.","zh":"對接讓人員、燃料、物資或艙段能在太空船之間轉移。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a precise connection operation in space.","zh":"這個短語描述太空中的精確連接操作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"approaches and landing","meaning":"接近及降落程序","examples":[{"en":"Approaches and landing on Mars require great concentration.","zh":"接近及降落火星的程序需要高度集中。"},{"en":"Approaches and landing are the final movements toward a destination and the act of touching down safely.","zh":"approaches and landing 指朝目的地最後接近的動作，以及安全着陸的行為。"},{"en":"Pilots must stay focused during approaches and landing because the aircraft is close to the ground.","zh":"飛行員在接近及降落程序中必須保持專注，因為飛機接近地面。"},{"en":"On Mars, approaches and landing are dangerous because the craft must slow down, aim accurately, and avoid hazards.","zh":"在火星上，接近及降落程序很危險，因為太空船必須減速、準確瞄準並避開危險。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the critical final stage of arrival.","zh":"這個短語指抵達時的關鍵最後階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"remote manipulation of machines","meaning":"遙距操控機器","examples":[{"en":"Astronauts may perform the remote manipulation of machines.","zh":"太空人可能進行遙距操控機器。"},{"en":"Remote manipulation of machines means controlling machines from a distance rather than touching them directly.","zh":"remote manipulation of machines 指從遠處控制機器，而不是直接觸碰它們。"},{"en":"A surgeon may use remote manipulation of machines to operate a robot-assisted surgical tool.","zh":"外科醫生可能使用遙距操控機器來操作機械人輔助手術工具。"},{"en":"On Mars, remote manipulation could let astronauts move rovers or arms without leaving a safe shelter.","zh":"在火星上，遙距操控可以讓太空人在不離開安全庇護所下移動探測車或機械臂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes operating equipment from afar.","zh":"這個短語描述從遠處操作設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"deal with emergencies","meaning":"處理緊急情況","examples":[{"en":"The crew must be ready to deal with emergencies.","zh":"機組人員必須準備好處理緊急情況。"},{"en":"To deal with emergencies means to respond quickly and effectively to dangerous or urgent situations.","zh":"deal with emergencies 指快速而有效地回應危險或緊急情況。"},{"en":"A school needs clear plans to deal with emergencies such as fires or serious injuries.","zh":"學校需要清晰計劃來處理火警或嚴重受傷等緊急情況。"},{"en":"Space crews must deal with emergencies because help from Earth cannot arrive quickly.","zh":"太空團隊必須處理緊急情況，因為地球援助無法很快到達。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical crisis response.","zh":"這個短語描述實際危機應對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"emergencies that arise","meaning":"突發的緊急事故","examples":[{"en":"Astronauts must respond quickly to any emergencies that arise.","zh":"太空人必須迅速回應任何突發的緊急事故。"},{"en":"Emergencies that arise are urgent problems that appear suddenly or unexpectedly.","zh":"emergencies that arise 指突然或意外出現的緊急問題。"},{"en":"During a school trip, teachers must handle emergencies that arise, such as a lost student or sudden illness.","zh":"在學校旅行中，老師必須處理突發的緊急事故，例如學生走失或突然生病。"},{"en":"A mission needs trained people because unexpected emergencies can threaten safety.","zh":"任務需要受訓人員，因為突發緊急事故可能威脅安全。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to crises that happen during an activity.","zh":"這個短語指活動期間發生的危機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"another hazard","meaning":"另一項危險","examples":[{"en":"Another hazard of a long mission is the spread of disease.","zh":"長期任務的另一項危險是疾病傳播。"},{"en":"Another hazard means an additional danger or risk besides those already mentioned.","zh":"another hazard 指除了已提到的危險之外，另一個額外風險。"},{"en":"During heavy rain, slippery stairs are one hazard; another hazard is poor visibility on the road.","zh":"大雨期間，濕滑樓梯是一項危險；另一項危險是路面能見度低。"},{"en":"Listing another hazard helps show that a situation has more than one kind of danger.","zh":"列出另一項危險幫助顯示一個情況不只有一種風險。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an extra risk.","zh":"這個短語引入額外風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"such duration","meaning":"如此長的時間","examples":[{"en":"A journey of such duration creates serious health risks.","zh":"如此長時間的旅程會造成嚴重健康風險。"},{"en":"Such duration means a period as long as the one being discussed.","zh":"such duration 指與正在討論的時間一樣長的一段期間。"},{"en":"A meeting of such duration would need breaks so participants can stay focused.","zh":"如此長時間的會議需要休息，讓參加者保持專注。"},{"en":"Long duration increases risk because tiredness, stress, and small problems build up over time.","zh":"時間長會增加風險，因為疲勞、壓力和小問題會隨時間累積。"},{"en":"The phrase points back to a long time already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指回已提到的長時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hermetically sealed spacecraft","meaning":"密封太空船","examples":[{"en":"The crew would live inside a hermetically sealed spacecraft.","zh":"機組人員會住在密封太空船內。"},{"en":"A hermetically sealed spacecraft is a spacecraft closed tightly so air, gas, and contamination cannot easily pass in or out.","zh":"hermetically sealed spacecraft 指緊密封閉、令空氣、氣體和污染物不易進出的太空船。"},{"en":"A laboratory container may be hermetically sealed to keep bacteria from entering a sample.","zh":"實驗室容器可能被密封，以防細菌進入樣本。"},{"en":"Sealing protects astronauts from space, but it also traps waste, moisture, and microbes inside.","zh":"密封能保護太空人免受太空環境影響，但也會把廢物、濕氣和微生物困在裏面。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an airtight and tightly controlled spacecraft environment.","zh":"這個短語描述密不透氣且受嚴格控制的太空船環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"constantly shed","meaning":"不斷脫落；排出","examples":[{"en":"Human bodies constantly shed biological material.","zh":"人體會不斷脫落或排出生物物質。"},{"en":"To constantly shed something means to release or lose it continuously over time.","zh":"constantly shed something 指隨時間持續釋出或失去某物。"},{"en":"People constantly shed tiny skin cells, even when they are simply sitting in a classroom.","zh":"人即使只是坐在課室中，也會不斷脫落微小皮膚細胞。"},{"en":"In a closed spacecraft, constantly shed material can build up and support microbial growth.","zh":"在封閉太空船中，不斷脫落的物質會累積並支持微生物生長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a continuous natural release.","zh":"這個短語描述持續的自然釋放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"waste material","meaning":"廢物","examples":[{"en":"The body produces many forms of waste material.","zh":"身體會產生多種形式的廢物。"},{"en":"Waste material is unwanted matter produced by living bodies, machines, homes, or workplaces.","zh":"waste material 指生物體、機器、家庭或工作場所產生的不需要物質。"},{"en":"A kitchen produces waste material such as food scraps, packaging, and dirty water.","zh":"廚房會產生廚餘、包裝和污水等廢物。"},{"en":"Waste material must be managed carefully in closed environments because it can cause smell, disease, or contamination.","zh":"在封閉環境中，廢物必須小心管理，因為它可能造成氣味、疾病或污染。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to material that must be removed, treated, or recycled.","zh":"這個短語指必須移除、處理或回收的物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"skin flakes","meaning":"脫落的皮屑","examples":[{"en":"Skin flakes can contribute to microbial growth in a spacecraft.","zh":"脫落的皮屑可以促成太空船內微生物生長。"},{"en":"Skin flakes are tiny pieces of dead skin that fall naturally from the body.","zh":"skin flakes 指自然從身體脫落的微小死皮碎片。"},{"en":"Dust in a bedroom often contains skin flakes from people who sleep there.","zh":"睡房中的塵埃常含有睡在那裏的人脫落的皮屑。"},{"en":"In a sealed spacecraft, skin flakes can become food or surfaces for microbes to grow on.","zh":"在密封太空船中，脫落的皮屑可以成為微生物生長的食物或表面。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to small shed pieces of skin.","zh":"這個短語指脫落的小塊皮膚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"products of digestion","meaning":"消化產物","examples":[{"en":"The products of digestion add to waste inside the spacecraft.","zh":"消化產物會增加太空船內的廢物。"},{"en":"Products of digestion are substances produced after the body breaks down food.","zh":"products of digestion 指身體分解食物後產生的物質。"},{"en":"In daily life, bathrooms and sewage systems remove products of digestion from homes safely.","zh":"在日常生活中，浴室和污水系統會安全地把消化產物帶離家居。"},{"en":"In space, products of digestion must be handled carefully because there is no normal drainage system.","zh":"在太空中，消化產物必須小心處理，因為沒有正常排水系統。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to bodily waste created by digestion.","zh":"這個短語指由消化產生的身體廢物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"allow microbes to breed","meaning":"讓微生物繁殖","examples":[{"en":"Organic waste allows microbes to breed rapidly.","zh":"有機廢物會讓微生物快速繁殖。"},{"en":"To allow microbes to breed means to create conditions where tiny organisms can multiply.","zh":"allow microbes to breed 指創造條件，使微小生物能繁殖。"},{"en":"Leaving wet food scraps in a bin can allow microbes to breed and create bad smells.","zh":"把濕廚餘留在垃圾桶中，可能讓微生物繁殖並產生臭味。"},{"en":"Warmth, moisture, and organic matter can allow microbes to breed quickly.","zh":"溫暖、濕氣和有機物可以讓微生物迅速繁殖。"},{"en":"The phrase describes conditions that support microbial growth.","zh":"這個短語描述支持微生物生長的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"breed prolifically","meaning":"大量繁殖","examples":[{"en":"Microbes can breed prolifically in warm, enclosed conditions.","zh":"微生物可以在溫暖、封閉條件下大量繁殖。"},{"en":"To breed prolifically means to reproduce in large numbers and very quickly.","zh":"breed prolifically 指大量而快速繁殖。"},{"en":"Mosquitoes may breed prolifically in standing water after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，蚊子可能在積水中大量繁殖。"},{"en":"If microbes breed prolifically in a spacecraft, infection risks can rise quickly.","zh":"如果微生物在太空船內大量繁殖，感染風險可以迅速上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rapid and abundant reproduction.","zh":"這個短語描述快速而大量的繁殖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"coughs and sneezes","meaning":"咳嗽和噴嚏","examples":[{"en":"Coughs and sneezes release fluids into the air.","zh":"咳嗽和噴嚏會把液體微粒釋放到空氣中。"},{"en":"Coughs and sneezes are sudden releases of air and droplets from the nose or mouth.","zh":"coughs and sneezes 指空氣和飛沫突然從鼻或口釋出。"},{"en":"In a classroom, coughs and sneezes can spread germs if students do not cover their mouths.","zh":"在課室中，如果學生不遮掩口部，咳嗽和噴嚏可以傳播細菌。"},{"en":"In microgravity, droplets from coughs and sneezes may not fall quickly to the floor.","zh":"在微重力下，咳嗽和噴嚏產生的飛沫可能不會很快落到地面。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to common actions that can spread infection.","zh":"這個短語指可能傳播感染的常見動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"spray fluids into the air","meaning":"將液體微粒噴到空氣中","examples":[{"en":"Coughs and sneezes spray fluids into the air.","zh":"咳嗽和噴嚏會將液體微粒噴到空氣中。"},{"en":"To spray fluids into the air means to send tiny liquid droplets outward through the air.","zh":"spray fluids into the air 指把微小液滴向外送入空氣中。"},{"en":"A perfume bottle sprays fluid into the air in very small droplets.","zh":"香水瓶會把液體以很小的液滴噴到空氣中。"},{"en":"When sick people spray fluids into the air, nearby people may breathe in germs.","zh":"當病人把液體微粒噴到空氣中，附近的人可能吸入病菌。"},{"en":"The phrase describes liquid particles being scattered through air.","zh":"這個短語描述液體粒子在空氣中散開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pull something down to surfaces","meaning":"把……拉落表面","examples":[{"en":"Gravity normally pulls airborne droplets down to surfaces.","zh":"重力通常會把空氣中的飛沫拉落到表面。"},{"en":"To pull something down to surfaces means to make it fall or settle onto floors, tables, walls, or other objects.","zh":"pull something down to surfaces 指使某物落下或停留在地板、桌子、牆壁或其他物體上。"},{"en":"Dust is pulled down to surfaces over time, which is why shelves need cleaning.","zh":"塵埃會隨時間被拉落到表面，所以架子需要清潔。"},{"en":"Without normal gravity, droplets may remain floating instead of being pulled down quickly.","zh":"沒有正常重力時，飛沫可能保持漂浮，而不是很快被拉落。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gravity moving particles from air to surfaces.","zh":"這個短語描述重力把粒子從空氣移到表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"airborne particles","meaning":"空氣懸浮粒子","examples":[{"en":"Without gravity, fluids may remain as airborne particles.","zh":"沒有重力時，液體可能以空氣懸浮粒子形式停留。"},{"en":"Airborne particles are tiny pieces of liquid or solid matter floating in the air.","zh":"airborne particles 指漂浮在空氣中的微小液體或固體物質。"},{"en":"Smoke contains airborne particles that can irritate the lungs.","zh":"煙含有會刺激肺部的空氣懸浮粒子。"},{"en":"Airborne particles are dangerous in enclosed spaces because people may breathe them in repeatedly.","zh":"空氣懸浮粒子在密閉空間中很危險，因為人們可能反覆吸入。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to small particles suspended in air.","zh":"這個短語指懸浮在空氣中的微小粒子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cramped confines","meaning":"狹窄密閉的空間","examples":[{"en":"Crew members must live together in cramped confines.","zh":"機組人員必須一起住在狹窄密閉的空間中。"},{"en":"Cramped confines are very small, crowded spaces with little room to move.","zh":"cramped confines 指非常細小、擠迫、幾乎沒有活動空間的地方。"},{"en":"Students may feel uncomfortable studying in cramped confines if a classroom is too full.","zh":"如果課室太擠，學生在狹窄空間中學習可能感到不舒服。"},{"en":"Cramped confines increase stress because people have little privacy or personal space.","zh":"狹窄密閉的空間會增加壓力，因為人們缺少私隱或個人空間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes tight physical surroundings.","zh":"這個短語描述狹窄的身體環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"microbial exchange","meaning":"微生物交換；交叉傳播","examples":[{"en":"Cramped living conditions cause easy microbial exchange.","zh":"狹窄生活條件會導致微生物容易交叉傳播。"},{"en":"Microbial exchange is the movement or sharing of microbes between people, surfaces, or environments.","zh":"microbial exchange 指微生物在人、表面或環境之間移動或共享。"},{"en":"In a crowded dormitory, microbial exchange can happen through shared bathrooms and close contact.","zh":"在擠迫宿舍中，微生物交換可以透過共用浴室和近距離接觸發生。"},{"en":"Microbial exchange increases infection risk when people live close together for long periods.","zh":"當人們長時間近距離生活，微生物交換會增加感染風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes germs passing from one place or person to another.","zh":"這個短語描述病菌從一個地方或一個人傳到另一處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"between crew members","meaning":"在機組人員之間","examples":[{"en":"Infections may pass easily between crew members.","zh":"感染可能很容易在機組人員之間傳播。"},{"en":"Between crew members means from one person in the team to another.","zh":"between crew members 指從團隊中的一個人傳到另一個人。"},{"en":"In a small office, colds may spread between workers who share the same air and equipment.","zh":"在小型辦公室中，感冒可能在共用空氣和設備的員工之間傳播。"},{"en":"Close contact between crew members makes hygiene and air cleaning very important.","zh":"機組人員之間的近距離接觸令衛生和空氣淨化非常重要。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on transmission within a team.","zh":"這個短語重點是團隊內部的傳播。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bacterial infections","meaning":"細菌感染","examples":[{"en":"Bacterial infections could be common during a long mission.","zh":"細菌感染在長期任務中可能很常見。"},{"en":"Bacterial infections are illnesses caused by harmful bacteria entering or growing in the body.","zh":"bacterial infections 指有害細菌進入或在身體內生長所造成的疾病。"},{"en":"A cut can lead to a bacterial infection if it is not cleaned properly.","zh":"如果傷口沒有妥善清潔，可能導致細菌感染。"},{"en":"In closed spacecraft, bacterial infections may spread more easily because people share air and surfaces.","zh":"在封閉太空船中，細菌感染可能較容易傳播，因為人們共用空氣和表面。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to disease caused by bacteria.","zh":"這個短語指由細菌造成的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fungal attacks","meaning":"真菌侵襲","examples":[{"en":"Fungal attacks may also occur inside a spacecraft.","zh":"真菌侵襲也可能在太空船內發生。"},{"en":"Fungal attacks are problems caused when fungi grow on the body, surfaces, or materials.","zh":"fungal attacks 指真菌在身體、表面或材料上生長所造成的問題。"},{"en":"Damp shoes can suffer fungal attacks if they are left wet for many days.","zh":"如果濕鞋放置多日不乾，可能受到真菌侵襲。"},{"en":"Fungi grow well in warm, moist spaces, so sealed spacecraft must control humidity carefully.","zh":"真菌在溫暖潮濕空間中生長良好，因此密封太空船必須小心控制濕度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes harmful fungal growth or infection.","zh":"這個短語描述有害真菌生長或感染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be prevalent","meaning":"普遍存在","examples":[{"en":"Infections may be prevalent in sealed living conditions.","zh":"在密封生活條件下，感染可能普遍存在。"},{"en":"To be prevalent means to be common or widespread in a place or situation.","zh":"be prevalent 指在某地方或情況中常見或廣泛存在。"},{"en":"Colds are prevalent in schools during winter because students spend time close together indoors.","zh":"冬天感冒在學校中普遍存在，因為學生長時間在室內近距離相處。"},{"en":"A problem becomes prevalent when conditions allow it to appear often.","zh":"當條件容許某問題經常出現，它就會變得普遍。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something occurring frequently.","zh":"這個短語描述某事頻繁發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"immune systems are weakened","meaning":"免疫系統變弱","examples":[{"en":"Human immune systems are weakened in microgravity.","zh":"人類免疫系統在微重力下會變弱。"},{"en":"Immune systems are weakened means the body becomes less able to fight infections and disease.","zh":"immune systems are weakened 指身體較不能抵抗感染和疾病。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can weaken immune systems and make students catch colds more easily.","zh":"睡眠不足可以令免疫系統變弱，使學生更容易感冒。"},{"en":"If astronauts’ immune systems are weakened, ordinary germs may become more dangerous.","zh":"如果太空人的免疫系統變弱，普通病菌可能變得更危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reduced bodily defence.","zh":"這個短語描述身體防禦能力降低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"air-cleansing system","meaning":"空氣淨化系統","examples":[{"en":"A Mars mission would require an advanced air-cleansing system.","zh":"火星任務需要先進空氣淨化系統。"},{"en":"An air-cleansing system is equipment that removes dust, droplets, microbes, or harmful substances from the air.","zh":"air-cleansing system 指從空氣中移除塵埃、飛沫、微生物或有害物質的設備。"},{"en":"A hospital uses air-cleansing systems to reduce infection risk in sensitive areas.","zh":"醫院在敏感區域使用空氣淨化系統，以降低感染風險。"},{"en":"In a sealed spacecraft, clean air is essential because the crew breathes the same air again and again.","zh":"在密封太空船中，清潔空氣很重要，因為機組人員反覆呼吸同一批空氣。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to technology that keeps air safe to breathe.","zh":"這個短語指保持空氣可安全呼吸的科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rigorous disinfecting procedures","meaning":"嚴格消毒程序","examples":[{"en":"The crew would need rigorous disinfecting procedures.","zh":"機組人員需要嚴格消毒程序。"},{"en":"Rigorous disinfecting procedures are strict cleaning steps designed to kill germs and prevent infection.","zh":"rigorous disinfecting procedures 指旨在殺滅病菌和防止感染的嚴格清潔步驟。"},{"en":"A clinic uses rigorous disinfecting procedures after treating a patient with a contagious illness.","zh":"診所治療傳染病患者後，會使用嚴格消毒程序。"},{"en":"Such procedures reduce risk because germs can survive on hands, tools, walls, and clothing.","zh":"這些程序降低風險，因為病菌可以在手、工具、牆壁和衣物上存活。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful, strict hygiene control.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細而嚴格的衛生控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hygiene procedures","meaning":"衛生程序","examples":[{"en":"Strict hygiene procedures would reduce infection risks.","zh":"嚴格衛生程序會降低感染風險。"},{"en":"Hygiene procedures are rules and actions for keeping people, equipment, and spaces clean and safe.","zh":"hygiene procedures 指保持人、設備和空間清潔安全的規則和行動。"},{"en":"Washing hands before cooking is a simple hygiene procedure at home.","zh":"煮食前洗手是家中簡單的衛生程序。"},{"en":"In closed living spaces, hygiene procedures prevent waste and germs from spreading.","zh":"在封閉生活空間中，衛生程序能防止廢物和病菌擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical cleanliness rules.","zh":"這個短語指實際清潔規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"an excellent supply of","meaning":"充足優良的……供應","examples":[{"en":"The spacecraft would need an excellent supply of antibiotics.","zh":"太空船需要充足優良的抗生素供應。"},{"en":"An excellent supply of something means a strong, reliable, and sufficient amount of it.","zh":"an excellent supply of something 指可靠、充足而質素良好的某物供應。"},{"en":"A school first-aid room needs an excellent supply of bandages during sports day.","zh":"學校急救室在運動日需要充足優良的繃帶供應。"},{"en":"A good supply matters when replacement is difficult or delayed.","zh":"當補給困難或延遲，良好供應就很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both quality and enough quantity.","zh":"這個短語同時強調質素和數量足夠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"antibiotics","meaning":"抗生素","examples":[{"en":"Antibiotics would be essential for treating infections.","zh":"抗生素對治療感染至關重要。"},{"en":"Antibiotics are medicines used to kill bacteria or stop them from growing.","zh":"antibiotics 指用來殺死細菌或阻止其生長的藥物。"},{"en":"A doctor may prescribe antibiotics for a serious bacterial throat infection.","zh":"醫生可能為嚴重細菌性喉嚨感染處方抗生素。"},{"en":"Antibiotics do not treat viruses, so they must be used carefully and only when appropriate.","zh":"抗生素不能治療病毒，因此必須小心並只在合適時使用。"},{"en":"The word refers to medicines against bacterial infections.","zh":"這個詞指對抗細菌感染的藥物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on reaching Mars","meaning":"到達火星時","examples":[{"en":"On reaching Mars, the astronauts would face further dangers.","zh":"到達火星時，太空人會面對更多危險。"},{"en":"On reaching Mars means when the astronauts arrive at Mars.","zh":"on reaching Mars 指太空人到達火星時。"},{"en":"On reaching a new school, students may first need to find their classroom and meet their teacher.","zh":"到達新學校時，學生可能首先需要找到課室並見老師。"},{"en":"Arrival does not end a difficult journey; new problems can begin at the destination.","zh":"抵達不會結束困難旅程；新問題可能在目的地開始。"},{"en":"The phrase marks what happens immediately after arrival.","zh":"這個短語標示抵達後立即發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"problems only increase","meaning":"問題只會增加","examples":[{"en":"Once the crew arrives, the problems only increase.","zh":"一旦機組人員抵達，問題只會增加。"},{"en":"Problems only increase means the difficulties become greater rather than disappear.","zh":"problems only increase 指困難變得更多，而不是消失。"},{"en":"If a student ignores missed lessons, the problems only increase before exams.","zh":"如果學生忽視缺課內容，考試前問題只會增加。"},{"en":"A Mars landing solves the travel problem but creates new survival and settlement problems.","zh":"火星降落解決了旅程問題，但創造新的生存和定居問題。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that reaching a goal may lead to more challenges.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們，達成目標可能帶來更多挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"significant length of time","meaning":"相當長的一段時間","examples":[{"en":"Staying on Mars for any significant length of time would be difficult.","zh":"在火星逗留相當長的一段時間會很困難。"},{"en":"A significant length of time is a long enough period to matter or create serious effects.","zh":"significant length of time 指長到足以產生重要影響的一段時間。"},{"en":"Sitting without movement for a significant length of time can make the legs stiff.","zh":"長時間不動坐着，可能令腿部僵硬。"},{"en":"On Mars, staying for a significant length of time requires food, shelter, air, water, and medical planning.","zh":"在火星逗留相當長一段時間，需要食物、庇護所、空氣、水和醫療規劃。"},{"en":"The phrase means more than a brief visit.","zh":"這個短語意思是不只是短暫到訪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the absence of","meaning":"在缺乏……的情況下","examples":[{"en":"In the absence of a thick atmosphere, the surface receives more radiation.","zh":"在缺乏厚大氣層的情況下，地表會接收更多輻射。"},{"en":"In the absence of something means when that thing is missing or not available.","zh":"in the absence of something 指在某物缺失或不可用時。"},{"en":"In the absence of clear instructions, students may complete the homework in different ways.","zh":"在缺乏清晰指示的情況下，學生可能用不同方式完成功課。"},{"en":"When protection is absent, risks that were normally controlled become more serious.","zh":"當保護缺失，原本受控制的風險會變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what happens when an important factor is missing.","zh":"這個短語解釋重要因素缺失時會發生甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"protective atmosphere","meaning":"具保護作用的大氣層","examples":[{"en":"Mars lacks a thick protective atmosphere.","zh":"火星缺乏厚而具保護作用的大氣層。"},{"en":"A protective atmosphere is a layer of gases that shields a planet from radiation, impacts, and extreme temperature changes.","zh":"protective atmosphere 指能保護行星免受輻射、撞擊和極端溫度變化影響的氣體層。"},{"en":"Earth’s protective atmosphere helps make outdoor life possible for humans.","zh":"地球具保護作用的大氣層幫助人類能在戶外生活。"},{"en":"Without a protective atmosphere, settlers need artificial shelters and special suits.","zh":"沒有具保護作用的大氣層，定居者需要人工庇護所和特殊太空衣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an atmosphere that acts like a natural shield.","zh":"這個短語描述像天然屏障一樣的大氣層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"magnetosphere","meaning":"磁層","examples":[{"en":"A magnetosphere can deflect dangerous particles.","zh":"磁層可以使危險粒子偏轉。"},{"en":"A magnetosphere is a region around a planet controlled by its magnetic field.","zh":"magnetosphere 指行星周圍由其磁場控制的區域。"},{"en":"Earth’s magnetosphere helps protect the planet from charged particles from the Sun.","zh":"地球磁層幫助保護地球免受來自太陽的帶電粒子影響。"},{"en":"Without a strong magnetosphere, a planet’s surface may receive more harmful space radiation.","zh":"沒有強大磁層，行星表面可能接收更多有害太空輻射。"},{"en":"The word refers to magnetic protection around a planet.","zh":"這個詞指行星周圍的磁性保護區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"burn up objects","meaning":"令物體燃燒殆盡","examples":[{"en":"A thick atmosphere can burn up some incoming objects.","zh":"厚大氣層可以令某些進入的物體燃燒殆盡。"},{"en":"To burn up objects means to make them heat, break apart, and disappear as they pass through an atmosphere.","zh":"burn up objects 指物體穿過大氣時被加熱、碎裂並消失。"},{"en":"Small meteors often burn up before reaching Earth’s surface.","zh":"小流星通常在到達地球表面前燃燒殆盡。"},{"en":"A thick atmosphere reduces danger because many small objects are destroyed before impact.","zh":"厚大氣層降低危險，因為許多小物體在撞擊前已被摧毀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes atmospheric protection through intense heating.","zh":"這個短語描述透過強烈加熱產生的大氣保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deflect objects","meaning":"使物體偏轉","examples":[{"en":"A magnetosphere can deflect charged particles away from a planet.","zh":"磁層可以把帶電粒子從行星旁偏轉出去。"},{"en":"To deflect objects means to turn them aside from their original path.","zh":"deflect objects 指使物體偏離原本路徑。"},{"en":"A goalkeeper can deflect a ball away from the goal with one hand.","zh":"守門員可以用一隻手把球從球門旁偏轉出去。"},{"en":"Deflection protects a planet when dangerous particles are pushed away before reaching the surface.","zh":"當危險粒子在到達地表前被推開，偏轉就能保護行星。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing the direction of moving objects.","zh":"這個短語描述改變移動物體方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be exposed to","meaning":"暴露於……","examples":[{"en":"Astronauts on the surface would be exposed to several hazards.","zh":"地表上的太空人會暴露於幾種危險之中。"},{"en":"To be exposed to something means to be left unprotected against it or come into contact with it.","zh":"be exposed to something 指在缺乏保護下受到某物影響，或與某物接觸。"},{"en":"Workers exposed to loud noise for years may suffer hearing problems.","zh":"長年暴露於巨大噪音中的工人，可能出現聽力問題。"},{"en":"On Mars, exposure to radiation is dangerous because there is little natural shielding.","zh":"在火星上，暴露於輻射很危險，因為天然屏障很少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes contact with risk or influence.","zh":"這個短語描述接觸風險或影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"potentially lethal","meaning":"可能致命的","examples":[{"en":"Solar radiation can be potentially lethal.","zh":"太陽輻射可能是致命的。"},{"en":"Potentially lethal means capable of causing death, even if it does not always do so.","zh":"potentially lethal 指有能力造成死亡，即使不一定每次都會如此。"},{"en":"A severe allergic reaction can be potentially lethal if treatment is delayed.","zh":"如果延遲治療，嚴重過敏反應可能致命。"},{"en":"A hazard is potentially lethal when one serious exposure or mistake could kill someone.","zh":"當一次嚴重暴露或錯誤可能殺死人，該危險就是可能致命的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a danger with possible fatal consequences.","zh":"這個短語描述可能帶來致命後果的危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ultraviolet radiation","meaning":"紫外線輻射","examples":[{"en":"Astronauts would need protection from ultraviolet radiation.","zh":"太空人需要防護，以免受紫外線輻射影響。"},{"en":"Ultraviolet radiation is invisible energy from the Sun that can damage skin, eyes, and living cells.","zh":"ultraviolet radiation 指來自太陽、看不見但能傷害皮膚、眼睛和活細胞的能量。"},{"en":"People use sunscreen to reduce harm from ultraviolet radiation at the beach.","zh":"人們在海灘使用防曬霜，以減少紫外線輻射的傷害。"},{"en":"Without atmospheric protection, ultraviolet radiation can become a serious danger on a planet’s surface.","zh":"沒有大氣保護時，紫外線輻射在行星表面可能成為嚴重危險。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a harmful form of solar radiation.","zh":"這個短語指一種有害太陽輻射。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"micrometeoroids","meaning":"微流星體","examples":[{"en":"Micrometeoroids may strike astronauts or surface structures.","zh":"微流星體可能撞擊太空人或地表結構。"},{"en":"Micrometeoroids are very small pieces of rock or metal moving through space at high speed.","zh":"micrometeoroids 指在太空中高速移動的非常小的岩石或金屬碎片。"},{"en":"A spacecraft needs shielding because even tiny micrometeoroids can cause damage when travelling fast.","zh":"太空船需要屏障，因為即使微小微流星體在高速下也能造成損害。"},{"en":"On a planet with little atmosphere, micrometeoroids are less likely to burn up before reaching the surface.","zh":"在大氣稀薄的行星上，微流星體在到達地表前較不容易燃燒殆盡。"},{"en":"The word refers to tiny space objects that can still be dangerous.","zh":"這個詞指微小但仍可能危險的太空物體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"solar flares","meaning":"太陽耀斑","examples":[{"en":"Solar flares release dangerous radiation and particles.","zh":"太陽耀斑會釋放危險輻射和粒子。"},{"en":"Solar flares are sudden bursts of energy from the Sun’s surface.","zh":"solar flares 指太陽表面突然爆發的能量。"},{"en":"Space weather reports monitor solar flares because they can affect satellites and communications.","zh":"太空天氣報告會監測太陽耀斑，因為它們可以影響衛星和通訊。"},{"en":"Solar flares are dangerous for astronauts because they can increase radiation exposure quickly.","zh":"太陽耀斑對太空人很危險，因為它們可以迅速增加輻射暴露。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to powerful solar eruptions.","zh":"這個短語指強大的太陽爆發。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"high-energy particles","meaning":"高能粒子","examples":[{"en":"High-energy particles regularly bombard the Martian surface.","zh":"高能粒子經常轟擊火星表面。"},{"en":"High-energy particles are tiny particles moving with enough energy to damage materials or living cells.","zh":"high-energy particles 指帶有足夠能量、能損害材料或活細胞的微小粒子。"},{"en":"Protective glass in a laboratory may be designed to block high-energy particles or radiation.","zh":"實驗室防護玻璃可能被設計來阻擋高能粒子或輻射。"},{"en":"On Mars, high-energy particles are dangerous because the planet has little natural protection.","zh":"在火星上，高能粒子很危險，因為行星幾乎沒有天然保護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fast, energetic particles from space or the Sun.","zh":"這個短語描述來自太空或太陽的高速高能粒子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"bombard the surface","meaning":"轟擊地表","examples":[{"en":"Radiation and particles regularly bombard the surface of Mars.","zh":"輻射和粒子經常轟擊火星地表。"},{"en":"To bombard the surface means to hit or strike the outer layer repeatedly and forcefully.","zh":"bombard the surface 指反覆而有力地撞擊或衝擊外層表面。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can bombard the surface of a roof for hours during a storm.","zh":"暴風雨期間，大雨可以連續數小時轟擊屋頂表面。"},{"en":"When particles bombard a surface, they can damage materials and threaten living tissue.","zh":"當粒子轟擊表面，它們可以損害材料並威脅活組織。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated impact or exposure.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆撞擊或暴露。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"land-based capsules","meaning":"地面太空艙","examples":[{"en":"Land-based capsules would protect astronauts on Mars.","zh":"地面太空艙會在火星上保護太空人。"},{"en":"Land-based capsules are enclosed living or working units placed on a planet’s surface.","zh":"land-based capsules 指放置在行星表面的封閉居住或工作單元。"},{"en":"A research station in Antarctica uses enclosed rooms in a similar way to protect people from extreme weather.","zh":"南極研究站使用封閉房間，以類似方式保護人免受極端天氣影響。"},{"en":"Capsules protect astronauts by giving them controlled air, temperature, and shielding.","zh":"太空艙透過提供受控空氣、溫度和屏障來保護太空人。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to surface shelters rather than spacecraft in orbit.","zh":"這個短語指地表庇護艙，而不是軌道上的太空船。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"special shielding","meaning":"特別屏障；防護層","examples":[{"en":"Living quarters would require special shielding.","zh":"居住艙需要特別防護層。"},{"en":"Special shielding is protective material or structure designed to block radiation, impacts, heat, or other dangers.","zh":"special shielding 指被設計來阻擋輻射、撞擊、熱力或其他危險的保護材料或結構。"},{"en":"A hospital X-ray room uses special shielding to protect staff and patients.","zh":"醫院 X 光室使用特別屏障來保護職員和病人。"},{"en":"On Mars, special shielding would reduce danger from radiation and small space objects.","zh":"在火星上，特別防護層會減少輻射和小型太空物體帶來的危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extra protection built into a place or object.","zh":"這個短語描述建在地方或物件中的額外保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"add to the weight and expense","meaning":"增加重量和開支","examples":[{"en":"Protective shielding adds to the weight and expense of the mission.","zh":"防護屏障會增加任務的重量和開支。"},{"en":"To add to the weight and expense means to make something heavier and more costly.","zh":"add to the weight and expense 指令某事變得更重和更昂貴。"},{"en":"Extra safety equipment can add to the weight and expense of a school camping trip.","zh":"額外安全設備可以增加學校露營旅行的重量和開支。"},{"en":"In space travel, every extra protective layer increases launch difficulty and budget pressure.","zh":"在太空旅行中，每一層額外防護都會增加發射難度和預算壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a practical trade-off between safety and cost.","zh":"這個短語描述安全與成本之間的實際取捨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"living quarters","meaning":"居住艙；生活區","examples":[{"en":"Settlers would need to construct secure living quarters.","zh":"定居者需要建造安全的居住艙。"},{"en":"Living quarters are the rooms or spaces where people sleep, rest, eat, and spend daily life.","zh":"living quarters 指人們睡覺、休息、進食和過日常生活的房間或空間。"},{"en":"A boarding school must provide clean and safe living quarters for students.","zh":"寄宿學校必須為學生提供清潔安全的生活區。"},{"en":"On Mars, living quarters must protect settlers from radiation, cold, pressure loss, and isolation.","zh":"在火星上，居住艙必須保護定居者免受輻射、寒冷、壓力流失和孤立影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical residential space.","zh":"這個短語指實際居住空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"time-consuming","meaning":"耗時的","examples":[{"en":"Building shelters on Mars would be time-consuming.","zh":"在火星上建造庇護所會很耗時。"},{"en":"Time-consuming means taking a lot of time to complete.","zh":"time-consuming 指需要很多時間才能完成。"},{"en":"Marking long essays is time-consuming because each sentence needs careful attention.","zh":"批改長作文很耗時，因為每一句都需要仔細注意。"},{"en":"A task becomes time-consuming when it has many steps, safety checks, or technical problems.","zh":"當任務有很多步驟、安全檢查或技術問題，它就會變得耗時。"},{"en":"The word describes something slow and demanding in terms of time.","zh":"這個詞描述在時間方面緩慢且要求高的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the only solution","meaning":"唯一解決方法","examples":[{"en":"For a long stay, the only solution may be to live underground.","zh":"對於長期逗留而言，唯一解決方法可能是住在地下。"},{"en":"The only solution means the single practical answer to a difficult problem.","zh":"the only solution 指某困難問題唯一實際可行的答案。"},{"en":"If a classroom roof is leaking badly, the only solution may be to repair it before lessons continue.","zh":"如果課室屋頂嚴重漏水，唯一解決方法可能是在繼續上課前維修。"},{"en":"On Mars, underground living may be the only solution if surface radiation is too dangerous.","zh":"在火星上，如果地表輻射太危險，地下居住可能是唯一解決方法。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that other options may not be realistic.","zh":"這個短語強調其他選項可能不現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"go underground","meaning":"轉到地下居住","examples":[{"en":"Settlers may need to go underground for protection.","zh":"定居者可能需要轉到地下居住以獲得保護。"},{"en":"To go underground means to move or live below the surface of the ground.","zh":"go underground 指移到或住到地面以下。"},{"en":"During extreme heat, some animals go underground to stay cool.","zh":"在極端高溫中，有些動物會到地下保持涼爽。"},{"en":"Mars settlers might go underground because soil and rock can block radiation better than thin air.","zh":"火星定居者可能轉到地下，因為土壤和岩石比稀薄空氣更能阻擋輻射。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using underground space as shelter.","zh":"這個短語描述使用地下空間作庇護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in this respect","meaning":"在這方面","examples":[{"en":"In this respect, Martian caves could be extremely valuable.","zh":"在這方面，火星洞穴可能極具價值。"},{"en":"In this respect means in this particular way or regarding this specific point.","zh":"in this respect 指以這種特定方式，或就這一點而言。"},{"en":"A small school may lack facilities; in this respect, a larger school has an advantage.","zh":"小學校可能缺乏設施；在這方面，較大型學校有優勢。"},{"en":"The phrase helps focus on one aspect of a comparison or argument.","zh":"這個短語幫助集中於比較或論點中的一個方面。"},{"en":"It means “when we consider this point.”","zh":"它的意思是「當我們考慮這一點時」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"possible cave entrances","meaning":"可能的洞穴入口","examples":[{"en":"Satellite images have revealed possible cave entrances.","zh":"衛星影像顯示可能的洞穴入口。"},{"en":"Possible cave entrances are openings that may lead into underground caves, though this has not yet been fully confirmed.","zh":"possible cave entrances 指可能通往地下洞穴的開口，但尚未完全確認。"},{"en":"Hikers may mark possible cave entrances on a map before a trained team checks them.","zh":"遠足者可能先在地圖上標記可能的洞穴入口，再由受訓團隊檢查。"},{"en":"On Mars, possible cave entrances are exciting because caves could provide shelter and resources.","zh":"在火星上，可能的洞穴入口令人興奮，因為洞穴可以提供庇護和資源。"},{"en":"The phrase shows uncertainty: the openings may be caves, but more evidence is needed.","zh":"這個短語顯示不確定性：那些開口可能是洞穴，但需要更多證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on the side of","meaning":"位於……側面","examples":[{"en":"The openings lie on the side of Arsia Mons.","zh":"這些開口位於 Arsia Mons 的側面。"},{"en":"On the side of something means located along its slope, edge, or outer part.","zh":"on the side of something 指位於某物的斜坡、邊緣或外側部分。"},{"en":"A small café may sit on the side of a hill, overlooking the town below.","zh":"小咖啡店可能位於山坡側面，俯瞰下方城鎮。"},{"en":"If cave openings are on the side of a volcano, they may be connected with old lava flows.","zh":"如果洞穴開口位於火山側面，它們可能與古老熔岩流有關。"},{"en":"The phrase describes position on a surface or slope.","zh":"這個短語描述在表面或斜坡上的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Martian volcano","meaning":"火星火山","examples":[{"en":"Arsia Mons is a large Martian volcano.","zh":"Arsia Mons 是一座大型火星火山。"},{"en":"A Martian volcano is a volcano located on Mars.","zh":"Martian volcano 指位於火星上的火山。"},{"en":"Students comparing planets may study a Martian volcano to learn how Mars once had major geological activity.","zh":"比較行星的學生可能研究火星火山，以了解火星曾有重大地質活動。"},{"en":"Volcanic areas may contain lava tubes, which could become useful shelters for future settlers.","zh":"火山地區可能含有熔岩管，而這些熔岩管可成為未來定居者的有用庇護所。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a volcanic feature on Mars.","zh":"這個短語指出火星上的火山地貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be identified in satellite imagery","meaning":"在衛星影像中被識別","examples":[{"en":"Seven possible entrances have been identified in satellite imagery.","zh":"七個可能入口已在衛星影像中被識別。"},{"en":"To be identified in satellite imagery means to be noticed or recognised in pictures taken from satellites.","zh":"be identified in satellite imagery 指在衛星拍攝的圖片中被注意到或認出。"},{"en":"Flooded roads can be identified in satellite imagery after a major storm.","zh":"大風暴後，水浸道路可以在衛星影像中被識別。"},{"en":"Satellite imagery helps scientists study places that are too distant or dangerous to visit directly.","zh":"衛星影像幫助科學家研究太遙遠或太危險而不能直接到訪的地方。"},{"en":"The phrase describes finding features through satellite pictures.","zh":"這個短語描述透過衛星圖片發現地貌特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"circular holes","meaning":"圓形洞口","examples":[{"en":"The images show several circular holes.","zh":"影像顯示幾個圓形洞口。"},{"en":"Circular holes are round openings or gaps in a surface.","zh":"circular holes 指表面上的圓形開口或缺口。"},{"en":"A builder may drill circular holes in a wall to install pipes or cables.","zh":"建築工人可能在牆上鑽圓形洞口，以安裝水管或電線。"},{"en":"On Mars, circular holes may suggest collapsed cave roofs or entrances to underground spaces.","zh":"在火星上，圓形洞口可能暗示洞穴頂部倒塌或通往地下空間的入口。"},{"en":"The phrase describes round surface openings.","zh":"這個短語描述圓形表面開口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"resemble the collapse of","meaning":"像是……倒塌","examples":[{"en":"The holes resemble the collapse of cave ceilings.","zh":"這些洞口像是洞穴頂部倒塌形成的。"},{"en":"To resemble the collapse of something means to look similar to the result of that thing falling down or breaking in.","zh":"resemble the collapse of something 指看起來與某物倒下或塌陷後的結果相似。"},{"en":"A broken roof may resemble the collapse of an old building after a storm.","zh":"風暴後破損屋頂可能像是舊建築倒塌。"},{"en":"Scientists use resemblance as a clue, but they still need more evidence before confirming the cause.","zh":"科學家把相似外觀當作線索，但仍需要更多證據才確認成因。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visual similarity to a collapse.","zh":"這個短語描述與倒塌現象在外觀上的相似。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cave ceilings","meaning":"洞穴頂部","examples":[{"en":"The openings may have formed when cave ceilings collapsed.","zh":"這些開口可能是在洞穴頂部倒塌時形成的。"},{"en":"Cave ceilings are the upper surfaces or roofs inside caves.","zh":"cave ceilings 指洞穴內部上方的表面或頂部。"},{"en":"Visitors should avoid unstable cave ceilings because falling rock can be deadly.","zh":"遊客應避免不穩定洞穴頂部，因為落石可能致命。"},{"en":"When cave ceilings collapse, holes may appear on the ground above the cave.","zh":"當洞穴頂部倒塌，洞穴上方地面可能出現洞口。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the roof-like upper part of a cave.","zh":"這個短語指洞穴中像屋頂一樣的上方部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"通往；導致","examples":[{"en":"The entrances may lead to larger cave formations.","zh":"這些入口可能通往更大型的洞穴結構。"},{"en":"To lead to a place means to connect to it or provide a route toward it.","zh":"lead to a place 指與某地連接，或提供前往該地的路線。"},{"en":"A narrow hallway may lead to a large school assembly hall.","zh":"狹窄走廊可能通往大型學校禮堂。"},{"en":"If Martian openings lead to caves, they could become important shelter sites.","zh":"如果火星開口通往洞穴，它們可能成為重要庇護地點。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe physical connection or cause-and-effect, depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可描述物理連接或因果關係，視語境而定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"extensive cave formations","meaning":"大型洞穴結構","examples":[{"en":"Scientists hope the openings lead to extensive cave formations.","zh":"科學家希望這些開口通往大型洞穴結構。"},{"en":"Extensive cave formations are large and connected underground cave structures.","zh":"extensive cave formations 指大型而互相連接的地下洞穴結構。"},{"en":"Tourists visit regions with extensive cave formations because there may be many chambers and tunnels.","zh":"遊客會到訪有大型洞穴結構的地區，因為那裏可能有許多洞室和隧道。"},{"en":"Extensive cave formations on Mars could offer more space for shelters, storage, and exploration.","zh":"火星上的大型洞穴結構可以為庇護所、儲存和探索提供更多空間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad underground cave systems.","zh":"這個短語描述廣闊地下洞穴系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lava tubes","meaning":"熔岩管","examples":[{"en":"Lava tubes could provide natural shelter for settlers.","zh":"熔岩管可以為定居者提供天然庇護。"},{"en":"Lava tubes are tunnel-like caves formed when the surface of flowing lava hardens while molten lava continues moving inside.","zh":"lava tubes 指流動熔岩表面硬化，而內部熔融熔岩繼續流動時形成的隧道狀洞穴。"},{"en":"Hikers sometimes visit old lava tubes in volcanic regions with trained guides.","zh":"遠足者有時會在受訓導遊帶領下，到火山地區參觀古老熔岩管。"},{"en":"Lava tubes may protect settlers because rock overhead can block radiation and impacts.","zh":"熔岩管可能保護定居者，因為上方岩石可以阻擋輻射和撞擊。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to natural volcanic tunnels.","zh":"這個短語指天然火山隧道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"offer the protection necessary","meaning":"提供所需保護","examples":[{"en":"Underground formations may offer the protection necessary for survival.","zh":"地下結構可能提供生存所需保護。"},{"en":"To offer the protection necessary means to provide the level of safety required for a person or system to continue living or working.","zh":"offer the protection necessary 指提供人或系統繼續生存或運作所需的安全程度。"},{"en":"A helmet offers the protection necessary for a cyclist’s head during a fall.","zh":"頭盔在單車手跌倒時，提供頭部所需保護。"},{"en":"Mars shelters must offer the protection necessary because the surface environment is dangerous.","zh":"火星庇護所必須提供所需保護，因為地表環境危險。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses protection that is essential, not optional.","zh":"這個短語強調保護是必要的，而不是可有可無。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"hostile terrain","meaning":"惡劣地形","examples":[{"en":"Martian settlers must survive in hostile terrain.","zh":"火星定居者必須在惡劣地形中生存。"},{"en":"Hostile terrain is land that is difficult or dangerous to move through or live on.","zh":"hostile terrain 指難以行走、穿越或居住的危險土地。"},{"en":"Mountain rescue teams train for hostile terrain with rocks, ice, cliffs, and sudden weather changes.","zh":"山地救援隊會為有岩石、冰、懸崖和突變天氣的惡劣地形接受訓練。"},{"en":"Hostile terrain increases risk because travel, construction, and emergency response become harder.","zh":"惡劣地形會增加風險，因為交通、建設和緊急應對都變得更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physically challenging land.","zh":"這個短語描述身體上具挑戰性的土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"additional benefit","meaning":"額外好處","examples":[{"en":"An additional benefit of caves is access to useful resources.","zh":"洞穴的額外好處是能接觸有用資源。"},{"en":"An additional benefit is an extra advantage beyond the main one already mentioned.","zh":"additional benefit 指已提到主要好處以外的另一個優勢。"},{"en":"A school garden teaches biology; an additional benefit is that students learn responsibility.","zh":"學校花園能教授生物；額外好處是學生學會責任感。"},{"en":"Caves may protect settlers, and their additional benefit is possible access to minerals or water.","zh":"洞穴可能保護定居者，而其額外好處是可能取得礦物或水。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces another positive point.","zh":"這個短語引入另一個正面重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"potential access to","meaning":"有可能取得……","examples":[{"en":"The caves may provide potential access to vital minerals.","zh":"洞穴可能提供取得重要礦物的可能途徑。"},{"en":"Potential access to something means a possible way to reach, obtain, or use it.","zh":"potential access to something 指可能到達、取得或使用某物的方法。"},{"en":"A new bus route gives students potential access to libraries and sports centres farther away.","zh":"新巴士路線讓學生有可能前往較遠的圖書館和運動中心。"},{"en":"Potential access matters only if people can actually reach and use the resource safely.","zh":"只有在人們真的能安全到達並使用資源時，潛在取得途徑才有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a possible but not yet guaranteed route to something useful.","zh":"這個短語描述通往有用事物的可能但未保證途徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"vital minerals","meaning":"重要礦物","examples":[{"en":"Future settlers would need access to vital minerals.","zh":"未來定居者需要取得重要礦物。"},{"en":"Vital minerals are essential natural materials needed for survival, construction, technology, or farming.","zh":"vital minerals 指生存、建築、科技或農業所必需的天然材料。"},{"en":"A community rebuilding after a storm needs vital materials such as stone, metal, and clean water supplies.","zh":"風暴後重建的社區需要石材、金屬和清潔水源等重要材料。"},{"en":"On Mars, vital minerals could help settlers make tools, shelters, chemicals, or soil treatments.","zh":"在火星上，重要礦物可以幫助定居者製造工具、庇護所、化學物或土壤處理物。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to minerals that are necessary, not merely useful.","zh":"這個短語指必要而不只是有用的礦物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"most importantly of all","meaning":"最重要的是","examples":[{"en":"Most importantly of all, the caves may contain frozen water.","zh":"最重要的是，這些洞穴可能含有冰封水源。"},{"en":"Most importantly of all introduces the single most important point in a list of reasons.","zh":"most importantly of all 引入一系列理由中最重要的一點。"},{"en":"A flat may be cheap and large; most importantly of all, it must be safe.","zh":"一個單位可能便宜又大；最重要的是，它必須安全。"},{"en":"This phrase tells readers that the next advantage outweighs the others.","zh":"這個短語告訴讀者，下一個優勢比其他優勢更重要。"},{"en":"It gives maximum emphasis to the final or strongest point.","zh":"它給最後或最強的一點最大強調。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"open up the possibility of","meaning":"開啟……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"The caves open up the possibility of permanent settlement.","zh":"這些洞穴開啟了永久殖民的可能性。"},{"en":"To open up the possibility of something means to make it possible or more realistic for the first time.","zh":"open up the possibility of something 指使某事首次變得可能或更現實。"},{"en":"Online lessons open up the possibility of learning from a teacher in another city.","zh":"網上課程開啟了向另一城市老師學習的可能性。"},{"en":"Martian caves open up settlement possibilities because they may provide protection and resources.","zh":"火星洞穴開啟殖民可能性，因為它們可能提供保護和資源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating a new opportunity.","zh":"這個短語描述創造新機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"independent settlement","meaning":"自給自足的殖民地","examples":[{"en":"Local resources could make an independent settlement possible.","zh":"本地資源可以令自給自足的殖民地成為可能。"},{"en":"An independent settlement is a community that can survive with limited outside support.","zh":"independent settlement 指能在有限外部支援下生存的社群。"},{"en":"A remote village becomes more independent if it can grow food, collect water, and generate power locally.","zh":"如果偏遠村落能本地種植食物、收集水和發電，它就變得更自給自足。"},{"en":"On Mars, an independent settlement would need local water, minerals, energy, and food production.","zh":"在火星上，自給自足的殖民地需要本地水、礦物、能源和食物生產。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses self-sufficiency rather than constant dependence.","zh":"這個短語強調自給自足，而不是持續依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"permanent settlement","meaning":"永久殖民","examples":[{"en":"Some caves may support permanent settlement on Mars.","zh":"有些洞穴可能支持火星上的永久殖民。"},{"en":"Permanent settlement means people living in a place for the long term rather than visiting temporarily.","zh":"permanent settlement 指人們長期居住在某地，而不是短暫到訪。"},{"en":"A research camp becomes a permanent settlement when families, services, and long-term housing appear.","zh":"當家庭、服務和長期房屋出現，研究營地就變成永久殖民地。"},{"en":"Permanent settlement requires resources, safety, social organisation, and ways to replace supplies.","zh":"永久殖民需要資源、安全、社會組織和補充物資的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lasting human habitation.","zh":"這個短語描述持久的人類居住。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the most exciting option","meaning":"最令人興奮的方案","examples":[{"en":"The most exciting option may be a one-way first mission.","zh":"最令人興奮的方案可能是首次任務採取單程形式。"},{"en":"The most exciting option is the choice that seems most interesting, bold, or full of possibility.","zh":"the most exciting option 指看起來最有趣、大膽或充滿可能性的選擇。"},{"en":"For a school exhibition, the most exciting option might be a live experiment rather than a poster.","zh":"對學校展覽而言，最令人興奮的方案可能是現場實驗，而不是海報。"},{"en":"A choice can be exciting because it solves problems in a dramatic or unusual way.","zh":"一個選擇令人興奮，可能是因為它以戲劇化或不尋常方式解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the option that attracts the strongest interest.","zh":"這個短語突出最吸引興趣的選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"attempt that on the first trip","meaning":"在首次旅程便作出嘗試","examples":[{"en":"Some proponents want to attempt permanent settlement on the first trip.","zh":"有些支持者希望在首次旅程便嘗試永久殖民。"},{"en":"To attempt that on the first trip means to try a difficult goal during the very first journey rather than later.","zh":"attempt that on the first trip 指在第一次旅程中嘗試困難目標，而不是留待之後。"},{"en":"A school team may attempt a full public performance on the first trip to a drama festival.","zh":"學校隊伍可能在第一次到戲劇節時，就嘗試完整公開演出。"},{"en":"Trying something on the first trip is risky because there is little experience to learn from.","zh":"在首次旅程便嘗試某事有風險，因為幾乎沒有經驗可借鑑。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses boldness and risk at the beginning.","zh":"這個短語強調開端時的膽量和風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in other words","meaning":"換言之","examples":[{"en":"In other words, the astronauts would not return to Earth.","zh":"換言之，太空人不會返回地球。"},{"en":"In other words introduces a clearer, simpler, or restated version of the previous idea.","zh":"in other words 引入前一個想法更清楚、更簡單或重新表述的版本。"},{"en":"The course is optional; in other words, students can choose whether to take it.","zh":"這課程是選修的；換言之，學生可以選擇是否修讀。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when they want to make a difficult point easier to understand.","zh":"當作者想令困難重點更易理解，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It signals that the same idea is being explained again.","zh":"它表示同一個想法正被重新解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"one-way journey","meaning":"單程旅程","examples":[{"en":"A one-way journey would halve the time spent travelling through space.","zh":"單程旅程會令太空旅行時間減半。"},{"en":"A one-way journey is a trip to a destination without a planned return to the starting point.","zh":"one-way journey 指前往目的地而沒有計劃返回起點的旅程。"},{"en":"Buying a one-way train ticket makes sense if a student is moving to another city permanently.","zh":"如果學生永久搬到另一個城市，購買單程火車票是合理的。"},{"en":"A one-way journey to Mars reduces travel time but creates permanent settlement problems.","zh":"前往火星的單程旅程減少旅行時間，但造成永久定居問題。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses going there without coming back.","zh":"這個短語強調去而不返。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"duration of space travel","meaning":"太空旅程的時長","examples":[{"en":"A one-way mission would reduce the duration of space travel.","zh":"單程任務會減少太空旅程的時長。"},{"en":"Duration of space travel means the amount of time spent travelling through space.","zh":"duration of space travel 指在太空中旅行所花的時間。"},{"en":"Scientists calculate the duration of space travel to plan food, water, oxygen, and medical supplies.","zh":"科學家計算太空旅程的時長，以規劃食物、水、氧氣和醫療物資。"},{"en":"A shorter duration reduces exposure to microgravity, isolation, and disease risk.","zh":"較短時長會減少暴露於微重力、孤立和疾病風險的時間。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how long the space journey lasts.","zh":"這個短語重點是太空旅程持續多久。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be immediately halved","meaning":"立即減半","examples":[{"en":"The total travel duration would be immediately halved.","zh":"總旅行時長會立即減半。"},{"en":"To be immediately halved means to be reduced by half at once.","zh":"be immediately halved 指立刻減少一半。"},{"en":"If a class is split into two equal groups, the number of students in each room is immediately halved.","zh":"如果一班學生被分成兩個相等小組，每間課室的人數就會立即減半。"},{"en":"Removing the return journey immediately halves the time astronauts spend travelling through space.","zh":"取消回程旅程會立即令太空人在太空旅行的時間減半。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a direct fifty-percent reduction.","zh":"這個短語描述直接減少百分之五十。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"technological challenges","meaning":"科技挑戰","examples":[{"en":"A shorter journey would reduce some technological challenges.","zh":"較短旅程會減少一些科技挑戰。"},{"en":"Technological challenges are difficulties involving machines, systems, engineering, or technical design.","zh":"technological challenges 指涉及機器、系統、工程或技術設計的困難。"},{"en":"Building a school website creates technological challenges such as security, storage, and user access.","zh":"建立學校網站會帶來安全、儲存和用戶存取等科技挑戰。"},{"en":"Mars missions face technological challenges because equipment must work far from Earth for a long time.","zh":"火星任務面對科技挑戰，因為設備必須長時間在遠離地球的地方運作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to problems that require technical solutions.","zh":"這個短語指需要技術解決方案的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"biological challenges","meaning":"生理方面的挑戰","examples":[{"en":"The one-way proposal would reduce some biological challenges.","zh":"單程方案會減少一些生理方面的挑戰。"},{"en":"Biological challenges are problems affecting living bodies, health, growth, disease, or physical survival.","zh":"biological challenges 指影響活體、健康、生長、疾病或身體生存的問題。"},{"en":"A hospital faces biological challenges when a virus spreads quickly among patients.","zh":"當病毒在病人之間快速傳播，醫院會面對生理方面的挑戰。"},{"en":"Space travel creates biological challenges because the human body is not built for microgravity and radiation.","zh":"太空旅行造成生理挑戰，因為人體不是為微重力和輻射而設。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to life and health-related difficulties.","zh":"這個短語指與生命和健康相關的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"financial challenges","meaning":"財政挑戰","examples":[{"en":"A return journey creates additional financial challenges.","zh":"回程旅程會造成額外財政挑戰。"},{"en":"Financial challenges are difficulties involving money, cost, funding, or budget limits.","zh":"financial challenges 指涉及金錢、成本、資金或預算限制的困難。"},{"en":"A family may face financial challenges if rent rises faster than income.","zh":"如果租金升幅快過收入，家庭可能面對財政挑戰。"},{"en":"Returning from Mars increases financial challenges because extra fuel, equipment, and supplies are needed.","zh":"從火星返回會增加財政挑戰，因為需要額外燃料、設備和物資。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to money-related obstacles.","zh":"這個短語指與金錢相關的障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"strong argument","meaning":"有力論據","examples":[{"en":"The shorter journey is a strong argument for a one-way mission.","zh":"較短旅程是支持單程任務的有力論據。"},{"en":"A strong argument is a powerful reason that supports a view or decision.","zh":"strong argument 指支持某觀點或決定的有力理由。"},{"en":"Lower cost is a strong argument for using public transport instead of driving every day.","zh":"較低成本是支持每天乘搭公共交通而不是駕車的有力論據。"},{"en":"An argument becomes strong when it solves a major problem or is supported by clear evidence.","zh":"當論據解決主要問題或得到清楚證據支持，它就變得有力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a persuasive reason.","zh":"這個短語描述具說服力的理由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be offset by","meaning":"被……抵銷","examples":[{"en":"The advantages are offset by the difficulty of permanent settlement.","zh":"這些優勢被永久殖民的困難抵銷。"},{"en":"To be offset by something means to be balanced, reduced, or cancelled out by a disadvantage or opposite factor.","zh":"be offset by something 指被某個缺點或相反因素平衡、減弱或抵銷。"},{"en":"The cheap price of a flat may be offset by high transport costs.","zh":"單位價格便宜這個優勢，可能被高交通費抵銷。"},{"en":"A one-way mission saves travel time, but that benefit is offset by the need to survive permanently on Mars.","zh":"單程任務節省旅行時間，但這個好處被必須永久在火星生存的需要抵銷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one factor reducing the value of another.","zh":"這個短語描述一個因素削弱另一個因素的價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"establish a permanent presence","meaning":"建立永久據點","examples":[{"en":"Settlers would have to establish a permanent presence on Mars.","zh":"定居者必須在火星建立永久據點。"},{"en":"To establish a permanent presence means to create a lasting base, community, or operation in a place.","zh":"establish a permanent presence 指在某地建立持久基地、社群或運作。"},{"en":"A university may establish a permanent presence in a city by opening a full campus there.","zh":"大學可能透過在某城市開設完整校園，建立永久據點。"},{"en":"On Mars, a permanent presence would require housing, supplies, power, communication, and social organisation.","zh":"在火星上，永久據點需要住房、物資、電力、通訊和社會組織。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses long-term existence, not a temporary visit.","zh":"這個短語強調長期存在，而不是短暫到訪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ongoing commitment","meaning":"持續承擔","examples":[{"en":"A permanent settlement requires ongoing commitment from Earth.","zh":"永久殖民地需要地球作出持續承擔。"},{"en":"Ongoing commitment is continued support, effort, money, or responsibility over time.","zh":"ongoing commitment 指隨時間持續提供的支持、努力、金錢或責任。"},{"en":"A school mentorship programme requires ongoing commitment from teachers, not just one meeting.","zh":"學校師友計劃需要老師持續承擔，而不只是一次會面。"},{"en":"Mars settlement would need ongoing commitment because supplies, repairs, and communication must continue.","zh":"火星殖民需要持續承擔，因為物資、維修和通訊必須繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long-term responsibility.","zh":"這個短語描述長期責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"delivery of food and supplies","meaning":"運送食物和物資","examples":[{"en":"The settlement would depend on the delivery of food and supplies.","zh":"殖民地會依賴食物和物資的運送。"},{"en":"Delivery of food and supplies means transporting essential items such as meals, tools, medicine, and equipment to a place.","zh":"delivery of food and supplies 指把膳食、工具、藥物和設備等必需品運送到某地。"},{"en":"During a flood, villages may depend on the delivery of food and supplies by rescue teams.","zh":"水災期間，村落可能依賴救援隊運送食物和物資。"},{"en":"If deliveries stop, a remote settlement can quickly face hunger, illness, and equipment failure.","zh":"如果運送停止，偏遠殖民地可能很快面對飢餓、疾病和設備故障。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to bringing necessary resources to people who need them.","zh":"這個短語指把必要資源帶給需要的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"unmanned spacecraft","meaning":"無人太空船","examples":[{"en":"Unmanned spacecraft could deliver supplies to the settlement.","zh":"無人太空船可以向殖民地運送物資。"},{"en":"An unmanned spacecraft is a spacecraft that operates without astronauts on board.","zh":"unmanned spacecraft 指沒有太空人在內運作的太空船。"},{"en":"A space agency may send an unmanned spacecraft before humans to test landing conditions.","zh":"太空機構可能先派無人太空船，測試降落條件，再派人類前往。"},{"en":"Unmanned spacecraft can reduce risk because no human life is directly on board during the flight.","zh":"無人太空船可以降低風險，因為飛行期間沒有真人生命直接在船上。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to robotic or automated spacecraft.","zh":"這個短語指機械人或自動化太空船。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"psychological effects","meaning":"心理影響","examples":[{"en":"Permanent isolation could have severe psychological effects.","zh":"永久隔離可能有嚴重心理影響。"},{"en":"Psychological effects are impacts on the mind, emotions, behaviour, mood, or mental health.","zh":"psychological effects 指對思想、情緒、行為、心情或心理健康的影響。"},{"en":"Long exam pressure can have psychological effects such as anxiety, irritability, and loss of confidence.","zh":"長期考試壓力可以造成焦慮、易怒和失去信心等心理影響。"},{"en":"Isolation can affect people psychologically because humans need social contact and variety.","zh":"隔離可以在心理上影響人，因為人類需要社交接觸和變化。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to mental and emotional consequences.","zh":"這個短語指心理和情緒後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"pioneers","meaning":"先驅；拓荒者","examples":[{"en":"The first permanent Martian settlers would be pioneers.","zh":"第一批永久火星定居者會是先驅。"},{"en":"Pioneers are people who are among the first to enter, explore, settle, or develop a new place or field.","zh":"pioneers 指最早進入、探索、定居或發展新地方或新領域的人。"},{"en":"Early doctors using a new treatment may be pioneers if they test it before it becomes common.","zh":"如果早期醫生在新療法普及前測試它，他們可能是先驅。"},{"en":"Pioneers face risk because they work before systems, rules, and support are fully developed.","zh":"先驅面對風險，因為他們在制度、規則和支援完全發展前工作。"},{"en":"The word describes first movers who open a path for others.","zh":"這個詞描述為後來者開路的先行者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"permanent isolation from Earth","meaning":"永久與地球隔離","examples":[{"en":"The settlers would face permanent isolation from Earth.","zh":"定居者會面對永久與地球隔離。"},{"en":"Permanent isolation from Earth means being separated from Earth for life, with no normal return or direct contact.","zh":"permanent isolation from Earth 指終身與地球分離，沒有正常回程或直接接觸。"},{"en":"A person moving to a remote island is isolated, but permanent isolation from Earth would be far more extreme.","zh":"搬到偏遠島嶼的人是孤立的，但永久與地球隔離會極端得多。"},{"en":"Such isolation could affect mental health because family, familiar places, and ordinary society would be unreachable.","zh":"這種隔離可能影響心理健康，因為家庭、熟悉地方和普通社會都無法接觸。"},{"en":"The phrase describes total and lasting separation from Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述與地球完全而持久的分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be crowded into","meaning":"擠在……之內","examples":[{"en":"The settlers would be crowded into confined living quarters.","zh":"定居者會擠在狹窄的居住空間之內。"},{"en":"To be crowded into a place means many people are forced to share a small space.","zh":"be crowded into a place 指許多人被迫共用一個狹小空間。"},{"en":"Students may be crowded into a small classroom if the school lacks enough rooms.","zh":"如果學校課室不足，學生可能被擠在小課室之內。"},{"en":"Crowding increases stress because people have little privacy and limited movement.","zh":"擁擠會增加壓力，因為人們幾乎沒有私隱，活動也受限制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes uncomfortable concentration of people in a tight area.","zh":"這個短語描述人群不舒適地集中在狹窄地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"confined living quarters","meaning":"狹窄的居住空間","examples":[{"en":"Confined living quarters could cause stress and conflict.","zh":"狹窄的居住空間可能造成壓力和衝突。"},{"en":"Confined living quarters are small enclosed spaces where people must live with limited privacy and movement.","zh":"confined living quarters 指人們必須在其中生活、私隱和活動空間有限的細小封閉空間。"},{"en":"Dormitory rooms can feel like confined living quarters if too many students share one room.","zh":"如果太多學生共用一間房，宿舍房間可能感覺像狹窄居住空間。"},{"en":"Confined living quarters increase conflict because people cannot easily escape noise, habits, or disagreement.","zh":"狹窄居住空間會增加衝突，因為人們難以避開噪音、習慣或分歧。"},{"en":"The phrase describes tight residential spaces.","zh":"這個短語描述狹小住宅空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the same companions","meaning":"同一批同伴","examples":[{"en":"The pioneers would live with the same companions indefinitely.","zh":"這些先驅會無限期與同一批同伴生活。"},{"en":"The same companions are the same people one continues to live, work, or travel with.","zh":"the same companions 指持續一起生活、工作或旅行的同一批人。"},{"en":"On a long school camp, students may become tired of spending every hour with the same companions.","zh":"在長時間學校營中，學生可能因每小時都與同一批同伴相處而感到疲倦。"},{"en":"Living with the same companions for years can strengthen friendship, but it can also create conflict.","zh":"與同一批同伴生活多年可以加強友誼，但也可能造成衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses lack of social variety.","zh":"這個短語強調缺乏社交變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"raise issues of whether","meaning":"引起……是否可行的問題","examples":[{"en":"The conditions raise issues of whether settlement is psychologically possible.","zh":"這些條件引起殖民在心理上是否可行的問題。"},{"en":"To raise issues of whether something is possible means to create serious questions about whether it can really happen.","zh":"raise issues of whether something is possible 指產生關於某事是否真的能做到的嚴肅問題。"},{"en":"A school’s lack of teachers raises issues of whether it can run extra classes safely.","zh":"學校缺乏老師會引起它是否能安全開辦額外課程的問題。"},{"en":"Harsh living conditions raise questions because human limits may be reached before technical limits are solved.","zh":"嚴酷生活條件會引起疑問，因為人類極限可能在技術限制解決前已被觸及。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces doubts about feasibility.","zh":"這個短語引入對可行性的懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"humanly feasible","meaning":"從人性角度是否可行","examples":[{"en":"Scientists question whether permanent isolation is humanly feasible.","zh":"科學家質疑永久隔離從人性角度是否可行。"},{"en":"Humanly feasible means possible for human beings to endure, perform, or achieve in real life.","zh":"humanly feasible 指人類在現實中能否承受、執行或達成。"},{"en":"Studying for sixteen hours every day may not be humanly feasible for most students.","zh":"對大多數學生而言，每天溫習十六小時可能並非從人性角度可行。"},{"en":"A plan can be technically possible but not humanly feasible if it ignores mental and physical limits.","zh":"如果計劃忽視心理和身體極限，它可以技術上可行，但從人性角度不可行。"},{"en":"The phrase judges whether humans can realistically cope with something.","zh":"這個短語判斷人類能否現實地應付某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"beg the question of why","meaning":"令人不禁問為何……","examples":[{"en":"The proposal begs the question of why humans should go at all.","zh":"這個提議令人不禁問，人類究竟為何要去。"},{"en":"To beg the question of why means to naturally make people ask why something should be done.","zh":"beg the question of why 指自然令人問某事為何應該做。"},{"en":"A very expensive school trip begs the question of why cheaper local learning is not enough.","zh":"非常昂貴的學校旅行令人不禁問，為何較便宜的本地學習不足夠。"},{"en":"Serious risk often begs the question of why the goal is worth pursuing.","zh":"嚴重風險常令人不禁問，目標為何值得追求。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a fundamental “why” question.","zh":"這個短語引入根本的「為何」問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"undertake such missions","meaning":"執行這類任務","examples":[{"en":"Some people question why humanity should undertake such missions.","zh":"有些人質疑人類為何應執行這類任務。"},{"en":"To undertake such missions means to begin and carry out missions of this kind.","zh":"undertake such missions 指開始並執行這一類任務。"},{"en":"A hospital may undertake such missions when it sends medical teams to disaster areas.","zh":"醫院派醫療隊到災區時，就是執行這類任務。"},{"en":"People question difficult missions when the cost, danger, and purpose are all serious.","zh":"當成本、危險和目的都很嚴重，人們會質疑艱難任務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes accepting responsibility for major operations.","zh":"這個短語描述承擔重大行動的責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"according to proponents","meaning":"據支持者所說","examples":[{"en":"According to proponents, space exploration is part of human destiny.","zh":"據支持者所說，太空探索是人類命運的一部分。"},{"en":"According to proponents means according to the people who support an idea or plan.","zh":"according to proponents 指根據支持某想法或計劃的人所說。"},{"en":"According to proponents of later school start times, teenagers learn better after more sleep.","zh":"據較遲上課支持者所說，青少年睡多一點後學得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces one side’s view, not necessarily a proven conclusion.","zh":"這個短語引入其中一方觀點，而不一定是已證實結論。"},{"en":"It tells readers whose opinion is being presented.","zh":"它告訴讀者正在呈現誰的意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be our destiny","meaning":"是我們的命運","examples":[{"en":"Some explorers believe that settling other worlds is our destiny.","zh":"有些探險者相信定居其他世界是我們的命運。"},{"en":"To be our destiny means to be something humans are meant or expected to do in the future.","zh":"be our destiny 指某事是人類未來注定或被期望要做的事。"},{"en":"Some teachers believe lifelong learning is our destiny in a world that keeps changing.","zh":"有些老師相信在不斷改變的世界中，終身學習是我們的命運。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they see a goal as more than a choice, almost as a historical calling.","zh":"當人們把目標看成不只是選擇，而近乎歷史使命時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses belief in a future path.","zh":"這個短語表達對未來道路的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"throughout history","meaning":"縱觀歷史","examples":[{"en":"Throughout history, explorers have accepted extraordinary risks.","zh":"縱觀歷史，探險者都接受過非凡風險。"},{"en":"Throughout history means across many periods of the past.","zh":"throughout history 指跨越過去許多時期。"},{"en":"Throughout history, people have moved to new places in search of safety, work, or knowledge.","zh":"縱觀歷史，人們為尋找安全、工作或知識而遷往新地方。"},{"en":"The phrase helps connect a modern issue with a long human pattern.","zh":"這個短語幫助把現代議題與長期人類模式連起來。"},{"en":"It means not just once, but repeatedly over time.","zh":"它意思是不只一次，而是隨時間反覆如此。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"embark on journeys","meaning":"展開旅程","examples":[{"en":"Explorers have embarked on dangerous journeys for centuries.","zh":"數百年來，探險者都展開危險旅程。"},{"en":"To embark on journeys means to begin trips, especially important, long, or difficult ones.","zh":"embark on journeys 指開始旅程，尤其是重要、漫長或困難的旅程。"},{"en":"A graduate may embark on a journey abroad to study medicine.","zh":"畢業生可能展開海外旅程去讀醫。"},{"en":"People embark on difficult journeys when they believe the goal is worth the risk and effort.","zh":"當人們相信目標值得風險和努力，就會展開艱難旅程。"},{"en":"The phrase is more formal than simply “start travelling.”","zh":"這個短語比單純 “start travelling” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"in the full knowledge that","meaning":"完全知道……","examples":[{"en":"Some pioneers travelled in the full knowledge that they might die.","zh":"有些先驅在完全知道自己可能死亡的情況下旅行。"},{"en":"In the full knowledge that means while fully understanding and accepting a fact or risk.","zh":"in the full knowledge that 指完全理解並接受某事實或風險。"},{"en":"A rescue worker may enter a dangerous building in the full knowledge that the structure could collapse.","zh":"救援人員可能在完全知道建築可能倒塌的情況下進入危險大樓。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the person is not ignorant of the danger.","zh":"這個短語顯示那個人並非不知道危險。"},{"en":"It stresses conscious acceptance of risk.","zh":"它強調有意識地接受風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"death may await them","meaning":"死亡可能正等候着他們","examples":[{"en":"Explorers accepted that death might await them.","zh":"探險者接受死亡可能正等候着他們。"},{"en":"Death may await them means they may face death in the future if they continue.","zh":"death may await them 指如果他們繼續前進，未來可能面對死亡。"},{"en":"Firefighters know that death may await them when they enter a burning building to save others.","zh":"消防員進入燃燒大樓救人時，知道死亡可能正等候着他們。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds dramatic because it personifies death as something waiting ahead.","zh":"這個短語聽起來戲劇化，因為它把死亡擬人化成在前方等待的事物。"},{"en":"It expresses extreme danger in a serious and literary way.","zh":"它以嚴肅而文學化的方式表達極端危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"severely compromised","meaning":"受到嚴重損害","examples":[{"en":"Even successful explorers sometimes had their health severely compromised.","zh":"即使成功的探險者，有時健康也會受到嚴重損害。"},{"en":"Severely compromised means seriously damaged, weakened, or put at risk.","zh":"severely compromised 指受到嚴重損害、削弱或置於風險中。"},{"en":"A student’s immune system may be severely compromised after weeks of poor sleep and stress.","zh":"學生在數週睡眠不足和壓力下，免疫系統可能受到嚴重損害。"},{"en":"Health can be compromised when people endure cold, hunger, isolation, or radiation for too long.","zh":"當人們長時間忍受寒冷、飢餓、孤立或輻射，健康可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious weakening of safety, health, or function.","zh":"這個短語描述安全、健康或功能被嚴重削弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"health and well-being","meaning":"健康和身心狀況","examples":[{"en":"Dangerous exploration may damage health and well-being.","zh":"危險探索可能損害健康和身心狀況。"},{"en":"Health and well-being means physical condition, mental state, safety, comfort, and overall quality of life.","zh":"health and well-being 指身體狀況、心理狀態、安全、舒適和整體生活質素。"},{"en":"Schools support students’ health and well-being through counselling, exercise, sleep education, and safe spaces.","zh":"學校透過輔導、運動、睡眠教育和安全空間支持學生健康和身心狀況。"},{"en":"A mission that harms health and well-being may succeed technically but fail humanly.","zh":"損害健康和身心狀況的任務，可能在技術上成功，但在人性上失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both body and mind.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋身體和心理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"practise extreme sports","meaning":"參與極限運動","examples":[{"en":"Many people willingly practise extreme sports.","zh":"許多人自願參與極限運動。"},{"en":"To practise extreme sports means to take part in high-risk sports such as rock climbing, skydiving, or big-wave surfing.","zh":"practise extreme sports 指參與高風險運動，例如攀岩、跳傘或大浪衝浪。"},{"en":"Some young people practise extreme sports because they enjoy challenge, speed, and fear.","zh":"有些年輕人參與極限運動，是因為喜歡挑戰、速度和恐懼感。"},{"en":"Extreme sports can build confidence, but they also require training and safety equipment.","zh":"極限運動可以建立信心，但也需要訓練和安全設備。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to risky physical activities done by choice.","zh":"這個短語指自願進行的高風險體能活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"dangerous occupations","meaning":"高危職業","examples":[{"en":"Some people choose dangerous occupations.","zh":"有些人選擇高危職業。"},{"en":"Dangerous occupations are jobs that involve serious risks to health, safety, or life.","zh":"dangerous occupations 指對健康、安全或生命有嚴重風險的工作。"},{"en":"Firefighting, deep-sea fishing, mining, and military service can be dangerous occupations.","zh":"消防、深海捕魚、採礦和軍事服務都可以是高危職業。"},{"en":"People choose dangerous occupations for duty, income, skill, identity, or a desire to help others.","zh":"人們因責任、收入、技能、身份或幫助他人的願望而選擇高危職業。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to risky forms of work.","zh":"這個短語指有風險的工作形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"lower life expectancy","meaning":"降低預期壽命","examples":[{"en":"Dangerous activities can significantly lower life expectancy.","zh":"危險活動可以大幅降低預期壽命。"},{"en":"To lower life expectancy means to reduce the average length of time a person or group is expected to live.","zh":"lower life expectancy 指減少個人或群體預期能活的平均時間。"},{"en":"Long-term smoking can lower life expectancy by increasing the risk of cancer and heart disease.","zh":"長期吸煙可以透過增加癌症和心臟病風險來降低預期壽命。"},{"en":"A job or lifestyle lowers life expectancy when it repeatedly exposes people to serious danger.","zh":"當工作或生活方式反覆令人物暴露於嚴重危險，它就會降低預期壽命。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a reduction in expected lifespan.","zh":"這個短語描述預期壽命縮短。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"risks involved in","meaning":"……所涉及的風險","examples":[{"en":"The risks involved in Martian settlement would be considerable.","zh":"火星殖民所涉及的風險會相當大。"},{"en":"The risks involved in something are the dangers or possible harms connected with it.","zh":"risks involved in something 指與某事相關的危險或可能傷害。"},{"en":"Parents should understand the risks involved in children travelling alone at night.","zh":"家長應了解兒童夜間獨自出行所涉及的風險。"},{"en":"Serious planning requires identifying risks before deciding whether an activity is worth doing.","zh":"嚴肅規劃需要先識別風險，再決定某活動是否值得做。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to dangers that come with an action or plan.","zh":"這個短語指某行動或計劃伴隨的危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be no different","meaning":"沒有分別","examples":[{"en":"Supporters argue that the risks are no different from those already accepted.","zh":"支持者認為這些風險與已被接受的風險沒有分別。"},{"en":"To be no different means to be essentially the same as something else.","zh":"be no different 指本質上與另一事物相同。"},{"en":"Online bullying is no different from other bullying if it causes fear and humiliation.","zh":"如果網絡欺凌造成恐懼和羞辱，它與其他欺凌沒有分別。"},{"en":"Supporters use this phrase to say Mars risks belong to a familiar human pattern of risk-taking.","zh":"支持者使用這個短語，是為了說火星風險屬於熟悉的人類冒險模式。"},{"en":"The phrase rejects the idea that something is special or unique.","zh":"這個短語否定某事特別或獨特的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"there is no reason why","meaning":"沒有理由……","examples":[{"en":"Proponents say there is no reason why the risks should stop exploration.","zh":"支持者說，沒有理由讓這些風險阻止探索。"},{"en":"There is no reason why means there is no good explanation or justification for preventing something.","zh":"there is no reason why 指沒有好的解釋或正當理由去阻止某事。"},{"en":"There is no reason why a hardworking student should be denied a chance to join the competition.","zh":"沒有理由拒絕讓努力的學生參加比賽。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they believe an objection is not strong enough.","zh":"當人們認為反對理由不夠有力，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It introduces a confident rejection of a barrier.","zh":"它引入對障礙的自信否定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"deter someone","meaning":"阻嚇某人","examples":[{"en":"The dangers should not necessarily deter pioneers from travelling.","zh":"危險不一定應阻嚇先驅前往。"},{"en":"To deter someone means to discourage or stop them from doing something by making it seem risky, costly, or difficult.","zh":"deter someone 指透過令某事看似有風險、昂貴或困難，勸阻或阻止某人做某事。"},{"en":"Bad weather may deter families from going hiking at the weekend.","zh":"惡劣天氣可能阻嚇家庭週末去遠足。"},{"en":"Strong motivation can prevent danger from deterring people completely.","zh":"強烈動機可以防止危險完全阻嚇人們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something reducing someone’s willingness to act.","zh":"這個短語描述某事降低某人行動意願。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與文章資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否與文章資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information means to match what the text says.","zh":"agree with the information 指與文本所說內容相符。"},{"en":"In a reading test, a statement agrees with the information if the passage clearly supports it.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，如果文章清楚支持某陳述，它就與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should check the exact wording because one changed word can make a statement false.","zh":"學生應檢查確切措辭，因為一個字改變就可能令陳述變錯。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in true-false-not-given questions.","zh":"這個短語用於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文章資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文本內容相反的意思。"},{"en":"If a passage says Mars has frozen water, a statement saying Mars has no water contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說火星有冰封水源，而陳述說火星沒有水，那就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction is different from missing information because the text clearly supports the opposite.","zh":"矛盾不同於沒有資料，因為文本清楚支持相反內容。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a false answer in reading questions.","zh":"這個短語指出閱讀題中的錯誤答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有關於此事的資料","examples":[{"en":"Not Given means that there is no information on the statement.","zh":"Not Given 表示沒有關於該陳述的資料。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有說明該陳述是真還是假。"},{"en":"If a passage describes Mars’s water but says nothing about its smell, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文章描述火星的水，但完全沒有提到其氣味，那就是沒有關於此事的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when the passage gives no relevant evidence.","zh":"當文章沒有相關證據，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the answer should be “Not Given.”","zh":"這個短語表示答案應為 “Not Given”。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"greatest advantage","meaning":"最大優勢","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what Mars’s greatest advantage is.","zh":"題目問火星最大的優勢是甚麼。"},{"en":"Greatest advantage means the most important benefit compared with other choices.","zh":"greatest advantage 指相較其他選擇最重要的好處。"},{"en":"A school near a train station has its greatest advantage in easy transport access.","zh":"位於火車站附近的學校，其最大優勢是交通方便。"},{"en":"Mars’s greatest advantage may be its resources if they help support settlement.","zh":"如果火星資源有助支持殖民，它的最大優勢可能就是資源。"},{"en":"The phrase asks which positive feature matters most.","zh":"這個短語詢問哪個正面特徵最重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"many basic minerals","meaning":"多種基本礦物","examples":[{"en":"Mars contains many basic minerals as well as frozen water.","zh":"火星含有多種基本礦物以及冰封水源。"},{"en":"Many basic minerals means a large number of simple useful substances found naturally in rock or soil.","zh":"many basic minerals 指岩石或土壤中天然存在的大量簡單有用物質。"},{"en":"A construction company needs many basic minerals such as sand, stone, and clay.","zh":"建築公司需要沙、石和黏土等多種基本礦物。"},{"en":"Basic minerals matter on Mars because settlers may need to build and repair things locally.","zh":"基本礦物在火星上很重要，因為定居者可能需要在當地建造和維修物件。"},{"en":"The phrase points to useful raw materials available in quantity.","zh":"這個短語指出大量可用的有用原材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be more expensive","meaning":"成本更高","examples":[{"en":"Settlement of one world may be more expensive than settlement of another.","zh":"在一個世界殖民可能比在另一個世界殖民成本更高。"},{"en":"To be more expensive means to cost more money than another option.","zh":"be more expensive 指比另一選項花更多錢。"},{"en":"Eating lunch near a tourist attraction is often more expensive than eating in a local neighbourhood.","zh":"在旅遊景點附近吃午餐通常比在本地社區吃飯成本更高。"},{"en":"A project becomes more expensive when it needs special materials, extra transport, or long-term support.","zh":"當項目需要特殊材料、額外運輸或長期支援，它就會變得更昂貴。"},{"en":"The phrase compares cost.","zh":"這個短語比較成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"one-way expedition","meaning":"單程遠征","examples":[{"en":"A one-way expedition would avoid the return journey.","zh":"單程遠征會避開回程旅程。"},{"en":"A one-way expedition is a planned journey of exploration with no return trip included.","zh":"one-way expedition 指沒有包括回程的計劃性探索旅程。"},{"en":"A one-way expedition to a remote research base would require long-term supplies and permanent housing.","zh":"前往偏遠研究基地的單程遠征，需要長期物資和永久住房。"},{"en":"Removing the return journey reduces travel demands but increases settlement demands.","zh":"取消回程會減少旅行需求，但增加定居需求。"},{"en":"The phrase describes exploration that goes outward without coming back.","zh":"這個短語描述向外前進而不返回的探索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete the table","meaning":"完成表格","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the table using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成表格。"},{"en":"To complete the table means to fill in missing information in a table.","zh":"complete the table 指填寫表格中缺漏的資料。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete the table by finding exact words that match each heading.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過找出與每個標題相符的精確字詞來完成表格。"},{"en":"Table completion requires careful scanning because answers are often factual and brief.","zh":"完成表格需要仔細掃讀，因為答案通常是事實性且簡短的。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案應包含不多於兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must use one or two English words only.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案只能使用一個或兩個英文詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “launch window,” it follows the rule because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “launch window”，它符合規則，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing extra words can make an answer wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫多了字也可以令答案變錯。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a strict word limit for exam answers.","zh":"這個短語為考試答案設定嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"problems involved in","meaning":"……所涉及的問題","examples":[{"en":"The table summarises problems involved in travelling to Mars.","zh":"該表格總結前往火星所涉及的問題。"},{"en":"Problems involved in something are the difficulties or risks connected with that activity.","zh":"problems involved in something 指與某活動相關的困難或風險。"},{"en":"A school plan should list the problems involved in taking students overseas.","zh":"學校計劃應列出帶學生到海外所涉及的問題。"},{"en":"Understanding the problems involved helps people prepare resources and safety measures.","zh":"理解所涉及的問題，幫助人們準備資源和安全措施。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to issues that come with a task or plan.","zh":"這個短語指某任務或計劃伴隨的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"associated fact","meaning":"相關事實","examples":[{"en":"Each problem must be matched with an associated fact.","zh":"每個問題必須與一項相關事實配對。"},{"en":"An associated fact is a piece of information connected with a particular issue or category.","zh":"associated fact 指與某特定問題或類別相連的一項資料。"},{"en":"In a history table, each event may be matched with an associated fact about its cause.","zh":"在歷史表格中，每個事件可能與其成因的相關事實配對。"},{"en":"Matching facts correctly helps students show they understand the relationship between ideas.","zh":"正確配對事實幫助學生顯示自己理解概念之間的關係。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to relevant supporting information.","zh":"這個短語指相關支持資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"inadequate rocketry","meaning":"火箭技術不足","examples":[{"en":"Inadequate rocketry limits how much equipment can be carried.","zh":"火箭技術不足限制了可運載設備的數量。"},{"en":"Inadequate rocketry means rocket technology that is not powerful, efficient, or capable enough for the task.","zh":"inadequate rocketry 指對任務而言不夠強大、有效或具能力的火箭技術。"},{"en":"A delivery company has inadequate transport if its vans cannot carry the required goods.","zh":"如果送貨公司的貨車無法運載所需貨物，它就有運輸能力不足的問題。"},{"en":"Inadequate rocketry creates problems because heavy life-support systems and supplies may not fit within launch limits.","zh":"火箭技術不足會造成問題，因為沉重生命維持系統和物資可能超出發射限制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes insufficient rocket capability.","zh":"這個短語描述火箭能力不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"infrequent launch windows","meaning":"罕有的發射時機","examples":[{"en":"Infrequent launch windows restrict when missions can depart.","zh":"罕有的發射窗口限制任務可以何時出發。"},{"en":"Infrequent launch windows are rare periods when a spacecraft can be launched efficiently.","zh":"infrequent launch windows 指太空船能有效發射的罕見時段。"},{"en":"If ferry departures are infrequent, travellers must plan carefully or wait a long time.","zh":"如果渡輪班次不頻密，旅客必須仔細計劃，否則要等很久。"},{"en":"Rare launch windows create pressure because one delay can postpone a mission for months or years.","zh":"罕有發射窗口造成壓力，因為一次延誤可以令任務推遲數月或數年。"},{"en":"The phrase describes launch opportunities that do not happen often.","zh":"這個短語描述不常出現的發射機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"effect of space on","meaning":"太空對……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The table asks about the effect of space on the human body.","zh":"表格詢問太空對人體的影響。"},{"en":"Effect of space on something means the way conditions in space change or influence it.","zh":"effect of space on something 指太空條件如何改變或影響某事物。"},{"en":"A science lesson may examine the effect of space on bones, muscles, sleep, and mood.","zh":"科學課可能研究太空對骨骼、肌肉、睡眠和心情的影響。"},{"en":"Space affects the body because gravity, radiation, isolation, and living conditions are different from Earth’s.","zh":"太空會影響人體，因為重力、輻射、隔離和生活條件都與地球不同。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how space changes a person or thing.","zh":"這個短語重點是太空如何改變人或事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"facilitate microbial exchange","meaning":"促進微生物傳播","examples":[{"en":"A lack of gravity may facilitate microbial exchange.","zh":"缺乏重力可能促進微生物傳播。"},{"en":"To facilitate microbial exchange means to make it easier for microbes to pass between people, air, or surfaces.","zh":"facilitate microbial exchange 指令微生物更容易在人、空氣或表面之間傳播。"},{"en":"Poor ventilation can facilitate microbial exchange in a crowded classroom.","zh":"通風不佳可以在擁擠課室中促進微生物傳播。"},{"en":"In microgravity, droplets may float longer, making microbial exchange easier.","zh":"在微重力下，飛沫可能漂浮更久，使微生物交換更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes conditions that help germs spread.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助病菌傳播的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"give two examples of","meaning":"舉出兩個……例子","examples":[{"en":"Students give two examples of each category.","zh":"學生為每個類別舉出兩個例子。"},{"en":"To give two examples of something means to provide two specific cases that fit that group or idea.","zh":"give two examples of something 指提供兩個符合某群體或概念的具體案例。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to give two examples of renewable energy, such as solar power and wind power.","zh":"老師可能要求學生舉出兩個可再生能源例子，例如太陽能和風能。"},{"en":"Examples help show understanding because students must choose items that match the category.","zh":"例子幫助顯示理解，因為學生必須選出符合類別的項目。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction in reading and writing tasks.","zh":"這個短語是閱讀和寫作任務中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"categories","meaning":"類別","examples":[{"en":"The question organises information into several categories.","zh":"題目把資料組織成幾個類別。"},{"en":"Categories are groups used to organise things that share similar features.","zh":"categories 指用來整理具有相似特徵事物的組別。"},{"en":"A supermarket uses categories such as fruit, drinks, cleaning products, and frozen food.","zh":"超級市場使用水果、飲品、清潔用品和急凍食品等類別。"},{"en":"Categories help students sort information instead of memorising a long messy list.","zh":"類別幫助學生整理資訊，而不是記住一長串混亂清單。"},{"en":"The word refers to organised groups.","zh":"這個詞指有組織的組別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"human attributes","meaning":"人類特質","examples":[{"en":"Physical strength and alertness are important human attributes.","zh":"體力和警覺性是重要人類特質。"},{"en":"Human attributes are qualities, abilities, or characteristics that people have.","zh":"human attributes 指人所擁有的品質、能力或特徵。"},{"en":"Patience, honesty, memory, and physical strength are human attributes that affect daily life.","zh":"耐性、誠實、記憶力和體力都是影響日常生活的人類特質。"},{"en":"Space missions require certain human attributes because machines cannot handle every situation alone.","zh":"太空任務需要某些人類特質，因為機器不能單獨處理每種情況。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to human qualities or capacities.","zh":"這個短語指人的品質或能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"important space activities","meaning":"重要太空活動","examples":[{"en":"Astronauts need special abilities for important space activities.","zh":"太空人需要特殊能力來完成重要太空活動。"},{"en":"Important space activities are essential tasks performed during space missions, such as docking, landing, repairing, or operating equipment.","zh":"important space activities 指太空任務中執行的必要工作，例如對接、降落、維修或操作設備。"},{"en":"A training centre may simulate important space activities so astronauts can practise safely on Earth.","zh":"訓練中心可能模擬重要太空活動，讓太空人在地球上安全練習。"},{"en":"These activities require strength, alertness, and technical skill because mistakes can be dangerous.","zh":"這些活動需要體力、警覺性和技術，因為錯誤可能很危險。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to key tasks in space operations.","zh":"這個短語指太空操作中的關鍵任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"specific medical conditions","meaning":"特定健康問題","examples":[{"en":"The mission could produce specific medical conditions.","zh":"該任務可能造成特定健康問題。"},{"en":"Specific medical conditions are particular illnesses, injuries, or health problems that can be named or described.","zh":"specific medical conditions 指可以被命名或描述的特定疾病、傷害或健康問題。"},{"en":"A school nurse records specific medical conditions such as asthma, allergies, and diabetes.","zh":"學校護士記錄哮喘、過敏和糖尿病等特定健康問題。"},{"en":"Long space travel may create specific medical conditions involving bones, muscles, lungs, and immunity.","zh":"長期太空旅行可能造成涉及骨骼、肌肉、肺部和免疫力的特定健康問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to identifiable health problems.","zh":"這個短語指可識別的健康問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"occur in space","meaning":"在太空中出現","examples":[{"en":"Several illnesses and infections could occur in space.","zh":"幾種疾病和感染可能在太空中出現。"},{"en":"To occur in space means to happen during a space mission or outside Earth’s normal environment.","zh":"occur in space 指在太空任務中或地球正常環境以外發生。"},{"en":"Equipment failures can occur in space, so astronauts must practise emergency repairs.","zh":"設備故障可能在太空中出現，因此太空人必須練習緊急維修。"},{"en":"Health problems may occur in space because gravity, air, radiation, and isolation are unusual.","zh":"健康問題可能在太空中出現，因為重力、空氣、輻射和隔離都不尋常。"},{"en":"The phrase describes events happening in a space environment.","zh":"這個短語描述在太空環境中發生的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"solid objects","meaning":"固體物件","examples":[{"en":"Solid objects such as micrometeoroids could strike astronauts.","zh":"微流星體等固體物件可能撞擊太空人。"},{"en":"Solid objects are physical things with a firm shape, unlike liquids or gases.","zh":"solid objects 指有固定形狀的實體物件，不同於液體或氣體。"},{"en":"A falling branch is a solid object that can injure someone during a storm.","zh":"在暴風雨中掉下的樹枝，是可能傷人的固體物件。"},{"en":"In space, even tiny solid objects are dangerous because they may travel at very high speed.","zh":"在太空中，即使微小固體物件也很危險，因為它們可能高速移動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to material objects that can hit or damage something.","zh":"這個短語指能撞擊或損害某物的實體物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"strike astronauts","meaning":"撞擊太空人","examples":[{"en":"Micrometeoroids may strike astronauts on the surface.","zh":"微流星體可能在地表撞擊太空人。"},{"en":"To strike astronauts means to hit astronauts with force.","zh":"strike astronauts 指以力量擊中太空人。"},{"en":"A falling tool could strike a worker if it is not tied securely.","zh":"如果工具沒有綁好，掉下來可能撞擊工人。"},{"en":"On Mars, small space rocks could strike astronauts because the thin atmosphere gives little protection.","zh":"在火星上，小型太空岩石可能撞擊太空人，因為稀薄大氣幾乎不提供保護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical impact against astronauts.","zh":"這個短語描述對太空人的物理撞擊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"useful substances","meaning":"有用物質","examples":[{"en":"Martian caves may contain useful substances.","zh":"火星洞穴可能含有有用物質。"},{"en":"Useful substances are materials that can help people survive, build, repair, grow food, or produce energy.","zh":"useful substances 指能幫助人類生存、建造、維修、種植食物或生產能源的材料。"},{"en":"A workshop needs useful substances such as glue, wood, metal, and cleaning chemicals.","zh":"工作坊需要膠水、木材、金屬和清潔化學品等有用物質。"},{"en":"Useful substances on Mars could reduce dependence on supplies from Earth.","zh":"火星上的有用物質可以減少對地球供應的依賴。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to materials with practical value.","zh":"這個短語指具有實際價值的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"inside Martian caves","meaning":"在火星洞穴內","examples":[{"en":"Frozen water and minerals may exist inside Martian caves.","zh":"冰封水源和礦物可能存在於火星洞穴內。"},{"en":"Inside Martian caves means within underground cave spaces on Mars.","zh":"inside Martian caves 指在火星地下洞穴空間之內。"},{"en":"A rover might explore inside Martian caves to check whether ice or minerals are present.","zh":"探測車可能探索火星洞穴內部，以檢查是否有冰或礦物。"},{"en":"Conditions inside caves may be safer than the open surface because rock can provide shielding.","zh":"洞穴內的條件可能比開放地表更安全，因為岩石可以提供屏障。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the interior of caves on Mars.","zh":"這個短語指火星洞穴內部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"high-risk activities","meaning":"高風險活動","examples":[{"en":"High-risk activities are common on Earth today.","zh":"高風險活動在今日地球上很常見。"},{"en":"High-risk activities are actions or jobs that involve a strong chance of injury, failure, or death.","zh":"high-risk activities 指有很大受傷、失敗或死亡機會的行動或工作。"},{"en":"Rock climbing without proper equipment is a high-risk activity.","zh":"沒有適當設備攀岩是一項高風險活動。"},{"en":"People accept high-risk activities when they value the reward, purpose, or challenge enough.","zh":"當人們足夠重視回報、目的或挑戰，就會接受高風險活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes activities with serious danger.","zh":"這個短語描述有嚴重危險的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"happening now on Earth","meaning":"現今在地球上進行","examples":[{"en":"The passage compares Mars exploration with risks happening now on Earth.","zh":"文章把火星探索與現今在地球上進行的風險作比較。"},{"en":"Happening now on Earth means taking place in the present world rather than in space or the future.","zh":"happening now on Earth 指在當前世界發生，而不是在太空或未來發生。"},{"en":"Extreme sports and dangerous rescue work are risks happening now on Earth.","zh":"極限運動和危險救援工作都是現今在地球上進行的風險。"},{"en":"This comparison makes Mars risks feel less unusual by linking them with risks people already accept.","zh":"這種比較透過把火星風險與人們已接受的風險連起來，令它們感覺較不異常。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts present Earth-based activities with future space exploration.","zh":"這個短語把現時地球上的活動與未來太空探索作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 5 - Destination Mars.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 6":[{"front":"the search for fresh water","meaning":"尋找淡水","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines the global search for fresh water.","zh":"文章探討全球尋找淡水的問題。"},{"en":"The search for fresh water means the effort to find reliable sources of water that people can drink or use.","zh":"「the search for fresh water」意思是尋找人們可以飲用或使用的可靠水源的努力。"},{"en":"A village may begin the search for fresh water when its wells dry up during a long drought.","zh":"當村莊的水井在長期乾旱中枯竭，村民可能開始尋找淡水。"},{"en":"Population growth can intensify the search for fresh water because more homes, farms, and factories need water.","zh":"人口增長會加劇尋找淡水的需要，因為更多家庭、農場和工廠都需要水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a practical global problem, not just scientific curiosity.","zh":"這個短語描述實際的全球問題，而不只是科學好奇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the assertion that","meaning":"……這個說法","examples":[{"en":"The assertion that water is essential to life is nothing new.","zh":"水是生命所必需的這個說法並不是新觀念。"},{"en":"The assertion that something is true means a statement or claim that presents it as fact.","zh":"「the assertion that」某事為真，意思是把某事當作事實提出的說法或主張。"},{"en":"The assertion that sleep improves learning is supported when students remember more after resting.","zh":"「睡眠改善學習」這個說法，在學生休息後記得更多時得到支持。"},{"en":"If an assertion is repeated often, people may accept it without examining the evidence.","zh":"如果一個說法被反覆提起，人們可能不檢查證據就接受它。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a claim that can be discussed, supported, or challenged.","zh":"這個短語引入一個可以被討論、支持或質疑的主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the essence of life","meaning":"生命的根本","examples":[{"en":"Water has always been regarded as the essence of life.","zh":"水一直被視為生命的根本。"},{"en":"The essence of life means the most basic and necessary element that makes life possible.","zh":"「the essence of life」意思是令生命成為可能的最基本和最必要元素。"},{"en":"For a plant, water and sunlight are close to the essence of life because it cannot grow without them.","zh":"對植物而言，水和陽光接近生命的根本，因為沒有它們便不能生長。"},{"en":"If a resource is called the essence of life, losing access to it becomes a survival issue.","zh":"如果某資源被稱為生命的根本，失去取得它的途徑就成為生存問題。"},{"en":"The phrase gives something a fundamental, life-sustaining importance.","zh":"這個短語賦予某物根本而維持生命的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"nothing new","meaning":"並不是新觀念","examples":[{"en":"The idea that water is vital to life is nothing new.","zh":"水對生命至關重要這個想法並不是新觀念。"},{"en":"Nothing new means not original, not surprising, or already known for a long time.","zh":"「nothing new」意思是不新穎、不令人驚訝，或早已被人知道。"},{"en":"Complaints about homework are nothing new; students have made them for generations.","zh":"對功課的抱怨並不是新事；學生幾代以來都這樣抱怨。"},{"en":"If a problem is nothing new, society may already have experience dealing with it.","zh":"如果一個問題並不是新問題，社會可能已有處理它的經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase often reminds readers that an idea has a long history.","zh":"這個短語常提醒讀者某個想法有悠久歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"come in many forms","meaning":"有多種形態","examples":[{"en":"Water comes in many forms, including rain, snow, fog and dew.","zh":"水有多種形態，包括雨、雪、霧和露水。"},{"en":"To come in many forms means to exist in several different types, shapes, or conditions.","zh":"「come in many forms」意思是以幾種不同類型、形狀或狀態存在。"},{"en":"Learning support can come in many forms, such as tutoring, videos, notes, and practice tests.","zh":"學習支援可以有多種形式，例如補習、影片、筆記和練習測驗。"},{"en":"If a resource comes in many forms, people may use different methods to collect or manage it.","zh":"如果一種資源有多種形態，人們可能使用不同方法收集或管理它。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show variety within one general category.","zh":"這個短語幫助展示同一大類之中的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"spring water","meaning":"泉水","examples":[{"en":"Spring water is one naturally occurring source of fresh water.","zh":"泉水是其中一種天然存在的淡水來源。"},{"en":"Spring water is water that flows naturally from the ground to the surface.","zh":"「spring water」是自然從地下流到地面的水。"},{"en":"Hikers may refill their bottles from spring water if it is clean and safe to drink.","zh":"如果泉水潔淨而可安全飲用，遠足者可能用它補充水壺。"},{"en":"If underground water pressure pushes water upward, spring water can appear at the surface.","zh":"如果地下水壓把水向上推，泉水就可以在地表出現。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a natural source, not water made by a factory.","zh":"這個短語指天然水源，而不是工廠製造的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sea and river water","meaning":"海水與河水","examples":[{"en":"Sea and river water differ greatly in their salt content.","zh":"海水與河水在含鹽量上差異很大。"},{"en":"Sea and river water refers to water from oceans and rivers, which usually have very different levels of salt.","zh":"「sea and river water」指來自海洋和河流的水，兩者通常含鹽量非常不同。"},{"en":"A child can taste the difference between sea and river water because seawater is salty.","zh":"孩子可以嚐出海水與河水的差別，因為海水是鹹的。"},{"en":"Because sea water contains salt, it must be treated before it can be used as drinking water.","zh":"因為海水含鹽，所以必須處理後才能作飲用水。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts two common water sources.","zh":"這個短語對比兩種常見水源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rainwater","meaning":"雨水","examples":[{"en":"Some communities collect rainwater for domestic use.","zh":"有些社區收集雨水作家居用途。"},{"en":"Rainwater is water that falls from clouds as rain.","zh":"「rainwater」是由雲層以雨的形式落下的水。"},{"en":"A family may store rainwater in a tank to water plants during dry months.","zh":"家庭可能把雨水儲存在水箱中，在乾旱月份澆花。"},{"en":"If rainfall is regular, rainwater collection can reduce pressure on public water supplies.","zh":"如果降雨規律，收集雨水可以減輕公共供水壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to water collected directly from rainfall.","zh":"這個短語指直接從降雨收集到的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fog and dew water","meaning":"霧水和露水","examples":[{"en":"Fog and dew water can be collected in dry regions.","zh":"在乾旱地區，霧水和露水可以被收集。"},{"en":"Fog and dew water means water obtained from tiny droplets in fog or from moisture that forms on cool surfaces.","zh":"「fog and dew water」意思是從霧中的微小水滴，或從在冷表面形成的水分取得的水。"},{"en":"A desert community may collect fog and dew water when rivers and wells are limited.","zh":"當河流和水井有限時，沙漠社區可能收集霧水和露水。"},{"en":"If nights are cool and air contains moisture, dew water can form even without rain.","zh":"如果夜晚清涼而空氣含有水分，即使沒有下雨也可以形成露水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes less obvious atmospheric sources of fresh water.","zh":"這個短語描述較不明顯的大氣淡水來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"become scarce","meaning":"變得短缺","examples":[{"en":"Fresh water is becoming scarce in many parts of the world.","zh":"淡水在世界許多地方正變得短缺。"},{"en":"To become scarce means to become difficult to find or not available in enough quantity.","zh":"「become scarce」意思是變得難以找到，或供應量不足。"},{"en":"During a transport strike, fresh food may become scarce in small shops.","zh":"交通罷工期間，小商店的新鮮食物可能變得短缺。"},{"en":"If rainfall decreases and demand rises, clean water can become scarce quickly.","zh":"如果降雨減少而需求上升，潔淨水可能迅速變得短缺。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shortage that develops over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間出現的短缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"water scarcity","meaning":"水資源短缺","examples":[{"en":"Water scarcity is a serious concern for governments worldwide.","zh":"水資源短缺是世界各地政府嚴重關注的問題。"},{"en":"Water scarcity is a shortage of usable water for people, farms, industry, or ecosystems.","zh":"「water scarcity」是供人、農場、工業或生態系統使用的水不足。"},{"en":"A town faces water scarcity when taps run dry and residents must queue for water trucks.","zh":"當水龍頭無水、居民必須排隊等水車時，城鎮就面對水資源短缺。"},{"en":"Water scarcity can lead to higher food prices because farms cannot irrigate crops properly.","zh":"水資源短缺可能導致食物價格上升，因為農場無法適當灌溉農作物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both limited supply and pressure from demand.","zh":"這個短語同時描述供應有限和需求壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a very real worry","meaning":"非常現實的憂慮","examples":[{"en":"The growing shortage of water is a very real worry.","zh":"日益嚴重的缺水是一個非常現實的憂慮。"},{"en":"A very real worry is a serious concern that is not imaginary or exaggerated.","zh":"「a very real worry」是並非想像或誇張的嚴重憂慮。"},{"en":"For parents, rising rent can be a very real worry when family income stays the same.","zh":"對父母而言，當家庭收入不變時，租金上升可以是非常現實的憂慮。"},{"en":"If water levels keep falling, future shortages become a practical danger rather than a distant fear.","zh":"如果水位持續下降，未來短缺就會成為實際危險，而不是遙遠恐懼。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that a problem deserves attention now.","zh":"這個短語強調問題現在就值得關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"governments around the world","meaning":"世界各地的政府","examples":[{"en":"Governments around the world are seeking alternative water sources.","zh":"世界各地的政府正在尋找替代水源。"},{"en":"Governments around the world means national authorities in many different countries.","zh":"「governments around the world」意思是許多不同國家的國家當局。"},{"en":"Governments around the world may invest in hospitals when a disease spreads across borders.","zh":"當疾病跨境傳播時，世界各地的政府可能投資醫院。"},{"en":"If many countries face the same water problem, international cooperation becomes more important.","zh":"如果許多國家面對同一缺水問題，國際合作就變得更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that an issue is global, not local.","zh":"這個短語顯示議題是全球性的，而非本地性的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the reality is that","meaning":"現實是","examples":[{"en":"The reality is that economic growth depends heavily on water supplies.","zh":"現實是，經濟增長高度依賴供水。"},{"en":"The reality is that introduces a practical truth, especially one people may overlook or dislike.","zh":"「the reality is that」引入一個實際真相，尤其是人們可能忽視或不喜歡的真相。"},{"en":"The reality is that good exam results require regular practice, not last-minute luck.","zh":"現實是，理想考試成績需要規律練習，而不是臨急靠運氣。"},{"en":"If people ignore the reality of limited water, planning decisions may become unrealistic.","zh":"如果人們忽視水資源有限的現實，規劃決策可能變得不切實際。"},{"en":"The phrase brings attention back to facts and practical limits.","zh":"這個短語把注意力拉回事實和實際限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"one of the main obstacles to","meaning":"……的主要障礙之一","examples":[{"en":"A lack of fresh water is one of the main obstacles to economic development.","zh":"缺乏淡水是經濟發展的主要障礙之一。"},{"en":"One of the main obstacles to something is one of the biggest things that prevents it from happening easily.","zh":"「one of the main obstacles to」某事，意思是最阻礙它順利發生的重要因素之一。"},{"en":"Poor internet access is one of the main obstacles to online learning in rural areas.","zh":"網絡差是鄉郊地區網上學習的主要障礙之一。"},{"en":"If factories and farms cannot get water, economic development slows down.","zh":"如果工廠和農場無法取得水，經濟發展就會放慢。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a major barrier, not a small inconvenience.","zh":"這個短語指出重大障礙，而不是小麻煩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"economic development","meaning":"經濟發展","examples":[{"en":"An adequate water supply is essential for economic development.","zh":"足夠供水對經濟發展至關重要。"},{"en":"Economic development means the growth of jobs, income, industry, services, and living standards in a place.","zh":"「economic development」意思是一個地方的就業、收入、工業、服務和生活水平增長。"},{"en":"A town may experience economic development when new businesses open and wages rise.","zh":"當新企業開業、工資上升時，一個城鎮可能經歷經濟發展。"},{"en":"Without reliable water, factories cannot operate smoothly and farms cannot produce enough food.","zh":"沒有可靠用水，工廠不能順利運作，農場也不能生產足夠食物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad improvement in an economy, not just company profit.","zh":"這個短語描述經濟的廣泛改善，而不只是公司利潤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a particular country","meaning":"某個國家","examples":[{"en":"Water shortages can limit the development of a particular country.","zh":"水短缺可以限制某個國家的發展。"},{"en":"A particular country means one specific country being discussed, not all countries in general.","zh":"「a particular country」意思是正在討論的一個特定國家，而不是泛指所有國家。"},{"en":"A report may focus on how drought affects a particular country’s farms and cities.","zh":"報告可能集中於乾旱如何影響某個國家的農場和城市。"},{"en":"If a particular country depends heavily on agriculture, water shortages can damage its whole economy.","zh":"如果某個國家高度依賴農業，缺水可以損害其整體經濟。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows a general issue to one specific national case.","zh":"這個短語把一般議題收窄到一個特定國家個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lack of an adequate supply of","meaning":"缺乏足夠的……供應","examples":[{"en":"Many regions suffer from a lack of an adequate supply of fresh water.","zh":"許多地區缺乏足夠的淡水供應。"},{"en":"A lack of an adequate supply of something means there is not enough of it to meet people’s needs.","zh":"「lack of an adequate supply of」某物，意思是該物不足以滿足人們需要。"},{"en":"A hospital may struggle because of a lack of an adequate supply of nurses and medicine.","zh":"醫院可能因缺乏足夠護士和藥物供應而運作困難。"},{"en":"If there is not enough fresh water, households, farms, and schools all face problems.","zh":"如果淡水不足，家庭、農場和學校都會面對問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shortage in relation to need.","zh":"這個短語以需要為基準描述短缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an adequate supply of fresh water","meaning":"足夠的淡水供應","examples":[{"en":"Every country needs an adequate supply of fresh water.","zh":"每個國家都需要足夠的淡水供應。"},{"en":"An adequate supply of fresh water is enough usable water to meet basic human, agricultural, and economic needs.","zh":"「an adequate supply of fresh water」是足以滿足基本人類、農業和經濟需要的可用水。"},{"en":"A school needs an adequate supply of fresh water for drinking, cleaning, and toilets.","zh":"學校需要足夠淡水供應，用於飲用、清潔和洗手間。"},{"en":"If a city lacks adequate water, public health and business activity may suffer.","zh":"如果城市缺乏足夠用水，公共衛生和商業活動可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase means enough clean water, not unlimited water.","zh":"這個短語意思是足夠潔淨水，而不是無限量水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"current figures show that","meaning":"現有數據顯示","examples":[{"en":"Current figures show that water use differs greatly between countries.","zh":"現有數據顯示，不同國家的用水量差異很大。"},{"en":"Current figures show that means recent data or statistics indicate something.","zh":"「current figures show that」意思是近期數據或統計顯示某事。"},{"en":"Current figures show that more students are choosing online courses than before.","zh":"現有數據顯示，選擇網上課程的學生比以前更多。"},{"en":"If current figures show rising water use, governments may need to plan new supply systems.","zh":"如果現有數據顯示用水上升，政府可能需要規劃新供水系統。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence based on numbers.","zh":"這個短語引入以數字為基礎的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an inhabitant of","meaning":"……的居民","examples":[{"en":"An inhabitant of a wealthy town may use hundreds of litres of water each day.","zh":"富裕城鎮的居民每天可能使用數百公升水。"},{"en":"An inhabitant of a place is someone who lives there.","zh":"「an inhabitant of」某地，是住在那裡的人。"},{"en":"An inhabitant of a small island may depend on rain tanks for drinking water.","zh":"小島居民可能依靠雨水箱作飲用水。"},{"en":"If many inhabitants use more water daily, total demand rises quickly.","zh":"如果許多居民每天使用更多水，總需求會迅速上升。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a resident of a specific place.","zh":"這個短語指出某特定地方的居民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a wealthy modern town","meaning":"富裕的現代城鎮","examples":[{"en":"People in a wealthy modern town generally consume more water.","zh":"富裕的現代城鎮居民通常消耗更多水。"},{"en":"A wealthy modern town is a developed place with high income, good services, and modern facilities.","zh":"「a wealthy modern town」是收入高、服務完善且設施現代化的地方。"},{"en":"A wealthy modern town may have gardens, washing machines, swimming pools, and many water-using businesses.","zh":"富裕的現代城鎮可能有花園、洗衣機、游泳池和許多用水商業活動。"},{"en":"Higher living standards can increase water use because people have more appliances and services.","zh":"較高生活水平會增加用水，因為人們有更多電器和服務。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts rich urban life with poorer or less developed settings.","zh":"這個短語對比富裕城市生活與較貧窮或欠發達環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"consume 100–400 litres daily","meaning":"每日消耗100至400公升","examples":[{"en":"Some urban residents consume 100–400 litres of water daily.","zh":"有些城市居民每日消耗100至400公升水。"},{"en":"To consume 100–400 litres daily means to use between 100 and 400 litres every day.","zh":"「consume 100–400 litres daily」意思是每天使用100至400公升。"},{"en":"A household may consume a large amount of water daily through showers, laundry, cooking, and cleaning.","zh":"家庭可能透過洗澡、洗衣、煮食和清潔，每日消耗大量水。"},{"en":"If each person consumes hundreds of litres, a city’s water demand becomes very high.","zh":"如果每人消耗數百公升，一個城市的用水需求就會非常高。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a measurable daily rate of use.","zh":"這個短語提供可量度的每日使用率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"developing countries","meaning":"發展中國家","examples":[{"en":"Water consumption is often much lower in developing countries.","zh":"發展中國家的用水量通常低得多。"},{"en":"Developing countries are countries with lower average income and less developed infrastructure than wealthy industrialised countries.","zh":"「developing countries」是平均收入較低、基礎設施較富裕工業國家欠發達的國家。"},{"en":"In developing countries, some families may collect water from wells rather than taps at home.","zh":"在發展中國家，有些家庭可能從水井取水，而不是在家中開水龍頭。"},{"en":"Limited infrastructure can reduce water consumption because people cannot access as much water easily.","zh":"有限的基礎設施會降低用水量，因為人們不容易取得大量水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad economic development status, not the worth of a country.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛經濟發展狀態，而不是一個國家的價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"not exceed","meaning":"不超過","examples":[{"en":"Daily water consumption may not exceed thirty litres in some regions.","zh":"在某些地區，每日用水量可能不超過三十公升。"},{"en":"To not exceed a number means to stay at or below that limit.","zh":"「not exceed」某數字，意思是保持在該上限或以下。"},{"en":"A school trip budget should not exceed $200 per student.","zh":"學校旅行預算不應超過每名學生200元。"},{"en":"If water use must not exceed a limit, people need to ration showers, washing, and cooking.","zh":"如果用水不能超過某上限，人們就需要限制洗澡、洗衣和煮食用水。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a maximum amount.","zh":"這個短語設定最高數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"per day","meaning":"每日","examples":[{"en":"Some households use fewer than thirty litres of water per day.","zh":"有些家庭每日使用少於三十公升水。"},{"en":"Per day means each day or for every day.","zh":"「per day」意思是每日或每一天。"},{"en":"A doctor may advise a patient to drink two litres of water per day.","zh":"醫生可能建議病人每日飲用兩公升水。"},{"en":"If each person uses less water per day, total household demand decreases.","zh":"如果每人每日用水較少，家庭總需求就會下降。"},{"en":"The phrase measures frequency or amount on a daily basis.","zh":"這個短語以每日為基準量度頻率或數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rich or poor","meaning":"無論貧富","examples":[{"en":"Rich or poor, almost every country has experienced rising water consumption.","zh":"無論貧富，幾乎每個國家都經歷用水量上升。"},{"en":"Rich or poor means whether wealthy or not wealthy, the statement applies to both groups.","zh":"「rich or poor」意思是無論富裕或不富裕，該說法都適用於兩類群體。"},{"en":"Rich or poor, students need time, sleep, and encouragement to learn well.","zh":"無論貧富，學生都需要時間、睡眠和鼓勵才能學得好。"},{"en":"If water demand rises in both rich and poor countries, the issue becomes universal.","zh":"如果富國和窮國的用水需求都上升，問題就變得普遍。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a point crosses economic differences.","zh":"這個短語顯示某觀點跨越經濟差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"annual water consumption","meaning":"每年用水量","examples":[{"en":"Annual water consumption has risen dramatically worldwide.","zh":"全球每年用水量已大幅上升。"},{"en":"Annual water consumption is the amount of water used in one year.","zh":"「annual water consumption」是一年內使用的水量。"},{"en":"A factory can reduce annual water consumption by recycling water used in cooling systems.","zh":"工廠可以透過循環使用冷卻系統用水，減少每年用水量。"},{"en":"If annual water consumption keeps rising, reservoirs and groundwater may come under pressure.","zh":"如果每年用水量持續上升，水庫和地下水可能承受壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase measures water use over a yearly period.","zh":"這個短語以年度為期間量度用水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"continue to grow","meaning":"持續增長","examples":[{"en":"Demand for fresh water continues to grow.","zh":"對淡水的需求持續增長。"},{"en":"To continue to grow means to keep increasing over time.","zh":"「continue to grow」意思是隨時間繼續增加。"},{"en":"The number of online learners continues to grow as internet access improves.","zh":"隨着網絡接入改善，網上學習者人數持續增長。"},{"en":"If demand continues to grow while supply stays limited, shortages become more likely.","zh":"如果需求持續增長而供應仍有限，短缺就更可能發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an ongoing upward trend.","zh":"這個短語描述持續向上的趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"increase fourfold","meaning":"增加至四倍","examples":[{"en":"Global water consumption has increased fourfold over fifty years.","zh":"全球用水量在五十年間增加至四倍。"},{"en":"To increase fourfold means to become four times as large as before.","zh":"「increase fourfold」意思是變成原來的四倍。"},{"en":"If a school club grows from 20 members to 80 members, it has increased fourfold.","zh":"如果學會由20名會員增至80名會員，就是增加至四倍。"},{"en":"A fourfold increase in water use can put huge pressure on rivers, lakes, and wells.","zh":"用水量增加至四倍，可以對河流、湖泊和水井造成巨大壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a very large multiplication, not a small rise.","zh":"這個短語描述非常大的倍數增長，而不是小幅上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"over the last 50 years","meaning":"在過去五十年間","examples":[{"en":"Water use has risen sharply over the last fifty years.","zh":"在過去五十年間，用水量急劇上升。"},{"en":"Over the last 50 years means during the most recent fifty-year period.","zh":"「over the last 50 years」意思是在最近五十年期間。"},{"en":"Over the last 50 years, many families have moved from villages to cities.","zh":"在過去五十年間，許多家庭由村莊搬到城市。"},{"en":"If water use has increased over this period, planners must consider long-term social change.","zh":"如果用水量在這段期間增加，規劃者就必須考慮長期社會變化。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a modern historical time frame.","zh":"這個短語提供現代歷史時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fresh water supplies","meaning":"淡水供應","examples":[{"en":"The world’s fresh water supplies come from several sources.","zh":"世界淡水供應來自幾個來源。"},{"en":"Fresh water supplies are the available sources or amounts of water that are not salty and can be used.","zh":"「fresh water supplies」是不含鹽並可供使用的水源或水量。"},{"en":"A city’s fresh water supplies may come from reservoirs, rivers, and underground wells.","zh":"城市淡水供應可能來自水庫、河流和地下井。"},{"en":"If fresh water supplies fall, authorities may impose water restrictions.","zh":"如果淡水供應下降，當局可能實施用水限制。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to usable water resources.","zh":"這個短語指可用水資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be drawn from","meaning":"取自……","examples":[{"en":"Fresh water supplies are drawn from glaciers, groundwater and rivers.","zh":"淡水供應取自冰川、地下水和河流。"},{"en":"To be drawn from a source means to be taken or obtained from it.","zh":"「be drawn from」某來源，意思是從其中取得或獲取。"},{"en":"School funding may be drawn from government grants and private donations.","zh":"學校資金可能取自政府撥款和私人捐款。"},{"en":"If water is drawn from underground faster than nature replaces it, wells may dry up.","zh":"如果地下水抽取速度快過自然補充速度，水井可能乾涸。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where something is obtained.","zh":"這個短語指出某物從哪裡取得。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a number of sources","meaning":"多個來源","examples":[{"en":"The global water supply is drawn from a number of sources.","zh":"全球供水取自多個來源。"},{"en":"A number of sources means several different places, materials, or origins.","zh":"「a number of sources」意思是幾個不同地方、材料或來源。"},{"en":"A student may use a number of sources, such as books, websites, and interviews, for a project.","zh":"學生做專題時可能使用多個來源，例如書籍、網站和訪問。"},{"en":"Using several sources can make a supply system more reliable if one source fails.","zh":"使用多個來源可以令供應系統更可靠，因為其中一個來源失效時仍有其他來源。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests more than one source, but not necessarily a huge number.","zh":"這個短語暗示多於一個來源，但不一定是極多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the largest cache of","meaning":"最大的……儲藏量","examples":[{"en":"Glaciers contain the largest cache of the world’s fresh water.","zh":"冰川含有全球最大淡水儲藏量。"},{"en":"The largest cache of something means the biggest stored amount of it.","zh":"「the largest cache of」某物，意思是該物最大的一批儲藏。"},{"en":"A library may hold the largest cache of old newspapers in the region.","zh":"圖書館可能保存該地區最大一批舊報紙。"},{"en":"If the largest cache of fresh water is frozen, it may not be easily usable.","zh":"如果最大淡水儲藏量是冰封的，它未必容易使用。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises storage size.","zh":"這個短語強調儲藏規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"estimated fresh water reserve","meaning":"估計淡水儲備","examples":[{"en":"The estimated fresh water reserve is distributed unevenly.","zh":"估計淡水儲備分布不均。"},{"en":"An estimated fresh water reserve is the approximate amount of fresh water believed to be stored or available.","zh":"「estimated fresh water reserve」是相信被儲存或可用的淡水大約數量。"},{"en":"Scientists may calculate an estimated water reserve before deciding whether a region can support more farms.","zh":"科學家可能先計算估計水儲備，再決定某地區能否支持更多農場。"},{"en":"If estimates are uncertain, governments should plan carefully and avoid overuse.","zh":"如果估計存在不確定，政府應謹慎規劃並避免過度使用。"},{"en":"The phrase combines measurement with uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語結合量度與不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be located in","meaning":"位於……","examples":[{"en":"Most of the largest reserves are located in glaciers and snow.","zh":"最大儲備大多位於冰川和積雪中。"},{"en":"To be located in a place means to be found or situated there.","zh":"「be located in」某地，意思是在那裡找到或位於那裡。"},{"en":"The school office is located in the main building near the entrance.","zh":"學校辦公室位於入口附近的主樓內。"},{"en":"If water reserves are located in remote mountains, accessing them may be difficult.","zh":"如果水儲備位於偏遠山區，取得它們可能很困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes position or location.","zh":"這個短語描述位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"glaciers and snow","meaning":"冰川與積雪","examples":[{"en":"Glaciers and snow hold a large proportion of the world’s fresh water.","zh":"冰川與積雪保存全球很大比例的淡水。"},{"en":"Glaciers and snow are frozen forms of water found mainly in cold regions and high mountains.","zh":"「glaciers and snow」是主要存在於寒冷地區和高山的冰凍水形態。"},{"en":"Mountain villages may depend on melting glaciers and snow for river water in summer.","zh":"山區村莊在夏季可能依靠融化的冰川與積雪供應河水。"},{"en":"If glaciers shrink, future river supplies may become less reliable.","zh":"如果冰川縮小，未來河流供水可能變得較不可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to frozen stores of fresh water.","zh":"這個短語指冰封淡水儲藏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be contained in","meaning":"儲存在……之中","examples":[{"en":"Huge quantities of fresh water are contained in frozen stores.","zh":"大量淡水儲存在冰封儲藏中。"},{"en":"To be contained in something means to be held or stored inside it.","zh":"「be contained in」某物，意思是被保存或儲存在其中。"},{"en":"Important school records may be contained in locked filing cabinets.","zh":"重要學校紀錄可能儲存在上鎖文件櫃中。"},{"en":"If fresh water is contained in ice, it is present but not immediately accessible.","zh":"如果淡水儲存在冰中，它雖然存在，但不能立即取得。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where something is held.","zh":"這個短語描述某物被保存在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"natural storehouses","meaning":"天然儲水庫","examples":[{"en":"Glaciers act as natural storehouses of fresh water.","zh":"冰川充當淡水的天然儲水庫。"},{"en":"Natural storehouses are places in nature that store a resource without human construction.","zh":"「natural storehouses」是大自然中無需人工建造而儲存資源的地方。"},{"en":"Forest soils can act as natural storehouses of water after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，森林土壤可以充當天然儲水庫。"},{"en":"If natural storehouses are damaged, communities may lose an important reserve.","zh":"如果天然儲藏地受損，社區可能失去重要儲備。"},{"en":"The phrase compares natural features to storage facilities.","zh":"這個短語把自然特徵比作儲存設施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be estimated to be","meaning":"估計為","examples":[{"en":"The amount of frozen fresh water is estimated to be enormous.","zh":"冰封淡水的數量估計非常巨大。"},{"en":"To be estimated to be means experts calculate or judge an amount approximately.","zh":"「be estimated to be」意思是專家大約計算或判斷某數量。"},{"en":"The repair cost is estimated to be around $10,000, but the final bill may change.","zh":"維修費估計約為一萬元，但最終帳單可能改變。"},{"en":"If a reserve is estimated to be large, planners still need to ask whether it is accessible.","zh":"如果某儲備估計很大，規劃者仍要問它是否可取得。"},{"en":"The phrase presents an informed approximation.","zh":"這個短語提出有根據的近似估算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"groundwater","meaning":"地下水","examples":[{"en":"Groundwater is a major contributor to global fresh water supplies.","zh":"地下水是全球淡水供應的主要來源。"},{"en":"Groundwater is water stored beneath the Earth’s surface in soil or rock layers.","zh":"「groundwater」是儲存在地表以下土壤或岩層中的水。"},{"en":"Farmers may pump groundwater from wells to irrigate crops during dry months.","zh":"農民可能從水井抽取地下水，在乾旱月份灌溉農作物。"},{"en":"If groundwater is pumped too quickly, wells may become deeper and more expensive to use.","zh":"如果地下水抽取太快，水井可能需要挖得更深，使用成本也更高。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to underground fresh water resources.","zh":"這個短語指地下淡水資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a major contributor to","meaning":"……的主要來源","examples":[{"en":"Groundwater is a major contributor to the world’s usable water supply.","zh":"地下水是世界可用水供應的主要來源。"},{"en":"A major contributor to something is an important source or cause of it.","zh":"「a major contributor to」某事，是其重要來源或成因。"},{"en":"Homework quality can be a major contributor to a student’s improvement.","zh":"功課質素可以是學生成績進步的主要因素。"},{"en":"If groundwater contributes greatly to supply, its overuse can create serious shortages.","zh":"如果地下水對供應貢獻很大，過度使用它會造成嚴重短缺。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights an important part of a larger result.","zh":"這個短語突出較大結果中的重要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"amount to","meaning":"總計達","examples":[{"en":"Groundwater reserves amount to millions of cubic kilometres.","zh":"地下水儲備總計達數百萬立方公里。"},{"en":"To amount to a figure means to add up to that total.","zh":"「amount to」某數字，意思是合計達到該總數。"},{"en":"The cost of books, uniforms, and transport may amount to a large sum for a family.","zh":"書本、校服和交通費可能對家庭而言總計達一大筆錢。"},{"en":"If small daily uses amount to a high annual total, conservation becomes important.","zh":"如果每日小量使用加起來達到很高年度總量，節約就變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the total size or value of something.","zh":"這個短語給出某物的總規模或總值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"total volume of water","meaning":"水的總體積","examples":[{"en":"The total volume of water includes both salt water and fresh water.","zh":"水的總體積包括鹹水和淡水。"},{"en":"Total volume of water means the complete amount of water being measured.","zh":"「total volume of water」意思是被量度的全部水量。"},{"en":"A reservoir manager calculates the total volume of water before deciding how much can be released.","zh":"水庫管理人員在決定可釋放多少水前，會計算水的總體積。"},{"en":"If the total volume is large but most is salty, usable fresh water may still be limited.","zh":"如果總體積很大但大部分是鹹水，可用淡水仍可能有限。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to overall quantity, not necessarily usable quantity.","zh":"這個短語指總數量，而不一定指可用數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"salt and fresh water","meaning":"鹹水與淡水","examples":[{"en":"The Earth contains both salt and fresh water.","zh":"地球同時含有鹹水與淡水。"},{"en":"Salt and fresh water means water with high salt content and water with little or no salt.","zh":"「salt and fresh water」意思是含鹽量高的水與少鹽或無鹽的水。"},{"en":"Fish that live in salt water may not survive in fresh water.","zh":"生活在鹹水中的魚未必能在淡水中生存。"},{"en":"Because humans need fresh water to drink, salt water usually requires treatment first.","zh":"因為人類需要淡水飲用，鹹水通常要先處理。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts two broad types of water.","zh":"這個短語對比兩大類水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"it can be clearly seen that","meaning":"可以清楚看到","examples":[{"en":"It can be clearly seen that accessible fresh water is limited.","zh":"可以清楚看到，可取得的淡水有限。"},{"en":"It can be clearly seen that means the evidence makes a conclusion easy to understand.","zh":"「it can be clearly seen that」意思是證據令某結論容易理解。"},{"en":"From the timetable, it can be clearly seen that the last train leaves before midnight.","zh":"從時間表可以清楚看到，尾班車午夜前開出。"},{"en":"If a chart shows tiny fresh water reserves beside vast seawater, the limitation becomes obvious.","zh":"如果圖表顯示龐大海水旁只有少量淡水儲備，限制就變得明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a clear conclusion from evidence.","zh":"這個短語從證據引入清楚結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fresh water available","meaning":"可供使用的淡水","examples":[{"en":"The amount of fresh water available for human use is relatively small.","zh":"可供人類使用的淡水量相對較少。"},{"en":"Fresh water available means the fresh water that people can actually access and use.","zh":"「fresh water available」意思是人們實際能取得並使用的淡水。"},{"en":"A town may have a river nearby, but the fresh water available may be low if the water is polluted.","zh":"一個城鎮附近可能有河流，但如果水受污染，可供使用的淡水可能很少。"},{"en":"If available fresh water is limited, governments must protect it carefully.","zh":"如果可用淡水有限，政府就必須小心保護。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on usable access, not total existence.","zh":"這個短語集中於可用取得，而不是總存在量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the proverbial drop in the bucket","meaning":"滄海一粟；微不足道的一小部分","examples":[{"en":"Accessible fresh water is only the proverbial drop in the bucket.","zh":"可取得的淡水只是滄海一粟。"},{"en":"The proverbial drop in the bucket means a very small amount compared with what is needed or available overall.","zh":"「the proverbial drop in the bucket」意思是與所需或總體相比非常少的一部分。"},{"en":"Donating one book may feel like a drop in the bucket when a school library needs thousands.","zh":"當學校圖書館需要數千本書時，捐一本書可能感覺只是杯水車薪。"},{"en":"If usable fresh water is tiny compared with all water on Earth, the shortage becomes easier to understand.","zh":"如果可用淡水相對地球所有水而言極少，短缺就更容易理解。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses smallness in proportion.","zh":"這個短語強調比例上的微小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"artesian wells","meaning":"自流井","examples":[{"en":"Artesian wells provide access to underground water under natural pressure.","zh":"自流井讓人取得受自然壓力推動的地下水。"},{"en":"Artesian wells are wells where underground pressure can push water upward naturally.","zh":"「artesian wells」是地下壓力能自然把水向上推的水井。"},{"en":"A farming community may rely on artesian wells when rivers are far away.","zh":"當河流很遠時，農業社區可能依靠自流井。"},{"en":"If underground pressure falls, an artesian well may produce less water.","zh":"如果地下壓力下降，自流井可能產水減少。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a special type of groundwater well.","zh":"這個短語指一種特殊地下水井。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"account for","meaning":"佔","examples":[{"en":"Rivers and lakes account for only a small proportion of fresh water.","zh":"河流和湖泊只佔淡水的一小部分。"},{"en":"To account for a proportion means to make up that share of the total.","zh":"「account for」某比例，意思是構成總數中的該份額。"},{"en":"Homework accounts for 20 percent of the final grade in some courses.","zh":"在某些課程中，功課佔最終成績20%。"},{"en":"If rivers account for only a small share, other sources must also be considered.","zh":"如果河流只佔小比例，就必須考慮其他來源。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how much of a total something represents.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物代表總量中的多少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"respectively","meaning":"分別","examples":[{"en":"Artesian wells and lakes account for different amounts respectively.","zh":"自流井和湖泊分別佔不同數量。"},{"en":"Respectively means in the same order as the items just mentioned.","zh":"「respectively」意思是按照剛才提到項目的相同次序分別對應。"},{"en":"Tom and Anna scored 80 and 90 respectively, meaning Tom scored 80 and Anna scored 90.","zh":"Tom 和 Anna 分別得80和90分，意思是 Tom 得80分，Anna 得90分。"},{"en":"If figures are listed respectively, readers must match each number to the correct item.","zh":"如果數字分別列出，讀者必須把每個數字配對到正確項目。"},{"en":"The word prevents confusion when comparing several items.","zh":"這個詞在比較多個項目時防止混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"atmospheric precipitation","meaning":"大氣降水","examples":[{"en":"Rain and snow are forms of atmospheric precipitation.","zh":"雨和雪是大氣降水的形式。"},{"en":"Atmospheric precipitation is water that falls from the atmosphere to the ground, such as rain, snow, or hail.","zh":"「atmospheric precipitation」是從大氣落到地面的水，例如雨、雪或冰雹。"},{"en":"Farmers depend on atmospheric precipitation when they do not have irrigation systems.","zh":"沒有灌溉系統時，農民依靠大氣降水。"},{"en":"If precipitation decreases for several seasons, rivers and reservoirs may shrink.","zh":"如果降水連續幾季減少，河流和水庫可能縮小。"},{"en":"The phrase is a scientific way to describe falling water from the sky.","zh":"這個短語是描述從天空落下水分的科學說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"such as rain and snow","meaning":"例如雨和雪","examples":[{"en":"Atmospheric precipitation includes water such as rain and snow.","zh":"大氣降水包括例如雨和雪等水分。"},{"en":"Such as rain and snow introduces examples of the larger category being discussed.","zh":"「such as rain and snow」引入正在討論的大類別中的例子。"},{"en":"Weather problems such as heavy rain and snow can delay buses and flights.","zh":"例如大雨和大雪等天氣問題，可以延誤巴士和航班。"},{"en":"If a sentence uses “such as”, the items that follow are examples, not the full list.","zh":"如果句子使用 “such as”，後面的項目是例子，不是完整清單。"},{"en":"The phrase helps clarify a general term through familiar cases.","zh":"這個短語透過熟悉例子釐清一般術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an important commodity","meaning":"重要資源；重要商品","examples":[{"en":"Fresh water is an important commodity for every society.","zh":"淡水對每個社會都是重要資源。"},{"en":"An important commodity is a valuable resource or product that people need and may trade, manage, or protect.","zh":"「an important commodity」是人們需要並可能交易、管理或保護的有價值資源或產品。"},{"en":"Rice is an important commodity in communities where many families eat it every day.","zh":"在許多家庭每天吃米飯的社區，米是重要商品。"},{"en":"If water becomes scarce, it may be treated as an economic commodity as well as a human need.","zh":"如果水變得短缺，它可能同時被視為經濟商品和人類需要。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights practical and economic value.","zh":"這個短語突出實際和經濟價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"attempts to acquire","meaning":"獲取……的嘗試","examples":[{"en":"Various attempts to acquire additional water supplies have been made.","zh":"人們已作出各種獲取額外供水的嘗試。"},{"en":"Attempts to acquire something are efforts to obtain or secure it.","zh":"「attempts to acquire」某物，是取得或確保得到它的努力。"},{"en":"A school may make attempts to acquire new computers through fundraising.","zh":"學校可能透過籌款嘗試獲取新電腦。"},{"en":"If normal water sources fail, governments attempt to acquire water from the sea, air, or underground.","zh":"如果正常水源失效，政府會嘗試從海洋、空氣或地下獲取水。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on effort, not guaranteed success.","zh":"這個短語集中於努力，而不是保證成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"stores of water","meaning":"水資源儲備","examples":[{"en":"Governments are looking for new stores of water.","zh":"政府正在尋找新的水資源儲備。"},{"en":"Stores of water are supplies or reserves of water kept or found for future use.","zh":"「stores of water」是為將來使用而保存或找到的水供應或儲備。"},{"en":"A household may keep emergency stores of water before a typhoon.","zh":"家庭可能在颱風前儲備緊急用水。"},{"en":"If natural stores of water are small, dry seasons become more dangerous.","zh":"如果天然水儲備很少，旱季就更危險。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to water reserves rather than daily use alone.","zh":"這個短語指水儲備，而不只是日常用水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"with varying degrees of success","meaning":"成功程度不一","examples":[{"en":"Water-collection projects have achieved varying degrees of success.","zh":"集水項目的成功程度不一。"},{"en":"With varying degrees of success means some attempts worked well, some partly worked, and some failed.","zh":"「with varying degrees of success」意思是有些嘗試很成功，有些部分成功，有些失敗。"},{"en":"Students tried different revision methods with varying degrees of success.","zh":"學生嘗試不同溫習方法，成功程度不一。"},{"en":"If a method depends on weather and geography, results may vary from place to place.","zh":"如果某方法取決於天氣和地理，各地結果可能不同。"},{"en":"The phrase avoids claiming that every attempt succeeded equally.","zh":"這個短語避免聲稱每次嘗試都同樣成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"alternative water sources","meaning":"替代水源","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are investigating alternative water sources.","zh":"科學家正在研究替代水源。"},{"en":"Alternative water sources are other possible sources of water when usual supplies are limited.","zh":"「alternative water sources」是平常供水有限時可用的其他可能水源。"},{"en":"A school may use collected rainwater as an alternative water source for gardening.","zh":"學校可能使用收集雨水作為園藝的替代水源。"},{"en":"If rivers and reservoirs cannot meet demand, cities may explore desalination or recycled water.","zh":"如果河流和水庫不能滿足需求，城市可能探索海水化淡或循環水。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests looking beyond traditional supplies.","zh":"這個短語暗示尋找傳統供水以外的選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be available to","meaning":"可供……使用","examples":[{"en":"Several alternative sources may be available to dry regions.","zh":"幾種替代水源可能可供乾旱地區使用。"},{"en":"To be available to someone or somewhere means they can access or use it.","zh":"「be available to」某人或某地，意思是他們可以取得或使用它。"},{"en":"Online lessons are available to students who cannot travel to school.","zh":"網上課程可供不能到校的學生使用。"},{"en":"If fog water is available to a coastal desert, local people may collect it with nets.","zh":"如果霧水可供沿海沙漠使用，本地人可能用網收集它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical access.","zh":"這個短語描述實際取得途徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not an easy question to answer","meaning":"並非容易回答的問題","examples":[{"en":"Finding an affordable water source is not an easy question to answer.","zh":"尋找負擔得起的水源並非容易回答的問題。"},{"en":"Not an easy question to answer means the problem is complex and has no simple solution.","zh":"「not an easy question to answer」意思是問題複雜，沒有簡單答案。"},{"en":"Deciding how much screen time children should have is not an easy question to answer.","zh":"決定孩子應有多少螢幕時間並非容易回答的問題。"},{"en":"If cost, technology, climate, and fairness all matter, the answer becomes difficult.","zh":"如果成本、科技、氣候和公平都重要，答案就變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase signals complexity and uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語標示複雜性和不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be worthy of","meaning":"值得……","examples":[{"en":"The problem is worthy of our best efforts.","zh":"這個問題值得我們付出最大努力。"},{"en":"To be worthy of something means to deserve it because it is important or valuable.","zh":"「be worthy of」某事，意思是因為重要或有價值而值得得到它。"},{"en":"A struggling student is worthy of patient support, not quick judgement.","zh":"有困難的學生值得耐心支援，而不是倉促評價。"},{"en":"If a problem affects health and survival, it deserves serious investment.","zh":"如果問題影響健康和生存，它就值得認真投資。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses that something deserves attention, respect, or effort.","zh":"這個短語表達某事值得關注、尊重或努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"our best efforts","meaning":"我們最大的努力","examples":[{"en":"Securing fresh water deserves our best efforts.","zh":"確保淡水供應值得我們付出最大努力。"},{"en":"Our best efforts means the strongest, most serious work we can give.","zh":"「our best efforts」意思是我們能付出的最強、最認真努力。"},{"en":"A sick family member deserves our best efforts to arrange proper care.","zh":"生病的家人值得我們盡最大努力安排適當照顧。"},{"en":"If water scarcity threatens millions, small careless attempts are not enough.","zh":"如果水資源短缺威脅數百萬人，小而粗心的嘗試並不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses full commitment.","zh":"這個短語強調全力投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"one area of interest","meaning":"一個受關注的領域","examples":[{"en":"Desalination is one major area of scientific interest.","zh":"海水化淡是科學上一個主要受關注領域。"},{"en":"One area of interest is one topic or field that people are studying or paying attention to.","zh":"「one area of interest」是一個人們正在研究或關注的主題或領域。"},{"en":"In education research, one area of interest is how sleep affects learning.","zh":"在教育研究中，其中一個受關注領域是睡眠如何影響學習。"},{"en":"If many scientists study desalination, it becomes an important area of interest.","zh":"如果許多科學家研究海水化淡，它就成為重要受關注領域。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a focused topic within a larger field.","zh":"這個短語指出較大領域中的一個集中主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"desalination","meaning":"海水化淡","examples":[{"en":"Desalination turns salt water into usable fresh water.","zh":"海水化淡把鹹水變成可用淡水。"},{"en":"Desalination is the process of removing salt from seawater or other salty water.","zh":"「desalination」是從海水或其他鹹水中去除鹽分的過程。"},{"en":"A coastal city may use desalination when rivers and reservoirs cannot meet demand.","zh":"當河流和水庫不能滿足需求時，沿海城市可能使用海水化淡。"},{"en":"Desalination can provide water, but it often requires energy and money.","zh":"海水化淡可以提供水，但通常需要能源和金錢。"},{"en":"The word describes a technological solution to water scarcity.","zh":"這個詞描述水資源短缺的科技解決方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"turn salt water into drinkable water","meaning":"把鹹水變成食水","examples":[{"en":"Desalination can turn salt water into drinkable water.","zh":"海水化淡可以把鹹水變成食水。"},{"en":"To turn salt water into drinkable water means to remove salt and make the water safe for people to drink.","zh":"「turn salt water into drinkable water」意思是去除鹽分，使水可供人安全飲用。"},{"en":"An island with little rain may need machines to turn seawater into drinking water.","zh":"雨水少的小島可能需要機器把海水變成食水。"},{"en":"If treatment fails to remove enough salt, the water remains unsuitable for drinking.","zh":"如果處理未能去除足夠鹽分，水仍不適合飲用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the practical goal of desalination.","zh":"這個短語描述海水化淡的實際目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dry land","meaning":"陸地","examples":[{"en":"The Earth contains far more salt water than dry land.","zh":"地球上的鹹水遠多於陸地。"},{"en":"Dry land is the part of the Earth’s surface that is not covered by water.","zh":"「dry land」是地球表面沒有被水覆蓋的部分。"},{"en":"After a flood, families may wait for dry land before returning home safely.","zh":"洪水後，家庭可能等到有乾地才安全回家。"},{"en":"If the planet has more ocean than dry land, seawater seems like an attractive resource.","zh":"如果地球海洋多於陸地，海水就看起來是有吸引力的資源。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts land with bodies of water.","zh":"這個短語把土地與水體作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"desalinated seawater","meaning":"經化淡的海水","examples":[{"en":"Desalinated seawater can supplement limited natural supplies.","zh":"經化淡的海水可以補充有限的天然供水。"},{"en":"Desalinated seawater is seawater that has had its salt removed so it can be used as fresh water.","zh":"「desalinated seawater」是已去除鹽分、可作淡水使用的海水。"},{"en":"A hotel on a dry island may use desalinated seawater for showers and cleaning.","zh":"乾旱島嶼上的酒店可能使用經化淡海水供淋浴和清潔。"},{"en":"If natural reservoirs are low, desalinated seawater can provide an additional supply.","zh":"如果天然水庫水位低，經化淡海水可以提供額外供應。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to treated seawater, not ordinary seawater.","zh":"這個短語指經處理的海水，而不是普通海水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"seem a logical solution","meaning":"看來是合理的解決方法","examples":[{"en":"Using seawater seems a logical solution to water scarcity.","zh":"使用海水看來是水資源短缺的合理解決方法。"},{"en":"To seem a logical solution means to appear sensible because it matches the problem clearly.","zh":"「seem a logical solution」意思是因為與問題明顯相關而看起來合理。"},{"en":"If students are tired, starting school later may seem a logical solution.","zh":"如果學生很疲倦，延遲上課時間可能看來是合理解決方法。"},{"en":"Since oceans contain huge amounts of water, desalination appears reasonable at first.","zh":"由於海洋含有大量水，海水化淡起初看起來很合理。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests an idea looks sensible, even if practical problems remain.","zh":"這個短語暗示某想法看似合理，即使仍有實際問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"annual quantity","meaning":"每年產量","examples":[{"en":"The annual quantity of desalinated water remains relatively small.","zh":"經化淡水的每年產量仍然相對較少。"},{"en":"Annual quantity means the total amount produced, used, or measured in one year.","zh":"「annual quantity」意思是一年內生產、使用或量度的總量。"},{"en":"A school can calculate the annual quantity of paper used by counting monthly orders.","zh":"學校可以透過計算每月訂單，算出每年用紙量。"},{"en":"If the annual quantity of desalinated water is small, it cannot solve global scarcity alone.","zh":"如果經化淡水每年產量很少，它就不能單獨解決全球缺水。"},{"en":"The phrase measures amount across a year.","zh":"這個短語以一年為單位量度數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"only around ten cubic kilometres","meaning":"只有約十立方公里","examples":[{"en":"Current desalinated-water production totals only around ten cubic kilometres.","zh":"目前經化淡水產量總共只有約十立方公里。"},{"en":"Only around ten cubic kilometres means approximately ten cubic kilometres, with emphasis that the amount is small in context.","zh":"「only around ten cubic kilometres」意思是約十立方公里，並強調在相關背景下數量偏少。"},{"en":"A reservoir holding only around ten percent of its usual water level is a serious warning.","zh":"如果水庫水量只有平常約百分之十，就是嚴重警號。"},{"en":"If production is tiny compared with global need, the method is limited despite being useful.","zh":"如果產量與全球需要相比極少，該方法即使有用也有限。"},{"en":"The phrase combines approximation with limitation.","zh":"這個短語結合近似數量與限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a tiny amount","meaning":"極少量","examples":[{"en":"The quantity produced is a tiny amount compared with the oceans.","zh":"與海洋相比，產生的數量只是極少量。"},{"en":"A tiny amount is a very small quantity.","zh":"「a tiny amount」是非常少的數量。"},{"en":"A tiny amount of salt can change the taste of a soup.","zh":"極少量鹽已可改變湯的味道。"},{"en":"If only a tiny amount of water is produced, it may help a village but not a large city.","zh":"如果只產生極少量水，它可能幫到村莊，但幫不到大城市。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses small scale.","zh":"這個短語強調規模很小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"given the amount of","meaning":"考慮到……的數量","examples":[{"en":"Production remains small given the amount of seawater available.","zh":"考慮到可用海水的數量，產量仍然很小。"},{"en":"Given the amount of something means considering how much of it exists or is involved.","zh":"「given the amount of」某物，意思是考慮到它存在或涉及的數量。"},{"en":"Given the amount of homework, students should start before the weekend.","zh":"考慮到功課量，學生應在週末前開始。"},{"en":"Given the amount of seawater on Earth, desalinated production seems surprisingly limited.","zh":"考慮到地球上的海水量，化淡水產量顯得出奇有限。"},{"en":"The phrase asks readers to judge one fact in light of another.","zh":"這個短語要求讀者根據另一事實判斷某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the greenhouse effect","meaning":"溫室效應","examples":[{"en":"A greenhouse effect can be used in small-scale desalination.","zh":"溫室效應可用於小規模海水化淡。"},{"en":"The greenhouse effect here means heat is trapped inside an enclosed space, helping water evaporate.","zh":"這裡的「the greenhouse effect」意思是熱量被困在封閉空間中，幫助水分蒸發。"},{"en":"A closed car becomes hot in the sun because of a greenhouse-like effect.","zh":"密閉汽車在陽光下變熱，是因為類似溫室效應。"},{"en":"If trapped heat warms seawater, water vapour can form and later condense as fresh water.","zh":"如果被困熱量加熱海水，就可形成水蒸氣，之後凝結成淡水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes heat being held in, not necessarily global climate change.","zh":"這個短語描述熱量被困住，不一定指全球氣候變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"one way to desalinate seawater","meaning":"化淡海水的一種方法","examples":[{"en":"Solar evaporation is one way to desalinate seawater.","zh":"太陽能蒸發是化淡海水的一種方法。"},{"en":"One way to desalinate seawater means one method for removing salt from seawater.","zh":"「one way to desalinate seawater」意思是去除海水鹽分的一種方法。"},{"en":"A small coastal school may demonstrate one way to desalinate seawater using a plastic cover and sunlight.","zh":"一所海邊小學可能用膠蓋和陽光示範化淡海水的一種方法。"},{"en":"If one method is cheap but slow, it may suit villages better than large cities.","zh":"如果一種方法便宜但慢，它可能比大城市更適合村莊。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces one method among several possible methods.","zh":"這個短語引入多種可能方法中的其中一種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"whereby","meaning":"藉此；在這過程中","examples":[{"en":"The method uses evaporation, whereby salt is separated from water.","zh":"這種方法使用蒸發，藉此把鹽從水中分離出來。"},{"en":"Whereby means by which or through which a process happens.","zh":"「whereby」意思是藉由某方法或透過某過程發生。"},{"en":"A school may use a system whereby older students help younger students with reading.","zh":"學校可能使用一套制度，讓高年級學生藉此幫助低年級學生閱讀。"},{"en":"If evaporation occurs, water leaves the salt behind and can be collected later.","zh":"如果發生蒸發，水會離開鹽分並之後被收集。"},{"en":"The word introduces the mechanism by which something is done.","zh":"這個詞引入某事如何完成的機制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be separated from","meaning":"從……分離","examples":[{"en":"During desalination, salt is separated from the water.","zh":"在海水化淡期間，鹽從水中分離出來。"},{"en":"To be separated from something means to be removed or divided from it.","zh":"「be separated from」某物，意思是從其中被移除或分開。"},{"en":"Recycling works better when paper is separated from plastic before collection.","zh":"如果收集前把紙張與塑膠分離，回收效果會更好。"},{"en":"If salt is separated from seawater, the remaining water may become drinkable.","zh":"如果鹽從海水中分離出來，剩下的水可能可飲用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes division into different parts.","zh":"這個短語描述分成不同部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"through a process of evaporation","meaning":"透過蒸發過程","examples":[{"en":"Fresh water is produced through a process of evaporation.","zh":"淡水透過蒸發過程產生。"},{"en":"Through a process of evaporation means by heating water so it changes into vapour.","zh":"「through a process of evaporation」意思是透過加熱水，使它變成蒸氣。"},{"en":"Wet clothes dry through a process of evaporation when water leaves the fabric into the air.","zh":"濕衣服變乾，是因為水透過蒸發過程從布料進入空氣。"},{"en":"In desalination, evaporation can leave salt behind while water vapour is collected.","zh":"在海水化淡中，蒸發可以留下鹽分，同時收集水蒸氣。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the method used to produce fresh water.","zh":"這個短語解釋產生淡水所用的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"water vapour","meaning":"水蒸氣","examples":[{"en":"Water vapour forms when seawater is heated.","zh":"海水被加熱時會形成水蒸氣。"},{"en":"Water vapour is water in gas form.","zh":"「water vapour」是氣體形態的水。"},{"en":"After a hot shower, water vapour may cover the bathroom mirror with mist.","zh":"熱水澡後，水蒸氣可能令浴室鏡子蒙上霧。"},{"en":"When water vapour cools, it can condense back into liquid water.","zh":"當水蒸氣冷卻，它可以凝結回液態水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes invisible or mist-like water in the air.","zh":"這個短語描述空氣中看不見或像霧一樣的水分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"form on panes of glass","meaning":"在玻璃板上形成","examples":[{"en":"Water vapour condenses and forms on large panes of glass.","zh":"水蒸氣凝結並在大幅玻璃板上形成。"},{"en":"To form on panes of glass means to appear as droplets on flat sheets of glass.","zh":"「form on panes of glass」意思是在平面玻璃片上以水滴形式出現。"},{"en":"On a cold morning, moisture may form on panes of glass in a classroom window.","zh":"寒冷早晨，水分可能在課室窗戶玻璃板上形成。"},{"en":"If warm vapour touches cooler glass, droplets can collect on the surface.","zh":"如果暖蒸氣接觸較冷玻璃，水滴就會聚集在表面。"},{"en":"The phrase describes condensation on glass surfaces.","zh":"這個短語描述玻璃表面的凝結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"large panes of glass","meaning":"大幅玻璃板","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse system uses large panes of glass to collect condensed water.","zh":"溫室系統使用大幅玻璃板收集凝結水。"},{"en":"Large panes of glass are big flat sheets of glass used in windows, roofs, or covers.","zh":"「large panes of glass」是用於窗戶、屋頂或覆蓋物的大型平面玻璃片。"},{"en":"A greenhouse uses large panes of glass to let sunlight in and keep heat inside.","zh":"溫室使用大幅玻璃板讓陽光進入並保持熱量。"},{"en":"If vapour condenses on glass, the water can run down into a container.","zh":"如果蒸氣在玻璃上凝結，水就可以流入容器。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the physical surface used for collection.","zh":"這個短語描述用於收集的實體表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at outside air temperature","meaning":"在室外氣溫下","examples":[{"en":"The vapour condenses at outside air temperature.","zh":"水蒸氣在室外氣溫下凝結。"},{"en":"At outside air temperature means at the temperature of the surrounding outdoor air.","zh":"「at outside air temperature」意思是在周圍戶外空氣的溫度下。"},{"en":"Food left at outside air temperature may spoil faster in summer.","zh":"夏天把食物放在室外氣溫下，可能較快變壞。"},{"en":"If glass is cooler than the heated vapour, condensation may occur naturally.","zh":"如果玻璃比加熱蒸氣冷，就可能自然發生凝結。"},{"en":"The phrase specifies the temperature condition of the surrounding air.","zh":"這個短語指明周圍空氣的溫度條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be transported via gravity","meaning":"藉重力輸送","examples":[{"en":"The collected water is transported via gravity into storage drums.","zh":"收集到的水藉重力輸送到儲水桶。"},{"en":"To be transported via gravity means to move downward naturally because of gravity, without pumping.","zh":"「be transported via gravity」意思是因重力自然向下移動，而不用抽水。"},{"en":"Rainwater from a roof can be transported via gravity into a tank below.","zh":"屋頂雨水可以藉重力輸送到下方水箱。"},{"en":"If water can flow downhill by itself, the system saves energy.","zh":"如果水能自行向下流，系統就能節省能源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement powered by natural downward force.","zh":"這個短語描述由自然向下力量推動的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"storage drums","meaning":"儲水桶","examples":[{"en":"Fresh water flows into storage drums.","zh":"淡水流入儲水桶。"},{"en":"Storage drums are large containers used to hold liquids or materials.","zh":"「storage drums」是用來盛載液體或材料的大型容器。"},{"en":"A farm may keep emergency water in storage drums during the dry season.","zh":"農場可能在旱季把緊急用水存放在儲水桶。"},{"en":"If collected water has no storage drums, much of it may be wasted.","zh":"如果收集到的水沒有儲水桶存放，很多可能被浪費。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical containers for storing water.","zh":"這個短語指用於儲水的實用容器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"yield a few cubic metres","meaning":"產出數立方米","examples":[{"en":"The system yields only a few cubic metres of fresh water each day.","zh":"該系統每天只產出數立方米淡水。"},{"en":"To yield a few cubic metres means to produce a small measured volume.","zh":"「yield a few cubic metres」意思是產生少量可量度體積。"},{"en":"A small community garden may yield only a few baskets of vegetables each week.","zh":"小型社區花園每週可能只產出幾籃蔬菜。"},{"en":"If a water system yields only a little, it may serve households but not a large city.","zh":"如果供水系統只產出少量水，它可能服務家庭，但不能服務大城市。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limited output.","zh":"這個短語描述有限產量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"surprisingly energy-efficient","meaning":"出乎意料地節能","examples":[{"en":"Small-scale greenhouse desalination is surprisingly energy-efficient.","zh":"小規模溫室海水化淡出乎意料地節能。"},{"en":"Surprisingly energy-efficient means using less energy than people might expect.","zh":"「surprisingly energy-efficient」意思是能源使用比人們預期少。"},{"en":"A small fan may be surprisingly energy-efficient if it cools a room without air conditioning.","zh":"如果小風扇不用冷氣也能令房間涼快，它可能出乎意料地節能。"},{"en":"If sunlight provides the heat, a desalination system may need little extra fuel.","zh":"如果陽光提供熱力，海水化淡系統可能只需很少額外燃料。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts expected high energy use with actual lower energy use.","zh":"這個短語對比預期高耗能與實際較低耗能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on a larger scale","meaning":"在較大規模下","examples":[{"en":"The process becomes less efficient on a larger scale.","zh":"在較大規模下，該過程變得較低效。"},{"en":"On a larger scale means when something is done in a bigger size, volume, or operation.","zh":"「on a larger scale」意思是以更大大小、數量或運作規模進行。"},{"en":"A recipe that works at home may be harder to manage on a larger scale in a restaurant.","zh":"家中可行的食譜，在餐廳較大規模下可能較難管理。"},{"en":"If water production expands greatly, energy and equipment demands may rise sharply.","zh":"如果產水量大幅擴大，能源和設備需求可能急劇上升。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how size changes practicality.","zh":"這個短語顯示規模如何改變實用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"large-scale production","meaning":"大規模生產","examples":[{"en":"Large-scale production requires much more energy.","zh":"大規模生產需要更多能源。"},{"en":"Large-scale production means producing something in large quantities.","zh":"「large-scale production」意思是大量生產某物。"},{"en":"A bakery moves into large-scale production when it supplies bread to supermarkets across the city.","zh":"當麵包店向全市超市供應麵包時，它就進入大規模生產。"},{"en":"If desalination enters large-scale production, fuel costs can become a serious problem.","zh":"如果海水化淡進入大規模生產，燃料成本可能成為嚴重問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes industrial or high-volume output.","zh":"這個短語描述工業或高產量輸出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"energy efficiency plummets","meaning":"能源效益急跌","examples":[{"en":"The energy efficiency of the process plummets at larger scales.","zh":"該過程在較大規模下能源效益急跌。"},{"en":"Energy efficiency plummets means the system suddenly becomes much less efficient in its energy use.","zh":"「energy efficiency plummets」意思是系統在能源使用上突然變得低效很多。"},{"en":"An old air conditioner’s energy efficiency may plummet when filters are blocked.","zh":"當濾網堵塞，舊冷氣機的能源效益可能急跌。"},{"en":"If a process needs much more fuel when expanded, its benefits may become weaker.","zh":"如果一個過程擴大後需要更多燃料，其好處可能變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a sharp fall in energy performance.","zh":"這個短語描述能源表現急劇下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"burn fossil fuel","meaning":"燃燒化石燃料","examples":[{"en":"Large desalination systems burn substantial quantities of fossil fuel.","zh":"大型海水化淡系統燃燒大量化石燃料。"},{"en":"To burn fossil fuel means to use coal, oil, or gas to produce energy.","zh":"「burn fossil fuel」意思是使用煤、石油或天然氣來產生能源。"},{"en":"A power station may burn fossil fuel to generate electricity for homes.","zh":"發電廠可能燃燒化石燃料為家庭發電。"},{"en":"If desalination plants burn fossil fuel, water production may also create pollution.","zh":"如果海水化淡廠燃燒化石燃料，產水也可能造成污染。"},{"en":"The phrase links energy use with non-renewable fuels.","zh":"這個短語把能源使用與不可再生燃料連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at least a tonne of","meaning":"至少一噸……","examples":[{"en":"Some systems burn at least a tonne of fuel.","zh":"有些系統燃燒至少一噸燃料。"},{"en":"At least a tonne of something means no less than one tonne of it.","zh":"「at least a tonne of」某物，意思是不少於一噸。"},{"en":"A construction project may need at least a tonne of concrete for a small wall.","zh":"一項建築工程可能需要至少一噸混凝土建造小牆。"},{"en":"If each batch requires at least a tonne of fuel, operating costs will be high.","zh":"如果每批生產需要至少一噸燃料，營運成本就會很高。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a minimum quantity.","zh":"這個短語設定最低數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"produce approximately","meaning":"生產約……","examples":[{"en":"A tonne of fuel may produce approximately one hundred cubic metres of water.","zh":"一噸燃料可能生產約一百立方米水。"},{"en":"To produce approximately a quantity means to produce about that amount, not exactly.","zh":"「produce approximately」某數量，意思是生產大約該數量，而不是完全精確。"},{"en":"A small printer may produce approximately twenty pages per minute.","zh":"小型打印機可能每分鐘生產約二十頁。"},{"en":"If estimates say a tonne of fuel produces about 100 cubic metres, actual output may vary slightly.","zh":"如果估計一噸燃料產出約100立方米水，實際產量可能略有不同。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate production figure.","zh":"這個短語提供近似產量數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"amount to","meaning":"相當於；總計達","examples":[{"en":"The production cost amounts to almost one dollar per cubic metre.","zh":"生產成本相當於每立方米近一美元。"},{"en":"To amount to a cost means to reach that total cost when calculated.","zh":"「amount to」某成本，意思是計算後達到該總成本。"},{"en":"Daily bus fares can amount to a large monthly expense for workers.","zh":"每日巴士費對工人而言，每月總計可以是一大筆開支。"},{"en":"If the cost per cubic metre is high, poor communities may not afford the water.","zh":"如果每立方米成本高，貧困社區可能負擔不起該水源。"},{"en":"The phrase calculates a total or final figure.","zh":"這個短語計算總數或最終數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a considerable cost","meaning":"相當高的成本","examples":[{"en":"Desalinated water can involve a considerable cost.","zh":"經化淡水可能涉及相當高的成本。"},{"en":"A considerable cost is a large or significant expense.","zh":"「a considerable cost」是很大或重要的開支。"},{"en":"Repairing a lift can involve a considerable cost for a small building.","zh":"對小型大廈而言，維修升降機可能涉及相當高的成本。"},{"en":"If producing water requires expensive fuel and equipment, the price may be difficult for users.","zh":"如果產水需要昂貴燃料和設備，價格對用戶而言可能困難。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that something is not cheap.","zh":"這個短語提醒某事並不便宜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"several different sources","meaning":"幾個不同來源","examples":[{"en":"Fresh water can be sourced from several different places.","zh":"淡水可以取自幾個不同地方。"},{"en":"Several different sources means more than one distinct origin or supply point.","zh":"「several different sources」意思是多於一個不同來源或供應點。"},{"en":"A school report may use several different sources, including books, interviews, and government data.","zh":"學校報告可能使用幾個不同來源，包括書籍、訪問和政府數據。"},{"en":"If one water source fails, having several different sources improves security.","zh":"如果其中一個水源失效，有幾個不同來源可以提高安全性。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises variety in supply.","zh":"這個短語強調供應多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be sourced from","meaning":"取自……","examples":[{"en":"Water can be sourced from the ground, atmosphere and oceans.","zh":"水可以取自地下、大氣和海洋。"},{"en":"To be sourced from something means to be obtained from that place or origin.","zh":"「be sourced from」某物，意思是從該地方或來源取得。"},{"en":"A café may use coffee beans sourced from small farms.","zh":"咖啡店可能使用取自小農場的咖啡豆。"},{"en":"If water is sourced from the atmosphere, technology must collect it from fog, dew, or vapour.","zh":"如果水取自大氣，科技就必須從霧、露水或水蒸氣中收集它。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the origin of a supply.","zh":"這個短語指出供應來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"paradoxically","meaning":"矛盾的是","examples":[{"en":"Paradoxically, the largest water sources are often the hardest to use.","zh":"矛盾的是，最大的水源往往最難使用。"},{"en":"Paradoxically means in a way that seems contradictory or surprising but may still be true.","zh":"「paradoxically」意思是以看似矛盾或令人驚訝但仍可能真實的方式。"},{"en":"Paradoxically, a student may learn more from mistakes than from easy success.","zh":"矛盾的是，學生可能從錯誤中學到比輕鬆成功更多。"},{"en":"If seawater is abundant but expensive to treat, a huge supply can still be difficult to use.","zh":"如果海水豐富但處理昂貴，龐大供應仍可能難以使用。"},{"en":"The word introduces an unexpected contrast.","zh":"這個詞引入意料之外的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the most extensive sources","meaning":"最廣泛的來源","examples":[{"en":"The most extensive sources of fresh water may be difficult to exploit.","zh":"最廣泛的淡水來源可能難以開發利用。"},{"en":"The most extensive sources are the largest or most widespread sources available.","zh":"「the most extensive sources」是最大或分布最廣的可用來源。"},{"en":"The most extensive sources of information online are not always the most reliable.","zh":"網上最廣泛的資訊來源未必最可靠。"},{"en":"If a source is large but hard to access, size alone does not solve the problem.","zh":"如果來源龐大但難以取得，單靠規模並不能解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights breadth or abundance.","zh":"這個短語突出廣度或豐富程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be difficult to tap","meaning":"難以開發利用","examples":[{"en":"Atmospheric water is abundant but difficult to tap.","zh":"大氣水分很豐富，但難以開發利用。"},{"en":"To be difficult to tap means to be hard to access, collect, or use as a resource.","zh":"「be difficult to tap」意思是難以取得、收集或作為資源使用。"},{"en":"A talented student’s potential may be difficult to tap without patient guidance.","zh":"如果沒有耐心引導，有才華學生的潛力可能難以開發。"},{"en":"If water exists as vapour spread through the air, collecting it cheaply is difficult.","zh":"如果水以水蒸氣形式散布在空氣中，廉價收集它就很困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a resource that exists but is hard to use.","zh":"這個短語描述存在但難以使用的資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"contain vast amounts of","meaning":"含有大量","examples":[{"en":"The atmosphere contains vast amounts of fresh water.","zh":"大氣含有大量淡水。"},{"en":"To contain vast amounts of something means to hold extremely large quantities of it.","zh":"「contain vast amounts of」某物，意思是包含極大量該物。"},{"en":"A digital archive may contain vast amounts of old photographs and letters.","zh":"數碼檔案館可能含有大量舊照片和信件。"},{"en":"Even if the atmosphere contains much water, collecting it in useful form can be difficult.","zh":"即使大氣含有大量水分，要以有用形式收集仍很困難。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises huge quantity.","zh":"這個短語強調巨大數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"condensed water","meaning":"凝結水","examples":[{"en":"Clouds consist partly of condensed water.","zh":"雲部分由凝結水組成。"},{"en":"Condensed water is water that has changed from vapour into tiny liquid droplets.","zh":"「condensed water」是由水蒸氣變成的小液態水滴。"},{"en":"Condensed water may appear on a cold bottle taken out of the refrigerator.","zh":"從雪櫃拿出的冷瓶表面可能出現凝結水。"},{"en":"When warm moist air cools, condensed water can form as clouds, fog, or dew.","zh":"當溫暖濕空氣冷卻，凝結水可形成雲、霧或露水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes water formed by cooling vapour.","zh":"這個短語描述水蒸氣冷卻後形成的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in the form of clouds","meaning":"以雲的形式","examples":[{"en":"Some atmospheric water exists in the form of clouds.","zh":"有些大氣水分以雲的形式存在。"},{"en":"In the form of clouds means appearing or existing as clouds.","zh":"「in the form of clouds」意思是以雲的形式出現或存在。"},{"en":"Water in the form of clouds can later fall as rain or snow.","zh":"以雲的形式存在的水之後可能以雨或雪落下。"},{"en":"If water exists in cloud form, it is visible but not immediately usable.","zh":"如果水以雲的形式存在，它可見但不能立即使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the physical form that water takes.","zh":"這個短語描述水所呈現的物理形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"water vapour","meaning":"水蒸氣","examples":[{"en":"Most atmospheric water exists as water vapour.","zh":"大部分大氣水分以水蒸氣形式存在。"},{"en":"Water vapour is the gas form of water in the air.","zh":"「water vapour」是空氣中氣態形式的水。"},{"en":"On a humid day, the air contains more water vapour than on a dry day.","zh":"潮濕日子裡，空氣含有比乾燥日子更多水蒸氣。"},{"en":"If water vapour cools enough, it may condense into fog, dew, or clouds.","zh":"如果水蒸氣冷卻到足夠程度，它可能凝結成霧、露水或雲。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why invisible air can still contain water.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何看不見的空氣仍可含水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the vastness of","meaning":"……的龐大程度","examples":[{"en":"The vastness of this water source makes it scientifically attractive.","zh":"這個水源的龐大程度令它在科學上具吸引力。"},{"en":"The vastness of something means its enormous size, amount, or extent.","zh":"「the vastness of」某物，意思是其巨大大小、數量或範圍。"},{"en":"The vastness of the night sky can make people feel small.","zh":"夜空的浩瀚可以令人感到渺小。"},{"en":"If a water source is vast, scientists naturally want to know whether it can be used.","zh":"如果水源非常龐大，科學家自然想知道它能否被利用。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises impressive scale.","zh":"這個短語強調令人印象深刻的規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be comparable to","meaning":"與……相若","examples":[{"en":"Atmospheric water is comparable to the renewable water of inhabited lands.","zh":"大氣水分與有人居住陸地上的可再生水資源相若。"},{"en":"To be comparable to something means to be similar enough in size, quality, or importance to be compared.","zh":"「be comparable to」某物，意思是在大小、質素或重要性上足以作比較。"},{"en":"A small college’s exam results may be comparable to those of larger schools.","zh":"小型學院的考試成績可能與大型學校相若。"},{"en":"If atmospheric water is comparable to land-based renewable water, it deserves serious study.","zh":"如果大氣水分與陸地可再生水相若，它就值得認真研究。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that two things are similar in an important respect.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩件事在某重要方面相似。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"renewable liquid-water resources","meaning":"可再生液態水資源","examples":[{"en":"Rivers and lakes form part of renewable liquid-water resources.","zh":"河流和湖泊構成可再生液態水資源的一部分。"},{"en":"Renewable liquid-water resources are supplies of liquid fresh water that can be naturally replenished.","zh":"「renewable liquid-water resources」是能自然補充的液態淡水供應。"},{"en":"Rain-fed rivers are renewable water resources if rainfall continues regularly.","zh":"如果降雨持續規律，靠雨水補給的河流就是可再生水資源。"},{"en":"If people use renewable water faster than it is replaced, even renewable resources can become strained.","zh":"如果人們使用可再生水的速度快過補充速度，即使可再生資源也會受壓。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to naturally renewed usable water in liquid form.","zh":"這個短語指以液態形式存在、自然更新的可用水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"inhabited lands","meaning":"有人居住的陸地","examples":[{"en":"The comparison includes all inhabited lands.","zh":"這項比較包括所有有人居住的陸地。"},{"en":"Inhabited lands are areas where people live.","zh":"「inhabited lands」是有人居住的地區。"},{"en":"Roads, schools, farms, and homes are usually found across inhabited lands.","zh":"道路、學校、農場和住宅通常分布於有人居住的陸地。"},{"en":"If water resources are measured only in inhabited lands, remote frozen areas may be excluded.","zh":"如果水資源只量度有人居住的陸地，偏遠冰封地區可能被排除。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts lived-in areas with uninhabited regions.","zh":"這個短語對比有人居住地區與無人居住地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be easy to calculate","meaning":"容易計算","examples":[{"en":"The total atmospheric water content is relatively easy to calculate.","zh":"大氣水分總含量相對容易計算。"},{"en":"To be easy to calculate means to be simple to work out using numbers or measurements.","zh":"「be easy to calculate」意思是容易透過數字或量度計算出來。"},{"en":"A student’s average mark is easy to calculate if all test scores are known.","zh":"如果所有測驗分數已知，學生平均分就容易計算。"},{"en":"Even if a resource is easy to calculate, it may still be difficult to collect.","zh":"即使資源容易計算，它仍可能難以收集。"},{"en":"The phrase separates measurement from practical use.","zh":"這個短語把量度與實際使用分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"economically obtain","meaning":"以符合經濟效益的方式取得","examples":[{"en":"The challenge is learning how to economically obtain water from the air.","zh":"挑戰在於學會如何以符合經濟效益的方式從空氣中取水。"},{"en":"To economically obtain something means to get it in a way that is financially practical and not too expensive.","zh":"「economically obtain」某物，意思是以財政上可行、不太昂貴的方式取得。"},{"en":"A school tries to economically obtain new books by buying second-hand copies.","zh":"學校嘗試透過購買二手書，以符合經濟效益的方式取得新書。"},{"en":"If collecting water from air costs too much, the method cannot help poor communities widely.","zh":"如果從空氣集水成本太高，該方法就不能廣泛幫助貧困社區。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on affordability, not just technical possibility.","zh":"這個短語集中於負擔能力，而不只是技術可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in liquid form","meaning":"以液態形式","examples":[{"en":"Atmospheric water must be collected in liquid form before use.","zh":"大氣水分必須以液態形式收集後才能使用。"},{"en":"In liquid form means existing as a liquid rather than gas, ice, or vapour.","zh":"「in liquid form」意思是以液體而不是氣體、冰或蒸氣形式存在。"},{"en":"Medicine in liquid form is sometimes easier for children to swallow.","zh":"液態藥物有時較容易讓兒童吞服。"},{"en":"If water exists as vapour, it must condense into liquid form before people can store it.","zh":"如果水以水蒸氣形式存在，就必須凝結成液態後人們才能儲存。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the physical state needed for use.","zh":"這個短語指出使用所需的物理狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"most challenging","meaning":"最具挑戰性","examples":[{"en":"Obtaining atmospheric water economically remains most challenging.","zh":"以符合經濟效益的方式取得大氣水分仍然最具挑戰性。"},{"en":"Most challenging means the most difficult part of a task or problem.","zh":"「most challenging」意思是任務或問題中最困難的部分。"},{"en":"For many students, speaking confidently is the most challenging part of learning English.","zh":"對許多學生而言，自信說話是學英文最具挑戰性的部分。"},{"en":"If technology can collect water but not cheaply, affordability becomes the hardest challenge.","zh":"如果科技能收集水但不能廉價做到，負擔能力就成為最困難挑戰。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the main difficulty.","zh":"這個短語突出主要困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"one approach to","meaning":"……的一種方法","examples":[{"en":"Fog nets are one approach to drawing water from the atmosphere.","zh":"集霧網是從大氣中收集水分的一種方法。"},{"en":"One approach to something means one method or way of dealing with it.","zh":"「one approach to」某事，意思是處理它的一種方法或方式。"},{"en":"Group discussion is one approach to helping shy students speak more.","zh":"小組討論是幫助害羞學生多說話的一種方法。"},{"en":"If one approach works only in certain climates, other methods are still needed elsewhere.","zh":"如果一種方法只在某些氣候中有效，其他地方仍需要其他方法。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a possible method, not the only method.","zh":"這個短語引入一種可能方法，而不是唯一方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"draw water from the atmosphere","meaning":"從大氣中收集水分","examples":[{"en":"Special nets can draw water from the atmosphere.","zh":"特製網可以從大氣中收集水分。"},{"en":"To draw water from the atmosphere means to collect water that exists in air as fog, dew, or vapour.","zh":"「draw water from the atmosphere」意思是收集空氣中以霧、露水或水蒸氣形式存在的水。"},{"en":"A dry coastal village may draw water from the atmosphere using fog nets.","zh":"乾旱沿海村莊可能使用集霧網從大氣中收集水分。"},{"en":"If the air contains moisture, technology may capture it before it disappears.","zh":"如果空氣含有濕氣，科技可以在它消散前捕捉它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes collecting water from air rather than from rivers or wells.","zh":"這個短語描述從空氣而不是河流或水井取水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fog nets","meaning":"集霧網","examples":[{"en":"Fog nets collect suspended droplets of water.","zh":"集霧網收集懸浮水滴。"},{"en":"Fog nets are mesh structures designed to catch tiny water droplets from fog.","zh":"「fog nets」是設計用來捕捉霧中微小水滴的網狀結構。"},{"en":"A mountain village may install fog nets where moist air passes through each morning.","zh":"山區村莊可能在每天早上濕空氣經過的地方安裝集霧網。"},{"en":"When fog touches the net, droplets gather and run down into containers.","zh":"當霧接觸網面，水滴聚集並流入容器。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a simple technology for collecting atmospheric water.","zh":"這個短語描述收集大氣水分的簡單科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"coastal deserts","meaning":"沿海沙漠","examples":[{"en":"Some coastal deserts have favourable conditions for collecting fog.","zh":"有些沿海沙漠具備收集霧水的有利條件。"},{"en":"Coastal deserts are dry regions located near the sea.","zh":"「coastal deserts」是位於海邊附近的乾旱地區。"},{"en":"A coastal desert may receive little rain but still have moist air from the ocean.","zh":"沿海沙漠可能降雨很少，但仍有來自海洋的濕空氣。"},{"en":"If ocean humidity moves inland and cools, fog can form even in dry coastal areas.","zh":"如果海洋濕氣向內陸移動並冷卻，即使在乾旱沿海地區也可形成霧。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a desert shaped partly by its position near the coast.","zh":"這個短語描述部分受海岸位置影響的沙漠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"favourable condensation conditions","meaning":"有利的凝結條件","examples":[{"en":"Parts of Chile have favourable condensation conditions.","zh":"智利部分地區有有利的凝結條件。"},{"en":"Favourable condensation conditions are conditions that help water vapour turn into liquid droplets.","zh":"「favourable condensation conditions」是有助水蒸氣變成液態水滴的條件。"},{"en":"A cool bathroom mirror creates favourable condensation conditions after a hot shower.","zh":"熱水澡後，冷浴室鏡面會形成有利的凝結條件。"},{"en":"If moist air meets cool mountain slopes, fog droplets may form more easily.","zh":"如果濕空氣遇到清涼山坡，霧滴可能更容易形成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes environmental conditions that encourage water to condense.","zh":"這個短語描述促進水分凝結的環境條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ocean humidity","meaning":"海洋濕氣","examples":[{"en":"Ocean humidity moves inland towards mountain areas.","zh":"海洋濕氣向內陸移動至山區。"},{"en":"Ocean humidity is moisture in the air that comes from the sea.","zh":"「ocean humidity」是來自海洋的空氣水分。"},{"en":"Coastal towns often feel sticky because ocean humidity raises moisture levels in the air.","zh":"沿海城鎮常感覺濕黏，因為海洋濕氣提高空氣濕度。"},{"en":"If ocean humidity is pushed toward cooler land, it may condense into fog.","zh":"如果海洋濕氣被推向較冷陸地，它可能凝結成霧。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how the sea can supply moisture to dry land.","zh":"這個短語解釋海洋如何向乾旱陸地提供水分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"condense in the form of fog","meaning":"凝結成霧","examples":[{"en":"Ocean humidity condenses in the form of fog.","zh":"海洋濕氣凝結成霧。"},{"en":"To condense in the form of fog means water vapour cools and becomes tiny droplets suspended in air.","zh":"「condense in the form of fog」意思是水蒸氣冷卻後變成懸浮在空氣中的微小水滴。"},{"en":"Warm breath may condense in the form of mist on a cold morning.","zh":"寒冷早晨，溫暖呼氣可能凝結成霧氣。"},{"en":"If moist air rises and cools near mountains, fog can appear.","zh":"如果濕空氣上升並在山區附近冷卻，霧就可以出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes vapour turning into visible suspended water droplets.","zh":"這個短語描述蒸氣變成可見懸浮水滴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mid-range mountains","meaning":"中等高度的山區","examples":[{"en":"Fog commonly forms on mid-range mountains near the coast.","zh":"霧常在近海的中等高度山區形成。"},{"en":"Mid-range mountains are mountains of moderate height, not very low hills or extremely high peaks.","zh":"「mid-range mountains」是中等高度的山，不是很低的丘陵，也不是極高山峰。"},{"en":"Hikers may choose mid-range mountains when they want a challenge but not a dangerous climb.","zh":"遠足者想有挑戰但不想危險攀登時，可能選擇中等高度山區。"},{"en":"If moist ocean air meets mid-range mountains, it may cool enough to form fog.","zh":"如果濕潤海洋空氣遇到中等高度山區，它可能冷卻到足以形成霧。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mountains of middle elevation.","zh":"這個短語描述中等海拔山區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be composed of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"Fog is composed of tiny suspended water droplets.","zh":"霧由微小懸浮水滴組成。"},{"en":"To be composed of something means to be made up of those parts.","zh":"「be composed of」某物，意思是由那些部分構成。"},{"en":"A class may be composed of students from several different schools.","zh":"一班學生可能由來自幾間不同學校的學生組成。"},{"en":"If fog is composed of droplets, nets can collect those droplets physically.","zh":"如果霧由水滴組成，網就可以實際收集那些水滴。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what something consists of.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物由甚麼構成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"droplets of suspended water","meaning":"懸浮水滴","examples":[{"en":"Fog contains droplets of suspended water.","zh":"霧含有懸浮水滴。"},{"en":"Droplets of suspended water are tiny drops of water floating in the air.","zh":"「droplets of suspended water」是在空氣中漂浮的微小水滴。"},{"en":"After boiling water, tiny droplets of suspended water may be seen near the kettle.","zh":"煲水後，水壺附近可能看見微小懸浮水滴。"},{"en":"If these droplets touch a net, they can join together and flow downward.","zh":"如果這些水滴接觸到網面，它們可以聚合並向下流。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the small water particles that make fog collectable.","zh":"這個短語描述令霧可被收集的小水粒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be collected in nets","meaning":"被網收集","examples":[{"en":"The droplets can be collected in specially designed nets.","zh":"這些水滴可以被特別設計的網收集。"},{"en":"To be collected in nets means to be caught by netting material and gathered for use.","zh":"「be collected in nets」意思是被網狀材料捕捉並聚集起來使用。"},{"en":"Fishermen collect fish in nets, while fog collectors gather water droplets in nets.","zh":"漁民用網收魚，而集霧者用網收集水滴。"},{"en":"If the net surface is suitable, tiny droplets can join together and drip into containers.","zh":"如果網面合適，微小水滴可以聚合並滴入容器。"},{"en":"The phrase describes collection by a mesh structure.","zh":"這個短語描述透過網狀結構收集。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"conduct an experiment","meaning":"進行實驗","examples":[{"en":"A university in northern Chile conducted early experiments with fog nets.","zh":"智利北部一所大學早期進行了集霧網實驗。"},{"en":"To conduct an experiment means to carry out a controlled test to learn something.","zh":"「conduct an experiment」意思是進行受控測試以了解某事。"},{"en":"A science class may conduct an experiment to see which material absorbs water best.","zh":"科學課可能進行實驗，看看哪種材料最能吸水。"},{"en":"If experiments show that fog nets work, communities may test them in real villages.","zh":"如果實驗顯示集霧網有效，社區可能在真實村莊試用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised scientific testing.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的科學測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"major experiments","meaning":"大型實驗","examples":[{"en":"The first major experiments demonstrated the potential of fog collection.","zh":"首批大型實驗展示了集霧的潛力。"},{"en":"Major experiments are important or large-scale tests that provide meaningful results.","zh":"「major experiments」是重要或大規模、能提供有意義結果的測試。"},{"en":"A hospital may run major experiments before introducing a new treatment widely.","zh":"醫院可能在廣泛引入新治療前進行大型實驗。"},{"en":"If major experiments succeed, researchers gain confidence in the method.","zh":"如果大型實驗成功，研究人員對該方法會更有信心。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to tests that matter because of their scale or impact.","zh":"這個短語指因規模或影響而重要的測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"draw on knowledge gained from","meaning":"運用從……所得的知識","examples":[{"en":"Later projects drew on knowledge gained from the original experiments.","zh":"後來的項目運用從最初實驗所得的知識。"},{"en":"To draw on knowledge gained from something means to use what was learned from it.","zh":"「draw on knowledge gained from」某事，意思是運用從中學到的東西。"},{"en":"A teacher may draw on knowledge gained from past classes to design better lessons.","zh":"老師可能運用從過往課堂所得的知識設計更好課堂。"},{"en":"If early experiments reveal problems, later projects can improve their design.","zh":"如果早期實驗揭示問題，後來項目就可以改善設計。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning from previous experience.","zh":"這個短語描述從先前經驗中學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"further testing","meaning":"進一步測試","examples":[{"en":"Further testing improved the design of the fog nets.","zh":"進一步測試改善了集霧網設計。"},{"en":"Further testing means additional tests carried out after the first ones.","zh":"「further testing」意思是在首次測試後進行的額外測試。"},{"en":"A doctor may request further testing if the first result is unclear.","zh":"如果第一次結果不清楚，醫生可能要求進一步測試。"},{"en":"If a fog net tears easily, further testing can help identify stronger materials.","zh":"如果集霧網容易破裂，進一步測試可以幫助找出更堅固材料。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one test is not enough.","zh":"這個短語顯示一次測試並不足夠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"culminate in","meaning":"最終促成","examples":[{"en":"The research culminated in a successful village water project.","zh":"研究最終促成一個成功村莊供水項目。"},{"en":"To culminate in something means to end in or lead finally to an important result.","zh":"「culminate in」某事，意思是最終以某重要結果結束或導致它。"},{"en":"Months of rehearsal may culminate in a successful school performance.","zh":"數月排練可能最終促成一次成功學校演出。"},{"en":"If experiments, testing, and planning work well, they may culminate in a practical solution.","zh":"如果實驗、測試和規劃順利，它們可能最終促成實際解決方案。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a final achievement after a process.","zh":"這個短語描述一個過程後的最終成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"yield a healthy daily average of","meaning":"每日平均產量可觀，達……","examples":[{"en":"The nets yielded a healthy daily average of 11,000 litres.","zh":"這些網每日平均產量可觀，達11,000公升。"},{"en":"To yield a healthy daily average of something means to produce a strong or satisfactory amount each day on average.","zh":"「yield a healthy daily average of」某數量，意思是每日平均產出強而令人滿意的數量。"},{"en":"A community garden may yield a healthy weekly average of vegetables during summer.","zh":"社區花園在夏季可能每週平均產出可觀蔬菜。"},{"en":"If fog nets produce thousands of litres daily, they can support village water needs.","zh":"如果集霧網每日產出數千公升，就可以支援村莊用水需要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a productive and useful average output.","zh":"這個短語描述具生產力且有用的平均產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on a smaller scale","meaning":"以較小規模","examples":[{"en":"Fog nets have also been used on a smaller scale elsewhere.","zh":"集霧網也曾在其他地方以較小規模使用。"},{"en":"On a smaller scale means in a smaller size, amount, or operation.","zh":"「on a smaller scale」意思是以較小大小、數量或運作規模進行。"},{"en":"A school may try a recycling scheme on a smaller scale before using it across the whole campus.","zh":"學校可能先以較小規模試行回收計劃，再推廣至全校。"},{"en":"If a village has fewer people, a smaller fog-collection system may be enough.","zh":"如果村莊人口較少，較小型集霧系統可能已足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a limited version of a larger idea.","zh":"這個短語描述較大想法的有限版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fog-collecting nets","meaning":"集霧網","examples":[{"en":"Fog-collecting nets have been installed in several dry regions.","zh":"集霧網已安裝在幾個乾旱地區。"},{"en":"Fog-collecting nets are nets designed to capture water droplets from fog.","zh":"「fog-collecting nets」是設計用來捕捉霧中水滴的網。"},{"en":"A dry mountain village may place fog-collecting nets where fog passes most often.","zh":"乾旱山村可能把集霧網放在霧最常經過的位置。"},{"en":"If the nets collect enough droplets, the water can be channelled into tanks.","zh":"如果網收集到足夠水滴，水就可以被引入水箱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the practical equipment used in fog-water projects.","zh":"這個短語描述集霧水項目中使用的實用設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"due to its need for","meaning":"由於需要……","examples":[{"en":"Fog collection is limited due to its need for several favourable conditions.","zh":"集霧因需要幾種有利條件而受限制。"},{"en":"Due to its need for something means because it requires that thing.","zh":"「due to its need for」某物，意思是因為它需要該物。"},{"en":"A school camping trip may be cancelled due to its need for safe weather.","zh":"學校露營可能因需要安全天氣而取消。"},{"en":"If fog collection needs special geography and climate, it cannot work everywhere.","zh":"如果集霧需要特殊地理和氣候，它就不能在每個地方運作。"},{"en":"The phrase explains a limitation by pointing to a requirement.","zh":"這個短語透過指出要求來解釋限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a combination of factors","meaning":"多項因素的配合","examples":[{"en":"Successful fog formation depends on a combination of factors.","zh":"成功形成霧取決於多項因素的配合。"},{"en":"A combination of factors means several causes or conditions working together.","zh":"「a combination of factors」意思是幾個原因或條件共同作用。"},{"en":"Good exam performance usually depends on a combination of sleep, practice, and clear teaching.","zh":"良好考試表現通常取決於睡眠、練習和清晰教學等多項因素配合。"},{"en":"If one required factor is missing, fog collection may fail even if other conditions are present.","zh":"如果缺少其中一個必要因素，即使其他條件存在，集霧也可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one cause alone is not enough.","zh":"這個短語顯示單一原因並不足夠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not readily available","meaning":"並非隨時可得","examples":[{"en":"Fog is not readily available in every dry region.","zh":"霧並非在每個乾旱地區都隨時可得。"},{"en":"Not readily available means not easy to obtain or not commonly present when needed.","zh":"「not readily available」意思是不容易取得，或在需要時不常出現。"},{"en":"Fresh vegetables may not be readily available in a remote village during winter.","zh":"冬季偏遠村莊可能並非隨時可得新鮮蔬菜。"},{"en":"If fog is rare in a desert, fog nets cannot provide regular water.","zh":"如果沙漠很少有霧，集霧網就不能提供穩定用水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limited access or supply.","zh":"這個短語描述取得或供應有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"appear far more frequently","meaning":"出現得頻密得多","examples":[{"en":"Dew appears far more frequently than fog.","zh":"露水出現得比霧頻密得多。"},{"en":"To appear far more frequently means to happen or be seen much more often.","zh":"「appear far more frequently」意思是發生或被看見的次數多很多。"},{"en":"Small spelling mistakes appear far more frequently than serious grammar errors in some essays.","zh":"在某些作文中，小拼寫錯誤出現得比嚴重文法錯誤頻密得多。"},{"en":"If dew appears more often than fog, it may be a more reliable water source in some places.","zh":"如果露水比霧更常出現，在某些地方它可能是較可靠水源。"},{"en":"The phrase compares how often two things occur.","zh":"這個短語比較兩件事出現頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be less subject to","meaning":"較少受……限制","examples":[{"en":"Dew is less subject to the constraints of geography.","zh":"露水較少受地理限制。"},{"en":"To be less subject to something means to be less affected or limited by it.","zh":"「be less subject to」某事，意思是較少受其影響或限制。"},{"en":"Online lessons are less subject to travel delays than face-to-face classes.","zh":"網上課程較少受交通延誤限制。"},{"en":"If dew can form in more places than fog, it is less restricted by geography.","zh":"如果露水能在比霧更多的地方形成，它就較少受地理限制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes having fewer limitations from a factor.","zh":"這個短語描述較少受到某因素限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the constraints of climate and geography","meaning":"氣候與地理限制","examples":[{"en":"Fog collection is strongly affected by the constraints of climate and geography.","zh":"集霧強烈受氣候與地理限制影響。"},{"en":"The constraints of climate and geography are the limits created by weather patterns and physical location.","zh":"「the constraints of climate and geography」是由天氣模式和實體位置造成的限制。"},{"en":"Farming in a mountain village is shaped by the constraints of climate and geography.","zh":"山村農業受氣候與地理限制塑造。"},{"en":"If an area lacks cool slopes and moist air, fog collection may not be practical.","zh":"如果某地缺少清涼山坡和濕空氣，集霧可能不切實際。"},{"en":"The phrase describes natural limits that affect what people can do.","zh":"這個短語描述影響人類可做事情的自然限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in order for dew to form","meaning":"要形成露水","examples":[{"en":"In order for dew to form, the air must contain some moisture.","zh":"要形成露水，空氣必須含有一些水分。"},{"en":"In order for dew to form means for dew formation to happen, certain conditions must exist.","zh":"「in order for dew to form」意思是為了讓露水形成，必須存在某些條件。"},{"en":"In order for ice to form, the temperature must fall below freezing.","zh":"要形成冰，溫度必須降至冰點以下。"},{"en":"If the air is completely dry, dew cannot form even if the ground cools.","zh":"如果空氣完全乾燥，即使地面冷卻也不能形成露水。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces necessary conditions.","zh":"這個短語引入必要條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"humidity in the air","meaning":"空氣中的濕度","examples":[{"en":"Dew formation requires some humidity in the air.","zh":"露水形成需要空氣中有一定濕度。"},{"en":"Humidity in the air is the amount of water vapour present in the atmosphere.","zh":"「humidity in the air」是大氣中存在的水蒸氣量。"},{"en":"On humid summer days, humidity in the air makes clothes feel sticky.","zh":"在潮濕夏日，空氣中的濕度令衣服感覺黏身。"},{"en":"If there is enough humidity and surfaces cool quickly, dew may appear.","zh":"如果濕度足夠，而表面快速冷卻，就可能出現露水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moisture held in the air.","zh":"這個短語描述空氣中含有的水分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a reasonably clear sky","meaning":"相當晴朗的天空","examples":[{"en":"A reasonably clear sky helps the ground cool rapidly.","zh":"相當晴朗的天空有助地面迅速冷卻。"},{"en":"A reasonably clear sky is a sky with few enough clouds to allow heat to escape easily.","zh":"「a reasonably clear sky」是雲量少到足以讓熱量容易散失的天空。"},{"en":"Stargazers prefer a reasonably clear sky because clouds block the view.","zh":"觀星者喜歡相當晴朗的天空，因為雲會遮擋視線。"},{"en":"If the sky is clear at night, the ground may lose heat and dew may form.","zh":"如果夜空晴朗，地面可能散失熱量並形成露水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes conditions that are clear enough, though not perfectly cloudless.","zh":"這個短語描述足夠晴朗的情況，但不一定完全無雲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"suffer from a lack of water","meaning":"面對缺水問題","examples":[{"en":"Many hot regions suffer from a lack of water.","zh":"許多炎熱地區面對缺水問題。"},{"en":"To suffer from a lack of water means to experience problems because there is not enough water.","zh":"「suffer from a lack of water」意思是因水不足而經歷問題。"},{"en":"A school may suffer from a lack of water if toilets cannot be cleaned and students cannot drink safely.","zh":"如果廁所無法清潔、學生不能安全飲水，學校可能面對缺水問題。"},{"en":"If a region lacks water, farming, hygiene, and health can all be affected.","zh":"如果一個地區缺水，農業、衛生和健康都可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes hardship caused by water shortage.","zh":"這個短語描述由缺水造成的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the Sahel region","meaning":"非洲北部薩赫勒地區","examples":[{"en":"The Sahel region of northern Africa experiences severe water shortages.","zh":"非洲北部薩赫勒地區經歷嚴重缺水。"},{"en":"The Sahel region is a dry belt of land south of the Sahara Desert in Africa.","zh":"「the Sahel region」是非洲撒哈拉沙漠以南的一條乾旱地帶。"},{"en":"Communities in the Sahel region may depend heavily on seasonal rainfall.","zh":"薩赫勒地區的社區可能高度依賴季節性降雨。"},{"en":"If rainfall fails in the Sahel, food production and drinking-water access can suffer.","zh":"如果薩赫勒地區降雨失敗，糧食生產和飲用水取得都可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific dry region of Africa.","zh":"這個短語命名非洲一個特定乾旱地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"significant quantities of dew","meaning":"大量露水","examples":[{"en":"Some dry regions experience significant quantities of dew.","zh":"有些乾旱地區會出現大量露水。"},{"en":"Significant quantities of dew means enough dew to be noticeable or potentially useful.","zh":"「significant quantities of dew」意思是露水多到明顯或可能有用。"},{"en":"A garden may collect significant quantities of dew on leaves after a cool night.","zh":"清涼夜晚後，花園葉片上可能收集到大量露水。"},{"en":"If dew appears in large enough amounts, it may become a possible small-scale water source.","zh":"如果露水量足夠大，它可能成為可能的小規模水源。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the amount is not tiny or meaningless.","zh":"這個短語強調數量不是微不足道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be lowered over a short period","meaning":"在短時間內下降","examples":[{"en":"Air temperature may be lowered rapidly over a short period.","zh":"空氣溫度可能在短時間內迅速下降。"},{"en":"To be lowered over a short period means to decrease within a brief time.","zh":"「be lowered over a short period」意思是在短時間內降低。"},{"en":"A classroom temperature may be lowered over a short period when air conditioning is turned on.","zh":"開啟冷氣後，課室溫度可能在短時間內下降。"},{"en":"If temperature drops quickly at night, moisture may condense into dew.","zh":"如果夜間溫度快速下降，水分可能凝結成露水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fast decrease within limited time.","zh":"這個短語描述有限時間內的快速下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"water-harvesting possibilities","meaning":"集水潛力","examples":[{"en":"A rapid temperature fall improves water-harvesting possibilities.","zh":"氣溫急降會改善集水潛力。"},{"en":"Water-harvesting possibilities are chances or opportunities to collect usable water.","zh":"「water-harvesting possibilities」是收集可用水的機會或可能性。"},{"en":"A village studies water-harvesting possibilities before building rain tanks or fog nets.","zh":"村莊在建雨水箱或集霧網前，會研究集水潛力。"},{"en":"If weather conditions create more dew, the possibility of collecting water improves.","zh":"如果天氣條件產生更多露水，收集水的可能性就提高。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical chances to gather water from nature.","zh":"這個短語描述從大自然收集水的實際機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"yield ten grams of water","meaning":"產出十克水","examples":[{"en":"Each cubic metre of air may yield ten grams of water.","zh":"每立方米空氣可能產出十克水。"},{"en":"To yield ten grams of water means to produce or provide ten grams of water.","zh":"「yield ten grams of water」意思是產生或提供十克水。"},{"en":"A small plant pot may yield only a few grams of water if moisture is collected from its leaves.","zh":"如果從葉片收集水分，一個小花盆可能只產出幾克水。"},{"en":"If each cubic metre of air yields little water, large volumes of air must be processed.","zh":"如果每立方米空氣產水很少，就必須處理大量空氣。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a measured output from air.","zh":"這個短語給出從空氣取得的量度產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"each cubic metre of air","meaning":"每立方米空氣","examples":[{"en":"The calculation is based on each cubic metre of air.","zh":"計算以每立方米空氣為基礎。"},{"en":"Each cubic metre of air means every block of air measuring one metre by one metre by one metre.","zh":"「each cubic metre of air」意思是每個一米乘一米乘一米的空氣體積。"},{"en":"Scientists may measure pollution in each cubic metre of air to compare city districts.","zh":"科學家可能量度每立方米空氣中的污染物，以比較城市區域。"},{"en":"If each cubic metre contains only a little water, collection systems need to handle large air volumes.","zh":"如果每立方米只含少量水分，收集系統就需要處理大量空氣。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a unit for measuring air content.","zh":"這個短語提供量度空氣含量的單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"significant drops in temperature","meaning":"顯著的溫度下降","examples":[{"en":"Significant drops in temperature produce greater quantities of dew.","zh":"顯著的溫度下降會產生更多露水。"},{"en":"Significant drops in temperature are large or meaningful decreases in temperature.","zh":"「significant drops in temperature」是大幅或有意義的溫度下降。"},{"en":"Significant drops in temperature overnight may make windows wet by morning.","zh":"夜間顯著降溫可能令窗戶到早上變濕。"},{"en":"If temperature falls sharply, water vapour is more likely to condense.","zh":"如果溫度急劇下降，水蒸氣更可能凝結。"},{"en":"The phrase describes temperature changes large enough to affect conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述大到足以影響條件的溫度變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"make for greater yields","meaning":"帶來更高產量","examples":[{"en":"Lower temperatures make for greater water yields.","zh":"較低溫度會帶來更高產水量。"},{"en":"To make for greater yields means to create conditions that lead to larger output.","zh":"「make for greater yields」意思是創造導致更高產出的條件。"},{"en":"Good soil and regular watering make for greater vegetable yields in a garden.","zh":"良好泥土和規律澆水會為花園帶來更高蔬菜產量。"},{"en":"If cooling increases condensation, more water can be collected.","zh":"如果冷卻增加凝結，就可以收集更多水。"},{"en":"The phrase links favourable conditions with higher production.","zh":"這個短語把有利條件與較高產量連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unlike fog","meaning":"與霧不同","examples":[{"en":"Unlike fog, dew can form in relatively dry air.","zh":"與霧不同，露水可以在相對乾燥的空氣中形成。"},{"en":"Unlike fog means different from fog in the way being discussed.","zh":"「unlike fog」意思是在所討論方面與霧不同。"},{"en":"Unlike buses, trains usually run on fixed tracks and cannot change route easily.","zh":"與巴士不同，火車通常在固定軌道上行駛，不能輕易改路線。"},{"en":"If dew is less dependent on thick moisture than fog, it may be useful in more places.","zh":"如果露水比霧較少依賴濃厚水氣，它可能在更多地方有用。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a contrast between two things.","zh":"這個短語引入兩件事之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a relatively dry atmosphere","meaning":"相對乾燥的大氣","examples":[{"en":"Dew may form even in a relatively dry atmosphere.","zh":"即使在相對乾燥的大氣中，露水也可能形成。"},{"en":"A relatively dry atmosphere is air that has less moisture than humid air but is not completely dry.","zh":"「a relatively dry atmosphere」是比潮濕空氣水分少，但並非完全乾燥的空氣。"},{"en":"A desert morning may still bring dew if the atmosphere is relatively dry but temperatures fall sharply.","zh":"如果大氣相對乾燥但溫度急降，沙漠清晨仍可能有露水。"},{"en":"If there is at least some moisture, cooling may allow dew to form.","zh":"如果至少有一些水分，冷卻就可能讓露水形成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes air with limited but not zero humidity.","zh":"這個短語描述濕度有限但不是零的空氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the right mix of","meaning":"適當的……組合","examples":[{"en":"Dew forms when the right mix of air and ground temperatures occurs.","zh":"當空氣和地面溫度出現適當組合時，露水便形成。"},{"en":"The right mix of things means the correct combination needed for a result.","zh":"「the right mix of」某些事物，意思是達成結果所需的正確組合。"},{"en":"A good study group needs the right mix of planning, discussion, and quiet work.","zh":"好的學習小組需要規劃、討論和安靜工作的適當組合。"},{"en":"If air temperature and ground temperature combine properly, dew can form.","zh":"如果空氣溫度和地面溫度適當結合，露水就能形成。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights balance between several conditions.","zh":"這個短語突出多個條件之間的平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"combine","meaning":"結合","examples":[{"en":"Dew forms when suitable temperatures combine with sufficient humidity.","zh":"當合適溫度與足夠濕度結合時，露水便形成。"},{"en":"To combine means to come together or join with something else.","zh":"「combine」意思是聚在一起或與另一事物結合。"},{"en":"A successful school event combines careful planning with student enthusiasm.","zh":"成功的學校活動結合仔細規劃和學生熱情。"},{"en":"If cool ground combines with moist air, condensation can occur.","zh":"如果清涼地面與濕空氣結合，就可能發生凝結。"},{"en":"The word describes different elements working together.","zh":"這個詞描述不同元素共同作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"dew formation occurs","meaning":"露水形成","examples":[{"en":"Dew formation occurs when the ground cools sufficiently.","zh":"當地面充分冷卻時，露水形成。"},{"en":"Dew formation occurs means dew begins to form under the right physical conditions.","zh":"「dew formation occurs」意思是在合適物理條件下，露水開始形成。"},{"en":"Dew formation occurs on grass when a cool night follows a humid day.","zh":"當潮濕日子後出現清涼夜晚，草地上便會有露水形成。"},{"en":"If the surface temperature falls enough, water vapour can condense into droplets.","zh":"如果表面溫度下降到足夠程度，水蒸氣可以凝結成水滴。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the event of dew appearing.","zh":"這個短語描述露水出現這一事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as a method of obtaining","meaning":"作為取得……的方法","examples":[{"en":"The question evaluates fog as a method of obtaining fresh water.","zh":"題目評估霧作為取得淡水的方法。"},{"en":"As a method of obtaining something means as a way to get or collect it.","zh":"「as a method of obtaining」某物，意思是作為取得或收集它的一種方法。"},{"en":"Some families use online shopping as a method of obtaining groceries when shops are far away.","zh":"當商店很遠時，有些家庭使用網購作為取得雜貨的方法。"},{"en":"If fog collection is unreliable, it may not be the best method of obtaining water everywhere.","zh":"如果集霧不可靠，它未必是在所有地方取得水的最佳方法。"},{"en":"The phrase frames something as a practical means to an end.","zh":"這個短語把某事表述為達成目的的實際手段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"form best when","meaning":"在……時形成得最好","examples":[{"en":"One option suggests that fog forms best when the air is dry.","zh":"其中一個選項指霧在空氣乾燥時形成得最好。"},{"en":"To form best when something happens means to develop most successfully under that condition.","zh":"「form best when」某事發生，意思是在該條件下最成功地形成。"},{"en":"Bread dough rises best when the temperature is warm and stable.","zh":"麵糰在溫暖而穩定的溫度下發得最好。"},{"en":"If fog forms best under moist conditions, dry air would not be ideal.","zh":"如果霧在潮濕條件下形成得最好，乾空氣就不是理想條件。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the most favourable condition for formation.","zh":"這個短語指出形成的最有利條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be easier to collect than","meaning":"比……更容易收集","examples":[{"en":"The question compares whether fog is easier to collect than dew.","zh":"題目比較霧是否比露水更容易收集。"},{"en":"To be easier to collect than something means to require less effort, cost, or technology to gather.","zh":"「be easier to collect than」某物，意思是收集時需要較少力氣、成本或科技。"},{"en":"Rainwater is usually easier to collect than underground water because it falls directly onto roofs.","zh":"雨水通常比地下水更容易收集，因為它直接落在屋頂上。"},{"en":"If dew appears more often but in smaller amounts, collection difficulty must be compared carefully.","zh":"如果露水出現更頻密但量較少，就必須仔細比較收集難度。"},{"en":"The phrase sets up a practical comparison.","zh":"這個短語建立實際比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be tried on a large scale","meaning":"以大規模試行","examples":[{"en":"Some water-collection methods have been tried on a large scale.","zh":"有些集水方法已以大規模試行。"},{"en":"To be tried on a large scale means to be tested with many people, places, or large systems.","zh":"「be tried on a large scale」意思是在多人、多地或大型系統中測試。"},{"en":"A recycling scheme may be tried on a large scale after a small pilot succeeds.","zh":"回收計劃在小型試點成功後，可能以大規模試行。"},{"en":"If a method works in one village, testing it on a larger scale shows whether it can help more people.","zh":"如果某方法在一條村可行，較大規模測試可以顯示它能否幫助更多人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad practical testing.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛實際測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"not easy to collect","meaning":"不容易收集","examples":[{"en":"Fog is not easy to collect because it requires specific conditions.","zh":"霧不容易收集，因為它需要特定條件。"},{"en":"Not easy to collect means difficult to gather in a useful amount.","zh":"「not easy to collect」意思是難以收集到有用數量。"},{"en":"Wild honey is not easy to collect if the hives are high in trees.","zh":"如果蜂巢在高樹上，野生蜂蜜就不容易收集。"},{"en":"If fog does not appear regularly, even good nets may collect little water.","zh":"如果霧不是規律出現，即使好網也可能收集很少水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical difficulty in gathering a resource.","zh":"這個短語描述收集資源時的實際困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"small-scale desalination","meaning":"小規模海水化淡","examples":[{"en":"Small-scale desalination can be relatively energy-efficient.","zh":"小規模海水化淡可以相對節能。"},{"en":"Small-scale desalination is desalination carried out in a limited system or for a small community.","zh":"「small-scale desalination」是在有限系統或為小社區進行的海水化淡。"},{"en":"A small island school may use small-scale desalination to produce drinking water for students.","zh":"小島學校可能使用小規模海水化淡為學生生產食水。"},{"en":"If the system stays small, sunlight and simple equipment may be enough.","zh":"如果系統維持小型，陽光和簡單設備可能已足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts local production with industrial-scale desalination.","zh":"這個短語對比本地小量生產與工業規模海水化淡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"use a considerable amount of energy","meaning":"使用大量能源","examples":[{"en":"Large desalination plants use a considerable amount of energy.","zh":"大型海水化淡廠使用大量能源。"},{"en":"To use a considerable amount of energy means to require a large quantity of power or fuel.","zh":"「use a considerable amount of energy」意思是需要大量電力或燃料。"},{"en":"An old freezer may use a considerable amount of energy if it runs all day.","zh":"如果舊冰箱整天運行，它可能使用大量能源。"},{"en":"If water production consumes much energy, it may become expensive and polluting.","zh":"如果產水消耗大量能源，它可能變得昂貴並造成污染。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that a process is energy-demanding.","zh":"這個短語提醒某過程能源需求高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the most effective way to","meaning":"……最有效的方法","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not describe desalination as the most effective way to obtain water.","zh":"文章並沒有把海水化淡描述為取得水的最有效方法。"},{"en":"The most effective way to do something is the method that works best overall.","zh":"「the most effective way to」做某事，是整體上效果最好的方法。"},{"en":"For many students, the most effective way to remember vocabulary is to use words in sentences.","zh":"對許多學生而言，記住詞彙最有效的方法是在句子中使用詞語。"},{"en":"If a method is costly or limited, it may not be the most effective solution despite being useful.","zh":"如果一種方法昂貴或有限，即使有用，也未必是最有效解決方法。"},{"en":"The phrase compares methods by results.","zh":"這個短語根據效果比較方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"obtain larger water reserves","meaning":"取得更多水資源儲備","examples":[{"en":"Countries need reliable methods to obtain larger water reserves.","zh":"各國需要可靠方法取得更多水資源儲備。"},{"en":"To obtain larger water reserves means to secure bigger supplies of water for future use.","zh":"「obtain larger water reserves」意思是確保取得更大量供未來使用的水。"},{"en":"A village may build extra tanks to obtain larger water reserves before the dry season.","zh":"村莊可能在旱季前建造額外水箱，以取得更多水資源儲備。"},{"en":"If reserves are larger, communities can survive longer during drought.","zh":"如果儲備較大，社區在乾旱中可以維持更久。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on increasing stored water security.","zh":"這個短語集中於增加儲水安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"use very little energy","meaning":"使用極少能源","examples":[{"en":"The small greenhouse system uses very little energy.","zh":"小型溫室系統使用極少能源。"},{"en":"To use very little energy means to require only a small amount of power or fuel.","zh":"「use very little energy」意思是只需要少量電力或燃料。"},{"en":"LED lights use very little energy compared with old bulbs.","zh":"LED 燈相比舊燈泡使用極少能源。"},{"en":"If a water system uses very little energy, it may be cheaper to run in poor communities.","zh":"如果供水系統使用極少能源，它在貧困社區可能較便宜運行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes low energy demand.","zh":"這個短語描述低能源需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"one of the largest stores of","meaning":"最大的……儲藏之一","examples":[{"en":"Groundwater is one of the largest stores of fresh water.","zh":"地下水是最大的淡水儲藏之一。"},{"en":"One of the largest stores of something is among the biggest reserves where it is kept.","zh":"「one of the largest stores of」某物，是保存該物的最大儲備之一。"},{"en":"A national archive may be one of the largest stores of historical photographs.","zh":"國家檔案館可能是歷史照片最大的儲藏之一。"},{"en":"If groundwater is one of the largest stores, protecting it from pollution is essential.","zh":"如果地下水是最大儲藏之一，保護它免受污染就至關重要。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a major reserve.","zh":"這個短語指出重大儲備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete each sentence","meaning":"完成每句句子","examples":[{"en":"Students complete each sentence with the correct ending.","zh":"學生用正確句末選項完成每句句子。"},{"en":"To complete each sentence means to fill in the missing part so the sentence makes sense.","zh":"「complete each sentence」意思是填上缺失部分，使句子意思完整。"},{"en":"In grammar practice, students complete each sentence by choosing the correct verb form.","zh":"在文法練習中，學生透過選擇正確動詞形式完成每句句子。"},{"en":"If students understand the passage, they can choose endings that match the meaning.","zh":"如果學生理解文章，他們就能選擇符合意思的句末。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the correct ending","meaning":"正確句末選項","examples":[{"en":"Each sentence must be matched with the correct ending.","zh":"每句句子必須配上正確句末選項。"},{"en":"The correct ending is the answer choice that completes the sentence accurately.","zh":"「the correct ending」是準確完成句子的答案選項。"},{"en":"A reading task may ask students to choose the correct ending from options A to F.","zh":"閱讀題可能要求學生從 A 至 F 選項中選出正確句末。"},{"en":"If the ending changes the meaning of the original information, it is not correct.","zh":"如果句末改變原文資訊的意思，它就不是正確答案。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the right sentence completion.","zh":"這個短語指正確的句子補全部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"turn salt water into drinking water","meaning":"把鹹水化成食水","examples":[{"en":"Desalination turns salt water into drinking water.","zh":"海水化淡把鹹水化成食水。"},{"en":"To turn salt water into drinking water means to remove enough salt to make it safe to drink.","zh":"「turn salt water into drinking water」意思是去除足夠鹽分，使它可安全飲用。"},{"en":"A dry coastal town may use a treatment plant to turn seawater into drinking water.","zh":"乾旱沿海城鎮可能使用處理廠把海水化成食水。"},{"en":"If salt remains too high, the water cannot be safely consumed.","zh":"如果鹽分仍然太高，水就不能安全飲用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making seawater useful for human needs.","zh":"這個短語描述把海水變成人類可用的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"via an evaporation process","meaning":"透過蒸發過程","examples":[{"en":"Small-scale desalination is being tried via an evaporation process.","zh":"小規模海水化淡正透過蒸發過程試行。"},{"en":"Via an evaporation process means by using evaporation as the method.","zh":"「via an evaporation process」意思是以蒸發作為方法。"},{"en":"Salt can be left behind via an evaporation process when water turns into vapour.","zh":"當水變成蒸氣時，鹽可以透過蒸發過程留下。"},{"en":"If sunlight drives evaporation, the system may require less external energy.","zh":"如果陽光推動蒸發，系統可能需要較少外部能源。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the route or method by which something happens.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事發生的途徑或方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"large-scale fresh water production","meaning":"大規模淡水生產","examples":[{"en":"Large-scale fresh water production through evaporation is energy-intensive.","zh":"透過蒸發進行大規模淡水生產需要大量能源。"},{"en":"Large-scale fresh water production means producing large amounts of usable fresh water.","zh":"「large-scale fresh water production」意思是大量生產可用淡水。"},{"en":"A city may need large-scale fresh water production if natural sources cannot meet demand.","zh":"如果天然水源不能滿足需求，城市可能需要大規模淡水生產。"},{"en":"If production is large-scale, small solar systems may no longer be enough.","zh":"如果生產是大規模的，小型太陽能系統可能不再足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes high-volume water production.","zh":"這個短語描述高產量產水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"not energy-efficient","meaning":"能源效益不高","examples":[{"en":"Large-scale desalination is often not energy-efficient.","zh":"大規模海水化淡通常能源效益不高。"},{"en":"Not energy-efficient means using too much energy for the amount of output produced.","zh":"「not energy-efficient」意思是相對產出而言使用太多能源。"},{"en":"An old washing machine may be not energy-efficient if it uses much electricity and water.","zh":"如果舊洗衣機耗用很多電和水，它可能能源效益不高。"},{"en":"If a desalination plant burns large amounts of fuel, the water may become costly.","zh":"如果海水化淡廠燃燒大量燃料，產出的水可能變得昂貴。"},{"en":"The phrase describes poor energy performance.","zh":"這個短語描述能源表現欠佳。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be made up of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"Atmospheric water is made up of clouds and water vapour.","zh":"大氣水分由雲和水蒸氣組成。"},{"en":"To be made up of something means to consist of those parts.","zh":"「be made up of」某物，意思是由那些部分組成。"},{"en":"A balanced meal may be made up of vegetables, rice, protein, and fruit.","zh":"均衡膳食可能由蔬菜、米飯、蛋白質和水果組成。"},{"en":"If atmospheric water is made up of vapour and clouds, collecting it requires different methods.","zh":"如果大氣水分由水蒸氣和雲組成，收集它就需要不同方法。"},{"en":"The phrase explains composition.","zh":"這個短語解釋組成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"both clouds and water vapour","meaning":"雲和水蒸氣兩者","examples":[{"en":"The atmosphere contains both clouds and water vapour.","zh":"大氣含有雲和水蒸氣兩者。"},{"en":"Both clouds and water vapour means the two forms are included together.","zh":"「both clouds and water vapour」意思是兩種形態都包括在內。"},{"en":"A weather lesson may discuss both clouds and water vapour to explain rainfall.","zh":"天氣課可能同時討論雲和水蒸氣，以解釋降雨。"},{"en":"If water exists in both visible and invisible forms, measurement and collection become more complex.","zh":"如果水同時以可見和不可見形式存在，量度和收集就變得更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that two related forms are present.","zh":"這個短語強調兩種相關形態都存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the use of dew as a water source","meaning":"以露水作為水源","examples":[{"en":"The use of dew as a water source is less restricted by location.","zh":"以露水作為水源較少受地點限制。"},{"en":"The use of dew as a water source means collecting dew for practical water supply.","zh":"「the use of dew as a water source」意思是收集露水作實際供水。"},{"en":"A dry village may study the use of dew as a water source when wells are unreliable.","zh":"當水井不可靠，乾旱村莊可能研究以露水作為水源。"},{"en":"If dew forms in more places than fog, it may serve more communities.","zh":"如果露水在比霧更多的地方形成，它可能服務更多社區。"},{"en":"The phrase treats dew as a practical resource rather than just a weather detail.","zh":"這個短語把露水視為實際資源，而不只是天氣現象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be affected by temperature and location","meaning":"受溫度和地點影響","examples":[{"en":"Water-collection methods may be affected by temperature and location.","zh":"集水方法可能受溫度和地點影響。"},{"en":"To be affected by temperature and location means to change depending on heat, cold, and place.","zh":"「be affected by temperature and location」意思是因冷熱和地點而改變。"},{"en":"Outdoor sports are affected by temperature and location because heat and terrain change performance.","zh":"戶外運動受溫度和地點影響，因為熱力和地形會改變表現。"},{"en":"If dew collection needs cool nights, warmer locations may produce less water.","zh":"如果集露需要清涼夜晚，較暖地方可能產水較少。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that environmental conditions matter.","zh":"這個短語顯示環境條件很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the amount collected","meaning":"收集到的數量","examples":[{"en":"The amount of dew collected depends partly on temperature change.","zh":"收集到的露水量部分取決於溫度變化。"},{"en":"The amount collected means the quantity gathered after a collection process.","zh":"「the amount collected」意思是收集過程後得到的數量。"},{"en":"After a charity sale, the amount collected may be counted and reported to students.","zh":"慈善義賣後，收集到的金額可能被點算並向學生報告。"},{"en":"If the temperature drops sharply, the amount collected from dew may increase.","zh":"如果溫度急劇下降，從露水收集到的數量可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the final collected quantity.","zh":"這個短語指最終收集量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"increase when temperatures fall rapidly","meaning":"在氣溫急降時增加","examples":[{"en":"Dew yield increases when temperatures fall rapidly.","zh":"露水產量在氣溫急降時增加。"},{"en":"To increase when temperatures fall rapidly means to become greater as temperatures drop quickly.","zh":"「increase when temperatures fall rapidly」意思是當溫度快速下降時變多。"},{"en":"Window condensation may increase when temperatures fall rapidly overnight.","zh":"當夜間溫度急降，窗戶凝結水可能增加。"},{"en":"If rapid cooling causes more vapour to condense, more dew can be collected.","zh":"如果快速冷卻令更多水蒸氣凝結，就可以收集更多露水。"},{"en":"The phrase links a fast temperature drop with a larger output.","zh":"這個短語把快速降溫與較高產量連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與文章資料相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷每個陳述是否與文章資料相符。"},{"en":"To agree with the information means to match what the passage says.","zh":"「agree with the information」意思是與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the passage says water use has risen and the statement says the same, it agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說用水量已上升，而陳述說同樣意思，它就與資料相符。"},{"en":"If a statement adds an unsupported claim, students should not mark it true too quickly.","zh":"如果陳述加入未被支持的說法，學生不應太快判為真。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN reading tasks.","zh":"這個短語用於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文章資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"「contradict the information」意思是說出與文章相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says dew is less restricted by location but a statement says it is more restricted, the statement contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說露水較少受地點限制，但陳述說它受更大限制，該陳述就與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"Direct contradiction means the evidence clearly goes against the statement.","zh":"直接矛盾意思是證據明顯反對該陳述。"},{"en":"The phrase describes conflict with the text.","zh":"這個短語描述與文本衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students write NOT GIVEN when there is no information on the issue.","zh":"當文中沒有相關資料時，學生寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not provide enough evidence to decide.","zh":"「no information on this」意思是文章沒有提供足夠證據作判斷。"},{"en":"If a passage discusses water volume but never mentions price in one country, there is no information on that price.","zh":"如果文章討論水量但從未提及某國價格，就沒有該價格的相關資料。"},{"en":"When information is missing, students should not guess from common knowledge.","zh":"當資料缺失時，學生不應憑常識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the NOT GIVEN answer type.","zh":"這個短語解釋 NOT GIVEN 答案類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"wealthier countries","meaning":"較富裕的國家","examples":[{"en":"People in wealthier countries generally consume more water.","zh":"較富裕國家的人通常消耗更多水。"},{"en":"Wealthier countries are countries with higher income and more developed services and infrastructure.","zh":"「wealthier countries」是收入較高、服務和基礎設施較發達的國家。"},{"en":"In wealthier countries, households may use more water for showers, gardens, and appliances.","zh":"在較富裕國家，家庭可能用更多水洗澡、澆花和使用電器。"},{"en":"If lifestyles involve more machines and services, water consumption may rise.","zh":"如果生活方式涉及更多機器和服務，用水量可能上升。"},{"en":"The phrase compares countries by economic resources.","zh":"這個短語以經濟資源比較國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"just as much as","meaning":"與……一樣多","examples":[{"en":"The statement compares whether wealthy countries use just as much water as poorer ones.","zh":"陳述比較富裕國家是否與較貧窮國家用水一樣多。"},{"en":"Just as much as means the same amount as another person or group.","zh":"「just as much as」意思是與另一人或群體數量相同。"},{"en":"A quiet student may contribute just as much as a loud student through written work.","zh":"安靜學生可能透過書面工作，貢獻與健談學生一樣多。"},{"en":"If one group does not use just as much water, the comparison is unequal.","zh":"如果一個群體用水並不一樣多，這個比較就不相等。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to compare quantity equally.","zh":"這個短語用於比較數量相等。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be sources of fresh water","meaning":"是淡水來源","examples":[{"en":"Glaciers, groundwater and rivers are all sources of fresh water.","zh":"冰川、地下水和河流都是淡水來源。"},{"en":"To be sources of fresh water means to provide or contain water that is not salty.","zh":"「be sources of fresh water」意思是提供或含有非鹹水。"},{"en":"Lakes and mountain streams can be sources of fresh water for nearby towns.","zh":"湖泊和山溪可以是附近城鎮的淡水來源。"},{"en":"If a source becomes polluted, it may no longer provide safe fresh water.","zh":"如果某來源受到污染，它可能不再提供安全淡水。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where fresh water can come from.","zh":"這個短語指出淡水可以來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"large bodies of water","meaning":"大型水體","examples":[{"en":"Large bodies of water contain enormous quantities of salt water.","zh":"大型水體含有大量鹹水。"},{"en":"Large bodies of water are big natural or artificial areas of water, such as oceans, seas, lakes, or reservoirs.","zh":"「large bodies of water」是大型天然或人工水域，例如海洋、海、湖泊或水庫。"},{"en":"Children may learn to identify large bodies of water on a world map.","zh":"孩子可能學習在世界地圖上辨認大型水體。"},{"en":"If a large body of water is salty, its size does not make it immediately drinkable.","zh":"如果大型水體是鹹的，其規模並不代表它可立即飲用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes major water areas.","zh":"這個短語描述主要水域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"yield the most fresh water","meaning":"產出最多淡水","examples":[{"en":"The largest bodies of water do not necessarily yield the most usable fresh water.","zh":"最大型水體不一定產出最多可用淡水。"},{"en":"To yield the most fresh water means to produce or provide the greatest amount of usable non-salty water.","zh":"「yield the most fresh water」意思是生產或提供最多可用非鹹水。"},{"en":"A small mountain spring may yield more drinking water than a polluted lake.","zh":"一個小山泉可能比受污染湖泊產出更多食水。"},{"en":"If ocean water is salty, it does not automatically yield usable water without treatment.","zh":"如果海水是鹹的，沒有處理就不會自動產出可用水。"},{"en":"The phrase compares actual usable output, not total water size.","zh":"這個短語比較實際可用產出，而不是總水量大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"become increasingly popular","meaning":"越來越普及","examples":[{"en":"Fog-net collection has become increasingly popular in some dry regions.","zh":"集霧網收集法在一些乾旱地區越來越普及。"},{"en":"To become increasingly popular means to be liked, used, or adopted by more and more people over time.","zh":"「become increasingly popular」意思是隨時間被越來越多人喜歡、使用或採納。"},{"en":"Reusable bottles have become increasingly popular as people worry about plastic waste.","zh":"隨着人們擔心塑膠垃圾，可重用水樽越來越普及。"},{"en":"If a water method is cheap and visible, more communities may begin to adopt it.","zh":"如果一種取水方法便宜而效果明顯，更多社區可能開始採用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a rising trend in acceptance or use.","zh":"這個短語描述接受度或使用量上升的趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"around the world","meaning":"世界各地","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have tested fog collection in several places around the world.","zh":"研究人員已在世界各地幾個地方測試集霧。"},{"en":"Around the world means in many different countries or regions globally.","zh":"「around the world」意思是在全球許多不同國家或地區。"},{"en":"Students around the world use online videos to learn languages.","zh":"世界各地的學生使用網上影片學習語言。"},{"en":"If a method is tested around the world, researchers can compare how it works in different climates.","zh":"如果一種方法在世界各地測試，研究人員就能比較它在不同氣候中的效果。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a global scope.","zh":"這個短語提供全球範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"if the sky is cloudy","meaning":"如果天空多雲","examples":[{"en":"Dew formation is less likely if the sky is heavily cloudy.","zh":"如果天空非常多雲，露水形成的可能性較低。"},{"en":"If the sky is cloudy means when many clouds cover the sky.","zh":"「if the sky is cloudy」意思是當大量雲層覆蓋天空時。"},{"en":"If the sky is cloudy, a family may cancel a picnic at the beach.","zh":"如果天空多雲，一家人可能取消海灘野餐。"},{"en":"Clouds can trap heat, so the ground may not cool enough for dew to form.","zh":"雲可以困住熱量，所以地面可能冷卻不足以形成露水。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a weather condition.","zh":"這個短語引入天氣條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"smaller villages","meaning":"較小型村落","examples":[{"en":"Alternative water systems can be useful in smaller villages.","zh":"替代供水系統在較小型村落可能有用。"},{"en":"Smaller villages are communities with fewer people and less infrastructure than towns or cities.","zh":"「smaller villages」是人口較少、基礎設施少於城鎮或城市的社區。"},{"en":"Smaller villages may rely on local wells, rain tanks, or simple collection systems.","zh":"較小型村落可能依靠本地水井、雨水箱或簡單收集系統。"},{"en":"If a technology produces only modest amounts of water, it may suit smaller villages better than large cities.","zh":"如果一種科技只產生中等水量，它可能比大城市更適合較小型村落。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to small rural or local communities.","zh":"這個短語指小型鄉村或本地社區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"isolated areas","meaning":"偏遠地區","examples":[{"en":"Fog and dew collection may benefit isolated areas.","zh":"集霧和集露可能有利於偏遠地區。"},{"en":"Isolated areas are places far from major towns, roads, services, or supply networks.","zh":"「isolated areas」是遠離主要城鎮、道路、服務或供應網絡的地方。"},{"en":"An isolated area may not receive regular water deliveries during bad weather.","zh":"天氣惡劣時，偏遠地區可能無法定期收到送水。"},{"en":"If pipes and roads are limited, local water collection becomes more valuable.","zh":"如果水管和道路有限，本地集水就變得更有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes places that are difficult to reach or connect.","zh":"這個短語描述難以到達或連接的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"major sources of water","meaning":"主要水源","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether fog and dew are major sources of water.","zh":"題目問霧和露水是否主要水源。"},{"en":"Major sources of water are important sources that provide a large or reliable share of supply.","zh":"「major sources of water」是提供大量或可靠供應份額的重要水源。"},{"en":"A city’s major sources of water may include reservoirs and rivers.","zh":"城市的主要水源可能包括水庫和河流。"},{"en":"If fog and dew provide only small amounts, they may be useful but not major sources.","zh":"如果霧和露水只提供少量水，它們可能有用，但不是主要水源。"},{"en":"The phrase distinguishes main supplies from supplementary ones.","zh":"這個短語區分主要供應與補充供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 6 - THE SEARCH FOR FRESH WATER.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 7":[{"front":"Australian visa application process","meaning":"澳洲簽證申請流程","examples":[{"en":"The guide explains the Australian visa application process.","zh":"這份指南解釋澳洲簽證申請流程。"},{"en":"The Australian visa application process is the set of steps people follow to apply for permission to enter Australia.","zh":"澳洲簽證申請流程，是人們申請入境澳洲許可時需要遵循的一系列步驟。"},{"en":"A student may read about the Australian visa application process before planning to study in Sydney.","zh":"學生計劃到悉尼讀書前，可能會先閱讀澳洲簽證申請流程。"},{"en":"If applicants misunderstand the process, they may submit the wrong form or miss important documents.","zh":"如果申請人誤解流程，可能會提交錯誤表格或遺漏重要文件。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the whole procedure, not just one form.","zh":"這個短語指整個程序，而不只是其中一份表格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be accepted online","meaning":"接受網上申請","examples":[{"en":"Applications for Australian visas are now accepted online.","zh":"澳洲簽證申請現已接受網上申請。"},{"en":"If applications are accepted online, people can submit them through a website instead of going to an office.","zh":"如果申請接受網上提交，人們可以透過網站遞交，而不用親身到辦公室。"},{"en":"A school registration form may be accepted online if parents can upload documents from home.","zh":"如果家長能在家上載文件，學校註冊表格也可能接受網上申請。"},{"en":"When applications are accepted online, applicants can save travel time and complete the process more conveniently.","zh":"當申請可在網上提交，申請人可以節省交通時間，更方便完成流程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a digital submission method.","zh":"這個短語描述數碼提交方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be in possession of","meaning":"持有……","examples":[{"en":"You should be in possession of the required documents before applying.","zh":"申請前，你應持有所需文件。"},{"en":"To be in possession of something means to have it with you or have legal control of it.","zh":"持有某物，指你擁有它、帶着它，或合法掌管它。"},{"en":"A traveller should be in possession of a valid passport before going to the airport.","zh":"旅客前往機場前應持有有效護照。"},{"en":"If you are not in possession of the right documents, your application may be delayed.","zh":"如果你沒有持有正確文件，申請可能會延誤。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds formal and is common in official instructions.","zh":"這個短語語氣正式，常見於官方指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"embark on the application process","meaning":"開始申請流程","examples":[{"en":"Applicants should prepare their documents before they embark on the application process.","zh":"申請人應在開始申請流程前準備好文件。"},{"en":"To embark on the application process means to begin the process of applying.","zh":"開始申請流程，指展開申請的程序。"},{"en":"A student should check school deadlines before they embark on a university application process.","zh":"學生在開始大學申請流程前，應先檢查學校截止日期。"},{"en":"If applicants prepare early, they can avoid problems after they start the application.","zh":"如果申請人及早準備，就能避免開始申請後出現問題。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and suggests starting a planned procedure.","zh":"這個短語較正式，暗示開始一個有計劃的程序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"current passport","meaning":"現時有效的護照","examples":[{"en":"You must provide details from your current passport.","zh":"你必須提供現時有效護照上的資料。"},{"en":"A current passport is the passport that is valid and being used now.","zh":"現時有效的護照，是目前有效並正在使用的護照。"},{"en":"When booking an international flight, travellers usually enter details from their current passport.","zh":"預訂國際航班時，旅客通常輸入現時有效護照上的資料。"},{"en":"If you use an old passport number, your visa record may not match your travel document.","zh":"如果你使用舊護照號碼，簽證記錄可能與旅行證件不相符。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the passport you can legally travel with at present.","zh":"這個短語指你目前可合法用來旅行的護照。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be valid for at least","meaning":"有效期至少為……","examples":[{"en":"Your passport must be valid for at least six months.","zh":"你的護照有效期必須至少為六個月。"},{"en":"If something is valid for at least a period of time, it remains legally acceptable for no less than that period.","zh":"如果某物有效期至少為某段時間，意思是它在不少於該段時間內仍然合法有效。"},{"en":"A student card may need to be valid for at least one semester to receive a discount.","zh":"學生證可能需要有效期至少為一個學期，才能享有折扣。"},{"en":"If a passport is not valid for long enough, an airline or immigration officer may refuse travel.","zh":"如果護照有效期不夠長，航空公司或入境人員可能拒絕旅客出行。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a minimum period of validity.","zh":"這個短語設定最低有效期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"at the date of application","meaning":"在申請當日","examples":[{"en":"The passport must have sufficient validity at the date of application.","zh":"護照在申請當日必須有足夠有效期。"},{"en":"At the date of application means on the exact day when the application is submitted.","zh":"在申請當日，指申請正式提交的那一天。"},{"en":"A scholarship applicant must be enrolled as a student at the date of application.","zh":"獎學金申請人在申請當日必須仍是註冊學生。"},{"en":"If a document is valid today but expires tomorrow, it may still be a problem for travel planning.","zh":"如果文件今天有效但明天到期，對旅行安排仍可能造成問題。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the official application day.","zh":"這個短語強調正式申請日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sponsor","meaning":"擔保人","examples":[{"en":"Some business-visa applicants must provide details of their sponsor.","zh":"一些商務簽證申請人必須提供擔保人的資料。"},{"en":"A sponsor is a person, company, or organisation that supports an applicant or takes responsibility for part of the application.","zh":"擔保人，是支援申請人或為部分申請承擔責任的個人、公司或機構。"},{"en":"A company may act as a sponsor when it invites a worker from another country.","zh":"公司邀請外國員工時，可能作為擔保人。"},{"en":"If the sponsor’s details are missing, the visa office may not be able to assess the application.","zh":"如果缺少擔保人資料，簽證部門可能無法評估申請。"},{"en":"The word often appears in immigration, business, and scholarship contexts.","zh":"這個詞常見於移民、商業和獎學金語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"associated nomination approval number","meaning":"相關提名批准編號","examples":[{"en":"The applicant may need an associated nomination approval number.","zh":"申請人可能需要相關提名批准編號。"},{"en":"An associated nomination approval number is an official reference number linked to an approved nomination.","zh":"相關提名批准編號，是與已獲批准提名相關的官方參考號碼。"},{"en":"An employer may give this number to a worker after the company’s nomination has been approved.","zh":"僱主的提名獲批後，可能會把這個編號交給員工。"},{"en":"If the number is entered incorrectly, the visa application may not match the sponsor’s approval.","zh":"如果編號輸入錯誤，簽證申請可能無法與擔保人的批准記錄相符。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a specific official code connected with a business application.","zh":"這個短語指與商務申請相關的特定官方代碼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"transaction reference number","meaning":"交易參考編號","examples":[{"en":"Keep your transaction reference number in a safe place.","zh":"請把交易參考編號妥善保存。"},{"en":"A transaction reference number is a code that identifies a payment or online transaction.","zh":"交易參考編號，是識別付款或網上交易的代碼。"},{"en":"After paying a school fee online, parents may receive a transaction reference number by email.","zh":"家長網上繳交學費後，可能會透過電郵收到交易參考編號。"},{"en":"If a payment problem occurs, the reference number helps staff find the record quickly.","zh":"如果付款出現問題，參考編號能幫助職員快速找到記錄。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an important payment-tracking code.","zh":"這個短語指重要的付款追蹤代碼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"apply only to","meaning":"只適用於……","examples":[{"en":"The document requirement applies only to certain business-visa applicants.","zh":"該文件要求只適用於某些商務簽證申請人。"},{"en":"If a rule applies only to a group, it affects that group and not everyone else.","zh":"如果規則只適用於某群體，它影響該群體，而不是所有人。"},{"en":"A school uniform rule may apply only to students attending official ceremonies.","zh":"校服規定可能只適用於出席正式典禮的學生。"},{"en":"If a requirement does not apply to you, you do not need to provide that document.","zh":"如果某要求不適用於你，你就不需要提供該文件。"},{"en":"The phrase limits a rule to specific people or cases.","zh":"這個短語把規則限制於特定人士或個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Long-Stay Temporary Business Visa","meaning":"長期臨時商務簽證","examples":[{"en":"The additional information is required for Long-Stay Temporary Business Visa applications.","zh":"長期臨時商務簽證申請需要額外資料。"},{"en":"A Long-Stay Temporary Business Visa is a visa for people staying in Australia temporarily for business-related purposes over a longer period.","zh":"長期臨時商務簽證，是讓人因商務相關目的在澳洲較長時間臨時逗留的簽證。"},{"en":"A company may help an overseas employee apply for a Long-Stay Temporary Business Visa.","zh":"公司可能協助海外員工申請長期臨時商務簽證。"},{"en":"If this visa type requires sponsor information, applicants must prepare business details carefully.","zh":"如果這類簽證需要擔保人資料，申請人就必須仔細準備商業資料。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific business-related visa category.","zh":"這個短語命名一種特定商務相關簽證類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in order to proceed online","meaning":"為了在網上繼續申請","examples":[{"en":"In order to proceed online, you need a suitable internet browser.","zh":"為了在網上繼續申請，你需要合適的網頁瀏覽器。"},{"en":"In order to proceed online means to continue the process through the internet.","zh":"為了在網上繼續申請，指透過互聯網繼續辦理流程。"},{"en":"In order to proceed online with a school form, parents may need an email address and password.","zh":"為了在網上繼續填寫學校表格，家長可能需要電郵地址和密碼。"},{"en":"If your browser is too old, you may not be able to continue the online application.","zh":"如果你的瀏覽器太舊，可能無法繼續網上申請。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what is needed before continuing digitally.","zh":"這個短語解釋繼續數碼流程前需要甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"up-to-date internet browser","meaning":"最新版本的網頁瀏覽器","examples":[{"en":"Applicants should use an up-to-date internet browser.","zh":"申請人應使用最新版本的網頁瀏覽器。"},{"en":"An up-to-date internet browser is a recent version of software used to view websites.","zh":"最新版本的網頁瀏覽器，是用來瀏覽網站的近期版本軟件。"},{"en":"A student may need an up-to-date browser to join an online exam platform.","zh":"學生可能需要最新版本的瀏覽器才能加入網上考試平台。"},{"en":"If the browser is outdated, pages may load incorrectly or security may be weaker.","zh":"如果瀏覽器過時，頁面可能載入錯誤，或安全性較弱。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to modern and properly updated browsing software.","zh":"這個短語指現代且已妥善更新的瀏覽軟件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be loaded on a computer","meaning":"安裝在電腦上","examples":[{"en":"The required browser should be loaded on your computer.","zh":"所需瀏覽器應安裝在你的電腦上。"},{"en":"If software is loaded on a computer, it is installed and ready to use there.","zh":"如果軟件安裝在電腦上，意思是它已被安裝並可在該電腦使用。"},{"en":"A school may require a reading app to be loaded on students’ tablets before class.","zh":"學校可能要求學生上課前先把閱讀應用程式安裝在平板電腦上。"},{"en":"If the browser is not loaded on your computer, you may need to install it first.","zh":"如果瀏覽器沒有安裝在你的電腦上，你可能需要先安裝它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes software being installed on a device.","zh":"這個短語描述軟件被安裝在裝置上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"internationally accepted credit card","meaning":"國際通用信用卡","examples":[{"en":"You need an internationally accepted credit card to pay the fee.","zh":"你需要國際通用信用卡來支付費用。"},{"en":"An internationally accepted credit card is a card that can be used for payments in many countries.","zh":"國際通用信用卡，是可在許多國家付款使用的信用卡。"},{"en":"Travellers often use internationally accepted credit cards to book hotels overseas.","zh":"旅客常用國際通用信用卡預訂海外酒店。"},{"en":"If your card is not accepted internationally, the online payment may fail.","zh":"如果你的信用卡不是國際通用，網上付款可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a payment card recognised across borders.","zh":"這個短語指跨境被認可的付款卡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pay the application charge","meaning":"支付申請費","examples":[{"en":"The credit card is used to pay the application charge.","zh":"信用卡用於支付申請費。"},{"en":"To pay the application charge means to pay the official fee required for an application.","zh":"支付申請費，指繳付申請所需的官方費用。"},{"en":"A student may need to pay the application charge before submitting a university form.","zh":"學生可能需要在提交大學表格前支付申請費。"},{"en":"If the charge is not paid, the application may not be processed.","zh":"如果沒有付款，申請可能不會被處理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes paying the required application fee.","zh":"這個短語描述繳付所需申請費。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"before embarking on","meaning":"在開始……之前","examples":[{"en":"Read the instructions before embarking on the application process.","zh":"在開始申請流程之前，請先閱讀指示。"},{"en":"Before embarking on something means before starting it, especially if it is a formal or important task.","zh":"在開始某事之前，指展開某項正式或重要任務之前。"},{"en":"Students should check the marking scheme before embarking on a long essay.","zh":"學生在開始寫長文之前，應先檢查評分準則。"},{"en":"If you read the instructions first, you are less likely to make mistakes later.","zh":"如果你先閱讀指示，之後犯錯的機會會較低。"},{"en":"The phrase gives advice to prepare before beginning.","zh":"這個短語給出開始前先準備的建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"understand what the process entails","meaning":"了解流程包含甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Applicants should understand what the process entails.","zh":"申請人應了解流程包含甚麼。"},{"en":"To understand what the process entails means to know what steps, duties, and requirements are involved.","zh":"了解流程包含甚麼，指知道其中涉及哪些步驟、責任和要求。"},{"en":"Before joining a school exchange, students should understand what the programme entails.","zh":"參加學校交流前，學生應了解該計劃包含甚麼。"},{"en":"If applicants do not understand the process, they may underestimate the time or documents needed.","zh":"如果申請人不了解流程，可能會低估所需時間或文件。"},{"en":"The phrase means knowing what the whole procedure includes.","zh":"這個短語指知道整個程序包括甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"steps involved","meaning":"所涉及的步驟","examples":[{"en":"The guide explains the steps involved in applying online.","zh":"這份指南解釋網上申請所涉及的步驟。"},{"en":"The steps involved are the actions that must be completed as part of a process.","zh":"所涉及的步驟，是流程中必須完成的行動。"},{"en":"A recipe explains the steps involved in baking bread, from mixing flour to cooling the loaf.","zh":"食譜解釋烘焙麵包所涉及的步驟，由混合麵粉到冷卻麵包。"},{"en":"If people know the steps involved, they can prepare documents in the right order.","zh":"如果人們知道所涉及的步驟，就能按正確次序準備文件。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the parts of a procedure.","zh":"這個短語強調程序的各部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be designed to","meaning":"被設計用來……","examples":[{"en":"This guide has been designed to explain the application procedure.","zh":"這份指南被設計用來解釋申請程序。"},{"en":"If something is designed to do a task, it is created for that purpose.","zh":"如果某物被設計用來做某事，意思是它是為該目的而製作。"},{"en":"A timetable is designed to help students organise classes and revision time.","zh":"時間表被設計用來幫助學生組織課堂和溫習時間。"},{"en":"If a guide is designed clearly, users can avoid confusion and complete tasks faster.","zh":"如果指南設計清晰，使用者就能避免混亂並更快完成任務。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the intended function of something.","zh":"這個短語指出某物的預期功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"read on","meaning":"繼續閱讀","examples":[{"en":"Please read on to learn what happens after you begin.","zh":"請繼續閱讀，以了解開始後會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Read on means continue reading the next part of the text.","zh":"繼續閱讀，指閱讀文本的下一部分。"},{"en":"If the first paragraph interests you, read on to find the full explanation.","zh":"如果第一段令你感興趣，請繼續閱讀以找到完整解釋。"},{"en":"Writers use “read on” to guide readers forward through instructions or a story.","zh":"作者使用 “read on” 來引導讀者繼續閱讀指示或故事。"},{"en":"The phrase is a friendly way to say “continue reading.”","zh":"這個短語是表示「繼續閱讀」的友善說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"get a better understanding of","meaning":"更深入了解……","examples":[{"en":"The guide will help you get a better understanding of the process.","zh":"這份指南會幫助你更深入了解流程。"},{"en":"To get a better understanding of something means to understand it more clearly and completely.","zh":"更深入了解某事，指更清楚、更完整地理解它。"},{"en":"Students get a better understanding of grammar when examples show real situations.","zh":"當例子展示真實情境，學生會更深入了解文法。"},{"en":"If applicants understand the process better, they may make fewer mistakes.","zh":"如果申請人更了解流程，犯錯可能較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improved comprehension.","zh":"這個短語描述理解改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what will happen next","meaning":"接下來會發生甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The instructions explain what will happen next.","zh":"指示解釋接下來會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"What will happen next means the next step or result after the current point.","zh":"接下來會發生甚麼，指目前階段之後的下一步或結果。"},{"en":"After submitting homework online, students may want to know what will happen next.","zh":"網上提交功課後，學生可能想知道接下來會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"If applicants know the next step, they can prepare payment, documents, or interviews calmly.","zh":"如果申請人知道下一步，就能冷靜準備付款、文件或面試。"},{"en":"The phrase helps reduce uncertainty in a process.","zh":"這個短語有助減少流程中的不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"once you start","meaning":"一旦開始……","examples":[{"en":"You should know what to expect once you start your application.","zh":"一旦開始申請，你應知道會遇到甚麼。"},{"en":"Once you start means after you begin doing something.","zh":"一旦開始，指開始做某事之後。"},{"en":"Once you start a timed exam, you should not waste time reading instructions again and again.","zh":"一旦開始限時考試，你就不應反覆浪費時間讀指示。"},{"en":"If you know the process before you start, you can complete it more confidently.","zh":"如果你在開始前已知道流程，就能更有信心完成它。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the point after an action begins.","zh":"這個短語標示某行動開始後的時間點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the first and most important thing to do","meaning":"首要及最重要的事情","examples":[{"en":"The first and most important thing to do is select the correct visa.","zh":"首要及最重要的事情是選擇正確簽證。"},{"en":"The first and most important thing to do is the step that should be done before anything else because it matters most.","zh":"首要及最重要的事情，是因最重要而應在其他事情之前完成的步驟。"},{"en":"Before writing an essay, the first and most important thing to do is understand the question.","zh":"寫作文前，首要及最重要的事情是理解題目。"},{"en":"If applicants choose the wrong visa, later steps may become useless.","zh":"如果申請人選錯簽證，後續步驟可能變得沒有用。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the top priority.","zh":"這個短語突出最高優先事項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"check that","meaning":"檢查並確認……","examples":[{"en":"Check that the visa is appropriate before proceeding.","zh":"繼續前，請檢查並確認該簽證是否合適。"},{"en":"To check that something is true means to make sure it is correct before continuing.","zh":"檢查並確認某事，指在繼續之前確保它正確。"},{"en":"Students should check that their name is on the answer sheet before handing it in.","zh":"學生交卷前應檢查並確認答題紙上有自己的名字。"},{"en":"If you check important details early, you can avoid problems later.","zh":"如果你及早檢查重要資料，之後就能避免問題。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a careful verification step.","zh":"這個短語引入仔細核實步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the visa you have selected","meaning":"你所選擇的簽證","examples":[{"en":"The visa you have selected must match your intended purpose.","zh":"你所選擇的簽證必須符合你的預定目的。"},{"en":"The visa you have selected means the particular visa type you have chosen.","zh":"你所選擇的簽證，指你已選定的特定簽證類別。"},{"en":"If a student selects a tourist visa instead of a student visa, the selected visa may not fit their plan.","zh":"如果學生選擇旅遊簽證而不是學生簽證，所選簽證可能不符合計劃。"},{"en":"If the visa you have selected is wrong, you may need to start again.","zh":"如果你所選擇的簽證錯誤，你可能需要重新開始。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the applicant’s chosen visa category.","zh":"這個短語指申請人選定的簽證類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be appropriate to your circumstances","meaning":"適合你的個人情況","examples":[{"en":"The visa must be appropriate to your circumstances.","zh":"該簽證必須適合你的個人情況。"},{"en":"If something is appropriate to your circumstances, it fits your personal situation and purpose.","zh":"如果某物適合你的個人情況，意思是它符合你的情況和目的。"},{"en":"A part-time course may be appropriate to a student’s circumstances if they also need to work.","zh":"如果學生也需要工作，兼讀課程可能適合其個人情況。"},{"en":"If a visa does not match your travel purpose, your application may fail.","zh":"如果簽證不符合你的旅行目的，申請可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses suitability to individual needs.","zh":"這個短語強調適合個人需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at the start of","meaning":"在……開始時","examples":[{"en":"Several questions appear at the start of the online application.","zh":"在網上申請開始時，會出現幾條問題。"},{"en":"At the start of something means at the beginning of it.","zh":"在某事開始時，指在其開端。"},{"en":"At the start of a lesson, the teacher may review yesterday’s key words.","zh":"在課堂開始時，老師可能重溫昨天的關鍵詞。"},{"en":"If important questions appear at the start, applicants should answer them carefully before moving on.","zh":"如果重要問題在開始時出現，申請人應先仔細回答再繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the beginning stage.","zh":"這個短語標示開始階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be asked a number of questions","meaning":"被問及若干問題","examples":[{"en":"You will be asked a number of questions about your circumstances.","zh":"你會被問及若干關於個人情況的問題。"},{"en":"To be asked a number of questions means to receive several questions that you must answer.","zh":"被問及若干問題，指收到幾條必須回答的問題。"},{"en":"At a doctor’s appointment, patients may be asked a number of questions about symptoms.","zh":"看醫生時，病人可能被問及若干關於症狀的問題。"},{"en":"If your answers show your situation clearly, staff can decide what form or service you need.","zh":"如果你的答案清楚顯示情況，職員就能決定你需要哪份表格或服務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a short questioning stage.","zh":"這個短語描述簡短提問階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"help someone confirm that","meaning":"幫助某人確認……","examples":[{"en":"The questions help applicants confirm that they selected the right visa.","zh":"這些問題幫助申請人確認自己選擇了正確簽證。"},{"en":"To help someone confirm that something is true means to help them check and be sure about it.","zh":"幫助某人確認某事，指幫助他們檢查並確定它是真的。"},{"en":"A checklist helps students confirm that they have answered every question.","zh":"清單幫助學生確認自己已回答每一題。"},{"en":"If screening questions confirm the correct visa type, applicants avoid choosing the wrong category.","zh":"如果篩選問題確認正確簽證類別，申請人就可避免選錯類別。"},{"en":"The phrase describes support for verification.","zh":"這個短語描述對核實的支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the right kind of visa","meaning":"正確類別的簽證","examples":[{"en":"It is important to apply for the right kind of visa.","zh":"申請正確類別的簽證很重要。"},{"en":"The right kind of visa is the visa type that matches the applicant’s purpose and situation.","zh":"正確類別的簽證，是符合申請人目的和情況的簽證類型。"},{"en":"A tourist should not apply for a student visa if they only plan to visit for a holiday.","zh":"如果旅客只是計劃度假，就不應申請學生簽證。"},{"en":"If you choose the wrong kind of visa, the application may be rejected or delayed.","zh":"如果你選錯簽證類別，申請可能被拒或延誤。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses correct visa category.","zh":"這個短語強調正確簽證類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"apply for a visa","meaning":"申請簽證","examples":[{"en":"Travellers must apply for an appropriate visa before departure.","zh":"旅客出發前必須申請合適簽證。"},{"en":"To apply for a visa means to formally request permission to enter or stay in a country.","zh":"申請簽證，指正式請求入境或逗留某國的許可。"},{"en":"A student may apply for a visa after receiving an offer from a foreign university.","zh":"學生收到外國大學錄取後，可能會申請簽證。"},{"en":"If travellers do not apply in time, they may have to change their flight plans.","zh":"如果旅客沒有及時申請，可能要更改航班安排。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the formal request for travel permission.","zh":"這個短語描述正式申請旅行許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be available for online application","meaning":"可供網上申請","examples":[{"en":"Certain visas are not available for online application.","zh":"某些簽證不可供網上申請。"},{"en":"If a visa is available for online application, people can apply for it through the internet.","zh":"如果某簽證可供網上申請，人們就能透過互聯網申請。"},{"en":"A school grant may be available for online application if students can upload supporting documents.","zh":"如果學生能上載證明文件，學校資助可能可供網上申請。"},{"en":"If a visa is not available online, applicants may need to visit an embassy or consulate.","zh":"如果簽證不可網上申請，申請人可能需要到大使館或領事館。"},{"en":"The phrase describes whether digital application is possible.","zh":"這個短語描述是否可以數碼申請。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"over the internet","meaning":"透過互聯網","examples":[{"en":"Most common visa types can be applied for over the internet.","zh":"大多數常見簽證類別可以透過互聯網申請。"},{"en":"Over the internet means using online services through a website or digital system.","zh":"透過互聯網，指使用網站或數碼系統的網上服務。"},{"en":"Many parents now pay school fees over the internet instead of visiting the office.","zh":"許多家長現在透過互聯網繳交學費，而不是到辦公室。"},{"en":"If forms can be submitted over the internet, applicants do not need to travel just to hand in papers.","zh":"如果表格可以透過互聯網提交，申請人就不需要只為交文件而出行。"},{"en":"The phrase means online.","zh":"這個短語意思是網上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"require your presence at","meaning":"需要你親身到……","examples":[{"en":"Some applications require your presence at an embassy or consulate.","zh":"有些申請需要你親身到大使館或領事館。"},{"en":"If something requires your presence at a place, you must go there in person.","zh":"如果某事需要你親身到某地，意思是你必須本人到場。"},{"en":"A driving test requires your presence at the test centre.","zh":"駕駛考試需要你親身到考試中心。"},{"en":"If a visa application requires your presence, online submission alone will not be enough.","zh":"如果簽證申請需要你親身到場，單靠網上提交並不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a need for physical attendance.","zh":"這個短語描述需要實體出席。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"local Australian embassy","meaning":"當地澳洲大使館","examples":[{"en":"You may need to visit your local Australian embassy.","zh":"你可能需要到訪當地澳洲大使館。"},{"en":"A local Australian embassy is the Australian government office in or near your country that handles diplomatic and visa matters.","zh":"當地澳洲大使館，是澳洲政府在你所在國家或附近處理外交及簽證事務的辦事處。"},{"en":"A traveller may contact the local Australian embassy if their visa cannot be completed online.","zh":"如果旅客無法網上完成簽證，可能會聯絡當地澳洲大使館。"},{"en":"If documents need to be checked in person, the embassy may ask the applicant to attend.","zh":"如果文件需要親身核實，大使館可能要求申請人到場。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an official Australian office overseas.","zh":"這個短語指澳洲在海外的官方辦事處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"consulate","meaning":"領事館","examples":[{"en":"A visa application may have to be completed at a consulate.","zh":"簽證申請可能需要在領事館完成。"},{"en":"A consulate is an official government office in another country that helps with visas and citizen services.","zh":"領事館，是一國政府在另一國設立、協助簽證和公民服務的官方辦事處。"},{"en":"Travellers may visit a consulate to replace a lost passport.","zh":"旅客可能到領事館補辦遺失的護照。"},{"en":"If an application cannot be handled online, a consulate may process it in person.","zh":"如果申請不能網上處理，領事館可能親身處理它。"},{"en":"The word refers to an official overseas office, usually smaller than an embassy.","zh":"這個詞指官方海外辦事處，通常比大使館小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"should you wish to proceed","meaning":"如你希望繼續辦理","examples":[{"en":"You may need to attend the embassy should you wish to proceed.","zh":"如你希望繼續辦理，可能需要到大使館。"},{"en":"Should you wish to proceed means if you want to continue.","zh":"如你希望繼續辦理，意思是如果你想繼續。"},{"en":"Should you wish to proceed with the course, you must pay the deposit by Friday.","zh":"如你希望繼續報讀該課程，必須在星期五前繳交訂金。"},{"en":"If applicants want to continue after online screening, they may need to attend an interview.","zh":"如果申請人在網上篩選後想繼續，可能需要參加面試。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to express a condition.","zh":"這個短語是表達條件的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in general","meaning":"一般而言","examples":[{"en":"In general, most common visas can be applied for online.","zh":"一般而言，大多數常見簽證可以網上申請。"},{"en":"In general means usually or in most cases.","zh":"一般而言，指通常或在大多數情況下。"},{"en":"In general, students learn better when examples are clear and practical.","zh":"一般而言，例子清楚而實用時，學生學得更好。"},{"en":"If a statement begins with “in general,” there may still be exceptions.","zh":"如果陳述以 “in general” 開始，仍可能有例外。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a broad rule, not an absolute rule.","zh":"這個短語引入廣泛規則，而不是絕對規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"most people will find that","meaning":"大部分人會發現……","examples":[{"en":"Most people will find that the online process is available to them.","zh":"大部分人會發現網上流程適用於他們。"},{"en":"Most people will find that means the majority of users are likely to discover or experience something.","zh":"大部分人會發現，指多數使用者很可能發現或經歷某事。"},{"en":"Most people will find that online banking saves time after they learn the basic steps.","zh":"大部分人在學會基本步驟後，會發現網上銀行節省時間。"},{"en":"If a process is available to most applicants, only special cases need extra arrangements.","zh":"如果流程適用於大部分申請人，就只有特殊個案需要額外安排。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces what is usually true for many people.","zh":"這個短語引入對許多人通常成立的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"common types of visa","meaning":"常見簽證類別","examples":[{"en":"Common types of visa include student and working-holiday visas.","zh":"常見簽證類別包括學生簽證和工作假期簽證。"},{"en":"Common types of visa are visa categories that many applicants frequently use.","zh":"常見簽證類別，是許多申請人經常使用的簽證種類。"},{"en":"Tourist visas, student visas, and work visas are common types in many countries.","zh":"在許多國家，旅遊簽證、學生簽證和工作簽證都是常見類別。"},{"en":"If a visa type is common, the online system may provide clearer standard instructions.","zh":"如果簽證類別常見，網上系統可能提供較清楚的標準指示。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to frequently used visa categories.","zh":"這個短語指經常使用的簽證類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"working-holiday visa","meaning":"工作假期簽證","examples":[{"en":"A working-holiday visa allows eligible travellers to work during their stay.","zh":"工作假期簽證容許合資格旅客在逗留期間工作。"},{"en":"A working-holiday visa is a visa that lets certain young travellers visit a country and take temporary work.","zh":"工作假期簽證，是讓某些年輕旅客到訪一個國家並從事臨時工作的簽證。"},{"en":"A graduate may apply for a working-holiday visa to travel and earn money abroad for a year.","zh":"畢業生可能申請工作假期簽證，到海外旅行並賺取生活費一年。"},{"en":"If the visa is approved, the traveller can combine tourism with short-term employment.","zh":"如果簽證獲批，旅客就能結合旅遊和短期工作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a visa for both travel and temporary work.","zh":"這個短語指兼具旅行和臨時工作用途的簽證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"student visa","meaning":"學生簽證","examples":[{"en":"Student-visa applicants must provide details of their intended studies.","zh":"學生簽證申請人必須提供擬修讀課程的詳細資料。"},{"en":"A student visa is a visa that allows someone to study in another country.","zh":"學生簽證，是容許某人在另一個國家讀書的簽證。"},{"en":"A teenager accepted by an Australian college may need a student visa before classes begin.","zh":"獲澳洲學院錄取的青少年，可能在開課前需要學生簽證。"},{"en":"If the course details are unclear, the visa office may ask for more information.","zh":"如果課程資料不清楚，簽證部門可能要求更多資料。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a visa connected with education.","zh":"這個短語指與教育相關的簽證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"employer-sponsored visa","meaning":"僱主擔保簽證","examples":[{"en":"An employer-sponsored visa requires information about the sponsoring business.","zh":"僱主擔保簽證需要擔保企業的資料。"},{"en":"An employer-sponsored visa is a visa supported by a company that wants to hire or employ the applicant.","zh":"僱主擔保簽證，是由想聘用申請人的公司支援的簽證。"},{"en":"A hospital may sponsor a nurse from overseas through an employer-sponsored visa.","zh":"醫院可能透過僱主擔保簽證擔保海外護士。"},{"en":"If the employer’s information is incomplete, the application may be delayed.","zh":"如果僱主資料不完整，申請可能延誤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a work visa connected with a sponsoring employer.","zh":"這個短語指與擔保僱主相關的工作簽證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be accessed online","meaning":"可在網上辦理","examples":[{"en":"Most common visa applications can be accessed online.","zh":"大多數常見簽證申請可在網上辦理。"},{"en":"If something can be accessed online, users can open or use it through the internet.","zh":"如果某物可在網上存取，使用者可以透過互聯網打開或使用它。"},{"en":"Students can access homework instructions online when they are absent from school.","zh":"學生缺席時，可以在網上查看功課指示。"},{"en":"If forms can be accessed online, applicants can begin without visiting an office.","zh":"如果表格可在網上取得，申請人不用到辦公室也能開始。"},{"en":"The phrase describes digital availability.","zh":"這個短語描述數碼可用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"start the process officially","meaning":"正式開始流程","examples":[{"en":"Clicking the button will start the process officially.","zh":"按下按鈕會正式開始流程。"},{"en":"To start the process officially means to begin the formal procedure in the system.","zh":"正式開始流程，指在系統中展開正式程序。"},{"en":"Paying a deposit may start a course registration process officially.","zh":"繳交訂金可能正式開始課程註冊流程。"},{"en":"Once the official process starts, the applicant may need to follow deadlines carefully.","zh":"一旦正式流程開始，申請人可能需要仔細遵守截止日期。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the formal beginning, not just preparation.","zh":"這個短語標示正式開始，而不只是準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"click the Apply Online button","meaning":"按下「網上申請」按鈕","examples":[{"en":"Applicants click the Apply Online button to begin.","zh":"申請人按下「網上申請」按鈕開始。"},{"en":"To click the Apply Online button means to press the website button that starts the online application.","zh":"按下「網上申請」按鈕，指按網站上開始網上申請的按鈕。"},{"en":"A student may click a “Submit Assignment” button after uploading homework.","zh":"學生上載功課後，可能按下「提交功課」按鈕。"},{"en":"If applicants click the wrong button, they may open the wrong form.","zh":"如果申請人按錯按鈕，可能會打開錯誤表格。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a simple but important website action.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單但重要的網站操作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"accompanying guidelines","meaning":"隨附指引","examples":[{"en":"Read all accompanying guidelines before completing the form.","zh":"填寫表格前，請閱讀所有隨附指引。"},{"en":"Accompanying guidelines are instructions provided together with a form or document.","zh":"隨附指引，是與表格或文件一同提供的指示。"},{"en":"A scholarship form may include accompanying guidelines explaining who can apply.","zh":"獎學金表格可能附有隨附指引，解釋誰可以申請。"},{"en":"If applicants ignore the guidelines, they may miss conditions or upload the wrong document.","zh":"如果申請人忽略指引，可能會錯過條件或上載錯誤文件。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to supporting instructions.","zh":"這個短語指支援性說明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"accompanying information","meaning":"隨附資料","examples":[{"en":"The accompanying information explains the conditions of the visa.","zh":"隨附資料解釋該簽證的條件。"},{"en":"Accompanying information is extra information provided together with the main document.","zh":"隨附資料，是與主要文件一同提供的額外資料。"},{"en":"A medicine bottle may include accompanying information about dosage and side effects.","zh":"藥瓶可能附有關於劑量和副作用的隨附資料。"},{"en":"If applicants read the accompanying information, they can understand rules before agreeing.","zh":"如果申請人閱讀隨附資料，就能在同意前理解規則。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to helpful supporting details.","zh":"這個短語指有用的輔助細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the type of visa application","meaning":"簽證申請類別","examples":[{"en":"The instructions depend on the type of visa application selected.","zh":"指示取決於所選擇的簽證申請類別。"},{"en":"The type of visa application means the specific category of visa form chosen by the applicant.","zh":"簽證申請類別，指申請人選擇的特定簽證表格種類。"},{"en":"A student visa application and a tourist visa application may ask for different evidence.","zh":"學生簽證申請和旅遊簽證申請可能要求不同證明。"},{"en":"If the application type changes, the required questions and documents may also change.","zh":"如果申請類別改變，所需問題和文件也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies which visa category is being applied for.","zh":"這個短語指出正在申請哪一類簽證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"appear on Page 1","meaning":"顯示於第一頁","examples":[{"en":"The relevant details will appear on Page 1.","zh":"相關資料將顯示於第一頁。"},{"en":"To appear on Page 1 means to be shown on the first page of a form or document.","zh":"顯示於第一頁，指在表格或文件的第一頁出現。"},{"en":"A student’s name and class may appear on Page 1 of an exam paper.","zh":"學生姓名和班別可能顯示於試卷第一頁。"},{"en":"If important conditions appear on the first page, applicants should read them before continuing.","zh":"如果重要條件顯示於第一頁，申請人應在繼續前閱讀。"},{"en":"The phrase tells users where to find information.","zh":"這個短語告訴使用者在哪裡找到資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"read through thoroughly","meaning":"徹底閱讀","examples":[{"en":"The guidelines should be read through thoroughly.","zh":"應徹底閱讀指引。"},{"en":"To read through thoroughly means to read all of something carefully from beginning to end.","zh":"徹底閱讀，指從頭到尾仔細閱讀全部內容。"},{"en":"Students should read through exam instructions thoroughly before answering.","zh":"學生作答前應徹底閱讀考試指示。"},{"en":"If applicants read carelessly, they may miss a condition that affects their application.","zh":"如果申請人粗心閱讀，可能會錯過影響申請的條件。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses complete and careful reading.","zh":"這個短語強調完整而仔細地閱讀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"before the applicant continues","meaning":"在申請人繼續之前","examples":[{"en":"The information must be reviewed before the applicant continues.","zh":"在申請人繼續之前，必須覆核資料。"},{"en":"Before the applicant continues means before the person applying moves to the next step.","zh":"在申請人繼續之前，指申請者進入下一步之前。"},{"en":"A website may ask students to check their answers before they continue to payment.","zh":"網站可能要求學生在繼續付款前檢查答案。"},{"en":"If information is reviewed first, later errors may be avoided.","zh":"如果先覆核資料，之後的錯誤可能得以避免。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a required action before moving forward.","zh":"這個短語設定繼續前必須完成的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"officially start","meaning":"正式開始","examples":[{"en":"The application does not officially start until the conditions are accepted.","zh":"申請在條件被接受前不會正式開始。"},{"en":"To officially start means to begin formally according to rules or a system.","zh":"正式開始，指按照規則或系統正式展開。"},{"en":"A competition may not officially start until all teams have registered.","zh":"比賽可能要到所有隊伍註冊後才正式開始。"},{"en":"If the terms are not accepted, the application remains only at the preparation stage.","zh":"如果條款未被接受，申請仍只停留在準備階段。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the formal beginning of a process.","zh":"這個短語標示流程的正式開端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be necessary to","meaning":"有必要……","examples":[{"en":"It is necessary to accept the conditions before continuing.","zh":"繼續前有必要接受條件。"},{"en":"If it is necessary to do something, that action is required and cannot be skipped.","zh":"如果有必要做某事，該行動是必須的，不能略過。"},{"en":"It is necessary to bring an ID card when collecting an exam certificate.","zh":"領取考試證書時有必要帶身份證。"},{"en":"If a required step is ignored, the system may not allow the user to continue.","zh":"如果忽略必需步驟，系統可能不容許使用者繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase shows obligation or requirement.","zh":"這個短語表示義務或要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"accept the terms and conditions","meaning":"接受條款及細則","examples":[{"en":"Applicants must accept the terms and conditions.","zh":"申請人必須接受條款及細則。"},{"en":"To accept the terms and conditions means to agree to the official rules before using a service or continuing a process.","zh":"接受條款及細則，指在使用服務或繼續流程前同意官方規則。"},{"en":"Before using a new app, users often need to accept the terms and conditions.","zh":"使用新應用程式前，使用者通常需要接受條款及細則。"},{"en":"If applicants accept them without reading, they may not understand their responsibilities.","zh":"如果申請人不閱讀就接受，可能不了解自己的責任。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formal agreement to rules.","zh":"這個短語描述正式同意規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"check the I Agree box","meaning":"勾選「我同意」方格","examples":[{"en":"Check the I Agree box to confirm your acceptance.","zh":"勾選「我同意」方格，以確認你接受。"},{"en":"To check the I Agree box means to tick a box showing that you accept the rules or conditions.","zh":"勾選「我同意」方格，指剔選一個表示你接受規則或條件的方格。"},{"en":"A website may not let users continue until they check the agreement box.","zh":"網站可能不讓使用者繼續，直到他們勾選同意方格。"},{"en":"If you tick the box, the system treats it as confirmation of your consent.","zh":"如果你勾選方格，系統會把它視為你同意的確認。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common online confirmation action.","zh":"這個短語描述常見的網上確認動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"move on to","meaning":"繼續進入……","examples":[{"en":"After accepting the conditions, you can move on to the application form.","zh":"接受條件後，你可以繼續進入申請表格。"},{"en":"To move on to something means to continue to the next stage or topic.","zh":"繼續進入某事，指前往下一個階段或主題。"},{"en":"After checking homework answers, a teacher may move on to a new grammar point.","zh":"檢查功課答案後，老師可能繼續進入新的文法重點。"},{"en":"If applicants complete one step correctly, they can move on to the next screen.","zh":"如果申請人正確完成一個步驟，就可以進入下一個頁面。"},{"en":"The phrase describes progression.","zh":"這個短語描述進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"actual application form","meaning":"正式申請表格","examples":[{"en":"The actual application form contains several short screens.","zh":"正式申請表格包含幾個簡短頁面。"},{"en":"The actual application form is the real form where applicants enter their required information.","zh":"正式申請表格，是申請人輸入所需資料的真正表格。"},{"en":"A school website may show instructions first before opening the actual application form.","zh":"學校網站可能先顯示指示，然後才打開正式申請表格。"},{"en":"If users confuse instructions with the form, they may think they have already applied when they have not.","zh":"如果使用者把指示和表格混淆，可能以為自己已申請，其實沒有。"},{"en":"The phrase separates the real form from the guidance around it.","zh":"這個短語把真正表格與周邊指引區分開來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"screens to complete","meaning":"需要填寫的頁面","examples":[{"en":"There will be between five and nine short screens to complete.","zh":"會有五至九個簡短頁面需要填寫。"},{"en":"Screens to complete are online pages where users must enter or check information.","zh":"需要填寫的頁面，是使用者必須輸入或檢查資料的網上頁面。"},{"en":"An online registration system may have several screens to complete before payment.","zh":"網上註冊系統在付款前可能有幾個頁面需要填寫。"},{"en":"If there are many screens, applicants should allow enough time and avoid rushing.","zh":"如果頁面很多，申請人應預留足夠時間，避免匆忙。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the pages in an online form.","zh":"這個短語指網上表格中的頁面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"depending on","meaning":"視乎……","examples":[{"en":"The number of screens varies depending on the type of visa.","zh":"頁面數目視乎簽證類別而不同。"},{"en":"Depending on means changing according to a particular factor.","zh":"視乎，指根據某個因素而改變。"},{"en":"Travel time may vary depending on traffic and weather.","zh":"交通時間可能視乎路面情況和天氣而不同。"},{"en":"If the visa type is more complex, the form may ask more questions.","zh":"如果簽證類別較複雜，表格可能詢問更多問題。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one thing is affected by another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一件事受另一件事影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as a rough estimate","meaning":"粗略估計","examples":[{"en":"As a rough estimate, each screen takes about four minutes.","zh":"粗略估計，每個頁面大約需時四分鐘。"},{"en":"As a rough estimate means the number is approximate, not exact.","zh":"粗略估計，指數字是約略的，而不是準確的。"},{"en":"As a rough estimate, a student may need two hours to finish a long essay draft.","zh":"粗略估計，學生可能需要兩小時完成長文初稿。"},{"en":"If the estimate is rough, applicants should leave extra time for mistakes or slow internet.","zh":"如果只是粗略估計，申請人應預留額外時間處理錯誤或網速慢的情況。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a practical but not precise calculation.","zh":"這個短語給出實用但不精確的計算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"allow yourself time to","meaning":"預留時間去……","examples":[{"en":"Allow yourself enough time to complete the application carefully.","zh":"請預留足夠時間仔細完成申請。"},{"en":"To allow yourself time to do something means to leave enough time for it instead of rushing.","zh":"預留時間做某事，指為它留下足夠時間，而不是匆忙處理。"},{"en":"Students should allow themselves time to check grammar before submitting essays.","zh":"學生在提交作文前應預留時間檢查文法。"},{"en":"If applicants rush, they may enter incorrect passport or payment details.","zh":"如果申請人太匆忙，可能輸入錯誤護照或付款資料。"},{"en":"The phrase gives advice to plan time responsibly.","zh":"這個短語建議負責任地安排時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fill in the information","meaning":"填寫資料","examples":[{"en":"Applicants should fill in the information on each screen.","zh":"申請人應在每個頁面填寫資料。"},{"en":"To fill in the information means to enter the required details in a form.","zh":"填寫資料，指在表格中輸入所需細節。"},{"en":"Parents fill in information about emergency contacts when enrolling a child at school.","zh":"家長為孩子入學時，會填寫緊急聯絡人資料。"},{"en":"If information is incomplete, the system may not let the applicant continue.","zh":"如果資料不完整，系統可能不讓申請人繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes entering form details.","zh":"這個短語描述輸入表格資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"on each screen","meaning":"在每個頁面上","examples":[{"en":"You should spend approximately four minutes on each screen.","zh":"你應在每個頁面上花大約四分鐘。"},{"en":"On each screen means on every page or section displayed in the online form.","zh":"在每個頁面上，指在網上表格顯示的每一頁或每一部分。"},{"en":"In an online quiz, students may answer one question on each screen.","zh":"在網上測驗中，學生可能在每個頁面上回答一條問題。"},{"en":"If applicants check each screen before moving on, errors are easier to catch.","zh":"如果申請人在繼續前檢查每個頁面，就更容易發現錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to every individual digital page.","zh":"這個短語指每一個獨立數碼頁面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"on this basis","meaning":"按此計算","examples":[{"en":"On this basis, the entire form should take no more than forty minutes.","zh":"按此計算，整份表格應不超過四十分鐘完成。"},{"en":"On this basis means using the information or calculation just mentioned.","zh":"按此計算，指根據剛才提到的資料或計算。"},{"en":"If each question takes two minutes, on this basis ten questions should take about twenty minutes.","zh":"如果每題需時兩分鐘，按此計算，十題應需約二十分鐘。"},{"en":"If the estimate is wrong, the final time may also be wrong.","zh":"如果估算錯誤，最終時間也可能錯。"},{"en":"The phrase links a conclusion to the reason before it.","zh":"這個短語把結論與前面的理由連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a maximum of","meaning":"最多……","examples":[{"en":"The application should take a maximum of about forty minutes.","zh":"申請最多應需約四十分鐘。"},{"en":"A maximum of something means no more than that amount or number.","zh":"最多某數量，指不超過該數量或數字。"},{"en":"Students may borrow a maximum of five library books at one time.","zh":"學生一次最多可借五本圖書館書籍。"},{"en":"If the process takes a maximum of forty minutes, most people should finish within that time.","zh":"如果流程最多需四十分鐘，大部分人應能在該時間內完成。"},{"en":"The phrase sets an upper limit.","zh":"這個短語設定上限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"complete the form","meaning":"填妥表格","examples":[{"en":"Most applicants can complete the form in under an hour.","zh":"大多數申請人可在一小時內填妥表格。"},{"en":"To complete the form means to fill in all required parts and finish it.","zh":"填妥表格，指填寫所有必需部分並完成它。"},{"en":"A parent may complete a school medical form before a field trip.","zh":"家長可能在實地考察前填妥學校醫療表格。"},{"en":"If the form is incomplete, the application may not be accepted.","zh":"如果表格未填完整，申請可能不被接受。"},{"en":"The phrase describes finishing all required sections of a form.","zh":"這個短語描述完成表格所有必需部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"personal details","meaning":"個人資料","examples":[{"en":"All applications require the applicant’s personal details.","zh":"所有申請都需要申請人的個人資料。"},{"en":"Personal details are basic information about a person, such as name, date of birth, address, and contact information.","zh":"個人資料，是關於一個人的基本資料，例如姓名、出生日期、地址和聯絡資料。"},{"en":"A school form may ask for a student’s personal details before enrolment.","zh":"學校表格可能在入學前要求學生提供個人資料。"},{"en":"If personal details are wrong, the record may not match official documents.","zh":"如果個人資料錯誤，記錄可能與官方文件不相符。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to identity-related information.","zh":"這個短語指與身份相關的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"namely","meaning":"即；也就是","examples":[{"en":"You must provide several details, namely your name and passport number.","zh":"你必須提供幾項資料，即你的姓名和護照號碼。"},{"en":"Namely means specifically or that is to say.","zh":"即，意思是具體來說或也就是。"},{"en":"Students need two things for the lesson, namely a notebook and a dictionary.","zh":"學生上課需要兩樣東西，即筆記簿和字典。"},{"en":"If a sentence uses “namely,” the words after it identify the exact examples.","zh":"如果句子使用 “namely”，其後詞語會指出確切例子。"},{"en":"The word introduces precise details.","zh":"這個詞引入精確細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"passport number","meaning":"護照號碼","examples":[{"en":"Enter your passport number exactly as it appears in your passport.","zh":"請按護照上的顯示準確輸入護照號碼。"},{"en":"A passport number is the unique identification number printed in a passport.","zh":"護照號碼，是印在護照上的獨特識別號碼。"},{"en":"Travellers often need their passport number when booking flights or applying for visas.","zh":"旅客預訂航班或申請簽證時，通常需要護照號碼。"},{"en":"If one digit is typed incorrectly, the application may not match the passport.","zh":"如果輸入錯一個數字，申請可能與護照不相符。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an official travel-document code.","zh":"這個短語指官方旅行證件代碼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"travel document details","meaning":"旅行證件資料","examples":[{"en":"The form asks for your travel document details.","zh":"表格要求提供你的旅行證件資料。"},{"en":"Travel document details are information from official documents used for international travel.","zh":"旅行證件資料，是來自用於國際旅行的官方文件的資料。"},{"en":"A passport number, expiry date, and issuing country are travel document details.","zh":"護照號碼、到期日和簽發國都是旅行證件資料。"},{"en":"If travel document details are inaccurate, immigration records may not match the traveller.","zh":"如果旅行證件資料不準確，入境記錄可能與旅客不相符。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to official travel identity information.","zh":"這個短語指官方旅行身份資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"current place of residence","meaning":"現居地","examples":[{"en":"Applicants must state their current place of residence.","zh":"申請人必須說明現居地。"},{"en":"Current place of residence means where a person is living now.","zh":"現居地，指一個人目前居住的地方。"},{"en":"A university form may ask for a student’s current place of residence during term time.","zh":"大學表格可能要求學生提供學期期間的現居地。"},{"en":"If someone has recently moved, they should enter their new address, not an old one.","zh":"如果某人最近搬家，應輸入新地址，而不是舊地址。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to present living location.","zh":"這個短語指目前居住地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"contact information","meaning":"聯絡資料","examples":[{"en":"Make sure your contact information is accurate and current.","zh":"請確保你的聯絡資料準確且最新。"},{"en":"Contact information is the phone number, email address, or postal address used to reach someone.","zh":"聯絡資料，是用來聯絡某人的電話號碼、電郵地址或郵寄地址。"},{"en":"A school keeps parents’ contact information in case of emergencies.","zh":"學校保存家長聯絡資料，以備緊急情況使用。"},{"en":"If contact information is wrong, important notices may not reach the applicant.","zh":"如果聯絡資料錯誤，重要通知可能無法送達申請人。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to details used for communication.","zh":"這個短語指用於溝通的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"declarations with respect to","meaning":"關於……的聲明","examples":[{"en":"The application includes declarations with respect to health and character.","zh":"申請包括關於健康及品格的聲明。"},{"en":"Declarations with respect to something are formal statements about that topic.","zh":"關於某事的聲明，是就該主題作出的正式陳述。"},{"en":"A job form may require declarations with respect to criminal history or professional qualifications.","zh":"工作表格可能要求關於犯罪紀錄或專業資格的聲明。"},{"en":"If an applicant gives a false declaration, the application may be refused.","zh":"如果申請人作出虛假聲明，申請可能被拒。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and common in official forms.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常見於官方表格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"health and character","meaning":"健康及品格","examples":[{"en":"Applicants must answer questions concerning their health and character.","zh":"申請人必須回答有關健康及品格的問題。"},{"en":"Health and character means a person’s medical condition and personal conduct or background.","zh":"健康及品格，指一個人的醫療狀況，以及個人行為或背景。"},{"en":"A visa form may ask health questions and character questions to assess risk.","zh":"簽證表格可能詢問健康問題和品格問題，以評估風險。"},{"en":"If an applicant has serious medical or legal issues, more information may be required.","zh":"如果申請人有嚴重醫療或法律問題，可能需要更多資料。"},{"en":"The phrase combines physical suitability with personal reliability.","zh":"這個短語結合身體適合性與個人可靠性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"business sponsor","meaning":"商業擔保人","examples":[{"en":"Business-visa applicants must provide details of their business sponsor.","zh":"商務簽證申請人必須提供商業擔保人的資料。"},{"en":"A business sponsor is a company or business organisation that supports a visa applicant.","zh":"商業擔保人，是支援簽證申請人的公司或商業機構。"},{"en":"An overseas manager may need a business sponsor before working in another country.","zh":"海外經理到另一國工作前，可能需要商業擔保人。"},{"en":"If the business sponsor cannot prove its role, the visa application may be questioned.","zh":"如果商業擔保人不能證明其角色，簽證申請可能受到質疑。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a commercial organisation acting as sponsor.","zh":"這個短語指作為擔保人的商業機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be asked for details of","meaning":"被要求提供……的詳細資料","examples":[{"en":"Some applicants will be asked for details of their sponsor.","zh":"一些申請人會被要求提供擔保人的詳細資料。"},{"en":"To be asked for details of something means to be required to provide specific information about it.","zh":"被要求提供某物的詳細資料，指被要求提供關於它的具體資料。"},{"en":"A school may ask parents for details of emergency contacts.","zh":"學校可能要求家長提供緊急聯絡人的詳細資料。"},{"en":"If the required details are missing, staff may contact the applicant again.","zh":"如果缺少所需細節，職員可能再次聯絡申請人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a request for specific information.","zh":"這個短語描述對具體資料的要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"outline your education history","meaning":"概述教育背景","examples":[{"en":"Student applicants should outline their education history.","zh":"學生申請人應概述教育背景。"},{"en":"To outline your education history means to give a brief summary of the schools, courses, or qualifications you have completed.","zh":"概述教育背景，指簡要說明你完成過的學校、課程或資格。"},{"en":"A job applicant may outline their education history on a CV.","zh":"求職者可能在履歷上概述教育背景。"},{"en":"If the outline is unclear, officers may not understand the applicant’s study background.","zh":"如果概述不清楚，官員可能不了解申請人的學習背景。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for a summary, not a long autobiography.","zh":"這個短語要求摘要，而不是長篇自傳。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"intended course of study","meaning":"擬修讀課程","examples":[{"en":"Students must provide details of their intended course of study.","zh":"學生必須提供擬修讀課程的詳細資料。"},{"en":"An intended course of study is the course or programme a student plans to take.","zh":"擬修讀課程，是學生計劃修讀的課程或項目。"},{"en":"A student applying to study nursing must state nursing as the intended course of study.","zh":"申請修讀護理的學生必須列明護理為擬修讀課程。"},{"en":"If the intended course is not clear, the visa office may ask for an offer letter.","zh":"如果擬修讀課程不清楚，簽證部門可能要求錄取信。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to planned education.","zh":"這個短語指計劃中的教育內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"travel plans","meaning":"旅遊計劃","examples":[{"en":"Tourist-visa applicants should outline their travel plans.","zh":"旅遊簽證申請人應概述旅遊計劃。"},{"en":"Travel plans are the details of where, when, and why someone intends to travel.","zh":"旅遊計劃，是關於某人打算到哪裡、何時和為何旅行的資料。"},{"en":"A family’s travel plans may include flights, hotels, tours, and dates.","zh":"一個家庭的旅遊計劃可能包括航班、酒店、行程和日期。"},{"en":"If travel plans are clear, visa officers can understand the purpose and length of the visit.","zh":"如果旅遊計劃清楚，簽證官就能理解到訪目的和逗留時間。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to planned travel arrangements.","zh":"這個短語指計劃中的旅行安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reason for visiting","meaning":"到訪原因","examples":[{"en":"The form asks tourists to state their reason for visiting Australia.","zh":"表格要求旅客說明到訪澳洲的原因。"},{"en":"A reason for visiting is the purpose behind a person’s trip.","zh":"到訪原因，是某人旅程背後的目的。"},{"en":"A traveller’s reason for visiting may be tourism, study, family, business, or medical treatment.","zh":"旅客的到訪原因可能是旅遊、學習、探親、商務或醫療。"},{"en":"If the reason is unclear, the application may require extra explanation.","zh":"如果原因不清楚，申請可能需要額外解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase asks why someone wants to enter a place.","zh":"這個短語詢問某人為何想入境某地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"employment status","meaning":"就業狀況","examples":[{"en":"Tourist applicants may be asked about their employment status.","zh":"旅遊簽證申請人可能被問及就業狀況。"},{"en":"Employment status means whether a person is employed, unemployed, self-employed, retired, or studying.","zh":"就業狀況，指一個人是否受僱、失業、自僱、退休或在學。"},{"en":"A bank form may ask for employment status before approving a credit card.","zh":"銀行表格可能在批准信用卡前詢問就業狀況。"},{"en":"If employment status is unclear, officers may ask for more evidence of the applicant’s situation.","zh":"如果就業狀況不清楚，官員可能要求更多證明申請人情況的資料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a person’s work situation.","zh":"這個短語描述一個人的工作情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"form part of","meaning":"構成……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Several short screens form part of the application form.","zh":"幾個簡短頁面構成申請表格的一部分。"},{"en":"To form part of something means to be included as one part of a larger whole.","zh":"構成某物的一部分，指被包含為較大整體中的一部分。"},{"en":"Group discussion may form part of a speaking exam.","zh":"小組討論可能構成口語考試的一部分。"},{"en":"If a screen forms part of the form, applicants must complete it before submission.","zh":"如果某頁面構成表格的一部分，申請人提交前必須完成它。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one element belongs to a bigger structure.","zh":"這個短語顯示某元素屬於更大結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as truly and honestly as possible","meaning":"盡可能如實及誠實地","examples":[{"en":"Answer all questions as truly and honestly as possible.","zh":"請盡可能如實及誠實地回答所有問題。"},{"en":"As truly and honestly as possible means with the greatest possible accuracy and honesty.","zh":"盡可能如實及誠實地，指以最大程度的準確和誠實回答。"},{"en":"Students should describe their own work as truly and honestly as possible in a reflection form.","zh":"學生在反思表中應盡可能如實及誠實地描述自己的工作。"},{"en":"If applicants hide important facts, the application may be refused or questioned later.","zh":"如果申請人隱瞞重要事實，申請日後可能被拒或受質疑。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses truthful answers.","zh":"這個短語強調真實作答。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be given the opportunity to","meaning":"獲得機會去……","examples":[{"en":"You will be given the opportunity to review your answers.","zh":"你將獲得機會覆核答案。"},{"en":"To be given the opportunity to do something means to be allowed or offered the chance to do it.","zh":"獲得機會做某事，指被允許或被提供機會去做它。"},{"en":"Students may be given the opportunity to correct mistakes after receiving feedback.","zh":"學生收到回饋後，可能獲得機會改正錯誤。"},{"en":"If applicants can review answers, they can fix errors before submission.","zh":"如果申請人可以覆核答案，就能在提交前修正錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being offered a chance.","zh":"這個短語描述得到一個機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"review the information","meaning":"覆核資料","examples":[{"en":"Applicants should review the information before submission.","zh":"申請人應在提交前覆核資料。"},{"en":"To review the information means to check it carefully again.","zh":"覆核資料，指再次仔細檢查資料。"},{"en":"Students should review information on an exam form before signing it.","zh":"學生簽署考試表格前，應覆核資料。"},{"en":"If applicants review their answers, they may find spelling or passport-number errors.","zh":"如果申請人覆核答案，可能會發現拼寫或護照號碼錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful checking before final action.","zh":"這個短語描述最終行動前的仔細檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"information you have supplied","meaning":"你所提供的資料","examples":[{"en":"Check that the information you have supplied is correct.","zh":"請檢查你所提供的資料是否正確。"},{"en":"Information you have supplied means the details you have entered or provided.","zh":"你所提供的資料，指你已輸入或提交的細節。"},{"en":"Before submitting a job application, check the information you have supplied about work experience.","zh":"提交求職申請前，請檢查你所提供的工作經驗資料。"},{"en":"If supplied information is false or outdated, the application may not be reliable.","zh":"如果所提供資料虛假或過時，申請可能不可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to data provided by the applicant.","zh":"這個短語指由申請人提供的數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"print a copy of","meaning":"列印一份……","examples":[{"en":"You may print a copy of the completed application.","zh":"你可以列印一份已完成的申請。"},{"en":"To print a copy of something means to produce a paper version of a digital document.","zh":"列印一份某文件，指製作該數碼文件的紙本版本。"},{"en":"A student may print a copy of an essay before giving it to a teacher.","zh":"學生可能列印一份作文交給老師。"},{"en":"If the website later becomes unavailable, a printed copy can still show what was submitted.","zh":"如果網站之後無法使用，紙本仍可顯示曾提交的內容。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a physical record.","zh":"這個短語描述製作實體記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for reference purposes","meaning":"供日後參考","examples":[{"en":"Keep a copy of the application for reference purposes.","zh":"請保留一份申請副本，供日後參考。"},{"en":"For reference purposes means for checking or looking back at later.","zh":"供日後參考，指日後用來查閱或回看。"},{"en":"Students may keep marked essays for reference purposes before the final exam.","zh":"學生可能保留已批改作文，供期末考前參考。"},{"en":"If an immigration officer asks a question later, a saved copy can help you answer accurately.","zh":"如果入境官日後提出問題，保存副本能幫助你準確回答。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why a record should be kept.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何應保存記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be ready to submit","meaning":"準備提交","examples":[{"en":"You are ready to submit the application after reviewing it.","zh":"覆核後，你就準備提交申請。"},{"en":"To be ready to submit means to have completed checking and be prepared to send the form officially.","zh":"準備提交，指已完成檢查，準備正式送出表格。"},{"en":"A student is ready to submit an essay after proofreading and saving the final version.","zh":"學生校對並保存最終版本後，就準備提交作文。"},{"en":"If you submit too early, mistakes may remain in the application.","zh":"如果你太早提交，申請中可能仍有錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the stage just before final submission.","zh":"這個短語標示最終提交前的階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"one more thing","meaning":"還有一件事","examples":[{"en":"There is one more thing to do before submission.","zh":"提交前還有一件事要做。"},{"en":"One more thing means one additional action or point remains.","zh":"還有一件事，指仍有一項額外行動或要點。"},{"en":"Before leaving the classroom, there is one more thing to do: return the library books.","zh":"離開課室前還有一件事要做：歸還圖書館書籍。"},{"en":"If one more step remains, the process is not finished yet.","zh":"如果還有一步未完成，流程就尚未結束。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an extra requirement.","zh":"這個短語引入額外要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"before the option appears","meaning":"在該選項出現前","examples":[{"en":"Payment must be made before the submit option appears.","zh":"在提交選項出現前，必須先付款。"},{"en":"Before the option appears means before that choice becomes visible or available on the screen.","zh":"在該選項出現前，指該選擇在螢幕上變得可見或可用之前。"},{"en":"In an online shop, delivery details may be needed before the payment option appears.","zh":"在網店中，可能需要先填送貨資料，付款選項才會出現。"},{"en":"If users have not completed a required step, the system may hide the next option.","zh":"如果使用者未完成必需步驟，系統可能隱藏下一個選項。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the order of online actions.","zh":"這個短語解釋網上操作次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make the payment","meaning":"付款","examples":[{"en":"You must make the payment before submitting the application.","zh":"提交申請前，你必須付款。"},{"en":"To make the payment means to pay the required amount of money.","zh":"付款，指繳付所需金額。"},{"en":"Parents make the payment for school trips through the online system.","zh":"家長透過網上系統支付學校旅行費用。"},{"en":"If the payment is not made, the application may remain unfinished.","zh":"如果沒有付款，申請可能仍未完成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes completing the money step.","zh":"這個短語描述完成金錢步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be prompted to enter","meaning":"系統會提示你輸入……","examples":[{"en":"You will be prompted to enter your payment information.","zh":"系統會提示你輸入付款資料。"},{"en":"To be prompted to enter something means the system will ask or guide you to type it in.","zh":"系統提示你輸入某物，指系統要求或引導你把它輸入。"},{"en":"A login page may prompt users to enter their email and password.","zh":"登入頁面可能提示使用者輸入電郵和密碼。"},{"en":"If the system prompts you for payment details, you should enter them carefully.","zh":"如果系統提示你輸入付款資料，你應小心填寫。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an instruction given by a digital system.","zh":"這個短語描述數碼系統給出的指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"payment information","meaning":"付款資料","examples":[{"en":"Enter your payment information carefully.","zh":"請小心輸入付款資料。"},{"en":"Payment information is the card or banking details needed to make a payment.","zh":"付款資料，是付款所需的信用卡或銀行資料。"},{"en":"Online shops ask for payment information before confirming an order.","zh":"網店在確認訂單前會要求付款資料。"},{"en":"If payment information is wrong, the bank may reject the transaction.","zh":"如果付款資料錯誤，銀行可能拒絕交易。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to financial details used for payment.","zh":"這個短語指用於付款的財務資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"confirm that","meaning":"確認……","examples":[{"en":"You must confirm that all entered details are accurate.","zh":"你必須確認所有輸入資料準確。"},{"en":"To confirm that something is true means to check and state that it is correct.","zh":"確認某事，指檢查並表明它正確。"},{"en":"Before a school trip, parents may confirm that emergency contact details are correct.","zh":"學校旅行前，家長可能確認緊急聯絡資料正確。"},{"en":"If applicants confirm false information, they may face problems later.","zh":"如果申請人確認虛假資料，日後可能遇到問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formal checking and agreement.","zh":"這個短語描述正式檢查和同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"details entered in the application","meaning":"申請表內所輸入的資料","examples":[{"en":"Review all details entered in the application.","zh":"請覆核申請表內所輸入的所有資料。"},{"en":"Details entered in the application are the pieces of information typed into the form.","zh":"申請表內所輸入的資料，是輸入表格中的各項資料。"},{"en":"These details may include name, passport number, address, course, and payment information.","zh":"這些資料可能包括姓名、護照號碼、地址、課程和付款資料。"},{"en":"If entered details do not match official documents, the application may be delayed.","zh":"如果輸入資料與官方文件不相符，申請可能延誤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to information already put into the form.","zh":"這個短語指已填入表格的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"to the best of your knowledge","meaning":"據你所知","examples":[{"en":"You must confirm that the information is true to the best of your knowledge.","zh":"你必須確認資料據你所知屬實。"},{"en":"To the best of your knowledge means as far as you honestly know.","zh":"據你所知，指就你誠實知道的範圍而言。"},{"en":"A witness may say the statement is accurate to the best of their knowledge.","zh":"證人可能說該陳述據其所知是準確的。"},{"en":"If applicants are unsure, they should check documents before confirming the information.","zh":"如果申請人不確定，確認資料前應先檢查文件。"},{"en":"The phrase allows honesty while recognising that people may not know everything.","zh":"這個短語承認人未必知道一切，同時要求誠實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"accept payment","meaning":"接受付款","examples":[{"en":"The application can proceed once the bank accepts payment.","zh":"銀行接受付款後，申請便可以繼續處理。"},{"en":"To accept payment means to approve and process the money transfer.","zh":"接受付款，指批准並處理金錢轉帳。"},{"en":"An online shop sends a receipt after the bank accepts payment.","zh":"網店在銀行接受付款後會發出收據。"},{"en":"If the bank does not accept payment, the application may not move forward.","zh":"如果銀行不接受付款，申請可能無法繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes successful payment approval.","zh":"這個短語描述付款成功獲批。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be automatically generated","meaning":"自動產生","examples":[{"en":"A reference number will be automatically generated.","zh":"參考編號將會自動產生。"},{"en":"If something is automatically generated, the computer system creates it without a person typing it manually.","zh":"如果某物自動產生，意思是電腦系統生成它，而不是人手輸入。"},{"en":"A school platform may automatically generate a receipt number after payment.","zh":"學校平台可能在付款後自動產生收據號碼。"},{"en":"If reference numbers are generated automatically, each application can receive a unique code.","zh":"如果參考編號自動產生，每份申請都可以收到獨特代碼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes computer-created information.","zh":"這個短語描述由電腦創建的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make a note of","meaning":"記下……","examples":[{"en":"Make a note of the reference number immediately.","zh":"請立即記下參考編號。"},{"en":"To make a note of something means to write it down or save it so you do not forget it.","zh":"記下某物，指把它寫下或保存，以免忘記。"},{"en":"Students should make a note of homework deadlines in their planners.","zh":"學生應在手冊中記下功課截止日期。"},{"en":"If you do not note the number, it may be difficult to ask about your application later.","zh":"如果你沒有記下編號，日後查詢申請可能會較困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recording important information.","zh":"這個短語描述記錄重要資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"keep something safe","meaning":"妥善保存……","examples":[{"en":"Keep the transaction reference number safe.","zh":"請妥善保存交易參考編號。"},{"en":"To keep something safe means to store or protect it so it is not lost or damaged.","zh":"妥善保存某物，指把它存放或保護好，避免遺失或損壞。"},{"en":"Travellers should keep their passports safe in a hotel safe or secure bag.","zh":"旅客應把護照妥善保存在酒店保險箱或安全袋中。"},{"en":"If you lose an important number, staff may take longer to locate your record.","zh":"如果你遺失重要編號，職員可能需要更長時間找到你的記錄。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful protection of something important.","zh":"這個短語描述小心保護重要物品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be quoted when making inquiries","meaning":"查詢時須引述……","examples":[{"en":"The reference number should be quoted when making inquiries.","zh":"查詢時須引述參考編號。"},{"en":"To be quoted when making inquiries means to be given or stated when asking for information.","zh":"查詢時引述某物，指在查詢資料時提供或說出它。"},{"en":"When calling a delivery company, customers may need to quote their order number.","zh":"致電速遞公司時，顧客可能需要引述訂單號碼。"},{"en":"If you quote the reference number, staff can find your application more quickly.","zh":"如果你引述參考編號，職員就能更快找到你的申請。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using a code during a query.","zh":"這個短語描述查詢時使用代碼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"inquiries related to","meaning":"與……相關的查詢","examples":[{"en":"Use the number for any inquiries related to your application.","zh":"請使用該編號作任何與你的申請相關的查詢。"},{"en":"Inquiries related to something are questions or requests for information about that thing.","zh":"與某事相關的查詢，是關於該事的問題或資料要求。"},{"en":"Parents may contact the school for inquiries related to uniforms or transport.","zh":"家長可能因與校服或交通相關的查詢聯絡學校。"},{"en":"If an inquiry is related to your application, the reference number helps identify your case.","zh":"如果查詢與你的申請相關，參考編號有助識別你的個案。"},{"en":"The phrase describes questions connected with a particular matter.","zh":"這個短語描述與特定事情相連的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in the future","meaning":"日後","examples":[{"en":"You may need the number when contacting immigration in the future.","zh":"日後聯絡入境部門時，你可能需要該編號。"},{"en":"In the future means at a later time, not now.","zh":"日後，指較後的時間，而不是現在。"},{"en":"Students may need their exam candidate number in the future when checking results.","zh":"學生日後查詢成績時，可能需要考生編號。"},{"en":"If you save the reference number now, future communication will be easier.","zh":"如果你現在保存參考編號，日後溝通會較容易。"},{"en":"The phrase points to later use or later events.","zh":"這個短語指向之後的用途或事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"once the application has been submitted","meaning":"申請提交後","examples":[{"en":"Further instructions may appear once the application has been submitted.","zh":"申請提交後，可能會出現進一步指示。"},{"en":"Once the application has been submitted means after the form has been officially sent.","zh":"申請提交後，指表格已被正式送出之後。"},{"en":"Once homework has been submitted, the platform may show a confirmation message.","zh":"功課提交後，平台可能顯示確認訊息。"},{"en":"If extra steps appear after submission, applicants should follow them carefully.","zh":"如果提交後出現額外步驟，申請人應仔細遵循。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the stage after official submission.","zh":"這個短語標示正式提交後的階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be prompted to download","meaning":"系統會提示下載……","examples":[{"en":"Some applicants may be prompted to download health forms.","zh":"一些申請人可能會被系統提示下載健康表格。"},{"en":"To be prompted to download something means the system asks or guides you to save a file from the internet.","zh":"系統提示下載某物，指系統要求或引導你從互聯網保存檔案。"},{"en":"A school website may prompt parents to download a consent form before a trip.","zh":"學校網站可能提示家長在旅行前下載同意書。"},{"en":"If the system prompts you to download a document, that document may be required later.","zh":"如果系統提示你下載文件，該文件日後可能需要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a digital instruction to save a file.","zh":"這個短語描述保存檔案的數碼指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"health forms","meaning":"健康申報表格","examples":[{"en":"Overseas applicants may need to complete certain health forms.","zh":"海外申請人可能需要填寫某些健康申報表格。"},{"en":"Health forms are documents asking for medical or health-related information.","zh":"健康申報表格，是詢問醫療或健康相關資料的文件。"},{"en":"A sports camp may require students to submit health forms before joining activities.","zh":"運動營可能要求學生在參加活動前提交健康申報表格。"},{"en":"If health forms are incomplete, medical checks or visa processing may be delayed.","zh":"如果健康表格不完整，醫療檢查或簽證處理可能延誤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to official forms about health conditions.","zh":"這個短語指關於健康狀況的官方表格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"apply from overseas","meaning":"從海外提出申請","examples":[{"en":"Additional health requirements may apply if you apply from overseas.","zh":"如果你從海外提出申請，可能適用額外健康要求。"},{"en":"To apply from overseas means to submit an application while you are outside the destination country.","zh":"從海外提出申請，指你在目的地國家以外提交申請。"},{"en":"A student in Hong Kong may apply from overseas for a course in Australia.","zh":"香港學生可能從海外申請澳洲課程。"},{"en":"If you apply from overseas, the office may require different documents or health checks.","zh":"如果你從海外申請，辦事處可能要求不同文件或健康檢查。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the applicant’s location when applying.","zh":"這個短語描述申請時申請人所在位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not be applicable to","meaning":"不適用於……","examples":[{"en":"The health-form requirement may not be applicable to applicants in Australia.","zh":"健康表格要求可能不適用於在澳洲境內的申請人。"},{"en":"If a rule is not applicable to someone, it does not apply to that person or situation.","zh":"如果某規則不適用於某人，意思是它不影響該人或情況。"},{"en":"A student discount may not be applicable to adults who are not studying.","zh":"學生折扣可能不適用於沒有讀書的成年人。"},{"en":"If a requirement is not applicable, applicants do not need to complete that step.","zh":"如果某要求不適用，申請人就不需要完成該步驟。"},{"en":"The phrase limits the use of a rule.","zh":"這個短語限制規則的適用範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"apply from inside Australia","meaning":"在澳洲境內提出申請","examples":[{"en":"Different requirements may apply to those who apply from inside Australia.","zh":"對在澳洲境內提出申請的人，可能適用不同要求。"},{"en":"To apply from inside Australia means to submit the application while physically in Australia.","zh":"在澳洲境內提出申請，指人在澳洲境內時提交申請。"},{"en":"A visitor already in Australia may apply from inside Australia if the visa rules allow it.","zh":"如果簽證規則容許，已在澳洲的訪客可能在澳洲境內提出申請。"},{"en":"If applicants are inside the country, the process may differ from overseas applications.","zh":"如果申請人在該國境內，流程可能與海外申請不同。"},{"en":"The phrase describes application location within Australia.","zh":"這個短語描述在澳洲境內申請。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"follow any other requirements","meaning":"遵從其他要求","examples":[{"en":"Applicants must follow any other requirements shown onscreen.","zh":"申請人必須遵從螢幕上顯示的其他要求。"},{"en":"To follow any other requirements means to obey all additional instructions that appear.","zh":"遵從其他要求，指遵守所有額外出現的指示。"},{"en":"A student must follow any other requirements on an exam paper, such as using a pencil.","zh":"學生必須遵從試卷上的其他要求，例如使用鉛筆。"},{"en":"If applicants ignore extra requirements, their application may remain incomplete.","zh":"如果申請人忽略額外要求，申請可能仍不完整。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds users to complete all additional steps.","zh":"這個短語提醒使用者完成所有額外步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as stipulated","meaning":"按照規定","examples":[{"en":"Complete all additional steps as stipulated on the screen.","zh":"請按照螢幕上的規定完成所有額外步驟。"},{"en":"As stipulated means exactly as stated or required in the instructions.","zh":"按照規定，指完全依照指示中所列明或要求的方式。"},{"en":"Students must submit the essay as stipulated in the assignment guidelines.","zh":"學生必須按照功課指引中的規定提交作文。"},{"en":"If applicants do not follow steps as stipulated, the system may not accept the application.","zh":"如果申請人不按照規定完成步驟，系統可能不接受申請。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and means “according to the stated rules.”","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是「根據所列明規則」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"special pre-entry conditions","meaning":"特別入境前條件","examples":[{"en":"Some visas have special pre-entry conditions.","zh":"有些簽證有特別入境前條件。"},{"en":"Special pre-entry conditions are extra rules that must be satisfied before entering a country.","zh":"特別入境前條件，是入境某國前必須符合的額外規則。"},{"en":"A school trip may have pre-entry conditions, such as submitting a health form before departure.","zh":"學校旅行可能有入場前條件，例如出發前提交健康表格。"},{"en":"If these conditions are not met, travellers may not be allowed to enter.","zh":"如果沒有符合這些條件，旅客可能不獲准入境。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to requirements before arrival.","zh":"這個短語指出抵達前的要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"conditions must be met","meaning":"必須符合條件","examples":[{"en":"All relevant conditions must be met before entry.","zh":"入境前必須符合所有相關條件。"},{"en":"If conditions must be met, the required rules have to be satisfied.","zh":"必須符合條件，指所要求的規則必須得到滿足。"},{"en":"A student may join a competition only after all age and registration conditions are met.","zh":"學生只有在年齡和註冊條件都符合後，才能參加比賽。"},{"en":"If visa conditions are not met, travel permission may not be valid.","zh":"如果簽證條件未符合，旅行許可可能無效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mandatory requirements.","zh":"這個短語描述強制要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be processed electronically","meaning":"以電子方式處理","examples":[{"en":"Most applications will be processed electronically.","zh":"大多數申請將以電子方式處理。"},{"en":"If an application is processed electronically, it is handled through computer systems rather than mainly on paper.","zh":"如果申請以電子方式處理，意思是透過電腦系統處理，而不是主要使用紙本。"},{"en":"A school admission form may be processed electronically after parents submit it online.","zh":"家長網上提交學校入學表格後，表格可能以電子方式處理。"},{"en":"Electronic processing can make records easier to store, check, and send.","zh":"電子處理能令記錄更容易儲存、檢查和傳送。"},{"en":"The phrase describes digital handling of applications.","zh":"這個短語描述以數碼方式處理申請。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"notification will be sent","meaning":"將會發出通知","examples":[{"en":"Notification will be sent after a decision has been made.","zh":"作出決定後，將會發出通知。"},{"en":"Notification will be sent means an official message will be delivered to the applicant.","zh":"將會發出通知，指官方訊息會被送給申請人。"},{"en":"A school may send notification when interview results are ready.","zh":"面試結果準備好時，學校可能發出通知。"},{"en":"If no notification arrives, applicants may need to check email, post, or the online account.","zh":"如果沒有收到通知，申請人可能需要檢查電郵、郵件或網上帳戶。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formal communication of a result or update.","zh":"這個短語描述正式傳達結果或更新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"by post or email","meaning":"以郵寄或電郵方式","examples":[{"en":"The result may be sent by post or email.","zh":"結果可能以郵寄或電郵方式送出。"},{"en":"By post or email means through physical mail or electronic mail.","zh":"以郵寄或電郵方式，指透過實體郵件或電子郵件。"},{"en":"A school may send admission results by post or email depending on family preference.","zh":"學校可能按家庭偏好，以郵寄或電郵方式發送錄取結果。"},{"en":"If applicants choose email, they should check the inbox and junk folder regularly.","zh":"如果申請人選擇電郵，就應定期檢查收件箱和垃圾郵件夾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes two possible communication methods.","zh":"這個短語描述兩種可能通訊方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"whichever method you selected","meaning":"以你所選擇的方式","examples":[{"en":"The result will be sent by whichever method you selected.","zh":"結果會以你所選擇的方式送出。"},{"en":"Whichever method you selected means the method that you chose, no matter which one it was.","zh":"以你所選擇的方式，指你選了哪一種方法，就用哪一種。"},{"en":"A school may contact parents by whichever method they selected on the form.","zh":"學校可能按家長在表格上所選擇的方式聯絡他們。"},{"en":"If you selected email, do not expect the result only by post.","zh":"如果你選擇電郵，就不要只期待郵寄結果。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to the applicant’s chosen option.","zh":"這個短語指回申請人選定的選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"within the time frame","meaning":"在指定時間範圍內","examples":[{"en":"The application should be finalised within the stated time frame.","zh":"申請應在指定時間範圍內完成審批。"},{"en":"Within the time frame means before the stated period ends.","zh":"在指定時間範圍內，指在所列明期間結束前。"},{"en":"Students must complete the project within the time frame given by the teacher.","zh":"學生必須在老師給出的時間範圍內完成項目。"},{"en":"If an application is not finalised within the expected time, applicants may contact the office.","zh":"如果申請未在預期時間內完成，申請人可能聯絡辦事處。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a time limit.","zh":"這個短語設定時間限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be outlined onscreen","meaning":"顯示於螢幕上","examples":[{"en":"The expected processing time is outlined onscreen.","zh":"預期處理時間會顯示於螢幕上。"},{"en":"If information is outlined onscreen, it is briefly shown or explained on the digital display.","zh":"如果資料顯示於螢幕上，意思是它在數碼畫面中被簡要展示或解釋。"},{"en":"Online exam rules may be outlined onscreen before students begin.","zh":"網上考試規則可能在學生開始前顯示於螢幕上。"},{"en":"If the processing time is shown onscreen, applicants can know roughly when to expect a result.","zh":"如果處理時間顯示在螢幕上，申請人就能大約知道何時期待結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes information displayed on a screen.","zh":"這個短語描述資料在螢幕上顯示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"working days","meaning":"工作天","examples":[{"en":"Student-visa applications may take about ten working days.","zh":"學生簽證申請可能需時約十個工作天。"},{"en":"Working days are days when offices normally operate, usually excluding weekends and public holidays.","zh":"工作天，是辦公室通常運作的日子，通常不包括週末和公眾假期。"},{"en":"A bank transfer may take three working days to appear in an account.","zh":"銀行轉帳可能需要三個工作天才顯示在帳戶中。"},{"en":"If an office says ten working days, two calendar weeks may not always be enough during holidays.","zh":"如果辦事處說十個工作天，在假期期間兩個日曆星期未必足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to business days, not all days.","zh":"這個短語指營業日，而不是所有日子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be finalised in less than","meaning":"在少於……內完成審批","examples":[{"en":"Tourist visas are normally finalised in less than two weeks.","zh":"旅遊簽證通常在少於兩星期內完成審批。"},{"en":"To be finalised in less than a period means to be completed before that amount of time has passed.","zh":"在少於某時間內完成，指在該時間過去之前完成。"},{"en":"A school transfer request may be finalised in less than five working days.","zh":"學校轉校申請可能在少於五個工作天內完成。"},{"en":"If an application is simple, it may be completed more quickly than a complex one.","zh":"如果申請簡單，可能比複雜申請更快完成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes completion within a shorter time limit.","zh":"這個短語描述在較短時間限制內完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take no more than","meaning":"所需時間不超過……","examples":[{"en":"Working-holiday visas normally take no more than two days.","zh":"工作假期簽證通常所需時間不超過兩天。"},{"en":"To take no more than a period means to require at most that amount of time.","zh":"所需時間不超過某段時間，指最多只需要該時間。"},{"en":"A short online quiz may take no more than ten minutes.","zh":"簡短網上測驗可能需時不超過十分鐘。"},{"en":"If a process takes no more than two days, applicants can expect a comparatively quick result.","zh":"如果流程所需時間不超過兩天，申請人可以期待相對快速的結果。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a maximum time needed.","zh":"這個短語設定所需時間上限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"occasionally","meaning":"偶爾","examples":[{"en":"Occasionally, the immigration department may request further information.","zh":"偶爾，入境部門可能要求進一步資料。"},{"en":"Occasionally means sometimes, but not often.","zh":"偶爾，指有時會發生，但不常發生。"},{"en":"A teacher may occasionally ask students to rewrite an essay if the first version is unclear.","zh":"如果第一稿不清楚，老師偶爾可能要求學生重寫作文。"},{"en":"If further information is occasionally requested, applicants should check messages after submission.","zh":"如果偶爾會要求補充資料，申請人提交後應檢查訊息。"},{"en":"The word describes something that happens from time to time.","zh":"這個詞描述不時發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"representative from the immigration department","meaning":"入境部門代表","examples":[{"en":"A representative from the immigration department may contact you.","zh":"入境部門代表可能會聯絡你。"},{"en":"A representative from the immigration department is an official person acting for the immigration office.","zh":"入境部門代表，是代表入境辦事處行事的官方人員。"},{"en":"A school representative may contact parents about an interview schedule.","zh":"學校代表可能聯絡家長安排面試時間。"},{"en":"If an immigration representative contacts you, you should respond using official channels.","zh":"如果入境部門代表聯絡你，你應透過官方渠道回覆。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an authorised person from the department.","zh":"這個短語指來自該部門的授權人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in some cases","meaning":"在某些情況下","examples":[{"en":"In some cases, applicants must attend an interview.","zh":"在某些情況下，申請人必須參加面試。"},{"en":"In some cases means in certain situations, but not all situations.","zh":"在某些情況下，指在特定情況中，但不是所有情況。"},{"en":"In some cases, students may need extra time because of illness or special needs.","zh":"在某些情況下，學生可能因疾病或特殊需要而需要額外時間。"},{"en":"If a case is unusual, the department may ask for an interview or more documents.","zh":"如果個案不尋常，部門可能要求面試或更多文件。"},{"en":"The phrase limits a statement to particular situations.","zh":"這個短語把陳述限制於特定情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"further health checks","meaning":"進一步健康檢查","examples":[{"en":"Further health checks may be required.","zh":"可能需要進一步健康檢查。"},{"en":"Further health checks are additional medical examinations or questions requested after the first stage.","zh":"進一步健康檢查，是第一階段後要求的額外醫療檢查或問題。"},{"en":"A school may ask for further health checks before a student joins a high-risk sport.","zh":"學生參加高風險運動前，學校可能要求進一步健康檢查。"},{"en":"If initial answers raise concerns, officials may request more medical evidence.","zh":"如果初步答案引起關注，官員可能要求更多醫療證明。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extra medical assessment.","zh":"這個短語描述額外醫療評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"formal interview","meaning":"正式面試","examples":[{"en":"Some applicants may be asked to attend a formal interview.","zh":"一些申請人可能被要求參加正式面試。"},{"en":"A formal interview is an official meeting where questions are asked for assessment.","zh":"正式面試，是為評估而提出問題的官方會面。"},{"en":"A scholarship applicant may attend a formal interview with a panel of teachers.","zh":"獎學金申請人可能與教師小組進行正式面試。"},{"en":"If an application needs clarification, an interview can help officers ask direct questions.","zh":"如果申請需要澄清，面試能讓官員直接提問。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an official questioning meeting.","zh":"這個短語指官方提問會面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"complete the flow chart","meaning":"完成流程圖","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the flow chart using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成流程圖。"},{"en":"To complete the flow chart means to fill missing steps or labels in a diagram showing a process.","zh":"完成流程圖，指在展示流程的圖表中填入缺少的步驟或標籤。"},{"en":"In a science lesson, students may complete a flow chart about how water is cleaned.","zh":"在科學課中，學生可能完成關於水如何被淨化的流程圖。"},{"en":"If the passage explains a process in order, a flow chart helps students follow the sequence.","zh":"如果文章按次序解釋流程，流程圖有助學生跟隨順序。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in reading-comprehension tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀理解題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"no more than three words and/or a number","meaning":"不超過三個字及／或一個數字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer may contain no more than three words and/or a number.","zh":"每個答案可包含不超過三個字及／或一個數字。"},{"en":"No more than three words and/or a number means the answer must stay within that word and number limit.","zh":"不超過三個字及／或一個數字，指答案必須留在該字數和數字限制內。"},{"en":"If the answer is “ten working days,” it fits because it has three words.","zh":"如果答案是 “ten working days”，它符合要求，因為有三個字。"},{"en":"If students write too many words, the answer may be marked wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"如果學生寫太多字，即使意思正確，也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict exam-answer limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格的考試答案限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"onscreen questionnaire","meaning":"螢幕上的問卷","examples":[{"en":"The onscreen questionnaire helps applicants select the correct visa.","zh":"螢幕上的問卷幫助申請人選擇正確簽證。"},{"en":"An onscreen questionnaire is a set of questions shown on a computer or phone screen.","zh":"螢幕上的問卷，是顯示在電腦或手機螢幕上的一組問題。"},{"en":"A health app may use an onscreen questionnaire to ask about symptoms.","zh":"健康應用程式可能使用螢幕上的問卷詢問症狀。"},{"en":"If applicants answer the questionnaire accurately, the system can guide them to the right visa type.","zh":"如果申請人準確回答問卷，系統就能引導他們選擇正確簽證類別。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a digital question form.","zh":"這個短語描述數碼問題表格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"confirm the correct type of visa","meaning":"確認正確簽證類別","examples":[{"en":"The questionnaire helps confirm the correct type of visa for your circumstances.","zh":"問卷幫助確認適合你情況的正確簽證類別。"},{"en":"To confirm the correct type of visa means to check which visa category matches your situation.","zh":"確認正確簽證類別，指檢查哪一種簽證符合你的情況。"},{"en":"A student should confirm the correct form before applying for a school subsidy.","zh":"學生申請學校資助前，應確認正確表格。"},{"en":"If the correct type is confirmed early, applicants avoid wasting time on the wrong application.","zh":"如果及早確認正確類別，申請人就能避免浪費時間在錯誤申請上。"},{"en":"The phrase describes verifying the right visa category.","zh":"這個短語描述核實正確簽證類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"not all types of visa","meaning":"並非所有簽證類別","examples":[{"en":"Not all types of visa can be applied for online.","zh":"並非所有簽證類別都可以網上申請。"},{"en":"Not all types of visa means some visa categories are included, but others are not.","zh":"並非所有簽證類別，指有些類別包括在內，但另一些不包括。"},{"en":"Not all school forms can be submitted online because some require original signatures.","zh":"並非所有學校表格都可以網上提交，因為有些需要原本簽名。"},{"en":"If not all visas are online, applicants must check the rules for their own category.","zh":"如果並非所有簽證都可網上辦理，申請人必須檢查自己類別的規則。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against assuming every type is the same.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要假設每種類別都一樣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"familiarise yourself with","meaning":"熟悉……","examples":[{"en":"Familiarise yourself with the conditions before accepting them.","zh":"接受條件前，請先熟悉它們。"},{"en":"To familiarise yourself with something means to learn about it until it feels clear and familiar.","zh":"熟悉某事，指學習了解它，直到它變得清楚而熟悉。"},{"en":"Students should familiarise themselves with the exam format before the test day.","zh":"學生在考試當日前應熟悉考試格式。"},{"en":"If applicants know the conditions well, they can avoid agreeing to rules they do not understand.","zh":"如果申請人熟悉條件，就能避免同意自己不了解的規則。"},{"en":"The phrase means to get to know something properly.","zh":"這個短語指好好了解某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tick a box","meaning":"勾選方格","examples":[{"en":"Tick the I Agree box to continue.","zh":"勾選「我同意」方格以繼續。"},{"en":"To tick a box means to mark a small square on a form to show a choice or agreement.","zh":"勾選方格，指在表格的小方格上作標記，以表示選擇或同意。"},{"en":"Students may tick a box to choose lunch, transport, or a club activity.","zh":"學生可能勾選方格來選擇午餐、交通或學會活動。"},{"en":"If the required box is not ticked, the system may not allow the next step.","zh":"如果必需方格未被勾選，系統可能不允許下一步。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a simple form action.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單的表格操作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"at most","meaning":"最多","examples":[{"en":"Allow approximately forty minutes at most to complete the form.","zh":"最多預留約四十分鐘填妥表格。"},{"en":"At most means no more than a stated amount.","zh":"最多，指不超過所列明的數量。"},{"en":"Students may borrow three books at most from a small classroom library.","zh":"學生最多可從小型課室圖書館借三本書。"},{"en":"If a task takes forty minutes at most, it may often take less.","zh":"如果任務最多需四十分鐘，實際上可能少於此時間。"},{"en":"The phrase sets an upper limit.","zh":"這個短語設定上限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"answer all questions truthfully","meaning":"如實回答所有問題","examples":[{"en":"Applicants should answer all questions truthfully.","zh":"申請人應如實回答所有問題。"},{"en":"To answer all questions truthfully means to give honest and accurate answers to every question.","zh":"如實回答所有問題，指對每條問題都給出誠實而準確的答案。"},{"en":"Students should answer scholarship questions truthfully, even if the answer seems less impressive.","zh":"學生應如實回答獎學金問題，即使答案看起來不那麼突出。"},{"en":"If applicants give false answers, their application may be refused or investigated.","zh":"如果申請人提供虛假答案，申請可能被拒或被調查。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses honesty in every response.","zh":"這個短語強調每個回答都要誠實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"review the details entered","meaning":"覆核已輸入的資料","examples":[{"en":"Review the details entered before making payment.","zh":"付款前，請覆核已輸入的資料。"},{"en":"To review the details entered means to check the information already typed into the form.","zh":"覆核已輸入的資料，指檢查已輸入表格中的資料。"},{"en":"Before submitting an online order, customers should review the address and phone number entered.","zh":"提交網上訂單前，顧客應覆核已輸入的地址和電話號碼。"},{"en":"If details are reviewed before payment, errors can be corrected in time.","zh":"如果在付款前覆核資料，錯誤就能及時更正。"},{"en":"The phrase describes checking typed information before the next step.","zh":"這個短語描述下一步前檢查已輸入資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"for your reference","meaning":"供你參考","examples":[{"en":"You may print a copy for your reference.","zh":"你可以列印一份副本供你參考。"},{"en":"For your reference means for you to look at later when you need to check information.","zh":"供你參考，指供你日後需要查資料時查看。"},{"en":"A teacher may send students a sample answer for their reference.","zh":"老師可能把範文發給學生供他們參考。"},{"en":"If you keep a copy, you can check what you submitted if questions arise later.","zh":"如果你保留副本，日後出現問題時就能查看自己提交了甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase explains that something is kept for later checking.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物被保留作日後查閱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"wait to be prompted","meaning":"等候系統提示","examples":[{"en":"Wait to be prompted before entering your payment information.","zh":"輸入付款資料前，請等候系統提示。"},{"en":"To wait to be prompted means to wait until the system asks you to do the next action.","zh":"等候系統提示，指等到系統要求你做下一個動作。"},{"en":"In an online exam, students should wait to be prompted before starting the recording.","zh":"在網上考試中，學生應等候系統提示後才開始錄音。"},{"en":"If users type payment details too early or in the wrong place, the payment may not work.","zh":"如果使用者太早或在錯誤位置輸入付款資料，付款可能無法成功。"},{"en":"The phrase tells users not to act before the system instructs them.","zh":"這個短語告訴使用者不要在系統指示前行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"record your reference number","meaning":"記錄參考編號","examples":[{"en":"Record your reference number after payment is accepted.","zh":"付款獲接受後，請記錄參考編號。"},{"en":"To record your reference number means to write it down, save it, or take a screenshot of it.","zh":"記錄參考編號，指把它寫下、保存或截圖。"},{"en":"After submitting a school form, parents should record the confirmation number.","zh":"提交學校表格後，家長應記錄確認編號。"},{"en":"If you record the number immediately, you can use it for future inquiries.","zh":"如果你立即記錄該編號，就能用於日後查詢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes saving an important code.","zh":"這個短語描述保存重要代碼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"payment request","meaning":"付款要求","examples":[{"en":"The bank must accept the payment request.","zh":"銀行必須接受付款要求。"},{"en":"A payment request is a request sent to a bank or payment system to approve a payment.","zh":"付款要求，是發送給銀行或付款系統以批准付款的要求。"},{"en":"When a customer buys something online, the website sends a payment request to the bank.","zh":"顧客網上購物時，網站會向銀行發送付款要求。"},{"en":"If the payment request is rejected, the purchase or application may not continue.","zh":"如果付款要求被拒，購買或申請可能無法繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the digital request for payment approval.","zh":"這個短語指數碼付款批准要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the application has gone through","meaning":"申請已成功提交","examples":[{"en":"A confirmation screen shows that the application has gone through.","zh":"確認畫面顯示申請已成功提交。"},{"en":"If an application has gone through, it has been successfully submitted or processed by the system.","zh":"如果申請已成功提交，意思是系統已成功收到或處理它。"},{"en":"After paying for a course online, students may see a message showing the registration has gone through.","zh":"網上繳付課程費用後，學生可能看到訊息顯示註冊已成功提交。"},{"en":"If no confirmation appears, applicants should not assume the application has been submitted.","zh":"如果沒有出現確認訊息，申請人不應假設申請已提交。"},{"en":"The phrase describes successful completion of an online step.","zh":"這個短語描述網上步驟成功完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be expected to have","meaning":"應備有……","examples":[{"en":"All applicants are expected to have a valid passport and credit card.","zh":"所有申請人應備有有效護照和信用卡。"},{"en":"To be expected to have something means people are assumed or required to possess it.","zh":"應備有某物，指人們被假定或要求持有它。"},{"en":"Students are expected to have a notebook and pen for every lesson.","zh":"學生每堂課應備有筆記簿和筆。"},{"en":"If applicants do not have the required items, they may not be able to complete the process.","zh":"如果申請人沒有必需物品，可能無法完成流程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a basic requirement or assumption.","zh":"這個短語描述基本要求或假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"globally recognised credit card","meaning":"全球通用信用卡","examples":[{"en":"A globally recognised credit card is required for payment.","zh":"付款需要全球通用信用卡。"},{"en":"A globally recognised credit card is a card accepted by payment systems in many countries.","zh":"全球通用信用卡，是被許多國家的付款系統接受的信用卡。"},{"en":"Travellers may use a globally recognised credit card to book flights and hotels abroad.","zh":"旅客可能使用全球通用信用卡預訂海外航班和酒店。"},{"en":"If a card is not globally recognised, the online payment system may reject it.","zh":"如果信用卡不是全球通用，網上付款系統可能拒絕它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a credit card accepted internationally.","zh":"這個短語指國際接受的信用卡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have six months’ validity left","meaning":"尚有六個月有效期","examples":[{"en":"The passport must have at least six months’ validity left.","zh":"護照必須尚有至少六個月有效期。"},{"en":"To have six months’ validity left means the document will remain valid for six more months.","zh":"尚有六個月有效期，指文件仍會再有效六個月。"},{"en":"A passport issued years ago may not have enough validity left for international travel.","zh":"多年前簽發的護照可能沒有足夠剩餘有效期作國際旅行。"},{"en":"If the passport expires soon, the applicant may need to renew it before applying.","zh":"如果護照快將到期，申請人可能需要先續領再申請。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the remaining valid period.","zh":"這個短語強調剩餘有效期間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"once an application has been submitted","meaning":"申請提交後","examples":[{"en":"Once an application has been submitted, it is normally processed electronically.","zh":"申請提交後，通常會以電子方式處理。"},{"en":"Once an application has been submitted means after the applicant has officially sent it.","zh":"申請提交後，指申請人已正式送出申請之後。"},{"en":"Once a school form has been submitted, parents may receive an automatic email confirmation.","zh":"學校表格提交後，家長可能收到自動電郵確認。"},{"en":"After submission, applicants usually cannot treat the form as a draft anymore.","zh":"提交後，申請人通常不能再把表格視為草稿。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the stage after formal submission.","zh":"這個短語標示正式提交後的階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be approved or rejected","meaning":"獲批或被拒","examples":[{"en":"Applicants will later be informed whether the visa is approved or rejected.","zh":"申請人稍後會獲通知簽證是獲批或被拒。"},{"en":"To be approved or rejected means to receive either a positive decision or a refusal.","zh":"獲批或被拒，指收到正面決定或拒絕。"},{"en":"A scholarship application may be approved or rejected after a committee reviews it.","zh":"獎學金申請在委員會審核後，可能獲批或被拒。"},{"en":"If a visa is rejected, the applicant may need to check the reasons before reapplying.","zh":"如果簽證被拒，申請人可能需要先檢查原因再重新申請。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the two possible decision outcomes.","zh":"這個短語描述兩種可能決定結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"outside Australia","meaning":"澳洲境外","examples":[{"en":"Applicants outside Australia may receive additional health forms.","zh":"澳洲境外的申請人可能收到額外健康表格。"},{"en":"Outside Australia means not physically located in Australia.","zh":"澳洲境外，指身體不在澳洲境內。"},{"en":"A student outside Australia may need to complete extra steps before travelling.","zh":"澳洲境外的學生可能需要在出發前完成額外步驟。"},{"en":"If applicants are outside the country, communication may happen mainly by email or post.","zh":"如果申請人在境外，溝通可能主要透過電郵或郵寄進行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the applicant’s location beyond Australian territory.","zh":"這個短語描述申請人位於澳洲領土以外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"handle an application electronically","meaning":"以電子方式處理申請","examples":[{"en":"Most submitted applications are handled electronically.","zh":"大多數已提交申請都以電子方式處理。"},{"en":"To handle an application electronically means to process it using computer systems.","zh":"以電子方式處理申請，指使用電腦系統處理它。"},{"en":"A school may handle enrolment forms electronically after parents submit them online.","zh":"家長網上提交入學表格後，學校可能以電子方式處理。"},{"en":"Electronic handling can make it easier to store records and send updates.","zh":"電子處理能更容易儲存記錄和發送更新。"},{"en":"The phrase describes digital processing of applications.","zh":"這個短語描述申請的數碼處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be told whether or not","meaning":"獲告知是否……","examples":[{"en":"Applicants will be told whether or not their application was successful.","zh":"申請人會獲告知其申請是否成功。"},{"en":"To be told whether or not something happened means to be informed if it did or did not happen.","zh":"獲告知某事是否發生，指被通知它有沒有發生。"},{"en":"Students will be told whether or not they passed the interview by email.","zh":"學生會透過電郵獲告知是否通過面試。"},{"en":"If applicants are not told clearly, they may not know whether they can travel.","zh":"如果申請人沒有獲清楚告知，就可能不知道自己能否出行。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a yes-or-no result.","zh":"這個短語引入是或否的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"timeframe stated onscreen","meaning":"螢幕上列明的時間範圍","examples":[{"en":"The decision should arrive within the timeframe stated onscreen.","zh":"決定應在螢幕上列明的時間範圍內到達。"},{"en":"The timeframe stated onscreen is the processing period shown on the website or digital form.","zh":"螢幕上列明的時間範圍，是網站或數碼表格上顯示的處理期間。"},{"en":"An online booking system may show the delivery timeframe onscreen before payment.","zh":"網上預訂系統可能在付款前於螢幕上顯示送貨時間範圍。"},{"en":"If the result does not arrive within that timeframe, applicants may need to make an inquiry.","zh":"如果結果未在該時間範圍內到達，申請人可能需要查詢。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the visible time estimate on the screen.","zh":"這個短語指螢幕上可見的時間估算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"take under two weeks","meaning":"處理時間少於兩星期","examples":[{"en":"Several common visa types normally take under two weeks to process.","zh":"幾種常見簽證類別通常處理時間少於兩星期。"},{"en":"To take under two weeks means to require less than fourteen days.","zh":"處理時間少於兩星期，指需時少於十四天。"},{"en":"A simple school application may take under two weeks if all documents are ready.","zh":"如果文件齊備，簡單學校申請可能處理時間少於兩星期。"},{"en":"If processing takes under two weeks, applicants may receive the result fairly quickly.","zh":"如果處理少於兩星期，申請人可能相當快收到結果。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a short processing-time estimate.","zh":"這個短語給出較短處理時間估算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"undertake a formal interview","meaning":"接受正式面試","examples":[{"en":"Only some applicants may be required to undertake a formal interview.","zh":"只有部分申請人可能被要求接受正式面試。"},{"en":"To undertake a formal interview means to attend and complete an official interview.","zh":"接受正式面試，指出席並完成官方面試。"},{"en":"A scholarship candidate may undertake a formal interview before the final decision.","zh":"獎學金候選人可能在最終決定前接受正式面試。"},{"en":"If officers need to clarify answers, they may require an interview.","zh":"如果官員需要澄清答案，可能要求面試。"},{"en":"The phrase describes taking part in an official assessment meeting.","zh":"這個短語描述參與官方評估會面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"conduct health checks","meaning":"進行健康檢查","examples":[{"en":"Immigration officials may conduct health checks on certain applicants.","zh":"入境官員可能對某些申請人進行健康檢查。"},{"en":"To conduct health checks means to carry out medical examinations or reviews.","zh":"進行健康檢查，指進行醫療檢查或審查。"},{"en":"A school nurse may conduct health checks before students join a sports camp.","zh":"學生參加運動營前，學校護士可能進行健康檢查。"},{"en":"If health checks reveal a concern, extra medical documents may be required.","zh":"如果健康檢查顯示有問題，可能需要額外醫療文件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised medical assessment.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的醫療評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"hold an interview with","meaning":"與……進行面試","examples":[{"en":"An immigration representative may hold an interview with an applicant.","zh":"入境部門代表可能與申請人進行面試。"},{"en":"To hold an interview with someone means to meet them formally and ask questions.","zh":"與某人進行面試，指正式與他會面並提問。"},{"en":"A school principal may hold an interview with parents before admitting a student.","zh":"校長可能在錄取學生前與家長進行面試。"},{"en":"If an officer holds an interview, the applicant should answer clearly and honestly.","zh":"如果官員進行面試，申請人應清楚且誠實回答。"},{"en":"The phrase describes arranging and conducting a formal interview.","zh":"這個短語描述安排並進行正式面試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"comparatively fast confirmation","meaning":"相對快速的結果通知","examples":[{"en":"Working-holiday applicants can expect comparatively fast confirmation.","zh":"工作假期申請人可以期待相對快速的結果通知。"},{"en":"Comparatively fast confirmation means a result or response that arrives faster than many other cases.","zh":"相對快速的結果通知，指比許多其他個案更快到達的結果或回覆。"},{"en":"Online library registration may give comparatively fast confirmation if identity checks are simple.","zh":"如果身份檢查簡單，網上圖書館註冊可能給出相對快速的確認。"},{"en":"If a visa type is processed quickly, applicants can plan travel sooner.","zh":"如果某簽證類別處理快速，申請人就能更早計劃旅行。"},{"en":"The phrase compares speed with other application types.","zh":"這個短語把速度與其他申請類別比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"application has been successful","meaning":"申請獲批","examples":[{"en":"Applicants are notified when their application has been successful.","zh":"申請獲批時，申請人會收到通知。"},{"en":"If an application has been successful, it has been approved or accepted.","zh":"如果申請獲批，意思是它已被批准或接受。"},{"en":"A student may receive an email saying their scholarship application has been successful.","zh":"學生可能收到電郵，表示其獎學金申請獲批。"},{"en":"If the application is successful, the applicant can usually move to the next stage.","zh":"如果申請成功，申請人通常可以進入下一階段。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a positive application result.","zh":"這個短語描述正面的申請結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a limited amount of time","meaning":"有限時間","examples":[{"en":"Some immigration procedures must be completed within a limited amount of time.","zh":"有些移民程序必須在有限時間內完成。"},{"en":"A limited amount of time means a fixed or short period available to do something.","zh":"有限時間，指可用來做某事的固定或短暫期間。"},{"en":"Students have a limited amount of time to finish an exam paper.","zh":"學生有有限時間完成試卷。"},{"en":"If a deadline is missed, the applicant may have to restart the process.","zh":"如果錯過截止日期，申請人可能需要重新開始流程。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses time pressure.","zh":"這個短語強調時間壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"within which to","meaning":"須在該期間內……","examples":[{"en":"The notice may specify a period within which to complete the next step.","zh":"通知可能列明一段期間，申請人須在該期間內完成下一步。"},{"en":"Within which to means inside the period of time allowed for doing something.","zh":"須在該期間內，指在獲准做某事的時間範圍內。"},{"en":"A school may give students seven days within which to submit missing documents.","zh":"學校可能給學生七天，須在該期間內提交欠交文件。"},{"en":"If applicants do not act within that period, their application may be delayed or closed.","zh":"如果申請人未在該期間內行動，申請可能延誤或被關閉。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and links a time limit to an action.","zh":"這個短語較正式，把時間限制與行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"finalise travel plans","meaning":"落實旅遊安排","examples":[{"en":"Travellers should finalise their travel plans only after receiving the visa result.","zh":"旅客應只在收到簽證結果後才落實旅遊安排。"},{"en":"To finalise travel plans means to make final decisions about flights, accommodation, dates, and arrangements.","zh":"落實旅遊安排，指對航班、住宿、日期和安排作出最終決定。"},{"en":"A family may finalise travel plans after confirming school holidays and hotel prices.","zh":"家庭可能在確認學校假期和酒店價格後落實旅遊安排。"},{"en":"If travellers book everything before the visa result, they may lose money if the visa is refused.","zh":"如果旅客在簽證結果前預訂所有東西，而簽證被拒，可能會損失金錢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making travel arrangements definite.","zh":"這個短語描述把旅行安排確定下來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 7 - The Australian Visa Application Process Explained.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 8":[{"front":"team building","meaning":"團隊建立","examples":[{"en":"Effective team building can strengthen relationships within an organisation.","zh":"有效的團隊建立可以加強機構內部的關係。"},{"en":"Team building means activities or processes that help people work better together.","zh":"團隊建立指幫助人們更好合作的活動或過程。"},{"en":"A school may use team building games to help new classmates trust one another.","zh":"學校可能使用團隊建立遊戲，幫助新同學互相信任。"},{"en":"If team building is done well, employees communicate more clearly and solve problems faster.","zh":"如果團隊建立做得好，員工會更清楚溝通並更快解決問題。"},{"en":"Team building is not just entertainment; it should improve cooperation in real work.","zh":"團隊建立不只是娛樂；它應改善真實工作中的合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"particularly in times of","meaning":"尤其在……的時候","examples":[{"en":"Efficiency becomes particularly important in times of economic difficulty.","zh":"效率尤其在經濟困難時期變得重要。"},{"en":"Particularly in times of means especially during periods when a certain situation is happening.","zh":"Particularly in times of 指尤其在某種情況出現的時期。"},{"en":"Clear communication is important, particularly in times of exam pressure.","zh":"清晰溝通很重要，尤其在考試壓力大的時候。"},{"en":"If money is tight, careful planning becomes particularly important in times of uncertainty.","zh":"如果資金緊張，在不明朗時期，仔細規劃就尤其重要。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights when something matters more than usual.","zh":"這個片語突出某事在某些時候比平常更重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"economic downturn","meaning":"經濟衰退","examples":[{"en":"Companies often reduce spending during an economic downturn.","zh":"公司在經濟衰退期間常會削減開支。"},{"en":"An economic downturn is a period when business activity, income, and confidence become weaker.","zh":"經濟衰退是商業活動、收入和信心變弱的一段時期。"},{"en":"During an economic downturn, families may spend less on restaurants and holidays.","zh":"在經濟衰退期間，家庭可能減少在餐廳和旅行上的開支。"},{"en":"If sales fall during an economic downturn, companies may delay hiring new staff.","zh":"如果銷售在經濟衰退期間下降，公司可能延遲聘請新員工。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a difficult period for the economy, not just one poor month.","zh":"這個片語描述經濟困難時期，而不只是某一個月表現差。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be of supreme importance","meaning":"極為重要","examples":[{"en":"Efficiency is of supreme importance during difficult economic periods.","zh":"在經濟困難時期，效率極為重要。"},{"en":"To be of supreme importance means to be extremely important.","zh":"To be of supreme importance 指極其重要。"},{"en":"Safety is of supreme importance when students are taken on a hiking trip.","zh":"當學生被帶去遠足時，安全極為重要。"},{"en":"If a hospital is short of staff, clear priorities are of supreme importance.","zh":"如果醫院人手不足，清晰的優先次序就極為重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than “important” and stresses absolute necessity.","zh":"這個片語比 important 更強，強調絕對必要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"across all industries","meaning":"在所有行業","examples":[{"en":"Efficiency is important across all industries.","zh":"效率在所有行業都很重要。"},{"en":"Across all industries means in every type of business or work sector.","zh":"Across all industries 指在每一種商業或工作範疇中。"},{"en":"Digital skills are useful across all industries, from banking to education.","zh":"數碼技能在所有行業都有用，從銀行到教育都是如此。"},{"en":"If costs rise everywhere, companies across all industries may review their spending.","zh":"如果各方面成本上升，所有行業的公司都可能重新檢視開支。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a point applies widely, not only to one field.","zh":"這個片語顯示某一點適用範圍很廣，不只限於一個領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"look to cut costs","meaning":"設法削減成本","examples":[{"en":"Many companies look to cut costs during an economic downturn.","zh":"許多公司在經濟衰退期間設法削減成本。"},{"en":"To look to cut costs means to try to find ways to spend less money.","zh":"To look to cut costs 指嘗試尋找減少開支的方法。"},{"en":"A school may look to cut costs by using less paper and sharing online materials.","zh":"學校可能透過少用紙張和分享網上教材來設法削減成本。"},{"en":"If profits fall, managers may look to cut costs before hiring more staff.","zh":"如果利潤下降，管理層可能先設法削減成本，再考慮聘請更多員工。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a planned attempt to reduce spending.","zh":"這個片語描述有計劃地嘗試減少開支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"invest in staff motivation","meaning":"投資於員工激勵","examples":[{"en":"Some organisations continue to invest in staff motivation.","zh":"一些機構繼續投資於員工激勵。"},{"en":"To invest in staff motivation means to spend time, money, or effort helping employees feel more willing to work well.","zh":"To invest in staff motivation 指投入時間、金錢或努力，幫助員工更願意做好工作。"},{"en":"A company may invest in staff motivation through training, recognition, and career support.","zh":"公司可能透過培訓、認可和事業支援來投資於員工激勵。"},{"en":"If workers feel valued, investment in motivation may reduce turnover.","zh":"如果員工感到被重視，對激勵的投資可能減少流失率。"},{"en":"This phrase treats employee energy and morale as something worth developing.","zh":"這個片語把員工能量和士氣視為值得發展的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"training and development programmes","meaning":"培訓和發展計劃","examples":[{"en":"Training and development programmes can improve staff performance.","zh":"培訓和發展計劃可以改善員工表現。"},{"en":"Training and development programmes are organised activities that help employees learn skills and grow professionally.","zh":"培訓和發展計劃是幫助員工學習技能和專業成長的有組織活動。"},{"en":"A school may offer training and development programmes for new teachers.","zh":"學校可能為新老師提供培訓和發展計劃。"},{"en":"If staff learn better communication skills, customer service may improve.","zh":"如果員工學到更好的溝通技巧，顧客服務可能改善。"},{"en":"These programmes should connect learning with real workplace needs.","zh":"這些計劃應把學習與真實工作需要連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"develop an understanding of","meaning":"加深對……的理解","examples":[{"en":"Managers need to develop an understanding of effective teamwork.","zh":"管理者需要加深對有效團隊合作的理解。"},{"en":"To develop an understanding of something means to gradually learn what it means and how it works.","zh":"To develop an understanding of something 指逐漸學懂某事的意思和運作方式。"},{"en":"Students develop an understanding of grammar by seeing many clear examples.","zh":"學生透過看許多清晰例子，加深對文法的理解。"},{"en":"If managers understand teamwork better, they can choose more useful training activities.","zh":"如果管理者更理解團隊合作，他們就能選擇更有用的培訓活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning deeply, not just hearing about a topic once.","zh":"這個片語描述深入學習，而不只是聽過一次某個題目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"internal relationships","meaning":"內部關係","examples":[{"en":"Strong internal relationships can improve organisational performance.","zh":"強大的內部關係可以改善機構表現。"},{"en":"Internal relationships are the working relationships among people inside the same organisation.","zh":"內部關係指同一機構內人與人之間的工作關係。"},{"en":"A school with strong internal relationships may have teachers who share materials willingly.","zh":"一間內部關係良好的學校，老師可能願意分享教材。"},{"en":"If internal relationships are weak, departments may hide information from one another.","zh":"如果內部關係薄弱，部門之間可能互相隱瞞資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on relationships inside the organisation, not with customers.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於機構內部的關係，而不是與顧客的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be crucial for success","meaning":"對成功至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Good communication is crucial for business success.","zh":"良好溝通對商業成功至關重要。"},{"en":"To be crucial for success means to be necessary for achieving a good result.","zh":"To be crucial for success 指對取得好結果而言是必要的。"},{"en":"Regular practice is crucial for success in learning a musical instrument.","zh":"定期練習對學習樂器成功至關重要。"},{"en":"If a team lacks trust, success becomes much harder to achieve.","zh":"如果團隊缺乏信任，成功就會變得更難達成。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies something that a goal strongly depends on.","zh":"這個片語指出某目標高度依賴的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one of the barriers","meaning":"其中一個障礙","examples":[{"en":"A lack of clarity is one of the barriers to successful team building.","zh":"缺乏清晰理解是成功團隊建立的其中一個障礙。"},{"en":"One of the barriers means one of the problems that prevents progress.","zh":"One of the barriers 指阻礙進展的其中一個問題。"},{"en":"Poor time management is one of the barriers to good exam preparation.","zh":"欠佳時間管理是良好備試的其中一個障礙。"},{"en":"If a barrier is not removed, even a good plan may fail.","zh":"如果障礙沒有被移除，即使計劃很好也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces one obstacle among several possible obstacles.","zh":"這個片語引出多個可能障礙中的其中一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"come across time and time again","meaning":"一次又一次遇到","examples":[{"en":"Louise Edwards comes across the same misunderstanding time and time again.","zh":"Louise Edwards 一次又一次遇到同一種誤解。"},{"en":"To come across something time and time again means to meet or notice it repeatedly.","zh":"To come across something time and time again 指反覆遇到或注意到某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may come across the same grammar mistake time and time again in students’ essays.","zh":"老師可能在學生作文中一次又一次遇到同一個文法錯誤。"},{"en":"If managers repeatedly misunderstand team building, training may not solve the real problem.","zh":"如果管理者反覆誤解團隊建立，培訓可能無法解決真正問題。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that something happens again and again.","zh":"這個片語強調某事一再發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"corporate heads","meaning":"企業高層","examples":[{"en":"Corporate heads often recognise the importance of team building.","zh":"企業高層常意識到團隊建立的重要性。"},{"en":"Corporate heads are senior leaders or executives in a company.","zh":"Corporate heads 是公司的高級領袖或行政人員。"},{"en":"Corporate heads may decide whether a company should invest in staff training.","zh":"企業高層可能決定公司是否應投資於員工培訓。"},{"en":"If corporate heads support a programme, employees may take it more seriously.","zh":"如果企業高層支持某計劃，員工可能更認真看待它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people at the top of a business organisation.","zh":"這個片語指商業機構最高層的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"seem to understand that","meaning":"似乎明白","examples":[{"en":"Managers seem to understand that strong teams are important.","zh":"管理者似乎明白強大團隊很重要。"},{"en":"Seem to understand that means appear to know or accept something, though their actions may not fully show it.","zh":"Seem to understand that 指看起來知道或接受某事，雖然行動未必完全顯示出來。"},{"en":"Students may seem to understand that revision matters, but still leave it too late.","zh":"學生可能似乎明白溫習重要，但仍然太遲才開始。"},{"en":"If managers understand the idea but not the method, they may still make poor decisions.","zh":"如果管理者明白概念但不懂方法，他們仍可能作出差的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest partial or surface-level understanding.","zh":"這個片語可以暗示部分或表面層次的理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not quite sure","meaning":"不太肯定","examples":[{"en":"Some managers are not quite sure how to build an effective team.","zh":"一些管理者不太肯定如何建立有效團隊。"},{"en":"Not quite sure means uncertain or not fully confident.","zh":"Not quite sure 指不確定或沒有完全信心。"},{"en":"A student may be not quite sure which paragraph contains the answer.","zh":"學生可能不太肯定哪一段包含答案。"},{"en":"If managers are not quite sure what a team means, they may choose unsuitable training.","zh":"如果管理者不太肯定團隊是甚麼意思，他們可能選擇不合適的培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase softens uncertainty without sounding completely lost.","zh":"這個片語以較溫和方式表達不確定，而不是完全不知道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in terms of","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"In terms of a sports club, the meaning of a team is obvious.","zh":"就體育會而言，團隊的意思很明顯。"},{"en":"In terms of means when considering a particular aspect, area, or example.","zh":"In terms of 指從某一方面、範疇或例子來看。"},{"en":"In terms of price, this phone is cheaper than the newer model.","zh":"就價格而言，這部電話比新型號便宜。"},{"en":"If we discuss teamwork in terms of sport, roles and goals are easier to see.","zh":"如果我們從體育角度討論團隊合作，角色和目標會更容易看見。"},{"en":"This phrase tells readers the angle from which something is being considered.","zh":"這個片語告訴讀者某事正從哪個角度被考慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sports club","meaning":"體育會","examples":[{"en":"A team is usually easy to identify within a sports club.","zh":"在體育會中，團隊通常容易辨認。"},{"en":"A sports club is an organisation where people train, play, or compete in sport.","zh":"體育會是人們訓練、玩運動或參加比賽的組織。"},{"en":"A local sports club may have football, tennis, and swimming teams.","zh":"本地體育會可能有足球、網球和游泳隊。"},{"en":"If a sports club has clear teams, members know who they train and compete with.","zh":"如果體育會有清晰團隊，成員會知道自己與誰訓練和比賽。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a simple example of a setting where teams are visible.","zh":"這個片語提供一個團隊容易看見的簡單場景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be easy to identify","meaning":"容易辨認","examples":[{"en":"The members of a sports team are easy to identify.","zh":"運動隊成員容易辨認。"},{"en":"To be easy to identify means to be simple to recognise or point out.","zh":"To be easy to identify 指容易認出或指出。"},{"en":"In a school uniform, students from the same school are easy to identify.","zh":"穿着校服時，同一間學校的學生容易辨認。"},{"en":"If a team has clear roles and a shared goal, its members are easier to identify.","zh":"如果團隊有清晰角色和共同目標，其成員就更容易辨認。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that is not confusing to recognise.","zh":"這個片語描述某事不難認出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"In contrast, workplace teams may be harder to define.","zh":"相比之下，工作場所中的團隊可能較難界定。"},{"en":"In contrast introduces a clear difference from what has just been mentioned.","zh":"In contrast 用來引出與剛提到內容清楚不同的情況。"},{"en":"Some students enjoy group work; in contrast, others prefer studying alone.","zh":"有些學生喜歡小組工作；相比之下，另一些學生較喜歡獨自學習。"},{"en":"If sports teams are obvious but workplace teams are unclear, the writer uses contrast to show the difference.","zh":"如果運動隊很明顯，但工作團隊不清晰，作者會用對比顯示差異。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare two different situations.","zh":"這個片語幫助比較兩種不同情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"within a company","meaning":"在公司內","examples":[{"en":"The meaning of a team may be unclear within a large company.","zh":"在大型公司內，團隊的意思可能不清晰。"},{"en":"Within a company means inside the organisation or business itself.","zh":"Within a company 指在機構或企業內部。"},{"en":"Within a company, different departments may have different ways of working.","zh":"在公司內，不同部門可能有不同工作方式。"},{"en":"If communication fails within a company, customers may receive inconsistent service.","zh":"如果公司內部溝通失敗，顧客可能收到不一致的服務。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what happens inside the business.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於企業內部發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"multi-layered organisation","meaning":"多層架構的機構","examples":[{"en":"Teams can be difficult to define in a multi-layered organisation.","zh":"在多層架構的機構中，團隊可能難以界定。"},{"en":"A multi-layered organisation has many levels of management, departments, and reporting lines.","zh":"多層架構的機構有許多管理層級、部門和匯報線。"},{"en":"A large hospital is a multi-layered organisation because doctors, nurses, administrators, and managers all work in different structures.","zh":"大型醫院是多層架構的機構，因為醫生、護士、行政人員和管理層都在不同結構中工作。"},{"en":"If an organisation has many layers, employees may not know which team they truly belong to.","zh":"如果機構有很多層級，員工可能不知道自己真正屬於哪個團隊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a complex organisation with several levels.","zh":"這個片語描述有多個層級的複雜機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"become more confused","meaning":"變得更混亂","examples":[{"en":"Definitions may become more confused as an organisation grows.","zh":"隨着機構成長，定義可能變得更混亂。"},{"en":"To become more confused means to become less clear and harder to understand.","zh":"To become more confused 指變得較不清晰和較難理解。"},{"en":"A class discussion can become more confused if everyone speaks at the same time.","zh":"如果人人同時發言，課堂討論可能變得更混亂。"},{"en":"If a company grows quickly without clear structures, team roles may become more confused.","zh":"如果公司快速擴張但沒有清晰結構，團隊角色可能變得更混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing uncertainty or lack of clarity.","zh":"這個片語描述不確定或不清晰程度增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"report to the same boss","meaning":"向同一位上司匯報","examples":[{"en":"Some people define a team as employees who report to the same boss.","zh":"有些人把團隊定義為向同一位上司匯報的員工。"},{"en":"To report to the same boss means to have the same manager or supervisor.","zh":"To report to the same boss 指擁有同一位經理或主管。"},{"en":"In a school office, several clerks may report to the same administrator.","zh":"在學校辦公室，幾名文員可能向同一位行政人員匯報。"},{"en":"If people report to the same boss but do unrelated work, they may not truly function as a team.","zh":"如果人們向同一位上司匯報但工作毫不相關，他們未必真正作為團隊運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a management relationship, not necessarily a shared goal.","zh":"這個片語描述管理關係，而不一定是共同目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a business team","meaning":"商業團隊","examples":[{"en":"A business team should work towards a shared objective.","zh":"商業團隊應朝着共同目標努力。"},{"en":"A business team is a group of people in a company who cooperate to achieve a work goal.","zh":"商業團隊是公司中合作達成工作目標的一群人。"},{"en":"A marketing team may plan an advertising campaign for a new product.","zh":"市場推廣團隊可能為新產品策劃廣告活動。"},{"en":"If a business team lacks direction, members may duplicate work or miss deadlines.","zh":"如果商業團隊缺乏方向，成員可能重複工作或錯過期限。"},{"en":"This phrase describes teamwork in a workplace rather than in sport.","zh":"這個片語描述工作場所中的團隊合作，而不是體育中的團隊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a group of people","meaning":"一群人","examples":[{"en":"A team is a group of people working towards a common goal.","zh":"團隊是一群朝着共同目標努力的人。"},{"en":"A group of people means several people considered together.","zh":"A group of people 指被視為一起的幾個人。"},{"en":"A group of people waiting at a bus stop is not necessarily a team.","zh":"一群在巴士站等車的人不一定是團隊。"},{"en":"If a group of people shares a task and helps one another, it may become a team.","zh":"如果一群人共享任務並互相幫助，它可能變成團隊。"},{"en":"This phrase is broad, so context decides whether the group is organised or casual.","zh":"這個片語很廣泛，所以語境決定這群人是有組織還是隨意聚集。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"work towards a common goal","meaning":"朝着共同目標努力","examples":[{"en":"Successful teams work towards a common goal.","zh":"成功團隊朝着共同目標努力。"},{"en":"To work towards a common goal means to make efforts together to achieve the same result.","zh":"To work towards a common goal 指共同努力以達到同一結果。"},{"en":"Students in a project group work towards a common goal when they prepare one presentation together.","zh":"專題小組學生一起準備一個匯報時，就是朝着共同目標努力。"},{"en":"If team members have different goals, cooperation becomes difficult.","zh":"如果團隊成員有不同目標，合作就會變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to defining a real team.","zh":"這個片語是界定真正團隊的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be more productive to","meaning":"……會更有效","examples":[{"en":"It is more productive to define a team by its shared goal.","zh":"以共同目標來界定團隊會更有效。"},{"en":"It is more productive to do something means that doing it gives better results.","zh":"It is more productive to do something 指做某事能帶來更好結果。"},{"en":"It is more productive to revise weak topics first than to reread what you already know.","zh":"先溫習弱項比重讀已懂內容會更有效。"},{"en":"If a definition helps people act clearly, it is more productive than a vague one.","zh":"如果某個定義幫助人清楚行動，它就比含糊定義更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase compares methods and chooses the one that works better.","zh":"這個片語比較方法，並選出較有效的一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in training terms","meaning":"從培訓角度而言","examples":[{"en":"In training terms, a team may include people from several departments.","zh":"從培訓角度而言，團隊可能包括來自幾個部門的人。"},{"en":"In training terms means from the point of view of staff training or learning design.","zh":"In training terms 指從員工培訓或學習設計角度來看。"},{"en":"In training terms, a mistake can be useful if it shows what skill needs practice.","zh":"從培訓角度而言，如果錯誤顯示需要練習哪項技能，它可以是有用的。"},{"en":"If training focuses on shared goals, department boundaries may matter less.","zh":"如果培訓聚焦於共同目標，部門界線可能較不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase frames a situation through the language of training.","zh":"這個片語透過培訓語境來框定情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"roles and responsibilities","meaning":"職能和責任","examples":[{"en":"Team members may have similar roles and responsibilities.","zh":"團隊成員可能有相似職能和責任。"},{"en":"Roles and responsibilities are the duties people are expected to perform.","zh":"Roles and responsibilities 是人們被期望履行的職責。"},{"en":"In a school project, one student may research while another designs the slides.","zh":"在學校專題中，一名學生可能負責研究，另一名負責設計簡報。"},{"en":"If roles and responsibilities are unclear, important tasks may be missed.","zh":"如果職能和責任不清晰，重要任務可能被遺漏。"},{"en":"This phrase explains who does what in a team.","zh":"這個片語解釋團隊中誰負責做甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sales team","meaning":"銷售團隊","examples":[{"en":"A sales team shares the common goal of increasing sales.","zh":"銷售團隊有增加銷售的共同目標。"},{"en":"A sales team is a group of employees responsible for selling products or services.","zh":"銷售團隊是負責銷售產品或服務的一組員工。"},{"en":"A sales team may call customers, prepare quotations, and follow up on orders.","zh":"銷售團隊可能致電顧客、準備報價並跟進訂單。"},{"en":"If the sales team understands customers well, revenue may increase.","zh":"如果銷售團隊很了解顧客，收入可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a team with a clear commercial purpose.","zh":"這個片語描述具有清晰商業目的的團隊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"common goal of","meaning":"……的共同目標","examples":[{"en":"The sales team has the common goal of selling the company’s products.","zh":"銷售團隊有銷售公司產品的共同目標。"},{"en":"A common goal of a group is the aim that all members share.","zh":"A common goal of a group 指所有成員共同擁有的目標。"},{"en":"A class may have the common goal of improving its English speaking confidence.","zh":"一個班級可能有提升英語口語信心的共同目標。"},{"en":"If everyone accepts the common goal, daily decisions become easier.","zh":"如果人人接受共同目標，日常決策會更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the shared purpose behind group effort.","zh":"這個片語解釋群體努力背後的共同目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the organisation as a whole","meaning":"整個機構","examples":[{"en":"Team-building activities can benefit the organisation as a whole.","zh":"團隊建立活動可以令整個機構受益。"},{"en":"The organisation as a whole means the entire organisation, not just one person or department.","zh":"The organisation as a whole 指整個機構，而不只是某個人或部門。"},{"en":"A new filing system may help the school as a whole if all offices use it.","zh":"如果所有辦公室都使用新存檔系統，它可能幫助整間學校。"},{"en":"If departments cooperate better, the organisation as a whole becomes more efficient.","zh":"如果部門之間合作更好，整個機構會變得更有效率。"},{"en":"This phrase widens the focus from individual parts to the complete organisation.","zh":"這個片語把焦點從個別部分擴展至整個機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"continued success","meaning":"持續成功","examples":[{"en":"Employees with different skills contribute to the organisation’s continued success.","zh":"擁有不同技能的員工為機構的持續成功作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Continued success means success that lasts over time rather than happening once.","zh":"Continued success 指隨時間維持的成功，而不是一次性的成功。"},{"en":"A school’s continued success depends on good teaching and strong student support.","zh":"學校的持續成功取決於良好教學和強大學生支援。"},{"en":"If a company stops improving, its continued success may be at risk.","zh":"如果公司停止改進，其持續成功可能面臨風險。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on long-term achievement.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於長期成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"contribute to","meaning":"為……作出貢獻","examples":[{"en":"Every department contributes to the company’s success.","zh":"每個部門都為公司的成功作出貢獻。"},{"en":"To contribute to something means to help cause or support it.","zh":"To contribute to something 指幫助造成或支持某事。"},{"en":"Regular sleep contributes to better concentration in class.","zh":"定期睡眠有助提升課堂專注力。"},{"en":"If everyone completes their part, each person contributes to the final result.","zh":"如果每個人完成自己的部分，每個人都為最終結果作出貢獻。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor helps produce a wider outcome.","zh":"這個片語顯示某因素幫助產生更大的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in a number of ways","meaning":"以多種方式","examples":[{"en":"Different employees contribute to the organisation in a number of ways.","zh":"不同員工以多種方式為機構作出貢獻。"},{"en":"In a number of ways means in several different ways.","zh":"In a number of ways 指以幾種不同方式。"},{"en":"Parents support children’s learning in a number of ways, such as reading with them and checking homework.","zh":"家長以多種方式支持孩子學習，例如陪讀和檢查功課。"},{"en":"If staff have different talents, they can help the company in many different ways.","zh":"如果員工有不同才能，他們可以以多種方式幫助公司。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that there is more than one method or form of contribution.","zh":"這個片語表示方法或貢獻形式不只一種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"believe it inevitable that","meaning":"認為……是無可避免的","examples":[{"en":"Brenda Durham believes it inevitable that some workplace conflict will occur.","zh":"Brenda Durham 認為某些工作場所衝突是無可避免的。"},{"en":"To believe it inevitable that something will happen means to think it cannot be avoided.","zh":"To believe it inevitable that something will happen 指認為某事不能避免。"},{"en":"A teacher may believe it inevitable that students will make mistakes when learning a new skill.","zh":"老師可能認為學生學新技能時犯錯是無可避免的。"},{"en":"If people with different habits work together, some disagreement may be unavoidable.","zh":"如果習慣不同的人一起工作，某些分歧可能無法避免。"},{"en":"This phrase presents a future event as almost certain.","zh":"這個片語把未來事件呈現為幾乎必然。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"to some extent","meaning":"在某程度上","examples":[{"en":"Conflict will exist to some extent in most workplaces.","zh":"在大多數工作場所，衝突在某程度上會存在。"},{"en":"To some extent means partly, but not completely.","zh":"To some extent 指部分如此，但不是完全如此。"},{"en":"Exam results reflect effort to some extent, but sleep and stress also matter.","zh":"考試成績在某程度上反映努力，但睡眠和壓力也重要。"},{"en":"If conflict exists only to some extent, it may be manageable.","zh":"如果衝突只在某程度上存在，它可能是可管理的。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a statement more balanced and less absolute.","zh":"這個片語令陳述更平衡，較不絕對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"successful workplace","meaning":"成功的工作場所","examples":[{"en":"A successful workplace still experiences occasional disagreement.","zh":"成功的工作場所仍會間中出現分歧。"},{"en":"A successful workplace is a working environment where people can perform well and cooperate effectively.","zh":"Successful workplace 是人們能表現良好並有效合作的工作環境。"},{"en":"A successful workplace gives employees clear goals, fair treatment, and useful support.","zh":"成功的工作場所給員工清晰目標、公平待遇和有用支援。"},{"en":"If a workplace handles conflict well, disagreement does not have to damage success.","zh":"如果工作場所妥善處理衝突，分歧不一定會破壞成功。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a workplace that functions well, not one without problems.","zh":"這個片語描述運作良好的工作場所，而不是完全沒有問題的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"diversity of skills","meaning":"技能多樣性","examples":[{"en":"A team needs a diversity of skills to perform effectively.","zh":"團隊需要技能多樣性才能有效表現。"},{"en":"Diversity of skills means a range of different abilities within a group.","zh":"Diversity of skills 指團體內擁有一系列不同能力。"},{"en":"A school project team may need writing, design, research, and presentation skills.","zh":"學校專題小組可能需要寫作、設計、研究和匯報技能。"},{"en":"If everyone has the same skill, the team may struggle with unfamiliar tasks.","zh":"如果每個人都有同一種技能，團隊面對陌生任務時可能吃力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that difference can make a team stronger.","zh":"這個片語顯示差異可以令團隊更強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"diversity of personalities","meaning":"性格多樣性","examples":[{"en":"A diversity of personalities may strengthen a team.","zh":"性格多樣性可能強化一個團隊。"},{"en":"Diversity of personalities means having people with different character types and ways of behaving.","zh":"Diversity of personalities 指擁有不同性格類型和行為方式的人。"},{"en":"A quiet planner and an energetic speaker can both help a project group.","zh":"安靜的規劃者和充滿活力的演說者都可以幫助專題小組。"},{"en":"If personalities differ too much without respect, conflict may increase.","zh":"如果性格差異太大而缺乏尊重，衝突可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that personality differences can be useful when managed well.","zh":"這個片語顯示性格差異在管理得好時可以有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be required for success","meaning":"成功所需要的","examples":[{"en":"Different skills and personalities are required for success.","zh":"不同技能和性格是成功所需要的。"},{"en":"To be required for success means to be needed in order to achieve a good result.","zh":"To be required for success 指為取得好結果而需要某事。"},{"en":"Patience and regular practice are required for success in learning a language.","zh":"耐性和定期練習是學習語言成功所需要的。"},{"en":"If a task is complex, several different abilities may be required for success.","zh":"如果任務複雜，成功可能需要幾種不同能力。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what a successful outcome depends on.","zh":"這個片語指出成功結果依賴甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"unavoidably lead to","meaning":"無可避免地導致","examples":[{"en":"Personality differences may unavoidably lead to misunderstandings.","zh":"性格差異可能無可避免地導致誤解。"},{"en":"To unavoidably lead to something means to cause it in a way that is difficult or impossible to prevent.","zh":"To unavoidably lead to something 指以難以或無法避免的方式造成某事。"},{"en":"If instructions are unclear, confusion may unavoidably lead to mistakes.","zh":"如果指示不清晰，混亂可能無可避免地導致錯誤。"},{"en":"When people communicate very differently, some misunderstanding may be hard to avoid.","zh":"當人們溝通方式非常不同，某些誤解可能難以避免。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with a likely negative result.","zh":"這個片語把原因與可能的負面結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"misunderstandings and disharmony","meaning":"誤解和不和","examples":[{"en":"Poor communication can cause misunderstandings and disharmony.","zh":"欠佳溝通可以造成誤解和不和。"},{"en":"Misunderstandings and disharmony are confusion and poor relationships within a group.","zh":"Misunderstandings and disharmony 指團體中的混亂理解和不良關係。"},{"en":"A class project may suffer misunderstandings and disharmony if tasks are not clearly divided.","zh":"如果任務沒有清楚分工，班級專題可能出現誤解和不和。"},{"en":"If people assume bad intentions, small errors can become larger conflicts.","zh":"如果人們假設對方有惡意，小錯誤可以變成較大衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both mental confusion and social tension.","zh":"這個片語同時描述理解上的混亂和社交上的緊張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"from time to time","meaning":"間中；不時","examples":[{"en":"Even successful teams experience conflict from time to time.","zh":"即使成功團隊也會間中經歷衝突。"},{"en":"From time to time means occasionally, not constantly.","zh":"From time to time 指偶爾，而不是經常。"},{"en":"Students may feel tired from time to time during a long exam period.","zh":"在漫長考試期間，學生可能不時感到疲倦。"},{"en":"If disagreement happens only from time to time, it may be normal and manageable.","zh":"如果分歧只是間中發生，它可能是正常且可管理的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that happens sometimes.","zh":"這個片語描述某事有時發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cohesive unit","meaning":"團結一致的團隊","examples":[{"en":"Good training can help develop a cohesive unit.","zh":"良好培訓可以幫助建立團結一致的團隊。"},{"en":"A cohesive unit is a group whose members work together closely and effectively.","zh":"Cohesive unit 是成員緊密而有效合作的團體。"},{"en":"A class becomes a cohesive unit when students help one another rather than compete cruelly.","zh":"當學生互相幫助而不是惡性競爭時，班級會成為團結一致的團隊。"},{"en":"If a team becomes more cohesive, communication and trust usually improve.","zh":"如果團隊變得更團結，溝通和信任通常會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a group that feels united rather than scattered.","zh":"這個片語描述感覺團結而不是分散的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"minimise friction","meaning":"將摩擦減至最低","examples":[{"en":"A cohesive team can minimise friction between employees.","zh":"團結的團隊可以將員工之間的摩擦減至最低。"},{"en":"To minimise friction means to reduce tension, disagreement, or conflict as much as possible.","zh":"To minimise friction 指盡量減少緊張、分歧或衝突。"},{"en":"Clear classroom rules can minimise friction between students during group work.","zh":"清晰課室規則可以在小組工作中將學生之間的摩擦減至最低。"},{"en":"If roles are clear, people argue less about who should do each task.","zh":"如果角色清晰，人們較少爭論誰應做哪項任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing unnecessary conflict.","zh":"這個片語描述減少不必要衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be developed in","meaning":"可在……中建立","examples":[{"en":"A cooperative team can be developed in any committed organisation.","zh":"合作團隊可在任何投入的機構中建立。"},{"en":"To be developed in a place means to be created or strengthened there over time.","zh":"To be developed in a place 指在某地方隨時間被建立或加強。"},{"en":"Good study habits can be developed in a supportive classroom.","zh":"良好學習習慣可在有支援的課室中建立。"},{"en":"If leaders give time and support, trust can be developed in a workplace.","zh":"如果領袖給予時間和支援，信任可以在工作場所中建立。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a quality can grow inside a particular environment.","zh":"這個片語顯示某種品質可以在特定環境中成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be committed to","meaning":"致力於……","examples":[{"en":"The company is committed to investing in its employees.","zh":"公司致力於投資員工。"},{"en":"To be committed to something means to be seriously dedicated to it.","zh":"To be committed to something 指認真投入某事。"},{"en":"A student committed to improvement attends lessons and practises regularly.","zh":"致力於進步的學生會上課並定期練習。"},{"en":"If a company is committed to staff development, it will not cancel training at the first difficulty.","zh":"如果公司致力於員工發展，它不會一遇到困難就取消培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes real dedication shown through action.","zh":"這個片語描述透過行動顯示的真正投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"invest in one’s people","meaning":"投資於員工","examples":[{"en":"Successful organisations are willing to invest in their people.","zh":"成功機構願意投資於員工。"},{"en":"To invest in one’s people means to support employees through training, development, and care.","zh":"To invest in one’s people 指透過培訓、發展和關懷支援員工。"},{"en":"A restaurant invests in its people when it trains waiters instead of replacing them quickly.","zh":"餐廳培訓侍應而不是快速換人，就是投資於員工。"},{"en":"If employees gain skills, the organisation may benefit for years.","zh":"如果員工獲得技能，機構可能多年受益。"},{"en":"This phrase treats workers as long-term assets, not just costs.","zh":"這個片語把員工視為長期資產，而不只是成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take on external expertise","meaning":"聘用外部專業服務","examples":[{"en":"Some organisations take on external expertise for staff training.","zh":"一些機構聘用外部專業服務進行員工培訓。"},{"en":"To take on external expertise means to bring in outside specialists or advisers.","zh":"To take on external expertise 指引入外部專家或顧問。"},{"en":"A school may take on external expertise to train teachers in special education.","zh":"學校可能聘用外部專業服務，培訓老師處理特殊教育。"},{"en":"If a company lacks knowledge internally, outside experts can fill the gap.","zh":"如果公司內部缺乏知識，外部專家可以填補缺口。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using help from outside the organisation.","zh":"這個片語描述使用機構外部的協助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"external expertise","meaning":"外部專業知識","examples":[{"en":"External expertise can provide specialist training and advice.","zh":"外部專業知識可以提供專門培訓和建議。"},{"en":"External expertise is knowledge or skill brought in from outside an organisation.","zh":"External expertise 是從機構外部引入的知識或技能。"},{"en":"A clinic may use external expertise when installing a new computer system.","zh":"診所在安裝新電腦系統時，可能使用外部專業知識。"},{"en":"If internal staff lack experience, external expertise can prevent costly mistakes.","zh":"如果內部員工缺乏經驗，外部專業知識可以防止代價高昂的錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to outside professional knowledge.","zh":"這個片語指外部專業知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"staff training programmes","meaning":"員工培訓計劃","examples":[{"en":"Staff training programmes can be costly to organise.","zh":"員工培訓計劃可能成本高昂。"},{"en":"Staff training programmes are planned courses or activities that teach employees useful skills.","zh":"Staff training programmes 是教員工實用技能的有計劃課程或活動。"},{"en":"A hotel may run staff training programmes on customer service and safety.","zh":"酒店可能舉辦關於顧客服務和安全的員工培訓計劃。"},{"en":"If training is practical, employees may perform better with guests or clients.","zh":"如果培訓實用，員工面對客人或客戶時可能表現更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised learning for workers.","zh":"這個片語描述為員工而設的有組織學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"team-building programmes","meaning":"團隊建立計劃","examples":[{"en":"Team-building programmes should reflect the organisation’s needs.","zh":"團隊建立計劃應反映機構需要。"},{"en":"Team-building programmes are planned activities designed to improve teamwork.","zh":"Team-building programmes 是旨在改善團隊合作的有計劃活動。"},{"en":"A company may use a team-building programme to help new departments work together.","zh":"公司可能使用團隊建立計劃，幫助新部門一起工作。"},{"en":"If the programme ignores real workplace problems, staff may see it as a waste of time.","zh":"如果計劃忽視真實工作問題，員工可能視它為浪費時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes structured efforts to strengthen teams.","zh":"這個片語描述有結構地強化團隊的努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be costly","meaning":"成本高昂","examples":[{"en":"External training programmes can be costly.","zh":"外部培訓計劃可能成本高昂。"},{"en":"To be costly means to require a lot of money, time, or resources.","zh":"To be costly 指需要大量金錢、時間或資源。"},{"en":"Replacing broken computers can be costly for a small school.","zh":"對小型學校而言，更換壞電腦可能成本高昂。"},{"en":"If training is costly, managers need to make sure it produces useful results.","zh":"如果培訓成本高昂，管理者需要確保它帶來有用結果。"},{"en":"This phrase usually warns that something is expensive or resource-heavy.","zh":"這個片語通常提醒某事昂貴或需要大量資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"robust human resources department","meaning":"健全的人力資源部門","examples":[{"en":"A robust human resources department can deliver training internally.","zh":"健全的人力資源部門可以在內部提供培訓。"},{"en":"A robust human resources department is a strong HR team with enough skill and capacity.","zh":"Robust human resources department 是具備足夠技能和能力的強大人力資源團隊。"},{"en":"A large company may rely on a robust HR department to handle hiring, training, and staff welfare.","zh":"大公司可能依靠健全的人力資源部門處理招聘、培訓和員工福利。"},{"en":"If the HR department is weak, training may need outside support.","zh":"如果人力資源部門薄弱，培訓可能需要外部支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an internal team strong enough to manage people-related work.","zh":"這個片語描述足以管理人事工作的內部團隊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"undertake the training themselves","meaning":"自行進行培訓","examples":[{"en":"Some companies undertake the training themselves.","zh":"一些公司自行進行培訓。"},{"en":"To undertake the training themselves means to organise and deliver training without outside providers.","zh":"To undertake the training themselves 指不依靠外部供應商，自行組織和提供培訓。"},{"en":"A school may undertake teacher training itself if senior staff have enough experience.","zh":"如果資深員工有足夠經驗，學校可能自行進行教師培訓。"},{"en":"If staff design the training internally, the activities may fit the company culture better.","zh":"如果員工在內部設計培訓，活動可能更配合公司文化。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses doing the training in-house.","zh":"這個片語強調在內部自行進行培訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be established in","meaning":"成立於……","examples":[{"en":"Liaison Wizards was established in 2001.","zh":"Liaison Wizards 成立於2001年。"},{"en":"To be established in a year means to be founded or started in that year.","zh":"To be established in a year 指在該年份成立或創辦。"},{"en":"A charity established in 1995 may have decades of community experience.","zh":"成立於1995年的慈善機構可能有數十年社區經驗。"},{"en":"If a company has been established for many years, customers may trust it more.","zh":"如果一間公司成立多年，顧客可能更信任它。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the founding time of an organisation.","zh":"這個片語給出機構的創立時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be headed by","meaning":"由……領導","examples":[{"en":"The company is headed by Jeff Blackshaw.","zh":"這間公司由 Jeff Blackshaw 領導。"},{"en":"To be headed by someone means to be led or managed by that person.","zh":"To be headed by someone 指由某人領導或管理。"},{"en":"The school committee is headed by the principal.","zh":"學校委員會由校長領導。"},{"en":"If a company is headed by an experienced leader, decisions may be clearer.","zh":"如果公司由有經驗的領袖領導，決策可能更清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who is in charge.","zh":"這個片語指出誰負責領導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"offer free advice","meaning":"提供免費建議","examples":[{"en":"Liaison Wizards offers free training and development advice.","zh":"Liaison Wizards 提供免費培訓和發展建議。"},{"en":"To offer free advice means to give suggestions without charging money.","zh":"To offer free advice 指不收費地提供建議。"},{"en":"A community centre may offer free advice on job applications.","zh":"社區中心可能提供關於求職申請的免費建議。"},{"en":"If advice is free, smaller companies may be more willing to try it.","zh":"如果建議免費，較小型公司可能更願意嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes support that does not require payment.","zh":"這個片語描述不需要付款的支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"training and development advice","meaning":"培訓和發展建議","examples":[{"en":"Companies can obtain training and development advice online.","zh":"公司可以在網上取得培訓和發展建議。"},{"en":"Training and development advice is guidance on how to improve employees’ skills and growth.","zh":"Training and development advice 是關於如何提升員工技能和成長的指導。"},{"en":"A manager may seek training and development advice before designing a new workshop.","zh":"管理者在設計新工作坊前，可能尋求培訓和發展建議。"},{"en":"If advice is practical, it can help companies avoid irrelevant activities.","zh":"如果建議實用，它可以幫助公司避免不相關活動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to guidance about staff learning and improvement.","zh":"這個片語指關於員工學習和改善的指導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"companies wishing to","meaning":"希望……的公司","examples":[{"en":"The service supports companies wishing to run their own seminars.","zh":"這項服務支援希望自行舉辦講座的公司。"},{"en":"Companies wishing to do something are companies that want or plan to do it.","zh":"Companies wishing to do something 指想要或計劃做某事的公司。"},{"en":"Companies wishing to hire graduates may attend university career fairs.","zh":"希望聘請畢業生的公司可能參加大學招聘會。"},{"en":"If companies wish to train staff internally, online guidance may help them begin.","zh":"如果公司希望在內部培訓員工，網上指導可能幫助它們開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal way to describe companies with a particular intention.","zh":"這個片語以正式方式描述有某種意圖的公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"motivation seminars","meaning":"員工激勵講座","examples":[{"en":"Some companies organise motivation seminars for their employees.","zh":"一些公司為員工舉辦激勵講座。"},{"en":"Motivation seminars are talks or workshops designed to encourage and energise staff.","zh":"Motivation seminars 是旨在鼓勵員工和提升活力的講座或工作坊。"},{"en":"A company may invite a speaker to a motivation seminar after a stressful sales period.","zh":"公司可能在壓力大的銷售期後邀請講者舉辦激勵講座。"},{"en":"If a seminar only entertains people but changes nothing, motivation may fade quickly.","zh":"如果講座只是娛樂員工卻沒有改變任何事情，動力可能很快消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal sessions aimed at improving morale.","zh":"這個片語描述旨在改善士氣的正式課節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be designed in-house","meaning":"由機構內部設計","examples":[{"en":"The motivation seminars are designed in-house.","zh":"這些激勵講座由機構內部設計。"},{"en":"To be designed in-house means to be planned by people inside the organisation.","zh":"To be designed in-house 指由機構內部的人規劃。"},{"en":"A school may design its own reading programme in-house because teachers know their students.","zh":"學校可能內部設計自己的閱讀計劃，因為老師了解學生。"},{"en":"If training is designed in-house, it can use examples from the company’s real problems.","zh":"如果培訓由內部設計，它可以使用來自公司真實問題的例子。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts internal design with buying an external package.","zh":"這個片語把內部設計與購買外部套裝作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in-house training","meaning":"內部培訓","examples":[{"en":"In-house training can be tailored to an organisation’s culture.","zh":"內部培訓可以按機構文化度身設計。"},{"en":"In-house training is training organised and delivered inside the organisation.","zh":"In-house training 是在機構內部組織和提供的培訓。"},{"en":"A bank may use in-house training to teach staff its own customer-service standards.","zh":"銀行可能使用內部培訓，教員工其自身顧客服務標準。"},{"en":"If trainers know the workplace well, in-house training may feel more relevant.","zh":"如果培訓者熟悉工作場所，內部培訓可能感覺更相關。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to training created within the company rather than outside it.","zh":"這個片語指由公司內部創建，而不是外部提供的培訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the belief that","meaning":"相信……","examples":[{"en":"The company offers advice in the belief that contextualised training is more effective.","zh":"該公司提供建議，是相信配合具體環境的培訓更有效。"},{"en":"In the belief that means because someone believes a particular idea is true.","zh":"In the belief that 指因為某人相信某個想法是真確的。"},{"en":"A parent may limit screen time in the belief that children will sleep better.","zh":"家長可能限制螢幕時間，相信孩子會睡得更好。"},{"en":"If a company believes tailored training works better, it may avoid generic courses.","zh":"如果公司相信度身培訓更有效，它可能避免一般化課程。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the belief behind an action.","zh":"這個片語解釋行動背後的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"contextualised training","meaning":"配合具體環境的培訓","examples":[{"en":"Contextualised training reflects the organisation’s actual circumstances.","zh":"配合具體環境的培訓反映機構的實際情況。"},{"en":"Contextualised training is training adapted to the real situation, culture, and needs of a group.","zh":"Contextualised training 是按群體的真實情況、文化和需要調整的培訓。"},{"en":"A school designs contextualised training when examples come from its own classrooms.","zh":"當例子來自學校自己的課室時，學校就是在設計配合具體環境的培訓。"},{"en":"If training matches real workplace problems, staff are more likely to use what they learn.","zh":"如果培訓配合真實工作問題，員工更可能使用所學內容。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts specific training with generic training.","zh":"這個片語把具體培訓與一般化培訓作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"business model","meaning":"商業模式","examples":[{"en":"The company’s business model depends on advertising revenue.","zh":"該公司的商業模式依靠廣告收入。"},{"en":"A business model is the way a company creates value and earns money.","zh":"Business model 是公司創造價值和賺錢的方式。"},{"en":"A free app may have a business model based on advertisements.","zh":"免費應用程式可能有以廣告為基礎的商業模式。"},{"en":"If a business model is weak, the company may attract users but still lose money.","zh":"如果商業模式薄弱，公司可能吸引用戶但仍然虧損。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how a business is financially designed to survive.","zh":"這個片語解釋企業在財政上如何設計以生存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"基於……","examples":[{"en":"The company’s business model is based on online advertising.","zh":"該公司的商業模式基於網上廣告。"},{"en":"To be based on something means to be built, founded, or planned around it.","zh":"To be based on something 指建基於、創立於或圍繞某事規劃。"},{"en":"A teacher’s lesson may be based on students’ common mistakes.","zh":"老師的課堂可能基於學生常犯錯誤而設計。"},{"en":"If a business is based on advertising, it needs many visitors to earn money.","zh":"如果企業基於廣告營運，它需要大量訪客才能賺錢。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the foundation of an idea, plan, or system.","zh":"這個片語指出想法、計劃或制度的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"generate revenue from","meaning":"從……獲取收入","examples":[{"en":"The website generates revenue from advertising.","zh":"該網站從廣告獲取收入。"},{"en":"To generate revenue from something means to earn money from it.","zh":"To generate revenue from something 指從某事賺取收入。"},{"en":"A school fair may generate revenue from ticket sales and food stalls.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能從門票銷售和食物攤位獲取收入。"},{"en":"If a website has many visitors, advertisements can generate more income.","zh":"如果網站有很多訪客，廣告可以帶來更多收入。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the source of money earned.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於收入來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"popular website","meaning":"受歡迎的網站","examples":[{"en":"The company operates a popular training website.","zh":"該公司營運一個受歡迎的培訓網站。"},{"en":"A popular website is a website that many people visit or use.","zh":"Popular website 是許多人瀏覽或使用的網站。"},{"en":"A popular school website may provide homework notices, exam dates, and learning resources.","zh":"受歡迎的學校網站可能提供功課通知、考試日期和學習資源。"},{"en":"If a website becomes popular, it may attract advertisers or paying customers.","zh":"如果網站變得受歡迎，它可能吸引廣告商或付費顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong user interest online.","zh":"這個片語描述網上用戶興趣強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"surpass financial projections","meaning":"超越財政預測","examples":[{"en":"The company has surpassed its financial projections each year.","zh":"該公司每年都超越其財政預測。"},{"en":"To surpass financial projections means to perform better financially than expected.","zh":"To surpass financial projections 指財務表現好過預期。"},{"en":"A school charity sale may surpass its financial projections if parents donate generously.","zh":"如果家長慷慨捐款，學校慈善義賣可能超越財政預測。"},{"en":"If revenue is higher than forecast, the company has exceeded expectations.","zh":"如果收入高於預測，公司就超越了預期。"},{"en":"This phrase compares actual financial results with predicted results.","zh":"這個片語把實際財務結果與預測結果作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be in operation","meaning":"投入運作","examples":[{"en":"The website has been in operation for several years.","zh":"該網站已投入運作多年。"},{"en":"To be in operation means to be working, active, or running.","zh":"To be in operation 指正在運作、活動或營運。"},{"en":"The school library is in operation from eight in the morning.","zh":"學校圖書館由早上八時起投入運作。"},{"en":"If a website has been in operation for years, it may have built a steady audience.","zh":"如果網站已運作多年，它可能已建立穩定受眾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something functioning over a period of time.","zh":"這個片語描述某物在一段時間內運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"to date","meaning":"至今","examples":[{"en":"The company has met all its targets to date.","zh":"該公司至今已達成所有目標。"},{"en":"To date means up to the present time.","zh":"To date 指截至目前為止。"},{"en":"The student has completed three essays to date.","zh":"該學生至今已完成三篇作文。"},{"en":"If a project has been successful to date, it has gone well so far.","zh":"如果項目至今成功，它到目前為止進展良好。"},{"en":"This phrase summarises progress up to now.","zh":"這個片語概括到現在為止的進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"liken something to","meaning":"將某事比作……","examples":[{"en":"Blackshaw likens successful team building to sporting tactics.","zh":"Blackshaw 將成功的團隊建立比作體育策略。"},{"en":"To liken something to something else means to compare the two because they share similar features.","zh":"To liken something to something else 指因兩者有相似特徵而作比較。"},{"en":"A teacher may liken essay planning to building a house with a strong structure.","zh":"老師可能把作文規劃比作建造有穩固結構的房屋。"},{"en":"If teamwork and sport both need trust and roles, the comparison helps explain the idea.","zh":"如果團隊合作和體育都需要信任和角色，這種比較有助解釋概念。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a comparison that makes an idea clearer.","zh":"這個片語引入令想法更清晰的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the key to","meaning":"……的關鍵","examples":[{"en":"Mutual respect is the key to successful teamwork.","zh":"相互尊重是成功團隊合作的關鍵。"},{"en":"The key to something is the most important factor that helps achieve it.","zh":"The key to something 是幫助達成某事的最重要因素。"},{"en":"Regular revision is the key to remembering vocabulary long term.","zh":"定期溫習是長期記住詞彙的關鍵。"},{"en":"If trust is missing, the key to teamwork may be broken.","zh":"如果缺乏信任，團隊合作的關鍵可能已被破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the central requirement for success.","zh":"這個片語指出成功的核心條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"successful corporate team building","meaning":"成功的企業團隊建立","examples":[{"en":"Trust is essential to successful corporate team building.","zh":"信任對成功的企業團隊建立至關重要。"},{"en":"Successful corporate team building is effective teamwork development inside a business organisation.","zh":"Successful corporate team building 是企業機構內有效的團隊合作發展。"},{"en":"A company may achieve successful corporate team building when departments stop blaming one another and start solving problems together.","zh":"當公司部門停止互相指責並開始共同解決問題時，可能達成成功的企業團隊建立。"},{"en":"If trust grows, employees may share information more freely.","zh":"如果信任增加，員工可能更自由地分享資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes team building in a business setting, not only general social bonding.","zh":"這個片語描述商業環境中的團隊建立，而不只是一般社交聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tactics employed in","meaning":"在……中採用的策略","examples":[{"en":"Similar tactics are employed in sport and business.","zh":"類似策略在體育和商業中被採用。"},{"en":"Tactics employed in a field are methods or strategies used there.","zh":"Tactics employed in a field 是在某領域中使用的方法或策略。"},{"en":"The tactics employed in exam preparation may include practice papers and timed writing.","zh":"在備試中採用的策略可能包括練習試卷和限時寫作。"},{"en":"If tactics used in sport also help business teams, managers may learn from coaches.","zh":"如果體育中使用的策略也幫助商業團隊，管理者可能向教練學習。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical methods used in a particular setting.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於特定場景中使用的實際方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"less formal sporting environment","meaning":"較不正式的體育環境","examples":[{"en":"Strong relationships often develop in a less formal sporting environment.","zh":"強大關係常在較不正式的體育環境中發展。"},{"en":"A less formal sporting environment is a relaxed sports setting with fewer official workplace rules.","zh":"Less formal sporting environment 是規則較少、氣氛較輕鬆的體育場景。"},{"en":"Staff may talk more naturally during a friendly football match than in a meeting room.","zh":"員工在友誼足球賽中，可能比在會議室更自然地交談。"},{"en":"If people relax together, they may build trust more easily.","zh":"如果人們一起放鬆，他們可能更容易建立信任。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts informal sport with formal office settings.","zh":"這個片語把非正式體育與正式辦公室場景作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bonds and connections","meaning":"情誼和聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Shared activities can create bonds and connections between colleagues.","zh":"共同活動可以在同事之間建立情誼和聯繫。"},{"en":"Bonds and connections are relationships that make people feel linked and supportive.","zh":"Bonds and connections 是令人感到彼此相連和互相支持的關係。"},{"en":"Students build bonds and connections when they work through a difficult project together.","zh":"學生一起完成困難專題時會建立情誼和聯繫。"},{"en":"If colleagues form stronger bonds, they may help one another during pressure.","zh":"如果同事形成更強情誼，他們在壓力下可能互相幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional and social links between people.","zh":"這個片語描述人與人之間的情感和社交連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"develop empathy","meaning":"培養同理心","examples":[{"en":"Team members need opportunities to develop empathy.","zh":"團隊成員需要機會培養同理心。"},{"en":"To develop empathy means to learn to understand and care about other people’s feelings and situations.","zh":"To develop empathy 指學會理解和關心他人的感受與處境。"},{"en":"Students develop empathy when they listen to classmates explain personal difficulties.","zh":"當學生聆聽同學解釋個人困難時，他們會培養同理心。"},{"en":"If employees understand one another’s pressures, they may judge less harshly.","zh":"如果員工理解彼此壓力，他們可能較少嚴厲批判。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growing emotional understanding.","zh":"這個片語描述情感理解的增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rugby team","meaning":"欖球隊","examples":[{"en":"The members of a rugby team depend heavily on one another.","zh":"欖球隊成員高度依賴彼此。"},{"en":"A rugby team is a group of players who compete together in the sport of rugby.","zh":"Rugby team 是一起參加欖球比賽的一組球員。"},{"en":"A rugby team needs strength, communication, trust, and clear roles.","zh":"欖球隊需要力量、溝通、信任和清晰角色。"},{"en":"If one player fails to support another, the whole team may lose ground.","zh":"如果一名球員沒有支援另一名球員，整隊可能失去優勢。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a sports example of close teamwork.","zh":"這個片語提供緊密團隊合作的體育例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"within a department","meaning":"在部門內","examples":[{"en":"Team spirit can be developed within a department.","zh":"團隊精神可以在部門內建立。"},{"en":"Within a department means inside one section or unit of an organisation.","zh":"Within a department 指在機構的一個部門或單位內。"},{"en":"Within a school’s English department, teachers may share lesson plans and exam materials.","zh":"在學校英文科內，老師可能分享教案和考試材料。"},{"en":"If trust grows within a department, daily cooperation becomes smoother.","zh":"如果信任在部門內增加，日常合作會更順暢。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows the focus to one internal part of an organisation.","zh":"這個片語把焦點收窄至機構內的一個部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at company level","meaning":"在公司層面","examples":[{"en":"Team-building principles can also be applied at company level.","zh":"團隊建立原則也可以在公司層面應用。"},{"en":"At company level means across the whole company rather than only in one team or department.","zh":"At company level 指在整間公司範圍內，而不只是一個團隊或部門。"},{"en":"A safety policy at company level applies to every office and branch.","zh":"公司層面的安全政策適用於每個辦公室和分店。"},{"en":"If teamwork is improved at company level, departments may cooperate more consistently.","zh":"如果團隊合作在公司層面得到改善，部門之間可能更一致地合作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organisation-wide action.","zh":"這個片語指全機構範圍的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"good teamwork","meaning":"良好團隊合作","examples":[{"en":"Good teamwork depends on trust and communication.","zh":"良好團隊合作取決於信任和溝通。"},{"en":"Good teamwork means people cooperate effectively to reach a shared goal.","zh":"Good teamwork 指人們有效合作以達成共同目標。"},{"en":"Students show good teamwork when they divide tasks fairly and help weaker members.","zh":"學生公平分工並幫助較弱成員時，就是展現良好團隊合作。"},{"en":"If teamwork is good, a group can finish difficult tasks with less conflict.","zh":"如果團隊合作良好，小組可以以較少衝突完成困難任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cooperation that actually improves results.","zh":"這個片語描述真正改善結果的合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be fostered by","meaning":"由……培養","examples":[{"en":"Good teamwork is fostered by respect and encouragement.","zh":"良好團隊合作由尊重和鼓勵培養出來。"},{"en":"To be fostered by something means to be encouraged, supported, or developed by it.","zh":"To be fostered by something 指由某事鼓勵、支持或培養。"},{"en":"A love of reading can be fostered by parents who read with children.","zh":"如果家長與孩子一起閱讀，閱讀興趣可以被培養。"},{"en":"If managers praise cooperation, teamwork may be fostered naturally.","zh":"如果管理者讚賞合作，團隊合作可能自然被培養。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the conditions that help something grow.","zh":"這個片語描述幫助某事成長的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"shared enthusiasm","meaning":"共同熱誠","examples":[{"en":"Shared enthusiasm can bring a team closer together.","zh":"共同熱誠可以令團隊更緊密。"},{"en":"Shared enthusiasm is excitement or interest felt by several people together.","zh":"Shared enthusiasm 是幾個人共同感受到的興奮或興趣。"},{"en":"A class may feel shared enthusiasm when preparing for a drama performance.","zh":"班級準備戲劇表演時，可能感到共同熱誠。"},{"en":"If people feel excited about the same goal, they may work harder together.","zh":"如果人們對同一目標感到興奮，他們可能更努力一起工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes common energy that supports cooperation.","zh":"這個片語描述支援合作的共同能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"caring and supportive workplace","meaning":"關懷和互相支持的工作環境","examples":[{"en":"Employees perform better in a caring and supportive workplace.","zh":"員工在關懷和互相支持的工作環境中表現更好。"},{"en":"A caring and supportive workplace is a work environment where people feel respected, helped, and valued.","zh":"Caring and supportive workplace 是人們感到被尊重、被幫助和被重視的工作環境。"},{"en":"A school office becomes more supportive when colleagues help new staff learn routines.","zh":"當同事幫助新員工熟悉日常程序，學校辦公室會變得更支持人。"},{"en":"If employees feel supported, they may be less afraid to ask questions.","zh":"如果員工感到被支持，他們可能較不害怕提問。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a healthy workplace culture.","zh":"這個片語描述健康的工作場所文化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"exploit personnel","meaning":"剝削員工","examples":[{"en":"Managers should not exploit personnel for short-term gains.","zh":"管理者不應為短期利益剝削員工。"},{"en":"To exploit personnel means to use employees unfairly for benefit or profit.","zh":"To exploit personnel 指為利益或利潤不公平地利用員工。"},{"en":"A company exploits personnel if it demands unpaid overtime every week.","zh":"如果公司每星期要求無薪加班，就是剝削員工。"},{"en":"If workers feel exploited, morale and loyalty may fall.","zh":"如果員工感到被剝削，士氣和忠誠度可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unfair treatment of staff.","zh":"這個片語描述對員工的不公平待遇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dictate to personnel","meaning":"對員工發號施令","examples":[{"en":"Managers who dictate to personnel may damage staff morale.","zh":"對員工發號施令的管理者可能損害員工士氣。"},{"en":"To dictate to personnel means to give orders in a controlling way without listening.","zh":"To dictate to personnel 指以控制方式下命令而不聆聽。"},{"en":"A teacher who dictates to students without discussion may reduce class motivation.","zh":"如果老師不經討論就對學生發號施令，可能降低班級動力。"},{"en":"If staff are never consulted, they may resist changes.","zh":"如果員工從不被諮詢，他們可能抗拒改變。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests top-down control rather than respectful leadership.","zh":"這個片語暗示由上而下的控制，而不是尊重式領導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be sure to lead to failure","meaning":"必然導致失敗","examples":[{"en":"Exploiting employees is sure to lead to failure.","zh":"剝削員工必然導致失敗。"},{"en":"To be sure to lead to failure means to be almost certain to cause an unsuccessful result.","zh":"To be sure to lead to failure 指幾乎肯定會造成不成功的結果。"},{"en":"Ignoring instructions in an exam is sure to lead to lost marks.","zh":"在考試中忽視指示必然導致失分。"},{"en":"If managers treat staff badly, the team may eventually break down.","zh":"如果管理者惡劣對待員工，團隊最終可能崩潰。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly warns that an action will end badly.","zh":"這個片語強烈警告某行動會有壞結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be inherently more likely to","meaning":"本質上更有可能……","examples":[{"en":"Internally developed programmes are inherently more likely to suit the company.","zh":"內部開發的計劃本質上更有可能適合公司。"},{"en":"To be inherently more likely to do something means to have a natural or built-in greater chance of doing it.","zh":"To be inherently more likely to do something 指因本身特質而有更大機會做到某事。"},{"en":"A lesson designed by the class teacher is inherently more likely to match students’ level.","zh":"由班主任設計的課堂本質上更有可能配合學生程度。"},{"en":"If internal trainers know the culture, their programme may fit better from the start.","zh":"如果內部培訓者了解文化，他們的計劃從一開始就可能更合適。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why one option has a natural advantage.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何某選項有天然優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"external offerings","meaning":"外部提供的方案","examples":[{"en":"External offerings may not reflect the organisation’s culture.","zh":"外部提供的方案可能不能反映機構文化。"},{"en":"External offerings are services, courses, or products provided by outside companies.","zh":"External offerings 是由外部公司提供的服務、課程或產品。"},{"en":"A school may buy external offerings such as online learning platforms or teacher workshops.","zh":"學校可能購買網上學習平台或教師工作坊等外部方案。"},{"en":"If external offerings are too generic, staff may not find them useful.","zh":"如果外部方案太一般化，員工可能覺得沒有用。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts outside products with internally designed support.","zh":"這個片語把外部產品與內部設計支援作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for two main reasons","meaning":"基於兩個主要原因","examples":[{"en":"Osborne supports internal training for two main reasons.","zh":"Osborne 基於兩個主要原因支持內部培訓。"},{"en":"For two main reasons means because of two important explanations.","zh":"For two main reasons 指因為兩個重要解釋。"},{"en":"A student may choose online lessons for two main reasons: flexibility and lower travel time.","zh":"學生可能基於兩個主要原因選擇網課：彈性和較少交通時間。"},{"en":"If a writer says there are two main reasons, readers should expect two supporting points.","zh":"如果作者說有兩個主要原因，讀者應預期兩個支持點。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise an argument clearly.","zh":"這個片語幫助清晰組織論證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be easier to motivate","meaning":"較容易受到激勵","examples":[{"en":"People are easier to motivate when they help design the activities.","zh":"當人們協助設計活動時，他們較容易受到激勵。"},{"en":"To be easier to motivate means to be more willing to become interested and active.","zh":"To be easier to motivate 指較願意變得有興趣和積極。"},{"en":"Students are easier to motivate when they choose topics they care about.","zh":"當學生選擇自己關心的題目時，他們較容易受到激勵。"},{"en":"If employees feel ownership, they may put more energy into the programme.","zh":"如果員工感到有參與感，他們可能把更多精力投入計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase links involvement with stronger motivation.","zh":"這個片語把參與與更強動力連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be involved in designing","meaning":"參與設計……","examples":[{"en":"Employees should be involved in designing training activities.","zh":"員工應參與設計培訓活動。"},{"en":"To be involved in designing something means to take part in planning or creating it.","zh":"To be involved in designing something 指參與規劃或創造某事。"},{"en":"Students may be involved in designing a class noticeboard.","zh":"學生可能參與設計班房告示板。"},{"en":"If staff help design training, the activities may feel more relevant to them.","zh":"如果員工協助設計培訓，活動可能對他們更相關。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises participation before the activity begins.","zh":"這個片語強調活動開始前的參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"decide activities","meaning":"決定活動","examples":[{"en":"Participants can help decide which activities are appropriate.","zh":"參加者可以幫助決定哪些活動合適。"},{"en":"To decide activities means to choose what tasks, games, or exercises will be used.","zh":"To decide activities 指選擇會使用哪些任務、遊戲或練習。"},{"en":"A class may decide activities for an English fun day together.","zh":"班級可能一起決定英文同樂日的活動。"},{"en":"If participants help decide activities, they may feel more responsible for the outcome.","zh":"如果參加者協助決定活動，他們可能對結果更有責任感。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to choosing the content of a programme.","zh":"這個片語指選擇計劃內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"level of consultation","meaning":"諮詢程度","examples":[{"en":"Internal programmes can provide a higher level of consultation.","zh":"內部計劃可以提供較高的諮詢程度。"},{"en":"Level of consultation means how much people are asked for opinions before decisions are made.","zh":"Level of consultation 指決策前有多大程度徵詢人們意見。"},{"en":"A school has a high level of consultation if teachers, parents, and students can give feedback.","zh":"如果老師、家長和學生都能給回饋，學校就有高諮詢程度。"},{"en":"If consultation is weak, people may feel decisions are forced on them.","zh":"如果諮詢薄弱，人們可能覺得決定被強加於他們。"},{"en":"This phrase measures how much discussion happens before action.","zh":"這個片語衡量行動前有多少討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at the planning stage","meaning":"在規劃階段","examples":[{"en":"Staff should be consulted at the planning stage.","zh":"員工應在規劃階段被諮詢。"},{"en":"At the planning stage means during the early period when ideas and details are being prepared.","zh":"At the planning stage 指在想法和細節正在準備的早期階段。"},{"en":"Students should discuss roles at the planning stage of a group project.","zh":"學生應在小組專題的規劃階段討論角色。"},{"en":"If problems are noticed at the planning stage, they are easier to fix.","zh":"如果問題在規劃階段被注意到，就較容易修正。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to early preparation before action begins.","zh":"這個片語指行動開始前的早期準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be easier to achieve","meaning":"較容易達成","examples":[{"en":"Meaningful consultation is easier to achieve internally.","zh":"有意義的諮詢在內部較容易達成。"},{"en":"To be easier to achieve means to be more possible or less difficult to accomplish.","zh":"To be easier to achieve 指更可能或較不難完成。"},{"en":"Regular reading is easier to achieve if students set a fixed daily time.","zh":"如果學生設定固定每日時間，定期閱讀較容易達成。"},{"en":"If trainers are inside the company, honest discussion may be easier to arrange.","zh":"如果培訓者在公司內部，坦誠討論可能較容易安排。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how difficult different goals are to reach.","zh":"這個片語比較不同目標達成的難度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"internal department","meaning":"內部部門","examples":[{"en":"An internal department understands the company’s culture.","zh":"內部部門了解公司文化。"},{"en":"An internal department is a unit inside the organisation, such as HR, finance, or marketing.","zh":"Internal department 是機構內部的單位，例如人力資源、財務或市場部。"},{"en":"A school’s internal department may know student needs better than an outside provider.","zh":"學校內部部門可能比外部供應商更了解學生需要。"},{"en":"If an internal department designs training, examples can come from real company experience.","zh":"如果內部部門設計培訓，例子可以來自公司真實經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a department within the organisation itself.","zh":"這個片語指機構本身內部的部門。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"external consultant","meaning":"外部顧問","examples":[{"en":"An external consultant may have limited knowledge of the staff.","zh":"外部顧問可能對員工了解有限。"},{"en":"An external consultant is an outside expert hired to give advice or support.","zh":"External consultant 是受聘提供建議或支援的外部專家。"},{"en":"A small business may hire an external consultant to improve its accounting system.","zh":"小企業可能聘請外部顧問來改善會計系統。"},{"en":"If the consultant does not understand the workplace culture, advice may be too general.","zh":"如果顧問不了解工作場所文化，建議可能太一般化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to expert help from outside the organisation.","zh":"這個片語指來自機構外部的專家協助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"of slightly less importance","meaning":"重要性稍低","examples":[{"en":"Participant perception is of slightly less importance than consultation.","zh":"參加者看法的重要性比諮詢稍低。"},{"en":"Of slightly less importance means less important, but still relevant.","zh":"Of slightly less importance 指較不重要，但仍然相關。"},{"en":"In exam writing, handwriting is of slightly less importance than clear ideas and grammar.","zh":"在考試寫作中，字體比清晰想法和文法重要性稍低。"},{"en":"If one factor matters less, it should not be ignored completely.","zh":"如果某因素較不重要，也不應完全忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase ranks priorities without dismissing the lower one.","zh":"這個片語排列優先次序，但不否定較低的一項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be perceived as","meaning":"被視為……","examples":[{"en":"Training should be perceived as useful by its participants.","zh":"培訓應被參加者視為有用。"},{"en":"To be perceived as something means to be seen or understood in that way.","zh":"To be perceived as something 指被看作或理解為某種樣子。"},{"en":"A strict teacher may be perceived as unfair if rules are not explained clearly.","zh":"如果規則沒有清楚解釋，嚴格老師可能被視為不公平。"},{"en":"If training is perceived as childish, staff may resist taking part.","zh":"如果培訓被視為幼稚，員工可能抗拒參與。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on people’s impression, not only the actual intention.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於人的印象，而不只是實際意圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"provide outcomes","meaning":"帶來成果","examples":[{"en":"The programme should provide practical outcomes for employees.","zh":"該計劃應為員工帶來實際成果。"},{"en":"To provide outcomes means to produce clear results or benefits.","zh":"To provide outcomes 指產生清晰結果或好處。"},{"en":"A study plan should provide outcomes such as better vocabulary and faster reading.","zh":"學習計劃應帶來更好詞彙和更快閱讀等成果。"},{"en":"If training provides no outcomes, employees may feel their time was wasted.","zh":"如果培訓沒有帶來成果，員工可能覺得浪費時間。"},{"en":"This phrase asks what useful results a programme creates.","zh":"這個片語詢問計劃創造甚麼有用結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be geared towards","meaning":"以……為目標","examples":[{"en":"The activities should be geared towards developing individual potential.","zh":"活動應以發展個人潛能為目標。"},{"en":"To be geared towards something means to be designed to achieve that purpose.","zh":"To be geared towards something 指被設計用來達成該目的。"},{"en":"A speaking course may be geared towards building confidence in interviews.","zh":"口語課程可能以建立面試信心為目標。"},{"en":"If training is geared towards real workplace skills, employees may use it immediately.","zh":"如果培訓以真實工作技能為目標，員工可能立即使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the purpose that a plan is aimed at.","zh":"這個片語描述計劃所指向的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"develop individual potential","meaning":"發展個人潛能","examples":[{"en":"Good training helps develop individual potential.","zh":"良好培訓幫助發展個人潛能。"},{"en":"To develop individual potential means to help each person grow their abilities and confidence.","zh":"To develop individual potential 指幫助每個人發展能力和信心。"},{"en":"A teacher develops individual potential by giving different students suitable challenges.","zh":"老師透過給不同學生合適挑戰來發展個人潛能。"},{"en":"If employees learn skills that match their strengths, they may contribute more effectively.","zh":"如果員工學習配合自己強項的技能，他們可能更有效地作出貢獻。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on personal growth inside a team or organisation.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於團隊或機構內的個人成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have insight into","meaning":"深入了解……","examples":[{"en":"Internal trainers have insight into the company’s culture.","zh":"內部培訓者深入了解公司文化。"},{"en":"To have insight into something means to understand it deeply or clearly.","zh":"To have insight into something 指深入或清楚理解某事。"},{"en":"A form teacher has insight into students’ habits after working with them daily.","zh":"班主任每天與學生相處後，會深入了解學生習慣。"},{"en":"If trainers understand staff personalities, they can design more suitable activities.","zh":"如果培訓者理解員工性格，他們可以設計更合適活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes informed understanding, not a surface guess.","zh":"這個片語描述有根據的理解，而不是表面猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"culture at hand","meaning":"當前的文化環境","examples":[{"en":"The programme should reflect the personalities and culture at hand.","zh":"該計劃應反映當前的人員性格和文化環境。"},{"en":"Culture at hand means the specific culture present in the current situation or organisation.","zh":"Culture at hand 指當前情況或機構中存在的特定文化。"},{"en":"A school activity should fit the culture at hand, not copy another school blindly.","zh":"學校活動應配合當前文化環境，而不是盲目複製另一間學校。"},{"en":"If a team values direct discussion, training should not force an artificial style.","zh":"如果團隊重視直接討論，培訓就不應強迫人工化風格。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the real culture already existing in that place.","zh":"這個片語指該地方已經存在的真實文化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be tailored to suit","meaning":"度身設計以配合……","examples":[{"en":"The activities can be tailored to suit a particular audience.","zh":"活動可以度身設計以配合特定對象。"},{"en":"To be tailored to suit someone means to be specially adjusted for their needs.","zh":"To be tailored to suit someone 指為某人的需要特別調整。"},{"en":"A teacher may tailor exercises to suit beginners and advanced students separately.","zh":"老師可能為初學者和高階學生分別度身設計練習。"},{"en":"If training is tailored to suit the audience, people are more likely to find it useful.","zh":"如果培訓度身設計以配合對象，人們更可能覺得有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful adaptation rather than one-size-fits-all design.","zh":"這個片語描述仔細調整，而不是一刀切設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"distinctive needs","meaning":"獨特需要","examples":[{"en":"Every organisation has its own distinctive needs.","zh":"每個機構都有自己的獨特需要。"},{"en":"Distinctive needs are special needs that make one group different from another.","zh":"Distinctive needs 是令某群體不同於另一群體的特殊需要。"},{"en":"A small school and a large university have very different distinctive needs.","zh":"小型學校和大型大學有非常不同的獨特需要。"},{"en":"If training ignores distinctive needs, it may solve the wrong problem.","zh":"如果培訓忽視獨特需要，它可能解決錯誤問題。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that one solution may not fit every organisation.","zh":"這個片語強調一個方案未必適合所有機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"particular audience","meaning":"特定對象","examples":[{"en":"The programme was designed for a particular audience.","zh":"該計劃是為特定對象設計的。"},{"en":"A particular audience is the specific group of people something is intended for.","zh":"Particular audience 是某事物 intended for 的特定群體。"},{"en":"A children’s museum designs activities for a particular audience: young learners and families.","zh":"兒童博物館為特定對象設計活動：年幼學習者和家庭。"},{"en":"If a speaker understands the audience, the message becomes clearer and more relevant.","zh":"如果講者了解對象，訊息會變得更清晰和更相關。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that communication should match the people receiving it.","zh":"這個片語提醒我們，溝通應配合接收訊息的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"biggest barriers to","meaning":"……的最大障礙","examples":[{"en":"Negative perceptions are among the biggest barriers to successful training.","zh":"負面看法是成功培訓的最大障礙之一。"},{"en":"Biggest barriers to something are the main obstacles that make it difficult to achieve.","zh":"Biggest barriers to something 是令某事難以達成的主要障礙。"},{"en":"Fear of speaking is one of the biggest barriers to improving oral English.","zh":"害怕說話是改善英語口語的最大障礙之一。"},{"en":"If staff believe training is useless, that belief may block participation.","zh":"如果員工相信培訓無用，這種信念可能阻礙參與。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the most serious obstacles.","zh":"這個片語指出最嚴重的障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"successful staff training","meaning":"成功的員工培訓","examples":[{"en":"Clear objectives are essential for successful staff training.","zh":"清晰目標對成功的員工培訓至關重要。"},{"en":"Successful staff training is training that improves employees’ skills, confidence, or performance.","zh":"Successful staff training 是改善員工技能、信心或表現的培訓。"},{"en":"A shop may achieve successful staff training if workers learn how to handle complaints calmly.","zh":"如果店舖員工學會冷靜處理投訴，該店可能達成成功的員工培訓。"},{"en":"If training has clear aims and follow-up, it is more likely to succeed.","zh":"如果培訓有清晰目標和跟進，它更可能成功。"},{"en":"This phrase describes training that produces real workplace benefits.","zh":"這個片語描述能帶來真實工作好處的培訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the perception that","meaning":"……的看法","examples":[{"en":"Some professionals have the perception that training games are childish.","zh":"一些專業人士有一種看法，認為培訓遊戲很幼稚。"},{"en":"The perception that means the belief or impression that something is true.","zh":"The perception that 指認為某事為真的信念或印象。"},{"en":"Some students have the perception that grammar is boring before they see useful examples.","zh":"一些學生在看到有用例子前，可能有文法很沉悶的看法。"},{"en":"If people perceive an activity negatively, they may resist it before trying it.","zh":"如果人們負面看待某活動，他們可能在嘗試前已抗拒它。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how people see something, whether or not the view is fair.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於人們如何看待某事，不論該看法是否公平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"game-focused","meaning":"過分以遊戲為主的","examples":[{"en":"Some activities may appear too game-focused.","zh":"一些活動可能看起來過分以遊戲為主。"},{"en":"Game-focused means centred mainly on games rather than serious discussion or practical outcomes.","zh":"Game-focused 指主要集中於遊戲，而不是認真討論或實際成果。"},{"en":"A lesson may feel too game-focused if students play a lot but learn little.","zh":"如果學生玩很多但學得很少，課堂可能感覺過分以遊戲為主。"},{"en":"If training is too game-focused, staff may not see the link with work.","zh":"如果培訓太以遊戲為主，員工可能看不到它與工作的連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest that games are overused or poorly explained.","zh":"這個片語可以暗示遊戲被過度使用或解釋不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have no real objectives","meaning":"沒有真正目標","examples":[{"en":"Employees may believe the games have no real objectives.","zh":"員工可能相信這些遊戲沒有真正目標。"},{"en":"To have no real objectives means to lack clear aims or practical purposes.","zh":"To have no real objectives 指缺乏清晰目標或實際目的。"},{"en":"A meeting has no real objectives if nobody knows what decision must be made.","zh":"如果沒有人知道會議要作出甚麼決定，該會議就是沒有真正目標。"},{"en":"If training games have no clear goal, participants may feel embarrassed or bored.","zh":"如果培訓遊戲沒有清晰目標，參加者可能感到尷尬或沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises activities that seem pointless.","zh":"這個片語批評看似沒有意義的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"trite or patronising","meaning":"陳腐或帶有高高在上態度的","examples":[{"en":"Some professionals consider training games trite or patronising.","zh":"一些專業人士認為培訓遊戲陳腐或帶有高高在上態度。"},{"en":"Trite or patronising means dull, overused, or treating adults as if they are less intelligent.","zh":"Trite or patronising 指沉悶、老套，或像對待較不聰明的人那樣對待成年人。"},{"en":"A workshop can feel patronising if it explains obvious ideas in a childish way.","zh":"如果工作坊用幼稚方式解釋顯而易見的想法，它可能令人覺得帶有高高在上態度。"},{"en":"If activities feel trite, participants may stop taking the trainer seriously.","zh":"如果活動感覺陳腐，參加者可能不再認真看待培訓者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a negative reaction to shallow or condescending training.","zh":"這個片語描述對膚淺或居高臨下培訓的負面反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be unable to appreciate","meaning":"未能理解……的價值","examples":[{"en":"Some participants are unable to appreciate the benefits of informal activities.","zh":"一些參加者未能理解非正式活動的好處。"},{"en":"To be unable to appreciate something means to fail to understand its value.","zh":"To be unable to appreciate something 指未能理解某事的價值。"},{"en":"Students may be unable to appreciate poetry until a teacher explains its emotions clearly.","zh":"學生可能要等老師清楚解釋詩中的情感後，才理解詩的價值。"},{"en":"If trainers do not explain the purpose, staff may miss the value of the activity.","zh":"如果培訓者沒有解釋目的，員工可能看不到活動的價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes not recognising why something matters.","zh":"這個片語描述未能認出某事為何重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hidden benefits","meaning":"隱藏的好處","examples":[{"en":"Training games may have hidden benefits.","zh":"培訓遊戲可能有隱藏的好處。"},{"en":"Hidden benefits are useful effects that are not obvious at first.","zh":"Hidden benefits 是一開始不明顯的有用效果。"},{"en":"Group discussion may have hidden benefits because quiet students learn to speak more confidently.","zh":"小組討論可能有隱藏的好處，因為安靜學生會學會更有信心地發言。"},{"en":"If games reveal communication problems, they can help trainers address real issues.","zh":"如果遊戲揭示溝通問題，它們可以幫助培訓者處理真實議題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes value that appears only after closer thought or experience.","zh":"這個片語描述經過更仔細思考或體驗後才出現的價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"build understanding","meaning":"建立相互理解","examples":[{"en":"Shared activities can build understanding within a group.","zh":"共同活動可以在團體內建立相互理解。"},{"en":"To build understanding means to help people know one another’s ideas, feelings, or situations better.","zh":"To build understanding 指幫助人們更了解彼此的想法、感受或處境。"},{"en":"A class debate can build understanding if students listen before responding.","zh":"如果學生先聆聽再回應，班級辯論可以建立相互理解。"},{"en":"If colleagues understand each other’s pressures, they may cooperate more patiently.","zh":"如果同事了解彼此壓力，他們可能更有耐性地合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradually improving mutual awareness.","zh":"這個片語描述逐步改善彼此認識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"camaraderie","meaning":"伙伴情誼","examples":[{"en":"Humour and shared challenges can develop camaraderie.","zh":"幽默和共同挑戰可以培養伙伴情誼。"},{"en":"Camaraderie is a friendly sense of trust and closeness among people in a group.","zh":"Camaraderie 是團體中友好、信任和親近的感覺。"},{"en":"A sports team may develop camaraderie after training hard together for months.","zh":"運動隊一起辛苦訓練數月後，可能培養伙伴情誼。"},{"en":"If colleagues laugh and solve problems together, they may feel more like a team.","zh":"如果同事一起笑和解決問題，他們可能更像一個團隊。"},{"en":"This word describes warm group spirit and friendship.","zh":"這個詞描述溫暖的團體精神和友誼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"within the group","meaning":"在團體內","examples":[{"en":"Trust needs to be developed within the group.","zh":"信任需要在團體內建立。"},{"en":"Within the group means among the members of that group.","zh":"Within the group 指在該團體成員之間。"},{"en":"In a class project, trust within the group grows when everyone completes their tasks.","zh":"在班級專題中，當每個人完成任務時，團體內的信任會增加。"},{"en":"If conflict remains within the group, outside support may not solve everything.","zh":"如果衝突仍留在團體內，外部支援未必能解決一切。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on relationships among group members.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於團體成員之間的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"if presented correctly","meaning":"如果以適當方式進行","examples":[{"en":"Games can be effective if presented correctly.","zh":"如果以適當方式進行，遊戲可以有效。"},{"en":"If presented correctly means if explained and introduced in the right way.","zh":"If presented correctly 指如果以正確方式解釋和引入。"},{"en":"A grammar game can help students if presented correctly as serious practice, not just play.","zh":"如果文法遊戲被適當地呈現為認真練習，而不只是玩樂，它可以幫助學生。"},{"en":"If trainers explain the purpose clearly, participants may accept informal activities more easily.","zh":"如果培訓者清楚解釋目的，參加者可能更容易接受非正式活動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that delivery affects whether an activity succeeds.","zh":"這個片語顯示呈現方式會影響活動是否成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"within the correct context","meaning":"在適當情境下","examples":[{"en":"Informal activities should be used within the correct context.","zh":"非正式活動應在適當情境下使用。"},{"en":"Within the correct context means in the right situation and for the right purpose.","zh":"Within the correct context 指在正確情況和正確目的下。"},{"en":"A joke may work within the correct context but sound rude in a formal meeting.","zh":"笑話在適當情境下可能有效，但在正式會議中可能顯得無禮。"},{"en":"If games are used after a serious discussion, they may reinforce learning.","zh":"如果遊戲在認真討論後使用，它們可能鞏固學習。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that an activity’s value depends on situation.","zh":"這個片語提醒我們，活動價值取決於情境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in conjunction with","meaning":"與……配合","examples":[{"en":"Games work best in conjunction with more formal training.","zh":"遊戲與較正式培訓配合時效果最好。"},{"en":"In conjunction with means together with another method or thing.","zh":"In conjunction with 指與另一種方法或事物一起。"},{"en":"Students learn vocabulary better when examples are used in conjunction with practice questions.","zh":"當例子與練習題配合使用時，學生詞彙學得更好。"},{"en":"If informal games are combined with formal reflection, learning may become deeper.","zh":"如果非正式遊戲與正式反思結合，學習可能更深入。"},{"en":"This phrase shows two things working together.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩件事共同作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"staid approaches","meaning":"較傳統沉悶的方法","examples":[{"en":"Informal games may complement more staid approaches.","zh":"非正式遊戲可能補充較傳統沉悶的方法。"},{"en":"Staid approaches are serious, traditional, and sometimes rather dull methods.","zh":"Staid approaches 是嚴肅、傳統，有時較沉悶的方法。"},{"en":"A lecture can be a staid approach if students only listen and never participate.","zh":"如果學生只聽而不參與，講課可能是一種較傳統沉悶的方法。"},{"en":"If a training course is too staid, adding interaction may keep participants engaged.","zh":"如果培訓課程太沉悶，加入互動可能保持參加者投入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal methods that may need livelier support.","zh":"這個片語描述可能需要較活潑支援的正式方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"enormous asset","meaning":"極有價值的工具","examples":[{"en":"Well-designed games can be an enormous asset in staff training.","zh":"設計良好的遊戲可以是員工培訓中極有價值的工具。"},{"en":"An enormous asset is something extremely valuable or useful.","zh":"Enormous asset 是極其有價值或有用的東西。"},{"en":"A bilingual teacher can be an enormous asset in a school with many new immigrant students.","zh":"在有許多新移民學生的學校，雙語老師可以是極有價值的人才。"},{"en":"If an activity builds trust quickly, it becomes a valuable training tool.","zh":"如果活動能快速建立信任，它就成為有價值的培訓工具。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly praises something for its usefulness.","zh":"這個片語強烈讚揚某事的實用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in simple terms","meaning":"簡單來說","examples":[{"en":"In simple terms, team building follows four main stages.","zh":"簡單來說，團隊建立遵循四個主要階段。"},{"en":"In simple terms means explained in an easy and direct way.","zh":"In simple terms 指以容易和直接的方式解釋。"},{"en":"In simple terms, saving money means spending less than you earn.","zh":"簡單來說，儲錢就是花得比賺得少。"},{"en":"If an idea is complex, explaining it in simple terms helps learners understand it first.","zh":"如果概念複雜，用簡單方式解釋能幫助學習者先理解它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a clearer, less technical explanation.","zh":"這個片語引入更清楚、較少技術性的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"define the objectives of","meaning":"界定……的目標","examples":[{"en":"Edwards defines the objectives of team building as a process.","zh":"Edwards 將團隊建立的目標界定為一個過程。"},{"en":"To define the objectives of something means to state clearly what it is meant to achieve.","zh":"To define the objectives of something 指清楚說明某事旨在達成甚麼。"},{"en":"A teacher defines the objectives of a lesson before choosing activities.","zh":"老師在選擇活動前會界定課堂目標。"},{"en":"If objectives are unclear, people cannot judge whether the programme succeeded.","zh":"如果目標不清晰，人們就不能判斷計劃是否成功。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on clarifying purpose.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於釐清目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"clarification of","meaning":"釐清……","examples":[{"en":"The process begins with the clarification of collective goals.","zh":"這個過程由釐清集體目標開始。"},{"en":"Clarification of something means making it clearer and easier to understand.","zh":"Clarification of something 指令某事更清楚和更容易理解。"},{"en":"A student may ask for clarification of homework instructions before starting.","zh":"學生可能在開始前要求釐清功課指示。"},{"en":"If goals are clarified early, the team can avoid confusion later.","zh":"如果目標早早被釐清，團隊之後可以避免混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the act of removing uncertainty.","zh":"這個片語描述消除不確定的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"collective goals","meaning":"集體目標","examples":[{"en":"The team must first agree on its collective goals.","zh":"團隊必須首先同意其集體目標。"},{"en":"Collective goals are aims shared by all members of a group.","zh":"Collective goals 是團體所有成員共同擁有的目標。"},{"en":"A class may set collective goals for improving attendance and homework completion.","zh":"班級可能設定改善出席率和功課完成率的集體目標。"},{"en":"If collective goals are accepted by everyone, members can coordinate their efforts.","zh":"如果集體目標被所有人接受，成員就能協調努力。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses shared aims rather than individual wishes.","zh":"這個片語強調共同目標，而不是個人願望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lead to the identification of","meaning":"導致識別……","examples":[{"en":"Clarifying the goals leads to the identification of barriers.","zh":"釐清目標會導致識別障礙。"},{"en":"To lead to the identification of something means to help people recognise or find it.","zh":"To lead to the identification of something 指幫助人們認出或找出某事。"},{"en":"Reviewing test mistakes can lead to the identification of weak grammar areas.","zh":"檢視測驗錯誤可以導致識別薄弱文法範疇。"},{"en":"If a team knows its goal, it can more easily see what is blocking progress.","zh":"如果團隊知道自己的目標，就更容易看見甚麼正在阻礙進展。"},{"en":"This phrase links one step with discovering the next problem.","zh":"這個片語把一個步驟與發現下一個問題連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"inhibitors","meaning":"阻礙因素","examples":[{"en":"The team must identify the inhibitors that prevent progress.","zh":"團隊必須識別妨礙進展的阻礙因素。"},{"en":"Inhibitors are factors that slow down or stop something from developing.","zh":"Inhibitors 是拖慢或阻止某事發展的因素。"},{"en":"Fear of making mistakes can be an inhibitor in speaking lessons.","zh":"害怕犯錯可以是口語課中的阻礙因素。"},{"en":"If a team identifies its inhibitors, it can remove or reduce them.","zh":"如果團隊識別其阻礙因素，就可以移除或減少它們。"},{"en":"This word describes barriers that hold progress back.","zh":"這個詞描述拖住進展的障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"prevent achievement","meaning":"妨礙達成……","examples":[{"en":"Poor communication may prevent the achievement of team goals.","zh":"欠佳溝通可能妨礙團隊目標的達成。"},{"en":"To prevent achievement means to stop a goal from being reached.","zh":"To prevent achievement 指阻止目標被達成。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can prevent achievement in exams because students cannot think clearly.","zh":"睡眠不足可以妨礙考試成功，因為學生不能清楚思考。"},{"en":"If staff do not share information, the team may fail to complete its task.","zh":"如果員工不分享資訊，團隊可能無法完成任務。"},{"en":"This phrase links an obstacle with failure to reach a goal.","zh":"這個片語把障礙與未能達成目標連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"goal achievement","meaning":"目標達成","examples":[{"en":"Clear communication can improve goal achievement.","zh":"清晰溝通可以改善目標達成。"},{"en":"Goal achievement means successfully reaching a target or aim.","zh":"Goal achievement 指成功達到目標或目的。"},{"en":"A student improves goal achievement by setting small weekly targets.","zh":"學生透過設定每週小目標來改善目標達成。"},{"en":"If progress is measured, goal achievement becomes easier to track.","zh":"如果進展被量度，目標達成就更容易追蹤。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether aims are actually reached.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於目標是否真正達到。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"introduction of enablers","meaning":"引入促進因素","examples":[{"en":"The next stage involves the introduction of enablers.","zh":"下一階段涉及引入促進因素。"},{"en":"Introduction of enablers means bringing in tools, actions, or conditions that help progress.","zh":"Introduction of enablers 指引入幫助進展的工具、行動或條件。"},{"en":"A school may introduce mentors as enablers for new students.","zh":"學校可能引入導師作為新學生的促進因素。"},{"en":"If communication is weak, regular meetings may act as enablers.","zh":"如果溝通薄弱，定期會議可能成為促進因素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding supports that make success easier.","zh":"這個片語描述加入令成功更容易的支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"assist in","meaning":"協助……","examples":[{"en":"New systems can assist in goal achievement.","zh":"新制度可以協助目標達成。"},{"en":"To assist in something means to help with it.","zh":"To assist in something 指幫助某事。"},{"en":"Revision checklists can assist in exam preparation.","zh":"溫習清單可以協助備試。"},{"en":"If a new reporting system assists in communication, staff may solve issues faster.","zh":"如果新匯報系統協助溝通，員工可能更快解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes support that helps a process succeed.","zh":"這個片語描述幫助過程成功的支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be followed by","meaning":"其後是……","examples":[{"en":"The introduction of enablers is followed by an evaluation stage.","zh":"引入促進因素之後是評估階段。"},{"en":"To be followed by something means to have that thing come next.","zh":"To be followed by something 指之後接着出現某事。"},{"en":"A short lecture may be followed by group discussion.","zh":"短講座之後可能是小組討論。"},{"en":"If training is followed by evaluation, managers can see whether it worked.","zh":"如果培訓之後有評估，管理者可以看見它是否有效。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the order of steps.","zh":"這個片語顯示步驟次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"final stage","meaning":"最後階段","examples":[{"en":"Measuring the results is the final stage of the process.","zh":"衡量結果是這個過程的最後階段。"},{"en":"The final stage is the last part of a process.","zh":"Final stage 是一個過程的最後部分。"},{"en":"Proofreading is the final stage before submitting an essay.","zh":"校對是提交作文前的最後階段。"},{"en":"If the final stage is skipped, people may not know whether the project succeeded.","zh":"如果跳過最後階段，人們可能不知道項目是否成功。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the end of a structured sequence.","zh":"這個片語標示有結構次序的結尾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"measure outcomes","meaning":"衡量成果","examples":[{"en":"The organisation must measure outcomes after the training.","zh":"機構必須在培訓後衡量成果。"},{"en":"To measure outcomes means to check and evaluate the results produced.","zh":"To measure outcomes 指檢查和評估所產生的結果。"},{"en":"A teacher measures outcomes by comparing students’ writing before and after a course.","zh":"老師透過比較課程前後的學生寫作來衡量成果。"},{"en":"If outcomes are not measured, success becomes only an opinion.","zh":"如果成果沒有被衡量，成功就只是一種意見。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses evidence-based evaluation.","zh":"這個片語強調以證據為本的評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"from that point on","meaning":"從那時起","examples":[{"en":"From that point on, progress should be monitored regularly.","zh":"從那時起，進展應定期被監察。"},{"en":"From that point on means starting from that moment and continuing afterwards.","zh":"From that point on 指由那一刻開始並在之後持續。"},{"en":"After the first test, from that point on the teacher tracked every student’s progress.","zh":"第一次測驗後，從那時起老師追蹤每位學生的進展。"},{"en":"If goals are set, progress should be checked from that point on.","zh":"如果目標已設定，從那時起就應檢查進展。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the beginning of a continuing action.","zh":"這個片語標示持續行動的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"monitor progress","meaning":"監察進展","examples":[{"en":"Managers should monitor progress after the programme ends.","zh":"管理者應在計劃結束後監察進展。"},{"en":"To monitor progress means to regularly check how much improvement or movement has happened.","zh":"To monitor progress 指定期檢查有多少改善或進展。"},{"en":"A student can monitor progress by keeping a vocabulary record each week.","zh":"學生可以透過每週記錄詞彙來監察進展。"},{"en":"If managers monitor progress, they can adjust the programme before problems grow.","zh":"如果管理者監察進展，他們可以在問題擴大前調整計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing checking, not a one-time review.","zh":"這個片語描述持續檢查，而不是一次性檢討。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ensure that goals are achieved","meaning":"確保目標得以達成","examples":[{"en":"Regular follow-up helps ensure that goals are achieved.","zh":"定期跟進有助確保目標得以達成。"},{"en":"To ensure that goals are achieved means to make sure targets are actually reached.","zh":"To ensure that goals are achieved 指確保目標真正被達到。"},{"en":"A teacher may check drafts weekly to ensure that writing goals are achieved.","zh":"老師可能每週檢查草稿，以確保寫作目標得以達成。"},{"en":"If nobody follows up, goals may remain words on paper.","zh":"如果沒有人跟進，目標可能只停留在紙上。"},{"en":"This phrase connects supervision with successful completion.","zh":"這個片語把監督與成功完成連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"continue to be achieved","meaning":"繼續得以達成","examples":[{"en":"The outcomes should be monitored so that the goals continue to be achieved.","zh":"成果應被監察，以便目標繼續得以達成。"},{"en":"To continue to be achieved means to keep being reached over time.","zh":"To continue to be achieved 指隨時間持續被達到。"},{"en":"A school may review reading results monthly so improvement continues to be achieved.","zh":"學校可能每月檢視閱讀結果，讓改善繼續得以達成。"},{"en":"If good habits disappear after training, goals may stop being achieved.","zh":"如果培訓後良好習慣消失，目標可能不再被達成。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on maintaining success, not only reaching it once.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於維持成功，而不只是達成一次。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"positive alternatives","meaning":"正面替代方法","examples":[{"en":"Teams should replace barriers with positive alternatives.","zh":"團隊應以正面替代方法取代障礙。"},{"en":"Positive alternatives are better options that solve or reduce a problem.","zh":"Positive alternatives 是能解決或減少問題的較好選項。"},{"en":"Instead of blaming late students, a school may offer positive alternatives such as reminder messages.","zh":"學校可以提供提示訊息等正面替代方法，而不是責備遲到學生。"},{"en":"If conflict is caused by unclear roles, a clear task chart can be a positive alternative.","zh":"如果衝突由角色不清造成，清晰任務表可以是正面替代方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes constructive replacements for harmful patterns.","zh":"這個片語描述用建設性方法取代有害模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"use of humour","meaning":"運用幽默","examples":[{"en":"The use of humour can reduce tension between colleagues.","zh":"運用幽默可以減少同事之間的緊張。"},{"en":"The use of humour means using jokes, lightness, or friendly amusement to improve a situation.","zh":"The use of humour 指運用笑話、輕鬆感或友善趣味來改善情況。"},{"en":"A teacher may use humour to relax students before a difficult exam topic.","zh":"老師可能運用幽默，讓學生在學困難考試題目前放鬆。"},{"en":"If humour is respectful, it can make people less defensive.","zh":"如果幽默是尊重人的，它可以令人較少防衛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes humour as a tool, not just entertainment.","zh":"這個片語把幽默描述為工具，而不只是娛樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"go a long way towards","meaning":"對……大有幫助","examples":[{"en":"Humour can go a long way towards building relationships.","zh":"幽默對建立關係大有幫助。"},{"en":"To go a long way towards something means to help greatly in achieving it.","zh":"To go a long way towards something 指大大幫助達成某事。"},{"en":"A sincere apology can go a long way towards repairing a friendship.","zh":"真誠道歉對修補友誼大有幫助。"},{"en":"If colleagues laugh together, it can greatly reduce distance between them.","zh":"如果同事一起笑，它可以大大減少彼此距離。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong contribution to a goal.","zh":"這個片語描述對目標作出強大貢獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"relationship building","meaning":"關係建立","examples":[{"en":"Empathy is important in relationship building.","zh":"同理心在關係建立中很重要。"},{"en":"Relationship building is the process of creating trust, understanding, and cooperation between people.","zh":"Relationship building 是在人與人之間建立信任、理解和合作的過程。"},{"en":"A new teacher begins relationship building by learning students’ names and interests.","zh":"新老師透過認識學生姓名和興趣開始關係建立。"},{"en":"If people spend time listening to one another, relationships can grow stronger.","zh":"如果人們花時間聆聽彼此，關係可以變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the gradual creation of better human connections.","zh":"這個片語描述逐步創造更好人際連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"on a personal level","meaning":"在個人層面","examples":[{"en":"Humour can improve communication on a personal level.","zh":"幽默可以在個人層面改善溝通。"},{"en":"On a personal level means in relation to individual feelings, relationships, or experiences.","zh":"On a personal level 指與個人感受、關係或經歷有關。"},{"en":"A teacher may support students on a personal level by noticing when they are anxious.","zh":"老師注意到學生焦慮時，可以在個人層面支援他們。"},{"en":"If colleagues connect personally, formal cooperation may become easier.","zh":"如果同事在個人層面建立連繫，正式合作可能變得更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on human connection rather than official structure.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於人際連繫，而不是正式結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"development of empathy","meaning":"同理心的培養","examples":[{"en":"Shared activities encourage the development of empathy.","zh":"共同活動鼓勵同理心的培養。"},{"en":"Development of empathy means the growth of people’s ability to understand others’ feelings.","zh":"Development of empathy 指人們理解他人感受的能力增長。"},{"en":"Group service projects can encourage the development of empathy in students.","zh":"小組服務項目可以鼓勵學生同理心的培養。"},{"en":"If staff see the pressures other departments face, empathy may grow.","zh":"如果員工看見其他部門面對的壓力，同理心可能增長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional growth through experience.","zh":"這個片語描述透過經驗而來的情感成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"removal of antipathy","meaning":"消除反感","examples":[{"en":"Humour may contribute to the removal of antipathy.","zh":"幽默可能有助消除反感。"},{"en":"Removal of antipathy means reducing or getting rid of dislike, hostility, or negative feeling.","zh":"Removal of antipathy 指減少或消除不喜歡、敵意或負面感受。"},{"en":"A sincere conversation can help remove antipathy between two classmates after an argument.","zh":"爭吵後，真誠對話可以幫助兩名同學消除反感。"},{"en":"If people laugh together safely, old hostility may soften.","zh":"如果人們安全地一起笑，舊有敵意可能軟化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes replacing dislike with more open relations.","zh":"這個片語描述以更開放關係取代反感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"foster cooperation","meaning":"促進合作","examples":[{"en":"Positive activities can foster cooperation between employees.","zh":"正面活動可以促進員工之間的合作。"},{"en":"To foster cooperation means to encourage people to work together more willingly.","zh":"To foster cooperation 指鼓勵人們更願意一起工作。"},{"en":"A shared class project can foster cooperation if every student has a meaningful role.","zh":"如果每位學生都有有意義的角色，共同班級專題可以促進合作。"},{"en":"If staff trust one another, they are more likely to share resources and information.","zh":"如果員工互相信任，他們更可能分享資源和資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes helping cooperation grow.","zh":"這個片語描述幫助合作成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"formal level","meaning":"正式層面","examples":[{"en":"Personal trust can lead to cooperation on a more formal level.","zh":"個人信任可以帶來更正式層面的合作。"},{"en":"Formal level means the official or organised side of relationships and work.","zh":"Formal level 指關係和工作的官方或有組織層面。"},{"en":"A friendly class may still need rules on a formal level to manage group projects fairly.","zh":"友好的班級在正式層面仍可能需要規則，以公平管理小組專題。"},{"en":"If personal respect grows, formal meetings may become more productive.","zh":"如果個人尊重增加，正式會議可能變得更有成效。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts official cooperation with personal feeling.","zh":"這個片語把正式合作與個人感受作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"within a training context","meaning":"在培訓情境中","examples":[{"en":"Humour can be valuable within a training context.","zh":"幽默在培訓情境中可以很有價值。"},{"en":"Within a training context means in a situation where people are learning or being trained.","zh":"Within a training context 指在人們正在學習或接受培訓的情況中。"},{"en":"Within a training context, a simple game can reveal how people communicate under pressure.","zh":"在培訓情境中，簡單遊戲可以揭示人們在壓力下如何溝通。"},{"en":"If humour supports learning, it is not just a distraction.","zh":"如果幽默支援學習，它就不只是分心事物。"},{"en":"This phrase places an activity inside a learning situation.","zh":"這個片語把活動放在學習情境之內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"help an organisation achieve its goals","meaning":"幫助機構達成目標","examples":[{"en":"Games can help an organisation achieve its goals.","zh":"遊戲可以幫助機構達成目標。"},{"en":"To help an organisation achieve its goals means to support the organisation in reaching its aims.","zh":"To help an organisation achieve its goals 指支援機構達到其目的。"},{"en":"Better communication training can help a school achieve its goal of fewer misunderstandings.","zh":"更好的溝通培訓可以幫助學校達成減少誤解的目標。"},{"en":"If games build trust, they may help teams work more effectively.","zh":"如果遊戲建立信任，它們可能幫助團隊更有效地工作。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an activity with practical organisational success.","zh":"這個片語把活動與實際機構成功連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"two-month-long programme","meaning":"為期兩個月的計劃","examples":[{"en":"Alan Kidman designed a two-month-long team-building programme.","zh":"Alan Kidman 設計了一個為期兩個月的團隊建立計劃。"},{"en":"A two-month-long programme is a programme that lasts for two months.","zh":"Two-month-long programme 是持續兩個月的計劃。"},{"en":"A school may run a two-month-long reading challenge before exams.","zh":"學校可能在考試前舉辦為期兩個月的閱讀挑戰。"},{"en":"If a programme lasts two months, participants have time to practise and reflect.","zh":"如果計劃持續兩個月，參加者有時間練習和反思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the length of a planned activity.","zh":"這個片語描述有計劃活動的長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"senior management","meaning":"高級管理層","examples":[{"en":"The programme was designed for senior management.","zh":"該計劃是為高級管理層設計的。"},{"en":"Senior management refers to the high-level managers who make important decisions.","zh":"Senior management 指作出重要決策的高層管理者。"},{"en":"Senior management may decide company strategy, budgets, and major policies.","zh":"高級管理層可能決定公司策略、預算和主要政策。"},{"en":"If senior management joins training, the rest of the company may take it more seriously.","zh":"如果高級管理層參與培訓，公司的其他人可能更認真看待它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the top decision-making level in an organisation.","zh":"這個片語描述機構中的最高決策層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"deliver a workshop","meaning":"主持工作坊","examples":[{"en":"Kidman will deliver the first workshop in the series.","zh":"Kidman 將主持系列中的第一個工作坊。"},{"en":"To deliver a workshop means to lead or present a practical training session.","zh":"To deliver a workshop 指帶領或呈現實用培訓課節。"},{"en":"A teacher may deliver a workshop on exam-writing skills for senior students.","zh":"老師可能為高年級學生主持考試寫作技巧工作坊。"},{"en":"If the workshop is delivered clearly, participants can practise the new skill immediately.","zh":"如果工作坊清楚進行，參加者可以立即練習新技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes actively running a learning session.","zh":"這個片語描述主動進行學習課節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a series of","meaning":"一系列……","examples":[{"en":"The programme consists of a series of workshops and activities.","zh":"該計劃由一系列工作坊和活動組成。"},{"en":"A series of something means several related things arranged one after another.","zh":"A series of something 指幾個相關事物一個接一個安排。"},{"en":"A school may offer a series of revision classes before public exams.","zh":"學校可能在公開考試前提供一系列溫習課。"},{"en":"If learning happens through a series of sessions, ideas can build gradually.","zh":"如果學習透過一系列課節進行，想法可以逐步建立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes connected events, not just one activity.","zh":"這個片語描述相連活動，而不只是單一活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"strengthen communication","meaning":"加強溝通","examples":[{"en":"The project aims to strengthen communication between departments.","zh":"該項目旨在加強部門之間的溝通。"},{"en":"To strengthen communication means to make the sharing of information clearer and more effective.","zh":"To strengthen communication 指令資訊分享更清晰和更有效。"},{"en":"A class group can strengthen communication by agreeing where to post updates.","zh":"班級小組可以透過同意在哪裏發布更新來加強溝通。"},{"en":"If departments communicate better, mistakes and delays may decrease.","zh":"如果部門溝通更好，錯誤和延誤可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improving how people exchange information.","zh":"這個片語描述改善人們交換資訊的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"extremely diverse departments","meaning":"差異極大的部門","examples":[{"en":"The organisation contains several extremely diverse departments.","zh":"該機構包含幾個差異極大的部門。"},{"en":"Extremely diverse departments are departments that differ greatly in work, culture, skills, or priorities.","zh":"Extremely diverse departments 是在工作、文化、技能或優先次序上非常不同的部門。"},{"en":"In a hospital, the emergency department and finance office are extremely diverse departments.","zh":"在醫院中，急症室和財務辦公室是差異極大的部門。"},{"en":"If departments are very different, team building may need to bridge large gaps.","zh":"如果部門非常不同，團隊建立可能需要彌合很大差距。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights strong internal variety within an organisation.","zh":"這個片語突出機構內部強烈多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"department heads","meaning":"部門主管","examples":[{"en":"Six department heads will participate in the programme.","zh":"六名部門主管將參與該計劃。"},{"en":"Department heads are managers who lead particular departments.","zh":"Department heads 是領導特定部門的管理者。"},{"en":"A school’s department heads may include the heads of English, Maths, and Science.","zh":"學校的部門主管可能包括英文科、數學科和科學科主任。"},{"en":"If department heads cooperate, their teams may also communicate better.","zh":"如果部門主管合作，他們的團隊也可能更好溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people responsible for leading sections of an organisation.","zh":"這個片語指負責領導機構不同部分的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be collectively responsible for","meaning":"共同負責……","examples":[{"en":"The six managers are collectively responsible for over 200 employees.","zh":"這六名管理者共同負責超過200名員工。"},{"en":"To be collectively responsible for something means to share responsibility for it as a group.","zh":"To be collectively responsible for something 指作為一個群體共同承擔責任。"},{"en":"Teachers may be collectively responsible for student discipline during a school trip.","zh":"老師在學校旅行期間可能共同負責學生紀律。"},{"en":"If managers share responsibility, they must coordinate their decisions.","zh":"如果管理者共同負責，他們必須協調決定。"},{"en":"This phrase shows responsibility held together, not by one person alone.","zh":"這個片語顯示責任由多人共同承擔，而不是只由一人承擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be involved in","meaning":"參與……","examples":[{"en":"Senior managers will be involved in the seminar series.","zh":"高級管理者將參與該系列講座。"},{"en":"To be involved in something means to take part in it.","zh":"To be involved in something 指參與某事。"},{"en":"Students become more responsible when they are involved in planning class activities.","zh":"當學生參與規劃班級活動時，他們會變得更有責任感。"},{"en":"If managers are involved in training, they may understand staff problems better.","zh":"如果管理者參與培訓，他們可能更了解員工問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active participation.","zh":"這個片語描述積極參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"experimental programme","meaning":"實驗性計劃","examples":[{"en":"The organisation is testing an experimental programme.","zh":"該機構正在測試一個實驗性計劃。"},{"en":"An experimental programme is a new programme being tried to see whether it works.","zh":"Experimental programme 是正在試行、以查看是否有效的新計劃。"},{"en":"A school may test an experimental programme for improving students’ reading speed.","zh":"學校可能測試一個改善學生閱讀速度的實驗性計劃。"},{"en":"If the programme succeeds, it may later become a regular part of training.","zh":"如果計劃成功，它之後可能成為培訓的固定部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a trial rather than an established method.","zh":"這個片語描述試驗，而不是已確立的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"prove to be a success","meaning":"證明是成功的","examples":[{"en":"If the programme proves to be a success, it will be expanded.","zh":"如果該計劃證明是成功的，它將會擴展。"},{"en":"To prove to be a success means to show through results that something works well.","zh":"To prove to be a success 指透過結果顯示某事運作良好。"},{"en":"A new homework system may prove to be a success if students submit work more regularly.","zh":"如果學生更定期交功課，新功課制度可能證明是成功的。"},{"en":"If the trial produces better cooperation, managers may use it more widely.","zh":"如果試驗帶來更好合作，管理者可能更廣泛使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes success confirmed by experience or evidence.","zh":"這個片語描述由經驗或證據證實的成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be intended for use","meaning":"擬供……使用","examples":[{"en":"The programme is also intended for use in overseas branches.","zh":"該計劃也擬供海外分公司使用。"},{"en":"To be intended for use means to be planned or designed to be used in a particular place or way.","zh":"To be intended for use 指被計劃或設計用於特定地方或方式。"},{"en":"A worksheet may be intended for use with beginner students.","zh":"工作紙可能擬供初學學生使用。"},{"en":"If a programme is intended for overseas use, it may need cultural adjustment.","zh":"如果計劃擬供海外使用，它可能需要文化調整。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the planned application of something.","zh":"這個片語解釋某事的預定用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"branches overseas","meaning":"海外分公司","examples":[{"en":"The company may introduce the training in its branches overseas.","zh":"公司可能在其海外分公司引入培訓。"},{"en":"Branches overseas are offices or business units located in other countries.","zh":"Branches overseas 是位於其他國家的辦公室或業務單位。"},{"en":"A restaurant chain may have branches overseas in several major cities.","zh":"連鎖餐廳可能在幾個主要城市有海外分店。"},{"en":"If training is used in overseas branches, language and culture may need adjustment.","zh":"如果培訓在海外分公司使用，語言和文化可能需要調整。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a company’s foreign offices or locations.","zh":"這個片語指公司的海外辦公室或地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"formalised approach","meaning":"較制度化的方法","examples":[{"en":"The organisation previously used a more formalised approach.","zh":"該機構之前使用較制度化的方法。"},{"en":"A formalised approach is a structured, official, and rule-based method.","zh":"Formalised approach 是有結構、官方和以規則為本的方法。"},{"en":"A school may use a formalised approach to discipline with written warnings and meetings.","zh":"學校可能使用較制度化的紀律方法，包括書面警告和會議。"},{"en":"If an approach is too formalised, it may feel stiff or impersonal.","zh":"如果方法太制度化，它可能感覺僵硬或缺乏人情味。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts structured methods with more flexible ones.","zh":"這個片語把有結構方法與較靈活方法作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"staff-development training","meaning":"員工發展培訓","examples":[{"en":"The company has changed its approach to staff-development training.","zh":"該公司已改變其員工發展培訓方法。"},{"en":"Staff-development training is training that helps employees grow their abilities and careers.","zh":"Staff-development training 是幫助員工發展能力和事業的培訓。"},{"en":"A school may provide staff-development training for teachers learning new assessment methods.","zh":"學校可能為學習新評估方法的老師提供員工發展培訓。"},{"en":"If staff-development training is useful, employees may feel the company invests in them.","zh":"如果員工發展培訓有用，員工可能覺得公司投資於他們。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on long-term employee growth.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於員工長期成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"rely on methods such as","meaning":"依賴……等方法","examples":[{"en":"The earlier programme relied on methods such as psychometric testing.","zh":"早期計劃依賴心理測量測試等方法。"},{"en":"To rely on methods such as something means to use those methods as important tools.","zh":"To rely on methods such as something 指把這些方法作為重要工具使用。"},{"en":"A teacher may rely on methods such as quizzes, discussion, and rewriting to improve writing.","zh":"老師可能依賴小測、討論和重寫等方法來改善寫作。"},{"en":"If a programme relies only on tests, it may miss human relationships.","zh":"如果計劃只依賴測試，它可能忽略人際關係。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples of the tools being used.","zh":"這個片語引入所使用工具的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"psychometric testing","meaning":"心理測量測試","examples":[{"en":"Psychometric testing is often used to assess personality and ability.","zh":"心理測量測試常用於評估性格和能力。"},{"en":"Psychometric testing uses structured tests to measure traits, skills, or mental abilities.","zh":"Psychometric testing 使用有結構的測試來量度特質、技能或心智能力。"},{"en":"A company may use psychometric testing when hiring managers.","zh":"公司招聘管理者時可能使用心理測量測試。"},{"en":"If tests are poorly interpreted, they may label people too simply.","zh":"如果測試被錯誤解讀，它們可能過分簡化地標籤人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal measurement of psychological or ability-related features.","zh":"這個片語描述對心理或能力相關特徵的正式量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"motivational conferences","meaning":"激勵會議","examples":[{"en":"The organisation previously held motivational conferences.","zh":"該機構以前舉辦激勵會議。"},{"en":"Motivational conferences are large meetings intended to encourage people and improve energy or commitment.","zh":"Motivational conferences 是旨在鼓勵人和提升能量或投入感的大型會議。"},{"en":"A company may hold a motivational conference after a difficult business year.","zh":"公司可能在艱難商業年份後舉辦激勵會議。"},{"en":"If speeches are inspiring but no action follows, motivation may not last.","zh":"如果演講鼓舞人心但之後沒有行動，動力可能不能持久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal events aimed at raising morale.","zh":"這個片語描述旨在提升士氣的正式活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"formal appraisals","meaning":"正式工作評核","examples":[{"en":"Formal appraisals were part of the earlier training approach.","zh":"正式工作評核是早期培訓方法的一部分。"},{"en":"Formal appraisals are official reviews of an employee’s performance.","zh":"Formal appraisals 是對員工表現的正式檢討。"},{"en":"A teacher may receive a formal appraisal after a classroom observation.","zh":"老師在課堂觀察後可能收到正式工作評核。"},{"en":"If appraisals focus only on criticism, staff may become defensive.","zh":"如果評核只聚焦於批評，員工可能變得防衛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes structured evaluation in the workplace.","zh":"這個片語描述工作場所中的結構化評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"as yet untried","meaning":"尚未試行的","examples":[{"en":"The new approach is as yet untried.","zh":"新方法尚未試行。"},{"en":"As yet untried means not tested or used so far.","zh":"As yet untried 指到目前為止尚未被測試或使用。"},{"en":"A school may hesitate to use an as yet untried marking system in a public exam year.","zh":"學校可能猶豫是否在公開試年份使用尚未試行的評分制度。"},{"en":"If a method is untried, managers should monitor results carefully.","zh":"如果方法尚未試行，管理者應仔細監察結果。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights uncertainty because evidence is still missing.","zh":"這個片語突出因證據仍缺乏而存在的不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"challenge participants","meaning":"挑戰參加者","examples":[{"en":"The new activities will challenge participants in unfamiliar ways.","zh":"新活動將以陌生方式挑戰參加者。"},{"en":"To challenge participants means to push them to think, act, or cooperate beyond their usual habits.","zh":"To challenge participants 指推動參加者超越平常習慣去思考、行動或合作。"},{"en":"A debate activity may challenge shy students to speak in front of others.","zh":"辯論活動可能挑戰害羞學生在人前說話。"},{"en":"If participants are challenged safely, they may discover new strengths.","zh":"如果參加者在安全情況下被挑戰，他們可能發現新強項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making people stretch their abilities.","zh":"這個片語描述令人拓展能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"by comparison","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"By comparison, the new programme is much less formal.","zh":"相比之下，新計劃較不正式得多。"},{"en":"By comparison introduces how one thing differs when compared with another.","zh":"By comparison 引出某事與另一事比較時如何不同。"},{"en":"The first essay was confusing; by comparison, the second was much clearer.","zh":"第一篇作文很混亂；相比之下，第二篇清楚得多。"},{"en":"If an old method is formal and a new one is relaxed, this phrase helps show the contrast.","zh":"如果舊方法正式而新方法輕鬆，這個片語有助顯示對比。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a direct comparison.","zh":"這個片語表示直接比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"radical approach","meaning":"大膽創新的方法","examples":[{"en":"The theatrical activity represents a rather radical approach.","zh":"戲劇活動代表一種頗為大膽創新的方法。"},{"en":"A radical approach is a bold and very different method that challenges normal practice.","zh":"Radical approach 是大膽而非常不同、挑戰正常做法的方法。"},{"en":"Letting students design the whole lesson would be a radical approach in a traditional classroom.","zh":"讓學生設計整堂課，在傳統課室中會是大膽創新的方法。"},{"en":"If a company usually uses formal tests, drama-based training may feel radical.","zh":"如果公司通常使用正式測試，以戲劇為本的培訓可能感覺大膽創新。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a method that is unusually new or daring.","zh":"這個片語描述異常新穎或大膽的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"one initiative","meaning":"其中一項新措施","examples":[{"en":"One initiative requires managers to produce a theatrical performance.","zh":"其中一項新措施要求管理者製作戲劇表演。"},{"en":"One initiative means one planned action or project among others.","zh":"One initiative 指多項行動或項目中的其中一項有計劃措施。"},{"en":"One initiative at a school might be a peer-mentoring programme for new students.","zh":"學校其中一項新措施可能是為新生而設的朋輩導師計劃。"},{"en":"If one initiative works well, the organisation may expand it later.","zh":"如果其中一項措施效果良好，機構之後可能擴展它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a specific action within a broader plan.","zh":"這個片語在較大計劃中引入一項具體行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"require someone to","meaning":"要求某人去……","examples":[{"en":"The activity requires participants to work together creatively.","zh":"該活動要求參加者創意地一起工作。"},{"en":"To require someone to do something means to make it necessary for them to do it.","zh":"To require someone to do something 指使某人必須做某事。"},{"en":"The exam requires students to answer all questions in English.","zh":"考試要求學生用英語回答所有問題。"},{"en":"If an activity requires cooperation, participants cannot succeed alone.","zh":"如果活動要求合作，參加者就不能獨自成功。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what a person must do.","zh":"這個片語解釋某人必須做甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"organise and deliver","meaning":"籌辦和呈現","examples":[{"en":"The managers must organise and deliver a performance.","zh":"管理者必須籌辦和呈現一場表演。"},{"en":"To organise and deliver something means to plan it and then carry it out or present it.","zh":"To organise and deliver something 指規劃某事，然後執行或呈現它。"},{"en":"Students may organise and deliver a class presentation on climate change.","zh":"學生可能籌辦和呈現關於氣候變化的班級匯報。"},{"en":"If a team must both plan and perform, members need clear roles.","zh":"如果團隊必須既規劃又表演，成員需要清晰角色。"},{"en":"This phrase covers preparation and execution together.","zh":"這個片語同時涵蓋準備和執行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"theatrical performance","meaning":"戲劇表演","examples":[{"en":"The team will write and perform a theatrical production.","zh":"團隊將編寫並演出一場戲劇作品。"},{"en":"A theatrical performance is a staged acting performance before an audience.","zh":"Theatrical performance 是在觀眾面前上演的戲劇表演。"},{"en":"A school may use a theatrical performance to teach students about history.","zh":"學校可能使用戲劇表演來教學生歷史。"},{"en":"If managers create a performance together, they must plan, communicate, and trust one another.","zh":"如果管理者一起創作表演，他們必須規劃、溝通和互相信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes drama-based presentation.","zh":"這個片語描述以戲劇為本的呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be invited to attend","meaning":"獲邀出席","examples":[{"en":"All staff members will be invited to attend the performance.","zh":"所有員工都將獲邀出席表演。"},{"en":"To be invited to attend means to be formally asked to go to an event.","zh":"To be invited to attend 指被正式邀請前往某活動。"},{"en":"Parents may be invited to attend a school open day.","zh":"家長可能獲邀出席學校開放日。"},{"en":"If all staff are invited, the performance becomes a shared company event.","zh":"如果所有員工都獲邀，表演就成為共同的公司活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving permission or a request to be present.","zh":"這個片語描述獲得出席的許可或邀請。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"motivational approaches","meaning":"激勵方法","examples":[{"en":"Organisations use many different motivational approaches.","zh":"機構使用許多不同激勵方法。"},{"en":"Motivational approaches are methods used to encourage people to work, learn, or participate with more energy.","zh":"Motivational approaches 是用來鼓勵人更有活力地工作、學習或參與的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may use praise, goals, and choice as motivational approaches.","zh":"老師可能使用讚賞、目標和選擇作為激勵方法。"},{"en":"If one approach fails, another may suit the group better.","zh":"如果一種方法失效，另一種可能更適合該群體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes different ways of building motivation.","zh":"這個片語描述建立動力的不同方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a wide variety of","meaning":"多種多樣的……","examples":[{"en":"Team-building programmes include a wide variety of techniques.","zh":"團隊建立計劃包括多種多樣的技巧。"},{"en":"A wide variety of something means many different kinds of it.","zh":"A wide variety of something 指某事物有許多不同種類。"},{"en":"A good library offers a wide variety of books for different ages and interests.","zh":"好圖書館為不同年齡和興趣的人提供多種多樣的書籍。"},{"en":"If training uses a wide variety of methods, it can suit more learning styles.","zh":"如果培訓使用多種多樣的方法，它可以配合更多學習風格。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises broad range and diversity.","zh":"這個片語強調範圍廣和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"methodologies and techniques","meaning":"方法和技巧","examples":[{"en":"Experts use different methodologies and techniques in staff training.","zh":"專家在員工培訓中使用不同方法和技巧。"},{"en":"Methodologies and techniques are systems and practical methods used to do something.","zh":"Methodologies and techniques 是用來做某事的系統和實際方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may use different methodologies and techniques for reading, writing, and speaking.","zh":"老師可能在閱讀、寫作和口語中使用不同方法和技巧。"},{"en":"If the method is wrong, even a useful technique may not work well.","zh":"如果方法錯誤，即使有用技巧也可能效果不好。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to both overall approaches and specific tools.","zh":"這個片語同時指整體方法和具體工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"theories and tools","meaning":"理論和工具","examples":[{"en":"Team-building approaches are based on different theories and tools.","zh":"團隊建立方法基於不同理論和工具。"},{"en":"Theories and tools are ideas that explain a process and practical methods used to apply those ideas.","zh":"Theories and tools 是解釋過程的想法，以及用來應用這些想法的實際方法。"},{"en":"A writing course may use theories about learning together with tools such as checklists.","zh":"寫作課程可能同時使用學習理論和清單等工具。"},{"en":"If tools are not supported by a clear theory, training may feel random.","zh":"如果工具沒有清晰理論支持，培訓可能感覺隨意。"},{"en":"This phrase combines thinking frameworks with practical resources.","zh":"這個片語把思考框架與實用資源結合起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"generally agree that","meaning":"普遍同意","examples":[{"en":"Experts generally agree that no single method suits every company.","zh":"專家普遍同意沒有單一方法適合每間公司。"},{"en":"Generally agree that means most people in a group accept an idea, though not necessarily everyone.","zh":"Generally agree that 指群體中大多數人接受某想法，但不一定人人同意。"},{"en":"Teachers generally agree that students need both practice and feedback.","zh":"老師普遍同意學生需要練習和回饋。"},{"en":"If experts generally agree, the idea has broad support but may still have exceptions.","zh":"如果專家普遍同意，該想法有廣泛支持，但仍可能有例外。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses common agreement without claiming total agreement.","zh":"這個片語表達普遍共識，而不是聲稱完全一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"succeed or fail","meaning":"成功或失敗","examples":[{"en":"A training method may succeed or fail depending on the organisation.","zh":"培訓方法可能成功或失敗，視乎機構而定。"},{"en":"To succeed or fail means to work well or not work well.","zh":"To succeed or fail 指運作良好或運作不良。"},{"en":"A study plan may succeed or fail depending on whether the student follows it regularly.","zh":"學習計劃可能成功或失敗，視乎學生是否定期執行。"},{"en":"If a method fits the culture, it is more likely to succeed; if not, it may fail.","zh":"如果方法配合文化，它更可能成功；如果不配合，可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase presents two possible outcomes.","zh":"這個片語呈現兩種可能結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"depending upon","meaning":"視乎……","examples":[{"en":"The result depends upon the organisation’s culture.","zh":"結果視乎機構文化而定。"},{"en":"Depending upon means being influenced or decided by something.","zh":"Depending upon 指受某事影響或由某事決定。"},{"en":"A student’s revision plan may change depending upon the exam date.","zh":"學生的溫習計劃可能視乎考試日期而改變。"},{"en":"If success depends upon culture, the same programme may work differently in different companies.","zh":"如果成功視乎文化，同一計劃在不同公司可能有不同效果。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the condition that affects the result.","zh":"這個片語引出影響結果的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"organisational culture","meaning":"機構文化","examples":[{"en":"Training programmes must suit the organisational culture.","zh":"培訓計劃必須配合機構文化。"},{"en":"Organisational culture is the shared habits, values, attitudes, and ways of working inside an organisation.","zh":"Organisational culture 是機構內共同的習慣、價值觀、態度和工作方式。"},{"en":"A school’s organisational culture may value discipline, creativity, or student independence.","zh":"學校的機構文化可能重視紀律、創意或學生自主。"},{"en":"If a programme clashes with organisational culture, staff may reject it.","zh":"如果計劃與機構文化衝突，員工可能拒絕它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the “personality” of an organisation.","zh":"這個片語描述機構的「性格」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be implemented","meaning":"被推行","examples":[{"en":"New methods should be carefully implemented.","zh":"新方法應被小心推行。"},{"en":"To be implemented means to be put into practice or carried out.","zh":"To be implemented 指被付諸實行或執行。"},{"en":"A new school rule should be implemented only after teachers and students understand it.","zh":"新校規應在老師和學生理解後才被推行。"},{"en":"If a good idea is implemented badly, it may still fail.","zh":"如果好想法推行得差，它仍可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on turning a plan into real action.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於把計劃變成實際行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a fit with","meaning":"與……的配合","examples":[{"en":"A good fit with the participants’ personalities is essential.","zh":"與參加者性格的良好配合是必要的。"},{"en":"A fit with something means a suitable match with it.","zh":"A fit with something 指與某事合適配合。"},{"en":"A teaching method must be a good fit with students’ age and level.","zh":"教學方法必須與學生年齡和程度有良好配合。"},{"en":"If training does not fit participants’ personalities, they may feel uncomfortable or resistant.","zh":"如果培訓不配合參加者性格，他們可能感到不舒服或抗拒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes suitability between two things.","zh":"這個片語描述兩件事之間的合適程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"personalities involved","meaning":"涉及其中的人的性格","examples":[{"en":"The method must suit the personalities involved.","zh":"方法必須適合涉及其中的人的性格。"},{"en":"Personalities involved are the character types of the people taking part.","zh":"Personalities involved 是參與者的性格類型。"},{"en":"A quiet class may need different activities from a very outspoken class because the personalities involved differ.","zh":"安靜班級可能需要不同於非常外向班級的活動，因為涉及其中的人的性格不同。"},{"en":"If the personalities involved are competitive, cooperation tasks may need careful rules.","zh":"如果參與者性格好勝，合作任務可能需要仔細規則。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the people’s character traits in a situation.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於情境中人們的性格特質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be crucial to success","meaning":"對成功至關重要","examples":[{"en":"A good cultural fit is crucial to success.","zh":"良好的文化配合對成功至關重要。"},{"en":"To be crucial to success means to be extremely important for a successful result.","zh":"To be crucial to success 指對成功結果極其重要。"},{"en":"Clear instructions are crucial to success in group exams or projects.","zh":"清晰指示對小組考試或專題成功至關重要。"},{"en":"If a programme fits the culture, staff are more likely to accept it.","zh":"如果計劃配合文化，員工更可能接受它。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a factor that strongly affects whether something succeeds.","zh":"這個片語指出強烈影響某事是否成功的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"delivery of training sessions","meaning":"培訓課節的進行","examples":[{"en":"The delivery of training sessions should be professional.","zh":"培訓課節的進行應具專業水準。"},{"en":"Delivery of training sessions means the way training is presented, led, and managed.","zh":"Delivery of training sessions 指培訓呈現、帶領和管理的方式。"},{"en":"A teacher’s delivery of a lesson affects whether students stay focused.","zh":"老師進行課堂的方式會影響學生是否保持專注。"},{"en":"If delivery is unclear, even good content may fail to help participants.","zh":"如果進行方式不清晰，即使內容好也可能幫不到參加者。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how training is actually conducted.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於培訓實際如何進行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"appropriate training sessions","meaning":"合適的培訓課節","examples":[{"en":"Managers must select appropriate training sessions.","zh":"管理者必須選擇合適的培訓課節。"},{"en":"Appropriate training sessions are sessions that suit the learners’ needs, level, and goals.","zh":"Appropriate training sessions 是配合學習者需要、程度和目標的課節。"},{"en":"A beginner should attend an appropriate grammar session rather than an advanced writing workshop.","zh":"初學者應參加合適的文法課，而不是高階寫作工作坊。"},{"en":"If training is appropriate, participants can use the content in real work.","zh":"如果培訓合適，參加者可以在真實工作中使用內容。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses suitability.","zh":"這個片語強調合適性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"measurable follow-up","meaning":"可量度的跟進工作","examples":[{"en":"Every programme should include measurable follow-up.","zh":"每個計劃都應包括可量度的跟進工作。"},{"en":"Measurable follow-up means later checking that can be counted, compared, or evaluated.","zh":"Measurable follow-up 指之後可以計算、比較或評估的檢查。"},{"en":"A teacher may use monthly writing scores as measurable follow-up after a grammar course.","zh":"老師可能在文法課後使用每月寫作分數作為可量度的跟進。"},{"en":"If follow-up is measurable, managers can see whether behaviour actually changed.","zh":"如果跟進可量度，管理者可以看見行為是否真正改變。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses evidence after training.","zh":"這個片語強調培訓後的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be a must","meaning":"是不可或缺的","examples":[{"en":"Professional follow-up is a must after staff training.","zh":"專業跟進在員工培訓後是不可或缺的。"},{"en":"To be a must means to be necessary or extremely important.","zh":"To be a must 指必要或極其重要。"},{"en":"Reading the question carefully is a must in any exam.","zh":"在任何考試中，仔細閱讀題目是不可或缺的。"},{"en":"If training is expensive, follow-up is a must to check whether it was worthwhile.","zh":"如果培訓昂貴，跟進就是不可或缺的，以檢查它是否值得。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly states that something should not be skipped.","zh":"這個片語強烈表示某事不應被跳過。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether statements agree with the information given.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與所給資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"To agree with the information given 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"In a reading test, a statement agrees with the information if the text clearly supports it.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，如果文本清楚支持某陳述，它就與資料一致。"},{"en":"If the passage says training is costly, a statement saying it is expensive agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說培訓成本高昂，而陳述說它很昂貴，這就與資料一致。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN reading tasks.","zh":"這個片語用於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"To contradict the information 指說出與文章相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says a programme lasted two months, “it lasted two weeks” contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說計劃持續兩個月，而陳述說它持續兩星期，這就與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"When a statement contradicts the text, the answer is usually FALSE.","zh":"當陳述與文本矛盾時，答案通常是 FALSE。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct conflict with the source.","zh":"這個片語描述與來源直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"The answer is not given if there is no information on the statement.","zh":"如果文章沒有關於該陳述的資料，答案就是 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not tell us enough to decide.","zh":"No information on this 指文章沒有提供足夠內容讓我們判斷。"},{"en":"If a text mentions training cost but not staff salaries, a salary statement may be NOT GIVEN.","zh":"如果文本提到培訓成本但沒有提到員工薪酬，薪酬陳述可能是 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when there is no information in the passage.","zh":"當文章沒有資料時，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is important for avoiding unsupported answers.","zh":"這個片語對避免無根據答案很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"typical stresses","meaning":"常見壓力","examples":[{"en":"Typical stresses may arise when people with different personalities work together.","zh":"當不同性格的人一起工作時，常見壓力可能出現。"},{"en":"Typical stresses are common pressures or difficulties that often happen in a situation.","zh":"Typical stresses 是某情況中常會出現的壓力或困難。"},{"en":"Students face typical stresses before exams, such as lack of sleep and fear of failure.","zh":"學生考試前面對常見壓力，例如睡眠不足和害怕失敗。"},{"en":"If a workplace has many personalities, typical stresses may include conflict and misunderstanding.","zh":"如果工作場所中有許多性格，常見壓力可能包括衝突和誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes normal, expected sources of pressure.","zh":"這個片語描述正常、可預期的壓力來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be removed with","meaning":"可透過……消除","examples":[{"en":"The statement suggests that workplace stresses can be removed with training.","zh":"該陳述暗示工作場所壓力可透過培訓消除。"},{"en":"To be removed with something means to be taken away or solved by using that method.","zh":"To be removed with something 指使用某方法把某事移除或解決。"},{"en":"Some confusion can be removed with clearer instructions.","zh":"一些混亂可以透過更清晰指示消除。"},{"en":"If conflict is deep, training may reduce it but not remove it completely.","zh":"如果衝突很深，培訓可能減少它，但未必完全消除。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a problem with a possible solution.","zh":"這個片語把問題與可能解決方法連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"correct training","meaning":"適當培訓","examples":[{"en":"Appropriate training may reduce workplace conflict.","zh":"適當培訓可能減少工作場所衝突。"},{"en":"Correct training means training that is suitable for the real problem and the people involved.","zh":"Correct training 指適合真實問題和相關人員的培訓。"},{"en":"Correct training for new teachers may include classroom management, not only subject knowledge.","zh":"對新老師而言，適當培訓可能包括課室管理，而不只是學科知識。"},{"en":"If training targets the wrong issue, it will not reduce conflict.","zh":"如果培訓針對錯誤問題，它就不能減少衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that training must be relevant, not merely available.","zh":"這個片語強調培訓必須相關，而不只是存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"claim that","meaning":"聲稱","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Liaison Wizards claims that training increased its income.","zh":"該陳述問 Liaison Wizards 是否聲稱培訓增加了其收入。"},{"en":"To claim that means to state something as true, especially when it may need evidence.","zh":"To claim that 指聲明某事為真，尤其是可能需要證據時。"},{"en":"A company may claim that its course improves speaking confidence in one month.","zh":"公司可能聲稱其課程能在一個月內改善口語信心。"},{"en":"If a claim is not supported by the passage, students should not treat it as true.","zh":"如果主張沒有文章支持，學生不應把它視為真。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a statement that needs to be checked.","zh":"這個片語引入需要檢查的陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"increase one’s income","meaning":"增加收入","examples":[{"en":"A successful business model can increase a company’s income.","zh":"成功的商業模式可以增加公司的收入。"},{"en":"To increase one’s income means to earn more money than before.","zh":"To increase one’s income 指賺取比以前更多金錢。"},{"en":"A student may increase their income by tutoring younger pupils after school.","zh":"學生可能透過放學後補習低年級學生來增加收入。"},{"en":"If a website attracts more advertisers, it may increase the company’s income.","zh":"如果網站吸引更多廣告商，它可能增加公司收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth in money earned.","zh":"這個片語描述賺取金錢的增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"since the company started","meaning":"自公司成立以來","examples":[{"en":"The company has exceeded projections since it started operating.","zh":"自公司開始營運以來，它已超越預測。"},{"en":"Since the company started means from the time the company began until now.","zh":"Since the company started 指由公司開始至今。"},{"en":"Since the school started its reading scheme, library borrowing has increased.","zh":"自學校開始閱讀計劃以來，圖書館借書量已增加。"},{"en":"If performance has improved since the company started, the early results are positive.","zh":"如果表現自公司成立以來有所改善，早期結果就是正面的。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a time period beginning with the organisation’s launch.","zh":"這個片語標示由機構成立開始的一段時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be dogmatic","meaning":"武斷的；教條式的","examples":[{"en":"Managers who are dogmatic may ignore useful staff feedback.","zh":"武斷的管理者可能忽視有用的員工回饋。"},{"en":"To be dogmatic means to insist on one’s views too strongly and refuse to consider alternatives.","zh":"To be dogmatic 指過分堅持自己看法並拒絕考慮其他選項。"},{"en":"A teacher is dogmatic if they never accept a student’s reasonable explanation.","zh":"如果老師從不接受學生合理解釋，就是武斷的。"},{"en":"If leaders are dogmatic, consultation becomes meaningless.","zh":"如果領袖武斷，諮詢就變得沒有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rigid and closed-minded behaviour.","zh":"這個片語描述僵化和封閉的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"take advantage of staff","meaning":"利用；剝削員工","examples":[{"en":"Companies should not take advantage of their staff.","zh":"公司不應利用或剝削員工。"},{"en":"To take advantage of staff means to use employees unfairly for benefit.","zh":"To take advantage of staff 指為了利益不公平地利用員工。"},{"en":"A shop takes advantage of staff if it asks them to work extra hours without pay.","zh":"如果店舖要求員工無薪加班，就是利用員工。"},{"en":"If workers feel used, trust in management will decline.","zh":"如果工人感到被利用，他們對管理層的信任會下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unfair exploitation of employees.","zh":"這個片語描述對員工的不公平剝削。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"primarily because","meaning":"主要因為","examples":[{"en":"Internal training may succeed primarily because employees are involved.","zh":"內部培訓可能成功，主要因為員工有參與。"},{"en":"Primarily because means mainly because of one important reason.","zh":"Primarily because 指主要由於一個重要原因。"},{"en":"A student may improve primarily because they practise every day.","zh":"學生可能進步，主要因為每天練習。"},{"en":"If staff help design the programme, their involvement may be the main reason it works.","zh":"如果員工協助設計計劃，他們的參與可能是計劃有效的主要原因。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the chief cause behind a result.","zh":"這個片語指出結果背後的主要成因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"feel involved in","meaning":"覺得自己參與了……","examples":[{"en":"Employees are more motivated when they feel involved in the planning.","zh":"當員工覺得自己參與了規劃，他們會更有動力。"},{"en":"To feel involved in something means to feel included and able to contribute.","zh":"To feel involved in something 指感到被包括在內並能作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Students feel involved in a lesson when they can ask questions and choose examples.","zh":"當學生可以提問和選擇例子時，他們會覺得自己參與了課堂。"},{"en":"If staff feel involved, they may support changes more willingly.","zh":"如果員工覺得自己有參與，他們可能更願意支持改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sense of participation and ownership.","zh":"這個片語描述參與感和擁有感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"value of games","meaning":"遊戲的價值","examples":[{"en":"The value of games in staff training may be overlooked.","zh":"遊戲在員工培訓中的價值可能被忽視。"},{"en":"The value of games means the usefulness or benefit that games can provide.","zh":"Value of games 指遊戲可以提供的用處或好處。"},{"en":"In language lessons, the value of games may be that students practise without fear.","zh":"在語言課中，遊戲的價值可能是學生能不怕犯錯地練習。"},{"en":"If games build trust and communication, they have real training value.","zh":"如果遊戲建立信任和溝通，它們就有真正培訓價值。"},{"en":"This phrase asks why games are useful, not whether they are childish.","zh":"這個片語問遊戲為何有用，而不是問它們是否幼稚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"training tool","meaning":"培訓工具","examples":[{"en":"A game can be an effective training tool.","zh":"遊戲可以是有效的培訓工具。"},{"en":"A training tool is a method, activity, or resource used to help people learn.","zh":"Training tool 是用來幫助人學習的方法、活動或資源。"},{"en":"A checklist can be a training tool for students learning essay structure.","zh":"清單可以是學生學習作文結構的培訓工具。"},{"en":"If a game reveals how people cooperate, it can train more than one skill at once.","zh":"如果遊戲揭示人們如何合作，它可以同時訓練多種技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something used for learning and development.","zh":"這個片語描述用於學習和發展的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be misunderstood","meaning":"被誤解","examples":[{"en":"The purpose of informal activities can be misunderstood.","zh":"非正式活動的目的可能被誤解。"},{"en":"To be misunderstood means to be understood wrongly.","zh":"To be misunderstood 指被錯誤理解。"},{"en":"A teacher’s strict rule may be misunderstood as anger if it is not explained.","zh":"如果老師沒有解釋，嚴格規則可能被誤解為憤怒。"},{"en":"If games are not introduced clearly, staff may think they are childish.","zh":"如果遊戲沒有被清楚引入，員工可能認為它們很幼稚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes confusion between intended meaning and received meaning.","zh":"這個片語描述原意和接收意思之間的混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"list of statements","meaning":"陳述列表","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match a list of statements with the correct people.","zh":"考生把陳述列表與正確人物配對。"},{"en":"A list of statements is a set of sentences or claims given in a question.","zh":"List of statements 是題目中給出的一組句子或主張。"},{"en":"In a reading task, students should underline key words in the list of statements.","zh":"在閱讀題中，學生應在陳述列表中劃出關鍵詞。"},{"en":"If statements are paraphrased in the passage, students must match meaning rather than exact wording.","zh":"如果陳述在文章中被改寫，學生必須配對意思而不是完全相同字眼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes answer items in a matching task.","zh":"這個片語描述配對題中的答案項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"基於……","examples":[{"en":"The statements are based on information in the reading passage.","zh":"這些陳述基於閱讀篇章中的資料。"},{"en":"To be based on something means to come from or be supported by it.","zh":"To be based on something 指來自某事或由某事支持。"},{"en":"A teacher’s comments should be based on the student’s actual essay.","zh":"老師評語應基於學生的實際作文。"},{"en":"If an answer is not based on the passage, it may be marked wrong.","zh":"如果答案不是基於文章，它可能被判錯。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses using evidence as the foundation.","zh":"這個片語強調以證據作基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"match the statement with","meaning":"將陳述與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match each statement with the correct person.","zh":"考生將每項陳述與正確人物配對。"},{"en":"To match the statement with something means to connect it to the correct answer or category.","zh":"To match the statement with something 指把陳述連接到正確答案或類別。"},{"en":"Students may match a statement with the paragraph that contains the same idea.","zh":"學生可能把陳述與包含相同意思的段落配對。"},{"en":"If two people express similar views, students must read carefully before matching.","zh":"如果兩個人表達相似看法，學生配對前必須仔細閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common reading-test action.","zh":"這個片語描述常見閱讀測驗動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"use each letter more than once","meaning":"每個字母可使用多於一次","examples":[{"en":"Candidates may use each letter more than once.","zh":"考生可使用每個字母多於一次。"},{"en":"Use each letter more than once means the same answer option can be chosen for several questions.","zh":"Use each letter more than once 指同一答案選項可以用於幾條題目。"},{"en":"In a matching task, one speaker may match three different statements.","zh":"在配對題中，一位講者可能配對三項不同陳述。"},{"en":"If students assume each letter can be used only once, they may force wrong answers.","zh":"如果學生假設每個字母只能用一次，他們可能硬套錯誤答案。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds candidates that repeated answers are allowed.","zh":"這個片語提醒考生重複答案是容許的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"experience friction","meaning":"經歷摩擦","examples":[{"en":"Many companies experience friction between employees.","zh":"許多公司經歷員工之間的摩擦。"},{"en":"To experience friction means to have tension, disagreement, or conflict.","zh":"To experience friction 指出現緊張、分歧或衝突。"},{"en":"A class may experience friction when group members do not divide work fairly.","zh":"如果小組成員沒有公平分工，班級可能經歷摩擦。"},{"en":"If departments compete for resources, friction may increase.","zh":"如果部門競爭資源，摩擦可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uncomfortable human tension.","zh":"這個片語描述令人不舒服的人際緊張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be specifically tailored to","meaning":"特別度身設計以配合……","examples":[{"en":"Internal training can be specifically tailored to a company.","zh":"內部培訓可以特別度身設計以配合公司。"},{"en":"To be specifically tailored to something means to be carefully adjusted for that exact situation or group.","zh":"To be specifically tailored to something 指為該特定情況或群體仔細調整。"},{"en":"A writing course can be specifically tailored to DSE students.","zh":"寫作課程可以特別度身設計以配合 DSE 學生。"},{"en":"If training is tailored to a company, examples can match its real problems.","zh":"如果培訓度身配合公司，例子可以符合其真實問題。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses precise customisation.","zh":"這個片語強調精準客製化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"generic training","meaning":"一般化培訓","examples":[{"en":"Generic training may not address a company’s distinctive needs.","zh":"一般化培訓可能無法處理公司的獨特需要。"},{"en":"Generic training is general training not designed for one specific organisation or group.","zh":"Generic training 是不是為某一特定機構或群體設計的一般培訓。"},{"en":"A generic writing lesson may not help students with their particular grammar weaknesses.","zh":"一般化寫作課未必能幫助學生處理其特定文法弱點。"},{"en":"If a company has unusual problems, generic training may feel irrelevant.","zh":"如果公司有不尋常問題，一般化培訓可能感覺不相關。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts general training with tailored training.","zh":"這個片語把一般培訓與度身培訓作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"still being piloted","meaning":"仍在試行","examples":[{"en":"The modern training method is still being piloted.","zh":"現代培訓方法仍在試行。"},{"en":"Still being piloted means still being tested on a small scale before wider use.","zh":"Still being piloted 指在更廣泛使用前仍在小規模測試。"},{"en":"A new timetable may be still being piloted in two classes before the whole school adopts it.","zh":"新時間表可能先在兩個班級仍在試行，然後全校採用。"},{"en":"If a programme is being piloted, feedback should be collected carefully.","zh":"如果計劃正在試行，應仔細收集回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a trial stage.","zh":"這個片語描述試驗階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"bring different perspectives together","meaning":"將不同觀點結合","examples":[{"en":"Team-building exercises can bring different perspectives together.","zh":"團隊建立練習可以將不同觀點結合。"},{"en":"To bring different perspectives together means to combine different ways of seeing a problem.","zh":"To bring different perspectives together 指結合看待問題的不同方式。"},{"en":"A class discussion can bring different perspectives together when students share family, school, and community experiences.","zh":"當學生分享家庭、學校和社區經驗時，班級討論可以將不同觀點結合。"},{"en":"If departments see a problem differently, team building may help them understand the whole picture.","zh":"如果部門以不同方式看待問題，團隊建立可能幫助他們理解整體情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes combining viewpoints for better understanding.","zh":"這個片語描述為了更好理解而結合觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"positive work environment","meaning":"正面的工作環境","examples":[{"en":"Successful team relationships develop in a positive work environment.","zh":"成功的團隊關係在正面的工作環境中發展。"},{"en":"A positive work environment is a workplace where people feel respected, supported, and motivated.","zh":"Positive work environment 是令人感到被尊重、被支持和有動力的工作場所。"},{"en":"A school has a positive work environment when teachers can ask for help without embarrassment.","zh":"當老師可以不尷尬地求助時，學校就有正面的工作環境。"},{"en":"If the environment is positive, people are more willing to cooperate.","zh":"如果環境正面，人們更願意合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the conditions that help people work well.","zh":"這個片語描述幫助人們良好工作的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"lack of clarity","meaning":"缺乏清晰理解","examples":[{"en":"A lack of clarity can prevent managers from acting effectively.","zh":"缺乏清晰理解可以阻止管理者有效行動。"},{"en":"Lack of clarity means something is unclear or not well understood.","zh":"Lack of clarity 指某事不清楚或沒有被充分理解。"},{"en":"A lack of clarity in exam instructions can make students choose the wrong answer format.","zh":"考試指示缺乏清晰度可以令學生選錯答案格式。"},{"en":"If managers do not know what team building means, they may waste money on unsuitable activities.","zh":"如果管理者不知道團隊建立是甚麼意思，他們可能把錢浪費在不合適活動上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes confusion caused by unclear meaning or direction.","zh":"這個片語描述由意思或方向不清造成的混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"as to what","meaning":"關於……究竟是甚麼","examples":[{"en":"There is uncertainty as to what team building actually means.","zh":"關於團隊建立究竟是甚麼，人們存在不確定。"},{"en":"As to what means about what or concerning what.","zh":"As to what 指關於甚麼或涉及甚麼。"},{"en":"Students may be confused as to what the question is really asking.","zh":"學生可能不清楚題目究竟在問甚麼。"},{"en":"If managers are unsure as to what the goal is, planning becomes difficult.","zh":"如果管理者不確定目標究竟是甚麼，規劃就會變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the exact point of uncertainty.","zh":"這個片語引出不確定的具體點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to complete the summary using words from the passage.","zh":"考生需要使用文章中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill in missing words in a short version of the text.","zh":"To complete the summary 指在文章簡短版本中填補缺失字詞。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole summary before looking for answers.","zh":"學生應先讀完整段摘要，再尋找答案。"},{"en":"If grammar around a blank requires a noun, a verb will not fit.","zh":"如果空格附近文法需要名詞，動詞就不合適。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in reading exams.","zh":"這個片語是閱讀考試中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案應包含不多於兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must use two words or fewer.","zh":"No more than two words 指答案必須使用兩個或更少英文單詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “team goals,” it uses two words and fits the rule.","zh":"如果答案是 “team goals”，它用了兩個詞，符合規則。"},{"en":"If students write three words, they may lose the mark even if the idea is right.","zh":"如果學生寫三個詞，即使意思正確，也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit for exam answers.","zh":"這個片語為考試答案給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be considered to have","meaning":"可被視為具有……","examples":[{"en":"Team building can be considered to have several clear stages.","zh":"團隊建立可被視為具有幾個清晰階段。"},{"en":"To be considered to have something means to be thought of as possessing that feature.","zh":"To be considered to have something 指被認為擁有某種特徵。"},{"en":"A good essay can be considered to have a clear introduction, body, and conclusion.","zh":"好作文可被視為具有清晰引言、主體和結論。"},{"en":"If a process has stages, students can understand it step by step.","zh":"如果一個過程有階段，學生可以逐步理解它。"},{"en":"This phrase presents a way of analysing or classifying something.","zh":"這個片語呈現分析或分類某事的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"clear stages","meaning":"清晰階段","examples":[{"en":"The process is divided into several clear stages.","zh":"這個過程被分為幾個清晰階段。"},{"en":"Clear stages are steps that are easy to identify and follow.","zh":"Clear stages 是容易識別和跟隨的步驟。"},{"en":"A writing lesson may have clear stages: planning, drafting, editing, and checking.","zh":"寫作課可能有清晰階段：規劃、起草、修改和檢查。"},{"en":"If stages are clear, participants know what to do next.","zh":"如果階段清晰，參加者知道下一步要做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an organised process.","zh":"這個片語描述有組織的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"initially","meaning":"最初","examples":[{"en":"Initially, the team must identify its shared objectives.","zh":"最初，團隊必須識別其共同目標。"},{"en":"Initially means at the beginning or first.","zh":"Initially 指在開始時或首先。"},{"en":"Initially, students may feel nervous when speaking English in front of classmates.","zh":"最初，學生在同學面前說英語可能感到緊張。"},{"en":"If the first step is done well, later stages become easier.","zh":"如果第一步做得好，後續階段會更容易。"},{"en":"This word introduces the starting point of a process.","zh":"這個詞引出過程的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be clear as to","meaning":"清楚了解……","examples":[{"en":"Managers must be clear as to the goals of the programme.","zh":"管理者必須清楚了解該計劃的目標。"},{"en":"To be clear as to something means to understand it clearly.","zh":"To be clear as to something 指清楚理解某事。"},{"en":"Students must be clear as to whether the question asks for advantages or disadvantages.","zh":"學生必須清楚了解題目是問好處還是壞處。"},{"en":"If managers are not clear about the goals, they cannot choose suitable activities.","zh":"如果管理者不清楚目標，他們就不能選擇合適活動。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses precise understanding.","zh":"這個片語強調準確理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"the entire team","meaning":"整個團隊","examples":[{"en":"The goals should apply to the entire team.","zh":"目標應適用於整個團隊。"},{"en":"The entire team means every member of the team, not just some people.","zh":"The entire team 指團隊每一位成員，而不只是部分人。"},{"en":"A class rule applies to the entire team when every group member must follow it.","zh":"當每位小組成員都必須遵守某條規則，它就適用於整個團隊。"},{"en":"If goals include only managers, ordinary staff may feel excluded.","zh":"如果目標只包括管理者，普通員工可能感到被排除。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises full group inclusion.","zh":"這個片語強調整個群體都被包括在內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"prevent the team from","meaning":"阻礙團隊……","examples":[{"en":"Poor communication may prevent the team from achieving its aims.","zh":"欠佳溝通可能阻礙團隊達成其目標。"},{"en":"To prevent the team from doing something means to stop the team from doing it.","zh":"To prevent the team from doing something 指阻止團隊做某事。"},{"en":"Lack of planning can prevent a project group from finishing on time.","zh":"缺乏規劃可以阻礙專題小組準時完成。"},{"en":"If members do not share updates, the team may miss deadlines.","zh":"如果成員不分享更新，團隊可能錯過期限。"},{"en":"This phrase links a barrier with blocked team action.","zh":"這個片語把障礙與團隊行動受阻連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"achieve these aims","meaning":"達成這些目標","examples":[{"en":"The organisation must remove barriers to achieve these aims.","zh":"機構必須移除障礙，才能達成這些目標。"},{"en":"To achieve these aims means to reach the goals just mentioned.","zh":"To achieve these aims 指達到剛提到的目標。"},{"en":"A student may need a timetable to achieve these aims of reading more and writing better.","zh":"學生可能需要時間表來達成增加閱讀和改善寫作這些目標。"},{"en":"If barriers remain, the stated aims may not become real outcomes.","zh":"如果障礙仍存在，所述目標可能不會變成真實成果。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to goals that have already been identified.","zh":"這個片語回指已被識別的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be identified as","meaning":"被識別為……","examples":[{"en":"Barriers are identified as inhibitors within the process.","zh":"障礙在這個過程中被識別為阻礙因素。"},{"en":"To be identified as something means to be recognised or classified as that thing.","zh":"To be identified as something 指被認出或歸類為某事物。"},{"en":"A repeated grammar mistake may be identified as a weakness in sentence structure.","zh":"反覆文法錯誤可能被識別為句子結構弱點。"},{"en":"If poor communication is identified as a barrier, training can target it directly.","zh":"如果欠佳溝通被識別為障礙，培訓可以直接針對它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes naming or classifying a problem.","zh":"這個片語描述命名或分類問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be addressed by","meaning":"透過……處理","examples":[{"en":"The barriers are addressed by introducing positive alternatives.","zh":"這些障礙透過引入正面替代方法處理。"},{"en":"To be addressed by something means to be dealt with or improved through that method.","zh":"To be addressed by something 指透過某方法處理或改善。"},{"en":"A student’s weak vocabulary can be addressed by regular reading and review.","zh":"學生詞彙薄弱可以透過定期閱讀和溫習處理。"},{"en":"If the barrier is mistrust, it may be addressed by honest discussion.","zh":"如果障礙是不信任，它可能透過坦誠討論處理。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a problem with the action used to handle it.","zh":"這個片語把問題與處理它的行動連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"introduce enablers","meaning":"引入促進因素","examples":[{"en":"The next stage is to introduce enablers that support progress.","zh":"下一階段是引入支援進展的促進因素。"},{"en":"To introduce enablers means to bring in things that help people succeed.","zh":"To introduce enablers 指引入幫助人成功的事物。"},{"en":"A teacher may introduce checklists as enablers for weak writers.","zh":"老師可能引入清單作為寫作較弱學生的促進因素。"},{"en":"If meetings are confusing, a clear agenda can be introduced as an enabler.","zh":"如果會議混亂，清晰議程可以作為促進因素被引入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding support rather than only removing problems.","zh":"這個片語描述加入支援，而不只是移除問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"cooperative relationship","meaning":"合作關係","examples":[{"en":"Humour can help build a cooperative relationship.","zh":"幽默可以幫助建立合作關係。"},{"en":"A cooperative relationship is a relationship in which people work together willingly and helpfully.","zh":"Cooperative relationship 是人們願意並有幫助地一起工作的關係。"},{"en":"A teacher and parent need a cooperative relationship to support a struggling student.","zh":"老師和家長需要合作關係來支援有困難的學生。"},{"en":"If people trust one another, cooperation becomes easier.","zh":"如果人們互相信任，合作會變得更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a relationship based on shared effort rather than conflict.","zh":"這個片語描述基於共同努力而不是衝突的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be quantified","meaning":"被量化","examples":[{"en":"The success of a programme should be quantified.","zh":"計劃的成功應被量化。"},{"en":"To be quantified means to be measured or expressed in numbers.","zh":"To be quantified 指被量度或以數字表示。"},{"en":"A school may quantify improvement by comparing test scores before and after a course.","zh":"學校可能透過比較課程前後測驗分數來量化進步。"},{"en":"If success is quantified, managers can judge results more objectively.","zh":"如果成功被量化，管理者可以更客觀判斷結果。"},{"en":"This phrase turns a general idea into measurable evidence.","zh":"這個片語把一般想法變成可量度證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be continually monitored","meaning":"被持續監察","examples":[{"en":"The results should be continually monitored.","zh":"結果應被持續監察。"},{"en":"To be continually monitored means to be checked regularly over time.","zh":"To be continually monitored 指隨時間定期被檢查。"},{"en":"A student’s reading speed may be continually monitored during a ten-week course.","zh":"學生的閱讀速度可能在十週課程期間被持續監察。"},{"en":"If results are monitored continuously, problems can be found early.","zh":"如果結果被持續監察，問題可以及早被發現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing observation rather than a single check.","zh":"這個片語描述持續觀察，而不是一次性檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 8 - TEAM BUILDING.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 9":[{"front":"problem solving and decision making","meaning":"解決問題和作出決策","examples":[{"en":"Problem solving and decision making are essential skills in business.","zh":"解決問題和作出決策是商業中的基本技能。"},{"en":"Problem solving and decision making mean finding solutions and choosing what action to take.","zh":"problem solving and decision making 指找出解決方案並選擇採取甚麼行動。"},{"en":"A student uses problem solving and decision making when choosing how to finish a group project.","zh":"學生選擇如何完成小組專題時，就是在運用解決問題和作出決策的能力。"},{"en":"Good problem solving and decision making can prevent small issues from becoming serious.","zh":"良好的解決問題和決策能力可以防止小問題變嚴重。"},{"en":"Without these skills, people may react emotionally instead of acting wisely.","zh":"沒有這些技能，人們可能會情緒化反應，而不是明智行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the business world","meaning":"商業世界","examples":[{"en":"Managers face many challenges in the business world.","zh":"經理在商業世界中面對許多挑戰。"},{"en":"The business world refers to companies, workplaces, markets and commercial decisions.","zh":"the business world 指公司、工作場所、市場和商業決策。"},{"en":"In the business world, a poor decision can affect customers, workers and profit.","zh":"在商業世界中，錯誤決定可以影響顧客、員工和利潤。"},{"en":"Competition in the business world forces companies to improve their services.","zh":"商業世界中的競爭迫使公司改善服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing work, management and commerce.","zh":"討論工作、管理和商業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"much as in life in general","meaning":"與日常生活大致一樣","examples":[{"en":"Much as in life in general, business involves difficult choices.","zh":"與日常生活大致一樣，商業涉及艱難選擇。"},{"en":"Much as in life in general means in a way similar to ordinary life.","zh":"much as in life in general 指與普通生活相似。"},{"en":"Much as in life in general, school leadership involves listening, planning and compromise.","zh":"與日常生活大致一樣，學校領導涉及聆聽、規劃和妥協。"},{"en":"The phrase connects business problems with everyday human decisions.","zh":"這個短語把商業問題與日常人類決定連接起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing that a business idea also applies to normal life.","zh":"當要顯示某商業概念同樣適用於正常生活時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"challenges that need to be faced","meaning":"需要面對的挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Every organisation encounters challenges that need to be faced.","zh":"每個組織都會遇到需要面對的挑戰。"},{"en":"Challenges that need to be faced are difficulties that cannot be ignored.","zh":"challenges that need to be faced 指不能被忽視的困難。"},{"en":"A school with falling results has challenges that need to be faced by teachers and parents.","zh":"成績下降的學校有老師和家長需要面對的挑戰。"},{"en":"If challenges are not faced early, they may grow into larger problems.","zh":"如果挑戰沒有及早面對，它們可能變成更大問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when action and responsibility are required.","zh":"當需要行動和責任時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"problems that need solutions","meaning":"需要解決方案的問題","examples":[{"en":"Managers regularly deal with problems that need solutions.","zh":"經理經常處理需要解決方案的問題。"},{"en":"Problems that need solutions are issues requiring practical answers or action.","zh":"problems that need solutions 指需要實際答案或行動的問題。"},{"en":"A broken lift is a problem that needs a solution because residents cannot use the building easily.","zh":"壞掉的升降機是需要解決方案的問題，因為居民不能方便使用大廈。"},{"en":"Problems that need solutions should be understood before people rush to act.","zh":"需要解決方案的問題應先被理解，然後人們才採取行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a difficulty must be fixed, not just discussed.","zh":"當困難必須被修正，而不只是被討論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"decisions that need to be made","meaning":"需要作出的決定","examples":[{"en":"Some decisions need to be made quickly but carefully.","zh":"有些決定需要迅速但小心地作出。"},{"en":"Decisions that need to be made are choices that cannot be postponed forever.","zh":"decisions that need to be made 指不能永遠推遲的選擇。"},{"en":"A family facing a medical emergency has decisions that need to be made immediately.","zh":"面對醫療緊急情況的家庭有需要立即作出的決定。"},{"en":"Delaying important decisions can increase confusion and stress.","zh":"拖延重要決定可能增加混亂和壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when action depends on choosing between options.","zh":"當行動取決於在選項之間作選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"act upon a decision","meaning":"按決定採取行動","examples":[{"en":"A decision is useful only when managers act upon it.","zh":"只有當經理按決定採取行動時，決定才有用。"},{"en":"Act upon a decision means take real action after choosing what to do.","zh":"act upon a decision 指在選擇做法後真正採取行動。"},{"en":"If a school decides to improve reading, it must act upon the decision by changing lessons.","zh":"如果學校決定改善閱讀，就必須透過改變課堂來按決定採取行動。"},{"en":"A decision without action rarely solves the original problem.","zh":"沒有行動的決定很少能解決原本問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a choice must be put into practice.","zh":"當選擇必須被實行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"over recent years","meaning":"近年來","examples":[{"en":"Over recent years, researchers have examined business decision making.","zh":"近年來，研究人員研究了商業決策。"},{"en":"Over recent years means during the last several years.","zh":"over recent years 指在過去數年間。"},{"en":"Over recent years, many schools have used more online learning tools.","zh":"近年來，許多學校使用了更多網上學習工具。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a trend developing across a period of time.","zh":"這個短語顯示某趨勢在一段時間內形成。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing recent changes, research or patterns.","zh":"討論近期變化、研究或模式時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the psychology behind","meaning":"……背後的心理","examples":[{"en":"The course examines the psychology behind managerial decisions.","zh":"這門課研究管理決策背後的心理。"},{"en":"The psychology behind something means the mental processes, feelings and beliefs that influence it.","zh":"psychology behind something 指影響某事的心理過程、感受和信念。"},{"en":"Teachers study the psychology behind exam anxiety to support students better.","zh":"老師研究考試焦慮背後的心理，以更好支援學生。"},{"en":"Understanding psychology helps explain why people do not always choose logically.","zh":"理解心理有助解釋為何人們不總是合乎邏輯地選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when hidden mental reasons matter.","zh":"當隱藏心理原因很重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in a business context","meaning":"在商業環境中","examples":[{"en":"Problem-solving strategies may work differently in a business context.","zh":"解決問題策略在商業環境中可能有不同運作方式。"},{"en":"In a business context means in a situation involving companies, work or commercial decisions.","zh":"in a business context 指在涉及公司、工作或商業決策的情況中。"},{"en":"Honesty matters in daily life, but it also matters in a business context when customers trust a brand.","zh":"誠實在日常生活中重要，在顧客信任品牌的商業環境中也重要。"},{"en":"A strategy that works at home may need adjustment in a business context.","zh":"在家中有效的策略，在商業環境中可能需要調整。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when applying an idea specifically to business.","zh":"當把概念特別應用於商業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be analysed and taught","meaning":"被分析和教授","examples":[{"en":"Decision-making psychology is analysed and taught at universities.","zh":"決策心理學在大學中被分析和教授。"},{"en":"Be analysed and taught means be studied carefully and then explained to learners.","zh":"be analysed and taught 指被仔細研究，然後向學習者解釋。"},{"en":"Good writing can be analysed and taught through examples of structure and word choice.","zh":"良好寫作可以透過結構和用詞例子被分析和教授。"},{"en":"When a skill is analysed and taught, students can learn it more systematically.","zh":"當一項技能被分析和教授，學生就能更有系統地學習。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when practical behaviour becomes an academic subject.","zh":"當實際行為變成學術科目時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"at a tertiary level","meaning":"在大專程度","examples":[{"en":"Business psychology is often taught at a tertiary level.","zh":"商業心理學常在大專程度教授。"},{"en":"At a tertiary level means at college, university or other post-secondary education level.","zh":"at a tertiary level 指在學院、大學或其他中學後教育程度。"},{"en":"Academic research methods are usually taught at a tertiary level rather than in primary school.","zh":"學術研究方法通常在大專程度教授，而不是在小學教授。"},{"en":"Subjects become more specialised at a tertiary level.","zh":"科目在大專程度會變得更專門。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing higher education.","zh":"討論高等教育時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"senior lecturer","meaning":"高級講師","examples":[{"en":"Marie Scrive is a senior lecturer at Carling University.","zh":"Marie Scrive 是 Carling University 的高級講師。"},{"en":"A senior lecturer is an experienced university teacher with an established academic role.","zh":"senior lecturer 指有經驗、具正式學術職位的大學教師。"},{"en":"A senior lecturer may teach courses, supervise students and conduct research.","zh":"高級講師可能教授課程、指導學生並進行研究。"},{"en":"Senior lecturers often explain complex ideas through lectures and seminars.","zh":"高級講師常透過講座和研討課解釋複雜概念。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying an academic position.","zh":"識別學術職位時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"poor management skills","meaning":"欠佳的管理技巧","examples":[{"en":"Poor management skills can damage an organisation’s performance.","zh":"欠佳的管理技巧可以損害組織表現。"},{"en":"Poor management skills are weak abilities in planning, leading, communicating or making decisions.","zh":"poor management skills 指規劃、領導、溝通或決策方面能力薄弱。"},{"en":"A manager with poor management skills may confuse staff with unclear instructions.","zh":"管理技巧欠佳的經理可能用不清晰指示令員工混亂。"},{"en":"Poor management skills can lower morale and reduce productivity.","zh":"欠佳的管理技巧可以降低士氣並減少生產力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when leadership weaknesses cause workplace problems.","zh":"當領導弱點造成工作場所問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be identified in","meaning":"可在……中識別出來","examples":[{"en":"Weak leadership can be identified in many areas of management.","zh":"薄弱領導可在多個管理範疇中識別出來。"},{"en":"Be identified in means be recognised or found within a particular place, field or situation.","zh":"be identified in 指在某地方、領域或情況中被認出或發現。"},{"en":"Common grammar mistakes can be identified in students’ essays.","zh":"常見文法錯誤可在學生作文中識別出來。"},{"en":"Problems must be identified before they can be properly solved.","zh":"問題必須先被識別，才可以被妥善解決。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when detecting where something appears.","zh":"偵測某事出現在哪裏時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in many arenas","meaning":"在多個範疇","examples":[{"en":"Poor management skills appear in many arenas.","zh":"欠佳的管理技巧出現在多個範疇。"},{"en":"In many arenas means in many areas, fields or situations.","zh":"in many arenas 指在許多領域、範疇或情況中。"},{"en":"Communication skills matter in many arenas, from school to customer service.","zh":"溝通技巧在多個範疇都重要，從學校到客戶服務皆然。"},{"en":"A weakness may be serious if it appears in many arenas rather than one small area.","zh":"如果弱點出現在多個範疇，而不是一個小範圍，它可能很嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one issue appears across different contexts.","zh":"當一個問題出現在不同情境時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"few are as illustrative as","meaning":"很少有……像……般具代表性","examples":[{"en":"Few skills are as illustrative as the ability to make sound judgements.","zh":"很少有技能像作出穩妥判斷的能力般具代表性。"},{"en":"Few are as illustrative as means few examples show the point as clearly as this one.","zh":"few are as illustrative as 指很少例子能像這個例子一樣清楚說明重點。"},{"en":"Few school problems are as illustrative as poor attendance when discussing student motivation.","zh":"討論學生動機時，很少有學校問題像低出席率般具代表性。"},{"en":"A clear example helps people understand a wider problem quickly.","zh":"清楚例子幫助人快速理解更廣泛問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one example strongly represents a bigger issue.","zh":"當一個例子強烈代表更大議題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"make accurate judgements about","meaning":"對……作出準確判斷","examples":[{"en":"Good managers make accurate judgements about possible solutions.","zh":"優秀經理會對可能解決方案作出準確判斷。"},{"en":"Make accurate judgements about means assess something correctly based on evidence.","zh":"make accurate judgements about 指根據證據正確評估某事。"},{"en":"A doctor must make accurate judgements about symptoms before choosing treatment.","zh":"醫生在選擇治療前，必須對症狀作出準確判斷。"},{"en":"Accurate judgements reduce the chance of choosing a weak solution.","zh":"準確判斷可減少選擇薄弱方案的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when careful evaluation is needed.","zh":"當需要仔細評估時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a course of action","meaning":"行動方案","examples":[{"en":"The team must agree on an appropriate course of action.","zh":"團隊必須就適當的行動方案達成一致。"},{"en":"A course of action is a planned way of dealing with a situation.","zh":"course of action 指處理某情況的計劃方法。"},{"en":"If a student is often late, the school needs a course of action, such as meeting the parents.","zh":"如果學生經常遲到，學校需要一個行動方案，例如約見家長。"},{"en":"A clear course of action helps people know what to do next.","zh":"清晰行動方案幫助人知道下一步做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when moving from discussion to practical steps.","zh":"當由討論轉向實際步驟時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"overcome an obstacle","meaning":"克服障礙","examples":[{"en":"Managers need a clear strategy to overcome an obstacle.","zh":"經理需要清晰策略來克服障礙。"},{"en":"Overcome an obstacle means deal successfully with something that blocks progress.","zh":"overcome an obstacle 指成功處理阻礙進展的事物。"},{"en":"A student may overcome an obstacle in maths by asking for extra practice.","zh":"學生可能透過要求額外練習來克服數學障礙。"},{"en":"Obstacles become easier to overcome when people understand what is causing them.","zh":"當人們理解障礙成因，障礙就更容易克服。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when difficulty stands in the way of a goal.","zh":"當困難阻礙目標時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a tendency for","meaning":"有……的傾向","examples":[{"en":"There is a tendency for managers to make decisions too quickly.","zh":"經理有過快作決定的傾向。"},{"en":"A tendency for means a common habit or pattern that often happens.","zh":"tendency for 指常見習慣或經常出現的模式。"},{"en":"There is a tendency for tired students to make careless mistakes.","zh":"疲倦學生有犯粗心錯誤的傾向。"},{"en":"A tendency can be harmful if people do not notice and correct it.","zh":"如果人們沒有注意並修正某傾向，它可能有害。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing repeated behaviour.","zh":"描述重複行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"make decisions quickly","meaning":"迅速作出決定","examples":[{"en":"Pressure can cause managers to make decisions quickly.","zh":"壓力可以令經理迅速作出決定。"},{"en":"Make decisions quickly means choose what to do in a short time.","zh":"make decisions quickly 指在短時間內選擇做甚麼。"},{"en":"A nurse may need to make decisions quickly in an emergency.","zh":"護士在緊急情況下可能需要迅速作出決定。"},{"en":"Quick decisions can be helpful, but they may be risky without enough information.","zh":"快速決定可以有幫助，但若資料不足也可能有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when time pressure affects judgement.","zh":"當時間壓力影響判斷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"Rushed decisions can lead to ineffective solutions.","zh":"倉促決定可能導致無效解決方案。"},{"en":"Lead to means cause something to happen as a result.","zh":"lead to 指造成某結果發生。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can lead to lower concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致課堂專注力下降。"},{"en":"In business, weak planning can lead to wasted money and unhappy customers.","zh":"在商業中，薄弱規劃可以導致金錢浪費和顧客不滿。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining cause and effect.","zh":"解釋因果關係時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"short-term solutions","meaning":"短期解決方案","examples":[{"en":"Short-term solutions may not address the underlying problem.","zh":"短期解決方案未必處理根本問題。"},{"en":"Short-term solutions are quick fixes that solve an immediate issue but may not last.","zh":"short-term solutions 指能處理眼前問題但未必持久的快速補救方法。"},{"en":"Giving a tired student coffee is a short-term solution if the real problem is lack of sleep.","zh":"如果真正問題是睡眠不足，給疲倦學生咖啡只是短期解決方案。"},{"en":"Short-term solutions can be useful in emergencies but dangerous if treated as final answers.","zh":"短期解決方案在緊急情況下可以有用，但若被當成最終答案就危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a fix works only for now.","zh":"當補救方法只暫時有效時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a recurrence of the problem","meaning":"問題再次出現","examples":[{"en":"A temporary solution may result in a recurrence of the problem.","zh":"暫時解決方案可能導致問題再次出現。"},{"en":"A recurrence of the problem means the same problem happens again after seeming to disappear.","zh":"recurrence of the problem 指同一問題看似消失後再次發生。"},{"en":"If a leaking roof is only painted over, there may be a recurrence of the problem after rain.","zh":"如果漏水屋頂只是被重新粉刷，下雨後問題可能再次出現。"},{"en":"Recurrence often means the root cause was not solved.","zh":"問題再次出現通常表示根本原因未被解決。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a problem returns.","zh":"當問題回來時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at a later date","meaning":"日後","examples":[{"en":"The same difficulty may return at a later date.","zh":"同一困難日後可能再次出現。"},{"en":"At a later date means at some future time.","zh":"at a later date 指在將來某個時間。"},{"en":"A meeting may be postponed and held at a later date.","zh":"會議可能被延期，日後再舉行。"},{"en":"If a problem is ignored now, it may become more expensive at a later date.","zh":"如果問題現在被忽視，日後可能變得更昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something happens after the present moment.","zh":"當某事在現在之後發生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pressure from","meaning":"來自……的壓力","examples":[{"en":"Pressure from senior staff can influence middle managers.","zh":"來自高級職員的壓力可以影響中層管理人員。"},{"en":"Pressure from means stress or influence coming from a person, group or situation.","zh":"pressure from 指來自某人、群體或情況的壓力或影響。"},{"en":"Students may feel pressure from parents before important exams.","zh":"學生在重要考試前可能感到來自父母的壓力。"},{"en":"Pressure from above can make people rush decisions they should examine carefully.","zh":"來自上級的壓力可以令人倉促作出本應仔細檢視的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when outside influence affects behaviour.","zh":"當外來影響改變行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"senior staff","meaning":"高級職員","examples":[{"en":"Senior staff may expect managers to respond immediately.","zh":"高級職員可能期望經理立即回應。"},{"en":"Senior staff are higher-ranking employees with more authority or responsibility.","zh":"senior staff 指職級較高、權力或責任較大的員工。"},{"en":"Senior staff in a school may include the principal and department heads.","zh":"學校中的高級職員可能包括校長和科主任。"},{"en":"Their expectations can shape how quickly junior staff act.","zh":"他們的期望可以影響下級員工行動的速度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing workplace hierarchy.","zh":"討論工作場所階級時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"middle management","meaning":"中層管理人員","examples":[{"en":"People in middle management often face pressure from several directions.","zh":"中層管理人員常面對來自多方面的壓力。"},{"en":"Middle management refers to managers between senior leaders and frontline staff.","zh":"middle management 指位於高層領導和前線員工之間的管理人員。"},{"en":"A department manager in a shop may be part of middle management.","zh":"商店部門經理可能屬於中層管理人員。"},{"en":"Middle management can be stressful because it must satisfy both bosses and workers.","zh":"中層管理可以很有壓力，因為它必須同時滿足上司和員工。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing managers caught between levels.","zh":"討論夾在不同層級之間的經理時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"react at speed to","meaning":"迅速回應……","examples":[{"en":"Some managers react at speed to a problem without examining it fully.","zh":"有些經理在未完全檢視問題前，就迅速回應問題。"},{"en":"React at speed to means respond very quickly to something.","zh":"react at speed to 指非常快速地回應某事。"},{"en":"A driver must react at speed to a child running into the road.","zh":"司機必須迅速回應衝出馬路的孩子。"},{"en":"Quick reaction is useful in emergencies, but business problems often need more analysis.","zh":"快速反應在緊急情況下有用，但商業問題通常需要更多分析。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when speed may help or harm judgement.","zh":"當速度可能幫助或損害判斷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be better solved by","meaning":"採用……會更妥善解決","examples":[{"en":"The issue would be better solved by a calmer approach.","zh":"這個問題採用較冷靜的方法會更妥善解決。"},{"en":"Be better solved by means would be handled more effectively through a particular method.","zh":"be better solved by 指透過某特定方法會更有效地處理。"},{"en":"A class conflict may be better solved by discussion than by punishment alone.","zh":"班級衝突透過討論可能比單靠懲罰更妥善解決。"},{"en":"Some problems are better solved by patience because rushing hides the real cause.","zh":"有些問題採用耐心方法會更好，因為倉促會掩蓋真正原因。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing solution methods.","zh":"比較解決方法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"calmer management style","meaning":"較冷靜的管理方式","examples":[{"en":"A calmer management style may produce a better decision.","zh":"較冷靜的管理方式可能產生更好的決定。"},{"en":"A calmer management style is a way of leading that avoids panic and emotional reaction.","zh":"calmer management style 指避免恐慌和情緒化反應的領導方式。"},{"en":"A calm manager listens before speaking when staff are upset.","zh":"當員工不滿時，冷靜的經理會先聆聽再說話。"},{"en":"Calm management reduces conflict because people feel heard rather than attacked.","zh":"冷靜管理減少衝突，因為人們感到被聆聽，而不是被攻擊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when leadership tone affects outcomes.","zh":"當領導語氣影響結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"inclusive style of management","meaning":"共融的管理方式","examples":[{"en":"An inclusive style of management considers different viewpoints.","zh":"共融的管理方式會考慮不同觀點。"},{"en":"An inclusive style of management invites input from different people before decisions are made.","zh":"inclusive style of management 指在作決定前邀請不同人士提供意見。"},{"en":"A school principal uses an inclusive style when teachers, students and parents are consulted.","zh":"當校長諮詢老師、學生和家長，就是使用共融的管理方式。"},{"en":"Inclusion can improve decisions because hidden problems may be noticed by frontline staff.","zh":"共融可以改善決策，因為前線員工可能注意到隱藏問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when leadership values participation.","zh":"當領導重視參與時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the root of the issue","meaning":"問題的根源","examples":[{"en":"Martin believes that the root of the issue is poor problem definition.","zh":"Martin 認為問題的根源是問題定義不清。"},{"en":"The root of the issue is the deepest or main cause of a problem.","zh":"root of the issue 指問題最深層或最主要的成因。"},{"en":"If students keep failing vocabulary tests, the root of the issue may be weak revision habits.","zh":"如果學生一直在詞彙測驗中失敗，問題的根源可能是溫習習慣薄弱。"},{"en":"Solving surface symptoms will not help if the root of the issue remains.","zh":"如果問題根源仍在，解決表面症狀也沒有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when looking for the real cause.","zh":"尋找真正原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the speed at which","meaning":"……的速度","examples":[{"en":"The problem is not always the speed at which managers respond.","zh":"問題不總是在於經理回應的速度。"},{"en":"The speed at which means how fast something happens.","zh":"speed at which 指某事發生得有多快。"},{"en":"The speed at which students read can affect how much they understand.","zh":"學生閱讀的速度可以影響他們理解多少。"},{"en":"Fast response is not always bad, but speed must be matched with accuracy.","zh":"快速回應不一定壞，但速度必須配合準確性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when measuring how quickly an action occurs.","zh":"衡量某行動發生得多快時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a response is required","meaning":"需要作出回應","examples":[{"en":"Managers may face situations in which an immediate response is required.","zh":"經理可能面對需要立即作出回應的情況。"},{"en":"A response is required means action, an answer or a reaction is needed.","zh":"a response is required 指需要行動、答案或反應。"},{"en":"If a fire alarm rings, a response is required from everyone in the building.","zh":"如果火警鐘響起，大廈內每個人都需要作出回應。"},{"en":"Some situations require quick response because delay can cause harm.","zh":"有些情況需要快速回應，因為拖延可能造成傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when silence or inaction is not acceptable.","zh":"當沉默或不行動不可接受時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a flawed way of looking at","meaning":"看待……的錯誤方式","examples":[{"en":"A flawed way of looking at the problem can produce repeated failure.","zh":"看待問題的錯誤方式可以造成反覆失敗。"},{"en":"A flawed way of looking at something is an incorrect or incomplete way of understanding it.","zh":"flawed way of looking at something 指對某事不正確或不完整的理解方式。"},{"en":"Thinking a quiet student is lazy may be a flawed way of looking at anxiety.","zh":"認為安靜學生懶惰，可能是看待焦慮的錯誤方式。"},{"en":"A flawed view leads to poor solutions because the real issue is missed.","zh":"錯誤看法會導致差劣解決方案，因為真正問題被錯過。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when wrong interpretation causes bad decisions.","zh":"當錯誤理解造成錯誤決策時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"from the outset","meaning":"從一開始","examples":[{"en":"The problem should be examined carefully from the outset.","zh":"問題應從一開始就被仔細檢視。"},{"en":"From the outset means from the very beginning.","zh":"from the outset 指從最開始。"},{"en":"A project works better if responsibilities are clear from the outset.","zh":"如果責任從一開始就清楚，項目會運作得更好。"},{"en":"Mistakes made from the outset can shape the whole process badly.","zh":"從一開始犯下的錯誤可能嚴重影響整個過程。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when early planning matters.","zh":"當早期規劃很重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"repetitive problems","meaning":"反覆出現的問題","examples":[{"en":"Repetitive problems often indicate that the original cause remains unresolved.","zh":"反覆出現的問題通常表示原本原因仍未解決。"},{"en":"Repetitive problems are problems that happen again and again.","zh":"repetitive problems 指一次又一次發生的問題。"},{"en":"If a computer keeps crashing every week, the office has a repetitive problem.","zh":"如果電腦每星期都死機，辦公室就有一個反覆出現的問題。"},{"en":"Repetition suggests that previous solutions may have treated symptoms, not causes.","zh":"反覆出現暗示之前的解決方法可能只是處理症狀，而非原因。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the same difficulty keeps returning.","zh":"當同一困難不斷回來時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be permanently resolved","meaning":"獲得永久解決","examples":[{"en":"The problem was never permanently resolved.","zh":"這個問題從未獲得永久解決。"},{"en":"Be permanently resolved means be solved fully so that it does not keep returning.","zh":"be permanently resolved 指被完全解決，以致不再反覆出現。"},{"en":"A leaking pipe is permanently resolved only when the broken part is repaired.","zh":"漏水水管只有在破損部分被修好時，才算獲得永久解決。"},{"en":"Temporary action may reduce pressure without permanently resolving the issue.","zh":"暫時行動可能減輕壓力，但未必永久解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a solution must last.","zh":"當解決方案必須持久時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a lack of focus","meaning":"缺乏焦點","examples":[{"en":"A lack of focus can prevent managers from identifying the real issue.","zh":"缺乏焦點可以阻止經理識別真正問題。"},{"en":"A lack of focus means not paying clear attention to the main point.","zh":"lack of focus 指沒有清楚集中於重點。"},{"en":"A student’s essay may lose marks because of a lack of focus on the question.","zh":"學生作文可能因缺乏對題目的焦點而失分。"},{"en":"Lack of focus wastes time because people discuss side issues instead of the real problem.","zh":"缺乏焦點會浪費時間，因為人們討論旁枝問題而非真正問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when attention is scattered.","zh":"當注意力分散時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the true nature of","meaning":"……的真正本質","examples":[{"en":"Managers must understand the true nature of the problem.","zh":"經理必須理解問題的真正本質。"},{"en":"The true nature of something is what it really is, beyond first appearances.","zh":"true nature of something 指某事在表面之外真正是甚麼。"},{"en":"A child’s anger may hide the true nature of the problem, such as fear or tiredness.","zh":"孩子的憤怒可能掩蓋問題的真正本質，例如恐懼或疲倦。"},{"en":"Understanding the true nature of an issue helps people choose the right solution.","zh":"理解問題的真正本質有助人選擇正確解決方案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when surface appearances may mislead.","zh":"當表面現象可能誤導時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"advocate a system","meaning":"提倡一套制度","examples":[{"en":"Hewings advocates a system based on careful questioning.","zh":"Hewings 提倡一套以仔細提問為基礎的制度。"},{"en":"Advocate a system means publicly support or recommend an organised method.","zh":"advocate a system 指公開支持或建議一套有組織的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may advocate a system of weekly revision instead of last-minute cramming.","zh":"老師可能提倡一套每週溫習制度，而不是臨急抱佛腳。"},{"en":"People advocate systems when they believe structure improves results.","zh":"當人們相信結構能改善結果，就會提倡制度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone recommends a method.","zh":"當某人建議一種方法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a system whereby","meaning":"一套讓……的制度","examples":[{"en":"He proposes a system whereby each problem is clearly defined.","zh":"他提出一套讓每個問題被清楚界定的制度。"},{"en":"A system whereby means a system in which something happens in a particular way.","zh":"system whereby 指一套在其中某事以特定方式發生的制度。"},{"en":"A school may use a system whereby students book consultation times online.","zh":"學校可能使用一套讓學生網上預約諮詢時間的制度。"},{"en":"Such a system makes procedures clearer because everyone follows the same process.","zh":"這類制度令程序更清楚，因為每個人都跟隨同一流程。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how a system works.","zh":"解釋制度如何運作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be clearly defined","meaning":"被清楚界定","examples":[{"en":"The problem must be clearly defined before action is taken.","zh":"問題必須在採取行動前被清楚界定。"},{"en":"Be clearly defined means be described in a precise and understandable way.","zh":"be clearly defined 指被精確而易明地描述。"},{"en":"A homework task should be clearly defined so students know what to submit.","zh":"功課任務應被清楚界定，讓學生知道要提交甚麼。"},{"en":"Clear definition prevents people from solving the wrong problem.","zh":"清楚界定可防止人們解決錯誤問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when clarity is needed before action.","zh":"當行動前需要清晰時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"appropriate course of action","meaning":"適當的行動方案","examples":[{"en":"A clear definition helps managers choose the appropriate course of action.","zh":"清楚定義幫助經理選擇適當的行動方案。"},{"en":"An appropriate course of action is the right practical step for a particular situation.","zh":"appropriate course of action 指適合某特定情況的正確實際步驟。"},{"en":"If a child is sick, the appropriate course of action may be to call a doctor.","zh":"如果孩子生病，適當的行動方案可能是致電醫生。"},{"en":"The best course of action depends on the real cause, not just the visible symptom.","zh":"最佳行動方案取決於真正原因，而不只是可見症狀。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when choosing a suitable response.","zh":"選擇合適回應時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be decided upon","meaning":"被決定","examples":[{"en":"No solution should be decided upon before the problem is understood.","zh":"在問題被理解前，不應決定任何解決方案。"},{"en":"Be decided upon means be chosen after consideration or discussion.","zh":"be decided upon 指經考慮或討論後被選定。"},{"en":"The date of a school trip should be decided upon after checking weather and transport.","zh":"學校旅行日期應在檢查天氣和交通後被決定。"},{"en":"Decisions made too early may ignore important information.","zh":"太早作出的決定可能忽略重要資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a final choice is being made.","zh":"當作出最終選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"apply questions to","meaning":"向……提出問題","examples":[{"en":"Managers can apply a series of questions to the problem.","zh":"經理可以向問題提出一系列問題。"},{"en":"Apply questions to means use questions to examine or analyse something.","zh":"apply questions to 指使用問題來檢視或分析某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may apply questions to a poem to help students understand its meaning.","zh":"老師可能向一首詩提出問題，以幫助學生理解意思。"},{"en":"Good questions reveal causes, people involved and possible solutions.","zh":"好問題揭示原因、涉事者和可能解決方案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when careful questioning is used as a method.","zh":"當仔細提問被用作方法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the problem itself","meaning":"問題本身","examples":[{"en":"The questions should focus on the problem itself.","zh":"這些問題應集中於問題本身。"},{"en":"The problem itself means the actual issue, not surrounding blame, emotion or distraction.","zh":"problem itself 指實際問題，而不是周圍的責怪、情緒或干擾。"},{"en":"In a family argument, focusing on the problem itself may prevent personal attacks.","zh":"在家庭爭執中，集中於問題本身可能防止人身攻擊。"},{"en":"People solve issues better when they separate the problem from the people involved.","zh":"當人們把問題與涉事者分開，他們能更好解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when attention must return to the real issue.","zh":"當注意力必須回到真正問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"why something is happening","meaning":"某事為何發生","examples":[{"en":"Managers should ask why the problem is happening.","zh":"經理應問問題為何發生。"},{"en":"Why something is happening means the reason or cause behind an event.","zh":"why something is happening 指事件背後的理由或原因。"},{"en":"If students are late, teachers should ask why it is happening before punishing them.","zh":"如果學生遲到，老師應先問為何會這樣發生，再懲罰他們。"},{"en":"Asking why helps reveal hidden causes rather than surface symptoms.","zh":"問為何有助揭示隱藏原因，而不是表面症狀。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when cause matters more than immediate reaction.","zh":"當原因比即時反應更重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"with whom something is happening","meaning":"某事涉及哪些人","examples":[{"en":"It may also be useful to identify with whom the problem is happening.","zh":"識別問題涉及哪些人也可能有用。"},{"en":"With whom something is happening means which people are involved in the situation.","zh":"with whom something is happening 指哪些人牽涉在情況之中。"},{"en":"A teacher asks with whom the conflict is happening before arranging a meeting.","zh":"老師在安排會議前，會問衝突涉及哪些人。"},{"en":"Knowing who is involved helps managers understand relationships and responsibilities.","zh":"知道誰牽涉其中，有助經理理解關係和責任。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a problem involves specific people.","zh":"當問題涉及特定人士時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"managing director","meaning":"董事總經理","examples":[{"en":"Garen Filke is the managing director of a paper supply company.","zh":"Garen Filke 是一家紙張供應公司的董事總經理。"},{"en":"A managing director is a senior executive responsible for running a company or major organisation.","zh":"managing director 指負責營運公司或大型機構的高級行政人員。"},{"en":"The managing director may make final decisions about strategy, budgets and staffing.","zh":"董事總經理可能對策略、預算和人手作最終決定。"},{"en":"This role carries responsibility because poor decisions can affect the whole company.","zh":"這個職位承擔責任，因為錯誤決定可以影響整間公司。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying a top business leader.","zh":"識別高層商業領導人時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"paper supply company","meaning":"紙張供應公司","examples":[{"en":"The study was tested in a large paper supply company.","zh":"這項研究在一家大型紙張供應公司中測試。"},{"en":"A paper supply company sells or distributes paper products to offices, schools or businesses.","zh":"paper supply company 指向辦公室、學校或企業銷售或分發紙製品的公司。"},{"en":"A school may order notebooks and printing paper from a paper supply company.","zh":"學校可能向紙張供應公司訂購筆記簿和打印紙。"},{"en":"Such companies need good stock control because customers depend on regular delivery.","zh":"這類公司需要良好庫存控制，因為顧客依賴定期送貨。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a business that supplies paper materials.","zh":"描述供應紙張材料的企業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"put something to the test","meaning":"把……付諸測試","examples":[{"en":"Filke put Hewings’ problem-solving steps to the test.","zh":"Filke 把 Hewings 的解難步驟付諸測試。"},{"en":"Put something to the test means try it in practice to see whether it works.","zh":"put something to the test 指在實際中嘗試某事，以看看它是否有效。"},{"en":"A teacher may put a new revision method to the test before using it with every class.","zh":"老師可能先把新的溫習方法付諸測試，再用於每一班。"},{"en":"Testing an idea shows whether it is useful beyond theory.","zh":"測試想法能顯示它是否不只在理論上有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an approach is tried in real conditions.","zh":"當方法在真實條件下被嘗試時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"potentially encouraging","meaning":"可能令人鼓舞的","examples":[{"en":"Filke described the initial results as potentially encouraging.","zh":"Filke 形容初步結果可能令人鼓舞。"},{"en":"Potentially encouraging means possibly positive, but not yet fully proven.","zh":"potentially encouraging 指可能是正面的，但尚未完全證實。"},{"en":"A student’s first improved test result is potentially encouraging if the progress continues.","zh":"如果進步持續，學生第一次改善的測驗結果可能令人鼓舞。"},{"en":"Early results can raise hope, but more evidence is needed.","zh":"初步結果可以帶來希望，但仍需要更多證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something looks promising but remains uncertain.","zh":"當某事看似有希望但仍不確定時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"there remains a concern that","meaning":"仍有人擔心","examples":[{"en":"There remains a concern that focusing on blame may weaken a solution.","zh":"仍有人擔心集中追究責任可能削弱解決方案。"},{"en":"There remains a concern that means people still worry that something may be true or may happen.","zh":"there remains a concern that 指人們仍然擔心某事可能是真的或可能發生。"},{"en":"There remains a concern that online learning may leave some quiet students behind.","zh":"仍有人擔心網上學習可能令一些安靜學生被落下。"},{"en":"A concern remains when evidence has not fully removed the risk.","zh":"當證據未完全消除風險，憂慮仍會存在。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a warning continues despite progress.","zh":"當進展之後仍有警告時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"focus on who is causing the problem","meaning":"集中追究誰造成問題","examples":[{"en":"A focus on who is causing the problem can create conflict.","zh":"集中追究誰造成問題可以引起衝突。"},{"en":"Focus on who is causing the problem means concentrate on blaming a person rather than understanding the issue.","zh":"focus on who is causing the problem 指集中責怪某人，而不是理解問題。"},{"en":"In a group project, focusing only on who failed may stop the team from fixing the plan.","zh":"在小組專題中，只集中追究誰失職，可能阻止團隊修正計劃。"},{"en":"Blame can make people defensive and reduce cooperation.","zh":"責怪會令人防衛，並減少合作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when responsibility is confused with personal attack.","zh":"當責任與人身攻擊被混淆時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in itself","meaning":"本身","examples":[{"en":"The search for someone to blame can in itself become a problem.","zh":"尋找責怪對象本身可以成為一個問題。"},{"en":"In itself means by its own nature, separately from anything else.","zh":"in itself 指就其本身而言，與其他事物分開看。"},{"en":"Homework is not harmful in itself, but too much homework can create stress.","zh":"功課本身並非有害，但太多功課可以造成壓力。"},{"en":"A process can become a problem in itself if it wastes time or damages trust.","zh":"如果一個過程浪費時間或損害信任，它本身就可能成為問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something becomes important on its own.","zh":"當某事本身變得重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"implemented solution","meaning":"已實施的解決方案","examples":[{"en":"An implemented solution may fail if employees do not support it.","zh":"如果員工不支持，已實施的解決方案可能失敗。"},{"en":"An implemented solution is a solution that has actually been put into practice.","zh":"implemented solution 指已真正付諸實行的解決方案。"},{"en":"A new school timetable is an implemented solution once students begin following it.","zh":"新校時間表一旦學生開始跟隨，就是已實施的解決方案。"},{"en":"Implementation can fail if people affected by the plan resist it.","zh":"如果受計劃影響的人抗拒，實施可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a solution has moved beyond planning.","zh":"當解決方案已超越規劃階段時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"falter if not fail","meaning":"即使不完全失敗也可能受挫","examples":[{"en":"A blame-based solution may falter, if not fail completely.","zh":"以責怪為基礎的解決方案即使不完全失敗，也可能受挫。"},{"en":"Falter if not fail means become weak or partly unsuccessful, even if it does not totally collapse.","zh":"falter if not fail 指即使不徹底崩潰，也會變弱或部分失敗。"},{"en":"A study plan may falter, if not fail, when students set unrealistic goals.","zh":"當學生設定不切實際目標，學習計劃即使不完全失敗，也可能受挫。"},{"en":"Solutions falter when people lose trust or stop cooperating.","zh":"當人們失去信任或停止合作，解決方案就會受挫。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something may not fully fail but still performs badly.","zh":"當某事未必完全失敗但表現很差時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"management experience","meaning":"管理經驗","examples":[{"en":"Filke has more than 30 years of management experience.","zh":"Filke 擁有三十多年管理經驗。"},{"en":"Management experience is practical knowledge gained from leading people or organisations.","zh":"management experience 指從領導人員或組織中獲得的實際知識。"},{"en":"A shop supervisor gains management experience by training staff and handling complaints.","zh":"商店主管透過培訓員工和處理投訴累積管理經驗。"},{"en":"Experience helps managers recognise problems they have seen before.","zh":"經驗幫助經理識別以前見過的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when practical leadership history matters.","zh":"當實際領導經歷重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hold that","meaning":"認為；主張","examples":[{"en":"Filke holds that blame should be separated from problem analysis.","zh":"Filke 認為責怪應與問題分析分開。"},{"en":"Hold that means believe or argue that something is true.","zh":"hold that 指相信或主張某事為真。"},{"en":"Some teachers hold that reading aloud improves pronunciation.","zh":"有些老師認為朗讀可以改善發音。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to report someone’s opinion formally.","zh":"這個短語常用於正式報告某人的觀點。"},{"en":"It is useful when presenting a view in academic or business writing.","zh":"在學術或商業寫作中呈現觀點時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"organic entity","meaning":"有機整體","examples":[{"en":"He treats the problem as an organic entity in itself.","zh":"他把問題本身視為一個有機整體。"},{"en":"An organic entity is something viewed as a whole system with connected parts.","zh":"organic entity 指被視為由互相關連部分組成的完整系統。"},{"en":"A school can be seen as an organic entity because students, teachers and parents affect one another.","zh":"學校可以被視為有機整體，因為學生、老師和家長互相影響。"},{"en":"Treating a problem this way helps managers study relationships, not just individuals.","zh":"這樣看待問題有助經理研究關係，而不只是研究個人。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is understood as a living, connected system.","zh":"當某事被理解為活生生、互相關連的系統時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"without reference to","meaning":"不涉及；不提及……","examples":[{"en":"The issue should first be examined without reference to individual blame.","zh":"這個問題應先在不涉及個人責任的情況下被檢視。"},{"en":"Without reference to means without mentioning, considering or depending on something.","zh":"without reference to 指不提及、不考慮或不依賴某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may first mark grammar without reference to handwriting.","zh":"老師可能先在不考慮字跡的情況下批改文法。"},{"en":"Separating blame from analysis can make people discuss facts more calmly.","zh":"把責怪與分析分開，可以令人更冷靜地討論事實。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one factor is deliberately left out.","zh":"當某因素被刻意排除時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be at fault","meaning":"有過錯；應負責任","examples":[{"en":"Managers should not immediately decide who is at fault.","zh":"經理不應立即判斷誰有過錯。"},{"en":"Be at fault means be responsible for causing a mistake or problem.","zh":"be at fault 指對造成錯誤或問題負有責任。"},{"en":"In a car accident, police may investigate who is at fault.","zh":"在交通意外中，警方可能調查誰有過錯。"},{"en":"Deciding fault too early may stop people from understanding the system failure.","zh":"太早判斷責任可能阻止人們理解系統失誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when responsibility for a problem is being discussed.","zh":"討論問題責任時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"exacerbate the issue","meaning":"使問題惡化","examples":[{"en":"Poor communication may exacerbate the issue.","zh":"溝通不良可能使問題惡化。"},{"en":"Exacerbate the issue means make the problem worse.","zh":"exacerbate the issue 指使問題變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"Ignoring a student’s stress may exacerbate the issue instead of helping.","zh":"忽視學生壓力可能使問題惡化，而不是幫助。"},{"en":"Blaming people publicly can exacerbate workplace conflict.","zh":"公開責怪別人可以使工作場所衝突惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an action worsens an existing problem.","zh":"當某行動令已有問題變差時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a lasting solution","meaning":"長久的解決方案","examples":[{"en":"A lasting solution addresses the cause rather than the individual.","zh":"長久的解決方案處理原因，而不是針對個人。"},{"en":"A lasting solution is a solution that continues to work over time.","zh":"lasting solution 指能長期持續有效的解決方案。"},{"en":"Fixing a broken timetable may be a lasting solution if it removes repeated clashes.","zh":"如果修正時間表能消除反覆衝突，它可能是長久的解決方案。"},{"en":"Lasting solutions deal with root causes, not just immediate discomfort.","zh":"長久解決方案處理根本原因，而不只是眼前不適。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a solution must prevent future recurrence.","zh":"當解決方案必須防止日後重複出現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"finger-pointing","meaning":"互相指責","examples":[{"en":"Finger-pointing creates tension within the workplace.","zh":"互相指責會在工作場所中製造緊張。"},{"en":"Finger-pointing means blaming others instead of solving the problem.","zh":"finger-pointing 指責怪他人，而不是解決問題。"},{"en":"In a group project, finger-pointing can destroy trust between classmates.","zh":"在小組專題中，互相指責可以破壞同學之間的信任。"},{"en":"Finger-pointing wastes time because people defend themselves rather than cooperate.","zh":"互相指責浪費時間，因為人們會自我辯護，而不是合作。"},{"en":"This word is useful when blame becomes unhelpful and personal.","zh":"當責怪變得無助且針對個人時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"blaming","meaning":"歸咎他人","examples":[{"en":"Blaming individuals rarely produces a cooperative environment.","zh":"歸咎個人很少能產生合作環境。"},{"en":"Blaming means saying that someone is responsible for a problem or mistake.","zh":"blaming 指說某人對問題或錯誤負責。"},{"en":"Parents may start blaming each other when a child’s homework is unfinished.","zh":"當孩子功課未完成，父母可能開始互相歸咎。"},{"en":"Constant blaming makes people defensive and less willing to discuss the truth.","zh":"持續歸咎他人會令人防衛，並更不願討論真相。"},{"en":"This word is useful when responsibility turns into accusation.","zh":"當責任變成指控時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"uncomfortable work environment","meaning":"令人不安的工作環境","examples":[{"en":"Constant criticism creates an uncomfortable work environment.","zh":"持續批評會造成令人不安的工作環境。"},{"en":"An uncomfortable work environment is a workplace where people feel tense, unsafe or disrespected.","zh":"uncomfortable work environment 指令人感到緊張、不安全或不受尊重的工作場所。"},{"en":"Staff may avoid speaking honestly in an uncomfortable work environment.","zh":"在令人不安的工作環境中，員工可能避免誠實發言。"},{"en":"Such an environment reduces cooperation because people fear being blamed.","zh":"這種環境會減少合作，因為人們害怕被責怪。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when workplace atmosphere harms performance.","zh":"當工作場所氣氛損害表現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ultimately","meaning":"最終","examples":[{"en":"Unresolved problems ultimately affect the whole organisation.","zh":"未解決的問題最終會影響整個組織。"},{"en":"Ultimately means in the end or after everything is considered.","zh":"ultimately 指最終或在考慮所有事情之後。"},{"en":"A student may try many study methods, but ultimately success depends on consistent practice.","zh":"學生可能嘗試許多學習方法，但最終成功取決於持續練習。"},{"en":"Small problems can ultimately become serious if no one deals with them.","zh":"如果沒有人處理，小問題最終可以變嚴重。"},{"en":"This word is useful when stating the final result.","zh":"說明最終結果時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have a detrimental effect on","meaning":"對……產生不良影響","examples":[{"en":"Workplace conflict can have a detrimental effect on productivity.","zh":"工作場所衝突可以對生產力產生不良影響。"},{"en":"Have a detrimental effect on means harm or damage something.","zh":"have a detrimental effect on 指傷害或損害某事物。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can have a detrimental effect on memory and mood.","zh":"睡眠不足可以對記憶和情緒產生不良影響。"},{"en":"When workers argue constantly, teamwork and efficiency suffer.","zh":"當員工經常爭吵，團隊合作和效率就會受損。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing negative impact.","zh":"描述負面影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"workplace productivity","meaning":"工作場所生產力","examples":[{"en":"Good management can improve workplace productivity.","zh":"良好管理可以改善工作場所生產力。"},{"en":"Workplace productivity is how effectively people produce work in a workplace.","zh":"workplace productivity 指人們在工作場所中產出工作的效率。"},{"en":"Clear instructions can improve workplace productivity because staff waste less time.","zh":"清楚指示可以改善工作場所生產力，因為員工浪費較少時間。"},{"en":"Conflict, confusion and poor tools can reduce workplace productivity.","zh":"衝突、混亂和差劣工具可以降低工作場所生產力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing efficiency at work.","zh":"討論工作效率時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"problem-solving abilities","meaning":"解決問題的能力","examples":[{"en":"Wicks believes that our problem-solving abilities are shaped by several filters.","zh":"Wicks 認為我們的解決問題能力受到幾個過濾層塑造。"},{"en":"Problem-solving abilities are skills used to understand difficulties and find workable answers.","zh":"problem-solving abilities 指用來理解困難並找出可行答案的技能。"},{"en":"A student uses problem-solving abilities when planning how to catch up after absence.","zh":"學生計劃缺課後如何追回進度時，就是在使用解決問題的能力。"},{"en":"These abilities improve when people ask better questions and examine evidence.","zh":"當人們提出更好問題並檢視證據，這些能力會提升。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how people handle difficulties.","zh":"討論人們如何處理困難時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be run through","meaning":"經過……處理","examples":[{"en":"Our decisions are first run through a series of mental filters.","zh":"我們的決定首先經過一系列心理過濾層處理。"},{"en":"Be run through means be processed or passed through something before reaching a result.","zh":"be run through 指在得出結果前被處理或經過某系統。"},{"en":"A school announcement may be run through the office before it is sent to parents.","zh":"學校通告在發給家長前，可能先經校務處處理。"},{"en":"Decisions are shaped when information passes through beliefs, feelings and attitudes.","zh":"當資訊經過信念、感受和態度，決定就會被塑造。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is filtered or processed.","zh":"當某事被過濾或處理時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"distinct filters","meaning":"不同的過濾層","examples":[{"en":"Wicks identifies five distinct filters in decision making.","zh":"Wicks 在決策中識別五個不同的過濾層。"},{"en":"Distinct filters are separate stages or influences that shape how information is judged.","zh":"distinct filters 指塑造資訊如何被判斷的分開階段或影響。"},{"en":"A teacher may use distinct filters, such as accuracy and clarity, when marking essays.","zh":"老師批改作文時可能使用不同過濾層，例如準確性和清晰度。"},{"en":"Filters matter because they can change what people notice or ignore.","zh":"過濾層很重要，因為它們可以改變人們注意或忽略甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when decision making has several separate influences.","zh":"當決策有幾個分開影響因素時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"negotiate these filters","meaning":"妥善處理這些過濾層","examples":[{"en":"Good managers can negotiate these filters successfully.","zh":"優秀經理能成功妥善處理這些過濾層。"},{"en":"Negotiate these filters means work through mental influences carefully without being controlled by them.","zh":"negotiate these filters 指小心處理心理影響，而不被它們控制。"},{"en":"A student negotiates emotional filters when staying calm after harsh feedback.","zh":"學生在嚴厲回饋後保持冷靜，就是在處理情緒過濾層。"},{"en":"Managers negotiate filters by checking whether bias is shaping their judgement.","zh":"經理透過檢查偏見是否影響判斷來處理過濾層。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when people manage hidden mental influences.","zh":"當人們管理隱藏心理影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"arrive at a solution","meaning":"得出解決方案","examples":[{"en":"Managers must work through the evidence to arrive at a solution.","zh":"經理必須審視證據以得出解決方案。"},{"en":"Arrive at a solution means reach a solution after thinking, discussion or analysis.","zh":"arrive at a solution 指經思考、討論或分析後得到解決方案。"},{"en":"A class may arrive at a solution after debating how to share limited resources.","zh":"一班學生討論如何分享有限資源後，可能得出解決方案。"},{"en":"Good solutions are usually arrived at through evidence, not guesswork.","zh":"好的解決方案通常透過證據得出，而不是靠猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a solution is reached gradually.","zh":"當解決方案逐步得出時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"unbiased solution","meaning":"不偏不倚的解決方案","examples":[{"en":"A good manager aims to reach an unbiased solution.","zh":"優秀經理以達致不偏不倚的解決方案為目標。"},{"en":"An unbiased solution is a fair solution not controlled by personal prejudice or preference.","zh":"unbiased solution 指不受個人偏見或偏好控制的公平解決方案。"},{"en":"A teacher seeks an unbiased solution when listening to both students in an argument.","zh":"老師聆聽爭執中雙方學生時，就是尋求不偏不倚的解決方案。"},{"en":"Bias can lead to unfair decisions and damage trust.","zh":"偏見可以導致不公平決定並損害信任。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when fairness and objectivity matter.","zh":"當公平和客觀很重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"logical and clear","meaning":"合乎邏輯而清晰的","examples":[{"en":"The final decision should be logical and clear.","zh":"最終決定應合乎邏輯而清晰。"},{"en":"Logical and clear means reasonable, well-organised and easy to understand.","zh":"logical and clear 指合理、有組織且容易理解。"},{"en":"A school rule is logical and clear when students know why it exists and how to follow it.","zh":"當學生知道校規為何存在及如何遵守，校規就是合乎邏輯而清晰的。"},{"en":"Decisions become easier to accept when the reasoning is logical and clear.","zh":"當推理合乎邏輯而清晰，決定就較容易被接受。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the quality of a good decision.","zh":"解釋良好決定的質素時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"build something into","meaning":"把……納入","examples":[{"en":"Wicks built the filters into a decision-making ladder.","zh":"Wicks 把這些過濾層納入一個決策階梯。"},{"en":"Build something into means include it as part of a larger structure or system.","zh":"build something into 指把某物納入較大結構或系統的一部分。"},{"en":"A teacher can build revision time into every lesson.","zh":"老師可以把溫習時間納入每一課。"},{"en":"When a step is built into a process, people are less likely to forget it.","zh":"當某步驟被納入流程，人們較不容易忘記它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when adding an element to a system.","zh":"當把元素加入系統時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"decision-making ladder","meaning":"決策階梯","examples":[{"en":"The ladder represents several stages in decision making.","zh":"這個階梯代表決策中的幾個階段。"},{"en":"A decision-making ladder is a model showing steps or levels that influence a decision.","zh":"decision-making ladder 指展示影響決定的步驟或層級的模型。"},{"en":"A student may use a simple decision-making ladder before choosing subjects.","zh":"學生在選科前可能使用簡單的決策階梯。"},{"en":"The ladder helps people slow down and examine each stage of judgement.","zh":"這個階梯幫助人放慢速度並檢視判斷的每個階段。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when decision making is explained as a step-by-step process.","zh":"當決策被解釋為逐步過程時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have the potential to","meaning":"有可能","examples":[{"en":"Every decision has the potential to be influenced by personal bias.","zh":"每個決定都有可能受個人偏見影響。"},{"en":"Have the potential to means be able to possibly do or become something.","zh":"have the potential to 指有可能做到或變成某事。"},{"en":"A quiet student may have the potential to become a strong speaker with practice.","zh":"安靜的學生透過練習，有可能成為出色講者。"},{"en":"Potential does not guarantee a result, but it shows possibility.","zh":"潛力不保證結果，但顯示可能性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing what may happen.","zh":"討論可能發生的事情時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be coloured by","meaning":"受……影響","examples":[{"en":"Decisions can be coloured by beliefs and emotions.","zh":"決定可能受信念和情緒影響。"},{"en":"Be coloured by means be influenced by something, often in a way that changes judgement.","zh":"be coloured by 指受某事影響，常以改變判斷的方式發生。"},{"en":"A teacher’s view of a student may be coloured by one bad incident.","zh":"老師對學生的看法可能受一次不良事件影響。"},{"en":"Emotions colour decisions when people choose based on fear or anger.","zh":"當人們基於恐懼或憤怒選擇時，情緒就影響決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when hidden influence affects judgement.","zh":"當隱藏影響改變判斷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the first step being","meaning":"第一步是……","examples":[{"en":"The ladder has five stages, the first step being programming.","zh":"這個階梯有五個階段，第一步是思想程式。"},{"en":"The first step being introduces the first item in a sequence.","zh":"the first step being 用來引出一個序列中的第一項。"},{"en":"The project has three stages, the first step being research.","zh":"這個項目有三個階段，第一步是研究。"},{"en":"Naming the first step helps readers follow a process clearly.","zh":"說明第一步有助讀者清楚跟隨流程。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when listing stages in formal writing.","zh":"在正式寫作中列出階段時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"programming","meaning":"思想程式；既有心理設定","examples":[{"en":"Programming refers to the conditioning acquired from early life.","zh":"programming 指早期生活中獲得的制約。"},{"en":"Programming here means deep mental habits and assumptions formed by upbringing and experience.","zh":"programming 在此指由成長和經驗形成的深層心理習慣與假設。"},{"en":"A child’s programming may include ideas about politeness learned at home.","zh":"孩子的思想程式可能包括在家學到的禮貌觀念。"},{"en":"Early programming shapes what people accept, reject or notice automatically.","zh":"早期思想程式塑造人們自動接受、拒絕或注意甚麼。"},{"en":"This word is useful when behaviour is influenced by early conditioning.","zh":"當行為受早期制約影響時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"from the day we are born","meaning":"從我們出生那天起","examples":[{"en":"Conditioning begins from the day we are born.","zh":"制約從我們出生那天起就開始。"},{"en":"From the day we are born means starting at the beginning of life.","zh":"from the day we are born 指從生命開始時。"},{"en":"From the day we are born, family language shapes how we communicate.","zh":"從我們出生那天起，家庭語言就塑造我們如何溝通。"},{"en":"Early experiences matter because they begin shaping habits immediately.","zh":"早期經驗重要，因為它們立即開始塑造習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something starts extremely early in life.","zh":"當某事極早在人生中開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an amount of conditioning","meaning":"一定程度的制約","examples":[{"en":"Everyone is influenced by an amount of social conditioning.","zh":"每個人都受到一定程度的社會制約影響。"},{"en":"An amount of conditioning means some degree of learned influence from society, family or culture.","zh":"an amount of conditioning 指來自社會、家庭或文化的某種程度習得影響。"},{"en":"A child may receive an amount of conditioning about gender roles from toys and adverts.","zh":"孩子可能從玩具和廣告中受到一定程度關於性別角色的制約。"},{"en":"Conditioning affects judgement because people may see familiar ideas as automatically normal.","zh":"制約影響判斷，因為人們可能把熟悉觀念自動視為正常。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when behaviour is partly learned from surroundings.","zh":"當行為部分從環境中學來時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"accept or reject","meaning":"接受或拒絕","examples":[{"en":"People may automatically accept or reject certain viewpoints.","zh":"人們可能自動接受或拒絕某些觀點。"},{"en":"Accept or reject means agree with something or refuse to agree with it.","zh":"accept or reject 指同意某事或拒絕同意它。"},{"en":"Students may accept or reject an argument after checking the evidence.","zh":"學生可能在檢查證據後接受或拒絕某論點。"},{"en":"People sometimes accept familiar ideas and reject unfamiliar ones too quickly.","zh":"人們有時太快接受熟悉觀念並拒絕陌生觀念。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when choices involve approval or refusal.","zh":"當選擇涉及認同或拒絕時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"points of view","meaning":"觀點","examples":[{"en":"Our background influences how we respond to different points of view.","zh":"我們的背景影響我們如何回應不同觀點。"},{"en":"Points of view are opinions or ways of seeing a situation.","zh":"points of view 指意見或看待情況的方式。"},{"en":"A class debate helps students hear different points of view on the same issue.","zh":"課堂辯論幫助學生聽到同一議題上的不同觀點。"},{"en":"Listening to different views reduces narrow thinking.","zh":"聆聽不同觀點可以減少狹隘思維。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when people disagree or interpret things differently.","zh":"當人們不同意或以不同方式理解事情時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"almost a reflex action","meaning":"幾乎是反射動作","examples":[{"en":"Some reactions occur almost as a reflex action.","zh":"有些反應幾乎像反射動作般出現。"},{"en":"Almost a reflex action means happening very automatically, with little conscious thought.","zh":"almost a reflex action 指非常自動地發生，幾乎沒有自覺思考。"},{"en":"A driver may brake almost as a reflex action when a dog runs onto the road.","zh":"當狗衝出馬路，司機可能幾乎反射性地煞車。"},{"en":"Bias can feel automatic because it has been learned for many years.","zh":"偏見可能感覺自動，因為它已被學習多年。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reactions are quick and instinctive.","zh":"當反應快速而本能時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"vary from person to person","meaning":"因人而異","examples":[{"en":"Personal conditioning varies from person to person.","zh":"個人制約因人而異。"},{"en":"Vary from person to person means be different for each individual.","zh":"vary from person to person 指每個人都不同。"},{"en":"Learning speed varies from person to person, so students need different support.","zh":"學習速度因人而異，所以學生需要不同支援。"},{"en":"Personal experiences differ, so people may judge the same problem differently.","zh":"個人經驗不同，因此人們可能對同一問題作出不同判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when individual differences matter.","zh":"當個人差異重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be more marked","meaning":"更為明顯","examples":[{"en":"Cultural differences may be more marked between nationalities.","zh":"不同國籍之間的文化差異可能更為明顯。"},{"en":"Be more marked means be more noticeable or obvious.","zh":"be more marked 指更加可見或明顯。"},{"en":"Differences in pronunciation may be more marked between speakers from distant regions.","zh":"遠距離地區說話者之間的發音差異可能更為明顯。"},{"en":"Marked differences can affect communication if people do not recognise them.","zh":"如果人們沒有識別明顯差異，溝通可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a difference is especially clear.","zh":"當差異特別清楚時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"when comparing nationalities","meaning":"比較不同國籍人士時","examples":[{"en":"Programming is often clearer when comparing nationalities.","zh":"比較不同國籍人士時，思想程式通常更清楚。"},{"en":"When comparing nationalities means when looking at people from different countries side by side.","zh":"when comparing nationalities 指把來自不同國家的人並列比較時。"},{"en":"Teachers notice different classroom habits when comparing nationalities in an international school.","zh":"在國際學校中，老師比較不同國籍學生時，會注意到不同課堂習慣。"},{"en":"National comparisons can reveal cultural assumptions people usually take for granted.","zh":"國籍比較可以揭示人們平時視為理所當然的文化假設。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when cultural background is being compared.","zh":"當文化背景被比較時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the base of our character","meaning":"性格的基礎","examples":[{"en":"Our early programming forms the base of our character.","zh":"我們早期的思想程式形成性格的基礎。"},{"en":"The base of our character means the foundation on which our personality and habits develop.","zh":"base of our character 指我們性格和習慣發展的基礎。"},{"en":"Childhood routines may become part of the base of a person’s character.","zh":"童年日常規律可能成為一個人性格基礎的一部分。"},{"en":"Early values matter because later decisions are often built on them.","zh":"早期價值觀重要，因為後來的決定常建基於它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing deep personal foundations.","zh":"討論深層個人基礎時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be built on","meaning":"建基於","examples":[{"en":"Our beliefs are built on our earlier conditioning.","zh":"我們的信念建基於早期制約。"},{"en":"Be built on means be based on or developed from something.","zh":"be built on 指以某事為基礎或由某事發展而成。"},{"en":"Strong writing is built on clear ideas and good examples.","zh":"有力寫作建基於清晰想法和好例子。"},{"en":"If a decision is built on false beliefs, the result may be weak.","zh":"如果決定建基於錯誤信念，結果可能薄弱。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining foundations or causes.","zh":"解釋基礎或原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"believe something to be true","meaning":"相信某事是真的","examples":[{"en":"People may believe something to be true without evidence.","zh":"人們可能在沒有證據下相信某事是真的。"},{"en":"Believe something to be true means think something is correct or real.","zh":"believe something to be true 指認為某事正確或真實。"},{"en":"A child may believe a rumour to be true until a teacher explains the facts.","zh":"孩子可能相信謠言是真的，直到老師解釋事實。"},{"en":"Beliefs can influence decisions even when evidence is weak.","zh":"即使證據薄弱，信念仍可影響決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when opinion is treated as fact.","zh":"當意見被當作事實時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not necessarily mean","meaning":"不一定表示","examples":[{"en":"Believing something does not necessarily mean that it is true.","zh":"相信某事不一定表示它是真的。"},{"en":"Not necessarily mean means does not automatically prove or imply something.","zh":"not necessarily mean 指不會自動證明或意味某事。"},{"en":"A high price does not necessarily mean a product is better.","zh":"高價不一定表示產品更好。"},{"en":"Feelings can be strong without being accurate evidence.","zh":"感受可以很強烈，但不一定是準確證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when separating assumption from fact.","zh":"當要區分假設與事實時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"next on the ladder","meaning":"階梯上的下一層","examples":[{"en":"Feelings are next on the ladder after beliefs.","zh":"在信念之後，感受是階梯上的下一層。"},{"en":"Next on the ladder means the next stage in an ordered model or process.","zh":"next on the ladder 指有序模型或流程中的下一階段。"},{"en":"After learning vocabulary, grammar may be next on the ladder for language students.","zh":"學完詞彙後，文法可能是語言學生階梯上的下一層。"},{"en":"A ladder model helps people see how one stage leads to another.","zh":"階梯模型幫助人看見一個階段如何通向另一個階段。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining a sequence.","zh":"解釋序列時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"personally react to","meaning":"親自對……作出反應","examples":[{"en":"Feelings influence how we personally react to an issue.","zh":"感受影響我們如何親自對某議題作出反應。"},{"en":"Personally react to means respond based on one’s own emotions, experience or viewpoint.","zh":"personally react to 指基於自己的情緒、經驗或觀點作出回應。"},{"en":"Two students may personally react to criticism in very different ways.","zh":"兩個學生可能對批評有非常不同的個人反應。"},{"en":"Personal reactions can be useful signals, but they should not replace evidence.","zh":"個人反應可以是有用訊號，但不應取代證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when individual emotional response matters.","zh":"當個人情緒反應重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"skew how we look at","meaning":"扭曲我們看待……的方式","examples":[{"en":"Strong emotions can skew how we look at a problem.","zh":"強烈情緒可以扭曲我們看待問題的方式。"},{"en":"Skew how we look at means distort or bias our understanding of something.","zh":"skew how we look at 指扭曲或使我們對某事的理解帶有偏見。"},{"en":"Fear can skew how a student looks at an exam and make it seem impossible.","zh":"恐懼可以扭曲學生看待考試的方式，令它看似不可能完成。"},{"en":"Emotions skew judgement when they make one detail seem more important than it is.","zh":"當情緒令某細節看起來比實際更重要，就會扭曲判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when perception becomes biased.","zh":"當感知變得有偏差時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"solve an issue","meaning":"解決問題","examples":[{"en":"Managers should consider evidence carefully before trying to solve an issue.","zh":"經理在嘗試解決問題前應仔細考慮證據。"},{"en":"Solve an issue means find and apply a way to deal with a problem.","zh":"solve an issue 指找出並應用方法來處理問題。"},{"en":"A class can solve an issue about noise by agreeing on clearer group-work rules.","zh":"一班學生可以透過同意更清晰的小組工作規則來解決噪音問題。"},{"en":"Issues are solved better when people know the cause and the people affected.","zh":"當人們知道原因和受影響人士，問題會更容易被解決。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a problem needs action.","zh":"當問題需要行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"someone involved","meaning":"涉事者","examples":[{"en":"A manager may have strong feelings about someone involved.","zh":"經理可能對某位涉事者有強烈感受。"},{"en":"Someone involved is a person connected to or taking part in a situation.","zh":"someone involved 指與某情況有關或參與其中的人。"},{"en":"A teacher should listen to everyone involved before judging a playground conflict.","zh":"老師判斷操場衝突前，應聆聽所有涉事者。"},{"en":"Feelings about one person involved can bias the whole decision.","zh":"對某位涉事者的感受可以令整個決定有偏差。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a situation includes specific people.","zh":"當情況包括特定人士時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be unfair or unreasonable","meaning":"不公平或不合理","examples":[{"en":"A manager may believe that an employee is being unfair or unreasonable.","zh":"經理可能相信某員工不公平或不合理。"},{"en":"Be unfair or unreasonable means act without fairness, logic or proper consideration.","zh":"be unfair or unreasonable 指行事欠公平、欠邏輯或欠適當考慮。"},{"en":"A student may think a rule is unfair or unreasonable if no one explains its purpose.","zh":"如果沒有人解釋規則目的，學生可能認為規則不公平或不合理。"},{"en":"Judging someone as unfair too quickly can damage trust.","zh":"太快判斷某人不公平可能損害信任。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when behaviour is seen as unjust or illogical.","zh":"當行為被視為不公正或不合邏輯時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"over-compensate for","meaning":"過度補償","examples":[{"en":"A proposed solution may over-compensate for perceived unfairness.","zh":"擬議解決方案可能對被感知的不公平作出過度補償。"},{"en":"Over-compensate for means react too strongly while trying to correct a problem.","zh":"over-compensate for 指在嘗試修正問題時反應過度。"},{"en":"A teacher may over-compensate for being strict by giving students too much freedom.","zh":"老師可能因為曾經太嚴格而過度補償，給學生太多自由。"},{"en":"Over-compensation can create a new imbalance instead of solving the original issue.","zh":"過度補償可能造成新的失衡，而不是解決原本問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when correction goes too far.","zh":"當修正走得太遠時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in the long run","meaning":"長遠而言","examples":[{"en":"An emotionally driven solution may be ineffective in the long run.","zh":"由情緒驅動的解決方案長遠而言可能無效。"},{"en":"In the long run means over a long period, not just immediately.","zh":"in the long run 指長時間來看，而不只是立即。"},{"en":"Skipping sleep may help tonight, but it hurts learning in the long run.","zh":"熬夜可能今晚有幫助，但長遠而言會損害學習。"},{"en":"Short-term comfort can create long-term weakness.","zh":"短期舒適可以造成長期弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when considering future consequences.","zh":"考慮未來後果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have the potential to impact on","meaning":"有可能影響","examples":[{"en":"Personal feelings have the potential to impact on attitudes.","zh":"個人感受有可能影響態度。"},{"en":"Have the potential to impact on means may influence or affect something.","zh":"have the potential to impact on 指可能影響某事。"},{"en":"A teacher’s encouragement has the potential to impact on a shy student’s confidence.","zh":"老師的鼓勵有可能影響害羞學生的信心。"},{"en":"Feelings can shape attitudes before people realise it.","zh":"感受可以在人們察覺之前塑造態度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an influence is possible but not guaranteed.","zh":"當影響可能存在但不保證發生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"resistant to change","meaning":"抗拒改變的","examples":[{"en":"Some attitudes are resistant to change.","zh":"有些態度抗拒改變。"},{"en":"Resistant to change means unwilling or slow to accept new ideas, methods or conditions.","zh":"resistant to change 指不願或很慢接受新想法、方法或情況。"},{"en":"A school may be resistant to change if teachers are used to old routines.","zh":"如果老師習慣舊日常，學校可能抗拒改變。"},{"en":"Resistance can delay improvement even when evidence supports a new approach.","zh":"即使證據支持新方法，抗拒也可能延遲改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when people or systems do not adapt easily.","zh":"當人或系統不容易適應時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"daily modifications","meaning":"日常變化","examples":[{"en":"Our attitudes also include daily modifications in how we feel.","zh":"我們的態度也包括感受上的日常變化。"},{"en":"Daily modifications are small changes that happen from day to day.","zh":"daily modifications 指每天發生的小改變。"},{"en":"A student’s study plan may need daily modifications during exam week.","zh":"考試週期間，學生的學習計劃可能需要日常調整。"},{"en":"Mood changes can modify attitudes even when deeper beliefs stay the same.","zh":"即使較深層信念不變，情緒變化也可以改變態度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when small everyday adjustments matter.","zh":"當每日小調整很重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"one’s mood","meaning":"某人的情緒","examples":[{"en":"A person’s mood may affect how they respond to a problem.","zh":"一個人的情緒可能影響他如何回應問題。"},{"en":"One’s mood is the emotional state a person is in at a particular time.","zh":"one’s mood 指某人在特定時間的情緒狀態。"},{"en":"A tired student’s mood may make a small comment feel like criticism.","zh":"疲倦學生的情緒可能令一句小評論感覺像批評。"},{"en":"Mood affects decisions because it changes what feels urgent, fair or annoying.","zh":"情緒影響決定，因為它改變甚麼感覺緊急、公平或惱人。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when temporary emotion influences judgement.","zh":"當暫時情緒影響判斷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a combination of","meaning":"……的組合","examples":[{"en":"A combination of beliefs and feelings shapes behaviour.","zh":"信念和感受的組合塑造行為。"},{"en":"A combination of means two or more things working together.","zh":"combination of 指兩個或更多事物一起作用。"},{"en":"Success in exams often depends on a combination of revision, sleep and confidence.","zh":"考試成功常取決於溫習、睡眠和信心的組合。"},{"en":"Behaviour is rarely caused by one factor alone.","zh":"行為很少只由單一因素造成。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when several elements create one result.","zh":"當幾個元素共同造成一個結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"culminate in","meaning":"最終形成；以……告終","examples":[{"en":"The earlier stages culminate in our actions.","zh":"較早階段最終形成我們的行動。"},{"en":"Culminate in means finally lead to or end in a particular result.","zh":"culminate in 指最終導致或以某特定結果告終。"},{"en":"Months of practice may culminate in a confident public performance.","zh":"數月練習可能最終形成自信的公開表演。"},{"en":"Thoughts, feelings and attitudes culminate in what people actually do.","zh":"思想、感受和態度最終形成人的實際行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a process reaches its final outcome.","zh":"當過程達到最終結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"choose to do or not do","meaning":"選擇做或不做","examples":[{"en":"Actions are what we choose to do or not do.","zh":"行動就是我們選擇做或不做的事。"},{"en":"Choose to do or not do means decide whether to take action or avoid action.","zh":"choose to do or not do 指決定是否採取行動或避免行動。"},{"en":"A student may choose to ask for help or not do so because of pride.","zh":"學生可能因自尊而選擇求助或不求助。"},{"en":"Decisions become real through what people choose to do or avoid.","zh":"決定透過人們選擇做甚麼或避免做甚麼而變成現實。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when action and inaction are both choices.","zh":"當行動和不行動都是選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"most directly control","meaning":"最直接控制","examples":[{"en":"Actions most directly control the outcome of a decision.","zh":"行動最直接控制決策結果。"},{"en":"Most directly control means have the clearest and strongest immediate influence on something.","zh":"most directly control 指對某事有最清楚和最強的直接影響。"},{"en":"In a fire drill, following instructions most directly controls student safety.","zh":"在火警演習中，遵守指示最直接控制學生安全。"},{"en":"Beliefs matter, but actions most directly shape real-world results.","zh":"信念重要，但行動最直接塑造現實結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying the strongest practical influence.","zh":"識別最強實際影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"success or failure","meaning":"成功或失敗","examples":[{"en":"Actions determine the success or failure of the process.","zh":"行動決定過程的成功或失敗。"},{"en":"Success or failure means whether something works well or does not work.","zh":"success or failure 指某事是否運作良好。"},{"en":"A revision plan’s success or failure depends on whether the student follows it consistently.","zh":"溫習計劃的成功或失敗取決於學生是否持續執行。"},{"en":"Good ideas can still fail if actions are weak.","zh":"即使想法好，如果行動薄弱，也仍可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evaluating the final result.","zh":"評估最終結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"decision-making process","meaning":"決策過程","examples":[{"en":"Bias can affect every stage of the decision-making process.","zh":"偏見可以影響決策過程的每個階段。"},{"en":"The decision-making process is the series of steps used to reach a decision.","zh":"decision-making process 指用來達成決定的一系列步驟。"},{"en":"Choosing a university involves a decision-making process of comparing cost, courses and location.","zh":"選擇大學涉及比較費用、課程和地點的決策過程。"},{"en":"A clear process reduces emotional or rushed choices.","zh":"清晰過程能減少情緒化或倉促選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when decision making is treated as a sequence.","zh":"當決策被視為一連串步驟時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"psycho-analytical approach","meaning":"精神分析式方法","examples":[{"en":"Some executives reject a psycho-analytical approach to business decisions.","zh":"有些行政人員拒絕以精神分析式方法處理商業決策。"},{"en":"A psycho-analytical approach examines hidden mental motives, emotions and past influences.","zh":"psycho-analytical approach 指檢視隱藏心理動機、情緒和過去影響的方法。"},{"en":"A counsellor may use a psycho-analytical approach to explore why someone fears conflict.","zh":"輔導員可能使用精神分析式方法，探索某人為何害怕衝突。"},{"en":"Some business leaders dislike this approach because it feels less practical than clear procedures.","zh":"有些商業領導不喜歡這方法，因為它感覺不如清晰程序實際。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when psychology is used to interpret behaviour.","zh":"當心理學被用來解讀行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have little place in","meaning":"在……中沒有多大位置","examples":[{"en":"Some managers believe psychology has little place in practical decision making.","zh":"有些經理認為心理學在實際決策中沒有多大位置。"},{"en":"Have little place in means be seen as not very relevant or useful in a particular area.","zh":"have little place in 指被視為在某特定範疇不太相關或不太有用。"},{"en":"Some people think memorisation has little place in creative writing, but vocabulary still matters.","zh":"有些人認為背誦在創意寫作中沒有多大位置，但詞彙仍然重要。"},{"en":"Saying something has little place may show a preference for another method.","zh":"說某事沒有多大位置，可能顯示人偏好另一方法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone rejects the relevance of an idea.","zh":"當某人否定某概念的相關性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a point of view held by","meaning":"……所持的觀點","examples":[{"en":"This is a point of view held by John Tate.","zh":"這是 John Tate 所持的觀點。"},{"en":"A point of view held by someone is an opinion or belief that person has.","zh":"point of view held by someone 指某人擁有的意見或信念。"},{"en":"The idea that homework should be limited is a point of view held by many parents.","zh":"功課應受限制這個想法，是許多家長所持的觀點。"},{"en":"Identifying who holds a view helps readers understand the argument’s source.","zh":"識別誰持有某觀點，有助讀者理解論點來源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when attributing an opinion.","zh":"引述觀點來源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"former CEO","meaning":"前行政總裁","examples":[{"en":"John Tate is the former CEO of Allied Enterprise and Shipping.","zh":"John Tate 是 Allied Enterprise and Shipping 的前行政總裁。"},{"en":"A former CEO is someone who used to be the chief executive officer of a company.","zh":"former CEO 指曾經擔任公司行政總裁的人。"},{"en":"A former CEO may give advice based on years of leadership experience.","zh":"前行政總裁可能根據多年領導經驗提供建議。"},{"en":"Former leaders can influence debate because people trust their practical background.","zh":"前領導人能影響討論，因為人們信任他們的實際背景。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a past senior business role.","zh":"描述過去的高級商業職位時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the secret behind","meaning":"……背後的秘訣","examples":[{"en":"Tate believes the secret behind a solid decision is mechanical.","zh":"Tate 認為穩妥決定背後的秘訣是機械化的。"},{"en":"The secret behind something is the hidden reason or key factor that explains it.","zh":"secret behind something 指解釋某事的隱藏原因或關鍵因素。"},{"en":"The secret behind a strong essay is often clear planning before writing.","zh":"有力文章背後的秘訣常是在寫作前清晰規劃。"},{"en":"People look for the secret behind success when they want to copy good results.","zh":"人們尋找成功背後的秘訣，是因為想複製好結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying what really makes something work.","zh":"識別真正令某事有效的因素時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"solid decision","meaning":"穩妥的決定","examples":[{"en":"A solid decision should be based on a careful review of alternatives.","zh":"穩妥的決定應建基於對替代方案的仔細檢視。"},{"en":"A solid decision is a reliable, well-supported decision.","zh":"solid decision 指可靠且有充分支持的決定。"},{"en":"A family makes a solid decision about moving house after comparing cost, transport and schools.","zh":"家庭在比較費用、交通和學校後，對搬屋作出穩妥決定。"},{"en":"Decisions become solid when they are based on evidence rather than impulse.","zh":"當決定建基於證據而非衝動，它就變得穩妥。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a decision is strong and defensible.","zh":"當決定有力且站得住腳時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"more mechanical","meaning":"更機械化的","examples":[{"en":"Tate’s approach to decision making is more mechanical than psychological.","zh":"Tate 的決策方法比心理式方法更機械化。"},{"en":"More mechanical means more based on procedures, steps and structure than feelings or interpretation.","zh":"more mechanical 指更建基於程序、步驟和結構，而不是感受或詮釋。"},{"en":"A checklist is a more mechanical way to pack for a trip than relying on memory.","zh":"使用清單收拾行李，比依靠記憶是更機械化的方法。"},{"en":"Mechanical approaches reduce emotion by forcing people to follow clear steps.","zh":"機械化方法透過迫使人跟隨清晰步驟來減少情緒。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing process-based and psychology-based methods.","zh":"比較以流程為本和以心理為本的方法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"after consideration of","meaning":"在考慮……之後","examples":[{"en":"A decision should be made after consideration of all alternatives.","zh":"決定應在考慮所有替代方案之後作出。"},{"en":"After consideration of means after thinking carefully about something.","zh":"after consideration of 指仔細思考某事之後。"},{"en":"A student should choose subjects after consideration of interests, ability and future plans.","zh":"學生應在考慮興趣、能力和未來計劃之後選科。"},{"en":"Careful consideration prevents people from choosing the first option too quickly.","zh":"仔細考慮能防止人太快選擇第一個選項。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a decision follows review.","zh":"當決定在檢視後作出時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"all alternatives","meaning":"所有替代方案","examples":[{"en":"Managers should examine all alternatives before deciding.","zh":"經理在決定前應檢視所有替代方案。"},{"en":"All alternatives means every possible option or choice.","zh":"all alternatives 指所有可能選項或選擇。"},{"en":"Before buying a phone, a customer should compare all alternatives within the budget.","zh":"購買電話前，顧客應比較預算內所有替代方案。"},{"en":"Ignoring alternatives may cause people to miss a better solution.","zh":"忽略替代方案可能令人錯過更好解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when every option should be reviewed.","zh":"當每個選項都應被檢視時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hierarchical structure","meaning":"階級式組織架構","examples":[{"en":"A hierarchical structure makes lines of responsibility clear.","zh":"階級式組織架構令責任線清晰。"},{"en":"A hierarchical structure is an organisation system with different levels of authority.","zh":"hierarchical structure 指有不同權力層級的組織系統。"},{"en":"A school has a hierarchical structure with principals, department heads and teachers.","zh":"學校有校長、科主任和老師構成的階級式組織架構。"},{"en":"Hierarchy can improve accountability because people know who is responsible.","zh":"階級架構可以改善問責，因為人們知道誰負責。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing ranks and responsibility.","zh":"討論職級和責任時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take responsibility for","meaning":"對……負責","examples":[{"en":"One person should take responsibility for the final decision.","zh":"應有一個人對最終決定負責。"},{"en":"Take responsibility for means accept duty or accountability for something.","zh":"take responsibility for 指接受對某事的責任或問責。"},{"en":"A team leader should take responsibility for organising the presentation schedule.","zh":"組長應對安排匯報時間表負責。"},{"en":"Responsibility matters because someone must check whether the plan works.","zh":"責任很重要，因為必須有人檢查計劃是否有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when ownership of an action is needed.","zh":"當行動需要有人承擔時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"most importantly","meaning":"最重要的是","examples":[{"en":"Most importantly, the decision must be followed through.","zh":"最重要的是，決定必須被貫徹到底。"},{"en":"Most importantly introduces the point that matters most.","zh":"most importantly 用來引出最重要的一點。"},{"en":"You should revise vocabulary and grammar, but most importantly, practise writing full answers.","zh":"你應溫習詞彙和文法，但最重要的是，練習寫完整答案。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the next idea is central, not just additional.","zh":"這個短語表示下一個想法是核心，而不只是補充。"},{"en":"It is useful when ranking ideas by importance.","zh":"按重要性排列想法時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"follow a decision through","meaning":"把決定貫徹到底","examples":[{"en":"Managers should follow a decision through until its effects are known.","zh":"經理應把決定貫徹到底，直到其效果清楚。"},{"en":"Follow a decision through means continue implementing and checking a decision after making it.","zh":"follow a decision through 指在作出決定後繼續執行並檢查。"},{"en":"A school must follow a new discipline policy through by monitoring student behaviour.","zh":"學校必須透過監察學生行為，把新的紀律政策貫徹到底。"},{"en":"Decisions fail when leaders announce them but do not check the results.","zh":"當領導只宣布決定卻不檢查結果，決定就會失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when commitment after a decision matters.","zh":"當決定後的承諾很重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"verify whether","meaning":"核實是否……","examples":[{"en":"The manager must verify whether the problem has been resolved.","zh":"經理必須核實問題是否已經解決。"},{"en":"Verify whether means check if something is true or has happened.","zh":"verify whether 指檢查某事是否真實或已發生。"},{"en":"A teacher may verify whether students understood the lesson by asking short questions.","zh":"老師可能透過提出簡短問題來核實學生是否理解課堂。"},{"en":"Verification prevents people from assuming a problem is solved when it is not.","zh":"核實可以防止人們在問題未解決時誤以為已解決。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when confirmation is needed.","zh":"當需要確認時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have indeed been resolved","meaning":"確實已獲解決","examples":[{"en":"The process should confirm that the problem has indeed been resolved.","zh":"這個過程應確認問題確實已獲解決。"},{"en":"Have indeed been resolved means have truly and actually been solved.","zh":"have indeed been resolved 指真正並實際上已被解決。"},{"en":"A repaired lift has indeed been resolved only after residents can use it safely again.","zh":"已維修升降機只有在居民能再次安全使用時，才算確實已獲解決。"},{"en":"Confirmation matters because a problem can look solved while still existing underneath.","zh":"確認很重要，因為問題可能看似已解決，但底下仍存在。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when emphasising real completion.","zh":"強調真正完成時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"from his point of view","meaning":"從他的角度來看","examples":[{"en":"From his point of view, accountability matters more than unanimity.","zh":"從他的角度來看，問責比一致同意更重要。"},{"en":"From his point of view means according to his opinion or perspective.","zh":"from his point of view 指根據他的意見或角度。"},{"en":"From a student’s point of view, the homework deadline may feel unreasonable.","zh":"從學生角度來看，功課期限可能感覺不合理。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds readers that this is one person’s interpretation.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者，這是一個人的詮釋。"},{"en":"It is useful when presenting a specific perspective.","zh":"呈現特定角度時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a flawed decision","meaning":"有缺陷的決定","examples":[{"en":"A flawed decision may lack a clearly responsible person.","zh":"有缺陷的決定可能缺乏一個明確負責的人。"},{"en":"A flawed decision is a decision with a weakness, error or missing element.","zh":"flawed decision 指有弱點、錯誤或缺失元素的決定。"},{"en":"Choosing a school without checking transport may be a flawed decision.","zh":"沒有檢查交通就選學校，可能是有缺陷的決定。"},{"en":"Decisions become flawed when important facts or responsibilities are ignored.","zh":"當重要事實或責任被忽略，決定就變得有缺陷。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a decision is defective.","zh":"當決定有問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be decided on by","meaning":"由……共同決定","examples":[{"en":"The proposal was decided on by too many people.","zh":"這個建議由太多人共同決定。"},{"en":"Be decided on by means be chosen or agreed by particular people.","zh":"be decided on by 指由特定人士選定或同意。"},{"en":"The class picnic location may be decided on by a student committee.","zh":"班級野餐地點可能由學生委員會共同決定。"},{"en":"Too many decision makers can make accountability unclear.","zh":"太多決策者可能令問責不清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying who made a decision.","zh":"識別誰作出決定時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"leave no single person with","meaning":"沒有讓任何一個人擁有……","examples":[{"en":"A group decision may leave no single person with clear responsibility.","zh":"小組決定可能沒有讓任何一個人擁有清晰責任。"},{"en":"Leave no single person with means result in nobody individually having something.","zh":"leave no single person with 指結果是沒有任何個別人士擁有某物。"},{"en":"A shared project may leave no single student with responsibility if roles are unclear.","zh":"如果角色不清晰，共同專題可能沒有讓任何一個學生擁有責任。"},{"en":"When responsibility is too widely spread, follow-up becomes weak.","zh":"當責任過度分散，跟進就會變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when accountability disappears in a group.","zh":"當問責在群體中消失時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sufficient accountability","meaning":"足夠的問責","examples":[{"en":"A successful decision requires sufficient accountability.","zh":"成功決定需要足夠的問責。"},{"en":"Sufficient accountability means enough clear responsibility for actions and results.","zh":"sufficient accountability 指對行動和結果有足夠清晰的責任。"},{"en":"A school project has sufficient accountability when each student knows their role.","zh":"當每個學生都知道自己的角色，學校專題就有足夠問責。"},{"en":"Accountability helps ensure that someone checks progress and solves new problems.","zh":"問責有助確保有人檢查進度並解決新問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when responsibility must be clear enough.","zh":"當責任必須足夠清楚時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ensure its success","meaning":"確保其成功","examples":[{"en":"A responsible manager should monitor the plan to ensure its success.","zh":"負責任的經理應監察計劃，以確保其成功。"},{"en":"Ensure its success means make sure something works well or reaches its goal.","zh":"ensure its success 指確保某事運作良好或達成目標。"},{"en":"A teacher checks students’ drafts to ensure the success of a writing task.","zh":"老師檢查學生草稿，以確保寫作任務成功。"},{"en":"Success is more likely when progress is monitored after action begins.","zh":"行動開始後若有監察，成功就更有可能。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when follow-up is needed to make a plan work.","zh":"當需要跟進以令計劃有效時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"match each statement with","meaning":"把每項陳述與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match each statement with the correct person.","zh":"考生把每項陳述與正確人物配對。"},{"en":"Match each statement with means connect each sentence or idea to the correct answer.","zh":"match each statement with 指把每句陳述或想法連接到正確答案。"},{"en":"Students match each statement with a paragraph after identifying its main idea.","zh":"學生識別主旨後，把每項陳述與段落配對。"},{"en":"This task tests careful reading because similar ideas may appear in different places.","zh":"這項任務測試仔細閱讀，因為相似想法可能出現在不同位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in matching exercises.","zh":"這個短語適用於配對練習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"list of people","meaning":"人物列表","examples":[{"en":"The task provides a list of people and their views.","zh":"這項任務提供人物列表及其觀點。"},{"en":"A list of people is a set of names given for reference or matching.","zh":"list of people 指供參考或配對的一組人名。"},{"en":"An exam question may provide a list of people mentioned in a passage.","zh":"考題可能提供文章中提到的人物列表。"},{"en":"Students should connect each name with the correct opinion or action.","zh":"學生應把每個名字與正確觀點或行動連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when answers depend on named individuals.","zh":"當答案取決於具名人物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"clear corporate structure","meaning":"清晰的公司架構","examples":[{"en":"A clear corporate structure can establish responsibility for decisions.","zh":"清晰的公司架構可以建立決策責任。"},{"en":"A clear corporate structure is an organised company system showing roles and authority.","zh":"clear corporate structure 指顯示角色和權力的有組織公司系統。"},{"en":"A small business needs a clear corporate structure when it grows and hires more staff.","zh":"小企業成長並聘請更多員工時，需要清晰公司架構。"},{"en":"Clear structure prevents confusion about who approves, checks and carries out decisions.","zh":"清晰架構防止人們混淆誰批准、檢查和執行決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when company roles must be understood.","zh":"當公司角色必須被理解時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"corporate decision making","meaning":"企業決策","examples":[{"en":"Corporate decision making requires clear lines of responsibility.","zh":"企業決策需要清晰責任線。"},{"en":"Corporate decision making means the process by which a company chooses actions and policies.","zh":"corporate decision making 指公司選擇行動和政策的過程。"},{"en":"Corporate decision making may involve budgets, hiring, marketing and risk management.","zh":"企業決策可能涉及預算、招聘、市場推廣和風險管理。"},{"en":"Poor corporate decisions can affect employees, customers and investors.","zh":"差劣企業決策可以影響員工、顧客和投資者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing decisions inside companies.","zh":"討論公司內部決定時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"full consideration of","meaning":"充分考慮……","examples":[{"en":"Decisions should be made only after full consideration of the details.","zh":"決定應只在充分考慮細節後作出。"},{"en":"Full consideration of means careful attention to all important facts or factors.","zh":"full consideration of 指對所有重要事實或因素作仔細注意。"},{"en":"A family should move house only after full consideration of cost, transport and school needs.","zh":"家庭應在充分考慮費用、交通和學校需要後才搬屋。"},{"en":"Full consideration reduces the risk of missing a serious problem.","zh":"充分考慮可減少錯過嚴重問題的風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when careful review is necessary.","zh":"當需要仔細檢視時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"potential by-product of","meaning":"……的潛在副產品","examples":[{"en":"Rushed judgement may be a potential by-product of workplace pressure.","zh":"倉促判斷可能是工作場所壓力的潛在副產品。"},{"en":"A potential by-product of something is a possible secondary result of it.","zh":"potential by-product of something 指某事可能產生的次要結果。"},{"en":"Stress may be a potential by-product of too many exams in one week.","zh":"壓力可能是一週內太多考試的潛在副產品。"},{"en":"Workplace pressure can create fast decisions even when nobody intends to rush.","zh":"工作場所壓力可以造成快速決定，即使沒有人有意倉促行事。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one problem produces another side effect.","zh":"當一個問題產生另一個副作用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"look into motives","meaning":"深入研究動機","examples":[{"en":"Some approaches look into the motives behind a problem.","zh":"有些方法會深入研究問題背後的動機。"},{"en":"Look into motives means examine the reasons why people act in certain ways.","zh":"look into motives 指檢視人們為何以某種方式行動。"},{"en":"A teacher may look into a student’s motives before judging disruptive behaviour.","zh":"老師可能在判斷擾亂課堂行為前，深入了解學生動機。"},{"en":"Understanding motives can reveal fear, pressure or misunderstanding behind actions.","zh":"理解動機可以揭示行動背後的恐懼、壓力或誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when behaviour needs deeper explanation.","zh":"當行為需要更深層解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the primary reason for","meaning":"……的主要原因","examples":[{"en":"Poor problem definition may be the primary reason for repeated failure.","zh":"問題定義不清可能是反覆失敗的主要原因。"},{"en":"The primary reason for means the main cause of something.","zh":"primary reason for 指某事的主要成因。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep may be the primary reason for a student’s poor concentration.","zh":"睡眠不足可能是學生專注力差的主要原因。"},{"en":"Identifying the primary reason helps people avoid wasting time on minor causes.","zh":"識別主要原因有助人避免把時間浪費在次要原因上。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when naming the main cause.","zh":"說明主要成因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"continued problems","meaning":"持續出現的問題","examples":[{"en":"Temporary solutions can result in continued problems.","zh":"暫時解決方案可能導致持續出現的問題。"},{"en":"Continued problems are problems that keep happening because they have not been properly solved.","zh":"continued problems 指因未被妥善解決而持續發生的問題。"},{"en":"A building may have continued problems with leaks if only the ceiling is painted.","zh":"如果只是粉刷天花，大廈可能持續出現漏水問題。"},{"en":"Continued problems show that earlier action was incomplete or misdirected.","zh":"持續問題顯示早前行動不完整或方向錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when trouble does not stop.","zh":"當麻煩沒有停止時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"easily identified form of","meaning":"容易辨認的……形式","examples":[{"en":"Poor judgement may be an easily identified form of weak management.","zh":"差劣判斷可能是欠佳管理能力中容易辨認的形式。"},{"en":"An easily identified form of something is a clear example that can be recognised quickly.","zh":"easily identified form of something 指能快速被認出的清楚例子。"},{"en":"Frequent lateness is an easily identified form of poor time management.","zh":"經常遲到是時間管理差中容易辨認的形式。"},{"en":"Clear examples help people understand a wider weakness.","zh":"清楚例子幫助人理解更廣泛弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one visible sign represents a larger issue.","zh":"當一個可見跡象代表更大問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"weak managerial ability","meaning":"欠佳的管理能力","examples":[{"en":"Poor decisions may reveal weak managerial ability.","zh":"差劣決定可能揭示欠佳的管理能力。"},{"en":"Weak managerial ability means limited skill in leading, organising and making decisions.","zh":"weak managerial ability 指在領導、組織和決策方面能力有限。"},{"en":"A manager with weak managerial ability may avoid difficult conversations with staff.","zh":"管理能力欠佳的經理可能避免與員工進行困難對話。"},{"en":"Weak ability can cause confusion, low morale and repeated mistakes.","zh":"欠佳能力可以造成混亂、低士氣和反覆錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when poor leadership skill is being judged.","zh":"當評估差劣領導技能時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"seek a staff member","meaning":"尋找一名職員","examples":[{"en":"Managers should not immediately seek a staff member to blame.","zh":"經理不應立即尋找一名職員來責怪。"},{"en":"Seek a staff member means look for an employee for a particular purpose.","zh":"seek a staff member 指為某特定目的尋找一名員工。"},{"en":"A teacher should not seek a student to blame before understanding why a window broke.","zh":"老師在理解窗戶為何破裂前，不應尋找學生來責怪。"},{"en":"Looking for a person to blame too early can stop real investigation.","zh":"太早尋找責怪對象會阻止真正調查。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone is searching for a particular employee.","zh":"當某人正在尋找特定員工時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"place responsibility on","meaning":"把責任推到……身上","examples":[{"en":"Finger-pointing places responsibility on a particular employee.","zh":"互相指責會把責任推到某個特定員工身上。"},{"en":"Place responsibility on means say that a person or group is responsible for something.","zh":"place responsibility on 指說某人或某群體對某事負責。"},{"en":"A school should not place responsibility on one child before checking all facts.","zh":"學校在查清所有事實前，不應把責任推到一個孩子身上。"},{"en":"Responsibility should be based on evidence, not emotion or convenience.","zh":"責任應建基於證據，而不是情緒或方便。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when blame or accountability is assigned.","zh":"當責任或問責被歸屬時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have negative effects","meaning":"產生負面影響","examples":[{"en":"Blame can have negative effects on workplace relationships.","zh":"責怪可以對工作場所關係產生負面影響。"},{"en":"Have negative effects means cause harmful results.","zh":"have negative effects 指造成有害結果。"},{"en":"Too much screen time can have negative effects on sleep.","zh":"太多螢幕時間可以對睡眠產生負面影響。"},{"en":"Blame damages relationships because people become defensive and fearful.","zh":"責怪會損害關係，因為人們變得防衛和害怕。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an action causes harm.","zh":"當某行動造成傷害時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be formulated long before","meaning":"早在……之前形成","examples":[{"en":"Decision-making habits may be formulated long before entering business.","zh":"決策習慣可能早在進入商業世界前已形成。"},{"en":"Be formulated long before means be formed much earlier than a later event.","zh":"be formulated long before 指早在之後某事件之前已形成。"},{"en":"Study habits may be formulated long before students enter university.","zh":"學習習慣可能早在學生進入大學之前已形成。"},{"en":"Early experiences shape later behaviour before people notice the connection.","zh":"早期經驗在人們察覺關聯之前，已塑造後來行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when later actions have early roots.","zh":"當後來行動有早期根源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"business application","meaning":"商業應用","examples":[{"en":"Personal conditioning exists before it has any business application.","zh":"個人制約在有任何商業應用之前已存在。"},{"en":"Business application means practical use in business situations.","zh":"business application 指在商業情況中的實際用途。"},{"en":"A communication theory has business application if it helps managers handle conflict.","zh":"如果溝通理論幫助經理處理衝突，它就有商業應用。"},{"en":"Some ideas begin as personal habits before they affect workplace decisions.","zh":"有些想法先是個人習慣，之後才影響工作場所決策。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an idea is applied to commercial practice.","zh":"當某概念被應用於商業實踐時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"long-term solutions","meaning":"長遠解決方案","examples":[{"en":"Long-term solutions require an accurate understanding of the problem.","zh":"長遠解決方案需要準確理解問題。"},{"en":"Long-term solutions are solutions designed to last and prevent future recurrence.","zh":"long-term solutions 指旨在持久並防止日後重複出現的解決方案。"},{"en":"Better sleep habits are a long-term solution to constant tiredness.","zh":"較好的睡眠習慣是不斷疲倦的長遠解決方案。"},{"en":"Long-term solutions often take more effort than quick fixes.","zh":"長遠解決方案通常比快速補救需要更多努力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when future stability matters.","zh":"當未來穩定性重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"ask the right questions","meaning":"提出正確問題","examples":[{"en":"Managers can identify the real issue by asking the right questions.","zh":"經理可以透過提出正確問題來識別真正問題。"},{"en":"Ask the right questions means use questions that reveal useful facts and causes.","zh":"ask the right questions 指使用能揭示有用事實和原因的問題。"},{"en":"A doctor asks the right questions to understand when symptoms began and what makes them worse.","zh":"醫生提出正確問題，以理解症狀何時開始及甚麼令症狀惡化。"},{"en":"Wrong questions can lead people away from the real problem.","zh":"錯誤問題可能把人帶離真正問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when good investigation depends on questioning.","zh":"當良好調查取決於提問時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete the flowchart","meaning":"完成流程圖","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the flowchart with words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的詞語完成流程圖。"},{"en":"Complete the flowchart means fill missing labels or steps in a diagram showing a process.","zh":"complete the flowchart 指在展示過程的圖表中填入缺失標籤或步驟。"},{"en":"Students complete the flowchart after understanding the order of events.","zh":"學生理解事件次序後完成流程圖。"},{"en":"This task tests whether readers can follow sequence and cause.","zh":"這項任務測試讀者能否跟隨次序和因果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading-comprehension instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於閱讀理解指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"one word only","meaning":"只可填一個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain one word only.","zh":"每個答案只應包含一個字。"},{"en":"One word only means the answer must use exactly one word.","zh":"one word only 指答案必須剛好使用一個詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “beliefs”, students should not write “personal beliefs” in a one-word-only gap.","zh":"如果答案是 “beliefs”，學生在只可填一個字的空格中不應寫 “personal beliefs”。"},{"en":"Word limits matter because extra words can make an answer wrong.","zh":"字數限制很重要，因為額外詞語可能令答案錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in IELTS-style completion tasks.","zh":"這個短語適用於 IELTS 式填空題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"opt to","meaning":"選擇去……","examples":[{"en":"Our actions reflect what we opt to do or not do.","zh":"我們的行動反映我們選擇去做或不做甚麼。"},{"en":"Opt to means choose to do something.","zh":"opt to 指選擇去做某事。"},{"en":"A student may opt to revise early rather than wait until the night before an exam.","zh":"學生可能選擇提早溫習，而不是等到考試前一晚。"},{"en":"What people opt to do reveals their priorities.","zh":"人們選擇去做的事揭示他們的優先次序。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing deliberate choice.","zh":"討論有意識選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"at a particular time","meaning":"在某一特定時刻","examples":[{"en":"A person’s mood may change at a particular time.","zh":"一個人的情緒可能在某一特定時刻改變。"},{"en":"At a particular time means at one specific moment or period.","zh":"at a particular time 指在某個特定時刻或時段。"},{"en":"A student may feel nervous at a particular time, such as just before a speech.","zh":"學生可能在某一特定時刻感到緊張，例如演講前。"},{"en":"Timing matters because mood and pressure can change judgement.","zh":"時間重要，因為情緒和壓力可以改變判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a situation depends on a specific moment.","zh":"當情況取決於特定時刻時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"personally held beliefs","meaning":"個人所持的信念","examples":[{"en":"Some beliefs are only personally held beliefs.","zh":"有些信念只是個人所持的信念。"},{"en":"Personally held beliefs are ideas that an individual believes, not necessarily proven facts.","zh":"personally held beliefs 指個人相信的想法，不一定是已證實的事實。"},{"en":"A manager may have personally held beliefs about what makes workers lazy.","zh":"經理可能對甚麼令員工懶惰有個人所持的信念。"},{"en":"Such beliefs can bias decisions if they are not tested against evidence.","zh":"如果這類信念沒有用證據檢驗，就可能令決定有偏差。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when private belief is separated from truth.","zh":"當私人信念與真相被分開時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"universally true","meaning":"普遍正確的","examples":[{"en":"A personally held belief is not necessarily universally true.","zh":"個人所持的信念不一定普遍正確。"},{"en":"Universally true means true for everyone, everywhere or in all cases.","zh":"universally true 指對所有人、所有地方或所有情況都成立。"},{"en":"The idea that silence means agreement is not universally true across cultures.","zh":"沉默代表同意這個想法在不同文化中並不普遍正確。"},{"en":"Treating personal beliefs as universal truths can create unfair decisions.","zh":"把個人信念當作普遍真理，可能造成不公平決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when warning against overgeneralisation.","zh":"警告不要過度概括時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be conditioned to react","meaning":"受到制約而作出反應","examples":[{"en":"People may be conditioned to react in particular ways.","zh":"人們可能受到制約而以特定方式作出反應。"},{"en":"Be conditioned to react means be trained by experience or culture to respond automatically.","zh":"be conditioned to react 指因經驗或文化訓練而自動回應。"},{"en":"A child may be conditioned to react nervously when adults raise their voices.","zh":"孩子可能受到制約，在成年人提高聲線時緊張反應。"},{"en":"Conditioning shapes reactions before people consciously choose them.","zh":"制約在人們有意識選擇前已塑造反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when learned habits influence response.","zh":"當習得習慣影響回應時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be influenced by place of birth","meaning":"受出生地影響","examples":[{"en":"Early conditioning is often influenced by a person’s place of birth.","zh":"早期制約常受一個人的出生地影響。"},{"en":"Be influenced by place of birth means be shaped partly by the culture and society where someone was born.","zh":"be influenced by place of birth 指部分受到某人出生地的文化和社會塑造。"},{"en":"A person born in a quiet village may have different social habits from someone born in a busy city.","zh":"出生在安靜村莊的人，可能與出生在繁忙城市的人有不同社交習慣。"},{"en":"Place of birth can affect language, values and ideas about authority.","zh":"出生地可以影響語言、價值觀和對權威的看法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when background shapes behaviour.","zh":"當背景塑造行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"agree with the views given","meaning":"與文中觀點一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether statements agree with the views given in the passage.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與文章中給出的觀點一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the views given means match the opinions expressed in the text.","zh":"agree with the views given 指與文本中表達的意見相符。"},{"en":"Students should not use personal opinion when deciding whether a statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與文章一致時，不應使用個人意見。"},{"en":"This task checks understanding of the writer’s or speakers’ views.","zh":"這項任務檢查對作者或說話者觀點的理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in YES, NO, NOT GIVEN reading questions.","zh":"這個短語適用於 YES、NO、NOT GIVEN 閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"contradict the views","meaning":"與觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement is marked NO if it contradicts the writer’s views.","zh":"如果陳述與作者觀點相矛盾，就標記為 NO。"},{"en":"Contradict the views means say the opposite of what someone believes or states.","zh":"contradict the views 指說出與某人相信或陳述內容相反的意思。"},{"en":"If an article supports homework but a statement says the writer opposes homework, it contradicts the views.","zh":"如果文章支持功課，但陳述說作者反對功課，它就與觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction is different from missing information because the text clearly says the opposite.","zh":"矛盾不同於資料缺失，因為文本清楚說出相反內容。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading-comprehension judgement tasks.","zh":"這個短語適用於閱讀理解判斷題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write NOT GIVEN when it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"當無法判斷作者想法時，考生寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means the information is not provided clearly enough to decide.","zh":"impossible to say 指資訊沒有清楚提供，不能作出判斷。"},{"en":"If a passage mentions a teacher but not her age, it is impossible to say how old she is.","zh":"如果文章提到一位老師但沒有提及年齡，就無法判斷她幾歲。"},{"en":"In reading tests, guessing beyond the text can lead to wrong answers.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，超出文本猜測可能導致錯誤答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence is insufficient.","zh":"當證據不足時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"mental processes behind","meaning":"……背後的心理過程","examples":[{"en":"Researchers study the mental processes behind decision making.","zh":"研究人員研究決策背後的心理過程。"},{"en":"Mental processes behind means the thinking, feeling and judgement that influence an action.","zh":"mental processes behind 指影響行動的思考、感受和判斷。"},{"en":"Teachers may study the mental processes behind exam fear to help anxious students.","zh":"老師可能研究考試恐懼背後的心理過程，以幫助焦慮學生。"},{"en":"Understanding mental processes explains why decisions are not always logical.","zh":"理解心理過程可以解釋為何決定不總是合乎邏輯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when hidden thinking shapes behaviour.","zh":"當隱藏思維塑造行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"completely disagree with","meaning":"完全不同意……","examples":[{"en":"Filke does not completely disagree with Hewings’ approach.","zh":"Filke 並非完全不同意 Hewings 的方法。"},{"en":"Completely disagree with means reject an idea fully or strongly.","zh":"completely disagree with 指完全或強烈拒絕某想法。"},{"en":"A student may completely disagree with a rule but still follow it respectfully.","zh":"學生可能完全不同意某條規則，但仍尊重地遵守。"},{"en":"Not completely disagreeing means accepting some parts while questioning others.","zh":"並非完全不同意，意思是接受部分內容，同時質疑其他部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing the strength of disagreement.","zh":"顯示不同意的程度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"conclusion drawn by","meaning":"由……得出的結論","examples":[{"en":"Filke questions part of the conclusion drawn by Hewings.","zh":"Filke 質疑 Hewings 得出的部分結論。"},{"en":"A conclusion drawn by someone is an opinion or judgement they reach after thinking or analysis.","zh":"conclusion drawn by someone 指某人經思考或分析後得出的意見或判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher may question the conclusion drawn by a student if the evidence is weak.","zh":"如果證據薄弱，老師可能質疑學生得出的結論。"},{"en":"Conclusions should be tested because reasoning can be incomplete.","zh":"結論應被檢驗，因為推理可能不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing someone’s final judgement.","zh":"討論某人的最終判斷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be related to psychology","meaning":"與心理學有關","examples":[{"en":"Some managers believe successful decision making is related to psychology.","zh":"有些經理相信成功決策與心理學有關。"},{"en":"Be related to psychology means be connected with thinking, emotion, motivation or mental habits.","zh":"be related to psychology 指與思考、情緒、動機或心理習慣有關。"},{"en":"A student’s fear of speaking may be related to psychology rather than language ability alone.","zh":"學生害怕說話可能與心理學有關，而不只是語言能力問題。"},{"en":"Decision making is related to psychology because beliefs and feelings shape judgement.","zh":"決策與心理學有關，因為信念和感受塑造判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when mental factors help explain behaviour.","zh":"當心理因素有助解釋行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 9 - PROBLEM SOLVING AND DECISION MAKING.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 14":[{"front":"Clinical Trials","meaning":"臨床試驗","examples":[{"en":"Clinical trials determine whether new treatments are safe and effective.","zh":"臨床試驗判斷新療法是否安全有效。"},{"en":"Clinical trials are research studies that test medical treatments in people.","zh":"臨床試驗是在人身上測試醫療方法的研究。"},{"en":"A hospital may run clinical trials to see whether a new cancer drug works better than an older one.","zh":"醫院可能進行臨床試驗，以了解一種新癌症藥是否比舊藥更有效。"},{"en":"If clinical trials show serious side-effects, the treatment may not be approved.","zh":"如果臨床試驗顯示嚴重副作用，該療法可能不會獲批准。"},{"en":"Clinical trials protect patients by testing treatments carefully before wide use.","zh":"臨床試驗透過在廣泛使用前仔細測試療法來保護病人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the benefits of","meaning":"……的好處","examples":[{"en":"The benefits of vitamins to human well-being are now widely understood.","zh":"維他命對身心健康的好處如今已被廣泛理解。"},{"en":"The benefits of something are the good effects or advantages it brings.","zh":"The benefits of something 指某事帶來的好影響或優點。"},{"en":"The benefits of regular sleep include better memory, mood and concentration.","zh":"規律睡眠的好處包括更好的記憶、心情和專注力。"},{"en":"If people understand the benefits of exercise, they may be more willing to walk every day.","zh":"如果人們理解運動的好處，他們可能更願意每天步行。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why something is valuable.","zh":"這個片語適合用來解釋某事為何有價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"human well-being","meaning":"身心健康","examples":[{"en":"A balanced diet contributes to physical and mental well-being.","zh":"均衡飲食有助身體和心理健康。"},{"en":"Human well-being means people’s overall health, happiness and quality of life.","zh":"Human well-being 指人的整體健康、幸福感和生活質素。"},{"en":"Safe housing, clean water and enough rest all support human well-being.","zh":"安全住屋、清潔食水和充足休息都支持身心健康。"},{"en":"Poor working conditions can damage human well-being by causing stress and illness.","zh":"惡劣工作條件可透過造成壓力和疾病損害身心健康。"},{"en":"This phrase includes both body and mind, not only survival.","zh":"這個片語包括身體和心理，而不只是生存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be familiar to most people","meaning":"為大多數人所熟悉","examples":[{"en":"The health benefits of vitamins are familiar to most people.","zh":"維他命的健康好處為大多數人所熟悉。"},{"en":"If something is familiar to most people, many people already know or recognise it.","zh":"如果某事 familiar to most people，即許多人已經知道或認得它。"},{"en":"The idea that sleep helps learning is familiar to most students.","zh":"睡眠有助學習這個想法為大多數學生所熟悉。"},{"en":"When a problem is familiar to most people, writers do not need to explain every basic detail.","zh":"當某問題為大多數人所熟悉，作者不需要解釋每個基本細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes common public knowledge.","zh":"這個片語描述常見的公眾知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"diets lacking in","meaning":"缺乏……的飲食","examples":[{"en":"Diets lacking in fresh fruit may cause serious nutritional deficiencies.","zh":"缺乏新鮮水果的飲食可能造成嚴重營養缺乏。"},{"en":"Diets lacking in something are eating patterns that do not contain enough of it.","zh":"Diets lacking in something 指沒有足夠某物的飲食模式。"},{"en":"A diet lacking in vegetables may leave a child short of fibre and minerals.","zh":"缺乏蔬菜的飲食可能令孩子缺少纖維和礦物質。"},{"en":"If a diet is lacking in protein, recovery after illness may become slower.","zh":"如果飲食缺乏蛋白質，病後恢復可能變慢。"},{"en":"This phrase points to what is missing from someone’s food.","zh":"這個片語指出某人的食物中缺少甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"citrus fruits","meaning":"柑橘類水果","examples":[{"en":"Citrus fruits are an important source of Vitamin C.","zh":"柑橘類水果是維他命 C 的重要來源。"},{"en":"Citrus fruits are fruits such as oranges, lemons, limes and grapefruits.","zh":"Citrus fruits 是橙、檸檬、青檸和西柚等水果。"},{"en":"A parent may pack citrus fruits in a lunch box to add vitamins naturally.","zh":"家長可能把柑橘類水果放入飯盒，以自然補充維他命。"},{"en":"Eating citrus fruits can help prevent problems linked to very low Vitamin C intake.","zh":"食用柑橘類水果可以幫助預防與維他命 C 攝取極低有關的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a group of sharp-tasting fruits rich in juice.","zh":"這個片語指一類味道酸爽而多汁的水果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the development of","meaning":"……的形成；發展","examples":[{"en":"A lack of Vitamin C can lead to the development of scurvy.","zh":"缺乏維他命 C 可導致壞血病的形成。"},{"en":"The development of a disease means the process by which it begins and becomes worse.","zh":"The development of a disease 指疾病開始並惡化的過程。"},{"en":"Poor posture can contribute to the development of back pain over time.","zh":"姿勢不良可隨時間促成背痛的形成。"},{"en":"Early treatment may stop the development of a small problem into a serious illness.","zh":"早期治療可能阻止小問題發展成嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a condition forming gradually.","zh":"這個片語描述某種狀況逐漸形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the affliction scurvy","meaning":"壞血病這種疾病","examples":[{"en":"Scurvy was once a common affliction among sailors.","zh":"壞血病這種疾病曾經在水手之中很常見。"},{"en":"The affliction scurvy means the disease called scurvy, especially when described as a source of suffering.","zh":"The affliction scurvy 指稱為壞血病的疾病，尤其是把它描述為痛苦來源時。"},{"en":"In old sea voyages, the affliction scurvy could weaken whole crews.","zh":"在古代遠洋航行中，壞血病這種疾病可削弱整支船員隊伍。"},{"en":"If sailors lacked fresh food for months, the affliction scurvy became more likely.","zh":"如果水手數月缺乏新鮮食物，壞血病這種疾病就更可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase presents scurvy as a painful medical problem.","zh":"這個片語把壞血病呈現為痛苦的醫學問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be first discovered by","meaning":"最先由……發現","examples":[{"en":"The connection between citrus fruit and scurvy was first studied by James Lind.","zh":"柑橘類水果與壞血病之間的關係最先由 James Lind 研究。"},{"en":"If something was first discovered by someone, that person was the earliest known person to identify it.","zh":"If something was first discovered by someone，指某人是最早已知識別該事物的人。"},{"en":"A new plant species may be first discovered by a local researcher during fieldwork.","zh":"一種新植物物種可能最先由本地研究人員在田野考察中發現。"},{"en":"First discoveries often become important because they open a new line of investigation.","zh":"最早發現常變得重要，因為它們開啟新的研究方向。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the person linked to the earliest finding.","zh":"這個片語指出與最早發現相關的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the concept of vitamins","meaning":"維他命的概念","examples":[{"en":"The concept of vitamins had not yet been developed in the eighteenth century.","zh":"維他命的概念在十八世紀尚未形成。"},{"en":"The concept of vitamins means the scientific idea that certain small nutrients are essential for health.","zh":"The concept of vitamins 指某些微量營養素對健康不可或缺這個科學想法。"},{"en":"Before this concept existed, doctors could see results without knowing the exact nutrient involved.","zh":"在這個概念存在之前，醫生可能看到效果，卻不知道涉及哪種確切營養素。"},{"en":"A new scientific concept can help people explain observations that once seemed mysterious.","zh":"新科學概念可以幫助人解釋曾經神秘的觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an idea in science, not to the vitamins themselves.","zh":"這個片語指科學中的一個想法，而不是維他命本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"yet to be discovered","meaning":"尚未被發現","examples":[{"en":"Vitamin C was yet to be discovered when Lind conducted his trial.","zh":"Lind 進行試驗時，維他命 C 尚未被發現。"},{"en":"Yet to be discovered means not discovered at that time, though it may be discovered later.","zh":"Yet to be discovered 指在當時尚未被發現，雖然之後可能被發現。"},{"en":"Many causes of disease were yet to be discovered before modern microscopes.","zh":"在現代顯微鏡出現之前，許多疾病成因尚未被發現。"},{"en":"When an answer is yet to be discovered, researchers can only work with limited evidence.","zh":"當答案尚未被發現，研究人員只能使用有限證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes knowledge that still lies in the future.","zh":"這個片語描述仍屬未來的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"scurvy","meaning":"壞血病","examples":[{"en":"Scurvy results from a severe deficiency of Vitamin C.","zh":"壞血病由嚴重缺乏維他命 C 引起。"},{"en":"Scurvy is a disease caused by not having enough Vitamin C for a long time.","zh":"Scurvy 是長期沒有足夠維他命 C 所造成的疾病。"},{"en":"Sailors on long voyages once developed scurvy when they lacked fresh fruit and vegetables.","zh":"遠洋航行的水手曾因缺乏新鮮水果和蔬菜而患上壞血病。"},{"en":"Scurvy can weaken the gums, skin and body because connective tissues are affected.","zh":"壞血病可因結締組織受影響而削弱牙肉、皮膚和身體。"},{"en":"This word names a nutritional disease, not a general infection.","zh":"這個詞命名一種營養缺乏病，而不是一般感染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"softening of the gums","meaning":"牙肉變軟","examples":[{"en":"Scurvy can cause softening of the gums.","zh":"壞血病可以導致牙肉變軟。"},{"en":"Softening of the gums means the gum tissue becomes weak, tender or less firm.","zh":"Softening of the gums 指牙肉組織變弱、敏感或不再堅實。"},{"en":"A dentist may notice softening of the gums during an oral examination.","zh":"牙醫可能在口腔檢查中注意到牙肉變軟。"},{"en":"If the gums soften, brushing and eating may become painful.","zh":"如果牙肉變軟，刷牙和進食可能變得疼痛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one possible mouth symptom of disease.","zh":"這個片語描述疾病可能造成的一種口腔症狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"oral bleeding","meaning":"口腔出血","examples":[{"en":"Oral bleeding is one possible symptom of advanced scurvy.","zh":"口腔出血是晚期壞血病的一個可能症狀。"},{"en":"Oral bleeding means bleeding from the mouth, gums or other oral tissues.","zh":"Oral bleeding 指口腔、牙肉或其他口腔組織出血。"},{"en":"A patient should tell a dentist if oral bleeding occurs without clear injury.","zh":"如果沒有明顯受傷卻出現口腔出血，病人應告訴牙醫。"},{"en":"Serious vitamin deficiency can make oral bleeding more likely.","zh":"嚴重維他命缺乏可令口腔出血更可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bleeding that happens inside the mouth.","zh":"這個片語描述口腔內發生的出血。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in extreme cases","meaning":"在極端情況下","examples":[{"en":"In extreme cases, the disease can cause tooth loss.","zh":"在極端情況下，這種疾病可導致牙齒脫落。"},{"en":"In extreme cases means in the most serious or unusual situations.","zh":"In extreme cases 指在最嚴重或最不尋常的情況下。"},{"en":"In extreme cases, heatstroke can require urgent hospital treatment.","zh":"在極端情況下，中暑可能需要緊急入院治療。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when describing what may happen if a problem becomes very severe.","zh":"這個片語用於描述問題變得非常嚴重時可能發生甚麼。"},{"en":"It warns that the result is possible but not ordinary.","zh":"它提醒讀者該結果可能發生，但並不普通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tooth loss","meaning":"牙齒脫落","examples":[{"en":"Advanced gum disease may eventually result in tooth loss.","zh":"晚期牙周疾病最終可能導致牙齒脫落。"},{"en":"Tooth loss means losing one or more teeth.","zh":"Tooth loss 指失去一隻或多隻牙齒。"},{"en":"A dentist may warn that untreated infection can lead to tooth loss.","zh":"牙醫可能警告，未經治療的感染可導致牙齒脫落。"},{"en":"Tooth loss can affect eating, speech and confidence.","zh":"牙齒脫落可影響進食、說話和自信。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious result of dental or nutritional problems.","zh":"這個片語描述牙科或營養問題的嚴重結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be known to result from","meaning":"已知由……引起","examples":[{"en":"Scurvy is now known to result from a lack of Vitamin C.","zh":"壞血病現已知由缺乏維他命 C 引起。"},{"en":"Be known to result from means scientists or experts understand that something is caused by something else.","zh":"Be known to result from 指科學家或專家理解某事由另一事物造成。"},{"en":"Some headaches are known to result from dehydration and lack of sleep.","zh":"一些頭痛已知由脫水和睡眠不足引起。"},{"en":"Once a disease is known to result from a deficiency, prevention becomes easier.","zh":"一旦疾病已知由缺乏某物引起，預防就變得更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase links a condition with an established cause.","zh":"這個片語把某狀況與已確立原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lack of Vitamin C","meaning":"缺乏維他命 C","examples":[{"en":"A lack of Vitamin C weakens the body’s connective tissues.","zh":"缺乏維他命 C 會削弱身體的結締組織。"},{"en":"A lack of Vitamin C means the body does not receive enough of this essential nutrient.","zh":"Lack of Vitamin C 指身體沒有攝取足夠這種必需營養素。"},{"en":"People who rarely eat fruit or vegetables may risk a lack of Vitamin C.","zh":"很少吃水果或蔬菜的人可能有缺乏維他命 C 的風險。"},{"en":"A long-term lack of Vitamin C can lead to scurvy.","zh":"長期缺乏維他命 C 可導致壞血病。"},{"en":"This phrase names the nutritional shortage behind the disease.","zh":"這個片語命名該疾病背後的營養缺乏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"additional symptoms","meaning":"其他症狀","examples":[{"en":"Additional symptoms may appear as the illness becomes more severe.","zh":"隨着疾病變得更嚴重，其他症狀可能出現。"},{"en":"Additional symptoms are extra signs of illness beyond the first or main ones.","zh":"Additional symptoms 是主要或最初症狀以外的額外病徵。"},{"en":"A doctor may ask whether a fever comes with additional symptoms such as coughing or pain.","zh":"醫生可能詢問發燒是否伴隨咳嗽或疼痛等其他症狀。"},{"en":"If additional symptoms appear, the illness may need closer attention.","zh":"如果其他症狀出現，疾病可能需要更密切注意。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe how a condition becomes more complex.","zh":"這個片語幫助描述病情如何變得更複雜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"liver spots","meaning":"皮膚色素斑","examples":[{"en":"Some patients develop dark liver spots on their skin.","zh":"一些病人皮膚上會出現深色皮膚色素斑。"},{"en":"Liver spots are dark patches or marks that appear on the skin.","zh":"Liver spots 是出現在皮膚上的深色斑點或痕跡。"},{"en":"A nurse may record liver spots if they appear with other unusual symptoms.","zh":"如果皮膚色素斑伴隨其他異常症狀出現，護士可能會記錄。"},{"en":"Skin marks can help doctors understand what is happening inside the body.","zh":"皮膚斑點可幫助醫生理解身體內部正在發生甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible discolouration on the skin.","zh":"這個片語描述皮膚上可見的變色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"loss of colour in the face","meaning":"面色變得蒼白","examples":[{"en":"Scurvy may cause a noticeable loss of colour in the face.","zh":"壞血病可能導致面色明顯變得蒼白。"},{"en":"Loss of colour in the face means the face becomes pale or less healthy-looking.","zh":"Loss of colour in the face 指面部變得蒼白或看起來較不健康。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice loss of colour in a student’s face before the student faints.","zh":"學生暈倒前，老師可能注意到他的面色變得蒼白。"},{"en":"Illness, shock or weakness can cause the face to lose colour.","zh":"疾病、驚嚇或虛弱可導致面色變得蒼白。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible paleness as a sign of poor condition.","zh":"這個片語描述作為健康狀況差的可見蒼白。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"partial immobility","meaning":"局部行動不便","examples":[{"en":"Severe illness may lead to pain and partial immobility.","zh":"嚴重疾病可能導致疼痛和局部行動不便。"},{"en":"Partial immobility means a person can move only with difficulty or cannot move some body parts fully.","zh":"Partial immobility 指人移動困難，或某些身體部位不能完全活動。"},{"en":"After a knee injury, an athlete may suffer partial immobility for several weeks.","zh":"膝傷後，運動員可能有數星期局部行動不便。"},{"en":"Pain and weakness can cause partial immobility by limiting normal movement.","zh":"疼痛和虛弱可透過限制正常活動而造成局部行動不便。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited movement, not complete paralysis.","zh":"這個片語描述活動受限，而不是完全癱瘓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a high incidence of","meaning":"……的高發病率","examples":[{"en":"There was a high incidence of scurvy aboard long-distance ships.","zh":"長途船隻上壞血病發病率很高。"},{"en":"A high incidence of something means it happens often in a particular group or place.","zh":"A high incidence of something 指某事在特定群體或地方經常發生。"},{"en":"A school may report a high incidence of flu during winter.","zh":"學校可能報告冬季流感發病率很高。"},{"en":"If there is a high incidence of illness, prevention and monitoring become important.","zh":"如果疾病發病率很高，預防和監察就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for describing how common a problem is.","zh":"這個片語適合描述問題有多常見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the ailment","meaning":"這種疾病","examples":[{"en":"The ailment severely affected sailors on long voyages.","zh":"這種疾病嚴重影響長途航行的水手。"},{"en":"The ailment means the illness or medical condition being discussed.","zh":"The ailment 指正在討論的疾病或醫療狀況。"},{"en":"A doctor may ask how long the ailment has affected the patient’s daily life.","zh":"醫生可能詢問這種疾病影響病人日常生活多久。"},{"en":"If an ailment spreads through a workplace, productivity and attendance may fall.","zh":"如果一種疾病在工作場所蔓延，生產力和出勤率可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating the disease name.","zh":"這個片語避免重複疾病名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"aboard ships","meaning":"在船上","examples":[{"en":"Scurvy was particularly common aboard ships.","zh":"壞血病在船上特別常見。"},{"en":"Aboard ships means on or inside ships.","zh":"Aboard ships 指在船上或船內。"},{"en":"Food supplies aboard ships must be planned carefully before a long journey.","zh":"長途旅程前，船上的食物供應必須仔細規劃。"},{"en":"If fresh food is unavailable aboard ships, sailors may face nutritional problems.","zh":"如果船上沒有新鮮食物，水手可能面對營養問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something happening on vessels at sea.","zh":"這個片語描述在海上船隻中發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"take an enormous toll on","meaning":"對……造成沉重打擊","examples":[{"en":"The illness took an enormous toll on the crew’s working ability.","zh":"這種疾病對船員的工作能力造成沉重打擊。"},{"en":"To take an enormous toll on something means to damage it very seriously over time.","zh":"To take an enormous toll on something 指隨時間對某事造成非常嚴重的損害。"},{"en":"Long working hours can take an enormous toll on a nurse’s health.","zh":"長時間工作可對護士健康造成沉重打擊。"},{"en":"If a disease takes an enormous toll on workers, essential tasks may be delayed.","zh":"如果疾病對工人造成沉重打擊，必要工作可能被延誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes heavy damage or burden.","zh":"這個片語描述沉重損害或負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the crew’s ability to","meaning":"船員做……的能力","examples":[{"en":"Scurvy reduced the crew’s ability to complete essential tasks.","zh":"壞血病削弱船員完成必要工作的能力。"},{"en":"The crew’s ability to do something means how well the ship workers can perform that action.","zh":"The crew’s ability to do something 指船上工作人員完成某行動的能力。"},{"en":"Bad weather can reduce the crew’s ability to repair equipment safely.","zh":"惡劣天氣可降低船員安全修理設備的能力。"},{"en":"If many crew members become sick, the crew’s ability to operate the ship declines.","zh":"如果許多船員患病，船員操作船隻的能力會下降。"},{"en":"This phrase connects workers’ health with their capacity to work.","zh":"這個片語把工人健康與工作能力連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"complete essential tasks","meaning":"完成必要工作","examples":[{"en":"Healthy sailors were needed to complete essential tasks at sea.","zh":"海上需要健康水手完成必要工作。"},{"en":"To complete essential tasks means to finish necessary jobs that cannot be ignored.","zh":"To complete essential tasks 指完成不能忽視的必要工作。"},{"en":"In a hospital, nurses must complete essential tasks such as giving medicine and checking patients.","zh":"在醫院，護士必須完成派藥和檢查病人等必要工作。"},{"en":"If too many workers are absent, essential tasks may be left unfinished.","zh":"如果太多工人缺勤，必要工作可能無法完成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doing work that is necessary for safety or normal operation.","zh":"這個片語描述完成對安全或正常運作必需的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"while at sea","meaning":"在海上期間","examples":[{"en":"Sailors had limited access to fresh food while at sea.","zh":"水手在海上期間獲得新鮮食物的機會有限。"},{"en":"While at sea means during the time when a ship is away from land.","zh":"While at sea 指船隻離開陸地期間。"},{"en":"Passengers may lose phone signal while at sea.","zh":"乘客在海上期間可能失去電話訊號。"},{"en":"Food and medical supplies must be managed carefully while at sea because shops are not nearby.","zh":"在海上期間，食物和醫療用品必須小心管理，因為附近沒有商店。"},{"en":"This phrase describes conditions during a sea journey.","zh":"這個片語描述海上旅程期間的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lower the incidence of","meaning":"降低……的發病率","examples":[{"en":"Citrus fruit was believed to lower the incidence of scurvy.","zh":"柑橘類水果被認為可以降低壞血病的發病率。"},{"en":"To lower the incidence of something means to reduce how often it happens.","zh":"To lower the incidence of something 指減少某事發生的頻率。"},{"en":"Vaccination can lower the incidence of some infectious diseases.","zh":"疫苗接種可以降低某些傳染病的發病率。"},{"en":"Better hygiene can lower the incidence of stomach illness in schools.","zh":"更好衛生可降低學校腸胃病發病率。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing the frequency of a problem.","zh":"這個片語描述減少問題出現頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prevent scurvy","meaning":"預防壞血病","examples":[{"en":"Regular consumption of citrus fruit can prevent scurvy.","zh":"定期食用柑橘類水果可以預防壞血病。"},{"en":"To prevent scurvy means to stop the disease from developing.","zh":"To prevent scurvy 指阻止壞血病形成。"},{"en":"Sailors could prevent scurvy by receiving enough Vitamin C during long voyages.","zh":"水手在長途航行中攝取足夠維他命 C，就可以預防壞血病。"},{"en":"If a diet lacks fresh produce for months, preventing scurvy becomes difficult.","zh":"如果飲食數月缺乏新鮮農產品，預防壞血病就變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on stopping the disease before it appears.","zh":"這個片語集中於在疾病出現前阻止它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"as early as 1600","meaning":"早於1600年","examples":[{"en":"The protective effect of citrus fruit was suggested as early as 1600.","zh":"柑橘類水果的保護作用早於1600年已被提出。"},{"en":"As early as 1600 means surprisingly far back in time, already by the year 1600.","zh":"As early as 1600 指早至1600年，時間比人們可能想像更早。"},{"en":"Some public health ideas were discussed as early as the nineteenth century.","zh":"一些公共健康想法早於十九世紀已被討論。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that an idea existed earlier than readers may expect.","zh":"這個片語強調某想法比讀者預期更早存在。"},{"en":"It is often used to highlight historical depth.","zh":"它常用來突出歷史深度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"conduct the first clinical trial","meaning":"進行首個臨床試驗","examples":[{"en":"James Lind conducted what is often regarded as the first clinical trial.","zh":"James Lind 進行了常被視為首個臨床試驗的研究。"},{"en":"To conduct the first clinical trial means to carry out the earliest known organised test of a treatment on people.","zh":"To conduct the first clinical trial 指進行最早已知、在人身上有組織地測試療法的試驗。"},{"en":"A doctor who tests two treatments carefully may conduct a simple clinical trial.","zh":"仔細測試兩種療法的醫生可能進行一個簡單臨床試驗。"},{"en":"Conducting a trial requires planning, comparison and careful observation.","zh":"進行試驗需要規劃、比較和仔細觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of modern treatment testing.","zh":"這個片語描述現代療法測試的開端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"study the effect of","meaning":"研究……的效果","examples":[{"en":"Lind studied the effect of different dietary supplements on scurvy.","zh":"Lind 研究不同膳食補充品對壞血病的效果。"},{"en":"To study the effect of something means to examine what change it causes.","zh":"To study the effect of something 指檢視某事會造成甚麼變化。"},{"en":"A teacher may study the effect of daily reading on students’ vocabulary.","zh":"老師可能研究每日閱讀對學生詞彙量的效果。"},{"en":"If researchers study an effect carefully, they need a clear comparison group.","zh":"如果研究人員仔細研究某種效果，他們需要清楚的比較組。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an action or treatment with its result.","zh":"這個片語把行動或療法與其結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"scientific experimental parameters","meaning":"科學實驗準則","examples":[{"en":"The trial was conducted within scientific experimental parameters.","zh":"該試驗在科學實驗準則之內進行。"},{"en":"Scientific experimental parameters are the rules and conditions that shape a fair experiment.","zh":"Scientific experimental parameters 是塑造公平實驗的規則和條件。"},{"en":"A school experiment needs parameters such as equal time, equal materials and a clear measurement.","zh":"學校實驗需要相同時間、相同材料和清楚量度等準則。"},{"en":"Without experimental parameters, results may be confusing or unfair.","zh":"沒有實驗準則，結果可能混亂或不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the controlled framework of a scientific test.","zh":"這個片語描述科學測試的受控框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"correlation between A and B","meaning":"A 與 B 之間的關聯","examples":[{"en":"Lind established a correlation between citrus consumption and recovery.","zh":"Lind 確立柑橘類水果攝取與康復之間的關聯。"},{"en":"A correlation between A and B means A and B are connected or tend to happen together.","zh":"Correlation between A and B 指 A 和 B 有聯繫，或傾向一起發生。"},{"en":"A school may find a correlation between regular homework and higher test scores.","zh":"學校可能發現定期做功課與較高測驗分數之間有關聯。"},{"en":"A correlation does not always prove that one thing directly causes the other.","zh":"關聯不一定證明一件事直接導致另一件事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a statistical or observed relationship.","zh":"這個片語描述統計上或觀察到的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"consume citrus fruit","meaning":"食用柑橘類水果","examples":[{"en":"Sailors who consumed citrus fruit showed rapid improvement.","zh":"食用柑橘類水果的水手顯示迅速改善。"},{"en":"To consume citrus fruit means to eat or drink fruits such as oranges and lemons.","zh":"To consume citrus fruit 指吃或飲用橙和檸檬等水果。"},{"en":"A child may consume citrus fruit by eating an orange after lunch.","zh":"孩子午飯後吃橙，就是食用柑橘類水果。"},{"en":"If people consume citrus fruit regularly, they may receive more Vitamin C.","zh":"如果人們定期食用柑橘類水果，他們可能攝取更多維他命 C。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on taking the fruit into the body.","zh":"這個片語集中於把水果攝入身體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"avoidance of scurvy","meaning":"避免患上壞血病","examples":[{"en":"Citrus fruit was associated with the avoidance of scurvy.","zh":"柑橘類水果與避免患上壞血病有關。"},{"en":"Avoidance of scurvy means preventing the disease from occurring.","zh":"Avoidance of scurvy 指防止壞血病發生。"},{"en":"On long voyages, the avoidance of scurvy depended on access to suitable food.","zh":"在長途航行中，避免患上壞血病取決於是否有合適食物。"},{"en":"If sailors lacked citrus fruit, avoidance of scurvy became much harder.","zh":"如果水手缺乏柑橘類水果，避免患上壞血病就困難得多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes staying free from the disease.","zh":"這個片語描述不患上該疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"establish a correlation","meaning":"確立關聯","examples":[{"en":"The trial established a correlation but not the correct biological explanation.","zh":"該試驗確立了關聯，但沒有得出正確的生物學解釋。"},{"en":"To establish a correlation means to show that two things are connected in some way.","zh":"To establish a correlation 指顯示兩件事在某方面有聯繫。"},{"en":"Researchers may establish a correlation between exercise and lower stress.","zh":"研究人員可能確立運動與較低壓力之間的關聯。"},{"en":"Establishing a correlation is useful, but it may not explain the exact cause.","zh":"確立關聯有用，但未必能解釋確切原因。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a relationship without always proving mechanism.","zh":"這個片語顯示關係，但不一定證明機制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"preventative properties","meaning":"預防功效","examples":[{"en":"The preventative properties of citrus fruit were misunderstood.","zh":"柑橘類水果的預防功效被誤解。"},{"en":"Preventative properties are qualities that help stop a problem or disease from happening.","zh":"Preventative properties 是幫助阻止問題或疾病發生的特質。"},{"en":"Sunscreen has preventative properties because it reduces skin damage from sunlight.","zh":"防曬霜有預防功效，因為它減少陽光對皮膚的傷害。"},{"en":"If a food has preventative properties, it may lower the risk of a disease.","zh":"如果某種食物有預防功效，它可能降低疾病風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protective qualities.","zh":"這個片語描述保護性特質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be attributed to","meaning":"被歸因於……","examples":[{"en":"The benefits were mistakenly attributed to acids in the fruit.","zh":"這些好處被錯誤地歸因於水果中的酸性物質。"},{"en":"Be attributed to means be explained as being caused by something.","zh":"Be attributed to 指被解釋為由某事造成。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be attributed to regular practice and feedback.","zh":"學生的進步可能被歸因於定期練習和回饋。"},{"en":"If a cause is wrongly attributed, people may choose the wrong solution.","zh":"如果原因被錯誤歸因，人們可能選擇錯誤解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase links an effect with a supposed cause.","zh":"這個片語把結果與被認為的原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the presence of acids","meaning":"酸性物質的存在","examples":[{"en":"Doctors believed that the presence of acids explained the fruit’s effect.","zh":"醫生相信酸性物質的存在解釋了水果的效果。"},{"en":"The presence of acids means that acidic substances are found in something.","zh":"Presence of acids 指某物中含有酸性物質。"},{"en":"The sharp taste of lemon juice shows the presence of acids.","zh":"檸檬汁的酸味顯示酸性物質的存在。"},{"en":"If doctors focus only on the presence of acids, they may miss other important nutrients.","zh":"如果醫生只專注酸性物質的存在，他們可能錯過其他重要營養素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what substances exist inside a material or food.","zh":"這個片語描述某材料或食物內存在甚麼物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"vitamin content","meaning":"維他命含量","examples":[{"en":"The fruit’s vitamin content was not understood at the time.","zh":"當時人們並不了解水果的維他命含量。"},{"en":"Vitamin content means the amount and type of vitamins contained in a food.","zh":"Vitamin content 指食物中所含維他命的種類和分量。"},{"en":"A nutrition label may show the vitamin content of a breakfast cereal.","zh":"營養標籤可能顯示早餐穀物的維他命含量。"},{"en":"If a food has high vitamin content, it may help prevent nutritional deficiencies.","zh":"如果食物維他命含量高，它可能幫助預防營養缺乏。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the nutrients inside food.","zh":"這個片語集中於食物內的營養素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"subjects for a trial","meaning":"試驗對象","examples":[{"en":"Lind’s subjects for the trial were twelve sailors with scurvy.","zh":"Lind 的試驗對象是十二名患有壞血病的水手。"},{"en":"Subjects for a trial are the people who take part in a research study.","zh":"Subjects for a trial 是參與研究的人。"},{"en":"A vaccine study may need healthy adults as subjects for a trial.","zh":"疫苗研究可能需要健康成年人作為試驗對象。"},{"en":"If suitable subjects cannot be found, the trial may be delayed.","zh":"如果找不到合適試驗對象，試驗可能延誤。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to human participants in an experiment.","zh":"這個片語指實驗中的人體參加者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"consist of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"The study group consisted of twelve sailors.","zh":"研究組由十二名水手組成。"},{"en":"Consist of means be made up of particular parts or members.","zh":"Consist of 指由特定部分或成員組成。"},{"en":"A school team may consist of six players and two substitutes.","zh":"學校隊伍可能由六名球員和兩名後備組成。"},{"en":"If a study consists of too few people, its results may be limited.","zh":"如果研究由太少人組成，其結果可能有限。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what something includes.","zh":"這個片語解釋某事包括甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"exhibit symptoms of","meaning":"出現……的症狀","examples":[{"en":"All twelve sailors were already exhibiting symptoms of scurvy.","zh":"十二名水手當時已經出現壞血病症狀。"},{"en":"To exhibit symptoms of a disease means to show signs that the disease is present.","zh":"To exhibit symptoms of a disease 指顯示某疾病存在的病徵。"},{"en":"A child exhibiting symptoms of flu may have a fever, cough and tiredness.","zh":"出現流感症狀的孩子可能有發燒、咳嗽和疲倦。"},{"en":"If patients exhibit symptoms before treatment, doctors can track whether they improve.","zh":"如果病人在治療前出現症狀，醫生可以追蹤他們是否改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible signs of illness.","zh":"這個片語描述可見的疾病徵象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be split into groups","meaning":"被分成多組","examples":[{"en":"The sailors were split into six treatment groups.","zh":"水手被分成六個治療組。"},{"en":"Be split into groups means be divided into smaller sets for comparison or organisation.","zh":"Be split into groups 指為了比較或組織而被分成較小組別。"},{"en":"Students may be split into groups to discuss different essay topics.","zh":"學生可能被分成多組，討論不同作文題目。"},{"en":"In a trial, splitting people into groups allows researchers to compare treatments.","zh":"在試驗中，把人分成多組讓研究人員比較療法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised division.","zh":"這個片語描述有組織的分組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"each pair","meaning":"每一對","examples":[{"en":"Each pair of sailors received a different supplement.","zh":"每一對水手接受不同補充品。"},{"en":"Each pair means every group of two people or things.","zh":"Each pair 指每一組兩個人或兩件事物。"},{"en":"In a speaking activity, each pair of students may practise one dialogue.","zh":"在口語活動中，每一對學生可能練習一段對話。"},{"en":"If each pair receives a different task, the class can compare several results.","zh":"如果每一對收到不同任務，全班可以比較幾個結果。"},{"en":"This phrase organises people or items in twos.","zh":"這個片語把人或物以二人或兩件一組組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a common diet","meaning":"相同的基本飲食","examples":[{"en":"All the sailors shared a common basic diet.","zh":"所有水手都有相同的基本飲食。"},{"en":"A common diet means the same basic food given to everyone in a study or group.","zh":"Common diet 指研究或群體中每個人得到的相同基本食物。"},{"en":"In a school camp, students may share a common diet prepared by the kitchen.","zh":"在學校營地，學生可能吃由廚房準備的相同基本飲食。"},{"en":"Using a common diet in a trial helps researchers compare only the added treatment.","zh":"在試驗中使用相同基本飲食，有助研究人員只比較額外療法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shared food conditions.","zh":"這個片語描述共同的食物條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be rationed","meaning":"獲定量供應","examples":[{"en":"One pair was rationed a daily quantity of cider.","zh":"其中一對水手獲定量供應每日一定分量的蘋果酒。"},{"en":"Be rationed means be given a fixed limited amount of something.","zh":"Be rationed 指獲得固定而有限的某物分量。"},{"en":"During a shortage, families may be rationed water or food.","zh":"在短缺期間，家庭可能獲定量供應食水或食物。"},{"en":"Rationing helps control supplies when there is not enough for unlimited use.","zh":"定量供應在物資不足以無限制使用時有助控制供應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled distribution.","zh":"這個片語描述受控制的分配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a daily quart of cider","meaning":"每日一夸脫蘋果酒","examples":[{"en":"One treatment group received a daily quart of cider.","zh":"其中一個治療組每日收到一夸脫蘋果酒。"},{"en":"A daily quart of cider means a measured amount of cider given every day.","zh":"Daily quart of cider 指每天給予的量好的一定分量蘋果酒。"},{"en":"In a trial, a daily dose must be recorded clearly so results can be compared.","zh":"在試驗中，每日劑量必須清楚記錄，結果才可比較。"},{"en":"If each group receives a different daily amount, researchers can study different effects.","zh":"如果每組收到不同每日分量，研究人員可以研究不同效果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fixed daily ration.","zh":"這個片語描述固定每日配給。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"elixir of vitriol","meaning":"硫酸酏劑","examples":[{"en":"One pair was given elixir of vitriol, a diluted acidic preparation.","zh":"其中一對水手獲給予硫酸酏劑，即一種稀釋酸性製劑。"},{"en":"Elixir of vitriol was an old acidic medical preparation used in Lind’s trial.","zh":"Elixir of vitriol 是 Lind 試驗中使用的一種古老酸性醫療製劑。"},{"en":"Historical medical texts may mention elixir of vitriol even though it is not a modern vitamin treatment.","zh":"歷史醫學文本可能提到硫酸酏劑，雖然它不是現代維他命療法。"},{"en":"Using elixir of vitriol showed that Lind was comparing several possible remedies.","zh":"使用硫酸酏劑顯示 Lind 正在比較幾種可能療法。"},{"en":"This phrase names one of the treatments used in the historical experiment.","zh":"這個片語命名歷史實驗中使用的其中一種治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a given quantity of","meaning":"指定分量的……","examples":[{"en":"Another group received a given quantity of vinegar.","zh":"另一組收到指定分量的醋。"},{"en":"A given quantity of something is a fixed amount decided in advance.","zh":"Given quantity of something 是事先決定的固定分量。"},{"en":"A recipe may require a given quantity of salt so the taste stays consistent.","zh":"食譜可能需要指定分量的鹽，以保持味道一致。"},{"en":"In a trial, a given quantity helps researchers control what each group receives.","zh":"在試驗中，指定分量有助研究人員控制每組收到甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an exact or predetermined amount.","zh":"這個片語描述精確或預先決定的分量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"barley water","meaning":"大麥水","examples":[{"en":"One pair was treated with barley water.","zh":"其中一對水手接受大麥水治療。"},{"en":"Barley water is a drink made by boiling barley in water.","zh":"Barley water 是用水煮大麥製成的飲品。"},{"en":"Some families drink barley water when they want a mild, simple drink.","zh":"一些家庭想喝溫和簡單飲品時會飲大麥水。"},{"en":"In Lind’s trial, barley water was tested as one possible treatment.","zh":"在 Lind 的試驗中，大麥水被測試為一種可能療法。"},{"en":"This phrase names a food-based preparation used in the comparison.","zh":"這個片語命名比較中使用的一種食物製劑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have to be aborted","meaning":"被迫中止","examples":[{"en":"The trial had to be aborted after only five days.","zh":"試驗只進行五天後便被迫中止。"},{"en":"Have to be aborted means must be stopped before completion.","zh":"Have to be aborted 指必須在完成前停止。"},{"en":"A school trip may have to be aborted if a storm makes travel unsafe.","zh":"如果暴風雨令出行不安全，學校旅行可能被迫中止。"},{"en":"If supplies run out, an experiment may have to be aborted before enough data is collected.","zh":"如果物資耗盡，實驗可能在收集足夠數據前被迫中止。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an early forced ending.","zh":"這個片語描述被迫提早結束。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"supplies be depleted","meaning":"物資被耗盡","examples":[{"en":"The study ended when the supplies of citrus fruit were depleted.","zh":"當柑橘類水果供應被耗盡，研究便結束。"},{"en":"Supplies are depleted when they are used up or reduced to nothing.","zh":"Supplies are depleted 指物資被用盡或減少至沒有。"},{"en":"A school event may stop early if water supplies are depleted on a hot day.","zh":"在炎熱日子，如果食水物資被耗盡，學校活動可能提早停止。"},{"en":"If medical supplies are depleted, treatment plans may have to change.","zh":"如果醫療物資被耗盡，治療計劃可能必須改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes resources running out.","zh":"這個片語描述資源用完。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"findings of the study","meaning":"研究結果","examples":[{"en":"The findings of the study showed a clear benefit from fruit.","zh":"研究結果顯示水果帶來明顯好處。"},{"en":"Findings of the study are the results or conclusions produced by research.","zh":"Findings of the study 是研究產生的結果或結論。"},{"en":"The findings of a school survey may show that students need more quiet study space.","zh":"學校問卷的研究結果可能顯示學生需要更多安靜自修空間。"},{"en":"If findings are clear, they can influence future decisions.","zh":"如果研究結果清楚，它們可以影響未來決定。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to what researchers learn from a study.","zh":"這個片語指研究人員從研究中得知的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"interventional study","meaning":"干預性研究","examples":[{"en":"Lind’s experiment was an early interventional study.","zh":"Lind 的實驗是一項早期干預性研究。"},{"en":"An interventional study is research in which investigators actively give a treatment or change a condition.","zh":"Interventional study 是研究人員主動給予療法或改變條件的研究。"},{"en":"A diet study is interventional if researchers assign one group a new meal plan.","zh":"如果研究人員安排一組人採用新飲食計劃，該飲食研究就是干預性研究。"},{"en":"Interventional studies can show more than observation because researchers test a planned change.","zh":"干預性研究比單純觀察顯示更多，因為研究人員測試有計劃改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research involving active intervention.","zh":"這個片語描述涉及主動干預的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fruit supplements","meaning":"水果補充品","examples":[{"en":"The group receiving fruit supplements improved rapidly.","zh":"接受水果補充品的一組迅速改善。"},{"en":"Fruit supplements are added portions of fruit given in addition to the basic diet.","zh":"Fruit supplements 是在基本飲食之外額外給予的水果分量。"},{"en":"A school lunch programme may provide fruit supplements to children who rarely eat fresh produce.","zh":"學校午餐計劃可能向很少吃新鮮農產品的孩子提供水果補充品。"},{"en":"If fruit supplements provide missing nutrients, health may improve.","zh":"如果水果補充品提供缺失營養，健康可能改善。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to fruit used as an extra dietary addition.","zh":"這個片語指作為額外飲食補充的水果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"show significant improvement","meaning":"顯示明顯改善","examples":[{"en":"Only the sailors given citrus fruit showed significant improvement.","zh":"只有獲給予柑橘類水果的水手顯示明顯改善。"},{"en":"To show significant improvement means to become clearly and importantly better.","zh":"To show significant improvement 指變得清楚而重要地更好。"},{"en":"A student may show significant improvement after practising writing every week.","zh":"學生每週練習寫作後，可能顯示明顯改善。"},{"en":"If only one treatment group improves significantly, that treatment may deserve closer study.","zh":"如果只有一個治療組明顯改善，該療法可能值得進一步研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improvement large enough to matter.","zh":"這個片語描述大到有意義的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"recover to the extent that","meaning":"康復至……的程度","examples":[{"en":"One sailor recovered to the extent that he could return to work.","zh":"一名水手康復至能夠恢復工作的程度。"},{"en":"Recover to the extent that means improve so much that a particular action becomes possible.","zh":"Recover to the extent that 指改善很多，以致某個行動變得可能。"},{"en":"After physiotherapy, a patient may recover to the extent that she can walk without help.","zh":"物理治療後，病人可能康復至可以不用攙扶行走的程度。"},{"en":"If someone recovers to that extent, the treatment has produced a practical benefit.","zh":"如果某人康復至那種程度，治療就產生了實際好處。"},{"en":"This phrase links recovery with a concrete ability.","zh":"這個片語把康復與具體能力連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be fit enough to","meaning":"健康狀況足以……","examples":[{"en":"The sailor became fit enough to resume his duties.","zh":"該水手健康狀況足以恢復職務。"},{"en":"Be fit enough to means be healthy or strong enough to do something.","zh":"Be fit enough to 指健康或體力足以做某事。"},{"en":"After resting for two days, a student may be fit enough to return to school.","zh":"休息兩天後，學生可能健康狀況足以回校。"},{"en":"If a worker is not fit enough to lift heavy boxes, someone else should help.","zh":"如果工人健康狀況不足以搬重箱，應由其他人協助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical readiness for an action.","zh":"這個片語描述身體上準備好做某行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"return to work","meaning":"恢復工作","examples":[{"en":"One participant recovered sufficiently to return to work.","zh":"一名參加者康復至足以恢復工作。"},{"en":"To return to work means to go back to one’s job or duties after absence or illness.","zh":"To return to work 指在缺席或患病後回到工作或職務。"},{"en":"A teacher may return to work after recovering from flu.","zh":"老師從流感康復後可能恢復工作。"},{"en":"Returning to work shows that a person is well enough to handle normal responsibilities.","zh":"恢復工作顯示一個人健康狀況足以處理正常責任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes resuming regular duties.","zh":"這個片語描述重新開始日常職務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"immediate impact on","meaning":"對……的即時影響","examples":[{"en":"The findings had limited immediate impact on sailors’ health.","zh":"這些研究結果對水手健康的即時影響有限。"},{"en":"Immediate impact on something means the direct effect that happens soon after an event or discovery.","zh":"Immediate impact on something 指某事件或發現之後很快出現的直接影響。"},{"en":"A new school rule may have an immediate impact on students’ morning routines.","zh":"新校規可能對學生早上日常有即時影響。"},{"en":"If research has little immediate impact, its importance may still grow later.","zh":"如果研究即時影響很小，其重要性仍可能日後增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes short-term influence.","zh":"這個片語描述短期影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"incidence of scurvy","meaning":"壞血病的發病率","examples":[{"en":"The incidence of scurvy remained high for many years.","zh":"壞血病的發病率多年來仍然很高。"},{"en":"Incidence of scurvy means how often scurvy occurred in a population or group.","zh":"Incidence of scurvy 指壞血病在某人口或群體中出現的頻率。"},{"en":"Doctors tried to reduce the incidence of scurvy among sailors.","zh":"醫生嘗試降低水手之中的壞血病發病率。"},{"en":"If citrus fruit was not used properly, the incidence of scurvy could remain high.","zh":"如果柑橘類水果沒有被正確使用，壞血病發病率可能仍然很高。"},{"en":"This phrase measures how common the disease was.","zh":"這個片語量度該疾病有多常見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"remain convinced that","meaning":"仍然深信","examples":[{"en":"Many physicians remained convinced that acids caused the curative effect.","zh":"許多醫生仍然深信酸性物質造成治療作用。"},{"en":"Remain convinced that means continue to strongly believe something.","zh":"Remain convinced that 指繼續強烈相信某事。"},{"en":"Some parents remain convinced that children learn best through practice.","zh":"有些家長仍然深信孩子透過練習學得最好。"},{"en":"If experts remain convinced of a wrong explanation, better evidence may be ignored.","zh":"如果專家仍然深信錯誤解釋，更好的證據可能被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a belief that continues over time.","zh":"這個片語描述隨時間持續的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"curative effect","meaning":"治療作用","examples":[{"en":"The curative effect of citrus fruit was incorrectly explained.","zh":"柑橘類水果的治療作用被錯誤解釋。"},{"en":"Curative effect means the ability of something to help cure or improve a disease.","zh":"Curative effect 指某物幫助治癒或改善疾病的能力。"},{"en":"Doctors test whether a new medicine has a curative effect on an infection.","zh":"醫生測試新藥是否對感染有治療作用。"},{"en":"If a treatment has a curative effect, patients should improve after receiving it.","zh":"如果療法有治療作用，病人接受後應會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes healing power or treatment effect.","zh":"這個片語描述治癒能力或治療效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be acid-based","meaning":"以酸性作用為基礎","examples":[{"en":"Doctors mistakenly believed that the treatment’s effect was acid-based.","zh":"醫生錯誤地相信該療法的效果以酸性作用為基礎。"},{"en":"Be acid-based means be caused by or mainly dependent on acids.","zh":"Be acid-based 指由酸性物質造成或主要依賴酸性物質。"},{"en":"A cleaning product may be acid-based if it removes limescale with acidic chemicals.","zh":"如果清潔產品用酸性化學物去除水垢，它可能是以酸性作用為基礎。"},{"en":"If a medical effect is wrongly believed to be acid-based, doctors may choose ineffective substitutes.","zh":"如果醫療效果被錯誤地認為以酸性作用為基礎，醫生可能選擇無效替代品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an explanation centred on acids.","zh":"這個片語描述以酸性物質為中心的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"consumption of citrus fruit","meaning":"食用柑橘類水果","examples":[{"en":"The consumption of citrus fruit was recommended to sailors.","zh":"食用柑橘類水果被建議給水手。"},{"en":"Consumption of citrus fruit means eating or drinking citrus fruits.","zh":"Consumption of citrus fruit 指吃或飲用柑橘類水果。"},{"en":"A nutritionist may encourage the consumption of citrus fruit as part of a balanced diet.","zh":"營養師可能鼓勵把食用柑橘類水果作為均衡飲食的一部分。"},{"en":"Regular consumption of citrus fruit can increase Vitamin C intake.","zh":"定期食用柑橘類水果可以增加維他命 C 攝取。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking citrus fruit into the diet.","zh":"這個片語描述把柑橘類水果納入飲食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be recommended","meaning":"獲建議使用","examples":[{"en":"Citrus fruit was recommended even before its vitamin content was understood.","zh":"柑橘類水果在其維他命含量被理解前已獲建議使用。"},{"en":"Be recommended means be advised as a good or useful choice.","zh":"Be recommended 指被建議為良好或有用選擇。"},{"en":"Rest may be recommended after a mild injury.","zh":"輕傷後可能獲建議休息。"},{"en":"A treatment can be recommended before experts fully understand why it works.","zh":"療法可以在專家完全理解其原理前獲建議使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes professional or practical advice.","zh":"這個片語描述專業或實際建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be replaced by","meaning":"被……取代","examples":[{"en":"Fresh fruit was often replaced by cheaper acid supplements.","zh":"新鮮水果常被較便宜的酸性補充品取代。"},{"en":"Be replaced by means be removed and substituted with something else.","zh":"Be replaced by 指被移走並由其他東西替代。"},{"en":"Paper notices may be replaced by school app messages.","zh":"紙本通告可能被學校應用程式訊息取代。"},{"en":"If an effective treatment is replaced by a weaker one, results may become worse.","zh":"如果有效療法被較弱療法取代，結果可能變差。"},{"en":"This phrase describes substitution.","zh":"這個片語描述替換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cheaper substitutes","meaning":"較便宜的替代品","examples":[{"en":"Cheaper substitutes were used even though they were less effective.","zh":"較便宜的替代品被使用，即使它們效果較差。"},{"en":"Cheaper substitutes are lower-cost replacements for the original item.","zh":"Cheaper substitutes 是成本較低、用來取代原物的東西。"},{"en":"A school may buy cheaper substitutes for art materials when the budget is tight.","zh":"當預算緊張，學校可能購買較便宜的美術材料替代品。"},{"en":"Cheaper substitutes can save money, but they may not work as well.","zh":"較便宜的替代品可以省錢，但未必同樣有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes replacement items chosen mainly for lower cost.","zh":"這個片語描述主要因成本較低而選擇的替代物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be truly recognised","meaning":"得到真正認可","examples":[{"en":"The preventative qualities of citrus fruit were not truly recognised until 1800.","zh":"柑橘類水果的預防特質直到1800年才得到真正認可。"},{"en":"Be truly recognised means be fully understood and accepted as important.","zh":"Be truly recognised 指被充分理解並接受為重要。"},{"en":"A student’s effort may not be truly recognised until their final results improve.","zh":"學生的努力可能直到最終成績改善才得到真正認可。"},{"en":"If evidence is ignored, an important discovery may not be truly recognised for years.","zh":"如果證據被忽視，重要發現可能多年未得到真正認可。"},{"en":"This phrase describes full acceptance, not just partial notice.","zh":"這個片語描述完全接受，而不只是部分注意到。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"throughout the latter part of","meaning":"在……的後期","examples":[{"en":"Lemon juice was increasingly used throughout the latter part of the eighteenth century.","zh":"檸檬汁在十八世紀後期越來越常被使用。"},{"en":"Throughout the latter part of a period means during the later section of that time.","zh":"Throughout the latter part of a period 指在某段時間的後半部分期間。"},{"en":"Smartphones became common throughout the latter part of the 2000s.","zh":"智能電話在二零零零年代後期變得普遍。"},{"en":"If a practice spreads throughout the latter part of a century, it becomes more common over time.","zh":"如果某做法在一個世紀後期擴散，它會隨時間變得更常見。"},{"en":"This phrase places change in the later stage of a time period.","zh":"這個片語把變化放在某時期的後段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"administer something as a cure","meaning":"將……用作治療","examples":[{"en":"Doctors administered lemon juice as a cure for afflicted sailors.","zh":"醫生將檸檬汁用作治療患病水手。"},{"en":"To administer something as a cure means to give it as treatment for an illness.","zh":"To administer something as a cure 指把某物作為疾病治療給予病人。"},{"en":"A nurse may administer medicine as a cure only under approved medical instructions.","zh":"護士只可在獲批准醫療指示下將藥物用作治療。"},{"en":"If a substance is administered without evidence, patients may receive ineffective treatment.","zh":"如果某物在沒有證據下被給予，病人可能接受無效治療。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving a treatment for healing.","zh":"這個片語描述給予治療以達到治癒目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be afflicted with","meaning":"患有……","examples":[{"en":"Many sailors were already afflicted with scurvy before receiving treatment.","zh":"許多水手在接受治療前已患有壞血病。"},{"en":"Be afflicted with means be suffering from a disease or serious problem.","zh":"Be afflicted with 指正受某種疾病或嚴重問題折磨。"},{"en":"A village afflicted with drought may need emergency water supplies.","zh":"患有旱災問題的村莊可能需要緊急供水。"},{"en":"If patients are afflicted with a painful condition, they may be less willing to join trials.","zh":"如果病人患有痛苦疾病，他們可能較不願意參加試驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being seriously affected by something harmful.","zh":"這個片語描述受到有害事物嚴重影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"implementation of findings","meaning":"研究結果的實際應用","examples":[{"en":"The implementation of research findings into medicine can take many years.","zh":"研究結果在醫學中的實際應用可能需要多年。"},{"en":"Implementation of findings means putting research results into real practice.","zh":"Implementation of findings 指把研究結果放入真實實踐。"},{"en":"A school may delay the implementation of findings from a learning study until teachers are trained.","zh":"學校可能在教師接受培訓前，延遲學習研究結果的實際應用。"},{"en":"If findings are not implemented, research may not help the people it was meant to support.","zh":"如果研究結果沒有被實際應用，研究可能幫不到原本要支援的人。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on turning evidence into action.","zh":"這個片語集中於把證據轉化為行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"mainstream medicine","meaning":"主流醫療","examples":[{"en":"Clinical findings must be carefully assessed before entering mainstream medicine.","zh":"臨床發現進入主流醫療前必須被仔細評估。"},{"en":"Mainstream medicine means the widely accepted medical practice used by doctors and hospitals.","zh":"Mainstream medicine 指醫生和醫院廣泛接受和使用的醫療實踐。"},{"en":"A treatment enters mainstream medicine only after strong evidence and approval.","zh":"一種療法只有在有強證據和批准後才進入主流醫療。"},{"en":"If a remedy lacks testing, it should not quickly become part of mainstream medicine.","zh":"如果療法缺乏測試，它不應很快成為主流醫療的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to standard accepted healthcare.","zh":"這個片語指標準而被接受的醫療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an arduous and lengthy process","meaning":"艱辛而漫長的過程","examples":[{"en":"Developing a new medicine is an arduous and lengthy process.","zh":"研發新藥是一個艱辛而漫長的過程。"},{"en":"An arduous and lengthy process is difficult, demanding and takes a long time.","zh":"Arduous and lengthy process 是困難、要求高而且需時很長的過程。"},{"en":"Preparing for a major public exam can be an arduous and lengthy process.","zh":"準備大型公開考試可以是一個艱辛而漫長的過程。"},{"en":"Because drug development is arduous and lengthy, many ideas fail before reaching patients.","zh":"因為藥物研發艱辛而漫長，許多想法在到達病人前已失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses both difficulty and duration.","zh":"這個片語同時強調困難和時間長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"represent only a small stage","meaning":"只佔一個小階段","examples":[{"en":"Clinical trials represent only a small stage of drug development.","zh":"臨床試驗只佔藥物研發的一個小階段。"},{"en":"Represent only a small stage means form just one limited part of a larger process.","zh":"Represent only a small stage 指只構成較大過程中的有限一部分。"},{"en":"The interview may represent only a small stage of a long hiring process.","zh":"面試可能只佔漫長招聘過程中的一個小階段。"},{"en":"If people see only one stage, they may underestimate how much work happens before and after it.","zh":"如果人們只看見一個階段，他們可能低估前後有多少工作。"},{"en":"This phrase puts one part into a larger context.","zh":"這個片語把一部分放入較大背景中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"drug development","meaning":"藥物研發","examples":[{"en":"Drug development involves scientific, clinical and regulatory stages.","zh":"藥物研發涉及科學、臨床和監管階段。"},{"en":"Drug development is the process of discovering, testing and approving a medicine.","zh":"Drug development 是發現、測試和批准藥物的過程。"},{"en":"A pharmaceutical company may spend years on drug development before a product reaches hospitals.","zh":"製藥公司可能在產品到達醫院前花多年進行藥物研發。"},{"en":"Drug development can fail if a compound is unsafe or ineffective.","zh":"如果化合物不安全或無效，藥物研發可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the full journey from idea to approved medicine.","zh":"這個片語描述由想法到獲批藥物的完整旅程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"from research stage to launch","meaning":"從研究階段到推出市場","examples":[{"en":"A drug passes through many stages from research to market launch.","zh":"一種藥物從研究階段到推出市場會經過許多階段。"},{"en":"From research stage to launch means from early investigation to public release for use or sale.","zh":"From research stage to launch 指由早期研究到公開推出使用或出售。"},{"en":"A new app may take months from research stage to launch.","zh":"一個新應用程式可能由研究階段到推出市場需要數月。"},{"en":"Many checks happen from research stage to launch so mistakes can be found early.","zh":"從研究階段到推出市場期間會有許多檢查，以便及早發現錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the whole development timeline.","zh":"這個片語描述整個發展時間線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"launch in the marketplace","meaning":"推出市場","examples":[{"en":"Only a small proportion of new drugs reach launch in the marketplace.","zh":"只有一小部分新藥能推出市場。"},{"en":"Launch in the marketplace means become available for sale or general use.","zh":"Launch in the marketplace 指可供出售或普遍使用。"},{"en":"A new phone may reach launch in the marketplace after design and testing are complete.","zh":"新手機在設計和測試完成後可能推出市場。"},{"en":"If a drug fails safety testing, it will not launch in the marketplace.","zh":"如果藥物安全測試失敗，它就不會推出市場。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the final public release of a product.","zh":"這個片語描述產品最終公開推出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on average","meaning":"平均而言","examples":[{"en":"On average, only one in a thousand drug concepts reaches clinical testing.","zh":"平均而言，每一千個藥物概念中只有一個進入臨床測試。"},{"en":"On average means when typical results are calculated across many cases.","zh":"On average 指把許多個案的典型結果計算出來。"},{"en":"On average, students may need several drafts before producing a strong essay.","zh":"平均而言，學生可能需要幾份草稿才寫出強文章。"},{"en":"Averages help show the general pattern, even if individual cases differ.","zh":"平均數幫助顯示一般模式，即使個別情況不同。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a typical or statistical estimate.","zh":"這個片語引入典型或統計估算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"drugs conceived","meaning":"構思中的藥物","examples":[{"en":"Most drugs conceived by researchers never enter human trials.","zh":"大多數由研究人員構思中的藥物從未進入人體試驗。"},{"en":"Drugs conceived by researchers are medicine ideas or compounds first imagined or designed by scientists.","zh":"Drugs conceived by researchers 是科學家最初想像或設計出的藥物想法或化合物。"},{"en":"A scientist may conceive a drug after studying how a disease attacks cells.","zh":"科學家研究疾病如何攻擊細胞後，可能構思一種藥物。"},{"en":"Many conceived drugs fail because early testing shows problems.","zh":"許多構思中的藥物失敗，因為早期測試顯示問題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to drug ideas at the very beginning.","zh":"這個片語指藥物想法的最初階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make it to the stage of","meaning":"成功進入……階段","examples":[{"en":"Only a tiny proportion of compounds make it to the stage of clinical trial.","zh":"只有極小部分化合物成功進入臨床試驗階段。"},{"en":"Make it to the stage of means successfully reach a later step in a process.","zh":"Make it to the stage of 指成功到達某過程中較後的步驟。"},{"en":"Only a few applicants make it to the stage of final interview.","zh":"只有少數申請者成功進入最後面試階段。"},{"en":"If a compound fails laboratory testing, it will not make it to clinical trials.","zh":"如果化合物未能通過實驗室測試，它就不能成功進入臨床試驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes surviving earlier stages and moving forward.","zh":"這個片語描述通過早期階段並繼續前進。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be abandoned for","meaning":"因……而被放棄","examples":[{"en":"Many drug-development projects are abandoned for scientific or financial reasons.","zh":"許多藥物研發項目因科學或財政原因而被放棄。"},{"en":"Be abandoned for a reason means be stopped because of that reason.","zh":"Be abandoned for a reason 指因某原因而停止。"},{"en":"A school trip may be abandoned for safety reasons during a typhoon.","zh":"颱風期間，學校旅行可能因安全原因而被放棄。"},{"en":"If research becomes too costly or unsafe, it may be abandoned.","zh":"如果研究變得太昂貴或不安全，它可能被放棄。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a project is given up.","zh":"這個片語解釋項目為何被放棄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a variety of reasons","meaning":"各種原因","examples":[{"en":"Projects fail for a variety of scientific and commercial reasons.","zh":"項目會因各種科學和商業原因而失敗。"},{"en":"A variety of reasons means several different causes or explanations.","zh":"A variety of reasons 指幾個不同成因或解釋。"},{"en":"Students may miss homework for a variety of reasons, including illness, stress or poor planning.","zh":"學生可能因疾病、壓力或規劃不良等各種原因欠交功課。"},{"en":"When failure has a variety of reasons, one simple solution may not be enough.","zh":"當失敗有各種原因，一個簡單解決方法可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that causes are multiple, not single.","zh":"這個片語顯示原因是多重的，而不是單一的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be fulfilled prior to","meaning":"必須在……之前完成","examples":[{"en":"Several stages must be fulfilled prior to clinical testing.","zh":"幾個階段必須在臨床測試之前完成。"},{"en":"Be fulfilled prior to means be completed before something else happens.","zh":"Be fulfilled prior to 指在另一件事發生前完成。"},{"en":"Safety checks must be fulfilled prior to opening a new playground.","zh":"安全檢查必須在新遊樂場開放前完成。"},{"en":"If early requirements are not fulfilled, later stages should not begin.","zh":"如果早期要求未完成，後期階段不應開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes necessary steps before the next stage.","zh":"這個片語描述下一階段前的必要步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"prior to clinical trial","meaning":"在臨床試驗之前","examples":[{"en":"Extensive laboratory work is required prior to clinical trial.","zh":"在臨床試驗之前，需要大量實驗室工作。"},{"en":"Prior to clinical trial means before a treatment is tested in people.","zh":"Prior to clinical trial 指在療法被用於人體測試之前。"},{"en":"A drug must be studied in the laboratory prior to clinical trial.","zh":"藥物必須在臨床試驗之前於實驗室中研究。"},{"en":"If risks appear prior to clinical trial, researchers may stop development early.","zh":"如果在臨床試驗之前出現風險，研究人員可能提早停止研發。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the testing period before human studies.","zh":"這個片語指人體研究之前的測試期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"human subjects","meaning":"人體試驗參加者","examples":[{"en":"Clinical trials test treatments on human subjects.","zh":"臨床試驗在人體試驗參加者身上測試療法。"},{"en":"Human subjects are people who take part in medical or scientific research.","zh":"Human subjects 是參與醫學或科學研究的人。"},{"en":"Researchers must protect human subjects through consent, monitoring and ethical rules.","zh":"研究人員必須透過同意書、監察和倫理規則保護人體試驗參加者。"},{"en":"If human subjects face unnecessary risk, a study should not continue.","zh":"如果人體試驗參加者面對不必要風險，研究不應繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people participating in experiments.","zh":"這個片語指參與實驗的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"drug discovery","meaning":"藥物發現","examples":[{"en":"Drug discovery is the earliest stage of pharmaceutical development.","zh":"藥物發現是製藥研發的最早階段。"},{"en":"Drug discovery means finding or designing substances that may become medicines.","zh":"Drug discovery 指尋找或設計可能成為藥物的物質。"},{"en":"Scientists may begin drug discovery by studying a disease target in cells.","zh":"科學家可能透過研究細胞中的疾病靶點開始藥物發現。"},{"en":"If no useful compound is found, drug discovery may not move forward.","zh":"如果找不到有用化合物，藥物發現可能不能繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first search for possible medicines.","zh":"這個片語描述對可能藥物的最初搜尋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"purification","meaning":"純化","examples":[{"en":"Purification removes unwanted substances from a drug compound.","zh":"純化會從藥物化合物中移除不需要的物質。"},{"en":"Purification is the process of making a substance cleaner by removing impurities.","zh":"Purification 是透過移除雜質令物質更潔淨的過程。"},{"en":"Water purification removes dirt and germs before people drink it.","zh":"食水純化在人飲用前去除污物和細菌。"},{"en":"If a compound is not purified, test results may be unreliable.","zh":"如果化合物沒有被純化，測試結果可能不可靠。"},{"en":"This word describes cleaning a substance for safer or clearer use.","zh":"這個詞描述為了更安全或更清楚使用而清潔物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"characterisation","meaning":"特性鑑定","examples":[{"en":"Characterisation identifies the chemical and biological properties of a compound.","zh":"特性鑑定識別化合物的化學和生物特性。"},{"en":"Characterisation means carefully describing what something is like and how it behaves.","zh":"Characterisation 指仔細描述某物的特點和行為方式。"},{"en":"In a lab, characterisation may show whether a material is stable, toxic or reactive.","zh":"在實驗室中，特性鑑定可能顯示材料是否穩定、有毒或會反應。"},{"en":"Without characterisation, researchers may not know how a compound works.","zh":"沒有特性鑑定，研究人員可能不知道化合物如何運作。"},{"en":"This word describes detailed scientific identification.","zh":"這個詞描述詳細的科學識別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"laboratory testing","meaning":"實驗室測試","examples":[{"en":"Laboratory testing takes place before a drug is given to humans.","zh":"藥物給予人類之前會進行實驗室測試。"},{"en":"Laboratory testing means examining something under controlled scientific conditions in a lab.","zh":"Laboratory testing 指在實驗室受控科學條件下檢查某物。"},{"en":"Food samples may undergo laboratory testing before a safety warning is issued.","zh":"食物樣本可能在發出安全警告前接受實驗室測試。"},{"en":"If laboratory testing finds danger, human testing may be delayed or stopped.","zh":"如果實驗室測試發現危險，人體測試可能被延遲或停止。"},{"en":"This phrase describes early controlled testing outside the human body.","zh":"這個片語描述人體外的早期受控測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a new pharmaceutical","meaning":"新藥","examples":[{"en":"A new pharmaceutical may take many years to reach patients.","zh":"新藥可能需要多年才到達病人手上。"},{"en":"A new pharmaceutical is a newly developed medicine or drug product.","zh":"New pharmaceutical 是新研發的藥物或藥品。"},{"en":"A company may invest heavily in a new pharmaceutical for treating rare disease.","zh":"公司可能大量投資一種治療罕見病的新藥。"},{"en":"If a new pharmaceutical fails safety tests, it cannot be widely used.","zh":"如果新藥安全測試失敗，它就不能被廣泛使用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a medicine in development or newly created.","zh":"這個片語指正在研發或新創造的藥物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"treatment of a disease","meaning":"疾病治療","examples":[{"en":"The company developed a pharmaceutical for the treatment of cancer.","zh":"該公司研發了一種用於癌症治療的新藥。"},{"en":"Treatment of a disease means medical action used to cure, control or reduce illness.","zh":"Treatment of a disease 指用來治癒、控制或減輕疾病的醫療行動。"},{"en":"The treatment of asthma may include inhalers and avoiding triggers.","zh":"哮喘治療可能包括吸入器和避開誘因。"},{"en":"Effective treatment of a disease can improve survival and quality of life.","zh":"有效疾病治療可以改善存活率和生活質素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes medical care aimed at a specific illness.","zh":"這個片語描述針對特定疾病的醫療護理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"typically take a period of","meaning":"一般需要……時間","examples":[{"en":"A new cancer drug typically takes a period of six years to reach clinical trials.","zh":"一種新癌症藥一般需要六年時間才進入臨床試驗。"},{"en":"Typically take a period of means usually require a certain amount of time.","zh":"Typically take a period of 指通常需要某段時間。"},{"en":"Learning a language typically takes a period of years, not weeks.","zh":"學習語言一般需要數年時間，而不是數星期。"},{"en":"If a process typically takes a long period, delays should not surprise people.","zh":"如果某過程通常需時很長，延誤就不應令人驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the usual duration of a process.","zh":"這個片語描述某過程的通常所需時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reach the clinical-trial stage","meaning":"進入臨床試驗階段","examples":[{"en":"Most proposed drugs never reach the clinical-trial stage.","zh":"大多數提議中的藥物從未進入臨床試驗階段。"},{"en":"Reach the clinical-trial stage means progress far enough to be tested in people.","zh":"Reach the clinical-trial stage 指進展到足以在人身上測試。"},{"en":"A treatment idea must pass lab tests before it can reach the clinical-trial stage.","zh":"療法構想必須通過實驗室測試，才能進入臨床試驗階段。"},{"en":"If early data is weak, a drug may never reach this stage.","zh":"如果早期數據薄弱，藥物可能永遠不能進入這個階段。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the move from pre-human testing to human studies.","zh":"這個片語標示由人體前測試走向人體研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"legislation requires that","meaning":"法例規定","examples":[{"en":"Legislation requires that trial participants be carefully monitored.","zh":"法例規定試驗參加者必須受到仔細監察。"},{"en":"Legislation requires that means the law says something must be done.","zh":"Legislation requires that 指法律規定某事必須做。"},{"en":"Legislation requires that restaurants keep kitchens clean to protect customers.","zh":"法例規定餐廳保持廚房清潔，以保護顧客。"},{"en":"If legislation requires careful monitoring, researchers cannot ignore patient safety.","zh":"如果法例規定仔細監察，研究人員不能忽視病人安全。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a legal requirement.","zh":"這個片語引入法律要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"subjects participating in trials","meaning":"參加試驗的受試者","examples":[{"en":"Subjects participating in trials must give informed consent.","zh":"參加試驗的受試者必須給予知情同意。"},{"en":"Subjects participating in trials are people who take part in medical research studies.","zh":"Subjects participating in trials 是參與醫學研究的人。"},{"en":"Patients participating in trials should understand the possible risks and benefits.","zh":"參加試驗的病人應了解可能風險和益處。"},{"en":"If subjects are not properly informed, the trial may be unethical.","zh":"如果受試者沒有獲充分告知，該試驗可能不符合倫理。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people involved in clinical research.","zh":"這個片語指參與臨床研究的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be monitored for","meaning":"在……期間受到監察","examples":[{"en":"Participants are monitored for a considerable period of time.","zh":"參加者在一段相當長時間內受到監察。"},{"en":"Be monitored for a period means be watched, checked or measured during that time.","zh":"Be monitored for a period 指在該段時間內被觀察、檢查或量度。"},{"en":"A patient may be monitored for several hours after surgery.","zh":"病人手術後可能在數小時內受到監察。"},{"en":"Monitoring helps doctors notice side-effects or improvement early.","zh":"監察幫助醫生及早注意副作用或改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing observation.","zh":"這個片語描述持續觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a considerable period of time","meaning":"一段相當長的時間","examples":[{"en":"Long-term effects must be studied over a considerable period of time.","zh":"長期影響必須經歷一段相當長時間研究。"},{"en":"A considerable period of time means quite a long time.","zh":"Considerable period of time 指相當長的一段時間。"},{"en":"Building reading confidence may take a considerable period of time.","zh":"建立閱讀信心可能需要一段相當長的時間。"},{"en":"Some side-effects appear only after a considerable period of time has passed.","zh":"有些副作用只有在一段相當長時間後才出現。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the process is not quick.","zh":"這個片語強調過程並不快速。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"side-effects and benefits","meaning":"副作用與益處","examples":[{"en":"Researchers assess both the side-effects and benefits of a drug.","zh":"研究人員評估一種藥物的副作用與益處。"},{"en":"Side-effects and benefits are the harmful and helpful results of a treatment.","zh":"Side-effects and benefits 是療法的有害和有幫助結果。"},{"en":"A doctor explains side-effects and benefits before a patient starts a new medicine.","zh":"醫生在病人開始新藥前會解釋副作用與益處。"},{"en":"If benefits are small but side-effects are serious, the treatment may not be suitable.","zh":"如果益處很小但副作用嚴重，該療法可能不合適。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the risks and advantages of treatment.","zh":"這個片語比較治療的風險和優點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be assessed correctly","meaning":"得到正確評估","examples":[{"en":"The treatment must be monitored so that its effects can be assessed correctly.","zh":"該療法必須受到監察，以便其效果得到正確評估。"},{"en":"Be assessed correctly means be judged accurately using proper evidence.","zh":"Be assessed correctly 指使用適當證據準確判斷。"},{"en":"A student’s writing should be assessed correctly with clear marking criteria.","zh":"學生寫作應使用清楚評分準則得到正確評估。"},{"en":"If data is incomplete, a drug’s safety may not be assessed correctly.","zh":"如果數據不完整，藥物安全性可能不能得到正確評估。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on fair and accurate evaluation.","zh":"這個片語集中於公平而準確的評價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a further eight years","meaning":"再多八年","examples":[{"en":"A further eight years may pass before a drug is approved.","zh":"一種藥物獲批准前可能再過八年。"},{"en":"A further eight years means another eight years in addition to the time already spent.","zh":"A further eight years 指在已花費時間之外再多八年。"},{"en":"A building project may need a further two years if safety problems appear.","zh":"如果出現安全問題，建築項目可能需要再多兩年。"},{"en":"If approval takes a further eight years, patients must wait much longer.","zh":"如果批准需時再多八年，病人就必須等更久。"},{"en":"This phrase adds extra time to an already long process.","zh":"這個片語在已漫長過程中加入額外時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be approved for general use","meaning":"獲批准普遍使用","examples":[{"en":"A successful drug may eventually be approved for general use.","zh":"成功藥物最終可能獲批准普遍使用。"},{"en":"Be approved for general use means be officially allowed for widespread use by patients or the public.","zh":"Be approved for general use 指獲官方允許由病人或公眾廣泛使用。"},{"en":"A vaccine must pass safety checks before it is approved for general use.","zh":"疫苗必須通過安全檢查，才獲批准普遍使用。"},{"en":"Once a drug is approved for general use, doctors can prescribe it more widely.","zh":"一旦藥物獲批准普遍使用，醫生便可更廣泛地處方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official permission for broad use.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛使用的官方許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"one of the greatest barriers to","meaning":"……的最大障礙之一","examples":[{"en":"Volunteer recruitment is one of the greatest barriers to clinical testing.","zh":"志願者招募是臨床測試的最大障礙之一。"},{"en":"One of the greatest barriers to something means one of the biggest obstacles that makes it difficult.","zh":"One of the greatest barriers to something 指令某事困難的最大障礙之一。"},{"en":"High rent is one of the greatest barriers to opening a small shop.","zh":"高租金是開小店的最大障礙之一。"},{"en":"If volunteer recruitment is a major barrier, research may be delayed for months.","zh":"如果志願者招募是主要障礙，研究可能延誤數月。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a serious obstacle.","zh":"這個片語指出嚴重障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"clinical-trial procedures","meaning":"臨床試驗程序","examples":[{"en":"Clinical-trial procedures are governed by strict ethical rules.","zh":"臨床試驗程序受嚴格倫理規則規管。"},{"en":"Clinical-trial procedures are the steps and methods used when running a clinical trial.","zh":"Clinical-trial procedures 是進行臨床試驗時使用的步驟和方法。"},{"en":"Procedures may include consent forms, dosage schedules and safety checks.","zh":"程序可能包括同意書、劑量安排和安全檢查。"},{"en":"If clinical-trial procedures are unclear, participants may not be properly protected.","zh":"如果臨床試驗程序不清楚，參加者可能得不到適當保護。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the organised rules of a trial.","zh":"這個片語指試驗的有組織規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"availability of subjects","meaning":"試驗對象的供應情況","examples":[{"en":"The availability of suitable subjects can delay a trial.","zh":"合適試驗對象的供應情況可以延誤試驗。"},{"en":"Availability of subjects means whether enough suitable participants can be found.","zh":"Availability of subjects 指能否找到足夠合適參加者。"},{"en":"A study of a rare disease may struggle with low availability of subjects.","zh":"研究罕見病時，試驗對象供應情況可能不足。"},{"en":"If subjects are not available, researchers cannot test the treatment properly.","zh":"如果沒有可用受試者，研究人員不能適當測試療法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the supply of research participants.","zh":"這個片語描述研究參加者的供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be willing to participate","meaning":"願意參加","examples":[{"en":"Researchers need suitable volunteers who are willing to participate.","zh":"研究人員需要願意參加的合適志願者。"},{"en":"Be willing to participate means agree or feel ready to take part.","zh":"Be willing to participate 指同意或準備好參與。"},{"en":"Students are more willing to participate when classroom activities feel safe and respectful.","zh":"當課堂活動令人感到安全和受尊重，學生會更願意參加。"},{"en":"If patients fear side-effects, they may be less willing to participate in a trial.","zh":"如果病人害怕副作用，他們可能較不願意參加試驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes readiness to join an activity.","zh":"這個片語描述參與活動的意願。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"selection criteria","meaning":"挑選準則","examples":[{"en":"The selection criteria for medical trials are rigorous.","zh":"醫療試驗的挑選準則很嚴格。"},{"en":"Selection criteria are the rules used to decide who is suitable for a study, job or programme.","zh":"Selection criteria 是用來決定誰適合研究、工作或計劃的規則。"},{"en":"A scholarship may have selection criteria such as grades, need and community service.","zh":"獎學金可能有成績、需要和社區服務等挑選準則。"},{"en":"Clear selection criteria help researchers choose safe and relevant participants.","zh":"清楚挑選準則幫助研究人員選擇安全和相關的參加者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the standards for choosing people.","zh":"這個片語描述選人的標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be rigorous","meaning":"嚴格","examples":[{"en":"Eligibility requirements for clinical trials are often rigorous.","zh":"臨床試驗的資格要求通常很嚴格。"},{"en":"Be rigorous means be strict, careful and demanding.","zh":"Be rigorous 指嚴謹、仔細且要求高。"},{"en":"A rigorous exam checks not only memory but also understanding and application.","zh":"嚴格考試不只測記憶，也測理解和應用。"},{"en":"Rigorous requirements can protect patients by excluding unsuitable participants.","zh":"嚴格要求可以透過排除不合適參加者來保護病人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes high standards and careful control.","zh":"這個片語描述高標準和仔細控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"suffer from the disease in question","meaning":"患有相關疾病","examples":[{"en":"Some trials require participants to suffer from the disease in question.","zh":"一些試驗要求參加者患有相關疾病。"},{"en":"Suffer from the disease in question means have the particular disease being studied.","zh":"Suffer from the disease in question 指患有正在研究的特定疾病。"},{"en":"A diabetes trial may need volunteers who suffer from the disease in question.","zh":"糖尿病試驗可能需要患有相關疾病的志願者。"},{"en":"If participants do not have the disease, researchers may not be able to test treatment effectiveness.","zh":"如果參加者沒有該疾病，研究人員可能無法測試治療成效。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the condition relevant to the trial.","zh":"這個片語指出與試驗相關的病症。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"recruitment difficulties","meaning":"招募困難","examples":[{"en":"Trials involving seriously ill patients face tremendous recruitment difficulties.","zh":"涉及重病患者的試驗面對巨大的招募困難。"},{"en":"Recruitment difficulties are problems in finding enough suitable people to join.","zh":"Recruitment difficulties 是尋找足夠合適參加者時遇到的問題。"},{"en":"A school club may face recruitment difficulties if meetings are held too late.","zh":"如果會議太晚舉行，學校學會可能面對招募困難。"},{"en":"In medical trials, recruitment difficulties can delay important research.","zh":"在醫療試驗中，招募困難可以延誤重要研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes obstacles in bringing participants into a project.","zh":"這個片語描述把參加者招入項目時的障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"vulnerable due to","meaning":"因……而處於脆弱狀態","examples":[{"en":"Patients may already be vulnerable due to the effects of their condition.","zh":"病人可能已因疾病影響而處於脆弱狀態。"},{"en":"Vulnerable due to means easily harmed or weakened because of a particular reason.","zh":"Vulnerable due to 指因某特定原因而容易受傷害或變弱。"},{"en":"Older people may be vulnerable due to poor housing during very cold weather.","zh":"在非常寒冷天氣中，長者可能因住屋條件差而處於脆弱狀態。"},{"en":"If patients are vulnerable due to illness, researchers must reduce unnecessary risk.","zh":"如果病人因疾病而處於脆弱狀態，研究人員必須減少不必要風險。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why someone needs extra protection.","zh":"這個片語解釋某人為何需要額外保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the effects of a condition","meaning":"疾病的影響","examples":[{"en":"The effects of a serious condition may make trial participation difficult.","zh":"嚴重疾病的影響可能令參加試驗變得困難。"},{"en":"The effects of a condition are the physical, mental or practical problems caused by an illness.","zh":"Effects of a condition 是疾病造成的身體、心理或實際問題。"},{"en":"The effects of asthma may include coughing, breathlessness and tiredness.","zh":"哮喘的影響可能包括咳嗽、氣促和疲倦。"},{"en":"If the effects of a condition are severe, daily activities may become harder.","zh":"如果疾病的影響嚴重，日常活動可能變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what an illness does to a person.","zh":"這個片語描述疾病對人的作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be reluctant to","meaning":"不願意","examples":[{"en":"Some patients are reluctant to accept additional medical risks.","zh":"一些病人不願意接受額外醫療風險。"},{"en":"Be reluctant to means be unwilling or hesitant to do something.","zh":"Be reluctant to 指不願意或猶豫去做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be reluctant to speak in class if classmates laugh at mistakes.","zh":"如果同學取笑錯誤，學生可能不願意在課堂發言。"},{"en":"If patients feel afraid, they may be reluctant to join a trial.","zh":"如果病人感到害怕，他們可能不願意參加試驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hesitation, not complete refusal.","zh":"這個片語描述猶豫，而不是完全拒絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"put one’s health at risk","meaning":"令自己的健康冒險","examples":[{"en":"Participants may feel that joining a trial could put their health at risk.","zh":"參加者可能覺得加入試驗會令自己的健康冒險。"},{"en":"To put one’s health at risk means to expose oneself to possible harm or illness.","zh":"To put one’s health at risk 指使自己暴露於可能傷害或疾病之中。"},{"en":"Working without safety equipment can put a worker’s health at risk.","zh":"不使用安全設備工作會令工人的健康冒險。"},{"en":"If a trial has unknown side-effects, patients may worry it will put their health at risk.","zh":"如果試驗有未知副作用，病人可能擔心它會令自己的健康冒險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing the chance of harm to health.","zh":"這個片語描述增加健康受害機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"higher levels of risk","meaning":"較高風險","examples":[{"en":"Experimental treatments may expose patients to higher levels of risk.","zh":"實驗性療法可能使病人暴露於較高風險。"},{"en":"Higher levels of risk mean a greater chance of harm, failure or danger.","zh":"Higher levels of risk 指較大機會出現傷害、失敗或危險。"},{"en":"Driving in heavy rain creates higher levels of risk than driving in clear weather.","zh":"在大雨中駕駛比在晴朗天氣駕駛有較高風險。"},{"en":"If a treatment is new, uncertainty may create higher levels of risk for participants.","zh":"如果療法很新，不確定性可能為參加者造成較高風險。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the seriousness of possible danger.","zh":"這個片語比較可能危險的嚴重程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be conducted in line with","meaning":"按照……進行","examples":[{"en":"Clinical trials are conducted in line with a strict protocol.","zh":"臨床試驗按照嚴格規程進行。"},{"en":"Be conducted in line with means be carried out according to rules or standards.","zh":"Be conducted in line with 指根據規則或標準進行。"},{"en":"School exams must be conducted in line with official instructions.","zh":"學校考試必須按照官方指示進行。"},{"en":"If a trial is not conducted in line with protocol, its results may be questioned.","zh":"如果試驗沒有按照規程進行，其結果可能受質疑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes following an agreed method.","zh":"這個片語描述遵循已同意的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"strict protocol","meaning":"嚴格規程","examples":[{"en":"Every stage of a clinical trial follows a strict protocol.","zh":"臨床試驗每個階段都遵循嚴格規程。"},{"en":"A strict protocol is a detailed set of rules that must be followed carefully.","zh":"Strict protocol 是必須仔細遵循的一套詳細規則。"},{"en":"A laboratory uses a strict protocol when handling dangerous chemicals.","zh":"實驗室處理危險化學品時會使用嚴格規程。"},{"en":"Strict protocol protects participants by reducing careless or inconsistent decisions.","zh":"嚴格規程透過減少粗心或不一致決定來保護參加者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful step-by-step control.","zh":"這個片語描述仔細逐步控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"distinct phases","meaning":"不同階段","examples":[{"en":"Clinical testing is generally divided into five distinct phases.","zh":"臨床測試一般分為五個不同階段。"},{"en":"Distinct phases are separate stages with different purposes.","zh":"Distinct phases 是具有不同目的的分開階段。"},{"en":"A school project may have distinct phases: research, writing, editing and presentation.","zh":"學校專題可能有不同階段：研究、寫作、修改和匯報。"},{"en":"Dividing work into distinct phases helps people know what to do next.","zh":"把工作分成不同階段，幫助人知道下一步要做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clearly separated steps in a process.","zh":"這個片語描述過程中清楚分開的步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be deemed safe and effective","meaning":"被判定為安全有效","examples":[{"en":"A drug must be deemed safe and effective before approval.","zh":"藥物在獲批准前必須被判定為安全有效。"},{"en":"Be deemed safe and effective means be officially judged to be safe and to work well.","zh":"Be deemed safe and effective 指被正式判斷為安全且有效。"},{"en":"A vaccine must be deemed safe and effective before public use.","zh":"疫苗在公眾使用前必須被判定為安全有效。"},{"en":"If a treatment is not deemed safe, effectiveness alone is not enough.","zh":"如果療法未被判定為安全，單有成效並不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal approval based on evidence.","zh":"這個片語描述基於證據的正式批准判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reach the end of","meaning":"完成……階段","examples":[{"en":"A successful drug must reach the end of Phase III.","zh":"成功藥物必須完成第三期試驗階段。"},{"en":"Reach the end of something means complete that stage or process.","zh":"Reach the end of something 指完成某階段或過程。"},{"en":"A student must reach the end of the course before taking the final assessment.","zh":"學生必須完成課程後才參加最終評估。"},{"en":"If a drug does not reach the end of Phase III, approval is unlikely.","zh":"如果藥物未能完成第三期試驗，批准機會不大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes completing an important stage.","zh":"這個片語描述完成重要階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be approved for use","meaning":"獲批准使用","examples":[{"en":"Drugs that pass Phase III are often approved for use.","zh":"通過第三期試驗的藥物通常獲批准使用。"},{"en":"Be approved for use means receive official permission to be used.","zh":"Be approved for use 指獲得官方使用許可。"},{"en":"A new medical device must be approved for use before hospitals buy it.","zh":"新醫療儀器必須獲批准使用，醫院才會購買。"},{"en":"If a drug is approved for use, doctors may prescribe it under the rules.","zh":"如果藥物獲批准使用，醫生可按規則處方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes permission after testing.","zh":"這個片語描述測試後的許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"first-in-human trial","meaning":"首次人體試驗","examples":[{"en":"Phase 0 is usually a small first-in-human trial.","zh":"第零期通常是小規模首次人體試驗。"},{"en":"A first-in-human trial is the first study in which a treatment is given to people.","zh":"First-in-human trial 是首次把療法給予人類的研究。"},{"en":"Researchers use a first-in-human trial carefully because human safety is the main concern.","zh":"研究人員會小心進行首次人體試驗，因為人體安全是主要關注。"},{"en":"If early human results raise concerns, the drug may not move forward.","zh":"如果早期人體結果引起疑慮，藥物可能不會繼續發展。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the first step from lab research to human testing.","zh":"這個片語標示由實驗室研究走向人體測試的第一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a small population","meaning":"小規模受試者群體","examples":[{"en":"Phase 0 normally involves a small population of subjects.","zh":"第零期通常涉及小規模受試者群體。"},{"en":"A small population means a limited number of people in a study or group.","zh":"Small population 指研究或群體中有限數量的人。"},{"en":"A pilot survey may use a small population before a larger study begins.","zh":"試行問卷可能在大型研究開始前使用小規模群體。"},{"en":"Testing a small population first can reduce risk and reveal early problems.","zh":"先測試小規模群體可以降低風險並揭示早期問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a limited study group.","zh":"這個片語描述有限的研究群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"with the purpose of","meaning":"目的是","examples":[{"en":"The trial is conducted with the purpose of confirming earlier predictions.","zh":"試驗進行的目的是確認早前預測。"},{"en":"With the purpose of means with the aim or intention of doing something.","zh":"With the purpose of 指以做某事為目的或意圖。"},{"en":"A school meeting may be held with the purpose of improving student safety.","zh":"學校會議舉行的目的可能是改善學生安全。"},{"en":"If the purpose is clear, the design of the activity becomes easier to judge.","zh":"如果目的清楚，活動設計就更容易被評估。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why an action is done.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何採取某行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ascertain that","meaning":"確定","examples":[{"en":"Researchers use Phase 0 to ascertain that the drug behaves as predicted.","zh":"研究人員使用第零期試驗來確定藥物如預測般運作。"},{"en":"Ascertain that means find out or confirm that something is true.","zh":"Ascertain that 指查明或確認某事為真。"},{"en":"A teacher may check homework to ascertain that students understand the rule.","zh":"老師可能檢查功課，以確定學生理解規則。"},{"en":"Researchers gather early evidence to ascertain that the treatment is not behaving unexpectedly.","zh":"研究人員收集早期證據，以確定療法沒有出現意外反應。"},{"en":"This phrase means confirm through checking.","zh":"這個片語指透過檢查來確認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the same as predicted","meaning":"與預測相同","examples":[{"en":"The drug’s effect should be the same as predicted in earlier research.","zh":"藥物效果應與早前研究中的預測相同。"},{"en":"The same as predicted means matching what researchers expected beforehand.","zh":"The same as predicted 指與研究人員事先預期相配。"},{"en":"If a weather forecast is the same as predicted, the rain arrives at the expected time.","zh":"如果天氣與預測相同，雨會在預期時間到來。"},{"en":"When results are not the same as predicted, researchers must investigate why.","zh":"當結果與預測不同，研究人員必須調查原因。"},{"en":"This phrase compares actual results with earlier expectations.","zh":"這個片語把實際結果與早前預期比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"pre-clinical studies","meaning":"臨床前研究","examples":[{"en":"Pre-clinical studies are completed before a drug is tested on humans.","zh":"臨床前研究在藥物用於人體測試前完成。"},{"en":"Pre-clinical studies are research tests done before human trials begin.","zh":"Pre-clinical studies 是人體試驗開始前進行的研究測試。"},{"en":"A drug may undergo pre-clinical studies in cells or animals before Phase 0.","zh":"藥物可能在第零期前於細胞或動物中接受臨床前研究。"},{"en":"If pre-clinical studies show danger, human testing may not proceed.","zh":"如果臨床前研究顯示危險，人體測試可能不會進行。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the research stage before clinical trials.","zh":"這個片語指臨床試驗前的研究階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"no concerns are raised","meaning":"沒有引起疑慮","examples":[{"en":"The drug moves forward if no serious concerns are raised.","zh":"如果沒有引起嚴重疑慮，藥物便會繼續前進。"},{"en":"No concerns are raised means no important problems or doubts are identified.","zh":"No concerns are raised 指沒有識別出重要問題或疑問。"},{"en":"A school trip can proceed if no safety concerns are raised.","zh":"如果沒有引起安全疑慮，學校旅行可以繼續。"},{"en":"If concerns are raised during testing, researchers may stop or redesign the study.","zh":"如果測試期間引起疑慮，研究人員可能停止或重新設計研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes absence of warning signs.","zh":"這個片語描述沒有警告訊號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"enter Phase I","meaning":"進入第一期試驗","examples":[{"en":"A promising drug enters Phase I after successful preliminary testing.","zh":"有前景的藥物在成功初步測試後進入第一期試驗。"},{"en":"Enter Phase I means move into the first main stage of clinical testing.","zh":"Enter Phase I 指進入臨床測試的第一個主要階段。"},{"en":"A medicine cannot enter Phase I until earlier safety checks look acceptable.","zh":"藥物必須在早期安全檢查看似可接受後，才可進入第一期試驗。"},{"en":"If early results are poor, the drug may never enter Phase I.","zh":"如果早期結果差，藥物可能永遠不能進入第一期試驗。"},{"en":"This phrase marks progress into early human testing.","zh":"這個片語標示進入早期人體測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a modest selection of","meaning":"數量不多的……","examples":[{"en":"Phase I involves a modest selection of volunteers.","zh":"第一期試驗涉及數量不多的志願者。"},{"en":"A modest selection of means a fairly small number or limited group.","zh":"Modest selection of 指數量相當小或有限的一組。"},{"en":"A teacher may choose a modest selection of essays to discuss in class.","zh":"老師可能選取數量不多的作文在課堂討論。"},{"en":"Using a modest selection first can make early testing safer and easier to control.","zh":"先使用數量不多的一組，可以令早期測試更安全和更易控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small but purposeful sample.","zh":"這個片語描述小但有目的的樣本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"healthy volunteers","meaning":"健康志願者","examples":[{"en":"Phase I commonly uses healthy volunteers.","zh":"第一期試驗通常使用健康志願者。"},{"en":"Healthy volunteers are people without the disease who agree to join a medical study.","zh":"Healthy volunteers 是沒有該疾病並同意參加醫學研究的人。"},{"en":"A university hospital may recruit healthy volunteers for a low-risk early trial.","zh":"大學醫院可能為低風險早期試驗招募健康志願者。"},{"en":"Healthy volunteers help researchers see how a drug behaves in a body without the target disease.","zh":"健康志願者幫助研究人員了解藥物在沒有目標疾病的身體中如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to research participants who are not currently ill with the condition being studied.","zh":"這個片語指目前沒有患上所研究疾病的研究參加者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be exposed to a drug","meaning":"接受某種藥物","examples":[{"en":"Participants are exposed to carefully controlled doses of the drug.","zh":"參加者接受經仔細控制劑量的藥物。"},{"en":"Be exposed to a drug means receive or come into contact with the drug in a study.","zh":"Be exposed to a drug 指在研究中接受或接觸某種藥物。"},{"en":"Volunteers should know how often they will be exposed to a drug before joining a trial.","zh":"志願者參加試驗前應知道自己會多頻密接受某種藥物。"},{"en":"If people are exposed to a drug repeatedly, researchers must monitor side-effects closely.","zh":"如果人們反覆接受某種藥物，研究人員必須密切監察副作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes contact with a tested medicine.","zh":"這個片語描述接觸被測試藥物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"for HIV and cancer drugs","meaning":"對愛滋病及癌症藥物而言","examples":[{"en":"Different procedures may apply for HIV and cancer drugs.","zh":"對愛滋病及癌症藥物而言，可能適用不同程序。"},{"en":"For HIV and cancer drugs means in the case of medicines designed for HIV or cancer.","zh":"For HIV and cancer drugs 指在為愛滋病或癌症而設計的藥物情況下。"},{"en":"Safety rules may be different for HIV and cancer drugs because the patients’ needs are serious.","zh":"對愛滋病及癌症藥物而言，安全規則可能不同，因為病人需要嚴重。"},{"en":"For these drugs, early trials may involve patients rather than healthy volunteers.","zh":"對這些藥物而言，早期試驗可能涉及病人，而不是健康志願者。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows the discussion to two special treatment areas.","zh":"這個片語把討論收窄至兩個特殊治療範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"patients with the condition","meaning":"患有相關疾病的病人","examples":[{"en":"Early cancer-drug trials often involve patients with the condition.","zh":"早期癌症藥物試驗通常涉及患有相關疾病的病人。"},{"en":"Patients with the condition are people who actually have the illness being studied.","zh":"Patients with the condition 是實際患有所研究疾病的人。"},{"en":"A trial for migraine treatment needs patients with the condition, not people who never have headaches.","zh":"偏頭痛療法試驗需要患有相關疾病的病人，而不是從不頭痛的人。"},{"en":"Testing patients with the condition helps researchers assess whether the treatment works for the target illness.","zh":"測試患有相關疾病的病人，有助研究人員評估療法是否對目標疾病有效。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the relevant patient group.","zh":"這個片語指出相關病人群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"main variations of","meaning":"……的主要變化形式","examples":[{"en":"There are two main variations of Phase I testing.","zh":"第一期測試有兩種主要變化形式。"},{"en":"Main variations of something are the major different forms it can take.","zh":"Main variations of something 是某事可以採取的幾種主要不同形式。"},{"en":"There are several main variations of online learning, including live lessons and recorded videos.","zh":"網上學習有幾種主要變化形式，包括直播課和錄影課。"},{"en":"Knowing the main variations helps students understand how one process can be done differently.","zh":"認識主要變化形式幫助學生理解同一過程可以如何不同地進行。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces important types within one category.","zh":"這個片語引入同一類別中的重要類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"single ascending dose","meaning":"單次遞增劑量","examples":[{"en":"A single ascending dose study gives each group one controlled dose.","zh":"單次遞增劑量研究給予每組一個受控劑量。"},{"en":"Single ascending dose means one dose is given, and later groups may receive higher doses.","zh":"Single ascending dose 指給予一次劑量，而後續組別可能接受較高劑量。"},{"en":"In early testing, researchers may use a single ascending dose design to check safety step by step.","zh":"在早期測試中，研究人員可能使用單次遞增劑量設計，逐步檢查安全性。"},{"en":"If a low dose causes problems, higher doses may not be tested.","zh":"如果低劑量造成問題，較高劑量可能不會被測試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a cautious one-dose testing method.","zh":"這個片語描述謹慎的一次性劑量測試方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"multiple ascending dose","meaning":"多次遞增劑量","examples":[{"en":"A multiple ascending dose study involves a sequence of doses.","zh":"多次遞增劑量研究涉及一連串劑量。"},{"en":"Multiple ascending dose means participants receive repeated doses that may increase according to a plan.","zh":"Multiple ascending dose 指參加者按計劃接受可能逐漸增加的重複劑量。"},{"en":"Researchers use multiple ascending dose testing to see how the body responds over time.","zh":"研究人員使用多次遞增劑量測試，以了解身體隨時間如何反應。"},{"en":"Repeated dosing can reveal side-effects that one dose may not show.","zh":"重複給藥可以揭示單次劑量未必顯示的副作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated-dose testing method.","zh":"這個片語描述重複劑量測試方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the former","meaning":"前者","examples":[{"en":"The former involves a single administration of the drug.","zh":"前者涉及單次給藥。"},{"en":"The former means the first of two things just mentioned.","zh":"The former 指剛提到兩件事中的第一件。"},{"en":"Students may choose live lessons or recorded lessons; the former allows instant questions.","zh":"學生可能選擇直播課或錄影課；前者容許即時提問。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating the name of the first option.","zh":"這個片語避免重複第一個選項的名稱。"},{"en":"It should only be used when two items have already been clearly stated.","zh":"只有在兩項已清楚說明時，才應使用它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a single administration","meaning":"單次給藥","examples":[{"en":"The first method involves a single administration at a predetermined level.","zh":"第一種方法涉及在預先決定的水平作單次給藥。"},{"en":"A single administration means giving one dose or treatment one time.","zh":"Single administration 指一次給予一個劑量或治療。"},{"en":"A vaccine appointment may involve a single administration of one injection.","zh":"疫苗預約可能涉及單次給予一針。"},{"en":"A single administration is easier to monitor than repeated dosing.","zh":"單次給藥比重複給藥較容易監察。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one controlled act of giving treatment.","zh":"這個片語描述一次受控的給予治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"predetermined level","meaning":"預先決定的水平","examples":[{"en":"The dosage is administered at a predetermined level.","zh":"劑量以預先決定的水平給予。"},{"en":"A predetermined level is an amount decided before the test begins.","zh":"Predetermined level 是測試開始前已決定的分量或水平。"},{"en":"A teacher may set a predetermined level of difficulty for a practice paper.","zh":"老師可能為練習卷設定預先決定的難度水平。"},{"en":"Predetermined levels help researchers avoid changing the dose casually during a trial.","zh":"預先決定的水平幫助研究人員避免在試驗期間隨意改變劑量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a level fixed in advance.","zh":"這個片語描述事先固定的水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a sequence of dosages","meaning":"一連串預定劑量","examples":[{"en":"The second method involves a predetermined sequence of dosages.","zh":"第二種方法涉及一連串預定劑量。"},{"en":"A sequence of dosages is an ordered series of doses given over time.","zh":"Sequence of dosages 是隨時間給予、按次序排列的一系列劑量。"},{"en":"A doctor may prescribe a sequence of dosages that gradually decreases after symptoms improve.","zh":"醫生可能處方一連串劑量，在症狀改善後逐漸減少。"},{"en":"A planned sequence helps researchers see how repeated exposure affects the body.","zh":"有計劃的次序幫助研究人員了解重複接觸如何影響身體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doses arranged in a set order.","zh":"這個片語描述按固定次序安排的劑量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be geared towards","meaning":"旨在；以……為目標","examples":[{"en":"The early phases are geared towards establishing safety.","zh":"早期階段旨在確立安全性。"},{"en":"Be geared towards means be designed or directed to achieve a particular aim.","zh":"Be geared towards 指被設計或引導去達成某個特定目的。"},{"en":"Beginner lessons are geared towards building confidence, not testing advanced grammar.","zh":"初學課程旨在建立信心，而不是測試高階文法。"},{"en":"If a trial phase is geared towards safety, researchers focus on risk first.","zh":"如果某試驗階段以安全性為目標，研究人員會先專注風險。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the main purpose of an activity.","zh":"這個片語解釋活動的主要目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"establish the safety of","meaning":"確立……的安全性","examples":[{"en":"Phases 0 and I establish the safety of a pharmaceutical.","zh":"第零期和第一期確立一種藥物的安全性。"},{"en":"To establish the safety of something means to show through evidence that it is acceptably safe.","zh":"To establish the safety of something 指透過證據顯示它在可接受程度上安全。"},{"en":"Engineers test bridges to establish the safety of the design.","zh":"工程師測試橋樑，以確立設計的安全性。"},{"en":"If researchers cannot establish the safety of a drug, later trials should not continue.","zh":"如果研究人員不能確立藥物安全性，後期試驗不應繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes proving that risk is controlled.","zh":"這個片語描述證明風險受控。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"once this has been confirmed","meaning":"一旦這點得到確認","examples":[{"en":"Once safety has been confirmed, effectiveness can be studied more fully.","zh":"一旦安全性得到確認，成效便可更全面研究。"},{"en":"Once this has been confirmed means after this point has been checked and accepted as true.","zh":"Once this has been confirmed 指在這一點已被檢查並接受為真之後。"},{"en":"Once attendance has been confirmed, the school can book the correct number of seats.","zh":"一旦出席人數得到確認，學校便可預訂正確座位數。"},{"en":"Confirming one step allows the next step to begin with more confidence.","zh":"確認一個步驟後，下一步便可更有信心地開始。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one action depends on an earlier confirmation.","zh":"這個片語顯示某行動取決於較早確認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"pass into Phase II","meaning":"進入第二期試驗","examples":[{"en":"Safe drugs pass into Phase II testing.","zh":"安全藥物會進入第二期測試。"},{"en":"Pass into Phase II means move from the first major stage to the second stage of clinical testing.","zh":"Pass into Phase II 指由第一個主要階段進入臨床測試第二階段。"},{"en":"A drug cannot pass into Phase II unless early safety results are acceptable.","zh":"除非早期安全結果可接受，藥物不能進入第二期試驗。"},{"en":"Moving into Phase II allows researchers to study effectiveness more closely.","zh":"進入第二期讓研究人員更仔細研究成效。"},{"en":"This phrase marks progress to a later clinical stage.","zh":"這個片語標示進展到較後臨床階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"continue to be monitored","meaning":"繼續受到監察","examples":[{"en":"Safety continues to be monitored throughout Phase II.","zh":"安全性在整個第二期試驗中繼續受到監察。"},{"en":"Continue to be monitored means keep being checked over time.","zh":"Continue to be monitored 指隨時間繼續被檢查。"},{"en":"A patient’s heart rate may continue to be monitored after surgery.","zh":"病人手術後心率可能繼續受到監察。"},{"en":"Ongoing monitoring helps researchers catch problems that appear later.","zh":"持續監察幫助研究人員發現較後出現的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes observation that does not stop after the first stage.","zh":"這個片語描述第一階段後仍不停止的觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"assess effectiveness","meaning":"評估成效","examples":[{"en":"Phase II begins to assess the drug’s effectiveness.","zh":"第二期試驗開始評估藥物成效。"},{"en":"To assess effectiveness means to judge how well something works.","zh":"To assess effectiveness 指判斷某事運作得有多好。"},{"en":"A teacher may assess the effectiveness of a new reading method by comparing test results.","zh":"老師可能透過比較測驗成績來評估新閱讀方法的成效。"},{"en":"If a drug is safe but not effective, it may not be useful.","zh":"如果藥物安全但無效，它可能沒有用。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether a treatment achieves its purpose.","zh":"這個片語集中於療法是否達到目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a larger group of subjects","meaning":"較大的受試者群體","examples":[{"en":"Phase II uses a larger group of subjects than Phase I.","zh":"第二期試驗使用比第一期較大的受試者群體。"},{"en":"A larger group of subjects means more research participants than before.","zh":"Larger group of subjects 指比之前更多的研究參加者。"},{"en":"After a small pilot survey, a school may test the idea with a larger group of students.","zh":"小型試行問卷後，學校可能用較大的學生群體測試該想法。"},{"en":"A larger group can provide stronger evidence than a very small group.","zh":"較大的群體能比很小的群體提供更有力證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes expanding the number of participants.","zh":"這個片語描述擴大參加者數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"range from A to B","meaning":"由 A 至 B 不等","examples":[{"en":"Phase II trials may range from twenty to three hundred participants.","zh":"第二期試驗參加者可能由二十人至三百人不等。"},{"en":"Range from A to B means vary between a lower number and a higher number.","zh":"Range from A to B 指在較低數字與較高數字之間變化。"},{"en":"Class sizes may range from ten to thirty students depending on the course.","zh":"班級人數可按課程由十人至三十人不等。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe variation in size, cost or amount.","zh":"這個片語幫助描述大小、成本或數量上的變化。"},{"en":"It gives readers the minimum and maximum range.","zh":"它給讀者最低和最高範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"involve two sub-stages","meaning":"包含兩個分階段","examples":[{"en":"Phase II may involve two sub-stages.","zh":"第二期試驗可能包含兩個分階段。"},{"en":"Involve two sub-stages means include two smaller stages within a larger stage.","zh":"Involve two sub-stages 指在較大階段內包括兩個較小階段。"},{"en":"A writing course may involve two sub-stages: planning and drafting.","zh":"寫作課程可能包含兩個分階段：規劃和起草。"},{"en":"Sub-stages help separate different aims inside one phase.","zh":"分階段幫助把同一階段內不同目標分開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes internal division within a process.","zh":"這個片語描述過程內部的劃分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be concerned with","meaning":"關乎；專注於","examples":[{"en":"Phase II(a) may be concerned with establishing dosage levels.","zh":"第二期甲階段可能專注於確立劑量水平。"},{"en":"Be concerned with means focus on or deal with a particular matter.","zh":"Be concerned with 指專注於或處理某特定事項。"},{"en":"A meeting may be concerned with student safety rather than exam results.","zh":"會議可能關乎學生安全，而不是考試成績。"},{"en":"If a trial stage is concerned with dosage, researchers study the best amount to give.","zh":"如果試驗階段關乎劑量，研究人員會研究最佳給藥分量。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main focus.","zh":"這個片語指出主要焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"optimum dosage levels","meaning":"最理想劑量水平","examples":[{"en":"Researchers use Phase II to establish optimum dosage levels.","zh":"研究人員使用第二期試驗確立最理想劑量水平。"},{"en":"Optimum dosage levels are the best amounts of a drug for safety and effect.","zh":"Optimum dosage levels 是在安全和效果上最合適的藥物分量。"},{"en":"A doctor adjusts medicine to find the optimum dosage level for a patient.","zh":"醫生調整藥物，以找出病人的最理想劑量水平。"},{"en":"Too low a dose may not work, while too high a dose may cause side-effects.","zh":"劑量太低可能無效，太高則可能造成副作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the most suitable drug amount.","zh":"這個片語描述最合適的藥物分量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"evaluate effectiveness","meaning":"評估成效","examples":[{"en":"Phase II(b) is used to evaluate effectiveness.","zh":"第二期乙階段用來評估成效。"},{"en":"To evaluate effectiveness means to judge whether something works well enough.","zh":"To evaluate effectiveness 指判斷某事是否足夠有效。"},{"en":"A school may evaluate the effectiveness of tutoring by comparing student progress.","zh":"學校可能透過比較學生進步來評估補習成效。"},{"en":"If a medicine does not show effectiveness, it may not move to larger trials.","zh":"如果藥物沒有顯示成效，它可能不會進入更大型試驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful judgement of results.","zh":"這個片語描述對結果作出仔細判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the most expensive stage","meaning":"成本最高的階段","examples":[{"en":"Phase III is usually the most expensive stage of testing.","zh":"第三期通常是測試中成本最高的階段。"},{"en":"The most expensive stage is the part of a process that costs the most money.","zh":"Most expensive stage 是一個過程中花費最多金錢的部分。"},{"en":"In building a school, construction is often the most expensive stage.","zh":"在興建學校時，施工通常是成本最高的階段。"},{"en":"Phase III costs more because it may involve many patients and complex monitoring.","zh":"第三期成本較高，因為它可能涉及許多病人和複雜監察。"},{"en":"This phrase compares cost across stages.","zh":"這個片語比較各階段成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"time-consuming and complex","meaning":"耗時而複雜","examples":[{"en":"Large clinical trials are time-consuming and complex.","zh":"大型臨床試驗耗時而複雜。"},{"en":"Time-consuming and complex means taking a lot of time and involving many difficult parts.","zh":"Time-consuming and complex 指需要很多時間並涉及許多困難部分。"},{"en":"Organising a school open day can be time-consuming and complex.","zh":"組織學校開放日可以是耗時而複雜的。"},{"en":"Clinical trials become complex when many patients, hospitals and measurements are involved.","zh":"當涉及許多病人、醫院和量度時，臨床試驗會變得複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses both length and difficulty.","zh":"這個片語同時強調時間長和困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"involve as many as","meaning":"涉及多達……","examples":[{"en":"A Phase III trial may involve as many as 3,000 patients.","zh":"第三期試驗可能涉及多達三千名病人。"},{"en":"Involve as many as means include a surprisingly large number up to that amount.","zh":"Involve as many as 指包括多達某個令人注意的高數量。"},{"en":"A charity event may involve as many as 500 volunteers.","zh":"慈善活動可能涉及多達五百名志願者。"},{"en":"A large number of participants can make a study more powerful but harder to manage.","zh":"大量參加者可以令研究更有力，但也更難管理。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a high possible number.","zh":"這個片語突出可能的高數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be rigorously tested","meaning":"接受嚴格測試","examples":[{"en":"The drug’s effectiveness is rigorously tested in Phase III.","zh":"藥物成效在第三期試驗中接受嚴格測試。"},{"en":"Be rigorously tested means be examined very carefully and strictly.","zh":"Be rigorously tested 指受到非常仔細和嚴格的檢查。"},{"en":"A new lift system must be rigorously tested before people use it.","zh":"新升降機系統在人們使用前必須接受嚴格測試。"},{"en":"Rigorous testing helps reveal weaknesses that simple testing may miss.","zh":"嚴格測試有助揭示簡單測試可能錯過的弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strict, thorough examination.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴謹而全面的檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be compared with","meaning":"與……比較","examples":[{"en":"The new treatment is compared with existing alternatives.","zh":"新療法會與現有替代療法比較。"},{"en":"Be compared with means be examined alongside something else to see differences or value.","zh":"Be compared with 指與另一事物並列檢查，以了解差異或價值。"},{"en":"A new teaching method may be compared with traditional lessons.","zh":"新教學方法可能與傳統課堂比較。"},{"en":"Comparing a new drug with current treatment helps show whether it is truly better.","zh":"把新藥與現有療法比較，有助顯示它是否真的更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evaluation through comparison.","zh":"這個片語描述透過比較進行評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"existing alternatives","meaning":"現有替代療法","examples":[{"en":"Researchers compare the drug with the best existing alternatives.","zh":"研究人員把該藥物與最佳現有替代療法比較。"},{"en":"Existing alternatives are choices or treatments that are already available.","zh":"Existing alternatives 是已經可用的選擇或療法。"},{"en":"A shopper may compare a new phone with existing alternatives before buying.","zh":"購物者購買前可能把新手機與現有替代選擇比較。"},{"en":"If a new treatment is no better than existing alternatives, approval may be harder to justify.","zh":"如果新療法不比現有替代療法好，批准可能較難合理化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to current available options.","zh":"這個片語指目前可用的選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"already approved","meaning":"已獲批准","examples":[{"en":"The comparison treatment is usually already approved for use.","zh":"比較用的療法通常已獲批准使用。"},{"en":"Already approved means officially accepted or permitted before the current comparison.","zh":"Already approved 指在目前比較之前已被官方接受或允許。"},{"en":"A school may use a textbook that is already approved by the education authority.","zh":"學校可能使用已獲教育當局批准的教科書。"},{"en":"Comparing with an already approved treatment gives researchers a practical standard.","zh":"與已獲批准的療法比較，給研究人員一個實際標準。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that has passed earlier official checks.","zh":"這個片語描述已通過早前官方檢查的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in common use","meaning":"普遍使用中","examples":[{"en":"The existing treatment may already be in common use.","zh":"現有療法可能已經普遍使用中。"},{"en":"In common use means widely used by many people or organisations.","zh":"In common use 指被許多人或機構廣泛使用。"},{"en":"Email is in common use in schools and workplaces.","zh":"電郵在學校和工作場所普遍使用中。"},{"en":"If a treatment is in common use, doctors already have practical experience with it.","zh":"如果療法普遍使用中，醫生已對它有實際經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that is not rare or experimental.","zh":"這個片語描述某物並不罕見或仍屬實驗性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"pass all requirements","meaning":"通過所有要求","examples":[{"en":"A drug must pass all requirements before regulatory submission.","zh":"藥物在提交監管申請前必須通過所有要求。"},{"en":"Pass all requirements means meet every rule or condition needed to move forward.","zh":"Pass all requirements 指符合繼續前進所需的每條規則或條件。"},{"en":"A student must pass all requirements before graduating.","zh":"學生畢業前必須通過所有要求。"},{"en":"If one requirement is not met, approval may be delayed.","zh":"如果有一項要求未符合，批准可能被延遲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes satisfying every necessary standard.","zh":"這個片語描述滿足每個必要標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"make submissions to","meaning":"向……提交申請","examples":[{"en":"The company then makes submissions to regulatory bodies.","zh":"公司其後向監管機構提交申請。"},{"en":"Make submissions to means formally send documents or evidence to an authority for review.","zh":"Make submissions to 指正式把文件或證據送交權威機構審閱。"},{"en":"A school may make submissions to the government when applying for funding.","zh":"學校申請資助時可能向政府提交申請。"},{"en":"Drug companies make submissions so officials can judge safety and effectiveness.","zh":"藥廠提交申請，讓官員判斷安全性和成效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal application or reporting.","zh":"這個片語描述正式申請或報告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"relevant regulatory bodies","meaning":"相關監管機構","examples":[{"en":"Relevant regulatory bodies examine the evidence for safety and effectiveness.","zh":"相關監管機構審查安全性和成效證據。"},{"en":"Relevant regulatory bodies are the official organisations responsible for checking rules in that field.","zh":"Relevant regulatory bodies 是負責檢查該領域規則的官方機構。"},{"en":"A new medicine must be reviewed by relevant regulatory bodies before approval.","zh":"新藥獲批准前必須由相關監管機構審閱。"},{"en":"If regulatory bodies reject the evidence, the drug cannot enter the market.","zh":"如果監管機構拒絕證據，藥物不能進入市場。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the authorities with the power to regulate.","zh":"這個片語指有權監管的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"licensing bodies","meaning":"發牌機構","examples":[{"en":"Licensing bodies decide whether a drug can enter the market.","zh":"發牌機構決定藥物能否進入市場。"},{"en":"Licensing bodies are organisations that grant official permission for products or services.","zh":"Licensing bodies 是向產品或服務授予官方許可的組織。"},{"en":"A driving licensing body decides who may legally drive.","zh":"駕駛發牌機構決定誰可合法駕駛。"},{"en":"If a medicine fails standards, licensing bodies may refuse approval.","zh":"如果藥物未達標，發牌機構可能拒絕批准。"},{"en":"This phrase describes authorities that issue permission.","zh":"這個片語描述發出許可的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the final phase","meaning":"最後階段","examples":[{"en":"Phase IV is the final phase of clinical testing.","zh":"第四期是臨床測試的最後階段。"},{"en":"The final phase means the last stage in a process.","zh":"Final phase 指一個過程中的最後階段。"},{"en":"Editing is often the final phase before students submit an essay.","zh":"修改通常是學生提交作文前的最後階段。"},{"en":"Even the final phase can reveal problems that earlier stages missed.","zh":"即使最後階段也可以揭示早前階段錯過的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the end stage of a sequence.","zh":"這個片語標示一連串步驟中的終段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"over a lengthy period","meaning":"經歷一段漫長時間","examples":[{"en":"Post-launch monitoring continues over a lengthy period.","zh":"推出市場後監察會經歷一段漫長時間持續。"},{"en":"Over a lengthy period means during a long stretch of time.","zh":"Over a lengthy period 指在一段很長時間內。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may grow over a lengthy period through steady practice.","zh":"學生的信心可能經歷一段漫長時間，透過穩定練習而增長。"},{"en":"Rare side-effects may appear only over a lengthy period of real-world use.","zh":"罕見副作用可能只有在一段漫長真實使用時間後才出現。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises long-term observation.","zh":"這個片語強調長期觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"post-launch","meaning":"推出市場後","examples":[{"en":"Phase IV begins post-launch, after the drug enters general use.","zh":"第四期在藥物進入普遍使用後，即推出市場後開始。"},{"en":"Post-launch means after a product has been released or made available.","zh":"Post-launch 指產品推出或可供使用之後。"},{"en":"A company may collect customer feedback post-launch to improve an app.","zh":"公司可能在推出市場後收集顧客回饋，以改善應用程式。"},{"en":"Post-launch monitoring matters because real-world users are more varied than trial participants.","zh":"推出市場後監察很重要，因為真實世界用戶比試驗參加者更多樣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the period after market release.","zh":"這個片語描述產品推出市場後的時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"general usage","meaning":"普遍使用","examples":[{"en":"Phase IV studies the medicine during general usage.","zh":"第四期研究藥物在普遍使用期間的情況。"},{"en":"General usage means ordinary widespread use by many people in real situations.","zh":"General usage 指許多人在真實情況中的一般廣泛使用。"},{"en":"A school app may work well in testing but show problems during general usage.","zh":"學校應用程式在測試中可能運作良好，但在普遍使用中顯示問題。"},{"en":"Medicines can behave differently during general usage because patients vary widely.","zh":"藥物在普遍使用中可能表現不同，因為病人差異很大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes use outside the controlled trial setting.","zh":"這個片語描述受控試驗環境以外的使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in essence","meaning":"實質上","examples":[{"en":"In essence, Phase IV acts as a long-term safety net.","zh":"實質上，第四期充當長期安全保障。"},{"en":"In essence means basically or in its most important meaning.","zh":"In essence 指基本上或就其最重要意思而言。"},{"en":"In essence, good teaching helps students understand, practise and improve.","zh":"實質上，好教學幫助學生理解、練習和進步。"},{"en":"This phrase helps simplify a complex idea into its core meaning.","zh":"這個片語幫助把複雜想法簡化為核心意思。"},{"en":"It is useful before a short summary.","zh":"它適合用於簡短總結之前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a safety net","meaning":"安全保障","examples":[{"en":"Continued monitoring provides a safety net after approval.","zh":"持續監察在批准後提供安全保障。"},{"en":"A safety net is a backup protection that catches problems if something goes wrong.","zh":"Safety net 是在出現問題時接住風險的後備保護。"},{"en":"Savings can act as a safety net if a worker loses a job.","zh":"如果工人失業，儲蓄可以充當安全保障。"},{"en":"In medicine, post-launch monitoring is a safety net for rare side-effects.","zh":"在醫學中，推出市場後監察是罕見副作用的安全保障。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extra protection after the main process.","zh":"這個片語描述主要程序後的額外保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"continued monitoring","meaning":"持續監察","examples":[{"en":"Continued monitoring may reveal rare side-effects.","zh":"持續監察可能揭示罕見副作用。"},{"en":"Continued monitoring means ongoing checking after the first tests are finished.","zh":"Continued monitoring 指在最初測試完成後繼續檢查。"},{"en":"A doctor may use continued monitoring to track blood pressure over several months.","zh":"醫生可能用持續監察追蹤數月血壓。"},{"en":"Without continued monitoring, late problems may remain unnoticed.","zh":"沒有持續監察，較後出現的問題可能不被注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-term observation.","zh":"這個片語描述長期觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"drug properties","meaning":"藥物特性","examples":[{"en":"Researchers continue to study the drug’s properties after launch.","zh":"研究人員在藥物推出後繼續研究其藥物特性。"},{"en":"Drug properties are the features of a medicine, including how it works, moves and affects the body.","zh":"Drug properties 是藥物的特徵，包括它如何運作、移動和影響身體。"},{"en":"Scientists study drug properties before deciding how often patients should take it.","zh":"科學家在決定病人應多頻密服用前研究藥物特性。"},{"en":"Unexpected drug properties may appear only when many people use the medicine.","zh":"意外藥物特性可能只有在許多人使用該藥後才出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the characteristics of a drug.","zh":"這個片語描述藥物的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"long-term adverse reactions","meaning":"長期不良反應","examples":[{"en":"Phase IV can identify long-term adverse reactions.","zh":"第四期可以識別長期不良反應。"},{"en":"Long-term adverse reactions are harmful effects that appear or continue over a long time.","zh":"Long-term adverse reactions 是長時間後出現或持續的有害影響。"},{"en":"A medicine may seem safe at first but later show long-term adverse reactions.","zh":"藥物起初可能看似安全，但之後顯示長期不良反應。"},{"en":"Detecting these reactions helps regulators protect patients after approval.","zh":"偵測這些反應幫助監管者在批准後保護病人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes delayed or lasting harmful effects.","zh":"這個片語描述延遲或持續的有害影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"remain undetected","meaning":"仍未被發現","examples":[{"en":"Rare side-effects may remain undetected during shorter trials.","zh":"罕見副作用在較短試驗期間可能仍未被發現。"},{"en":"Remain undetected means continue not to be found or noticed.","zh":"Remain undetected 指繼續沒有被找到或注意到。"},{"en":"A small leak may remain undetected until the ceiling becomes wet.","zh":"小漏水可能直到天花板變濕才被發現，在此之前仍未被發現。"},{"en":"Rare problems can remain undetected if too few people are tested.","zh":"如果測試人數太少，罕見問題可能仍未被發現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something hidden from observation.","zh":"這個片語描述某事仍隱藏於觀察之外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"pre-launch testing","meaning":"推出市場前的測試","examples":[{"en":"Not every adverse effect appears during pre-launch testing.","zh":"並非每種不良影響都會在推出市場前的測試中出現。"},{"en":"Pre-launch testing is testing done before a product or medicine is released.","zh":"Pre-launch testing 是產品或藥物推出前進行的測試。"},{"en":"A phone may pass pre-launch testing but still develop problems after many users buy it.","zh":"手機可能通過推出市場前的測試，但在許多用戶購買後仍出現問題。"},{"en":"Pre-launch testing reduces risk but cannot reveal every rare problem.","zh":"推出市場前的測試降低風險，但不能揭示每個罕見問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes checks before public release.","zh":"這個片語描述公開推出前的檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"clinical-testing time frame","meaning":"臨床測試時限","examples":[{"en":"Some reactions occur outside the original clinical-testing time frame.","zh":"一些反應出現在原本臨床測試時限之外。"},{"en":"Clinical-testing time frame means the period during which clinical tests take place.","zh":"Clinical-testing time frame 指臨床測試進行的時間期間。"},{"en":"A side-effect may appear after the clinical-testing time frame has ended.","zh":"副作用可能在臨床測試時限結束後才出現。"},{"en":"If monitoring stops too early, late reactions may be missed.","zh":"如果監察太早停止，較後反應可能被錯過。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the time limits of a clinical study.","zh":"這個片語描述臨床研究的時間限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"identification of harmful effects","meaning":"發現有害影響","examples":[{"en":"The identification of harmful effects may lead to regulatory action.","zh":"發現有害影響可能導致監管行動。"},{"en":"Identification of harmful effects means discovering and recognising negative effects caused by a treatment.","zh":"Identification of harmful effects 指發現並辨認療法造成的負面影響。"},{"en":"A doctor’s report may help with the identification of harmful effects after a medicine is launched.","zh":"藥物推出後，醫生報告可能有助發現有害影響。"},{"en":"Once harmful effects are identified, warnings or restrictions may be added.","zh":"一旦有害影響被識別，可能加入警告或限制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finding dangerous results.","zh":"這個片語描述找出危險結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"lead to withdrawal from the market","meaning":"導致藥物退市","examples":[{"en":"Serious side-effects can lead to withdrawal of a drug from the market.","zh":"嚴重副作用可導致藥物退市。"},{"en":"Lead to withdrawal from the market means cause a product to be removed from sale or use.","zh":"Lead to withdrawal from the market 指導致產品從銷售或使用中移除。"},{"en":"A toy defect may lead to withdrawal from the market if children could be harmed.","zh":"如果玩具有缺陷並可能傷害兒童，可能導致產品退市。"},{"en":"If a drug causes severe harm, regulators may order its withdrawal from the market.","zh":"如果藥物造成嚴重傷害，監管者可能命令其退市。"},{"en":"This phrase describes removal after serious concerns appear.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重疑慮出現後的移除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"on occasion","meaning":"偶爾","examples":[{"en":"On occasion, post-launch findings have had fatal consequences.","zh":"偶爾，推出市場後的發現會帶來致命後果。"},{"en":"On occasion means sometimes, but not usually.","zh":"On occasion 指有時候，但並不通常。"},{"en":"On occasion, a school may close early because of extreme weather.","zh":"偶爾，學校可能因極端天氣提早關閉。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when something happens from time to time.","zh":"這個片語用於某事不時發生時。"},{"en":"It suggests the event is possible but not frequent.","zh":"它暗示事件可能發生，但並不頻繁。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"cholesterol-lowering drug","meaning":"降膽固醇藥物","examples":[{"en":"Cerivastatin was a cholesterol-lowering drug.","zh":"Cerivastatin 是一種降膽固醇藥物。"},{"en":"A cholesterol-lowering drug is a medicine used to reduce cholesterol levels in the blood.","zh":"Cholesterol-lowering drug 是用來降低血液中膽固醇水平的藥物。"},{"en":"A doctor may prescribe a cholesterol-lowering drug to a patient at risk of heart disease.","zh":"醫生可能向有心臟病風險的病人處方降膽固醇藥物。"},{"en":"Such drugs must be monitored because benefits and side-effects both matter.","zh":"這類藥物必須受監察，因為益處和副作用都重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a medicine by its intended effect.","zh":"這個片語按預期效果描述藥物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"adverse effect on","meaning":"對……有不良影響","examples":[{"en":"The drug was found to have an adverse effect on muscle function.","zh":"該藥物被發現對肌肉功能有不良影響。"},{"en":"An adverse effect on something is a harmful or negative effect on it.","zh":"Adverse effect on something 指對某事有有害或負面影響。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can have an adverse effect on memory and mood.","zh":"睡眠不足可對記憶和心情有不良影響。"},{"en":"If a medicine has an adverse effect on the heart, doctors may stop using it.","zh":"如果藥物對心臟有不良影響，醫生可能停止使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harm to a specific function or system.","zh":"這個片語描述對特定功能或系統的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"muscle reaction","meaning":"肌肉反應","examples":[{"en":"Some patients experienced a serious muscle reaction.","zh":"一些病人出現嚴重肌肉反應。"},{"en":"A muscle reaction is an abnormal response in the muscles, such as pain, weakness or damage.","zh":"Muscle reaction 是肌肉中的異常反應，例如疼痛、虛弱或損傷。"},{"en":"A patient should report a muscle reaction after starting a new medicine.","zh":"病人開始新藥後如出現肌肉反應，應向醫生報告。"},{"en":"Serious muscle reactions may require doctors to stop the drug.","zh":"嚴重肌肉反應可能要求醫生停止該藥。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a body response involving muscles.","zh":"這個片語描述涉及肌肉的身體反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"fatal consequences","meaning":"致命後果","examples":[{"en":"In rare cases, the adverse reaction had fatal consequences.","zh":"在罕見個案中，不良反應帶來致命後果。"},{"en":"Fatal consequences are results that cause death.","zh":"Fatal consequences 是導致死亡的結果。"},{"en":"A severe allergic reaction can have fatal consequences without urgent treatment.","zh":"嚴重過敏反應如果沒有緊急治療，可能有致命後果。"},{"en":"If a drug has even rare fatal consequences, regulators must take the risk seriously.","zh":"如果藥物即使罕見地有致命後果，監管者也必須認真看待風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the most serious possible outcome.","zh":"這個片語描述最嚴重的可能結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"complete the sentences","meaning":"完成句子","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the sentences using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成句子。"},{"en":"To complete the sentences means to fill in missing words so the sentences make sense.","zh":"To complete the sentences 指填入缺漏字詞，使句子意思完整。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete the sentences by locating exact words in the text.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過在文章中定位確切字詞來完成句子。"},{"en":"If the grammar does not fit, the completed sentence is likely wrong.","zh":"如果文法不合，完成後的句子很可能錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common gap-fill task.","zh":"這個片語描述常見填充題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個詞","examples":[{"en":"Each answer must contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案必須包含不多於兩個詞。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must use two words or fewer.","zh":"No more than two words 指答案必須使用兩個詞或更少。"},{"en":"If the answer is “fruit acids”, it follows the rule because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “fruit acids”，它有兩個詞，所以符合規則。"},{"en":"Writing three words may lose marks even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫三個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個片語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"advanced cases of","meaning":"……的嚴重個案","examples":[{"en":"Advanced cases of scurvy may involve severe physical symptoms.","zh":"壞血病的嚴重個案可能涉及嚴重身體症狀。"},{"en":"Advanced cases of a disease are serious later-stage cases.","zh":"Advanced cases of a disease 是處於較後期、較嚴重的疾病個案。"},{"en":"Advanced cases of tooth decay may require extraction rather than a simple filling.","zh":"蛀牙的嚴重個案可能需要拔牙，而不是簡單補牙。"},{"en":"If treatment is delayed, mild illness can become advanced cases of disease.","zh":"如果治療延遲，輕微疾病可以變成嚴重個案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious developed forms of a condition.","zh":"這個片語描述已發展得嚴重的病況形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"along with numerous other symptoms","meaning":"連同多種其他症狀","examples":[{"en":"Tooth loss may occur along with numerous other symptoms.","zh":"牙齒脫落可能連同多種其他症狀出現。"},{"en":"Along with numerous other symptoms means together with many additional signs of illness.","zh":"Along with numerous other symptoms 指與許多額外病徵一起出現。"},{"en":"A fever may appear along with numerous other symptoms, such as coughing and body aches.","zh":"發燒可能連同咳嗽和全身痠痛等多種其他症狀出現。"},{"en":"When many symptoms occur together, doctors can understand the illness more clearly.","zh":"當許多症狀一起出現，醫生可以更清楚理解疾病。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one symptom is part of a larger pattern.","zh":"這個片語顯示一種症狀是較大模式的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"fruit acids","meaning":"水果中的酸性物質","examples":[{"en":"Fruit acids were mistakenly believed to prevent scurvy.","zh":"水果中的酸性物質被錯誤地認為可以預防壞血病。"},{"en":"Fruit acids are acidic substances naturally found in fruit.","zh":"Fruit acids 是水果中天然存在的酸性物質。"},{"en":"Lemons taste sharp because they contain fruit acids.","zh":"檸檬味道酸，因為它含有水果中的酸性物質。"},{"en":"In Lind’s time, doctors confused fruit acids with the real protective nutrient.","zh":"在 Lind 的時代，醫生把水果酸性物質與真正保護性營養素混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase names the acid content of fruit.","zh":"這個片語命名水果中的酸性含量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be mistakenly heralded as","meaning":"被錯誤地譽為","examples":[{"en":"Acids were mistakenly heralded as the source of the cure.","zh":"酸性物質被錯誤地譽為治療來源。"},{"en":"Be mistakenly heralded as means be wrongly praised or announced as something important.","zh":"Be mistakenly heralded as 指被錯誤地讚揚或宣稱為某個重要事物。"},{"en":"A study tip may be mistakenly heralded as a miracle solution even though it helps only some students.","zh":"某學習技巧可能被錯誤地譽為神奇解決方法，雖然它只幫到部分學生。"},{"en":"If the wrong cause is heralded as the answer, better explanations may be ignored.","zh":"如果錯誤原因被譽為答案，更好的解釋可能被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public praise based on misunderstanding.","zh":"這個片語描述基於誤解的公開讚揚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a reduction in incidents","meaning":"病例減少","examples":[{"en":"Citrus consumption was linked to a reduction in incidents of scurvy.","zh":"食用柑橘類水果與壞血病病例減少有關。"},{"en":"A reduction in incidents means fewer cases or events happen.","zh":"Reduction in incidents 指個案或事件發生得較少。"},{"en":"Better street lighting may lead to a reduction in incidents of night-time accidents.","zh":"更好街燈可能導致夜間意外事件減少。"},{"en":"If prevention works, researchers should see a reduction in incidents over time.","zh":"如果預防有效，研究人員應看見事件隨時間減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decrease in how often something occurs.","zh":"這個片語描述某事發生頻率下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be at the time exhibiting","meaning":"當時正出現……","examples":[{"en":"The sailors were at the time exhibiting symptoms of scurvy.","zh":"水手當時正出現壞血病症狀。"},{"en":"Be at the time exhibiting means were showing something during that specific period.","zh":"Be at the time exhibiting 指在該特定時期正顯示某事。"},{"en":"A patient was at the time exhibiting a fever and a rash.","zh":"病人當時正出現發燒和皮疹。"},{"en":"This phrase helps locate symptoms at the moment the study began.","zh":"這個片語幫助定位研究開始時的症狀。"},{"en":"It describes what was visible or present then.","zh":"它描述當時可見或存在的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"specific rations","meaning":"指定配給品","examples":[{"en":"Each treatment group received different specific rations.","zh":"每個治療組收到不同指定配給品。"},{"en":"Specific rations are fixed and clearly defined portions of food or drink.","zh":"Specific rations 是固定且清楚界定的食物或飲品份量。"},{"en":"During a camping trip, each group may receive specific rations of water and snacks.","zh":"露營旅行中，每組可能收到指定配給品，如食水和小食。"},{"en":"Specific rations help researchers control what each participant receives.","zh":"指定配給品幫助研究人員控制每位參加者收到甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes carefully assigned supplies.","zh":"這個片語描述仔細分配的物資。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the planned protocol","meaning":"預定試驗規程","examples":[{"en":"The short trial length was not part of the planned protocol.","zh":"短暫試驗時間並不是預定試驗規程的一部分。"},{"en":"The planned protocol is the intended set of rules and steps for a study.","zh":"Planned protocol 是研究原本打算使用的一套規則和步驟。"},{"en":"A teacher’s planned protocol for an exam may include timing, seating and answer collection.","zh":"老師的考試預定規程可能包括時間、座位和收集答案。"},{"en":"If researchers stop early, the actual procedure may differ from the planned protocol.","zh":"如果研究人員提早停止，實際程序可能不同於預定規程。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the original study plan.","zh":"這個片語指原本的研究計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"relevant treatment group","meaning":"相關治療組","examples":[{"en":"The relevant treatment group received oranges and a lemon.","zh":"相關治療組收到橙和一個檸檬。"},{"en":"The relevant treatment group is the group connected to the point or answer being discussed.","zh":"Relevant treatment group 是與正在討論的重點或答案有關的組別。"},{"en":"In a school experiment, the relevant group may be the class that received extra reading practice.","zh":"在學校實驗中，相關組別可能是接受額外閱讀練習的班別。"},{"en":"Identifying the relevant treatment group helps students avoid choosing the wrong comparison.","zh":"識別相關治療組幫助學生避免選錯比較對象。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the specific group that matters.","zh":"這個片語指出重要的特定組別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"recover before the trial ended","meaning":"在試驗結束前康復","examples":[{"en":"One sailor recovered before the trial ended.","zh":"一名水手在試驗結束前康復。"},{"en":"Recover before the trial ended means become well again before the study was finished.","zh":"Recover before the trial ended 指在研究完成前恢復健康。"},{"en":"A patient may recover before treatment is officially completed.","zh":"病人可能在治療正式完成前康復。"},{"en":"Early recovery can show that a treatment may be working quickly.","zh":"早期康復可以顯示療法可能快速有效。"},{"en":"This phrase links improvement with the timing of the trial.","zh":"這個片語把改善與試驗時間連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"resources fundamental to","meaning":"對……不可或缺的資源","examples":[{"en":"The fruit was a resource fundamental to the experiment.","zh":"水果是對該實驗不可或缺的資源。"},{"en":"Resources fundamental to something are supplies or materials that are essential for it to work.","zh":"Resources fundamental to something 是令某事能運作的必要物資或材料。"},{"en":"Internet access is a resource fundamental to online learning.","zh":"互聯網連接是對網上學習不可或缺的資源。"},{"en":"If a fundamental resource runs out, the whole activity may stop.","zh":"如果不可或缺的資源用完，整個活動可能停止。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something necessary, not optional.","zh":"這個片語描述必要而非可有可無的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be used up","meaning":"被用盡","examples":[{"en":"The citrus-fruit supplies were used up after five days.","zh":"柑橘類水果供應在五天後被用盡。"},{"en":"Be used up means be completely consumed or finished.","zh":"Be used up 指被完全消耗或用完。"},{"en":"The printer paper was used up before the exam notices were printed.","zh":"考試通告印完前，打印紙已被用盡。"},{"en":"If trial supplies are used up, researchers may have to stop early.","zh":"如果試驗物資被用盡，研究人員可能不得不提早停止。"},{"en":"This phrase describes resources running out.","zh":"這個片語描述資源耗盡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be too sick to continue","meaning":"病重得無法繼續","examples":[{"en":"The trial did not end because the subjects were too sick to continue.","zh":"試驗並非因受試者病重得無法繼續而結束。"},{"en":"Be too sick to continue means be so ill that continuing an activity is impossible or unsafe.","zh":"Be too sick to continue 指病得太嚴重，以致繼續活動不可能或不安全。"},{"en":"A student may be too sick to continue an exam and need medical help.","zh":"學生可能病重得無法繼續考試，需要醫療協助。"},{"en":"If participants are too sick to continue, ethical rules may require stopping the trial.","zh":"如果參加者病重得無法繼續，倫理規則可能要求停止試驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes illness severe enough to stop participation.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重到足以停止參與的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"not be used to full potential","meaning":"未獲充分運用","examples":[{"en":"The findings were not used to their full potential.","zh":"研究結果未獲充分運用。"},{"en":"Not be used to full potential means not be applied as effectively or completely as possible.","zh":"Not be used to full potential 指沒有被盡可能有效或完整地應用。"},{"en":"A library is not used to full potential if students only enter it before exams.","zh":"如果學生只在考試前進入圖書館，圖書館就未獲充分運用。"},{"en":"If research findings are not fully used, patients may wait longer for better care.","zh":"如果研究結果未獲充分運用，病人可能要更久才得到更好護理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wasted or underused value.","zh":"這個片語描述價值被浪費或未充分使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"fail to recommend","meaning":"未有建議……","examples":[{"en":"Lind did not fail to recommend citrus fruit.","zh":"Lind 並非未有建議使用柑橘類水果。"},{"en":"Fail to recommend means not advise people to use or consider something.","zh":"Fail to recommend 指沒有建議人們使用或考慮某事。"},{"en":"A doctor may fail to recommend exercise if the patient has a serious injury.","zh":"如果病人有嚴重受傷，醫生可能未有建議運動。"},{"en":"In this context, the phrase says Lind did recommend citrus fruit, despite later misuse of the findings.","zh":"在這個語境中，這個片語表示 Lind 的確建議使用柑橘類水果，儘管後來研究結果被誤用。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether advice was given.","zh":"這個片語集中於是否提出建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"ineffective substitutes","meaning":"無效的替代品","examples":[{"en":"Cheaper but ineffective substitutes were often provided instead.","zh":"較便宜但無效的替代品常被改為提供。"},{"en":"Ineffective substitutes are replacements that do not work well.","zh":"Ineffective substitutes 是效果不佳的替代品。"},{"en":"Cheap earphones may be ineffective substitutes for proper hearing protection in a factory.","zh":"在工廠中，廉價耳機可能是正式聽力保護設備的無效替代品。"},{"en":"If an ineffective substitute replaces a real treatment, patients may not recover.","zh":"如果無效替代品取代真正療法，病人可能無法康復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes replacements that fail to do the job.","zh":"這個片語描述未能發揮作用的替代物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be unconvinced by evidence","meaning":"不信服相關證據","examples":[{"en":"Some physicians remained unconvinced by the explanation of the evidence.","zh":"一些醫生仍不信服對證據的解釋。"},{"en":"Be unconvinced by evidence means not accept the conclusion even after seeing evidence.","zh":"Be unconvinced by evidence 指即使看見證據，仍不接受結論。"},{"en":"A student may remain unconvinced by evidence if the explanation is unclear.","zh":"如果解釋不清楚，學生可能不信服相關證據。"},{"en":"If experts are unconvinced by evidence, new findings may not change practice quickly.","zh":"如果專家不信服證據，新發現可能不會很快改變實踐。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doubt despite available support.","zh":"這個片語描述在有支持下仍有懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be valid","meaning":"有效；具可信性","examples":[{"en":"A trial must follow an appropriate design to be considered valid.","zh":"試驗必須遵循適當設計，才被視為有效。"},{"en":"Be valid means be acceptable, reliable or properly supported.","zh":"Be valid 指可接受、可靠或有適當支持。"},{"en":"An exam answer is valid only if it is supported by the passage.","zh":"考試答案只有在有文章支持時才有效。"},{"en":"If a trial design is weak, its results may not be valid.","zh":"如果試驗設計薄弱，其結果可能不具可信性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes whether something can be trusted.","zh":"這個片語描述某事是否可信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"one of the greatest hindrances","meaning":"最大障礙之一","examples":[{"en":"Volunteer recruitment is one of the greatest hindrances to modern trials.","zh":"志願者招募是現代試驗的最大障礙之一。"},{"en":"One of the greatest hindrances means one of the biggest things slowing or blocking progress.","zh":"One of the greatest hindrances 指最阻慢或阻礙進展的事情之一。"},{"en":"Lack of transport is one of the greatest hindrances to rural students attending school.","zh":"缺乏交通是鄉郊學生上學的最大障礙之一。"},{"en":"A major hindrance can delay even a well-designed project.","zh":"重大障礙可以延誤即使設計良好的項目。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a serious obstacle.","zh":"這個片語突出嚴重障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"low volunteer rate","meaning":"志願參加率偏低","examples":[{"en":"A low volunteer rate can significantly delay clinical research.","zh":"志願參加率偏低可大幅延誤臨床研究。"},{"en":"A low volunteer rate means not enough people agree to take part.","zh":"Low volunteer rate 指沒有足夠人同意參與。"},{"en":"A charity event may struggle if it has a low volunteer rate.","zh":"如果志願參加率偏低，慈善活動可能難以運作。"},{"en":"If few patients volunteer for a trial, researchers may not collect enough data.","zh":"如果很少病人自願參加試驗，研究人員可能收集不到足夠數據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes poor participation.","zh":"這個片語描述參與度不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"poor success rate","meaning":"成功率偏低","examples":[{"en":"Drug development has a poor overall success rate.","zh":"藥物研發整體成功率偏低。"},{"en":"A poor success rate means only a small number of attempts succeed.","zh":"Poor success rate 指只有少數嘗試成功。"},{"en":"A difficult scholarship may have a poor success rate because many strong students apply.","zh":"困難獎學金可能因許多優秀學生申請而成功率偏低。"},{"en":"If drug development has a poor success rate, companies must expect many failures.","zh":"如果藥物研發成功率偏低，公司必須預期許多失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes low probability of success.","zh":"這個片語描述成功機會低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"shortage of laboratory staff","meaning":"實驗室人手短缺","examples":[{"en":"A shortage of laboratory staff can also delay scientific work.","zh":"實驗室人手短缺也可以延誤科學工作。"},{"en":"A shortage of laboratory staff means there are not enough trained lab workers.","zh":"Shortage of laboratory staff 指沒有足夠受訓實驗室工作人員。"},{"en":"A hospital may face delays if there is a shortage of laboratory staff to process tests.","zh":"如果實驗室人手短缺，醫院處理測試可能延誤。"},{"en":"When staff are lacking, experiments may take longer to complete.","zh":"當人手不足，實驗可能需要更久才完成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a staffing problem in scientific work.","zh":"這個片語描述科學工作中的人手問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"differ from usual procedures","meaning":"與一般程序不同","examples":[{"en":"HIV and cancer-drug trials differ from usual procedures in Phase I.","zh":"愛滋病和癌症藥物試驗在第一期與一般程序不同。"},{"en":"Differ from usual procedures means not follow the normal method used in most cases.","zh":"Differ from usual procedures 指不跟隨大多數情況中的正常方法。"},{"en":"Emergency lessons may differ from usual procedures when a school suddenly loses electricity.","zh":"當學校突然停電，緊急課堂可能與一般程序不同。"},{"en":"Some trials differ from usual procedures because patient needs or risks are special.","zh":"一些試驗因病人需要或風險特殊而與一般程序不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an exception to the standard process.","zh":"這個片語描述標準流程的例外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"subjects exhibiting no symptoms","meaning":"沒有症狀的受試者","examples":[{"en":"Healthy subjects exhibiting no symptoms are not normally used in some cancer trials.","zh":"沒有症狀的健康受試者通常不會用於某些癌症試驗。"},{"en":"Subjects exhibiting no symptoms are participants who show no signs of the disease.","zh":"Subjects exhibiting no symptoms 是沒有顯示疾病徵象的參加者。"},{"en":"A person exhibiting no symptoms may still be tested if researchers need healthy volunteers.","zh":"如果研究人員需要健康志願者，沒有症狀的人仍可能接受測試。"},{"en":"In serious disease trials, researchers may need patients with symptoms instead.","zh":"在嚴重疾病試驗中，研究人員可能反而需要有症狀病人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes symptom-free research participants.","zh":"這個片語描述沒有症狀的研究參加者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be more rigorously tested than","meaning":"比……受到更嚴格測試","examples":[{"en":"Effectiveness is not necessarily tested more rigorously than safety in Phase I.","zh":"在第一期試驗中，成效不一定比安全性受到更嚴格測試。"},{"en":"Be more rigorously tested than means be examined more strictly and carefully than something else.","zh":"Be more rigorously tested than 指比另一事物受到更嚴格和仔細檢查。"},{"en":"In early medicine trials, safety may be more rigorously tested than effectiveness.","zh":"在早期藥物試驗中，安全性可能比成效受到更嚴格測試。"},{"en":"If one area is tested more rigorously than another, researchers may know more about that area.","zh":"如果一個範疇比另一個受到更嚴格測試，研究人員可能對該範疇了解更多。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the strictness of testing.","zh":"這個片語比較測試嚴格程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"complete the flowchart","meaning":"完成流程圖","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the flowchart using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成流程圖。"},{"en":"To complete the flowchart means to fill in missing steps in a process diagram.","zh":"To complete the flowchart 指填補流程圖中缺失的步驟。"},{"en":"Students may complete a flowchart to show how water moves through a treatment plant.","zh":"學生可能完成流程圖，以顯示水如何經過處理廠。"},{"en":"Flowcharts help learners see order, cause and sequence.","zh":"流程圖幫助學習者看見次序、原因和流程。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in process-based reading questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於以過程為基礎的閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"one word only","meaning":"只限一個詞","examples":[{"en":"Each flowchart answer must contain one word only.","zh":"每個流程圖答案只限一個詞。"},{"en":"One word only means the answer must be exactly one word.","zh":"One word only 指答案必須正好是一個詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “safety”, students must not write “drug safety”.","zh":"如果答案是 “safety”，學生不可寫 “drug safety”。"},{"en":"This rule tests whether students can select the exact word needed.","zh":"這條規則測試學生能否選出所需的確切詞語。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a very strict answer limit.","zh":"這個片語給出非常嚴格的答案限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"confirm assumptions","meaning":"確認假設","examples":[{"en":"Phase 0 is used to confirm assumptions made during earlier studies.","zh":"第零期用來確認早期研究中作出的假設。"},{"en":"To confirm assumptions means to check whether earlier beliefs or predictions are correct.","zh":"To confirm assumptions 指檢查早前信念或預測是否正確。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a quiz to confirm assumptions about what students already know.","zh":"老師可能用小測確認關於學生已有知識的假設。"},{"en":"If assumptions are not confirmed, the plan may need to change.","zh":"如果假設未被確認，計劃可能需要改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes testing whether expectations are true.","zh":"這個片語描述測試預期是否為真。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"pre-clinical stages","meaning":"臨床前階段","examples":[{"en":"Predictions are first made during the pre-clinical stages.","zh":"預測首先在臨床前階段作出。"},{"en":"Pre-clinical stages are the research steps before testing begins in humans.","zh":"Pre-clinical stages 是開始人體測試前的研究步驟。"},{"en":"In the pre-clinical stages, scientists may test a compound in cells or animals.","zh":"在臨床前階段，科學家可能在細胞或動物中測試化合物。"},{"en":"If pre-clinical stages suggest danger, human trials may not start.","zh":"如果臨床前階段暗示危險，人體試驗可能不會開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the early testing period before clinical trials.","zh":"這個片語描述臨床試驗前的早期測試期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"one-off exposure","meaning":"一次性接觸","examples":[{"en":"A single-dose study involves one-off exposure to the drug.","zh":"單次劑量研究涉及一次性接觸該藥物。"},{"en":"One-off exposure means a single instance of contact with or receiving something.","zh":"One-off exposure 指一次接觸或接受某物。"},{"en":"A student’s one-off exposure to a topic is rarely enough for deep understanding.","zh":"學生對某題目的一次性接觸很少足以建立深入理解。"},{"en":"In drug testing, one-off exposure may reveal immediate reactions.","zh":"在藥物測試中，一次性接觸可能揭示即時反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes contact that happens once, not repeatedly.","zh":"這個片語描述只發生一次而非反覆的接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"predetermined sequence","meaning":"預定次序","examples":[{"en":"The multiple-dose method uses a predetermined sequence of dosages.","zh":"多次劑量方法使用預定劑量次序。"},{"en":"A predetermined sequence is an order decided before the process begins.","zh":"Predetermined sequence 是過程開始前已決定的次序。"},{"en":"A teacher may follow a predetermined sequence of lessons from easy to difficult.","zh":"老師可能按照由易到難的預定課堂次序。"},{"en":"A predetermined sequence helps researchers avoid random changes during testing.","zh":"預定次序幫助研究人員避免在測試期間隨意改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an order fixed in advance.","zh":"這個片語描述事先固定的次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"optimum quantities","meaning":"最理想分量","examples":[{"en":"Researchers aim to identify optimum quantities of the drug.","zh":"研究人員旨在識別藥物的最理想分量。"},{"en":"Optimum quantities are the best amounts for achieving a desired result safely.","zh":"Optimum quantities 是安全地達到理想結果的最佳分量。"},{"en":"A recipe needs optimum quantities of sugar and salt so the taste is balanced.","zh":"食譜需要最理想的糖和鹽分量，味道才平衡。"},{"en":"In medicine, too much or too little may reduce safety or effectiveness.","zh":"在醫學中，太多或太少都可能降低安全性或成效。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the most suitable amounts.","zh":"這個片語指最合適分量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"usefulness of a drug","meaning":"藥物的用途與成效","examples":[{"en":"Phase II examines the usefulness and effectiveness of a treatment.","zh":"第二期試驗檢視治療的用途與成效。"},{"en":"Usefulness of a drug means how helpful the drug is for treating a condition.","zh":"Usefulness of a drug 指藥物對治療某病有多大幫助。"},{"en":"A drug may be safe but have limited usefulness if symptoms do not improve.","zh":"如果症狀沒有改善，藥物可能安全但用途有限。"},{"en":"Doctors judge usefulness by looking at real benefits for patients.","zh":"醫生透過查看病人的實際益處來判斷用途。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical value, not only laboratory results.","zh":"這個片語集中於實際價值，而不只是實驗室結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"protracted and costly","meaning":"漫長而昂貴","examples":[{"en":"Phase III is the most complex, protracted and costly stage.","zh":"第三期是最複雜、漫長而昂貴的階段。"},{"en":"Protracted and costly means lasting a long time and requiring a lot of money.","zh":"Protracted and costly 指持續很久並需要大量金錢。"},{"en":"A legal dispute can become protracted and costly if both sides refuse to compromise.","zh":"如果雙方拒絕妥協，法律爭議可能變得漫長而昂貴。"},{"en":"Large trials are protracted and costly because they involve many patients and strict monitoring.","zh":"大型試驗漫長而昂貴，因為它涉及許多病人和嚴格監察。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a process that is slow and expensive.","zh":"這個片語描述緩慢而昂貴的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"post-testing submissions","meaning":"測試後提交的申請","examples":[{"en":"Post-testing submissions are made to regulatory authorities.","zh":"測試後提交的申請會送交監管機構。"},{"en":"Post-testing submissions are documents sent after testing is completed.","zh":"Post-testing submissions 是測試完成後送出的文件。"},{"en":"A company may prepare post-testing submissions with data, safety reports and trial results.","zh":"公司可能準備包含數據、安全報告和試驗結果的測試後申請。"},{"en":"If submissions are incomplete, approval may be delayed.","zh":"如果申請不完整，批准可能延遲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal documents sent after tests.","zh":"這個片語描述測試後送交的正式文件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"if all is satisfactory","meaning":"如果一切結果令人滿意","examples":[{"en":"A submission is made if all the trial results are satisfactory.","zh":"如果所有試驗結果令人滿意，便會提交申請。"},{"en":"If all is satisfactory means if everything meets the required standard.","zh":"If all is satisfactory 指如果一切都符合所需標準。"},{"en":"If all is satisfactory after inspection, the building can open to the public.","zh":"如果檢查後一切令人滿意，建築物便可向公眾開放。"},{"en":"In drug approval, satisfactory results allow the next official step to begin.","zh":"在藥物批准中，令人滿意的結果讓下一個官方步驟開始。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a condition for moving forward.","zh":"這個片語設定繼續前進的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"precautionary monitoring","meaning":"預防性監察","examples":[{"en":"Phase IV provides precautionary monitoring after launch.","zh":"第四期在推出市場後提供預防性監察。"},{"en":"Precautionary monitoring is careful checking done to prevent or detect possible problems.","zh":"Precautionary monitoring 是為預防或偵測可能問題而進行的仔細檢查。"},{"en":"A school may use precautionary monitoring after a student returns from injury.","zh":"學生受傷後復課，學校可能使用預防性監察。"},{"en":"In medicine, precautionary monitoring helps identify rare risks after approval.","zh":"在醫學中，預防性監察有助在批准後識別罕見風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes monitoring used as a safety measure.","zh":"這個片語描述作為安全措施的監察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"serious issues be uncovered","meaning":"發現嚴重問題","examples":[{"en":"A drug may be withdrawn if serious issues are uncovered.","zh":"如果發現嚴重問題，藥物可能被撤回。"},{"en":"Serious issues are uncovered means major problems are discovered.","zh":"Serious issues are uncovered 指重大問題被發現。"},{"en":"A school trip may be cancelled if serious safety issues are uncovered.","zh":"如果發現嚴重安全問題，學校旅行可能被取消。"},{"en":"When serious issues are uncovered after launch, regulators may act quickly.","zh":"當推出市場後發現嚴重問題，監管者可能迅速行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes important hidden problems being found.","zh":"這個片語描述重要隱藏問題被找出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"result in withdrawal","meaning":"導致退市","examples":[{"en":"Severe adverse effects may result in withdrawal from the market.","zh":"嚴重不良影響可能導致退市。"},{"en":"Result in withdrawal means cause something to be removed or stopped.","zh":"Result in withdrawal 指導致某物被移除或停止。"},{"en":"Serious faults in a toy may result in withdrawal from shops.","zh":"玩具中的嚴重缺陷可能導致它從商店退市。"},{"en":"If a medicine causes severe harm, the findings may result in withdrawal.","zh":"如果藥物造成嚴重傷害，相關發現可能導致退市。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious consequence of safety problems.","zh":"這個片語描述安全問題的嚴重後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 14 - CLINICAL TRIALS.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 15":[{"front":"genealogy","meaning":"家譜學；族譜研究","examples":[{"en":"Genealogy is the study of family connections and relationships through history.","zh":"家譜學是研究歷史中家族聯繫和關係的學問。"},{"en":"Genealogy means researching who your ancestors were and how family members are connected.","zh":"genealogy 指研究你的祖先是誰，以及家庭成員之間如何相連。"},{"en":"A student may use genealogy to discover where their great-grandparents lived.","zh":"學生可以用族譜研究來發現曾祖父母住在哪裡。"},{"en":"Genealogy can reveal migration, marriage, adoption, and social change across generations.","zh":"家譜學可以揭示跨世代的移民、婚姻、領養和社會變遷。"},{"en":"Genealogy is not just a list of names; it helps people understand family history.","zh":"家譜學不只是姓名列表；它幫助人了解家族歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"trace family connections","meaning":"追溯家族關係","examples":[{"en":"Genealogists trace family connections through historical records.","zh":"家譜學家透過歷史紀錄追溯家族關係。"},{"en":"To trace family connections means to follow evidence showing how relatives are linked.","zh":"trace family connections 指根據證據追查親屬之間如何相連。"},{"en":"A person may trace family connections by checking birth certificates and old letters.","zh":"一個人可以透過查閱出生證明和舊信件來追溯家族關係。"},{"en":"If records are missing, it becomes harder to trace family connections accurately.","zh":"如果紀錄缺失，就更難準確追溯家族關係。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on finding links between people across time.","zh":"這個片語集中於尋找跨時間的人際聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"family relationships","meaning":"家庭關係","examples":[{"en":"Genealogy examines family relationships across several generations.","zh":"家譜學研究跨越幾代人的家庭關係。"},{"en":"Family relationships are the connections between parents, children, siblings, spouses, and relatives.","zh":"family relationships 指父母、子女、兄弟姊妹、配偶和親屬之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"A family tree can show family relationships more clearly than a written paragraph.","zh":"族譜比一段文字更能清楚展示家庭關係。"},{"en":"When people migrate, family relationships may be separated across countries.","zh":"當人們移民，家庭關係可能被分隔在不同國家。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to how family members are connected to one another.","zh":"這個片語指家庭成員彼此如何相連。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"through history","meaning":"貫穿歷史；歷來","examples":[{"en":"Researchers trace family connections through history.","zh":"研究人員貫穿歷史追溯家族關係。"},{"en":"Through history means across many years or historical periods.","zh":"through history 指跨越多年或多個歷史時期。"},{"en":"A museum shows how clothing has changed through history.","zh":"博物館展示服飾如何貫穿歷史而改變。"},{"en":"Family names may change through history because of migration, marriage, or spelling errors.","zh":"家族姓氏可能因移民、婚姻或拼寫錯誤而歷來有所改變。"},{"en":"The phrase looks at change over time, not only one moment.","zh":"這個片語看的是隨時間的變化，而不只是某一刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"build a cohesive family tree","meaning":"建立連貫完整的族譜","examples":[{"en":"Genealogists use reliable records to build a cohesive family tree.","zh":"家譜學家使用可靠紀錄來建立連貫完整的族譜。"},{"en":"To build a cohesive family tree means to create a clear and connected record of relatives.","zh":"build a cohesive family tree 指建立一份清楚而互相連接的親屬紀錄。"},{"en":"A beginner may build a cohesive family tree by starting with parents and grandparents.","zh":"初學者可以先從父母和祖父母開始，建立連貫完整的族譜。"},{"en":"If dates and names conflict, it becomes difficult to build a cohesive family tree.","zh":"如果日期和姓名互相矛盾，就很難建立連貫完整的族譜。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses accuracy, connection, and organisation.","zh":"這個片語強調準確、連接和組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"family tree","meaning":"族譜；家族樹","examples":[{"en":"A family tree shows how relatives are connected across generations.","zh":"族譜顯示親屬如何跨世代相連。"},{"en":"A family tree is a diagram or record showing parents, children, and ancestors.","zh":"family tree 指展示父母、子女和祖先的圖表或紀錄。"},{"en":"A child may draw a simple family tree for a school project.","zh":"孩子可能為學校專題畫一個簡單的族譜。"},{"en":"A family tree can help people see where cousins, grandparents, and great-grandparents fit.","zh":"族譜可以幫助人看清堂表親、祖父母和曾祖父母的位置。"},{"en":"The phrase turns family relationships into a clear visual structure.","zh":"這個片語把家庭關係變成清楚的視覺結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"increasingly popular hobby","meaning":"日益普及的興趣","examples":[{"en":"Genealogy has become an increasingly popular hobby.","zh":"家譜研究已成為日益普及的興趣。"},{"en":"An increasingly popular hobby is an activity that more and more people enjoy doing in their free time.","zh":"increasingly popular hobby 指越來越多人在空閒時間喜歡做的活動。"},{"en":"Home baking became an increasingly popular hobby when people spent more time at home.","zh":"當人們花更多時間在家，家居烘焙成為日益普及的興趣。"},{"en":"Genealogy has grown because online records make family research easier.","zh":"家譜研究變得更普及，因為網上紀錄令家族研究更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that interest is rising over time.","zh":"這個片語顯示興趣隨時間上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"non-specialist enthusiasts","meaning":"非專業愛好者","examples":[{"en":"Genealogy is popular among non-specialist enthusiasts.","zh":"家譜研究在非專業愛好者之間很受歡迎。"},{"en":"Non-specialist enthusiasts are interested people who are not trained professionals.","zh":"non-specialist enthusiasts 指有興趣但不是受訓專業人士的人。"},{"en":"A non-specialist enthusiast may study old maps simply because they enjoy local history.","zh":"非專業愛好者可能只因喜歡本地歷史而研究舊地圖。"},{"en":"Online tools allow non-specialist enthusiasts to start research without formal training.","zh":"網上工具讓非專業愛好者無需正式訓練也能開始研究。"},{"en":"The phrase describes keen amateurs rather than experts.","zh":"這個片語描述熱心業餘人士，而不是專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"over recent decades","meaning":"在近數十年間","examples":[{"en":"Interest in family history has grown over recent decades.","zh":"在近數十年間，人們對家族史的興趣有所增長。"},{"en":"Over recent decades means during the last several ten-year periods.","zh":"over recent decades 指在最近幾個十年期間。"},{"en":"Over recent decades, smartphones have changed how people communicate.","zh":"在近數十年間，智能手機改變了人們的溝通方式。"},{"en":"Interest in genealogy has grown as more records have moved online.","zh":"隨着更多紀錄轉到網上，人們對家譜研究的興趣有所增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a gradual change across many years.","zh":"這個片語描述多年來的逐步改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the introduction of the Internet","meaning":"互聯網的引入","examples":[{"en":"The introduction of the Internet has transformed genealogical research.","zh":"互聯網的引入改變了家譜研究。"},{"en":"The introduction of the Internet means the arrival and spread of online technology.","zh":"introduction of the Internet 指網絡科技的出現和普及。"},{"en":"The introduction of the Internet changed how students find information for homework.","zh":"互聯網的引入改變了學生為功課尋找資料的方式。"},{"en":"Because of the Internet, family records that once required travel can now be searched at home.","zh":"因為互聯網，以前需要親身出行查找的家族紀錄，現在可以在家搜尋。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a major technological turning point.","zh":"這個片語標誌一個重大的科技轉折點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in many ways","meaning":"在多方面","examples":[{"en":"The Internet has, in many ways, made research easier.","zh":"互聯網在多方面令研究更容易。"},{"en":"In many ways means in several different respects or for several reasons.","zh":"in many ways 指在幾個不同方面或基於幾個原因。"},{"en":"In many ways, online lessons are more flexible than traditional lessons.","zh":"在多方面，網上課堂比傳統課堂更靈活。"},{"en":"The Internet helps genealogy in many ways, including access, sharing, and communication.","zh":"互聯網在多方面幫助家譜研究，包括取得資料、分享和溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a broad statement with multiple supporting points.","zh":"這個片語引出一個有多項支持點的概括說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"spur interest","meaning":"激發興趣","examples":[{"en":"Online records have helped spur interest in genealogy.","zh":"網上紀錄幫助激發人們對家譜研究的興趣。"},{"en":"To spur interest means to encourage or increase people’s curiosity about something.","zh":"spur interest 指鼓勵或增加人們對某事的好奇心。"},{"en":"A school science fair can spur interest in experiments among younger students.","zh":"學校科學展可以激發低年級學生對實驗的興趣。"},{"en":"When people discover one old family record, it may spur interest in finding more.","zh":"當人們發現一份舊家族紀錄，可能會激發他們尋找更多資料的興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something causes curiosity to grow.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事令人好奇心增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"interest levels","meaning":"興趣程度","examples":[{"en":"The availability of records online has raised interest levels.","zh":"網上紀錄的可取得性提高了興趣程度。"},{"en":"Interest levels are the degree to which people are curious or involved in something.","zh":"interest levels 指人們對某事的好奇或投入程度。"},{"en":"A teacher can raise interest levels by using real stories and clear examples.","zh":"老師可以透過真實故事和清楚例子提高學生興趣程度。"},{"en":"If records become easier to find, interest levels in family history may increase.","zh":"如果紀錄變得更容易找到，人們對家族史的興趣程度可能提高。"},{"en":"The phrase measures how much attention people give to a topic.","zh":"這個片語量度人們對某主題給予多少注意力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"historical information","meaning":"歷史資料","examples":[{"en":"The Internet provides access to large amounts of historical information.","zh":"互聯網提供大量歷史資料的取得途徑。"},{"en":"Historical information means facts, records, and evidence about the past.","zh":"historical information 指關於過去的事實、紀錄和證據。"},{"en":"Old newspapers contain historical information about prices, jobs, and daily life.","zh":"舊報紙包含關於價格、工作和日常生活的歷史資料。"},{"en":"Genealogists need historical information to connect names with real events.","zh":"家譜學家需要歷史資料，把姓名與真實事件連接起來。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to information that helps explain earlier times.","zh":"這個片語指幫助解釋早期時代的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be made far more accessible","meaning":"變得更容易取得","examples":[{"en":"Historical information has been made far more accessible online.","zh":"歷史資料在網上變得更容易取得。"},{"en":"Be made far more accessible means become much easier for people to reach, use, or understand.","zh":"be made far more accessible 指變得更容易讓人取得、使用或理解。"},{"en":"A school can make learning materials far more accessible by putting them online.","zh":"學校可以透過把學習材料放到網上，使它們更容易取得。"},{"en":"When records are digitised, people no longer need to travel to distant archives.","zh":"當紀錄被數碼化，人們不再需要到遙遠檔案館查閱。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a major improvement in access.","zh":"這個片語強調取得機會大大改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"than previously","meaning":"比以前","examples":[{"en":"Family records are easier to locate than previously.","zh":"家族紀錄比以前更容易找到。"},{"en":"Than previously means compared with an earlier time.","zh":"than previously 指與較早時候相比。"},{"en":"Students can now submit homework more easily than previously because of online platforms.","zh":"因為有網上平台，學生現在比以前更容易交功課。"},{"en":"Genealogy is faster than previously because many records are searchable online.","zh":"家譜研究比以前更快，因為許多紀錄可在網上搜尋。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the present situation with the past.","zh":"這個片語把現在情況與過去作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"warn that","meaning":"警告說","examples":[{"en":"Experts warn that online sources may contain errors.","zh":"專家警告說，網上資料來源可能含有錯誤。"},{"en":"Warn that means tell people about a possible danger or problem.","zh":"warn that 指告訴人們某個可能的危險或問題。"},{"en":"Doctors warn that poor sleep can damage memory and mood.","zh":"醫生警告說，睡眠不足會損害記憶和情緒。"},{"en":"If experts warn that records may be inaccurate, researchers should check them carefully.","zh":"如果專家警告說紀錄可能不準確，研究人員就應仔細核對。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces advice based on risk.","zh":"這個片語引出基於風險的建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sources obtained from the Internet","meaning":"從互聯網取得的資料來源","examples":[{"en":"Sources obtained from the Internet should be checked carefully.","zh":"從互聯網取得的資料來源應仔細核查。"},{"en":"Sources obtained from the Internet are records or information found online.","zh":"sources obtained from the Internet 指在網上找到的紀錄或資訊。"},{"en":"A student should not copy sources obtained from the Internet without checking their reliability.","zh":"學生不應在未檢查可靠性的情況下抄用從互聯網取得的資料來源。"},{"en":"Online family trees may contain mistakes if users copy information without evidence.","zh":"如果用戶在沒有證據下複製資料，網上族譜可能含有錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds researchers that online information is convenient but not always accurate.","zh":"這個片語提醒研究者，網上資訊方便但不一定準確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be considered with caution","meaning":"必須審慎看待","examples":[{"en":"Online family records must be considered with caution.","zh":"網上家族紀錄必須審慎看待。"},{"en":"Be considered with caution means be treated carefully because the information may be uncertain.","zh":"be considered with caution 指因資料可能不確定而需要小心處理。"},{"en":"A rumour on social media should be considered with caution before being shared.","zh":"社交媒體上的傳聞在分享前應審慎看待。"},{"en":"If a family record lacks a named source, it should be checked before use.","zh":"如果家族紀錄缺乏具名資料來源，使用前應先核查。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against accepting information too quickly.","zh":"這個片語提醒不要太快接受資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"contain inaccuracies","meaning":"含有不準確資料","examples":[{"en":"Some online sources may contain inaccuracies.","zh":"有些網上資料來源可能含有不準確資料。"},{"en":"Contain inaccuracies means include mistakes or incorrect details.","zh":"contain inaccuracies 指包含錯誤或不正確細節。"},{"en":"A student’s notes may contain inaccuracies if they copy too quickly in class.","zh":"如果學生上課抄得太快，筆記可能含有不準確資料。"},{"en":"If a birth date is typed wrongly, a genealogy record can lead researchers to the wrong person.","zh":"如果出生日期被打錯，家譜紀錄可能令研究者找錯人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes information that is not fully reliable.","zh":"這個片語描述不完全可靠的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"novice genealogists","meaning":"家譜研究初學者","examples":[{"en":"Novice genealogists may benefit from guidance and training.","zh":"家譜研究初學者可能受益於指導和訓練。"},{"en":"Novice genealogists are beginners who are just starting to research family history.","zh":"novice genealogists 指剛開始研究家族史的初學者。"},{"en":"A novice genealogist may first interview grandparents before searching archives.","zh":"家譜研究初學者可能先訪問祖父母，再搜尋檔案。"},{"en":"Without guidance, novice genealogists may trust unreliable online records too easily.","zh":"沒有指導時，家譜研究初學者可能太容易相信不可靠的網上紀錄。"},{"en":"The phrase describes people new to genealogy.","zh":"這個片語描述剛接觸家譜研究的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"family history society","meaning":"家族史學會","examples":[{"en":"A family history society can provide advice and research support.","zh":"家族史學會可以提供建議和研究支援。"},{"en":"A family history society is an organisation for people interested in researching ancestry.","zh":"family history society 指為對祖先研究有興趣的人而設的組織。"},{"en":"A beginner may join a family history society to learn how to read old records.","zh":"初學者可以加入家族史學會，學習如何閱讀舊紀錄。"},{"en":"Such societies help members avoid mistakes by sharing experience and sources.","zh":"這類學會透過分享經驗和資料來源，幫助會員避免錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a community group built around genealogy.","zh":"這個片語指圍繞家譜研究建立的社群組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"learn useful skills","meaning":"學習實用技巧","examples":[{"en":"Beginners can learn useful skills from experienced researchers.","zh":"初學者可以向經驗豐富的研究人員學習實用技巧。"},{"en":"Learn useful skills means gain practical abilities that help someone do a task better.","zh":"learn useful skills 指獲得能幫助某人更好完成任務的實際能力。"},{"en":"Students learn useful skills when they practise note-taking, searching, and checking sources.","zh":"學生練習記筆記、搜尋和核查資料時，就是在學習實用技巧。"},{"en":"In genealogy, useful skills help beginners judge whether records are reliable.","zh":"在家譜研究中，實用技巧幫助初學者判斷紀錄是否可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on practical learning, not only theory.","zh":"這個片語集中於實際學習，而不只是理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"experienced researchers","meaning":"經驗豐富的研究人員","examples":[{"en":"Experienced researchers can help beginners evaluate historical evidence.","zh":"經驗豐富的研究人員可以幫助初學者評估歷史證據。"},{"en":"Experienced researchers are people who have spent a long time doing careful study.","zh":"experienced researchers 指長時間進行仔細研究的人。"},{"en":"An experienced researcher may notice a spelling error that a beginner misses.","zh":"經驗豐富的研究人員可能注意到初學者錯過的拼寫錯誤。"},{"en":"Their experience can prevent false conclusions based on weak records.","zh":"他們的經驗可以防止根據薄弱紀錄得出錯誤結論。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to researchers with practical knowledge and judgement.","zh":"這個片語指具實際知識和判斷力的研究者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prior to developing","meaning":"在發展……之前","examples":[{"en":"Prior to developing a mainstream following, genealogy had a narrower purpose.","zh":"在發展出主流支持者群體之前，家譜研究的目的較狹窄。"},{"en":"Prior to developing means before something had developed or become established.","zh":"prior to developing 指在某事發展或確立之前。"},{"en":"Prior to developing confidence, many students feel nervous speaking English.","zh":"在建立信心之前，許多學生說英文時會緊張。"},{"en":"Before genealogy became popular, it was often used for inheritance and status.","zh":"在家譜研究變得普及之前，它常用於繼承和身份地位。"},{"en":"The phrase sets up an earlier stage before later change.","zh":"這個片語建立後來改變之前的早期階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mainstream following","meaning":"主流支持者群體","examples":[{"en":"Genealogy later developed a more mainstream following.","zh":"家譜研究後來發展出更主流的支持者群體。"},{"en":"A mainstream following is a large group of ordinary people who become interested in something.","zh":"mainstream following 指大量普通人開始對某事感興趣。"},{"en":"A music style develops a mainstream following when it moves beyond small specialist circles.","zh":"當某種音樂風格走出小型專門圈子，就會發展出主流支持者群體。"},{"en":"Online access helped genealogy attract people outside academic or noble circles.","zh":"網上取得資料幫助家譜研究吸引學術或貴族圈以外的人。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that an activity has become widely accepted.","zh":"這個片語顯示某活動已被廣泛接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the practice of genealogy","meaning":"家譜研究這項做法","examples":[{"en":"The practice of genealogy has changed considerably over time.","zh":"家譜研究這項做法隨時間有相當大改變。"},{"en":"The practice of genealogy means the actual methods and purposes used in family-history research.","zh":"practice of genealogy 指家族史研究中實際使用的方法和目的。"},{"en":"Today, the practice of genealogy often includes online searches and DNA databases.","zh":"今天，家譜研究這項做法常包括網上搜尋和 DNA 資料庫。"},{"en":"As technology changes, genealogy moves from private archives to wider public access.","zh":"隨着科技改變，家譜研究由私人檔案走向更廣泛公共使用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to how genealogy is actually done.","zh":"這個片語指家譜研究實際如何進行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"focus on establishing","meaning":"專注於確立","examples":[{"en":"Early genealogy focused on establishing ancestral links.","zh":"早期家譜研究專注於確立祖先關係。"},{"en":"Focus on establishing means give most attention to proving or creating something clearly.","zh":"focus on establishing 指把大部分注意力放在清楚證明或建立某事。"},{"en":"A school report may focus on establishing why attendance has fallen.","zh":"學校報告可能專注於確立出席率下降的原因。"},{"en":"Early genealogists focused on proving family lines because inheritance depended on them.","zh":"早期家譜學家專注於證明家族血統，因為繼承依賴這些證據。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the main goal of an investigation.","zh":"這個片語顯示調查的主要目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ancestral links","meaning":"祖先關係","examples":[{"en":"Genealogists once concentrated on the ancestral links of rulers.","zh":"家譜學家曾集中研究統治者的祖先關係。"},{"en":"Ancestral links are connections between a person and earlier generations of their family.","zh":"ancestral links 指一個人與其早期家族世代之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"A person may search baptism records to prove ancestral links with a particular village.","zh":"一個人可能搜尋洗禮紀錄，以證明與某村莊的祖先關係。"},{"en":"In noble families, ancestral links could support claims to property or titles.","zh":"在貴族家庭中，祖先關係可以支持財產或頭銜申索。"},{"en":"The phrase connects living people with their ancestors.","zh":"這個片語把在世的人與祖先連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rulers and noblemen","meaning":"統治者和貴族","examples":[{"en":"Early genealogy was often conducted for rulers and noblemen.","zh":"早期家譜研究常為統治者和貴族進行。"},{"en":"Rulers and noblemen are kings, leaders, aristocrats, or men of high inherited status.","zh":"rulers and noblemen 指國王、領袖、貴族或具有高等繼承身份的人。"},{"en":"A nobleman might use genealogy to prove that his family had held land for generations.","zh":"貴族可能使用家譜證明其家族已持有土地多代。"},{"en":"Because power and wealth were inherited, rulers needed records to support their claims.","zh":"因為權力和財富可被繼承，統治者需要紀錄支持其主張。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to powerful historical elites.","zh":"這個片語指歷史上的權力精英。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"with the purpose of","meaning":"目的是","examples":[{"en":"Family histories were compiled with the purpose of confirming inherited rights.","zh":"家族史被編寫，目的是確認繼承權。"},{"en":"With the purpose of means with the aim or intention of doing something.","zh":"with the purpose of 指以做某事為目標或意圖。"},{"en":"A school may collect feedback with the purpose of improving lessons.","zh":"學校可能收集意見，目的是改善課堂。"},{"en":"Genealogies were sometimes created to prove who had the right to land or titles.","zh":"家譜有時被建立，目的是證明誰有土地或頭銜權利。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why an action is done.","zh":"這個片語解釋行動的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"dispute or confirm","meaning":"質疑或確認","examples":[{"en":"Genealogical evidence could dispute or confirm a person’s claim.","zh":"家譜證據可以質疑或確認某人的申索。"},{"en":"Dispute or confirm means challenge something as doubtful or prove that it is true.","zh":"dispute or confirm 指質疑某事是否可靠，或證明它是真實的。"},{"en":"A receipt can dispute or confirm whether a customer has already paid.","zh":"收據可以質疑或確認顧客是否已付款。"},{"en":"In inheritance cases, family records may support one person’s claim and weaken another’s.","zh":"在繼承案件中，家族紀錄可能支持一人的主張，並削弱另一人的主張。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that evidence can work in two opposite ways.","zh":"這個片語顯示證據可以以兩種相反方式發揮作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"legitimacy of","meaning":"……的合法性","examples":[{"en":"Genealogy was used to establish the legitimacy of inherited rights.","zh":"家譜研究曾用來確立繼承權的合法性。"},{"en":"The legitimacy of something is its legal, accepted, or rightful status.","zh":"legitimacy of something 指某事的法律上、被接受或正當的地位。"},{"en":"A school may check documents to confirm the legitimacy of an application.","zh":"學校可能檢查文件，以確認申請的合法性。"},{"en":"If a noble family could prove ancestry, it strengthened the legitimacy of its claim.","zh":"如果貴族家庭能證明血統，就加強了其申索的合法性。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on whether something is recognised as valid.","zh":"這個片語集中於某事是否被承認為有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"inherited rights","meaning":"繼承權","examples":[{"en":"Noble families used genealogies to support inherited rights.","zh":"貴族家庭使用族譜支持繼承權。"},{"en":"Inherited rights are rights passed down from parents or ancestors, often involving property or titles.","zh":"inherited rights 指由父母或祖先傳下來的權利，通常涉及財產或頭銜。"},{"en":"A family may use old wills to prove inherited rights to land.","zh":"家庭可能使用舊遺囑證明土地繼承權。"},{"en":"If inherited rights are disputed, genealogical records can become important evidence.","zh":"如果繼承權受爭議，家譜紀錄可能成為重要證據。"},{"en":"The phrase connects family descent with legal claims.","zh":"這個片語把家族血統與法律申索連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"wealth or position","meaning":"財富或地位","examples":[{"en":"Ancestry could determine a person’s right to wealth or position.","zh":"祖先血統可以決定一個人對財富或地位的權利。"},{"en":"Wealth or position means money, property, rank, or social status.","zh":"wealth or position 指金錢、財產、階級或社會身份。"},{"en":"In some societies, family background affected a person’s wealth or position.","zh":"在一些社會中，家庭背景影響一個人的財富或地位。"},{"en":"If inheritance depends on ancestry, proving family links can affect someone’s future.","zh":"如果繼承取決於血統，證明家族關係就能影響某人的未來。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to material advantage and social rank.","zh":"這個片語指物質優勢和社會階級。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"more recently","meaning":"近年來","examples":[{"en":"More recently, genealogists have studied ordinary family life.","zh":"近年來，家譜學家研究普通家庭生活。"},{"en":"More recently means in a later or nearer period of time.","zh":"more recently 指在較後或較接近現在的時期。"},{"en":"More recently, many students have used online videos to revise difficult subjects.","zh":"近年來，許多學生使用網上影片溫習困難科目。"},{"en":"Genealogy has shifted from noble inheritance to ordinary people’s lives.","zh":"家譜研究已由貴族繼承轉向普通人的生活。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a newer development compared with the past.","zh":"這個片語標示與過去相比的較新發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"previous generations","meaning":"前幾代人","examples":[{"en":"Researchers examine where previous generations lived.","zh":"研究人員考察前幾代人住在哪裡。"},{"en":"Previous generations are the people in a family or society who lived before the present generation.","zh":"previous generations 指家庭或社會中生活在當代之前的人。"},{"en":"A grandparent belongs to a previous generation, while a child belongs to a later one.","zh":"祖父母屬於前一代，而孩子屬於較後一代。"},{"en":"Studying previous generations can show how work, housing, and education have changed.","zh":"研究前幾代人可以顯示工作、住屋和教育如何改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people who came before us.","zh":"這個片語指在我們之前的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"details of their lifestyle","meaning":"他們生活方式的細節","examples":[{"en":"Modern genealogists are interested in details of their ancestors’ lifestyle.","zh":"現代家譜學家對祖先生活方式的細節感興趣。"},{"en":"Details of their lifestyle means specific information about how people lived, worked, ate, and behaved.","zh":"details of their lifestyle 指關於人們如何生活、工作、飲食和行為的具體資料。"},{"en":"Old photographs may reveal details of a family’s lifestyle, such as clothing and housing.","zh":"舊照片可能揭示家庭生活方式的細節，例如衣着和住屋。"},{"en":"If researchers know lifestyle details, ancestors become real people rather than just names.","zh":"如果研究者知道生活方式細節，祖先就不只是姓名，而變成真實的人。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on everyday life.","zh":"這個片語集中於日常生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"motivations","meaning":"動機","examples":[{"en":"Researchers may try to understand the motivations behind an ancestor’s decisions.","zh":"研究人員可能嘗試理解祖先決定背後的動機。"},{"en":"Motivations are the reasons or desires that make people act in a certain way.","zh":"motivations 指令人以某種方式行動的原因或願望。"},{"en":"A student’s motivation for studying may be a dream job or family pressure.","zh":"學生讀書的動機可能是理想工作或家庭壓力。"},{"en":"Understanding motivations can explain why a family migrated, married, or changed work.","zh":"理解動機可以解釋為何一個家庭移民、結婚或轉工。"},{"en":"The word asks why people made particular choices.","zh":"這個詞詢問人們為何作出特定選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"interpret the effects of","meaning":"解讀……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Genealogists interpret the effects of social conditions on family behaviour.","zh":"家譜學家解讀社會狀況對家庭行為的影響。"},{"en":"Interpret the effects of means explain how something influenced a situation or people.","zh":"interpret the effects of 指解釋某事如何影響一個情況或人。"},{"en":"A teacher may interpret the effects of stress on students’ exam performance.","zh":"老師可能解讀壓力對學生考試表現的影響。"},{"en":"Genealogists look at poverty, war, and law to explain family decisions.","zh":"家譜學家會看貧窮、戰爭和法律，以解釋家庭決定。"},{"en":"The phrase connects causes with human behaviour.","zh":"這個片語把原因與人的行為連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"political restrictions","meaning":"政治限制","examples":[{"en":"Political restrictions may have influenced where families lived.","zh":"政治限制可能影響家庭住在哪裡。"},{"en":"Political restrictions are rules or limits created by governments or authorities.","zh":"political restrictions 指由政府或當局制定的規則或限制。"},{"en":"Travel bans are political restrictions that can stop people from crossing borders.","zh":"旅遊禁令是政治限制，可以阻止人跨越邊境。"},{"en":"If political restrictions limit work or movement, families may migrate or hide information.","zh":"如果政治限制限制工作或流動，家庭可能移民或隱瞞資料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes government-related limits on people’s choices.","zh":"這個片語描述與政府有關、限制人們選擇的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"immigration","meaning":"移民","examples":[{"en":"Immigration can significantly change the course of a family’s history.","zh":"移民可以大幅改變一個家庭的歷史走向。"},{"en":"Immigration means moving into another country to live there, temporarily or permanently.","zh":"immigration 指搬到另一個國家生活，暫時或永久皆可。"},{"en":"A family may keep old passports and letters as evidence of immigration.","zh":"家庭可能保存舊護照和信件作為移民證據。"},{"en":"Immigration can separate relatives but also create new opportunities for later generations.","zh":"移民可以分隔親屬，但也為後代創造新機會。"},{"en":"The word refers to movement into a new country.","zh":"這個詞指移入一個新國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"social conditions","meaning":"社會狀況","examples":[{"en":"Social conditions can shape an individual’s behaviour.","zh":"社會狀況可以塑造個人的行為。"},{"en":"Social conditions are the circumstances of society, such as class, poverty, education, law, and work.","zh":"social conditions 指社會環境，例如階級、貧窮、教育、法律和工作。"},{"en":"Poor social conditions may make it difficult for children to stay in school.","zh":"惡劣社會狀況可能令孩子難以繼續上學。"},{"en":"In genealogy, social conditions help explain why ancestors made certain choices.","zh":"在家譜研究中，社會狀況幫助解釋祖先為何作出某些選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the wider environment surrounding people’s lives.","zh":"這個片語指包圍人們生活的更廣泛環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at a given time","meaning":"在某個特定時期","examples":[{"en":"Family behaviour must be understood within the conditions at a given time.","zh":"家庭行為必須在某個特定時期的條件下理解。"},{"en":"At a given time means at a particular period or moment being discussed.","zh":"at a given time 指在所討論的某個特定時期或時刻。"},{"en":"A student’s choices must be judged according to the school rules at a given time.","zh":"學生的選擇必須根據某個特定時期的校規來判斷。"},{"en":"An ancestor’s decision may look strange today but sensible at the time.","zh":"祖先的決定今天看似奇怪，但在當時可能合理。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds readers to consider historical context.","zh":"這個片語提醒讀者考慮歷史語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"result in the location of","meaning":"導致找到……","examples":[{"en":"A genealogy search may result in the location of living relatives.","zh":"家譜搜尋可能導致找到仍然在世的親屬。"},{"en":"Result in the location of means lead to finding where someone or something is.","zh":"result in the location of 指導致找到某人或某物的位置。"},{"en":"A missing-person appeal may result in the location of a lost elderly man.","zh":"尋人呼籲可能導致找到一名走失長者。"},{"en":"If a family tree connects two branches, it may help people find relatives still alive today.","zh":"如果族譜連接兩個家族分支，可能幫助人找到今天仍在世的親屬。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that research leads to discovery.","zh":"這個片語顯示研究帶來發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"living relatives","meaning":"仍然在世的親屬","examples":[{"en":"Some people use genealogy to find living relatives.","zh":"有些人使用家譜研究來尋找仍然在世的親屬。"},{"en":"Living relatives are family members who are still alive.","zh":"living relatives 指仍然活着的家庭成員。"},{"en":"A person adopted as a baby may search for living relatives later in life.","zh":"一個嬰兒時被領養的人，長大後可能尋找仍然在世的親屬。"},{"en":"Finding living relatives can lead to emotional meetings and new family relationships.","zh":"找到仍然在世的親屬可以帶來感人的會面和新的家庭關係。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts living family members with ancestors who have died.","zh":"這個片語把在世家人與已故祖先作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"family reunion","meaning":"家庭團聚","examples":[{"en":"Locating relatives may lead to a family reunion.","zh":"找到親屬可能帶來家庭團聚。"},{"en":"A family reunion is a meeting where relatives come together again, often after a long time apart.","zh":"family reunion 指親屬再次聚在一起的會面，通常是在長時間分離後。"},{"en":"A family may hold a reunion when cousins return from different countries.","zh":"當堂表親從不同國家回來，家庭可能舉行團聚。"},{"en":"Genealogy can lead to a reunion by helping separated relatives contact one another.","zh":"家譜研究可以透過幫助分離親屬互相聯絡而促成家庭團聚。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests reconnection and shared family memory.","zh":"這個片語暗示重新連接和共享家族記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"help to reunite","meaning":"幫助……重聚","examples":[{"en":"Genealogical research can help to reunite separated family members.","zh":"家譜研究可以幫助分離的家庭成員重聚。"},{"en":"Help to reunite means make it possible for people who were separated to meet or connect again.","zh":"help to reunite 指令曾分離的人可以再次見面或聯繫。"},{"en":"Social media can help to reunite old classmates who lost contact.","zh":"社交媒體可以幫助失去聯絡的舊同學重聚。"},{"en":"If records reveal an address or married name, they may help relatives find each other.","zh":"如果紀錄揭示地址或婚後姓氏，就可能幫助親屬找到彼此。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses bringing people back together.","zh":"這個片語強調把人重新帶回一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be separated in the past","meaning":"過去被迫分離","examples":[{"en":"Some relatives were separated in the past by migration or war.","zh":"有些親屬過去因移民或戰爭而被分離。"},{"en":"Be separated in the past means people were divided or lost contact earlier in history.","zh":"be separated in the past 指人們在較早歷史中被分開或失去聯絡。"},{"en":"Siblings may have been separated in the past because of adoption.","zh":"兄弟姊妹過去可能因領養而被分離。"},{"en":"War, poverty, and forced migration can divide families for generations.","zh":"戰爭、貧窮和被迫遷移可以令家庭分離幾代。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why people may need genealogy to reconnect.","zh":"這個片語解釋人們為何可能需要家譜研究來重新聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fostering and adoption","meaning":"寄養和領養","examples":[{"en":"Fostering and adoption may separate children from biological relatives.","zh":"寄養和領養可能令孩子與血緣親屬分離。"},{"en":"Fostering and adoption are arrangements in which children are cared for by people other than their birth parents.","zh":"fostering and adoption 指孩子由親生父母以外的人照顧的安排。"},{"en":"A child in fostering may later search for information about their birth family.","zh":"寄養中的孩子日後可能尋找關於親生家庭的資料。"},{"en":"Adoption can create a loving home but may also leave questions about biological ancestry.","zh":"領養可以創造有愛的家庭，但也可能留下關於血緣祖先的問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to care arrangements that can affect family identity.","zh":"這個片語指會影響家庭身份的照顧安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"migration or war","meaning":"移民或戰爭","examples":[{"en":"Families may become separated because of migration or war.","zh":"家庭可能因移民或戰爭而分離。"},{"en":"Migration or war means movement to another place or violent conflict that disrupts lives.","zh":"migration or war 指遷往另一地方或暴力衝突，兩者都會打亂生活。"},{"en":"A family may move because of work migration or be forced apart during war.","zh":"家庭可能因工作移民而搬走，也可能在戰爭期間被迫分開。"},{"en":"These events can destroy records, change names, and make relatives difficult to find.","zh":"這些事件可以破壞紀錄、改變姓名，並令親屬難以尋找。"},{"en":"The phrase names two common causes of family separation.","zh":"這個片語指出家庭分離的兩個常見原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a great deal of interest","meaning":"大量興趣","examples":[{"en":"There has been a great deal of interest in convict ancestry in Australia.","zh":"澳洲人對囚犯祖先背景有大量興趣。"},{"en":"A great deal of interest means a large amount of attention or curiosity.","zh":"a great deal of interest 指大量關注或好奇心。"},{"en":"There is a great deal of interest in healthy eating when food prices rise.","zh":"當食物價格上升，人們對健康飲食會有大量興趣。"},{"en":"When people start valuing a once-shameful past, public interest can grow quickly.","zh":"當人們開始重視曾被視為羞恥的過去，公眾興趣可以迅速增加。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that many people care about the topic.","zh":"這個片語顯示許多人關心該主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"of late","meaning":"近來","examples":[{"en":"Of late, many Australian families have researched their ancestry.","zh":"近來，許多澳洲家庭研究自己的祖先。"},{"en":"Of late means recently or in the recent past.","zh":"of late 指最近或在近一段時間。"},{"en":"Of late, more students have been using online flashcards to revise vocabulary.","zh":"近來，更多學生使用網上字卡溫習詞彙。"},{"en":"If interest has grown of late, something recent may have encouraged it.","zh":"如果興趣近來增加，可能有近期因素推動它。"},{"en":"The phrase is a slightly formal way to say recently.","zh":"這個片語是較正式地表示 recently。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"trace their links to","meaning":"追溯與……的關係","examples":[{"en":"Some families wish to trace their links to the early settlers.","zh":"有些家庭希望追溯自己與早期定居者的關係。"},{"en":"Trace their links to means find evidence connecting them with a particular person or group in the past.","zh":"trace their links to 指尋找證據，把他們與過去某個人或群體連接起來。"},{"en":"A family may trace its links to a village through old church records.","zh":"一個家庭可能透過舊教堂紀錄追溯與某村莊的關係。"},{"en":"If people can trace links to early settlers, they may feel closer to national history.","zh":"如果人們能追溯與早期定居者的關係，可能更接近國家歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase connects present identity with historical ancestry.","zh":"這個片語把當代身份與歷史祖先連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"early settlers","meaning":"早期定居者","examples":[{"en":"Many Australians have ancestors among the early European settlers.","zh":"許多澳洲人的祖先屬於早期歐洲定居者。"},{"en":"Early settlers are people who first moved to and established homes in a new colony or region.","zh":"early settlers 指最早遷入並在新殖民地或地區建立家園的人。"},{"en":"Early settlers often faced unfamiliar land, climate, and food supplies.","zh":"早期定居者常面對陌生土地、氣候和食物供應。"},{"en":"Records of early settlers can become important for family and national history.","zh":"早期定居者的紀錄可以對家族和國家歷史很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the first groups who established a new community.","zh":"這個片語指建立新社群的第一批人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as a result of","meaning":"由於；作為……的結果","examples":[{"en":"Britain needed a new penal destination as a result of losing its American colonies.","zh":"由於失去美洲殖民地，英國需要新的流放目的地。"},{"en":"As a result of means because of something that happened earlier.","zh":"as a result of 指因較早發生的某事。"},{"en":"As a result of heavy rain, the school sports day was postponed.","zh":"由於大雨，學校運動會被延期。"},{"en":"Britain’s loss of colonies created a practical problem for its prison system.","zh":"英國失去殖民地，為其監獄制度造成實際問題。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly links a cause with its consequence.","zh":"這個片語清楚連接原因與後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the loss of","meaning":"……的喪失","examples":[{"en":"The loss of the American colonies created a problem for Britain.","zh":"美洲殖民地的喪失為英國造成問題。"},{"en":"The loss of something means no longer having it, often after defeat, damage, or change.","zh":"loss of something 指不再擁有某物，通常是在失敗、破壞或改變之後。"},{"en":"The loss of a phone can cause stress because contacts and photos may disappear.","zh":"手機的遺失可能造成壓力，因為聯絡人和照片可能消失。"},{"en":"The loss of colonies meant Britain needed another place to send prisoners.","zh":"殖民地的喪失意味英國需要另一個地方流放囚犯。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses what has been taken away or no longer exists.","zh":"這個片語強調某物被奪去或不再存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"American colonies","meaning":"美洲殖民地","examples":[{"en":"Britain lost its American colonies in the eighteenth century.","zh":"英國在十八世紀失去了美洲殖民地。"},{"en":"American colonies were territories in North America once controlled by Britain.","zh":"American colonies 指北美洲曾受英國控制的領土。"},{"en":"History lessons often discuss how the American colonies became independent.","zh":"歷史課常討論美洲殖民地如何獨立。"},{"en":"When Britain lost these colonies, its old system for transporting convicts was disrupted.","zh":"當英國失去這些殖民地，其舊有流放囚犯制度受到打亂。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to Britain’s former colonial possessions in America.","zh":"這個片語指英國在美洲的前殖民地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be in need of","meaning":"需要……","examples":[{"en":"Britain was in need of an alternative destination for prisoners.","zh":"英國需要一個囚犯的替代目的地。"},{"en":"Be in need of means require something because there is a problem or shortage.","zh":"be in need of 指因有問題或短缺而需要某事物。"},{"en":"A school may be in need of more teachers if class sizes are too large.","zh":"如果班級人數太多，學校可能需要更多老師。"},{"en":"Because prisons were overcrowded, Britain needed another place to send convicts.","zh":"因為監獄過度擠迫，英國需要另一個地方流放囚犯。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses practical necessity.","zh":"這個片語表達實際需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"alternative destination","meaning":"替代目的地","examples":[{"en":"Australia became an alternative destination for British prisoners.","zh":"澳洲成為英國囚犯的替代目的地。"},{"en":"An alternative destination is another place that can be used when the original place is unavailable.","zh":"alternative destination 指原本地方不可用時可使用的另一個地方。"},{"en":"If a train is cancelled, passengers may need an alternative destination or route.","zh":"如果火車取消，乘客可能需要替代目的地或路線。"},{"en":"Britain needed an alternative destination after it could no longer use America for transportation.","zh":"英國不能再使用美洲作流放地後，需要替代目的地。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a replacement place.","zh":"這個片語突出一個替代地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be accommodated in","meaning":"被安置於……","examples":[{"en":"Many prisoners could not be accommodated in Britain’s prisons.","zh":"許多囚犯無法被安置於英國監獄中。"},{"en":"Be accommodated in means be housed or placed somewhere with enough space.","zh":"be accommodated in 指被安排住在或放置於有足夠空間的地方。"},{"en":"New students may be accommodated in temporary classrooms during construction.","zh":"建築工程期間，新學生可能被安置於臨時課室。"},{"en":"If prisons are full, more prisoners cannot be safely accommodated there.","zh":"如果監獄已滿，就無法安全安置更多囚犯。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on where people can be placed.","zh":"這個片語集中於人可以被安排在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"overcrowded penal facilities","meaning":"過度擠迫的懲教設施","examples":[{"en":"Britain’s overcrowded penal facilities could not hold more prisoners.","zh":"英國過度擠迫的懲教設施無法容納更多囚犯。"},{"en":"Overcrowded penal facilities are prisons or detention places with too many people inside.","zh":"overcrowded penal facilities 指囚禁或拘留場所內人數太多。"},{"en":"Overcrowded classrooms make learning harder; overcrowded prisons create safety problems.","zh":"過度擠迫的課室令學習更困難；過度擠迫的監獄造成安全問題。"},{"en":"If penal facilities are overcrowded, governments may search for other solutions.","zh":"如果懲教設施過度擠迫，政府可能尋找其他解決方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a prison-capacity problem.","zh":"這個片語描述監獄容量問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the First Fleet","meaning":"第一艦隊","examples":[{"en":"The First Fleet carried convicts and officials to Australia.","zh":"第一艦隊把囚犯和官員運送到澳洲。"},{"en":"The First Fleet was the group of British ships that transported the first convicts and settlers to Australia.","zh":"First Fleet 指把第一批囚犯和定居者運送到澳洲的英國船隊。"},{"en":"Students studying Australian history often learn about the First Fleet’s arrival in 1788.","zh":"學習澳洲歷史的學生常會學到第一艦隊在1788年抵達。"},{"en":"Because many families trace ancestry to it, the First Fleet has genealogical importance.","zh":"因為許多家庭追溯祖先至此，第一艦隊具有家譜研究重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a founding event in European Australian history.","zh":"這個片語指歐洲人澳洲史中的建基事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"consist of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"The First Fleet consisted of a flotilla of ships.","zh":"第一艦隊由一支小型船隊組成。"},{"en":"Consist of means be made up of particular parts or members.","zh":"consist of 指由特定部分或成員組成。"},{"en":"A good essay may consist of an introduction, body paragraphs, and a conclusion.","zh":"好文章可以由引言、主體段和結論組成。"},{"en":"If a fleet consists of many ships, each ship may carry different people or supplies.","zh":"如果艦隊由多艘船組成，每艘船可能運載不同人員或物資。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what something includes.","zh":"這個片語解釋某事物包含甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a flotilla of ships","meaning":"一支小型船隊","examples":[{"en":"A flotilla of ships left Britain for Australia in 1787.","zh":"一支小型船隊在1787年離開英國前往澳洲。"},{"en":"A flotilla of ships is a small group of ships travelling together.","zh":"flotilla of ships 指一起航行的一小隊船隻。"},{"en":"A rescue flotilla may bring food and medicine after a coastal disaster.","zh":"沿海災難後，一支救援船隊可能帶來食物和藥物。"},{"en":"Travelling as a flotilla made it easier to carry convicts, officers, and supplies together.","zh":"以船隊形式航行，更容易同時運送囚犯、官員和物資。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a group of vessels moving as one unit.","zh":"這個片語描述一組船隻作為一個單位移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"carry just over","meaning":"載有略多於……","examples":[{"en":"The fleet carried just over 1,300 people.","zh":"該艦隊載有略多於1,300人。"},{"en":"Carry just over means transport slightly more than a stated number.","zh":"carry just over 指運載比某個數字稍多的人或物。"},{"en":"A bus may carry just over 50 passengers when every seat is full.","zh":"當每個座位都坐滿，巴士可能載有略多於50名乘客。"},{"en":"If a ship carries just over 1,300 people, the number is a little higher than 1,300.","zh":"如果一艘船載有略多於1,300人，數量就是稍高於1,300。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate number just above a figure.","zh":"這個片語給出略高於某數字的約數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"convicts and their children","meaning":"囚犯及其子女","examples":[{"en":"Many passengers were convicts or their children.","zh":"許多乘客是囚犯或其子女。"},{"en":"Convicts and their children means prisoners and the sons or daughters travelling with them.","zh":"convicts and their children 指囚犯以及與他們同行的兒女。"},{"en":"Some children travelled with convicted parents because families were not always separated.","zh":"有些孩子與被定罪父母同行，因為家庭不一定被分開。"},{"en":"Transporting convicts also affected children who had committed no crime themselves.","zh":"流放囚犯也影響了本身沒有犯罪的孩子。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds readers that punishment could shape whole families.","zh":"這個片語提醒讀者，懲罰可以塑造整個家庭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the remainder","meaning":"其餘的人","examples":[{"en":"The remainder of the passengers were marines, officers, and relatives.","zh":"其餘乘客是海軍陸戰隊員、軍官和親屬。"},{"en":"The remainder means the people or things left after the first group has been counted.","zh":"the remainder 指第一組被計算後剩下的人或事物。"},{"en":"If ten students choose football and the remainder choose basketball, the rest picked basketball.","zh":"如果十名學生選足球，其餘學生選籃球，剩下的人就是選籃球。"},{"en":"In the First Fleet, not everyone was a convict; the remainder had official or family roles.","zh":"在第一艦隊中，並非所有人都是囚犯；其餘的人有官方或家庭角色。"},{"en":"The phrase separates the remaining part from an earlier group.","zh":"這個片語把剩餘部分與早前群體分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"family members","meaning":"家庭成員","examples":[{"en":"Some officers travelled with their family members.","zh":"有些軍官與家庭成員同行。"},{"en":"Family members are people who belong to the same family, such as parents, spouses, children, or siblings.","zh":"family members 指屬於同一家庭的人，例如父母、配偶、子女或兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"A patient may ask family members to attend a medical appointment for support.","zh":"病人可能請家庭成員陪同出席醫療預約，以獲得支援。"},{"en":"If family members travelled together, migration affected more than one individual.","zh":"如果家庭成員一起旅行，移民就影響不只一個人。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to relatives within a family unit.","zh":"這個片語指家庭單位中的親屬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"leave Britain’s shores","meaning":"離開英國海岸","examples":[{"en":"The First Fleet left Britain’s shores in 1787.","zh":"第一艦隊在1787年離開英國海岸。"},{"en":"Leave Britain’s shores means depart from Britain by sea.","zh":"leave Britain’s shores 指從英國經海路出發離開。"},{"en":"A ship leaving a country’s shores begins a journey away from that land.","zh":"船隻離開一個國家的海岸，就開始遠離該地的旅程。"},{"en":"When the First Fleet left, passengers faced a long and uncertain voyage.","zh":"當第一艦隊離開時，乘客面對漫長而不確定的航程。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a dramatic image of departure from Britain.","zh":"這個片語給出離開英國的戲劇性畫面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"land at","meaning":"在……登岸","examples":[{"en":"The fleet landed at Sydney Cove in January 1788.","zh":"艦隊在1788年1月於悉尼灣登岸。"},{"en":"Land at means arrive and come ashore at a particular place.","zh":"land at 指抵達並在某特定地方上岸。"},{"en":"A ferry may land at a small island pier after a short journey.","zh":"渡輪可能在短程航行後於小島碼頭登岸。"},{"en":"When the First Fleet landed at Sydney Cove, European settlement began there.","zh":"當第一艦隊在悉尼灣登岸，歐洲人在當地的定居便開始。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the place of arrival.","zh":"這個片語標示抵達地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Sydney Cove","meaning":"悉尼灣","examples":[{"en":"Sydney Cove was the landing place of the First Fleet.","zh":"悉尼灣是第一艦隊的登岸地點。"},{"en":"Sydney Cove is the historical place where the First Fleet landed in Australia.","zh":"Sydney Cove 指第一艦隊在澳洲登岸的歷史地點。"},{"en":"A history class may study Sydney Cove as a starting point of European settlement.","zh":"歷史課可能把悉尼灣作為歐洲人定居的起點來研究。"},{"en":"Because many records begin there, Sydney Cove matters to Australian genealogy.","zh":"因為許多紀錄從那裡開始，悉尼灣對澳洲家譜研究重要。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific historical location.","zh":"這個片語命名一個特定歷史地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be celebrated as","meaning":"被慶祝為","examples":[{"en":"January 26 is now celebrated as Australia Day.","zh":"1月26日現在被慶祝為澳洲日。"},{"en":"Be celebrated as means be officially or commonly marked as a special occasion.","zh":"be celebrated as 指被官方或普遍標記為特別日子。"},{"en":"A town’s founding date may be celebrated as a local holiday.","zh":"城鎮的創立日期可能被慶祝為本地假日。"},{"en":"When a date is celebrated nationally, it can shape public memory.","zh":"當某日期被全國慶祝，它可以塑造公共記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how an event becomes commemorated.","zh":"這個片語顯示事件如何被紀念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"European settlement","meaning":"歐洲人定居","examples":[{"en":"The landing marked the beginning of European settlement in Australia.","zh":"登岸標誌着歐洲人在澳洲定居的開始。"},{"en":"European settlement means Europeans moving into and establishing homes or colonies in a place.","zh":"European settlement 指歐洲人遷入某地並建立家園或殖民地。"},{"en":"European settlement changed land use, government, and relations with Indigenous peoples.","zh":"歐洲人定居改變了土地使用、政府和與原住民的關係。"},{"en":"In genealogy, European settlement provides a starting point for many colonial family records.","zh":"在家譜研究中，歐洲人定居為許多殖民地家族紀錄提供起點。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a historical process, not only one landing.","zh":"這個片語指歷史過程，而不只是一次登岸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the first steps towards","meaning":"邁向……的最初步伐","examples":[{"en":"The First Fleet represented the first steps towards European settlement.","zh":"第一艦隊代表邁向歐洲人定居的最初步伐。"},{"en":"The first steps towards something are the earliest actions that begin a longer process.","zh":"first steps towards something 指開始一個較長過程的最早行動。"},{"en":"Saving a small amount each week can be the first steps towards financial independence.","zh":"每星期儲一小筆錢，可以是邁向財務獨立的最初步伐。"},{"en":"The First Fleet did not create modern Australia immediately, but it began a major historical process.","zh":"第一艦隊沒有立即創造現代澳洲，但它開始了一個重大歷史過程。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the beginning of a larger development.","zh":"這個片語顯示較大發展的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lead to a shift in attitudes","meaning":"令態度有所轉變","examples":[{"en":"Genealogical research has led to a shift in attitudes towards convict ancestry.","zh":"家譜研究令澳洲人對囚犯祖先背景的態度有所轉變。"},{"en":"Lead to a shift in attitudes means cause people to change how they think or feel about something.","zh":"lead to a shift in attitudes 指令人們改變對某事的想法或感受。"},{"en":"Meeting disabled athletes can lead to a shift in attitudes about ability.","zh":"接觸殘疾運動員可以令人對能力的態度有所轉變。"},{"en":"When families learn their convict ancestors were not dangerous criminals, shame may turn into pride.","zh":"當家庭知道囚犯祖先並非危險罪犯，羞恥可能變成自豪。"},{"en":"The phrase connects new information with changed opinions.","zh":"這個片語把新資訊與觀點改變連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"convict heritage","meaning":"囚犯祖先背景","examples":[{"en":"Many Australians now take pride in their convict heritage.","zh":"許多澳洲人現在為自己的囚犯祖先背景感到自豪。"},{"en":"Convict heritage means family or national history connected with transported prisoners.","zh":"convict heritage 指與被流放囚犯有關的家族或國家歷史。"},{"en":"A person may discover convict heritage through old court records or transportation lists.","zh":"一個人可能透過舊法庭紀錄或流放名單發現囚犯祖先背景。"},{"en":"What was once embarrassing can become a source of identity when society’s attitudes change.","zh":"當社會態度改變，曾經尷尬的事可以成為身份來源。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to ancestry linked to convicts.","zh":"這個片語指與囚犯有關的祖先背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"contemporary Australian society","meaning":"當代澳洲社會","examples":[{"en":"Attitudes towards convict heritage have changed in contemporary Australian society.","zh":"當代澳洲社會對囚犯祖先背景的態度已經改變。"},{"en":"Contemporary Australian society means Australia as it exists today or in the modern period.","zh":"contemporary Australian society 指今天或現代時期的澳洲社會。"},{"en":"Contemporary Australian society includes people from many cultural and family backgrounds.","zh":"當代澳洲社會包括來自許多文化和家庭背景的人。"},{"en":"In modern Australia, convict ancestry may be viewed differently from how it was viewed before.","zh":"在現代澳洲，囚犯祖先可能被看得與過去不同。"},{"en":"The phrase places an issue in present-day Australia.","zh":"這個片語把議題放在今天的澳洲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"establish that","meaning":"證實","examples":[{"en":"Family members have established that many ancestors were not dangerous criminals.","zh":"家庭成員已證實許多祖先並非危險罪犯。"},{"en":"Establish that means prove or show that something is true.","zh":"establish that 指證明或顯示某事是真實的。"},{"en":"A school investigation may establish that bullying happened during lunch break.","zh":"學校調查可能證實欺凌發生在午膳時間。"},{"en":"Genealogical records can establish that a person was punished for a minor offence.","zh":"家譜紀錄可以證實某人因輕微罪行受罰。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a conclusion supported by evidence.","zh":"這個片語引出有證據支持的結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hardened criminals","meaning":"積犯；慣犯","examples":[{"en":"Many transported convicts were not hardened criminals.","zh":"許多被流放的囚犯並不是積犯。"},{"en":"Hardened criminals are experienced criminals who have repeatedly committed serious crimes.","zh":"hardened criminals 指有經驗、反覆犯下嚴重罪行的罪犯。"},{"en":"A teenager stealing bread out of hunger is not the same as a hardened criminal.","zh":"因飢餓偷麵包的青少年，並不等同於慣犯。"},{"en":"If transported convicts were mostly minor offenders, public shame around their ancestry may weaken.","zh":"如果被流放囚犯多數只是輕微罪犯，社會對這種祖先背景的羞恥感可能減弱。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests serious, habitual criminality.","zh":"這個片語暗示嚴重而慣常的犯罪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dangerous criminals","meaning":"危險罪犯","examples":[{"en":"Most transported prisoners did not pose a serious danger to society.","zh":"大多數被流放囚犯並未對社會構成嚴重危險。"},{"en":"Dangerous criminals are offenders likely to harm people or threaten public safety.","zh":"dangerous criminals 指可能傷害他人或威脅公共安全的罪犯。"},{"en":"A violent robber is usually treated differently from someone who steals food.","zh":"暴力劫匪通常會被視為不同於偷食物的人。"},{"en":"If many convicts were not dangerous criminals, their punishment may seem harsh today.","zh":"如果許多囚犯不是危險罪犯，他們的懲罰今天看來可能嚴厲。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on threat and harm.","zh":"這個片語集中於威脅和傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in most cases","meaning":"在大多數情況下","examples":[{"en":"In most cases, the convicts had committed relatively minor offences.","zh":"在大多數情況下，囚犯犯下的是相對輕微罪行。"},{"en":"In most cases means in the majority of situations.","zh":"in most cases 指在大部分情況中。"},{"en":"In most cases, students improve when feedback is clear and specific.","zh":"在大多數情況下，當回饋清楚而具體，學生會進步。"},{"en":"If most convicts committed minor crimes, their transportation needs historical context.","zh":"如果大多數囚犯犯下輕罪，他們被流放就需要歷史語境理解。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a general pattern, not an absolute rule.","zh":"這個片語給出一般模式，而不是絕對規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be harshly punished for","meaning":"因……受到嚴厲懲罰","examples":[{"en":"Many people were harshly punished for minor crimes.","zh":"許多人因輕微罪行受到嚴厲懲罰。"},{"en":"Be harshly punished for means receive a punishment that seems severe compared with the offence.","zh":"be harshly punished for 指受到與罪行相比顯得嚴重的懲罰。"},{"en":"A student is harshly punished if they are suspended for one forgotten homework task.","zh":"如果學生只因忘記一次功課就被停課，就是受到嚴厲懲罰。"},{"en":"If poor people were harshly punished for theft, social inequality may explain part of the history.","zh":"如果窮人因盜竊受到嚴厲懲罰，社會不平等可能解釋部分歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses punishment that feels too severe.","zh":"這個片語強調懲罰顯得過重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"minor crimes","meaning":"輕微罪行","examples":[{"en":"Some convicts were deported for minor crimes.","zh":"有些囚犯因輕微罪行被流放。"},{"en":"Minor crimes are offences that are less serious than violent or major crimes.","zh":"minor crimes 指比暴力或重大罪行較不嚴重的犯罪。"},{"en":"Shoplifting a small item is usually treated as a minor crime compared with armed robbery.","zh":"與持械行劫相比，偷取小件商品通常被視為輕微罪行。"},{"en":"If minor crimes led to deportation, the justice system was very severe.","zh":"如果輕微罪行導致流放，司法制度就是非常嚴厲。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts small offences with serious criminal acts.","zh":"這個片語把小罪行與嚴重犯罪作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be inspired by desperation","meaning":"由絕望所驅使","examples":[{"en":"Some offences were inspired by desperation rather than greed.","zh":"有些罪行是由絕望而非貪婪所驅使。"},{"en":"Be inspired by desperation means be driven by extreme need or hopelessness.","zh":"be inspired by desperation 指由極端需要或無望感推動。"},{"en":"A hungry person may steal food out of desperation, not because they enjoy crime.","zh":"飢餓的人可能因絕望而偷食物，而不是因為喜歡犯罪。"},{"en":"Dire poverty can push people into choices they would not make in better circumstances.","zh":"極度貧窮可以把人推向在較好環境下不會作出的選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase explains action as caused by urgent need.","zh":"這個片語把行動解釋為由迫切需要造成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dire economic circumstances","meaning":"極端惡劣的經濟環境","examples":[{"en":"Dire economic circumstances pushed some people towards crime.","zh":"極端惡劣的經濟環境把一些人推向犯罪。"},{"en":"Dire economic circumstances are extremely serious financial conditions, such as poverty, hunger, or unemployment.","zh":"dire economic circumstances 指極其嚴重的財政狀況，例如貧窮、飢餓或失業。"},{"en":"A family in dire economic circumstances may struggle to pay rent or buy food.","zh":"處於極端惡劣經濟環境的家庭，可能難以交租或買食物。"},{"en":"When economic conditions are desperate, minor theft may become a survival strategy.","zh":"當經濟環境令人絕望，輕微盜竊可能成為生存策略。"},{"en":"The phrase describes severe financial hardship.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重的經濟困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"so dramatic has the shift been that","meaning":"轉變之大，以致……","examples":[{"en":"So dramatic has the shift been that convict ancestry is now prestigious.","zh":"轉變之大，以致囚犯祖先背景現在被視為有聲望。"},{"en":"So dramatic has the shift been that means the change has been so great that it produced a surprising result.","zh":"so dramatic has the shift been that 指轉變非常大，以致產生令人意外的結果。"},{"en":"So dramatic has the improvement been that the once-failing student now helps classmates.","zh":"進步之大，以致那位曾經不合格的學生現在幫助同學。"},{"en":"A major change in public attitudes can turn shame into pride.","zh":"公眾態度的重大改變可以把羞恥變成自豪。"},{"en":"The phrase uses inversion to emphasise the size of a change.","zh":"這個片語使用倒裝來強調轉變幅度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"family connections to","meaning":"與……的家族關係","examples":[{"en":"Family connections to First Fleet passengers are now highly valued.","zh":"與第一艦隊乘客的家族關係現在被高度重視。"},{"en":"Family connections to means relatives or ancestry linked with a person, group, or event.","zh":"family connections to 指與某人、群體或事件有關的親屬或祖先關係。"},{"en":"A person may feel proud of family connections to a historic village.","zh":"一個人可能為自己與某歷史村莊的家族關係感到自豪。"},{"en":"When an event becomes important nationally, family links to it may gain status.","zh":"當事件在國家層面變得重要，與它的家族關係可能獲得地位。"},{"en":"The phrase connects personal ancestry with a wider historical group.","zh":"這個片語把個人祖先與更廣泛歷史群體連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be considered prestigious","meaning":"被視為有聲望","examples":[{"en":"First Fleet ancestry is now considered prestigious.","zh":"第一艦隊祖先背景現在被視為有聲望。"},{"en":"Be considered prestigious means be regarded as high-status, respected, or impressive.","zh":"be considered prestigious 指被看作地位高、受尊重或令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"A scholarship from a famous university may be considered prestigious.","zh":"來自著名大學的獎學金可能被視為有聲望。"},{"en":"When public attitudes change, a once-embarrassing background may become prestigious.","zh":"當公眾態度改變，曾經令人尷尬的背景可能變得有聲望。"},{"en":"The phrase shows social respect attached to something.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事附帶社會尊重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"nothing less than","meaning":"絕對是；簡直就是","examples":[{"en":"Such ancestry is considered nothing less than prestigious.","zh":"這種祖先背景被視為絕對有聲望。"},{"en":"Nothing less than means absolutely or fully, often with strong emphasis.","zh":"nothing less than 指絕對是或完全是，通常帶強調。"},{"en":"For a small charity, raising a million dollars is nothing less than remarkable.","zh":"對小型慈善機構來說，籌得一百萬美元簡直就是了不起。"},{"en":"If convict ancestry becomes nothing less than prestigious, the change in attitude is huge.","zh":"如果囚犯祖先背景變得絕對有聲望，態度轉變就是巨大。"},{"en":"The phrase intensifies the description that follows.","zh":"這個片語加強後面的描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be among the first to","meaning":"是最早……的其中之一","examples":[{"en":"Margaret Dawson was among the first European women to reach Australia.","zh":"Margaret Dawson 是最早到達澳洲的歐洲女性之一。"},{"en":"Be among the first to means be one of the earliest people to do something.","zh":"be among the first to 指是最早做某事的人之一。"},{"en":"A school may be among the first to introduce a new digital learning system.","zh":"一所學校可能是最早引入新數碼學習系統的學校之一。"},{"en":"Being among the first settlers can make a person important in later family history.","zh":"成為最早定居者之一，可以令一個人在後來家族史中變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights early participation in an event.","zh":"這個片語突出早期參與某事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"set foot on","meaning":"踏足","examples":[{"en":"They were among the first European women to set foot on Australian soil.","zh":"她們是最早踏足澳洲土地的歐洲女性之一。"},{"en":"Set foot on means physically arrive at and step onto a place.","zh":"set foot on 指親身到達並踏上一個地方。"},{"en":"A traveller may feel excited when they set foot on a country they have long wanted to visit.","zh":"旅客踏足一直想去的國家時，可能感到興奮。"},{"en":"Setting foot on new land can mark the beginning of migration or settlement.","zh":"踏足新土地可以標誌移民或定居的開始。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a vivid image of arrival.","zh":"這個片語給出抵達的生動畫面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Australian soil","meaning":"澳洲土地","examples":[{"en":"The women arrived on Australian soil with the First Fleet.","zh":"這些女性隨第一艦隊抵達澳洲土地。"},{"en":"Australian soil means the land or territory of Australia.","zh":"Australian soil 指澳洲的土地或領土。"},{"en":"A migrant may remember the first day they stood on Australian soil.","zh":"移民可能記得自己第一天站在澳洲土地上的情景。"},{"en":"In historical writing, “soil” often gives land a symbolic meaning.","zh":"在歷史寫作中，soil 常給土地一種象徵意義。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to physical land as well as national place.","zh":"這個片語既指實際土地，也指國家地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"initial death sentence","meaning":"最初的死刑判決","examples":[{"en":"Margaret Dawson initially received a death sentence.","zh":"Margaret Dawson 最初被判死刑。"},{"en":"An initial death sentence is the first legal decision ordering a person to be executed.","zh":"initial death sentence 指最初作出的、命令處決某人的法律判決。"},{"en":"A sentence may later be reduced if authorities change the punishment.","zh":"如果當局改變懲罰，刑罰日後可能被減輕。"},{"en":"If a death sentence is commuted, the original punishment is replaced by a lesser one.","zh":"如果死刑被減刑，原本懲罰會被較輕刑罰取代。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the first punishment before later change.","zh":"這個片語集中於後來改變前的最初懲罰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pass a sentence","meaning":"判處刑罰","examples":[{"en":"A death sentence was passed for the theft.","zh":"法庭因該盜竊案判處死刑。"},{"en":"Pass a sentence means officially decide a legal punishment in court.","zh":"pass a sentence 指法庭正式決定法律懲罰。"},{"en":"A judge may pass a sentence after hearing evidence and arguments.","zh":"法官可能在聽取證據和論點後判處刑罰。"},{"en":"If courts pass harsh sentences for minor crimes, society may later judge the system as unfair.","zh":"如果法庭因輕微罪行判處嚴厲刑罰，社會日後可能認為制度不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to formal legal punishment.","zh":"這個片語指正式法律懲罰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"steal clothes from","meaning":"從……偷取衣物","examples":[{"en":"Dawson was convicted of stealing clothes from her employer.","zh":"Dawson 被裁定從僱主那裡偷取衣物罪成。"},{"en":"Steal clothes from means take clothing belonging to another person without permission.","zh":"steal clothes from 指未經許可拿走屬於他人的衣物。"},{"en":"A worker who steals clothes from a shop may face legal punishment.","zh":"從商店偷取衣物的員工可能面臨法律懲罰。"},{"en":"If poverty drives someone to steal basic items, the offence may be viewed with more sympathy.","zh":"如果貧窮驅使某人偷取基本物品，該罪行可能較令人同情。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the object stolen and the person it was taken from.","zh":"這個片語指出被偷物件和被偷取的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be commuted to","meaning":"被減刑為","examples":[{"en":"Her death sentence was commuted to deportation.","zh":"她的死刑被減刑為流放。"},{"en":"Be commuted to means a punishment is officially changed to a lighter one.","zh":"be commuted to 指懲罰被正式改為較輕的刑罰。"},{"en":"A prison sentence may be commuted to community service in special circumstances.","zh":"在特殊情況下，監禁刑罰可能被減刑為社區服務。"},{"en":"If a death sentence is commuted to deportation, the person is no longer executed but is sent away.","zh":"如果死刑被減刑為流放，該人不再被處決，而是被送走。"},{"en":"The phrase describes legal reduction of punishment.","zh":"這個片語描述法律上的減刑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deportation","meaning":"流放；驅逐出境","examples":[{"en":"Deportation was used as a punishment for many British convicts.","zh":"流放曾被用作許多英國囚犯的懲罰。"},{"en":"Deportation means forcing someone to leave a country or sending them away as punishment.","zh":"deportation 指強迫某人離開一個國家，或作為懲罰把他送走。"},{"en":"A person who breaks immigration law may face deportation today.","zh":"今天，違反移民法的人可能面臨驅逐出境。"},{"en":"In the convict system, deportation separated people from Britain, often permanently.","zh":"在囚犯制度中，流放把人與英國分隔，往往是永久分隔。"},{"en":"The word refers to forced removal from a place.","zh":"這個詞指被強制移離某地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be expelled for","meaning":"因……被流放","examples":[{"en":"Elizabeth Thackeray was expelled for stealing handkerchiefs.","zh":"Elizabeth Thackeray 因偷手帕而被流放。"},{"en":"Be expelled for means be forced to leave because of a particular action or offence.","zh":"be expelled for 指因某行為或罪行而被強制離開。"},{"en":"A student may be expelled for repeated serious misconduct.","zh":"學生可能因反覆嚴重違規而被開除。"},{"en":"If people were expelled for small thefts, punishment was much harsher than today.","zh":"如果人們因小型盜竊被流放，懲罰就比今天嚴厲得多。"},{"en":"The phrase connects removal with its cause.","zh":"這個片語把被移離與原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"of similar fate","meaning":"有相似命運的","examples":[{"en":"Many other convicts suffered a similar fate.","zh":"許多其他囚犯有相似命運。"},{"en":"Of similar fate means having the same or nearly the same outcome in life.","zh":"of similar fate 指人生中有相同或接近相同的結果。"},{"en":"Two shops may suffer a similar fate if both close because of high rent.","zh":"如果兩間店都因高租金結業，它們就有相似命運。"},{"en":"If several convicts were transported for minor theft, their lives followed similar paths.","zh":"如果幾名囚犯都因輕微盜竊被流放，他們的人生就走上相似道路。"},{"en":"The phrase links people through shared outcomes.","zh":"這個片語透過共同結果把人連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"eager descendants","meaning":"熱切追查的後人","examples":[{"en":"Eager descendants can now trace these convicts online.","zh":"熱切追查的後人現在可以在網上追溯這些囚犯。"},{"en":"Eager descendants are later family members who are keen to learn about their ancestors.","zh":"eager descendants 指熱切想了解祖先的後代家庭成員。"},{"en":"An eager descendant may spend weekends searching old records and ship lists.","zh":"熱切追查的後人可能在週末搜尋舊紀錄和船隻名單。"},{"en":"When online databases become available, eager descendants can research more quickly.","zh":"當網上資料庫可用，熱切追查的後人可以更快研究。"},{"en":"The phrase describes interested later generations.","zh":"這個片語描述有興趣的後代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"track an ancestor","meaning":"追查祖先","examples":[{"en":"Online databases allow descendants to track an ancestor’s history.","zh":"網上資料庫讓後人追查祖先的歷史。"},{"en":"Track an ancestor means follow records to learn where an ancestor lived, moved, or worked.","zh":"track an ancestor 指根據紀錄追查祖先住在哪裡、遷往何處或做甚麼工作。"},{"en":"A person may track an ancestor by searching census records and marriage certificates.","zh":"一個人可能透過搜尋人口普查紀錄和結婚證書來追查祖先。"},{"en":"If records are copied wrongly, it becomes harder to track an ancestor accurately.","zh":"如果紀錄被錯誤複製，就更難準確追查祖先。"},{"en":"The phrase describes following historical evidence about one family member.","zh":"這個片語描述追蹤某位家庭成員的歷史證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"deported convicts","meaning":"被流放的囚犯","examples":[{"en":"Many deported convicts were forbidden to return to Britain.","zh":"許多被流放的囚犯被禁止返回英國。"},{"en":"Deported convicts were prisoners sent away from Britain as punishment.","zh":"deported convicts 指作為懲罰被英國送走的囚犯。"},{"en":"A deported convict might begin a new life in Australia after completing a sentence.","zh":"被流放的囚犯服刑完畢後，可能在澳洲開始新生活。"},{"en":"If return was impossible or too expensive, deportation became almost permanent.","zh":"如果返回不可能或太昂貴，流放就幾乎變成永久。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to transported prisoners.","zh":"這個片語指被運送流放的囚犯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be forbidden to return","meaning":"被禁止返回","examples":[{"en":"Some convicts were forbidden to return to Britain.","zh":"有些囚犯被禁止返回英國。"},{"en":"Be forbidden to return means be officially not allowed to go back to a place.","zh":"be forbidden to return 指被官方禁止回到某地方。"},{"en":"A student may be forbidden to return to a competition after breaking serious rules.","zh":"學生嚴重違規後，可能被禁止返回比賽。"},{"en":"If convicts were forbidden to return, they had to build lives elsewhere.","zh":"如果囚犯被禁止返回，他們就必須在其他地方建立生活。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an official ban on going back.","zh":"這個片語描述官方禁止回去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in theory","meaning":"理論上","examples":[{"en":"In theory, some convicts were expelled only for a fixed term.","zh":"理論上，有些囚犯只是在固定刑期內被流放。"},{"en":"In theory means according to the rule or idea, even if reality may be different.","zh":"in theory 指根據規則或想法，即使現實可能不同。"},{"en":"In theory, online learning gives everyone access, but weak internet can create problems.","zh":"理論上，網上學習讓每個人都能取得教育，但網絡差會造成問題。"},{"en":"Convicts might have been allowed to return in theory, but many could not afford the journey.","zh":"囚犯理論上可能被允許返回，但許多人負擔不起旅程。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts official possibility with practical reality.","zh":"這個片語把官方可能性與實際現實作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"for a given term","meaning":"在指定刑期內","examples":[{"en":"Some prisoners were transported for a given term rather than for life.","zh":"有些囚犯是在指定刑期內被流放，而不是終身流放。"},{"en":"For a given term means for a fixed or specified period of time.","zh":"for a given term 指在固定或指定的一段時間內。"},{"en":"A tenant may rent a flat for a given term of one year.","zh":"租客可能以一年為指定期限租住單位。"},{"en":"If punishment lasts for a given term, it has an official end date.","zh":"如果懲罰在指定刑期內持續，它就有官方結束日期。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a set period, not an unlimited one.","zh":"這個片語指設定好的期間，而不是無限期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in reality","meaning":"實際上","examples":[{"en":"In reality, very few former convicts could afford to return home.","zh":"實際上，極少前囚犯負擔得起回家。"},{"en":"In reality means in the actual situation, not just in theory.","zh":"in reality 指在實際情況中，而不只是理論上。"},{"en":"In reality, saving money is harder when rent and food prices are high.","zh":"實際上，當租金和食物價格高，儲錢更困難。"},{"en":"Convicts could sometimes return in theory, but in reality the cost stopped most of them.","zh":"囚犯理論上有時可以返回，但實際上費用阻止了大多數人。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the practical truth.","zh":"這個片語引出實際真相。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the mother country","meaning":"祖國；宗主國","examples":[{"en":"Britain remained the mother country for the transported prisoners.","zh":"對被流放囚犯而言，英國仍是祖國。"},{"en":"The mother country is the original country connected to a colony or emigrant group.","zh":"mother country 指與殖民地或移民群體相連的原本國家。"},{"en":"Migrants may still feel emotional ties to the mother country after years abroad.","zh":"移民在海外多年後，仍可能對祖國有情感聯繫。"},{"en":"For transported convicts, Britain was home but often impossible to return to.","zh":"對被流放囚犯而言，英國是家鄉，但往往無法返回。"},{"en":"The phrase carries historical and emotional meaning.","zh":"這個片語帶有歷史和情感意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"well beyond the means of","meaning":"遠超……的負擔能力","examples":[{"en":"The cost of returning was well beyond the means of most ex-convicts.","zh":"返回英國的費用遠超大多數前囚犯的負擔能力。"},{"en":"Well beyond the means of means far too expensive for someone to afford.","zh":"well beyond the means of 指遠遠超出某人能負擔的範圍。"},{"en":"A luxury flat may be well beyond the means of an ordinary family.","zh":"豪宅可能遠超普通家庭的負擔能力。"},{"en":"If the journey home was beyond their means, ex-convicts had little real choice.","zh":"如果回家的旅費超出負擔能力，前囚犯幾乎沒有真正選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses financial impossibility.","zh":"這個片語強調財政上不可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the majority","meaning":"大多數","examples":[{"en":"The majority of former convicts lacked the money to return.","zh":"大多數前囚犯缺乏返回英國的金錢。"},{"en":"The majority means more than half of a group.","zh":"the majority 指一個群體中超過一半的人或事物。"},{"en":"The majority of students may prefer online notes if they are easier to search.","zh":"如果網上筆記較易搜尋，大多數學生可能較喜歡它們。"},{"en":"If the majority could not afford the journey, returning home was rare in practice.","zh":"如果大多數人負擔不起旅程，實際上回家就很少見。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the larger part of a group.","zh":"這個片語指出群體中較大的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"attribute something to","meaning":"將……歸因於","examples":[{"en":"Genealogists attribute Australia’s early development partly to ex-convicts.","zh":"家譜學家把澳洲早期發展部分歸因於前囚犯。"},{"en":"Attribute something to means say that something was caused by or connected with a particular reason.","zh":"attribute something to 指認為某事由某原因造成或與某原因有關。"},{"en":"A teacher may attribute a student’s improvement to regular practice.","zh":"老師可能把學生進步歸因於定期練習。"},{"en":"If ex-convicts built farms, businesses, and towns, historians may attribute development partly to them.","zh":"如果前囚犯建立農場、企業和城鎮，歷史學家可能把發展部分歸因於他們。"},{"en":"The phrase explains cause or contribution.","zh":"這個片語解釋原因或貢獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"successful early development","meaning":"早期的成功發展","examples":[{"en":"Former prisoners contributed to Australia’s successful early development.","zh":"前囚犯對澳洲早期的成功發展作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Successful early development means strong progress during the beginning stage of a place or system.","zh":"successful early development 指某地方或制度在初期階段有良好進展。"},{"en":"A new school’s successful early development may depend on committed teachers and supportive parents.","zh":"新學校早期的成功發展可能依賴投入的老師和支持的家長。"},{"en":"In early Australia, labour, building, farming, and trade helped society grow.","zh":"在早期澳洲，勞動、建築、農業和貿易幫助社會成長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes positive growth at an early stage.","zh":"這個片語描述早期階段的正面發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ex-convicts","meaning":"前囚犯","examples":[{"en":"Many ex-convicts became productive members of society.","zh":"許多前囚犯成為有生產力的社會成員。"},{"en":"Ex-convicts are people who were once prisoners but have completed their sentences or left prison.","zh":"ex-convicts 指曾經是囚犯、但已完成刑期或離開監獄的人。"},{"en":"An ex-convict may rebuild life through work, family, and community support.","zh":"前囚犯可能透過工作、家庭和社區支援重建生活。"},{"en":"If ex-convicts receive opportunities, they can contribute to society after punishment.","zh":"如果前囚犯獲得機會，他們可以在受罰後貢獻社會。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on a person’s past imprisonment, not their whole identity.","zh":"這個片語集中於一個人曾入獄的過去，而不是其全部身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"contribute fully to society","meaning":"全面貢獻社會","examples":[{"en":"Some former prisoners chose to contribute fully to society.","zh":"有些前囚犯選擇全面貢獻社會。"},{"en":"Contribute fully to society means take an active and useful role in a community or country.","zh":"contribute fully to society 指在社區或國家中發揮積極而有用的角色。"},{"en":"A retired teacher may contribute fully to society by mentoring young volunteers.","zh":"退休老師可以透過指導年輕義工來全面貢獻社會。"},{"en":"When ex-convicts work, build, and lead, they help society develop.","zh":"當前囚犯工作、建設和領導，他們就幫助社會發展。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses meaningful participation and service.","zh":"這個片語強調有意義的參與和服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"serve a sentence","meaning":"服刑","examples":[{"en":"Many prisoners entered ordinary society after serving their sentences.","zh":"許多囚犯服刑後進入普通社會。"},{"en":"Serve a sentence means complete the punishment ordered by a court.","zh":"serve a sentence 指完成法庭判處的刑罰。"},{"en":"A prisoner may serve a sentence of five years before being released.","zh":"囚犯可能服刑五年後獲釋。"},{"en":"After serving a sentence, a person may try to find work and rebuild relationships.","zh":"服刑後，一個人可能嘗試找工作並重建關係。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to completing legal punishment.","zh":"這個片語指完成法律懲罰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rewards were available to","meaning":"……可獲得獎勵","examples":[{"en":"Rewards were available to prisoners who behaved well.","zh":"表現良好的囚犯可獲得獎勵。"},{"en":"Rewards were available to means certain benefits could be given to a particular group.","zh":"rewards were available to 指某些好處可給予特定群體。"},{"en":"Scholarships may be available to students who show strong effort.","zh":"努力表現突出的學生可獲得獎學金。"},{"en":"If prisoners behaved well, rewards encouraged discipline and useful work.","zh":"如果囚犯表現良好，獎勵就鼓勵紀律和有用工作。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that benefits were possible under certain conditions.","zh":"這個片語顯示在特定條件下可以得到好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"display exemplary behaviour","meaning":"表現出模範行為","examples":[{"en":"Prisoners who displayed exemplary behaviour could receive land.","zh":"表現出模範行為的囚犯可以獲得土地。"},{"en":"Display exemplary behaviour means behave in a very good way that others could follow.","zh":"display exemplary behaviour 指行為非常良好，可作他人榜樣。"},{"en":"A student displays exemplary behaviour by helping classmates and following rules consistently.","zh":"學生透過幫助同學並持續守規，表現出模範行為。"},{"en":"If prisoners showed discipline and responsibility, authorities might reward them.","zh":"如果囚犯展現紀律和責任感，當局可能獎勵他們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes behaviour seen as a model for others.","zh":"這個片語描述被視為榜樣的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"land grant","meaning":"土地批授","examples":[{"en":"Some well-behaved prisoners received a land grant.","zh":"有些表現良好的囚犯獲得土地批授。"},{"en":"A land grant is an official gift or allocation of land by an authority.","zh":"land grant 指由當局正式贈予或分配土地。"},{"en":"A government may give a land grant to encourage farming in a new settlement.","zh":"政府可能給予土地批授，以鼓勵在新定居地耕作。"},{"en":"If ex-convicts received land grants, they could begin farming and building stable lives.","zh":"如果前囚犯獲得土地批授，他們就可以開始耕作並建立穩定生活。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to officially awarded land.","zh":"這個片語指正式授予的土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"farming the land","meaning":"耕種土地","examples":[{"en":"Prisoners received tools for developing and farming the land.","zh":"囚犯獲得工具，用來開發和耕種土地。"},{"en":"Farming the land means using land to grow crops or raise animals.","zh":"farming the land 指使用土地種植農作物或飼養動物。"},{"en":"A family may farm the land by planting vegetables and keeping chickens.","zh":"家庭可能透過種菜和養雞來耕種土地。"},{"en":"Farming the land helped early settlers produce food and support the colony.","zh":"耕種土地幫助早期定居者生產食物並支持殖民地。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on practical agricultural use.","zh":"這個片語集中於實際農業用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"access to convict labour","meaning":"使用囚犯勞工的權利","examples":[{"en":"Some former prisoners were given access to convict labour.","zh":"有些前囚犯被給予使用囚犯勞工的權利。"},{"en":"Access to convict labour means the right or opportunity to use prisoners as workers.","zh":"access to convict labour 指使用囚犯作為工人的權利或機會。"},{"en":"Early landowners might use convict labour to build roads, farms, or houses.","zh":"早期地主可能使用囚犯勞工修路、建農場或建屋。"},{"en":"If ex-convicts received labour support, they could develop land more quickly.","zh":"如果前囚犯獲得勞工支援，就能更快開發土地。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to controlled use of prisoner work.","zh":"這個片語指受控制地使用囚犯工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"go on to hold","meaning":"後來擔任","examples":[{"en":"Some former prisoners went on to hold powerful positions.","zh":"有些前囚犯後來擔任有權力的職位。"},{"en":"Go on to hold means later have or occupy a role, job, or position.","zh":"go on to hold 指後來擁有或擔任某角色、工作或職位。"},{"en":"A student who struggles at first may go on to hold a leadership role at university.","zh":"起初吃力的學生後來可能在大學擔任領導職位。"},{"en":"If ex-convicts later held public office, their social status changed greatly.","zh":"如果前囚犯後來擔任公職，他們的社會地位就大大改變。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a later achievement after an earlier stage.","zh":"這個片語顯示早期階段之後的後來成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"powerful positions","meaning":"有權力的職位","examples":[{"en":"Several ex-convicts later held powerful positions in society.","zh":"幾名前囚犯後來在社會中擔任有權力的職位。"},{"en":"Powerful positions are roles that give people influence, authority, or control.","zh":"powerful positions 指給人影響力、權威或控制力的角色。"},{"en":"A mayor, judge, or company director holds a powerful position.","zh":"市長、法官或公司董事都擔任有權力的職位。"},{"en":"If former prisoners reached powerful positions, society allowed some upward movement.","zh":"如果前囚犯能取得有權力的職位，社會就容許某種向上流動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to roles with real influence.","zh":"這個片語指具有實際影響力的角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"newly forming society","meaning":"新形成的社會","examples":[{"en":"Former convicts helped build the newly forming Australian society.","zh":"前囚犯幫助建設新形成的澳洲社會。"},{"en":"A newly forming society is a community or nation still in the early stage of development.","zh":"newly forming society 指仍處於早期發展階段的社群或國家。"},{"en":"A new town with few institutions is a newly forming society in miniature.","zh":"一個制度不多的新城鎮，就是縮小版的新形成社會。"},{"en":"In early Australia, many roles had to be created as settlements grew.","zh":"在早期澳洲，隨着定居地成長，許多角色都需要建立。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a society still being built.","zh":"這個片語描述仍在建設中的社會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"British architect","meaning":"英國建築師","examples":[{"en":"Francis Greenway was a British architect transported to Australia.","zh":"Francis Greenway 是一位被流放到澳洲的英國建築師。"},{"en":"A British architect is a person from Britain trained to design buildings.","zh":"British architect 指來自英國、受訓設計建築物的人。"},{"en":"An architect may design public buildings, houses, churches, or bridges.","zh":"建築師可能設計公共建築、住宅、教堂或橋樑。"},{"en":"If a transported architect designed major buildings, he helped shape the colony’s appearance.","zh":"如果被流放的建築師設計主要建築，他就幫助塑造殖民地面貌。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies nationality and profession.","zh":"這個片語指出國籍和職業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be convicted of fraud","meaning":"被裁定詐騙罪成","examples":[{"en":"Greenway was expelled after being convicted of fraud.","zh":"Greenway 在被裁定詐騙罪成後被流放。"},{"en":"Be convicted of fraud means be found guilty in court of dishonest financial behaviour.","zh":"be convicted of fraud 指在法庭上被裁定犯有不誠實財務行為。"},{"en":"A business owner may be convicted of fraud for using false documents to get money.","zh":"企業主可能因使用假文件取得金錢而被裁定詐騙罪成。"},{"en":"If a skilled person is convicted of fraud, their punishment may still lead to unexpected later contributions.","zh":"如果有技能的人被裁定詐騙罪成，其懲罰仍可能帶來意想不到的後來貢獻。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a legal finding of dishonesty.","zh":"這個片語描述法律上對不誠實行為的定罪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"prominent colonial buildings","meaning":"著名殖民地建築","examples":[{"en":"Greenway designed several prominent colonial buildings in Sydney.","zh":"Greenway 在悉尼設計了幾座著名殖民地建築。"},{"en":"Prominent colonial buildings are important or well-known buildings from the colonial period.","zh":"prominent colonial buildings 指殖民時期重要或著名的建築物。"},{"en":"A city may preserve prominent colonial buildings as part of its heritage.","zh":"城市可能保存著名殖民地建築作為文化遺產。"},{"en":"Such buildings can show how early society organised government, worship, and public life.","zh":"這些建築可以顯示早期社會如何組織政府、宗教和公共生活。"},{"en":"The phrase describes historically noticeable architecture.","zh":"這個片語描述歷史上顯著的建築。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be transported after","meaning":"在……之後被流放","examples":[{"en":"Alexander Munro was transported after stealing cheese.","zh":"Alexander Munro 在偷芝士後被流放。"},{"en":"Be transported after means be sent away as punishment following a particular offence.","zh":"be transported after 指在犯下某罪行後，被作為懲罰送往外地。"},{"en":"In early penal history, people could be transported after crimes that now seem minor.","zh":"在早期刑罰史中，人們可能因今天看來輕微的罪行後被流放。"},{"en":"If someone was transported after stealing food, poverty may have shaped the offence.","zh":"如果某人偷食物後被流放，貧窮可能塑造了該罪行。"},{"en":"The phrase links the punishment with the action that caused it.","zh":"這個片語把懲罰與造成它的行為連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"gas works","meaning":"煤氣廠","examples":[{"en":"Munro later built Australia’s first gas works.","zh":"Munro 後來建立了澳洲第一座煤氣廠。"},{"en":"Gas works are facilities where gas is produced or processed for lighting, heating, or industry.","zh":"gas works 指生產或處理煤氣以供照明、取暖或工業使用的設施。"},{"en":"A nineteenth-century city might depend on gas works for street lighting.","zh":"十九世紀城市可能依賴煤氣廠提供街燈照明。"},{"en":"Building gas works could help a growing town modernise its services.","zh":"建立煤氣廠可以幫助發展中的城鎮現代化其服務。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to industrial infrastructure for gas supply.","zh":"這個片語指煤氣供應的工業基礎設施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"hold the position of","meaning":"擔任……職位","examples":[{"en":"Alexander Munro later held the position of town mayor.","zh":"Alexander Munro 後來擔任市長職位。"},{"en":"Hold the position of means officially have a particular job or role.","zh":"hold the position of 指正式擁有某個工作或角色。"},{"en":"A teacher may hold the position of head of department for several years.","zh":"老師可能擔任科主任職位多年。"},{"en":"If an ex-convict held the position of mayor, social mobility was possible.","zh":"如果前囚犯能擔任市長職位，社會流動就是可能的。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies someone’s official role.","zh":"這個片語指出某人的正式角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Town Mayor","meaning":"市長","examples":[{"en":"A former convict eventually became a Town Mayor.","zh":"一名前囚犯最終成為市長。"},{"en":"A Town Mayor is an official leader of a town’s local government.","zh":"Town Mayor 指城鎮地方政府的正式領導人。"},{"en":"A Town Mayor may attend public events, support local services, and represent residents.","zh":"市長可能出席公共活動、支持本地服務並代表居民。"},{"en":"If a former convict became mayor, his public reputation must have changed greatly.","zh":"如果前囚犯成為市長，他的公共聲譽必然有很大改變。"},{"en":"The phrase names a local leadership position.","zh":"這個片語命名一個地方領導職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Mormon Church","meaning":"摩門教會","examples":[{"en":"The Mormon Church maintains major genealogical databases.","zh":"摩門教會維持大型家譜資料庫。"},{"en":"The Mormon Church is a religious organisation known for its interest in family history records.","zh":"Mormon Church 指一個以關注家族史紀錄而聞名的宗教組織。"},{"en":"Genealogy researchers may use resources developed by the Mormon Church.","zh":"家譜研究者可能使用摩門教會建立的資源。"},{"en":"Because the church collects family records, its databases are useful to researchers worldwide.","zh":"因為該教會收集家族紀錄，其資料庫對全球研究者有用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an institution connected with major genealogy resources.","zh":"這個片語指與大型家譜資源有關的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be headquartered in","meaning":"總部設於……","examples":[{"en":"The church is headquartered in Salt Lake City.","zh":"該教會總部設於鹽湖城。"},{"en":"Be headquartered in means have the main office or central base in a particular place.","zh":"be headquartered in 指主要辦公室或中央基地位於某地。"},{"en":"A technology company may be headquartered in Shenzhen but sell products worldwide.","zh":"科技公司可能總部設於深圳，但產品銷往全球。"},{"en":"If an organisation is headquartered in one city, major decisions are often made there.","zh":"如果組織總部設於某城市，重大決定通常在那裡作出。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main location of an organisation.","zh":"這個片語指出組織的主要所在地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"genealogical database","meaning":"家譜資料庫","examples":[{"en":"A genealogical database may contain millions of historical records.","zh":"家譜資料庫可能載有數以百萬計的歷史紀錄。"},{"en":"A genealogical database is an organised digital collection of family-history information.","zh":"genealogical database 指有組織的數碼家族史資料集合。"},{"en":"A researcher may search a genealogical database for births, marriages, and deaths.","zh":"研究者可能在家譜資料庫搜尋出生、婚姻和死亡紀錄。"},{"en":"Databases make research faster, but each record still needs checking.","zh":"資料庫令研究更快，但每項紀錄仍需要核查。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a structured store of ancestry data.","zh":"這個片語指有結構的祖先資料儲存庫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"International Genealogical Index","meaning":"國際家譜索引","examples":[{"en":"The International Genealogical Index contains records of many individuals.","zh":"國際家譜索引載有許多個人的紀錄。"},{"en":"The International Genealogical Index is a major collection of genealogical records.","zh":"International Genealogical Index 指一個大型家譜紀錄集合。"},{"en":"A researcher may use the index to search for names across countries and periods.","zh":"研究者可以使用該索引搜尋跨國家和時期的姓名。"},{"en":"Large indexes help connect scattered family records, but they can still contain errors.","zh":"大型索引幫助連接分散的家族紀錄，但仍可能含有錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific genealogy resource.","zh":"這個片語命名一項特定家譜資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Ancestral File","meaning":"祖先檔案資料庫","examples":[{"en":"The Ancestral File is another major genealogy database.","zh":"祖先檔案資料庫是另一個大型家譜資料庫。"},{"en":"Ancestral File refers to a database containing family-history information submitted or compiled for research.","zh":"Ancestral File 指載有提交或彙編家族史資料以供研究的資料庫。"},{"en":"A beginner may search the Ancestral File before checking original documents.","zh":"初學者可能先搜尋祖先檔案資料庫，再核對原始文件。"},{"en":"Like other compiled sources, it should be used carefully and verified.","zh":"像其他彙編資料來源一樣，它應被小心使用和核實。"},{"en":"The phrase names a genealogy database connected with ancestry records.","zh":"這個片語命名一個與祖先紀錄有關的家譜資料庫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"contain records of","meaning":"載有……的紀錄","examples":[{"en":"The databases contain records of hundreds of millions of people.","zh":"這些資料庫載有數以億計人士的紀錄。"},{"en":"Contain records of means include written or digital information about people, events, or facts.","zh":"contain records of 指包括關於人、事件或事實的書面或數碼資訊。"},{"en":"A school database may contain records of attendance and exam results.","zh":"學校資料庫可能載有出席率和考試成績紀錄。"},{"en":"If a database contains records of many people, it can help researchers find family links.","zh":"如果資料庫載有許多人的紀錄，就能幫助研究者找到家族關係。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what information is stored.","zh":"這個片語指出儲存了甚麼資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"hundreds of millions of","meaning":"數以億計的","examples":[{"en":"The databases contain information about hundreds of millions of individuals.","zh":"這些資料庫載有數以億計個人的資料。"},{"en":"Hundreds of millions of means an extremely large number, more than one hundred million.","zh":"hundreds of millions of 指非常龐大的數量，超過一億。"},{"en":"Hundreds of millions of people use messaging apps every day.","zh":"數以億計的人每天使用即時通訊應用程式。"},{"en":"A database of this size can support searches across many families and countries.","zh":"這種規模的資料庫可以支援跨越許多家庭和國家的搜尋。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses very large scale.","zh":"這個片語強調規模非常大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"genealogy enthusiasts","meaning":"家譜研究愛好者","examples":[{"en":"Several libraries and websites serve genealogy enthusiasts.","zh":"幾間圖書館和網站服務家譜研究愛好者。"},{"en":"Genealogy enthusiasts are people who are very interested in researching family history.","zh":"genealogy enthusiasts 指對研究家族史很感興趣的人。"},{"en":"A genealogy enthusiast may spend evenings comparing census records and old photographs.","zh":"家譜研究愛好者可能晚上比較人口普查紀錄和舊照片。"},{"en":"Enthusiasts help keep family history alive by sharing findings with relatives.","zh":"愛好者透過與親屬分享發現，幫助延續家族史。"},{"en":"The phrase describes people with strong interest, not necessarily professional training.","zh":"這個片語描述有強烈興趣的人，不一定受過專業訓練。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Family History Library","meaning":"家族史圖書館","examples":[{"en":"The Family History Library is a major genealogical resource.","zh":"家族史圖書館是一項重要家譜資源。"},{"en":"The Family History Library is a library that provides records and tools for researching family history.","zh":"Family History Library 指提供紀錄和工具以研究家族史的圖書館。"},{"en":"Researchers may use such a library to view old registers, microfilms, or family records.","zh":"研究者可以使用這類圖書館查閱舊登記冊、縮微膠卷或家族紀錄。"},{"en":"A major library can support both beginners and experienced genealogists.","zh":"大型圖書館可以同時支援初學者和經驗豐富的家譜學家。"},{"en":"The phrase names an important institution for genealogy research.","zh":"這個片語命名家譜研究的重要機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"more than 4,000 branches","meaning":"超過四千間分館","examples":[{"en":"The library has more than 4,000 branches.","zh":"該圖書館有超過四千間分館。"},{"en":"More than 4,000 branches means over four thousand local offices or service points.","zh":"more than 4,000 branches 指超過四千個本地辦公處或服務點。"},{"en":"A bank with more than 4,000 branches can reach customers in many towns.","zh":"擁有超過四千間分行的銀行，可以接觸許多城鎮的顧客。"},{"en":"Many branches make genealogy resources easier to access for people far from the main library.","zh":"許多分館令遠離主圖書館的人更容易取得家譜資源。"},{"en":"The phrase shows wide physical distribution.","zh":"這個片語顯示廣泛的實體分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"microfilm and microfiche","meaning":"縮微膠卷和縮微平片","examples":[{"en":"Historical records may be stored on microfilm and microfiche.","zh":"歷史紀錄可能儲存在縮微膠卷和縮微平片上。"},{"en":"Microfilm and microfiche are small photographic formats used to store documents in reduced size.","zh":"microfilm and microfiche 指用縮小影像儲存文件的小型攝影格式。"},{"en":"A library may keep old newspapers on microfilm to save space.","zh":"圖書館可能把舊報紙保存在縮微膠卷上以節省空間。"},{"en":"Researchers use readers to enlarge and view these stored records.","zh":"研究者使用閱讀器放大和查看這些儲存紀錄。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to older document-storage technologies.","zh":"這個片語指較舊的文件儲存技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be rented for research","meaning":"可租用作研究","examples":[{"en":"Microfilms can be rented for genealogical research.","zh":"縮微膠卷可租用作家譜研究。"},{"en":"Be rented for research means be borrowed or paid for temporarily so someone can study it.","zh":"be rented for research 指暫時借用或付費使用某物以作研究。"},{"en":"A student may rent equipment for research if the school does not own it.","zh":"如果學校沒有設備，學生可能租用器材作研究。"},{"en":"Renting microfilm allows researchers to view records without travelling to the original archive.","zh":"租用縮微膠卷讓研究者無需前往原檔案館也能查看紀錄。"},{"en":"The phrase shows temporary access for study.","zh":"這個片語顯示為研究而取得臨時使用權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"provide open access to","meaning":"提供……的公開使用權","examples":[{"en":"The FamilySearch website provides open access to numerous databases.","zh":"FamilySearch 網站提供眾多資料庫的公開使用權。"},{"en":"Provide open access to means allow people to use something freely or without major barriers.","zh":"provide open access to 指讓人自由或在少障礙下使用某物。"},{"en":"A school website may provide open access to revision guides before exams.","zh":"學校網站可能在考試前提供溫習指南的公開使用權。"},{"en":"Open access helps non-specialists begin research without paying high fees.","zh":"公開使用權幫助非專業人士無需支付高費用也能開始研究。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses easy public availability.","zh":"這個片語強調容易公開取得。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"numerous databases","meaning":"眾多資料庫","examples":[{"en":"The website gives researchers access to numerous databases.","zh":"該網站讓研究者使用眾多資料庫。"},{"en":"Numerous databases means many organised collections of digital information.","zh":"numerous databases 指許多有組織的數碼資訊集合。"},{"en":"A university library may offer numerous databases for journals, newspapers, and statistics.","zh":"大學圖書館可能提供眾多關於期刊、報紙和統計數據的資料庫。"},{"en":"When many databases are available, researchers can compare records from different sources.","zh":"當眾多資料庫可用，研究者可以比較不同來源的紀錄。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses variety and quantity of information sources.","zh":"這個片語強調資訊來源的種類和數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"research sources","meaning":"研究資料來源","examples":[{"en":"Genealogists use a wide variety of research sources.","zh":"家譜學家使用各式各樣的研究資料來源。"},{"en":"Research sources are materials that provide evidence or information for a study.","zh":"research sources 指為研究提供證據或資訊的材料。"},{"en":"A student’s essay may use books, interviews, statistics, and websites as research sources.","zh":"學生文章可能使用書本、訪問、統計數據和網站作研究資料來源。"},{"en":"In genealogy, sources include certificates, censuses, letters, wills, and family stories.","zh":"在家譜研究中，資料來源包括證書、人口普查、信件、遺囑和家庭故事。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to where research information comes from.","zh":"這個片語指研究資訊來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"data-sharing practices","meaning":"資料共享做法","examples":[{"en":"Data-sharing practices are central to genealogical research.","zh":"資料共享做法是家譜研究的核心。"},{"en":"Data-sharing practices are ways people exchange records, findings, or digital information.","zh":"data-sharing practices 指人們交換紀錄、發現或數碼資訊的方式。"},{"en":"Teachers use data-sharing practices when they share exam results to plan support.","zh":"老師分享考試結果以規劃支援時，就是使用資料共享做法。"},{"en":"Genealogists can solve missing links faster when they share information responsibly.","zh":"當家譜研究者負責任地分享資訊，他們可以更快解決缺失關係。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to habits and systems for exchanging data.","zh":"這個片語指交換資料的習慣和制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"central and crucial to","meaning":"對……既核心又重要","examples":[{"en":"The exchange of information is central and crucial to genealogy.","zh":"資訊交換對家譜研究既核心又重要。"},{"en":"Central and crucial to means extremely important and at the heart of something.","zh":"central and crucial to 指極其重要，並位於某事的核心。"},{"en":"Trust is central and crucial to a successful teacher-student relationship.","zh":"信任對成功的師生關係既核心又重要。"},{"en":"Without information exchange, genealogists may repeat work or miss important links.","zh":"沒有資訊交換，家譜研究者可能重複工作或錯過重要關係。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that something is not optional but essential.","zh":"這個片語強調某事不是可有可無，而是必不可少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"prove to be a major tool","meaning":"證明是重要工具","examples":[{"en":"The Internet has proven to be a major tool for genealogists.","zh":"互聯網已證明是家譜學家的重要工具。"},{"en":"Prove to be a major tool means turn out to be a very useful method or resource.","zh":"prove to be a major tool 指結果證明是非常有用的方法或資源。"},{"en":"Online dictionaries have proven to be a major tool for language learners.","zh":"網上字典已證明是語言學習者的重要工具。"},{"en":"Because the Internet makes records searchable, it has transformed family-history research.","zh":"因為互聯網令紀錄可搜尋，它改變了家族史研究。"},{"en":"The phrase judges usefulness after results are clear.","zh":"這個片語是在結果明確後判斷有用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"facilitate the transfer of","meaning":"促進……的傳送","examples":[{"en":"The Internet facilitates the transfer of information.","zh":"互聯網促進資訊的傳送。"},{"en":"Facilitate the transfer of means make it easier to move or share something from one person or place to another.","zh":"facilitate the transfer of 指令某物更容易從一個人或地方移動或分享至另一處。"},{"en":"Cloud storage facilitates the transfer of homework between students and teachers.","zh":"雲端儲存促進學生與老師之間功課的傳送。"},{"en":"In genealogy, faster transfer of information helps researchers compare findings.","zh":"在家譜研究中，更快傳送資訊幫助研究者比較發現。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses making exchange easier.","zh":"這個片語強調令交換更容易。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ease of transfer","meaning":"傳送的便利程度","examples":[{"en":"Digital formats improve the ease of transfer of information.","zh":"數碼格式改善資訊傳送的便利程度。"},{"en":"Ease of transfer means how easily something can be sent, moved, or shared.","zh":"ease of transfer 指某物被傳送、移動或分享有多容易。"},{"en":"Email improves the ease of transfer for school notices and homework files.","zh":"電郵改善學校通告和功課檔案傳送的便利程度。"},{"en":"When genealogical data is digital, researchers can share it across countries quickly.","zh":"當家譜資料是數碼格式，研究者可以快速跨國分享。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on convenience in moving information.","zh":"這個片語集中於移動資訊的方便程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"suitable for use in","meaning":"適合用於……","examples":[{"en":"Researchers share data in formats suitable for use in online forums.","zh":"研究者以適合用於網上論壇的格式分享資料。"},{"en":"Suitable for use in means appropriate or practical for a particular setting or purpose.","zh":"suitable for use in 指適合或實用於某特定環境或目的。"},{"en":"Short video clips may be suitable for use in a beginner English class.","zh":"短影片可能適合用於初級英語課堂。"},{"en":"If data is in a suitable format, other researchers can read and compare it easily.","zh":"如果資料格式合適，其他研究者就能容易閱讀和比較。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on fitness for a specific use.","zh":"這個片語集中於是否適合某特定用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"via email","meaning":"透過電郵","examples":[{"en":"Genealogical information can easily be exchanged via email.","zh":"家譜資料可以輕易透過電郵交換。"},{"en":"Via email means by using email as the method of communication.","zh":"via email 指使用電郵作為溝通方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may send feedback via email after checking a student’s essay.","zh":"老師可能在批改學生文章後透過電郵發送回饋。"},{"en":"Sharing records via email allows relatives in different countries to work together.","zh":"透過電郵分享紀錄，讓不同國家的親屬可以一起研究。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the communication channel.","zh":"這個片語指出溝通渠道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"global level of interest","meaning":"全球興趣程度","examples":[{"en":"There is a high global level of interest in family history.","zh":"全球對家族史有高度興趣。"},{"en":"Global level of interest means how much attention people around the world give to something.","zh":"global level of interest 指世界各地的人對某事給予多少關注。"},{"en":"A global level of interest in climate change can push governments to act.","zh":"全球對氣候變化的興趣程度可以推動政府行動。"},{"en":"When family-history websites attract users worldwide, demand for records increases.","zh":"當家族史網站吸引全球用戶，對紀錄的需求就增加。"},{"en":"The phrase measures international curiosity or attention.","zh":"這個片語量度國際層面的好奇或關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"demand for information","meaning":"對資料的需求","examples":[{"en":"Demand for genealogical information has become intense.","zh":"對家譜資料的需求變得非常強烈。"},{"en":"Demand for information means many people want to obtain particular facts or records.","zh":"demand for information 指許多人想取得特定事實或紀錄。"},{"en":"During exam season, demand for revision notes may rise sharply.","zh":"考試季節期間，對溫習筆記的需求可能急劇上升。"},{"en":"If many people search the same census records at once, websites may struggle.","zh":"如果許多人同時搜尋同一批人口普查紀錄，網站可能難以應付。"},{"en":"The phrase shows strong need or desire for information.","zh":"這個片語顯示對資訊的強烈需要或渴望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"prove so intense that","meaning":"強烈得令……","examples":[{"en":"Demand proved so intense that some servers temporarily collapsed.","zh":"需求強烈得令一些伺服器暫時癱瘓。"},{"en":"Prove so intense that means turn out to be so strong that it causes a result.","zh":"prove so intense that 指結果證明非常強烈，以致造成某結果。"},{"en":"Interest in concert tickets proved so intense that the website crashed.","zh":"演唱會門票需求強烈得令網站崩潰。"},{"en":"If genealogy demand overloads servers, public interest is clearly very high.","zh":"如果家譜需求令伺服器超載，公眾興趣顯然非常高。"},{"en":"The phrase connects extreme strength with consequence.","zh":"這個片語把極強程度與後果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"traffic load","meaning":"網絡流量負荷","examples":[{"en":"A sudden traffic load overwhelmed the website.","zh":"突然的網絡流量負荷壓垮了網站。"},{"en":"Traffic load is the amount of user activity or data demand on a website or server.","zh":"traffic load 指網站或伺服器上的用戶活動或資料需求量。"},{"en":"A school website may face a heavy traffic load when exam results are released.","zh":"考試成績公布時，學校網站可能面對沉重網絡流量負荷。"},{"en":"Too much traffic load can slow a website or make it stop working.","zh":"過大的網絡流量負荷會令網站變慢或停止運作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to pressure caused by online visitors.","zh":"這個片語指由網上訪客造成的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"on release of","meaning":"在……發布時","examples":[{"en":"Traffic increased sharply on release of the census data.","zh":"在人口普查資料發布時，流量急劇增加。"},{"en":"On release of means at the time when something is made public or available.","zh":"on release of 指某事公開或可取得的時候。"},{"en":"A film website may crash on release of tickets for a popular movie.","zh":"熱門電影門票發布時，電影網站可能崩潰。"},{"en":"When census data is released, many genealogists may search it immediately.","zh":"當人口普查資料發布，許多家譜學家可能立即搜尋。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the moment new information becomes available.","zh":"這個片語標示新資訊可用的一刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"temporary collapse","meaning":"暫時癱瘓","examples":[{"en":"The host servers suffered a temporary collapse.","zh":"主機伺服器出現暫時癱瘓。"},{"en":"Temporary collapse means a system stops working for a short time.","zh":"temporary collapse 指系統短時間停止運作。"},{"en":"A payment system may suffer a temporary collapse during a major online sale.","zh":"大型網上促銷期間，付款系統可能出現暫時癱瘓。"},{"en":"If servers collapse temporarily, users cannot access information until service returns.","zh":"如果伺服器暫時癱瘓，用戶在服務恢復前無法取得資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a short-lived failure.","zh":"這個片語描述短暫失靈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"host server","meaning":"主機伺服器","examples":[{"en":"The website’s host servers could not handle the demand.","zh":"該網站的主機伺服器無法應付需求。"},{"en":"A host server is a computer system that stores and delivers website data to users.","zh":"host server 指儲存並向用戶傳送網站資料的電腦系統。"},{"en":"A school website needs a reliable host server when many parents log in.","zh":"當許多家長登入時，學校網站需要可靠的主機伺服器。"},{"en":"If a host server receives too many requests, the website may slow down or crash.","zh":"如果主機伺服器收到太多請求，網站可能變慢或崩潰。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the technical system behind a website.","zh":"這個片語指網站背後的技術系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reliability of sources","meaning":"資料來源的可靠性","examples":[{"en":"Genealogists must evaluate the reliability of sources.","zh":"家譜學家必須評估資料來源的可靠性。"},{"en":"Reliability of sources means how trustworthy and accurate information sources are.","zh":"reliability of sources 指資訊來源有多可信和準確。"},{"en":"A student should check the reliability of sources before using them in an essay.","zh":"學生在文章中使用資料前應檢查資料來源的可靠性。"},{"en":"If a source has no author or date, its reliability may be weaker.","zh":"如果資料來源沒有作者或日期，其可靠性可能較弱。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on whether evidence can be trusted.","zh":"這個片語集中於證據是否可信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be evaluated in light of","meaning":"根據……來評估","examples":[{"en":"Evidence should be evaluated in light of several factors.","zh":"證據應根據幾項因素來評估。"},{"en":"Be evaluated in light of means be judged while considering particular information or conditions.","zh":"be evaluated in light of 指在考慮特定資訊或條件下作判斷。"},{"en":"A student’s performance should be evaluated in light of illness or family difficulties.","zh":"學生表現應根據疾病或家庭困難等情況來評估。"},{"en":"Genealogical records should be judged by source, date, bias, and copying history.","zh":"家譜紀錄應根據來源、日期、偏見和複製歷史來判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase means assessment must consider context.","zh":"這個片語意思是評估必須考慮語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"influence accuracy","meaning":"影響準確性","examples":[{"en":"Several factors may influence the accuracy of a historical record.","zh":"幾項因素可能影響歷史紀錄的準確性。"},{"en":"Influence accuracy means affect how correct or reliable something is.","zh":"influence accuracy 指影響某事有多正確或可靠。"},{"en":"Poor lighting can influence the accuracy of a witness’s memory.","zh":"光線不足可以影響目擊者記憶的準確性。"},{"en":"In genealogy, time, bias, and copying can all affect record accuracy.","zh":"在家譜研究中，時間、偏見和複製都可以影響紀錄準確性。"},{"en":"The phrase shows what can make information more or less correct.","zh":"這個片語顯示甚麼會令資訊較準確或較不準確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"knowledge of the informant","meaning":"資料提供者的知識","examples":[{"en":"Researchers should consider the knowledge of the informant.","zh":"研究者應考慮資料提供者的知識。"},{"en":"Knowledge of the informant means what the person giving information actually knew.","zh":"knowledge of the informant 指提供資料的人實際知道甚麼。"},{"en":"A neighbour may know where someone lived but not their exact birth date.","zh":"鄰居可能知道某人住在哪裡，但不知道其準確出生日期。"},{"en":"If an informant did not witness an event, their account may be less reliable.","zh":"如果資料提供者沒有親眼見證事件，其敘述可能較不可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase asks whether the source was in a position to know the truth.","zh":"這個片語詢問資料來源是否有條件知道真相。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"bias and mental state","meaning":"偏見和精神狀態","examples":[{"en":"An informant’s bias and mental state can affect accuracy.","zh":"資料提供者的偏見和精神狀態可以影響準確性。"},{"en":"Bias and mental state mean personal prejudice and the person’s condition of mind.","zh":"bias and mental state 指個人偏見以及該人的心理或精神狀況。"},{"en":"A tired witness may remember events differently from a calm witness.","zh":"疲倦目擊者記住事件的方式，可能不同於冷靜目擊者。"},{"en":"If someone benefits from hiding the truth, bias may distort their information.","zh":"如果某人因隱瞞真相而受益，偏見可能扭曲其資料。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why even a human source can be unreliable.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何即使是人提供的資料也可能不可靠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"passage of time","meaning":"時間流逝","examples":[{"en":"The passage of time may weaken a person’s memory.","zh":"時間流逝可能削弱一個人的記憶。"},{"en":"Passage of time means time passing between an event and the moment it is remembered or recorded.","zh":"passage of time 指事件發生與被記起或記錄之間經過的時間。"},{"en":"The passage of time can make childhood memories less detailed.","zh":"時間流逝可以令童年記憶變得較少細節。"},{"en":"If a record is written many years later, forgotten details may reduce accuracy.","zh":"如果紀錄在多年後才寫下，被遺忘的細節可能降低準確性。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that memory changes as time passes.","zh":"這個片語強調記憶會隨時間改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"potential for compilation error","meaning":"彙編出錯的可能性","examples":[{"en":"Copied documents have a greater potential for compilation error.","zh":"複製文件有較大的彙編出錯可能性。"},{"en":"Potential for compilation error means the chance of mistakes when information is copied or combined.","zh":"potential for compilation error 指在複製或整合資料時出錯的機會。"},{"en":"A class list may contain compilation errors if names are copied from several forms.","zh":"如果班級名單從幾份表格抄錄而成，可能含有彙編錯誤。"},{"en":"Each time records are transcribed or summarised, new mistakes can be introduced.","zh":"每次紀錄被轉錄或摘要，都可能引入新錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that compiled material needs checking.","zh":"這個片語提醒彙編材料需要核查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"provide information","meaning":"提供資料","examples":[{"en":"Researchers should identify the person who provided the information.","zh":"研究者應識別提供資料的人。"},{"en":"Provide information means give facts, details, or evidence to someone.","zh":"provide information 指向某人給出事實、細節或證據。"},{"en":"A patient provides information when they describe symptoms to a doctor.","zh":"病人向醫生描述症狀時，就是提供資料。"},{"en":"If the person who provided information is unknown, the record may be harder to trust.","zh":"如果提供資料的人不明，該紀錄可能較難信任。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the act of supplying details.","zh":"這個片語集中於提供細節的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"ascertain what someone knew","meaning":"確定某人知道甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Genealogists should ascertain what an informant could reasonably have known.","zh":"家譜學家應確定資料提供者合理地可能知道甚麼。"},{"en":"Ascertain what someone knew means find out what information a person truly had.","zh":"ascertain what someone knew 指查明某人真正掌握甚麼資訊。"},{"en":"A teacher may ascertain what students already know before starting a new topic.","zh":"老師可能在開始新課題前確定學生已知道甚麼。"},{"en":"If an informant was not present at an event, they may not have known the details.","zh":"如果資料提供者不在事件現場，他們可能不知道細節。"},{"en":"The phrase asks researchers to check the limits of a source’s knowledge.","zh":"這個片語要求研究者檢查資料來源知識的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"census record","meaning":"人口普查紀錄","examples":[{"en":"A census record may not identify the original informant.","zh":"人口普查紀錄可能沒有指出原本的資料提供者。"},{"en":"A census record is an official record collecting information about people in a population.","zh":"census record 指收集人口資料的官方紀錄。"},{"en":"A census record may list names, ages, occupations, and addresses.","zh":"人口普查紀錄可能列出姓名、年齡、職業和地址。"},{"en":"Genealogists use census records to find where families lived at a particular time.","zh":"家譜學家使用人口普查紀錄找出家庭在某時期住在哪裡。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to population data used as historical evidence.","zh":"這個片語指可作歷史證據的人口資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be considered unreliable","meaning":"被視為不可靠","examples":[{"en":"A record without a named source may be considered unreliable.","zh":"沒有具名資料來源的紀錄可能被視為不可靠。"},{"en":"Be considered unreliable means be judged not fully trustworthy.","zh":"be considered unreliable 指被判斷為不完全可信。"},{"en":"A news story with no evidence may be considered unreliable by careful readers.","zh":"沒有證據的新聞故事可能被細心讀者視為不可靠。"},{"en":"If no one knows who gave the information, mistakes are harder to check.","zh":"如果沒有人知道資料由誰提供，錯誤就更難核查。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence that should not be accepted too quickly.","zh":"這個片語描述不應太快接受的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"named source","meaning":"具名資料來源","examples":[{"en":"A census record may lack a named source for its information.","zh":"人口普查紀錄可能缺乏其資料的具名資料來源。"},{"en":"A named source is an identified person or document that provided the information.","zh":"named source 指提供資料的身分明確的人或文件。"},{"en":"A school report is more reliable when it has a named source for each quotation.","zh":"如果學校報告每段引文都有具名資料來源，就更可靠。"},{"en":"If a record has a named source, researchers can judge whether that source was knowledgeable.","zh":"如果紀錄有具名資料來源，研究者就能判斷該來源是否知情。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on traceable origin of information.","zh":"這個片語集中於資訊可追溯的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"death certificate","meaning":"死亡證明書","examples":[{"en":"A death certificate can provide strong evidence about a person’s death.","zh":"死亡證明書可以提供關於某人死亡的有力證據。"},{"en":"A death certificate is an official document recording that someone has died.","zh":"death certificate 指記錄某人已死亡的官方文件。"},{"en":"Genealogists use death certificates to confirm dates, places, and family details.","zh":"家譜學家使用死亡證明書確認日期、地點和家庭細節。"},{"en":"If a certificate is signed by a doctor, it may be more reliable than family memory.","zh":"如果證明書由醫生簽署，它可能比家庭記憶更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an official death record.","zh":"這個片語指官方死亡紀錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be signed by","meaning":"由……簽署","examples":[{"en":"A death certificate signed by an identified doctor is more reliable.","zh":"由身分明確醫生簽署的死亡證明書較可靠。"},{"en":"Be signed by means have someone’s signature showing approval, responsibility, or confirmation.","zh":"be signed by 指有某人的簽名，顯示批准、責任或確認。"},{"en":"A permission form must be signed by a parent before a school trip.","zh":"學校旅行前，許可表格必須由家長簽署。"},{"en":"If a certificate is signed by a named professional, its source is clearer.","zh":"如果證明書由具名專業人士簽署，其來源就更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase shows who officially confirmed the document.","zh":"這個片語顯示誰正式確認文件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"identified doctor","meaning":"身分明確的醫生","examples":[{"en":"Information from an identified doctor can be checked more easily.","zh":"來自身分明確醫生的資料較容易核查。"},{"en":"An identified doctor is a doctor whose name or identity is known.","zh":"identified doctor 指姓名或身分已知的醫生。"},{"en":"A medical note from an identified doctor is easier to verify than an unsigned note.","zh":"來自身分明確醫生的醫療證明，比沒有簽名的證明更容易核實。"},{"en":"If the doctor is known, researchers can judge the reliability of the certificate.","zh":"如果醫生身分已知，研究者可以判斷證明書的可靠性。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses clear professional identity.","zh":"這個片語強調清楚的專業身分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be accepted as reliable","meaning":"可被視為可靠","examples":[{"en":"A properly signed certificate can be accepted as more reliable.","zh":"正確簽署的證明書可被視為較可靠。"},{"en":"Be accepted as reliable means be treated as trustworthy after checking its source or quality.","zh":"be accepted as reliable 指在核查來源或質素後被視為可信。"},{"en":"A receipt from a shop is usually accepted as reliable proof of purchase.","zh":"商店收據通常可被視為可靠的購買證明。"},{"en":"If a document has a clear source and date, researchers may trust it more.","zh":"如果文件有清楚來源和日期，研究者可能更信任它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence judged strong enough to use.","zh":"這個片語描述被判斷為足夠有力可使用的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in the case of","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"In the case of bias, even a knowledgeable informant may be untruthful.","zh":"就偏見而言，即使知情的資料提供者也可能不誠實。"},{"en":"In the case of means when dealing with a particular situation or example.","zh":"in the case of 指在處理某個特定情況或例子時。"},{"en":"In the case of illness, students should tell the school as early as possible.","zh":"就疾病而言，學生應盡早通知學校。"},{"en":"In the case of biased witnesses, accurate knowledge does not guarantee honesty.","zh":"就有偏見的目擊者而言，準確認知不保證誠實。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a specific condition for discussion.","zh":"這個片語引出要討論的特定情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reliable source","meaning":"可靠資料來源","examples":[{"en":"Information may still be false even when it comes from a reliable source.","zh":"即使資料來自可靠資料來源，它仍可能是假的。"},{"en":"A reliable source is a person, document, or organisation that can usually be trusted.","zh":"reliable source 指通常可信的人、文件或組織。"},{"en":"An official school notice is usually a more reliable source than a rumour from classmates.","zh":"官方學校通告通常比同學之間的傳聞更可靠。"},{"en":"Even reliable sources can contain mistakes if the original information was wrong.","zh":"即使可靠資料來源也可能含有錯誤，如果原始資料本身錯了。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to trustworthy evidence, not perfect evidence.","zh":"這個片語指可信證據，而不是完美證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"motivation to be untruthful","meaning":"說謊的動機","examples":[{"en":"An informant may have had a motivation to be untruthful.","zh":"資料提供者可能有說謊的動機。"},{"en":"Motivation to be untruthful means a reason for someone to lie or hide facts.","zh":"motivation to be untruthful 指某人說謊或隱瞞事實的原因。"},{"en":"A witness may have a motivation to be untruthful if honesty would cost them money.","zh":"如果誠實會令目擊者損失金錢，他可能有說謊的動機。"},{"en":"In genealogy, someone might hide age, marriage, or parentage for social or financial reasons.","zh":"在家譜研究中，有人可能因社會或金錢原因隱瞞年齡、婚姻或親子關係。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why information may be deliberately false.","zh":"這個片語解釋資訊為何可能被故意扭曲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"continue to claim","meaning":"繼續申領","examples":[{"en":"A person might hide information to continue to claim a benefit.","zh":"一個人可能隱瞞資料以繼續申領福利。"},{"en":"Continue to claim means keep receiving or requesting something, especially money or support.","zh":"continue to claim 指繼續收取或申請某物，尤其是金錢或支援。"},{"en":"Someone may continue to claim a discount after their eligibility has ended.","zh":"某人可能在資格結束後仍繼續申領折扣。"},{"en":"If truth would stop a payment, a person may have reason to hide facts.","zh":"如果真相會停止付款，一個人可能有理由隱瞞事實。"},{"en":"The phrase links repeated claiming with possible dishonesty.","zh":"這個片語把反覆申領與可能的不誠實連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"government benefit","meaning":"政府福利","examples":[{"en":"Someone may lie in order to receive a government benefit.","zh":"某人可能為了領取政府福利而說謊。"},{"en":"A government benefit is financial help or support provided by the state.","zh":"government benefit 指由國家提供的財政幫助或支援。"},{"en":"Unemployment payments and housing assistance are examples of government benefits.","zh":"失業津貼和住房援助都是政府福利的例子。"},{"en":"If a record affects access to benefits, the informant may not be fully honest.","zh":"如果紀錄影響取得福利的資格，資料提供者可能不完全誠實。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to official support given by government.","zh":"這個片語指政府提供的官方支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"avoidance of taxation","meaning":"避稅","examples":[{"en":"A desire for avoidance of taxation may influence an informant.","zh":"避稅的慾望可能影響資料提供者。"},{"en":"Avoidance of taxation means trying to reduce or escape paying tax.","zh":"avoidance of taxation 指嘗試減少或逃避繳稅。"},{"en":"A business may hide income for avoidance of taxation, which can be illegal if dishonest.","zh":"企業可能為避稅而隱瞞收入；如屬不誠實，可能違法。"},{"en":"If tax records affect money, people may have a reason to report facts inaccurately.","zh":"如果稅務紀錄影響金錢，人們可能有理由不準確報告事實。"},{"en":"The phrase connects financial interest with possible false information.","zh":"這個片語把金錢利益與可能的錯誤資料連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be recorded at the same time as","meaning":"與……同時記錄","examples":[{"en":"Information recorded at the same time as an event is often more reliable.","zh":"與事件同時記錄的資料通常較可靠。"},{"en":"Be recorded at the same time as means be written down when the event happened or very close to it.","zh":"be recorded at the same time as 指在事件發生時或非常接近該時刻寫下。"},{"en":"Attendance taken during class is usually more accurate than memory a week later.","zh":"課堂期間點名通常比一星期後憑記憶更準確。"},{"en":"Records made immediately after birth or death often contain fewer memory errors.","zh":"出生或死亡後立即製作的紀錄通常較少記憶錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the value of timing in evidence.","zh":"這個片語強調證據中時間的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"close to the event","meaning":"接近事件發生時間","examples":[{"en":"A record made close to the event is usually more accurate.","zh":"接近事件發生時間製作的紀錄通常較準確。"},{"en":"Close to the event means soon before, during, or soon after something happened.","zh":"close to the event 指在某事發生前不久、期間或之後不久。"},{"en":"A witness statement written close to the event may contain clearer details.","zh":"接近事件發生時間寫下的目擊者陳述可能包含更清楚細節。"},{"en":"The longer people wait, the more likely memory mistakes become.","zh":"人們等待越久，記憶出錯的可能性越高。"},{"en":"The phrase connects timing with reliability.","zh":"這個片語把時間與可靠性連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"at a later point in time","meaning":"在較後時間","examples":[{"en":"Records written at a later point in time may contain mistakes.","zh":"在較後時間寫下的紀錄可能含有錯誤。"},{"en":"At a later point in time means after the event or after an earlier stage.","zh":"at a later point in time 指在事件之後或較早階段之後。"},{"en":"A student may understand a difficult lesson at a later point in time after more practice.","zh":"學生在更多練習後，可能在較後時間理解困難課堂。"},{"en":"If a record is written years later, memory and bias may affect it.","zh":"如果紀錄多年後才寫下，記憶和偏見可能影響它。"},{"en":"The phrase marks distance from the original event.","zh":"這個片語標示與原本事件的時間距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"intend to give","meaning":"有意提供","examples":[{"en":"An individual may intend to give a truthful account.","zh":"一個人可能有意提供真實敘述。"},{"en":"Intend to give means plan or mean to provide something.","zh":"intend to give 指計劃或打算提供某事物。"},{"en":"A witness may intend to give accurate details but still forget important facts.","zh":"目擊者可能有意提供準確細節，但仍忘記重要事實。"},{"en":"Good intention does not always guarantee accurate information.","zh":"好意不一定保證資訊準確。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on purpose, not final correctness.","zh":"這個片語集中於意圖，而不是最終正確性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"true representation of events","meaning":"對事件的真實描述","examples":[{"en":"Witnesses may try to give a true representation of events.","zh":"目擊者可能嘗試提供對事件的真實描述。"},{"en":"A true representation of events is an accurate account of what happened.","zh":"true representation of events 指對發生事情的準確敘述。"},{"en":"A school report should give a true representation of an accident, not protect one side.","zh":"學校報告應提供事故的真實描述，而不是保護某一方。"},{"en":"Memory gaps can prevent even honest people from giving a completely true account.","zh":"記憶缺口可以令誠實的人也無法提供完全真實的描述。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses accurate description of events.","zh":"這個片語強調對事件的準確描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"factual information","meaning":"事實資料","examples":[{"en":"Even factual information can be misremembered.","zh":"即使是事實資料也可能被錯記。"},{"en":"Factual information means information based on facts, such as dates, names, or places.","zh":"factual information 指基於事實的資料，例如日期、姓名或地點。"},{"en":"A passport number is factual information, while an opinion about travel is not.","zh":"護照號碼是事實資料，而對旅行的看法則不是。"},{"en":"If factual information is remembered years later, small errors may appear.","zh":"如果事實資料在多年後被記起，可能出現小錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to objective details, not feelings or interpretations.","zh":"這個片語指客觀細節，而不是感受或詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be misrepresented","meaning":"被錯誤陳述","examples":[{"en":"Historical details may be misrepresented because of memory problems.","zh":"歷史細節可能因記憶問題而被錯誤陳述。"},{"en":"Be misrepresented means be described inaccurately or in a misleading way.","zh":"be misrepresented 指被不準確或誤導地描述。"},{"en":"A student’s opinion may be misrepresented if only half the sentence is quoted.","zh":"如果只引用半句話，學生意見可能被錯誤陳述。"},{"en":"In genealogy, a wrong age or name can misrepresent a person’s identity.","zh":"在家譜研究中，錯誤年齡或姓名可以錯誤呈現一個人的身分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes inaccurate presentation of information.","zh":"這個片語描述資訊被不準確呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"lapses in memory","meaning":"記憶失誤","examples":[{"en":"Lapses in memory can reduce the accuracy of a record.","zh":"記憶失誤可以降低紀錄的準確性。"},{"en":"Lapses in memory are moments when someone forgets or remembers incorrectly.","zh":"lapses in memory 指某人忘記或記錯的情況。"},{"en":"An elderly witness may have lapses in memory about events from childhood.","zh":"年長目擊者可能對童年事件有記憶失誤。"},{"en":"If records rely on memory alone, forgotten details can create mistakes.","zh":"如果紀錄只依賴記憶，被遺忘的細節可以造成錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase explains one reason personal accounts may be unreliable.","zh":"這個片語解釋個人敘述可能不可靠的一個原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"forgotten details","meaning":"被遺忘的細節","examples":[{"en":"Forgotten details may lead to an incomplete account.","zh":"被遺忘的細節可能導致敘述不完整。"},{"en":"Forgotten details are pieces of information that someone no longer remembers.","zh":"forgotten details 指某人不再記得的資訊片段。"},{"en":"A witness may remember the accident but forget the exact time.","zh":"目擊者可能記得事故，但忘記準確時間。"},{"en":"In family history, forgotten details can hide important links between relatives.","zh":"在家族史中，被遺忘的細節可能隱藏親屬之間的重要關係。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how memory loss weakens evidence.","zh":"這個片語顯示記憶流失如何削弱證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be classified as","meaning":"被分類為","examples":[{"en":"Genealogical sources may be classified as original or derivative.","zh":"家譜資料來源可以被分類為原始或衍生資料來源。"},{"en":"Be classified as means be placed into a particular category.","zh":"be classified as 指被放入某個特定類別。"},{"en":"A book may be classified as fiction, history, or science.","zh":"一本書可以被分類為小說、歷史或科學。"},{"en":"Classifying sources helps researchers judge how close they are to the original information.","zh":"把資料來源分類幫助研究者判斷它們與原始資訊有多接近。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised categorisation.","zh":"這個片語描述有組織的分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"original source","meaning":"原始資料來源","examples":[{"en":"An original source is usually closer to the first recorded information.","zh":"原始資料來源通常較接近最初記錄的資訊。"},{"en":"An original source is the first or earliest available record of information.","zh":"original source 指最初或最早可取得的資訊紀錄。"},{"en":"A birth certificate is more original than a later typed family summary.","zh":"出生證明書比後來打字製作的家庭摘要更接近原始資料。"},{"en":"Original sources usually reduce the risk of copying errors.","zh":"原始資料來源通常降低複製錯誤的風險。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to evidence closest to the event or first record.","zh":"這個片語指最接近事件或首次紀錄的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"derivative source","meaning":"衍生資料來源","examples":[{"en":"A derivative source is based on an earlier document.","zh":"衍生資料來源是基於較早文件而成的資料。"},{"en":"A derivative source is a copy, summary, transcription, or version made from another source.","zh":"derivative source 指由另一來源製成的副本、摘要、謄本或版本。"},{"en":"A typed list copied from old church records is a derivative source.","zh":"從舊教堂紀錄抄成的打字名單就是衍生資料來源。"},{"en":"Derivative sources may be useful, but mistakes can enter during copying.","zh":"衍生資料來源可能有用，但複製期間可能引入錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to evidence one step away from the original.","zh":"這個片語指離原始資料有一步距離的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the latter refers to","meaning":"後者指的是","examples":[{"en":"The latter refers to copies, transcriptions, and summaries.","zh":"後者指的是副本、謄本和摘要。"},{"en":"The latter refers to means the second of two things just mentioned means or includes something.","zh":"the latter refers to 指剛提到的兩件事中第二件事的意思或包括內容。"},{"en":"If we compare books and films, the latter refers to films.","zh":"如果我們比較書和電影，後者指的是電影。"},{"en":"In a contrast between original and derivative sources, the latter means derivative sources.","zh":"在原始與衍生資料來源的對比中，後者指衍生資料來源。"},{"en":"The phrase helps readers follow a two-part comparison.","zh":"這個片語幫助讀者跟上雙項比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"photocopy","meaning":"影印本","examples":[{"en":"A photocopy may omit details from the original document.","zh":"影印本可能遺漏原始文件中的細節。"},{"en":"A photocopy is a paper copy made from an original document using a copying machine.","zh":"photocopy 指用影印機由原始文件製成的紙本副本。"},{"en":"A photocopy of a certificate may be easier to share than the original.","zh":"證書影印本可能比原件更容易分享。"},{"en":"If the photocopy is unclear, important names or dates may be hard to read.","zh":"如果影印本不清楚，重要姓名或日期可能難以閱讀。"},{"en":"The word refers to a copied document, not the original.","zh":"這個詞指複製文件，而不是原件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"transcription","meaning":"謄本；文字轉錄","examples":[{"en":"A transcription may contain typing or interpretation errors.","zh":"謄本可能含有打字或解讀錯誤。"},{"en":"A transcription is a written or typed copy of spoken words or handwritten text.","zh":"transcription 指把口述內容或手寫文字寫下或打字成副本。"},{"en":"A researcher may make a transcription of an old handwritten letter.","zh":"研究者可能為一封舊手寫信製作謄本。"},{"en":"If old handwriting is difficult, the transcription may misread a name.","zh":"如果舊筆跡難讀，謄本可能誤讀姓名。"},{"en":"The word refers to text copied into a readable form.","zh":"這個詞指把文字轉成可讀形式的文本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"abstract","meaning":"摘要","examples":[{"en":"An abstract summarises the main information in a longer record.","zh":"摘要概括較長紀錄中的主要資料。"},{"en":"An abstract is a short summary of a longer document or record.","zh":"abstract 指較長文件或紀錄的簡短總結。"},{"en":"A journal article usually begins with an abstract to show the main argument.","zh":"期刊文章通常以摘要開始，以展示主要論點。"},{"en":"Because an abstract is shortened, it may leave out details useful to genealogists.","zh":"因為摘要被縮短，它可能省略對家譜研究者有用的細節。"},{"en":"The word refers to a condensed version of information.","zh":"這個詞指資訊的濃縮版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"extraction","meaning":"資料摘錄","examples":[{"en":"An extraction includes selected details taken from an original source.","zh":"資料摘錄包括從原始資料來源取出的選定細節。"},{"en":"Extraction means taking particular pieces of information from a larger record.","zh":"extraction 指從較大紀錄中取出特定資訊。"},{"en":"A student may make an extraction of key dates from a long history chapter.","zh":"學生可能從長篇歷史章節中摘錄重要日期。"},{"en":"If only selected details are extracted, other useful facts may be missed.","zh":"如果只摘錄選定細節，其他有用事實可能被錯過。"},{"en":"The word refers to pulling information out of a source.","zh":"這個詞指從來源中抽取資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"compilation","meaning":"彙編","examples":[{"en":"A compilation combines information from several sources.","zh":"彙編把來自幾個來源的資訊結合起來。"},{"en":"A compilation is a collected work made by putting together information from different places.","zh":"compilation 指把不同地方的資訊集合而成的作品。"},{"en":"A teacher may create a compilation of useful grammar examples for students.","zh":"老師可能為學生製作有用文法例句的彙編。"},{"en":"If a compilation relies on weak sources, its final information may be unreliable.","zh":"如果彙編依賴薄弱資料來源，其最終資訊可能不可靠。"},{"en":"The word refers to gathered and combined material.","zh":"這個詞指收集並結合而成的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"have more room for error","meaning":"有較大的出錯空間","examples":[{"en":"Derivative sources have more room for error than originals.","zh":"衍生資料來源比原始資料來源有較大的出錯空間。"},{"en":"Have more room for error means have a greater chance that mistakes can occur.","zh":"have more room for error 指有更大機會出現錯誤。"},{"en":"A message copied by five people has more room for error than the original message.","zh":"經五個人轉抄的訊息，比原本訊息有較大的出錯空間。"},{"en":"Each transcription or summary can introduce new mistakes into a record.","zh":"每次謄寫或摘要都可能為紀錄引入新錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that indirect sources may be less reliable.","zh":"這個片語提醒間接來源可能較不可靠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"possible misinterpretation","meaning":"可能的誤解","examples":[{"en":"A transcription may contain a possible misinterpretation of the original.","zh":"謄本可能含有對原文的可能誤解。"},{"en":"Possible misinterpretation means a chance that something has been understood wrongly.","zh":"possible misinterpretation 指某事可能被錯誤理解。"},{"en":"A teacher may clarify instructions to avoid possible misinterpretation by students.","zh":"老師可能澄清指示，以避免學生可能誤解。"},{"en":"Old handwriting can cause possible misinterpretation of names and places.","zh":"舊筆跡可以造成對姓名和地點的可能誤解。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a risk of wrong understanding.","zh":"這個片語指出錯誤理解的風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"typing error","meaning":"打字錯誤","examples":[{"en":"A simple typing error can alter an important name or date.","zh":"一個簡單打字錯誤可以改變重要姓名或日期。"},{"en":"A typing error is a mistake made while entering text on a keyboard.","zh":"typing error 指用鍵盤輸入文字時出現的錯誤。"},{"en":"Writing “1889” instead of “1898” is a typing error that can change a record.","zh":"把 “1898” 打成 “1889” 是會改變紀錄的打字錯誤。"},{"en":"In genealogy, one typing error may send researchers to the wrong family.","zh":"在家譜研究中，一個打字錯誤可能令研究者走向錯誤家庭。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a small mistake with potentially serious results.","zh":"這個片語指小錯誤，但可能造成嚴重結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"loss of crucial information","meaning":"重要資料的遺失","examples":[{"en":"Copying a record may result in the loss of crucial information.","zh":"複製紀錄可能導致重要資料的遺失。"},{"en":"Loss of crucial information means important details disappear or are left out.","zh":"loss of crucial information 指重要細節消失或被省略。"},{"en":"If a hospital form loses crucial information, treatment may be delayed.","zh":"如果醫院表格遺失重要資料，治療可能延誤。"},{"en":"A copied record may omit witnesses, dates, or notes that matter to researchers.","zh":"複製紀錄可能省略對研究者重要的證人、日期或備註。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the danger of missing essential details.","zh":"這個片語強調遺漏必要細節的危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"original documentation","meaning":"原始文件","examples":[{"en":"Researchers should compare derivative sources with the original documentation.","zh":"研究者應把衍生資料來源與原始文件比較。"},{"en":"Original documentation means the first or official documents that record information.","zh":"original documentation 指記錄資訊的最初或官方文件。"},{"en":"A passport application should be checked against original documentation such as a birth certificate.","zh":"護照申請應根據出生證明書等原始文件核對。"},{"en":"Comparing copies with originals helps find mistakes introduced later.","zh":"把副本與原件比較有助找出後來引入的錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the most authoritative documents available.","zh":"這個片語指可取得的最具權威文件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct heading for each paragraph.","zh":"考生為每段選出正確標題。"},{"en":"Choose the correct heading means select the title that best matches a paragraph’s main idea.","zh":"choose the correct heading 指選擇最符合段落主旨的標題。"},{"en":"In IELTS Reading, students should read the whole paragraph before choosing a heading.","zh":"在 IELTS 閱讀中，學生應閱讀整段後再選標題。"},{"en":"If a heading only matches one detail, it may not be the correct answer.","zh":"如果標題只符合一個細節，它未必是正確答案。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a common reading-question task.","zh":"這個片語指常見閱讀題型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"more headings than paragraphs","meaning":"標題多於段落","examples":[{"en":"The task provides more headings than paragraphs.","zh":"題目提供的標題多於段落。"},{"en":"More headings than paragraphs means there are extra heading choices that will not be used.","zh":"more headings than paragraphs 指標題選項有多餘項目，不會全部用上。"},{"en":"In a matching task, more options than questions prevent students from guessing too easily.","zh":"在配對題中，選項多於題目可以防止學生太容易猜答案。"},{"en":"Students must eliminate headings that are too narrow, too broad, or irrelevant.","zh":"學生必須排除過窄、過闊或無關的標題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an exam design with distractors.","zh":"這個片語描述有干擾選項的考試設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"an embarrassing heritage","meaning":"令人尷尬的祖先背景","examples":[{"en":"Convict ancestry was once regarded as an embarrassing heritage.","zh":"囚犯祖先背景曾被視為令人尷尬的祖先背景。"},{"en":"An embarrassing heritage is a family or historical background that people feel ashamed of.","zh":"embarrassing heritage 指令人感到羞恥的家族或歷史背景。"},{"en":"A family may hide an embarrassing heritage if society judges it harshly.","zh":"如果社會嚴厲評價某背景，家庭可能隱藏令人尷尬的祖先背景。"},{"en":"When attitudes change, an embarrassing heritage can become a source of pride.","zh":"當態度改變，令人尷尬的祖先背景可以成為自豪來源。"},{"en":"The phrase links history with social shame.","zh":"這個片語把歷史與社會羞恥連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"assess validity","meaning":"評估可信性","examples":[{"en":"Researchers must assess the validity of genealogical evidence.","zh":"研究者必須評估家譜證據的可信性。"},{"en":"Assess validity means judge whether something is true, sound, or acceptable as evidence.","zh":"assess validity 指判斷某事是否真實、合理或可作證據。"},{"en":"A teacher assesses the validity of an argument by checking its evidence.","zh":"老師透過檢查證據來評估論點的可信性。"},{"en":"In genealogy, validity depends on source, date, bias, and copying history.","zh":"在家譜研究中，可信性取決於來源、日期、偏見和複製歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on judging whether evidence can be trusted.","zh":"這個片語集中於判斷證據是否可信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"diversity of application","meaning":"用途的多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Genealogy has a diversity of applications in modern society.","zh":"家譜研究在現代社會有用途的多樣性。"},{"en":"Diversity of application means something can be used in many different ways.","zh":"diversity of application 指某事物可以有許多不同用途。"},{"en":"Smartphones show diversity of application because they can be used for learning, banking, maps, and communication.","zh":"智能手機展現用途的多樣性，因為它們可用於學習、銀行、地圖和溝通。"},{"en":"Genealogy can help with identity, family reunions, migration history, and legal questions.","zh":"家譜研究可以幫助身份認同、家庭團聚、移民史和法律問題。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses many possible uses.","zh":"這個片語強調許多可能用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"interpretation errors","meaning":"解讀錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Derivative records may contain interpretation errors.","zh":"衍生紀錄可能含有解讀錯誤。"},{"en":"Interpretation errors are mistakes caused by understanding information wrongly.","zh":"interpretation errors 指因錯誤理解資訊而造成的錯誤。"},{"en":"A student may make interpretation errors if they misunderstand a question’s wording.","zh":"如果學生誤解題目措辭，可能犯解讀錯誤。"},{"en":"Old handwriting can lead to interpretation errors in names, dates, and places.","zh":"舊筆跡可能導致姓名、日期和地點上的解讀錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mistakes in meaning, not just typing.","zh":"這個片語描述意思上的錯誤，而不只是打字錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"past usage","meaning":"過往用途","examples":[{"en":"Genealogy’s past usage focused on inheritance and noble ancestry.","zh":"家譜研究的過往用途集中於繼承和貴族祖先。"},{"en":"Past usage means how something was used in earlier times.","zh":"past usage 指某事物在早期如何被使用。"},{"en":"The past usage of a building may explain why it still has large storage rooms.","zh":"建築物的過往用途可能解釋為何它仍有大型儲物室。"},{"en":"Understanding past usage shows how genealogy changed from elite proof to popular hobby.","zh":"了解過往用途顯示家譜研究如何由精英證明變成大眾興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to former purposes or functions.","zh":"這個片語指以前的目的或功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"useful sources","meaning":"有用的資料來源","examples":[{"en":"Libraries, databases, and websites are useful sources for genealogists.","zh":"圖書館、資料庫和網站是家譜學家的有用資料來源。"},{"en":"Useful sources are materials that provide helpful and relevant information.","zh":"useful sources 指提供有幫助和相關資訊的材料。"},{"en":"A student writing about history may use useful sources such as archives and interviews.","zh":"寫歷史文章的學生可能使用檔案和訪問等有用資料來源。"},{"en":"In genealogy, useful sources can save time and confirm family links.","zh":"在家譜研究中，有用資料來源可以節省時間並確認家族關係。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to information sources that support research.","zh":"這個片語指支持研究的資訊來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"Australasian importance","meaning":"對澳大拉西亞的重要性","examples":[{"en":"The First Fleet has particular Australasian importance.","zh":"第一艦隊對澳大拉西亞有特殊重要性。"},{"en":"Australasian importance means significance for Australia, New Zealand, and the surrounding region.","zh":"Australasian importance 指對澳洲、新西蘭及周邊地區的重要性。"},{"en":"A historical event may have Australasian importance if it shaped settlement or identity in the region.","zh":"如果歷史事件塑造該地區的定居或身份，它就可能有澳大拉西亞重要性。"},{"en":"The First Fleet matters especially to Australian history and family ancestry.","zh":"第一艦隊對澳洲歷史和家族祖先尤其重要。"},{"en":"The phrase links importance to the Australasian region.","zh":"這個片語把重要性連接到澳大拉西亞地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"changing viewpoints","meaning":"不斷轉變的觀點","examples":[{"en":"Genealogy has contributed to changing viewpoints about convicts.","zh":"家譜研究促成了人們對囚犯不斷轉變的觀點。"},{"en":"Changing viewpoints are opinions or attitudes that are shifting over time.","zh":"changing viewpoints 指隨時間轉變的意見或態度。"},{"en":"Changing viewpoints about mental health have made schools more open to counselling.","zh":"對心理健康不斷轉變的觀點令學校更願意接受輔導。"},{"en":"When families learn more about convict ancestors, old shame may turn into pride.","zh":"當家庭更了解囚犯祖先，舊有羞恥可能變成自豪。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual changes in how people think.","zh":"這個片語描述人們想法的逐步改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"significant roles","meaning":"重要角色","examples":[{"en":"Former convicts later played significant roles in Australian society.","zh":"前囚犯後來在澳洲社會扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"Significant roles are important parts or positions in a situation, organisation, or society.","zh":"significant roles 指在某情況、組織或社會中的重要部分或職位。"},{"en":"Nurses play significant roles in hospitals because they care for patients every day.","zh":"護士在醫院中扮演重要角色，因為他們每天照顧病人。"},{"en":"If ex-convicts became architects, mayors, or business builders, their roles were significant.","zh":"如果前囚犯成為建築師、市長或企業建立者，他們的角色就是重要的。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights meaningful contribution.","zh":"這個片語突出有意義的貢獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether statements agree with the information given.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與所給資料相符。"},{"en":"Agree with the information given means match what the passage actually says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文章實際所說內容一致。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students must check the text rather than rely on memory or opinion.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生必須檢查文本，而不是依賴記憶或意見。"},{"en":"A statement agrees only if the passage clearly supports it.","zh":"只有當文章清楚支持某陳述，它才與資料相符。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個片語用於 TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章中的資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradict the information means say the opposite of what the text states.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文本所述相反的內容。"},{"en":"If a passage says most people stayed, a statement saying most left contradicts it.","zh":"如果文章說大多數人留下，而陳述說大多數人離開，就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should choose FALSE only when the statement clearly conflicts with the text.","zh":"只有當陳述清楚與文本衝突時，學生才應選 FALSE。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct disagreement with given evidence.","zh":"這個片語描述與所給證據直接不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students choose “NOT GIVEN” when there is no relevant information.","zh":"當沒有相關資料時，學生選擇 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not say enough to decide.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文章沒有提供足夠資料作判斷。"},{"en":"If the text gives no age, there is no information on whether the person was young or old.","zh":"如果文本沒有給出年齡，就沒有資料判斷該人年輕還是年老。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from background knowledge when the passage is silent.","zh":"當文章沒有提及時，學生不應根據背景知識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the meaning of NOT GIVEN.","zh":"這個片語解釋 NOT GIVEN 的意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"early applications of","meaning":"……的早期用途","examples":[{"en":"Early applications of genealogy focused on inherited status.","zh":"家譜研究的早期用途集中於繼承身份。"},{"en":"Early applications of something are the first ways it was used.","zh":"early applications of something 指某事物最早被使用的方式。"},{"en":"Early applications of computers were often limited to calculation and data storage.","zh":"電腦的早期用途常限於計算和資料儲存。"},{"en":"Genealogy first served legal and social status purposes before becoming a hobby.","zh":"家譜研究先服務於法律和社會地位目的，之後才成為興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to original or earlier uses.","zh":"這個片語指原本或早期的用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"population movement","meaning":"人口遷移","examples":[{"en":"Modern genealogy may examine population movement and migration.","zh":"現代家譜研究可能考察人口遷移和移民。"},{"en":"Population movement means people moving from one place to another over time.","zh":"population movement 指人們隨時間從一地遷往另一地。"},{"en":"Census records can show population movement from villages to cities.","zh":"人口普查紀錄可以顯示人口由村莊遷往城市。"},{"en":"Wars, jobs, and political restrictions can all cause population movement.","zh":"戰爭、工作和政治限制都可以造成人口遷移。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement of groups, not only individuals.","zh":"這個片語描述群體的移動，而不只是個人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be reserved for","meaning":"專門留給……","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether deportation was reserved for serious criminals.","zh":"該陳述問流放是否專門留給嚴重罪犯。"},{"en":"Be reserved for means be kept only for a particular person, group, or purpose.","zh":"be reserved for 指只保留給特定人士、群體或用途。"},{"en":"Some seats on a bus are reserved for elderly passengers.","zh":"巴士上有些座位專門留給長者乘客。"},{"en":"If deportation was not reserved for serious criminals, minor offenders could also be transported.","zh":"如果流放不是專門留給嚴重罪犯，輕微犯人也可能被流放。"},{"en":"The phrase shows exclusive use or restriction.","zh":"這個片語顯示專門用途或限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"pose a serious threat to","meaning":"對……構成嚴重威脅","examples":[{"en":"Many transported convicts did not pose a serious threat to society.","zh":"許多被流放囚犯並未對社會構成嚴重威脅。"},{"en":"Pose a serious threat to means create a real danger for someone or something.","zh":"pose a serious threat to 指對某人或某事造成真正危險。"},{"en":"A broken bridge may pose a serious threat to drivers and pedestrians.","zh":"破損橋樑可能對司機和行人構成嚴重威脅。"},{"en":"If convicts were minor offenders, they may not have endangered society in a major way.","zh":"如果囚犯是輕微犯人，他們可能沒有重大危害社會。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on risk and danger.","zh":"這個片語集中於風險和危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"choose to stay","meaning":"選擇留下","examples":[{"en":"Some ex-convicts chose to stay in Australia after their sentences.","zh":"有些前囚犯服刑後選擇留在澳洲。"},{"en":"Choose to stay means decide not to leave a place when leaving is possible.","zh":"choose to stay 指在可以離開時決定不離開某地。"},{"en":"A student may choose to stay after class to ask the teacher questions.","zh":"學生可能選擇下課後留下來問老師問題。"},{"en":"If ex-convicts saw opportunity in Australia, they may have stayed willingly.","zh":"如果前囚犯在澳洲看見機會，他們可能自願留下。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses personal decision.","zh":"這個片語強調個人決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"opportunities it presented","meaning":"它所提供的機會","examples":[{"en":"Australia presented opportunities that were unavailable in Britain.","zh":"澳洲提供了英國沒有的機會。"},{"en":"Opportunities it presented means the chances or advantages that a place or situation offered.","zh":"opportunities it presented 指某地方或情況所提供的機會或優勢。"},{"en":"A new job may be attractive because of the training opportunities it presents.","zh":"新工作可能因它提供的培訓機會而吸引人。"},{"en":"Land, work, and social mobility may have encouraged ex-convicts to stay.","zh":"土地、工作和社會流動可能鼓勵前囚犯留下。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on benefits created by a situation.","zh":"這個片語集中於某情況創造的好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"overwhelming interest","meaning":"壓倒性的興趣","examples":[{"en":"Overwhelming interest in genealogy has caused technical problems.","zh":"對家譜研究的壓倒性興趣造成了技術問題。"},{"en":"Overwhelming interest means extremely strong attention or demand from many people.","zh":"overwhelming interest 指大量人群非常強烈的關注或需求。"},{"en":"Overwhelming interest in concert tickets can crash a ticketing website.","zh":"對演唱會門票的壓倒性興趣可以令售票網站崩潰。"},{"en":"If too many people search genealogy records at once, servers may fail.","zh":"如果太多人同時搜尋家譜紀錄，伺服器可能失靈。"},{"en":"The phrase shows interest so strong that it creates pressure.","zh":"這個片語顯示興趣強烈得造成壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"obtaining genealogical information","meaning":"取得家譜資料","examples":[{"en":"The Internet has simplified the process of obtaining genealogical information.","zh":"互聯網簡化了取得家譜資料的過程。"},{"en":"Obtaining genealogical information means getting records or facts about family history.","zh":"obtaining genealogical information 指取得關於家族史的紀錄或事實。"},{"en":"A beginner may obtain genealogical information from birth records, wills, and online databases.","zh":"初學者可以從出生紀錄、遺囑和網上資料庫取得家譜資料。"},{"en":"Easier access can encourage more people to begin researching their ancestry.","zh":"更容易取得資料可以鼓勵更多人開始研究祖先。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on acquiring family-history evidence.","zh":"這個片語集中於取得家族史證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"technological difficulties","meaning":"技術困難","examples":[{"en":"Heavy online demand has led to technological difficulties.","zh":"沉重網上需求導致技術困難。"},{"en":"Technological difficulties are problems involving computer systems, websites, software, or equipment.","zh":"technological difficulties 指涉及電腦系統、網站、軟件或設備的問題。"},{"en":"A school may face technological difficulties if online lessons start but the platform crashes.","zh":"如果網上課堂開始但平台崩潰，學校可能面對技術困難。"},{"en":"In genealogy, high traffic can overload servers and prevent access to records.","zh":"在家譜研究中，高流量可以令伺服器超載，阻止人們取得紀錄。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical problems caused by technology.","zh":"這個片語指由科技造成的實際問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"recreational genealogy","meaning":"業餘家譜研究","examples":[{"en":"Recreational genealogy has become increasingly popular.","zh":"業餘家譜研究變得越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"Recreational genealogy means researching family history as a hobby rather than as professional work.","zh":"recreational genealogy 指把研究家族史作為興趣，而不是專業工作。"},{"en":"A retired person may enjoy recreational genealogy by building a family tree online.","zh":"退休人士可能透過在網上建立族譜來享受業餘家譜研究。"},{"en":"The Internet has made this hobby easier for ordinary people to begin.","zh":"互聯網令普通人更容易開始這項興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase distinguishes hobby research from formal professional research.","zh":"這個片語把興趣研究與正式專業研究區分開來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"become more popular","meaning":"變得更受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Genealogy has become more popular because records are easier to access.","zh":"家譜研究因紀錄更容易取得而變得更受歡迎。"},{"en":"Become more popular means attract more interest, users, or supporters over time.","zh":"become more popular 指隨時間吸引更多興趣、用戶或支持者。"},{"en":"Cycling may become more popular when cities build safer bike lanes.","zh":"當城市建設更安全單車徑，踩單車可能變得更受歡迎。"},{"en":"When family records move online, more people can try genealogy at home.","zh":"當家族紀錄轉到網上，更多人可以在家嘗試家譜研究。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rising public interest.","zh":"這個片語描述公眾興趣上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"fashionable hobby","meaning":"時尚興趣","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that genealogy has become a fashionable hobby.","zh":"該選項暗示家譜研究已成為一種時尚興趣。"},{"en":"A fashionable hobby is an activity that becomes popular or socially attractive for a time.","zh":"fashionable hobby 指一段時間內變得受歡迎或在社會上吸引人的活動。"},{"en":"Making sourdough bread became a fashionable hobby for many people staying at home.","zh":"對許多留在家的人來說，製作酸種麵包曾成為時尚興趣。"},{"en":"If genealogy is fashionable, people may try it because friends and media talk about it.","zh":"如果家譜研究成為時尚興趣，人們可能因朋友和媒體談論它而嘗試。"},{"en":"The phrase can suggest popularity driven by trend.","zh":"這個片語可暗示由潮流推動的受歡迎程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"trace missing relatives","meaning":"尋找失散親屬","examples":[{"en":"Some people use genealogy to trace missing relatives.","zh":"有些人使用家譜研究尋找失散親屬。"},{"en":"Trace missing relatives means search for family members whose location or identity is unknown.","zh":"trace missing relatives 指搜尋位置或身分不明的家庭成員。"},{"en":"An adopted adult may trace missing relatives through records and DNA tests.","zh":"被領養成人可能透過紀錄和 DNA 測試尋找失散親屬。"},{"en":"If war or migration separated a family, genealogy may help reconnect its branches.","zh":"如果戰爭或移民分隔家庭，家譜研究可能幫助重新連接家族分支。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on finding lost family connections.","zh":"這個片語集中於尋找失去的家庭聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"political barriers","meaning":"政治障礙","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to a reduction in political barriers.","zh":"該選項提到政治障礙的減少。"},{"en":"Political barriers are government rules, borders, or restrictions that make action difficult.","zh":"political barriers 指令行動變困難的政府規則、邊界或限制。"},{"en":"Visa rules can create political barriers for families trying to reunite.","zh":"簽證規則可以為想團聚的家庭造成政治障礙。"},{"en":"If political barriers fall, records and relatives may become easier to access.","zh":"如果政治障礙降低，紀錄和親屬可能變得更容易接觸。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to obstacles created by political systems.","zh":"這個片語指由政治制度造成的障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"require less effort","meaning":"需要較少工夫","examples":[{"en":"Online research means genealogy may require less effort than before.","zh":"網上研究意味家譜研究可能比以前需要較少工夫。"},{"en":"Require less effort means need less time, energy, or difficulty to complete.","zh":"require less effort 指完成某事需要較少時間、精力或困難。"},{"en":"Using a search function can require less effort than reading every page manually.","zh":"使用搜尋功能可能比手動閱讀每一頁需要較少工夫。"},{"en":"If records are searchable online, beginners can start without travelling to archives.","zh":"如果紀錄可在網上搜尋，初學者無需前往檔案館也能開始。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a task becoming easier.","zh":"這個片語描述任務變得更容易。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"original sentence","meaning":"原本判決","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whose original sentence was reduced.","zh":"題目問誰的原本判決被減輕。"},{"en":"Original sentence means the first punishment decided by the court before any change.","zh":"original sentence 指在任何改變之前，法庭最初決定的懲罰。"},{"en":"A court may reduce an original sentence if new evidence or mercy is considered.","zh":"如果考慮新證據或寬恕，法庭可能減輕原本判決。"},{"en":"In convict history, a death sentence could be reduced to deportation.","zh":"在囚犯歷史中，死刑可以被減輕為流放。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the first legal punishment, not a grammar sentence.","zh":"這個片語指最初法律懲罰，而不是文法上的句子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"break the law","meaning":"違反法律","examples":[{"en":"Several convicts were punished for breaking the law.","zh":"幾名囚犯因違反法律而受罰。"},{"en":"Break the law means do something illegal.","zh":"break the law 指做違法的事情。"},{"en":"A driver breaks the law if they drive through a red light.","zh":"司機衝紅燈就是違反法律。"},{"en":"In the past, even minor law-breaking could lead to very severe punishment.","zh":"在過去，即使輕微違法也可能導致非常嚴厲的懲罰。"},{"en":"The phrase describes actions against legal rules.","zh":"這個片語描述違反法律規則的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"be reduced","meaning":"被減輕","examples":[{"en":"A death sentence could be reduced to deportation.","zh":"死刑可以被減輕為流放。"},{"en":"Be reduced means be made smaller, lighter, or less severe.","zh":"be reduced 指被降低、減少或變得較不嚴重。"},{"en":"A school fine may be reduced if a student explains the situation honestly.","zh":"如果學生誠實解釋情況，學校罰款可能被減輕。"},{"en":"When a punishment is reduced, the final sentence is less harsh than the original one.","zh":"當懲罰被減輕，最終刑罰比原本刑罰較輕。"},{"en":"The phrase can refer to numbers, costs, or legal severity.","zh":"這個片語可以指數字、成本或法律嚴重程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"be fundamental to","meaning":"對……至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Data sharing is fundamental to genealogical research.","zh":"資料共享對家譜研究至關重要。"},{"en":"Be fundamental to means be basic and essential to something.","zh":"be fundamental to 指對某事基本且必不可少。"},{"en":"Clear communication is fundamental to good teamwork.","zh":"清楚溝通對良好團隊合作至關重要。"},{"en":"Genealogy depends on shared records because one family’s evidence may help another.","zh":"家譜研究依賴共享紀錄，因為一個家庭的證據可能幫助另一個家庭。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that a process cannot work well without.","zh":"這個片語描述某過程不可缺少的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"original records","meaning":"原始紀錄","examples":[{"en":"Original records are valuable because they reduce copying errors.","zh":"原始紀錄有價值，因為它們減少複製錯誤。"},{"en":"Original records are the first or official documents made closest to the event.","zh":"original records 指最接近事件而製作的最初或官方文件。"},{"en":"A birth certificate is an original record of a person’s birth.","zh":"出生證明書是一個人出生的原始紀錄。"},{"en":"If researchers use original records, they avoid mistakes introduced by later copies.","zh":"如果研究者使用原始紀錄，就能避免後來副本引入的錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to primary evidence.","zh":"這個片語指一手證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"electronic transfer","meaning":"電子傳送","examples":[{"en":"The Internet allows rapid electronic transfer of genealogical data.","zh":"互聯網容許家譜資料快速電子傳送。"},{"en":"Electronic transfer means sending information digitally through computers or networks.","zh":"electronic transfer 指透過電腦或網絡以數碼方式傳送資訊。"},{"en":"Banks use electronic transfer to move money between accounts.","zh":"銀行使用電子傳送在帳戶之間轉移金錢。"},{"en":"Genealogists can share family trees quickly through electronic transfer.","zh":"家譜學家可以透過電子傳送快速分享族譜。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to digital movement of information or data.","zh":"這個片語指資訊或數據的數碼傳送。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"pooling of information","meaning":"匯集資料","examples":[{"en":"Pooling of information allows genealogists to share findings.","zh":"匯集資料讓家譜學家分享發現。"},{"en":"Pooling of information means collecting knowledge from several people or sources into one shared place.","zh":"pooling of information 指把幾個人或來源的知識集合到一個共享地方。"},{"en":"Teachers may improve lessons by pooling information about students’ common mistakes.","zh":"老師可以透過匯集學生常見錯誤的資料來改善課堂。"},{"en":"In genealogy, pooled information can connect family branches that one person could not find alone.","zh":"在家譜研究中，匯集資料可以連接一個人單獨找不到的家族分支。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses cooperative sharing.","zh":"這個片語強調合作分享。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"approach with caution","meaning":"必須審慎看待","examples":[{"en":"Census information must be approached with caution.","zh":"人口普查資料必須審慎看待。"},{"en":"Approach with caution means treat something carefully because it may contain risks or errors.","zh":"approach with caution 指因某事可能有風險或錯誤而小心處理。"},{"en":"A student should approach online summaries with caution before trusting them.","zh":"學生在相信網上摘要前應審慎看待。"},{"en":"Census records may be useful but can lack named informants or contain mistakes.","zh":"人口普查紀錄可能有用，但可能缺乏具名資料提供者或含有錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against careless acceptance.","zh":"這個片語提醒不要草率接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"be attributed to","meaning":"歸於……提供","examples":[{"en":"Census information may not be attributed to a particular individual.","zh":"人口普查資料可能無法歸於某個特定人士提供。"},{"en":"Be attributed to means be identified as coming from a particular person or source.","zh":"be attributed to 指被指出來自某個特定人士或來源。"},{"en":"A quote should be attributed to its original speaker.","zh":"引文應歸於其原本發言者。"},{"en":"If information cannot be attributed to anyone, its reliability becomes harder to judge.","zh":"如果資訊不能歸於任何人，其可靠性就較難判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase links information with its source.","zh":"這個片語把資訊與其來源連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"particular individual","meaning":"某個特定人士","examples":[{"en":"A census record may not name the particular individual who supplied the information.","zh":"人口普查紀錄可能沒有列明提供資料的某個特定人士。"},{"en":"A particular individual is a specific person, not a general group.","zh":"particular individual 指某一個具體的人，而不是泛指群體。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask which particular individual witnessed an incident.","zh":"老師可能詢問是哪個特定人士目擊了事件。"},{"en":"If the particular individual is unnamed, researchers cannot assess their knowledge or bias.","zh":"如果該特定人士沒有具名，研究者就無法評估其知識或偏見。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses exact personal identity.","zh":"這個片語強調準確個人身分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"be validated by","meaning":"得到……核實","examples":[{"en":"A death certificate may be validated by an identified doctor.","zh":"死亡證明書可能得到身分明確醫生核實。"},{"en":"Be validated by means be confirmed or supported by a trusted person, process, or evidence.","zh":"be validated by 指得到可信人士、程序或證據確認或支持。"},{"en":"A student’s absence may be validated by a doctor’s note.","zh":"學生缺席可能得到醫生紙核實。"},{"en":"If a document is validated by a named professional, it becomes easier to trust.","zh":"如果文件由具名專業人士核實，就更容易信任。"},{"en":"The phrase describes official or credible confirmation.","zh":"這個片語描述官方或可信確認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"administrative practices","meaning":"行政做法","examples":[{"en":"The option questions whether past administrative practices were unreliable.","zh":"該選項質疑過去的行政做法是否不可靠。"},{"en":"Administrative practices are the routine methods used by organisations to record, manage, and process information.","zh":"administrative practices 指組織用來記錄、管理和處理資訊的日常方法。"},{"en":"A school’s administrative practices include keeping attendance and exam records.","zh":"學校的行政做法包括保存出席紀錄和考試紀錄。"},{"en":"If old administrative practices were careless, historical records may contain mistakes.","zh":"如果舊行政做法粗疏，歷史紀錄可能含有錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to office or record-keeping procedures.","zh":"這個片語指辦公室或紀錄保存程序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"financial motivation","meaning":"金錢動機","examples":[{"en":"An informant may hide the truth because of financial motivation.","zh":"資料提供者可能因金錢動機而隱瞞真相。"},{"en":"Financial motivation is a money-related reason for doing something.","zh":"financial motivation 指與金錢有關的行動原因。"},{"en":"A worker may take extra shifts because of financial motivation.","zh":"工人可能因金錢動機而多做額外班次。"},{"en":"If someone gains a benefit by lying, their financial motivation can affect the record’s accuracy.","zh":"如果某人透過說謊獲得利益，其金錢動機可能影響紀錄準確性。"},{"en":"The phrase connects money with behaviour or decision-making.","zh":"這個片語把金錢與行為或決策連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 15 - GENEALOGY.pdf","sourcePage":25}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 16":[{"front":"a library at your fingertips","meaning":"觸手可及的圖書館","examples":[{"en":"Digitised books can place an enormous library at your fingertips.","zh":"數碼化書籍可以把一個龐大圖書館放到你觸手可及之處。"},{"en":"A library at your fingertips means a huge collection of books or information that you can reach easily and quickly.","zh":"a library at your fingertips 指一個龐大的書籍或資訊集合，可以輕易而快速地取得。"},{"en":"With a good reading app, a student can have a library at her fingertips on the bus.","zh":"有了好的閱讀應用程式，學生在巴士上也可以擁有觸手可及的圖書館。"},{"en":"Online access can save time because users do not need to travel to a physical library.","zh":"網上查閱可以節省時間，因為使用者不需要前往實體圖書館。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests convenience, speed, and easy access to knowledge.","zh":"這個短語暗示方便、快速，以及容易取得知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"at the height of","meaning":"在……的高峰期","examples":[{"en":"Many people made bold predictions at the height of the dotcom boom.","zh":"許多人在科網熱潮的高峰期作出大膽預測。"},{"en":"At the height of something means during its most intense, successful, or active period.","zh":"at the height of 某事，指在它最強烈、最成功或最活躍的時期。"},{"en":"At the height of the summer holiday, the airport is crowded with families and tourists.","zh":"在暑假高峰期，機場擠滿家庭和旅客。"},{"en":"People often make extreme predictions at the height of excitement because everything seems possible.","zh":"人們常在興奮情緒高峰時作出極端預測，因為一切似乎都有可能。"},{"en":"The phrase places an event at the peak of a trend or situation.","zh":"這個短語把事件放在某趨勢或情況的頂峰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the dotcom boom","meaning":"科網熱潮","examples":[{"en":"Online businesses expanded rapidly during the dotcom boom.","zh":"網上企業在科網熱潮期間迅速擴張。"},{"en":"The dotcom boom was a period when internet companies grew quickly and attracted huge investment.","zh":"dotcom boom 是互聯網公司快速增長並吸引大量投資的時期。"},{"en":"During a boom, investors may put money into new companies before knowing whether they will succeed.","zh":"在熱潮期間，投資者可能在尚未知公司會否成功前就投入資金。"},{"en":"The dotcom boom created excitement about online shopping, search engines, and digital services.","zh":"科網熱潮令人對網上購物、搜尋器和數碼服務感到興奮。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a period of strong internet-business growth and optimism.","zh":"這個短語描述互聯網業務強勁增長和樂觀情緒的時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"it was widely assumed that","meaning":"人們普遍以為","examples":[{"en":"It was widely assumed that computers would replace printed books.","zh":"人們普遍以為電腦會取代印刷書籍。"},{"en":"It was widely assumed that means many people believed something was true without necessarily proving it.","zh":"it was widely assumed that 指許多人相信某事為真，但未必已證明。"},{"en":"It was widely assumed that online lessons would be easier, but many teachers found them difficult to manage.","zh":"人們普遍以為網上課堂會較容易，但許多老師發現它們難以管理。"},{"en":"A widely held assumption can later be challenged by real experience.","zh":"廣泛存在的假設後來可以被真實經驗挑戰。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a common belief that may or may not be correct.","zh":"這個短語引出一個常見信念，而它可能正確，也可能不正確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a publishing revolution","meaning":"出版業革命","examples":[{"en":"Commentators predicted that a publishing revolution was about to begin.","zh":"評論者預測一場出版業革命即將開始。"},{"en":"A publishing revolution means a major change in how books, newspapers, or written works are produced and distributed.","zh":"publishing revolution 指書籍、報紙或文字作品的製作和發行方式出現重大改變。"},{"en":"Cheap printing once created a publishing revolution by making books available to more people.","zh":"廉價印刷曾帶來出版業革命，使更多人能取得書籍。"},{"en":"Digital platforms can change publishing because writers can reach readers without traditional bookshops.","zh":"數碼平台可以改變出版業，因為作者能不經傳統書店接觸讀者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a deep transformation in the world of written material.","zh":"這個短語描述文字材料世界中的深層轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the printed word","meaning":"印刷文字；紙本出版物","examples":[{"en":"The printed word has survived despite the growth of digital media.","zh":"儘管數碼媒體增長，印刷文字仍然存活下來。"},{"en":"The printed word means written material in physical printed form, such as books, newspapers, and magazines.","zh":"printed word 指以實體印刷形式出現的文字材料，例如書籍、報紙和雜誌。"},{"en":"Many readers still trust the printed word because a paper book feels permanent and carefully edited.","zh":"許多讀者仍信任印刷文字，因為紙本書感覺持久且經過仔細編輯。"},{"en":"Digital media may grow quickly, but printed material can remain valuable for comfort and concentration.","zh":"數碼媒體可能迅速增長，但紙本材料仍可因舒適和專注而保持價值。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to paper-based writing and publishing.","zh":"這個短語指以紙本為基礎的文字和出版。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be supplanted by","meaning":"被……取代","examples":[{"en":"Some people expected printed books to be supplanted by computer screens.","zh":"有些人預期印刷書籍會被電腦屏幕取代。"},{"en":"To be supplanted by something means to be replaced by it, often because the new thing seems more useful or modern.","zh":"be supplanted by 某物，指被它取代，常因新事物看似更有用或更現代。"},{"en":"Paper maps have been partly supplanted by phone navigation apps.","zh":"紙本地圖已部分被手機導航應用程式取代。"},{"en":"A tool may be supplanted when people find a faster or cheaper alternative.","zh":"當人們找到更快或更便宜的替代品，一種工具就可能被取代。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one thing losing its place to another.","zh":"這個短語描述一物失去位置，由另一物接替。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"computer screen","meaning":"電腦屏幕","examples":[{"en":"Many readers still dislike reading long novels from a computer screen.","zh":"許多讀者仍不喜歡從電腦屏幕閱讀長篇小說。"},{"en":"A computer screen is the display surface on a computer where text, images, and videos appear.","zh":"computer screen 是電腦上顯示文字、影像和影片的顯示面。"},{"en":"A student may read short articles on a computer screen but prefer paper for a long textbook.","zh":"學生可能在電腦屏幕上閱讀短文章，但長篇教科書則較喜歡紙本。"},{"en":"Long screen reading can make some people feel tired because the eyes remain focused on bright light.","zh":"長時間看屏幕閱讀會令某些人疲倦，因為眼睛一直集中於明亮光線。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the visual display used for digital reading and work.","zh":"這個短語指用於數碼閱讀和工作的視覺顯示器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be just around the corner","meaning":"即將發生","examples":[{"en":"A complete transition to digital books once seemed just around the corner.","zh":"完全轉向數碼書籍曾一度似乎即將發生。"},{"en":"To be just around the corner means to be expected very soon.","zh":"be just around the corner 指預期很快就會發生。"},{"en":"Final exams are just around the corner, so students should start revising seriously.","zh":"期末考試即將到來，所以學生應開始認真溫習。"},{"en":"When people feel a change is very close, they may prepare before it actually happens.","zh":"當人們覺得變化很接近，他們可能在它真正發生前先作準備。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that appears imminent.","zh":"這個短語描述某事看似迫在眉睫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"little to match","meaning":"沒有甚麼能比得上……","examples":[{"en":"For many readers, there is little to match the pleasure of opening a good book.","zh":"對許多讀者來說，沒有甚麼能比得上翻開一本好書的樂趣。"},{"en":"Little to match means very few things are as good as or comparable with something.","zh":"little to match 指很少東西能與某事一樣好或相比。"},{"en":"For many grandparents, there is little to match the joy of seeing grandchildren visit.","zh":"對許多祖父母來說，沒有甚麼能比得上孫兒探訪的喜悅。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses that an experience is difficult to equal.","zh":"這個短語表達某種經驗很難被媲美。"},{"en":"It is often used to praise something strongly but gently.","zh":"它常用來強烈但溫和地讚賞某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"crack the spine of a book","meaning":"翻開新書；把書脊翻鬆","examples":[{"en":"Some readers enjoy cracking the spine of a new book.","zh":"有些讀者享受翻開新書並把書脊翻鬆。"},{"en":"To crack the spine of a book means to open a book wide enough that its spine bends or loosens.","zh":"crack the spine of a book 指把書打開到書脊彎曲或鬆開的程度。"},{"en":"A reader may gently crack the spine of a paperback before settling into a long story.","zh":"讀者可能在投入長篇故事前，輕輕把平裝書的書脊翻鬆。"},{"en":"The action can make a book easier to hold open, but it may also damage a treasured copy.","zh":"這個動作可以令書更容易攤開，但也可能損壞珍貴書本。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the physical pleasure or handling of a paper book.","zh":"這個短語描述紙本書的實體閱讀樂趣或處理方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"settle down for","meaning":"安頓下來享受……","examples":[{"en":"She settled down for an hour of uninterrupted reading.","zh":"她安頓下來，享受一小時不受打擾的閱讀。"},{"en":"To settle down for something means to get comfortable and prepare to spend time doing it.","zh":"settle down for 某事，指讓自己舒服地準備花時間做某事。"},{"en":"After dinner, a student may settle down for two hours of revision at her desk.","zh":"晚飯後，學生可能在書桌前安頓下來溫習兩小時。"},{"en":"People settle down for an activity when they expect to focus without rushing.","zh":"當人們預期會專注而不趕急地做某活動，就會安頓下來。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests comfort, readiness, and a period of concentration.","zh":"這個短語暗示舒適、準備好，以及一段專注時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a flurry of activity","meaning":"一連串密集行動","examples":[{"en":"A recent flurry of activity has revived interest in online books.","zh":"近期一連串密集行動重新激起人們對網上書籍的興趣。"},{"en":"A flurry of activity means a sudden burst of many actions happening quickly.","zh":"flurry of activity 指許多行動突然快速發生。"},{"en":"Before a school open day, there may be a flurry of activity as teachers prepare displays.","zh":"在學校開放日前，老師準備展板時可能會有一連串密集行動。"},{"en":"A flurry of activity can make people feel that a topic is becoming important again.","zh":"一連串密集行動可以令人覺得某主題再次變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fast, concentrated movement or effort.","zh":"這個短語描述快速而集中的活動或努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"technology companies","meaning":"科技公司","examples":[{"en":"Several major technology companies are investing in digital publishing.","zh":"幾間大型科技公司正在投資數碼出版。"},{"en":"Technology companies are businesses that create, sell, or manage digital tools, software, hardware, or online services.","zh":"technology companies 是創造、銷售或管理數碼工具、軟件、硬件或網上服務的企業。"},{"en":"A technology company may build a reading app, a search engine, or a cloud storage service.","zh":"科技公司可能開發閱讀應用程式、搜尋器或雲端儲存服務。"},{"en":"When technology companies enter publishing, they can change how books are found and read.","zh":"當科技公司進入出版業，它們可以改變書籍被尋找和閱讀的方式。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to firms whose main work is based on technology.","zh":"這個短語指主要工作以科技為基礎的公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"suggest that","meaning":"顯示；表明","examples":[{"en":"Recent corporate initiatives suggest that online books still have a future.","zh":"近期企業計劃顯示，網上書籍仍有未來。"},{"en":"Suggest that means show, indicate, or make an idea seem likely without proving it completely.","zh":"suggest that 指顯示、表明或令某想法看似可能，但未必完全證明。"},{"en":"Empty seats in a class may suggest that students find the lesson difficult or uninteresting.","zh":"課室空座位可能顯示學生覺得課堂困難或沒趣。"},{"en":"Researchers and writers use “suggest” when evidence points toward a conclusion cautiously.","zh":"當證據謹慎地指向某結論時，研究人員和作者會使用 “suggest”。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a careful claim based on signs or evidence.","zh":"這個短語引出基於跡象或證據的謹慎主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"bring books online","meaning":"把書籍帶到網上","examples":[{"en":"Technology companies are developing new ways to bring books online.","zh":"科技公司正在發展新方法，把書籍帶到網上。"},{"en":"To bring books online means to make books available through the internet in digital form.","zh":"bring books online 指以數碼形式透過互聯網提供書籍。"},{"en":"A library can bring books online by scanning old texts and adding them to a searchable website.","zh":"圖書館可以透過掃描舊文本並把它們加入可搜尋網站，把書籍帶到網上。"},{"en":"Bringing books online can help readers who live far from major libraries.","zh":"把書籍帶到網上可以幫助住得離大型圖書館很遠的讀者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving books from physical shelves into digital access.","zh":"這個短語描述把書籍由實體書架轉移到數碼查閱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"still very much alive","meaning":"仍然十分活躍；依然存在","examples":[{"en":"The dream of a comprehensive online library is still very much alive.","zh":"建立全面網上圖書館的夢想仍然十分活躍。"},{"en":"Still very much alive means still active, important, or likely to continue.","zh":"still very much alive 指仍然活躍、重要或有可能繼續。"},{"en":"After many failed attempts, the plan for a community garden is still very much alive.","zh":"在多次失敗嘗試後，社區花園計劃仍然存在。"},{"en":"An idea can remain alive when people continue to invest time, money, or belief in it.","zh":"當人們繼續投入時間、金錢或信念，一個想法就能繼續存在。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that something has not disappeared.","zh":"這個短語強調某事尚未消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"digitise printed volumes","meaning":"把印刷書籍數碼化","examples":[{"en":"Several companies have begun to digitise thousands of printed volumes.","zh":"幾間公司已開始把數以千計的印刷書籍數碼化。"},{"en":"To digitise printed volumes means to turn physical books into digital files that computers can store and display.","zh":"digitise printed volumes 指把實體書轉成電腦可儲存和顯示的數碼檔案。"},{"en":"A museum may digitise printed volumes so researchers can read rare books without touching them.","zh":"博物館可能把印刷書籍數碼化，讓研究人員不用觸碰珍本也能閱讀。"},{"en":"Digitising books can protect fragile copies and make them easier to search.","zh":"把書籍數碼化可以保護脆弱副本，並令搜尋更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes converting paper books into digital form.","zh":"這個短語描述把紙本書轉換成數碼形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"thousands of volumes","meaning":"數以千計的書籍","examples":[{"en":"The project aims to scan thousands of volumes from major libraries.","zh":"該項目旨在掃描大型圖書館中數以千計的書籍。"},{"en":"Thousands of volumes means a very large number of books or bound works.","zh":"thousands of volumes 指非常大量的書籍或裝訂作品。"},{"en":"A university library may store thousands of volumes on history, science, and literature.","zh":"大學圖書館可能收藏數以千計關於歷史、科學和文學的書籍。"},{"en":"Scanning thousands of volumes requires time, equipment, and careful organisation.","zh":"掃描數以千計的書籍需要時間、設備和仔細組織。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used when discussing large library collections.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論大型圖書館收藏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not without controversy","meaning":"並非沒有爭議","examples":[{"en":"The mass digitisation of books is not without controversy.","zh":"大規模把書籍數碼化並非沒有爭議。"},{"en":"Not without controversy means something has caused disagreement, criticism, or public debate.","zh":"not without controversy 指某事引起分歧、批評或公共辯論。"},{"en":"A school’s decision to ban phones may be not without controversy because parents and students disagree.","zh":"學校禁止手機的決定可能並非沒有爭議，因為家長和學生意見不同。"},{"en":"Controversy often appears when benefits and risks affect different groups differently.","zh":"當好處和風險對不同群體有不同影響，爭議常會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase means an idea may be useful but still disputed.","zh":"這個短語表示某想法可能有用，但仍有爭議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the world’s most popular search engine","meaning":"全球最受歡迎的搜尋器","examples":[{"en":"Google became the world’s most popular search engine.","zh":"Google 成為全球最受歡迎的搜尋器。"},{"en":"The world’s most popular search engine means the search service used by the largest number of people globally.","zh":"world’s most popular search engine 指全球最多人使用的搜尋服務。"},{"en":"A search engine helps users find websites, images, books, news, and other information.","zh":"搜尋器幫助使用者尋找網站、圖片、書籍、新聞和其他資訊。"},{"en":"Popular search engines can strongly influence what information people see first.","zh":"受歡迎的搜尋器可以強烈影響人們最先看到甚麼資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes global dominance in online search.","zh":"這個短語描述網上搜尋方面的全球主導地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"post a first instalment of","meaning":"發布首批……","examples":[{"en":"The company posted a first instalment of digitised books online.","zh":"該公司在網上發布首批數碼化書籍。"},{"en":"To post a first instalment of something means to publish or upload the first part of a larger project.","zh":"post a first instalment of 某物，指發布或上載較大項目的第一部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may post a first instalment of revision notes before uploading the rest later.","zh":"老師可能先發布首批溫習筆記，之後再上載其餘部分。"},{"en":"Releasing a first instalment lets users see the project before it is complete.","zh":"發布首批內容讓使用者在項目完成前先看到成果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making the first portion publicly available.","zh":"這個短語描述公開提供第一部分內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"an initiative","meaning":"新計劃；倡議","examples":[{"en":"Google Print was an initiative to make books searchable online.","zh":"Google Print 是一項旨在令書籍可在網上搜尋的新計劃。"},{"en":"An initiative is a new plan or action started to solve a problem or achieve a goal.","zh":"initiative 是為了解決問題或達成目標而開始的新計劃或行動。"},{"en":"A school may launch an initiative to help students read for twenty minutes every day.","zh":"學校可能推出一項倡議，幫助學生每天閱讀二十分鐘。"},{"en":"Initiatives often require planning, funding, and cooperation from several people.","zh":"新計劃常需要規劃、資金和多人合作。"},{"en":"The word describes a purposeful new project.","zh":"這個詞描述有目的的新項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be first mooted","meaning":"首次被提出","examples":[{"en":"The digital-library initiative was first mooted a year earlier.","zh":"數碼圖書館計劃在一年前首次被提出。"},{"en":"To be first mooted means to be first suggested or raised for discussion.","zh":"be first mooted 指首次被建議或提出來討論。"},{"en":"The idea of a new homework policy was first mooted at a teachers’ meeting.","zh":"新功課政策的想法首次在教師會議上被提出。"},{"en":"A proposal may be mooted long before it becomes an official project.","zh":"一項提案可能在成為正式項目前很久已被提出。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the first public mention of an idea.","zh":"這個短語描述某想法首次公開被提及。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"collaborative effort","meaning":"協作項目","examples":[{"en":"The project was a collaborative effort between Google and research libraries.","zh":"該項目是 Google 與研究圖書館之間的協作項目。"},{"en":"A collaborative effort is work done jointly by different people, groups, or organisations.","zh":"collaborative effort 是由不同人物、群體或機構共同完成的工作。"},{"en":"A school concert is a collaborative effort involving students, teachers, parents, and technicians.","zh":"學校音樂會是一項協作項目，涉及學生、老師、家長和技術人員。"},{"en":"Collaboration matters when one group has resources and another has knowledge or access.","zh":"當一個群體有資源，另一個群體有知識或渠道，合作就很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses shared work rather than one person acting alone.","zh":"這個短語強調共同工作，而不是單獨行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"leading research libraries","meaning":"頂尖研究圖書館","examples":[{"en":"Several leading research libraries supplied books for digitisation.","zh":"幾間頂尖研究圖書館提供書籍作數碼化。"},{"en":"Leading research libraries are important libraries with major academic collections and strong research resources.","zh":"leading research libraries 是擁有大型學術收藏和強大研究資源的重要圖書館。"},{"en":"A leading research library may hold rare manuscripts, old newspapers, and specialist journals.","zh":"頂尖研究圖書館可能收藏珍貴手稿、舊報紙和專門期刊。"},{"en":"Such libraries can support digitisation because they own valuable books and know how to preserve them.","zh":"這些圖書館能支持數碼化，因為它們擁有珍貴書籍並知道如何保存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes top-level libraries used by scholars.","zh":"這個短語描述供學者使用的頂級圖書館。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"aim to make something available","meaning":"旨在提供……","examples":[{"en":"The project aims to make thousands of books available online.","zh":"該項目旨在網上提供數以千計的書籍。"},{"en":"To aim to make something available means to plan to let people access or use it.","zh":"aim to make something available 指計劃讓人們能取得或使用某物。"},{"en":"A school website may aim to make past papers available to all students.","zh":"學校網站可能旨在向所有學生提供歷屆試卷。"},{"en":"Making resources available can reduce inequality when people cannot reach them physically.","zh":"提供資源可以在有人無法親身取得時減少不平等。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a goal of improving access.","zh":"這個短語描述改善取得途徑的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be searched and read online","meaning":"可在網上搜尋及閱讀","examples":[{"en":"Digitised books can be searched and read online.","zh":"數碼化書籍可在網上搜尋及閱讀。"},{"en":"To be searched and read online means users can look for words in a digital text and read it through the internet.","zh":"be searched and read online 指使用者能在數碼文本中尋找字詞，並透過互聯網閱讀。"},{"en":"A student can search and read an online textbook to find a chapter quickly.","zh":"學生可以搜尋和閱讀網上教科書，快速找到某一章。"},{"en":"Searchable digital text saves time because readers do not need to turn every page.","zh":"可搜尋的數碼文本節省時間，因為讀者不用翻每一頁。"},{"en":"The phrase describes two key functions of digital books.","zh":"這個短語描述數碼書籍的兩個主要功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"free of charge","meaning":"免費","examples":[{"en":"Users can read some of the digitised material free of charge.","zh":"使用者可以免費閱讀部分數碼化材料。"},{"en":"Free of charge means without paying any money.","zh":"free of charge 指不用支付任何金錢。"},{"en":"A museum may allow students to enter free of charge on weekdays.","zh":"博物館可能容許學生在平日免費入場。"},{"en":"Free access can attract more users, especially people who cannot afford paid services.","zh":"免費查閱可以吸引更多使用者，尤其是負擔不起付費服務的人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something provided at no cost.","zh":"這個短語描述無需費用提供的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be covered by copyright","meaning":"受版權保障","examples":[{"en":"The first books released were not covered by copyright.","zh":"首批發布的書籍不受版權保障。"},{"en":"To be covered by copyright means to be legally protected so others cannot copy or publish it freely.","zh":"be covered by copyright 指受法律保護，使他人不能自由複製或出版。"},{"en":"A modern novel is usually covered by copyright, so teachers cannot reproduce the whole book without permission.","zh":"現代小說通常受版權保障，所以老師不能未經許可複製整本書。"},{"en":"Copyright protection affects what companies can scan, share, or sell online.","zh":"版權保障會影響公司可以在網上掃描、分享或銷售甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes legal protection for creative work.","zh":"這個短語描述對創作作品的法律保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"attract the ire of","meaning":"招致……的不滿","examples":[{"en":"The digitisation plan attracted the ire of several publishers.","zh":"該數碼化計劃招致幾間出版商的不滿。"},{"en":"To attract the ire of someone means to make them angry or strongly dissatisfied.","zh":"attract the ire of 某人，指令他們憤怒或強烈不滿。"},{"en":"A school policy may attract the ire of parents if it is introduced without consultation.","zh":"如果學校政策未經諮詢便推出，可能招致家長不滿。"},{"en":"Companies can attract public ire when people feel their rights have been ignored.","zh":"當人們覺得權利被忽視，公司可能招致公眾憤怒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes causing anger from a particular group.","zh":"這個短語描述引起某特定群體的怒氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"publishing firms","meaning":"出版公司","examples":[{"en":"Several large publishing firms challenged Google in court.","zh":"幾間大型出版公司在法庭上挑戰 Google。"},{"en":"Publishing firms are companies that produce, edit, market, and sell books or other written works.","zh":"publishing firms 是製作、編輯、推廣和銷售書籍或其他文字作品的公司。"},{"en":"A publishing firm may work with writers, designers, printers, and bookshops.","zh":"出版公司可能與作家、設計師、印刷商和書店合作。"},{"en":"Publishing firms care about copyright because books are their main business assets.","zh":"出版公司重視版權，因為書籍是它們的主要商業資產。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to companies in the publishing industry.","zh":"這個短語指出版業中的公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sue someone for","meaning":"因……起訴某人","examples":[{"en":"Five publishers sued Google for allegedly violating copyright.","zh":"五間出版商因 Google 被指侵犯版權而起訴它。"},{"en":"To sue someone for something means to take legal action against them because of a claimed wrong.","zh":"sue someone for 某事，指因聲稱的錯誤行為而對某人採取法律行動。"},{"en":"A customer may sue a company for selling a dangerous product.","zh":"顧客可能因公司出售危險產品而起訴該公司。"},{"en":"Lawsuits can force a dispute to be decided by a court rather than private argument.","zh":"訴訟可以迫使爭議由法庭而不是私人爭論來裁決。"},{"en":"The phrase describes starting a legal case against someone.","zh":"這個短語描述對某人展開法律案件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"violate copyright","meaning":"侵犯版權","examples":[{"en":"Publishers claimed that scanning protected books violated copyright.","zh":"出版商聲稱掃描受保護書籍侵犯版權。"},{"en":"To violate copyright means to break the legal rules protecting someone’s creative work.","zh":"violate copyright 指違反保護某人創作作品的法律規則。"},{"en":"Uploading a full paid textbook for strangers to download may violate copyright.","zh":"把完整付費教科書上載給陌生人下載，可能侵犯版權。"},{"en":"Copyright violation can lead to lawsuits, fines, or removal of online material.","zh":"侵犯版權可能導致訴訟、罰款或移除網上內容。"},{"en":"The phrase describes illegal use of protected creative content.","zh":"這個短語描述非法使用受保護創作內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"scanned material","meaning":"掃描所得的資料","examples":[{"en":"The dispute concerned scanned material that remained legally protected.","zh":"爭議涉及仍受法律保護的掃描所得資料。"},{"en":"Scanned material is text or images copied from a physical source into digital form.","zh":"scanned material 是從實體來源複製成數碼形式的文字或圖像。"},{"en":"A student may create scanned material by using a phone to scan pages from a worksheet.","zh":"學生可能用手機掃描工作紙頁面，製作掃描資料。"},{"en":"Scanned material can be useful, but sharing it may be restricted by copyright.","zh":"掃描資料可以有用，但分享它可能受版權限制。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to digital copies made from physical documents or books.","zh":"這個短語指由實體文件或書籍製成的數碼副本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"out of print","meaning":"已絕版","examples":[{"en":"A book may be out of print but still protected by copyright.","zh":"一本書可能已絕版，但仍受版權保障。"},{"en":"Out of print means a book is no longer being produced or sold in new printed copies by the publisher.","zh":"out of print 指出版社不再生產或銷售新的印刷副本。"},{"en":"A reader may search second-hand shops for an out-of-print novel.","zh":"讀者可能到二手書店尋找一本已絕版小說。"},{"en":"Being out of print does not automatically mean a book can be copied freely.","zh":"已絕版不自動代表書籍可以被自由複製。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a publishing status, not necessarily a copyright status.","zh":"這個短語描述出版狀態，而不一定描述版權狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be protected by law","meaning":"受法律保障","examples":[{"en":"Some older publications are still protected by law.","zh":"有些較舊出版物仍受法律保障。"},{"en":"To be protected by law means to have rights or restrictions supported by legal rules.","zh":"be protected by law 指擁有由法律規則支持的權利或限制。"},{"en":"Employees are protected by law when employers must provide safe working conditions.","zh":"當僱主必須提供安全工作環境時，員工就是受法律保障。"},{"en":"Legal protection can stop others from copying, selling, or misusing certain materials.","zh":"法律保障可以阻止他人複製、銷售或濫用某些材料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes official protection created by the legal system.","zh":"這個短語描述由法律制度創造的官方保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"short extracts from","meaning":"……的簡短摘錄","examples":[{"en":"Google said it would publish only short extracts from protected works.","zh":"Google 表示只會發布受保護作品的簡短摘錄。"},{"en":"Short extracts from a work are small selected parts taken from a longer text.","zh":"short extracts from 某作品，是從較長文本中抽取的小部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may show short extracts from a novel to discuss style without copying the whole book.","zh":"老師可能展示小說的簡短摘錄來討論風格，而不是複製整本書。"},{"en":"Extracts let readers sample a work while limiting how much material is reproduced.","zh":"摘錄讓讀者試看作品，同時限制被重製的材料數量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes brief portions taken from a larger piece of writing.","zh":"這個短語描述從較大文字作品中取出的簡短部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"material under copyright","meaning":"受版權保障的內容","examples":[{"en":"Express permission is normally required to reproduce material under copyright.","zh":"複製受版權保障的內容通常需要明確許可。"},{"en":"Material under copyright is creative content legally protected from unauthorised copying or distribution.","zh":"material under copyright 是受法律保護、不得未經授權複製或分發的創作內容。"},{"en":"A textbook chapter may be material under copyright even if it is old.","zh":"教科書章節即使很舊，也可能是受版權保障的內容。"},{"en":"Using copyrighted material without permission can create legal problems for schools and companies.","zh":"未經許可使用受版權保障內容，可以為學校和公司帶來法律問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes content that cannot be freely copied.","zh":"這個短語描述不能自由複製的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"express permission","meaning":"明確許可","examples":[{"en":"The company would publish more only with the copyright holder’s express permission.","zh":"該公司只有在版權持有人明確許可下才會發布更多內容。"},{"en":"Express permission means clear, direct, and explicit approval.","zh":"express permission 指清楚、直接和明確的批准。"},{"en":"A school needs a parent’s express permission before taking a child on an overnight trip.","zh":"學校帶孩子參加過夜旅行前，需要家長明確許可。"},{"en":"Express permission reduces confusion because everyone knows approval has been given.","zh":"明確許可可以減少混亂，因為每個人都知道批准已經給予。"},{"en":"The phrase describes permission that is clearly stated, not merely assumed.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚說明的許可，而不是單憑假設的許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be unconvinced","meaning":"不信服","examples":[{"en":"Publishers remained unconvinced by Google’s assurances.","zh":"出版商仍不信服 Google 的保證。"},{"en":"To be unconvinced means not to believe that an explanation, promise, or argument is strong enough.","zh":"be unconvinced 指不相信某解釋、承諾或論點足夠有力。"},{"en":"A parent may be unconvinced by a child’s excuse for missing homework.","zh":"家長可能不信服孩子沒有交功課的藉口。"},{"en":"People remain unconvinced when evidence does not answer their main concern.","zh":"當證據沒有回答主要憂慮，人們就會仍然不信服。"},{"en":"The phrase describes doubt after hearing someone’s explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述聽過解釋後仍有懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ironically","meaning":"諷刺的是","examples":[{"en":"Ironically, some publishers were simultaneously collaborating with Google.","zh":"諷刺的是，有些出版商同時正與 Google 合作。"},{"en":"Ironically means in a surprising or opposite way compared with what people might expect.","zh":"ironically 指以令人意外或與預期相反的方式。"},{"en":"Ironically, the student who hated speeches became the best presenter in class.","zh":"諷刺的是，那個討厭演講的學生成為班上最好的匯報者。"},{"en":"Irony often appears when actions or results contradict the situation around them.","zh":"當行動或結果與周圍情況相矛盾時，就常出現諷刺。"},{"en":"The word signals an unexpected contrast.","zh":"這個詞表示出乎意料的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"collaborate with","meaning":"與……合作","examples":[{"en":"Publishers collaborated with Google on a separate commercial project.","zh":"出版商與 Google 在另一個商業項目上合作。"},{"en":"To collaborate with someone means to work together with them on a shared task or goal.","zh":"collaborate with 某人，指與他們共同處理一項共同任務或目標。"},{"en":"Two teachers may collaborate with each other to design a reading programme.","zh":"兩位老師可能合作設計閱讀計劃。"},{"en":"Collaboration can combine different strengths, such as technology, content, and audience access.","zh":"合作可以結合不同優勢，例如科技、內容和接觸觀眾的渠道。"},{"en":"The phrase describes joint work between people or organisations.","zh":"這個短語描述人物或機構之間的共同工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a separate venture","meaning":"另一項商業計劃","examples":[{"en":"Google Print Publisher was a separate venture from the library project.","zh":"Google Print Publisher 是獨立於圖書館項目的另一項商業計劃。"},{"en":"A separate venture is a different business project or activity from another one.","zh":"separate venture 是與另一項目不同的商業項目或活動。"},{"en":"A restaurant may open a separate venture selling frozen meals online.","zh":"餐廳可能開展另一項商業計劃，在網上銷售冷凍餐。"},{"en":"Separate ventures may share a company name but have different goals and customers.","zh":"不同商業計劃可能共享公司名稱，但有不同目標和顧客。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a distinct business undertaking.","zh":"這個短語描述一項獨立的商業行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"give readers an online taste of","meaning":"讓讀者在網上試讀……","examples":[{"en":"The service gives readers an online taste of commercially available books.","zh":"該服務讓讀者在網上試讀市面有售的書籍。"},{"en":"To give readers an online taste of something means to let them preview a small part of it on the internet.","zh":"give readers an online taste of 某物，指讓讀者在互聯網上預覽其中一小部分。"},{"en":"A publisher may give readers an online taste of a novel by showing the first chapter.","zh":"出版商可能透過展示第一章，讓讀者在網上試讀小說。"},{"en":"A preview can tempt readers because they can judge the style before buying.","zh":"預覽可以吸引讀者，因為他們可在購買前判斷風格。"},{"en":"The phrase describes offering a sample to create interest.","zh":"這個短語描述提供樣本以引起興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"commercially available","meaning":"市面有售的","examples":[{"en":"The publisher project featured books that were commercially available.","zh":"出版商項目展示市面有售的書籍。"},{"en":"Commercially available means being sold to the public through normal markets or shops.","zh":"commercially available 指透過普通市場或商店向公眾銷售。"},{"en":"A textbook is commercially available if students can buy it from a bookshop or online store.","zh":"如果學生能在書店或網店買到某教科書，它就是市面有售的。"},{"en":"Commercial availability matters because readers can purchase the full product after sampling it.","zh":"市面有售很重要，因為讀者試讀後可以購買完整產品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that can be bought by ordinary customers.","zh":"這個短語描述普通顧客能買到的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"searchable collection","meaning":"可供搜尋的資料庫","examples":[{"en":"The website contained a searchable collection of book extracts.","zh":"該網站包含一個可供搜尋的書籍摘錄資料庫。"},{"en":"A searchable collection is a set of materials that users can search by typing words or terms.","zh":"searchable collection 是使用者可透過輸入字詞或術語來搜尋的一組材料。"},{"en":"A school may create a searchable collection of past exam papers for students.","zh":"學校可能建立可供搜尋的歷屆試卷資料庫供學生使用。"},{"en":"Searchability helps users find relevant information quickly instead of browsing everything manually.","zh":"可搜尋性幫助使用者快速找到相關資訊，而不用手動瀏覽全部內容。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a digital collection designed for easy searching.","zh":"這個短語描述為方便搜尋而設計的數碼收藏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"book information","meaning":"書籍資料","examples":[{"en":"The collection included extracts and detailed book information.","zh":"該收藏包括摘錄和詳細書籍資料。"},{"en":"Book information means details about a book, such as title, author, publisher, price, summary, and edition.","zh":"book information 指關於一本書的詳情，例如書名、作者、出版社、價格、摘要和版本。"},{"en":"A library catalogue gives book information so readers can decide whether a book is useful.","zh":"圖書館目錄提供書籍資料，讓讀者決定某書是否有用。"},{"en":"Good book information can help customers find, compare, and buy books more easily.","zh":"良好書籍資料可以幫助顧客更容易尋找、比較和購買書籍。"},{"en":"The phrase describes supporting details about a book.","zh":"這個短語描述關於一本書的輔助詳情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be intended to tempt someone to","meaning":"旨在吸引某人去……","examples":[{"en":"The samples were intended to tempt readers to buy complete books.","zh":"這些樣本旨在吸引讀者購買完整書籍。"},{"en":"To be intended to tempt someone to do something means to be designed to attract or persuade them to do it.","zh":"be intended to tempt someone to do something 指被設計來吸引或說服某人去做某事。"},{"en":"Free food samples are intended to tempt shoppers to buy the full product.","zh":"免費食物試食旨在吸引顧客購買完整產品。"},{"en":"A tempting preview can turn curiosity into a purchase.","zh":"吸引人的預覽可以把好奇心轉化為購買。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a planned attempt to attract someone’s interest.","zh":"這個短語描述有計劃地吸引某人興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"complete book","meaning":"完整書籍","examples":[{"en":"Readers could purchase the complete book after viewing an extract.","zh":"讀者看過摘錄後可以購買完整書籍。"},{"en":"A complete book is the full book, not just a sample, extract, chapter, or preview.","zh":"complete book 是整本書，而不是樣本、摘錄、章節或預覽。"},{"en":"A student may read one chapter online and then buy the complete book for class.","zh":"學生可能先在網上閱讀一章，然後為課堂購買完整書籍。"},{"en":"Samples are useful because they help readers decide whether the complete book is worth buying.","zh":"樣本很有用，因為它們幫助讀者決定完整書籍是否值得購買。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts the full work with partial access.","zh":"這個短語把完整作品與部分查閱作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in print form","meaning":"以紙本形式","examples":[{"en":"Customers could buy the title online or in print form.","zh":"顧客可以在網上購買該書，或以紙本形式購買。"},{"en":"In print form means as a physical printed copy rather than a digital file.","zh":"in print form 指以實體印刷副本形式，而不是數碼檔案。"},{"en":"Some students prefer novels in print form because they can write notes in the margins.","zh":"有些學生較喜歡紙本形式的小說，因為可以在頁邊寫筆記。"},{"en":"Print form may feel more comfortable for long reading than a screen.","zh":"對長時間閱讀而言，紙本形式可能比屏幕更舒適。"},{"en":"The phrase describes paper-based publication.","zh":"這個短語描述以紙張為基礎的出版形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not to be outdone","meaning":"不甘示弱","examples":[{"en":"Not to be outdone, Amazon announced its own digital-book services.","zh":"不甘示弱，Amazon 公布了自己的數碼書籍服務。"},{"en":"Not to be outdone means not wanting to let another person or company appear more successful or active.","zh":"not to be outdone 指不想讓另一人或公司顯得更成功或更積極。"},{"en":"Not to be outdone by her classmates, a student improved her presentation with clearer pictures.","zh":"不甘示弱於同學，學生用更清楚的圖片改善自己的匯報。"},{"en":"Competition can push organisations to act quickly when rivals make bold moves.","zh":"當競爭對手作出大膽行動，競爭可以推動機構迅速行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a response driven by rivalry or pride.","zh":"這個短語描述由競爭或自尊推動的回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"online retailer","meaning":"網上零售商","examples":[{"en":"Amazon began as an online retailer specialising in books.","zh":"Amazon 最初是一間專門售賣書籍的網上零售商。"},{"en":"An online retailer is a business that sells goods or services through the internet.","zh":"online retailer 是透過互聯網銷售貨品或服務的商戶。"},{"en":"An online retailer may deliver groceries, clothes, books, or electronics to customers’ homes.","zh":"網上零售商可能把雜貨、衣服、書籍或電子產品送到顧客家中。"},{"en":"Online retailers can grow quickly because customers can shop without visiting physical stores.","zh":"網上零售商可以迅速增長，因為顧客不必到實體店購物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a seller operating mainly through the web.","zh":"這個短語描述主要透過網絡營運的賣家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"unveil plans for","meaning":"公布……的計劃","examples":[{"en":"The company unveiled plans for its own e-book platform.","zh":"該公司公布了自己電子書平台的計劃。"},{"en":"To unveil plans for something means to announce or reveal a planned project publicly.","zh":"unveil plans for 某事，指公開宣布或揭示一個計劃項目。"},{"en":"A school may unveil plans for a new library during a parent meeting.","zh":"學校可能在家長會上公布新圖書館計劃。"},{"en":"Companies unveil plans to attract attention, investors, customers, or partners.","zh":"公司公布計劃是為了吸引注意、投資者、顧客或合作夥伴。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making future plans known.","zh":"這個短語描述公開未來計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a foray into","meaning":"首次進軍……","examples":[{"en":"The new services marked Amazon’s foray into the mass e-book market.","zh":"這些新服務標誌着 Amazon 首次進軍大眾電子書市場。"},{"en":"A foray into something is a first attempt to enter a new activity, market, or field.","zh":"foray into 某事，是首次嘗試進入一項新活動、市場或領域。"},{"en":"A café’s foray into online delivery may begin with a small menu on an app.","zh":"咖啡店首次進軍網上外送，可能先在應用程式上推出小型餐牌。"},{"en":"A foray can be risky because the company may not yet understand the new field fully.","zh":"首次進軍可能有風險，因為公司未必完全理解新領域。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an initial move into new territory.","zh":"這個短語描述進入新領域的初步行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"mass e-book market","meaning":"大眾電子書市場","examples":[{"en":"Several technology firms hoped to dominate the mass e-book market.","zh":"幾間科技公司希望主導大眾電子書市場。"},{"en":"The mass e-book market is the large consumer market for electronic books aimed at ordinary readers.","zh":"mass e-book market 是面向普通讀者的大型電子書消費市場。"},{"en":"A cheap reading app may help the mass e-book market grow among students and commuters.","zh":"廉價閱讀應用程式可能幫助大眾電子書市場在學生和通勤者之間增長。"},{"en":"A mass market expands when technology becomes easy, affordable, and attractive to many people.","zh":"當科技變得簡單、便宜且吸引許多人，大眾市場就會擴大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes e-books as a mainstream consumer business.","zh":"這個短語把電子書描述為主流消費業務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"begin as","meaning":"最初是……","examples":[{"en":"Amazon began as an online book retailer.","zh":"Amazon 最初是一間網上書籍零售商。"},{"en":"To begin as something means to start in a particular form, role, or business area.","zh":"begin as 某物，指以某種形式、角色或業務範疇開始。"},{"en":"A small bakery may begin as a family kitchen business before opening shops.","zh":"小麵包店最初可能是家庭廚房生意，之後才開店。"},{"en":"Companies can begin as one thing and later expand into many other fields.","zh":"公司可以最初是一種業務，後來擴展到許多其他領域。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an original starting identity.","zh":"這個短語描述原本的起始身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a vast array of goods","meaning":"種類繁多的商品","examples":[{"en":"The retailer now sells a vast array of goods.","zh":"該零售商現在銷售種類繁多的商品。"},{"en":"A vast array of goods means a very large and varied selection of products.","zh":"vast array of goods 指非常龐大而多樣的產品選擇。"},{"en":"A department store may sell a vast array of goods, from socks to washing machines.","zh":"百貨公司可能銷售種類繁多的商品，由襪子到洗衣機都有。"},{"en":"Offering many products can attract more customers but also makes management more complex.","zh":"提供許多產品可以吸引更多顧客，但也令管理更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase describes great variety in what is sold.","zh":"這個短語描述所售商品種類非常多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be piqued that","meaning":"因……感到不悅","examples":[{"en":"Amazon may have been piqued that Google was entering its traditional market.","zh":"Amazon 可能因 Google 進入其傳統市場而感到不悅。"},{"en":"To be piqued that something happened means to feel slightly annoyed or offended by it.","zh":"be piqued that 某事發生，指因它而感到稍微惱怒或被冒犯。"},{"en":"A student may be piqued that a classmate copied her idea and received praise.","zh":"學生可能因同學抄襲她的想法並受到讚賞而感到不悅。"},{"en":"Companies may feel piqued when a rival moves into an area they consider theirs.","zh":"當競爭者進入公司認為屬於自己的領域，公司可能感到不悅。"},{"en":"The phrase describes irritation caused by someone else’s action.","zh":"這個短語描述由他人行動引起的不滿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"relative newcomer","meaning":"相對較新的參與者","examples":[{"en":"Google was a relative newcomer to online book retailing.","zh":"Google 是網上書籍零售中相對較新的參與者。"},{"en":"A relative newcomer is someone or something that has joined a field more recently than others.","zh":"relative newcomer 是比其他人較近期才加入某領域的人或事物。"},{"en":"A new café may be a relative newcomer in a street full of old family restaurants.","zh":"在滿是老字號家庭餐廳的街道上，新咖啡店可能是相對較新的參與者。"},{"en":"Newcomers may bring fresh ideas, but established players may see them as threats.","zh":"新加入者可能帶來新想法，但既有參與者可能把他們視為威脅。"},{"en":"The phrase describes someone new compared with longer-standing participants.","zh":"這個短語描述相對於長期參與者而言較新的角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"impinge upon","meaning":"侵犯；涉足……","examples":[{"en":"Amazon did not want another company to impinge upon its core business.","zh":"Amazon 不希望另一間公司涉足其核心業務。"},{"en":"To impinge upon something means to affect, intrude into, or interfere with it.","zh":"impinge upon 某事，指影響、侵入或干擾它。"},{"en":"A noisy renovation may impinge upon students’ ability to study at home.","zh":"嘈吵裝修可能影響學生在家溫習的能力。"},{"en":"Businesses worry when rivals impinge upon their strongest market area.","zh":"當競爭對手涉足其最強市場領域，企業會感到擔心。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests unwanted pressure or intrusion.","zh":"這個短語常暗示不受歡迎的壓力或侵入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"central territory","meaning":"核心業務領域","examples":[{"en":"Online book sales were part of Amazon’s central territory.","zh":"網上書籍銷售是 Amazon 核心業務領域的一部分。"},{"en":"Central territory means the main area of activity, strength, or control for a person or company.","zh":"central territory 指一個人或公司主要活動、優勢或控制的範圍。"},{"en":"For a language school, exam preparation may be its central territory.","zh":"對語言學校來說，考試準備可能是其核心業務領域。"},{"en":"A company protects its central territory because losing it can weaken the whole business.","zh":"公司會保護核心業務領域，因為失去它可能削弱整個業務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a core area someone strongly identifies with or controls.","zh":"這個短語描述某人強烈認同或控制的核心範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"introduce a new service","meaning":"推出新服務","examples":[{"en":"Amazon announced that it would introduce two new services.","zh":"Amazon 宣布將推出兩項新服務。"},{"en":"To introduce a new service means to start offering a new useful function or business activity to customers.","zh":"introduce a new service 指開始向顧客提供新的有用功能或業務活動。"},{"en":"A bank may introduce a new service that lets customers open accounts through a phone app.","zh":"銀行可能推出一項新服務，讓顧客透過手機應用程式開戶。"},{"en":"New services can attract users if they solve a practical problem.","zh":"如果新服務解決實際問題，就能吸引使用者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes launching something customers can use.","zh":"這個短語描述推出顧客可使用的新東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"search for key terms","meaning":"搜尋關鍵字詞","examples":[{"en":"Customers would be able to search for key terms within selected books.","zh":"顧客將能在指定書籍內搜尋關鍵字詞。"},{"en":"To search for key terms means to look for important words or phrases in a text or database.","zh":"search for key terms 指在文本或資料庫中尋找重要字詞或短語。"},{"en":"A student may search for key terms such as “copyright” or “e-book” in a long article.","zh":"學生可能在長文章中搜尋 “copyright” 或 “e-book” 等關鍵字詞。"},{"en":"Searching key terms helps readers find relevant sections quickly.","zh":"搜尋關鍵字詞幫助讀者快速找到相關部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes targeted searching by important vocabulary.","zh":"這個短語描述按重要詞彙作目標搜尋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"selected books","meaning":"指定書籍","examples":[{"en":"The new search function applied only to selected books.","zh":"新搜尋功能只適用於指定書籍。"},{"en":"Selected books are books chosen from a larger collection for a particular service or purpose.","zh":"selected books 是從較大收藏中為某服務或目的挑選出來的書籍。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students selected books for a holiday reading list.","zh":"老師可能給學生指定書籍作假期閱讀清單。"},{"en":"A service may limit access to selected books because of cost, copyright, or publisher agreements.","zh":"服務可能因成本、版權或出版商協議而限制只可查閱指定書籍。"},{"en":"The phrase describes books chosen rather than all books available.","zh":"這個短語描述被挑選的書籍，而不是所有可用書籍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"buy individual pages","meaning":"購買個別頁面","examples":[{"en":"Customers could buy individual pages rather than the entire book.","zh":"顧客可以購買個別頁面，而不是整本書。"},{"en":"To buy individual pages means to purchase only specific pages instead of a whole book.","zh":"buy individual pages 指只購買特定頁面，而不是整本書。"},{"en":"A student may want to buy individual pages of a manual if only one diagram is needed.","zh":"如果學生只需要一幅圖表，可能想購買手冊的個別頁面。"},{"en":"Page-by-page purchasing can reduce cost but may not suit readers who need the whole argument.","zh":"按頁購買可以降低成本，但未必適合需要完整論述的讀者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes buying small parts of a text.","zh":"這個短語描述購買文本的小部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"complete works","meaning":"完整作品","examples":[{"en":"The service allowed purchases ranging from single pages to complete works.","zh":"該服務容許購買由單頁到完整作品不等的內容。"},{"en":"Complete works are full books, texts, or creations rather than selected parts.","zh":"complete works 是完整書籍、文本或創作，而不是選取部分。"},{"en":"A literature student may need the complete works of a poet for detailed study.","zh":"文學學生可能需要某位詩人的完整作品作詳細研究。"},{"en":"Complete works give readers full context that extracts cannot provide.","zh":"完整作品給讀者摘錄無法提供的完整語境。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts whole texts with fragments or samples.","zh":"這個短語把完整文本與片段或樣本作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"online access to","meaning":"網上查閱……的權限","examples":[{"en":"Amazon Upgrade would give customers online access to purchased books.","zh":"Amazon Upgrade 會給顧客網上查閱已購書籍的權限。"},{"en":"Online access to something means the ability to reach, view, or use it through the internet.","zh":"online access to 某物，指能透過互聯網取得、查看或使用它。"},{"en":"Students may receive online access to course notes through a school platform.","zh":"學生可能透過學校平台獲得網上查閱課堂筆記的權限。"},{"en":"Online access is useful when people need information away from the physical copy.","zh":"當人們離開實體副本仍需要資訊時，網上查閱很有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes internet-based availability.","zh":"這個短語描述基於互聯網的可用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hard copy","meaning":"實體書；紙本副本","examples":[{"en":"Customers could access online versions of books already bought as hard copies.","zh":"顧客可以查閱已作為實體書購買的書籍網上版本。"},{"en":"A hard copy is a physical printed version of a document or book.","zh":"hard copy 是文件或書籍的實體印刷版本。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to submit both an online file and a hard copy of an essay.","zh":"老師可能要求學生同時提交作文的網上檔案和紙本副本。"},{"en":"Hard copies are useful when readers want to mark pages or read without a screen.","zh":"當讀者想標記頁面或不看屏幕閱讀時，實體副本很有用。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts physical print with digital versions.","zh":"這個短語把實體印刷本與數碼版本作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be likely to have to pay","meaning":"很可能需要付款","examples":[{"en":"Customers were likely to have to pay a small fee per page.","zh":"顧客很可能需要按每頁支付小額費用。"},{"en":"To be likely to have to pay means probably needing to pay in the future.","zh":"be likely to have to pay 指將來很可能需要付款。"},{"en":"Students are likely to have to pay extra if they print colour pages at a copy shop.","zh":"如果學生在影印店列印彩色頁面，很可能需要額外付款。"},{"en":"When a service has costs, users may be asked to pay even a small amount.","zh":"當服務有成本，使用者可能被要求支付即使很小的金額。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a probable payment requirement.","zh":"這個短語描述很可能出現的付款要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"per page","meaning":"每頁","examples":[{"en":"The proposed charge was around five cents per page.","zh":"擬議收費約為每頁五美仙。"},{"en":"Per page means for each individual page.","zh":"per page 指每一個單獨頁面。"},{"en":"A copy shop may charge two dollars per page for colour printing.","zh":"影印店彩色列印可能每頁收兩元。"},{"en":"Per-page pricing lets customers pay according to how much material they use.","zh":"按頁收費讓顧客根據自己使用多少材料付款。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a cost calculated page by page.","zh":"這個短語描述逐頁計算的費用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the bulk of","meaning":"大部分","examples":[{"en":"The bulk of the payment would go to the publisher.","zh":"大部分付款會給予出版商。"},{"en":"The bulk of something means the largest part or majority of it.","zh":"bulk of 某物，指其中最大部分或大多數。"},{"en":"The bulk of a student’s revision time may be spent on the weakest subject.","zh":"學生的大部分溫習時間可能花在最弱的科目上。"},{"en":"If the bulk of income goes to rent, a family has little money left for savings.","zh":"如果收入大部分用於租金，家庭剩下可儲蓄的錢就很少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the main portion of a whole amount.","zh":"這個短語描述整體數量中的主要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"join the bandwagon","meaning":"跟隨這股熱潮","examples":[{"en":"Microsoft also joined the online-book bandwagon.","zh":"Microsoft 也跟隨了網上書籍這股熱潮。"},{"en":"To join the bandwagon means to start doing something because it has become popular or fashionable.","zh":"join the bandwagon 指因某事變得受歡迎或時興而開始跟着做。"},{"en":"Many shops joined the bubble-tea bandwagon when young customers began buying it every day.","zh":"當年輕顧客每天買珍珠奶茶，許多商店也跟隨這股熱潮。"},{"en":"Companies may join a bandwagon to avoid being left behind by competitors.","zh":"公司可能跟隨熱潮，以免被競爭對手拋離。"},{"en":"The phrase can suggest following a trend rather than starting it.","zh":"這個短語可暗示跟隨趨勢，而不是開創趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"software giant","meaning":"軟件巨擘","examples":[{"en":"The software giant planned to spend heavily on digitisation.","zh":"這間軟件巨擘計劃在數碼化上大花金錢。"},{"en":"A software giant is a very large and powerful company that makes or sells software.","zh":"software giant 是製作或銷售軟件的非常大型且有影響力的公司。"},{"en":"A software giant may develop operating systems, office tools, games, and cloud services.","zh":"軟件巨擘可能開發操作系統、辦公工具、遊戲和雲端服務。"},{"en":"When a software giant enters a market, smaller firms may feel pressure to compete.","zh":"當軟件巨擘進入某市場，較小公司可能感到競爭壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a dominant company in the software industry.","zh":"這個短語描述軟件業中的主導公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"spend money to digitise","meaning":"花錢把……數碼化","examples":[{"en":"Microsoft said it would spend around $200 million to digitise texts.","zh":"Microsoft 表示會花約二億美元把文本數碼化。"},{"en":"To spend money to digitise something means to use funds to convert physical materials into digital form.","zh":"spend money to digitise 某物，指使用資金把實體材料轉換成數碼形式。"},{"en":"A university may spend money to digitise old exam papers so students can search them online.","zh":"大學可能花錢把舊試卷數碼化，讓學生在網上搜尋。"},{"en":"Digitisation costs money because scanning, checking, storing, and indexing materials take labour and technology.","zh":"數碼化需要成本，因為掃描、檢查、儲存和索引材料都需要人力和科技。"},{"en":"The phrase describes funding the conversion of physical texts into digital files.","zh":"這個短語描述資助把實體文本轉成數碼檔案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"public domain","meaning":"公有領域","examples":[{"en":"The company began with texts in the public domain.","zh":"該公司先從公有領域中的文本開始。"},{"en":"The public domain is the category of works not protected by copyright and available for public use.","zh":"public domain 是不受版權保護、可供公眾使用的作品類別。"},{"en":"Old poems may enter the public domain after copyright has expired.","zh":"舊詩在版權到期後可能進入公有領域。"},{"en":"Public-domain texts are easier to digitise because companies do not need permission from copyright owners.","zh":"公有領域文本較容易數碼化，因為公司不需要版權持有人許可。"},{"en":"The phrase describes material that the public can use freely under copyright law.","zh":"這個短語描述在版權法下公眾可自由使用的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"avoid legal problems","meaning":"避免法律問題","examples":[{"en":"Microsoft selected copyright-free works to avoid legal problems.","zh":"Microsoft 選擇無版權作品，以避免法律問題。"},{"en":"To avoid legal problems means to act in a way that prevents disputes, lawsuits, or law-breaking.","zh":"avoid legal problems 指以某種方式行事，防止爭議、訴訟或違法。"},{"en":"A school can avoid legal problems by asking permission before using copyrighted photos.","zh":"學校可在使用受版權保護照片前先取得許可，以避免法律問題。"},{"en":"Careful planning reduces risk because unclear rights can lead to court action.","zh":"仔細規劃能降低風險，因為權利不清可能導致法律行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preventing trouble with the law.","zh":"這個短語描述防止法律上的麻煩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in collaboration with","meaning":"與……合作","examples":[{"en":"The project was developed in collaboration with the Open Content Alliance.","zh":"該項目與 Open Content Alliance 合作開發。"},{"en":"In collaboration with means working together with another person, group, or organisation.","zh":"in collaboration with 指與另一個人、群體或機構共同工作。"},{"en":"A school may create a reading programme in collaboration with a public library.","zh":"學校可能與公共圖書館合作建立閱讀計劃。"},{"en":"Collaboration allows each partner to contribute different resources or skills.","zh":"合作讓每個夥伴貢獻不同資源或技能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes joint effort with a named partner.","zh":"這個短語描述與指定夥伴共同努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a consortium of","meaning":"由……組成的聯盟","examples":[{"en":"The alliance was a consortium of libraries and universities.","zh":"該聯盟是由圖書館和大學組成的聯盟。"},{"en":"A consortium of organisations is a group that works together for a shared project or purpose.","zh":"consortium of 機構，是為共同項目或目的而合作的組織群體。"},{"en":"Several schools may form a consortium to buy educational software at a lower price.","zh":"幾間學校可能組成聯盟，以較低價格購買教育軟件。"},{"en":"A consortium can handle large projects because costs and expertise are shared.","zh":"聯盟能處理大型項目，因為成本和專業知識由成員分擔。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a formal group of cooperating organisations.","zh":"這個短語描述正式合作的組織群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"libraries and universities","meaning":"圖書館及大學","examples":[{"en":"Libraries and universities worked together on the digitisation project.","zh":"圖書館及大學在數碼化項目上共同合作。"},{"en":"Libraries and universities are institutions that store knowledge, support research, and provide learning resources.","zh":"libraries and universities 是收藏知識、支援研究並提供學習資源的機構。"},{"en":"A university may rely on libraries to give students access to journals and rare books.","zh":"大學可能依賴圖書館讓學生查閱期刊和珍本書。"},{"en":"When libraries and universities cooperate, they can preserve and share academic materials more widely.","zh":"當圖書館及大學合作，它們可以更廣泛地保存和分享學術材料。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to two major knowledge institutions.","zh":"這個短語指兩類主要知識機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pledge to","meaning":"承諾……","examples":[{"en":"Yahoo! pledged to make thousands of books available online.","zh":"Yahoo! 承諾在網上提供數以千計的書籍。"},{"en":"To pledge to do something means to make a serious public promise to do it.","zh":"pledge to do something 指作出嚴肅公開承諾去做某事。"},{"en":"A company may pledge to reduce plastic waste by half within five years.","zh":"公司可能承諾在五年內把塑膠廢物減半。"},{"en":"A pledge creates expectations because people can later judge whether the promise was kept.","zh":"承諾會產生期望，因為人們日後可判斷承諾是否兌現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a formal commitment.","zh":"這個短語描述正式承諾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in conjunction with","meaning":"聯同……","examples":[{"en":"Yahoo! worked in conjunction with the same organisation.","zh":"Yahoo! 聯同同一機構合作。"},{"en":"In conjunction with means together with or in cooperation with another person or organisation.","zh":"in conjunction with 指與另一人或機構一起或合作。"},{"en":"A hospital may run a health campaign in conjunction with local schools.","zh":"醫院可能聯同本地學校推行健康宣傳。"},{"en":"Working in conjunction with others can make a project larger and more credible.","zh":"聯同他人工作可以令項目更大、更可信。"},{"en":"The phrase describes coordinated work between partners.","zh":"這個短語描述夥伴之間的協調工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"coincidentally","meaning":"巧合地","examples":[{"en":"Coincidentally, several companies made announcements on the same day.","zh":"巧合地，幾間公司在同一天作出公布。"},{"en":"Coincidentally means by chance, not because something was planned together.","zh":"coincidentally 指出於偶然，而不是因共同計劃。"},{"en":"Coincidentally, two classmates wore the same colour on presentation day.","zh":"巧合地，兩位同學在匯報當天穿了同一種顏色。"},{"en":"Coincidences can look meaningful even when there is no direct connection.","zh":"巧合即使沒有直接聯繫，也可能看似有意義。"},{"en":"The word signals that timing or similarity happened unexpectedly.","zh":"這個詞表示時間或相似性意外地同時出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"announce an initiative","meaning":"公布一項計劃","examples":[{"en":"Google and Amazon announced new initiatives on the same Thursday.","zh":"Google 和 Amazon 在同一個星期四公布新計劃。"},{"en":"To announce an initiative means to publicly reveal a new plan or project.","zh":"announce an initiative 指公開揭示一項新計劃或項目。"},{"en":"A school may announce an initiative to provide free breakfast for students.","zh":"學校可能公布一項計劃，為學生提供免費早餐。"},{"en":"Public announcements help people understand what an organisation plans to do next.","zh":"公開公布幫助人們理解機構接下來打算做甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a new project known.","zh":"這個短語描述公開一項新項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"release details of","meaning":"公布……的詳情","examples":[{"en":"Microsoft released details of a deal with the British Library.","zh":"Microsoft 公布了與英國圖書館協議的詳情。"},{"en":"To release details of something means to make information about it publicly available.","zh":"release details of 某事，指公開關於它的資訊。"},{"en":"A school may release details of a new timetable before the term begins.","zh":"學校可能在學期開始前公布新時間表詳情。"},{"en":"Releasing details helps people know the cost, timing, partners, and purpose of a plan.","zh":"公布詳情幫助人知道計劃的成本、時間、夥伴和目的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes publicly sharing specific information.","zh":"這個短語描述公開分享具體資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sign a deal with","meaning":"與……簽訂協議","examples":[{"en":"The company signed a deal with the British Library.","zh":"該公司與英國圖書館簽訂協議。"},{"en":"To sign a deal with someone means to formally agree to a business arrangement with them.","zh":"sign a deal with 某人，指與他們正式同意一項商業安排。"},{"en":"A school may sign a deal with a bus company to provide student transport.","zh":"學校可能與巴士公司簽訂協議，提供學生交通服務。"},{"en":"Signed deals usually set out responsibilities, costs, and expected results.","zh":"已簽署協議通常列明責任、成本和預期結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making an agreement official.","zh":"這個短語描述令協議正式化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"main reference library","meaning":"主要參考圖書館","examples":[{"en":"The British Library is the country’s main reference library.","zh":"英國圖書館是該國的主要參考圖書館。"},{"en":"A main reference library is a major library used for research, consultation, and access to important materials.","zh":"main reference library 是用於研究、查閱和取得重要材料的大型圖書館。"},{"en":"Students may use a reference library to check old newspapers, maps, and specialist books.","zh":"學生可能使用參考圖書館查閱舊報紙、地圖和專門書籍。"},{"en":"Reference libraries are important because they preserve materials that ordinary bookshops may not sell.","zh":"參考圖書館很重要，因為它們保存普通書店未必出售的材料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a central library for research and information.","zh":"這個短語描述研究和資訊的中央圖書館。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be made available through","meaning":"透過……提供","examples":[{"en":"The digitised pages would be made available through MSN Book Search.","zh":"數碼化頁面將透過 MSN Book Search 提供。"},{"en":"To be made available through a service means to be provided or accessed by using that service.","zh":"be made available through 某服務，指透過使用該服務來提供或取得某物。"},{"en":"Class notes may be made available through the school’s online platform.","zh":"課堂筆記可能透過學校網上平台提供。"},{"en":"The platform matters because it controls how users find and use the material.","zh":"平台很重要，因為它控制使用者如何尋找和使用材料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the channel through which access is provided.","zh":"這個短語描述提供查閱的渠道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be launched","meaning":"被推出","examples":[{"en":"The new search service was expected to be launched the following year.","zh":"這項新搜尋服務預期於翌年推出。"},{"en":"To be launched means to be officially started, introduced, or made available to the public.","zh":"be launched 指被正式開始、推出或向公眾提供。"},{"en":"A school app may be launched at the beginning of the new term.","zh":"學校應用程式可能在新學期開始時推出。"},{"en":"Launching a service usually requires testing, publicity, and user support.","zh":"推出服務通常需要測試、宣傳和使用者支援。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the official beginning of a product or service.","zh":"這個短語描述產品或服務的正式開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hope for a return to","meaning":"希望回復到……","examples":[{"en":"Publishers hoped for a return to the earlier enthusiasm for e-books.","zh":"出版商希望回復到早前對電子書的熱情。"},{"en":"To hope for a return to something means to want a previous situation or feeling to come back.","zh":"hope for a return to 某事，指希望以前的情況或感覺回來。"},{"en":"A shop may hope for a return to busy sales after renovations finish.","zh":"店舖可能在裝修完成後，希望回復到繁忙銷售情況。"},{"en":"People hope for a return to earlier success when later results have become weaker.","zh":"當後來結果變弱，人們會希望回到早前的成功。"},{"en":"The phrase describes wanting a past positive condition to reappear.","zh":"這個短語描述希望過去的正面狀態重新出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"levels of interest","meaning":"關注程度；興趣水平","examples":[{"en":"The companies hoped to revive previous levels of interest in electronic books.","zh":"這些公司希望重新激起以往對電子書的興趣水平。"},{"en":"Levels of interest means the amount or degree of attention, curiosity, or enthusiasm people show.","zh":"levels of interest 指人們表現出的注意、好奇或熱情程度。"},{"en":"A teacher may measure students’ levels of interest by asking how many choose a book voluntarily.","zh":"老師可能透過詢問有多少學生自願選書，量度學生興趣水平。"},{"en":"Interest levels rise when people see clear benefits or exciting new features.","zh":"當人們看見明確好處或令人興奮的新功能，興趣水平會上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how strongly people care about a topic.","zh":"這個短語描述人們對某主題有多關心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"best-selling author","meaning":"暢銷作家","examples":[{"en":"Stephen King was already a best-selling author when he experimented with online publishing.","zh":"Stephen King 嘗試網上出版時，已經是暢銷作家。"},{"en":"A best-selling author is a writer whose books sell in very large numbers.","zh":"best-selling author 是書籍銷量非常大的作家。"},{"en":"A best-selling author can attract readers even when trying a new publishing format.","zh":"暢銷作家即使嘗試新出版形式，也能吸引讀者。"},{"en":"Strong name recognition can make a new book launch more successful.","zh":"強大的知名度可以令新書發布更成功。"},{"en":"The phrase describes commercial success in book sales.","zh":"這個短語描述書籍銷售上的商業成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"horror writer","meaning":"恐怖小說作家","examples":[{"en":"The horror writer released a story exclusively online.","zh":"這位恐怖小說作家只在網上發布一個故事。"},{"en":"A horror writer is an author who writes frightening stories about fear, danger, monsters, death, or suspense.","zh":"horror writer 是寫關於恐懼、危險、怪物、死亡或懸疑等驚悚故事的作家。"},{"en":"A horror writer may use dark settings and sudden surprises to make readers nervous.","zh":"恐怖小說作家可能使用陰暗場景和突如其來的驚嚇令讀者緊張。"},{"en":"Horror writing attracts readers who enjoy being scared in a safe way.","zh":"恐怖寫作吸引那些喜歡在安全方式下受驚的讀者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a writer specialising in scary fiction.","zh":"這個短語描述專門寫驚悚小說的作家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"publish exclusively online","meaning":"只在網上出版","examples":[{"en":"Stephen King published “Riding the Bullet” exclusively online.","zh":"Stephen King 只在網上出版《Riding the Bullet》。"},{"en":"To publish exclusively online means to release a work only on the internet, not in print or other formats at first.","zh":"publish exclusively online 指只在互聯網上發布作品，起初不以紙本或其他形式推出。"},{"en":"A magazine may publish an interview exclusively online to attract website visitors.","zh":"雜誌可能只在網上發布訪問，以吸引網站訪客。"},{"en":"Online-only publication can test whether readers are willing to use digital formats.","zh":"只在網上出版可以測試讀者是否願意使用數碼形式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limiting publication to the web.","zh":"這個短語描述把出版限制於網絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be downloaded","meaning":"被下載","examples":[{"en":"Half a million copies were downloaded within two days.","zh":"五十萬份副本在兩天內被下載。"},{"en":"To be downloaded means to be copied from the internet onto a device.","zh":"be downloaded 指從互聯網複製到裝置上。"},{"en":"A homework file can be downloaded from the school platform before a lesson.","zh":"功課檔案可以在上課前從學校平台下載。"},{"en":"High download numbers can show strong public interest in digital content.","zh":"高下載數字可以顯示公眾對數碼內容有強烈興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes digital material being received by users.","zh":"這個短語描述數碼材料被使用者接收。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"within the first 48 hours","meaning":"在最初四十八小時內","examples":[{"en":"The story was downloaded extensively within the first 48 hours.","zh":"該故事在最初四十八小時內被大量下載。"},{"en":"Within the first 48 hours means during the first two days after something begins or is released.","zh":"within the first 48 hours 指某事開始或發布後的最初兩天內。"},{"en":"A new app may receive thousands of users within the first 48 hours after launch.","zh":"新應用程式推出後，可能在最初四十八小時內獲得數以千計使用者。"},{"en":"Early activity can show whether a release has captured public attention.","zh":"早期活動可以顯示某次發布是否抓住公眾注意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a very early time period after an event.","zh":"這個短語描述事件發生後非常早的一段時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"prove to be","meaning":"證明是……","examples":[{"en":"The early success proved to be an exceptional peak.","zh":"早期成功最終證明是一個特殊高峰。"},{"en":"To prove to be something means to turn out to be that thing after time or evidence reveals the result.","zh":"prove to be 某物，指隨着時間或證據揭示結果，最終顯示為該事物。"},{"en":"A difficult teacher may prove to be helpful when students later see their improvement.","zh":"困難的老師可能在學生後來看到進步時，證明是有幫助的。"},{"en":"First impressions can change because later results show what something truly was.","zh":"第一印象可以改變，因為後來結果會顯示某事真正是甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how something is eventually shown to be.","zh":"這個短語描述某事最終被證明為何物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a high-water mark","meaning":"高峰","examples":[{"en":"The Stephen King release became a high-water mark for early e-books.","zh":"Stephen King 的發布成為早期電子書的一個高峰。"},{"en":"A high-water mark is the highest point or most successful moment reached by something.","zh":"high-water mark 是某事達到的最高點或最成功時刻。"},{"en":"A school’s highest exam result may become a high-water mark for later students to match.","zh":"學校最高考試成績可能成為後來學生追趕的高峰。"},{"en":"A high-water mark can be impressive even if later results fall below it.","zh":"即使後來結果低於它，高峰仍可以令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a peak of achievement or success.","zh":"這個短語描述成就或成功的頂點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a taste of things to come","meaning":"未來趨勢的先兆","examples":[{"en":"The success was not a taste of things to come.","zh":"這次成功並不是未來趨勢的先兆。"},{"en":"A taste of things to come means an early sign of what will happen more often in the future.","zh":"taste of things to come 指未來會更常發生之事的早期跡象。"},{"en":"A small rise in online orders may be a taste of things to come if customers are changing habits.","zh":"如果顧客正在改變習慣，網上訂單小幅上升可能是未來趨勢的先兆。"},{"en":"Sometimes an early success looks like a future trend but later proves temporary.","zh":"有時早期成功看似未來趨勢，但後來證明只是暫時現象。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a preview of future developments.","zh":"這個短語描述未來發展的預覽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be reluctant to","meaning":"不願意……","examples":[{"en":"Many readers were reluctant to read novels from computer screens.","zh":"許多讀者不願意從電腦屏幕閱讀小說。"},{"en":"To be reluctant to do something means to feel unwilling or hesitant to do it.","zh":"be reluctant to do something 指不願意或猶豫去做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be reluctant to speak in front of the class because she fears mistakes.","zh":"學生可能因害怕犯錯而不願意在班上發言。"},{"en":"People are often reluctant when a new method feels uncomfortable or unfamiliar.","zh":"當新方法令人感到不舒服或陌生，人們常會不願意接受。"},{"en":"The phrase describes hesitation or unwillingness.","zh":"這個短語描述猶豫或不情願。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sit in front of a screen","meaning":"坐在屏幕前","examples":[{"en":"Buyers did not want to sit in front of a screen for hours.","zh":"買家不想連續幾小時坐在屏幕前。"},{"en":"To sit in front of a screen means to spend time facing a computer, tablet, phone, or television display.","zh":"sit in front of a screen 指花時間面對電腦、平板、手機或電視顯示器。"},{"en":"After a full day of online lessons, students may not want to sit in front of a screen again.","zh":"一整天網課後，學生可能不想再坐在屏幕前。"},{"en":"Long screen time can make reading feel tiring for some people.","zh":"長時間看屏幕會令某些人覺得閱讀疲累。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physically spending time using a digital display.","zh":"這個短語描述親身花時間使用數碼顯示器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"dedicated e-book reader","meaning":"專用電子書閱讀器","examples":[{"en":"Early dedicated e-book readers failed to attract a large audience.","zh":"早期專用電子書閱讀器未能吸引大量讀者。"},{"en":"A dedicated e-book reader is a device made mainly for reading electronic books.","zh":"dedicated e-book reader 是主要為閱讀電子書而製造的裝置。"},{"en":"A dedicated e-book reader may have a screen designed to feel easier on the eyes than a laptop.","zh":"專用電子書閱讀器可能有比手提電腦更護眼的屏幕。"},{"en":"Such devices succeed only if readers find them convenient, affordable, and comfortable.","zh":"這些裝置只有在讀者覺得方便、便宜和舒適時才會成功。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a specialised gadget for digital reading.","zh":"這個短語描述用於數碼閱讀的專門裝置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fail to catch on","meaning":"未能流行起來","examples":[{"en":"Dedicated reading gadgets failed to catch on with consumers.","zh":"專用閱讀裝置未能在消費者之間流行起來。"},{"en":"To fail to catch on means not to become popular or widely accepted.","zh":"fail to catch on 指沒有變得受歡迎或被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"A school app may fail to catch on if students find it confusing to use.","zh":"如果學生覺得學校應用程式難用，它可能未能流行起來。"},{"en":"New products fail when people do not see enough benefit to change their habits.","zh":"當人們看不到足夠好處去改變習慣，新產品就會失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a trend or product not becoming popular.","zh":"這個短語描述趨勢或產品沒有變得流行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"bookshop chain","meaning":"連鎖書店","examples":[{"en":"Barnes and Noble was a leading American bookshop chain.","zh":"Barnes and Noble 是美國一間領先連鎖書店。"},{"en":"A bookshop chain is a group of bookshops with the same brand and ownership in many locations.","zh":"bookshop chain 是在多個地點以同一品牌和所有權經營的一組書店。"},{"en":"A bookshop chain may sell novels, textbooks, magazines, stationery, and gifts.","zh":"連鎖書店可能售賣小說、教科書、雜誌、文具和禮品。"},{"en":"Large chains can reach many customers but may face pressure from online retailers.","zh":"大型連鎖店可以接觸許多顧客，但也可能面對網上零售商壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a branded network of bookstores.","zh":"這個短語描述書店的品牌網絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"with great fanfare","meaning":"大張旗鼓地","examples":[{"en":"The company began selling e-books with great fanfare.","zh":"該公司大張旗鼓地開始銷售電子書。"},{"en":"With great fanfare means with a lot of publicity, excitement, and attention.","zh":"with great fanfare 指帶着大量宣傳、興奮和關注。"},{"en":"A school may open a new sports centre with great fanfare and invite local reporters.","zh":"學校可能大張旗鼓地開放新體育中心，並邀請本地記者。"},{"en":"Fanfare can create high expectations, but the product still has to succeed in practice.","zh":"大量宣傳可以創造高期望，但產品實際上仍必須成功。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a noisy and highly public launch.","zh":"這個短語描述高調而公開的推出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"quietly pull the plug","meaning":"悄悄終止","examples":[{"en":"Barnes and Noble quietly pulled the plug on its e-book operation.","zh":"Barnes and Noble 悄悄終止其電子書業務。"},{"en":"To quietly pull the plug means to stop a project or service without making much publicity.","zh":"quietly pull the plug 指在沒有太多宣傳下停止某項目或服務。"},{"en":"A company may quietly pull the plug on an app if too few customers use it.","zh":"如果太少顧客使用某應用程式，公司可能悄悄終止它。"},{"en":"Projects are often ended quietly when managers want to avoid embarrassment.","zh":"當管理層想避免尷尬，項目常會被低調結束。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ending something, usually after it fails to grow.","zh":"這個短語描述終止某事，通常因它未能增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"interest fade","meaning":"興趣減退","examples":[{"en":"The company withdrew from the market as consumer interest faded.","zh":"隨着消費者興趣減退，該公司退出市場。"},{"en":"When interest fades, people become less curious, enthusiastic, or willing to spend time or money.","zh":"interest fades 指人們變得較少好奇、熱情或願意花時間和金錢。"},{"en":"Interest in a school club may fade if meetings become repetitive.","zh":"如果會議變得重複，學生對學會的興趣可能減退。"},{"en":"When consumer interest fades, sales usually fall and companies may stop investing.","zh":"當消費者興趣減退，銷售通常下跌，公司可能停止投資。"},{"en":"The phrase describes enthusiasm gradually weakening.","zh":"這個短語描述熱情逐漸減弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"grow from a tiny base","meaning":"從極小的基數增長","examples":[{"en":"The e-book market was growing again, although from a tiny base.","zh":"電子書市場再次增長，雖然是從極小的基數增長。"},{"en":"To grow from a tiny base means to increase from a very small starting point.","zh":"grow from a tiny base 指從非常小的起點增加。"},{"en":"A new tutoring centre may double its students but still grow from a tiny base if it started with only five learners.","zh":"如果補習中心一開始只有五名學生，即使學生人數翻倍，也仍是從極小的基數增長。"},{"en":"Fast growth can look impressive even when the total size remains small.","zh":"快速增長可以看似令人印象深刻，即使總規模仍然很小。"},{"en":"The phrase warns readers to consider the starting number.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者考慮起始數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"digital publishing forum","meaning":"數碼出版論壇","examples":[{"en":"The International Digital Publishing Forum collected industry statistics.","zh":"國際數碼出版論壇收集行業統計數字。"},{"en":"A digital publishing forum is an organisation or platform where people discuss and track electronic publishing.","zh":"digital publishing forum 是讓人討論和追蹤電子出版的機構或平台。"},{"en":"A forum may collect sales figures, set standards, and share industry information.","zh":"論壇可能收集銷售數字、制定標準和分享行業資訊。"},{"en":"Such groups help companies understand whether digital reading is growing.","zh":"這類組織幫助公司了解數碼閱讀是否正在增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a body focused on digital publishing issues.","zh":"這個短語描述專注於數碼出版議題的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"collate figures from","meaning":"彙整來自……的數據","examples":[{"en":"The organisation collated figures from leading publishers.","zh":"該組織彙整來自頂尖出版商的數據。"},{"en":"To collate figures from sources means to collect, organise, and compare numerical information from them.","zh":"collate figures from 來源，指從它們收集、整理和比較數字資訊。"},{"en":"A school may collate figures from different classes to see how many students joined activities.","zh":"學校可能彙整來自不同班級的數據，以了解有多少學生參加活動。"},{"en":"Collating data helps people see patterns that individual numbers may not show clearly.","zh":"彙整數據幫助人看見單個數字未必清楚顯示的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organising statistics from several sources.","zh":"這個短語描述整理來自多個來源的統計數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"top publishers","meaning":"頂尖出版商","examples":[{"en":"Many of the world’s top publishers supplied sales data.","zh":"世界許多頂尖出版商提供銷售數據。"},{"en":"Top publishers are leading companies in the book or publishing industry.","zh":"top publishers 是書籍或出版行業中的領先公司。"},{"en":"A top publisher may release best-selling novels, textbooks, academic titles, and children’s books.","zh":"頂尖出版商可能出版暢銷小說、教科書、學術書籍和兒童書。"},{"en":"Data from top publishers can strongly influence how people understand the market.","zh":"來自頂尖出版商的數據可以強烈影響人們如何理解市場。"},{"en":"The phrase describes major and influential publishing companies.","zh":"這個短語描述主要且有影響力的出版公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the third quarter of","meaning":"……的第三季","examples":[{"en":"Worldwide sales rose during the third quarter of 2004.","zh":"全球銷售額在2004年第三季上升。"},{"en":"The third quarter of a year means the three-month period from July to September.","zh":"third quarter of 一年，指由七月至九月的三個月時期。"},{"en":"A company may review profits in the third quarter of the year before planning Christmas sales.","zh":"公司可能在一年第三季檢視利潤，再規劃聖誕銷售。"},{"en":"Business data are often divided into quarters so changes can be tracked more clearly.","zh":"商業數據常被分成季度，以便更清楚追蹤變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a specific three-month business period.","zh":"這個短語描述特定三個月商業時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be higher than the year before","meaning":"比前一年高","examples":[{"en":"E-book sales were 25% higher than the year before.","zh":"電子書銷售額比前一年高25%。"},{"en":"To be higher than the year before means to be greater compared with the same period in the previous year.","zh":"be higher than the year before 指與前一年同期相比更高。"},{"en":"A school’s library visits may be higher than the year before after a new reading campaign.","zh":"新閱讀活動後，學校圖書館到訪次數可能比前一年高。"},{"en":"Yearly comparison helps people see whether growth is real or temporary.","zh":"年度比較幫助人看出增長是真實還是暫時。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an increase compared with last year.","zh":"這個短語描述與去年相比的增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"amount to","meaning":"合共達到","examples":[{"en":"The higher sales still amounted to only a few million dollars.","zh":"較高的銷售額仍然只合共達到幾百萬美元。"},{"en":"To amount to a number means to add up to that total.","zh":"amount to 某數字，指加起來達到該總數。"},{"en":"A family’s small daily savings may amount to a large sum after a year.","zh":"家庭每天小額儲蓄，一年後可能合共達到一大筆錢。"},{"en":"A number can sound large or small depending on what it is compared with.","zh":"一個數字聽起來大或小，取決於與甚麼比較。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the total value or result.","zh":"這個短語描述總值或總結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a paltry sum","meaning":"微不足道的金額","examples":[{"en":"Worldwide e-book sales amounted to a paltry $3.2 million.","zh":"全球電子書銷售額合共只有微不足道的320萬美元。"},{"en":"A paltry sum is an amount of money considered very small or disappointing.","zh":"paltry sum 是被認為非常少或令人失望的金額。"},{"en":"A school fair that raises only twenty dollars after weeks of work may produce a paltry sum.","zh":"學校嘉年華籌備數星期後只籌到二十元，可能就是微不足道的金額。"},{"en":"A sum can seem paltry when compared with the size of the whole industry.","zh":"當一筆金額與整個行業規模比較，它可能顯得微不足道。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses that the amount is unimpressively small.","zh":"這個短語表達數額小得不令人印象深刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be split between","meaning":"由……瓜分","examples":[{"en":"The revenue was split between twenty-three publishers.","zh":"收入由二十三間出版商瓜分。"},{"en":"To be split between people or groups means to be divided among them.","zh":"be split between 多個人或群體，指在他們之間分配。"},{"en":"A restaurant bill may be split between four friends after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後，餐廳帳單可能由四位朋友分攤。"},{"en":"When revenue is split among many parties, each one may receive only a small share.","zh":"當收入由許多方面瓜分，每一方可能只得到很小份額。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dividing a total amount among several recipients.","zh":"這個短語描述把總額分給幾個接收者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"an industry worth","meaning":"價值……的行業","examples":[{"en":"The total publishing industry was worth more than $100 billion.","zh":"整個出版業是價值超過一千億美元的行業。"},{"en":"An industry worth a certain amount is a business sector with that estimated total value.","zh":"industry worth 某金額，指估計總值達該金額的商業領域。"},{"en":"A tourism industry worth billions can support hotels, restaurants, transport, and local shops.","zh":"價值數十億的旅遊業可以支撐酒店、餐廳、交通和本地商店。"},{"en":"Industry value helps show whether a small market is important or still minor.","zh":"行業價值幫助顯示某小市場是重要還是仍屬次要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the economic size of a sector.","zh":"這個短語描述某行業的經濟規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reckon that","meaning":"認為；估計","examples":[{"en":"Retailers and publishers reckon that online reading will eventually grow.","zh":"零售商和出版商認為網上閱讀最終會增長。"},{"en":"To reckon that means to think, estimate, or believe something is likely.","zh":"reckon that 指認為、估計或相信某事很可能。"},{"en":"A shop owner may reckon that sales will improve once the weather turns cooler.","zh":"店主可能估計天氣轉涼後銷售會改善。"},{"en":"Reckoning is often based on experience, signs, or business judgement rather than certainty.","zh":"估計常基於經驗、跡象或商業判斷，而不是確定事實。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an opinion or estimate.","zh":"這個短語引出意見或估算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"eventually persuade someone to","meaning":"最終說服某人去……","examples":[{"en":"Companies hope eventually to persuade more consumers to read online.","zh":"公司希望最終說服更多消費者在網上閱讀。"},{"en":"To eventually persuade someone to do something means to convince them after time, effort, or repeated attempts.","zh":"eventually persuade someone to do something 指經過時間、努力或反覆嘗試後說服某人做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may eventually persuade a shy student to join the debate team.","zh":"老師可能最終說服害羞學生加入辯論隊。"},{"en":"Persuasion often takes time when people must change habits or beliefs.","zh":"當人們必須改變習慣或信念，說服常需要時間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes successful convincing after a process.","zh":"這個短語描述經過過程後成功說服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"do more reading on the web","meaning":"在網上閱讀更多","examples":[{"en":"Publishers want consumers to do more of their reading on the web.","zh":"出版商希望消費者在網上閱讀更多。"},{"en":"To do more reading on the web means to read more articles, books, or documents through internet platforms.","zh":"do more reading on the web 指透過互聯網平台閱讀更多文章、書籍或文件。"},{"en":"Students may do more reading on the web when teachers upload materials to a learning site.","zh":"當老師把材料上載到學習網站，學生可能在網上閱讀更多。"},{"en":"Web reading can grow if devices become comfortable and content becomes easy to find.","zh":"如果裝置變得舒適，內容變得容易尋找，網上閱讀可以增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shifting reading activity from paper to online sources.","zh":"這個短語描述把閱讀活動由紙本轉向網上來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"become to online books what…is to…","meaning":"成為網上書籍界的……","examples":[{"en":"Some firms hope to become to online books what iTunes is to online music.","zh":"有些公司希望成為網上書籍界的 iTunes，就像 iTunes 之於網上音樂一樣。"},{"en":"Become to A what B is to C means to play the same successful role in one field that another thing plays in another field.","zh":"become to A what B is to C 指在一個領域扮演另一事物在另一領域中的同樣成功角色。"},{"en":"A tutoring app may hope to become to exam practice what YouTube is to online video.","zh":"補習應用程式可能希望成為考試練習界的 YouTube，就像 YouTube 之於網上影片一樣。"},{"en":"The phrase compares ambition by using a famous model from another market.","zh":"這個短語透過另一市場的著名模式來比較野心。"},{"en":"It describes wanting to become the leading platform or symbol in a field.","zh":"它描述希望成為某領域的領先平台或象徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"crucial differences between","meaning":"……之間的關鍵差異","examples":[{"en":"There are crucial differences between downloading music and downloading books.","zh":"下載音樂和下載書籍之間有關鍵差異。"},{"en":"Crucial differences between two things are very important differences that affect the result.","zh":"crucial differences between 兩事物，是會影響結果的非常重要差異。"},{"en":"There are crucial differences between studying alone and studying with feedback from a teacher.","zh":"獨自學習與在老師回饋下學習之間有關鍵差異。"},{"en":"Ignoring crucial differences can lead to poor business decisions.","zh":"忽視關鍵差異可能導致糟糕商業決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes differences that matter, not minor details.","zh":"這個短語描述真正重要的差異，而不是小細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be driven from the bottom up","meaning":"由民間自下而上推動","examples":[{"en":"Online music was initially driven from the bottom up by consumers.","zh":"網上音樂最初由消費者自下而上推動。"},{"en":"To be driven from the bottom up means to be pushed by ordinary users or the public rather than by leaders or large organisations.","zh":"be driven from the bottom up 指由普通使用者或公眾，而不是由領導者或大型機構推動。"},{"en":"A school recycling programme can be driven from the bottom up if students start it before teachers do.","zh":"如果學生比老師更早開始，學校回收計劃就可以由民間自下而上推動。"},{"en":"Bottom-up change can grow quickly because many ordinary people adopt the behaviour first.","zh":"自下而上的改變可以迅速增長，因為許多普通人最先採用該行為。"},{"en":"The phrase describes change led by users or grassroots demand.","zh":"這個短語描述由使用者或基層需求帶動的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"illegal file-sharing services","meaning":"非法檔案分享服務","examples":[{"en":"Illegal file-sharing services helped create demand for digital music.","zh":"非法檔案分享服務幫助創造了對數碼音樂的需求。"},{"en":"Illegal file-sharing services are online systems that let people share copyrighted files without permission.","zh":"illegal file-sharing services 是讓人未經許可分享受版權保護檔案的網上系統。"},{"en":"A student who downloads a paid song from an unauthorised site may be using an illegal file-sharing service.","zh":"學生從未獲授權網站下載付費歌曲，可能就是在使用非法檔案分享服務。"},{"en":"Such services can become popular because they are easy and free, but they break copyright rules.","zh":"這些服務可能因方便和免費而流行，但它們違反版權規則。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unauthorised online sharing platforms.","zh":"這個短語描述未經授權的網上分享平台。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"become wildly popular","meaning":"變得極受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"File-sharing platforms became wildly popular.","zh":"檔案分享平台變得極受歡迎。"},{"en":"To become wildly popular means to become extremely popular very quickly or widely.","zh":"become wildly popular 指非常快速或廣泛地變得極受歡迎。"},{"en":"A short video app may become wildly popular if students share it with friends every day.","zh":"如果學生每天與朋友分享，短片應用程式可能變得極受歡迎。"},{"en":"Wild popularity can attract investors, competitors, and legal attention.","zh":"極受歡迎可以吸引投資者、競爭者和法律關注。"},{"en":"The phrase describes explosive public enthusiasm.","zh":"這個短語描述爆發式的公眾熱情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"legal firms take over","meaning":"合法企業接手","examples":[{"en":"Legal providers later took over much of the online music market.","zh":"合法供應商後來接手了大部分網上音樂市場。"},{"en":"When legal firms take over a market, authorised companies replace illegal or informal providers as the main suppliers.","zh":"legal firms take over 市場，指獲授權公司取代非法或非正式供應商成為主要供應者。"},{"en":"Legal streaming services took over when many users found them safer and more convenient than piracy.","zh":"當許多使用者覺得合法串流服務比盜版更安全和方便時，合法服務就接手市場。"},{"en":"A market can shift when customers are willing to pay for a reliable legal option.","zh":"當顧客願意為可靠合法選項付款，市場就可能轉移。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lawful companies gaining control of a market.","zh":"這個短語描述合法公司取得市場控制權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be forced to retreat","meaning":"被迫退卻","examples":[{"en":"Illegal services were forced to retreat after extensive legal action.","zh":"非法服務在大規模法律行動後被迫退卻。"},{"en":"To be forced to retreat means to have to withdraw, reduce activity, or give up because of pressure.","zh":"be forced to retreat 指因壓力而必須撤回、減少活動或放棄。"},{"en":"A shop may be forced to retreat from a new market if rent and competition become too high.","zh":"如果租金和競爭變得太高，店舖可能被迫退出新市場。"},{"en":"Legal pressure can make illegal businesses stop operating openly.","zh":"法律壓力可以令非法企業停止公開運作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes backing away because continuing has become too difficult.","zh":"這個短語描述因繼續下去太困難而退後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a wave of lawsuits","meaning":"一連串訴訟","examples":[{"en":"A wave of lawsuits weakened illegal file-sharing companies.","zh":"一連串訴訟削弱了非法檔案分享公司。"},{"en":"A wave of lawsuits means many legal cases brought around the same time.","zh":"wave of lawsuits 指大約同一時間提出的許多法律案件。"},{"en":"A wave of lawsuits may follow if many customers are harmed by the same faulty product.","zh":"如果許多顧客被同一有缺陷產品傷害，可能出現一連串訴訟。"},{"en":"Multiple lawsuits can damage a company through legal costs, bad publicity, and forced changes.","zh":"多宗訴訟可以透過法律成本、負面宣傳和被迫改變來損害公司。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large series of legal actions.","zh":"這個短語描述大量連續法律行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"legal providers","meaning":"合法供應商","examples":[{"en":"Legal providers offered consumers a convenient alternative to piracy.","zh":"合法供應商為消費者提供了取代盜版的方便選擇。"},{"en":"Legal providers are authorised companies or services that supply products lawfully.","zh":"legal providers 是合法供應產品的獲授權公司或服務。"},{"en":"A legal music platform lets users pay for songs instead of downloading illegal copies.","zh":"合法音樂平台讓使用者為歌曲付款，而不是下載非法副本。"},{"en":"Legal providers succeed when they are convenient enough to compete with illegal options.","zh":"當合法供應商足夠方便，能與非法選項競爭時，它們就會成功。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lawful suppliers in a market.","zh":"這個短語描述市場中的合法供應者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"pay a small sum for","meaning":"為……支付小額費用","examples":[{"en":"Many consumers were willing to pay a small sum for individual songs.","zh":"許多消費者願意為個別歌曲支付小額費用。"},{"en":"To pay a small sum for something means to spend a little money to get it.","zh":"pay a small sum for 某物，指花少量金錢取得它。"},{"en":"Students may pay a small sum for printing a worksheet at a copy shop.","zh":"學生可能在影印店為列印工作紙支付小額費用。"},{"en":"Small payments feel acceptable when the product is useful, legal, and easy to access.","zh":"當產品有用、合法且容易取得，小額付款會令人較容易接受。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a low-cost purchase.","zh":"這個短語描述低成本購買。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"remain beyond the law","meaning":"繼續違法；逍遙法外","examples":[{"en":"Paying legally was preferable to remaining beyond the law.","zh":"合法付款比繼續違法更可取。"},{"en":"To remain beyond the law means to continue acting outside legal rules or protection.","zh":"remain beyond the law 指繼續在法律規則或保護之外行事。"},{"en":"A business that sells fake products remains beyond the law and risks punishment.","zh":"售賣假貨的商戶繼續違法，並面臨懲罰風險。"},{"en":"Legal services attract users when people want convenience without breaking rules.","zh":"當人們想要方便又不違規，合法服務就能吸引用戶。"},{"en":"The phrase describes staying outside lawful behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述停留在合法行為之外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"prove fashionable and popular","meaning":"證明時尚且受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Portable music players proved fashionable and popular.","zh":"便攜式音樂播放器證明時尚且受歡迎。"},{"en":"To prove fashionable and popular means to turn out to be stylish and widely liked.","zh":"prove fashionable and popular 指結果顯示某物時尚且被廣泛喜愛。"},{"en":"A new school hoodie may prove fashionable and popular if students enjoy wearing it outside school.","zh":"如果學生喜歡在校外穿新校隊連帽衫，它可能證明時尚且受歡迎。"},{"en":"A product grows faster when it is both useful and socially attractive.","zh":"當產品既有用又具社交吸引力，它會增長得更快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something becoming both trendy and widely accepted.","zh":"這個短語描述某物變得時髦且被廣泛接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a new way to","meaning":"……的新方式","examples":[{"en":"The iPod provided a new way to listen to music.","zh":"iPod 提供了一種聽音樂的新方式。"},{"en":"A new way to do something means a different method for doing it.","zh":"new way to do something 指做某事的不同方法。"},{"en":"Online lessons gave students a new way to attend class during school closures.","zh":"在停課期間，網上課堂給學生一種上課的新方式。"},{"en":"New ways become popular when they are easier, cheaper, or more enjoyable than old ones.","zh":"當新方式比舊方式更容易、更便宜或更愉快，它就會流行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a fresh method or approach.","zh":"這個短語描述新的方法或做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have no equivalent","meaning":"沒有對應產品","examples":[{"en":"The book industry had no equivalent of the iPod.","zh":"圖書業沒有 iPod 的對應產品。"},{"en":"To have no equivalent means to have nothing similar in function, influence, or appeal.","zh":"have no equivalent 指沒有在功能、影響力或吸引力上相似的東西。"},{"en":"A small town may have no equivalent of a major city’s underground railway.","zh":"小鎮可能沒有大城市地鐵的對應系統。"},{"en":"Without an equivalent device, online books may struggle to become fashionable.","zh":"沒有對應裝置，網上書籍可能難以變得時尚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the absence of a comparable thing.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏可比較之物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the book world","meaning":"圖書業界","examples":[{"en":"The book world lacked a device with the appeal of the iPod.","zh":"圖書業界缺少一款具有 iPod 吸引力的裝置。"},{"en":"The book world means the industry, culture, and community connected with books, writers, publishers, sellers, and readers.","zh":"book world 指與書籍、作家、出版商、銷售者和讀者有關的行業、文化和社群。"},{"en":"A major prize can influence the book world by making a novel suddenly famous.","zh":"重要獎項可以令小說突然成名，從而影響圖書業界。"},{"en":"The book world changes when technology alters how readers discover and buy texts.","zh":"當科技改變讀者發現和購買文本的方式，圖書業界就會改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the wider ecosystem around books.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞書籍的更廣泛生態系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"commercial prospects","meaning":"商業前景","examples":[{"en":"The commercial prospects for online books remained uncertain.","zh":"網上書籍的商業前景仍不明朗。"},{"en":"Commercial prospects are the chances that a product or business will make money in the future.","zh":"commercial prospects 是產品或業務將來賺錢的可能性。"},{"en":"A new café has better commercial prospects if it is near offices and schools.","zh":"如果新咖啡店靠近辦公室和學校，它的商業前景會較好。"},{"en":"Prospects are uncertain when customers are interested but not yet willing to pay.","zh":"當顧客有興趣但尚未願意付款，前景就不明朗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes future business potential.","zh":"這個短語描述未來商業潛力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"not look very bright","meaning":"看來不太樂觀","examples":[{"en":"The immediate commercial prospects did not look very bright.","zh":"即時商業前景看來不太樂觀。"},{"en":"Not look very bright means not seem hopeful, successful, or promising.","zh":"not look very bright 指看起來不太有希望、不太成功或不太有前途。"},{"en":"A student’s exam prospects may not look very bright if she has missed many lessons.","zh":"如果學生缺了很多課，她的考試前景可能看來不太樂觀。"},{"en":"A situation can look weak when early results are disappointing.","zh":"當早期結果令人失望，情況可能看起來很弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a pessimistic view of likely success.","zh":"這個短語描述對成功可能性的悲觀看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"get a lift from","meaning":"從……得到提振","examples":[{"en":"Online book sales may get a lift from new technology.","zh":"網上書籍銷售可能從新科技得到提振。"},{"en":"To get a lift from something means to receive help, encouragement, or improvement from it.","zh":"get a lift from 某事，指從它獲得幫助、鼓勵或改善。"},{"en":"A local shop may get a lift from a new train station nearby.","zh":"本地商店可能因附近新火車站而得到提振。"},{"en":"New technology can lift sales if it makes buying easier or more enjoyable.","zh":"如果新科技令購買更容易或更愉快，它可以提振銷售。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a boost caused by another factor.","zh":"這個短語描述由另一因素帶來的推動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"novel innovations","meaning":"新穎的創新方法","examples":[{"en":"Sellers hoped that novel innovations would stimulate demand.","zh":"銷售者希望新穎的創新方法能刺激需求。"},{"en":"Novel innovations are new and unusual ideas, tools, or methods.","zh":"novel innovations 是新的而不尋常的想法、工具或方法。"},{"en":"A school may use novel innovations such as interactive quizzes to make revision less boring.","zh":"學校可能使用互動測驗等新穎創新方法，令溫習較不沉悶。"},{"en":"New innovations can attract attention because they solve old problems in fresh ways.","zh":"新創新可以吸引注意，因為它們用新方式解決舊問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fresh inventions or methods with novelty.","zh":"這個短語描述具有新意的新發明或方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"download parts of books","meaning":"下載書籍的部分內容","examples":[{"en":"The ability to download parts of books may attract practical readers.","zh":"下載書籍部分內容的能力可能吸引實用型讀者。"},{"en":"To download parts of books means to obtain only selected pages, chapters, or sections in digital form.","zh":"download parts of books 指只取得書籍中選定頁面、章節或部分的數碼版本。"},{"en":"A student may download parts of books when only one chapter is needed for a project.","zh":"當項目只需要一章，學生可能下載書籍的部分內容。"},{"en":"Partial downloading can save money, storage space, and reading time.","zh":"部分下載可以節省金錢、儲存空間和閱讀時間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes digital access to selected portions rather than whole books.","zh":"這個短語描述取得選定部分，而不是整本書的數碼查閱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"sections of manuals","meaning":"手冊的部分章節","examples":[{"en":"Customers may purchase only the relevant sections of manuals.","zh":"顧客可能只購買手冊的相關部分章節。"},{"en":"Sections of manuals are particular parts or chapters of instruction books.","zh":"sections of manuals 是說明書或指南中的特定部分或章節。"},{"en":"A cyclist may need only the brake-repair section of a bicycle manual.","zh":"踩單車的人可能只需要單車手冊中維修煞車的部分。"},{"en":"Buying sections can be useful when the full manual is long, expensive, or unnecessary.","zh":"當完整手冊很長、昂貴或不必要時，購買部分章節很有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes specific instructional parts of a guidebook.","zh":"這個短語描述指南中的特定說明部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"course textbooks","meaning":"課程教科書","examples":[{"en":"Students may download selected chapters from course textbooks.","zh":"學生可能從課程教科書下載指定章節。"},{"en":"Course textbooks are books assigned for study in a school, college, or university course.","zh":"course textbooks 是學校、學院或大學課程指定研讀的書籍。"},{"en":"A biology course textbook may explain cells, genetics, plants, and evolution.","zh":"生物課程教科書可能解釋細胞、遺傳、植物和演化。"},{"en":"Textbooks can be expensive, so students may prefer access to only the chapters they need.","zh":"教科書可以很昂貴，所以學生可能較喜歡只取得需要的章節。"},{"en":"The phrase describes official learning books used in a course.","zh":"這個短語描述課程中使用的正式學習書籍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"tempt some customers","meaning":"吸引部分顧客","examples":[{"en":"Low-cost extracts may tempt some customers to try online books.","zh":"低成本摘錄可能吸引部分顧客嘗試網上書籍。"},{"en":"To tempt some customers means to attract or persuade some buyers by offering something appealing.","zh":"tempt some customers 指透過提供吸引人的東西來吸引或說服部分買家。"},{"en":"A free trial may tempt some customers to join a streaming service.","zh":"免費試用可能吸引部分顧客加入串流服務。"},{"en":"Customers are more easily tempted when the risk and cost feel low.","zh":"當風險和成本感覺低，顧客較容易被吸引。"},{"en":"The phrase describes drawing people toward a purchase or trial.","zh":"這個短語描述引導人們購買或試用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"relevant sections","meaning":"相關部分；相關章節","examples":[{"en":"Students may need only the relevant sections of a course book.","zh":"學生可能只需要課程書中的相關章節。"},{"en":"Relevant sections are the parts that are directly connected to the user’s need, topic, or question.","zh":"relevant sections 是與使用者需要、主題或問題直接相關的部分。"},{"en":"A student writing about climate change may read only the relevant sections of a geography textbook.","zh":"寫氣候變化的學生可能只閱讀地理教科書中的相關章節。"},{"en":"Choosing relevant sections saves time because readers avoid material they do not need.","zh":"選擇相關部分能節省時間，因為讀者避開不需要的材料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes useful parts selected for a specific purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述為特定目的挑選的有用部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"sample a book","meaning":"試讀一本書","examples":[{"en":"Readers may sample a book before buying the complete edition.","zh":"讀者可能在購買完整版前試讀一本書。"},{"en":"To sample a book means to read a small part of it before deciding whether to buy or continue reading.","zh":"sample a book 指在決定是否購買或繼續閱讀前，先讀其中一小部分。"},{"en":"A reader may sample a book by reading the first chapter in a bookshop.","zh":"讀者可能在書店閱讀第一章來試讀一本書。"},{"en":"Sampling helps customers judge style, difficulty, and interest before spending money.","zh":"試讀幫助顧客在花錢前判斷風格、難度和興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes trying a book briefly before committing to it.","zh":"這個短語描述在投入購買或閱讀前短暫嘗試一本書。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"subsequently buy","meaning":"其後購買","examples":[{"en":"A reader may subsequently buy the book in hard copy.","zh":"讀者其後可能購買該書的實體版。"},{"en":"To subsequently buy something means to purchase it later, after an earlier action or decision.","zh":"subsequently buy 某物，指在較早行動或決定之後再購買它。"},{"en":"A student may borrow a novel from the library and subsequently buy it because she enjoys it.","zh":"學生可能先從圖書館借小說，因為喜歡而其後購買。"},{"en":"A preview can lead to a later purchase if the reader becomes interested.","zh":"如果讀者產生興趣，預覽可以導致後來購買。"},{"en":"The phrase describes buying after something else happens first.","zh":"這個短語描述先有另一件事發生，之後才購買。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"reading matter","meaning":"閱讀材料","examples":[{"en":"Portable devices allow users to download different kinds of reading matter.","zh":"便攜裝置讓使用者下載不同種類的閱讀材料。"},{"en":"Reading matter means written material that people read, such as books, articles, magazines, or documents.","zh":"reading matter 指供人閱讀的文字材料，例如書籍、文章、雜誌或文件。"},{"en":"A student may carry reading matter on a tablet for the train ride home.","zh":"學生可能在平板電腦中攜帶閱讀材料，供回家火車途中閱讀。"},{"en":"Digital devices make reading matter easier to store and move around.","zh":"數碼裝置令閱讀材料更容易儲存和攜帶。"},{"en":"The phrase broadly refers to material intended for reading.","zh":"這個短語廣泛指用作閱讀的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"increasingly ubiquitous","meaning":"日益普及的","examples":[{"en":"Hand-held electronic devices are becoming increasingly ubiquitous.","zh":"手提電子裝置正變得日益普及。"},{"en":"Increasingly ubiquitous means becoming more and more common everywhere.","zh":"increasingly ubiquitous 指在各處變得越來越常見。"},{"en":"Smartphones have become increasingly ubiquitous in schools, homes, shops, and public transport.","zh":"智能手機在學校、家庭、商店和公共交通中變得日益普及。"},{"en":"When a device becomes ubiquitous, companies can design services assuming many people already own it.","zh":"當裝置變得普及，公司可以在設計服務時假設許多人已擁有它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something spreading widely across daily life.","zh":"這個短語描述某物廣泛滲透日常生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"hand-held electronic devices","meaning":"手提電子裝置","examples":[{"en":"Readers can carry thousands of pages on hand-held electronic devices.","zh":"讀者可以在手提電子裝置中攜帶數以千計的頁面。"},{"en":"Hand-held electronic devices are small digital tools that people can hold and carry, such as phones, tablets, or e-readers.","zh":"hand-held electronic devices 是人們可以手持和攜帶的小型數碼工具，例如手機、平板或電子閱讀器。"},{"en":"A student may read notes on a hand-held electronic device while travelling to school.","zh":"學生可能在上學途中用手提電子裝置閱讀筆記。"},{"en":"Portable devices make digital reading practical outside the home or office.","zh":"便攜裝置令數碼閱讀在家中或辦公室以外也變得實用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes small mobile digital reading or computing tools.","zh":"這個短語描述小型流動數碼閱讀或運算工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"further encourage uptake","meaning":"進一步提高使用率","examples":[{"en":"Mobile devices may further encourage the uptake of e-books.","zh":"流動裝置可能進一步提高電子書使用率。"},{"en":"To further encourage uptake means to make more people adopt or start using something.","zh":"further encourage uptake 指令更多人採用或開始使用某物。"},{"en":"Free training can further encourage the uptake of a new school learning platform.","zh":"免費培訓可以進一步提高新學校學習平台的使用率。"},{"en":"Uptake increases when a product becomes easier, cheaper, or more useful.","zh":"當產品變得更容易、更便宜或更有用，使用率就會提高。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making adoption more likely.","zh":"這個短語描述令採用更有可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"mobile-phone delivery","meaning":"手機內容傳送","examples":[{"en":"Mobile-phone delivery became an important market in Japan.","zh":"手機內容傳送在日本成為重要市場。"},{"en":"Mobile-phone delivery means sending digital content directly to users’ mobile phones.","zh":"mobile-phone delivery 指把數碼內容直接傳送到使用者手機。"},{"en":"A news service may use mobile-phone delivery to send short articles to commuters.","zh":"新聞服務可能使用手機內容傳送，把短文章發給通勤者。"},{"en":"Content delivery to phones works well when people want quick access while travelling.","zh":"當人們想在途中快速查閱，向手機傳送內容就很有效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes distributing digital material through mobile phones.","zh":"這個短語描述透過手機分發數碼材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"jump in value","meaning":"價值急升","examples":[{"en":"The value of mobile e-books jumped rapidly in Japan.","zh":"日本手機電子書的價值迅速急升。"},{"en":"To jump in value means to increase sharply in financial worth.","zh":"jump in value 指財務價值急劇上升。"},{"en":"A small company’s shares may jump in value after it announces a successful product.","zh":"小公司宣布成功產品後，其股票價值可能急升。"},{"en":"A rapid jump can signal sudden demand or investor excitement.","zh":"快速上升可以顯示突然需求或投資者興奮。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a quick and large rise in value.","zh":"這個短語描述價值快速而大幅上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"manga comic books","meaning":"日本漫畫書","examples":[{"en":"Most Japanese mobile e-books in the example were manga comic books.","zh":"例子中的大部分日本手機電子書都是日本漫畫書。"},{"en":"Manga comic books are Japanese-style comics, often told through illustrated panels and speech bubbles.","zh":"manga comic books 是日本風格漫畫，常透過圖格和對話框講故事。"},{"en":"A teenager may read manga comic books on a phone during a train journey.","zh":"青少年可能在火車途中用手機閱讀日本漫畫書。"},{"en":"Manga works well on mobile screens because pictures can be read in short sections.","zh":"日本漫畫很適合手機屏幕，因為圖片可以分短段閱讀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes Japanese comics as a reading format.","zh":"這個短語描述作為閱讀形式的日本漫畫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"according to estimates","meaning":"根據估算","examples":[{"en":"The market was expected to reach ¥6 billion, according to estimates.","zh":"根據估算，該市場預期達到六十億日圓。"},{"en":"According to estimates means based on calculated guesses or projections, not final confirmed figures.","zh":"according to estimates 指基於計算出來的估計或預測，而不是最終確認數字。"},{"en":"According to estimates, the new bus route may serve 10,000 passengers a week.","zh":"根據估算，新巴士路線每星期可能服務一萬名乘客。"},{"en":"Estimates help people plan, but they can change when real data arrives.","zh":"估算幫助人規劃，但真實數據出現後可以改變。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces information based on projected figures.","zh":"這個短語引出基於預測數字的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"only one choice is correct","meaning":"只有一個選項正確","examples":[{"en":"For each question, only one choice is correct.","zh":"每題只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"Only one choice is correct means just one option matches the information or answer required.","zh":"only one choice is correct 指只有一個選項符合所需資訊或答案。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice grammar question, only one choice is correct even if another sounds natural.","zh":"在文法選擇題中，即使另一個選項聽起來自然，也只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"Students should avoid choosing two answers when the instruction says only one is allowed.","zh":"當指示說只容許一個答案，學生應避免選兩個。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strict single-answer question.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴格的單一答案題目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"corresponding letter","meaning":"對應字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the corresponding letter on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生在答題紙上寫下對應字母。"},{"en":"A corresponding letter is the letter that matches the chosen answer or option.","zh":"corresponding letter 是與所選答案或選項相配的字母。"},{"en":"If the answer is option C, students should write the corresponding letter C clearly.","zh":"如果答案是選項 C，學生應清楚寫下對應字母 C。"},{"en":"Writing the wrong letter can lose marks even if the student knows the right idea.","zh":"即使學生知道正確想法，寫錯字母也可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the letter linked to a selected answer.","zh":"這個短語描述與所選答案相連的字母。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"appropriate box","meaning":"適當的方格","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should be written in the appropriate box.","zh":"每個答案應寫在適當的方格內。"},{"en":"The appropriate box is the correct space on an answer sheet for a particular answer.","zh":"appropriate box 是答題紙上某個答案應填寫的正確空格。"},{"en":"Students should write answer 12 in the box labelled 12, not beside question 13.","zh":"學生應把第12題答案寫在標示12的方格，而不是第13題旁邊。"},{"en":"Using the correct box prevents confusion when answers are marked.","zh":"使用正確方格可在改卷時避免混亂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the proper place for writing an answer.","zh":"這個短語描述填寫答案的適當位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"it was widely thought that","meaning":"人們普遍認為","examples":[{"en":"A few years ago, it was widely thought that paper books would decline.","zh":"幾年前，人們普遍認為紙本書會衰落。"},{"en":"It was widely thought that means many people believed something at the time.","zh":"it was widely thought that 指當時許多人相信某事。"},{"en":"It was widely thought that young people would stop using libraries, but many still study there.","zh":"人們普遍認為年輕人會停止使用圖書館，但許多人仍在那裏溫習。"},{"en":"A common belief can be wrong if people underestimate habit, comfort, or culture.","zh":"如果人們低估習慣、舒適感或文化，常見信念可能是錯的。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a belief shared by many people.","zh":"這個短語引出許多人共同持有的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"paper books","meaning":"紙本書","examples":[{"en":"Many readers still prefer paper books to digital editions.","zh":"許多讀者仍較喜歡紙本書而非數碼版本。"},{"en":"Paper books are physical books printed on paper, not read as digital files.","zh":"paper books 是印在紙上的實體書，而不是以數碼檔案閱讀。"},{"en":"A child may enjoy paper books because she can turn pages and see pictures clearly.","zh":"孩子可能喜歡紙本書，因為她可以翻頁並清楚看圖。"},{"en":"Paper books remain popular when readers value touch, smell, ownership, and screen-free reading.","zh":"當讀者重視觸感、氣味、擁有感和無屏幕閱讀，紙本書仍會受歡迎。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts printed books with electronic books.","zh":"這個短語把印刷書與電子書作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"read fewer paper books","meaning":"閱讀較少紙本書","examples":[{"en":"Some commentators predicted that people would read fewer paper books.","zh":"有些評論者預測人們會閱讀較少紙本書。"},{"en":"To read fewer paper books means to spend less time reading printed books than before.","zh":"read fewer paper books 指比以前花較少時間閱讀印刷書籍。"},{"en":"A student may read fewer paper books after receiving most school materials online.","zh":"學生收到大部分網上學習材料後，可能閱讀較少紙本書。"},{"en":"People may read fewer printed books if screens become more convenient and comfortable.","zh":"如果屏幕變得更方便和舒適，人們可能閱讀較少印刷書。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a decline in paper-based reading.","zh":"這個短語描述紙本閱讀減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"go bankrupt","meaning":"破產","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that major online companies would go bankrupt.","zh":"該選項暗示大型網上公司會破產。"},{"en":"To go bankrupt means to be legally unable to pay debts and continue operating normally.","zh":"go bankrupt 指在法律上無法償還債務並正常繼續營運。"},{"en":"A small shop may go bankrupt if rent rises and sales fall for many months.","zh":"如果租金上升而銷售連續多月下降，小店可能破產。"},{"en":"Bankruptcy can force a company to close, sell assets, or restructure.","zh":"破產可以迫使公司關閉、出售資產或重組。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious financial failure.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重財務失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"come to an end","meaning":"結束","examples":[{"en":"The dotcom boom eventually came to an end.","zh":"科網熱潮最終結束。"},{"en":"To come to an end means to finish or stop continuing.","zh":"come to an end 指完成或停止繼續。"},{"en":"A school term comes to an end after final exams and report cards are finished.","zh":"學期在期末考試和成績表完成後結束。"},{"en":"Booms often come to an end when excitement is replaced by financial reality.","zh":"當興奮被財務現實取代，熱潮常會結束。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the closing point of a period or event.","zh":"這個短語描述某段時期或事件的終點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be unhappy with","meaning":"對……感到不滿","examples":[{"en":"Publishers were unhappy with Google’s approach to copyrighted books.","zh":"出版商對 Google 處理受版權保護書籍的做法感到不滿。"},{"en":"To be unhappy with something means to feel dissatisfied, annoyed, or worried about it.","zh":"be unhappy with 某事，指對它感到不滿、惱怒或擔心。"},{"en":"Parents may be unhappy with a school policy if it is unclear or unfair.","zh":"如果校政不清楚或不公平，家長可能對它感到不滿。"},{"en":"People become unhappy when they feel their interests are ignored.","zh":"當人們覺得自己的利益被忽視，就會感到不滿。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dissatisfaction with a person, plan, or action.","zh":"這個短語描述對人物、計劃或行動的不滿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be in breach of copyright","meaning":"違反版權法","examples":[{"en":"Publishers argued that Google was in breach of copyright.","zh":"出版商主張 Google 違反版權法。"},{"en":"To be in breach of copyright means to break copyright law or copyright agreements.","zh":"be in breach of copyright 指違反版權法律或版權協議。"},{"en":"A website may be in breach of copyright if it offers full paid books for free download.","zh":"如果網站提供完整付費書籍免費下載，它可能違反版權法。"},{"en":"A breach can lead to legal claims from the copyright owner.","zh":"違規可導致版權持有人提出法律申索。"},{"en":"The phrase describes violating copyright rules.","zh":"這個短語描述違反版權規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"co-operate with","meaning":"與……合作","examples":[{"en":"Google co-operated with several leading research libraries.","zh":"Google 與幾間頂尖研究圖書館合作。"},{"en":"To co-operate with someone means to work together with them to achieve a shared goal.","zh":"co-operate with 某人，指與他們共同工作以達成共同目標。"},{"en":"Students must co-operate with group members to finish a project on time.","zh":"學生必須與小組成員合作，才能準時完成項目。"},{"en":"Cooperation works best when each side understands its role and responsibility.","zh":"當每一方理解自己的角色和責任，合作最有效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes working jointly rather than separately.","zh":"這個短語描述共同工作，而不是各自分開行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"allow someone to buy only","meaning":"讓某人只購買……","examples":[{"en":"The service would allow customers to buy only the sections they wanted.","zh":"該服務會讓顧客只購買他們想要的部分。"},{"en":"To allow someone to buy only something means to give them permission or ability to purchase just that part.","zh":"allow someone to buy only 某物，指容許或使某人能只購買該部分。"},{"en":"A website may allow students to buy only one chapter instead of the whole textbook.","zh":"網站可能讓學生只購買一章，而不是整本教科書。"},{"en":"This option can reduce cost when users need a specific section rather than a full product.","zh":"當使用者需要特定部分而非完整產品，這種選項可以降低成本。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limiting a purchase to the desired part.","zh":"這個短語描述把購買限制於想要的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"parts one wants to read","meaning":"想閱讀的部分","examples":[{"en":"Some readers may buy only the parts they want to read.","zh":"有些讀者可能只購買自己想閱讀的部分。"},{"en":"Parts one wants to read are the specific pages, chapters, or sections that are useful or interesting to a reader.","zh":"parts one wants to read 是對讀者有用或有趣的特定頁面、章節或部分。"},{"en":"A student preparing a report may need only the parts she wants to read about climate data.","zh":"準備報告的學生可能只需要想閱讀的氣候數據部分。"},{"en":"Buying only selected parts can be cheaper than buying the whole book.","zh":"只購買選定部分可以比買整本書便宜。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reading based on personal need rather than full coverage.","zh":"這個短語描述根據個人需要而非完整覆蓋的閱讀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"if given the choice","meaning":"如果可以選擇","examples":[{"en":"If given the choice, many readers still prefer printed books.","zh":"如果可以選擇，許多讀者仍較喜歡印刷書。"},{"en":"If given the choice means if people are allowed to choose freely between options.","zh":"if given the choice 指如果人們被容許在選項之間自由選擇。"},{"en":"If given the choice, some students prefer handwritten notes to typed notes.","zh":"如果可以選擇，有些學生較喜歡手寫筆記而非打字筆記。"},{"en":"Preferences become clearer when people are not forced into one format.","zh":"當人們沒有被迫使用一種形式，偏好會更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces what people would choose under free conditions.","zh":"這個短語引出人在自由條件下會作出的選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"prefer one format to another","meaning":"較喜歡一種形式而非另一種","examples":[{"en":"Some consumers prefer paper books to reading from screens.","zh":"有些消費者較喜歡紙本書，而不是從屏幕閱讀。"},{"en":"To prefer one format to another means to like one form of presentation more than a different form.","zh":"prefer one format to another 指較喜歡一種呈現形式，而不是另一種。"},{"en":"A student may prefer audio lessons to printed notes because she learns better by listening.","zh":"學生可能較喜歡音頻課堂而非印刷筆記，因為她透過聆聽學得更好。"},{"en":"Format preference affects how people choose to study, shop, or read.","zh":"形式偏好會影響人們如何選擇學習、購物或閱讀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes choosing between different ways of presenting the same content.","zh":"這個短語描述在同一內容的不同呈現方式之間作選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the sentences","meaning":"完成句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the sentences using words from the text.","zh":"考生使用文本中的字詞完成句子。"},{"en":"To complete the sentences means to fill in missing words so the sentences become correct and meaningful.","zh":"complete the sentences 指填入缺失字詞，使句子變得正確而有意義。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete the sentences by finding exact information in the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過在文章中尋找準確資訊來完成句子。"},{"en":"Checking grammar before and after each gap helps students choose the right word form.","zh":"檢查每個空格前後的文法，能幫助學生選擇正確詞形。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an exam task involving sentence gaps.","zh":"這個短語描述涉及句子空格的考試任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than three words.","zh":"每個答案應包含不多於三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must have three words or fewer.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案必須有三個詞或以下。"},{"en":"“Public domain texts” has three words, so it fits the instruction.","zh":"“public domain texts” 有三個詞，所以符合指示。"},{"en":"Writing four words may lose marks even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫四個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit for exam answers.","zh":"這個短語為考試答案設定嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"for each gap","meaning":"每個空格","examples":[{"en":"Candidates select a short phrase for each gap.","zh":"考生為每個空格選擇一個短語。"},{"en":"For each gap means for every blank space that needs an answer.","zh":"for each gap 指對每一個需要答案的空白位置。"},{"en":"Students should check the grammar for each gap before copying words from the passage.","zh":"學生在從文章抄字前，應檢查每個空格的文法。"},{"en":"Each gap may require a noun, verb, number, or short phrase.","zh":"每個空格可能需要名詞、動詞、數字或短語。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated attention to every blank in a task.","zh":"這個短語描述對任務中每個空白位逐一處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"publish books online","meaning":"在網上出版書籍","examples":[{"en":"Companies may publish copyright-free books online.","zh":"公司可能在網上出版無版權書籍。"},{"en":"To publish books online means to make books available to readers through the internet.","zh":"publish books online 指透過互聯網向讀者提供書籍。"},{"en":"A school may publish student storybooks online so parents can read them at home.","zh":"學校可能在網上出版學生故事書，讓家長在家閱讀。"},{"en":"Online publishing can reach readers faster than printing and shipping paper copies.","zh":"網上出版比印刷和運送紙本副本更快接觸讀者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes releasing books in digital form.","zh":"這個短語描述以數碼形式發布書籍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"avoid legal problems","meaning":"避免法律問題","examples":[{"en":"Using public-domain texts helps companies avoid legal problems.","zh":"使用公有領域文本有助公司避免法律問題。"},{"en":"To avoid legal problems means to prevent conflict with laws, contracts, or rights.","zh":"avoid legal problems 指防止與法律、合約或權利產生衝突。"},{"en":"A teacher can avoid legal problems by using images that are free for classroom use.","zh":"老師可以使用可供課堂免費使用的圖片，以避免法律問題。"},{"en":"Legal problems may arise when ownership, permission, or copyright is unclear.","zh":"當所有權、許可或版權不清楚，法律問題可能出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes acting carefully so the law is not broken.","zh":"這個短語描述謹慎行事，以免違法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the e-book market","meaning":"電子書市場","examples":[{"en":"The e-book market remains small but continues to grow.","zh":"電子書市場仍然細小，但繼續增長。"},{"en":"The e-book market is the business area involving the sale and distribution of electronic books.","zh":"e-book market 是涉及電子書銷售和發行的商業領域。"},{"en":"The e-book market may grow when students, commuters, and travellers prefer lightweight reading.","zh":"當學生、通勤者和旅客較喜歡輕便閱讀，電子書市場可能增長。"},{"en":"A market can remain small even when its growth rate looks strong.","zh":"即使增長率看似強勁，市場仍可能保持細小。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the commercial world of electronic books.","zh":"這個短語描述電子書的商業世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"get larger","meaning":"逐漸擴大","examples":[{"en":"The market is currently small but gradually getting larger.","zh":"該市場目前細小，但正逐漸擴大。"},{"en":"To get larger means to increase in size, amount, number, or importance.","zh":"get larger 指在大小、數量、人數或重要性上增加。"},{"en":"A school club may get larger when more students hear about its activities.","zh":"當更多學生聽到學會活動，學會可能逐漸擴大。"},{"en":"Markets get larger when more customers buy and more companies enter.","zh":"當更多顧客購買、更多公司進入市場，市場就會擴大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual growth.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"convince more people to","meaning":"說服更多人去……","examples":[{"en":"Retailers expect to convince more people to read online.","zh":"零售商預期能說服更多人在網上閱讀。"},{"en":"To convince more people to do something means to persuade a larger number of people to accept or try it.","zh":"convince more people to do something 指說服更多人接受或嘗試某事。"},{"en":"A school may convince more students to read by creating comfortable reading corners.","zh":"學校可能透過設立舒適閱讀角，說服更多學生閱讀。"},{"en":"People are easier to convince when they see clear benefits and low risk.","zh":"當人們看見明確好處和低風險，就較容易被說服。"},{"en":"The phrase describes expanding acceptance through persuasion.","zh":"這個短語描述透過說服擴大接受度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"have nothing similar to","meaning":"沒有類似……的東西","examples":[{"en":"The book world has nothing similar to the iPod.","zh":"圖書業界沒有類似 iPod 的東西。"},{"en":"To have nothing similar to something means to lack anything comparable in function, attraction, or success.","zh":"have nothing similar to 某物，指缺乏在功能、吸引力或成功程度上可比較的東西。"},{"en":"A small town may have nothing similar to a large city’s subway system.","zh":"小鎮可能沒有類似大城市地鐵系統的東西。"},{"en":"Without a similar product, an industry may struggle to copy another industry’s success.","zh":"沒有類似產品，某行業可能難以複製另一行業的成功。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the absence of a comparable model.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏可比較模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be sent to mobile phones","meaning":"被傳送到手機","examples":[{"en":"Many electronic publications are sent directly to mobile phones.","zh":"許多電子出版物被直接傳送到手機。"},{"en":"To be sent to mobile phones means to be delivered digitally to users’ phones.","zh":"be sent to mobile phones 指以數碼方式傳送到使用者手機。"},{"en":"A school notice can be sent to mobile phones so parents receive it immediately.","zh":"學校通告可以被傳送到手機，讓家長即時收到。"},{"en":"Phone delivery is convenient because users carry their devices almost everywhere.","zh":"手機傳送很方便，因為使用者幾乎到處都帶着裝置。"},{"en":"The phrase describes content being distributed through mobile devices.","zh":"這個短語描述內容透過流動裝置分發。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether each statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"考生判斷每項陳述是否與文章資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information means to match what the text says.","zh":"agree with the information 指與文本所說內容相符。"},{"en":"In a reading test, a statement agrees with the information if the passage clearly supports it.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，如果文章清楚支持某陳述，它就與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge if the passage gives a different answer.","zh":"如果文章給出不同答案，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"The phrase describes checking whether a statement is true according to the text.","zh":"這個短語描述檢查陳述是否按文本為真。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information given.","zh":"錯誤陳述與所給資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文本所說相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says sales rose, a statement saying sales fell contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說銷售上升，而陳述說銷售下降，就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should look for direct conflict between the statement and the passage.","zh":"學生應尋找陳述與文章之間的直接衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a clear mismatch with the text.","zh":"這個短語描述與文本清楚不符。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"“Not Given” means that the passage contains no information on the point.","zh":"“Not Given” 意味着文章沒有關於該點的相關資料。"},{"en":"No information on this means the text does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"no information on this 指文本沒有說明該陳述是真還是假。"},{"en":"If a passage describes book sales but not authors’ ages, there is no information on authors’ ages.","zh":"如果文章描述書籍銷售但沒有提及作者年齡，就沒有關於作者年齡的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from general knowledge when the passage gives no evidence.","zh":"當文章沒有證據時，學生不應憑常識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an unsupported point in a reading task.","zh":"這個短語描述閱讀題中沒有文本支持的一點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"out-of-print books","meaning":"絕版書籍","examples":[{"en":"Out-of-print books may still be protected by copyright law.","zh":"絕版書籍可能仍受版權法保障。"},{"en":"Out-of-print books are books that publishers no longer produce in new printed copies.","zh":"out-of-print books 是出版社不再生產新印刷副本的書籍。"},{"en":"A collector may search for out-of-print books in second-hand shops or online auctions.","zh":"收藏家可能在二手書店或網上拍賣尋找絕版書籍。"},{"en":"Being out of print can make a book hard to find, but not necessarily free to copy.","zh":"已絕版會令書難以找到，但不一定可自由複製。"},{"en":"The phrase describes books no longer commercially printed by the publisher.","zh":"這個短語描述出版社不再商業印刷的書籍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be covered by copyright law","meaning":"受版權法保障","examples":[{"en":"A publication can remain covered by copyright law after going out of print.","zh":"出版物絕版後仍可以受版權法保障。"},{"en":"To be covered by copyright law means to be protected by legal rules controlling copying and distribution.","zh":"be covered by copyright law 指受控制複製和分發的法律規則保護。"},{"en":"A song can be covered by copyright law even if it was written many years ago.","zh":"歌曲即使多年前寫成，仍可能受版權法保障。"},{"en":"Legal coverage matters because users may still need permission to reproduce the work.","zh":"法律保障很重要，因為使用者可能仍需要許可才能複製作品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes protection under copyright rules.","zh":"這個短語描述受版權規則保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"begin by doing something","meaning":"最初以做某事起家","examples":[{"en":"Amazon began by selling books online.","zh":"Amazon 最初以在網上賣書起家。"},{"en":"To begin by doing something means to start with a particular action before later developments.","zh":"begin by doing something 指先以某個特定行動開始，之後再有後續發展。"},{"en":"A student may begin by reading the question carefully before writing an essay.","zh":"學生寫文章前，可能先仔細閱讀題目。"},{"en":"Starting with one clear action can create a foundation for later growth.","zh":"以一個清楚行動開始，可以為後來增長建立基礎。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the first step in a process.","zh":"這個短語描述過程中的第一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"sign a deal with","meaning":"與……簽訂協議","examples":[{"en":"Microsoft signed a digitisation deal with the British Library.","zh":"Microsoft 與英國圖書館簽訂數碼化協議。"},{"en":"To sign a deal with an organisation means to formally agree to work with it under stated terms.","zh":"sign a deal with 某機構，指在列明條款下正式同意與它合作。"},{"en":"A school may sign a deal with a technology company to provide tablets for students.","zh":"學校可能與科技公司簽訂協議，為學生提供平板電腦。"},{"en":"A signed deal gives both sides clearer duties and expectations.","zh":"已簽協議讓雙方有更清楚的責任和期望。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a formal agreement with a partner.","zh":"這個短語描述與夥伴訂立正式協議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"on the same day as","meaning":"與……在同一天","examples":[{"en":"Microsoft released its details on the same day as the other announcements.","zh":"Microsoft 在其他公布的同一天發布其詳情。"},{"en":"On the same day as means happening on the identical date as another event.","zh":"on the same day as 指與另一事件在完全相同日期發生。"},{"en":"A school concert may take place on the same day as a sports competition.","zh":"學校音樂會可能與運動比賽在同一天舉行。"},{"en":"Events on the same day can attract comparison because people notice the timing.","zh":"同一天發生的事件容易被比較，因為人們會注意時間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes matching dates between events.","zh":"這個短語描述事件之間日期相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"make an announcement","meaning":"發表公布","examples":[{"en":"Several technology companies made major announcements that week.","zh":"幾間科技公司在那星期發表重大公布。"},{"en":"To make an announcement means to tell people important news or information publicly.","zh":"make an announcement 指公開告訴人們重要消息或資訊。"},{"en":"A principal may make an announcement about a new school timetable.","zh":"校長可能發表關於新時間表的公布。"},{"en":"Announcements help organisations share changes with many people at once.","zh":"公布幫助機構一次過向很多人分享變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formally giving public information.","zh":"這個短語描述正式提供公共資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"publish something online","meaning":"在網上發布某物","examples":[{"en":"Stephen King published his story online rather than through Barnes and Noble.","zh":"Stephen King 在網上發布他的故事，而不是透過 Barnes and Noble。"},{"en":"To publish something online means to release written or creative material on the internet.","zh":"publish something online 指在互聯網上發布文字或創作材料。"},{"en":"A student newspaper may publish interviews online to reach more readers.","zh":"學生報可能在網上發布訪問，以接觸更多讀者。"},{"en":"Online publishing can bypass physical stores and reach readers quickly.","zh":"網上發布可以繞過實體店，迅速接觸讀者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making content available on the web.","zh":"這個短語描述把內容放到網上供人取得。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"sample a book online","meaning":"在網上試讀一本書","examples":[{"en":"Customers may sample a book online before purchasing it.","zh":"顧客可能在購買前在網上試讀一本書。"},{"en":"To sample a book online means to read a short part of it on the internet before buying.","zh":"sample a book online 指在購買前在互聯網上閱讀其中一小部分。"},{"en":"A reader may sample a book online by opening the preview pages on a retailer’s website.","zh":"讀者可能透過打開零售商網站上的預覽頁，在網上試讀一本書。"},{"en":"Online samples reduce risk because customers can check style and difficulty first.","zh":"網上試讀降低風險，因為顧客可以先檢查風格和難度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes previewing a book digitally before purchase.","zh":"這個短語描述購買前以數碼方式預覽書籍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"before buying","meaning":"購買之前","examples":[{"en":"Many consumers prefer to examine a product before buying it.","zh":"許多消費者較喜歡在購買之前檢查產品。"},{"en":"Before buying means before deciding to pay for and own something.","zh":"before buying 指在決定付款並擁有某物之前。"},{"en":"A reader may check the first chapter before buying a novel.","zh":"讀者可能在購買小說前先查看第一章。"},{"en":"Examining a product first can prevent disappointment and wasted money.","zh":"先檢查產品可以防止失望和浪費金錢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the stage before purchase.","zh":"這個短語描述購買前的階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"help sales","meaning":"促進銷售","examples":[{"en":"Online previews may help sales of complete printed books.","zh":"網上預覽可能促進完整印刷書籍的銷售。"},{"en":"To help sales means to increase purchases or make a product sell better.","zh":"help sales 指增加購買量或令產品賣得更好。"},{"en":"Good customer reviews can help sales of a new textbook.","zh":"良好顧客評價可以促進新教科書銷售。"},{"en":"Samples help sales when they make people confident enough to buy the full product.","zh":"當樣本令顧客有足夠信心購買完整產品，它們就能促進銷售。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improving commercial performance.","zh":"這個短語描述改善商業表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 16 - A LIBRARY AT YOUR FINGERTIPS.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 17":[{"front":"psychometrics","meaning":"心理計量學","examples":[{"en":"Psychometrics involves the scientific measurement of psychological characteristics.","zh":"心理計量學涉及對心理特徵作科學量度。"},{"en":"Psychometrics means using tests and statistics to measure the mind.","zh":"心理計量學是指使用測驗和統計來量度心智能力。"},{"en":"A school may use psychometrics to understand students’ learning strengths.","zh":"學校可能使用心理計量學來了解學生的學習強項。"},{"en":"Because it uses standardised tools, psychometrics can compare people more fairly.","zh":"由於它使用標準化工具，心理計量學可以較公平地比較不同人士。"},{"en":"This field studies how mental qualities can be measured reliably.","zh":"這個領域研究如何可靠地量度心理特質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"psychological and educational assessment","meaning":"心理及教育評估","examples":[{"en":"Psychometrics is used in psychological and educational assessment.","zh":"心理計量學被用於心理及教育評估。"},{"en":"Psychological and educational assessment means evaluating mental traits and learning ability.","zh":"心理及教育評估是指評估心理特質和學習能力。"},{"en":"A counsellor may use this assessment to understand a student’s needs.","zh":"輔導員可能使用這類評估來了解學生需要。"},{"en":"Good assessment can guide teaching, support and career planning.","zh":"良好評估可以指導教學、支援和職業規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase covers testing in both psychology and education.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋心理學和教育中的測驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"assessment of the subject","meaning":"對受試者的評估","examples":[{"en":"The assessment of the subject may cover personality, knowledge and ability.","zh":"對受試者的評估可能涵蓋性格、知識和能力。"},{"en":"Assessment of the subject means evaluating the person being tested.","zh":"對受試者的評估是指評估接受測驗的人。"},{"en":"In a school interview, the assessment of the subject may include speaking skills.","zh":"在學校面試中，對受試者的評估可能包括口語能力。"},{"en":"If the assessment is too narrow, it may miss important strengths.","zh":"如果評估範圍太窄，可能會忽略重要強項。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what is being measured in the test-taker.","zh":"這個短語聚焦測驗對象身上被量度的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"by way of","meaning":"透過；藉着","examples":[{"en":"Psychologists assess individuals by way of standardised tests.","zh":"心理學家透過標準化測驗評估個人。"},{"en":"By way of means through or by using a particular method.","zh":"by way of 是指透過某種方法或藉着某種方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain grammar by way of simple examples.","zh":"老師可能透過簡單例子解釋文法。"},{"en":"Using tests by way of assessment can make results easier to compare.","zh":"透過測驗作評估，可以令結果較容易比較。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the method used to do something.","zh":"這個短語引入做某事所用的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"measure attitudes","meaning":"量度態度","examples":[{"en":"Psychometric instruments can be used to measure attitudes.","zh":"心理計量工具可以用來量度態度。"},{"en":"To measure attitudes means to assess what people think or feel about something.","zh":"量度態度是指評估人們對某事的想法或感受。"},{"en":"A survey may measure attitudes toward online learning.","zh":"問卷可以量度人們對網上學習的態度。"},{"en":"Measuring attitudes helps organisations understand support, resistance or concern.","zh":"量度態度有助組織了解支持、抗拒或憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes turning opinions into assessable data.","zh":"這個短語描述把意見轉化成可評估資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"personality and abilities","meaning":"性格和能力","examples":[{"en":"The assessment considers personality and abilities as well as knowledge.","zh":"評估除了考慮知識，也考慮性格和能力。"},{"en":"Personality and abilities mean a person’s character traits and what they can do.","zh":"性格和能力是指一個人的性格特質和他能做到的事。"},{"en":"A job interview may assess both personality and abilities.","zh":"求職面試可能同時評估性格和能力。"},{"en":"Someone may know a lot but lack the personality needed for teamwork.","zh":"有人可能知識豐富，但缺乏團隊合作所需的性格。"},{"en":"This phrase separates who a person is from what a person can do.","zh":"這個短語把一個人的個性和能力分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have two primary focuses","meaning":"有兩個主要焦點","examples":[{"en":"The field has two primary focuses.","zh":"這個領域有兩個主要焦點。"},{"en":"To have two primary focuses means to centre mainly on two major areas.","zh":"有兩個主要焦點，是指主要集中於兩大範疇。"},{"en":"A school project may have two primary focuses: research and presentation.","zh":"學校專題可能有兩個主要焦點：研究和匯報。"},{"en":"Clear focuses help readers understand the structure of a subject.","zh":"清晰焦點幫助讀者理解一個主題的結構。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the main areas of attention.","zh":"這個短語引入主要關注範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"creation of measurement instruments","meaning":"建立測量工具","examples":[{"en":"One focus is the creation of measurement instruments.","zh":"其中一個焦點是建立測量工具。"},{"en":"Creation of measurement instruments means designing tools that can assess something.","zh":"建立測量工具是指設計能評估某事的工具。"},{"en":"Researchers may create a questionnaire to measure student motivation.","zh":"研究人員可能設計問卷來量度學生動機。"},{"en":"Without good instruments, test results may be unclear or unfair.","zh":"沒有良好工具，測驗結果可能不清晰或不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to building reliable testing tools.","zh":"這個短語指建立可靠測驗工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"measurement procedures","meaning":"測量程序","examples":[{"en":"Researchers develop reliable measurement procedures.","zh":"研究人員發展可靠的測量程序。"},{"en":"Measurement procedures are the steps used to measure something consistently.","zh":"測量程序是用來一致地量度某事的步驟。"},{"en":"A teacher may follow clear marking procedures when grading essays.","zh":"老師批改作文時可能遵循清晰評分程序。"},{"en":"Good procedures reduce random error and personal bias.","zh":"良好程序可以減少隨機錯誤和個人偏見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process behind measurement.","zh":"這個短語描述量度背後的流程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"development and enhancement of","meaning":"發展及改良……","examples":[{"en":"The field includes the development and enhancement of existing methods.","zh":"這個領域包括發展及改良現有方法。"},{"en":"Development and enhancement of something means creating it further and improving it.","zh":"發展及改良某事，是指進一步建立並改善它。"},{"en":"A school may focus on the development and enhancement of its online platform.","zh":"學校可能專注於發展及改良網上平台。"},{"en":"Enhancement makes old methods more accurate, useful or efficient.","zh":"改良能令舊方法更準確、有用或有效率。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both growth and improvement.","zh":"這個短語同時描述發展和改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"existing methodology","meaning":"現有方法","examples":[{"en":"Researchers continually improve the existing methodology.","zh":"研究人員不斷改善現有方法。"},{"en":"Existing methodology means the methods already being used.","zh":"現有方法是指已經正在使用的方法。"},{"en":"A school may review its existing methodology for teaching grammar.","zh":"學校可能檢討教授文法的現有方法。"},{"en":"Improving existing methodology can make old systems work better.","zh":"改善現有方法可以令舊系統運作得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to current methods, not new ones.","zh":"這個短語指目前的方法，而不是新方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"methodology employed","meaning":"所採用的方法","examples":[{"en":"The methodology employed must be valid and reliable.","zh":"所採用的方法必須有效而可靠。"},{"en":"Methodology employed means the method or system actually used.","zh":"所採用的方法，是指實際使用的方法或系統。"},{"en":"In research, the methodology employed affects how trustworthy the results are.","zh":"在研究中，所採用的方法會影響結果是否可信。"},{"en":"Poor methodology can lead to misleading conclusions.","zh":"不良方法可能導致具誤導性的結論。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the chosen research method.","zh":"這個短語聚焦被選用的研究方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"concept of psychometric testing","meaning":"心理計量測驗的概念","examples":[{"en":"The concept of psychometric testing existed before modern IQ tests.","zh":"心理計量測驗的概念早於現代智商測驗已存在。"},{"en":"The concept of psychometric testing means the idea of measuring mental traits through tests.","zh":"心理計量測驗的概念，是指透過測驗量度心理特質的想法。"},{"en":"A school aptitude test is based on this concept.","zh":"學校能力傾向測驗就是建基於這個概念。"},{"en":"The concept became more advanced as testing methods improved.","zh":"隨着測驗方法改善，這個概念變得更先進。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the basic idea behind mental measurement.","zh":"這個短語指心智量度背後的基本想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"long before the establishment of","meaning":"遠在……建立之前","examples":[{"en":"Psychometric testing began long before the establishment of current IQ methods.","zh":"心理計量測驗遠在現行智商方法建立之前已開始。"},{"en":"Long before the establishment of something means much earlier than it was created.","zh":"遠在某事建立之前，是指比它被創立早很多。"},{"en":"People studied stars long before the establishment of modern astronomy.","zh":"人們遠在現代天文學建立之前已研究星星。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights that an idea has older roots.","zh":"這個短語強調一個想法有更早根源。"},{"en":"It contrasts early beginnings with later formal systems.","zh":"它把早期起源與後來正式系統作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"IQ testing","meaning":"智商測驗","examples":[{"en":"IQ testing attempts to measure aspects of intelligence.","zh":"智商測驗嘗試量度智力的某些方面。"},{"en":"IQ testing means using tests to estimate a person’s intellectual ability.","zh":"智商測驗是指使用測驗估計一個人的智力能力。"},{"en":"A psychologist may use IQ testing to understand a child’s learning profile.","zh":"心理學家可能使用智商測驗了解孩子的學習能力組合。"},{"en":"IQ testing can be useful, but it may not capture every kind of ability.","zh":"智商測驗可以有用，但未必能捕捉每一種能力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal tests of intelligence.","zh":"這個短語指正式智力測驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"current methodologies","meaning":"現行方法","examples":[{"en":"Current methodologies are more sophisticated than early testing procedures.","zh":"現行方法比早期測驗程序更精密。"},{"en":"Current methodologies mean the methods used today.","zh":"現行方法是指今天使用的方法。"},{"en":"Current methodologies in schools may include online tests and data analysis.","zh":"學校的現行方法可能包括網上測驗和數據分析。"},{"en":"Newer methods can improve accuracy by learning from older weaknesses.","zh":"較新的方法可以從舊方法弱點中學習，從而提高準確度。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts modern methods with earlier ones.","zh":"這個短語把現代方法與早期方法作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"first explored by","meaning":"最先由……研究","examples":[{"en":"The idea was first explored by Francis Galton.","zh":"這個想法最先由 Francis Galton 研究。"},{"en":"First explored by someone means first studied or investigated by that person.","zh":"最先由某人研究，是指最早由那人探討或調查。"},{"en":"A teaching method may be first explored by a small group of researchers.","zh":"一種教學方法可能最先由一小群研究人員研究。"},{"en":"Early exploration can influence later studies even if it is imperfect.","zh":"早期研究即使不完美，也可以影響後來研究。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the first major investigator.","zh":"這個短語指出最早的重要研究者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"testing procedures","meaning":"測驗程序","examples":[{"en":"Galton developed some of the first testing procedures.","zh":"Galton 發展了一些最早期的測驗程序。"},{"en":"Testing procedures are the steps used to conduct a test.","zh":"測驗程序是進行測驗所使用的步驟。"},{"en":"A driving test has procedures such as checking mirrors and parking safely.","zh":"駕駛考試有檢查鏡子和安全泊車等程序。"},{"en":"Clear procedures make test results more consistent.","zh":"清晰程序令測驗結果更一致。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the organised process of testing.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的測驗流程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"supposedly related to","meaning":"據稱與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The early procedures were supposedly related to intelligence.","zh":"早期程序據稱與智力有關。"},{"en":"Supposedly related to something means believed to be connected, though not certainly proven.","zh":"據稱與某事有關，是指被認為有聯繫，但未必確定證明。"},{"en":"A study habit may be supposedly related to better grades, but evidence is needed.","zh":"某種學習習慣據稱與更好成績有關，但仍需要證據。"},{"en":"The word suggests some doubt about the connection.","zh":"這個詞暗示對該聯繫有一定懷疑。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a claim may be questionable.","zh":"當某主張可能有問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in fact based upon","meaning":"其實以……為基礎","examples":[{"en":"The measurements were in fact based upon physical characteristics.","zh":"這些測量其實以身體特徵為基礎。"},{"en":"In fact based upon means actually built on or relying on something.","zh":"其實以某事為基礎，是指實際上建基於或依賴某事。"},{"en":"A school rumour may be in fact based upon a misunderstood notice.","zh":"一個學校謠言可能其實以一份被誤解的通告為基礎。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects what people might wrongly assume.","zh":"這個短語修正人們可能錯誤作出的假設。"},{"en":"It reveals the real foundation of an idea or method.","zh":"它揭示一個想法或方法的真正基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"physical and physiological benchmarks","meaning":"身體及生理基準","examples":[{"en":"Galton used physical and physiological benchmarks.","zh":"Galton 使用身體及生理基準。"},{"en":"Physical and physiological benchmarks are body-based standards or measurements.","zh":"身體及生理基準是以身體為本的標準或測量。"},{"en":"Height, weight and reaction speed can be physical or physiological benchmarks.","zh":"身高、體重和反應速度都可以是身體或生理基準。"},{"en":"Such benchmarks may measure the body, but not necessarily intelligence.","zh":"這些基準可能量度身體，但未必量度智力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to bodily measures used as comparison points.","zh":"這個短語指用作比較點的身體量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"The tests measured the body rather than the mind itself.","zh":"這些測驗量度身體，而不是心智本身。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of, and it creates a contrast.","zh":"rather than 是指「而不是」，用來製造對比。"},{"en":"A student should answer the question directly rather than write everything they know.","zh":"學生應直接回答題目，而不是寫下自己知道的一切。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate the real focus from the rejected one.","zh":"這個短語幫助把真正焦點與被排除的焦點分開。"},{"en":"It is useful when correcting a misunderstanding.","zh":"它適合用來修正誤解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"testing of the mind itself","meaning":"對心智能力本身的測試","examples":[{"en":"The early procedures did not involve direct testing of the mind itself.","zh":"早期程序並不涉及對心智能力本身的直接測試。"},{"en":"Testing of the mind itself means directly assessing mental ability or thought processes.","zh":"對心智能力本身的測試，是指直接評估心智能力或思考過程。"},{"en":"A reasoning test is closer to testing the mind itself than measuring height.","zh":"推理測驗比量度身高更接近對心智能力本身的測試。"},{"en":"Without direct mental tasks, a test may not truly measure intelligence.","zh":"如果沒有直接心智任務，測驗未必真正量度智力。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts mental testing with physical measurement.","zh":"這個短語把心智測試與身體測量作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"physical power","meaning":"體力","examples":[{"en":"Galton recorded the physical power of his subjects.","zh":"Galton 記錄受試者的體力。"},{"en":"Physical power means bodily strength or physical force.","zh":"體力是指身體力量或身體發力能力。"},{"en":"A sports coach may measure a player’s physical power through jumping or lifting tests.","zh":"運動教練可能透過跳躍或舉重測驗量度運動員體力。"},{"en":"Physical power may help in sport, but it does not prove intelligence.","zh":"體力可能有助運動，但不能證明智力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to strength of the body.","zh":"這個短語指身體力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"height and weight","meaning":"身高和體重","examples":[{"en":"The measurements included the subjects’ height and weight.","zh":"這些測量包括受試者的身高和體重。"},{"en":"Height and weight are basic physical measurements of body size.","zh":"身高和體重是身體大小的基本身體量度。"},{"en":"A nurse may record a child’s height and weight during a health check.","zh":"護士可能在健康檢查中記錄孩子的身高和體重。"},{"en":"These measurements can describe the body but not the whole person.","zh":"這些量度可以描述身體，但不能描述整個人。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to simple body-size data.","zh":"這個短語指簡單的身體大小資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be recorded","meaning":"被記錄","examples":[{"en":"The subjects’ physical measurements were carefully recorded.","zh":"受試者的身體測量被仔細記錄。"},{"en":"To be recorded means to be written down, stored or officially noted.","zh":"被記錄，是指被寫下、儲存或正式記下。"},{"en":"A student’s attendance is recorded every morning.","zh":"學生出席率每天早上都會被記錄。"},{"en":"Recording data helps researchers check and compare results later.","zh":"記錄數據有助研究人員日後檢查和比較結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping information for future use.","zh":"這個短語描述保存資訊以供日後使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be used to estimate","meaning":"被用來估計……","examples":[{"en":"The physical results were used to estimate intelligence.","zh":"身體結果被用來估計智力。"},{"en":"To be used to estimate something means to help make an approximate judgement about it.","zh":"被用來估計某事，是指幫助對某事作出近似判斷。"},{"en":"Past test scores may be used to estimate a student’s future performance.","zh":"過往測驗分數可能被用來估計學生未來表現。"},{"en":"Estimates are not perfect because they depend on the data chosen.","zh":"估計並不完美，因為它取決於所選數據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using evidence to make an approximate assessment.","zh":"這個短語描述用證據作出近似評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"intelligence of subjects","meaning":"受試者的智力","examples":[{"en":"The researcher attempted to estimate the intelligence of the subjects.","zh":"研究人員嘗試估計受試者的智力。"},{"en":"Intelligence of subjects means the mental ability of the people being tested.","zh":"受試者的智力是指接受測驗者的心智能力。"},{"en":"A study may compare the intelligence of subjects using reasoning tasks.","zh":"研究可能使用推理任務比較受試者的智力。"},{"en":"If the test is poorly designed, it may misjudge the subjects’ intelligence.","zh":"如果測驗設計不良，可能會誤判受試者的智力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the test-takers’ intellectual ability.","zh":"這個短語指測驗對象的智力能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"while the approach was not successful","meaning":"雖然這種方法並不成功","examples":[{"en":"While the approach was not successful, it influenced later research.","zh":"雖然這種方法並不成功，它仍影響後來研究。"},{"en":"This phrase means although the method failed, it still had some effect.","zh":"這個短語表示雖然方法失敗，但仍有某種影響。"},{"en":"While the class activity was not successful, it gave the teacher useful feedback.","zh":"雖然課堂活動並不成功，它給了老師有用回饋。"},{"en":"Failed attempts can still guide future improvements.","zh":"失敗嘗試仍可以指導未來改良。"},{"en":"This structure balances failure with later value.","zh":"這個結構把失敗與後來價值並列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"studies conducted by","meaning":"由……進行的研究","examples":[{"en":"The studies conducted by Galton influenced later researchers.","zh":"由 Galton 進行的研究影響了後來研究人員。"},{"en":"Studies conducted by someone are studies carried out by that person.","zh":"由某人進行的研究，是該人執行的研究。"},{"en":"Studies conducted by a university may examine students’ sleep habits.","zh":"由大學進行的研究可能調查學生睡眠習慣。"},{"en":"Who conducts a study matters because methods and aims may differ.","zh":"由誰進行研究很重要，因為方法和目的可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the researcher responsible for the work.","zh":"這個短語指出負責研究的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"influence the work of","meaning":"影響……的研究工作","examples":[{"en":"Galton’s research influenced the work of future scientists.","zh":"Galton 的研究影響了後來科學家的研究工作。"},{"en":"To influence the work of someone means to affect how that person studies, thinks or creates.","zh":"影響某人的工作，是指影響那人如何研究、思考或創作。"},{"en":"A good teacher can influence the work of young writers.","zh":"好老師可以影響年輕作者的寫作工作。"},{"en":"Early research may influence later work even when its conclusions are wrong.","zh":"早期研究即使結論錯誤，也可能影響後來研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intellectual impact.","zh":"這個短語描述思想上的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"future researchers","meaning":"後來的研究人員","examples":[{"en":"Future researchers developed more direct ways of assessing intelligence.","zh":"後來的研究人員發展出更直接評估智力的方法。"},{"en":"Future researchers means the researchers who came later.","zh":"後來的研究人員是指較後出現的研究者。"},{"en":"Future researchers may use today’s data to answer new questions.","zh":"後來的研究人員可能使用今天的數據回答新問題。"},{"en":"Later researchers often improve on earlier methods.","zh":"後來研究者通常會改良早期方法。"},{"en":"This phrase places research in a timeline.","zh":"這個短語把研究放在時間線中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"approaches to the measurement of","meaning":"量度……的方法","examples":[{"en":"New approaches to the measurement of intelligence were later developed.","zh":"後來發展出量度智力的新方法。"},{"en":"Approaches to the measurement of something are methods for assessing it.","zh":"量度某事的方法是評估它的方式。"},{"en":"Schools use different approaches to the measurement of reading ability.","zh":"學校使用不同方法量度閱讀能力。"},{"en":"Better approaches can make assessment more accurate and useful.","zh":"更好的方法可以令評估更準確和有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ways of measuring a quality.","zh":"這個短語描述量度某種特質的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be defined as","meaning":"被定義為……","examples":[{"en":"Intelligence can be defined as the mind’s ability to reason and learn.","zh":"智力可以被定義為心智推理和學習的能力。"},{"en":"To be defined as something means to be explained by that meaning.","zh":"被定義為某事，是指以該意思來解釋。"},{"en":"A noun can be defined as a word that names a person, place or thing.","zh":"名詞可以被定義為命名人、地方或事物的詞。"},{"en":"Definitions help readers know exactly how a term is being used.","zh":"定義幫助讀者知道術語如何被使用。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a formal meaning.","zh":"這個短語引入正式意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"relative ability to","meaning":"……的相對能力","examples":[{"en":"Intelligence concerns the mind’s relative ability to solve problems.","zh":"智力關乎心智解決問題的相對能力。"},{"en":"Relative ability to do something means how well someone can do it compared with others or other tasks.","zh":"做某事的相對能力，是指與其他人或其他任務相比能做得多好。"},{"en":"A student’s relative ability to speak may be stronger than their writing.","zh":"學生的口語相對能力可能比寫作更強。"},{"en":"Relative ability helps show strengths and weaknesses.","zh":"相對能力有助顯示強項和弱項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ability in comparison.","zh":"這個短語描述比較中的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reason and think","meaning":"推理和思考","examples":[{"en":"Intelligence includes the ability to reason and think clearly.","zh":"智力包括清楚推理和思考的能力。"},{"en":"To reason and think means to use logic and understanding to make sense of something.","zh":"推理和思考是指使用邏輯和理解來明白事情。"},{"en":"Students must reason and think when solving a difficult maths problem.","zh":"學生解決困難數學題時必須推理和思考。"},{"en":"Clear reasoning helps people avoid guessing blindly.","zh":"清晰推理幫助人避免盲目猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes logical mental activity.","zh":"這個短語描述合乎邏輯的心智活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"plan conceptually","meaning":"以概念方式作出規劃","examples":[{"en":"An intelligent person may be able to plan conceptually.","zh":"有智力的人可能能夠以概念方式作出規劃。"},{"en":"To plan conceptually means to plan using ideas, principles and abstract relationships.","zh":"以概念方式規劃，是指使用想法、原則和抽象關係來計劃。"},{"en":"A project leader may plan conceptually before writing detailed tasks.","zh":"項目負責人可能先以概念方式規劃，再寫出詳細任務。"},{"en":"Conceptual planning helps people see the big picture before acting.","zh":"概念式規劃幫助人在行動前看見整體圖像。"},{"en":"This phrase describes idea-based planning.","zh":"這個短語描述以想法為本的規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"solve problems","meaning":"解決問題","examples":[{"en":"Psychometric tests often assess the ability to solve problems.","zh":"心理計量測驗經常評估解決問題的能力。"},{"en":"To solve problems means to find answers or workable solutions.","zh":"解決問題是指找出答案或可行方案。"},{"en":"A student solves problems when they work out why an experiment failed.","zh":"學生弄清實驗為何失敗時，就是在解決問題。"},{"en":"Strong problem-solving ability helps people adapt to new situations.","zh":"強大的解難能力幫助人適應新情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dealing successfully with difficulties.","zh":"這個短語描述成功處理困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"understand and learn","meaning":"理解和學習","examples":[{"en":"Intelligence includes the capacity to understand and learn.","zh":"智力包括理解和學習的能力。"},{"en":"To understand and learn means to grasp information and use it later.","zh":"理解和學習是指掌握資訊並在之後使用。"},{"en":"A child understands and learns when they can explain a new rule in their own words.","zh":"孩子能用自己的話解釋新規則時，就是在理解和學習。"},{"en":"Learning becomes deeper when understanding comes before memorisation.","zh":"當理解先於記憶，學習會更深入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving and making sense of knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述接收並理解知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be developed by pioneers such as","meaning":"由……等先驅發展","examples":[{"en":"Later approaches were developed by pioneers such as Charles Spearman.","zh":"後來的方法由 Charles Spearman 等先驅發展。"},{"en":"Developed by pioneers such as someone means created by early important figures in a field.","zh":"由某人等先驅發展，是指由某領域早期重要人物創立。"},{"en":"Early computer ideas were developed by pioneers such as Alan Turing.","zh":"早期電腦思想由 Alan Turing 等先驅發展。"},{"en":"Naming pioneers shows whose work shaped the field.","zh":"提及先驅可顯示誰的工作塑造了該領域。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces influential early developers.","zh":"這個短語引入具影響力的早期發展者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"significant contributions","meaning":"重大貢獻","examples":[{"en":"Several psychologists made significant contributions to psychometrics.","zh":"多位心理學家對心理計量學作出重大貢獻。"},{"en":"Significant contributions are important additions that help a field develop.","zh":"重大貢獻是幫助一個領域發展的重要加入。"},{"en":"A student may make a significant contribution to a group project by organising the data.","zh":"學生透過整理數據，可能對小組專題作出重大貢獻。"},{"en":"Contributions matter when they change methods, ideas or results.","zh":"當貢獻改變方法、想法或結果，它就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaningful input or achievement.","zh":"這個短語描述有意義的投入或成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"early development","meaning":"早期發展","examples":[{"en":"Many researchers contributed to the early development of intelligence testing.","zh":"許多研究人員對智力測驗的早期發展作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Early development means the first stages of growth or formation.","zh":"早期發展是成長或形成的最初階段。"},{"en":"Parents support a child’s early development through language, play and care.","zh":"父母透過語言、遊戲和照顧支持孩子早期發展。"},{"en":"Early development shapes what a system later becomes.","zh":"早期發展塑造一個系統日後變成甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the beginning phase of something.","zh":"這個短語指某事的初期階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"most well-known traditional approach","meaning":"最廣為人知的傳統方法","examples":[{"en":"The Stanford-Binet test is a well-known traditional approach.","zh":"史丹福—比奈測驗是廣為人知的傳統方法。"},{"en":"The most well-known traditional approach is the familiar older method most people recognise.","zh":"最廣為人知的傳統方法，是大多數人認識的熟悉舊方法。"},{"en":"In language learning, dictation is a well-known traditional approach.","zh":"在語言學習中，默書是廣為人知的傳統方法。"},{"en":"Traditional approaches may remain important because they influenced later methods.","zh":"傳統方法可能仍然重要，因為它們影響後來方法。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a famous older method.","zh":"這個短語指出著名的舊方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"development of psychometric instruments","meaning":"心理計量工具的發展","examples":[{"en":"Researchers developed psychometric instruments to measure intelligence.","zh":"研究人員發展心理計量工具來量度智力。"},{"en":"Development of psychometric instruments means creating tools for psychological measurement.","zh":"心理計量工具的發展，是指建立心理量度工具。"},{"en":"A university may develop a questionnaire to measure exam anxiety.","zh":"大學可能發展問卷來量度考試焦慮。"},{"en":"Better instruments can make assessment more accurate.","zh":"更好的工具可以令評估更準確。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to building tools for mental testing.","zh":"這個短語指建立心智測驗工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"measure intelligence","meaning":"量度智力","examples":[{"en":"The Stanford-Binet test was designed to measure intelligence.","zh":"史丹福—比奈測驗被設計用來量度智力。"},{"en":"To measure intelligence means to assess mental ability through tasks or tests.","zh":"量度智力是指透過任務或測驗評估心智能力。"},{"en":"A reasoning test may measure intelligence by asking students to solve patterns.","zh":"推理測驗可能透過要求學生解決圖案題來量度智力。"},{"en":"Measuring intelligence is difficult because intelligence has many aspects.","zh":"量度智力很困難，因為智力有很多方面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal assessment of intellectual ability.","zh":"這個短語描述對智力能力的正式評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Stanford-Binet IQ test","meaning":"史丹福—比奈智力測驗","examples":[{"en":"The Stanford-Binet IQ test remains historically important.","zh":"史丹福—比奈智力測驗在歷史上仍然重要。"},{"en":"The Stanford-Binet IQ test is a traditional intelligence test developed from Binet’s work.","zh":"史丹福—比奈智力測驗是由 Binet 研究發展而來的傳統智力測驗。"},{"en":"Psychology students may study the Stanford-Binet IQ test as part of testing history.","zh":"心理學學生可能把史丹福—比奈智力測驗作為測驗史的一部分來學習。"},{"en":"Its importance comes from its role in shaping later intelligence testing.","zh":"它的重要性來自它對後來智力測驗的塑造。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major historical IQ test.","zh":"這個短語命名一項重要的歷史智商測驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"originally developed by","meaning":"最初由……研發","examples":[{"en":"The test was originally developed by Alfred Binet.","zh":"這項測驗最初由 Alfred Binet 研發。"},{"en":"Originally developed by someone means first created by that person.","zh":"最初由某人研發，是指最早由那人創造。"},{"en":"A school app may be originally developed by a group of teachers.","zh":"學校應用程式可能最初由一群老師研發。"},{"en":"Later versions may change, but the original developer remains important.","zh":"後來版本可能改變，但最初研發者仍然重要。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the first creator.","zh":"這個短語指出最初創造者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"French psychologist","meaning":"法國心理學家","examples":[{"en":"Alfred Binet was a French psychologist.","zh":"Alfred Binet 是法國心理學家。"},{"en":"A French psychologist is a psychologist from France.","zh":"法國心理學家是來自法國的心理學家。"},{"en":"A French psychologist may study learning, memory or child development.","zh":"法國心理學家可能研究學習、記憶或兒童發展。"},{"en":"Mentioning nationality can help place a researcher historically and culturally.","zh":"提及國籍有助把研究者放在歷史和文化背景中。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both profession and origin.","zh":"這個短語同時指出職業和來源地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"define intelligence as separate from","meaning":"將智力界定為有別於……","examples":[{"en":"Researchers define intelligence as separate from personality and character.","zh":"研究人員將智力界定為有別於性格和品格。"},{"en":"To define A as separate from B means to treat A as different from B.","zh":"將 A 界定為有別於 B，是指把 A 視為不同於 B。"},{"en":"A teacher may define effort as separate from natural talent.","zh":"老師可能將努力界定為有別於天賦。"},{"en":"Separating ideas helps assessment focus on one quality at a time.","zh":"分開概念有助評估一次聚焦一種特質。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a boundary between concepts.","zh":"這個短語顯示概念之間的界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"other attributes","meaning":"其他特質","examples":[{"en":"Intelligence is assessed separately from certain other attributes.","zh":"智力與某些其他特質分開評估。"},{"en":"Other attributes are other qualities or characteristics a person has.","zh":"其他特質是指一個人擁有的其他品質或特徵。"},{"en":"Confidence, patience and creativity are other attributes that may affect performance.","zh":"自信、耐性和創造力都是可能影響表現的其他特質。"},{"en":"A test may focus on one attribute while ignoring others.","zh":"測驗可能聚焦一項特質，而忽略其他特質。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to additional personal qualities.","zh":"這個短語指額外的個人品質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"personality and character","meaning":"性格和品格","examples":[{"en":"Personality and character are not identical to intelligence.","zh":"性格和品格不等同於智力。"},{"en":"Personality and character mean a person’s typical behaviour, values and moral qualities.","zh":"性格和品格是指一個人的典型行為、價值觀和道德品質。"},{"en":"A student may have strong character even if they find exams difficult.","zh":"即使學生覺得考試困難，也可能有堅強品格。"},{"en":"Intelligence tests do not fully measure kindness, honesty or courage.","zh":"智力測驗不能完全量度善良、誠實或勇氣。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to personal and moral qualities.","zh":"這個短語指個人和道德品質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"creativity","meaning":"創造力","examples":[{"en":"Creativity is often treated as distinct from general intelligence.","zh":"創造力通常被視為有別於一般智力。"},{"en":"Creativity means the ability to produce original or imaginative ideas.","zh":"創造力是指產生原創或富想像力想法的能力。"},{"en":"A student shows creativity when they design a new solution for a school project.","zh":"學生為學校專題設計新解決方案時，就展現創造力。"},{"en":"Creative ability may not always appear in a standard IQ test.","zh":"創造能力未必總能在標準智商測驗中出現。"},{"en":"This word describes the power to create something new.","zh":"這個詞描述創造新事物的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"knowledge and wisdom","meaning":"知識和智慧","examples":[{"en":"Knowledge and wisdom are not necessarily the same as intelligence.","zh":"知識和智慧不一定等同於智力。"},{"en":"Knowledge is information, while wisdom is good judgement from experience.","zh":"知識是資訊，而智慧是來自經驗的良好判斷。"},{"en":"A person may know many facts but still make unwise decisions.","zh":"一個人可能知道很多事實，但仍作出不明智決定。"},{"en":"Intelligence tests may measure reasoning more than life experience.","zh":"智力測驗可能更多量度推理，而不是人生經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase separates information, judgement and mental ability.","zh":"這個短語區分資訊、判斷和心智能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for the purpose of assessment","meaning":"為了進行評估","examples":[{"en":"These qualities are separated for the purpose of assessment.","zh":"這些品質為了進行評估而被分開。"},{"en":"For the purpose of assessment means in order to evaluate something clearly.","zh":"為了進行評估，是指為了清楚評價某事。"},{"en":"Teachers may separate grammar and content for the purpose of assessment.","zh":"老師可能為了進行評估而把文法和內容分開。"},{"en":"Separating categories makes marking easier and more focused.","zh":"分開類別令評分更容易、更聚焦。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a distinction is made.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何作出區分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be intended to determine","meaning":"旨在確定……","examples":[{"en":"IQ tests are not intended to determine purely genetic intelligence.","zh":"智商測驗並非旨在確定純粹遺傳智力。"},{"en":"To be intended to determine something means to be designed to find it out.","zh":"旨在確定某事，是指被設計來找出它。"},{"en":"A placement test is intended to determine a student’s class level.","zh":"分班試旨在確定學生的班級水平。"},{"en":"If a test is not designed for a purpose, it should not be judged by that purpose.","zh":"如果測驗不是為某目的而設計，就不應用該目的評價它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the aim of a test or method.","zh":"這個短語描述測驗或方法的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"level of genetic intelligence","meaning":"遺傳智力水平","examples":[{"en":"Tests cannot isolate a person’s level of genetic intelligence completely.","zh":"測驗不能完全分離一個人的遺傳智力水平。"},{"en":"Level of genetic intelligence means the amount of intelligence assumed to come from inherited factors.","zh":"遺傳智力水平是指被認為來自遺傳因素的智力程度。"},{"en":"No school exam can measure only the level of genetic intelligence.","zh":"沒有學校考試能只量度遺傳智力水平。"},{"en":"Environment, education and health also affect performance.","zh":"環境、教育和健康也會影響表現。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to inherited intellectual potential.","zh":"這個短語指遺傳而來的智力潛能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"separate from and unaffected by","meaning":"與……分開且不受……影響","examples":[{"en":"Intelligence cannot easily be separated from and unaffected by environment.","zh":"智力不容易與環境分開且不受環境影響。"},{"en":"Separate from and unaffected by means independent of something and not influenced by it.","zh":"與某事分開且不受其影響，是指獨立於它，而且不被它影響。"},{"en":"A student’s result is rarely separate from and unaffected by sleep, stress and preparation.","zh":"學生成績很少能與睡眠、壓力和準備分開且不受其影響。"},{"en":"If many factors influence performance, pure separation is difficult.","zh":"如果許多因素影響表現，純粹分離就很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses independence and lack of influence.","zh":"這個短語強調獨立和不受影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"environment to which someone is exposed","meaning":"某人所接觸的環境","examples":[{"en":"Development is influenced by the environment to which a person is exposed.","zh":"發展受一個人所接觸的環境影響。"},{"en":"The environment to which someone is exposed means the surroundings and experiences they encounter.","zh":"某人所接觸的環境，是指他遇到的周圍條件和經驗。"},{"en":"A child exposed to many books may develop stronger reading habits.","zh":"接觸許多書籍的孩子可能發展出較強閱讀習慣。"},{"en":"Different environments can shape learning, confidence and behaviour.","zh":"不同環境可以塑造學習、信心和行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the conditions a person experiences.","zh":"這個短語描述一個人經歷的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"during life","meaning":"一生之中","examples":[{"en":"People are exposed to many environmental influences during life.","zh":"人們一生之中會接觸許多環境影響。"},{"en":"During life means throughout a person’s lifetime.","zh":"一生之中，是指貫穿一個人的生命期間。"},{"en":"People may change careers several times during life.","zh":"人一生之中可能多次轉換職業。"},{"en":"Experiences during life can shape ability and personality.","zh":"一生之中的經驗可以塑造能力和性格。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the whole period of living.","zh":"這個短語指整個生命時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rather, to measure","meaning":"而是量度……","examples":[{"en":"The aim is not to isolate nature, but rather to measure actual performance.","zh":"目的不是分離先天因素，而是量度實際表現。"},{"en":"Rather, to measure means instead, the real aim is to measure.","zh":"而是量度，是指真正目的反而是進行量度。"},{"en":"The test is not meant to punish students, but rather to measure progress.","zh":"測驗不是為了懲罰學生，而是量度進步。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects one aim and replaces it with another.","zh":"這個短語修正一個目的，並用另一個目的取代。"},{"en":"It clarifies the true purpose of an action.","zh":"它澄清行動的真正目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"apparent as a result of","meaning":"作為……的結果而顯現","examples":[{"en":"A person’s intelligence is apparent as a result of many influences.","zh":"一個人的智力作為許多影響的結果而顯現。"},{"en":"Apparent as a result of something means visible or noticeable because of it.","zh":"作為某事的結果而顯現，是指因它而變得可見或可察覺。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may become apparent as a result of repeated practice.","zh":"學生的信心可能作為反覆練習的結果而顯現。"},{"en":"When many influences combine, the final ability becomes visible in performance.","zh":"當許多影響結合，最終能力會在表現中變得可見。"},{"en":"This phrase links an observed quality to its causes.","zh":"這個短語把被觀察到的特質與其原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"nature and nurture","meaning":"先天與後天因素","examples":[{"en":"Intelligence develops through both nature and nurture.","zh":"智力透過先天與後天因素共同發展。"},{"en":"Nature and nurture mean inherited factors and environmental influences.","zh":"先天與後天因素是指遺傳因素和環境影響。"},{"en":"A child’s language ability may reflect both nature and nurture.","zh":"孩子的語言能力可能同時反映先天與後天因素。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that development is rarely caused by one factor only.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，發展很少只由單一因素造成。"},{"en":"It contrasts what we are born with and what we experience.","zh":"它對比與生俱來的東西和後天經歷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"useful and widely used tool","meaning":"有用且廣泛採用的工具","examples":[{"en":"Psychometrics is a useful and widely used assessment tool.","zh":"心理計量學是有用且廣泛採用的評估工具。"},{"en":"A useful and widely used tool is something helpful and commonly adopted.","zh":"有用且廣泛採用的工具，是有幫助並被普遍使用的東西。"},{"en":"Online quizzes are a useful and widely used tool for vocabulary review.","zh":"網上小測是詞彙溫習中有用且廣泛採用的工具。"},{"en":"Tools become widely used when they solve common problems well.","zh":"當工具能有效解決常見問題，它就會被廣泛採用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something both practical and common.","zh":"這個短語描述既實用又常見的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"measurement of abilities","meaning":"能力的量度","examples":[{"en":"Psychometric tests support the measurement of abilities.","zh":"心理計量測驗支援能力的量度。"},{"en":"Measurement of abilities means assessing what people can do.","zh":"能力的量度，是指評估人們能做甚麼。"},{"en":"A music audition measures abilities such as rhythm and listening.","zh":"音樂試音會量度節奏和聆聽等能力。"},{"en":"Measuring abilities helps match people with suitable support or roles.","zh":"量度能力有助把人配對到合適支援或角色。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to evaluating skills and capacities.","zh":"這個短語指評估技能和能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"academic areas","meaning":"學術範疇","examples":[{"en":"Tests may assess ability in several academic areas.","zh":"測驗可能評估幾個學術範疇中的能力。"},{"en":"Academic areas are school or study subjects.","zh":"學術範疇是學校或學習科目。"},{"en":"Reading, science and mathematics are academic areas.","zh":"閱讀、科學和數學都是學術範疇。"},{"en":"A student may be strong in one academic area but weaker in another.","zh":"學生可能在一個學術範疇較強，而在另一個較弱。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to areas of formal learning.","zh":"這個短語指正式學習範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reading, writing and mathematics","meaning":"閱讀、寫作和數學","examples":[{"en":"Psychometrics is used to measure reading, writing and mathematics skills.","zh":"心理計量學被用來量度閱讀、寫作和數學能力。"},{"en":"Reading, writing and mathematics are core academic skills.","zh":"閱讀、寫作和數學是核心學術技能。"},{"en":"A school placement test may assess reading, writing and mathematics.","zh":"學校分班試可能評估閱讀、寫作和數學。"},{"en":"Weakness in one of these skills can affect many school subjects.","zh":"其中一項技能薄弱，可能影響許多學科。"},{"en":"This phrase names three basic learning areas.","zh":"這個短語命名三個基本學習範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"commonly used to test","meaning":"通常被用來測試……","examples":[{"en":"IQ tests are commonly used to test intelligence.","zh":"智商測驗通常被用來測試智力。"},{"en":"Commonly used to test means often used for assessment.","zh":"通常被用來測試，是指經常用於評估。"},{"en":"Spelling quizzes are commonly used to test vocabulary learning.","zh":"拼字小測通常被用來測試詞彙學習。"},{"en":"A common test is familiar, but it may still have limitations.","zh":"常見測驗雖然熟悉，但仍可能有限制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frequent use in assessment.","zh":"這個短語描述在評估中的頻繁使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be unfair","meaning":"不公平","examples":[{"en":"Some critics believe that conventional intelligence testing is unfair.","zh":"有些批評者認為傳統智力測驗不公平。"},{"en":"To be unfair means to treat people in a way that is not equal or reasonable.","zh":"不公平是指以不平等或不合理方式對待人。"},{"en":"A test may be unfair if some students were not taught the material.","zh":"如果有些學生未學過測驗內容，測驗可能不公平。"},{"en":"Unfair assessment can misrepresent a person’s true ability.","zh":"不公平評估可能錯誤呈現一個人的真實能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lack of fairness.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏公平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not truly representative of","meaning":"未能真正代表……","examples":[{"en":"A single test may not be truly representative of a person’s intellect.","zh":"單一測驗可能未能真正代表一個人的智力。"},{"en":"Not truly representative of something means not accurately showing the whole thing.","zh":"未能真正代表某事，是指未能準確顯示整體。"},{"en":"One bad essay is not truly representative of a student’s writing ability.","zh":"一篇差作文未必真正代表學生的寫作能力。"},{"en":"A narrow test may miss hidden strengths.","zh":"狹窄測驗可能忽略隱藏強項。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that one result may not show the full picture.","zh":"這個短語提醒一個結果未必顯示全貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"subject’s intellect","meaning":"受試者的智力","examples":[{"en":"The score may not reflect the subject’s complete intellect.","zh":"分數可能未能反映受試者完整的智力。"},{"en":"Subject’s intellect means the mental ability of the person being tested.","zh":"受試者的智力，是指接受測驗者的心智能力。"},{"en":"A quiet student’s intellect may not be obvious in a timed oral test.","zh":"安靜學生的智力未必在限時口試中明顯呈現。"},{"en":"A score can show part of intellect but not necessarily all of it.","zh":"分數可以顯示部分智力，但未必顯示全部。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the test-taker’s intellectual capacity.","zh":"這個短語指測驗對象的智力能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"excel in different areas","meaning":"在不同範疇表現出色","examples":[{"en":"Different individuals may excel in different areas of reasoning.","zh":"不同個人可能在不同推理範疇表現出色。"},{"en":"To excel in different areas means to be very good at different types of tasks.","zh":"在不同範疇表現出色，是指非常擅長不同類型任務。"},{"en":"One student may excel in writing, while another excels in mathematics.","zh":"一名學生可能擅長寫作，而另一名擅長數學。"},{"en":"Because strengths differ, one test may not suit everyone equally.","zh":"由於強項不同，一項測驗未必同樣適合所有人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes varied strengths.","zh":"這個短語描述多樣化強項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"areas of reasoning","meaning":"推理範疇","examples":[{"en":"People may have strengths in different areas of reasoning.","zh":"人們可能在不同推理範疇有強項。"},{"en":"Areas of reasoning are types of thinking, such as verbal, logical or spatial thinking.","zh":"推理範疇是不同思考類型，例如語言、邏輯或空間思考。"},{"en":"A puzzle test may assess one area of reasoning more than another.","zh":"謎題測驗可能比其他範疇更多評估某一推理範疇。"},{"en":"Different reasoning areas explain why students solve problems in different ways.","zh":"不同推理範疇解釋了為何學生以不同方式解題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to categories of thinking ability.","zh":"這個短語指思考能力的類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"work on the assumption that","meaning":"基於……的假設進行研究","examples":[{"en":"Gardner worked on the assumption that intelligence has multiple forms.","zh":"Gardner 基於智力有多種形式的假設進行研究。"},{"en":"To work on the assumption that something is true means to base your thinking on that belief.","zh":"基於某事為真的假設進行，是指把思考建立在該信念上。"},{"en":"A teacher may plan on the assumption that students have read the chapter.","zh":"老師可能基於學生已讀該章的假設來設計課堂。"},{"en":"If the assumption is wrong, the plan may need to change.","zh":"如果假設錯誤，計劃可能需要改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the belief behind an approach.","zh":"這個短語描述某種方法背後的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"introduce the concept of","meaning":"引入……的概念","examples":[{"en":"Gardner introduced the concept of an individual cognitive profile.","zh":"Gardner 引入個人認知能力組合的概念。"},{"en":"To introduce the concept of something means to present a new idea for discussion.","zh":"引入某概念，是指提出一個新想法供討論。"},{"en":"A science teacher may introduce the concept of energy conservation.","zh":"科學老師可能引入能量守恆的概念。"},{"en":"Introducing a concept gives people a new way to understand a topic.","zh":"引入概念能給人理解主題的新方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bringing an idea into use.","zh":"這個短語描述把一個想法帶入使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"individual cognitive profile","meaning":"個人認知能力組合","examples":[{"en":"Each person may have a distinctive individual cognitive profile.","zh":"每個人可能有獨特的個人認知能力組合。"},{"en":"An individual cognitive profile is a person’s unique pattern of mental strengths and weaknesses.","zh":"個人認知能力組合是一個人獨特的心智強弱模式。"},{"en":"A student may have strong verbal skills but weaker spatial skills.","zh":"學生可能語言能力強，但空間能力較弱。"},{"en":"Understanding a cognitive profile can help teachers choose better support.","zh":"理解認知能力組合可以幫助老師選擇更好支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a person’s mental ability pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述一個人的心智能力模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Frames of Mind","meaning":"《心智架構》","examples":[{"en":"Gardner introduced his theory in the book Frames of Mind.","zh":"Gardner 在《心智架構》一書中提出他的理論。"},{"en":"Frames of Mind is the title of Gardner’s book on multiple intelligences.","zh":"《心智架構》是 Gardner 關於多元智能的書名。"},{"en":"A psychology student may read Frames of Mind to understand Gardner’s theory.","zh":"心理學學生可能閱讀《心智架構》來理解 Gardner 的理論。"},{"en":"Book titles often mark where major theories were first presented.","zh":"書名通常標示重要理論首次提出的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase names the work connected with the theory.","zh":"這個短語命名與該理論相關的作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Theory of Multiple Intelligences","meaning":"多元智能理論","examples":[{"en":"The Theory of Multiple Intelligences proposes several forms of ability.","zh":"多元智能理論提出幾種能力形式。"},{"en":"This theory says intelligence is not one single ability.","zh":"這個理論認為智力不是單一能力。"},{"en":"A teacher using this theory may value music, movement and social skills as well as maths.","zh":"使用這理論的老師可能重視音樂、動作和社交能力，也重視數學。"},{"en":"It challenges tests that focus too narrowly on one kind of intelligence.","zh":"它挑戰只狹窄聚焦一種智力的測驗。"},{"en":"This phrase names Gardner’s theory of varied intelligences.","zh":"這個短語命名 Gardner 關於多種智能的理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hold that","meaning":"認為；主張","examples":[{"en":"Gardner holds that people can show different patterns of intelligence.","zh":"Gardner 認為人們可以展現不同智力模式。"},{"en":"To hold that something is true means to believe or argue it.","zh":"hold that 是指相信或主張某事為真。"},{"en":"Some teachers hold that feedback is more useful than grades alone.","zh":"有些老師認為回饋比單純分數更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces someone’s view or claim.","zh":"這個短語引入某人的觀點或主張。"},{"en":"It is common in academic writing.","zh":"它常見於學術寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"perform excellently in","meaning":"在……表現出色","examples":[{"en":"A child may perform excellently in one intellectual area.","zh":"孩子可能在某一智力範疇表現出色。"},{"en":"To perform excellently in something means to do extremely well in that area.","zh":"在某方面表現出色，是指在該範疇做得非常好。"},{"en":"A student may perform excellently in music but struggle with grammar.","zh":"學生可能在音樂方面表現出色，但文法較弱。"},{"en":"Excellent performance can reveal a specific strength.","zh":"出色表現可以揭示特定強項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes outstanding ability in a field.","zh":"這個短語描述某領域中的優秀能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"one aspect","meaning":"某一方面","examples":[{"en":"A person may succeed in one aspect but struggle in another.","zh":"一個人可能在某一方面成功，但在另一方面困難。"},{"en":"One aspect means one part or side of a larger subject.","zh":"某一方面是較大主題中的一個部分或面向。"},{"en":"A student may be strong in one aspect of English, such as speaking.","zh":"學生可能在英語某一方面很強，例如口語。"},{"en":"Looking at one aspect alone may give an incomplete judgement.","zh":"只看某一方面可能得出不完整判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to one part of a whole.","zh":"這個短語指整體中的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"yet fail in another","meaning":"但在另一方面表現欠佳","examples":[{"en":"A child may excel in language yet fail in another area.","zh":"孩子可能在語言方面出色，但在另一方面表現欠佳。"},{"en":"Yet fail in another means do well in one area but poorly in a different one.","zh":"但在另一方面表現欠佳，是指一方面做得好，另一不同方面做得差。"},{"en":"A student may write beautifully yet fail in timed grammar tasks.","zh":"學生可能寫作優美，但在限時文法題表現欠佳。"},{"en":"This contrast shows why one score may not tell the whole story.","zh":"這種對比顯示單一分數未必說明全貌。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights uneven performance.","zh":"這個短語突出表現不均。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"overall performance","meaning":"整體表現","examples":[{"en":"The child’s overall performance should be considered.","zh":"應該考慮孩子的整體表現。"},{"en":"Overall performance means the full pattern of results across different areas.","zh":"整體表現是指不同範疇結果的完整模式。"},{"en":"A teacher looks at tests, homework and participation to judge overall performance.","zh":"老師會看測驗、功課和參與度來判斷整體表現。"},{"en":"Considering overall performance prevents one weak area from defining the whole person.","zh":"考慮整體表現可避免一項弱點定義整個人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes performance as a whole.","zh":"這個短語描述整體而言的表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a number of intellectual areas","meaning":"多個智力範疇","examples":[{"en":"Assessment should cover a number of intellectual areas.","zh":"評估應涵蓋多個智力範疇。"},{"en":"A number of intellectual areas means several kinds of mental ability.","zh":"多個智力範疇是指幾種心智能力類型。"},{"en":"A broad test may include language, logic, memory and spatial tasks.","zh":"廣泛測驗可能包括語言、邏輯、記憶和空間任務。"},{"en":"Covering several areas gives a fuller picture of ability.","zh":"涵蓋多個範疇能更完整呈現能力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to multiple thinking domains.","zh":"這個短語指多種思考領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"identify different types of intelligence","meaning":"辨認不同種類的智能","examples":[{"en":"Gardner initially identified seven different types of intelligence.","zh":"Gardner 最初辨認出七種不同智能。"},{"en":"To identify different types of intelligence means to name and separate forms of ability.","zh":"辨認不同種類的智能，是指命名並區分不同能力形式。"},{"en":"A teacher may identify different types of strength in a class.","zh":"老師可能辨認班上不同種類的強項。"},{"en":"Identifying types helps people see ability beyond one single score.","zh":"辨認類型幫助人們看見單一分數以外的能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes classifying intelligence into categories.","zh":"這個短語描述把智能分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"linguistic intelligence","meaning":"語言智能","examples":[{"en":"Linguistic intelligence concerns skill in language.","zh":"語言智能關乎語言能力。"},{"en":"Linguistic intelligence is the ability to use words effectively.","zh":"語言智能是有效使用文字和語言的能力。"},{"en":"A student with linguistic intelligence may enjoy writing stories and giving speeches.","zh":"有語言智能的學生可能喜歡寫故事和演講。"},{"en":"Strong language ability can help in teaching, law and journalism.","zh":"強語言能力可以幫助從事教學、法律和新聞工作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to intelligence connected with language.","zh":"這個短語指與語言相關的智能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"logical-mathematical intelligence","meaning":"邏輯數學智能","examples":[{"en":"Logical-mathematical intelligence involves reasoning and calculation.","zh":"邏輯數學智能涉及推理和計算。"},{"en":"Logical-mathematical intelligence is the ability to think logically and work with numbers.","zh":"邏輯數學智能是邏輯思考和處理數字的能力。"},{"en":"A student strong in this area may enjoy puzzles and maths problems.","zh":"這方面強的學生可能喜歡謎題和數學題。"},{"en":"This intelligence can support careers in science, finance and engineering.","zh":"這種智能可以支持科學、金融和工程職業。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to logic-based and number-based ability.","zh":"這個短語指以邏輯和數字為本的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"spatial intelligence","meaning":"空間智能","examples":[{"en":"Spatial intelligence involves visual and spatial judgement.","zh":"空間智能涉及視覺和空間判斷。"},{"en":"Spatial intelligence is the ability to understand shapes, space and visual patterns.","zh":"空間智能是理解形狀、空間和視覺圖案的能力。"},{"en":"A student with spatial intelligence may enjoy maps, drawing and design.","zh":"有空間智能的學生可能喜歡地圖、繪畫和設計。"},{"en":"It helps people imagine how objects fit or move in space.","zh":"它幫助人想像物件如何在空間中配合或移動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to visual-spatial ability.","zh":"這個短語指視覺空間能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bodily-kinesthetic intelligence","meaning":"身體動覺智能","examples":[{"en":"Bodily-kinesthetic intelligence concerns learning through physical action.","zh":"身體動覺智能關乎透過身體動作學習。"},{"en":"Bodily-kinesthetic intelligence is the ability to use the body skilfully.","zh":"身體動覺智能是熟練運用身體的能力。"},{"en":"A dancer or athlete may show strong bodily-kinesthetic intelligence.","zh":"舞者或運動員可能展現強身體動覺智能。"},{"en":"These learners may understand best by doing rather than only reading.","zh":"這類學習者可能透過親身做，而不只是閱讀，理解得最好。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to body-based intelligence.","zh":"這個短語指以身體為本的智能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"musical intelligence","meaning":"音樂智能","examples":[{"en":"Musical intelligence includes sensitivity to rhythm and tone.","zh":"音樂智能包括對節奏和音調的敏感度。"},{"en":"Musical intelligence is the ability to understand and create patterns of sound.","zh":"音樂智能是理解和創造聲音模式的能力。"},{"en":"A student with musical intelligence may learn songs quickly.","zh":"有音樂智能的學生可能很快學會歌曲。"},{"en":"This ability can help in singing, composing and playing instruments.","zh":"這種能力可以幫助唱歌、作曲和演奏樂器。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to intelligence related to music and sound.","zh":"這個短語指與音樂和聲音相關的智能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"interpersonal intelligence","meaning":"人際智能","examples":[{"en":"Interpersonal intelligence involves understanding and communicating with others.","zh":"人際智能涉及理解他人和與他人溝通。"},{"en":"Interpersonal intelligence is the ability to understand people and social situations.","zh":"人際智能是理解人和社交情境的能力。"},{"en":"A class monitor may need interpersonal intelligence to solve conflicts.","zh":"班長可能需要人際智能來解決衝突。"},{"en":"Strong interpersonal intelligence can support teamwork and leadership.","zh":"強人際智能可以支持團隊合作和領導。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to social intelligence.","zh":"這個短語指社交智能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"intrapersonal intelligence","meaning":"內省智能","examples":[{"en":"Intrapersonal intelligence concerns self-awareness and independent thought.","zh":"內省智能關乎自我意識和獨立思考。"},{"en":"Intrapersonal intelligence is the ability to understand one’s own feelings and thinking.","zh":"內省智能是理解自己感受和思維的能力。"},{"en":"A reflective student may know which study method works best for them.","zh":"善於反思的學生可能知道哪種學習方法最適合自己。"},{"en":"Self-awareness helps people set goals and manage emotions.","zh":"自我意識幫助人設定目標和管理情緒。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to intelligence directed inward.","zh":"這個短語指向內觀察自己的智能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"after further research","meaning":"經過進一步研究後","examples":[{"en":"Gardner added another category after further research.","zh":"Gardner 經過進一步研究後加入另一個類別。"},{"en":"After further research means after doing more study and investigation.","zh":"經過進一步研究後，是指在做更多研究和調查之後。"},{"en":"A teacher may change a lesson plan after further research into student needs.","zh":"老師可能在進一步研究學生需要後改變課堂計劃。"},{"en":"Further research can make an earlier theory more complete.","zh":"進一步研究可以令早期理論更完整。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that new findings came later.","zh":"這個短語顯示新發現較後出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"add an eighth element","meaning":"加入第八項元素","examples":[{"en":"Gardner later added an eighth element to his theory.","zh":"Gardner 後來在他的理論中加入第八項元素。"},{"en":"To add an eighth element means to include one more category after the first seven.","zh":"加入第八項元素，是指在原本七項之後再加入一個類別。"},{"en":"A school programme may add an eighth element if a new skill becomes important.","zh":"如果新技能變得重要，學校課程可能加入第八項元素。"},{"en":"Adding another element can expand the original framework.","zh":"加入另一元素可以擴展原本框架。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extending a list or theory.","zh":"這個短語描述擴展清單或理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"naturalistic intelligence","meaning":"自然觀察智能","examples":[{"en":"Naturalistic intelligence concerns understanding and working with nature.","zh":"自然觀察智能關乎理解自然和與自然工作。"},{"en":"Naturalistic intelligence is the ability to recognise plants, animals and natural patterns.","zh":"自然觀察智能是辨認植物、動物和自然模式的能力。"},{"en":"A student with this intelligence may enjoy gardening or wildlife observation.","zh":"有這種智能的學生可能喜歡園藝或野生動物觀察。"},{"en":"It can support farming, biology and environmental work.","zh":"它可以支持農業、生物學和環境工作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to intelligence connected with the natural world.","zh":"這個短語指與自然世界相關的智能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"investigate the possibility of","meaning":"研究……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"Gardner has investigated the possibility of a ninth intelligence.","zh":"Gardner 研究第九種智能的可能性。"},{"en":"To investigate the possibility of something means to study whether it may exist or happen.","zh":"研究某事的可能性，是指探討它是否可能存在或發生。"},{"en":"A school may investigate the possibility of adding a new subject.","zh":"學校可能研究加入新科目的可能性。"},{"en":"Investigation is needed before accepting a new idea.","zh":"接受新想法之前需要調查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful exploration of a possible claim.","zh":"這個短語描述對可能主張的謹慎探索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"existential intelligence","meaning":"存在智能","examples":[{"en":"Existential intelligence concerns profound questions about human existence.","zh":"存在智能關乎有關人類存在的深層問題。"},{"en":"Existential intelligence is the ability to think about life, death, purpose and meaning.","zh":"存在智能是思考生命、死亡、目的和意義的能力。"},{"en":"A student may show existential intelligence by asking deep questions about human life.","zh":"學生若提出關於人生的深層問題，可能展現存在智能。"},{"en":"This category is more abstract and more debated than some others.","zh":"這個類別比其他一些類別更抽象，也更具爭議。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to intelligence about ultimate human questions.","zh":"這個短語指關於終極人生問題的智能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as defined by","meaning":"按照……的定義","examples":[{"en":"Linguistic intelligence is the first category as defined by Gardner.","zh":"按照 Gardner 的定義，語言智能是第一個類別。"},{"en":"As defined by someone means according to that person’s definition.","zh":"按照某人的定義，是指根據那人的解釋。"},{"en":"A “pass” may mean different things as defined by different exams.","zh":"按照不同考試的定義，「合格」可能有不同意思。"},{"en":"This phrase tells readers whose definition is being followed.","zh":"這個短語告訴讀者正在跟隨誰的定義。"},{"en":"It is useful when a term has more than one meaning.","zh":"當術語有多於一個意思時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"relate to an individual’s ability to","meaning":"與個人……的能力有關","examples":[{"en":"Linguistic intelligence relates to an individual’s ability to use language.","zh":"語言智能與個人使用語言的能力有關。"},{"en":"To relate to an individual’s ability to do something means to be connected with that person’s capacity.","zh":"與個人做某事的能力有關，是指與那人的能力相連。"},{"en":"Maths confidence may relate to a student’s ability to solve problems calmly.","zh":"數學信心可能與學生冷靜解題的能力有關。"},{"en":"This phrase links a quality with a specific skill.","zh":"這個短語把一種特質與具體技能連接起來。"},{"en":"It helps explain what an intelligence category covers.","zh":"它幫助解釋某個智能類別涵蓋甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"process and communicate","meaning":"處理和傳達","examples":[{"en":"Language users process and communicate complex ideas.","zh":"語言使用者處理和傳達複雜想法。"},{"en":"To process and communicate ideas means to understand them and express them to others.","zh":"處理和傳達想法，是指理解它們並向他人表達。"},{"en":"A student processes and communicates ideas when summarising a difficult article.","zh":"學生概括一篇困難文章時，就是在處理和傳達想法。"},{"en":"Strong language skills help people organise thoughts clearly.","zh":"強語言能力幫助人清楚組織思想。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both understanding and expression.","zh":"這個短語同時描述理解和表達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"written and spoken words","meaning":"書面及口頭語言","examples":[{"en":"Linguistic intelligence covers both written and spoken words.","zh":"語言智能涵蓋書面及口頭語言。"},{"en":"Written and spoken words mean language in writing and speech.","zh":"書面及口頭語言，是指文字和說話中的語言。"},{"en":"Essays use written words, while presentations use spoken words.","zh":"作文使用書面語言，而匯報使用口頭語言。"},{"en":"Strong language ability may appear in both writing and speaking.","zh":"強語言能力可能同時出現在寫作和說話中。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to two forms of language.","zh":"這個短語指兩種語言形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be said to excel at","meaning":"據說擅長……","examples":[{"en":"People with linguistic intelligence are said to excel at language tasks.","zh":"據說有語言智能的人擅長語言任務。"},{"en":"Be said to excel at something means people claim or believe someone is very good at it.","zh":"據說擅長某事，是指人們聲稱或相信某人很擅長該事。"},{"en":"A student may be said to excel at public speaking.","zh":"某學生可能據說擅長公開演說。"},{"en":"This phrase reports a common judgement rather than proving it directly.","zh":"這個短語轉述常見判斷，而不是直接證明。"},{"en":"It describes recognised strength.","zh":"它描述被認可的強項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"storytelling","meaning":"說故事","examples":[{"en":"People with linguistic ability may excel at storytelling.","zh":"有語言能力的人可能擅長說故事。"},{"en":"Storytelling means telling stories clearly, interestingly and effectively.","zh":"說故事是指清楚、有趣和有效地講述故事。"},{"en":"A teacher uses storytelling to make history lessons more memorable.","zh":"老師用說故事令歷史課更令人難忘。"},{"en":"Good storytelling helps listeners follow events and care about characters.","zh":"好的說故事能力幫助聽眾跟上事件並關心角色。"},{"en":"This word refers to the skill of presenting a story.","zh":"這個詞指呈現故事的技巧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"learn a foreign language","meaning":"學習外語","examples":[{"en":"Linguistically intelligent people may learn a foreign language easily.","zh":"語言智能強的人可能容易學習外語。"},{"en":"To learn a foreign language means to study a language that is not one’s native language.","zh":"學習外語是指學習並非自己母語的語言。"},{"en":"A student may learn a foreign language through classes, songs and conversation.","zh":"學生可能透過課堂、歌曲和對話學習外語。"},{"en":"Strong memory and language awareness can make foreign-language learning easier.","zh":"強記憶力和語言意識可以令外語學習更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes acquiring another language.","zh":"這個短語描述掌握另一種語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"memorise words and dates","meaning":"記憶詞語和日期","examples":[{"en":"Some people are particularly good at memorising words and dates.","zh":"有些人特別擅長記憶詞語和日期。"},{"en":"To memorise words and dates means to remember vocabulary and specific times accurately.","zh":"記憶詞語和日期，是指準確記住詞彙和特定時間。"},{"en":"A history student may memorise dates for important wars and treaties.","zh":"歷史學生可能記憶重要戰爭和條約的日期。"},{"en":"Strong memory can help with languages, history and exams.","zh":"強記憶力可以幫助語言、歷史和考試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes remembering exact verbal and factual information.","zh":"這個短語描述記住精確語言和事實資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be related to a person’s ability to","meaning":"與某人……的能力有關","examples":[{"en":"Logical intelligence is related to a person’s ability to reason.","zh":"邏輯智能與某人的推理能力有關。"},{"en":"Be related to a person’s ability to do something means connected with that skill.","zh":"與某人做某事的能力有關，是指與該技能相連。"},{"en":"Reading speed may be related to a student’s ability to recognise words quickly.","zh":"閱讀速度可能與學生快速辨認詞語的能力有關。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the skill behind a broader quality.","zh":"這個短語解釋較大特質背後的技能。"},{"en":"It links an intelligence category to a practical ability.","zh":"它把智能類別與實際能力連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"reason logically","meaning":"進行邏輯推理","examples":[{"en":"Logical-mathematical thinkers can reason logically.","zh":"邏輯數學型思考者能進行邏輯推理。"},{"en":"To reason logically means to think in a clear, ordered and evidence-based way.","zh":"進行邏輯推理，是指以清楚、有次序和有證據的方式思考。"},{"en":"A student reasons logically when they explain each step in a maths solution.","zh":"學生解釋數學解題每一步時，就是在進行邏輯推理。"},{"en":"Logical reasoning reduces careless guessing.","zh":"邏輯推理可以減少粗心猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes structured thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述有結構的思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"think scientifically","meaning":"以科學方式思考","examples":[{"en":"Scientific intelligence involves the ability to think scientifically.","zh":"科學智能涉及以科學方式思考的能力。"},{"en":"To think scientifically means to use evidence, testing and careful reasoning.","zh":"以科學方式思考，是指使用證據、測試和仔細推理。"},{"en":"A student thinks scientifically when they test whether sunlight affects plant growth.","zh":"學生測試陽光是否影響植物生長時，就是以科學方式思考。"},{"en":"Scientific thinking helps separate guesses from supported conclusions.","zh":"科學思考幫助區分猜測和有支持的結論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence-based thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述以證據為本的思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make deductions","meaning":"作出推論","examples":[{"en":"Logical thinkers can make deductions from available evidence.","zh":"邏輯思考者能從現有證據作出推論。"},{"en":"To make deductions means to reach conclusions by reasoning from evidence.","zh":"作出推論，是指根據證據透過推理得出結論。"},{"en":"A detective makes deductions from footprints and witness statements.","zh":"偵探根據腳印和證人供詞作出推論。"},{"en":"Good deductions depend on accurate information.","zh":"良好推論取決於準確資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes drawing logical conclusions.","zh":"這個短語描述得出合乎邏輯的結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"perform mathematical calculations","meaning":"進行數學運算","examples":[{"en":"Some individuals perform mathematical calculations very accurately.","zh":"有些人非常準確地進行數學運算。"},{"en":"To perform mathematical calculations means to work out numerical problems.","zh":"進行數學運算，是指計算數字問題。"},{"en":"A cashier performs calculations when giving correct change.","zh":"收銀員找回正確零錢時，就是在進行運算。"},{"en":"Accuracy matters because one wrong number can change the result.","zh":"準確很重要，因為一個錯誤數字可以改變結果。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to doing maths operations.","zh":"這個短語指進行數學操作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"spatial judgement","meaning":"空間判斷力","examples":[{"en":"Spatial intelligence includes strong spatial judgement.","zh":"空間智能包括良好的空間判斷力。"},{"en":"Spatial judgement is the ability to understand position, distance and shape.","zh":"空間判斷力是理解位置、距離和形狀的能力。"},{"en":"A driver uses spatial judgement when parking a car.","zh":"司機泊車時會使用空間判斷力。"},{"en":"Weak spatial judgement can make map reading or design harder.","zh":"空間判斷力弱可能令閱讀地圖或設計更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to judging space accurately.","zh":"這個短語指準確判斷空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be related to vision","meaning":"與視覺有關","examples":[{"en":"Spatial intelligence is closely related to vision.","zh":"空間智能與視覺密切相關。"},{"en":"Be related to vision means connected with seeing and visual understanding.","zh":"與視覺有關，是指與觀看和視覺理解相連。"},{"en":"Drawing ability is often related to vision and observation.","zh":"繪畫能力通常與視覺和觀察有關。"},{"en":"If a skill depends on visual patterns, it may be related to vision.","zh":"如果一項技能依賴視覺圖案，它可能與視覺有關。"},{"en":"This phrase links an ability with sight.","zh":"這個短語把能力與視力連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"strong visual memory","meaning":"良好的視覺記憶","examples":[{"en":"People with spatial intelligence often have a strong visual memory.","zh":"有空間智能的人通常有良好的視覺記憶。"},{"en":"Strong visual memory means the ability to remember images, shapes and locations well.","zh":"良好的視覺記憶，是指能很好記住影像、形狀和位置。"},{"en":"A student with strong visual memory may remember diagrams easily.","zh":"有良好視覺記憶的學生可能容易記住圖表。"},{"en":"This ability helps with maps, art and design.","zh":"這種能力有助地圖、藝術和設計。"},{"en":"This phrase describes memory based on what someone sees.","zh":"這個短語描述以所見事物為本的記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"potential to excel in","meaning":"有潛力在……表現出色","examples":[{"en":"They may have the potential to excel in artistic subjects.","zh":"他們可能有潛力在藝術科目表現出色。"},{"en":"Potential to excel in something means possible future ability to do very well in it.","zh":"有潛力在某方面表現出色，是指將來可能在該方面做得很好。"},{"en":"A child who loves building models may have potential to excel in design.","zh":"喜歡砌模型的孩子可能有潛力在設計方面表現出色。"},{"en":"Potential needs practice and support before it becomes achievement.","zh":"潛力需要練習和支援，才會變成成就。"},{"en":"This phrase describes future strong performance.","zh":"這個短語描述未來的強表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"artistic subjects","meaning":"藝術科目","examples":[{"en":"Spatially intelligent learners may succeed in artistic subjects.","zh":"空間智能強的學習者可能在藝術科目取得成功。"},{"en":"Artistic subjects are school subjects connected with art, design or creative expression.","zh":"藝術科目是與藝術、設計或創意表達相關的學科。"},{"en":"Drawing, painting and graphic design are artistic subjects.","zh":"繪畫、油畫和平面設計都是藝術科目。"},{"en":"Visual-spatial strengths can help students create effective artwork.","zh":"視覺空間強項可以幫助學生創作有效藝術作品。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to creative visual learning areas.","zh":"這個短語指創意視覺學習範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"exhibit a leaning towards","meaning":"表現出偏向……的傾向","examples":[{"en":"Some learners exhibit a leaning towards physical activity.","zh":"有些學習者表現出偏向身體活動的傾向。"},{"en":"To exhibit a leaning towards something means to show a preference for it.","zh":"表現出偏向某事的傾向，是指顯示對它的偏好。"},{"en":"A child who chooses science books may exhibit a leaning towards biology.","zh":"選擇科學書的孩子可能表現出偏向生物學的傾向。"},{"en":"A leaning can guide learning style and career interest.","zh":"傾向可以指導學習方式和職業興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a noticeable preference.","zh":"這個短語描述可察覺的偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"learn best by","meaning":"透過……學得最好","examples":[{"en":"Some people learn best by physically practising an action.","zh":"有些人透過親身練習動作學得最好。"},{"en":"To learn best by doing something means that method helps someone learn most effectively.","zh":"透過某方法學得最好，是指該方法最有效幫助某人學習。"},{"en":"Some students learn best by drawing diagrams instead of reading long notes.","zh":"有些學生透過畫圖表，而不是讀長筆記，學得最好。"},{"en":"Matching methods to learning style can improve understanding.","zh":"把方法配合學習方式可以改善理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the most effective learning route.","zh":"這個短語描述最有效的學習途徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"physically practise an action","meaning":"親身練習動作","examples":[{"en":"Bodily-kinesthetic learners benefit from physically practising an action.","zh":"身體動覺型學習者能從親身練習動作中受益。"},{"en":"To physically practise an action means to learn by actually doing the movement.","zh":"親身練習動作，是指透過實際做出動作來學習。"},{"en":"A student learns a basketball shot by physically practising it on court.","zh":"學生透過在球場親身練習來學會投籃。"},{"en":"Physical practice builds muscle memory and confidence.","zh":"身體練習建立肌肉記憶和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning through bodily action.","zh":"這個短語描述透過身體行動學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rather than by reading or seeing","meaning":"而不是透過閱讀或觀看","examples":[{"en":"They learn through movement rather than by reading or seeing.","zh":"他們透過動作學習，而不是透過閱讀或觀看。"},{"en":"Rather than by reading or seeing means instead of learning mainly through words or observation.","zh":"而不是透過閱讀或觀看，是指不主要靠文字或觀察學習。"},{"en":"Some students learn cooking by doing it rather than by reading a recipe only.","zh":"有些學生透過實際下廚學習，而不是只讀食譜。"},{"en":"This contrast shows that action is the preferred learning method.","zh":"這種對比顯示行動是較偏好的學習方式。"},{"en":"The phrase separates hands-on learning from passive learning.","zh":"這個短語把動手學習與被動學習分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as the name suggests","meaning":"顧名思義","examples":[{"en":"As the name suggests, musical intelligence concerns sound.","zh":"顧名思義，音樂智能關乎聲音。"},{"en":"As the name suggests means the meaning is clear from the name itself.","zh":"顧名思義，是指意思可以從名稱本身看出。"},{"en":"As the name suggests, a reading club is mainly about reading.","zh":"顧名思義，閱讀會主要關於閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain a term by pointing to its wording.","zh":"這個短語透過指出詞語本身來解釋術語。"},{"en":"It introduces an obvious explanation.","zh":"它引入明顯解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"define differences in","meaning":"分辨……的差異","examples":[{"en":"Musically intelligent people can define differences in rhythm and tone.","zh":"有音樂智能的人能分辨節奏和音調的差異。"},{"en":"To define differences in something means to identify and describe how things are not the same.","zh":"分辨某事的差異，是指識別並描述事物如何不同。"},{"en":"A music teacher can define differences in pitch between two notes.","zh":"音樂老師能分辨兩個音符之間的音高差異。"},{"en":"Clear distinction helps people hear and improve musical performance.","zh":"清楚區分有助人聽辨並改善音樂表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognising fine differences.","zh":"這個短語描述辨認細微差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rhythm and tones","meaning":"節奏和音調","examples":[{"en":"Musical intelligence includes sensitivity to rhythm and tones.","zh":"音樂智能包括對節奏和音調的敏感度。"},{"en":"Rhythm and tones are patterns of beat and sound quality or pitch.","zh":"節奏和音調是拍子模式和聲音質素或音高。"},{"en":"A drummer focuses on rhythm, while a singer must control tone.","zh":"鼓手專注節奏，而歌手必須控制音調。"},{"en":"Sensitivity to rhythm and tones helps musicians perform accurately.","zh":"對節奏和音調敏感有助音樂家準確表演。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to key features of music.","zh":"這個短語指音樂的重要特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"possess musical intelligence","meaning":"具有音樂智能","examples":[{"en":"People who possess musical intelligence often perform well musically.","zh":"具有音樂智能的人通常在音樂方面表現良好。"},{"en":"To possess musical intelligence means to have strong ability with music and sound.","zh":"具有音樂智能，是指在音樂和聲音方面有強能力。"},{"en":"A child who easily copies melodies may possess musical intelligence.","zh":"容易模仿旋律的孩子可能具有音樂智能。"},{"en":"This ability can appear in listening, singing, composing or playing.","zh":"這種能力可以出現在聆聽、唱歌、作曲或演奏中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes having music-related intelligence.","zh":"這個短語描述擁有音樂相關智能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"play musical instruments","meaning":"演奏樂器","examples":[{"en":"They may be able to play musical instruments skilfully.","zh":"他們可能能夠熟練地演奏樂器。"},{"en":"To play musical instruments means to produce music using tools such as a piano or guitar.","zh":"演奏樂器，是指使用鋼琴或結他等工具產生音樂。"},{"en":"A student may learn to play musical instruments in a school orchestra.","zh":"學生可能在學校管弦樂團學習演奏樂器。"},{"en":"Regular practice improves timing, tone and control.","zh":"定期練習改善節奏、音色和控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes performing music with instruments.","zh":"這個短語描述使用樂器表演音樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"compose music","meaning":"作曲","examples":[{"en":"Some musically intelligent individuals can compose music.","zh":"有些音樂智能強的人能夠作曲。"},{"en":"To compose music means to create original musical pieces.","zh":"作曲是指創作原創音樂作品。"},{"en":"A student may compose music for a school drama performance.","zh":"學生可能為學校戲劇演出作曲。"},{"en":"Composing requires imagination, musical knowledge and structure.","zh":"作曲需要想像力、音樂知識和結構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes writing new music.","zh":"這個短語描述創作新音樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"to a high standard","meaning":"達到高水平","examples":[{"en":"They may sing or play instruments to a high standard.","zh":"他們可能唱歌或演奏樂器達到高水平。"},{"en":"To a high standard means at a level of good quality or skill.","zh":"達到高水平，是指達到良好質素或技能程度。"},{"en":"A student writes to a high standard when their essay is clear and accurate.","zh":"學生作文清楚準確時，就是寫作達到高水平。"},{"en":"High standards usually require practice and feedback.","zh":"高水平通常需要練習和回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong quality of performance.","zh":"這個短語描述表現質素高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"high level of audio-related ability","meaning":"高水平的聽覺相關能力","examples":[{"en":"These individuals possess a high level of audio-related ability.","zh":"這些人具有高水平的聽覺相關能力。"},{"en":"Audio-related ability means skill connected with hearing, sound and music.","zh":"聽覺相關能力是與聆聽、聲音和音樂有關的技能。"},{"en":"A sound engineer needs a high level of audio-related ability.","zh":"音響工程師需要高水平的聽覺相關能力。"},{"en":"Strong listening ability can help people notice subtle differences in tone.","zh":"強聆聽能力可以幫助人注意音調的細微差異。"},{"en":"This phrase describes advanced sound-based skill.","zh":"這個短語描述高階聲音能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lecture situation","meaning":"講課環境","examples":[{"en":"Some learners perform well in a lecture situation.","zh":"有些學習者在講課環境中表現良好。"},{"en":"A lecture situation is a learning setting where someone speaks and others listen.","zh":"講課環境是有人講解、其他人聆聽的學習情境。"},{"en":"University students often learn in lecture situations.","zh":"大學生通常在講課環境中學習。"},{"en":"Students who listen well may benefit from this setting.","zh":"善於聆聽的學生可能受益於這種環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a teaching environment based on listening.","zh":"這個短語描述以聆聽為本的教學環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be required to listen attentively","meaning":"需要專心聆聽","examples":[{"en":"Students in lectures are required to listen attentively.","zh":"講課中的學生需要專心聆聽。"},{"en":"To be required to listen attentively means to need to listen carefully and with focus.","zh":"需要專心聆聽，是指必須仔細而集中地聽。"},{"en":"During safety training, workers are required to listen attentively.","zh":"在安全培訓期間，工人需要專心聆聽。"},{"en":"Careful listening helps people remember instructions and avoid mistakes.","zh":"仔細聆聽幫助人記住指示並避免錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an expected listening behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述被期待的聆聽行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"communicate and empathise with","meaning":"與……溝通並產生同理心","examples":[{"en":"Interpersonal intelligence involves the ability to communicate and empathise with others.","zh":"人際智能涉及與他人溝通並產生同理心的能力。"},{"en":"To communicate and empathise with others means to express ideas and understand their feelings.","zh":"與他人溝通並產生同理心，是指表達想法並理解他人感受。"},{"en":"A good nurse must communicate and empathise with patients.","zh":"好護士必須與病人溝通並產生同理心。"},{"en":"Empathy improves relationships because people feel understood.","zh":"同理心改善關係，因為人們會感到被理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both speaking effectively and feeling with others.","zh":"這個短語描述有效說話和理解他人感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"typically extroverted","meaning":"通常性格外向","examples":[{"en":"People with strong interpersonal intelligence are typically extroverted.","zh":"人際智能強的人通常性格外向。"},{"en":"Typically extroverted means usually outgoing and comfortable with social interaction.","zh":"通常性格外向，是指一般外向並對社交互動感到自在。"},{"en":"A typically extroverted student may enjoy group discussions and presentations.","zh":"通常性格外向的學生可能喜歡小組討論和匯報。"},{"en":"Extroverted people often gain energy from being with others.","zh":"外向的人通常從與他人相處中獲得能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common social personality pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述常見社交性格模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"learn through discussion","meaning":"透過討論學習","examples":[{"en":"Some learners understand ideas best through discussion.","zh":"有些學習者透過討論最能理解想法。"},{"en":"To learn through discussion means to learn by talking, asking and exchanging views.","zh":"透過討論學習，是指透過說話、提問和交換觀點來學習。"},{"en":"A student may understand a poem better through discussion with classmates.","zh":"學生可能透過與同學討論更好理解一首詩。"},{"en":"Discussion helps because it allows people to hear different explanations.","zh":"討論有幫助，因為它讓人聽到不同解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social learning through conversation.","zh":"這個短語描述透過對話進行社交學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"debate and interaction","meaning":"辯論和互動","examples":[{"en":"Interpersonal learners benefit from debate and interaction with others.","zh":"人際型學習者能從辯論和與他人互動中受益。"},{"en":"Debate and interaction mean arguing ideas and communicating actively with people.","zh":"辯論和互動是指討論觀點並與人積極溝通。"},{"en":"A class debate gives students debate and interaction at the same time.","zh":"課堂辯論同時給學生辯論和互動。"},{"en":"Interaction can deepen understanding because students must respond to others.","zh":"互動可以加深理解，因為學生必須回應他人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active social exchange.","zh":"這個短語描述積極的社交交流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"fit the opposite description","meaning":"符合相反的描述","examples":[{"en":"Intrapersonal intelligence fits the opposite description of interpersonal intelligence.","zh":"內省智能符合人際智能相反的描述。"},{"en":"To fit the opposite description means to match the reverse set of qualities.","zh":"符合相反的描述，是指符合相反的一組特質。"},{"en":"If one student loves group work, another may fit the opposite description and prefer studying alone.","zh":"如果一名學生喜歡小組活動，另一名可能符合相反描述，較喜歡獨自學習。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights contrast between two types.","zh":"這個短語突出兩種類型之間的對比。"},{"en":"It shows that the second idea is different from the first.","zh":"它顯示第二個想法不同於第一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"work best independently","meaning":"獨立工作時表現最佳","examples":[{"en":"Intrapersonal learners often work best independently.","zh":"內省型學習者通常獨立工作時表現最佳。"},{"en":"To work best independently means to perform most effectively when working alone.","zh":"獨立工作時表現最佳，是指單獨工作時最有效。"},{"en":"Some writers work best independently in a quiet room.","zh":"有些作家在安靜房間獨立工作時表現最佳。"},{"en":"Independent work suits people who need silence and self-reflection.","zh":"獨立工作適合需要安靜和自我反省的人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes effective solo working.","zh":"這個短語描述有效的單獨工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be capable of","meaning":"有能力……","examples":[{"en":"They are capable of high levels of self-reflection.","zh":"他們有能力進行高度自我反省。"},{"en":"To be capable of something means to have the ability to do it.","zh":"有能力做某事，是指具備做該事的能力。"},{"en":"A careful student is capable of improving quickly after feedback.","zh":"細心學生有能力在收到回饋後快速改善。"},{"en":"Capability means potential, even if it is not always used.","zh":"能力表示潛能，即使未必總是被使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ability or possibility.","zh":"這個短語描述能力或可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"high levels of self-reflection","meaning":"高度自我反省","examples":[{"en":"Intrapersonal intelligence involves high levels of self-reflection.","zh":"內省智能涉及高度自我反省。"},{"en":"High levels of self-reflection mean deep thinking about one’s own thoughts, feelings and actions.","zh":"高度自我反省，是指深入思考自己的想法、感受和行動。"},{"en":"A student shows self-reflection by asking why they lost focus during revision.","zh":"學生思考自己溫習時為何失去專注，就是展現自我反省。"},{"en":"Self-reflection helps people understand habits and improve choices.","zh":"自我反省幫助人理解習慣並改善選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong inner awareness.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈的內在意識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"perfectionists","meaning":"完美主義者","examples":[{"en":"Some people with intrapersonal intelligence are perfectionists.","zh":"有些具內省智能的人是完美主義者。"},{"en":"Perfectionists are people who want work to be extremely correct or complete.","zh":"完美主義者是希望作品極度正確或完整的人。"},{"en":"A perfectionist may rewrite an essay many times before submitting it.","zh":"完美主義者可能在交作文前重寫很多次。"},{"en":"Perfectionism can improve quality, but it can also slow people down.","zh":"完美主義可以提升質素，但也可能拖慢人。"},{"en":"This word describes people who strongly pursue flawlessness.","zh":"這個詞描述強烈追求毫無瑕疵的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"psychometric experts","meaning":"心理計量學專家","examples":[{"en":"A number of psychometric experts oppose Gardner’s theory.","zh":"一些心理計量學專家反對 Gardner 的理論。"},{"en":"Psychometric experts are specialists in psychological measurement and testing.","zh":"心理計量學專家是心理測量和測驗方面的專家。"},{"en":"A psychometric expert may design a reliable workplace ability test.","zh":"心理計量學專家可能設計可靠的職場能力測驗。"},{"en":"Experts may criticise a theory if its categories are hard to measure.","zh":"如果理論類別難以量度，專家可能批評該理論。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to professionals in mental assessment.","zh":"這個短語指心理評估方面的專業人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"oppose someone’s views","meaning":"反對某人的觀點","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers oppose Gardner’s views.","zh":"有些研究人員反對 Gardner 的觀點。"},{"en":"To oppose someone’s views means to disagree with their ideas or arguments.","zh":"反對某人的觀點，是指不同意其想法或論點。"},{"en":"Some parents may oppose a school’s new homework policy.","zh":"有些家長可能反對學校的新功課政策。"},{"en":"Opposition often appears when people think evidence is weak.","zh":"當人們認為證據薄弱，反對意見通常會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active disagreement.","zh":"這個短語描述積極不同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have reservations about","meaning":"對……有所保留","examples":[{"en":"Critics have reservations about the validity of the theory.","zh":"批評者對該理論的有效性有所保留。"},{"en":"To have reservations about something means to feel doubtful or not fully convinced.","zh":"對某事有所保留，是指感到懷疑或未完全信服。"},{"en":"A student may have reservations about joining a group project with unreliable partners.","zh":"學生可能對與不可靠組員合作做專題有所保留。"},{"en":"Reservations do not always mean total rejection; they show caution.","zh":"有所保留不一定代表完全拒絕，而是顯示謹慎。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doubt or concern.","zh":"這個短語描述疑慮或擔心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"validity of a theory","meaning":"理論的有效性","examples":[{"en":"Researchers continue to debate the validity of Gardner’s theory.","zh":"研究人員繼續爭論 Gardner 理論的有效性。"},{"en":"Validity of a theory means whether the theory is well-supported and accurate.","zh":"理論的有效性，是指該理論是否有充分支持並準確。"},{"en":"Scientists test the validity of a theory by checking evidence.","zh":"科學家透過檢查證據來測試理論的有效性。"},{"en":"If evidence is weak, the validity of the theory is questioned.","zh":"如果證據薄弱，理論有效性就會受到質疑。"},{"en":"This phrase concerns whether a theory should be trusted.","zh":"這個短語關乎理論是否可信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"detractors","meaning":"批評者；反對者","examples":[{"en":"Gardner’s detractors question his definition of intelligence.","zh":"Gardner 的批評者質疑他對智力的定義。"},{"en":"Detractors are people who criticise or oppose someone or something.","zh":"批評者是批評或反對某人或某事的人。"},{"en":"A new school policy may have detractors who think it is unfair.","zh":"新校政可能有批評者認為它不公平。"},{"en":"Detractors can force supporters to provide stronger evidence.","zh":"批評者可以迫使支持者提供更強證據。"},{"en":"This word refers to critics or opponents.","zh":"這個詞指批評者或反對者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"disagree with","meaning":"不同意……","examples":[{"en":"Some detractors disagree with Gardner’s overall definition.","zh":"有些批評者不同意 Gardner 的整體定義。"},{"en":"To disagree with something means to think it is wrong or not fully acceptable.","zh":"不同意某事，是指認為它錯誤或不完全可接受。"},{"en":"A student may disagree with a teacher’s marking decision.","zh":"學生可能不同意老師的評分決定。"},{"en":"Disagreement often leads to debate and clarification.","zh":"不同意通常會引起辯論和澄清。"},{"en":"This phrase describes having a different view.","zh":"這個短語描述持有不同看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"overall definition of intelligence","meaning":"智力的整體定義","examples":[{"en":"Critics challenge the overall definition of intelligence used in the theory.","zh":"批評者挑戰該理論所使用的智力整體定義。"},{"en":"Overall definition of intelligence means the broad meaning given to intelligence.","zh":"智力的整體定義，是指對智力給出的廣泛意思。"},{"en":"A narrow definition of intelligence may focus only on exam reasoning.","zh":"狹窄的智力定義可能只聚焦考試推理。"},{"en":"If the overall definition is too broad, many talents may be called intelligence.","zh":"如果整體定義太廣，許多才能可能都被稱為智力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the general meaning of intelligence.","zh":"這個短語指智力的一般意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"hold that","meaning":"認為","examples":[{"en":"Some experts hold that several categories describe personality rather than intelligence.","zh":"有些專家認為幾個類別描述的是性格，而不是智力。"},{"en":"To hold that means to believe or argue that something is true.","zh":"hold that 是指相信或主張某事為真。"},{"en":"Some teachers hold that effort matters more than natural talent.","zh":"有些老師認為努力比天賦更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a viewpoint in a formal way.","zh":"這個短語以正式方式引入觀點。"},{"en":"It is often used before an academic claim.","zh":"它常用於學術主張之前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"relate more to personality than","meaning":"與性格的關係多於……","examples":[{"en":"Some categories may relate more to personality than cognitive ability.","zh":"有些類別可能與性格的關係多於與認知能力的關係。"},{"en":"Relate more to A than B means be more connected with A than with B.","zh":"與 A 的關係多於 B，是指更接近 A，而不是 B。"},{"en":"Being quiet may relate more to personality than intelligence.","zh":"安靜可能與性格的關係多於與智力的關係。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate character traits from mental performance.","zh":"這個短語幫助把性格特質與心智表現分開。"},{"en":"It shows which factor is more relevant.","zh":"它顯示哪個因素更相關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"cognitive performance","meaning":"認知表現","examples":[{"en":"Intelligence tests are intended to evaluate cognitive performance.","zh":"智力測驗旨在評估認知表現。"},{"en":"Cognitive performance means how well a person thinks, reasons, remembers or solves problems.","zh":"認知表現是指一個人在思考、推理、記憶或解難方面做得如何。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can reduce a student’s cognitive performance in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以降低學生在課堂中的認知表現。"},{"en":"A test score may change if cognitive performance is affected by stress.","zh":"如果認知表現受壓力影響，測驗分數可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to mental task performance.","zh":"這個短語指心智任務表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"more recently identified","meaning":"較近期辨認出的","examples":[{"en":"Naturalistic intelligence was a more recently identified category.","zh":"自然觀察智能是較近期辨認出的類別。"},{"en":"More recently identified means recognised later than the earlier categories.","zh":"較近期辨認出的，是指比早期類別更後被承認。"},{"en":"A new learning difficulty may be more recently identified by researchers.","zh":"某種新學習困難可能是研究人員較近期辨認出的。"},{"en":"Later identification can show that a theory has changed over time.","zh":"較後辨認可以顯示理論隨時間改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something recognised at a later stage.","zh":"這個短語描述在較後階段被識別的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"affinity with the natural world","meaning":"對自然世界的親近感","examples":[{"en":"Naturalistic intelligence involves an affinity with the natural world.","zh":"自然觀察智能涉及對自然世界的親近感。"},{"en":"Affinity with the natural world means a strong connection with nature.","zh":"對自然世界的親近感，是指與自然有強烈連繫。"},{"en":"A child who loves identifying birds may show affinity with the natural world.","zh":"喜歡辨認鳥類的孩子可能展現對自然世界的親近感。"},{"en":"This affinity can lead to interest in biology, farming or conservation.","zh":"這種親近感可以帶來對生物、農業或保育的興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes closeness to nature.","zh":"這個短語描述與自然的接近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ability to nurture and cultivate","meaning":"培育和種植的能力","examples":[{"en":"The category includes an ability to nurture and cultivate living things.","zh":"這個類別包括培育和種植生命體的能力。"},{"en":"Ability to nurture and cultivate means skill in caring for and growing living things.","zh":"培育和種植的能力，是照顧並栽培生命體的技能。"},{"en":"A gardener needs the ability to nurture and cultivate plants.","zh":"園丁需要培育和種植植物的能力。"},{"en":"This ability helps living things survive, grow and stay healthy.","zh":"這種能力幫助生命體生存、成長並保持健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical care for plants or animals.","zh":"這個短語描述對植物或動物的實際照顧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be dismissed completely","meaning":"被完全否定","examples":[{"en":"Some critics have dismissed naturalistic intelligence completely.","zh":"有些批評者完全否定自然觀察智能。"},{"en":"To be dismissed completely means to be rejected entirely.","zh":"被完全否定，是指被完全拒絕。"},{"en":"A student’s idea should not be dismissed completely without discussion.","zh":"學生的想法不應未經討論就被完全否定。"},{"en":"Complete dismissal means critics see little or no value in the idea.","zh":"完全否定表示批評者認為該想法幾乎沒有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes total rejection.","zh":"這個短語描述徹底拒絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"no more than a hobby","meaning":"只不過是一種興趣","examples":[{"en":"Critics argue that naturalistic intelligence is no more than a hobby.","zh":"批評者認為自然觀察智能只不過是一種興趣。"},{"en":"No more than a hobby means only an interest, not a true intelligence or skill category.","zh":"只不過是一種興趣，是指只是喜好，而不是真正智能或技能類別。"},{"en":"Someone may say photography is no more than a hobby if it is not treated professionally.","zh":"如果攝影不被視為專業，有人可能說它只不過是一種興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase reduces the importance of something.","zh":"這個短語降低某事的重要性。"},{"en":"It is often used critically.","zh":"它常帶批評意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"doubts have been raised","meaning":"有人提出質疑","examples":[{"en":"Doubts have been raised about whether some categories are true intelligences.","zh":"有人提出質疑，懷疑某些類別是否真正智能。"},{"en":"Doubts have been raised means people have expressed uncertainty or criticism.","zh":"有人提出質疑，是指有人表達不確定或批評。"},{"en":"Doubts have been raised about whether the new exam is fair.","zh":"有人提出質疑，懷疑新考試是否公平。"},{"en":"Raised doubts can lead to further research and debate.","zh":"被提出的質疑可以引發進一步研究和討論。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces criticism or uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語引入批評或不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"in reality","meaning":"實際上","examples":[{"en":"Some supposed intelligences may in reality be talents.","zh":"某些所謂智能實際上可能是才能。"},{"en":"In reality means in fact or in the real situation.","zh":"實際上，是指事實上或在真實情況中。"},{"en":"The homework looked easy, but in reality it took two hours.","zh":"功課看起來容易，但實際上花了兩小時。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts appearance or claim with truth.","zh":"這個短語把表面或聲稱與真相作對比。"},{"en":"It helps correct a possible misunderstanding.","zh":"它幫助修正可能誤解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"final criticism","meaning":"最後一項批評","examples":[{"en":"A final criticism concerns whether the intelligences are genuinely separate.","zh":"最後一項批評關乎這些智能是否真正分開。"},{"en":"A final criticism is the last critical point in a discussion.","zh":"最後一項批評，是討論中的最後批評重點。"},{"en":"A teacher’s final criticism of an essay may concern weak evidence.","zh":"老師對作文的最後一項批評可能關於證據薄弱。"},{"en":"Final criticisms often summarise a major remaining problem.","zh":"最後批評通常概括仍然存在的主要問題。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the last objection.","zh":"這個短語引入最後反對意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be attached to a theory","meaning":"針對某理論提出","examples":[{"en":"Several criticisms have been attached to Gardner’s theory.","zh":"多項批評針對 Gardner 的理論提出。"},{"en":"Criticisms attached to a theory are objections connected with it.","zh":"針對某理論提出的批評，是與該理論相關的反對意見。"},{"en":"Many concerns may be attached to a new school policy.","zh":"新校政可能面對多項相關疑慮。"},{"en":"A theory with many attached criticisms may still remain influential.","zh":"即使一個理論有許多批評，仍可能保持影響力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes criticisms linked to an idea.","zh":"這個短語描述與某想法相連的批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be treated as separate entities","meaning":"被視為獨立個體","examples":[{"en":"The intelligences may not be treated as completely separate entities.","zh":"這些智能未必可被視為完全獨立個體。"},{"en":"To be treated as separate entities means to be regarded as independent things.","zh":"被視為獨立個體，是指被看作互相獨立的事物。"},{"en":"Reading and writing should not always be treated as separate entities because they influence each other.","zh":"閱讀和寫作不應總被視為獨立個體，因為它們互相影響。"},{"en":"If abilities overlap, treating them as separate may be misleading.","zh":"如果能力重疊，把它們視為分開可能有誤導性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes viewing things as independent units.","zh":"這個短語描述把事物看作獨立單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"perform equally well in","meaning":"在……表現同樣出色","examples":[{"en":"Some individuals perform equally well in several intellectual areas.","zh":"有些人在幾個智力範疇表現同樣出色。"},{"en":"To perform equally well in several areas means to do similarly well across them.","zh":"在幾個範疇表現同樣出色，是指在這些範疇做得差不多一樣好。"},{"en":"A student may perform equally well in English and science.","zh":"學生可能在英文和科學表現同樣出色。"},{"en":"Equal performance can challenge the idea that abilities are fully separate.","zh":"均衡表現可以挑戰能力完全分開的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes balanced strength across areas.","zh":"這個短語描述跨範疇的均衡強項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"diverse areas","meaning":"不同的範疇","examples":[{"en":"A person may show strong ability in two diverse areas.","zh":"一個人可能在兩個不同範疇展現強能力。"},{"en":"Diverse areas are different or varied fields.","zh":"不同的範疇是不同或多樣的領域。"},{"en":"Music and mathematics are diverse areas, but one student may enjoy both.","zh":"音樂和數學是不同範疇，但一名學生可能兩者都喜歡。"},{"en":"Strength in diverse areas suggests ability can be broad.","zh":"在不同範疇都有強項，表示能力可以很廣泛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes areas that are not closely alike.","zh":"這個短語描述不太相似的領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"maintain that","meaning":"堅持認為","examples":[{"en":"Gardner maintains that his theory is sound.","zh":"Gardner 堅持認為他的理論可靠。"},{"en":"To maintain that something is true means to continue to argue or believe it.","zh":"堅持認為某事為真，是指繼續主張或相信它。"},{"en":"A student may maintain that their answer is correct after checking the text.","zh":"學生查閱文本後可能堅持認為自己的答案正確。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests holding a view despite disagreement.","zh":"這個短語暗示即使有分歧仍持有觀點。"},{"en":"It is common in academic debate.","zh":"它常見於學術辯論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"theories are sound","meaning":"理論是可靠的","examples":[{"en":"Gardner argues that his theories are sound.","zh":"Gardner 認為他的理論是可靠的。"},{"en":"Theories are sound means they are reasonable, well-supported and reliable.","zh":"理論是可靠的，是指它們合理、有充分支持並可信。"},{"en":"A teacher’s explanation is sound if it fits the evidence and examples.","zh":"如果老師的解釋符合證據和例子，它就是可靠的。"},{"en":"A sound theory can survive criticism better than a weak one.","zh":"可靠理論比薄弱理論更能承受批評。"},{"en":"This phrase describes theoretical reliability.","zh":"這個短語描述理論上的可信度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"identifiable and separate part of the brain","meaning":"可辨認而獨立的大腦區域","examples":[{"en":"He argues that each intelligence is linked to an identifiable and separate part of the brain.","zh":"他認為每種智能都與可辨認而獨立的大腦區域相連。"},{"en":"An identifiable and separate part of the brain is a brain area that can be recognised as distinct.","zh":"可辨認而獨立的大腦區域，是可被識別為不同的大腦部位。"},{"en":"Doctors may identify a separate brain area responsible for a specific function.","zh":"醫生可能辨認出負責特定功能的獨立腦區。"},{"en":"Physical brain evidence can make a psychological theory seem stronger.","zh":"生理腦部證據可以令心理理論看起來更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a distinct brain region.","zh":"這個短語描述獨特腦部區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be responsible for controlling","meaning":"負責控制……","examples":[{"en":"Different brain regions are responsible for controlling different functions.","zh":"不同大腦區域負責控制不同功能。"},{"en":"To be responsible for controlling something means to manage or direct that function.","zh":"負責控制某事，是指管理或指揮該功能。"},{"en":"The school office is responsible for controlling visitor entry.","zh":"學校辦公室負責控制訪客進入。"},{"en":"If one part controls a function, damage there may affect that function.","zh":"如果某部位控制某功能，該處受損可能影響該功能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes control or management responsibility.","zh":"這個短語描述控制或管理責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"aspects related to","meaning":"與……有關的方面","examples":[{"en":"Each brain region controls aspects related to a particular intelligence.","zh":"每個腦區控制與特定智能有關的方面。"},{"en":"Aspects related to something are parts or features connected with it.","zh":"與某事有關的方面，是與它相連的部分或特徵。"},{"en":"A writing lesson may cover aspects related to grammar, structure and tone.","zh":"寫作課可能涵蓋與文法、結構和語氣有關的方面。"},{"en":"Looking at related aspects gives a fuller understanding.","zh":"觀察相關方面能帶來更完整理解。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to connected parts of a topic.","zh":"這個短語指主題中相連的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"despite the criticism received","meaning":"儘管受到批評","examples":[{"en":"Despite the criticism received, Gardner’s theory remains influential.","zh":"儘管受到批評，Gardner 的理論仍有影響力。"},{"en":"Despite the criticism received means although people have criticised it.","zh":"儘管受到批評，是指雖然有人批評它。"},{"en":"Despite the criticism received, the new timetable was kept for another year.","zh":"儘管受到批評，新時間表仍保留多一年。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts negative reactions with continued success or importance.","zh":"這個短語把負面反應與持續成功或重要性作對比。"},{"en":"It shows that criticism did not end the influence.","zh":"它顯示批評沒有終止影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contemporaries","meaning":"同時代學者","examples":[{"en":"Some of Gardner’s contemporaries rejected parts of his theory.","zh":"Gardner 的一些同時代學者否定了他理論的部分內容。"},{"en":"Contemporaries are people living or working during the same period.","zh":"同時代學者是指生活或工作於同一時期的人。"},{"en":"A writer’s contemporaries may include other authors from the same generation.","zh":"作家的同時代人可能包括同一代的其他作者。"},{"en":"Contemporary criticism shows how people at the time responded.","zh":"同時代批評顯示當時人們如何回應。"},{"en":"This word refers to people from the same era.","zh":"這個詞指同一時代的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be well respected","meaning":"備受尊重","examples":[{"en":"Gardner’s ideas are well respected in education.","zh":"Gardner 的想法在教育界備受尊重。"},{"en":"To be well respected means to be regarded highly by many people.","zh":"備受尊重，是指被很多人高度評價。"},{"en":"A teacher may be well respected because she is fair and knowledgeable.","zh":"老師可能因公平和知識豐富而備受尊重。"},{"en":"An idea can be respected even if people debate parts of it.","zh":"一個想法即使部分內容有爭議，也可以受尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong professional approval.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈專業認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"often applied in","meaning":"經常應用於……","examples":[{"en":"The theory is often applied in the world of education.","zh":"這個理論經常應用於教育界。"},{"en":"Often applied in something means frequently used in that field or setting.","zh":"經常應用於某處，是指頻繁用於該領域或情境。"},{"en":"Mind maps are often applied in revision and brainstorming.","zh":"思維導圖經常應用於溫習和腦力激盪。"},{"en":"A theory becomes practical when teachers can apply it in real classrooms.","zh":"當老師能在真實課室應用理論，理論就變得實用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes common practical use.","zh":"這個短語描述常見實際使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the world of education","meaning":"教育界","examples":[{"en":"Multiple-intelligence theory is influential in the world of education.","zh":"多元智能理論在教育界有影響力。"},{"en":"The world of education means the field involving schools, teaching and learning.","zh":"教育界是指涉及學校、教學和學習的領域。"},{"en":"New technology can change the world of education quickly.","zh":"新科技可以快速改變教育界。"},{"en":"Ideas in this world affect teachers, students and curriculum design.","zh":"這個領域中的想法影響老師、學生和課程設計。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the education field.","zh":"這個短語指教育領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a tool for identifying","meaning":"辨認……的工具","examples":[{"en":"The theory is used as a tool for identifying children’s abilities.","zh":"這個理論被用作辨認兒童能力的工具。"},{"en":"A tool for identifying something is a method that helps recognise it.","zh":"辨認某事的工具，是幫助識別它的方法。"},{"en":"A reading test can be a tool for identifying students who need support.","zh":"閱讀測驗可以作為辨認需要支援學生的工具。"},{"en":"Identification helps people provide suitable guidance.","zh":"辨認有助人們提供合適指導。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a method for recognising something.","zh":"這個短語描述用來識別某事的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"differing abilities","meaning":"不同能力","examples":[{"en":"Teachers use the framework to recognise children’s differing abilities.","zh":"老師使用這個框架來辨認兒童的不同能力。"},{"en":"Differing abilities means abilities that vary from person to person.","zh":"不同能力是指因人而異的能力。"},{"en":"In one class, students may show differing abilities in speaking, maths and drawing.","zh":"在同一班中，學生可能在口語、數學和繪畫方面展現不同能力。"},{"en":"Recognising differences helps teachers avoid judging everyone by one standard.","zh":"辨認差異幫助老師避免用單一標準評價所有人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes varied strengths and weaknesses.","zh":"這個短語描述多樣化強弱項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"potential career paths","meaning":"潛在職業方向","examples":[{"en":"The theory may help identify potential career paths.","zh":"這個理論可能有助辨認潛在職業方向。"},{"en":"Potential career paths are possible future jobs or professional directions.","zh":"潛在職業方向是將來可能的工作或專業路向。"},{"en":"A student good at languages may consider career paths in teaching or translation.","zh":"擅長語言的學生可能考慮教學或翻譯職業方向。"},{"en":"Knowing strengths can help people choose more suitable careers.","zh":"了解強項可以幫助人選擇更合適職業。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to possible work futures.","zh":"這個短語指可能的工作未來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"For instance, linguistic ability may suit a career in writing.","zh":"例如，語言能力可能適合寫作職業。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance 意思是例如。"},{"en":"Good study habits help in many subjects; for instance, planning helps with writing.","zh":"良好學習習慣幫助許多科目；例如，規劃有助寫作。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a specific example of a general point.","zh":"這個短語引入一般重點的具體例子。"},{"en":"It makes explanations clearer and more concrete.","zh":"它令解釋更清楚、更具體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"show linguistic capabilities","meaning":"展現語言能力","examples":[{"en":"Some children show strong linguistic capabilities.","zh":"有些孩子展現強語言能力。"},{"en":"To show linguistic capabilities means to demonstrate strong language skills.","zh":"展現語言能力，是指顯示強語言技能。"},{"en":"A child who tells clear stories may show linguistic capabilities early.","zh":"能清楚說故事的孩子可能早早展現語言能力。"},{"en":"These capabilities can support reading, writing and speaking.","zh":"這些能力可以支援閱讀、寫作和說話。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible language ability.","zh":"這個短語描述可見的語言能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be ideal for roles in","meaning":"適合擔任……的職位","examples":[{"en":"Linguistically skilled people may be ideal for roles in teaching.","zh":"語言能力強的人可能適合擔任教學職位。"},{"en":"To be ideal for roles in something means to be very suitable for those jobs.","zh":"適合擔任某類職位，是指非常適合那些工作。"},{"en":"A patient person may be ideal for roles in childcare.","zh":"有耐性的人可能適合擔任幼兒照顧職位。"},{"en":"Matching abilities to roles can improve job satisfaction and performance.","zh":"把能力與職位配對可以提升工作滿意度和表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong suitability for work.","zh":"這個短語描述對工作的高度適合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"logical-mathematical thinkers","meaning":"邏輯數學型思考者","examples":[{"en":"Logical-mathematical thinkers may be suited to scientific careers.","zh":"邏輯數學型思考者可能適合科學職業。"},{"en":"Logical-mathematical thinkers are people who reason well and handle numbers effectively.","zh":"邏輯數學型思考者是善於推理並有效處理數字的人。"},{"en":"Such thinkers may enjoy coding, finance or physics.","zh":"這類思考者可能喜歡編程、金融或物理。"},{"en":"Their strengths help them analyse patterns and solve structured problems.","zh":"他們的強項幫助他們分析模式並解決有結構問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people strong in logic and mathematics.","zh":"這個短語描述邏輯和數學能力強的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be suited to careers in","meaning":"適合從事……職業","examples":[{"en":"These individuals may be suited to careers in science or law.","zh":"這些人可能適合從事科學或法律職業。"},{"en":"To be suited to careers in a field means to have abilities that match that field.","zh":"適合從事某領域職業，是指能力與該領域相配。"},{"en":"A creative student may be suited to careers in design or media.","zh":"有創意的學生可能適合從事設計或媒體職業。"},{"en":"Suitability depends on skills, interests and personality.","zh":"適合與否取決於技能、興趣和性格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes career fit.","zh":"這個短語描述職業配合度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"exhibit spatial intelligence","meaning":"展現空間智能","examples":[{"en":"Architects often exhibit strong spatial intelligence.","zh":"建築師通常展現強空間智能。"},{"en":"To exhibit spatial intelligence means to show ability in understanding space and visual form.","zh":"展現空間智能，是指顯示理解空間和視覺形態的能力。"},{"en":"A student who builds detailed models may exhibit spatial intelligence.","zh":"能製作細緻模型的學生可能展現空間智能。"},{"en":"This intelligence helps with design, maps and three-dimensional thinking.","zh":"這種智能有助設計、地圖和三維思考。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible spatial ability.","zh":"這個短語描述可見的空間能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a career such as","meaning":"例如……的職業","examples":[{"en":"Spatial intelligence may support a career such as architecture.","zh":"空間智能可能支持例如建築的職業。"},{"en":"A career such as something introduces an example of a possible job.","zh":"例如某職業，是用來引入一個可能工作的例子。"},{"en":"Strong writing ability may lead to a career such as journalism.","zh":"強寫作能力可能通向例如新聞工作的職業。"},{"en":"This phrase gives one example without limiting all possibilities.","zh":"這個短語給出一個例子，而不限制所有可能性。"},{"en":"It helps connect ability to real work.","zh":"它幫助把能力與真實工作連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"have a leaning towards","meaning":"偏向於……","examples":[{"en":"Some people have a leaning towards bodily-kinesthetic activities.","zh":"有些人偏向於身體動覺活動。"},{"en":"To have a leaning towards something means to prefer or be naturally drawn to it.","zh":"偏向於某事，是指較喜歡或自然被它吸引。"},{"en":"A student may have a leaning towards science after enjoying experiments.","zh":"學生做實驗後可能偏向於科學。"},{"en":"A leaning can suggest future strengths or interests.","zh":"傾向可以暗示未來強項或興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a natural preference.","zh":"這個短語描述自然偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"excel in areas such as","meaning":"在……等範疇表現出色","examples":[{"en":"Bodily-kinesthetic learners may excel in areas such as athletics.","zh":"身體動覺型學習者可能在運動等範疇表現出色。"},{"en":"To excel in areas such as something means to do very well in examples of that field.","zh":"在某些範疇表現出色，是指在該領域的例子中做得很好。"},{"en":"A musical student may excel in areas such as singing and rhythm.","zh":"有音樂感的學生可能在唱歌和節奏等範疇表現出色。"},{"en":"Giving examples helps readers see the kind of ability being discussed.","zh":"給出例子有助讀者理解正在討論的能力類型。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces possible strong areas.","zh":"這個短語引入可能的強項範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"craft-making","meaning":"手工藝製作","examples":[{"en":"Some people with bodily intelligence excel in craft-making.","zh":"有些具身體智能的人在手工藝製作方面表現出色。"},{"en":"Craft-making means making things skilfully by hand.","zh":"手工藝製作是指用雙手有技巧地製作物品。"},{"en":"Students practise craft-making when they create models, pottery or handmade cards.","zh":"學生製作模型、陶器或手製卡時，就是在進行手工藝製作。"},{"en":"Craft-making uses hand control, planning and physical skill.","zh":"手工藝製作運用手部控制、規劃和身體技巧。"},{"en":"This word refers to practical creative handwork.","zh":"這個詞指實用而具創意的手作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"strengths in the area of","meaning":"在……方面的優勢","examples":[{"en":"Strengths in the area of music may support a performing career.","zh":"在音樂方面的優勢可能支持表演職業。"},{"en":"Strengths in the area of something means strong ability in that field.","zh":"在某方面的優勢，是指在該領域有強能力。"},{"en":"A student with strengths in the area of speaking may enjoy debates.","zh":"在口語方面有優勢的學生可能喜歡辯論。"},{"en":"Knowing one’s strengths helps with subject and career choices.","zh":"了解自己的優勢有助科目和職業選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where ability is strong.","zh":"這個短語指出能力在哪裏強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"lead to success as","meaning":"令某人成為成功的……","examples":[{"en":"Musical ability may lead to success as a conductor or singer.","zh":"音樂能力可能令人成為成功的指揮或歌手。"},{"en":"To lead to success as something means to help someone become successful in that role.","zh":"令某人成為成功的某角色，是指幫助某人在該角色取得成功。"},{"en":"Strong organisation skills may lead to success as a project manager.","zh":"強組織能力可能令人成為成功的項目經理。"},{"en":"Ability alone may help, but practice and opportunity also matter.","zh":"能力本身可能有幫助，但練習和機會也重要。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a skill with a successful role.","zh":"這個短語把技能與成功角色連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"display strong interpersonal skills","meaning":"展現良好人際技巧","examples":[{"en":"Effective managers often display strong interpersonal skills.","zh":"能幹的經理通常展現良好人際技巧。"},{"en":"To display strong interpersonal skills means to show good ability in dealing with people.","zh":"展現良好人際技巧，是指顯示善於與人相處的能力。"},{"en":"A class leader displays interpersonal skills by calming arguments fairly.","zh":"班長公平地平息爭執，就是展現人際技巧。"},{"en":"These skills help teams communicate and cooperate.","zh":"這些技巧幫助團隊溝通和合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible social ability.","zh":"這個短語描述可見的社交能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be recognised as","meaning":"被認為是……","examples":[{"en":"People with social intelligence are recognised as effective communicators.","zh":"有社交智能的人被認為是有效溝通者。"},{"en":"To be recognised as something means to be accepted or regarded in that way.","zh":"被認為是某種人，是指被接受或視為那樣。"},{"en":"A helpful student may be recognised as a good team member.","zh":"樂於助人的學生可能被認為是好組員。"},{"en":"Recognition often comes from repeated behaviour or achievement.","zh":"認可通常來自反覆行為或成就。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being acknowledged by others.","zh":"這個短語描述被他人承認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"make effective politicians","meaning":"成為能幹的政治人物","examples":[{"en":"Strong interpersonal skills may help people make effective politicians.","zh":"強人際技巧可能幫助人成為能幹的政治人物。"},{"en":"To make effective politicians means to help people become capable political leaders.","zh":"成為能幹的政治人物，是指有能力成為有效的政治領袖。"},{"en":"A person who listens well may make an effective community representative.","zh":"善於聆聽的人可能成為能幹的社區代表。"},{"en":"Politicians need communication skills because they work with many groups.","zh":"政治人物需要溝通技巧，因為他們與許多群體合作。"},{"en":"This phrase links social ability to political effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語把社交能力與政治效能連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"dominant intrapersonal intelligence","meaning":"佔主導的內省智能","examples":[{"en":"Some people show dominant intrapersonal intelligence.","zh":"有些人展現佔主導的內省智能。"},{"en":"Dominant intrapersonal intelligence means self-awareness is the strongest or most noticeable intelligence.","zh":"佔主導的內省智能，是指自我意識是最強或最明顯的智能。"},{"en":"A reflective writer may show dominant intrapersonal intelligence.","zh":"善於反思的作家可能展現佔主導的內省智能。"},{"en":"When this intelligence is dominant, independent work may feel natural.","zh":"當這種智能佔主導，獨立工作可能感覺自然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inner awareness as a main strength.","zh":"這個短語描述內在覺察作為主要強項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be better suited to","meaning":"較適合……","examples":[{"en":"Independent thinkers may be better suited to solitary professions.","zh":"獨立思考者可能較適合獨自工作的職業。"},{"en":"To be better suited to something means to fit it more naturally or effectively.","zh":"較適合某事，是指更自然或更有效地配合它。"},{"en":"A quiet student may be better suited to research than constant public speaking.","zh":"安靜學生可能較適合研究，而不是不斷公開演說。"},{"en":"Suitability depends on strengths, preferences and work conditions.","zh":"適合與否取決於強項、偏好和工作條件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a stronger match.","zh":"這個短語描述更強的配合度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"professions involving","meaning":"涉及……的職業","examples":[{"en":"They may prefer professions involving substantial independent work.","zh":"他們可能較喜歡涉及大量獨立工作的職業。"},{"en":"Professions involving something are jobs that include that feature.","zh":"涉及某事的職業，是包含該特徵的工作。"},{"en":"Writing and programming are professions involving long periods of concentration.","zh":"寫作和編程是涉及長時間專注的職業。"},{"en":"The nature of a profession affects who may enjoy it.","zh":"職業性質會影響誰可能喜歡它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes jobs by their main activities.","zh":"這個短語按主要活動描述工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"lower levels of interaction","meaning":"較低程度的互動","examples":[{"en":"Some occupations involve lower levels of interaction with other people.","zh":"有些職業涉及與他人較低程度的互動。"},{"en":"Lower levels of interaction mean less frequent contact or communication with others.","zh":"較低程度的互動，是指與他人的接觸或溝通較少。"},{"en":"A data-entry job may involve lower levels of interaction than customer service.","zh":"資料輸入工作可能比客戶服務涉及較低程度的互動。"},{"en":"Some people prefer less interaction because it allows deep focus.","zh":"有些人偏好較少互動，因為它容許深度專注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reduced social contact.","zh":"這個短語描述較少社交接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"outside world","meaning":"外界","examples":[{"en":"Writers may work with relatively little interaction with the outside world.","zh":"作家可能在與外界相對較少互動的情況下工作。"},{"en":"The outside world means people and activities beyond one’s private working space.","zh":"外界是指個人私人工作空間以外的人和活動。"},{"en":"A student studying alone for exams may feel cut off from the outside world.","zh":"獨自備考的學生可能感到與外界隔絕。"},{"en":"Less contact with the outside world can help focus but may feel isolating.","zh":"與外界較少接觸可以幫助專注，但也可能令人孤立。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the wider social environment.","zh":"這個短語指更廣泛的社會環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"contain the following information","meaning":"包含以下資料","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which paragraph contains the following information.","zh":"學生辨認哪一段包含以下資料。"},{"en":"To contain the following information means to include the listed details.","zh":"包含以下資料，是指包括所列出的細節。"},{"en":"A paragraph may contain the following information about Galton’s early tests.","zh":"某段可能包含關於 Galton 早期測驗的以下資料。"},{"en":"Students must locate ideas, not just match repeated words.","zh":"學生必須定位想法，而不只是配對重複字眼。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in paragraph-matching tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於段落配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"use any letter more than once","meaning":"每個字母可使用多於一次","examples":[{"en":"Students may use any paragraph letter more than once.","zh":"學生可以使用任何段落字母多於一次。"},{"en":"Use any letter more than once means an answer option can be repeated.","zh":"每個字母可使用多於一次，是指答案選項可以重複。"},{"en":"In a matching task, the same paragraph may answer two questions.","zh":"在配對題中，同一段可能回答兩條問題。"},{"en":"This instruction prevents students from forcing each letter to be used once only.","zh":"這項指示防止學生以為每個字母只能用一次。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"physiological evidence","meaning":"生理證據","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for physiological evidence supporting the theory.","zh":"題目要求找出支持該理論的生理證據。"},{"en":"Physiological evidence is evidence from the body or its biological functions.","zh":"生理證據是來自身體或其生物功能的證據。"},{"en":"Brain-scan results can be physiological evidence in psychology.","zh":"腦掃描結果可以是心理學中的生理證據。"},{"en":"Such evidence can support a theory by linking it to the body.","zh":"這類證據可以透過把理論連接到身體來支持它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to biological proof.","zh":"這個短語指生物學上的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"intelligence theories are sound","meaning":"智力理論是可靠的","examples":[{"en":"Gardner presents evidence that his intelligence theories are sound.","zh":"Gardner 提出證據顯示他的智力理論是可靠的。"},{"en":"Intelligence theories are sound means the theories are reasonable and supported.","zh":"智力理論是可靠的，是指這些理論合理並有支持。"},{"en":"A theory is sound if its claims match the evidence.","zh":"如果理論主張符合證據，它就是可靠的。"},{"en":"Sound theories can still be debated, but they are not baseless.","zh":"可靠理論仍可以被討論，但不是毫無根據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reliable theories about intelligence.","zh":"這個短語描述關於智力的可信理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"aims of intelligence testing","meaning":"智力測驗的目的","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains the aims of intelligence testing.","zh":"篇章解釋智力測驗的目的。"},{"en":"Aims of intelligence testing are the purposes these tests are meant to serve.","zh":"智力測驗的目的，是這些測驗被設計來服務的目標。"},{"en":"One aim may be to understand a student’s learning needs.","zh":"其中一個目的可能是了解學生學習需要。"},{"en":"Knowing the aims prevents people from expecting the test to measure everything.","zh":"了解目的可防止人期望測驗量度一切。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the purposes of IQ-style tests.","zh":"這個短語指智商類測驗的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"initial failure","meaning":"最初的失敗","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to an initial failure in measurement.","zh":"題目指的是測量中的最初失敗。"},{"en":"Initial failure means a failure at the beginning of an attempt or process.","zh":"最初的失敗，是嘗試或過程開始時的失敗。"},{"en":"A first lesson plan may be an initial failure if students do not understand it.","zh":"如果學生不理解，第一份教案可能是最初的失敗。"},{"en":"Initial failure can still lead to later improvement.","zh":"最初失敗仍可以帶來後來改進。"},{"en":"This phrase describes early unsuccessful results.","zh":"這個短語描述早期不成功的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"successful measurement","meaning":"成功量度","examples":[{"en":"Early methods failed to achieve successful measurement of intelligence.","zh":"早期方法未能成功量度智力。"},{"en":"Successful measurement means measuring something accurately and usefully.","zh":"成功量度是指準確而有用地量度某事。"},{"en":"A thermometer provides successful measurement only if it gives accurate temperature.","zh":"溫度計只有在給出準確溫度時，才提供成功量度。"},{"en":"Measurement fails if it does not measure the intended quality.","zh":"如果量度沒有測到目標特質，量度就失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes effective assessment.","zh":"這個短語描述有效評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"high-level social skills","meaning":"高水平社交技巧","examples":[{"en":"High-level social skills are linked to interpersonal intelligence.","zh":"高水平社交技巧與人際智能有關。"},{"en":"High-level social skills are advanced abilities in communication, empathy and cooperation.","zh":"高水平社交技巧是溝通、同理心和合作方面的高階能力。"},{"en":"A team leader needs high-level social skills to handle conflict.","zh":"團隊領袖需要高水平社交技巧來處理衝突。"},{"en":"These skills help people build trust and manage relationships.","zh":"這些技巧幫助人建立信任和管理關係。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong ability in social situations.","zh":"這個短語描述在社交情境中的強能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be linked and classified as","meaning":"被聯繫並歸類為……","examples":[{"en":"Social abilities may be linked and classified as interpersonal intelligence.","zh":"社交能力可能被聯繫並歸類為人際智能。"},{"en":"To be linked and classified as something means to be connected with it and placed in that category.","zh":"被聯繫並歸類為某事，是指與它相連並被放入該類別。"},{"en":"A student’s drawing skill may be linked and classified as spatial ability.","zh":"學生的繪畫能力可能被聯繫並歸類為空間能力。"},{"en":"Classification helps organise different strengths.","zh":"分類有助組織不同強項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes connecting evidence to a category.","zh":"這個短語描述把證據連接到某類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"what constitutes","meaning":"甚麼構成……","examples":[{"en":"Critics disagree about what constitutes intelligence.","zh":"批評者對甚麼構成智力意見不同。"},{"en":"What constitutes something means what counts as or forms that thing.","zh":"甚麼構成某事，是指甚麼算作或形成該事。"},{"en":"Teachers may debate what constitutes good writing.","zh":"老師可能爭論甚麼構成好寫作。"},{"en":"If people disagree about the definition, they may disagree about assessment.","zh":"如果人們不同意定義，就可能不同意評估。"},{"en":"This phrase asks what truly makes up a concept.","zh":"這個短語詢問真正組成概念的是甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"talent or intelligence","meaning":"才能或智力","examples":[{"en":"The debate concerns whether certain abilities are talents or forms of intelligence.","zh":"這場辯論關乎某些能力是才能還是智力形式。"},{"en":"Talent or intelligence contrasts a special skill with a broader mental ability.","zh":"才能或智力對比特殊技能和較廣泛的心智能力。"},{"en":"Someone may ask whether drawing well is talent or intelligence.","zh":"有人可能問畫畫好是才能還是智力。"},{"en":"The distinction matters because it affects how abilities are assessed.","zh":"這種區分很重要，因為它影響能力如何被評估。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a classification debate.","zh":"這個短語顯示分類上的爭議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與文章資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷每句陳述是否與文章資料一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the information means match what the text says.","zh":"與資料一致，是指符合文本所說內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says a test was developed by Binet, the same statement agrees with the information.","zh":"如果篇章說某測驗由 Binet 研發，相同陳述就與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should check the text, not rely on memory.","zh":"學生應檢查文本，而不是依靠記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個短語用於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文章資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"與資料相矛盾，是指說出與文本相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says seven categories but the statement says five, it contradicts the information.","zh":"如果篇章說有七類，但陳述說五類，它就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction requires clear conflict with the text.","zh":"矛盾需要與文本有清楚衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a statement that is false according to the passage.","zh":"這個短語描述根據文章為錯的陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有關於此事的資料","examples":[{"en":"Not Given means that no relevant information is provided.","zh":"Not Given 表示沒有提供相關資料。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not say whether it is true or false.","zh":"沒有關於此事的資料，是指篇章沒有說它是真或假。"},{"en":"If the text never mentions a researcher’s age, a claim about age has no information on this.","zh":"如果文本從未提及研究者年齡，關於年齡的說法就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when the passage is silent.","zh":"當篇章沒有提及時，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the NOT GIVEN answer.","zh":"這個短語解釋 NOT GIVEN 答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be misguided","meaning":"方向錯誤；受到誤導","examples":[{"en":"Early studies into intelligence were partly misguided.","zh":"早期智力研究部分方向錯誤。"},{"en":"To be misguided means to be based on a wrong idea or poor judgement.","zh":"方向錯誤，是指建基於錯誤想法或不良判斷。"},{"en":"A study plan is misguided if it ignores the exam format.","zh":"如果溫習計劃忽略考試格式，它就是方向錯誤。"},{"en":"Misguided methods can still teach later researchers what to avoid.","zh":"方向錯誤的方法仍可以教後來研究者避免甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a wrong direction.","zh":"這個短語描述錯誤方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"have no impact on","meaning":"對……沒有影響","examples":[{"en":"The statement claims that early studies had no impact on later methods.","zh":"該陳述聲稱早期研究對後來方法沒有影響。"},{"en":"To have no impact on something means not to affect it at all.","zh":"對某事沒有影響，是指完全不影響它。"},{"en":"One missed homework task may have no impact on the final grade if it is not counted.","zh":"如果一次欠交功課不計分，它可能對最終成績沒有影響。"},{"en":"If something influences later work, it does not have no impact.","zh":"如果某事影響後來工作，它就不是沒有影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes absence of influence.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be designed to determine","meaning":"旨在確定……","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether IQ research is designed to determine inborn intelligence.","zh":"該陳述詢問智商研究是否旨在確定天生智力。"},{"en":"Be designed to determine means be created to find out a specific thing.","zh":"旨在確定，是指被設計來找出某特定事情。"},{"en":"A placement interview may be designed to determine a student’s speaking level.","zh":"分班面試可能旨在確定學生口語水平。"},{"en":"Tests should be judged by what they are designed to determine.","zh":"評價測驗應根據它旨在確定甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the purpose of a test or study.","zh":"這個短語描述測驗或研究的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"intelligence an individual is born with","meaning":"個人與生俱來的智力","examples":[{"en":"Some people assume that tests measure the intelligence an individual is born with.","zh":"有些人假設測驗量度個人與生俱來的智力。"},{"en":"Intelligence an individual is born with means inherited intellectual ability.","zh":"個人與生俱來的智力，是指遺傳而來的智力能力。"},{"en":"A child’s test score cannot show only the intelligence they were born with.","zh":"孩子的測驗分數不能只顯示他與生俱來的智力。"},{"en":"Education, family and health also shape test performance.","zh":"教育、家庭和健康也會塑造測驗表現。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to innate intelligence.","zh":"這個短語指天生智力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"confirm different types of intelligence","meaning":"確認不同種類的智能","examples":[{"en":"Gardner has confirmed several categories but continues to consider another.","zh":"Gardner 已確認幾個類別，但仍繼續考慮另一個。"},{"en":"To confirm different types of intelligence means to identify them with enough confidence.","zh":"確認不同種類的智能，是指有足夠信心辨認它們。"},{"en":"A researcher may confirm different learning styles after repeated studies.","zh":"研究者可能經過反覆研究後確認不同學習風格。"},{"en":"Confirmation suggests stronger support than a simple guess.","zh":"確認暗示比簡單猜測有更強支持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognising categories as valid.","zh":"這個短語描述把類別認可為有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be linked to creativity","meaning":"與創造力有關","examples":[{"en":"Spatial ability may be linked to creativity and visual art.","zh":"空間能力可能與創造力和視覺藝術有關。"},{"en":"To be linked to creativity means to be connected with original or artistic thinking.","zh":"與創造力有關，是指與原創或藝術思考相連。"},{"en":"Drawing skill may be linked to creativity in design class.","zh":"繪畫技能可能在設計課中與創造力有關。"},{"en":"A link does not always mean one thing directly causes the other.","zh":"有關聯不一定表示一事直接造成另一事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a connection with creative ability.","zh":"這個短語描述與創造能力的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"demonstrate high levels of","meaning":"展現高水平的……","examples":[{"en":"A person may demonstrate high levels of ability in several areas.","zh":"一個人可能在幾個範疇展現高水平能力。"},{"en":"To demonstrate high levels of something means to show a strong degree of it.","zh":"展現高水平的某事，是指顯示很強程度的該特質。"},{"en":"A student may demonstrate high levels of concentration during a difficult exam.","zh":"學生可能在困難考試中展現高水平專注力。"},{"en":"Demonstrated ability is visible through performance or behaviour.","zh":"被展現出的能力可透過表現或行為看見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clearly showing strong ability.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚顯示強能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"contradictory areas","meaning":"看似互相矛盾的範疇","examples":[{"en":"An individual may perform well in apparently contradictory areas.","zh":"一個人可能在看似互相矛盾的範疇表現良好。"},{"en":"Contradictory areas are fields that seem opposite or difficult to combine.","zh":"看似互相矛盾的範疇，是表面上相反或難以結合的領域。"},{"en":"A student strong in both poetry and advanced maths may seem strong in contradictory areas.","zh":"同時擅長詩歌和高階數學的學生，看起來可能在矛盾範疇都有強項。"},{"en":"Such cases challenge simple labels about ability.","zh":"這類例子挑戰對能力的簡單標籤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes areas that appear inconsistent with each other.","zh":"這個短語描述表面上互不一致的領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"make bad managers","meaning":"成為不稱職的經理","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether intrapersonal thinkers always make bad managers.","zh":"該陳述問內省型思考者是否總會成為不稱職的經理。"},{"en":"To make bad managers means to become ineffective people in management roles.","zh":"成為不稱職的經理，是指在管理職位上表現無效。"},{"en":"A quiet person does not necessarily make a bad manager.","zh":"安靜的人不一定會成為不稱職的經理。"},{"en":"Management quality depends on judgement, communication and organisation, not one trait only.","zh":"管理質素取決於判斷、溝通和組織，而不只是一項特質。"},{"en":"This phrase describes poor suitability for management.","zh":"這個短語描述不適合管理或管理表現差。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each answer.","zh":"學生為每個答案選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choose the correct letter means select the option marked by the right letter.","zh":"選出正確字母，是指選擇標有正確字母的選項。"},{"en":"In multiple-choice questions, students may choose the correct letter A, B, C or D.","zh":"在多項選擇題中，學生可能選出 A、B、C 或 D 的正確字母。"},{"en":"Careful reading helps prevent choosing a tempting but wrong option.","zh":"仔細閱讀有助避免選擇吸引但錯誤的選項。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"correctly estimate","meaning":"正確估計","examples":[{"en":"Some critics argue that IQ tests do not correctly estimate intelligence.","zh":"有些批評者認為智商測驗未能正確估計智力。"},{"en":"To correctly estimate something means to judge it approximately but accurately.","zh":"正確估計某事，是指作出近似但準確的判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher may correctly estimate a student’s level after several writing samples.","zh":"老師可能在看過幾篇作文後正確估計學生水平。"},{"en":"One short test may fail to estimate ability correctly.","zh":"一個短測驗可能未能正確估計能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making an accurate assessment.","zh":"這個短語描述作出準確評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"perform badly on the day","meaning":"在測驗當日表現欠佳","examples":[{"en":"A person may perform badly on the day of a test.","zh":"一個人可能在測驗當日表現欠佳。"},{"en":"To perform badly on the day means to do poorly at that particular time.","zh":"在當日表現欠佳，是指在該特定時間做得不好。"},{"en":"A strong student may perform badly on the day because of illness.","zh":"強學生可能因生病在當日表現欠佳。"},{"en":"One poor performance may not reflect usual ability.","zh":"一次差表現未必反映平時能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes temporary poor performance during an event.","zh":"這個短語描述某事件中的暫時差表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"weaknesses in one area","meaning":"某一範疇的弱項","examples":[{"en":"A person may have weaknesses in one intellectual area.","zh":"一個人可能在某一智力範疇有弱項。"},{"en":"Weaknesses in one area are difficulties or lower ability in a specific field.","zh":"某一範疇的弱項，是指在特定領域有困難或能力較低。"},{"en":"A student may have weaknesses in grammar but strengths in speaking.","zh":"學生可能在文法有弱項，但口語有強項。"},{"en":"Weakness in one area should not define the whole learner.","zh":"一個範疇的弱項不應定義整個學習者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited difficulty in a particular domain.","zh":"這個短語描述特定領域中的有限困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"strengths in others","meaning":"其他方面的強項","examples":[{"en":"The same person may have strengths in other areas.","zh":"同一個人可能在其他方面有強項。"},{"en":"Strengths in others means strong abilities in different areas from the weak one.","zh":"其他方面的強項，是指在不同於弱項的領域中有強能力。"},{"en":"A student weak in spelling may have strengths in ideas and speaking.","zh":"拼字弱的學生可能在想法和口語方面有強項。"},{"en":"Recognising other strengths gives a fairer view of ability.","zh":"辨認其他強項能帶來更公平的能力觀。"},{"en":"This phrase balances weakness with ability elsewhere.","zh":"這個短語把弱項與其他能力平衡起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"accurately assess","meaning":"準確評估","examples":[{"en":"A well-designed test should accurately assess the relevant ability.","zh":"設計良好的測驗應準確評估相關能力。"},{"en":"To accurately assess means to evaluate correctly and fairly.","zh":"準確評估是指正確而公平地評價。"},{"en":"A speaking test should accurately assess communication, not handwriting.","zh":"口語測驗應準確評估溝通，而不是書寫。"},{"en":"Accurate assessment depends on suitable tasks and clear criteria.","zh":"準確評估取決於合適任務和清晰準則。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reliable evaluation.","zh":"這個短語描述可靠評價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"ability to reason, think and solve problems","meaning":"推理、思考及解決問題的能力","examples":[{"en":"Intelligence includes the ability to reason, think and solve problems.","zh":"智力包括推理、思考及解決問題的能力。"},{"en":"This ability means using the mind to understand situations and find solutions.","zh":"這種能力是指使用心智理解情況並找出解決方法。"},{"en":"A student uses this ability when explaining how to fix a failed experiment.","zh":"學生解釋如何修正失敗實驗時，就是在使用這種能力。"},{"en":"Strong reasoning and problem-solving help people handle unfamiliar tasks.","zh":"強推理和解難能力幫助人處理陌生任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes core intellectual ability.","zh":"這個短語描述核心智力能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"ability to memorise items seen","meaning":"記憶所見事物的能力","examples":[{"en":"A strong visual memory supports the ability to memorise items seen.","zh":"強視覺記憶支持記憶所見事物的能力。"},{"en":"Ability to memorise items seen means remembering things after looking at them.","zh":"記憶所見事物的能力，是指看過東西後能記住它們。"},{"en":"A student may memorise a map after studying it for a few minutes.","zh":"學生可能看幾分鐘地圖後記住它。"},{"en":"Visual memory helps with diagrams, directions and design.","zh":"視覺記憶有助圖表、方向和設計。"},{"en":"This phrase describes memory based on visual information.","zh":"這個短語描述以視覺資訊為本的記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"be classified by Gardner","meaning":"被 Gardner 歸類為……","examples":[{"en":"The ability is classified by Gardner as a particular intelligence.","zh":"該能力被 Gardner 歸類為某一種智能。"},{"en":"To be classified by Gardner means to be placed in one of Gardner’s categories.","zh":"被 Gardner 歸類，是指被放入 Gardner 的其中一個類別。"},{"en":"Musical skill may be classified by Gardner as musical intelligence.","zh":"音樂技能可能被 Gardner 歸類為音樂智能。"},{"en":"Classification depends on the framework being used.","zh":"分類取決於所使用的框架。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how Gardner labels an ability.","zh":"這個短語描述 Gardner 如何標籤一種能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"harshest criticism","meaning":"最嚴厲的批評","examples":[{"en":"The harshest criticism was directed at one of the later categories.","zh":"最嚴厲的批評針對其中一個較後提出的類別。"},{"en":"Harshest criticism means the strongest or most severe objection.","zh":"最嚴厲的批評，是最強烈或最嚴重的反對意見。"},{"en":"A new school rule may receive the harshest criticism from students who feel it is unfair.","zh":"新校規可能受到覺得它不公平的學生最嚴厲批評。"},{"en":"Harsh criticism usually targets the weakest or most controversial point.","zh":"嚴厲批評通常針對最薄弱或最具爭議的點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the most severe negative judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述最嚴重的負面判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"be focused on","meaning":"集中針對……","examples":[{"en":"Much criticism has been focused on naturalistic intelligence.","zh":"許多批評集中針對自然觀察智能。"},{"en":"To be focused on something means to be mainly directed at it.","zh":"集中針對某事，是指主要指向它。"},{"en":"The class discussion was focused on the causes of exam stress.","zh":"課堂討論集中於考試壓力的原因。"},{"en":"When criticism is focused on one area, that area is under special pressure.","zh":"當批評集中於某一範疇，該範疇承受特別壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main target of attention.","zh":"這個短語描述注意力的主要目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 17 - PSYCHOMETRICS.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 19":[{"front":"the Rainmaker design","meaning":"「造雨者」設計","examples":[{"en":"The Rainmaker design produces fresh water and cool air from seawater and sunlight.","zh":"「造雨者」設計利用海水和陽光產生淡水和冷空氣。"},{"en":"The Rainmaker design is a system that uses natural heat, seawater, and condensation to create useful water and cooling.","zh":"「造雨者」設計是一個利用自然熱力、海水和凝結作用來產生有用水源和冷卻效果的系統。"},{"en":"A dry coastal village could use the Rainmaker design to grow vegetables without depending on rainfall.","zh":"乾旱沿海村莊可以使用「造雨者」設計種植蔬菜，而不用依賴降雨。"},{"en":"Because it uses sunlight and seawater, the Rainmaker design can help places where fresh water is limited.","zh":"由於它使用陽光和海水，「造雨者」設計可以幫助淡水有限的地方。"},{"en":"The Rainmaker design shows how a simple natural process can become a practical environmental solution.","zh":"「造雨者」設計顯示，一個簡單自然過程可以變成實用的環保方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pop up out of the blue","meaning":"突然出現；出乎意料地想到","examples":[{"en":"Sometimes useful ideas simply pop up out of the blue.","zh":"有時有用的想法就是突然出現。"},{"en":"To pop up out of the blue means to appear suddenly and unexpectedly.","zh":"pop up out of the blue 指突然並出乎意料地出現。"},{"en":"A solution to a maths problem may pop up out of the blue while a student is walking home.","zh":"學生在回家路上，可能突然想到一道數學題的解法。"},{"en":"When an idea pops up out of the blue, it can feel surprising because nobody planned it.","zh":"當想法突然出現時，會令人驚訝，因為沒有人事先計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for thoughts, chances, or events that arrive without warning.","zh":"這個短語用於沒有預警地出現的想法、機會或事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in someone’s case","meaning":"就某人的情況而言","examples":[{"en":"In Charlie Paton’s case, the idea came from an experience on a rainy bus.","zh":"就 Charlie Paton 的情況而言，這個想法來自一次在雨中巴士上的經歷。"},{"en":"In someone’s case means in that particular person’s situation.","zh":"in someone’s case 指就某個特定人士的情況而言。"},{"en":"In Maria’s case, online lessons work well because she studies after her children sleep.","zh":"就 Maria 的情況而言，網上課堂很有效，因為她在孩子睡後學習。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers move from a general idea to one person’s specific example.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者由一般想法轉到某人的具體例子。"},{"en":"We use it when the same topic affects different people in different ways.","zh":"當同一主題以不同方式影響不同人時，我們會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"out of the rain","meaning":"從雨水中得到靈感","examples":[{"en":"In Paton’s case, the idea came out of the rain rather than out of the blue.","zh":"就 Paton 的情況而言，這個想法不是憑空出現，而是從雨水中得到靈感。"},{"en":"Out of the rain here means the idea came from a rainy experience, not from nowhere.","zh":"out of the rain 在這裡指想法來自一次下雨經歷，而不是無中生有。"},{"en":"A writer may say an invention came out of the rain if wet weather directly inspired it.","zh":"如果潮濕天氣直接啟發某項發明，作者可能說該發明來自雨水。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with “out of the blue” by showing a real cause behind the idea.","zh":"這個短語與 “out of the blue” 形成對比，顯示想法背後有真實原因。"},{"en":"It is a playful way to say that rain helped create the inspiration.","zh":"它是一種帶玩味的說法，表示雨水幫助產生靈感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"travel through the desert","meaning":"穿越沙漠","examples":[{"en":"Paton was travelling through the Moroccan desert by bus.","zh":"Paton 當時正乘巴士穿越摩洛哥沙漠。"},{"en":"To travel through the desert means to move across a dry, sandy, and often difficult landscape.","zh":"travel through the desert 指穿過乾燥、多沙且通常艱難的地貌。"},{"en":"Tourists travelling through the desert must carry enough water and protect themselves from the sun.","zh":"穿越沙漠的遊客必須帶足夠水，並保護自己免受烈日影響。"},{"en":"Travelling through the desert can be dangerous because heat and distance make small problems serious.","zh":"穿越沙漠可能很危險，因為高溫和距離會令小問題變嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes crossing a desert area rather than just visiting its edge.","zh":"這個短語描述穿過沙漠地區，而不只是到沙漠邊緣遊覽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be full of","meaning":"充滿……","examples":[{"en":"The bus was full of hot, wet passengers.","zh":"巴士充滿又熱又濕的乘客。"},{"en":"To be full of something means to contain many people or a large amount of something.","zh":"be full of something 指包含許多人或大量某物。"},{"en":"The classroom was full of nervous students before the speaking exam.","zh":"口試前，課室充滿緊張的學生。"},{"en":"If a room is full of warm, wet air, water may form on cold surfaces.","zh":"如果房間充滿溫暖潮濕的空氣，水可能在冷表面形成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place or thing that contains a lot of something.","zh":"這個短語描述某地方或物件含有大量某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"steam up","meaning":"蒙上水氣","examples":[{"en":"The bus windows steamed up because of the warm, humid air.","zh":"由於溫暖潮濕的空氣，巴士車窗蒙上水氣。"},{"en":"To steam up means to become covered with tiny water droplets so that glass looks cloudy.","zh":"steam up 指被微小水滴覆蓋，使玻璃看起來模糊。"},{"en":"Bathroom mirrors often steam up after a hot shower.","zh":"熱水澡後，浴室鏡子常會蒙上水氣。"},{"en":"Windows steam up when warm moist air touches a colder surface.","zh":"當溫暖潮濕的空氣接觸較冷表面時，窗戶會蒙上水氣。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for glass, mirrors, or car windows.","zh":"這個短語常用於玻璃、鏡子或車窗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"against the glass","meaning":"貼着玻璃","examples":[{"en":"Paton fell asleep with a towel against the glass.","zh":"Paton 睡着時，一條毛巾貼着玻璃。"},{"en":"Against the glass means touching or pressed next to a glass surface.","zh":"against the glass 指接觸或貼近玻璃表面。"},{"en":"A child may press his face against the glass to look at cakes in a shop window.","zh":"孩子可能把臉貼着玻璃，看商店櫥窗裡的蛋糕。"},{"en":"When warm cloth rests against cold glass, moisture may collect there.","zh":"當溫暖布料貼着冷玻璃時，水分可能在那裡聚集。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical contact with a glass surface.","zh":"這個短語描述與玻璃表面的實體接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"soaking wet","meaning":"濕透的","examples":[{"en":"When he woke up, the towel was soaking wet.","zh":"他醒來時，毛巾濕透了。"},{"en":"Soaking wet means completely wet, not just slightly damp.","zh":"soaking wet 指完全濕透，而不是微濕。"},{"en":"A student caught in heavy rain may arrive at school soaking wet.","zh":"遇上大雨的學生到校時可能全身濕透。"},{"en":"If a towel is soaking wet, water may drip from it when it is lifted.","zh":"如果毛巾濕透，拿起時可能會滴水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that has absorbed a lot of water.","zh":"這個短語描述吸收了大量水分的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"wring something out","meaning":"把……扭乾","examples":[{"en":"Paton had to wring the water out of the towel.","zh":"Paton 必須把毛巾中的水扭乾。"},{"en":"To wring something out means to twist it tightly to remove water.","zh":"wring something out 指用力扭轉某物以擠出水分。"},{"en":"After washing a cloth by hand, you wring it out before hanging it up.","zh":"手洗抹布後，你會先把它扭乾，再掛起來。"},{"en":"If a shirt is not wrung out, it may drip water onto the floor.","zh":"如果襯衫沒有扭乾，可能會滴水到地上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes removing liquid by twisting wet material.","zh":"這個短語描述透過扭轉濕材料去除液體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"make someone think","meaning":"令某人思考","examples":[{"en":"The wet towel made Paton think about how water could be produced.","zh":"濕毛巾令 Paton 思考水如何可以被製造出來。"},{"en":"To make someone think means to cause a person to consider an idea more carefully.","zh":"make someone think 指令某人更仔細考慮一個想法。"},{"en":"A teacher’s question can make students think about why their answer is wrong.","zh":"老師的問題可以令學生思考自己的答案為何錯。"},{"en":"Strange everyday events can make someone think and lead to new ideas.","zh":"奇怪的日常事件可以令某人思考，並帶來新想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that starts reflection or curiosity.","zh":"這個短語描述某事引發反思或好奇心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the answer was condensation","meaning":"答案是凝結作用","examples":[{"en":"The answer to Paton’s question was condensation.","zh":"Paton 問題的答案是凝結作用。"},{"en":"The answer was condensation means the key explanation was water vapour turning into liquid water.","zh":"the answer was condensation 指關鍵解釋是水蒸氣變成液態水。"},{"en":"If your cold drink makes the table wet, the answer is often condensation, not a leaking cup.","zh":"如果你的冷飲令桌面變濕，答案通常是凝結作用，而不是杯子漏水。"},{"en":"Condensation explains why warm wet air can produce water on a cold surface.","zh":"凝結作用解釋了為何溫暖潮濕空氣可以在冷表面產生水。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the scientific process behind the observation.","zh":"這個短語指出觀察背後的科學過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"condensation","meaning":"凝結作用","examples":[{"en":"Condensation caused droplets of water to form on the window.","zh":"凝結作用令水滴在窗上形成。"},{"en":"Condensation is the process in which water vapour cools and becomes liquid water.","zh":"condensation 指水蒸氣冷卻並變成液態水的過程。"},{"en":"Condensation appears on a cold bottle when it is taken out of the fridge.","zh":"從雪櫃拿出的冷凍瓶子表面會出現凝結水。"},{"en":"When humid air cools below its dew point, condensation can occur.","zh":"當潮濕空氣冷卻至露點以下，凝結作用就可能發生。"},{"en":"This word explains why water can appear even when nothing is leaking.","zh":"這個字解釋為何沒有東西漏水時也會出現水分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"back home in London","meaning":"回到倫敦後","examples":[{"en":"Back home in London, Paton discussed the experience with a physicist.","zh":"回到倫敦後，Paton 與一位物理學家討論這次經歷。"},{"en":"Back home in London means after returning to his home city, London.","zh":"back home in London 指回到他的家所在城市倫敦之後。"},{"en":"Back home in Hong Kong, a student may tell her family about what she learned abroad.","zh":"回到香港後，學生可能向家人講述自己在海外學到的事。"},{"en":"This phrase moves the story from a journey back to a familiar home setting.","zh":"這個短語把故事從旅程轉回熟悉的家中環境。"},{"en":"We use it when someone returns and thinks about what happened elsewhere.","zh":"當某人回來並思考在其他地方發生的事時，我們會使用它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a physicist friend","meaning":"一位物理學家朋友","examples":[{"en":"A physicist friend explained why the bus window had become wet.","zh":"一位物理學家朋友解釋了為何巴士車窗會變濕。"},{"en":"A physicist friend is a friend who studies or works in physics.","zh":"physicist friend 指研究或從事物理學工作的朋友。"},{"en":"If your phone overheats, a physicist friend might explain how heat builds up in small devices.","zh":"如果你的手機過熱，一位物理學家朋友可能解釋熱力如何在小型裝置中累積。"},{"en":"A physicist friend can turn an everyday puzzle into a scientific explanation.","zh":"物理學家朋友可以把日常疑問轉化為科學解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a personal contact with specialist scientific knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述一位擁有專門科學知識的個人朋友。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be chilled by","meaning":"被……冷卻","examples":[{"en":"The glass was chilled by the rain outside.","zh":"玻璃被外面的雨水冷卻。"},{"en":"To be chilled by something means to be cooled by it.","zh":"be chilled by something 指被某物冷卻。"},{"en":"A bottle can be chilled by ice before guests arrive.","zh":"客人到達前，瓶子可以被冰塊冷卻。"},{"en":"When glass is chilled by rain, warm moist air touching it may condense.","zh":"當玻璃被雨水冷卻，接觸它的溫暖潮濕空氣可能凝結。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something becoming colder because of an outside cause.","zh":"這個短語描述某物因外在原因變冷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hot, humid air","meaning":"炎熱潮濕的空氣","examples":[{"en":"The bus contained hot, humid air from the wet passengers.","zh":"巴士裡有來自濕乘客的炎熱潮濕空氣。"},{"en":"Hot, humid air is warm air that contains a lot of water vapour.","zh":"hot, humid air 指含有大量水蒸氣的暖空氣。"},{"en":"A crowded kitchen can fill with hot, humid air when soup is boiling.","zh":"煮湯時，擁擠的廚房可能充滿炎熱潮濕的空氣。"},{"en":"Hot, humid air can feel uncomfortable because sweat does not evaporate easily.","zh":"炎熱潮濕的空氣令人不舒服，因為汗水不易蒸發。"},{"en":"When hot, humid air meets a cold surface, water droplets may form.","zh":"當炎熱潮濕的空氣接觸冷表面，水滴可能形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cool something below its dew point","meaning":"把……冷卻至露點以下","examples":[{"en":"The cold glass cooled the humid air below its dew point.","zh":"冷玻璃把潮濕空氣冷卻至露點以下。"},{"en":"To cool something below its dew point means to lower moist air to the temperature where water starts to condense.","zh":"cool something below its dew point 指把潮濕空氣降到水分開始凝結的溫度。"},{"en":"An air conditioner cools indoor air below its dew point when water drips from the unit.","zh":"當冷氣機滴水時，它就是把室內空氣冷卻至露點以下。"},{"en":"If humid air is cooled below its dew point, droplets form on nearby cold surfaces.","zh":"如果潮濕空氣被冷卻至露點以下，水滴會在附近冷表面形成。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the temperature change needed for condensation.","zh":"這個短語解釋凝結所需的溫度變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"dew point","meaning":"露點","examples":[{"en":"Water condenses when air is cooled below its dew point.","zh":"當空氣被冷卻至露點以下，水便會凝結。"},{"en":"The dew point is the temperature at which water vapour in air begins to turn into liquid.","zh":"dew point 指空氣中的水蒸氣開始變成液體的溫度。"},{"en":"On a humid morning, dew forms on grass when the air cools to its dew point.","zh":"在潮濕早晨，當空氣冷卻至露點，草地上會形成露水。"},{"en":"A higher dew point usually means the air feels more humid.","zh":"較高露點通常代表空氣感覺更潮濕。"},{"en":"This term helps explain why moisture appears on cold surfaces.","zh":"這個術語幫助解釋為何水分會出現在冷表面上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cause droplets to form","meaning":"令水滴形成","examples":[{"en":"The drop in temperature caused water droplets to form.","zh":"溫度下降令水滴形成。"},{"en":"To cause droplets to form means to make tiny drops of liquid appear.","zh":"cause droplets to form 指令微小液滴出現。"},{"en":"A cold glass of water can cause droplets to form on its outside surface.","zh":"一杯冷水可以令水滴在杯外表面形成。"},{"en":"When warm moist air cools quickly, it can cause droplets to form on windows.","zh":"當溫暖潮濕的空氣迅速冷卻時，可能令水滴在窗上形成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the result of condensation.","zh":"這個短語描述凝結作用的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on the inside of","meaning":"在……的內側","examples":[{"en":"The droplets formed on the inside of the window.","zh":"水滴在窗戶內側形成。"},{"en":"On the inside of something means on its inner surface, not the outside surface.","zh":"on the inside of something 指在某物的內部表面，而不是外部表面。"},{"en":"In winter, water may collect on the inside of a bedroom window.","zh":"冬天時，水可能聚集在睡房窗戶內側。"},{"en":"If moisture forms on the inside of glass, the air inside the room is probably humid.","zh":"如果水分在玻璃內側形成，房間內的空氣可能很潮濕。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the exact side or surface where something appears.","zh":"這個短語顯示某物出現的準確一面或表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be intrigued by","meaning":"對……深感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Paton was intrigued by the explanation of condensation.","zh":"Paton 對凝結作用的解釋深感興趣。"},{"en":"To be intrigued by something means to be very interested and curious about it.","zh":"be intrigued by something 指對某事非常感興趣並好奇。"},{"en":"A student may be intrigued by how a phone can recognise a fingerprint.","zh":"學生可能對手機如何辨認指紋深感興趣。"},{"en":"When people are intrigued by a problem, they often ask more questions and experiment.","zh":"當人對問題深感興趣，他們通常會問更多問題並進行實驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes curiosity that pulls someone deeper into a topic.","zh":"這個短語描述把人吸引到主題深處的好奇心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a lighting engineer by profession","meaning":"職業是燈光工程師","examples":[{"en":"Paton was a lighting engineer by profession.","zh":"Paton 的職業是燈光工程師。"},{"en":"A lighting engineer by profession is someone whose job is to design or manage lighting systems.","zh":"lighting engineer by profession 指職業上負責設計或管理燈光系統的人。"},{"en":"A lighting engineer by profession may work in theatres, buildings, concerts, or exhibitions.","zh":"職業是燈光工程師的人可能在劇院、建築、演唱會或展覽工作。"},{"en":"Paton’s profession helped him think practically about energy, light, and design.","zh":"Paton 的職業幫助他實際地思考能源、光線和設計。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a person’s job or trained occupation.","zh":"這個短語指出一個人的工作或受訓職業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rig up equipment","meaning":"臨時裝配設備","examples":[{"en":"Paton began rigging up his own experimental equipment.","zh":"Paton 開始臨時裝配自己的實驗設備。"},{"en":"To rig up equipment means to put together a temporary or improvised set of tools or machines.","zh":"rig up equipment 指把工具或機器臨時、即興地組裝起來。"},{"en":"A science teacher may rig up equipment using bottles, tubes, and tape for a classroom experiment.","zh":"科學老師可能用瓶子、膠管和膠紙臨時裝配設備來做課堂實驗。"},{"en":"People rig up equipment when they want to test an idea before building a proper version.","zh":"當人想在製作正式版本前測試想法，就會臨時裝配設備。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests practical, hands-on invention with available materials.","zh":"這個短語暗示用現有材料進行實際動手發明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"solar stills","meaning":"太陽能蒸餾器","examples":[{"en":"Paton constructed solar stills to produce fresh water.","zh":"Paton 建造太陽能蒸餾器來產生淡水。"},{"en":"Solar stills are simple devices that use sunlight to evaporate water and then condense it as fresh water.","zh":"solar stills 指利用陽光蒸發水，再把它凝結成淡水的簡單裝置。"},{"en":"A solar still can help a remote camp collect drinking water from salty or dirty water.","zh":"太陽能蒸餾器可以幫助偏遠營地從鹹水或污水中收集飲用水。"},{"en":"Solar stills work slowly, but they can be useful where fuel or electricity is limited.","zh":"太陽能蒸餾器運作較慢，但在燃料或電力有限的地方可以有用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to water-purifying devices powered by the sun.","zh":"這個短語指由太陽供能的淨水裝置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it occurred to someone that","meaning":"某人突然想到","examples":[{"en":"It occurred to Paton that the same process might work in the desert.","zh":"Paton 突然想到，同樣過程可能在沙漠中有效。"},{"en":"It occurred to someone that means someone suddenly realised or thought of an idea.","zh":"it occurred to someone that 指某人突然意識到或想到一個想法。"},{"en":"It occurred to a teacher that students might learn better if examples came from daily life.","zh":"老師突然想到，如果例子來自日常生活，學生可能學得更好。"},{"en":"When a new idea occurs to someone, it may begin as a simple question.","zh":"當一個新想法浮現在某人腦中，它可能只是由一個簡單問題開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the moment an idea enters someone’s mind.","zh":"這個短語描述想法進入某人腦海的一刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be able to produce","meaning":"能夠生產","examples":[{"en":"He wondered whether the system would be able to produce fresh water.","zh":"他想知道該系統是否能夠生產淡水。"},{"en":"To be able to produce something means to have the capacity to make or create it.","zh":"be able to produce something 指有能力製造或創造某物。"},{"en":"A small bakery may be able to produce two hundred loaves every morning.","zh":"小麵包店可能每天早上能夠生產二百條麵包。"},{"en":"If a machine is able to produce clean water, it can help places with limited supplies.","zh":"如果機器能夠生產清潔食水，就可以幫助供水有限的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical capability.","zh":"這個短語描述實際能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in this way","meaning":"以這種方式","examples":[{"en":"Water might be produced in this way simply by cooling humid air.","zh":"水可能以這種方式產生，只需把潮濕空氣冷卻。"},{"en":"In this way means by using the method just described.","zh":"in this way 指使用剛才描述的方法。"},{"en":"A student can improve vocabulary in this way: read, write down useful phrases, and reuse them in sentences.","zh":"學生可以以這種方式改善詞彙：閱讀、寫下有用短語，並在句子中重用。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a result with the method that produces it.","zh":"這個短語把結果與產生結果的方法連接起來。"},{"en":"We use it when explaining how something can be done.","zh":"當解釋某事如何做到時，我們會使用它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"simply by cooling the air","meaning":"只需把空氣冷卻","examples":[{"en":"The system produces water simply by cooling the air.","zh":"該系統只需把空氣冷卻便能產生水。"},{"en":"Simply by cooling the air means using only the cooling of air as the main method.","zh":"simply by cooling the air 指只以冷卻空氣作為主要方法。"},{"en":"A cold window can collect water simply by cooling the air touching it.","zh":"冷窗戶只需把接觸它的空氣冷卻，就可以收集水分。"},{"en":"If warm humid air is cooled enough, water can appear without adding chemicals.","zh":"如果溫暖潮濕的空氣被充分冷卻，不加化學物也可以出現水。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the method is surprisingly simple.","zh":"這個短語強調方法出奇地簡單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"irrigate fields","meaning":"灌溉田地","examples":[{"en":"Paton wondered whether the water could be used to irrigate fields.","zh":"Paton 想知道這些水是否可以用來灌溉田地。"},{"en":"To irrigate fields means to supply water to farmland so crops can grow.","zh":"irrigate fields 指向農田供水，使農作物能生長。"},{"en":"Farmers irrigate fields with pipes, channels, or sprinklers during dry seasons.","zh":"農民在旱季用水管、水渠或灑水器灌溉田地。"},{"en":"Without enough water to irrigate fields, crops may dry out and fail.","zh":"如果沒有足夠水灌溉田地，農作物可能枯乾並歉收。"},{"en":"This phrase describes watering land for agriculture.","zh":"這個短語描述為農業用途給土地供水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"grow crops","meaning":"種植農作物","examples":[{"en":"A reliable water supply would allow farmers to grow crops in the desert.","zh":"可靠水源會讓農民能在沙漠中種植農作物。"},{"en":"To grow crops means to plant and raise food or useful plants.","zh":"grow crops 指種植並培育食物或有用植物。"},{"en":"A family farm may grow crops such as tomatoes, rice, or corn.","zh":"家庭農場可能種植番茄、稻米或粟米等農作物。"},{"en":"Farmers need soil, water, light, and suitable temperatures to grow crops successfully.","zh":"農民需要泥土、水、光線和合適溫度，才能成功種植農作物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes producing plants for food or trade.","zh":"這個短語描述為食物或貿易生產植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a decade on","meaning":"十年後","examples":[{"en":"A decade on, Paton’s original idea had become a working greenhouse.","zh":"十年後，Paton 最初的想法已變成一座能運作的溫室。"},{"en":"A decade on means ten years later.","zh":"a decade on 指十年之後。"},{"en":"A decade on, a small school project may become a city-wide recycling programme.","zh":"十年後，一個小型學校專案可能變成全市回收計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how an idea or situation has changed after ten years.","zh":"這個短語顯示十年後一個想法或情況如何改變。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing an early beginning with a later result.","zh":"它適合用來比較早期開始與後來結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take shape","meaning":"逐漸成形","examples":[{"en":"Paton’s dream eventually took shape as a giant greenhouse.","zh":"Paton 的夢想最終以一座巨型溫室的形式逐漸成形。"},{"en":"To take shape means to gradually become real, clear, or developed.","zh":"take shape 指逐漸變得真實、清楚或發展成熟。"},{"en":"A student’s essay takes shape when the main argument and paragraphs become clear.","zh":"當主要論點和段落變清楚時，學生的作文就逐漸成形。"},{"en":"A project may take shape after people test ideas and solve practical problems.","zh":"人們測試想法並解決實際問題後，項目可能逐漸成形。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an idea becoming a real form.","zh":"這個短語描述想法變成真實形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a giant greenhouse","meaning":"巨型溫室","examples":[{"en":"The project took the form of a giant greenhouse on a desert island.","zh":"該項目以荒漠島嶼上一座巨型溫室的形式出現。"},{"en":"A giant greenhouse is a very large structure where plants are grown under controlled conditions.","zh":"giant greenhouse 指一個很大的建築，用於在受控條件下種植植物。"},{"en":"A giant greenhouse can protect crops from extreme heat, wind, or dryness.","zh":"巨型溫室可以保護農作物免受極端高溫、強風或乾旱影響。"},{"en":"In Paton’s design, the giant greenhouse also cools air and produces fresh water.","zh":"在 Paton 的設計中，巨型溫室也能冷卻空氣並產生淡水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large controlled growing space.","zh":"這個短語描述大型受控種植空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a desert island","meaning":"荒漠島嶼","examples":[{"en":"The first commercial greenhouse was built on a desert island near Abu Dhabi.","zh":"第一座商業溫室建於阿布扎比附近一個荒漠島嶼上。"},{"en":"A desert island is an island with very dry conditions and little natural vegetation.","zh":"desert island 指非常乾燥、天然植被很少的島嶼。"},{"en":"A desert island may have plenty of seawater but very little fresh water.","zh":"荒漠島嶼可能有大量海水，但淡水很少。"},{"en":"Growing food on a desert island is difficult unless people can control heat and water supply.","zh":"除非人們能控制熱力和水源，否則在荒漠島嶼上種植食物很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a dry island environment, not necessarily an empty tropical island.","zh":"這個短語描述乾燥島嶼環境，而不一定是空無一人的熱帶小島。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"off Abu Dhabi","meaning":"位於阿布扎比對開","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse was constructed on an island off Abu Dhabi.","zh":"這座溫室建於阿布扎比對開的一個島上。"},{"en":"Off Abu Dhabi means near the coast of Abu Dhabi, usually in the sea nearby.","zh":"off Abu Dhabi 指在阿布扎比海岸附近，通常位於附近海域。"},{"en":"A small research station may be built on an island off a coastal city.","zh":"小型研究站可能建於某沿海城市對開的島上。"},{"en":"This phrase helps locate something close to, but not inside, the main place.","zh":"這個短語幫助定位某物在主要地方附近，但不在其內部。"},{"en":"It is often used for islands, ships, or coastal areas.","zh":"它常用於島嶼、船隻或沿海地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the Persian Gulf","meaning":"波斯灣","examples":[{"en":"Abu Dhabi lies beside the Persian Gulf.","zh":"阿布扎比位於波斯灣旁邊。"},{"en":"The Persian Gulf is a body of water bordered by several Middle Eastern countries.","zh":"Persian Gulf 指被幾個中東國家包圍的一片水域。"},{"en":"Coastal cities near the Persian Gulf often face heat and water challenges.","zh":"波斯灣附近的沿海城市常面對高溫和水源挑戰。"},{"en":"Seawater from the Persian Gulf can be used in systems that produce fresh water.","zh":"波斯灣的海水可以用於產生淡水的系統。"},{"en":"This phrase names the sea area beside Abu Dhabi and nearby countries.","zh":"這個短語指阿布扎比及附近國家旁邊的海域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the first commercially viable version","meaning":"首個具商業可行性的版本","examples":[{"en":"The project was the first commercially viable version of Paton’s design.","zh":"該項目是 Paton 設計首個具商業可行性的版本。"},{"en":"The first commercially viable version is the first form that can work in business, not just in experiments.","zh":"first commercially viable version 指第一個能在商業上運作，而不只是實驗中的形式。"},{"en":"A new battery may be tested for years before the first commercially viable version is sold.","zh":"新電池可能經過多年測試後，首個具商業可行性的版本才出售。"},{"en":"A design becomes commercially viable when it can cover costs and serve real users.","zh":"當設計能覆蓋成本並服務真實用戶，它就具商業可行性。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the step from prototype to practical business use.","zh":"這個短語標誌從原型走向實際商業用途的一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"commercially viable","meaning":"具商業可行性的","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse had to be commercially viable as well as technically successful.","zh":"這座溫室既要技術上成功，也要具商業可行性。"},{"en":"Commercially viable means able to succeed financially in the real market.","zh":"commercially viable 指能在真實市場中在財政上成功。"},{"en":"A product may work in a lab but not be commercially viable if it is too expensive to make.","zh":"產品可能在實驗室有效，但如果製造成本太高，就不具商業可行性。"},{"en":"Investors usually support designs that are both useful and commercially viable.","zh":"投資者通常支持既有用又具商業可行性的設計。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical business success, not just technical possibility.","zh":"這個短語描述實際商業成功，而不只是技術上可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"seawater greenhouse","meaning":"海水溫室","examples":[{"en":"A seawater greenhouse uses seawater to cool air and produce fresh water.","zh":"海水溫室利用海水來冷卻空氣並產生淡水。"},{"en":"A seawater greenhouse is a greenhouse that uses seawater in its cooling and water-production system.","zh":"seawater greenhouse 指在冷卻和產水系統中使用海水的溫室。"},{"en":"A coastal farm may use a seawater greenhouse when fresh water is scarce.","zh":"當淡水稀少時，沿海農場可能使用海水溫室。"},{"en":"Because it uses seawater, the system is suitable for dry places near the sea.","zh":"由於它使用海水，這個系統適合近海乾旱地區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a greenhouse that turns a local saltwater resource into a farming advantage.","zh":"這個短語描述把本地鹹水資源轉化為農業優勢的溫室。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"local scientists","meaning":"本地科學家","examples":[{"en":"Local scientists worked with Paton on the Abu Dhabi project.","zh":"本地科學家與 Paton 合作進行阿布扎比項目。"},{"en":"Local scientists are researchers who live or work in the area where a project takes place.","zh":"local scientists 指在項目所在地生活或工作的研究人員。"},{"en":"Local scientists can help foreign designers understand climate, soil, and community needs.","zh":"本地科學家可以幫助外來設計者理解氣候、土壤和社區需要。"},{"en":"Projects often improve when local scientists combine regional knowledge with technical expertise.","zh":"當本地科學家把地區知識與技術專長結合，項目通常會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes experts connected to the project location.","zh":"這個短語描述與項目地點有關的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"water the desert","meaning":"灌溉沙漠","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse makes it possible to water part of the desert.","zh":"這座溫室使灌溉部分沙漠成為可能。"},{"en":"To water the desert means to bring water to an extremely dry area so plants can grow.","zh":"water the desert 指把水帶到極乾旱地區，使植物能生長。"},{"en":"Farmers cannot water the desert easily unless they have a reliable source of fresh water.","zh":"除非有可靠淡水來源，否則農民不容易灌溉沙漠。"},{"en":"If technology can water the desert, land that once seemed useless may support crops.","zh":"如果科技能灌溉沙漠，曾經看似無用的土地可能可以支持農作物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making dry land productive through water supply.","zh":"這個短語描述透過供水令乾旱土地具生產力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a dew-making machine","meaning":"製造露水的機器","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse is essentially a giant dew-making machine.","zh":"這座溫室本質上是一部巨型製造露水的機器。"},{"en":"A dew-making machine is a device that creates water droplets by cooling moist air.","zh":"dew-making machine 指透過冷卻潮濕空氣來製造水滴的裝置。"},{"en":"A small dew-making machine could collect water from humid night air in a remote village.","zh":"小型製造露水的機器可以在偏遠村莊從潮濕夜間空氣中收集水。"},{"en":"It works because water vapour becomes liquid when conditions are cool enough.","zh":"它能運作，是因為水蒸氣在足夠冷的條件下會變成液體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a machine that copies the natural formation of dew.","zh":"這個短語描述模仿天然露水形成的機器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"produce fresh water and cool air","meaning":"生產淡水和冷空氣","examples":[{"en":"The system produces fresh water and cool air from seawater and sunlight.","zh":"該系統利用海水和陽光生產淡水和冷空氣。"},{"en":"To produce fresh water and cool air means to create usable non-salty water while lowering air temperature.","zh":"produce fresh water and cool air 指製造可用的非鹹水，同時降低空氣溫度。"},{"en":"A desert greenhouse that can produce fresh water and cool air helps both crops and workers.","zh":"能生產淡水和冷空氣的沙漠溫室，同時幫助農作物和工人。"},{"en":"Producing both water and cooling makes the system more useful than a simple water machine.","zh":"同時產水和冷卻令系統比簡單產水機器更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two practical results from one design.","zh":"這個短語描述一個設計帶來的兩個實際結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"award someone first prize","meaning":"頒發一等獎給某人","examples":[{"en":"The judges awarded Paton first prize in a design competition.","zh":"評判在設計比賽中頒發一等獎給 Paton。"},{"en":"To award someone first prize means to give that person the top honour in a contest.","zh":"award someone first prize 指在比賽中把最高榮譽頒給某人。"},{"en":"A school may award a student first prize for the best science project.","zh":"學校可能因最佳科學專案而頒發一等獎給學生。"},{"en":"Winning first prize can bring attention, funding, and confidence to an inventor.","zh":"贏得一等獎可以為發明者帶來關注、資金和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formally recognising the best entry.","zh":"這個短語描述正式表揚最佳作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a design competition","meaning":"設計比賽","examples":[{"en":"Paton’s invention won first prize in a design competition.","zh":"Paton 的發明在設計比賽中贏得一等獎。"},{"en":"A design competition is a contest where people submit ideas, products, or plans to be judged.","zh":"design competition 指人們提交想法、產品或方案讓評判評審的比賽。"},{"en":"Students may enter a design competition by creating a model bridge or eco-friendly chair.","zh":"學生可能透過製作模型橋或環保椅參加設計比賽。"},{"en":"Design competitions encourage people to solve problems creatively.","zh":"設計比賽鼓勵人創意地解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a contest focused on invention, planning, and practical creativity.","zh":"這個短語描述集中於發明、規劃和實用創意的比賽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a truly original idea","meaning":"真正具原創性的構思","examples":[{"en":"The judges described the greenhouse as a truly original idea.","zh":"評判形容這座溫室是真正具原創性的構思。"},{"en":"A truly original idea is a genuinely new and creative concept, not just a copy of something else.","zh":"truly original idea 指真正新穎和有創意的概念，而不只是複製別人的東西。"},{"en":"A student has a truly original idea when she solves a school problem in a way nobody expected.","zh":"當學生以沒有人預期的方式解決學校問題，她就有真正原創的構思。"},{"en":"Original ideas often combine familiar things in a new and useful way.","zh":"原創想法通常把熟悉事物以新而有用的方式結合。"},{"en":"This phrase praises creativity and freshness.","zh":"這個短語讚揚創意和新鮮感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have the potential to","meaning":"有潛力去……","examples":[{"en":"The design has the potential to improve millions of lives.","zh":"這項設計有潛力改善數百萬人的生活。"},{"en":"To have the potential to do something means to be capable of doing it in the future.","zh":"have the potential to do something 指將來有能力做到某事。"},{"en":"A small reading programme has the potential to improve students’ confidence over time.","zh":"小型閱讀計劃有潛力隨時間改善學生信心。"},{"en":"Potential does not guarantee success, but it shows that the idea could become valuable.","zh":"潛力不保證成功，但顯示想法可能變得有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes future possibility and promise.","zh":"這個短語描述未來可能性和希望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"impact on the lives of","meaning":"對……的生活產生影響","examples":[{"en":"The system could have a major impact on the lives of people in dry regions.","zh":"該系統可以對乾旱地區人民的生活產生重大影響。"},{"en":"An impact on the lives of people is an effect on how they live, work, eat, or stay healthy.","zh":"impact on the lives of people 指對人們如何生活、工作、飲食或保持健康產生影響。"},{"en":"Clean public transport can have a positive impact on the lives of elderly residents.","zh":"清潔公共交通可以對長者居民的生活產生正面影響。"},{"en":"If a technology changes water supply, it can deeply affect daily life.","zh":"如果科技改變供水，它可以深刻影響日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes real effects on people’s everyday experience.","zh":"這個短語描述對人們日常經驗的真實影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"coastal areas","meaning":"沿海地區","examples":[{"en":"The invention is particularly suitable for dry coastal areas.","zh":"這項發明特別適合乾旱沿海地區。"},{"en":"Coastal areas are places near the sea or ocean.","zh":"coastal areas 指靠近海洋的地方。"},{"en":"Coastal areas may have plenty of seawater but not enough fresh water.","zh":"沿海地區可能有大量海水，但淡水不足。"},{"en":"Storms, salt, fishing, tourism, and ports often shape life in coastal areas.","zh":"風暴、鹽分、漁業、旅遊和港口常塑造沿海地區的生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes land close to the coast.","zh":"這個短語描述靠近海岸的土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"water-starved areas","meaning":"嚴重缺水地區","examples":[{"en":"The technology could benefit coastal water-starved areas.","zh":"這項科技可以惠及沿海嚴重缺水地區。"},{"en":"Water-starved areas are places that do not have enough fresh water for people, farms, or industry.","zh":"water-starved areas 指沒有足夠淡水供人、農場或工業使用的地方。"},{"en":"A village may become water-starved after years of drought and population growth.","zh":"多年乾旱和人口增長後，村莊可能變成嚴重缺水地區。"},{"en":"Water-starved areas need reliable sources of water to protect health and food production.","zh":"嚴重缺水地區需要可靠水源，以保護健康和糧食生產。"},{"en":"This phrase describes places suffering from serious water shortage.","zh":"這個短語描述正受嚴重缺水困擾的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"around the world","meaning":"世界各地","examples":[{"en":"Coastal communities around the world could use the system.","zh":"世界各地的沿海社區都可以使用該系統。"},{"en":"Around the world means in many different countries or places globally.","zh":"around the world 指在全球許多不同國家或地方。"},{"en":"Students around the world use online videos to learn languages.","zh":"世界各地的學生使用網上影片學習語言。"},{"en":"If an invention works around the world, it can help people in many climates and cultures.","zh":"如果一項發明能在世界各地運作，它可以幫助不同氣候和文化中的人。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses wide global reach.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛的全球覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as developed by","meaning":"由……所研發的","examples":[{"en":"The seawater greenhouse as developed by Paton has three main parts.","zh":"由 Paton 所研發的海水溫室有三個主要部分。"},{"en":"As developed by someone means in the form designed, improved, or created by that person.","zh":"as developed by someone 指以某人設計、改良或創造出的形式。"},{"en":"The teaching method as developed by the school includes videos, practice, and feedback.","zh":"由該學校研發的教學方法包括影片、練習和回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase gives credit to the person responsible for shaping the idea.","zh":"這個短語把構思成形的功勞歸給相關人士。"},{"en":"It is often used when describing a particular version of a design or theory.","zh":"它常用於描述某設計或理論的特定版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"three main parts","meaning":"三個主要部分","examples":[{"en":"The seawater greenhouse consists of three main parts.","zh":"海水溫室由三個主要部分組成。"},{"en":"Three main parts means three important sections or components that make the system work.","zh":"three main parts 指令系統運作的三個重要部分或組件。"},{"en":"A good essay often has three main parts: introduction, body, and conclusion.","zh":"一篇好文章通常有三個主要部分：引言、正文和結論。"},{"en":"Dividing a system into main parts helps students understand how each part functions.","zh":"把系統分成主要部分，有助學生理解每部分如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the basic structure of something.","zh":"這個短語引出某事物的基本結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"collectively air-condition","meaning":"共同為……調節空氣","examples":[{"en":"The three parts collectively air-condition the greenhouse.","zh":"這三個部分共同為溫室調節空氣。"},{"en":"To collectively air-condition a space means several parts work together to cool and control the air.","zh":"collectively air-condition a space 指幾個部分一起運作，以冷卻並控制空氣。"},{"en":"In a large office, fans, vents, and cooling units collectively air-condition the room.","zh":"在大型辦公室中，風扇、通風口和冷卻裝置共同為房間調節空氣。"},{"en":"If one part fails, the whole cooling process may become less effective.","zh":"如果其中一部分失效，整個冷卻過程可能變得較低效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shared action by different components.","zh":"這個短語描述不同組件共同作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"provide water for irrigation","meaning":"提供灌溉用水","examples":[{"en":"The system provides water for irrigation as well as cooling the air.","zh":"該系統既冷卻空氣，也提供灌溉用水。"},{"en":"To provide water for irrigation means to supply water that can be used to water crops.","zh":"provide water for irrigation 指供應可用來灌溉農作物的水。"},{"en":"A reservoir provides water for irrigation during the dry season.","zh":"水庫在旱季提供灌溉用水。"},{"en":"If a farm cannot get irrigation water, crops may stop growing or die.","zh":"如果農場得不到灌溉用水，農作物可能停止生長或死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes supplying water for agriculture.","zh":"這個短語描述為農業供水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"face into the prevailing wind","meaning":"面向盛行風","examples":[{"en":"The front of the greenhouse faces into the prevailing wind.","zh":"溫室前方朝向盛行風。"},{"en":"To face into the prevailing wind means to point toward the usual direction from which the wind blows.","zh":"face into the prevailing wind 指面向通常吹來的風向。"},{"en":"A wind-powered device may face into the prevailing wind to catch more air.","zh":"風力裝置可能面向盛行風，以捕捉更多空氣。"},{"en":"If a greenhouse faces the wind correctly, air can enter more naturally.","zh":"如果溫室正確面向風向，空氣可以更自然地進入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes positioning a structure to use the regular wind direction.","zh":"這個短語描述把建築定位成利用常見風向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"prevailing wind","meaning":"盛行風","examples":[{"en":"The prevailing wind carries hot, dry air towards the greenhouse.","zh":"盛行風把炎熱乾燥的空氣帶向溫室。"},{"en":"The prevailing wind is the wind that usually blows from a particular direction in an area.","zh":"prevailing wind 指某地區通常從某一方向吹來的風。"},{"en":"Sailors and farmers often pay attention to the prevailing wind.","zh":"水手和農民常會留意盛行風。"},{"en":"Knowing the prevailing wind helps designers decide where to place openings and walls.","zh":"了解盛行風有助設計者決定開口和牆壁的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the most common local wind direction.","zh":"這個短語描述本地最常見的風向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hot, dry air","meaning":"炎熱乾燥的空氣","examples":[{"en":"Hot, dry desert air enters through the front wall.","zh":"炎熱乾燥的沙漠空氣經前牆進入。"},{"en":"Hot, dry air is warm air with very little moisture.","zh":"hot, dry air 指水分很少的暖空氣。"},{"en":"Hot, dry air can make plants lose water quickly through their leaves.","zh":"炎熱乾燥的空氣可以令植物透過葉片快速失水。"},{"en":"In deserts, hot, dry air makes farming difficult without shade and irrigation.","zh":"在沙漠中，沒有遮蔭和灌溉時，炎熱乾燥的空氣令耕作困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the harsh air conditions common in dry climates.","zh":"這個短語描述乾旱氣候中常見的惡劣空氣條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"blow in through","meaning":"經……吹入","examples":[{"en":"Desert air blows in through the front wall of the greenhouse.","zh":"沙漠空氣經溫室前牆吹入。"},{"en":"To blow in through something means to enter through an opening because of wind or airflow.","zh":"blow in through something 指因風或氣流而經某開口進入。"},{"en":"Cold air may blow in through a broken window during winter.","zh":"冬天時，冷空氣可能經破窗吹入。"},{"en":"If air blows in through a wet surface, it can become cooler and moister.","zh":"如果空氣經濕表面吹入，它可以變得較涼和較濕。"},{"en":"This phrase describes air moving into a space through an entrance.","zh":"這個短語描述空氣經入口進入某空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a front wall","meaning":"前牆","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse has a specially designed front wall.","zh":"這座溫室有一面特別設計的前牆。"},{"en":"A front wall is the wall at the front side of a building or structure.","zh":"front wall 指建築或結構前方的一面牆。"},{"en":"A shop’s front wall may include large glass windows to attract customers.","zh":"商店前牆可能包括大型玻璃窗，以吸引顧客。"},{"en":"In the seawater greenhouse, the front wall helps change incoming air.","zh":"在海水溫室中，前牆幫助改變進入的空氣。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the front-facing part of a structure.","zh":"這個短語指出結構面向前方的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"perforated cardboard","meaning":"有孔紙板","examples":[{"en":"The front wall is made from perforated cardboard.","zh":"前牆由有孔紙板製成。"},{"en":"Perforated cardboard is cardboard with many small holes in it.","zh":"perforated cardboard 指有許多小孔的紙板。"},{"en":"Perforated cardboard lets air pass through while still holding water on its surface.","zh":"有孔紙板讓空氣通過，同時仍能在表面保持水分。"},{"en":"If seawater flows over perforated cardboard, incoming air can be cooled and moistened.","zh":"如果海水流過有孔紙板，進入的空氣可以被冷卻並加濕。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple material designed to let air move through it.","zh":"這個短語描述一種讓空氣穿過的簡單材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be kept moist","meaning":"保持濕潤","examples":[{"en":"The cardboard is kept moist with seawater.","zh":"紙板以海水保持濕潤。"},{"en":"To be kept moist means to be kept slightly wet, not dry.","zh":"be kept moist 指保持微濕，而不是乾燥。"},{"en":"Garden soil must be kept moist when young seeds are starting to grow.","zh":"幼苗開始生長時，園土必須保持濕潤。"},{"en":"If the cardboard is kept moist, air passing through it can pick up water vapour.","zh":"如果紙板保持濕潤，穿過它的空氣可以吸收水蒸氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes maintaining a wet condition over time.","zh":"這個短語描述長時間維持潮濕狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a constant trickle of","meaning":"持續流動的少量……","examples":[{"en":"A constant trickle of seawater flows over the cardboard.","zh":"持續流動的少量海水流過紙板。"},{"en":"A constant trickle of something is a small but continuous flow of liquid.","zh":"constant trickle of something 指少量但持續流動的液體。"},{"en":"A constant trickle of water from a tap can waste a surprising amount over a day.","zh":"水龍頭持續流出少量水，一天下來也可能浪費驚人的水量。"},{"en":"In the greenhouse, a constant trickle keeps the cardboard wet without flooding it.","zh":"在溫室中，持續少量水流讓紙板保持濕潤而不被淹沒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a steady, gentle flow.","zh":"這個短語描述穩定而輕微的流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be pumped up from","meaning":"從……抽上來","examples":[{"en":"Seawater is pumped up from the ocean.","zh":"海水從海洋中被抽上來。"},{"en":"To be pumped up from somewhere means to be moved upward from that place using a pump.","zh":"be pumped up from somewhere 指用泵把某物從某地方向上移動。"},{"en":"Water can be pumped up from an underground well to supply a village.","zh":"水可以從地下井抽上來供應村莊。"},{"en":"If seawater is pumped up from the ocean, it can be used in cooling and desalination systems.","zh":"如果海水從海洋抽上來，它可以用於冷卻和化淡系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mechanically lifting liquid from a lower source.","zh":"這個短語描述用機械方式把液體從較低來源提升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the purpose is to","meaning":"目的是","examples":[{"en":"The purpose is to cool and moisten the incoming air.","zh":"目的是冷卻並加濕進入的空氣。"},{"en":"The purpose is to means the main aim or reason is to do something.","zh":"the purpose is to 指主要目標或原因是做某事。"},{"en":"The purpose of a fire drill is to help students leave the building safely.","zh":"火警演習的目的是幫助學生安全離開建築物。"},{"en":"Stating the purpose helps readers understand why a design or action exists.","zh":"說明目的有助讀者理解設計或行動為何存在。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the reason behind a process.","zh":"這個短語引出過程背後的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cool and moisten","meaning":"冷卻並加濕","examples":[{"en":"The wet wall cools and moistens the desert air.","zh":"濕牆會冷卻並加濕沙漠空氣。"},{"en":"To cool and moisten air means to lower its temperature and add water vapour to it.","zh":"cool and moisten air 指降低空氣溫度並加入水蒸氣。"},{"en":"A humidifier can moisten dry room air, while a fan may help cool it.","zh":"加濕器可以加濕乾燥室內空氣，而風扇可能幫助冷卻它。"},{"en":"Cooling and moistening air can make conditions better for plants and people.","zh":"冷卻並加濕空氣可以令植物和人的環境更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing air from hot and dry to cooler and wetter.","zh":"這個短語描述把空氣由炎熱乾燥變成較涼較濕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"incoming desert air","meaning":"進入的沙漠空氣","examples":[{"en":"The first wall changes the temperature and humidity of the incoming desert air.","zh":"第一面牆改變進入的沙漠空氣的溫度和濕度。"},{"en":"Incoming desert air is the hot, dry air entering from the desert outside.","zh":"incoming desert air 指從外面沙漠進入的炎熱乾燥空氣。"},{"en":"A greenhouse must treat incoming desert air before it reaches delicate plants.","zh":"溫室必須先處理進入的沙漠空氣，才讓它接觸脆弱植物。"},{"en":"If incoming desert air is not cooled, plants may lose water too quickly.","zh":"如果進入的沙漠空氣沒有被冷卻，植物可能太快失水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes desert air as it enters a structure.","zh":"這個短語描述沙漠空氣進入結構時的狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"allow plants to grow faster","meaning":"讓植物生長得更快","examples":[{"en":"The cool, moist air allows the plants to grow faster.","zh":"涼爽濕潤的空氣讓植物生長得更快。"},{"en":"To allow plants to grow faster means to create conditions that help plants develop more quickly.","zh":"allow plants to grow faster 指創造有助植物更快發育的條件。"},{"en":"Good soil and regular watering allow vegetables to grow faster in a school garden.","zh":"良好泥土和定期澆水讓學校花園的蔬菜生長得更快。"},{"en":"Plants grow faster when they lose less water and receive enough light.","zh":"當植物失水較少並得到足夠光線時，會生長得更快。"},{"en":"This phrase links better conditions with quicker plant growth.","zh":"這個短語把較好條件與更快植物生長連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"crucially","meaning":"關鍵的是","examples":[{"en":"Crucially, the cooler conditions reduce water loss from the plants.","zh":"關鍵的是，較涼條件會減少植物失水。"},{"en":"Crucially means most importantly, especially when the next point is essential.","zh":"crucially 指最重要的是，尤其當下一點是必要時。"},{"en":"Crucially, students must read the question carefully before writing an answer.","zh":"關鍵的是，學生寫答案前必須仔細讀題。"},{"en":"This word signals that the following information is central to understanding the argument.","zh":"這個字表示接下來的資料對理解論點很核心。"},{"en":"We use it to highlight the key reason something works.","zh":"我們用它來突出某事有效的關鍵原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"much less water evaporates","meaning":"蒸發的水分少得多","examples":[{"en":"Much less water evaporates from leaves inside the greenhouse.","zh":"溫室內葉片蒸發的水分少得多。"},{"en":"Much less water evaporates means a far smaller amount of water turns into vapour and leaves a surface.","zh":"much less water evaporates 指少得多的水變成水蒸氣並離開表面。"},{"en":"In a cool room, much less water evaporates from a wet towel than under hot sun.","zh":"在涼爽房間中，濕毛巾蒸發的水分比在烈日下少得多。"},{"en":"If less water evaporates from plants, they need less irrigation.","zh":"如果植物蒸發的水分較少，它們需要的灌溉也較少。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how cooler conditions save water.","zh":"這個短語解釋較涼條件如何節省水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"evaporate from the leaves","meaning":"從葉片蒸發","examples":[{"en":"In hot conditions, large quantities of water evaporate from the leaves.","zh":"在炎熱條件下，大量水分會從葉片蒸發。"},{"en":"To evaporate from the leaves means water leaves plant leaves as vapour.","zh":"evaporate from the leaves 指水分以水蒸氣形式離開植物葉片。"},{"en":"On a hot afternoon, water can evaporate from the leaves of garden plants very quickly.","zh":"炎熱下午，水分可以很快從園中植物葉片蒸發。"},{"en":"When too much water evaporates from leaves, plants may wilt.","zh":"當太多水分從葉片蒸發，植物可能枯萎。"},{"en":"This phrase describes plant water loss into the air.","zh":"這個短語描述植物水分流失到空氣中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"need much less moisture","meaning":"所需水分少得多","examples":[{"en":"The plants need much less moisture in the cooler greenhouse.","zh":"在較涼的溫室中，植物所需水分少得多。"},{"en":"To need much less moisture means to require far less water or humidity.","zh":"need much less moisture 指需要少得多的水分或濕度。"},{"en":"Indoor plants need much less moisture in winter than in a hot, dry summer.","zh":"室內植物在冬天所需水分比炎熱乾燥夏天少得多。"},{"en":"If air is cooler and less drying, plants do not need as much water to survive.","zh":"如果空氣較涼且較不乾燥，植物生存所需的水就不那麼多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reduced water requirement.","zh":"這個短語描述水分需求減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be irrigated in","meaning":"在……環境下接受灌溉","examples":[{"en":"The same plants would require more water if they were irrigated in desert air.","zh":"如果同樣植物在沙漠空氣中接受灌溉，就需要更多水。"},{"en":"To be irrigated in a condition means to be watered while growing under that condition.","zh":"be irrigated in a condition 指在某種條件下生長時接受澆水。"},{"en":"Crops irrigated in hot open fields may need more water than crops under shade.","zh":"在炎熱露天田地中灌溉的作物，可能比在遮蔭下的作物需要更多水。"},{"en":"If plants are irrigated in dry air, much of the water may be lost through evaporation.","zh":"如果植物在乾燥空氣中接受灌溉，許多水可能因蒸發而流失。"},{"en":"This phrase connects watering with the surrounding growing environment.","zh":"這個短語把灌溉與周圍生長環境連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"outside the greenhouse","meaning":"在溫室外","examples":[{"en":"The air outside the greenhouse is much hotter and drier.","zh":"溫室外的空氣熱得多也乾得多。"},{"en":"Outside the greenhouse means in the area beyond the greenhouse structure.","zh":"outside the greenhouse 指在溫室結構以外的區域。"},{"en":"Workers may feel the difference immediately when they step outside the greenhouse.","zh":"工人一走到溫室外，可能立即感到差別。"},{"en":"If outside air is too hot, the greenhouse must control conditions inside carefully.","zh":"如果外面空氣太熱，溫室必須仔細控制內部條件。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the protected inside with the natural outside environment.","zh":"這個短語對比受保護的內部與自然外部環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the interior of","meaning":"……的內部","examples":[{"en":"The roof helps control the temperature of the interior of the greenhouse.","zh":"屋頂幫助控制溫室內部的溫度。"},{"en":"The interior of something means the inside part or inner space of it.","zh":"interior of something 指某物的內部部分或內部空間。"},{"en":"The interior of a classroom should be bright, safe, and comfortable for students.","zh":"課室內部應明亮、安全並令學生舒適。"},{"en":"Controlling the interior of a greenhouse helps protect plants from outside weather.","zh":"控制溫室內部有助保護植物免受外面天氣影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the inside area of a structure.","zh":"這個短語描述結構的內部區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be completed by","meaning":"由……完成","examples":[{"en":"The air-conditioning process is completed by the specially designed roof.","zh":"空氣調節過程由特別設計的屋頂完成。"},{"en":"To be completed by something means the final necessary part is provided by it.","zh":"be completed by something 指由某物提供最後所需部分。"},{"en":"A meal may be completed by a simple dessert after the main course.","zh":"主菜後一道簡單甜品可以令一餐完整。"},{"en":"In the greenhouse, the cooling process is not finished until the roof controls heat and light.","zh":"在溫室中，直到屋頂控制熱力和光線，冷卻過程才完成。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the part that finishes a process.","zh":"這個短語指出完成過程的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the second feature","meaning":"第二項設計特色","examples":[{"en":"The roof is the second major feature of the system.","zh":"屋頂是該系統的第二項主要設計特色。"},{"en":"The second feature means the second important design element being described.","zh":"second feature 指正在描述的第二個重要設計元素。"},{"en":"In a good app, the second feature might be reminders after the first feature of tracking progress.","zh":"在好應用程式中，第一項功能可能是追蹤進度，第二項功能可能是提醒。"},{"en":"Listing features one by one helps readers understand a complex design.","zh":"逐項列出特色有助讀者理解複雜設計。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces another important part of a system.","zh":"這個短語引出系統的另一個重要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have two layers","meaning":"有兩層","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse roof has two separate layers.","zh":"溫室屋頂有兩個分開的層面。"},{"en":"To have two layers means to contain two sheets, levels, or surfaces placed one over the other.","zh":"have two layers 指有兩片、兩層或兩個表面一上一下放置。"},{"en":"A winter jacket may have two layers to keep warm air inside and cold air outside.","zh":"冬天外套可能有兩層，以把暖空氣留在內，把冷空氣擋在外。"},{"en":"Two layers can perform different jobs, such as admitting light and blocking heat.","zh":"兩層可以執行不同功能，例如讓光進入並阻隔熱力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a double structure.","zh":"這個短語描述雙層結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an outer layer","meaning":"外層","examples":[{"en":"The outer layer of the roof is made of clear polyethylene.","zh":"屋頂外層由透明聚乙烯製成。"},{"en":"An outer layer is the outside sheet or surface of a structure.","zh":"outer layer 指結構外面的片層或表面。"},{"en":"The outer layer of a lunch box protects the food inside.","zh":"飯盒外層保護裡面的食物。"},{"en":"In the greenhouse roof, the outer layer lets visible light pass through.","zh":"在溫室屋頂中，外層讓可見光穿過。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the layer closest to the outside environment.","zh":"這個短語描述最接近外部環境的一層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"clear polyethylene","meaning":"透明聚乙烯","examples":[{"en":"Visible light passes through the clear polyethylene layer.","zh":"可見光穿過透明聚乙烯層。"},{"en":"Clear polyethylene is a transparent plastic material that lets light pass through.","zh":"clear polyethylene 是一種透明塑膠材料，可以讓光線穿過。"},{"en":"Some food bags are made from clear polyethylene so people can see what is inside.","zh":"有些食物袋由透明聚乙烯製成，讓人能看見裡面的東西。"},{"en":"In a greenhouse, clear polyethylene can admit sunlight while protecting plants from wind.","zh":"在溫室中，透明聚乙烯可以讓陽光進入，同時保護植物免受風影響。"},{"en":"This phrase names a light-transmitting plastic material.","zh":"這個短語指一種透光塑膠材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"an inner coated layer","meaning":"內層塗層","examples":[{"en":"The inner coated layer reflects infrared radiation.","zh":"內層塗層反射紅外線輻射。"},{"en":"An inner coated layer is the inside layer covered with a special material for a particular purpose.","zh":"inner coated layer 指內側被特殊材料覆蓋，以達到某特定目的的一層。"},{"en":"A lunch flask may have an inner coated layer that helps keep drinks warm.","zh":"保溫瓶可能有內層塗層，幫助飲品保持溫暖。"},{"en":"In the greenhouse, the coating helps reflect heat away from the plants.","zh":"在溫室中，塗層幫助把熱力反射離開植物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a treated inner surface.","zh":"這個短語描述經處理的內部表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"reflect infrared radiation","meaning":"反射紅外線輻射","examples":[{"en":"The roof coating reflects infrared radiation away from the plants.","zh":"屋頂塗層把紅外線輻射反射離開植物。"},{"en":"To reflect infrared radiation means to send heat-related radiation back instead of allowing it through.","zh":"reflect infrared radiation 指把與熱有關的輻射反射回去，而不是讓它穿過。"},{"en":"Special window films can reflect infrared radiation to keep rooms cooler.","zh":"特殊窗膜可以反射紅外線輻射，使房間保持較涼。"},{"en":"If infrared radiation is reflected away, plants receive light without too much heat.","zh":"如果紅外線輻射被反射走，植物可以得到光線而不承受太多熱力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes blocking heat while managing light.","zh":"這個短語描述在管理光線的同時阻隔熱力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"infrared radiation","meaning":"紅外線輻射","examples":[{"en":"Infrared radiation carries heat that could damage the plants.","zh":"紅外線輻射帶有可能傷害植物的熱力。"},{"en":"Infrared radiation is a form of energy associated with heat and not visible to the human eye.","zh":"infrared radiation 是一種與熱相關、肉眼不可見的能量形式。"},{"en":"Remote controls and heat cameras use infrared radiation in different ways.","zh":"遙控器和熱成像相機以不同方式使用紅外線輻射。"},{"en":"Too much infrared radiation can make a greenhouse too hot for crops.","zh":"太多紅外線輻射可以令溫室對農作物而言太熱。"},{"en":"This term helps explain how sunlight can bring both light and heat.","zh":"這個術語幫助解釋陽光如何同時帶來光和熱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"this combination ensures that","meaning":"這種組合確保","examples":[{"en":"This combination ensures that light enters while excess heat is excluded.","zh":"這種組合確保光線進入，而多餘熱力被排除。"},{"en":"This combination ensures that means these parts together make a result certain or very likely.","zh":"this combination ensures that 指這些部分共同作用，令某結果確定或很可能發生。"},{"en":"Clear rules and regular practice ensure that students know what to do in an exam.","zh":"清晰規則和定期練習確保學生知道考試時要做甚麼。"},{"en":"In the roof, the two layers work together so light enters but heat is controlled.","zh":"在屋頂中，兩層共同運作，使光線進入但熱力受控。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how combined features produce a planned effect.","zh":"這個短語解釋結合的特色如何產生預期效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"visible light","meaning":"可見光","examples":[{"en":"Visible light passes through the roof to the plants.","zh":"可見光穿過屋頂到達植物。"},{"en":"Visible light is the part of light that human eyes can see.","zh":"visible light 指人眼可以看見的光線部分。"},{"en":"Plants need visible light for photosynthesis and healthy growth.","zh":"植物需要可見光進行光合作用和健康生長。"},{"en":"A window that admits visible light can make a room bright without turning on lamps.","zh":"讓可見光進入的窗戶可以令房間明亮，而不用開燈。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts light we can see with invisible heat radiation.","zh":"這個短語把我們看得見的光與看不見的熱輻射作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stream through","meaning":"大量穿過","examples":[{"en":"Sunlight can stream through the clear outer roof.","zh":"陽光可以大量穿過透明外層屋頂。"},{"en":"To stream through means to flow or pass through in a steady or strong way.","zh":"stream through 指以持續或強烈方式流過或穿過。"},{"en":"Morning light streams through the classroom windows and brightens the desks.","zh":"早晨陽光大量穿過課室窗戶，照亮書桌。"},{"en":"If sunlight streams through the roof, plants can receive enough light to grow.","zh":"如果陽光穿過屋頂，植物可以得到足夠光線生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes light, air, or people moving continuously through an opening.","zh":"這個短語描述光、空氣或人群持續穿過開口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"maximise the rate of","meaning":"將……的速度提升至最高","examples":[{"en":"The design maximises the rate of plant growth.","zh":"這項設計將植物生長速度提升至最高。"},{"en":"To maximise the rate of something means to make its speed or level as high as possible.","zh":"maximise the rate of something 指令某事的速度或水平盡可能高。"},{"en":"A study plan can maximise the rate of improvement by mixing practice with feedback.","zh":"學習計劃可以透過結合練習和回饋，將進步速度提升至最高。"},{"en":"In the greenhouse, good light and cooler air help maximise plant growth.","zh":"在溫室中，良好光線和較涼空氣幫助最大化植物生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing a process to its best possible level.","zh":"這個短語描述把某過程提升至最佳可能水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"plant growth","meaning":"植物生長","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse creates favourable conditions for plant growth.","zh":"這座溫室為植物生長創造有利條件。"},{"en":"Plant growth is the process by which plants become larger, stronger, and more developed.","zh":"plant growth 指植物變得更大、更強壯和更成熟的過程。"},{"en":"Plant growth needs light, water, nutrients, and suitable temperature.","zh":"植物生長需要光、水、養分和合適溫度。"},{"en":"Poor soil or too much heat can slow plant growth.","zh":"貧瘠土壤或過多熱力可以拖慢植物生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the development of plants over time.","zh":"這個短語描述植物隨時間發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"through photosynthesis","meaning":"透過光合作用","examples":[{"en":"Visible light supports plant growth through photosynthesis.","zh":"可見光透過光合作用支援植物生長。"},{"en":"Through photosynthesis means by the process plants use to turn light, water, and carbon dioxide into food.","zh":"through photosynthesis 指透過植物把光、水和二氧化碳轉化為養分的過程。"},{"en":"Leaves use sunlight through photosynthesis to produce energy for the plant.","zh":"葉片透過光合作用利用陽光為植物產生能量。"},{"en":"Without enough light for photosynthesis, plants may grow slowly or weakly.","zh":"沒有足夠光線進行光合作用，植物可能生長緩慢或虛弱。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the biological process that connects light with plant growth.","zh":"這個短語解釋把光線與植物生長連起來的生物過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"與此同時","examples":[{"en":"The roof admits light and, at the same time, keeps heat away.","zh":"屋頂讓光線進入，與此同時把熱力隔開。"},{"en":"At the same time means two things happen together or are true together.","zh":"at the same time 指兩件事同時發生或同時成立。"},{"en":"A good teacher can be kind and, at the same time, set clear rules.","zh":"好老師可以善良，與此同時設定清晰規則。"},{"en":"In design, one feature may solve one problem while at the same time preventing another.","zh":"在設計中，一項特色可能解決一個問題，與此同時防止另一個問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows two simultaneous effects.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個同時發生的效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be trapped between","meaning":"被困在……之間","examples":[{"en":"Heat is trapped in the space between the two roof layers.","zh":"熱力被困在兩層屋頂之間的空間。"},{"en":"To be trapped between two things means to be held or stuck in the space separating them.","zh":"be trapped between two things 指被困住或留在兩者之間的空間。"},{"en":"Air can be trapped between two layers of clothing and keep the body warm.","zh":"空氣可以被困在兩層衣物之間，使身體保持溫暖。"},{"en":"If heat is trapped between roof layers, it can be kept away from the plants below.","zh":"如果熱力被困在屋頂層之間，它就可以遠離下方植物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something being held in an in-between space.","zh":"這個短語描述某物被留在中間空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be kept away from","meaning":"遠離……","examples":[{"en":"Infrared heat is kept away from the plants.","zh":"紅外線熱力被保持遠離植物。"},{"en":"To be kept away from something means to be prevented from reaching or touching it.","zh":"be kept away from something 指被阻止到達或接觸某物。"},{"en":"Cleaning chemicals should be kept away from young children.","zh":"清潔化學品應遠離幼童。"},{"en":"If too much heat is kept away from crops, they can grow in safer conditions.","zh":"如果過多熱力遠離農作物，它們可以在較安全條件下生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protection through separation.","zh":"這個短語描述透過分隔來保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"keep the air cool","meaning":"令空氣保持涼快","examples":[{"en":"The roof helps keep the air around the plants cool.","zh":"屋頂幫助令植物周圍的空氣保持涼快。"},{"en":"To keep the air cool means to maintain a lower, more comfortable air temperature.","zh":"keep the air cool 指維持較低、較舒適的空氣溫度。"},{"en":"Curtains can help keep the air cool in a classroom during hot afternoons.","zh":"炎熱下午，窗簾可以幫助令課室空氣保持涼快。"},{"en":"Cool air reduces stress on plants and lowers their need for water.","zh":"涼爽空氣減少植物壓力，並降低它們對水分的需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes maintaining cooler conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述維持較涼條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at the back of","meaning":"在……的後方","examples":[{"en":"The main water-production unit sits at the back of the greenhouse.","zh":"主要產水裝置位於溫室後方。"},{"en":"At the back of something means in the rear part or behind the main area.","zh":"at the back of something 指在某物的後部或主要區域後面。"},{"en":"The emergency exit is at the back of the classroom.","zh":"緊急出口位於課室後方。"},{"en":"Placing a machine at the back can keep the front area clear for movement.","zh":"把機器放在後方可以讓前方區域保持通行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location inside or behind a space.","zh":"這個短語描述某空間內部或後面的方位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the third element","meaning":"第三個組成部分","examples":[{"en":"The condenser system forms the third element of the greenhouse.","zh":"冷凝器系統構成溫室的第三個組成部分。"},{"en":"The third element means the third important part in a system or explanation.","zh":"third element 指系統或解釋中的第三個重要部分。"},{"en":"In a study plan, the third element might be review after learning and practice.","zh":"在學習計劃中，學習和練習後的第三個組成部分可能是重溫。"},{"en":"Naming the third element helps readers complete the structure of the design.","zh":"指出第三個組成部分有助讀者完整理解設計結構。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the final or another major component.","zh":"這個短語引出最後或另一個主要組件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the main water-production unit","meaning":"主要產水裝置","examples":[{"en":"The third element is the main water-production unit.","zh":"第三個組成部分是主要產水裝置。"},{"en":"The main water-production unit is the central part of a system that creates or collects water.","zh":"main water-production unit 指系統中負責產生或收集水的核心部分。"},{"en":"In a desalination plant, the main water-production unit removes salt from seawater.","zh":"在海水化淡廠中，主要產水裝置會從海水中去除鹽分。"},{"en":"If this unit fails, the system may still cool air but produce little water.","zh":"如果這個裝置失效，系統可能仍能冷卻空氣，但產水很少。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the key part responsible for making water.","zh":"這個短語指出負責造水的關鍵部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hit a second wall","meaning":"接觸第二面牆","examples":[{"en":"The air hits a second moist cardboard wall.","zh":"空氣接觸第二面濕紙板牆。"},{"en":"To hit a second wall means to reach and come into contact with another wall after passing through the first area.","zh":"hit a second wall 指穿過第一區域後到達並接觸另一面牆。"},{"en":"In a filter system, dirty air may hit a second wall of material for extra cleaning.","zh":"在過濾系統中，骯髒空氣可能接觸第二層材料，以進一步清潔。"},{"en":"When air hits a moist wall, it can take up more water vapour.","zh":"當空氣接觸濕牆，它可以吸收更多水蒸氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes air moving into contact with another barrier or surface.","zh":"這個短語描述空氣移動並接觸另一個屏障或表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"increase its humidity","meaning":"提高其濕度","examples":[{"en":"The second wet wall increases the humidity of the air.","zh":"第二面濕牆提高空氣濕度。"},{"en":"To increase its humidity means to raise the amount of water vapour in the air.","zh":"increase its humidity 指提高空氣中的水蒸氣含量。"},{"en":"A humidifier increases the humidity of a dry bedroom in winter.","zh":"加濕器在冬天提高乾燥睡房的濕度。"},{"en":"Increasing air humidity can help prepare the air for condensation later.","zh":"提高空氣濕度可以幫助空氣之後進行凝結。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making air wetter.","zh":"這個短語描述令空氣更濕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reach the condenser","meaning":"到達冷凝器","examples":[{"en":"The humid air eventually reaches the condenser.","zh":"潮濕空氣最終到達冷凝器。"},{"en":"To reach the condenser means to arrive at the part of the machine where moisture is cooled and collected.","zh":"reach the condenser 指到達機器中冷卻並收集水分的部分。"},{"en":"In a cooling system, warm air must reach the condenser before water can form.","zh":"在冷卻系統中，暖空氣必須到達冷凝器，水才能形成。"},{"en":"If air does not reach the condenser, the system cannot collect much moisture.","zh":"如果空氣不到達冷凝器，系統就不能收集太多水分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes air arriving at the water-collecting unit.","zh":"這個短語描述空氣到達集水裝置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"condenser","meaning":"冷凝器","examples":[{"en":"The condenser removes moisture from the hot, humid air.","zh":"冷凝器從炎熱潮濕的空氣中去除水分。"},{"en":"A condenser is a device that cools vapour so it becomes liquid.","zh":"condenser 指冷卻蒸氣，使其變成液體的裝置。"},{"en":"An air conditioner has a condenser that helps remove heat and moisture.","zh":"冷氣機有冷凝器，幫助去除熱力和水分。"},{"en":"In Paton’s greenhouse, the condenser turns humid air into distilled water.","zh":"在 Paton 的溫室中，冷凝器把潮濕空氣轉化為蒸餾水。"},{"en":"This word names the machine part that makes condensation useful.","zh":"這個字指出令凝結作用變得有用的機器部件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"collect moisture from","meaning":"從……收集水分","examples":[{"en":"The condenser collects moisture from the air.","zh":"冷凝器從空氣中收集水分。"},{"en":"To collect moisture from something means to gather water vapour or droplets from it.","zh":"collect moisture from something 指從某物中收集水蒸氣或水滴。"},{"en":"A dehumidifier collects moisture from a damp room.","zh":"抽濕機從潮濕房間中收集水分。"},{"en":"If a machine collects moisture from humid air, it may produce usable water.","zh":"如果機器從潮濕空氣中收集水分，它可能產生可用水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes removing water from air or another source.","zh":"這個短語描述從空氣或其他來源移除水分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"irrigate the plants","meaning":"灌溉植物","examples":[{"en":"The collected water is used to irrigate the plants.","zh":"收集到的水用來灌溉植物。"},{"en":"To irrigate the plants means to water them in a planned way so they can grow.","zh":"irrigate the plants 指有計劃地給植物供水，使其生長。"},{"en":"A gardener irrigates tomato plants with a drip system during hot weather.","zh":"園丁在炎熱天氣用滴灌系統灌溉番茄植物。"},{"en":"If plants are not irrigated regularly, their leaves may wilt and their growth may slow.","zh":"如果植物沒有定期灌溉，葉片可能枯萎，生長也可能放慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes supplying water directly to plants.","zh":"這個短語描述直接向植物供水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a metal surface","meaning":"金屬表面","examples":[{"en":"The condenser consists of a cool metal surface.","zh":"冷凝器由一個冷金屬表面組成。"},{"en":"A metal surface is the outer area of an object made of metal.","zh":"metal surface 指由金屬製成物件的外部表面。"},{"en":"Water droplets often form on a cold metal surface in a humid room.","zh":"在潮濕房間中，水滴常在冷金屬表面形成。"},{"en":"Metal can conduct heat well, so it is useful in cooling equipment.","zh":"金屬導熱良好，因此在冷卻設備中很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the surface where condensation may occur.","zh":"這個短語描述可能發生凝結的表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be kept cool by","meaning":"由……保持低溫","examples":[{"en":"The metal surface is kept cool by additional seawater.","zh":"金屬表面由額外海水保持低溫。"},{"en":"To be kept cool by something means to stay at a low temperature because that thing removes heat.","zh":"be kept cool by something 指因某物移除熱力而保持低溫。"},{"en":"A laptop may be kept cool by a small fan inside it.","zh":"手提電腦可能由內部小風扇保持低溫。"},{"en":"If the condenser is kept cool, humid air touching it can release water.","zh":"如果冷凝器保持低溫，接觸它的潮濕空氣就能釋放水分。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what maintains a low temperature.","zh":"這個短語解釋甚麼維持低溫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"still more seawater","meaning":"更多海水","examples":[{"en":"Still more seawater is used to cool the condenser.","zh":"更多海水被用來冷卻冷凝器。"},{"en":"Still more seawater means an additional amount of seawater beyond what has already been used.","zh":"still more seawater 指在已使用的海水之外，再額外使用的海水。"},{"en":"A factory may need still more water if production increases in summer.","zh":"如果夏季產量增加，工廠可能需要更多水。"},{"en":"In the greenhouse, seawater is used more than once for different cooling purposes.","zh":"在溫室中，海水被多次用於不同冷卻目的。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that extra seawater is needed for another stage.","zh":"這個短語強調另一階段需要額外海水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the equivalent of","meaning":"相當於……的東西","examples":[{"en":"The condenser is the equivalent of the cold window on Paton’s bus.","zh":"冷凝器相當於 Paton 巴士上的冷窗戶。"},{"en":"The equivalent of something means something that has the same function, value, or effect.","zh":"equivalent of something 指具有相同功能、價值或效果的東西。"},{"en":"In online learning, a discussion board can be the equivalent of a classroom conversation.","zh":"在網上學習中，討論區可以相當於課堂對話。"},{"en":"The condenser plays the same role as the cold bus window because both cause condensation.","zh":"冷凝器扮演與冷巴士車窗相同的角色，因為兩者都造成凝結。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain a new idea by comparing it to a familiar one.","zh":"這個短語透過把新想法與熟悉事物比較來幫助解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pure distilled water","meaning":"純蒸餾水","examples":[{"en":"The condenser produces drops of pure distilled water.","zh":"冷凝器產生一滴滴純蒸餾水。"},{"en":"Pure distilled water is clean water produced by evaporation and condensation, with many impurities removed.","zh":"pure distilled water 指透過蒸發和凝結產生、去除了許多雜質的清潔水。"},{"en":"A science lab may use pure distilled water for experiments because ordinary tap water contains minerals.","zh":"科學實驗室可能使用純蒸餾水做實驗，因為普通自來水含有礦物質。"},{"en":"Distilled water is useful when salt or dirt must be left behind.","zh":"當鹽分或污垢必須被留下時，蒸餾水很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very clean water made through distillation.","zh":"這個短語描述透過蒸餾製成的非常清潔的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"form on the condenser","meaning":"在冷凝器上形成","examples":[{"en":"Drops of distilled water form on the condenser.","zh":"蒸餾水滴在冷凝器上形成。"},{"en":"To form on the condenser means to appear on its cool surface as vapour turns into liquid.","zh":"form on the condenser 指蒸氣變成液體時，在其冷表面上出現。"},{"en":"Water droplets form on a cold bottle in the same way they form on the condenser.","zh":"水滴在冷瓶子上形成的方式，與在冷凝器上形成相似。"},{"en":"If the condenser surface is not cold enough, fewer drops will form on it.","zh":"如果冷凝器表面不夠冷，形成的水滴會較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where condensation becomes visible.","zh":"這個短語描述凝結作用在哪裡變得可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"flow into a tank","meaning":"流入水箱","examples":[{"en":"The water flows into a tank for storage and irrigation.","zh":"水流入水箱，以供儲存和灌溉。"},{"en":"To flow into a tank means to move as liquid into a container designed to hold it.","zh":"flow into a tank 指液體流入設計用來盛載它的容器。"},{"en":"Rainwater can flow into a tank from a roof during a storm.","zh":"暴雨時，雨水可以從屋頂流入水箱。"},{"en":"Storing water in a tank makes it available for later use.","zh":"把水儲存在水箱中，可以讓它之後使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes liquid being collected in a storage container.","zh":"這個短語描述液體被收集到儲存容器中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"irrigate the crops","meaning":"灌溉農作物","examples":[{"en":"The collected water is used to irrigate the crops.","zh":"收集到的水用來灌溉農作物。"},{"en":"To irrigate the crops means to supply water to cultivated plants such as vegetables or grain.","zh":"irrigate the crops 指向蔬菜或穀物等栽培植物供水。"},{"en":"Farmers irrigate the crops early in the morning to reduce evaporation.","zh":"農民在清晨灌溉農作物，以減少蒸發。"},{"en":"If crops are not irrigated during dry weather, yields may fall.","zh":"如果乾旱天氣中農作物沒有被灌溉，產量可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes watering farm plants for production.","zh":"這個短語描述為生產而給農作物供水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"more or less","meaning":"大致上；差不多","examples":[{"en":"The Abu Dhabi greenhouse more or less runs itself.","zh":"阿布扎比的溫室大致上可以自行運作。"},{"en":"More or less means almost, approximately, or mostly true.","zh":"more or less 指幾乎、大約或大致如此。"},{"en":"After a month of practice, the student more or less understood the grammar rule.","zh":"練習一個月後，學生大致上明白了文法規則。"},{"en":"If a machine more or less runs itself, people still check it but do not control every step.","zh":"如果機器大致上自行運作，人們仍會檢查它，但不控制每一步。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a careful, not absolute, statement.","zh":"這個短語給出謹慎而非絕對的說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"run itself","meaning":"自行運作","examples":[{"en":"Once properly adjusted, the greenhouse can largely run itself.","zh":"一旦妥善調校，溫室大致上可以自行運作。"},{"en":"To run itself means to operate automatically with little human control.","zh":"run itself 指在很少人手控制下自動運作。"},{"en":"A smart irrigation system can run itself after the farmer sets the schedule.","zh":"智能灌溉系統在農民設定時間表後，可以自行運作。"},{"en":"If a system runs itself, workers save time because sensors and controls manage routine actions.","zh":"如果系統自行運作，工人可以節省時間，因為感應器和控制器管理例行動作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes automatic operation.","zh":"這個短語描述自動運行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sensors","meaning":"感應器","examples":[{"en":"Sensors monitor environmental conditions throughout the day.","zh":"感應器全日監測環境條件。"},{"en":"Sensors are devices that detect changes such as temperature, light, movement, or humidity.","zh":"sensors 指偵測溫度、光線、動作或濕度等變化的裝置。"},{"en":"A school may use sensors to turn lights off when classrooms are empty.","zh":"學校可能使用感應器，在課室沒有人時關燈。"},{"en":"Sensors help machines respond automatically instead of waiting for human instructions.","zh":"感應器幫助機器自動回應，而不用等待人類指令。"},{"en":"This word describes devices that notice and measure conditions.","zh":"這個字描述察覺並量度條件的裝置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"switch everything on","meaning":"啟動所有設備","examples":[{"en":"The sensors switch everything on when the sun rises.","zh":"日出時，感應器會啟動所有設備。"},{"en":"To switch everything on means to turn on all the necessary machines or systems.","zh":"switch everything on 指開啟所有必要機器或系統。"},{"en":"A teacher may switch everything on before class, including the projector and speakers.","zh":"老師上課前可能啟動所有設備，包括投影機和喇叭。"},{"en":"Automatic switching saves time because people do not need to start each device by hand.","zh":"自動啟動可以節省時間，因為人們不用逐一手動開機。"},{"en":"This phrase describes starting all parts of a system.","zh":"這個短語描述啟動系統的所有部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"when the sun rises","meaning":"日出時","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse begins operating automatically when the sun rises.","zh":"日出時，溫室開始自動運作。"},{"en":"When the sun rises means at the time the sun appears in the morning.","zh":"when the sun rises 指早上太陽出現的時候。"},{"en":"Farmers often begin work when the sun rises to avoid the hottest part of the day.","zh":"農民常在日出時開始工作，以避開一天最熱時段。"},{"en":"In a solar-powered system, operation may begin when the sun rises because light becomes available.","zh":"在太陽能系統中，日出時有光可用，系統可能開始運作。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the beginning of daylight.","zh":"這個短語標誌日光開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"alter the flow of","meaning":"調節……的流量","examples":[{"en":"The sensors alter the flow of air and seawater.","zh":"感應器調節空氣和海水的流量。"},{"en":"To alter the flow of something means to change how fast, how much, or where it moves.","zh":"alter the flow of something 指改變某物移動的速度、數量或方向。"},{"en":"A traffic officer can alter the flow of cars after an accident.","zh":"意外後，交通警可以調節車流。"},{"en":"In the greenhouse, changing the flow of air and seawater controls temperature and humidity.","zh":"在溫室中，改變空氣和海水流量可以控制溫度和濕度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adjusting movement through a system.","zh":"這個短語描述調整某物在系統中的流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"throughout the day","meaning":"全日；整天","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse adjusts its operation throughout the day.","zh":"溫室全日調整其運作。"},{"en":"Throughout the day means during the whole day or at many points across the day.","zh":"throughout the day 指整天期間，或在一天中多個時段。"},{"en":"A nurse checks patients throughout the day to make sure they are stable.","zh":"護士全日檢查病人，確保他們情況穩定。"},{"en":"Conditions change throughout the day, so automatic systems may need to adjust often.","zh":"條件全日都會改變，因此自動系統可能需要經常調整。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something happening across the whole day.","zh":"這個短語描述某事在整天中發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in response to","meaning":"因應……","examples":[{"en":"The system changes its settings in response to environmental conditions.","zh":"系統因應環境條件改變設定。"},{"en":"In response to something means because of it or as a reaction to it.","zh":"in response to something 指因為某事或作為對某事的反應。"},{"en":"A school may close windows in response to heavy rain.","zh":"學校可能因應大雨而關窗。"},{"en":"If temperature rises, a cooling system may increase airflow in response.","zh":"如果溫度上升，冷卻系統可能因應情況增加氣流。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a reaction with the condition that caused it.","zh":"這個短語把反應與造成反應的條件連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"changes in temperature and humidity","meaning":"溫度和濕度的變化","examples":[{"en":"The sensors respond to changes in temperature and humidity.","zh":"感應器會回應溫度和濕度的變化。"},{"en":"Changes in temperature and humidity are increases or decreases in heat and moisture in the air.","zh":"changes in temperature and humidity 指空氣熱度和水分的上升或下降。"},{"en":"A museum monitors changes in temperature and humidity to protect old paintings.","zh":"博物館監測溫度和濕度的變化，以保護古老畫作。"},{"en":"If humidity rises too high, machines may need to remove moisture from the air.","zh":"如果濕度升得太高，機器可能需要從空氣中去除水分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes environmental changes that affect comfort, materials, and plants.","zh":"這個短語描述會影響舒適度、材料和植物的環境變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on windless days","meaning":"在沒有風的日子","examples":[{"en":"Fans are used on windless days.","zh":"在沒有風的日子會使用風扇。"},{"en":"On windless days means on days when there is little or no wind.","zh":"on windless days 指風很小或沒有風的日子。"},{"en":"On windless days, smoke may stay in the air instead of being blown away.","zh":"在沒有風的日子，煙霧可能停留在空氣中，而不是被吹走。"},{"en":"A greenhouse may need fans on windless days to keep air moving.","zh":"溫室在沒有風的日子可能需要風扇保持空氣流動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weather conditions with no natural airflow.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有自然氣流的天氣條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ensure a constant flow of air","meaning":"確保持續的氣流","examples":[{"en":"Fans ensure a constant flow of air through the greenhouse.","zh":"風扇確保空氣持續流過溫室。"},{"en":"To ensure a constant flow of air means to make sure air keeps moving steadily.","zh":"ensure a constant flow of air 指確保空氣持續穩定流動。"},{"en":"A classroom fan can ensure a constant flow of air on a hot still afternoon.","zh":"在炎熱無風的下午，課室風扇可以確保持續氣流。"},{"en":"A constant airflow prevents air from becoming too hot, stale, or humid.","zh":"持續氣流防止空氣變得太熱、悶或潮濕。"},{"en":"This phrase describes maintaining steady ventilation.","zh":"這個短語描述維持穩定通風。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be tuned to","meaning":"調校至適合……","examples":[{"en":"Once the system is tuned to the local environment, it operates automatically.","zh":"一旦系統調校至適合本地環境，它就會自動運作。"},{"en":"To be tuned to something means to be adjusted carefully so it works well with that condition.","zh":"be tuned to something 指被仔細調整，使其能配合某條件良好運作。"},{"en":"A radio must be tuned to the right frequency before the sound is clear.","zh":"收音機必須調校至正確頻率，聲音才清楚。"},{"en":"A greenhouse system must be tuned to local heat, wind, and humidity.","zh":"溫室系統必須調校至適合本地熱力、風和濕度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful adjustment for best performance.","zh":"這個短語描述為最佳表現而作出的仔細調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the local environment","meaning":"本地環境","examples":[{"en":"The system must be adjusted to suit the local environment.","zh":"系統必須調整至適合本地環境。"},{"en":"The local environment is the climate, land, water, wind, and conditions of a particular place.","zh":"local environment 指某特定地方的氣候、土地、水、風和條件。"},{"en":"Farmers choose crops according to the local environment.","zh":"農民會根據本地環境選擇農作物。"},{"en":"A design that ignores the local environment may fail even if it works elsewhere.","zh":"忽視本地環境的設計，即使在其他地方有效，也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the specific natural conditions of a place.","zh":"這個短語描述某地的具體自然條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"do not need anyone there","meaning":"不需要有人留守","examples":[{"en":"Once adjusted, the greenhouse does not need anyone there for it to work.","zh":"一旦調整好，溫室不需要有人留守也能運作。"},{"en":"To not need anyone there means the system can operate without a person physically present.","zh":"do not need anyone there 指系統可以在沒有人實體在場的情況下運作。"},{"en":"A smart light system does not need anyone there to turn lights on and off.","zh":"智能照明系統不需要有人留守也能開關燈。"},{"en":"If machines do not need anyone there, workers can focus on checking results instead of constant control.","zh":"如果機器不需要有人留守，工人可以集中檢查結果，而不是不斷控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes low need for human attendance.","zh":"這個短語描述對人手在場的需求很低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"run the entire operation","meaning":"操作整套系統","examples":[{"en":"A single electrical supply can run the entire operation.","zh":"單一電力供應可以操作整套系統。"},{"en":"To run the entire operation means to power or manage all parts of a system.","zh":"run the entire operation 指為整個系統所有部分供電或管理它們。"},{"en":"One small generator can run the entire operation of a temporary medical tent.","zh":"一部小型發電機可以操作臨時醫療帳篷的整套系統。"},{"en":"If one power source runs the whole operation, the system is simpler to install.","zh":"如果一個電源能運行整個系統，安裝就較簡單。"},{"en":"This phrase describes supporting all parts of a project or machine.","zh":"這個短語描述支援項目或機器的所有部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"from one 13-amp plug","meaning":"只使用一個13安培插頭","examples":[{"en":"The entire greenhouse can run from one 13-amp plug.","zh":"整座溫室只使用一個13安培插頭就能運作。"},{"en":"From one 13-amp plug means using only a single ordinary electrical plug with a 13-amp rating.","zh":"from one 13-amp plug 指只使用一個普通、額定13安培的電插頭。"},{"en":"A small office printer can run from one 13-amp plug.","zh":"小型辦公室打印機可以只使用一個13安培插頭運作。"},{"en":"If a large system runs from one plug, it probably uses surprisingly little electricity.","zh":"如果大型系統只用一個插頭運行，它可能耗電量出奇地低。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights low power demand.","zh":"這個短語突出低電力需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"entirely independent of","meaning":"完全不依賴……","examples":[{"en":"Future versions could be entirely independent of the electricity grid.","zh":"未來版本可以完全不依賴電網。"},{"en":"Entirely independent of something means not needing or relying on it at all.","zh":"entirely independent of something 指完全不需要或依賴某物。"},{"en":"A cabin with solar panels and batteries may be entirely independent of public electricity.","zh":"配有太陽能板和電池的小屋可能完全不依賴公共電力。"},{"en":"If a system is independent of the grid, it can operate in remote places.","zh":"如果系統不依賴電網，就可以在偏遠地方運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete self-sufficiency from a support system.","zh":"這個短語描述完全不依靠某支援系統的自給能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the electricity grid","meaning":"電網","examples":[{"en":"The designers hope to operate the greenhouse without the electricity grid.","zh":"設計者希望不靠電網也能操作溫室。"},{"en":"The electricity grid is the network that supplies electrical power to homes, buildings, and businesses.","zh":"electricity grid 指向住宅、建築物和企業供電的網絡。"},{"en":"After a storm, some villages may lose connection to the electricity grid.","zh":"風暴後，有些村莊可能與電網失去連接。"},{"en":"Solar panels can reduce dependence on the electricity grid.","zh":"太陽能板可以減少對電網的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the public power-supply network.","zh":"這個短語描述公共供電網絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be powered by","meaning":"由……供電","examples":[{"en":"The system could eventually be powered by solar panels.","zh":"該系統最終可以由太陽能板供電。"},{"en":"To be powered by something means to receive energy from it.","zh":"be powered by something 指從某物獲得能量。"},{"en":"A calculator may be powered by a small solar cell.","zh":"計算機可能由小型太陽能電池供電。"},{"en":"If a machine is powered by renewable energy, it may produce less pollution.","zh":"如果機器由可再生能源供電，它可能產生較少污染。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the energy source of a device or system.","zh":"這個短語描述裝置或系統的能源來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"solar panels","meaning":"太陽能板","examples":[{"en":"A few solar panels could supply all the power required.","zh":"幾塊太陽能板就可以供應所需的全部電力。"},{"en":"Solar panels are devices that turn sunlight into electricity.","zh":"solar panels 指把陽光轉化為電力的裝置。"},{"en":"A school may install solar panels on its roof to reduce electricity bills.","zh":"學校可能在屋頂安裝太陽能板，以減少電費。"},{"en":"Solar panels are useful in sunny places where grid power is expensive or unavailable.","zh":"在陽光充足且電網電力昂貴或無法取得的地方，太陽能板很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes equipment for generating electricity from sunlight.","zh":"這個短語描述利用陽光發電的設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"critics point out that","meaning":"批評者指出","examples":[{"en":"Critics point out that the construction costs are relatively high.","zh":"批評者指出建造成本相對較高。"},{"en":"Critics point out that means people who disagree or question the idea mention a weakness or problem.","zh":"critics point out that 指不同意或質疑該想法的人提出弱點或問題。"},{"en":"Critics point out that online learning can exclude students without good Internet access.","zh":"批評者指出，網上學習可能排除沒有良好互聯網的學生。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an objection that should be considered fairly.","zh":"這個短語引出應被公平考慮的反對意見。"},{"en":"It helps writers show the other side of an argument.","zh":"它幫助作者展示論點的另一面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"construction costs","meaning":"建造成本","examples":[{"en":"The construction costs are approximately four dollars per square foot.","zh":"建造成本約為每平方呎四美元。"},{"en":"Construction costs are the money needed to build something.","zh":"construction costs 指建造某物所需的金錢。"},{"en":"A school must calculate construction costs before building a new sports hall.","zh":"學校建新體育館前，必須計算建造成本。"},{"en":"If construction costs are too high, a good design may be difficult to afford.","zh":"如果建造成本太高，好設計也可能難以負擔。"},{"en":"This phrase describes building expenses before operation begins.","zh":"這個短語描述運作開始前的建築開支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"per square foot","meaning":"每平方呎","examples":[{"en":"The cost is calculated at around four dollars per square foot.","zh":"成本按每平方呎約四美元計算。"},{"en":"Per square foot means for each square foot of area.","zh":"per square foot 指每一平方呎面積。"},{"en":"Rent in a shopping mall is often calculated per square foot.","zh":"商場租金通常按每平方呎計算。"},{"en":"Using cost per square foot helps compare buildings of different sizes fairly.","zh":"使用每平方呎成本有助公平比較不同大小的建築。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a price based on area.","zh":"這個短語描述按面積計算的價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"quite high","meaning":"相當高","examples":[{"en":"Some critics consider the initial construction cost quite high.","zh":"有些批評者認為最初建造成本相當高。"},{"en":"Quite high means fairly expensive, large, or above what people may expect.","zh":"quite high 指頗昂貴、頗大或高於人們可能預期。"},{"en":"The price of textbooks can feel quite high for families with several children.","zh":"對有幾個孩子的家庭而言，教科書價格可能感覺相當高。"},{"en":"If a cost is quite high, people may ask whether the benefits justify it.","zh":"如果成本相當高，人們可能問好處是否足以證明它合理。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a moderate but clear judgement about size or price.","zh":"這個短語對大小或價格給出溫和但清楚的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"by way of illustration","meaning":"舉例說明","examples":[{"en":"By way of illustration, Paton compares the greenhouse with a large air conditioner.","zh":"舉例說明，Paton 把溫室與大型冷氣機比較。"},{"en":"By way of illustration means as an example to make a point clearer.","zh":"by way of illustration 指作為例子，以令重點更清楚。"},{"en":"By way of illustration, a teacher may compare paragraph structure to building a sandwich.","zh":"舉例說明，老師可能把段落結構比作製作三文治。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that an example or comparison is coming next.","zh":"這個短語表示接下來會有例子或比較。"},{"en":"It helps readers understand an abstract claim through a concrete case.","zh":"它幫助讀者透過具體個案理解抽象說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"point out that","meaning":"指出","examples":[{"en":"Paton points out that the greenhouse uses very little electricity.","zh":"Paton 指出溫室使用很少電力。"},{"en":"To point out that means to mention or explain a fact that people should notice.","zh":"point out that 指提及或解釋人們應注意的事實。"},{"en":"A teacher may point out that an essay answer has not addressed the question.","zh":"老師可能指出作文答案沒有回應題目。"},{"en":"People point out important facts to correct misunderstandings or support an argument.","zh":"人們指出重要事實，是為了糾正誤解或支持論點。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a detail that matters.","zh":"這個短語引出重要細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"cool as efficiently as","meaning":"冷卻效能與……一樣高","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse can cool as efficiently as a large air-conditioning system.","zh":"這座溫室的冷卻效能可以與大型空調系統一樣高。"},{"en":"To cool as efficiently as something means to provide a similar cooling effect while using resources well.","zh":"cool as efficiently as something 指提供相似冷卻效果，同時有效使用資源。"},{"en":"A small fan cannot usually cool as efficiently as a proper air conditioner in a large room.","zh":"在大房間中，小風扇通常不能像正式冷氣機那樣高效冷卻。"},{"en":"If one system cools as efficiently as another but uses less power, it may be more economical.","zh":"如果一個系統冷卻效能與另一個相同但用電較少，它可能更經濟。"},{"en":"This phrase compares cooling performance and efficiency.","zh":"這個短語比較冷卻表現和效率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a 500-kilowatt air conditioner","meaning":"500千瓦冷氣系統","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse can match the cooling effect of a 500-kilowatt air conditioner.","zh":"這座溫室可以媲美500千瓦冷氣系統的冷卻效果。"},{"en":"A 500-kilowatt air conditioner is a very powerful cooling system that uses or provides a large amount of power.","zh":"500-kilowatt air conditioner 指非常強大的冷卻系統，使用或提供大量功率。"},{"en":"A small classroom would not need a 500-kilowatt air conditioner.","zh":"小課室不會需要500千瓦冷氣系統。"},{"en":"Comparing the greenhouse with such a large air conditioner shows how strong its cooling effect is.","zh":"把溫室與如此大型冷氣系統比較，顯示其冷卻效果有多強。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a concrete measure of cooling power.","zh":"這個短語給出冷卻能力的具體量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"use less than","meaning":"使用少於……","examples":[{"en":"The system uses less than three kilowatts of electricity.","zh":"該系統使用少於三千瓦電力。"},{"en":"To use less than an amount means to consume a smaller amount than that limit.","zh":"use less than an amount 指消耗比該限制更少的數量。"},{"en":"A phone charger uses less electricity than a microwave oven.","zh":"手機充電器使用的電力少於微波爐。"},{"en":"If a system uses less power, it may cost less to operate.","zh":"如果系統用電較少，操作成本可能較低。"},{"en":"This phrase sets an upper limit on consumption.","zh":"這個短語設定消耗量上限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"only an eighth of","meaning":"只有八分之一","examples":[{"en":"The plants need only an eighth of the usual volume of water.","zh":"植物只需要通常用水量的八分之一。"},{"en":"Only an eighth of something means just one out of eight equal parts.","zh":"only an eighth of something 指八等份中的一份而已。"},{"en":"If a recipe needs only an eighth of a teaspoon of salt, the amount is very small.","zh":"如果食譜只需要八分之一茶匙鹽，份量就很少。"},{"en":"Using only an eighth of the usual water shows a major reduction.","zh":"只使用通常用水量的八分之一，顯示大幅減少。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a small fraction of a normal amount.","zh":"這個短語表達正常數量中的一小部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the volume of water","meaning":"用水量","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse greatly reduces the volume of water required.","zh":"這座溫室大大減少所需用水量。"},{"en":"The volume of water is the amount of water, often measured in litres or cubic metres.","zh":"volume of water 指水的數量，通常以公升或立方米量度。"},{"en":"A household can reduce the volume of water used by fixing leaking taps.","zh":"家庭可以透過修理漏水水龍頭來減少用水量。"},{"en":"If the volume of water required falls, farming becomes easier in dry regions.","zh":"如果所需用水量下降，乾旱地區耕作會變得較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the total quantity of water.","zh":"這個短語指水的總數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be grown conventionally","meaning":"以傳統方式種植","examples":[{"en":"Conventionally grown crops require substantially more water.","zh":"以傳統方式種植的農作物需要多得多的水。"},{"en":"To be grown conventionally means to be cultivated using normal or traditional farming methods.","zh":"be grown conventionally 指使用一般或傳統農業方法栽培。"},{"en":"Vegetables grown conventionally in open fields may need more irrigation than greenhouse crops.","zh":"在露天田地以傳統方式種植的蔬菜，可能比溫室作物需要更多灌溉。"},{"en":"Conventional growing methods may be less efficient in very hot and dry climates.","zh":"傳統種植方法在非常炎熱乾燥的氣候中可能較低效。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts ordinary farming with a special new method.","zh":"這個短語把普通耕作與特殊新方法作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"effective cost","meaning":"實際成本","examples":[{"en":"The effective cost of the desalinated water is relatively low.","zh":"化淡水的實際成本相對較低。"},{"en":"Effective cost means the real practical cost after considering savings, output, or extra benefits.","zh":"effective cost 指考慮節省、產量或額外好處後的真實實際成本。"},{"en":"A printer may seem cheap, but its effective cost is high if ink is expensive.","zh":"打印機可能看似便宜，但如果墨水昂貴，其實際成本就很高。"},{"en":"If a system produces water and cooling together, the effective cost of each benefit may fall.","zh":"如果系統同時產生水和冷卻效果，每項好處的實際成本可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the true cost in practice, not just the starting price.","zh":"這個短語描述實際上的真實成本，而不只是起始價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"desalinated water","meaning":"化淡水","examples":[{"en":"The system produces desalinated water at a reduced cost.","zh":"該系統以較低成本生產化淡水。"},{"en":"Desalinated water is seawater or salty water that has had its salt removed.","zh":"desalinated water 指已去除鹽分的海水或鹹水。"},{"en":"Many dry coastal cities depend on desalinated water for drinking and farming.","zh":"許多乾旱沿海城市依賴化淡水作飲用和農業用途。"},{"en":"Producing desalinated water can be expensive if the process uses a lot of electricity.","zh":"如果過程耗用大量電力，生產化淡水可能很昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fresh water made from salty water.","zh":"這個短語描述由鹹水製成的淡水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"only a quarter of","meaning":"只有……的四分之一","examples":[{"en":"The water costs only a quarter of the amount produced by standard equipment.","zh":"這種水的成本只有標準設備所產水成本的四分之一。"},{"en":"Only a quarter of something means just one out of four equal parts.","zh":"only a quarter of something 指四等份中的一份而已。"},{"en":"If a trip costs only a quarter of the usual price, it is much cheaper.","zh":"如果一次旅行的費用只有平常價格的四分之一，它就便宜很多。"},{"en":"A cost of only a quarter of the usual level suggests strong savings.","zh":"成本只有通常水平的四分之一，顯示有很大節省。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a large reduction to 25 percent of the original amount.","zh":"這個短語表示大幅減少至原數的百分之二十五。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a standard desalinator","meaning":"標準海水化淡設備","examples":[{"en":"A standard desalinator produces water at a higher cost.","zh":"標準海水化淡設備以較高成本產水。"},{"en":"A standard desalinator is a normal machine used to remove salt from seawater.","zh":"standard desalinator 指用來從海水中去除鹽分的一般機器。"},{"en":"A coastal hotel may use a standard desalinator if local fresh water is limited.","zh":"如果本地淡水有限，沿海酒店可能使用標準海水化淡設備。"},{"en":"Standard desalinators can be useful, but they often require significant energy.","zh":"標準化淡設備可以有用，但通常需要大量能源。"},{"en":"This phrase names ordinary desalination equipment.","zh":"這個短語指一般海水化淡設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"good economics","meaning":"符合經濟效益","examples":[{"en":"The relatively low operating cost represents good economics.","zh":"相對較低的營運成本代表符合經濟效益。"},{"en":"Good economics means a plan makes financial sense because benefits are high compared with costs.","zh":"good economics 指計劃在財政上合理，因為相對成本而言好處很大。"},{"en":"Repairing a reliable old bus may be good economics if buying a new one is too expensive.","zh":"如果買新巴士太昂貴，維修可靠舊巴士可能符合經濟效益。"},{"en":"A design shows good economics when it saves money over time.","zh":"當設計能長期省錢，就顯示符合經濟效益。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decision that is financially sensible.","zh":"這個短語描述在財政上合理的決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"besides","meaning":"此外；況且","examples":[{"en":"Besides, the system provides both water and air-conditioning.","zh":"此外，該系統同時提供水和空氣調節。"},{"en":"Besides means in addition or another point is that.","zh":"besides 指除此之外，或另一點是。"},{"en":"This library is quiet; besides, it has free study rooms.","zh":"這間圖書館很安靜；此外，它有免費自修室。"},{"en":"We use besides to add an extra reason that strengthens an argument.","zh":"我們用 besides 加入額外理由，以加強論點。"},{"en":"This word signals one more useful point.","zh":"這個字表示再補充一個有用觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"environmentally friendly","meaning":"環保的","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse offers an environmentally friendly form of cooling.","zh":"這座溫室提供一種環保的冷卻方式。"},{"en":"Environmentally friendly means causing less harm to nature, energy resources, or living things.","zh":"environmentally friendly 指對自然、能源資源或生物造成較少傷害。"},{"en":"Buses can be more environmentally friendly than private cars if many passengers use them.","zh":"如果有很多乘客使用，巴士可以比私家車更環保。"},{"en":"A system is more environmentally friendly when it uses less electricity and creates less pollution.","zh":"當系統用電較少並產生較少污染，它就更環保。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a design or action that is kinder to the environment.","zh":"這個短語描述對環境較友善的設計或行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"provide air-conditioning","meaning":"提供空氣調節","examples":[{"en":"The design provides air-conditioning without enormous electricity use.","zh":"這項設計提供空氣調節，而不需要大量用電。"},{"en":"To provide air-conditioning means to cool and control the air in a space.","zh":"provide air-conditioning 指冷卻並控制某空間的空氣。"},{"en":"A library provides air-conditioning so students can study comfortably in summer.","zh":"圖書館提供空氣調節，讓學生在夏天舒適自修。"},{"en":"If a system provides cooling with little electricity, it can lower operating costs.","zh":"如果系統以少量電力提供冷卻，就可以降低營運成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes supplying cooled indoor air.","zh":"這個短語描述供應經冷卻的室內空氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"on a large scale","meaning":"以大規模","examples":[{"en":"The system could provide cooling on a large scale.","zh":"該系統可以大規模提供冷卻效果。"},{"en":"On a large scale means involving a big area, many people, or a large amount of activity.","zh":"on a large scale 指涉及大範圍、很多人或大量活動。"},{"en":"A city collects rubbish on a large scale every day.","zh":"城市每天大規模收集垃圾。"},{"en":"If cooling can be provided on a large scale, whole farms or buildings may benefit.","zh":"如果冷卻能大規模提供，整個農場或建築物可能受益。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something happening widely or in large quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述某事廣泛或大量發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"large enough to","meaning":"大得足以……","examples":[{"en":"The design is large enough to cool commercial greenhouses.","zh":"這項設計大得足以冷卻商業溫室。"},{"en":"Large enough to do something means having sufficient size or capacity for that purpose.","zh":"large enough to do something 指有足夠大小或容量達到某目的。"},{"en":"A classroom must be large enough to seat all students safely.","zh":"課室必須大得足以讓所有學生安全坐下。"},{"en":"If a water tank is large enough, it can supply a farm through dry days.","zh":"如果水箱足夠大，就能在乾旱日子供應農場。"},{"en":"This phrase connects size with ability.","zh":"這個短語把大小與能力連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"despite high outside temperatures","meaning":"儘管室外氣溫很高","examples":[{"en":"Crops can grow inside despite high outside temperatures.","zh":"儘管室外氣溫很高，農作物仍能在裡面生長。"},{"en":"Despite high outside temperatures means although the air outside is very hot.","zh":"despite high outside temperatures 指雖然外面的空氣非常炎熱。"},{"en":"Students can stay comfortable in a library despite high outside temperatures if the cooling works well.","zh":"如果冷卻系統運作良好，儘管室外氣溫很高，學生仍可在圖書館保持舒適。"},{"en":"The greenhouse protects plants so external heat does not fully control their growing conditions.","zh":"溫室保護植物，使外部熱力不會完全控制其生長條件。"},{"en":"This phrase shows contrast between harsh outside conditions and better inside results.","zh":"這個短語顯示惡劣外部條件與較好內部結果之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agree with the claims of","meaning":"符合……的說法","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements agree with the writer’s claims.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否符合作者的說法。"},{"en":"To agree with the claims of someone means to match what that person says or argues.","zh":"agree with the claims of someone 指與某人所說或主張的內容相符。"},{"en":"If a passage says the system uses little electricity, a statement saying the same thing agrees with the writer’s claim.","zh":"如果文章說系統用電很少，而陳述說同樣內容，就符合作者的說法。"},{"en":"Students should check the text carefully rather than rely on outside knowledge.","zh":"學生應仔細檢查文本，而不是依賴外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading questions about TRUE, FALSE, and NOT GIVEN.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE、FALSE 和 NOT GIVEN 閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contradict the claims of","meaning":"與……的說法相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the claims made in the passage.","zh":"陳述可能與文章中的說法相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the claims of someone means to say the opposite of what that person says.","zh":"contradict the claims of someone 指說出與某人說法相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says the greenhouse uses little electricity, a statement saying it uses huge amounts would contradict it.","zh":"如果文章說溫室用電很少，而陳述說它使用大量電力，就與文章相矛盾。"},{"en":"A contradiction must be clearly shown by the text, not guessed from opinion.","zh":"矛盾必須由文本清楚顯示，而不是由意見猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct disagreement with a stated claim.","zh":"這個短語描述與已陳述說法直接不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Students write NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to determine the writer’s view.","zh":"如果無法判斷作者觀點，學生寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide confidently.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資料作出有信心的判斷。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions the cost of a machine, it is impossible to say whether it was cheap.","zh":"如果文章從未提及機器成本，就無法判斷它是否便宜。"},{"en":"In reading tests, “impossible to say” usually means the answer is NOT GIVEN.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，impossible to say 通常代表答案是 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"This phrase warns students not to guess beyond the text.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生不要超出文本猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"come to someone by accident","meaning":"某人偶然想到","examples":[{"en":"The original idea came to Paton by accident.","zh":"Paton 偶然想到最初的想法。"},{"en":"If an idea comes to someone by accident, they think of it unexpectedly, not through planned searching.","zh":"come to someone by accident 指某人意外想到某想法，而不是經計劃尋找。"},{"en":"A student’s science idea may come to her by accident after she notices steam on a mirror.","zh":"學生注意到鏡子上的水氣後，可能偶然想到科學點子。"},{"en":"Accidental ideas can become important if someone studies them carefully afterwards.","zh":"偶然想法如果之後被仔細研究，也可以變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unexpected inspiration.","zh":"這個短語描述出乎意料的靈感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be well ventilated","meaning":"通風良好","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that the bus was well ventilated.","zh":"該選項暗示巴士通風良好。"},{"en":"To be well ventilated means to have enough fresh air moving through a space.","zh":"be well ventilated 指某空間有足夠新鮮空氣流通。"},{"en":"A classroom should be well ventilated so students do not feel sleepy or uncomfortable.","zh":"課室應通風良好，讓學生不會感到睏倦或不舒服。"},{"en":"If a bus is not well ventilated, warm humid air can build up inside.","zh":"如果巴士通風不好，溫暖潮濕的空氣可能在車內累積。"},{"en":"This phrase describes good airflow in a room or vehicle.","zh":"這個短語描述房間或車輛中良好的空氣流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"after waking up","meaning":"醒來後","examples":[{"en":"After waking up, Paton discovered that the towel was wet.","zh":"醒來後，Paton 發現毛巾濕了。"},{"en":"After waking up means after someone stops sleeping and becomes conscious again.","zh":"after waking up 指某人停止睡眠並再次有意識之後。"},{"en":"After waking up, a student may check the weather before going to school.","zh":"醒來後，學生可能先查看天氣再上學。"},{"en":"This phrase helps place an event immediately after sleep.","zh":"這個短語幫助把事件放在睡眠之後。"},{"en":"It is often used to describe the first thing someone notices or does in the morning.","zh":"它常用來描述某人早上第一件注意到或做的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"find something wet","meaning":"發現……濕了","examples":[{"en":"Paton found his towel soaking wet.","zh":"Paton 發現他的毛巾濕透了。"},{"en":"To find something wet means to discover that it is covered with or full of water.","zh":"find something wet 指發現某物被水覆蓋或充滿水分。"},{"en":"A parent may find the kitchen floor wet after a pipe leaks.","zh":"水管漏水後，家長可能發現廚房地板濕了。"},{"en":"Finding something wet can reveal that condensation, rain, or a leak has occurred.","zh":"發現某物濕了，可能顯示發生了凝結、下雨或漏水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes noticing the wet condition of an object.","zh":"這個短語描述注意到某物處於潮濕狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"work properly","meaning":"正常運作","examples":[{"en":"One statement concerns whether a fan on the bus worked properly.","zh":"其中一項陳述涉及巴士上的風扇是否正常運作。"},{"en":"To work properly means to function as it should, without faults.","zh":"work properly 指按應有方式運作，沒有故障。"},{"en":"A printer does not work properly if it prints only half the page.","zh":"如果打印機只印出半頁，它就沒有正常運作。"},{"en":"If a fan works properly, it should move air and improve ventilation.","zh":"如果風扇正常運作，它應能推動空氣並改善通風。"},{"en":"This phrase describes correct operation.","zh":"這個短語描述正確運行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"immediately set up a business","meaning":"立即開設業務","examples":[{"en":"Paton did not immediately set up a business after speaking to Davies.","zh":"Paton 與 Davies 交談後，並沒有立即開設業務。"},{"en":"To immediately set up a business means to start a company right away without much delay.","zh":"immediately set up a business 指毫不拖延地立刻創辦公司。"},{"en":"A student with a good idea should not immediately set up a business without testing the product.","zh":"有好想法的學生不應未測試產品就立即開設業務。"},{"en":"Waiting before starting a business can allow time for research, experiments, and planning.","zh":"開業前等待一段時間，可以留出研究、實驗和規劃時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes starting commercial activity at once.","zh":"這個短語描述立刻開始商業活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"after talking with","meaning":"與……交談後","examples":[{"en":"Paton began experimenting after talking with his physicist friend.","zh":"Paton 與他的物理學家朋友交談後開始實驗。"},{"en":"After talking with someone means after having a conversation with that person.","zh":"after talking with someone 指與某人對話之後。"},{"en":"After talking with her teacher, a student may realise how to improve her essay.","zh":"與老師交談後，學生可能明白如何改善作文。"},{"en":"A useful conversation can lead to action, experiments, or a new plan.","zh":"有用對話可以導致行動、實驗或新計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a conversation with what happens next.","zh":"這個短語把對話與接下來發生的事連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"label the diagram","meaning":"為圖表填上標示","examples":[{"en":"Students label the diagram using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞為圖表填上標示。"},{"en":"To label the diagram means to write the correct names beside parts of a picture or drawing.","zh":"label the diagram 指在圖片或圖畫的各部分旁寫上正確名稱。"},{"en":"In a biology test, students may label the diagram of a plant cell.","zh":"在生物測驗中，學生可能要為植物細胞圖填上標示。"},{"en":"Diagram labels help show that students understand both vocabulary and structure.","zh":"圖表標示幫助顯示學生理解詞彙和結構。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in reading and science tasks.","zh":"這個短語是閱讀和科學任務中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個字詞","examples":[{"en":"Each diagram label must contain no more than three words.","zh":"每個圖表標示不得超過三個字詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer can use one, two, or three words, but not four.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案可以用一、二或三個字詞，但不能用四個。"},{"en":"If the instruction says no more than three words, “clear outer roof layer” may be too long.","zh":"如果指示說不多於三個字詞，“clear outer roof layer” 可能太長。"},{"en":"Students must count words carefully because extra words can make an answer wrong.","zh":"學生必須仔細計算字數，因為多出的字可能令答案錯。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語設定嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary with words from the passage.","zh":"學生用文章中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill missing words in a short version of the passage.","zh":"complete the summary 指在文章簡短版本中填入缺失字詞。"},{"en":"A student should read the sentence before and after each gap when completing a summary.","zh":"完成摘要時，學生應閱讀每個空格前後的句子。"},{"en":"Summary completion tests whether students understand meaning, grammar, and location in the text.","zh":"摘要填充測試學生是否理解意思、文法和文本位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個字詞","examples":[{"en":"Each summary answer must contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個摘要答案不得超過兩個字詞。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer may contain one or two words, but not three.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案可以包含一個或兩個字詞，但不能三個。"},{"en":"If the answer is “clear polyethylene”, it fits a two-word limit.","zh":"如果答案是 “clear polyethylene”，就符合兩個字詞限制。"},{"en":"Students should not add articles or extra words if the limit is strict.","zh":"如果字數限制嚴格，學生不應加入冠詞或額外字。"},{"en":"This phrase tells candidates exactly how long the answer can be.","zh":"這個短語準確告訴考生答案可以多長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"to some extent","meaning":"在某程度上","examples":[{"en":"To some extent, the greenhouse functions automatically.","zh":"在某程度上，這座溫室自動運作。"},{"en":"To some extent means partly, but not completely.","zh":"to some extent 指部分如此，但不是完全如此。"},{"en":"To some extent, online learning saves time, but students still need discipline.","zh":"在某程度上，網上學習節省時間，但學生仍需要自律。"},{"en":"This phrase helps make a claim more careful and balanced.","zh":"這個短語幫助令說法更謹慎和平衡。"},{"en":"It is useful when something is true only in a limited way.","zh":"當某事只在有限程度上成立時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"function automatically","meaning":"自動運作","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse can function automatically after being properly adjusted.","zh":"溫室在妥善調校後可以自動運作。"},{"en":"To function automatically means to work by itself through sensors, settings, or programmed controls.","zh":"function automatically 指透過感應器、設定或程式控制自行運作。"},{"en":"Automatic doors function automatically when they detect a person nearby.","zh":"自動門偵測到附近有人時會自動運作。"},{"en":"If a system functions automatically, people do not need to control every action manually.","zh":"如果系統自動運作，人們不需要手動控制每個動作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes machine operation without constant human input.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有持續人手輸入的機器運行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"respond to changes in","meaning":"因應……的變化","examples":[{"en":"The equipment responds to changes in several natural conditions.","zh":"設備會因應幾種自然條件的變化作出反應。"},{"en":"To respond to changes in something means to react when that condition becomes different.","zh":"respond to changes in something 指當某條件變得不同時作出反應。"},{"en":"A smart thermostat responds to changes in room temperature.","zh":"智能恆溫器會因應室溫變化作出反應。"},{"en":"If machines respond to changes quickly, they can keep conditions stable.","zh":"如果機器快速回應變化，就可以保持條件穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes automatic or deliberate reaction to changing conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述對變化條件的自動或有意反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"natural elements","meaning":"自然因素","examples":[{"en":"Temperature, humidity and sunlight are important natural elements.","zh":"溫度、濕度和陽光是重要自然因素。"},{"en":"Natural elements are features of the physical environment, such as light, wind, water, heat, and air.","zh":"natural elements 指實體環境中的特徵，例如光、風、水、熱和空氣。"},{"en":"Farmers pay close attention to natural elements before planting crops.","zh":"農民在種植農作物前會密切留意自然因素。"},{"en":"If a design uses natural elements well, it may need less artificial energy.","zh":"如果設計善用自然因素，可能需要較少人工能源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes environmental factors found in nature.","zh":"這個短語描述自然界中的環境因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"retain the flow of air","meaning":"維持氣流","examples":[{"en":"Fans help maintain the flow of air when there is no wind.","zh":"沒有風時，風扇幫助維持氣流。"},{"en":"To retain the flow of air means to keep air moving steadily through a space.","zh":"retain the flow of air 指保持空氣在某空間中穩定流動。"},{"en":"In a classroom, open windows and fans can retain the flow of air.","zh":"在課室中，開窗和風扇可以維持氣流。"},{"en":"Without airflow, a greenhouse may become too hot, humid, or stale.","zh":"沒有氣流，溫室可能變得太熱、太濕或太悶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping ventilation going.","zh":"這個短語描述保持通風運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in the future","meaning":"將來","examples":[{"en":"In the future, solar panels could power the whole greenhouse.","zh":"將來，太陽能板可以為整座溫室供電。"},{"en":"In the future means at a later time, not now.","zh":"in the future 指在較後時間，而不是現在。"},{"en":"In the future, schools may use more blended learning than traditional lectures.","zh":"將來，學校可能比傳統講課更多使用混合學習。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a possibility, plan, or prediction that may happen later.","zh":"這個短語引出之後可能發生的可能性、計劃或預測。"},{"en":"It helps separate present reality from future development.","zh":"它幫助區分目前現實與未來發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"an ideal plan","meaning":"理想方案","examples":[{"en":"The designers have an ideal plan to make the greenhouse energy-independent.","zh":"設計者有一個理想方案，要令溫室能源獨立。"},{"en":"An ideal plan is the best or most desired plan, even if it has not fully happened yet.","zh":"ideal plan 指最佳或最希望實現的方案，即使尚未完全發生。"},{"en":"A school’s ideal plan may be to give every student personal feedback each week.","zh":"學校的理想方案可能是每星期給每名學生個人回饋。"},{"en":"Ideal plans often show the direction people hope to reach.","zh":"理想方案通常顯示人們希望達到的方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a preferred future arrangement.","zh":"這個短語描述理想中的未來安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"argue that","meaning":"主張；認為","examples":[{"en":"Some critics argue that the construction costs are too high.","zh":"有些批評者認為建造成本太高。"},{"en":"To argue that means to state a view and support it with reasons.","zh":"argue that 指提出一個觀點並用理由支持它。"},{"en":"Some students argue that school should start later because teenagers need more sleep.","zh":"有些學生主張學校應較遲開始，因為青少年需要更多睡眠。"},{"en":"When people argue that a design is too expensive, they are questioning its practicality.","zh":"當人們認為設計太昂貴，他們是在質疑其實用性。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an opinion or claim in a debate.","zh":"這個短語引出爭論中的意見或主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"not good economics","meaning":"不符合經濟效益","examples":[{"en":"Critics claim that the high construction costs do not represent good economics.","zh":"批評者聲稱高建造成本不符合經濟效益。"},{"en":"Not good economics means not financially sensible because costs may be too high for the benefits.","zh":"not good economics 指在財政上不合理，因為成本相對好處可能太高。"},{"en":"Buying a cheap printer with very expensive ink may not be good economics.","zh":"購買便宜但墨水很貴的打印機，可能不符合經濟效益。"},{"en":"A project is not good economics if it saves little money after costing a lot to build.","zh":"如果項目建造成本很高但節省很少，就不符合經濟效益。"},{"en":"This phrase judges whether a decision makes financial sense.","zh":"這個短語判斷某決定是否在財政上合理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"justify the design","meaning":"證明該設計合理","examples":[{"en":"Paton uses performance figures to justify the design.","zh":"Paton 使用性能數據來證明該設計合理。"},{"en":"To justify the design means to give reasons or evidence showing that the design is sensible or worthwhile.","zh":"justify the design 指給出理由或證據，顯示設計合理或值得採用。"},{"en":"An architect may justify a school design by explaining how it improves safety and saves energy.","zh":"建築師可能透過解釋如何改善安全和節省能源，證明學校設計合理。"},{"en":"Strong data can justify a costly project if it shows long-term savings.","zh":"如果強有力數據顯示長期節省，就可以證明昂貴項目合理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes defending a design with reasons.","zh":"這個短語描述用理由為設計辯護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"present favourable arguments","meaning":"提出有利論據","examples":[{"en":"Paton presents favourable arguments in response to his critics.","zh":"Paton 提出有利論據回應批評者。"},{"en":"To present favourable arguments means to give reasons that support an idea or make it look stronger.","zh":"present favourable arguments 指給出支持某想法或令其更有力的理由。"},{"en":"A student presents favourable arguments for public transport by discussing lower cost and less pollution.","zh":"學生透過討論較低成本和較少污染，為公共交通提出有利論據。"},{"en":"Favourable arguments can balance criticism by showing benefits that critics may ignore.","zh":"有利論據可以透過展示批評者可能忽略的好處，平衡批評。"},{"en":"This phrase describes putting forward supportive reasons.","zh":"這個短語描述提出支持性理由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"argue against the critics","meaning":"反駁批評者","examples":[{"en":"Paton argues against the critics by comparing operating costs.","zh":"Paton 透過比較營運成本來反駁批評者。"},{"en":"To argue against the critics means to respond to their objections and explain why they may be wrong or incomplete.","zh":"argue against the critics 指回應批評者的反對意見，並解釋為何它們可能錯誤或不完整。"},{"en":"A teacher may argue against critics of homework by showing that short practice improves memory.","zh":"老師可能透過顯示短練習改善記憶，反駁批評功課的人。"},{"en":"Comparing evidence can help someone argue against criticism more convincingly.","zh":"比較證據可以幫助人更有說服力地反駁批評。"},{"en":"This phrase describes defending an idea against objections.","zh":"這個短語描述面對反對意見時為想法辯護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"an environmentally friendly approach","meaning":"一種環保方法","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse is an environmentally friendly approach to cooling and irrigation.","zh":"這座溫室是冷卻和灌溉的一種環保方法。"},{"en":"An environmentally friendly approach is a method that solves a problem while causing less harm to nature.","zh":"environmentally friendly approach 指在解決問題的同時，對自然造成較少傷害的方法。"},{"en":"Cycling to school is an environmentally friendly approach to daily transport.","zh":"騎單車上學是日常交通的一種環保方法。"},{"en":"If a system uses less electricity and less fresh water, it may be more environmentally friendly.","zh":"如果系統使用較少電力和較少淡水，它可能更環保。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a greener way to achieve a goal.","zh":"這個短語描述達成目標的較綠色方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"provide cooling on a large scale","meaning":"大規模提供冷卻效果","examples":[{"en":"The design can provide cooling on a large scale with little electricity.","zh":"這項設計可以用少量電力大規模提供冷卻效果。"},{"en":"To provide cooling on a large scale means to lower temperatures across a large area or for many users.","zh":"provide cooling on a large scale 指為大範圍或許多使用者降低溫度。"},{"en":"A shopping mall needs a system that can provide cooling on a large scale during summer.","zh":"商場在夏天需要能大規模提供冷卻效果的系統。"},{"en":"If cooling can be provided on a large scale with little electricity, operating costs and emissions may fall.","zh":"如果能以少量電力大規模提供冷卻效果，營運成本和排放可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes widespread cooling capacity.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛冷卻能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 19 - The Rainmaker design.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 20":[{"front":"unexpected benefits for the human brain","meaning":"對人類大腦意想不到的好處","examples":[{"en":"The passage explores the unexpected benefits of video games for the human brain.","zh":"文章探討電子遊戲對人類大腦意想不到的好處。"},{"en":"Unexpected benefits for the human brain are positive effects on thinking, attention, or learning that people may not expect.","zh":"unexpected benefits for the human brain 指對思考、注意力或學習產生的正面影響，而這些影響可能出乎人們意料。"},{"en":"A difficult puzzle game may bring unexpected benefits for the human brain by training patience and memory.","zh":"困難的解謎遊戲可能透過訓練耐性和記憶，帶來對人類大腦意想不到的好處。"},{"en":"When an activity challenges people to focus and solve problems, it may strengthen mental skills.","zh":"當一項活動挑戰人集中和解決問題，它可能強化心理技能。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something often criticised turns out to help the mind in surprising ways.","zh":"這個短語適合用於某些常被批評的事物，結果卻以令人意外的方式幫助大腦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"play one’s first video game","meaning":"第一次玩電子遊戲","examples":[{"en":"James Paul Gee played his first video game many years ago.","zh":"James Paul Gee 多年前第一次玩電子遊戲。"},{"en":"To play one’s first video game means to experience a video game for the first time.","zh":"play one’s first video game 指第一次體驗電子遊戲。"},{"en":"A child may play her first video game on a tablet during a family holiday.","zh":"孩子可能在家庭旅行中用平板電腦第一次玩電子遊戲。"},{"en":"Playing a first game can make someone curious about how games teach rules and challenges.","zh":"第一次玩遊戲可能令人好奇遊戲如何教授規則和挑戰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of someone’s personal experience with gaming.","zh":"這個短語描述某人個人遊戲經驗的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"support someone’s problem solving","meaning":"協助某人解決問題","examples":[{"en":"Gee played the game so that he could support his son’s problem solving.","zh":"Gee 玩這個遊戲，是為了協助兒子解決問題。"},{"en":"To support someone’s problem solving means to help them think through a difficulty and find a solution.","zh":"support someone’s problem solving 指幫助某人思考困難並找出解決方法。"},{"en":"A parent can support a child’s problem solving by asking questions instead of giving the answer immediately.","zh":"家長可以透過提問而不是立即給答案，協助孩子解決問題。"},{"en":"Good support helps learners become more independent rather than dependent on adults.","zh":"良好支援幫助學習者變得更獨立，而不是依賴成年人。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on helping the thinking process, not simply solving the problem for someone.","zh":"這個短語著重幫助思考過程，而不是替某人直接解決問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"educational game","meaning":"教育遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Pajama Sam was not specifically designed as an educational game.","zh":"Pajama Sam 並不是特別被設計成教育遊戲。"},{"en":"An educational game is a game designed to help players learn knowledge, skills, or ways of thinking.","zh":"educational game 指旨在幫助玩家學習知識、技能或思維方式的遊戲。"},{"en":"A spelling game can be an educational game if it helps students practise new words.","zh":"如果拼字遊戲能幫助學生練習新詞，它可以是教育遊戲。"},{"en":"Educational games work best when learning is built into the challenge, not added as boring instruction.","zh":"教育遊戲在學習融入挑戰，而不是被加成沉悶指示時效果最好。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to games with a learning purpose.","zh":"這個短語指具有學習目的的遊戲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be replete with","meaning":"充滿……","examples":[{"en":"The game was replete with problems involving thinking and learning.","zh":"這個遊戲充滿涉及思考和學習的問題。"},{"en":"To be replete with something means to be full of it.","zh":"be replete with something 指充滿某事物。"},{"en":"A good reading passage may be replete with examples that show how an idea works.","zh":"好的閱讀文章可能充滿例子，顯示一個概念如何運作。"},{"en":"If a lesson is replete with difficult words, students may need extra explanations.","zh":"如果一堂課充滿艱深詞語，學生可能需要額外解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something containing a large amount of a particular feature.","zh":"這個短語描述某物含有大量某種特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"types of problems","meaning":"各類問題","examples":[{"en":"The game contained the types of problems that psychologists study.","zh":"這個遊戲包含心理學家研究的各類問題。"},{"en":"Types of problems are different categories of difficulties or tasks that require thinking.","zh":"types of problems 指需要思考的不同類別困難或任務。"},{"en":"In school, students face types of problems such as calculation, reading comprehension, and decision-making.","zh":"在學校，學生面對計算、閱讀理解和決策等各類問題。"},{"en":"Different types of problems train different skills, so one activity may challenge the brain in several ways.","zh":"不同類型問題訓練不同技能，所以一項活動可能以多種方式挑戰大腦。"},{"en":"This phrase helps group problems by nature or skill.","zh":"這個短語幫助按性質或技能把問題分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"study thinking and learning","meaning":"研究思考及學習","examples":[{"en":"Psychologists study thinking and learning through different kinds of task.","zh":"心理學家透過不同種類的任務研究思考及學習。"},{"en":"To study thinking and learning means to examine how people understand, remember, decide, and improve.","zh":"study thinking and learning 指研究人如何理解、記憶、決策和進步。"},{"en":"A psychologist may study thinking and learning by watching how children solve puzzles.","zh":"心理學家可能透過觀察兒童如何解謎來研究思考及學習。"},{"en":"Research on thinking and learning can help teachers design better lessons.","zh":"關於思考及學習的研究可以幫助老師設計更好的課堂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes scientific investigation of how the mind works.","zh":"這個短語描述對心智如何運作的科學研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hold someone’s attention","meaning":"吸引某人的注意力","examples":[{"en":"The game held the child’s attention for a long time.","zh":"這個遊戲長時間吸引了孩子的注意力。"},{"en":"To hold someone’s attention means to keep them interested and focused.","zh":"hold someone’s attention 指令某人保持興趣和集中。"},{"en":"A clear story can hold students’ attention better than a long list of facts.","zh":"清楚的故事比一長串事實更能吸引學生的注意力。"},{"en":"When an activity holds attention, learners are more likely to keep trying.","zh":"當活動能吸引注意，學習者較可能繼續嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sustained interest and focus.","zh":"這個短語描述持續的興趣和專注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"wonder what sort of beast","meaning":"想知道……究竟是甚麼樣的東西","examples":[{"en":"Gee wondered what sort of beast a more advanced video game might be.","zh":"Gee 想知道較高階的電子遊戲究竟是甚麼樣的東西。"},{"en":"To wonder what sort of beast something is means to be curious about what kind of thing it really is.","zh":"wonder what sort of beast something is 指好奇某物真正是甚麼類型的東西。"},{"en":"A teacher may wonder what sort of beast a new exam will be before seeing sample questions.","zh":"老師在看到樣本題目前，可能想知道新考試究竟是甚麼樣的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is slightly playful because it treats something unfamiliar as if it were a strange creature.","zh":"這個短語略帶玩味，因為它把陌生事物說得像奇怪生物一樣。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing curiosity about a complex or unknown thing.","zh":"它適合描述對複雜或未知事物的好奇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a more mature video game","meaning":"較成熟的電子遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Gee became curious about the design of a more mature video game.","zh":"Gee 開始對較成熟的電子遊戲設計感到好奇。"},{"en":"A more mature video game is a game designed for older players, with more complex ideas, rules, or challenges.","zh":"more mature video game 指為較年長玩家設計、含有較複雜想法、規則或挑戰的遊戲。"},{"en":"A teenager may prefer a more mature video game that requires planning and long-term decisions.","zh":"青少年可能較喜歡需要規劃和長遠決策的成熟電子遊戲。"},{"en":"More mature games may demand reading, strategy, patience, and flexible thinking.","zh":"較成熟的遊戲可能要求閱讀、策略、耐性和靈活思維。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts simple children’s games with more complex gaming experiences.","zh":"這個短語把簡單兒童遊戲與較複雜的遊戲體驗作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"popular and entertaining activities","meaning":"受歡迎而具娛樂性的活動","examples":[{"en":"Video games are popular and entertaining activities among children.","zh":"電子遊戲是兒童之間受歡迎而具娛樂性的活動。"},{"en":"Popular and entertaining activities are things many people enjoy doing because they are fun and engaging.","zh":"popular and entertaining activities 指很多人喜歡做的事情，因為它們有趣而吸引人。"},{"en":"School sports days are popular and entertaining activities when students can join games with friends.","zh":"當學生可以和朋友一起參加遊戲，學校運動日就是受歡迎而具娛樂性的活動。"},{"en":"If an activity is both popular and entertaining, it can hold people’s attention for a long time.","zh":"如果活動既受歡迎又具娛樂性，它可以長時間吸引人的注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes activities that attract many participants and give enjoyment.","zh":"這個短語描述能吸引許多參與者並帶來樂趣的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"addictive activities","meaning":"容易令人上癮的活動","examples":[{"en":"Some parents regard video games as potentially addictive activities.","zh":"有些家長把電子遊戲視為可能令人上癮的活動。"},{"en":"Addictive activities are activities that people may find difficult to stop doing.","zh":"addictive activities 指人們可能覺得難以停止的活動。"},{"en":"Scrolling short videos can become an addictive activity if a student loses track of time every night.","zh":"如果學生每晚都忘記時間地刷短片，刷短片可以變成令人上癮的活動。"},{"en":"Addictive activities can reduce sleep, study time, and family communication if not controlled.","zh":"如果不加控制，令人上癮的活動可以減少睡眠、學習時間和家庭溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes activities that may create unhealthy attachment.","zh":"這個短語描述可能造成不健康依附的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be looked down upon","meaning":"被看不起；不受重視","examples":[{"en":"Video games are looked down upon by many parents.","zh":"電子遊戲被許多家長看不起。"},{"en":"To be looked down upon means to be disrespected or considered unimportant.","zh":"be looked down upon 指被不尊重或被視為不重要。"},{"en":"Some students look down upon vocational training, even though it can lead to skilled careers.","zh":"有些學生看不起職業訓練，雖然它可以通往專業技能職業。"},{"en":"When an activity is looked down upon, people may ignore its possible value.","zh":"當一項活動被看不起，人們可能忽視其可能價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes negative judgement or social disrespect.","zh":"這個短語描述負面判斷或社會上的不尊重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"time-wasters","meaning":"浪費時間的事物","examples":[{"en":"Some adults dismiss video games as time-wasters.","zh":"有些成年人把電子遊戲貶為浪費時間的事物。"},{"en":"Time-wasters are activities that people think use time without producing value.","zh":"time-wasters 指人們認為耗費時間卻沒有產生價值的活動。"},{"en":"A poorly planned meeting can become a time-waster if no decision is made.","zh":"如果沒有作出任何決定，規劃差劣的會議可以變成浪費時間的事物。"},{"en":"Calling something a time-waster may be unfair if it teaches useful skills or helps people relax.","zh":"如果某事教授有用技能或幫助人放鬆，稱它為浪費時間可能並不公平。"},{"en":"This word describes an activity judged as useless or unproductive.","zh":"這個詞描述被判定為無用或沒生產力的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rot the brain","meaning":"令大腦退化","examples":[{"en":"Some parents incorrectly believe that video games rot the brain.","zh":"有些家長錯誤地相信電子遊戲會令大腦退化。"},{"en":"To rot the brain means to damage thinking ability or make the mind weaker.","zh":"rot the brain 指損害思考能力或令心智變弱。"},{"en":"Some adults say too much mindless television can rot the brain, meaning it may reduce active thinking.","zh":"有些成年人說過多無腦電視會令大腦退化，意思是它可能減少主動思考。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used emotionally rather than scientifically.","zh":"這個短語常帶有情緒性，而不一定是科學說法。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly suggests mental harm or decline.","zh":"這個短語強烈暗示心智傷害或衰退。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"violent video games","meaning":"暴力電子遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Violent video games are often criticised by the media.","zh":"暴力電子遊戲常受到傳媒批評。"},{"en":"Violent video games are games that include fighting, weapons, killing, or aggressive scenes.","zh":"violent video games 指包含打鬥、武器、殺戮或攻擊性場面的遊戲。"},{"en":"Parents may check age ratings before allowing children to play violent video games.","zh":"家長可能在讓孩子玩暴力電子遊戲前查看年齡分級。"},{"en":"Violent content can raise concern because children may repeatedly watch or control aggressive actions.","zh":"暴力內容會引起憂慮，因為兒童可能反覆觀看或控制攻擊行為。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to games whose main content includes violence.","zh":"這個短語指主要內容包含暴力的遊戲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be readily blamed for","meaning":"很容易被歸咎於……","examples":[{"en":"Video games are readily blamed for violent behaviour among young people.","zh":"電子遊戲很容易被歸咎於年輕人的暴力行為。"},{"en":"To be readily blamed for something means to be quickly and easily treated as the cause of it.","zh":"be readily blamed for something 指很快而容易地被視為某事成因。"},{"en":"Social media is readily blamed for poor concentration, even when sleep and stress also matter.","zh":"社交媒體很容易被歸咎於專注力差，即使睡眠和壓力也很重要。"},{"en":"When one cause is readily blamed, people may ignore deeper or more complicated causes.","zh":"當某個原因很容易被歸咎，人們可能忽視更深層或更複雜的成因。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quick blame that may be too simple.","zh":"這個短語描述可能過於簡化的快速歸咎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"commit extreme anti-social behaviour","meaning":"作出極端反社會行為","examples":[{"en":"Some young people commit extreme anti-social behaviour.","zh":"有些年輕人作出極端反社會行為。"},{"en":"To commit extreme anti-social behaviour means to carry out very harmful actions against other people or society.","zh":"commit extreme anti-social behaviour 指作出對他人或社會非常有害的行動。"},{"en":"Destroying public property and attacking strangers are examples of extreme anti-social behaviour.","zh":"破壞公共財物和襲擊陌生人都是極端反社會行為的例子。"},{"en":"Such behaviour can create fear, damage communities, and lead to legal punishment.","zh":"這類行為可以造成恐懼、破壞社區並導致法律懲罰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious actions that violate social norms and harm others.","zh":"這個短語描述違反社會規範並傷害他人的嚴重行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"content analysis","meaning":"內容分析","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have conducted content analyses of popular video games.","zh":"研究人員對受歡迎電子遊戲進行了內容分析。"},{"en":"Content analysis is a research method that examines what appears in texts, media, games, or messages.","zh":"content analysis 指研究文本、媒體、遊戲或訊息中出現甚麼內容的方法。"},{"en":"A researcher may use content analysis to count how often advertisements show unhealthy food.","zh":"研究人員可能使用內容分析來計算廣告展示不健康食物的頻率。"},{"en":"Content analysis helps people move from opinion to evidence by looking systematically at material.","zh":"內容分析透過有系統地檢視材料，幫助人們由意見走向證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised study of content.","zh":"這個短語描述對內容的有組織研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as many as","meaning":"多達……","examples":[{"en":"As many as 89% of the games contained some violent content.","zh":"多達 89% 的遊戲包含某些暴力內容。"},{"en":"As many as means a surprisingly large number or amount, up to the figure mentioned.","zh":"as many as 指數量或比例高得令人注意，達到所提數字。"},{"en":"As many as thirty students may join the club if the activity becomes popular.","zh":"如果活動變得受歡迎，多達三十名學生可能加入社團。"},{"en":"This phrase often highlights that the number is higher than expected.","zh":"這個短語常突出數字比預期高。"},{"en":"It is useful when emphasising the scale of a finding.","zh":"它適合用於強調研究結果的規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"violent content","meaning":"暴力內容","examples":[{"en":"Many games contain at least some violent content.","zh":"許多遊戲至少包含某些暴力內容。"},{"en":"Violent content means material that shows fighting, injury, weapons, killing, or threats.","zh":"violent content 指展示打鬥、受傷、武器、殺戮或威脅的材料。"},{"en":"Parents may avoid films with violent content if their children are very young.","zh":"如果孩子很年幼，家長可能避免有暴力內容的電影。"},{"en":"Violent content can affect how people judge whether a game is suitable.","zh":"暴力內容可以影響人們判斷遊戲是否合適。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the violent parts inside a media product.","zh":"這個短語描述媒體產品中的暴力部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"aggressive content","meaning":"攻擊性內容","examples":[{"en":"A large proportion of popular games contain no aggressive content.","zh":"很大比例的受歡迎遊戲並不包含攻擊性內容。"},{"en":"Aggressive content means material showing hostile, threatening, or attacking behaviour.","zh":"aggressive content 指展示敵意、威脅或攻擊行為的材料。"},{"en":"A classroom video has aggressive content if it shows people shouting threats or trying to hurt others.","zh":"如果課堂影片展示人們大聲威脅或試圖傷害他人，它就含有攻擊性內容。"},{"en":"Aggressive content may be less extreme than graphic violence, but it can still worry parents.","zh":"攻擊性內容可能沒有血腥暴力那麼極端，但仍可能令家長擔心。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on hostile behaviour, not necessarily physical injury.","zh":"這個短語著重敵意行為，不一定涉及身體受傷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"actually have many benefits","meaning":"實際上有很多好處","examples":[{"en":"Many psychologists believe that video games actually have many benefits.","zh":"許多心理學家相信電子遊戲實際上有很多好處。"},{"en":"To actually have many benefits means to bring several advantages despite what people may assume.","zh":"actually have many benefits 指儘管人們可能有某些假設，某事仍帶來多項優點。"},{"en":"Group projects may actually have many benefits if students learn to divide work and communicate.","zh":"如果學生學會分工和溝通，小組專題實際上可以有很多好處。"},{"en":"When something has benefits, it can improve skills, confidence, or understanding.","zh":"當某事有好處，它可以改善技能、信心或理解。"},{"en":"This phrase often corrects a negative assumption.","zh":"這個短語常用來修正負面假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the main benefit being","meaning":"主要好處是……","examples":[{"en":"Video games may have several advantages, the main benefit being cognitive development.","zh":"電子遊戲可能有幾個優點，主要好處是認知發展。"},{"en":"The main benefit being introduces the most important advantage among several benefits.","zh":"the main benefit being 用來引入多個好處中最重要的一個。"},{"en":"Reading aloud has several advantages, the main benefit being better pronunciation and fluency.","zh":"大聲朗讀有幾個優點，主要好處是較好的發音和流暢度。"},{"en":"This phrase lets a writer add the key benefit after naming a wider group of benefits.","zh":"這個短語讓作者在提及一組好處後補充關鍵好處。"},{"en":"It is useful when one advantage is more important than the others.","zh":"當某一優點比其他優點更重要時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make children smarter","meaning":"令兒童更聰明","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers argue that video games can make children smarter.","zh":"有些研究人員認為電子遊戲可以令兒童更聰明。"},{"en":"To make children smarter means to improve children’s thinking, problem-solving, memory, or learning ability.","zh":"make children smarter 指改善兒童的思考、解難、記憶或學習能力。"},{"en":"Strategy games may make children smarter if they require planning and careful choices.","zh":"如果策略遊戲要求規劃和謹慎選擇，它們可能令兒童更聰明。"},{"en":"Activities make children smarter when they challenge the brain rather than simply entertain passively.","zh":"當活動挑戰大腦，而不是只提供被動娛樂，它們就能令兒童更聰明。"},{"en":"This phrase describes possible cognitive improvement in children.","zh":"這個短語描述兒童認知能力可能提升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"high-level thinking skills","meaning":"高階思維技巧","examples":[{"en":"Video games may teach children high-level thinking skills.","zh":"電子遊戲可能教兒童高階思維技巧。"},{"en":"High-level thinking skills are advanced mental skills such as planning, analysing, judging, and solving complex problems.","zh":"high-level thinking skills 指規劃、分析、判斷和解決複雜問題等高階心理能力。"},{"en":"A debate lesson can build high-level thinking skills because students must evaluate evidence.","zh":"辯論課可以建立高階思維技巧，因為學生必須評估證據。"},{"en":"Games may develop these skills when players compare options and predict results.","zh":"當玩家比較選項並預測結果，遊戲可能發展這些技能。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to thinking beyond simple memory.","zh":"這個短語指超越簡單記憶的思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be needed in the future","meaning":"將來會需要","examples":[{"en":"These problem-solving skills may be needed in the future.","zh":"這些解決問題的技巧將來可能會需要。"},{"en":"To be needed in the future means to become useful or necessary later in life or work.","zh":"be needed in the future 指在人生或工作較後階段變得有用或必要。"},{"en":"Digital skills may be needed in the future even for jobs that are not purely technical.","zh":"即使不是純技術工作，數碼技能將來也可能會需要。"},{"en":"If children practise flexible thinking now, those skills may help them later.","zh":"如果兒童現在練習靈活思考，這些技能日後可能幫到他們。"},{"en":"This phrase links present learning with future usefulness.","zh":"這個短語把現時學習與未來用途連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"change the brain","meaning":"改變大腦","examples":[{"en":"Research suggests that video games can change the brain.","zh":"研究顯示電子遊戲可以改變大腦。"},{"en":"To change the brain means to alter how the brain works or how its connections develop.","zh":"change the brain 指改變大腦運作方式或其連接如何發展。"},{"en":"Learning a new language can change the brain by strengthening memory and attention systems.","zh":"學習新語言可以透過強化記憶和注意系統改變大腦。"},{"en":"Repeated practice can change the brain because the same mental circuits are used again and again.","zh":"反覆練習可以改變大腦，因為同一心理迴路被一次又一次使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical or functional effects on the brain.","zh":"這個短語描述對大腦的物理或功能影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"physical structure","meaning":"物理結構","examples":[{"en":"Learning can change the brain’s physical structure.","zh":"學習可以改變大腦的物理結構。"},{"en":"Physical structure refers to the actual form, connections, or arrangement of something.","zh":"physical structure 指某物實際的形態、連接或排列。"},{"en":"Exercise can change the physical structure of muscles by making them stronger.","zh":"運動可以透過令肌肉更強壯而改變肌肉的物理結構。"},{"en":"In the brain, repeated learning may strengthen connections between nerve cells.","zh":"在大腦中，反覆學習可能強化神經細胞之間的連接。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on real bodily form, not just ideas or feelings.","zh":"這個短語著重真實身體形態，而不只是想法或感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the same way as","meaning":"與……方式相同","examples":[{"en":"Gaming changes the brain in the same way as learning other complex skills.","zh":"玩遊戲改變大腦的方式，與學習其他複雜技能相同。"},{"en":"In the same way as means by a similar method or process.","zh":"in the same way as 指以相似方法或過程。"},{"en":"Practising speaking improves fluency in the same way as practising piano improves performance.","zh":"練習說話改善流暢度的方式，與練習鋼琴改善表現相同。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two processes that work similarly.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個以相似方式運作的過程。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining an unfamiliar idea through a familiar one.","zh":"它適合用熟悉概念解釋陌生想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"learn to read","meaning":"學習閱讀","examples":[{"en":"Learning to read produces changes in the brain.","zh":"學習閱讀會在大腦中產生變化。"},{"en":"To learn to read means to develop the ability to understand written words and texts.","zh":"learn to read 指發展理解書面詞語和文本的能力。"},{"en":"A child learns to read by connecting letters, sounds, words, and meaning.","zh":"孩子透過連接字母、聲音、詞語和意思來學習閱讀。"},{"en":"Reading practice can improve vocabulary, attention, and understanding over time.","zh":"閱讀練習可以隨時間改善詞彙、注意力和理解力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one of the major learning achievements in childhood.","zh":"這個短語描述童年其中一項重要學習成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"play the piano","meaning":"彈鋼琴","examples":[{"en":"Playing the piano requires practice and concentration.","zh":"彈鋼琴需要練習和專注。"},{"en":"To play the piano means to produce music by pressing piano keys with the hands.","zh":"play the piano 指用手按鋼琴鍵來演奏音樂。"},{"en":"A student may play the piano every evening to prepare for a music exam.","zh":"學生可能每天晚上彈鋼琴，準備音樂考試。"},{"en":"Piano practice can train memory, hand control, listening, and patience.","zh":"鋼琴練習可以訓練記憶、手部控制、聆聽和耐性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a skill that combines mental focus and physical movement.","zh":"這個短語描述結合心理專注和身體動作的技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"navigate using a map","meaning":"使用地圖辨別方向","examples":[{"en":"People use spatial skills to navigate using a map.","zh":"人們使用空間技巧來用地圖辨別方向。"},{"en":"To navigate using a map means to find one’s way by reading directions, distances, and locations on a map.","zh":"navigate using a map 指透過閱讀地圖上的方向、距離和位置來找路。"},{"en":"A tourist may navigate using a map when the phone signal is weak.","zh":"當電話訊號弱，遊客可能使用地圖辨別方向。"},{"en":"Map navigation trains people to connect symbols with real places.","zh":"地圖導航訓練人把符號與真實地方連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finding direction through visual information.","zh":"這個短語描述透過視覺資訊尋找方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"much like","meaning":"很像；正如……","examples":[{"en":"Much like physical exercise, mental training can strengthen the brain.","zh":"正如體能運動一樣，心理訓練可以強化大腦。"},{"en":"Much like means in a very similar way to something else.","zh":"much like 指以非常相似的方式。"},{"en":"Much like learning a sport, learning English requires practice, feedback, and time.","zh":"正如學習運動一樣，學英文需要練習、回饋和時間。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers understand one idea by comparing it with another.","zh":"這個短語透過把一個想法與另一個比較，幫助讀者理解。"},{"en":"It is useful when two different activities share the same pattern.","zh":"當兩種不同活動有相同模式時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"build muscle","meaning":"鍛鍊肌肉","examples":[{"en":"Physical exercise can build muscle.","zh":"體能運動可以鍛鍊肌肉。"},{"en":"To build muscle means to make muscles stronger or larger through repeated exercise.","zh":"build muscle 指透過反覆運動令肌肉更強壯或更大。"},{"en":"A person may build muscle by lifting weights regularly and eating enough protein.","zh":"一個人可能透過定期舉重和攝取足夠蛋白質來鍛鍊肌肉。"},{"en":"Muscles grow stronger when they are challenged and then allowed to recover.","zh":"當肌肉受到挑戰並獲得恢復，它們會變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used as a comparison for strengthening the brain through practice.","zh":"這個短語常被用作透過練習強化大腦的比喻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"powerful combination of","meaning":"……的強大結合","examples":[{"en":"Gaming involves a powerful combination of concentration and reward.","zh":"玩遊戲涉及專注和獎勵的強大結合。"},{"en":"A powerful combination of things means several elements working together to create a strong effect.","zh":"powerful combination of things 指幾個元素共同作用，產生強大效果。"},{"en":"A good lesson may use a powerful combination of clear examples, practice, and feedback.","zh":"好課堂可能使用清楚例子、練習和回饋的強大結合。"},{"en":"When focus and reward happen together, learners may stay motivated longer.","zh":"當專注和獎勵同時出現，學習者可能保持更長時間的動機。"},{"en":"This phrase describes elements that become especially effective when joined.","zh":"這個短語描述多個元素結合時變得特別有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"intense concentration","meaning":"高度集中","examples":[{"en":"Many video games require intense concentration.","zh":"許多電子遊戲需要高度集中。"},{"en":"Intense concentration is very strong focus on a task, often with little attention left for anything else.","zh":"intense concentration 指對任務非常強烈地專注，通常幾乎無法注意其他事情。"},{"en":"A surgeon needs intense concentration during a delicate operation.","zh":"外科醫生在精細手術中需要高度集中。"},{"en":"Tasks requiring intense concentration can train attention but may also be tiring.","zh":"需要高度集中的任務可以訓練注意力，但也可能令人疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep mental focus.","zh":"這個短語描述深度心理專注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rewarding surges of neurotransmitters","meaning":"令人產生滿足感的神經傳導物質激增","examples":[{"en":"Success in a game may produce rewarding surges of neurotransmitters.","zh":"遊戲中的成功可能產生令人滿足的神經傳導物質激增。"},{"en":"Rewarding surges of neurotransmitters are bursts of brain chemicals that create feelings of pleasure, motivation, or satisfaction.","zh":"rewarding surges of neurotransmitters 指大腦化學物質突然增加，帶來愉悅、動機或滿足感。"},{"en":"A student may feel a small reward response after finally solving a difficult maths problem.","zh":"學生終於解出困難數學題後，可能感到一種小小的獎勵反應。"},{"en":"These rewarding surges can encourage people to repeat the behaviour that caused them.","zh":"這些令人滿足的激增可以鼓勵人重複導致它們的行為。"},{"en":"This phrase links brain chemistry with motivation.","zh":"這個短語把大腦化學與動機連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"neurotransmitters","meaning":"神經傳導物質","examples":[{"en":"Neurotransmitters carry signals between nerve cells.","zh":"神經傳導物質在神經細胞之間傳遞訊號。"},{"en":"Neurotransmitters are chemicals in the brain and nervous system that help cells communicate.","zh":"neurotransmitters 指大腦和神經系統中幫助細胞溝通的化學物質。"},{"en":"When a person learns, moves, or feels pleasure, neurotransmitters help pass messages.","zh":"當人學習、移動或感到愉快時，神經傳導物質幫助傳遞訊息。"},{"en":"Changes in neurotransmitters can affect mood, attention, motivation, and learning.","zh":"神經傳導物質的變化可以影響情緒、注意力、動機和學習。"},{"en":"This word refers to chemical messengers in the nervous system.","zh":"這個詞指神經系統中的化學信使。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"dopamine","meaning":"多巴胺","examples":[{"en":"Dopamine is associated with reward, motivation and learning.","zh":"多巴胺與獎勵、動機和學習有關。"},{"en":"Dopamine is a neurotransmitter involved in pleasure, motivation, attention, and reinforcement.","zh":"dopamine 指一種參與愉悅、動機、注意力和強化作用的神經傳導物質。"},{"en":"A student may feel motivated after small successes because reward systems involving dopamine become active.","zh":"學生可能在小成功後感到有動力，因為涉及多巴胺的獎勵系統被啟動。"},{"en":"When an activity repeatedly feels rewarding, people may want to return to it.","zh":"當一項活動反覆帶來獎勵感，人們可能想回到該活動。"},{"en":"This word names a brain chemical often linked with reward and learning.","zh":"這個詞命名一種常與獎勵和學習相關的大腦化學物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"strengthen neural circuits","meaning":"強化神經迴路","examples":[{"en":"Repeated mental activity can strengthen neural circuits.","zh":"反覆心理活動可以強化神經迴路。"},{"en":"To strengthen neural circuits means to make connections in the brain work more efficiently through repeated use.","zh":"strengthen neural circuits 指透過反覆使用令大腦中的連接運作更有效。"},{"en":"Practising multiplication every day may strengthen neural circuits related to number facts.","zh":"每天練習乘法可能強化與數字事實有關的神經迴路。"},{"en":"The more often a brain pathway is used, the easier it may become to use again.","zh":"大腦路徑被使用得越頻繁，之後再使用可能越容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how practice can build stronger brain connections.","zh":"這個短語描述練習如何建立更強的大腦連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"neural circuits","meaning":"神經迴路","examples":[{"en":"Learning and practice help develop neural circuits in the brain.","zh":"學習和練習有助發展大腦中的神經迴路。"},{"en":"Neural circuits are networks of connected nerve cells that work together to process information.","zh":"neural circuits 指由相連神經細胞組成、共同處理資訊的網絡。"},{"en":"Reading, music practice, and problem solving all use neural circuits.","zh":"閱讀、音樂練習和解難都會使用神經迴路。"},{"en":"Neural circuits can become more efficient when the same skill is practised repeatedly.","zh":"當同一技能被反覆練習，神經迴路可以變得更有效率。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the brain’s working networks.","zh":"這個短語指大腦的工作網絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"give the brain a real workout","meaning":"讓大腦得到真正的鍛鍊","examples":[{"en":"Challenging video games give the brain a real workout.","zh":"具挑戰性的電子遊戲讓大腦得到真正的鍛鍊。"},{"en":"To give the brain a real workout means to make the mind work hard through challenge and concentration.","zh":"give the brain a real workout 指透過挑戰和專注令大腦努力工作。"},{"en":"A difficult logic puzzle can give the brain a real workout after a long day of routine tasks.","zh":"在一天例行工作後，困難邏輯謎題可以讓大腦得到真正的鍛鍊。"},{"en":"Mental workouts can improve skills when they require effort, feedback, and persistence.","zh":"當心理鍛鍊需要努力、回饋和堅持，它可以改善技能。"},{"en":"This phrase compares mental challenge to physical exercise.","zh":"這個短語把心理挑戰比作體能運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"skills required to win","meaning":"取勝所需的技巧","examples":[{"en":"The skills required to win often involve complex thinking.","zh":"取勝所需的技巧常涉及複雜思考。"},{"en":"Skills required to win are the abilities a person needs in order to succeed in a game or competition.","zh":"skills required to win 指人在遊戲或比賽中成功所需的能力。"},{"en":"In a debate, the skills required to win include evidence, timing, and clear speech.","zh":"在辯論中，取勝所需的技巧包括證據、時間掌握和清楚說話。"},{"en":"Games can train useful skills if winning depends on planning, attention, and adaptation.","zh":"如果取勝取決於規劃、注意力和適應能力，遊戲可以訓練有用技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the abilities needed for success.","zh":"這個短語著重成功所需的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"abstract and high-level thinking","meaning":"抽象及高階思維","examples":[{"en":"Many games require abstract and high-level thinking.","zh":"許多遊戲需要抽象及高階思維。"},{"en":"Abstract and high-level thinking means thinking about patterns, systems, strategies, and ideas beyond simple facts.","zh":"abstract and high-level thinking 指思考模式、系統、策略和超越簡單事實的想法。"},{"en":"Planning a school event requires abstract and high-level thinking because students must imagine problems before they happen.","zh":"規劃學校活動需要抽象及高階思維，因為學生必須在問題發生前想像它們。"},{"en":"Games may train this thinking when players must predict, compare, and adjust strategies.","zh":"當玩家必須預測、比較和調整策略，遊戲可能訓練這種思維。"},{"en":"This phrase describes advanced mental work.","zh":"這個短語描述高階心理工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not even be taught at school","meaning":"甚至沒有在學校教授","examples":[{"en":"Some skills developed through gaming are not even taught at school.","zh":"有些透過遊戲發展出的技能甚至沒有在學校教授。"},{"en":"Not even be taught at school means something is absent from formal lessons despite being useful.","zh":"not even be taught at school 指某事雖然有用，卻不在正式課堂中出現。"},{"en":"Many students learn teamwork online, although it may not even be taught at school directly.","zh":"許多學生在網上學會團隊合作，雖然它可能甚至沒有在學校被直接教授。"},{"en":"If useful skills are not taught at school, students may learn them through hobbies or daily life.","zh":"如果有用技能沒有在學校教授，學生可能透過興趣或日常生活學會。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a surprising gap in formal education.","zh":"這個短語突出正式教育中令人意外的缺口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"follow instructions","meaning":"遵從指示","examples":[{"en":"Players must follow instructions to understand a game.","zh":"玩家必須遵從指示才能理解遊戲。"},{"en":"To follow instructions means to read, listen to, and do what directions tell you to do.","zh":"follow instructions 指閱讀、聆聽並按指示要求去做。"},{"en":"Students must follow instructions carefully when a test says “use no more than three words.”","zh":"當測驗寫着「不超過三個詞」時，學生必須仔細遵從指示。"},{"en":"If people do not follow instructions, they may make mistakes even when they know the topic.","zh":"如果人們不遵從指示，即使懂得主題，也可能犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes obeying directions in order to complete a task correctly.","zh":"這個短語描述為了正確完成任務而遵照方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"problem-solving skills","meaning":"解決問題的技巧","examples":[{"en":"Video games can help develop problem-solving skills.","zh":"電子遊戲可以幫助發展解決問題的技巧。"},{"en":"Problem-solving skills are the abilities used to understand a difficulty and find a workable solution.","zh":"problem-solving skills 指用來理解困難並找出可行解決方案的能力。"},{"en":"A student uses problem-solving skills when she tries a new method after the first answer fails.","zh":"當學生第一個答案失敗後嘗試新方法，她就在使用解決問題的技巧。"},{"en":"These skills grow when people face challenges, test ideas, and learn from mistakes.","zh":"當人們面對挑戰、測試想法並從錯誤中學習，這些技巧會成長。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical thinking used to overcome obstacles.","zh":"這個短語指用於克服障礙的實用思維。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"logical thinking","meaning":"邏輯思考","examples":[{"en":"Strategy games frequently require logical thinking.","zh":"策略遊戲經常需要邏輯思考。"},{"en":"Logical thinking means using reason, order, and evidence to reach a sensible conclusion.","zh":"logical thinking 指使用理性、次序和證據得出合理結論。"},{"en":"A student uses logical thinking when she checks each step of a maths solution.","zh":"當學生檢查數學解答的每一步，她就在使用邏輯思考。"},{"en":"Games require logical thinking when players must decide what action will lead to the best result.","zh":"當玩家必須判斷哪個行動會帶來最佳結果，遊戲就需要邏輯思考。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clear, reasoned thought.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚而有理據的思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hand-eye coordination","meaning":"手眼協調","examples":[{"en":"Action games can improve hand-eye coordination.","zh":"動作遊戲可以改善手眼協調。"},{"en":"Hand-eye coordination is the ability to make the hands respond accurately to what the eyes see.","zh":"hand-eye coordination 指雙手能準確回應眼睛所見的能力。"},{"en":"Catching a ball, typing quickly, and using a computer mouse all require hand-eye coordination.","zh":"接球、快速打字和使用電腦滑鼠都需要手眼協調。"},{"en":"Fast games may train coordination because players must react to moving images quickly.","zh":"快速遊戲可能訓練協調，因為玩家必須迅速回應移動畫面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the link between seeing and precise movement.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺和精準動作之間的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fine motor skills","meaning":"小肌肉活動技巧","examples":[{"en":"Controlling a game can develop fine motor skills.","zh":"控制遊戲可以發展小肌肉活動技巧。"},{"en":"Fine motor skills are small, precise movements of the fingers, hands, or wrists.","zh":"fine motor skills 指手指、手或手腕的小而精準動作。"},{"en":"Writing neatly, buttoning a shirt, and using chopsticks all require fine motor skills.","zh":"寫字整齊、扣襯衫鈕扣和使用筷子都需要小肌肉活動技巧。"},{"en":"Repeated controller movements may train small muscles and precise timing.","zh":"反覆操作控制器可能訓練小肌肉和精準時機。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful control of small movements.","zh":"這個短語描述對小動作的細緻控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"spatial skills","meaning":"空間技巧","examples":[{"en":"Players use spatial skills to judge distance and direction.","zh":"玩家使用空間技巧來判斷距離和方向。"},{"en":"Spatial skills are abilities used to understand space, position, distance, shape, and direction.","zh":"spatial skills 指理解空間、位置、距離、形狀和方向的能力。"},{"en":"Reading a floor plan or packing a suitcase efficiently requires spatial skills.","zh":"閱讀平面圖或有效率地收拾行李都需要空間技巧。"},{"en":"Games can train spatial skills when players move through maps or judge where objects are.","zh":"當玩家穿越地圖或判斷物件位置，遊戲可以訓練空間技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to thinking about space and location.","zh":"這個短語指關於空間和位置的思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"visual attention skills","meaning":"視覺專注技巧","examples":[{"en":"Fast-moving games may improve visual attention skills.","zh":"快速移動的遊戲可能改善視覺專注技巧。"},{"en":"Visual attention skills are abilities that help people notice and focus on important things they see.","zh":"visual attention skills 指幫助人注意並集中於所見重要事物的能力。"},{"en":"A driver needs visual attention skills to notice traffic lights, pedestrians, and road signs.","zh":"司機需要視覺專注技巧來注意交通燈、行人和路牌。"},{"en":"Fast games may train these skills because players must track several moving objects at once.","zh":"快速遊戲可能訓練這些技能，因為玩家必須同時追蹤多個移動物件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes focused attention through sight.","zh":"這個短語描述透過視覺進行的集中注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"iconic skills","meaning":"圖像辨識技巧","examples":[{"en":"Players learn to interpret icons and other visual symbols.","zh":"玩家學會解讀圖標和其他視覺符號。"},{"en":"Iconic skills are skills used to understand icons, signs, symbols, and visual representations.","zh":"iconic skills 指用來理解圖標、標誌、符號和視覺呈現的能力。"},{"en":"A student uses iconic skills when reading weather icons on a phone app.","zh":"學生閱讀手機應用程式上的天氣圖標時，就在使用圖像辨識技巧。"},{"en":"Games develop iconic skills because players must quickly understand health bars, maps, and warning symbols.","zh":"遊戲發展圖像辨識技巧，因為玩家必須快速理解生命值條、地圖和警告符號。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to reading meaning from visual signs.","zh":"這個短語指從視覺符號中讀取意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"there have even been studies","meaning":"甚至有研究……","examples":[{"en":"There have even been studies involving adult video-game players.","zh":"甚至有涉及成年電子遊戲玩家的研究。"},{"en":"There have even been studies means research exists, and the word “even” suggests the evidence may be surprising.","zh":"there have even been studies 指已有研究存在，而 even 暗示證據可能令人意外。"},{"en":"There have even been studies showing that short walks can improve mood during exams.","zh":"甚至有研究顯示，短途步行可以改善考試期間的情緒。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces research that strengthens or adds interest to an argument.","zh":"這個短語引入能加強論點或增加趣味的研究。"},{"en":"It is useful when evidence goes beyond what readers may expect.","zh":"當證據超出讀者預期時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"experience with video games","meaning":"玩電子遊戲的經驗","examples":[{"en":"Experience with video games may be related to certain professional skills.","zh":"玩電子遊戲的經驗可能與某些專業技能有關。"},{"en":"Experience with video games means time spent playing and learning how games work.","zh":"experience with video games 指花時間玩遊戲並學會遊戲如何運作的經驗。"},{"en":"A teenager with experience with video games may react quickly to visual instructions on a screen.","zh":"有玩電子遊戲經驗的青少年，可能能迅速回應螢幕上的視覺指示。"},{"en":"Gaming experience may matter if it trains attention, timing, or hand control.","zh":"如果遊戲經驗訓練注意力、時機或手部控制，它可能有重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical familiarity gained by playing games.","zh":"這個短語指透過玩遊戲獲得的實際熟悉程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be related to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Gaming experience may be related to improved surgical performance.","zh":"遊戲經驗可能與改善外科手術表現有關。"},{"en":"To be related to something means to have a connection with it.","zh":"be related to something 指與某事有連繫。"},{"en":"Regular reading may be related to stronger vocabulary, although other factors also matter.","zh":"定期閱讀可能與較強詞彙量有關，雖然其他因素也重要。"},{"en":"A relationship between two things does not always prove that one directly causes the other.","zh":"兩件事之間有關係，並不一定證明一方直接造成另一方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a connection or association.","zh":"這個短語描述連繫或關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"surgical skills","meaning":"外科技巧","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers have linked video gaming with better surgical skills.","zh":"有些研究人員把電子遊戲與較佳外科技巧聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Surgical skills are the abilities doctors use to perform operations safely and precisely.","zh":"surgical skills 指醫生安全而精準地進行手術所需的能力。"},{"en":"A surgeon needs surgical skills such as steady hand movement, visual judgement, and careful decision-making.","zh":"外科醫生需要穩定手部動作、視覺判斷和謹慎決策等外科技巧。"},{"en":"If a task trains precision and coordination, it may support some surgical skills.","zh":"如果一項任務訓練精準度和協調，它可能支援某些外科技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical abilities used in surgery.","zh":"這個短語指手術中使用的實際能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"find a direct link between","meaning":"發現……之間有直接關係","examples":[{"en":"Jacob Benjamin found a direct link between gaming and surgical ability.","zh":"Jacob Benjamin 發現遊戲與外科能力之間有直接關係。"},{"en":"To find a direct link between two things means to discover a clear connection between them.","zh":"find a direct link between two things 指發現兩件事之間有清楚連繫。"},{"en":"A school may find a direct link between attendance and exam performance after analysing records.","zh":"學校分析紀錄後，可能發現出席率與考試表現之間有直接關係。"},{"en":"A direct link suggests the two things are closely connected, though the reason still needs careful study.","zh":"直接關係表示兩件事緊密相連，雖然原因仍需仔細研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes discovering a clear relationship.","zh":"這個短語描述發現清楚關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"skill at video gaming","meaning":"玩電子遊戲的技巧","examples":[{"en":"Skill at video gaming may transfer to other precise activities.","zh":"玩電子遊戲的技巧可能轉移到其他精細活動。"},{"en":"Skill at video gaming means the ability to play games well through timing, strategy, attention, and control.","zh":"skill at video gaming 指透過時機掌握、策略、注意力和控制把遊戲玩好的能力。"},{"en":"A player with skill at video gaming may react quickly and manage several tasks at once.","zh":"有電子遊戲技巧的玩家可能反應快速，並能同時管理幾項任務。"},{"en":"Such skills may transfer if another activity also requires precision and fast decisions.","zh":"如果另一項活動也需要精準和快速決策，這類技巧可能轉移。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gaming ability as a learned skill.","zh":"這個短語把遊戲能力描述為學得的技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"keyhole surgery","meaning":"微創手術","examples":[{"en":"Keyhole surgery is performed through very small openings in the body.","zh":"微創手術是透過身體上的很小開口進行的。"},{"en":"Keyhole surgery is a type of surgery done through small cuts rather than one large opening.","zh":"keyhole surgery 指透過小切口而不是一個大開口進行的手術。"},{"en":"A patient may recover faster after keyhole surgery because the cuts are smaller.","zh":"病人可能在微創手術後恢復較快，因為切口較小。"},{"en":"This surgery requires precise tools, steady hands, and careful visual control.","zh":"這種手術需要精準工具、穩定雙手和仔細視覺控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes minimally invasive surgery.","zh":"這個短語描述低侵入性的手術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"laparoscopic surgery","meaning":"腹腔鏡手術","examples":[{"en":"Laparoscopic surgery requires precise hand movements.","zh":"腹腔鏡手術需要精準手部動作。"},{"en":"Laparoscopic surgery is surgery inside the abdomen using small cuts, a camera, and special instruments.","zh":"laparoscopic surgery 指透過小切口、鏡頭和特殊器械在腹部內進行的手術。"},{"en":"A surgeon performing laparoscopic surgery watches a screen while controlling tools inside the body.","zh":"進行腹腔鏡手術的外科醫生會看着螢幕，同時控制體內工具。"},{"en":"Because the movements are small and indirect, coordination and visual attention are very important.","zh":"因為動作細小且間接，協調和視覺注意非常重要。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific form of keyhole surgery.","zh":"這個短語命名一種特定的微創手術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fighter pilots","meaning":"戰鬥機機師","examples":[{"en":"Modern fighter pilots require excellent reactions and coordination.","zh":"現代戰鬥機機師需要優秀反應和協調能力。"},{"en":"Fighter pilots are military pilots trained to fly fast combat aircraft.","zh":"fighter pilots 指受訓駕駛快速作戰飛機的軍事機師。"},{"en":"Fighter pilots must read instruments, watch the sky, and make quick decisions under pressure.","zh":"戰鬥機機師必須閱讀儀表、觀察天空，並在壓力下迅速作決定。"},{"en":"Their work requires attention, spatial judgement, and hand-eye coordination.","zh":"他們的工作需要注意力、空間判斷和手眼協調。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to pilots who operate military fighter aircraft.","zh":"這個短語指操作軍用戰鬥機的機師。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"one reason experts give for","meaning":"專家提出的一個原因是……","examples":[{"en":"One reason experts give for pilots’ improved skills is their gaming experience.","zh":"專家提出機師技能改善的一個原因是他們的遊戲經驗。"},{"en":"One reason experts give for something is one explanation that specialists offer for it.","zh":"one reason experts give for something 指專家為某事提供的一個解釋。"},{"en":"One reason experts give for better student results is more regular feedback from teachers.","zh":"專家提出學生表現較佳的一個原因是老師更定期給予回饋。"},{"en":"Expert reasons can help people understand a pattern without relying only on opinion.","zh":"專家原因可以幫助人理解模式，而不只依賴意見。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an explanation from knowledgeable people.","zh":"這個短語引入知情人士提出的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be weaned on","meaning":"從小接觸……；在……中成長","examples":[{"en":"Many members of the younger generation were weaned on video games.","zh":"許多年輕一代成員從小接觸電子遊戲。"},{"en":"To be weaned on something means to grow up with it from an early age and become very familiar with it.","zh":"be weaned on something 指從小在某事物中成長，並對它非常熟悉。"},{"en":"Some children today are weaned on touchscreens before they can write fluently.","zh":"今天有些孩子在能流利書寫之前，已經從小接觸觸控螢幕。"},{"en":"Being weaned on a technology can shape habits, skills, and expectations.","zh":"從小接觸某種科技可以塑造習慣、技能和期望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes early and repeated exposure while growing up.","zh":"這個短語描述成長期間早期且反覆的接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"manage limited resources","meaning":"管理有限資源","examples":[{"en":"Players learn to manage limited resources carefully.","zh":"玩家學會謹慎管理有限資源。"},{"en":"To manage limited resources means to use a small supply of money, time, materials, or energy wisely.","zh":"manage limited resources 指明智使用有限的金錢、時間、材料或精力。"},{"en":"A student must manage limited resources when preparing for exams with only two evenings left.","zh":"當學生只剩兩個晚上準備考試時，就必須管理有限資源。"},{"en":"If resources are limited, poor choices can make later problems harder to solve.","zh":"如果資源有限，錯誤選擇會令之後問題更難解決。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful planning when there is not enough of everything.","zh":"這個短語描述在不是所有東西都充足時進行仔細規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"make the best use of","meaning":"充分利用……","examples":[{"en":"Strategy-game players must make the best use of the resources available.","zh":"策略遊戲玩家必須充分利用可用資源。"},{"en":"To make the best use of something means to use it as effectively as possible.","zh":"make the best use of something 指盡可能有效地使用某物。"},{"en":"A student can make the best use of a short lesson by asking questions and taking clear notes.","zh":"學生可以透過提問和做清楚筆記，充分利用短短一堂課。"},{"en":"When resources are limited, making the best use of them can decide success or failure.","zh":"當資源有限，能否充分利用它們可以決定成敗。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on using what you have wisely.","zh":"這個短語著重明智使用手上已有的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the same way as in real life","meaning":"與現實生活中的方式相同","examples":[{"en":"Players manage resources in much the same way as in real life.","zh":"玩家管理資源的方式與現實生活中的方式大致相同。"},{"en":"The same way as in real life means in a manner similar to how things happen outside the game or story.","zh":"the same way as in real life 指以類似遊戲或故事之外真實情況的方式。"},{"en":"A budgeting game may teach money choices in the same way as in real life.","zh":"預算遊戲可能以與現實生活相同的方式教授金錢選擇。"},{"en":"When games copy real-life constraints, players practise decisions that feel meaningful.","zh":"當遊戲模仿真實生活限制，玩家練習的決策會更有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a simulated situation with everyday reality.","zh":"這個短語把模擬情境與日常現實連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"strategy game","meaning":"策略遊戲","examples":[{"en":"A strategy game requires planning and careful decision-making.","zh":"策略遊戲需要規劃和謹慎決策。"},{"en":"A strategy game is a game where success depends on planning, resource use, and long-term choices.","zh":"strategy game 指成功取決於規劃、資源使用和長遠選擇的遊戲。"},{"en":"Chess is a strategy game because players must think several moves ahead.","zh":"國際象棋是策略遊戲，因為玩家必須預想幾步之後。"},{"en":"Strategy games can train patience because quick action is not always the best answer.","zh":"策略遊戲可以訓練耐性，因為快速行動不一定是最佳答案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes games centred on planning rather than only speed.","zh":"這個短語描述以規劃為中心，而不只是速度的遊戲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"develop a city","meaning":"發展一座城市","examples":[{"en":"Players may have to develop a city while managing its resources.","zh":"玩家可能必須在管理資源的同時發展一座城市。"},{"en":"To develop a city means to build and improve housing, transport, services, and economic activity.","zh":"develop a city 指建設並改善住屋、交通、服務和經濟活動。"},{"en":"A mayor may develop a city by adding parks, schools, hospitals, and better roads.","zh":"市長可能透過增加公園、學校、醫院和更好的道路來發展城市。"},{"en":"City development requires balancing growth with money, land, and citizens’ needs.","zh":"城市發展需要在增長、金錢、土地和市民需要之間取得平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised growth and improvement of an urban area.","zh":"這個短語描述城市地區有組織的增長和改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"an unexpected event","meaning":"突發事件","examples":[{"en":"An unexpected event may force the player to change plans.","zh":"突發事件可能迫使玩家改變計劃。"},{"en":"An unexpected event is something that happens suddenly and was not planned or predicted.","zh":"unexpected event 指突然發生、未被計劃或預測的事情。"},{"en":"A sudden bus delay is an unexpected event that can make a student late for school.","zh":"突然巴士延誤是一個突發事件，可以令學生上學遲到。"},{"en":"Unexpected events test flexibility because people must adjust quickly.","zh":"突發事件考驗靈活性，因為人們必須快速調整。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a surprise situation that changes what people should do.","zh":"這個短語描述改變人們應如何行動的意外情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an enemy might emerge","meaning":"敵人可能突然出現","examples":[{"en":"An enemy might emerge while the player is developing a city.","zh":"當玩家正在發展城市時，敵人可能突然出現。"},{"en":"An enemy might emerge means an opponent may suddenly appear or become a threat.","zh":"an enemy might emerge 指對手可能突然出現或變成威脅。"},{"en":"In a debate, a new objection might emerge when another team notices a weak point.","zh":"在辯論中，當另一隊注意到弱點時，新反駁可能突然出現。"},{"en":"When an enemy emerges, plans may need to change immediately.","zh":"當敵人出現，計劃可能需要立即改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a new threat appearing during an ongoing task.","zh":"這個短語描述正在進行任務期間新威脅出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"force someone to be flexible","meaning":"迫使某人靈活應變","examples":[{"en":"Changing conditions force players to be flexible.","zh":"不斷改變的情況迫使玩家靈活應變。"},{"en":"To force someone to be flexible means to make them adjust their plans because the situation changes.","zh":"force someone to be flexible 指因情況改變而令某人調整計劃。"},{"en":"A sudden timetable change can force teachers to be flexible with lesson plans.","zh":"突然改時間表可以迫使老師在教案上靈活應變。"},{"en":"Flexibility becomes necessary when old methods no longer work.","zh":"當舊方法不再有效，靈活性就變得必要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pressure that makes people adapt.","zh":"這個短語描述使人適應的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"change tactics","meaning":"改變策略","examples":[{"en":"Players must quickly change tactics when a strategy fails.","zh":"當策略失敗，玩家必須迅速改變策略。"},{"en":"To change tactics means to switch to a different method for reaching a goal.","zh":"change tactics 指轉用另一種方法去達成目標。"},{"en":"A student may change tactics by studying with flashcards after reading notes does not work.","zh":"如果讀筆記沒有成效，學生可能透過使用單字卡來改變策略。"},{"en":"Changing tactics can prevent repeated failure when conditions are different from expected.","zh":"當情況與預期不同，改變策略可以避免重複失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adjusting the method, not abandoning the goal.","zh":"這個短語描述調整方法，而不是放棄目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"almost every second","meaning":"幾乎每一秒","examples":[{"en":"Some games require players to make decisions almost every second.","zh":"有些遊戲要求玩家幾乎每一秒都作決定。"},{"en":"Almost every second means very frequently, with almost no break between actions.","zh":"almost every second 指非常頻繁地，行動之間幾乎沒有停頓。"},{"en":"A busy receptionist may answer calls and check bookings almost every second during lunchtime.","zh":"繁忙接待員在午飯時間可能幾乎每一秒都要接電話和查預約。"},{"en":"When decisions come almost every second, people need speed, attention, and calmness.","zh":"當決定幾乎每一秒都出現，人需要速度、注意力和冷靜。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises very rapid and repeated action.","zh":"這個短語強調非常快速而反覆的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"simulate stressful events","meaning":"模擬具壓力的事件","examples":[{"en":"Action games often simulate stressful events.","zh":"動作遊戲常模擬具壓力的事件。"},{"en":"To simulate stressful events means to create artificial situations that feel tense or urgent.","zh":"simulate stressful events 指創造人工情境，讓人感到緊張或急迫。"},{"en":"A driving simulator may simulate stressful events such as sudden braking or heavy rain.","zh":"駕駛模擬器可能模擬突然煞車或大雨等具壓力事件。"},{"en":"Simulations can train people safely before they face similar events in real life.","zh":"模擬可以在人們面對相似真實事件前安全地訓練他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practising difficult situations in a controlled setting.","zh":"這個短語描述在受控環境中練習困難情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"battle or action games","meaning":"戰鬥或動作遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Battle or action games require rapid reactions.","zh":"戰鬥或動作遊戲需要快速反應。"},{"en":"Battle or action games are games focused on fighting, movement, speed, and quick responses.","zh":"battle or action games 指以戰鬥、移動、速度和快速回應為核心的遊戲。"},{"en":"A player in an action game may need to jump, dodge, and aim within seconds.","zh":"動作遊戲玩家可能需要在數秒內跳躍、閃避和瞄準。"},{"en":"These games can train reaction time because the screen changes quickly.","zh":"這些遊戲可以訓練反應時間，因為畫面迅速改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to fast games built around conflict or movement.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞衝突或移動建立的快速遊戲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a training tool for","meaning":"用於……的訓練工具","examples":[{"en":"Video games could be used as a training tool for real-world situations.","zh":"電子遊戲可被用作現實世界情況的訓練工具。"},{"en":"A training tool for something is a method or device used to practise a skill before using it for real.","zh":"training tool for something 指在真實使用前用來練習技能的方法或裝置。"},{"en":"Flight simulators are training tools for pilots learning emergency procedures.","zh":"飛行模擬器是用於機師學習緊急程序的訓練工具。"},{"en":"A good training tool allows people to make mistakes safely and learn from them.","zh":"良好的訓練工具讓人安全地犯錯並從中學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something used to develop practical ability.","zh":"這個短語描述用來發展實際能力的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"real-world situations","meaning":"現實世界的情況","examples":[{"en":"Simulated games may prepare people for real-world situations.","zh":"模擬遊戲可能使人準備好面對現實世界的情況。"},{"en":"Real-world situations are actual situations people face outside games, classrooms, or theories.","zh":"real-world situations 指人們在遊戲、課堂或理論之外真正面對的情況。"},{"en":"A first-aid course prepares students for real-world situations such as accidents or sudden illness.","zh":"急救課程讓學生準備好面對意外或突發疾病等現實世界情況。"},{"en":"Training is more useful when it connects practice with real-world situations.","zh":"當訓練把練習與現實世界情況連接起來，它會更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts actual life with simulation or theory.","zh":"這個短語把真實生活與模擬或理論作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"prime the brain to","meaning":"使大腦準備好去……","examples":[{"en":"Action games may prime the brain to make quick decisions.","zh":"動作遊戲可能使大腦準備好去迅速作決定。"},{"en":"To prime the brain to do something means to prepare it to respond in a certain way.","zh":"prime the brain to do something 指使大腦準備以某種方式回應。"},{"en":"A warm-up question can prime the brain to focus before a difficult reading task.","zh":"熱身問題可以在困難閱讀任務前，使大腦準備好集中。"},{"en":"Repeated fast choices may prepare the brain to react more quickly later.","zh":"反覆快速選擇可能使大腦日後準備好更快反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental preparation through previous experience.","zh":"這個短語描述透過先前經驗進行心理準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make quick decisions","meaning":"迅速作出決定","examples":[{"en":"Players frequently have to make quick decisions under pressure.","zh":"玩家經常必須在壓力下迅速作出決定。"},{"en":"To make quick decisions means to choose what to do in a short time.","zh":"make quick decisions 指在短時間內選擇要做甚麼。"},{"en":"A nurse may need to make quick decisions when a patient’s condition suddenly changes.","zh":"當病人情況突然改變，護士可能需要迅速作出決定。"},{"en":"Quick decisions can be useful, but they still need enough information to avoid careless mistakes.","zh":"迅速決策可以有用，但仍需要足夠資料以避免粗心錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fast choice-making in urgent situations.","zh":"這個短語描述緊急情況中的快速選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be used to train","meaning":"被用作訓練……","examples":[{"en":"Video games can be used to train soldiers and surgeons.","zh":"電子遊戲可以被用作訓練士兵和外科醫生。"},{"en":"To be used to train someone means to serve as a tool for teaching or practising skills.","zh":"be used to train someone 指作為教授或練習技能的工具。"},{"en":"A simulator can be used to train drivers before they enter busy roads.","zh":"模擬器可以被用作訓練司機，讓他們在進入繁忙道路前練習。"},{"en":"Training tools help people practise risky skills without immediate real-world danger.","zh":"訓練工具幫助人練習高風險技能，而不立即面對真實世界危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the purpose of an activity or device in skill development.","zh":"這個短語描述某活動或裝置在技能發展中的用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"deal with immediate problems","meaning":"處理眼前問題","examples":[{"en":"Gamers must deal with immediate problems as they arise.","zh":"玩家必須在眼前問題出現時處理它們。"},{"en":"To deal with immediate problems means to handle urgent issues that need attention now.","zh":"deal with immediate problems 指處理需要立即關注的緊急問題。"},{"en":"A teacher must deal with immediate problems when the projector stops working during a lesson.","zh":"當投影機在課堂中停止運作，老師必須處理眼前問題。"},{"en":"If immediate problems are ignored, they may prevent long-term plans from working.","zh":"如果眼前問題被忽視，它們可能阻礙長遠計劃運作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on urgent problem handling.","zh":"這個短語著重緊急問題處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"long-term goals","meaning":"長遠目標","examples":[{"en":"Successful players do not lose sight of their long-term goals.","zh":"成功玩家不會忘記自己的長遠目標。"},{"en":"Long-term goals are aims that take a long time to reach and require planning.","zh":"long-term goals 指需要長時間達成並需要規劃的目標。"},{"en":"A student’s long-term goal may be entering university, even while doing daily homework.","zh":"學生的長遠目標可能是升讀大學，即使每天仍要做功課。"},{"en":"Short-term problems should be solved without forgetting the larger goal.","zh":"人應解決短期問題，同時不忘更大的目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes future aims that guide present choices.","zh":"這個短語描述引導當前選擇的未來目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"keep something on the horizon","meaning":"時刻留意……的長遠目標","examples":[{"en":"Players keep their long-term goals on the horizon while solving immediate problems.","zh":"玩家在解決眼前問題時，仍時刻留意自己的長遠目標。"},{"en":"To keep something on the horizon means to continue thinking about a future aim while dealing with the present.","zh":"keep something on the horizon 指在處理當前事情時，仍繼續想着未來目標。"},{"en":"A student may keep university on the horizon while studying for weekly quizzes.","zh":"學生可能在準備每週小測時，仍把大學目標放在視野中。"},{"en":"This helps people avoid being trapped by only short-term worries.","zh":"這幫助人避免只被短期憂慮困住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping a future goal in view.","zh":"這個短語描述把未來目標保持在視野內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"force oneself to read","meaning":"迫使自己閱讀","examples":[{"en":"Young gamers may force themselves to read in order to progress.","zh":"年輕玩家可能為了進展而迫使自己閱讀。"},{"en":"To force oneself to read means to make oneself read even when it feels difficult or unattractive.","zh":"force oneself to read 指即使覺得困難或不吸引，也要求自己閱讀。"},{"en":"A student may force herself to read instructions carefully after losing marks for missing details.","zh":"學生因忽略細節而失分後，可能迫使自己仔細閱讀指示。"},{"en":"People may push themselves to read when reading is necessary to reach a goal.","zh":"當閱讀對達成目標是必要時，人們可能推動自己閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes self-pressure used to complete needed reading.","zh":"這個短語描述為完成必要閱讀而施加自我壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"get instructions","meaning":"取得指示","examples":[{"en":"Players read game text to get instructions.","zh":"玩家閱讀遊戲文字以取得指示。"},{"en":"To get instructions means to receive directions about what to do.","zh":"get instructions 指收到關於要做甚麼的指引。"},{"en":"A student reads the task sheet to get instructions before starting a project.","zh":"學生在開始專題前閱讀任務紙以取得指示。"},{"en":"Without instructions, people may waste time guessing the rules or next steps.","zh":"沒有指示，人們可能浪費時間猜測規則或下一步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes obtaining guidance for action.","zh":"這個短語描述取得行動指引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"follow storylines","meaning":"跟隨故事情節","examples":[{"en":"Gamers must follow storylines to understand what is happening.","zh":"玩家必須跟隨故事情節，才能理解正在發生甚麼。"},{"en":"To follow storylines means to understand the sequence of events in a story.","zh":"follow storylines 指理解故事中事件的先後發展。"},{"en":"Viewers must follow storylines in a TV drama to understand why characters make choices.","zh":"觀眾必須跟隨電視劇故事情節，才能理解角色為何作出選擇。"},{"en":"If a player cannot follow the storyline, missions and goals may become confusing.","zh":"如果玩家不能跟隨故事情節，任務和目標可能變得混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes tracking the development of a narrative.","zh":"這個短語描述追蹤敘事發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"obtain information from","meaning":"從……取得資料","examples":[{"en":"Players obtain information from instructions and game texts.","zh":"玩家從指示和遊戲文字中取得資料。"},{"en":"To obtain information from something means to get useful facts or guidance from it.","zh":"obtain information from something 指從某物取得有用事實或指引。"},{"en":"Students obtain information from charts when answering data questions.","zh":"學生回答數據題時，會從圖表中取得資料。"},{"en":"Good readers know where to obtain information from a passage instead of guessing.","zh":"好讀者知道從文章哪裡取得資料，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes getting knowledge from a source.","zh":"這個短語描述從來源取得知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be similar to","meaning":"與……相似","examples":[{"en":"Playing a video game can be similar to working through a science problem.","zh":"玩電子遊戲可以與逐步處理科學問題相似。"},{"en":"To be similar to something means to share important features with it.","zh":"be similar to something 指與某事共享重要特徵。"},{"en":"Planning a trip is similar to managing a project because both require time, budget, and choices.","zh":"規劃旅行與管理項目相似，因為兩者都需要時間、預算和選擇。"},{"en":"If two activities are similar, skills from one may help with the other.","zh":"如果兩項活動相似，一項活動中的技能可能幫到另一項。"},{"en":"This phrase compares things that are not identical but have common features.","zh":"這個短語比較並不完全相同但有共同特徵的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"work through a problem","meaning":"逐步處理問題","examples":[{"en":"Students must work through a problem step by step.","zh":"學生必須一步一步處理問題。"},{"en":"To work through a problem means to solve it carefully by dealing with each part in order.","zh":"work through a problem 指按次序處理每個部分，仔細解決問題。"},{"en":"A student may work through a grammar problem by checking the subject, verb, and tense.","zh":"學生可能透過檢查主語、動詞和時態來逐步處理文法問題。"},{"en":"Working through a problem reduces panic because the task becomes smaller and clearer.","zh":"逐步處理問題可以減少恐慌，因為任務變得更小更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a careful step-by-step solving process.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細逐步解決的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"come up with a hypothesis","meaning":"提出假設","examples":[{"en":"Gamers often come up with a hypothesis about how to succeed.","zh":"玩家常提出關於如何成功的假設。"},{"en":"To come up with a hypothesis means to form a possible explanation or plan that can be tested.","zh":"come up with a hypothesis 指形成一個可測試的可能解釋或計劃。"},{"en":"A student may come up with a hypothesis that plants grow faster with more sunlight.","zh":"學生可能提出假設，認為植物在更多陽光下生長更快。"},{"en":"If the evidence does not support the hypothesis, the learner should revise it.","zh":"如果證據不支持假設，學習者應修正它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes forming a testable idea.","zh":"這個短語描述形成可測試想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"try out combinations of","meaning":"嘗試不同的……組合","examples":[{"en":"Players try out combinations of weapons and powers.","zh":"玩家嘗試不同的武器和能力組合。"},{"en":"To try out combinations of things means to test different mixtures or pairings to see what works best.","zh":"try out combinations of things 指測試不同混合或配搭，看哪一種最有效。"},{"en":"A cook may try out combinations of spices before choosing the best flavour.","zh":"廚師可能先嘗試不同香料組合，再選出最佳味道。"},{"en":"Trying different combinations helps people learn through experiment and comparison.","zh":"嘗試不同組合幫助人透過實驗和比較學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes testing several possible mixtures.","zh":"這個短語描述測試幾種可能配搭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"weapons and powers","meaning":"武器和能力","examples":[{"en":"Some games allow players to combine different weapons and powers.","zh":"有些遊戲容許玩家結合不同武器和能力。"},{"en":"Weapons and powers are tools, abilities, or special strengths used by characters in a game.","zh":"weapons and powers 指遊戲角色使用的工具、能力或特殊力量。"},{"en":"A player may choose a sword as a weapon and healing as a power.","zh":"玩家可能選擇劍作為武器，並選擇治療作為能力。"},{"en":"Combining weapons and powers can change how a player solves challenges.","zh":"結合武器和能力可以改變玩家解決挑戰的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the tools and abilities available for action in a game.","zh":"這個短語指遊戲中可用於行動的工具和能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"defeat an enemy","meaning":"擊敗敵人","examples":[{"en":"Players experiment with different methods to defeat an enemy.","zh":"玩家嘗試不同方法來擊敗敵人。"},{"en":"To defeat an enemy means to overcome or beat an opponent.","zh":"defeat an enemy 指克服或打敗對手。"},{"en":"A chess player may defeat an enemy by planning several moves ahead.","zh":"棋手可能透過預想幾步之後來擊敗敵人。"},{"en":"If one method fails, trying another strategy may help defeat the opponent.","zh":"如果一種方法失敗，嘗試另一種策略可能有助擊敗對手。"},{"en":"This phrase describes overcoming opposition.","zh":"這個短語描述克服阻力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"if one approach does not work","meaning":"如果一種方法行不通","examples":[{"en":"If one approach does not work, the player tries another.","zh":"如果一種方法行不通，玩家就嘗試另一種。"},{"en":"If one approach does not work means if one method fails to solve the problem.","zh":"if one approach does not work 指如果一種方法未能解決問題。"},{"en":"If one study method does not work, a student may try flashcards or practice questions.","zh":"如果一種溫習方法行不通，學生可能嘗試單字卡或練習題。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages flexibility after failure.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵失敗後保持靈活。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing trial, adjustment, and improvement.","zh":"它適合描述嘗試、調整和改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"change one’s hypothesis","meaning":"改變自己的假設","examples":[{"en":"Players change their hypothesis when the evidence does not support it.","zh":"當證據不支持假設時，玩家會改變自己的假設。"},{"en":"To change one’s hypothesis means to revise a possible explanation after testing it.","zh":"change one’s hypothesis 指在測試後修正一個可能解釋。"},{"en":"A student may change her hypothesis when plants without extra water grow better than expected.","zh":"當沒有額外澆水的植物比預期生長更好，學生可能改變自己的假設。"},{"en":"Changing a hypothesis shows learning because the thinker responds to evidence.","zh":"改變假設顯示學習，因為思考者會回應證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes updating an idea after new information appears.","zh":"這個短語描述在新資訊出現後更新想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"try the next one","meaning":"嘗試下一個方法","examples":[{"en":"If one strategy fails, the player tries the next one.","zh":"如果一個策略失敗，玩家就嘗試下一個方法。"},{"en":"To try the next one means to move on to another option after the first option fails.","zh":"try the next one 指在第一個選項失敗後轉向另一個選項。"},{"en":"If one bus route is closed, a commuter tries the next one on the map.","zh":"如果一條巴士路線關閉，通勤者會嘗試地圖上的下一條。"},{"en":"Trying the next option prevents people from stopping after a single failure.","zh":"嘗試下一個選項可以防止人們在一次失敗後停下來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes persistence through alternatives.","zh":"這個短語描述透過替代方案堅持下去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"goal-driven experience","meaning":"目標導向的體驗","examples":[{"en":"A video game is a goal-driven experience.","zh":"電子遊戲是一種目標導向的體驗。"},{"en":"A goal-driven experience is an activity organised around reaching a clear aim.","zh":"goal-driven experience 指圍繞達成清楚目標而組織起來的活動。"},{"en":"Preparing for a speaking exam is a goal-driven experience because each practice session has a purpose.","zh":"準備口語考試是目標導向的體驗，因為每次練習都有目的。"},{"en":"Clear goals can make people more willing to practise and improve.","zh":"清楚目標可以令人更願意練習和進步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning or action guided by a target.","zh":"這個短語描述由目標引導的學習或行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be fundamental to learning","meaning":"是學習的基礎","examples":[{"en":"Goal-driven experiences are fundamental to learning.","zh":"目標導向的體驗是學習的基礎。"},{"en":"To be fundamental to learning means to be basic, necessary, or deeply important for learning to happen.","zh":"be fundamental to learning 指對學習發生而言是基本、必要或非常重要的。"},{"en":"Feedback is fundamental to learning because students need to know what to improve.","zh":"回饋是學習的基礎，因為學生需要知道要改善甚麼。"},{"en":"If goals are missing, learners may practise without direction.","zh":"如果缺少目標，學習者可能沒有方向地練習。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies something as a foundation of learning.","zh":"這個短語指出某事是學習的根基。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"use mathematical skills","meaning":"運用數學技巧","examples":[{"en":"Players use mathematical skills when calculating resources.","zh":"玩家在計算資源時運用數學技巧。"},{"en":"To use mathematical skills means to apply number sense, calculation, measurement, or logical patterns.","zh":"use mathematical skills 指應用數字感、計算、量度或邏輯模式。"},{"en":"A shopper uses mathematical skills when comparing prices and discounts.","zh":"購物者比較價錢和折扣時，就在運用數學技巧。"},{"en":"Games may require mathematical skills if players must calculate costs, time, or probability.","zh":"如果玩家必須計算成本、時間或機率，遊戲可能需要數學技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical use of maths.","zh":"這個短語描述數學的實際使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"quantitative analysis","meaning":"定量分析","examples":[{"en":"Resource management often involves quantitative analysis.","zh":"資源管理常涉及定量分析。"},{"en":"Quantitative analysis means examining numbers, amounts, or measurable data to make decisions.","zh":"quantitative analysis 指檢視數字、數量或可量度數據以作決策。"},{"en":"A school uses quantitative analysis when it compares test scores across classes.","zh":"學校比較不同班級的測驗分數時，就是使用定量分析。"},{"en":"Quantitative analysis helps people see patterns that may not be obvious from feelings alone.","zh":"定量分析幫助人看見單靠感覺未必明顯的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to number-based analysis.","zh":"這個短語指以數字為基礎的分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"higher levels of a game","meaning":"遊戲的較高級別","examples":[{"en":"The challenges become more difficult at higher levels of a game.","zh":"在遊戲的較高級別，挑戰會變得更困難。"},{"en":"Higher levels of a game are later stages where tasks become more complex or demanding.","zh":"higher levels of a game 指任務變得更複雜或要求更高的較後階段。"},{"en":"In higher levels of a game, players may face stronger enemies and less time.","zh":"在遊戲較高級別中，玩家可能面對更強敵人和更少時間。"},{"en":"Increasing difficulty keeps players learning instead of repeating easy tasks.","zh":"難度增加令玩家繼續學習，而不是重複簡單任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes advanced stages in a game.","zh":"這個短語描述遊戲中的進階階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fail the first time around","meaning":"第一次嘗試時失敗","examples":[{"en":"Players often fail the first time around.","zh":"玩家常在第一次嘗試時失敗。"},{"en":"To fail the first time around means to be unsuccessful on the first attempt.","zh":"fail the first time around 指在第一次嘗試時未能成功。"},{"en":"A student may fail the first time around when trying a new grammar exercise.","zh":"學生嘗試新的文法練習時，可能第一次嘗試時失敗。"},{"en":"First failure can be useful if it shows what needs to change.","zh":"第一次失敗可以有用，如果它顯示需要改變甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase normalises failure as part of learning.","zh":"這個短語把失敗視為學習的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"keep on trying","meaning":"不斷嘗試","examples":[{"en":"Successful gamers keep on trying after they fail.","zh":"成功玩家在失敗後會不斷嘗試。"},{"en":"To keep on trying means to continue making attempts even after difficulty or failure.","zh":"keep on trying 指即使遇到困難或失敗仍繼續嘗試。"},{"en":"A learner may keep on trying to pronounce a word until it becomes clearer.","zh":"學習者可能不斷嘗試發某個詞，直到發音更清楚。"},{"en":"Persistence helps because improvement often comes after repeated correction.","zh":"堅持有幫助，因為進步常在反覆修正後出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes not giving up.","zh":"這個短語描述不放棄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"move on to the next level","meaning":"進入下一關","examples":[{"en":"Players must solve the problem before they can move on to the next level.","zh":"玩家必須解決問題，才能進入下一關。"},{"en":"To move on to the next level means to progress to a more advanced stage after completing the current one.","zh":"move on to the next level 指完成當前階段後進入更進階階段。"},{"en":"A student moves on to the next level of reading when easier books are no longer challenging.","zh":"當較容易的書不再有挑戰性，學生便進入下一級閱讀。"},{"en":"Reaching the next level often requires proving that earlier skills are secure.","zh":"到達下一級通常需要證明早前技能穩固。"},{"en":"This phrase describes progress after completing a challenge.","zh":"這個短語描述完成挑戰後的進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be played online","meaning":"在網上進行","examples":[{"en":"Many modern games are played online.","zh":"許多現代遊戲在網上進行。"},{"en":"To be played online means to be played through the internet, often with other people.","zh":"be played online 指透過互聯網進行，通常與其他人一起玩。"},{"en":"A board-game style app may be played online by friends living in different cities.","zh":"住在不同城市的朋友可能在網上玩桌遊式應用程式。"},{"en":"Online play can create cooperation, competition, and communication across distance.","zh":"網上遊玩可以跨距離創造合作、競爭和溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes internet-based gaming.","zh":"這個短語描述以互聯網為基礎的遊戲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"involve cooperation with","meaning":"涉及與……合作","examples":[{"en":"Online games often involve cooperation with other players.","zh":"網上遊戲常涉及與其他玩家合作。"},{"en":"To involve cooperation with someone means to require people to work together toward a shared goal.","zh":"involve cooperation with someone 指需要人們為共同目標一起工作。"},{"en":"A school project may involve cooperation with classmates to research and present findings.","zh":"學校專題可能涉及與同學合作研究並展示結果。"},{"en":"Cooperation can improve results because different people bring different strengths.","zh":"合作可以改善結果，因為不同人帶來不同強項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes teamwork as part of an activity.","zh":"這個短語描述活動中的團隊合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in order to win","meaning":"為了取勝","examples":[{"en":"Players may need to cooperate in order to win.","zh":"玩家可能需要合作，為了取勝。"},{"en":"In order to win means for the purpose of achieving victory or success.","zh":"in order to win 指為了取得勝利或成功。"},{"en":"A debate team must organise evidence clearly in order to win.","zh":"辯論隊必須清楚組織證據，為了取勝。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an action with the goal of success.","zh":"這個短語把行動與成功目標連接起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining why someone does something.","zh":"它適合用於解釋某人為何做某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"gain self-confidence","meaning":"建立自信","examples":[{"en":"Successfully completing difficult tasks can help children gain self-confidence.","zh":"成功完成困難任務可以幫助兒童建立自信。"},{"en":"To gain self-confidence means to become more willing to trust one’s own ability.","zh":"gain self-confidence 指變得更願意相信自己的能力。"},{"en":"A shy student may gain self-confidence after giving a short presentation successfully.","zh":"害羞學生成功完成短演講後，可能建立自信。"},{"en":"Success after effort can build confidence because the child sees real progress.","zh":"努力後的成功可以建立信心，因為孩子看見真實進步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growing belief in oneself.","zh":"這個短語描述對自己的信念增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"以……為題材；建基於……","examples":[{"en":"Many games are based on history, governance or city building.","zh":"許多遊戲以歷史、管治或城市建設為題材。"},{"en":"To be based on something means to use it as the main idea, foundation, or source.","zh":"be based on something 指以某事作為主要想法、基礎或來源。"},{"en":"A film may be based on a true story from a local community.","zh":"電影可能以本地社區的真實故事為題材。"},{"en":"If a game is based on history, it may introduce players to real events or systems.","zh":"如果遊戲以歷史為題材，它可能向玩家介紹真實事件或制度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the foundation behind a work or idea.","zh":"這個短語描述作品或想法背後的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"city building","meaning":"城市建設","examples":[{"en":"City-building games teach players about planning and resource management.","zh":"城市建設遊戲教玩家關於規劃和資源管理。"},{"en":"City building means designing, expanding, and managing an urban area.","zh":"city building 指設計、擴展和管理城市地區。"},{"en":"In a city-building game, players may decide where to place roads, homes, schools, and hospitals.","zh":"在城市建設遊戲中，玩家可能決定道路、住宅、學校和醫院的位置。"},{"en":"City building requires choices because space, money, and public needs are limited.","zh":"城市建設需要選擇，因為空間、金錢和公共需要有限。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the process of creating and managing cities.","zh":"這個短語指創造和管理城市的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"governance","meaning":"管治","examples":[{"en":"Some games introduce players to ideas about governance.","zh":"有些遊戲向玩家介紹關於管治的概念。"},{"en":"Governance means the way a country, city, school, or organisation is managed and decisions are made.","zh":"governance 指國家、城市、學校或組織如何被管理及如何作出決定。"},{"en":"Student councils teach basic governance because students discuss rules and represent classmates.","zh":"學生會教授基本管治，因為學生討論規則並代表同學。"},{"en":"Good governance affects fairness, public trust, and how resources are used.","zh":"良好管治影響公平、公共信任和資源如何使用。"},{"en":"This word refers to systems of decision-making and management.","zh":"這個詞指決策和管理制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"indirectly teach","meaning":"間接教導","examples":[{"en":"Games can indirectly teach children about society and history.","zh":"遊戲可以間接教導兒童認識社會和歷史。"},{"en":"To indirectly teach means to help someone learn without giving a direct lesson.","zh":"indirectly teach 指在沒有直接上課的情況下幫助某人學習。"},{"en":"A story can indirectly teach kindness by showing how characters help one another.","zh":"故事可以透過展示角色如何互相幫助，間接教導善良。"},{"en":"Indirect teaching works when learners discover ideas through experience.","zh":"當學習者透過經驗發現想法，間接教導就會發揮作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning that happens through activity, not direct instruction.","zh":"這個短語描述透過活動而非直接指令發生的學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"aspects of life on Earth","meaning":"地球生活的不同方面","examples":[{"en":"Educational themes can expose children to different aspects of life on Earth.","zh":"教育主題可以讓兒童接觸地球生活的不同方面。"},{"en":"Aspects of life on Earth are different parts of human, animal, social, and environmental existence.","zh":"aspects of life on Earth 指人類、動物、社會和環境存在的不同部分。"},{"en":"A documentary may show aspects of life on Earth such as farming, migration, climate, and family life.","zh":"紀錄片可能展示農業、遷徙、氣候和家庭生活等地球生活的不同方面。"},{"en":"Learning about different aspects of life can broaden children’s understanding beyond their own routines.","zh":"認識生活的不同方面可以把兒童的理解擴展到自己的日常以外。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the many parts of life in the world.","zh":"這個短語描述世界生活的許多部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"upcoming study","meaning":"即將發表的研究","examples":[{"en":"The researchers described their findings in an upcoming study.","zh":"研究人員在即將發表的研究中描述他們的發現。"},{"en":"An upcoming study is research that is expected to be published or released soon.","zh":"upcoming study 指預期很快出版或發布的研究。"},{"en":"A university may announce an upcoming study on how sleep affects exam performance.","zh":"大學可能宣布一項關於睡眠如何影響考試表現的即將發表研究。"},{"en":"Upcoming studies can give early signs of new evidence, but readers should still wait for full details.","zh":"即將發表的研究可以提供新證據的早期跡象，但讀者仍應等待完整細節。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to research that is not yet fully available.","zh":"這個短語指尚未完全公開的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"report that","meaning":"報告指出","examples":[{"en":"The authors report that games may improve reaction speed.","zh":"作者報告指出遊戲可能改善反應速度。"},{"en":"To report that means to state or present information, often after research or observation.","zh":"report that 指陳述或呈現資料，通常是在研究或觀察後。"},{"en":"Doctors report that regular exercise can improve mood and sleep.","zh":"醫生報告指出定期運動可以改善情緒和睡眠。"},{"en":"Reporting a finding does not always mean it is final; it may invite further study.","zh":"報告一項發現不一定代表它是最終結論；它可能引出進一步研究。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces information from researchers, writers, or witnesses.","zh":"這個短語引入來自研究人員、作者或目擊者的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"potent training regimen","meaning":"強效訓練方案","examples":[{"en":"Action gaming may provide a potent training regimen.","zh":"動作遊戲可能提供一種強效訓練方案。"},{"en":"A potent training regimen is a powerful and effective programme of repeated practice.","zh":"potent training regimen 指強而有效的反覆練習計劃。"},{"en":"Daily speaking practice with feedback can be a potent training regimen for language learners.","zh":"每日有回饋的口語練習，可以是語言學習者的強效訓練方案。"},{"en":"A training regimen becomes potent when it combines challenge, repetition, and motivation.","zh":"當訓練方案結合挑戰、重複和動機，它就變得強效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong method for building skill.","zh":"這個短語描述建立技能的強力方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"speed up reactions","meaning":"加快反應","examples":[{"en":"Video-game practice may speed up reactions in real-life situations.","zh":"電子遊戲練習可能在現實生活情況中加快反應。"},{"en":"To speed up reactions means to make responses faster.","zh":"speed up reactions 指令回應變得更快。"},{"en":"Sports drills can speed up reactions when players practise responding to sudden movements.","zh":"當球員練習回應突然動作，體育訓練可以加快反應。"},{"en":"Faster reactions can help in driving, surgery, sports, and emergency situations.","zh":"更快反應可以幫助駕駛、手術、運動和緊急情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improving response speed.","zh":"這個短語描述改善回應速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"many types of real-life situations","meaning":"多種現實生活情況","examples":[{"en":"Quick decision-making is useful in many types of real-life situations.","zh":"快速決策在多種現實生活情況中很有用。"},{"en":"Many types of real-life situations means many different actual circumstances people face outside practice or games.","zh":"many types of real-life situations 指人們在練習或遊戲之外面對的許多不同真實情況。"},{"en":"Quick thinking may help in real-life situations such as crossing a road, helping a patient, or solving a work crisis.","zh":"快速思考可能在過馬路、幫助病人或處理工作危機等現實生活情況中有用。"},{"en":"Training is valuable when it prepares people for different real situations, not just one task.","zh":"當訓練讓人準備好多種真實情況，而不只是一項任務，它就有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses variety in everyday and professional contexts.","zh":"這個短語強調日常和專業情境中的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"test dozens of participants","meaning":"測試數十名參加者","examples":[{"en":"The researchers tested dozens of young adults.","zh":"研究人員測試了數十名年輕成年人。"},{"en":"To test dozens of participants means to study many people, usually several tens of them, in an experiment.","zh":"test dozens of participants 指在實驗中研究許多人，通常是幾十人。"},{"en":"A psychology class may test dozens of participants to see how sleep affects memory.","zh":"心理學課可能測試數十名參加者，以了解睡眠如何影響記憶。"},{"en":"Testing many participants can make findings more reliable than using only one or two people.","zh":"測試許多參加者比只使用一兩個人更能令發現可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research involving a fairly large group of people.","zh":"這個短語描述涉及相當多人的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ordinarily play video games","meaning":"平時玩電子遊戲","examples":[{"en":"The participants did not ordinarily play video games.","zh":"參加者平時並不玩電子遊戲。"},{"en":"To ordinarily play video games means to usually or regularly play them in normal life.","zh":"ordinarily play video games 指在正常生活中通常或定期玩電子遊戲。"},{"en":"A student who ordinarily plays video games may already be familiar with controllers and game rules.","zh":"平時玩電子遊戲的學生可能已熟悉控制器和遊戲規則。"},{"en":"Researchers may choose people who do not ordinarily play games to measure the effect of training more clearly.","zh":"研究人員可能選擇平時不玩遊戲的人，以更清楚量度訓練效果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone’s usual gaming habit.","zh":"這個短語描述某人的平常遊戲習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"split the subjects into two groups","meaning":"將實驗對象分成兩組","examples":[{"en":"The researchers split the subjects into two groups.","zh":"研究人員將實驗對象分成兩組。"},{"en":"To split the subjects into two groups means to divide the participants into two separate sets for comparison.","zh":"split the subjects into two groups 指把參加者分成兩個獨立組別作比較。"},{"en":"A teacher may split the class into two groups to compare two revision methods.","zh":"老師可能把全班分成兩組，以比較兩種溫習方法。"},{"en":"Dividing subjects into groups helps researchers see whether different treatments produce different results.","zh":"把實驗對象分組有助研究人員了解不同處理是否產生不同結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common experimental design step.","zh":"這個短語描述常見實驗設計步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"fast-paced action game","meaning":"節奏明快的動作遊戲","examples":[{"en":"One group played fast-paced action games.","zh":"其中一組玩節奏明快的動作遊戲。"},{"en":"A fast-paced action game is a game with quick movement, rapid events, and little time to react.","zh":"fast-paced action game 指有快速移動、急速事件和很少反應時間的遊戲。"},{"en":"A racing game with sudden turns and obstacles can be a fast-paced action game.","zh":"有突然轉彎和障礙物的賽車遊戲可以是節奏明快的動作遊戲。"},{"en":"Fast-paced games may train attention because players must respond immediately.","zh":"節奏快的遊戲可能訓練注意力，因為玩家必須立即回應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes action games with high speed and pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述速度和壓力高的動作遊戲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"slow-moving strategy game","meaning":"節奏緩慢的策略遊戲","examples":[{"en":"The other group played a slow-moving strategy game.","zh":"另一組玩節奏緩慢的策略遊戲。"},{"en":"A slow-moving strategy game is a game that gives players more time to think and plan.","zh":"slow-moving strategy game 指給玩家較多時間思考和規劃的遊戲。"},{"en":"A city-building game can be slow-moving if players pause to choose where to spend resources.","zh":"如果玩家可以停下來選擇如何使用資源，城市建設遊戲可以是節奏緩慢的。"},{"en":"Slow-moving games may train planning more than reaction speed.","zh":"節奏緩慢的遊戲可能更多訓練規劃，而不是反應速度。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts thoughtful strategy with fast action.","zh":"這個短語把深思策略與快速動作作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"training period","meaning":"訓練期","examples":[{"en":"The participants completed fifty hours of gaming during the training period.","zh":"參加者在訓練期內完成了五十小時遊戲。"},{"en":"A training period is the set time during which people practise or receive instruction.","zh":"training period 指人們練習或接受指導的一段固定時間。"},{"en":"New employees may learn company rules during a two-week training period.","zh":"新員工可能在兩星期訓練期內學習公司規則。"},{"en":"A clear training period lets researchers measure improvement before and after practice.","zh":"清楚的訓練期讓研究人員量度練習前後的改善。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the time allocated for training.","zh":"這個短語指分配給訓練的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make quick decisions","meaning":"迅速作決定","examples":[{"en":"After training, the subjects had to make quick decisions.","zh":"訓練後，實驗對象必須迅速作決定。"},{"en":"To make quick decisions means to choose an answer or action with very little delay.","zh":"make quick decisions 指幾乎不延遲地選擇答案或行動。"},{"en":"A cashier may need to make quick decisions when a payment machine stops working during a queue.","zh":"當付款機在排隊期間停止運作，收銀員可能需要迅速作決定。"},{"en":"Quick decision-making can improve with practice if people learn to notice the right clues.","zh":"如果人們學會注意正確線索，快速決策可以透過練習改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rapid choice under time pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述時間壓力下的快速選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tasks designed by researchers","meaning":"由研究人員設計的任務","examples":[{"en":"The subjects completed several tasks designed by the researchers.","zh":"實驗對象完成了幾項由研究人員設計的任務。"},{"en":"Tasks designed by researchers are activities created for an experiment to measure a specific ability.","zh":"tasks designed by researchers 指為實驗而創造、用來量度特定能力的活動。"},{"en":"A memory test designed by researchers may ask students to recall words after five minutes.","zh":"由研究人員設計的記憶測試，可能要求學生五分鐘後回想詞語。"},{"en":"Carefully designed tasks help ensure the study measures what it intends to measure.","zh":"仔細設計的任務幫助確保研究量度其想量度的內容。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research activities made for testing.","zh":"這個短語描述為測試而製作的研究活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"up to 25 per cent faster","meaning":"快達25%","examples":[{"en":"The action-game players reached decisions up to 25 per cent faster.","zh":"動作遊戲玩家作決定快達 25%。"},{"en":"Up to 25 per cent faster means as much as a quarter faster, but not necessarily exactly that amount every time.","zh":"up to 25 per cent faster 指最多快四分之一，但不一定每次都正好是這個幅度。"},{"en":"A new bus route may get students to school up to 25 per cent faster during rush hour.","zh":"新巴士路線可能在繁忙時間令學生上學快達 25%。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the maximum size of improvement found.","zh":"這個短語突出所發現改善的最大幅度。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to express a measurable increase in speed.","zh":"這個短語用於表達可量度的速度增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"come to a conclusion","meaning":"得出結論","examples":[{"en":"The action-game players came to a conclusion more quickly.","zh":"動作遊戲玩家更快得出結論。"},{"en":"To come to a conclusion means to decide what is true or what should be done after thinking.","zh":"come to a conclusion 指思考後決定甚麼是真的或應該怎樣做。"},{"en":"A student comes to a conclusion after comparing evidence in a reading passage.","zh":"學生在比較閱讀文章中的證據後得出結論。"},{"en":"Good conclusions should be based on clues, not random guessing.","zh":"好結論應基於線索，而不是隨機猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching a decision or judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述作出決定或判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"answer just as many questions correctly","meaning":"正確回答同樣數目的問題","examples":[{"en":"The faster players answered just as many questions correctly as the others.","zh":"較快的玩家正確回答了與其他人同樣數目的問題。"},{"en":"To answer just as many questions correctly means to get the same number of correct answers as another group.","zh":"answer just as many questions correctly 指取得與另一組相同數目的正確答案。"},{"en":"A student may work faster but still answer just as many questions correctly as slower classmates.","zh":"學生可能做得更快，但仍正確回答與較慢同學同樣數目的問題。"},{"en":"This matters because speed is less useful if accuracy falls.","zh":"這很重要，因為如果準確度下降，速度較快也沒那麼有用。"},{"en":"This phrase compares accuracy between groups while discussing speed.","zh":"這個短語在討論速度時比較組別之間的準確度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"strategy-game-playing peers","meaning":"玩策略遊戲的同輩","examples":[{"en":"The action gamers were compared with their strategy-game-playing peers.","zh":"動作遊戲玩家被拿來與玩策略遊戲的同輩比較。"},{"en":"Strategy-game-playing peers are people of a similar group who played strategy games.","zh":"strategy-game-playing peers 指同類群體中玩策略遊戲的人。"},{"en":"In an experiment, action-game players may be compared with strategy-game-playing peers to see which training has stronger effects.","zh":"在實驗中，動作遊戲玩家可能與玩策略遊戲的同輩比較，以了解哪種訓練效果較強。"},{"en":"Comparing peers helps reduce unfair differences such as age or background.","zh":"比較同輩有助減少年齡或背景等不公平差異。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the comparison group in a study.","zh":"這個短語指出研究中的比較組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the main purpose of","meaning":"……的主要目的","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the main purpose of the first paragraph.","zh":"題目問第一段的主要目的。"},{"en":"The main purpose of something is its most important aim or function.","zh":"main purpose of something 指某事最重要的目標或功能。"},{"en":"The main purpose of an introduction is often to give background and prepare the reader.","zh":"引言的主要目的通常是提供背景並讓讀者作好準備。"},{"en":"Identifying the main purpose helps students understand why a paragraph is included.","zh":"識別主要目的幫助學生理解某段為何被放入文章。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about the writer’s reason for writing a section.","zh":"這個短語詢問作者寫某部分的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"introduce the background to","meaning":"介紹……的背景","examples":[{"en":"The opening paragraph introduces the background to the passage.","zh":"開首段介紹文章的背景。"},{"en":"To introduce the background to something means to provide context before the main discussion begins.","zh":"introduce the background to something 指在主要討論開始前提供脈絡。"},{"en":"A teacher may introduce the background to a novel before students read chapter one.","zh":"老師可能在學生閱讀第一章前介紹小說背景。"},{"en":"Background helps readers understand why the topic matters.","zh":"背景幫助讀者理解主題為何重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes setting up the context for later ideas.","zh":"這個短語描述為後續想法建立脈絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"what the author wants to express","meaning":"作者想表達甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what the author wants to express in the paragraph.","zh":"題目問作者在該段想表達甚麼。"},{"en":"What the author wants to express means the idea, feeling, or message the writer intends to communicate.","zh":"what the author wants to express 指作者打算傳達的想法、感受或訊息。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students must infer what the author wants to express from word choice and examples.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生必須從用詞和例子推斷作者想表達甚麼。"},{"en":"Understanding author intention helps readers avoid focusing only on isolated details.","zh":"理解作者意圖幫助讀者避免只集中於孤立細節。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about the writer’s intended meaning.","zh":"這個短語詢問作者意圖中的意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be widely considered harmful","meaning":"被廣泛視為有害","examples":[{"en":"Video games are widely considered harmful by some parents.","zh":"電子遊戲被一些家長廣泛視為有害。"},{"en":"To be widely considered harmful means many people believe something causes damage or danger.","zh":"be widely considered harmful 指許多人相信某事會造成傷害或危險。"},{"en":"Excessive screen time is widely considered harmful when it reduces sleep and exercise.","zh":"當過多螢幕時間減少睡眠和運動，它會被廣泛視為有害。"},{"en":"Something may be widely considered harmful even if research shows a more complicated picture.","zh":"即使研究顯示情況更複雜，某事仍可能被廣泛視為有害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common negative belief about something.","zh":"這個短語描述對某事常見的負面看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"juvenile delinquency","meaning":"青少年犯罪","examples":[{"en":"Violent games are sometimes blamed for juvenile delinquency.","zh":"暴力遊戲有時被歸咎於青少年犯罪。"},{"en":"Juvenile delinquency means illegal or seriously antisocial behaviour by young people.","zh":"juvenile delinquency 指年輕人的違法或嚴重反社會行為。"},{"en":"Theft, vandalism, or violent behaviour by teenagers may be described as juvenile delinquency.","zh":"青少年的盜竊、破壞公物或暴力行為，可被稱為青少年犯罪。"},{"en":"Blaming one cause for juvenile delinquency may ignore family, school, and social factors.","zh":"把青少年犯罪歸咎於單一原因，可能忽視家庭、學校和社會因素。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to youth crime or serious misconduct.","zh":"這個短語指青少年犯罪或嚴重不當行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a certain proportion of","meaning":"一定比例的……","examples":[{"en":"A certain proportion of video games contains violent material.","zh":"一定比例的電子遊戲含有暴力材料。"},{"en":"A certain proportion of something means a particular share or percentage of a whole group.","zh":"a certain proportion of something 指整體中的某一份額或百分比。"},{"en":"A certain proportion of students may prefer online lessons to classroom lessons.","zh":"一定比例的學生可能較喜歡網上課堂多於實體課堂。"},{"en":"Talking about proportion helps readers understand scale rather than isolated examples.","zh":"談比例幫助讀者理解規模，而不是孤立例子。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to part of a larger total.","zh":"這個短語指較大整體中的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"children’s intellectual abilities","meaning":"兒童的智力能力","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are interested in how gaming affects children’s intellectual abilities.","zh":"研究人員對遊戲如何影響兒童的智力能力感興趣。"},{"en":"Children’s intellectual abilities are mental abilities such as reasoning, memory, attention, and problem-solving.","zh":"children’s intellectual abilities 指推理、記憶、注意力和解難等心理能力。"},{"en":"Reading, puzzles, and discussion can all support children’s intellectual abilities.","zh":"閱讀、謎題和討論都可以支援兒童的智力能力。"},{"en":"If an activity improves reasoning or attention, it may strengthen intellectual development.","zh":"如果一項活動改善推理或注意力，它可能強化智力發展。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to children’s thinking and learning capacity.","zh":"這個短語指兒童的思考和學習能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be correctly mentioned","meaning":"被正確提及","examples":[{"en":"Students must identify which idea is correctly mentioned in the paragraph.","zh":"學生必須識別哪個想法在該段被正確提及。"},{"en":"To be correctly mentioned means to be stated accurately according to the passage.","zh":"be correctly mentioned 指根據文章被準確陳述。"},{"en":"In a reading question, an option is correctly mentioned only if the text clearly says it.","zh":"在閱讀題中，只有文本清楚說出某選項，它才算被正確提及。"},{"en":"Students should check wording carefully because small changes can make an answer wrong.","zh":"學生應仔細檢查措辭，因為細微改動可以令答案錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accurate reference to information in a text.","zh":"這個短語描述準確引用文本資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in various aspects","meaning":"在多個方面","examples":[{"en":"Video games may improve brain function in various aspects.","zh":"電子遊戲可能在多個方面改善大腦功能。"},{"en":"In various aspects means in several different areas or ways.","zh":"in various aspects 指在幾個不同範疇或方式上。"},{"en":"A school programme may help students in various aspects, including confidence, reading, and teamwork.","zh":"學校計劃可能在自信、閱讀和團隊合作等多個方面幫助學生。"},{"en":"When improvement happens in various aspects, the benefit is broader than one single skill.","zh":"當改善發生在多個方面，好處就比單一技能更廣泛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes multiple sides of an issue.","zh":"這個短語描述一個議題的多個面向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"better surgical performance","meaning":"較好的外科手術表現","examples":[{"en":"Gaming experience has been associated with better surgical performance.","zh":"遊戲經驗與較好的外科手術表現有關。"},{"en":"Better surgical performance means improved ability to carry out operations accurately, safely, and efficiently.","zh":"better surgical performance 指更準確、安全和有效地進行手術的能力改善。"},{"en":"A surgeon with better surgical performance may make fewer errors and finish delicate tasks more smoothly.","zh":"有較好外科手術表現的外科醫生，可能犯較少錯並更順利完成精細任務。"},{"en":"If training improves hand control and visual attention, surgical performance may improve.","zh":"如果訓練改善手部控制和視覺注意，外科手術表現可能提升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes higher quality in surgical work.","zh":"這個短語描述外科工作中的較高質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the expected result of an experiment","meaning":"實驗的預期結果","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the expected result of the experiment.","zh":"題目問實驗的預期結果。"},{"en":"The expected result of an experiment is the outcome researchers think may happen before or during the study.","zh":"expected result of an experiment 指研究人員在研究前或研究期間認為可能出現的結果。"},{"en":"In a memory experiment, the expected result may be that students who sleep more remember more words.","zh":"在記憶實驗中，預期結果可能是睡得更多的學生記得更多詞語。"},{"en":"Expected results guide research design, but actual results may still surprise researchers.","zh":"預期結果引導研究設計，但實際結果仍可能令研究人員意外。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the predicted outcome of a test.","zh":"這個短語指測試的預測結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"improve reaction speed effectively","meaning":"有效提升反應速度","examples":[{"en":"The experiment examined whether games improve reaction speed effectively.","zh":"該實驗檢視遊戲是否能有效提升反應速度。"},{"en":"To improve reaction speed effectively means to make responses faster in a clear and useful way.","zh":"improve reaction speed effectively 指以清楚而有用的方式令回應變快。"},{"en":"A sports drill improves reaction speed effectively if players respond faster without making more mistakes.","zh":"如果球員反應更快而沒有犯更多錯，體育訓練就有效提升反應速度。"},{"en":"Effective improvement should increase speed while keeping accuracy acceptable.","zh":"有效改善應提高速度，同時保持可接受準確度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes useful improvement in how quickly someone responds.","zh":"這個短語描述人在回應速度上的有用改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與文中資料相符","examples":[{"en":"Decide whether each statement agrees with the information given in the passage.","zh":"判斷每項陳述是否與文章中提供的資料相符。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文章所說內容一致。"},{"en":"If the passage says action gamers were faster, a matching statement agrees with the information given.","zh":"如果文章說動作遊戲玩家更快，意思相符的陳述就與資料相符。"},{"en":"Students should base their answer on the text, not on personal opinion.","zh":"學生應根據文本作答，而不是個人意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading-comprehension tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀理解題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文中資料矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to state the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"contradict the information 指陳述與文本所說相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says players were faster but an option says they were slower, it contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說玩家更快，但選項說他們更慢，就是與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be checked against the text carefully.","zh":"矛盾必須仔細對照文本來檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a direct conflict with the passage.","zh":"這個短語描述與文章直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Choose “NOT GIVEN” if there is no information on the statement.","zh":"如果文章沒有關於該陳述的資料，選擇 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not say enough to decide whether it is true or false.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文章沒有說出足夠資料來判斷真假。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions addiction levels, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文章從未提及上癮程度，就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge to fill a gap in the passage.","zh":"學生不應使用外部知識填補文章空白。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a NOT GIVEN answer.","zh":"這個短語表示 NOT GIVEN 答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be popular because of","meaning":"因……而受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not claim that games are popular because of violent content.","zh":"文章並沒有聲稱遊戲因暴力內容而受歡迎。"},{"en":"To be popular because of something means to be liked or widely used for that reason.","zh":"be popular because of something 指因某原因而被喜歡或廣泛使用。"},{"en":"A café may be popular because of its friendly staff and cheap lunch sets.","zh":"咖啡店可能因友善員工和便宜午餐套餐而受歡迎。"},{"en":"When explaining popularity, the cause must be supported by evidence.","zh":"解釋受歡迎原因時，該原因必須有證據支持。"},{"en":"This phrase links popularity with a reason.","zh":"這個短語把受歡迎程度與原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"minimise the number of mistakes","meaning":"將錯誤數目減至最低","examples":[{"en":"The action gamers did not necessarily minimise the number of mistakes.","zh":"動作遊戲玩家不一定將錯誤數目減至最低。"},{"en":"To minimise the number of mistakes means to reduce errors as much as possible.","zh":"minimise the number of mistakes 指盡可能減少錯誤。"},{"en":"A student can minimise the number of mistakes by checking grammar before handing in an essay.","zh":"學生可以在交作文前檢查文法，將錯誤數目減至最低。"},{"en":"Faster work is valuable only if the number of mistakes does not increase too much.","zh":"只有在錯誤數目沒有增加太多時，更快完成才有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on reducing errors.","zh":"這個短語著重減少錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"apply video games in classrooms","meaning":"在課堂上應用電子遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Some educators consider applying video games in classrooms.","zh":"有些教育工作者考慮在課堂上應用電子遊戲。"},{"en":"To apply video games in classrooms means to use games as part of teaching and learning.","zh":"apply video games in classrooms 指把遊戲作為教學和學習的一部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may apply video games in classrooms to teach planning, teamwork, or problem solving.","zh":"老師可能在課堂上應用電子遊戲來教授規劃、團隊合作或解難。"},{"en":"Games should be used carefully so entertainment supports learning rather than replaces it.","zh":"遊戲應被謹慎使用，讓娛樂支援學習，而不是取代學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes educational use of gaming in school.","zh":"這個短語描述在學校中對遊戲的教育用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be addicted to video games","meaning":"沉迷電子遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Some people become addicted to video games.","zh":"有些人會沉迷電子遊戲。"},{"en":"To be addicted to video games means to find it very difficult to stop playing, even when it harms life.","zh":"be addicted to video games 指即使遊戲傷害生活，仍非常難停止玩。"},{"en":"A student may be addicted to video games if he plays all night and misses school repeatedly.","zh":"如果學生整晚玩遊戲並反覆缺課，他可能沉迷電子遊戲。"},{"en":"Addiction can affect sleep, study, family relationships, and health.","zh":"沉迷可以影響睡眠、學習、家庭關係和健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unhealthy dependence on gaming.","zh":"這個短語描述對遊戲的不健康依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"dopamine levels","meaning":"多巴胺水平","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not compare dopamine levels in addicted and non-addicted gamers.","zh":"文章沒有比較沉迷和非沉迷玩家的多巴胺水平。"},{"en":"Dopamine levels are the amounts of dopamine present or active in the brain or body.","zh":"dopamine levels 指大腦或身體中存在或活躍的多巴胺數量。"},{"en":"Scientists may study dopamine levels when examining reward, motivation, or addiction.","zh":"科學家研究獎勵、動機或成癮時，可能研究多巴胺水平。"},{"en":"Without data, readers should not assume one group has higher dopamine levels than another.","zh":"沒有數據時，讀者不應假設某組人的多巴胺水平高於另一組。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to measurable amounts of a brain chemical.","zh":"這個短語指某種大腦化學物質的可量度數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"match people with opinions or deeds","meaning":"將人物與觀點或行為配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match each person with the relevant opinion or deed.","zh":"學生將每個人物與相關觀點或行為配對。"},{"en":"To match people with opinions or deeds means to connect each person to what they said, believed, or did.","zh":"match people with opinions or deeds 指把每個人與他們所說、所相信或所做的事連接起來。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may match scientists with their research findings.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能把科學家與他們的研究發現配對。"},{"en":"This task requires careful scanning for names and actions.","zh":"這項任務需要仔細掃讀姓名和行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a matching activity based on source details.","zh":"這個短語描述基於來源細節的配對活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"appropriate letters","meaning":"適當字母","examples":[{"en":"Students write the appropriate letters in the answer boxes.","zh":"學生在答題方格內寫上適當字母。"},{"en":"Appropriate letters are the correct option letters that match the answer choices.","zh":"appropriate letters 指與答案選項相配的正確字母。"},{"en":"If the answer is option B, students must write the appropriate letter clearly in the box.","zh":"如果答案是 B 選項，學生必須在方格內清楚寫上適當字母。"},{"en":"Writing the wrong letter may lose marks even if the student understands the passage.","zh":"即使學生理解文章，寫錯字母也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"without hesitation","meaning":"毫不猶豫地","examples":[{"en":"Training may help players make decisions without hesitation.","zh":"訓練可能幫助玩家毫不猶豫地作決定。"},{"en":"Without hesitation means without pausing because of doubt or fear.","zh":"without hesitation 指沒有因懷疑或恐懼而停頓。"},{"en":"A well-trained nurse may act without hesitation when a patient stops breathing.","zh":"當病人停止呼吸，訓練有素的護士可能毫不猶豫地行動。"},{"en":"Practice can reduce hesitation because people recognise what to do more quickly.","zh":"練習可以減少猶豫，因為人們更快認出該做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes confident and immediate action.","zh":"這個短語描述自信而立即的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be immersed in","meaning":"投入於……；沉浸在……","examples":[{"en":"Players may make faster decisions when they are immersed in stressful games.","zh":"當玩家沉浸在具壓力的遊戲中，他們可能作出更快決定。"},{"en":"To be immersed in something means to be deeply involved in it and focused on it.","zh":"be immersed in something 指深深投入並專注於某事。"},{"en":"A student may be immersed in a novel and forget to check the time.","zh":"學生可能沉浸在小說中，忘記查看時間。"},{"en":"Immersion can increase attention because the activity feels immediate and absorbing.","zh":"沉浸感可以增加注意力，因為活動感覺即時而吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep involvement or absorption.","zh":"這個短語描述深度投入或被吸引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"alter the brain’s physical structure","meaning":"改變大腦的物理結構","examples":[{"en":"Complex activities can alter the brain’s physical structure.","zh":"複雜活動可以改變大腦的物理結構。"},{"en":"To alter the brain’s physical structure means to change the brain’s connections or organisation through experience.","zh":"alter the brain’s physical structure 指透過經驗改變大腦連接或組織。"},{"en":"Learning music for years may alter the brain’s physical structure in areas linked to hearing and movement.","zh":"多年學習音樂可能改變與聽覺和動作有關的大腦區域的物理結構。"},{"en":"Repeated practice can change the brain because frequently used pathways become stronger.","zh":"反覆練習可以改變大腦，因為經常使用的路徑會變強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes real changes in the brain caused by learning.","zh":"這個短語描述學習造成的大腦真實變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"purpose-motivated experience","meaning":"由目標推動的體驗","examples":[{"en":"A purpose-motivated experience encourages learners to work towards a goal.","zh":"由目標推動的體驗鼓勵學習者朝目標努力。"},{"en":"A purpose-motivated experience is an activity driven by a clear reason or aim.","zh":"purpose-motivated experience 指由清楚原因或目標推動的活動。"},{"en":"Preparing a class presentation is purpose-motivated because students know they must explain ideas to others.","zh":"準備課堂匯報是由目標推動的，因為學生知道自己必須向他人解釋想法。"},{"en":"Purpose can increase effort because learners understand why the task matters.","zh":"目標可以增加努力，因為學習者明白任務為何重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes experience guided by meaningful goals.","zh":"這個短語描述由有意義目標引導的經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"play an essential role in learning","meaning":"在學習中發揮重要作用","examples":[{"en":"Goal-driven activities play an essential role in learning.","zh":"目標導向活動在學習中發揮重要作用。"},{"en":"To play an essential role in learning means to be necessary or very important for learning to happen well.","zh":"play an essential role in learning 指對良好學習而言是必要或非常重要的。"},{"en":"Clear feedback plays an essential role in learning because students need to know how to improve.","zh":"清楚回饋在學習中發揮重要作用，因為學生需要知道如何改善。"},{"en":"If an element is essential, learning becomes weaker without it.","zh":"如果某元素是必要的，缺少它時學習會變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies something as central to successful learning.","zh":"這個短語指出某事對成功學習至關重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"tackle immediate issues","meaning":"處理眼前問題","examples":[{"en":"Gamers learn to tackle immediate issues quickly.","zh":"玩家學會快速處理眼前問題。"},{"en":"To tackle immediate issues means to deal with urgent problems directly and actively.","zh":"tackle immediate issues 指直接而主動地處理緊急問題。"},{"en":"A manager must tackle immediate issues when staff are absent and customers are waiting.","zh":"當員工缺勤而顧客正在等待，經理必須處理眼前問題。"},{"en":"Handling immediate issues well prevents small problems from disrupting larger plans.","zh":"良好處理眼前問題可以防止小問題打亂更大計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active response to urgent matters.","zh":"這個短語描述對緊急事情的主動回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"keep future goals in mind","meaning":"緊記未來目標","examples":[{"en":"Players tackle immediate problems while keeping future goals in mind.","zh":"玩家在處理眼前問題時，同時緊記未來目標。"},{"en":"To keep future goals in mind means to remember long-term aims while making present choices.","zh":"keep future goals in mind 指在作當前選擇時記住長遠目標。"},{"en":"A student may keep future goals in mind by choosing revision over late-night entertainment before exams.","zh":"學生可能在考試前選擇溫習而不是深夜娛樂，以緊記未來目標。"},{"en":"This helps people avoid choices that solve today’s problem but harm tomorrow’s success.","zh":"這幫助人避免作出解決今天問題卻傷害明天成功的選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes balancing immediate action with long-term planning.","zh":"這個短語描述在即時行動與長遠規劃之間取得平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"broaden children’s horizons","meaning":"擴闊兒童的眼界","examples":[{"en":"Games based on history and society may broaden children’s horizons.","zh":"以歷史和社會為題材的遊戲可能擴闊兒童的眼界。"},{"en":"To broaden children’s horizons means to help children understand more about the world beyond their own daily experience.","zh":"broaden children’s horizons 指幫助兒童理解自己日常經驗以外更廣闊的世界。"},{"en":"Visiting a museum can broaden children’s horizons by showing them different cultures and periods of history.","zh":"參觀博物館可以透過展示不同文化和歷史時期，擴闊兒童的眼界。"},{"en":"When children encounter new ideas, they may become more curious and open-minded.","zh":"當兒童接觸新想法，他們可能變得更好奇和更開放。"},{"en":"This phrase describes expanding children’s knowledge, imagination, and perspective.","zh":"這個短語描述擴展兒童的知識、想像力和視野。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 20 - Unexpected Benefits to Human Brain.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 22":[{"front":"communication in science","meaning":"科學傳意","examples":[{"en":"Clear communication in science helps the public understand new developments.","zh":"清晰的科學傳意幫助公眾理解新發展。"},{"en":"Communication in science means explaining scientific ideas, evidence, and discoveries clearly to other people.","zh":"communication in science 指清楚向他人解釋科學概念、證據和發現。"},{"en":"A teacher uses communication in science when she explains vaccines with simple diagrams and examples.","zh":"老師用簡單圖表和例子解釋疫苗時，就是在進行科學傳意。"},{"en":"Good communication in science reduces fear because people can understand what researchers actually found.","zh":"良好的科學傳意能減少恐懼，因為人們能理解研究人員實際發現了甚麼。"},{"en":"Without clear communication in science, correct research may still be misunderstood by the public.","zh":"如果沒有清晰的科學傳意，正確研究仍可能被公眾誤解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"play an increasingly significant role","meaning":"擔當日益重要的角色","examples":[{"en":"Science plays an increasingly significant role in people’s lives.","zh":"科學在人們生活中擔當日益重要的角色。"},{"en":"To play an increasingly significant role means to become more and more important in a situation.","zh":"play an increasingly significant role 指在某情況中變得越來越重要。"},{"en":"Online learning plays an increasingly significant role in education as more students use digital platforms.","zh":"隨着更多學生使用數碼平台，網上學習在教育中擔當日益重要的角色。"},{"en":"A subject plays a larger role when people rely on it more often for decisions and daily life.","zh":"當人們更經常依賴某事作決定和處理日常生活，它就會擔當更重要角色。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that importance is growing over time.","zh":"這個短語顯示重要性正在隨時間增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"faithful communication of","meaning":"對……作準確傳達","examples":[{"en":"The faithful communication of scientific developments is more important than ever.","zh":"對科學發展作準確傳達比以往任何時候都重要。"},{"en":"Faithful communication of something means explaining it accurately without twisting, exaggerating, or leaving out key facts.","zh":"faithful communication of something 指準確解釋某事，不扭曲、不誇大，也不省略關鍵事實。"},{"en":"A doctor needs faithful communication of test results so patients understand both risks and limits.","zh":"醫生需要對檢查結果作準確傳達，讓病人理解風險和限制。"},{"en":"If information is not communicated faithfully, people may make decisions based on a distorted picture.","zh":"如果資訊沒有被準確傳達，人們可能根據被扭曲的畫面作決定。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses accuracy and honesty in explanation.","zh":"這個短語強調解釋中的準確和誠實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"scientific developments","meaning":"科學發展","examples":[{"en":"The public needs reliable information about scientific developments.","zh":"公眾需要關於科學發展的可靠資訊。"},{"en":"Scientific developments are new discoveries, methods, technologies, or understandings produced by scientific research.","zh":"scientific developments 指科學研究產生的新發現、新方法、新科技或新理解。"},{"en":"New cancer treatments and climate models are examples of scientific developments.","zh":"新癌症治療方法和氣候模型都是科學發展的例子。"},{"en":"Scientific developments affect public life because they can change healthcare, energy, food, and policy.","zh":"科學發展影響公共生活，因為它們可以改變醫療、能源、食物和政策。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to progress or change in scientific knowledge.","zh":"這個短語指科學知識上的進步或改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"more important than ever","meaning":"比以往任何時候都重要","examples":[{"en":"Accurate science communication is more important than ever.","zh":"準確的科學傳意比以往任何時候都重要。"},{"en":"More important than ever means more important now than at any previous time.","zh":"more important than ever 指現在比過去任何時候都更加重要。"},{"en":"Digital safety is more important than ever because students use the internet every day.","zh":"數碼安全比以往任何時候都重要，因為學生每天使用互聯網。"},{"en":"Something becomes more important than ever when new risks or responsibilities grow.","zh":"當新風險或責任增加，某事便會比以往任何時候都重要。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly emphasises present urgency.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調當下的迫切性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be fraught with challenges","meaning":"充滿挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Science communication is fraught with challenges.","zh":"科學傳意充滿挑戰。"},{"en":"To be fraught with challenges means to be full of difficulties, risks, or complications.","zh":"be fraught with challenges 指充滿困難、風險或複雜情況。"},{"en":"Organising an overseas school trip can be fraught with challenges because of visas, safety, and budget limits.","zh":"組織海外學校旅行可能充滿挑戰，因為涉及簽證、安全和預算限制。"},{"en":"A task is fraught with challenges when even small mistakes can create serious problems.","zh":"當一項任務中即使小錯誤也會造成嚴重問題，它就是充滿挑戰的。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that something is difficult from many directions.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事從多方面來看都很困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"distort discussions","meaning":"扭曲討論","examples":[{"en":"Inaccurate terminology can easily distort scientific discussions.","zh":"不準確的術語很容易扭曲科學討論。"},{"en":"To distort discussions means to twist the meaning of a debate so people no longer understand the issue fairly.","zh":"distort discussions 指扭曲辯論的意思，使人們不能公平理解議題。"},{"en":"A misleading headline can distort discussions about school policy before people read the full report.","zh":"誤導性標題可以在人們閱讀完整報告前，扭曲關於學校政策的討論。"},{"en":"Discussions become distorted when emotional language replaces accurate evidence.","zh":"當情緒化語言取代準確證據，討論就會被扭曲。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that poor wording can damage understanding.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們，用詞不佳會損害理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lead to unnecessary confusion","meaning":"導致不必要的混亂","examples":[{"en":"Poor explanations can lead to unnecessary confusion.","zh":"差劣解釋可以導致不必要的混亂。"},{"en":"To lead to unnecessary confusion means to cause misunderstanding that could have been avoided with clearer explanation.","zh":"lead to unnecessary confusion 指造成本可透過更清晰解釋避免的誤解。"},{"en":"A teacher’s unclear instructions can lead to unnecessary confusion during a group project.","zh":"老師不清楚的指示可以在小組項目中導致不必要的混亂。"},{"en":"Confusion becomes unnecessary when the problem is not the topic itself but the way it is explained.","zh":"當問題不在主題本身，而在解釋方式，混亂就是不必要的。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that better communication could prevent the problem.","zh":"這個短語顯示更好的溝通本可以防止問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"misunderstandings","meaning":"誤解","examples":[{"en":"Ambiguous language can cause serious misunderstandings.","zh":"含糊語言可以造成嚴重誤解。"},{"en":"Misunderstandings are situations in which people get the wrong idea about what something means.","zh":"misunderstandings 指人們錯誤理解某事意思的情況。"},{"en":"A misunderstanding may happen if a student thinks a deadline is Friday when it is actually Thursday.","zh":"如果學生以為限期是星期五，但實際上是星期四，就可能發生誤解。"},{"en":"Misunderstandings can cause wrong decisions, arguments, and loss of trust.","zh":"誤解可以導致錯誤決定、爭執和信任流失。"},{"en":"The word describes confusion caused by incorrect interpretation.","zh":"這個詞描述由錯誤詮釋造成的混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"stem from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"Some communication problems stem from the complexity of modern research.","zh":"有些溝通問題源自現代研究的複雜性。"},{"en":"To stem from something means to come from it or be caused by it.","zh":"stem from something 指來自某事或由某事造成。"},{"en":"A student’s anxiety may stem from lack of sleep rather than lack of ability.","zh":"學生的焦慮可能源自睡眠不足，而不是能力不足。"},{"en":"If a problem stems from a deeper cause, solving only the surface issue will not be enough.","zh":"如果問題源自更深層原因，只處理表面問題並不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of a problem or situation.","zh":"這個短語指出問題或情況的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"esoteric nature of","meaning":"……深奧難懂的性質","examples":[{"en":"The esoteric nature of some research makes it difficult to explain.","zh":"某些研究深奧難懂的性質令它難以解釋。"},{"en":"The esoteric nature of something is its specialised, difficult, and hard-to-understand character.","zh":"esoteric nature of something 指某事專門、困難而難以理解的特性。"},{"en":"The esoteric nature of legal documents can confuse ordinary citizens.","zh":"法律文件深奧難懂的性質可以令普通市民困惑。"},{"en":"When a subject is esoteric, experts must translate it into clearer language for non-specialists.","zh":"當某主題深奧難懂，專家必須把它轉化成非專家能理解的清晰語言。"},{"en":"The phrase describes knowledge that is not easily accessible to the general public.","zh":"這個短語描述一般公眾不容易接觸或理解的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"current research","meaning":"當前研究","examples":[{"en":"Current research may involve concepts unfamiliar to the public.","zh":"當前研究可能涉及公眾不熟悉的概念。"},{"en":"Current research is research being carried out now or in the present period.","zh":"current research 指現在或當前時期正在進行的研究。"},{"en":"Current research on sleep is helping schools rethink early morning timetables.","zh":"關於睡眠的當前研究正幫助學校重新思考清晨時間表。"},{"en":"Current research can be difficult to explain because findings may still be uncertain or changing.","zh":"當前研究可能難以解釋，因為發現仍可能不確定或正在改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to research that is ongoing or recent.","zh":"這個短語指正在進行或近期的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"associated difficulty of","meaning":"隨之而來的……困難","examples":[{"en":"Scientists face the associated difficulty of finding accurate terminology.","zh":"科學家面對隨之而來的尋找準確術語的困難。"},{"en":"The associated difficulty of something is the related problem that comes with a situation.","zh":"associated difficulty of something 指伴隨某情況而來的相關問題。"},{"en":"Online learning brings flexibility, but also the associated difficulty of keeping students focused.","zh":"網上學習帶來彈性，但也有隨之而來的讓學生保持專注的困難。"},{"en":"A new method may create benefits while also producing related difficulties that must be managed.","zh":"新方法可能帶來好處，同時也產生必須處理的相關困難。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a problem connected with another issue.","zh":"這個短語指出與另一議題相連的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sufficiently faithful terminology","meaning":"足夠準確的術語","examples":[{"en":"Researchers need sufficiently faithful terminology to describe complex ideas.","zh":"研究人員需要足夠準確的術語來描述複雜概念。"},{"en":"Sufficiently faithful terminology means words accurate enough to represent the idea without serious distortion.","zh":"sufficiently faithful terminology 指足以準確代表概念、而不造成嚴重扭曲的字詞。"},{"en":"A doctor needs sufficiently faithful terminology when explaining a diagnosis to a patient.","zh":"醫生向病人解釋診斷時，需要足夠準確的術語。"},{"en":"If terminology is not faithful enough, people may remember a catchy phrase but misunderstand the science.","zh":"如果術語不夠準確，人們可能記住易記短語，卻誤解科學內容。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that words must match the idea closely enough.","zh":"這個短語強調用詞必須足夠貼近原意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"abstraction and complexity","meaning":"抽象性與複雜性","examples":[{"en":"Abstraction and complexity are common features of advanced science.","zh":"抽象性與複雜性是高階科學的常見特徵。"},{"en":"Abstraction and complexity refer to ideas that are less concrete and involve many connected parts.","zh":"abstraction and complexity 指較不具體、並涉及許多互相關連部分的概念。"},{"en":"University mathematics often involves abstraction and complexity that beginners find difficult.","zh":"大學數學常涉及令初學者感到困難的抽象性與複雜性。"},{"en":"Abstraction and complexity make communication harder because people cannot easily picture the idea.","zh":"抽象性與複雜性令溝通更困難，因為人們不容易在腦中想像該概念。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ideas that are not simple, visible, or easy to explain.","zh":"這個短語描述不簡單、不可見或不易解釋的概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"signs that","meaning":"……的跡象","examples":[{"en":"Complexity is not necessarily a sign that a scientific direction is wrong.","zh":"複雜性不一定是某個科學方向錯誤的跡象。"},{"en":"A sign that something is true is an indication or clue suggesting it.","zh":"sign that something is true 指暗示某事為真的跡象或線索。"},{"en":"A student’s silence is not always a sign that she does not understand; she may be thinking carefully.","zh":"學生沉默不一定是她不明白的跡象；她可能正在仔細思考。"},{"en":"People should be careful because one sign alone may not prove the whole conclusion.","zh":"人們應該小心，因為單一跡象未必能證明整個結論。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence or an indication.","zh":"這個短語引入證據或提示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"scientific direction","meaning":"科學研究方向","examples":[{"en":"A complex scientific direction may still be highly productive.","zh":"複雜的科學研究方向仍可能非常有成果。"},{"en":"A scientific direction is a line of research or a path that scientists choose to investigate.","zh":"scientific direction 指科學家選擇研究的一條研究路線或方向。"},{"en":"A university may support a new scientific direction in renewable energy research.","zh":"大學可能支持可再生能源研究中的新科學研究方向。"},{"en":"A scientific direction becomes productive when it leads to useful questions, methods, and discoveries.","zh":"當科學方向帶來有用問題、方法和發現，它就會變得有成果。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the focus or pathway of scientific work.","zh":"這個短語指科學工作的焦點或路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"commentators have suggested","meaning":"評論者曾提出","examples":[{"en":"Some commentators have suggested that complex theories are unreliable.","zh":"有些評論者曾提出複雜理論並不可靠。"},{"en":"Commentators have suggested means writers, speakers, or analysts have put forward an opinion or explanation.","zh":"commentators have suggested 指作家、講者或分析者提出了一種意見或解釋。"},{"en":"Some commentators have suggested that homework should be reduced to protect students’ sleep.","zh":"有些評論者曾提出應減少功課，以保護學生睡眠。"},{"en":"A suggestion from commentators may influence public debate even if experts disagree with it.","zh":"評論者提出的看法即使與專家意見不同，也可能影響公共討論。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an opinion rather than a proven fact.","zh":"這個短語引入意見，而不是已證實事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a tribute to","meaning":"對……成就的肯定","examples":[{"en":"Scientific complexity can be a tribute to human ingenuity.","zh":"科學複雜性可以是對人類創造力成就的肯定。"},{"en":"A tribute to something is a sign of respect, recognition, or admiration for it.","zh":"tribute to something 指對某事的尊重、認可或讚賞。"},{"en":"A school prize can be a tribute to a teacher’s years of patient work.","zh":"學校獎項可以是對一位老師多年耐心工作的肯定。"},{"en":"Complex technology may be a tribute to human creativity because it shows what people can build and understand.","zh":"複雜科技可以是對人類創造力的肯定，因為它展示人類能建造和理解甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase presents something as evidence of value or achievement.","zh":"這個短語把某事呈現為價值或成就的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"human ingenuity","meaning":"人類智慧；創造力","examples":[{"en":"Modern research demonstrates remarkable human ingenuity.","zh":"現代研究展示了非凡的人類智慧。"},{"en":"Human ingenuity is people’s ability to think creatively, solve problems, and invent new methods.","zh":"human ingenuity 指人類創意思考、解決問題和發明新方法的能力。"},{"en":"A simple water filter made from cheap materials can show human ingenuity in a poor village.","zh":"用廉價材料製成的簡單濾水器，可以展示貧困村落中的人類創造力。"},{"en":"Human ingenuity matters because difficult problems often require fresh and practical solutions.","zh":"人類智慧很重要，因為困難問題通常需要新鮮而實用的解決方案。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights intelligence used creatively.","zh":"這個短語突出被創意運用的智慧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"meet complex challenges","meaning":"應對複雜挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Science helps humanity meet increasingly complex challenges.","zh":"科學幫助人類應對日益複雜的挑戰。"},{"en":"To meet complex challenges means to face and deal with difficult problems successfully.","zh":"meet complex challenges 指面對並成功處理困難問題。"},{"en":"Hospitals meet complex challenges when many patients need care during a disease outbreak.","zh":"疾病爆發期間，當許多病人需要照顧，醫院就在應對複雜挑戰。"},{"en":"Societies need knowledge, planning, and cooperation to meet complex challenges.","zh":"社會需要知識、規劃和合作來應對複雜挑戰。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests active response, not passive waiting.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動回應，而不是被動等待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"nature presents","meaning":"大自然帶來的……","examples":[{"en":"Researchers respond to the challenges that nature presents.","zh":"研究人員回應大自然帶來的挑戰。"},{"en":"The challenges that nature presents are problems or conditions created by the natural world.","zh":"challenges that nature presents 指由自然世界造成的問題或條件。"},{"en":"Farmers respond to the challenges nature presents when drought, pests, or floods damage crops.","zh":"當乾旱、害蟲或水災破壞農作物，農民就在回應大自然帶來的挑戰。"},{"en":"Science develops because nature presents puzzles that people want to understand and solve.","zh":"科學之所以發展，是因為大自然帶來人們想理解和解決的謎題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes difficulties arising from natural processes.","zh":"這個短語描述由自然過程產生的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make communication more difficult","meaning":"令溝通更加困難","examples":[{"en":"Abstract ideas can make communication more difficult.","zh":"抽象概念可以令溝通更加困難。"},{"en":"To make communication more difficult means to make ideas harder to explain, understand, or discuss clearly.","zh":"make communication more difficult 指令概念更難清楚解釋、理解或討論。"},{"en":"Too many technical words can make communication more difficult in a parent-teacher meeting.","zh":"在家長教師會中，過多專業詞彙可以令溝通更加困難。"},{"en":"Communication becomes harder when listeners cannot connect the idea with familiar experience.","zh":"當聽眾無法把概念與熟悉經驗連起來，溝通就會更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something creates an obstacle to understanding.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事造成理解障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"science reporting","meaning":"科學新聞報道","examples":[{"en":"Science reporting must explain uncertain and evolving research.","zh":"科學新聞報道必須解釋不確定而不斷發展的研究。"},{"en":"Science reporting is journalism or public writing that explains scientific research and discoveries.","zh":"science reporting 指解釋科學研究和發現的新聞或公共寫作。"},{"en":"A newspaper uses science reporting when it explains a new vaccine study to ordinary readers.","zh":"報紙向普通讀者解釋一項新疫苗研究時，就是在做科學新聞報道。"},{"en":"Good science reporting helps people understand evidence without exaggerating hope or fear.","zh":"良好的科學新聞報道幫助人們理解證據，而不誇大希望或恐懼。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to reporting science for the public.","zh":"這個短語指為公眾報道科學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"areas of evolving research","meaning":"不斷發展的研究領域","examples":[{"en":"Scientists often work in areas of evolving research.","zh":"科學家常在不斷發展的研究領域工作。"},{"en":"Areas of evolving research are fields where knowledge is still developing and conclusions may change.","zh":"areas of evolving research 指知識仍在發展、結論可能改變的領域。"},{"en":"Artificial intelligence in education is an area of evolving research because schools are still testing its effects.","zh":"教育中的人工智能是不斷發展的研究領域，因為學校仍在測試其影響。"},{"en":"In evolving research areas, early findings may be useful but not yet final.","zh":"在不斷發展的研究領域，早期發現可能有用，但未必是最終結論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research fields that are still moving and changing.","zh":"這個短語描述仍在推進和改變的研究領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"partly understand","meaning":"部分理解","examples":[{"en":"Scientists may only partly understand a new discovery at first.","zh":"科學家起初可能只部分理解一項新發現。"},{"en":"To partly understand something means to understand some of it, but not the full meaning or consequences.","zh":"partly understand something 指理解其中一部分，但未完全理解其意思或後果。"},{"en":"A student may partly understand a grammar rule before she can use it accurately in writing.","zh":"學生可能部分理解文法規則，然後才逐漸能在寫作中準確使用。"},{"en":"Partial understanding can improve over time as people collect more evidence and experience.","zh":"隨着人們收集更多證據和經驗，部分理解可以隨時間改善。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that knowledge is incomplete.","zh":"這個短語顯示知識並不完整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"full implications of","meaning":"……的全面影響","examples":[{"en":"Researchers may not yet understand the full implications of an advance.","zh":"研究人員可能尚未理解一項進展的全面影響。"},{"en":"The full implications of something are all the possible meanings, effects, or consequences it may have.","zh":"full implications of something 指某事可能具有的所有意思、影響或後果。"},{"en":"A school may not understand the full implications of banning phones until students begin using laptops instead.","zh":"學校可能在學生開始改用手提電腦後，才理解禁止手機的全面影響。"},{"en":"New discoveries can have implications that appear only after years of use or further research.","zh":"新發現可能有些影響要在多年使用或進一步研究後才出現。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the wider effects beyond the first result.","zh":"這個短語重點是第一個結果以外的更廣泛影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"particular advance","meaning":"某項特定進展","examples":[{"en":"A particular scientific advance may have unexpected consequences.","zh":"某項特定科學進展可能有意想不到的後果。"},{"en":"A particular advance is one specific step forward in knowledge, technology, or method.","zh":"particular advance 指知識、科技或方法上的某一項具體進步。"},{"en":"A particular advance in battery design may make electric buses cheaper to run.","zh":"電池設計中的某項特定進展，可能令電動巴士營運更便宜。"},{"en":"One advance can change many things if it affects cost, safety, speed, or access.","zh":"如果一項進展影響成本、安全、速度或可及性，它可以改變許多事情。"},{"en":"The phrase points to one specific development rather than progress in general.","zh":"這個短語指出一項具體發展，而不是泛指進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"dynamic applies to","meaning":"這種情況適用於……","examples":[{"en":"This dynamic applies to many areas of scientific research.","zh":"這種情況適用於許多科學研究領域。"},{"en":"If a dynamic applies to something, the same pattern, process, or situation is true there too.","zh":"dynamic applies to something 指同一模式、過程或情況在該處也成立。"},{"en":"The same classroom dynamic applies to sports teams: trust improves cooperation.","zh":"同一課室互動情況也適用於運動隊：信任會改善合作。"},{"en":"A pattern applies more widely when different situations show the same cause-and-effect relationship.","zh":"當不同情況顯示相同因果關係，一種模式就能更廣泛適用。"},{"en":"The phrase extends an idea from one case to other cases.","zh":"這個短語把一個想法由一個案例延伸到其他案例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"directly affect people’s lives","meaning":"直接影響人們的生活","examples":[{"en":"Medical and environmental research directly affect people’s lives.","zh":"醫學和環境研究直接影響人們的生活。"},{"en":"To directly affect people’s lives means to have an immediate or clear influence on their health, choices, work, safety, or daily routines.","zh":"directly affect people’s lives 指對人們的健康、選擇、工作、安全或日常習慣有即時或清楚影響。"},{"en":"Public transport policy directly affects people’s lives because it changes how they get to school and work.","zh":"公共交通政策直接影響人們的生活，因為它改變他們如何上學和上班。"},{"en":"Research matters more to the public when its effects are visible in everyday decisions.","zh":"當研究影響可在日常決定中看見，它對公眾就更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses practical impact, not distant theory.","zh":"這個短語強調實際影響，而不是遙遠理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"global warming","meaning":"全球暖化","examples":[{"en":"Global warming is frequently discussed in scientific reporting.","zh":"全球暖化常在科學新聞報道中被討論。"},{"en":"Global warming usually refers to the long-term rise in Earth’s average temperature caused largely by greenhouse gases.","zh":"global warming 通常指主要由溫室氣體造成的地球平均氣溫長期上升。"},{"en":"Students may learn about global warming by studying heatwaves, melting ice, and rising sea levels.","zh":"學生可以透過研究熱浪、冰層融化和海平面上升來了解全球暖化。"},{"en":"The term can confuse people if they think it means every place must become warmer every day.","zh":"如果人們以為它表示每個地方每天都必須變暖，這個詞就可能令人困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase names an important climate issue but must be explained carefully.","zh":"這個短語命名一個重要氣候議題，但必須仔細解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cancer research","meaning":"癌症研究","examples":[{"en":"Cancer research often produces complex and developing findings.","zh":"癌症研究常產生複雜而仍在發展的發現。"},{"en":"Cancer research is scientific work that studies the causes, detection, treatment, and prevention of cancer.","zh":"cancer research 指研究癌症成因、偵測、治療和預防的科學工作。"},{"en":"A hospital may join cancer research by testing whether a new drug helps a specific group of patients.","zh":"醫院可能透過測試新藥是否幫助特定病人群體來參與癌症研究。"},{"en":"Cancer research is complex because different cancers may behave differently in different people.","zh":"癌症研究很複雜，因為不同癌症在不同人身上可能表現不同。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to medical research focused on cancer.","zh":"這個短語指以癌症為焦點的醫學研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"diet studies","meaning":"飲食研究","examples":[{"en":"Diet studies may produce results that appear contradictory.","zh":"飲食研究可能產生看似互相矛盾的結果。"},{"en":"Diet studies are research studies about how food, nutrients, and eating habits affect health.","zh":"diet studies 指關於食物、營養和飲食習慣如何影響健康的研究。"},{"en":"A diet study may compare students who eat breakfast with those who skip it.","zh":"飲食研究可能比較吃早餐和不吃早餐的學生。"},{"en":"Results can seem contradictory when different studies examine different people, foods, or time periods.","zh":"當不同研究考察不同人群、食物或時間長度，結果可能看似矛盾。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to scientific research on eating and health.","zh":"這個短語指關於飲食和健康的科學研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"learn how to overcome","meaning":"學會如何克服……","examples":[{"en":"Science communicators must learn how to overcome these difficulties.","zh":"科學傳意者必須學會如何克服這些困難。"},{"en":"To learn how to overcome something means to find and practise ways to deal successfully with a problem.","zh":"learn how to overcome something 指找到並練習成功處理問題的方法。"},{"en":"A shy student can learn how to overcome speaking anxiety through short daily practice.","zh":"害羞學生可以透過每日短時間練習，學會如何克服演說焦慮。"},{"en":"People overcome difficulties when they understand the cause and use practical strategies.","zh":"當人們理解成因並使用實際策略，就能克服困難。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on developing the ability to solve a challenge.","zh":"這個短語重點是培養解決挑戰的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be critical to","meaning":"對……至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Clear reporting is critical to promoting informed debate.","zh":"清晰報道對推動有充分資料支持的討論至關重要。"},{"en":"To be critical to something means to be extremely important for making it happen or work well.","zh":"be critical to something 指對某事發生或良好運作極其重要。"},{"en":"Regular sleep is critical to memory and concentration before exams.","zh":"考試前，規律睡眠對記憶和專注至關重要。"},{"en":"If a factor is critical, failure in that area can weaken the whole result.","zh":"如果某因素至關重要，該方面失敗就會削弱整體結果。"},{"en":"The phrase means essential, not merely helpful.","zh":"這個短語意思是不可或缺，而不只是有幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"spur a debate","meaning":"推動討論","examples":[{"en":"Accurate information can spur a more informed public debate.","zh":"準確資訊可以推動更有資料支持的公眾討論。"},{"en":"To spur a debate means to encourage, trigger, or push people to discuss an issue.","zh":"spur a debate 指鼓勵、觸發或推動人們討論某議題。"},{"en":"A new school policy may spur a debate among parents about homework pressure.","zh":"新學校政策可能推動家長之間關於功課壓力的討論。"},{"en":"Public debate begins when information makes people notice a problem or disagreement.","zh":"當資訊令人注意到問題或分歧，公共討論便會開始。"},{"en":"The phrase describes causing discussion to start or become more active.","zh":"這個短語描述促使討論開始或變得更活躍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"informed scientific debate","meaning":"有充分資料支持的科學討論","examples":[{"en":"The public needs access to informed scientific debate.","zh":"公眾需要接觸有充分資料支持的科學討論。"},{"en":"Informed scientific debate is discussion based on evidence, expert knowledge, and accurate understanding of research.","zh":"informed scientific debate 指以證據、專家知識和對研究的準確理解為基礎的討論。"},{"en":"A classroom can hold an informed scientific debate on vaccination after students read reliable sources.","zh":"學生閱讀可靠資料後，課堂可以就疫苗舉行有充分資料支持的科學討論。"},{"en":"Debate becomes more useful when participants understand the evidence instead of relying on slogans.","zh":"當參與者理解證據而不是依賴口號，討論會更有用。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts serious evidence-based discussion with empty argument.","zh":"這個短語把嚴肅的證據本位討論與空洞爭論作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"broader public","meaning":"廣大公眾","examples":[{"en":"Complex findings must be explained to the broader public.","zh":"複雜發現必須向廣大公眾解釋。"},{"en":"The broader public means ordinary people in society, not only experts or specialists.","zh":"broader public 指社會中的普通人，而不只是專家或專門人士。"},{"en":"A museum exhibition can help the broader public understand ancient history through simple displays.","zh":"博物館展覽可以透過簡單展示，幫助廣大公眾理解古代歷史。"},{"en":"Research matters socially when the broader public can understand its risks, benefits, and limits.","zh":"當廣大公眾能理解研究的風險、好處和限制，研究才具有社會意義。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a wide general audience.","zh":"這個短語指廣泛的一般受眾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ambiguous word choices","meaning":"含糊的用詞","examples":[{"en":"Ambiguous word choices are a source of scientific misunderstandings.","zh":"含糊的用詞是科學誤解的來源。"},{"en":"Ambiguous word choices are words or phrases that can be understood in more than one way.","zh":"ambiguous word choices 指可以用多於一種方式理解的字詞或短語。"},{"en":"A teacher’s phrase “finish it soon” is ambiguous because students may not know the exact deadline.","zh":"老師說 “finish it soon” 是含糊的，因為學生可能不知道確實限期。"},{"en":"Ambiguity causes problems when listeners choose the wrong meaning.","zh":"當聽眾選擇了錯誤意思，含糊便會造成問題。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights how unclear wording can create confusion.","zh":"這個短語突出不清晰用詞如何製造混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"source of misunderstandings","meaning":"誤解的來源","examples":[{"en":"Technical language can become a source of misunderstandings.","zh":"技術語言可以成為誤解的來源。"},{"en":"A source of misunderstandings is something that causes people to get the wrong meaning.","zh":"source of misunderstandings 指導致人們理解錯誤的事物。"},{"en":"Different date formats can be a source of misunderstandings when one country writes the month first.","zh":"當某國先寫月份，不同日期格式可以成為誤解的來源。"},{"en":"Misunderstandings often begin when people assume a word means the same thing in every context.","zh":"當人們假設一個詞在每個語境中意思相同，誤解常會開始。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what creates confusion.","zh":"這個短語指出造成混亂的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"employ colloquial terminology","meaning":"使用日常用語","examples":[{"en":"Scientists sometimes employ colloquial terminology in a specialised way.","zh":"科學家有時以專門方式使用日常用語。"},{"en":"To employ colloquial terminology means to use everyday words or informal expressions.","zh":"employ colloquial terminology 指使用日常詞語或非正式表達。"},{"en":"A doctor may employ colloquial terminology like “heartburn” before explaining the medical term.","zh":"醫生在解釋醫學術語前，可能使用 “heartburn” 這類日常用語。"},{"en":"Everyday words can help communication, but they can also confuse people if scientists use them differently.","zh":"日常用語可以幫助溝通，但如果科學家用法不同，也可以令人困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using ordinary language, often for technical purposes.","zh":"這個短語描述使用普通語言，通常用於技術目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"colloquial terminology","meaning":"口語化術語","examples":[{"en":"Colloquial terminology may have a different scientific meaning.","zh":"口語化術語可能有不同的科學意思。"},{"en":"Colloquial terminology is ordinary everyday language rather than formal or technical language.","zh":"colloquial terminology 指普通日常語言，而不是正式或技術語言。"},{"en":"Students often use colloquial terminology when they say “bugs” instead of “software errors”.","zh":"學生說 “bugs” 而不是 “software errors” 時，就是使用口語化術語。"},{"en":"Problems arise when a common word has one meaning in daily speech and another meaning in science.","zh":"當常見詞在日常說話中有一個意思，在科學中有另一個意思，就會出現問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to informal words used in ordinary conversation.","zh":"這個短語指普通對話中使用的非正式詞語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"assign a specific meaning to","meaning":"賦予……特定意思","examples":[{"en":"Scientists may assign a specific meaning to an ordinary word.","zh":"科學家可能賦予普通詞語特定意思。"},{"en":"To assign a specific meaning to a word means to give it a clear, fixed meaning in a particular context.","zh":"assign a specific meaning to a word 指在特定語境中給它清楚固定的意思。"},{"en":"In a classroom, a teacher may assign a specific meaning to “evidence” before a debate.","zh":"在課堂辯論前，老師可能賦予 “evidence” 特定意思。"},{"en":"Specific meanings reduce confusion because everyone knows exactly how the word is being used.","zh":"特定意思能減少混亂，因為每個人都知道該詞究竟如何被使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes defining a word for careful use.","zh":"這個短語描述為了謹慎使用而定義詞語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"impossible to fathom","meaning":"難以理解","examples":[{"en":"The intended meaning may be impossible to fathom without training.","zh":"如果沒有訓練，人們可能難以理解原本意思。"},{"en":"If something is impossible to fathom, it is extremely difficult or impossible to understand.","zh":"impossible to fathom 指極難或無法理解。"},{"en":"A legal contract may be impossible to fathom for ordinary readers if it uses too much technical language.","zh":"如果法律合約使用太多專門語言，普通讀者可能難以理解。"},{"en":"People struggle to fathom an idea when it requires background knowledge they do not have.","zh":"當一個概念需要人們沒有的背景知識，人們就難以理解它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep difficulty in understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述理解上的深層困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"without proper training","meaning":"沒有適當訓練","examples":[{"en":"Some technical ideas cannot be understood without proper training.","zh":"有些技術概念沒有適當訓練便無法理解。"},{"en":"Without proper training means without the necessary teaching, practice, or preparation.","zh":"without proper training 指沒有必要教學、練習或準備。"},{"en":"A person should not operate heavy machinery without proper training.","zh":"一個人不應在沒有適當訓練下操作重型機械。"},{"en":"Technical subjects become dangerous or confusing when people try to use them without preparation.","zh":"當人們在沒有準備下嘗試使用技術主題，它們會變得危險或令人困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that knowledge or skill is needed first.","zh":"這個短語顯示知識或技能必須先具備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"theory of relativity","meaning":"相對論","examples":[{"en":"The theory of relativity is often misunderstood by non-specialists.","zh":"相對論常被非專家誤解。"},{"en":"The theory of relativity is Einstein’s physical theory about space, time, gravity, and motion.","zh":"theory of relativity 指愛因斯坦關於空間、時間、重力和運動的物理理論。"},{"en":"Students may first meet the theory of relativity through examples about clocks, light, and fast-moving objects.","zh":"學生可能最初透過關於時鐘、光和高速移動物體的例子接觸相對論。"},{"en":"The theory is difficult to communicate because its name sounds simpler than the mathematics behind it.","zh":"這個理論難以傳達，因為其名稱聽起來比背後數學簡單。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a major scientific theory, not a casual opinion.","zh":"這個短語指一套重要科學理論，而不是隨意意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"intrinsically misleading","meaning":"本質上容易引起誤解","examples":[{"en":"The term “relativity” can be intrinsically misleading.","zh":"“relativity” 這個詞本質上容易引起誤解。"},{"en":"Intrinsically misleading means misleading by its very nature, not only because of poor explanation.","zh":"intrinsically misleading 指其本身性質就容易誤導，而不只是因解釋差劣。"},{"en":"A product name can be intrinsically misleading if it suggests health benefits that do not exist.","zh":"如果產品名稱暗示不存在的健康好處，它本身就可能容易引起誤解。"},{"en":"A misleading term can create confusion before any detailed explanation begins.","zh":"容易誤導的術語可以在任何詳細解釋開始前就製造混亂。"},{"en":"The phrase means the problem is built into the word or idea itself.","zh":"這個短語意思是問題內置於該詞或概念本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"interpret the theory to mean","meaning":"把該理論理解為……","examples":[{"en":"Some people interpret the theory to mean that nothing is absolute.","zh":"有些人把該理論理解為沒有任何事物是絕對的。"},{"en":"To interpret the theory to mean something is to understand or explain the theory in that particular way.","zh":"interpret the theory to mean something 指以某種特定方式理解或解釋該理論。"},{"en":"A student may interpret a poem to mean that childhood memory is painful.","zh":"學生可能把一首詩理解為童年記憶是痛苦的。"},{"en":"Interpretations can be wrong if people focus on the title but ignore the actual content.","zh":"如果人們只集中於標題而忽略實際內容，詮釋可能是錯的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how people understand or explain a theory.","zh":"這個短語描述人們如何理解或解釋一套理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"everything is relative","meaning":"一切都是相對的","examples":[{"en":"The theory does not simply claim that everything is relative.","zh":"該理論並不只是聲稱一切都是相對的。"},{"en":"Everything is relative means everything depends on viewpoint, situation, or comparison.","zh":"everything is relative 指一切都取決於觀點、情況或比較。"},{"en":"In daily speech, people say everything is relative when a cheap meal in one city seems expensive in another.","zh":"在日常說話中，當某城市便宜的一餐在另一城市看似昂貴，人們會說一切都是相對的。"},{"en":"The phrase can oversimplify science if people use it to mean there are no fixed truths at all.","zh":"如果人們用這個短語表示完全沒有固定真理，它可能會過度簡化科學。"},{"en":"It is a broad expression and should not be confused with the precise physics of relativity.","zh":"它是一個寬泛表達，不應與相對論中精確的物理內容混淆。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"there are no absolutes","meaning":"沒有任何絕對事物","examples":[{"en":"Some people mistakenly believe that relativity means there are no absolutes.","zh":"有些人錯誤地相信，相對論表示沒有任何絕對事物。"},{"en":"There are no absolutes means nothing is fixed, definite, or universally true.","zh":"there are no absolutes 指沒有任何事物是固定、明確或普遍真實的。"},{"en":"In ethics class, students may debate whether there are no absolutes in moral judgment.","zh":"在倫理課中，學生可能辯論道德判斷中是否沒有任何絕對事物。"},{"en":"This idea can mislead readers if it is wrongly attached to a scientific theory.","zh":"如果這個想法被錯誤套在科學理論上，就會誤導讀者。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses a philosophical claim, not the actual meaning of relativity.","zh":"這個短語表達哲學主張，而不是相對論的實際意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"measurements an observer makes","meaning":"觀察者所作的測量","examples":[{"en":"The measurements an observer makes depend on the chosen coordinates.","zh":"觀察者所作的測量取決於所選坐標。"},{"en":"Measurements an observer makes are the values recorded by someone observing an event or object.","zh":"measurements an observer makes 指某人觀察事件或物體時記錄的數值。"},{"en":"Two students may make different measurements of a desk if one uses inches and the other uses centimetres.","zh":"如果一名學生用英寸，另一名學生用厘米，他們對書桌所作的測量可能不同。"},{"en":"Measurements can differ when observers use different frames, tools, or reference points.","zh":"當觀察者使用不同框架、工具或參考點，測量可能不同。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on recorded values from a particular observer’s position.","zh":"這個短語重點是從特定觀察者位置記錄的數值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"depend on","meaning":"取決於……","examples":[{"en":"Scientific measurements may depend on the observer’s reference frame.","zh":"科學測量可能取決於觀察者的參考系。"},{"en":"To depend on something means to be affected or determined by it.","zh":"depend on something 指受某事影響或由某事決定。"},{"en":"A student’s route to school may depend on the weather and traffic.","zh":"學生上學路線可能取決於天氣和交通。"},{"en":"Results depend on conditions when changing those conditions changes the outcome.","zh":"當改變條件會改變結果，結果就取決於條件。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one thing is linked to another as a condition or cause.","zh":"這個短語顯示一件事以另一件事為條件或原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"coordinates and reference frame","meaning":"坐標及參考系","examples":[{"en":"The observer’s coordinates and reference frame affect the measurements.","zh":"觀察者的坐標及參考系會影響測量。"},{"en":"Coordinates and reference frame are the system and viewpoint used to describe position, motion, and measurement.","zh":"coordinates and reference frame 指用來描述位置、運動和測量的系統與觀點。"},{"en":"A map uses coordinates so people can locate a building precisely.","zh":"地圖使用坐標，讓人們能準確定位建築物。"},{"en":"Measurements change if observers describe motion from different positions or systems.","zh":"如果觀察者從不同位置或系統描述運動，測量會改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the framework used for describing physical events.","zh":"這個短語指用來描述物理事件的框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"physical phenomena","meaning":"物理現象","examples":[{"en":"The theory describes physical phenomena in an invariant way.","zh":"該理論以不變方式描述物理現象。"},{"en":"Physical phenomena are events or processes in the natural world that can be observed, measured, or explained by physics.","zh":"physical phenomena 指自然世界中可被觀察、測量或由物理解釋的事件或過程。"},{"en":"Falling objects, light, heat, and electricity are physical phenomena.","zh":"物體下墜、光、熱和電都是物理現象。"},{"en":"Scientists study physical phenomena to find patterns that remain true beyond one situation.","zh":"科學家研究物理現象，以尋找超越單一情況仍成立的規律。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to real events in nature, not opinions or feelings.","zh":"這個短語指自然界中的真實事件，而不是意見或感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"invariant description","meaning":"不變的描述","examples":[{"en":"Relativity seeks an invariant description of physical phenomena.","zh":"相對論尋求對物理現象作不變的描述。"},{"en":"An invariant description is an explanation that remains valid even when coordinates or viewpoints change.","zh":"invariant description 指即使坐標或觀點改變仍然有效的解釋。"},{"en":"A good classroom rule should have an invariant description: it applies fairly to all students, not only one group.","zh":"好的課室規則應有不變的描述：它公平適用於所有學生，而不只是某一群體。"},{"en":"In physics, invariant descriptions help scientists separate real laws from observer-dependent measurements.","zh":"在物理學中，不變的描述幫助科學家把真正定律與依賴觀察者的測量分開。"},{"en":"The phrase means a stable description that does not change with perspective.","zh":"這個短語意思是不隨視角改變的穩定描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"transcend particular coordinates","meaning":"超越特定坐標","examples":[{"en":"A physical law can transcend an observer’s particular coordinates.","zh":"物理定律可以超越觀察者的特定坐標。"},{"en":"To transcend particular coordinates means to go beyond one specific system of measurement or viewpoint.","zh":"transcend particular coordinates 指超越某一特定測量系統或觀點。"},{"en":"A fair rule should transcend one classroom and apply across the whole school.","zh":"公平規則應超越一間課室，並適用於整間學校。"},{"en":"Scientific laws are powerful when they remain true beyond one observer’s coordinate system.","zh":"當科學定律在一個觀察者坐標系以外仍然成立，它就很有力量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving beyond a limited frame.","zh":"這個短語描述超越有限框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"really about","meaning":"真正關乎……","examples":[{"en":"Einstein’s theory is really about finding invariant descriptions.","zh":"愛因斯坦的理論真正關乎尋找不變描述。"},{"en":"If something is really about an idea, that idea is its true central meaning or purpose.","zh":"如果 something is really about an idea，該想法就是其真正核心意思或目的。"},{"en":"A school rule about uniforms may be really about discipline and equality, not clothing itself.","zh":"關於校服的校規可能真正關乎紀律和平等，而不是衣服本身。"},{"en":"This phrase helps correct a surface misunderstanding and point to the deeper issue.","zh":"這個短語幫助修正表面誤解，並指出更深層議題。"},{"en":"It tells readers what the main point actually is.","zh":"它告訴讀者主要重點實際是甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"would have been better named","meaning":"如改稱……會更恰當","examples":[{"en":"Einstein agreed that the theory would have been better named differently.","zh":"愛因斯坦同意，如果該理論改用另一個名稱會更恰當。"},{"en":"Would have been better named means the name would have been more accurate or helpful if it had been different.","zh":"would have been better named 指如果名稱不同，會更準確或更有幫助。"},{"en":"A confusing school programme would have been better named if students could tell its purpose from the title.","zh":"如果學生能從標題看出目的，一個令人困惑的學校計劃就會命名得更好。"},{"en":"Names matter because a poor name can create wrong expectations before people learn the details.","zh":"名稱很重要，因為差劣名稱可以在人們學習細節前造成錯誤期望。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises a name after seeing its effects.","zh":"這個短語是在看到名稱影響後對名稱作批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be entrenched","meaning":"已根深蒂固","examples":[{"en":"The term “relativity” was already entrenched in scientific language.","zh":"“relativity” 這個詞在科學語言中已經根深蒂固。"},{"en":"To be entrenched means to be firmly established and difficult to change.","zh":"be entrenched 指已牢固建立並難以改變。"},{"en":"A bad habit can become entrenched if a student repeats it for years.","zh":"如果學生多年重複一個壞習慣，它可能變得根深蒂固。"},{"en":"Once a word is entrenched in public use, replacing it becomes difficult even if it is imperfect.","zh":"一旦某詞在公眾用法中根深蒂固，即使它並不完美，也很難取代。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something deeply fixed in a system or habit.","zh":"這個短語描述某事在系統或習慣中深深固定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at the time","meaning":"當時","examples":[{"en":"The name was already widely established at the time.","zh":"這個名稱當時已經被廣泛使用。"},{"en":"At the time means during the particular period being discussed.","zh":"at the time 指在正被討論的那個特定時期。"},{"en":"I did not understand the teacher’s advice at the time, but it helped me later.","zh":"我當時不明白老師的建議，但它後來幫了我。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers understand decisions in their original historical context.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者在原本歷史語境中理解決定。"},{"en":"It refers to the period of the event, not necessarily the present.","zh":"它指事件發生的時期，不一定是現在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"uncertainty principle","meaning":"不確定性原理","examples":[{"en":"The uncertainty principle is another frequently misunderstood term.","zh":"不確定性原理是另一個經常被誤解的術語。"},{"en":"The uncertainty principle is a principle in quantum physics about limits on precisely knowing certain pairs of quantities at the same time.","zh":"uncertainty principle 指量子物理中關於某些成對物理量無法同時精確知道的限制。"},{"en":"Students may wrongly think the uncertainty principle only means scientists have poor measuring tools.","zh":"學生可能錯誤地以為不確定性原理只表示科學家的測量工具不好。"},{"en":"The term causes confusion because “uncertainty” has a broader everyday meaning.","zh":"這個術語造成混亂，因為 “uncertainty” 在日常語言中意思更廣。"},{"en":"The phrase names a precise scientific principle, not general doubt.","zh":"這個短語命名一項精確科學原理，而不是一般懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"frequently abused term","meaning":"經常被誤用的術語","examples":[{"en":"The phrase has become a frequently abused scientific term.","zh":"這個短語已成為經常被誤用的科學術語。"},{"en":"A frequently abused term is a word or phrase often misused, overused, or twisted away from its proper meaning.","zh":"frequently abused term 指常被誤用、濫用或扭離正確意思的字詞或短語。"},{"en":"“Addiction” can become a frequently abused term when people use it for any strong liking.","zh":"當人們用 “addiction” 形容任何強烈喜好，它就可能成為經常被誤用的詞。"},{"en":"A term is abused when popularity makes people repeat it without understanding it.","zh":"當流行令人在不理解下重複某詞，該詞就被誤用。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that common usage may be inaccurate.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們常見用法可能不準確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be interpreted as","meaning":"被理解為……","examples":[{"en":"The principle is sometimes interpreted as a limitation on observers.","zh":"該原理有時被理解為對觀察者的限制。"},{"en":"To be interpreted as something means to be understood or explained in that way.","zh":"be interpreted as something 指被以某種方式理解或解釋。"},{"en":"A quiet student’s silence may be interpreted as rudeness, even though she is shy.","zh":"安靜學生的沉默可能被理解為無禮，即使她只是害羞。"},{"en":"Misinterpretation happens when people read more into a word or action than it actually means.","zh":"當人們把字詞或行動理解得超出其實際意思，就會出現誤解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how meaning is assigned by readers or listeners.","zh":"這個短語描述讀者或聽眾如何賦予意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"limitation on","meaning":"對……的限制","examples":[{"en":"The principle is not simply a limitation on measurement techniques.","zh":"該原理並不只是對測量技術的限制。"},{"en":"A limitation on something is a restriction that prevents it from being done fully or freely.","zh":"limitation on something 指阻止某事被完全或自由完成的限制。"},{"en":"A time limit is a limitation on how much a student can write in an exam.","zh":"時間限制是對學生在考試中能寫多少的限制。"},{"en":"Limitations matter because they show what a method or system cannot do.","zh":"限制很重要，因為它們顯示方法或系統不能做到甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a boundary or restriction.","zh":"這個短語指出界限或約束。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ability to make measurements","meaning":"進行測量的能力","examples":[{"en":"Technology can improve our ability to make measurements.","zh":"科技可以改善我們進行測量的能力。"},{"en":"Ability to make measurements means the capacity to measure things accurately and reliably.","zh":"ability to make measurements 指準確而可靠地量度事物的能力。"},{"en":"A digital thermometer improves a nurse’s ability to make measurements of body temperature.","zh":"電子探熱針改善護士測量體溫的能力。"},{"en":"Better instruments can improve measurement ability, but they may not remove every scientific limit.","zh":"更好儀器可以改善測量能力，但未必能消除每一種科學限制。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on practical measuring skill or capacity.","zh":"這個短語重點是實際測量技能或能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"intrinsic limitations","meaning":"內在限制","examples":[{"en":"The principle does not concern intrinsic limitations on one measurement.","zh":"該原理並不關乎某一次測量的內在限制。"},{"en":"Intrinsic limitations are limits built into the nature of something, not caused only by outside problems.","zh":"intrinsic limitations 指內置於某事本質之中的限制，而不只是由外部問題造成。"},{"en":"A small classroom has intrinsic limitations because it cannot hold fifty students safely.","zh":"小課室有內在限制，因為它不能安全容納五十名學生。"},{"en":"Intrinsic limits remain even when people work carefully or use better tools.","zh":"即使人們仔細工作或使用更好工具，內在限制仍然存在。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limits that come from the thing itself.","zh":"這個短語描述來自事物本身的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"particular measurement","meaning":"某一次特定測量","examples":[{"en":"The issue is not the accuracy of one particular measurement.","zh":"問題並不在某一次特定測量的準確性。"},{"en":"A particular measurement is one specific act or result of measuring something.","zh":"particular measurement 指某一次具體測量行為或結果。"},{"en":"A teacher may check one particular measurement in a science experiment to see if the ruler was read correctly.","zh":"老師可能檢查科學實驗中的某一次特定測量，以看尺是否讀得正確。"},{"en":"One measurement can be wrong because of human error, but a scientific principle may concern a deeper limit.","zh":"一次測量可能因人為錯誤而錯，但科學原理可能關乎更深層限制。"},{"en":"The phrase points to one specific measurement, not measuring in general.","zh":"這個短語指出某一次具體測量，而不是泛指測量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"inability to precisely measure","meaning":"無法精確測量","examples":[{"en":"The principle concerns the inability to precisely measure paired quantities.","zh":"該原理關乎無法精確測量成對物理量。"},{"en":"Inability to precisely measure something means being unable to measure it with exact accuracy.","zh":"inability to precisely measure something 指不能以完全準確度量度某物。"},{"en":"A cheap kitchen scale may create an inability to precisely measure very small amounts of medicine.","zh":"廉價廚房磅可能導致無法精確測量極少量藥物。"},{"en":"Measurement limits matter because uncertain values can affect predictions and conclusions.","zh":"測量限制很重要，因為不確定數值可以影響預測和結論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a lack of exact measuring capacity.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏精確測量能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pairs of quantities","meaning":"成對的物理量","examples":[{"en":"Certain pairs of quantities cannot be measured precisely at the same time.","zh":"某些成對的物理量不能同時被精確測量。"},{"en":"Pairs of quantities are two related measurable properties considered together.","zh":"pairs of quantities 指一起考慮的兩個相關可測量性質。"},{"en":"In a simple experiment, speed and time can be treated as a pair of quantities.","zh":"在簡單實驗中，速度和時間可以被視為一對物理量。"},{"en":"Some paired quantities matter because improving precision in one may affect precision in the other.","zh":"有些成對物理量很重要，因為提高其中一個的精確度可能影響另一個的精確度。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to two measurable values discussed as a pair.","zh":"這個短語指被成對討論的兩個可測量數值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"simultaneously","meaning":"同時地","examples":[{"en":"Some physical quantities cannot be precisely measured simultaneously.","zh":"有些物理量不能同時被精確測量。"},{"en":"Simultaneously means at the same time.","zh":"simultaneously 指在同一時間。"},{"en":"A student cannot speak clearly and drink water simultaneously.","zh":"學生不能同時清楚說話和喝水。"},{"en":"Problems become harder when two tasks must be done simultaneously rather than one after another.","zh":"當兩項任務必須同時完成，而不是一前一後完成，問題會變得更困難。"},{"en":"The word stresses timing: two things happen together.","zh":"這個詞強調時間：兩件事一起發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"more engaging from a philosophical perspective","meaning":"從哲學角度看更吸引","examples":[{"en":"The inaccurate interpretation may seem more engaging from a philosophical perspective.","zh":"這種不準確詮釋從哲學角度看可能更吸引。"},{"en":"More engaging from a philosophical perspective means more interesting when considered as a broad question about truth, knowledge, or existence.","zh":"more engaging from a philosophical perspective 指從關於真理、知識或存在的廣泛問題來看更有趣。"},{"en":"A film about memory may be more engaging from a philosophical perspective than a simple action story.","zh":"一部關於記憶的電影，從哲學角度看可能比簡單動作片更吸引。"},{"en":"An idea can sound philosophically exciting but still be scientifically inaccurate.","zh":"一個想法可能在哲學上聽起來令人興奮，但在科學上仍不準確。"},{"en":"The phrase separates intellectual appeal from scientific correctness.","zh":"這個短語把思想吸引力與科學正確性分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"political perspective","meaning":"政治角度","examples":[{"en":"Scientific ideas are sometimes interpreted from a political perspective.","zh":"科學概念有時會從政治角度被詮釋。"},{"en":"A political perspective is a way of understanding something in relation to power, policy, government, or social interests.","zh":"political perspective 指從權力、政策、政府或社會利益關係來理解某事。"},{"en":"A school funding debate can be viewed from a political perspective because it involves public money and priorities.","zh":"學校撥款辯論可以從政治角度觀看，因為它涉及公共金錢和優先次序。"},{"en":"Scientific issues become political when they affect laws, budgets, or public behaviour.","zh":"當科學議題影響法律、預算或公眾行為，它們就變得政治化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one angle for interpreting an issue.","zh":"這個短語描述詮釋議題的一個角度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not what science is about","meaning":"並非該科學原理的真正內容","examples":[{"en":"The popular interpretation is not what the scientific principle is about.","zh":"流行詮釋並非該科學原理的真正內容。"},{"en":"Not what science is about means not the real subject, purpose, or meaning of the scientific idea.","zh":"not what science is about 指並非該科學概念的真正主題、目的或意思。"},{"en":"Saying “healthy food is always expensive” is not what nutrition science is about.","zh":"說「健康食物總是昂貴」並非營養科學的真正內容。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects a misunderstanding by separating popular belief from the actual topic.","zh":"這個短語透過區分流行信念和實際主題來修正誤解。"},{"en":"It tells readers that the common explanation misses the point.","zh":"它告訴讀者常見解釋錯過了重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"even the word “theory”","meaning":"就連「理論」一詞","examples":[{"en":"Even the word “theory” can cause confusion.","zh":"就連「理論」一詞也可以造成混亂。"},{"en":"Even the word “theory” means that this ordinary-looking word itself can create misunderstanding.","zh":"even the word “theory” 指這個看似普通的詞本身也可以造成誤解。"},{"en":"Even the word “fair” can cause arguments if students and teachers define it differently.","zh":"如果學生和老師對「公平」定義不同，就連「公平」一詞也可以引起爭論。"},{"en":"A familiar word can be confusing when its everyday meaning differs from its technical meaning.","zh":"當熟悉詞語的日常意思與技術意思不同，它就可能令人困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises that the problem can begin with a very common word.","zh":"這個短語強調問題可以從非常常見的詞開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"passing conjecture","meaning":"一時的猜測","examples":[{"en":"In everyday speech, a theory may mean a passing conjecture.","zh":"在日常說話中，理論可能指一時的猜測。"},{"en":"A passing conjecture is a quick, temporary guess that has not been carefully tested.","zh":"passing conjecture 指快速、暫時而未經仔細測試的猜想。"},{"en":"If a student says the teacher is absent because of traffic, that may be only a passing conjecture.","zh":"如果學生說老師因交通問題缺席，那可能只是一時的猜測。"},{"en":"Passing conjectures can be useful starting points but should not be treated as proven facts.","zh":"一時的猜測可以是有用起點，但不應被視為已證實事實。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a casual guess, not a scientific theory.","zh":"這個短語描述隨意猜想，而不是科學理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"regard something as suspect","meaning":"認為……可疑","examples":[{"en":"People often regard an unsupported theory as suspect.","zh":"人們常認為缺乏支持的理論可疑。"},{"en":"To regard something as suspect means to consider it doubtful, questionable, or possibly false.","zh":"regard something as suspect 指認為某事可疑、有問題或可能不真實。"},{"en":"A teacher may regard an essay as suspect if it suddenly uses vocabulary far above the student’s usual level.","zh":"如果一篇作文突然使用遠高於學生平常水平的詞彙，老師可能認為它可疑。"},{"en":"People become suspicious when a claim lacks evidence or sounds too convenient.","zh":"當主張缺乏證據或聽起來太方便，人們會產生懷疑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes distrust toward something.","zh":"這個短語描述對某事的不信任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have specific ideas in mind","meaning":"心中有特定概念","examples":[{"en":"Physicists have specific ideas in mind when they discuss theories.","zh":"物理學家討論理論時，心中有特定概念。"},{"en":"To have specific ideas in mind means to be thinking of clear and particular meanings, not vague ones.","zh":"have specific ideas in mind 指想着清楚而特定的意思，而不是模糊意思。"},{"en":"A teacher has specific ideas in mind when she asks students to write a formal complaint letter.","zh":"老師要求學生寫正式投訴信時，心中有特定概念。"},{"en":"Communication improves when speakers explain the specific meaning they have in mind.","zh":"當說話者解釋自己心中的特定意思，溝通會改善。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a word is being used with a precise intention.","zh":"這個短語顯示某詞被帶着精確意圖使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"entail a definite framework","meaning":"包含一套明確框架","examples":[{"en":"A scientific theory entails a definite physical framework.","zh":"科學理論包含一套明確的物理框架。"},{"en":"To entail a definite framework means to include a clear structure of assumptions, concepts, and rules.","zh":"entail a definite framework 指包含一套由假設、概念和規則組成的清晰結構。"},{"en":"A school assessment system entails a definite framework of criteria, marks, and feedback.","zh":"學校評估制度包含一套由準則、分數和回饋組成的明確框架。"},{"en":"A framework helps people understand how different parts of an idea fit together.","zh":"框架幫助人們理解概念中不同部分如何配合。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a theory is organised, not just guessed.","zh":"這個短語顯示理論是有組織的，而不只是猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"physical framework","meaning":"物理框架","examples":[{"en":"A theory provides a physical framework for understanding observations.","zh":"理論提供一套物理框架，用來理解觀察結果。"},{"en":"A physical framework is an organised set of ideas and equations used to describe physical reality.","zh":"physical framework 指用來描述物理現實的一套有組織概念和方程式。"},{"en":"A simple framework about forces helps students understand why objects fall or stop moving.","zh":"關於力的簡單框架幫助學生理解物體為何下墜或停止移動。"},{"en":"Frameworks guide interpretation because they tell scientists what relationships to look for.","zh":"框架指導詮釋，因為它告訴科學家應尋找甚麼關係。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the structure behind a scientific explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述科學解釋背後的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be embodied in","meaning":"體現在……之中","examples":[{"en":"The framework is embodied in fundamental assumptions and equations.","zh":"該框架體現在基本假設和方程式之中。"},{"en":"To be embodied in something means to be expressed, represented, or made concrete through it.","zh":"be embodied in something 指透過某事被表達、代表或具體化。"},{"en":"A school’s values are embodied in how teachers treat weaker students.","zh":"學校價值觀體現在老師如何對待較弱學生之中。"},{"en":"Abstract ideas become clearer when they are embodied in rules, examples, or equations.","zh":"當抽象概念體現在規則、例子或方程式中，它們會更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase shows where an idea takes visible form.","zh":"這個短語顯示概念在哪裏取得可見形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fundamental assumptions","meaning":"基本假設","examples":[{"en":"Scientific theories begin with a set of fundamental assumptions.","zh":"科學理論由一套基本假設開始。"},{"en":"Fundamental assumptions are basic ideas accepted at the start of an argument, model, or theory.","zh":"fundamental assumptions 指一個論證、模型或理論一開始接受的基本想法。"},{"en":"A school budget plan may begin with the fundamental assumption that student numbers will not fall.","zh":"學校預算計劃可能由學生人數不會下降這個基本假設開始。"},{"en":"If fundamental assumptions are wrong, the conclusions built on them may also be weak.","zh":"如果基本假設錯誤，建立在其上的結論也可能薄弱。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the basic starting points of reasoning.","zh":"這個短語指推理的基本起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"導致；產生","examples":[{"en":"The assumptions lead to specific equations and predictions.","zh":"這些假設產生特定方程式和預測。"},{"en":"To lead to something means to cause it, produce it, or result in it.","zh":"lead to something 指造成、產生或導致某結果。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can lead to weak concentration during morning lessons.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致早上課堂專注力弱。"},{"en":"Small causes can lead to large results when they affect a whole system.","zh":"當小原因影響整個系統，它可以導致巨大結果。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a cause-and-effect relationship.","zh":"這個短語顯示因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a specific set of","meaning":"一套特定的……","examples":[{"en":"A theory produces a specific set of testable predictions.","zh":"理論產生一套特定的可測試預測。"},{"en":"A specific set of something means a clearly defined group of things.","zh":"specific set of something 指一組被清楚界定的事物。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students a specific set of vocabulary items to review before a quiz.","zh":"老師可能給學生一套特定詞彙，在小測前溫習。"},{"en":"Clear sets are useful because people know exactly what is included and what is not.","zh":"清晰組合很有用，因為人們準確知道包括甚麼和不包括甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses precision and boundaries.","zh":"這個短語強調精確和界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"equations and predictions","meaning":"方程式和預測","examples":[{"en":"The physical framework generates equations and predictions.","zh":"物理框架產生方程式和預測。"},{"en":"Equations and predictions are mathematical relationships and expected results based on a theory.","zh":"equations and predictions 指基於理論的數學關係和預期結果。"},{"en":"In a physics lesson, students use equations and predictions to estimate how far a ball will travel.","zh":"在物理課中，學生使用方程式和預測來估算球會飛多遠。"},{"en":"Predictions matter because scientists can compare them with real evidence.","zh":"預測很重要，因為科學家可以把它們與真實證據比較。"},{"en":"The phrase connects mathematical structure with testable outcomes.","zh":"這個短語把數學結構與可測試結果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be borne out by","meaning":"得到……證實","examples":[{"en":"A theory gains support when its predictions are borne out by evidence.","zh":"當理論的預測得到證據證實，該理論便獲得支持。"},{"en":"To be borne out by evidence means to be supported or confirmed by facts or observations.","zh":"be borne out by evidence 指得到事實或觀察支持或證實。"},{"en":"A student’s claim about poor sleep is borne out by her sleep diary and falling test scores.","zh":"學生關於睡眠不足的說法，得到她的睡眠日記和下降的測驗成績證實。"},{"en":"Evidence strengthens an idea when real results match what the idea predicted.","zh":"當真實結果與某想法預測相符，證據便加強該想法。"},{"en":"The phrase means supported by evidence, not merely believed.","zh":"這個短語意思是由證據支持，而不只是被相信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"successful predictions","meaning":"成功的預測","examples":[{"en":"Successful predictions strengthen confidence in a theory.","zh":"成功的預測加強人們對理論的信心。"},{"en":"Successful predictions are forecasts that turn out to match what later happens or is observed.","zh":"successful predictions 指後來證實與實際發生或觀察相符的預測。"},{"en":"A weather app makes successful predictions when it says rain will start at 3 p.m. and it does.","zh":"天氣應用程式預測下午三時開始下雨，而事實也是如此，就是作出成功預測。"},{"en":"Predictions build trust when they repeatedly match real outcomes.","zh":"當預測反覆符合真實結果，就會建立信任。"},{"en":"The phrase describes predictions confirmed by later evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述後來被證據確認的預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not necessarily shown to be","meaning":"不一定立即被證明為……","examples":[{"en":"Theories are not necessarily shown to be correct immediately.","zh":"理論不一定立即被證明為正確。"},{"en":"Not necessarily shown to be means not always proven or demonstrated as something.","zh":"not necessarily shown to be 指不一定總是被證明或展示為某種情況。"},{"en":"A new teaching method is not necessarily shown to be effective after only one lesson.","zh":"新教學方法不一定在一堂課後就被證明有效。"},{"en":"Some ideas need long testing before their value becomes clear.","zh":"有些想法需要長時間測試，其價值才會變得清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against expecting instant proof.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們不要期待即時證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"correct or complete","meaning":"正確或完整","examples":[{"en":"A new theory may not initially be correct or complete.","zh":"新理論起初可能並不正確或完整。"},{"en":"Correct or complete means accurate and fully developed with no major missing parts.","zh":"correct or complete 指準確並充分發展，沒有重大缺漏。"},{"en":"A student’s first essay plan may not be correct or complete, but feedback can improve it.","zh":"學生第一份作文大綱可能不正確或不完整，但回饋可以改善它。"},{"en":"Early scientific ideas may need revision before they explain all the evidence well.","zh":"早期科學想法可能需要修訂，才能好好解釋所有證據。"},{"en":"The phrase separates truth from fullness: an idea can be partly right but incomplete.","zh":"這個短語區分真確性與完整性：想法可以部分正確但不完整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take the better part of a decade","meaning":"花了接近十年","examples":[{"en":"Einstein took the better part of a decade to refine his theory.","zh":"愛因斯坦花了接近十年完善他的理論。"},{"en":"To take the better part of a decade means to take most of ten years.","zh":"take the better part of a decade 指花了十年中的大部分時間。"},{"en":"Building a new railway line may take the better part of a decade from planning to opening.","zh":"建造新鐵路線從規劃到開通，可能花了接近十年。"},{"en":"Difficult work takes years when it requires testing, revision, and careful checking.","zh":"當困難工作需要測試、修訂和仔細檢查，它就會花上多年。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a long period of effort.","zh":"這個短語強調長時間努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"develop the correct version","meaning":"發展出正確版本","examples":[{"en":"Einstein needed years to develop the correct version of the theory.","zh":"愛因斯坦需要多年才發展出該理論的正確版本。"},{"en":"To develop the correct version means to improve an idea until it becomes accurate and usable.","zh":"develop the correct version 指改善某想法，直到它變得準確而可用。"},{"en":"A student may need several drafts to develop the correct version of an essay argument.","zh":"學生可能需要幾份草稿，才能發展出作文論點的正確版本。"},{"en":"Correct versions often emerge through mistakes, feedback, and careful revision.","zh":"正確版本通常透過錯誤、回饋和仔細修訂而出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reaching a more accurate final form.","zh":"這個短語描述達到較準確的最終形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"general relativity","meaning":"廣義相對論","examples":[{"en":"General relativity was developed over many years.","zh":"廣義相對論是經多年發展而成的。"},{"en":"General relativity is Einstein’s theory that explains gravity as connected with the structure of space and time.","zh":"general relativity 指愛因斯坦將重力與空間和時間結構連起來解釋的理論。"},{"en":"Students may first hear about general relativity when learning why gravity affects light.","zh":"學生學習重力為何影響光時，可能首次聽到廣義相對論。"},{"en":"General relativity took years to develop because it required new mathematics and deep physical insight.","zh":"廣義相對論需要多年發展，因為它需要新數學和深刻物理洞察。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific scientific theory in physics.","zh":"這個短語命名物理學中的一套特定科學理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"eventually","meaning":"最終","examples":[{"en":"Eventually, scientific ideas and measurements become more settled.","zh":"最終，科學想法和測量會變得較穩定。"},{"en":"Eventually means after some time, especially after delay, effort, or development.","zh":"eventually 指經過一段時間後，尤其是在延遲、努力或發展之後。"},{"en":"A student may struggle with pronunciation for months but eventually speak more naturally.","zh":"學生可能數月來在發音上掙扎，但最終說得更自然。"},{"en":"Some questions become clearer eventually because evidence accumulates over time.","zh":"有些問題最終會變得更清楚，因為證據隨時間累積。"},{"en":"The word points to a later result.","zh":"這個詞指出較後出現的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"settle down","meaning":"逐漸穩定；明朗化","examples":[{"en":"Scientific debates may settle down as more evidence becomes available.","zh":"隨着更多證據出現，科學爭論可能逐漸明朗化。"},{"en":"To settle down means to become calmer, clearer, or more stable after uncertainty or activity.","zh":"settle down 指在不確定或活動之後變得較平靜、清楚或穩定。"},{"en":"A noisy class may settle down after the teacher gives a clear task.","zh":"當老師給出清晰任務，嘈雜班級可能安靜下來。"},{"en":"Debates settle down when enough evidence reduces disagreement.","zh":"當足夠證據減少分歧，爭論便會逐漸穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement from confusion toward stability.","zh":"這個短語描述由混亂走向穩定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be proven correct","meaning":"被證明正確","examples":[{"en":"Some theories are eventually proven correct.","zh":"有些理論最終被證明正確。"},{"en":"To be proven correct means to be shown by evidence to be accurate or true.","zh":"be proven correct 指由證據顯示為準確或真實。"},{"en":"A student’s answer may be proven correct when the teacher checks the calculation step by step.","zh":"當老師逐步檢查計算，學生的答案可能被證明正確。"},{"en":"Scientific claims are proven correct only when evidence supports them strongly enough.","zh":"科學主張只有在證據足夠有力支持時，才會被證明正確。"},{"en":"The phrase describes confirmation by evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述由證據作出的確認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be abandoned","meaning":"被放棄","examples":[{"en":"Unsupported theories may eventually be abandoned.","zh":"缺乏支持的理論最終可能被放棄。"},{"en":"To be abandoned means to be given up or no longer used.","zh":"be abandoned 指被放棄或不再使用。"},{"en":"A school may abandon a new timetable if it makes students more tired.","zh":"如果新時間表令學生更疲倦，學校可能放棄它。"},{"en":"Ideas are abandoned when evidence shows they do not work or cannot explain the facts.","zh":"當證據顯示想法無效或不能解釋事實，想法就會被放棄。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stopping support for something.","zh":"這個短語描述停止支持某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be absorbed into","meaning":"被納入……","examples":[{"en":"An older theory may be absorbed into a more comprehensive one.","zh":"較舊理論可能被納入一套更全面的理論。"},{"en":"To be absorbed into something means to become part of a larger system, theory, or organisation.","zh":"be absorbed into something 指成為更大系統、理論或組織的一部分。"},{"en":"A small school club may be absorbed into a larger student association.","zh":"小型學會可能被納入較大型學生會。"},{"en":"Older ideas are absorbed when a newer framework explains them and goes beyond them.","zh":"當新框架能解釋舊想法並超越它們，舊想法就會被納入其中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being included within something broader.","zh":"這個短語描述被包括在更廣泛事物之內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"more encompassing theories","meaning":"涵蓋範圍更廣的理論","examples":[{"en":"Some theories become part of more encompassing theories.","zh":"有些理論成為涵蓋範圍更廣的理論的一部分。"},{"en":"More encompassing theories are theories that cover a wider range of facts, cases, or situations.","zh":"more encompassing theories 指涵蓋更多事實、案例或情況的理論。"},{"en":"A broader school policy may become more encompassing when it covers homework, mental health, and assessment together.","zh":"當較廣泛的學校政策同時涵蓋功課、心理健康和評估，它就變得更全面。"},{"en":"More encompassing theories are useful because they explain both old evidence and new evidence.","zh":"涵蓋範圍更廣的理論很有用，因為它們能解釋舊證據和新證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes theories with wider explanatory power.","zh":"這個短語描述具有更廣解釋力的理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"problematic terminology","meaning":"容易引起問題的術語","examples":[{"en":"“Global warming” is an example of problematic terminology.","zh":"“全球暖化” 是容易引起問題的術語例子。"},{"en":"Problematic terminology means wording that can cause confusion, misunderstanding, or unfair debate.","zh":"problematic terminology 指可能造成混亂、誤解或不公平討論的用詞。"},{"en":"A hospital form with problematic terminology may scare patients because they do not understand the words.","zh":"使用容易引起問題術語的醫院表格，可能因病人不理解字詞而嚇到他們。"},{"en":"Terminology becomes problematic when ordinary meanings pull people away from the technical meaning.","zh":"當日常意思把人們拉離技術意思，術語就會變得有問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes words that create communication problems.","zh":"這個短語描述造成溝通問題的字詞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"climatologists","meaning":"氣候學家","examples":[{"en":"Climatologists study long-term changes in climate.","zh":"氣候學家研究氣候的長期變化。"},{"en":"Climatologists are scientists who study climate patterns, climate change, and long-term weather conditions.","zh":"climatologists 指研究氣候模式、氣候變化和長期天氣狀況的科學家。"},{"en":"A climatologist may compare temperature records from many decades to identify trends.","zh":"氣候學家可能比較數十年的氣溫記錄，以找出趨勢。"},{"en":"Climatologists help governments plan for floods, droughts, heatwaves, and sea-level rise.","zh":"氣候學家幫助政府規劃水災、乾旱、熱浪和海平面上升。"},{"en":"The word refers to climate scientists, not daily weather presenters.","zh":"這個詞指氣候科學家，而不是每日天氣主播。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"drastic fluctuations","meaning":"劇烈波動","examples":[{"en":"Climate change may cause more drastic fluctuations in weather.","zh":"氣候變化可能導致天氣出現更劇烈波動。"},{"en":"Drastic fluctuations are large, sudden, or extreme changes up and down.","zh":"drastic fluctuations 指大幅、突然或極端的上下變化。"},{"en":"A shop may suffer drastic fluctuations in sales if customers rush in during holidays but disappear afterward.","zh":"如果顧客在假期湧入但之後消失，小店銷售可能出現劇烈波動。"},{"en":"Fluctuations are harder to manage when they are extreme and unpredictable.","zh":"當波動極端且難以預測，它們就更難管理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sharp changes rather than steady movement.","zh":"這個短語描述急劇變化，而不是穩定移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"temperature and rainfall","meaning":"氣溫和降雨量","examples":[{"en":"Climate models predict changes in temperature and rainfall.","zh":"氣候模型預測氣溫和降雨量的變化。"},{"en":"Temperature and rainfall are two major climate measurements: heat level and the amount of rain.","zh":"temperature and rainfall 是兩個主要氣候測量項目：熱度水平和雨量。"},{"en":"Farmers watch temperature and rainfall because both affect when crops should be planted.","zh":"農民留意氣溫和降雨量，因為兩者都影響何時應種植作物。"},{"en":"Changes in temperature and rainfall can influence water supply, food production, and public health.","zh":"氣溫和降雨量的變化可以影響供水、糧食生產和公共健康。"},{"en":"The phrase names two key features of climate.","zh":"這個短語命名氣候的兩個關鍵特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not necessarily","meaning":"不一定","examples":[{"en":"Climate change does not necessarily make every location warmer.","zh":"氣候變化不一定令每個地方都變暖。"},{"en":"Not necessarily means not always or not in every case.","zh":"not necessarily 指不總是，或並非在每種情況下都如此。"},{"en":"A high exam score does not necessarily mean a student understands the subject deeply.","zh":"高考試分數不一定表示學生深入理解該科目。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when correcting overgeneralised statements.","zh":"這個短語適合用來修正過度概括的說法。"},{"en":"It reminds readers that a claim may be true in some cases but not all.","zh":"它提醒讀者，某主張可能在部分情況下成立，但不是全部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"subvert the debate","meaning":"扭曲討論","examples":[{"en":"An inaccurate name can subvert the scientific debate.","zh":"不準確名稱可以扭曲科學討論。"},{"en":"To subvert the debate means to undermine or distort discussion so it no longer focuses on the real issue.","zh":"subvert the debate 指削弱或扭曲討論，使其不再集中於真正問題。"},{"en":"A political slogan can subvert the debate about housing if it hides the actual causes of high rent.","zh":"如果政治口號掩蓋高租金的實際成因，它可以扭曲房屋討論。"},{"en":"Debate is subverted when language makes people argue about the wrong question.","zh":"當語言令人爭論錯誤問題，討論就被扭曲。"},{"en":"The phrase describes damaging the direction and quality of discussion.","zh":"這個短語描述損害討論方向和質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"argue that","meaning":"主張","examples":[{"en":"Some people argue that a cold winter disproves global warming.","zh":"有些人主張寒冷冬天證明全球暖化並不存在。"},{"en":"To argue that something is true means to state and support a claim with reasons.","zh":"argue that something is true 指提出並用理由支持某主張。"},{"en":"A student may argue that school should start later because teenagers need more sleep.","zh":"學生可能主張學校應較遲上課，因為青少年需要更多睡眠。"},{"en":"Arguments are stronger when they use evidence rather than one isolated example.","zh":"當論點使用證據而不是單一孤立例子，它會更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a claim someone wants others to accept.","zh":"這個短語引入某人希望別人接受的主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"global climate change","meaning":"全球氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"“Global climate change” is a more accurate description of the phenomenon.","zh":"“全球氣候變化” 是對該現象更準確的描述。"},{"en":"Global climate change refers to broad long-term changes in climate patterns across the Earth.","zh":"global climate change 指地球各地氣候模式的廣泛長期變化。"},{"en":"Global climate change can involve heatwaves, storms, droughts, rainfall shifts, and sea-level rise.","zh":"全球氣候變化可以涉及熱浪、風暴、乾旱、降雨轉變和海平面上升。"},{"en":"The term is clearer than “global warming” because it does not suggest that every place simply gets warmer.","zh":"這個詞比 “全球暖化” 更清楚，因為它不暗示每個地方只是變暖。"},{"en":"The phrase describes wider climate changes, not only temperature rise.","zh":"這個短語描述更廣泛的氣候變化，而不只是氣溫上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"stem solely from","meaning":"完全源自……","examples":[{"en":"Communication problems do not stem solely from poor word choices.","zh":"溝通問題並不完全源自差劣用詞。"},{"en":"To stem solely from something means to come only from that one cause.","zh":"stem solely from something 指只來自那一個原因。"},{"en":"A student’s poor performance may not stem solely from laziness; illness and stress may also matter.","zh":"學生成績差未必完全源自懶惰；疾病和壓力也可能有關。"},{"en":"Problems are often complex because several causes operate together.","zh":"問題通常複雜，因為幾個原因共同作用。"},{"en":"The phrase rejects an overly simple single-cause explanation.","zh":"這個短語否定過分簡化的單一成因解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"intrinsically complex nature","meaning":"本質上複雜的性質","examples":[{"en":"Modern science often has an intrinsically complex nature.","zh":"現代科學通常具有本質上複雜的性質。"},{"en":"An intrinsically complex nature means something is complex because of what it is, not because people explain it badly.","zh":"intrinsically complex nature 指某事因自身本質而複雜，而不是因人們解釋得不好。"},{"en":"Human health has an intrinsically complex nature because diet, sleep, genes, stress, and environment interact.","zh":"人類健康具有本質上複雜的性質，因為飲食、睡眠、基因、壓力和環境會互相作用。"},{"en":"Some subjects remain complex even when teachers explain them clearly.","zh":"有些科目即使老師解釋清楚，仍然複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase describes complexity built into the topic itself.","zh":"這個短語描述內置於主題本身的複雜性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"transcend a limitation","meaning":"超越限制","examples":[{"en":"Clear evidence can sometimes transcend this communication limitation.","zh":"清楚證據有時可以超越這種溝通限制。"},{"en":"To transcend a limitation means to go beyond it or overcome its restricting effect.","zh":"transcend a limitation 指超越某限制，或克服其約束效果。"},{"en":"A strong diagram can transcend a language limitation when students do not share the same first language.","zh":"當學生母語不同，一幅有力圖表可以超越語言限制。"},{"en":"Some evidence is so clear that it helps people understand despite difficult terminology.","zh":"有些證據非常清楚，即使用語困難，也能幫助人理解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes overcoming a boundary or obstacle.","zh":"這個短語描述克服界限或障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"remarkably","meaning":"令人驚訝的是","examples":[{"en":"Remarkably, chemists identified the process in precise detail.","zh":"令人驚訝的是，化學家精確而詳細地識別了該過程。"},{"en":"Remarkably means surprisingly or unusually in a way that deserves attention.","zh":"remarkably 指以令人驚訝或不尋常、值得注意的方式。"},{"en":"Remarkably, the quiet student gave the clearest speech in the competition.","zh":"令人驚訝的是，那位安靜學生在比賽中作出了最清晰演講。"},{"en":"Writers use this word when a result is impressive, unexpected, or worth noticing.","zh":"當結果令人印象深刻、出乎意料或值得注意，作者會使用這個詞。"},{"en":"The word signals that the following point is notable.","zh":"這個詞表示接下來的重點值得留意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"detail the precise chemical processes","meaning":"詳細說明精確的化學過程","examples":[{"en":"Chemists detailed the precise chemical processes involved.","zh":"化學家詳細說明所涉及的精確化學過程。"},{"en":"To detail the precise chemical processes means to explain the exact chemical steps, reactions, and substances in a process.","zh":"detail the precise chemical processes 指解釋某過程中的確切化學步驟、反應和物質。"},{"en":"A science teacher may detail the precise chemical processes that make bread rise.","zh":"科學老師可能詳細說明令麵包發起的精確化學過程。"},{"en":"Precise explanation matters because vague descriptions cannot show exactly what causes the result.","zh":"精確解釋很重要，因為模糊描述不能顯示究竟甚麼造成結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful step-by-step scientific explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細的逐步科學解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be involved in","meaning":"涉及……","examples":[{"en":"Several reactions are involved in ozone destruction.","zh":"臭氧破壞涉及幾種反應。"},{"en":"To be involved in something means to be part of a process, event, or activity.","zh":"be involved in something 指成為某過程、事件或活動的一部分。"},{"en":"Several teachers are involved in planning the school open day.","zh":"幾位老師參與籌備學校開放日。"},{"en":"Understanding what is involved in a process helps people see why the result happens.","zh":"理解某過程涉及甚麼，幫助人們看出結果為何發生。"},{"en":"The phrase shows participation or inclusion in a larger process.","zh":"這個短語顯示參與或包含於較大過程中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"destruction of the ozone layer","meaning":"臭氧層的破壞","examples":[{"en":"Certain gases contribute to the destruction of the ozone layer.","zh":"某些氣體促成臭氧層的破壞。"},{"en":"Destruction of the ozone layer means damage to the protective layer of ozone high in the atmosphere.","zh":"destruction of the ozone layer 指大氣高層保護性臭氧層受到損害。"},{"en":"Science lessons may explain the destruction of the ozone layer through diagrams of chemicals and sunlight.","zh":"科學課可能透過化學物和陽光的圖解來解釋臭氧層的破壞。"},{"en":"Ozone destruction is serious because it can allow more harmful radiation to reach Earth.","zh":"臭氧破壞很嚴重，因為它可以讓更多有害輻射到達地球。"},{"en":"The phrase describes environmental damage to an atmospheric shield.","zh":"這個短語描述對大氣保護屏障的環境破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ozone layer","meaning":"臭氧層","examples":[{"en":"The ozone layer protects the Earth from harmful radiation.","zh":"臭氧層保護地球免受有害輻射影響。"},{"en":"The ozone layer is a layer of ozone gas in the atmosphere that absorbs much of the Sun’s harmful ultraviolet radiation.","zh":"ozone layer 指大氣中由臭氧氣體組成、能吸收太陽大量有害紫外線的層。"},{"en":"Students may learn about the ozone layer when studying why sunscreen is important.","zh":"學生學習防曬為何重要時，可能認識臭氧層。"},{"en":"If the ozone layer is damaged, people, animals, and plants may face greater radiation risks.","zh":"如果臭氧層受損，人類、動物和植物可能面對更大輻射風險。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a protective atmospheric layer.","zh":"這個短語指一層具保護作用的大氣層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"chlorofluorocarbon gases","meaning":"氯氟碳化合物氣體","examples":[{"en":"Chlorofluorocarbon gases were shown to damage the ozone layer.","zh":"氯氟碳化合物氣體被證明會破壞臭氧層。"},{"en":"Chlorofluorocarbon gases are human-made chemicals once widely used in products such as refrigerants and aerosols.","zh":"chlorofluorocarbon gases 指曾廣泛用於製冷劑和噴霧產品等的人造化學物。"},{"en":"A textbook may mention chlorofluorocarbon gases when explaining why some older products were banned.","zh":"教科書解釋為何某些舊產品被禁止時，可能提到氯氟碳化合物氣體。"},{"en":"These gases became important in environmental debates because they could break down ozone high in the atmosphere.","zh":"這些氣體在環境討論中變得重要，因為它們可以在大氣高層分解臭氧。"},{"en":"The phrase names a group of chemicals linked to ozone damage.","zh":"這個短語命名一組與臭氧破壞有關的化學物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"indisputable evidence","meaning":"無可爭辯的證據","examples":[{"en":"The chemical evidence became indisputable.","zh":"化學證據變得無可爭辯。"},{"en":"Indisputable evidence is evidence so strong that it is very difficult to argue against.","zh":"indisputable evidence 指非常有力、難以反駁的證據。"},{"en":"Clear video footage can be indisputable evidence that a shop was closed at the time of the incident.","zh":"清晰錄像可以成為無可爭辯的證據，證明事發時商店已關門。"},{"en":"Evidence becomes indisputable when different tests and observations all support the same conclusion.","zh":"當不同測試和觀察都支持同一結論，證據便變得無可爭辯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes proof that leaves little room for serious doubt.","zh":"這個短語描述幾乎沒有嚴肅懷疑空間的證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"better understanding of","meaning":"對……有更深入理解","examples":[{"en":"A better understanding of statistics would improve scientific discussions.","zh":"對統計有更深入理解，會改善科學討論。"},{"en":"A better understanding of something means clearer, deeper, or more accurate knowledge about it.","zh":"better understanding of something 指對某事有更清晰、更深入或更準確的知識。"},{"en":"Students gain a better understanding of grammar when examples show real mistakes and corrections.","zh":"當例子展示真實錯誤和修正，學生會對文法有更深入理解。"},{"en":"Better understanding helps people judge claims instead of reacting only to headlines.","zh":"更深入理解幫助人們判斷主張，而不是只對標題作反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improved insight or knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述洞察或知識有所改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"mathematical significance","meaning":"結果在數學上的重要性","examples":[{"en":"The mathematical significance of results should be explained clearly.","zh":"結果在數學上的重要性應被清楚解釋。"},{"en":"Mathematical significance is the importance of results when judged through numbers, probability, or statistical reasoning.","zh":"mathematical significance 指透過數字、概率或統計推理判斷結果的重要性。"},{"en":"A small difference in test scores may have little mathematical significance if it could happen by chance.","zh":"如果測驗分數的小差異可能只是偶然，它在數學上可能沒有太大重要性。"},{"en":"Explaining mathematical significance helps people avoid overreacting to tiny differences.","zh":"解釋數學上的重要性幫助人們避免對微小差異反應過度。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what numbers actually mean in a study.","zh":"這個短語指研究中的數字實際代表甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"less insistence on","meaning":"減少堅持要求……","examples":[{"en":"Less insistence on a simple story would reduce distortion.","zh":"減少堅持要求簡單故事，會減少扭曲。"},{"en":"Less insistence on something means putting less pressure on demanding or forcing it.","zh":"less insistence on something 指減少要求或強迫某事的壓力。"},{"en":"Less insistence on perfect scores may help students focus more on real learning.","zh":"減少堅持要求滿分，可能幫助學生更集中於真正學習。"},{"en":"When people stop demanding oversimple answers, complex truth can be explained more honestly.","zh":"當人們停止要求過度簡化答案，複雜真相就能被更誠實地解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reducing pressure for one preferred approach.","zh":"這個短語描述減少對某一偏好方式的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"clarify scientific discussions","meaning":"釐清科學討論","examples":[{"en":"Clearer statistical explanations would clarify scientific discussions.","zh":"更清晰的統計解釋會釐清科學討論。"},{"en":"To clarify scientific discussions means to make scientific debates easier to understand and less confused.","zh":"clarify scientific discussions 指令科學辯論更容易理解、較少混亂。"},{"en":"A simple chart can clarify scientific discussions about air pollution levels in a city.","zh":"一幅簡單圖表可以釐清關於城市空氣污染水平的科學討論。"},{"en":"Discussions become clearer when evidence, uncertainty, and limits are explained directly.","zh":"當證據、不確定性和限制被直接解釋，討論會更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes removing confusion from science-related debate.","zh":"這個短語描述消除科學相關辯論中的混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"empty debates","meaning":"缺乏實質內容的辯論","examples":[{"en":"Harvard experienced months of largely empty debates about scientific ability.","zh":"哈佛經歷了數月關於科學能力、基本缺乏實質內容的辯論。"},{"en":"Empty debates are arguments with little real evidence, substance, or useful progress.","zh":"empty debates 指缺乏真正證據、內容或有用進展的爭論。"},{"en":"A class may have an empty debate if students repeat opinions without giving reasons.","zh":"如果學生只重複意見而不給理由，課堂可能出現空洞辯論。"},{"en":"Debates become empty when people care more about winning than understanding the evidence.","zh":"當人們更在乎取勝而不是理解證據，辯論就變得空洞。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises discussion that sounds active but teaches little.","zh":"這個短語批評聽起來活躍但幾乎沒有教益的討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"relative intrinsic abilities","meaning":"相對的先天能力","examples":[{"en":"The debate concerned the relative intrinsic abilities of men and women.","zh":"該辯論關乎男女相對的先天能力。"},{"en":"Relative intrinsic abilities are natural abilities compared between groups or individuals.","zh":"relative intrinsic abilities 指在群體或個人之間比較的自然能力。"},{"en":"A discussion about whether children are naturally better at music than adults would involve relative intrinsic abilities.","zh":"討論孩子是否天生比成年人更擅長音樂，會涉及相對先天能力。"},{"en":"Claims about intrinsic ability need strong evidence because social factors can also affect performance.","zh":"關於先天能力的主張需要有力證據，因為社會因素也可以影響表現。"},{"en":"The phrase compares supposedly natural capacities.","zh":"這個短語比較所謂自然具備的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"amusing aspect of","meaning":"……有趣的一面","examples":[{"en":"One amusing aspect of the debate was that both sides used the same evidence.","zh":"該辯論有趣的一面是雙方使用相同證據。"},{"en":"An amusing aspect of something is a part of it that is funny, ironic, or strangely interesting.","zh":"amusing aspect of something 指某事中有趣、諷刺或奇特的一面。"},{"en":"An amusing aspect of group work is that everyone wants leadership but no one wants to write the minutes.","zh":"小組工作有趣的一面是每個人都想領導，但沒有人想寫會議紀錄。"},{"en":"Something becomes amusing when expectations and reality do not match.","zh":"當期望與現實不一致，某事就會變得有趣。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a humorous or ironic feature.","zh":"這個短語指出幽默或諷刺的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"those who believed in","meaning":"相信……的人","examples":[{"en":"Those who believed in innate differences cited the same data.","zh":"相信先天差異的人引用了相同數據。"},{"en":"Those who believed in something means the people who accepted or supported that idea.","zh":"those who believed in something 指接受或支持某想法的人。"},{"en":"Those who believed in later school start times argued that teenagers need more sleep.","zh":"相信學校應較遲上課的人主張青少年需要更多睡眠。"},{"en":"A group’s belief shapes how it interprets evidence.","zh":"一個群體的信念會塑造其如何詮釋證據。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies people by the idea they support.","zh":"這個短語用所支持的想法來識別人群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"use the same evidence","meaning":"使用相同證據","examples":[{"en":"Both sides of the debate used the same evidence.","zh":"爭論雙方使用相同證據。"},{"en":"To use the same evidence means to rely on the same data, facts, or observations to support different claims.","zh":"use the same evidence 指依靠相同數據、事實或觀察來支持不同主張。"},{"en":"Two students may use the same evidence from a novel but reach different interpretations.","zh":"兩名學生可能使用同一本小說中的相同證據，但得出不同詮釋。"},{"en":"Evidence does not speak completely for itself because people may frame it differently.","zh":"證據不會完全自行說明一切，因為人們可能以不同方式框定它。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights how interpretation can differ even when data are shared.","zh":"這個短語突出即使數據相同，詮釋也可能不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"gender-specific spatial ability","meaning":"與性別相關的空間能力","examples":[{"en":"The discussion concerned possible gender-specific spatial ability.","zh":"討論關乎可能與性別相關的空間能力。"},{"en":"Gender-specific spatial ability means spatial skill that is claimed to differ by gender.","zh":"gender-specific spatial ability 指被聲稱會因性別而不同的空間技能。"},{"en":"A test of mental rotation may be used to study spatial ability in students.","zh":"心理旋轉測試可能用來研究學生的空間能力。"},{"en":"Claims about gender-specific ability are sensitive because social training and expectations may also shape results.","zh":"關於與性別相關能力的主張很敏感，因為社會訓練和期望也可能塑造結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a possible difference in spatial skills between genders.","zh":"這個短語描述性別之間可能存在的空間技能差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"how could that be?","meaning":"怎麼會這樣？","examples":[{"en":"Both groups used identical data, so how could that be?","zh":"兩組人使用完全相同數據，那怎麼會這樣？"},{"en":"How could that be? means how is that possible or how can this situation be explained?","zh":"how could that be? 指那怎麼可能，或這種情況如何解釋。"},{"en":"If two students studied the same notes but one failed badly, a teacher may ask, “How could that be?”","zh":"如果兩名學生讀同一份筆記，但其中一人嚴重不合格，老師可能問：「怎麼會這樣？」"},{"en":"The question is used when facts seem surprising or contradictory.","zh":"當事實看似令人驚訝或矛盾，便會使用這個問題。"},{"en":"The phrase invites explanation of an apparent puzzle.","zh":"這個短語邀請人解釋一個表面上的謎團。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"no substantial effects","meaning":"沒有顯著影響","examples":[{"en":"The data showed no substantial effects.","zh":"數據顯示沒有顯著影響。"},{"en":"No substantial effects means no large, meaningful, or important effects were found.","zh":"no substantial effects 指沒有發現大型、有意義或重要的影響。"},{"en":"A new study method may show no substantial effects if students’ scores remain almost the same.","zh":"如果學生分數幾乎沒有變化，新學習方法可能顯示沒有顯著影響。"},{"en":"A tiny difference may exist but still be too small to matter practically.","zh":"微小差異可能存在，但在實際上仍小到不重要。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that not every measured difference is important.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們，不是每個被量度到的差異都重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"social factors","meaning":"社會因素","examples":[{"en":"Social factors might explain the small observed differences.","zh":"社會因素可能解釋觀察到的小差異。"},{"en":"Social factors are influences from society, such as education, family expectations, culture, income, and opportunity.","zh":"social factors 指來自社會的影響，例如教育、家庭期望、文化、收入和機會。"},{"en":"A student’s exam performance may be affected by social factors like home support and access to tutoring.","zh":"學生考試表現可能受家庭支援和補習機會等社會因素影響。"},{"en":"Social factors matter because behaviour is not shaped by biology alone.","zh":"社會因素很重要，因為行為不只是由生物因素塑造。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to influences created by social life.","zh":"這個短語指由社會生活造成的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"account for","meaning":"解釋……的原因","examples":[{"en":"Social conditions might account for tiny differences in performance.","zh":"社會條件可能解釋表現上微小差異的原因。"},{"en":"To account for something means to explain why it happens or why it exists.","zh":"account for something 指解釋某事為何發生或存在。"},{"en":"Lack of practice may account for a student’s weak speaking score.","zh":"缺乏練習可能解釋學生口語分數低的原因。"},{"en":"A good explanation accounts for the evidence without ignoring inconvenient facts.","zh":"好解釋能說明證據，而不忽略不方便的事實。"},{"en":"The phrase means explain the cause of something.","zh":"這個短語意思是解釋某事的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tiny differences","meaning":"微小差異","examples":[{"en":"The study found only tiny differences between the groups.","zh":"該研究只發現兩組之間有微小差異。"},{"en":"Tiny differences are very small differences that may or may not matter.","zh":"tiny differences 指非常小、可能重要也可能不重要的差異。"},{"en":"Two essays may have tiny differences in wording but express the same main idea.","zh":"兩篇作文在用詞上可能有微小差異，但表達相同主旨。"},{"en":"Tiny differences should not be exaggerated unless evidence shows they have real consequences.","zh":"除非證據顯示微小差異有真實後果，否則不應誇大它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes differences that are small in size or importance.","zh":"這個短語描述在大小或重要性上都很小的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in any case","meaning":"無論如何","examples":[{"en":"In any case, the differences had an unclear scientific meaning.","zh":"無論如何，這些差異的科學意義並不清楚。"},{"en":"In any case means whatever the situation is, or regardless of the previous point.","zh":"in any case 指不管情況如何，或不論前一點怎樣。"},{"en":"The bus may be late; in any case, we should leave now to be safe.","zh":"巴士可能會遲；無論如何，為安全起見我們現在應該出發。"},{"en":"The phrase helps move to a conclusion even when earlier details remain uncertain.","zh":"即使之前細節仍不確定，這個短語也幫助轉向結論。"},{"en":"It often means “anyway” in a more formal style.","zh":"它常相當於較正式的 “anyway”。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unclear connection to","meaning":"與……的關係並不清楚","examples":[{"en":"The differences had an unclear connection to scientific ability.","zh":"這些差異與科學能力的關係並不清楚。"},{"en":"An unclear connection to something means the relationship with it is not obvious or well proven.","zh":"unclear connection to something 指與某事的關係不明顯或未被充分證明。"},{"en":"A student’s neat handwriting may have an unclear connection to her actual understanding of history.","zh":"學生字跡工整與她對歷史的實際理解之間，關係可能並不清楚。"},{"en":"If the connection is unclear, people should avoid drawing strong conclusions.","zh":"如果關係不清楚，人們應避免得出強烈結論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a weak or uncertain relationship.","zh":"這個短語描述薄弱或不確定的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"not much of a headline","meaning":"並非吸引人的新聞標題","examples":[{"en":"A finding of almost no difference is not much of a headline.","zh":"幾乎沒有差異的發現並非吸引人的新聞標題。"},{"en":"Not much of a headline means not dramatic, exciting, or attention-grabbing enough for news.","zh":"not much of a headline 指不夠戲劇化、刺激或吸引注意成為新聞標題。"},{"en":"“Students improved by one percent” is not much of a headline, even if it is accurate.","zh":"「學生成績提升百分之一」即使準確，也不是很吸引的標題。"},{"en":"Media may prefer dramatic claims because quiet findings attract less attention.","zh":"傳媒可能偏好戲劇化主張，因為平淡發現較少吸引注意。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why accurate results may be underreported.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何準確結果可能被較少報道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"when phrased that way","meaning":"以那種方式表述時","examples":[{"en":"The result seems less dramatic when phrased that way.","zh":"以那種方式表述時，結果看起來較不戲劇化。"},{"en":"When phrased that way means when expressed using those words or that style.","zh":"when phrased that way 指用那些字詞或那種風格表達時。"},{"en":"“You failed” sounds harsh; when phrased that way, feedback may hurt more than help.","zh":"「你失敗了」聽起來很刺耳；以那種方式表述時，回饋可能傷害多於幫助。"},{"en":"Wording changes impact because the same fact can sound dramatic, neutral, or reassuring.","zh":"用詞會改變影響，因為同一事實可以聽起來戲劇化、中性或令人安心。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how expression affects interpretation.","zh":"這個短語顯示表達方式如何影響詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"each type of science","meaning":"每一類科學","examples":[{"en":"Each type of science has its own communication difficulties.","zh":"每一類科學都有自身的溝通困難。"},{"en":"Each type of science means every scientific field or branch, such as physics, biology, chemistry, or climate science.","zh":"each type of science 指每個科學領域或分支，例如物理、生物、化學或氣候科學。"},{"en":"Each type of science needs different examples because students cannot learn genetics and astronomy in exactly the same way.","zh":"每一類科學都需要不同例子，因為學生不能以完全相同方式學遺傳學和天文學。"},{"en":"Communication problems differ because different fields use different evidence, methods, and terminology.","zh":"溝通問題各有不同，因為不同領域使用不同證據、方法和術語。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that science is not one single uniform subject.","zh":"這個短語強調科學不是單一而完全一致的科目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"source of complexity","meaning":"複雜性的來源","examples":[{"en":"Different scientific fields have different sources of complexity.","zh":"不同科學領域有不同的複雜性來源。"},{"en":"A source of complexity is something that makes a topic difficult, layered, or hard to explain.","zh":"source of complexity 指令主題困難、多層次或難以解釋的因素。"},{"en":"In school timetabling, one source of complexity is matching teachers, rooms, and student groups.","zh":"在學校排課中，其中一個複雜性來源是配對老師、課室和學生組別。"},{"en":"Identifying the source of complexity helps people explain a difficult issue more clearly.","zh":"找出複雜性的來源，幫助人們更清楚解釋困難議題。"},{"en":"The phrase points to where difficulty comes from.","zh":"這個短語指出困難來自哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"potential for miscommunication","meaning":"引起誤解的可能性","examples":[{"en":"Complex subjects create considerable potential for miscommunication.","zh":"複雜主題造成相當大的誤解可能性。"},{"en":"Potential for miscommunication means the possibility that people may misunderstand one another.","zh":"potential for miscommunication 指人們可能互相誤解的可能性。"},{"en":"Group projects have potential for miscommunication if roles and deadlines are not clearly written.","zh":"如果角色和限期沒有清楚寫下，小組項目就有引起誤解的可能性。"},{"en":"Miscommunication becomes more likely when a topic uses specialised words or uncertain evidence.","zh":"當主題使用專門詞彙或不確定證據，誤解更容易出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the risk of unclear communication.","zh":"這個短語描述溝通不清的風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take steps to","meaning":"採取措施去……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists and the public can take steps to improve communication.","zh":"科學家和公眾可以採取措施去改善溝通。"},{"en":"To take steps to do something means to begin practical actions to achieve it.","zh":"take steps to do something 指開始採取實際行動去達成某事。"},{"en":"A student can take steps to improve writing by reading feedback and rewriting weak sentences.","zh":"學生可以透過閱讀回饋並重寫薄弱句子，採取措施改善寫作。"},{"en":"Problems improve when people move from complaining to taking concrete action.","zh":"當人們由抱怨轉向採取具體行動，問題就會改善。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active effort toward a goal.","zh":"這個短語描述朝目標作出的主動努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"improve public understanding","meaning":"提升公眾理解","examples":[{"en":"Clear explanations can improve public understanding of science.","zh":"清晰解釋可以提升公眾對科學的理解。"},{"en":"To improve public understanding means to help ordinary people understand a topic more clearly and accurately.","zh":"improve public understanding 指幫助普通人更清楚、更準確理解某主題。"},{"en":"A city can improve public understanding of recycling by using simple posters and school talks.","zh":"城市可以透過簡單海報和學校講座提升公眾對回收的理解。"},{"en":"Public understanding improves when experts explain evidence, limits, and practical effects.","zh":"當專家解釋證據、限制和實際影響，公眾理解就會提升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes raising the general level of knowledge in society.","zh":"這個短語描述提高社會一般知識水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in all cases","meaning":"在所有情況下","examples":[{"en":"General communication principles can help in all cases.","zh":"一般溝通原則在所有情況下都有幫助。"},{"en":"In all cases means in every situation or example being discussed.","zh":"in all cases 指在所討論的每一種情況或例子中。"},{"en":"In all cases, students should read the question carefully before answering.","zh":"在所有情況下，學生回答前都應仔細閱讀題目。"},{"en":"A principle is more useful when it works across many different situations.","zh":"當一項原則適用於許多不同情況，它就更有用。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses universal application.","zh":"這個短語強調普遍適用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"inculcate greater understanding","meaning":"灌輸更深入的理解","examples":[{"en":"Education can inculcate greater understanding of scientific evidence.","zh":"教育可以灌輸對科學證據更深入的理解。"},{"en":"To inculcate greater understanding means to teach or build deeper understanding gradually and repeatedly.","zh":"inculcate greater understanding 指透過逐步和反覆教學，建立更深理解。"},{"en":"Schools can inculcate greater understanding of online safety through regular lessons and real examples.","zh":"學校可以透過定期課堂和真實例子，灌輸對網上安全更深入的理解。"},{"en":"Understanding grows when learners meet the idea many times in clear, meaningful contexts.","zh":"當學習者多次在清晰而有意義的語境中接觸概念，理解就會增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful long-term teaching.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細而長期的教導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"acceptance of","meaning":"對……的接受","examples":[{"en":"The public needs greater acceptance of indirect scientific evidence.","zh":"公眾需要更能接受間接科學證據。"},{"en":"Acceptance of something means willingness to recognise it as valid, useful, or true.","zh":"acceptance of something 指願意承認某事有效、有用或真實。"},{"en":"Acceptance of online medical appointments increased when patients found them convenient.","zh":"當病人發現網上診症方便，對它的接受程度便增加。"},{"en":"Acceptance grows when people understand why something is reliable.","zh":"當人們理解某事為何可靠，接受程度就會提高。"},{"en":"The phrase describes willingness to trust or recognise something.","zh":"這個短語描述願意信任或承認某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"indirect scientific evidence","meaning":"間接科學證據","examples":[{"en":"Indirect scientific evidence can still be highly reliable.","zh":"間接科學證據仍然可以非常可靠。"},{"en":"Indirect scientific evidence is evidence that supports a conclusion without being direct personal observation.","zh":"indirect scientific evidence 指不是直接親身觀察，但仍支持結論的證據。"},{"en":"Footprints are indirect evidence that someone walked through a wet corridor.","zh":"腳印是有人走過濕走廊的間接證據。"},{"en":"Indirect evidence can be powerful when many independent signs point to the same conclusion.","zh":"當許多獨立跡象指向同一結論，間接證據可以非常有力。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds readers that evidence need not be seen directly to be useful.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者，證據不必被直接看見才有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"unmanned space mission","meaning":"無人太空任務","examples":[{"en":"An unmanned space mission can collect legitimate scientific information.","zh":"無人太空任務可以收集合理可信的科學資訊。"},{"en":"An unmanned space mission is a space mission that uses machines or probes without astronauts on board.","zh":"unmanned space mission 指使用機器或探測器、沒有太空人登上的太空任務。"},{"en":"A robot sent to Mars is an unmanned space mission if no human travels with it.","zh":"如果沒有真人同行，送往火星的機械人就是無人太空任務。"},{"en":"Unmanned missions can be safer and cheaper when conditions are too dangerous for humans.","zh":"當環境對人類太危險，無人任務可以更安全和更便宜。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to space exploration carried out without a human crew.","zh":"這個短語指沒有載人團隊的太空探索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no less legitimate than","meaning":"與……同樣合理可信","examples":[{"en":"Data from an unmanned mission is no less legitimate than data collected by astronauts.","zh":"無人任務取得的數據與太空人收集的數據同樣合理可信。"},{"en":"No less legitimate than means just as valid, proper, or acceptable as something else.","zh":"no less legitimate than 指與另一事物同樣有效、合適或可接受。"},{"en":"Online learning records are no less legitimate than paper attendance records if the system is reliable.","zh":"如果系統可靠，網上學習記錄與紙本出席記錄同樣合理可信。"},{"en":"A source should be judged by quality, not by whether it feels traditional.","zh":"來源應按質素判斷，而不是按它是否感覺傳統。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly states equal validity.","zh":"這個短語強烈表明同等有效性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"on board","meaning":"在交通工具上","examples":[{"en":"A crewed mission has people on board the spacecraft.","zh":"載人任務有真人在太空船上。"},{"en":"On board means inside or travelling in a vehicle, ship, aircraft, or spacecraft.","zh":"on board 指在車輛、船、飛機或太空船內，或正乘坐其中。"},{"en":"Students must be on board the school bus before it leaves at 8 a.m.","zh":"學生必須在早上八時校巴開出前上車。"},{"en":"Having people on board changes safety needs because human life must be protected.","zh":"有人在交通工具上會改變安全需要，因為必須保護人命。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being physically inside a transport vehicle.","zh":"這個短語描述身處交通工具內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"question an interpretation","meaning":"質疑某種詮釋","examples":[{"en":"Scientists should remain willing to question an interpretation.","zh":"科學家應保持願意質疑某種詮釋。"},{"en":"To question an interpretation means to doubt, examine, or test one way of explaining evidence.","zh":"question an interpretation 指懷疑、檢查或測試某種解釋證據的方法。"},{"en":"A literature student may question an interpretation of a poem if another line suggests the opposite.","zh":"如果詩中另一句暗示相反意思，文學學生可能質疑某種詮釋。"},{"en":"Science improves when researchers test interpretations instead of accepting them too quickly.","zh":"當研究人員測試詮釋，而不是太快接受它們，科學便會進步。"},{"en":"The phrase describes critical examination of meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述對意思作批判性檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"equate A with B","meaning":"把A等同於B","examples":[{"en":"People should not equate indirect evidence with blind belief.","zh":"人們不應把間接證據等同於盲目信念。"},{"en":"To equate A with B means to treat two things as the same, even though they may be different.","zh":"equate A with B 指把兩件可能不同的事物視為相同。"},{"en":"Parents should not equate high marks with real happiness.","zh":"家長不應把高分等同於真正快樂。"},{"en":"Equating different things can create unfair judgments and poor decisions.","zh":"把不同事物等同起來，可能造成不公平判斷和差劣決定。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against treating unlike things as identical.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們不要把不同事物視為完全相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"blind belief","meaning":"盲目信念","examples":[{"en":"Scientific evidence should not be confused with blind belief.","zh":"科學證據不應與盲目信念混淆。"},{"en":"Blind belief is belief without evidence, questioning, or careful thought.","zh":"blind belief 指沒有證據、質疑或仔細思考的信念。"},{"en":"Buying a product only because an influencer praises it can be blind belief.","zh":"只因網紅稱讚就購買產品，可能是盲目信念。"},{"en":"Blind belief is risky because it can make people accept false claims too easily.","zh":"盲目信念有風險，因為它會令人太容易接受虛假主張。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts unsupported belief with evidence-based judgment.","zh":"這個短語把缺乏支持的信念與證據本位判斷作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"different standards for evaluating","meaning":"評估……的不同標準","examples":[{"en":"Different research areas may require different standards for evaluating evidence.","zh":"不同研究領域可能需要不同標準來評估證據。"},{"en":"Different standards for evaluating something are different rules or criteria used to judge it.","zh":"different standards for evaluating something 指用來判斷某事的不同規則或準則。"},{"en":"A school may use different standards for evaluating essays, speeches, and science projects.","zh":"學校可能使用不同標準來評估作文、演講和科學項目。"},{"en":"Standards differ because different tasks produce different kinds of evidence.","zh":"標準不同，因為不同任務產生不同種類的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using suitable criteria for each context.","zh":"這個短語描述為每個語境使用合適準則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"urgent policy implications","meaning":"迫切的政策影響","examples":[{"en":"Some scientific research has urgent policy implications.","zh":"有些科學研究有迫切的政策影響。"},{"en":"Urgent policy implications are important effects that require governments or institutions to consider action soon.","zh":"urgent policy implications 指需要政府或機構盡快考慮行動的重要影響。"},{"en":"Research showing unsafe drinking water has urgent policy implications for public health officials.","zh":"顯示飲用水不安全的研究，對公共衛生官員有迫切的政策影響。"},{"en":"Findings become urgent when delay could cause harm, cost, or public risk.","zh":"當延誤可能造成傷害、成本或公共風險，研究發現就變得迫切。"},{"en":"The phrase links research results with immediate policy decisions.","zh":"這個短語把研究結果與即時政策決定連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"purely theoretical value","meaning":"純理論價值","examples":[{"en":"Other research may have mainly theoretical value.","zh":"其他研究可能主要具有純理論價值。"},{"en":"Purely theoretical value means importance for ideas, understanding, or models rather than immediate practical use.","zh":"purely theoretical value 指對概念、理解或模型的重要性，而不是即時實際用途。"},{"en":"A maths discovery may have purely theoretical value at first before anyone finds an application.","zh":"數學發現一開始可能只有純理論價值，直到有人找到應用。"},{"en":"Theoretical value still matters because today’s abstract idea can become tomorrow’s technology.","zh":"理論價值仍然重要，因為今天的抽象想法可以成為明天的科技。"},{"en":"The phrase describes intellectual importance rather than direct practical benefit.","zh":"這個短語描述思想上的重要性，而不是直接實際好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be certain about","meaning":"對……有把握","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are not always certain about their predictions.","zh":"科學家並不總是對自己的預測有把握。"},{"en":"To be certain about something means to feel or know that it is definitely true or will definitely happen.","zh":"be certain about something 指感到或知道某事肯定真實或肯定會發生。"},{"en":"A student may not be certain about an answer if two options look similar.","zh":"如果兩個選項看似相似，學生可能對答案沒有把握。"},{"en":"Uncertainty is normal when evidence is incomplete or the situation is complex.","zh":"當證據不完整或情況複雜，不確定是正常的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes confidence in knowledge or prediction.","zh":"這個短語描述對知識或預測的信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"not necessarily mean","meaning":"不一定表示","examples":[{"en":"Uncertainty does not necessarily mean that the results are unimportant.","zh":"不確定並不一定表示結果不重要。"},{"en":"Does not necessarily mean means does not always prove, show, or imply.","zh":"does not necessarily mean 指不一定證明、顯示或暗示某事。"},{"en":"A quiet student does not necessarily mean a weak student.","zh":"安靜的學生不一定表示是能力弱的學生。"},{"en":"This phrase prevents people from jumping to an oversimplified conclusion.","zh":"這個短語防止人們跳到過度簡化的結論。"},{"en":"It shows that one fact does not automatically lead to another.","zh":"它顯示一個事實不會自動導向另一個事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"find nothing substantial","meaning":"沒有發現任何實質結果","examples":[{"en":"Uncertain findings may still reveal something substantial.","zh":"不確定的發現仍可能揭示某些實質內容。"},{"en":"To find nothing substantial means to discover no meaningful, important, or strong result.","zh":"find nothing substantial 指沒有發現有意義、重要或有力的結果。"},{"en":"A survey may find nothing substantial if students’ opinions are almost evenly split and no pattern appears.","zh":"如果學生意見幾乎平均分裂且沒有模式，調查可能沒有發現任何實質結果。"},{"en":"Even when researchers find little, that result can still prevent people from exaggerating a claim.","zh":"即使研究人員發現很少，該結果仍可防止人們誇大某主張。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the absence of a strong finding.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏有力發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be more open about","meaning":"更坦率地說明……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists should be more open about the statistical strength of their findings.","zh":"科學家應更坦率地說明其研究發現在統計上的力度。"},{"en":"To be more open about something means to explain it more honestly, clearly, and directly.","zh":"be more open about something 指更誠實、清楚和直接地解釋某事。"},{"en":"Schools should be more open about how homework affects students’ sleep.","zh":"學校應更坦率地說明功課如何影響學生睡眠。"},{"en":"Openness builds trust because people can see both strengths and limits.","zh":"坦誠會建立信任，因為人們能看見優點和限制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes greater transparency.","zh":"這個短語描述更高透明度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"treat mathematics as scary","meaning":"把數學視為可怕的東西","examples":[{"en":"The public should not treat mathematics as quite so scary.","zh":"公眾不應把數學視為那麼可怕的東西。"},{"en":"To treat mathematics as scary means to think of maths as frightening, impossible, or only for experts.","zh":"treat mathematics as scary 指把數學想成令人害怕、不可能理解或只有專家才能處理的東西。"},{"en":"Some students treat mathematics as scary because they remember being embarrassed by mistakes.","zh":"有些學生把數學視為可怕，是因為記得曾因錯誤而尷尬。"},{"en":"Maths becomes less frightening when teachers connect numbers with daily decisions.","zh":"當老師把數字與日常決定連起來，數學會變得較不可怕。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises fear of mathematics.","zh":"這個短語批評對數學的恐懼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"statistics and errors","meaning":"統計數據及誤差","examples":[{"en":"Statistics and errors help scientists interpret measurements.","zh":"統計數據及誤差幫助科學家詮釋測量結果。"},{"en":"Statistics and errors are numerical tools that show patterns, uncertainty, and possible differences between measured and true values.","zh":"statistics and errors 指顯示模式、不確定性，以及測量值與真實值可能差距的數字工具。"},{"en":"A teacher may use statistics and errors to explain why one test score does not tell the whole story.","zh":"老師可能使用統計數據及誤差來解釋為何一次測驗分數不能說明全部。"},{"en":"Understanding errors prevents people from treating every number as perfectly exact.","zh":"理解誤差能防止人們把每個數字都視為完全精確。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to tools for judging evidence carefully.","zh":"這個短語指謹慎判斷證據的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"uncertainty in a measurement","meaning":"測量中的不確定性","examples":[{"en":"Error values show the uncertainty in a measurement.","zh":"誤差值顯示測量中的不確定性。"},{"en":"Uncertainty in a measurement is the range of possible error or doubt around a measured value.","zh":"uncertainty in a measurement 指圍繞某測量值的可能誤差或疑問範圍。"},{"en":"A bathroom scale may show uncertainty in a measurement if it gives slightly different weights each time.","zh":"如果浴室磅每次給出略有不同的體重，它就顯示測量中的不確定性。"},{"en":"Measurement uncertainty matters because decisions based on tiny differences may be unreliable.","zh":"測量不確定性很重要，因為基於微小差異的決定可能不可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how exact or inexact a measurement is.","zh":"這個短語描述測量有多精確或不精確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"give someone the tools to","meaning":"為某人提供……的工具","examples":[{"en":"Statistics give the public the tools to evaluate claims.","zh":"統計為公眾提供評估主張的工具。"},{"en":"To give someone the tools to do something means to provide the knowledge, skills, or methods needed for it.","zh":"give someone the tools to do something 指提供做某事所需的知識、技能或方法。"},{"en":"Reading practice gives students the tools to understand difficult exam passages.","zh":"閱讀練習為學生提供理解困難考試篇章的工具。"},{"en":"People make better judgments when they have tools for checking evidence instead of relying on feelings.","zh":"當人們有工具檢查證據，而不是依賴感覺，他們會作出更好判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes equipping someone to act or think effectively.","zh":"這個短語描述裝備某人有效行動或思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"evaluate developments fairly","meaning":"公平評估新發展","examples":[{"en":"Statistical knowledge helps people evaluate new developments fairly.","zh":"統計知識幫助人們公平評估新發展。"},{"en":"To evaluate developments fairly means to judge new changes or discoveries using balanced evidence rather than fear or excitement.","zh":"evaluate developments fairly 指用平衡證據，而不是恐懼或興奮，來判斷新變化或新發現。"},{"en":"Parents should evaluate new education apps fairly by checking both benefits and limits.","zh":"家長應透過檢查好處和限制，公平評估新教育應用程式。"},{"en":"Fair evaluation prevents people from accepting hype or rejecting useful ideas too quickly.","zh":"公平評估能防止人們太快接受炒作或拒絕有用想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes balanced judgment of new progress.","zh":"這個短語描述對新進展作平衡判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"most importantly","meaning":"最重要的是","examples":[{"en":"Most importantly, people must recognise that science can be complex.","zh":"最重要的是，人們必須意識到科學可以很複雜。"},{"en":"Most importantly introduces the point that matters more than the others.","zh":"most importantly 引入比其他重點更重要的一點。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “Most importantly, read the question before choosing an answer.”","zh":"老師可能說：「最重要的是，選答案前先讀題目。」"},{"en":"The phrase helps organise ideas by signalling the strongest priority.","zh":"這個短語透過標示最強優先事項來幫助組織想法。"},{"en":"It tells readers to pay special attention to the next point.","zh":"它告訴讀者要特別注意下一點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"recognise that","meaning":"意識到","examples":[{"en":"The public must recognise that scientific truth can be complicated.","zh":"公眾必須意識到科學真相可以很複雜。"},{"en":"To recognise that something is true means to accept or become aware of it.","zh":"recognise that something is true 指接受或意識到某事為真。"},{"en":"Students must recognise that improvement takes practice, not only talent.","zh":"學生必須意識到進步需要練習，而不只是天分。"},{"en":"Recognition matters because people cannot respond well to a fact they refuse to see.","zh":"意識很重要，因為人們如果拒絕看見事實，就無法好好回應它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes awareness and acceptance of a point.","zh":"這個短語描述對某一點的覺察和接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"accept only simple stories","meaning":"只接受簡單說法","examples":[{"en":"We risk misunderstanding science if we accept only simple stories.","zh":"如果我們只接受簡單說法，就有誤解科學的風險。"},{"en":"To accept only simple stories means to believe only easy explanations and reject complexity.","zh":"accept only simple stories 指只相信容易的解釋，並拒絕複雜性。"},{"en":"A student who accepts only simple stories about history may miss economic, social, and political causes.","zh":"只接受歷史簡單說法的學生，可能錯過經濟、社會和政治成因。"},{"en":"Oversimple stories feel comfortable, but they can hide important details.","zh":"過度簡化的說法令人舒服，但可能掩蓋重要細節。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against reducing complex truth to neat slogans.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們不要把複雜真相化約成整齊口號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"necessarily be distorted","meaning":"必然被扭曲","examples":[{"en":"A complex finding will necessarily be distorted if it is oversimplified.","zh":"如果複雜發現被過度簡化，它必然被扭曲。"},{"en":"Necessarily be distorted means must become twisted or inaccurate because of the conditions described.","zh":"necessarily be distorted 指由於所描述條件，必定變得被扭曲或不準確。"},{"en":"A long novel will necessarily be distorted if a student reduces it to one sentence.","zh":"如果學生把一部長篇小說縮成一句話，它必然被扭曲。"},{"en":"Oversimplification creates distortion because it removes the details that make the idea accurate.","zh":"過度簡化造成扭曲，因為它移除了令概念準確的細節。"},{"en":"The phrase shows an unavoidable negative result.","zh":"這個短語顯示無可避免的負面結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"subtle or complicated","meaning":"細微或複雜","examples":[{"en":"Many important scientific advances are subtle or complicated.","zh":"許多重要科學進展都是細微或複雜的。"},{"en":"Subtle or complicated means not obvious, simple, or easy to explain.","zh":"subtle or complicated 指不明顯、不簡單或不容易解釋。"},{"en":"A friendship problem can be subtle or complicated if no one clearly did one wrong thing.","zh":"如果沒有人明確做錯一件事，友誼問題可能很細微或複雜。"},{"en":"Subtle ideas require careful explanation because quick summaries may miss the real meaning.","zh":"細微概念需要仔細解釋，因為快速摘要可能錯過真正意思。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that needs patience and close attention.","zh":"這個短語描述需要耐性和細心注意的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be willing to","meaning":"願意去……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists should be willing to provide fuller explanations.","zh":"科學家應願意提供更完整解釋。"},{"en":"To be willing to do something means to be ready and open to doing it.","zh":"be willing to do something 指準備好並願意做某事。"},{"en":"A good classmate is willing to explain homework instructions to someone who was absent.","zh":"好同學願意向缺席的人解釋功課指示。"},{"en":"People cooperate better when they are willing to spend extra effort on clarity.","zh":"當人們願意為清晰多花努力，合作會更好。"},{"en":"The phrase describes readiness rather than being forced.","zh":"這個短語描述自願準備，而不是被強迫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"go the extra distance","meaning":"額外付出努力","examples":[{"en":"Scientists should go the extra distance to explain difficult findings.","zh":"科學家應額外付出努力去解釋困難發現。"},{"en":"To go the extra distance means to make extra effort beyond the basic requirement.","zh":"go the extra distance 指作出超出基本要求的額外努力。"},{"en":"A teacher goes the extra distance when she writes extra examples for students who are struggling.","zh":"當老師為有困難的學生寫額外例子，她就是額外付出努力。"},{"en":"Difficult ideas require extra effort because basic explanations may not be enough.","zh":"困難概念需要額外努力，因為基本解釋可能不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase praises additional effort to help others.","zh":"這個短語讚賞為幫助他人而多走一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"give proper explanations","meaning":"作出適當解釋","examples":[{"en":"Researchers should give proper explanations of complicated results.","zh":"研究人員應對複雜結果作出適當解釋。"},{"en":"To give proper explanations means to explain something fully, accurately, and clearly enough for the audience.","zh":"give proper explanations 指為受眾充分、準確而清楚地解釋某事。"},{"en":"A maths teacher gives proper explanations when she shows each step instead of only the final answer.","zh":"數學老師展示每一步，而不只是最終答案時，就是作出適當解釋。"},{"en":"Proper explanations prevent misunderstanding because they include reasons, limits, and examples.","zh":"適當解釋能防止誤解，因為它包括原因、限制和例子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes responsible and adequate explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述負責任而足夠的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be patient about","meaning":"對……更有耐性","examples":[{"en":"The public should be more patient about complex scientific truth.","zh":"公眾應對複雜科學真相更有耐性。"},{"en":"To be patient about something means to accept that it takes time to understand, explain, or resolve.","zh":"be patient about something 指接受理解、解釋或解決某事需要時間。"},{"en":"Parents need to be patient about a child’s language development because fluency grows slowly.","zh":"家長需要對孩子語言發展更有耐性，因為流利度是慢慢增長的。"},{"en":"Patience matters when quick answers would be inaccurate or misleading.","zh":"當快速答案會不準確或具誤導性，耐性就很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes calm acceptance of difficulty or delay.","zh":"這個短語描述對困難或延遲的平靜接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"even so","meaning":"即使如此","examples":[{"en":"Even so, some communication difficulties are unavoidable.","zh":"即使如此，有些溝通困難仍無法避免。"},{"en":"Even so means despite what has just been said.","zh":"even so 指儘管剛才所說的情況如此。"},{"en":"The school gave clear instructions; even so, some students still went to the wrong room.","zh":"學校已給出清楚指示；即使如此，仍有些學生去了錯誤課室。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast or limitation after a positive point.","zh":"這個短語在正面重點後引入對比或限制。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing that a problem remains.","zh":"它適合用來顯示問題仍然存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be unavoidable","meaning":"無法避免","examples":[{"en":"Some misunderstandings may be unavoidable during early research.","zh":"在早期研究期間，有些誤解可能無法避免。"},{"en":"To be unavoidable means impossible to prevent completely.","zh":"be unavoidable 指完全不能防止。"},{"en":"Some noise is unavoidable when a school building is being repaired.","zh":"當學校建築正在維修，有些噪音是無法避免的。"},{"en":"Problems are unavoidable when a situation is new, uncertain, or changing quickly.","zh":"當情況新、不確定或快速改變，問題往往無法避免。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that cannot be fully escaped.","zh":"這個短語描述不能完全避開的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reflect work in progress","meaning":"反映尚在進行中的工作","examples":[{"en":"Most new scientific developments reflect work in progress.","zh":"大多數新科學發展反映尚在進行中的工作。"},{"en":"To reflect work in progress means to show that something is still being developed, tested, or improved.","zh":"reflect work in progress 指顯示某事仍在發展、測試或改善中。"},{"en":"A first draft of an essay reflects work in progress because ideas and wording may still change.","zh":"作文初稿反映尚在進行中的工作，因為想法和措辭仍可能改變。"},{"en":"Early research findings may change as scientists collect more data and refine methods.","zh":"隨着科學家收集更多數據和改進方法，早期研究發現可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds readers that the process is not finished yet.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者，過程尚未完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no one yet knows","meaning":"尚未有人知道","examples":[{"en":"The story remains complex because no one yet knows the full answer.","zh":"故事仍然複雜，因為尚未有人知道完整答案。"},{"en":"No one yet knows means nobody currently has the complete information or final answer.","zh":"no one yet knows 指目前沒有人擁有完整資訊或最終答案。"},{"en":"No one yet knows exactly how a new school policy will affect students after five years.","zh":"尚未有人確切知道新學校政策五年後會如何影響學生。"},{"en":"When no one yet knows the answer, honest communication should admit uncertainty.","zh":"當尚未有人知道答案，誠實溝通應承認不確定性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes present lack of complete knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述目前缺乏完整知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"big picture","meaning":"整體情況；全貌","examples":[{"en":"Scientists may not yet understand the big picture.","zh":"科學家可能尚未理解整體情況。"},{"en":"The big picture is the overall situation, pattern, or meaning rather than one small detail.","zh":"big picture 指整體情況、模式或意思，而不是單一細節。"},{"en":"A student may know many vocabulary words but still miss the big picture of a reading passage.","zh":"學生可能認識許多詞彙，但仍錯過閱讀篇章的全貌。"},{"en":"Understanding the big picture helps people connect details and avoid narrow conclusions.","zh":"理解全貌幫助人們連接細節，避免狹窄結論。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the whole view of a situation.","zh":"這個短語指對情況的整體視野。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生為每條題目選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option that matches the correct response.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇與正確答案相符的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should choose the correct letter only after checking the passage carefully.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應仔細檢查文章後才選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Careful matching prevents students from choosing an option that sounds right but is not supported.","zh":"仔細配對能防止學生選擇聽起來正確但沒有支持的選項。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard multiple-choice instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準選擇題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"faithful science communication","meaning":"準確的科學傳意","examples":[{"en":"Faithful science communication accurately represents research findings.","zh":"準確的科學傳意能準確呈現研究發現。"},{"en":"Faithful science communication means explaining science honestly and accurately without exaggeration or distortion.","zh":"faithful science communication 指誠實而準確地解釋科學，不誇大也不扭曲。"},{"en":"A health leaflet uses faithful science communication when it states both the benefits and side effects of a medicine.","zh":"當健康單張同時列出藥物好處和副作用，它就是使用準確的科學傳意。"},{"en":"Faithful communication builds trust because people can see the evidence and its limits.","zh":"準確傳意建立信任，因為人們能看見證據及其限制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes responsible public explanation of science.","zh":"這個短語描述負責任地向公眾解釋科學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"increasingly important","meaning":"日益重要","examples":[{"en":"Science communication is becoming increasingly important.","zh":"科學傳意正變得日益重要。"},{"en":"Increasingly important means becoming more important over time.","zh":"increasingly important 指隨時間變得更加重要。"},{"en":"Digital literacy is increasingly important because many services have moved online.","zh":"數碼素養日益重要，因為許多服務已轉到網上。"},{"en":"A skill becomes increasingly important when more people need it in daily life.","zh":"當更多人在日常生活中需要某技能，它就變得日益重要。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a rising level of importance.","zh":"這個短語顯示重要性正在上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"public interest in","meaning":"公眾對……的興趣","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to public interest in scientific challenges.","zh":"該選項指公眾對科學挑戰的興趣。"},{"en":"Public interest in something is the attention, curiosity, or concern ordinary people have about it.","zh":"public interest in something 指普通人對某事的注意、好奇或關注。"},{"en":"Public interest in mental health has grown as more students talk about stress openly.","zh":"隨着更多學生公開談論壓力，公眾對心理健康的興趣增加。"},{"en":"Strong public interest can push schools, media, and governments to explain an issue more clearly.","zh":"強烈公眾興趣可以推動學校、媒體和政府更清楚解釋議題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what the general public cares about.","zh":"這個短語描述一般公眾關心甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"nature of complexity","meaning":"複雜性的本質","examples":[{"en":"The nature of complexity can make science difficult to communicate.","zh":"複雜性的本質可以令科學難以傳達。"},{"en":"The nature of complexity means the basic character of being difficult, layered, or made of many connected parts.","zh":"nature of complexity 指困難、多層次或由許多相連部分組成的基本特性。"},{"en":"The nature of complexity in family problems is that money, emotions, and expectations often overlap.","zh":"家庭問題複雜性的本質在於金錢、情感和期望常互相重疊。"},{"en":"Complex topics are hard to explain because removing one detail may change the whole meaning.","zh":"複雜主題難以解釋，因為移除一個細節可能改變整體意思。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what complexity is like and why it matters.","zh":"這個短語指複雜性是甚麼樣子，以及為何重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"lead to confusion","meaning":"導致混亂","examples":[{"en":"Oversimplification can lead to confusion.","zh":"過度簡化可以導致混亂。"},{"en":"To lead to confusion means to cause people to become unsure or misunderstand the issue.","zh":"lead to confusion 指令人變得不確定或誤解議題。"},{"en":"Changing classroom rules without explanation can lead to confusion among students.","zh":"不作解釋就改變課室規則，可以導致學生混亂。"},{"en":"Confusion grows when information is incomplete, unclear, or contradictory.","zh":"當資訊不完整、不清楚或互相矛盾，混亂就會增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a cause of misunderstanding.","zh":"這個短語描述誤解的成因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"scientific inventions","meaning":"科學發明","examples":[{"en":"Scientific inventions can have a major impact on daily life.","zh":"科學發明可以對日常生活有重大影響。"},{"en":"Scientific inventions are new devices, methods, or technologies created through scientific knowledge.","zh":"scientific inventions 指透過科學知識創造的新裝置、方法或科技。"},{"en":"Vaccines, solar panels, and medical scanners are examples of scientific inventions.","zh":"疫苗、太陽能板和醫學掃描器都是科學發明的例子。"},{"en":"Inventions affect daily life when they change how people work, travel, communicate, or receive treatment.","zh":"當發明改變人們工作、旅行、溝通或接受治療的方式，它們就影響日常生活。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical creations based on science.","zh":"這個短語指以科學為基礎的實用創造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"biggest challenges for","meaning":"……面對的最大挑戰","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the biggest challenges for science reporting.","zh":"題目問科學新聞報道面對的最大挑戰。"},{"en":"The biggest challenges for someone are the most difficult problems they must deal with.","zh":"biggest challenges for someone 指某人必須處理的最困難問題。"},{"en":"One of the biggest challenges for new teachers is managing a noisy class calmly.","zh":"新老師面對的最大挑戰之一，是冷靜管理嘈雜班級。"},{"en":"Identifying the biggest challenges helps people decide where effort is most needed.","zh":"找出最大挑戰幫助人們決定最需要在哪裏付出努力。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the most serious difficulties.","zh":"這個短語指出最嚴重困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"phenomena such as","meaning":"……等現象","examples":[{"en":"Phenomena such as global warming are difficult to explain simply.","zh":"全球暖化等現象難以簡單解釋。"},{"en":"Phenomena such as something means events or processes of that kind, with one or more examples given.","zh":"phenomena such as something 指該類事件或過程，並給出一個或多個例子。"},{"en":"Phenomena such as traffic jams and air pollution show how city planning affects daily life.","zh":"交通擠塞和空氣污染等現象顯示城市規劃如何影響日常生活。"},{"en":"Examples help readers understand a broad category more concretely.","zh":"例子幫助讀者更具體理解一個廣泛類別。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces examples of a wider type.","zh":"這個短語引入較大類別中的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"totally comprehend","meaning":"完全理解","examples":[{"en":"Scientists may not yet totally comprehend a recent development.","zh":"科學家可能尚未完全理解一項近期發展。"},{"en":"To totally comprehend something means to understand it fully and deeply.","zh":"totally comprehend something 指充分而深入理解某事。"},{"en":"A student may not totally comprehend a poem after the first reading.","zh":"學生第一次閱讀後可能未能完全理解一首詩。"},{"en":"Full comprehension often requires time, background knowledge, and repeated analysis.","zh":"完全理解通常需要時間、背景知識和反覆分析。"},{"en":"The phrase means complete understanding.","zh":"這個短語意思是完整理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"meaning of a scientific development","meaning":"科學發展的意義","examples":[{"en":"The meaning of a scientific development may take years to become clear.","zh":"科學發展的意義可能需要多年才變得清楚。"},{"en":"The meaning of a scientific development is what a discovery or advance really shows, changes, or implies.","zh":"meaning of a scientific development 指某發現或進展真正顯示、改變或暗示甚麼。"},{"en":"The meaning of a new medical test may not be clear until doctors use it with many patients.","zh":"新醫學測試的意義可能要到醫生在許多病人身上使用後才清楚。"},{"en":"New developments can take time to interpret because early evidence may be incomplete.","zh":"新發展可能需要時間詮釋，因為早期證據可能不完整。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the wider significance of a scientific advance.","zh":"這個短語指科學進展的更廣泛重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"Theory of Evolution","meaning":"進化論","examples":[{"en":"The Theory of Evolution explains how species change over time.","zh":"進化論解釋物種如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"The Theory of Evolution is the scientific theory that living things change across generations through processes such as natural selection.","zh":"Theory of Evolution 指生物透過自然選擇等過程，跨世代改變的科學理論。"},{"en":"Students may study the Theory of Evolution through fossils, DNA, and examples of adaptation.","zh":"學生可能透過化石、DNA 和適應例子學習進化論。"},{"en":"The theory helps explain why different species share similarities and why they also differ.","zh":"該理論幫助解釋為何不同物種有相似之處，也有差異。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major biological theory, not a casual guess.","zh":"這個短語命名一套重要生物學理論，而不是隨意猜想。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"demonstrate that","meaning":"說明；證明","examples":[{"en":"The example demonstrates that terminology can mislead the public.","zh":"這個例子說明術語可以誤導公眾。"},{"en":"To demonstrate that something is true means to show it clearly through evidence, examples, or explanation.","zh":"demonstrate that something is true 指透過證據、例子或解釋清楚顯示某事為真。"},{"en":"A teacher may demonstrate that punctuation matters by showing two sentences with different meanings.","zh":"老師可能透過展示兩句意思不同的句子，說明標點很重要。"},{"en":"Examples demonstrate ideas by making abstract points visible and concrete.","zh":"例子透過令抽象重點變得可見和具體來說明概念。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces what evidence or an example shows.","zh":"這個短語引入證據或例子所顯示的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"common people","meaning":"一般大眾","examples":[{"en":"Non-specialists may misunderstand inaccurate scientific terminology.","zh":"非專家可能誤解不準確的科學術語。"},{"en":"Common people means ordinary members of the public rather than experts, rulers, or specialists.","zh":"common people 指普通公眾，而不是專家、統治者或專門人士。"},{"en":"A law should be written clearly enough for common people to understand their rights.","zh":"法律應寫得足夠清楚，讓一般大眾理解自己的權利。"},{"en":"Communication fails when experts speak as if common people already know technical background.","zh":"當專家說話時好像一般大眾已知道技術背景，溝通就會失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to ordinary people, though it can sound old-fashioned.","zh":"這個短語指普通人，但語氣可能較舊式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be misled by","meaning":"被……誤導","examples":[{"en":"The public may be misled by an inaccurate scientific phrase.","zh":"公眾可能被不準確的科學短語誤導。"},{"en":"To be misled by something means to be guided toward a wrong idea or conclusion by it.","zh":"be misled by something 指被某事引向錯誤想法或結論。"},{"en":"Customers may be misled by packaging that makes a snack look healthier than it is.","zh":"顧客可能被令零食看似更健康的包裝誤導。"},{"en":"People are misled when wording creates a false impression.","zh":"當用詞造成錯誤印象，人們就會被誤導。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being pushed into misunderstanding.","zh":"這個短語描述被推向誤解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"inaccurate choice of words","meaning":"不準確的用詞","examples":[{"en":"An inaccurate choice of words can distort scientific understanding.","zh":"不準確的用詞可以扭曲科學理解。"},{"en":"An inaccurate choice of words is wording that does not match the intended meaning closely enough.","zh":"inaccurate choice of words 指未能足夠貼近原意的措辭。"},{"en":"Calling a small disagreement a “war” is an inaccurate choice of words that may increase tension.","zh":"把小分歧稱為「戰爭」是不準確的用詞，可能增加緊張。"},{"en":"Wrong wording matters because people often remember the phrase more than the explanation.","zh":"錯誤用詞很重要，因為人們常記住短語多於解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes poor word choice that can mislead.","zh":"這個短語描述可能誤導人的差劣用詞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be designed to mislead","meaning":"被刻意設計來誤導","examples":[{"en":"Scientific terminology is not deliberately designed to mislead the public.","zh":"科學術語並不是被刻意設計來誤導公眾。"},{"en":"To be designed to mislead means to be intentionally created to make people believe something false.","zh":"be designed to mislead 指被有意創造出來，使人相信錯誤事情。"},{"en":"A fake discount sign may be designed to mislead shoppers about the real price.","zh":"虛假折扣標示可能被刻意設計來誤導顧客對真實價格的理解。"},{"en":"Some wording misleads by accident, while other wording is deliberately deceptive.","zh":"有些用詞是意外誤導，有些則是刻意欺騙。"},{"en":"The phrase describes intentional deception.","zh":"這個短語描述有意欺騙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"appropriate word choice","meaning":"恰當用詞","examples":[{"en":"Appropriate word choice can make complex science easier to understand.","zh":"恰當用詞可以令複雜科學更容易理解。"},{"en":"Appropriate word choice means selecting words that fit the meaning, audience, and context well.","zh":"appropriate word choice 指選擇能配合意思、受眾和語境的字詞。"},{"en":"A teacher uses appropriate word choice when she says “main idea” instead of “central thesis” for younger students.","zh":"老師對較年幼學生說 “main idea” 而不是 “central thesis” 時，就是使用恰當用詞。"},{"en":"Good word choice reduces confusion because it matches what listeners can understand.","zh":"良好用詞能減少混亂，因為它配合聽眾能理解的內容。"},{"en":"The phrase describes suitable and effective wording.","zh":"這個短語描述合適而有效的措辭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"destructive process","meaning":"破壞過程","examples":[{"en":"Chemists explained the destructive process affecting the ozone layer.","zh":"化學家解釋影響臭氧層的破壞過程。"},{"en":"A destructive process is a series of actions or reactions that damages or breaks something down.","zh":"destructive process 指一連串會損害或分解某物的行動或反應。"},{"en":"Rust is a destructive process that slowly damages metal gates and railings.","zh":"生鏽是會慢慢損害金屬閘門和欄杆的破壞過程。"},{"en":"Understanding a destructive process helps people stop or reduce the damage.","zh":"理解破壞過程幫助人們停止或減少損害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how damage happens step by step.","zh":"這個短語描述損害如何逐步發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"environmental damage","meaning":"環境破壞","examples":[{"en":"Certain gases can cause serious environmental damage.","zh":"某些氣體可以造成嚴重環境破壞。"},{"en":"Environmental damage is harm done to air, water, land, ecosystems, animals, or plants.","zh":"environmental damage 指對空氣、水、土地、生態系統、動物或植物造成的傷害。"},{"en":"Dumping waste into a river can cause environmental damage and threaten nearby communities.","zh":"把廢物倒入河流可以造成環境破壞，並威脅附近社區。"},{"en":"Environmental damage may last for years if pollution enters soil or water systems.","zh":"如果污染進入土壤或水系統，環境破壞可能持續多年。"},{"en":"The phrase describes harm to the natural environment.","zh":"這個短語描述對自然環境的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"surprising finding","meaning":"令人意外的發現","examples":[{"en":"The Harvard debate produced a surprising finding.","zh":"哈佛辯論產生了一個令人意外的發現。"},{"en":"A surprising finding is a result that people did not expect.","zh":"surprising finding 指人們沒有預期的結果。"},{"en":"A school survey may produce a surprising finding that students want more quiet study space than sports facilities.","zh":"學校調查可能產生令人意外的發現：學生想要更多安靜自修空間，多於運動設施。"},{"en":"Surprising findings are useful because they challenge assumptions.","zh":"令人意外的發現很有用，因為它們挑戰假設。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an unexpected result from research or discussion.","zh":"這個短語描述研究或討論中的意外結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"intrinsic scientific abilities","meaning":"先天科學能力","examples":[{"en":"The debate concerned possible differences in intrinsic scientific abilities.","zh":"該辯論關乎先天科學能力上可能存在的差異。"},{"en":"Intrinsic scientific abilities are natural or inborn capacities thought to affect scientific thinking or performance.","zh":"intrinsic scientific abilities 指被認為會影響科學思維或表現的自然或天生能力。"},{"en":"A discussion about whether mathematical talent is inborn concerns intrinsic ability.","zh":"關於數學天分是否天生的討論，涉及先天能力。"},{"en":"Claims about intrinsic ability need careful evidence because education and opportunity also shape achievement.","zh":"關於先天能力的主張需要仔細證據，因為教育和機會也塑造成就。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to supposedly natural scientific capacity.","zh":"這個短語指所謂自然具備的科學能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"both sides","meaning":"爭論雙方","examples":[{"en":"Both sides of the argument relied on the same evidence.","zh":"爭論雙方都依靠相同證據。"},{"en":"Both sides means the two opposing groups or viewpoints in a disagreement or debate.","zh":"both sides 指分歧或辯論中的兩個相對群體或觀點。"},{"en":"In a school uniform debate, both sides may care about students but disagree about freedom and discipline.","zh":"在校服辯論中，爭論雙方可能都關心學生，但在自由和紀律上意見不同。"},{"en":"Understanding both sides helps people judge an issue more fairly.","zh":"理解爭論雙方幫助人們更公平判斷議題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to two positions in a dispute.","zh":"這個短語指爭議中的兩個立場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"no significant difference","meaning":"沒有顯著差異","examples":[{"en":"The evidence showed no significant difference between the groups.","zh":"證據顯示兩組之間沒有顯著差異。"},{"en":"No significant difference means no difference large or reliable enough to matter scientifically or practically.","zh":"no significant difference 指沒有大到或可靠到在科學或實際上重要的差異。"},{"en":"Two teaching methods may show no significant difference if students perform almost the same after using them.","zh":"如果學生使用兩種教學方法後表現幾乎相同，兩者可能沒有顯著差異。"},{"en":"A small difference should not be exaggerated when statistics show it is not meaningful.","zh":"當統計顯示差異沒有意義，小差異不應被誇大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the absence of an important measurable gap.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏重要可測量差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"substantial figures","meaning":"具實質意義的數據","examples":[{"en":"The data did not provide substantial figures supporting the claim.","zh":"數據沒有提供支持該主張的具實質意義數字。"},{"en":"Substantial figures are meaningful numerical results large or reliable enough to support a point.","zh":"substantial figures 指大到或可靠到足以支持某觀點的有意義數字結果。"},{"en":"A school cannot claim success if it has no substantial figures showing better attendance or grades.","zh":"如果沒有顯示出席率或成績改善的實質數據，學校不能聲稱成功。"},{"en":"Strong claims need substantial figures rather than vague impressions.","zh":"強烈主張需要具實質意義的數據，而不是模糊印象。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to important supporting numbers.","zh":"這個短語指重要的支持性數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"clear connection","meaning":"明確關係","examples":[{"en":"No clear connection was found between the differences and scientific ability.","zh":"未發現這些差異與科學能力之間有明確關係。"},{"en":"A clear connection is an obvious or well-supported relationship between two things.","zh":"clear connection 指兩件事之間明顯或有充分支持的關係。"},{"en":"A teacher may find a clear connection between missing homework and low test scores.","zh":"老師可能發現欠交功課與低測驗分數之間有明確關係。"},{"en":"Without a clear connection, people should avoid claiming that one thing causes another.","zh":"如果沒有明確關係，人們應避免聲稱一件事導致另一件事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a relationship supported by evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述由證據支持的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與文章資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否與文章資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information means to match what the text says.","zh":"agree with the information 指與文本所說內容相符。"},{"en":"In a reading test, a statement agrees with the information if the passage clearly supports it.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，如果文章清楚支持某陳述，它就與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should check exact wording because an answer may sound right but not match the text.","zh":"學生應檢查確切措辭，因為答案可能聽起來正確，但不符合文本。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in true-false reading tasks.","zh":"這個短語用於判斷正誤的閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文章資料相反","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相反。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文本內容相反的意思。"},{"en":"If a passage says the meeting is on Monday, “the meeting is on Tuesday” contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說會議在星期一，「會議在星期二」就與資料相反。"},{"en":"Contradiction is different from missing information because the text clearly says something else.","zh":"矛盾不同於沒有資料，因為文本清楚說了另一回事。"},{"en":"The phrase is important in true-false-not-given questions.","zh":"這個短語在 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題中很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students write “NOT GIVEN” when the passage provides no relevant information.","zh":"當文章沒有提供相關資料，學生寫 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the text does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文本沒有說明該陳述是真還是假。"},{"en":"If an article says a scientist works in London but says nothing about her age, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文章說某科學家在倫敦工作，但沒有提及她的年齡，文中就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from general knowledge when the passage gives no evidence.","zh":"當文章沒有證據，學生不應根據常識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase signals a “not given” answer.","zh":"這個短語表示答案是 “NOT GIVEN”。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"scientifically refer to","meaning":"在科學上指……","examples":[{"en":"“Global warming” scientifically refers to broad climatic changes.","zh":"“全球暖化” 在科學上指廣泛的氣候變化。"},{"en":"To scientifically refer to something means to mean that thing in a scientific or technical sense.","zh":"scientifically refer to something 指在科學或技術意義上表示某事。"},{"en":"In biology, “fitness” scientifically refers to reproductive success, not gym strength.","zh":"在生物學中，“fitness” 在科學上指繁殖成功，而不是健身力量。"},{"en":"Scientific meanings can differ from everyday meanings, so definitions matter.","zh":"科學意思可以不同於日常意思，因此定義很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase clarifies the technical meaning of a term.","zh":"這個短語釐清術語的技術意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"greater fluctuations","meaning":"較劇烈的波動","examples":[{"en":"Climate change may involve greater fluctuations in temperature and rainfall.","zh":"氣候變化可能涉及氣溫和降雨量較劇烈的波動。"},{"en":"Greater fluctuations are larger changes up and down over time.","zh":"greater fluctuations 指隨時間出現更大幅度的上下變化。"},{"en":"A shop may see greater fluctuations in income during tourist seasons than during normal months.","zh":"小店在旅遊季節的收入波動可能比平常月份更劇烈。"},{"en":"Larger fluctuations make planning harder because future conditions become less stable.","zh":"較大波動令規劃更困難，因為未來情況變得較不穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stronger variation.","zh":"這個短語描述更強烈的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"universal temperature rise","meaning":"全球所有地區的氣溫上升","examples":[{"en":"Climate change does not mean a universal temperature rise in every location.","zh":"氣候變化不代表每個地方都出現全球所有地區的氣溫上升。"},{"en":"Universal temperature rise means temperature increasing everywhere without exception.","zh":"universal temperature rise 指氣溫在所有地方無一例外地上升。"},{"en":"A country may experience warming overall without every town showing a universal temperature rise every season.","zh":"一個國家整體可能變暖，但不代表每個城鎮每個季節都出現普遍升溫。"},{"en":"The phrase can mislead if people expect climate change to look identical in every place.","zh":"如果人們期待氣候變化在每個地方看起來完全一樣，這個短語可能誤導。"},{"en":"It describes an all-place increase, which is not the same as complex climate change.","zh":"它描述所有地方都上升，這不同於複雜的氣候變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"media coverage of","meaning":"對……的傳媒報道","examples":[{"en":"Media coverage of climate change can shape public understanding.","zh":"對氣候變化的傳媒報道可以塑造公眾理解。"},{"en":"Media coverage of something is the way newspapers, television, websites, and other media report it.","zh":"media coverage of something 指報紙、電視、網站和其他媒體報道某事的方式。"},{"en":"Media coverage of exam reform can influence how parents feel about the new system.","zh":"對考試改革的傳媒報道可以影響家長對新制度的感受。"},{"en":"Coverage shapes opinion because many people learn about issues through headlines and short reports.","zh":"報道會塑造意見，因為許多人透過標題和短報道認識議題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to public reporting by media organisations.","zh":"這個短語指傳媒機構的公共報道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"recognise the phenomenon","meaning":"認識該現象","examples":[{"en":"Clear evidence can help the public recognise the phenomenon.","zh":"清晰證據可以幫助公眾認識該現象。"},{"en":"To recognise the phenomenon means to understand that the event or pattern exists and identify what it is.","zh":"recognise the phenomenon 指理解某事件或模式存在，並識別它是甚麼。"},{"en":"Photos of repeated flooding can help residents recognise the phenomenon of rising flood risk.","zh":"反覆水浸的照片可以幫助居民認識洪水風險上升這一現象。"},{"en":"People recognise a phenomenon more easily when examples connect it with real experience.","zh":"當例子把現象與真實經驗連起來，人們更容易認識它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes awareness of a visible or measurable pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述對可見或可量度模式的覺察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"focus more on","meaning":"更集中於……","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that the debate should focus more on individual scientists.","zh":"該選項暗示辯論應更集中於個別科學家。"},{"en":"To focus more on something means to give it greater attention than before or than other things.","zh":"focus more on something 指比以前或比其他事物給予某事更多注意。"},{"en":"A student should focus more on grammar accuracy if repeated mistakes lower her writing score.","zh":"如果反覆錯誤拉低寫作分數，學生應更集中於文法準確度。"},{"en":"Focusing more on the wrong issue can pull attention away from the real problem.","zh":"更集中於錯誤議題會把注意力從真正問題拉走。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shifting attention toward one area.","zh":"這個短語描述把注意力轉向某一範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"female and male scientists","meaning":"女性及男性科學家","examples":[{"en":"The debate concerned claims about female and male scientists.","zh":"該辯論關乎有關女性及男性科學家的主張。"},{"en":"Female and male scientists are women and men who work in scientific research or scientific professions.","zh":"female and male scientists 指從事科學研究或科學專業工作的女性和男性。"},{"en":"A university may study whether female and male scientists receive equal promotion opportunities.","zh":"大學可能研究女性及男性科學家是否獲得平等晉升機會。"},{"en":"Discussions about scientists by gender require careful evidence to avoid stereotypes.","zh":"按性別討論科學家需要仔細證據，以避免刻板印象。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies scientists according to gender.","zh":"這個短語按性別識別科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"lead to confusion","meaning":"導致混亂","examples":[{"en":"Accepting reliable indirect evidence should not lead to confusion.","zh":"接受可靠的間接證據不應導致混亂。"},{"en":"To lead to confusion means to cause uncertainty, misunderstanding, or unclear thinking.","zh":"lead to confusion 指造成不確定、誤解或思路不清。"},{"en":"Unclear exam instructions can lead to confusion even among well-prepared students.","zh":"不清楚的考試指示即使對準備充分的學生也會導致混亂。"},{"en":"Confusion can be avoided when key terms and limits are explained carefully.","zh":"當關鍵術語和限制被仔細解釋，混亂可以避免。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating misunderstanding or uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語描述製造誤解或不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill in missing words so the shortened version of the text makes sense.","zh":"complete the summary 指填入缺漏字詞，使文本的縮短版本意思完整。"},{"en":"In a reading exam, students complete the summary by locating matching ideas in the passage.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生透過在文章中定位相配想法來完成摘要。"},{"en":"Summary completion tests both understanding and careful attention to word limits.","zh":"摘要填充同時測試理解和對字數限制的細心。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個詞","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案應包含不多於兩個詞。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must use one or two words only.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案只能使用一個或兩個英文詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “global warming”, it follows the instruction because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “global warming”，它符合指示，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Students can lose marks if they write three words when only two are allowed.","zh":"如果只允許兩個詞而學生寫三個詞，就可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語設定嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"ambiguous word choices","meaning":"含糊的用詞","examples":[{"en":"Ambiguous word choices can distort scientific meaning.","zh":"含糊的用詞可以扭曲科學意思。"},{"en":"Ambiguous word choices are words that can be understood in more than one way.","zh":"ambiguous word choices 指可以用多於一種方式理解的字詞。"},{"en":"The instruction “finish soon” is ambiguous because students may not know whether it means today or this week.","zh":"“finish soon” 這個指示很含糊，因為學生可能不知道它指今天還是本週。"},{"en":"Ambiguous wording creates risk because different readers may choose different meanings.","zh":"含糊措辭造成風險，因為不同讀者可能選擇不同意思。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unclear word selection.","zh":"這個短語描述不清楚的選詞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"understand clearly or deeply","meaning":"清楚或深入理解","examples":[{"en":"Without training, people may not understand the terminology clearly or deeply.","zh":"沒有訓練，人們可能無法清楚或深入理解術語。"},{"en":"To understand clearly or deeply means to know both the basic meaning and the deeper reasons behind it.","zh":"understand clearly or deeply 指既知道基本意思，也理解其背後更深層原因。"},{"en":"A student may understand a formula clearly or deeply only after seeing how it is used in real problems.","zh":"學生可能只有在看到公式如何用於真實問題後，才清楚或深入理解它。"},{"en":"Deep understanding takes time because learners must connect facts, examples, and principles.","zh":"深入理解需要時間，因為學習者必須連接事實、例子和原則。"},{"en":"The phrase describes more than surface recognition.","zh":"這個短語描述不只是表面認識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"terminology scientists employ","meaning":"科學家使用的術語","examples":[{"en":"The terminology scientists employ may have specialised meanings.","zh":"科學家使用的術語可能有專門意思。"},{"en":"Terminology scientists employ means the technical words and phrases scientists use in their work.","zh":"terminology scientists employ 指科學家在工作中使用的技術詞語和短語。"},{"en":"The terminology doctors employ can confuse patients if it is not explained in everyday language.","zh":"如果醫生使用的術語沒有用日常語言解釋，可能令病人困惑。"},{"en":"Technical terminology helps experts be precise but can create barriers for the public.","zh":"技術術語幫助專家精確表達，但也可能為公眾製造障礙。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to specialist language used by scientists.","zh":"這個短語指科學家使用的專門語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"observer","meaning":"觀察者","examples":[{"en":"An observer makes measurements from a particular reference frame.","zh":"觀察者從特定參考系作出測量。"},{"en":"An observer is a person or instrument that watches, measures, or records an event.","zh":"observer 指觀看、測量或記錄事件的人或儀器。"},{"en":"In a classroom experiment, one observer may time the reaction while another records the result.","zh":"在課堂實驗中，一名觀察者可能計算反應時間，另一名則記錄結果。"},{"en":"Observers matter because where and how they observe can affect what they measure.","zh":"觀察者很重要，因為他們在哪裏和如何觀察，可能影響測量結果。"},{"en":"The word refers to someone or something collecting information.","zh":"這個詞指收集資訊的人或物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be confined to","meaning":"受限於……","examples":[{"en":"A physical description should not be confined to one observer’s coordinates.","zh":"物理描述不應受限於單一觀察者的坐標。"},{"en":"To be confined to something means to be limited within it.","zh":"be confined to something 指被限制在某範圍之內。"},{"en":"A discussion should not be confined to exam scores if student well-being also matters.","zh":"如果學生福祉也很重要，討論就不應只受限於考試分數。"},{"en":"Being confined to one viewpoint can hide wider patterns and better explanations.","zh":"受限於單一觀點可能掩蓋更廣泛模式和更好解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limitation to a narrow area, idea, or system.","zh":"這個短語描述被限制於狹窄範圍、想法或系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"constant reference frame","meaning":"固定參考系","examples":[{"en":"Measurements may be described within a particular reference frame.","zh":"測量可以在特定參考系內被描述。"},{"en":"A constant reference frame is a fixed system or viewpoint used to describe measurements consistently.","zh":"constant reference frame 指用來一致描述測量的固定系統或觀點。"},{"en":"A classroom map provides a constant reference frame when students describe where desks and doors are.","zh":"當學生描述課桌和門的位置，課室地圖提供固定參考系。"},{"en":"Fixed reference frames help people compare measurements without changing the rules halfway.","zh":"固定參考系幫助人們比較測量，而不會中途改變規則。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a stable system for describing position or motion.","zh":"這個短語指描述位置或運動的穩定系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"improve a theory","meaning":"改進理論","examples":[{"en":"Scientists may improve a theory as new evidence becomes available.","zh":"隨着新證據出現，科學家可能改進理論。"},{"en":"To improve a theory means to revise it so it explains evidence more accurately or completely.","zh":"improve a theory 指修訂理論，使它更準確或更完整地解釋證據。"},{"en":"A student can improve a theory about why plants grew slowly after checking sunlight and water levels.","zh":"學生檢查陽光和水分後，可以改進關於植物生長緩慢原因的理論。"},{"en":"Theories improve when weaknesses are found and corrected.","zh":"當弱點被發現並修正，理論就會改進。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strengthening an explanation through evidence and revision.","zh":"這個短語描述透過證據和修訂加強解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"better version of","meaning":"更完善的版本","examples":[{"en":"Einstein developed a better version of his theory over several years.","zh":"愛因斯坦多年來發展出其理論更完善的版本。"},{"en":"A better version of something is an improved form that is clearer, more accurate, or more effective.","zh":"better version of something 指更清楚、更準確或更有效的改良形式。"},{"en":"After teacher feedback, a student writes a better version of her introduction.","zh":"經老師回饋後，學生寫出引言更完善的版本。"},{"en":"Better versions appear when people revise weak parts and keep useful parts.","zh":"當人們修訂薄弱部分並保留有用部分，更好版本就會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improvement from an earlier form.","zh":"這個短語描述由早期形式改善而來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"specific theory","meaning":"某一特定理論","examples":[{"en":"A specific theory may change as research progresses.","zh":"隨着研究推進，某一特定理論可能改變。"},{"en":"A specific theory is one particular theory, not theories in general.","zh":"specific theory 指某一套特定理論，而不是泛指理論。"},{"en":"A science class may test a specific theory about why one plant grows faster than another.","zh":"科學課可能測試某一特定理論，解釋為何一株植物比另一株長得快。"},{"en":"Specific theories can be revised when new evidence does not fit them well.","zh":"當新證據與特定理論不太吻合，它們可以被修訂。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows attention to one defined explanation.","zh":"這個短語把注意力收窄到一個明確解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"recognise scientific complexity","meaning":"認識科學的複雜性","examples":[{"en":"People need to recognise scientific complexity.","zh":"人們需要認識科學的複雜性。"},{"en":"To recognise scientific complexity means to accept that scientific issues may have many parts, limits, and uncertainties.","zh":"recognise scientific complexity 指接受科學議題可能有許多部分、限制和不確定性。"},{"en":"Students recognise scientific complexity when they understand that diet, sleep, genes, and stress all affect health.","zh":"當學生明白飲食、睡眠、基因和壓力都會影響健康，他們就是在認識科學的複雜性。"},{"en":"Recognising complexity prevents people from demanding one-line answers to difficult questions.","zh":"認識複雜性能防止人們要求用一句話回答困難問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes awareness that science is often layered and difficult.","zh":"這個短語描述意識到科學往往是多層次而困難的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 22 - Communication in science.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 23":[{"front":"a leap into history","meaning":"躍進歷史","examples":[{"en":"A journey along this coastline feels like a leap into history.","zh":"沿着這條海岸線旅遊，感覺像躍進歷史。"},{"en":"A leap into history means an experience that suddenly makes the past feel close and vivid.","zh":"「a leap into history」指一種突然令過去變得貼近而鮮活的經歷。"},{"en":"Walking through an old village can feel like a leap into history when every street has a story.","zh":"走過古老村落時，如果每條街都有故事，就可能感覺像躍進歷史。"},{"en":"If a place preserves castles, legends, and old roads, visitors may feel transported into the past.","zh":"如果一個地方保存城堡、傳說和古道，遊客可能感到自己被帶回過去。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests more than learning facts; it suggests entering a historical atmosphere.","zh":"這個短語暗示的不只是學習史實，而是進入一種歷史氛圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lie between…and…","meaning":"位於……與……之間","examples":[{"en":"Some of Western Europe’s most captivating landscapes lie between Inishowen and the Glens of Antrim.","zh":"西歐一些最迷人的景觀位於 Inishowen 與安特里姆峽谷之間。"},{"en":"To lie between A and B means to be located in the space or area separating two places.","zh":"「lie between A and B」意思是位於兩個地方之間的空間或地區。"},{"en":"The school lies between the library and the sports centre, so students can reach both easily.","zh":"學校位於圖書館與體育中心之間，所以學生很容易到達兩處。"},{"en":"If a village lies between two tourist towns, travellers may pass through it on the way.","zh":"如果村莊位於兩個旅遊城鎮之間，旅客可能會在途中經過它。"},{"en":"The phrase is mainly used to describe location.","zh":"這個短語主要用來描述位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Inishowen Peninsula","meaning":"伊尼肖恩半島","examples":[{"en":"The Inishowen Peninsula lies north-west of Derry.","zh":"伊尼肖恩半島位於德里西北面。"},{"en":"The Inishowen Peninsula is a named land area that extends into the sea in north-west Ireland.","zh":"「Inishowen Peninsula」是一片伸入海中的具名土地，位於愛爾蘭西北部。"},{"en":"Travellers may visit the Inishowen Peninsula for coastal views, villages, and quiet roads.","zh":"旅客可能到伊尼肖恩半島欣賞海岸景色、村落和寧靜道路。"},{"en":"Because it is a peninsula, it is surrounded by water on several sides.","zh":"因為它是半島，所以幾面被海水包圍。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific geographical place, not a general type of landscape.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定地理地點，而不是一般地貌類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"north-west of","meaning":"在……西北面","examples":[{"en":"The peninsula is situated north-west of Derry.","zh":"該半島位於德里西北面。"},{"en":"North-west of a place means in the direction between north and west from that place.","zh":"「north-west of」某地，意思是從該地看向北與西之間的方向。"},{"en":"The hospital is north-west of the train station, so you should turn left after the main road.","zh":"醫院在火車站西北面，所以你過了大路後應該左轉。"},{"en":"If a storm moves north-west of the city, the city may escape the worst weather.","zh":"如果風暴移到城市西北面，城市可能避過最惡劣天氣。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a compass direction from one location to another.","zh":"這個短語提供一個地點相對另一地點的羅盤方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the Glens of Antrim","meaning":"安特里姆峽谷","examples":[{"en":"The Glens of Antrim lie to the east beyond the Sperrin Mountains.","zh":"安特里姆峽谷位於東面，在斯佩林山脈以外。"},{"en":"The Glens of Antrim are a group of scenic valleys in County Antrim.","zh":"「the Glens of Antrim」是安特里姆郡一組風景優美的峽谷。"},{"en":"Visitors may go to the Glens of Antrim for walking routes, coastal roads, and green hills.","zh":"遊客可能到安特里姆峽谷行山、走海岸公路和欣賞綠色山丘。"},{"en":"Valleys like these attract tourists because they combine natural beauty with local history.","zh":"這類峽谷吸引旅客，因為它們結合自然美景與本地歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a specific landscape area in Northern Ireland.","zh":"這個短語指北愛爾蘭一個特定地貌區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"beyond the Sperrin Mountains","meaning":"在斯佩林山脈以外","examples":[{"en":"The eastern landscape lies beyond the Sperrin Mountains.","zh":"東面的景觀位於斯佩林山脈以外。"},{"en":"Beyond the Sperrin Mountains means on the far side of those mountains.","zh":"「beyond the Sperrin Mountains」意思是在斯佩林山脈的另一邊。"},{"en":"A small village may lie beyond the hills, hidden from the main road.","zh":"一條小村莊可能位於山丘以外，從大路看不到。"},{"en":"If a place is beyond a mountain range, reaching it may require a longer journey.","zh":"如果一個地方在山脈以外，到達它可能需要較長路程。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests location past a natural barrier.","zh":"這個短語暗示位於天然屏障之後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"captivating and alluring","meaning":"迷人而吸引的","examples":[{"en":"The region contains captivating and alluring scenery.","zh":"該地區有迷人而吸引的景色。"},{"en":"Captivating and alluring means very attractive in a way that holds people’s attention.","zh":"「captivating and alluring」意思是非常吸引人，能抓住人的注意力。"},{"en":"A quiet seaside town can feel captivating and alluring when the light changes at sunset.","zh":"當夕陽光線改變時，一個寧靜海邊小鎮可能顯得迷人而吸引。"},{"en":"If a place is captivating, visitors may want to stay longer and explore more slowly.","zh":"如果一個地方很迷人，遊客可能想逗留更久並慢慢探索。"},{"en":"The phrase describes beauty that draws people in emotionally.","zh":"這個短語描述能在情感上吸引人的美。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Western Europe","meaning":"西歐","examples":[{"en":"The area contains some of the finest landscapes in Western Europe.","zh":"該地區擁有西歐一些最優美的景觀。"},{"en":"Western Europe refers to the western part of the European continent.","zh":"「Western Europe」指歐洲大陸西部。"},{"en":"Many tourists visit Western Europe for historic cities, coastlines, museums, and mountain scenery.","zh":"許多遊客到西歐遊覽歷史城市、海岸線、博物館和山景。"},{"en":"If a landscape is praised as one of the finest in Western Europe, it is being compared with a very wide region.","zh":"如果一處景觀被稱為西歐最優美之一，它就是在與很廣泛的地區比較。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a broad geographical area.","zh":"這個短語指出廣泛地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Roe Valley Park","meaning":"羅伊河谷公園","examples":[{"en":"Roe Valley Park is located about 15 miles east of Derry.","zh":"羅伊河谷公園位於德里以東約15英里。"},{"en":"Roe Valley Park is a named park area around the River Roe.","zh":"「Roe Valley Park」是圍繞羅伊河的一個具名公園區域。"},{"en":"Families may visit Roe Valley Park to walk, picnic, and enjoy woodland paths.","zh":"家庭可能到羅伊河谷公園散步、野餐和享受林間小徑。"},{"en":"Because it combines river scenery and local history, the park can attract both walkers and heritage visitors.","zh":"因為它結合河流景色和本地歷史，公園可以吸引步行者和文化遺產遊客。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific park, not just any valley.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定公園，而不只是任何河谷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"some 15 miles east of","meaning":"在……以東約15英里","examples":[{"en":"The park lies some 15 miles east of Derry.","zh":"該公園位於德里以東約15英里。"},{"en":"Some 15 miles east of means approximately 15 miles to the east of a place.","zh":"「some 15 miles east of」意思是在某地以東大約15英里。"},{"en":"The campsite is some 10 miles north of town, so visitors usually drive there.","zh":"營地位於市鎮以北約10英里，所以遊客通常駕車前往。"},{"en":"If a site is some 15 miles away, it is close enough for a short trip but not a city-centre location.","zh":"如果一處地點約15英里外，它適合短途旅程，但不是市中心位置。"},{"en":"The word “some” here means “about”.","zh":"這裡的 “some” 意思是「大約」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"prime example","meaning":"典型例子","examples":[{"en":"Roe Valley Park is a prime example of the region’s natural beauty.","zh":"羅伊河谷公園是該地區自然美景的典型例子。"},{"en":"A prime example is a very clear or excellent example of something.","zh":"「prime example」是非常清楚或出色地代表某事的例子。"},{"en":"A well-organised notebook is a prime example of good study habits.","zh":"一本整理良好的筆記簿是良好學習習慣的典型例子。"},{"en":"If one case shows a quality especially clearly, it can be used as a prime example.","zh":"如果一個個案特別清楚顯示某種特質，它就可作典型例子。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights an example that represents a larger idea well.","zh":"這個短語突出能很好代表較大概念的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Celtic places","meaning":"凱爾特地方","examples":[{"en":"Many Celtic places are rich in history and legend.","zh":"許多凱爾特地方充滿歷史和傳說。"},{"en":"Celtic places are locations connected with Celtic peoples, languages, culture, or traditions.","zh":"「Celtic places」是與凱爾特民族、語言、文化或傳統有關的地方。"},{"en":"A village with old Celtic names, songs, and stories may be described as a Celtic place.","zh":"一條有古老凱爾特地名、歌曲和故事的村莊，可被稱為凱爾特地方。"},{"en":"If a place has Celtic roots, its landscape may carry layers of myth and memory.","zh":"如果一個地方有凱爾特根源，其地貌可能承載多層神話和記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase connects geography with cultural heritage.","zh":"這個短語把地理與文化遺產連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be steeped in","meaning":"充滿……；深受……薰陶","examples":[{"en":"Roe Valley Park is steeped in history and legend.","zh":"羅伊河谷公園充滿歷史和傳說。"},{"en":"To be steeped in something means to be deeply filled with it or strongly connected to it.","zh":"「be steeped in」某事，意思是深深充滿它或與它有強烈關聯。"},{"en":"An old school may be steeped in tradition if generations of students have studied there.","zh":"如果一間老學校有幾代學生就讀，它可能深受傳統薰陶。"},{"en":"If a town is steeped in legend, visitors may hear stories attached to streets, rivers, and buildings.","zh":"如果城鎮充滿傳說，遊客可能聽到與街道、河流和建築有關的故事。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a deep atmosphere, not a small connection.","zh":"這個短語暗示深厚氛圍，而不是小小關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"history and legend","meaning":"歷史和傳說","examples":[{"en":"The valley is associated with both history and legend.","zh":"該山谷同時與歷史和傳說有關。"},{"en":"History and legend means real past events together with traditional stories that may not be fully proven.","zh":"「history and legend」意思是真實過去事件加上未必完全可證的傳統故事。"},{"en":"A castle may have history in its records and legend in stories about ghosts or heroes.","zh":"一座城堡可能在記錄中有歷史，也在鬼魂或英雄故事中有傳說。"},{"en":"If history and legend mix, a place can feel both factual and mysterious.","zh":"如果歷史和傳說混合，一個地方可以同時感覺真實又神秘。"},{"en":"The phrase combines documented past with remembered storytelling.","zh":"這個短語結合有記載的過去與流傳故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"trickle down through","meaning":"潺潺流過……","examples":[{"en":"The Roe trickles down through the heather bogs.","zh":"羅伊河潺潺流過石楠沼澤。"},{"en":"To trickle down through something means to flow slowly and gently through it.","zh":"「trickle down through」某處，意思是水慢慢而輕柔地流過其中。"},{"en":"Rainwater may trickle down through soil before reaching a stream.","zh":"雨水可能先慢慢滲過泥土，然後到達溪流。"},{"en":"If water trickles rather than rushes, the scene feels quiet and gradual.","zh":"如果水是潺潺流動而不是奔流，景象就顯得安靜而緩慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow movement of liquid through a place.","zh":"這個短語描述液體慢慢流經某地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"heather bogs","meaning":"石楠沼澤","examples":[{"en":"The river begins among the heather bogs of the Sperrin Mountains.","zh":"這條河始於斯佩林山脈的石楠沼澤之中。"},{"en":"Heather bogs are wet, marshy areas where heather plants grow.","zh":"「heather bogs」是生長石楠植物的潮濕沼澤地。"},{"en":"Hikers may need waterproof boots when crossing heather bogs after rain.","zh":"遠足者雨後穿越石楠沼澤時，可能需要防水靴。"},{"en":"Because bogs hold water, streams can begin in them and flow downhill.","zh":"因為沼澤能蓄水，溪流可以從其中開始並向下流。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a wet upland landscape with heather vegetation.","zh":"這個短語描述長有石楠的潮濕高地景觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the Sperrin Mountains","meaning":"斯佩林山脈","examples":[{"en":"The Roe flows down from the Sperrin Mountains.","zh":"羅伊河從斯佩林山脈流下。"},{"en":"The Sperrin Mountains are a mountain range associated with the landscape of Northern Ireland.","zh":"「the Sperrin Mountains」是與北愛爾蘭景觀相關的一條山脈。"},{"en":"Visitors may drive through the Sperrin Mountains for open views and quiet countryside.","zh":"遊客可能駕車穿越斯佩林山脈，欣賞開闊景色和寧靜鄉郊。"},{"en":"Rivers often begin in mountain areas because rainwater gathers and flows downhill.","zh":"河流常從山區開始，因為雨水聚集並向下流。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific mountain region.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定山區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"by the time","meaning":"到……的時候","examples":[{"en":"By the time it reaches the valley, the stream has become a river.","zh":"到它到達山谷時，溪流已變成河流。"},{"en":"By the time means when a later point or stage is reached.","zh":"「by the time」意思是到達較後時間點或階段時。"},{"en":"By the time students finish the course, they should be able to write a full essay.","zh":"到學生完成課程時，他們應能寫一篇完整文章。"},{"en":"If a small stream gathers more water, by the time it reaches lower ground it may become a river.","zh":"如果小溪聚集更多水，到它到達低地時可能已變成河。"},{"en":"The phrase links an earlier process with a later result.","zh":"這個短語把較早過程與較後結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cut through","meaning":"穿過；切穿","examples":[{"en":"The river cuts through an area once called Gortenanima.","zh":"這條河穿過一片曾被稱為 Gortenanima 的地區。"},{"en":"To cut through a place means to pass across or carve a route through it.","zh":"「cut through」某地，意思是穿越它或在其中切出路線。"},{"en":"A footpath may cut through a park, giving students a shorter way to school.","zh":"一條小路可能穿過公園，給學生一條較短上學路線。"},{"en":"If a river cuts through rock over many years, it may create a valley.","zh":"如果河流多年切穿岩石，它可能形成山谷。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests movement through the middle of something.","zh":"這個短語暗示穿過某物中間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what was once called","meaning":"曾被稱為……的地方","examples":[{"en":"The river passes through what was once called the garden of the soul.","zh":"這條河流經曾被稱為「靈魂花園」的地方。"},{"en":"What was once called means the name formerly used for a place or thing.","zh":"「what was once called」意思是某地或某物以往使用的名稱。"},{"en":"A modern shopping street may stand where there was once a fishing village.","zh":"一條現代購物街可能位於曾經是一條漁村的地方。"},{"en":"If a name has changed, old documents may still show what the area was once called.","zh":"如果名稱已改變，舊文件可能仍顯示該地曾被稱為甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an older name or identity.","zh":"這個短語引入舊名稱或舊身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"garden of the soul","meaning":"靈魂花園","examples":[{"en":"Gortenanima means the garden of the soul in Celtic.","zh":"Gortenanima 在凱爾特語中意思是「靈魂花園」。"},{"en":"Garden of the soul is a poetic name suggesting a place of spiritual beauty or peace.","zh":"「garden of the soul」是一個詩意名稱，暗示具有精神美感或安寧的地方。"},{"en":"A quiet cemetery garden may feel like a garden of the soul because people go there to remember loved ones.","zh":"一個寧靜墓園花園可能感覺像靈魂花園，因為人們到那裡悼念摯愛。"},{"en":"If a place has such a name, visitors may expect mystery, calm, and meaning.","zh":"如果一個地方有這樣的名字，遊客可能期待神秘、平靜和意義。"},{"en":"The phrase is symbolic rather than literal.","zh":"這個短語是象徵性的，而不是字面意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Celtic name","meaning":"凱爾特名稱","examples":[{"en":"Gortenanima is an old Celtic name for the area.","zh":"Gortenanima 是該地區一個古老凱爾特名稱。"},{"en":"A Celtic name is a name that comes from a Celtic language or cultural tradition.","zh":"「Celtic name」是源自凱爾特語言或文化傳統的名稱。"},{"en":"Many place names in Ireland and Scotland preserve old Celtic names.","zh":"愛爾蘭和蘇格蘭許多地名保存了古老凱爾特名稱。"},{"en":"If a town keeps a Celtic name, it may preserve part of its early history.","zh":"如果一個城鎮保留凱爾特名稱，它可能保存早期歷史的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase connects naming with cultural origin.","zh":"這個短語把命名與文化源頭連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"once stood here","meaning":"曾經矗立在這裏","examples":[{"en":"The castle of O’Cahan once stood here.","zh":"奧卡漢城堡曾經矗立在這裏。"},{"en":"Once stood here means a building or object existed in this place in the past.","zh":"「once stood here」意思是某建築或物件過去存在於這個地方。"},{"en":"A sign may say that an old market once stood here before the new station was built.","zh":"標示牌可能寫着，新車站建成前，一個舊市場曾經在這裏。"},{"en":"If a castle once stood here, the land may still contain ruins or memories.","zh":"如果一座城堡曾經矗立在這裏，土地可能仍有遺跡或記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a vanished or changed historical site.","zh":"這個短語指向已消失或已改變的歷史地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the castle of O’Cahan","meaning":"奧卡漢城堡","examples":[{"en":"The castle of O’Cahan formed part of the area’s early settlement.","zh":"奧卡漢城堡是該地區早期聚落的一部分。"},{"en":"The castle of O’Cahan was a historic castle associated with the O’Cahan family or clan.","zh":"「the castle of O’Cahan」是一座與 O’Cahan 家族或氏族相關的歷史城堡。"},{"en":"A local guide may mention the castle of O’Cahan when explaining Limavady’s early history.","zh":"本地導遊解釋 Limavady 早期歷史時，可能提到奧卡漢城堡。"},{"en":"If a castle belonged to an important family, it often became a centre of local power.","zh":"如果一座城堡屬於重要家族，它常成為本地權力中心。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific historical stronghold.","zh":"這個短語命名一座特定歷史堡壘。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make up the town","meaning":"組成城鎮","examples":[{"en":"A number of houses once made up the town of Limavady.","zh":"若干房屋曾經組成 Limavady 鎮。"},{"en":"To make up a town means to form or constitute that town.","zh":"「make up a town」意思是形成或構成該城鎮。"},{"en":"A few shops, houses, and a school may make up a small village.","zh":"幾間商店、房屋和一所學校可能組成一條小村莊。"},{"en":"If more families arrive, the small group of houses can grow into a larger town.","zh":"如果更多家庭到來，小小房屋群可以發展成較大的城鎮。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the parts that form a whole place.","zh":"這個短語描述構成整個地方的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"take its name from","meaning":"名稱源自……","examples":[{"en":"Limavady takes its name from an old local legend.","zh":"Limavady 的名稱源自一個古老本地傳說。"},{"en":"To take its name from something means to be named after that source.","zh":"「take its name from」某事，意思是以該來源命名。"},{"en":"A street may take its name from a famous doctor who once lived there.","zh":"一條街道可能以曾住在那裡的著名醫生命名。"},{"en":"If a town takes its name from a legend, the name preserves a story.","zh":"如果一個城鎮名稱源自傳說，該名稱就保存了一個故事。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the origin of a name.","zh":"這個短語解釋名稱的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the legend of","meaning":"……的傳說","examples":[{"en":"The town’s name is associated with the legend of a leaping dog.","zh":"該鎮名稱與一隻跳躍之犬的傳說有關。"},{"en":"The legend of something is a traditional story about it, often passed down over generations.","zh":"「the legend of」某事，是關於它的傳統故事，常代代相傳。"},{"en":"Children may hear the legend of a mountain spirit from their grandparents.","zh":"孩子可能從祖父母那裡聽到山神的傳說。"},{"en":"If a place is linked with a legend, visitors may remember it more easily.","zh":"如果一個地方與傳說有關，遊客可能更容易記住它。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a traditional story connected with a person, animal, or place.","zh":"這個短語引入與人物、動物或地方相關的傳統故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"leap into the river","meaning":"跳進河裏","examples":[{"en":"According to legend, a dog leapt into the River Roe.","zh":"根據傳說，一隻狗跳進羅伊河。"},{"en":"To leap into the river means to jump suddenly into the river.","zh":"「leap into the river」意思是突然跳進河裏。"},{"en":"A child should never leap into a river without checking the depth and current.","zh":"孩子絕不應在未檢查水深和水流前跳進河裏。"},{"en":"If an animal leaps into a river during a chase, the action may become part of a dramatic story.","zh":"如果動物在追逐中跳進河裏，這個動作可能成為戲劇性故事的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a quick, forceful jump into water.","zh":"這個短語描述快速有力地跳進水中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"carry a message","meaning":"傳遞訊息","examples":[{"en":"The dog may have been carrying a message.","zh":"那隻狗可能正在傳遞訊息。"},{"en":"To carry a message means to transport or deliver information from one person or place to another.","zh":"「carry a message」意思是把資訊從一個人或地方帶到另一個人或地方。"},{"en":"Before mobile phones, a child might carry a message from one neighbour to another.","zh":"在沒有手機以前，孩子可能替鄰居之間傳遞訊息。"},{"en":"If roads are blocked, someone may need to carry a message on foot.","zh":"如果道路受阻，可能需要有人步行傳遞訊息。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physically or symbolically delivering information.","zh":"這個短語描述實際或象徵性地傳遞資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"chase a stag","meaning":"追逐雄鹿","examples":[{"en":"Another version says that the dog was chasing a stag.","zh":"另一版本說那隻狗正在追逐雄鹿。"},{"en":"To chase a stag means to run after a male deer.","zh":"「chase a stag」意思是追趕一隻雄鹿。"},{"en":"In a forest story, hunters may chase a stag through trees and across streams.","zh":"在森林故事中，獵人可能追逐雄鹿穿過樹林和溪流。"},{"en":"If a dog chases a stag too close to a river, it may leap into the water after it.","zh":"如果狗追逐雄鹿太接近河邊，它可能跟着跳進水裏。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pursuit of a male deer.","zh":"這個短語描述追趕雄性鹿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"trace its way through","meaning":"蜿蜒流經……","examples":[{"en":"The water traces its way through rock and woodland.","zh":"河水蜿蜒流經岩石和林地。"},{"en":"To trace its way through a place means to follow a winding path through it.","zh":"「trace its way through」某地，意思是沿着彎曲路線穿過它。"},{"en":"A small path may trace its way through a housing estate before reaching the park.","zh":"一條小路可能蜿蜒穿過屋苑，然後到達公園。"},{"en":"If water traces its way through rock, it may slowly shape the landscape.","zh":"如果水蜿蜒流經岩石，它可能慢慢塑造地貌。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests slow, winding movement.","zh":"這個短語暗示緩慢而彎曲的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rock and woodland","meaning":"岩石和林地","examples":[{"en":"The river winds through rock and woodland.","zh":"河流蜿蜒穿過岩石和林地。"},{"en":"Rock and woodland means rocky areas together with land covered by trees.","zh":"「rock and woodland」意思是岩石地區加上有樹木覆蓋的土地。"},{"en":"A hiking route through rock and woodland may feel varied and peaceful.","zh":"穿過岩石和林地的行山路線可能感覺多變而寧靜。"},{"en":"If a river passes through both rock and woodland, it creates changing scenery.","zh":"如果河流同時穿過岩石和林地，它會形成變化豐富的景色。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a mixed natural landscape.","zh":"這個短語描述混合自然景觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at times","meaning":"有時","examples":[{"en":"At times, the river becomes calm and dark.","zh":"有時，河流會變得平靜而幽暗。"},{"en":"At times means sometimes or on certain occasions.","zh":"「at times」意思是有時或在某些時候。"},{"en":"At times, students feel confident; at other times, they need encouragement.","zh":"有時學生感到自信；其他時候，他們需要鼓勵。"},{"en":"If a river changes at times, its mood may feel different along the route.","zh":"如果河流有時改變，其沿途氣氛可能感覺不同。"},{"en":"The phrase marks occasional, not constant, situations.","zh":"這個短語標示偶爾出現，而非持續出現的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"linger in","meaning":"緩緩停留在……","examples":[{"en":"The water lingers in deep pools beneath the trees.","zh":"河水緩緩停留在樹下深潭中。"},{"en":"To linger in a place means to stay there slowly or for longer than expected.","zh":"「linger in」某處，意思是慢慢停留或比預期逗留更久。"},{"en":"The smell of fresh bread may linger in a kitchen after breakfast.","zh":"早餐後，新鮮麵包香味可能仍停留在廚房中。"},{"en":"If water lingers in deep pools, the scene feels still rather than fast-moving.","zh":"如果水停留在深潭中，景象感覺靜止而非快速流動。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests slow staying or remaining.","zh":"這個短語暗示慢慢停留或殘留。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"brooding pools","meaning":"幽暗深沉的水潭","examples":[{"en":"The river forms brooding pools of dark, cool water.","zh":"河流形成幽暗深沉、清涼的水潭。"},{"en":"Brooding pools are dark, still pools that feel serious, mysterious, or slightly gloomy.","zh":"「brooding pools」是黑暗而靜止，感覺嚴肅、神秘或略帶陰鬱的水潭。"},{"en":"In an old forest, brooding pools may make the path feel quiet and haunted.","zh":"在古老森林中，幽暗深沉的水潭可能令小路感覺安靜而帶鬼魅氣氛。"},{"en":"If water is dark and motionless, it can create a brooding atmosphere.","zh":"如果水面黑暗而不動，它可以營造深沉氣氛。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both the physical pools and their mood.","zh":"這個短語同時描述水潭本身和其氣氛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"under the shade of","meaning":"在……的樹蔭下","examples":[{"en":"The pools lie under the shade of summer trees.","zh":"水潭位於夏日樹木的樹蔭下。"},{"en":"Under the shade of something means beneath an area protected from direct sunlight by it.","zh":"「under the shade of」某物，意思是在由它遮擋直射陽光的陰影下。"},{"en":"Students may eat lunch under the shade of a large tree on a hot day.","zh":"炎熱日子，學生可能在大樹樹蔭下吃午飯。"},{"en":"If water lies under shade, it may stay cooler and darker.","zh":"如果水位於樹蔭下，它可能保持較涼和較暗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shelter from sunlight.","zh":"這個短語描述遮蔽陽光。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"form weirs","meaning":"形成堰","examples":[{"en":"In other places, the river forms weirs.","zh":"在其他地方，河流形成堰。"},{"en":"To form weirs means to create low barriers or dam-like structures across a river.","zh":"「form weirs」意思是形成橫跨河流的低矮屏障或類似水壩的結構。"},{"en":"A stream may form small natural weirs when rocks block part of the water flow.","zh":"當岩石阻擋部分水流，小溪可能形成小型天然堰。"},{"en":"If a weir forms, water may collect behind it and flow over the top.","zh":"如果形成堰，水可能在其後方聚集並從頂部流過。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the creation of river barriers.","zh":"這個短語描述河流屏障的形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mill leads","meaning":"水磨坊引水渠","examples":[{"en":"The river once supplied mill leads for nearby water mills.","zh":"這條河曾為附近水磨坊供應引水渠。"},{"en":"Mill leads are channels that guide water towards a mill so it can power machinery.","zh":"「mill leads」是把水引向磨坊以推動機械的水道。"},{"en":"In the past, a village mill might depend on mill leads to turn its wheel.","zh":"過去，村莊磨坊可能依靠引水渠轉動水輪。"},{"en":"If a river supplied mill leads, it helped local people grind grain or run machinery.","zh":"如果河流供應磨坊引水渠，它就幫助本地人磨穀或運行機械。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to old water channels connected with mills.","zh":"這個短語指與磨坊相關的古老水道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"water mills","meaning":"水磨坊","examples":[{"en":"The river once powered several water mills.","zh":"這條河曾推動幾座水磨坊。"},{"en":"Water mills are mills that use flowing water to power machinery.","zh":"「water mills」是利用流動水力推動機械的磨坊。"},{"en":"A water mill might grind grain into flour for a village.","zh":"水磨坊可能為村莊把穀物磨成麵粉。"},{"en":"If a river flows strongly, it can provide energy for water mills.","zh":"如果河流流勢強，它可以為水磨坊提供能源。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to old technology using river power.","zh":"這個短語指使用河流水力的古老技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"long gone","meaning":"早已消失","examples":[{"en":"The water mills are now long gone.","zh":"那些水磨坊現在早已消失。"},{"en":"Long gone means disappeared or no longer existing for a long time.","zh":"「long gone」意思是消失已久或很久以前已不再存在。"},{"en":"The old cinema is long gone, but older residents still remember it.","zh":"舊戲院早已消失，但年長居民仍記得它。"},{"en":"If a building is long gone, only stories, photos, or ruins may remain.","zh":"如果一座建築早已消失，可能只剩故事、照片或遺跡。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses loss over a long period.","zh":"這個短語表達長時間後的失去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be witness to","meaning":"見證……","examples":[{"en":"The River Roe has been witness to centuries of history and change.","zh":"羅伊河見證了數百年的歷史和變遷。"},{"en":"To be witness to something means to have seen or existed through it.","zh":"「be witness to」某事，意思是曾看見或經歷它。"},{"en":"An old school building may be witness to generations of students growing up.","zh":"一座舊校舍可能見證幾代學生成長。"},{"en":"If a river has flowed through a town for centuries, it has witnessed wars, work, and daily life.","zh":"如果一條河流經城鎮數百年，它就見證戰爭、工作和日常生活。"},{"en":"The phrase personifies a place or object as an observer of history.","zh":"這個短語把地方或物件擬人化為歷史觀察者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"history and change","meaning":"歷史和變遷","examples":[{"en":"Like all rivers, the Roe has witnessed history and change.","zh":"像所有河流一樣，羅伊河見證了歷史和變遷。"},{"en":"History and change means past events together with the transformations that followed them.","zh":"「history and change」意思是過去事件以及隨之而來的轉變。"},{"en":"A city square may show history and change through old monuments beside new shops.","zh":"城市廣場可能透過舊紀念碑旁的新商店展示歷史和變遷。"},{"en":"If a place survives for centuries, it often carries signs of both memory and transformation.","zh":"如果一個地方存在數百年，它常帶有記憶和轉變的痕跡。"},{"en":"The phrase links the past with ongoing development.","zh":"這個短語把過去與持續發展連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"west bank","meaning":"西岸","examples":[{"en":"Mullagh Hill lies on the west bank of the River Roe.","zh":"Mullagh Hill 位於羅伊河西岸。"},{"en":"The west bank of a river is the land on the western side of the river.","zh":"「west bank」是河流西側的土地。"},{"en":"A school may be on the west bank of a river, while the market is on the east bank.","zh":"一所學校可能在河流西岸，而市場在東岸。"},{"en":"If a bridge connects both banks, people can cross between the two sides easily.","zh":"如果橋連接兩岸，人們就能輕易往返兩邊。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies one side of a river.","zh":"這個短語指出河流其中一側。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"just outside","meaning":"就在……外面","examples":[{"en":"The hill stands just outside the present-day town.","zh":"那座山就在現今城鎮外面。"},{"en":"Just outside means very near but not inside a place.","zh":"「just outside」意思是非常接近某地，但不在其內部。"},{"en":"The bus stop is just outside the school gate, so students can see it easily.","zh":"巴士站就在校門外面，所以學生很容易看見。"},{"en":"If a site is just outside town, it is close enough to visit without a long journey.","zh":"如果一處地點就在城鎮外面，它很近，無需長途旅程就能到訪。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a nearby external location.","zh":"這個短語描述近在外部的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"present-day town","meaning":"現今的城鎮","examples":[{"en":"The site lies close to the present-day town of Limavady.","zh":"該遺址靠近現今的 Limavady 鎮。"},{"en":"Present-day town means the town as it exists now, not as it was in the past.","zh":"「present-day town」意思是現時存在的城鎮，而不是過去的城鎮。"},{"en":"The present-day town may be larger than the original settlement.","zh":"現今的城鎮可能比最早聚居地大。"},{"en":"If historians compare old ruins with the present-day town, they can see how the area has changed.","zh":"如果歷史學家把舊遺跡與現今城鎮比較，就能看見該地區如何改變。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts modern geography with historical geography.","zh":"這個短語對比現代地理與歷史地理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the Convention of Drumceatt","meaning":"德拉姆凱特會議","examples":[{"en":"St Columba came to the area for the Convention of Drumceatt.","zh":"聖 Columba 為德拉姆凱特會議來到該地區。"},{"en":"The Convention of Drumceatt was a named historical gathering associated with the area.","zh":"「the Convention of Drumceatt」是一場與該地區相關的具名歷史聚會。"},{"en":"A local history guide may mention the Convention of Drumceatt to explain the region’s early importance.","zh":"本地歷史導遊可能提到德拉姆凱特會議，以解釋該地區早期的重要性。"},{"en":"If an important religious figure attended a convention, the event may become part of regional memory.","zh":"如果重要宗教人物出席一場會議，該事件可能成為地區記憶的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific historical event.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定歷史事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be unaware that","meaning":"不知道；沒有察覺","examples":[{"en":"Many people are unaware that they know something associated with Limavady.","zh":"許多人不知道自己認識某些與 Limavady 有關的東西。"},{"en":"To be unaware that something is true means not to realise or know it.","zh":"「be unaware that」某事為真，意思是沒有意識到或不知道它。"},{"en":"A student may be unaware that a word they use every day comes from another language.","zh":"學生可能不知道自己每天使用的詞來自另一種語言。"},{"en":"If people are unaware of a connection, they may miss the history behind a familiar song.","zh":"如果人們沒有察覺某種關聯，就可能錯過熟悉歌曲背後的歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase describes hidden knowledge or unnoticed facts.","zh":"這個短語描述隱藏知識或未被注意的事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"Limavady is, in fact, associated with a famous melody.","zh":"事實上，Limavady 與一段著名旋律有關。"},{"en":"In fact introduces a true point, often one that corrects or adds to what people expect.","zh":"「in fact」引入真實資訊，常用來修正或補充人們的預期。"},{"en":"The old building looks empty; in fact, it is now a community centre.","zh":"那座舊建築看起來空置；事實上，它現在是社區中心。"},{"en":"If people think a town is unknown, “in fact” can introduce its surprising importance.","zh":"如果人們以為某城鎮不知名，“in fact” 可以引入其令人意外的重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase signals a factual clarification.","zh":"這個短語標示事實澄清。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be renowned for","meaning":"以……聞名","examples":[{"en":"Limavady is renowned for its association with the melody used for “Danny Boy.”","zh":"Limavady 以與《Danny Boy》所用旋律的關聯聞名。"},{"en":"To be renowned for something means to be widely known or famous because of it.","zh":"「be renowned for」某事，意思是因為它而廣為人知或著名。"},{"en":"A school may be renowned for excellent music training.","zh":"一所學校可能以優秀音樂訓練聞名。"},{"en":"If a town is renowned for a song, visitors may connect the place with that music.","zh":"如果一個城鎮以一首歌聞名，遊客可能把該地與那段音樂連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong reputation.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈名聲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Danny Boy","meaning":"《Danny Boy》","examples":[{"en":"The melody associated with Limavady later became famous as “Danny Boy.”","zh":"與 Limavady 相關的旋律後來以《Danny Boy》之名聞名。"},{"en":"“Danny Boy” is the title of a famous song connected with an Irish melody.","zh":"“Danny Boy” 是一首與愛爾蘭旋律相關的著名歌曲名稱。"},{"en":"People may hear “Danny Boy” at concerts, ceremonies, or family gatherings.","zh":"人們可能在音樂會、典禮或家庭聚會聽到《Danny Boy》。"},{"en":"If a melody becomes attached to a famous song, the place connected with it may also gain fame.","zh":"如果一段旋律與著名歌曲連上關係，與它相關的地方也可能變得有名。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific song rather than a general tune.","zh":"這個短語命名一首特定歌曲，而不是一般旋律。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be written to a tune","meaning":"按照一段旋律填詞","examples":[{"en":"The words were written to a traditional Irish tune.","zh":"歌詞按照一段傳統愛爾蘭旋律填寫。"},{"en":"To be written to a tune means lyrics are created to fit an existing melody.","zh":"「be written to a tune」意思是歌詞被創作出來以配合已有旋律。"},{"en":"A school song may be written to a familiar tune so students can learn it quickly.","zh":"校歌可能按照熟悉旋律填詞，讓學生快速學會。"},{"en":"If words are written to an old tune, the new song can carry older musical memory.","zh":"如果歌詞按照古老旋律填寫，新歌就能承載較舊音樂記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase connects lyrics with melody.","zh":"這個短語把歌詞與旋律連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a tune once played by","meaning":"一段曾由……演奏的旋律","examples":[{"en":"The tune was said to have been played by a travelling musician in the street.","zh":"據說這段旋律曾由一位流浪樂師在街上演奏。"},{"en":"A tune once played by someone is a melody that person reportedly performed in the past.","zh":"「a tune once played by」某人，是據稱該人在過去演奏過的旋律。"},{"en":"A village song may be remembered as a tune once played by an old flute player.","zh":"一首村歌可能被記作一段曾由老笛手演奏的旋律。"},{"en":"If a tune was once played in public, listeners may preserve it through memory and repetition.","zh":"如果一段旋律曾在公共場合演奏，聽眾可能透過記憶和重複保存它。"},{"en":"The phrase links music with a past performer.","zh":"這個短語把音樂與過去的演奏者連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"travelling musician","meaning":"流浪樂師","examples":[{"en":"A travelling musician was said to have played the melody in Limavady.","zh":"據說一位流浪樂師曾在 Limavady 演奏這段旋律。"},{"en":"A travelling musician is a musician who moves from place to place to perform.","zh":"「travelling musician」是四處移動演出的音樂人。"},{"en":"A travelling musician may play in streets, markets, inns, and village festivals.","zh":"流浪樂師可能在街頭、市集、旅店和村莊節日演奏。"},{"en":"Because travelling musicians move widely, they can spread songs between communities.","zh":"因為流浪樂師四處走動，他們可以把歌曲傳到不同社區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a performer without one fixed local stage.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有固定本地舞台的表演者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"surrounding villages","meaning":"周邊村落","examples":[{"en":"Many of the surrounding villages have Celtic roots.","zh":"許多周邊村落都有凱爾特根源。"},{"en":"Surrounding villages are the villages located around a main town or area.","zh":"「surrounding villages」是位於主要城鎮或地區周圍的村落。"},{"en":"A town market may serve farmers from the surrounding villages.","zh":"城鎮市場可能服務來自周邊村落的農民。"},{"en":"If surrounding villages share similar names and customs, they may have a common cultural past.","zh":"如果周邊村落有相似地名和習俗，它們可能有共同文化過去。"},{"en":"The phrase describes nearby village communities.","zh":"這個短語描述附近村莊社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Celtic roots","meaning":"凱爾特根源","examples":[{"en":"Limavady and its surrounding villages have Celtic roots.","zh":"Limavady 及其周邊村落有凱爾特根源。"},{"en":"Celtic roots are origins or influences connected with Celtic culture, language, or people.","zh":"「Celtic roots」是與凱爾特文化、語言或民族相關的起源或影響。"},{"en":"A local festival may have Celtic roots if its music, names, or rituals come from old Celtic traditions.","zh":"如果本地節日的音樂、名稱或儀式來自古老凱爾特傳統，它可能有凱爾特根源。"},{"en":"If a place has Celtic roots, its modern culture may still contain ancient traces.","zh":"如果一個地方有凱爾特根源，其現代文化可能仍含有古老痕跡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cultural origin or ancestry.","zh":"這個短語描述文化起源或祖源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"no one knows for sure","meaning":"沒有人能確定","examples":[{"en":"No one knows for sure how old the original settlement is.","zh":"沒有人能確定最早的聚居地有多古老。"},{"en":"No one knows for sure means nobody can state something with certainty.","zh":"「no one knows for sure」意思是沒有人能確定地說出某事。"},{"en":"No one knows for sure why the old house was abandoned.","zh":"沒有人能確定那座舊屋為何被棄置。"},{"en":"If evidence is missing or unclear, historians may admit that no one knows for sure.","zh":"如果證據缺失或不清楚，歷史學家可能承認沒有人能確定。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses uncertainty honestly.","zh":"這個短語誠實表達不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"original settlement","meaning":"最早的聚居地","examples":[{"en":"The exact age of the original settlement remains unknown.","zh":"最早聚居地的確切年代仍然未知。"},{"en":"An original settlement is the earliest community or group of homes established in a place.","zh":"「original settlement」是在某地建立的最早社群或房屋群。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may search for pottery to date the original settlement.","zh":"考古學家可能尋找陶器，以推定最早聚居地的年代。"},{"en":"If the original settlement grew over centuries, it may become a modern town.","zh":"如果最早聚居地經數百年發展，它可能變成現代城鎮。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the first known stage of human habitation.","zh":"這個短語指人類居住的最早已知階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"along the coast road","meaning":"沿着海岸公路","examples":[{"en":"Dunluce Castle lies about 30 miles along the coast road from Limavady.","zh":"鄧路斯城堡位於從 Limavady 沿着海岸公路約30英里處。"},{"en":"Along the coast road means following the road that runs beside or near the coast.","zh":"「along the coast road」意思是沿着靠近海岸或在海岸旁的道路。"},{"en":"A family may drive along the coast road to enjoy sea views on the way to a beach.","zh":"一家人可能沿着海岸公路駕車，到海灘途中欣賞海景。"},{"en":"If a castle lies along the coast road, it can be visited as part of a scenic route.","zh":"如果城堡位於海岸公路沿線，就可以作為風景路線的一站遊覽。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement or location on a coastal route.","zh":"這個短語描述海岸路線上的移動或位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"come upon","meaning":"偶然遇見；來到","examples":[{"en":"Travellers eventually come upon the ruins of Dunluce Castle.","zh":"旅客最終會來到鄧路斯城堡遺跡前。"},{"en":"To come upon something means to find or reach it, often unexpectedly while travelling.","zh":"「come upon」某物，意思是在旅途中找到或到達它，常帶意外感。"},{"en":"While walking through a village, you may come upon a small old temple behind the shops.","zh":"走過村莊時，你可能在商店後面偶然遇見一座小古廟。"},{"en":"If a ruin appears suddenly after a bend in the road, visitors may feel surprised.","zh":"如果遺跡在道路轉彎後突然出現，遊客可能感到驚喜。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests discovery during movement.","zh":"這個短語暗示移動中的發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"forlorn but imposing","meaning":"荒涼但宏偉的","examples":[{"en":"Dunluce Castle is a forlorn but imposing ruin.","zh":"鄧路斯城堡是一處荒涼但宏偉的遺跡。"},{"en":"Forlorn but imposing means sad, abandoned, or lonely, yet still grand and impressive.","zh":"「forlorn but imposing」意思是悲涼、被遺棄或孤寂，但仍宏大而令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"An empty old theatre may look forlorn but imposing after decades of neglect.","zh":"一座空置舊劇院荒廢數十年後，可能看起來荒涼但宏偉。"},{"en":"If a building is ruined but massive, it can feel both tragic and powerful.","zh":"如果建築已成廢墟但仍巨大，它可以同時令人感到悲劇性和有力量。"},{"en":"The phrase combines emotional sadness with visual strength.","zh":"這個短語結合情感上的荒涼與視覺上的氣勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"imposing ruin","meaning":"宏偉的遺跡","examples":[{"en":"The castle remains an imposing ruin above the Atlantic.","zh":"這座城堡仍是大西洋上方一處宏偉的遺跡。"},{"en":"An imposing ruin is a ruined building that still looks large, powerful, or impressive.","zh":"「imposing ruin」是雖已破敗但仍顯得巨大、有力量或令人印象深刻的建築遺跡。"},{"en":"A broken city wall can be an imposing ruin if it still dominates the skyline.","zh":"如果一段破碎城牆仍主導天際線，它可以是宏偉的遺跡。"},{"en":"If a ruin stands high above the sea, its position can make it more dramatic.","zh":"如果遺跡矗立在海上高處，其位置會令它更具戲劇感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a ruin that still commands attention.","zh":"這個短語描述仍能吸引注意的遺跡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Dunluce Castle","meaning":"鄧路斯城堡","examples":[{"en":"Dunluce Castle stands dramatically above the Atlantic coast.","zh":"鄧路斯城堡戲劇性地矗立在大西洋海岸上方。"},{"en":"Dunluce Castle is a historic castle ruin located on a coastal cliff.","zh":"「Dunluce Castle」是一處位於海岸懸崖上的歷史城堡遺跡。"},{"en":"Visitors may photograph Dunluce Castle because its ruined walls stand against the sea.","zh":"遊客可能拍攝鄧路斯城堡，因為其殘牆立於海景之前。"},{"en":"If a castle is placed above a rough coast, it can look both defensive and romantic.","zh":"如果城堡位於崎嶇海岸上方，它可以顯得既具防禦性又浪漫。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific historic site.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定歷史地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"stand on","meaning":"矗立在……上","examples":[{"en":"The castle stands on a soft basalt outcrop.","zh":"城堡矗立在一片較軟的玄武岩露頭上。"},{"en":"To stand on something means to be positioned or built on top of it.","zh":"「stand on」某物，意思是位於或建於其上方。"},{"en":"A school may stand on land that was once a farm.","zh":"一所學校可能建在曾經是農田的土地上。"},{"en":"If a building stands on weak rock, weather and erosion may damage it over time.","zh":"如果建築矗立在脆弱岩石上，風化和侵蝕可能隨時間損壞它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical position or foundation.","zh":"這個短語描述實際位置或基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"basalt outcrop","meaning":"玄武岩露頭","examples":[{"en":"Dunluce Castle occupies a basalt outcrop above the sea.","zh":"鄧路斯城堡佔據海上方一處玄武岩露頭。"},{"en":"A basalt outcrop is an exposed area of dark volcanic rock at the surface.","zh":"「basalt outcrop」是地表露出的深色火山岩區域。"},{"en":"A hiking path may lead to a basalt outcrop where visitors can see layers of old rock.","zh":"行山路徑可能通往玄武岩露頭，讓遊客看見古老岩層。"},{"en":"If a castle is built on an outcrop, it may gain height and protection.","zh":"如果城堡建在岩石露頭上，它可能獲得高度和保護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a geological feature used as a natural platform.","zh":"這個短語描述可作天然平台的地質特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in defiance of","meaning":"不畏……；抗衡……","examples":[{"en":"The castle stands in defiance of the turbulent Atlantic.","zh":"這座城堡不畏波濤洶湧的大西洋而矗立。"},{"en":"In defiance of something means resisting or standing boldly against it.","zh":"「in defiance of」某事，意思是抵抗或勇敢面對它。"},{"en":"A small tree may grow in defiance of strong winds on a cliff.","zh":"一棵小樹可能在懸崖上不畏強風生長。"},{"en":"If a building faces a violent sea for centuries, it seems to challenge nature.","zh":"如果建築數百年面對猛烈海浪，它看起來像在挑戰自然。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests courage, resistance, or stubborn survival.","zh":"這個短語暗示勇氣、抗衡或頑強生存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"turbulent Atlantic","meaning":"波濤洶湧的大西洋","examples":[{"en":"The turbulent Atlantic lashes the rocks beneath the castle.","zh":"波濤洶湧的大西洋猛烈拍打城堡下方岩石。"},{"en":"The turbulent Atlantic means the rough, stormy, and powerful Atlantic Ocean.","zh":"「turbulent Atlantic」指粗暴、多風暴而強大的大西洋。"},{"en":"Sailors may avoid a harbour when the sea is turbulent and dangerous.","zh":"當海面洶湧危險時，水手可能避開港口。"},{"en":"If waves are turbulent, they can erode cliffs and damage coastal buildings.","zh":"如果海浪洶湧，它們可以侵蝕懸崖並損壞海岸建築。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the ocean a forceful and restless character.","zh":"這個短語賦予海洋強而不安的性格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lash something on all sides","meaning":"從四面猛烈拍打……","examples":[{"en":"The Atlantic lashes the rocky outcrop on all sides.","zh":"大西洋從四面猛烈拍打岩石露頭。"},{"en":"To lash something on all sides means to hit it violently from every direction, usually with wind, rain, or waves.","zh":"「lash something on all sides」意思是風、雨或海浪從每個方向猛烈擊打某物。"},{"en":"During a storm, rain may lash a bus stop on all sides.","zh":"暴風雨中，雨水可能從四面猛烈拍打巴士站。"},{"en":"If waves lash rocks on all sides, erosion can happen faster.","zh":"如果海浪從四面拍打岩石，侵蝕可能更快發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated violent striking from around a place.","zh":"這個短語描述從周圍反覆猛烈撞擊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"jagged-toothed ruins","meaning":"鋸齒狀的遺跡","examples":[{"en":"The jagged-toothed ruins create a dramatic outline.","zh":"鋸齒狀的遺跡形成戲劇性的輪廓。"},{"en":"Jagged-toothed ruins are broken walls with sharp, uneven edges that look like teeth.","zh":"「jagged-toothed ruins」是邊緣尖銳不平、看起來像牙齒的破牆。"},{"en":"An old factory with jagged-toothed ruins may look striking against the evening sky.","zh":"一座有鋸齒狀遺跡的舊工廠，在傍晚天空前可能十分突出。"},{"en":"If stone walls break unevenly, they can form a dramatic silhouette.","zh":"如果石牆不均勻地破裂，就能形成戲劇性剪影。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the sharp visual shape of ruined buildings.","zh":"這個短語描述廢墟建築尖銳的視覺形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sit proud","meaning":"雄踞","examples":[{"en":"The castle ruins sit proud on their rocky summit.","zh":"城堡遺跡雄踞於岩石頂峰。"},{"en":"To sit proud means to stand or be positioned boldly and prominently.","zh":"「sit proud」意思是醒目而有氣勢地矗立或位於某處。"},{"en":"A statue may sit proud in the middle of a town square.","zh":"一座雕像可能雄踞於城鎮廣場中央。"},{"en":"If ruins sit proud on high rock, they dominate the surrounding view.","zh":"如果遺跡雄踞高岩上，它們就主導周圍景觀。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests confidence, height, and visibility.","zh":"這個短語暗示自信、高度和可見性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rocky summit","meaning":"岩石頂峰","examples":[{"en":"The ruins dominate the coast from their rocky summit.","zh":"遺跡從岩石頂峰俯視並主導海岸。"},{"en":"A rocky summit is the top of a hill, cliff, or outcrop made of rock.","zh":"「rocky summit」是由岩石構成的山丘、懸崖或露頭頂部。"},{"en":"Hikers may rest on a rocky summit after climbing a steep path.","zh":"遠足者爬上陡路後，可能在岩石頂峰休息。"},{"en":"If a building stands on a rocky summit, it gains a wide view over the land or sea.","zh":"如果建築位於岩石頂峰，就能廣泛俯瞰陸地或海洋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a high rocky top.","zh":"這個短語描述高處的岩石頂部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"command the coastline","meaning":"俯瞰海岸線","examples":[{"en":"The castle commands the coastline to the east and west.","zh":"城堡俯瞰東西兩面的海岸線。"},{"en":"To command the coastline means to overlook and dominate a long stretch of coast.","zh":"「command the coastline」意思是俯瞰並主導一長段海岸。"},{"en":"A lighthouse commands the bay because it can be seen from far away.","zh":"燈塔俯瞰海灣，因為很遠也能看見它。"},{"en":"If a castle commands the coastline, it was probably useful for defence and observation.","zh":"如果城堡俯瞰海岸線，它過去很可能有防禦和觀察用途。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a strong visual and strategic position.","zh":"這個短語暗示強烈視覺和戰略位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"to east and west","meaning":"向東和向西","examples":[{"en":"The view extends along the coast to east and west.","zh":"景色沿海岸向東和向西延伸。"},{"en":"To east and west means in both the eastern and western directions.","zh":"「to east and west」意思是向東面和西面兩個方向。"},{"en":"From the hilltop, visitors can see villages to east and west.","zh":"從山頂，遊客可以看見東西兩面的村莊。"},{"en":"If a viewpoint opens to east and west, it offers a wide panoramic view.","zh":"如果觀景點向東和向西都開闊，就能提供寬廣全景。"},{"en":"The phrase describes two opposite directions.","zh":"這個短語描述兩個相反方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"connection to the mainland","meaning":"與大陸的連接","examples":[{"en":"A narrow bridge provides the only connection to the mainland.","zh":"一條狹窄橋樑提供與大陸的唯一連接。"},{"en":"A connection to the mainland is a route linking an island or isolated place to the main land area.","zh":"「connection to the mainland」是把島嶼或孤立地方連接到主要陸地的路線。"},{"en":"A ferry may be the only connection to the mainland for a small island community.","zh":"對小島社區而言，渡輪可能是與大陸的唯一連接。"},{"en":"If the connection is cut, residents or visitors may be trapped.","zh":"如果連接被切斷，居民或遊客可能被困。"},{"en":"The phrase describes access from a separate place to the main land.","zh":"這個短語描述從分離地點通往主要陸地的通道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"narrow bridge","meaning":"狹窄橋樑","examples":[{"en":"The castle can be reached only by a narrow bridge.","zh":"城堡只能經由一條狹窄橋樑到達。"},{"en":"A narrow bridge is a bridge with limited width, often allowing only careful passage.","zh":"「narrow bridge」是寬度有限、通常需要小心通過的橋。"},{"en":"Two cyclists may need to slow down when crossing a narrow bridge.","zh":"兩名單車人士過狹窄橋樑時可能需要減速。"},{"en":"If a bridge is narrow and high, nervous visitors may feel unsafe.","zh":"如果橋又窄又高，緊張的遊客可能感到不安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a physically limited crossing.","zh":"這個短語描述實際寬度有限的通道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"kitchen court","meaning":"廚房庭院","examples":[{"en":"The castle’s kitchen court fell into the sea in 1639.","zh":"城堡的廚房庭院於1639年墜入海中。"},{"en":"A kitchen court is an area of a castle or large house connected with kitchen work and service space.","zh":"「kitchen court」是城堡或大宅中與廚房工作和服務空間相關的區域。"},{"en":"In an old castle, servants may have carried food from the kitchen court to the dining hall.","zh":"在舊城堡中，僕人可能從廚房庭院把食物送到飯廳。"},{"en":"If a kitchen court collapses, daily life in the building becomes impossible.","zh":"如果廚房庭院倒塌，建築內的日常生活就變得不可能。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a functional part of a historic building.","zh":"這個短語指歷史建築中的功能性部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fall into the sea","meaning":"墜入海中","examples":[{"en":"Part of the castle fell into the sea during a violent storm.","zh":"城堡一部分在猛烈風暴中墜入海中。"},{"en":"To fall into the sea means to collapse or drop down into seawater.","zh":"「fall into the sea」意思是倒塌或掉進海水中。"},{"en":"A cliff path may fall into the sea after years of erosion.","zh":"懸崖小路經多年侵蝕後可能墜入海中。"},{"en":"If waves weaken the rock beneath a building, part of it may eventually fall into the sea.","zh":"如果海浪削弱建築下方岩石，其一部分最終可能墜入海中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical collapse into the ocean.","zh":"這個短語描述實際倒塌進海洋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"kill several servants","meaning":"導致數名僕人死亡","examples":[{"en":"The collapse reportedly killed several servants.","zh":"據報這次倒塌導致數名僕人死亡。"},{"en":"To kill several servants means to cause the deaths of several household workers.","zh":"「kill several servants」意思是造成幾名家務或服務工作人員死亡。"},{"en":"A fire in an old mansion could kill servants if they were trapped in service rooms.","zh":"如果舊宅發生火災，而僕人被困在服務房間內，可能導致僕人死亡。"},{"en":"If part of a castle collapses without warning, people working inside may die.","zh":"如果城堡一部分毫無預警倒塌，在內工作的人可能死亡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a fatal consequence of a disaster.","zh":"這個短語描述災難造成的致命後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fully inhabited","meaning":"仍有人全面居住的","examples":[{"en":"The castle had been fully inhabited before the disaster.","zh":"災難發生前，城堡仍有人全面居住。"},{"en":"Fully inhabited means completely lived in or occupied by people.","zh":"「fully inhabited」意思是完全有人居住或使用。"},{"en":"A block of flats is fully inhabited when every apartment has residents.","zh":"當一幢公寓每個單位都有住戶時，它就是全面有人居住。"},{"en":"If a castle is fully inhabited, a collapse can endanger many people inside.","zh":"如果城堡仍有人全面居住，倒塌可能危及內裡很多人。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts an occupied building with an abandoned one.","zh":"這個短語對比有人居住的建築與荒廢建築。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"over the next hundred years or so","meaning":"在其後約一百年間","examples":[{"en":"Over the next hundred years or so, the building gradually deteriorated.","zh":"在其後約一百年間，建築逐漸惡化。"},{"en":"Over the next hundred years or so means during roughly the following century.","zh":"「over the next hundred years or so」意思是在之後大約一個世紀期間。"},{"en":"Over the next ten years or so, a small town may grow into a busy suburb.","zh":"在之後約十年間，一個小鎮可能發展成繁忙郊區。"},{"en":"If maintenance stops, a building can deteriorate slowly over many decades.","zh":"如果維修停止，建築可能在數十年間慢慢惡化。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate long time span.","zh":"這個短語提供大約的長時間跨度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"gradually fall into","meaning":"逐漸陷入……","examples":[{"en":"The castle gradually fell into serious disrepair.","zh":"城堡逐漸陷入嚴重失修狀態。"},{"en":"To gradually fall into a condition means to slowly enter that state over time.","zh":"「gradually fall into」某狀態，意思是隨時間慢慢進入該狀態。"},{"en":"A garden may gradually fall into neglect if nobody waters or cuts it.","zh":"如果沒有人澆水或修剪，花園可能逐漸陷入荒廢。"},{"en":"If a building is abandoned, weather damage can make it fall into disrepair.","zh":"如果建築被棄置，風雨損壞會令它陷入失修。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow decline into a worse state.","zh":"這個短語描述慢慢衰落至較差狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"present state of disrepair","meaning":"現今失修狀態","examples":[{"en":"The castle eventually reached its present state of disrepair.","zh":"城堡最終到達現今失修狀態。"},{"en":"Present state of disrepair means the damaged and poorly maintained condition it is in now.","zh":"「present state of disrepair」意思是它目前所處的損壞和缺乏維修狀況。"},{"en":"An old theatre’s present state of disrepair may include broken seats, leaking roofs, and cracked walls.","zh":"一座舊劇院的現今失修狀態可能包括破椅、漏水屋頂和裂牆。"},{"en":"If repairs are delayed for years, the present state of disrepair becomes harder to reverse.","zh":"如果維修拖延多年，現今失修狀態就更難逆轉。"},{"en":"The phrase describes current physical neglect and damage.","zh":"這個短語描述目前的實體荒廢和損壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be stripped of","meaning":"被剝去……","examples":[{"en":"The structure was stripped of its roofs by wind and weather.","zh":"該結構被風雨剝去了屋頂。"},{"en":"To be stripped of something means to have it removed, often forcefully or completely.","zh":"「be stripped of」某物，意思是被移除該物，常帶強行或完全的感覺。"},{"en":"A tree may be stripped of its leaves during a typhoon.","zh":"颱風期間，一棵樹可能被剝去葉子。"},{"en":"If a ruin is stripped of its roof, rain and wind can damage the inside more quickly.","zh":"如果遺跡被剝去屋頂，雨水和風會更快損壞內部。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests loss of an important covering or feature.","zh":"這個短語暗示失去重要覆蓋物或特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"wind and weather","meaning":"風雨","examples":[{"en":"Wind and weather gradually damaged the abandoned castle.","zh":"風雨逐漸損壞了被棄置的城堡。"},{"en":"Wind and weather means natural outdoor forces such as storms, rain, sun, and cold.","zh":"「wind and weather」指風暴、雨水、陽光和寒冷等戶外自然力量。"},{"en":"Wooden signs can fade and crack after years of wind and weather.","zh":"木製招牌經多年風雨後可能褪色和裂開。"},{"en":"If a building is not protected, wind and weather slowly wear it down.","zh":"如果建築沒有受到保護，風雨會慢慢侵蝕它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long-term natural exposure.","zh":"這個短語描述長期自然暴露。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be robbed of","meaning":"被奪去……","examples":[{"en":"The castle was robbed of much of its carved stonework.","zh":"城堡被奪去了大量雕刻石材。"},{"en":"To be robbed of something means to lose it because it was taken away unfairly or violently.","zh":"「be robbed of」某物，意思是因被不公平或強行取走而失去它。"},{"en":"A historic building may be robbed of its character if old windows are removed carelessly.","zh":"如果舊窗被粗心拆走，歷史建築可能被奪去其特色。"},{"en":"If people steal carved stone, a ruin is robbed of part of its beauty and history.","zh":"如果人們偷走雕刻石材，遺跡就被奪去部分美感和歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase describes loss caused by removal or theft.","zh":"這個短語描述因移除或偷竊造成的失去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"carved stonework","meaning":"雕刻石材","examples":[{"en":"People removed some of the castle’s carved stonework.","zh":"人們移走了城堡部分雕刻石材。"},{"en":"Carved stonework is stone that has been shaped or decorated by cutting designs into it.","zh":"「carved stonework」是經切割圖案而成形或裝飾的石材。"},{"en":"A church doorway may contain carved stonework showing flowers, animals, or saints.","zh":"教堂門口可能有展示花、動物或聖人的雕刻石材。"},{"en":"If carved stonework is removed, a building loses artistic and historical detail.","zh":"如果雕刻石材被移走，建築就失去藝術和歷史細節。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to decorative stone craftsmanship.","zh":"這個短語指裝飾性石工技藝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ruined and forlorn","meaning":"破敗而荒涼的","examples":[{"en":"The castle appears ruined and forlorn.","zh":"城堡看起來破敗而荒涼。"},{"en":"Ruined and forlorn means badly damaged and looking lonely or abandoned.","zh":"「ruined and forlorn」意思是嚴重損壞，而且看起來孤寂或被遺棄。"},{"en":"An empty railway station may look ruined and forlorn after decades without trains.","zh":"一座空置火車站若數十年沒有列車，可能看起來破敗而荒涼。"},{"en":"If people leave a building to decay, it may become both physically broken and emotionally sad.","zh":"如果人們任由建築腐朽，它可能同時在實體上破損、情感上悲涼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes damage together with loneliness.","zh":"這個短語同時描述損壞與孤寂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"one’s aspect","meaning":"……的外觀","examples":[{"en":"The castle’s aspect may be ruined, yet it remains impressive.","zh":"城堡的外觀雖然破敗，但仍令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"One’s aspect means one’s appearance, especially the way something looks from outside.","zh":"「one’s aspect」意思是某物的外觀，尤其是從外面看起來的樣子。"},{"en":"A building’s aspect can change completely when its windows, roof, and colour are altered.","zh":"如果窗戶、屋頂和顏色改變，建築的外觀可以完全不同。"},{"en":"If a ruin’s aspect is dramatic, visitors may admire it even in decay.","zh":"如果遺跡外觀具戲劇性，即使衰敗，遊客也可能欣賞它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to outward look or visual character.","zh":"這個短語指外在樣貌或視覺特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"haunting Celtic twilight","meaning":"令人難忘的凱爾特暮色","examples":[{"en":"The castle is especially atmospheric in the haunting Celtic twilight.","zh":"城堡在令人難忘的凱爾特暮色中特別有氣氛。"},{"en":"Haunting Celtic twilight means a mysterious, memorable evening light associated with Celtic atmosphere or imagination.","zh":"「haunting Celtic twilight」指一種神秘、難忘，並與凱爾特氛圍或想像相關的傍晚光線。"},{"en":"A quiet ruin can feel haunting at twilight when shadows cover the stones.","zh":"當暮色陰影覆蓋石頭時，寧靜遺跡可能顯得令人難忘。"},{"en":"If evening light makes a place feel ancient and magical, it becomes more atmospheric.","zh":"如果傍晚光線令地方感覺古老而有魔力，它就更有氣氛。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a mood of beauty, memory, and mystery.","zh":"這個短語營造美、記憶和神秘感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"long summer evenings","meaning":"漫長的夏日傍晚","examples":[{"en":"The ruins are striking during the long summer evenings.","zh":"遺跡在漫長的夏日傍晚格外引人注目。"},{"en":"Long summer evenings are late daylight hours in summer, when the light lasts longer than usual.","zh":"「long summer evenings」是夏季日照較長的傍晚時分。"},{"en":"Families may walk by the sea during long summer evenings because it stays bright after dinner.","zh":"家庭可能在漫長的夏日傍晚到海邊散步，因為晚飯後天仍光亮。"},{"en":"If evening light lasts longer, visitors have more time to enjoy the landscape slowly.","zh":"如果傍晚光線持續較久，遊客就有更多時間慢慢欣賞景觀。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests warmth, lingering light, and relaxed time.","zh":"這個短語暗示溫暖、停留的光線和放鬆時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be redolent of","meaning":"令人聯想到……","examples":[{"en":"The castle is redolent of another age.","zh":"這座城堡令人聯想到另一個時代。"},{"en":"To be redolent of something means to strongly remind people of it.","zh":"「be redolent of」某事，意思是強烈令人想起它。"},{"en":"An old classroom with wooden desks may be redolent of school life from decades ago.","zh":"一間有木書桌的舊課室，可能令人聯想到數十年前的校園生活。"},{"en":"If a ruin keeps old shapes and atmosphere, it can remind visitors of a vanished world.","zh":"如果遺跡保留舊形態和氣氛，它可以令遊客想起已消失的世界。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong association or evocation.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈聯想或喚起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"another age","meaning":"另一個時代","examples":[{"en":"The ruins evoke another age and another way of life.","zh":"遺跡令人想起另一個時代和另一種生活方式。"},{"en":"Another age means a different historical period, especially one that feels far removed from the present.","zh":"「another age」意思是另一個歷史時期，尤其是感覺離現代很遠的時期。"},{"en":"An old black-and-white photograph can make a city seem to belong to another age.","zh":"一張黑白舊照片可以令城市看起來屬於另一個時代。"},{"en":"If a place has ancient ruins, visitors may imagine how people lived in another time.","zh":"如果一個地方有古老遺跡，遊客可能想像另一時代的人如何生活。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests distance from modern life.","zh":"這個短語暗示與現代生活有距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"another dream","meaning":"另一個夢境","examples":[{"en":"In the twilight, the castle seems to belong to another dream.","zh":"在暮色中，城堡似乎屬於另一個夢境。"},{"en":"Another dream means a different, imagined, or unreal world or atmosphere.","zh":"「another dream」意思是另一個想像中或不真實的世界或氛圍。"},{"en":"A quiet beach at dawn may feel like another dream before the crowds arrive.","zh":"清晨人群到來前的寧靜海灘，可能感覺像另一個夢境。"},{"en":"If light, silence, and ruins combine, a real place can feel almost unreal.","zh":"如果光線、寂靜和遺跡結合，真實地方也可以感覺近乎不真實。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a poetic sense of mystery and distance.","zh":"這個短語營造詩意的神秘和距離感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a mile or so to the east","meaning":"在城堡以東約一英里","examples":[{"en":"Port na Spaniagh lies a mile or so to the east of the castle.","zh":"西班牙人港位於城堡以東約一英里。"},{"en":"A mile or so to the east means approximately one mile in the eastern direction.","zh":"「a mile or so to the east」意思是向東約一英里。"},{"en":"The old pier is a kilometre or so to the south of the hotel.","zh":"舊碼頭位於酒店以南約一公里。"},{"en":"If a site is only a mile or so away, visitors may walk there after seeing the castle.","zh":"如果一處地點只有大約一英里遠，遊客看完城堡後可能步行前往。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate nearby direction and distance.","zh":"這個短語提供大約的附近方向和距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Port na Spaniagh","meaning":"西班牙人港","examples":[{"en":"Port na Spaniagh is associated with a major maritime disaster.","zh":"西班牙人港與一場重大海難有關。"},{"en":"Port na Spaniagh is a named coastal location linked with Spanish history in the passage.","zh":"「Port na Spaniagh」是文中一個與西班牙歷史有關的具名海岸地點。"},{"en":"A guide may mention Port na Spaniagh when telling visitors about shipwrecks along the coast.","zh":"導遊講述沿岸沉船故事時，可能提到西班牙人港。"},{"en":"If a place is connected with a famous wreck, its name can carry historical weight.","zh":"如果一個地方與著名沉船有關，其名稱就可能承載歷史重量。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific coastal site.","zh":"這個短語命名一處特定海岸地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Neapolitan galleass","meaning":"那不勒斯大型槳帆船","examples":[{"en":"Girona was a Neapolitan galleass serving with the Spanish Armada.","zh":"Girona 是一艘隸屬西班牙無敵艦隊的那不勒斯大型槳帆船。"},{"en":"A Neapolitan galleass was a large oared and sailed warship from Naples or associated with Naples.","zh":"「Neapolitan galleass」是來自或與那不勒斯有關的大型槳帆戰船。"},{"en":"A museum label may describe an old warship as a galleass to show its size and military function.","zh":"博物館標籤可能把一艘古戰船描述為 galleass，以顯示其大小和軍事功能。"},{"en":"If such a vessel was part of a fleet, it could carry many soldiers and sailors.","zh":"如果這類船隻是一支艦隊的一部分，它可以載運許多士兵和水手。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific historical type of ship.","zh":"這個短語命名一種特定歷史船類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the Spanish Armada","meaning":"西班牙無敵艦隊","examples":[{"en":"Girona formed part of the Spanish Armada.","zh":"Girona 是西班牙無敵艦隊的一部分。"},{"en":"The Spanish Armada was a large Spanish naval fleet in the sixteenth century.","zh":"「the Spanish Armada」是十六世紀一支大型西班牙海軍艦隊。"},{"en":"Students learning European history may study the Spanish Armada as an example of naval conflict.","zh":"學習歐洲史的學生可能研究西班牙無敵艦隊，作為海戰衝突例子。"},{"en":"If a ship belonged to the Armada, its wreck connects local coastline with wider European history.","zh":"如果一艘船屬於無敵艦隊，其沉船就把本地海岸線與更廣泛歐洲歷史連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major historical fleet.","zh":"這個短語命名一支重大歷史艦隊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"go down","meaning":"沉沒","examples":[{"en":"Girona went down during a dark October night in 1588.","zh":"Girona 在1588年一個漆黑十月晚上沉沒。"},{"en":"For a ship, to go down means to sink.","zh":"對船隻而言，「go down」意思是沉沒。"},{"en":"A fishing boat may go down if a storm fills it with water.","zh":"如果風暴令漁船進水，它可能沉沒。"},{"en":"If a ship goes down near a rocky coast, only a few people may survive.","zh":"如果船隻在岩石海岸附近沉沒，可能只有少數人生還。"},{"en":"The phrase is a simple way to describe a sinking.","zh":"這個短語是描述船隻沉沒的簡單說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"one dark October night","meaning":"一個漆黑的十月晚上","examples":[{"en":"The ship was wrecked one dark October night.","zh":"那艘船在一個漆黑的十月晚上失事。"},{"en":"One dark October night means on a particular night in October when it was dark and possibly ominous.","zh":"「one dark October night」意思是在十月某個漆黑、可能帶不祥氣氛的晚上。"},{"en":"One dark winter night, the village lost electricity during a storm.","zh":"一個漆黑冬夜，村莊在風暴中停電。"},{"en":"If a disaster happens on a dark night, the story can feel more dramatic and frightening.","zh":"如果災難發生在漆黑夜晚，故事會感覺更戲劇化和可怕。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a specific, atmospheric time.","zh":"這個短語設定具體而有氣氛的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on its way to","meaning":"在前往……途中","examples":[{"en":"The vessel sank while it was on its way to Scotland.","zh":"該船在前往蘇格蘭途中沉沒。"},{"en":"On its way to a place means travelling towards that destination.","zh":"「on its way to」某地，意思是正朝該目的地前進。"},{"en":"The bus broke down while it was on its way to the airport.","zh":"巴士在前往機場途中壞了。"},{"en":"If a ship sinks on its way to port, it never reaches its intended destination.","zh":"如果船在前往港口途中沉沒，它就永遠無法抵達原定目的地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a journey in progress.","zh":"這個短語描述正在進行的旅程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"1,500-odd men","meaning":"約1,500人","examples":[{"en":"There were approximately 1,500 men on board.","zh":"船上約有1,500人。"},{"en":"1,500-odd men means roughly 1,500 men, perhaps slightly more or less.","zh":"「1,500-odd men」意思是大約1,500名男子，可能略多或略少。"},{"en":"A concert with 2,000-odd people is crowded, but the exact number is not important.","zh":"一場有約2,000人的音樂會很擁擠，但確切數字不是重點。"},{"en":"If 1,500-odd men were on a ship, a wreck would be a major disaster.","zh":"如果船上有約1,500人，失事就會是重大災難。"},{"en":"The word “odd” here means approximate, not strange.","zh":"這裡的 “odd” 意思是大約，而不是奇怪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"on board","meaning":"在船上","examples":[{"en":"Only nine of the men on board survived.","zh":"船上只有九人生還。"},{"en":"On board means on or inside a ship, plane, train, or other vehicle.","zh":"「on board」意思是在船、飛機、火車或其他交通工具上。"},{"en":"Passengers on board the plane were asked to fasten their seat belts.","zh":"飛機上的乘客被要求扣好安全帶。"},{"en":"If only a few people on board survive, the accident is extremely serious.","zh":"如果交通工具上只有少數人生還，事故就極其嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies people or things carried by a vehicle.","zh":"這個短語指出交通工具上載有的人或物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"survive the disaster","meaning":"在災難中生還","examples":[{"en":"Only a handful of men survived the disaster.","zh":"只有少數人在災難中生還。"},{"en":"To survive the disaster means to stay alive after a terrible accident or event.","zh":"「survive the disaster」意思是在可怕事故或事件後仍然生存。"},{"en":"Families may survive a flood by moving to higher ground before the water rises.","zh":"家庭可能在洪水上升前移到高地，因而在洪災中生還。"},{"en":"If a ship sinks in stormy water, surviving the disaster can depend on luck, strength, and rescue.","zh":"如果船在風暴海面沉沒，能否生還可能取決於運氣、體力和救援。"},{"en":"The phrase describes living through danger.","zh":"這個短語描述經歷危險後仍活着。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"even further to the east","meaning":"再往東面","examples":[{"en":"The Giant’s Causeway lies even further to the east.","zh":"巨人堤道位於再往東面。"},{"en":"Even further to the east means at a location still farther in the eastern direction.","zh":"「even further to the east」意思是在更遠的東面位置。"},{"en":"The museum is east of the hotel, and the harbour is even further to the east.","zh":"博物館在酒店東面，而港口再往東面。"},{"en":"If travellers continue eastward, they may reach another famous site.","zh":"如果旅客繼續向東，他們可能到達另一著名景點。"},{"en":"The phrase extends a direction beyond a previous point.","zh":"這個短語把方向延伸到前一點以外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the Giant’s Causeway","meaning":"巨人堤道","examples":[{"en":"The Giant’s Causeway is one of the region’s greatest natural attractions.","zh":"巨人堤道是該地區最重要的自然景點之一。"},{"en":"The Giant’s Causeway is a famous coastal rock formation made of basalt columns.","zh":"「the Giant’s Causeway」是一處由玄武岩柱形成的著名海岸岩石地貌。"},{"en":"Tourists visit the Giant’s Causeway to walk among unusual stone shapes beside the sea.","zh":"遊客到巨人堤道，在海邊奇特石形之間步行。"},{"en":"Because its rocks look almost designed, visitors often connect it with legend and geology.","zh":"因為其岩石看起來幾乎像被設計過，遊客常把它與傳說和地質連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific natural landmark.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定自然地標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stunning coastline","meaning":"壯麗海岸線","examples":[{"en":"The Giant’s Causeway forms part of a stunning coastline.","zh":"巨人堤道是壯麗海岸線的一部分。"},{"en":"A stunning coastline is a stretch of coast that is extremely beautiful or impressive.","zh":"「stunning coastline」是一段極其美麗或令人印象深刻的海岸。"},{"en":"A drive beside cliffs, beaches, and blue water can reveal a stunning coastline.","zh":"沿懸崖、海灘和藍色海水駕車，可以展現壯麗海岸線。"},{"en":"If a coastline is stunning, it may attract photographers, walkers, and nature lovers.","zh":"如果海岸線壯麗，它可能吸引攝影者、步行者和自然愛好者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes coastal scenery with strong visual impact.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺衝擊強烈的海岸景色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"strangely symmetrical","meaning":"異常對稱的","examples":[{"en":"The basalt columns appear strangely symmetrical.","zh":"玄武岩柱看起來異常對稱。"},{"en":"Strangely symmetrical means unusually balanced, regular, or matching in shape.","zh":"「strangely symmetrical」意思是在形狀上異常平衡、規律或相配。"},{"en":"A row of natural stones may look strangely symmetrical, almost like a human design.","zh":"一排天然石頭可能看起來異常對稱，幾乎像人造設計。"},{"en":"If natural rocks look too regular, visitors may wonder how they were formed.","zh":"如果天然岩石看起來太規律，遊客可能好奇它們如何形成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes surprising order in appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述外觀上令人驚訝的秩序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"columns of dark basalt","meaning":"深色玄武岩柱","examples":[{"en":"The coastline contains columns of dark basalt.","zh":"海岸線上有深色玄武岩柱。"},{"en":"Columns of dark basalt are tall or pillar-like pieces of dark volcanic rock.","zh":"「columns of dark basalt」是高而像柱子的深色火山岩。"},{"en":"Children may think basalt columns look like stone steps made by giants.","zh":"孩子可能覺得玄武岩柱看起來像巨人造的石階。"},{"en":"If lava cools in certain ways, it can form regular basalt columns.","zh":"如果熔岩以某些方式冷卻，它可以形成規律玄武岩柱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a distinctive volcanic rock formation.","zh":"這個短語描述獨特火山岩地貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"geological wonder","meaning":"地質奇觀","examples":[{"en":"The Giant’s Causeway is a remarkable geological wonder.","zh":"巨人堤道是一處非凡的地質奇觀。"},{"en":"A geological wonder is a natural rock or landform feature that is scientifically interesting and visually impressive.","zh":"「geological wonder」是科學上有趣、視覺上令人印象深刻的天然岩石或地貌。"},{"en":"A canyon, cave system, or volcanic island can be a geological wonder.","zh":"峽谷、洞穴系統或火山島都可以是地質奇觀。"},{"en":"If a place shows unusual rock formation, it can attract both tourists and scientists.","zh":"如果一個地方顯示不尋常岩石形成，它可以吸引遊客和科學家。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a natural feature shaped by Earth processes.","zh":"這個短語描述由地球過程塑造的自然特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be worth seeing","meaning":"值得一看","examples":[{"en":"The Causeway is certainly worth seeing.","zh":"巨人堤道確實值得一看。"},{"en":"To be worth seeing means to be interesting, beautiful, or important enough to visit or look at.","zh":"「be worth seeing」意思是有趣、美麗或重要到值得參觀或觀看。"},{"en":"A small museum may be worth seeing if it explains local history clearly.","zh":"如果小博物館清楚解釋本地歷史，它可能值得一看。"},{"en":"If a place is worth seeing, travellers feel the time and effort are justified.","zh":"如果一個地方值得一看，旅客會覺得花時間和力氣是合理的。"},{"en":"The phrase recommends a place or sight.","zh":"這個短語用來推薦地方或景點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not worth going to see","meaning":"不值得特意前往觀看","examples":[{"en":"One traveller once claimed that it was not worth going to see.","zh":"曾有一位旅客聲稱它不值得特意前往觀看。"},{"en":"Not worth going to see means not interesting or impressive enough to justify the trip.","zh":"「not worth going to see」意思是不夠有趣或令人印象深刻，不值得為它跑一趟。"},{"en":"A restaurant may be not worth going to see if the food is ordinary and the journey is long.","zh":"如果餐廳食物普通而路程很長，它可能不值得特意前往。"},{"en":"If travel is difficult, people judge more carefully whether a place is worth the effort.","zh":"如果交通困難，人們會更仔細判斷一個地方是否值得費力前往。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a negative travel judgement.","zh":"這個短語給出負面的旅遊評價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the days of horses and carriages","meaning":"馬車年代","examples":[{"en":"Travel was far more difficult in the days of horses and carriages.","zh":"在馬車年代，旅行困難得多。"},{"en":"The days of horses and carriages means the period before modern cars, when people travelled by horse-drawn transport.","zh":"「the days of horses and carriages」指現代汽車以前，人們使用馬拉交通工具的時代。"},{"en":"In the days of horses and carriages, a journey of 30 miles could take many hours.","zh":"在馬車年代，30英里的旅程可能需要許多小時。"},{"en":"If transport was slow and uncomfortable, people might avoid distant tourist sites.","zh":"如果交通緩慢又不舒服，人們可能避開遙遠景點。"},{"en":"The phrase evokes an older era of travel.","zh":"這個短語喚起較古老的旅行時代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be well worth a visit","meaning":"非常值得遊覽","examples":[{"en":"The Giant’s Causeway is well worth a visit.","zh":"巨人堤道非常值得遊覽。"},{"en":"To be well worth a visit means definitely worth the time and effort to go there.","zh":"「be well worth a visit」意思是絕對值得花時間和力氣前往。"},{"en":"A small old temple can be well worth a visit if it tells the story of the neighbourhood.","zh":"如果一座小古廟講述社區故事，它可以非常值得遊覽。"},{"en":"If a place is beautiful, meaningful, and unusual, it is well worth visiting.","zh":"如果一個地方美麗、有意義又不尋常，它就非常值得去。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly recommends a place.","zh":"這個短語強烈推薦一個地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"last lingering moments","meaning":"暮色最後停留的片刻","examples":[{"en":"The last lingering moments of twilight are particularly beautiful.","zh":"暮色最後停留的片刻特別美麗。"},{"en":"Last lingering moments are the final moments that remain slowly before something ends.","zh":"「last lingering moments」是某事結束前最後慢慢停留的片刻。"},{"en":"The last lingering moments of a school holiday can feel both peaceful and sad.","zh":"學校假期最後停留的片刻，可能同時令人感到平靜和傷感。"},{"en":"If twilight lingers, the landscape may glow softly before night falls.","zh":"如果暮色停留，夜幕降臨前地貌可能柔和發亮。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the beauty of something almost ending.","zh":"這個短語突出某事快將結束時的美。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"twilight hours","meaning":"黃昏時分","examples":[{"en":"The twilight hours are the best time to experience the coast.","zh":"黃昏時分是體驗海岸的最佳時間。"},{"en":"Twilight hours are the period just after sunset or just before darkness when the light is soft.","zh":"「twilight hours」是日落後或天黑前光線柔和的一段時間。"},{"en":"Photographers often prefer twilight hours because colours look gentle and dramatic.","zh":"攝影師常喜歡黃昏時分，因為色彩看起來柔和而有戲劇感。"},{"en":"If visitors arrive during twilight hours, crowds may be smaller and the atmosphere deeper.","zh":"如果遊客在黃昏時分到達，人群可能較少，氣氛更深。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the special light between day and night.","zh":"這個短語指日與夜之間的特殊光線時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the best time to savour","meaning":"細味……的最佳時間","examples":[{"en":"Evening is the best time to savour the landscape’s atmosphere.","zh":"傍晚是細味地貌氣氛的最佳時間。"},{"en":"The best time to savour something is the moment when it can be enjoyed most fully and slowly.","zh":"「the best time to savour」某事，是最能充分而慢慢享受它的時刻。"},{"en":"Early morning may be the best time to savour a quiet city before traffic begins.","zh":"清晨可能是細味寧靜城市的最佳時間，因為交通尚未開始。"},{"en":"If crowds disappear at dusk, visitors can savour the place more deeply.","zh":"如果人群在黃昏散去，遊客就能更深入細味該處。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests slow appreciation, not a quick glance.","zh":"這個短語暗示慢慢欣賞，而不是匆匆一看。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"savour the full power of","meaning":"細味……的全部魅力","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can savour the full power of the coastline’s magic.","zh":"遊客可以細味海岸線魅力的全部力量。"},{"en":"To savour the full power of something means to slowly experience and appreciate its complete effect.","zh":"「savour the full power of」某事，意思是慢慢體驗並欣賞其完整效果。"},{"en":"A listener may savour the full power of a song when hearing it live in a quiet hall.","zh":"聽眾在寧靜音樂廳現場聽歌時，可能細味歌曲的全部力量。"},{"en":"If visitors slow down and stay until dusk, they may feel the landscape more intensely.","zh":"如果遊客慢下來並留到黃昏，他們可能更強烈感受地貌。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests deep, deliberate enjoyment.","zh":"這個短語暗示深入而有意識的享受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"coastline’s magic","meaning":"海岸線的魅力","examples":[{"en":"The quiet evening reveals the coastline’s magic.","zh":"寧靜傍晚展現海岸線的魅力。"},{"en":"The coastline’s magic means the special beauty, atmosphere, or emotional effect of the coast.","zh":"「coastline’s magic」意思是海岸的特殊美感、氛圍或情感效果。"},{"en":"A misty morning can reveal a harbour’s magic when boats appear slowly through fog.","zh":"霧氣清晨，當船隻慢慢從霧中出現，港口魅力可能展現出來。"},{"en":"If light, sea, and silence combine, the coastline can feel almost enchanted.","zh":"如果光線、大海和寂靜結合，海岸線可能感覺近乎被施了魔法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes emotional attraction rather than literal magic.","zh":"這個短語描述情感吸引力，而不是字面魔法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"come into its own","meaning":"展現真正魅力","examples":[{"en":"The Giant’s Causeway comes into its own after most tourists leave.","zh":"大多數遊客離開後，巨人堤道才展現真正魅力。"},{"en":"To come into its own means to show its true value or beauty in the right conditions.","zh":"「come into its own」意思是在合適條件下展現真正價值或美。"},{"en":"A quiet café comes into its own on rainy afternoons when people want warmth and calm.","zh":"雨天下午，人們需要溫暖和寧靜時，安靜咖啡店會展現真正魅力。"},{"en":"If a place is crowded by day, it may come into its own when silence returns.","zh":"如果一個地方日間擁擠，當寂靜回來時，它可能展現真正魅力。"},{"en":"The phrase means something finally shows what makes it special.","zh":"這個短語意思是某事終於顯示其特別之處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"if you are very lucky","meaning":"如果你非常幸運","examples":[{"en":"If you are very lucky, you may have the Causeway to yourself.","zh":"如果你非常幸運，你可能可以獨享巨人堤道。"},{"en":"If you are very lucky means only if circumstances are unusually favourable.","zh":"「if you are very lucky」意思是只有在情況異常有利時。"},{"en":"If you are very lucky, the museum may be almost empty when you arrive.","zh":"如果你非常幸運，到達博物館時裡面可能幾乎沒有人。"},{"en":"If few tourists are present, a famous place can feel private and peaceful.","zh":"如果遊客很少，著名景點可以感覺私密而寧靜。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a pleasant but uncertain possibility.","zh":"這個短語暗示令人愉快但不確定的可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have the place to oneself","meaning":"獨享該處","examples":[{"en":"Late visitors may have the place entirely to themselves.","zh":"晚到的遊客可能完全獨享該處。"},{"en":"To have the place to oneself means to be the only person or group there, without crowds.","zh":"「have the place to oneself」意思是自己或自己的小組是那裡唯一的人，沒有群眾。"},{"en":"A student may have the library to herself early in the morning.","zh":"學生清晨可能獨享圖書館。"},{"en":"If you have a famous viewpoint to yourself, the experience feels quieter and more personal.","zh":"如果你獨享一個著名觀景點，經歷會感覺更寧靜和個人化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes private enjoyment of a usually public place.","zh":"這個短語描述私密地享受通常公共的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"circular walk","meaning":"環形步行路線","examples":[{"en":"A fine circular walk leads visitors through the site.","zh":"一條優美環形步行路線帶領遊客穿過該景點。"},{"en":"A circular walk is a walking route that starts and ends at the same point.","zh":"「circular walk」是起點和終點相同的步行路線。"},{"en":"A park may offer a circular walk around a lake for families and joggers.","zh":"公園可能提供環繞湖泊的環形步行路線，供家庭和跑步人士使用。"},{"en":"If a route is circular, visitors do not need to return by the same path.","zh":"如果路線是環形的，遊客就不需要沿原路返回。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a loop-shaped walking route.","zh":"這個短語描述環狀步行路線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"take someone down to","meaning":"帶某人下到……","examples":[{"en":"The walking route takes visitors down to the Grand Causeway.","zh":"步行路線帶遊客下到巨人堤道主體。"},{"en":"To take someone down to a place means to lead or bring them to a lower or nearby location.","zh":"「take someone down to」某地，意思是帶領或引導某人到較低或附近的位置。"},{"en":"A guide may take tourists down to the harbour after showing them the old town.","zh":"導遊介紹舊城後，可能帶遊客下到港口。"},{"en":"If a path descends from cliffs to the shore, it takes walkers down to the sea.","zh":"如果小路從懸崖下降到岸邊，它就帶步行者下到海邊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes guided or route-based movement to a place.","zh":"這個短語描述由導遊或路線引導前往某處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the Grand Causeway","meaning":"巨人堤道主體","examples":[{"en":"The circular route passes through the Grand Causeway.","zh":"環形路線經過巨人堤道主體。"},{"en":"The Grand Causeway is the main or most prominent section of the Giant’s Causeway formation.","zh":"「the Grand Causeway」是巨人堤道地貌中主要或最突出的部分。"},{"en":"Visitors may spend the most time at the Grand Causeway because the stone columns are easy to see there.","zh":"遊客可能在巨人堤道主體花最多時間，因為石柱在那裡最容易看見。"},{"en":"If a route passes through the main feature, tourists experience the heart of the site.","zh":"如果路線經過主要景觀，旅客就能體驗景點核心。"},{"en":"The phrase names a principal part of the natural landmark.","zh":"這個短語命名自然地標的主要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"amphitheatres of stone columns","meaning":"圓形劇場般的石柱群","examples":[{"en":"The path passes amphitheatres of stone columns.","zh":"小路經過圓形劇場般的石柱群。"},{"en":"Amphitheatres of stone columns are curved or enclosed-looking groups of rock columns that resemble theatre spaces.","zh":"「amphitheatres of stone columns」是彎曲或像圍合空間的岩柱群，外觀類似劇場。"},{"en":"A circle of cliffs may look like an amphitheatre when people stand inside it.","zh":"當人站在其中，一圈懸崖可能看起來像圓形劇場。"},{"en":"If stone columns surround visitors, the landscape can feel architectural and dramatic.","zh":"如果石柱包圍遊客，地貌會感覺具建築感和戲劇性。"},{"en":"The phrase compares natural rock shapes to built performance spaces.","zh":"這個短語把天然岩石形狀比作人造表演空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rock formations","meaning":"岩石形態","examples":[{"en":"The site contains many remarkable rock formations.","zh":"該景點有許多非凡岩石形態。"},{"en":"Rock formations are natural shapes or structures made of rock.","zh":"「rock formations」是由岩石形成的天然形狀或結構。"},{"en":"Caves, cliffs, arches, and columns are different kinds of rock formations.","zh":"洞穴、懸崖、拱門和石柱都是不同種類的岩石形態。"},{"en":"If a coastline has unusual rock formations, tourists may stop to photograph them.","zh":"如果海岸線有不尋常岩石形態，遊客可能停下來拍照。"},{"en":"The phrase describes natural geological shapes.","zh":"這個短語描述天然地質形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not frightening, but…","meaning":"並不可怕，但……","examples":[{"en":"The place is not frightening, but it possesses an unusual power.","zh":"這個地方並不可怕，但它擁有一種不尋常力量。"},{"en":"Not frightening, but… means something is not scary in an obvious way, yet still has a strong or strange effect.","zh":"「not frightening, but…」意思是某事不是明顯令人害怕，卻仍有強烈或奇異效果。"},{"en":"An empty church at night may be not frightening, but deeply quiet and powerful.","zh":"夜晚空無一人的教堂可能並不可怕，但非常寧靜而有力量。"},{"en":"If a place feels strange without causing fear, this contrast helps describe the mood.","zh":"如果一個地方感覺奇特但不令人恐懼，這種對比有助描述氣氛。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a subtle emotional contrast.","zh":"這個短語引入細微情感對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a power in the place","meaning":"該處有一股力量","examples":[{"en":"Visitors often sense a power in the place.","zh":"遊客常感覺該處有一股力量。"},{"en":"A power in the place means a strong atmosphere or emotional force that people can feel there.","zh":"「a power in the place」意思是人們在那裡能感到的一種強烈氣氛或情感力量。"},{"en":"A memorial garden may have a power in the place because people go there to remember loss.","zh":"紀念花園可能有一股力量，因為人們到那裡記念失去。"},{"en":"If history, silence, and landscape combine, a place may feel unusually powerful.","zh":"如果歷史、寂靜和地貌結合，一個地方可能感覺異常有力量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes atmosphere rather than physical strength.","zh":"這個短語描述氛圍，而不是實際力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tangible yet inexplicable","meaning":"可以感受到但難以解釋的","examples":[{"en":"The atmosphere feels tangible yet inexplicable.","zh":"氣氛感覺可以感受到但難以解釋。"},{"en":"Tangible yet inexplicable means clearly felt but difficult to explain logically.","zh":"「tangible yet inexplicable」意思是清楚感覺得到，但難以用邏輯解釋。"},{"en":"The sadness in an old family home may feel tangible yet inexplicable to visitors.","zh":"一間舊家庭住所中的傷感，對訪客而言可能可以感受到但難以解釋。"},{"en":"If people can sense a mood but cannot identify its cause, it feels mysterious.","zh":"如果人們能感到某種氣氛卻說不出成因，它就顯得神秘。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something emotionally real but hard to define.","zh":"這個短語描述情感上真實但難以定義的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the blackness of the night","meaning":"夜色的漆黑","examples":[{"en":"The blackness of the night can make the landscape unsettling.","zh":"夜色的漆黑可以令地貌顯得令人不安。"},{"en":"The blackness of the night means the deep darkness after daylight has completely disappeared.","zh":"「the blackness of the night」意思是日光完全消失後的深沉黑暗。"},{"en":"The blackness of the night can make an empty road feel longer and quieter.","zh":"夜色的漆黑可以令空蕩道路感覺更長和更安靜。"},{"en":"If a coastline is dark and silent, visitors may feel small or uneasy.","zh":"如果海岸線黑暗而寂靜，遊客可能感到渺小或不安。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises intense darkness.","zh":"這個短語強調強烈黑暗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"conjure up","meaning":"喚起；使人產生……","examples":[{"en":"The darkness can conjure up feelings of unease.","zh":"黑暗可以喚起不安感。"},{"en":"To conjure up something means to bring it to mind or make people feel it vividly.","zh":"「conjure up」某事，意思是令人想起它或鮮明地感受到它。"},{"en":"The smell of old books can conjure up memories of school libraries.","zh":"舊書氣味可以喚起學校圖書館的記憶。"},{"en":"If a place is dark and silent, it may conjure up fear or mystery.","zh":"如果一個地方黑暗而寂靜，它可能喚起恐懼或神秘感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating a strong image, memory, or feeling.","zh":"這個短語描述創造強烈畫面、記憶或感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"feelings of eeriness","meaning":"詭異感","examples":[{"en":"The black landscape can create feelings of eeriness.","zh":"黑暗地貌可以產生詭異感。"},{"en":"Feelings of eeriness are sensations of strangeness, mystery, or slight fear.","zh":"「feelings of eeriness」是奇怪、神秘或略帶恐懼的感覺。"},{"en":"A quiet corridor at night may give students feelings of eeriness even if nothing is dangerous.","zh":"夜晚寧靜走廊即使沒有危險，也可能給學生詭異感。"},{"en":"If shadows hide familiar shapes, a place can begin to feel eerie.","zh":"如果陰影遮住熟悉形狀，一個地方可能開始顯得詭異。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strange and unsettling mood.","zh":"這個短語描述奇異而令人不安的氣氛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"unease","meaning":"不安","examples":[{"en":"The site can produce a subtle sense of unease.","zh":"該景點可以產生一種微妙的不安感。"},{"en":"Unease is a quiet feeling of worry, discomfort, or nervousness.","zh":"「unease」是安靜的憂慮、不適或緊張感。"},{"en":"A student may feel unease before opening an important exam result.","zh":"學生打開重要考試成績前可能感到不安。"},{"en":"If a place is silent, dark, and unfamiliar, it can create unease.","zh":"如果一個地方寂靜、黑暗又陌生，它可以造成不安。"},{"en":"The word describes mild anxiety rather than extreme fear.","zh":"這個詞描述輕微焦慮，而不是極度恐懼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"realise one’s place","meaning":"意識到自己的位置","examples":[{"en":"The visitor realises his or her place within the enormous landscape.","zh":"遊客意識到自己在巨大地貌中的位置。"},{"en":"To realise one’s place means to understand one’s size, role, or importance in relation to something larger.","zh":"「realise one’s place」意思是理解自己相對於更大事物的大小、角色或重要性。"},{"en":"Looking at the stars can make a person realise their place in the universe.","zh":"觀看星空可以令人意識到自己在宇宙中的位置。"},{"en":"If a landscape is huge and ancient, visitors may feel small and humbled.","zh":"如果地貌巨大而古老，遊客可能感到渺小和謙卑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a moment of perspective.","zh":"這個短語描述獲得視角的一刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in the scheme of","meaning":"在……的整體格局中","examples":[{"en":"People may feel small in the scheme of the natural spectacle.","zh":"在自然奇觀的整體格局中，人們可能感到渺小。"},{"en":"In the scheme of something means within the larger arrangement, scale, or context of it.","zh":"「in the scheme of」某事，意思是在其更大安排、尺度或背景中。"},{"en":"One test is important, but in the scheme of a whole education, it is only one part.","zh":"一次測驗很重要，但在整個教育的格局中，它只是一部分。"},{"en":"If a person stands before a vast cliff, they may feel tiny in the scheme of nature.","zh":"如果一個人站在巨大懸崖前，可能在自然格局中感到渺小。"},{"en":"The phrase places something within a larger context.","zh":"這個短語把某事置於更大背景中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"magnificent spectacle","meaning":"壯麗景象","examples":[{"en":"The coastline forms a magnificent natural spectacle.","zh":"海岸線形成一幅壯麗自然景象。"},{"en":"A magnificent spectacle is an impressive and beautiful sight that attracts attention.","zh":"「magnificent spectacle」是令人印象深刻、吸引注意的美麗景象。"},{"en":"Fireworks over a harbour can be a magnificent spectacle during a festival.","zh":"節日期間港口上空的煙花可以是壯麗景象。"},{"en":"If cliffs, sea, and evening light combine, the result can be visually powerful.","zh":"如果懸崖、大海和傍晚光線結合，結果可以非常有視覺力量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a grand scene, not an ordinary view.","zh":"這個短語描述宏大的景象，而不是普通景色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"once experienced","meaning":"一經體驗","examples":[{"en":"Once experienced, the landscape is difficult to forget.","zh":"一經體驗，這片地貌便難以忘記。"},{"en":"Once experienced means after someone has personally gone through or seen it.","zh":"「once experienced」意思是當某人親身經歷或看見它之後。"},{"en":"Once experienced, a kind teacher’s encouragement can stay with a student for years.","zh":"一經體驗，一位好老師的鼓勵可以在學生心中停留多年。"},{"en":"If a place creates a strong emotional impression, it remains in memory after the visit.","zh":"如果一個地方造成強烈情感印象，遊覽後仍會留在記憶中。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that direct experience changes how something is remembered.","zh":"這個短語顯示親身經驗會改變某事被記住的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"impossible to forget","meaning":"難以忘記","examples":[{"en":"The grandeur of the Causeway is impossible to forget.","zh":"巨人堤道的宏偉氣勢令人難以忘記。"},{"en":"Impossible to forget means so powerful or memorable that it stays in the mind.","zh":"「impossible to forget」意思是強烈或難忘到會留在腦海中。"},{"en":"A student’s first successful public speech may be impossible to forget.","zh":"學生第一次成功公開演講可能難以忘記。"},{"en":"If a place combines beauty, danger, and mystery, visitors may remember it for life.","zh":"如果一個地方結合美、危險和神秘，遊客可能一生記得。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a lasting memory.","zh":"這個短語描述持久記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"grandeur of the landscape","meaning":"地貌的宏偉氣勢","examples":[{"en":"Visitors remember the grandeur of the landscape.","zh":"遊客記得地貌的宏偉氣勢。"},{"en":"The grandeur of the landscape is the impressive greatness, beauty, and scale of the natural scene.","zh":"「grandeur of the landscape」是自然景象令人印象深刻的宏大、美感和尺度。"},{"en":"The grandeur of a mountain valley can make hikers stop speaking for a moment.","zh":"山谷的宏偉氣勢可以令遠足者一時間停止說話。"},{"en":"If a landscape is vast and dramatic, people may feel awe rather than simple pleasure.","zh":"如果地貌廣闊而具戲劇性，人們可能感到敬畏，而不只是愉快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes majestic natural beauty.","zh":"這個短語描述莊嚴宏偉的自然美。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"beyond the Causeway","meaning":"在巨人堤道以外","examples":[{"en":"The Carrick-a-Rede Rope Bridge lies beyond the Causeway.","zh":"卡里克索橋位於巨人堤道以外。"},{"en":"Beyond the Causeway means farther away than the Causeway, usually along the route being described.","zh":"「beyond the Causeway」意思是在巨人堤道更遠處，通常沿着所描述路線。"},{"en":"Beyond the museum, visitors can find a small garden and café.","zh":"博物館以外，遊客可以找到小花園和咖啡店。"},{"en":"If an attraction lies beyond a famous site, travellers may continue their journey to reach it.","zh":"如果一個景點位於著名地點以外，旅客可能繼續旅程前往。"},{"en":"The phrase places one location farther along from another.","zh":"這個短語把一個位置放在另一位置更遠處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"connect the mainland with","meaning":"將大陸與……連接","examples":[{"en":"The bridge connects the mainland with a rocky island.","zh":"這座橋將大陸與一個岩石小島連接。"},{"en":"To connect the mainland with a place means to link the main land area to that separate place.","zh":"「connect the mainland with」某地，意思是把主要陸地與該分離地點連起來。"},{"en":"A ferry connects the mainland with the small island every morning.","zh":"渡輪每天早上將大陸與小島連接。"},{"en":"If a bridge connects the mainland with an island, people can cross without a boat.","zh":"如果橋將大陸與島連接，人們就可以不用船過去。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a physical link between two land areas.","zh":"這個短語描述兩片土地之間的實體連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"outcrop of rock","meaning":"岩石露頭","examples":[{"en":"The bridge leads to an outcrop of rock in the Atlantic.","zh":"這座橋通往大西洋中的一處岩石露頭。"},{"en":"An outcrop of rock is a piece or mass of rock that sticks out from the surrounding surface.","zh":"「outcrop of rock」是從周圍表面突出的一塊或一大片岩石。"},{"en":"A climber may stand on an outcrop of rock to look over the valley.","zh":"攀山者可能站在岩石露頭上俯瞰山谷。"},{"en":"If an outcrop rises from the sea, it can become a small island-like feature.","zh":"如果露頭從海中升起，它可以成為像小島的地貌。"},{"en":"The phrase describes exposed rock projecting outward.","zh":"這個短語描述向外突出的外露岩石。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"jut out of","meaning":"從……突出","examples":[{"en":"The rocky island juts out of the turbulent Atlantic.","zh":"岩石小島從波濤洶湧的大西洋中突出。"},{"en":"To jut out of something means to stick out sharply or noticeably from it.","zh":"「jut out of」某物，意思是從其中明顯或尖銳地伸出。"},{"en":"A balcony may jut out of an apartment building above the street.","zh":"陽台可能從公寓大樓伸出到街道上方。"},{"en":"If a rock juts out of the sea, waves may crash around it strongly.","zh":"如果岩石從海中突出，海浪可能猛烈地在其周圍拍打。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a projecting shape.","zh":"這個短語描述突出的形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Carrick-a-Rede Rope Bridge","meaning":"卡里克索橋","examples":[{"en":"The Carrick-a-Rede Rope Bridge crosses a deep sea chasm.","zh":"卡里克索橋跨越一道深海裂谷。"},{"en":"The Carrick-a-Rede Rope Bridge is a famous rope bridge linking the mainland to a rocky island.","zh":"「Carrick-a-Rede Rope Bridge」是一座著名繩索橋，將大陸與岩石小島連接。"},{"en":"Visitors may feel nervous crossing the Carrick-a-Rede Rope Bridge because it hangs high above the water.","zh":"遊客過卡里克索橋時可能感到緊張，因為它懸在海水上方高處。"},{"en":"If a bridge crosses a deep chasm, it can become both a practical route and a tourist challenge.","zh":"如果橋跨越深谷，它可以同時成為實用通道和旅遊挑戰。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific coastal bridge.","zh":"這個短語命名一座特定海岸橋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"when first constructed","meaning":"最初建造時","examples":[{"en":"When first constructed, the bridge was extremely simple.","zh":"最初建造時，這座橋極為簡單。"},{"en":"When first constructed means at the time when something was originally built.","zh":"「when first constructed」意思是在某物最初建成的時候。"},{"en":"When first constructed, the old school had only four classrooms.","zh":"最初建造時，那所舊學校只有四間課室。"},{"en":"If a structure was simple when first constructed, later versions may be safer and stronger.","zh":"如果結構最初建造時很簡單，後來版本可能更安全和堅固。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts original design with later changes.","zh":"這個短語對比原初設計與後來變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rope handrail","meaning":"繩索扶手","examples":[{"en":"The original bridge had only a simple rope handrail.","zh":"原本的橋只有一條簡單繩索扶手。"},{"en":"A rope handrail is a rope used as a support for people to hold while crossing or walking.","zh":"「rope handrail」是供人通過或步行時握住支撐的繩索。"},{"en":"A temporary path may have a rope handrail to help hikers keep balance.","zh":"臨時小路可能有繩索扶手，幫助遠足者保持平衡。"},{"en":"If a bridge has only a rope handrail, crossing it may feel exposed and unsafe.","zh":"如果橋只有繩索扶手，通過時可能感覺暴露而不安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a basic safety feature made of rope.","zh":"這個短語描述由繩索製成的基本安全設施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"widely spaced slats","meaning":"間距很大的踏板","examples":[{"en":"The bridge originally had widely spaced wooden slats.","zh":"這座橋原本有間距很大的木踏板。"},{"en":"Widely spaced slats are narrow pieces of wood placed with large gaps between them.","zh":"「widely spaced slats」是彼此之間有大空隙的窄木條。"},{"en":"A garden bench with widely spaced slats may feel uncomfortable for small children.","zh":"有間距很大木條的花園長椅，對小孩而言可能不舒服。"},{"en":"If bridge slats are widely spaced, people can see the drop below and feel nervous.","zh":"如果橋上踏板間距很大，人們可以看見下方落差，因而緊張。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a structure with noticeable gaps.","zh":"這個短語描述有明顯空隙的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be used mainly by","meaning":"主要由……使用","examples":[{"en":"The early bridge was used mainly by salmon fishermen.","zh":"早期的橋主要由鮭魚漁民使用。"},{"en":"To be used mainly by a group means that group is the primary user.","zh":"「be used mainly by」某群體，意思是該群體是主要使用者。"},{"en":"A staff entrance is used mainly by employees, not by customers.","zh":"員工入口主要由員工使用，而不是顧客。"},{"en":"If a bridge is used mainly by fishermen, it may be designed for work rather than tourism.","zh":"如果一座橋主要由漁民使用，它可能是為工作而非旅遊設計。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main users of something.","zh":"這個短語指出某物的主要使用者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"salmon fishermen","meaning":"鮭魚漁民","examples":[{"en":"Salmon fishermen used the bridge to reach the island.","zh":"鮭魚漁民使用這座橋到達小島。"},{"en":"Salmon fishermen are people who catch salmon for work or livelihood.","zh":"「salmon fishermen」是以捕捉鮭魚作工作或生計的人。"},{"en":"Salmon fishermen may travel early in the morning when fish are more active.","zh":"鮭魚漁民可能清晨出發，因為魚較活躍。"},{"en":"If salmon fishing takes place near an island, fishermen need a safe way to reach their nets.","zh":"如果鮭魚捕撈在小島附近進行，漁民需要安全方法到達漁網。"},{"en":"The phrase describes workers connected with salmon fishing.","zh":"這個短語描述與鮭魚捕撈相關的工作者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"travel from the island to the mainland","meaning":"從島上前往大陸","examples":[{"en":"The fishermen used the bridge to travel between the island and the mainland.","zh":"漁民使用這座橋在小島與大陸之間往返。"},{"en":"To travel from the island to the mainland means to move from an island back to the main land area.","zh":"「travel from the island to the mainland」意思是從島上移動回主要陸地。"},{"en":"Residents may travel from the island to the mainland for school, work, or shopping.","zh":"居民可能從島上前往大陸上學、工作或購物。"},{"en":"If weather is bad, travelling from the island to the mainland can become difficult.","zh":"如果天氣惡劣，從島上前往大陸可能變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement between separated land areas.","zh":"這個短語描述分離土地之間的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in time","meaning":"後來；隨着時間過去","examples":[{"en":"In time, the original bridge was replaced by a safer structure.","zh":"後來，原本的橋被較安全的結構取代。"},{"en":"In time means eventually, after a period has passed.","zh":"「in time」意思是最終，或經過一段時間後。"},{"en":"A shy student may, in time, become comfortable speaking in front of the class.","zh":"害羞學生隨着時間過去，可能變得習慣在全班面前說話。"},{"en":"If a structure proves dangerous, it may in time be improved or replaced.","zh":"如果一個結構證明危險，它後來可能被改善或取代。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual development or eventual change.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸發展或最終改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be replaced with","meaning":"被……取代","examples":[{"en":"The single handrail was replaced with a sturdy caged bridge.","zh":"單一扶手被一座堅固籠式吊橋取代。"},{"en":"To be replaced with something means to be removed and have another thing put in its place.","zh":"「be replaced with」某物，意思是被移除，並由另一物放在其位置。"},{"en":"Old classroom fans may be replaced with air conditioners.","zh":"舊課室風扇可能被冷氣機取代。"},{"en":"If a bridge is replaced with a safer design, more visitors may feel comfortable using it.","zh":"如果橋被較安全設計取代，更多遊客可能願意使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes substitution.","zh":"這個短語描述替換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"sturdy caged bridge","meaning":"堅固的籠式吊橋","examples":[{"en":"The modern structure is a sturdier caged bridge.","zh":"現代結構是一座更堅固的籠式吊橋。"},{"en":"A sturdy caged bridge is a strong bridge with protective sides or enclosure.","zh":"「sturdy caged bridge」是有防護側面或圍欄的堅固橋樑。"},{"en":"A caged bridge over a busy road can help pedestrians feel protected.","zh":"橫跨繁忙道路的籠式橋可以令行人感到受保護。"},{"en":"If a rope bridge is made sturdier, nervous visitors may cross more safely.","zh":"如果繩索橋變得更堅固，緊張遊客可以更安全通過。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a stronger and more enclosed bridge design.","zh":"這個短語描述更強、更封閉的橋樑設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"not a crossing for","meaning":"並非適合……通過的地方","examples":[{"en":"The rope bridge is not a crossing for nervous visitors.","zh":"這座繩索橋並非適合緊張遊客通過的地方。"},{"en":"Not a crossing for someone means not a suitable place or route for that type of person.","zh":"「not a crossing for」某人，意思是不適合該類人通過的地方或路線。"},{"en":"A steep mountain path is not a crossing for people afraid of heights.","zh":"陡峭山路並非適合畏高人士通過的地方。"},{"en":"If a bridge swings above deep water, nervous visitors may avoid it.","zh":"如果橋在深水上方搖晃，緊張遊客可能避開它。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that a route may be unsuitable for some people.","zh":"這個短語警告某路線可能不適合某些人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the faint-hearted","meaning":"膽小的人","examples":[{"en":"The crossing is not suitable for the faint-hearted.","zh":"這條通道不適合膽小的人。"},{"en":"The faint-hearted are people who are easily frightened or lack courage in risky situations.","zh":"「the faint-hearted」是容易受驚，或在危險情況中缺乏勇氣的人。"},{"en":"A glass-floor viewing platform is not ideal for the faint-hearted.","zh":"玻璃地板觀景台不太適合膽小的人。"},{"en":"If a bridge sways high above the sea, the faint-hearted may turn back.","zh":"如果橋在高高海面上搖晃，膽小的人可能折返。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people who become nervous easily.","zh":"這個短語指容易緊張害怕的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"swing above","meaning":"在……上方搖擺","examples":[{"en":"The bridge swings above a deep chasm.","zh":"這座橋在深谷上方搖擺。"},{"en":"To swing above something means to move back and forth while hanging over it.","zh":"「swing above」某物，意思是懸在其上方來回搖動。"},{"en":"A playground bridge may swing above soft sand when children run across it.","zh":"當孩子跑過時，遊樂場吊橋可能在軟沙上方搖擺。"},{"en":"If a bridge swings above deep water, crossing it can feel dramatic.","zh":"如果橋在深水上方搖擺，通過它會感覺很有戲劇性。"},{"en":"The phrase combines movement with height over something below.","zh":"這個短語結合下方高度與搖動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a chasm of","meaning":"充滿……的深谷","examples":[{"en":"The bridge crosses a chasm of rushing water.","zh":"這座橋跨越一道充滿奔流水流的深谷。"},{"en":"A chasm of something is a deep gap or opening filled with or marked by that thing.","zh":"「a chasm of」某物，是充滿或以該物為特徵的深裂口或深谷。"},{"en":"A mountain path may pass beside a chasm of shadow between two cliffs.","zh":"山路可能經過兩座懸崖之間一道充滿陰影的深谷旁。"},{"en":"If a bridge crosses a chasm of water, falling would be extremely dangerous.","zh":"如果橋跨越充滿海水的深谷，跌下去會極其危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a deep dramatic gap.","zh":"這個短語描述深而具戲劇性的裂口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"rushing, foaming water","meaning":"奔騰起泡的海水","examples":[{"en":"Rushing, foaming water crashes beneath the bridge.","zh":"奔騰起泡的海水在橋下撞擊。"},{"en":"Rushing, foaming water is fast-moving water full of white bubbles and spray.","zh":"「rushing, foaming water」是快速流動、充滿白色泡沫和水花的水。"},{"en":"After heavy rain, rushing, foaming water may fill a mountain stream.","zh":"大雨後，山溪可能充滿奔騰起泡的水流。"},{"en":"If water is rushing and foaming below a bridge, the crossing feels more dangerous.","zh":"如果橋下海水奔騰起泡，過橋會感覺更危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes powerful, noisy moving water.","zh":"這個短語描述強而有聲勢的流動水體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"drag the unwary down","meaning":"將沒有防備的人拖下去","examples":[{"en":"The water seems capable of dragging the unwary down.","zh":"海水看起來能把沒有防備的人拖下去。"},{"en":"To drag the unwary down means to pull people who are not careful into danger.","zh":"「drag the unwary down」意思是把不小心的人拉入危險。"},{"en":"A strong current can drag the unwary down if they swim too close to rocks.","zh":"如果泳客游得太近岩石，強勁水流可能將沒有防備的人拖下去。"},{"en":"If visitors underestimate fast water, they may be caught by its force.","zh":"如果遊客低估急流，他們可能被水力捲住。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that danger can trap careless people.","zh":"這個短語警告危險可以困住粗心的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the unwary","meaning":"沒有防備的人","examples":[{"en":"The bridge can be intimidating to the unwary.","zh":"這座橋對沒有防備的人來說可能令人害怕。"},{"en":"The unwary are people who are not cautious or prepared for danger.","zh":"「the unwary」是對危險不夠小心或沒有準備的人。"},{"en":"Wet rocks can be dangerous for the unwary because they look safer than they are.","zh":"濕滑岩石對沒有防備的人很危險，因為它們看起來比實際安全。"},{"en":"If visitors ignore warning signs, they become more vulnerable to accidents.","zh":"如果遊客忽視警告牌，就更容易發生意外。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people who are not careful enough.","zh":"這個短語指不夠小心的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make the walk one way","meaning":"只完成單程步行","examples":[{"en":"Some visitors make the walk to the island in one direction only.","zh":"有些遊客只完成前往小島的單程步行。"},{"en":"To make the walk one way means to go there but not return by the same walking route.","zh":"「make the walk one way」意思是走到那裡，但不沿同一條步行路線回來。"},{"en":"A nervous hiker may walk across a bridge once but refuse to walk back.","zh":"緊張的遠足者可能過橋一次，但拒絕走回來。"},{"en":"If fear increases after the first crossing, visitors may need another way to return.","zh":"如果第一次過橋後恐懼增加，遊客可能需要其他方法返回。"},{"en":"The phrase describes completing only the outward part of a walk.","zh":"這個短語描述只完成去程步行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be unable to return","meaning":"無法返回","examples":[{"en":"Some visitors become unable to return across the bridge.","zh":"有些遊客變得無法經橋返回。"},{"en":"To be unable to return means not to be able to go back.","zh":"「be unable to return」意思是不能回去。"},{"en":"A passenger may be unable to return home if the last train is cancelled.","zh":"如果尾班火車取消，乘客可能無法回家。"},{"en":"If fear stops someone from crossing again, they may need help returning.","zh":"如果恐懼阻止某人再次過橋，他們可能需要協助返回。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being prevented physically, emotionally, or practically from going back.","zh":"這個短語描述在身體、情緒或實際情況上被阻止回去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"result in someone doing something","meaning":"導致某人做某事","examples":[{"en":"Their fear results in them leaving the island by boat.","zh":"他們的恐懼導致他們乘船離開小島。"},{"en":"To result in someone doing something means to cause that person to take a particular action.","zh":"「result in someone doing something」意思是造成某人採取某個行動。"},{"en":"Heavy rain may result in students staying indoors during lunch.","zh":"大雨可能導致學生午飯時間留在室內。"},{"en":"If visitors are too frightened to cross back, the situation may result in a boat rescue.","zh":"如果遊客太害怕而不敢走回橋上，情況可能導致船隻救援。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a cause with someone’s action.","zh":"這個短語把原因與某人的行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be taken off the island","meaning":"被接離小島","examples":[{"en":"Some visitors have to be taken off the island by boat.","zh":"有些遊客必須乘船被接離小島。"},{"en":"To be taken off the island means to be removed or transported away from the island.","zh":"「be taken off the island」意思是被帶離或運離小島。"},{"en":"Injured hikers may be taken off a remote island by rescue boat.","zh":"受傷遠足者可能由救援船接離偏遠小島。"},{"en":"If visitors cannot cross the bridge back, staff may need to arrange another exit.","zh":"如果遊客不能走橋返回，職員可能需要安排另一種離開方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being helped or transported away from an island.","zh":"這個短語描述被協助或運送離開小島。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"by boat","meaning":"乘船","examples":[{"en":"Nervous visitors may return to the mainland by boat.","zh":"緊張的遊客可能乘船返回大陸。"},{"en":"By boat means using a boat as the method of travel.","zh":"「by boat」意思是以船作為交通方式。"},{"en":"Residents of a small island may go to school by boat every morning.","zh":"小島居民可能每天早上乘船上學。"},{"en":"If a bridge is unsafe or frightening, people may choose to travel by boat instead.","zh":"如果橋不安全或令人害怕，人們可能改為乘船。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the means of transport.","zh":"這個短語指出交通方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"look at the following list","meaning":"查看以下列表","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should look at the following list of places.","zh":"考生應查看以下地點列表。"},{"en":"Look at the following list means read the items shown below before answering.","zh":"「look at the following list」意思是在作答前閱讀下方列出的項目。"},{"en":"In a test, students should look at the following list before matching names to descriptions.","zh":"在測驗中，學生應先查看以下列表，再把名稱與描述配對。"},{"en":"If candidates skip the list, they may not know what options are available.","zh":"如果考生跳過列表，就可能不知道有哪些選項。"},{"en":"The phrase is a direct exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是直接考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"list of places","meaning":"地點列表","examples":[{"en":"The question provides a list of places from the passage.","zh":"題目提供文章中的地點列表。"},{"en":"A list of places is a set of location names arranged for reference or matching.","zh":"「list of places」是為參考或配對而排列的一組地名。"},{"en":"A travel worksheet may include a list of places for students to mark on a map.","zh":"旅遊工作紙可能包括地點列表，讓學生在地圖上標示。"},{"en":"If the list includes distractors, candidates must choose carefully.","zh":"如果列表包含干擾項，考生必須小心選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies location options in a task.","zh":"這個短語指出題目中的地點選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"locations on the map","meaning":"地圖上的位置","examples":[{"en":"Candidates must identify the locations on the map.","zh":"考生必須識別地圖上的位置。"},{"en":"Locations on the map are the places marked or represented on a map.","zh":"「locations on the map」是地圖上標示或代表的地方。"},{"en":"Students may identify schools, rivers, and roads as locations on the map.","zh":"學生可能把學校、河流和道路識別為地圖上的位置。"},{"en":"If a candidate cannot connect a place name with its map position, the answer may be wrong.","zh":"如果考生不能把地名與地圖位置連接，答案可能錯。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to mapped positions.","zh":"這個短語指地圖中的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"match each place with","meaning":"將每個地方與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match each place with its location on the map.","zh":"考生將每個地方與其地圖位置配對。"},{"en":"To match each place with something means to connect every place name to the correct item or position.","zh":"「match each place with」某物，意思是把每個地名連接到正確項目或位置。"},{"en":"In geography class, students match each city with its country.","zh":"在地理課中，學生把每個城市與其國家配對。"},{"en":"If candidates understand direction words, they can match places with map locations more easily.","zh":"如果考生理解方向詞，就能更容易把地方與地圖位置配對。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a place-matching task.","zh":"這個短語描述地點配對任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"write your answers in boxes","meaning":"在方格內寫上答案","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should write their answers in boxes on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生應在答題紙方格內寫上答案。"},{"en":"Write your answers in boxes means put each answer in the numbered spaces provided.","zh":"「write your answers in boxes」意思是把每個答案填入指定編號空格。"},{"en":"In an exam, writing outside the answer boxes may make answers hard to mark.","zh":"在考試中，寫在答案方格外可能令答案難以評改。"},{"en":"If candidates use the wrong box, even a correct answer may be counted incorrectly.","zh":"如果考生用錯方格，即使答案正確也可能被錯誤計算。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a formatting instruction for test answers.","zh":"這個短語提供考試答案格式指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reflect the claims of","meaning":"反映……的主張","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether the statements reflect the claims of the writer.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否反映作者的主張。"},{"en":"To reflect the claims of someone means to match or represent what that person argues or says.","zh":"「reflect the claims of」某人，意思是符合或代表該人所主張或所說的內容。"},{"en":"A summary should reflect the claims of an article, not the student’s personal opinion.","zh":"摘要應反映文章主張，而不是學生個人意見。"},{"en":"If a statement changes the writer’s meaning, it does not accurately reflect the claim.","zh":"如果陳述改變作者意思，它就不能準確反映主張。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in reading questions about author views.","zh":"這個短語常見於關於作者觀點的閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agree with the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點一致","examples":[{"en":"A “Yes” statement agrees with the views of the writer.","zh":"“Yes” 陳述與作者的觀點一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the views of someone means to match that person’s opinion or position.","zh":"「agree with the views of」某人，意思是與該人的意見或立場相符。"},{"en":"If the writer recommends visiting at twilight, a statement saying twilight is ideal agrees with the writer’s view.","zh":"如果作者建議黃昏遊覽，而陳述說黃昏理想，就與作者觀點一致。"},{"en":"If a statement says the opposite of the writer’s opinion, it does not agree.","zh":"如果陳述說出作者意見的相反意思，它就不一致。"},{"en":"The phrase helps students identify support in YES/NO/NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個短語幫助學生在 YES/NO/NOT GIVEN 題中識別支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A “No” statement contradicts the views of the writer.","zh":"“No” 陳述與作者的觀點矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to express the opposite of that person’s opinion.","zh":"「contradict the views of」某人，意思是表達與該人意見相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the writer says a place is worth visiting but a statement says it is not, the statement contradicts the writer’s view.","zh":"如果作者說某地值得遊覽，而陳述說不值得，該陳述就與作者觀點矛盾。"},{"en":"If evidence directly opposes the statement, the answer is usually “No”.","zh":"如果證據直接反對陳述，答案通常是 “No”。"},{"en":"The phrase describes conflict with an opinion, not just missing information.","zh":"這個短語描述與觀點衝突，而不只是資料缺失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"The answer is not given if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"如果無法判斷作者怎樣想，答案就是 not given。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to make a clear judgement.","zh":"「impossible to say」意思是沒有足夠資料作出清楚判斷。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions ticket prices, it is impossible to say whether the attraction is expensive.","zh":"如果文章從未提及票價，就無法判斷景點是否昂貴。"},{"en":"If evidence is absent, students should not guess from background knowledge.","zh":"如果證據不存在，學生不應憑背景知識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase explains uncertainty in reading comprehension.","zh":"這個短語解釋閱讀理解中的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"after 1639","meaning":"1639年之後","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the condition of Dunluce Castle after 1639.","zh":"題目問鄧路斯城堡在1639年之後的狀況。"},{"en":"After 1639 means during the period following the year 1639.","zh":"「after 1639」意思是在1639年之後的時期。"},{"en":"After 1997, many records in the office were stored digitally.","zh":"1997年之後，辦公室許多記錄以數碼方式儲存。"},{"en":"If a collapse happened in 1639, the period after 1639 may show decline or repair.","zh":"如果倒塌發生於1639年，1639年之後的時期可能顯示衰敗或修復。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a time reference after a specific year.","zh":"這個短語提供某一特定年份之後的時間參照。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"completely uninhabited","meaning":"完全無人居住的","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether the castle became completely uninhabited.","zh":"陳述問城堡是否變得完全無人居住。"},{"en":"Completely uninhabited means no people lived there at all.","zh":"「completely uninhabited」意思是完全沒有人居住。"},{"en":"A village may become completely uninhabited if all residents move away after a disaster.","zh":"如果災難後所有居民搬走，村莊可能變得完全無人居住。"},{"en":"If a castle is still partly used, it is not completely uninhabited.","zh":"如果城堡仍有部分被使用，它就不是完全無人居住。"},{"en":"The phrase describes total absence of residents.","zh":"這個短語描述完全沒有居民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"evoke another period","meaning":"令人想起另一個時代","examples":[{"en":"Dunluce Castle evokes another period of history.","zh":"鄧路斯城堡令人想起歷史中的另一個時代。"},{"en":"To evoke another period means to make people think of a different historical time.","zh":"「evoke another period」意思是令人想到另一個歷史時期。"},{"en":"Old gas lamps in a street can evoke another period before electric lighting.","zh":"街上的舊煤氣燈可以令人想起電燈以前的另一個時代。"},{"en":"If a ruin preserves old shapes and materials, it may bring the past to mind.","zh":"如果遺跡保存舊形態和材料，它可能令人想起過去。"},{"en":"The phrase describes historical atmosphere created by a place or object.","zh":"這個短語描述地方或物件營造出的歷史氛圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"more than 1,500","meaning":"超過1,500","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether more than 1,500 men were aboard Girona.","zh":"題目問是否有超過1,500人在 Girona 船上。"},{"en":"More than 1,500 means a number greater than 1,500.","zh":"「more than 1,500」意思是數量高於1,500。"},{"en":"More than 1,500 people joined the charity walk, so the organisers needed extra volunteers.","zh":"超過1,500人參加慈善步行，所以主辦方需要額外義工。"},{"en":"If a ship carried more than 1,500 people, rescue would be extremely difficult after a wreck.","zh":"如果船載有超過1,500人，失事後救援會極其困難。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses a quantity above a stated number.","zh":"這個短語表達高於某指定數字的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be worth visiting","meaning":"值得遊覽","examples":[{"en":"The writer clearly believes that the Causeway is worth visiting.","zh":"作者明顯認為巨人堤道值得遊覽。"},{"en":"To be worth visiting means to deserve the time and effort required to go there.","zh":"「be worth visiting」意思是值得花時間和力氣前往。"},{"en":"A small local museum may be worth visiting if it explains the town’s history well.","zh":"如果小型本地博物館很好地解釋城鎮歷史，它可能值得遊覽。"},{"en":"If a place is worth visiting, travellers usually feel satisfied after the trip.","zh":"如果一個地方值得遊覽，旅客旅行後通常感到滿足。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to recommend a destination.","zh":"這個短語用來推薦目的地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"recommend twilight","meaning":"建議在黃昏時分","examples":[{"en":"The writer recommends twilight as an ideal time to visit.","zh":"作者建議在黃昏時分遊覽，認為那是理想時間。"},{"en":"To recommend twilight means to suggest visiting during the soft light between day and night.","zh":"「recommend twilight」意思是建議在日與夜之間柔和光線時段到訪。"},{"en":"A photographer may recommend twilight because crowds are smaller and colours are warmer.","zh":"攝影師可能建議黃昏時分，因為人群較少、色彩較溫暖。"},{"en":"If a place feels more magical at dusk, writers may recommend twilight to visitors.","zh":"如果一個地方在傍晚更有魔力，作者可能建議遊客黃昏到訪。"},{"en":"The phrase gives advice about the best visiting time.","zh":"這個短語給出最佳遊覽時間的建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the best time to visit","meaning":"遊覽的最佳時間","examples":[{"en":"Twilight may be the best time to visit the coastline.","zh":"黃昏可能是遊覽海岸線的最佳時間。"},{"en":"The best time to visit is the period when a place can be enjoyed most fully.","zh":"「the best time to visit」是最能充分欣賞某地的時段。"},{"en":"Early morning may be the best time to visit a market before it becomes crowded.","zh":"清晨可能是遊覽市場的最佳時間，因為那時尚未擁擠。"},{"en":"If weather, light, and crowds are favourable, that time becomes ideal for visitors.","zh":"如果天氣、光線和人流都有利，該時間就成為遊客理想時段。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the most suitable visiting time.","zh":"這個短語指出最合適的遊覽時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"increase the number of visitors","meaning":"增加遊客數目","examples":[{"en":"The statement suggests that the improved bridge increased visitor numbers.","zh":"陳述暗示改良後的橋增加了遊客數目。"},{"en":"To increase the number of visitors means to make more people come to a place.","zh":"「increase the number of visitors」意思是令更多人來到某地。"},{"en":"Better transport can increase the number of visitors to a museum.","zh":"更好的交通可以增加博物館遊客數目。"},{"en":"If a dangerous bridge is made safer, more tourists may feel willing to cross it.","zh":"如果危險橋樑變得更安全，更多遊客可能願意通過。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growth in visitor attendance.","zh":"這個短語描述遊客到訪量增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"考生需要為每題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option that matches the evidence.","zh":"「choose the correct letter」意思是選擇與證據相符的答案選項字母。"},{"en":"In multiple-choice questions, students must choose the correct letter rather than write a full sentence.","zh":"在多項選擇題中，學生必須選出正確字母，而不是寫完整句子。"},{"en":"If candidates misunderstand one keyword, they may choose the wrong letter.","zh":"如果考生誤解一個關鍵詞，就可能選錯字母。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the writer feels that","meaning":"作者認為……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what the writer feels about the Giant’s Causeway.","zh":"題目問作者對巨人堤道有甚麼感受。"},{"en":"The writer feels that means the question is asking for the writer’s opinion or emotional response.","zh":"「the writer feels that」意思是題目要求找出作者的意見或情感反應。"},{"en":"If the writer uses words like “magic” and “impossible to forget”, readers can infer how the writer feels.","zh":"如果作者使用 “magic” 和 “impossible to forget” 等詞，讀者可以推斷作者感受。"},{"en":"If a passage describes a place warmly, the writer likely feels positively about it.","zh":"如果文章以溫暖語氣描述一個地方，作者很可能對它有正面感受。"},{"en":"The phrase points to attitude, not just factual information.","zh":"這個短語指向態度，而不只是事實資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"unsettling place","meaning":"令人不安的地方","examples":[{"en":"The darkness can make the Causeway feel like an unsettling place.","zh":"黑暗可以令巨人堤道感覺像令人不安的地方。"},{"en":"An unsettling place is somewhere that makes people feel uneasy, disturbed, or slightly afraid.","zh":"「unsettling place」是令人感到不安、受擾或略為害怕的地方。"},{"en":"An empty hospital corridor at night can feel like an unsettling place.","zh":"夜晚空無一人的醫院走廊，可以感覺像令人不安的地方。"},{"en":"If darkness hides familiar shapes, even a beautiful landscape may become unsettling.","zh":"如果黑暗遮住熟悉形狀，即使美麗地貌也可能變得令人不安。"},{"en":"The phrase describes emotional discomfort caused by a place.","zh":"這個短語描述地方造成的情緒不適。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"relaxing place","meaning":"令人放鬆的地方","examples":[{"en":"Some visitors may experience the coastline as a relaxing place.","zh":"有些遊客可能把海岸線體驗為令人放鬆的地方。"},{"en":"A relaxing place is somewhere that helps people feel calm, comfortable, and rested.","zh":"「relaxing place」是幫助人感到平靜、舒服和休息到的地方。"},{"en":"A quiet garden can be a relaxing place after a stressful school day.","zh":"緊張上課日後，一個寧靜花園可以是令人放鬆的地方。"},{"en":"If there are few people and soft evening light, a coastline may feel peaceful.","zh":"如果人少而傍晚光線柔和，海岸線可能感覺平和。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a place that reduces tension.","zh":"這個短語描述能減少緊張的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"exciting place","meaning":"令人興奮的地方","examples":[{"en":"The dramatic landscape can also feel like an exciting place.","zh":"戲劇性的地貌也可以感覺像令人興奮的地方。"},{"en":"An exciting place is somewhere that creates interest, energy, or a sense of adventure.","zh":"「exciting place」是令人產生興趣、活力或冒險感的地方。"},{"en":"A busy night market can be an exciting place for visitors trying new food.","zh":"對嘗試新食物的遊客而言，繁忙夜市可以是令人興奮的地方。"},{"en":"If cliffs, waves, and a rope bridge are involved, a trip may feel adventurous.","zh":"如果行程涉及懸崖、海浪和繩索橋，旅行可能感覺很冒險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a place that stimulates curiosity or thrill.","zh":"這個短語描述激發好奇或刺激感的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"which of the following","meaning":"以下哪一項","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose which of the following titles best suits the passage.","zh":"考生選擇以下哪一個標題最適合文章。"},{"en":"Which of the following means select one option from the choices listed below.","zh":"「which of the following」意思是從下方列出的選項中選出一項。"},{"en":"In a reading test, “Which of the following is true?” asks students to compare all options with the text.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，“Which of the following is true?” 要求學生把所有選項與文本比較。"},{"en":"If several options look similar, students must check the evidence carefully.","zh":"如果幾個選項看起來相似，學生必須仔細檢查證據。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a multiple-choice question.","zh":"這個短語引入多項選擇題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a good title for","meaning":"……的合適標題","examples":[{"en":"“A Leap into History” is presented as a possible title for the passage.","zh":"“A Leap into History” 被列為文章可能的合適標題。"},{"en":"A good title for something is a heading that captures its main idea, mood, or focus.","zh":"「a good title for」某物，是能概括其主旨、氣氛或焦點的標題。"},{"en":"“Life Under Pressure” could be a good title for an article about exam stress.","zh":"“Life Under Pressure” 可以是一篇關於考試壓力文章的合適標題。"},{"en":"If a title reflects both travel and history, it may suit a passage about historic landscapes.","zh":"如果標題同時反映旅遊和歷史，它可能適合一篇關於歷史地貌的文章。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a suitable name for a text, film, or project.","zh":"這個短語描述文本、電影或項目的合適名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 23 - A leap into history.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 24":[{"front":"living languages","meaning":"現存語言","examples":[{"en":"There are about 6,500 living languages in the world.","zh":"世界上大約有6,500種現存語言。"},{"en":"Living languages are languages that are still spoken by people today.","zh":"現存語言，是今天仍有人使用的語言。"},{"en":"Cantonese, English, Japanese, and Arabic are living languages because people use them in daily life.","zh":"粵語、英語、日語和阿拉伯語都是現存語言，因為人們在日常生活中使用它們。"},{"en":"If children stop learning a language, it may slowly stop being a living language.","zh":"如果孩子停止學習一種語言，它可能慢慢不再是現存語言。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts languages still in use with dead or extinct languages.","zh":"這個短語把仍在使用的語言與死亡或滅絕語言作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be expected to die out","meaning":"預計會消亡；預計會消失","examples":[{"en":"Around half of the world’s living languages are expected to die out by the end of this century.","zh":"世界上大約一半現存語言預計會在本世紀末消亡。"},{"en":"To be expected to die out means people predict that something will disappear completely.","zh":"預計會消亡，指人們預測某事物將會完全消失。"},{"en":"A local custom may be expected to die out if young people no longer practise it.","zh":"如果年輕人不再實踐某本地習俗，它可能預計會消失。"},{"en":"If a language is expected to die out, there may be too few young speakers to keep it alive.","zh":"如果一種語言預計會消亡，可能是因為年輕使用者太少，無法讓它存續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a predicted disappearance, not something that has already happened.","zh":"這個短語描述預測中的消失，而不是已經發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"by the end of this century","meaning":"到本世紀末","examples":[{"en":"Around half of the world’s living languages may disappear by the end of this century.","zh":"世界上大約一半現存語言可能到本世紀末消失。"},{"en":"By the end of this century means before this hundred-year period finishes.","zh":"到本世紀末，指在這一百年結束之前。"},{"en":"Many cities may need stronger flood defences by the end of this century.","zh":"許多城市到本世紀末可能需要更強的防洪設施。"},{"en":"If a language may disappear by the end of this century, action is needed before that time.","zh":"如果一種語言可能到本世紀末消失，就需要在那之前採取行動。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a long-term deadline.","zh":"這個短語設定一個長遠期限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"according to UNESCO","meaning":"根據聯合國教科文組織","examples":[{"en":"According to UNESCO, many living languages are at risk of disappearing.","zh":"根據聯合國教科文組織，許多現存語言有消失風險。"},{"en":"According to UNESCO means the information comes from the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization.","zh":"根據聯合國教科文組織，指資料來自 United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization。"},{"en":"According to a school notice, students must arrive before 8:00 a.m.","zh":"根據學校通告，學生必須在上午八時前到達。"},{"en":"If a claim is made according to UNESCO, the writer is using an international organisation as a source.","zh":"如果一項主張是根據聯合國教科文組織提出，作者就是使用國際組織作資料來源。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces where the information comes from.","zh":"這個短語引入資料來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"spoken by more than half of","meaning":"為超過一半……所使用","examples":[{"en":"Just 11 languages are spoken by more than half of Earth’s population.","zh":"僅11種語言為超過一半地球人口所使用。"},{"en":"Spoken by more than half of a group means used by over 50 per cent of that group.","zh":"為某群體超過一半所使用，指由該群體中超過百分之五十的人使用。"},{"en":"A school language may be spoken by more than half of the students if most families use it at home.","zh":"如果大多數家庭在家中使用某語言，該語言可能為超過一半學生所使用。"},{"en":"If a few languages are spoken by most people, smaller languages may receive less attention.","zh":"如果少數語言由大部分人使用，較小語言可能得到較少注意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes majority use.","zh":"這個短語描述多數使用情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Earth’s population","meaning":"地球人口","examples":[{"en":"Just 11 languages are spoken by more than half of Earth’s population.","zh":"僅11種語言為超過一半地球人口所使用。"},{"en":"Earth’s population means all the people living on the planet.","zh":"地球人口，指生活在地球上的所有人。"},{"en":"Earth’s population lives in cities, villages, islands, deserts, and mountain regions.","zh":"地球人口生活在城市、村莊、島嶼、沙漠和山區。"},{"en":"If only a few languages are used by much of Earth’s population, language power becomes uneven.","zh":"如果只有少數語言由大量地球人口使用，語言力量就會變得不均。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the whole human population.","zh":"這個短語指全人類人口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"it is little wonder that","meaning":"難怪","examples":[{"en":"It is little wonder that languages used by only a few people are being left behind.","zh":"難怪只由少數人使用的語言正在被拋低。"},{"en":"It is little wonder that means something is not surprising because the reason is clear.","zh":"難怪，指某事並不令人驚訝，因為原因很清楚。"},{"en":"It is little wonder that students feel tired if they sleep only four hours a night.","zh":"如果學生每晚只睡四小時，難怪他們會疲倦。"},{"en":"If most people use major global languages, it is little wonder that small languages struggle.","zh":"如果大多數人使用主要全球語言，難怪小語言會掙扎求存。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an understandable result.","zh":"這個短語引入可理解的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"used by only a few","meaning":"只由少數人使用","examples":[{"en":"Languages used by only a few speakers may struggle to survive.","zh":"只由少數說話者使用的語言可能難以存續。"},{"en":"Used by only a few means used by a very small number of people.","zh":"只由少數人使用，指使用者數量非常少。"},{"en":"A family recipe used by only a few relatives may disappear if no one writes it down.","zh":"如果家庭食譜只由少數親戚使用，而沒有人寫下來，它可能會消失。"},{"en":"If a language is used by only a few elders, children may not learn it naturally.","zh":"如果一種語言只由少數長者使用，孩子可能不會自然學會它。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests vulnerability because the user base is small.","zh":"這個短語暗示因使用者基礎小而脆弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be left behind","meaning":"被拋低；被邊緣化","examples":[{"en":"Minority languages are being left behind as society becomes more global.","zh":"隨着社會變得更全球化，少數族群語言正在被拋低。"},{"en":"To be left behind means to be ignored, forgotten, or unable to keep up with others.","zh":"被拋低，指被忽視、遺忘，或無法跟上其他人。"},{"en":"A student may be left behind if the class moves too quickly and no one explains the basics.","zh":"如果課堂進度太快而沒有人解釋基礎，學生可能被拋低。"},{"en":"If schools and media use only major languages, smaller languages may be left behind.","zh":"如果學校和媒體只使用主要語言，較小語言可能被邊緣化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being pushed to the margins.","zh":"這個短語描述被推到邊緣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a more homogeneous society","meaning":"更同質化的社會","examples":[{"en":"We are becoming a more homogeneous, global society.","zh":"我們正在變成一個更同質化的全球社會。"},{"en":"A more homogeneous society is a society where people become more similar in language, habits, values, or lifestyle.","zh":"更同質化的社會，是人們在語言、習慣、價值觀或生活方式上變得更相似的社會。"},{"en":"If every shopping street has the same chain stores, the city may feel more homogeneous.","zh":"如果每條購物街都有相同連鎖店，城市可能感覺更同質化。"},{"en":"When society becomes more homogeneous, local differences may become less visible.","zh":"當社會變得更同質化，本地差異可能變得較不明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reduced diversity.","zh":"這個短語描述多樣性減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in short","meaning":"簡而言之","examples":[{"en":"In short, most languages are spoken by only a small minority of people.","zh":"簡而言之，大多數語言只由少數人使用。"},{"en":"In short means to state the main idea briefly.","zh":"簡而言之，指簡短說出主要意思。"},{"en":"In short, the plan failed because nobody had enough time to prepare.","zh":"簡而言之，計劃失敗是因為沒有人有足夠時間準備。"},{"en":"If an explanation is long, “in short” helps summarise the key point.","zh":"如果解釋很長，“in short” 有助總結重點。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a concise summary.","zh":"這個短語引入簡潔總結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"linguistic diversity","meaning":"語言多樣性","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes a remarkable level of linguistic diversity.","zh":"文章描述了驚人的語言多樣性程度。"},{"en":"Linguistic diversity means the existence of many different languages or varieties of language.","zh":"語言多樣性，指存在許多不同語言或語言變體。"},{"en":"A city has linguistic diversity if people there speak Cantonese, Urdu, Tagalog, English, and many other languages.","zh":"如果一個城市的人說粵語、烏爾都語、他加祿語、英語和許多其他語言，它就有語言多樣性。"},{"en":"If linguistic diversity declines, the world loses different ways of expressing knowledge and identity.","zh":"如果語言多樣性下降，世界會失去不同表達知識和身份的方式。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to variety in human language.","zh":"這個短語指人類語言中的多樣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tiny pockets of speakers","meaning":"小型說話者群體","examples":[{"en":"Linguistic diversity is stored in tiny pockets of speakers around the world.","zh":"語言多樣性保存在世界各地的小型說話者群體中。"},{"en":"Tiny pockets of speakers are small, scattered groups of people who still use a language.","zh":"小型說話者群體，是仍在使用某語言的小而分散的人群。"},{"en":"A mountain village may contain a tiny pocket of speakers of an old local language.","zh":"一條山村可能有一個使用古老本地語言的小型說話者群體。"},{"en":"If these groups disappear, the language they carry may disappear with them.","zh":"如果這些群體消失，它們承載的語言也可能一起消失。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that some languages survive in very small communities.","zh":"這個短語顯示一些語言在非常小的社群中存續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"launch a project","meaning":"發起一項計劃","examples":[{"en":"Mark Turin has launched a project to help protect endangered languages.","zh":"Mark Turin 發起了一項計劃，以幫助保護瀕危語言。"},{"en":"To launch a project means to start and publicly begin a planned piece of work.","zh":"發起一項計劃，指開始並公開展開一項有規劃的工作。"},{"en":"A school may launch a project to record old neighbourhood stories.","zh":"學校可能發起一項計劃，記錄舊社區故事。"},{"en":"If a project is launched with funding and partners, it can begin collecting materials.","zh":"如果計劃在有資金和合作伙伴下發起，就可以開始收集材料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formally starting an organised effort.","zh":"這個短語描述正式開始有組織的努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"World Oral Literature Project","meaning":"世界口述文學計劃","examples":[{"en":"The World Oral Literature Project aims to record endangered oral traditions.","zh":"世界口述文學計劃旨在記錄瀕危口述傳統。"},{"en":"The World Oral Literature Project is a project that helps document spoken stories, songs, and traditions.","zh":"世界口述文學計劃，是幫助記錄口頭故事、歌曲和傳統的計劃。"},{"en":"A community may work with the World Oral Literature Project to record elders telling myths.","zh":"社群可能與世界口述文學計劃合作，錄下長者講述神話。"},{"en":"If oral traditions are recorded, future generations can hear materials that might otherwise vanish.","zh":"如果口述傳統被記錄，後代就能聽到原本可能消失的材料。"},{"en":"The phrase names a project focused on protecting oral culture.","zh":"這個短語命名一項專注保護口述文化的計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"prevent languages from reaching","meaning":"阻止語言走到……的地步","examples":[{"en":"The project tries to prevent languages from reaching the brink of extinction.","zh":"該計劃嘗試阻止語言走到瀕臨滅絕的地步。"},{"en":"To prevent languages from reaching a stage means to stop them before they arrive at that dangerous point.","zh":"阻止語言走到某階段，指在語言到達該危險點之前阻止它。"},{"en":"Teachers try to prevent students from reaching a point where they completely give up.","zh":"老師嘗試阻止學生走到完全放棄的地步。"},{"en":"If communities record and use their languages early, those languages may avoid extinction.","zh":"如果社群及早記錄和使用自己的語言，那些語言可能避免滅絕。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stopping a decline before it becomes too serious.","zh":"這個短語描述在衰退變得太嚴重前阻止它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the brink of extinction","meaning":"瀕臨滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Some languages are already on the brink of extinction.","zh":"一些語言已經瀕臨滅絕。"},{"en":"The brink of extinction is the point where a species, language, or tradition is very close to disappearing completely.","zh":"瀕臨滅絕，是物種、語言或傳統非常接近完全消失的狀態。"},{"en":"A family craft may be on the brink of extinction if only one elderly person still knows it.","zh":"如果只有一位長者仍懂某家庭手藝，它可能瀕臨滅絕。"},{"en":"If a language reaches the brink of extinction, every remaining speaker becomes important.","zh":"如果一種語言走到瀕臨滅絕的地步，每一位剩餘使用者都變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extreme danger of disappearance.","zh":"這個短語描述消失的極端危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"indigenous communities","meaning":"原住民社群","examples":[{"en":"Turin wants indigenous communities to record their own oral literature.","zh":"Turin 希望原住民社群記錄自己的口述文學。"},{"en":"Indigenous communities are original local peoples with long-standing ties to a land, language, and culture.","zh":"原住民社群，是與土地、語言和文化有長久連繫的原本本地民族。"},{"en":"Indigenous communities may pass down history through songs, stories, ceremonies, and place names.","zh":"原住民社群可能透過歌曲、故事、儀式和地名傳承歷史。"},{"en":"If indigenous communities record their own traditions, they can control how their culture is represented.","zh":"如果原住民社群記錄自己的傳統，他們就能控制文化如何被呈現。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to native peoples and their communities.","zh":"這個短語指原住民族群及其社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"encourage someone to","meaning":"鼓勵某人去","examples":[{"en":"The project encourages indigenous communities to collaborate with researchers.","zh":"該計劃鼓勵原住民社群與研究人員合作。"},{"en":"To encourage someone to do something means to support or persuade them to do it.","zh":"鼓勵某人去做某事，指支持或說服某人去做。"},{"en":"A teacher may encourage shy students to speak by praising small attempts.","zh":"老師可能透過稱讚小小嘗試，鼓勵害羞學生說話。"},{"en":"If communities are encouraged to record stories, they may feel their language matters.","zh":"如果社群被鼓勵記錄故事，他們可能覺得自己的語言很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes positive support toward action.","zh":"這個短語描述推動行動的正面支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"collaborate with anthropologists","meaning":"與人類學家合作","examples":[{"en":"Indigenous communities are encouraged to collaborate with anthropologists.","zh":"原住民社群被鼓勵與人類學家合作。"},{"en":"To collaborate with anthropologists means to work together with experts who study human cultures and societies.","zh":"與人類學家合作，指與研究人類文化和社會的專家一起工作。"},{"en":"A village may collaborate with anthropologists to record wedding songs and rituals.","zh":"村莊可能與人類學家合作，記錄婚禮歌曲和儀式。"},{"en":"If communities collaborate with researchers, documentation can combine local knowledge and academic skills.","zh":"如果社群與研究人員合作，記錄工作就能結合本地知識和學術技能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes partnership in cultural research.","zh":"這個短語描述文化研究中的伙伴合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"around the world","meaning":"世界各地","examples":[{"en":"Anthropologists around the world can help record endangered languages.","zh":"世界各地的人類學家都可以幫助記錄瀕危語言。"},{"en":"Around the world means in many countries or regions globally.","zh":"世界各地，指在全球許多國家或地區。"},{"en":"Students around the world use phones, but they may use them in different ways.","zh":"世界各地的學生都使用手機，但使用方式可能不同。"},{"en":"If researchers around the world share methods, language documentation can improve.","zh":"如果世界各地研究人員分享方法，語言記錄工作可以改善。"},{"en":"The phrase describes wide international reach.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛國際範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"oral literature","meaning":"口述文學","examples":[{"en":"Turin uses the term oral literature to describe stories passed down by speech.","zh":"Turin 使用「口述文學」這個詞來描述透過說話傳承的故事。"},{"en":"Oral literature is literature preserved and shared through spoken words rather than writing.","zh":"口述文學，是透過口語而非書寫保存和分享的文學。"},{"en":"Grandparents telling old village stories to children is a form of oral literature.","zh":"祖父母向孩子講述舊村莊故事，就是一種口述文學。"},{"en":"If oral literature is not recorded, it may disappear when speakers pass away.","zh":"如果口述文學沒有被記錄，使用者去世時它可能消失。"},{"en":"The phrase includes spoken stories, songs, myths, chants, and histories.","zh":"這個短語包括口頭故事、歌曲、神話、吟誦和歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"multimedia tools","meaning":"多媒體工具","examples":[{"en":"Video cameras and voice recorders are useful multimedia tools for language documentation.","zh":"攝影機和錄音機是語言記錄中有用的多媒體工具。"},{"en":"Multimedia tools are devices or software that record or present sound, images, video, or text.","zh":"多媒體工具，是記錄或呈現聲音、圖像、影片或文字的設備或軟件。"},{"en":"A teacher may use multimedia tools to record students’ speeches and give feedback.","zh":"老師可能使用多媒體工具錄下學生演講並給予回饋。"},{"en":"If researchers use multimedia tools, they can capture both pronunciation and performance.","zh":"如果研究人員使用多媒體工具，就能捕捉發音和表演方式。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to technology that handles more than one form of media.","zh":"這個短語指處理多於一種媒體形式的科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"award grants","meaning":"發放資助金","examples":[{"en":"The project awards grants to support language-recording work.","zh":"該計劃發放資助金，以支援語言記錄工作。"},{"en":"To award grants means to give money officially to support a project or person.","zh":"發放資助金，指正式給予金錢以支援項目或個人。"},{"en":"A school may award grants to students who want to run community service projects.","zh":"學校可能向想推行社區服務項目的學生發放資助金。"},{"en":"If researchers receive grants, they can buy equipment and travel to field sites.","zh":"如果研究人員獲得資助金，就能購買設備並前往田野地點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formal financial support.","zh":"這個短語描述正式財政支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"secure funding","meaning":"取得資金；獲得資助","examples":[{"en":"The project has secured funding to support its work this year.","zh":"該計劃已取得資金，以支援今年的工作。"},{"en":"To secure funding means to successfully obtain money for a project.","zh":"取得資金，指成功為項目獲得金錢。"},{"en":"A charity must secure funding before it can open a new shelter.","zh":"慈善機構必須先取得資金，才能開設新庇護中心。"},{"en":"If a language project secures funding, it can pay for recording tools and travel.","zh":"如果語言計劃取得資金，就能支付錄音工具和旅費。"},{"en":"The phrase describes obtaining financial resources.","zh":"這個短語描述獲得財政資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"collate this literature","meaning":"匯集這些文學資料","examples":[{"en":"The project aims to collate this literature in a digital archive.","zh":"該計劃旨在把這些文學資料匯集於數碼檔案庫中。"},{"en":"To collate this literature means to collect, organise, and arrange these spoken materials systematically.","zh":"匯集這些文學資料，指有系統地收集、整理和排列這些口述材料。"},{"en":"A teacher may collate students’ essays into one class booklet.","zh":"老師可能把學生作文匯集成一本班級文集。"},{"en":"If oral stories are collated, researchers and communities can find them more easily.","zh":"如果口述故事被匯集，研究人員和社群就能更容易找到它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised collection.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的收集。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a digital archive","meaning":"數碼檔案庫","examples":[{"en":"Recordings of oral literature can be stored in a digital archive.","zh":"口述文學錄音可以儲存在數碼檔案庫中。"},{"en":"A digital archive is an online or computer-based collection of stored materials.","zh":"數碼檔案庫，是網上或電腦化的資料收藏系統。"},{"en":"A school may keep old photos and newsletters in a digital archive.","zh":"學校可能把舊照片和校訊保存在數碼檔案庫中。"},{"en":"If language recordings are stored digitally, they can be copied and shared more safely.","zh":"如果語言錄音以數碼方式儲存，就能更安全地複製和分享。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a modern storage system for records.","zh":"這個短語指現代記錄儲存系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"accessed on demand","meaning":"按需要存取","examples":[{"en":"The archive can be accessed on demand by researchers and communities.","zh":"研究人員和社群可以按需要存取該檔案庫。"},{"en":"Accessed on demand means people can open or use the material whenever they need it.","zh":"按需要存取，指人們可以在需要時打開或使用材料。"},{"en":"Online lessons can be accessed on demand if students miss a live class.","zh":"如果學生錯過直播課堂，網上課程可以按需要存取。"},{"en":"If recordings are available on demand, communities can use them for teaching and memory.","zh":"如果錄音可按需要使用，社群就能把它們用於教學和記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase describes convenient access when needed.","zh":"這個短語描述在需要時方便取得。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the nuts and bolts of","meaning":"基本細節；實際內容","examples":[{"en":"The archive will make the nuts and bolts of lost cultures readily available.","zh":"該檔案庫會令失落文化的基本細節容易取得。"},{"en":"The nuts and bolts of something are its basic practical details and workings.","zh":"某事的基本細節，是其實際細節和運作方式。"},{"en":"Before running a school event, students must learn the nuts and bolts of booking rooms and inviting guests.","zh":"在舉辦學校活動前，學生必須學會預訂房間和邀請嘉賓等實際細節。"},{"en":"If researchers record songs, stories, names, and rituals, they preserve the practical details of culture.","zh":"如果研究人員記錄歌曲、故事、名稱和儀式，他們就保存文化的實際細節。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the real working details, not just general ideas.","zh":"這個短語強調真正運作細節，而不只是一般想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lost cultures","meaning":"失落的文化","examples":[{"en":"Oral literature can preserve important knowledge from lost cultures.","zh":"口述文學可以保存來自失落文化的重要知識。"},{"en":"Lost cultures are cultures that have disappeared or are no longer fully practised.","zh":"失落的文化，是已經消失或不再被完整實踐的文化。"},{"en":"A lost culture may survive only through objects, stories, old songs, or place names.","zh":"失落的文化可能只透過物件、故事、舊歌或地名保存。"},{"en":"If a language dies, knowledge from its culture may become harder to recover.","zh":"如果語言死亡，其文化知識可能變得更難恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cultures no longer living in a complete form.","zh":"這個短語描述不再以完整形式存在的文化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"readily available","meaning":"容易取得；方便使用","examples":[{"en":"The project makes cultural materials readily available.","zh":"該計劃令文化材料容易取得。"},{"en":"Readily available means easy to obtain, find, or use.","zh":"容易取得，指容易獲得、找到或使用。"},{"en":"Clean drinking water should be readily available in schools and hospitals.","zh":"學校和醫院應有容易取得的清潔飲用水。"},{"en":"If recordings are readily available, teachers can use them in community language classes.","zh":"如果錄音容易取得，老師就能在社群語言課中使用它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes easy access.","zh":"這個短語描述容易存取。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"oral tradition","meaning":"口述傳統","examples":[{"en":"For many communities, the oral tradition is at the heart of their culture.","zh":"對許多社群來說，口述傳統位於其文化核心。"},{"en":"Oral tradition is the passing down of stories, history, songs, and knowledge by speech.","zh":"口述傳統，是透過說話傳承故事、歷史、歌曲和知識。"},{"en":"A grandmother telling family history at dinner is part of oral tradition.","zh":"祖母在晚飯時講述家族歷史，就是口述傳統的一部分。"},{"en":"If oral tradition weakens, children may lose access to community memory.","zh":"如果口述傳統削弱，孩子可能失去接觸社群記憶的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to cultural knowledge carried by speaking and listening.","zh":"這個短語指由說話和聆聽承載的文化知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at the heart of","meaning":"位於……的核心","examples":[{"en":"The oral tradition is at the heart of many indigenous cultures.","zh":"口述傳統位於許多原住民文化的核心。"},{"en":"At the heart of something means at the centre or most important part of it.","zh":"位於某事的核心，指在其中心或最重要部分。"},{"en":"Trust is at the heart of a good teacher-student relationship.","zh":"信任位於良好師生關係的核心。"},{"en":"If language is at the heart of culture, losing it affects more than communication.","zh":"如果語言位於文化核心，失去它影響的不只是溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the core of something.","zh":"這個短語指出某事的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"creative as well as communicative","meaning":"既具創意又具溝通功能","examples":[{"en":"The stories are creative as well as communicative.","zh":"這些故事既具創意又具溝通功能。"},{"en":"Creative as well as communicative means something expresses imagination and also carries information or meaning.","zh":"既具創意又具溝通功能，指某事表達想像力，同時傳遞資訊或意思。"},{"en":"A good classroom poster can be creative as well as communicative if it looks interesting and explains clearly.","zh":"如果課室海報既有趣又解釋清楚，它就可以既具創意又具溝通功能。"},{"en":"If oral stories entertain and teach, they serve both artistic and practical purposes.","zh":"如果口述故事既娛樂又教導，它們就同時有藝術和實用目的。"},{"en":"The phrase joins imagination with communication.","zh":"這個短語把想像力與溝通連在一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"celebrated written traditions","meaning":"著名的書寫傳統","examples":[{"en":"Sanskrit, Hebrew and Ancient Greek have celebrated written traditions.","zh":"梵語、希伯來語和古希臘語都有著名的書寫傳統。"},{"en":"Celebrated written traditions are famous and respected bodies of texts in a language.","zh":"著名的書寫傳統，是某語言中知名而受尊重的文本體系。"},{"en":"Classical Chinese has a celebrated written tradition of poetry, history, and philosophy.","zh":"古典中文有詩歌、歷史和哲學方面的著名書寫傳統。"},{"en":"If a language has a celebrated written tradition, its texts may be studied for centuries.","zh":"如果一種語言有著名書寫傳統，其文本可能被研究數百年。"},{"en":"The phrase describes written culture that is widely admired.","zh":"這個短語描述廣受欣賞的書面文化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"such as","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"Some languages, such as Sanskrit and Hebrew, have long written traditions.","zh":"一些語言，例如梵語和希伯來語，有悠久書寫傳統。"},{"en":"Such as introduces examples of the thing being discussed.","zh":"例如，用來引入正在討論事物的例子。"},{"en":"Students need basic supplies, such as pens, notebooks, and a dictionary.","zh":"學生需要基本用品，例如筆、筆記簿和字典。"},{"en":"If a writer says “such as,” the words after it are examples, not the whole list.","zh":"如果作者說 “such as”，其後詞語是例子，而不是完整清單。"},{"en":"The phrase helps make a general idea concrete.","zh":"這個短語幫助把一般想法具體化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"recorded their own languages","meaning":"記錄自己的語言","examples":[{"en":"Few indigenous communities have recorded their own languages.","zh":"很少原住民社群記錄了自己的語言。"},{"en":"Recorded their own languages means made audio, video, or written records of the languages they speak.","zh":"記錄自己的語言，指為自己所說的語言製作錄音、影片或文字記錄。"},{"en":"A community may record its own language by filming elders telling stories.","zh":"社群可能透過拍攝長者講故事來記錄自己的語言。"},{"en":"If communities record their own languages, they can preserve pronunciation and cultural meaning.","zh":"如果社群記錄自己的語言，就能保存發音和文化意義。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses self-documentation by the speakers themselves.","zh":"這個短語強調由說話者自己進行記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"until now","meaning":"直到現在","examples":[{"en":"Many of these languages had never been recorded until now.","zh":"這些語言中有許多直到現在都從未被記錄。"},{"en":"Until now means up to the present moment, before this current time.","zh":"直到現在，指一直到目前這一刻，在此之前。"},{"en":"The school had never offered Italian until now.","zh":"學校直到現在才首次開辦意大利語。"},{"en":"If a language has never been recorded until now, the first recording is historically important.","zh":"如果一種語言直到現在都從未被記錄，第一次記錄就有歷史重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a change from the past to the present.","zh":"這個短語標示從過去到現在的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"suggest itself","meaning":"自然浮現；應運而生","examples":[{"en":"The project suggested itself when Turin was teaching in Nepal.","zh":"Turin 在尼泊爾教書時，這項計劃自然浮現。"},{"en":"If an idea suggests itself, it seems to appear naturally because the situation makes it obvious.","zh":"如果一個想法自然浮現，意思是情況令它看起來自然出現而且明顯。"},{"en":"When students kept asking the same grammar question, a new worksheet suggested itself.","zh":"當學生不斷問同一個文法問題，一份新工作紙就自然浮現。"},{"en":"If a problem appears again and again, a project to solve it may naturally suggest itself.","zh":"如果問題一次又一次出現，解決它的計劃可能自然應運而生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an idea arising naturally from circumstances.","zh":"這個短語描述想法由情況自然產生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"study for a PhD","meaning":"攻讀博士學位","examples":[{"en":"Turin wanted to study for a PhD in endangered languages.","zh":"Turin 想攻讀瀕危語言博士學位。"},{"en":"To study for a PhD means to do advanced university research for a doctoral degree.","zh":"攻讀博士學位，指為博士學位進行高階大學研究。"},{"en":"A student may study for a PhD after completing a master’s degree.","zh":"學生完成碩士學位後可能攻讀博士學位。"},{"en":"If someone studies for a PhD, they usually focus deeply on one research question for several years.","zh":"如果某人攻讀博士學位，通常會用數年深入研究一個問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to doctoral-level academic study.","zh":"這個短語指博士層次的學術研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"endangered languages","meaning":"瀕危語言","examples":[{"en":"Turin chose to study endangered languages.","zh":"Turin 選擇研究瀕危語言。"},{"en":"Endangered languages are languages at risk of disappearing because too few people speak them.","zh":"瀕危語言，是因使用者太少而有消失風險的語言。"},{"en":"A language spoken only by elderly villagers may be an endangered language.","zh":"只由年老村民使用的語言可能是瀕危語言。"},{"en":"If children do not learn an endangered language, it may die with the older generation.","zh":"如果孩子不學瀕危語言，它可能隨年長一代逝去而消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes languages needing urgent protection.","zh":"這個短語描述需要緊急保護的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"while discussing it with","meaning":"與……討論此事時","examples":[{"en":"While discussing it with his professor, Turin noticed a map on the wall.","zh":"與教授討論此事時，Turin 注意到牆上的一幅地圖。"},{"en":"While discussing it with someone means during a conversation about that topic with that person.","zh":"與某人討論此事時，指在與該人談論該主題的過程中。"},{"en":"While discussing the project with her teacher, a student realised she needed clearer data.","zh":"與老師討論項目時，學生意識到自己需要更清楚數據。"},{"en":"If an idea changes while being discussed, conversation can shape research direction.","zh":"如果想法在討論時改變，對話可以塑造研究方向。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the background action happening at the same time.","zh":"這個短語交代同時發生的背景動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be drawn to","meaning":"被……吸引","examples":[{"en":"Turin was drawn to a map on his tutor’s wall.","zh":"Turin 被導師牆上的一幅地圖吸引。"},{"en":"To be drawn to something means to feel attracted to it or interested in it.","zh":"被某物吸引，指對它感到吸引或有興趣。"},{"en":"A child may be drawn to a colourful book cover in a library.","zh":"孩子可能被圖書館中一本色彩鮮艷的書封面吸引。"},{"en":"If a researcher is drawn to a map full of unknown languages, curiosity may lead to fieldwork.","zh":"如果研究者被一幅充滿未知語言的地圖吸引，好奇心可能導致田野調查。"},{"en":"The phrase describes attention being pulled toward something.","zh":"這個短語描述注意力被某物拉過去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a map full of pins","meaning":"插滿圖釘的地圖","examples":[{"en":"The professor had a map full of pins on his wall.","zh":"教授牆上有一幅插滿圖釘的地圖。"},{"en":"A map full of pins is a map with many small markers placed on it.","zh":"插滿圖釘的地圖，是放有許多小標記的地圖。"},{"en":"A travel planner may use a map full of pins to mark places already visited.","zh":"旅行規劃者可能用插滿圖釘的地圖標示已到訪地方。"},{"en":"If each pin marks an undocumented language, the map shows many research possibilities.","zh":"如果每枚圖釘標示一種未記錄語言，該地圖就顯示許多研究可能性。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a visual image of many marked locations.","zh":"這個短語創造出許多地點被標記的視覺圖像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a variety of colours","meaning":"各種顏色","examples":[{"en":"The pins on the map were a variety of colours.","zh":"地圖上的圖釘有各種顏色。"},{"en":"A variety of colours means several different colours.","zh":"各種顏色，指幾種不同顏色。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a variety of colours to mark grammar, vocabulary, and organisation in an essay.","zh":"老師可能用各種顏色標示文章中的文法、詞彙和組織。"},{"en":"If map pins use different colours, each colour may represent a different category.","zh":"如果地圖圖釘使用不同顏色，每種顏色可能代表不同類別。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visual variety.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"represent all the world’s languages","meaning":"代表世界上的語言","examples":[{"en":"The pins represented languages that were completely undocumented.","zh":"這些圖釘代表完全沒有記錄的語言。"},{"en":"To represent languages means to stand for or indicate those languages on a map, chart, or record.","zh":"代表語言，指在地圖、圖表或記錄中表示那些語言。"},{"en":"A blue dot on a map may represent a school, while a red dot may represent a hospital.","zh":"地圖上的藍點可能代表學校，而紅點可能代表醫院。"},{"en":"If pins represent undocumented languages, the map shows where research is needed.","zh":"如果圖釘代表未記錄語言，地圖就顯示哪裡需要研究。"},{"en":"The phrase describes symbols standing for languages.","zh":"這個短語描述符號代表語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"completely undocumented","meaning":"完全沒有記錄","examples":[{"en":"The map showed languages that were completely undocumented.","zh":"地圖顯示完全沒有記錄的語言。"},{"en":"Completely undocumented means not recorded at all in writing, audio, video, or formal research.","zh":"完全沒有記錄，指在文字、錄音、影片或正式研究中完全沒有被記下。"},{"en":"A family story is completely undocumented if nobody has written it down or recorded it.","zh":"如果沒有人寫下或錄下某家庭故事，它就是完全沒有記錄。"},{"en":"If a language is completely undocumented, losing its speakers may mean losing all evidence of it.","zh":"如果一種語言完全沒有記錄，失去其說話者可能意味失去所有證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes total absence of records.","zh":"這個短語描述記錄完全缺失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at random","meaning":"隨機地","examples":[{"en":"Turin chose a language to document at random.","zh":"Turin 隨機地選擇一種語言來記錄。"},{"en":"At random means without a planned reason, pattern, or careful selection.","zh":"隨機地，指沒有計劃原因、模式或仔細選擇。"},{"en":"A teacher may pick a student at random by drawing a name from a box.","zh":"老師可能從盒子抽名字，隨機地選一名學生。"},{"en":"If a research topic is chosen at random, chance rather than strategy decides it.","zh":"如果研究題目是隨機選擇，就是由機會而非策略決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes selection by chance.","zh":"這個短語描述由偶然決定的選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"happen to belong to","meaning":"碰巧屬於","examples":[{"en":"The pin happened to belong to the Thangmi tribe.","zh":"那枚圖釘碰巧屬於 Thangmi 部族。"},{"en":"To happen to belong to something means to belong to it by chance rather than design.","zh":"碰巧屬於某事物，指不是有意安排，而是偶然屬於它。"},{"en":"The book I picked happened to belong to my old teacher.","zh":"我拿起的那本書碰巧屬於我的舊老師。"},{"en":"If a selected pin happens to belong to one tribe, chance can shape a researcher’s career.","zh":"如果被選中的圖釘碰巧屬於某部族，偶然可以塑造研究者的事業。"},{"en":"The phrase shows accidental connection.","zh":"這個短語顯示偶然連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the Thangmi tribe","meaning":"Thangmi 部族","examples":[{"en":"The Thangmi tribe lives in the hills east of Kathmandu.","zh":"Thangmi 部族生活在加德滿都以東的山區。"},{"en":"The Thangmi tribe is an ethnic community associated with the Thangmi language and culture.","zh":"Thangmi 部族，是與 Thangmi 語言和文化相關的族群社區。"},{"en":"A researcher may work with the Thangmi tribe to record stories, vocabulary, and rituals.","zh":"研究者可能與 Thangmi 部族合作，記錄故事、詞彙和儀式。"},{"en":"If young Thangmi people stop speaking the language, the tribe’s oral traditions may weaken.","zh":"如果年輕 Thangmi 人停止說該語言，該部族的口述傳統可能削弱。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific indigenous community.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定原住民社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in the hills east of","meaning":"在……以東的山區","examples":[{"en":"The community lives in the hills east of Kathmandu.","zh":"該社群生活在加德滿都以東的山區。"},{"en":"In the hills east of a place means in the hilly area located to its east.","zh":"在某地以東的山區，指位於該地東面的丘陵或山區。"},{"en":"A village may lie in the hills east of a city, far from main roads.","zh":"一條村莊可能位於城市以東的山區，遠離主要道路。"},{"en":"If a community lives in remote hills, language documentation may require difficult travel.","zh":"如果社群生活在偏遠山區，語言記錄工作可能需要艱難旅程。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a geographic location.","zh":"這個短語給出地理位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the capital of Nepal","meaning":"尼泊爾首都","examples":[{"en":"Kathmandu is the capital of Nepal.","zh":"加德滿都是尼泊爾首都。"},{"en":"The capital of Nepal means the main city where the country’s government is based.","zh":"尼泊爾首都，指該國政府所在地的主要城市。"},{"en":"Students may learn that Paris is the capital of France and Kathmandu is the capital of Nepal.","zh":"學生可能學到巴黎是法國首都，而加德滿都是尼泊爾首都。"},{"en":"If a village is east of the capital, the capital can be used as a reference point on a map.","zh":"如果村莊位於首都以東，首都就可以作為地圖上的參照點。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a country’s main political city.","zh":"這個短語指出一個國家的主要政治城市。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"choices made by","meaning":"由……作出的選擇","examples":[{"en":"Many choices made by anthropologists are quite random.","zh":"許多由人類學家作出的選擇都相當隨機。"},{"en":"Choices made by someone are decisions that person or group takes.","zh":"由某人作出的選擇，是該人或群體所作的決定。"},{"en":"Choices made by parents can affect where children study and what language they use at home.","zh":"由父母作出的選擇可以影響孩子在哪裡讀書和在家使用甚麼語言。"},{"en":"If choices made by researchers are random, some communities may be studied while others are ignored.","zh":"如果由研究者作出的選擇是隨機的，一些社群可能被研究，而另一些被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who made the decision.","zh":"這個短語指出誰作出決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"traditional fieldwork projects","meaning":"傳統田野調查項目","examples":[{"en":"Anthropologists and linguists often work on traditional fieldwork projects.","zh":"人類學家和語言學家常從事傳統田野調查項目。"},{"en":"Traditional fieldwork projects are research projects where scholars go into communities to collect direct evidence.","zh":"傳統田野調查項目，是學者進入社群收集直接證據的研究項目。"},{"en":"A student may do fieldwork by visiting a market and interviewing shop owners.","zh":"學生可能透過到訪街市並訪問店主來做田野調查。"},{"en":"If language researchers do fieldwork, they can hear how people actually speak.","zh":"如果語言研究人員做田野調查，就能聽到人們實際如何說話。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to research outside the classroom or office.","zh":"這個短語指課室或辦公室以外的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"continue his work with","meaning":"繼續與……合作；繼續研究","examples":[{"en":"Turin continued his work with the Thangmi community in the 1990s.","zh":"Turin 在1990年代繼續與 Thangmi 社群合作研究。"},{"en":"To continue his work with a community means to keep researching or cooperating with that group.","zh":"繼續與某社群合作，指繼續研究或與該群體合作。"},{"en":"A teacher may continue her work with a reading club for several years.","zh":"老師可能多年繼續與閱讀小組合作。"},{"en":"If a researcher continues work with a community, trust and understanding can grow.","zh":"如果研究者持續與社群合作，信任和理解可以增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sustained cooperation.","zh":"這個短語描述持續合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"begin to record","meaning":"開始記錄","examples":[{"en":"Turin began to record the language he was hearing.","zh":"Turin 開始記錄他聽到的語言。"},{"en":"To begin to record something means to start making written, audio, or video records of it.","zh":"開始記錄某事，指開始為它製作文字、錄音或影片記錄。"},{"en":"A student may begin to record interviews for a history project.","zh":"學生可能開始為歷史項目記錄訪問。"},{"en":"If a language has never been recorded, the first recordings can preserve sounds and stories.","zh":"如果一種語言從未被記錄，最早錄音可以保存聲音和故事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the start of documentation.","zh":"這個短語描述記錄工作的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"known to few outside","meaning":"鮮為……以外的人所知","examples":[{"en":"The language was known to few outside the tiny community.","zh":"該語言鮮為這個小型社群以外的人所知。"},{"en":"Known to few outside a group means only a small number of people beyond that group know about it.","zh":"鮮為某群體以外的人所知，指在該群體之外只有少數人知道它。"},{"en":"A local recipe may be known to few outside one village.","zh":"一道本地食譜可能鮮為某條村以外的人所知。"},{"en":"If a language is known to few outsiders, it may receive little research attention.","zh":"如果一種語言鮮為外人所知，它可能得到很少研究關注。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limited outside awareness.","zh":"這個短語描述外界認識有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a tiny community","meaning":"小型社群","examples":[{"en":"The language was known to few outside the tiny community.","zh":"該語言鮮為這個小型社群以外的人所知。"},{"en":"A tiny community is a very small group of people living together or sharing an identity.","zh":"小型社群，是一起生活或共享身份的很小群體。"},{"en":"A tiny island community may have only a few hundred residents.","zh":"小型島嶼社群可能只有數百名居民。"},{"en":"If a language belongs to a tiny community, it may have very few speakers.","zh":"如果一種語言屬於小型社群，它可能只有很少說話者。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses small population size.","zh":"這個短語強調人口規模小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"set about trying to","meaning":"著手嘗試去","examples":[{"en":"Turin set about trying to record the language and its origin myth.","zh":"Turin 著手嘗試記錄該語言及其起源神話。"},{"en":"To set about trying to do something means to begin working seriously on it.","zh":"著手嘗試做某事，指開始認真努力處理它。"},{"en":"After receiving feedback, a student set about trying to rewrite the essay.","zh":"收到回饋後，學生著手嘗試重寫文章。"},{"en":"If a researcher sets about recording a language, they must plan interviews, tools, and translations.","zh":"如果研究者著手記錄一種語言，就必須規劃訪問、工具和翻譯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes starting a difficult task with effort.","zh":"這個短語描述開始努力處理困難任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"origin myth","meaning":"起源神話","examples":[{"en":"Turin wanted to record the community’s origin myth.","zh":"Turin 想記錄該社群的起源神話。"},{"en":"An origin myth is a traditional story explaining how a people, place, or custom began.","zh":"起源神話，是解釋一個民族、地方或習俗如何開始的傳統故事。"},{"en":"A village origin myth may explain how the first families arrived there.","zh":"村莊起源神話可能解釋最早的家庭如何到達那裡。"},{"en":"If an origin myth disappears, a community may lose part of its shared memory.","zh":"如果起源神話消失，社群可能失去部分共同記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a story of beginnings.","zh":"這個短語指關於起源的故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a 1,000-page grammar","meaning":"一本一千頁的語法書","examples":[{"en":"Turin wrote a 1,000-page grammar in English that nobody could use.","zh":"Turin 用英語寫了一本沒有人能使用的一千頁語法書。"},{"en":"A 1,000-page grammar is a very long book explaining the rules of a language.","zh":"一本一千頁的語法書，是解釋一種語言規則的非常長的書。"},{"en":"A student may find a 1,000-page grammar too difficult for daily learning.","zh":"學生可能覺得一本一千頁語法書太難以作日常學習。"},{"en":"If a grammar book is too long and technical, the community may not benefit from it.","zh":"如果語法書太長又太技術化，社群可能無法受益。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests an impressive but possibly impractical academic product.","zh":"這個短語暗示令人印象深刻但可能不實用的學術成果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"that wasn’t enough","meaning":"那並不足夠","examples":[{"en":"Turin realised that a 1,000-page grammar wasn’t enough.","zh":"Turin 意識到一本一千頁語法書並不足夠。"},{"en":"That wasn’t enough means something did not fully solve the problem or meet the need.","zh":"那並不足夠，指某事沒有完全解決問題或滿足需要。"},{"en":"A student may revise vocabulary, but if they never practise writing, that may not be enough.","zh":"學生可能溫習詞彙，但如果從不練習寫作，那可能並不足夠。"},{"en":"If research produces a book nobody can use, documentation alone is not enough.","zh":"如果研究產生一本沒有人能用的書，單是記錄並不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a missing practical purpose.","zh":"這個短語指出缺少實際用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not going to work","meaning":"不會奏效","examples":[{"en":"The grammar was not going to work as a useful resource for the community.","zh":"那本語法書不會作為社群的有用資源而奏效。"},{"en":"Not going to work means not likely to succeed or be useful.","zh":"不會奏效，指不大可能成功或有用。"},{"en":"A revision plan is not going to work if it leaves no time for sleep.","zh":"如果溫習計劃完全不留睡眠時間，它就不會奏效。"},{"en":"If a resource is written in a language the community cannot use, it will not serve them well.","zh":"如果資源用社群不能使用的語言寫成，它就不能好好服務他們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical failure.","zh":"這個短語描述實際失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"work as something for","meaning":"作為……的有用東西","examples":[{"en":"The grammar did not work as something useful for the community.","zh":"那本語法書不能作為對社群有用的東西。"},{"en":"To work as something for someone means to function effectively in that role for them.","zh":"對某人作為某物而奏效，指對他們有效發揮該角色。"},{"en":"A phone can work as a dictionary for students who need quick word meanings.","zh":"手機可以作為需要快速查詞學生的字典。"},{"en":"If a book is too technical, it may not work as a teaching tool for children.","zh":"如果一本書太技術化，它可能不能作為兒童教學工具。"},{"en":"The phrase describes whether something serves a practical role.","zh":"這個短語描述某物是否發揮實際角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a trilingual word list","meaning":"三語詞彙表","examples":[{"en":"Turin produced a trilingual word list in Thangmi, Nepali and English.","zh":"Turin 製作了一份 Thangmi、尼泊爾語和英語三語詞彙表。"},{"en":"A trilingual word list is a list of words presented in three languages.","zh":"三語詞彙表，是以三種語言呈現詞語的列表。"},{"en":"A school may create a trilingual word list for English, Chinese, and Urdu-speaking families.","zh":"學校可能為說英語、中文和烏爾都語的家庭製作三語詞彙表。"},{"en":"If a word list includes local and national languages, it can help both children and outsiders learn.","zh":"如果詞彙表包括本地語言和國語，就能幫助孩子和外人學習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a simple three-language learning resource.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單的三語學習資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the first ever publication of","meaning":"……的首份出版物","examples":[{"en":"The word list was the first ever publication of the Thangmi language.","zh":"該詞彙表是 Thangmi 語言的首份出版物。"},{"en":"The first ever publication of something means the first printed or released work of that kind.","zh":"某物的首份出版物，指該類作品第一次被印刷或發行。"},{"en":"A school magazine may be the first ever publication of students’ poems in a new club.","zh":"學校雜誌可能是新學會中學生詩作的首份出版物。"},{"en":"If a language has its first publication, it gains a visible written presence.","zh":"如果一種語言有首份出版物，它就得到可見的書面存在。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a historical first.","zh":"這個短語標示歷史上的第一次。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a modest 20 rupees","meaning":"區區二十盧比","examples":[{"en":"The small dictionary is sold for a modest 20 rupees.","zh":"這本小字典以區區二十盧比出售。"},{"en":"A modest 20 rupees means a small and affordable amount of money.","zh":"區區二十盧比，指小額而負擔得起的金錢。"},{"en":"A school booklet sold for a modest price can reach more families.","zh":"以低廉價格出售的學校小冊子可以接觸更多家庭。"},{"en":"If a dictionary is cheap, more children and parents can buy it.","zh":"如果字典便宜，更多孩子和家長就能購買。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests low cost and practical access.","zh":"這個短語暗示低成本和實際可及性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as part of","meaning":"作為……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"The dictionary is used as part of a wider cultural regeneration process.","zh":"這本字典作為更廣泛文化復興過程的一部分被使用。"},{"en":"As part of something means included within a larger plan, process, or activity.","zh":"作為某事的一部分，指包含在較大的計劃、過程或活動之內。"},{"en":"Students may do interviews as part of a history project.","zh":"學生可能作為歷史項目的一部分進行訪問。"},{"en":"If a dictionary is part of cultural revival, it supports more than vocabulary learning.","zh":"如果字典是文化復興的一部分，它支援的不只是詞彙學習。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one action belongs to a bigger effort.","zh":"這個短語顯示一項行動屬於更大努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a wider cultural regeneration process","meaning":"更廣泛的文化復興過程","examples":[{"en":"The dictionary supports a wider cultural regeneration process.","zh":"這本字典支援更廣泛的文化復興過程。"},{"en":"A wider cultural regeneration process is a broader effort to revive and strengthen a community’s culture.","zh":"更廣泛的文化復興過程，是復興並強化社群文化的較大努力。"},{"en":"A village may begin cultural regeneration by teaching songs, festivals, crafts, and language to children.","zh":"村莊可能透過教孩子歌曲、節日、手藝和語言來開始文化復興。"},{"en":"If language materials are created, they can support a larger revival of identity and heritage.","zh":"如果語言材料被創造出來，它們可以支援更大的身份和文化遺產復興。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cultural recovery beyond one small product.","zh":"這個短語描述超越一個小產品的文化恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"educate children about","meaning":"讓兒童認識；教育兒童了解","examples":[{"en":"The dictionary helps educate children about their heritage and language.","zh":"這本字典幫助兒童認識自己的文化遺產和語言。"},{"en":"To educate children about something means to teach them to understand it.","zh":"教育兒童了解某事，指教他們理解它。"},{"en":"Schools educate children about road safety through signs, stories, and practice.","zh":"學校透過標誌、故事和練習教育兒童了解道路安全。"},{"en":"If children learn about their heritage, they may feel more connected to their community.","zh":"如果孩子了解自己的文化遺產，他們可能更感到與社群相連。"},{"en":"The phrase describes teaching for understanding, not just memorising.","zh":"這個短語描述為理解而教，而不只是背誦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"heritage and language","meaning":"文化遺產和語言","examples":[{"en":"Children learn about their heritage and language through the dictionary.","zh":"兒童透過這本字典學習自己的文化遺產和語言。"},{"en":"Heritage and language means a community’s inherited culture together with the language that carries it.","zh":"文化遺產和語言，指社群繼承下來的文化，以及承載該文化的語言。"},{"en":"A family may pass on heritage and language through stories, festivals, names, and songs.","zh":"家庭可能透過故事、節日、名字和歌曲傳承文化遺產和語言。"},{"en":"If children lose their language, part of their heritage may become harder to understand.","zh":"如果孩子失去自己的語言，部分文化遺產可能變得更難理解。"},{"en":"The phrase links cultural inheritance with speech.","zh":"這個短語把文化繼承與說話連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"no small undertaking","meaning":"絕非小事；艱巨任務","examples":[{"en":"Recording languages in Nepal is no small undertaking.","zh":"在尼泊爾記錄語言絕非小事。"},{"en":"No small undertaking means a difficult, large, or serious task.","zh":"絕非小事，指困難、龐大或嚴肅的任務。"},{"en":"Organising a school concert for 800 people is no small undertaking.","zh":"為800人組織學校音樂會絕非小事。"},{"en":"If a country has many ethnic groups and languages, recording them is a major challenge.","zh":"如果一個國家有許多族群和語言，記錄它們就是重大挑戰。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that a task is demanding.","zh":"這個短語強調任務艱巨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"massive ethnic and linguistic diversity","meaning":"大規模的族群及語言多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Nepal has massive ethnic and linguistic diversity.","zh":"尼泊爾有大規模的族群及語言多樣性。"},{"en":"Massive ethnic and linguistic diversity means a very large variety of ethnic groups and languages.","zh":"大規模的族群及語言多樣性，指族群和語言種類非常多。"},{"en":"A city with many migrant communities may show ethnic and linguistic diversity in schools and markets.","zh":"有許多移民社群的城市，可能在學校和街市中展現族群及語言多樣性。"},{"en":"If diversity is massive, one national language may not represent everyone’s identity.","zh":"如果多樣性很大，單一國語未必能代表每個人的身份。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights great human and language variety.","zh":"這個短語突出巨大的人群和語言多樣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"language families","meaning":"語系","examples":[{"en":"Nepal is home to languages from four different language families.","zh":"尼泊爾擁有來自四個不同語系的語言。"},{"en":"Language families are groups of languages that developed from a common historical source.","zh":"語系，是從共同歷史來源發展出來的語言群組。"},{"en":"English, German, and Dutch belong to the same broad language family.","zh":"英語、德語和荷蘭語屬於同一個大語系。"},{"en":"If a country has several language families, its linguistic history is especially complex.","zh":"如果一個國家有幾個語系，其語言歷史就特別複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase groups languages by origin and relationship.","zh":"這個短語按起源和關係把語言分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"what’s more","meaning":"而且","examples":[{"en":"What’s more, few ethnic Thangmi still speak the Thangmi language.","zh":"而且，很少 Thangmi 族人仍然說 Thangmi 語。"},{"en":"What’s more introduces an additional point, often one that strengthens the previous idea.","zh":"而且，用來引入額外觀點，通常加強前面的想法。"},{"en":"The flat is far from school; what’s more, the rent is too high.","zh":"那間公寓離學校很遠；而且，租金太高。"},{"en":"If a language is undocumented and few people speak it, the danger becomes even greater.","zh":"如果一種語言沒有記錄，而且很少人使用，危險就更大。"},{"en":"The phrase adds another important detail.","zh":"這個短語加入另一個重要細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ethnic Thangmi","meaning":"Thangmi 族人","examples":[{"en":"Few ethnic Thangmi still speak the Thangmi language.","zh":"很少 Thangmi 族人仍然說 Thangmi 語。"},{"en":"Ethnic Thangmi refers to people who belong to the Thangmi ethnic group.","zh":"Thangmi 族人，指屬於 Thangmi 族群的人。"},{"en":"An ethnic Thangmi child may grow up hearing Nepali at school and Thangmi from grandparents.","zh":"Thangmi 族孩子可能在學校聽尼泊爾語，在祖父母身邊聽 Thangmi 語。"},{"en":"If ethnic Thangmi people shift to another language, their ancestral language may weaken.","zh":"如果 Thangmi 族人轉用另一種語言，其祖傳語言可能削弱。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies people by ethnic community.","zh":"這個短語按族群社區辨認人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take to doing something","meaning":"開始習慣做某事；轉而做某事","examples":[{"en":"Many community members have taken to speaking Nepali.","zh":"許多社群成員已開始習慣說尼泊爾語。"},{"en":"To take to doing something means to begin doing it regularly or develop the habit of doing it.","zh":"開始習慣做某事，指開始經常做它或養成做它的習慣。"},{"en":"A student may take to reading English news every morning.","zh":"學生可能開始習慣每天早上閱讀英文新聞。"},{"en":"If young people take to speaking the national language, the local language may be used less.","zh":"如果年輕人開始習慣說國語，本地語言可能被使用得較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adopting a new habit or practice.","zh":"這個短語描述採納新習慣或做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the national language","meaning":"國語；全國通用語言","examples":[{"en":"Nepali is the national language taught in schools.","zh":"尼泊爾語是在學校教授的國語。"},{"en":"The national language is the language officially or widely used to represent a country.","zh":"國語，是正式或廣泛用來代表一個國家的語言。"},{"en":"A national language may be used in schools, government offices, television, and official signs.","zh":"國語可能用於學校、政府辦公室、電視和官方標誌。"},{"en":"If education uses the national language only, smaller community languages may weaken.","zh":"如果教育只使用國語，較小社群語言可能削弱。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a language connected with national identity and public life.","zh":"這個短語指與國家身份和公共生活相關的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"spread through the media","meaning":"透過媒體傳播","examples":[{"en":"Nepali is taught in schools and spread through the media.","zh":"尼泊爾語在學校教授，並透過媒體傳播。"},{"en":"To spread through the media means to become widely known or used through television, radio, newspapers, or the internet.","zh":"透過媒體傳播，指透過電視、電台、報紙或互聯網變得廣為人知或被使用。"},{"en":"A new slang word may spread through the media after it appears in a popular drama.","zh":"新潮語可能在流行劇集中出現後透過媒體傳播。"},{"en":"If a national language spreads through media, young people may hear it more than their local language.","zh":"如果國語透過媒體傳播，年輕人可能聽到它多於本地語言。"},{"en":"The phrase describes transmission by communication channels.","zh":"這個短語描述透過傳播渠道傳送。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"community elders","meaning":"社群長者","examples":[{"en":"Community elders are dying without passing on their knowledge.","zh":"社群長者正在離世，卻沒有傳承他們的知識。"},{"en":"Community elders are older respected members of a community who often carry memory, language, and traditions.","zh":"社群長者，是社群中年長而受尊重的成員，常承載記憶、語言和傳統。"},{"en":"A village may invite community elders to teach children old songs and stories.","zh":"村莊可能邀請社群長者教孩子舊歌和故事。"},{"en":"If community elders pass away before recording their knowledge, valuable traditions may be lost.","zh":"如果社群長者在記錄知識前離世，寶貴傳統可能流失。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to older knowledge-holders.","zh":"這個短語指年長的知識持有者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pass on knowledge","meaning":"傳承知識","examples":[{"en":"Some elders die without passing on their knowledge.","zh":"一些長者離世時沒有傳承知識。"},{"en":"To pass on knowledge means to teach or share what one knows with the next person or generation.","zh":"傳承知識，指把自己知道的事情教導或分享給下一個人或下一代。"},{"en":"A chef may pass on knowledge by teaching apprentices how to prepare a traditional dish.","zh":"廚師可能透過教徒弟準備傳統菜式來傳承知識。"},{"en":"If elders do not pass on knowledge, younger people may lose skills and stories.","zh":"如果長者不傳承知識，年輕人可能失去技能和故事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes transmission of learning across people.","zh":"這個短語描述知識在人之間傳遞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"despite someone’s enthusiasm for","meaning":"儘管某人對……充滿熱誠","examples":[{"en":"Despite Turin’s enthusiasm for his subject, he is baffled by many linguists’ response.","zh":"儘管 Turin 對自己的研究主題充滿熱誠，他仍對許多語言學家的反應感到困惑。"},{"en":"Despite someone’s enthusiasm for something means although that person feels strong interest or excitement about it.","zh":"儘管某人對某事充滿熱誠，指雖然該人對它有強烈興趣或興奮感。"},{"en":"Despite a teacher’s enthusiasm for poetry, some students may still find it difficult.","zh":"儘管老師對詩歌充滿熱誠，一些學生仍可能覺得它困難。"},{"en":"If someone is enthusiastic but others refuse to engage, they may feel frustrated.","zh":"如果某人很有熱誠，但其他人拒絕參與，他可能感到沮喪。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces contrast between passion and difficulty.","zh":"這個短語引入熱情與困難之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be baffled by","meaning":"對……感到困惑","examples":[{"en":"Turin is baffled by many linguists’ refusal to engage with the issue.","zh":"Turin 對許多語言學家拒絕處理這個議題感到困惑。"},{"en":"To be baffled by something means to feel confused because it is difficult to understand.","zh":"對某事感到困惑，指因難以理解而感到混亂。"},{"en":"A student may be baffled by a maths question if the steps are not clear.","zh":"如果步驟不清楚，學生可能對數學題感到困惑。"},{"en":"If experts ignore an urgent problem, other researchers may be baffled by their reaction.","zh":"如果專家忽視緊急問題，其他研究者可能對他們的反應感到困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes confusion and surprise.","zh":"這個短語描述困惑和驚訝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"refusal to engage with","meaning":"拒絕參與；拒絕處理","examples":[{"en":"Turin criticises many linguists’ refusal to engage with endangered languages.","zh":"Turin 批評許多語言學家拒絕處理瀕危語言。"},{"en":"Refusal to engage with something means unwillingness to deal with, discuss, or take part in it.","zh":"拒絕處理某事，指不願意處理、討論或參與它。"},{"en":"A manager’s refusal to engage with staff complaints can make workers angry.","zh":"經理拒絕處理員工投訴，可能令工人憤怒。"},{"en":"If scholars refuse to engage with endangered languages, documentation may be delayed.","zh":"如果學者拒絕參與瀕危語言工作，記錄工作可能被延誤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes avoidance of an important issue.","zh":"這個短語描述逃避重要議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"spoken forms","meaning":"口語形式","examples":[{"en":"Many spoken forms are endangered because they have no written tradition.","zh":"許多口語形式因沒有書寫傳統而瀕危。"},{"en":"Spoken forms are versions of language used in speech rather than writing.","zh":"口語形式，是用於說話而非書寫的語言形式。"},{"en":"A dialect may survive as a spoken form even if people rarely write it down.","zh":"方言可能作為口語形式存續，即使人們很少把它寫下來。"},{"en":"If a spoken form has no written record, audio recording becomes especially important.","zh":"如果口語形式沒有文字記錄，錄音就特別重要。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights language as people actually speak it.","zh":"這個短語強調人們實際說出的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in this day and age","meaning":"在現今這個時代","examples":[{"en":"Turin is surprised that, in this day and age, our image of linguistic diversity is still incomplete.","zh":"Turin 感到驚訝，在現今這個時代，我們對語言多樣性的認識仍不完整。"},{"en":"In this day and age means in the modern world or present time.","zh":"在現今這個時代，指在現代世界或當下。"},{"en":"In this day and age, students often use phones to search for vocabulary instantly.","zh":"在現今這個時代，學生常用手機即時搜尋詞彙。"},{"en":"If modern technology exists, it may seem surprising that many languages remain undocumented.","zh":"如果現代科技已存在，許多語言仍未被記錄就可能令人驚訝。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts modern conditions with an unexpected problem.","zh":"這個短語把現代條件與意外問題作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an incomplete image of","meaning":"對……不完整的認識","examples":[{"en":"We still have an incomplete image of the world’s linguistic diversity.","zh":"我們對世界語言多樣性仍有不完整的認識。"},{"en":"An incomplete image of something is an understanding that is missing important parts.","zh":"對某事不完整的認識，是缺少重要部分的理解。"},{"en":"A teacher has an incomplete image of a student if they only look at test scores.","zh":"如果老師只看測驗分數，就會對學生有不完整的認識。"},{"en":"If many languages are undocumented, our picture of human language remains incomplete.","zh":"如果許多語言未被記錄，我們對人類語言的圖像仍不完整。"},{"en":"The phrase describes partial understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述部分理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the world’s linguistic diversity","meaning":"世界語言多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Researchers still do not fully understand the world’s linguistic diversity.","zh":"研究人員仍未完全理解世界語言多樣性。"},{"en":"The world’s linguistic diversity means the full range of languages and language varieties across the planet.","zh":"世界語言多樣性，指全球語言和語言變體的完整範圍。"},{"en":"A language map can show part of the world’s linguistic diversity.","zh":"語言地圖可以顯示世界語言多樣性的一部分。"},{"en":"If small languages disappear, the world’s linguistic diversity becomes poorer.","zh":"如果小語言消失，世界語言多樣性就變得更貧乏。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to global language variety.","zh":"這個短語指全球語言種類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"do PhDs on","meaning":"以……為題攻讀博士","examples":[{"en":"Some people do PhDs on very narrow topics in language.","zh":"有些人以非常狹窄的語言題目攻讀博士。"},{"en":"To do a PhD on a topic means to research that topic deeply for a doctoral degree.","zh":"以某題目攻讀博士，指為博士學位深入研究該題目。"},{"en":"A student may do a PhD on how children learn two languages at home.","zh":"學生可能以兒童如何在家學習兩種語言為題攻讀博士。"},{"en":"If scholars do PhDs on tiny details but ignore endangered languages, priorities may be questioned.","zh":"如果學者以細微細節攻讀博士卻忽視瀕危語言，其優先次序可能受質疑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes advanced academic research focus.","zh":"這個短語描述高階學術研究焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the apostrophe in French","meaning":"法語中的撇號","examples":[{"en":"Turin mentions the apostrophe in French as an example of a narrow research topic.","zh":"Turin 提到法語中的撇號，作為狹窄研究題目的例子。"},{"en":"The apostrophe in French is the small punctuation mark used in forms such as l’homme.","zh":"法語中的撇號，是用於 l’homme 等形式中的小標點符號。"},{"en":"A grammar student may study the apostrophe in French when learning elision.","zh":"文法學生學習省音時，可能研究法語中的撇號。"},{"en":"If researchers focus only on small punctuation details, wider language loss may be overlooked.","zh":"如果研究者只聚焦於細小標點細節，更廣泛的語言流失可能被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase is used here to represent a very specific academic topic.","zh":"這個短語在此代表非常具體的學術題目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"yet we still do not know","meaning":"然而我們仍然不知道","examples":[{"en":"People study tiny details of language, yet we still do not know how many languages are spoken.","zh":"人們研究語言的細微細節，然而我們仍然不知道有多少語言被使用。"},{"en":"Yet we still do not know means despite other knowledge, an important fact remains unknown.","zh":"然而我們仍然不知道，指儘管有其他知識，一個重要事實仍然未知。"},{"en":"We have many exam statistics, yet we still do not know why some students feel hopeless.","zh":"我們有許多考試統計，然而仍然不知道為何一些學生感到絕望。"},{"en":"If scholars know small details but not the number of languages, the field has a serious gap.","zh":"如果學者知道小細節卻不知道語言數量，該領域就有嚴重缺口。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights contrast between knowledge and ignorance.","zh":"這個短語突出知識與無知之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"become endangered","meaning":"變得瀕危","examples":[{"en":"When a language becomes endangered, a cultural world view is also at risk.","zh":"當一種語言變得瀕危，一種文化世界觀也同樣面臨風險。"},{"en":"To become endangered means to become at risk of disappearing or dying out.","zh":"變得瀕危，指變得有消失或滅絕風險。"},{"en":"A local festival may become endangered if only a few elderly people still organise it.","zh":"如果只有少數長者仍然組織某本地節日，它可能變得瀕危。"},{"en":"If young people stop using a language, it can become endangered within a generation.","zh":"如果年輕人停止使用一種語言，它可能在一代人內變得瀕危。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement into a dangerous state.","zh":"這個短語描述進入危險狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"so too does","meaning":"……也同樣如此","examples":[{"en":"When a language becomes endangered, so too does a cultural world view.","zh":"當一種語言變得瀕危，一種文化世界觀也同樣如此。"},{"en":"So too does means the same thing also happens to another subject.","zh":"也同樣如此，指同一件事也發生在另一個主體上。"},{"en":"When a school loses good teachers, so too does the quality of learning.","zh":"當學校失去好老師，學習質素也同樣下降。"},{"en":"If a language weakens, cultural memory may weaken as well.","zh":"如果語言削弱，文化記憶也可能同樣削弱。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a parallel relationship.","zh":"這個短語建立平行關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a cultural world view","meaning":"文化世界觀","examples":[{"en":"An endangered language carries a cultural world view.","zh":"瀕危語言承載一種文化世界觀。"},{"en":"A cultural world view is the way a community understands life, nature, relationships, and values.","zh":"文化世界觀，是一個社群理解生活、自然、關係和價值的方式。"},{"en":"A fishing community’s world view may include special words for tides, winds, and sea animals.","zh":"漁民社群的世界觀可能包括描述潮汐、風和海洋動物的特殊詞語。"},{"en":"If a language disappears, its cultural world view may become harder to express.","zh":"如果語言消失，其文化世界觀可能變得更難表達。"},{"en":"The phrase links language with a community’s way of seeing the world.","zh":"這個短語把語言與社群看世界的方式連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"engage with indigenous people","meaning":"與原住民互動；與原住民合作","examples":[{"en":"The project wants to engage with indigenous people to document their traditions.","zh":"該計劃希望與原住民合作，以記錄他們的傳統。"},{"en":"To engage with indigenous people means to communicate and work respectfully with native communities.","zh":"與原住民互動，指與原住民社群尊重地溝通和合作。"},{"en":"A museum should engage with indigenous people before displaying their sacred objects.","zh":"博物館展示原住民神聖物件前，應先與原住民互動。"},{"en":"If researchers engage with communities, records may be more accurate and respectful.","zh":"如果研究人員與社群合作，記錄可能更準確也更尊重。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses active, respectful involvement.","zh":"這個短語強調積極而尊重的參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"document their myths and folklore","meaning":"記錄他們的神話和民間傳說","examples":[{"en":"Researchers want to document the myths and folklore of indigenous communities.","zh":"研究人員希望記錄原住民社群的神話和民間傳說。"},{"en":"To document their myths and folklore means to record traditional stories, beliefs, and folk knowledge.","zh":"記錄他們的神話和民間傳說，指記下傳統故事、信念和民間知識。"},{"en":"Students can document local folklore by interviewing elders about ghost stories and festivals.","zh":"學生可以透過訪問長者關於鬼故事和節日的內容，記錄本地民間傳說。"},{"en":"If myths and folklore are documented, they can be taught even after storytellers pass away.","zh":"如果神話和民間傳說被記錄，即使講故事者離世，它們仍可被教導。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preserving traditional spoken culture.","zh":"這個短語描述保存傳統口述文化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"myths and folklore","meaning":"神話和民間傳說","examples":[{"en":"Myths and folklore can be difficult to fund as research topics.","zh":"神話和民間傳說作為研究題目可能難以獲得資助。"},{"en":"Myths and folklore are traditional stories, legends, beliefs, and customs passed down in a community.","zh":"神話和民間傳說，是社群中傳承的傳統故事、傳奇、信念和習俗。"},{"en":"A village’s myths and folklore may explain mountains, rivers, spirits, or old heroes.","zh":"村莊的神話和民間傳說可能解釋山、河、神靈或古代英雄。"},{"en":"If myths and folklore are lost, a community loses part of its imagination and memory.","zh":"如果神話和民間傳說消失，社群就失去部分想像力和記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to traditional cultural storytelling and belief.","zh":"這個短語指傳統文化敘事和信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"find funding for","meaning":"為……尋找資助","examples":[{"en":"It can be hard to find funding for documenting myths and folklore.","zh":"為記錄神話和民間傳說尋找資助可能很困難。"},{"en":"To find funding for something means to obtain money to support it.","zh":"為某事尋找資助，指獲得金錢來支援它。"},{"en":"A school club may need to find funding for a community exhibition.","zh":"學校學會可能需要為社區展覽尋找資助。"},{"en":"If researchers cannot find funding, important recording work may never begin.","zh":"如果研究人員找不到資助，重要記錄工作可能永遠不會開始。"},{"en":"The phrase describes securing financial support.","zh":"這個短語描述取得財政支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be based outside","meaning":"以……以外的地方為基地","examples":[{"en":"It can be harder to find funding if you are based outside Western universities.","zh":"如果你以西方大學以外的地方為基地，尋找資助可能更困難。"},{"en":"To be based outside a place means to work or operate from somewhere other than that place.","zh":"以某地以外的地方為基地，指在該地之外工作或運作。"},{"en":"A charity based outside the city may understand rural problems better.","zh":"以城市以外地區為基地的慈善機構，可能更了解鄉郊問題。"},{"en":"If researchers are based outside wealthy institutions, they may have fewer funding opportunities.","zh":"如果研究人員不以富裕機構為基地，他們可能有較少資助機會。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where someone’s work is located.","zh":"這個短語指出某人的工作位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Western universities","meaning":"西方大學","examples":[{"en":"Researchers outside Western universities may find it harder to get funding.","zh":"西方大學以外的研究人員可能覺得更難取得資助。"},{"en":"Western universities are universities located mainly in Europe, North America, or other Western academic systems.","zh":"西方大學，主要指位於歐洲、北美或其他西方學術系統中的大學。"},{"en":"A researcher in a small local college may not have the same resources as major Western universities.","zh":"小型本地學院的研究人員未必有大型西方大學同樣的資源。"},{"en":"If funding is concentrated in Western universities, local scholars may be excluded.","zh":"如果資助集中在西方大學，本地學者可能被排除在外。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to powerful institutions in Western academic contexts.","zh":"這個短語指西方學術環境中的有力機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"struggles facing","meaning":"……面對的困難","examples":[{"en":"The paragraph discusses the struggles facing projects such as WOLP.","zh":"該段討論 WOLP 等項目面對的困難。"},{"en":"Struggles facing something are the difficulties or challenges it must deal with.","zh":"某事面對的困難，是它必須處理的困難或挑戰。"},{"en":"The struggles facing new teachers may include workload, discipline, and lesson planning.","zh":"新老師面對的困難可能包括工作量、紀律和備課。"},{"en":"If a language project lacks money and time, its struggles become more serious.","zh":"如果語言項目缺乏金錢和時間，其困難就更嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies problems confronting a person or project.","zh":"這個短語指出某人或項目面對的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"initiatives such as","meaning":"例如……的倡議","examples":[{"en":"Initiatives such as the World Oral Literature Project face many struggles.","zh":"例如世界口述文學計劃這類倡議面對許多困難。"},{"en":"Initiatives such as means projects or actions like the examples being named.","zh":"例如某某的倡議，指像被點名例子那樣的項目或行動。"},{"en":"Initiatives such as recycling schemes and food banks depend on community support.","zh":"例如回收計劃和食物銀行這類倡議，都依靠社區支持。"},{"en":"If initiatives such as WOLP lack funding, endangered traditions may remain undocumented.","zh":"如果 WOLP 等倡議缺乏資助，瀕危傳統可能仍未被記錄。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces examples of organised action.","zh":"這個短語引入有組織行動的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"historical examples","meaning":"歷史例子","examples":[{"en":"There are historical examples of successful language revival.","zh":"有一些成功語言復興的歷史例子。"},{"en":"Historical examples are cases from the past that help explain or support an idea.","zh":"歷史例子，是來自過去、幫助解釋或支持某想法的個案。"},{"en":"A teacher may use historical examples to show how cities recovered after disasters.","zh":"老師可能使用歷史例子，展示城市如何在災難後恢復。"},{"en":"If historical examples show revival is possible, endangered languages may not be hopeless.","zh":"如果歷史例子顯示復興是可能的，瀕危語言就未必沒有希望。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to evidence from history.","zh":"這個短語指來自歷史的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"point to the possibility that","meaning":"顯示……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"Historical examples point to the possibility that language restoration can succeed.","zh":"歷史例子顯示語言復興可能成功。"},{"en":"To point to the possibility that means to suggest that something may be true or achievable.","zh":"顯示某事的可能性，指暗示某事可能是真的或可以達成。"},{"en":"Improved test scores point to the possibility that the new teaching method is working.","zh":"改善了的測驗分數顯示新教學方法可能正在奏效。"},{"en":"If one language has been revived, it suggests other languages may also recover.","zh":"如果一種語言曾被復興，就暗示其他語言也可能恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces cautious evidence for hope.","zh":"這個短語引入帶有謹慎希望的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"language restoration","meaning":"語言復興","examples":[{"en":"The passage suggests that language restoration is possible.","zh":"文章暗示語言復興是可能的。"},{"en":"Language restoration is the process of bringing a weakened or unused language back into active use.","zh":"語言復興，是把已削弱或不再使用的語言重新帶回活躍使用的過程。"},{"en":"A community may begin language restoration by teaching children songs and everyday phrases.","zh":"社群可能透過教孩子歌曲和日常短語來開始語言復興。"},{"en":"If restoration succeeds, a language can return to homes, schools, and public life.","zh":"如果復興成功，語言可以重返家庭、學校和公共生活。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to reviving language use.","zh":"這個短語指恢復語言使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"no mere academic pipe dream","meaning":"並非純粹的學術空想","examples":[{"en":"Language restoration is no mere academic pipe dream.","zh":"語言復興並非純粹的學術空想。"},{"en":"No mere academic pipe dream means not just an unrealistic idea discussed by scholars.","zh":"並非純粹的學術空想，指不只是學者討論的不切實際想法。"},{"en":"A school garden is no mere dream if students, teachers, and parents actually build it.","zh":"如果學生、老師和家長真的建成學校花園，它就不是純粹夢想。"},{"en":"If Hebrew was revived, language restoration can be more than theory.","zh":"如果希伯來語曾被復興，語言復興就不只是理論。"},{"en":"The phrase rejects the idea that something is only unrealistic talk.","zh":"這個短語否定某事只是空談的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the revival of","meaning":"……的復興","examples":[{"en":"The revival of Hebrew is often cited as an important example.","zh":"希伯來語的復興常被引用為重要例子。"},{"en":"The revival of something is the process of bringing it back after decline or disappearance.","zh":"某事的復興，是它在衰退或消失後被帶回來的過程。"},{"en":"The revival of a local festival may begin when young people start organising it again.","zh":"當年輕人重新開始組織某本地節日，其復興可能開始。"},{"en":"If a language revival succeeds, speakers may use it again in daily life.","zh":"如果語言復興成功，使用者可能再次在日常生活中使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes return to life or activity.","zh":"這個短語描述重返生命或活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a modern form of Hebrew","meaning":"希伯來文的現代形式","examples":[{"en":"The revival of a modern form of Hebrew began in the 19th century.","zh":"希伯來文的現代形式在19世紀開始復興。"},{"en":"A modern form of Hebrew means a version of Hebrew adapted for contemporary everyday use.","zh":"希伯來文的現代形式，指適應當代日常使用的希伯來語版本。"},{"en":"A modern form of an old language may need new words for buses, phones, and computers.","zh":"古老語言的現代形式可能需要描述巴士、手機和電腦的新詞。"},{"en":"If a revived language is used in modern life, it must express modern ideas.","zh":"如果復興語言用於現代生活，它就必須表達現代想法。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that revival can involve adaptation.","zh":"這個短語顯示復興可以涉及適應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be cited as","meaning":"被引用為","examples":[{"en":"The revival of Hebrew is often cited as proof that languages can return to common use.","zh":"希伯來語的復興常被引用為語言可以重新普遍使用的證據。"},{"en":"To be cited as something means to be mentioned as evidence or an example of it.","zh":"被引用為某物，指被提及作為其證據或例子。"},{"en":"A successful school programme may be cited as a model for other schools.","zh":"成功的學校計劃可能被引用為其他學校的典範。"},{"en":"If Hebrew is cited as proof, it supports the argument that revival is possible.","zh":"如果希伯來語被引用為證據，它就支持復興是可能的這個論點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using something as supporting evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述用某物作支持證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"one of the best proofs that","meaning":"證明……的最佳例子之一","examples":[{"en":"Hebrew is one of the best proofs that a language can be revived.","zh":"希伯來語是證明語言可以復興的最佳例子之一。"},{"en":"One of the best proofs that means one of the strongest examples showing that something is true.","zh":"證明某事的最佳例子之一，指顯示某事為真的最有力例子之一。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement after daily practice is one of the best proofs that habits matter.","zh":"學生每天練習後進步，是證明習慣重要的最佳例子之一。"},{"en":"If a once-unused language becomes widely spoken, it strongly supports the possibility of revival.","zh":"如果一種一度不用的語言變得廣泛使用，它就強烈支持復興的可能性。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights especially powerful evidence.","zh":"這個短語突出特別有力的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"long dead","meaning":"停止使用已久的","examples":[{"en":"Languages long dead can sometimes be resurrected.","zh":"停止使用已久的語言有時可以被復興。"},{"en":"Long dead means not used or active for a very long time.","zh":"停止使用已久，指很長時間不再被使用或活躍。"},{"en":"A long-dead tradition may return when young people become interested in their heritage.","zh":"當年輕人對文化遺產產生興趣，停止已久的傳統可能回歸。"},{"en":"If a language is long dead, revival requires teaching materials, speakers, and social motivation.","zh":"如果一種語言停止使用已久，復興就需要教材、使用者和社會動力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something inactive for a long period.","zh":"這個短語描述長時間不活躍的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"small communities","meaning":"小社群","examples":[{"en":"Some endangered languages belong to small communities.","zh":"一些瀕危語言屬於小社群。"},{"en":"Small communities are groups with relatively few members, often living close together or sharing an identity.","zh":"小社群，是成員相對較少、通常住得接近或共享身份的群體。"},{"en":"A small fishing community may have special words for boats, tides, and storms.","zh":"小型漁民社群可能有描述船、潮汐和風暴的特殊詞語。"},{"en":"If a language belongs to a small community, every speaker can matter greatly.","zh":"如果一種語言屬於小社群，每一位使用者都可能非常重要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses limited population size.","zh":"這個短語強調人口規模有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be resurrected","meaning":"被復興；被重新使用","examples":[{"en":"Hebrew shows that a language can be resurrected.","zh":"希伯來語顯示語言可以被復興。"},{"en":"To be resurrected means to be brought back to life or active use after seeming dead.","zh":"被復興，指在看似死亡後被重新帶回生命或活躍使用。"},{"en":"An old market may be resurrected if residents restore it and start using it again.","zh":"如果居民修復舊街市並重新使用它，舊街市可能被復興。"},{"en":"If a language is resurrected, people must learn, teach, and use it regularly.","zh":"如果語言被復興，人們必須定期學習、教導和使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong form of revival.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈形式的復興。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be embraced by","meaning":"被……接受","examples":[{"en":"A revived language can be embraced by a large number of people.","zh":"復興語言可以被大量人接受。"},{"en":"To be embraced by people means to be accepted, welcomed, and used by them.","zh":"被人接受，指被他們接納、歡迎和使用。"},{"en":"A new school rule is embraced by students if they think it is fair and useful.","zh":"如果學生認為新校規公平又有用，它就會被學生接受。"},{"en":"If a revived language is embraced by families and schools, it can become strong again.","zh":"如果復興語言被家庭和學校接受，它就可以再次變強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes positive acceptance.","zh":"這個短語描述正面接納。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be well on its way to becoming","meaning":"快將成為；逐漸成為","examples":[{"en":"By the 20th century, Hebrew was well on its way to becoming a main language in Palestine.","zh":"到20世紀，希伯來語已逐漸成為巴勒斯坦的主要語言。"},{"en":"To be well on its way to becoming something means to be making strong progress toward that state.","zh":"快將成為某事，指正朝該狀態取得明顯進展。"},{"en":"A student who reads daily and writes weekly is well on their way to becoming fluent.","zh":"每天閱讀、每週寫作的學生，已逐漸走向流利。"},{"en":"If a language is used in schools and homes, it may be well on its way to common use.","zh":"如果一種語言在學校和家庭中使用，它可能快將成為常用語言。"},{"en":"The phrase describes clear progress toward a goal.","zh":"這個短語描述朝目標的清楚進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the Jewish population","meaning":"猶太人口","examples":[{"en":"Hebrew became important among the Jewish population of Ottoman and British Palestine.","zh":"希伯來語在奧斯曼和英屬巴勒斯坦的猶太人口中變得重要。"},{"en":"The Jewish population means the group of Jewish people living in a particular place.","zh":"猶太人口，指生活在特定地方的猶太人群體。"},{"en":"A city’s Jewish population may preserve traditions through schools, synagogues, festivals, and language.","zh":"一個城市的猶太人口可能透過學校、猶太會堂、節日和語言保存傳統。"},{"en":"If a language becomes important within a population, it can help strengthen shared identity.","zh":"如果語言在某人口群體中變得重要，它可以幫助加強共同身份。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a community by religion, culture, and history.","zh":"這個短語按宗教、文化和歷史辨認社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the fate of","meaning":"……的命運","examples":[{"en":"Turin believes that the fate of endangered languages is not sealed.","zh":"Turin 相信瀕危語言的命運未成定局。"},{"en":"The fate of something means what will happen to it in the future.","zh":"某事的命運，指它將來會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"The fate of an old cinema may depend on whether the community supports it.","zh":"舊戲院的命運可能取決於社區是否支持它。"},{"en":"If a language’s fate is not fixed, people can still influence its future.","zh":"如果一種語言的命運不是固定的，人們仍可影響它的未來。"},{"en":"The phrase points to future outcome.","zh":"這個短語指向未來結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not sealed","meaning":"未成定局","examples":[{"en":"The fate of the world’s endangered languages is not sealed.","zh":"世界瀕危語言的命運未成定局。"},{"en":"Not sealed means not finally decided or impossible to change.","zh":"未成定局，指尚未最終決定，仍可以改變。"},{"en":"A student’s future is not sealed by one bad exam result.","zh":"學生的未來不會由一次差考試成績定局。"},{"en":"If language loss is not sealed, communities can still take action.","zh":"如果語言流失未成定局，社群仍可採取行動。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses remaining possibility and hope.","zh":"這個短語表達仍有可能性和希望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not necessarily","meaning":"未必；不一定","examples":[{"en":"Globalisation is not necessarily only harmful to languages.","zh":"全球化未必只對語言有害。"},{"en":"Not necessarily means not always or not in every case.","zh":"未必，指不總是如此或不是每種情況都如此。"},{"en":"A difficult exam is not necessarily unfair if students were taught the skills properly.","zh":"如果學生已被適當教授技能，困難考試未必不公平。"},{"en":"If globalisation brings recording tools, it may help as well as harm languages.","zh":"如果全球化帶來記錄工具，它可能既幫助也傷害語言。"},{"en":"The phrase prevents an over-simple conclusion.","zh":"這個短語避免過分簡單的結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the nefarious perpetrator of evil","meaning":"邪惡禍首","examples":[{"en":"Globalisation is not simply the nefarious perpetrator of evil that people often describe.","zh":"全球化並不只是人們常描述的邪惡禍首。"},{"en":"The nefarious perpetrator of evil means a wicked cause blamed for harmful actions or results.","zh":"邪惡禍首，指被指責造成有害行為或結果的邪惡原因。"},{"en":"In a story, a villain may be presented as the nefarious perpetrator of every problem.","zh":"在故事中，反派可能被描繪成所有問題的邪惡禍首。"},{"en":"If globalisation also provides tools for preservation, it cannot be described only as evil.","zh":"如果全球化也提供保存工具，它就不能只被描述成邪惡。"},{"en":"The phrase is dramatic and strongly negative.","zh":"這個短語語氣戲劇化且非常負面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be presented to be","meaning":"被描繪成","examples":[{"en":"Globalisation is not always the harmful force it is presented to be.","zh":"全球化並不總是它被描繪成的那種有害力量。"},{"en":"To be presented to be something means to be shown or described as that thing.","zh":"被描繪成某物，指被展示或描述成那樣。"},{"en":"A student may be presented as lazy, even though the real problem is lack of sleep.","zh":"學生可能被描繪成懶惰，即使真正問題是睡眠不足。"},{"en":"If something is presented as entirely harmful, we should check whether the evidence is balanced.","zh":"如果某事被描繪成完全有害，我們應檢查證據是否平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how something is portrayed.","zh":"這個短語描述某事如何被呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the globalisation paradox","meaning":"全球化悖論","examples":[{"en":"Turin calls this situation the globalisation paradox.","zh":"Turin 稱這種情況為全球化悖論。"},{"en":"The globalisation paradox is the idea that globalisation can harm diversity while also providing tools to protect it.","zh":"全球化悖論，是全球化既可能傷害多樣性，又提供工具保護多樣性的想法。"},{"en":"The internet can create a globalisation paradox because it spreads dominant languages but also helps record small ones.","zh":"互聯網可以造成全球化悖論，因為它傳播主流語言，但也幫助記錄小語言。"},{"en":"If one force both damages and helps languages, the situation is paradoxical.","zh":"如果一種力量既損害又幫助語言，情況就是悖論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a contradiction within globalisation.","zh":"這個短語描述全球化內部的矛盾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on the one hand","meaning":"一方面","examples":[{"en":"On the one hand, globalisation can erode diversity.","zh":"一方面，全球化可以侵蝕多樣性。"},{"en":"On the one hand introduces one side of an argument or situation.","zh":"一方面，用來引入論點或情況的一面。"},{"en":"On the one hand, online learning is convenient; on the other, it can feel lonely.","zh":"一方面，網上學習很方便；另一方面，它可能令人感到孤單。"},{"en":"If a writer uses this phrase, a balancing point often comes later.","zh":"如果作者使用這個短語，後面常會出現平衡觀點。"},{"en":"The phrase helps present two-sided thinking.","zh":"這個短語幫助呈現雙面思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rapid socioeconomic change","meaning":"快速的社會經濟變化","examples":[{"en":"Rapid socioeconomic change can challenge linguistic diversity.","zh":"快速的社會經濟變化可以挑戰語言多樣性。"},{"en":"Rapid socioeconomic change means fast change in society, work, income, education, and living conditions.","zh":"快速的社會經濟變化，指社會、工作、收入、教育和生活條件快速改變。"},{"en":"A village may experience rapid socioeconomic change when factories, roads, and schools arrive quickly.","zh":"當工廠、道路和學校迅速出現，村莊可能經歷快速社會經濟變化。"},{"en":"If people move to cities for work, local languages may be used less at home.","zh":"如果人們為工作搬到城市，本地語言在家中可能較少被使用。"},{"en":"The phrase connects social and economic change with cultural pressure.","zh":"這個短語把社會和經濟變化與文化壓力連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"erode and challenge diversity","meaning":"侵蝕並挑戰多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Globalisation and rapid change can erode and challenge diversity.","zh":"全球化和快速變化可以侵蝕並挑戰多樣性。"},{"en":"To erode and challenge diversity means to slowly weaken variety and put it under pressure.","zh":"侵蝕並挑戰多樣性，指慢慢削弱多樣性並對其施加壓力。"},{"en":"Chain stores can erode and challenge diversity when they replace small local shops.","zh":"當連鎖店取代小型本地商店，它們可以侵蝕並挑戰多樣性。"},{"en":"If media use only dominant languages, smaller languages may gradually lose space.","zh":"如果媒體只使用主導語言，較小語言可能逐漸失去空間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pressure on variety.","zh":"這個短語描述多樣性所受的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"On the other hand, globalisation provides tools for documentation.","zh":"另一方面，全球化提供記錄工具。"},{"en":"On the other hand introduces the opposite or balancing side of an argument.","zh":"另一方面，引入論點中相反或平衡的一面。"},{"en":"A phone can distract students; on the other hand, it can also help them learn vocabulary.","zh":"手機可以令學生分心；另一方面，它也可以幫助他們學詞彙。"},{"en":"If globalisation threatens languages but provides recording technology, both sides must be considered.","zh":"如果全球化威脅語言但也提供錄音科技，就必須考慮兩面。"},{"en":"The phrase signals contrast or balance.","zh":"這個短語表示對比或平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"provide someone with tools","meaning":"為某人提供工具","examples":[{"en":"Globalisation provides researchers with tools to document endangered languages.","zh":"全球化為研究人員提供工具，以記錄瀕危語言。"},{"en":"To provide someone with tools means to give them equipment, methods, or resources to do a task.","zh":"為某人提供工具，指給他們設備、方法或資源去完成任務。"},{"en":"A teacher provides students with tools for writing when she gives sentence frames and examples.","zh":"老師給學生句式框架和例子時，就是為他們提供寫作工具。"},{"en":"If researchers receive cameras, recorders, and online storage, they can document languages more effectively.","zh":"如果研究人員得到攝影機、錄音機和網上儲存，就能更有效記錄語言。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving practical support.","zh":"這個短語描述提供實際支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tools and facilities","meaning":"工具和設施","examples":[{"en":"New tools and facilities make language documentation easier.","zh":"新工具和設施令語言記錄更容易。"},{"en":"Tools and facilities are equipment, spaces, systems, or services that help people do work.","zh":"工具和設施，是幫助人們工作的設備、空間、系統或服務。"},{"en":"A school language lab provides tools and facilities for listening practice.","zh":"學校語言實驗室提供聆聽練習的工具和設施。"},{"en":"If communities have good tools and facilities, they can record their own language more easily.","zh":"如果社群有良好工具和設施，就能更容易記錄自己的語言。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical resources.","zh":"這個短語指實用資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"get to places","meaning":"前往不同地方","examples":[{"en":"Researchers can now get to places where endangered languages are spoken.","zh":"研究人員現在可以前往瀕危語言被使用的地方。"},{"en":"To get to places means to travel to or reach those locations.","zh":"前往不同地方，指旅行到或到達那些地點。"},{"en":"Better roads help students get to schools that were once hard to reach.","zh":"更好的道路幫助學生前往以前難以到達的學校。"},{"en":"If researchers can get to remote villages, they can record languages directly from speakers.","zh":"如果研究人員能到達偏遠村莊，就能直接從說話者記錄語言。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical access.","zh":"這個短語描述實體上的可達性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"document those things","meaning":"記錄那些事物","examples":[{"en":"Researchers can document those things that globalisation is eroding.","zh":"研究人員可以記錄那些正在被全球化侵蝕的事物。"},{"en":"To document those things means to record them carefully before they are lost or changed.","zh":"記錄那些事物，指在它們失去或改變前仔細把它們記下。"},{"en":"A museum may document old shop signs before a neighbourhood is redeveloped.","zh":"博物館可能在社區重建前記錄舊店舖招牌。"},{"en":"If globalisation changes traditions quickly, recording them becomes urgent.","zh":"如果全球化迅速改變傳統，記錄它們就變得迫切。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preserving evidence through records.","zh":"這個短語描述透過記錄保存證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at the coal-face of change","meaning":"身處變革前線","examples":[{"en":"Communities at the coal-face of change may value what globalisation offers.","zh":"身處變革前線的社群可能重視全球化所提供的東西。"},{"en":"At the coal-face of change means directly experiencing the difficult front line of change.","zh":"身處變革前線，指直接經歷變化中困難的最前線。"},{"en":"Teachers are at the coal-face of education reform because they deal with students every day.","zh":"老師身處教育改革前線，因為他們每天面對學生。"},{"en":"If communities face change directly, they may understand both its dangers and benefits.","zh":"如果社群直接面對變化，就可能理解它的危險和好處。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being closest to practical impact.","zh":"這個短語描述最接近實際影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have to offer","meaning":"可提供的東西","examples":[{"en":"Some communities are excited by what globalisation has to offer.","zh":"一些社群對全球化可提供的東西感到興奮。"},{"en":"What something has to offer means the benefits, opportunities, or resources it can provide.","zh":"某事可提供的東西，指它能帶來的好處、機會或資源。"},{"en":"A university open day shows students what the school has to offer.","zh":"大學開放日向學生展示學校可提供的東西。"},{"en":"If globalisation offers recording tools and wider audiences, communities may use them for preservation.","zh":"如果全球化提供記錄工具和更廣泛受眾，社群可能用它們來保存文化。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on possible benefits.","zh":"這個短語強調可能好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in the meantime","meaning":"在此期間","examples":[{"en":"In the meantime, the race is on to collect and protect endangered languages.","zh":"在此期間，收集並保護瀕危語言的競賽已經展開。"},{"en":"In the meantime means during the period while something else is happening or before a final result is known.","zh":"在此期間，指在另一件事發生期間，或最終結果知道之前。"},{"en":"The new library will open next year; in the meantime, students can use the temporary study room.","zh":"新圖書館明年開幕；在此期間，學生可以使用臨時自修室。"},{"en":"While scholars debate long-term solutions, recordings can begin immediately.","zh":"當學者討論長遠方案時，錄音可以立即開始。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces action during an interim period.","zh":"這個短語引入過渡期間的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the race is on to","meaning":"競賽已經展開去","examples":[{"en":"The race is on to collect and protect as many languages as possible.","zh":"收集並保護盡可能多語言的競賽已經展開。"},{"en":"The race is on to do something means urgent effort has begun because time is limited.","zh":"競賽已經展開去做某事，指因時間有限而開始緊急努力。"},{"en":"When a typhoon is coming, the race is on to secure windows and move supplies indoors.","zh":"當颱風快到時，固定窗戶和把物資搬入室內的競賽已經展開。"},{"en":"If speakers are ageing, the race is on to record their language before it disappears.","zh":"如果說話者正在老去，記錄語言防止消失的競賽就已展開。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a sense of urgency.","zh":"這個短語營造緊迫感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"collect and protect","meaning":"收集並保護","examples":[{"en":"The project aims to collect and protect endangered oral traditions.","zh":"該計劃旨在收集並保護瀕危口述傳統。"},{"en":"To collect and protect something means to gather it and keep it safe from loss or damage.","zh":"收集並保護某物，指把它收集起來，並使它免於流失或受損。"},{"en":"A museum may collect and protect old photographs from a neighbourhood.","zh":"博物館可能收集並保護一個社區的舊照片。"},{"en":"If oral stories are collected and protected, they can survive beyond the lives of individual storytellers.","zh":"如果口述故事被收集並保護，它們就能在個別講故事者離世後仍然存續。"},{"en":"The phrase combines gathering with preservation.","zh":"這個短語結合收集與保存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as many languages as possible","meaning":"盡可能多的語言","examples":[{"en":"Researchers want to protect as many languages as possible.","zh":"研究人員想保護盡可能多的語言。"},{"en":"As many languages as possible means the greatest number of languages that can realistically be protected.","zh":"盡可能多的語言，指在現實上能保護的最大數量語言。"},{"en":"A teacher may help as many students as possible before the exam.","zh":"老師可能在考試前幫助盡可能多的學生。"},{"en":"If time is short, researchers may record as many languages as possible before speakers disappear.","zh":"如果時間緊迫，研究人員可能在說話者消失前記錄盡可能多的語言。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses a maximum effort within limits.","zh":"這個短語表達在限制內作最大努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"generations that follow","meaning":"後代","examples":[{"en":"Future generations should be able to continue their traditions.","zh":"後代應該能夠延續自己的傳統。"},{"en":"Generations that follow are the people who will live after the current generation.","zh":"後代，是在當前一代之後生活的人。"},{"en":"Parents save family photos so generations that follow can understand their roots.","zh":"父母保存家庭照片，使後代能理解自己的根。"},{"en":"If languages are recorded now, future generations may learn what their ancestors spoke.","zh":"如果語言現在被記錄，後代可能學到祖先說過甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people in the future.","zh":"這個短語指未來的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"continue their traditions","meaning":"延續傳統","examples":[{"en":"Communities can continue their traditions through their own languages.","zh":"社群可以透過自己的語言延續傳統。"},{"en":"To continue their traditions means to keep practising customs, stories, rituals, and values over time.","zh":"延續傳統，指隨時間繼續實踐習俗、故事、儀式和價值。"},{"en":"A family continues its traditions when children learn festival recipes from grandparents.","zh":"當孩子從祖父母學習節日食譜，家庭就在延續傳統。"},{"en":"If a language survives, songs and ceremonies connected to it may continue too.","zh":"如果語言存續，與它相關的歌曲和儀式也可能繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cultural continuity.","zh":"這個短語描述文化延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have a sense of identity","meaning":"擁有身份認同","examples":[{"en":"Language helps communities have a sense of identity.","zh":"語言幫助社群擁有身份認同。"},{"en":"To have a sense of identity means to feel who you are and where you belong.","zh":"擁有身份認同，指感覺到自己是誰，以及自己屬於哪裡。"},{"en":"Students may have a stronger sense of identity when they learn their family history.","zh":"當學生學習自己的家族歷史時，可能有更強的身份認同。"},{"en":"If a community speaks its own language, members may feel connected to one another.","zh":"如果社群說自己的語言，成員可能感到彼此相連。"},{"en":"The phrase describes belonging and self-understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述歸屬感和自我理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"project’s limits","meaning":"項目的局限","examples":[{"en":"Turin understands his project’s limits.","zh":"Turin 明白自己項目的局限。"},{"en":"A project’s limits are the things it cannot realistically do or achieve.","zh":"項目的局限，是它在現實上不能做到或達成的事情。"},{"en":"A school recycling project’s limits may include budget, space, and student participation.","zh":"學校回收項目的局限可能包括預算、空間和學生參與。"},{"en":"If a language project can record materials but cannot force people to speak, its limits must be clear.","zh":"如果語言項目能記錄材料但不能強迫人們說該語言，其局限必須清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes realistic boundaries.","zh":"這個短語描述現實邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"it is inevitable that","meaning":"不可避免的是","examples":[{"en":"Turin believes it is inevitable that many languages will disappear.","zh":"Turin 相信不可避免的是，許多語言將會消失。"},{"en":"It is inevitable that means something cannot be avoided or is almost certain to happen.","zh":"不可避免的是，指某事無法避免或幾乎肯定會發生。"},{"en":"If no one repairs the roof, it is inevitable that rainwater will enter the room.","zh":"如果沒有人修理屋頂，雨水進入房間就是不可避免的。"},{"en":"If a language has no young speakers, disappearance may become unavoidable.","zh":"如果一種語言沒有年輕說話者，消失可能變得無法避免。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an unavoidable result.","zh":"這個短語引入無法避免的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a large number of","meaning":"大量","examples":[{"en":"A large number of endangered languages may disappear.","zh":"大量瀕危語言可能會消失。"},{"en":"A large number of means many.","zh":"大量，指很多。"},{"en":"A large number of students joined the school clean-up day.","zh":"大量學生參加了學校清潔日。"},{"en":"If a large number of languages disappear, humanity loses many cultural memories.","zh":"如果大量語言消失，人類就失去許多文化記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises quantity.","zh":"這個短語強調數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be in no position to","meaning":"無力去；沒有條件去","examples":[{"en":"The project is in no position to keep languages alive by itself.","zh":"該計劃無力單靠自己讓語言存續。"},{"en":"To be in no position to do something means not to have the power, resources, or ability to do it.","zh":"無力做某事，指沒有權力、資源或能力去做。"},{"en":"A student with no notes is in no position to teach the whole chapter to others.","zh":"沒有筆記的學生沒有條件把整章教給別人。"},{"en":"If a project lacks community control, it cannot keep a language alive alone.","zh":"如果一個項目缺乏社群控制，它就不能單獨讓語言存續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being unable to act effectively.","zh":"這個短語描述無法有效行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be designed to","meaning":"為……而設計","examples":[{"en":"The project was not designed to keep languages alive by itself.","zh":"該計劃不是為了單靠自己讓語言存續而設計。"},{"en":"To be designed to do something means to be made or planned for that purpose.","zh":"為做某事而設計，指為該目的而製作或規劃。"},{"en":"A dictionary app is designed to help students check meanings quickly.","zh":"字典應用程式是為幫助學生快速查意思而設計。"},{"en":"If a project is designed to record languages, it may not be designed to teach them daily.","zh":"如果項目是為記錄語言而設計，它未必是為每天教語言而設計。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies purpose and function.","zh":"這個短語指出目的和功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"keep languages alive","meaning":"讓語言存續；讓語言保持活力","examples":[{"en":"A project alone cannot keep languages alive.","zh":"單靠一個計劃不能讓語言存續。"},{"en":"To keep languages alive means to make sure people continue speaking, teaching, and using them.","zh":"讓語言存續，指確保人們繼續說、教和使用它們。"},{"en":"Families can keep languages alive by speaking them with children at home.","zh":"家庭可以透過在家與孩子說自己的語言來讓語言存續。"},{"en":"If a language is only stored in an archive, it is preserved but not fully alive.","zh":"如果一種語言只儲存在檔案庫中，它是被保存了，但並不完全活着。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active continued use.","zh":"這個短語描述持續活躍使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"help languages survive","meaning":"幫助語言存續","examples":[{"en":"Only the communities themselves can help languages survive.","zh":"只有社群本身才能幫助語言存續。"},{"en":"To help languages survive means to support them so they continue being spoken and understood.","zh":"幫助語言存續，指支援它們，使它們繼續被說和被理解。"},{"en":"Schools can help languages survive by offering classes and reading materials.","zh":"學校可以透過提供課堂和閱讀材料來幫助語言存續。"},{"en":"If children use the language at home and in festivals, survival becomes more likely.","zh":"如果孩子在家中和節日中使用該語言，語言存續就更有可能。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on practical support for continued language use.","zh":"這個短語強調對持續語言使用的實際支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be reminded that","meaning":"被提醒","examples":[{"en":"Communities need to be reminded that it is good to speak their own language.","zh":"社群需要被提醒，說自己的語言是好的。"},{"en":"To be reminded that means to be told again so that one does not forget an important idea.","zh":"被提醒，指再次被告知，以免忘記重要想法。"},{"en":"Students are reminded that sleep is part of good exam preparation.","zh":"學生被提醒，睡眠是良好考試準備的一部分。"},{"en":"If people feel ashamed of their language, reminders can rebuild pride and confidence.","zh":"如果人們為自己的語言感到羞恥，提醒可以重建自豪感和信心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bringing an important truth back to attention.","zh":"這個短語描述把重要真相重新帶回注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"speak their own language","meaning":"說自己的語言","examples":[{"en":"People should be encouraged to speak their own language.","zh":"人們應被鼓勵說自己的語言。"},{"en":"To speak their own language means to use the language of their family, community, or cultural group.","zh":"說自己的語言，指使用自己家庭、社群或文化群體的語言。"},{"en":"Children may speak their own language with grandparents even if school uses another language.","zh":"即使學校使用另一種語言，孩子也可能與祖父母說自己的語言。"},{"en":"If people stop speaking their own language, daily use may disappear first.","zh":"如果人們停止說自己的語言，日常使用可能最先消失。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses linguistic identity and belonging.","zh":"這個短語強調語言身份和歸屬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"becoming modern","meaning":"走向現代化","examples":[{"en":"Becoming modern does not mean losing your language.","zh":"走向現代化並不等於失去你的語言。"},{"en":"Becoming modern means adopting new ways of living, working, learning, or communicating.","zh":"走向現代化，指採納新的生活、工作、學習或溝通方式。"},{"en":"A village can become modern by using internet access while still keeping local festivals.","zh":"村莊可以透過使用互聯網走向現代化，同時仍保留本地節日。"},{"en":"If modern life is seen as requiring language loss, communities may feel forced to choose.","zh":"如果現代生活被視為要求失去語言，社群可能感到被迫選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase describes social change toward contemporary life.","zh":"這個短語描述走向當代生活的社會變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lose your language","meaning":"失去自己的語言","examples":[{"en":"Becoming modern does not mean you have to lose your language.","zh":"走向現代化並不代表你必須失去自己的語言。"},{"en":"To lose your language means to stop speaking, understanding, or passing on your community’s language.","zh":"失去自己的語言，指停止說、理解或傳承自己社群的語言。"},{"en":"A child may lose their language if no one uses it with them at home.","zh":"如果家中沒有人與孩子使用某語言，孩子可能失去自己的語言。"},{"en":"If people lose their language, they may also lose songs, jokes, and family stories linked to it.","zh":"如果人們失去自己的語言，也可能失去與它相關的歌曲、笑話和家庭故事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cultural and linguistic loss.","zh":"這個短語描述文化和語言流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates must complete the summary using the list of words.","zh":"考生必須使用詞語列表完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill in missing words in a shortened version of the passage.","zh":"完成摘要，指在文章的縮短版本中填入缺少的字詞。"},{"en":"Students complete a summary by reading the sentences before and after each gap.","zh":"學生透過閱讀每個空格前後的句子來完成摘要。"},{"en":"If the summary follows the passage order, students can locate answers more easily.","zh":"如果摘要跟隨文章次序，學生就能更容易定位答案。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"using the list of words","meaning":"使用詞語列表","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using the list of words provided.","zh":"學生使用所提供的詞語列表完成摘要。"},{"en":"Using the list of words means choosing answers only from the words given in the box or list.","zh":"使用詞語列表，指只從方框或列表中給出的詞語選擇答案。"},{"en":"In a vocabulary exercise, students may complete sentences using the list of words at the top.","zh":"在詞彙練習中，學生可能使用上方詞語列表完成句子。"},{"en":"If students use a word outside the list, the answer may be marked wrong.","zh":"如果學生使用列表以外的詞，答案可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a limit on possible answers.","zh":"這個短語限制可能答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"write the correct letter","meaning":"填寫正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the correct letter on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生在答題紙上填寫正確字母。"},{"en":"To write the correct letter means to record the option letter that matches the answer.","zh":"填寫正確字母，指記下與答案相符的選項字母。"},{"en":"If option B is correct, students should write B, not the full sentence.","zh":"如果選項 B 正確，學生應寫 B，而不是整句。"},{"en":"If the correct letter is copied into the wrong box, the answer may not be counted.","zh":"如果正確字母抄到錯誤方格，答案可能不被計算。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an exam-answer instruction.","zh":"這個短語給出考試作答指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"answer sheet","meaning":"答題紙","examples":[{"en":"Answers should be written on the answer sheet.","zh":"答案應寫在答題紙上。"},{"en":"An answer sheet is the official paper or digital form where exam answers are recorded.","zh":"答題紙，是記錄考試答案的正式紙張或數碼表格。"},{"en":"A student may make notes in the question booklet but must write final answers on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生可以在試題簿上做筆記，但必須把最終答案寫在答題紙上。"},{"en":"If answers are not on the answer sheet, markers may not see them.","zh":"如果答案不在答題紙上，評卷員可能看不到。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the formal place for answers.","zh":"這個短語指正式作答位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"become extinct","meaning":"滅絕","examples":[{"en":"About half of the world’s living languages are expected to become extinct.","zh":"世界上大約一半現存語言預計會滅絕。"},{"en":"To become extinct means to disappear completely and no longer exist in active use.","zh":"滅絕，指完全消失，不再活躍存在。"},{"en":"A local craft may become extinct if no young people learn how to make it.","zh":"如果沒有年輕人學習如何製作，本地手藝可能滅絕。"},{"en":"If a language becomes extinct, no community uses it naturally in daily life.","zh":"如果語言滅絕，就沒有社群在日常生活中自然使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes complete disappearance.","zh":"這個短語描述完全消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"set up a project","meaning":"成立一項計劃","examples":[{"en":"Professor Turin set up a project to record endangered languages.","zh":"Turin 教授成立了一項記錄瀕危語言的計劃。"},{"en":"To set up a project means to organise and start it.","zh":"成立一項計劃，指組織並開始它。"},{"en":"Students may set up a project to collect old photos from their neighbourhood.","zh":"學生可能成立一項計劃，收集自己社區的舊照片。"},{"en":"If a project is set up properly, it needs goals, people, tools, and funding.","zh":"如果項目被妥善成立，就需要目標、人手、工具和資金。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating an organised activity.","zh":"這個短語描述創立有組織活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"prevent the disappearance of","meaning":"防止……消失","examples":[{"en":"The project aims to prevent the disappearance of endangered languages.","zh":"該計劃旨在防止瀕危語言消失。"},{"en":"To prevent the disappearance of something means to stop it from being lost completely.","zh":"防止某物消失，指阻止它完全流失。"},{"en":"A museum can prevent the disappearance of old photographs by scanning them.","zh":"博物館可以透過掃描舊照片來防止它們消失。"},{"en":"If a language is taught to children, its disappearance may be slowed or prevented.","zh":"如果語言被教給孩子，其消失可能被減慢或防止。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stopping loss before it is final.","zh":"這個短語描述在流失成為定局前阻止它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"enable people to","meaning":"使人能夠","examples":[{"en":"The project provides support to enable people to record their languages.","zh":"該計劃提供支援，使人能夠記錄自己的語言。"},{"en":"To enable people to do something means to make it possible for them to do it.","zh":"使人能夠做某事，指令他們有可能做到該事。"},{"en":"Scholarships enable students to continue studying when their families cannot afford fees.","zh":"獎學金使家庭無法負擔學費的學生能夠繼續學習。"},{"en":"If communities receive recorders and training, they can document their own speech.","zh":"如果社群得到錄音機和培訓，就能記錄自己的說話。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving people the ability or means to act.","zh":"這個短語描述給人能力或方法去行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"record endangered languages","meaning":"記錄瀕危語言","examples":[{"en":"Communities can use multimedia tools to record endangered languages.","zh":"社群可以使用多媒體工具記錄瀕危語言。"},{"en":"To record endangered languages means to make audio, video, or written records of languages at risk.","zh":"記錄瀕危語言，指為有風險的語言製作錄音、影片或文字記錄。"},{"en":"A community may record endangered languages by filming elders telling stories.","zh":"社群可能透過拍攝長者講故事來記錄瀕危語言。"},{"en":"If endangered languages are recorded, future learners can hear their sounds and structures.","zh":"如果瀕危語言被記錄，未來學習者就能聽到其聲音和結構。"},{"en":"The phrase describes documentation before possible loss.","zh":"這個短語描述在可能流失前進行記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"cultural significance","meaning":"文化意義","examples":[{"en":"The oral tradition has great cultural significance.","zh":"口述傳統有很大文化意義。"},{"en":"Cultural significance is the importance something has for a community’s identity, memory, values, or way of life.","zh":"文化意義，是某事對社群身份、記憶、價值或生活方式的重要性。"},{"en":"A temple, song, or family recipe may have cultural significance beyond its practical use.","zh":"寺廟、歌曲或家庭食譜可能有超越實際用途的文化意義。"},{"en":"If oral stories explain who a community is, they have strong cultural significance.","zh":"如果口述故事解釋社群是誰，它們就有強烈文化意義。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cultural importance.","zh":"這個短語描述文化上的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"an important difference exists between","meaning":"……之間存在重要差異","examples":[{"en":"An important difference exists between oral traditions and written traditions.","zh":"口述傳統與書寫傳統之間存在重要差異。"},{"en":"An important difference exists between two things means they are not the same in a meaningful way.","zh":"兩者之間存在重要差異，指它們在有意義的方面並不相同。"},{"en":"An important difference exists between memorising a word and being able to use it naturally.","zh":"背熟一個詞和能自然使用它之間存在重要差異。"},{"en":"If oral tradition depends on memory and performance, it needs different protection from written texts.","zh":"如果口述傳統依賴記憶和表演，它就需要不同於書面文本的保護方式。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a key contrast.","zh":"這個短語引入關鍵對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"languages spoken by few people","meaning":"由少數人使用的語言","examples":[{"en":"Languages spoken by few people are often at greater risk.","zh":"由少數人使用的語言通常面臨更大風險。"},{"en":"Languages spoken by few people are languages with only a small number of speakers.","zh":"由少數人使用的語言，是只有少量說話者的語言。"},{"en":"A language used by one village and not taught in schools may be spoken by few people.","zh":"只由一條村使用且不在學校教授的語言，可能是由少數人使用的語言。"},{"en":"If few people speak a language, it may disappear when those speakers age.","zh":"如果很少人說一種語言，當那些說話者年老時，它可能消失。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights risk caused by a small speaker population.","zh":"這個短語突出由少量說話者造成的風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements agree with the information given.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與所給資料相符。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage actually says.","zh":"與所給資料相符，指與文章實際所說內容一致。"},{"en":"In a reading test, an answer agrees with the text only if there is clear evidence.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，答案只有在有清楚證據時才與文本相符。"},{"en":"If a statement adds outside knowledge, it may not agree with the information given.","zh":"如果陳述加入外部知識，它未必與所給資料相符。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in TRUE, FALSE, and NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語用於 TRUE、FALSE 和 NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章中的資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"與資料相矛盾，指說出與文本內容相反的東西。"},{"en":"If the passage says the project began in Nepal, saying it began in France would contradict the information.","zh":"如果文章說計劃在尼泊爾開始，說它在法國開始就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"In reading tests, contradiction is different from missing information.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，矛盾不同於資料缺失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a direct conflict with the text.","zh":"這個短語描述與文本直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students write “NOT GIVEN” when there is no information on this in the passage.","zh":"當文章中沒有相關資料時，學生寫 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not say enough about the point.","zh":"沒有相關資料，指文章對該點沒有說足夠內容。"},{"en":"If a text never mentions cost, there is no information on whether the project was expensive.","zh":"如果文本從未提到成本，就沒有資料判斷項目是否昂貴。"},{"en":"When there is no information, students should not answer from personal knowledge.","zh":"當沒有相關資料時，學生不應根據個人知識作答。"},{"en":"The phrase signals insufficient evidence in the passage.","zh":"這個短語表示文章證據不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"think carefully before","meaning":"在……之前仔細考慮","examples":[{"en":"The statement says researchers think carefully before selecting an area to research.","zh":"該陳述說研究人員在選擇研究範圍之前會仔細考慮。"},{"en":"To think carefully before doing something means to consider the decision seriously first.","zh":"在做某事之前仔細考慮，指先認真思考該決定。"},{"en":"Students should think carefully before choosing essay examples.","zh":"學生在選擇作文例子之前應仔細考慮。"},{"en":"If researchers do not think carefully before fieldwork, they may choose sites by chance.","zh":"如果研究人員在田野調查前沒有仔細考慮，就可能偶然選擇地點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes thoughtful preparation before action.","zh":"這個短語描述行動前的周詳準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"select an area to research","meaning":"選擇研究範圍","examples":[{"en":"Anthropologists may select an area to research for fieldwork.","zh":"人類學家可能為田野調查選擇研究範圍。"},{"en":"To select an area to research means to choose a place or topic for investigation.","zh":"選擇研究範圍，指選擇一個地方或題目進行調查。"},{"en":"A student may select a neighbourhood to research for a geography project.","zh":"學生可能為地理項目選擇一個社區作研究範圍。"},{"en":"If a research area is selected randomly, the project may depend on chance.","zh":"如果研究範圍是隨機選擇的，項目可能取決於偶然。"},{"en":"The phrase describes choosing a research focus.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇研究焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"have few similarities with","meaning":"與……相似之處很少","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Thangmi has few similarities with other languages.","zh":"題目問 Thangmi 是否與其他語言相似之處很少。"},{"en":"To have few similarities with something means to share only a small number of features with it.","zh":"與某物相似之處很少，指只共享少量特徵。"},{"en":"Two students may have few similarities in study habits if one learns by reading and the other by speaking.","zh":"如果一名學生靠閱讀學習，另一名靠說話學習，他們在學習習慣上可能相似之處很少。"},{"en":"If a language has few similarities with nearby languages, it may be difficult for outsiders to learn.","zh":"如果一種語言與附近語言相似之處很少，外人可能難以學習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limited resemblance.","zh":"這個短語描述相似程度有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be inappropriate for","meaning":"不適合……","examples":[{"en":"Turin realised that his long grammar was inappropriate for the Thangmi community.","zh":"Turin 意識到他的長篇語法書不適合 Thangmi 社群。"},{"en":"To be inappropriate for someone means to be unsuitable for their needs, situation, or level.","zh":"不適合某人，指不符合其需要、情況或程度。"},{"en":"A university textbook may be inappropriate for young children.","zh":"大學教科書可能不適合年幼兒童。"},{"en":"If a grammar book is too technical, it may be inappropriate for community education.","zh":"如果語法書太技術化，可能不適合社群教育。"},{"en":"The phrase describes poor fit.","zh":"這個短語描述配合度差。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lack resources to devote to","meaning":"缺乏可投入……的資源","examples":[{"en":"Some schools may lack resources to devote to language teaching.","zh":"一些學校可能缺乏可投入語言教學的資源。"},{"en":"To lack resources to devote to something means not to have enough money, time, staff, or materials for it.","zh":"缺乏可投入某事的資源，指沒有足夠金錢、時間、人手或材料支援它。"},{"en":"A small clinic may lack resources to devote to mental health services.","zh":"小型診所可能缺乏可投入心理健康服務的資源。"},{"en":"If schools lack resources for minority languages, classes may not be offered.","zh":"如果學校缺乏少數語言資源，就可能不開辦相關課程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shortage of support for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述為某目的提供支援的資源不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"language teaching","meaning":"語言教學","examples":[{"en":"The statement mentions resources for language teaching.","zh":"該陳述提到語言教學資源。"},{"en":"Language teaching is the process of helping people learn to understand, speak, read, or write a language.","zh":"語言教學，是幫助人們學會理解、說、讀或寫一種語言的過程。"},{"en":"Good language teaching uses examples, practice, correction, and meaningful communication.","zh":"良好語言教學使用例子、練習、改正和有意義溝通。"},{"en":"If language teaching is weak, young people may not learn their community language well.","zh":"如果語言教學薄弱，年輕人可能無法好好學會社群語言。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised language education.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的語言教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for each multiple-choice question.","zh":"考生為每條選擇題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the option letter that best answers the question.","zh":"選出正確字母，指選擇最能回答問題的選項字母。"},{"en":"In an exam, students may choose A, B, C, or D as the correct letter.","zh":"在考試中，學生可能選 A、B、C 或 D 作為正確字母。"},{"en":"If students match the evidence carefully, they can choose the correct letter more accurately.","zh":"如果學生仔細配對證據，就能更準確選出正確字母。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard multiple-choice instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準選擇題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a limited role in","meaning":"在……中的有限作用","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that researchers have a limited role in language research.","zh":"該選項暗示研究人員在語言研究中只有有限作用。"},{"en":"A limited role in something means a small or restricted part in that activity.","zh":"在某事中的有限作用，指在該活動中有較小或受限制的部分。"},{"en":"A student may have a limited role in a group project if they only design the cover.","zh":"如果學生只設計封面，他在小組項目中可能只有有限作用。"},{"en":"If researchers only record languages but communities decide whether to speak them, researchers have a limited role.","zh":"如果研究人員只記錄語言，而社群決定是否使用它們，研究人員的作用就有限。"},{"en":"The phrase describes restricted influence.","zh":"這個短語描述受限制的影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"research into languages","meaning":"語言研究","examples":[{"en":"The question concerns research into languages.","zh":"題目涉及語言研究。"},{"en":"Research into languages is the study of how languages work, change, survive, or disappear.","zh":"語言研究，是研究語言如何運作、改變、存續或消失。"},{"en":"A university may support research into languages spoken by migrant communities.","zh":"大學可能支援對移民社群語言的研究。"},{"en":"If research into languages includes endangered speech, it can help protect cultural knowledge.","zh":"如果語言研究包括瀕危口語，它就能幫助保護文化知識。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to academic investigation of language.","zh":"這個短語指對語言的學術調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"result in","meaning":"導致；產生","examples":[{"en":"Research can result in a more diverse cultural outlook.","zh":"研究可以產生更 多元的文化視野。"},{"en":"To result in something means to cause that thing to happen.","zh":"導致某事，指造成該事發生。"},{"en":"Regular reading can result in better vocabulary and clearer writing.","zh":"定期閱讀可以帶來更好的詞彙和更清楚的寫作。"},{"en":"If language research reveals many world views, it can lead to broader cultural understanding.","zh":"如果語言研究揭示許多世界觀，就可以導致更廣闊的文化理解。"},{"en":"The phrase connects cause and effect.","zh":"這個短語連接原因和結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a diverse cultural outlook","meaning":"多元的文化視野","examples":[{"en":"Language research may support a diverse cultural outlook.","zh":"語言研究可能支持多元的文化視野。"},{"en":"A diverse cultural outlook is a way of seeing the world that values different cultures and perspectives.","zh":"多元的文化視野，是重視不同文化和觀點的看世界方式。"},{"en":"Travel can give students a more diverse cultural outlook by showing different family and school systems.","zh":"旅遊可以透過展示不同家庭和學校制度，給學生更 多元的文化視野。"},{"en":"If people learn about many languages, they may become less narrow in how they judge others.","zh":"如果人們了解許多語言，他們判斷別人時可能較不狹隘。"},{"en":"The phrase describes openness to cultural variety.","zh":"這個短語描述對文化多樣性的開放態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"focus on more general aspects","meaning":"聚焦於更一般性的方面","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that French research should focus on more general aspects.","zh":"該選項暗示法語研究應聚焦於更一般性的方面。"},{"en":"To focus on more general aspects means to study broader issues rather than tiny details.","zh":"聚焦於更一般性的方面，指研究較廣泛議題，而不是細微細節。"},{"en":"A teacher may focus on more general aspects of writing before correcting every small punctuation mark.","zh":"老師可能先聚焦於寫作中較一般性的方面，再糾正每個小標點。"},{"en":"If language research focuses only on narrow topics, bigger questions may remain unanswered.","zh":"如果語言研究只聚焦狹窄題目，更大的問題可能仍未回答。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts broad focus with narrow detail.","zh":"這個短語把廣泛焦點與狹窄細節作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"lead people to believe","meaning":"令某人相信","examples":[{"en":"The paragraph discusses factors that lead people to believe endangered languages can survive.","zh":"該段討論令某人相信瀕危語言能夠存續的因素。"},{"en":"To lead people to believe something means to make them think it is true or possible.","zh":"令某人相信某事，指使他們認為它是真的或可能的。"},{"en":"A student’s steady improvement may lead teachers to believe the new method works.","zh":"學生穩定進步可能令老師相信新方法有效。"},{"en":"If a language has been revived before, it may lead people to believe revival can happen again.","zh":"如果一種語言曾被復興，它可能令人相信復興可以再次發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence shaping belief.","zh":"這個短語描述證據如何塑造信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"endangered languages can survive","meaning":"瀕危語言能夠存續","examples":[{"en":"Historical examples suggest that endangered languages can survive.","zh":"歷史例子顯示瀕危語言能夠存續。"},{"en":"Endangered languages can survive means languages at risk can continue if people protect and use them.","zh":"瀕危語言能夠存續，指有風險的語言如果被保護和使用，就可以延續。"},{"en":"A village language can survive if children hear it at home, school, and festivals.","zh":"如果孩子在家中、學校和節日聽到村莊語言，它就能夠存續。"},{"en":"If communities create lessons, songs, and recordings, survival becomes more possible.","zh":"如果社群創造課程、歌曲和錄音，存續就變得更有可能。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses hope for language continuation.","zh":"這個短語表達語言延續的希望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"language revival","meaning":"語言復興","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions a community where people distrust language revival.","zh":"題目提到一個人們不信任語言復興的社群。"},{"en":"Language revival is the effort to bring a declining or unused language back into active use.","zh":"語言復興，是把衰退或不再使用的語言帶回活躍使用的努力。"},{"en":"Language revival may include classes, dictionaries, songs, children’s books, and public events.","zh":"語言復興可能包括課堂、字典、歌曲、兒童書和公共活動。"},{"en":"If people distrust revival, they may doubt whether the language can be useful again.","zh":"如果人們不信任復興，他們可能懷疑該語言是否能再次有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised language recovery.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的語言恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"methods of research","meaning":"研究方法","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to methods of research that have improved language restoration.","zh":"該選項提到改善語言復興的研究方法。"},{"en":"Methods of research are the ways researchers collect, analyse, and interpret information.","zh":"研究方法，是研究人員收集、分析和解讀資料的方式。"},{"en":"Interviews, recordings, surveys, and field notes are methods of research.","zh":"訪問、錄音、問卷和田野筆記都是研究方法。"},{"en":"If methods improve, language documentation may become more accurate and useful.","zh":"如果方法改善，語言記錄可能變得更準確和有用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to research techniques.","zh":"這個短語指研究技巧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"improve language restoration","meaning":"改善語言復興","examples":[{"en":"Some methods of research may improve language restoration.","zh":"一些研究方法可能改善語言復興。"},{"en":"To improve language restoration means to make efforts to revive a language more effective.","zh":"改善語言復興，指令復興語言的努力更有效。"},{"en":"Better recordings can improve language restoration by preserving pronunciation clearly.","zh":"更好的錄音可以透過清楚保存發音來改善語言復興。"},{"en":"If teaching materials are simple and local, they can help communities revive language use.","zh":"如果教材簡單而本地化，就能幫助社群恢復語言使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making revival work better.","zh":"這個短語描述令復興工作更有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"undertake initiatives","meaning":"推行倡議","examples":[{"en":"The option asks about initiatives the World Oral Literature Project is undertaking.","zh":"該選項問世界口述文學計劃正在推行哪些倡議。"},{"en":"To undertake initiatives means to begin or carry out organised actions or projects.","zh":"推行倡議，指開始或執行有組織的行動或項目。"},{"en":"A school may undertake initiatives to reduce plastic waste and save electricity.","zh":"學校可能推行減少塑膠廢物和節省電力的倡議。"},{"en":"If WOLP undertakes recording projects, it actively works to preserve oral traditions.","zh":"如果 WOLP 推行記錄項目，它就是積極保存口述傳統。"},{"en":"The phrase describes taking organised action.","zh":"這個短語描述採取有組織行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the prospects for","meaning":"……的前景","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the prospects for WOLP.","zh":"題目問 WOLP 的前景。"},{"en":"The prospects for something are its chances of future success or development.","zh":"某事的前景，是它未來成功或發展的機會。"},{"en":"The prospects for a small business improve when it gains loyal customers.","zh":"當小企業獲得忠實顧客，其前景會改善。"},{"en":"If a language project gains funding, its prospects may become stronger.","zh":"如果語言項目獲得資金，其前景可能變得更強。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on future possibility.","zh":"這個短語強調未來可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"raise enough funds","meaning":"籌集足夠資金","examples":[{"en":"A project may fail if it cannot raise enough funds.","zh":"如果項目不能籌集足夠資金，可能會失敗。"},{"en":"To raise enough funds means to collect sufficient money for a purpose.","zh":"籌集足夠資金，指為某目的收集足夠金錢。"},{"en":"Students may raise enough funds for a charity trip by selling handmade cards.","zh":"學生可能透過售賣手工卡片為慈善旅程籌集足夠資金。"},{"en":"If a project cannot raise money, it may not buy equipment or pay researchers.","zh":"如果項目不能籌錢，就可能無法購買設備或支付研究人員。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gathering the money needed.","zh":"這個短語描述收集所需金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"achieve its aims","meaning":"達成目標","examples":[{"en":"Funding can help a project achieve its aims.","zh":"資金可以幫助項目達成目標。"},{"en":"To achieve its aims means to successfully reach the goals it was created for.","zh":"達成目標，指成功達到其設立時的目的。"},{"en":"A school reading programme achieves its aims if students read more confidently.","zh":"如果學生更有信心閱讀，學校閱讀計劃就達成目標。"},{"en":"If WOLP records endangered traditions, it moves closer to achieving its aims.","zh":"如果 WOLP 記錄瀕危傳統，它就更接近達成目標。"},{"en":"The phrase describes successful goal completion.","zh":"這個短語描述成功完成目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"have a chance of","meaning":"有機會","examples":[{"en":"WOLP has a chance of protecting endangered languages.","zh":"WOLP 有機會保護瀕危語言。"},{"en":"To have a chance of doing something means it is possible that the action will succeed.","zh":"有機會做某事，指該行動有可能成功。"},{"en":"A student has a chance of improving if they practise a little every day.","zh":"如果學生每天練習一點，就有機會進步。"},{"en":"If a project has funding and community support, it has a better chance of success.","zh":"如果項目有資金和社群支持，就有更大成功機會。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses possibility, not certainty.","zh":"這個短語表達可能性，而不是確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"protect endangered languages","meaning":"保護瀕危語言","examples":[{"en":"The project has a chance of protecting endangered languages.","zh":"該計劃有機會保護瀕危語言。"},{"en":"To protect endangered languages means to help languages at risk continue to be recorded, taught, and spoken.","zh":"保護瀕危語言，指幫助有風險的語言繼續被記錄、教授和使用。"},{"en":"A community can protect endangered languages by teaching children and recording elders.","zh":"社群可以透過教孩子和記錄長者來保護瀕危語言。"},{"en":"If endangered languages are protected, cultural knowledge may survive with them.","zh":"如果瀕危語言受到保護，文化知識可能與它們一起存續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active language preservation.","zh":"這個短語描述積極保存語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"main point about","meaning":"關於……的主要觀點","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for Turin’s main point about globalisation.","zh":"題目問 Turin 關於全球化的主要觀點。"},{"en":"The main point about something is the most important idea someone wants to communicate.","zh":"關於某事的主要觀點，是某人想傳達的最重要想法。"},{"en":"The main point about homework may be that quality matters more than quantity.","zh":"關於功課的主要觀點可能是質素比數量更重要。"},{"en":"If Turin says globalisation both harms and helps, that may be his central point.","zh":"如果 Turin 說全球化既傷害又幫助，那可能是他的核心觀點。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for the key idea.","zh":"這個短語要求找出重點想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"advantages and disadvantages","meaning":"優點和缺點","examples":[{"en":"Turin suggests that globalisation has both advantages and disadvantages.","zh":"Turin 指出全球化有優點和缺點。"},{"en":"Advantages and disadvantages are the good points and bad points of something.","zh":"優點和缺點，是某事的好處和壞處。"},{"en":"Online learning has advantages and disadvantages: it is convenient, but students may feel isolated.","zh":"網上學習有優點和缺點：它方便，但學生可能感到孤立。"},{"en":"If globalisation provides tools but also erodes diversity, it has both sides.","zh":"如果全球化提供工具但也侵蝕多樣性，它就有兩面。"},{"en":"The phrase supports balanced discussion.","zh":"這個短語支援平衡討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a more critical view of","meaning":"對……持更批判的看法","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that we should have a more critical view of globalisation.","zh":"該選項暗示我們應對全球化持更批判的看法。"},{"en":"A more critical view of something means a more questioning and careful attitude toward it.","zh":"對某事持更批判的看法，指對它有更質疑和審慎的態度。"},{"en":"Students should have a more critical view of online information instead of trusting every post.","zh":"學生應對網上資訊持更批判的看法，而不是相信每個帖文。"},{"en":"If globalisation is often praised, a critical view may ask who loses from it.","zh":"如果全球化常被讚揚，批判看法可能會問誰因此受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes thoughtful questioning, not simple rejection.","zh":"這個短語描述深思熟慮的質疑，而不是簡單否定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in the face of globalisation","meaning":"面對全球化","examples":[{"en":"Communities may try to protect their identity in the face of globalisation.","zh":"面對全球化，社群可能嘗試保護自己的身份認同。"},{"en":"In the face of globalisation means when dealing with the pressures and changes caused by globalisation.","zh":"面對全球化，指在處理全球化造成的壓力和變化時。"},{"en":"Local shops may change their services in the face of global chain stores.","zh":"面對全球連鎖店，本地商店可能改變自己的服務。"},{"en":"If communities face global media and national languages, they may need stronger ways to protect local speech.","zh":"如果社群面對全球媒體和國語，就可能需要更強方法保護本地語言。"},{"en":"The phrase describes responding to a powerful outside force.","zh":"這個短語描述回應強大的外在力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"protect our identity above all else","meaning":"首要保護身份認同","examples":[{"en":"One option suggests that communities should protect their identity above all else.","zh":"一個選項暗示社群應首要保護身份認同。"},{"en":"To protect our identity above all else means to treat identity as the most important thing to defend.","zh":"首要保護身份認同，指把身份認同視為最重要、最需要守護的東西。"},{"en":"A family may protect its identity above all else by continuing its language and rituals after migration.","zh":"移民後，家庭可能透過延續語言和儀式來首要保護身份認同。"},{"en":"If identity is placed above everything, economic or practical needs may receive less attention.","zh":"如果身份認同被置於一切之上，經濟或實際需要可能得到較少注意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving identity top priority.","zh":"這個短語描述把身份認同放在最高優先次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"keep up with modern society","meaning":"跟上現代社會","examples":[{"en":"Communities can keep up with modern society without losing their language.","zh":"社群可以在不失去語言的情況下跟上現代社會。"},{"en":"To keep up with modern society means to adapt to contemporary technology, education, work, and public life.","zh":"跟上現代社會，指適應當代科技、教育、工作和公共生活。"},{"en":"Older workers may take computer classes to keep up with modern society.","zh":"年長員工可能上電腦課，以跟上現代社會。"},{"en":"If communities use modern tools in their own language, they can modernise without abandoning it.","zh":"如果社群用自己的語言使用現代工具，就能在不放棄語言下現代化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes staying current while adapting.","zh":"這個短語描述適應並保持與時並進。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"without losing their language","meaning":"在不失去語言的情況下","examples":[{"en":"People can become modern without losing their language.","zh":"人們可以在不失去語言的情況下走向現代化。"},{"en":"Without losing their language means while still keeping and using their own language.","zh":"在不失去語言的情況下，指仍然保留和使用自己的語言。"},{"en":"Children can learn English without losing their home language if both are valued.","zh":"如果兩種語言都被重視，孩子可以學英語而不失去家庭語言。"},{"en":"If modern education includes local languages, communities do not have to choose between progress and identity.","zh":"如果現代教育包括本地語言，社群就不必在進步和身份之間二選一。"},{"en":"The phrase rejects the idea that modernity requires language loss.","zh":"這個短語否定現代化必須伴隨語言流失的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"join the race to","meaning":"加入……的競賽","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that people should join the race to protect languages.","zh":"該選項暗示人們應加入保護語言的競賽。"},{"en":"To join the race to do something means to take part in an urgent effort before time runs out.","zh":"加入做某事的競賽，指在時間耗盡前參與緊急努力。"},{"en":"Volunteers may join the race to deliver supplies before a storm arrives.","zh":"義工可能在風暴到來前加入運送物資的競賽。"},{"en":"If languages are disappearing quickly, more people may need to join the preservation effort.","zh":"如果語言正在快速消失，更多人可能需要加入保存工作。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses urgent participation.","zh":"這個短語表達緊急參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be realistic","meaning":"要務實","examples":[{"en":"Turin says people must be realistic about what projects can achieve.","zh":"Turin 說，人們必須對項目能達成甚麼保持務實。"},{"en":"To be realistic means to understand what is actually possible, not only what one hopes for.","zh":"要務實，指理解現實上甚麼可能做到，而不只是自己希望甚麼。"},{"en":"A student should be realistic about how much can be revised in one night.","zh":"學生應務實看待一晚可以溫習多少內容。"},{"en":"If a project can record a language but cannot force people to speak it, expectations must be practical.","zh":"如果項目能記錄語言但不能強迫人們說它，期望就必須實際。"},{"en":"The phrase describes honest judgement about limits and possibilities.","zh":"這個短語描述對限制和可能性的誠實判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 24 - The future of the World’s Language.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 25":[{"front":"Real Tennis, Royal Tennis, Court Tennis and Jeu de Paume","meaning":"真網球、皇家網球、場地網球和掌球戲","examples":[{"en":"Real Tennis, Royal Tennis, Court Tennis and Jeu de Paume are different names for the same ancient game.","zh":"真網球、皇家網球、場地網球和掌球戲是同一種古老遊戲的不同名稱。"},{"en":"These names refer to an old indoor racket game that developed before modern lawn tennis.","zh":"這些名稱指一種比現代草地網球更早發展出來的室內球拍運動。"},{"en":"A sports historian may use different names depending on whether the game is discussed in Britain, America or France.","zh":"體育史學家可能按英國、美國或法國語境使用不同名稱。"},{"en":"If students see these four names in a passage, they should understand that the writer is not describing four separate sports.","zh":"如果學生在文章中看到這四個名稱，應理解作者並不是在描述四種不同運動。"},{"en":"This entry shows how one historical game can have several names in different traditions.","zh":"這個詞條顯示同一種歷史遊戲可以在不同傳統中有多個名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as it is called in","meaning":"在……被稱為","examples":[{"en":"Real Tennis is the name of the game as it is called in Britain.","zh":"Real Tennis 是這項運動在英國被稱為的名稱。"},{"en":"As it is called in a place means the name used for something in that country or region.","zh":"As it is called in a place 指某事物在某國家或地區所使用的名稱。"},{"en":"Football, as it is called in Britain, is called soccer in some other countries.","zh":"Football 是這項運動在英國的稱呼，在一些其他國家則叫 soccer。"},{"en":"If a term changes by country, this phrase helps explain the local name.","zh":"如果用語因國家而異，這個片語可以幫助解釋本地名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one thing has different names in different places.","zh":"當同一事物在不同地方有不同名稱時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as it is properly known","meaning":"正式名稱是","examples":[{"en":"The game is simply tennis, as it is properly known by traditional players.","zh":"這項運動其實就是 tennis，這是傳統球手所認為的正式名稱。"},{"en":"As it is properly known means according to the correct or traditional name.","zh":"As it is properly known 指按正確或傳統名稱而言。"},{"en":"Some people say Big Ben, but properly speaking the name refers to the bell, not the whole tower.","zh":"有些人說 Big Ben，但嚴格來說這名稱指鐘本身，而不是整座塔。"},{"en":"If a writer uses this phrase, they are correcting or clarifying the formal name.","zh":"如果作者使用這個片語，他是在修正或澄清正式名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears when popular usage and proper terminology are different.","zh":"當通俗用法和正式術語不同時，這個片語常會出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the oldest of all the racket games","meaning":"所有球拍類運動中最古老的","examples":[{"en":"Real tennis is the oldest of all the racket games.","zh":"真網球是所有球拍類運動中最古老的。"},{"en":"The oldest of all the racket games means it developed before other sports played with rackets.","zh":"The oldest of all the racket games 指它比其他用球拍進行的運動更早發展。"},{"en":"A museum exhibit might introduce real tennis as the ancestor of later racket sports.","zh":"博物館展覽可能把真網球介紹為後來球拍運動的祖先。"},{"en":"If a sport is the oldest in its group, later games may have borrowed ideas from it.","zh":"如果一項運動是同類中最古老的，後來的運動可能借用了它的理念。"},{"en":"This phrase places real tennis at the beginning of racket-sport history.","zh":"這個片語把真網球放在球拍運動歷史的開端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"unlike most of the others","meaning":"不像其他大多數……","examples":[{"en":"Unlike most of the others, real tennis developed gradually over time.","zh":"不像其他大多數球拍運動，真網球是隨時間逐漸發展而成的。"},{"en":"Unlike most of the others means it is different from the majority of the things being compared.","zh":"Unlike most of the others 指它與正在比較的大多數事物不同。"},{"en":"Unlike most of the other students, she revised every week instead of waiting until the exam.","zh":"不像其他大多數學生，她每星期溫習，而不是等到考試前。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show contrast between one example and the larger group.","zh":"這個片語幫助顯示一個例子與較大群體之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when one case does not follow the usual pattern.","zh":"當某個個案不跟隨一般模式時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a product of evolution","meaning":"演變而成的產物","examples":[{"en":"Real tennis is a product of evolution rather than pure invention.","zh":"真網球是演變而成的產物，而不是純粹發明。"},{"en":"A product of evolution means something developed slowly through many small changes.","zh":"A product of evolution 指某物透過許多細小改變慢慢發展而成。"},{"en":"Modern English spelling is a product of evolution, not one person’s perfect design.","zh":"現代英語拼寫是演變而成的產物，不是一個人的完美設計。"},{"en":"If a game changes rules, equipment and spaces over centuries, it becomes a product of evolution.","zh":"如果一項遊戲幾個世紀以來改變規則、器材和場地，它就是演變而成的產物。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts gradual historical development with sudden creation.","zh":"這個片語把逐步歷史發展與突然創造作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rather than pure invention","meaning":"而不是純粹發明","examples":[{"en":"The sport grew through gradual change rather than pure invention.","zh":"這項運動透過逐步改變而成長，而不是純粹發明。"},{"en":"Rather than pure invention means not created suddenly from nothing, but developed from earlier forms.","zh":"Rather than pure invention 指不是突然從零創造，而是由早期形式發展而來。"},{"en":"Many school traditions grow from repeated habits rather than pure invention.","zh":"許多學校傳統來自反覆習慣，而不是純粹發明。"},{"en":"If a practice changes slowly over time, it should not be treated as one person’s new idea.","zh":"如果一種做法隨時間慢慢改變，就不應把它視為某個人的全新想法。"},{"en":"This phrase separates gradual development from instant creation.","zh":"這個片語把逐步發展與即時創造分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"started to form into","meaning":"開始形成為","examples":[{"en":"The game started to form into something recognisable in the 11th century.","zh":"這項遊戲在十一世紀開始形成為某種可辨認的東西。"},{"en":"Started to form into means began to develop into a clearer shape or identity.","zh":"Started to form into 指開始發展成較清晰的形態或身份。"},{"en":"A student’s rough notes may start to form into an essay after they organise the main ideas.","zh":"當學生整理主要想法後，粗略筆記可能開始形成為一篇文章。"},{"en":"When rules and playing spaces became more regular, the game started to take shape.","zh":"當規則和比賽場地變得更固定，這項遊戲就開始成形。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the early stage of becoming something more definite.","zh":"這個片語描述變成更明確事物的早期階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"something recognisable","meaning":"可辨認的東西","examples":[{"en":"By the 11th century, the game had become something recognisable.","zh":"到十一世紀，這項遊戲已成為某種可辨認的東西。"},{"en":"Something recognisable is something clear enough to identify.","zh":"Something recognisable 是清楚到可以識別的東西。"},{"en":"A child’s drawing becomes something recognisable when others can tell it is a house or a tree.","zh":"當其他人看得出兒童畫的是房屋或樹時，那幅畫就成為可辨認的東西。"},{"en":"If a sport has repeated rules and familiar movements, people can recognise it as a distinct game.","zh":"如果一項運動有重複規則和熟悉動作，人們就能把它認作一種獨立遊戲。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an early form has become identifiable.","zh":"這個片語顯示早期形式已變得可以辨認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the 11th century","meaning":"在十一世紀","examples":[{"en":"The game started to take shape in the 11th century.","zh":"這項遊戲在十一世紀開始成形。"},{"en":"In the 11th century means during the years from 1001 to 1100.","zh":"In the 11th century 指在1001年至1100年期間。"},{"en":"A history lesson may describe how castles and monasteries developed in the 11th century.","zh":"歷史課可能描述城堡和修道院在十一世紀如何發展。"},{"en":"If a game can be traced to the 11th century, it has a very long history.","zh":"如果一項遊戲可追溯至十一世紀，它就有非常悠久的歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event in a specific medieval period.","zh":"這個片語把事件放在特定中世紀時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"played by monks","meaning":"由修士玩","examples":[{"en":"The early form of tennis was played by monks in Italy and France.","zh":"網球的早期形式由意大利和法國的修士玩。"},{"en":"Played by monks means monks were the people who took part in the game.","zh":"Played by monks 指修士是參與這項遊戲的人。"},{"en":"A simple ball game might be played by students during lunch break.","zh":"簡單球類遊戲可能由學生在午飯時間玩。"},{"en":"If a sport was first played by monks, its early setting was religious rather than professional.","zh":"如果一項運動最初由修士玩，它的早期場景就是宗教性的，而不是職業性的。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the early players of the game.","zh":"這個片語指出這項遊戲的早期玩家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the cloisters of monasteries","meaning":"修道院的迴廊","examples":[{"en":"Monks played the game around the cloisters of monasteries.","zh":"修士在修道院迴廊周圍玩這項遊戲。"},{"en":"The cloisters of monasteries are covered walkways around open spaces in religious buildings.","zh":"The cloisters of monasteries 是宗教建築中圍繞開放空間的有蓋走廊。"},{"en":"Visitors may walk through monastery cloisters to see old stone arches and courtyards.","zh":"旅客可能走過修道院迴廊，欣賞古老石拱和庭院。"},{"en":"If monks played in cloisters, the building’s shape may have influenced the game’s layout.","zh":"如果修士在迴廊中玩，建築形狀可能影響了遊戲佈局。"},{"en":"This phrase names the architectural setting where the early game developed.","zh":"這個片語命名早期遊戲發展的建築場景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"much as","meaning":"很像；正如","examples":[{"en":"Monks played handball much as schoolchildren do today.","zh":"修士玩手球的方式，很像今日學童玩遊戲。"},{"en":"Much as means in a similar way to how someone else does something.","zh":"Much as 指以與其他人做某事相似的方式。"},{"en":"Children learn words by copying adults, much as musicians learn songs by listening carefully.","zh":"孩子透過模仿成人學詞語，很像音樂人透過仔細聆聽學歌曲。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare an old action with a modern familiar action.","zh":"這個片語幫助把古代行動與現代熟悉行動比較。"},{"en":"It makes the historical scene easier to imagine.","zh":"它令歷史場景更容易想像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"school playground","meaning":"學校操場","examples":[{"en":"Children still play games in corners of their school playground.","zh":"孩子們現在仍在學校操場的角落玩遊戲。"},{"en":"A school playground is an outdoor area where students play during breaks.","zh":"School playground 是學生小息時玩耍的戶外地方。"},{"en":"Students may play football, skipping games or handball in the school playground.","zh":"學生可能在學校操場踢足球、跳繩或玩手球。"},{"en":"If a wall or corner is available, children often invent simple games around it.","zh":"如果有牆或角落，孩子常會圍繞它發明簡單遊戲。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a familiar modern comparison for old courtyard games.","zh":"這個片語為古老庭院遊戲提供熟悉的現代比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"gradually","meaning":"逐漸地","examples":[{"en":"Gradually, the game became more enjoyable and organised.","zh":"逐漸地，這項遊戲變得更有趣和更有組織。"},{"en":"Gradually means slowly over time, not suddenly.","zh":"Gradually 指隨時間慢慢地，而不是突然地。"},{"en":"A student’s pronunciation improves gradually through repeated practice.","zh":"學生的發音會透過反覆練習逐漸改善。"},{"en":"If rules change little by little, a game can gradually become more organised.","zh":"如果規則一點一點改變，遊戲可以逐漸變得更有組織。"},{"en":"This word shows slow development across a period of time.","zh":"這個詞顯示一段時間內的緩慢發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"adopt rules","meaning":"採納規則","examples":[{"en":"Players adopted more enjoyable rules as the game developed.","zh":"隨着遊戲發展，玩家採納了更有趣的規則。"},{"en":"To adopt rules means to accept and start using them.","zh":"To adopt rules 指接受並開始使用規則。"},{"en":"A class may adopt rules about speaking turns to make discussions fairer.","zh":"班級可能採納關於輪流發言的規則，令討論更公平。"},{"en":"If players adopt clearer rules, arguments during a game may decrease.","zh":"如果玩家採納更清晰的規則，遊戲中的爭拗可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing rules and making them part of normal practice.","zh":"這個片語描述選擇規則並把它變成正常做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"bizarre rules","meaning":"古怪的規則","examples":[{"en":"Some bizarre rules were abandoned over time.","zh":"一些古怪的規則隨時間被放棄。"},{"en":"Bizarre rules are very strange or unusual rules.","zh":"Bizarre rules 是非常奇怪或不尋常的規則。"},{"en":"A game would have bizarre rules if players had to hop on one foot before every throw.","zh":"如果玩家每次投球前都必須單腳跳，這項遊戲就有古怪的規則。"},{"en":"If rules are too bizarre, new players may feel confused and lose interest.","zh":"如果規則太古怪，新玩家可能感到困惑並失去興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rules that seem odd rather than sensible.","zh":"這個片語描述顯得奇怪而不是合理的規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be abandoned","meaning":"被放棄","examples":[{"en":"The less enjoyable rules were abandoned by later players.","zh":"較少趣味的規則被後來的玩家放棄。"},{"en":"To be abandoned means to be given up or stopped.","zh":"To be abandoned 指被放棄或停止使用。"},{"en":"A school rule may be abandoned if it creates more problems than it solves.","zh":"如果校規造成的問題多於解決的問題，它可能被放棄。"},{"en":"If players abandon a rule, the game can become easier or more enjoyable.","zh":"如果玩家放棄某條規則，遊戲可以變得更容易或更有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something no longer being used.","zh":"這個片語描述某事不再被使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"add features to","meaning":"為……加上特色設施","examples":[{"en":"People started to add features to their courtyards.","zh":"人們開始為庭院加上特色設施。"},{"en":"To add features to something means to put in extra parts or details.","zh":"To add features to something 指加入額外部分或細節。"},{"en":"A school may add features to its playground, such as benches, shade and sports markings.","zh":"學校可能為操場加上長椅、遮蔭和運動標線等設施。"},{"en":"If players add walls, lines or openings to a court, the game may become more varied.","zh":"如果玩家為球場加入牆、線或開口，遊戲可能變得更多變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improving or changing a space by adding elements.","zh":"這個片語描述透過加入元素改善或改變空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"improve the pastime","meaning":"改善這項消遣活動","examples":[{"en":"Some courtyard features improved the pastime.","zh":"一些庭院特色設施改善了這項消遣活動。"},{"en":"To improve the pastime means to make the leisure activity more enjoyable or interesting.","zh":"To improve the pastime 指令休閒活動更有趣或更吸引。"},{"en":"Adding lights to a community court can improve the pastime by allowing evening play.","zh":"為社區球場加燈可以讓人晚上玩，從而改善這項消遣活動。"},{"en":"If a game becomes more fun, more people may continue playing it.","zh":"如果遊戲變得更有趣，更多人可能繼續玩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a hobby or casual activity better.","zh":"這個片語描述改善一項嗜好或休閒活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"demolish or modify","meaning":"拆除或改建","examples":[{"en":"People demolished or modified features that made the game less enjoyable.","zh":"人們拆除或改建令遊戲較少趣味的特色設施。"},{"en":"To demolish or modify something means to knock it down or change its form.","zh":"To demolish or modify something 指拆掉某物或改變其形態。"},{"en":"A school may demolish or modify an old wall if it blocks a safe playground route.","zh":"如果舊牆阻礙安全操場路線，學校可能拆除或改建它。"},{"en":"If a court feature interrupts play too often, players may remove or alter it.","zh":"如果球場某設施太常打斷比賽，玩家可能移除或改動它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes destroying something completely or changing it partly.","zh":"這個片語描述完全摧毀某物或局部改變某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"detract from","meaning":"減損；削弱","examples":[{"en":"Some courtyard features detracted from the game.","zh":"一些庭院特色設施減損了遊戲的趣味。"},{"en":"To detract from something means to reduce its quality, enjoyment or value.","zh":"To detract from something 指降低某事的質素、樂趣或價值。"},{"en":"Loud noise can detract from a lesson because students cannot concentrate.","zh":"噪音可以減損課堂效果，因為學生不能專心。"},{"en":"If a rule makes a sport less fair, it detracts from the game.","zh":"如果規則令運動變得較不公平，它就削弱了比賽。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something weakening the overall experience.","zh":"這個片語描述某物削弱整體體驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ban the playing of","meaning":"禁止玩……","examples":[{"en":"The Pope banned the playing of the game.","zh":"教宗禁止玩這項遊戲。"},{"en":"To ban the playing of a game means to officially forbid people from playing it.","zh":"To ban the playing of a game 指正式禁止人們玩某項遊戲。"},{"en":"A school may ban the playing of a rough game if students keep getting hurt.","zh":"如果學生不斷受傷，學校可能禁止玩某種粗野遊戲。"},{"en":"If authorities think an activity is harmful or distracting, they may ban it.","zh":"如果當局認為某活動有害或令人分心，他們可能禁止它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an official prohibition on an activity.","zh":"這個片語描述對某活動的正式禁令。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"spread from cloister to castle","meaning":"從修道院傳到城堡","examples":[{"en":"By the 14th century, the game had spread from cloister to castle.","zh":"到十四世紀，這項遊戲已從修道院傳到城堡。"},{"en":"To spread from cloister to castle means to move from religious spaces into noble or royal spaces.","zh":"To spread from cloister to castle 指從宗教空間傳到貴族或王室空間。"},{"en":"A song may spread from classrooms to social media when students share it widely.","zh":"當學生廣泛分享，一首歌可能從課室傳到社交媒體。"},{"en":"If a game spreads to castles, it becomes connected with wealth and status.","zh":"如果遊戲傳到城堡，它就與財富和地位連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the game moving from monks to the nobility.","zh":"這個片語顯示遊戲由修士傳到貴族。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a game of the nobility","meaning":"貴族的遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Tennis became a game of the nobility.","zh":"網球成為貴族的遊戲。"},{"en":"A game of the nobility is a sport mainly played by aristocrats or high-status people.","zh":"A game of the nobility 是主要由貴族或高地位人士玩的運動。"},{"en":"In the past, expensive sports often became games of the nobility because ordinary people lacked space and money.","zh":"過去，昂貴運動常成為貴族遊戲，因為普通人缺乏空間和金錢。"},{"en":"If a sport needs private courts and leisure time, it may become associated with upper classes.","zh":"如果一項運動需要私人球場和閒暇時間，它可能與上層階級連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a sport with social rank.","zh":"這個片語把運動與社會階級連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"theories about the origins of","meaning":"關於……起源的理論","examples":[{"en":"There are other theories about the origins of the game.","zh":"關於這項遊戲的起源還有其他理論。"},{"en":"Theories about the origins of something are explanations of how it first began.","zh":"Theories about the origins of something 是解釋某事最初如何開始的說法。"},{"en":"Historians have different theories about the origins of some festivals.","zh":"歷史學家對某些節日的起源有不同理論。"},{"en":"If early evidence is incomplete, several origin theories may exist.","zh":"如果早期證據不完整，可能會存在幾種起源理論。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces competing explanations about beginnings.","zh":"這個片語引出關於起點的不同解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a tennis historian","meaning":"網球史學家","examples":[{"en":"A tennis historian has offered another theory about the game’s origins.","zh":"一位網球史學家提出了另一個關於這項遊戲起源的理論。"},{"en":"A tennis historian is a person who studies the history and development of tennis.","zh":"Tennis historian 是研究網球歷史和發展的人。"},{"en":"A sports museum may invite a tennis historian to explain old rackets and courts.","zh":"體育博物館可能邀請網球史學家解釋舊球拍和球場。"},{"en":"If a historian studies old documents, they may challenge popular stories about a sport.","zh":"如果史學家研究舊文件，他們可能挑戰關於運動的流行故事。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specialist in tennis history.","zh":"這個片語命名網球歷史方面的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"theorise that","meaning":"提出理論認為","examples":[{"en":"Roger Morgan theorised that tennis began in medieval streets.","zh":"Roger Morgan 提出理論認為網球起源於中世紀街道。"},{"en":"To theorise that means to suggest an explanation based on reasoning or evidence.","zh":"To theorise that 指根據推理或證據提出解釋。"},{"en":"A scientist may theorise that sleep affects memory after observing many students.","zh":"科學家觀察許多學生後，可能提出理論認為睡眠影響記憶。"},{"en":"If proof is not complete, a researcher may theorise rather than state a fact.","zh":"如果證據不完整，研究者可能提出理論，而不是陳述事實。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an informed but debatable explanation.","zh":"這個片語引出有根據但可爭論的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"owe its origins to","meaning":"起源於……","examples":[{"en":"The game may owe its origins to medieval street games.","zh":"這項遊戲可能起源於中世紀街頭遊戲。"},{"en":"To owe its origins to something means to have begun because of or from that thing.","zh":"To owe its origins to something 指因某事或由某事開始。"},{"en":"A school tradition may owe its origins to a small event that students repeated every year.","zh":"學校傳統可能起源於一件學生每年重複的小事。"},{"en":"If a sport owes its origins to street play, its early form was probably informal.","zh":"如果一項運動起源於街頭遊戲，它的早期形式大概很非正式。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the source from which something developed.","zh":"這個片語解釋某事發展出來的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"medieval streets","meaning":"中世紀街道","examples":[{"en":"Some historians believe the game began in medieval streets.","zh":"一些歷史學家相信這項遊戲起源於中世紀街道。"},{"en":"Medieval streets were streets in European towns during the Middle Ages.","zh":"Medieval streets 是中世紀歐洲城鎮中的街道。"},{"en":"Medieval streets were often narrow, crowded and dirty compared with modern roads.","zh":"與現代道路相比，中世紀街道通常狹窄、擁擠且骯髒。"},{"en":"If a game was played in medieval streets, space and hygiene may have shaped how it developed.","zh":"如果遊戲在中世紀街道中進行，空間和衛生可能影響了其發展。"},{"en":"This phrase places the activity in an old urban setting.","zh":"這個片語把活動放在古老城市場景中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be used as sewers","meaning":"被用作污水渠","examples":[{"en":"Medieval streets were also used as sewers.","zh":"中世紀街道也被用作污水渠。"},{"en":"To be used as sewers means waste water and refuse were allowed to flow through them.","zh":"To be used as sewers 指污水和廢物被容許在其中流過。"},{"en":"Before modern drainage, some streets were used as places for dirty water to run away.","zh":"在現代排水系統以前，一些街道被用作髒水流走的地方。"},{"en":"If streets were used as sewers, playing there would be unpleasant and unhealthy.","zh":"如果街道被用作污水渠，在那裏玩耍會令人不舒服且不衛生。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why medieval street games may have been uncomfortable.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何中世紀街頭遊戲可能不舒服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"couldn’t have been much fun","meaning":"不可能太有趣","examples":[{"en":"Playing games in streets used as sewers couldn’t have been much fun.","zh":"在被用作污水渠的街道上玩遊戲不可能太有趣。"},{"en":"Couldn’t have been much fun means it was probably unpleasant or not enjoyable.","zh":"Couldn’t have been much fun 指某事大概令人不快或不享受。"},{"en":"Waiting for a bus in heavy rain couldn’t have been much fun for the students.","zh":"學生在大雨中等巴士不可能太有趣。"},{"en":"If a place is dirty and crowded, playing there is unlikely to feel enjoyable.","zh":"如果地方骯髒又擁擠，在那裏玩大概不會愉快。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a negative judgement in a conversational way.","zh":"這個片語用較口語方式作出負面判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the heyday of","meaning":"……的全盛時期","examples":[{"en":"The 16th and 17th centuries were the heyday of tennis.","zh":"十六及十七世紀是真網球的全盛時期。"},{"en":"The heyday of something is the period when it was most successful or popular.","zh":"The heyday of something 是某事最成功或最流行的時期。"},{"en":"The 1980s may be seen as the heyday of some classic video games.","zh":"1980年代可被視為某些經典電子遊戲的全盛時期。"},{"en":"If a sport has many courts and famous players, it may be in its heyday.","zh":"如果一項運動有許多球場和著名球手，它可能正處於全盛時期。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a golden period of strength or popularity.","zh":"這個片語描述力量或受歡迎程度的黃金時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the nobility of","meaning":"……的貴族","examples":[{"en":"The game was played by the nobility of France and Britain.","zh":"這項遊戲由法國和英國的貴族玩。"},{"en":"The nobility of a country means its aristocratic or high-born social class.","zh":"The nobility of a country 指該國的貴族或出身高貴的社會階層。"},{"en":"In history lessons, students may study the nobility of France before the revolution.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生可能研究法國大革命前的法國貴族。"},{"en":"If a sport is played by the nobility, it may require wealth, land or leisure time.","zh":"如果一項運動由貴族玩，它可能需要財富、土地或閒暇時間。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a high-status social group in a country.","zh":"這個片語指出某國的高地位社會群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reputedly","meaning":"據說；據傳","examples":[{"en":"There were reputedly 1,800 tennis courts in Paris alone.","zh":"據說單是在巴黎就有1,800個網球場。"},{"en":"Reputedly means according to what people say, though it may not be fully proven.","zh":"Reputedly 指根據人們所說，雖然未必完全證實。"},{"en":"The old building is reputedly haunted, but no one has shown clear evidence.","zh":"據說那座舊建築鬧鬼，但沒有人提出清晰證據。"},{"en":"If a number is introduced with reputedly, readers should treat it as reported rather than certain.","zh":"如果數字以 reputedly 引出，讀者應把它視為報稱資料，而非確定事實。"},{"en":"This word signals that information comes from reputation or report.","zh":"這個詞表示資訊來自傳聞或報道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in Paris alone","meaning":"單是在巴黎","examples":[{"en":"There were reputedly 1,800 courts in Paris alone.","zh":"據說單是在巴黎就有1,800個球場。"},{"en":"In Paris alone means only in Paris, not counting other places.","zh":"In Paris alone 指只計巴黎，不包括其他地方。"},{"en":"The charity raised 50,000 dollars in one district alone.","zh":"該慈善機構單是在一個地區就籌得五萬美元。"},{"en":"If so many courts existed in Paris alone, the sport must have been very popular there.","zh":"如果單是在巴黎就有這麼多球場，這項運動在當地必定很流行。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the number is large even before other places are included.","zh":"這個片語強調即使未計其他地方，數字已經很大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ramshackle structures","meaning":"破舊簡陋的建築","examples":[{"en":"Many of the courts were quite ramshackle structures.","zh":"許多球場都是相當破舊簡陋的建築。"},{"en":"Ramshackle structures are buildings or constructions that are old, weak or poorly built.","zh":"Ramshackle structures 是老舊、脆弱或建造粗劣的建築物。"},{"en":"A village classroom may become a ramshackle structure if it is never repaired.","zh":"如果從不維修，鄉村課室可能變成破舊簡陋的建築。"},{"en":"If sports courts are ramshackle, they may be unsafe or uncomfortable to use.","zh":"如果運動場地破舊簡陋，使用時可能不安全或不舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase describes buildings in poor physical condition.","zh":"這個片語描述實體狀況差的建築物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the game flourished","meaning":"這項運動蓬勃發展","examples":[{"en":"The game flourished in Britain during this period.","zh":"這項運動在這段時期於英國蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"The game flourished means it became successful, active and popular.","zh":"The game flourished 指這項運動變得成功、活躍和流行。"},{"en":"A school debating club may flourish if many students join and teachers support it.","zh":"如果許多學生加入且老師支持，學校辯論學會可能蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"If courts, players and competitions increase, a sport is flourishing.","zh":"如果球場、球手和比賽增加，一項運動就是在蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong growth and popularity.","zh":"這個片語描述強勁增長和受歡迎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"royalty","meaning":"王室成員","examples":[{"en":"Royalty included several famous tennis players.","zh":"王室成員中包括幾位著名網球球手。"},{"en":"Royalty means kings, queens, princes, princesses and other members of royal families.","zh":"Royalty 指國王、女王、王子、公主和其他王室家族成員。"},{"en":"In history, royalty often had access to private courts, horses and expensive sports.","zh":"在歷史上，王室成員常能使用私人球場、馬匹和昂貴運動。"},{"en":"If royalty played a sport, the activity could gain prestige and attention.","zh":"如果王室成員玩某項運動，該活動可能獲得聲望和關注。"},{"en":"This word refers to members of ruling families.","zh":"這個詞指統治家族的成員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"enthusiastic though not skilled","meaning":"熱衷但技術不高","examples":[{"en":"Henry VII was enthusiastic though not skilled.","zh":"Henry VII 熱衷但技術不高。"},{"en":"Enthusiastic though not skilled means eager and interested, but not very good at the activity.","zh":"Enthusiastic though not skilled 指很有興趣和熱情，但做得不太好。"},{"en":"A beginner may be enthusiastic though not skilled when learning the piano.","zh":"初學鋼琴的人可能熱衷但技術不高。"},{"en":"If someone enjoys a sport despite weak technique, enthusiasm matters more than ability.","zh":"如果某人即使技術弱仍享受運動，熱情就比能力更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts attitude with competence.","zh":"這個片語把態度與能力作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"an adept","meaning":"高手；熟手","examples":[{"en":"Henry VIII was an adept at tennis.","zh":"Henry VIII 是網球高手。"},{"en":"An adept is someone who is highly skilled at an activity.","zh":"An adept 是在某活動上技術高超的人。"},{"en":"A student who can solve difficult maths problems quickly is an adept at problem-solving.","zh":"能快速解決困難數學題的學生，是解難高手。"},{"en":"If someone practises for years, they may become an adept rather than a casual player.","zh":"如果某人練習多年，他可能成為高手，而不只是普通玩家。"},{"en":"This word describes a person with strong ability in a field.","zh":"這個詞描述在某領域能力強的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"keen players","meaning":"熱衷的球手","examples":[{"en":"Kings Charles I and II were both keen players.","zh":"Charles I 和 Charles II 兩位國王都是熱衷的球手。"},{"en":"Keen players are people who are very interested in playing a game or sport.","zh":"Keen players 是對玩某遊戲或運動非常有興趣的人。"},{"en":"Keen chess players may spend weekends at tournaments.","zh":"熱衷的棋手可能週末參加錦標賽。"},{"en":"If a king was a keen player, the game could become fashionable at court.","zh":"如果國王是熱衷球手，這項遊戲可能在宮廷中流行起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes enthusiasm and regular participation.","zh":"這個片語描述熱情和經常參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"indirectly led to","meaning":"間接導致","examples":[{"en":"The game indirectly led to the death of King James I.","zh":"這項遊戲間接導致 King James I 的死亡。"},{"en":"Indirectly led to means helped cause something through a chain of events, not in a direct way.","zh":"Indirectly led to 指透過一連串事件促成某事，而不是直接造成。"},{"en":"Poor planning can indirectly lead to stress when students leave everything until the last day.","zh":"欠佳規劃可能間接導致壓力，因為學生把所有事留到最後一天。"},{"en":"If one event creates conditions for another event, it may indirectly lead to the final result.","zh":"如果一件事為另一件事創造條件，它可能間接導致最終結果。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a less obvious cause-and-effect relationship.","zh":"這個片語顯示較不明顯的因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"as a result of being hit by","meaning":"因被……擊中而","examples":[{"en":"One French king died as a result of being hit by a tennis ball.","zh":"一位法國國王因被網球擊中而死亡。"},{"en":"As a result of being hit by something means because that object struck the person.","zh":"As a result of being hit by something 指因某物撞擊該人而發生。"},{"en":"A student may get a bruise as a result of being hit by a football.","zh":"學生可能因被足球擊中而瘀傷。"},{"en":"If an injury follows a direct impact, this phrase explains the cause.","zh":"如果傷害來自直接撞擊，這個片語可以解釋原因。"},{"en":"This phrase links a physical accident with its result.","zh":"這個片語把身體意外與其結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"virtually indistinguishable from","meaning":"與……幾乎難以分辨","examples":[{"en":"Modern real tennis is virtually indistinguishable from the game played in those days.","zh":"現代真網球與當時玩的遊戲幾乎難以分辨。"},{"en":"Virtually indistinguishable from means almost impossible to tell apart from something else.","zh":"Virtually indistinguishable from 指幾乎無法與另一事物區分。"},{"en":"Two school uniforms may be virtually indistinguishable from each other if only the badge differs.","zh":"如果兩套校服只有校徽不同，它們可能彼此幾乎難以分辨。"},{"en":"If a game changes very little over centuries, modern players may experience something close to the original.","zh":"如果一項遊戲幾個世紀以來變化很少，現代玩家可能體驗到接近原始形式的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses extremely strong similarity.","zh":"這個片語強調極強相似性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"played with the bare hand","meaning":"徒手玩","examples":[{"en":"Originally, the game was played with the bare hand.","zh":"最初，這項遊戲是徒手玩的。"},{"en":"Played with the bare hand means players hit the ball using only their hand, without a racket or glove.","zh":"Played with the bare hand 指玩家不用球拍或手套，只用手擊球。"},{"en":"Children may play a simple wall game with the bare hand during recess.","zh":"孩子們可能在小息時徒手玩簡單牆球遊戲。"},{"en":"If a hard ball is hit with the bare hand, players may later invent protection or equipment.","zh":"如果用手擊打一個硬球，玩家後來可能發明保護裝備或器材。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the simplest early form of play.","zh":"這個片語描述最簡單的早期玩法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"with a glove","meaning":"戴着手套","examples":[{"en":"Later, the game was played with a glove.","zh":"後來，這項遊戲改為戴着手套玩。"},{"en":"With a glove means wearing a glove to protect the hand or improve play.","zh":"With a glove 指戴手套以保護手或改善玩法。"},{"en":"A goalkeeper plays with gloves to grip the ball and protect the fingers.","zh":"守門員戴着手套比賽，以抓住皮球並保護手指。"},{"en":"If bare hands become painful, gloves can make a game safer and more comfortable.","zh":"如果徒手很痛，手套可以令遊戲更安全和更舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a small step from hand play toward equipment-based play.","zh":"這個片語顯示從徒手遊戲走向器材遊戲的小一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"had the bright idea of","meaning":"想出……的妙計","examples":[{"en":"Someone had the bright idea of attaching cord to the fingers.","zh":"有人想出把繩索繫在手指上的妙計。"},{"en":"To have the bright idea of doing something means to think of a clever or useful solution.","zh":"To have the bright idea of doing something 指想到聰明或有用的解決方法。"},{"en":"A student had the bright idea of using flashcards to remember difficult vocabulary.","zh":"學生想出用記憶卡記困難詞彙的妙計。"},{"en":"If a simple idea solves a repeated problem, people may copy it.","zh":"如果一個簡單想法解決反覆問題，人們可能模仿它。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes an inventive step that changes a practice.","zh":"這個片語常描述改變做法的創新一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"attach something to","meaning":"把某物繫在……上","examples":[{"en":"Players attached cord or tendons to their fingers.","zh":"玩家把繩索或肌腱繫在手指上。"},{"en":"To attach something to something else means to fasten or connect it there.","zh":"To attach something to something else 指把某物固定或連接到另一物上。"},{"en":"A teacher may attach labels to boxes so students know where materials belong.","zh":"老師可能把標籤貼在盒子上，讓學生知道材料應放哪裏。"},{"en":"If players attach cord to gloves or fingers, they may hit the ball with more control.","zh":"如果玩家把繩索繫在手套或手指上，他們擊球時可能更有控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physically joining one thing to another.","zh":"這個片語描述把一物實體連接到另一物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cord or tendons","meaning":"繩索或肌腱","examples":[{"en":"Early players attached cord or tendons to the fingers.","zh":"早期玩家把繩索或肌腱繫在手指上。"},{"en":"Cord or tendons refers to strong string-like materials used before proper rackets existed.","zh":"Cord or tendons 指在正式球拍出現前使用的強韌線狀材料。"},{"en":"In a craft lesson, students may use cord to tie parts of a model together.","zh":"在手工課中，學生可能用繩索把模型部分綁在一起。"},{"en":"If early players needed a stronger hitting surface, cord or tendons could help.","zh":"如果早期玩家需要更強的擊球面，繩索或肌腱可以幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase names simple materials used in early equipment.","zh":"這個片語命名早期器材中使用的簡單材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a short step from","meaning":"離……只是很小一步","examples":[{"en":"It was a short step from attaching cords to making a racket.","zh":"從繫上繩索到製造球拍，只是很小一步。"},{"en":"A short step from A to B means only a small development was needed to move from A to B.","zh":"A short step from A to B 指從A發展到B只需要小小一步。"},{"en":"Once students can write clear sentences, it is a short step from sentences to short paragraphs.","zh":"一旦學生能寫清楚句子，從句子到短段落只是很小一步。"},{"en":"If players already used cords on their hands, adding a handle was a natural next move.","zh":"如果玩家已在手上使用繩索，加上手柄就是自然的下一步。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a close connection between two stages of development.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩個發展階段之間關係很近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"add a handle to","meaning":"為……加上手柄","examples":[{"en":"A handle was added to make a racket.","zh":"人們加上手柄來製成球拍。"},{"en":"To add a handle to something means to attach a part that can be held by the hand.","zh":"To add a handle to something 指加上一個可以用手握住的部分。"},{"en":"A designer may add a handle to a box so people can carry it more easily.","zh":"設計師可能為盒子加上手柄，讓人更容易攜帶。"},{"en":"If a hitting surface gets a handle, it becomes easier to swing and control.","zh":"如果擊球面加上手柄，它就更容易揮動和控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical design improvement.","zh":"這個片語描述實用的設計改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"similar in appearance to","meaning":"外觀與……相似","examples":[{"en":"The ball is similar in appearance to a lawn tennis ball.","zh":"這種球的外觀與草地網球球相似。"},{"en":"Similar in appearance to means it looks like something else.","zh":"Similar in appearance to 指外表看起來像另一物。"},{"en":"A toy phone may be similar in appearance to a real smartphone.","zh":"玩具電話的外觀可能與真正智能手機相似。"},{"en":"If two balls look similar, beginners may assume they are used in the same sport.","zh":"如果兩種球看起來相似，初學者可能以為它們用於同一運動。"},{"en":"This phrase compares outward look, not necessarily material or use.","zh":"這個片語比較外觀，而不一定比較材料或用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a core of cork","meaning":"軟木芯","examples":[{"en":"The ball is made with a core of cork.","zh":"這種球有一個軟木芯。"},{"en":"A core of cork means the centre of the ball is made from cork, a light natural material.","zh":"A core of cork 指球的中心由軟木這種輕質天然材料製成。"},{"en":"A science teacher may cut open a model ball to show its core and outer layers.","zh":"科學老師可能切開模型球，展示其核心和外層。"},{"en":"If the core is light, the ball may behave differently from a solid rubber ball.","zh":"如果核心很輕，球的表現可能與實心橡膠球不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the material inside the centre of the ball.","zh":"這個片語描述球中心內部的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"covered with cloth","meaning":"用布包着","examples":[{"en":"The cork core is covered with cloth.","zh":"軟木芯用布包着。"},{"en":"Covered with cloth means wrapped or surrounded by fabric.","zh":"Covered with cloth 指被布料包裹或覆蓋。"},{"en":"A table may be covered with cloth before a formal dinner.","zh":"正式晚餐前，桌子可能用布蓋着。"},{"en":"If the cork core is covered with cloth, the ball gains another protective layer.","zh":"如果軟木芯用布包着，球就多了一層保護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one layer placed around another material.","zh":"這個片語描述一層材料包在另一種材料外面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"tightly bound in string","meaning":"用線緊緊綁住","examples":[{"en":"The ball is tightly bound in string.","zh":"這種球用線緊緊綁住。"},{"en":"Tightly bound in string means wrapped firmly with string so it holds its shape.","zh":"Tightly bound in string 指用線牢牢包紮，使它保持形狀。"},{"en":"A parcel may be tightly bound in string before being posted.","zh":"包裹寄出前可能用線緊緊綁住。"},{"en":"If a ball is tightly bound, its layers stay compact during play.","zh":"如果球被緊緊綁住，其各層在比賽中會保持結實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes firm wrapping with string.","zh":"這個片語描述用線作牢固包裹。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"covered in felt","meaning":"外層包上毛氈","examples":[{"en":"The outside of the ball is covered in felt.","zh":"球的外層包上毛氈。"},{"en":"Covered in felt means the outer surface has a soft wool-like fabric layer.","zh":"Covered in felt 指外表有一層柔軟、像羊毛的布料。"},{"en":"A noticeboard may be covered in felt so pins can hold paper easily.","zh":"告示板可能包上毛氈，讓圖釘容易固定紙張。"},{"en":"If a ball is covered in felt, it may grip the court surface differently.","zh":"如果球包上毛氈，它可能以不同方式抓住場地表面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the soft outer covering of the ball.","zh":"這個片語描述球的柔軟外層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hand-stitched","meaning":"手工縫製的","examples":[{"en":"The balls are all hand-stitched.","zh":"這些球全都是手工縫製的。"},{"en":"Hand-stitched means sewn by people’s hands rather than by machine.","zh":"Hand-stitched 指由人手而不是機器縫製。"},{"en":"A hand-stitched bag may take longer to make but feel more carefully finished.","zh":"手工縫製的袋可能需要較長時間製作，但感覺完成得更細緻。"},{"en":"If sports balls are hand-stitched, each one may require skilled manual work.","zh":"如果運動用球是手工縫製的，每個都可能需要熟練人手。"},{"en":"This word describes traditional craft production.","zh":"這個詞描述傳統手工製作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"last about two weeks","meaning":"可用約兩星期","examples":[{"en":"The balls last about two weeks.","zh":"這些球可用約兩星期。"},{"en":"Last about two weeks means they remain usable for roughly fourteen days.","zh":"Last about two weeks 指它們大約十四天內仍可使用。"},{"en":"A phone battery may last about two days if it is used lightly.","zh":"如果輕度使用，手機電池可能可用約兩天。"},{"en":"If a ball lasts only two weeks, players need regular replacements.","zh":"如果球只可用兩星期，球手就需要定期更換。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the approximate useful life of an object.","zh":"這個片語描述物件大約的可用壽命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"throughout history","meaning":"縱觀歷史；一直以來","examples":[{"en":"This method has been used throughout history.","zh":"這種方法縱觀歷史一直被使用。"},{"en":"Throughout history means across many periods of the past.","zh":"Throughout history 指橫跨過去許多時期。"},{"en":"People have used stories to teach children throughout history.","zh":"人們縱觀歷史一直使用故事來教孩子。"},{"en":"If a method survives throughout history, it has probably been useful or practical.","zh":"如果一種方法歷史上長期保留下來，它大概有用或實際。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long-term use over many generations.","zh":"這個片語強調跨越多代人的長期使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"other substances such as","meaning":"其他物料，例如……","examples":[{"en":"Other substances such as hair or wool were used for the centre.","zh":"其他物料，例如毛髮或羊毛，曾被用作球心。"},{"en":"Other substances such as introduces additional materials or examples.","zh":"Other substances such as 用來引入額外材料或例子。"},{"en":"Art students may use other substances such as clay, fabric or recycled paper.","zh":"美術學生可能使用其他物料，例如黏土、布料或再造紙。"},{"en":"If one material is unavailable, people may use other substances to serve the same purpose.","zh":"如果一種材料不可用，人們可能使用其他物料達到同一目的。"},{"en":"This phrase gives examples without listing every possibility.","zh":"這個片語提供例子，而不是列出所有可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a good deal lighter","meaning":"輕很多","examples":[{"en":"The old balls were a good deal lighter.","zh":"舊球輕很多。"},{"en":"A good deal lighter means much lighter, not just slightly lighter.","zh":"A good deal lighter 指輕得多，不只是稍微較輕。"},{"en":"A modern laptop is a good deal lighter than many older models.","zh":"現代手提電腦比許多舊型號輕很多。"},{"en":"If a ball is much lighter, it may travel and bounce differently.","zh":"如果球輕很多，它的飛行和彈跳方式可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a noticeable difference in weight.","zh":"這個片語強調重量上的明顯差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the influence of real tennis","meaning":"真網球的影響","examples":[{"en":"The influence of real tennis can be seen in several later sports.","zh":"真網球的影響可見於幾種後來的運動。"},{"en":"The influence of real tennis means the way real tennis affected later games.","zh":"Influence of real tennis 指真網球如何影響後來的遊戲。"},{"en":"A teacher may show how an older sport influenced the rules of modern sports.","zh":"老師可能展示一項較古老運動如何影響現代運動規則。"},{"en":"If later games copy court layouts or scoring ideas, earlier influence is visible.","zh":"如果後來的遊戲借用球場佈局或計分概念，早期影響就很明顯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes historical impact from one sport to others.","zh":"這個片語描述一項運動對其他運動的歷史影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"can most clearly be seen in","meaning":"最明顯見於……","examples":[{"en":"The influence of real tennis can most clearly be seen in pelota.","zh":"真網球的影響最明顯見於 pelota。"},{"en":"Can most clearly be seen in means the example shows the influence most obviously.","zh":"Can most clearly be seen in 指某例子最明顯展示該影響。"},{"en":"A school’s values can most clearly be seen in how it treats weaker students.","zh":"學校價值最明顯見於它如何對待能力較弱的學生。"},{"en":"If one later sport shares many features with real tennis, the connection is easy to notice.","zh":"如果一項後來運動與真網球有許多共同特徵，這種連繫就容易看見。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the clearest evidence of an influence.","zh":"這個片語指出某種影響最清晰的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Basque games","meaning":"巴斯克球類遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Pelota is a group of Basque games.","zh":"Pelota 是一組巴斯克球類遊戲。"},{"en":"Basque games are games associated with the Basque people and their region.","zh":"Basque games 是與巴斯克人及其地區相關的遊戲。"},{"en":"A sports class may study Basque games to see how local culture shapes sport.","zh":"體育課可能研究巴斯克球類遊戲，以了解本地文化如何塑造運動。"},{"en":"If a game belongs to a regional tradition, its rules may reflect local history.","zh":"如果一項遊戲屬於地區傳統，其規則可能反映本地歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase connects sport with Basque cultural identity.","zh":"這個片語把運動與巴斯克文化身份連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the catchall name of","meaning":"……這個統稱","examples":[{"en":"Pelota is the catchall name for several related games.","zh":"Pelota 是幾種相關遊戲的統稱。"},{"en":"A catchall name is a general name that covers several similar things.","zh":"Catchall name 是涵蓋幾種相似事物的一般名稱。"},{"en":"“Public transport” is a catchall name for buses, trains, trams and ferries.","zh":"“Public transport” 是巴士、火車、電車和渡輪的統稱。"},{"en":"If several games are related but not identical, one catchall name can group them together.","zh":"如果幾種遊戲相關但不完全相同，一個統稱可以把它們歸在一起。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broad label for a family of things.","zh":"這個片語描述一類事物的廣泛標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"various forms of","meaning":"各種形式的……","examples":[{"en":"There are various forms of pelota.","zh":"Pelota 有各種形式。"},{"en":"Various forms of something means several different types or versions of it.","zh":"Various forms of something 指某事有幾種不同類型或版本。"},{"en":"There are various forms of online learning, including live lessons and recorded videos.","zh":"網上學習有各種形式，包括直播課堂和錄影課程。"},{"en":"If a sport has various forms, equipment and rules may differ between them.","zh":"如果一項運動有各種形式，它們之間的器材和規則可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one activity can appear in different versions.","zh":"這個片語顯示同一活動可以以不同版本出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"different types of","meaning":"不同類型的……","examples":[{"en":"Pelota uses different types of court, ball and racket.","zh":"Pelota 使用不同類型的球場、球和球拍。"},{"en":"Different types of something means more than one kind of that thing.","zh":"Different types of something 指某事物有不止一種種類。"},{"en":"A school uses different types of exercises, such as quizzes, essays and presentations.","zh":"學校使用不同類型的練習，例如小測、作文和匯報。"},{"en":"If players use different types of equipment, each version of the game may feel different.","zh":"如果玩家使用不同類型的器材，每個版本的遊戲可能感覺不同。"},{"en":"This phrase classifies things into categories.","zh":"這個片語把事物分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a basket-type racket","meaning":"籃形球拍","examples":[{"en":"Some forms of pelota still use a basket-type racket.","zh":"某些形式的 pelota 仍使用籃形球拍。"},{"en":"A basket-type racket is a curved catching or throwing tool shaped somewhat like a basket.","zh":"Basket-type racket 是一種彎曲、像籃子的接球或擲球工具。"},{"en":"A sports teacher may show a basket-type racket to explain how pelota differs from tennis.","zh":"體育老師可能展示籃形球拍，以解釋 pelota 與網球如何不同。"},{"en":"If a racket is shaped like a basket, it can catch and launch the ball differently.","zh":"如果球拍形狀像籃子，它可以以不同方式接住並發出球。"},{"en":"This phrase names a special piece of sports equipment.","zh":"這個片語命名一種特殊運動器材。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"similarities can be seen in","meaning":"相似之處可見於……","examples":[{"en":"Similarities can be seen in the court layout and rules.","zh":"相似之處可見於球場佈局和規則。"},{"en":"Similarities can be seen in means the shared features are visible in those parts.","zh":"Similarities can be seen in 指共同特徵可在那些部分看見。"},{"en":"Similarities can be seen in the uniforms of two schools if both use the same colours.","zh":"如果兩間學校的校服都使用相同顏色，相似之處可見於校服。"},{"en":"If two sports share layout and rules, historians may suspect a connection.","zh":"如果兩項運動共享佈局和規則，歷史學家可能懷疑兩者有連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase points to where resemblance appears.","zh":"這個片語指出相似之處出現在哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"court layout","meaning":"球場佈局","examples":[{"en":"The court layout of pelota shows the influence of real tennis.","zh":"Pelota 的球場佈局顯示真網球的影響。"},{"en":"Court layout means the arrangement of walls, lines, spaces and playing areas on a court.","zh":"Court layout 指球場上牆、線、空間和比賽區域的安排。"},{"en":"A basketball court layout includes lines for the centre circle and free-throw area.","zh":"籃球場佈局包括中圈和罰球區的線。"},{"en":"If the layout changes, players may need to change their movement and strategy.","zh":"如果佈局改變，球員可能需要改變移動和策略。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a sports space is physically arranged.","zh":"這個片語描述運動空間的實體安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"owe something to","meaning":"多少源自；多少受惠於","examples":[{"en":"Most racket sports owe something to real tennis.","zh":"大多數球拍運動多少受惠於真網球。"},{"en":"To owe something to something else means to have been influenced by it or developed partly from it.","zh":"To owe something to something else 指受其影響或部分由其發展而來。"},{"en":"Modern classrooms owe something to older traditions of lectures and discussion.","zh":"現代課室多少源自較古老的講課和討論傳統。"},{"en":"If a later sport borrows rules from an earlier one, it owes something to that older game.","zh":"如果後來的運動借用早期運動的規則，它就多少受惠於那項古老遊戲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes partial historical debt or influence.","zh":"這個片語描述部分歷史承繼或影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"to some extent","meaning":"在某程度上","examples":[{"en":"Most racket sports owe something to real tennis to some extent.","zh":"大多數球拍運動在某程度上都受惠於真網球。"},{"en":"To some extent means partly, but not completely.","zh":"To some extent 指部分如此，但不是完全如此。"},{"en":"Exam results reflect effort to some extent, but sleep and stress also matter.","zh":"考試成績在某程度上反映努力，但睡眠和壓力也重要。"},{"en":"If modern sports share only a few features with real tennis, the influence exists only partly.","zh":"如果現代運動只與真網球共享少數特徵，影響就只是部分存在。"},{"en":"This phrase limits a claim so it does not sound too absolute.","zh":"這個片語限制說法，令它不會顯得太絕對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"derive from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"Squash derives from a game known as rackets.","zh":"壁球源自一種名為 rackets 的遊戲。"},{"en":"To derive from something means to come from or develop from it.","zh":"To derive from something 指源自或由某事發展而來。"},{"en":"Many English words derive from Latin or French.","zh":"許多英文字源自拉丁語或法語。"},{"en":"If one sport derives from another, its rules or equipment may show traces of the older game.","zh":"如果一項運動源自另一項運動，其規則或器材可能留下舊遊戲痕跡。"},{"en":"This phrase explains origin or source.","zh":"這個片語解釋起源或來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a game known as","meaning":"一種名為……的遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Squash derives from a game known as rackets.","zh":"壁球源自一種名為 rackets 的遊戲。"},{"en":"A game known as something means a game called by that name.","zh":"A game known as something 指一種以該名稱稱呼的遊戲。"},{"en":"Chess is a board game known as one of the world’s great strategy games.","zh":"國際象棋是一種被稱為世界偉大策略遊戲之一的棋盤遊戲。"},{"en":"If readers do not know an old game, this phrase introduces its name clearly.","zh":"如果讀者不認識某種古老遊戲，這個片語可以清楚介紹其名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a named activity.","zh":"這個片語指出一項有名稱的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"debtor prisons","meaning":"債務人監獄","examples":[{"en":"Rackets was developed in the debtor prisons of Britain.","zh":"Rackets 在英國的債務人監獄中發展出來。"},{"en":"Debtor prisons were prisons where people could be held because they owed money.","zh":"Debtor prisons 是人們因欠債而可能被關押的監獄。"},{"en":"In history lessons, debtor prisons show how harsh old debt laws could be.","zh":"在歷史課中，債務人監獄顯示舊債務法律可以多嚴苛。"},{"en":"If a game developed in debtor prisons, its early players were not nobles but confined debtors.","zh":"如果一項遊戲在債務人監獄中發展，其早期玩家不是貴族，而是被監禁的債務人。"},{"en":"This phrase names a historical institution linked to debt punishment.","zh":"這個片語命名與債務懲罰相關的歷史機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"17th- and 18th-century Britain","meaning":"十七及十八世紀的英國","examples":[{"en":"Rackets was developed in 17th- and 18th-century Britain.","zh":"Rackets 在十七及十八世紀的英國發展出來。"},{"en":"17th- and 18th-century Britain means Britain during the 1600s and 1700s.","zh":"17th- and 18th-century Britain 指1600年代和1700年代的英國。"},{"en":"A history project on 18th-century Britain may discuss prisons, trade and social class.","zh":"關於十八世紀英國的歷史專題可能討論監獄、貿易和社會階級。"},{"en":"If a sport developed in that period, its origins belong to early modern Britain.","zh":"如果一項運動在該時期發展，其起源就屬於近代早期英國。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event in a particular historical period and country.","zh":"這個片語把事件放在特定歷史時期和國家中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"of one kind or another","meaning":"某種形式的……","examples":[{"en":"Tennis of one kind or another has been played in France for centuries.","zh":"某種形式的網球在法國已經玩了數百年。"},{"en":"Of one kind or another means in some form, though the exact type may vary.","zh":"Of one kind or another 指以某種形式存在，雖然具體類型可能不同。"},{"en":"Students have used notes of one kind or another for generations.","zh":"學生幾代以來都使用某種形式的筆記。"},{"en":"If a sport exists in many changing forms, this phrase avoids naming every version.","zh":"如果一項運動以許多變化形式存在，這個片語可避免逐一命名。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broad category with different variations.","zh":"這個片語描述包含不同變體的廣泛類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as far back as","meaning":"早於……","examples":[{"en":"Tennis was played in France as far back as the 12th century.","zh":"網球早於十二世紀已在法國被玩。"},{"en":"As far back as means as early as a surprisingly old time.","zh":"As far back as 指早在一個令人意外的古老時間。"},{"en":"The school has records as far back as the 19th century.","zh":"學校有早於十九世紀的紀錄。"},{"en":"If evidence goes back many centuries, the tradition is older than many people expect.","zh":"如果證據可追溯到多個世紀以前，該傳統就比許多人想像更古老。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises historical depth.","zh":"這個片語強調歷史深度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the late nineteenth century","meaning":"十九世紀末","examples":[{"en":"Lawn tennis became popular in the late nineteenth century.","zh":"草地網球在十九世紀末變得流行。"},{"en":"The late nineteenth century means the later part of the 1800s.","zh":"The late nineteenth century 指1800年代後期。"},{"en":"Many modern sports clubs began in the late nineteenth century.","zh":"許多現代體育會在十九世紀末開始。"},{"en":"If a sport became popular then, it spread during a period of organised leisure and clubs.","zh":"如果一項運動在當時變得流行，它是在有組織休閒和會所興起的時期傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event near the end of the 19th century.","zh":"這個片語把事件放在十九世紀接近末期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"became popular","meaning":"變得流行","examples":[{"en":"Lawn tennis became popular in the late nineteenth century.","zh":"草地網球在十九世紀末變得流行。"},{"en":"Became popular means started to be liked or played by many people.","zh":"Became popular 指開始被很多人喜歡或參與。"},{"en":"Bubble tea became popular when many young people began sharing it online.","zh":"當許多年輕人在網上分享珍珠奶茶，它就變得流行。"},{"en":"If a sport becomes popular, more clubs, courts and competitions usually appear.","zh":"如果一項運動變得流行，通常會出現更多會所、球場和比賽。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth in public interest.","zh":"這個片語描述公眾興趣的增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in search of","meaning":"尋找……","examples":[{"en":"Major Walter Wingfield was in search of a more vigorous game than croquet.","zh":"Walter Wingfield 少校正在尋找一種比槌球更有活力的遊戲。"},{"en":"In search of means looking for something.","zh":"In search of 指正在尋找某物。"},{"en":"A student may visit the library in search of examples for an essay.","zh":"學生可能到圖書館尋找作文例子。"},{"en":"If someone is in search of a better activity, they are dissatisfied with the current option.","zh":"如果某人正在尋找更好的活動，他對現有選項並不滿足。"},{"en":"This phrase describes purposeful looking.","zh":"這個片語描述有目的的尋找。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a more vigorous game","meaning":"更有活力的遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Wingfield wanted a more vigorous game than croquet.","zh":"Wingfield 想要一種比槌球更有活力的遊戲。"},{"en":"A more vigorous game is a game requiring more movement, energy or physical effort.","zh":"A more vigorous game 是需要更多移動、能量或體力的遊戲。"},{"en":"Some students prefer basketball because it is more vigorous than board games.","zh":"有些學生較喜歡籃球，因為它比棋盤遊戲更有活力。"},{"en":"If an activity is too slow, players may look for a more active alternative.","zh":"如果活動太慢，玩家可能尋找更活躍的替代選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts energetic sport with gentler leisure.","zh":"這個片語把充滿活力的運動與較溫和的休閒活動作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the leisure classes","meaning":"有閒階級","examples":[{"en":"Croquet was popular among the leisure classes.","zh":"槌球在有閒階級中很流行。"},{"en":"The leisure classes were people wealthy enough to have free time for recreation.","zh":"The leisure classes 指富裕到有閒暇時間進行娛樂活動的人。"},{"en":"In Victorian Britain, the leisure classes often played sports in gardens and clubs.","zh":"在維多利亞時代英國，有閒階級常在花園和會所玩運動。"},{"en":"If a game requires time, space and equipment, it may first spread among the leisure classes.","zh":"如果一項遊戲需要時間、空間和器材，它可能先在有閒階級中傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people whose social position allowed regular leisure.","zh":"這個片語描述社會地位容許經常休閒的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"devise an activity","meaning":"設計一項活動","examples":[{"en":"Wingfield devised an activity that combined badminton and real tennis.","zh":"Wingfield 設計了一項結合羽毛球和真網球的活動。"},{"en":"To devise an activity means to design or invent a planned activity.","zh":"To devise an activity 指設計或創造一項有規劃的活動。"},{"en":"A teacher may devise an activity that helps students practise speaking naturally.","zh":"老師可能設計一項活動，幫助學生自然練習說話。"},{"en":"If existing games feel unsuitable, someone may devise a new version.","zh":"如果現有遊戲不合適，有人可能設計一個新版本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating a structured activity through thought and planning.","zh":"這個片語描述透過思考和規劃創造有結構的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a hybrid of","meaning":"……的混合體","examples":[{"en":"Sphairistike was a hybrid of badminton and real tennis.","zh":"Sphairistike 是羽毛球和真網球的混合體。"},{"en":"A hybrid of two things is something that combines features of both.","zh":"A hybrid of two things 是結合兩者特徵的東西。"},{"en":"A café-library is a hybrid of a reading space and a coffee shop.","zh":"咖啡圖書館是閱讀空間和咖啡店的混合體。"},{"en":"If a game borrows from two sports, players may recognise elements of both.","zh":"如果一項遊戲借用兩項運動的元素，玩家可能認出兩者特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mixed form.","zh":"這個片語描述混合形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Greek for","meaning":"希臘語中指","examples":[{"en":"Sphairistike was Greek for ball games.","zh":"Sphairistike 是希臘語中指球類遊戲的詞。"},{"en":"Greek for something means the Greek word or phrase meaning that thing.","zh":"Greek for something 指希臘語中表示某事物的詞或片語。"},{"en":"Biology comes partly from Greek for life and study.","zh":"Biology 部分來自希臘語中表示生命和研究的詞。"},{"en":"If a sport uses a Greek name, the inventor may want it to sound classical or learned.","zh":"如果一項運動使用希臘名稱，發明者可能想令它聽起來古典或有學問。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the meaning of a word by reference to Greek.","zh":"這個片語透過希臘語解釋詞義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"later to be known as","meaning":"後來被稱為","examples":[{"en":"The All England Club held a tournament later to be known as Wimbledon.","zh":"All England Club 舉辦了一項後來被稱為 Wimbledon 的錦標賽。"},{"en":"Later to be known as means it received that famous name after the earlier event.","zh":"Later to be known as 指該事物在早期事件後得到那個著名名稱。"},{"en":"A small school competition may later be known as a major annual festival.","zh":"一項小型學校比賽後來可能被稱為大型年度節日。"},{"en":"If an event grows in importance, its later name may become more famous than its original one.","zh":"如果一項活動重要性增加，其後來名稱可能比原名更有名。"},{"en":"This phrase links an early beginning with a later recognised name.","zh":"這個片語把早期開始與後來被認可的名稱連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hold a tournament","meaning":"舉辦錦標賽","examples":[{"en":"The All England Club held a tournament in 1877.","zh":"All England Club 在1877年舉辦錦標賽。"},{"en":"To hold a tournament means to organise a formal competition.","zh":"To hold a tournament 指組織正式比賽。"},{"en":"A school may hold a chess tournament after exams.","zh":"學校可能在考試後舉辦象棋錦標賽。"},{"en":"If a club holds a tournament, players gather to compete under agreed rules.","zh":"如果會所舉辦錦標賽，球手會聚集並按共同規則比賽。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organising a competitive event.","zh":"這個片語描述組織競賽活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be modified from","meaning":"從……修改而成","examples":[{"en":"The game was modified from Wingfield’s original rules.","zh":"這項遊戲從 Wingfield 的原始規則修改而成。"},{"en":"To be modified from something means to be changed from an earlier version.","zh":"To be modified from something 指由較早版本改變而來。"},{"en":"A school worksheet may be modified from last year’s exam paper.","zh":"學校工作紙可能從去年的試卷修改而成。"},{"en":"If original rules are impractical, later players may modify them.","zh":"如果原始規則不實際，後來玩家可能修改它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adaptation from an earlier model.","zh":"這個片語描述由早期模式作出調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"prescriptions laid out by","meaning":"由……訂下的規定","examples":[{"en":"The rules were modified from the prescriptions laid out by Major Wingfield.","zh":"這些規則是從 Wingfield 少校訂下的規定修改而成。"},{"en":"Prescriptions laid out by someone are detailed rules or instructions set by that person.","zh":"Prescriptions laid out by someone 是由某人訂下的詳細規則或指示。"},{"en":"A teacher may follow the marking prescriptions laid out by an exam board.","zh":"老師可能遵循考試局訂下的評分規定。"},{"en":"If later players changed Wingfield’s prescriptions, the modern game became less like his first design.","zh":"如果後來玩家改變 Wingfield 的規定，現代遊戲就變得較不像他的最初設計。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal instructions provided earlier.","zh":"這個片語指早前提供的正式指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"For instance, Wingfield wanted the court to be shaped like an hourglass.","zh":"例如，Wingfield 希望球場呈沙漏形。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"For instance 指例如。"},{"en":"Some sports changed their equipment; for instance, tennis rackets moved from wood to modern materials.","zh":"有些運動改變了器材；例如，網球拍由木製轉向現代材料。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to make a general point clearer with a specific example.","zh":"作者使用這個片語，以具體例子令一般觀點更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces evidence or illustration.","zh":"這個片語引出證據或例證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"call for","meaning":"要求；規定","examples":[{"en":"Wingfield’s rules called for an hourglass-shaped court.","zh":"Wingfield 的規則要求使用沙漏形球場。"},{"en":"To call for something means to require or demand it.","zh":"To call for something 指要求或規定某事。"},{"en":"The recipe calls for two eggs and a cup of flour.","zh":"這個食譜要求兩隻雞蛋和一杯麵粉。"},{"en":"If rules call for a special court shape, players must build the court accordingly.","zh":"如果規則要求特殊球場形狀，玩家就必須相應建造球場。"},{"en":"This phrase states what is required.","zh":"這個片語說明所需條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the shape of","meaning":"呈……形狀","examples":[{"en":"The court was in the shape of an hourglass.","zh":"球場呈沙漏形狀。"},{"en":"In the shape of means having the form or outline of something.","zh":"In the shape of 指具有某物的形式或輪廓。"},{"en":"A birthday cake may be made in the shape of a football.","zh":"生日蛋糕可能做成足球形狀。"},{"en":"If a court is in an unusual shape, movement and strategy may be affected.","zh":"如果球場形狀不尋常，移動和策略可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical form.","zh":"這個片語描述實體形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"an hourglass","meaning":"沙漏","examples":[{"en":"Wingfield’s original court was shaped like an hourglass.","zh":"Wingfield 的原始球場形狀像沙漏。"},{"en":"An hourglass is an old timing device with sand flowing through a narrow middle.","zh":"Hourglass 是一種舊式計時工具，沙會從狹窄中部流過。"},{"en":"A teacher may use an hourglass to time a short classroom activity.","zh":"老師可能用沙漏為短課堂活動計時。"},{"en":"If something is hourglass-shaped, it is wider at both ends and narrower in the middle.","zh":"如果某物呈沙漏形，它兩端較寬，中間較窄。"},{"en":"This word helps readers imagine the proposed court shape.","zh":"這個詞幫助讀者想像所提出的球場形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a rectangular court","meaning":"長方形球場","examples":[{"en":"Soon the game was played on a rectangular court.","zh":"很快，這項遊戲改在長方形球場上進行。"},{"en":"A rectangular court is a playing area with four straight sides and right angles.","zh":"Rectangular court 是有四條直邊和直角的比賽區域。"},{"en":"Basketball and tennis are both played on rectangular courts.","zh":"籃球和網球都在長方形球場上進行。"},{"en":"If the court becomes rectangular, rules and movement may become simpler to standardise.","zh":"如果球場變成長方形，規則和移動可能更容易標準化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the familiar modern court shape.","zh":"這個片語描述熟悉的現代球場形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"changes in the quality and type of","meaning":"……的質素和種類上的轉變","examples":[{"en":"There have been changes in the quality and type of clothing and equipment used.","zh":"使用的服裝和器材在質素和種類上都有轉變。"},{"en":"Changes in the quality and type of something means both how good it is and what kind it is have changed.","zh":"Changes in the quality and type of something 指某物的好壞程度和種類都發生改變。"},{"en":"Schools may see changes in the quality and type of technology students use.","zh":"學校可能看到學生使用科技的質素和種類上的轉變。"},{"en":"If materials improve, equipment may become lighter, stronger or safer.","zh":"如果材料改善，器材可能變得更輕、更堅固或更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improvement or variation in both standard and category.","zh":"這個片語描述標準和類別上的改善或變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a radical idea","meaning":"激進的想法","examples":[{"en":"In the early twentieth century, shorts were a radical idea.","zh":"在二十世紀初，短褲是一個激進的想法。"},{"en":"A radical idea is an idea that seems very new, bold or different from accepted practice.","zh":"Radical idea 是看起來非常新、大膽或不同於既有做法的想法。"},{"en":"Allowing students to choose their own projects may once have seemed like a radical idea.","zh":"讓學生選擇自己的專題，可能曾經看起來像激進想法。"},{"en":"If clothing rules are strict, even a small change can look radical at first.","zh":"如果服裝規則嚴格，即使小改變一開始也可能顯得激進。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an idea that challenges tradition.","zh":"這個片語描述挑戰傳統的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the last few decades","meaning":"過去數十年","examples":[{"en":"Racket materials have changed greatly in the last few decades.","zh":"球拍材料在過去數十年大幅改變。"},{"en":"The last few decades means the most recent several periods of ten years.","zh":"The last few decades 指最近幾個十年。"},{"en":"Mobile phones have changed greatly in the last few decades.","zh":"手提電話在過去數十年大幅改變。"},{"en":"If equipment changes over recent decades, modern players may use very different tools from older players.","zh":"如果器材在近數十年改變，現代球手可能使用與舊球手非常不同的工具。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to recent long-term change.","zh":"這個片語指近期的長期變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"radically changed","meaning":"徹底改變","examples":[{"en":"Racket materials have radically changed.","zh":"球拍材料已經徹底改變。"},{"en":"Radically changed means changed deeply or completely, not just slightly.","zh":"Radically changed 指深層或完全改變，而不只是輕微改變。"},{"en":"Online learning radically changed how some students attend lessons.","zh":"網上學習徹底改變了一些學生上課的方式。"},{"en":"If rackets move from wood to advanced compounds, equipment has changed radically.","zh":"如果球拍從木製轉向先進複合材料，器材就是徹底改變了。"},{"en":"This phrase describes major transformation.","zh":"這個片語描述重大轉化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"graphite and other compounds","meaning":"石墨及其他複合材料","examples":[{"en":"Modern rackets use graphite and other compounds.","zh":"現代球拍使用石墨及其他複合材料。"},{"en":"Graphite and other compounds are modern materials used to make rackets lighter and stronger.","zh":"Graphite and other compounds 是用來令球拍更輕和更堅固的現代材料。"},{"en":"A sports shop may explain that graphite rackets are easier to swing than wooden ones.","zh":"體育用品店可能解釋石墨球拍比木製球拍更容易揮動。"},{"en":"If equipment uses advanced compounds, performance and durability may improve.","zh":"如果器材使用先進複合材料，表現和耐用度可能改善。"},{"en":"This phrase names modern racket materials.","zh":"這個片語命名現代球拍材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"wooden rackets","meaning":"木製球拍","examples":[{"en":"Wooden rackets are now an anachronism.","zh":"木製球拍現在已是過時事物。"},{"en":"Wooden rackets are rackets made mainly from wood rather than modern synthetic materials.","zh":"Wooden rackets 是主要由木材而非現代合成材料製成的球拍。"},{"en":"A museum may display wooden rackets to show how tennis equipment used to look.","zh":"博物館可能展示木製球拍，顯示網球器材過去的樣子。"},{"en":"If modern rackets are lighter and stronger, wooden rackets may disappear from professional play.","zh":"如果現代球拍更輕更強，木製球拍可能從職業比賽中消失。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to traditional sports equipment from an earlier era.","zh":"這個片語指較早時代的傳統運動器材。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an anachronism","meaning":"過時的事物","examples":[{"en":"Wooden rackets are now an anachronism.","zh":"木製球拍現在已是過時的事物。"},{"en":"An anachronism is something that seems old-fashioned or out of place in the present.","zh":"An anachronism 是在現代顯得過時或不合時宜的東西。"},{"en":"Using a typewriter in a modern office may feel like an anachronism.","zh":"在現代辦公室使用打字機可能像過時事物。"},{"en":"If equipment belongs to an older era, it may look strange beside modern technology.","zh":"如果器材屬於較舊時代，它在現代科技旁可能顯得奇怪。"},{"en":"This word describes something that no longer fits its time.","zh":"這個詞描述不再符合其時代的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"to the lament of","meaning":"令……惋惜的是","examples":[{"en":"Wooden rackets have disappeared, to the lament of the purists.","zh":"木製球拍已經消失，令純粹主義者惋惜。"},{"en":"To the lament of someone means making that group feel regret or sadness.","zh":"To the lament of someone 指令某群人感到遺憾或傷感。"},{"en":"The old school garden was replaced by a car park, to the lament of former students.","zh":"舊學校花園被停車場取代，令舊生惋惜。"},{"en":"If traditional equipment disappears, purists may feel that part of the sport’s soul has gone.","zh":"如果傳統器材消失，純粹主義者可能覺得運動的一部分靈魂也消失了。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces who regrets a change.","zh":"這個片語引出誰對改變感到惋惜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"purists","meaning":"純粹主義者；正統派","examples":[{"en":"Purists regret the disappearance of wooden rackets.","zh":"純粹主義者對木製球拍的消失感到惋惜。"},{"en":"Purists are people who want to preserve the traditional or original form of something.","zh":"Purists 是想保存某事傳統或原始形式的人。"},{"en":"Language purists may dislike new slang or borrowed words.","zh":"語言純粹主義者可能不喜歡新俚語或外來詞。"},{"en":"If a sport changes too much, purists may argue that its old character is being lost.","zh":"如果一項運動改變太多，正統派可能認為其舊特色正在消失。"},{"en":"This word describes defenders of tradition and original standards.","zh":"這個詞描述維護傳統和原始標準的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a real tennis circuit","meaning":"真網球巡迴賽","examples":[{"en":"Nowadays there is a real tennis circuit as there is for lawn tennis.","zh":"如今真網球也像草地網球一樣有巡迴賽。"},{"en":"A real tennis circuit is a series of organised competitions for real tennis players.","zh":"Real tennis circuit 是為真網球球手組織的一系列比賽。"},{"en":"Professional players may travel from one court to another as part of a tournament circuit.","zh":"職業球手可能作為巡迴賽一部分，從一個球場到另一個球場比賽。"},{"en":"If a sport has a circuit, it has become organised beyond casual local play.","zh":"如果一項運動有巡迴賽，它就不只是本地休閒遊戲，而是變得有組織。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the competitive structure of modern real tennis.","zh":"這個片語描述現代真網球的競賽結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"top professionals","meaning":"頂尖職業球手","examples":[{"en":"The top professionals in real tennis are extremely fit and skilled.","zh":"真網球的頂尖職業球手非常健壯且技術高超。"},{"en":"Top professionals are the best paid or highest-level players in a sport.","zh":"Top professionals 是一項運動中最高水平或最頂尖的職業球手。"},{"en":"Top professionals often train daily and travel for major competitions.","zh":"頂尖職業球手通常每日訓練並四處參加大型比賽。"},{"en":"If players reach the top professional level, they need both technique and physical strength.","zh":"如果球手達到頂尖職業水平，他們需要技術和體能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes elite athletes in a sport.","zh":"這個片語描述一項運動中的精英運動員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as fit and skilled as","meaning":"與……一樣健壯和技術高超","examples":[{"en":"Real tennis professionals are as fit and skilled as their lawn tennis counterparts.","zh":"真網球職業球手與草地網球同行一樣健壯和技術高超。"},{"en":"As fit and skilled as means equal in physical condition and ability.","zh":"As fit and skilled as 指在身體狀態和能力上相等。"},{"en":"A school basketball team may be as fit and skilled as teams from larger schools.","zh":"學校籃球隊可能與大型學校的隊伍一樣健壯和技術高超。"},{"en":"If one group is less famous but equally capable, this phrase helps make the comparison fair.","zh":"如果一個群體較不知名但能力相等，這個片語有助作出公平比較。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two groups as equal in ability.","zh":"這個片語比較兩個群體在能力上相等。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"counterparts","meaning":"對應的人；同類同行","examples":[{"en":"Real tennis players are less famous than their lawn tennis counterparts.","zh":"真網球球手比他們的草地網球同行較不出名。"},{"en":"Counterparts are people or things with similar roles in a different group or context.","zh":"Counterparts 是在不同群體或語境中擁有相似角色的人或事物。"},{"en":"A school principal may meet counterparts from other schools to share ideas.","zh":"校長可能與其他學校的同類同行見面交流想法。"},{"en":"If two sports have professional players, the players can be called counterparts.","zh":"如果兩項運動都有職業球手，這些球手可稱為 counterparts。"},{"en":"This word helps compare equivalent people or roles.","zh":"這個詞幫助比較對等的人或角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"if not as famous and well paid","meaning":"即使沒有那麼有名和高薪","examples":[{"en":"They are highly skilled, if not as famous and well paid.","zh":"他們技術高超，即使沒有那麼有名和高薪。"},{"en":"If not as famous and well paid means although they may not have the same fame or salary.","zh":"If not as famous and well paid 指雖然他們可能沒有同等名氣或薪酬。"},{"en":"Nurses are highly valuable, if not as publicly celebrated as famous doctors.","zh":"護士非常有價值，即使不像著名醫生那樣受到公開讚揚。"},{"en":"This phrase recognises ability while admitting a difference in recognition or money.","zh":"這個片語承認能力，同時承認名氣或金錢上的差異。"},{"en":"It is useful when one group deserves respect despite receiving less attention.","zh":"當某群體雖較少受到注意但仍值得尊重時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"travel round the world","meaning":"周遊世界","examples":[{"en":"Professional players travel round the world for competitions.","zh":"職業球手為比賽周遊世界。"},{"en":"To travel round the world means to visit many different countries or regions internationally.","zh":"To travel round the world 指到訪許多不同國家或地區。"},{"en":"A musician may travel round the world to perform in concerts.","zh":"音樂人可能為舉行音樂會而周遊世界。"},{"en":"If a sport has global competitions, its best players may spend much of the year travelling.","zh":"如果一項運動有全球比賽，頂尖球手可能一年大部分時間都在旅途中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wide international movement.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛的國際流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"top competitions","meaning":"頂級比賽","examples":[{"en":"The players take part in the top competitions.","zh":"球手參加頂級比賽。"},{"en":"Top competitions are the most important or highest-level events in a sport.","zh":"Top competitions 是一項運動中最重要或最高水平的賽事。"},{"en":"A swimmer may train for years to enter top competitions.","zh":"游泳運動員可能訓練多年，以參加頂級比賽。"},{"en":"If players compete at top events, their skill level must be very high.","zh":"如果球手參加頂級賽事，他們的技術水平必須很高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes elite competitive events.","zh":"這個片語描述精英級競賽活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"look after their home courts","meaning":"照料；管理自己的主場球場","examples":[{"en":"Players also look after their home courts.","zh":"球手也照料自己的主場球場。"},{"en":"To look after their home courts means to care for, manage or maintain the courts where they are based.","zh":"To look after their home courts 指照顧、管理或維護他們所在的球場。"},{"en":"A school team may look after its home court by cleaning it after practice.","zh":"學校隊伍可能在練習後清潔球場，以照料自己的主場。"},{"en":"If courts require special maintenance, players may have responsibilities beyond playing matches.","zh":"如果球場需要特殊維護，球手可能有比比賽更多的責任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical care for sports facilities.","zh":"這個片語描述對運動設施的實際照顧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at a higher standard than","meaning":"達到比……更高的水平","examples":[{"en":"Real tennis is now played at a higher standard than before.","zh":"真網球現在達到比以前更高的水平。"},{"en":"At a higher standard than means at a better level of quality or skill than another time or group.","zh":"At a higher standard than 指比另一時間或群體有更好質素或技術水平。"},{"en":"Students may write at a higher standard than last term after receiving feedback.","zh":"學生在收到回饋後，寫作可能達到比上學期更高的水平。"},{"en":"If training improves, players can perform at a higher standard.","zh":"如果訓練改善，球手可以以更高水平表現。"},{"en":"This phrase compares quality or skill level.","zh":"這個片語比較質素或技術水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at any other time in its history","meaning":"在其歷史上的任何其他時期","examples":[{"en":"The sport may now be played better than at any other time in its history.","zh":"這項運動現在的水平可能比其歷史上的任何其他時期都高。"},{"en":"At any other time in its history means during any previous period of the sport’s existence.","zh":"At any other time in its history 指在該運動存在以來的任何以前時期。"},{"en":"A school may have better exam results now than at any other time in its history.","zh":"一間學校現在的考試成績可能比其歷史上的任何其他時期都好。"},{"en":"If current players are the strongest ever, the modern period becomes a peak moment.","zh":"如果現代球手是歷來最強，現代時期就成為高峰時刻。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the present with the whole past.","zh":"這個片語把現在與整個過去作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a renaissance in","meaning":"……的復興","examples":[{"en":"In the mid-nineteenth century, there was a renaissance in tennis.","zh":"在十九世紀中期，網球出現復興。"},{"en":"A renaissance in something is a revival or renewed interest after decline.","zh":"Renaissance in something 是某事衰落後重新興起或受到關注。"},{"en":"A town may see a renaissance in local crafts when young people learn old skills again.","zh":"當年輕人重新學習舊技藝，城鎮可能出現本地手工藝復興。"},{"en":"If new courts are built and more people play, a sport may experience a renaissance.","zh":"如果新球場興建且更多人參與，一項運動可能經歷復興。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a return of energy and popularity.","zh":"這個片語描述活力和受歡迎程度的回歸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a flurry of","meaning":"一連串；大量","examples":[{"en":"There was a flurry of court construction.","zh":"當時出現一連串球場建設。"},{"en":"A flurry of something means a sudden burst of many related activities.","zh":"A flurry of something 指突然出現大量相關活動。"},{"en":"There was a flurry of messages after the exam timetable was announced.","zh":"考試時間表公布後，出現一連串訊息。"},{"en":"If many courts are built quickly, the sport is probably gaining momentum.","zh":"如果許多球場快速興建，這項運動大概正在 gaining momentum。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a short period of busy activity.","zh":"這個片語描述一段短時間內的繁忙活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"court construction","meaning":"球場建設","examples":[{"en":"A flurry of court construction took place in the mid-nineteenth century.","zh":"十九世紀中期出現一連串球場建設。"},{"en":"Court construction means the building of sports courts.","zh":"Court construction 指建造運動球場。"},{"en":"A school may plan court construction if many students want to play basketball.","zh":"如果許多學生想打籃球，學校可能規劃球場建設。"},{"en":"If court construction is expensive, only well-funded clubs may be able to expand.","zh":"如果球場建設昂貴，只有資金充足的會所可能能擴展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical building of playing facilities.","zh":"這個片語描述比賽設施的實體建造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cut short","meaning":"使……提早中止","examples":[{"en":"The First World War cut short tennis’s re-emergence.","zh":"第一次世界大戰使網球的重新興起提早中止。"},{"en":"To cut short something means to stop it earlier than expected.","zh":"To cut short something 指令某事比預期更早停止。"},{"en":"Heavy rain cut short the school sports day.","zh":"大雨使學校運動會提早中止。"},{"en":"If war interrupts a revival, growth may stop before it fully develops.","zh":"如果戰爭打斷復興，增長可能在完全發展前停止。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an early ending caused by an outside event.","zh":"這個片語描述由外部事件造成的提早結束。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"re-emergence","meaning":"重新興起","examples":[{"en":"The war interrupted tennis’s re-emergence.","zh":"戰爭打斷了網球的重新興起。"},{"en":"Re-emergence means appearing or becoming active again after a period of decline or absence.","zh":"Re-emergence 指在衰落或消失一段時間後重新出現或活躍起來。"},{"en":"The re-emergence of vinyl records surprised many music shops.","zh":"黑膠唱片的重新興起令許多唱片店驚訝。"},{"en":"If a sport gains new players after years of low interest, it is re-emerging.","zh":"如果一項運動多年低迷後獲得新玩家，它就是正在重新興起。"},{"en":"This word describes a return after disappearing or weakening.","zh":"這個詞描述消失或轉弱後的回歸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"over the last 25 years","meaning":"在過去二十五年間","examples":[{"en":"Over the last 25 years, real tennis has begun to grow again.","zh":"在過去二十五年間，真網球開始再次增長。"},{"en":"Over the last 25 years means during the most recent twenty-five-year period.","zh":"Over the last 25 years 指在最近二十五年期間。"},{"en":"Over the last 25 years, mobile technology has changed how students learn.","zh":"在過去二十五年間，流動科技改變了學生學習方式。"},{"en":"If a sport grows over twenty-five years, the change is gradual but meaningful.","zh":"如果一項運動在二十五年間增長，變化是逐步但有意義的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a long recent time span.","zh":"這個片語描述較長的近期時間跨度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the high cost of building courts","meaning":"建造球場的高昂成本","examples":[{"en":"The high cost of building courts inhibits growth.","zh":"建造球場的高昂成本阻礙發展。"},{"en":"The high cost of building courts means courts require a lot of money to construct.","zh":"The high cost of building courts 指建造球場需要大量金錢。"},{"en":"A small school may delay building a new sports court because of high construction costs.","zh":"小型學校可能因建造成本高昂而延遲興建新運動場。"},{"en":"If facilities are expensive, fewer communities can afford to support the sport.","zh":"如果設施昂貴，較少社區能負擔支持這項運動。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a financial barrier to expansion.","zh":"這個片語解釋擴展上的金錢障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"inhibit growth","meaning":"抑制增長；阻礙發展","examples":[{"en":"High construction costs inhibit growth.","zh":"高昂建造成本抑制增長。"},{"en":"To inhibit growth means to slow down or prevent development.","zh":"To inhibit growth 指拖慢或阻止發展。"},{"en":"Lack of practice can inhibit a student’s progress in speaking.","zh":"缺乏練習可以阻礙學生口語進步。"},{"en":"If a sport lacks affordable courts, its number of players may grow slowly.","zh":"如果一項運動缺乏可負擔球場，其球手數量可能增長緩慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something holding development back.","zh":"這個片語描述某事阻礙發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"springing up","meaning":"不斷湧現","examples":[{"en":"New courts have been springing up in several countries.","zh":"新球場在幾個國家不斷湧現。"},{"en":"Springing up means appearing suddenly or quickly in several places.","zh":"Springing up 指在幾個地方突然或快速出現。"},{"en":"New coffee shops have been springing up near the station.","zh":"新咖啡店在車站附近不斷湧現。"},{"en":"If new courts are springing up, interest in the sport is probably increasing.","zh":"如果新球場不斷湧現，這項運動的興趣大概正在增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fresh growth or appearance.","zh":"這個片語描述新的增長或出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"talk of court construction","meaning":"有關興建球場的討論","examples":[{"en":"There is talk of court construction in Holland, Russia and South Africa.","zh":"荷蘭、俄羅斯和南非有關興建球場的討論。"},{"en":"Talk of court construction means people are discussing plans or possibilities for building courts.","zh":"Talk of court construction 指人們正在討論建造球場的計劃或可能性。"},{"en":"There may be talk of a new school hall before the budget is confirmed.","zh":"在預算確認前，可能會有興建新學校禮堂的討論。"},{"en":"If there is talk of building courts in new countries, the sport may be spreading.","zh":"如果在新國家有關興建球場的討論，這項運動可能正在傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase describes discussion before action is certain.","zh":"這個片語描述行動確定前的討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the future looks bright","meaning":"前景看好","examples":[{"en":"The future again looks bright for real tennis.","zh":"真網球的前景再次看好。"},{"en":"The future looks bright means the future seems hopeful or promising.","zh":"The future looks bright 指未來看起來有希望或有前途。"},{"en":"After better exam results and more enrolment, the future looks bright for the school.","zh":"在考試成績改善和收生增加後，學校前景看好。"},{"en":"If new courts and new players appear, a sport’s future may look positive.","zh":"如果新球場和新球手出現，一項運動的未來可能看起來正面。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses optimism about what may happen next.","zh":"這個片語表達對未來發展的樂觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"from the list of headings below","meaning":"從以下標題列表中","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the most suitable headings from the list of headings below.","zh":"學生從以下標題列表中選擇最合適標題。"},{"en":"From the list of headings below means answers must be selected from the headings printed underneath the instruction.","zh":"From the list of headings below 指答案必須從指示下方列出的標題中選擇。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should scan all headings before matching them to paragraphs.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先掃讀所有標題，再把它們配對段落。"},{"en":"If the list contains extra headings, students must reject options that only partly fit.","zh":"如果列表包含額外標題，學生必須排除只部分合適的選項。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in heading-matching tasks.","zh":"這個片語是標題配對題中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the most suitable headings","meaning":"最合適的標題","examples":[{"en":"The task asks students to choose the most suitable headings for the paragraphs.","zh":"題目要求學生為段落選擇最合適的標題。"},{"en":"The most suitable headings are the titles that best summarise the main ideas.","zh":"The most suitable headings 是最能概括主旨的標題。"},{"en":"Students should choose a heading that matches the whole paragraph, not just one word.","zh":"學生應選擇配合整段的標題，而不只是配合一個字。"},{"en":"If a heading is too narrow, it may not be the most suitable one.","zh":"如果標題太狹窄，它可能不是最合適的一個。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the best overall match.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於整體上最好的配對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the appropriate number","meaning":"適當的編號","examples":[{"en":"Students write the appropriate number in each box.","zh":"學生在每個方格中寫上適當的編號。"},{"en":"The appropriate number is the number that correctly matches the chosen answer.","zh":"The appropriate number 是與所選答案正確配對的編號。"},{"en":"In a heading task, students may write roman numerals or numbers in the answer boxes.","zh":"在標題題中，學生可能要在答案框寫羅馬數字或編號。"},{"en":"If students choose the right heading but write the wrong number, the answer becomes wrong.","zh":"如果學生選對標題卻寫錯編號，答案就變錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction about recording answers accurately.","zh":"這個片語是關於準確記錄答案的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"more headings than paragraphs","meaning":"標題比段落多","examples":[{"en":"There are more headings than paragraphs in the question.","zh":"題目中的標題比段落多。"},{"en":"More headings than paragraphs means some heading options will not be used.","zh":"More headings than paragraphs 指有些標題選項不會被使用。"},{"en":"In reading exams, extra headings are included to test careful understanding.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，額外標題用來測試細心理解。"},{"en":"If there are more headings than paragraphs, students should not try to use every heading.","zh":"如果標題比段落多，學生不應試圖每個標題都用上。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that the task contains distractors.","zh":"這個片語提醒題目包含干擾項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"you will not use them all","meaning":"你不會全部用上","examples":[{"en":"There are extra options, so students will not use them all.","zh":"題目有額外選項，所以學生不會全部用上。"},{"en":"You will not use them all means some choices are not needed for the answers.","zh":"You will not use them all 指有些選項不需要用作答案。"},{"en":"In a vocabulary list with ten words and six blanks, students will not use them all.","zh":"如果詞彙列表有十個詞而空格只有六個，學生不會全部用上。"},{"en":"If students try to use every option, they may force wrong answers into the task.","zh":"如果學生試圖用盡所有選項，可能把錯誤答案硬放進題目。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds learners to select carefully.","zh":"這個片語提醒學習者仔細選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the Golden Age of","meaning":"……的黃金時代","examples":[{"en":"The 16th and 17th centuries were the Golden Age of tennis.","zh":"十六及十七世紀是網球的黃金時代。"},{"en":"The Golden Age of something is the period when it was especially successful, admired or active.","zh":"Golden Age of something 是某事特別成功、受欣賞或活躍的時期。"},{"en":"Some people call the 1990s the Golden Age of certain pop music styles.","zh":"有些人把1990年代稱為某些流行音樂風格的黃金時代。"},{"en":"If a sport has many players, courts and royal supporters, it may be in its Golden Age.","zh":"如果一項運動有許多球手、球場和王室支持者，它可能處於黃金時代。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a peak historical period.","zh":"這個片語描述歷史上的高峰時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"court construction techniques","meaning":"球場建造技術","examples":[{"en":"The heading refers to court construction techniques.","zh":"這個標題指球場建造技術。"},{"en":"Court construction techniques are the methods used to build sports courts.","zh":"Court construction techniques 是建造運動球場所用的方法。"},{"en":"Engineers may study court construction techniques before building an indoor tennis court.","zh":"工程師在建造室內網球場前，可能研究球場建造技術。"},{"en":"If techniques improve, courts may become safer, stronger and easier to maintain.","zh":"如果技術改善，球場可能變得更安全、更堅固和更易維護。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how courts are built, not just where they are built.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於球場如何被建造，而不只是建在哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the real tennis revival","meaning":"真網球的復興","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes the real tennis revival.","zh":"文章描述真網球的復興。"},{"en":"The real tennis revival means renewed interest and growth in real tennis after decline.","zh":"Real tennis revival 指真網球衰落後重新受到關注並增長。"},{"en":"A sport revival may begin when clubs reopen courts and young players join.","zh":"當會所重開球場且年輕球手加入，運動復興可能開始。"},{"en":"If new courts are built in several countries, the revival becomes more visible.","zh":"如果幾個國家興建新球場，復興就變得更明顯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes real tennis becoming active again.","zh":"這個片語描述真網球再次活躍起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tournament tennis","meaning":"錦標賽形式的網球","examples":[{"en":"The modern sport includes tournament tennis around the world.","zh":"現代運動包括在世界各地舉行的錦標賽形式網球。"},{"en":"Tournament tennis is tennis played through organised competitions.","zh":"Tournament tennis 是透過有組織比賽進行的網球。"},{"en":"Students may first play casually, then enter tournament tennis when they become stronger.","zh":"學生可能先隨意玩，變強後再參加錦標賽形式的網球。"},{"en":"If a sport develops a tournament scene, ranking and professional travel may follow.","zh":"如果一項運動發展出錦標賽場景，排名和職業旅行可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the competitive side of tennis.","zh":"這個片語描述網球的競技一面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"descendants of tennis","meaning":"網球的後代運動","examples":[{"en":"Pelota and squash can be seen as descendants of tennis.","zh":"Pelota 和壁球可以被視為網球的後代運動。"},{"en":"Descendants of tennis are later sports that developed from or were influenced by tennis.","zh":"Descendants of tennis 是由網球發展而來或受其影響的後來運動。"},{"en":"Modern sports often have descendants when older games change into new forms.","zh":"當舊遊戲變成新形式，現代運動常會有後代運動。"},{"en":"If squash borrowed from rackets and real tennis, it belongs to a wider family of related games.","zh":"如果壁球借鑑 rackets 和真網球，它就屬於更廣泛的相關遊戲家族。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sports with historical ancestry.","zh":"這個片語描述具有歷史祖源的運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words from the box.","zh":"學生使用方框中的詞語完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill in missing words in a shortened version of the text.","zh":"To complete the summary 指在文章的縮短版本中填上缺失字詞。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole summary before choosing answers.","zh":"學生選答案前應先讀完整段摘要。"},{"en":"If the grammar around a blank requires a noun, a verb will not fit.","zh":"如果空格附近文法需要名詞，動詞就不合適。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"words from the box","meaning":"方框中的詞語","examples":[{"en":"The summary should be completed using words from the box.","zh":"摘要應使用方框中的詞語完成。"},{"en":"Words from the box are the answer choices provided in a boxed list.","zh":"Words from the box 是方框列表中提供的答案選項。"},{"en":"In an exam, students must choose words from the box rather than invent their own.","zh":"在考試中，學生必須從方框中的詞語選答案，而不是自己創造。"},{"en":"If the box contains extra words, meaning and grammar become very important.","zh":"如果方框中有額外詞語，意思和文法就非常重要。"},{"en":"This phrase tells students where their answers must come from.","zh":"這個片語告訴學生答案必須來自哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"more words than spaces","meaning":"詞語比空格多","examples":[{"en":"There are more words than spaces, so some words are not needed.","zh":"詞語比空格多，所以有些詞語不需要使用。"},{"en":"More words than spaces means the answer list has extra choices.","zh":"More words than spaces 指答案列表有額外選項。"},{"en":"A worksheet may give eight words for five blanks, so students must reject three.","zh":"工作紙可能為五個空格提供八個詞，學生必須排除三個。"},{"en":"If there are extra choices, guessing becomes risky.","zh":"如果有額外選項，猜測會變得有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase warns students not to use every word.","zh":"這個片語提醒學生不要用盡每個詞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"an ancient game","meaning":"古老的遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Tennis is described as an ancient game.","zh":"網球被描述為一項古老的遊戲。"},{"en":"An ancient game is a game that began a very long time ago.","zh":"Ancient game 是很久以前開始的遊戲。"},{"en":"Chess is often treated as an ancient game because it has a long history.","zh":"國際象棋常被視為古老遊戲，因為它有悠久歷史。"},{"en":"If a game has existed for centuries, its rules may have changed many times.","zh":"如果一項遊戲存在了多個世紀，其規則可能改變過許多次。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises historical age.","zh":"這個片語強調歷史久遠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in different countries","meaning":"在不同國家","examples":[{"en":"The game has various names in different countries.","zh":"這項遊戲在不同國家有不同名稱。"},{"en":"In different countries means in separate nations or places around the world.","zh":"In different countries 指在世界上不同國家或地方。"},{"en":"The same food may have different names in different countries.","zh":"同一種食物在不同國家可能有不同名稱。"},{"en":"If a sport spreads internationally, local names and customs may develop.","zh":"如果一項運動傳播到國際，各地名稱和習俗可能發展出來。"},{"en":"This phrase compares variation across nations.","zh":"這個片語比較國家之間的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rules developed into","meaning":"規則演變成","examples":[{"en":"The rules developed into the game played today.","zh":"規則演變成今日所玩的遊戲。"},{"en":"Rules developed into something means they gradually changed until they became the present form.","zh":"Rules developed into something 指規則逐漸改變，直至形成現今形式。"},{"en":"Classroom habits may develop into official school rules over time.","zh":"課室習慣可能隨時間演變成正式校規。"},{"en":"If players keep changing rules for fairness and enjoyment, a modern game can emerge.","zh":"如果玩家不斷為公平和趣味改變規則，現代遊戲就可以出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual rule evolution.","zh":"這個片語描述規則的逐步演變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the game played today","meaning":"今日所玩的遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Old rules developed into the game played today.","zh":"舊規則演變成今日所玩的遊戲。"},{"en":"The game played today means the modern version that people now play.","zh":"The game played today 指現在人們玩的現代版本。"},{"en":"The basketball played today is faster and more organised than its earliest form.","zh":"今日所玩的籃球比最早形式更快和更有組織。"},{"en":"If old rules survive in the modern game, history remains visible in present practice.","zh":"如果舊規則在現代遊戲中保留下來，歷史仍可在現今做法中看見。"},{"en":"This phrase connects earlier development with current play.","zh":"這個片語把早期發展與當前玩法連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"hundreds of courts in use","meaning":"數以百計的球場在使用中","examples":[{"en":"There were hundreds of courts in use during the sport’s heyday.","zh":"在這項運動全盛時期，數以百計的球場在使用中。"},{"en":"Hundreds of courts in use means many courts were actively being played on.","zh":"Hundreds of courts in use 指許多球場正被實際使用。"},{"en":"A city with hundreds of sports courts in use would have a very active sports culture.","zh":"如果一座城市有數以百計的運動場地在使用中，它就有非常活躍的體育文化。"},{"en":"If many courts are in use, the sport is probably popular and well supported.","zh":"如果許多球場正在使用，這項運動大概流行且受到支持。"},{"en":"This phrase measures popularity through facilities.","zh":"這個片語透過設施衡量受歡迎程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"albeit","meaning":"雖然；儘管","examples":[{"en":"The courts were widely used, albeit some were rather dilapidated.","zh":"這些球場被廣泛使用，雖然有些相當破舊失修。"},{"en":"Albeit means although or even though.","zh":"Albeit 指雖然或儘管。"},{"en":"The school concert was successful, albeit shorter than expected.","zh":"學校音樂會很成功，雖然比預期短。"},{"en":"This word adds a contrast or limitation after a positive statement.","zh":"這個詞在正面陳述後加入對比或限制。"},{"en":"It is more formal than although and common in written English.","zh":"它比 although 更正式，常見於書面英語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rather dilapidated","meaning":"相當破舊失修","examples":[{"en":"Some of the old courts were rather dilapidated.","zh":"一些舊球場相當破舊失修。"},{"en":"Rather dilapidated means quite old, damaged or poorly maintained.","zh":"Rather dilapidated 指相當老舊、受損或缺乏維修。"},{"en":"A rather dilapidated classroom may have broken chairs and peeling paint.","zh":"相當破舊失修的課室可能有破椅和剝落油漆。"},{"en":"If a court is dilapidated, it may still be used but needs repair.","zh":"如果球場破舊失修，它可能仍被使用，但需要維修。"},{"en":"This phrase describes worn-down physical condition.","zh":"這個片語描述破落的實體狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"much the same","meaning":"大致相同","examples":[{"en":"Equipment is much the same today as it was hundreds of years ago.","zh":"今日的器材與數百年前大致相同。"},{"en":"Much the same means very similar, with little important difference.","zh":"Much the same 指非常相似，沒有重要差別。"},{"en":"The school’s morning routine is much the same as it was last year.","zh":"學校早上的日常安排與去年大致相同。"},{"en":"If equipment is much the same after centuries, the sport has preserved its traditions.","zh":"如果器材幾個世紀後仍大致相同，這項運動就保存了傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises continuity rather than change.","zh":"這個片語強調延續而非改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"made by hand","meaning":"人手製造","examples":[{"en":"Some tennis equipment is still made by hand.","zh":"一些網球器材仍然人手製造。"},{"en":"Made by hand means produced manually rather than by machine.","zh":"Made by hand 指由人手而不是機器製作。"},{"en":"A handmade notebook may feel special because each one is slightly different.","zh":"手工筆記簿可能感覺特別，因為每本都有些微不同。"},{"en":"If equipment is made by hand, production may be slower but more traditional.","zh":"如果器材人手製造，生產可能較慢但更傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes craft-based production.","zh":"這個片語描述以工藝為本的製作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"influence the development of","meaning":"影響……的發展","examples":[{"en":"Tennis influenced the development of other racket sports.","zh":"網球影響了其他球拍運動的發展。"},{"en":"To influence the development of something means to affect how it grows or changes.","zh":"To influence the development of something 指影響某事如何成長或改變。"},{"en":"A good teacher can influence the development of a student’s confidence.","zh":"好老師可以影響學生信心的發展。"},{"en":"If one sport gives later sports ideas about courts and rackets, it shapes their development.","zh":"如果一項運動給後來運動關於球場和球拍的想法，它就塑造了它們的發展。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an earlier source with later change.","zh":"這個片語把早期來源與後來變化連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the more recognisable form","meaning":"較為人熟悉的形式","examples":[{"en":"Lawn tennis is now the more recognisable form of the sport.","zh":"草地網球現在是這項運動較為人熟悉的形式。"},{"en":"The more recognisable form is the version that more people can easily identify.","zh":"The more recognisable form 是更多人容易識別的版本。"},{"en":"Modern football is more recognisable to most children than many older local ball games.","zh":"對大多數孩子而言，現代足球比許多古老本地球類遊戲更熟悉。"},{"en":"If television shows one version often, that version becomes more familiar to the public.","zh":"如果電視經常展示某個版本，該版本就變得更為公眾熟悉。"},{"en":"This phrase compares public familiarity between forms.","zh":"這個片語比較不同形式的公眾熟悉程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"revolutionise equipment","meaning":"徹底革新器材","examples":[{"en":"The newer form of tennis has revolutionised equipment.","zh":"較新的網球形式徹底革新了器材。"},{"en":"To revolutionise equipment means to change sports tools completely and dramatically.","zh":"To revolutionise equipment 指徹底而巨大地改變運動工具。"},{"en":"Lightweight materials revolutionised cycling equipment by making bicycles faster.","zh":"輕質材料透過令單車更快，徹底革新了單車器材。"},{"en":"If new technology changes how players hit, move or train, it can revolutionise equipment.","zh":"如果新科技改變球手擊球、移動或訓練方式，它可以徹底革新器材。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major transformation in tools.","zh":"這個片語描述工具上的重大轉化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a professional tournament circuit","meaning":"職業巡迴錦標賽","examples":[{"en":"Real tennis now has a professional tournament circuit.","zh":"真網球現在有職業巡迴錦標賽。"},{"en":"A professional tournament circuit is a series of events where professional players compete.","zh":"Professional tournament circuit 是職業球手參與的一系列賽事。"},{"en":"Golf and tennis players often travel across countries on professional circuits.","zh":"高爾夫和網球球手常在職業巡迴賽中跨國比賽。"},{"en":"If a sport has a professional circuit, it supports rankings, prize money and regular competition.","zh":"如果一項運動有職業巡迴賽，它就支持排名、獎金和定期競賽。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an organised professional competition system.","zh":"這個片語描述有組織的職業比賽系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"competitions played around the world","meaning":"在世界各地舉行的比賽","examples":[{"en":"There are competitions played around the world.","zh":"有在世界各地舉行的比賽。"},{"en":"Competitions played around the world are events held in many different countries.","zh":"Competitions played around the world 是在許多不同國家舉辦的賽事。"},{"en":"A sport becomes more international when competitions are played around the world.","zh":"當比賽在世界各地舉行，一項運動就變得更國際化。"},{"en":"If players travel globally for events, the sport has moved beyond a local tradition.","zh":"如果球手為賽事全球旅行，該運動就已超越本地傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes worldwide competitive activity.","zh":"這個片語描述全球性的競賽活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"despite high construction costs","meaning":"儘管建造成本高昂","examples":[{"en":"New courts are appearing despite high construction costs.","zh":"儘管建造成本高昂，新球場仍正在出現。"},{"en":"Despite high construction costs means although building them is expensive.","zh":"Despite high construction costs 指雖然建造它們很昂貴。"},{"en":"The school built a new library despite high construction costs because students needed space.","zh":"儘管建造成本高昂，學校仍興建新圖書館，因為學生需要空間。"},{"en":"If people invest despite high costs, their commitment is probably strong.","zh":"如果人們在成本高昂下仍投資，他們的投入大概很強。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts financial difficulty with continued action.","zh":"這個片語把財政困難與持續行動作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"hindered","meaning":"被阻礙","examples":[{"en":"The growth of the sport has been hindered by high costs.","zh":"這項運動的發展受到高成本阻礙。"},{"en":"Hindered means slowed down, blocked or made more difficult.","zh":"Hindered 指被拖慢、阻擋或變得更困難。"},{"en":"A student’s progress may be hindered by frequent absences.","zh":"學生進步可能因經常缺席而被阻礙。"},{"en":"If court building is expensive, the sport’s spread can be hindered.","zh":"如果建造球場昂貴，這項運動的傳播可能被阻礙。"},{"en":"This word describes something being held back.","zh":"這個詞描述某事被拖住。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"resurgence","meaning":"復興；再度興盛","examples":[{"en":"Real tennis is enjoying a resurgence.","zh":"真網球正在享受復興。"},{"en":"A resurgence is a new rise in popularity, activity or strength after decline.","zh":"Resurgence 是在衰落後重新流行、活躍或強盛。"},{"en":"A town may see a resurgence of traditional markets after young families move in.","zh":"年輕家庭搬入後，城鎮可能出現傳統市場復興。"},{"en":"If a sport gains new courts and players, it may be experiencing a resurgence.","zh":"如果一項運動獲得新球場和新球手，它可能正在再度興盛。"},{"en":"This word describes renewed growth.","zh":"這個詞描述重新增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"desirable","meaning":"令人嚮往的；合意的","examples":[{"en":"A more vigorous sport was desirable for the leisure classes.","zh":"對有閒階級而言，更有活力的運動是令人嚮往的。"},{"en":"Desirable means wanted, attractive or worth having.","zh":"Desirable 指令人想要、有吸引力或值得擁有。"},{"en":"Flexible working hours are desirable for many parents.","zh":"彈性工作時間對許多家長而言是合意的。"},{"en":"If an activity is more energetic and fashionable, it may become desirable to wealthy players.","zh":"如果活動更有活力且時髦，它可能變得令富裕玩家嚮往。"},{"en":"This word describes something people see as appealing or beneficial.","zh":"這個詞描述人們視為吸引或有益的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"insurance costs","meaning":"保險費用","examples":[{"en":"Insurance costs can affect the running of expensive sports facilities.","zh":"保險費用可以影響昂貴運動設施的營運。"},{"en":"Insurance costs are the money paid to protect against financial loss from accidents or damage.","zh":"Insurance costs 是為防止意外或損壞造成財政損失而支付的費用。"},{"en":"A school may pay insurance costs before taking students on a sports trip.","zh":"學校帶學生參加體育旅行前可能支付保險費用。"},{"en":"If insurance costs rise, clubs may charge higher membership fees.","zh":"如果保險費用上升，會所可能收取更高會費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a financial cost connected with risk protection.","zh":"這個片語描述與風險保障相關的財務成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be played around the world","meaning":"在世界各地進行","examples":[{"en":"Competitions are now played around the world.","zh":"比賽現在在世界各地進行。"},{"en":"To be played around the world means to take place in many countries internationally.","zh":"To be played around the world 指在許多國家進行。"},{"en":"Football is played around the world by children, amateurs and professionals.","zh":"足球由世界各地的孩子、業餘球員和職業球員進行。"},{"en":"If a sport is played globally, players from different cultures can compete and learn from one another.","zh":"如果一項運動在全球進行，不同文化的球手可以競爭並互相學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes international reach.","zh":"這個片語描述國際覆蓋範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"new courts are appearing","meaning":"新球場正在出現","examples":[{"en":"New courts are appearing in the US, France, Australia and the UK.","zh":"新球場正在美國、法國、澳洲和英國出現。"},{"en":"New courts are appearing means new playing facilities are being built or opened.","zh":"New courts are appearing 指新的比賽設施正在興建或開放。"},{"en":"New basketball courts are appearing in the district after the government improved sports funding.","zh":"政府改善體育資助後，區內正在出現新的籃球場。"},{"en":"If new courts appear in several countries, the sport is likely growing.","zh":"如果新球場在幾個國家出現，這項運動很可能正在增長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible expansion through new facilities.","zh":"這個片語描述透過新設施可見的擴展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 25 - The Game of Tennis.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 26":[{"front":"amateur naturalists","meaning":"業餘自然觀察者","examples":[{"en":"Amateur naturalists have collected records that are useful to professional scientists.","zh":"業餘自然觀察者收集了對專業科學家有用的記錄。"},{"en":"Amateur naturalists are people who study plants, animals or natural events as a hobby, not as a paid profession.","zh":"amateur naturalists 指把研究植物、動物或自然事件作為興趣，而非受薪職業的人。"},{"en":"A retired teacher may become an amateur naturalist by recording birds seen in a local park.","zh":"一位退休老師可能透過記錄本地公園見到的鳥類，成為業餘自然觀察者。"},{"en":"Amateur naturalists can help science because they observe ordinary places over many years.","zh":"業餘自然觀察者可以幫助科學，因為他們多年來觀察普通地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when non-professionals make careful observations of nature.","zh":"當非專業人士細心觀察自然時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an annual Alaskan betting contest","meaning":"阿拉斯加一年一度的博彩比賽","examples":[{"en":"An annual Alaskan betting contest has provided useful clues about climate change.","zh":"阿拉斯加一年一度的博彩比賽提供了關於氣候變化的有用線索。"},{"en":"An annual Alaskan betting contest is a yearly competition in Alaska where people guess when river ice will break.","zh":"an annual Alaskan betting contest 指阿拉斯加每年舉行、讓人猜測河冰何時融破的比賽。"},{"en":"A local community event can become scientific evidence if it records the same natural event every year.","zh":"如果本地社區活動每年記錄同一自然事件，它可以成為科學證據。"},{"en":"Because the contest happens annually, its records can show whether thawing is becoming earlier.","zh":"因為比賽每年舉行，其記錄可以顯示融冰是否變得更早。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a playful tradition unexpectedly becomes climate data.","zh":"當一項有趣傳統意外成為氣候數據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sightings of migratory birds","meaning":"候鳥目擊記錄","examples":[{"en":"Ecologists study sightings of migratory birds to understand seasonal change.","zh":"生態學家研究候鳥目擊記錄，以理解季節變化。"},{"en":"Sightings of migratory birds are records of when and where people see birds that travel between regions.","zh":"sightings of migratory birds 指人們在何時何地看見遷徙鳥類的記錄。"},{"en":"Birdwatchers may write down sightings of migratory birds in spring and autumn.","zh":"觀鳥人士可能在春天和秋天記下候鳥目擊記錄。"},{"en":"These sightings help scientists see whether birds are arriving earlier as temperatures rise.","zh":"這些目擊記錄幫助科學家了解鳥類是否因氣溫上升而更早到達。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when animal movement is used to study environmental change.","zh":"當動物移動被用來研究環境變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ecologists","meaning":"生態學家","examples":[{"en":"Ecologists are using unusual data to predict environmental change.","zh":"生態學家正在使用不尋常數據來預測環境變化。"},{"en":"Ecologists are scientists who study relationships between living things and their environment.","zh":"ecologists 指研究生物與其環境之間關係的科學家。"},{"en":"Ecologists may study how warmer winters affect flowers, insects and birds.","zh":"生態學家可能研究較暖冬天如何影響花、昆蟲和鳥類。"},{"en":"Their work helps explain how small changes in climate can affect whole ecosystems.","zh":"他們的工作幫助解釋氣候中的小變化如何影響整個生態系統。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing scientific study of nature and environmental systems.","zh":"討論自然和環境系統的科學研究時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a wealth of unusual data","meaning":"大量不尋常的數據","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are using a wealth of unusual data from amateur records.","zh":"研究人員正在使用來自業餘記錄的大量不尋常數據。"},{"en":"A wealth of unusual data means a large amount of valuable information from unexpected sources.","zh":"a wealth of unusual data 指來自意想不到來源的大量有價值資料。"},{"en":"Old family calendars may contain a wealth of unusual data about local weather and flowering dates.","zh":"舊家庭月曆可能包含大量關於本地天氣和開花日期的不尋常數據。"},{"en":"Such data become useful when many small observations are collected over a long period.","zh":"當許多小觀察被長期收集，這類數據就變得有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when valuable evidence comes from surprising places.","zh":"當有價值證據來自令人意外的地方時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"predict the impact of","meaning":"預測……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Scientists use old records to predict the impact of climate change.","zh":"科學家使用舊記錄來預測氣候變化的影響。"},{"en":"Predict the impact of means estimate what effects something will have in the future.","zh":"predict the impact of 指估計某事日後會產生甚麼效果。"},{"en":"A school may predict the impact of shorter lessons before changing the timetable.","zh":"學校在改時間表前，可能預測縮短課堂的影響。"},{"en":"Scientists predict the impact of warming by comparing past temperatures with natural events.","zh":"科學家透過比較過去氣溫與自然事件來預測暖化的影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence is used to forecast future effects.","zh":"當證據被用來預測未來效果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"climate change","meaning":"氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"The records help scientists understand the effects of climate change.","zh":"這些記錄幫助科學家理解氣候變化的影響。"},{"en":"Climate change refers to long-term changes in temperature, rainfall, seasons and weather patterns.","zh":"climate change 指氣溫、降雨、季節和天氣模式的長期改變。"},{"en":"Farmers may notice climate change when crops flower earlier or droughts become more frequent.","zh":"當農作物較早開花或乾旱變得更頻繁，農民可能注意到氣候變化。"},{"en":"Climate change affects ecosystems because many plants and animals depend on seasonal timing.","zh":"氣候變化影響生態系統，因為許多植物和動物依賴季節時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing long-term environmental change.","zh":"討論長期環境變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"slide something out of","meaning":"從……中抽出某物","examples":[{"en":"Tim Sparks slides a small notebook out of an envelope.","zh":"Tim Sparks 從信封中抽出一本小筆記簿。"},{"en":"Slide something out of means move something smoothly from inside a container or space.","zh":"slide something out of 指把某物從容器或空間中順滑地移出。"},{"en":"A student may slide a worksheet out of a folder before class begins.","zh":"學生可能在上課前從文件夾中抽出工作紙。"},{"en":"People slide fragile objects out carefully to avoid tearing or damaging them.","zh":"人們會小心抽出易損物件，以免撕破或損壞它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is gently removed from inside something else.","zh":"當某物被輕輕從另一物內取出時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"leather-bound notebook","meaning":"皮面裝訂筆記簿","examples":[{"en":"The leather-bound notebook contains beekeeping notes.","zh":"這本皮面裝訂筆記簿載有養蜂筆記。"},{"en":"A leather-bound notebook is a notebook with a cover made of leather or leather-like material.","zh":"leather-bound notebook 指封面由皮革或仿皮材料製成的筆記簿。"},{"en":"A researcher may handle a leather-bound notebook carefully because it is old and fragile.","zh":"研究人員可能小心處理皮面裝訂筆記簿，因為它古老而脆弱。"},{"en":"Such notebooks can preserve observations for decades if they are stored safely.","zh":"如果安全保存，這類筆記簿可以保存觀察記錄數十年。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing an old, formal or carefully kept notebook.","zh":"描述古老、正式或被細心保存的筆記簿時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"yellowing pages","meaning":"泛黃的書頁","examples":[{"en":"The book’s yellowing pages contain notes made many decades ago.","zh":"這本書泛黃的書頁載有多年前寫下的筆記。"},{"en":"Yellowing pages are old pages that have turned yellow with age.","zh":"yellowing pages 指因年代久遠而變黃的舊書頁。"},{"en":"A library may keep books with yellowing pages in a special archive room.","zh":"圖書館可能把有泛黃書頁的書保存在特別檔案室。"},{"en":"Yellowing pages show that a record may be old but still valuable.","zh":"泛黃的書頁顯示一份記錄可能古老，但仍然有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing aged paper and historical documents.","zh":"描述老化紙張和歷史文件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"beekeeping notes","meaning":"養蜂筆記","examples":[{"en":"Walter Coates kept beekeeping notes between 1941 and 1969.","zh":"Walter Coates 在1941年至1969年間保存養蜂筆記。"},{"en":"Beekeeping notes are written records about bees, hives, honey production or related natural events.","zh":"beekeeping notes 指關於蜜蜂、蜂箱、蜂蜜產量或相關自然事件的書面記錄。"},{"en":"A beekeeper may keep beekeeping notes to record when flowers open and bees become active.","zh":"養蜂人可能保存養蜂筆記，記錄花何時開放和蜜蜂何時活躍。"},{"en":"These notes can become useful climate data if they show changes over many years.","zh":"如果這些筆記顯示多年變化，它們可以成為有用氣候數據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when everyday work records become scientific evidence.","zh":"當日常工作記錄變成科學證據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the late","meaning":"已故的……","examples":[{"en":"The notes were made by the late Walter Coates.","zh":"這些筆記由已故的 Walter Coates 所寫。"},{"en":"The late is used before a person’s name to show that the person has died.","zh":"the late 用於人名之前，表示該人已經去世。"},{"en":"The award was named after the late school principal who helped many students.","zh":"該獎項以已故校長命名，他曾幫助許多學生。"},{"en":"This phrase shows respect while making clear that the person is no longer alive.","zh":"這個短語表達尊重，同時清楚說明該人已不在人世。"},{"en":"It is useful in formal writing about someone who has passed away.","zh":"在正式寫作中提及已故人士時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a growing pile of","meaning":"越來越多的……","examples":[{"en":"Sparks adds the notebook to his growing pile of local records.","zh":"Sparks 把筆記簿加入他越來越多的本地記錄中。"},{"en":"A growing pile of means an increasing collection or amount of something.","zh":"a growing pile of 指不斷增加的一批或一堆東西。"},{"en":"A teacher may have a growing pile of essays to mark before the weekend.","zh":"老師週末前可能有越來越多的作文要批改。"},{"en":"The pile grows when more people send old records to the researcher.","zh":"當更多人把舊記錄寄給研究員，這堆資料就會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when things keep accumulating.","zh":"當事物不斷累積時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"local journals","meaning":"地方日誌","examples":[{"en":"Local journals can contain valuable observations about nature.","zh":"地方日誌可以包含關於自然的有價值觀察。"},{"en":"Local journals are written records, diaries or publications about events in a particular area.","zh":"local journals 指關於某特定地區事件的書面記錄、日記或出版物。"},{"en":"A village history group may keep local journals about weather, farming and community events.","zh":"鄉村歷史小組可能保存關於天氣、農務和社區事件的地方日誌。"},{"en":"Local journals help researchers because they preserve details that national records may miss.","zh":"地方日誌幫助研究人員，因為它們保存全國記錄可能遺漏的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when small-area records become important evidence.","zh":"當小地區記錄成為重要證據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"birdwatchers’ lists","meaning":"觀鳥人士的記錄清單","examples":[{"en":"Birdwatchers’ lists may become useful scientific records.","zh":"觀鳥人士的記錄清單可能成為有用的科學記錄。"},{"en":"Birdwatchers’ lists are notes showing which birds people saw, and often when and where they saw them.","zh":"birdwatchers’ lists 指記錄人們看見哪些鳥，並常包括時間和地點的筆記。"},{"en":"A birdwatcher may keep a list of swallows returning each spring.","zh":"觀鳥人士可能保存每年春天燕子回歸的清單。"},{"en":"These lists help scientists track changes in migration and local bird populations.","zh":"這些清單幫助科學家追蹤遷徙和本地鳥類數量的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when hobby records are used for ecological study.","zh":"當興趣記錄被用於生態研究時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"gardening diaries","meaning":"園藝日記","examples":[{"en":"Gardening diaries often record when plants first flower.","zh":"園藝日記常記錄植物第一次開花的時間。"},{"en":"Gardening diaries are personal records of planting, flowering, weather and garden changes.","zh":"gardening diaries 指關於種植、開花、天氣和花園變化的個人記錄。"},{"en":"A gardener may write in a diary when roses first bloom each year.","zh":"園丁可能在日記中寫下玫瑰每年首次開花的時間。"},{"en":"Gardening diaries can show whether spring flowers are appearing earlier over time.","zh":"園藝日記可以顯示春天花朵是否隨時間更早出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when private garden notes become environmental records.","zh":"當私人花園筆記成為環境記錄時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"uncover a record","meaning":"發掘一項記錄","examples":[{"en":"Researchers uncover about one major new record each month.","zh":"研究人員每月大約發掘一項重要新記錄。"},{"en":"Uncover a record means discover an old or hidden record that was not being used before.","zh":"uncover a record 指發現以前未被使用的舊記錄或隱藏記錄。"},{"en":"A historian may uncover a record of village births in an old church cupboard.","zh":"歷史學家可能在舊教堂櫃中發掘一項村莊出生記錄。"},{"en":"Researchers uncover records by following clues, asking local people and checking archives.","zh":"研究人員透過追查線索、詢問本地人和檢查檔案來發掘記錄。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when hidden information is found and made useful.","zh":"當隱藏資料被找到並變得有用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"around two centuries before","meaning":"大約兩個世紀前","examples":[{"en":"Around two centuries before Coates, Marsham began recording natural events.","zh":"大約在 Coates 之前兩個世紀，Marsham 開始記錄自然事件。"},{"en":"Around two centuries before means about two hundred years earlier.","zh":"around two centuries before 指大約早二百年。"},{"en":"Around two centuries before modern buses, people travelled mostly by horse or on foot.","zh":"大約在現代巴士出現前兩個世紀，人們主要騎馬或步行出行。"},{"en":"This phrase helps place one event far earlier than another.","zh":"這個短語幫助把一件事定位在另一件事很久之前。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining historical time gaps.","zh":"解釋歷史時間差距時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a landowner from","meaning":"來自……的地主","examples":[{"en":"Robert Marsham was a landowner from Norfolk.","zh":"Robert Marsham 是來自 Norfolk 的地主。"},{"en":"A landowner from a place is someone who owns land in or comes from that area.","zh":"landowner from a place 指在某地擁有土地或來自該地的人。"},{"en":"A landowner from a rural village may record weather because farming depends on it.","zh":"來自鄉村的地主可能記錄天氣，因為農務依賴天氣。"},{"en":"Landowners sometimes kept detailed records because they managed farms, woods and estates.","zh":"地主有時保存詳細記錄，因為他們管理農場、林地和莊園。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying a person by place and social role.","zh":"以地點和社會角色識別人物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"record the life cycles of","meaning":"記錄……的生命週期","examples":[{"en":"Marsham recorded the life cycles of plants and animals.","zh":"Marsham 記錄植物和動物的生命週期。"},{"en":"Record the life cycles of means write down stages such as flowering, nesting, breeding or migration.","zh":"record the life cycles of 指寫下開花、築巢、繁殖或遷徙等階段。"},{"en":"Students may record the life cycle of a butterfly from egg to adult.","zh":"學生可能記錄蝴蝶從卵到成蟲的生命週期。"},{"en":"Such records help scientists compare seasonal timing across many years.","zh":"這類記錄幫助科學家比較多年來的季節時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when natural development is observed step by step.","zh":"當自然發展被逐步觀察時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on his estate","meaning":"在他的莊園上","examples":[{"en":"He observed plants and animals on his estate.","zh":"他在自己的莊園上觀察植物和動物。"},{"en":"On his estate means on the land or property that he owned.","zh":"on his estate 指在他擁有的土地或產業上。"},{"en":"A farmer may plant trees on his estate to prevent soil erosion.","zh":"農夫可能在自己的莊園上種樹，以防止土壤侵蝕。"},{"en":"Observing one estate over many years can reveal long-term local environmental change.","zh":"多年觀察同一莊園可以揭示本地長期環境變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when activities happen on privately owned land.","zh":"當活動發生在私人擁有土地上時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the dates on which","meaning":"……的日期","examples":[{"en":"Marsham recorded the dates on which the oaks burst into leaf.","zh":"Marsham 記錄橡樹長出嫩葉的日期。"},{"en":"The dates on which means the exact days when something happened.","zh":"the dates on which 指某事發生的確實日期。"},{"en":"A school secretary records the dates on which students join or leave the school.","zh":"學校文員會記錄學生入學或離校的日期。"},{"en":"Exact dates allow researchers to compare events across different years.","zh":"確實日期讓研究人員比較不同年份的事件。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when timing matters.","zh":"當時間很重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"wood anemones","meaning":"林地銀蓮花","examples":[{"en":"Marsham noted when the first wood anemones flowered.","zh":"Marsham 記下第一批林地銀蓮花何時開花。"},{"en":"Wood anemones are small woodland flowers that often bloom in spring.","zh":"wood anemones 指常在春天開花的小型林地花卉。"},{"en":"Walkers may notice wood anemones on the forest floor before trees are fully in leaf.","zh":"在樹木完全長葉前，行人可能在森林地面注意到林地銀蓮花。"},{"en":"Their flowering dates can help show whether spring is arriving earlier.","zh":"它們的開花日期可以幫助顯示春天是否更早來臨。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing plant records in woodland habitats.","zh":"討論林地棲息地中的植物記錄時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"burst into leaf","meaning":"長出嫩葉；枝葉初展","examples":[{"en":"The oaks burst into leaf in spring.","zh":"橡樹在春天長出嫩葉。"},{"en":"Burst into leaf means suddenly begin to grow fresh leaves after winter.","zh":"burst into leaf 指冬天後突然開始長出新鮮葉子。"},{"en":"A tree outside a classroom may burst into leaf after several warm days.","zh":"課室外的樹可能在幾天暖和天氣後枝葉初展。"},{"en":"Trees burst into leaf earlier when spring temperatures rise sooner.","zh":"當春季氣溫較早上升，樹木會更早長出嫩葉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the first strong growth of leaves.","zh":"描述葉子最初大量生長時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"begin nesting","meaning":"開始築巢","examples":[{"en":"The rooks began nesting at a particular time each year.","zh":"白嘴鴉每年在特定時間開始築巢。"},{"en":"Begin nesting means start building nests or preparing places to lay eggs.","zh":"begin nesting 指開始築巢或準備產卵地點。"},{"en":"Birds may begin nesting in school trees when spring weather becomes warmer.","zh":"當春天天氣變暖，鳥類可能開始在學校樹上築巢。"},{"en":"If birds begin nesting earlier, it may show that seasonal conditions have changed.","zh":"如果鳥類更早開始築巢，可能顯示季節條件已改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when studying animal breeding behaviour.","zh":"研究動物繁殖行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"successive generations","meaning":"一代又一代","examples":[{"en":"Successive generations of the Marsham family continued the records.","zh":"Marsham 家族一代又一代繼續這些記錄。"},{"en":"Successive generations are generations that follow one after another.","zh":"successive generations 指一代接一代的人。"},{"en":"Successive generations of a family may live in the same village and keep the same traditions.","zh":"一個家庭一代又一代可能住在同一村莊並保持相同傳統。"},{"en":"Long records become possible when successive generations continue the same habit.","zh":"當一代又一代持續同一習慣，長期記錄才成為可能。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when work or tradition passes through a family over time.","zh":"當工作或傳統在家庭中隨時間傳承時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"compile notes","meaning":"彙編筆記；整理記錄","examples":[{"en":"The Marshams continued compiling these notes for 211 years.","zh":"Marsham 家族持續整理這些筆記長達211年。"},{"en":"Compile notes means collect, organise and keep written observations over time.","zh":"compile notes 指長期收集、組織並保存書面觀察。"},{"en":"A student may compile notes from several lessons before an exam.","zh":"學生可能在考試前整理幾課的筆記。"},{"en":"Notes become more useful when they are compiled carefully and consistently.","zh":"當筆記被仔細而一致地整理，它們會更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when scattered observations are organised into a record.","zh":"當零散觀察被組織成記錄時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be put to scientific use","meaning":"被用於科學用途","examples":[{"en":"Old nature records are now being put to scientific use.","zh":"舊自然記錄現在被用於科學用途。"},{"en":"Be put to scientific use means be used as evidence or data for scientific research.","zh":"be put to scientific use 指被用作科學研究的證據或數據。"},{"en":"Old hospital records can be put to scientific use if they show long-term health patterns.","zh":"如果舊醫院記錄顯示長期健康模式，它們可以被用於科學用途。"},{"en":"Amateur observations are put to scientific use when researchers compare them with climate data.","zh":"當研究人員把業餘觀察與氣候數據比較，這些觀察就被用於科學用途。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when ordinary records become research material.","zh":"當普通記錄變成研究材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"could not possibly have expected","meaning":"不可能預料到","examples":[{"en":"The authors could not possibly have expected these modern uses.","zh":"這些作者不可能預料到這些現代用途。"},{"en":"Could not possibly have expected means there was no realistic way for someone to predict something.","zh":"could not possibly have expected 指某人沒有任何實際可能預測某事。"},{"en":"A teacher who wrote notes thirty years ago could not possibly have expected students to read them online today.","zh":"三十年前寫筆記的老師不可能預料到今天學生會在網上閱讀它們。"},{"en":"The recorders wrote for their own purposes, not knowing future scientists would use their data.","zh":"記錄者是為自己的目的寫下資料，並不知道未來科學家會使用他們的數據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when later uses are far beyond original expectations.","zh":"當後來用途遠超原本預期時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"data sets","meaning":"數據集","examples":[{"en":"These data sets are proving useful to ecologists.","zh":"這些數據集正證明對生態學家有用。"},{"en":"Data sets are organised collections of information used for analysis.","zh":"data sets 指為分析而組織起來的資料集合。"},{"en":"A school may create data sets of attendance, test scores and reading progress.","zh":"學校可能建立出席率、測驗分數和閱讀進度的數據集。"},{"en":"Data sets become powerful when they cover many years or many places.","zh":"當數據集涵蓋多年或許多地方，它們就變得有力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when information is grouped for research.","zh":"當資料被整理作研究時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prove invaluable to","meaning":"證明對……極有價值","examples":[{"en":"Amateur records are proving invaluable to climate researchers.","zh":"業餘記錄正證明對氣候研究人員極有價值。"},{"en":"Prove invaluable to means turn out to be extremely useful or important to someone.","zh":"prove invaluable to 指結果顯示對某人極其有用或重要。"},{"en":"A clear timetable can prove invaluable to new students during their first week at school.","zh":"清晰時間表可在新生開學第一週證明對他們極有價值。"},{"en":"Old records prove invaluable when they provide evidence that no modern instrument collected.","zh":"當舊記錄提供現代儀器沒有收集到的證據，它們就證明極有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something becomes unexpectedly valuable.","zh":"當某物變得出乎意料地有價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the timing of biological events","meaning":"生物事件發生的時間","examples":[{"en":"Phenology focuses on the timing of biological events.","zh":"物候學集中研究生物事件發生的時間。"},{"en":"The timing of biological events means when living things flower, breed, migrate, hatch or change.","zh":"timing of biological events 指生物何時開花、繁殖、遷徙、孵化或改變。"},{"en":"A scientist may record the timing of biological events such as birds nesting and trees leafing.","zh":"科學家可能記錄鳥類築巢和樹木長葉等生物事件發生的時間。"},{"en":"Changes in timing can show how climate affects living organisms.","zh":"時間上的改變可以顯示氣候如何影響生物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when studying seasonal patterns in nature.","zh":"研究自然界季節模式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"phenology","meaning":"物候學","examples":[{"en":"Phenology is the study of the timing of biological events.","zh":"物候學是研究生物事件發生時間的學科。"},{"en":"Phenology examines when natural events happen, such as flowering, migration and leaf fall.","zh":"phenology 研究自然事件何時發生，例如開花、遷徙和落葉。"},{"en":"A student can practise phenology by recording when the first butterflies appear each spring.","zh":"學生可以透過記錄每年春天第一批蝴蝶何時出現來練習物候學。"},{"en":"Phenology helps scientists see whether seasons are shifting because of climate change.","zh":"物候學幫助科學家看出季節是否因氣候變化而轉移。"},{"en":"This word is useful when nature’s calendar is being studied.","zh":"當研究自然界的時間表時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"combine records with climate data","meaning":"將記錄與氣候數據結合","examples":[{"en":"Researchers combine old records with climate data.","zh":"研究人員將舊記錄與氣候數據結合。"},{"en":"Combine records with climate data means compare observations with information about temperature, rainfall or weather patterns.","zh":"combine records with climate data 指把觀察記錄與氣溫、降雨或天氣模式資料比較。"},{"en":"A scientist may combine garden diaries with climate data to study earlier flowering.","zh":"科學家可能將園藝日記與氣候數據結合，以研究較早開花。"},{"en":"Combining the two helps show whether natural changes match changes in temperature.","zh":"把兩者結合有助顯示自然變化是否與氣溫變化一致。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when different sources of evidence are used together.","zh":"當不同證據來源被一起使用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reveal how","meaning":"揭示……如何","examples":[{"en":"The records reveal how temperature affects the arrival of spring.","zh":"這些記錄揭示氣溫如何影響春天的來臨。"},{"en":"Reveal how means show the way in which something happens or influences something else.","zh":"reveal how 指顯示某事如何發生或如何影響另一事物。"},{"en":"Test results can reveal how much extra practice improves spelling.","zh":"測驗結果可以揭示額外練習如何改善串字。"},{"en":"Long-term records reveal how natural events respond to warmer or colder years.","zh":"長期記錄揭示自然事件如何回應較暖或較冷年份。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence explains a process.","zh":"當證據解釋一個過程時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"changes in temperature","meaning":"氣溫變化","examples":[{"en":"Changes in temperature can affect the arrival of spring.","zh":"氣溫變化可以影響春天的來臨。"},{"en":"Changes in temperature are increases or decreases in how warm or cold the air or environment is.","zh":"changes in temperature 指空氣或環境冷暖程度的上升或下降。"},{"en":"Changes in temperature can make students bring jackets one day and short sleeves the next.","zh":"氣溫變化可以令學生一天穿外套，翌日穿短袖。"},{"en":"In nature, temperature changes can alter flowering, migration and breeding times.","zh":"在自然界中，氣溫變化可以改變開花、遷徙和繁殖時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when warming or cooling affects events.","zh":"當變暖或變冷影響事件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the arrival of spring","meaning":"春天的來臨","examples":[{"en":"The records show changes in the arrival of spring.","zh":"這些記錄顯示春天來臨時間的變化。"},{"en":"The arrival of spring means the time when spring conditions begin, such as warmer weather and new growth.","zh":"arrival of spring 指春天條件開始出現的時間，例如天氣變暖和新生長出現。"},{"en":"People may notice the arrival of spring when flowers open and birds sing more often.","zh":"當花開和鳥叫更頻繁，人們可能注意到春天的來臨。"},{"en":"If the arrival of spring becomes earlier, plants and animals may change their behaviour.","zh":"如果春天的來臨變得更早，植物和動物可能改變行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing seasonal timing.","zh":"討論季節時間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"allow someone to","meaning":"使某人能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The records allow ecologists to make improved predictions.","zh":"這些記錄使生態學家能夠作出更準確的預測。"},{"en":"Allow someone to means make it possible for someone to do something.","zh":"allow someone to 指令某人能夠做某事。"},{"en":"Clear instructions allow students to finish a task without asking many questions.","zh":"清楚指示使學生能夠不用問太多問題也完成任務。"},{"en":"Long-term records allow scientists to compare today’s patterns with the past.","zh":"長期記錄使科學家能夠把今日模式與過去比較。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one thing gives people the ability or chance to act.","zh":"當一件事給人能力或機會行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"make improved predictions about","meaning":"對……作出更準確的預測","examples":[{"en":"Ecologists can make improved predictions about climate change.","zh":"生態學家可以對氣候變化作出更準確的預測。"},{"en":"Make improved predictions about means produce more accurate forecasts because better evidence is available.","zh":"make improved predictions about 指因有更好證據而作出更準確預測。"},{"en":"Doctors can make improved predictions about recovery when they have detailed test results.","zh":"醫生有詳細檢查結果時，可以對康復情況作出更準確預測。"},{"en":"Better data help scientists predict future natural changes with more confidence.","zh":"更好數據幫助科學家更有信心地預測未來自然變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when prediction becomes more reliable.","zh":"當預測變得更可靠時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a small band of researchers","meaning":"一小群研究人員","examples":[{"en":"A small band of researchers is studying centuries of amateur records.","zh":"一小群研究人員正在研究數個世紀的業餘記錄。"},{"en":"A small band of researchers is a small group of researchers working together.","zh":"small band of researchers 指一起工作的一小組研究人員。"},{"en":"A small band of teachers may design a new reading programme for the whole school.","zh":"一小群老師可能為全校設計新的閱讀計劃。"},{"en":"Small research groups can do important work when they focus on overlooked evidence.","zh":"小型研究團隊若集中於被忽視的證據，也能做重要工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a small team takes on a large task.","zh":"當小團隊承擔大型任務時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"comb through","meaning":"仔細翻查","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are combing through hundreds of years of records.","zh":"研究人員正在仔細翻查數百年的記錄。"},{"en":"Comb through means search carefully and thoroughly through a large amount of material.","zh":"comb through 指仔細而徹底地搜尋大量材料。"},{"en":"A teacher may comb through exam papers to find common mistakes.","zh":"老師可能仔細翻查試卷，以找出常見錯誤。"},{"en":"Researchers comb through old records because useful details may be hidden in ordinary notes.","zh":"研究人員仔細翻查舊記錄，因為有用細節可能藏在普通筆記中。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when careful searching is needed.","zh":"當需要仔細搜尋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"hundreds of years of records","meaning":"數百年的記錄","examples":[{"en":"The researchers examine hundreds of years of records.","zh":"研究人員檢查數百年的記錄。"},{"en":"Hundreds of years of records means written observations collected across several centuries.","zh":"hundreds of years of records 指跨越幾個世紀收集的書面觀察。"},{"en":"A town archive may contain hundreds of years of records about births, weather and farming.","zh":"城鎮檔案館可能包含關於出生、天氣和農務的數百年記錄。"},{"en":"Such long records help scientists see slow changes that one lifetime cannot reveal.","zh":"這類長期記錄幫助科學家看到一生無法揭示的緩慢變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence covers a very long time.","zh":"當證據涵蓋很長時間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"taken by thousands of","meaning":"由數以千計的……記錄下來","examples":[{"en":"The records were taken by thousands of amateur naturalists.","zh":"這些記錄由數以千計的業餘自然觀察者記下。"},{"en":"Taken by thousands of means recorded, collected or written down by a very large number of people.","zh":"taken by thousands of 指由非常多人記錄、收集或寫下。"},{"en":"Photos taken by thousands of volunteers can help map flood damage.","zh":"由數以千計義工拍攝的照片可以幫助繪製水災破壞地圖。"},{"en":"Data taken by many observers can cover more places than one scientist could visit alone.","zh":"由許多觀察者記下的數據，可以涵蓋比一位科學家獨自到訪更多的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when many people contribute observations.","zh":"當許多人貢獻觀察時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"systematic projects","meaning":"有系統的項目","examples":[{"en":"More systematic projects have also started up.","zh":"更多有系統的項目也已開始運作。"},{"en":"Systematic projects are organised projects that follow clear methods and regular procedures.","zh":"systematic projects 指遵循清楚方法和定期程序的有組織項目。"},{"en":"A school may run a systematic project to track students’ reading progress every month.","zh":"學校可能推行有系統的項目，每月追蹤學生閱讀進度。"},{"en":"Systematic projects produce better data because everyone records information in the same way.","zh":"有系統的項目產生更好數據，因為每個人以相同方式記錄資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when work is planned and structured.","zh":"當工作有計劃和結構時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"start up","meaning":"開展；開始運作","examples":[{"en":"Several recording projects have started up.","zh":"幾個記錄項目已經開展。"},{"en":"Start up means begin operating or begin to exist.","zh":"start up 指開始運作或開始存在。"},{"en":"A new homework club may start up when many students ask for after-school help.","zh":"當許多學生要求課後支援，新的功課小組可能會開展。"},{"en":"Projects start up when people see a need and organise a response.","zh":"當人們看見需要並組織回應，項目就會開始運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a group, project or activity begins.","zh":"當團體、項目或活動開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an overwhelming response","meaning":"熱烈得令人難以應付的反應","examples":[{"en":"The new projects have produced an overwhelming response.","zh":"新項目引起了熱烈得令人難以應付的反應。"},{"en":"An overwhelming response is a reaction so large that it is difficult to manage.","zh":"overwhelming response 指大到難以處理的反應。"},{"en":"A school charity drive may receive an overwhelming response if hundreds of families donate items.","zh":"如果數百個家庭捐贈物品，學校慈善活動可能得到熱烈得令人難以應付的反應。"},{"en":"Such a response can be encouraging, but it may also create too much work for organisers.","zh":"這種反應令人鼓舞，但也可能為組織者帶來太多工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when interest or participation is surprisingly high.","zh":"當興趣或參與度出乎意料地高時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the amount of interest","meaning":"關注程度；興趣之大","examples":[{"en":"The amount of interest in the projects is almost frightening.","zh":"人們對這些項目的關注程度幾乎令人害怕。"},{"en":"The amount of interest means how much attention, curiosity or participation something receives.","zh":"amount of interest 指某事獲得多少注意、好奇或參與。"},{"en":"A new course may surprise a school by the amount of interest from students.","zh":"新課程可能因學生興趣之大而令學校意外。"},{"en":"High interest can show public support, but it can also create pressure to manage responses.","zh":"高關注度可以顯示公眾支持，但也可能造成處理回應的壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when measuring how strongly people care about something.","zh":"衡量人們有多關心某事時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"climate researcher","meaning":"氣候研究員","examples":[{"en":"Sparks is a climate researcher at the Centre for Ecology and Hydrology.","zh":"Sparks 是生態學與水文學中心的氣候研究員。"},{"en":"A climate researcher is a scientist who studies climate patterns and long-term environmental change.","zh":"climate researcher 指研究氣候模式和長期環境變化的科學家。"},{"en":"A climate researcher may compare old flowering dates with temperature records.","zh":"氣候研究員可能把舊開花日期與氣溫記錄比較。"},{"en":"Climate researchers use data to understand how warming affects people, plants and animals.","zh":"氣候研究員使用數據來理解暖化如何影響人、植物和動物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing scientific work on climate.","zh":"討論氣候方面的科學工作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ecology and hydrology","meaning":"生態學與水文學","examples":[{"en":"The Centre for Ecology and Hydrology is based in Cambridgeshire.","zh":"生態學與水文學中心位於 Cambridgeshire。"},{"en":"Ecology and hydrology are fields that study living systems and water systems.","zh":"ecology and hydrology 指研究生物系統和水系統的領域。"},{"en":"A researcher in ecology and hydrology may study how rainfall affects wetlands and wildlife.","zh":"生態學與水文學研究員可能研究降雨如何影響濕地和野生動物。"},{"en":"These fields connect because water changes can strongly affect plants and animals.","zh":"這兩個領域互相關連，因為水的變化會強烈影響植物和動物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when environmental research includes both life and water.","zh":"當環境研究同時包括生命和水時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"become aware of","meaning":"察覺；知道","examples":[{"en":"Sparks first became aware of the amateur records through a colleague.","zh":"Sparks 最初透過一位同事知道這些業餘記錄。"},{"en":"Become aware of means begin to know about or notice something.","zh":"become aware of 指開始知道或注意到某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may become aware of a student’s problem after reading their homework comments.","zh":"老師可能在閱讀學生功課評語後察覺學生的問題。"},{"en":"People often become aware of hidden resources only when someone tells them where to look.","zh":"人們常在有人告訴他們去哪裏找時，才察覺隱藏資源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone first notices important information.","zh":"當某人首次注意到重要資訊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an army of","meaning":"大批；一大群","examples":[{"en":"Sparks discovered an army of “closet phenologists”.","zh":"Sparks 發現了一大群「隱藏身份的物候學愛好者」。"},{"en":"An army of means a very large number of people doing something.","zh":"an army of 指大量正在做某事的人。"},{"en":"A charity event may need an army of volunteers to pack food and answer questions.","zh":"慈善活動可能需要大批義工包裝食物和回答問題。"},{"en":"An army of observers can collect far more local data than one research team.","zh":"一大群觀察者可以收集比一個研究團隊更多的本地數據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when emphasising a large group working in the same area.","zh":"強調大量人員在同一領域工作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"closet phenologists","meaning":"隱藏身份的物候學愛好者","examples":[{"en":"Sparks describes hidden amateur recorders as “closet phenologists”.","zh":"Sparks 把隱藏的業餘記錄者描述為「隱藏身份的物候學愛好者」。"},{"en":"Closet phenologists are people who record natural events privately without seeing themselves as scientists.","zh":"closet phenologists 指私下記錄自然事件，但不把自己視為科學家的人。"},{"en":"A gardener who quietly notes first flowering dates every year may be a closet phenologist.","zh":"每年默默記下首次開花日期的園丁，可能是隱藏身份的物候學愛好者。"},{"en":"They become important when researchers discover that their private notes form long-term data.","zh":"當研究人員發現他們的私人筆記構成長期數據，他們就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when hidden hobbyists are actually doing scientific observation.","zh":"當隱藏的興趣愛好者其實在做科學觀察時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a retiring colleague","meaning":"即將退休的同事","examples":[{"en":"A retiring colleague gave Sparks the Marsham records.","zh":"一位即將退休的同事把 Marsham 記錄交給 Sparks。"},{"en":"A retiring colleague is a co-worker who is leaving work permanently, usually because of age or career stage.","zh":"retiring colleague 指即將永久離開工作的同事，通常因年齡或職業階段。"},{"en":"A retiring teacher may pass old lesson files to younger colleagues.","zh":"即將退休的老師可能把舊教材檔案交給較年輕同事。"},{"en":"Important knowledge can be transferred when retiring colleagues share records before they leave.","zh":"當即將退休的同事離開前分享記錄，重要知識就能被轉移。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a person near retirement passes on work or information.","zh":"當接近退休的人傳遞工作或資訊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"follow leads","meaning":"追查線索","examples":[{"en":"Sparks follows leads from one historical data set to another.","zh":"Sparks 從一個歷史數據集追查線索到另一個。"},{"en":"Follow leads means pursue clues that may guide you to more information.","zh":"follow leads 指追尋可能引導你找到更多資訊的線索。"},{"en":"A journalist may follow leads from one interview to another until the full story appears.","zh":"記者可能從一個訪問追查線索到另一個，直到完整故事出現。"},{"en":"Researchers follow leads because one archive can point to another hidden source.","zh":"研究人員追查線索，因為一個檔案可能指向另一個隱藏來源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when investigation moves from clue to clue.","zh":"當調查從一條線索移向另一條時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"historical data set","meaning":"歷史數據集","examples":[{"en":"He spends much of his time studying historical data sets.","zh":"他花很多時間研究歷史數據集。"},{"en":"A historical data set is an organised collection of information from the past.","zh":"historical data set 指來自過去並被組織起來的資料集合。"},{"en":"A hospital may keep a historical data set of patient numbers over fifty years.","zh":"醫院可能保存五十年來病人數目的歷史數據集。"},{"en":"Historical data sets help researchers compare present patterns with past ones.","zh":"歷史數據集幫助研究人員把現時模式與過去模式比較。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when old information is analysed systematically.","zh":"當舊資料被有系統地分析時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as news of his quest spreads","meaning":"隨着他的尋找行動傳開","examples":[{"en":"As news of his quest spreads, people send Sparks more records.","zh":"隨着他的尋找行動傳開，人們把更多記錄寄給 Sparks。"},{"en":"As news of his quest spreads means when more people hear about his search or project.","zh":"as news of his quest spreads 指當更多人聽到他的尋找行動或項目時。"},{"en":"As news of a lost dog spreads, neighbours may begin checking gardens and streets.","zh":"隨着尋找失犬的消息傳開，鄰居可能開始檢查花園和街道。"},{"en":"Public attention can bring hidden records to light when people learn what researchers need.","zh":"當人們知道研究人員需要甚麼，公眾注意可以令隱藏記錄曝光。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when information spreads and creates new responses.","zh":"當資訊傳開並引發新回應時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tip someone off to","meaning":"向某人透露……的線索","examples":[{"en":"People tip Sparks off to other historical records.","zh":"人們向 Sparks 透露其他歷史記錄的線索。"},{"en":"Tip someone off to means give someone useful information about something they may not know.","zh":"tip someone off to 指向某人提供他可能不知道的有用資訊。"},{"en":"A student may tip a teacher off to a broken classroom projector before the lesson starts.","zh":"學生可能在上課前向老師透露課室投影機壞了的線索。"},{"en":"Tips help researchers find records that are hidden in private homes or local archives.","zh":"線索幫助研究人員找到藏在私人家中或地方檔案中的記錄。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone provides a helpful clue.","zh":"當有人提供有用線索時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"come out of their closets","meaning":"公開身份；走出隱藏狀態","examples":[{"en":"More amateur phenologists come out of their closets when they hear about the project.","zh":"更多業餘物候學愛好者聽到這個項目後走出隱藏狀態。"},{"en":"Come out of their closets means stop hiding an interest or identity and reveal it publicly.","zh":"come out of their closets 指不再隱藏某種興趣或身份，並公開出來。"},{"en":"A student who secretly writes poems may come out of their closet after joining a writing club.","zh":"秘密寫詩的學生加入寫作學會後，可能公開自己的興趣。"},{"en":"People reveal hidden hobbies when they feel their work is valued.","zh":"當人們覺得自己的工作被重視，就會揭示隱藏的興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when private interests become publicly known.","zh":"當私人興趣變得公開時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"devotion to recording and collecting","meaning":"對記錄和收藏的熱衷","examples":[{"en":"The British devotion to recording and collecting makes Sparks’s job easier.","zh":"英國人對記錄和收藏的熱衷使 Sparks 的工作更容易。"},{"en":"Devotion to recording and collecting means strong commitment to writing things down and preserving them.","zh":"devotion to recording and collecting 指對寫下和保存事物有強烈投入。"},{"en":"A family’s devotion to recording birthdays can create a useful family history.","zh":"一個家庭對記錄生日的熱衷可以形成有用的家族歷史。"},{"en":"Such devotion helps research because old details are not lost.","zh":"這種熱衷有助研究，因為舊細節不會流失。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when careful record-keeping becomes valuable.","zh":"當細心保存記錄變得有價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"30 years’ worth of","meaning":"長達三十年的……","examples":[{"en":"A man sent Sparks 30 years’ worth of kitchen calendars.","zh":"一名男子寄給 Sparks 長達三十年的廚房月曆。"},{"en":"30 years’ worth of means an amount collected over thirty years.","zh":"30 years’ worth of 指三十年間累積下來的數量。"},{"en":"A teacher may keep 30 years’ worth of student thank-you cards in a box.","zh":"老師可能在盒子裏保存長達三十年的學生感謝卡。"},{"en":"Long collections are valuable because they show change over time.","zh":"長期收藏有價值，因為它們顯示隨時間發生的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing the length and amount of accumulated material.","zh":"顯示累積材料的時間長度和數量時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"kitchen calendars","meaning":"廚房月曆","examples":[{"en":"The kitchen calendars contained notes about a magnolia tree.","zh":"這些廚房月曆載有關於一棵木蘭樹的筆記。"},{"en":"Kitchen calendars are calendars kept at home, often used to mark appointments, reminders or observations.","zh":"kitchen calendars 指家中使用的月曆，常用來標記事件、提醒或觀察。"},{"en":"A family may write school events and medical appointments on kitchen calendars.","zh":"家庭可能把學校活動和醫療預約寫在廚房月曆上。"},{"en":"Kitchen calendars can become records if people note the same natural event each year.","zh":"如果人們每年記下同一自然事件，廚房月曆可以成為記錄。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when ordinary household items preserve information.","zh":"當普通家居物品保存資訊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"note the date that","meaning":"記下……的日期","examples":[{"en":"The man noted the date that his neighbour’s magnolia tree flowered.","zh":"這名男子記下鄰居木蘭樹開花的日期。"},{"en":"Note the date that means write down the exact day when something happened.","zh":"note the date that 指寫下某事發生的確實日期。"},{"en":"A gardener may note the date that tomatoes first appear on the plant.","zh":"園丁可能記下番茄首次在植株上出現的日期。"},{"en":"Dates become useful when the same event is recorded year after year.","zh":"當同一事件年復年被記錄，日期就變得有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when timing needs to be remembered accurately.","zh":"當需要準確記住時間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"magnolia tree","meaning":"木蘭樹","examples":[{"en":"The neighbour’s magnolia tree flowered on different dates each year.","zh":"鄰居的木蘭樹每年在不同日期開花。"},{"en":"A magnolia tree is a tree known for large, attractive flowers, often appearing in spring.","zh":"magnolia tree 指以大型美麗花朵聞名的樹，通常在春天開花。"},{"en":"A family may notice a magnolia tree blooming outside their window every March.","zh":"一個家庭可能每年三月注意到窗外的木蘭樹開花。"},{"en":"Changes in its flowering date can show how local spring conditions vary.","zh":"它開花日期的變化可以顯示本地春季條件如何不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a single familiar tree becomes a natural record.","zh":"當一棵熟悉的樹成為自然記錄時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"unearth data from","meaning":"從……發掘數據","examples":[{"en":"Other researchers have unearthed data from equally odd sources.","zh":"其他研究人員也從同樣不尋常的來源發掘數據。"},{"en":"Unearth data from means discover useful information in a place where people may not expect it.","zh":"unearth data from 指在意想不到的地方發現有用資訊。"},{"en":"A historian may unearth data from old shop receipts and family letters.","zh":"歷史學家可能從舊商店收據和家書中發掘數據。"},{"en":"Data are unearthed when researchers look beyond official scientific records.","zh":"當研究人員不只查看正式科學記錄，數據就可能被發掘出來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when hidden information is discovered.","zh":"當隱藏資訊被發現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"odd sources","meaning":"不尋常的來源","examples":[{"en":"Useful climate data can come from odd sources.","zh":"有用的氣候數據可以來自不尋常的來源。"},{"en":"Odd sources are unusual or unexpected places where information can be found.","zh":"odd sources 指可以找到資料的不尋常或意想不到地方。"},{"en":"A teacher may find useful examples in odd sources such as shopping receipts or bus notices.","zh":"老師可能從購物收據或巴士告示等不尋常來源找到有用例子。"},{"en":"Odd sources can be valuable because they record real life in ways official documents do not.","zh":"不尋常來源可以有價值，因為它們以官方文件沒有的方式記錄真實生活。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence comes from surprising materials.","zh":"當證據來自令人驚訝的材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"study records of","meaning":"研究……的記錄","examples":[{"en":"Rafe Sagarin studied records of an Alaskan betting contest.","zh":"Rafe Sagarin 研究一項阿拉斯加博彩比賽的記錄。"},{"en":"Study records of means examine written information about a particular event, activity or pattern.","zh":"study records of 指檢查關於某事件、活動或模式的書面資料。"},{"en":"A school may study records of late arrivals to improve transport arrangements.","zh":"學校可能研究遲到記錄，以改善交通安排。"},{"en":"Studying records helps researchers find patterns that were not obvious at first.","zh":"研究記錄幫助研究人員找出起初不明顯的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when past information is analysed.","zh":"當過去資料被分析時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"participants attempt to","meaning":"參加者嘗試……","examples":[{"en":"Participants attempt to guess the exact time of the thaw.","zh":"參加者嘗試猜中融冰的確實時間。"},{"en":"Participants attempt to means people taking part try to do something.","zh":"participants attempt to 指參與者嘗試做某事。"},{"en":"In a school competition, participants attempt to solve puzzles within ten minutes.","zh":"在學校比賽中，參加者嘗試在十分鐘內解謎。"},{"en":"Attempts matter because the contest creates a record of guesses and results each year.","zh":"這些嘗試很重要，因為比賽每年產生猜測和結果記錄。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing what people in an activity try to do.","zh":"描述活動參加者嘗試做甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"guess the exact time","meaning":"猜中確實時間","examples":[{"en":"Participants try to guess the exact time at which the tripod will fall.","zh":"參加者嘗試猜中三腳架倒下的確實時間。"},{"en":"Guess the exact time means predict the precise moment when something will happen.","zh":"guess the exact time 指預測某事發生的精確時刻。"},{"en":"Children may try to guess the exact time a cake will be ready without checking the oven.","zh":"孩子可能不看焗爐，嘗試猜中蛋糕完成的確實時間。"},{"en":"Exact guesses become useful data when the real time is recorded each year.","zh":"當每年記錄真實時間，精確猜測就成為有用數據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when timing is central to a contest or prediction.","zh":"當時間是比賽或預測核心時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a specially erected wooden tripod","meaning":"特別豎立的木製三腳架","examples":[{"en":"A specially erected wooden tripod stands on the river.","zh":"一個特別豎立的木製三腳架站在河上。"},{"en":"A specially erected wooden tripod is a three-legged wooden structure put up for a particular purpose.","zh":"specially erected wooden tripod 指為特定目的搭建的三腳木製結構。"},{"en":"Workers may build a specially erected wooden frame to mark a construction site.","zh":"工人可能建起特別豎立的木架來標示建築地盤。"},{"en":"In the contest, the tripod marks the moment when river ice becomes weak enough to break.","zh":"在比賽中，三腳架標記河冰弱到足以破裂的時刻。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an object is deliberately set up for measurement or ceremony.","zh":"當物件被刻意設置作測量或儀式用途時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fall through the surface of","meaning":"穿過……表面掉下去","examples":[{"en":"The tripod falls through the surface of a thawing river.","zh":"三腳架穿過正在融冰的河面掉下去。"},{"en":"Fall through the surface of means drop down after breaking or passing through the top layer.","zh":"fall through the surface of 指穿破或穿過上層表面後向下掉落。"},{"en":"A child’s foot may fall through the surface of thin snow covering a hole.","zh":"孩子的腳可能穿過覆蓋洞口的薄雪表面掉下去。"},{"en":"The tripod falls through when the ice becomes too weak to support it.","zh":"當冰太弱而無法支撐三腳架，它就會穿過表面掉下去。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something breaks through a surface and drops below.","zh":"當某物破開表面並掉到下方時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a thawing river","meaning":"正在融冰的河流","examples":[{"en":"The contest takes place on a thawing river in Alaska.","zh":"這項比賽在阿拉斯加一條正在融冰的河流上舉行。"},{"en":"A thawing river is a river whose ice is melting as temperatures rise.","zh":"thawing river 指隨氣溫上升而冰層正在融化的河流。"},{"en":"People may avoid walking on a thawing river because the ice can become weak.","zh":"人們可能避免走在正在融冰的河流上，因為冰層可能變弱。"},{"en":"A thawing river provides visible evidence that winter is ending.","zh":"正在融冰的河流提供冬天即將結束的可見證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing ice melt and seasonal change.","zh":"討論融冰和季節變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take place annually","meaning":"每年舉行","examples":[{"en":"The competition has taken place annually since 1917.","zh":"這項比賽自1917年起每年舉行。"},{"en":"Take place annually means happen once every year.","zh":"take place annually 指每年發生一次。"},{"en":"A school sports day may take place annually in November.","zh":"學校運動會可能每年十一月舉行。"},{"en":"Annual events create useful records because the same thing is observed repeatedly.","zh":"年度事件會創造有用記錄，因為同一事情被反覆觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an event happens every year.","zh":"當活動每年發生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"analysis of the results","meaning":"對結果的分析","examples":[{"en":"Analysis of the results showed that the thaw now arrives earlier.","zh":"對結果的分析顯示融冰期現在更早到來。"},{"en":"Analysis of the results means careful study of the collected outcomes to find meaning or patterns.","zh":"analysis of the results 指仔細研究收集到的結果，以找出意義或模式。"},{"en":"Analysis of test results can show which grammar points students still misunderstand.","zh":"對測驗結果的分析可以顯示學生仍誤解哪些文法點。"},{"en":"In the contest, analysis revealed a long-term change in thaw timing.","zh":"在這項比賽中，分析揭示融冰時間的長期變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when raw results are studied for conclusions.","zh":"當原始結果被研究以得出結論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the thaw","meaning":"融冰期","examples":[{"en":"The thaw now arrives earlier than it did in the past.","zh":"融冰期現在比過去更早到來。"},{"en":"The thaw is the time when ice or snow melts after winter.","zh":"thaw 指冬天後冰雪融化的時期。"},{"en":"Farmers may wait for the thaw before preparing fields in cold regions.","zh":"在寒冷地區，農民可能等待融冰期後才準備田地。"},{"en":"An earlier thaw can show that winter conditions are ending sooner.","zh":"較早的融冰期可以顯示冬季條件更早結束。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing seasonal melting.","zh":"討論季節性融化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"five days earlier than","meaning":"比……早五天","examples":[{"en":"The thaw now arrives five days earlier than it did before.","zh":"融冰期現在比以前早五天到來。"},{"en":"Five days earlier than means happening five days before a previous or expected time.","zh":"five days earlier than 指比過去或預期時間早五天發生。"},{"en":"A school trip may be moved five days earlier than planned because of bad weather.","zh":"因為天氣惡劣，學校旅行可能比原定時間早五天舉行。"},{"en":"A shift of five days can matter in nature if plants and animals depend on timing.","zh":"如果植物和動物依賴時間安排，五天的轉變在自然界中也可以很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing exact timing.","zh":"比較確切時間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Compared with 20 years ago, many natural events now occur earlier.","zh":"與二十年前相比，許多自然事件現在更早發生。"},{"en":"Compared with means when one thing is considered in relation to another.","zh":"compared with 指把一件事與另一件事放在一起考慮。"},{"en":"Compared with last term, the class now writes essays more confidently.","zh":"與上學期相比，這班現在寫作文更有信心。"},{"en":"Comparisons help reveal change because they show what is different from the past.","zh":"比較幫助揭示變化，因為它顯示與過去有何不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when two times, groups or situations are being compared.","zh":"比較兩個時間、群體或情況時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a raft of","meaning":"大量；一連串","examples":[{"en":"A raft of natural events now occur earlier across the northern hemisphere.","zh":"大量自然事件現在在北半球大部分地區更早發生。"},{"en":"A raft of means a large number of things.","zh":"a raft of 指大量或一連串事物。"},{"en":"A new school policy may create a raft of questions from parents.","zh":"新校政可能引起家長一連串問題。"},{"en":"A raft of similar observations is more convincing than one isolated example.","zh":"大量相似觀察比單一孤立例子更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when many related examples appear together.","zh":"當許多相關例子一起出現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"natural events","meaning":"自然事件","examples":[{"en":"The records show that many natural events now happen earlier.","zh":"記錄顯示許多自然事件現在更早發生。"},{"en":"Natural events are things that happen in nature, such as flowering, migration, thawing or hibernation ending.","zh":"natural events 指自然界中發生的事情，例如開花、遷徙、融冰或冬眠結束。"},{"en":"A class may record natural events in the school garden throughout the year.","zh":"一班學生可能全年記錄學校花園中的自然事件。"},{"en":"Changes in natural events can show how climate affects living systems.","zh":"自然事件的變化可以顯示氣候如何影響生命系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing observable changes in nature.","zh":"討論自然界可觀察變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"occur earlier","meaning":"更早發生","examples":[{"en":"Many natural events occur earlier than they did 20 years ago.","zh":"許多自然事件比二十年前更早發生。"},{"en":"Occur earlier means happen sooner than before or sooner than expected.","zh":"occur earlier 指比以前或比預期更早發生。"},{"en":"Exams may occur earlier this year if the school calendar changes.","zh":"如果校曆改變，今年考試可能更早發生。"},{"en":"Flowers may occur earlier in spring when temperatures rise sooner.","zh":"當氣溫更早上升，春天花朵可能更早出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when timing shifts forward.","zh":"當時間向前移時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"across much of","meaning":"遍及……大部分地區","examples":[{"en":"These changes are seen across much of the northern hemisphere.","zh":"這些變化見於北半球大部分地區。"},{"en":"Across much of means over a large part of an area.","zh":"across much of 指遍布某地區的大部分範圍。"},{"en":"Heavy rain may fall across much of the city during a typhoon.","zh":"颱風期間，大雨可能遍及城市大部分地區。"},{"en":"A pattern seen across much of a region is harder to dismiss as a local accident.","zh":"如果某模式遍及一個地區大部分地方，就較難被視為本地偶然現象。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a change covers a wide area.","zh":"當變化覆蓋廣闊區域時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the northern hemisphere","meaning":"北半球","examples":[{"en":"The pattern appears across much of the northern hemisphere.","zh":"這個模式出現在北半球大部分地區。"},{"en":"The northern hemisphere is the half of Earth north of the equator.","zh":"northern hemisphere 指地球赤道以北的一半。"},{"en":"Europe, North America and much of Asia are in the northern hemisphere.","zh":"歐洲、北美和亞洲大部分地區位於北半球。"},{"en":"Seasonal patterns in the northern hemisphere can be compared across many countries.","zh":"北半球的季節模式可以在許多國家之間比較。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing global geography and climate patterns.","zh":"討論全球地理和氣候模式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the opening of leaves","meaning":"樹葉展開","examples":[{"en":"The opening of leaves now happens earlier in many places.","zh":"樹葉展開現在在許多地方更早發生。"},{"en":"The opening of leaves means leaves unfolding from buds at the start of the growing season.","zh":"opening of leaves 指生長季開始時葉子從芽中展開。"},{"en":"Children may notice the opening of leaves on trees outside school after warm spring days.","zh":"春天暖和幾天後，孩子可能注意到學校外樹木的樹葉展開。"},{"en":"Earlier leaf opening can indicate that spring temperatures are rising sooner.","zh":"較早樹葉展開可以顯示春季氣溫更早上升。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when tracking plant responses to seasons.","zh":"追蹤植物對季節的反應時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the return of birds from migration","meaning":"鳥類遷徙後回歸","examples":[{"en":"The return of birds from migration is one event recorded by amateurs.","zh":"鳥類遷徙後回歸是業餘人士記錄的事件之一。"},{"en":"The return of birds from migration means birds coming back after travelling to another region for a season.","zh":"return of birds from migration 指鳥類在某季節前往另一地區後回來。"},{"en":"Villagers may record the return of swallows from migration each spring.","zh":"村民可能每年春天記錄燕子遷徙後回歸。"},{"en":"If birds return earlier, it may show that seasonal conditions are changing.","zh":"如果鳥類較早回歸，可能顯示季節條件正在改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when studying bird movement and climate timing.","zh":"研究鳥類移動和氣候時間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the emergence of butterflies from hibernation","meaning":"蝴蝶從冬眠中出現","examples":[{"en":"The emergence of butterflies from hibernation may now occur earlier.","zh":"蝴蝶從冬眠中出現現在可能更早發生。"},{"en":"The emergence of butterflies from hibernation means butterflies becoming active again after a winter rest period.","zh":"emergence of butterflies from hibernation 指蝴蝶在冬季休眠後再次活躍。"},{"en":"A gardener may notice the emergence of butterflies from hibernation on the first warm days of spring.","zh":"園丁可能在春天最初幾個暖日注意到蝴蝶從冬眠中出現。"},{"en":"Warmer weather can cause butterflies to emerge earlier than in colder years.","zh":"較暖天氣可以令蝴蝶比寒冷年份更早出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when studying seasonal insect activity.","zh":"研究昆蟲季節性活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hint at","meaning":"暗示；顯示……的跡象","examples":[{"en":"The data can hint at how nature will change in the future.","zh":"這些數據可以暗示自然將來會如何改變。"},{"en":"Hint at means suggest something indirectly without proving it completely.","zh":"hint at 指間接提示某事，但未完全證明。"},{"en":"A student’s tired face may hint at a lack of sleep.","zh":"學生疲倦的臉可能顯示睡眠不足的跡象。"},{"en":"Early flowering records may hint at wider climate changes.","zh":"較早開花記錄可能暗示更廣泛的氣候變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence suggests a possibility but does not give a full answer.","zh":"當證據提示一種可能但未給出完整答案時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"together with","meaning":"連同……；與……一起","examples":[{"en":"Together with climate models, amateur records could help guide conservation.","zh":"連同氣候模型，業餘記錄可以幫助指導保育工作。"},{"en":"Together with means combined with or used alongside something else.","zh":"together with 指與另一事物結合或一起使用。"},{"en":"A teacher may use quizzes together with homework to understand student progress.","zh":"老師可能把小測連同功課一起使用，以了解學生進度。"},{"en":"Amateur records become more powerful together with climate models because each supports the other.","zh":"業餘記錄連同氣候模型會更有力，因為兩者互相支援。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when two sources or methods work together.","zh":"當兩種來源或方法一起運作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"models of climate change","meaning":"氣候變化模型","examples":[{"en":"Researchers combine amateur records with models of climate change.","zh":"研究人員把業餘記錄與氣候變化模型結合。"},{"en":"Models of climate change are scientific tools used to estimate how climate may change in the future.","zh":"models of climate change 指用來估計未來氣候如何改變的科學工具。"},{"en":"Scientists may use climate models to predict future droughts or warmer winters.","zh":"科學家可能使用氣候模型預測未來乾旱或較暖冬天。"},{"en":"Models become more useful when tested against real observations from the past.","zh":"當模型以過去真實觀察檢驗，它們就變得更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing scientific prediction of climate effects.","zh":"討論氣候影響的科學預測時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"guide conservation","meaning":"指導保育工作","examples":[{"en":"Amateurs’ records could help guide conservation.","zh":"業餘人士的記錄可以幫助指導保育工作。"},{"en":"Guide conservation means help decide how to protect plants, animals and habitats.","zh":"guide conservation 指幫助決定如何保護植物、動物和棲息地。"},{"en":"Bird records can guide conservation by showing which wetlands need protection.","zh":"鳥類記錄可以透過顯示哪些濕地需要保護來指導保育工作。"},{"en":"Good data guide conservation because they show where risks are greatest.","zh":"良好數據能指導保育工作，因為它顯示風險最大的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence supports environmental protection decisions.","zh":"當證據支援環境保護決策時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"birdwatchers’ counts","meaning":"觀鳥人士的點算記錄","examples":[{"en":"Root collected birdwatchers’ counts of wildfowl.","zh":"Root 收集觀鳥人士對野禽的點算記錄。"},{"en":"Birdwatchers’ counts are numbers of birds recorded by people who observe birds.","zh":"birdwatchers’ counts 指觀察鳥類的人記錄下來的鳥類數目。"},{"en":"A birdwatcher may count ducks on a pond every Sunday morning.","zh":"觀鳥人士可能每星期日上午點算池塘上的鴨子。"},{"en":"These counts help scientists track whether bird populations are rising or falling.","zh":"這些點算記錄幫助科學家追蹤鳥類數量是上升還是下降。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when amateur counting becomes scientific data.","zh":"當業餘點算變成科學數據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"wildfowl","meaning":"野禽","examples":[{"en":"Wildfowl were counted on seasonal ponds in the American Midwest.","zh":"野禽在美國中西部的季節性池塘上被點算。"},{"en":"Wildfowl are wild water birds such as ducks and geese.","zh":"wildfowl 指野生水鳥，例如鴨和鵝。"},{"en":"Families may see wildfowl resting on a lake during winter.","zh":"家庭可能在冬天看見野禽在湖上休息。"},{"en":"Wildfowl populations can decline if ponds dry up during breeding season.","zh":"如果池塘在繁殖季節乾涸，野禽種群可能下降。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing birds that live near water.","zh":"討論生活在水邊的鳥類時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"seasonal ponds","meaning":"季節性池塘","examples":[{"en":"The bird counts were taken on seasonal ponds.","zh":"鳥類點算在季節性池塘上進行。"},{"en":"Seasonal ponds are ponds that appear or fill with water only during certain seasons.","zh":"seasonal ponds 指只在某些季節出現或有水的池塘。"},{"en":"A seasonal pond may form after spring rain and dry up in late summer.","zh":"季節性池塘可能在春雨後形成，並在夏末乾涸。"},{"en":"Water birds depend on seasonal ponds for feeding and breeding in some regions.","zh":"在某些地區，水鳥依靠季節性池塘覓食和繁殖。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when water habitats change with the seasons.","zh":"當水域棲息地隨季節變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the American Midwest","meaning":"美國中西部","examples":[{"en":"The records came from ponds in the American Midwest.","zh":"這些記錄來自美國中西部的池塘。"},{"en":"The American Midwest is a region in the central northern United States.","zh":"American Midwest 指美國中北部的一個地區。"},{"en":"States such as Iowa, Illinois and Minnesota are often associated with the American Midwest.","zh":"Iowa、Illinois 和 Minnesota 等州常與美國中西部相關。"},{"en":"Wetlands in the American Midwest can be important for migratory and breeding birds.","zh":"美國中西部的濕地對遷徙和繁殖鳥類可能很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying a broad US region.","zh":"識別美國一個廣闊地區時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"models of future warming","meaning":"未來氣候暖化模型","examples":[{"en":"Root combined bird counts with models of future warming.","zh":"Root 把鳥類點算與未來氣候暖化模型結合。"},{"en":"Models of future warming are scientific predictions of how temperatures may rise in coming years.","zh":"models of future warming 指對未來年份氣溫可能如何上升的科學預測。"},{"en":"City planners may use models of future warming to prepare for heatwaves.","zh":"城市規劃者可能使用未來氣候暖化模型來準備應對熱浪。"},{"en":"These models help scientists estimate how droughts may affect birds and wetlands.","zh":"這些模型幫助科學家估計乾旱會如何影響鳥類和濕地。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when future temperature rise is being predicted.","zh":"當預測未來氣溫上升時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"increased droughts","meaning":"加劇的乾旱","examples":[{"en":"Increased droughts could reduce breeding populations.","zh":"加劇的乾旱可能減少繁殖群體。"},{"en":"Increased droughts means more frequent or more severe periods with too little rain.","zh":"increased droughts 指缺雨時期變得更頻繁或更嚴重。"},{"en":"Farmers may struggle if increased droughts reduce water for crops.","zh":"如果加劇的乾旱減少農作物用水，農民可能陷入困難。"},{"en":"Increased droughts can dry ponds and reduce places where birds breed.","zh":"加劇的乾旱可以令池塘乾涸，減少鳥類繁殖地點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when lack of rain becomes more common or serious.","zh":"當缺雨變得更常見或更嚴重時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"halve the breeding populations","meaning":"令繁殖群體減半","examples":[{"en":"Increased droughts could halve the breeding populations at the ponds.","zh":"加劇的乾旱可能令池塘上的繁殖群體減半。"},{"en":"Halve the breeding populations means reduce the number of breeding animals by fifty percent.","zh":"halve the breeding populations 指把繁殖動物數量減少百分之五十。"},{"en":"A disease could halve the breeding population of fish in a small lake.","zh":"疾病可能令小湖中的魚類繁殖群體減半。"},{"en":"If ponds dry up, fewer birds can raise young, so breeding populations may fall sharply.","zh":"如果池塘乾涸，能養育幼鳥的鳥類就更少，因此繁殖群體可能大幅下降。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a population is reduced by half.","zh":"當種群數量減少一半時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"breeding populations","meaning":"繁殖群體","examples":[{"en":"The breeding populations at the ponds may decline sharply.","zh":"池塘上的繁殖群體可能急劇下降。"},{"en":"Breeding populations are groups of animals that reproduce in a particular area.","zh":"breeding populations 指在某特定地區繁殖的動物群體。"},{"en":"A wetland may support breeding populations of ducks during spring.","zh":"濕地可能在春天支援鴨子的繁殖群體。"},{"en":"If food or nesting space disappears, breeding populations can fall quickly.","zh":"如果食物或築巢空間消失，繁殖群體可以快速下降。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when studying animals that reproduce in a habitat.","zh":"研究在棲息地中繁殖的動物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"waterfowl","meaning":"水禽","examples":[{"en":"The number of waterfowl in North America may drop significantly.","zh":"北美水禽數量可能大幅下降。"},{"en":"Waterfowl are birds that live on or near water, especially ducks and geese.","zh":"waterfowl 指生活在水上或水邊的鳥類，尤其是鴨和鵝。"},{"en":"Visitors may feed waterfowl at a park pond, although this is not always recommended.","zh":"遊客可能在公園池塘餵水禽，雖然這並不總是被建議。"},{"en":"Waterfowl depend on wetlands, so drought can reduce their breeding success.","zh":"水禽依賴濕地，因此乾旱可以降低牠們的繁殖成功率。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing water birds and wetland habitats.","zh":"討論水鳥和濕地棲息地時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"drop significantly","meaning":"大幅下降","examples":[{"en":"The number of waterfowl may drop significantly with global warming.","zh":"隨着全球暖化，水禽數量可能大幅下降。"},{"en":"Drop significantly means fall by a large or important amount.","zh":"drop significantly 指下降幅度大或重要。"},{"en":"A shop’s sales may drop significantly if a nearby road closes for months.","zh":"如果附近道路封閉數月，商店銷售可能大幅下降。"},{"en":"Bird numbers can drop significantly when breeding habitats dry out.","zh":"當繁殖棲息地乾涸，鳥類數量可能大幅下降。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a decrease is serious, not minor.","zh":"當下降嚴重而非輕微時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"global warming","meaning":"全球暖化","examples":[{"en":"Global warming may affect waterfowl populations in North America.","zh":"全球暖化可能影響北美水禽種群。"},{"en":"Global warming is the long-term rise in Earth’s average temperature.","zh":"global warming 指地球平均氣溫的長期上升。"},{"en":"Global warming can make heatwaves more common and winters shorter.","zh":"全球暖化可以令熱浪更常見、冬天更短。"},{"en":"It affects wildlife because temperature changes can alter habitats and food supplies.","zh":"它影響野生動物，因為氣溫變化可以改變棲息地和食物供應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing rising global temperatures.","zh":"討論全球氣溫上升時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not all professionals are happy to","meaning":"並非所有專業人士都樂意……","examples":[{"en":"Not all professionals are happy to use amateur data.","zh":"並非所有專業人士都樂意使用業餘數據。"},{"en":"Not all professionals are happy to means some experts are unwilling or doubtful about doing something.","zh":"not all professionals are happy to 指有些專家不願意或懷疑是否應做某事。"},{"en":"Not all teachers are happy to replace books with tablets in class.","zh":"並非所有老師都樂意在課堂上用平板電腦取代書本。"},{"en":"Professionals may hesitate when evidence is useful but collected in uneven ways.","zh":"當證據有用但收集方式不一致，專業人士可能會猶豫。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing mixed expert attitudes.","zh":"顯示專家態度不一致時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"amateur data","meaning":"業餘人士收集的數據","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists are reluctant to use amateur data.","zh":"有些科學家不願使用業餘人士收集的數據。"},{"en":"Amateur data are information collected by non-professionals rather than trained researchers.","zh":"amateur data 指由非專業人士而非受訓研究員收集的資料。"},{"en":"Bird counts from local volunteers are one form of amateur data.","zh":"本地義工的鳥類點算是一種業餘人士收集的數據。"},{"en":"Amateur data can be valuable but need checking for accuracy and consistency.","zh":"業餘數據可以有價值，但需要檢查準確性和一致性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when public observations are used in research.","zh":"當公眾觀察被用於研究時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"won’t touch","meaning":"不願使用；避之則吉","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists won’t touch amateur data because of its problems.","zh":"有些科學家因業餘數據問題太多而不願使用。"},{"en":"Won’t touch means refuse to use, accept or deal with something.","zh":"won’t touch 指拒絕使用、接受或處理某物。"},{"en":"A careful teacher won’t touch an answer key if they suspect it contains mistakes.","zh":"如果老師懷疑答案紙有錯，謹慎的老師可能避之則吉。"},{"en":"Scientists may avoid data they believe are too unreliable to analyse.","zh":"科學家可能避免分析他們認為太不可靠的數據。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and useful when someone strongly refuses to use something.","zh":"當某人強烈拒絕使用某物時，這個較口語短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be too full of problems","meaning":"問題太多","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers think amateur records are too full of problems.","zh":"有些研究人員認為業餘記錄問題太多。"},{"en":"Be too full of problems means contain so many difficulties or weaknesses that it may not be useful.","zh":"be too full of problems 指包含太多困難或弱點，以致可能無用。"},{"en":"A survey may be too full of problems if questions are unclear and many answers are missing.","zh":"如果問題不清晰且許多答案缺失，調查可能問題太多。"},{"en":"Data become hard to trust when methods differ too much between recorders.","zh":"當記錄者之間的方法差異太大，數據就變得難以信任。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when flaws may overwhelm value.","zh":"當缺陷可能壓倒價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"different observers","meaning":"不同觀察者","examples":[{"en":"Different observers may define the same event differently.","zh":"不同觀察者可能以不同方式界定同一事件。"},{"en":"Different observers are different people who watch and record the same kind of event.","zh":"different observers 指觀看和記錄同類事件的不同人士。"},{"en":"In a classroom, different observers may describe the same student presentation in different ways.","zh":"在課室中，不同觀察者可能以不同方式描述同一個學生匯報。"},{"en":"Data become less consistent if different observers use different definitions.","zh":"如果不同觀察者使用不同定義，數據就變得較不一致。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when human judgement affects records.","zh":"當人的判斷影響記錄時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"what constitutes","meaning":"甚麼構成……","examples":[{"en":"Observers may disagree about what constitutes an open snowdrop.","zh":"觀察者可能不同意甚麼構成一朵已開花的雪花蓮。"},{"en":"What constitutes means what counts as or what is considered to be something.","zh":"what constitutes 指甚麼算作或被視為某事。"},{"en":"Students may disagree about what constitutes cheating in a group assignment.","zh":"學生可能不同意在小組作業中甚麼構成作弊。"},{"en":"Clear definitions are needed when observers must decide whether an event has occurred.","zh":"當觀察者必須判斷事件是否發生，就需要清楚定義。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when boundaries or criteria are being discussed.","zh":"討論界線或標準時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an open snowdrop","meaning":"已開花的雪花蓮","examples":[{"en":"Different observers may have different ideas of an open snowdrop.","zh":"不同觀察者可能對已開花的雪花蓮有不同理解。"},{"en":"An open snowdrop is a snowdrop flower whose petals have opened enough to be counted as flowering.","zh":"open snowdrop 指花瓣已張開到足以被算作開花的雪花蓮。"},{"en":"A gardener may record the first open snowdrop as a sign of early spring.","zh":"園丁可能把第一朵已開花的雪花蓮記作早春跡象。"},{"en":"If people define “open” differently, their records may not match.","zh":"如果人們對「開放」定義不同，他們的記錄可能不一致。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when precise plant-observation standards matter.","zh":"當精確植物觀察標準很重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the biggest concern with","meaning":"對……最大的憂慮","examples":[{"en":"The biggest concern with ad hoc observations is how systematic they are.","zh":"對臨時性觀察最大的憂慮是它們有多有系統。"},{"en":"The biggest concern with means the most serious worry about something.","zh":"biggest concern with 指對某事最嚴重的擔憂。"},{"en":"The biggest concern with online exams may be whether students have stable internet.","zh":"對網上考試最大的憂慮可能是學生是否有穩定網絡。"},{"en":"Researchers worry most about amateur records when methods are unclear or irregular.","zh":"當方法不清楚或不規則，研究人員最擔心業餘記錄。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying the main problem.","zh":"識別主要問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ad hoc observations","meaning":"臨時性觀察；非正式觀察","examples":[{"en":"Ad hoc observations may not be taken systematically.","zh":"臨時性觀察未必是有系統地進行的。"},{"en":"Ad hoc observations are observations made casually or for a particular moment, not through a planned system.","zh":"ad hoc observations 指隨意或因某一時刻而作的觀察，而非透過計劃系統進行。"},{"en":"A teacher’s quick note about a student’s mood is an ad hoc observation.","zh":"老師對學生情緒作出的快速記錄是一項臨時性觀察。"},{"en":"These observations can be useful, but they may miss events because they are not regular.","zh":"這些觀察可以有用，但因不定期而可能錯過事件。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when records are informal rather than planned.","zh":"當記錄屬非正式而非有計劃時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"carefully and systematically","meaning":"細心而有系統地","examples":[{"en":"Researchers ask how carefully and systematically the observations were taken.","zh":"研究人員會問這些觀察是多麼細心而有系統地進行。"},{"en":"Carefully and systematically means with attention, accuracy and a clear repeated method.","zh":"carefully and systematically 指以專注、準確和清楚重複的方法進行。"},{"en":"Students collect survey answers carefully and systematically if they ask every class the same questions.","zh":"如果學生向每班問相同問題，他們就是細心而有系統地收集調查答案。"},{"en":"Data are more reliable when observations are made carefully and systematically.","zh":"當觀察細心而有系統地進行，數據更可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when quality depends on method.","zh":"當質素取決於方法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pretty precisely","meaning":"相當準確地","examples":[{"en":"Scientists need to know pretty precisely what a person has been observing.","zh":"科學家需要相當準確地知道一個人一直在觀察甚麼。"},{"en":"Pretty precisely means fairly exactly, with enough detail to be useful.","zh":"pretty precisely 指相當精確，有足夠細節可供使用。"},{"en":"A doctor needs to know pretty precisely when a patient’s pain began.","zh":"醫生需要相當準確地知道病人的疼痛何時開始。"},{"en":"Scientific records need precision because vague notes are difficult to compare.","zh":"科學記錄需要精確，因為含糊筆記難以比較。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when accuracy matters but absolute perfection is not required.","zh":"當準確度重要但不要求絕對完美時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"leaves came out","meaning":"樹葉長出來","examples":[{"en":"A record saying that the leaves came out may not be precise enough.","zh":"一項只說樹葉長出來的記錄可能不夠精確。"},{"en":"Leaves came out means new leaves appeared or unfolded on a plant or tree.","zh":"leaves came out 指植物或樹木的新葉出現或展開。"},{"en":"A child may notice that leaves came out on the playground trees after a warm week.","zh":"暖和一週後，孩子可能注意到操場樹木的樹葉長出來。"},{"en":"The phrase can be too vague if it does not say which leaves, how many or exactly when.","zh":"如果沒有說明哪些葉、多少葉或確實時間，這個短語可能太含糊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing leaf growth in simple language.","zh":"用簡單語言描述葉子生長時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the onset of autumn","meaning":"秋天的開始","examples":[{"en":"Measuring the onset of autumn can be particularly problematic.","zh":"量度秋天的開始可能特別棘手。"},{"en":"The onset of autumn is the beginning of autumn conditions, such as cooler weather or leaves changing colour.","zh":"onset of autumn 指秋季條件開始出現，例如天氣變涼或樹葉變色。"},{"en":"People may disagree about the onset of autumn if some trees change colour earlier than others.","zh":"如果有些樹比其他樹更早變色，人們可能不同意秋天何時開始。"},{"en":"Autumn is harder to measure because colour change can be gradual and subjective.","zh":"秋天較難量度，因為變色可以是漸進和主觀的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing when a season begins.","zh":"討論季節何時開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"particularly problematic","meaning":"特別有問題；特別棘手","examples":[{"en":"Autumn records can be particularly problematic.","zh":"秋天記錄可能特別有問題。"},{"en":"Particularly problematic means especially difficult or likely to cause problems.","zh":"particularly problematic 指尤其困難或特別容易造成問題。"},{"en":"Group projects can be particularly problematic if no one agrees on responsibilities.","zh":"如果沒有人同意責任分工，小組專題可能特別棘手。"},{"en":"Autumn observations are problematic because leaf colour changes slowly and unevenly.","zh":"秋天觀察很棘手，因為葉色變化緩慢且不均勻。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one case is more difficult than others.","zh":"當某情況比其他情況更困難時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"more subjective than","meaning":"比……更主觀","examples":[{"en":"Deciding when leaves change colour is more subjective than noting when they appear.","zh":"判斷樹葉何時變色比記錄它們何時出現更主觀。"},{"en":"More subjective than means depending more on personal judgement than clear facts.","zh":"more subjective than 指比另一事物更依賴個人判斷，而非清楚事實。"},{"en":"Judging whether an essay is “interesting” is more subjective than counting spelling mistakes.","zh":"判斷文章是否「有趣」比點算串字錯誤更主觀。"},{"en":"Leaf colour is subjective because different observers may choose different stages as the start.","zh":"葉色具主觀性，因為不同觀察者可能把不同階段選作開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing clear measurement with personal judgement.","zh":"比較清楚量度與個人判斷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"change colour","meaning":"變色","examples":[{"en":"Leaves change colour in autumn.","zh":"樹葉在秋天變色。"},{"en":"Change colour means become a different colour.","zh":"change colour 指變成不同顏色。"},{"en":"Bananas change colour from green to yellow as they ripen.","zh":"香蕉成熟時會由綠色變成黃色。"},{"en":"Leaves change colour when seasonal conditions affect the chemicals in them.","zh":"當季節條件影響樹葉中的化學物質，樹葉就會變色。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing visible natural change.","zh":"描述可見自然變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be positive about","meaning":"對……持正面態度","examples":[{"en":"Most phenologists are positive about the contribution amateurs can make.","zh":"大多數物候學家對業餘人士可作出的貢獻持正面態度。"},{"en":"Be positive about means feel hopeful, supportive or approving toward something.","zh":"be positive about 指對某事感到有希望、支持或認同。"},{"en":"A teacher may be positive about a new reading programme after seeing students enjoy books more.","zh":"老師看到學生更享受閱讀後，可能對新的閱讀計劃持正面態度。"},{"en":"Scientists may feel positive about amateur data if quality control is strong.","zh":"如果質素控制嚴謹，科學家可能對業餘數據持正面態度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone has a favourable attitude.","zh":"當某人有正面看法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the contribution that amateurs can make","meaning":"業餘人士可作出的貢獻","examples":[{"en":"Scientists recognise the contribution that amateurs can make.","zh":"科學家承認業餘人士可作出的貢獻。"},{"en":"The contribution that amateurs can make means the useful help non-professionals can provide.","zh":"contribution that amateurs can make 指非專業人士可以提供的有用幫助。"},{"en":"Amateur photographers can contribute by recording changes in local streets after a flood.","zh":"業餘攝影者可以透過記錄水災後本地街道變化作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Amateurs can help because they observe many places professionals cannot visit regularly.","zh":"業餘人士能幫忙，因為他們觀察許多專業人士不能定期到訪的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when public participation supports expert work.","zh":"當公眾參與支援專家工作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the raw power of science","meaning":"科學最根本的力量","examples":[{"en":"Careful observation shows the raw power of science.","zh":"細心觀察顯示科學最根本的力量。"},{"en":"The raw power of science means the basic strength of science: observing carefully, collecting evidence and finding patterns.","zh":"raw power of science 指科學的基本力量：細心觀察、收集證據和找出模式。"},{"en":"A simple plant-growth experiment can show students the raw power of science.","zh":"簡單的植物生長實驗可以向學生顯示科學最根本的力量。"},{"en":"Science does not always begin with expensive machines; it can begin with patient observation.","zh":"科學不一定始於昂貴機器；它可以始於耐心觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when science is shown in its simplest, most direct form.","zh":"當科學以最簡單、最直接形式呈現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"careful observation of","meaning":"對……的細心觀察","examples":[{"en":"Amateurs contribute through careful observation of the natural world.","zh":"業餘人士透過對自然世界的細心觀察作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Careful observation of means watching something closely and accurately over time.","zh":"careful observation of 指長時間仔細而準確地觀察某事物。"},{"en":"A nurse’s careful observation of a patient can reveal small changes in health.","zh":"護士對病人的細心觀察可以揭示健康上的小變化。"},{"en":"Careful observation of plants and birds helps detect seasonal shifts.","zh":"對植物和鳥類的細心觀察有助偵測季節轉移。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when attention to detail creates useful knowledge.","zh":"當對細節的注意創造有用知識時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"acknowledge the need for","meaning":"承認有……的需要","examples":[{"en":"Professionals acknowledge the need for careful quality control.","zh":"專業人士承認有細心質素控制的需要。"},{"en":"Acknowledge the need for means accept that something is necessary.","zh":"acknowledge the need for 指接受某事是必要的。"},{"en":"A school may acknowledge the need for mental-health support after students report stress.","zh":"學生反映壓力後，學校可能承認有心理健康支援的需要。"},{"en":"Scientists support amateur data but acknowledge the need for checking its accuracy.","zh":"科學家支持業餘數據，但承認有檢查其準確性的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when agreement includes a practical requirement.","zh":"當認同同時包括實際要求時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"quality control","meaning":"質素控制","examples":[{"en":"Amateur data require careful quality control.","zh":"業餘數據需要細心的質素控制。"},{"en":"Quality control is the process of checking that information, products or work meet a good standard.","zh":"quality control 指檢查資訊、產品或工作是否達到良好標準的過程。"},{"en":"A restaurant uses quality control to make sure food is safe and consistent.","zh":"餐廳使用質素控制來確保食物安全和一致。"},{"en":"In research, quality control removes weak records and checks uncertain data.","zh":"在研究中，質素控制會移除薄弱記錄並檢查不確定數據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reliability must be protected.","zh":"當可靠性必須受到保護時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"gauge the quality of","meaning":"評估……的質素","examples":[{"en":"Root tries to gauge the quality of an amateur archive.","zh":"Root 嘗試評估一個業餘人士檔案的質素。"},{"en":"Gauge the quality of means judge or estimate how reliable, accurate or useful something is.","zh":"gauge the quality of 指判斷或估計某物有多可靠、準確或有用。"},{"en":"A teacher may gauge the quality of an essay by checking structure, evidence and language.","zh":"老師可能透過檢查結構、證據和語言來評估文章質素。"},{"en":"Researchers gauge quality before deciding whether data can be used scientifically.","zh":"研究人員在決定數據能否科學使用前，會評估其質素。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evaluating usefulness or reliability.","zh":"評估有用性或可靠性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"amateur archive","meaning":"業餘人士的檔案","examples":[{"en":"She assesses an amateur archive by interviewing its collector.","zh":"她透過訪問其收集者來評估一個業餘人士的檔案。"},{"en":"An amateur archive is a collection of records kept by a non-professional observer.","zh":"amateur archive 指由非專業觀察者保存的一批記錄。"},{"en":"A birdwatcher’s notebooks and calendars can form an amateur archive.","zh":"觀鳥者的筆記簿和月曆可以形成一個業餘人士的檔案。"},{"en":"Such archives may contain valuable data, but researchers must check how they were made.","zh":"這類檔案可能包含有價值數據，但研究人員必須檢查其製作方式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when private records are treated as research material.","zh":"當私人記錄被視為研究材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"interview its collector","meaning":"訪問其收集者","examples":[{"en":"Root gauges the archive by interviewing its collector.","zh":"Root 透過訪問其收集者來評估檔案。"},{"en":"Interview its collector means ask the person who gathered the records questions about how they were made.","zh":"interview its collector 指向收集記錄的人提問，以了解記錄如何製作。"},{"en":"A museum may interview a collector before accepting old photographs.","zh":"博物館接受舊照片前，可能訪問其收集者。"},{"en":"Interviews help reveal whether records were kept regularly, carefully and honestly.","zh":"訪問有助揭示記錄是否定期、細心和誠實地保存。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the creator of an archive helps explain its reliability.","zh":"當檔案創建者幫助解釋其可靠性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"things as trivial as","meaning":"像……般微不足道的事情","examples":[{"en":"Things as trivial as vacations can affect measurement.","zh":"像假期般微不足道的事情也可以影響測量。"},{"en":"Things as trivial as means things that seem small or unimportant, but may still matter.","zh":"things as trivial as 指看似細小或不重要，但仍可能有影響的事情。"},{"en":"Things as trivial as a missing pen can delay a student during an exam.","zh":"像遺失一支筆般微不足道的事情，也可以在考試中拖慢學生。"},{"en":"A vacation can affect records if the observer is away when a flower opens.","zh":"如果觀察者在花開時外出度假，假期就會影響記錄。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when small details unexpectedly affect results.","zh":"當小細節意外影響結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"affect measurement","meaning":"影響測量","examples":[{"en":"Vacations can affect measurement in amateur records.","zh":"假期可以影響業餘記錄中的測量。"},{"en":"Affect measurement means change the accuracy, timing or completeness of what is being recorded.","zh":"affect measurement 指改變正在記錄內容的準確性、時間或完整性。"},{"en":"A broken ruler can affect measurement in a science experiment.","zh":"斷尺可以影響科學實驗中的測量。"},{"en":"If an observer is away, measurements may miss the exact date of an event.","zh":"如果觀察者外出，測量可能錯過事件的確實日期。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when data quality depends on how information is collected.","zh":"當數據質素取決於資訊如何收集時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"disregard records","meaning":"不採用記錄","examples":[{"en":"Root disregards records that are not rigorous enough.","zh":"Root 不採用不夠嚴謹的記錄。"},{"en":"Disregard records means choose not to use records because they are unreliable or unsuitable.","zh":"disregard records 指因記錄不可靠或不合適而選擇不使用。"},{"en":"A teacher may disregard homework answers copied from the internet.","zh":"老師可能不採用從網上抄來的功課答案。"},{"en":"Researchers disregard weak records to protect the quality of their conclusions.","zh":"研究人員不採用薄弱記錄，以保護結論質素。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when information is rejected after evaluation.","zh":"當資訊經評估後被拒絕時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rigorous enough","meaning":"足夠嚴謹","examples":[{"en":"Some records are not rigorous enough for scientific use.","zh":"有些記錄對科學用途來說不夠嚴謹。"},{"en":"Rigorous enough means careful, strict and accurate enough to meet a standard.","zh":"rigorous enough 指足夠仔細、嚴格和準確，以符合標準。"},{"en":"A survey is not rigorous enough if it asks only three friends and calls the result national.","zh":"如果調查只問三個朋友，卻把結果稱為全國情況，它就不夠嚴謹。"},{"en":"Scientific records must be rigorous enough to compare with other data.","zh":"科學記錄必須足夠嚴謹，才能與其他數據比較。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when judging whether work meets a serious standard.","zh":"判斷工作是否符合嚴格標準時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"iron out problems","meaning":"解決問題；消除問題","examples":[{"en":"The right statistics can iron out some problems with amateur data.","zh":"合適的統計方法可以解決業餘數據中的一些問題。"},{"en":"Iron out problems means reduce, correct or smooth away difficulties.","zh":"iron out problems 指減少、修正或逐步消除困難。"},{"en":"A teacher may iron out problems in a timetable before the new term begins.","zh":"老師可能在新學期開始前解決時間表中的問題。"},{"en":"Statistics can iron out problems by allowing for missing or uncertain data.","zh":"統計方法可以透過顧及缺失或不確定數據來消除問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when difficulties are solved gradually and practically.","zh":"當困難被逐步而實際地解決時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"account for uncertainty","meaning":"顧及不確定性","examples":[{"en":"Statistical techniques can account for uncertainty in amateur data.","zh":"統計技術可以顧及業餘數據中的不確定性。"},{"en":"Account for uncertainty means include possible error or doubt when analysing information.","zh":"account for uncertainty 指分析資料時包括可能錯誤或疑問。"},{"en":"A weather forecast accounts for uncertainty by giving a chance of rain rather than a promise.","zh":"天氣預報透過給出下雨機率而非保證來顧及不確定性。"},{"en":"Researchers account for uncertainty because amateur records may not all be equally precise.","zh":"研究人員顧及不確定性，因為業餘記錄未必同樣精確。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when analysis must handle imperfect data.","zh":"當分析必須處理不完美數據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"phenological data","meaning":"物候數據","examples":[{"en":"Amateur phenological data may contain uncertainty.","zh":"業餘物候數據可能包含不確定性。"},{"en":"Phenological data are records about the timing of natural biological events.","zh":"phenological data 指關於自然生物事件發生時間的記錄。"},{"en":"First flowering dates, bird arrival dates and leaf-fall dates are phenological data.","zh":"首次開花日期、鳥類到達日期和落葉日期都是物候數據。"},{"en":"These data help scientists study whether seasonal events are shifting over time.","zh":"這些數據幫助科學家研究季節事件是否隨時間轉移。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when timing records from nature are used scientifically.","zh":"當自然時間記錄被科學使用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"evident from past records","meaning":"從過往記錄中可見","examples":[{"en":"The enthusiasm of amateur phenologists is evident from past records.","zh":"業餘物候學愛好者的熱情從過往記錄中可見。"},{"en":"Evident from past records means clearly shown by old written evidence.","zh":"evident from past records 指由舊書面證據清楚顯示。"},{"en":"A school’s long tradition of music may be evident from past records of concerts.","zh":"學校悠久的音樂傳統可能從過往音樂會記錄中可見。"},{"en":"Past records can show people’s interests even if those people are no longer alive.","zh":"即使那些人已不在人世，過往記錄仍能顯示他們的興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when old documents clearly reveal a pattern or attitude.","zh":"當舊文件清楚揭示模式或態度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"standardised recording schemes","meaning":"標準化記錄計劃","examples":[{"en":"Researchers want to create standardised recording schemes.","zh":"研究人員想建立標準化記錄計劃。"},{"en":"Standardised recording schemes are organised systems where everyone records information in the same agreed way.","zh":"standardised recording schemes 指每個人按照同一套約定方法記錄資料的有組織系統。"},{"en":"A school may use a standardised recording scheme for attendance so every class reports absences consistently.","zh":"學校可能使用標準化出席記錄計劃，讓每班一致地報告缺席。"},{"en":"Standardisation improves data quality because different observers follow the same rules.","zh":"標準化改善數據質素，因為不同觀察者遵循相同規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when many people collect comparable records.","zh":"當許多人收集可比較記錄時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"well-designed studies","meaning":"設計良好的研究","examples":[{"en":"Well-designed studies can generate many useful observations.","zh":"設計良好的研究可以產生許多有用觀察。"},{"en":"Well-designed studies are research projects planned carefully with clear methods and reliable procedures.","zh":"well-designed studies 指以清楚方法和可靠程序仔細規劃的研究項目。"},{"en":"A well-designed school survey asks clear questions and includes enough students.","zh":"設計良好的學校調查會提出清晰問題，並包括足夠學生。"},{"en":"Good design reduces bias, confusion and missing information.","zh":"良好設計能減少偏見、混亂和資料缺失。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research quality depends on planning.","zh":"當研究質素取決於規劃時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"generate a volume of observations","meaning":"產生大量觀察記錄","examples":[{"en":"Standardised schemes can generate a volume of observations.","zh":"標準化計劃可以產生大量觀察記錄。"},{"en":"Generate a volume of observations means produce a large amount of recorded information.","zh":"generate a volume of observations 指產生大量記錄下來的資訊。"},{"en":"A city-wide traffic survey can generate a volume of observations about bus delays.","zh":"全市交通調查可以產生大量關於巴士延誤的觀察記錄。"},{"en":"Large volumes of observations help reduce the influence of individual mistakes.","zh":"大量觀察記錄有助減少個別錯誤的影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a project produces a lot of data.","zh":"當項目產生大量數據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"large enough to","meaning":"大到足以……","examples":[{"en":"The volume of observations may be large enough to reduce individual bias.","zh":"觀察記錄的數量可能大到足以減少個人偏差。"},{"en":"Large enough to means sufficiently big to produce a certain result.","zh":"large enough to 指大到足以產生某結果。"},{"en":"A classroom must be large enough to hold all students safely.","zh":"課室必須大到足以安全容納所有學生。"},{"en":"A data set large enough to include many observers can balance out personal differences.","zh":"足夠大的數據集若包括許多觀察者，就能平衡個人差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when size makes something possible.","zh":"當大小令某事成為可能時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"drown out the idiosyncrasies of","meaning":"抵消……的個人差異","examples":[{"en":"Large data sets may drown out the idiosyncrasies of individual recorders.","zh":"大型數據集可能抵消個別記錄者的個人差異。"},{"en":"Drown out the idiosyncrasies of means reduce the effect of personal habits or unusual differences.","zh":"drown out the idiosyncrasies of 指減少個人習慣或不尋常差異的影響。"},{"en":"In a large class survey, many answers can drown out the idiosyncrasies of one unusual respondent.","zh":"在大型班級調查中，許多答案可以抵消一位不尋常回應者的個人差異。"},{"en":"Big data sets reduce individual quirks because no single recorder controls the pattern.","zh":"大型數據集減少個人特性影響，因為沒有單一記錄者控制整體模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when large numbers reduce the effect of personal variation.","zh":"當大量數據減少個人差異影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"individual recorders","meaning":"個別記錄者","examples":[{"en":"Large studies reduce the effect of individual recorders.","zh":"大型研究減少個別記錄者的影響。"},{"en":"Individual recorders are single people who collect and write down observations.","zh":"individual recorders 指個別收集和寫下觀察的人。"},{"en":"One individual recorder may always check flowers in the morning, while another checks in the evening.","zh":"一位個別記錄者可能總是在早上檢查花朵，另一位則在晚上檢查。"},{"en":"Differences between individual recorders can affect data if the study is small.","zh":"如果研究規模小，個別記錄者之間的差異可能影響數據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when personal recording habits matter.","zh":"當個人記錄習慣重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cheap to collect","meaning":"收集成本低","examples":[{"en":"Amateur data are cheap to collect.","zh":"業餘數據收集成本低。"},{"en":"Cheap to collect means not requiring much money to gather.","zh":"cheap to collect 指收集時不需要很多金錢。"},{"en":"Student feedback through online forms is cheap to collect compared with printed surveys.","zh":"與印刷問卷相比，透過網上表格收集學生回饋成本低。"},{"en":"Amateur observations are cheap because volunteers already live near the places being observed.","zh":"業餘觀察成本低，因為義工本來就住在被觀察地點附近。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when data collection costs are low.","zh":"當數據收集成本低時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"breadth in space, time and range of species","meaning":"在地域、時間和物種範圍上的廣度","examples":[{"en":"The data provide breadth in space, time and range of species.","zh":"這些數據提供地域、時間和物種範圍上的廣度。"},{"en":"Breadth in space, time and range of species means wide coverage across places, years and kinds of living things.","zh":"breadth in space, time and range of species 指在地點、年份和生物種類上都有廣泛覆蓋。"},{"en":"A wildlife project has breadth if it covers many regions, many seasons and many species.","zh":"如果野生動物項目涵蓋許多地區、許多季節和許多物種，它就有廣度。"},{"en":"Broad coverage helps scientists see large patterns rather than isolated cases.","zh":"廣泛覆蓋幫助科學家看見大模式，而不是孤立個案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when data are valuable because they cover many dimensions.","zh":"當數據因涵蓋多個層面而有價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a large geographical scale","meaning":"大規模地理範圍","examples":[{"en":"It is difficult to collect data on a large geographical scale.","zh":"在大規模地理範圍收集數據很困難。"},{"en":"A large geographical scale means across a wide physical area or many regions.","zh":"large geographical scale 指橫跨廣闊實體區域或許多地區。"},{"en":"A survey on a large geographical scale may include schools from cities, villages and islands.","zh":"大規模地理範圍的調查可能包括城市、鄉村和島嶼的學校。"},{"en":"Collecting data over wide areas is hard because researchers cannot be everywhere at once.","zh":"在廣闊地區收集數據很難，因為研究人員不能同時到處出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when space and coverage are important.","zh":"當空間和覆蓋範圍重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"enlist an army of observers","meaning":"招募大批觀察者","examples":[{"en":"Scientists may need to enlist an army of observers.","zh":"科學家可能需要招募大批觀察者。"},{"en":"Enlist an army of observers means recruit a very large number of people to watch and record events.","zh":"enlist an army of observers 指招募非常多人去觀察和記錄事件。"},{"en":"A city may enlist volunteers to count trees in every district.","zh":"城市可能招募義工點算每個區的樹木。"},{"en":"Many observers are needed when data must cover large areas and many species.","zh":"當數據必須涵蓋廣大地區和許多物種，就需要大量觀察者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when public participation is needed for large-scale observation.","zh":"當大規模觀察需要公眾參與時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"drive home messages about","meaning":"有力傳達關於……的信息","examples":[{"en":"Phenology helps to drive home messages about climate change.","zh":"物候學有助有力傳達關於氣候變化的信息。"},{"en":"Drive home messages about means make people understand an idea clearly and strongly.","zh":"drive home messages about 指令人清楚而強烈地理解某個信息。"},{"en":"A real accident story can drive home messages about road safety better than a poster alone.","zh":"真實意外故事比單靠海報更能有力傳達道路安全信息。"},{"en":"Phenology makes climate change feel real because people can see local seasonal changes.","zh":"物候學令氣候變化感覺真實，因為人們可以看見本地季節變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence makes a message more powerful.","zh":"當證據令信息更有力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"potentially unpleasant consequences","meaning":"潛在而令人不快的後果","examples":[{"en":"Phenology can illustrate potentially unpleasant consequences.","zh":"物候學可以說明潛在而令人不快的後果。"},{"en":"Potentially unpleasant consequences are possible negative results that may happen later.","zh":"potentially unpleasant consequences 指日後可能發生的負面結果。"},{"en":"A poor diet may have potentially unpleasant consequences such as tiredness and weight gain.","zh":"不良飲食可能有潛在而令人不快的後果，例如疲倦和體重增加。"},{"en":"Climate-related seasonal changes may lead to pests, crop problems or wildlife decline.","zh":"與氣候相關的季節變化可能導致害蟲、農作物問題或野生動物下降。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when warning about possible future harm.","zh":"警告可能的未來傷害時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rat infestations","meaning":"鼠患","examples":[{"en":"More rat infestations are reported in warmer years.","zh":"較暖年份有更多鼠患被報告。"},{"en":"Rat infestations are situations where too many rats live in or invade an area.","zh":"rat infestations 指太多老鼠生活或入侵某地區的情況。"},{"en":"A restaurant may face rat infestations if rubbish is not stored properly.","zh":"如果垃圾沒有妥善存放，餐廳可能面對鼠患。"},{"en":"Warmer years may help rats survive and reproduce more easily.","zh":"較暖年份可能幫助老鼠更容易存活和繁殖。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing pest problems.","zh":"討論害蟲問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"local councils","meaning":"地方議會","examples":[{"en":"Rat infestations are reported to local councils.","zh":"鼠患會被報告給地方議會。"},{"en":"Local councils are local government bodies that manage services in a town, district or community.","zh":"local councils 指管理城鎮、地區或社區服務的地方政府機構。"},{"en":"Residents may contact local councils about rubbish collection, street lights or pest control.","zh":"居民可能就垃圾收集、街燈或滅鼠聯絡地方議會。"},{"en":"Local councils receive reports because they are responsible for many public health services.","zh":"地方議會接收報告，因為它們負責許多公共衛生服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing local government action.","zh":"討論地方政府行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in warmer years","meaning":"在較暖的年份","examples":[{"en":"More infestations are reported in warmer years.","zh":"在較暖的年份，更多鼠患被報告。"},{"en":"In warmer years means during years with higher-than-usual temperatures.","zh":"in warmer years 指在氣溫高於平常的年份中。"},{"en":"In warmer years, people may use air-conditioning earlier in spring.","zh":"在較暖的年份，人們可能在春天更早使用冷氣。"},{"en":"Warmer years can change animal behaviour, pest numbers and plant growth.","zh":"較暖年份可以改變動物行為、害蟲數量和植物生長。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing years by temperature.","zh":"按氣溫比較年份時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"get people involved","meaning":"讓人參與","examples":[{"en":"Getting people involved is good for public relations.","zh":"讓人參與對公關有好處。"},{"en":"Get people involved means encourage ordinary people to participate in an activity or project.","zh":"get people involved 指鼓勵普通人參與活動或項目。"},{"en":"A school can get parents involved by inviting them to reading workshops.","zh":"學校可以透過邀請家長參加閱讀工作坊來讓他們參與。"},{"en":"People care more about science when they help collect real data themselves.","zh":"當人們親自幫助收集真實數據，他們會更關心科學。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when participation is part of the goal.","zh":"當參與本身是目標之一時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"public relations","meaning":"公關；公共關係","examples":[{"en":"Public involvement can be great for public relations.","zh":"公眾參與可以對公共關係非常有利。"},{"en":"Public relations means how an organisation communicates with people and builds a positive public image.","zh":"public relations 指機構如何與人溝通並建立正面公眾形象。"},{"en":"A school improves public relations when it explains decisions clearly to parents.","zh":"學校向家長清楚解釋決定時，可以改善公共關係。"},{"en":"Citizen science can improve public relations because people feel included and respected.","zh":"公民科學可以改善公關，因為人們感到被包括和被尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing trust between organisations and the public.","zh":"討論機構與公眾之間的信任時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be thrilled to think that","meaning":"一想到……便感到興奮","examples":[{"en":"People are thrilled to think that their hobby can help science.","zh":"人們一想到自己的興趣可以幫助科學便感到興奮。"},{"en":"Be thrilled to think that means feel very excited or pleased by an idea.","zh":"be thrilled to think that 指因某個想法而感到非常興奮或高興。"},{"en":"A student may be thrilled to think that their drawing will appear on a school poster.","zh":"學生一想到自己的畫會出現在學校海報上，可能便感到興奮。"},{"en":"People feel proud when they realise ordinary hobbies can have real value.","zh":"當人們意識到普通興趣有真正價值，他們會感到自豪。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an idea brings excitement and pride.","zh":"當某想法帶來興奮和自豪時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"collect as a hobby","meaning":"作為興趣收集","examples":[{"en":"Some people collect natural records as a hobby.","zh":"有些人作為興趣收集自然記錄。"},{"en":"Collect as a hobby means gather items or information for enjoyment rather than for work.","zh":"collect as a hobby 指為享受而收集物品或資訊，而不是為工作。"},{"en":"A child may collect stamps as a hobby and arrange them in an album.","zh":"孩子可能作為興趣收集郵票，並把它們整理在相簿中。"},{"en":"Hobby collecting can become valuable if the collection is detailed and long-term.","zh":"如果收藏詳細而長期，興趣收藏可以變得有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when private interest leads to organised records.","zh":"當私人興趣帶來有組織記錄時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be used for something scientific","meaning":"可用於科學用途","examples":[{"en":"Their data can be used for something scientific.","zh":"他們的數據可用於科學用途。"},{"en":"Be used for something scientific means serve a purpose in research, analysis or evidence-based study.","zh":"be used for something scientific 指在研究、分析或以證據為本的學習中發揮作用。"},{"en":"Photos of the same beach taken every year can be used for something scientific if they show erosion.","zh":"如果每年拍攝同一海灘的照片顯示侵蝕，它們可用於科學用途。"},{"en":"Ordinary records become scientific when researchers analyse them carefully.","zh":"當研究人員仔細分析普通記錄，它們就變成科學材料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when everyday material supports science.","zh":"當日常材料支援科學時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"empower someone","meaning":"賦權予某人；使某人感到有能力","examples":[{"en":"Using amateur data empowers the people who collected it.","zh":"使用業餘數據會賦權予收集數據的人。"},{"en":"Empower someone means make someone feel able, valued or capable of making a difference.","zh":"empower someone 指令某人感到有能力、被重視，或能帶來改變。"},{"en":"A teacher empowers students by letting them lead a class discussion.","zh":"老師讓學生主導課堂討論，就是在賦權予學生。"},{"en":"Citizen science empowers volunteers because their observations contribute to real research.","zh":"公民科學賦權予義工，因為他們的觀察有份貢獻真實研究。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when participation gives people confidence and influence.","zh":"當參與給予人信心和影響力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"contains the following information","meaning":"包含以下資料","examples":[{"en":"The paragraph contains the following information.","zh":"該段包含以下資料。"},{"en":"Contains the following information means includes the details listed after the instruction.","zh":"contains the following information 指包括指示後列出的細節。"},{"en":"In a reading task, students must find which paragraph contains the following information.","zh":"在閱讀題中，學生必須找出哪一段包含以下資料。"},{"en":"This instruction tests whether students can locate ideas, not just understand vocabulary.","zh":"這項指示測試學生能否定位想法，而不只是理解詞彙。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in paragraph-matching questions.","zh":"這個短語適用於段落配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"write the correct letter","meaning":"寫上正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should write the correct letter on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生應在答題紙上寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"Write the correct letter means put the letter of the chosen answer in the required place.","zh":"write the correct letter 指在指定位置填寫所選答案的字母。"},{"en":"In matching questions, students write the correct letter after identifying the right paragraph.","zh":"在配對題中，學生識別正確段落後寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"Accuracy matters because one wrong letter changes the answer completely.","zh":"準確很重要，因為一個錯誤字母會完全改變答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the definition of","meaning":"……的定義","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for the definition of phenology.","zh":"題目要求物候學的定義。"},{"en":"The definition of something is the explanation of what it means.","zh":"definition of something 指某事物意思的解釋。"},{"en":"A science worksheet may ask for the definition of evaporation.","zh":"科學工作紙可能要求蒸發的定義。"},{"en":"Clear definitions help students avoid confusing similar terms.","zh":"清晰定義幫助學生避免混淆相似術語。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when meaning must be explained precisely.","zh":"當意思必須被精確解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"first became aware of","meaning":"首次察覺……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks how Sparks first became aware of amateur records.","zh":"題目問 Sparks 如何首次察覺業餘記錄。"},{"en":"First became aware of means first found out about or noticed something.","zh":"first became aware of 指第一次得知或注意到某事。"},{"en":"A teacher first became aware of a bullying problem after a student wrote about it.","zh":"老師在學生寫下事件後，首次察覺欺凌問題。"},{"en":"Knowing how someone first became aware of information can explain how a project began.","zh":"知道某人如何首次察覺資訊，可以解釋項目如何開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when tracing the beginning of knowledge or discovery.","zh":"追溯知識或發現的開端時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"involvement in data collection","meaning":"參與數據收集","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes people’s involvement in data collection.","zh":"文章描述人們參與數據收集。"},{"en":"Involvement in data collection means participation in gathering information for a study or record.","zh":"involvement in data collection 指參與為研究或記錄收集資料。"},{"en":"Students’ involvement in data collection can include counting traffic outside school.","zh":"學生參與數據收集可以包括點算學校外交通流量。"},{"en":"Public involvement increases the amount of data researchers can gather.","zh":"公眾參與增加研究人員能收集的數據量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when ordinary people help collect evidence.","zh":"當普通人協助收集證據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the necessity to encourage","meaning":"鼓勵……的必要性","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to the necessity to encourage amateur data collection.","zh":"題目提到鼓勵業餘數據收集的必要性。"},{"en":"The necessity to encourage means the need to support or persuade people to do something.","zh":"necessity to encourage 指需要支持或說服人們做某事。"},{"en":"A school may recognise the necessity to encourage reading at home.","zh":"學校可能意識到鼓勵在家閱讀的必要性。"},{"en":"Encouragement is necessary when useful work depends on voluntary participation.","zh":"當有用工作依賴自願參與，鼓勵就是必要的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when support is needed to make an activity continue.","zh":"當需要支援才能令活動持續時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make predictions","meaning":"作出預測","examples":[{"en":"Amateur records can help scientists make predictions.","zh":"業餘記錄可以幫助科學家作出預測。"},{"en":"Make predictions means say what is likely to happen in the future based on evidence.","zh":"make predictions 指根據證據說出未來可能發生甚麼。"},{"en":"A teacher may make predictions about exam results after seeing several practice papers.","zh":"老師看過幾份練習卷後，可能對考試結果作出預測。"},{"en":"Predictions are stronger when they are based on long-term data rather than guesses.","zh":"當預測基於長期數據而非猜測，它們會更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence is used to think about the future.","zh":"當證據被用來思考未來時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"provide clues about","meaning":"提供關於……的線索","examples":[{"en":"Competition records can provide clues about climate change.","zh":"比賽記錄可以提供關於氣候變化的線索。"},{"en":"Provide clues about means give pieces of information that help explain something.","zh":"provide clues about 指提供有助解釋某事的資料片段。"},{"en":"A student’s repeated errors can provide clues about which grammar rule they misunderstand.","zh":"學生反覆犯的錯可以提供關於他誤解哪條文法規則的線索。"},{"en":"Old records provide clues when they show patterns that match environmental changes.","zh":"當舊記錄顯示與環境變化一致的模式，它們就提供線索。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence suggests an explanation.","zh":"當證據提示某種解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"compiled by generations of","meaning":"由一代又一代……彙編","examples":[{"en":"The records were compiled by generations of amateur naturalists.","zh":"這些記錄由一代又一代業餘自然觀察者彙編而成。"},{"en":"Compiled by generations of means collected and organised by many generations over time.","zh":"compiled by generations of 指由多個世代隨時間收集和整理。"},{"en":"A family recipe book may be compiled by generations of grandparents, parents and children.","zh":"家庭食譜書可能由祖父母、父母和孩子一代又一代彙編。"},{"en":"Records gain value when generations keep adding observations in a consistent way.","zh":"當一代又一代以一致方式加入觀察，記錄就更有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when long-term work is passed down.","zh":"當長期工作被傳承下去時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete the sentences below","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the sentences below with words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的詞語完成以下句子。"},{"en":"Complete the sentences below means fill missing words into the sentences that follow.","zh":"complete the sentences below 指把缺失詞語填入下方句子。"},{"en":"Students complete the sentences below by locating the exact phrase in the reading text.","zh":"學生透過在閱讀文本中定位準確短語來完成以下句子。"},{"en":"This task checks both meaning and grammar because the answer must fit the sentence.","zh":"這項任務同時檢查意思和文法，因為答案必須配合句子。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading-completion instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於閱讀填空指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個字","examples":[{"en":"The answer should contain no more than two words.","zh":"答案應包含不多於兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must use one or two words only.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案只能使用一個或兩個詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “climate data”, students should not write “the climate data records”.","zh":"如果答案是 “climate data”，學生不應寫 “the climate data records”。"},{"en":"Word limits prevent students from copying too much from the passage.","zh":"字數限制防止學生從文章中抄太多。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in IELTS-style completion tasks.","zh":"這個短語適用於 IELTS 式填空題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"largely contain information about","meaning":"主要包含關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"Coates’s records largely contain information about beekeeping.","zh":"Coates 的記錄主要包含關於養蜂的資料。"},{"en":"Largely contain information about means mostly include details on a particular subject.","zh":"largely contain information about 指主要包括某特定主題的細節。"},{"en":"A school report may largely contain information about attendance and exam performance.","zh":"學校報告可能主要包含關於出席率和考試表現的資料。"},{"en":"Researchers check what records contain before deciding whether they fit a study.","zh":"研究人員會先檢查記錄包含甚麼，再決定是否適合研究。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the main content of records.","zh":"描述記錄的主要內容時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be famous for recording","meaning":"因記錄……而聞名","examples":[{"en":"Marsham is famous for recording the life cycles of plants and animals.","zh":"Marsham 因記錄植物和動物生命週期而聞名。"},{"en":"Be famous for recording means be well known because one carefully wrote down particular information.","zh":"be famous for recording 指因仔細寫下特定資料而廣為人知。"},{"en":"A local historian may be famous for recording old village stories.","zh":"本地歷史學家可能因記錄舊村莊故事而聞名。"},{"en":"Marsham’s fame comes from the length and consistency of his natural observations.","zh":"Marsham 的名聲來自其自然觀察的長度和一致性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a person is known for keeping important records.","zh":"當某人因保存重要記錄而知名時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"According to some phenologists, global warming may affect waterfowl.","zh":"根據一些物候學家的說法，全球暖化可能影響水禽。"},{"en":"According to means based on what a person, source or piece of evidence says.","zh":"according to 指根據某人、來源或證據所說。"},{"en":"According to the school notice, the meeting will start at three o’clock.","zh":"根據學校通告，會議將於三點開始。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers show where information comes from.","zh":"這個短語幫助寫作者顯示資訊來源。"},{"en":"It is useful when reporting someone else’s view or finding.","zh":"報告他人的看法或發現時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"due to increased","meaning":"由於……增加","examples":[{"en":"Waterfowl numbers may fall due to increased droughts.","zh":"水禽數量可能由於乾旱增加而下降。"},{"en":"Due to increased means because something has become greater in amount, frequency or intensity.","zh":"due to increased 指因某事在數量、頻率或強度上增加。"},{"en":"Students may feel tired due to increased homework before exams.","zh":"考試前，學生可能由於功課增加而感到疲倦。"},{"en":"Bird numbers may fall when increased droughts reduce wetland habitats.","zh":"當加劇的乾旱減少濕地棲息地，鳥類數量可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a rise in one factor causes a result.","zh":"當某因素增加造成結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"discredit data collected by","meaning":"質疑……收集的數據","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists discredit data collected by amateurs.","zh":"有些科學家質疑業餘人士收集的數據。"},{"en":"Discredit data collected by means reject or question information because of who collected it or how it was collected.","zh":"discredit data collected by 指因收集者或收集方法而拒絕或質疑資料。"},{"en":"A teacher may discredit survey data collected by students if the questions were unclear.","zh":"如果問題不清晰，老師可能質疑學生收集的調查數據。"},{"en":"Scientists may discredit amateur data when records lack consistency or precision.","zh":"當記錄缺乏一致性或精確度，科學家可能質疑業餘數據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the reliability of data is challenged.","zh":"當數據可靠性受到挑戰時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"scientific methods","meaning":"科學方法","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether scientific methods were used in data collection.","zh":"選項問數據收集中是否使用了科學方法。"},{"en":"Scientific methods are careful, organised ways of asking questions, collecting evidence and testing ideas.","zh":"scientific methods 指提出問題、收集證據和測試想法的仔細而有組織的方法。"},{"en":"Students use scientific methods when they change only one variable in an experiment.","zh":"學生在實驗中只改變一個變數時，就是在使用科學方法。"},{"en":"Data are more reliable when scientific methods are followed consistently.","zh":"當科學方法被一致遵循，數據會更可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how research should be conducted.","zh":"討論研究應如何進行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"data collection","meaning":"數據收集","examples":[{"en":"Different standards of data collection can affect reliability.","zh":"不同數據收集標準可以影響可靠性。"},{"en":"Data collection is the process of gathering information for study, analysis or records.","zh":"data collection 指為研究、分析或記錄而收集資料的過程。"},{"en":"A class may practise data collection by surveying how students travel to school.","zh":"一班學生可能透過調查同學如何上學來練習數據收集。"},{"en":"Poor data collection can lead to weak conclusions because the information is incomplete or biased.","zh":"差劣數據收集會導致薄弱結論，因為資料不完整或有偏差。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how evidence is gathered.","zh":"討論證據如何被收集時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"not reliable","meaning":"不可靠","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists argue that amateur data are not reliable.","zh":"有些科學家認為業餘數據不可靠。"},{"en":"Not reliable means not trustworthy or not consistently accurate.","zh":"not reliable 指不值得信任或不持續準確。"},{"en":"A bus timetable is not reliable if buses often arrive at different times from those printed.","zh":"如果巴士經常不按印刷時間到達，巴士時間表就不可靠。"},{"en":"Data may be not reliable if observers use different rules or miss important dates.","zh":"如果觀察者使用不同規則或錯過重要日期，數據可能不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when trustworthiness is questioned.","zh":"當可信度受到質疑時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"unsuitable observers","meaning":"不適合的觀察者","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that the data were collected by unsuitable observers.","zh":"選項暗示數據由不適合的觀察者收集。"},{"en":"Unsuitable observers are people who may not be appropriate for collecting reliable observations.","zh":"unsuitable observers 指可能不適合收集可靠觀察的人。"},{"en":"A person who cannot identify bird species would be an unsuitable observer for a bird survey.","zh":"不能識別鳥類品種的人，不適合做鳥類調查的觀察者。"},{"en":"Observers become unsuitable if they lack training, consistency or access to the thing being studied.","zh":"如果觀察者缺乏訓練、一致性或接觸研究對象的機會，就會變得不適合。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when data quality depends on who observes.","zh":"當數據質素取決於觀察者是誰時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"use the example of…to illustrate","meaning":"用……例子說明","examples":[{"en":"Schwartz uses the example of leaves to illustrate the need for precision.","zh":"Schwartz 用樹葉的例子說明精確性的需要。"},{"en":"Use the example of…to illustrate means explain an idea by showing a clear case.","zh":"use the example of…to illustrate 指透過展示清楚個案來解釋想法。"},{"en":"A teacher may use the example of a late bus to illustrate why students need extra travel time.","zh":"老師可能用巴士遲到的例子說明學生為何需要額外交通時間。"},{"en":"Examples make abstract problems easier to understand.","zh":"例子令抽象問題更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one case helps explain a wider point.","zh":"當一個個案幫助解釋更廣泛重點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"valuable information","meaning":"有價值的資料","examples":[{"en":"Precise records can provide valuable information.","zh":"精確記錄可以提供有價值的資料。"},{"en":"Valuable information is information that is useful, important or worth keeping.","zh":"valuable information 指有用、重要或值得保存的資料。"},{"en":"A doctor’s note about symptoms can be valuable information during later treatment.","zh":"醫生關於症狀的筆記可在之後治療中成為有價值的資料。"},{"en":"Information becomes valuable when it helps people make better decisions or predictions.","zh":"當資訊幫助人們作出更好決定或預測，它就變得有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when data or details have practical importance.","zh":"當數據或細節有實際重要性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"apply statistical techniques","meaning":"應用統計技術","examples":[{"en":"Scientists can apply statistical techniques to amateur data.","zh":"科學家可以把統計技術應用於業餘數據。"},{"en":"Apply statistical techniques means use mathematical methods to analyse data and handle variation.","zh":"apply statistical techniques 指使用數學方法分析數據並處理變異。"},{"en":"A school may apply statistical techniques to test scores to see whether a new course helps.","zh":"學校可能把統計技術應用於測驗分數，以了解新課程是否有幫助。"},{"en":"Statistics can reduce uncertainty by showing patterns across many observations.","zh":"統計可以透過顯示許多觀察中的模式來減少不確定性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when numbers are analysed scientifically.","zh":"當數字被科學分析時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"one implication of","meaning":"……的一項影響","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about one implication of phenology for ordinary people.","zh":"題目問物候學對普通人的一項影響。"},{"en":"One implication of means one possible meaning, result or consequence of something.","zh":"one implication of 指某事的一個可能含意、結果或後果。"},{"en":"One implication of online learning is that students need reliable internet at home.","zh":"網上學習的一項影響是學生在家需要可靠網絡。"},{"en":"Phenology implies that ordinary people can see climate change in local natural events.","zh":"物候學意味着普通人可以在本地自然事件中看見氣候變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining what a fact may mean in practice.","zh":"解釋某事實在實際上可能意味甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"ordinary people","meaning":"普通人","examples":[{"en":"Phenology can have meaning for ordinary people.","zh":"物候學對普通人也可以有意義。"},{"en":"Ordinary people are people who are not experts, officials or specialists.","zh":"ordinary people 指不是專家、官員或專業人士的人。"},{"en":"Ordinary people may notice climate change when flowers bloom earlier in their neighbourhood.","zh":"當附近花朵更早開放，普通人可能注意到氣候變化。"},{"en":"Science becomes more powerful when ordinary people can connect it with daily life.","zh":"當普通人能把科學與日常生活連接，科學就變得更有力量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the public rather than professionals.","zh":"討論公眾而非專業人士時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"public awareness of climate change","meaning":"公眾對氣候變化的意識","examples":[{"en":"Phenology may raise public awareness of climate change.","zh":"物候學可能提高公眾對氣候變化的意識。"},{"en":"Public awareness of climate change means how much ordinary people know and care about climate change.","zh":"public awareness of climate change 指普通人對氣候變化有多少認識和關注。"},{"en":"School exhibitions can raise public awareness of climate change by showing local flood photos.","zh":"學校展覽可以透過展示本地水災照片，提高公眾對氣候變化的意識。"},{"en":"Awareness grows when people see climate effects in familiar plants, birds and seasons.","zh":"當人們在熟悉的植物、鳥類和季節中看見氣候影響，意識就會提升。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when science communication aims to reach the wider public.","zh":"當科學傳播旨在接觸更廣泛公眾時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 26 - Amateur Naturalists.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 27":[{"front":"derived from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"The name dinosaur is derived from the Greek for “terrible lizard”.","zh":"Dinosaur 這個名稱源自希臘語中表示「可怕的蜥蜴」的詞。"},{"en":"Derived from means coming from a particular source, origin, or earlier form.","zh":"Derived from 指來自某個來源、起源或較早形式。"},{"en":"Many English words are derived from Latin, so their spelling can look unusual.","zh":"許多英文字源自拉丁語，所以拼法可能看起來不尋常。"},{"en":"If a dish is derived from an old family recipe, it may keep the same basic flavours.","zh":"如果一道菜源自舊家庭食譜，它可能保留相同的基本味道。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain where a word, idea, custom, or product originally comes from.","zh":"這個片語幫助解釋某個詞、想法、習俗或產品原本來自哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the Greek for","meaning":"希臘語中表示……的詞","examples":[{"en":"The word dinosaur comes from the Greek for “terrible lizard”.","zh":"Dinosaur 這個詞來自希臘語中表示「可怕的蜥蜴」的詞。"},{"en":"The Greek for something means the Greek word or expression that carries that meaning.","zh":"The Greek for something 指希臘語中帶有該意思的詞或表達。"},{"en":"A science teacher may explain the Greek for “life” before introducing the word biology.","zh":"科學老師可能在介紹 biology 一詞前，解釋希臘語中表示「生命」的詞。"},{"en":"Knowing the Greek for a technical word can help students remember its meaning.","zh":"知道技術詞彙的希臘語來源，可以幫助學生記住意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when explaining the language origin of a word.","zh":"這個片語用於解釋詞語的語言來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"terrible lizard","meaning":"可怕的蜥蜴","examples":[{"en":"Although dinosaur means “terrible lizard”, dinosaurs were not lizards at all.","zh":"雖然 dinosaur 的意思是「可怕的蜥蜴」，但恐龍完全不是蜥蜴。"},{"en":"Terrible lizard is the literal meaning behind the word dinosaur.","zh":"Terrible lizard 是 dinosaur 一詞背後的字面意思。"},{"en":"A museum label may explain that “terrible lizard” is historical wording, not an exact scientific description.","zh":"博物館標籤可能解釋「可怕的蜥蜴」是歷史用語，而不是準確科學描述。"},{"en":"Because old names can be misleading, students should check what scientists mean today.","zh":"因為舊名稱可能有誤導性，學生應查看科學家今天的意思。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds learners that word origins do not always match modern classification.","zh":"這個片語提醒學習者，詞源不一定符合現代分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"not, in fact, … at all","meaning":"事實上完全不是……","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs were not, in fact, lizards at all.","zh":"恐龍事實上完全不是蜥蜴。"},{"en":"Not, in fact, … at all means the truth is completely different from what people may think.","zh":"Not, in fact, … at all 指真相與人們可能以為的完全不同。"},{"en":"A tomato is not, in fact, a vegetable at all in botanical terms.","zh":"從植物學角度來說，番茄事實上完全不是蔬菜。"},{"en":"This pattern is useful when correcting a common misunderstanding clearly.","zh":"這個句式適合用來清楚糾正常見誤解。"},{"en":"It strongly denies an idea while adding a factual correction.","zh":"它強烈否定某想法，同時加入事實修正。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"included in the class Reptilia","meaning":"被歸入爬行綱","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs are included in the class Reptilia.","zh":"恐龍被歸入爬行綱。"},{"en":"Included in the class Reptilia means placed in the scientific group of reptiles.","zh":"Included in the class Reptilia 指被放入爬行動物這個科學類別。"},{"en":"In a biology chart, turtles, snakes and crocodiles may be included in the class Reptilia.","zh":"在生物圖表中，龜、蛇和鱷魚可能被歸入爬行綱。"},{"en":"Classification helps scientists organise animals by shared features.","zh":"分類幫助科學家根據共同特徵整理動物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where an animal belongs in a scientific classification system.","zh":"這個片語描述動物在科學分類系統中屬於哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"reptiles","meaning":"爬行動物","examples":[{"en":"Reptiles are one of the five main classes of Vertebrata.","zh":"爬行動物是脊椎動物五個主要綱之一。"},{"en":"Reptiles are animals such as snakes, lizards, turtles and crocodiles.","zh":"Reptiles 是蛇、蜥蜴、龜和鱷魚等動物。"},{"en":"Children may see reptiles in a zoo and learn that many have scales or lay eggs.","zh":"孩子可能在動物園看見爬行動物，並學到許多有鱗片或會產卵。"},{"en":"Reptiles are grouped together because they share important body features.","zh":"爬行動物被歸為一組，因為牠們有重要的共同身體特徵。"},{"en":"This word names a major group of backbone animals.","zh":"這個詞命名一大類有脊骨的動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Vertebrata","meaning":"脊椎動物","examples":[{"en":"Vertebrata are animals with backbones.","zh":"脊椎動物是有脊骨的動物。"},{"en":"Vertebrata is the scientific group that includes animals with a backbone or spinal column.","zh":"Vertebrata 是包括有脊骨或脊柱動物的科學類群。"},{"en":"Fish, birds, mammals, reptiles and amphibians are all part of Vertebrata.","zh":"魚類、鳥類、哺乳類、爬行類和兩棲類都屬於脊椎動物。"},{"en":"Animals in Vertebrata have internal skeletons that support their bodies.","zh":"脊椎動物有支撐身體的內部骨骼。"},{"en":"This term helps separate backbone animals from animals such as insects and worms.","zh":"這個術語幫助把有脊骨動物與昆蟲、蠕蟲等動物分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"animals with backbones","meaning":"有脊骨的動物","examples":[{"en":"Vertebrata are animals with backbones.","zh":"脊椎動物是有脊骨的動物。"},{"en":"Animals with backbones have a spine inside the body that supports movement and posture.","zh":"Animals with backbones 指身體內有脊柱，用來支撐活動和姿勢的動物。"},{"en":"A dog, a pigeon and a fish are animals with backbones.","zh":"狗、鴿子和魚都是有脊骨的動物。"},{"en":"Animals with backbones are classified differently from insects, which do not have spines.","zh":"有脊骨的動物與沒有脊柱的昆蟲分類不同。"},{"en":"This phrase explains Vertebrata in simple everyday language.","zh":"這個片語用簡單日常語言解釋脊椎動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the next level of classification","meaning":"下一個分類層級","examples":[{"en":"At the next level of classification, lizards and dinosaurs are placed in different superorders.","zh":"在下一個分類層級，蜥蜴和恐龍被放入不同的總目。"},{"en":"The next level of classification means the more detailed group below the previous category.","zh":"The next level of classification 指上一個類別之下更詳細的分組。"},{"en":"In school, students may first sort books by subject, then at the next level of classification by author.","zh":"在學校，學生可能先按科目分類書本，再在下一個分類層級按作者分類。"},{"en":"More detailed classification helps people see differences inside a broad group.","zh":"更詳細的分類幫助人看見大類別內部的差異。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving from a general category to a more specific one.","zh":"這個片語描述由一般類別走向更具體類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"significant differences in","meaning":"在……方面有顯著差異","examples":[{"en":"There are significant differences in the skeletal anatomy of lizards and dinosaurs.","zh":"蜥蜴和恐龍的骨骼解剖結構有顯著差異。"},{"en":"Significant differences in something are important differences that affect how we understand it.","zh":"Significant differences in something 指影響我們理解某事的重要差異。"},{"en":"There are significant differences in the way students learn vocabulary and grammar.","zh":"學生學習詞彙和文法的方式有顯著差異。"},{"en":"If there are significant differences in two groups, they may need to be classified separately.","zh":"如果兩個群體有顯著差異，它們可能需要分開分類。"},{"en":"This phrase points to differences that are too important to ignore.","zh":"這個片語指出重要到不能忽視的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"skeletal anatomy","meaning":"骨骼解剖結構","examples":[{"en":"The skeletal anatomy of lizards and dinosaurs led scientists to separate them.","zh":"蜥蜴和恐龍的骨骼解剖結構使科學家把牠們分開。"},{"en":"Skeletal anatomy means the structure and arrangement of bones in an animal’s body.","zh":"Skeletal anatomy 指動物身體中骨骼的結構和排列。"},{"en":"Doctors study skeletal anatomy to understand fractures and joint problems.","zh":"醫生研究骨骼解剖結構，以理解骨折和關節問題。"},{"en":"Differences in skeletal anatomy can show how animals stood, walked or ate.","zh":"骨骼解剖結構的差異可以顯示動物如何站立、行走或進食。"},{"en":"This phrase describes body structure through the bones.","zh":"這個片語透過骨骼描述身體結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"led scientists to","meaning":"使科學家……；導致科學家……","examples":[{"en":"Significant skeletal differences led scientists to place these animals into two different superorders.","zh":"顯著骨骼差異使科學家把這些動物歸入兩個不同總目。"},{"en":"Led scientists to means caused scientists to reach a decision, belief, or action.","zh":"Led scientists to 指使科學家作出某個決定、形成某種信念或採取行動。"},{"en":"Strange test results led doctors to order a second blood test.","zh":"奇怪測試結果使醫生安排第二次驗血。"},{"en":"Strong evidence can lead researchers to change an old theory.","zh":"有力證據可以導致研究人員改變舊理論。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how evidence causes experts to think or act differently.","zh":"這個片語顯示證據如何令專家改變想法或行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"place these groups into","meaning":"將這些類群歸入……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists place these groups of animals into two different superorders.","zh":"科學家將這些動物類群歸入兩個不同總目。"},{"en":"To place these groups into categories means to classify them according to shared or different features.","zh":"To place these groups into categories 指根據共同或不同特徵把類群分類。"},{"en":"A librarian may place books into history, science and fiction sections.","zh":"圖書館員可能把書歸入歷史、科學和小說區。"},{"en":"Placing groups into categories helps people compare them more clearly.","zh":"把類群歸入類別有助人們更清楚比較它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the act of scientific or practical sorting.","zh":"這個片語描述科學或實際分類的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"two different superorders","meaning":"兩個不同的總目","examples":[{"en":"Lizards and dinosaurs belong to two different superorders.","zh":"蜥蜴和恐龍屬於兩個不同的總目。"},{"en":"Two different superorders means two separate high-level groups within biological classification.","zh":"Two different superorders 指生物分類中兩個分開的高層級類群。"},{"en":"In a simple filing system, two different folders may hold documents that look similar at first.","zh":"在簡單檔案系統中，兩個不同資料夾可能存放起初看似相似的文件。"},{"en":"If animals belong to different superorders, scientists see major structural differences between them.","zh":"如果動物屬於不同總目，科學家會看見牠們之間有重大結構差異。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a formal separation in scientific classification.","zh":"這個片語描述科學分類中的正式分隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"classified as","meaning":"被歸類為……","examples":[{"en":"Lizards and snakes are classified as lepidosaurs.","zh":"蜥蜴和蛇被歸類為鱗龍類。"},{"en":"Classified as means officially placed in a category or group.","zh":"Classified as 指被正式放入某個類別或群組。"},{"en":"A library book may be classified as science fiction if it imagines future technology.","zh":"如果一本圖書想像未來科技，它可能被歸類為科幻小說。"},{"en":"Classification helps people find patterns and avoid confusion.","zh":"分類幫助人們找出模式並避免混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining what group something belongs to.","zh":"這個片語適合用來解釋某事屬於哪個群組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lepidosaurs","meaning":"鱗龍類","examples":[{"en":"Lizards and snakes are classified as lepidosaurs.","zh":"蜥蜴和蛇被歸類為鱗龍類。"},{"en":"Lepidosaurs are a reptile group that includes lizards, snakes and their relatives.","zh":"Lepidosaurs 是包括蜥蜴、蛇及其近親的爬行動物類群。"},{"en":"A biology diagram may show lepidosaurs separately from crocodiles and dinosaurs.","zh":"生物圖表可能把鱗龍類與鱷魚和恐龍分開展示。"},{"en":"Scientists use the term lepidosaurs to show that not all reptiles belong to the same branch.","zh":"科學家使用鱗龍類這個術語，顯示不是所有爬行動物都屬於同一分支。"},{"en":"This word names one major group within reptiles.","zh":"這個詞命名爬行動物中的一個主要類群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"prehistoric ancestors","meaning":"史前祖先","examples":[{"en":"Lizards and snakes share a group with their prehistoric ancestors.","zh":"蜥蜴和蛇與其史前祖先同屬一個類群。"},{"en":"Prehistoric ancestors are ancient relatives that lived before written history.","zh":"Prehistoric ancestors 是生活在文字歷史以前的古代親屬。"},{"en":"Museums display fossils to help visitors imagine the prehistoric ancestors of modern animals.","zh":"博物館展示化石，幫助訪客想像現代動物的史前祖先。"},{"en":"Studying prehistoric ancestors helps scientists trace how living species changed over time.","zh":"研究史前祖先幫助科學家追溯現存物種如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"This phrase connects modern animals with older evolutionary relatives.","zh":"這個片語把現代動物與較古老的演化親屬連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"included among","meaning":"包括在……之中","examples":[{"en":"Included among the archosaurs are prehistoric and modern crocodiles.","zh":"主龍類之中包括史前及現代鱷魚。"},{"en":"Included among means listed as part of a larger group.","zh":"Included among 指被列為較大群組的一部分。"},{"en":"Included among the school’s services are counselling, library support and career advice.","zh":"學校服務之中包括輔導、圖書館支援和就業建議。"},{"en":"When something is included among a group, it shares enough features to belong there.","zh":"當某物包括在某群組中，它有足夠共同特徵屬於該處。"},{"en":"This phrase helps introduce members of a category.","zh":"這個片語幫助引入某類別的成員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"archosaurs","meaning":"主龍類","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs are included among the archosaurs.","zh":"恐龍被包括在主龍類之中。"},{"en":"Archosaurs are a reptile group that includes dinosaurs, crocodiles and related extinct forms.","zh":"Archosaurs 是包括恐龍、鱷魚及相關滅絕類群的爬行動物群。"},{"en":"A museum chart may place dinosaurs and crocodiles under archosaurs to show their relationship.","zh":"博物館圖表可能把恐龍和鱷魚放在主龍類之下，以顯示牠們的關係。"},{"en":"Archosaurs are important because they include several major prehistoric animal groups.","zh":"主龍類重要，因為它包括幾個主要史前動物類群。"},{"en":"This term names a broad reptile branch in classification.","zh":"這個術語命名分類中的一個廣闊爬行動物分支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ruling reptiles","meaning":"統治爬行動物","examples":[{"en":"Archosaurs are sometimes described as “ruling reptiles”.","zh":"主龍類有時被描述為「統治爬行動物」。"},{"en":"Ruling reptiles is a descriptive phrase for archosaurs, suggesting their dominance in ancient ecosystems.","zh":"Ruling reptiles 是對主龍類的描述性說法，暗示牠們在古代生態系統中的主導地位。"},{"en":"A textbook may use “ruling reptiles” to make the group easier for students to remember.","zh":"教科書可能使用「統治爬行動物」來令學生更容易記住這個類群。"},{"en":"Names like this can be memorable, but students still need the scientific classification.","zh":"這類名稱可以令人印象深刻，但學生仍需要科學分類。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a vivid label to an important reptile group.","zh":"這個片語為重要爬行動物類群提供生動標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"prehistoric and modern crocodiles","meaning":"史前及現代鱷魚","examples":[{"en":"Archosaurs include prehistoric and modern crocodiles.","zh":"主龍類包括史前及現代鱷魚。"},{"en":"Prehistoric and modern crocodiles means ancient crocodile relatives as well as crocodiles living today.","zh":"Prehistoric and modern crocodiles 指古代鱷魚親屬以及今日仍生存的鱷魚。"},{"en":"A museum may compare prehistoric and modern crocodiles to show how some body plans last for a long time.","zh":"博物館可能比較史前及現代鱷魚，以展示某些身體模式如何持續很久。"},{"en":"Studying both old and living forms helps scientists understand evolutionary change.","zh":"研究古代和現存形式，幫助科學家理解演化變化。"},{"en":"This phrase connects fossil animals with their present-day relatives.","zh":"這個片語把化石動物與現代親屬連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"now-extinct","meaning":"現已滅絕的","examples":[{"en":"The now-extinct thecodonts, pterosaurs and dinosaurs were archosaurs.","zh":"現已滅絕的槽齒類、翼龍和恐龍都是主龍類。"},{"en":"Now-extinct means no longer living anywhere in the world today.","zh":"Now-extinct 指今天世界上任何地方都不再存活。"},{"en":"The dodo is a now-extinct bird that people know from drawings and specimens.","zh":"渡渡鳥是現已滅絕的鳥類，人們透過圖畫和標本認識牠。"},{"en":"If a species becomes extinct, future generations can learn about it only through evidence such as fossils or records.","zh":"如果物種滅絕，後代只能透過化石或紀錄等證據了解它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes animals or plants that once existed but no longer survive.","zh":"這個片語描述曾經存在但不再存活的動植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"thecodonts","meaning":"槽齒類爬行動物","examples":[{"en":"Thecodonts are included among the archosaurs.","zh":"槽齒類爬行動物被包括在主龍類之中。"},{"en":"Thecodonts were ancient reptiles linked to the ancestry of several archosaur groups.","zh":"Thecodonts 是與幾個主龍類群祖先有關的古代爬行動物。"},{"en":"A fossil display may mention thecodonts when explaining early dinosaur relatives.","zh":"化石展示可能在解釋早期恐龍親屬時提到槽齒類爬行動物。"},{"en":"Studying thecodonts helps scientists discuss how later reptiles may have evolved.","zh":"研究槽齒類幫助科學家討論後來爬行動物可能如何演化。"},{"en":"This term refers to an extinct reptile group in prehistoric classification.","zh":"這個術語指史前分類中的一個已滅絕爬行動物類群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pterosaurs","meaning":"翼龍","examples":[{"en":"Pterosaurs were now-extinct archosaurs.","zh":"翼龍是現已滅絕的主龍類。"},{"en":"Pterosaurs were flying reptiles that lived alongside dinosaurs but were not dinosaurs themselves.","zh":"Pterosaurs 是與恐龍同時代生活的飛行爬行動物，但牠們本身不是恐龍。"},{"en":"Children often confuse pterosaurs with dinosaurs because both appear in prehistoric exhibitions.","zh":"孩子常把翼龍與恐龍混淆，因為兩者都出現在史前展覽中。"},{"en":"Wings helped pterosaurs occupy the skies while many dinosaurs lived mainly on land.","zh":"翅膀幫助翼龍佔據天空，而許多恐龍主要生活在陸地上。"},{"en":"This word names an extinct group of flying reptiles.","zh":"這個詞命名一個已滅絕的飛行爬行動物類群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"palaeontologists believe that","meaning":"古生物學家認為","examples":[{"en":"Palaeontologists believe that dinosaurs and crocodiles evolved from pseudosuchian thecodonts.","zh":"古生物學家認為恐龍和鱷魚由偽鱷類槽齒動物演化而來。"},{"en":"Palaeontologists believe that means fossil scientists think something is true based on evidence.","zh":"Palaeontologists believe that 指研究化石的科學家根據證據認為某事為真。"},{"en":"Palaeontologists believe that some fossils show how animals changed over millions of years.","zh":"古生物學家認為一些化石顯示動物如何在數百萬年間改變。"},{"en":"When fossil evidence is incomplete, scientists may state what they believe rather than claim total certainty.","zh":"當化石證據不完整，科學家可能說他們認為某事，而不是聲稱完全確定。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a scientific view based on fossil study.","zh":"這個片語引出基於化石研究的科學觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"evolved from","meaning":"由……演化而來","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs and crocodiles evolved from creatures called pseudosuchian thecodonts.","zh":"恐龍和鱷魚由名為偽鱷類槽齒動物的生物演化而來。"},{"en":"Evolved from means developed gradually from an earlier living form over a long period.","zh":"Evolved from 指在很長時間內由較早的生命形式逐漸發展而來。"},{"en":"Modern birds are often taught as animals that evolved from earlier dinosaur relatives.","zh":"現代鳥類常被教導為由較早的恐龍親屬演化而來的動物。"},{"en":"Evolution happens across many generations, not within one individual’s lifetime.","zh":"演化發生於許多世代之中，而不是在一個個體的一生中。"},{"en":"This phrase explains ancestry and long-term biological change.","zh":"這個片語解釋祖先關係和長期生物變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Triassic Period","meaning":"三疊紀","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs evolved in the later years of the Triassic Period.","zh":"恐龍在三疊紀較後期演化出來。"},{"en":"The Triassic Period was an early period of the Mesozoic Era before the Jurassic Period.","zh":"The Triassic Period 是中生代早期的一個時期，早於侏羅紀。"},{"en":"In a museum timeline, the Triassic Period may appear before the famous age of giant Jurassic dinosaurs.","zh":"在博物館時間線中，三疊紀可能出現在著名巨型侏羅紀恐龍時代之前。"},{"en":"Knowing the Triassic Period helps students place dinosaurs in geological time.","zh":"認識三疊紀幫助學生把恐龍放入地質時間中。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major period in Earth’s prehistoric history.","zh":"這個片語命名地球史前歷史中的一個主要時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"creatures called","meaning":"名為……的生物","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs evolved from creatures called pseudosuchian thecodonts.","zh":"恐龍由名為偽鱷類槽齒動物的生物演化而來。"},{"en":"Creatures called means animals or living beings known by a particular name.","zh":"Creatures called 指以某特定名稱為人所知的動物或生物。"},{"en":"Children may learn about sea creatures called plankton in a science lesson.","zh":"孩子可能在科學課學到名為浮游生物的海洋生物。"},{"en":"Naming creatures helps scientists discuss them clearly and compare them with others.","zh":"命名生物幫助科學家清楚討論並與其他生物比較。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the name of an animal group.","zh":"這個片語引出某個動物類群的名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pseudosuchian thecodonts","meaning":"偽鱷類槽齒動物","examples":[{"en":"Pseudosuchian thecodonts were ancestral creatures linked to dinosaurs and crocodiles.","zh":"偽鱷類槽齒動物是與恐龍和鱷魚有關的祖先生物。"},{"en":"Pseudosuchian thecodonts were prehistoric reptiles described as possible ancestors of some archosaurs.","zh":"Pseudosuchian thecodonts 是被描述為某些主龍類可能祖先的史前爬行動物。"},{"en":"A fossil textbook may mention pseudosuchian thecodonts when explaining early reptile evolution.","zh":"化石教科書可能在解釋早期爬行動物演化時提到偽鱷類槽齒動物。"},{"en":"These animals matter because they help link older reptile forms with later groups.","zh":"這些動物重要，因為牠們幫助連接較古老爬行動物形式與後來類群。"},{"en":"This technical term refers to ancient reptiles in the dinosaur ancestry discussion.","zh":"這個技術術語指恐龍祖先討論中的古代爬行動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"different types of","meaning":"不同種類的……","examples":[{"en":"Different types of thecodont evolved earlier in the Triassic Period.","zh":"不同種類的槽齒動物在三疊紀較早期演化出來。"},{"en":"Different types of means several kinds or varieties of something.","zh":"Different types of 指某事物的幾種或多種種類。"},{"en":"Students may use different types of notes, such as mind maps, tables and flashcards.","zh":"學生可能使用不同種類的筆記，例如心智圖、表格和字卡。"},{"en":"Different types can have shared features but still differ in important details.","zh":"不同種類可以有共同特徵，但仍在重要細節上不同。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show variety inside one broad group.","zh":"這個片語幫助顯示一個大類別內部的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reptiles known as","meaning":"被稱為……的爬行動物","examples":[{"en":"Lizards and snakes evolved from reptiles known as eosuchians.","zh":"蜥蜴和蛇由被稱為曙鱷類的爬行動物演化而來。"},{"en":"Reptiles known as means reptiles that are called by a particular scientific name.","zh":"Reptiles known as 指被某個特定科學名稱稱呼的爬行動物。"},{"en":"A textbook may introduce reptiles known as archosaurs before discussing dinosaurs.","zh":"教科書可能先介紹被稱為主龍類的爬行動物，再討論恐龍。"},{"en":"Scientific names help readers know exactly which animal group is being discussed.","zh":"科學名稱幫助讀者準確知道正在討論哪個動物類群。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a general animal type with a more specific name.","zh":"這個片語把一般動物類型與更具體名稱連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"eosuchians","meaning":"曙鱷類爬行動物","examples":[{"en":"Eosuchians were reptiles from which lizards and snakes are believed to have evolved.","zh":"曙鱷類爬行動物被認為是蜥蜴和蛇演化而來的來源。"},{"en":"Eosuchians were ancient reptiles linked in the passage to the ancestry of lizards and snakes.","zh":"Eosuchians 是文章中與蜥蜴和蛇祖先有關的古代爬行動物。"},{"en":"A palaeontology class may mention eosuchians when comparing early reptile branches.","zh":"古生物課可能在比較早期爬行動物分支時提到曙鱷類。"},{"en":"Knowing eosuchians helps students see that dinosaurs and lizards had different ancestry lines.","zh":"認識曙鱷類幫助學生看見恐龍和蜥蜴有不同祖先線。"},{"en":"This technical word names an ancient reptile group in the passage.","zh":"這個技術詞命名文章中的一個古代爬行動物類群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"skeletal differences between","meaning":"……之間的骨骼差異","examples":[{"en":"The most important skeletal differences between dinosaurs and other archosaurs are in the skull, pelvis and limbs.","zh":"恐龍與其他主龍類之間最重要的骨骼差異在頭骨、骨盆及四肢。"},{"en":"Skeletal differences between two animals are differences in their bone structure.","zh":"Skeletal differences between two animals 指兩種動物骨骼結構上的差異。"},{"en":"Doctors notice skeletal differences between children and adults when reading X-rays.","zh":"醫生閱讀 X 光片時，會注意兒童和成人之間的骨骼差異。"},{"en":"Skeletal differences can explain why two animals move in different ways.","zh":"骨骼差異可以解釋兩種動物為何以不同方式移動。"},{"en":"This phrase compares bodies by looking at bones.","zh":"這個片語透過骨骼比較身體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"bones of the skull","meaning":"頭骨的骨骼","examples":[{"en":"Some key dinosaur features are found in the bones of the skull.","zh":"一些關鍵恐龍特徵可在頭骨的骨骼中找到。"},{"en":"Bones of the skull are the hard parts that form and protect the head.","zh":"Bones of the skull 是形成並保護頭部的堅硬部分。"},{"en":"In biology class, students may label the bones of the skull on a diagram.","zh":"在生物課中，學生可能在圖表上標示頭骨的骨骼。"},{"en":"Skull bones can reveal how an animal ate, breathed or sensed its surroundings.","zh":"頭骨骨骼可以揭示動物如何進食、呼吸或感知周圍環境。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the head bones used in anatomical comparison.","zh":"這個片語指用於解剖比較的頭部骨骼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pelvis and limbs","meaning":"骨盆及四肢","examples":[{"en":"The pelvis and limbs help distinguish dinosaurs from other archosaurs.","zh":"骨盆及四肢幫助把恐龍與其他主龍類區分開。"},{"en":"Pelvis and limbs means the hip region and the arms or legs of an animal.","zh":"Pelvis and limbs 指動物的髖部區域以及手臂或腿。"},{"en":"A doctor may examine the pelvis and limbs after a serious fall.","zh":"嚴重跌倒後，醫生可能檢查骨盆及四肢。"},{"en":"In dinosaurs, the pelvis and limbs reveal how the animal stood and moved.","zh":"在恐龍身上，骨盆及四肢揭示動物如何站立和移動。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on body parts important for movement and posture.","zh":"這個片語集中於對移動和姿勢重要的身體部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a great range of","meaning":"各式各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaur skulls are found in a great range of shapes and sizes.","zh":"恐龍頭骨有各式各樣的形狀和大小。"},{"en":"A great range of means a very wide variety of something.","zh":"A great range of 指非常多樣化的某事物。"},{"en":"A supermarket sells a great range of fruit, from apples to dragon fruit.","zh":"超級市場售賣各式各樣的水果，由蘋果到火龍果都有。"},{"en":"A great range of forms suggests that animals may have lived in different ways.","zh":"各式各樣的形式暗示動物可能以不同方式生活。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights variety and diversity.","zh":"這個片語突出變化和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"shapes and sizes","meaning":"形狀和大小","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaur skulls came in many shapes and sizes.","zh":"恐龍頭骨有許多形狀和大小。"},{"en":"Shapes and sizes means the forms and physical dimensions of objects or bodies.","zh":"Shapes and sizes 指物件或身體的形式和實際尺寸。"},{"en":"School bags come in different shapes and sizes for different students’ needs.","zh":"書包有不同形狀和大小，以配合不同學生需要。"},{"en":"Different shapes and sizes can show that objects are designed for different purposes.","zh":"不同形狀和大小可以顯示物件為不同用途而設計。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to describe physical variety.","zh":"這個片語常用來描述外形上的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reflecting","meaning":"反映","examples":[{"en":"The shapes of dinosaur skulls reflect different eating habits and lifestyles.","zh":"恐龍頭骨形狀反映不同飲食習慣和生活方式。"},{"en":"Reflecting means showing, indicating or being connected with something deeper.","zh":"Reflecting 指顯示、表明或與較深層事物有關。"},{"en":"A student’s timetable may reflect their priorities if study time is clearly protected.","zh":"如果學習時間被清楚保護，學生時間表可能反映他的優先事項。"},{"en":"In animals, body shape can reflect behaviour, diet and environment.","zh":"在動物身上，身體形狀可以反映行為、飲食和環境。"},{"en":"This word explains how one visible feature can show a hidden pattern.","zh":"這個詞解釋一個可見特徵如何顯示隱藏模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"eating habits","meaning":"飲食習慣","examples":[{"en":"Skull shapes can reflect the eating habits of dinosaurs.","zh":"頭骨形狀可以反映恐龍的飲食習慣。"},{"en":"Eating habits are the kinds of food an animal or person usually eats and how they eat them.","zh":"Eating habits 是動物或人通常吃甚麼以及如何進食的方式。"},{"en":"A dentist may notice a child’s eating habits from tooth decay or healthy gums.","zh":"牙醫可能從蛀牙或健康牙齦看出孩子的飲食習慣。"},{"en":"An animal’s teeth and jaws can reveal its eating habits.","zh":"動物的牙齒和顎部可以揭示牠的飲食習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase connects diet with regular behaviour.","zh":"這個片語把飲食與常規行為連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lifestyles","meaning":"生活方式","examples":[{"en":"Different skull shapes reflected different dinosaur lifestyles.","zh":"不同頭骨形狀反映不同恐龍生活方式。"},{"en":"Lifestyles are the ways living things usually live, behave, move and interact with their environment.","zh":"Lifestyles 是生物通常如何生活、行動、移動和與環境互動的方式。"},{"en":"City and village lifestyles can differ in transport, work and family routines.","zh":"城市和鄉村生活方式可以在交通、工作和家庭日常上不同。"},{"en":"In animals, body features can reveal whether lifestyles were active, slow, solitary or social.","zh":"在動物身上，身體特徵可以揭示生活方式是活躍、緩慢、獨居或群居。"},{"en":"This word describes regular patterns of living.","zh":"這個詞描述生活的常規模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a large and varied group of","meaning":"大型而種類繁多的……","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs were a large and varied group of animals.","zh":"恐龍是一個大型而種類繁多的動物群。"},{"en":"A large and varied group of something means a big group containing many different types.","zh":"A large and varied group of something 指一個包含許多不同種類的大群體。"},{"en":"A school library may have a large and varied group of books for different reading levels.","zh":"學校圖書館可能有大型而種類繁多的書籍，適合不同閱讀程度。"},{"en":"When a group is varied, one example cannot represent all its members.","zh":"當一個群體種類繁多，一個例子不能代表所有成員。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights both size and diversity.","zh":"這個片語同時突出規模和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dominated life on Earth","meaning":"主宰地球生命","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs dominated life on Earth for 165 million years.","zh":"恐龍主宰地球生命達一億六千五百萬年。"},{"en":"Dominated life on Earth means became the most powerful or widespread animal group in many environments.","zh":"Dominated life on Earth 指在許多環境中成為最有力量或最廣泛分布的動物群。"},{"en":"Humans now dominate many parts of Earth through farming, cities and technology.","zh":"人類如今透過農業、城市和科技主宰地球許多地方。"},{"en":"A group can dominate when it spreads widely and strongly shapes ecosystems.","zh":"當一個群體廣泛分布並強烈塑造生態系統，它就可以主宰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-lasting ecological importance.","zh":"這個片語描述長期的生態重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an extraordinary 165 million years","meaning":"長達一億六千五百萬年的非凡時期","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs dominated life on Earth for an extraordinary 165 million years.","zh":"恐龍主宰地球生命長達一億六千五百萬年的非凡時期。"},{"en":"An extraordinary 165 million years means an unusually long and impressive period of time.","zh":"An extraordinary 165 million years 指一段異常漫長而令人驚嘆的時間。"},{"en":"A building that lasts five hundred years is impressive, but 165 million years is on a geological scale.","zh":"一座建築能維持五百年已很了不起，但一億六千五百萬年是地質尺度。"},{"en":"Such a long time shows that dinosaurs were highly successful as a group.","zh":"如此漫長時間顯示恐龍作為一個群體非常成功。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the surprising length of dinosaur dominance.","zh":"這個片語強調恐龍主宰時間長得驚人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"unlike","meaning":"與……不同","examples":[{"en":"Unlike the skulls of other known animals, dinosaur skulls had two long bones called vomers.","zh":"與其他已知動物的頭骨不同，恐龍頭骨有兩條被稱為犁骨的長骨。"},{"en":"Unlike means different from or in contrast to something else.","zh":"Unlike 指與某事物不同或形成對比。"},{"en":"Unlike adults, young children may need pictures to understand a new word.","zh":"與成人不同，年幼孩子可能需要圖片來理解新詞。"},{"en":"This word helps writers compare two things by showing difference.","zh":"這個詞幫助作者透過顯示差異來比較兩件事。"},{"en":"It is useful when one group has a feature another group does not have.","zh":"當一個群體有某特徵而另一個沒有時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"known as vomers","meaning":"被稱為犁骨","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaur skulls had two long bones known as vomers.","zh":"恐龍頭骨有兩條被稱為犁骨的長骨。"},{"en":"Known as vomers means called vomers in anatomical terminology.","zh":"Known as vomers 指在解剖術語中被稱為犁骨。"},{"en":"In a biology lesson, a bone may be known by a technical name that students must learn.","zh":"在生物課中，某塊骨可能有學生必須學習的技術名稱。"},{"en":"Scientific names allow researchers to identify body parts precisely.","zh":"科學名稱讓研究人員準確識別身體部位。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the technical name for a bone.","zh":"這個片語引出某塊骨的技術名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"extended on either side of","meaning":"延伸至……兩側","examples":[{"en":"The vomers extended on either side of the head.","zh":"犁骨延伸至頭部兩側。"},{"en":"Extended on either side of means stretched along both sides of something.","zh":"Extended on either side of 指沿某物兩邊伸展。"},{"en":"A long balcony may extend on either side of a hotel room window.","zh":"長陽台可能延伸至酒店房窗戶兩側。"},{"en":"Describing where a body part extends helps readers imagine its position.","zh":"描述身體部位延伸到哪裏，幫助讀者想像其位置。"},{"en":"This phrase explains length and location on both sides.","zh":"這個片語解釋長度和兩側位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the front of the snout","meaning":"鼻吻前端","examples":[{"en":"The vomers ran from the front of the snout towards the skull openings.","zh":"犁骨由鼻吻前端延伸向頭骨開口。"},{"en":"The front of the snout means the forward part of an animal’s nose or muzzle.","zh":"The front of the snout 指動物鼻部或吻部的前方部分。"},{"en":"A dog may touch food with the front of its snout before eating.","zh":"狗進食前可能用鼻吻前端碰觸食物。"},{"en":"In fossil anatomy, the front of the snout can help show how an animal fed.","zh":"在化石解剖中，鼻吻前端可以幫助顯示動物如何進食。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific part of an animal’s head.","zh":"這個片語描述動物頭部的特定部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"antorbital fenestrae","meaning":"眶前孔","examples":[{"en":"The antorbital fenestrae were holes situated in front of the eye sockets.","zh":"眶前孔是位於眼眶前方的孔洞。"},{"en":"Antorbital fenestrae are skull openings located before the eye sockets in some ancient reptiles.","zh":"Antorbital fenestrae 是某些古代爬行動物頭骨中位於眼眶前的開口。"},{"en":"A palaeontology diagram may label the antorbital fenestrae to show dinosaur skull structure.","zh":"古生物圖表可能標示眶前孔，以展示恐龍頭骨結構。"},{"en":"These openings help scientists compare dinosaurs with other archosaurs.","zh":"這些開口幫助科學家把恐龍與其他主龍類比較。"},{"en":"This technical term names particular holes in the skull.","zh":"這個技術術語命名頭骨中的特定孔洞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"situated in front of","meaning":"位於……前方","examples":[{"en":"The antorbital fenestrae were situated in front of the dinosaur’s eye sockets.","zh":"眶前孔位於恐龍眼眶前方。"},{"en":"Situated in front of means located before something in position.","zh":"Situated in front of 指在位置上位於某物之前。"},{"en":"A school office may be situated in front of the library, near the main entrance.","zh":"學校辦公室可能位於圖書館前方，靠近正門。"},{"en":"Location words help readers understand the arrangement of parts or places.","zh":"位置詞幫助讀者理解部位或地方的排列。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear positional relationship.","zh":"這個片語給出清楚的位置關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"orbits or eye sockets","meaning":"眼眶","examples":[{"en":"The antorbital fenestrae sat in front of the orbits or eye sockets.","zh":"眶前孔位於眼眶前方。"},{"en":"Orbits or eye sockets are the skull spaces where the eyes sit.","zh":"Orbits or eye sockets 是頭骨中眼睛所在的空間。"},{"en":"In anatomy class, students may label the orbits or eye sockets on a skull model.","zh":"在解剖課中，學生可能在頭骨模型上標示眼眶。"},{"en":"Eye sockets protect the eyes and help define the shape of the skull.","zh":"眼眶保護眼睛，並幫助決定頭骨形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase gives both the technical and everyday term for the same structure.","zh":"這個片語同時給出同一結構的技術和日常名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"whether large or small","meaning":"無論大小","examples":[{"en":"All dinosaurs, whether large or small, shared a common body plan.","zh":"所有恐龍，無論大小，都擁有共同的身體結構模式。"},{"en":"Whether large or small means regardless of size.","zh":"Whether large or small 指不論大小如何。"},{"en":"All students, whether strong or weak, need clear feedback to improve.","zh":"所有學生，無論強弱，都需要清楚回饋來進步。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a statement applies to every member of a group.","zh":"這個片語顯示某說法適用於群體中的每個成員。"},{"en":"It is useful when size or level does not change the main point.","zh":"當大小或程度不改變主要觀點時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"quadrupedal or bipedal","meaning":"四足或雙足行走的","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs could be quadrupedal or bipedal.","zh":"恐龍可以是四足或雙足行走的。"},{"en":"Quadrupedal or bipedal means walking on four legs or on two legs.","zh":"Quadrupedal or bipedal 指用四隻腳或兩隻腳行走。"},{"en":"A dog is quadrupedal, while a human is bipedal.","zh":"狗是四足行走的，而人類是雙足行走的。"},{"en":"Whether an animal is quadrupedal or bipedal affects its balance and movement.","zh":"動物是四足還是雙足，會影響牠的平衡和移動。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two basic ways of walking.","zh":"這個片語比較兩種基本行走方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fleet-footed or slow-moving","meaning":"步履敏捷或行動緩慢的","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs could be fleet-footed or slow-moving.","zh":"恐龍可以是步履敏捷或行動緩慢的。"},{"en":"Fleet-footed or slow-moving means quick on the feet or moving slowly.","zh":"Fleet-footed or slow-moving 指腳步快速或移動緩慢。"},{"en":"In a sports class, one student may be fleet-footed while another is slow-moving but strong.","zh":"在體育課中，一位學生可能步履敏捷，而另一位行動較慢但強壯。"},{"en":"Speed affects how an animal hunts, escapes or travels.","zh":"速度影響動物如何捕獵、逃走或移動。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts fast movement with slow movement.","zh":"這個片語把快速移動與緩慢移動作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"shared a common body plan","meaning":"擁有共同的身體結構模式","examples":[{"en":"All dinosaurs shared a common body plan.","zh":"所有恐龍都擁有共同的身體結構模式。"},{"en":"Shared a common body plan means had the same basic arrangement of body parts.","zh":"Shared a common body plan 指有相同的基本身體部位排列。"},{"en":"Different car models may share a common design plan even if their colours and sizes differ.","zh":"不同汽車型號即使顏色和大小不同，也可能擁有共同設計模式。"},{"en":"A common body plan helps scientists recognise members of the same broad group.","zh":"共同身體結構模式幫助科學家辨認同一大類群成員。"},{"en":"This phrase explains similarity beneath surface variety.","zh":"這個片語解釋表面多樣性之下的相似性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"identification of this plan","meaning":"辨認出這種結構模式","examples":[{"en":"Identification of this plan helps scientists recognise dinosaurs.","zh":"辨認出這種結構模式幫助科學家識別恐龍。"},{"en":"Identification of this plan means recognising the shared body structure described.","zh":"Identification of this plan 指辨認出所描述的共同身體結構。"},{"en":"A teacher’s identification of a student’s writing pattern can help correct repeated mistakes.","zh":"老師辨認出學生的寫作模式，可以幫助修正常見錯誤。"},{"en":"Once scientists identify a pattern, they can classify new evidence more confidently.","zh":"一旦科學家辨認出模式，他們可以更有信心地分類新證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognising an important structure or pattern.","zh":"這個片語描述辨認重要結構或模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make it possible to","meaning":"使……成為可能","examples":[{"en":"This body plan makes it possible to differentiate dinosaurs from other animals.","zh":"這種身體結構模式使將恐龍與其他動物區分開成為可能。"},{"en":"Make it possible to means allow something to happen or be done.","zh":"Make it possible to 指容許某事發生或被完成。"},{"en":"Online dictionaries make it possible to check pronunciation at home.","zh":"網上字典使在家查發音成為可能。"},{"en":"A clear classification system makes it possible to compare animals accurately.","zh":"清楚分類系統使準確比較動物成為可能。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what enables an action.","zh":"這個片語顯示甚麼令某行動能夠發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"differentiate dinosaurs from","meaning":"將恐龍與……區分開","examples":[{"en":"The common body plan helps differentiate dinosaurs from other animals.","zh":"共同身體結構模式幫助將恐龍與其他動物區分開。"},{"en":"To differentiate dinosaurs from other animals means to tell dinosaurs apart from other animal groups.","zh":"To differentiate dinosaurs from other animals 指把恐龍與其他動物類群分辨出來。"},{"en":"Teachers use key features to differentiate similar vocabulary words from one another.","zh":"老師使用關鍵特徵把相似詞彙彼此區分開。"},{"en":"Clear differences prevent students from confusing dinosaurs with lizards or crocodiles.","zh":"清楚差異防止學生把恐龍與蜥蜴或鱷魚混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a careful distinction.","zh":"這個片語描述作出仔細區分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"most significantly","meaning":"最重要的是","examples":[{"en":"Most significantly, dinosaurs held their hind limbs beneath the body.","zh":"最重要的是，恐龍把後肢置於身體下方。"},{"en":"Most significantly means most importantly or most worth noticing.","zh":"Most significantly 指最重要或最值得注意。"},{"en":"A student improved vocabulary and grammar, but most significantly, their ideas became clearer.","zh":"學生改善了詞彙和文法，但最重要的是，想法變得更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the key point among several details.","zh":"這個片語在多個細節中突出關鍵點。"},{"en":"It tells readers which feature matters most.","zh":"它告訴讀者哪個特徵最重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pelvis and femur","meaning":"骨盆和股骨","examples":[{"en":"The pelvis and femur had evolved in a distinctive way in dinosaurs.","zh":"恐龍的骨盆和股骨以獨特方式演化。"},{"en":"Pelvis and femur means the hip structure and the thigh bone.","zh":"Pelvis and femur 指髖部結構和大腿骨。"},{"en":"A doctor may examine the pelvis and femur after a person suffers a serious leg injury.","zh":"人嚴重腿傷後，醫生可能檢查骨盆和股骨。"},{"en":"In dinosaurs, the pelvis and femur shaped how the hind limbs supported the body.","zh":"在恐龍身上，骨盆和股骨塑造後肢如何支撐身體。"},{"en":"This phrase names two important bones for posture and movement.","zh":"這個片語命名對姿勢和移動重要的兩塊骨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hind limbs","meaning":"後肢","examples":[{"en":"The hind limbs of dinosaurs were held vertically beneath the body.","zh":"恐龍的後肢垂直支撐在身體下方。"},{"en":"Hind limbs are the back legs of an animal.","zh":"Hind limbs 是動物的後腿。"},{"en":"A rabbit uses its powerful hind limbs to jump.","zh":"兔子用強壯後肢跳躍。"},{"en":"The position of hind limbs can affect balance, speed and walking style.","zh":"後肢的位置可以影響平衡、速度和行走方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the rear limbs used for support and movement.","zh":"這個片語描述用於支撐和移動的後方肢體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"held vertically beneath","meaning":"垂直支撐在……下方","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaur hind limbs were held vertically beneath the body.","zh":"恐龍後肢垂直支撐在身體下方。"},{"en":"Held vertically beneath means positioned straight down under something.","zh":"Held vertically beneath 指筆直向下位於某物下方。"},{"en":"A table leg is held vertically beneath the tabletop to support its weight.","zh":"桌腳垂直支撐在桌面下方，以承托重量。"},{"en":"When limbs are held vertically beneath the body, weight can be supported more efficiently.","zh":"當肢體垂直支撐在身體下方，重量可以更有效地被承托。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a straight downward support position.","zh":"這個片語解釋筆直向下的支撐位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rather than sprawling out","meaning":"而不是向外張開","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaur limbs were held beneath the body rather than sprawling out to the sides.","zh":"恐龍四肢置於身體下方，而不是向兩側外展。"},{"en":"Rather than sprawling out means instead of spreading outward in a low, sideways position.","zh":"Rather than sprawling out 指不是以低而向側面的姿勢向外伸展。"},{"en":"Good posture means keeping the feet under the body rather than sprawling out awkwardly.","zh":"良好姿勢是把腳放在身體下方，而不是笨拙地向外張開。"},{"en":"This contrast helps explain why dinosaur movement differed from lizard movement.","zh":"這個對比幫助解釋恐龍移動方式為何不同於蜥蜴。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly contrasts upright support with sideways extension.","zh":"這個片語清楚對比直立支撐與側向伸展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sprawling out to the sides","meaning":"向兩側外展","examples":[{"en":"The limbs of a lizard tend to sprawl out to the sides.","zh":"蜥蜴的四肢往往向兩側外展。"},{"en":"Sprawling out to the sides means spreading sideways rather than standing straight underneath the body.","zh":"Sprawling out to the sides 指向側面伸展，而不是直立位於身體下方。"},{"en":"A tired child may sprawl out on the sofa with arms and legs spread wide.","zh":"疲倦孩子可能攤在沙發上，手腳大幅張開。"},{"en":"Sideways limb position can make an animal’s body stay closer to the ground.","zh":"側向肢體位置可以令動物身體更接近地面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a spread-out, low posture.","zh":"這個片語描述伸展開來的低姿勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a sharply inward-turned neck","meaning":"急劇向內彎曲的頸部","examples":[{"en":"The femur of a dinosaur had a sharply inward-turned neck.","zh":"恐龍的股骨有急劇向內彎曲的頸部。"},{"en":"A sharply inward-turned neck is a bone section that bends strongly toward the inside.","zh":"Sharply inward-turned neck 是一段骨頭明顯向內彎曲的部分。"},{"en":"In anatomy diagrams, arrows may show where a bone turns inward.","zh":"在解剖圖中，箭嘴可能顯示骨頭在哪裏向內彎曲。"},{"en":"This feature helped the femur fit into the hip structure in a particular way.","zh":"這個特徵幫助股骨以特定方式嵌入髖部結構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the shape of a bone, not an animal’s neck.","zh":"這個片語描述骨頭形狀，而不是動物的頸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a ball-shaped head","meaning":"球狀頭部","examples":[{"en":"The femur had a ball-shaped head.","zh":"股骨有球狀頭部。"},{"en":"A ball-shaped head is a rounded end of a bone that can fit into a socket.","zh":"Ball-shaped head 是骨頭末端的圓形部分，可以嵌入關節窩。"},{"en":"The human thigh bone also has a rounded head that helps form the hip joint.","zh":"人類大腿骨也有圓形頭部，幫助形成髖關節。"},{"en":"A ball-shaped head allows smoother movement inside a joint.","zh":"球狀頭部讓關節內的活動更順暢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rounded bone end used in joint movement.","zh":"這個片語描述用於關節活動的圓形骨端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"slotted into","meaning":"嵌入……","examples":[{"en":"The ball-shaped head slotted into a fully open acetabulum.","zh":"球狀頭部嵌入完全開放的髖臼。"},{"en":"Slotted into means fitted neatly into a space made for it.","zh":"Slotted into 指整齊地嵌入為它而設的空間。"},{"en":"A key card slotted into the hotel-room holder can turn on the lights.","zh":"房卡嵌入酒店房間插槽後，可以開啟燈光。"},{"en":"When one part slots into another, the two parts can work together securely.","zh":"當一個部分嵌入另一個部分，兩者可以穩固地一起運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a precise fit between two parts.","zh":"這個片語描述兩個部件之間的精確配合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a fully open acetabulum","meaning":"完全開放的髖臼","examples":[{"en":"The ball-shaped head slotted into a fully open acetabulum.","zh":"球狀頭部嵌入完全開放的髖臼。"},{"en":"A fully open acetabulum is an open hip socket where the femur fits.","zh":"Fully open acetabulum 是股骨嵌入的開放髖臼。"},{"en":"In a skeleton model, the acetabulum is the cup-like area of the pelvis.","zh":"在骨骼模型中，髖臼是骨盆上像杯狀的區域。"},{"en":"This open socket helped dinosaurs hold the hind limb beneath the body.","zh":"這種開放窩位幫助恐龍把後肢置於身體下方。"},{"en":"This technical phrase describes a key hip feature in dinosaur anatomy.","zh":"這個技術片語描述恐龍解剖中的關鍵髖部特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hip socket","meaning":"髖臼","examples":[{"en":"The acetabulum is also called the hip socket.","zh":"Acetabulum 也稱為髖臼。"},{"en":"A hip socket is the part of the pelvis where the thigh bone fits.","zh":"Hip socket 是骨盆中股骨嵌入的位置。"},{"en":"A doctor may check the hip socket if a patient feels pain when walking.","zh":"如果病人走路時感到疼痛，醫生可能檢查髖臼。"},{"en":"The shape of the hip socket affects how the leg moves.","zh":"髖臼的形狀影響腿部如何活動。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an everyday name for the acetabulum.","zh":"這個片語給出 acetabulum 的日常名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"supra-acetabular crest","meaning":"髖臼上嵴","examples":[{"en":"A supra-acetabular crest helped prevent dislocation of the femur.","zh":"髖臼上嵴幫助防止股骨脫臼。"},{"en":"A supra-acetabular crest is a bony ridge above the hip socket.","zh":"Supra-acetabular crest 是髖臼上方的骨質嵴。"},{"en":"In an anatomy diagram, this crest may be shown as a raised edge over the acetabulum.","zh":"在解剖圖中，這道嵴可能顯示為髖臼上方凸起的邊緣。"},{"en":"A ridge like this can help keep the femur in position.","zh":"這類嵴可以幫助股骨保持在正確位置。"},{"en":"This technical term names a supporting feature of the hip.","zh":"這個技術術語命名髖部的一個支撐特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prevent dislocation","meaning":"防止脫臼","examples":[{"en":"The crest helped prevent dislocation of the femur.","zh":"這道嵴幫助防止股骨脫臼。"},{"en":"To prevent dislocation means to stop a bone from slipping out of its joint.","zh":"To prevent dislocation 指防止骨頭滑出關節位置。"},{"en":"Strong muscles can help prevent dislocation during sport.","zh":"強壯肌肉可以在運動中幫助防止脫臼。"},{"en":"If a joint is poorly supported, dislocation becomes more likely.","zh":"如果關節支撐不足，脫臼會更容易發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protecting a joint from being forced out of place.","zh":"這個片語描述保護關節不被迫離原位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"knee joint","meaning":"膝關節","examples":[{"en":"The knee joint was aligned below the acetabulum.","zh":"膝關節與髖臼下方對齊。"},{"en":"The knee joint is the place where the upper and lower leg bones meet.","zh":"Knee joint 是上腿骨和下腿骨相接的位置。"},{"en":"A runner may feel pain in the knee joint after training too hard.","zh":"跑手訓練過度後，可能感到膝關節疼痛。"},{"en":"The position of the knee joint affects walking, running and balance.","zh":"膝關節的位置影響行走、奔跑和平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major joint in the leg.","zh":"這個片語命名腿部的一個主要關節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"aligned below","meaning":"與……下方對齊","examples":[{"en":"The knee joint was aligned below the hip socket.","zh":"膝關節與髖臼下方對齊。"},{"en":"Aligned below means placed directly or neatly under something else.","zh":"Aligned below 指直接或整齊地放在某物下方。"},{"en":"A chair leg should be aligned below the seat so the chair stays stable.","zh":"椅腳應與座位下方對齊，椅子才穩定。"},{"en":"Proper alignment can make movement stronger and more efficient.","zh":"正確對齊可以令動作更強和更有效率。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordered vertical positioning.","zh":"這個片語描述有秩序的垂直位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"swing backwards and forwards","meaning":"前後擺動","examples":[{"en":"This arrangement allowed the hind limb to swing backwards and forwards.","zh":"這種排列使後肢能夠前後擺動。"},{"en":"To swing backwards and forwards means to move repeatedly to the back and to the front.","zh":"To swing backwards and forwards 指反覆向後和向前移動。"},{"en":"A child on a playground swing moves backwards and forwards.","zh":"遊樂場鞦韆上的孩子會前後擺動。"},{"en":"Limbs that swing this way can help an animal walk efficiently.","zh":"能這樣擺動的肢體可以幫助動物有效行走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated forward-and-back movement.","zh":"這個片語描述反覆前後移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a unique combination of features","meaning":"獨特的特徵組合","examples":[{"en":"A unique combination of features gave dinosaurs a fully improved gait.","zh":"一組獨特的特徵組合給予恐龍完全改良的步態。"},{"en":"A unique combination of features means a special set of characteristics working together.","zh":"Unique combination of features 指一套特殊特徵共同發揮作用。"},{"en":"A good school may have a unique combination of caring teachers, clear rules and strong support.","zh":"好學校可能有關懷老師、清楚規則和強大支援的獨特組合。"},{"en":"When several features work together, the result can be very different from any single feature alone.","zh":"當幾個特徵一起運作，結果可以非常不同於任何單一特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights how multiple characteristics create something distinctive.","zh":"這個片語突出多個特徵如何創造獨特事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fully improved gait","meaning":"完全改良的步態","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs had what is known as a fully improved gait.","zh":"恐龍具有所謂完全改良的步態。"},{"en":"A fully improved gait is an efficient way of walking with limbs held under the body.","zh":"Fully improved gait 是一種四肢置於身體下方的高效行走方式。"},{"en":"A physiotherapist studies gait when helping a patient walk after injury.","zh":"物理治療師幫助病人傷後行走時，會研究步態。"},{"en":"A better gait can reduce wasted movement and support body weight more effectively.","zh":"更好的步態可以減少浪費動作，並更有效支撐體重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an advanced walking pattern.","zh":"這個片語描述一種進階行走模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a highly efficient method of walking","meaning":"高效率的行走方式","examples":[{"en":"This was a highly efficient method of walking.","zh":"這是一種高效率的行走方式。"},{"en":"A highly efficient method of walking uses less wasted energy and supports movement well.","zh":"Highly efficient method of walking 指浪費較少能量並能良好支撐活動的行走方式。"},{"en":"Walking with good posture can be a more efficient method than dragging the feet.","zh":"以良好姿勢行走比拖着腳走更有效率。"},{"en":"Efficient movement helps animals travel, hunt or escape more successfully.","zh":"高效移動幫助動物更成功地移動、捕獵或逃走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a walking style that works especially well.","zh":"這個片語描述特別有效的行走方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"evolved in mammals","meaning":"在哺乳類動物中演化出來","examples":[{"en":"A similar method of walking also evolved in mammals.","zh":"相似的行走方式也在哺乳類動物中演化出來。"},{"en":"Evolved in mammals means developed among animals that feed their young with milk.","zh":"Evolved in mammals 指在以乳汁餵養幼崽的動物群中發展出來。"},{"en":"Upright limb posture evolved in mammals because it supported active movement.","zh":"直立肢體姿勢在哺乳類動物中演化出來，因為它支援活躍移動。"},{"en":"When a feature evolves in different groups, it may show that the feature is useful.","zh":"當某特徵在不同群體中演化出來，它可能顯示該特徵有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a trait developing within the mammal group.","zh":"這個片語描述某特徵在哺乳類群中發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"among reptiles","meaning":"在爬行動物之中","examples":[{"en":"Among reptiles, this gait occurred only in dinosaurs.","zh":"在爬行動物之中，這種步態只出現在恐龍身上。"},{"en":"Among reptiles means within the group of reptile animals.","zh":"Among reptiles 指在爬行動物這個群體之內。"},{"en":"Among students, some learn best by listening while others need visual notes.","zh":"在學生之中，有些人靠聆聽學得最好，另一些人需要視覺筆記。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows a statement to one group and compares members inside it.","zh":"這個片語把說法限制在一個群體內，並比較其成員。"},{"en":"It helps show what is special within a broader category.","zh":"它幫助顯示某事在較大類別中有何特別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"occurred only in","meaning":"只出現在……","examples":[{"en":"Among reptiles, this method of walking occurred only in dinosaurs.","zh":"在爬行動物之中，這種行走方式只出現在恐龍身上。"},{"en":"Occurred only in means appeared or existed exclusively in one group or place.","zh":"Occurred only in 指只在某一群體或地方出現或存在。"},{"en":"A rare spelling mistake occurred only in one student’s essay.","zh":"一個罕見拼寫錯誤只出現在一位學生的作文中。"},{"en":"If a feature occurs only in one group, it can help identify that group.","zh":"如果某特徵只出現在一個群體中，它可以幫助辨認該群體。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights exclusiveness.","zh":"這個片語突出排他性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"for the purpose of","meaning":"為了……","examples":[{"en":"For the purpose of further classification, dinosaurs are divided into two orders.","zh":"為了進一步分類，恐龍被分為兩個目。"},{"en":"For the purpose of means in order to achieve a particular aim.","zh":"For the purpose of 指為了達成某個特定目的。"},{"en":"For the purpose of revision, a student may divide vocabulary into themes.","zh":"為了溫習，學生可能把詞彙分成不同主題。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why an action is taken.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何採取某個行動。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing the reason behind a method or decision.","zh":"當顯示某方法或決定背後的原因時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"further classification","meaning":"進一步分類","examples":[{"en":"Further classification divides dinosaurs into two orders.","zh":"進一步分類把恐龍分為兩個目。"},{"en":"Further classification means more detailed sorting after the first broad grouping.","zh":"Further classification 指在第一個大分類後作更詳細分類。"},{"en":"A teacher may first group essays by grade, then use further classification by grammar problem.","zh":"老師可能先按分數把作文分組，再按文法問題作進一步分類。"},{"en":"Further classification helps reveal smaller differences inside a large category.","zh":"進一步分類幫助揭示大類別內較細的差異。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a second, more precise stage of sorting.","zh":"這個片語描述第二個更精確的分類階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"divided into two orders","meaning":"被分為兩個目","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs are divided into two orders.","zh":"恐龍被分為兩個目。"},{"en":"Divided into two orders means separated into two major scientific groups below a higher category.","zh":"Divided into two orders 指在較高分類之下被分成兩個主要科學類群。"},{"en":"A school competition may be divided into two age groups so younger students are treated fairly.","zh":"學校比賽可能被分為兩個年齡組，讓較年幼學生得到公平對待。"},{"en":"Dividing a large group helps people study its members more clearly.","zh":"分開一個大群體有助人們更清楚研究其成員。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal separation into two categories.","zh":"這個片語描述正式分成兩個類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Saurischia","meaning":"蜥臀目","examples":[{"en":"Saurischia is one of the two orders of dinosaurs.","zh":"蜥臀目是恐龍兩個目之一。"},{"en":"Saurischia is the dinosaur order commonly described as lizard-hipped dinosaurs.","zh":"Saurischia 是通常被描述為蜥臀類恐龍的恐龍目。"},{"en":"A museum chart may place Tyrannosaurus rex under Saurischia.","zh":"博物館圖表可能把暴龍放在蜥臀目之下。"},{"en":"Saurischia is important because it includes theropods and sauropodomorphs.","zh":"蜥臀目重要，因為它包括獸腳類和蜥腳形類。"},{"en":"This term names one of the two major dinosaur orders in the passage.","zh":"這個術語命名文章中兩個主要恐龍目之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"saurischian dinosaurs","meaning":"蜥臀目恐龍","examples":[{"en":"Saurischian dinosaurs are also known as lizard-hipped dinosaurs.","zh":"蜥臀目恐龍也被稱為蜥臀類恐龍。"},{"en":"Saurischian dinosaurs are dinosaurs classified by a particular pelvic structure.","zh":"Saurischian dinosaurs 是按特定骨盆結構分類的恐龍。"},{"en":"Tyrannosaurus rex is often used as an example of a saurischian dinosaur.","zh":"暴龍常被用作蜥臀目恐龍的例子。"},{"en":"Their hip structure helps separate them from ornithischian dinosaurs.","zh":"牠們的髖部結構幫助把牠們與鳥臀目恐龍分開。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to dinosaurs belonging to Saurischia.","zh":"這個片語指屬於蜥臀目的恐龍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Ornithischia","meaning":"鳥臀目","examples":[{"en":"Ornithischia is the other major order of dinosaurs.","zh":"鳥臀目是另一個主要恐龍目。"},{"en":"Ornithischia is the dinosaur order commonly described as bird-hipped dinosaurs.","zh":"Ornithischia 是通常被描述為鳥臀類恐龍的恐龍目。"},{"en":"Triceratops and Stegosaurus are often discussed within Ornithischia.","zh":"三角龍和劍龍常在鳥臀目之內被討論。"},{"en":"This order is separated from Saurischia by pelvic anatomy.","zh":"這個目透過骨盆解剖結構與蜥臀目分開。"},{"en":"This term names one of the two main dinosaur orders in the passage.","zh":"這個術語命名文章中兩個主要恐龍目之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ornithischian dinosaurs","meaning":"鳥臀目恐龍","examples":[{"en":"Ornithischian dinosaurs are also known as bird-hipped dinosaurs.","zh":"鳥臀目恐龍也被稱為鳥臀類恐龍。"},{"en":"Ornithischian dinosaurs are herbivorous dinosaurs classified by a backward-pointing pubis.","zh":"Ornithischian dinosaurs 是按向後指的恥骨分類的草食性恐龍。"},{"en":"A dinosaur textbook may introduce Stegosaurus as an ornithischian dinosaur.","zh":"恐龍教科書可能把劍龍介紹為鳥臀目恐龍。"},{"en":"Their pelvic structure helps distinguish them from saurischian dinosaurs.","zh":"牠們的骨盆結構幫助把牠們與蜥臀目恐龍區分開。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to dinosaurs belonging to Ornithischia.","zh":"這個片語指屬於鳥臀目的恐龍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"made on the basis of","meaning":"根據……作出","examples":[{"en":"This division is made on the basis of pelvic anatomy.","zh":"這個劃分是根據骨盆解剖結構作出的。"},{"en":"Made on the basis of means decided according to a particular reason, feature or evidence.","zh":"Made on the basis of 指根據某個原因、特徵或證據作出決定。"},{"en":"A teacher may group students on the basis of reading level.","zh":"老師可能根據閱讀程度把學生分組。"},{"en":"If classification is made on the basis of bones, appearance alone is not enough.","zh":"如果分類根據骨骼作出，單靠外觀就不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the evidence used for a decision.","zh":"這個片語解釋作決定所使用的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pelvic anatomy","meaning":"骨盆解剖結構","examples":[{"en":"The two dinosaur orders are separated by pelvic anatomy.","zh":"兩個恐龍目由骨盆解剖結構分開。"},{"en":"Pelvic anatomy means the structure and arrangement of the bones around the hip area.","zh":"Pelvic anatomy 指髖部周圍骨骼的結構和排列。"},{"en":"Doctors study pelvic anatomy to understand movement, childbirth and injury.","zh":"醫生研究骨盆解剖結構，以理解活動、生產和受傷。"},{"en":"In dinosaurs, pelvic anatomy is important for classification.","zh":"在恐龍身上，骨盆解剖結構對分類很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the bones of the hip region.","zh":"這個片語集中於髖部區域的骨骼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pelvic girdle","meaning":"骨盆帶","examples":[{"en":"All dinosaurs had a pelvic girdle.","zh":"所有恐龍都有骨盆帶。"},{"en":"A pelvic girdle is the bony structure around the hips that supports the legs.","zh":"Pelvic girdle 是髖部周圍支撐腿部的骨質結構。"},{"en":"In a skeleton model, the pelvic girdle connects the spine to the lower limbs.","zh":"在骨骼模型中，骨盆帶把脊柱連接到下肢。"},{"en":"A strong pelvic girdle helps support body weight during movement.","zh":"強壯骨盆帶幫助在移動時支撐體重。"},{"en":"This phrase names the hip-bone structure used in classification.","zh":"這個片語命名用於分類的髖部骨骼結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"comprising three bones","meaning":"由三塊骨組成","examples":[{"en":"Each side of the pelvic girdle comprised three bones.","zh":"骨盆帶每一側由三塊骨組成。"},{"en":"Comprising three bones means being made up of three separate bones.","zh":"Comprising three bones 指由三塊分開的骨組成。"},{"en":"A simple lunch box may comprise three parts: a lid, a base and a divider.","zh":"簡單飯盒可能由三部分組成：蓋、底和分隔格。"},{"en":"Knowing what a structure comprises helps students understand how it is built.","zh":"知道一個結構由甚麼組成，幫助學生理解它如何構成。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the components of a structure.","zh":"這個片語解釋結構的組成部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pubis, ilium and ischium","meaning":"恥骨、髂骨及坐骨","examples":[{"en":"The pelvic girdle comprised the pubis, ilium and ischium.","zh":"骨盆帶由恥骨、髂骨及坐骨組成。"},{"en":"Pubis, ilium and ischium are the three bones that make up each side of the pelvic girdle.","zh":"Pubis, ilium and ischium 是構成骨盆帶每一側的三塊骨。"},{"en":"In anatomy class, students may label the pubis, ilium and ischium on a pelvis diagram.","zh":"在解剖課中，學生可能在骨盆圖上標示恥骨、髂骨及坐骨。"},{"en":"Their position helps scientists compare different dinosaur groups.","zh":"它們的位置幫助科學家比較不同恐龍類群。"},{"en":"This phrase names three important bones in the hip structure.","zh":"這個片語命名髖部結構中的三塊重要骨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the orientation of these bones","meaning":"這些骨骼的朝向","examples":[{"en":"The orientation of these bones follows one of two patterns.","zh":"這些骨骼的朝向遵循兩種模式之一。"},{"en":"The orientation of these bones means the direction in which the bones point or are arranged.","zh":"Orientation of these bones 指這些骨骼指向或排列的方向。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain the orientation of arrows on a diagram before students read it.","zh":"老師可能在學生閱讀圖表前解釋箭嘴的朝向。"},{"en":"Bone orientation can affect classification because direction is a visible structural feature.","zh":"骨骼朝向可以影響分類，因為方向是可見的結構特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on direction and arrangement.","zh":"這個片語集中於方向和排列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"follows one of two patterns","meaning":"遵循兩種模式之一","examples":[{"en":"The orientation of the pelvic bones follows one of two patterns.","zh":"骨盆骨骼的朝向遵循兩種模式之一。"},{"en":"Follows one of two patterns means fits into either of two possible arrangements.","zh":"Follows one of two patterns 指符合兩種可能排列其中之一。"},{"en":"Students’ revision habits may follow one of two patterns: steady weekly work or last-minute study.","zh":"學生溫習習慣可能遵循兩種模式之一：穩定每週學習或臨急抱佛腳。"},{"en":"Recognising the pattern helps people sort examples more easily.","zh":"辨認模式幫助人更容易分類例子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a choice between two repeated forms.","zh":"這個片語描述兩種反覆形式之間的選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lizard-hipped dinosaurs","meaning":"蜥臀類恐龍","examples":[{"en":"Saurischian dinosaurs are lizard-hipped dinosaurs.","zh":"蜥臀目恐龍是蜥臀類恐龍。"},{"en":"Lizard-hipped dinosaurs are dinosaurs whose hip structure resembles the pattern named after lizards.","zh":"Lizard-hipped dinosaurs 是髖部結構類似以蜥蜴命名的模式的恐龍。"},{"en":"A teacher may use “lizard-hipped dinosaurs” to help students remember Saurischia.","zh":"老師可能使用「蜥臀類恐龍」幫助學生記住蜥臀目。"},{"en":"The name refers to pelvic anatomy, not to dinosaurs being actual lizards.","zh":"這個名稱指骨盆解剖結構，而不是指恐龍真的是蜥蜴。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a descriptive name for saurischian dinosaurs.","zh":"這個片語為蜥臀目恐龍提供描述性名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"points forwards","meaning":"指向前方","examples":[{"en":"In saurischian dinosaurs, the pubis points forwards.","zh":"在蜥臀目恐龍中，恥骨指向前方。"},{"en":"Points forwards means faces or extends toward the front.","zh":"Points forwards 指面向或延伸向前方。"},{"en":"In a classroom, arrows on the floor may point forwards to guide students to the exit.","zh":"在課室中，地上的箭嘴可能指向前方，引導學生往出口。"},{"en":"The direction a bone points can help scientists classify an animal.","zh":"骨骼指向的方向可以幫助科學家分類動物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes orientation toward the front.","zh":"這個片語描述朝向前方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"by contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"By contrast, the pubis points backwards in ornithischian dinosaurs.","zh":"相比之下，在鳥臀目恐龍中，恥骨指向後方。"},{"en":"By contrast introduces a clear difference from the previous point.","zh":"By contrast 用來引出與前一點的清楚差異。"},{"en":"Some students enjoy group work; by contrast, others concentrate better alone.","zh":"有些學生喜歡小組工作；相比之下，另一些學生獨自工作時更專注。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers compare two things sharply.","zh":"這個片語幫助作者鮮明比較兩件事。"},{"en":"It is useful when the second idea is noticeably different from the first.","zh":"當第二個想法明顯不同於第一個時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"bird-hipped dinosaurs","meaning":"鳥臀類恐龍","examples":[{"en":"Ornithischian dinosaurs are bird-hipped dinosaurs.","zh":"鳥臀目恐龍是鳥臀類恐龍。"},{"en":"Bird-hipped dinosaurs are dinosaurs whose hip structure resembles the pattern seen in birds.","zh":"Bird-hipped dinosaurs 是髖部結構類似鳥類所見模式的恐龍。"},{"en":"A museum guide may explain that bird-hipped dinosaurs were not necessarily ancestors of birds.","zh":"博物館導賞員可能解釋鳥臀類恐龍不一定是鳥類祖先。"},{"en":"The name helps students remember the backward-pointing pubis.","zh":"這個名稱幫助學生記住向後指的恥骨。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a descriptive name for ornithischian dinosaurs.","zh":"這個片語為鳥臀目恐龍提供描述性名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"points backwards towards","meaning":"向後指向……","examples":[{"en":"In ornithischian dinosaurs, the pubis points backwards towards the rear.","zh":"在鳥臀目恐龍中，恥骨向後指向動物後方。"},{"en":"Points backwards towards means faces or extends in the direction of the back.","zh":"Points backwards towards 指面向或延伸向背後方向。"},{"en":"A sign may point backwards towards the entrance if visitors walk past it.","zh":"如果訪客走過入口，指示牌可能向後指向入口。"},{"en":"In anatomy, direction words help describe how bones are arranged.","zh":"在解剖學中，方向詞幫助描述骨骼如何排列。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a backward orientation.","zh":"這個片語描述向後的朝向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the rear of the animal","meaning":"動物的後方","examples":[{"en":"The pubis points towards the rear of the animal.","zh":"恥骨指向動物的後方。"},{"en":"The rear of the animal means the back end of its body.","zh":"The rear of the animal 指動物身體的後端。"},{"en":"A horse’s tail is located at the rear of the animal.","zh":"馬尾位於動物的後方。"},{"en":"Knowing the front and rear helps students understand anatomical directions.","zh":"知道前方和後方幫助學生理解解剖方向。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the back part of an animal’s body.","zh":"這個片語指出動物身體後部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"true of birds","meaning":"鳥類也是如此","examples":[{"en":"The backward-pointing pubis is also true of birds.","zh":"向後指的恥骨在鳥類也是如此。"},{"en":"True of birds means also correct when applied to birds.","zh":"True of birds 指該說法應用於鳥類時也正確。"},{"en":"Warm-bloodedness is true of birds as well as mammals.","zh":"溫血這一點在鳥類以及哺乳類動物中也是如此。"},{"en":"If a feature is true of two groups, scientists may compare their structures more closely.","zh":"如果某特徵在兩個群體中都成立，科學家可能更仔細比較牠們的結構。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a statement applies to another group too.","zh":"這個片語顯示某說法也適用於另一群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"of the two orders","meaning":"在兩個目之中","examples":[{"en":"Of the two orders of dinosaurs, Saurischia was the larger.","zh":"在恐龍兩個目之中，蜥臀目較大。"},{"en":"Of the two orders means when comparing the two dinosaur groups just mentioned.","zh":"Of the two orders 指在比較剛提到的兩個恐龍類群時。"},{"en":"Of the two exam sections, the writing part took longer for most students.","zh":"在兩個考試部分之中，寫作部分對大多數學生來說較花時間。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows comparison to two specific items.","zh":"這個片語把比較限制在兩個特定項目。"},{"en":"It helps readers understand which group is being compared.","zh":"它幫助讀者理解正在比較哪個群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the first to evolve","meaning":"最先演化出現的","examples":[{"en":"Saurischia was the first dinosaur order to evolve.","zh":"蜥臀目是最先演化出現的恐龍目。"},{"en":"The first to evolve means the earliest group to develop in evolutionary history.","zh":"The first to evolve 指在演化歷史中最早發展出來的群體。"},{"en":"In a technology timeline, early mobile phones were the first to evolve before smartphones.","zh":"在科技時間線中，早期手提電話比智能手機更早演化出現。"},{"en":"Knowing which group evolved first helps scientists build a historical sequence.","zh":"知道哪個群體最先演化出現，幫助科學家建立歷史次序。"},{"en":"This phrase describes earliest appearance in development.","zh":"這個片語描述發展中最早出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"divided into two suborders","meaning":"被分為兩個亞目","examples":[{"en":"Saurischia is divided into two suborders.","zh":"蜥臀目被分為兩個亞目。"},{"en":"Divided into two suborders means separated into two smaller groups under the same order.","zh":"Divided into two suborders 指在同一目之下分成兩個較小類群。"},{"en":"A school club may be divided into two teams for different projects.","zh":"學校學會可能被分為兩隊，負責不同項目。"},{"en":"Subdivision helps people study smaller groups more carefully.","zh":"細分有助人們更仔細研究較小群體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a more detailed classification within a larger group.","zh":"這個片語描述較大類群內更詳細的分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Theropoda","meaning":"獸腳亞目","examples":[{"en":"Theropoda is a suborder of Saurischia.","zh":"獸腳亞目是蜥臀目的一個亞目。"},{"en":"Theropoda is the dinosaur suborder that includes many bipedal predatory dinosaurs.","zh":"Theropoda 是包括許多雙足捕食性恐龍的恐龍亞目。"},{"en":"Tyrannosaurus rex is commonly placed within Theropoda.","zh":"暴龍通常被放在獸腳亞目之內。"},{"en":"This group is important because many famous meat-eating dinosaurs belonged to it.","zh":"這個類群重要，因為許多著名肉食恐龍屬於其中。"},{"en":"This term names one branch of saurischian dinosaurs.","zh":"這個術語命名蜥臀目恐龍的一個分支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"theropods","meaning":"獸腳類","examples":[{"en":"The theropods were bipedal, predatory carnivores.","zh":"獸腳類是雙足、捕食性的肉食動物。"},{"en":"Theropods were dinosaurs that usually walked on two legs and often hunted other animals.","zh":"Theropods 是通常用兩腿行走且常捕獵其他動物的恐龍。"},{"en":"A child may recognise theropods from museum displays of Tyrannosaurus rex.","zh":"孩子可能從暴龍的博物館展示中認出獸腳類。"},{"en":"Their body structure helped them run, balance and attack prey.","zh":"牠們的身體結構幫助牠們奔跑、平衡和攻擊獵物。"},{"en":"This word refers to a major group of mostly meat-eating dinosaurs.","zh":"這個詞指一個主要多為肉食的恐龍類群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Sauropodomorpha","meaning":"蜥腳形亞目","examples":[{"en":"Sauropodomorpha is another suborder of Saurischia.","zh":"蜥腳形亞目是蜥臀目的另一個亞目。"},{"en":"Sauropodomorpha is the dinosaur suborder that includes sauropods and related long-necked forms.","zh":"Sauropodomorpha 是包括蜥腳類及相關長頸形式的恐龍亞目。"},{"en":"A museum may introduce Sauropodomorpha when explaining giant dinosaurs such as Diplodocus.","zh":"博物館解釋梁龍等巨型恐龍時，可能介紹蜥腳形亞目。"},{"en":"This group includes dinosaurs with very different body sizes and diets across time.","zh":"這個類群包括在不同時期有不同體型和飲食的恐龍。"},{"en":"This term names another branch of saurischian dinosaurs.","zh":"這個術語命名蜥臀目恐龍的另一個分支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sauropodomorphs","meaning":"蜥腳形類","examples":[{"en":"The sauropodomorphs included both bipedal and quadrupedal dinosaurs.","zh":"蜥腳形類包括雙足和四足恐龍。"},{"en":"Sauropodomorphs were dinosaurs in a group that later included many large long-necked herbivores.","zh":"Sauropodomorphs 是一個後來包括許多大型長頸草食恐龍的類群。"},{"en":"Diplodocus is a well-known sauropodomorph often shown in museums.","zh":"梁龍是著名的蜥腳形類，常出現在博物館。"},{"en":"Some early members differed from later giants in diet and walking style.","zh":"一些早期成員在飲食和行走方式上不同於後來的巨型恐龍。"},{"en":"This word refers to a varied dinosaur group within Saurischia.","zh":"這個詞指蜥臀目中一個種類多樣的恐龍類群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"beast feet","meaning":"獸足","examples":[{"en":"Theropods are described as “beast feet”.","zh":"獸腳類被描述為「獸足」。"},{"en":"Beast feet is a literal descriptive meaning associated with the name Theropoda.","zh":"Beast feet 是與 Theropoda 這個名稱相關的字面描述意思。"},{"en":"A teacher may mention “beast feet” to help students remember the Greek-based name.","zh":"老師可能提到「獸足」，幫助學生記住這個源自希臘語的名稱。"},{"en":"Literal name meanings can be memorable, even if they are not full scientific definitions.","zh":"字面名稱意思可以令人容易記住，即使它們不是完整科學定義。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a simple translation-style clue to a technical term.","zh":"這個片語為技術術語提供簡單翻譯式線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"predatory carnivores","meaning":"捕食性肉食動物","examples":[{"en":"Theropods were predatory carnivores.","zh":"獸腳類是捕食性肉食動物。"},{"en":"Predatory carnivores are meat-eating animals that hunt other animals for food.","zh":"Predatory carnivores 是捕獵其他動物作食物的肉食動物。"},{"en":"Lions are predatory carnivores because they catch prey rather than eat plants.","zh":"獅子是捕食性肉食動物，因為牠們捕捉獵物而不是吃植物。"},{"en":"Sharp teeth, strong legs or good eyesight can help predatory carnivores hunt.","zh":"尖牙、強壯腿部或良好視力可以幫助捕食性肉食動物狩獵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both diet and hunting behaviour.","zh":"這個片語同時描述飲食和捕獵行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ranged in size from … to …","meaning":"大小由……到……不等","examples":[{"en":"Theropods ranged in size from the mighty Tyrannosaurus rex to the tiny Compsognathus.","zh":"獸腳類大小由強大的暴龍到細小的美頜龍不等。"},{"en":"Ranged in size from … to … means varied between a small example and a large example.","zh":"Ranged in size from … to … 指大小在小例子與大例子之間變化。"},{"en":"The school bags ranged in size from tiny lunch bags to large hiking backpacks.","zh":"書包大小由細小午餐袋到大型行山背囊不等。"},{"en":"This pattern helps show the full variety within a group.","zh":"這個句式幫助顯示一個群體內的完整多樣性。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing the smallest and largest examples.","zh":"當比較最小和最大例子時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the mighty Tyrannosaurus rex","meaning":"強大的暴龍","examples":[{"en":"The mighty Tyrannosaurus rex was about 12 m long.","zh":"強大的暴龍大約長十二米。"},{"en":"The mighty Tyrannosaurus rex means the powerful and famous dinosaur species Tyrannosaurus rex.","zh":"Mighty Tyrannosaurus rex 指強大且著名的暴龍物種。"},{"en":"Children often recognise the mighty Tyrannosaurus rex from films and museum skeletons.","zh":"孩子常從電影和博物館骨架認出強大的暴龍。"},{"en":"Its large size and predatory features make it a strong example of theropods.","zh":"牠的大體型和捕食特徵使牠成為獸腳類的有力例子。"},{"en":"This phrase gives Tyrannosaurus rex a dramatic but clear description.","zh":"這個片語給暴龍一個戲劇化但清楚的描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"weighing an estimated","meaning":"估計重達……","examples":[{"en":"Tyrannosaurus rex weighed an estimated 6.4 tonnes.","zh":"暴龍估計重達六點四噸。"},{"en":"Weighing an estimated amount means having an approximate weight rather than an exact known weight.","zh":"Weighing an estimated amount 指重量是大約估算，而不是確切已知。"},{"en":"A rescue dog may be described as weighing an estimated 20 kilograms before a vet checks it.","zh":"在獸醫檢查前，一隻救援犬可能被描述為估計重達二十公斤。"},{"en":"Fossil animals often require estimated weights because no living specimen can be measured.","zh":"化石動物常需要估算重量，因為沒有活體標本可量度。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the number is a careful approximation.","zh":"這個片語表示數字是仔細估算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a mere","meaning":"僅僅；只有","examples":[{"en":"Compsognathus was a mere 1.4 m long.","zh":"美頜龍僅僅長一點四米。"},{"en":"A mere means only, used to stress that something is small or limited.","zh":"A mere 指僅僅或只有，用來強調某事很小或有限。"},{"en":"A student finished the quiz in a mere five minutes.","zh":"學生只用了五分鐘便完成小測。"},{"en":"This phrase often creates contrast with something much larger or more impressive.","zh":"這個片語常與更大或更令人印象深刻的東西形成對比。"},{"en":"It makes the smallness of the number feel more noticeable.","zh":"它令數字之小更加明顯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fully grown","meaning":"完全成年","examples":[{"en":"Compsognathus weighed about 3 kg when fully grown.","zh":"美頜龍完全成年時重約三公斤。"},{"en":"Fully grown means having reached adult size.","zh":"Fully grown 指已達成年體型。"},{"en":"A puppy becomes much heavier when it is fully grown.","zh":"小狗完全成年後會重很多。"},{"en":"Knowing whether an animal is fully grown helps people compare sizes fairly.","zh":"知道動物是否完全成年，幫助人公平比較大小。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the mature stage of growth.","zh":"這個片語描述成長的成熟階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lizard feet forms","meaning":"蜥腳形類","examples":[{"en":"Sauropodomorphs are described as “lizard feet forms”.","zh":"蜥腳形類被描述為「蜥腳形類」。"},{"en":"Lizard feet forms is a literal descriptive meaning associated with the name Sauropodomorpha.","zh":"Lizard feet forms 是與 Sauropodomorpha 這個名稱相關的字面描述意思。"},{"en":"A teacher may use “lizard feet forms” as a memory aid for this difficult term.","zh":"老師可能用「蜥腳形類」作為記住這個困難術語的提示。"},{"en":"Such literal meanings help students remember technical names more easily.","zh":"這類字面意思幫助學生更容易記住技術名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a translation-style explanation of a scientific name.","zh":"這個片語為科學名稱提供翻譯式解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"both bipedal and quadrupedal","meaning":"既有雙足亦有四足的","examples":[{"en":"Sauropodomorphs included both bipedal and quadrupedal dinosaurs.","zh":"蜥腳形類既包括雙足恐龍，也包括四足恐龍。"},{"en":"Both bipedal and quadrupedal means including animals that walk on two legs and animals that walk on four.","zh":"Both bipedal and quadrupedal 指同時包括用兩腿行走和用四腿行走的動物。"},{"en":"A display may compare both bipedal and quadrupedal dinosaurs to show different movement styles.","zh":"展覽可能比較雙足和四足恐龍，以展示不同移動方式。"},{"en":"A group with both forms is more varied than a group with only one walking style.","zh":"同時有兩種形式的群體，比只有一種行走方式的群體更多樣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two contrasting types are included.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩種相反類型都被包括。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"carnivorous or omnivorous","meaning":"肉食或雜食的","examples":[{"en":"Some sauropodomorphs were carnivorous or omnivorous.","zh":"一些蜥腳形類是肉食或雜食的。"},{"en":"Carnivorous or omnivorous means meat-eating or eating both plants and animals.","zh":"Carnivorous or omnivorous 指吃肉，或同時吃植物和動物。"},{"en":"A cat is carnivorous, while a person is often omnivorous.","zh":"貓是肉食性的，而人通常是雜食性的。"},{"en":"Diet words help scientists understand what an animal’s teeth and jaws were used for.","zh":"飲食詞彙幫助科學家理解動物牙齒和顎部用來做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two types of feeding behaviour.","zh":"這個片語比較兩種進食行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"later species","meaning":"較後期的物種","examples":[{"en":"Later species of sauropodomorphs were typically herbivorous.","zh":"較後期的蜥腳形類物種通常是草食性的。"},{"en":"Later species means species that evolved or appeared after earlier ones.","zh":"Later species 指在較早物種之後演化或出現的物種。"},{"en":"Later phone models usually have better cameras than earlier models.","zh":"較後期的手機型號通常比早期型號有更好的相機。"},{"en":"Comparing earlier and later species helps scientists study change over time.","zh":"比較早期和較後期物種，幫助科學家研究隨時間發生的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase places species in a historical sequence.","zh":"這個片語把物種放入歷史次序中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"typically herbivorous","meaning":"通常是草食性的","examples":[{"en":"Later sauropodomorph species were typically herbivorous.","zh":"較後期的蜥腳形類物種通常是草食性的。"},{"en":"Typically herbivorous means usually feeding on plants.","zh":"Typically herbivorous 指通常以植物為食。"},{"en":"Cows are typically herbivorous because they mainly eat grass and other plants.","zh":"牛通常是草食性的，因為牠們主要吃草和其他植物。"},{"en":"If an animal is herbivorous, its teeth and digestive system may suit plant food.","zh":"如果動物是草食性的，其牙齒和消化系統可能適合植物食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the usual diet of a group.","zh":"這個片語描述一個群體的通常飲食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"largest and best-known","meaning":"最大且最知名的","examples":[{"en":"Sauropodomorphs included some of the largest and best-known dinosaurs.","zh":"蜥腳形類包括一些最大且最知名的恐龍。"},{"en":"Largest and best-known means biggest in size and most familiar to many people.","zh":"Largest and best-known 指體型最大，且為許多人最熟悉。"},{"en":"Some of the largest and best-known animals today include elephants and whales.","zh":"今日一些最大且最知名的動物包括大象和鯨魚。"},{"en":"Famous size can make an animal easier for students to remember.","zh":"著名的體型可以令學生更容易記住某動物。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights both physical scale and public familiarity.","zh":"這個片語同時突出身體規模和公眾熟悉度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"such as Diplodocus","meaning":"例如梁龍","examples":[{"en":"They included huge dinosaurs such as Diplodocus.","zh":"牠們包括例如梁龍這樣的巨型恐龍。"},{"en":"Such as Diplodocus introduces Diplodocus as an example of the group being discussed.","zh":"Such as Diplodocus 把梁龍作為正在討論群體的一個例子。"},{"en":"Museums often display long-necked dinosaurs such as Diplodocus to impress visitors.","zh":"博物館常展示例如梁龍這樣的長頸恐龍，以令訪客印象深刻。"},{"en":"“Such as” helps give a concrete example after a general statement.","zh":"“Such as” 在一般陳述後提供具體例子。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a broad category easier to picture.","zh":"這個片語令廣泛類別更容易想像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a huge quadruped","meaning":"巨型四足動物","examples":[{"en":"Diplodocus was a huge quadruped.","zh":"梁龍是一種巨型四足動物。"},{"en":"A huge quadruped is a very large animal that walks on four legs.","zh":"Huge quadruped 是用四隻腳行走的非常大型動物。"},{"en":"An elephant is a huge quadruped in the modern world.","zh":"大象是現代世界中的巨型四足動物。"},{"en":"A huge quadruped needs strong limbs to support its body weight.","zh":"巨型四足動物需要強壯四肢支撐體重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both size and walking style.","zh":"這個片語同時描述體型和行走方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"an elephant-like body","meaning":"像大象的身體","examples":[{"en":"Diplodocus had an elephant-like body.","zh":"梁龍有像大象的身體。"},{"en":"An elephant-like body means a large, heavy body supported by strong legs.","zh":"Elephant-like body 指由強壯四肢支撐的大而重身體。"},{"en":"A child may imagine an elephant-like body as wide, solid and powerful.","zh":"孩子可能把像大象的身體想像成寬闊、結實而有力。"},{"en":"Comparing an extinct animal with a living one helps readers picture its shape.","zh":"把已滅絕動物與現存動物比較，幫助讀者想像其形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a familiar animal to explain body form.","zh":"這個片語使用熟悉動物來解釋身體形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a long, thin tail and neck","meaning":"又長又幼的尾巴和頸","examples":[{"en":"Diplodocus had a long, thin tail and neck.","zh":"梁龍有又長又幼的尾巴和頸。"},{"en":"A long, thin tail and neck means the tail and neck were extended and narrow.","zh":"Long, thin tail and neck 指尾巴和頸部延長且狹幼。"},{"en":"A drawing of Diplodocus often shows a long, thin tail and neck stretching from a large body.","zh":"梁龍圖畫常顯示又長又幼的尾巴和頸從巨大身體伸出。"},{"en":"Such features can affect balance, feeding height and overall body length.","zh":"這些特徵可以影響平衡、進食高度和整體身長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two striking body parts.","zh":"這個片語描述兩個顯眼身體部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a total length of","meaning":"總長度達……","examples":[{"en":"The tail and neck gave Diplodocus a total length of 27 m.","zh":"尾巴和頸使梁龍總長度達二十七米。"},{"en":"A total length of means the full distance from one end of the body or object to the other.","zh":"Total length of 指由身體或物件一端到另一端的完整距離。"},{"en":"A bus may have a total length of twelve metres.","zh":"巴士總長度可能達十二米。"},{"en":"Including the tail and neck can greatly increase an animal’s total length.","zh":"把尾巴和頸包括在內，可以大幅增加動物總長度。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a complete measurement.","zh":"這個片語給出完整量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a tiny head","meaning":"細小的頭部","examples":[{"en":"Diplodocus had a tiny head.","zh":"梁龍有細小的頭部。"},{"en":"A tiny head means a very small head compared with the rest of the body.","zh":"Tiny head 指與身體其他部分相比非常小的頭。"},{"en":"In a cartoon, a huge body with a tiny head may look funny because the proportions are unusual.","zh":"在卡通中，巨大身體配上細小頭部可能顯得有趣，因為比例不尋常。"},{"en":"A tiny head on a giant animal can make the body shape seem even more striking.","zh":"巨型動物上的細小頭部可以令身體形狀更加突出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes small size in strong contrast to the body.","zh":"這個片語描述與身體形成強烈對比的小尺寸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"herbivores","meaning":"草食動物","examples":[{"en":"Ornithischian dinosaurs were herbivores.","zh":"鳥臀目恐龍是草食動物。"},{"en":"Herbivores are animals that eat plants.","zh":"Herbivores 是吃植物的動物。"},{"en":"Horses, cows and rabbits are common herbivores.","zh":"馬、牛和兔子都是常見草食動物。"},{"en":"Herbivores often need teeth or digestive systems suited to leaves, grass or other plant food.","zh":"草食動物通常需要適合樹葉、草或其他植物食物的牙齒或消化系統。"},{"en":"This word describes animals by what they eat.","zh":"這個詞按飲食描述動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"now usually divided into","meaning":"現時通常被分為……","examples":[{"en":"Ornithischian dinosaurs are now usually divided into three suborders.","zh":"鳥臀目恐龍現時通常被分為三個亞目。"},{"en":"Now usually divided into means commonly classified in this way today.","zh":"Now usually divided into 指今天通常以這種方式分類。"},{"en":"A school subject may now usually be divided into reading, writing, speaking and listening.","zh":"學校科目現在通常可分為閱讀、寫作、口語和聆聽。"},{"en":"Classification can change as experts study more evidence.","zh":"分類可以隨專家研究更多證據而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the current common way of organising a group.","zh":"這個片語顯示目前常見的組織方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Ornithopoda","meaning":"鳥腳亞目","examples":[{"en":"Ornithopoda is one suborder of ornithischian dinosaurs.","zh":"鳥腳亞目是鳥臀目恐龍的一個亞目。"},{"en":"Ornithopoda is a dinosaur suborder whose name is linked with “bird feet”.","zh":"Ornithopoda 是名稱與「鳥足」有關的恐龍亞目。"},{"en":"Iguanodon is often discussed as an example within Ornithopoda.","zh":"禽龍常被作為鳥腳亞目中的例子討論。"},{"en":"This group helps show variety among herbivorous dinosaurs.","zh":"這個類群幫助顯示草食恐龍之間的多樣性。"},{"en":"This term names one branch of ornithischian dinosaurs.","zh":"這個術語命名鳥臀目恐龍的一個分支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Thyreophora","meaning":"裝甲亞目","examples":[{"en":"Thyreophora is another suborder of ornithischian dinosaurs.","zh":"裝甲亞目是鳥臀目恐龍的另一個亞目。"},{"en":"Thyreophora is the group of armoured dinosaurs with protective body structures.","zh":"Thyreophora 是具有保護性身體結構的裝甲恐龍類群。"},{"en":"Stegosaurus is commonly introduced as a thyreophoran dinosaur.","zh":"劍龍通常被介紹為裝甲亞目恐龍。"},{"en":"Armour features helped these dinosaurs defend themselves from predators.","zh":"裝甲特徵幫助這些恐龍防禦捕食者。"},{"en":"This term names an armoured branch of ornithischian dinosaurs.","zh":"這個術語命名鳥臀目恐龍中的裝甲分支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Marginocephalia","meaning":"頭緣亞目","examples":[{"en":"Marginocephalia is a suborder of ornithischian dinosaurs.","zh":"頭緣亞目是鳥臀目恐龍的一個亞目。"},{"en":"Marginocephalia is a dinosaur group known for special structures around the back or edge of the skull.","zh":"Marginocephalia 是以頭骨後方或邊緣特殊結構著稱的恐龍類群。"},{"en":"Triceratops is a famous dinosaur placed within Marginocephalia.","zh":"三角龍是被歸入頭緣亞目的著名恐龍。"},{"en":"Skull features help scientists recognise this group.","zh":"頭骨特徵幫助科學家辨認這個類群。"},{"en":"This term names a head-feature-based branch of ornithischian dinosaurs.","zh":"這個術語命名鳥臀目恐龍中以頭部特徵為基礎的分支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"ornithopods","meaning":"鳥腳類","examples":[{"en":"Ornithopods could walk or run on their long hind legs.","zh":"鳥腳類可以用長後腿行走或奔跑。"},{"en":"Ornithopods were bird-footed herbivorous dinosaurs within Ornithopoda.","zh":"Ornithopods 是鳥腳亞目中鳥足型的草食恐龍。"},{"en":"Iguanodon is a common example used when teaching ornithopods.","zh":"教授鳥腳類時，禽龍是常見例子。"},{"en":"Their long hind legs helped them move effectively.","zh":"牠們的長後腿幫助牠們有效移動。"},{"en":"This word refers to a group of plant-eating dinosaurs with strong hind limbs.","zh":"這個詞指一群具有強壯後肢的食植物恐龍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"bird feet","meaning":"鳥足","examples":[{"en":"Ornithopods are described as “bird feet”.","zh":"鳥腳類被描述為「鳥足」。"},{"en":"Bird feet is a literal meaning used to help explain the name Ornithopoda.","zh":"Bird feet 是用來解釋 Ornithopoda 名稱的字面意思。"},{"en":"A teacher may use “bird feet” as a memory clue for students learning dinosaur groups.","zh":"老師可能用「鳥足」作為學生學習恐龍類群時的記憶提示。"},{"en":"Literal meanings can make technical terms easier to remember.","zh":"字面意思可以令技術術語更容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a simple descriptive clue to a scientific name.","zh":"這個片語為科學名稱提供簡單描述線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"walk or run on","meaning":"用……行走或奔跑","examples":[{"en":"Ornithopods could walk or run on their long hind legs.","zh":"鳥腳類可以用長後腿行走或奔跑。"},{"en":"Walk or run on means use particular body parts to move by walking or running.","zh":"Walk or run on 指使用特定身體部位行走或奔跑。"},{"en":"Humans walk or run on two legs, while dogs use four.","zh":"人類用兩條腿行走或奔跑，而狗使用四條腿。"},{"en":"The body parts used for movement affect speed, balance and posture.","zh":"用於移動的身體部位影響速度、平衡和姿勢。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what supports movement.","zh":"這個片語解釋甚麼支撐移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"long hind legs","meaning":"長後腿","examples":[{"en":"Ornithopods used their long hind legs to walk or run.","zh":"鳥腳類用長後腿行走或奔跑。"},{"en":"Long hind legs are back legs that are extended and relatively long.","zh":"Long hind legs 是較長並延伸的後腿。"},{"en":"Kangaroos use long hind legs to jump powerfully.","zh":"袋鼠使用長後腿有力跳躍。"},{"en":"Long hind legs can help an animal move quickly or balance its body.","zh":"長後腿可以幫助動物快速移動或平衡身體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rear limbs important for movement.","zh":"這個片語描述對移動重要的後方肢體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"balancing their body by","meaning":"透過……平衡身體","examples":[{"en":"Ornithopods balanced their body by holding their tails stiffly behind them.","zh":"鳥腳類透過把尾巴僵直地放在身後來平衡身體。"},{"en":"Balancing their body by means keeping the body steady through a particular action.","zh":"Balancing their body by 指透過某個特定動作保持身體穩定。"},{"en":"A cyclist balances their body by leaning slightly when turning.","zh":"單車手轉彎時透過稍微傾斜來平衡身體。"},{"en":"If an animal has a long tail, it may use that tail to keep steady while moving.","zh":"如果動物有長尾巴，牠可能用尾巴在移動時保持穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how balance is achieved.","zh":"這個片語解釋如何達到平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"holding their tails stiffly","meaning":"僵直地保持尾巴","examples":[{"en":"They held their tails stiffly off the ground behind them.","zh":"牠們把尾巴僵直地保持在身後離地。"},{"en":"Holding their tails stiffly means keeping the tail straight and firm instead of relaxed.","zh":"Holding their tails stiffly 指把尾巴保持筆直和固定，而不是放鬆。"},{"en":"A cat may hold its tail stiffly when it is alert or tense.","zh":"貓警覺或緊張時，可能僵直地保持尾巴。"},{"en":"A stiff tail can help balance the rest of the body.","zh":"僵直尾巴可以幫助平衡身體其他部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a firm tail position.","zh":"這個片語描述固定的尾巴姿勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"off the ground","meaning":"離開地面","examples":[{"en":"Their tails were held off the ground.","zh":"牠們的尾巴保持離開地面。"},{"en":"Off the ground means not touching the ground.","zh":"Off the ground 指沒有接觸地面。"},{"en":"A child lifts a wet schoolbag off the ground to keep it clean.","zh":"孩子把濕書包提離地面，以保持清潔。"},{"en":"Keeping a body part off the ground can reduce dragging and help movement.","zh":"讓身體部位離開地面可以減少拖行並幫助移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical separation from the floor or earth.","zh":"這個片語描述與地板或土地分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"up to 9 m long","meaning":"長達九米","examples":[{"en":"Iguanodon was up to 9 m long.","zh":"禽龍長達九米。"},{"en":"Up to 9 m long means reaching a maximum length of about nine metres.","zh":"Up to 9 m long 指最長可達大約九米。"},{"en":"A bus may be up to twelve metres long depending on the model.","zh":"巴士可長達十二米，視乎型號而定。"},{"en":"“Up to” gives a maximum, so not every individual must reach that size.","zh":"“Up to” 給出最高值，所以不是每個個體都必須達到該大小。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses the largest possible or recorded length.","zh":"這個片語表達可能或記錄中的最大長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"thyreophorans","meaning":"裝甲類恐龍","examples":[{"en":"Thyreophorans are also known as armoured dinosaurs.","zh":"裝甲類恐龍也被稱為裝甲恐龍。"},{"en":"Thyreophorans were dinosaurs with protective body armour such as plates or spikes.","zh":"Thyreophorans 是具有骨板或骨刺等保護性身體裝甲的恐龍。"},{"en":"Stegosaurus is a well-known example of a thyreophoran.","zh":"劍龍是裝甲類恐龍的著名例子。"},{"en":"Their armour helped protect them from attacks.","zh":"牠們的裝甲幫助保護牠們免受攻擊。"},{"en":"This word refers to the armoured dinosaur group.","zh":"這個詞指裝甲恐龍類群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"shield bearers","meaning":"盾牌承載者","examples":[{"en":"Thyreophorans are described as “shield bearers”.","zh":"裝甲類恐龍被描述為「盾牌承載者」。"},{"en":"Shield bearers is a descriptive meaning that suggests animals carrying protective armour.","zh":"Shield bearers 是暗示動物帶有保護裝甲的描述性意思。"},{"en":"A teacher may use “shield bearers” to help students remember Thyreophora.","zh":"老師可能使用「盾牌承載者」幫助學生記住 Thyreophora。"},{"en":"The phrase fits because these dinosaurs had protective plates, spikes or armour.","zh":"這個片語合適，因為這些恐龍有保護性骨板、骨刺或裝甲。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a vivid clue to the group’s defensive features.","zh":"這個片語為該類群的防禦特徵提供生動線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"armoured dinosaurs","meaning":"裝甲恐龍","examples":[{"en":"Thyreophorans are also known as armoured dinosaurs.","zh":"裝甲類恐龍也被稱為裝甲恐龍。"},{"en":"Armoured dinosaurs were dinosaurs with protective bony structures on their bodies.","zh":"Armoured dinosaurs 是身體上有保護性骨質結構的恐龍。"},{"en":"A museum model of Stegosaurus shows why some dinosaurs are called armoured dinosaurs.","zh":"劍龍的博物館模型顯示為何一些恐龍被稱為裝甲恐龍。"},{"en":"Body armour could help protect them from predators.","zh":"身體裝甲可以幫助牠們抵禦捕食者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dinosaurs by their defensive features.","zh":"這個片語按防禦特徵描述恐龍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"rows of protective bony spikes","meaning":"一排排保護性的骨刺","examples":[{"en":"Armoured dinosaurs had rows of protective bony spikes.","zh":"裝甲恐龍有一排排保護性的骨刺。"},{"en":"Rows of protective bony spikes are lines of hard bone points used for defence.","zh":"Rows of protective bony spikes 是一列列用於防禦的堅硬骨質尖刺。"},{"en":"A drawing of an armoured dinosaur may show spikes arranged along the back.","zh":"裝甲恐龍圖畫可能顯示沿背部排列的骨刺。"},{"en":"Protective spikes can make an animal harder for predators to attack.","zh":"保護性骨刺可以令動物較難被捕食者攻擊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated defensive structures on the body.","zh":"這個片語描述身體上重複排列的防禦結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"studs or plates","meaning":"骨突或骨板","examples":[{"en":"Their backs and tails had bony spikes, studs or plates.","zh":"牠們背部和尾部有骨刺、骨突或骨板。"},{"en":"Studs or plates are raised hard structures on the body, used here as forms of armour.","zh":"Studs or plates 是身體上凸起的堅硬結構，在這裏作為裝甲形式。"},{"en":"A leather jacket may have metal studs, while an armoured vehicle may have metal plates.","zh":"皮褸可能有金屬釘飾，而裝甲車可能有金屬板。"},{"en":"In dinosaurs, bony plates could provide protection or display.","zh":"在恐龍身上，骨板可以提供保護或展示功能。"},{"en":"This phrase names possible hard protective structures.","zh":"這個片語命名可能的堅硬保護結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"along their backs and tails","meaning":"沿着背部和尾部","examples":[{"en":"The protective plates ran along their backs and tails.","zh":"保護性骨板沿着牠們的背部和尾部延伸。"},{"en":"Along their backs and tails means extending over the back and tail areas.","zh":"Along their backs and tails 指延伸覆蓋背部和尾部區域。"},{"en":"A stripe may run along a cat’s back and tail.","zh":"一條條紋可能沿着貓的背部和尾巴延伸。"},{"en":"Location phrases help readers picture where body features were placed.","zh":"位置片語幫助讀者想像身體特徵放在哪裏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the path of features across an animal’s body.","zh":"這個片語描述特徵在動物身體上的路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"they included Stegosaurus","meaning":"當中包括劍龍","examples":[{"en":"The armoured dinosaurs included Stegosaurus.","zh":"裝甲恐龍當中包括劍龍。"},{"en":"They included Stegosaurus means Stegosaurus was one example within that group.","zh":"They included Stegosaurus 指劍龍是該群體中的一個例子。"},{"en":"A list of school sports may include basketball, football and swimming.","zh":"學校運動列表可能包括籃球、足球和游泳。"},{"en":"Giving a familiar example helps students understand a larger category.","zh":"提供熟悉例子幫助學生理解較大類別。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a member of a group.","zh":"這個片語引入某群體中的成員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"marginocephalians","meaning":"頭緣類恐龍","examples":[{"en":"Marginocephalians were bipedal or quadrupedal ornithischians.","zh":"頭緣類恐龍是雙足或四足的鳥臀目恐龍。"},{"en":"Marginocephalians were ornithischian dinosaurs known for special structures at the back of the skull.","zh":"Marginocephalians 是以頭骨後方特殊結構著稱的鳥臀目恐龍。"},{"en":"Triceratops is a famous marginocephalian with a large frill and horns.","zh":"三角龍是著名的頭緣類恐龍，有大型頸盾和角。"},{"en":"Their skull features help distinguish them from other herbivorous dinosaurs.","zh":"牠們的頭骨特徵幫助把牠們與其他草食恐龍區分開。"},{"en":"This word refers to a head-feature-based dinosaur group.","zh":"這個詞指以頭部特徵為基礎的恐龍類群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"margined heads","meaning":"邊緣頭部","examples":[{"en":"Marginocephalians are described as “margined heads”.","zh":"頭緣類恐龍被描述為「邊緣頭部」。"},{"en":"Margined heads is a descriptive meaning referring to structures around the edge or back of the skull.","zh":"Margined heads 是指頭骨邊緣或後方結構的描述性意思。"},{"en":"A teacher may use “margined heads” to help students remember Marginocephalia.","zh":"老師可能使用「邊緣頭部」幫助學生記住 Marginocephalia。"},{"en":"The phrase fits because these dinosaurs had frills or shelves at the back of the skull.","zh":"這個片語合適，因為這些恐龍頭骨後方有頸盾或骨質平台。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a memory clue based on head shape.","zh":"這個片語根據頭部形狀提供記憶提示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a deep bony frill","meaning":"深而堅硬的骨質頸盾","examples":[{"en":"Marginocephalians had a deep bony frill at the back of the skull.","zh":"頭緣類恐龍在頭骨後方有深而堅硬的骨質頸盾。"},{"en":"A deep bony frill is a large solid bone structure extending from the back of the head.","zh":"Deep bony frill 是由頭部後方伸出的巨大堅硬骨質結構。"},{"en":"Triceratops is often drawn with a deep bony frill behind its horns.","zh":"三角龍常被畫成角後方有深而堅硬的骨質頸盾。"},{"en":"Such a frill could affect protection, display or recognition.","zh":"這種頸盾可能影響保護、展示或辨認。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a striking skull feature.","zh":"這個片語描述顯眼的頭骨特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a narrow shelf","meaning":"狹窄的骨質平台","examples":[{"en":"Some marginocephalians had a narrow shelf at the back of the skull.","zh":"一些頭緣類恐龍在頭骨後方有狹窄的骨質平台。"},{"en":"A narrow shelf is a thin projecting structure, here made of bone.","zh":"Narrow shelf 是薄而向外伸出的結構，在這裏由骨頭構成。"},{"en":"A small shelf on a wall projects outward but does not take up much space.","zh":"牆上的小架向外伸出，但不佔很多空間。"},{"en":"In anatomy, a shelf-like bone can help identify a group.","zh":"在解剖學中，像平台的骨頭可以幫助辨認一個群體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a thin extension at the skull’s back.","zh":"這個片語描述頭骨後方的薄延伸部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"at the back of the skull","meaning":"位於頭骨後方","examples":[{"en":"The frill or shelf was at the back of the skull.","zh":"頸盾或骨質平台位於頭骨後方。"},{"en":"At the back of the skull means located on the rear part of the head bone.","zh":"At the back of the skull 指位於頭骨的後部。"},{"en":"A doctor may examine the back of the skull after a person falls backwards.","zh":"人向後跌倒後，醫生可能檢查頭骨後方。"},{"en":"Location details help scientists describe exactly where a feature appears.","zh":"位置細節幫助科學家準確描述特徵出現在哪裏。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific skull position.","zh":"這個片語指出特定頭骨位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a rhinoceros-like dinosaur","meaning":"像犀牛的恐龍","examples":[{"en":"Triceratops was a rhinoceros-like dinosaur.","zh":"三角龍是一種像犀牛的恐龍。"},{"en":"A rhinoceros-like dinosaur is a dinosaur whose body or head features remind people of a rhinoceros.","zh":"Rhinoceros-like dinosaur 是身體或頭部特徵令人想起犀牛的恐龍。"},{"en":"Children may compare Triceratops with a rhinoceros because both have large horns.","zh":"孩子可能把三角龍與犀牛比較，因為兩者都有大角。"},{"en":"Comparing extinct animals with living animals helps readers imagine their appearance.","zh":"把已滅絕動物與現代動物比較，幫助讀者想像其外觀。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a familiar modern animal to describe an extinct one.","zh":"這個片語用熟悉的現代動物描述已滅絕動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"bearing a prominent neck frill","meaning":"長有明顯的頸盾","examples":[{"en":"Triceratops bore a prominent neck frill and three large horns.","zh":"三角龍長有明顯的頸盾和三隻大角。"},{"en":"Bearing a prominent neck frill means having or carrying a large noticeable bony frill around the neck area.","zh":"Bearing a prominent neck frill 指長有或帶有頸部區域大型而明顯的骨質頸盾。"},{"en":"A parade costume bearing a bright feather collar would be easy to notice.","zh":"長有鮮艷羽毛領圈的巡遊服裝會很容易被注意到。"},{"en":"A prominent feature can help people recognise an animal quickly.","zh":"明顯特徵可以幫助人快速辨認動物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visible physical feature an animal carries.","zh":"這個片語描述動物帶有的可見身體特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"three large horns","meaning":"三隻大角","examples":[{"en":"Triceratops had three large horns.","zh":"三角龍有三隻大角。"},{"en":"Three large horns means three big pointed structures growing from the head.","zh":"Three large horns 指三個從頭部長出的巨大尖形結構。"},{"en":"A child may recognise Triceratops quickly because of its three large horns.","zh":"孩子可能因三角龍的三隻大角而快速認出牠。"},{"en":"Horns can be used for defence, display or competition in many animals.","zh":"在許多動物中，角可用於防禦、展示或競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one of Triceratops’s most famous features.","zh":"這個片語描述三角龍最著名特徵之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"choose the most suitable heading","meaning":"選出最合適的標題","examples":[{"en":"Students must choose the most suitable heading for each paragraph.","zh":"學生必須為每段選出最合適的標題。"},{"en":"To choose the most suitable heading means to select the title that best summarises the paragraph’s main idea.","zh":"To choose the most suitable heading 指選出最能概括段落主旨的標題。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should read the whole paragraph before choosing the heading.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先閱讀整段，再選標題。"},{"en":"A heading that matches only one detail may still be wrong.","zh":"只符合一個細節的標題仍可能是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in paragraph-matching tasks.","zh":"這個片語是段落配對題中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The list of headings contains more options than paragraphs.","zh":"標題列表包含比段落更多的選項。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a set of possible paragraph titles in a reading task.","zh":"List of headings 是閱讀任務中一組可能的段落標題。"},{"en":"Students should compare each heading with the main idea, not just repeated words.","zh":"學生應把每個標題與主旨比較，而不只是看重複字。"},{"en":"Extra headings make the question harder because not all choices are used.","zh":"額外標題令題目更難，因為不是所有選項都會使用。"},{"en":"This phrase names the answer choices in a heading-matching exercise.","zh":"這個片語命名標題配對練習中的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"write the appropriate numbers","meaning":"寫上合適的編號","examples":[{"en":"Students write the appropriate numbers on their answer sheet.","zh":"學生在答題紙上寫上合適的編號。"},{"en":"To write the appropriate numbers means to record the correct numbered options.","zh":"To write the appropriate numbers 指記下正確的編號選項。"},{"en":"In a matching task, students may write the appropriate numbers beside paragraph letters.","zh":"在配對題中，學生可能在段落字母旁寫上合適的編號。"},{"en":"Copying the wrong number can lose marks even if the student understood the passage.","zh":"即使學生理解文章，抄錯編號也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how answers should be entered.","zh":"這個片語描述答案應如何填寫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"more headings than paragraphs","meaning":"標題比段落多","examples":[{"en":"There are more headings than paragraphs in this question type.","zh":"在這種題型中，標題比段落多。"},{"en":"More headings than paragraphs means the number of title options is greater than the number of paragraphs.","zh":"More headings than paragraphs 指標題選項數量多於段落數量。"},{"en":"In a reading exercise, extra headings test whether students can reject tempting wrong answers.","zh":"在閱讀練習中，額外標題測試學生能否排除誘人的錯誤答案。"},{"en":"If there are more headings than paragraphs, some headings must remain unused.","zh":"如果標題比段落多，有些標題必然不會被使用。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why students should not force every option into the answer.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何學生不應把每個選項都硬套入答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"will not use all of them","meaning":"不會用上全部","examples":[{"en":"Students will not use all of the headings.","zh":"學生不會用上全部標題。"},{"en":"Will not use all of them means some options must be left unused.","zh":"Will not use all of them 指有些選項必須留下不用。"},{"en":"In a word bank exercise, students may not use all of the words provided.","zh":"在詞庫練習中，學生可能不會用上提供的全部詞語。"},{"en":"This instruction prevents students from forcing extra answers into places where they do not fit.","zh":"這個指示防止學生把額外答案硬塞到不合適位置。"},{"en":"This phrase warns learners to choose carefully, not completely.","zh":"這個片語提醒學習者要仔細選擇，而不是全部使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"complete the sentences below","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the sentences below with words from the passage.","zh":"學生用文章中的字詞完成以下句子。"},{"en":"To complete the sentences below means to fill in missing parts of the sentences that follow.","zh":"To complete the sentences below 指填補接下來句子的缺漏部分。"},{"en":"Students should read the grammar around each gap before completing the sentence.","zh":"學生在完成句子前，應閱讀每個空格周圍的文法。"},{"en":"A correct answer must fit both meaning and grammar.","zh":"正確答案必須同時符合意思和文法。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in gap-fill reading tasks.","zh":"這個片語是填充式閱讀題中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than three words.","zh":"每個答案應包含不多於三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must use three words or fewer.","zh":"No more than three words 指答案必須使用三個字或更少。"},{"en":"If the answer is “a tiny head”, it is allowed because it has three words.","zh":"如果答案是 “a tiny head”，它有三個字，所以可以接受。"},{"en":"Writing four words may lose marks even when the meaning is right.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫四個字也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit for answers.","zh":"這個片語為答案設定嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"from the passage","meaning":"來自文章","examples":[{"en":"The missing words must come from the passage.","zh":"缺漏字詞必須來自文章。"},{"en":"From the passage means the answer must be taken directly from the reading text.","zh":"From the passage 指答案必須直接取自閱讀文章。"},{"en":"Students should not invent a synonym if the instruction says the words must come from the passage.","zh":"如果指示說字詞必須來自文章，學生不應自創同義詞。"},{"en":"This rule tests careful locating and copying, not outside knowledge.","zh":"這條規則測試仔細定位和抄寫，而不是外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase tells students where the answer wording must come from.","zh":"這個片語告訴學生答案措辭必須來自哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"blank space","meaning":"空格","examples":[{"en":"Each blank space must be filled with a short phrase.","zh":"每個空格必須填入一個短語。"},{"en":"A blank space is an empty gap in a sentence where an answer should be written.","zh":"Blank space 是句子中應填寫答案的空白位置。"},{"en":"In a worksheet, a blank space may appear after “The answer is ____”.","zh":"在工作紙中，空格可能出現在 “The answer is ____” 之後。"},{"en":"Students should check the words before and after the blank space before answering.","zh":"學生回答前應檢查空格前後的字詞。"},{"en":"This phrase names the empty part of a completion question.","zh":"這個片語命名完成題中的空白部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose one phrase from","meaning":"從……中選擇一個短語","examples":[{"en":"Students choose one phrase from the list of features.","zh":"學生從特徵列表中選擇一個短語。"},{"en":"To choose one phrase from a list means to select a single suitable expression from several options.","zh":"To choose one phrase from a list 指從幾個選項中選出一個合適表達。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to choose one phrase from a vocabulary box to complete each sentence.","zh":"老師可能要求學生從詞彙框中選擇一個短語完成每句。"},{"en":"Choosing one phrase carefully prevents using an answer that fits grammar but not meaning.","zh":"仔細選擇短語，可以避免使用文法合適但意思不合的答案。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an instruction for selection from provided options.","zh":"這個片語給出從所提供選項中選擇的指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"list of features","meaning":"特徵列表","examples":[{"en":"The list of features contains more phrases than needed.","zh":"特徵列表包含比所需更多的短語。"},{"en":"A list of features is a set of characteristics that students can choose from.","zh":"List of features 是一組學生可以選擇的特徵。"},{"en":"In a dinosaur task, the list of features may include diet, movement and body structure.","zh":"在恐龍題目中，特徵列表可能包括飲食、移動方式和身體結構。"},{"en":"Extra features make students decide which detail truly matches each group.","zh":"額外特徵令學生決定哪個細節真正配對每個群體。"},{"en":"This phrase names the options in a feature-matching task.","zh":"這個片語命名特徵配對題中的選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"match with","meaning":"與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match each dinosaur group with one feature.","zh":"學生將每個恐龍類群與一個特徵配對。"},{"en":"To match with means to connect one item to the correct related item.","zh":"To match with 指把一項與正確相關項目連接。"},{"en":"In a vocabulary game, students match each word with its definition.","zh":"在詞彙遊戲中，學生把每個詞與其定義配對。"},{"en":"Matching requires meaning, not just similar-looking words.","zh":"配對需要理解意思，而不只是看相似字眼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes linking two items correctly.","zh":"這個片語描述正確連接兩項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"completed sentences","meaning":"完成後的句子","examples":[{"en":"The completed sentences should accurately summarise the writer’s points.","zh":"完成後的句子應準確概括作者的要點。"},{"en":"Completed sentences are sentences that have all missing parts filled in.","zh":"Completed sentences 是所有缺漏部分都已填上的句子。"},{"en":"Students should reread completed sentences to check that they sound natural and logical.","zh":"學生應重讀完成後的句子，檢查它們是否自然和合邏輯。"},{"en":"If a completed sentence changes the passage meaning, the answer is wrong.","zh":"如果完成後的句子改變文章意思，答案就是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to sentences after the blanks have been filled.","zh":"這個片語指空格已填好的句子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"an accurate summary of","meaning":"對……的準確概括","examples":[{"en":"The completed sentences should be an accurate summary of the passage.","zh":"完成後的句子應是對文章的準確概括。"},{"en":"An accurate summary of something gives the main ideas correctly without distortion.","zh":"Accurate summary of something 指正確呈現主要意思而不扭曲。"},{"en":"A student’s summary of a chapter is accurate if it includes the key points and leaves out personal guesses.","zh":"如果學生對章節的概括包括重點並排除個人猜測，它就是準確的。"},{"en":"If a summary adds unsupported information, it is no longer accurate.","zh":"如果摘要加入沒有支持的資料，它就不再準確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a faithful condensed version of a text.","zh":"這個片語描述忠實的濃縮版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"points made by the writer","meaning":"作者提出的要點","examples":[{"en":"The phrases should match the points made by the writer.","zh":"這些短語應配合作者提出的要點。"},{"en":"Points made by the writer are the ideas, claims or details the writer actually states.","zh":"Points made by the writer 是作者實際陳述的想法、主張或細節。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students must follow the points made by the writer, not their own opinions.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生必須跟隨作者提出的要點，而不是自己的意見。"},{"en":"If an answer contradicts the writer’s point, it cannot be correct.","zh":"如果答案與作者觀點相反，它不可能正確。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds students to stay close to the passage.","zh":"這個片語提醒學生緊貼文章。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"may use each phrase once only","meaning":"每個短語只可使用一次","examples":[{"en":"Students may use each phrase once only.","zh":"學生每個短語只可使用一次。"},{"en":"May use each phrase once only means each option can be chosen one time and no more.","zh":"May use each phrase once only 指每個選項只能選一次，不能更多。"},{"en":"In a matching exercise, using one phrase twice may leave another sentence without a correct answer.","zh":"在配對題中，把一個短語用兩次可能令另一句沒有正確答案。"},{"en":"This rule forces students to compare all options before deciding.","zh":"這條規則迫使學生在決定前比較所有選項。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a restriction on answer choices.","zh":"這個片語給出答案選擇的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"differed from","meaning":"與……不同","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs differed from lizards in their body structure.","zh":"恐龍在身體結構上與蜥蜴不同。"},{"en":"Differed from means were not the same as another thing.","zh":"Differed from 指與另一事物不相同。"},{"en":"Online lessons differed from classroom lessons because students needed more self-discipline.","zh":"網上課與面授課不同，因為學生需要更多自律。"},{"en":"If two animals differ in body structure, scientists may classify them separately.","zh":"如果兩種動物在身體結構上不同，科學家可能把牠們分開分類。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear difference between two things.","zh":"這個片語描述兩件事之間的清楚差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the former","meaning":"前者","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs and lizards are compared, and the former had a different gait.","zh":"恐龍和蜥蜴被比較，而前者有不同步態。"},{"en":"The former means the first of two people or things just mentioned.","zh":"The former 指剛提到的兩個人或事物中的第一個。"},{"en":"Students may choose online classes or face-to-face classes; the former needs stronger time management.","zh":"學生可能選擇網上課或面授課；前者需要更強時間管理。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating the first item in a pair.","zh":"這個片語避免重複一對事物中的第一項。"},{"en":"It should only be used when two items have already been clearly named.","zh":"只有當兩項已清楚命名時，才應使用它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"unlike theropods","meaning":"與獸腳類不同","examples":[{"en":"Unlike theropods, some sauropodomorphs did not always eat meat.","zh":"與獸腳類不同，一些蜥腳形類並非總是吃肉。"},{"en":"Unlike theropods means different from theropods in the point being discussed.","zh":"Unlike theropods 指在正在討論的方面不同於獸腳類。"},{"en":"Unlike younger children, older students may understand abstract examples more easily.","zh":"與年幼孩子不同，年長學生可能較容易理解抽象例子。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces contrast by comparing one group with another.","zh":"這個片語透過把一個群體與另一群體比較來引出對比。"},{"en":"It helps readers notice what makes the second group different.","zh":"它幫助讀者注意第二個群體有何不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"did not always eat meat","meaning":"並非總是吃肉","examples":[{"en":"Some sauropodomorphs did not always eat meat.","zh":"一些蜥腳形類並非總是吃肉。"},{"en":"Did not always eat meat means meat was not the only or regular diet for all members.","zh":"Did not always eat meat 指肉不是所有成員唯一或固定的飲食。"},{"en":"A family does not always eat meat if they sometimes cook vegetable meals.","zh":"如果家庭有時煮蔬菜餐，他們並非總是吃肉。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects the assumption that a group is entirely carnivorous.","zh":"這個片語糾正某群體全都是肉食性的假設。"},{"en":"It shows that diet can vary inside the same broad group.","zh":"它顯示同一大類群中的飲食可以有變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"used their tails to balance","meaning":"用尾巴保持平衡","examples":[{"en":"Some dinosaurs used their tails to balance while walking or running.","zh":"一些恐龍在行走或奔跑時用尾巴保持平衡。"},{"en":"Used their tails to balance means kept the body steady by positioning the tail.","zh":"Used their tails to balance 指透過擺放尾巴使身體保持穩定。"},{"en":"A tightrope walker uses a pole to balance in a similar way.","zh":"走鋼線的人以類似方式使用長桿保持平衡。"},{"en":"A tail can act like a counterweight when an animal moves.","zh":"當動物移動時，尾巴可以像平衡重物一樣發揮作用。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the practical function of the tail.","zh":"這個片語解釋尾巴的實際功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"rather than two","meaning":"而不是兩隻","examples":[{"en":"Some dinosaurs walked on four legs rather than two.","zh":"一些恐龍用四隻腳行走，而不是兩隻。"},{"en":"Rather than two means instead of two, used to contrast one number or option with another.","zh":"Rather than two 指而不是兩個，用來把一個數量或選項與另一個作對比。"},{"en":"A family may buy one large table rather than two small ones to save space.","zh":"家庭可能買一張大桌，而不是兩張小桌，以節省空間。"},{"en":"In animal movement, four legs rather than two can change balance and body support.","zh":"在動物移動中，用四隻腳而不是兩隻腳可以改變平衡和身體支撐。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly marks a contrast between alternatives.","zh":"這個片語清楚標示選項之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 27 - What is a dinosaur?.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 28":[{"front":"not every scientist who","meaning":"並非每一位……都會","examples":[{"en":"It is not every scientist who writes books for people who cannot read.","zh":"並非每一位科學家都會為不識字的人寫書。"},{"en":"Not every scientist who means this action is unusual among scientists.","zh":"not every scientist who 指這種行動在科學家之中並不常見。"},{"en":"It is not every teacher who can explain grammar clearly to beginners.","zh":"並非每一位老師都能向初學者清楚解釋文法。"},{"en":"If not every expert can speak simply, someone who can do so is especially valuable.","zh":"如果並非每位專家都能說得簡單，能做到的人就特別有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights that a person is unusual or exceptional within a group.","zh":"這個片語突出某人在一個群體中不尋常或出眾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"write books for people who cannot read","meaning":"為不識字的人寫書","examples":[{"en":"Patricia Shanley writes books for people who cannot read.","zh":"Patricia Shanley 為不識字的人寫書。"},{"en":"Write books for people who cannot read means create books using pictures, stories, and simple language for people with limited literacy.","zh":"write books for people who cannot read 指用圖畫、故事和簡單語言，為讀寫能力有限的人製作書。"},{"en":"A health worker may write leaflets for people who cannot read well by using drawings and symbols.","zh":"醫護人員可能透過圖畫和符號，為不太會閱讀的人寫小冊子。"},{"en":"If information is written for people who cannot read, knowledge becomes more accessible.","zh":"如果資訊是為不識字的人而寫，知識就變得更容易取得。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses communication beyond ordinary text.","zh":"這個片語強調超越普通文字的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as dog-eared as possible","meaning":"盡可能被翻得殘舊","examples":[{"en":"She wanted her books to look as dog-eared as possible.","zh":"她希望自己的書看起來盡可能被翻得殘舊。"},{"en":"As dog-eared as possible means used so often that the pages become worn, folded, or damaged at the corners.","zh":"as dog-eared as possible 指因頻繁使用而令書頁邊角磨損、摺皺或變舊。"},{"en":"A useful school dictionary may become as dog-eared as possible after years of daily use.","zh":"一本有用的學校字典經過多年日常使用後，可能被翻得非常殘舊。"},{"en":"If a community book becomes dog-eared, it probably means many people have handled and learned from it.","zh":"如果一本社區用書變得書頁摺皺，大概表示很多人曾經翻閱並從中學習。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests heavy use rather than neglect.","zh":"這個片語暗示大量使用，而不是被忽視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dog-eared","meaning":"書頁角摺皺的；翻殘的","examples":[{"en":"The book became dog-eared after being used by many local people.","zh":"這本書被許多本地人使用後，變得書頁角摺皺、被翻殘。"},{"en":"Dog-eared describes a book or paper with corners folded, worn, or damaged from frequent use.","zh":"dog-eared 形容書或紙張因經常使用而角位摺起、磨損或破舊。"},{"en":"A student’s favourite revision booklet may become dog-eared before the exam.","zh":"學生最常用的溫習小冊子在考試前可能變得翻殘。"},{"en":"When a manual becomes dog-eared, it often shows that people actually need it.","zh":"當手冊被翻得殘舊，通常顯示人們確實需要它。"},{"en":"The word usually suggests a well-used object, not a brand-new one.","zh":"這個詞通常暗示物件被經常使用，而不是嶄新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ethnobotanist","meaning":"民族植物學家","examples":[{"en":"Patricia Shanley is an ethnobotanist who studies the relationship between people and plants.","zh":"Patricia Shanley 是一位研究人與植物關係的民族植物學家。"},{"en":"An ethnobotanist studies how different communities use, understand, and depend on plants.","zh":"ethnobotanist 指研究不同社群如何使用、理解和依賴植物的人。"},{"en":"An ethnobotanist may ask villagers which leaves are used for medicine, food, or building materials.","zh":"民族植物學家可能詢問村民哪些葉子用於藥物、食物或建材。"},{"en":"If traditional plant knowledge is disappearing, ethnobotanists can help record it before it is lost.","zh":"如果傳統植物知識正在消失，民族植物學家可以幫助在其失傳前記錄下來。"},{"en":"The word connects botany with culture and local knowledge.","zh":"這個詞把植物學與文化及當地知識連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"give something back","meaning":"回饋","examples":[{"en":"Shanley wanted to give something back to the people who had helped her research.","zh":"Shanley 想回饋那些曾幫助她研究的人。"},{"en":"Give something back means return help, value, or benefit to people who have supported you.","zh":"give something back 指把幫助、價值或好處回饋給曾支持你的人。"},{"en":"A former student may give something back by mentoring younger students at their old school.","zh":"舊生可以透過指導母校的年輕學生來作出回饋。"},{"en":"If researchers take knowledge from a community, giving something back can make the relationship fairer.","zh":"如果研究人員從社群取得知識，回饋可以令關係較公平。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses gratitude and practical return.","zh":"這個片語強調感激和實際回報。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the poorest people of","meaning":"……中最貧困的人","examples":[{"en":"She worked with some of the poorest people of the Amazon.","zh":"她與亞馬遜地區中一些最貧困的人合作。"},{"en":"The poorest people of a place are those with the least money, resources, or security in that area.","zh":"the poorest people of a place 指該地金錢、資源或保障最少的人。"},{"en":"A charity may focus on the poorest people of a city because they have the fewest choices.","zh":"慈善機構可能集中幫助城市中最貧困的人，因為他們選擇最少。"},{"en":"If the poorest people lack access to information, they may be more easily exploited.","zh":"如果最貧困的人缺乏資訊，他們可能更容易被剝削。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the most economically vulnerable group in a place.","zh":"這個片語指出某地經濟上最脆弱的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"allow someone to study","meaning":"容許某人研究","examples":[{"en":"The local people allowed her to study their land and its ecology.","zh":"本地人容許她研究他們的土地及其生態。"},{"en":"Allow someone to study means give someone permission to examine or research something.","zh":"allow someone to study 指給某人許可去檢視或研究某事物。"},{"en":"A school may allow researchers to study how students use online learning tools.","zh":"學校可能容許研究人員研究學生如何使用網上學習工具。"},{"en":"If a community allows a scientist to study its land, trust is very important.","zh":"如果社群容許科學家研究其土地，信任就非常重要。"},{"en":"The phrase shows permission for research or investigation.","zh":"這個片語顯示對研究或調查的許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"land and its ecology","meaning":"土地及其生態","examples":[{"en":"Her research focused on the land and its ecology.","zh":"她的研究集中於土地及其生態。"},{"en":"Land and its ecology means the physical area and the living relationships among plants, animals, soil, water, and people there.","zh":"land and its ecology 指某片土地，以及當中的植物、動物、土壤、水和人之間的生命關係。"},{"en":"Farmers understand their land and its ecology when they know which crops grow best in each season.","zh":"當農民知道每個季節最適合種甚麼作物，就是理解自己的土地及其生態。"},{"en":"If logging damages the land and its ecology, local food and wildlife may decline.","zh":"如果伐木破壞土地及其生態，本地食物和野生動物可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase links a place with the natural systems that sustain it.","zh":"這個片語把一個地方與支撐它的自然系統連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"research findings","meaning":"研究結果","examples":[{"en":"She turned her research findings into a picture book.","zh":"她把研究結果變成一本圖畫書。"},{"en":"Research findings are the results, facts, or conclusions discovered through a study.","zh":"research findings 指透過研究發現的結果、事實或結論。"},{"en":"A school may use research findings to decide whether smaller classes improve learning.","zh":"學校可能使用研究結果來決定小班教學是否改善學習。"},{"en":"If research findings are shared clearly, people outside universities can benefit from them.","zh":"如果研究結果被清楚分享，大學以外的人也能受益。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what research has discovered.","zh":"這個片語指研究所發現的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"turn something into","meaning":"把……變成","examples":[{"en":"Shanley turned her research findings into a picture book.","zh":"Shanley 把她的研究結果變成一本圖畫書。"},{"en":"Turn something into means change it from one form or purpose into another.","zh":"turn something into 指把某事物由一種形式或用途改變成另一種。"},{"en":"A teacher can turn a difficult grammar rule into a simple classroom game.","zh":"老師可以把困難文法規則變成簡單課堂遊戲。"},{"en":"If researchers turn data into pictures, people with limited reading skills may understand it more easily.","zh":"如果研究人員把數據變成圖片，讀寫能力有限的人可能更容易理解。"},{"en":"The phrase shows transformation.","zh":"這個片語顯示轉化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"picture book","meaning":"圖畫書","examples":[{"en":"The picture book helped people with limited reading skills understand the research.","zh":"這本圖畫書幫助讀寫能力有限的人理解研究。"},{"en":"A picture book is a book that uses images as a major way to explain a story or information.","zh":"picture book 指以圖像作為解釋故事或資訊的重要方式的書。"},{"en":"Children often learn new words from picture books because images give meaning clues.","zh":"孩子常透過圖畫書學新詞，因為圖像提供意思線索。"},{"en":"If adults cannot read easily, a picture book can still teach practical information.","zh":"如果成年人不容易閱讀，圖畫書仍可以教授實用資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a visually guided book, not necessarily only a children’s book.","zh":"這個片語指以視覺引導的書，不一定只是兒童書。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"get a good return on","meaning":"從……取得良好回報","examples":[{"en":"The book explains how people can get a good return on their trees.","zh":"這本書解釋人們如何從自己的樹木取得良好回報。"},{"en":"Get a good return on something means gain worthwhile money, benefit, or value from it.","zh":"get a good return on something 指從某事物獲得值得的金錢、好處或價值。"},{"en":"A family may get a good return on education if better skills lead to better jobs.","zh":"如果更好技能帶來更好工作，家庭可能從教育取得良好回報。"},{"en":"If villagers keep fruit trees and sell fruit for years, they may get a better return than from one timber sale.","zh":"如果村民保留果樹並多年售賣水果，可能比一次木材銷售取得更好回報。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an asset with the benefit it produces.","zh":"這個片語把資產與它產生的好處連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"succumb to the lure of","meaning":"抵受不住……的誘惑","examples":[{"en":"The book helps people avoid succumbing to the lure of quick money from logging companies.","zh":"這本書幫助人們避免抵受不住伐木公司快錢的誘惑。"},{"en":"Succumb to the lure of something means give in to an attractive temptation, often despite later harm.","zh":"succumb to the lure of something 指屈服於吸引人的誘惑，往往即使日後有害。"},{"en":"A student may succumb to the lure of social media instead of revising for an exam.","zh":"學生可能抵受不住社交媒體的誘惑，而不是溫習考試。"},{"en":"If poor farmers succumb to the lure of quick cash, they may lose long-term forest resources.","zh":"如果貧困農民抵受不住快錢誘惑，可能失去長期森林資源。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that something attractive may be dangerous.","zh":"這個片語提醒人們，吸引人的東西可能危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a quick buck","meaning":"快錢","examples":[{"en":"Some logging companies offered a quick buck for valuable trees.","zh":"有些伐木公司為珍貴樹木提供快錢。"},{"en":"A quick buck means money earned quickly and easily, often without thinking about long-term effects.","zh":"quick buck 指快速而容易賺到的錢，通常沒有考慮長遠影響。"},{"en":"A shop may sell poor-quality products for a quick buck and lose customer trust later.","zh":"商店可能為了快錢售賣劣質產品，之後失去顧客信任。"},{"en":"If villagers accept a quick buck for trees, they may lose fruit, game, and future income.","zh":"如果村民為了快錢出售樹木，可能失去水果、野味和未來收入。"},{"en":"The phrase often sounds informal and slightly critical.","zh":"這個片語通常帶口語和略帶批評意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"logging company","meaning":"伐木公司","examples":[{"en":"A logging company may offer villagers money for their trees.","zh":"伐木公司可能向村民出錢購買他們的樹木。"},{"en":"A logging company is a business that cuts down trees and sells timber.","zh":"logging company 指砍伐樹木並出售木材的企業。"},{"en":"A logging company may build roads into a forest so workers can remove large trees.","zh":"伐木公司可能在森林中修路，讓工人移走大樹。"},{"en":"If a logging company pays too little for valuable trees, local people may lose wealth without realising it.","zh":"如果伐木公司以過低價購買珍貴樹木，本地人可能在不知情下失去財富。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a business involved in timber extraction.","zh":"這個片語指參與木材開採的企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"prove a big success","meaning":"證明大受歡迎；取得很大成功","examples":[{"en":"The fruit book has proved a big success.","zh":"這本水果書證明大受歡迎。"},{"en":"Prove a big success means turn out to be very successful after being tried or used.","zh":"prove a big success 指經過嘗試或使用後證明非常成功。"},{"en":"A school reading club may prove a big success if many students keep attending.","zh":"如果很多學生持續參加，學校讀書會可能證明大受歡迎。"},{"en":"If a book is useful to local people and requested by politicians, it has clearly proved successful.","zh":"如果一本書對本地人有用，並獲政客要求再版，它顯然取得很大成功。"},{"en":"The phrase judges success after results appear.","zh":"這個片語是在結果出現後判斷成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be better known as","meaning":"更廣為人知的名稱是","examples":[{"en":"The book is better known simply as the fruit book.","zh":"這本書更廣為人知的名稱只是「水果書」。"},{"en":"Be better known as means be more commonly recognised by another name.","zh":"be better known as 指更常被另一個名稱認識。"},{"en":"A teacher named Mr Chan may be better known as Coach Chan if he trains the school team.","zh":"如果陳老師訓練校隊，他可能更廣為人知的名稱是 Chan 教練。"},{"en":"If a formal title is too long, people may use a shorter name that becomes better known.","zh":"如果正式名稱太長，人們可能使用一個較短名稱，而那名稱變得更廣為人知。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the name people usually use.","zh":"這個片語引出人們通常使用的名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"second edition","meaning":"第二版","examples":[{"en":"The second edition was produced at the request of politicians.","zh":"第二版是應政客要求製作的。"},{"en":"A second edition is a later version of a book that is printed or published again, often with changes or new demand.","zh":"second edition 指一本書後來再次印刷或出版的版本，通常因修訂或新需求而出現。"},{"en":"A textbook may have a second edition when the syllabus changes.","zh":"當課程大綱改變，教科書可能推出第二版。"},{"en":"If many people ask for a book, a second edition may be produced to meet demand.","zh":"如果很多人要求一本書，第二版可能被製作以滿足需求。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a new published version after the first one.","zh":"這個片語指第一版之後的新出版版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at the request of","meaning":"應……要求","examples":[{"en":"The second edition was produced at the request of politicians in western Amazonia.","zh":"第二版是應亞馬遜西部地區政客要求製作的。"},{"en":"At the request of means because someone asked for it formally or clearly.","zh":"at the request of 指因某人正式或清楚要求而做。"},{"en":"A school may hold an extra parent meeting at the request of worried families.","zh":"學校可能應憂心家庭要求，舉行額外家長會。"},{"en":"If a book is reprinted at the request of officials, it shows the book has practical value.","zh":"如果一本書應官員要求再版，顯示它有實用價值。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who asked for an action.","zh":"這個片語指出誰要求某行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"western Amazonia","meaning":"亞馬遜西部地區","examples":[{"en":"Politicians in western Amazonia requested the second edition of the book.","zh":"亞馬遜西部地區的政客要求該書第二版。"},{"en":"Western Amazonia refers to the western part of the Amazon region in South America.","zh":"western Amazonia 指南美洲亞馬遜地區的西部。"},{"en":"A researcher working in western Amazonia may study forests, rivers, and local communities.","zh":"在亞馬遜西部地區工作的研究員，可能研究森林、河流和本地社群。"},{"en":"If politicians in a remote forest region request a book, the information may matter for local policy.","zh":"如果偏遠森林地區的政客要求一本書，該資訊可能對本地政策很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a geographical area within the Amazon.","zh":"這個片語指出亞馬遜內的一個地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a blend of","meaning":"……的結合","examples":[{"en":"The book contains a blend of hard science and local knowledge.","zh":"這本書包含嚴謹科學知識和當地知識的結合。"},{"en":"A blend of means a mixture or combination of different things.","zh":"blend of 指不同事物的混合或結合。"},{"en":"A good lesson may use a blend of explanation, examples, and student practice.","zh":"好課堂可能使用解釋、例子和學生練習的結合。"},{"en":"If research blends science with local knowledge, the result may be both accurate and useful.","zh":"如果研究把科學與當地知識結合，結果可能既準確又實用。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses combination rather than separation.","zh":"這個片語強調結合，而不是分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hard science","meaning":"嚴謹科學知識","examples":[{"en":"The fruit book combines hard science with local knowledge.","zh":"這本水果書把嚴謹科學知識與當地知識結合。"},{"en":"Hard science means rigorous scientific knowledge based on data, measurement, and careful methods.","zh":"hard science 指以數據、量度和嚴謹方法為基礎的可靠科學知識。"},{"en":"A public health guide may combine hard science with simple pictures so ordinary people can use it.","zh":"公共健康指南可能把嚴謹科學知識與簡單圖片結合，讓普通人使用。"},{"en":"If hard science is explained badly, people outside universities may not benefit from it.","zh":"如果嚴謹科學知識解釋得差，大學以外的人可能無法受益。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses reliable scientific evidence.","zh":"這個片語強調可靠的科學證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"local knowledge","meaning":"當地知識","examples":[{"en":"The book values local knowledge about forest plants.","zh":"這本書重視關於森林植物的當地知識。"},{"en":"Local knowledge is practical understanding held by people who live in a particular place.","zh":"local knowledge 指生活在某地的人所掌握的實用理解。"},{"en":"Fishermen may have local knowledge about tides, storms, and safe routes.","zh":"漁民可能有關於潮汐、風暴和安全路線的當地知識。"},{"en":"If scientists ignore local knowledge, they may miss details that communities have learned over generations.","zh":"如果科學家忽視當地知識，可能錯過社群經過幾代人學到的細節。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to knowledge rooted in lived experience.","zh":"這個片語指扎根於生活經驗的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the use and trade of","meaning":"……的使用與買賣","examples":[{"en":"The book explains the use and trade of native forest species.","zh":"這本書解釋原生森林物種的使用與買賣。"},{"en":"The use and trade of something means how it is used and how it is bought or sold.","zh":"use and trade of something 指某物如何被使用，以及如何被買賣。"},{"en":"A guide may explain the use and trade of medicinal herbs in local markets.","zh":"指南可能解釋藥草在本地市場中的使用與買賣。"},{"en":"If people understand both use and trade, they can judge whether selling a resource is wise.","zh":"如果人們理解使用與買賣兩方面，就能判斷出售某資源是否明智。"},{"en":"The phrase connects practical value with economic exchange.","zh":"這個片語把實用價值與經濟交換連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"native forest species","meaning":"原生森林物種","examples":[{"en":"The fruit book covers 35 native forest species.","zh":"這本水果書涵蓋35種原生森林物種。"},{"en":"Native forest species are plants or animals that naturally belong to a forest area.","zh":"native forest species 指自然屬於某森林地區的植物或動物。"},{"en":"A conservation worker may protect native forest species from invasive plants.","zh":"保育工作者可能保護原生森林物種免受入侵植物影響。"},{"en":"If native forest species disappear, local food, medicine, and wildlife may also be affected.","zh":"如果原生森林物種消失，本地食物、藥物和野生動物也可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to species originally found in that forest ecosystem.","zh":"這個片語指原本存在於該森林生態系統中的物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be well received","meaning":"廣受好評","examples":[{"en":"The book has been well received by many groups.","zh":"這本書受到許多群體廣泛好評。"},{"en":"Be well received means be accepted, liked, or praised by people.","zh":"be well received 指被人接受、喜歡或讚賞。"},{"en":"A new school lunch menu may be well received if students find it healthy and tasty.","zh":"如果學生覺得新學校午餐餐單健康又好味，它可能廣受好評。"},{"en":"If a research book is well received by villagers and officials, it probably meets real needs.","zh":"如果研究書受到村民和官員好評，它大概符合真實需要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a positive response from an audience.","zh":"這個片語描述受眾的正面反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"no less a dignitary than","meaning":"甚至連……這樣的要人","examples":[{"en":"No less a dignitary than Brazil’s environment minister wrote the foreword.","zh":"甚至連巴西環境部長這樣的要人也為此書撰寫前言。"},{"en":"No less a dignitary than means even such an important public figure did something.","zh":"no less a dignitary than 指甚至某位如此重要的公眾人物也做了某事。"},{"en":"No less a dignitary than the mayor opened the small community library.","zh":"甚至連市長這樣的要人也為小型社區圖書館揭幕。"},{"en":"If a high-ranking official supports a local book, the book may gain public credibility.","zh":"如果高級官員支持一本本地書，該書可能獲得公共可信度。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises the importance of the person involved.","zh":"這個片語強調參與人物的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"environment minister","meaning":"環境部長","examples":[{"en":"Brazil’s environment minister wrote the foreword to the book.","zh":"巴西環境部長為這本書撰寫前言。"},{"en":"An environment minister is a government official responsible for environmental policy and protection.","zh":"environment minister 指負責環境政策和保護的政府官員。"},{"en":"An environment minister may deal with forests, pollution, wildlife, and climate policy.","zh":"環境部長可能處理森林、污染、野生動物和氣候政策。"},{"en":"If an environment minister supports a forest book, the issue may receive political attention.","zh":"如果環境部長支持一本森林書，該議題可能獲得政治關注。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a senior official in environmental affairs.","zh":"這個片語指出環境事務中的高級官員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"write the foreword","meaning":"撰寫前言","examples":[{"en":"Marina Silva wrote the foreword to the fruit book.","zh":"Marina Silva 為這本水果書撰寫前言。"},{"en":"Write the foreword means write the introductory section at the beginning of a book, often to support or frame it.","zh":"write the foreword 指撰寫書本開首的引言部分，通常用來支持或介紹該書。"},{"en":"A respected teacher may write the foreword to a student magazine.","zh":"受尊重老師可能為學生雜誌撰寫前言。"},{"en":"If an important official writes the foreword, readers may take the book more seriously.","zh":"如果重要官員撰寫前言，讀者可能更認真看待該書。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to writing a short introduction before the main text.","zh":"這個片語指在正文前寫短引言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"there is nothing else like","meaning":"沒有其他……可與之相比","examples":[{"en":"There is nothing else like the Shanley book.","zh":"沒有其他書可與 Shanley 的書相比。"},{"en":"There is nothing else like means something is unique and no other thing is truly comparable.","zh":"there is nothing else like 指某事物獨一無二，沒有其他東西真正可比較。"},{"en":"A school may say there is nothing else like a teacher who can make every child feel safe.","zh":"學校可能說，沒有其他人可與一位能令每個孩子感到安全的老師相比。"},{"en":"If a book combines science, pictures, and local knowledge in a rare way, there may be nothing else like it.","zh":"如果一本書以罕見方式結合科學、圖片和當地知識，就可能沒有其他可與之相比。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly praises uniqueness.","zh":"這個片語強烈讚賞獨特性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"give science back to","meaning":"把科學回饋給……","examples":[{"en":"The book gives science back to the poor.","zh":"這本書把科學回饋給貧困人士。"},{"en":"Give science back to means return scientific knowledge to the people whose lives or land helped produce it.","zh":"give science back to 指把科學知識回饋給那些其生活或土地幫助產生知識的人。"},{"en":"A health project gives science back to patients when it explains research results in simple language.","zh":"健康項目用簡單語言解釋研究結果，就是把科學回饋給病人。"},{"en":"If scientists share findings with local communities, research becomes less one-sided.","zh":"如果科學家與本地社群分享研究結果，研究就不再那麼單向。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses fairness in who benefits from knowledge.","zh":"這個片語強調誰能從知識受益的公平性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a decade ago","meaning":"十年前","examples":[{"en":"Shanley’s work on the book began a decade ago.","zh":"Shanley 關於這本書的工作始於十年前。"},{"en":"A decade ago means ten years before the time being discussed.","zh":"a decade ago 指在所討論時間之前十年。"},{"en":"A school policy created a decade ago may need updating because students’ needs have changed.","zh":"十年前制定的校政可能需要更新，因為學生需要已改變。"},{"en":"If a project began a decade ago and still matters, its impact has lasted.","zh":"如果一個項目十年前開始而今天仍重要，其影響已經持續。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a time distance of ten years.","zh":"這個片語給出十年的時間距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a plea for help","meaning":"求助","examples":[{"en":"Her work began with a plea for help from a rural workers’ union.","zh":"她的工作始於一個農村工人聯盟的求助。"},{"en":"A plea for help is an urgent request for assistance.","zh":"plea for help 指迫切地請求協助。"},{"en":"A family may make a plea for help after a flood destroys their home.","zh":"水災摧毀房屋後，一個家庭可能發出求助。"},{"en":"If a community makes a plea for help, it usually means it cannot solve the problem alone.","zh":"如果社群求助，通常表示它無法獨自解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests need, urgency, and vulnerability.","zh":"這個片語暗示需要、迫切和脆弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rural workers’ union","meaning":"農村工人聯盟","examples":[{"en":"The Rural Workers’ Union of Paragominas asked Shanley for help.","zh":"Paragominas 的農村工人聯盟向 Shanley 求助。"},{"en":"A rural workers’ union is an organisation that represents workers in farming or countryside communities.","zh":"rural workers’ union 指代表農業或鄉郊社群工人的組織。"},{"en":"A rural workers’ union may help farmers negotiate wages, land rights, or safer working conditions.","zh":"農村工人聯盟可能幫助農民爭取工資、土地權利或更安全工作環境。"},{"en":"If isolated farmers face powerful companies, a union can give them a stronger collective voice.","zh":"如果與世隔絕的農民面對強大公司，工會可以給他們更強的集體聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised support for rural labourers.","zh":"這個片語指為農村勞動者提供的組織性支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"prosperity is based on","meaning":"繁榮建基於","examples":[{"en":"The town’s prosperity is based on the exploitation of timber.","zh":"該鎮的繁榮建基於木材開採。"},{"en":"Prosperity is based on means wealth or success depends mainly on something.","zh":"prosperity is based on 指財富或成功主要依賴某事物。"},{"en":"A fishing village’s prosperity may be based on clean seas and healthy fish stocks.","zh":"漁村的繁榮可能建基於清潔海洋和健康魚群。"},{"en":"If prosperity is based on one resource, the town may suffer when that resource declines.","zh":"如果繁榮建基於單一資源，當該資源減少時城鎮可能受苦。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the foundation of economic success.","zh":"這個片語解釋經濟成功的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"exploitation of timber","meaning":"木材開採","examples":[{"en":"Paragominas had become prosperous through the exploitation of timber.","zh":"Paragominas 透過木材開採變得繁榮。"},{"en":"Exploitation of timber means using forest trees for economic gain, especially by cutting and selling wood.","zh":"exploitation of timber 指為經濟利益使用森林樹木，尤其是砍伐和出售木材。"},{"en":"A region may grow rich through timber exploitation but lose wildlife habitat at the same time.","zh":"地區可能透過木材開採致富，同時失去野生動物棲息地。"},{"en":"If timber is exploited without planning, short-term income can cause long-term ecological damage.","zh":"如果木材未經規劃地開採，短期收入可能造成長期生態破壞。"},{"en":"The phrase can sound critical because it suggests heavy use of a resource.","zh":"這個片語可能帶批評意味，因為它暗示大量使用資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"knock on the doors of","meaning":"找上……門；接觸……","examples":[{"en":"The union knew that logging companies would soon be knocking on the doors of local farmers.","zh":"工會知道伐木公司很快會找上本地農民的門。"},{"en":"Knock on the doors of means approach people directly, often to ask for something or make an offer.","zh":"knock on the doors of 指直接接觸某些人，通常為了要求某事或提出交易。"},{"en":"Salespeople may knock on the doors of residents to sell internet packages.","zh":"銷售員可能找上居民的門推銷上網套餐。"},{"en":"If companies knock on farmers’ doors with quick cash offers, farmers need information before deciding.","zh":"如果公司帶着快錢提議找上農民，農民在決定前需要資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests direct contact and pressure.","zh":"這個片語暗示直接接觸和壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"peasant farmers","meaning":"農民；小農","examples":[{"en":"The caboclos were peasant farmers living near the Rio Capim.","zh":"caboclos 是住在 Rio Capim 附近的小農。"},{"en":"Peasant farmers are small-scale rural farmers who usually work with limited land, money, and technology.","zh":"peasant farmers 指通常土地、金錢和技術有限的小規模農村農民。"},{"en":"Peasant farmers may grow food mainly for their families and sell only small amounts.","zh":"小農可能主要為家庭種植食物，只出售少量產品。"},{"en":"If peasant farmers lack market information, buyers may take advantage of them.","zh":"如果小農缺乏市場資訊，買家可能佔他們便宜。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to poorer small farmers, often in rural communities.","zh":"這個片語指較貧困的小型農民，通常生活於農村社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"an Amazon tributary","meaning":"亞馬遜河支流","examples":[{"en":"The Rio Capim is an Amazon tributary in the Brazilian state of Pará.","zh":"Rio Capim 是巴西帕拉州的一條亞馬遜河支流。"},{"en":"An Amazon tributary is a smaller river or stream that flows into the Amazon River system.","zh":"Amazon tributary 指流入亞馬遜河水系的較小河流或溪流。"},{"en":"Villages along an Amazon tributary may depend on river boats for transport and trade.","zh":"位於亞馬遜河支流沿岸的村莊，可能依賴河船作交通和買賣。"},{"en":"If a tributary is polluted, communities downstream may lose fish and clean water.","zh":"如果支流受污染，下游社群可能失去魚類和清潔食水。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a river connected to the wider Amazon basin.","zh":"這個片語指出與更廣泛亞馬遜盆地相連的河流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"isolated and illiterate","meaning":"與世隔絕且不識字","examples":[{"en":"The caboclos were isolated and illiterate.","zh":"caboclos 與世隔絕且不識字。"},{"en":"Isolated and illiterate means living far from wider society and unable to read or write well.","zh":"isolated and illiterate 指遠離較大社會生活，並不能良好讀寫。"},{"en":"An isolated and illiterate community may struggle to understand contracts from outside companies.","zh":"與世隔絕且不識字的社群，可能難以理解外來公司的合約。"},{"en":"If people are isolated and illiterate, picture-based information can be much more useful than formal reports.","zh":"如果人們與世隔絕且不識字，以圖像為主的資訊會比正式報告有用得多。"},{"en":"The phrase shows both social distance and limited literacy.","zh":"這個片語同時顯示社會距離和有限讀寫能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have little concept of","meaning":"對……幾乎沒有概念","examples":[{"en":"The caboclos had little concept of the true value of their trees.","zh":"caboclos 對自己樹木的真正價值幾乎沒有概念。"},{"en":"Have little concept of means have very little understanding of something.","zh":"have little concept of 指對某事理解很少。"},{"en":"Young children may have little concept of money if they have never had to budget.","zh":"如果小孩從未需要做預算，可能對金錢幾乎沒有概念。"},{"en":"If farmers have little concept of market value, they may sell resources too cheaply.","zh":"如果農民對市場價值幾乎沒有概念，可能把資源賣得太便宜。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests limited awareness or understanding.","zh":"這個片語暗示有限意識或理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the true value of","meaning":"……的真正價值","examples":[{"en":"The farmers wanted to know the true value of their trees.","zh":"農民想知道自己樹木的真正價值。"},{"en":"The true value of something is its real worth, including hidden, long-term, or non-obvious benefits.","zh":"true value of something 指某物的真實價值，包括隱藏、長期或不明顯的好處。"},{"en":"The true value of education is not only exam results but also confidence and choices.","zh":"教育的真正價值不只是考試成績，也包括信心和選擇。"},{"en":"If people know the true value of a forest, they may not sell it for quick money.","zh":"如果人們知道森林的真正價值，就未必會為快錢出售它。"},{"en":"The phrase asks what something is really worth.","zh":"這個片語詢問某物真正值多少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"communities downstream","meaning":"下游社群","examples":[{"en":"Communities downstream had already sold large areas of forest.","zh":"下游社群已經出售大片森林。"},{"en":"Communities downstream are groups of people living farther along a river in the direction the water flows.","zh":"communities downstream 指住在河流下游方向、較遠位置的人群。"},{"en":"If a factory pollutes a river, communities downstream may suffer the effects first.","zh":"如果工廠污染河流，下游社群可能首先受影響。"},{"en":"When downstream villages sell their forest cheaply, nearby communities may fear the same pressure.","zh":"當下游村莊廉價出售森林，附近社群可能擔心同樣壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase locates communities by their position along a river.","zh":"這個片語按河流位置定位社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sell off","meaning":"出售；變賣","examples":[{"en":"Some communities had sold off large blocks of forest for very little money.","zh":"有些社群以很少錢變賣大片森林。"},{"en":"Sell off means sell something, often quickly or in large amounts, sometimes because of pressure or need.","zh":"sell off 指出售某物，通常是快速或大量出售，有時因壓力或需要。"},{"en":"A family may sell off old furniture quickly before moving to a smaller flat.","zh":"家庭搬到較小單位前，可能快速變賣舊家具。"},{"en":"If villagers sell off forest land without knowing its value, they may regret the loss later.","zh":"如果村民在不知道價值下出售森林土地，之後可能後悔損失。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests losing an asset.","zh":"這個片語常暗示失去一項資產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"large blocks of forest","meaning":"大片森林","examples":[{"en":"Communities downstream had sold off large blocks of forest for a pittance.","zh":"下游社群曾以極低價出售大片森林。"},{"en":"Large blocks of forest are big continuous areas of woodland.","zh":"large blocks of forest 指面積很大而連續的林地。"},{"en":"Large blocks of forest can provide fruit, wildlife habitat, water protection, and shade.","zh":"大片森林可以提供水果、野生動物棲息地、水源保護和遮蔭。"},{"en":"If large forest areas are sold to loggers, local families may lose many resources at once.","zh":"如果大片森林被賣給伐木商，本地家庭可能一次過失去許多資源。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the size of the forest being affected.","zh":"這個片語強調受影響森林的規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"for a pittance","meaning":"以極低價；以微薄價錢","examples":[{"en":"Some forests had been sold for a pittance.","zh":"有些森林曾以極低價出售。"},{"en":"For a pittance means for a very small amount of money, especially less than something is worth.","zh":"for a pittance 指以非常少的金錢，尤其是低於其應有價值的價錢。"},{"en":"A worker should not be expected to work long hours for a pittance.","zh":"不應期望工人長時間工作卻只得到微薄薪酬。"},{"en":"If valuable trees are sold for a pittance, the seller loses wealth while the buyer gains greatly.","zh":"如果珍貴樹木以極低價出售，賣方失去財富，買方則大大得益。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly suggests unfairly low payment.","zh":"這個片語強烈暗示報酬不公平地低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a researcher in the area","meaning":"該地區的研究員","examples":[{"en":"Shanley was a researcher in the area for the Woods Hole Research Centre.","zh":"Shanley 是 Woods Hole Research Centre 在該地區的研究員。"},{"en":"A researcher in the area is someone carrying out study in that particular place or field.","zh":"researcher in the area 指在某特定地方或領域進行研究的人。"},{"en":"A researcher in a village may interview families, measure crops, and observe daily routines.","zh":"村莊中的研究員可能訪問家庭、量度農作物並觀察日常生活。"},{"en":"If a researcher is already in the area, local people may ask them for practical help.","zh":"如果研究員已在該地區，本地人可能向他們尋求實際幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies both a role and a location.","zh":"這個片語同時指出角色和地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"harvesting wild fruits","meaning":"採集野生水果","examples":[{"en":"The union wanted to know whether harvesting wild fruits would make economic sense.","zh":"工會想知道採集野生水果是否符合經濟效益。"},{"en":"Harvesting wild fruits means collecting fruits that grow naturally in forests rather than on farms.","zh":"harvesting wild fruits 指收集自然生長於森林、而不是農場種植的水果。"},{"en":"Villagers may harvest wild fruits during certain seasons and sell them at local markets.","zh":"村民可能在特定季節採集野生水果，並在本地市場出售。"},{"en":"If wild fruits grow unpredictably, harvesting them may not provide stable income.","zh":"如果野生水果生長難以預測，採集它們可能無法提供穩定收入。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to gathering natural forest produce.","zh":"這個片語指收集天然森林產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make economic sense","meaning":"在經濟上合理；符合經濟效益","examples":[{"en":"The union asked whether harvesting wild fruits would make economic sense.","zh":"工會詢問採集野生水果是否在經濟上合理。"},{"en":"Make economic sense means be financially reasonable or worthwhile.","zh":"make economic sense 指在財務上合理或值得做。"},{"en":"Buying a monthly bus pass makes economic sense if a student travels every day.","zh":"如果學生每天乘車，購買月票在經濟上合理。"},{"en":"If selling fruit earns more over time than selling trees once, conservation may make economic sense.","zh":"如果長期賣水果比一次賣樹賺得更多，保育可能符合經濟效益。"},{"en":"The phrase judges whether an action is sensible in money terms.","zh":"這個片語從金錢角度判斷行動是否明智。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"non-timber forest products","meaning":"非木材森林產品","examples":[{"en":"There was strong interest in trading non-timber forest products.","zh":"人們對買賣非木材森林產品有濃厚興趣。"},{"en":"Non-timber forest products are forest goods other than wood, such as fruits, nuts, fibres, oils, and medicinal plants.","zh":"non-timber forest products 指木材以外的森林產品，例如水果、堅果、纖維、油和藥用植物。"},{"en":"Honey, mushrooms, and forest herbs can be non-timber forest products.","zh":"蜂蜜、蘑菇和森林草藥都可以是非木材森林產品。"},{"en":"If communities earn from non-timber forest products, they may have reasons to keep trees standing.","zh":"如果社群能從非木材森林產品賺錢，他們可能有理由保留樹木。"},{"en":"The phrase separates forest value from timber alone.","zh":"這個片語把森林價值與木材本身分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"environmental groups","meaning":"環保團體","examples":[{"en":"Environmental groups were promoting the idea of trading forest products.","zh":"環保團體正在推廣買賣森林產品的理念。"},{"en":"Environmental groups are organisations that work to protect nature, wildlife, land, water, or climate.","zh":"environmental groups 指致力保護自然、野生動物、土地、水或氣候的組織。"},{"en":"Environmental groups may campaign against pollution or support forest conservation.","zh":"環保團體可能發起反污染運動或支持森林保育。"},{"en":"If environmental groups promote forest products, they may hope conservation can also support local incomes.","zh":"如果環保團體推廣森林產品，他們可能希望保育也能支持本地收入。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised bodies focused on environmental protection.","zh":"這個片語指以環境保護為重點的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"green-minded businesses","meaning":"具環保意識的企業","examples":[{"en":"Green-minded businesses supported the trade in non-timber forest products.","zh":"具環保意識的企業支持非木材森林產品貿易。"},{"en":"Green-minded businesses are companies that care about environmental protection and sustainability.","zh":"green-minded businesses 指關注環境保護和可持續發展的公司。"},{"en":"A green-minded business may reduce packaging, use clean energy, or buy from sustainable suppliers.","zh":"具環保意識的企業可能減少包裝、使用清潔能源或向可持續供應商採購。"},{"en":"If green-minded businesses support forest products, they may create markets that reward conservation.","zh":"如果具環保意識的企業支持森林產品，就可能創造獎勵保育的市場。"},{"en":"The phrase describes businesses with environmental concerns.","zh":"這個片語描述有環境關注的企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"promote the idea","meaning":"推廣這個理念","examples":[{"en":"Environmental groups were promoting the idea of trading forest products.","zh":"環保團體正在推廣買賣森林產品這個理念。"},{"en":"Promote the idea means actively support, spread, or encourage people to accept an idea.","zh":"promote the idea 指積極支持、傳播或鼓勵人們接受某個想法。"},{"en":"A school may promote the idea of recycling by placing bins in every classroom.","zh":"學校可能透過在每間課室放回收箱，推廣回收這個理念。"},{"en":"If organisations promote an idea strongly, more people may treat it as a real option.","zh":"如果組織強力推廣一個理念，更多人可能把它視為真正選項。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on spreading support for a concept.","zh":"這個片語集中於傳播對概念的支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a seminal paper","meaning":"具開創性的論文","examples":[{"en":"The view was presented in a seminal paper published in Nature.","zh":"這個看法出現在一篇刊於 Nature 的具開創性論文中。"},{"en":"A seminal paper is an important academic article that strongly influences later research or debate.","zh":"seminal paper 指強烈影響後來研究或討論的重要學術文章。"},{"en":"A seminal paper in education may change how teachers think about reading difficulties.","zh":"教育領域的開創性論文可能改變老師對閱讀困難的看法。"},{"en":"If a paper becomes seminal, later researchers often cite it, test it, or argue against it.","zh":"如果論文變得具開創性，後來研究者常引用、測試或反駁它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a highly influential piece of research.","zh":"這個片語描述極具影響力的研究文章。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"valuation of","meaning":"對……的價值評估","examples":[{"en":"The paper focused on the valuation of an Amazonian rainforest.","zh":"該論文集中於對一片亞馬遜雨林的價值評估。"},{"en":"Valuation of something means estimating or calculating its economic worth.","zh":"valuation of something 指估計或計算某物的經濟價值。"},{"en":"A bank may request the valuation of a flat before approving a mortgage.","zh":"銀行在批准按揭前可能要求對單位作價值評估。"},{"en":"If forest valuation includes fruit and medicine, the forest may be worth more than its timber.","zh":"如果森林價值評估包括水果和藥物，森林可能比其木材更值錢。"},{"en":"The phrase asks how much something is worth.","zh":"這個片語詢問某物值多少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"calculate that","meaning":"計算出；估算出","examples":[{"en":"The researchers calculated that fruit revenues could exceed logging income.","zh":"研究人員計算出水果收入可能超過伐木收入。"},{"en":"Calculate that means work out or estimate something using numbers, evidence, or reasoning.","zh":"calculate that 指使用數字、證據或推理算出或估算某事。"},{"en":"A family may calculate that cooking at home saves more money than eating out.","zh":"家庭可能計算出在家煮飯比外出用餐更省錢。"},{"en":"If researchers calculate that fruit income is higher, they must show the data behind the claim.","zh":"如果研究人員估算水果收入更高，就必須展示該主張背後的數據。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a conclusion based on calculation.","zh":"這個片語引出基於計算的結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"revenues from the sale of","meaning":"銷售……所得收入","examples":[{"en":"Revenues from the sale of fruits could exceed those from timber.","zh":"銷售水果所得收入可能超過木材收入。"},{"en":"Revenues from the sale of something are the money earned by selling it.","zh":"revenues from the sale of something 指出售某物所得的金錢。"},{"en":"A school fair’s revenues from the sale of snacks may be used to buy library books.","zh":"學校賣物會銷售小食所得收入可能用來購買圖書館書籍。"},{"en":"If revenues from fruit sales continue every year, they may be more valuable than one timber payment.","zh":"如果水果銷售收入每年持續，它可能比一次木材付款更有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to income from selling a product.","zh":"這個片語指出售產品所得收入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"far exceed","meaning":"遠遠超過","examples":[{"en":"Fruit revenues could far exceed those from a one-off sale of trees.","zh":"水果收入可能遠遠超過一次性出售樹木所得收入。"},{"en":"Far exceed means be much greater than something else.","zh":"far exceed 指比另一事物大得多。"},{"en":"The cost of repairing a neglected roof may far exceed the cost of regular maintenance.","zh":"維修被忽視屋頂的費用可能遠遠超過定期保養費用。"},{"en":"If long-term fruit income far exceeds timber income, cutting the trees may be a poor choice.","zh":"如果長期水果收入遠遠超過木材收入，砍樹可能是不明智選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a large difference, not a small advantage.","zh":"這個片語強調巨大差距，而不是小優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a one-off sale of","meaning":"一次性出售……","examples":[{"en":"The researchers compared fruit income with a one-off sale of trees.","zh":"研究人員把水果收入與一次性出售樹木作比較。"},{"en":"A one-off sale of something is a single sale that happens once, not repeatedly.","zh":"one-off sale of something 指只發生一次、而非重複發生的出售。"},{"en":"Selling an old laptop is a one-off sale, while renting a room gives repeated income.","zh":"出售舊手提電腦是一次性銷售，而出租房間則帶來重複收入。"},{"en":"If villagers choose a one-off sale of trees, they may lose future fruit income.","zh":"如果村民選擇一次性出售樹木，可能失去未來水果收入。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts immediate payment with continuing returns.","zh":"這個片語把即時付款與持續回報作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"loggers","meaning":"伐木工；伐木商","examples":[{"en":"The sale of trees to loggers could bring quick money.","zh":"把樹木賣給伐木商可以帶來快錢。"},{"en":"Loggers are people or companies that cut down trees for timber.","zh":"loggers 指為木材砍伐樹木的人或公司。"},{"en":"Loggers may enter a forest to remove valuable hardwood trees.","zh":"伐木工可能進入森林移走珍貴硬木樹。"},{"en":"If loggers pay villagers quickly, the offer may look attractive even when the long-term loss is high.","zh":"如果伐木商迅速付錢給村民，即使長期損失很高，提議也可能看似吸引。"},{"en":"The word refers to those involved in tree cutting for wood.","zh":"這個詞指參與砍樹取木的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be keen to discover whether","meaning":"熱切想了解是否……","examples":[{"en":"The union was keen to discover whether conserving the forest made more sense.","zh":"工會熱切想了解保育森林是否更合理。"},{"en":"Be keen to discover whether means strongly want to find out if something is true or worthwhile.","zh":"be keen to discover whether 指非常想查明某事是否屬實或值得做。"},{"en":"A school may be keen to discover whether shorter homework improves student wellbeing.","zh":"學校可能熱切想了解較短功課是否改善學生身心健康。"},{"en":"If farmers are keen to discover whether fruit harvesting pays, they need reliable data.","zh":"如果農民熱切想了解採集水果是否賺錢，就需要可靠數據。"},{"en":"The phrase shows active curiosity about a practical question.","zh":"這個片語顯示對實際問題的主動好奇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"conserve the forest","meaning":"保育森林","examples":[{"en":"The union wanted to know whether it was better to conserve the forest.","zh":"工會想知道保育森林是否較好。"},{"en":"Conserve the forest means protect the forest so its trees, animals, and resources can continue to exist.","zh":"conserve the forest 指保護森林，讓其樹木、動物和資源能繼續存在。"},{"en":"A village may conserve the forest by limiting logging and collecting fruit carefully.","zh":"村莊可能透過限制伐木和小心採果來保育森林。"},{"en":"If people conserve forests, they may protect food, water, wildlife, and future income.","zh":"如果人們保育森林，可能保護食物、水源、野生動物和未來收入。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses protection and careful use.","zh":"這個片語強調保護和謹慎使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"subsistence use","meaning":"自給用途","examples":[{"en":"The forest could be conserved for subsistence use.","zh":"森林可以為自給用途而被保育。"},{"en":"Subsistence use means using resources mainly to support basic daily living, not large-scale trade.","zh":"subsistence use 指主要為支持基本日常生活而使用資源，而不是大規模買賣。"},{"en":"A family may collect firewood and fruit for subsistence use rather than for sale.","zh":"家庭可能收集柴木和水果作自給用途，而不是出售。"},{"en":"If researchers ignore subsistence use, they may underestimate the forest’s value to local people.","zh":"如果研究人員忽視自給用途，可能低估森林對本地人的價值。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on survival and household needs.","zh":"這個片語集中於生存和家庭需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"medicinal plants","meaning":"藥用植物","examples":[{"en":"The forest provided fruit, game and medicinal plants.","zh":"森林提供水果、野味和藥用植物。"},{"en":"Medicinal plants are plants used to treat illness, relieve symptoms, or support health.","zh":"medicinal plants 指用來治病、紓緩症狀或支持健康的植物。"},{"en":"Some families use medicinal plants for minor cuts, stomach pain, or fever.","zh":"有些家庭使用藥用植物處理小傷口、胃痛或發燒。"},{"en":"If medicinal plants disappear from a forest, local healthcare choices may become fewer.","zh":"如果藥用植物從森林消失，本地醫療選擇可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to plants valued for healing or health purposes.","zh":"這個片語指因治療或健康用途而有價值的植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"The union considered conserving the forest rather than selling trees for timber.","zh":"工會考慮保育森林，而不是把樹木賣作木材。"},{"en":"Rather than shows a contrast between the option chosen and the option rejected.","zh":"rather than 顯示被選擇的選項與被拒絕的選項之間的對比。"},{"en":"A student may revise with past papers rather than simply rereading notes.","zh":"學生可能用歷屆試題溫習，而不是只重讀筆記。"},{"en":"If villagers keep trees rather than sell them, they may protect long-term resources.","zh":"如果村民保留樹木而不是出售它們，可能保護長期資源。"},{"en":"The phrase helps separate two possible choices.","zh":"這個片語幫助分開兩個可能選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sell trees for timber","meaning":"把樹木賣作木材","examples":[{"en":"Some villagers were tempted to sell trees for timber.","zh":"有些村民受誘惑，把樹木賣作木材。"},{"en":"Sell trees for timber means cut or sell trees so their wood can be used commercially.","zh":"sell trees for timber 指砍伐或出售樹木，使其木材可作商業用途。"},{"en":"A landowner may sell trees for timber when they need money quickly.","zh":"地主急需錢時，可能把樹木賣作木材。"},{"en":"If people sell trees for timber without considering fruit or wildlife value, they may lose more than they gain.","zh":"如果人們出售樹木作木材而不考慮水果或野生動物價值，可能得不償失。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the wood value of trees.","zh":"這個片語集中於樹木的木材價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"far from clear","meaning":"遠未明朗；一點也不清楚","examples":[{"en":"Whether the plan would work for the caboclos was far from clear.","zh":"該計劃對 caboclos 是否有效，遠未明朗。"},{"en":"Far from clear means very uncertain or not at all obvious.","zh":"far from clear 指非常不確定或完全不明顯。"},{"en":"After one lesson, it may be far from clear whether a new teaching method really works.","zh":"上完一課後，新教學方法是否真正有效可能遠未明朗。"},{"en":"If fruit income is unpredictable, the economic answer is far from clear.","zh":"如果水果收入難以預測，經濟答案就一點也不清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses uncertainty.","zh":"這個片語強調不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be invited to work in","meaning":"受邀到……工作","examples":[{"en":"Shanley had been invited to work in the Rio Capim.","zh":"Shanley 受邀到 Rio Capim 工作。"},{"en":"Be invited to work in means be asked to do work or research in a particular place.","zh":"be invited to work in 指被邀請到某個特定地方工作或研究。"},{"en":"A doctor may be invited to work in a rural clinic where specialists are rare.","zh":"醫生可能受邀到專科醫生稀少的鄉村診所工作。"},{"en":"If a researcher is invited to work in a community, local trust may already be developing.","zh":"如果研究員受邀到社群工作，本地信任可能已開始形成。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that someone’s work in a place begins by invitation.","zh":"這個片語顯示某人在某地工作是由邀請開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be suspicious","meaning":"有戒心；起疑","examples":[{"en":"Some caboclos were suspicious of Shanley’s research.","zh":"有些 caboclos 對 Shanley 的研究有戒心。"},{"en":"Be suspicious means feel doubtful or distrustful because something may be wrong or dangerous.","zh":"be suspicious 指因某事可能有問題或危險而感到懷疑或不信任。"},{"en":"A customer may be suspicious of a deal that sounds too cheap to be true.","zh":"如果交易便宜得不像真，顧客可能會起疑。"},{"en":"If communities have been exploited before, they may be suspicious of outside researchers.","zh":"如果社群過去曾被剝削，他們可能對外來研究人員有戒心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes caution based on possible risk.","zh":"這個片語描述基於可能風險的謹慎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rob someone of","meaning":"奪去某人的……","examples":[{"en":"Some neighbours feared that Shanley had come to rob them of their trees.","zh":"有些鄰居擔心 Shanley 是來奪去他們樹木的。"},{"en":"Rob someone of something means take something valuable away from them, often unfairly.","zh":"rob someone of something 指奪走某人有價值的東西，通常是不公平地奪走。"},{"en":"A dishonest contract can rob workers of fair pay.","zh":"不誠實合約可以奪去工人的公平薪酬。"},{"en":"If logging companies buy forests for too little, they may rob communities of future resources.","zh":"如果伐木公司以過低價格購買森林，可能奪去社群未來資源。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses loss caused by unfair taking.","zh":"這個片語強調由不公平奪取造成的損失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"work on a study","meaning":"參與一項研究","examples":[{"en":"Mangueira welcomed Shanley and worked on her study.","zh":"Mangueira 歡迎 Shanley，並參與她的研究。"},{"en":"Work on a study means take part in research by helping collect, record, or analyse information.","zh":"work on a study 指透過協助收集、記錄或分析資料參與研究。"},{"en":"Students may work on a study about how sleep affects exam performance.","zh":"學生可能參與一項關於睡眠如何影響考試表現的研究。"},{"en":"If local people work on a study, the research may include more accurate everyday knowledge.","zh":"如果本地人參與研究，研究可能包含更準確的日常知識。"},{"en":"The phrase shows active participation in research.","zh":"這個片語顯示主動參與研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"almost entirely covered with","meaning":"幾乎完全被……覆蓋","examples":[{"en":"His land was almost entirely covered with primary forest.","zh":"他的土地幾乎完全被原始森林覆蓋。"},{"en":"Almost entirely covered with means nearly the whole area was covered by something.","zh":"almost entirely covered with 指幾乎整個範圍都被某物覆蓋。"},{"en":"After heavy snow, the playground was almost entirely covered with white ice.","zh":"大雪後，操場幾乎完全被白冰覆蓋。"},{"en":"If land is almost entirely covered with forest, cutting it changes the whole environment.","zh":"如果土地幾乎完全被森林覆蓋，砍伐會改變整個環境。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses near-total coverage.","zh":"這個片語強調接近完全覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"primary forest","meaning":"原始森林","examples":[{"en":"The land was almost entirely covered with primary forest.","zh":"這片土地幾乎完全被原始森林覆蓋。"},{"en":"Primary forest is natural forest that has not been heavily disturbed by humans.","zh":"primary forest 指未受人類嚴重干擾的天然森林。"},{"en":"Primary forest often contains old trees, rich wildlife, and complex ecological relationships.","zh":"原始森林通常包含老樹、豐富野生動物和複雜生態關係。"},{"en":"If primary forest is logged, it may take a very long time to recover its original structure.","zh":"如果原始森林被伐木，可能需要很長時間才能恢復原有結構。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to relatively undisturbed old forest.","zh":"這個片語指相對未受干擾的古老森林。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tracts of forest","meaning":"一片片森林；大片林地","examples":[{"en":"The communities selected several tracts of forest for the study.","zh":"這些社群選出幾片森林作研究。"},{"en":"Tracts of forest are large areas or stretches of forest land.","zh":"tracts of forest 指大片或一段段森林土地。"},{"en":"Researchers may compare different tracts of forest to see how fire affects wildlife.","zh":"研究人員可能比較不同大片林地，以了解火災如何影響野生動物。"},{"en":"If several tracts are studied, scientists can avoid relying on one small example.","zh":"如果研究幾片林地，科學家就可以避免只依賴一個小例子。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to sizeable pieces of forest.","zh":"這個片語指相當大的森林範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"enable someone to identify","meaning":"使某人能識別","examples":[{"en":"The study enabled Shanley to identify three important trees.","zh":"這項研究使 Shanley 能識別三種重要樹木。"},{"en":"Enable someone to identify means make it possible for someone to recognise or name something clearly.","zh":"enable someone to identify 指使某人能清楚認出或命名某事物。"},{"en":"Good revision notes enable students to identify the main grammar pattern quickly.","zh":"良好溫習筆記使學生能快速識別主要文法模式。"},{"en":"If research enables villagers to identify valuable trees, they can make better selling decisions.","zh":"如果研究使村民能識別有價值樹木，他們就能作出更好出售決定。"},{"en":"The phrase connects information with clearer recognition.","zh":"這個片語把資訊與更清楚辨認連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"found throughout","meaning":"遍佈……","examples":[{"en":"The three trees are found throughout the Amazon.","zh":"這三種樹遍佈亞馬遜。"},{"en":"Found throughout means existing in many places across a whole area.","zh":"found throughout 指存在於整個地區的許多地方。"},{"en":"Convenience stores are found throughout many large cities.","zh":"便利店遍佈許多大城市。"},{"en":"If a tree species is found throughout the Amazon, knowledge about it may help many communities.","zh":"如果一種樹遍佈亞馬遜，關於它的知識可能幫助許多社群。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses wide distribution.","zh":"這個片語強調廣泛分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be much favoured by","meaning":"深受……喜愛","examples":[{"en":"The fruit was much favoured by the caboclos.","zh":"這種水果深受 caboclos 喜愛。"},{"en":"Be much favoured by means be strongly liked or preferred by a person or group.","zh":"be much favoured by 指受到某人或群體強烈喜愛或偏好。"},{"en":"A school snack may be much favoured by students if it is cheap and filling.","zh":"如果學校小食便宜又飽肚，可能深受學生喜愛。"},{"en":"If a fruit is much favoured by local people, losing the tree affects daily diet and culture.","zh":"如果水果深受本地人喜愛，失去該樹會影響日常飲食和文化。"},{"en":"The phrase shows strong preference.","zh":"這個片語顯示強烈偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"extract oils from","meaning":"從……提取油","examples":[{"en":"The caboclos extracted oils from the fruits.","zh":"caboclos 從水果中提取油。"},{"en":"Extract oils from means remove or obtain oil from a plant, fruit, seed, or other material.","zh":"extract oils from 指從植物、水果、種子或其他材料中取出或取得油。"},{"en":"A factory may extract oil from olives to make cooking oil.","zh":"工廠可能從橄欖提取油來製作食用油。"},{"en":"If villagers can extract valuable oils from forest fruit, the tree may be worth keeping.","zh":"如果村民能從森林水果中提取有價值的油，該樹可能值得保留。"},{"en":"The phrase describes taking a useful substance out of something.","zh":"這個片語描述從某物中取出有用物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"wildlife","meaning":"野生動物","examples":[{"en":"The caboclos knew what sort of wildlife the fruits attracted.","zh":"caboclos 知道這些水果會吸引哪類野生動物。"},{"en":"Wildlife means animals and plants living naturally in the wild, not domesticated or farmed.","zh":"wildlife 指自然生活在野外、而非被馴養或養殖的動植物。"},{"en":"A forest with rich wildlife may contain birds, monkeys, insects, and small mammals.","zh":"野生動物豐富的森林可能有鳥、猴子、昆蟲和小型哺乳動物。"},{"en":"If fruit trees attract wildlife, they may support hunting, seed dispersal, and biodiversity.","zh":"如果果樹吸引野生動物，它們可能支持狩獵、種子傳播和生物多樣性。"},{"en":"The word refers to living nature outside human control.","zh":"這個詞指不受人類控制的自然生命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the face of","meaning":"面對……","examples":[{"en":"The caboclos lacked financial information in the face of aggressive tactics from logging companies.","zh":"面對伐木公司的強硬手段，caboclos 缺乏財務資訊。"},{"en":"In the face of means when dealing with or confronted by a difficulty, threat, or pressure.","zh":"in the face of 指在處理或面對困難、威脅或壓力時。"},{"en":"A student may stay calm in the face of a difficult exam question.","zh":"學生面對困難考題時可能保持冷靜。"},{"en":"If villagers lack information in the face of strong buyers, they may make poor decisions.","zh":"如果村民面對強勢買家時缺乏資訊，可能作出差劣決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pressure or challenge surrounding an action.","zh":"這個片語描述行動周圍的壓力或挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"aggressive tactics","meaning":"強硬手段","examples":[{"en":"Logging companies used aggressive tactics to buy trees.","zh":"伐木公司使用強硬手段購買樹木。"},{"en":"Aggressive tactics are forceful, pushy, or intimidating methods used to get what one wants.","zh":"aggressive tactics 指為達目的而使用強迫、進逼或嚇人的方法。"},{"en":"A salesperson uses aggressive tactics if they pressure customers to buy immediately.","zh":"如果銷售員迫顧客立即購買，就是使用強硬手段。"},{"en":"If poor farmers face aggressive tactics, clear information can protect them from unfair deals.","zh":"如果貧困農民面對強硬手段，清楚資訊可以保護他們免受不公平交易。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests pressure rather than fair persuasion.","zh":"這個片語暗示壓力，而不是公平說服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have no measure of","meaning":"無法衡量；無從掌握","examples":[{"en":"The caboclos had no measure of the trees’ financial worth.","zh":"caboclos 無法衡量樹木的經濟價值。"},{"en":"Have no measure of means have no way to judge, calculate, or understand something properly.","zh":"have no measure of 指沒有方法正確判斷、計算或理解某事。"},{"en":"A student has no measure of progress if they never check old mistakes.","zh":"如果學生從不檢查舊錯誤，就無法衡量進步。"},{"en":"If farmers have no measure of a tree’s value, buyers can set unfair prices.","zh":"如果農民無法掌握樹木價值，買家就能設定不公平價格。"},{"en":"The phrase shows lack of a reliable standard or calculation.","zh":"這個片語顯示缺乏可靠標準或計算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"financial worth","meaning":"經濟價值","examples":[{"en":"The farmers needed to understand the financial worth of their trees.","zh":"農民需要了解自己樹木的經濟價值。"},{"en":"Financial worth means the amount of money something is really worth.","zh":"financial worth 指某物真正值多少錢。"},{"en":"Before selling a flat, a family should understand its financial worth.","zh":"出售單位前，家庭應了解其經濟價值。"},{"en":"If people do not know the financial worth of a resource, they may accept too low a price.","zh":"如果人們不知道資源的經濟價值，可能接受過低價格。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on monetary value.","zh":"這個片語集中於金錢價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"find out","meaning":"查明；弄清楚","examples":[{"en":"Shanley wanted to find out the real value of the trees.","zh":"Shanley 想查明這些樹木的真正價值。"},{"en":"Find out means discover information by asking, checking, observing, or researching.","zh":"find out 指透過詢問、檢查、觀察或研究發現資訊。"},{"en":"A student may find out their weak grammar points by reviewing corrected essays.","zh":"學生可以透過重看批改文章，弄清楚自己的文法弱點。"},{"en":"If villagers find out the true value of fruit trees, they can bargain more confidently.","zh":"如果村民查明果樹真正價值，就能更有信心議價。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving from not knowing to knowing.","zh":"這個片語描述由不知道走向知道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"start from scratch","meaning":"從零開始","examples":[{"en":"Shanley decided to start from scratch with a scientific study.","zh":"Shanley 決定以科學研究從零開始。"},{"en":"Start from scratch means begin from the very beginning, without using existing work as a base.","zh":"start from scratch 指從最開始做起，不使用現成工作作基礎。"},{"en":"If a student loses all notes before an exam, they may have to start from scratch.","zh":"如果學生考試前遺失所有筆記，可能要從零開始。"},{"en":"When almost nothing is known scientifically, researchers must start from scratch by collecting basic data.","zh":"當科學上幾乎一無所知，研究人員必須透過收集基本數據從零開始。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests beginning with no ready foundation.","zh":"這個片語暗示沒有現成基礎地開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"from a scientific point of view","meaning":"從科學角度來看","examples":[{"en":"From a scientific point of view, little was known about the trees.","zh":"從科學角度來看，人們對這些樹知道得很少。"},{"en":"From a scientific point of view means when judged using scientific evidence, methods, and standards.","zh":"from a scientific point of view 指以科學證據、方法和標準來判斷。"},{"en":"From a scientific point of view, a claim needs evidence, not just tradition or opinion.","zh":"從科學角度來看，主張需要證據，而不只是傳統或意見。"},{"en":"If local people know a plant well but scientists have not studied it, knowledge may differ by viewpoint.","zh":"如果本地人很了解一種植物，但科學家尚未研究它，知識可能因角度而不同。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a science-based perspective.","zh":"這個片語引出以科學為基礎的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hardly anything was known about","meaning":"人們對……幾乎一無所知","examples":[{"en":"Hardly anything was known about these trees before Shanley’s research.","zh":"在 Shanley 的研究之前，人們對這些樹幾乎一無所知。"},{"en":"Hardly anything was known about means people had almost no reliable information about something.","zh":"hardly anything was known about 指人們對某事幾乎沒有可靠資訊。"},{"en":"Before the survey, hardly anything was known about why students skipped breakfast.","zh":"在調查前，人們對學生為何不吃早餐幾乎一無所知。"},{"en":"If hardly anything is known about a resource, careful research is needed before decisions are made.","zh":"如果人們對某資源幾乎一無所知，就需要在決定前仔細研究。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a serious lack of knowledge.","zh":"這個片語強調嚴重缺乏知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"field research","meaning":"實地研究","examples":[{"en":"Six years of field research produced a large amount of data.","zh":"六年的實地研究產生大量數據。"},{"en":"Field research is research carried out in real places outside the laboratory or office.","zh":"field research 指在實驗室或辦公室之外的真實地方進行的研究。"},{"en":"A sociologist may conduct field research by visiting homes, markets, and workplaces.","zh":"社會學家可能透過走訪家庭、市場和工作場所來進行實地研究。"},{"en":"If field research lasts many years, it can capture seasonal changes and everyday practices.","zh":"如果實地研究持續多年，就能捕捉季節變化和日常做法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to learning directly from real-world settings.","zh":"這個片語指直接從真實世界環境中學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"yield a mass of data","meaning":"產生大量數據","examples":[{"en":"Six years of field research yielded a mass of data.","zh":"六年的實地研究產生大量數據。"},{"en":"Yield a mass of data means produce a large amount of information through research.","zh":"yield a mass of data 指透過研究產生大量資訊。"},{"en":"A school survey of every class can yield a mass of data about homework habits.","zh":"對每個班級進行學校調查，可以產生大量關於功課習慣的數據。"},{"en":"If research yields much data, the challenge becomes organising it into useful conclusions.","zh":"如果研究產生大量數據，挑戰就變成把它整理成有用結論。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a large quantity of collected evidence.","zh":"這個片語強調大量收集得來的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"flowering and fruiting behaviour","meaning":"開花結果習性","examples":[{"en":"The research recorded the trees’ flowering and fruiting behaviour.","zh":"研究記錄了這些樹的開花結果習性。"},{"en":"Flowering and fruiting behaviour means when and how plants produce flowers and fruit.","zh":"flowering and fruiting behaviour 指植物何時及如何開花結果。"},{"en":"Farmers observe flowering and fruiting behaviour to know when crops may be ready.","zh":"農民觀察開花結果習性，以知道農作物何時可能成熟。"},{"en":"If a tree’s fruiting behaviour is unpredictable, income from its fruit may be unstable.","zh":"如果一棵樹的結果習性難以預測，其水果收入可能不穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a plant’s reproductive pattern.","zh":"這個片語描述植物的繁殖模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"forest resources","meaning":"森林資源","examples":[{"en":"The families weighed the forest resources they used.","zh":"這些家庭為他們使用的森林資源稱重。"},{"en":"Forest resources are useful things obtained from forests, such as fruit, wood, fibre, medicine, and game.","zh":"forest resources 指從森林取得的有用東西，例如水果、木材、纖維、藥物和野味。"},{"en":"A village may depend on forest resources for food, building materials, and daily income.","zh":"村莊可能依賴森林資源取得食物、建材和日常收入。"},{"en":"If forest resources decline after fire, household diets and livelihoods may change.","zh":"如果森林資源在火災後減少，家庭飲食和生計可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical benefits from forests.","zh":"這個片語指森林帶來的實際好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"game","meaning":"野味；獵物","examples":[{"en":"The families recorded the game they caught in the forest.","zh":"這些家庭記錄他們在森林中捕獲的野味。"},{"en":"Game means wild animals hunted for food.","zh":"game 指被獵取作食物的野生動物。"},{"en":"In some rural areas, families eat game such as birds, deer, or small mammals.","zh":"在一些鄉郊地區，家庭會食用鳥、鹿或小型哺乳動物等野味。"},{"en":"If fruit trees attract game, cutting those trees can reduce local meat supplies.","zh":"如果果樹吸引獵物，砍掉那些樹可能減少本地肉食供應。"},{"en":"The word refers to hunted wildlife, not children’s games.","zh":"這個詞指被捕獵的野生動物，而不是兒童遊戲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fibre","meaning":"纖維","examples":[{"en":"The families weighed the fibre they collected from the forest.","zh":"這些家庭為他們從森林收集的纖維稱重。"},{"en":"Fibre means thread-like plant material that can be used for rope, baskets, cloth, or other practical items.","zh":"fibre 指可用來製作繩、籃、布或其他實用品的線狀植物材料。"},{"en":"A community may collect palm fibre to weave mats and baskets.","zh":"社群可能收集棕櫚纖維來編織蓆和籃子。"},{"en":"If forest fibre becomes scarce, families may need to buy materials they once collected freely.","zh":"如果森林纖維變得稀少，家庭可能需要購買以往可免費收集的材料。"},{"en":"The word refers to useful plant material, not only dietary fibre.","zh":"這個詞指有用植物材料，而不只是膳食纖維。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"document its source","meaning":"記錄其來源","examples":[{"en":"The families documented the source of everything they used.","zh":"這些家庭記錄他們所用每樣東西的來源。"},{"en":"Document its source means record where something came from.","zh":"document its source 指記錄某物來自哪裡。"},{"en":"Students should document the source of every quotation in a research essay.","zh":"學生在研究文章中應記錄每段引文的來源。"},{"en":"If families document where fruit, fibre, and game come from, researchers can see which trees matter most.","zh":"如果家庭記錄水果、纖維和野味來自哪裡，研究人員就能看出哪些樹最重要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses careful recording of origins.","zh":"這個片語強調仔細記錄來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"logging sales","meaning":"伐木銷售","examples":[{"en":"Researchers studied the forest after three logging sales.","zh":"研究人員在三次伐木銷售後研究森林。"},{"en":"Logging sales are transactions in which trees or timber rights are sold to loggers or timber companies.","zh":"logging sales 指把樹木或木材權利賣給伐木工或木材公司的交易。"},{"en":"A village may receive money from logging sales but lose useful forest resources afterwards.","zh":"村莊可能從伐木銷售中收到錢，但之後失去有用森林資源。"},{"en":"If researchers study an area after logging sales, they can measure how forest use changes.","zh":"如果研究人員在伐木銷售後研究地區，就能量度森林使用如何改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to selling trees or timber access.","zh":"這個片語指出售樹木或木材使用權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a major fire","meaning":"一場大火","examples":[{"en":"A major fire in 1997 changed the forest ecosystem.","zh":"1997年的一場大火改變了森林生態系統。"},{"en":"A major fire is a large and serious fire that causes significant damage.","zh":"major fire 指造成重大破壞的大型嚴重火災。"},{"en":"A major fire in a market can destroy shops, stock, and years of savings.","zh":"市場中的一場大火可以摧毀店舖、貨物和多年積蓄。"},{"en":"If a major forest fire occurs, fruit, game, and household resources may all decline.","zh":"如果發生大型森林火災，水果、野味和家庭資源都可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both size and seriousness.","zh":"這個片語同時強調規模和嚴重性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the ecosystem’s reaction to","meaning":"生態系統對……的反應","examples":[{"en":"The researchers studied the ecosystem’s reaction to logging and fire.","zh":"研究人員研究生態系統對伐木和火災的反應。"},{"en":"The ecosystem’s reaction to something means how the plants, animals, soil, and natural processes change after an event.","zh":"ecosystem’s reaction to something 指植物、動物、土壤和自然過程在某事件後如何改變。"},{"en":"Scientists may study a lake ecosystem’s reaction to pollution.","zh":"科學家可能研究湖泊生態系統對污染的反應。"},{"en":"If an ecosystem reacts badly to logging, food chains and local livelihoods may suffer.","zh":"如果生態系統對伐木反應很差，食物鏈和本地生計可能受苦。"},{"en":"The phrase treats nature as a connected system responding to disturbance.","zh":"這個片語把自然視為一個會回應干擾的連繫系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"logging and disturbance","meaning":"伐木和干擾","examples":[{"en":"The study examined the effects of logging and disturbance.","zh":"研究檢視伐木和干擾的影響。"},{"en":"Logging and disturbance means tree cutting and other disruptions that change the forest environment.","zh":"logging and disturbance 指砍樹以及其他改變森林環境的干擾。"},{"en":"Road building can create disturbance even if only a few trees are cut.","zh":"修路即使只砍少量樹，也可能造成干擾。"},{"en":"If logging and disturbance damage key fruit trees, families may lose food and game.","zh":"如果伐木和干擾破壞關鍵果樹，家庭可能失去食物和野味。"},{"en":"The phrase combines commercial tree cutting with broader ecological disruption.","zh":"這個片語結合商業砍樹與更廣泛生態干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"carry out a study","meaning":"進行研究","examples":[{"en":"The researchers carried out a similar study in 1999.","zh":"研究人員在1999年進行了一項相似研究。"},{"en":"Carry out a study means conduct research in an organised way.","zh":"carry out a study 指以有組織方式進行研究。"},{"en":"A school may carry out a study to see whether breakfast affects attention in class.","zh":"學校可能進行研究，看看早餐是否影響課堂專注力。"},{"en":"If researchers carry out a second study, they can check whether earlier results still hold.","zh":"如果研究人員進行第二項研究，就能檢查早前結果是否仍然成立。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to doing research, not merely discussing it.","zh":"這個片語指實際做研究，而不只是討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a less exhaustive study","meaning":"較不詳盡的研究","examples":[{"en":"They carried out a less exhaustive study with 15 families.","zh":"他們與15個家庭進行了一項較不詳盡的研究。"},{"en":"A less exhaustive study is a study that is less complete or detailed than another one.","zh":"less exhaustive study 指比另一項研究較不完整或較不詳細的研究。"},{"en":"A teacher may do a less exhaustive survey by asking one class instead of the whole school.","zh":"老師可能只問一班而不是全校，做一項較不詳盡的調查。"},{"en":"If a study is less exhaustive, its results may still be useful but less comprehensive.","zh":"如果研究較不詳盡，其結果可能仍有用，但不那麼全面。"},{"en":"The phrase compares levels of detail and coverage.","zh":"這個片語比較詳細程度和涵蓋範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the changes were striking","meaning":"變化十分顯著","examples":[{"en":"The changes in forest use were striking.","zh":"森林使用上的變化十分顯著。"},{"en":"The changes were striking means the differences were very noticeable or surprising.","zh":"the changes were striking 指差異非常明顯或令人驚訝。"},{"en":"After a new study plan, the changes in a student’s confidence may be striking.","zh":"使用新溫習計劃後，學生信心的變化可能十分顯著。"},{"en":"If fruit consumption falls sharply after a fire, the change is striking because daily life is clearly affected.","zh":"如果火災後水果消耗量急跌，變化就很顯著，因為日常生活明顯受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that a change is hard to ignore.","zh":"這個片語強調變化難以忽視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"average annual household consumption","meaning":"平均每戶每年消耗量","examples":[{"en":"Average annual household consumption of forest fruit fell sharply.","zh":"森林水果的平均每戶每年消耗量急劇下降。"},{"en":"Average annual household consumption means the amount a typical family uses in one year.","zh":"average annual household consumption 指一般家庭一年內使用的數量。"},{"en":"Average annual household consumption of electricity may rise when families buy more air conditioners.","zh":"當家庭購買更多冷氣機，每戶每年平均用電量可能上升。"},{"en":"If household consumption of forest fruit falls, family diets may become less varied.","zh":"如果森林水果的家庭消耗量下降，家庭飲食可能變得較少變化。"},{"en":"The phrase measures use at the family level over a year.","zh":"這個片語以家庭為單位量度一年使用量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"forest fruit","meaning":"森林水果","examples":[{"en":"Household consumption of forest fruit fell after the fire.","zh":"火災後，家庭消耗森林水果的量下降。"},{"en":"Forest fruit means fruit that grows naturally in forests rather than in cultivated orchards.","zh":"forest fruit 指自然生長於森林、而非果園種植的水果。"},{"en":"Families may collect forest fruit for food, oil, medicine, or sale.","zh":"家庭可能收集森林水果作食物、油、藥物或出售。"},{"en":"If forest fruit becomes scarce, villagers may need to buy food they once collected freely.","zh":"如果森林水果變得稀少，村民可能需要購買以往免費收集的食物。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to edible fruit from wild forest trees.","zh":"這個片語指來自野生森林樹木的可食用水果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fall from…to…","meaning":"從……下降至……","examples":[{"en":"Forest fruit consumption fell from 89 to 28 kilogrammes.","zh":"森林水果消耗量從89公斤下降至28公斤。"},{"en":"Fall from A to B means decrease from a higher number to a lower number.","zh":"fall from A to B 指由較高數字下降至較低數字。"},{"en":"A student’s screen time may fall from five hours to two hours during exam revision.","zh":"考試溫習期間，學生螢幕時間可能從五小時下降至兩小時。"},{"en":"If fruit use falls from 89 to 28 kilogrammes, the decline is large and measurable.","zh":"如果水果使用量從89公斤下降至28公斤，跌幅就是巨大且可量度。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly shows the size of a decrease.","zh":"這個片語清楚顯示下降幅度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fruit collection","meaning":"水果採集","examples":[{"en":"Fruit collection could coexist with some logging.","zh":"水果採集可以與某些伐木共存。"},{"en":"Fruit collection means gathering fruit from trees, especially in forests or farms.","zh":"fruit collection 指從樹上收集水果，尤其是在森林或農場中。"},{"en":"Families may organise fruit collection during the season when trees produce ripe fruit.","zh":"家庭可能在樹木產生成熟水果的季節安排水果採集。"},{"en":"If logging is limited, fruit collection may continue without destroying the forest resource.","zh":"如果伐木受限制，水果採集可能繼續而不破壞森林資源。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to collecting fruit as a practical activity or livelihood.","zh":"這個片語指採集水果這項實際活動或生計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"coexist with","meaning":"與……共存","examples":[{"en":"Fruit collection could coexist with a certain amount of logging.","zh":"水果採集可以與一定程度的伐木共存。"},{"en":"Coexist with means exist or happen at the same time without necessarily destroying each other.","zh":"coexist with 指同時存在或發生，而不一定互相破壞。"},{"en":"A quiet study area can coexist with a busy school library if spaces are clearly separated.","zh":"如果空間清楚分隔，安靜自修區可以與繁忙學校圖書館共存。"},{"en":"If careful fruit collection coexists with limited logging, forest use may be more balanced.","zh":"如果小心水果採集與有限伐木共存，森林使用可能更平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests compatibility under the right conditions.","zh":"這個片語暗示在合適條件下可以兼容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a certain amount of","meaning":"一定程度的……","examples":[{"en":"The forest could tolerate a certain amount of logging.","zh":"森林可以承受一定程度的伐木。"},{"en":"A certain amount of means some, but not unlimited, quantity of something.","zh":"a certain amount of 指某些數量，但不是無限量。"},{"en":"A student can handle a certain amount of stress, but too much may harm sleep.","zh":"學生可以承受一定程度的壓力，但太多可能傷害睡眠。"},{"en":"If a forest can tolerate a certain amount of logging, excessive logging may still damage it.","zh":"如果森林可以承受一定程度的伐木，過度伐木仍可能破壞它。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a limited acceptable level.","zh":"這個片語暗示有限的可接受水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"drop dramatically","meaning":"急劇下降","examples":[{"en":"Fruit collection dropped dramatically after the forest fire.","zh":"森林火災後，水果採集量急劇下降。"},{"en":"Drop dramatically means fall suddenly and by a large amount.","zh":"drop dramatically 指突然且大幅下降。"},{"en":"Attendance may drop dramatically if a class is moved to a very early time.","zh":"如果課堂改到很早時間，出席率可能急劇下降。"},{"en":"If fruit collection drops dramatically, families may lose food and income quickly.","zh":"如果水果採集量急劇下降，家庭可能很快失去食物和收入。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a sharp and serious decline.","zh":"這個片語強調急速而嚴重的下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"over the same period","meaning":"同一時期內","examples":[{"en":"Fibre use also dropped over the same period.","zh":"纖維使用量在同一時期內也下降。"},{"en":"Over the same period means during the same stretch of time being discussed.","zh":"over the same period 指在所討論的同一段時間內。"},{"en":"A school’s exam results improved, while absences fell over the same period.","zh":"學校考試成績改善，而缺席率在同一時期內下降。"},{"en":"If fruit and fibre use both drop over the same period, the cause may be shared.","zh":"如果水果和纖維使用量在同一時期內都下降，原因可能相同。"},{"en":"The phrase compares changes happening within one time frame.","zh":"這個片語比較同一時間框架內發生的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fibre use","meaning":"纖維使用量","examples":[{"en":"Fibre use fell after logging and fire damaged the forest.","zh":"伐木和火災破壞森林後，纖維使用量下降。"},{"en":"Fibre use means the amount or manner in which plant fibre is collected and used.","zh":"fibre use 指植物纖維被收集和使用的數量或方式。"},{"en":"Fibre use may include making rope, baskets, mats, or household tools.","zh":"纖維使用可能包括製作繩、籃子、蓆或家居工具。"},{"en":"If forest fires reduce fibre use, families may lose materials for daily objects.","zh":"如果森林火災減少纖維使用，家庭可能失去日常物件材料。"},{"en":"The phrase measures practical use of plant fibre.","zh":"這個片語量度植物纖維的實際使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"change the nature of","meaning":"改變……的性質","examples":[{"en":"The fire and logging changed the nature of the caboclo diet.","zh":"火災和伐木改變了 caboclo 飲食的性質。"},{"en":"Change the nature of means alter the basic character, pattern, or quality of something.","zh":"change the nature of 指改變某事物的基本特徵、模式或質素。"},{"en":"Online learning can change the nature of homework by making research faster but distraction easier.","zh":"網上學習可以改變功課的性質，令資料搜集更快但分心更容易。"},{"en":"If forest food disappears, the nature of household meals may change from diverse to limited.","zh":"如果森林食物消失，家庭膳食的性質可能由多樣變得有限。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a deep change, not a small detail.","zh":"這個片語指深層改變，而不是小細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"household diet","meaning":"家庭飲食","examples":[{"en":"The fire affected the household diet of the caboclos.","zh":"火災影響了 caboclos 的家庭飲食。"},{"en":"Household diet means the food normally eaten by a family or household.","zh":"household diet 指一個家庭或住戶通常食用的食物。"},{"en":"A household diet may change when food prices rise or a family moves to a new city.","zh":"當食物價格上升或家庭搬到新城市，家庭飲食可能改變。"},{"en":"If forest fruit and game decline, the household diet may become less varied and less nutritious.","zh":"如果森林水果和野味減少，家庭飲食可能變得較少變化和較少營養。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on food at the family level.","zh":"這個片語集中於家庭層面的食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be fortunate if","meaning":"如果能……已算幸運","examples":[{"en":"Some families were fortunate if they ate game a few times a year.","zh":"有些家庭如果一年能吃幾次野味，已算幸運。"},{"en":"Be fortunate if means be lucky even to have or experience a small amount of something.","zh":"be fortunate if 指即使只有少量得到或經歷某事，也已經算幸運。"},{"en":"During a busy exam week, a student may be fortunate if they get eight hours of sleep once.","zh":"在繁忙考試週，學生如果有一次睡滿八小時，已算幸運。"},{"en":"If families are fortunate just to eat game a few times a year, forest food has become scarce.","zh":"如果家庭一年能吃幾次野味已算幸運，森林食物就是變得稀少。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the situation is difficult and limited.","zh":"這個片語顯示情況困難而有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the loss of certain species","meaning":"某些物種的流失","examples":[{"en":"The loss of certain species of tree was especially significant.","zh":"某些樹種的流失尤其重要。"},{"en":"The loss of certain species means particular types of plants or animals have disappeared or declined.","zh":"loss of certain species 指特定類型的植物或動物消失或減少。"},{"en":"The loss of certain bee species can reduce pollination in farms and gardens.","zh":"某些蜜蜂物種的流失可以減少農田和花園中的授粉。"},{"en":"If key fruit-tree species are lost, food, wildlife, and income may all be affected.","zh":"如果關鍵果樹物種流失，食物、野生動物和收入都可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that losing specific species can matter greatly.","zh":"這個片語強調特定物種的消失可能非常重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"especially significant","meaning":"尤其重要；尤其顯著","examples":[{"en":"The loss of certain tree species was especially significant.","zh":"某些樹種的流失尤其重要。"},{"en":"Especially significant means particularly important or meaningful.","zh":"especially significant 指特別重要或有意義。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement in writing may be especially significant if they previously failed every essay.","zh":"如果學生以前每篇文章都不合格，其寫作進步可能尤其顯著。"},{"en":"If one tree attracts more game than others, losing it is especially significant for local diets.","zh":"如果某種樹比其他樹吸引更多獵物，失去它對本地飲食尤其重要。"},{"en":"The phrase marks one detail as more important than the rest.","zh":"這個片語把某細節標示為比其他更重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"persuade someone to","meaning":"說服某人去……","examples":[{"en":"Shanley’s team persuaded local hunters to weigh their catch.","zh":"Shanley 的團隊說服本地獵人為獵物稱重。"},{"en":"Persuade someone to means convince a person to do something by giving reasons or building trust.","zh":"persuade someone to 指透過給理由或建立信任，說服某人做某事。"},{"en":"A doctor may persuade a patient to stop smoking by explaining the health risks clearly.","zh":"醫生可能透過清楚解釋健康風險，說服病人戒煙。"},{"en":"If researchers persuade hunters to collect data, the study can become more accurate.","zh":"如果研究人員說服獵人收集數據，研究就能更準確。"},{"en":"The phrase shows successful convincing.","zh":"這個片語顯示成功說服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"local hunters","meaning":"本地獵人","examples":[{"en":"Local hunters helped the researchers collect data.","zh":"本地獵人幫助研究人員收集數據。"},{"en":"Local hunters are people from the area who catch wild animals, usually for food.","zh":"local hunters 指來自該地、通常為食物捕獵野生動物的人。"},{"en":"Local hunters may know which trees attract animals during different seasons.","zh":"本地獵人可能知道不同季節哪些樹會吸引動物。"},{"en":"If local hunters share their knowledge, researchers can better understand wildlife patterns.","zh":"如果本地獵人分享知識，研究人員就能更了解野生動物模式。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to hunters with place-based experience.","zh":"這個片語指具有地方經驗的獵人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"weigh their catch","meaning":"為獵物稱重","examples":[{"en":"The hunters agreed to weigh their catch.","zh":"獵人同意為獵物稱重。"},{"en":"Weigh their catch means measure the weight of the animals or fish they have caught.","zh":"weigh their catch 指量度他們捕獲的動物或魚的重量。"},{"en":"Fishermen may weigh their catch before selling it at the market.","zh":"漁民可能在市場出售前為捕獲的魚稱重。"},{"en":"If hunters weigh their catch, researchers can compare how much game comes from different tree areas.","zh":"如果獵人為獵物稱重，研究人員就能比較不同樹區帶來多少野味。"},{"en":"The phrase describes measuring hunted or caught animals.","zh":"這個片語描述量度捕獲動物的重量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"species of game","meaning":"獵物種類","examples":[{"en":"The hunters trapped several species of game under the trees.","zh":"獵人在樹下捕獲幾種獵物。"},{"en":"Species of game are different types of wild animals hunted for food.","zh":"species of game 指被獵取作食物的不同野生動物種類。"},{"en":"In some forests, species of game may include birds, rodents, deer, or pigs.","zh":"在一些森林中，獵物種類可能包括鳥、齧齒動物、鹿或豬。"},{"en":"If certain trees attract many species of game, they may be important for local diets.","zh":"如果某些樹吸引多種獵物，它們可能對本地飲食重要。"},{"en":"The phrase classifies hunted animals by type.","zh":"這個片語按種類分類被捕獵動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"average 232 kilogrammes","meaning":"平均達232公斤","examples":[{"en":"The game caught under piquia trees averaged 232 kilogrammes.","zh":"在 piquia 樹下捕獲的獵物平均達232公斤。"},{"en":"Average 232 kilogrammes means the typical or calculated mean weight was 232 kilogrammes.","zh":"average 232 kilogrammes 指典型重量或計算出的平均重量是232公斤。"},{"en":"If a class’s reading time averages 30 minutes a day, some students read more and some less.","zh":"如果一班的閱讀時間平均每天30分鐘，有些學生讀得更多，有些更少。"},{"en":"If game under one tree species averages 232 kilogrammes, that tree may be valuable for hunting.","zh":"如果某樹種下的獵物平均達232公斤，該樹可能對狩獵有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a measured average amount.","zh":"這個片語給出量度所得的平均數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"get a handle on","meaning":"開始掌握；開始了解","examples":[{"en":"The team was getting a handle on which trees were worth keeping.","zh":"團隊開始掌握哪些樹值得保留。"},{"en":"Get a handle on means begin to understand or control a difficult situation.","zh":"get a handle on 指開始理解或控制困難情況。"},{"en":"A student gets a handle on grammar when they can explain why an answer is wrong.","zh":"當學生能解釋答案為何錯，就開始掌握文法。"},{"en":"If researchers get a handle on tree values, they can give communities clearer advice.","zh":"如果研究人員開始掌握樹木價值，就能給社群更清楚建議。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests moving from confusion toward understanding.","zh":"這個片語暗示由混亂走向理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"worth keeping","meaning":"值得保留","examples":[{"en":"The research showed which trees were worth keeping.","zh":"研究顯示哪些樹值得保留。"},{"en":"Worth keeping means valuable enough to preserve rather than remove or sell.","zh":"worth keeping 指有足夠價值應保留，而不是移除或出售。"},{"en":"Old family letters may be worth keeping because they preserve memories.","zh":"舊家庭信件可能值得保留，因為它們保存記憶。"},{"en":"If a tree provides fruit, oil, and attracts game, it may be worth keeping.","zh":"如果一棵樹提供水果、油並吸引獵物，就可能值得保留。"},{"en":"The phrase judges value against the option of getting rid of something.","zh":"這個片語把價值與放棄某物的選項作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reasonably be sold","meaning":"可合理出售","examples":[{"en":"The study showed which trees could reasonably be sold.","zh":"研究顯示哪些樹可合理出售。"},{"en":"Reasonably be sold means be sold in a sensible and defensible way after considering value and consequences.","zh":"reasonably be sold 指在考慮價值和後果後，可以明智且合理地出售。"},{"en":"A family car can reasonably be sold if repair costs are higher than its value.","zh":"如果家庭汽車的維修費高於其價值，就可合理出售。"},{"en":"If a tree has little local food value but good timber value, selling it may be reasonable.","zh":"如果一棵樹本地食物價值低但木材價值高，出售它可能合理。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a careful, balanced decision.","zh":"這個片語暗示仔細而平衡的決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make little sense","meaning":"不太合理；意義不大","examples":[{"en":"Selling piquia trees to loggers made little sense.","zh":"把 piquia 樹賣給伐木商不太合理。"},{"en":"Make little sense means be unreasonable, unwise, or not worth doing.","zh":"make little sense 指不合理、不明智或不值得做。"},{"en":"It makes little sense to buy a monthly bus pass if you only travel twice a month.","zh":"如果一個月只乘車兩次，買月票就不太合理。"},{"en":"If a tree’s fruit and flowers provide long-term value, selling it for timber may make little sense.","zh":"如果一棵樹的水果和花提供長期價值，把它賣作木材可能意義不大。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses practical disagreement.","zh":"這個片語表達實際上的不同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"local value lies in","meaning":"本地價值在於……","examples":[{"en":"The local value of piquia trees lies in their fruit and flowers.","zh":"piquia 樹的本地價值在於其水果和花。"},{"en":"Local value lies in means the main value for local people comes from a particular feature or use.","zh":"local value lies in 指對本地人而言，主要價值來自某特徵或用途。"},{"en":"The local value of a community centre lies in the support it gives elderly residents.","zh":"社區中心的本地價值在於它給予長者的支援。"},{"en":"If a tree’s local value lies in fruit and game, timber price does not tell the whole story.","zh":"如果一棵樹的本地價值在於水果和野味，木材價格就不能說明全部情況。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where the real local benefit is found.","zh":"這個片語指出真正本地好處在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"prized fruit","meaning":"珍貴水果；備受重視的果實","examples":[{"en":"Piquia trees provide a prized fruit.","zh":"piquia 樹提供一種珍貴水果。"},{"en":"Prized fruit means fruit that is highly valued, liked, or sought after.","zh":"prized fruit 指受到高度重視、喜愛或追求的果實。"},{"en":"A farmer may protect a tree that produces prized fruit every summer.","zh":"農民可能保護每年夏天結出珍貴水果的樹。"},{"en":"If a fruit is prized by local families, cutting the tree removes more than wood.","zh":"如果水果深受本地家庭珍視，砍掉該樹就不只是移除木材。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the fruit has special value.","zh":"這個片語顯示水果有特殊價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"以及；除了……之外也","examples":[{"en":"The trees provide fruit as well as flowers that attract game.","zh":"這些樹提供水果，也提供吸引獵物的花。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to something else.","zh":"as well as 指除了某事之外，也有另一事。"},{"en":"A good library offers quiet study space as well as books.","zh":"好圖書館除了書本之外，也提供安靜自修空間。"},{"en":"If trees provide fruit as well as attract game, their total value is higher than timber alone.","zh":"如果樹木既提供水果又吸引獵物，其總價值就高於木材本身。"},{"en":"The phrase adds another benefit or feature.","zh":"這個片語加入另一項好處或特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"attract more game than","meaning":"吸引比……更多獵物","examples":[{"en":"Piquia flowers attract more game than any other species.","zh":"piquia 花比任何其他物種吸引更多獵物。"},{"en":"Attract more game than means draw more hunted wild animals than another tree or place does.","zh":"attract more game than 指比另一種樹或地方吸引更多被獵取的野生動物。"},{"en":"A fruiting tree may attract more birds than a bare tree.","zh":"結果的樹可能比光禿的樹吸引更多鳥類。"},{"en":"If one species attracts more game than all others, hunters and families may depend on it heavily.","zh":"如果一個物種比所有其他物種吸引更多獵物，獵人和家庭可能高度依賴它。"},{"en":"The phrase compares how strongly different things draw wildlife.","zh":"這個片語比較不同事物吸引野生動物的程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as a result of","meaning":"由於；作為……的結果","examples":[{"en":"As a result of these studies, Shanley gave the union a more cautious answer.","zh":"由於這些研究，Shanley 給了工會一個更謹慎的答案。"},{"en":"As a result of means because of something that happened or was discovered.","zh":"as a result of 指因為某事發生或被發現。"},{"en":"As a result of regular practice, a student may become more confident in speaking.","zh":"由於定期練習，學生可能在說話方面變得更自信。"},{"en":"If research shows mixed evidence, the answer may become more cautious as a result.","zh":"如果研究顯示證據複雜，答案可能因此變得更謹慎。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly links cause and effect.","zh":"這個片語清楚連接原因和結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"apply wholesale to","meaning":"全盤套用於……","examples":[{"en":"The Nature thesis could not be applied wholesale to the Rio Capim community.","zh":"Nature 論文的觀點不能全盤套用於 Rio Capim 社群。"},{"en":"Apply wholesale to means use an idea completely in a new situation without adjusting it.","zh":"apply wholesale to 指把一個想法完全用於新情況，而不作調整。"},{"en":"A teaching method from one school should not be applied wholesale to another school with different students.","zh":"一所學校的教學方法不應全盤套用於學生不同的另一所學校。"},{"en":"If local conditions differ, a general theory may fail when applied wholesale.","zh":"如果本地條件不同，通用理論被全盤套用時可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against copying an idea without adaptation.","zh":"這個片語提醒不要不加調整地複製想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"harvest non-timber forest products","meaning":"採集非木材森林產品","examples":[{"en":"Harvesting non-timber forest products did not always bring more income than timber sales.","zh":"採集非木材森林產品並不總是比木材銷售帶來更多收入。"},{"en":"Harvest non-timber forest products means collect forest goods other than wood, such as fruit, fibres, oils, or medicines.","zh":"harvest non-timber forest products 指收集木材以外的森林產品，例如水果、纖維、油或藥物。"},{"en":"A village may harvest non-timber forest products to earn money while keeping trees alive.","zh":"村莊可能採集非木材森林產品，以在保留樹木的同時賺錢。"},{"en":"If harvests are irregular or markets are far away, these products may not provide stable income.","zh":"如果收成不規律或市場很遠，這些產品可能無法提供穩定收入。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using forests without mainly cutting trees for timber.","zh":"這個片語描述使用森林，但不主要砍樹取木。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"yield more than","meaning":"帶來比……更多收益","examples":[{"en":"Forest products would not always yield more than timber sales.","zh":"森林產品並不總是比木材銷售帶來更多收益。"},{"en":"Yield more than means produce greater income, quantity, or benefit than something else.","zh":"yield more than 指產生比另一事物更多收入、數量或好處。"},{"en":"A part-time job may yield more than expected if it leads to useful contacts.","zh":"如果兼職帶來有用人脈，它可能比預期帶來更多收益。"},{"en":"If fruit sales do not yield more than timber sales, conservation still may matter for food and medicine.","zh":"如果水果銷售不比木材銷售收益更高，保育對食物和藥物仍可能重要。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the results produced by two options.","zh":"這個片語比較兩個選項產生的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"timber sales","meaning":"木材銷售","examples":[{"en":"Harvesting fruit did not always yield more than timber sales.","zh":"採集水果並不總是比木材銷售帶來更多收益。"},{"en":"Timber sales are transactions in which wood or trees are sold for commercial use.","zh":"timber sales 指把木材或樹木出售作商業用途的交易。"},{"en":"Timber sales may bring quick money to a village, but the trees are gone afterwards.","zh":"木材銷售可能為村莊帶來快錢，但之後樹木就消失了。"},{"en":"If timber sales are compared only with fruit income, subsistence uses may be ignored.","zh":"如果木材銷售只與水果收入比較，自給用途可能被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to income from selling wood.","zh":"這個片語指出售木材所得收入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"fruiting patterns","meaning":"結果模式；結果規律","examples":[{"en":"The fruiting patterns of some trees were unpredictable.","zh":"某些樹的結果模式難以預測。"},{"en":"Fruiting patterns are the regular or irregular ways trees produce fruit over time.","zh":"fruiting patterns 指樹木隨時間產生果實的規律或不規律方式。"},{"en":"Farmers study fruiting patterns to know which months are best for harvest.","zh":"農民研究結果規律，以知道哪些月份最適合收成。"},{"en":"If fruiting patterns change from year to year, income from fruit may be unreliable.","zh":"如果結果模式年年改變，水果收入可能不可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how fruit production behaves over time.","zh":"這個片語描述水果生產隨時間如何表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unpredictable","meaning":"難以預測","examples":[{"en":"The fruiting patterns of uxi trees were unpredictable.","zh":"uxi 樹的結果模式難以預測。"},{"en":"Unpredictable means difficult or impossible to know in advance.","zh":"unpredictable 指難以或無法事先知道。"},{"en":"A bus service is unpredictable if it arrives early one day and very late the next.","zh":"如果巴士今天早到、明天很遲到，服務就是難以預測。"},{"en":"If fruit production is unpredictable, families cannot depend on it as a steady source of income.","zh":"如果水果產量難以預測，家庭就不能把它當成穩定收入來源。"},{"en":"The word describes uncertainty about future results.","zh":"這個詞描述對未來結果的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"none at all","meaning":"完全沒有","examples":[{"en":"One household collected many uxi fruits one year and none at all the next.","zh":"一個家庭某年收集很多 uxi 水果，翌年卻完全沒有。"},{"en":"None at all means not any amount, not even a small amount.","zh":"none at all 指沒有任何數量，連少量也沒有。"},{"en":"A student may have many homework tasks one week and none at all during a holiday.","zh":"學生某星期可能有很多功課，假期期間卻完全沒有。"},{"en":"If one year produces fruit and the next produces none at all, planning income becomes difficult.","zh":"如果一年有水果、下一年完全沒有，規劃收入就變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly emphasises zero.","zh":"這個片語強烈強調零。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"This is not to say that","meaning":"這並不是說……","examples":[{"en":"This is not to say that wild fruit trees were unimportant.","zh":"這並不是說野生果樹不重要。"},{"en":"This is not to say that means the writer wants to prevent a possible misunderstanding.","zh":"This is not to say that 指作者想防止可能的誤解。"},{"en":"This is not to say that homework is useless; rather, it should be meaningful and manageable.","zh":"這並不是說功課沒有用；相反，它應該有意義且可應付。"},{"en":"If a study questions commercial value, this does not mean the resource has no value at all.","zh":"如果研究質疑商業價值，這並不代表該資源完全沒有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase corrects an over-simple interpretation.","zh":"這個片語修正過於簡化的理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"on the contrary","meaning":"相反","examples":[{"en":"On the contrary, wild fruit trees were critical for subsistence.","zh":"相反，野生果樹對維持生計至關重要。"},{"en":"On the contrary means the opposite is true.","zh":"on the contrary 指事實正好相反。"},{"en":"Some people think quiet students are careless; on the contrary, they may be listening very carefully.","zh":"有些人認為安靜學生不在意；相反，他們可能正在非常仔細聆聽。"},{"en":"If fruit trees do not always bring high cash income, on the contrary they may still be vital for daily survival.","zh":"如果果樹不一定帶來高現金收入，相反，它們仍可能對日常生存很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a strong correction or opposite point.","zh":"這個片語引出強烈修正或相反觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"critical for subsistence","meaning":"對維持生計至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Wild fruit trees were critical for subsistence.","zh":"野生果樹對維持生計至關重要。"},{"en":"Critical for subsistence means essential for basic survival and daily living.","zh":"critical for subsistence 指對基本生存和日常生活必不可少。"},{"en":"Clean water is critical for subsistence in any village or city.","zh":"清潔食水對任何村莊或城市維持生計都至關重要。"},{"en":"If fruit trees provide food during hard seasons, they are critical for subsistence even without high market value.","zh":"如果果樹在困難季節提供食物，即使市場價值不高，也對維持生計至關重要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses survival value rather than commercial profit.","zh":"這個片語強調生存價值，而不是商業利潤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"current research on","meaning":"關於……的現有研究","examples":[{"en":"Current research on non-timber forest products often ignores subsistence value.","zh":"關於非木材森林產品的現有研究常忽視自給價值。"},{"en":"Current research on something means studies being done or discussed at the present time.","zh":"current research on something 指目前正在進行或討論的研究。"},{"en":"Current research on sleep shows that teenagers often need more rest than schools allow.","zh":"關於睡眠的現有研究顯示，青少年通常需要比學校時間表容許更多休息。"},{"en":"If current research focuses only on sales, it may miss how people use resources at home.","zh":"如果現有研究只集中於銷售，可能錯過人們在家中如何使用資源。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to present-day academic or scientific study.","zh":"這個片語指當前學術或科學研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"tend to focus on","meaning":"往往聚焦於……","examples":[{"en":"Research tends to focus on commercial potential.","zh":"研究往往聚焦於商業潛力。"},{"en":"Tend to focus on means usually give most attention to something.","zh":"tend to focus on 指通常把大部分注意力放在某事上。"},{"en":"Students tend to focus on marks, but feedback may be more useful for improvement.","zh":"學生往往聚焦於分數，但回饋可能對進步更有用。"},{"en":"If researchers focus mainly on commercial potential, they may overlook household survival needs.","zh":"如果研究人員主要聚焦於商業潛力，可能忽略家庭生存需要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common pattern of attention.","zh":"這個片語描述常見的注意力模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"commercial potential","meaning":"商業潛力","examples":[{"en":"Much research focuses on the commercial potential of forest products.","zh":"許多研究集中於森林產品的商業潛力。"},{"en":"Commercial potential is the possibility that something can be sold profitably.","zh":"commercial potential 指某物能被有利可圖地出售的可能性。"},{"en":"A new app has commercial potential if many people are willing to pay for it.","zh":"如果很多人願意付費，新應用程式就有商業潛力。"},{"en":"If a forest product has commercial potential but is hard to transport, profit may still be limited.","zh":"如果森林產品有商業潛力但難以運輸，利潤仍可能有限。"},{"en":"The phrase measures possible market value.","zh":"這個片語量度可能的市場價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"geography was another factor","meaning":"地理位置是另一個因素","examples":[{"en":"Geography was another factor preventing serious trade in wild fruit.","zh":"地理位置是阻礙野生水果穩定買賣的另一個因素。"},{"en":"Geography was another factor means location, distance, or physical landscape also affected the outcome.","zh":"geography was another factor 指位置、距離或自然地形也影響結果。"},{"en":"Geography is another factor when a student lives far from good schools.","zh":"當學生住得離好學校很遠，地理位置就是另一個因素。"},{"en":"If villages are remote, geography can limit access to markets even when products are valuable.","zh":"如果村莊偏遠，即使產品有價值，地理位置也會限制進入市場的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase adds place and distance as an explanation.","zh":"這個片語加入地方和距離作為解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"prevent someone from doing something","meaning":"阻止某人做某事","examples":[{"en":"Geography prevented the caboclos from establishing a serious trade in wild fruit.","zh":"地理位置阻止 caboclos 建立穩定野生水果買賣。"},{"en":"Prevent someone from doing something means stop someone from doing it or make it impossible.","zh":"prevent someone from doing something 指阻止某人做某事，或令其無法做到。"},{"en":"Heavy rain may prevent students from arriving at school on time.","zh":"大雨可能阻止學生準時到校。"},{"en":"If distance prevents villagers from reaching markets, valuable fruit may remain unsold.","zh":"如果距離阻止村民到達市場，有價值水果可能仍賣不出去。"},{"en":"The phrase shows an obstacle blocking an action.","zh":"這個片語顯示障礙阻擋某行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"establish a serious trade in","meaning":"建立穩定的……買賣","examples":[{"en":"The caboclos struggled to establish a serious trade in wild fruit.","zh":"caboclos 難以建立穩定的野生水果買賣。"},{"en":"Establish a serious trade in something means build a stable and meaningful business of selling it.","zh":"establish a serious trade in something 指建立穩定而有實質意義的銷售業務。"},{"en":"A village may establish a serious trade in handmade baskets if transport and buyers are reliable.","zh":"如果交通和買家可靠，村莊可能建立穩定的手工籃子買賣。"},{"en":"If markets are far away, establishing a serious trade in forest products becomes difficult.","zh":"如果市場很遠，建立穩定的森林產品買賣就變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests organised, regular trade rather than occasional selling.","zh":"這個片語暗示有組織、定期的貿易，而不是偶然出售。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"remote areas","meaning":"偏遠地區","examples":[{"en":"Villagers in remote areas could not compete with communities near urban markets.","zh":"偏遠地區的村民無法與靠近城市市場的社群競爭。"},{"en":"Remote areas are places far from cities, transport links, or major services.","zh":"remote areas 指遠離城市、交通連接或主要服務的地方。"},{"en":"Students in remote areas may have fewer libraries, tutors, and internet options.","zh":"偏遠地區的學生可能有較少圖書館、導師和上網選擇。"},{"en":"If producers live in remote areas, transport costs can make selling goods harder.","zh":"如果生產者住在偏遠地區，運輸成本會令銷售貨物更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights distance and limited access.","zh":"這個片語突出距離和有限取得機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"compete with","meaning":"與……競爭","examples":[{"en":"Remote villagers could not compete with communities close to urban markets.","zh":"偏遠村民無法與靠近城市市場的社群競爭。"},{"en":"Compete with means try to do better than another person, group, or business in the same area.","zh":"compete with 指在同一範疇中嘗試比另一人、群體或企業做得更好。"},{"en":"Small shops compete with supermarkets by offering friendlier service.","zh":"小店透過提供更友善服務與超市競爭。"},{"en":"If remote villagers must compete with sellers near cities, transport costs may put them at a disadvantage.","zh":"如果偏遠村民必須與城市附近賣家競爭，運輸成本可能令他們處於劣勢。"},{"en":"The phrase shows rivalry for customers, resources, marks, or success.","zh":"這個片語顯示為顧客、資源、分數或成功而競爭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"urban markets","meaning":"城市市場","examples":[{"en":"Communities near urban markets had an advantage in selling forest products.","zh":"靠近城市市場的社群在出售森林產品方面有優勢。"},{"en":"Urban markets are places in towns or cities where goods are bought and sold.","zh":"urban markets 指城鎮或城市中買賣貨物的地方。"},{"en":"Farmers living near urban markets can often sell fresh produce more quickly.","zh":"住近城市市場的農民通常可以更快出售新鮮農產品。"},{"en":"If villagers are far from urban markets, fruit may spoil before it reaches buyers.","zh":"如果村民遠離城市市場，水果可能在到達買家前變壞。"},{"en":"The phrase connects trade with city-based demand.","zh":"這個片語把貿易與城市需求連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"passing river boats","meaning":"路過的河船","examples":[{"en":"The villagers could sell wild fruit to passing river boats.","zh":"村民可以把野生水果賣給路過的河船。"},{"en":"Passing river boats are boats travelling along a river that happen to pass a village or area.","zh":"passing river boats 指沿河行駛、剛好經過村莊或地區的船隻。"},{"en":"A riverside shop may sell drinks and food to passing river boats.","zh":"河邊小店可能向路過的河船出售飲品和食物。"},{"en":"If villagers rely only on passing boats, their trade may be irregular and limited.","zh":"如果村民只依賴路過船隻，貿易可能不規律且有限。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests occasional contact rather than a stable market.","zh":"這個片語暗示偶然接觸，而不是穩定市場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"do more than just","meaning":"不只是……","examples":[{"en":"Shanley and her colleagues decided to do more than just report their results.","zh":"Shanley 和同事決定不只是報告結果。"},{"en":"Do more than just means go beyond a basic or expected action.","zh":"do more than just 指超越基本或預期行動。"},{"en":"A teacher can do more than just mark essays by explaining how students can improve.","zh":"老師可以不只是批改文章，而是解釋學生如何改善。"},{"en":"If researchers do more than just publish findings, their work may directly help communities.","zh":"如果研究人員不只是發表研究結果，其工作可能直接幫助社群。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses extra practical effort.","zh":"這個片語強調額外的實際努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"report results to","meaning":"向……報告結果","examples":[{"en":"The researchers reported their results to the union.","zh":"研究人員向工會報告結果。"},{"en":"Report results to means tell a person or group what a study, test, or investigation found.","zh":"report results to 指把研究、測試或調查所得告訴某人或某群體。"},{"en":"A doctor may report test results to a patient and explain what they mean.","zh":"醫生可能向病人報告測試結果，並解釋其意思。"},{"en":"If researchers report results clearly to local people, the findings become usable.","zh":"如果研究人員清楚向本地人報告結果，研究發現就變得可用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sharing findings with a relevant audience.","zh":"這個片語描述與相關受眾分享發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"research colleagues","meaning":"研究同事","examples":[{"en":"Shanley wrote the fruit book with two research colleagues.","zh":"Shanley 與兩位研究同事一起寫了水果書。"},{"en":"Research colleagues are people who work together on the same research project or field.","zh":"research colleagues 指在同一研究項目或領域中一起工作的人。"},{"en":"A scientist may discuss data with research colleagues before publishing a paper.","zh":"科學家可能在發表論文前與研究同事討論數據。"},{"en":"If research colleagues have different skills, the final work may become stronger.","zh":"如果研究同事有不同技能，最終作品可能更強。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to professional partners in research.","zh":"這個片語指研究中的專業夥伴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a publication on","meaning":"關於……的出版物","examples":[{"en":"Shanley also co-authored a publication on medicinal plants.","zh":"Shanley 也合著了一本關於藥用植物的出版物。"},{"en":"A publication on something is a printed or digital work about that topic.","zh":"publication on something 指關於某主題的印刷或數碼作品。"},{"en":"A school may produce a publication on student mental health for parents.","zh":"學校可能為家長製作一份關於學生心理健康的出版物。"},{"en":"If a publication on medicinal plants uses simple language, local families can apply the information.","zh":"如果關於藥用植物的出版物使用簡單語言，本地家庭就能應用資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the subject of a written work.","zh":"這個片語指出書面作品的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"co-authored by","meaning":"由……合著","examples":[{"en":"The publication on medicinal plants was co-authored by Shanley.","zh":"關於藥用植物的出版物由 Shanley 合著。"},{"en":"Co-authored by means written together with one or more other authors.","zh":"co-authored by 指由某人與一位或多位其他作者共同撰寫。"},{"en":"A research article may be co-authored by a teacher, a doctor, and a university professor.","zh":"研究文章可能由老師、醫生和大學教授合著。"},{"en":"If a book is co-authored, it may combine different knowledge and experience.","zh":"如果一本書由多人合著，它可能結合不同知識和經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies one of the people who helped write a work.","zh":"這個片語指出協助撰寫作品的人之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"minimal literacy skills","meaning":"最基本的讀寫能力","examples":[{"en":"The publication was designed for people with minimal literacy skills.","zh":"該出版物是為只有最基本讀寫能力的人設計的。"},{"en":"Minimal literacy skills means very basic ability to read and write.","zh":"minimal literacy skills 指非常基本的讀寫能力。"},{"en":"A public health poster for people with minimal literacy skills should use pictures and simple words.","zh":"給讀寫能力很低的人看的公共健康海報，應使用圖片和簡單字詞。"},{"en":"If readers have minimal literacy skills, long technical reports may be useless to them.","zh":"如果讀者只有最基本讀寫能力，長篇技術報告對他們可能沒有用。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the need for accessible communication.","zh":"這個片語強調可理解溝通的需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"along this stretch of","meaning":"沿着……這一段","examples":[{"en":"There were very few books along this stretch of the Rio Capim.","zh":"沿着 Rio Capim 這一段，書籍非常少。"},{"en":"Along this stretch of means along this particular part of a river, road, coast, or area.","zh":"along this stretch of 指沿着河流、道路、海岸或地區的某一特定部分。"},{"en":"There are several small cafés along this stretch of the road near the school.","zh":"沿着學校附近這一段路，有幾間小咖啡店。"},{"en":"If few books exist along a remote stretch of river, a picture book may become very important.","zh":"如果偏遠河段沿岸書籍很少，圖畫書可能變得非常重要。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies one section of a longer place.","zh":"這個片語指出較長地方中的某一段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"print run","meaning":"印刷量","examples":[{"en":"The first print run comprised only 3,000 copies.","zh":"第一次印刷量只有3,000本。"},{"en":"A print run is the number of copies of a book or publication printed at one time.","zh":"print run 指一本書或出版物一次印刷的份數。"},{"en":"A school magazine may have a print run of 500 copies if only students and parents receive it.","zh":"如果學校雜誌只給學生和家長，印刷量可能是500本。"},{"en":"If the first print run sells out quickly, a second edition may be needed.","zh":"如果首次印刷很快售罄，就可能需要第二版。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the size of one printing.","zh":"這個片語指一次印刷的規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"comprise","meaning":"包括；數量為","examples":[{"en":"The first print run comprised only 3,000 copies.","zh":"第一次印刷量只有3,000本。"},{"en":"Comprise means consist of, contain, or be made up of.","zh":"comprise 指由……組成、包含或包括。"},{"en":"A good revision plan may comprise reading, practice questions, and error correction.","zh":"良好溫習計劃可以包括閱讀、練習題和錯誤修正。"},{"en":"If a book’s first print run comprises only a few copies, access may be limited.","zh":"如果一本書首次印刷量只有少數本，取得機會可能有限。"},{"en":"The word introduces what something includes.","zh":"這個詞引出某事物包含甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"remarkably influential","meaning":"影響力相當大","examples":[{"en":"The fruit book has been remarkably influential.","zh":"這本水果書影響力相當大。"},{"en":"Remarkably influential means having a surprisingly strong effect on people, decisions, or later work.","zh":"remarkably influential 指對人、決定或後來工作有出乎意料強大的影響。"},{"en":"A simple school poster can be remarkably influential if it changes how students treat one another.","zh":"如果一張簡單學校海報改變學生如何對待彼此，它可以影響力相當大。"},{"en":"If a small print-run book affects colleges, unions, and industries, its influence is remarkable.","zh":"如果一本印量小的書影響學院、工會和產業，其影響就很顯著。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses influence greater than expected.","zh":"這個片語強調比預期更大的影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"peasant unions","meaning":"農民工會","examples":[{"en":"The book is used by colleges, industries and peasant unions.","zh":"這本書被學院、產業和農民工會使用。"},{"en":"Peasant unions are organisations that represent small farmers and rural workers.","zh":"peasant unions 指代表小農和農村工人的組織。"},{"en":"Peasant unions may help members understand land rights, prices, and company contracts.","zh":"農民工會可能幫助成員理解土地權利、價格和公司合約。"},{"en":"If peasant unions use a book, the information can reach many rural families.","zh":"如果農民工會使用一本書，資訊就可以到達許多農村家庭。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to collective organisations for poorer rural farmers.","zh":"這個片語指為較貧困農民而設的集體組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"largely due to the fact that","meaning":"主要由於……","examples":[{"en":"The book’s success is largely due to the fact that people with poor literacy skills can understand it.","zh":"這本書成功主要由於讀寫能力較低的人也能理解它。"},{"en":"Largely due to the fact that means mainly because of the reason that follows.","zh":"largely due to the fact that 指主要因為後面所說的原因。"},{"en":"A student’s progress may be largely due to the fact that they practise a little every day.","zh":"學生進步可能主要由於他每天練習一點。"},{"en":"If a book succeeds largely because it is easy to understand, accessibility is its key strength.","zh":"如果一本書成功主要因為易懂，可讀性就是其關鍵優勢。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the main reason for a result.","zh":"這個片語引出結果的主要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"poor literacy skills","meaning":"讀寫能力較低","examples":[{"en":"People with poor literacy skills can understand much of the book.","zh":"讀寫能力較低的人也能理解這本書的大部分內容。"},{"en":"Poor literacy skills means limited ability to read, write, and understand written information.","zh":"poor literacy skills 指閱讀、寫作和理解書面資訊的能力有限。"},{"en":"A person with poor literacy skills may struggle with forms, contracts, and medicine labels.","zh":"讀寫能力較低的人可能難以處理表格、合約和藥物標籤。"},{"en":"If a community has poor literacy skills, pictures and stories can make information more usable.","zh":"如果社群讀寫能力較低，圖片和故事可以令資訊更易使用。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on reading and writing difficulty.","zh":"這個片語集中於閱讀和寫作困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contain information about","meaning":"包含關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"The book contains information about non-timber forest products.","zh":"這本書包含關於非木材森林產品的資料。"},{"en":"Contain information about means include facts, explanations, or details on a topic.","zh":"contain information about 指包括某主題的事實、解釋或細節。"},{"en":"A school handbook contains information about rules, holidays, and emergency contacts.","zh":"學校手冊包含關於規則、假期和緊急聯絡人的資料。"},{"en":"If a book contains information about useful plants, readers can make better decisions in daily life.","zh":"如果一本書包含關於有用植物的資料，讀者可以在日常生活中作出更好決定。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what knowledge is inside a text.","zh":"這個片語指出文本內有甚麼知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"thanks to","meaning":"多虧；由於","examples":[{"en":"The book is easy to understand thanks to its illustrations and stories.","zh":"多虧插圖和故事，這本書容易理解。"},{"en":"Thanks to means because of something helpful or positive.","zh":"thanks to 指由於某件有幫助或正面的事。"},{"en":"Thanks to clear examples, students can understand difficult phrases more quickly.","zh":"多虧清楚例子，學生可以更快理解困難片語。"},{"en":"If a book succeeds thanks to pictures, design is part of its educational power.","zh":"如果一本書多虧圖片而成功，設計就是其教育力量的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a helpful cause.","zh":"這個片語引出有幫助的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"illustrations","meaning":"插圖","examples":[{"en":"The illustrations help readers understand the information.","zh":"插圖幫助讀者理解資料。"},{"en":"Illustrations are pictures, drawings, or images used to explain or decorate a text.","zh":"illustrations 指用來解釋或裝飾文本的圖片、繪圖或圖像。"},{"en":"A science textbook uses illustrations to show parts of a plant or human body.","zh":"科學教科書使用插圖展示植物或人體部位。"},{"en":"If readers have low literacy skills, illustrations can carry meaning that words alone cannot.","zh":"如果讀者讀寫能力較低，插圖可以承載單靠文字不能傳達的意思。"},{"en":"The word refers to visual support in a book or document.","zh":"這個詞指書本或文件中的視覺支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"anecdotes","meaning":"軼事；小故事","examples":[{"en":"The book uses anecdotes to explain scientific information.","zh":"這本書使用小故事來解釋科學資訊。"},{"en":"Anecdotes are short personal stories used to illustrate a point.","zh":"anecdotes 指用來說明一個重點的短小個人故事。"},{"en":"A teacher may use anecdotes from former students to explain why revision habits matter.","zh":"老師可能使用舊生小故事，解釋溫習習慣為何重要。"},{"en":"If scientific information is supported by anecdotes, readers may remember it more easily.","zh":"如果科學資訊有小故事支持，讀者可能更容易記住。"},{"en":"The word refers to small stories that make ideas more concrete.","zh":"這個詞指令想法更具體的小故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"tell people what to do","meaning":"告訴人們該怎樣做","examples":[{"en":"The book does not tell people what to do.","zh":"這本書沒有告訴人們該怎樣做。"},{"en":"Tell people what to do means give direct instructions or orders about their actions.","zh":"tell people what to do 指直接指示或命令人們如何行動。"},{"en":"A good adviser may explain choices instead of simply telling people what to do.","zh":"好顧問可能解釋選擇，而不是只告訴人們該怎樣做。"},{"en":"If a book only tells people what to do, readers may feel controlled rather than informed.","zh":"如果一本書只告訴人們該怎樣做，讀者可能感到被控制，而不是被告知。"},{"en":"The phrase can sound controlling depending on context.","zh":"這個片語視乎語境可能帶控制意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"provide someone with choices","meaning":"為某人提供選擇","examples":[{"en":"The book provides local people with choices.","zh":"這本書為本地人提供選擇。"},{"en":"Provide someone with choices means give people information or options so they can decide for themselves.","zh":"provide someone with choices 指給人資訊或選項，讓他們自行決定。"},{"en":"A careers teacher provides students with choices by explaining several study paths.","zh":"升學就業老師透過解釋幾條學習路徑，為學生提供選擇。"},{"en":"If villagers understand different tree values, they have choices instead of accepting the first offer.","zh":"如果村民了解不同樹木價值，他們就有選擇，而不是接受第一個出價。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses empowerment through options.","zh":"這個片語強調透過選項賦權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a much better understanding of","meaning":"對……有更深入了解","examples":[{"en":"The caboclos now have a much better understanding of which trees to protect.","zh":"caboclos 現在對哪些樹要保護有更深入了解。"},{"en":"A much better understanding of means a clearer, deeper, or more accurate grasp of something than before.","zh":"much better understanding of 指比以前更清楚、更深入或更準確地掌握某事。"},{"en":"After feedback, a student may have a much better understanding of how to organise an essay.","zh":"收到回饋後，學生可能對如何組織文章有更深入了解。"},{"en":"If villagers gain a better understanding of tree values, they can protect resources more wisely.","zh":"如果村民對樹木價值有更深入了解，就能更明智地保護資源。"},{"en":"The phrase shows improvement in knowledge.","zh":"這個片語顯示知識上的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"protect trees","meaning":"保護樹木","examples":[{"en":"The book helps people decide which trees to protect.","zh":"這本書幫助人們決定哪些樹木要保護。"},{"en":"Protect trees means keep trees safe from cutting, damage, fire, or misuse.","zh":"protect trees 指保護樹木免受砍伐、破壞、火災或誤用。"},{"en":"A school may protect trees on campus by building paths around their roots.","zh":"學校可能透過在樹根周圍修建小路來保護校園樹木。"},{"en":"If villagers protect fruit trees, they may preserve food, wildlife, and future income.","zh":"如果村民保護果樹，就可能保存食物、野生動物和未來收入。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on keeping valuable trees alive and useful.","zh":"這個片語集中於令有價值樹木存活並繼續有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reading passage","meaning":"閱讀篇章","examples":[{"en":"Reading Passage 3 has nine paragraphs.","zh":"閱讀篇章三共有九段。"},{"en":"A reading passage is a text that students read in an exam or lesson to answer questions.","zh":"reading passage 指學生在考試或課堂中閱讀並回答問題的文本。"},{"en":"Students should skim the reading passage first to understand the general topic.","zh":"學生應先略讀閱讀篇章，以理解大致主題。"},{"en":"If a reading passage has many details, students need to locate evidence carefully.","zh":"如果閱讀篇章有許多細節，學生需要小心定位證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the source text used for reading tasks.","zh":"這個片語指閱讀題使用的來源文本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"contain the following information","meaning":"包含以下資料","examples":[{"en":"Students must decide which paragraph contains the following information.","zh":"學生必須判斷哪一段包含以下資料。"},{"en":"Contain the following information means include the specific details listed in the question.","zh":"contain the following information 指包括題目列出的特定細節。"},{"en":"A paragraph may contain the following information even if it uses different words from the question.","zh":"即使段落使用與題目不同的字詞，也可能包含以下資料。"},{"en":"If students search only for identical wording, they may miss a paraphrased answer.","zh":"如果學生只尋找完全相同措辭，可能錯過改寫後的答案。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in paragraph-matching questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於段落配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"write the correct letter","meaning":"寫下正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students write the correct letter in the answer box.","zh":"學生在答題格內寫下正確字母。"},{"en":"Write the correct letter means put the option letter that matches the correct answer.","zh":"write the correct letter 指寫下與正確答案相符的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should write the correct letter clearly and in the right box.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應清楚地在正確方格寫下正確字母。"},{"en":"If a student understands the passage but writes the wrong letter, the answer may still be marked wrong.","zh":"如果學生理解文章但寫錯字母，答案仍可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an exam-format instruction.","zh":"這個片語給出考試格式指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a description of","meaning":"對……的描述","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for a description of Shanley’s initial data collection.","zh":"題目要求找出對 Shanley 初步數據收集的描述。"},{"en":"A description of something is an explanation of what it was like, how it happened, or what it included.","zh":"description of something 指解釋某事物是怎樣、如何發生或包括甚麼。"},{"en":"A report may give a description of how students travelled to school each day.","zh":"報告可能描述學生每天如何上學。"},{"en":"If a passage gives a description of data collection, it may mention who measured what and how often.","zh":"如果文章描述數據收集，可能提到誰量度甚麼以及多久一次。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for details, not just a title.","zh":"這個片語要求細節，而不只是標題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"initial data collection","meaning":"初步數據收集","examples":[{"en":"The passage includes a description of Shanley’s initial data collection.","zh":"文章包括對 Shanley 初步數據收集的描述。"},{"en":"Initial data collection is the first stage of gathering information for a study.","zh":"initial data collection 指研究中最初收集資訊的階段。"},{"en":"A school survey’s initial data collection may involve asking students about sleep and homework.","zh":"學校調查的初步數據收集可能包括詢問學生睡眠和功課情況。"},{"en":"If initial data collection is careful, later analysis becomes more reliable.","zh":"如果初步數據收集仔細，後來分析就更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the beginning of research evidence-gathering.","zh":"這個片語指研究證據收集的開端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"government official","meaning":"政府官員","examples":[{"en":"A government official contributed to the book.","zh":"一名政府官員為該書作出貢獻。"},{"en":"A government official is a person who works for the government and has official duties.","zh":"government official 指在政府工作並有官方職責的人。"},{"en":"A government official may approve a public project, write a policy, or speak at a community meeting.","zh":"政府官員可能批准公共項目、撰寫政策或在社區會議發言。"},{"en":"If a government official supports a book, it may reach more public institutions.","zh":"如果政府官員支持一本書，它可能接觸到更多公共機構。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies someone with a formal role in government.","zh":"這個片語指出在政府中有正式角色的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"contribute to the book","meaning":"為該書作出貢獻","examples":[{"en":"The question asks why a government official contributed to the book.","zh":"題目問為何一名政府官員為該書作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Contribute to the book means add something to the book, such as writing, knowledge, support, or approval.","zh":"contribute to the book 指為書本加入某些東西，例如文字、知識、支持或認可。"},{"en":"A doctor may contribute to a health book by checking whether the advice is safe.","zh":"醫生可能透過檢查建議是否安全，為健康書作出貢獻。"},{"en":"If an environment minister writes the foreword, she contributes authority and public support to the book.","zh":"如果環境部長撰寫前言，她就是為該書貢獻權威和公共支持。"},{"en":"The phrase describes helping create or strengthen a publication.","zh":"這個片語描述幫助創作或強化出版物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"conduct the research","meaning":"進行研究","examples":[{"en":"The community asked Shanley to conduct the research.","zh":"社群要求 Shanley 進行研究。"},{"en":"Conduct the research means carry out a study in an organised and systematic way.","zh":"conduct the research 指以有組織和系統方式進行研究。"},{"en":"A university team may conduct research into how students learn vocabulary best.","zh":"大學團隊可能研究學生如何最有效學習詞彙。"},{"en":"If a community asks someone to conduct research, it wants evidence to answer a practical question.","zh":"如果社群要求某人進行研究，它想用證據回答實際問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to actually doing the study.","zh":"這個片語指實際執行研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reference to","meaning":"提及……","examples":[{"en":"One paragraph contains a reference to the starting point of the research.","zh":"其中一段提及該研究的起點。"},{"en":"Reference to means a mention of something, often briefly or indirectly.","zh":"reference to 指提到某事，通常是簡短或間接地提到。"},{"en":"A teacher may make a reference to last week’s lesson before teaching a new topic.","zh":"老師可能在教授新課題前提及上星期的課。"},{"en":"If a paragraph contains a reference to the beginning of a project, it may not describe the whole project.","zh":"如果段落提及項目的開始，它未必描述整個項目。"},{"en":"The phrase means a text points to something.","zh":"這個片語意思是文本指向某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the starting point of","meaning":"……的起點","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the starting point of Shanley’s research.","zh":"題目問 Shanley 研究的起點。"},{"en":"The starting point of something is the event, question, or situation where it begins.","zh":"starting point of something 指某事開始的事件、問題或情況。"},{"en":"A student’s starting point for an essay may be one clear question.","zh":"學生文章的起點可能是一條清楚問題。"},{"en":"If a plea for help was the starting point of research, the study was shaped by community needs.","zh":"如果求助是研究的起點，該研究就受社群需要塑造。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where a process began.","zh":"這個片語指出過程從哪裡開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"alter food consumption patterns","meaning":"改變食物消耗模式","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about factors that alter food consumption patterns.","zh":"題目問哪些因素改變食物消耗模式。"},{"en":"Alter food consumption patterns means change what people eat, how much they eat, or how often they eat it.","zh":"alter food consumption patterns 指改變人們吃甚麼、吃多少或多久吃一次。"},{"en":"Rising prices can alter food consumption patterns when families buy cheaper ingredients.","zh":"當家庭購買較便宜食材，價格上升可以改變食物消耗模式。"},{"en":"If fire reduces forest fruit and game, it can alter household diets quickly.","zh":"如果火災減少森林水果和野味，就可以快速改變家庭飲食。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on changes in eating behaviour.","zh":"這個片語集中於飲食行為的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"Complete the summary means fill in missing words in a shortened version of the main information.","zh":"complete the summary 指在主要資訊的簡短版本中填上缺失詞語。"},{"en":"In IELTS Reading, students complete the summary by matching meaning and grammar.","zh":"在 IELTS 閱讀中，學生透過配對意思和文法來完成摘要。"},{"en":"If students understand the passage structure, summary completion becomes easier.","zh":"如果學生理解文章結構，摘要填充就會更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common reading-question task.","zh":"這個片語描述常見閱讀題型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個字詞","examples":[{"en":"Students must choose no more than three words from the passage.","zh":"學生必須從文章中選擇不多於三個字詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案必須包含三個或更少英文詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “wild fruit trees”, it uses exactly three words and fits the limit.","zh":"如果答案是 “wild fruit trees”，它剛好使用三個詞，符合限制。"},{"en":"If students write four words when only three are allowed, the answer may be marked wrong.","zh":"如果只容許三個詞而學生寫四個詞，答案可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word-limit instruction.","zh":"這個片語給出嚴格字數限制指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"consume less","meaning":"消耗較少……","examples":[{"en":"Forest fires caused local villagers to consume less forest food.","zh":"森林火災令本地村民消耗較少森林食物。"},{"en":"Consume less means use, eat, or buy a smaller amount than before.","zh":"consume less 指使用、食用或購買比以前更少的量。"},{"en":"A family may consume less electricity after buying energy-efficient lights.","zh":"家庭購買節能燈後，可能消耗較少電力。"},{"en":"If villagers consume less forest food after fire, the forest has become less able to support them.","zh":"如果村民在火災後消耗較少森林食物，森林支撐他們的能力就下降了。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a reduction in use or intake.","zh":"這個片語描述使用量或攝取量減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the least amount of","meaning":"最少量的……","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to the least amount of game hunted under a tree species.","zh":"題目提到某樹種下捕獲的最少量獵物。"},{"en":"The least amount of means the smallest quantity among several options.","zh":"the least amount of 指幾個選項中最小的數量。"},{"en":"A student may spend the least amount of time on the topic they understand best.","zh":"學生可能在最熟悉的課題上花最少量時間。"},{"en":"If one tree has the least amount of game under it, it may be less important for hunting.","zh":"如果某樹下的獵物量最少，它對狩獵可能較不重要。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the minimum quantity.","zh":"這個片語指出最低數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be hunted under","meaning":"在……下被捕獲","examples":[{"en":"Game was hunted under different species of trees.","zh":"獵物在不同樹種下被捕獲。"},{"en":"Be hunted under means be caught or hunted beneath a particular tree or area.","zh":"be hunted under 指在某棵樹或某個區域下方被捕捉或獵取。"},{"en":"Birds may be hunted under fruit trees because they come to feed there.","zh":"鳥類可能在果樹下被捕獲，因為牠們會來覓食。"},{"en":"If many animals are hunted under one tree species, that tree may attract wildlife strongly.","zh":"如果很多動物在同一樹種下被捕獲，該樹可能強烈吸引野生動物。"},{"en":"The phrase links hunting location with a tree or place.","zh":"這個片語把狩獵位置與樹木或地方連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be more reasonable to","meaning":"……更合理","examples":[{"en":"The research showed that it was more reasonable to keep certain trees.","zh":"研究顯示保留某些樹木更合理。"},{"en":"Be more reasonable to means be the more sensible or fair choice after considering the evidence.","zh":"be more reasonable to 指考慮證據後是較明智或公平的選擇。"},{"en":"It may be more reasonable to repair a laptop than buy a new one if the problem is small.","zh":"如果問題很小，維修手提電腦可能比買新電腦更合理。"},{"en":"If a tree provides long-term food and game, it may be more reasonable to keep it than sell it.","zh":"如果一棵樹提供長期食物和野味，保留它可能比出售它更合理。"},{"en":"The phrase compares choices and favours the more sensible one.","zh":"這個片語比較選擇，並支持較明智的一方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"besides being sold to","meaning":"除了被賣給……之外","examples":[{"en":"The trees had local uses besides being sold to loggers.","zh":"這些樹除了被賣給伐木商之外，還有本地用途。"},{"en":"Besides being sold to means in addition to the possibility of being sold to someone.","zh":"besides being sold to 指除了可能被賣給某人之外。"},{"en":"A classroom can be used for clubs besides being used for lessons.","zh":"課室除了用於上課之外，也可以用於學會活動。"},{"en":"If trees have uses besides being sold to loggers, their value is broader than timber money.","zh":"如果樹木除了賣給伐木商之外還有其他用途，其價值就比木材金錢更廣。"},{"en":"The phrase adds another function beyond sale.","zh":"這個片語加入出售以外的另一功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be often ignored because","meaning":"常被忽視，因為……","examples":[{"en":"Subsistence value is often ignored because research focuses on commercial potential.","zh":"自給價值常被忽視，因為研究集中於商業潛力。"},{"en":"Be often ignored because means be frequently overlooked for a specific reason.","zh":"be often ignored because 指因某特定原因而經常被忽略。"},{"en":"Quiet students are often ignored because teachers notice the loudest voices first.","zh":"安靜學生常被忽視，因為老師先注意到最大聲的人。"},{"en":"If household use is ignored because researchers focus on markets, the full value of resources is missed.","zh":"如果研究人員因聚焦市場而忽視家庭使用，資源的完整價值就會被錯過。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why something important receives too little attention.","zh":"這個片語解釋重要事情為何受到太少關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the purpose of","meaning":"……的目的","examples":[{"en":"The purpose of the book was to provide useful information to local people.","zh":"這本書的目的是為本地人提供有用資訊。"},{"en":"The purpose of something is the reason it exists or the goal it is meant to achieve.","zh":"purpose of something 指某事物存在的原因或想達成的目標。"},{"en":"The purpose of a revision timetable is to help students plan study time clearly.","zh":"溫習時間表的目的是幫助學生清楚規劃學習時間。"},{"en":"If the purpose of a book is to help local people, its language and design must be accessible.","zh":"如果一本書的目的是幫助本地人，其語言和設計就必須容易理解。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main aim.","zh":"這個片語指出主要目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"provide information about","meaning":"提供關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"The book provides information about useful plants and forest products.","zh":"這本書提供關於有用植物和森林產品的資料。"},{"en":"Provide information about means give facts, explanations, or practical details on a topic.","zh":"provide information about 指提供某主題的事實、解釋或實用細節。"},{"en":"A school website provides information about uniforms, timetables, and application deadlines.","zh":"學校網站提供關於校服、時間表和申請期限的資料。"},{"en":"If a book provides information about valuable trees, villagers can make better decisions.","zh":"如果一本書提供關於有價值樹木的資料，村民就能作出更好決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes supplying knowledge on a subject.","zh":"這個片語描述提供某主題的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 28 - The Fruit Book.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 29":[{"front":"a language we all speak","meaning":"人人都懂的語言","examples":[{"en":"Music may be a language we all speak.","zh":"音樂可能是一種人人都懂的語言。"},{"en":"A language we all speak means a form of expression that many people can understand without needing translation.","zh":"a language we all speak 指一種許多人不用翻譯也能理解的表達方式。"},{"en":"A smile can feel like a language we all speak because people in many cultures understand warmth and welcome.","zh":"微笑可以像人人都懂的語言，因為許多文化中的人都明白溫暖和歡迎。"},{"en":"Music can connect strangers because rhythm and emotion may be understood even when words are not.","zh":"音樂可以連接陌生人，因為即使沒有文字，節奏和情感也可能被理解。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that something communicates across culture, age, and background.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事能跨越文化、年齡和背景來傳達意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the human species","meaning":"人類物種","examples":[{"en":"Music is one of the human species’ relatively few universal abilities.","zh":"音樂是人類物種為數不多的普遍能力之一。"},{"en":"The human species means human beings considered as one biological group.","zh":"the human species 指作為一個生物群體的人類。"},{"en":"The human species shares certain abilities, such as using symbols, learning language, and forming social bonds.","zh":"人類物種共享某些能力，例如使用符號、學習語言和建立社會連繫。"},{"en":"Studying the human species helps scientists ask what all humans have in common.","zh":"研究人類物種幫助科學家追問所有人類有甚麼共同之處。"},{"en":"The phrase is more scientific and general than simply saying “people”.","zh":"這個短語比單純說 “people” 更科學、更概括。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"relatively few universal abilities","meaning":"為數不多的普遍能力","examples":[{"en":"Music is one of the human species’ relatively few universal abilities.","zh":"音樂是人類物種為數不多的普遍能力之一。"},{"en":"Relatively few universal abilities are a small number of abilities found across almost all human groups.","zh":"relatively few universal abilities 是幾乎所有人類群體都有的一小部分能力。"},{"en":"Language learning is one of the relatively few universal abilities that appear in nearly every society.","zh":"語言學習是幾乎每個社會都出現的為數不多的普遍能力之一。"},{"en":"An ability is universal when culture changes its form but does not remove it completely.","zh":"當文化改變某能力的形式，但沒有完全消除它，該能力就具有普遍性。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the ability is rare, widespread, and deeply human.","zh":"這個短語強調該能力稀少、廣泛存在，而且深深屬於人類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"without formal training","meaning":"沒有接受正規訓練","examples":[{"en":"People can recognise music without formal training.","zh":"人們即使沒有接受正規訓練，也能辨認音樂。"},{"en":"Without formal training means without lessons, professional instruction, or organised study.","zh":"without formal training 指沒有課堂、專業指導或有組織的學習。"},{"en":"A child may learn to sing a tune without formal training simply by hearing it many times.","zh":"孩子可能只是聽過很多次，便在沒有接受正規訓練下學會唱一段旋律。"},{"en":"If people can do something without formal training, the ability may come from ordinary experience or natural sensitivity.","zh":"如果人們沒有接受正規訓練也能做某事，該能力可能來自日常經驗或自然敏感度。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts natural or informal learning with professional education.","zh":"這個短語對比自然或非正式學習與專業教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"from a Stone Age tribesman to a suburban teenager","meaning":"從石器時代部落成員到郊區青少年","examples":[{"en":"Anyone, from a Stone Age tribesman to a suburban teenager, can recognise music.","zh":"任何人，從石器時代部落成員到郊區青少年，都能辨認音樂。"},{"en":"From a Stone Age tribesman to a suburban teenager means across extremely different historical periods and social settings.","zh":"from a Stone Age tribesman to a suburban teenager 指橫跨極其不同的歷史時期和社會環境。"},{"en":"People from a village elder to a city student may all recognise a sad melody.","zh":"從村中長者到城市學生，人們都可能辨認到悲傷旋律。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a wide range to show that music is not limited to one culture or era.","zh":"這個短語創造一個很廣的範圍，顯示音樂不限於某一文化或時代。"},{"en":"It is used to emphasise universality by comparing very different kinds of people.","zh":"它透過比較非常不同的人來強調普遍性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have the ability to recognise","meaning":"有能力辨認……","examples":[{"en":"Humans have the ability to recognise music.","zh":"人類有能力辨認音樂。"},{"en":"To have the ability to recognise something means to be able to identify it when seeing, hearing, or experiencing it.","zh":"have the ability to recognise 某事，指在看見、聽見或經歷它時能夠識別它。"},{"en":"A student may have the ability to recognise a familiar accent after hearing it often.","zh":"學生經常聽到某種口音後，可能有能力辨認那種熟悉口音。"},{"en":"Recognition helps people respond quickly because they know what kind of thing they are facing.","zh":"辨認能力幫助人快速回應，因為他們知道自己面對的是甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a basic skill of identifying something.","zh":"這個短語描述識別某物的基本技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in some fashion","meaning":"以某種方式","examples":[{"en":"Almost every individual can make music in some fashion.","zh":"幾乎每個人都能以某種方式製作音樂。"},{"en":"In some fashion means in some way, even if the method is simple or imperfect.","zh":"in some fashion 指以某種方式，即使方法簡單或不完美。"},{"en":"A child can tell a story in some fashion even before learning proper writing skills.","zh":"孩子即使尚未學會正式寫作技巧，也能以某種方式講故事。"},{"en":"People may join music by singing, tapping, clapping, humming, or dancing.","zh":"人們可以透過唱歌、敲拍子、拍手、哼唱或跳舞參與音樂。"},{"en":"The phrase allows many possible forms rather than one strict method.","zh":"這個短語容許多種可能形式，而不是只有一種嚴格方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"why this should be so","meaning":"為何會這樣","examples":[{"en":"Why this should be so is a mystery.","zh":"為何會這樣仍是一個謎。"},{"en":"Why this should be so means why this situation exists or why it happens in this way.","zh":"why this should be so 指為何這種情況存在，或為何事情以這種方式發生。"},{"en":"Many students enjoy songs more than poems, but why this should be so is not always clear.","zh":"許多學生比起詩更喜歡歌曲，但為何會這樣並不總是清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when a fact seems true but its reason is difficult to explain.","zh":"當某個事實似乎成立，但原因難以解釋時，就會用這個短語。"},{"en":"It signals that the writer is moving from observation to explanation.","zh":"它表示作者正由觀察轉向解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get through the day","meaning":"應付日常生活","examples":[{"en":"Music is not necessary for getting through the day.","zh":"音樂並不是應付日常生活所必需的。"},{"en":"To get through the day means to manage ordinary daily life from morning to night.","zh":"get through the day 指由早到晚應付普通日常生活。"},{"en":"A tired student may need coffee and a simple plan to get through the day.","zh":"疲倦學生可能需要咖啡和簡單計劃來應付一天。"},{"en":"Food, sleep, and shelter help people get through the day in a direct practical way.","zh":"食物、睡眠和住所能以直接實用的方式幫助人應付日常生活。"},{"en":"The phrase describes surviving or coping with normal daily demands.","zh":"這個短語描述在正常日常要求中生存或應付。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"aid in reproduction","meaning":"有助繁殖","examples":[{"en":"If music aids in reproduction, it does so only in highly indirect ways.","zh":"如果音樂有助繁殖，它也只是以非常間接的方式做到。"},{"en":"To aid in reproduction means to help living beings attract mates, have children, or pass on genes.","zh":"aid in reproduction 指幫助生物吸引伴侶、生育後代或傳遞基因。"},{"en":"Bright feathers may aid in reproduction if they help a bird attract a partner.","zh":"如果鮮艷羽毛能幫助鳥吸引伴侶，它就可能有助繁殖。"},{"en":"Music would aid reproduction only if it somehow made people more attractive or socially connected.","zh":"音樂只有在某種程度上令人更有吸引力或更有社交連繫時，才算有助繁殖。"},{"en":"The phrase is usually used in biological explanations of survival and mating.","zh":"這個短語通常用於關於生存和交配的生物學解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in highly indirect ways","meaning":"以非常間接的方式","examples":[{"en":"Music may aid reproduction only in highly indirect ways.","zh":"音樂可能只是以非常間接的方式有助繁殖。"},{"en":"In highly indirect ways means not directly, but through several hidden or intermediate steps.","zh":"in highly indirect ways 指不是直接地，而是透過幾個隱藏或中間步驟。"},{"en":"Good school music lessons may help confidence in highly indirect ways by encouraging students to perform in front of others.","zh":"良好的學校音樂課可能透過鼓勵學生在人前表演，以非常間接的方式幫助建立信心。"},{"en":"Something indirect is harder to prove because the effect does not appear immediately.","zh":"間接的事較難證明，因為效果不會立即出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a connection that exists only through a long chain of effects.","zh":"這個短語描述只透過一長串影響才存在的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"by contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"Language, by contrast, exists everywhere for more obvious reasons.","zh":"相比之下，語言因更明顯的原因而存在於各處。"},{"en":"By contrast introduces a difference between two ideas, people, or situations.","zh":"by contrast 引出兩個想法、人物或情況之間的差異。"},{"en":"Some students enjoy quiet reading; by contrast, others learn better through discussion.","zh":"有些學生喜歡安靜閱讀；相比之下，另一些學生透過討論學得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers see how one point differs from the previous point.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者看見一點與前一點有何不同。"},{"en":"It is useful when the writer wants to compare two things clearly.","zh":"當作者想清楚比較兩件事時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"members of your tribe","meaning":"你的部落成員","examples":[{"en":"Language helps you communicate with the members of your tribe.","zh":"語言幫助你與你的部落成員溝通。"},{"en":"Members of your tribe means people who belong to the same early social group or community.","zh":"members of your tribe 指屬於同一早期社會群體或社區的人。"},{"en":"In a small village, people may rely on members of their community for food, safety, and news.","zh":"在小村莊中，人們可能依賴社區成員取得食物、安全和消息。"},{"en":"Communication with group members helps people cooperate and survive.","zh":"與群體成員溝通幫助人合作和生存。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the social group a person belongs to.","zh":"這個短語指一個人所屬的社會群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"organise a migration across Africa","meaning":"組織橫越非洲的遷徙","examples":[{"en":"Language allows people to organise a migration across Africa.","zh":"語言讓人們能夠組織橫越非洲的遷徙。"},{"en":"To organise a migration across Africa means to plan and coordinate the movement of people over a huge area.","zh":"organise a migration across Africa 指規劃並協調人群在巨大地區中的移動。"},{"en":"A family moving to another city must organise transport, food, money, and timing.","zh":"一個家庭搬到另一個城市，也必須安排交通、食物、金錢和時間。"},{"en":"Large migrations need communication because people must agree on routes, dangers, and supplies.","zh":"大規模遷徙需要溝通，因為人們必須就路線、危險和補給達成共識。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how language can support complex group action.","zh":"這個短語顯示語言如何支持複雜的群體行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"build reed boats","meaning":"建造蘆葦船","examples":[{"en":"People can use language to plan how to build reed boats.","zh":"人們可以用語言計劃如何建造蘆葦船。"},{"en":"To build reed boats means to make boats from tall water plants called reeds.","zh":"build reed boats 指用稱為蘆葦的高大水生植物製作船隻。"},{"en":"A group building a simple raft must discuss materials, shape, safety, and timing.","zh":"一群人建造簡單木筏時，必須討論材料、形狀、安全和時間。"},{"en":"Building boats requires shared instructions because one mistake can make travel dangerous.","zh":"建造船隻需要共同指示，因為一個錯誤就可能令旅程危險。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a concrete example of language helping humans organise technology.","zh":"這個短語給出語言幫助人類組織科技活動的具體例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cross the seas","meaning":"橫渡海洋","examples":[{"en":"Early humans used communication to cross the seas.","zh":"早期人類使用溝通來橫渡海洋。"},{"en":"To cross the seas means to travel over large areas of ocean or water.","zh":"cross the seas 指穿越大片海洋或水域。"},{"en":"Sailors need maps, weather information, and teamwork to cross the seas safely.","zh":"水手需要地圖、天氣資料和團隊合作，才能安全橫渡海洋。"},{"en":"Crossing the seas is difficult because people must plan food, direction, and dangers before travelling.","zh":"橫渡海洋很困難，因為人們出發前必須規劃食物、方向和危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long-distance movement across water.","zh":"這個短語描述跨越水域的長距離移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"technological extravagance","meaning":"技術上的高度繁複","examples":[{"en":"Modern culture, in all its technological extravagance, springs from human language.","zh":"現代文化，連同其所有技術上的高度繁複，都源自人類語言。"},{"en":"Technological extravagance means highly complex, impressive, or excessive use of technology.","zh":"technological extravagance 指高度複雜、令人驚嘆或過度的科技使用。"},{"en":"A city full of smart screens, automatic trains, and digital payments shows technological extravagance.","zh":"一個充滿智能屏幕、自動列車和電子支付的城市，展現了技術上的高度繁複。"},{"en":"Technological extravagance can make modern life powerful but also complicated.","zh":"技術上的高度繁複可以令現代生活強大，但也更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase describes technology developed to an impressive and elaborate level.","zh":"這個短語描述科技發展到令人印象深刻而精巧的程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"spring directly from","meaning":"直接源自……","examples":[{"en":"Modern culture springs directly from the human talent for manipulating symbols.","zh":"現代文化直接源自人類操控符號的才能。"},{"en":"To spring directly from something means to come clearly and immediately from it as a source.","zh":"spring directly from 某事，指清楚而直接地由它作為來源而產生。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may spring directly from repeated practice and supportive feedback.","zh":"學生的信心可能直接源自反覆練習和支持性的回饋。"},{"en":"If a problem springs directly from poor planning, fixing the plan should reduce the problem.","zh":"如果問題直接源自規劃不善，修正計劃應能減少問題。"},{"en":"The phrase links a result strongly to its origin.","zh":"這個短語把結果與其起源強烈連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"manipulate symbols and syntax","meaning":"操控符號和句法","examples":[{"en":"Humans have a talent for manipulating symbols and syntax.","zh":"人類有操控符號和句法的才能。"},{"en":"To manipulate symbols and syntax means to use signs, words, and grammar rules to create meaning.","zh":"manipulate symbols and syntax 指使用符號、詞語和文法規則來創造意思。"},{"en":"A student manipulates symbols and syntax when she turns words into a clear sentence.","zh":"學生把詞語組成清楚句子時，就是在操控符號和句法。"},{"en":"This ability allows humans to tell stories, make laws, write code, and explain ideas.","zh":"這種能力讓人類講故事、制定法律、編寫程式和解釋想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a core ability behind language and complex thought.","zh":"這個短語描述語言和複雜思考背後的核心能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be intrigued by","meaning":"對……深感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have always been intrigued by the connection between music and language.","zh":"科學家一直對音樂與語言之間的聯繫深感興趣。"},{"en":"To be intrigued by something means to be strongly interested because it is unusual, puzzling, or worth exploring.","zh":"be intrigued by 某事，指因它不尋常、令人困惑或值得探索而強烈感興趣。"},{"en":"A student may be intrigued by why some songs are remembered after only one hearing.","zh":"學生可能對為何有些歌曲只聽一次就記得深感興趣。"},{"en":"Intrigue often leads people to ask questions and begin research.","zh":"興趣常引導人提出問題並開始研究。"},{"en":"The phrase describes curiosity mixed with intellectual interest.","zh":"這個短語描述帶有智性好奇的興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the connection between music and language","meaning":"音樂與語言之間的聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Researchers study the connection between music and language.","zh":"研究人員研究音樂與語言之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"The connection between music and language means the ways in which sound, rhythm, pitch, meaning, and communication may be related.","zh":"connection between music and language 指聲音、節奏、音高、意義和溝通可能如何相關。"},{"en":"A teacher may explore this connection by asking students to compare song lyrics with spoken sentences.","zh":"老師可能要求學生比較歌詞與口語句子，以探索這種聯繫。"},{"en":"Studying the connection can show whether music and speech use similar brain or sound patterns.","zh":"研究這種聯繫可以顯示音樂和說話是否使用相似的大腦或聲音模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a relationship between two forms of human expression.","zh":"這個短語描述兩種人類表達形式之間的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"over the years","meaning":"多年來","examples":[{"en":"Over the years, words and melody have acquired different status in research.","zh":"多年來，詞語和旋律在研究中獲得了不同地位。"},{"en":"Over the years means during a long period of time.","zh":"over the years 指在很長一段時間中。"},{"en":"Over the years, a shy student may become confident through regular speaking practice.","zh":"多年來，害羞學生可能透過定期口語練習變得自信。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that change has happened gradually rather than suddenly.","zh":"這個短語顯示變化是逐漸發生，而不是突然發生。"},{"en":"It is often used to introduce historical development.","zh":"它常用來引出歷史發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"acquire a vastly different status","meaning":"獲得截然不同的地位","examples":[{"en":"Words and melody have acquired a vastly different status in the lab.","zh":"詞語和旋律在實驗室中獲得了截然不同的地位。"},{"en":"To acquire a vastly different status means to come to be treated with a much higher, lower, or different level of importance.","zh":"acquire a vastly different status 指逐漸被賦予高得多、低得多或很不同的重要程度。"},{"en":"Online learning acquired a vastly different status after schools had to teach remotely.","zh":"學校必須遙距教學後，網上學習獲得了截然不同的地位。"},{"en":"A subject’s status changes when researchers, teachers, or society begin to value it differently.","zh":"當研究人員、老師或社會開始以不同方式重視某科目，其地位就會改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a major shift in how something is regarded.","zh":"這個短語描述某事被看待方式的重大轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the lab and the seminar room","meaning":"實驗室和研討室","examples":[{"en":"Language and music have different status in the lab and the seminar room.","zh":"語言和音樂在實驗室和研討室中有不同地位。"},{"en":"The lab and the seminar room means formal research and academic discussion settings.","zh":"the lab and the seminar room 指正式研究和學術討論環境。"},{"en":"An idea may be tested in the lab and debated in the seminar room before scholars accept it.","zh":"一個想法可能先在實驗室被測試，再在研討室被辯論，之後才被學者接受。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that both experiments and intellectual discussion shape academic value.","zh":"這個短語暗示實驗和知性討論都會塑造學術價值。"},{"en":"It describes the world of research, teaching, and scholarly debate.","zh":"它描述研究、教學和學術辯論的世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be considered essential to","meaning":"被視為對……至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Language has long been considered essential to understanding human intelligence.","zh":"語言長期被視為對理解人類智能至關重要。"},{"en":"To be considered essential to something means to be regarded as necessary for it.","zh":"be considered essential to 某事，指被認為對它是必要的。"},{"en":"Reading is considered essential to success in many school subjects.","zh":"閱讀被視為對許多學科成功至關重要。"},{"en":"If something is essential, people believe the goal cannot be fully achieved without it.","zh":"如果某物至關重要，人們相信沒有它就不能完全達到目標。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something treated as necessary, not just helpful.","zh":"這個短語描述某物被視為必要，而不只是有幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"unlock the mechanisms of","meaning":"解開……的機制","examples":[{"en":"Language may help scientists unlock the mechanisms of human intelligence.","zh":"語言可能幫助科學家解開人類智能的機制。"},{"en":"To unlock the mechanisms of something means to discover how it works internally.","zh":"unlock the mechanisms of 某事，指發現其內部如何運作。"},{"en":"Brain scans may help researchers unlock the mechanisms of memory.","zh":"腦掃描可能幫助研究人員解開記憶的機制。"},{"en":"Understanding mechanisms allows people to explain not only what happens, but why it happens.","zh":"理解機制讓人們不只解釋發生了甚麼，也能解釋為何發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes revealing the hidden workings of a system.","zh":"這個短語描述揭示一個系統隱藏的運作方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"human intelligence","meaning":"人類智能","examples":[{"en":"Language is essential to unlocking the mechanisms of human intelligence.","zh":"語言對解開人類智能的機制至關重要。"},{"en":"Human intelligence means the mental ability of humans to learn, reason, communicate, solve problems, and create meaning.","zh":"human intelligence 指人類學習、推理、溝通、解決問題和創造意義的心理能力。"},{"en":"Schools develop human intelligence through reading, discussion, problem-solving, and creativity.","zh":"學校透過閱讀、討論、解難和創意來發展人類智能。"},{"en":"Studying human intelligence helps researchers understand how people think differently from other animals.","zh":"研究人類智能幫助研究人員理解人類如何與其他動物有不同思考方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the thinking power of human beings.","zh":"這個短語描述人類的思考能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"evolutionary frippery","meaning":"進化上的奢侈附屬品","examples":[{"en":"Music is sometimes treated as evolutionary frippery.","zh":"音樂有時被視為進化上的奢侈附屬品。"},{"en":"Evolutionary frippery means something seen as attractive or enjoyable but not necessary for survival or evolution.","zh":"evolutionary frippery 指被看成吸引或愉快，但對生存或進化並非必要的東西。"},{"en":"Some people may treat fashion as social frippery if they think it is decorative rather than essential.","zh":"如果有人認為時裝只是裝飾而非必要，可能把它視為社交上的奢侈附屬品。"},{"en":"Calling music evolutionary frippery suggests it is a luxury, not a biological necessity.","zh":"稱音樂為進化上的奢侈附屬品，暗示它是奢侈品，而非生物必需。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something dismissed as unnecessary decoration.","zh":"這個短語描述被貶為不必要裝飾的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mere auditory cheesecake","meaning":"純粹的聽覺享受；非必要的感官享受","examples":[{"en":"Steven Pinker describes music as mere auditory cheesecake.","zh":"Steven Pinker 把音樂描述為純粹的聽覺享受。"},{"en":"Mere auditory cheesecake means a pleasant sound-based pleasure that is enjoyable but not biologically necessary.","zh":"mere auditory cheesecake 指令人愉快的聲音享受，好聽但在生物上並非必要。"},{"en":"Calling a game “mere digital candy” would mean it is entertaining but not essential.","zh":"稱遊戲為「純粹的數碼糖果」，意思是它有娛樂性但不是必需。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests music is like dessert for the ears rather than a survival tool.","zh":"這個短語暗示音樂像耳朵的甜品，而不是生存工具。"},{"en":"It is a memorable metaphor for treating music as pleasure, not necessity.","zh":"它是一個鮮明比喻，把音樂視為享受，而不是必需品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as someone puts it","meaning":"正如某人所說","examples":[{"en":"Music is mere auditory cheesecake, as Steven Pinker puts it.","zh":"音樂是純粹的聽覺享受，正如 Steven Pinker 所說。"},{"en":"As someone puts it means using another person’s words or way of expressing an idea.","zh":"as someone puts it 指使用另一個人的說法或表達方式。"},{"en":"Homework is “practice for the mind,” as my teacher puts it.","zh":"功課是「心智的練習」，正如我的老師所說。"},{"en":"The phrase gives credit to the person whose wording is being borrowed.","zh":"這個短語把借用的措辭歸功於原說話者。"},{"en":"It helps writers introduce a memorable quotation or expression.","zh":"它幫助作者引入令人記得的引文或表達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"thanks to","meaning":"由於；多虧","examples":[{"en":"Thanks to recent neuroscience research, that tune is changing.","zh":"由於近期神經科學研究，這種看法正在改變。"},{"en":"Thanks to means because of, usually when the cause produces a helpful or important result.","zh":"thanks to 指由於，通常用於原因帶來有幫助或重要結果。"},{"en":"Thanks to better public transport, students can reach school more easily.","zh":"多虧更好的公共交通，學生可以更容易到達學校。"},{"en":"The phrase links a positive change to the thing that made it possible.","zh":"這個短語把正面改變與令它成為可能的事物連起來。"},{"en":"It often expresses that a new development has improved the situation.","zh":"它常表達新發展改善了情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a decade-long wave of","meaning":"長達十年的一波……","examples":[{"en":"A decade-long wave of neuroscience research has changed views on music.","zh":"長達十年的一波神經科學研究改變了人們對音樂的看法。"},{"en":"A decade-long wave of something means a large movement or series of events lasting about ten years.","zh":"decade-long wave of 某事，指持續約十年的大型運動或一連串事件。"},{"en":"A decade-long wave of online learning tools has changed how many teachers prepare lessons.","zh":"長達十年的一波網上學習工具改變了許多老師準備課堂的方式。"},{"en":"A long wave of research can slowly change what experts believe.","zh":"長期一波研究可以慢慢改變專家的信念。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sustained activity over ten years, not a single event.","zh":"這個短語描述持續十年的活動，而不是單一事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"neuroscience research","meaning":"神經科學研究","examples":[{"en":"Neuroscience research has changed the way scientists view music.","zh":"神經科學研究改變了科學家看待音樂的方式。"},{"en":"Neuroscience research is scientific study of the brain, nerves, and how they support behaviour and experience.","zh":"neuroscience research 是對大腦、神經，以及它們如何支援行為和經驗的科學研究。"},{"en":"Neuroscience research may examine what happens in the brain when people listen to a sad song.","zh":"神經科學研究可能檢視人們聽悲傷歌曲時大腦發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Brain evidence can change theories about memory, emotion, language, and music.","zh":"大腦證據可以改變關於記憶、情緒、語言和音樂的理論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research focused on the nervous system and the brain.","zh":"這個短語描述以神經系統和大腦為中心的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"that tune is changing","meaning":"這種看法正在改變","examples":[{"en":"For a long time music was dismissed, but that tune is changing.","zh":"很長時間以來音樂被忽視，但這種看法正在改變。"},{"en":"That tune is changing means that an old opinion or attitude is beginning to change.","zh":"that tune is changing 指舊有意見或態度開始改變。"},{"en":"People once thought online lessons were weak, but that tune is changing as platforms improve.","zh":"人們曾認為網上課堂很弱，但隨着平台改善，這種看法正在改變。"},{"en":"The phrase plays on the idea of music while describing a shift in belief.","zh":"這個短語借用音樂的概念，同時描述信念的轉變。"},{"en":"It is often used when a familiar view is being replaced by new evidence.","zh":"當熟悉看法正被新證據取代時，常會使用它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a flurry of recent publications","meaning":"一連串近期發表的研究","examples":[{"en":"A flurry of recent publications suggests a link between music and biology.","zh":"一連串近期發表的研究顯示音樂與生物學之間有聯繫。"},{"en":"A flurry of recent publications means many new articles, books, or studies appearing in a short time.","zh":"flurry of recent publications 指短時間內出現許多新文章、書籍或研究。"},{"en":"A flurry of recent reports on sleep may make schools reconsider early morning lessons.","zh":"一連串關於睡眠的近期報告，可能令學校重新考慮清晨上課。"},{"en":"When many publications appear together, they can signal growing interest in a topic.","zh":"當許多出版物一起出現，可能表示某主題受到越來越多關注。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a sudden burst of published work.","zh":"這個短語描述出版作品突然大量湧現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"suggest that","meaning":"顯示；暗示","examples":[{"en":"Recent publications suggest that music and language can both reveal who we are.","zh":"近期研究顯示，音樂和語言都能揭示我們是誰。"},{"en":"Suggest that means show, indicate, or make an idea seem likely without proving it completely.","zh":"suggest that 指顯示、暗示或使某想法看似可能，但未必完全證明。"},{"en":"Low attendance may suggest that students find the course difficult or uninteresting.","zh":"出席率低可能顯示學生覺得課程困難或沒趣。"},{"en":"Researchers use “suggest” when evidence points to a conclusion but more proof may still be needed.","zh":"當證據指向某結論但仍可能需要更多證明時，研究人員會使用 “suggest”。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a careful, evidence-based claim.","zh":"這個短語引出謹慎、以證據為基礎的主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"equally be able to","meaning":"同樣能夠","examples":[{"en":"Music and language may equally be able to tell us where we come from.","zh":"音樂和語言可能同樣能夠告訴我們從何而來。"},{"en":"Equally be able to means have the same ability or potential to do something.","zh":"equally be able to 指具有相同能力或潛力去做某事。"},{"en":"A photograph and a diary may equally be able to show what life was like in the past.","zh":"照片和日記可能同樣能夠顯示過去生活是怎樣的。"},{"en":"The phrase compares two things and says both may be useful in the same way.","zh":"這個短語比較兩件事，並說兩者可能以相同方式有用。"},{"en":"It helps challenge the idea that only one source can provide understanding.","zh":"它幫助挑戰只有一個來源才能提供理解的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"emotionally, but biologically","meaning":"不只是情感上，更是生物學上","examples":[{"en":"Music may tell us who we are not just emotionally, but biologically.","zh":"音樂可能告訴我們自己是誰，不只是情感上，更是生物學上。"},{"en":"Emotionally, but biologically contrasts feelings with the body and brain as sources of explanation.","zh":"emotionally, but biologically 把感受與身體和大腦作為解釋來源形成對比。"},{"en":"A song may comfort us emotionally, but biologically it may also affect breathing and heart rate.","zh":"一首歌可能在情感上安慰我們，但在生物學上也可能影響呼吸和心跳。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that music may matter both in experience and in human biology.","zh":"這個短語顯示音樂可能在經驗和人類生物本質上都重要。"},{"en":"It moves the discussion from personal feeling to scientific explanation.","zh":"它把討論由個人感受轉向科學解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"devote a special issue to","meaning":"用一期特刊探討……","examples":[{"en":"Nature Neuroscience devoted a special issue to music and language.","zh":"Nature Neuroscience 用一期特刊探討音樂和語言。"},{"en":"To devote a special issue to a topic means to use one complete journal edition mainly for that topic.","zh":"devote a special issue to 某主題，指用一期完整期刊主要討論該主題。"},{"en":"A school magazine may devote a special issue to student mental health after exam stress increases.","zh":"考試壓力增加後，學校雜誌可能用一期特刊探討學生心理健康。"},{"en":"Journals do this when a topic becomes important enough to deserve focused attention.","zh":"當一個主題變得足夠重要，值得集中關注時，期刊會這樣做。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving an entire publication issue to one subject.","zh":"這個短語描述把整期出版物用於一個主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"argue that","meaning":"主張；認為","examples":[{"en":"Schwartz, Howe, and Purves argued that music and language are connected.","zh":"Schwartz、Howe 和 Purves 主張音樂與語言是相連的。"},{"en":"To argue that means to give reasons for believing a particular idea is true.","zh":"argue that 指提出理由來支持某個想法為真。"},{"en":"A student may argue that homework should be shorter because rest improves learning.","zh":"學生可能主張功課應較短，因為休息能改善學習。"},{"en":"Strong arguments need evidence, examples, and clear reasoning.","zh":"有力論點需要證據、例子和清晰推理。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a claim supported by reasoning.","zh":"這個短語引出由推理支持的主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be intricately connected","meaning":"錯綜複雜地相連","examples":[{"en":"The sounds of music and language are intricately connected.","zh":"音樂和語言的聲音錯綜複雜地相連。"},{"en":"To be intricately connected means to be linked in a complex and detailed way.","zh":"be intricately connected 指以複雜而細緻的方式相互連繫。"},{"en":"Sleep and memory are intricately connected because poor sleep can affect learning, mood, and attention.","zh":"睡眠和記憶錯綜複雜地相連，因為睡眠不足會影響學習、心情和注意力。"},{"en":"Complex connections are not always obvious until researchers study the details.","zh":"複雜聯繫在研究人員細看細節前，未必明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a deep relationship with many interacting parts.","zh":"這個短語描述包含許多互動部分的深層關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"grasp the originality of","meaning":"理解……的原創性","examples":[{"en":"To grasp the originality of this idea, we need to understand earlier theories.","zh":"要理解這個想法的原創性，我們需要理解較早的理論。"},{"en":"To grasp the originality of something means to understand what is new, unusual, or creative about it.","zh":"grasp the originality of 某事，指理解它有甚麼新的、不尋常或有創意之處。"},{"en":"Students grasp the originality of a new film better when they compare it with older films.","zh":"當學生把新電影與舊電影比較時，會更能理解其原創性。"},{"en":"Understanding old ideas helps people see why a new idea is genuinely different.","zh":"理解舊想法幫助人看出新想法為何真正不同。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recognising the newness of an idea.","zh":"這個短語描述辨認一個想法的新意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"traditionally be understood","meaning":"傳統上被理解","examples":[{"en":"Music has traditionally been understood in two main ways.","zh":"音樂傳統上以兩種主要方式被理解。"},{"en":"To traditionally be understood in a way means to have usually been explained or interpreted that way in the past.","zh":"traditionally be understood 某方式，指過去通常以該方式被解釋或詮釋。"},{"en":"Exams have traditionally been understood as tests of knowledge, though some teachers now see them as learning tools too.","zh":"考試傳統上被理解為知識測試，雖然有些老師現在也把它視為學習工具。"},{"en":"Traditional understanding can change when new evidence or new values appear.","zh":"當新證據或新價值出現，傳統理解可以改變。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an older or established explanation.","zh":"這個短語引出較舊或既定解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"musicologists","meaning":"音樂學者","examples":[{"en":"Musicologists have long studied the universal qualities of music.","zh":"音樂學者長期研究音樂的普遍特質。"},{"en":"Musicologists are scholars who study music, its history, structure, culture, and meaning.","zh":"musicologists 是研究音樂及其歷史、結構、文化和意義的學者。"},{"en":"A musicologist may compare folk songs from different countries to find shared patterns.","zh":"音樂學者可能比較不同國家的民歌，以尋找共同模式。"},{"en":"Musicologists help explain why music sounds different across cultures but still feels recognisable.","zh":"音樂學者幫助解釋為何音樂在不同文化中聽起來不同，卻仍可被辨認。"},{"en":"The word refers to academic experts in the study of music.","zh":"這個詞指研究音樂的學術專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have long emphasised that","meaning":"長期強調","examples":[{"en":"Musicologists have long emphasised that music has universal qualities.","zh":"音樂學者長期強調音樂具有普遍特質。"},{"en":"To have long emphasised that means to have repeatedly stressed an idea over a long period.","zh":"have long emphasised that 指長時間反覆強調某個想法。"},{"en":"Teachers have long emphasised that reading widely improves writing.","zh":"老師長期強調廣泛閱讀能改善寫作。"},{"en":"An idea repeatedly emphasised by experts usually becomes central to a field.","zh":"專家反覆強調的想法通常會成為某領域的核心。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a claim has been important for many years.","zh":"這個短語顯示某主張多年來都很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stamp a special identity onto","meaning":"為……賦予獨特身份","examples":[{"en":"Each culture stamps a special identity onto its music.","zh":"每種文化都為其音樂賦予獨特身份。"},{"en":"To stamp a special identity onto something means to give it a recognisable character or cultural mark.","zh":"stamp a special identity onto 某物，指給它一種可辨認的特色或文化標記。"},{"en":"A school may stamp its identity onto a sports day through its songs, colours, and traditions.","zh":"學校可能透過歌曲、顏色和傳統為運動會賦予自己的身份。"},{"en":"Culture shapes music by adding local instruments, rhythms, language, and emotions.","zh":"文化透過加入本地樂器、節奏、語言和情感來塑造音樂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making something clearly belong to a group.","zh":"這個短語描述令某物清楚屬於某群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"universal qualities","meaning":"普遍特質","examples":[{"en":"Music itself has some universal qualities.","zh":"音樂本身有一些普遍特質。"},{"en":"Universal qualities are features found across many or almost all cultures.","zh":"universal qualities 是在許多或幾乎所有文化中都能找到的特徵。"},{"en":"Rhythm may be a universal quality because people everywhere can respond to repeated beats.","zh":"節奏可能是一種普遍特質，因為各地的人都能對重複拍子作出反應。"},{"en":"Universal qualities help explain why people can recognise music from unfamiliar cultures.","zh":"普遍特質幫助解釋為何人們能辨認陌生文化中的音樂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes features that go beyond local differences.","zh":"這個短語描述超越本地差異的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in virtually all cultures","meaning":"在幾乎所有文化中","examples":[{"en":"In virtually all cultures, sound is divided into musical intervals.","zh":"在幾乎所有文化中，聲音都被分成音程。"},{"en":"In virtually all cultures means in almost every culture, with very few exceptions.","zh":"in virtually all cultures 指在幾乎每種文化中，只有極少例外。"},{"en":"In virtually all cultures, children learn some form of social rules from adults.","zh":"在幾乎所有文化中，孩子都會從成人身上學到某種社會規則。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when something is extremely widespread but not claimed as absolutely universal.","zh":"當某事極為廣泛，但不被說成絕對普遍時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It helps writers make a strong but careful generalisation.","zh":"它幫助作者作出強而謹慎的概括。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be divided into","meaning":"被分成","examples":[{"en":"Sound is divided into some or all of the 12 intervals.","zh":"聲音被分成十二個音程中的部分或全部。"},{"en":"To be divided into parts means to be separated into smaller groups, sections, or categories.","zh":"be divided into 部分，指被分成較小的組別、部分或類別。"},{"en":"A school year may be divided into two terms or three terms.","zh":"一個學年可能被分成兩個學期或三個學期。"},{"en":"Dividing something into parts helps people organise and understand it.","zh":"把某事分成部分，有助人組織和理解它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes separating one whole into smaller units.","zh":"這個短語描述把一個整體分成較小單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"intervals","meaning":"音程","examples":[{"en":"The chromatic scale is made up of 12 intervals.","zh":"半音音階由十二個音程構成。"},{"en":"Intervals are distances between two musical notes in pitch.","zh":"intervals 是兩個音符在音高上的距離。"},{"en":"A music student hears an interval when a teacher plays one note and then a higher note.","zh":"當老師先彈一個音再彈一個較高音，音樂學生就聽到一個音程。"},{"en":"Intervals matter because they help create melody, harmony, and musical structure.","zh":"音程很重要，因為它們幫助創造旋律、和聲和音樂結構。"},{"en":"The word describes the pitch gap between notes.","zh":"這個詞描述音符之間的音高距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make up the chromatic scale","meaning":"構成半音音階","examples":[{"en":"Twelve intervals make up the chromatic scale.","zh":"十二個音程構成半音音階。"},{"en":"To make up the chromatic scale means to form the full set of notes in that musical system.","zh":"make up the chromatic scale 指形成該音樂系統中的完整音符組合。"},{"en":"Letters make up the alphabet, just as notes make up a musical scale.","zh":"字母構成字母表，就像音符構成音階一樣。"},{"en":"When parts make up a whole, each part contributes to the complete structure.","zh":"當部分構成整體，每個部分都對完整結構有貢獻。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what components form the chromatic scale.","zh":"這個短語解釋哪些組成部分形成半音音階。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the chromatic scale","meaning":"半音音階","examples":[{"en":"The chromatic scale is represented by the keys on a piano.","zh":"半音音階由鋼琴琴鍵表示。"},{"en":"The chromatic scale is a musical scale containing all twelve notes within an octave.","zh":"chromatic scale 是在一個八度內包含全部十二個音的音階。"},{"en":"A piano keyboard shows the chromatic scale through both white and black keys.","zh":"鋼琴鍵盤透過白鍵和黑鍵展示半音音階。"},{"en":"Musicians use the chromatic scale to understand the full range of nearby pitch steps.","zh":"音樂人使用半音音階來理解鄰近音高步階的完整範圍。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a complete twelve-note musical pattern.","zh":"這個短語指完整的十二音音樂模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be represented by","meaning":"由……表示","examples":[{"en":"The chromatic scale is represented by the keys on a piano.","zh":"半音音階由鋼琴琴鍵表示。"},{"en":"To be represented by something means to be shown or symbolised by it.","zh":"be represented by 某物，指由它顯示或象徵。"},{"en":"A country may be represented by its flag in an international competition.","zh":"一個國家在國際比賽中可能由國旗代表。"},{"en":"Representation helps people understand an abstract idea through a visible example.","zh":"表示方式幫助人透過可見例子理解抽象概念。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one thing standing for or displaying another.","zh":"這個短語描述一件事物代表或展示另一件事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the keys on a piano","meaning":"鋼琴琴鍵","examples":[{"en":"The intervals are represented by the keys on a piano.","zh":"這些音程由鋼琴琴鍵表示。"},{"en":"The keys on a piano are the white and black parts pressed to produce musical notes.","zh":"keys on a piano 是按下後產生音符的白色和黑色部分。"},{"en":"A beginner often learns note names by looking at the keys on a piano.","zh":"初學者常透過看鋼琴琴鍵來學音名。"},{"en":"The arrangement of piano keys helps people see pitch differences visually.","zh":"鋼琴琴鍵的排列幫助人以視覺方式看見音高差異。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the physical parts of a piano used to play notes.","zh":"這個短語指鋼琴上用來彈奏音符的實體部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"attribute this preference to","meaning":"將這種偏好歸因於……","examples":[{"en":"Observers have attributed this preference to the mathematical properties of sound.","zh":"觀察者將這種偏好歸因於聲音的數學特性。"},{"en":"To attribute this preference to something means to say that the preference is caused by or explained by that thing.","zh":"attribute this preference to 某事，指說這種偏好由該事造成或可由它解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may attribute a student’s love of reading to early bedtime stories at home.","zh":"老師可能把學生熱愛閱讀歸因於家中早期的睡前故事。"},{"en":"Attributing a preference to a cause helps explain why people choose one thing over another.","zh":"把偏好歸因於某原因，有助解釋為何人們選擇一物而非另一物。"},{"en":"The phrase links a preference with its proposed reason.","zh":"這個短語把偏好與其被提出的原因連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"combinations of tones","meaning":"音調組合","examples":[{"en":"People have a preference for certain combinations of tones.","zh":"人們偏好某些音調組合。"},{"en":"Combinations of tones are groups of musical sounds played or heard together.","zh":"combinations of tones 是一起彈奏或聽到的一組音樂聲音。"},{"en":"A simple chord is a combination of tones that can sound pleasant or tense.","zh":"簡單和弦是一種音調組合，可以聽起來愉快或緊張。"},{"en":"Different tone combinations create different emotions in songs and film music.","zh":"不同音調組合在歌曲和電影配樂中創造不同情緒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes notes joined together in sound.","zh":"這個短語描述音符在聲音中結合起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the mathematical properties of sound","meaning":"聲音的數學特性","examples":[{"en":"Observers connected musical harmony with the mathematical properties of sound.","zh":"觀察者把音樂和聲與聲音的數學特性連起來。"},{"en":"The mathematical properties of sound are measurable features such as frequency, vibration, ratio, and wave pattern.","zh":"mathematical properties of sound 是頻率、振動、比例和波形等可量度特徵。"},{"en":"A science teacher may explain pitch by showing how faster vibrations produce higher sounds.","zh":"科學老師可能透過展示較快振動產生較高聲音來解釋音高。"},{"en":"These properties help explain why some note combinations sound stable or pleasant.","zh":"這些特性幫助解釋為何某些音符組合聽起來穩定或悅耳。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the number-based features behind sound.","zh":"這個短語描述聲音背後以數字為基礎的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a direct relationship between","meaning":"……之間的直接關係","examples":[{"en":"Pythagoras noted a direct relationship between harmony and physical dimensions.","zh":"畢達哥拉斯注意到和聲與物理尺寸之間的直接關係。"},{"en":"A direct relationship between two things means one is clearly connected with the other.","zh":"direct relationship between 兩事物，指其中一者與另一者清楚相連。"},{"en":"There is often a direct relationship between practice time and improvement in a musical instrument.","zh":"練習時間與樂器進步之間常有直接關係。"},{"en":"When a relationship is direct, changes in one thing are closely linked to changes in another.","zh":"當關係是直接的，一件事的變化會與另一件事的變化密切相連。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a clear connection, not a vague association.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚連繫，而不是模糊關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the harmoniousness of","meaning":"……的和諧度","examples":[{"en":"He studied the harmoniousness of a tone combination.","zh":"他研究音調組合的和諧度。"},{"en":"The harmoniousness of something is how pleasant, balanced, or musically fitting it sounds.","zh":"harmoniousness of 某物，是它聽起來有多悅耳、平衡或音樂上協調。"},{"en":"A choir teacher may judge the harmoniousness of voices singing together.","zh":"合唱老師可能評估多個聲音一起唱時的和諧度。"},{"en":"If sounds clash badly, the harmoniousness of the combination is low.","zh":"如果聲音嚴重衝突，該組合的和諧度就低。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the degree to which sounds fit together well.","zh":"這個短語描述聲音互相配合得有多好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a tone combination","meaning":"音調組合","examples":[{"en":"A tone combination can sound harmonious or unpleasant.","zh":"音調組合可以聽起來和諧或刺耳。"},{"en":"A tone combination is a group of two or more notes or pitches heard together.","zh":"tone combination 是一起被聽到的兩個或以上音符或音高。"},{"en":"A guitarist creates a tone combination when pressing several strings at once.","zh":"吉他手一次按幾條弦時，就創造了一個音調組合。"},{"en":"Some combinations feel calm, while others create tension or discomfort.","zh":"有些組合令人感到平靜，另一些則造成緊張或不適。"},{"en":"The phrase describes musical sounds joined together.","zh":"這個短語描述結合在一起的音樂聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"physical dimensions","meaning":"物理尺寸","examples":[{"en":"The physical dimensions of an object affect the sound it produces.","zh":"物件的物理尺寸會影響它產生的聲音。"},{"en":"Physical dimensions are measurable features such as length, width, thickness, or size.","zh":"physical dimensions 是長度、寬度、厚度或大小等可量度特徵。"},{"en":"A long ruler and a short ruler make different sounds when tapped because their physical dimensions differ.","zh":"長尺和短尺被敲擊時會發出不同聲音，因為它們的物理尺寸不同。"},{"en":"In musical instruments, size and shape can change pitch and tone quality.","zh":"在樂器中，大小和形狀可以改變音高和音色。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the measurable body or size of an object.","zh":"這個短語描述物件可量度的形體或大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a plucked string","meaning":"被撥動的弦","examples":[{"en":"A plucked string produces a musical tone.","zh":"被撥動的弦會產生音樂音調。"},{"en":"A plucked string is a string pulled and released so that it vibrates and makes sound.","zh":"plucked string 是被拉起再放開，因而振動並發聲的弦。"},{"en":"A guitarist creates sound by using a finger or pick on a plucked string.","zh":"吉他手用手指或撥片撥動弦來產生聲音。"},{"en":"The string’s length and tension affect the pitch after it is plucked.","zh":"弦被撥動後，其長度和張力會影響音高。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one basic way many string instruments make sound.","zh":"這個短語描述許多弦樂器發聲的基本方式之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"an octave lower than","meaning":"比……低八度","examples":[{"en":"A longer string may sound an octave lower than a shorter one.","zh":"較長的弦可能比較短的弦低八度。"},{"en":"An octave lower than means eight scale steps lower in pitch, with a similar note quality.","zh":"octave lower than 指在音高上低八個音階級，但音名感覺相似。"},{"en":"A man’s voice may sing the same melody an octave lower than a child’s voice.","zh":"男聲可能比童聲低八度唱同一旋律。"},{"en":"Octave differences let notes sound related even when one is much higher or lower.","zh":"八度差異令音符即使高低相差很大，仍聽起來相關。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a specific musical distance below another note.","zh":"這個短語描述位於另一音符下方的特定音樂距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a similar string half its size","meaning":"長度只有其一半的相似弦","examples":[{"en":"A plucked string sounds lower than a similar string half its size.","zh":"被撥動的弦比長度只有其一半的相似弦聽起來更低。"},{"en":"A similar string half its size means a string of the same kind but only half as long.","zh":"similar string half its size 指同一類型但長度只有一半的弦。"},{"en":"In a simple experiment, two rubber bands of different lengths can show how size affects pitch.","zh":"在簡單實驗中，兩條不同長度的橡筋可以展示大小如何影響音高。"},{"en":"Comparing similar strings helps isolate length as the cause of sound difference.","zh":"比較相似的弦有助把長度分離出來，作為聲音差異的原因。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a controlled comparison between two strings.","zh":"這個短語描述兩條弦之間的受控比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a fifth lower than","meaning":"比……低五度","examples":[{"en":"A string can sound a fifth lower than another string.","zh":"一條弦可以比另一條弦低五度。"},{"en":"A fifth lower than means five scale steps lower in pitch than another note.","zh":"fifth lower than 指比另一個音低五個音階級。"},{"en":"A singer may sing harmony a fifth lower than the main melody.","zh":"歌手可能比主旋律低五度唱和聲。"},{"en":"Musical distances such as fifths help create harmony that sounds stable to many listeners.","zh":"五度等音樂距離幫助創造對許多聽眾來說穩定的和聲。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a specific pitch relationship below another sound.","zh":"這個短語描述位於另一聲音下方的特定音高關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"two-thirds of its length","meaning":"其長度的三分之二","examples":[{"en":"The second string is two-thirds of its length.","zh":"第二條弦是其長度的三分之二。"},{"en":"Two-thirds of its length means a length equal to two out of three equal parts of the original length.","zh":"two-thirds of its length 指等於原本長度三等份中的兩份。"},{"en":"If a 30-centimetre string is shortened to 20 centimetres, it is two-thirds of its length.","zh":"如果30厘米的弦縮短到20厘米，它就是原長度的三分之二。"},{"en":"Simple fractions can change sound when they change the vibrating length of a string.","zh":"當簡單分數改變弦的振動長度時，就能改變聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an exact proportional comparison.","zh":"這個短語給出精確比例比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"simple ratios and harmony","meaning":"簡單比例與和聲","examples":[{"en":"The link between simple ratios and harmony has shaped music theory.","zh":"簡單比例與和聲之間的聯繫塑造了音樂理論。"},{"en":"Simple ratios and harmony refers to the idea that easy number relationships can produce pleasant musical sounds.","zh":"simple ratios and harmony 指簡單數字關係可以產生悅耳音樂聲音的想法。"},{"en":"A teacher may show simple ratios and harmony by comparing strings of different lengths.","zh":"老師可能透過比較不同長度的弦來展示簡單比例與和聲。"},{"en":"If two notes have a simple mathematical relationship, they may sound more stable together.","zh":"如果兩個音符有簡單數學關係，它們一起聽起來可能更穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase connects mathematics with musical pleasantness.","zh":"這個短語把數學與音樂悅耳感連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"music theory","meaning":"音樂理論","examples":[{"en":"This link has influenced music theory ever since.","zh":"這種聯繫從此以後影響了音樂理論。"},{"en":"Music theory is the study of how music is structured through notes, scales, rhythm, harmony, and form.","zh":"music theory 是研究音樂如何透過音符、音階、節奏、和聲和形式組成的學問。"},{"en":"A piano student studies music theory to understand why certain chords sound right together.","zh":"鋼琴學生學習音樂理論，以理解為何某些和弦一起聽起來合適。"},{"en":"Music theory helps musicians explain patterns that listeners may feel but not name.","zh":"音樂理論幫助音樂人解釋聽眾可能感受到但不能命名的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the organised explanation of how music works.","zh":"這個短語指對音樂如何運作的有組織解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ever since","meaning":"從此以後","examples":[{"en":"The theory has influenced music ever since.","zh":"該理論從此以後一直影響音樂。"},{"en":"Ever since means from that time until now.","zh":"ever since 指從那時起直到現在。"},{"en":"Ever since the teacher used songs in class, students have remembered vocabulary more easily.","zh":"自從老師在課堂使用歌曲後，學生更容易記住詞彙。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a starting point in the past with a continuing result.","zh":"這個短語把過去的起點與持續結果連起來。"},{"en":"It shows that an influence has lasted for a long time.","zh":"它顯示某種影響已持續很長時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the music-is-math idea","meaning":"「音樂即數學」的觀念","examples":[{"en":"The music-is-math idea has influenced traditional theories of music.","zh":"「音樂即數學」的觀念影響了傳統音樂理論。"},{"en":"The music-is-math idea is the belief that musical harmony can be explained mainly through numbers and ratios.","zh":"music-is-math idea 是認為音樂和聲主要可透過數字和比例解釋的信念。"},{"en":"A student sees the music-is-math idea when string lengths and pitch are compared in science class.","zh":"學生在科學課比較弦長與音高時，就看見「音樂即數學」的觀念。"},{"en":"This idea can explain some patterns in music, but it may not explain emotion or culture fully.","zh":"這個觀念可以解釋音樂中的某些模式，但未必能完全解釋情感或文化。"},{"en":"The phrase names a theory that connects music strongly with mathematics.","zh":"這個短語命名一種把音樂與數學強烈連接的理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be accompanied by the notion that","meaning":"伴隨著……這一觀念","examples":[{"en":"This idea is accompanied by the notion that music is abstract.","zh":"這個想法伴隨著音樂是抽象的這一觀念。"},{"en":"To be accompanied by the notion that means to come together with a related belief or assumption.","zh":"be accompanied by the notion that 指伴隨一個相關信念或假設出現。"},{"en":"The idea of strict exams is often accompanied by the notion that pressure improves performance.","zh":"嚴格考試的想法常伴隨著壓力會改善表現這一觀念。"},{"en":"A main belief can bring another belief with it, even if the second one needs testing.","zh":"一個主要信念可以帶來另一個信念，即使第二個仍需要測試。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one idea travelling alongside another.","zh":"這個短語描述一個想法與另一個想法同行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"formally speaking","meaning":"從形式上說","examples":[{"en":"Music, formally speaking at least, may seem separate from the world.","zh":"至少從形式上說，音樂可能看似與世界分離。"},{"en":"Formally speaking means when considered in terms of structure, rules, or form rather than feeling or context.","zh":"formally speaking 指從結構、規則或形式，而不是感受或語境來看。"},{"en":"Formally speaking, a sonnet has fourteen lines, though its emotional effect depends on more than structure.","zh":"從形式上說，十四行詩有十四行，雖然其情感效果不只取決於結構。"},{"en":"The phrase helps limit a claim to the formal side of a subject.","zh":"這個短語幫助把主張限制在某主題的形式層面。"},{"en":"It is useful when the writer knows there are other ways to view the issue.","zh":"當作者知道議題有其他觀看方式時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"exist apart from","meaning":"獨立於……而存在","examples":[{"en":"Some critics believe that music exists apart from the world.","zh":"有些評論者相信音樂獨立於世界而存在。"},{"en":"To exist apart from something means to be separate from it and not depend on it.","zh":"exist apart from 某事，指與它分離並不依賴它。"},{"en":"A school rule should not exist apart from students’ real needs.","zh":"校規不應獨立於學生真實需要而存在。"},{"en":"If music existed apart from the world, it would not reflect speech, nature, or human experience.","zh":"如果音樂獨立於世界而存在，它就不會反映說話、自然或人類經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes separation from a larger context.","zh":"這個短語描述與更大語境分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"long-standing notion","meaning":"長期存在的觀念","examples":[{"en":"Charles Rosen discussed a long-standing notion about abstract music.","zh":"Charles Rosen 討論了一個關於抽象音樂的長期存在的觀念。"},{"en":"A long-standing notion is an idea or belief that has existed for a long time.","zh":"long-standing notion 是已存在很長時間的想法或信念。"},{"en":"The long-standing notion that children learn best through punishment has been challenged by modern education.","zh":"孩子透過懲罰學得最好這個長期存在的觀念，已被現代教育挑戰。"},{"en":"Long-standing ideas can feel true simply because people have repeated them for years.","zh":"長期存在的想法可能只是因為被多年重複而感覺真實。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an old and familiar belief.","zh":"這個短語描述古老而熟悉的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"painting and sculpture","meaning":"繪畫和雕塑","examples":[{"en":"Painting and sculpture reproduce some aspects of the natural world.","zh":"繪畫和雕塑再現自然世界的某些方面。"},{"en":"Painting and sculpture are visual art forms that use images, colour, shape, and materials.","zh":"painting and sculpture 是使用影像、顏色、形狀和材料的視覺藝術形式。"},{"en":"A painting may show a landscape, while a sculpture may show a human body in stone.","zh":"繪畫可以展示風景，而雕塑可以用石頭呈現人體。"},{"en":"These art forms often help people see familiar objects in a new way.","zh":"這些藝術形式常幫助人以新方式觀看熟悉物件。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to two major forms of visual art.","zh":"這個短語指兩種主要視覺藝術形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reproduce aspects of","meaning":"再現……的某些方面","examples":[{"en":"Art can reproduce aspects of the natural world.","zh":"藝術可以再現自然世界的某些方面。"},{"en":"To reproduce aspects of something means to show, copy, or represent some parts of it.","zh":"reproduce aspects of 某事，指展示、複製或呈現其中某些部分。"},{"en":"A school diagram can reproduce aspects of the human heart without showing every detail.","zh":"學校圖表可以再現人類心臟的某些方面，而不展示每個細節。"},{"en":"Reproducing only aspects means the artwork or model selects certain features.","zh":"只再現某些方面，表示藝術品或模型選取了某些特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase describes partial representation rather than complete copying.","zh":"這個短語描述部分呈現，而不是完整複製。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the natural world","meaning":"自然世界","examples":[{"en":"The visual arts often reflect the natural world.","zh":"視覺藝術常反映自然世界。"},{"en":"The natural world means nature, including animals, plants, landscapes, weather, and physical environments.","zh":"natural world 指自然，包括動物、植物、景觀、天氣和物理環境。"},{"en":"Children learn about the natural world when they observe insects, trees, rain, and rivers.","zh":"孩子觀察昆蟲、樹木、雨和河流時，就是在學習自然世界。"},{"en":"Artists often use the natural world as a source of colour, shape, and movement.","zh":"藝術家常把自然世界用作顏色、形狀和動作的來源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the world of nature rather than human-made systems.","zh":"這個短語描述自然界，而不是人造系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"thoughts and feelings","meaning":"思想和感受","examples":[{"en":"Writing describes thoughts and feelings we are familiar with.","zh":"文字描述我們熟悉的思想和感受。"},{"en":"Thoughts and feelings are what people think in the mind and experience emotionally.","zh":"thoughts and feelings 是人們在心中思考和在情感上經歷的東西。"},{"en":"A diary helps a student record thoughts and feelings after a difficult day.","zh":"日記幫助學生記錄困難一天後的思想和感受。"},{"en":"Sharing thoughts and feelings can help people understand one another better.","zh":"分享思想和感受可以幫助人們更好理解彼此。"},{"en":"The phrase describes inner mental and emotional life.","zh":"這個短語描述內在心理和情緒生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be familiar with","meaning":"熟悉……","examples":[{"en":"Writing describes feelings we are all familiar with.","zh":"文字描述我們都熟悉的感受。"},{"en":"To be familiar with something means to know it well because you have seen, heard, or experienced it before.","zh":"be familiar with 某事，指因以前看過、聽過或經歷過而很了解它。"},{"en":"Students are familiar with school bells because they hear them every day.","zh":"學生熟悉學校鐘聲，因為他們每天都聽到。"},{"en":"Familiar things are easier to understand because they connect with past experience.","zh":"熟悉的事較容易理解，因為它們連接過往經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recognition through repeated experience.","zh":"這個短語描述透過重複經驗而產生的認識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be entirely abstracted from","meaning":"完全抽離於……","examples":[{"en":"Some people think music is entirely abstracted from the world.","zh":"有些人認為音樂完全抽離於世界。"},{"en":"To be entirely abstracted from something means to be completely separated from real objects, events, or experience.","zh":"be entirely abstracted from 某事，指完全與真實物件、事件或經驗分離。"},{"en":"A maths formula may feel abstracted from daily life until students apply it to shopping or travel.","zh":"數學公式在學生把它應用於購物或交通前，可能感覺抽離於日常生活。"},{"en":"If music is not entirely abstracted from the world, then real sounds may shape it.","zh":"如果音樂並非完全抽離於世界，那麼真實聲音可能塑造它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes complete separation from concrete reality.","zh":"這個短語描述與具體現實完全分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……所說","examples":[{"en":"Neither idea is right, according to Schwartz and his colleagues.","zh":"根據 Schwartz 和其同事所說，兩種想法都不正確。"},{"en":"According to means based on what a person, text, report, or source says.","zh":"according to 指根據某人、文本、報告或來源所說。"},{"en":"According to the timetable, the last bus leaves at eleven.","zh":"根據時間表，最後一班巴士在十一點開出。"},{"en":"The phrase shows where information or an opinion comes from.","zh":"這個短語顯示資訊或意見來自何處。"},{"en":"It helps writers attribute a claim to a source.","zh":"它幫助作者把主張歸屬於某來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be fundamentally shaped by","meaning":"從根本上受……塑造","examples":[{"en":"Human musical preferences are fundamentally shaped by real-life sounds.","zh":"人類音樂偏好從根本上受現實生活聲音塑造。"},{"en":"To be fundamentally shaped by something means to be deeply influenced at a basic level.","zh":"be fundamentally shaped by 某事，指在基本層面受到深刻影響。"},{"en":"A child’s eating habits may be fundamentally shaped by family meals at home.","zh":"孩子的飲食習慣可能從根本上受家中家庭飯局塑造。"},{"en":"If preferences are shaped by experience, changing the environment can change what people like.","zh":"如果偏好由經驗塑造，改變環境就可能改變人們喜歡甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a deep cause, not a small influence.","zh":"這個短語描述深層原因，而不是小影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"elegant algorithms","meaning":"精妙的演算法","examples":[{"en":"Musical preferences are not simply shaped by elegant algorithms.","zh":"音樂偏好並不只是由精妙的演算法塑造。"},{"en":"Elegant algorithms are neat, clever mathematical rules or procedures used to solve problems or explain patterns.","zh":"elegant algorithms 是用來解決問題或解釋模式的簡潔、巧妙數學規則或程序。"},{"en":"A calculator uses algorithms, but an elegant algorithm does the job simply and efficiently.","zh":"計算機使用演算法，而精妙的演算法會以簡單高效方式完成工作。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that music cannot be explained only by clean mathematical rules.","zh":"這個短語暗示音樂不能只用整潔的數學規則來解釋。"},{"en":"It contrasts tidy calculation with messy real-life experience.","zh":"它把整齊計算與混雜的現實生活經驗作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"messy sounds of real life","meaning":"現實生活中混雜的聲音","examples":[{"en":"Music may be shaped by the messy sounds of real life.","zh":"音樂可能由現實生活中混雜的聲音塑造。"},{"en":"Messy sounds of real life are the mixed, imperfect, everyday sounds people actually hear around them.","zh":"messy sounds of real life 是人們在身邊實際聽到的混合、不完美、日常聲音。"},{"en":"Street noise, footsteps, voices, traffic, and birds can all be messy sounds of real life.","zh":"街道噪音、腳步聲、人聲、交通聲和鳥聲都可以是現實生活中混雜的聲音。"},{"en":"These sounds may influence music because human ears develop in ordinary sound environments.","zh":"這些聲音可能影響音樂，因為人類耳朵在普通聲音環境中發展。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts real-world sound with clean abstract theory.","zh":"這個短語把真實世界聲音與乾淨抽象理論作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"speech in particular","meaning":"尤其是說話聲音","examples":[{"en":"Music is shaped by real-life sounds, and by speech in particular.","zh":"音樂由現實生活聲音塑造，尤其是說話聲音。"},{"en":"Speech in particular means speech especially, more than other examples in the group.","zh":"speech in particular 指尤其是說話聲音，比同一組其他例子更重要。"},{"en":"Children learn from sounds around them, and from parents’ speech in particular.","zh":"孩子從身邊聲音中學習，尤其是父母的說話聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows a general idea to the most important specific example.","zh":"這個短語把一般想法收窄到最重要的具體例子。"},{"en":"It tells readers which item deserves special attention.","zh":"它告訴讀者哪一項特別值得注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in turn","meaning":"反過來；繼而","examples":[{"en":"Speech, in turn, is shaped by our evolutionary heritage.","zh":"說話聲音反過來受我們的進化遺產塑造。"},{"en":"In turn means as the next step in a chain of cause and effect.","zh":"in turn 指作為一連串因果中的下一步。"},{"en":"Good sleep improves attention; attention, in turn, helps students learn faster.","zh":"良好睡眠改善注意力；注意力繼而幫助學生學得更快。"},{"en":"The phrase links one effect to the next effect.","zh":"這個短語把一個結果連到下一個結果。"},{"en":"It helps writers show a sequence of connected influences.","zh":"它幫助作者顯示一連串相連影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"evolutionary heritage","meaning":"進化遺產","examples":[{"en":"Speech is shaped by our evolutionary heritage.","zh":"說話聲音受我們的進化遺產塑造。"},{"en":"Evolutionary heritage means traits, abilities, or patterns inherited from the long history of human evolution.","zh":"evolutionary heritage 指由人類漫長進化歷史繼承下來的特徵、能力或模式。"},{"en":"Our ability to learn language may be part of our evolutionary heritage.","zh":"我們學習語言的能力可能是進化遺產的一部分。"},{"en":"Evolutionary heritage can influence behaviour even when people are not aware of it.","zh":"進化遺產可以在人們沒有意識到的情況下影響行為。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what modern humans carry from their biological past.","zh":"這個短語描述現代人從生物過去承載下來的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be rooted in biology","meaning":"根植於生物學","examples":[{"en":"The explanation of music must be rooted in biology.","zh":"對音樂的解釋必須根植於生物學。"},{"en":"To be rooted in biology means to be based on the body, brain, evolution, or living systems.","zh":"be rooted in biology 指以身體、大腦、進化或生命系統為基礎。"},{"en":"A fear of loud sudden sounds may be rooted in biology because it helps people notice danger.","zh":"對突然巨響的恐懼可能根植於生物學，因為它幫助人注意危險。"},{"en":"If music is rooted in biology, it is not just a cultural decoration.","zh":"如果音樂根植於生物學，它就不只是文化裝飾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a deep biological foundation.","zh":"這個短語描述深層生物基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not in numbers per se","meaning":"不是數字本身","examples":[{"en":"The explanation lies in biology, not in numbers per se.","zh":"解釋在於生物學，而不是數字本身。"},{"en":"Not in numbers per se means not in numbers themselves, even if numbers may still be involved.","zh":"not in numbers per se 指不是在數字本身，即使數字仍可能有關。"},{"en":"A student’s progress lies in practice, not in test scores per se.","zh":"學生的進步在於練習，而不是測驗分數本身。"},{"en":"The phrase separates a surface measure from the deeper cause.","zh":"這個短語把表面量度與更深原因分開。"},{"en":"It means the real explanation is not the thing people may first focus on.","zh":"它表示真正解釋不是人們最先注意到的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a vast selection of","meaning":"大量不同的……","examples":[{"en":"The researchers analysed a vast selection of speech sounds.","zh":"研究人員分析了大量不同的語音。"},{"en":"A vast selection of something means a very large and varied collection.","zh":"vast selection of 某物，指非常龐大且多樣的集合。"},{"en":"A library offers a vast selection of books for readers with different interests.","zh":"圖書館為有不同興趣的讀者提供大量不同的書籍。"},{"en":"A large selection helps researchers avoid relying on only a few examples.","zh":"大量選擇幫助研究人員避免只依賴少數例子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both size and variety.","zh":"這個短語同時描述數量和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"speech sounds","meaning":"語音","examples":[{"en":"The study examined speech sounds from many languages.","zh":"該研究檢視了許多語言中的語音。"},{"en":"Speech sounds are the sounds people produce when speaking, such as vowels, consonants, tones, and rhythms.","zh":"speech sounds 是人們說話時產生的聲音，例如元音、輔音、聲調和節奏。"},{"en":"Language learners practise speech sounds when they repeat difficult pronunciation.","zh":"語言學習者重複困難發音時，就是在練習語音。"},{"en":"Speech sounds can be studied without looking at meaning or grammar.","zh":"語音可以在不考慮意思或文法的情況下被研究。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the raw sounds of spoken language.","zh":"這個短語指口語語言的原始聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a variety of languages","meaning":"多種語言","examples":[{"en":"The researchers collected speech sounds from a variety of languages.","zh":"研究人員從多種語言中收集語音。"},{"en":"A variety of languages means several different languages, often from different groups or places.","zh":"variety of languages 指幾種不同語言，常來自不同群體或地方。"},{"en":"A school festival may include songs in a variety of languages.","zh":"學校節日可能包括多種語言的歌曲。"},{"en":"Studying many languages helps researchers find patterns that are not limited to one culture.","zh":"研究多種語言幫助研究人員找到不限於單一文化的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes linguistic diversity.","zh":"這個短語描述語言多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reveal the underlying patterns","meaning":"揭示深層模式","examples":[{"en":"The analysis revealed the underlying patterns common to speech.","zh":"分析揭示了語音共有的深層模式。"},{"en":"To reveal the underlying patterns means to show the hidden regular structures beneath surface differences.","zh":"reveal the underlying patterns 指顯示表面差異之下隱藏的規律結構。"},{"en":"A teacher may reveal the underlying patterns in grammar by comparing several example sentences.","zh":"老師可能透過比較幾個例句，揭示文法中的深層模式。"},{"en":"Finding hidden patterns helps people understand why many examples behave similarly.","zh":"找出隱藏模式幫助人理解為何許多例子有相似運作方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making deeper structure visible.","zh":"這個短語描述令深層結構變得可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"common to all utterances","meaning":"所有話語共有的","examples":[{"en":"The researchers looked for patterns common to all utterances.","zh":"研究人員尋找所有話語共有的模式。"},{"en":"Common to all utterances means shared by every piece of spoken language being studied.","zh":"common to all utterances 指被研究的每段口語都共享的特徵。"},{"en":"A speech researcher may look for rhythm patterns common to all utterances in a recording set.","zh":"語音研究者可能在一組錄音中尋找所有話語共有的節奏模式。"},{"en":"Features common to all examples may point to a deep rule or biological pattern.","zh":"所有例子共有的特徵可能指向深層規則或生物模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something shared across all spoken samples.","zh":"這個短語描述所有口語樣本共有的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in order to focus on","meaning":"為了專注於……","examples":[{"en":"In order to focus on raw sounds, they ignored theories of meaning.","zh":"為了專注於原始聲音，他們忽略了意義理論。"},{"en":"In order to focus on something means for the purpose of giving attention mainly to it.","zh":"in order to focus on 某事，指為了主要把注意力放在它上面。"},{"en":"In order to focus on pronunciation, a teacher may ask students to read without discussing meaning first.","zh":"為了專注於發音，老師可能先要求學生朗讀，而不討論意思。"},{"en":"Removing distractions can help researchers focus on one variable more clearly.","zh":"去除干擾可以幫助研究人員更清楚專注於一個變量。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the purpose behind an action.","zh":"這個短語引出某行動背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"raw sounds","meaning":"原始聲音","examples":[{"en":"The researchers focused only on the raw sounds of speech.","zh":"研究人員只專注於說話的原始聲音。"},{"en":"Raw sounds are sounds considered by themselves, before interpretation, meaning, or context is added.","zh":"raw sounds 是在加入詮釋、意義或語境前，單獨被考慮的聲音。"},{"en":"A language teacher may ask students to listen to raw sounds before looking at the written words.","zh":"語言老師可能要求學生先聆聽原始聲音，再看文字。"},{"en":"Studying raw sounds helps researchers analyse pitch, rhythm, and frequency without distraction.","zh":"研究原始聲音幫助研究人員在不受干擾下分析音高、節奏和頻率。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sound as pure audio material.","zh":"這個短語描述作為純粹音頻材料的聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"discard theories about","meaning":"摒棄關於……的理論","examples":[{"en":"They discarded all theories about speech and meaning.","zh":"他們摒棄所有關於語音與意義的理論。"},{"en":"To discard theories about something means to set them aside and not use them for the present analysis.","zh":"discard theories about 某事，指把相關理論放在一旁，在當前分析中不使用。"},{"en":"A researcher may discard theories about student motivation in order to measure only study time.","zh":"研究人員可能暫時摒棄關於學生動機的理論，以便只量度溫習時間。"},{"en":"Discarding a theory temporarily can help focus on raw data.","zh":"暫時摒棄理論可以幫助專注於原始數據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deliberately removing an explanation from consideration.","zh":"這個短語描述有意把某解釋排除在考慮之外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"speech and meaning","meaning":"語音與意義","examples":[{"en":"The study ignored theories about speech and meaning.","zh":"該研究忽略了關於語音與意義的理論。"},{"en":"Speech and meaning refers to spoken sounds and the ideas or messages those sounds carry.","zh":"speech and meaning 指口語聲音，以及這些聲音所承載的想法或信息。"},{"en":"A language lesson may separate speech and meaning by first practising pronunciation and then discussing content.","zh":"語言課可能先練習發音，再討論內容，從而分開語音與意義。"},{"en":"Researchers sometimes separate the sound of words from what the words mean.","zh":"研究人員有時會把詞語聲音與詞語意思分開。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both the sound form and the message of language.","zh":"這個短語描述語言的聲音形式和信息兩方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"slice sentences into random bites","meaning":"將句子切成隨機片段","examples":[{"en":"The researchers sliced sentences into random bites.","zh":"研究人員將句子切成隨機片段。"},{"en":"To slice sentences into random bites means to cut spoken sentences into small, randomly chosen pieces.","zh":"slice sentences into random bites 指把口語句子切成隨機選取的小片段。"},{"en":"A teacher might cut a listening passage into short clips so students focus on sound rather than full meaning.","zh":"老師可能把聆聽文章切成短片段，讓學生專注聲音而非完整意思。"},{"en":"Random pieces help researchers avoid selecting only examples that fit their expectations.","zh":"隨機片段幫助研究人員避免只選擇符合自己預期的例子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes breaking language into small sound segments for analysis.","zh":"這個短語描述把語言拆成小聲音片段以供分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a database of over","meaning":"超過……的資料庫","examples":[{"en":"They used a database of over 100,000 speech segments.","zh":"他們使用一個包含超過十萬個語音片段的資料庫。"},{"en":"A database of over a number means an organised collection containing more than that number of items.","zh":"database of over 某數量，指包含多於該數量項目的有組織資料集合。"},{"en":"A school may keep a database of over 5,000 library books.","zh":"學校可能保存一個超過五千本圖書的資料庫。"},{"en":"A large database gives researchers enough examples to find reliable patterns.","zh":"大型資料庫給研究人員足夠例子來找出可靠模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a big organised set of information.","zh":"這個短語描述大型有組織資訊集合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"brief segments of speech","meaning":"簡短語音片段","examples":[{"en":"The database contained brief segments of speech.","zh":"該資料庫包含簡短語音片段。"},{"en":"Brief segments of speech are short pieces of spoken language.","zh":"brief segments of speech 是短小的口語語言片段。"},{"en":"A pronunciation app may use brief segments of speech to train listening skills.","zh":"發音應用程式可能使用簡短語音片段來訓練聆聽技巧。"},{"en":"Short segments let researchers examine sound patterns without analysing full conversations.","zh":"短片段讓研究人員檢視聲音模式，而不必分析完整對話。"},{"en":"The phrase describes small units of spoken audio.","zh":"這個短語描述口語音頻的小單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have the greatest emphasis","meaning":"有最大的重音；最被強調","examples":[{"en":"They noted which frequency had the greatest emphasis in each sound.","zh":"他們記錄每個聲音中哪個頻率有最大重音。"},{"en":"To have the greatest emphasis means to be the strongest, most noticeable, or most stressed part.","zh":"have the greatest emphasis 指成為最強、最明顯或最被強調的部分。"},{"en":"In a sentence, one word may have the greatest emphasis if the speaker says it louder.","zh":"在一句話中，如果說話者把某個詞說得更大聲，該詞可能有最大重音。"},{"en":"Emphasis helps listeners notice which part of a sound or message matters most.","zh":"重音幫助聽者注意聲音或信息中哪部分最重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the most prominent part of something.","zh":"這個短語描述某物中最突出的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the resulting set of frequencies","meaning":"得出的頻率組合","examples":[{"en":"The resulting set of frequencies corresponded to the chromatic scale.","zh":"得出的頻率組合與半音音階相對應。"},{"en":"The resulting set of frequencies means the group of sound frequencies produced after analysis or calculation.","zh":"resulting set of frequencies 指分析或計算後產生的一組聲音頻率。"},{"en":"After measuring several voices, a researcher may compare the resulting set of frequencies with musical notes.","zh":"量度幾把聲音後，研究人員可能把得出的頻率組合與音符比較。"},{"en":"Results become meaningful when researchers compare them with an existing pattern.","zh":"當研究人員把結果與既有模式比較時，結果就變得有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the final frequency pattern obtained from data.","zh":"這個短語描述從數據中取得的最終頻率模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"correspond closely to","meaning":"與……非常吻合","examples":[{"en":"The frequencies corresponded closely to the chromatic scale.","zh":"這些頻率與半音音階非常吻合。"},{"en":"To correspond closely to something means to match it very nearly or show a strong similarity to it.","zh":"correspond closely to 某物，指與它幾乎相配或顯示強烈相似。"},{"en":"A student’s summary should correspond closely to the main ideas of the passage.","zh":"學生的摘要應與文章主要思想非常吻合。"},{"en":"Close correspondence suggests that two patterns may be related.","zh":"高度吻合暗示兩個模式可能相關。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong match between two things.","zh":"這個短語描述兩件事之間的強烈匹配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in short","meaning":"簡而言之","examples":[{"en":"In short, the building blocks of music are found in speech.","zh":"簡而言之，音樂的基本構成元素可在語音中找到。"},{"en":"In short means to summarise the main point briefly.","zh":"in short 指簡短總結主要重點。"},{"en":"The class is noisy, tired, and confused; in short, the lesson needs a reset.","zh":"班級嘈吵、疲倦又困惑；簡而言之，這堂課需要重新調整。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when they want to reduce a longer explanation to one clear idea.","zh":"當作者想把較長解釋縮減為一個清楚想法時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It signals a compact conclusion.","zh":"它表示一個簡潔結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the building blocks of","meaning":"……的基本構成元素","examples":[{"en":"The building blocks of music are found in speech.","zh":"音樂的基本構成元素可在語音中找到。"},{"en":"The building blocks of something are the basic parts from which it is made.","zh":"building blocks of 某物，是構成它的基本部分。"},{"en":"Vocabulary and grammar are the building blocks of sentence writing.","zh":"詞彙和文法是句子寫作的基本構成元素。"},{"en":"Understanding basic parts helps students understand the whole system more easily.","zh":"理解基本部分幫助學生更容易理解整個系統。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the foundation pieces of a larger structure.","zh":"這個短語描述較大結構的基礎部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be found in speech","meaning":"可在語音中找到","examples":[{"en":"The building blocks of music are to be found in speech.","zh":"音樂的基本構成元素可在語音中找到。"},{"en":"To be found in speech means to exist within the sounds, patterns, or structure of spoken language.","zh":"be found in speech 指存在於口語語言的聲音、模式或結構之中。"},{"en":"Rhythm can be found in speech when a speaker stresses some words more than others.","zh":"當說話者較強調某些詞語時，節奏可在語音中找到。"},{"en":"If musical patterns are found in speech, ordinary talking may help explain music.","zh":"如果音樂模式可在語音中找到，日常說話可能幫助解釋音樂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something being present in spoken language.","zh":"這個短語描述某物存在於口語語言中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"far from being abstract","meaning":"絕非抽象","examples":[{"en":"Far from being abstract, music reflects patterns in speech.","zh":"音樂絕非抽象，而是反映語音中的模式。"},{"en":"Far from being abstract means not abstract at all; instead, connected to concrete experience.","zh":"far from being abstract 指一點也不抽象；相反，與具體經驗相連。"},{"en":"Far from being useless, grammar helps students express ideas clearly.","zh":"文法絕非無用，而是幫助學生清楚表達想法。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly rejects one description and replaces it with another.","zh":"這個短語強烈否定一種描述，並以另一種描述取代。"},{"en":"It is useful when the writer wants to correct a mistaken impression.","zh":"當作者想糾正錯誤印象時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"present a strange analogue to","meaning":"呈現出與……奇妙相似的對應物","examples":[{"en":"Music presents a strange analogue to the patterns of speech.","zh":"音樂呈現出與語音模式奇妙相似的對應物。"},{"en":"To present a strange analogue to something means to show an unusual but similar version of it.","zh":"present a strange analogue to 某事，指展示一種不尋常但相似的版本。"},{"en":"A city map may present a simplified analogue to the real streets outside.","zh":"城市地圖可能呈現出與外面真實街道相似的簡化對應物。"},{"en":"An analogue is not identical, but it shares enough features to invite comparison.","zh":"對應物並不完全相同，但有足夠共同特徵可作比較。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an unexpected parallel between two things.","zh":"這個短語描述兩件事之間出乎意料的平行關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"patterns created by","meaning":"由……產生的模式","examples":[{"en":"Music reflects patterns created by the sounds of speech.","zh":"音樂反映由說話聲音產生的模式。"},{"en":"Patterns created by something are repeated structures or regularities produced by it.","zh":"patterns created by 某物，是由它產生的重複結構或規律。"},{"en":"A timetable shows patterns created by students’ daily movement between classes.","zh":"時間表顯示由學生每天在課堂之間移動產生的模式。"},{"en":"When repeated sounds create patterns, listeners may begin to hear rhythm or melody.","zh":"當重複聲音產生模式，聽者可能開始聽到節奏或旋律。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what produces a pattern.","zh":"這個短語指出模式由甚麼產生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the visual arts","meaning":"視覺藝術","examples":[{"en":"Music, like the visual arts, is rooted in experience.","zh":"音樂像視覺藝術一樣，根植於經驗。"},{"en":"The visual arts are art forms that are mainly seen, such as painting, drawing, sculpture, and photography.","zh":"visual arts 是主要以觀看為主的藝術形式，例如繪畫、素描、雕塑和攝影。"},{"en":"A museum teaches visual arts by showing how artists use colour, shape, and space.","zh":"博物館透過展示藝術家如何使用顏色、形狀和空間來教授視覺藝術。"},{"en":"Visual arts often reflect what people see in nature, cities, and daily life.","zh":"視覺藝術常反映人們在自然、城市和日常生活中看到的東西。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to arts that communicate mainly through sight.","zh":"這個短語指主要透過視覺溝通的藝術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be rooted in our experience of","meaning":"根植於我們對……的經驗","examples":[{"en":"Music is rooted in our experience of the natural world.","zh":"音樂根植於我們對自然世界的經驗。"},{"en":"To be rooted in our experience of something means to grow from what we have heard, seen, felt, or lived through.","zh":"be rooted in our experience of 某事，指從我們聽過、看過、感受過或經歷過的東西中生長出來。"},{"en":"A child’s idea of home may be rooted in her experience of family meals and familiar voices.","zh":"孩子對家的想法可能根植於她對家庭飯局和熟悉聲音的經驗。"},{"en":"If art is rooted in experience, it reflects life rather than floating apart from it.","zh":"如果藝術根植於經驗，它就反映生活，而不是漂浮於生活之外。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a deep connection with lived reality.","zh":"這個短語描述與親身現實的深層連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"emulate our sound environment","meaning":"模仿我們的聲音環境","examples":[{"en":"Music emulates our sound environment.","zh":"音樂模仿我們的聲音環境。"},{"en":"To emulate our sound environment means to imitate or echo the sounds people normally hear around them.","zh":"emulate our sound environment 指模仿或呼應人們平時在身邊聽到的聲音。"},{"en":"A composer may emulate a city sound environment by using rhythms like trains, footsteps, and voices.","zh":"作曲家可能使用像火車、腳步聲和人聲的節奏來模仿城市聲音環境。"},{"en":"Music can feel familiar when it reflects the sound patterns of everyday life.","zh":"當音樂反映日常生活的聲音模式，就可能令人感到熟悉。"},{"en":"The phrase describes music copying or transforming the sounds around us.","zh":"這個短語描述音樂複製或轉化我們身邊的聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the visual environment","meaning":"視覺環境","examples":[{"en":"The visual arts emulate the visual environment.","zh":"視覺藝術模仿視覺環境。"},{"en":"The visual environment is everything people see around them, including objects, landscapes, colours, and movement.","zh":"visual environment 是人們在身邊看見的一切，包括物件、景觀、顏色和動作。"},{"en":"A painter may use the visual environment of a market, with bright signs and moving crowds, as inspiration.","zh":"畫家可能把街市的視覺環境用作靈感，例如鮮艷招牌和移動人群。"},{"en":"Visual surroundings affect what artists notice and choose to represent.","zh":"視覺周遭環境會影響藝術家注意甚麼和選擇呈現甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the world as experienced through sight.","zh":"這個短語描述透過視覺經驗到的世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sound-making instrument","meaning":"發聲工具","examples":[{"en":"The vocal tract is our basic sound-making instrument.","zh":"聲道是我們基本的發聲工具。"},{"en":"A sound-making instrument is something that produces sound.","zh":"sound-making instrument 是能產生聲音的東西。"},{"en":"A flute is a sound-making instrument, but the human voice can also act like one.","zh":"長笛是發聲工具，但人聲也可以像發聲工具一樣運作。"},{"en":"The body produces speech and song by shaping air into sound.","zh":"身體透過把空氣塑造成聲音來產生說話和歌聲。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the tool or body part used to create sound.","zh":"這個短語描述用來創造聲音的工具或身體部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the vocal tract","meaning":"聲道","examples":[{"en":"In music we hear the echo of the vocal tract.","zh":"在音樂中，我們聽到聲道的迴響。"},{"en":"The vocal tract is the part of the body, including the throat, mouth, and nasal passages, used to shape speech sounds.","zh":"vocal tract 是身體中用來塑造語音的部分，包括喉嚨、口腔和鼻腔通道。"},{"en":"A language teacher may explain that the vocal tract changes shape when students pronounce different vowels.","zh":"語言老師可能解釋學生發不同元音時，聲道會改變形狀。"},{"en":"The vocal tract affects pitch, tone, resonance, and speech quality.","zh":"聲道影響音高、音色、共鳴和說話質素。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the body’s main system for shaping voice sounds.","zh":"這個短語指身體塑造人聲的主要系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"mathematical equations","meaning":"數學方程式","examples":[{"en":"The explanation for music may be simpler than mathematical equations.","zh":"對音樂的解釋可能比數學方程式更簡單。"},{"en":"Mathematical equations are number-based statements that show relationships between quantities.","zh":"mathematical equations 是以數字為基礎、顯示數量之間關係的陳述。"},{"en":"A physics teacher may use mathematical equations to explain sound waves.","zh":"物理老師可能使用數學方程式來解釋聲波。"},{"en":"Equations can explain some patterns, but they may not capture every human experience.","zh":"方程式可以解釋某些模式，但未必能捕捉每種人類經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to formal mathematical expressions.","zh":"這個短語指正式數學表達式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be familiar to","meaning":"為……所熟悉","examples":[{"en":"Humans like sounds that are familiar to them.","zh":"人類喜歡為自己所熟悉的聲音。"},{"en":"To be familiar to someone means to be known or recognised by that person.","zh":"be familiar to 某人，指被該人認識或辨認。"},{"en":"A childhood song may be familiar to an adult even after many years.","zh":"童年歌曲即使多年後，仍可能為成人所熟悉。"},{"en":"Familiar sounds can feel comforting because they connect with past experience.","zh":"熟悉聲音可以令人感到安慰，因為它們連接過往經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recognition from the listener’s point of view.","zh":"這個短語從聽者角度描述熟悉感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"remind us of","meaning":"令……想起","examples":[{"en":"We like sounds that remind us of ourselves.","zh":"我們喜歡令我們想起自己的聲音。"},{"en":"To remind us of something means to make us think of it or feel connected to it.","zh":"remind us of 某事，指令我們想到它或感到與它有連繫。"},{"en":"The smell of school lunches may remind adults of childhood.","zh":"學校午餐的氣味可能令成人想起童年。"},{"en":"Music can feel powerful when it reminds us of home, family, or our own voice.","zh":"當音樂令我們想起家、家庭或自己的聲音，它可以很有力量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a sound, sight, or experience bringing another thing to mind.","zh":"這個短語描述聲音、景象或經驗把另一事物帶到腦海中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"chicken-or-egg evolutionary questions","meaning":"先有雞還是先有蛋的進化問題","examples":[{"en":"The theory raises chicken-or-egg evolutionary questions.","zh":"這個理論提出先有雞還是先有蛋的進化問題。"},{"en":"Chicken-or-egg evolutionary questions ask which of two related things came first in evolution.","zh":"chicken-or-egg evolutionary questions 是問兩件相關事物在進化中哪一個先出現。"},{"en":"Scientists may ask a chicken-or-egg question about whether social life shaped language or language shaped social life.","zh":"科學家可能問一個先有雞還是先有蛋的問題：是社會生活塑造語言，還是語言塑造社會生活。"},{"en":"Such questions are difficult because two developments may have influenced each other.","zh":"這類問題困難，因為兩種發展可能互相影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a problem where cause and origin are hard to separate.","zh":"這個短語描述因果和起源難以分開的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"imitate speech directly","meaning":"直接模仿說話","examples":[{"en":"Music may imitate speech directly.","zh":"音樂可能直接模仿說話。"},{"en":"To imitate speech directly means to copy the sounds, rhythm, pitch, or patterns of spoken language closely.","zh":"imitate speech directly 指緊密複製口語的聲音、節奏、音高或模式。"},{"en":"A song may imitate speech directly when its melody follows the rise and fall of natural conversation.","zh":"當歌曲旋律跟隨自然對話的高低起伏，它可能直接模仿說話。"},{"en":"Direct imitation would suggest that music takes material from spoken language.","zh":"直接模仿會暗示音樂從口語中取材。"},{"en":"The phrase describes music closely copying how people talk.","zh":"這個短語描述音樂緊密複製人們說話的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in which case","meaning":"在這種情況下","examples":[{"en":"Music may imitate speech, in which case language evolved first.","zh":"音樂可能模仿說話；在這種情況下，語言可能率先演化。"},{"en":"In which case means if that situation is true, then the following result or conclusion follows.","zh":"in which case 指如果該情況為真，那麼接下來的結果或結論就成立。"},{"en":"The bus may be late, in which case we should take the train.","zh":"巴士可能遲到；在這種情況下，我們應乘火車。"},{"en":"The phrase links a possible condition with its logical consequence.","zh":"這個短語把可能條件與其邏輯後果連起來。"},{"en":"It is useful for exploring alternative explanations.","zh":"它有助探索不同解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"evolve first","meaning":"率先演化","examples":[{"en":"If music imitates speech, language may have evolved first.","zh":"如果音樂模仿說話，語言可能率先演化。"},{"en":"To evolve first means to develop earlier in evolutionary history than another trait or ability.","zh":"evolve first 指在進化歷史中比另一特徵或能力更早發展。"},{"en":"Some scientists ask whether gestures evolved first before spoken language.","zh":"有些科學家問手勢是否在口語之前率先演化。"},{"en":"Knowing what evolved first helps explain which ability may have shaped the other.","zh":"知道甚麼率先演化，有助解釋哪種能力可能塑造另一種。"},{"en":"The phrase describes order of development in evolution.","zh":"這個短語描述進化中的發展次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"it is conceivable that","meaning":"可以想像；有可能","examples":[{"en":"It is conceivable that music came before language.","zh":"可以想像音樂早於語言出現。"},{"en":"It is conceivable that means it is possible to imagine or reasonably consider that something may be true.","zh":"it is conceivable that 指可以想像或合理考慮某事可能是真的。"},{"en":"It is conceivable that future classrooms will mix online and face-to-face teaching permanently.","zh":"可以想像未來課室會永久混合網上和面授教學。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a possibility without claiming certainty.","zh":"這個短語引出一種可能性，而不是聲稱確定。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing theories that cannot be proved easily.","zh":"當討論不易證明的理論時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in effect","meaning":"實際上","examples":[{"en":"Language may be, in effect, an imitation of song.","zh":"語言實際上可能是對歌曲的模仿。"},{"en":"In effect means in practical meaning or real result, even if not officially described that way.","zh":"in effect 指在實際意思或真實結果上，即使官方上不這樣描述。"},{"en":"If a student does all the group work alone, the group project is, in effect, an individual project.","zh":"如果學生獨自完成所有小組工作，這個小組項目實際上就是個人項目。"},{"en":"The phrase helps explain the real function of something.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋某事的真正功能。"},{"en":"It often means “basically” or “for practical purposes”.","zh":"它常表示「基本上」或「就實際而言」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"an imitation of song","meaning":"對歌曲的模仿","examples":[{"en":"Language could be an imitation of song.","zh":"語言可能是對歌曲的模仿。"},{"en":"An imitation of song means something that copies the sound, rhythm, or melodic quality of singing.","zh":"imitation of song 指某物複製歌唱的聲音、節奏或旋律特質。"},{"en":"A baby’s playful speech may sound like an imitation of song when it rises and falls musically.","zh":"嬰兒玩耍式說話若有音樂般高低起伏，可能聽起來像對歌曲的模仿。"},{"en":"If language began as song-like sound, speech and music may share a deep origin.","zh":"如果語言始於像歌曲的聲音，說話和音樂可能有深層共同起源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes speech as possibly copied from musical vocal patterns.","zh":"這個短語把說話描述為可能複製音樂性發聲模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"everyday speech","meaning":"日常說話","examples":[{"en":"In everyday speech, we may hit musical notes we especially like.","zh":"在日常說話中，我們可能碰到自己特別喜歡的音符。"},{"en":"Everyday speech is ordinary talking used in daily life, not formal performance or writing.","zh":"everyday speech 是日常生活中使用的普通說話，而不是正式表演或寫作。"},{"en":"People use everyday speech when ordering food, greeting friends, or asking for directions.","zh":"人們點餐、問候朋友或問路時，都在使用日常說話。"},{"en":"Everyday speech still has rhythm, pitch, and melody-like movement.","zh":"日常說話仍有節奏、音高和類似旋律的變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes normal spoken language in ordinary situations.","zh":"這個短語描述普通情境中的正常口語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"musical notes","meaning":"音符","examples":[{"en":"In speech, we may use musical notes we especially like.","zh":"在說話中，我們可能使用自己特別喜歡的音符。"},{"en":"Musical notes are individual pitches used in music.","zh":"musical notes 是音樂中使用的個別音高。"},{"en":"A piano student learns musical notes by naming and playing them one by one.","zh":"鋼琴學生透過逐一命名和彈奏來學習音符。"},{"en":"Notes can create melody when they are arranged in a meaningful order.","zh":"當音符以有意義的次序排列，就能創造旋律。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the basic pitch units of music.","zh":"這個短語指音樂中的基本音高單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"alternatively","meaning":"另一種可能是","examples":[{"en":"Alternatively, music may imitate the human sound-making system.","zh":"另一種可能是，音樂模仿人類發聲系統。"},{"en":"Alternatively means as another possible choice, explanation, or way of thinking.","zh":"alternatively 指作為另一種可能選擇、解釋或思考方式。"},{"en":"We can take the bus; alternatively, we can walk if the weather is good.","zh":"我們可以乘巴士；另一種可能是，如果天氣好，我們可以步行。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a different possibility after one idea has already been given.","zh":"這個短語在已提出一個想法後，引入另一種可能性。"},{"en":"It helps writers compare alternative explanations.","zh":"它幫助作者比較不同解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the general products of","meaning":"……的一般產物","examples":[{"en":"Music may imitate the general products of the human sound-making system.","zh":"音樂可能模仿人類發聲系統的一般產物。"},{"en":"The general products of a system are the usual things that system produces.","zh":"general products of 某系統，是該系統通常產生的東西。"},{"en":"The general products of a school writing programme may include essays, reports, and presentations.","zh":"學校寫作課程的一般產物可能包括文章、報告和簡報。"},{"en":"If music imitates vocal products, it may reflect many human sounds, not speech alone.","zh":"如果音樂模仿聲音產物，它可能反映許多人類聲音，而不只是說話。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the broad output of a system.","zh":"這個短語描述一個系統的廣泛輸出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the human sound-making system","meaning":"人類發聲系統","examples":[{"en":"Music and language come from the human sound-making system.","zh":"音樂和語言來自人類發聲系統。"},{"en":"The human sound-making system is the body system that produces speech, song, cries, laughter, and other vocal sounds.","zh":"human sound-making system 是產生說話、歌唱、哭聲、笑聲和其他人聲的身體系統。"},{"en":"The lungs, vocal cords, mouth, and tongue all help the human sound-making system work.","zh":"肺、聲帶、口腔和舌頭都幫助人類發聲系統運作。"},{"en":"Because music and speech use the same body, they may share sound patterns.","zh":"因為音樂和說話使用同一身體，它們可能共享聲音模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the biological system behind human voice.","zh":"這個短語描述人聲背後的生物系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"happen to be","meaning":"碰巧是","examples":[{"en":"The human sound-making system happens to be mostly speech.","zh":"人類發聲系統碰巧主要是說話。"},{"en":"Happen to be means to be the case, often by chance or circumstance rather than deliberate design.","zh":"happen to be 指情況正是如此，常帶有偶然或情況使然，而非刻意設計。"},{"en":"The quietest room happens to be next to the library, so students use it for study.","zh":"最安靜的房間碰巧在圖書館旁邊，所以學生用它來溫習。"},{"en":"The phrase can make a statement sound less forced and more observational.","zh":"這個短語可以令陳述聽起來較不生硬，更像觀察所得。"},{"en":"It describes something that turns out to be true.","zh":"它描述某事結果正好是真的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"come from the same system","meaning":"來自同一系統","examples":[{"en":"Music and language both come from the same system.","zh":"音樂和語言都來自同一系統。"},{"en":"To come from the same system means to originate from one shared source or mechanism.","zh":"come from the same system 指源自一個共同來源或機制。"},{"en":"Two different school rules may come from the same system of safety concerns.","zh":"兩條不同校規可能來自同一套安全考慮系統。"},{"en":"If two abilities come from the same system, they may influence each other.","zh":"如果兩種能力來自同一系統，它們可能互相影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shared origin.","zh":"這個短語描述共同起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"shape our preferences","meaning":"塑造我們的偏好","examples":[{"en":"The sound-making system shapes our preferences.","zh":"發聲系統塑造我們的偏好。"},{"en":"To shape our preferences means to influence what we like, choose, or feel comfortable with.","zh":"shape our preferences 指影響我們喜歡、選擇或感到舒服的東西。"},{"en":"Childhood meals can shape our preferences for certain flavours.","zh":"童年飯菜可以塑造我們對某些味道的偏好。"},{"en":"Repeated experience shapes preferences because familiar patterns become easier to enjoy.","zh":"重複經驗會塑造偏好，因為熟悉模式變得更容易令人喜歡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how likes and dislikes are formed.","zh":"這個短語描述喜好和厭惡如何形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"cast light on","meaning":"闡明；使……更清楚","examples":[{"en":"Schwartz’s study casts light on how animals may understand music.","zh":"Schwartz 的研究闡明了動物可能如何理解音樂。"},{"en":"To cast light on something means to help explain it or make it easier to understand.","zh":"cast light on 某事，指幫助解釋它或令它更容易理解。"},{"en":"A student’s diary can cast light on why she has been absent from school.","zh":"學生的日記可以闡明她為何一直缺課。"},{"en":"New evidence casts light on a problem when it reveals causes or patterns.","zh":"當新證據揭示原因或模式，它就能使問題更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making something clearer.","zh":"這個短語描述令某事更清晰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the long-running question of whether","meaning":"關於是否……的長期爭論問題","examples":[{"en":"The study addresses the long-running question of whether animals appreciate music.","zh":"該研究處理動物是否欣賞音樂這個長期爭論問題。"},{"en":"The long-running question of whether means a question that has been debated for a long time.","zh":"long-running question of whether 指一個已被討論很久的問題。"},{"en":"Teachers still discuss the long-running question of whether exams measure real ability.","zh":"老師仍在討論考試是否量度真正能力這個長期爭論問題。"},{"en":"Long-running questions continue because evidence is incomplete or people interpret it differently.","zh":"長期爭論問題持續存在，因為證據不完整或人們有不同詮釋。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an old unresolved debate.","zh":"這個短語引出古老而未解決的爭論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"appreciate music","meaning":"欣賞音樂","examples":[{"en":"Scientists ask whether animals understand or appreciate music.","zh":"科學家問動物是否理解或欣賞音樂。"},{"en":"To appreciate music means to enjoy, recognise, or value music in some meaningful way.","zh":"appreciate music 指以某種有意義方式享受、辨認或重視音樂。"},{"en":"A child may appreciate music by moving to the rhythm even before learning note names.","zh":"孩子即使未學音名，也可能透過隨節奏移動來欣賞音樂。"},{"en":"Appreciation can include emotional response, recognition, or preference.","zh":"欣賞可以包括情緒反應、辨認或偏好。"},{"en":"The phrase describes more than hearing sound; it suggests meaningful response.","zh":"這個短語描述的不只是聽到聲音，而是有意義的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the apparent abundance of","meaning":"表面上大量的……","examples":[{"en":"There is an apparent abundance of music in the natural world.","zh":"自然世界中表面上有大量音樂。"},{"en":"The apparent abundance of something means there seems to be a large amount of it.","zh":"apparent abundance of 某物，指看似有大量該事物。"},{"en":"There is an apparent abundance of advice online, but not all of it is reliable.","zh":"網上表面上有大量建議，但並非全部可靠。"},{"en":"“Apparent” warns that what seems plentiful may need closer examination.","zh":"“Apparent” 提醒讀者，看似很多的東西可能需要仔細檢視。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that looks common or plentiful at first.","zh":"這個短語描述某事起初看似常見或豐富。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"birdsong","meaning":"鳥鳴；鳥歌","examples":[{"en":"Birdsong is one example of music-like sound in nature.","zh":"鳥鳴是自然界中類似音樂聲音的一個例子。"},{"en":"Birdsong means the patterned sounds birds make, often to communicate or attract mates.","zh":"birdsong 指鳥類發出的有模式聲音，常用於溝通或吸引伴侶。"},{"en":"People may hear birdsong early in the morning near trees or parks.","zh":"人們可能在清晨靠近樹木或公園時聽到鳥鳴。"},{"en":"Birdsong can sound musical because it often has rhythm, repetition, and pitch changes.","zh":"鳥鳴可以聽起來像音樂，因為它常有節奏、重複和音高變化。"},{"en":"The word describes natural bird vocal sounds that resemble song.","zh":"這個詞描述類似歌聲的自然鳥類發聲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"whalesong","meaning":"鯨歌","examples":[{"en":"Whalesong is often compared with music.","zh":"鯨歌常被拿來與音樂比較。"},{"en":"Whalesong means the long, patterned vocal sounds produced by whales.","zh":"whalesong 指鯨魚發出的長而有模式的聲音。"},{"en":"A documentary may play whalesong to show how whales communicate across the ocean.","zh":"紀錄片可能播放鯨歌，以展示鯨魚如何在海洋中溝通。"},{"en":"Whalesong sounds musical to humans because it can include repeated patterns and changing tones.","zh":"鯨歌對人類來說像音樂，因為它可以包括重複模式和變化音調。"},{"en":"The word describes whale vocalisations that resemble song.","zh":"這個詞描述類似歌聲的鯨魚發聲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"wolf howls","meaning":"狼嚎","examples":[{"en":"Wolf howls are part of the natural soundscape.","zh":"狼嚎是自然聲音景觀的一部分。"},{"en":"Wolf howls are long loud calls made by wolves, often to communicate across distance.","zh":"wolf howls 是狼發出的長而響亮叫聲，常用於遠距離溝通。"},{"en":"A wolf may howl to keep contact with its pack.","zh":"狼可能嚎叫來與狼群保持聯繫。"},{"en":"Howls can sound musical because they rise, fall, and carry through open spaces.","zh":"嚎叫可以聽起來有音樂感，因為它會升降並在空曠地方傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a natural animal sound rather than human music.","zh":"這個短語描述自然動物聲音，而不是人類音樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"synchronised chimpanzee hooting","meaning":"同步的黑猩猩叫聲","examples":[{"en":"Synchronised chimpanzee hooting may sound musical to humans.","zh":"同步的黑猩猩叫聲對人類來說可能聽起來有音樂感。"},{"en":"Synchronised chimpanzee hooting means chimpanzees calling out together in a coordinated pattern.","zh":"synchronised chimpanzee hooting 指黑猩猩以協調模式一起叫喊。"},{"en":"People at a zoo may hear several chimpanzees hooting at the same time.","zh":"人們在動物園可能聽到幾隻黑猩猩同時叫。"},{"en":"Synchronised calling can sound rhythmic because the animals produce repeated sounds together.","zh":"同步叫聲可以聽起來有節奏，因為動物一起產生重複聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes coordinated animal vocal behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述協調的動物發聲行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"previous studies have found that","meaning":"以往研究發現","examples":[{"en":"Previous studies have found that animals react differently to human music.","zh":"以往研究發現，動物對人類音樂有不同反應。"},{"en":"Previous studies have found that means earlier research has produced this result or conclusion.","zh":"previous studies have found that 指早期研究已產生這個結果或結論。"},{"en":"Previous studies have found that sleep affects memory, so a new study may test why.","zh":"以往研究發現睡眠會影響記憶，因此新研究可能測試原因。"},{"en":"The phrase uses past research to support the discussion.","zh":"這個短語使用過往研究來支持討論。"},{"en":"It tells readers that the claim is not based only on the present writer’s opinion.","zh":"它告訴讀者，該主張不只是基於當前作者的意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"laboratory animals","meaning":"實驗動物","examples":[{"en":"Laboratory animals do not always show interest in human music.","zh":"實驗動物不一定對人類音樂表現出興趣。"},{"en":"Laboratory animals are animals used in controlled scientific experiments.","zh":"laboratory animals 是用於受控科學實驗的動物。"},{"en":"Mice, rats, and monkeys may be laboratory animals in studies of hearing or behaviour.","zh":"老鼠、大鼠和猴子可能是聽覺或行為研究中的實驗動物。"},{"en":"Studying laboratory animals helps scientists control conditions more carefully than in the wild.","zh":"研究實驗動物幫助科學家比在野外更仔細控制條件。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to animals used for research, not pets or wild animals.","zh":"這個短語指用於研究的動物，而不是寵物或野生動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"show a great affinity for","meaning":"對……表現出強烈喜好","examples":[{"en":"Many laboratory animals do not show a great affinity for human music.","zh":"許多實驗動物並沒有對人類音樂表現出強烈喜好。"},{"en":"To show a great affinity for something means to show strong liking, attraction, or natural connection to it.","zh":"show a great affinity for 某物，指對它表現出強烈喜愛、吸引或自然連繫。"},{"en":"A child may show a great affinity for rhythm if she starts clapping whenever music plays.","zh":"如果孩子每次音樂響起都開始拍手，她可能對節奏表現出強烈喜好。"},{"en":"If animals do not show affinity for human music, they may not experience it as humans do.","zh":"如果動物沒有對人類音樂表現出喜好，牠們可能不像人類那樣經驗它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong preference or natural attraction.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈偏好或自然吸引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the human variety of music-making","meaning":"人類形式的音樂創作","examples":[{"en":"Animals may not respond strongly to the human variety of music-making.","zh":"動物可能不會強烈回應人類形式的音樂創作。"},{"en":"The human variety of music-making means the kinds of music humans create, organise, and enjoy.","zh":"human variety of music-making 指人類創造、組織和享受的各類音樂。"},{"en":"Human music-making includes singing, instruments, rhythm, melody, harmony, and performance.","zh":"人類音樂創作包括歌唱、樂器、節奏、旋律、和聲和表演。"},{"en":"Animals may prefer sounds shaped by their own species rather than human musical patterns.","zh":"動物可能較偏好由自身物種塑造的聲音，而不是人類音樂模式。"},{"en":"The phrase distinguishes human music from animal sound behaviour.","zh":"這個短語把人類音樂與動物聲音行為區分開來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"create or perceive music","meaning":"創作或感知音樂","examples":[{"en":"Animals do not create or perceive music the way humans do.","zh":"動物不像人類那樣創作或感知音樂。"},{"en":"To create or perceive music means to make music or mentally recognise it as music.","zh":"create or perceive music 指製作音樂，或在心理上把它辨認為音樂。"},{"en":"A child creates music by humming a tune and perceives music when she recognises rhythm in a song.","zh":"孩子哼唱旋律是在創作音樂；她辨認歌曲節奏時是在感知音樂。"},{"en":"Creating and perceiving involve both producing sound and understanding sound patterns.","zh":"創作和感知同時涉及產生聲音和理解聲音模式。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both making music and experiencing it.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋製作音樂和經驗音樂兩方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the way we do","meaning":"像我們一樣","examples":[{"en":"Animals may not perceive music the way we do.","zh":"動物可能不像我們一樣感知音樂。"},{"en":"The way we do means in the same manner or with the same experience as humans.","zh":"the way we do 指以與人類相同的方式或經驗。"},{"en":"Dogs may hear a doorbell, but they may not understand it the way we do.","zh":"狗可能聽到門鐘，但未必像我們一樣理解它。"},{"en":"The phrase compares another being’s experience with our own human experience.","zh":"這個短語把另一種生物的經驗與我們人類自己的經驗作比較。"},{"en":"It reminds readers that similar behaviour may not mean identical understanding.","zh":"它提醒讀者，相似行為不一定代表相同理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"recognition of human tunes","meaning":"辨認人類旋律","examples":[{"en":"Monkeys can show recognition of human tunes.","zh":"猴子可以顯示出辨認人類旋律的能力。"},{"en":"Recognition of human tunes means the ability to notice or identify melodies created by humans.","zh":"recognition of human tunes 指注意到或識別由人類創造的旋律的能力。"},{"en":"A child shows recognition of a tune when she smiles as a familiar cartoon song begins.","zh":"當熟悉的卡通歌曲響起時，孩子微笑，就是顯示辨認旋律。"},{"en":"Recognition does not always mean full musical understanding or enjoyment.","zh":"辨認不一定代表完整音樂理解或享受。"},{"en":"The phrase describes identifying a melody as familiar.","zh":"這個短語描述把旋律辨認為熟悉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"evidence of","meaning":"……的證據","examples":[{"en":"This recognition is evidence of shared auditory features.","zh":"這種辨認是共同聽覺特徵的證據。"},{"en":"Evidence of something is information that supports the idea that it exists or is true.","zh":"evidence of 某事，是支持它存在或為真的資訊。"},{"en":"A high fever can be evidence of infection, though doctors may need more tests.","zh":"高燒可以是感染的證據，雖然醫生可能需要更多檢查。"},{"en":"Evidence helps people move from guessing to a stronger conclusion.","zh":"證據幫助人由猜測走向較有力的結論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes support for a claim.","zh":"這個短語描述對主張的支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"shared general features","meaning":"共同的一般特徵","examples":[{"en":"Humans and monkeys have shared general features of the auditory system.","zh":"人類和猴子有聽覺系統的共同一般特徵。"},{"en":"Shared general features are broad characteristics that two or more groups have in common.","zh":"shared general features 是兩個或以上群體共同擁有的廣泛特徵。"},{"en":"Two schools may have shared general features, such as classrooms, timetables, and exams.","zh":"兩所學校可能有共同一般特徵，例如課室、時間表和考試。"},{"en":"Shared features can explain why different groups respond similarly in some situations.","zh":"共同特徵可以解釋為何不同群體在某些情況中有相似反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes common traits at a broad level.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛層面的共同特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the auditory system","meaning":"聽覺系統","examples":[{"en":"The auditory system allows humans and animals to perceive sound.","zh":"聽覺系統讓人類和動物感知聲音。"},{"en":"The auditory system is the body and brain system used for hearing and processing sound.","zh":"auditory system 是用來聽見和處理聲音的身體和大腦系統。"},{"en":"The ears collect sound, but the auditory system also includes brain areas that interpret it.","zh":"耳朵收集聲音，但聽覺系統也包括詮釋聲音的大腦區域。"},{"en":"If the auditory system is damaged, a person may have difficulty hearing speech or music.","zh":"如果聽覺系統受損，人可能難以聽見說話或音樂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the biological system behind hearing.","zh":"這個短語描述聽覺背後的生物系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"specific musical ability","meaning":"特有的音樂能力","examples":[{"en":"The study does not prove specific monkey musical ability.","zh":"該研究並不能證明猴子有特有的音樂能力。"},{"en":"Specific musical ability means a clear, specialised ability to understand, make, or respond to music as music.","zh":"specific musical ability 指明確而專門地理解、創作或回應音樂作為音樂的能力。"},{"en":"A child who can identify chords may have a specific musical ability beyond simply hearing sounds.","zh":"能辨認和弦的孩子可能有超越單純聽聲音的特有音樂能力。"},{"en":"Recognising a tune is not enough to prove a full musical ability.","zh":"辨認旋律不足以證明完整音樂能力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a specialised music-related skill.","zh":"這個短語描述專門的音樂相關技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"as for","meaning":"至於","examples":[{"en":"As for birds, they usually recognise their own tunes.","zh":"至於鳥類，牠們通常能辨認自己的旋律。"},{"en":"As for introduces a new topic or shifts attention to a particular person or group.","zh":"as for 引入新主題，或把注意力轉到特定人物或群體。"},{"en":"As for homework, the teacher said it must be submitted online.","zh":"至於功課，老師說必須網上提交。"},{"en":"The phrase helps organise discussion by moving from one example to another.","zh":"這個短語透過由一個例子轉到另一個例子來組織討論。"},{"en":"It means “with regard to” or “speaking about”.","zh":"它的意思是「關於」或「說到」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"musical beasts","meaning":"具音樂感的生物","examples":[{"en":"Birds are described as musical beasts.","zh":"鳥類被描述為具音樂感的生物。"},{"en":"Musical beasts means animals that seem to produce sounds resembling music.","zh":"musical beasts 指似乎能發出類似音樂聲音的動物。"},{"en":"A singing bird may be called a musical beast because its calls have pattern and melody.","zh":"會唱歌的鳥可能被稱為具音樂感的生物，因為其叫聲有模式和旋律。"},{"en":"The phrase is slightly playful and gives animals a music-like quality.","zh":"這個短語略帶玩味，賦予動物音樂般特質。"},{"en":"It describes animals through the way their sounds appear to humans.","zh":"它透過動物聲音在人類聽來的感覺來描述動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"recognise their own tunes","meaning":"辨認自己的旋律","examples":[{"en":"Birds generally recognise their own tunes.","zh":"鳥類通常能辨認自己的旋律。"},{"en":"To recognise their own tunes means to identify songs or calls typical of their own species or group.","zh":"recognise their own tunes 指識別其自身物種或群體典型的歌聲或叫聲。"},{"en":"A bird may respond when it hears a familiar call from its mate.","zh":"鳥聽到伴侶熟悉叫聲時，可能會作出回應。"},{"en":"Recognition of familiar sounds helps animals communicate and avoid confusion.","zh":"辨認熟悉聲音幫助動物溝通並避免混亂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes identifying familiar song patterns.","zh":"這個短語描述識別熟悉歌曲模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a narrow repertoire","meaning":"有限的曲目範圍","examples":[{"en":"Birds have a narrow repertoire of songs.","zh":"鳥類有有限的曲目範圍。"},{"en":"A narrow repertoire means a limited range of songs, skills, behaviours, or choices.","zh":"narrow repertoire 指歌曲、技能、行為或選擇的範圍有限。"},{"en":"A beginner pianist may have a narrow repertoire and play only three simple songs.","zh":"初學鋼琴者可能曲目範圍有限，只會彈三首簡單歌曲。"},{"en":"A narrow repertoire limits variety because the performer repeats the same few options.","zh":"有限曲目範圍限制多樣性，因為表演者反覆使用少數選項。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small set of available patterns.","zh":"這個短語描述可用模式的小集合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"generate novel melodies","meaning":"創作全新旋律","examples":[{"en":"Birds do not generate novel melodies like humans do.","zh":"鳥類不像人類那樣創作全新旋律。"},{"en":"To generate novel melodies means to create new tunes that have not simply been repeated from memory.","zh":"generate novel melodies 指創造新的曲調，而不只是憑記憶重複。"},{"en":"A songwriter generates novel melodies when she experiments with new note patterns.","zh":"作曲人嘗試新的音符模式時，就是在創作全新旋律。"},{"en":"Novel melody generation requires flexibility and creativity.","zh":"創作全新旋律需要靈活性和創造力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating original musical patterns.","zh":"這個短語描述創造原創音樂模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"avian Mozarts","meaning":"鳥類莫扎特；極具音樂創造力的鳥","examples":[{"en":"There are no avian Mozarts among birds.","zh":"鳥類之中沒有鳥類莫扎特。"},{"en":"Avian Mozarts means birds with extraordinary, human-like musical creativity, compared playfully to Mozart.","zh":"avian Mozarts 指被玩味地比作莫扎特、具有非凡人類式音樂創造力的鳥。"},{"en":"Calling a child a “little Mozart” suggests unusual musical talent.","zh":"稱孩子為「小莫扎特」，暗示他有不尋常音樂天分。"},{"en":"Saying there are no avian Mozarts means birds do not seem to compose new music like great human composers.","zh":"說沒有鳥類莫扎特，意思是鳥類似乎不像偉大人類作曲家那樣創作新音樂。"},{"en":"The phrase is a humorous way to deny advanced bird musical creativity.","zh":"這個短語以幽默方式否定鳥類有高階音樂創造力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"evolve preferences for sound","meaning":"演化出對聲音的偏好","examples":[{"en":"Animals may evolve preferences for sound in their own environment.","zh":"動物可能在自身環境中演化出對聲音的偏好。"},{"en":"To evolve preferences for sound means to develop liking or sensitivity to certain sounds through evolution.","zh":"evolve preferences for sound 指透過進化發展出對某些聲音的喜好或敏感度。"},{"en":"A species may evolve a preference for calls that travel well in its habitat.","zh":"某物種可能演化出對能在其棲息地清楚傳播的叫聲的偏好。"},{"en":"Sound preferences can help animals communicate, find mates, or avoid danger.","zh":"聲音偏好可以幫助動物溝通、尋找伴侶或避開危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sound-related preferences shaped over generations.","zh":"這個短語描述經過多代塑造的聲音相關偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"based upon","meaning":"以……為基礎","examples":[{"en":"Animals may prefer sounds based upon the soundscape in which they live.","zh":"動物可能偏好以牠們所處聲音景觀為基礎的聲音。"},{"en":"Based upon means built on, influenced by, or depending on something.","zh":"based upon 指建立在、受影響於或取決於某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may design exercises based upon the mistakes students made last week.","zh":"老師可能根據學生上星期犯的錯誤來設計練習。"},{"en":"If a preference is based upon experience, changing the environment may change the preference.","zh":"如果偏好以經驗為基礎，改變環境可能改變偏好。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the foundation or reason behind something.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事背後的基礎或原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the soundscape","meaning":"聲音景觀","examples":[{"en":"An animal’s music may depend on its soundscape.","zh":"動物的音樂可能取決於其聲音景觀。"},{"en":"The soundscape is the full set of sounds in an environment.","zh":"soundscape 是一個環境中完整的聲音集合。"},{"en":"A city soundscape may include traffic, footsteps, voices, sirens, and train noise.","zh":"城市聲音景觀可能包括交通聲、腳步聲、人聲、警號和火車聲。"},{"en":"Animals may respond to sounds that resemble the soundscape they live in.","zh":"動物可能回應類似其生活聲音景觀的聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an environment as heard through sound.","zh":"這個短語描述透過聲音聽到的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"fundamentally different from","meaning":"與……根本不同","examples":[{"en":"Animal music would be fundamentally different from human music.","zh":"動物音樂會與人類音樂根本不同。"},{"en":"Fundamentally different from means different at a basic or essential level.","zh":"fundamentally different from 指在基本或本質層面上不同。"},{"en":"Learning a language through conversation is fundamentally different from memorising word lists alone.","zh":"透過對話學語言與單靠背詞表有根本不同。"},{"en":"If two things are fundamentally different, small surface similarities may be misleading.","zh":"如果兩件事根本不同，表面上的小相似可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a deep difference, not a minor one.","zh":"這個短語描述深層差異，而不是小差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"derive from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"A cat’s idea of music may derive from yowls and meows.","zh":"貓對音樂的理解可能源自貓叫和喵叫。"},{"en":"To derive from something means to come from it as a source or origin.","zh":"derive from 某物，指以它為來源或起源。"},{"en":"Many English words derive from Latin or French.","zh":"許多英文字源自拉丁語或法語。"},{"en":"If a preference derives from daily experience, it may reflect what a person or animal often hears.","zh":"如果偏好源自日常經驗，它可能反映人或動物常聽到的東西。"},{"en":"The phrase describes origin or source.","zh":"這個短語描述起源或來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"yowls and meows","meaning":"貓叫和喵叫","examples":[{"en":"A cat’s idea of a good tune would derive from yowls and meows.","zh":"貓心目中的好旋律會源自貓叫和喵叫。"},{"en":"Yowls and meows are different vocal sounds made by cats.","zh":"yowls and meows 是貓發出的不同叫聲。"},{"en":"A cat may meow softly for food and yowl loudly when distressed or seeking attention.","zh":"貓可能為了食物輕聲喵叫，也可能在痛苦或想吸引注意時大聲叫。"},{"en":"If cat music were built from cat sounds, it might use yowls and meows rather than human notes.","zh":"如果貓音樂由貓聲音建構，它可能使用貓叫和喵叫，而不是人類音符。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to familiar cat vocalisations.","zh":"這個短語指熟悉的貓類發聲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"demonstrate that","meaning":"證明","examples":[{"en":"Researchers need evidence to demonstrate that animals respond differently.","zh":"研究人員需要證據來證明動物有不同反應。"},{"en":"To demonstrate that means to show clearly through evidence, examples, or proof.","zh":"demonstrate that 指透過證據、例子或證明清楚顯示某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may use student writing samples to demonstrate that practice improves grammar.","zh":"老師可能使用學生作文樣本來證明練習能改善文法。"},{"en":"Demonstrating a claim requires more than saying it is possible.","zh":"證明一項主張需要的不只是說它有可能。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence-based proof.","zh":"這個短語引出以證據為基礎的證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"respond to music","meaning":"對音樂作出反應","examples":[{"en":"Animals may respond to music based on their own sound environment.","zh":"動物可能根據自身聲音環境對音樂作出反應。"},{"en":"To respond to music means to react to music physically, emotionally, or behaviourally.","zh":"respond to music 指在身體、情感或行為上回應音樂。"},{"en":"A baby may respond to music by calming down, smiling, or moving to the beat.","zh":"嬰兒可能透過平靜下來、微笑或隨拍子移動來對音樂作出反應。"},{"en":"Responses to music can show interest, recognition, comfort, or discomfort.","zh":"對音樂的反應可以顯示興趣、辨認、安慰或不適。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a reaction to musical sound.","zh":"這個短語描述對音樂聲音的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be constructed from","meaning":"由……建構而成","examples":[{"en":"Animal music should be constructed from the animal’s own sound environment.","zh":"動物音樂應由動物自身的聲音環境建構而成。"},{"en":"To be constructed from something means to be built using it as material or foundation.","zh":"be constructed from 某物，指使用它作為材料或基礎來建立。"},{"en":"A lesson plan can be constructed from students’ real mistakes.","zh":"課堂計劃可以由學生真實錯誤建構而成。"},{"en":"If music is constructed from familiar sounds, listeners may respond more naturally.","zh":"如果音樂由熟悉聲音建構而成，聽者可能更自然地回應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what something is made or built from.","zh":"這個短語描述某物由甚麼製成或建立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"their own sound environment","meaning":"牠們自身的聲音環境","examples":[{"en":"Animals may prefer music from their own sound environment.","zh":"動物可能偏好來自牠們自身聲音環境的音樂。"},{"en":"Their own sound environment means the sounds normally heard in the world where they live.","zh":"their own sound environment 指牠們生活世界中通常聽到的聲音。"},{"en":"A forest bird’s sound environment includes other birds, wind, insects, and leaves.","zh":"森林鳥類的聲音環境包括其他鳥、風、昆蟲和樹葉聲。"},{"en":"Sounds from an animal’s own environment may feel more meaningful than human music.","zh":"來自動物自身環境的聲音，可能比人類音樂更有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase describes familiar surrounding sounds for a specific animal group.","zh":"這個短語描述特定動物群體熟悉的周遭聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no matter how","meaning":"不論如何","examples":[{"en":"No matter how the connection is parsed, music is rooted in biology.","zh":"不論這種聯繫如何被分析，音樂都根植於生物學。"},{"en":"No matter how means regardless of the way something happens or is explained.","zh":"no matter how 指不論某事如何發生或如何被解釋。"},{"en":"No matter how busy students are, they still need enough sleep.","zh":"不論學生多忙，他們仍需要足夠睡眠。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the main point remains true under different conditions.","zh":"這個短語顯示主要觀點在不同條件下仍然成立。"},{"en":"It is useful when several interpretations lead to the same conclusion.","zh":"當幾種詮釋都導向同一結論時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be parsed","meaning":"被分析；被解讀","examples":[{"en":"The connection between music and language can be parsed in different ways.","zh":"音樂與語言之間的聯繫可以用不同方式被分析。"},{"en":"To be parsed means to be analysed, broken down, or interpreted carefully.","zh":"be parsed 指被仔細分析、拆解或詮釋。"},{"en":"A difficult sentence can be parsed by identifying its subject, verb, and clauses.","zh":"困難句子可以透過找出主語、動詞和分句來分析。"},{"en":"Parsing helps people see how parts relate to one another.","zh":"分析幫助人看見各部分如何互相關聯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful analysis of structure or meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述對結構或意思的仔細分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"what is apparent is that","meaning":"顯而易見的是","examples":[{"en":"What is apparent is that our sense of music is rooted in biology.","zh":"顯而易見的是，我們的音樂感根植於生物學。"},{"en":"What is apparent is that means what is clear or easy to see is the following point.","zh":"what is apparent is that 指清楚或容易看見的是接下來這一點。"},{"en":"What is apparent is that students need more time to practise, not just more rules to memorise.","zh":"顯而易見的是，學生需要更多時間練習，而不只是更多規則去背誦。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the main conclusion after discussing uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語在討論不確定性後引出主要結論。"},{"en":"It tells readers which point has become clear.","zh":"它告訴讀者哪一點已變得清楚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"our sense of music","meaning":"我們的音樂感","examples":[{"en":"Our sense of music is deeply rooted in biology.","zh":"我們的音樂感深深根植於生物學。"},{"en":"Our sense of music means our ability to hear, recognise, enjoy, and respond to musical patterns.","zh":"our sense of music 指我們聽見、辨認、享受和回應音樂模式的能力。"},{"en":"A child’s sense of music may appear when she claps in time with a song.","zh":"當孩子隨歌曲準時拍手時，她的音樂感可能顯現出來。"},{"en":"This sense includes rhythm, pitch, emotion, and recognition of musical structure.","zh":"這種感覺包括節奏、音高、情感和對音樂結構的辨認。"},{"en":"The phrase describes human musical awareness.","zh":"這個短語描述人類對音樂的覺察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"our love for it","meaning":"我們對它的熱愛","examples":[{"en":"Our love for music is rooted in our brains.","zh":"我們對音樂的熱愛根植於我們的大腦。"},{"en":"Our love for it means our strong liking, attachment, or emotional attraction to something already mentioned.","zh":"our love for it 指我們對前面提及之物的強烈喜愛、依附或情感吸引。"},{"en":"A family may love a festival because its songs and food connect them to memory.","zh":"一個家庭可能熱愛某節日，因為其歌曲和食物把他們與記憶連起來。"},{"en":"Love for music can feel personal, but it may also have biological roots.","zh":"對音樂的熱愛可以感覺很個人，但也可能有生物根源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep affection for the subject being discussed.","zh":"這個短語描述對所討論對象的深厚喜愛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"as deeply rooted in...as","meaning":"像……一樣深深根植於……","examples":[{"en":"Music is as deeply rooted in our brains as language is.","zh":"音樂像語言一樣深深根植於我們的大腦。"},{"en":"As deeply rooted in A as B is means two things are equally strongly based in the same place or system.","zh":"as deeply rooted in A as B is 指兩件事同樣強烈地建立於同一地方或系統。"},{"en":"In many families, food traditions are as deeply rooted in memory as family photographs are.","zh":"在許多家庭中，飲食傳統像家庭照片一樣深深根植於記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase compares two things and says both have a strong foundation.","zh":"這個短語比較兩件事，並說兩者都有強大基礎。"},{"en":"It is used to challenge the idea that one thing is less basic than the other.","zh":"它用來挑戰一物比另一物不基本的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"our biology and our brains","meaning":"我們的生物本質和大腦","examples":[{"en":"Music is rooted in our biology and our brains.","zh":"音樂根植於我們的生物本質和大腦。"},{"en":"Our biology and our brains means the living body systems and brain processes that shape human behaviour.","zh":"our biology and our brains 指塑造人類行為的生命身體系統和大腦過程。"},{"en":"Sleep, emotion, memory, and language are all connected with our biology and our brains.","zh":"睡眠、情緒、記憶和語言都與我們的生物本質和大腦相連。"},{"en":"If music is rooted there, it may be part of human nature rather than simple entertainment.","zh":"如果音樂根植於其中，它可能是人性的一部分，而不只是娛樂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the biological and neural foundation of experience.","zh":"這個短語描述經驗的生物和神經基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be most obvious with","meaning":"在……身上最明顯","examples":[{"en":"The link between music and speech is most obvious with babies.","zh":"音樂與說話之間的聯繫在嬰兒身上最明顯。"},{"en":"To be most obvious with a group means to be easiest to see or understand when looking at that group.","zh":"be most obvious with 某群體，指觀察該群體時最容易看見或理解。"},{"en":"The need for routine is most obvious with young children when their bedtime changes.","zh":"當睡覺時間改變，規律的需要在幼童身上最明顯。"},{"en":"Some patterns become clearer in babies because their reactions are simple and direct.","zh":"有些模式在嬰兒身上更清楚，因為他們的反應簡單而直接。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where a connection can be seen most clearly.","zh":"這個短語指出某種聯繫在哪裏最清晰可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"publish a paper","meaning":"發表論文","examples":[{"en":"Sandra Trehub published a paper on babies, music, and speech.","zh":"Sandra Trehub 發表了一篇關於嬰兒、音樂和說話的論文。"},{"en":"To publish a paper means to make a research article available in an academic journal or formal publication.","zh":"publish a paper 指在學術期刊或正式出版物中公開研究文章。"},{"en":"A scientist may publish a paper after collecting data and passing peer review.","zh":"科學家可能在收集數據並通過同行評審後發表論文。"},{"en":"Publishing a paper allows other researchers to read, test, and build on the findings.","zh":"發表論文讓其他研究人員閱讀、測試並延伸其發現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formally sharing academic research.","zh":"這個短語描述正式分享學術研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a special issue","meaning":"特刊","examples":[{"en":"The journal published a special issue on music and language.","zh":"該期刊出版了一期關於音樂和語言的特刊。"},{"en":"A special issue is one edition of a journal or magazine focused on one particular topic.","zh":"special issue 是期刊或雜誌中專注於某特定主題的一期。"},{"en":"A school magazine may publish a special issue on climate action.","zh":"學校雜誌可能出版一期關於氣候行動的特刊。"},{"en":"Special issues show that a topic has become important enough for concentrated attention.","zh":"特刊顯示某主題已重要到值得集中關注。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a themed publication edition.","zh":"這個短語描述有主題的出版期數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be on a continuum","meaning":"處於連續體上","examples":[{"en":"For babies, music and speech are on a continuum.","zh":"對嬰兒來說，音樂和說話處於連續體上。"},{"en":"To be on a continuum means to be part of a gradual range rather than completely separate categories.","zh":"be on a continuum 指屬於一個漸進範圍，而不是完全分開的類別。"},{"en":"Speaking and singing may be on a continuum when a mother’s voice rises and falls musically.","zh":"當母親的聲音有音樂般高低起伏時，說話和歌唱可能處於連續體上。"},{"en":"If two things are on a continuum, there may be forms in between them.","zh":"如果兩件事處於連續體上，它們之間可能有中間形式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a gradual connection between related categories.","zh":"這個短語描述相關類別之間的漸進連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"musical speech","meaning":"具音樂性的說話方式","examples":[{"en":"Mothers use musical speech to calm babies.","zh":"母親使用具音樂性的說話方式來安撫嬰兒。"},{"en":"Musical speech is speech with song-like rhythm, pitch, repetition, or melody.","zh":"musical speech 是帶有像歌曲般節奏、音高、重複或旋律的說話。"},{"en":"A parent may use musical speech when saying “good night” in a soft rising-and-falling voice.","zh":"父母用柔和高低起伏的聲音說「晚安」時，可能在使用具音樂性的說話方式。"},{"en":"Musical speech can hold a baby’s attention and make the voice feel soothing.","zh":"具音樂性的說話方式可以吸引嬰兒注意，並令聲音感覺安撫。"},{"en":"The phrase describes speech that sounds close to singing.","zh":"這個短語描述聽起來接近歌唱的說話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"regulate infants’ emotional states","meaning":"調節嬰兒的情緒狀態","examples":[{"en":"Mothers use musical speech to regulate infants’ emotional states.","zh":"母親使用具音樂性的說話方式來調節嬰兒的情緒狀態。"},{"en":"To regulate infants’ emotional states means to help babies become calmer, happier, sleepier, or less distressed.","zh":"regulate infants’ emotional states 指幫助嬰兒變得更平靜、更快樂、更想睡或較少痛苦。"},{"en":"A parent may regulate a baby’s emotional state by speaking softly and rocking gently.","zh":"父母可能透過柔聲說話和輕輕搖晃來調節嬰兒的情緒狀態。"},{"en":"Regulation matters because babies cannot easily control their own emotions.","zh":"調節很重要，因為嬰兒不容易控制自己的情緒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes helping babies manage feelings through sound and care.","zh":"這個短語描述透過聲音和照顧幫助嬰兒管理感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"regardless of","meaning":"不論……","examples":[{"en":"Regardless of language, mothers use a similar voice with babies.","zh":"不論語言如何，母親與嬰兒說話時都使用相似聲音。"},{"en":"Regardless of means without being affected by or depending on something.","zh":"regardless of 指不受某事影響，或不取決於某事。"},{"en":"Students should be treated fairly regardless of their background.","zh":"不論學生背景如何，都應受到公平對待。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a pattern remains true even when one factor changes.","zh":"這個短語顯示即使某因素改變，某模式仍然成立。"},{"en":"It is useful for emphasising consistency across differences.","zh":"它有助強調跨越差異的一致性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"something between speech and song","meaning":"介乎說話與歌曲之間的東西","examples":[{"en":"Mothers use something between speech and song with babies.","zh":"母親對嬰兒使用介乎說話與歌曲之間的東西。"},{"en":"Something between speech and song means a form of communication that is not ordinary talking but not full singing either.","zh":"something between speech and song 指不是普通說話，但也不是完整歌唱的溝通形式。"},{"en":"A parent soothing a baby may use a soft voice that rises and falls like a tune.","zh":"父母安撫嬰兒時，可能使用像旋律般高低起伏的柔和聲音。"},{"en":"This in-between form can feel gentle because it carries both meaning and melody.","zh":"這種中間形式可以令人感到溫柔，因為它同時帶有意思和旋律。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a hybrid form of vocal communication.","zh":"這個短語描述混合型人聲溝通方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"this kind of communication","meaning":"這種溝通方式","examples":[{"en":"This kind of communication may help babies sleep.","zh":"這種溝通方式可能幫助嬰兒入睡。"},{"en":"This kind of communication means the particular way of sharing meaning, feeling, or signals just described.","zh":"this kind of communication 指剛描述的分享意思、情感或信號的特定方式。"},{"en":"Gentle eye contact and soft speech can be this kind of communication between parent and baby.","zh":"溫柔眼神接觸和輕聲說話，可以是父母與嬰兒之間的這種溝通方式。"},{"en":"Communication can affect mood even when the listener does not understand every word.","zh":"即使聽者不明白每個詞語，溝通也能影響心情。"},{"en":"The phrase points back to a specific communication method.","zh":"這個短語回指某種具體溝通方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"put someone in a trancelike state","meaning":"令某人進入恍惚狀態","examples":[{"en":"Musical speech can put a baby in a trancelike state.","zh":"具音樂性的說話方式可以令嬰兒進入恍惚狀態。"},{"en":"To put someone in a trancelike state means to make them very calm, absorbed, and almost sleepy.","zh":"put someone in a trancelike state 指令某人非常平靜、入神，幾乎想睡。"},{"en":"Soft repetitive music may put a tired child in a trancelike state before bedtime.","zh":"柔和重複音樂可能在睡前令疲倦孩子進入恍惚狀態。"},{"en":"Repetition and gentle rhythm can reduce alertness and help the body relax.","zh":"重複和溫柔節奏可以降低警覺，幫助身體放鬆。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating a deeply calm, dreamy condition.","zh":"這個短語描述創造深度平靜、夢幻般的狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"lead to sleep","meaning":"帶來睡眠；令人入睡","examples":[{"en":"The trancelike state may lead to sleep.","zh":"恍惚狀態可能令人入睡。"},{"en":"To lead to sleep means to cause or help someone fall asleep.","zh":"lead to sleep 指導致或幫助某人睡着。"},{"en":"A quiet bedtime routine can lead to sleep more easily than bright screens.","zh":"安靜的睡前程序比明亮屏幕更容易帶來睡眠。"},{"en":"Calm sounds and repeated rhythms may prepare the body for rest.","zh":"平靜聲音和重複節奏可能讓身體準備休息。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one thing helping sleep happen.","zh":"這個短語描述一件事幫助睡眠發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"extended periods of rapture","meaning":"長時間陶醉","examples":[{"en":"Music may lead to extended periods of rapture in babies.","zh":"音樂可能令嬰兒長時間陶醉。"},{"en":"Extended periods of rapture are long moments of intense pleasure, delight, or absorbed happiness.","zh":"extended periods of rapture 是長時間的強烈愉悅、欣喜或入神快樂。"},{"en":"A baby may show rapture by staring, smiling, and staying calm during a favourite song.","zh":"嬰兒在最喜歡的歌曲播放時，可能透過凝望、微笑和保持平靜來表現陶醉。"},{"en":"If music creates rapture, it does more than entertain; it deeply affects emotion.","zh":"如果音樂創造陶醉，它就不只是娛樂，而是深刻影響情緒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long-lasting joyful absorption.","zh":"這個短語描述長時間的快樂入神。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the latest research on","meaning":"關於……的最新研究","examples":[{"en":"Babies would not be surprised by the latest research on language and music.","zh":"嬰兒不會對關於語言和音樂的最新研究感到驚訝。"},{"en":"The latest research on a topic means the newest studies or findings about it.","zh":"latest research on 某主題，指關於它的最新研究或發現。"},{"en":"The latest research on sleep may change how schools plan homework.","zh":"關於睡眠的最新研究可能改變學校如何安排功課。"},{"en":"New research can confirm old ideas or challenge what experts used to believe.","zh":"新研究可以確認舊想法，也可以挑戰專家以往相信的事。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the most recent academic evidence.","zh":"這個短語指最新的學術證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the upshot","meaning":"結論；結果","examples":[{"en":"The upshot is that music may be more necessary than we realise.","zh":"結論是，音樂可能比我們意識到的更必要。"},{"en":"The upshot means the final result, main conclusion, or practical meaning of a discussion.","zh":"the upshot 指討論的最終結果、主要結論或實際意思。"},{"en":"The upshot of the meeting was that students needed more revision time.","zh":"會議的結論是學生需要更多溫習時間。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when they want to state the main takeaway.","zh":"當作者想說出主要重點時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the conclusion after several points have been discussed.","zh":"這個短語在討論幾點後引出結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"more of a necessity than","meaning":"比……更像必需品","examples":[{"en":"Music may be more of a necessity than we realise.","zh":"音樂可能比我們意識到的更像必需品。"},{"en":"More of a necessity than means closer to being something essential than people previously thought.","zh":"more of a necessity than 指比人們以往認為更接近必不可少的東西。"},{"en":"Sleep is more of a necessity than a luxury for students preparing for exams.","zh":"對準備考試的學生來說，睡眠比起奢侈品更像必需品。"},{"en":"If music helps regulate emotion and communication, it may not be merely entertainment.","zh":"如果音樂幫助調節情緒和溝通，它就可能不只是娛樂。"},{"en":"The phrase challenges the idea that something is optional or unimportant.","zh":"這個短語挑戰某事只是可有可無或不重要的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Students must choose the correct heading for each section.","zh":"學生必須為每個部分選出正確標題。"},{"en":"To choose the correct heading means to select the title that best summarises the main idea.","zh":"choose the correct heading 指選擇最能概括主旨的標題。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should read the whole paragraph before choosing the heading.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先讀完整段，再選標題。"},{"en":"A wrong heading may mention a detail but miss the paragraph’s main purpose.","zh":"錯誤標題可能提到細節，但錯過段落主要目的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common IELTS-style matching task.","zh":"這個短語描述常見的 IELTS 式配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The question provides a list of headings for the passage.","zh":"題目為文章提供標題列表。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a set of possible titles that students must match with sections.","zh":"list of headings 是一組可能標題，學生必須把它們與段落配對。"},{"en":"A reading paper may give a list of headings before asking students to label paragraphs.","zh":"閱讀試卷可能先給出標題列表，再要求學生標示段落。"},{"en":"Students should compare each heading with the main idea, not just one repeated word.","zh":"學生應把每個標題與主旨比較，而不只是找一個重複字。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the answer choices in a heading-matching task.","zh":"這個短語描述標題配對題中的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"communication in music with animals","meaning":"透過音樂與動物溝通","examples":[{"en":"The heading refers to communication in music with animals.","zh":"該標題指透過音樂與動物溝通。"},{"en":"Communication in music with animals means using musical or sound patterns to connect with or study animals.","zh":"communication in music with animals 指使用音樂或聲音模式與動物連接或研究牠們。"},{"en":"A researcher may test communication in music with animals by playing sounds based on their own calls.","zh":"研究人員可能播放根據動物自身叫聲製作的聲音，來測試透過音樂與動物溝通。"},{"en":"Such communication may fail if the music is based only on human sound preferences.","zh":"如果音樂只基於人類聲音偏好，這種溝通可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the possible link between animal sound response and music.","zh":"這個短語描述動物聲音反應與音樂之間的可能聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"new discoveries on animal music","meaning":"關於動物音樂的新發現","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses new discoveries on animal music.","zh":"文章討論關於動物音樂的新發現。"},{"en":"New discoveries on animal music are recent findings about whether animals create, recognise, or respond to music-like sounds.","zh":"new discoveries on animal music 是關於動物是否創造、辨認或回應類似音樂聲音的近期發現。"},{"en":"A study of whalesong may produce new discoveries on animal music.","zh":"對鯨歌的研究可能產生關於動物音樂的新發現。"},{"en":"Such discoveries can change how scientists compare human music with animal sound.","zh":"這些發現可以改變科學家如何比較人類音樂與動物聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recent research findings about animal sound and music.","zh":"這個短語描述關於動物聲音和音樂的近期研究發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"contrast music and language","meaning":"對比音樂與語言","examples":[{"en":"The passage contrasts music and language.","zh":"文章對比音樂與語言。"},{"en":"To contrast music and language means to compare them by showing their differences.","zh":"contrast music and language 指透過展示差異來比較兩者。"},{"en":"A teacher may contrast music and language by asking which one communicates meaning more directly.","zh":"老師可能透過問哪一個更直接傳達意思來對比音樂與語言。"},{"en":"Contrast helps readers see why language has often seemed more useful than music.","zh":"對比幫助讀者看見為何語言常似乎比音樂更有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes comparison through difference.","zh":"這個短語描述透過差異作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"current research on music","meaning":"目前關於音樂的研究","examples":[{"en":"The article reviews current research on music.","zh":"文章回顧目前關於音樂的研究。"},{"en":"Current research on music means recent academic studies about how music works, affects people, or develops.","zh":"current research on music 指關於音樂如何運作、影響人或發展的近期學術研究。"},{"en":"Current research on music may examine the brain, emotions, infants, or animal responses.","zh":"目前關於音樂的研究可能檢視大腦、情緒、嬰兒或動物反應。"},{"en":"Recent studies can challenge older views that treated music as unimportant.","zh":"近期研究可以挑戰把音樂視為不重要的舊看法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes up-to-date scholarly investigation of music.","zh":"這個短語描述關於音樂的最新學術探究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be beneficial for infants","meaning":"對嬰兒有益","examples":[{"en":"Music may be beneficial for infants.","zh":"音樂可能對嬰兒有益。"},{"en":"To be beneficial for infants means to help babies in some useful way.","zh":"be beneficial for infants 指以某種有用方式幫助嬰兒。"},{"en":"Gentle singing may be beneficial for infants because it can calm them before sleep.","zh":"溫柔歌唱可能對嬰兒有益，因為它可以在睡前安撫他們。"},{"en":"If a sound helps regulate emotion, it may support early development or comfort.","zh":"如果聲音幫助調節情緒，它可能支持早期發展或安慰。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something helpful to babies.","zh":"這個短語描述對嬰兒有幫助的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"transcend cultures","meaning":"超越文化","examples":[{"en":"Music appears to transcend cultures.","zh":"音樂似乎超越文化。"},{"en":"To transcend cultures means to go beyond cultural differences and be understood or felt across societies.","zh":"transcend cultures 指超越文化差異，在不同社會中被理解或感受到。"},{"en":"A lullaby may transcend cultures because many parents use gentle sound to calm babies.","zh":"搖籃曲可能超越文化，因為許多父母都用柔和聲音安撫嬰兒。"},{"en":"If something transcends cultures, local differences remain but do not block recognition.","zh":"如果某事超越文化，本地差異仍存在，但不會阻礙辨認。"},{"en":"The phrase describes crossing cultural boundaries.","zh":"這個短語描述跨越文化界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a look back at","meaning":"回顧……","examples":[{"en":"The passage takes a look back at historical theories of music.","zh":"文章回顧了音樂的歷史理論。"},{"en":"A look back at something is a review or return to earlier events, ideas, or history.","zh":"look back at 某事，是對較早事件、想法或歷史的回顧。"},{"en":"A teacher may take a look back at last week’s lesson before starting a new topic.","zh":"老師可能在開始新主題前回顧上星期課堂。"},{"en":"Looking back helps readers understand how present ideas developed.","zh":"回顧過去幫助讀者理解現在想法如何發展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reviewing the past.","zh":"這個短語描述檢視過去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"historical theories","meaning":"歷史理論","examples":[{"en":"The article discusses historical theories about harmony.","zh":"文章討論關於和聲的歷史理論。"},{"en":"Historical theories are explanations or ideas developed in earlier periods.","zh":"historical theories 是在較早時期發展出來的解釋或想法。"},{"en":"Students study historical theories of medicine to see how scientific understanding has changed.","zh":"學生研究醫學歷史理論，以了解科學理解如何改變。"},{"en":"Older theories may be partly useful even when modern research revises them.","zh":"即使現代研究修正舊理論，較早理論仍可能部分有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes past explanations that shaped later thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述塑造後來思想的過去解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be genetically designed for","meaning":"基因上被設計成……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether humans are genetically designed for music.","zh":"題目問人類是否在基因上被設計成適合音樂。"},{"en":"To be genetically designed for something means to have inherited biological features that make one suited to it.","zh":"be genetically designed for 某事，指擁有使自己適合它的遺傳生物特徵。"},{"en":"Some animals are genetically designed for flying because their bodies have wings and light bones.","zh":"有些動物在基因上被設計成適合飛行，因為牠們身體有翅膀和輕骨骼。"},{"en":"If humans are genetically designed for music, musical ability may be part of our biological nature.","zh":"如果人類在基因上被設計成適合音樂，音樂能力可能是我們生物本質的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an ability as built into inherited biology.","zh":"這個短語把能力描述為內置於遺傳生物基礎中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"match each person with","meaning":"將每個人與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match each person with the correct statement.","zh":"學生將每個人與正確陳述配對。"},{"en":"To match each person with something means to connect each named person to the right idea, role, or description.","zh":"match each person with 某物，指把每個具名人物與正確想法、角色或描述連起來。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may match each scientist with the theory he or she supported.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能將每位科學家與其支持的理論配對。"},{"en":"Matching requires careful reading because names and ideas may appear in different sentences.","zh":"配對需要仔細閱讀，因為名字和想法可能出現在不同句子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an exam task based on linking people and information.","zh":"這個短語描述把人物與資訊連結的考試任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the correct statement","meaning":"正確陳述","examples":[{"en":"Each person must be matched with the correct statement.","zh":"每個人都必須與正確陳述配對。"},{"en":"The correct statement is the option that accurately matches the information in the passage.","zh":"correct statement 是準確符合文章資料的選項。"},{"en":"A statement may sound true, but it is not correct unless the text supports it.","zh":"一項陳述可能聽起來正確，但除非文本支持，否則並非正確。"},{"en":"Students should check the exact evidence before choosing a statement.","zh":"學生在選擇陳述前，應檢查準確證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the right answer in a matching task.","zh":"這個短語指配對題中的正確答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"exist outside of","meaning":"存在於……之外","examples":[{"en":"Some critics think music exists outside of the world it is created in.","zh":"有些評論者認為音樂存在於它被創造的世界之外。"},{"en":"To exist outside of something means to be separate from it or not influenced by it.","zh":"exist outside of 某事，指與它分離或不受它影響。"},{"en":"A school policy should not exist outside of students’ real learning needs.","zh":"校政不應存在於學生真實學習需要之外。"},{"en":"If music exists outside of its world, culture and experience would not shape it.","zh":"如果音樂存在於其世界之外，文化和經驗就不會塑造它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes separation from context.","zh":"這個短語描述與語境分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"universal character","meaning":"普遍特性","examples":[{"en":"Music has a universal character despite cultural differences.","zh":"儘管有文化差異，音樂具有普遍特性。"},{"en":"Universal character means a quality that appears across many cultures and human groups.","zh":"universal character 指在許多文化和人類群體中出現的特質。"},{"en":"Storytelling has a universal character because people everywhere tell stories to share memory and meaning.","zh":"講故事具有普遍特性，因為各地的人都講故事來分享記憶和意義。"},{"en":"A universal character can appear in different forms in different societies.","zh":"普遍特性可以在不同社會中以不同形式出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shared human quality.","zh":"這個短語描述共同的人類特質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"cultural influences on","meaning":"對……的文化影響","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to cultural influences on music.","zh":"題目指對音樂的文化影響。"},{"en":"Cultural influences on something are the ways culture shapes its form, meaning, or use.","zh":"cultural influences on 某事，是文化塑造其形式、意義或用途的方式。"},{"en":"Local festivals can have strong cultural influences on music through rhythm, language, and instruments.","zh":"本地節日可以透過節奏、語言和樂器對音樂產生強烈文化影響。"},{"en":"Cultural influences explain why music sounds different in different societies.","zh":"文化影響解釋為何音樂在不同社會中聽起來不同。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how culture affects a subject.","zh":"這個短語描述文化如何影響某主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"a necessity for humans","meaning":"人類的必需品","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers suggest that music is a necessity for humans.","zh":"有些研究人員指出音樂是人類的必需品。"},{"en":"A necessity for humans is something humans need in an important way, not merely a luxury.","zh":"necessity for humans 是人類以重要方式需要的東西，而不只是奢侈品。"},{"en":"Social connection is a necessity for humans because isolation can damage mental health.","zh":"社交連繫是人類的必需品，因為孤立可以損害心理健康。"},{"en":"If music helps emotion and communication, it may be closer to a necessity than entertainment.","zh":"如果音樂幫助情緒和溝通，它可能比娛樂更接近必需品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something considered deeply needed by people.","zh":"這個短語描述被視為人類深切需要的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"music preference","meaning":"音樂偏好","examples":[{"en":"Music preference may be related to the surrounding environment.","zh":"音樂偏好可能與周圍環境有關。"},{"en":"Music preference means the kinds of music a person or group tends to like.","zh":"music preference 指一個人或群體傾向喜歡的音樂種類。"},{"en":"A teenager’s music preference may be shaped by friends, family, online videos, and local culture.","zh":"青少年的音樂偏好可能受朋友、家庭、網上影片和本地文化塑造。"},{"en":"Preferences can change when people hear new sounds repeatedly.","zh":"當人們反覆聽到新聲音，偏好可以改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what music someone is drawn to.","zh":"這個短語描述某人被哪種音樂吸引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be related to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Music preference is related to surrounding influences.","zh":"音樂偏好與周圍影響有關。"},{"en":"To be related to something means to have a connection with it.","zh":"be related to 某事，指與它有聯繫。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be related to poor sleep rather than laziness.","zh":"學生疲倦可能與睡眠不足有關，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"When two things are related, one may affect or help explain the other.","zh":"當兩件事有關，其中一件可能影響或幫助解釋另一件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a connection, not always a direct cause.","zh":"這個短語描述聯繫，但不一定是直接原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"surrounding influences","meaning":"周圍環境影響","examples":[{"en":"Musical tastes may reflect surrounding influences.","zh":"音樂品味可能反映周圍環境影響。"},{"en":"Surrounding influences are the people, sounds, culture, media, and environment around someone that shape them.","zh":"surrounding influences 是某人身邊塑造其思想或行為的人、聲音、文化、媒體和環境。"},{"en":"A child’s accent may change because of surrounding influences at school.","zh":"孩子的口音可能因學校中的周圍環境影響而改變。"},{"en":"Surrounding influences matter because people absorb patterns from what they repeatedly experience.","zh":"周圍環境影響很重要，因為人們會吸收反覆經歷的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the context that shapes preferences or behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述塑造偏好或行為的語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"the mathematical basis of music","meaning":"音樂的數學基礎","examples":[{"en":"Pythagoras discovered the mathematical basis of music.","zh":"畢達哥拉斯發現了音樂的數學基礎。"},{"en":"The mathematical basis of music means the number relationships that help explain musical pitch and harmony.","zh":"mathematical basis of music 指幫助解釋音樂音高和和聲的數字關係。"},{"en":"A teacher may show the mathematical basis of music by comparing string lengths and sound frequencies.","zh":"老師可能透過比較弦長和聲音頻率來展示音樂的數學基礎。"},{"en":"This basis helps explain why some intervals sound more stable than others.","zh":"這個基礎幫助解釋為何某些音程比另一些更穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the numerical foundation behind musical patterns.","zh":"這個短語描述音樂模式背後的數字基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"receive the same level of research attention as","meaning":"獲得與……相同程度的研究關注","examples":[{"en":"Music did not receive the same level of research attention as language.","zh":"音樂沒有獲得與語言相同程度的研究關注。"},{"en":"To receive the same level of research attention as something means to be studied as much and as seriously as it.","zh":"receive the same level of research attention as 某事，指被研究的程度和嚴肅程度與它相同。"},{"en":"Mental health once did not receive the same level of school attention as exam results.","zh":"心理健康曾經沒有獲得與考試成績相同程度的學校關注。"},{"en":"A topic may seem less important if researchers study it less often.","zh":"如果研究人員較少研究某主題，它可能看起來較不重要。"},{"en":"The phrase compares how much academic focus two subjects receive.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個主題獲得多少學術關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"research attention","meaning":"研究關注","examples":[{"en":"Music has received less research attention than language.","zh":"音樂獲得的研究關注少於語言。"},{"en":"Research attention means the amount of study, discussion, and investigation a topic receives from researchers.","zh":"research attention 指某主題從研究人員得到的研究、討論和調查程度。"},{"en":"A disease may receive more research attention after it affects many people.","zh":"某疾病影響許多人後，可能獲得更多研究關注。"},{"en":"More research attention can lead to better theories, stronger evidence, and new methods.","zh":"更多研究關注可以帶來更好理論、更強證據和新方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes academic focus on a topic.","zh":"這個短語描述對某主題的學術焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"similar traits in perceiving sound","meaning":"在感知聲音方面有相似特徵","examples":[{"en":"Humans and monkeys may have similar traits in perceiving sound.","zh":"人類和猴子在感知聲音方面可能有相似特徵。"},{"en":"Similar traits in perceiving sound are shared features in how different species hear or process sound.","zh":"similar traits in perceiving sound 是不同物種在聽見或處理聲音方面共享的特徵。"},{"en":"Two children may have similar traits in listening if both notice rhythm before meaning.","zh":"如果兩個孩子都先注意節奏而非意思，他們在聆聽方面可能有相似特徵。"},{"en":"Shared auditory traits can explain why different animals respond to some sounds in similar ways.","zh":"共同聽覺特徵可以解釋為何不同動物對某些聲音有相似反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes common features in sound perception.","zh":"這個短語描述聲音感知中的共同特點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each answer.","zh":"學生為每個答案選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the option, such as A, B, C, or D, that matches the passage.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇符合文章的選項，例如 A、B、C 或 D。"},{"en":"In multiple-choice reading, students should check evidence before choosing the correct letter.","zh":"在閱讀選擇題中，學生應在選出正確字母前檢查證據。"},{"en":"A tempting option may use words from the text but still be wrong.","zh":"有吸引力的選項可能使用文本字眼，但仍然錯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語描述常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"inconclusive","meaning":"未有定論","examples":[{"en":"The studies of animal music were inconclusive.","zh":"關於動物音樂的研究未有定論。"},{"en":"Inconclusive means not leading to a clear or final answer.","zh":"inconclusive 指沒有帶來清楚或最終答案。"},{"en":"A medical test may be inconclusive if it does not clearly show whether a patient has an illness.","zh":"如果醫學檢查不能清楚顯示病人是否患病，結果可能未有定論。"},{"en":"Inconclusive results often lead researchers to design more careful studies.","zh":"未有定論的結果常會促使研究人員設計更仔細的研究。"},{"en":"The word describes evidence that is not strong enough to settle the question.","zh":"這個詞描述不足以解決問題的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"tests on animal music","meaning":"對動物音樂的測試","examples":[{"en":"Tests on animal music may be too limited.","zh":"對動物音樂的測試可能太有限。"},{"en":"Tests on animal music are experiments examining how animals create, hear, or respond to music-like sounds.","zh":"tests on animal music 是檢視動物如何創造、聽見或回應類似音樂聲音的實驗。"},{"en":"A researcher might run tests on animal music by playing species-specific sounds to cats or birds.","zh":"研究人員可能透過向貓或鳥播放物種特定聲音，進行對動物音樂的測試。"},{"en":"Limited tests may not show what animals truly prefer in natural conditions.","zh":"有限測試未必能顯示動物在自然條件下真正偏好甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes experimental study of animals and music-like sound.","zh":"這個短語描述對動物和類似音樂聲音的實驗研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be limited","meaning":"有限","examples":[{"en":"The tests on animal music are limited.","zh":"對動物音樂的測試是有限的。"},{"en":"To be limited means to be restricted in size, range, amount, or usefulness.","zh":"be limited 指在大小、範圍、數量或用途上受限制。"},{"en":"A survey is limited if it only asks ten students from one class.","zh":"如果問卷只問一班中的十名學生，它就是有限的。"},{"en":"Limited evidence can suggest an idea but usually cannot prove it fully.","zh":"有限證據可以暗示一個想法，但通常不能完全證明。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something not broad or strong enough.","zh":"這個短語描述某事不夠廣泛或不夠有力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"make up new tunes","meaning":"創作新曲調","examples":[{"en":"Some animals cannot make up new tunes.","zh":"有些動物不能創作新曲調。"},{"en":"To make up new tunes means to invent original melodies rather than repeat existing ones.","zh":"make up new tunes 指創作原創旋律，而不是重複已有旋律。"},{"en":"A child may make up new tunes while singing in the shower.","zh":"孩子在洗澡時唱歌，可能會創作新曲調。"},{"en":"Making up tunes shows musical creativity because the pattern did not simply come from memory.","zh":"創作曲調顯示音樂創造力，因為該模式不是單純來自記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating new melodies.","zh":"這個短語描述創造新旋律。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"involve a wide range of","meaning":"涉及廣泛的……","examples":[{"en":"Researchers need tests involving a wide range of animals.","zh":"研究人員需要涉及廣泛動物種類的測試。"},{"en":"To involve a wide range of something means to include many different types or examples.","zh":"involve a wide range of 某物，指包括許多不同種類或例子。"},{"en":"A school survey should involve a wide range of students from different year levels.","zh":"學校問卷應涉及來自不同年級的廣泛學生。"},{"en":"A wider range gives stronger evidence because results are not based on one small group.","zh":"更廣泛的範圍提供更強證據，因為結果不是基於一個小群體。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad inclusion and variety.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛納入和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"the main theme of","meaning":"……的主題","examples":[{"en":"Students identify the main theme of the passage.","zh":"學生辨認文章的主題。"},{"en":"The main theme of a text is its central idea or most important message.","zh":"main theme of 文本，是其中心思想或最重要信息。"},{"en":"The main theme of a story about a poor student may be resilience rather than poverty itself.","zh":"關於貧困學生的故事，其主題可能是抗逆力，而不是貧窮本身。"},{"en":"Finding the main theme helps students choose answers that match the whole passage.","zh":"找出主題幫助學生選擇符合整篇文章的答案。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the overall idea, not a small detail.","zh":"這個短語描述整體想法，而不是小細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"the evolution of music","meaning":"音樂的演化","examples":[{"en":"The evolution of music is a central issue in the passage.","zh":"音樂的演化是文章中的核心問題。"},{"en":"The evolution of music means how music may have developed in human history and biology.","zh":"evolution of music 指音樂可能如何在人類歷史和生物學中發展。"},{"en":"Researchers study the evolution of music by comparing human song, speech, infant communication, and animal sound.","zh":"研究人員透過比較人類歌唱、說話、嬰兒溝通和動物聲音來研究音樂的演化。"},{"en":"Understanding evolution can explain why music appears so widespread among humans.","zh":"理解演化可以解釋為何音樂在人類中如此普遍。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the origin and development of music over time.","zh":"這個短語描述音樂隨時間的起源和發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"the role of music in human society","meaning":"音樂在人類社會中的角色","examples":[{"en":"The passage explores the role of music in human society.","zh":"文章探討音樂在人類社會中的角色。"},{"en":"The role of music in human society means what music does for people, relationships, emotions, culture, and communication.","zh":"role of music in human society 指音樂對人、關係、情感、文化和溝通所發揮的作用。"},{"en":"Music plays a role in human society when people use songs at weddings, funerals, schools, and protests.","zh":"當人們在婚禮、葬禮、學校和抗議中使用歌曲，音樂就在社會中發揮角色。"},{"en":"Studying this role helps explain why music is more than background entertainment.","zh":"研究這種角色有助解釋為何音樂不只是背景娛樂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes music’s function and importance in human life.","zh":"這個短語描述音樂在人類生活中的功能和重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 29 - Music - Language We All Speak.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 30":[{"front":"talc powder","meaning":"滑石粉","examples":[{"en":"Talc powder has surprising uses in food and agriculture.","zh":"滑石粉在食品和農業中有令人意想不到的用途。"},{"en":"Talc powder is a fine mineral powder made from talc.","zh":"滑石粉是由滑石製成的細礦物粉末。"},{"en":"A factory may use talc powder to stop sticky materials from clumping together.","zh":"工廠可能使用滑石粉防止黏性材料結塊。"},{"en":"Because talc powder is smooth and chemically stable, it can be useful in industrial processing.","zh":"由於滑石粉順滑且化學性質穩定，它在工業加工中很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to powdered talc, not only baby powder.","zh":"這個短語指粉末狀滑石，不只是嬰兒爽身粉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"discover how","meaning":"探討……如何","examples":[{"en":"Peter Brigg discovers how talc is used in food and agricultural products.","zh":"Peter Brigg 探討滑石如何被用於食品及農產品。"},{"en":"To discover how something happens means to find out the method or process behind it.","zh":"探討某事如何發生，是指找出其背後的方法或過程。"},{"en":"Students may discover how plants grow by observing them every day.","zh":"學生可能透過每天觀察植物，探討植物如何生長。"},{"en":"When we discover how a material is used, we understand its practical value better.","zh":"當我們探討一種材料如何被使用，就能更好理解其實用價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing an explanation of a hidden process.","zh":"這個短語適合用來引入對隱藏過程的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"find its way into","meaning":"被用於；進入","examples":[{"en":"Talc from Trimouns finds its way into chewing gum and olive oil.","zh":"來自 Trimouns 的滑石被用於香口膠和橄欖油。"},{"en":"To find its way into something means to be used in it, often in a surprising or indirect way.","zh":"被用於某物，是指以令人意外或間接的方式出現在其中。"},{"en":"A scientific idea may find its way into school textbooks after many years of research.","zh":"一個科學想法可能在多年研究後進入學校教科書。"},{"en":"When a material finds its way into everyday products, consumers may not realise it is there.","zh":"當一種材料被用於日常產品，消費者可能不知道它存在其中。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that something appears in a place where people may not expect it.","zh":"這個短語暗示某物出現在人們未必預期的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"food and agricultural products","meaning":"食品及農產品","examples":[{"en":"Talc is used in many food and agricultural products.","zh":"滑石被用於許多食品及農產品。"},{"en":"Food and agricultural products are items connected with eating, farming, crops or food processing.","zh":"食品及農產品是與食用、農業、作物或食品加工有關的物品。"},{"en":"Olive oil, fruit crops and chewing gum can all be discussed as food or agricultural products.","zh":"橄欖油、水果作物和香口膠都可以作為食品或農產品來討論。"},{"en":"Materials used in these products must be safe, useful and suitable for processing.","zh":"用於這些產品的材料必須安全、有用並適合加工。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both finished foods and products connected with farming.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋成品食品，以及與農業相關的產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"from chewing gum to olive oil","meaning":"由香口膠到橄欖油","examples":[{"en":"Talc appears in products ranging from chewing gum to olive oil.","zh":"滑石出現在由香口膠到橄欖油等產品中。"},{"en":"From chewing gum to olive oil means across a surprisingly wide range of products.","zh":"由香口膠到橄欖油，是指跨越令人意外的廣泛產品範圍。"},{"en":"A company may sell products from notebooks to computer screens.","zh":"一家公司可能銷售由筆記簿到電腦螢幕的產品。"},{"en":"This structure shows variety by naming two very different examples.","zh":"這個結構透過列出兩個很不同的例子來顯示多樣性。"},{"en":"The phrase helps readers understand that talc has more uses than they might expect.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者理解滑石的用途比想像中更多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"high in the French Pyrenees","meaning":"位於法國庇里牛斯山脈高處","examples":[{"en":"High in the French Pyrenees lies a huge talc deposit.","zh":"法國庇里牛斯山脈高處有一個巨大的滑石礦床。"},{"en":"High in the French Pyrenees means located high up in the Pyrenees mountains in France.","zh":"位於法國庇里牛斯山脈高處，是指處於法國境內庇里牛斯山的高海拔位置。"},{"en":"A mountain village high in the French Pyrenees may be difficult to reach in winter.","zh":"位於法國庇里牛斯山脈高處的山村，在冬天可能難以到達。"},{"en":"Because the site is high in the mountains, mining and transport may require careful planning.","zh":"因為地點位於高山，採礦和運輸可能需要仔細規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase gives both the location and the mountainous setting.","zh":"這個短語同時交代位置和山區環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"above sea level","meaning":"海拔","examples":[{"en":"Trimouns lies about 1,700 metres above sea level.","zh":"Trimouns 位於海拔約 1,700 米。"},{"en":"Above sea level means higher than the average level of the sea.","zh":"海拔，是指高於平均海平面的高度。"},{"en":"A city 500 metres above sea level is higher than a coastal town.","zh":"一個海拔 500 米的城市比沿海城鎮更高。"},{"en":"Places high above sea level may have colder weather and thinner air.","zh":"海拔高的地方可能天氣較冷，空氣較稀薄。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to describe altitude.","zh":"這個短語用來描述高度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a huge deposit of","meaning":"大型……礦床","examples":[{"en":"Trimouns is a huge deposit of hydrated magnesium silicate.","zh":"Trimouns 是一個大型含水矽酸鎂礦床。"},{"en":"A huge deposit of a mineral is a very large natural amount of it in the ground.","zh":"大型某種礦床，是地下天然存在的大量該礦物。"},{"en":"A country may become important in mining if it has a huge deposit of copper.","zh":"如果一個國家有大型銅礦床，它可能在採礦業中變得重要。"},{"en":"A huge deposit can support long-term industrial production.","zh":"大型礦床可以支援長期工業生產。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large natural supply of a material.","zh":"這個短語描述某種材料的大型天然儲量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hydrated magnesium silicate","meaning":"含水矽酸鎂","examples":[{"en":"Talc is a form of hydrated magnesium silicate.","zh":"滑石是一種含水矽酸鎂。"},{"en":"Hydrated magnesium silicate is the chemical description of talc.","zh":"含水矽酸鎂是滑石的化學描述。"},{"en":"In science class, students may learn that common materials often have formal chemical names.","zh":"在科學課中，學生可能學到常見材料往往有正式化學名稱。"},{"en":"A chemical name sounds technical, but it can refer to a familiar everyday substance.","zh":"化學名稱聽起來技術性很強，但可以指熟悉的日常物質。"},{"en":"This phrase names talc in scientific terms.","zh":"這個短語以科學術語命名滑石。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"to you and me","meaning":"用一般說法就是","examples":[{"en":"Hydrated magnesium silicate is talc to you and me.","zh":"含水矽酸鎂，用一般說法就是滑石。"},{"en":"To you and me means in ordinary everyday language for non-specialists.","zh":"用一般說法就是，是指對非專業人士而言，用日常語言來說。"},{"en":"Sodium chloride is table salt to you and me.","zh":"氯化鈉，用一般說法就是食鹽。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a technical term easier by translating it into common speech.","zh":"這個短語透過把技術術語轉成普通說法，使它更容易理解。"},{"en":"It contrasts expert language with everyday understanding.","zh":"它把專業語言與日常理解作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"across the globe","meaning":"遍佈全球","examples":[{"en":"Luzenac has talc mines across the globe.","zh":"Luzenac 在全球各地都有滑石礦場。"},{"en":"Across the globe means in many different parts of the world.","zh":"遍佈全球，是指在世界許多不同地方。"},{"en":"A popular app may have users across the globe.","zh":"一個流行應用程式可能有遍佈全球的用戶。"},{"en":"When a company operates across the globe, it can serve many markets.","zh":"當公司在全球各地營運，它就能服務許多市場。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises worldwide reach.","zh":"這個短語強調全球範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be used in the manufacture of","meaning":"用於製造……","examples":[{"en":"Talc is used in the manufacture of many everyday products.","zh":"滑石用於製造許多日常用品。"},{"en":"To be used in the manufacture of something means to be used when that product is made.","zh":"用於製造某物，是指在製作該產品時被使用。"},{"en":"Plastic may be used in the manufacture of lunch boxes and water bottles.","zh":"塑膠可用於製造飯盒和水樽。"},{"en":"A material can be important even if consumers never notice it in the final product.","zh":"即使消費者在成品中沒有注意到某種材料，它也可能很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes use during production.","zh":"這個短語描述生產過程中的用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a vast array of","meaning":"大量不同種類的……","examples":[{"en":"Talc is found in a vast array of everyday products.","zh":"滑石存在於大量不同種類的日常用品中。"},{"en":"A vast array of things means a very large variety of them.","zh":"大量不同種類的事物，是指種類非常多。"},{"en":"A supermarket sells a vast array of snacks, drinks and household items.","zh":"超級市場銷售大量不同種類的零食、飲品和家居用品。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests both quantity and variety.","zh":"這個短語同時暗示數量多和種類多。"},{"en":"It helps show that talc is used far more widely than expected.","zh":"它幫助顯示滑石的使用比預期廣泛得多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"everyday products","meaning":"日常用品","examples":[{"en":"Talc is used in many everyday products.","zh":"滑石被用於許多日常用品。"},{"en":"Everyday products are ordinary things people use in daily life.","zh":"日常用品是人們在日常生活中使用的普通物品。"},{"en":"Toothpaste, paper and cosmetics are examples of everyday products.","zh":"牙膏、紙張和化妝品都是日常用品的例子。"},{"en":"A hidden material can be important in everyday products even if users do not recognise it.","zh":"隱藏材料即使用者不認出，也可能在日常用品中很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to common consumer items.","zh":"這個短語指常見消費品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"extending from…to…","meaning":"由……延伸至……","examples":[{"en":"The products extend from paper and paint to cosmetics and car tyres.","zh":"這些產品由紙張和油漆延伸至化妝品和汽車輪胎。"},{"en":"Extending from one thing to another means covering a wide range between those examples.","zh":"由某物延伸至另一物，是指涵蓋這些例子之間的廣泛範圍。"},{"en":"The course topics extend from grammar to public speaking.","zh":"課程主題由文法延伸至公開演說。"},{"en":"This structure shows that the range includes very different items.","zh":"這個結構顯示範圍包含很不同的項目。"},{"en":"It helps readers understand breadth and variety.","zh":"它幫助讀者理解廣度和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"paper, paint and plaster","meaning":"紙張、油漆及灰泥","examples":[{"en":"Paper, paint and plaster can all contain talc.","zh":"紙張、油漆及灰泥都可以含有滑石。"},{"en":"Paper, paint and plaster are common materials used in writing, decoration and building.","zh":"紙張、油漆及灰泥是用於書寫、裝飾和建築的常見材料。"},{"en":"A classroom may contain paper worksheets, painted walls and plaster surfaces.","zh":"課室可能有紙本工作紙、油漆牆壁和灰泥表面。"},{"en":"Talc can improve materials by changing texture, strength or processing quality.","zh":"滑石可以透過改變質感、強度或加工質素來改善材料。"},{"en":"This phrase lists ordinary products where talc may appear.","zh":"這個短語列出滑石可能出現的普通產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cosmetics, plastics and car tyres","meaning":"化妝品、塑膠及汽車輪胎","examples":[{"en":"Talc is also used in cosmetics, plastics and car tyres.","zh":"滑石也被用於化妝品、塑膠及汽車輪胎。"},{"en":"Cosmetics, plastics and car tyres are products from very different industries.","zh":"化妝品、塑膠及汽車輪胎來自非常不同的行業。"},{"en":"A single mineral can appear in makeup, packaging and vehicle parts.","zh":"同一種礦物可以出現在化妝品、包裝材料和汽車部件中。"},{"en":"This variety shows how versatile talc is as an industrial material.","zh":"這種多樣性顯示滑石作為工業材料有多用途。"},{"en":"This phrase lists examples that show talc’s wide range of uses.","zh":"這個短語列出能顯示滑石用途廣泛的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"best-known end use","meaning":"最廣為人知的最終用途","examples":[{"en":"Talcum powder is talc’s best-known end use.","zh":"爽身粉是滑石最廣為人知的最終用途。"},{"en":"A best-known end use is the final product or application that most people recognise.","zh":"最廣為人知的最終用途，是大多數人認出的最終產品或應用。"},{"en":"Drinking is the best-known end use of bottled water, although water also has industrial uses.","zh":"飲用是瓶裝水最廣為人知的最終用途，雖然水也有工業用途。"},{"en":"A material may have many uses, but the public may know only the most familiar one.","zh":"一種材料可能有許多用途，但公眾可能只知道最熟悉的一種。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the most famous final application.","zh":"這個短語指最著名的最終應用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"talcum powder","meaning":"爽身粉；滑石粉","examples":[{"en":"Talcum powder is commonly associated with babies.","zh":"爽身粉通常與嬰兒聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Talcum powder is a soft powder made from talc and often used on the skin.","zh":"爽身粉是由滑石製成、常用於皮膚上的柔滑粉末。"},{"en":"Some people think of talcum powder as a bathroom or baby-care product.","zh":"有些人把爽身粉視為浴室用品或嬰兒護理產品。"},{"en":"Because talcum powder is familiar, people may be surprised by talc’s industrial uses.","zh":"因為爽身粉很熟悉，人們可能對滑石的工業用途感到驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the everyday powder form of talc.","zh":"這個短語指滑石的日常粉末形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"true versatility","meaning":"真正的多用途性","examples":[{"en":"The true versatility of talc is shown in its many different uses.","zh":"滑石的真正多用途性體現在它許多不同用途之中。"},{"en":"True versatility means real ability to be used effectively in many different ways.","zh":"真正的多用途性，是指能以許多不同方式有效使用的實際能力。"},{"en":"A smartphone’s true versatility is shown when it is used for study, payment, maps and photos.","zh":"智能手機可用於學習、付款、地圖和拍照時，就顯示其真正多用途性。"},{"en":"A material is versatile when it works across very different industries.","zh":"當一種材料能在非常不同的行業中發揮作用，它就是多用途的。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses genuine multi-purpose usefulness.","zh":"這個短語強調真實的多功能用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"remarkable mineral","meaning":"非凡的礦物","examples":[{"en":"Talc is a remarkable mineral with many industrial applications.","zh":"滑石是一種有許多工業應用的非凡礦物。"},{"en":"A remarkable mineral is a natural substance that is unusual or impressive because of its properties.","zh":"非凡的礦物，是因其特性而顯得不尋常或令人印象深刻的天然物質。"},{"en":"Salt is a remarkable mineral because it is used in food, medicine and industry.","zh":"鹽是一種非凡的礦物，因為它用於食品、醫藥和工業。"},{"en":"Talc is remarkable because it is soft, stable and useful in many products.","zh":"滑石非凡，因為它柔軟、穩定，而且在許多產品中有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mineral that deserves special attention.","zh":"這個短語描述值得特別注意的礦物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be nowhere better displayed than in","meaning":"在……最能體現","examples":[{"en":"Talc’s versatility is nowhere better displayed than in its niche uses.","zh":"滑石的多用途性在其細分用途中最能體現。"},{"en":"Be nowhere better displayed than in something means be shown most clearly in that place or example.","zh":"在某事中最能體現，是指在該地方或例子中最清楚顯示。"},{"en":"A teacher’s patience is nowhere better displayed than in helping weaker students after class.","zh":"老師的耐性在課後幫助較弱學生時最能體現。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the best evidence for a quality.","zh":"這個短語突出某特質的最佳證據。"},{"en":"It means one example shows the point better than any other.","zh":"它表示某例子比其他例子更能顯示重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"surprising use in","meaning":"在……中的意想不到用途","examples":[{"en":"Talc has a surprising use in the food industry.","zh":"滑石在食品業中有意想不到的用途。"},{"en":"A surprising use in a field is an application that people do not expect.","zh":"在某領域中的意想不到用途，是人們沒有預期的應用。"},{"en":"Baking soda has a surprising use in cleaning as well as cooking.","zh":"小蘇打除了烹飪外，在清潔中也有意想不到的用途。"},{"en":"A surprising use can change how people think about an ordinary material.","zh":"意想不到用途可以改變人們對普通材料的看法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an unexpected application.","zh":"這個短語引入出乎意料的應用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"niche markets","meaning":"細分市場","examples":[{"en":"Talc is valuable in certain niche markets.","zh":"滑石在某些細分市場中很有價值。"},{"en":"Niche markets are small, specialised parts of a larger market.","zh":"細分市場是較大市場中小型而專門化的部分。"},{"en":"A shop selling handmade violin cases serves a niche market.","zh":"銷售手製小提琴盒的商店服務一個細分市場。"},{"en":"Niche markets may be small, but customers often need very specific quality.","zh":"細分市場可能規模小，但顧客通常需要非常特定的質素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes specialised market segments.","zh":"這個短語描述專門化市場板塊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the food and agriculture industries","meaning":"食品及農業","examples":[{"en":"Talc has applications in the food and agriculture industries.","zh":"滑石在食品及農業中有應用。"},{"en":"The food and agriculture industries include businesses that produce, process or protect food and crops.","zh":"食品及農業包括生產、加工或保護食品和作物的業務。"},{"en":"Farmers, olive oil processors and chewing gum makers can all be part of these industries.","zh":"農民、橄欖油加工商和香口膠製造商都可以屬於這些行業。"},{"en":"Materials used in these industries often help with processing, protection or product quality.","zh":"這些行業使用的材料通常有助加工、保護或提升產品質素。"},{"en":"This phrase groups together food processing and farming-related businesses.","zh":"這個短語把食品加工和農業相關業務合在一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Take, for example,…","meaning":"以……為例","examples":[{"en":"Take, for example, the chewing gum business.","zh":"以香口膠行業為例。"},{"en":"Take, for example, is used to introduce a specific example of a general point.","zh":"以某事為例，是用來引入一般重點的具體例子。"},{"en":"Many school rules protect safety. Take, for example, the rule against running in corridors.","zh":"許多校規保障安全。以禁止在走廊奔跑的規則為例。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers move from a broad idea to a clear case.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者由廣泛想法轉到清楚個案。"},{"en":"It is useful when the writer wants to prove a point through an example.","zh":"當作者想透過例子證明觀點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the chewing gum business","meaning":"香口膠業務；香口膠行業","examples":[{"en":"The chewing gum business is an important niche market for talc.","zh":"香口膠行業是滑石的重要細分市場。"},{"en":"The chewing gum business means the industry that produces and sells chewing gum.","zh":"香口膠行業是生產和銷售香口膠的行業。"},{"en":"A supplier may work with the chewing gum business by providing ingredients for gum base.","zh":"供應商可能透過提供膠基材料與香口膠行業合作。"},{"en":"This business values reliable materials because changing ingredients can affect the product.","zh":"這個行業重視可靠材料，因為更換成分可能影響產品。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to chewing gum as a commercial sector.","zh":"這個短語指香口膠作為商業板塊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"own and operate","meaning":"擁有並營運","examples":[{"en":"Talc de Luzenac France owns and operates the Trimouns mine.","zh":"Talc de Luzenac France 擁有並營運 Trimouns 礦場。"},{"en":"To own and operate something means to possess it and manage its daily running.","zh":"擁有並營運某物，是指擁有它並管理其日常運作。"},{"en":"A family may own and operate a small restaurant in their neighbourhood.","zh":"一個家庭可能擁有並營運社區中的小餐廳。"},{"en":"Owning a mine is different from operating it, because operation involves workers, equipment and planning.","zh":"擁有礦場不同於營運礦場，因為營運涉及工人、設備和規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both ownership and management.","zh":"這個短語描述所有權和管理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Trimouns mine","meaning":"Trimouns 礦場","examples":[{"en":"The Trimouns mine supplies talc for many industries.","zh":"Trimouns 礦場為許多行業供應滑石。"},{"en":"The Trimouns mine is a talc mine in the French Pyrenees.","zh":"Trimouns 礦場是位於法國庇里牛斯山脈的滑石礦場。"},{"en":"A mining company may transport material from the Trimouns mine to factories across Europe.","zh":"採礦公司可能把 Trimouns 礦場的材料運往歐洲各地工廠。"},{"en":"Because the mine produces high-quality talc, it can supply specialised markets.","zh":"由於該礦場生產高質素滑石，它可以供應專門市場。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific talc-producing site.","zh":"這個短語指一個特定滑石生產地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be a member of","meaning":"是……的成員","examples":[{"en":"The company is a member of the international Luzenac Group.","zh":"該公司是國際 Luzenac 集團的成員。"},{"en":"To be a member of an organisation means to belong to it.","zh":"是某組織的成員，是指屬於該組織。"},{"en":"A student can be a member of the school science club.","zh":"學生可以是學校科學學會的成員。"},{"en":"Membership can connect a smaller company with a larger network.","zh":"成員身份可以把較小公司與較大網絡連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes belonging to a group or organisation.","zh":"這個短語描述屬於某群體或組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"international group","meaning":"國際集團","examples":[{"en":"Luzenac Group is an international group in the minerals industry.","zh":"Luzenac Group 是礦物業中的國際集團。"},{"en":"An international group is an organisation that operates in more than one country.","zh":"國際集團是在多於一個國家營運的組織。"},{"en":"An international hotel group may manage hotels in Asia, Europe and America.","zh":"國際酒店集團可能在亞洲、歐洲和美洲管理酒店。"},{"en":"International groups can share resources, technology and customers across borders.","zh":"國際集團可以跨國共享資源、技術和客戶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a company or organisation with global operations.","zh":"這個短語描述具有全球營運的公司或組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"supply something to someone","meaning":"向某人供應某物","examples":[{"en":"The company supplies talc to chewing gum manufacturers in Europe.","zh":"該公司向歐洲香口膠製造商供應滑石。"},{"en":"To supply something to someone means to provide it for their use.","zh":"向某人供應某物，是指提供它給對方使用。"},{"en":"A farm may supply vegetables to local restaurants.","zh":"農場可能向本地餐廳供應蔬菜。"},{"en":"Reliable supply helps manufacturers keep production steady.","zh":"可靠供應幫助製造商保持生產穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes providing goods or materials to a customer.","zh":"這個短語描述向客戶提供貨品或材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"chewing gum manufacturers","meaning":"香口膠製造商","examples":[{"en":"Chewing gum manufacturers use talc in the gum base.","zh":"香口膠製造商在膠基中使用滑石。"},{"en":"Chewing gum manufacturers are companies that make chewing gum.","zh":"香口膠製造商是製造香口膠的公司。"},{"en":"Chewing gum manufacturers need safe ingredients that create the right texture.","zh":"香口膠製造商需要能產生合適質感的安全成分。"},{"en":"If they change suppliers, manufacturers may need to reformulate the gum.","zh":"如果他們轉換供應商，製造商可能需要重新調整香口膠配方。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to businesses that produce chewing gum.","zh":"這個短語指生產香口膠的企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sales manager","meaning":"銷售經理","examples":[{"en":"Laurent Fournier is a sales manager in Luzenac’s Specialties business unit.","zh":"Laurent Fournier 是 Luzenac Specialties 業務部門的銷售經理。"},{"en":"A sales manager is a person who manages the selling of products or services.","zh":"銷售經理是管理產品或服務銷售的人。"},{"en":"A sales manager may speak with customers, set targets and organise supply agreements.","zh":"銷售經理可能與客戶溝通、設定目標和安排供應協議。"},{"en":"Sales managers are important because they connect a company’s products with buyers.","zh":"銷售經理很重要，因為他們把公司的產品與買家連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a business role focused on sales.","zh":"這個短語描述專注於銷售的商業職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"business unit","meaning":"業務部門","examples":[{"en":"Fournier works in Luzenac’s Specialties business unit in Toulouse.","zh":"Fournier 在 Luzenac 位於圖盧茲的 Specialties 業務部門工作。"},{"en":"A business unit is a section of a company responsible for a particular type of work or market.","zh":"業務部門是公司中負責某類工作或市場的部分。"},{"en":"A large school may have a technology unit that handles computers and online systems.","zh":"大型學校可能有科技部門，負責電腦和網上系統。"},{"en":"Business units help large organisations manage specialised tasks.","zh":"業務部門幫助大型組織管理專門任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a division inside a company.","zh":"這個短語描述公司內部的分部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sector of the market","meaning":"市場板塊","examples":[{"en":"Luzenac has sold to this sector of the market since the 1960s.","zh":"Luzenac 自 1960 年代以來一直向這個市場板塊銷售。"},{"en":"A sector of the market is one particular part of a larger market.","zh":"市場板塊是較大市場中的某個特定部分。"},{"en":"Organic baby food is a small sector of the food market.","zh":"有機嬰兒食品是食品市場中的一個小板塊。"},{"en":"Companies study market sectors so they can meet specialised customer needs.","zh":"公司研究市場板塊，以滿足專門客戶需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific commercial segment.","zh":"這個短語描述特定商業部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"since the 1960s","meaning":"自1960年代以來","examples":[{"en":"The company has sold talc to this market since the 1960s.","zh":"該公司自 1960 年代以來一直向這個市場銷售滑石。"},{"en":"Since the 1960s means from the decade 1960 to 1969 until now or until the time discussed.","zh":"自 1960 年代以來，是指由 1960 至 1969 年這個十年開始直到現在或文中所指時間。"},{"en":"The school has used the same hall for assemblies since the 1960s.","zh":"學校自 1960 年代以來一直使用同一禮堂舉行早會。"},{"en":"A relationship lasting since the 1960s suggests long experience and reliability.","zh":"自 1960 年代以來持續的關係暗示長期經驗和可靠性。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a long historical time frame.","zh":"這個短語給出很長的歷史時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"admittedly","meaning":"誠然","examples":[{"en":"Admittedly, the amount supplied to gum manufacturers is relatively small.","zh":"誠然，供應給香口膠製造商的數量相對較小。"},{"en":"Admittedly is used to accept a point before giving a different or stronger point.","zh":"誠然，是用來先承認一點，再提出不同或更強的重點。"},{"en":"Admittedly, the classroom is small, but the teacher uses the space well.","zh":"誠然，課室很小，但老師善用空間。"},{"en":"This word makes writing fairer because it recognises a limitation.","zh":"這個詞令寫作較公平，因為它承認限制。"},{"en":"It often means the writer is saying “this is true, but there is more to consider.”","zh":"它通常表示作者在說「這是真的，但還有更多需要考慮」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in terms of","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"In terms of total annual sales, the amount is relatively small.","zh":"就全年總銷售額而言，該數量相對較小。"},{"en":"In terms of something means when considering that particular aspect.","zh":"就某事而言，是指從該特定方面來考慮。"},{"en":"In terms of price, the old phone is cheaper, but the new one is faster.","zh":"就價格而言，舊手機較便宜，但新手機較快。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers focus on one measure or viewpoint.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者集中於一個量度或角度。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing different aspects of a situation.","zh":"它適合比較情況中的不同方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"total annual sales","meaning":"全年總銷售額","examples":[{"en":"The chewing gum market represents a small part of total annual sales.","zh":"香口膠市場只佔全年總銷售額的一小部分。"},{"en":"Total annual sales are the full amount sold by a company in one year.","zh":"全年總銷售額是公司一年內售出的完整數量或金額。"},{"en":"A shop may review its total annual sales to see whether business is growing.","zh":"商店可能檢視全年總銷售額，以了解業務是否增長。"},{"en":"A small market can still be valuable even if it is a small part of annual sales.","zh":"即使某市場只佔全年銷售額一小部分，它仍可能很有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes yearly sales volume or value.","zh":"這個短語描述一年的銷售量或銷售價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"relatively small","meaning":"相對較小","examples":[{"en":"The amount of talc supplied to gum manufacturers is relatively small.","zh":"供應給香口膠製造商的滑石數量相對較小。"},{"en":"Relatively small means small when compared with something else.","zh":"相對較小，是指與其他東西比較時較小。"},{"en":"A class of twenty students is relatively small compared with a lecture hall of two hundred.","zh":"與二百人的演講廳相比，二十人的班級相對較小。"},{"en":"Something can be relatively small but still important for quality or customer loyalty.","zh":"某事可以相對較小，但仍對質素或客戶忠誠很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes size in comparison, not absolute size alone.","zh":"這個短語描述比較中的大小，而不只是絕對大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"valuable niche market","meaning":"有價值的細分市場","examples":[{"en":"Chewing gum is a valuable niche market for Luzenac.","zh":"香口膠是 Luzenac 的有價值細分市場。"},{"en":"A valuable niche market is a small specialised market that is still profitable or important.","zh":"有價值的細分市場，是小型專門市場，但仍有盈利或重要性。"},{"en":"A bakery selling gluten-free cakes may serve a valuable niche market.","zh":"銷售無麩質蛋糕的麵包店可能服務一個有價值的細分市場。"},{"en":"Niche markets can be valuable because customers may need trusted suppliers and special quality.","zh":"細分市場可以有價值，因為客戶可能需要可信供應商和特殊質素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specialised market worth serving.","zh":"這個短語描述值得服務的專門市場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"place a premium on","meaning":"重視；願意為……付出較高代價","examples":[{"en":"Customers place a premium on reliable, high-quality supplies.","zh":"客戶重視可靠而優質的供應。"},{"en":"To place a premium on something means to value it highly and be willing to pay or care more for it.","zh":"重視某事，是指高度看重它，並願意為它付出更多金錢或注意。"},{"en":"Parents may place a premium on a school’s safety record.","zh":"父母可能非常重視學校的安全記錄。"},{"en":"When switching suppliers is risky, companies place a premium on reliability.","zh":"當轉換供應商有風險，公司就會特別重視可靠性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving special importance to something.","zh":"這個短語描述對某事賦予特別重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"securing supplies","meaning":"確保供應","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers place a premium on securing supplies from a reliable source.","zh":"製造商重視從可靠來源確保供應。"},{"en":"Securing supplies means making sure the needed materials will be available.","zh":"確保供應，是指確保所需材料能夠取得。"},{"en":"A restaurant secures supplies of fresh vegetables before a busy weekend.","zh":"餐廳會在繁忙週末前確保新鮮蔬菜供應。"},{"en":"Secure supplies prevent production delays and quality problems.","zh":"穩定供應可以防止生產延誤和質素問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ensuring a steady supply of materials.","zh":"這個短語描述確保材料穩定供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"reliable, high-quality source","meaning":"可靠而優質的來源","examples":[{"en":"Chewing gum manufacturers want a reliable, high-quality source of talc.","zh":"香口膠製造商想要可靠而優質的滑石來源。"},{"en":"A reliable, high-quality source is a supplier that provides good materials consistently.","zh":"可靠而優質的來源，是能持續提供良好材料的供應商。"},{"en":"A school canteen needs a reliable, high-quality source of fresh food.","zh":"學校飯堂需要可靠而優質的新鮮食物來源。"},{"en":"Manufacturers prefer such sources because poor materials can damage the final product.","zh":"製造商偏好這類來源，因為劣質材料會損害最終產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a trusted supplier of good-quality material.","zh":"這個短語描述值得信任的優質材料供應者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"long-term allegiance to","meaning":"對……的長期忠誠","examples":[{"en":"Long-term allegiance to a proven supplier is common in this sector.","zh":"對經驗證可靠供應商的長期忠誠在這個板塊很常見。"},{"en":"Long-term allegiance to someone means continuing loyalty or commitment over a long period.","zh":"對某人的長期忠誠，是指長時間持續的忠誠或承諾。"},{"en":"A family may show long-term allegiance to the same doctor because they trust her.","zh":"一個家庭可能因信任同一位醫生而長期忠誠於她。"},{"en":"In business, long-term allegiance reduces risk when changing suppliers would be costly.","zh":"在商業中，當更換供應商成本高，長期忠誠可以降低風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sustained loyalty.","zh":"這個短語描述持續忠誠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"proven supplier","meaning":"經驗證可靠的供應商","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers prefer to buy from a proven supplier.","zh":"製造商較喜歡向經驗證可靠的供應商購買。"},{"en":"A proven supplier is a supplier that has already shown it is reliable and effective.","zh":"經驗證可靠的供應商，是已顯示自己可靠而有效的供應商。"},{"en":"A school may choose a proven supplier for exam papers because mistakes would be serious.","zh":"學校可能選擇經驗證可靠的考卷供應商，因為出錯會很嚴重。"},{"en":"Proven suppliers reduce uncertainty because customers know what quality to expect.","zh":"經驗證可靠的供應商減少不確定性，因為客戶知道可期待甚麼質素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a supplier with a trusted track record.","zh":"這個短語描述有可信往績的供應商。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a feature of this sector","meaning":"這個行業板塊的特徵","examples":[{"en":"Supplier loyalty is a feature of this sector of the talc market.","zh":"供應商忠誠是滑石市場這個板塊的特徵。"},{"en":"A feature of this sector means a characteristic commonly found in that part of the market.","zh":"這個板塊的特徵，是該市場部分中常見的特性。"},{"en":"High customer trust is a feature of the private tutoring sector.","zh":"高客戶信任是私人補習行業板塊的特徵。"},{"en":"Understanding sector features helps companies sell products more effectively.","zh":"理解板塊特徵幫助公司更有效銷售產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a typical characteristic of a market segment.","zh":"這個短語描述市場板塊的典型特性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"switching sources","meaning":"轉換供應來源","examples":[{"en":"Switching sources is not an easy option for chewing gum manufacturers.","zh":"對香口膠製造商來說，轉換供應來源不是容易的選擇。"},{"en":"Switching sources means changing from one supplier or source of materials to another.","zh":"轉換供應來源，是指從一個供應商或材料來源改到另一個。"},{"en":"A bakery may avoid switching flour sources if the new flour changes the bread texture.","zh":"如果新麵粉改變麵包質感，麵包店可能避免轉換麵粉來源。"},{"en":"Switching sources can create extra testing, cost and quality risks.","zh":"轉換供應來源可能帶來額外測試、成本和質素風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing where materials are obtained.","zh":"這個短語描述改變材料取得來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not an easy option","meaning":"不是容易的選擇","examples":[{"en":"Changing supplier is not an easy option for these manufacturers.","zh":"對這些製造商來說，更換供應商不是容易的選擇。"},{"en":"Not an easy option means difficult, costly or risky to choose.","zh":"不是容易的選擇，是指難以選擇、成本高或有風險。"},{"en":"Moving house is not an easy option for a family with children in school.","zh":"對有孩子上學的家庭來說，搬屋不是容易的選擇。"},{"en":"If a choice creates many extra problems, it is not an easy option.","zh":"如果一個選擇帶來許多額外問題，它就不是容易的選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a choice that is possible but hard.","zh":"這個短語描述一個可行但困難的選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"A manufacturer may choose one supplier rather than another.","zh":"製造商可能選擇一個供應商，而不是另一個。"},{"en":"Rather than shows contrast and means instead of.","zh":"rather than 表示對比，意思是「而不是」。"},{"en":"A student may revise with practice questions rather than only rereading notes.","zh":"學生可能用練習題溫習，而不是只重讀筆記。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show which option is chosen and which is rejected.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示哪個選項被選擇，哪個被排除。"},{"en":"It makes comparison clear.","zh":"它令比較清楚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the cost of reformulating","meaning":"重新調整配方的成本","examples":[{"en":"The cost of reformulating chewing gum is high.","zh":"重新調整香口膠配方的成本很高。"},{"en":"The cost of reformulating means the money, time and effort needed to change a product’s formula.","zh":"重新調整配方的成本，是改變產品配方所需的金錢、時間和努力。"},{"en":"A drink company may face the cost of reformulating if a sweetener is banned.","zh":"如果某種甜味劑被禁，飲品公司可能面對重新調整配方的成本。"},{"en":"High reformulation costs make companies reluctant to change suppliers.","zh":"高昂的配方調整成本令公司不願更換供應商。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the burden of changing a product recipe.","zh":"這個短語描述改變產品配方的負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"reformulate","meaning":"重新調整配方","examples":[{"en":"Chewing gum manufacturers may need to reformulate their product if they change suppliers.","zh":"如果香口膠製造商更換供應商，可能需要重新調整產品配方。"},{"en":"To reformulate a product means to change its ingredients or recipe.","zh":"重新調整產品配方，是指改變其成分或製法。"},{"en":"A skincare company may reformulate a cream to remove an ingredient customers dislike.","zh":"護膚品公司可能重新調整面霜配方，以移除顧客不喜歡的成分。"},{"en":"Reformulating can be expensive because the new product must be tested again.","zh":"重新調整配方可能昂貴，因為新產品必須再次測試。"},{"en":"This word describes changing a product’s formula.","zh":"這個詞描述改變產品配方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"talc grade","meaning":"滑石等級","examples":[{"en":"Customers often continue using a talc grade that works well.","zh":"客戶通常繼續使用效果良好的滑石等級。"},{"en":"A talc grade is a particular quality or type of talc used for a specific purpose.","zh":"滑石等級是用於特定目的的某種質素或類型的滑石。"},{"en":"A factory may choose a talc grade based on particle size and purity.","zh":"工廠可能根據粒子大小和純度選擇滑石等級。"},{"en":"If one grade gives the right texture, customers may not want to change it.","zh":"如果某一等級帶來合適質感，客戶可能不想改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific category or quality level of talc.","zh":"這個短語描述滑石的特定類別或質素級別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"understandably reluctant to","meaning":"可以理解地不願意……","examples":[{"en":"Customers are understandably reluctant to switch suppliers.","zh":"客戶可以理解地不願意轉換供應商。"},{"en":"Understandably reluctant to do something means unwilling to do it for reasons that are easy to understand.","zh":"可以理解地不願意做某事，是指因為容易理解的原因而不願做。"},{"en":"A student may be understandably reluctant to change schools before final exams.","zh":"學生可能可以理解地不願意在期末考前轉校。"},{"en":"People become reluctant when change brings risk, cost or uncertainty.","zh":"當改變帶來風險、成本或不確定性，人們就會不願意。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that hesitation is reasonable.","zh":"這個短語顯示猶豫是合理的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be used in the manufacture of chewing gum","meaning":"用於香口膠製造","examples":[{"en":"Talc is used in the manufacture of chewing gum.","zh":"滑石用於香口膠製造。"},{"en":"To be used in the manufacture of chewing gum means to be part of the process of making chewing gum.","zh":"用於香口膠製造，是指成為製作香口膠過程的一部分。"},{"en":"A factory may use talc in the gum base before flavourings are added.","zh":"工廠可能在加入調味料前，把滑石用於膠基。"},{"en":"Talc helps production by acting as a filler and reducing stickiness.","zh":"滑石透過充當填充劑和減少黏性來幫助生產。"},{"en":"This phrase describes talc’s role in making chewing gum.","zh":"這個短語描述滑石在製造香口膠中的角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"an engineer with a degree in","meaning":"擁有……學位的工程師","examples":[{"en":"Patrick Delord is an engineer with a degree in agronomics.","zh":"Patrick Delord 是一名擁有農藝學學位的工程師。"},{"en":"An engineer with a degree in a subject is a trained engineer who studied that field at university.","zh":"擁有某學位的工程師，是在大學修讀該領域並受過訓練的工程師。"},{"en":"A company may hire an engineer with a degree in environmental science to design safer systems.","zh":"公司可能聘請擁有環境科學學位的工程師來設計更安全系統。"},{"en":"A specialised degree gives technical knowledge for solving industry problems.","zh":"專門學位提供解決行業問題的技術知識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both a job role and educational background.","zh":"這個短語同時描述職位和教育背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"agronomics","meaning":"農藝學","examples":[{"en":"Delord has a degree in agronomics.","zh":"Delord 擁有農藝學學位。"},{"en":"Agronomics is the study of farming, crops and agricultural production.","zh":"農藝學是研究農業、作物和農業生產的學科。"},{"en":"A student interested in improving fruit crops may study agronomics.","zh":"對改善水果作物感興趣的學生可能修讀農藝學。"},{"en":"Knowledge of agronomics helps companies understand how minerals can be used in agriculture.","zh":"農藝學知識幫助公司理解礦物如何用於農業。"},{"en":"This word refers to the scientific study of crop production.","zh":"這個詞指對作物生產的科學研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have been with a company for","meaning":"在某公司任職已有……","examples":[{"en":"Delord has been with Luzenac for 22 years.","zh":"Delord 在 Luzenac 任職已有 22 年。"},{"en":"To have been with a company for a period means to have worked there during that time.","zh":"在某公司任職已有某段時間，是指在那段時間一直在該公司工作。"},{"en":"A teacher who has been with a school for ten years knows its students and culture well.","zh":"在學校任職已有十年的老師，很熟悉學生和校園文化。"},{"en":"Long service can suggest experience and deep knowledge of the company’s products.","zh":"長期任職可以暗示經驗和對公司產品的深入了解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes length of employment.","zh":"這個短語描述受僱時間長短。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"senior market development manager","meaning":"高級市場開發經理","examples":[{"en":"Delord is a senior market development manager in Europe.","zh":"Delord 是歐洲的高級市場開發經理。"},{"en":"A senior market development manager is an experienced manager who finds and grows markets for products.","zh":"高級市場開發經理是尋找並拓展產品市場的資深經理。"},{"en":"A company may ask a senior market development manager to explore new customers overseas.","zh":"公司可能要求高級市場開發經理開拓海外新客戶。"},{"en":"This role matters when a company wants to turn a technical product into a commercial opportunity.","zh":"當公司想把技術產品變成商業機會，這個職位很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a high-level business development position.","zh":"這個短語描述高級業務開發職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"main components","meaning":"主要成分","examples":[{"en":"Chewing gum has four main components.","zh":"香口膠有四種主要成分。"},{"en":"Main components are the most important parts that make up something.","zh":"主要成分是構成某物的最重要部分。"},{"en":"A simple sandwich has main components such as bread, filling and sauce.","zh":"簡單三文治有麵包、餡料和醬汁等主要成分。"},{"en":"Understanding the main components helps explain how a product works.","zh":"理解主要成分有助解釋產品如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the key ingredients or parts.","zh":"這個短語指關鍵材料或部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"gum base","meaning":"香口膠膠基","examples":[{"en":"The gum base is the most important component of chewing gum.","zh":"膠基是香口膠最重要的成分。"},{"en":"Gum base is the chewy material that gives chewing gum its structure.","zh":"香口膠膠基是賦予香口膠結構的可咀嚼材料。"},{"en":"A factory adds sweeteners and flavourings to gum base to make finished chewing gum.","zh":"工廠會在膠基中加入甜味劑和調味料，製成成品香口膠。"},{"en":"Without a proper gum base, chewing gum would not have the right chewiness.","zh":"沒有合適膠基，香口膠就不會有正確咀嚼感。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the basic chewy foundation of gum.","zh":"這個短語指香口膠的基本咀嚼基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"put the chew into","meaning":"賦予……咀嚼口感","examples":[{"en":"The gum base puts the chew into chewing gum.","zh":"膠基賦予香口膠咀嚼口感。"},{"en":"To put the chew into something means to give it the texture that makes it chewable.","zh":"賦予某物咀嚼口感，是指給它可咀嚼的質感。"},{"en":"Good dough puts the chew into a bagel.","zh":"好麵團賦予貝果咀嚼口感。"},{"en":"In chewing gum, the base creates the elastic feel people expect.","zh":"在香口膠中，膠基創造人們期待的彈性口感。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what gives a product its chewy quality.","zh":"這個短語解釋甚麼賦予產品咀嚼質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"bind the ingredients together","meaning":"把材料黏合在一起","examples":[{"en":"The gum base binds all the ingredients together.","zh":"膠基把所有材料黏合在一起。"},{"en":"To bind ingredients together means to hold them in one mixture or structure.","zh":"把材料黏合在一起，是指把它們固定在同一混合物或結構中。"},{"en":"Eggs can bind ingredients together in a cake mixture.","zh":"雞蛋可以把蛋糕混合物中的材料黏合在一起。"},{"en":"If ingredients are not bound together, the product may fall apart or lose texture.","zh":"如果材料沒有被黏合在一起，產品可能散開或失去質感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making separate materials hold together.","zh":"這個短語描述令分開材料結合在一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ingredients","meaning":"材料；成分","examples":[{"en":"The gum base binds all the ingredients together.","zh":"膠基把所有成分黏合在一起。"},{"en":"Ingredients are the materials used to make a food, product or mixture.","zh":"材料或成分是用來製作食品、產品或混合物的物質。"},{"en":"Flour, sugar and eggs are common ingredients in a cake.","zh":"麵粉、糖和雞蛋是蛋糕中的常見成分。"},{"en":"Choosing the right ingredients affects taste, texture and quality.","zh":"選擇合適成分會影響味道、質感和質素。"},{"en":"This word refers to the things combined to make something.","zh":"這個詞指合成某物的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"soft, smooth texture","meaning":"柔軟順滑的質感","examples":[{"en":"The gum base creates a soft, smooth texture.","zh":"膠基創造柔軟順滑的質感。"},{"en":"A soft, smooth texture feels gentle, even and not rough.","zh":"柔軟順滑的質感，是感覺溫和、均勻、不粗糙。"},{"en":"A good pudding should have a soft, smooth texture rather than lumps.","zh":"好布甸應有柔軟順滑的質感，而不是有顆粒。"},{"en":"Texture affects whether a product feels pleasant to eat or use.","zh":"質感會影響產品吃起來或用起來是否舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical feel of a product.","zh":"這個短語描述產品的實際觸感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sweeteners, softeners and flavourings","meaning":"甜味劑、軟化劑及調味料","examples":[{"en":"The manufacturer adds sweeteners, softeners and flavourings to the gum base.","zh":"製造商在膠基中加入甜味劑、軟化劑及調味料。"},{"en":"Sweeteners, softeners and flavourings are ingredients that add sweetness, texture and taste.","zh":"甜味劑、軟化劑及調味料是加入甜味、質感和味道的成分。"},{"en":"A candy maker may adjust sweeteners and flavourings to create a new fruit taste.","zh":"糖果製造商可能調整甜味劑和調味料，以創造新水果味。"},{"en":"These ingredients turn a basic gum base into a product people enjoy chewing.","zh":"這些成分把基本膠基變成人們喜歡咀嚼的產品。"},{"en":"This phrase lists additives that improve the final product.","zh":"這個短語列出改善成品的添加成分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be used as a filler","meaning":"被用作填充劑","examples":[{"en":"Talc is used as a filler in the gum base.","zh":"滑石在膠基中被用作填充劑。"},{"en":"To be used as a filler means to be added to give body, volume or structure to a product.","zh":"被用作填充劑，是指被加入產品中以提供體積、份量或結構。"},{"en":"Some foods use fibre as a filler to improve texture without adding much flavour.","zh":"有些食品使用纖維作填充劑，以改善質感而不加入太多味道。"},{"en":"Fillers can make a product easier to process and more stable.","zh":"填充劑可以令產品更易加工並更穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a material used to fill out a mixture.","zh":"這個短語描述用來填充混合物的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"varies between…and…","meaning":"介乎……至……之間","examples":[{"en":"The amount of talc varies between ten and 35 per cent.","zh":"滑石用量介乎百分之十至百分之三十五之間。"},{"en":"Varies between two amounts means changes within that range.","zh":"介乎兩個數量之間，是指在該範圍內變動。"},{"en":"The number of students in each tutorial group varies between five and eight.","zh":"每個補習小組的學生人數介乎五至八人之間。"},{"en":"Variation often depends on product type, purpose or customer need.","zh":"變動通常取決於產品種類、目的或客戶需要。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a range instead of one fixed number.","zh":"這個短語給出範圍，而不是固定數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"depending on the type of","meaning":"視乎……種類而定","examples":[{"en":"The amount of talc depends on the type of gum.","zh":"滑石用量視乎香口膠種類而定。"},{"en":"Depending on the type of something means changing according to which kind it is.","zh":"視乎某物種類而定，是指會根據其類別而改變。"},{"en":"Cooking time may differ depending on the type of rice.","zh":"烹調時間可能視乎米的種類而定。"},{"en":"Different products need different materials because their properties are not the same.","zh":"不同產品需要不同材料，因為它們的特性並不相同。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why one amount or method may vary.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何某數量或方法會變動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fruit-flavoured chewing gum","meaning":"水果味香口膠","examples":[{"en":"Fruit-flavoured chewing gum is slightly acidic.","zh":"水果味香口膠略帶酸性。"},{"en":"Fruit-flavoured chewing gum is gum that tastes like fruit.","zh":"水果味香口膠是味道像水果的香口膠。"},{"en":"A child may choose fruit-flavoured chewing gum instead of mint gum.","zh":"孩子可能選擇水果味香口膠，而不是薄荷味香口膠。"},{"en":"Fruit flavours can make the gum more acidic, which affects what fillers can be used.","zh":"水果味可以令香口膠更酸，影響可使用甚麼填充劑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes chewing gum with a fruit taste.","zh":"這個短語描述帶水果味的香口膠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"slightly acidic","meaning":"略帶酸性","examples":[{"en":"Fruit-flavoured chewing gum is slightly acidic.","zh":"水果味香口膠略帶酸性。"},{"en":"Slightly acidic means having a small amount of acidity.","zh":"略帶酸性，是指有少量酸性。"},{"en":"Lemon water is acidic, while some fruit drinks are only slightly acidic.","zh":"檸檬水有酸性，而有些水果飲品只是略帶酸性。"},{"en":"If a mixture is acidic, it may react with certain ingredients.","zh":"如果混合物有酸性，它可能與某些成分產生反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mild acidity, not a strong acid.","zh":"這個短語描述輕微酸性，而不是強酸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"react with","meaning":"與……產生反應","examples":[{"en":"Acidic chewing gum would react with calcium carbonate.","zh":"酸性香口膠會與碳酸鈣產生反應。"},{"en":"To react with something means to undergo a chemical change when mixed with it.","zh":"與某物產生反應，是指與它混合時發生化學變化。"},{"en":"Vinegar reacts with baking soda and produces bubbles.","zh":"醋會與小蘇打產生反應並產生氣泡。"},{"en":"If one ingredient reacts with another, the product’s texture or quality may change.","zh":"如果一種成分與另一種成分反應，產品質感或質素可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes chemical interaction.","zh":"這個短語描述化學互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"calcium carbonate","meaning":"碳酸鈣","examples":[{"en":"Calcium carbonate can be used as a filler in some products.","zh":"碳酸鈣可在某些產品中用作填充劑。"},{"en":"Calcium carbonate is a common mineral compound found in limestone and chalk.","zh":"碳酸鈣是一種常見礦物化合物，存在於石灰岩和粉筆中。"},{"en":"A toothpaste may contain calcium carbonate as a mild abrasive.","zh":"牙膏可能含有碳酸鈣作為溫和磨料。"},{"en":"In acidic products, calcium carbonate may react and become unsuitable.","zh":"在酸性產品中，碳酸鈣可能產生反應而不適合使用。"},{"en":"This phrase names a mineral material often used in manufacturing.","zh":"這個短語命名一種常用於製造的礦物材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"Talc, on the other hand, makes an ideal filler.","zh":"另一方面，滑石是理想的填充劑。"},{"en":"On the other hand introduces a contrasting point.","zh":"另一方面，用來引入對比重點。"},{"en":"Sugar adds sweetness; on the other hand, salt can balance flavour.","zh":"糖增加甜味；另一方面，鹽可以平衡味道。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing two materials with different properties.","zh":"比較兩種特性不同的材料時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It signals that the second point differs from the first.","zh":"它表示第二點與第一點不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ideal filler","meaning":"理想的填充劑","examples":[{"en":"Talc makes an ideal filler for fruit-flavoured chewing gum.","zh":"滑石是水果味香口膠的理想填充劑。"},{"en":"An ideal filler is a material that suits the product very well and fills a functional role.","zh":"理想的填充劑，是非常適合產品並發揮功能的材料。"},{"en":"Rice can be an ideal filler in a lunch box because it is cheap, filling and mild in flavour.","zh":"米飯可以是飯盒中的理想填充食物，因為它便宜、飽肚且味道溫和。"},{"en":"Talc is ideal here because it does not react chemically with acidic gum.","zh":"滑石在這裡很理想，因為它不會與酸性香口膠產生化學反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a filler that fits the purpose especially well.","zh":"這個短語描述特別符合目的的填充劑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"chemically non-reactive","meaning":"化學性質不活潑；不易產生化學反應","examples":[{"en":"Talc is chemically non-reactive.","zh":"滑石化學性質不活潑。"},{"en":"Chemically non-reactive means not easily changing or reacting with other substances.","zh":"化學性質不活潑，是指不容易與其他物質改變或反應。"},{"en":"A chemically non-reactive container is useful for storing sensitive liquids.","zh":"化學性質不活潑的容器適合儲存敏感液體。"},{"en":"Non-reactive materials are valuable because they do not alter the product.","zh":"不易反應的材料有價值，因為它們不會改變產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes chemical stability.","zh":"這個短語描述化學穩定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dust the gum base pellets","meaning":"在膠基顆粒上撒粉","examples":[{"en":"Talc is used to dust the gum base pellets.","zh":"滑石被用來在膠基顆粒上撒粉。"},{"en":"To dust the gum base pellets means to cover the small gum base pieces with a fine powder.","zh":"在膠基顆粒上撒粉，是指用細粉覆蓋小塊膠基。"},{"en":"A baker may dust dough with flour to stop it sticking to the table.","zh":"麵包師可能在麵團上撒麵粉，防止它黏在桌上。"},{"en":"Dusting pellets with talc keeps them separate during production.","zh":"在顆粒上撒滑石粉可令它們在生產過程中保持分離。"},{"en":"This phrase describes applying powder to small pieces of gum base.","zh":"這個短語描述把粉末施加在小塊膠基上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"gum base pellets","meaning":"膠基顆粒","examples":[{"en":"The factory dusts the gum base pellets with talc.","zh":"工廠用滑石粉撒在膠基顆粒上。"},{"en":"Gum base pellets are small pieces of gum base used in chewing gum production.","zh":"膠基顆粒是香口膠生產中使用的小塊膠基材料。"},{"en":"A factory may store gum base pellets before mixing them with sweeteners.","zh":"工廠可能在把膠基顆粒與甜味劑混合前儲存它們。"},{"en":"Pellets are easier to handle when they do not stick together.","zh":"當顆粒不黏在一起，就較容易處理。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to small units of chewing gum base material.","zh":"這個短語指香口膠膠基材料的小單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stop something from sticking","meaning":"防止……黏住","examples":[{"en":"Talc stops the chewing gum from sticking during production.","zh":"滑石防止香口膠在生產過程中黏住。"},{"en":"To stop something from sticking means to prevent it from attaching to surfaces or other pieces.","zh":"防止某物黏住，是指避免它黏附在表面或其他物件上。"},{"en":"Flour can stop dough from sticking to a rolling pin.","zh":"麵粉可以防止麵團黏住擀麵棍。"},{"en":"Preventing stickiness makes machines cleaner and production smoother.","zh":"防止黏住能令機器更乾淨，生產更順暢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preventing unwanted adhesion.","zh":"這個短語描述防止不需要的黏附。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lamination and packing process","meaning":"壓片及包裝過程","examples":[{"en":"Talc prevents sticking during the lamination and packing process.","zh":"滑石在壓片及包裝過程中防止黏住。"},{"en":"The lamination and packing process is the stage where gum is flattened, layered and packaged.","zh":"壓片及包裝過程，是香口膠被壓平、分層和包裝的階段。"},{"en":"A food factory needs clean machines during lamination and packing.","zh":"食品工廠在壓片及包裝過程中需要乾淨機器。"},{"en":"If gum sticks during this process, production may slow down or packaging may be damaged.","zh":"如果香口膠在這個過程中黏住，生產可能減慢或包裝可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the final shaping and packaging stages.","zh":"這個短語描述最後成形和包裝階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"food sector","meaning":"食品業","examples":[{"en":"Chewing gum is one example of talc’s use in the food sector.","zh":"香口膠是滑石在食品業中用途的一個例子。"},{"en":"The food sector is the part of the economy involved in making, processing or selling food.","zh":"食品業是經濟中涉及製造、加工或銷售食品的部分。"},{"en":"Bakeries, snack factories and oil processors all belong to the food sector.","zh":"麵包店、零食工廠和榨油商都屬於食品業。"},{"en":"A material used in the food sector must be suitable for contact with food products.","zh":"用於食品業的材料必須適合接觸食品產品。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to food-related businesses and production.","zh":"這個短語指與食品相關的企業和生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for the past 20 years or so","meaning":"在過去約20年來","examples":[{"en":"Olive oil processors have used talc for the past 20 years or so.","zh":"橄欖油加工商在過去約 20 年來一直使用滑石。"},{"en":"For the past 20 years or so means during approximately the last twenty years.","zh":"在過去約 20 年來，是指在最近大約二十年間。"},{"en":"A school may have used online registration for the past five years or so.","zh":"學校可能在過去約五年來一直使用網上登記。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate period rather than an exact date.","zh":"這個短語給出近似時段，而不是精確日期。"},{"en":"It shows that the practice is not new.","zh":"它顯示該做法並不是新的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"olive oil processors","meaning":"橄欖油加工商","examples":[{"en":"Olive oil processors in Spain use talc to improve extraction.","zh":"西班牙橄欖油加工商使用滑石改善提取過程。"},{"en":"Olive oil processors are companies or factories that turn olives into olive oil.","zh":"橄欖油加工商是把橄欖製成橄欖油的公司或工廠。"},{"en":"An olive oil processor crushes olives and separates the oil from water and solids.","zh":"橄欖油加工商會壓碎橄欖，並把油與水和固體分離。"},{"en":"Processors use techniques that improve yield and product quality.","zh":"加工商使用改善出油率和產品質素的技術。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to businesses that produce olive oil from olives.","zh":"這個短語指由橄欖生產橄欖油的企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take advantage of","meaning":"利用","examples":[{"en":"Olive oil processors take advantage of talc’s unique characteristics.","zh":"橄欖油加工商利用滑石的獨特特性。"},{"en":"To take advantage of something means to use it in a helpful or beneficial way.","zh":"利用某事，是指以有幫助或有益的方式使用它。"},{"en":"Students can take advantage of free library resources before exams.","zh":"學生可以在考試前利用免費圖書館資源。"},{"en":"Processors take advantage of talc because its properties solve a practical problem.","zh":"加工商利用滑石，因為其特性能解決實際問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making good use of something.","zh":"這個短語描述善用某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"unique characteristics","meaning":"獨特特性","examples":[{"en":"Talc has unique characteristics that help with olive oil extraction.","zh":"滑石具有幫助橄欖油提取的獨特特性。"},{"en":"Unique characteristics are special qualities that make something different from others.","zh":"獨特特性是令某物有別於其他東西的特殊品質。"},{"en":"A good school may have unique characteristics such as small classes and strong mentoring.","zh":"好學校可能有小班教學和強大導師制度等獨特特性。"},{"en":"Talc’s unique characteristics allow it to absorb emulsifiers and remain chemically inert.","zh":"滑石的獨特特性使它能吸收乳化劑並保持化學惰性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes special features that create usefulness.","zh":"這個短語描述創造用途的特殊特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"boost the amount of oil","meaning":"提高出油量","examples":[{"en":"Talc can boost the amount of oil extracted from olives.","zh":"滑石可以提高從橄欖中提取的出油量。"},{"en":"To boost the amount of oil means to increase how much oil is produced or collected.","zh":"提高出油量，是指增加產生或收集到的油量。"},{"en":"Better machinery can boost the amount of juice extracted from fruit.","zh":"更好的機器可以提高從水果中榨出的果汁量。"},{"en":"If talc helps oil droplets separate, processors can recover more oil.","zh":"如果滑石幫助油滴分離，加工商就能回收更多油。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing output.","zh":"這個短語描述增加產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"extract from crushed olives","meaning":"從壓碎的橄欖中提取","examples":[{"en":"Processors extract oil from crushed olives.","zh":"加工商從壓碎的橄欖中提取油。"},{"en":"To extract from crushed olives means to remove oil from olives after they have been broken into a paste.","zh":"從壓碎的橄欖中提取，是指橄欖被壓成糊狀後從中取出油。"},{"en":"A juice maker extracts liquid from crushed grapes.","zh":"果汁製造商從壓碎的葡萄中提取液體。"},{"en":"Crushing helps release the liquid inside the fruit.","zh":"壓碎有助釋出水果內部液體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes removing a useful substance from crushed plant material.","zh":"這個短語描述從壓碎植物材料中取出有用物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……所說","examples":[{"en":"According to Patrick Delord, talc is especially useful for difficult olives.","zh":"根據 Patrick Delord 所說，滑石對難加工的橄欖特別有用。"},{"en":"According to means as stated by a person or source.","zh":"根據某人或某來源所說，是指按照該人或來源陳述的內容。"},{"en":"According to the school notice, the exam will begin at 9 a.m.","zh":"根據學校通告，考試將於上午九時開始。"},{"en":"This phrase tells readers where the information comes from.","zh":"這個短語告訴讀者資訊來自哪裡。"},{"en":"It is useful when reporting expert opinion.","zh":"它適合用來轉述專家意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"especially useful for","meaning":"對……特別有用","examples":[{"en":"Talc is especially useful for treating difficult olives.","zh":"滑石對處理難加工的橄欖特別有用。"},{"en":"Especially useful for something means particularly helpful in that situation.","zh":"對某事特別有用，是指在該情況中特別有幫助。"},{"en":"Flashcards are especially useful for memorising vocabulary.","zh":"抽認卡對記憶詞彙特別有用。"},{"en":"A tool is especially useful when it solves a problem that other methods handle poorly.","zh":"當一種工具能解決其他方法處理不好的問題，它就特別有用。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a strong practical benefit.","zh":"這個短語突出強烈實際好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"treating difficult olives","meaning":"處理難加工的橄欖","examples":[{"en":"Talc is useful for treating difficult olives.","zh":"滑石有助處理難加工的橄欖。"},{"en":"Treating difficult olives means processing olives that do not release oil easily.","zh":"處理難加工的橄欖，是指加工不容易釋出油分的橄欖。"},{"en":"A factory may need special methods for treating difficult olives at the end of the season.","zh":"工廠可能在季尾需要特殊方法處理難加工的橄欖。"},{"en":"Talc helps because it improves the separation of oil droplets.","zh":"滑石有幫助，因為它改善油滴分離。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to handling olives that are hard to process.","zh":"這個短語指處理難以加工的橄欖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"difficult olives","meaning":"難加工的橄欖","examples":[{"en":"Difficult olives do not easily yield their full oil content.","zh":"難加工的橄欖不容易釋出全部油分。"},{"en":"Difficult olives are olives that are hard to process because they do not release oil well.","zh":"難加工的橄欖，是因不容易出油而難以加工的橄欖。"},{"en":"Olives with too much water or fine solid matter may become difficult olives.","zh":"含水量太高或含有太多細小固體物的橄欖可能成為難加工橄欖。"},{"en":"Difficult olives reduce yield unless processors use a method to improve separation.","zh":"除非加工商使用改善分離的方法，難加工橄欖會降低出油率。"},{"en":"This phrase describes olives that resist normal oil extraction.","zh":"這個短語描述抗拒正常榨油過程的橄欖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"harvested","meaning":"採收；收成","examples":[{"en":"After the olives are harvested, they are taken to the processing plant.","zh":"橄欖採收後會被送到加工廠。"},{"en":"Harvested means picked or gathered from plants when ready.","zh":"採收，是指作物成熟時從植物上摘取或收集。"},{"en":"Apples are harvested in autumn when they are ripe.","zh":"蘋果在秋天成熟時採收。"},{"en":"After crops are harvested, they must often be transported and processed quickly.","zh":"作物採收後通常必須迅速運送和加工。"},{"en":"This word describes collecting crops from the field or tree.","zh":"這個詞描述從田地或樹上收集作物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"preferably","meaning":"最好；以……為佳","examples":[{"en":"Olives are preferably harvested early in the morning.","zh":"橄欖最好在清晨採收。"},{"en":"Preferably means ideally or if possible.","zh":"preferably 是指理想地或如可行的話。"},{"en":"Students should submit homework before Friday, preferably by Thursday evening.","zh":"學生應在星期五前交功課，最好在星期四晚上前完成。"},{"en":"This word suggests the best choice, though another option may still be possible.","zh":"這個詞表示最佳選擇，雖然其他選項仍可能可行。"},{"en":"It is used when giving a recommended condition.","zh":"它用於提出建議條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"early in the morning","meaning":"清晨","examples":[{"en":"Olives are preferably gathered early in the morning.","zh":"橄欖最好在清晨採摘。"},{"en":"Early in the morning means during the first part of the morning.","zh":"清晨，是指早上最初的時段。"},{"en":"A runner may train early in the morning before the streets become busy.","zh":"跑手可能在街道變得繁忙前於清晨訓練。"},{"en":"Crops may be collected early in the morning because the weather is cooler.","zh":"作物可能在清晨收集，因為天氣較涼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a time shortly after day begins.","zh":"這個短語描述一天開始後不久的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"gathered in the cool of the day","meaning":"在一天較涼爽的時段採摘","examples":[{"en":"Olives taste better if they are gathered in the cool of the day.","zh":"如果橄欖在一天較涼爽的時段採摘，味道會更好。"},{"en":"Gathered in the cool of the day means collected during the cooler part of the day.","zh":"在一天較涼爽的時段採摘，是指在氣溫較低的時候收集作物。"},{"en":"Farmers may pick vegetables in the cool of the day to keep them fresh.","zh":"農民可能在一天較涼爽的時段採摘蔬菜，以保持新鮮。"},{"en":"Cooler harvesting conditions can protect flavour and reduce heat damage.","zh":"較涼爽的採收條件可以保護味道並減少熱損害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collecting crops when temperatures are lower.","zh":"這個短語描述在較低溫時收集作物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"processing plant","meaning":"加工廠","examples":[{"en":"The olives are taken to the processing plant after harvest.","zh":"橄欖採收後會被送到加工廠。"},{"en":"A processing plant is a factory where raw materials are turned into finished or semi-finished products.","zh":"加工廠是把原材料變成成品或半成品的工廠。"},{"en":"Milk may be sent to a processing plant before it becomes cheese or yoghurt.","zh":"牛奶可能先被送到加工廠，然後製成芝士或乳酪。"},{"en":"Processing plants use machines to clean, crush, separate or package materials.","zh":"加工廠使用機器清洗、壓碎、分離或包裝材料。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an industrial site for processing raw goods.","zh":"這個短語指加工原材料的工業場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"crushed and stirred","meaning":"壓碎並攪拌","examples":[{"en":"The olives are crushed and stirred for 30 to 45 minutes.","zh":"橄欖會被壓碎並攪拌 30 至 45 分鐘。"},{"en":"Crushed and stirred means broken into smaller pieces and mixed by movement.","zh":"壓碎並攪拌，是指把某物弄成較小塊並透過移動混合。"},{"en":"A cook may crush and stir berries to make a sauce.","zh":"廚師可能壓碎並攪拌莓果來製作醬汁。"},{"en":"Crushing releases liquid, while stirring helps mix and separate useful parts.","zh":"壓碎會釋出液體，而攪拌有助混合並分離有用部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two steps in processing food material.","zh":"這個短語描述食品材料加工中的兩個步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"resulting paste","meaning":"所得的糊狀物","examples":[{"en":"The resulting paste was traditionally passed through an olive press.","zh":"所得的糊狀物傳統上會通過橄欖榨油機。"},{"en":"The resulting paste is the thick mixture produced after crushing and stirring.","zh":"所得的糊狀物，是壓碎和攪拌後產生的濃稠混合物。"},{"en":"After beans are crushed, the resulting paste can be used to make a sauce.","zh":"豆被壓碎後，所得的糊狀物可以用來製作醬汁。"},{"en":"This paste is important because it contains oil, water and solid matter together.","zh":"這種糊狀物很重要，因為它同時含有油、水和固體物質。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what is produced by the previous process.","zh":"這個短語描述上一個過程產生的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pass through","meaning":"通過；經過","examples":[{"en":"The olive paste was passed through an olive press.","zh":"橄欖糊通過橄欖榨油機。"},{"en":"To pass through a machine means to go into it and come out after being processed.","zh":"通過一部機器，是指進入其中，經處理後再出來。"},{"en":"Dough may pass through rollers to become thin sheets.","zh":"麵團可能通過滾輪，變成薄片。"},{"en":"Passing material through a machine can press, shape or separate it.","zh":"材料通過機器時，可以被壓榨、成形或分離。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement through a processing device.","zh":"這個短語描述材料經過加工裝置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"olive press","meaning":"橄欖榨油機","examples":[{"en":"In the old days, producers used an olive press.","zh":"以前，生產商使用橄欖榨油機。"},{"en":"An olive press is a machine used to press oil out of olives.","zh":"橄欖榨油機是用來從橄欖中壓出油的機器。"},{"en":"A traditional olive press may use pressure to squeeze oil from olive paste.","zh":"傳統橄欖榨油機可能使用壓力從橄欖糊中擠出油。"},{"en":"Olive presses were important before modern centrifuge systems became common.","zh":"在現代離心系統普及前，橄欖榨油機很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to equipment for extracting olive oil.","zh":"這個短語指提取橄欖油的設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"nowadays","meaning":"現時；如今","examples":[{"en":"Nowadays, processors usually add water and centrifuge the mixture.","zh":"如今，加工商通常加水並把混合物離心分離。"},{"en":"Nowadays means at the present time or in modern times.","zh":"現時，是指在目前或現代。"},{"en":"Nowadays, many students submit homework online.","zh":"現時，許多學生在網上提交功課。"},{"en":"This word contrasts current practice with older methods.","zh":"這個詞把當前做法與舊方法作對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing how things have changed.","zh":"它適合描述事情如何改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"centrifuge the mixture","meaning":"把混合物離心分離","examples":[{"en":"Processors add water and centrifuge the mixture.","zh":"加工商加水並把混合物離心分離。"},{"en":"To centrifuge the mixture means to spin it rapidly so its parts separate by density.","zh":"把混合物離心分離，是指快速旋轉它，使其各部分按密度分開。"},{"en":"A laboratory may centrifuge a blood sample to separate plasma from cells.","zh":"實驗室可能把血液樣本離心分離，以分開血漿和細胞。"},{"en":"Centrifuging helps separate oil, water and solid matter efficiently.","zh":"離心分離有助有效分開油、水和固體物質。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using spinning force to separate a mixture.","zh":"這個短語描述使用旋轉力分離混合物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"separate A from B","meaning":"把……與……分離","examples":[{"en":"Centrifuging separates the water and oil from the solid matter.","zh":"離心分離把水和油與固體物質分離。"},{"en":"To separate A from B means to divide two things so they are no longer mixed together.","zh":"把 A 與 B 分離，是指把兩者分開，使它們不再混在一起。"},{"en":"A filter can separate tea leaves from hot tea.","zh":"濾網可以把茶葉與熱茶分離。"},{"en":"Separation is important when only one part of a mixture is valuable.","zh":"當混合物中只有某一部分有價值，分離就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dividing mixed materials.","zh":"這個短語描述把混合材料分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"solid matter","meaning":"固體物質","examples":[{"en":"The process separates the liquid from the solid matter.","zh":"這個過程把液體與固體物質分離。"},{"en":"Solid matter is the non-liquid material in a mixture.","zh":"固體物質是混合物中非液體的材料。"},{"en":"After making juice, fruit skins and seeds may remain as solid matter.","zh":"榨汁後，果皮和果籽可能作為固體物質留下。"},{"en":"Removing solid matter can make the final liquid cleaner and easier to bottle.","zh":"移除固體物質可以令最終液體更清澈、更易裝瓶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the solid part left in a mixture.","zh":"這個短語描述混合物中留下的固體部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be allowed to settle","meaning":"被靜置沉澱","examples":[{"en":"The oil and water are allowed to settle after centrifuging.","zh":"離心後，油和水被靜置沉澱。"},{"en":"To be allowed to settle means to be left still so layers or particles can separate naturally.","zh":"被靜置沉澱，是指被放着不動，讓層次或粒子自然分開。"},{"en":"Muddy water may be allowed to settle before the clearer water is poured off.","zh":"泥水可能先被靜置沉澱，然後倒出較清的水。"},{"en":"Settling helps heavier or lighter materials form separate layers.","zh":"沉澱有助較重或較輕材料形成分層。"},{"en":"This phrase describes leaving a mixture undisturbed.","zh":"這個短語描述讓混合物不受打擾地放置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"olive oil layer","meaning":"橄欖油層","examples":[{"en":"The olive oil layer can be decanted off and bottled.","zh":"橄欖油層可以倒出分離並裝瓶。"},{"en":"The olive oil layer is the layer of oil that separates from water and solids.","zh":"橄欖油層是從水和固體中分離出來的油層。"},{"en":"In a jar of salad dressing, an oil layer may form above the vinegar.","zh":"在沙律醬瓶中，油層可能形成於醋上方。"},{"en":"Once the olive oil layer is clear, processors can remove it more easily.","zh":"一旦橄欖油層清楚，加工商就能更容易移走它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the separated oil portion.","zh":"這個短語描述分離出來的油部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"decanted off","meaning":"倒出分離","examples":[{"en":"The olive oil layer can be decanted off after settling.","zh":"沉澱後，橄欖油層可以倒出分離。"},{"en":"Decanted off means carefully poured away from another liquid or solid layer.","zh":"倒出分離，是指小心把液體從另一液體或固體層中倒出。"},{"en":"A cook may decant clear broth off after the solids sink to the bottom.","zh":"當固體沉到底部後，廚師可能把清湯倒出分離。"},{"en":"Decanting helps separate a useful liquid without disturbing the lower layer.","zh":"倒出分離有助取出有用液體，而不擾動下層。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful pouring to separate liquid.","zh":"這個短語描述透過小心倒出來分離液體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"bottled","meaning":"裝瓶","examples":[{"en":"The olive oil is decanted off and bottled.","zh":"橄欖油被倒出分離並裝瓶。"},{"en":"Bottled means put into bottles for storage, sale or transport.","zh":"裝瓶，是指放入瓶中以便儲存、銷售或運輸。"},{"en":"Fresh juice may be bottled before it is delivered to shops.","zh":"新鮮果汁可能先裝瓶，然後送到商店。"},{"en":"Bottling protects the product and makes it easier to sell.","zh":"裝瓶可以保護產品，也令它更容易出售。"},{"en":"This word describes placing a liquid into bottles.","zh":"這個詞描述把液體放入瓶中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"more reluctant than the norm to","meaning":"比一般情況更難……","examples":[{"en":"Difficult olives are more reluctant than the norm to release their oil.","zh":"難加工的橄欖比一般情況更難釋出油分。"},{"en":"More reluctant than the norm to do something means less willing or less able to do it than usual.","zh":"比一般情況更難做某事，是指比通常更不願意或更不能做到。"},{"en":"A printer may be more reluctant than the norm to feed thick paper.","zh":"打印機可能比一般情況更難送入厚紙。"},{"en":"In the passage, the olives resist releasing oil compared with ordinary olives.","zh":"在篇章中，這些橄欖相比普通橄欖更難釋出油分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unusual difficulty compared with the normal case.","zh":"這個短語描述與正常情況相比出現異常困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"yield up their full oil content","meaning":"釋出全部油分","examples":[{"en":"Difficult olives do not easily yield up their full oil content.","zh":"難加工的橄欖不容易釋出全部油分。"},{"en":"To yield up their full oil content means to release all the oil they contain.","zh":"釋出全部油分，是指把內含的所有油釋放出來。"},{"en":"Some seeds must be crushed hard before they yield up their oil content.","zh":"有些種子必須被用力壓碎，才會釋出其中油分。"},{"en":"If olives do not yield up enough oil, production becomes less efficient.","zh":"如果橄欖未能釋出足夠油分，生產效率就會降低。"},{"en":"This phrase describes releasing the full amount of oil inside.","zh":"這個短語描述釋放內部全部油量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be attributable to","meaning":"可歸因於……","examples":[{"en":"The problem may be attributable to the species of olive.","zh":"這個問題可能可歸因於橄欖品種。"},{"en":"To be attributable to something means to be caused by or linked to that factor.","zh":"可歸因於某事，是指由該因素造成或與之相關。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be attributable to lack of sleep.","zh":"學生疲倦可能可歸因於睡眠不足。"},{"en":"Identifying what a problem is attributable to helps people choose the right solution.","zh":"找出問題可歸因於甚麼，有助人們選擇正確解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a likely cause.","zh":"這個短語描述可能原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"particular species of","meaning":"特定……品種","examples":[{"en":"The oil yield may depend on the particular species of olive.","zh":"出油率可能取決於特定橄欖品種。"},{"en":"A particular species of something is one specific biological type within a larger group.","zh":"特定某物品種，是較大群體中的一種具體生物類型。"},{"en":"A gardener may choose a particular species of tomato because it grows well in hot weather.","zh":"園丁可能選擇特定番茄品種，因為它在炎熱天氣中生長良好。"},{"en":"Different species can have different water content, texture or productivity.","zh":"不同品種可以有不同含水量、質感或產量。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a specific biological variety.","zh":"這個短語指特定生物品種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"water content","meaning":"含水量","examples":[{"en":"The water content of olives can affect oil extraction.","zh":"橄欖的含水量可以影響榨油。"},{"en":"Water content is the amount of water inside a material or food.","zh":"含水量是材料或食物內部的水分多少。"},{"en":"Bread with high water content may feel softer and moister.","zh":"含水量高的麵包可能感覺更柔軟濕潤。"},{"en":"Too much or too little water content can change how a crop is processed.","zh":"含水量過高或過低都可以改變作物加工方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how much water something contains.","zh":"這個短語描述某物含有多少水分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the time of year","meaning":"一年中的時節","examples":[{"en":"The time of year can affect the olives’ water content.","zh":"一年中的時節可以影響橄欖的含水量。"},{"en":"The time of year means the season or period within the year.","zh":"一年中的時節，是指一年內的季節或時段。"},{"en":"The time of year affects what clothes students wear to school.","zh":"一年中的時節會影響學生上學穿甚麼衣服。"},{"en":"Crops may change during the year because weather and ripeness change.","zh":"作物在一年中會改變，因為天氣和成熟程度會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to seasonal timing.","zh":"這個短語指季節性時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at the beginning and end of the season","meaning":"在季初和季尾","examples":[{"en":"The water content may be too high or too low at the beginning and end of the season.","zh":"含水量在季初和季尾可能過高或過低。"},{"en":"At the beginning and end of the season means during the early and late parts of a production or harvest period.","zh":"在季初和季尾，是指生產或收成期的早段和後段。"},{"en":"Fruit prices may change at the beginning and end of the season.","zh":"水果價格可能在季初和季尾改變。"},{"en":"Crops are often less consistent during these periods.","zh":"作物在這些時段通常較不穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies two edge periods of a season.","zh":"這個短語指出季節兩端的時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"easy to recognise","meaning":"容易辨認","examples":[{"en":"Difficult olives are easy to recognise because they produce extra foam.","zh":"難加工的橄欖容易辨認，因為它們會產生額外泡沫。"},{"en":"Easy to recognise means simple to identify or notice.","zh":"容易辨認，是指容易識別或注意到。"},{"en":"A school uniform makes students easy to recognise during a field trip.","zh":"校服令學生在考察期間容易辨認。"},{"en":"Visible signs help workers quickly identify a problem.","zh":"明顯跡象幫助工人快速識別問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that can be identified without difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述不難識別的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"produce extra foam","meaning":"產生額外泡沫","examples":[{"en":"Difficult olives produce extra foam during the stirring process.","zh":"難加工的橄欖在攪拌過程中產生額外泡沫。"},{"en":"To produce extra foam means to create more bubbles or froth than usual.","zh":"產生額外泡沫，是指比平常製造更多氣泡或泡沫。"},{"en":"Soap produces extra foam if too much is added to a bucket of water.","zh":"如果在一桶水中加入太多肥皂，就會產生額外泡沫。"},{"en":"Extra foam may signal that something in the mixture is behaving differently.","zh":"額外泡沫可能顯示混合物中某些東西有不同反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unusually high froth formation.","zh":"這個短語描述異常多泡沫形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"during the stirring process","meaning":"在攪拌過程中","examples":[{"en":"The olives may produce extra foam during the stirring process.","zh":"橄欖在攪拌過程中可能產生額外泡沫。"},{"en":"During the stirring process means while the mixture is being mixed or moved around.","zh":"在攪拌過程中，是指混合物正在被攪拌或移動時。"},{"en":"A cake mixture may become smoother during the stirring process.","zh":"蛋糕混合物在攪拌過程中可能變得更順滑。"},{"en":"Changes that appear during stirring can show how ingredients are interacting.","zh":"攪拌期間出現的變化可以顯示成分如何互相作用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the stage when a mixture is being stirred.","zh":"這個短語指混合物被攪拌的階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a consequence of","meaning":"……的結果","examples":[{"en":"The foam is a consequence of an excess of fine solid.","zh":"泡沫是過量細小固體顆粒的結果。"},{"en":"A consequence of something is a result caused by it.","zh":"某事的結果，是由它造成的後果。"},{"en":"Late buses may be a consequence of heavy traffic.","zh":"巴士遲到可能是交通擠塞的結果。"},{"en":"Identifying the consequence helps explain why the problem appears.","zh":"找出結果有助解釋問題為何出現。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a result to its cause.","zh":"這個短語把結果與原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"an excess of","meaning":"過量的……","examples":[{"en":"The foam is caused by an excess of fine solid.","zh":"泡沫由過量的細小固體顆粒造成。"},{"en":"An excess of something means too much of it.","zh":"過量的某物，是指該物太多。"},{"en":"An excess of sugar can make a drink unpleasantly sweet.","zh":"過量的糖會令飲品甜得令人不舒服。"},{"en":"Too much of one substance can change how a mixture behaves.","zh":"某一物質太多可以改變混合物的表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an amount greater than is useful or normal.","zh":"這個短語描述超出有用或正常程度的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"fine solid","meaning":"細小固體顆粒","examples":[{"en":"A fine solid in the olives acts as a natural emulsifier.","zh":"橄欖中的細小固體顆粒充當天然乳化劑。"},{"en":"A fine solid is a very small solid particle in a mixture.","zh":"細小固體顆粒是混合物中的非常小的固體粒子。"},{"en":"Flour is a fine solid that can float in the air when poured quickly.","zh":"麵粉是一種細小固體顆粒，快速倒出時可以在空氣中飄浮。"},{"en":"Fine solids can affect texture, foaming and separation.","zh":"細小固體顆粒可以影響質感、起泡和分離。"},{"en":"This phrase describes tiny solid particles rather than large pieces.","zh":"這個短語描述微小固體粒子，而不是大塊物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"act as a natural emulsifier","meaning":"充當天然乳化劑","examples":[{"en":"The fine solid acts as a natural emulsifier.","zh":"細小固體顆粒充當天然乳化劑。"},{"en":"To act as a natural emulsifier means to help oil and water stay mixed naturally.","zh":"充當天然乳化劑，是指自然地幫助油和水保持混合。"},{"en":"Egg yolk can act as a natural emulsifier in mayonnaise.","zh":"蛋黃可以在蛋黃醬中充當天然乳化劑。"},{"en":"If an emulsifier traps oil in water, it becomes harder to separate the oil.","zh":"如果乳化劑把油困在水中，油就更難分離。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a substance performing the role of an emulsifier.","zh":"這個短語描述某物發揮乳化劑的作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"natural emulsifier","meaning":"天然乳化劑","examples":[{"en":"A natural emulsifier can trap oil in the water.","zh":"天然乳化劑可以把油困在水中。"},{"en":"A natural emulsifier is a substance from nature that helps oil and water mix.","zh":"天然乳化劑是來自自然、幫助油和水混合的物質。"},{"en":"Mustard can act as a natural emulsifier in salad dressing.","zh":"芥末可以在沙律醬中充當天然乳化劑。"},{"en":"Natural emulsifiers can be helpful in cooking but problematic in oil extraction.","zh":"天然乳化劑在烹飪中可以有用，但在榨油中可能造成問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a natural substance that stabilises a mixture.","zh":"這個短語描述穩定混合物的天然物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"emulsion","meaning":"乳狀液；乳化液","examples":[{"en":"The oil in this emulsion is lost when the water is disposed of.","zh":"當水被棄置時，這種乳狀液中的油會流失。"},{"en":"An emulsion is a mixture in which tiny droplets of one liquid are held inside another liquid.","zh":"乳狀液是一種混合物，其中一種液體的小液滴被困在另一種液體中。"},{"en":"Mayonnaise is an emulsion of oil and water-based ingredients.","zh":"蛋黃醬是油和水性成分形成的乳化液。"},{"en":"If oil remains trapped in an emulsion, processors may lose part of their product.","zh":"如果油被困在乳狀液中，加工商可能失去部分產品。"},{"en":"This word describes a mixed liquid system that resists separation.","zh":"這個詞描述不易分離的混合液體系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"emulsified oil","meaning":"乳化油","examples":[{"en":"Emulsified oil may take some time to biodegrade.","zh":"乳化油可能需要一段時間才能生物降解。"},{"en":"Emulsified oil is oil dispersed in water as tiny droplets.","zh":"乳化油是以微小油滴形式分散在水中的油。"},{"en":"Dishwashing liquid can turn cooking oil into emulsified oil in dirty water.","zh":"洗潔精可以把煮食油變成污水中的乳化油。"},{"en":"Emulsified oil can be harder to remove and may create environmental problems.","zh":"乳化油可能較難移除，並可能造成環境問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes oil trapped in an emulsion.","zh":"這個短語描述被困在乳化液中的油。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be disposed of directly into","meaning":"被直接棄置到……","examples":[{"en":"Waste water may be disposed of directly into local fields.","zh":"廢水可能被直接棄置到本地田地。"},{"en":"To be disposed of directly into somewhere means to be thrown away or released there without further treatment.","zh":"被直接棄置到某處，是指沒有進一步處理就被丟棄或排放到那裡。"},{"en":"Factory liquid should not be disposed of directly into rivers.","zh":"工廠液體不應被直接棄置到河流中。"},{"en":"Direct disposal can harm the environment if the waste contains pollutants.","zh":"如果廢物含污染物，直接棄置可能傷害環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes waste being released straight into a place.","zh":"這個短語描述廢物直接排放到某地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"waste water","meaning":"廢水","examples":[{"en":"The waste water may contain emulsified oil.","zh":"廢水可能含有乳化油。"},{"en":"Waste water is used water that is no longer clean and must be treated or disposed of.","zh":"廢水是已使用、不再清潔並需要處理或棄置的水。"},{"en":"A factory may produce waste water during washing or processing.","zh":"工廠在清洗或加工期間可能產生廢水。"},{"en":"If waste water contains oil, it can affect soil, rivers or local ecosystems.","zh":"如果廢水含油，可能影響土壤、河流或本地生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to dirty water left after use.","zh":"這個短語指使用後留下的污水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"local fields","meaning":"本地田地","examples":[{"en":"Some smaller operations dispose of waste water into local fields.","zh":"有些小型加工場把廢水棄置到本地田地。"},{"en":"Local fields are nearby areas of farmland or open land.","zh":"本地田地是附近的農田或空地。"},{"en":"Farmers may spread compost on local fields to improve the soil.","zh":"農民可能把堆肥撒在本地田地，以改善土壤。"},{"en":"Waste released into local fields can affect crops and surrounding land.","zh":"排放到本地田地的廢物可能影響作物和周圍土地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fields in the nearby area.","zh":"這個短語描述附近地區的田地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"smaller processing operations","meaning":"小型加工場","examples":[{"en":"Smaller processing operations may dispose of waste water directly into fields.","zh":"小型加工場可能把廢水直接棄置到田地。"},{"en":"Smaller processing operations are small-scale factories or businesses that process raw materials.","zh":"小型加工場是小規模處理原材料的工廠或企業。"},{"en":"A family-run olive press may be a smaller processing operation.","zh":"家庭經營的橄欖榨油場可能是小型加工場。"},{"en":"Small operations may lack expensive waste-treatment systems.","zh":"小型加工場可能缺乏昂貴的廢水處理系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes smaller businesses involved in processing.","zh":"這個短語描述從事加工的小型企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"biodegrade","meaning":"生物降解","examples":[{"en":"Emulsified oil may take some time to biodegrade.","zh":"乳化油可能需要一段時間才能生物降解。"},{"en":"To biodegrade means to break down naturally through the action of living organisms.","zh":"生物降解，是指透過生物作用自然分解。"},{"en":"Food waste can biodegrade in a compost bin.","zh":"食物廢料可以在堆肥箱中生物降解。"},{"en":"If a substance cannot biodegrade quickly, it may remain in the environment longer.","zh":"如果一種物質不能快速生物降解，它可能在環境中停留更久。"},{"en":"This word describes natural breakdown by biological processes.","zh":"這個詞描述透過生物過程自然分解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"harmful to the environment","meaning":"對環境有害","examples":[{"en":"Emulsified oil can be harmful to the environment.","zh":"乳化油可能對環境有害。"},{"en":"Harmful to the environment means damaging to land, water, air, plants or animals.","zh":"對環境有害，是指損害土地、水、空氣、植物或動物。"},{"en":"Pouring oil into drains can be harmful to the environment.","zh":"把油倒入排水渠可能對環境有害。"},{"en":"Waste becomes an environmental concern when it affects ecosystems or natural resources.","zh":"當廢物影響生態系統或自然資源，它就成為環境問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes environmental damage or risk.","zh":"這個短語描述環境損害或風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"between a half and 2 per cent","meaning":"介乎0.5%至2%","examples":[{"en":"Processors add between a half and 2 per cent of talc by weight.","zh":"加工商按重量加入介乎 0.5% 至 2% 的滑石。"},{"en":"Between a half and 2 per cent means within the range from 0.5 per cent to 2 per cent.","zh":"介乎 0.5% 至 2%，是指在百分之零點五到百分之二的範圍內。"},{"en":"A recipe may use between a half and 2 per cent salt by weight.","zh":"食譜可能按重量使用介乎 0.5% 至 2% 的鹽。"},{"en":"Small percentages can still have important effects in processing.","zh":"小百分比在加工中仍可以有重要效果。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a precise percentage range.","zh":"這個短語給出精確百分比範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"by weight","meaning":"按重量計","examples":[{"en":"The amount of talc is measured by weight.","zh":"滑石用量按重量計。"},{"en":"By weight means measured according to mass rather than volume or number.","zh":"按重量計，是指根據質量而不是體積或數量來量度。"},{"en":"Flour in a bakery is often measured by weight for accuracy.","zh":"麵包店中的麵粉通常按重量計，以求準確。"},{"en":"Measuring by weight helps factories add consistent amounts of ingredients.","zh":"按重量量度幫助工廠加入一致份量的成分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a method of measurement.","zh":"這個短語描述一種量度方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"absorb the natural emulsifier","meaning":"吸收天然乳化劑","examples":[{"en":"Talc absorbs the natural emulsifier in the olives.","zh":"滑石吸收橄欖中的天然乳化劑。"},{"en":"To absorb the natural emulsifier means to take in the substance that keeps oil and water mixed.","zh":"吸收天然乳化劑，是指吸收使油和水保持混合的物質。"},{"en":"A paper towel absorbs spilled water from a desk.","zh":"紙巾會吸收桌上的水。"},{"en":"By absorbing the emulsifier, talc helps oil droplets separate more easily.","zh":"透過吸收乳化劑，滑石幫助油滴更容易分離。"},{"en":"This phrase describes talc taking in a substance that causes emulsification.","zh":"這個短語描述滑石吸收造成乳化的物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"flat, platy structure","meaning":"扁平片狀結構","examples":[{"en":"Talc’s flat, platy structure helps increase the size of oil droplets.","zh":"滑石的扁平片狀結構有助增加油滴大小。"},{"en":"A flat, platy structure means a shape made of thin, flat layers or plates.","zh":"扁平片狀結構，是由薄而平的層片或片狀物組成的形態。"},{"en":"Some minerals have a flat, platy structure that makes them feel smooth.","zh":"有些礦物有扁平片狀結構，因此觸感順滑。"},{"en":"This structure can affect how particles interact with oil and water.","zh":"這種結構可以影響粒子如何與油和水互動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical shape of talc particles.","zh":"這個短語描述滑石粒子的物理形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"oil droplets","meaning":"油滴","examples":[{"en":"Talc helps increase the size of the oil droplets.","zh":"滑石有助增加油滴大小。"},{"en":"Oil droplets are tiny drops of oil within another liquid or mixture.","zh":"油滴是在另一種液體或混合物中的細小油珠。"},{"en":"Salad dressing may contain small oil droplets mixed with vinegar.","zh":"沙律醬可能含有與醋混合的小油滴。"},{"en":"Larger oil droplets are easier to separate from water.","zh":"較大的油滴更容易與水分離。"},{"en":"This phrase describes small units of oil dispersed in a mixture.","zh":"這個短語描述分散在混合物中的小油單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"liberated during stirring","meaning":"在攪拌期間釋出","examples":[{"en":"Oil droplets are liberated during stirring.","zh":"油滴在攪拌期間釋出。"},{"en":"Liberated during stirring means released while the mixture is being stirred.","zh":"在攪拌期間釋出，是指混合物被攪拌時被釋放出來。"},{"en":"Juice may be liberated from crushed fruit during stirring.","zh":"果汁可能在攪拌壓碎水果期間釋出。"},{"en":"Stirring can free substances trapped inside plant material.","zh":"攪拌可以釋放困在植物材料內的物質。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something being released during mixing.","zh":"這個短語描述某物在混合期間被釋放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"improve the yield","meaning":"提高產量；提高出油率","examples":[{"en":"Larger oil droplets improve the yield of olive oil.","zh":"較大的油滴提高橄欖油的出油率。"},{"en":"To improve the yield means to increase the amount produced or collected.","zh":"提高產量，是指增加生產或收集到的數量。"},{"en":"Better irrigation can improve the yield of a rice field.","zh":"更好的灌溉可以提高稻田產量。"},{"en":"If processors recover more oil from the same olives, the yield improves.","zh":"如果加工商從同一批橄欖中回收更多油，出油率就會提高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing production efficiency.","zh":"這個短語描述提高生產效率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"chemically inert","meaning":"化學惰性","examples":[{"en":"Talc is chemically inert and does not change the oil.","zh":"滑石具有化學惰性，不會改變油。"},{"en":"Chemically inert means not likely to react chemically with other substances.","zh":"化學惰性，是指不太可能與其他物質產生化學反應。"},{"en":"Glass is chemically inert enough to store many drinks safely.","zh":"玻璃具有足夠化學惰性，可以安全儲存許多飲品。"},{"en":"Inert materials are useful because they do not affect colour, taste or composition.","zh":"惰性材料有用，因為它們不影響顏色、味道或成分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes chemical stability and non-reactivity.","zh":"這個短語描述化學穩定和不易反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"affect the colour, taste, appearance or composition","meaning":"影響顏色、味道、外觀或成分","examples":[{"en":"Talc does not affect the colour, taste, appearance or composition of the oil.","zh":"滑石不會影響油的顏色、味道、外觀或成分。"},{"en":"To affect the colour, taste, appearance or composition means to change how a product looks, tastes or is made up.","zh":"影響顏色、味道、外觀或成分，是指改變產品看起來、吃起來或組成上的特質。"},{"en":"A food additive may be rejected if it affects the taste or appearance of a drink.","zh":"如果食品添加劑影響飲品味道或外觀，它可能會被拒用。"},{"en":"A processing aid is safer commercially when it does not change the final product.","zh":"當加工助劑不改變最終產品，商業上就更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes possible changes to product quality.","zh":"這個短語描述產品質素可能出現的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"resulting olive oil","meaning":"所得橄欖油","examples":[{"en":"Talc does not change the resulting olive oil.","zh":"滑石不會改變所得橄欖油。"},{"en":"Resulting olive oil is the olive oil produced at the end of the process.","zh":"所得橄欖油是加工過程最後產生的橄欖油。"},{"en":"A processor checks the resulting olive oil for taste and clarity before bottling.","zh":"加工商在裝瓶前會檢查所得橄欖油的味道和清澈度。"},{"en":"If talc improves extraction without changing the resulting oil, it is useful as a processing aid.","zh":"如果滑石能改善提取而不改變所得油，它就是有用的加工助劑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the final oil obtained after processing.","zh":"這個短語描述加工後取得的最終油。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"olive oil processing","meaning":"橄欖油加工","examples":[{"en":"The use of talc in olive oil processing is long established.","zh":"滑石在橄欖油加工中的使用早已確立。"},{"en":"Olive oil processing is the work of turning olives into olive oil.","zh":"橄欖油加工是把橄欖變成橄欖油的工作。"},{"en":"Olive oil processing includes crushing, stirring, separating, settling and bottling.","zh":"橄欖油加工包括壓碎、攪拌、分離、沉澱和裝瓶。"},{"en":"Efficient processing helps producers recover more oil from the same olives.","zh":"有效率加工幫助生產商從同一批橄欖中回收更多油。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the production process for olive oil.","zh":"這個短語描述橄欖油的生產過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"long established","meaning":"早已確立","examples":[{"en":"The use of talc in olive oil processing is long established.","zh":"滑石在橄欖油加工中的使用早已確立。"},{"en":"Long established means used, known or accepted for a long time.","zh":"早已確立，是指已使用、已知或已被接受很長時間。"},{"en":"The school’s morning assembly tradition is long established.","zh":"學校早會傳統早已確立。"},{"en":"A long-established method is less likely to be experimental or new.","zh":"早已確立的方法較不像實驗性或新方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something with a long history.","zh":"這個短語描述有悠久歷史的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"new applications","meaning":"新用途；新應用","examples":[{"en":"Luzenac is constantly seeking new applications for talc.","zh":"Luzenac 不斷尋找滑石的新用途。"},{"en":"New applications are new uses for a material, idea or technology.","zh":"新用途是材料、想法或科技的新使用方式。"},{"en":"A company may seek new applications for recycled plastic in furniture and clothing.","zh":"公司可能為再生塑膠在家具和服裝中尋找新用途。"},{"en":"Finding new applications can open new markets and increase product value.","zh":"找到新應用可以開拓新市場並提高產品價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fresh practical uses.","zh":"這個短語描述新的實際用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"constantly being sought","meaning":"不斷被尋求","examples":[{"en":"New applications in food and agriculture are constantly being sought.","zh":"食品和農業中的新應用正不斷被尋求。"},{"en":"Constantly being sought means continuously being looked for.","zh":"不斷被尋求，是指持續被尋找。"},{"en":"New teaching methods are constantly being sought by schools that want better results.","zh":"想取得更好成績的學校不斷尋求新教學方法。"},{"en":"Continuous searching shows that a company believes more opportunities exist.","zh":"持續尋找顯示公司相信還有更多機會存在。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an ongoing search.","zh":"這個短語描述持續搜尋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"promising new market","meaning":"有前景的新市場","examples":[{"en":"Fruit crop protection is a promising new market for talc.","zh":"水果作物保護是滑石有前景的新市場。"},{"en":"A promising new market is a new business area that seems likely to succeed.","zh":"有前景的新市場，是看來可能成功的新商業領域。"},{"en":"Electric school buses may be a promising new market for battery companies.","zh":"電動校巴可能是電池公司有前景的新市場。"},{"en":"A market is promising when there is a clear problem and a product that can solve it.","zh":"當有清楚問題和能解決問題的產品，市場就有前景。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a new commercial opportunity with potential.","zh":"這個短語描述具有潛力的新商業機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"fruit crop protection","meaning":"水果作物保護","examples":[{"en":"Fruit crop protection is being pioneered in the United States.","zh":"水果作物保護正在美國率先試行。"},{"en":"Fruit crop protection means methods used to prevent damage to fruit grown by farmers.","zh":"水果作物保護，是防止農民種植的水果受損的方法。"},{"en":"Farmers may use nets, sprays or shade to improve fruit crop protection.","zh":"農民可能使用網、噴劑或遮蔭來改善水果作物保護。"},{"en":"Protection matters because damaged fruit may be rejected by buyers.","zh":"保護很重要，因為受損水果可能被買家拒收。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protecting fruit before harvest.","zh":"這個短語描述在收成前保護水果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"being pioneered","meaning":"正在開創；率先試行","examples":[{"en":"The use of talc for fruit crop protection is being pioneered in the US.","zh":"使用滑石保護水果作物正在美國率先試行。"},{"en":"Being pioneered means being developed or tried for the first time by early users.","zh":"正在開創，是指由早期使用者首次發展或試用。"},{"en":"A new teaching app may be pioneered by a few experimental schools.","zh":"新教學應用程式可能由幾間實驗學校率先試行。"},{"en":"When a method is being pioneered, it is still relatively new and being tested.","zh":"當一種方法正在開創，它仍相對較新並處於測試中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes early innovation.","zh":"這個短語描述早期創新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"just like people","meaning":"就像人一樣","examples":[{"en":"Just like people, fruit can get sunburned.","zh":"就像人一樣，水果也會曬傷。"},{"en":"Just like people means in the same way as humans.","zh":"就像人一樣，是指以與人類相同的方式。"},{"en":"Just like people, pets can feel stress when their routine changes.","zh":"就像人一樣，寵物在日常規律改變時也會感到壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase makes an unfamiliar idea easier by comparing it with human experience.","zh":"這個短語透過與人類經驗比較，使陌生想法更易理解。"},{"en":"It shows similarity between humans and another subject.","zh":"它顯示人類與另一對象之間的相似性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"get sunburned","meaning":"曬傷","examples":[{"en":"Fruit can get sunburned in very sunny regions.","zh":"水果在陽光猛烈的地區會曬傷。"},{"en":"To get sunburned means to be damaged by strong sunlight.","zh":"曬傷，是指被強烈陽光傷害。"},{"en":"A person can get sunburned after spending hours at the beach without protection.","zh":"一個人如果沒有保護地在沙灘待數小時，可能會曬傷。"},{"en":"Fruit can also suffer damage when surface temperature becomes too high.","zh":"當表面溫度過高，水果也會受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harm caused by exposure to strong sun.","zh":"這個短語描述暴露於強烈陽光造成的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"very sunny regions","meaning":"陽光猛烈的地區","examples":[{"en":"Fruit crops are at risk in very sunny regions.","zh":"水果作物在陽光猛烈的地區面臨風險。"},{"en":"Very sunny regions are areas that receive strong sunlight for long periods.","zh":"陽光猛烈的地區，是長時間接受強烈陽光的地方。"},{"en":"Farms in very sunny regions may need irrigation, shade or crop protection.","zh":"位於陽光猛烈地區的農場可能需要灌溉、遮蔭或作物保護。"},{"en":"Strong sunlight can increase surface temperature and damage fruit.","zh":"強烈陽光可以提高表面溫度並損害水果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes places with intense sun exposure.","zh":"這個短語描述日照強烈的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"up to 45 per cent of","meaning":"高達45%的……","examples":[{"en":"Up to 45 per cent of a typical crop can be affected.","zh":"高達 45% 的一般作物可能受影響。"},{"en":"Up to 45 per cent of something means as much as 45 per cent, but not necessarily always that much.","zh":"高達某物的 45%，是指最多可達 45%，但不一定每次都那麼多。"},{"en":"Up to 30 per cent of a class may join a school trip if places are limited.","zh":"如果名額有限，高達全班 30% 的學生可能參加學校旅行。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the maximum possible scale of a problem.","zh":"這個短語顯示問題可能達到的最大規模。"},{"en":"It warns that the damage can be serious.","zh":"它提醒損害可能很嚴重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"typical crop","meaning":"一般收成；典型作物","examples":[{"en":"Heat stress can affect a typical crop.","zh":"熱壓力可以影響一般作物。"},{"en":"A typical crop is an ordinary or average crop of that kind.","zh":"一般作物是該種類中普通或平均的作物。"},{"en":"A typical apple crop may include thousands of pieces of fruit on one farm.","zh":"一般蘋果收成可能包括一個農場上的數千個水果。"},{"en":"If a typical crop suffers sunburn, the financial loss can be large.","zh":"如果一般收成受到曬傷，財政損失可能很大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a normal harvest or group of plants.","zh":"這個短語描述正常收成或一組植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be affected by","meaning":"受……影響","examples":[{"en":"Fruit can be affected by heat stress and sunburn.","zh":"水果可能受熱壓力和曬傷影響。"},{"en":"To be affected by something means to be changed, damaged or influenced by it.","zh":"受某事影響，是指被它改變、損害或影響。"},{"en":"Students may be affected by noise when studying in a crowded room.","zh":"學生在擁擠房間中溫習時可能受噪音影響。"},{"en":"Crops affected by heat may become lower in quality or harder to sell.","zh":"受高溫影響的作物可能質素下降或較難出售。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being influenced by an outside factor.","zh":"這個短語描述受到外部因素影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"heat stress","meaning":"熱壓力","examples":[{"en":"Heat stress can damage fruit crops.","zh":"熱壓力可以損害水果作物。"},{"en":"Heat stress is harm or strain caused by high temperature.","zh":"熱壓力是由高溫造成的傷害或負擔。"},{"en":"Outdoor workers may suffer heat stress during a very hot afternoon.","zh":"戶外工人在炎熱下午可能受到熱壓力。"},{"en":"In fruit, heat stress can raise surface temperature and cause visible damage.","zh":"對水果而言，熱壓力可以提高表面溫度並造成可見損害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pressure or damage caused by heat.","zh":"這個短語描述由熱造成的壓力或損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"it’s not so much…as…","meaning":"與其說是……不如說是……","examples":[{"en":"It is not so much ultraviolet rays as high surface temperature that harms the crop.","zh":"傷害作物的與其說是紫外線，不如說是高表面溫度。"},{"en":"It’s not so much A as B means B is the real or more important cause, not A.","zh":"與其說是 A 不如說是 B，是指 B 才是真正或更重要的原因，而不是 A。"},{"en":"The problem is not so much the homework as the lack of time to finish it.","zh":"問題與其說是功課，不如說是沒有足夠時間完成。"},{"en":"This structure helps correct a misunderstanding about the main cause.","zh":"這個結構幫助修正對主要原因的誤解。"},{"en":"It clearly contrasts a less important factor with the real focus.","zh":"它清楚對比較不重要因素與真正焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"ultraviolet rays","meaning":"紫外線","examples":[{"en":"Ultraviolet rays are not the main cause of damage to the fruit.","zh":"紫外線不是水果受損的主要原因。"},{"en":"Ultraviolet rays are invisible rays from the sun that can damage skin and other surfaces.","zh":"紫外線是來自太陽、不可見且能損害皮膚和其他表面的光線。"},{"en":"Sunscreen helps protect people from ultraviolet rays.","zh":"防曬霜幫助人們抵禦紫外線。"},{"en":"In the passage, fruit damage is linked more to heat than to ultraviolet rays.","zh":"在篇章中，水果受損更多與熱有關，而不是紫外線。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a type of solar radiation.","zh":"這個短語指一種太陽輻射。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"high surface temperature","meaning":"高表面溫度","examples":[{"en":"High surface temperature can harm the crop.","zh":"高表面溫度可以傷害作物。"},{"en":"High surface temperature means the outside of something becomes very hot.","zh":"高表面溫度，是指某物外部變得很熱。"},{"en":"A car parked under the sun can have a high surface temperature.","zh":"停在太陽下的汽車可能有高表面溫度。"},{"en":"Fruit with a high surface temperature may suffer sunburn-like damage.","zh":"表面溫度高的水果可能出現類似曬傷的損害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes heat on the outer surface of an object.","zh":"這個短語描述物件外層表面的熱度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the sun’s rays","meaning":"太陽光線","examples":[{"en":"The sun’s rays create high surface temperatures.","zh":"太陽光線造成高表面溫度。"},{"en":"The sun’s rays are the light and heat energy coming from the sun.","zh":"太陽光線是來自太陽的光和熱能。"},{"en":"The sun’s rays can warm a classroom through a window.","zh":"太陽光線可以透過窗戶令課室變暖。"},{"en":"Strong rays can raise the temperature of fruit, soil and buildings.","zh":"強烈光線可以提高水果、土壤和建築物的溫度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sunlight as beams of energy.","zh":"這個短語把陽光描述為能量光束。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"to combat this","meaning":"為應對這個問題","examples":[{"en":"To combat this, farmers normally use chemicals or mist.","zh":"為應對這個問題，農民通常使用化學品或幼霧。"},{"en":"To combat this means to deal with or fight against the problem just mentioned.","zh":"為應對這個問題，是指處理或對抗剛提到的問題。"},{"en":"To combat exam stress, students may plan revision earlier.","zh":"為應對考試壓力，學生可能更早規劃溫習。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a method used to reduce or prevent a problem.","zh":"這個短語引入用來減少或防止問題的方法。"},{"en":"It is often used before a solution.","zh":"它常用於解決方法之前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"spray a continuous fine canopy of mist","meaning":"噴灑連續的幼霧覆蓋層","examples":[{"en":"Farmers may spray a continuous fine canopy of mist above the fruit trees.","zh":"農民可能在果樹上方噴灑連續的幼霧覆蓋層。"},{"en":"To spray a continuous fine canopy of mist means to release a steady layer of tiny water droplets.","zh":"噴灑連續的幼霧覆蓋層，是指釋放穩定一層微小水滴。"},{"en":"A greenhouse may spray a fine mist to cool plants on a hot day.","zh":"溫室可能在炎熱日子噴灑幼霧來冷卻植物。"},{"en":"Mist can lower temperature, but it may use a lot of water.","zh":"幼霧可以降溫，但可能使用大量水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating a cooling layer above crops.","zh":"這個短語描述在作物上方形成冷卻水霧層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"fruit trees or bushes","meaning":"果樹或果叢","examples":[{"en":"The mist is sprayed above the fruit trees or bushes.","zh":"幼霧被噴灑在果樹或果叢上方。"},{"en":"Fruit trees or bushes are plants that produce fruit, either on trees or smaller bush-like plants.","zh":"果樹或果叢是會結果的植物，包括樹木和較小的灌木狀植物。"},{"en":"Apples grow on fruit trees, while blueberries grow on bushes.","zh":"蘋果長在果樹上，而藍莓長在果叢上。"},{"en":"Farmers protect fruit trees or bushes because damaged fruit reduces income.","zh":"農民保護果樹或果叢，因為受損水果會減少收入。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to fruit-producing plants of different sizes.","zh":"這個短語指不同大小的結果植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"The trouble is,…","meaning":"問題是……","examples":[{"en":"The trouble is, this method uses a lot of water.","zh":"問題是，這種方法使用大量水。"},{"en":"The trouble is means the problem is.","zh":"The trouble is 意思是「問題是」。"},{"en":"The trouble is, the cheaper printer uses very expensive ink.","zh":"問題是，較便宜的打印機使用非常昂貴的墨水。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a drawback after a possible solution has been mentioned.","zh":"這個短語在提到可能解決方法後，引入其缺點。"},{"en":"It helps show why another solution may be needed.","zh":"它幫助顯示為何可能需要另一個解決方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a precious commodity","meaning":"珍貴資源","examples":[{"en":"Water is a precious commodity in hot, sunny areas.","zh":"水在炎熱陽光猛烈的地區是珍貴資源。"},{"en":"A precious commodity is a valuable resource that people need and should not waste.","zh":"珍貴資源是人們需要並不應浪費的有價值資源。"},{"en":"During a drought, clean water becomes a precious commodity.","zh":"在乾旱期間，清潔食水會成為珍貴資源。"},{"en":"If water is precious, farmers need methods that use less of it.","zh":"如果水很珍貴，農民就需要用水較少的方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something valuable and limited.","zh":"這個短語描述有價值且有限的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"waterlogged","meaning":"積水；水浸","examples":[{"en":"The ground can quickly become waterlogged.","zh":"地面可以很快變得積水。"},{"en":"Waterlogged means filled with too much water.","zh":"積水，是指充滿過多水分。"},{"en":"A football field may become waterlogged after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，足球場可能變得水浸。"},{"en":"Waterlogged soil can damage plants because roots may not get enough air.","zh":"積水土壤可能損害植物，因為根部可能得不到足夠空氣。"},{"en":"This word describes land or material soaked with excessive water.","zh":"這個詞描述土地或材料被過量水浸透。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"coat the fruit with","meaning":"用……覆蓋水果表面","examples":[{"en":"The idea was to coat the fruit with talc.","zh":"這個想法是用滑石覆蓋水果表面。"},{"en":"To coat the fruit with something means to cover its surface with a layer of that material.","zh":"用某物覆蓋水果表面，是指在水果外層加上一層該材料。"},{"en":"A cook may coat apple slices with lemon juice to stop browning.","zh":"廚師可能用檸檬汁覆蓋蘋果片表面，以防變啡。"},{"en":"Coating fruit can protect its surface from heat, air or damage.","zh":"覆蓋水果表面可以保護它免受熱、空氣或損害影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes covering fruit with a protective layer.","zh":"這個短語描述用保護層覆蓋水果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"protect it from the sun","meaning":"保護它免受陽光傷害","examples":[{"en":"Talc can protect the fruit from the sun.","zh":"滑石可以保護水果免受陽光傷害。"},{"en":"To protect it from the sun means to prevent sunlight or heat from damaging it.","zh":"保護它免受陽光傷害，是指防止陽光或熱損害它。"},{"en":"A hat can protect a child from the sun during a sports day.","zh":"帽子可以在運動會期間保護孩子免受陽光傷害。"},{"en":"Fruit needs protection when strong sunlight raises its surface temperature.","zh":"當強烈陽光提高水果表面溫度，水果就需要保護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing damage from sunlight.","zh":"這個短語描述減少陽光造成的損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"technical challenges","meaning":"技術挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Several technical challenges first had to be overcome.","zh":"幾項技術挑戰首先必須被克服。"},{"en":"Technical challenges are practical or engineering problems that must be solved.","zh":"技術挑戰是必須解決的實際或工程問題。"},{"en":"Building a school website may involve technical challenges such as login security.","zh":"建立學校網站可能涉及登入安全等技術挑戰。"},{"en":"A product cannot work commercially until its technical challenges are solved.","zh":"產品在技術挑戰解決前不能商業化運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficulties related to design, science or engineering.","zh":"這個短語描述與設計、科學或工程相關的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"had to be overcome","meaning":"必須被克服","examples":[{"en":"Several technical challenges had to be overcome.","zh":"幾項技術挑戰必須被克服。"},{"en":"Had to be overcome means needed to be solved before progress was possible.","zh":"必須被克服，是指必須被解決，才可能有進展。"},{"en":"Before the school concert, sound problems had to be overcome.","zh":"學校音樂會前，音響問題必須被克服。"},{"en":"Problems that block success must be overcome before a plan can work.","zh":"阻礙成功的問題必須被克服，計劃才能行得通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes necessary problem-solving.","zh":"這個短語描述必要的解難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"hydrophobic","meaning":"疏水的","examples":[{"en":"Talc is very hydrophobic and does not like water.","zh":"滑石非常疏水，不喜歡水。"},{"en":"Hydrophobic means tending not to mix with or absorb water.","zh":"疏水的，是指傾向不與水混合或不吸收水。"},{"en":"Oil is hydrophobic because it separates from water.","zh":"油是疏水的，因為它會與水分離。"},{"en":"A hydrophobic powder is difficult to spray unless it is specially prepared.","zh":"疏水粉末若沒有特別處理，就難以噴灑。"},{"en":"This word describes a material that resists water.","zh":"這個詞描述抗拒水的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"viable product","meaning":"可行產品","examples":[{"en":"The company needed a viable product that farmers could spray.","zh":"公司需要一種農民可以噴灑的可行產品。"},{"en":"A viable product is a product that can actually work in practice and be used successfully.","zh":"可行產品是實際上能運作並成功使用的產品。"},{"en":"A school app is viable only if students can use it easily on their phones.","zh":"學校應用程式只有在學生能用手機輕鬆使用時才可行。"},{"en":"A product may be scientifically interesting but not viable if users cannot apply it.","zh":"一種產品可以在科學上有趣，但如果用戶不能應用，就不可行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical and usable product.","zh":"這個短語描述實用且可使用的產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"wettable powder","meaning":"可濕性粉劑","examples":[{"en":"The product needed to be a wettable powder.","zh":"產品需要是可濕性粉劑。"},{"en":"A wettable powder is a powder that can mix with water to form a sprayable suspension.","zh":"可濕性粉劑是能與水混合形成可噴灑懸浮液的粉末。"},{"en":"Some garden pesticides are sold as wettable powders that farmers mix with water.","zh":"有些園藝農藥以可濕性粉劑出售，讓農民與水混合。"},{"en":"A wettable powder is useful when dry particles need to be sprayed evenly.","zh":"當乾粉粒子需要被均勻噴灑，可濕性粉劑很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a powder designed to mix with water.","zh":"這個短語描述設計成可與水混合的粉末。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"go readily into suspension","meaning":"容易形成懸浮液","examples":[{"en":"The powder had to go readily into suspension.","zh":"粉末必須容易形成懸浮液。"},{"en":"To go readily into suspension means to mix easily into liquid and remain evenly spread.","zh":"容易形成懸浮液，是指容易混入液體並保持均勻分散。"},{"en":"A medicine powder must go readily into suspension if patients need to drink it mixed with water.","zh":"如果病人需要把藥粉與水混合飲用，藥粉必須容易形成懸浮液。"},{"en":"If powder does not suspend well, it may sink, clump or block the sprayer.","zh":"如果粉末不能良好懸浮，它可能沉底、結塊或堵塞噴霧器。"},{"en":"This phrase describes easy mixing into a sprayable liquid.","zh":"這個短語描述容易混入可噴灑液體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"suspension","meaning":"懸浮液","examples":[{"en":"The powder had to stay in suspension so it could be sprayed.","zh":"粉末必須保持在懸浮液中，才能被噴灑。"},{"en":"A suspension is a mixture in which solid particles are spread through a liquid but not dissolved.","zh":"懸浮液是固體粒子分散在液體中但沒有溶解的混合物。"},{"en":"Muddy water is a simple suspension of soil particles in water.","zh":"泥水是泥土粒子在水中的簡單懸浮液。"},{"en":"A spray product needs a stable suspension so the active material reaches the crop evenly.","zh":"噴灑產品需要穩定懸浮液，活性材料才能均勻到達作物。"},{"en":"This word describes solid particles floating in liquid.","zh":"這個詞描述固體粒子漂浮在液體中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be sprayed onto","meaning":"被噴灑到……上","examples":[{"en":"The product could be sprayed onto the fruit.","zh":"產品可以被噴灑到水果上。"},{"en":"To be sprayed onto something means to be applied as tiny droplets onto its surface.","zh":"被噴灑到某物上，是指以微小液滴形式施加到其表面。"},{"en":"Water may be sprayed onto classroom plants on a hot day.","zh":"在炎熱日子，水可能被噴灑到課室植物上。"},{"en":"Spraying allows a thin, even layer to cover a large surface.","zh":"噴灑能讓薄而均勻的一層覆蓋大表面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes applying liquid or suspension by spray.","zh":"這個短語描述透過噴霧施加液體或懸浮液。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"surface tension","meaning":"表面張力","examples":[{"en":"The powder had to break the surface tension of the cutin.","zh":"粉末必須打破角質素的表面張力。"},{"en":"Surface tension is the force that makes the surface of a liquid or coating resist being spread.","zh":"表面張力是使液體或塗層表面抗拒被鋪展的力量。"},{"en":"Water droplets stay round on a waxy leaf because of surface tension.","zh":"水滴因表面張力而在蠟質葉面上保持圓形。"},{"en":"Breaking surface tension helps a spray spread evenly over a surface.","zh":"打破表面張力有助噴劑均勻鋪展在表面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical force at a surface.","zh":"這個短語描述表面上的物理力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"break the surface tension of","meaning":"打破……的表面張力","examples":[{"en":"The product had to break the surface tension of the cutin.","zh":"產品必須打破角質素的表面張力。"},{"en":"To break the surface tension of something means to reduce the force that prevents liquid from spreading on it.","zh":"打破某物的表面張力，是指降低阻止液體在其表面鋪展的力量。"},{"en":"Soap breaks the surface tension of water so it spreads more easily.","zh":"肥皂會打破水的表面張力，使它更容易鋪展。"},{"en":"If the spray cannot break surface tension, it may form drops instead of coating the fruit.","zh":"如果噴劑不能打破表面張力，它可能形成水滴而不是覆蓋水果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a surface easier to wet.","zh":"這個短語描述使表面更容易被潤濕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"cutin","meaning":"角質素","examples":[{"en":"Cutin is the natural waxy, waterproof layer on fruit.","zh":"角質素是水果上的天然蠟質防水層。"},{"en":"Cutin is a protective substance on the surface of plants and fruit.","zh":"角質素是植物和水果表面的保護物質。"},{"en":"The shiny surface of an apple is partly protected by cutin.","zh":"蘋果發亮的表面部分由角質素保護。"},{"en":"Because cutin is waxy and waterproof, sprays may not spread on it easily.","zh":"因為角質素帶蠟質且防水，噴劑未必容易在其上鋪展。"},{"en":"This word refers to a natural protective coating on plant surfaces.","zh":"這個詞指植物表面的天然保護層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"natural waxy, waterproof layer","meaning":"天然蠟質防水層","examples":[{"en":"Cutin is the natural waxy, waterproof layer on the fruit.","zh":"角質素是水果上的天然蠟質防水層。"},{"en":"A natural waxy, waterproof layer is a plant surface coating that repels water.","zh":"天然蠟質防水層是植物表面排斥水分的覆蓋層。"},{"en":"Leaves often have a natural waxy, waterproof layer that makes raindrops roll off.","zh":"葉子通常有天然蠟質防水層，使雨滴滾落。"},{"en":"Such a layer protects plants but can make spraying more difficult.","zh":"這種層可以保護植物，但也可能令噴灑較困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a protective water-resistant coating.","zh":"這個短語描述具防水性的保護塗層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"wash off easily","meaning":"容易洗掉","examples":[{"en":"The talc had to wash off easily when the fruit was harvested.","zh":"水果採收時，滑石必須容易洗掉。"},{"en":"To wash off easily means to be removed easily with water.","zh":"容易洗掉，是指能用水輕易移除。"},{"en":"A washable marker should wash off easily from a child’s hands.","zh":"可水洗筆應該容易從孩子手上洗掉。"},{"en":"If talc remains on fruit after harvest, consumers may reject it.","zh":"如果滑石在收成後仍留在水果上，消費者可能拒絕購買。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being easy to remove by washing.","zh":"這個短語描述容易透過清洗移除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"No one’s going to want…","meaning":"沒有人會想要……","examples":[{"en":"No one’s going to want an apple that is covered in talc.","zh":"沒有人會想要一個覆蓋着滑石粉的蘋果。"},{"en":"No one’s going to want means people will not be willing to accept or buy it.","zh":"沒有人會想要，是指人們不願意接受或購買它。"},{"en":"No one’s going to want a notebook with half the pages missing.","zh":"沒有人會想要一本少了一半頁數的筆記簿。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a practical concern about customer acceptance.","zh":"這個短語表達對顧客接受度的實際憂慮。"},{"en":"It is often used to explain why a product must meet expectations.","zh":"它常用來解釋產品為何必須符合期望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"covered in talc","meaning":"覆蓋着滑石粉","examples":[{"en":"No one wants an apple that is covered in talc.","zh":"沒有人想要覆蓋着滑石粉的蘋果。"},{"en":"Covered in talc means having talc powder all over the surface.","zh":"覆蓋着滑石粉，是指表面到處都有滑石粉。"},{"en":"A table covered in flour looks messy after baking practice.","zh":"烘焙練習後，覆蓋着麵粉的桌子看起來很凌亂。"},{"en":"Fruit covered in visible powder may look unattractive to buyers.","zh":"覆蓋着可見粉末的水果可能對買家不吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a surface coated with talc powder.","zh":"這個短語描述表面被滑石粉覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"initial trials","meaning":"初步試驗","examples":[{"en":"Initial trials in Washington showed promising results.","zh":"華盛頓州的初步試驗顯示出有前景的結果。"},{"en":"Initial trials are early tests used to see whether an idea works.","zh":"初步試驗是早期測試，用來了解想法是否有效。"},{"en":"A school may run initial trials of a new timetable before using it for everyone.","zh":"學校可能先進行新時間表的初步試驗，再讓所有人使用。"},{"en":"Positive initial trials can encourage wider use or further testing.","zh":"正面的初步試驗可以鼓勵更廣泛使用或進一步測試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first stage of testing.","zh":"這個短語描述測試的第一階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the state of Washington","meaning":"華盛頓州","examples":[{"en":"The product was tested in the state of Washington.","zh":"產品在華盛頓州進行測試。"},{"en":"The state of Washington is a state in the northwestern United States.","zh":"華盛頓州是美國西北部的一個州。"},{"en":"Apple growers in the state of Washington may face strong sunlight in some growing areas.","zh":"華盛頓州的蘋果種植者在某些種植地區可能面對強烈陽光。"},{"en":"Testing in one state helps companies see how a product performs under local conditions.","zh":"在某一州測試有助公司了解產品在當地條件下的表現。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific U.S. state, not the capital city Washington, D.C.","zh":"這個短語指美國一個州，而不是首都華盛頓特區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"Granny Smith apples","meaning":"Granny Smith 青蘋果","examples":[{"en":"The product was sprayed onto Granny Smith apples.","zh":"該產品被噴灑到 Granny Smith 青蘋果上。"},{"en":"Granny Smith apples are green apples known for their firm texture and tart taste.","zh":"Granny Smith 青蘋果是一種以結實質感和酸味著稱的綠蘋果。"},{"en":"A supermarket may sell Granny Smith apples for eating or baking.","zh":"超級市場可能銷售 Granny Smith 青蘋果供食用或烘焙。"},{"en":"Because their surface is exposed to sunlight, these apples can be tested for sunburn protection.","zh":"由於其表面會暴露在陽光下，這些蘋果可以用來測試防曬傷保護。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific apple variety.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定蘋果品種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"reduce surface temperature","meaning":"降低表面溫度","examples":[{"en":"The product reduced the apples’ surface temperature.","zh":"該產品降低了蘋果的表面溫度。"},{"en":"To reduce surface temperature means to make the outside of something less hot.","zh":"降低表面溫度，是指令某物外部沒有那麼熱。"},{"en":"Shade cloth can reduce surface temperature on playground equipment.","zh":"遮陽布可以降低遊樂場設備的表面溫度。"},{"en":"Lower surface temperature can reduce heat damage and sunburn.","zh":"較低表面溫度可以減少熱損害和曬傷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cooling the outer layer of an object.","zh":"這個短語描述冷卻物件外層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"lower the incidence of","meaning":"降低……的發生率","examples":[{"en":"The product lowered the incidence of sunburn.","zh":"該產品降低了曬傷的發生率。"},{"en":"To lower the incidence of something means to reduce how often it happens.","zh":"降低某事的發生率，是指減少它發生的頻率。"},{"en":"Handwashing can lower the incidence of illness in a classroom.","zh":"洗手可以降低課室中疾病的發生率。"},{"en":"If fewer apples are sunburned after spraying, the incidence has been lowered.","zh":"如果噴灑後較少蘋果曬傷，發生率就被降低。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing the rate of a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述減少問題出現的比率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"incidence of sunburn","meaning":"曬傷發生率","examples":[{"en":"The incidence of sunburn fell after the product was used.","zh":"使用該產品後，曬傷發生率下降。"},{"en":"Incidence of sunburn means how often sunburn occurs in a crop or group.","zh":"曬傷發生率，是作物或群體中曬傷出現的頻率。"},{"en":"A school may track the incidence of flu during winter.","zh":"學校可能在冬季追蹤流感發生率。"},{"en":"A lower incidence of sunburn means fewer fruits are damaged by sun exposure.","zh":"較低曬傷發生率表示較少水果因日曬受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the frequency of sunburn cases.","zh":"這個短語描述曬傷個案出現的頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"by up to 60 per cent","meaning":"高達60%","examples":[{"en":"The product lowered the incidence of sunburn by up to 60 per cent.","zh":"該產品把曬傷發生率降低高達 60%。"},{"en":"By up to 60 per cent means by as much as 60 per cent at most.","zh":"高達 60%，是指最多可達 60%。"},{"en":"A new bus route may reduce travel time by up to 30 per cent.","zh":"新巴士路線可能把交通時間減少高達 30%。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the maximum improvement reported.","zh":"這個短語給出所報告的最大改善幅度。"},{"en":"It does not mean the result is exactly 60 per cent every time.","zh":"它不表示每次結果都剛好是 60%。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be known as","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"The new product is known as Invelop Maximum SPF.","zh":"這款新產品被稱為 Invelop Maximum SPF。"},{"en":"To be known as something means to be called by that name.","zh":"被稱為某物，是指以該名稱稱呼。"},{"en":"The school hall is known as the Assembly Hall.","zh":"學校禮堂被稱為 Assembly Hall。"},{"en":"A product name helps customers recognise and ask for it.","zh":"產品名稱幫助顧客辨認並要求購買它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the name of a person, place or product.","zh":"這個短語引入人物、地方或產品的名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"in its second commercial year","meaning":"推出市場後第二個銷售年","examples":[{"en":"The product is in its second commercial year on the US market.","zh":"該產品正在美國市場推出後第二個銷售年。"},{"en":"In its second commercial year means in the second year after being sold commercially.","zh":"推出市場後第二個銷售年，是指商業銷售開始後的第二年。"},{"en":"A new textbook may be in its second commercial year after its first year of sales.","zh":"一本新教科書在銷售第一年後，可能進入第二個商業銷售年。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the product has moved beyond testing and entered the market.","zh":"這個短語顯示產品已超越測試階段並進入市場。"},{"en":"It refers to the product’s stage in commercial sales.","zh":"它指產品在商業銷售中的階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"on the US market","meaning":"在美國市場","examples":[{"en":"The product is now on the US market.","zh":"該產品現在在美國市場銷售。"},{"en":"On the US market means available for sale in the United States.","zh":"在美國市場，是指在美國可供銷售。"},{"en":"A new phone may be on the US market before it reaches Europe.","zh":"新手機可能先在美國市場推出，再到歐洲。"},{"en":"Being on a market means customers in that place can buy the product.","zh":"在某市場銷售，表示該地顧客可以購買產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where a product is sold.","zh":"這個短語描述產品在哪裡出售。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"primary target","meaning":"主要目標對象","examples":[{"en":"Apple growers are the primary target for the product.","zh":"蘋果種植者是該產品的主要目標對象。"},{"en":"A primary target is the main group a product or campaign is aimed at.","zh":"主要目標對象，是產品或宣傳主要針對的群體。"},{"en":"Parents may be the primary target of a school safety notice.","zh":"家長可能是學校安全通告的主要目標對象。"},{"en":"Companies identify a primary target so they can focus marketing and sales efforts.","zh":"公司識別主要目標對象，以集中市場推廣和銷售工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main intended audience or customer group.","zh":"這個短語描述主要預期受眾或客戶群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"apple growers","meaning":"蘋果種植者","examples":[{"en":"Apple growers are the primary target for Invelop Maximum SPF.","zh":"蘋果種植者是 Invelop Maximum SPF 的主要目標對象。"},{"en":"Apple growers are farmers or businesses that grow apples.","zh":"蘋果種植者是種植蘋果的農民或企業。"},{"en":"Apple growers may protect fruit from insects, disease and sunburn.","zh":"蘋果種植者可能保護水果免受昆蟲、疾病和曬傷影響。"},{"en":"If sunburn damages apples, growers may lose income at harvest time.","zh":"如果曬傷損害蘋果，種植者在收成時可能失去收入。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people who cultivate apple crops.","zh":"這個短語指栽培蘋果作物的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"represent another sector","meaning":"代表另一個板塊","examples":[{"en":"Grape growers represent another sector with long-term potential.","zh":"葡萄種植者代表另一個具有長遠潛力的板塊。"},{"en":"To represent another sector means to form or stand for another part of the market.","zh":"代表另一個板塊，是指形成或代表市場中的另一部分。"},{"en":"Adult learners may represent another sector for an English education business.","zh":"成人學習者可能代表英語教育業務的另一個板塊。"},{"en":"A new sector matters when it may become a future customer group.","zh":"當新板塊可能成為未來客戶群，它就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes another market segment.","zh":"這個短語描述另一個市場部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"grape growers","meaning":"葡萄種植者","examples":[{"en":"Grape growers may become another important target group.","zh":"葡萄種植者可能成為另一個重要目標群體。"},{"en":"Grape growers are farmers or businesses that grow grapes.","zh":"葡萄種植者是種植葡萄的農民或企業。"},{"en":"Grape growers may sell their fruit to supermarkets or wine producers.","zh":"葡萄種植者可能把水果賣給超級市場或葡萄酒生產商。"},{"en":"If grapes suffer sunburn, growers may need crop protection products.","zh":"如果葡萄受到曬傷，種植者可能需要作物保護產品。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people who cultivate grape crops.","zh":"這個短語指栽培葡萄作物的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"long-term potential","meaning":"長遠潛力","examples":[{"en":"Grape growers represent a sector with long-term potential.","zh":"葡萄種植者代表一個具有長遠潛力的板塊。"},{"en":"Long-term potential means a strong possibility of future growth or success over time.","zh":"長遠潛力，是指長期而言有很大機會增長或成功。"},{"en":"A small online course may have long-term potential if students keep recommending it.","zh":"如果學生不斷推薦，小型網上課程可能有長遠潛力。"},{"en":"Companies invest in markets with long-term potential because they may grow later.","zh":"公司投資有長遠潛力的市場，因為它們日後可能增長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes future promise rather than immediate results only.","zh":"這個短語描述未來前景，而不只是即時成果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be hopeful of","meaning":"對……抱有希望","examples":[{"en":"Hunter is hopeful of extending sales to overseas markets.","zh":"Hunter 對把銷售擴展至海外市場抱有希望。"},{"en":"To be hopeful of something means to believe it may happen successfully.","zh":"對某事抱有希望，是指相信它可能成功發生。"},{"en":"A student may be hopeful of improving their speaking after regular practice.","zh":"學生可能對透過定期練習改善口語抱有希望。"},{"en":"Hopefulness often comes from early positive results or clear opportunities.","zh":"希望通常來自早期正面結果或清楚機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cautious optimism.","zh":"這個短語描述謹慎樂觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"extend sales to","meaning":"把銷售擴展至……","examples":[{"en":"The company hopes to extend sales to overseas markets.","zh":"公司希望把銷售擴展至海外市場。"},{"en":"To extend sales to a market means to start selling or sell more in that market.","zh":"把銷售擴展至某市場，是指開始在該市場銷售或增加銷售。"},{"en":"A bakery may extend sales to nearby schools by offering lunch boxes.","zh":"麵包店可能透過提供午餐盒，把銷售擴展至附近學校。"},{"en":"Extending sales can increase revenue and spread a product to new customers.","zh":"擴展銷售可以增加收入，並把產品帶給新客戶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes expanding commercial reach.","zh":"這個短語描述擴大商業覆蓋範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"overseas markets","meaning":"海外市場","examples":[{"en":"The company hopes to sell the product in overseas markets.","zh":"公司希望在海外市場銷售該產品。"},{"en":"Overseas markets are foreign countries or regions where a company sells products.","zh":"海外市場是公司銷售產品的外國或外地市場。"},{"en":"A Hong Kong brand may enter overseas markets such as Singapore and Canada.","zh":"香港品牌可能進入新加坡和加拿大等海外市場。"},{"en":"Overseas markets can offer growth, but they may require new regulations and customer research.","zh":"海外市場可以帶來增長，但可能需要研究新規例和客戶。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to markets outside a company’s home country.","zh":"這個短語指公司本國以外的市場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"such as","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"The company hopes to sell in overseas markets such as Australia and southern Europe.","zh":"公司希望在澳洲和南歐等海外市場銷售。"},{"en":"Such as introduces examples of a larger group.","zh":"such as 用來引入較大群體中的例子。"},{"en":"Students need school supplies such as pens, notebooks and folders.","zh":"學生需要筆、筆記簿和文件夾等學校用品。"},{"en":"This phrase gives examples without listing every possible item.","zh":"這個短語給出例子，而不列出所有可能項目。"},{"en":"It helps make a general idea more concrete.","zh":"它幫助令一般想法更具體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"southern Europe","meaning":"南歐","examples":[{"en":"Southern Europe may become an overseas market for the product.","zh":"南歐可能成為該產品的海外市場。"},{"en":"Southern Europe refers to the southern part of Europe, including countries with warm climates.","zh":"南歐指歐洲南部，包括氣候溫暖的國家。"},{"en":"Fruit growers in southern Europe may face strong sunlight during summer.","zh":"南歐的水果種植者在夏季可能面對強烈陽光。"},{"en":"A sun-protection product for crops may be useful in warm southern regions.","zh":"作物防曬產品在溫暖南方地區可能有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a geographical market area.","zh":"這個短語描述一個地理市場區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"use the information in the passage","meaning":"運用文章資料","examples":[{"en":"Students use the information in the passage to complete the task.","zh":"學生運用文章資料完成任務。"},{"en":"To use the information in the passage means to base answers only on what the text says.","zh":"運用文章資料，是指只根據文本所說內容作答。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should use the information in the passage rather than outside knowledge.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應運用文章資料，而不是外部知識。"},{"en":"This prevents guessing and keeps answers evidence-based.","zh":"這可以防止猜測，並令答案以證據為本。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction about source use.","zh":"這個短語是關於資料來源使用的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"match each use of","meaning":"將……的每種用途配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match each use of talc powder with the correct application.","zh":"學生將滑石粉的每種用途與正確應用配對。"},{"en":"To match each use of something means to connect every use with the right description or category.","zh":"將某物的每種用途配對，是指把每個用途連接到正確描述或類別。"},{"en":"Students may match each use of a camera with science, security or entertainment.","zh":"學生可能把相機的每種用途與科學、安全或娛樂配對。"},{"en":"Matching requires careful reading because one material may have several uses.","zh":"配對需要仔細閱讀，因為一種材料可能有多種用途。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a classification task.","zh":"這個短語描述分類任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"correct application","meaning":"正確應用；正確用途","examples":[{"en":"Each use of talc powder should be matched with the correct application.","zh":"滑石粉的每種用途應與正確應用配對。"},{"en":"The correct application is the right practical use or purpose for something.","zh":"正確應用，是某物正確的實際用途或目的。"},{"en":"If talc prevents gum from sticking, the correct application is preventing stickiness.","zh":"如果滑石防止香口膠黏住，正確應用就是防止黏住。"},{"en":"Choosing the correct application shows that the student understands function, not just vocabulary.","zh":"選擇正確應用顯示學生理解功能，而不只是詞彙。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the right use of a material or method.","zh":"這個短語指材料或方法的正確用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"may use any letter more than once","meaning":"可以重複使用任何字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates may use any letter more than once in this type of task.","zh":"在這類題目中，考生可以重複使用任何字母。"},{"en":"May use any letter more than once means an answer option can be chosen repeatedly.","zh":"可以重複使用任何字母，是指答案選項可以被多次選用。"},{"en":"In a matching question, students may use the same letter for two different items if both match.","zh":"在配對題中，如果兩項都相符，學生可以為兩個不同項目使用同一字母。"},{"en":"This instruction prevents students from assuming every option is used only once.","zh":"這項指示防止學生以為每個選項只能使用一次。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in IELTS-style matching tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於 IELTS 式配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"prevent foaming","meaning":"防止起泡","examples":[{"en":"Talc can be used to prevent foaming during olive oil processing.","zh":"滑石可用於橄欖油加工期間防止起泡。"},{"en":"To prevent foaming means to stop too many bubbles or froth from forming.","zh":"防止起泡，是指阻止過多氣泡或泡沫形成。"},{"en":"A cook may lower the heat to prevent foaming in a pot of soup.","zh":"廚師可能調低火力，以防止一鍋湯起泡。"},{"en":"Preventing foam helps processors separate oil more efficiently.","zh":"防止泡沫有助加工商更有效分離油。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stopping unwanted froth.","zh":"這個短語描述阻止不需要的泡沫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"prevent stickiness","meaning":"防止黏住","examples":[{"en":"Talc can help prevent stickiness during chewing gum production.","zh":"滑石可以在香口膠生產過程中幫助防止黏住。"},{"en":"To prevent stickiness means to stop materials from sticking to each other or to machines.","zh":"防止黏住，是指阻止材料互相黏住或黏在機器上。"},{"en":"Flour can prevent stickiness when rolling dough.","zh":"擀麵團時，麵粉可以防止黏住。"},{"en":"Preventing stickiness keeps production smooth and reduces waste.","zh":"防止黏住可以令生產順暢並減少浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes avoiding unwanted adhesion.","zh":"這個短語描述避免不需要的黏附。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"boost production","meaning":"提高產量","examples":[{"en":"Talc can boost production in some food-processing contexts.","zh":"滑石可以在某些食品加工情況中提高產量。"},{"en":"To boost production means to increase the amount produced.","zh":"提高產量，是指增加生產數量。"},{"en":"A factory may boost production by using faster machines.","zh":"工廠可能透過使用更快機器來提高產量。"},{"en":"Talc boosts production when it helps processors extract more oil from the same olives.","zh":"當滑石幫助加工商從同一批橄欖中提取更多油，它就提高產量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing output.","zh":"這個短語描述增加產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"provide a base","meaning":"提供基底","examples":[{"en":"Talc can be used as a filler to provide a base.","zh":"滑石可被用作填充劑以提供基底。"},{"en":"To provide a base means to supply the basic material or foundation for a product.","zh":"提供基底，是指提供產品的基本材料或基礎。"},{"en":"Rice can provide a base for a simple lunch bowl.","zh":"米飯可以為簡單午餐碗提供基底。"},{"en":"In chewing gum, filler materials help create body and structure.","zh":"在香口膠中，填充材料有助創造份量和結構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving a product its underlying substance or support.","zh":"這個短語描述提供產品的底層物質或支撐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"prevent sunburn","meaning":"防止曬傷","examples":[{"en":"Talc can help prevent sunburn in fruit crops.","zh":"滑石可以幫助防止水果作物曬傷。"},{"en":"To prevent sunburn means to stop damage caused by strong sunlight and heat.","zh":"防止曬傷，是指阻止強烈陽光和熱造成的損害。"},{"en":"Sunscreen helps prevent sunburn on human skin.","zh":"防曬霜幫助防止人體皮膚曬傷。"},{"en":"A protective coating can prevent sunburn by lowering fruit surface temperature.","zh":"保護塗層可以透過降低水果表面溫度防止曬傷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stopping sun-related damage.","zh":"這個短語描述阻止陽光相關損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"increase the size of","meaning":"增加……的大小","examples":[{"en":"Talc helps increase the size of oil droplets.","zh":"滑石有助增加油滴的大小。"},{"en":"To increase the size of something means to make it larger.","zh":"增加某物的大小，是指令它變得更大。"},{"en":"A teacher may increase the size of text on a slide so students can read it easily.","zh":"老師可能增加投影片文字的大小，使學生容易閱讀。"},{"en":"Larger oil droplets are easier to separate, so increasing their size improves yield.","zh":"較大的油滴更容易分離，所以增加其大小能提高出油率。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making something bigger.","zh":"這個短語描述令某物變大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"complete the summary below","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary below using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"Complete the summary below means fill in missing words in the short text provided.","zh":"完成以下摘要，是指填上題目提供的短文中的缺失字詞。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete the summary by locating exact information in the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過在篇章中定位準確資料來完成摘要。"},{"en":"This task checks both understanding and careful word choice.","zh":"這項任務同時檢查理解和仔細選詞。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個詞","examples":[{"en":"The instruction asks students to use no more than two words.","zh":"指示要求學生使用不多於兩個詞。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must contain one or two words only.","zh":"不多於兩個詞，是指答案只能包含一個或兩個英文詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “olive press,” it follows the rule because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “olive press”，它符合規則，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing three words may be wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫三個詞也可能錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"from the Reading Passage","meaning":"來自閱讀文章","examples":[{"en":"The answers must come from the Reading Passage.","zh":"答案必須來自閱讀文章。"},{"en":"From the Reading Passage means taken directly from the text given in the reading task.","zh":"來自閱讀文章，是指直接取自閱讀題所給文本。"},{"en":"Students should choose words from the Reading Passage rather than inventing their own answers.","zh":"學生應從閱讀文章中選字，而不是自己創作答案。"},{"en":"This instruction keeps answers based on evidence in the text.","zh":"這項指示令答案以文本證據為本。"},{"en":"This phrase tells candidates where to find the answer wording.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生到哪裡找答案措辭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"has been around for","meaning":"已存在；已沿用……時間","examples":[{"en":"The use of talc in olive oil processing has been around for many years.","zh":"滑石在橄欖油加工中的使用已沿用多年。"},{"en":"Has been around for a period means has existed or been used for that length of time.","zh":"已存在某段時間，是指存在或被使用了那段時間。"},{"en":"The school library has been around for more than fifty years.","zh":"學校圖書館已存在超過五十年。"},{"en":"If a method has been around for many years, it is not a brand-new experiment.","zh":"如果一種方法已沿用多年，它就不是全新的實驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how long something has existed.","zh":"這個短語描述某事存在了多久。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be useful in dealing with","meaning":"對處理……有用","examples":[{"en":"Talc is useful in dealing with difficult olives.","zh":"滑石對處理難加工的橄欖有用。"},{"en":"To be useful in dealing with something means to help manage or solve that problem.","zh":"對處理某事有用，是指有助管理或解決該問題。"},{"en":"A checklist is useful in dealing with exam stress because it organises tasks.","zh":"清單對處理考試壓力有用，因為它能整理任務。"},{"en":"Talc helps deal with difficult olives by improving oil separation.","zh":"滑石透過改善油分離來幫助處理難加工橄欖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical usefulness in handling a challenge.","zh":"這個短語描述在應對挑戰時的實際用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"high content of","meaning":"高含量的……","examples":[{"en":"Difficult olives may contain a high content of solid matter.","zh":"難加工的橄欖可能含有高含量的固體物質。"},{"en":"High content of something means a large amount of that substance inside a material.","zh":"高含量的某物，是指材料中有大量該物質。"},{"en":"A drink with a high content of sugar may taste very sweet.","zh":"高糖含量的飲品可能味道很甜。"},{"en":"A high content of fine solids can affect foaming and oil separation.","zh":"高含量的細小固體可以影響起泡和油分離。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large proportion of a substance.","zh":"這個短語描述某物質比例較高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"traditional method of","meaning":"……的傳統方法","examples":[{"en":"The traditional method of oil extraction used an olive press.","zh":"榨油的傳統方法使用橄欖榨油機。"},{"en":"The traditional method of something is the older or customary way of doing it.","zh":"某事的傳統方法，是較舊或按慣例使用的做法。"},{"en":"The traditional method of learning times tables is repeated recitation.","zh":"學習乘數表的傳統方法是反覆背誦。"},{"en":"Traditional methods may be replaced when newer technology becomes more efficient.","zh":"當新科技更有效率，傳統方法可能被取代。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an established older way of doing a task.","zh":"這個短語描述一種早已確立的舊方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"oil extraction","meaning":"榨油；提油","examples":[{"en":"Talc can improve oil extraction from crushed olives.","zh":"滑石可以改善從壓碎橄欖中提油的過程。"},{"en":"Oil extraction is the process of removing oil from a plant, seed or fruit.","zh":"榨油是從植物、種子或水果中取出油的過程。"},{"en":"Factories use machines for oil extraction from sunflower seeds.","zh":"工廠使用機器從葵花籽中榨油。"},{"en":"Better extraction means more oil can be recovered from the same raw material.","zh":"更好的提油過程表示可以從同一原材料中回收更多油。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of obtaining oil.","zh":"這個短語描述取得油的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"smaller plants","meaning":"小型工廠；小型加工廠","examples":[{"en":"Some smaller plants may use older processing methods.","zh":"有些小型工廠可能使用較舊加工方法。"},{"en":"Smaller plants are smaller factories or processing facilities.","zh":"小型工廠是規模較小的工廠或加工設施。"},{"en":"A smaller plant may not have the money to buy the newest equipment.","zh":"小型工廠可能沒有資金購買最新設備。"},{"en":"Smaller plants may keep traditional methods because they are cheaper or familiar.","zh":"小型工廠可能保留傳統方法，因為它們較便宜或較熟悉。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to small industrial sites, not living plants.","zh":"這個短語指小型工業場所，而不是植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"directly disposed of","meaning":"被直接棄置","examples":[{"en":"Waste water may be directly disposed of into local fields.","zh":"廢水可能被直接棄置到本地田地。"},{"en":"Directly disposed of means thrown away or released without extra treatment or delay.","zh":"被直接棄置，是指沒有額外處理或延遲就被丟棄或排放。"},{"en":"Used cooking oil should not be directly disposed of into a sink.","zh":"用過的煮食油不應被直接倒入洗手盆。"},{"en":"Direct disposal can create environmental problems if waste contains harmful substances.","zh":"如果廢物含有有害物質，直接棄置可能造成環境問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes waste being removed in a direct way.","zh":"這個短語描述廢物以直接方式被處理掉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"cannot biodegrade quickly","meaning":"不能快速生物降解","examples":[{"en":"Emulsified oil cannot biodegrade quickly in some conditions.","zh":"乳化油在某些情況下不能快速生物降解。"},{"en":"Cannot biodegrade quickly means cannot break down naturally in a short time.","zh":"不能快速生物降解，是指不能在短時間內自然分解。"},{"en":"Some plastics cannot biodegrade quickly, so they remain in landfills for years.","zh":"有些塑膠不能快速生物降解，因此會在堆填區停留多年。"},{"en":"Slow biodegradation can make waste more harmful to the environment.","zh":"緩慢生物降解會令廢物對環境更有害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow natural breakdown.","zh":"這個短語描述自然分解速度慢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"increase the production","meaning":"增加產量","examples":[{"en":"Adding talc can increase the production of olive oil.","zh":"加入滑石可以增加橄欖油產量。"},{"en":"To increase the production of something means to make more of it.","zh":"增加某物產量，是指製造更多該物。"},{"en":"A factory may increase the production of masks during a health emergency.","zh":"工廠可能在健康危機期間增加口罩產量。"},{"en":"If a processing aid improves yield, production rises without needing more raw materials.","zh":"如果加工助劑改善出油率，產量就會在不需要更多原材料下上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes raising output.","zh":"這個短語描述提高產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"final two stages","meaning":"最後兩個階段","examples":[{"en":"The final two stages of the process involve lamination and packing.","zh":"這個過程的最後兩個階段涉及壓片和包裝。"},{"en":"Final two stages means the last two steps in a process.","zh":"最後兩個階段，是過程中的最後兩個步驟。"},{"en":"In essay writing, the final two stages may be proofreading and checking word count.","zh":"在文章寫作中，最後兩個階段可能是校對和檢查字數。"},{"en":"Knowing the final stages helps explain when a problem may occur.","zh":"了解最後階段有助解釋問題可能在何時出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the last pair of steps.","zh":"這個短語描述最後一組兩個步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"intend to target","meaning":"打算以……為目標","examples":[{"en":"The company intends to target another group of farmers.","zh":"公司打算以另一群農民為目標。"},{"en":"To intend to target a group means to plan to focus sales, marketing or support on that group.","zh":"打算以某群體為目標，是指計劃把銷售、市場推廣或支援集中在該群體上。"},{"en":"A language school may intend to target working adults with evening classes.","zh":"語言學校可能打算以在職成人為目標，提供夜間課程。"},{"en":"Companies target groups that are likely to need or buy their products.","zh":"公司會以可能需要或購買其產品的群體為目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a planned commercial focus.","zh":"這個短語描述有計劃的商業焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 30 - Talc Powder.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 31":[{"front":"communication style","meaning":"溝通風格","examples":[{"en":"A person’s communication style can affect how they respond to conflict.","zh":"一個人的溝通風格可以影響他如何回應衝突。"},{"en":"Communication style means the usual way a person speaks, listens, explains ideas, and reacts to others.","zh":"溝通風格指一個人說話、聆聽、解釋想法和回應別人的慣常方式。"},{"en":"A teacher with a warm communication style may make shy students feel safer asking questions.","zh":"溝通風格溫暖的老師，可能令害羞學生更安心提問。"},{"en":"If two colleagues have very different communication styles, they may misunderstand each other even when both are trying to help.","zh":"如果兩名同事的溝通風格非常不同，即使兩人都想幫忙，也可能互相誤解。"},{"en":"Understanding communication style helps people see behaviour as a pattern, not always as a personal attack.","zh":"理解溝通風格有助人把行為看成一種模式，而不總是視為個人攻擊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a mix of styles","meaning":"多種風格的組合","examples":[{"en":"Having a mix of styles on your team can help the team deal with different situations.","zh":"團隊中有多種風格的組合，可以幫助團隊處理不同情況。"},{"en":"A mix of styles means a group contains people with different ways of thinking, speaking, or working.","zh":"多種風格的組合指一個群體中有不同思考、說話或工作方式的人。"},{"en":"A project team may need a mix of styles: one person checks details while another motivates the group.","zh":"專案團隊可能需要多種風格的組合：有人檢查細節，有人推動團隊。"},{"en":"When a team has a mix of styles, it can handle both people’s feelings and the practical task.","zh":"當團隊有多種風格的組合，就能同時處理人的感受和實際任務。"},{"en":"Too much of one style may make a team unbalanced, but a mix of styles can make it stronger.","zh":"太多單一風格可能令團隊失衡，但多種風格的組合可以令團隊更強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"provide a positive force for","meaning":"為……提供正面力量","examples":[{"en":"A mix of communication styles can provide a positive force for resolving conflict.","zh":"多種溝通風格的組合可以為化解衝突提供正面力量。"},{"en":"To provide a positive force for something means to help it move in a good direction.","zh":"provide a positive force for something 指幫助某事朝好的方向發展。"},{"en":"Clear rules can provide a positive force for improving classroom behaviour.","zh":"清晰規則可以為改善課堂行為提供正面力量。"},{"en":"In a team, respectful discussion can provide a positive force for solving problems instead of blaming people.","zh":"在團隊中，尊重的討論可以為解決問題提供正面力量，而不是責怪別人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that actively supports a good result.","zh":"這個短語描述某事物主動支援好結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"resolving conflict","meaning":"化解衝突","examples":[{"en":"Understanding different styles is useful for resolving conflict.","zh":"理解不同風格對化解衝突很有用。"},{"en":"Resolving conflict means dealing with disagreement so that people can move forward more calmly.","zh":"化解衝突指處理分歧，讓人能更冷靜地繼續合作。"},{"en":"Two classmates may resolve conflict by explaining what hurt them and agreeing on clearer boundaries.","zh":"兩名同學可以透過解釋自己受傷之處，並同意更清晰界線來化解衝突。"},{"en":"If conflict is not resolved, small misunderstandings can grow into long-term resentment.","zh":"如果衝突沒有被化解，小誤會可以發展成長期怨氣。"},{"en":"Resolving conflict does not always mean everyone agrees; it means the problem is handled constructively.","zh":"化解衝突不一定代表人人同意；它代表問題以建設性方式處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as far back as","meaning":"早於……；遠至……","examples":[{"en":"As far back as Hippocrates’ time, people tried to understand personality differences.","zh":"早於希波克拉底時代，人們已嘗試理解性格差異。"},{"en":"As far back as means as early as a very distant time in the past.","zh":"as far back as 指早至很久以前的某個時期。"},{"en":"As far back as ancient China, people recorded medical knowledge and farming practices.","zh":"遠至古代中國，人們已記錄醫學知識和農耕做法。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an idea, habit, or problem has existed for a very long time.","zh":"這個短語顯示某個想法、習慣或問題已存在很長時間。"},{"en":"We use it to emphasise how old the history of something is.","zh":"我們用它來強調某事的歷史有多悠久。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Hippocrates’ time","meaning":"希波克拉底時代","examples":[{"en":"Ideas about temperament existed as far back as Hippocrates’ time.","zh":"關於氣質的想法早於希波克拉底時代已經存在。"},{"en":"Hippocrates’ time refers to the ancient Greek period associated with the physician Hippocrates.","zh":"Hippocrates’ time 指與古希臘醫師希波克拉底相關的古希臘時期。"},{"en":"In Hippocrates’ time, people explained health and personality very differently from modern scientists.","zh":"在希波克拉底時代，人們對健康和性格的解釋與現代科學家很不同。"},{"en":"Referring to Hippocrates’ time shows that the discussion has ancient roots.","zh":"提及希波克拉底時代顯示討論有古代根源。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when tracing an idea back to early medical history.","zh":"這個短語用於把某想法追溯到早期醫學史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"characterise someone according to","meaning":"根據……來描述某人","examples":[{"en":"Early thinkers tried to characterise people according to personality type.","zh":"早期思想家嘗試根據性格類型來描述人。"},{"en":"To characterise someone according to something means to describe them based on that feature or category.","zh":"characterise someone according to something 指根據某特徵或類別來描述某人。"},{"en":"A teacher should not characterise students according to one bad test result.","zh":"老師不應根據一次差的測驗成績來描述學生。"},{"en":"If people are characterised only by labels, their real complexity may be ignored.","zh":"如果人只被標籤描述，他們真正的複雜性可能被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase describes classifying or describing people using a chosen standard.","zh":"這個短語描述用某個標準來分類或描述人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"personality type","meaning":"性格類型","examples":[{"en":"People have long tried to understand others by personality type.","zh":"人們長久以來都嘗試透過性格類型理解別人。"},{"en":"A personality type is a category used to describe common patterns in how people think, feel, and behave.","zh":"personality type 指用來描述人如何思考、感受和行動的常見模式類別。"},{"en":"A quiet student may be wrongly placed into one personality type if teachers do not know them well.","zh":"如果老師不夠了解學生，安靜學生可能被錯誤歸入某一性格類型。"},{"en":"Personality types can help discussion, but they should not be used to limit people.","zh":"性格類型可以幫助討論，但不應用來限制人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a general pattern, not a complete identity.","zh":"這個短語描述一般模式，而不是完整身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"temperament","meaning":"氣質；性情","examples":[{"en":"Hippocrates believed that body fluids influenced a person’s temperament.","zh":"希波克拉底相信體液會影響一個人的氣質。"},{"en":"Temperament means a person’s natural emotional style, such as being calm, energetic, sensitive, or quick-tempered.","zh":"temperament 指一個人的自然情緒風格，例如冷靜、活躍、敏感或易怒。"},{"en":"A child with a calm temperament may stay relaxed even when the classroom is noisy.","zh":"氣質冷靜的孩子，即使課室很嘈雜，也可能保持放鬆。"},{"en":"Temperament can affect how people respond to stress, change, and disagreement.","zh":"氣質可以影響人如何回應壓力、轉變和分歧。"},{"en":"This word describes a person’s basic emotional tendency.","zh":"這個字描述一個人的基本情緒傾向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"body fluids","meaning":"體液","examples":[{"en":"Hippocrates believed there were four different body fluids.","zh":"希波克拉底相信人體有四種不同體液。"},{"en":"Body fluids are liquids inside the body, though ancient thinkers used the idea differently from modern medicine.","zh":"body fluids 指身體內的液體，但古代思想家使用這概念的方式與現代醫學不同。"},{"en":"Blood, saliva, and sweat are examples of body fluids in ordinary modern language.","zh":"血液、唾液和汗液都是現代日常語言中的體液例子。"},{"en":"In ancient theories, body fluids were wrongly believed to explain personality differences.","zh":"在古代理論中，體液被錯誤地認為能解釋性格差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is important here because it shows an old physical explanation for temperament.","zh":"這個短語在此重要，因為它顯示古人對氣質的生理解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"influence basic types of","meaning":"影響基本類型的……","examples":[{"en":"He thought body fluids could influence basic types of temperament.","zh":"他認為體液可以影響基本類型的氣質。"},{"en":"To influence basic types of something means to affect the main categories or forms of it.","zh":"influence basic types of something 指影響某事物的主要類別或形式。"},{"en":"Family habits can influence basic types of behaviour, such as how children speak to adults.","zh":"家庭習慣可以影響基本類型的行為，例如孩子如何與成年人說話。"},{"en":"If one factor influences basic types of response, people may react differently to the same situation.","zh":"如果某因素影響基本反應類型，人們可能對同一情況有不同反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a cause shaping broad categories.","zh":"這個短語描述某原因塑造廣泛類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be further developed","meaning":"得到進一步發展","examples":[{"en":"His work was further developed 500 years later by Galen.","zh":"他的學說在五百年後由 Galen 進一步發展。"},{"en":"To be further developed means to be expanded, improved, or made more detailed later.","zh":"be further developed 指後來被擴展、改善或變得更詳細。"},{"en":"A student’s first essay idea can be further developed after teacher feedback.","zh":"學生最初的作文想法可以在老師回饋後得到進一步發展。"},{"en":"When an idea is further developed, later thinkers add structure, examples, or clearer explanation.","zh":"當想法得到進一步發展，後來的思想家會加入結構、例子或更清晰解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an idea did not stop at its first version.","zh":"這個短語顯示想法沒有停留在最初版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"self-assessment tools","meaning":"自我評估工具","examples":[{"en":"These days, there are many self-assessment tools related to personality and communication.","zh":"現今有許多與性格和溝通有關的自我評估工具。"},{"en":"Self-assessment tools are questionnaires or activities that help people reflect on their own traits or habits.","zh":"self-assessment tools 指幫助人反思自身特質或習慣的問卷或活動。"},{"en":"A student may use a self-assessment tool to understand whether they learn better by listening or reading.","zh":"學生可能使用自我評估工具，了解自己透過聆聽還是閱讀學得更好。"},{"en":"These tools can start useful discussion, but they should not be treated as perfect scientific labels.","zh":"這些工具可以開啟有用討論，但不應被視為完美科學標籤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes tools that help people examine themselves.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助人檢視自己的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"relate to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Many modern tools relate to the basic descriptions developed by Galen.","zh":"許多現代工具與 Galen 發展出的基本描述有關。"},{"en":"To relate to something means to be connected with it in meaning, topic, or origin.","zh":"relate to something 指在意思、主題或起源上與某事有連繫。"},{"en":"A health lesson may relate to students’ daily habits, such as sleep and diet.","zh":"健康課可能與學生的日常習慣有關，例如睡眠和飲食。"},{"en":"When new ideas relate to older theories, they may share some concepts even if the explanation has changed.","zh":"當新想法與舊理論有關，它們可能共享某些概念，即使解釋已改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a connection between two things.","zh":"這個短語描述兩件事之間的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"basic descriptions","meaning":"基本描述","examples":[{"en":"The basic descriptions of temperament were developed centuries ago.","zh":"氣質的基本描述在多個世紀前已被發展出來。"},{"en":"Basic descriptions are simple explanations of the main features of something.","zh":"basic descriptions 指對某事主要特徵的簡單解釋。"},{"en":"A textbook may give basic descriptions of different essay types before showing examples.","zh":"教科書可能先給出不同作文類型的基本描述，再展示例子。"},{"en":"Basic descriptions help beginners understand a topic before studying details.","zh":"基本描述幫助初學者在研究細節前理解主題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to simple starting explanations, not complete analysis.","zh":"這個短語指簡單的起始解釋，而不是完整分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"no longer believe","meaning":"不再相信","examples":[{"en":"We no longer believe that temperament is determined by body fluids.","zh":"我們不再相信氣質由體液決定。"},{"en":"To no longer believe something means to stop accepting it as true.","zh":"no longer believe something 指停止接受某事為真。"},{"en":"People no longer believe that the Earth is flat because scientific evidence shows otherwise.","zh":"人們不再相信地球是平的，因為科學證據顯示並非如此。"},{"en":"When evidence changes, society may no longer believe an old explanation.","zh":"當證據改變，社會可能不再相信舊解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a past belief has been rejected.","zh":"這個短語顯示過去信念已被放棄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be determined by","meaning":"由……決定","examples":[{"en":"Temperament is no longer believed to be determined by body fluids.","zh":"氣質不再被認為由體液決定。"},{"en":"To be determined by something means to be decided or strongly shaped by it.","zh":"be determined by something 指由某事決定或強烈塑造。"},{"en":"A student’s final grade may be determined by exams, coursework, and attendance.","zh":"學生的最終成績可能由考試、課業和出席率決定。"},{"en":"If behaviour is determined by many factors, one simple explanation is usually not enough.","zh":"如果行為由多種因素決定，單一簡單解釋通常不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what controls or decides a result.","zh":"這個短語解釋甚麼控制或決定結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"dominate our systems","meaning":"主導我們的身體系統","examples":[{"en":"People no longer believe that certain body fluids dominate our systems.","zh":"人們不再相信某些體液會主導我們的身體系統。"},{"en":"To dominate our systems means to control or strongly influence how our bodies or inner processes work.","zh":"dominate our systems 指控制或強烈影響我們身體或內在過程如何運作。"},{"en":"Stress can dominate a person’s system if it affects sleep, appetite, and mood every day.","zh":"如果壓力每天影響睡眠、食慾和情緒，它可能主導一個人的身體狀態。"},{"en":"Ancient thinkers believed body fluids dominated the body, but modern science explains temperament differently.","zh":"古代思想家相信體液主導身體，但現代科學以不同方式解釋氣質。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests strong control over the body or a system.","zh":"這個短語暗示對身體或系統有強烈控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the value of","meaning":"……的價值","examples":[{"en":"The value of self-assessments is that they can help explain people’s differences.","zh":"自我評估的價值在於它們可以幫助解釋人們的差異。"},{"en":"The value of something means its usefulness, importance, or benefit.","zh":"value of something 指某事的用途、重要性或好處。"},{"en":"The value of practice is that students can learn from mistakes before the exam.","zh":"練習的價值在於學生可以在考試前從錯誤中學習。"},{"en":"When people understand the value of a tool, they know why it is worth using.","zh":"當人們理解工具的價值，就知道為何值得使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why something matters.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事為何重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"identify personality","meaning":"識別性格","examples":[{"en":"Self-assessments can help identify personality and communication styles.","zh":"自我評估可以幫助識別性格和溝通風格。"},{"en":"To identify personality means to recognise patterns in how a person thinks, feels, and behaves.","zh":"identify personality 指辨認一個人思考、感受和行為上的模式。"},{"en":"A counsellor may use questions to help students identify personality strengths and weaknesses.","zh":"輔導員可能使用問題幫助學生識別性格上的強項和弱點。"},{"en":"Identifying personality patterns can help people choose better study or teamwork strategies.","zh":"識別性格模式可以幫助人選擇更好的學習或團隊合作策略。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognising personal traits, not judging someone’s worth.","zh":"這個短語描述辨認個人特質，而不是評價人的價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"conflict-handling styles","meaning":"處理衝突的風格","examples":[{"en":"Some tools help people understand their conflict-handling styles.","zh":"有些工具幫助人理解自己處理衝突的風格。"},{"en":"Conflict-handling styles are the usual ways people respond when disagreement or tension appears.","zh":"conflict-handling styles 指人在出現分歧或緊張時的慣常回應方式。"},{"en":"One worker may avoid conflict, while another may discuss it directly and quickly.","zh":"一名員工可能逃避衝突，另一名員工可能直接而快速地討論它。"},{"en":"Understanding these styles can prevent people from assuming that others are rude or careless.","zh":"理解這些風格可以防止人以為別人無禮或粗心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes patterns in dealing with disagreement.","zh":"這個短語描述處理分歧時的模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"aspects of individuals","meaning":"個人的不同方面","examples":[{"en":"Self-assessments can identify different aspects of individuals.","zh":"自我評估可以識別個人的不同方面。"},{"en":"Aspects of individuals are different parts of a person’s character, habits, abilities, or preferences.","zh":"aspects of individuals 指一個人的性格、習慣、能力或偏好中的不同部分。"},{"en":"A school report may describe aspects of individuals such as effort, teamwork, and organisation.","zh":"學校報告可能描述個人的不同方面，例如努力、團隊合作和組織能力。"},{"en":"Looking at several aspects gives a fairer picture than focusing on one weakness.","zh":"看幾個方面比只集中於一個弱點更公平。"},{"en":"This phrase describes different sides of a person.","zh":"這個短語描述一個人的不同面向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"depersonalise conflict","meaning":"令衝突不再個人化","examples":[{"en":"Understanding communication styles can help depersonalise conflict.","zh":"理解溝通風格可以幫助令衝突不再個人化。"},{"en":"To depersonalise conflict means to stop treating disagreement as a personal attack and see it as a difference in needs, habits, or style.","zh":"depersonalise conflict 指不再把分歧視為個人攻擊，而是看成需要、習慣或風格上的差異。"},{"en":"A manager can depersonalise conflict by saying, “We have different information needs,” instead of blaming one worker.","zh":"經理可以說「我們有不同資料需求」，而不是責怪某名員工，從而令衝突不再個人化。"},{"en":"When conflict is depersonalised, people usually become calmer and more willing to solve the problem.","zh":"當衝突不再個人化，人們通常更冷靜，也更願意解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase helps teams focus on the issue rather than the person.","zh":"這個短語幫助團隊集中於問題，而不是人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"interpersonal relationships","meaning":"人際關係","examples":[{"en":"Conflict often happens within interpersonal relationships.","zh":"衝突經常在人際關係中發生。"},{"en":"Interpersonal relationships are connections between people, such as friends, classmates, colleagues, or family members.","zh":"interpersonal relationships 指人與人之間的連繫，例如朋友、同學、同事或家人。"},{"en":"A student’s interpersonal relationships can affect whether they feel safe in a class.","zh":"學生的人際關係可以影響他在班上是否感到安全。"},{"en":"Poor communication can damage interpersonal relationships even when the original problem is small.","zh":"即使原本問題很小，差劣溝通也可以損害人際關係。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relationships between people, not a person’s private thoughts alone.","zh":"這個短語描述人與人之間的關係，而不只是個人的私人想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"realise that","meaning":"意識到","examples":[{"en":"You may realise that others are not trying to be difficult.","zh":"你可能意識到別人並非故意刁難。"},{"en":"To realise that something is true means to understand it clearly, often after thinking or noticing evidence.","zh":"realise that something is true 指清楚明白某事是真的，通常是在思考或注意到證據後。"},{"en":"A student may realise that a strict teacher is trying to help them improve.","zh":"學生可能意識到嚴格老師是在嘗試幫助自己進步。"},{"en":"When people realise the reason behind someone’s behaviour, they may feel less angry.","zh":"當人意識到某人行為背後的原因，他們可能較不憤怒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes coming to a clearer understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸有更清晰理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"try to be difficult","meaning":"故意刁難","examples":[{"en":"Some people are not trying to be difficult; they simply need more information.","zh":"有些人並非故意刁難；他們只是需要更多資料。"},{"en":"To try to be difficult means to deliberately make things harder for others.","zh":"try to be difficult 指故意令事情對別人更困難。"},{"en":"A classmate who asks many questions may not be trying to be difficult; they may just be confused.","zh":"問很多問題的同學未必是在故意刁難；他可能只是困惑。"},{"en":"Assuming someone is trying to be difficult can create unnecessary conflict.","zh":"以為某人在故意刁難，可能造成不必要衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intentional unhelpful behaviour, not honest disagreement.","zh":"這個短語描述有意的不合作行為，而不是誠實的不同意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"different or more information","meaning":"不同或更多資料","examples":[{"en":"Some colleagues need different or more information before making decisions.","zh":"有些同事在作決定前需要不同或更多資料。"},{"en":"Different or more information means information that is either not the same type or greater in amount.","zh":"different or more information 指資料類型不同，或數量更多。"},{"en":"A doctor may need different or more information before deciding which test a patient needs.","zh":"醫生在決定病人需要哪項檢查前，可能需要不同或更多資料。"},{"en":"When people lack the information they need, they may delay decisions or ask many questions.","zh":"當人缺乏所需資料，他們可能延遲決定或提出很多問題。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why some people seem slow or cautious.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何有些人看似緩慢或謹慎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"intend to be rude","meaning":"有意無禮","examples":[{"en":"They are not intending to be rude when they focus mainly on the task.","zh":"當他們主要專注於任務時，他們並不是有意無禮。"},{"en":"To intend to be rude means to deliberately act in an impolite or disrespectful way.","zh":"intend to be rude 指故意以不禮貌或不尊重的方式行事。"},{"en":"A busy nurse who speaks briefly may not intend to be rude; she may be handling an emergency.","zh":"說話簡短的忙碌護士未必有意無禮；她可能正在處理緊急情況。"},{"en":"If we assume rude intention too quickly, we may turn a small style difference into conflict.","zh":"如果我們太快假設別人有意無禮，可能把小小風格差異變成衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether the behaviour was deliberate.","zh":"這個短語集中於該行為是否故意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be focused on the task","meaning":"專注於任務","examples":[{"en":"Some people are so focused on the task that they forget about greetings.","zh":"有些人太專注於任務，以致忘記打招呼。"},{"en":"To be focused on the task means to give most attention to completing the work.","zh":"be focused on the task 指把大部分注意力放在完成工作上。"},{"en":"A chef during lunch rush may be focused on the task and speak very briefly to colleagues.","zh":"午餐繁忙時段的廚師可能專注於任務，並對同事說話非常簡短。"},{"en":"Task focus can improve efficiency, but it may make people seem cold if they ignore relationships.","zh":"專注任務可以提升效率，但如果忽略關係，可能令人看起來冷淡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong attention to work rather than social interaction.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈注意工作，而不是社交互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"forget about greeting people","meaning":"忘記打招呼","examples":[{"en":"Task-focused people may forget about greeting people.","zh":"專注任務的人可能忘記打招呼。"},{"en":"To forget about greeting people means to fail to say hello or acknowledge others politely.","zh":"forget about greeting people 指忘記向別人問好或禮貌地表示注意到對方。"},{"en":"A manager rushing to fix a technical problem may forget about greeting people in the meeting room.","zh":"急着處理技術問題的經理，可能忘記向會議室的人打招呼。"},{"en":"If greetings are ignored too often, colleagues may feel unimportant or disrespected.","zh":"如果問候太常被忽略，同事可能覺得自己不重要或不被尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how task focus can accidentally hurt relationships.","zh":"這個短語顯示專注任務如何可能無意中傷害關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at the risk of","meaning":"冒着……的風險","examples":[{"en":"Some people want to work faster, but not at the risk of damaging relationships.","zh":"有些人想工作更快，但不想冒着損害關係的風險。"},{"en":"At the risk of something means with the possibility of causing that negative result.","zh":"at the risk of something 指有可能造成某個負面結果。"},{"en":"A student should not finish homework quickly at the risk of making careless mistakes.","zh":"學生不應冒着犯粗心錯誤的風險快速完成功課。"},{"en":"Working too fast can save time, but it may create conflict if people feel ignored.","zh":"工作太快可以省時間，但如果人們感到被忽略，可能造成衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that one benefit may come with a danger.","zh":"這個短語警告某個好處可能伴隨危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"damage relationships","meaning":"損害關係","examples":[{"en":"Working too quickly may damage relationships within a team.","zh":"工作太快可能損害團隊內的關係。"},{"en":"To damage relationships means to harm trust, respect, or positive feelings between people.","zh":"damage relationships 指傷害人與人之間的信任、尊重或正面感受。"},{"en":"Ignoring a friend’s messages for weeks can damage relationships even if you are busy.","zh":"即使你很忙，幾星期不理朋友訊息也可能損害關係。"},{"en":"In a workplace, harsh words can damage relationships and make cooperation harder.","zh":"在工作場所中，嚴厲說話可以損害關係，令合作更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harm to human connections.","zh":"這個短語描述對人際連繫的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get the job done","meaning":"完成工作","examples":[{"en":"Strong working relationships are often needed to get the job done.","zh":"要完成工作，通常需要良好的工作關係。"},{"en":"To get the job done means to complete the task successfully.","zh":"get the job done 指成功完成任務。"},{"en":"A restaurant team must cooperate well to get the job done during a busy dinner shift.","zh":"餐廳團隊在繁忙晚市時必須良好合作，才能完成工作。"},{"en":"If people refuse to communicate, even simple work may not get done properly.","zh":"如果人們拒絕溝通，即使簡單工作也可能做不好。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical completion rather than discussion alone.","zh":"這個短語集中於實際完成，而不只是討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be done right","meaning":"做得正確；做好","examples":[{"en":"The task can only be done right with the appropriate information.","zh":"任務只有在有適當資料時才能做得正確。"},{"en":"To be done right means to be completed correctly, carefully, and to the needed standard.","zh":"be done right 指以正確、仔細並符合所需標準的方式完成。"},{"en":"A medicine order must be done right because mistakes can harm patients.","zh":"藥物指令必須做得正確，因為錯誤可能傷害病人。"},{"en":"If workers do not have enough information, the task may be finished quickly but not done right.","zh":"如果員工沒有足夠資料，任務可能快速完成，但未必做好。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses quality and correctness, not just completion.","zh":"這個短語強調質素和正確性，而不只是完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"appropriate information","meaning":"適當資料","examples":[{"en":"A task can be completed properly with the appropriate information.","zh":"有適當資料，任務才能妥善完成。"},{"en":"Appropriate information is the right kind and amount of information needed for a decision or task.","zh":"appropriate information 指作決定或完成任務所需的正確種類和數量的資料。"},{"en":"A doctor needs appropriate information about symptoms before giving advice.","zh":"醫生在給建議前，需要有關症狀的適當資料。"},{"en":"Without appropriate information, people may guess, delay, or make mistakes.","zh":"沒有適當資料，人們可能猜測、延誤或犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information that fits the purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述配合目的的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take time to collect","meaning":"需要時間收集","examples":[{"en":"The appropriate information takes time to collect.","zh":"適當資料需要時間收集。"},{"en":"To take time to collect means to require a period of effort before the information or items are gathered.","zh":"take time to collect 指資料或物品需要一段努力過程才能收集齊。"},{"en":"A teacher’s feedback takes time to collect if every student writes a long essay.","zh":"如果每名學生都寫長文，老師的回饋資料需要時間收集。"},{"en":"Good decisions may be slower because reliable information cannot always be gathered immediately.","zh":"好決定可能較慢，因為可靠資料不一定能立即取得。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why careful people may not decide quickly.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何謹慎的人未必很快作決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"when used appropriately","meaning":"使用得宜時","examples":[{"en":"When used appropriately, communication styles can help teams manage conflict.","zh":"使用得宜時，溝通風格可以幫助團隊管理衝突。"},{"en":"When used appropriately means when something is used in the right way and in the right situation.","zh":"when used appropriately 指某物在正確方式和正確情況下被使用。"},{"en":"Technology helps learning when used appropriately, but it can distract students if used carelessly.","zh":"科技使用得宜時有助學習，但如果粗心使用，可能分散學生注意力。"},{"en":"A direct style may solve urgent problems when used appropriately.","zh":"直接風格使用得宜時，可能解決緊急問題。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that a tool or style depends on wise use.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，工具或風格取決於明智使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"resolve conflict on teams","meaning":"化解團隊中的衝突","examples":[{"en":"Understanding communication styles can help resolve conflict on teams.","zh":"理解溝通風格可以幫助化解團隊中的衝突。"},{"en":"To resolve conflict on teams means to help group members handle disagreement and work together again.","zh":"resolve conflict on teams 指幫助團隊成員處理分歧並再次合作。"},{"en":"A project leader can resolve conflict on teams by clarifying roles and listening to concerns.","zh":"專案領袖可以透過澄清角色和聆聽憂慮，化解團隊中的衝突。"},{"en":"If team conflict is resolved early, the group can avoid delays and resentment.","zh":"如果團隊衝突及早化解，群體可以避免延誤和怨氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes solving disagreement within a working group.","zh":"這個短語描述解決工作團隊中的分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"true personality issues","meaning":"真正的性格問題","examples":[{"en":"Very rarely are conflicts true personality issues.","zh":"衝突很少是真正的性格問題。"},{"en":"True personality issues are conflicts caused by deep character problems rather than simple differences in style or information needs.","zh":"true personality issues 指由深層性格問題造成的衝突，而不是簡單的風格或資料需求差異。"},{"en":"A colleague asking for more data may not show a true personality issue; they may simply work carefully.","zh":"同事要求更多數據未必顯示真正的性格問題；他可能只是工作謹慎。"},{"en":"If teams treat every disagreement as a personality problem, conflict becomes harder to solve.","zh":"如果團隊把每個分歧都視為性格問題，衝突會更難解決。"},{"en":"This phrase separates deep personal problems from ordinary communication differences.","zh":"這個短語把深層個人問題與普通溝通差異分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"issues of style","meaning":"風格上的問題","examples":[{"en":"Many conflicts are issues of style rather than real personality problems.","zh":"許多衝突是風格上的問題，而不是真正的性格問題。"},{"en":"Issues of style are problems caused by different habits, methods, or ways of communicating.","zh":"issues of style 指由不同習慣、方法或溝通方式造成的問題。"},{"en":"One teammate may want quick action while another wants detailed discussion; this can be an issue of style.","zh":"一名隊友可能想快速行動，另一名想詳細討論；這可以是風格上的問題。"},{"en":"When people recognise style differences, they can adjust instead of blaming each other.","zh":"當人們認出風格差異，就可以調整，而不是互相責怪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes conflict caused by approach, not bad character.","zh":"這個短語描述由處理方式造成的衝突，而不是品格差劣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"information needs","meaning":"對資料的需求","examples":[{"en":"Conflicts may result from different information needs.","zh":"衝突可能源於不同的資料需求。"},{"en":"Information needs are the amount or type of information a person requires before acting or deciding.","zh":"information needs 指一個人在行動或決定前所需的資料數量或種類。"},{"en":"A careful accountant may have higher information needs than a salesperson who wants a quick answer.","zh":"謹慎會計員的資料需求可能比想快速得到答案的銷售員更高。"},{"en":"If information needs are ignored, one person may feel rushed while another feels blocked.","zh":"如果資料需求被忽視，一個人可能覺得被催促，另一個人可能覺得受阻。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why some people ask for more details than others.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何有些人比其他人要求更多細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"basic temperaments","meaning":"基本氣質類型","examples":[{"en":"Hippocrates and Galen identified four basic temperaments.","zh":"希波克拉底和 Galen 識別出四種基本氣質類型。"},{"en":"Basic temperaments are broad categories used to describe common emotional and behavioural tendencies.","zh":"basic temperaments 指用來描述常見情緒和行為傾向的廣泛類別。"},{"en":"A training course may use basic temperaments to help workers discuss communication differences.","zh":"培訓課程可能使用基本氣質類型，幫助員工討論溝通差異。"},{"en":"These categories can simplify discussion, but real people are usually more complex.","zh":"這些類別可以簡化討論，但真人通常更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes simple personality groupings.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單的性格分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sanguine","meaning":"多血質的；活潑型的","examples":[{"en":"Sanguine people are often expressive and energetic.","zh":"多血質的人通常富表現力而充滿活力。"},{"en":"Sanguine describes a lively, optimistic, and sociable temperament.","zh":"sanguine 描述活潑、樂觀和愛社交的氣質。"},{"en":"A sanguine student may enjoy group presentations and encourage nervous classmates.","zh":"活潑型學生可能喜歡小組匯報，並鼓勵緊張的同學。"},{"en":"This style can energise a team, but it may sometimes miss details.","zh":"這種風格可以為團隊帶來能量，但有時可能忽略細節。"},{"en":"This word describes a bright and outgoing personality style.","zh":"這個字描述明朗外向的性格風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"phlegmatic","meaning":"黏液質的；冷靜型的","examples":[{"en":"Phlegmatic people are often calm, systematic and persevering.","zh":"黏液質的人通常冷靜、有系統而堅忍。"},{"en":"Phlegmatic describes a calm and steady temperament that usually avoids emotional extremes.","zh":"phlegmatic 描述冷靜穩定、通常避免情緒極端的氣質。"},{"en":"A phlegmatic worker may quietly check every step before submitting a report.","zh":"冷靜型員工可能安靜地檢查每個步驟，然後才提交報告。"},{"en":"This style can improve accuracy, but it may need time to adapt to sudden change.","zh":"這種風格可以改善準確度，但可能需要時間適應突然轉變。"},{"en":"This word describes a cool, careful, and persistent personality style.","zh":"這個字描述冷靜、謹慎而堅持的性格風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"melancholic","meaning":"憂鬱質的；體貼型的","examples":[{"en":"Melancholic people are often considerate and sympathetic.","zh":"憂鬱質的人通常體貼而富同情心。"},{"en":"Melancholic describes a sensitive, thoughtful, and caring temperament.","zh":"melancholic 描述敏感、深思和關心別人的氣質。"},{"en":"A melancholic teammate may notice when someone feels left out and try to include them.","zh":"體貼型隊友可能注意到有人被冷落，並嘗試把他包括進來。"},{"en":"This style can protect relationships, but it may sometimes delay decisions because everyone’s feelings are considered.","zh":"這種風格可以保護關係，但有時可能因考慮每個人的感受而延遲決定。"},{"en":"This word describes a careful and emotionally aware personality style.","zh":"這個字描述謹慎且有情緒覺察的性格風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"choleric","meaning":"膽汁質的；果斷型的","examples":[{"en":"Choleric people often communicate in a bold and direct way.","zh":"膽汁質的人通常以大膽而直接的方式溝通。"},{"en":"Choleric describes a strong, decisive, and action-oriented temperament.","zh":"choleric 描述強勢、果斷和重視行動的氣質。"},{"en":"A choleric manager may quickly set a goal and tell the team what must be done.","zh":"果斷型經理可能迅速設定目標，並告訴團隊必須做甚麼。"},{"en":"This style can move work forward, but it may seem forceful to quieter people.","zh":"這種風格可以推動工作前進，但對較安靜的人而言可能顯得強勢。"},{"en":"This word describes a direct and determined personality style.","zh":"這個字描述直接而堅決的性格風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"somewhat apt","meaning":"頗為貼切","examples":[{"en":"The old descriptions are still somewhat apt today.","zh":"這些舊描述在今天仍然頗為貼切。"},{"en":"Somewhat apt means partly suitable or reasonably accurate, though not perfect.","zh":"somewhat apt 指部分合適或相當準確，但不完美。"},{"en":"Calling a busy library “the heart of the school” is somewhat apt because many students gather there.","zh":"把繁忙圖書館稱為「學校的心臟」頗為貼切，因為許多學生聚集在那裡。"},{"en":"An old theory may be somewhat apt if parts of it still describe real behaviour.","zh":"如果舊理論部分仍能描述真實行為，它可能頗為貼切。"},{"en":"This phrase shows careful agreement without saying something is completely correct.","zh":"這個短語表示謹慎同意，而不是說某事完全正確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"update the wording","meaning":"更新措辭","examples":[{"en":"We could update the wording of the old temperament descriptions.","zh":"我們可以更新舊氣質描述的措辭。"},{"en":"To update the wording means to change old language into clearer or more modern words.","zh":"update the wording 指把舊語言改成更清楚或更現代的字句。"},{"en":"A school may update the wording of its rules so students understand them better.","zh":"學校可能更新校規措辭，讓學生更容易理解。"},{"en":"Updating wording can make an old idea easier to use without changing its basic meaning.","zh":"更新措辭可以令舊想法更易使用，而不改變其基本意思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes modernising the language of an explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述把解釋中的語言現代化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"translate into","meaning":"轉化為；相當於","examples":[{"en":"The four temperaments translate into four common communication styles.","zh":"四種氣質轉化為四種常見溝通風格。"},{"en":"To translate into something means to become, correspond to, or be expressed as that thing in another form.","zh":"translate into something 指變成、對應於或以另一形式表達為某事。"},{"en":"A student’s effort can translate into better marks if the practice is focused.","zh":"如果練習有焦點，學生的努力可以轉化為更好分數。"},{"en":"In this passage, old temperament terms translate into modern communication categories.","zh":"在這篇文章中，舊氣質術語轉化為現代溝通分類。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how one idea appears in a new form.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個想法如何以新形式出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fairly common","meaning":"相當常見的","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes four fairly common communication styles.","zh":"文章描述四種相當常見的溝通風格。"},{"en":"Fairly common means quite often seen or not unusual.","zh":"fairly common 指頗常見或並不罕見。"},{"en":"It is fairly common for students to feel nervous before speaking exams.","zh":"學生在口試前感到緊張是相當常見的。"},{"en":"If a behaviour is fairly common, teachers should prepare for it rather than be surprised by it.","zh":"如果某行為相當常見，老師應有所準備，而不是感到驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that happens often enough to be familiar.","zh":"這個短語描述常見到令人熟悉的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"correspond to","meaning":"對應於","examples":[{"en":"The sanguine temperament corresponds to the expressive style of communication.","zh":"多血質氣質對應於富表現力的溝通風格。"},{"en":"To correspond to something means to match or be connected with it.","zh":"correspond to something 指與某事匹配或有連繫。"},{"en":"A student’s answer must correspond to the question, not just discuss the same topic generally.","zh":"學生答案必須對應題目，而不只是泛泛討論同一主題。"},{"en":"When two categories correspond, they describe similar ideas in different systems.","zh":"當兩個分類互相對應，它們是在不同系統中描述相似想法。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a relationship of matching or equivalence.","zh":"這個短語顯示匹配或等同關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"expressive style of communication","meaning":"富表現力的溝通風格","examples":[{"en":"The expressive style of communication involves emotion and energy.","zh":"富表現力的溝通風格涉及情感和能量。"},{"en":"An expressive style of communication means speaking with feeling, movement, stories, and visible enthusiasm.","zh":"expressive style of communication 指帶着感情、動作、故事和明顯熱情說話。"},{"en":"A presenter with an expressive style may use gestures, facial expressions, and vivid examples.","zh":"具有富表現力風格的演講者可能使用手勢、面部表情和生動例子。"},{"en":"This style can motivate people, but it may sometimes move away from details.","zh":"這種風格可以激勵人，但有時可能偏離細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lively and emotionally rich way of communicating.","zh":"這個短語描述活潑且情感豐富的溝通方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"spirited style of communication","meaning":"充滿活力的溝通風格","examples":[{"en":"The spirited style of communication is lively and energetic.","zh":"充滿活力的溝通風格是活潑而有能量的。"},{"en":"A spirited style of communication means speaking with enthusiasm, animation, and strong personal energy.","zh":"spirited style of communication 指以熱情、生動感和強烈個人能量說話。"},{"en":"A spirited student may make a group discussion feel exciting and less tense.","zh":"充滿活力的學生可能令小組討論變得有趣並較不緊張。"},{"en":"This style can lift the team’s mood, but it may overwhelm quieter members if too intense.","zh":"這種風格可以提升團隊氣氛，但如果太強烈，可能令較安靜成員吃不消。"},{"en":"This phrase describes communication full of life and energy.","zh":"這個短語描述充滿生命力和能量的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"speak in pictures","meaning":"用圖像式語言表達","examples":[{"en":"Expressive people often speak in pictures.","zh":"富表現力的人常用圖像式語言表達。"},{"en":"To speak in pictures means to use vivid images, stories, or comparisons rather than plain facts alone.","zh":"speak in pictures 指使用生動畫面、故事或比較，而不只是平淡事實。"},{"en":"A teacher speaks in pictures when she explains memory as “a library with shelves.”","zh":"老師把記憶解釋成「有書架的圖書館」時，就是用圖像式語言表達。"},{"en":"This style can make ideas easier to imagine, but it may take longer than direct explanation.","zh":"這種風格可以令想法更容易想像，但可能比直接解釋更花時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes colourful, image-based communication.","zh":"這個短語描述色彩豐富、以畫面為基礎的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"invest emotion and energy in","meaning":"在……投入情感和精力","examples":[{"en":"They invest a lot of emotion and energy in their communication.","zh":"他們在溝通中投入很多情感和精力。"},{"en":"To invest emotion and energy in something means to put strong feeling and effort into it.","zh":"invest emotion and energy in something 指在某事上投入強烈感受和努力。"},{"en":"A drama teacher may invest emotion and energy in every class to keep students engaged.","zh":"戲劇老師可能在每堂課投入情感和精力，令學生投入。"},{"en":"When people invest much emotion in a discussion, the conversation can feel exciting but intense.","zh":"當人在討論中投入大量情感，對話可以令人興奮但也強烈。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong personal involvement.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈的個人投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put their whole body into it","meaning":"全身投入其中","examples":[{"en":"Expressive communicators often put their whole body into it.","zh":"富表現力的溝通者常常全身投入其中。"},{"en":"To put one’s whole body into it means to communicate with voice, gestures, movement, and facial expression.","zh":"put one’s whole body into it 指用聲音、手勢、動作和面部表情來溝通。"},{"en":"A storyteller may put her whole body into it when acting out different characters for children.","zh":"說故事的人為孩子演繹不同角色時，可能全身投入其中。"},{"en":"This can make communication memorable, but it may seem too intense in a formal meeting.","zh":"這可以令溝通令人難忘，但在正式會議中可能顯得太強烈。"},{"en":"This phrase describes full physical involvement in expression.","zh":"這個短語描述在表達中投入整個身體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be easily sidetracked","meaning":"容易離題","examples":[{"en":"They are easily sidetracked onto a story.","zh":"他們容易被帶到故事上而離題。"},{"en":"To be easily sidetracked means to be quickly pulled away from the main topic or task.","zh":"be easily sidetracked 指很快被拉離主要話題或任務。"},{"en":"A student may be easily sidetracked by phone messages while doing homework.","zh":"學生做功課時可能容易被手機訊息分心。"},{"en":"If a meeting is easily sidetracked, the team may run out of time before decisions are made.","zh":"如果會議容易離題，團隊可能在作出決定前已用完時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes losing focus because something else catches attention.","zh":"這個短語描述因其他東西吸引注意而失去焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"illustrate the point","meaning":"說明重點","examples":[{"en":"The story may or may not illustrate the point they are trying to make.","zh":"這個故事可能說明，也可能沒有說明他們想表達的重點。"},{"en":"To illustrate the point means to give an example that makes an idea clearer.","zh":"illustrate the point 指給出例子令想法更清楚。"},{"en":"A teacher may tell a short story to illustrate the point that practice matters.","zh":"老師可能講一個短故事來說明練習很重要這個重點。"},{"en":"If the example does not match the idea, it fails to illustrate the point.","zh":"如果例子與想法不配合，它就不能說明重點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using examples to clarify meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述用例子澄清意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make a point","meaning":"表達一個觀點","examples":[{"en":"They may tell a story to make a point.","zh":"他們可能講故事來表達一個觀點。"},{"en":"To make a point means to express an idea clearly, often in order to persuade or explain.","zh":"make a point 指清楚表達想法，通常為了說服或解釋。"},{"en":"A student may use a real example to make a point in an essay.","zh":"學生可能在作文中使用真實例子來表達一個觀點。"},{"en":"If people take too long to make a point, listeners may lose focus.","zh":"如果人花太長時間才說出重點，聽眾可能失去焦點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stating or proving an idea.","zh":"這個短語描述說明或證明一個想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"because of their enthusiasm","meaning":"由於他們的熱情","examples":[{"en":"Because of their enthusiasm, they are often great team motivators.","zh":"由於他們的熱情，他們通常是很好的團隊推動者。"},{"en":"Because of their enthusiasm means their energy and excitement are the reason for the result.","zh":"because of their enthusiasm 指他們的能量和興奮感是結果的原因。"},{"en":"Because of her enthusiasm, the teacher makes even difficult grammar feel interesting.","zh":"由於老師的熱情，即使困難文法也變得有趣。"},{"en":"Enthusiasm can encourage others to participate and keep trying.","zh":"熱情可以鼓勵別人參與並繼續嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how positive energy leads to an effect.","zh":"這個短語解釋正面能量如何導致某種效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"team motivators","meaning":"團隊鼓勵者；團隊推動者","examples":[{"en":"Expressive people can be great team motivators.","zh":"富表現力的人可以是很好的團隊鼓勵者。"},{"en":"Team motivators are people who encourage a group and help members feel energetic and willing to work.","zh":"team motivators 指鼓勵群體，並幫助成員感到有精神和願意工作的人。"},{"en":"In a class project, a team motivator may praise others and remind them why the task matters.","zh":"在班級專案中，團隊推動者可能讚賞別人，並提醒他們任務為何重要。"},{"en":"Good motivators can lift morale when a team feels tired or discouraged.","zh":"好的推動者可以在團隊疲倦或氣餒時提升士氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people who help a team keep moving forward.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助團隊繼續前進的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be concerned about","meaning":"關心……","examples":[{"en":"They are concerned about people and relationships.","zh":"他們關心人和關係。"},{"en":"To be concerned about something means to care about it or feel it is important.","zh":"be concerned about something 指關心某事或覺得它重要。"},{"en":"A parent may be concerned about a child’s sleep if the child looks tired every morning.","zh":"如果孩子每天早上看起來疲倦，家長可能關心孩子的睡眠。"},{"en":"If a manager is concerned about relationships, they may check whether staff feel respected.","zh":"如果經理關心關係，他可能檢查員工是否感到被尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes care, attention, or worry.","zh":"這個短語描述關心、注意或擔憂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"high levels of energy","meaning":"高度精力","examples":[{"en":"Their high levels of energy can come on strong at times.","zh":"他們高度精力有時會給人強烈感覺。"},{"en":"High levels of energy mean a person has a lot of enthusiasm, activity, and force in their behaviour.","zh":"high levels of energy 指一個人在行為中有很多熱情、活動力和力量。"},{"en":"A sports coach with high levels of energy can make tired students try again.","zh":"高度精力的體育教練可以令疲倦學生再次嘗試。"},{"en":"High energy can motivate a group, but it may also overwhelm people who prefer calm discussion.","zh":"高能量可以激勵群體，但也可能令喜歡冷靜討論的人吃不消。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong visible enthusiasm.","zh":"這個短語描述明顯而強烈的熱情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"come on strong","meaning":"給人強烈感覺；表現得很強勢","examples":[{"en":"Their enthusiasm can come on strong at times.","zh":"他們的熱情有時會給人強烈感覺。"},{"en":"To come on strong means to seem very intense, forceful, or overwhelming to others.","zh":"come on strong 指在別人眼中顯得非常強烈、強勢或令人吃不消。"},{"en":"A salesperson may come on strong if they talk too quickly and push too hard.","zh":"如果銷售員說話太快、推銷太用力，就可能給人強勢感覺。"},{"en":"Strong enthusiasm can help a team, but it can also make quieter members withdraw.","zh":"強烈熱情可以幫助團隊，但也可能令較安靜成員退縮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes energy that feels powerful, sometimes too powerful.","zh":"這個短語描述令人感覺很強、有時過強的能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at times","meaning":"有時","examples":[{"en":"Their communication style can seem intense at times.","zh":"他們的溝通風格有時可能顯得強烈。"},{"en":"At times means sometimes or on certain occasions.","zh":"at times 指有時或在某些情況下。"},{"en":"A usually calm student may feel nervous at times before public speaking.","zh":"通常冷靜的學生在公開演說前有時也可能緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something does not happen always, only occasionally.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事不是總會發生，而是偶爾發生。"},{"en":"It is useful for making a statement more balanced.","zh":"它有助令陳述更平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"focus on the bigger picture","meaning":"著眼於大局","examples":[{"en":"Their focus is usually on the bigger picture.","zh":"他們的焦點通常著眼於大局。"},{"en":"To focus on the bigger picture means to pay attention to the overall goal, direction, or meaning rather than small details.","zh":"focus on the bigger picture 指注意整體目標、方向或意義，而不是小細節。"},{"en":"A school principal must focus on the bigger picture when planning long-term student support.","zh":"校長規劃長期學生支援時，必須著眼於大局。"},{"en":"Big-picture thinking helps teams understand purpose, but details still need checking.","zh":"大局思考幫助團隊理解目的，但細節仍需要檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attention to the whole situation.","zh":"這個短語描述對整體情況的注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"miss the details","meaning":"忽略細節","examples":[{"en":"They sometimes miss the details or the proper order of things.","zh":"他們有時會忽略細節或事情的正確次序。"},{"en":"To miss the details means to fail to notice small but important pieces of information.","zh":"miss the details 指沒有注意到細小但重要的資料。"},{"en":"A student may miss the details in a reading passage if they only read the first sentence.","zh":"如果學生只讀第一句，可能會忽略閱讀文章中的細節。"},{"en":"Missing details can lead to errors, even when the main idea is understood.","zh":"即使理解主旨，忽略細節也可能導致錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes overlooking small information that matters.","zh":"這個短語描述忽視重要的小資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the proper order of things","meaning":"事情的正確次序","examples":[{"en":"They may miss the details or the proper order of things.","zh":"他們可能忽略細節或事情的正確次序。"},{"en":"The proper order of things is the correct sequence in which tasks or steps should happen.","zh":"proper order of things 指任務或步驟應發生的正確順序。"},{"en":"In a recipe, the proper order of things matters because adding ingredients too late can ruin the dish.","zh":"在食譜中，事情的正確次序很重要，因為太遲加入材料可能破壞菜式。"},{"en":"If a team ignores the proper order, work may need to be redone.","zh":"如果團隊忽略正確次序，工作可能需要重做。"},{"en":"This phrase describes correct sequencing.","zh":"這個短語描述正確排序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"differences of opinion","meaning":"意見分歧","examples":[{"en":"They find conflict or differences of opinion invigorating.","zh":"他們覺得衝突或意見分歧令人振奮。"},{"en":"Differences of opinion are situations where people think differently about the same issue.","zh":"differences of opinion 指人們對同一問題有不同想法的情況。"},{"en":"Students may have differences of opinion about whether school uniforms are useful.","zh":"學生可能對校服是否有用有意見分歧。"},{"en":"Differences of opinion can improve a plan if people listen and explain their reasons.","zh":"如果人們聆聽並解釋理由，意見分歧可以改善計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disagreement in ideas, not necessarily personal conflict.","zh":"這個短語描述想法上的不同，不一定是個人衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"find something invigorating","meaning":"覺得某事令人振奮","examples":[{"en":"Expressive people may find disagreement invigorating.","zh":"富表現力的人可能覺得分歧令人振奮。"},{"en":"To find something invigorating means to feel that it gives energy, excitement, or fresh motivation.","zh":"find something invigorating 指覺得某事帶來能量、興奮或新動力。"},{"en":"Some students find debate invigorating because it makes them think faster.","zh":"有些學生覺得辯論令人振奮，因為它令他們思考更快。"},{"en":"A lively challenge can be invigorating for one person but stressful for another.","zh":"活潑的挑戰對某人可能令人振奮，對另一個人卻可能有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that makes people feel more alive or energetic.","zh":"這個短語描述令人氣氛活起來或更有精神的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"engage in a spirited discussion","meaning":"參與熱烈討論","examples":[{"en":"They love to engage in a spirited discussion.","zh":"他們喜歡參與熱烈討論。"},{"en":"To engage in a spirited discussion means to take part in a lively and energetic conversation.","zh":"engage in a spirited discussion 指參與活躍而充滿能量的對話。"},{"en":"Students may engage in a spirited discussion about whether homework should be reduced.","zh":"學生可能就應否減少功課參與熱烈討論。"},{"en":"Spirited discussion can produce good ideas if people remain respectful.","zh":"如果人們保持尊重，熱烈討論可以產生好想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active, energetic debate.","zh":"這個短語描述主動而有活力的辯論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be constantly looking for","meaning":"不斷尋找……","examples":[{"en":"They are constantly looking for new and exciting adventures.","zh":"他們不斷尋找新奇刺激的經歷。"},{"en":"To be constantly looking for something means to keep searching for it again and again.","zh":"be constantly looking for something 指一次又一次持續尋找某事。"},{"en":"A curious student may be constantly looking for new books, experiments, or questions.","zh":"好奇的學生可能不斷尋找新書、實驗或問題。"},{"en":"Constant searching can bring fresh ideas, but it may also make routine tasks feel boring.","zh":"持續尋找可以帶來新想法，但也可能令例行任務顯得沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated and active seeking.","zh":"這個短語描述重複而主動的尋求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"new and exciting adventures","meaning":"新奇刺激的經歷","examples":[{"en":"Expressive people often enjoy new and exciting adventures.","zh":"富表現力的人通常喜歡新奇刺激的經歷。"},{"en":"New and exciting adventures are fresh experiences that feel interesting, energetic, or unfamiliar.","zh":"new and exciting adventures 指令人感到有趣、有活力或陌生的新鮮經驗。"},{"en":"Joining a drama club may feel like a new and exciting adventure for a quiet student.","zh":"對安靜學生而言，加入戲劇學會可能像一段新奇刺激的經歷。"},{"en":"Such adventures can build confidence, but they may also distract people from routine duties.","zh":"這類經歷可以建立信心，但也可能令人分心於例行職責。"},{"en":"This phrase describes experiences that feel fresh and stimulating.","zh":"這個短語描述感覺新鮮而刺激的經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cool and persevering","meaning":"冷靜而堅忍的","examples":[{"en":"The phlegmatic person is described as cool and persevering.","zh":"黏液質的人被描述為冷靜而堅忍。"},{"en":"Cool and persevering means calm under pressure and able to continue despite difficulty.","zh":"cool and persevering 指在壓力下保持冷靜，並能在困難中繼續。"},{"en":"A cool and persevering nurse can keep working carefully during a busy emergency shift.","zh":"冷靜而堅忍的護士可以在繁忙急症班次中繼續小心工作。"},{"en":"This quality helps people finish long tasks without becoming emotional or giving up quickly.","zh":"這種特質幫助人完成長任務，而不會情緒化或很快放棄。"},{"en":"This phrase describes steady strength rather than loud energy.","zh":"這個短語描述穩定力量，而不是高聲能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"technical style of communication","meaning":"技術型溝通風格","examples":[{"en":"The technical style of communication focuses on facts and details.","zh":"技術型溝通風格專注於事實和細節。"},{"en":"A technical style of communication uses precise information, clear evidence, and detailed explanation.","zh":"technical style of communication 使用精確資料、清楚證據和詳細解釋。"},{"en":"An engineer may use a technical style when explaining why a machine has stopped working.","zh":"工程師解釋機器為何停止運作時，可能使用技術型溝通風格。"},{"en":"This style can prevent mistakes, but it may feel dry to people who want emotional support.","zh":"這種風格可以防止錯誤，但對想得到情感支援的人而言可能顯得枯燥。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fact-based and detail-focused communication.","zh":"這個短語描述以事實和細節為中心的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"systematic communication style","meaning":"系統化的溝通風格","examples":[{"en":"The systematic communication style is orderly and methodical.","zh":"系統化的溝通風格有條理而有方法。"},{"en":"A systematic communication style explains ideas step by step in a clear and organised way.","zh":"systematic communication style 指以清晰而有組織的方式逐步解釋想法。"},{"en":"A teacher uses a systematic style when she explains an essay structure one paragraph at a time.","zh":"老師逐段解釋作文結構時，就是使用系統化風格。"},{"en":"This style helps people follow complex instructions without confusion.","zh":"這種風格幫助人不混亂地跟隨複雜指示。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised communication with a clear sequence.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織且有清晰次序的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be focused on facts","meaning":"專注於事實","examples":[{"en":"This communication style is focused on facts and technical details.","zh":"這種溝通風格專注於事實和技術細節。"},{"en":"To be focused on facts means to give most attention to evidence, data, and what is objectively true.","zh":"be focused on facts 指把大部分注意力放在證據、數據和客觀真實的事情上。"},{"en":"A doctor may be focused on facts when checking symptoms, test results, and medical history.","zh":"醫生檢查症狀、化驗結果和病歷時，可能專注於事實。"},{"en":"Fact focus can improve accuracy, but it may not always address people’s feelings.","zh":"專注事實可以提高準確度，但未必總能照顧人的感受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes communication centred on evidence rather than emotion.","zh":"這個短語描述以證據而非情感為中心的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"technical details","meaning":"技術細節","examples":[{"en":"Phlegmatic people often care about technical details.","zh":"黏液質的人通常關心技術細節。"},{"en":"Technical details are specific pieces of information about how something works or should be done.","zh":"technical details 指關於某事如何運作或應如何完成的具體資料。"},{"en":"A computer technician needs technical details such as error messages and system settings.","zh":"電腦技術員需要錯誤訊息和系統設定等技術細節。"},{"en":"Missing technical details can cause mistakes in repairs, reports, or instructions.","zh":"忽略技術細節可以在維修、報告或指示中造成錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes precise practical information.","zh":"這個短語描述精確的實務資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an orderly, methodical way of","meaning":"有條理而有方法地……","examples":[{"en":"They have an orderly, methodical way of approaching tasks.","zh":"他們有條理而有方法地處理任務。"},{"en":"An orderly, methodical way of doing something means doing it in a clear, planned, step-by-step manner.","zh":"orderly, methodical way of doing something 指以清晰、有計劃、逐步的方式做某事。"},{"en":"A student may revise in an orderly, methodical way by listing topics and checking them one by one.","zh":"學生可以透過列出課題並逐一檢查，有條理而有方法地溫習。"},{"en":"This approach reduces mistakes because each step is considered carefully.","zh":"這種方法減少錯誤，因為每個步驟都被仔細考慮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful organisation rather than random action.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細組織，而不是隨機行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"approaching tasks","meaning":"處理任務","examples":[{"en":"They have a methodical way of approaching tasks.","zh":"他們以有方法的方式處理任務。"},{"en":"Approaching tasks means starting and dealing with work in a particular way.","zh":"approaching tasks 指以某種方式開始並處理工作。"},{"en":"A student may approach homework by reading instructions first and then planning the answer.","zh":"學生可能透過先閱讀指示再規劃答案來處理功課。"},{"en":"The way people approach tasks affects speed, accuracy, and stress.","zh":"人們處理任務的方式會影響速度、準確度和壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how someone begins and handles work.","zh":"這個短語描述某人如何開始和處理工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be very much on","meaning":"非常集中於……","examples":[{"en":"Their focus is very much on the task.","zh":"他們的焦點非常集中於任務。"},{"en":"To be very much on something means to be strongly centred on it.","zh":"be very much on something 指強烈集中於某事。"},{"en":"During exam week, a student’s attention may be very much on revision.","zh":"考試週期間，學生的注意力可能非常集中於溫習。"},{"en":"If a manager’s focus is very much on deadlines, they may forget to check staff feelings.","zh":"如果經理非常集中於截止日期，可能忘記了解員工感受。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong emphasis on one area.","zh":"這個短語顯示對某一範疇的強烈重視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the concerns that something may evoke","meaning":"某事可能引起的憂慮","examples":[{"en":"They may pay less attention to the concerns that the task may evoke.","zh":"他們可能較少注意該任務可能引起的憂慮。"},{"en":"The concerns that something may evoke are worries, feelings, or questions that it may cause in people.","zh":"concerns that something may evoke 指某事可能在人們心中造成的擔心、感受或疑問。"},{"en":"A new school rule may evoke concerns about fairness and pressure.","zh":"新校規可能引起關於公平和壓力的憂慮。"},{"en":"If leaders ignore concerns that a change evokes, people may resist the change.","zh":"如果領袖忽視改變引起的憂慮，人們可能抗拒改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the worries created by an action or situation.","zh":"這個短語描述某行動或情況造成的擔心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"accomplish a task","meaning":"完成任務","examples":[{"en":"They focus on the details necessary to accomplish a task.","zh":"他們專注於完成任務所需的細節。"},{"en":"To accomplish a task means to complete it successfully.","zh":"accomplish a task 指成功完成任務。"},{"en":"A student can accomplish a difficult project by breaking it into smaller steps.","zh":"學生可以透過把困難專題拆成小步驟來完成任務。"},{"en":"To accomplish a task well, people often need time, information, and clear roles.","zh":"要把任務做好，人們通常需要時間、資料和清晰角色。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses successful completion.","zh":"這個短語強調成功完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"overwhelm the big picture","meaning":"細節蓋過大局","examples":[{"en":"Sometimes the details overwhelm the big picture.","zh":"有時細節會蓋過大局。"},{"en":"To overwhelm the big picture means small details become so dominant that people lose sight of the main goal.","zh":"overwhelm the big picture 指小細節變得太主導，以致人們看不到主要目標。"},{"en":"A student may focus so much on font size that it overwhelms the big picture of the essay argument.","zh":"學生可能太專注字體大小，以致細節蓋過作文論點的大局。"},{"en":"When details overwhelm the big picture, teams may work hard but forget why the task matters.","zh":"當細節蓋過大局，團隊可能很努力工作，卻忘記任務為何重要。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that details can hide the overall purpose.","zh":"這個短語提醒人，細節可以遮蓋整體目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be brought back to","meaning":"被帶回到……","examples":[{"en":"The focus sometimes needs to be brought back to the context of the task.","zh":"焦點有時需要被帶回到任務的背景。"},{"en":"To be brought back to something means to be returned to the main topic, purpose, or situation.","zh":"be brought back to something 指被重新帶回主要話題、目的或情況。"},{"en":"If a class discussion becomes too personal, the teacher may bring it back to the question.","zh":"如果課堂討論變得太個人化，老師可能把它帶回問題本身。"},{"en":"Bringing focus back helps people stop wandering and continue useful work.","zh":"把焦點帶回來有助人停止偏離，並繼續有用工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes redirecting attention to what matters.","zh":"這個短語描述把注意力重新引向重要事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the context of the task","meaning":"任務的背景","examples":[{"en":"The team may need to return to the context of the task.","zh":"團隊可能需要回到任務的背景。"},{"en":"The context of the task is the background, purpose, limits, and situation surrounding the work.","zh":"context of the task 指圍繞工作的背景、目的、限制和情況。"},{"en":"Before writing a report, students should understand the context of the task, including audience and purpose.","zh":"寫報告前，學生應理解任務背景，包括讀者和目的。"},{"en":"If people ignore context, they may produce work that is accurate but not useful.","zh":"如果人們忽略背景，他們可能做出準確但不實用的工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the bigger situation that gives a task meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述賦予任務意義的較大情境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"speak for themselves","meaning":"不言自明","examples":[{"en":"People with this style think the facts should speak for themselves.","zh":"具有這種風格的人認為事實應該不言自明。"},{"en":"If facts speak for themselves, they seem clear enough without emotional explanation or persuasion.","zh":"如果事實 speak for themselves，意思是它們看來已足夠清楚，不需要情感解釋或說服。"},{"en":"A chart showing falling sales may speak for itself in a business meeting.","zh":"顯示銷售下跌的圖表在商業會議中可能不言自明。"},{"en":"Some people trust evidence more than long speeches because they believe facts speak for themselves.","zh":"有些人比起長篇演說更相信證據，因為他們認為事實不言自明。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the evidence is strong and obvious.","zh":"這個短語暗示證據強而明顯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be comfortable with conflict","meaning":"對衝突感到自在","examples":[{"en":"They are not as comfortable with conflict.","zh":"他們對衝突沒有那麼自在。"},{"en":"To be comfortable with conflict means to feel able to face disagreement without strong fear or avoidance.","zh":"be comfortable with conflict 指能夠面對分歧，而不強烈害怕或逃避。"},{"en":"A debate-team student may be comfortable with conflict because disagreement is part of the activity.","zh":"辯論隊學生可能對衝突感到自在，因為分歧是活動的一部分。"},{"en":"People who are uncomfortable with conflict may delay difficult conversations.","zh":"對衝突不自在的人可能延遲困難對話。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how relaxed someone feels when disagreement appears.","zh":"這個短語描述某人在出現分歧時有多放鬆。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"adapt to change","meaning":"適應轉變","examples":[{"en":"Phlegmatic people need time to adapt to change.","zh":"黏液質的人需要時間適應轉變。"},{"en":"To adapt to change means to adjust habits, thinking, or behaviour when a situation becomes different.","zh":"adapt to change 指當情況變得不同時，調整習慣、想法或行為。"},{"en":"Students may need time to adapt to a new timetable after moving to a new school.","zh":"學生轉到新學校後，可能需要時間適應新時間表。"},{"en":"Change becomes easier when people understand the reason and the steps involved.","zh":"當人們理解原因和涉及步驟，轉變會變得較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adjusting to new conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述適應新情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the logic of","meaning":"……的邏輯","examples":[{"en":"They need to understand the logic of the change.","zh":"他們需要理解轉變的邏輯。"},{"en":"The logic of something is the reason, structure, or thinking behind it.","zh":"logic of something 指某事背後的原因、結構或思路。"},{"en":"Students understand maths better when they understand the logic of a formula, not just memorise it.","zh":"學生理解公式的邏輯，而不只是背誦時，會更理解數學。"},{"en":"If workers see the logic of a new rule, they are more likely to accept it.","zh":"如果員工看見新規則的邏輯，他們較可能接受它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the reasoning that makes something make sense.","zh":"這個短語描述令某事合理的推理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the steps involved","meaning":"當中涉及的步驟","examples":[{"en":"They need to understand the steps involved in the change.","zh":"他們需要理解轉變中涉及的步驟。"},{"en":"The steps involved are the actions or stages needed to complete a process.","zh":"steps involved 指完成某過程所需的行動或階段。"},{"en":"Before applying to university, students should understand the steps involved, such as forms, deadlines, and interviews.","zh":"申請大學前，學生應理解當中涉及的步驟，例如表格、截止日期和面試。"},{"en":"Knowing the steps involved reduces fear because people can see what will happen next.","zh":"知道涉及步驟可以減少恐懼，因為人們看見下一步會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the practical stages of a process.","zh":"這個短語描述過程中的實際階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"soft-hearted","meaning":"心腸軟的；富同情心的","examples":[{"en":"The melancholic person is described as soft-hearted.","zh":"憂鬱質的人被描述為心腸軟。"},{"en":"Soft-hearted means kind, sympathetic, and easily moved by other people’s feelings.","zh":"soft-hearted 指善良、富同情心，並容易受別人感受打動。"},{"en":"A soft-hearted teacher may notice when a student is upset and offer quiet support.","zh":"心腸軟的老師可能注意到學生不開心，並安靜地提供支援。"},{"en":"Being soft-hearted can protect relationships, but it may make it hard to say no.","zh":"心腸軟可以保護關係，但也可能令人難以拒絕別人。"},{"en":"This word describes emotional kindness and sensitivity.","zh":"這個字描述情感上的善良和敏感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be oriented toward","meaning":"以……為導向","examples":[{"en":"Melancholic people are oriented toward doing things for others.","zh":"憂鬱質的人以為別人做事為導向。"},{"en":"To be oriented toward something means to be naturally directed toward or focused on it.","zh":"be oriented toward something 指自然地朝向或專注於某事。"},{"en":"A service team is oriented toward helping customers solve problems quickly.","zh":"服務團隊以幫助顧客快速解決問題為導向。"},{"en":"If someone is oriented toward people, they may notice feelings before tasks.","zh":"如果某人以人為導向，他可能先注意感受，再注意任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a main direction of attention or behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述注意力或行為的主要方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"doing things for others","meaning":"為別人做事","examples":[{"en":"They are oriented toward doing things for others.","zh":"他們以為別人做事為導向。"},{"en":"Doing things for others means helping people, supporting them, or meeting their needs.","zh":"doing things for others 指幫助別人、支援他們或滿足他們的需要。"},{"en":"A student may spend lunch doing things for others, such as helping classmates revise.","zh":"學生可能在午飯時間為別人做事，例如幫同學溫習。"},{"en":"Helping others builds trust, but it can become tiring if personal work is ignored.","zh":"幫助別人建立信任，但如果忽略自己的工作，可能變得疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical care shown through action.","zh":"這個短語描述透過行動表現的實際關懷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"considerate style of communication","meaning":"體貼型溝通風格","examples":[{"en":"The considerate style of communication focuses on people and relationships.","zh":"體貼型溝通風格專注於人和關係。"},{"en":"A considerate style of communication means speaking in a way that respects feelings, needs, and relationships.","zh":"considerate style of communication 指以尊重感受、需要和關係的方式說話。"},{"en":"A considerate manager asks whether the team has concerns before making a major change.","zh":"體貼型經理在作重大改變前，會詢問團隊是否有憂慮。"},{"en":"This style can reduce hurt feelings, but it may slow decisions if everyone must be consulted.","zh":"這種風格可以減少受傷感受，但如果每個人都要被諮詢，可能拖慢決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes caring and relationship-aware communication.","zh":"這個短語描述關懷並注意關係的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sympathetic communication style","meaning":"富同理心的溝通風格","examples":[{"en":"The sympathetic communication style is people-centred.","zh":"富同理心的溝通風格以人為中心。"},{"en":"A sympathetic communication style shows understanding of other people’s feelings and difficulties.","zh":"sympathetic communication style 顯示對別人感受和困難的理解。"},{"en":"A nurse uses a sympathetic style when she explains treatment gently to a worried patient.","zh":"護士溫和地向擔心的病人解釋治療時，就是使用富同理心的風格。"},{"en":"This style can build trust because people feel heard and respected.","zh":"這種風格可以建立信任，因為人們感到被聆聽和尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes communication with empathy and emotional care.","zh":"這個短語描述帶有同理心和情感關懷的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be focused on people and relationships","meaning":"專注於人和關係","examples":[{"en":"This style is focused on people and relationships.","zh":"這種風格專注於人和關係。"},{"en":"To be focused on people and relationships means to give most attention to feelings, trust, cooperation, and social harmony.","zh":"be focused on people and relationships 指把大部分注意力放在感受、信任、合作和社交和諧上。"},{"en":"A class monitor may focus on people and relationships by checking whether everyone feels included.","zh":"班長可能透過確認每個人是否被包括進來，專注於人和關係。"},{"en":"This focus can prevent hurt feelings, but the task still needs clear deadlines.","zh":"這種焦點可以防止感受受傷，但任務仍需要清晰截止日期。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a people-centred approach.","zh":"這個短語描述以人為中心的取向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"good listeners","meaning":"善於聆聽的人","examples":[{"en":"People with this communication style are often good listeners.","zh":"有這種溝通風格的人通常是善於聆聽的人。"},{"en":"Good listeners pay attention, let others finish, and try to understand before responding.","zh":"good listeners 會專心聽、讓別人說完，並在回應前嘗試理解。"},{"en":"A good listener in a group project notices when a quiet member wants to speak.","zh":"小組專案中的好聆聽者會注意到安靜成員想發言。"},{"en":"Listening well can reduce conflict because people feel respected.","zh":"善於聆聽可以減少衝突，因為人們感到被尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people who understand others through careful attention.","zh":"這個短語描述透過仔細注意來理解別人的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"to the detriment of","meaning":"損害了……；以犧牲……為代價","examples":[{"en":"They help others, sometimes to the detriment of their own work.","zh":"他們幫助別人，有時以犧牲自己工作為代價。"},{"en":"To the detriment of something means causing harm or disadvantage to it.","zh":"to the detriment of something 指對某事造成傷害或不利。"},{"en":"A student may help classmates too much, to the detriment of their own revision.","zh":"學生可能太多幫助同學，以致損害自己的溫習。"},{"en":"Helping others is good, but it becomes a problem when personal responsibilities suffer.","zh":"幫助別人是好事，但如果個人責任受損，就會變成問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one positive action may harm another important area.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個正面行動可能傷害另一個重要範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get things done for themselves","meaning":"為自己完成事情","examples":[{"en":"They may neglect getting things done for themselves.","zh":"他們可能忽略為自己完成事情。"},{"en":"To get things done for themselves means to complete their own tasks and responsibilities.","zh":"get things done for themselves 指完成自己的任務和責任。"},{"en":"A helpful student may forget to get things done for herself because she keeps helping classmates.","zh":"樂於助人的學生可能因一直幫同學，而忘記為自己完成事情。"},{"en":"If people never finish their own tasks, kindness can turn into stress and missed deadlines.","zh":"如果人們從不完成自己的任務，善意可以變成壓力和錯過截止日期。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking care of one’s own work.","zh":"這個短語描述照顧自己的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"solicit everyone’s opinion","meaning":"徵詢每個人的意見","examples":[{"en":"They want to solicit everyone’s opinion before making a decision.","zh":"他們想在作決定前徵詢每個人的意見。"},{"en":"To solicit everyone’s opinion means to actively ask all people involved what they think.","zh":"solicit everyone’s opinion 指主動詢問所有相關人士的想法。"},{"en":"A class chairperson may solicit everyone’s opinion before choosing a theme for the class party.","zh":"班主席在選擇班會派對主題前，可能徵詢每個人的意見。"},{"en":"Asking for opinions can increase fairness, but it may also take more time.","zh":"徵詢意見可以提高公平性，但也可能花更多時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes actively gathering views from all members.","zh":"這個短語描述主動收集所有成員的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make sure someone is comfortable with","meaning":"確保某人對……感到自在","examples":[{"en":"They want to make sure everyone is comfortable with the decision.","zh":"他們想確保每個人對決定感到自在。"},{"en":"To make sure someone is comfortable with something means to check that they accept it and do not feel worried or pressured.","zh":"make sure someone is comfortable with something 指確認某人接受某事，並不感到擔心或受壓。"},{"en":"A teacher may make sure students are comfortable with a group presentation before assigning roles.","zh":"老師在分配角色前，可能確保學生對小組匯報感到自在。"},{"en":"When people feel comfortable with a decision, they are more likely to support it.","zh":"當人們對決定感到自在，他們較可能支持它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes checking emotional acceptance.","zh":"這個短語描述確認情感上的接受程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"whatever is required","meaning":"所需的一切","examples":[{"en":"They want everyone to be comfortable with whatever is required.","zh":"他們希望每個人都對所需的一切感到自在。"},{"en":"Whatever is required means anything that is needed or expected in the situation.","zh":"whatever is required 指在該情況下所需或被期望的一切。"},{"en":"A new employee may ask questions to understand whatever is required in the first week.","zh":"新員工可能提出問題，以理解第一星期所需的一切。"},{"en":"If people do not understand what is required, they may feel anxious or unprepared.","zh":"如果人們不了解需要做甚麼，可能感到焦慮或未準備好。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to all necessary actions or conditions.","zh":"這個短語指所有必要行動或條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"distract from","meaning":"令人分心於；使人偏離……","examples":[{"en":"Their focus on others can distract from the task.","zh":"他們對別人的關注可能使人偏離任務。"},{"en":"To distract from something means to take attention away from it.","zh":"distract from something 指把注意力從某事移開。"},{"en":"Loud music can distract from homework even if the student enjoys it.","zh":"即使學生喜歡大聲音樂，它也可能令人分心於功課。"},{"en":"Caring for feelings is important, but too much discussion can distract from urgent work.","zh":"關心感受很重要，但太多討論可能使人偏離緊急工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attention being pulled away from the main focus.","zh":"這個短語描述注意力被拉離主要焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the task at hand","meaning":"手頭上的任務","examples":[{"en":"This focus on others can distract from the task at hand.","zh":"這種對別人的關注可能令人偏離手頭上的任務。"},{"en":"The task at hand is the work or problem that needs attention right now.","zh":"task at hand 指現在需要注意的工作或問題。"},{"en":"During an exam, the task at hand is answering the question, not worrying about yesterday’s mistake.","zh":"考試期間，手頭上的任務是回答問題，而不是擔心昨天的錯誤。"},{"en":"If people forget the task at hand, they may spend time on side issues.","zh":"如果人們忘記手頭上的任務，可能把時間花在旁枝問題上。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the immediate job that must be dealt with.","zh":"這個短語指必須處理的當前工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the needs of others","meaning":"別人的需要","examples":[{"en":"They are deeply concerned with the needs of others.","zh":"他們非常關心別人的需要。"},{"en":"The needs of others are what other people require physically, emotionally, or practically.","zh":"needs of others 指其他人在身體、情感或實際上需要的東西。"},{"en":"A good nurse notices the needs of others, such as pain, fear, or confusion.","zh":"好護士會注意別人的需要，例如痛楚、恐懼或困惑。"},{"en":"Caring about others’ needs can build trust, but personal limits are also important.","zh":"關心別人的需要可以建立信任，但個人界線也重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attention to what other people require.","zh":"這個短語描述對別人所需事物的注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"smooth over issues","meaning":"緩和問題；平息分歧","examples":[{"en":"They often try to smooth over issues within the team.","zh":"他們經常嘗試緩和團隊內的問題。"},{"en":"To smooth over issues means to reduce tension or make a problem seem less serious so people can continue working together.","zh":"smooth over issues 指減少緊張或令問題看起來較不嚴重，使人們能繼續合作。"},{"en":"A class monitor may smooth over an argument by helping both sides apologise.","zh":"班長可能透過幫助雙方道歉來平息爭執。"},{"en":"Smoothing things over can protect relationships, but serious problems still need honest discussion.","zh":"緩和問題可以保護關係，但嚴重問題仍需要誠實討論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes calming conflict rather than fully analysing it.","zh":"這個短語描述平息衝突，而不是完全分析它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"threaten the status quo","meaning":"威脅現狀","examples":[{"en":"They believe that change threatens the status quo.","zh":"他們相信轉變會威脅現狀。"},{"en":"To threaten the status quo means to challenge the existing situation or usual way of doing things.","zh":"threaten the status quo 指挑戰現有情況或慣常做法。"},{"en":"A new school rule may threaten the status quo if students are used to more freedom.","zh":"如果學生習慣較多自由，新校規可能威脅現狀。"},{"en":"People may resist change when they feel their routines or roles are being threatened.","zh":"當人覺得自己的常規或角色受到威脅，可能會抗拒改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes change as a challenge to what already exists.","zh":"這個短語把改變描述為對既有狀態的挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"feel uneasy","meaning":"感到不安","examples":[{"en":"Change tends to make people feel uneasy.","zh":"轉變往往令人感到不安。"},{"en":"To feel uneasy means to feel uncomfortable, worried, or not fully safe.","zh":"feel uneasy 指感到不舒服、擔心或不完全安心。"},{"en":"A student may feel uneasy on the first day at a new school.","zh":"學生在新學校第一天可能感到不安。"},{"en":"People often feel uneasy when they do not know what will happen next.","zh":"當人不知道接下來會發生甚麼，通常會感到不安。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mild anxiety or discomfort.","zh":"這個短語描述輕微焦慮或不舒服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"consider the changes","meaning":"考慮轉變","examples":[{"en":"They need time to consider the changes before adapting.","zh":"他們需要時間在適應前考慮轉變。"},{"en":"To consider the changes means to think carefully about what is different and what it will affect.","zh":"consider the changes 指仔細思考有甚麼不同，以及它會影響甚麼。"},{"en":"Staff may need a meeting to consider the changes before a new work schedule begins.","zh":"新工作時間表開始前，員工可能需要開會考慮轉變。"},{"en":"Thinking through changes can reduce fear and prevent careless mistakes.","zh":"仔細思考轉變可以減少恐懼並防止粗心錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful reflection before response.","zh":"這個短語描述回應前的仔細反思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in order to adapt to","meaning":"為了適應……","examples":[{"en":"They need time in order to adapt to change.","zh":"他們需要時間，為了適應轉變。"},{"en":"In order to adapt to something means so that a person can adjust to a new situation.","zh":"in order to adapt to something 指為了讓人能調整至新情況。"},{"en":"Students may need extra guidance in order to adapt to online learning.","zh":"學生可能需要額外指引，為了適應網上學習。"},{"en":"People adapt better when they understand the reason, steps, and support available.","zh":"當人們理解原因、步驟和可用支援，他們會適應得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose of time, help, or preparation.","zh":"這個短語解釋時間、幫助或準備的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"bold style of communication","meaning":"大膽果斷的溝通風格","examples":[{"en":"The choleric temperament translates into the bold style of communication.","zh":"膽汁質氣質轉化為大膽果斷的溝通風格。"},{"en":"A bold style of communication is confident, strong, and willing to speak directly.","zh":"bold style of communication 指有信心、強而有力，並願意直接說話。"},{"en":"A bold team leader may say clearly, “This deadline will not work unless we change the plan.”","zh":"大膽果斷的團隊領袖可能清楚說：「除非我們改變計劃，否則這個截止日期不可行。」"},{"en":"This style can speed up decisions, but it may make some people feel pressured.","zh":"這種風格可以加快決定，但也可能令有些人感到受壓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes communication that is confident and forceful.","zh":"這個短語描述有信心且有力量的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"direct style of communication","meaning":"直接型溝通風格","examples":[{"en":"People with a direct style of communication use fewer words.","zh":"具有直接型溝通風格的人使用較少字句。"},{"en":"A direct style of communication means speaking clearly, briefly, and without hiding the main point.","zh":"direct style of communication 指清楚、簡短並不隱藏重點地說話。"},{"en":"A direct manager may say, “We need the report by Friday,” instead of giving a long explanation first.","zh":"直接型經理可能說：「我們星期五前需要報告」，而不是先作長篇解釋。"},{"en":"Direct communication can save time, but it may sound harsh if tone is not careful.","zh":"直接溝通可以節省時間，但如果語氣不小心，可能聽起來嚴厲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes straightforward communication.","zh":"這個短語描述直截了當的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be brief in","meaning":"在……方面簡短直接","examples":[{"en":"They are brief in their communication.","zh":"他們在溝通方面簡短直接。"},{"en":"To be brief in communication means to use few words and get to the point quickly.","zh":"be brief in communication 指使用較少字句並快速說到重點。"},{"en":"A busy doctor may be brief in instructions but still give the key information clearly.","zh":"忙碌醫生在指示方面可能簡短直接，但仍清楚給出關鍵資料。"},{"en":"Being brief can save time, but it may feel cold if no warmth is shown.","zh":"簡短可以省時間，但如果沒有溫度，可能令人感到冷淡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes short and direct expression.","zh":"這個短語描述短而直接的表達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the fewer words, the better","meaning":"說話越少越好","examples":[{"en":"For direct communicators, the fewer words, the better.","zh":"對直接型溝通者而言，說話越少越好。"},{"en":"The fewer words, the better means short and clear communication is preferred.","zh":"the fewer words, the better 指較喜歡短而清楚的溝通。"},{"en":"In an emergency, the fewer words, the better because people need instructions quickly.","zh":"在緊急情況下，說話越少越好，因為人們需要快速指示。"},{"en":"This approach can help efficiency, but it may not suit sensitive conversations.","zh":"這種取向可以提高效率，但未必適合敏感對話。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a preference for concise speech.","zh":"這個短語表達對簡潔說話的偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"big-picture thinkers","meaning":"著眼大局的人","examples":[{"en":"People with this style are big-picture thinkers.","zh":"具有這種風格的人是著眼大局的人。"},{"en":"Big-picture thinkers focus on overall goals, direction, and outcomes rather than small details first.","zh":"big-picture thinkers 先專注於整體目標、方向和成果，而不是小細節。"},{"en":"A school principal is often a big-picture thinker when planning the school’s future development.","zh":"校長規劃學校未來發展時，通常是著眼大局的人。"},{"en":"Big-picture thinkers can set direction, but they may need detail-focused people to plan the steps.","zh":"著眼大局的人可以設定方向，但可能需要重細節的人規劃步驟。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people who see the whole situation.","zh":"這個短語描述看見整體情況的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be involved in many things at once","meaning":"同時參與很多事情","examples":[{"en":"They love to be involved in many things at once.","zh":"他們喜歡同時參與很多事情。"},{"en":"To be involved in many things at once means to take part in several activities or projects at the same time.","zh":"be involved in many things at once 指同時參加幾項活動或項目。"},{"en":"A student council leader may be involved in many things at once, from meetings to charity events.","zh":"學生會領袖可能同時參與很多事情，由會議到慈善活動都有。"},{"en":"This can create energy and variety, but it may also lead to missed details or overwork.","zh":"這可以帶來能量和多樣性，但也可能導致忽略細節或過勞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes handling multiple commitments simultaneously.","zh":"這個短語描述同時處理多項承擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tasks and outcomes","meaning":"任務和成果","examples":[{"en":"They are focused on tasks and outcomes.","zh":"他們專注於任務和成果。"},{"en":"Tasks and outcomes are the work that must be done and the results that should be achieved.","zh":"tasks and outcomes 指必須完成的工作和應達成的結果。"},{"en":"A project manager thinks about tasks and outcomes when assigning duties and checking deadlines.","zh":"專案經理分配職責和檢查截止日期時，會考慮任務和成果。"},{"en":"Focusing on outcomes helps a team know what success should look like.","zh":"專注成果幫助團隊知道成功應是甚麼樣子。"},{"en":"This phrase combines action with results.","zh":"這個短語結合行動與結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"carry out tasks","meaning":"執行任務","examples":[{"en":"They may forget that people carrying out tasks have needs.","zh":"他們可能忘記執行任務的人也有需要。"},{"en":"To carry out tasks means to perform or complete pieces of work.","zh":"carry out tasks 指進行或完成工作項目。"},{"en":"Hospital staff carry out tasks such as checking patients, giving medicine, and updating records.","zh":"醫院職員執行檢查病人、派藥和更新紀錄等任務。"},{"en":"People who carry out tasks need time, tools, and support to do them well.","zh":"執行任務的人需要時間、工具和支援才能做好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doing practical work.","zh":"這個短語描述進行實務工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"detail work","meaning":"細節工作","examples":[{"en":"They do not do detail work easily.","zh":"他們不容易做細節工作。"},{"en":"Detail work is work that requires careful attention to small facts, steps, or errors.","zh":"detail work 指需要仔細注意小事實、步驟或錯誤的工作。"},{"en":"Proofreading a legal contract is detail work because every word matters.","zh":"校對法律合約是細節工作，因為每個字都重要。"},{"en":"People who dislike detail work may need checklists or partners who enjoy accuracy.","zh":"不喜歡細節工作的人可能需要清單，或需要喜歡準確的伙伴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful small-scale work.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細的小範圍工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, they may underestimate the time needed.","zh":"因此，他們可能低估所需時間。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what was just mentioned, this consequence happens.","zh":"as a result 指由於剛才提到的事情，所以出現這個結果。"},{"en":"The train was delayed; as a result, many students arrived late for class.","zh":"火車延誤；因此，許多學生上課遲到。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links a cause to an effect.","zh":"這個短語清楚把原因連到結果。"},{"en":"It is useful for explaining consequences in writing.","zh":"它適合在寫作中解釋後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"underestimate how much time","meaning":"低估需要多少時間","examples":[{"en":"They often underestimate how much time it takes to complete a task.","zh":"他們常低估完成任務需要多少時間。"},{"en":"To underestimate how much time something takes means to think it will take less time than it really does.","zh":"underestimate how much time something takes 指以為某事所需時間比實際少。"},{"en":"A student may underestimate how much time an essay needs and start too late.","zh":"學生可能低估作文需要多少時間，然後太遲開始。"},{"en":"Underestimating time can lead to stress, missed deadlines, and lower-quality work.","zh":"低估時間可以導致壓力、錯過截止日期和較低質素工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes judging the required time too low.","zh":"這個短語描述把所需時間估得太少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"achieve the task","meaning":"完成任務","examples":[{"en":"They may underestimate how much time it takes to achieve the task.","zh":"他們可能低估完成任務需要多少時間。"},{"en":"To achieve the task means to complete the task successfully and reach the intended result.","zh":"achieve the task 指成功完成任務並達到預期結果。"},{"en":"A team can achieve the task if everyone understands their role and deadline.","zh":"如果每個人都理解自己的角色和截止日期，團隊就能完成任務。"},{"en":"Achieving a task often requires both planning and follow-through.","zh":"完成任務通常需要規劃和真正跟進。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on successful completion, not simply starting the work.","zh":"這個短語集中於成功完成，而不只是開始工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"seem forceful","meaning":"顯得強勢","examples":[{"en":"Because they are direct, they often seem forceful.","zh":"因為他們直接，所以經常顯得強勢。"},{"en":"To seem forceful means to appear strong, firm, or possibly too pushy.","zh":"seem forceful 指看起來強硬、堅決，或可能太有壓迫感。"},{"en":"A teacher may seem forceful when giving urgent safety instructions during a fire drill.","zh":"老師在火警演習中給出緊急安全指示時，可能顯得強勢。"},{"en":"Direct language can seem forceful if the listener expects a softer tone.","zh":"如果聽者期待較柔和語氣，直接語言可能顯得強勢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how behaviour appears to others.","zh":"這個短語描述行為在別人眼中看起來如何。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be intimidating to others","meaning":"令別人感到畏懼","examples":[{"en":"Direct communicators can be intimidating to others.","zh":"直接型溝通者可能令別人感到畏懼。"},{"en":"To be intimidating to others means to make other people feel nervous, pressured, or afraid to speak.","zh":"be intimidating to others 指令其他人感到緊張、受壓或不敢說話。"},{"en":"A very strict manager may be intimidating to new employees.","zh":"非常嚴格的經理可能令新員工感到畏懼。"},{"en":"If someone seems intimidating, quieter team members may hide useful concerns.","zh":"如果某人顯得令人畏懼，較安靜的團隊成員可能隱藏有用憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the effect of strong behaviour on other people.","zh":"這個短語描述強勢行為對別人的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"welcome someone challenging them","meaning":"歡迎別人挑戰自己","examples":[{"en":"They would usually welcome someone challenging them.","zh":"他們通常會歡迎別人挑戰自己。"},{"en":"To welcome someone challenging them means to accept or even enjoy another person questioning their idea or decision.","zh":"welcome someone challenging them 指接受甚至喜歡別人質疑自己的想法或決定。"},{"en":"A confident debate coach may welcome students challenging his argument.","zh":"有信心的辯論教練可能歡迎學生挑戰他的論點。"},{"en":"People who welcome challenge may see disagreement as useful rather than disrespectful.","zh":"歡迎挑戰的人可能把分歧視為有用，而不是不尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes openness to being questioned.","zh":"這個短語描述對被質疑持開放態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be afraid to do so","meaning":"不敢這樣做","examples":[{"en":"Most other styles are afraid to do so.","zh":"大多數其他風格都不敢這樣做。"},{"en":"To be afraid to do so means to feel nervous or unwilling to take that action.","zh":"be afraid to do so 指感到緊張或不願採取該行動。"},{"en":"Some students are afraid to ask questions because they worry classmates will laugh.","zh":"有些學生不敢提問，因為擔心同學會笑。"},{"en":"If people are afraid to challenge a manager, important problems may remain hidden.","zh":"如果人們不敢挑戰經理，重要問題可能被隱藏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fear that stops action.","zh":"這個短語描述阻止行動的恐懼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"thrive on change","meaning":"在轉變中表現得更好；喜歡變化","examples":[{"en":"People with this style often thrive on change.","zh":"具有這種風格的人通常在轉變中表現得更好。"},{"en":"To thrive on change means to do well, feel energised, or become more effective when things are changing.","zh":"thrive on change 指在事情改變時表現良好、感到有能量或變得更有效。"},{"en":"An entrepreneur may thrive on change because new problems create new opportunities.","zh":"企業家可能喜歡變化，因為新問題創造新機會。"},{"en":"People who thrive on change may become bored when work is too predictable.","zh":"在轉變中表現更好的人，可能在工作太可預測時感到沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone who performs better in changing situations.","zh":"這個短語描述在變動情況中表現更好的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the more, the better","meaning":"越多越好","examples":[{"en":"For them, the more change there is, the better.","zh":"對他們而言，轉變越多越好。"},{"en":"The more, the better means a larger amount is preferred.","zh":"the more, the better 指較大的數量更受歡迎。"},{"en":"For some students, the more practice examples there are, the better they understand the grammar.","zh":"對有些學生而言，練習例子越多，他們越能理解文法。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that someone welcomes quantity rather than fearing it.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人歡迎數量，而不是害怕它。"},{"en":"It can sound enthusiastic, but it may not suit people who prefer stability.","zh":"它可以聽起來很熱情，但未必適合喜歡穩定的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a well-functioning team","meaning":"運作良好的團隊","examples":[{"en":"A well-functioning team should include different communication styles.","zh":"運作良好的團隊應包括不同溝通風格。"},{"en":"A well-functioning team is a group that works smoothly, communicates clearly, and reaches goals effectively.","zh":"well-functioning team 指運作順暢、溝通清晰並有效達成目標的群體。"},{"en":"A school project group becomes well-functioning when members share tasks and solve problems early.","zh":"當成員分工並及早解決問題，學校專案小組就會變成運作良好的團隊。"},{"en":"Teams function well when they balance relationships, details, speed, and big-picture thinking.","zh":"團隊在平衡關係、細節、速度和大局思考時，會運作良好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a team that works properly and productively.","zh":"這個短語描述正常而有生產力地工作的團隊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"truly effective","meaning":"真正有效","examples":[{"en":"A team needs different styles to be truly effective.","zh":"團隊需要不同風格才會真正有效。"},{"en":"Truly effective means genuinely successful in producing the intended result.","zh":"truly effective 指真正成功產生預期結果。"},{"en":"A study plan is truly effective if students can use what they learn, not just feel busy.","zh":"如果學生能運用所學，而不只是感到忙碌，學習計劃才真正有效。"},{"en":"A team becomes truly effective when it handles both tasks and relationships well.","zh":"當團隊能妥善處理任務和關係，它就真正有效。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses real usefulness, not just appearance.","zh":"這個短語強調真正有用，而不只是表面上好看。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take care of relationships","meaning":"照顧關係","examples":[{"en":"Teams need to take care of relationships as well as tasks.","zh":"團隊需要照顧關係，也需要照顧任務。"},{"en":"To take care of relationships means to protect trust, respect, and communication between people.","zh":"take care of relationships 指保護人與人之間的信任、尊重和溝通。"},{"en":"A manager takes care of relationships by listening to complaints before they become serious.","zh":"經理在投訴變嚴重前聆聽它們，就是在照顧關係。"},{"en":"If relationships are ignored, task completion may become harder because people stop cooperating.","zh":"如果關係被忽略，任務完成可能變得更困難，因為人們停止合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes actively maintaining human connections.","zh":"這個短語描述主動維持人際連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in order to achieve","meaning":"為了達成……","examples":[{"en":"They need to manage relationships in order to achieve their tasks.","zh":"他們需要管理關係，為了達成任務。"},{"en":"In order to achieve something means so that a goal can be reached successfully.","zh":"in order to achieve something 指為了成功達到某目標。"},{"en":"Students must manage their time well in order to achieve strong exam results.","zh":"學生必須好好管理時間，為了取得好考試成績。"},{"en":"If the goal is teamwork, people may need to communicate respectfully in order to achieve it.","zh":"如果目標是團隊合作，人們可能需要尊重地溝通，為了達成它。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose behind an action.","zh":"這個短語解釋行動背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"big-picture perspective","meaning":"大局視角","examples":[{"en":"Teams need the big-picture perspective as well as the details.","zh":"團隊既需要細節，也需要大局視角。"},{"en":"A big-picture perspective is a view of the overall goal, context, and direction.","zh":"big-picture perspective 指看見整體目標、背景和方向的視角。"},{"en":"A principal needs a big-picture perspective when deciding how a school should develop over five years.","zh":"校長決定學校五年發展方向時，需要大局視角。"},{"en":"Without a big-picture perspective, people may finish small tasks but miss the main purpose.","zh":"沒有大局視角，人們可能完成小任務，卻錯過主要目的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes seeing the whole situation.","zh":"這個短語描述看見整體情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the context of their work","meaning":"工作背景","examples":[{"en":"Teams need to understand the context of their work.","zh":"團隊需要理解自己的工作背景。"},{"en":"The context of their work is the situation, purpose, people, limits, and background surrounding what they do.","zh":"context of their work 指圍繞他們工作的情況、目的、人員、限制和背景。"},{"en":"A hospital team must understand the context of their work, including patient safety and limited time.","zh":"醫院團隊必須理解工作背景，包括病人安全和時間有限。"},{"en":"Understanding context helps people choose the right method, tone, and priority.","zh":"理解背景幫助人選擇正確方法、語氣和優先次序。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the wider situation that gives work meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述賦予工作意義的更廣泛情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be identified and addressed","meaning":"被識別並處理","examples":[{"en":"The details need to be identified and addressed.","zh":"細節需要被識別並處理。"},{"en":"To be identified and addressed means to be noticed clearly and then dealt with properly.","zh":"be identified and addressed 指被清楚發現，然後被妥善處理。"},{"en":"In a school safety plan, risks must be identified and addressed before an accident happens.","zh":"在學校安全計劃中，風險必須在意外發生前被識別並處理。"},{"en":"Problems that are identified but not addressed may continue to cause trouble.","zh":"被識別但沒有被處理的問題，可能繼續造成麻煩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finding an issue and taking action on it.","zh":"這個短語描述找出問題並採取行動處理它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"if the team is to succeed","meaning":"如果團隊要成功","examples":[{"en":"The details must be addressed if the team is to succeed.","zh":"如果團隊要成功，細節就必須被處理。"},{"en":"If the team is to succeed means if the team is going to achieve its goal.","zh":"if the team is to succeed 指如果團隊將要達成目標。"},{"en":"If the class project is to succeed, everyone must know their role before the deadline.","zh":"如果班級專案要成功，每個人必須在截止日期前知道自己的角色。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a necessary condition for success.","zh":"這個短語引出成功所需的必要條件。"},{"en":"It is often used to show what must happen first.","zh":"它常用來顯示甚麼事情必須先發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have aspects of","meaning":"具有……的某些方面","examples":[{"en":"We all have aspects of each communication style within us.","zh":"我們每個人內心都有每種溝通風格的某些方面。"},{"en":"To have aspects of something means to contain some features or parts of it.","zh":"have aspects of something 指包含某事的一些特徵或部分。"},{"en":"A quiet student may still have aspects of a bold communicator when discussing a topic they love.","zh":"安靜學生在討論自己喜歡的題目時，仍可能具有大膽溝通者的某些方面。"},{"en":"People are complex, so one label rarely describes every part of them.","zh":"人是複雜的，所以單一標籤很少能描述所有部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes partial features rather than a complete identity.","zh":"這個短語描述部分特徵，而不是完整身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"move from one style to another","meaning":"從一種風格轉到另一種風格","examples":[{"en":"Some people can easily move from one style to another.","zh":"有些人可以輕易從一種風格轉到另一種風格。"},{"en":"To move from one style to another means to change the way one communicates according to the situation.","zh":"move from one style to another 指根據情況改變溝通方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may move from a warm style with nervous students to a direct style during an emergency.","zh":"老師面對緊張學生時可能用溫暖風格，在緊急情況中則轉到直接風格。"},{"en":"Moving between styles helps people respond to different needs more effectively.","zh":"在風格之間轉換幫助人更有效回應不同需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes flexible communication.","zh":"這個短語描述靈活溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"adapt our style to","meaning":"使我們的風格適應……","examples":[{"en":"We can adapt our style to the needs of the situation.","zh":"我們可以使自己的風格適應情況的需要。"},{"en":"To adapt our style to something means to change our usual way of communicating so it fits that need.","zh":"adapt our style to something 指改變我們慣常的溝通方式，使其配合某需要。"},{"en":"A manager may adapt her style to a new employee by giving clearer and gentler explanations.","zh":"經理可能透過給出更清楚和更溫和的解釋，讓自己的風格適應新員工。"},{"en":"Adapting style can reduce misunderstanding because different situations need different approaches.","zh":"調整風格可以減少誤解，因為不同情況需要不同方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing communication to fit context.","zh":"這個短語描述改變溝通以配合語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the situation at hand","meaning":"當前的情況","examples":[{"en":"Some people adapt their style to the situation at hand.","zh":"有些人會讓自己的風格適應當前的情況。"},{"en":"The situation at hand is the current situation that needs attention now.","zh":"situation at hand 指現在需要注意的當前情況。"},{"en":"In a fire drill, the situation at hand requires clear instructions, not long discussion.","zh":"在火警演習中，當前情況需要清晰指示，而不是長篇討論。"},{"en":"Understanding the current situation helps people choose the right tone and response.","zh":"理解當前情況幫助人選擇正確語氣和回應。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the immediate circumstances.","zh":"這個短語指眼前的情境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"whether the focus is on","meaning":"無論重點在於……","examples":[{"en":"We may adapt our style whether the focus is on tasks or relationships.","zh":"無論重點在於任務還是關係，我們都可能調整風格。"},{"en":"Whether the focus is on something means regardless of which main area needs attention.","zh":"whether the focus is on something 指不論主要注意力放在哪個範疇。"},{"en":"A teacher may change methods whether the focus is on exam skills or student confidence.","zh":"無論重點在於考試技巧還是學生信心，老師都可能改變方法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces two possible centres of attention.","zh":"這個短語引出兩個可能的注意中心。"},{"en":"It helps show that adaptation depends on what matters most at the moment.","zh":"它幫助顯示調整取決於當下最重要的是甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a dominant style","meaning":"主導風格","examples":[{"en":"For some people, a dominant style is very evident.","zh":"對有些人而言，主導風格非常明顯。"},{"en":"A dominant style is the communication style that appears most often or most strongly in a person.","zh":"dominant style 指一個人最常出現或最強烈的溝通風格。"},{"en":"A student with a dominant direct style may give short answers even in friendly discussions.","zh":"具有直接型主導風格的學生，即使在友善討論中也可能給出簡短答案。"},{"en":"A dominant style can shape how others experience working with that person.","zh":"主導風格可以塑造別人與該人合作時的感受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main style that stands out.","zh":"這個短語描述最突出的主要風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be very evident","meaning":"非常明顯","examples":[{"en":"A dominant communication style can be very evident.","zh":"主導溝通風格可以非常明顯。"},{"en":"To be very evident means to be clearly noticeable or easy to see.","zh":"be very evident 指清楚可見或容易看出。"},{"en":"A student’s nervousness may be very evident if their voice shakes during a presentation.","zh":"如果學生匯報時聲音顫抖，他的緊張可能非常明顯。"},{"en":"When a style is very evident, others quickly notice it in meetings or conversations.","zh":"當一種風格非常明顯，別人在會議或對話中很快注意到它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something obvious.","zh":"這個短語描述明顯的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"from the perspective of","meaning":"從……的角度","examples":[{"en":"It can be difficult to see the situation from the perspective of another style.","zh":"從另一種風格的角度看情況可能很困難。"},{"en":"From the perspective of someone or something means from that point of view.","zh":"from the perspective of someone or something 指從某人或某事的觀點看。"},{"en":"From the perspective of a new student, the school rules may feel confusing.","zh":"從新生的角度看，校規可能令人困惑。"},{"en":"Seeing from another perspective helps reduce unfair judgement.","zh":"從另一角度看事情有助減少不公平判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes looking at a situation through another viewpoint.","zh":"這個短語描述透過另一觀點看情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the work environment","meaning":"工作環境","examples":[{"en":"The work environment can influence communication styles.","zh":"工作環境可以影響溝通風格。"},{"en":"The work environment is the physical, social, and organisational setting in which people do their jobs.","zh":"work environment 指人們工作的實體、社交和組織環境。"},{"en":"A quiet office and a busy restaurant create very different work environments.","zh":"安靜辦公室和繁忙餐廳會創造非常不同的工作環境。"},{"en":"If the work environment is stressful, people may communicate more quickly and less warmly.","zh":"如果工作環境有壓力，人們可能溝通得更快但較不溫暖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the setting that shapes workplace behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述塑造職場行為的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the type of work that is required","meaning":"所需的工作類型","examples":[{"en":"Communication style can be influenced by the type of work that is required.","zh":"溝通風格可以受所需的工作類型影響。"},{"en":"The type of work that is required means the kind of task people must do in that job or situation.","zh":"type of work that is required 指人們在該工作或情況中必須做的任務種類。"},{"en":"Emergency medical work requires faster and more direct communication than a relaxed planning meeting.","zh":"緊急醫療工作比輕鬆規劃會議更需要快速和直接溝通。"},{"en":"Different work demands can reward different communication styles.","zh":"不同工作要求可以鼓勵不同溝通風格。"},{"en":"This phrase links job requirements with behaviour.","zh":"這個短語把工作要求與行為連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the predominance of","meaning":"……佔主導地位","examples":[{"en":"The predominance of one style may shape the work environment.","zh":"一種風格佔主導地位可能塑造工作環境。"},{"en":"The predominance of something means that it is the strongest, most common, or most influential element.","zh":"predominance of something 指某事物是最強、最常見或最有影響力的元素。"},{"en":"The predominance of exam practice in a school may leave little time for creative projects.","zh":"如果學校中考試練習佔主導地位，創意專案可能沒有多少時間。"},{"en":"If one communication style predominates, other styles may feel less valued.","zh":"如果一種溝通風格佔主導，其他風格可能感到較不被重視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one thing having the greatest presence or influence.","zh":"這個短語描述某事物具有最大存在感或影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be reflected in","meaning":"反映在……之中","examples":[{"en":"One communication style may be reflected in the work environment.","zh":"一種溝通風格可能反映在工作環境之中。"},{"en":"To be reflected in something means to be shown or expressed through it.","zh":"be reflected in something 指透過某事顯示或表達出來。"},{"en":"A school’s values may be reflected in how teachers speak to students.","zh":"學校的價值觀可能反映在老師如何與學生說話之中。"},{"en":"If a workplace values speed, this may be reflected in short meetings and direct emails.","zh":"如果工作場所重視速度，這可能反映在短會議和直接電郵之中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how an idea or pattern appears in visible form.","zh":"這個短語描述想法或模式如何以可見形式出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"at work and at home","meaning":"在工作和在家中","examples":[{"en":"Some people use one style at work and another at home.","zh":"有些人在工作中使用一種風格，在家中使用另一種風格。"},{"en":"At work and at home means in the workplace and in one’s private family life.","zh":"at work and at home 指在工作場所和私人家庭生活中。"},{"en":"A person may be direct at work but gentle at home with children.","zh":"一個人可能在工作中直接，但在家中對孩子溫和。"},{"en":"Different settings can bring out different communication habits.","zh":"不同環境可以引出不同溝通習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts professional and personal environments.","zh":"這個短語對比專業和個人環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the ability to develop flexibility","meaning":"培養靈活性的能力","examples":[{"en":"We have the ability to develop flexibility in our communication styles.","zh":"我們有能力在自己的溝通風格中培養靈活性。"},{"en":"The ability to develop flexibility means people can learn to adjust their behaviour more easily over time.","zh":"ability to develop flexibility 指人們可以隨時間學會更容易調整行為。"},{"en":"A student can develop flexibility by learning to speak differently to friends, teachers, and customers.","zh":"學生可以透過學習以不同方式與朋友、老師和顧客說話來培養靈活性。"},{"en":"Flexibility grows when people practise noticing what each situation needs.","zh":"當人們練習注意每個情況需要甚麼，靈活性就會增長。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that communication style can improve through effort.","zh":"這個短語強調溝通風格可以透過努力改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"develop flexibility","meaning":"培養靈活性","examples":[{"en":"People can develop flexibility in their communication styles.","zh":"人們可以在溝通風格中培養靈活性。"},{"en":"To develop flexibility means to become better at adjusting to different situations or people.","zh":"develop flexibility 指變得更善於適應不同情況或不同人。"},{"en":"A teacher develops flexibility when she uses games for younger students and discussion for older ones.","zh":"老師為年幼學生使用遊戲，為較年長學生使用討論，就是在培養靈活性。"},{"en":"Flexibility helps people avoid using the same method in every situation.","zh":"靈活性幫助人避免在每種情況中都使用同一方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes building the ability to adapt.","zh":"這個短語描述建立適應能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the greater…, the more…","meaning":"越……就越……","examples":[{"en":"The greater the flexibility we have, the more skilled we usually are at handling conflict.","zh":"我們的靈活性越大，通常就越善於處理衝突。"},{"en":"The greater…, the more… is a structure showing that when one thing increases, another thing also increases.","zh":"the greater…, the more… 是一種結構，表示一件事增加時，另一件事也增加。"},{"en":"The more students read, the wider their vocabulary usually becomes.","zh":"學生閱讀越多，詞彙通常就越廣。"},{"en":"This structure is useful for showing a clear relationship between two changes.","zh":"這個結構有助顯示兩種變化之間的清晰關係。"},{"en":"It often helps express cause and result in a concise way.","zh":"它常有助簡潔表達原因和結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be skilled at handling","meaning":"善於處理……","examples":[{"en":"Flexible communicators are usually skilled at handling conflict.","zh":"靈活的溝通者通常善於處理衝突。"},{"en":"To be skilled at handling something means to be good at managing or dealing with it.","zh":"be skilled at handling something 指善於管理或處理某事。"},{"en":"A nurse is skilled at handling worried patients if she can calm them while explaining clearly.","zh":"如果護士能安撫擔心的病人並清楚解釋，就是善於處理焦慮病人。"},{"en":"People become skilled at handling conflict through practice, reflection, and listening.","zh":"人們透過練習、反思和聆聽，會變得善於處理衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical ability in dealing with a situation.","zh":"這個短語描述處理某情況的實用能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"possible and actual conflicts","meaning":"潛在和實際的衝突","examples":[{"en":"Flexibility helps people handle possible and actual conflicts.","zh":"靈活性幫助人處理潛在和實際的衝突。"},{"en":"Possible and actual conflicts are conflicts that may happen and conflicts that are already happening.","zh":"possible and actual conflicts 指可能發生的衝突，以及已經正在發生的衝突。"},{"en":"A manager can prevent possible conflicts by explaining changes early.","zh":"經理可以透過及早解釋改變來預防潛在衝突。"},{"en":"Actual conflicts need direct attention because people are already disagreeing or hurt.","zh":"實際衝突需要直接關注，因為人們已經有分歧或受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both future risks and present problems.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋未來風險和當前問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be relevant to","meaning":"與……有關；對……有意義","examples":[{"en":"Changing our communication style usually has to be relevant to us.","zh":"改變我們的溝通風格通常必須與我們有關。"},{"en":"To be relevant to someone means to matter to them or connect with their needs, goals, or situation.","zh":"be relevant to someone 指對某人重要，或與其需要、目標或情況有連繫。"},{"en":"Exam tips are more relevant to students when they match the paper they are taking.","zh":"當考試技巧配合學生正在應考的試卷，它們對學生就更有意義。"},{"en":"If advice is not relevant, people are less likely to use it.","zh":"如果建議沒有相關性，人們較不可能使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a meaningful connection.","zh":"這個短語描述有意義的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"incentives in our environment","meaning":"環境中的誘因","examples":[{"en":"There may be incentives in our environment to encourage flexibility.","zh":"我們的環境中可能有誘因鼓勵靈活性。"},{"en":"Incentives in our environment are rewards, pressures, or conditions around us that encourage certain behaviour.","zh":"incentives in our environment 指我們周圍鼓勵某種行為的獎勵、壓力或條件。"},{"en":"A workplace that praises teamwork creates incentives for employees to communicate more respectfully.","zh":"表揚團隊合作的工作場所，會創造誘因讓員工更尊重地溝通。"},{"en":"If the environment rewards only speed, people may have little incentive to listen carefully.","zh":"如果環境只獎勵速度，人們可能沒有多少誘因仔細聆聽。"},{"en":"This phrase describes outside factors that push behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述推動行為的外在因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"encourage someone to","meaning":"鼓勵某人去……","examples":[{"en":"Some environments encourage people to become more flexible.","zh":"有些環境鼓勵人變得更靈活。"},{"en":"To encourage someone to do something means to support, motivate, or make them more willing to do it.","zh":"encourage someone to do something 指支持、推動或令某人更願意做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher can encourage students to speak by praising effort rather than laughing at mistakes.","zh":"老師可以透過讚賞努力而不是取笑錯誤，鼓勵學生開口說話。"},{"en":"Encouragement can change behaviour because people feel safer trying something new.","zh":"鼓勵可以改變行為，因為人們在嘗試新事物時感到更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving support that leads to action.","zh":"這個短語描述給予支援並促成行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the key is that","meaning":"關鍵在於","examples":[{"en":"The key is that we have to want to become flexible.","zh":"關鍵在於我們必須想變得靈活。"},{"en":"The key is that means the most important point is this.","zh":"the key is that 指最重要的一點是這個。"},{"en":"The key is that students must understand the question before writing the answer.","zh":"關鍵在於學生寫答案前必須理解題目。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the central idea in an explanation.","zh":"這個短語突出解釋中的中心想法。"},{"en":"It is useful when separating the main point from smaller details.","zh":"它適合用來把主旨與小細節分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"become flexible in","meaning":"在……方面變得靈活","examples":[{"en":"We have to want to become flexible in our communication style.","zh":"我們必須想在溝通風格方面變得靈活。"},{"en":"To become flexible in something means to become able to adjust it when situations change.","zh":"become flexible in something 指在情況改變時，變得能夠調整某方面。"},{"en":"A teacher may become flexible in lesson planning when different classes learn at different speeds.","zh":"當不同班級學習速度不同，老師可能在課堂規劃方面變得靈活。"},{"en":"Flexibility grows when people practise changing tone, detail, and speed according to the listener.","zh":"當人們練習根據聽者改變語氣、細節和速度，靈活性就會增長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning to adapt in a specific area.","zh":"這個短語描述在特定範疇學會適應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"whether you think you can or you can’t","meaning":"無論你認為自己能還是不能","examples":[{"en":"Henry Ford said that whether you think you can or you can’t, you’re right.","zh":"Henry Ford 說，無論你認為自己能還是不能，你都是對的。"},{"en":"Whether you think you can or you can’t means your belief about your own ability can strongly affect what you try and achieve.","zh":"whether you think you can or you can’t 指你對自己能力的信念可以強烈影響你會嘗試甚麼和達成甚麼。"},{"en":"A student who believes they can improve is more likely to practise than one who believes improvement is impossible.","zh":"相信自己能進步的學生，比相信進步不可能的學生更可能練習。"},{"en":"If people believe flexibility can be learned, they are more likely to attempt it.","zh":"如果人們相信靈活性可以學會，他們較可能嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the power of mindset.","zh":"這個短語突出心態的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to choose the correct heading for each section.","zh":"考生需要為每一部分選出正確標題。"},{"en":"To choose the correct heading means to select the title that best matches the main idea of a section.","zh":"choose the correct heading 指選擇最符合某部分主旨的標題。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should read the whole section before choosing the heading.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生選標題前應先讀完整個部分。"},{"en":"A heading that matches only one small detail may not be correct.","zh":"只符合一個小細節的標題未必正確。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in matching-headings questions.","zh":"這個短語是標題配對題中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The question provides a list of headings for the reading sections.","zh":"題目為閱讀部分提供標題列表。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a group of possible titles used for matching with paragraphs or sections.","zh":"list of headings 指一組可能標題，用來與段落或部分配對。"},{"en":"Students compare each section with the list of headings before choosing an answer.","zh":"學生選答案前會把每部分與標題列表比較。"},{"en":"Extra headings are often included to test whether students understand the main idea.","zh":"額外標題通常會被加入，以測試學生是否理解主旨。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the answer options in a heading-matching task.","zh":"這個短語描述標題配對題中的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"write the correct number","meaning":"寫上正確編號","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the correct number on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生在答題紙上寫上正確編號。"},{"en":"To write the correct number means to record the number that matches the chosen heading or option.","zh":"write the correct number 指記下與所選標題或選項相符的編號。"},{"en":"If heading iv matches Section B, candidates should write iv on the answer sheet.","zh":"如果標題 iv 配對 B 部分，考生應在答題紙上寫 iv。"},{"en":"Correct numbering matters because the examiner marks the number, not the idea in your head.","zh":"正確編號很重要，因為考官批改的是編號，而不是你腦中的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase tells candidates how to record their answer.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生如何記錄答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"on your answer sheet","meaning":"在答題紙上","examples":[{"en":"Answers should be written on your answer sheet.","zh":"答案應寫在答題紙上。"},{"en":"On your answer sheet means in the official place where exam answers must be recorded.","zh":"on your answer sheet 指在考試答案必須記錄的正式位置。"},{"en":"A student may know the answer but lose marks if it is not written on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生可能知道答案，但如果沒有寫在答題紙上，仍可能失分。"},{"en":"Exam papers often allow notes, but final answers must go on the answer sheet.","zh":"試卷通常容許筆記，但最終答案必須寫在答題紙上。"},{"en":"This phrase tells candidates where the final answer belongs.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生最終答案應放在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"summarise personality types","meaning":"概述性格類型","examples":[{"en":"One heading asks candidates to summarise personality types.","zh":"其中一個標題要求考生概述性格類型。"},{"en":"To summarise personality types means to give the main points about different character categories briefly.","zh":"summarise personality types 指簡短說明不同性格類別的重點。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to summarise personality types after reading a passage on communication styles.","zh":"老師可能在學生讀完溝通風格文章後，要求他們概述性格類型。"},{"en":"A good summary includes the key features, not every example or minor detail.","zh":"好摘要包括關鍵特徵，而不是每個例子或小細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving a short overview of personality categories.","zh":"這個短語描述對性格分類作簡短概覽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"combine styles in the workplace","meaning":"在職場中結合不同風格","examples":[{"en":"A successful team may combine styles in the workplace.","zh":"成功團隊可能在職場中結合不同風格。"},{"en":"To combine styles in the workplace means to use different communication or working styles together at work.","zh":"combine styles in the workplace 指在工作中一起使用不同溝通或工作風格。"},{"en":"A team may combine a direct manager, a careful planner, and a supportive listener.","zh":"團隊可能結合直接型經理、謹慎規劃者和支持型聆聽者。"},{"en":"Combining styles can help a workplace handle deadlines, details, and relationships.","zh":"結合不同風格可以幫助職場處理截止日期、細節和關係。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using differences as a resource at work.","zh":"這個短語描述在工作中把差異用作資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"physical explanation","meaning":"生理上的解釋","examples":[{"en":"The old theory gave a physical explanation for temperament.","zh":"舊理論為氣質提供了生理上的解釋。"},{"en":"A physical explanation is an explanation based on the body, body processes, or material causes.","zh":"physical explanation 指基於身體、身體過程或物質原因的解釋。"},{"en":"Tiredness may have a physical explanation, such as lack of sleep or low blood sugar.","zh":"疲倦可能有生理上的解釋，例如睡眠不足或血糖低。"},{"en":"Ancient theories sometimes used physical explanations for personality that modern science no longer accepts.","zh":"古代理論有時用現代科學不再接受的生理解釋來說明性格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes explaining something through the body rather than emotions or society.","zh":"這個短語描述透過身體，而不是情緒或社會來解釋某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a lively person who encourages others","meaning":"活潑並鼓勵別人的人","examples":[{"en":"The expressive style describes a lively person who encourages others.","zh":"富表現力風格描述一個活潑並鼓勵別人的人。"},{"en":"A lively person who encourages others is energetic, expressive, and able to lift people’s motivation.","zh":"lively person who encourages others 指有活力、表達力強，並能提升別人動機的人。"},{"en":"In a group project, this person may make tired classmates feel excited again.","zh":"在小組專案中，這種人可能令疲倦同學再次感到興奮。"},{"en":"Encouraging others can improve team spirit and make difficult work feel possible.","zh":"鼓勵別人可以改善團隊精神，並令困難工作感覺可行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone who brings energy and support to a group.","zh":"這個短語描述為群體帶來能量和支持的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"demanding and unsympathetic","meaning":"要求多而欠缺同理心的","examples":[{"en":"The heading describes a demanding and unsympathetic personality.","zh":"該標題描述一種要求多而欠缺同理心的性格。"},{"en":"Demanding and unsympathetic means expecting a lot from others while showing little understanding of their feelings.","zh":"demanding and unsympathetic 指對別人要求很高，卻很少理解他們的感受。"},{"en":"A demanding and unsympathetic boss may set impossible deadlines and ignore staff stress.","zh":"要求多而欠缺同理心的老闆可能設定不可能的截止日期，並忽視員工壓力。"},{"en":"This behaviour can damage trust because people feel pressured rather than supported.","zh":"這種行為可以損害信任，因為人們感到受壓而不是被支持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a harsh personality or management style.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴苛的性格或管理風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"lazy and careless","meaning":"懶惰而粗心的","examples":[{"en":"The heading mentions a lazy and careless personality.","zh":"該標題提到一種懶惰而粗心的性格。"},{"en":"Lazy and careless means unwilling to make effort and not paying enough attention to accuracy or responsibility.","zh":"lazy and careless 指不願努力，也沒有足夠注意準確性或責任。"},{"en":"A lazy and careless student may submit homework late and full of avoidable mistakes.","zh":"懶惰而粗心的學生可能遲交功課，且充滿可避免錯誤。"},{"en":"Carelessness can cause problems for others when teamwork depends on reliable work.","zh":"當團隊合作依賴可靠工作時，粗心可以為別人造成問題。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a negative description of poor effort and poor attention.","zh":"這個短語對努力不足和注意力不足作負面描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the benefits of understanding","meaning":"理解……的好處","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains the benefits of understanding communication styles.","zh":"文章解釋理解溝通風格的好處。"},{"en":"The benefits of understanding something are the advantages gained when people know it more clearly.","zh":"benefits of understanding something 指人們更清楚了解某事後得到的優點。"},{"en":"The benefits of understanding exam instructions include fewer mistakes and better time use.","zh":"理解考試指示的好處包括較少錯誤和更好運用時間。"},{"en":"Understanding communication styles can reduce blame and improve cooperation.","zh":"理解溝通風格可以減少責怪並改善合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the positive results of clearer knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述更清晰知識帶來的正面結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"cautious and caring","meaning":"謹慎而關心別人的","examples":[{"en":"The considerate style can be described as cautious and caring.","zh":"體貼型風格可以被描述為謹慎而關心別人的。"},{"en":"Cautious and caring means careful about decisions and concerned about people’s feelings.","zh":"cautious and caring 指作決定時小心，並關心別人的感受。"},{"en":"A cautious and caring teacher checks whether students understand before moving on.","zh":"謹慎而關心別人的老師在繼續前，會確認學生是否理解。"},{"en":"This style can protect people from sudden pressure, but it may take more time.","zh":"這種風格可以保護人免受突然壓力，但可能花更多時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a careful and people-centred attitude.","zh":"這個短語描述小心且以人為中心的態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"factual and analytical","meaning":"重事實、善分析的","examples":[{"en":"The systematic style is factual and analytical.","zh":"系統化風格是重事實、善分析的。"},{"en":"Factual and analytical means based on facts and careful examination rather than emotion alone.","zh":"factual and analytical 指基於事實和仔細分析，而不只是情感。"},{"en":"A factual and analytical report uses data, reasons, and clear comparisons.","zh":"重事實、善分析的報告會使用數據、理由和清楚比較。"},{"en":"This style helps people make accurate decisions, especially when details matter.","zh":"這種風格幫助人作出準確決定，尤其在細節重要時。"},{"en":"This phrase describes thinking that is evidence-based and logical.","zh":"這個短語描述以證據和邏輯為基礎的思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"determine one’s temperament","meaning":"決定一個人的氣質","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions whether self-assessment determines one’s temperament.","zh":"題目提到自我評估是否決定一個人的氣質。"},{"en":"To determine one’s temperament means to decide or define a person’s natural emotional style.","zh":"determine one’s temperament 指決定或定義一個人的自然情緒風格。"},{"en":"A short quiz should not fully determine one’s temperament because people behave differently in different situations.","zh":"短測驗不應完全決定一個人的氣質，因為人在不同情況中行為不同。"},{"en":"Self-assessment may suggest patterns, but it should not become a fixed label.","zh":"自我評估可能提示模式，但不應變成固定標籤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes defining someone’s basic personality tendency.","zh":"這個短語描述定義某人的基本性格傾向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether the statements agree with the information given.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與所給資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the passage says expressive people enjoy discussion, a statement saying the same thing agrees with the information given.","zh":"如果文章說富表現力的人喜歡討論，而陳述說同樣內容，就與所給資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge if the task asks about the passage only.","zh":"如果任務只問文章內容，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN reading tasks.","zh":"這個短語用於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement is false if it contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"如果陳述與文章資料矛盾，它就是錯誤的。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文本相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says direct communicators use fewer words, a statement saying they speak at length contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說直接型溝通者使用較少字句，而陳述說他們說話冗長，就與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"A contradiction must be clear from the passage, not guessed from personal opinion.","zh":"矛盾必須從文章清楚看出，而不是靠個人意見猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct conflict with the text.","zh":"這個短語描述與文本直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"The answer is not given if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果沒有這方面的資料，答案就是 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not provide enough evidence to decide.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有提供足夠證據去判斷。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions a person’s age, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文章從未提及某人的年齡，就沒有這方面的資料。"},{"en":"Students should choose NOT GIVEN when the text is silent, even if the statement sounds possible.","zh":"即使陳述聽起來可能正確，只要文本沒有說明，學生也應選 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"This phrase describes missing evidence in a reading passage.","zh":"這個短語描述閱讀文章中缺少證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"it is believed that","meaning":"人們相信；據認為","examples":[{"en":"It is believed that some communication styles respond differently to change.","zh":"人們相信某些溝通風格對轉變有不同反應。"},{"en":"It is believed that means people generally think or accept something, though it may not be directly proven here.","zh":"it is believed that 指人們一般認為或接受某事，雖然這裡未必直接證明。"},{"en":"It is believed that regular sleep helps students concentrate better.","zh":"人們相信規律睡眠有助學生更好專注。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to report a common view without naming one specific person.","zh":"這個短語常用來報告普遍看法，而不指出某一個特定人士。"},{"en":"It presents an idea as generally accepted or widely thought.","zh":"它把想法呈現為一般被接受或被廣泛認為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"dislike variety","meaning":"不喜歡多樣性","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether sanguine people dislike variety.","zh":"該陳述問多血質的人是否不喜歡多樣性。"},{"en":"To dislike variety means to prefer sameness and feel uncomfortable with many different experiences or choices.","zh":"dislike variety 指較喜歡一致性，並對許多不同經驗或選擇感到不自在。"},{"en":"A child who dislikes variety may want the same breakfast every morning.","zh":"不喜歡多樣性的孩子可能每天早上都想吃同一種早餐。"},{"en":"People who dislike variety may feel safer with routine, while others may feel bored by it.","zh":"不喜歡多樣性的人可能在常規中感到安全，而其他人可能覺得沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes discomfort with change or difference.","zh":"這個短語描述對改變或差異感到不自在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"similar characteristics","meaning":"相似特徵","examples":[{"en":"Some styles may have similar characteristics.","zh":"有些風格可能有相似特徵。"},{"en":"Similar characteristics are features that are alike or shared between people, groups, or things.","zh":"similar characteristics 指人、群體或事物之間相似或共有的特點。"},{"en":"Two students may have similar characteristics if both are careful, quiet, and detail-focused.","zh":"如果兩名學生都謹慎、安靜並重視細節，他們可能有相似特徵。"},{"en":"Similar characteristics can make categories overlap, so labels are not always exact.","zh":"相似特徵可以令分類重疊，因此標籤不一定精確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shared qualities.","zh":"這個短語描述共有特質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"select their best employees","meaning":"挑選最佳員工","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to managers selecting their best employees.","zh":"該陳述提到經理挑選最佳員工。"},{"en":"To select their best employees means to choose the workers who perform most strongly or fit a purpose best.","zh":"select their best employees 指選出表現最強或最適合某目的的員工。"},{"en":"A manager may select the best employees for a difficult client project.","zh":"經理可能為困難客戶專案挑選最佳員工。"},{"en":"Choosing only by personality type may be unfair if skills and effort are ignored.","zh":"如果只根據性格類型選人，而忽略技能和努力，可能不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing top workers for a role or task.","zh":"這個短語描述為某角色或任務挑選頂尖員工。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"according to personality types","meaning":"根據性格類型","examples":[{"en":"Some managers may think about employees according to personality types.","zh":"有些經理可能根據性格類型思考員工。"},{"en":"According to personality types means based on categories of personality.","zh":"according to personality types 指基於性格分類。"},{"en":"A teacher may group students according to personality types, but should also consider ability and friendship.","zh":"老師可能根據性格類型為學生分組，但也應考慮能力和友誼。"},{"en":"Organising people this way can help discussion, but it may oversimplify real individuals.","zh":"以這種方式組織人可以幫助討論，但可能過度簡化真實個體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using personality categories as a basis for judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述使用性格類別作為判斷基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"it is possible to","meaning":"有可能……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether it is possible to change one’s personality type.","zh":"題目問是否有可能改變一個人的性格類型。"},{"en":"It is possible to do something means that it can be done or can happen.","zh":"it is possible to do something 指某事可以做到或可以發生。"},{"en":"It is possible to improve pronunciation with regular listening and speaking practice.","zh":"透過定期聆聽和口語練習，有可能改善發音。"},{"en":"Possibility does not mean something is easy; it only means it can happen.","zh":"有可能不代表容易；只代表它可以發生。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what can be done.","zh":"這個短語引出可以做到的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"affect which communication style is most effective","meaning":"影響哪種溝通風格最有效","examples":[{"en":"The workplace environment can affect which communication style is most effective.","zh":"工作環境可以影響哪種溝通風格最有效。"},{"en":"To affect which communication style is most effective means to influence which style works best in a situation.","zh":"affect which communication style is most effective 指影響哪種風格在某情況中效果最好。"},{"en":"In an emergency room, a direct style may be most effective; in counselling, a sympathetic style may work better.","zh":"在急症室中，直接風格可能最有效；在輔導中，富同理心風格可能更有效。"},{"en":"Different environments reward different ways of speaking, listening, and deciding.","zh":"不同環境會鼓勵不同的說話、聆聽和決策方式。"},{"en":"This phrase explains that effectiveness depends on context.","zh":"這個短語解釋有效性取決於語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for the multiple-choice question.","zh":"考生為選擇題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the option marked by the right letter.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇以正確字母標示的選項。"},{"en":"If option C matches the passage, candidates should write C, not the whole sentence.","zh":"如果 C 選項與文章相符，考生應寫 C，而不是整句。"},{"en":"Students must compare all options because wrong answers may contain partly true information.","zh":"學生必須比較所有選項，因為錯誤答案可能含有部分正確資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase is a standard multiple-choice instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準選擇題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"using self-assessment tools","meaning":"使用自我評估工具","examples":[{"en":"The writer discusses the value of using self-assessment tools.","zh":"作者討論使用自我評估工具的價值。"},{"en":"Using self-assessment tools means completing questionnaires or activities to reflect on one’s own traits or habits.","zh":"using self-assessment tools 指完成問卷或活動，以反思自己的特質或習慣。"},{"en":"A student may use self-assessment tools to understand why group work feels stressful.","zh":"學生可能使用自我評估工具來理解為何小組工作令人有壓力。"},{"en":"These tools can start reflection, but they should not replace real conversation and observation.","zh":"這些工具可以啟動反思，但不應取代真實對話和觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using structured tools to understand oneself.","zh":"這個短語描述使用有結構工具來理解自己。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"develop one’s personality","meaning":"培養個人性格","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that self-assessment tools can help develop one’s personality.","zh":"該選項暗示自我評估工具可以幫助培養個人性格。"},{"en":"To develop one’s personality means to shape, improve, or strengthen personal qualities over time.","zh":"develop one’s personality 指隨時間塑造、改善或強化個人特質。"},{"en":"A student may develop confidence by joining debates and receiving supportive feedback.","zh":"學生可能透過參加辯論和得到支持性回饋來培養信心。"},{"en":"Personality development takes practice and experience, not just one short quiz.","zh":"性格培養需要練習和經驗，而不只是一次短測驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual growth in personal qualities.","zh":"這個短語描述個人特質的逐步成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"understand colleagues’ behaviour","meaning":"理解同事的行為","examples":[{"en":"Self-assessment tools can help people understand colleagues’ behaviour.","zh":"自我評估工具可以幫助人理解同事的行為。"},{"en":"To understand colleagues’ behaviour means to recognise why coworkers speak, react, or work in certain ways.","zh":"understand colleagues’ behaviour 指辨認同事為何以某些方式說話、反應或工作。"},{"en":"A worker may understand a colleague’s behaviour better after learning that the colleague needs detailed information before decisions.","zh":"員工得知同事在決定前需要詳細資料後，可能更理解該同事的行為。"},{"en":"Better understanding can reduce blame and make teamwork smoother.","zh":"更好的理解可以減少責怪，並令團隊合作更順暢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes interpreting workplace actions more fairly.","zh":"這個短語描述更公平地解讀職場行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"improve one’s relationship with","meaning":"改善與……的關係","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests improving one’s relationship with the employer.","zh":"該選項暗示改善與僱主的關係。"},{"en":"To improve one’s relationship with someone means to make the connection more trusting, respectful, or cooperative.","zh":"improve one’s relationship with someone 指令與某人的連繫更有信任、尊重或合作。"},{"en":"An employee can improve their relationship with a manager by communicating problems early and politely.","zh":"員工可以透過及早並有禮地溝通問題，改善與經理的關係。"},{"en":"Relationships improve when both sides listen, explain expectations, and follow through.","zh":"當雙方聆聽、解釋期望並真正跟進，關係就會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a human connection better.","zh":"這個短語描述令一段人際連繫變好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"directly resolve conflicts","meaning":"直接解決衝突","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether self-assessment tools can directly resolve conflicts.","zh":"該選項問自我評估工具是否可以直接解決衝突。"},{"en":"To directly resolve conflicts means to solve disagreements themselves without needing further steps.","zh":"directly resolve conflicts 指不需要進一步步驟而直接解決分歧本身。"},{"en":"A quiz may help people understand conflict, but it may not directly resolve conflicts without conversation.","zh":"測驗可能幫助人理解衝突，但沒有對話未必能直接解決衝突。"},{"en":"Conflicts usually require discussion, listening, and agreement on what should change.","zh":"衝突通常需要討論、聆聽和同意應作出甚麼改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes solving conflict immediately and by itself.","zh":"這個短語描述立即並自行解決衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 31 - Communicating Styles and Conflict.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 32":[{"front":"the Columbian Exchange","meaning":"哥倫布大交換","examples":[{"en":"The Columbian Exchange was one of the most significant ecological events of the past millennium.","zh":"哥倫布大交換是過去一千年最重要的生態事件之一。"},{"en":"The Columbian Exchange means the movement of plants, animals, diseases, and people between the Old World and the New World after European contact with the Americas.","zh":"哥倫布大交換 指歐洲人接觸美洲後，植物、動物、疾病和人口在舊世界與新世界之間流動。"},{"en":"Potatoes moving to Europe and horses moving to the Americas are examples of the Columbian Exchange.","zh":"馬鈴薯傳到歐洲、馬匹傳到美洲，都是哥倫布大交換的例子。"},{"en":"The Columbian Exchange changed diets, farming, disease patterns, and populations on both sides of the Atlantic.","zh":"哥倫布大交換改變了大西洋兩岸的飲食、農業、疾病模式和人口。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a huge historical exchange, not just one trade journey.","zh":"這個短語描述一次巨大的歷史交換，而不只是一趟貿易旅程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"continental drift","meaning":"大陸漂移","examples":[{"en":"Continental drift carried the Old World and New World apart.","zh":"大陸漂移把舊世界和新世界分隔開。"},{"en":"Continental drift is the slow movement of continents across the Earth’s surface over millions of years.","zh":"continental drift 指大陸在數百萬年間於地球表面緩慢移動。"},{"en":"A geography teacher may use maps to show how continental drift once joined and later separated landmasses.","zh":"地理老師可能用地圖展示大陸漂移如何曾經連接、後來分離陸塊。"},{"en":"Because of continental drift, species on separated continents can develop in different directions.","zh":"由於大陸漂移，分隔大陸上的物種可以向不同方向發展。"},{"en":"This phrase explains very slow geological movement, not ordinary travel.","zh":"這個短語解釋非常緩慢的地質移動，而不是一般旅行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the Old World","meaning":"舊世界","examples":[{"en":"The Old World included Eurasia and Africa.","zh":"舊世界包括歐亞大陸和非洲。"},{"en":"The Old World means Europe, Asia, and Africa, especially when compared with the Americas after 1492.","zh":"the Old World 指歐洲、亞洲和非洲，尤其是在 1492 年後與美洲作比較時使用。"},{"en":"Wheat, cattle, and many infectious diseases were associated with the Old World before the exchange.","zh":"小麥、牛和許多傳染病在交換前與舊世界有關。"},{"en":"When Europeans crossed the Atlantic, they carried Old World crops and animals with them.","zh":"當歐洲人橫越大西洋時，他們把舊世界作物和動物帶到美洲。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in historical geography to contrast Europe, Asia, and Africa with the Americas.","zh":"這個短語用於歷史地理，將歐亞非與美洲作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the New World","meaning":"新世界","examples":[{"en":"The New World included North and South America.","zh":"新世界包括北美洲和南美洲。"},{"en":"The New World means the Americas, especially from the viewpoint of Europeans after they reached them.","zh":"the New World 指美洲，尤其是從歐洲人抵達後的角度來說。"},{"en":"Maize, potatoes, and manioc were important crops from the New World.","zh":"粟米、馬鈴薯和木薯是來自新世界的重要作物。"},{"en":"European arrival brought Old World animals and diseases into the New World.","zh":"歐洲人的到來把舊世界動物和疾病帶入新世界。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the Americas in the context of early modern exploration and exchange.","zh":"這個短語在近代早期探險和交換的語境中指美洲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"carry something apart","meaning":"把……分隔開","examples":[{"en":"Continental drift carried the Old World and New World apart.","zh":"大陸漂移把舊世界和新世界分隔開。"},{"en":"To carry something apart means to move two things away from each other over time.","zh":"carry something apart 指隨時間把兩件事物移離彼此。"},{"en":"Slow movement in a river can carry floating branches apart until they reach different banks.","zh":"河流中的緩慢水流可以把漂浮樹枝分隔開，直到它們到達不同河岸。"},{"en":"When continents were carried apart, plants and animals evolved separately.","zh":"當大陸被分隔開，植物和動物便分開演化。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on separation caused by movement.","zh":"這個短語著重由移動造成的分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"split A from B","meaning":"把 A 從 B 分離出來","examples":[{"en":"Continental drift split North and South America from Eurasia and Africa.","zh":"大陸漂移把南北美洲從歐亞大陸和非洲分離出來。"},{"en":"To split A from B means to separate one thing or group from another.","zh":"split A from B 指把一件事物或一個群體從另一方分開。"},{"en":"A new road may split a quiet neighbourhood from the park it once used every day.","zh":"新道路可能把安靜社區從居民每天使用的公園分隔開。"},{"en":"When people are split from their community, daily communication becomes harder.","zh":"當人們與社群分離，日常溝通會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear division between two sides.","zh":"這個短語描述兩方之間清楚的分隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Eurasia","meaning":"歐亞大陸","examples":[{"en":"Eurasia was separated from the Americas by continental drift.","zh":"歐亞大陸因大陸漂移而與美洲分離。"},{"en":"Eurasia means the combined landmass of Europe and Asia.","zh":"Eurasia 指歐洲和亞洲合在一起的陸塊。"},{"en":"A history map may show trade routes crossing Eurasia from China to Europe.","zh":"歷史地圖可能顯示由中國通往歐洲、橫跨歐亞大陸的貿易路線。"},{"en":"Because Eurasia was separated from the Americas, many species developed differently on each side.","zh":"由於歐亞大陸與美洲分離，兩邊許多物種以不同方式發展。"},{"en":"This word is useful when Europe and Asia are discussed as one connected landmass.","zh":"當歐洲和亞洲被視為相連陸塊來討論時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"foster divergent evolution","meaning":"促成分歧演化","examples":[{"en":"The long separation fostered divergent evolution.","zh":"長期分隔促成分歧演化。"},{"en":"To foster divergent evolution means to encourage species in separated places to develop different traits over time.","zh":"foster divergent evolution 指促使分隔地方的物種隨時間發展出不同特徵。"},{"en":"If two bird populations live on different islands, isolation may foster divergent evolution.","zh":"如果兩群鳥生活在不同島嶼，隔離可能促成分歧演化。"},{"en":"Separation limits mixing, so each group adapts to its own environment.","zh":"分隔限制混合，因此每個群體適應自己的環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes conditions that help living things evolve differently.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助生物以不同方式演化的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"divergent evolution","meaning":"分歧演化","examples":[{"en":"Divergent evolution produced different species on different sides of the Atlantic.","zh":"分歧演化在大西洋兩岸產生了不同物種。"},{"en":"Divergent evolution is the process by which related organisms become more different after living in separate environments.","zh":"divergent evolution 指相關生物在分開環境中生活後變得越來越不同的過程。"},{"en":"Students can understand divergent evolution by comparing island animals with their mainland relatives.","zh":"學生可以透過比較島嶼動物和其大陸親緣物種來理解分歧演化。"},{"en":"Different climates, predators, and food sources can push species along different evolutionary paths.","zh":"不同氣候、捕食者和食物來源可以把物種推向不同演化路徑。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why once-related life forms may become very different.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何原本相關的生命形式可能變得非常不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"For instance, rattlesnakes developed on one side of the Atlantic.","zh":"例如，響尾蛇在大西洋的一邊發展出來。"},{"en":"For instance means for example, and it introduces a specific case that explains a general idea.","zh":"for instance 指例如，用來引入能解釋一般想法的具體例子。"},{"en":"Many foods changed after global trade; for instance, potatoes became common in parts of Europe.","zh":"全球貿易後許多食物改變了；例如，馬鈴薯在歐洲部分地區變得常見。"},{"en":"Writers use for instance to make an explanation clearer and more concrete.","zh":"作者使用 for instance 令解釋更清楚和具體。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers move from a broad claim to a real example.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者由廣泛聲稱轉向真實例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on one side of the Atlantic","meaning":"在大西洋的一邊","examples":[{"en":"Rattlesnakes developed on one side of the Atlantic.","zh":"響尾蛇在大西洋的一邊發展出來。"},{"en":"On one side of the Atlantic means in the lands west or east of the Atlantic Ocean, depending on the contrast being made.","zh":"on one side of the Atlantic 指在大西洋以西或以東的地方，視乎所作對比而定。"},{"en":"On one side of the Atlantic, people grew maize; on the other, many farmers grew wheat.","zh":"在大西洋的一邊，人們種植粟米；在另一邊，許多農民種植小麥。"},{"en":"Comparing the two sides helps explain why plants and animals developed differently.","zh":"比較兩邊有助解釋植物和動物為何發展不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when contrasting the Americas with Europe or Africa.","zh":"這個短語用於對比美洲與歐洲或非洲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on the other","meaning":"在另一邊","examples":[{"en":"Vipers developed on the other side of the Atlantic.","zh":"蝰蛇在大西洋的另一邊發展出來。"},{"en":"On the other means on the other side or in the other case already being compared.","zh":"on the other 指在另一邊，或在已比較的另一個情況中。"},{"en":"One school teaches in English; on the other, lessons are mainly in the students’ home language.","zh":"一所學校以英語教學；在另一邊，課堂主要使用學生的家庭語言。"},{"en":"The phrase helps avoid repeating the full comparison.","zh":"這個短語有助避免重複完整比較。"},{"en":"It is useful when two sides, places, or examples are being contrasted.","zh":"當兩邊、兩地或兩個例子被對比時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"human voyagers","meaning":"人類航海者","examples":[{"en":"Human voyagers partly reversed this separation after 1492.","zh":"人類航海者在 1492 年後部分扭轉了這種分隔。"},{"en":"Human voyagers are people who travel long distances, especially by sea, to new lands.","zh":"human voyagers 指長途旅行，尤其是乘船前往新地方的人。"},{"en":"Sailors, explorers, traders, and migrants can all be human voyagers.","zh":"水手、探險家、商人和移民都可以是人類航海者。"},{"en":"When human voyagers crossed oceans, they carried food, animals, diseases, and ideas with them.","zh":"當人類航海者橫越海洋，他們也帶着食物、動物、疾病和思想。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights people as agents of movement and exchange.","zh":"這個短語突出人類作為移動和交換的推動者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in part","meaning":"在某程度上","examples":[{"en":"Human voyagers in part reversed this tendency.","zh":"人類航海者在某程度上扭轉了這種趨勢。"},{"en":"In part means partly, but not completely.","zh":"in part 指部分地，但不是完全地。"},{"en":"A student’s poor result may be caused in part by lack of sleep and in part by weak revision.","zh":"學生成績不佳可能部分由睡眠不足造成，也部分由溫習薄弱造成。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor explains only some of the situation.","zh":"這個短語顯示某因素只解釋情況的一部分。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving a balanced explanation with several causes.","zh":"當需要給出包含多個原因的平衡解釋時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reverse this tendency","meaning":"扭轉這種趨勢","examples":[{"en":"Human voyagers reversed this tendency by reconnecting the two worlds.","zh":"人類航海者透過重新連接兩個世界，扭轉了這種趨勢。"},{"en":"To reverse this tendency means to make an existing pattern move in the opposite direction.","zh":"reverse this tendency 指使一個既有模式朝相反方向發展。"},{"en":"If fewer students read books each year, a school library programme may reverse this tendency.","zh":"如果每年讀書的學生越來越少，學校圖書館計劃可能扭轉這種趨勢。"},{"en":"Reconnecting separated regions can reverse a tendency toward isolation.","zh":"重新連接分隔地區，可以扭轉走向孤立的趨勢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing a trend so it no longer continues in the same way.","zh":"這個短語描述改變趨勢，使其不再以相同方式延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"artificial re-establishment of connections","meaning":"人為重新建立聯繫","examples":[{"en":"The Columbian Exchange involved the artificial re-establishment of connections.","zh":"哥倫布大交換涉及人為重新建立聯繫。"},{"en":"Artificial re-establishment of connections means humans deliberately or indirectly rebuilt links that nature had long separated.","zh":"artificial re-establishment of connections 指人類有意或間接重新建立自然界長期分隔的聯繫。"},{"en":"A new bridge can be an artificial re-establishment of connections between two towns separated by a river.","zh":"新橋可以是兩個被河流分隔城鎮之間的人為重新建立聯繫。"},{"en":"In history, ships reconnected continents that had been biologically separate for a very long time.","zh":"在歷史上，船隻重新連接了在生物上分隔已久的大陸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes human-made reconnection after separation.","zh":"這個短語描述分離之後由人類造成的重新連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"commingling of","meaning":"……的混合","examples":[{"en":"The exchange involved the commingling of plants, animals, and bacteria.","zh":"這場交換涉及植物、動物和細菌的混合。"},{"en":"The commingling of things means their mixing together after they were once separate.","zh":"commingling of things 指原本分開的事物混在一起。"},{"en":"A busy international school may involve the commingling of languages, habits, and food traditions.","zh":"一所繁忙的國際學校可能涉及語言、習慣和飲食傳統的混合。"},{"en":"Commingling can create new combinations, but it can also spread risks such as disease.","zh":"混合可以創造新組合，但也可能傳播疾病等風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mixing across groups, places, or categories.","zh":"這個短語描述跨群體、地點或類別的混合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"plants, animals, and bacteria","meaning":"植物、動物和細菌","examples":[{"en":"Plants, animals, and bacteria moved between the Old World and New World.","zh":"植物、動物和細菌在舊世界與新世界之間移動。"},{"en":"Plants, animals, and bacteria are living things that can move naturally or be carried by people.","zh":"plants, animals, and bacteria 指可以自然移動或由人類攜帶的生物。"},{"en":"Seeds in soil, rats on ships, and bacteria in human bodies can all travel with human movement.","zh":"土壤中的種子、船上的老鼠和人體內的細菌都可以隨人類移動。"},{"en":"When plants, animals, and bacteria enter new environments, they can change ecosystems.","zh":"當植物、動物和細菌進入新環境，它們可以改變生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase groups together major forms of life involved in ecological exchange.","zh":"這個短語把參與生態交換的主要生命形式歸在一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"commonly known as","meaning":"通常稱為","examples":[{"en":"This process is commonly known as the Columbian Exchange.","zh":"這個過程通常稱為哥倫布大交換。"},{"en":"Commonly known as means usually called by a particular name.","zh":"commonly known as 指通常以某特定名稱稱呼。"},{"en":"The midday meal at school is commonly known as lunch.","zh":"學校中的中午一餐通常稱為午餐。"},{"en":"Using the common name helps readers recognise the idea quickly.","zh":"使用常見名稱幫助讀者快速辨認該概念。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the familiar name for something.","zh":"這個短語引入某事物的熟悉名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"spectacular and significant","meaning":"壯觀而重要的","examples":[{"en":"The Columbian Exchange was a spectacular and significant ecological event.","zh":"哥倫布大交換是一場壯觀而重要的生態事件。"},{"en":"Spectacular and significant means impressive to see or imagine and important in effect.","zh":"spectacular and significant 指看起來或想像起來令人震撼，而且在影響上很重要。"},{"en":"A city’s first underground railway can be spectacular and significant because it changes how people travel.","zh":"一個城市第一條地下鐵路可以是壯觀而重要的，因為它改變人們出行方式。"},{"en":"An event may be spectacular because it is large, and significant because it changes history.","zh":"一件事可能因規模巨大而壯觀，並因改變歷史而重要。"},{"en":"This phrase combines visual force with real importance.","zh":"這個短語結合了視覺震撼和真正重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ecological event","meaning":"生態事件","examples":[{"en":"The Columbian Exchange was a major ecological event.","zh":"哥倫布大交換是一場重大的生態事件。"},{"en":"An ecological event is something that changes relationships among living things and their environments.","zh":"ecological event 指改變生物與其環境之間關係的事情。"},{"en":"A new invasive plant spreading through a forest can be an ecological event.","zh":"一種新的入侵植物在森林中擴散，可以是一場生態事件。"},{"en":"Ecological events can affect food chains, farming, disease, and population size.","zh":"生態事件可以影響食物鏈、農業、疾病和人口數量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an event with effects on nature and living systems.","zh":"這個短語描述對自然和生命系統有影響的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"past millennium","meaning":"過去一千年","examples":[{"en":"It was one of the most important ecological events of the past millennium.","zh":"它是過去一千年最重要的生態事件之一。"},{"en":"The past millennium means the last one thousand years.","zh":"past millennium 指過去一千年。"},{"en":"Historians may ask which inventions most changed human life in the past millennium.","zh":"歷史學家可能問過去一千年哪些發明最改變人類生活。"},{"en":"Calling something important in the past millennium suggests its impact was extremely large.","zh":"稱某事在過去一千年中重要，表示其影響極大。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event within a very long historical time frame.","zh":"這個短語把事件放入很長的歷史時間框架中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"first touched the shores of","meaning":"首次抵達……海岸","examples":[{"en":"Europeans first touched the shores of the Americas after 1492.","zh":"歐洲人在 1492 年後首次抵達美洲海岸。"},{"en":"To first touch the shores of a place means to arrive at its coast for the first time.","zh":"first touch the shores of a place 指首次到達某地海岸。"},{"en":"Migrants may feel nervous when their boat first touches the shores of a new country.","zh":"當移民船首次抵達新國家的海岸，他們可能感到緊張。"},{"en":"When voyagers first reached new shores, they often began trade, settlement, or conflict.","zh":"當航海者首次抵達新海岸，他們往往開始貿易、定居或衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a vivid way to describe first arrival by sea.","zh":"這個短語以生動畫面描述經海路首次到達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Americas","meaning":"美洲","examples":[{"en":"Europeans brought Old World crops to the Americas.","zh":"歐洲人把舊世界作物帶到美洲。"},{"en":"The Americas means North America, Central America, South America, and nearby islands.","zh":"the Americas 指北美洲、中美洲、南美洲和附近島嶼。"},{"en":"Maize and potatoes came from the Americas before spreading to other parts of the world.","zh":"粟米和馬鈴薯來自美洲，後來傳到世界其他地方。"},{"en":"European contact changed the animals, plants, and populations of the Americas.","zh":"歐洲接觸改變了美洲的動物、植物和人口。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the American continents as a broad region.","zh":"這個短語把美洲大陸作為廣泛地區來指稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Old World crops","meaning":"舊世界作物","examples":[{"en":"Old World crops such as wheat and barley had not travelled west.","zh":"小麥和大麥等舊世界作物此前並未向西傳播。"},{"en":"Old World crops are plants grown for food that originally came from Europe, Asia, or Africa.","zh":"Old World crops 指原本來自歐洲、亞洲或非洲、供食用種植的植物。"},{"en":"Wheat, rice, and barley are examples of Old World crops in historical discussions.","zh":"在歷史討論中，小麥、稻米和大麥都是舊世界作物的例子。"},{"en":"When settlers carried Old World crops overseas, they changed farming in new lands.","zh":"當移民把舊世界作物帶到海外，他們改變了新土地上的農業。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts crops from Eurasia and Africa with crops from the Americas.","zh":"這個短語把歐亞非作物與美洲作物作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"travel west across","meaning":"向西橫越……","examples":[{"en":"Wheat and rice had not travelled west across the Atlantic.","zh":"小麥和稻米此前並未向西橫越大西洋。"},{"en":"To travel west across something means to move westward over or through that space.","zh":"travel west across something 指向西移動，橫越某空間。"},{"en":"A cargo ship may travel west across the Pacific to deliver goods to another continent.","zh":"貨船可能向西橫越太平洋，把貨物送到另一大陸。"},{"en":"When crops travel west across an ocean, they can enter new farms and diets.","zh":"當作物向西橫越海洋，它們可以進入新的農田和飲食。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direction and movement across a large barrier.","zh":"這個短語描述方向，以及穿越巨大屏障的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Atlantic","meaning":"大西洋","examples":[{"en":"Many crops crossed the Atlantic after European contact.","zh":"歐洲接觸後，許多作物橫越大西洋。"},{"en":"The Atlantic is the ocean between the Americas and Europe and Africa.","zh":"the Atlantic 指位於美洲與歐洲、非洲之間的海洋。"},{"en":"Ships crossing the Atlantic carried people, animals, seeds, and diseases.","zh":"橫越大西洋的船隻運載人口、動物、種子和疾病。"},{"en":"The Atlantic became a route of exchange after the Old World and New World were reconnected.","zh":"舊世界與新世界重新連接後，大西洋成為交換路線。"},{"en":"This phrase often refers to the ocean linking both sides of the Columbian Exchange.","zh":"這個短語常指連接哥倫布大交換兩邊的海洋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"New World crops","meaning":"新世界作物","examples":[{"en":"New World crops such as maize and potatoes later travelled east.","zh":"粟米和馬鈴薯等新世界作物後來向東傳播。"},{"en":"New World crops are food plants that originally came from the Americas.","zh":"New World crops 指原本來自美洲的食用植物。"},{"en":"Maize, white potatoes, sweet potatoes, and manioc are important New World crops.","zh":"粟米、馬鈴薯、番薯和木薯都是重要的新世界作物。"},{"en":"These crops helped support population growth when they spread into Old World diets.","zh":"這些作物傳入舊世界飲食後，有助支持人口增長。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts American crops with crops originally from Eurasia and Africa.","zh":"這個短語把美洲作物與原產歐亞非的作物作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"travel east to","meaning":"向東傳到……","examples":[{"en":"New World crops had not travelled east to Europe before the exchange.","zh":"在這場交換之前，新世界作物並未向東傳到歐洲。"},{"en":"To travel east to a place means to move toward that place in an eastward direction.","zh":"travel east to a place 指朝東方移動到某地。"},{"en":"Tea once travelled west to Europe, while some crops travelled east to Asia and Africa.","zh":"茶曾向西傳到歐洲，而有些作物則向東傳到亞洲和非洲。"},{"en":"When crops travel east to new regions, local diets can change over generations.","zh":"當作物向東傳到新地區，當地飲食可能在幾代之間改變。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly shows both direction and destination.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示方向和目的地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"maize","meaning":"粟米；玉米","examples":[{"en":"Maize became one of the important New World crops.","zh":"粟米成為重要的新世界作物之一。"},{"en":"Maize is a grain crop from the Americas, also commonly called corn.","zh":"maize 指來自美洲的穀物作物，也常稱為 corn。"},{"en":"Families may eat maize as boiled corn, flour, porridge, or tortillas.","zh":"家庭可能以煮粟米、粟米粉、粥或薄餅形式食用玉米。"},{"en":"When maize spread to new regions, it became a reliable food source for many people.","zh":"當粟米傳到新地區，它成為許多人可靠的食物來源。"},{"en":"This word refers to an important crop in global food history.","zh":"這個詞指全球食物史中的重要作物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"white potatoes","meaning":"馬鈴薯","examples":[{"en":"White potatoes travelled from the New World to the Old World.","zh":"馬鈴薯從新世界傳到舊世界。"},{"en":"White potatoes are starchy tubers originally from the Americas and later widely grown elsewhere.","zh":"white potatoes 指原產美洲、後來在其他地方廣泛種植的澱粉塊莖。"},{"en":"A family may eat white potatoes boiled, roasted, fried, or mashed.","zh":"家庭可能以水煮、烤焗、油炸或壓成泥的方式食用馬鈴薯。"},{"en":"Because potatoes produce much food from limited land, they supported population growth in some regions.","zh":"因為馬鈴薯能在有限土地上產出大量食物，它們在某些地區支持人口增長。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to ordinary potatoes, not sweet potatoes.","zh":"這個短語指普通馬鈴薯，而不是番薯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sweet potatoes","meaning":"番薯","examples":[{"en":"Sweet potatoes became important in Old World diets.","zh":"番薯在舊世界飲食中變得重要。"},{"en":"Sweet potatoes are sweet, starchy root crops originally from the New World.","zh":"sweet potatoes 指原本來自新世界、帶甜味且富含澱粉的根莖作物。"},{"en":"People may bake sweet potatoes, cook them in soup, or use them in desserts.","zh":"人們可能烤番薯、把番薯煮湯，或用番薯做甜品。"},{"en":"When sweet potatoes spread to new regions, they offered a useful food source in difficult farming conditions.","zh":"當番薯傳到新地區，它們在困難耕作條件下提供有用食物來源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a New World crop that became important far beyond its origin.","zh":"這個短語指一種影響遠超原產地的新世界作物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"manioc","meaning":"木薯","examples":[{"en":"Manioc was one of the New World crops that spread eastward.","zh":"木薯是向東傳播的新世界作物之一。"},{"en":"Manioc is a starchy root crop from the Americas, also known as cassava.","zh":"manioc 指來自美洲的澱粉根莖作物，也稱為 cassava。"},{"en":"In some communities, manioc is processed into flour, bread, or porridge.","zh":"在某些社區，木薯被加工成粉、麵包或粥。"},{"en":"Manioc can become important where other crops grow poorly, so it can support food security.","zh":"木薯可以在其他作物難以生長的地方變得重要，因此能支持糧食安全。"},{"en":"This word refers to a crop whose value comes from its useful edible root.","zh":"這個詞指一種價值來自可食用根部的作物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"of Old World origin","meaning":"源自舊世界的","examples":[{"en":"Horses and cattle were animals of Old World origin.","zh":"馬和牛是源自舊世界的動物。"},{"en":"Of Old World origin means originally coming from Europe, Asia, or Africa rather than the Americas.","zh":"of Old World origin 指原本來自歐洲、亞洲或非洲，而不是美洲。"},{"en":"Wheat is of Old World origin, while maize is of New World origin.","zh":"小麥源自舊世界，而粟米源自新世界。"},{"en":"Knowing a species’ origin helps explain how it spread during the Columbian Exchange.","zh":"了解物種起源有助解釋它在哥倫布大交換中如何傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where something first came from in historical terms.","zh":"這個短語以歷史角度指出某物最初來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"with the exception of","meaning":"除……之外","examples":[{"en":"With the exception of the llama, the New World had few domesticated animals.","zh":"除駱馬之外，新世界少有馴養動物。"},{"en":"With the exception of means except for one person, thing, or case.","zh":"with the exception of 指除了一個人、事物或情況之外。"},{"en":"With the exception of one rainy day, the school trip had perfect weather.","zh":"除了一天下雨外，學校旅行的天氣都很完美。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a general rule while naming the case that does not fit it.","zh":"這個短語突出一般規律，同時指出不符合該規律的例外。"},{"en":"It is useful when an example is different from the rest of a group.","zh":"當某個例子與群體其他部分不同時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"domesticated animals","meaning":"馴養動物","examples":[{"en":"The New World had few domesticated animals before European contact.","zh":"在歐洲接觸之前，新世界少有馴養動物。"},{"en":"Domesticated animals are animals that humans have bred or trained to live with them and serve human purposes.","zh":"domesticated animals 指人類經繁殖或訓練，使其與人共同生活並服務人類用途的動物。"},{"en":"Cattle, sheep, horses, chickens, and dogs are common domesticated animals.","zh":"牛、羊、馬、雞和狗都是常見馴養動物。"},{"en":"Domesticated animals can provide transport, meat, milk, labour, or companionship.","zh":"馴養動物可以提供交通、肉、奶、勞力或陪伴。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to animals shaped by long contact with humans.","zh":"這個短語指經長期與人類接觸而被塑造的動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be associated with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Some pathogens were associated with dense Old World populations.","zh":"有些病原體與舊世界密集人口有關。"},{"en":"To be associated with something means to be connected with it in people’s minds or in reality.","zh":"be associated with something 指在觀念上或實際上與某事有連繫。"},{"en":"Fast food is often associated with convenience, but also with health concerns.","zh":"快餐常與方便有關，但也與健康憂慮有關。"},{"en":"If a disease is associated with crowded cities, it may spread more easily there.","zh":"如果一種疾病與擁擠城市有關，它可能更容易在那裡傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a link between two things.","zh":"這個短語描述兩件事之間的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pathogens","meaning":"病原體","examples":[{"en":"The New World lacked many pathogens common in the Old World.","zh":"新世界缺乏許多在舊世界常見的病原體。"},{"en":"Pathogens are microorganisms or agents that can cause disease.","zh":"pathogens 指能引起疾病的微生物或因素。"},{"en":"Bacteria, viruses, and parasites can be pathogens if they make people or animals sick.","zh":"如果細菌、病毒和寄生蟲令人或動物生病，它們可以是病原體。"},{"en":"When pathogens enter a population with little immunity, they can cause deadly outbreaks.","zh":"當病原體進入免疫力低的人群，它們可以造成致命爆發。"},{"en":"This word is often used in medicine, biology, and public health.","zh":"這個詞常用於醫學、生物學和公共衞生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"dense populations of humans","meaning":"密集的人口","examples":[{"en":"Dense populations of humans helped spread Old World diseases.","zh":"密集的人口幫助舊世界疾病傳播。"},{"en":"Dense populations of humans are large numbers of people living close together in one place.","zh":"dense populations of humans 指大量人口緊密居住在同一地方。"},{"en":"A crowded city has dense populations of humans in housing, transport, and workplaces.","zh":"擁擠城市在住房、交通和工作場所中都有密集人口。"},{"en":"Dense populations can help diseases spread because people meet one another often.","zh":"密集人口可以幫助疾病傳播，因為人們經常彼此接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both many people and close physical contact.","zh":"這個短語同時描述人口多和身體距離近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"associated creatures","meaning":"相關生物","examples":[{"en":"Chickens, cattle, black rats, and mosquitoes were associated creatures.","zh":"雞、牛、黑鼠和蚊子都是相關生物。"},{"en":"Associated creatures are animals or insects connected with human settlements, trade, or disease movement.","zh":"associated creatures 指與人類聚居、貿易或疾病移動有關的動物或昆蟲。"},{"en":"Rats in a port city can be associated creatures because they travel with ships and stored food.","zh":"港口城市中的老鼠可以是相關生物，因為牠們隨船隻和儲糧移動。"},{"en":"Such creatures can carry germs or change local environments when they move with people.","zh":"這類生物隨人類移動時，可以攜帶病菌或改變本地環境。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to living things linked to a larger process.","zh":"這個短語指與較大過程相連的生物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Aedes aegypti mosquitoes","meaning":"埃及斑蚊","examples":[{"en":"Aedes aegypti mosquitoes helped carry certain diseases.","zh":"埃及斑蚊幫助攜帶某些疾病。"},{"en":"Aedes aegypti mosquitoes are mosquitoes known for spreading diseases such as yellow fever in suitable environments.","zh":"Aedes aegypti mosquitoes 指一種在合適環境中會傳播黃熱病等疾病的蚊子。"},{"en":"Public health workers may target Aedes aegypti mosquitoes by removing standing water near homes.","zh":"公共衞生人員可能透過清除住家附近積水來針對埃及斑蚊。"},{"en":"If these mosquitoes spread into a new region, disease risks can increase.","zh":"如果這些蚊子擴散到新地區，疾病風險可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific mosquito species important in disease history.","zh":"這個短語命名一種在疾病史中重要的特定蚊種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"germs that carried","meaning":"攜帶……的病菌","examples":[{"en":"Some germs carried smallpox, measles, and yellow fever.","zh":"有些病菌攜帶天花、麻疹和黃熱病。"},{"en":"Germs that carried a disease are microorganisms or infection agents that spread that disease.","zh":"germs that carried a disease 指傳播該疾病的微生物或感染因素。"},{"en":"Germs carried by unwashed hands can move from one child to another at school.","zh":"未洗手所攜帶的病菌可以在學校由一個孩子傳到另一個孩子。"},{"en":"When germs are carried across oceans, they may reach people with no previous protection.","zh":"當病菌被帶過海洋，它們可能接觸到沒有先前保護的人。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how disease can travel through living carriers or contact.","zh":"這個短語解釋疾病如何透過生物載體或接觸傳播。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"smallpox","meaning":"天花","examples":[{"en":"Smallpox was one of the most destructive diseases in the New World.","zh":"天花是新世界最具破壞性的疾病之一。"},{"en":"Smallpox was a highly contagious viral disease that caused fever, rash, scarring, and many deaths.","zh":"smallpox 指一種高度傳染性的病毒病，會造成發燒、皮疹、疤痕和大量死亡。"},{"en":"A history lesson on public health may discuss how vaccination helped eliminate smallpox.","zh":"公共衞生歷史課可能討論疫苗如何幫助消滅天花。"},{"en":"When smallpox reached populations without immunity, it could devastate entire communities.","zh":"當天花傳到沒有免疫力的人群，它可以摧毀整個社群。"},{"en":"This word names a disease that played a major role in the Columbian Exchange.","zh":"這個詞命名一種在哥倫布大交換中扮演重要角色的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"measles","meaning":"麻疹","examples":[{"en":"Measles was among the diseases brought from the Old World.","zh":"麻疹是從舊世界帶來的疾病之一。"},{"en":"Measles is a highly infectious disease that causes fever and a red rash.","zh":"measles 指一種高度傳染性疾病，會造成發燒和紅疹。"},{"en":"Schools may warn parents about measles because one sick child can infect many classmates.","zh":"學校可能提醒家長注意麻疹，因為一名患病兒童可以感染許多同學。"},{"en":"When measles enters a population with low immunity, outbreaks can spread quickly.","zh":"當麻疹進入免疫力低的人群，疫情可以迅速擴散。"},{"en":"This word refers to a contagious disease that moved as part of disease exchange.","zh":"這個詞指在疾病交換中移動的一種傳染病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"chickenpox","meaning":"水痘","examples":[{"en":"Chickenpox was one of the germs associated with the Old World.","zh":"水痘是與舊世界有關的病菌之一。"},{"en":"Chickenpox is a contagious disease that usually causes itchy spots and fever.","zh":"chickenpox 指一種通常引起痕癢水泡和發燒的傳染病。"},{"en":"A child with chickenpox may stay home from school to avoid infecting classmates.","zh":"患水痘的孩子可能留在家中，避免感染同學。"},{"en":"Diseases like chickenpox can spread easily when people live close together.","zh":"像水痘這樣的疾病在人們近距離生活時容易傳播。"},{"en":"This word names one of the infectious diseases linked to population contact.","zh":"這個詞命名一種與人口接觸有關的傳染病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"influenza","meaning":"流感","examples":[{"en":"Influenza spread as part of the disease exchange.","zh":"流感作為疾病交換的一部分而傳播。"},{"en":"Influenza is a contagious viral illness commonly called the flu.","zh":"influenza 指一種傳染性病毒病，通常稱為 flu。"},{"en":"A worker with influenza may need to rest at home because fever and tiredness make work difficult.","zh":"患流感的員工可能需要在家休息，因為發燒和疲倦令工作困難。"},{"en":"Influenza can spread quickly in crowded schools, offices, and transport systems.","zh":"流感可以在擁擠的學校、辦公室和交通系統中迅速傳播。"},{"en":"This word refers to a disease that can move rapidly through human contact.","zh":"這個詞指一種能透過人類接觸快速移動的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"malaria","meaning":"瘧疾","examples":[{"en":"Malaria was one of the diseases carried across worlds.","zh":"瘧疾是跨世界傳播的疾病之一。"},{"en":"Malaria is a serious disease spread by mosquitoes and often linked to fever and weakness.","zh":"malaria 指一種由蚊子傳播、常與發燒和虛弱有關的嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"Travellers to some tropical areas may take medicine to reduce the risk of malaria.","zh":"前往某些熱帶地區的旅客可能服藥以降低瘧疾風險。"},{"en":"If mosquito populations increase, malaria can become harder to control.","zh":"如果蚊子數量增加，瘧疾可能變得更難控制。"},{"en":"This word names a mosquito-borne disease important in human and environmental history.","zh":"這個詞命名一種在人類和環境史中重要的蚊媒疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"yellow fever","meaning":"黃熱病","examples":[{"en":"Yellow fever was among the dangerous imported diseases.","zh":"黃熱病是危險外來疾病之一。"},{"en":"Yellow fever is a serious viral disease spread by mosquitoes in some warm regions.","zh":"yellow fever 指在某些溫暖地區由蚊子傳播的嚴重病毒病。"},{"en":"Port cities may fear yellow fever if infected mosquitoes arrive on ships or in cargo areas.","zh":"如果受感染蚊子隨船隻或貨物區到達，港口城市可能擔心黃熱病。"},{"en":"The movement of people and mosquitoes can spread yellow fever to new places.","zh":"人口和蚊子的移動可以把黃熱病傳到新地方。"},{"en":"This phrase names a disease linked to both ecology and travel.","zh":"這個短語命名一種與生態和旅行都有關的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as might be expected","meaning":"正如可以預料","examples":[{"en":"As might be expected, European settlers cultivated familiar crops.","zh":"正如可以預料，歐洲定居者種植熟悉的作物。"},{"en":"As might be expected means as people would naturally predict in that situation.","zh":"as might be expected 指正如人們在該情況下自然會預測的那樣。"},{"en":"As might be expected, students revise harder when an important exam is near.","zh":"正如可以預料，重要考試臨近時學生會更努力溫習。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the result is not surprising.","zh":"這個短語顯示結果並不令人意外。"},{"en":"It is useful when an action follows logically from people’s needs or habits.","zh":"當行動合乎人們需要或習慣時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"settle on the east coast of","meaning":"在……東岸定居","examples":[{"en":"Europeans settled on the east coast of the United States.","zh":"歐洲人在美國東岸定居。"},{"en":"To settle on the east coast of a place means to begin living permanently along its eastern shoreline.","zh":"settle on the east coast of a place 指開始在某地東部海岸長期居住。"},{"en":"Fishing families may settle on the east coast of an island because the sea provides work.","zh":"漁民家庭可能在島嶼東岸定居，因為海洋提供工作。"},{"en":"Where settlers live affects what crops they grow and whom they meet.","zh":"定居者住在哪裡會影響他們種甚麼作物和遇見甚麼人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both location and permanent residence.","zh":"這個短語同時描述位置和永久居住。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cultivate crops","meaning":"種植農作物","examples":[{"en":"The settlers cultivated crops like wheat and apples.","zh":"定居者種植小麥和蘋果等農作物。"},{"en":"To cultivate crops means to grow plants for food, trade, or other human use.","zh":"cultivate crops 指為食物、貿易或其他人類用途而種植植物。"},{"en":"Farmers cultivate crops by preparing soil, planting seeds, watering plants, and harvesting.","zh":"農民透過整地、播種、澆水和收割來種植農作物。"},{"en":"If settlers cultivate familiar crops in a new land, they may change the local environment.","zh":"如果定居者在新土地種植熟悉作物，他們可能改變本地環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised farming, not wild plant growth.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的農業，而不是野生植物生長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bring with them","meaning":"隨身帶來","examples":[{"en":"Europeans cultivated crops that they had brought with them.","zh":"歐洲人種植他們隨身帶來的作物。"},{"en":"To bring something with them means to carry it when people move to another place.","zh":"bring something with them 指人們搬到另一地方時把某物帶去。"},{"en":"A family moving abroad may bring recipes, books, and family photos with them.","zh":"搬到海外的家庭可能隨身帶來食譜、書本和家庭照片。"},{"en":"What migrants bring with them can shape life in the new community.","zh":"移民隨身帶來的事物可以塑造新社區的生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes carrying objects, habits, or ideas during movement.","zh":"這個短語描述在移動中帶着物件、習慣或思想。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"European weeds","meaning":"歐洲雜草","examples":[{"en":"European weeds also fared well in the New World.","zh":"歐洲雜草在新世界也生長良好。"},{"en":"European weeds are unwanted plants from Europe that spread in new environments.","zh":"European weeds 指來自歐洲、在新環境中擴散的不受歡迎植物。"},{"en":"Weeds may arrive with crop seeds, animal feed, or soil stuck to tools.","zh":"雜草可能隨農作物種子、動物飼料或黏在工具上的泥土到達。"},{"en":"If European weeds grow faster than native plants, they can change farmland and roadsides.","zh":"如果歐洲雜草比本土植物生長更快，它們可以改變農田和路旁環境。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to introduced plants that spread without being deliberately cultivated.","zh":"這個短語指未被有意種植但擴散開來的外來植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"prefer to uproot","meaning":"寧願連根拔起","examples":[{"en":"The colonists preferred to uproot unwanted weeds.","zh":"殖民者寧願把不想要的雜草連根拔起。"},{"en":"To prefer to uproot plants means to choose to pull them out by the roots.","zh":"prefer to uproot plants 指選擇把植物連根拔出。"},{"en":"Gardeners may prefer to uproot weeds instead of cutting only the leaves.","zh":"園丁可能寧願連根拔起雜草，而不是只剪掉葉子。"},{"en":"Uprooting removes the root, so the plant is less likely to grow back.","zh":"連根拔起會移除根部，因此植物較不容易再生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing a more complete way to remove plants.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇較徹底的植物移除方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fare well","meaning":"生長良好；發展順利","examples":[{"en":"European weeds fared well in the New World.","zh":"歐洲雜草在新世界生長良好。"},{"en":"To fare well means to do well, succeed, or survive successfully in a situation.","zh":"fare well 指在某情況中表現良好、成功或順利生存。"},{"en":"A small shop may fare well if it offers friendly service and useful products.","zh":"如果小店提供友善服務和實用產品，它可能發展順利。"},{"en":"Plants fare well when the soil, climate, and competition suit them.","zh":"當土壤、氣候和競爭情況適合，植物會生長良好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes successful performance or survival.","zh":"這個短語描述成功表現或生存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"amateur naturalist","meaning":"業餘博物學家","examples":[{"en":"John Josselyn was an Englishman and amateur naturalist.","zh":"John Josselyn 是一名英國人和業餘博物學家。"},{"en":"An amateur naturalist is someone who studies plants, animals, or nature seriously without being a full-time professional scientist.","zh":"amateur naturalist 指認真研究植物、動物或自然，但並非全職專業科學家的人。"},{"en":"A teacher who records local birds every weekend may be an amateur naturalist.","zh":"每週末記錄本地鳥類的老師可以是一名業餘博物學家。"},{"en":"Amateur naturalists can provide useful observations because they notice changes in everyday environments.","zh":"業餘博物學家可以提供有用觀察，因為他們注意日常環境中的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a non-professional but interested observer of nature.","zh":"這個短語描述非專業但對自然感興趣的觀察者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"leave us a list","meaning":"留下一份清單給我們","examples":[{"en":"Josselyn left us a list of plants that had sprung up.","zh":"Josselyn 留下一份清單給我們，記錄那些已冒出的植物。"},{"en":"To leave us a list means to record information that later readers can still use.","zh":"leave us a list 指記錄資料，使後來讀者仍可使用。"},{"en":"A careful teacher may leave us a list of common mistakes for future students.","zh":"細心老師可能為未來學生留下一份常見錯誤清單。"},{"en":"Historical lists help later researchers know what people observed at the time.","zh":"歷史清單幫助後來研究者知道當時人們觀察到甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes written evidence passed down to later people.","zh":"這個短語描述傳給後人的書面證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"spring up","meaning":"冒出；出現","examples":[{"en":"Many plants sprang up after the English arrived.","zh":"英國人抵達後，許多植物冒了出來。"},{"en":"To spring up means to appear, grow, or develop suddenly or quickly.","zh":"spring up 指突然或迅速出現、生長或發展。"},{"en":"New cafés may spring up near a train station after more people move into the area.","zh":"當更多人搬入某區，新咖啡店可能在火車站附近冒出。"},{"en":"Plants spring up when seeds find suitable soil, water, and sunlight.","zh":"當種子遇到合適泥土、水分和陽光，植物就會冒出。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes something appearing in noticeable numbers.","zh":"這個短語常描述某事物以明顯數量出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"couch grass","meaning":"匍匐冰草","examples":[{"en":"Couch grass was one of the European plants found in New England.","zh":"匍匐冰草是在新英格蘭發現的歐洲植物之一。"},{"en":"Couch grass is a tough grass-like weed that can spread quickly through roots.","zh":"couch grass 指一種堅韌、像草的雜草，能透過根部迅速擴散。"},{"en":"A gardener may struggle to remove couch grass because pieces of root can grow again.","zh":"園丁可能難以清除匍匐冰草，因為根部碎片可以再次生長。"},{"en":"If couch grass spreads through a field, it can compete with crops for space and nutrients.","zh":"如果匍匐冰草在田地擴散，它可以與農作物競爭空間和養分。"},{"en":"This phrase names a common weed rather than a crop.","zh":"這個短語命名一種常見雜草，而不是農作物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dandelion","meaning":"蒲公英","examples":[{"en":"Dandelion appeared among the plants introduced to New England.","zh":"蒲公英出現在被引入新英格蘭的植物之中。"},{"en":"A dandelion is a small yellow-flowered plant that often grows in lawns and fields.","zh":"dandelion 指一種開黃色小花、常生長在草坪和田野中的植物。"},{"en":"Children may blow the white seed head of a dandelion and watch the seeds fly away.","zh":"孩子可能吹蒲公英的白色種子球，看着種子飛走。"},{"en":"Because dandelion seeds spread easily, the plant can appear in many new places.","zh":"因為蒲公英種子容易擴散，這種植物可以出現在許多新地方。"},{"en":"This word names a familiar plant that can behave like a weed.","zh":"這個詞命名一種熟悉、可像雜草般生長的植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"shepherd’s purse","meaning":"薺菜","examples":[{"en":"Shepherd’s purse was listed among the plants that had sprung up.","zh":"薺菜被列入那些冒出來的植物之中。"},{"en":"Shepherd’s purse is a small weed with seed pods that look like tiny purses or hearts.","zh":"shepherd’s purse 指一種小型雜草，其種莢像小錢包或心形。"},{"en":"A student may find shepherd’s purse growing beside a path or in disturbed soil.","zh":"學生可能在小路旁或受擾動泥土中發現薺菜。"},{"en":"Like many weeds, shepherd’s purse can spread quickly in open ground.","zh":"像許多雜草一樣，薺菜可以在開闊地迅速擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase names a plant noticed among introduced or spreading weeds.","zh":"這個短語命名一種在外來或擴散雜草中被注意到的植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"groundsel","meaning":"千里光","examples":[{"en":"Groundsel was included in Josselyn’s list of plants.","zh":"千里光被包括在 Josselyn 的植物清單中。"},{"en":"Groundsel is a small weed that often grows in gardens, fields, and disturbed soil.","zh":"groundsel 指一種常在花園、田地和受擾動泥土中生長的小型雜草。"},{"en":"A gardener may pull out groundsel before it produces more seeds.","zh":"園丁可能在千里光產生更多種子前把它拔走。"},{"en":"If groundsel is left alone, it can spread and compete with other plants.","zh":"如果任由千里光生長，它可以擴散並與其他植物競爭。"},{"en":"This word names a common weed recorded in early plant lists.","zh":"這個詞命名一種早期植物清單中記錄的常見雜草。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sow thistle","meaning":"苦苣菜","examples":[{"en":"Sow thistle was one of the weeds found in New England.","zh":"苦苣菜是在新英格蘭發現的雜草之一。"},{"en":"Sow thistle is a weed with soft leaves and yellow flowers that can spread by seed.","zh":"sow thistle 指一種有柔軟葉片和黃色花朵、能以種子擴散的雜草。"},{"en":"Farmers may remove sow thistle because it competes with crops in open fields.","zh":"農民可能清除苦苣菜，因為它在開闊田地中與農作物競爭。"},{"en":"When soil is cleared, sow thistle may grow quickly in the new space.","zh":"當泥土被清理，苦苣菜可能在新空間中迅速生長。"},{"en":"This phrase names a plant often treated as an unwanted weed.","zh":"這個短語命名一種常被視為不受歡迎雜草的植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"chickweed","meaning":"繁縷","examples":[{"en":"Chickweed appeared after English settlement.","zh":"英國人定居後，繁縷出現了。"},{"en":"Chickweed is a small, low-growing plant that often spreads across moist soil.","zh":"chickweed 指一種低矮小植物，常在潮濕泥土上擴散。"},{"en":"A gardener may find chickweed growing between vegetables after rainy weather.","zh":"下雨後，園丁可能在蔬菜之間發現繁縷生長。"},{"en":"Because chickweed grows close to the ground, it can cover open soil quickly.","zh":"因為繁縷貼近地面生長，它可以迅速覆蓋開闊泥土。"},{"en":"This word names a common weed that can spread in disturbed places.","zh":"這個詞命名一種能在受擾動地方擴散的常見雜草。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"plantain","meaning":"車前草","examples":[{"en":"A plantain was named “Englishman’s Foot” by Amerindians.","zh":"一種車前草被美洲原住民稱為「英國人的腳印」。"},{"en":"In this context, plantain is a low-growing weed, not the banana-like fruit.","zh":"在這個語境中，plantain 指低矮雜草，而不是像香蕉的水果。"},{"en":"People may find plantain growing in paths, lawns, and compacted soil where feet often pass.","zh":"人們可能在小路、草坪和常被踩踏的硬實泥土中發現車前草。"},{"en":"Because plantain spread where settlers walked, it became linked with English movement.","zh":"因為車前草在定居者走過的地方擴散，它與英國人的移動聯繫起來。"},{"en":"This word needs context because it can refer to different plants.","zh":"這個詞需要看語境，因為它可以指不同植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be named by","meaning":"由……命名","examples":[{"en":"The plantain was named by the Amerindians of New England and Virginia.","zh":"這種車前草由新英格蘭和維珍尼亞的美洲原住民命名。"},{"en":"To be named by someone means to receive a name from that person or group.","zh":"be named by someone 指由某人或某群體給予名稱。"},{"en":"A new school building may be named by students after a respected teacher.","zh":"一座新校舍可能由學生以一位受尊敬老師命名。"},{"en":"Names often show what people noticed or believed about the thing being named.","zh":"名稱常顯示人們注意到或相信該事物的甚麼特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes who gave a name to something.","zh":"這個短語描述誰給某物命名。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Englishman’s Foot","meaning":"英國人的腳印","examples":[{"en":"The plantain was called “Englishman’s Foot.”","zh":"這種車前草被稱為「英國人的腳印」。"},{"en":"Englishman’s Foot was a name for plantain because it seemed to grow where English settlers walked.","zh":"Englishman’s Foot 是車前草的一個名稱，因為它似乎在英國定居者走過的地方生長。"},{"en":"A community may give a plant a nickname if it reminds people of a particular event or group.","zh":"如果一種植物令人想起某事件或群體，社區可能給它一個外號。"},{"en":"The name connects a spreading plant with the movement of colonists.","zh":"這個名稱把一種擴散植物與殖民者移動連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how local names can record historical observation.","zh":"這個短語顯示本地名稱如何記錄歷史觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Amerindians","meaning":"美洲原住民","examples":[{"en":"Amerindians believed the plant grew where the English had walked.","zh":"美洲原住民相信這種植物在英國人走過的地方生長。"},{"en":"Amerindians means the Indigenous peoples of the Americas.","zh":"Amerindians 指美洲原住民族群。"},{"en":"Amerindians had their own languages, farming systems, beliefs, and trade networks before European arrival.","zh":"在歐洲人到來前，美洲原住民有自己的語言、農業制度、信仰和貿易網絡。"},{"en":"European contact brought disease, violence, land loss, and major cultural change to many Amerindian communities.","zh":"歐洲接觸為許多美洲原住民社群帶來疾病、暴力、土地流失和重大文化變化。"},{"en":"This word refers to Native peoples of the Americas in historical writing.","zh":"這個詞在歷史寫作中指美洲本土民族。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have trodden","meaning":"曾踏過","examples":[{"en":"The plant was believed to grow where the English had trodden.","zh":"人們相信這種植物在英國人曾踏過的地方生長。"},{"en":"Have trodden means have walked on or stepped on a place.","zh":"have trodden 指曾走過或踩過某地方。"},{"en":"Muddy footprints show where children have trodden after playing in the rain.","zh":"泥腳印顯示孩子雨後玩耍時曾踏過哪些地方。"},{"en":"If many people have trodden on soil, the ground may become hard and compacted.","zh":"如果許多人曾踏過泥土，地面可能變硬和壓實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes past movement by foot.","zh":"這個短語描述過去用腳移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"intentionally sow","meaning":"有意播種","examples":[{"en":"European settlers intentionally sowed Old World crop seeds.","zh":"歐洲定居者有意播種舊世界農作物種子。"},{"en":"To intentionally sow seeds means to plant them on purpose.","zh":"intentionally sow seeds 指有目的地播下種子。"},{"en":"A farmer intentionally sows rice seeds when the field is ready.","zh":"當稻田準備好，農民會有意播種稻米種子。"},{"en":"Intentional sowing spreads useful crops, while accidental seed movement may spread weeds.","zh":"有意播種會傳播有用作物，而意外種子移動可能傳播雜草。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planned planting rather than accidental growth.","zh":"這個短語描述有計劃的種植，而非偶然生長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"crop seeds","meaning":"農作物種子","examples":[{"en":"The settlers brought and sowed Old World crop seeds.","zh":"定居者帶來並播種舊世界農作物種子。"},{"en":"Crop seeds are seeds planted to grow food or useful plants.","zh":"crop seeds 指用來種植食物或有用植物的種子。"},{"en":"A gardener may buy crop seeds for tomatoes, beans, or lettuce before spring.","zh":"園丁可能在春天前購買番茄、豆和生菜的農作物種子。"},{"en":"Crop seeds can change farming when they are carried into new environments.","zh":"當農作物種子被帶入新環境，它們可以改變農業。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to seeds meant for cultivated plants, not random wild seeds.","zh":"這個短語指用於栽培植物的種子，而不是隨機野生種子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"unintentionally contaminate","meaning":"無意中污染","examples":[{"en":"The settlers unintentionally contaminated American fields with weed seeds.","zh":"定居者無意中以雜草種子污染了美洲田地。"},{"en":"To unintentionally contaminate something means to pollute or mix it with unwanted material by accident.","zh":"unintentionally contaminate something 指意外地以不想要的物質污染或混入某物。"},{"en":"A student may unintentionally contaminate a science sample by touching it with dirty hands.","zh":"學生可能因用髒手觸碰科學樣本而無意中污染它。"},{"en":"If crop seed bags contain weed seeds, farmers may contaminate fields without knowing it.","zh":"如果農作物種子袋含有雜草種子，農民可能在不知情下污染田地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accidental pollution or unwanted mixing.","zh":"這個短語描述意外污染或不想要的混合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"American fields","meaning":"美洲田地","examples":[{"en":"European weeds spread into American fields.","zh":"歐洲雜草擴散到美洲田地。"},{"en":"American fields are areas of farmland in the Americas where crops are grown.","zh":"American fields 指美洲用來種植農作物的農田地區。"},{"en":"Wheat, maize, or vegetables may grow in American fields depending on region and climate.","zh":"視乎地區和氣候，美洲田地中可能種小麥、粟米或蔬菜。"},{"en":"When foreign weeds enter American fields, they can compete with crops for water and sunlight.","zh":"當外來雜草進入美洲田地，它們可以與作物競爭水分和陽光。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to cultivated land in the Americas.","zh":"這個短語指美洲的耕作土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"weed seeds","meaning":"雜草種子","examples":[{"en":"Weed seeds were unintentionally spread by settlers.","zh":"雜草種子被定居者無意中傳播。"},{"en":"Weed seeds are seeds from unwanted plants that may grow where people do not want them.","zh":"weed seeds 指來自不受歡迎植物、可能在人們不想要的地方生長的種子。"},{"en":"Weed seeds can hide among crop seeds, animal feed, or soil on shoes.","zh":"雜草種子可以藏在農作物種子、動物飼料或鞋上的泥土中。"},{"en":"If weed seeds reach a new field, they may grow faster than the crop plants.","zh":"如果雜草種子到達新田地，它們可能比農作物生長更快。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how unwanted plants begin to spread.","zh":"這個短語解釋不受歡迎植物如何開始擴散。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"strip and burn forests","meaning":"砍伐並焚燒森林","examples":[{"en":"European settlers stripped and burned forests.","zh":"歐洲定居者砍伐並焚燒森林。"},{"en":"To strip and burn forests means to clear trees and vegetation, often by cutting and fire.","zh":"strip and burn forests 指清除樹木和植被，通常透過砍伐和火燒。"},{"en":"Farmers may strip and burn forest land to create open fields for planting.","zh":"農民可能砍伐並焚燒森林土地，以創造開闊田地來種植。"},{"en":"Forest clearing exposes soil and native plants to sunlight, erosion, and grazing animals.","zh":"清除森林會令泥土和本土植物暴露於陽光、侵蝕和放牧動物之下。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a destructive way of turning forest into open land.","zh":"這個短語描述把森林變成開闊土地的破壞性方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"expose something to direct sunlight","meaning":"使……暴露於陽光直射下","examples":[{"en":"Forest clearing exposed native flora to direct sunlight.","zh":"清除森林使本土植物群暴露於陽光直射下。"},{"en":"To expose something to direct sunlight means to remove cover so sunlight reaches it fully.","zh":"expose something to direct sunlight 指移除遮蔽物，令陽光完全照射到某物。"},{"en":"Moving a houseplant from shade to a bright window can expose it to direct sunlight.","zh":"把室內植物從陰涼處移到明亮窗邊，可能使它暴露於陽光直射下。"},{"en":"Plants not adapted to strong light may dry out or die when suddenly exposed.","zh":"不適應強光的植物突然暴露時可能乾枯或死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes removing protection from strong sun.","zh":"這個短語描述移除強烈陽光下的保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"native minor flora","meaning":"本土小型植物群","examples":[{"en":"The native minor flora could not tolerate the new stress.","zh":"本土小型植物群無法承受新的壓力。"},{"en":"Native minor flora means the smaller local plant life naturally growing in an area.","zh":"native minor flora 指某地自然生長的較小型本地植物。"},{"en":"Small wildflowers, grasses, and ground plants can be part of native minor flora.","zh":"小野花、草和地被植物可以是本土小型植物群的一部分。"},{"en":"When forests are cleared, native minor flora may lose shade and protection.","zh":"當森林被清除，本土小型植物群可能失去陰影和保護。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to local small plants, not large trees or imported crops.","zh":"這個短語指本地小型植物，而不是大型樹木或外來作物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hooves and teeth","meaning":"蹄和牙齒","examples":[{"en":"Native plants were exposed to the hooves and teeth of Old World livestock.","zh":"本土植物暴露於舊世界牲畜的蹄和牙齒之下。"},{"en":"Hooves and teeth refer to the trampling and eating effects of grazing animals.","zh":"hooves and teeth 指放牧動物踩踏和啃食造成的影響。"},{"en":"A garden can be damaged by the hooves and teeth of goats if they wander in.","zh":"如果山羊走進花園，牠們的蹄和牙齒可以破壞花園。"},{"en":"Animals with hooves can crush plants, while their teeth remove leaves and stems.","zh":"有蹄動物可以踩碎植物，而牙齒則移除葉和莖。"},{"en":"This phrase vividly describes physical damage caused by livestock.","zh":"這個短語生動描述牲畜造成的身體破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Old World livestock","meaning":"舊世界牲畜","examples":[{"en":"Old World livestock damaged native plants.","zh":"舊世界牲畜破壞了本土植物。"},{"en":"Old World livestock are domesticated farm animals originally from Europe, Asia, or Africa.","zh":"Old World livestock 指原本來自歐洲、亞洲或非洲的馴養農場動物。"},{"en":"Horses, cattle, pigs, sheep, and goats can be examples of Old World livestock.","zh":"馬、牛、豬、羊和山羊都可以是舊世界牲畜的例子。"},{"en":"When Old World livestock entered the Americas, they grazed, trampled plants, and changed landscapes.","zh":"當舊世界牲畜進入美洲，牠們放牧、踩踏植物並改變地貌。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to imported farm animals from the Old World.","zh":"這個短語指來自舊世界的外來農場動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"native flora","meaning":"本土植物群","examples":[{"en":"The native flora struggled under the pressure of imported animals.","zh":"本土植物群在外來動物壓力下艱難生存。"},{"en":"Native flora means the plant life that naturally belongs to a particular region.","zh":"native flora 指自然屬於某一地區的植物生命。"},{"en":"A park may protect native flora by removing invasive plants and limiting grazing.","zh":"公園可能透過移除入侵植物和限制放牧來保護本土植物群。"},{"en":"When imported animals eat or trample local plants, native flora may decline.","zh":"當外來動物啃食或踩踏本地植物，本土植物群可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to local plant life, not introduced species.","zh":"這個短語指本地植物生命，而非外來物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tolerate the stress","meaning":"承受壓力","examples":[{"en":"The native flora could not tolerate the stress.","zh":"本土植物群無法承受這種壓力。"},{"en":"To tolerate the stress means to survive pressure, difficulty, or harmful conditions.","zh":"tolerate the stress 指在壓力、困難或有害條件下仍能存活。"},{"en":"A student may not tolerate the stress of constant exams without rest and support.","zh":"如果沒有休息和支援，學生可能無法承受連續考試的壓力。"},{"en":"Plants may fail to tolerate stress from strong sun, grazing, or poor soil.","zh":"植物可能無法承受強光、放牧或貧瘠土壤造成的壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the ability to endure pressure without serious damage.","zh":"這個短語描述在壓力下不受嚴重傷害地承受的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"imported weeds","meaning":"外來雜草","examples":[{"en":"Imported weeds survived better than native plants.","zh":"外來雜草比本土植物更能存活。"},{"en":"Imported weeds are unwanted plants brought from another region or continent.","zh":"imported weeds 指從另一地區或大陸帶來的不受歡迎植物。"},{"en":"Imported weeds may arrive accidentally with seeds, soil, animals, or cargo.","zh":"外來雜草可能隨種子、泥土、動物或貨物意外到達。"},{"en":"If imported weeds are already adapted to grazing, they may survive where native plants fail.","zh":"如果外來雜草已適應放牧，它們可能在本土植物失敗的地方存活。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to foreign weeds that enter and spread in a new environment.","zh":"這個短語指進入並擴散到新環境的外來雜草。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"grazing animals","meaning":"放牧動物","examples":[{"en":"Imported weeds had lived with grazing animals for thousands of years.","zh":"外來雜草已與放牧動物共同生活數千年。"},{"en":"Grazing animals are animals that feed on grass and low plants.","zh":"grazing animals 指吃草和低矮植物的動物。"},{"en":"Cattle, sheep, goats, and horses are common grazing animals on farms.","zh":"牛、羊、山羊和馬是農場上常見的放牧動物。"},{"en":"Plants that survive grazing animals may regrow after being eaten or avoid being eaten.","zh":"能在放牧動物下生存的植物，可能在被吃後再生，或避免被吃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes animals that shape plant life by feeding on it.","zh":"這個短語描述透過取食塑造植物生命的動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for thousands of years","meaning":"數千年來","examples":[{"en":"The weeds had adapted to grazing animals for thousands of years.","zh":"這些雜草數千年來已適應放牧動物。"},{"en":"For thousands of years means during a very long period of many centuries.","zh":"for thousands of years 指在許多世紀的非常長時期內。"},{"en":"Farmers have saved seeds and improved crops for thousands of years.","zh":"農民數千年來一直保存種子並改良作物。"},{"en":"A habit or adaptation that develops for thousands of years can become very strong.","zh":"一種習慣或適應若發展數千年，可能變得非常強。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long historical time.","zh":"這個短語強調漫長歷史時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be brought ashore","meaning":"被帶上岸","examples":[{"en":"Cattle and horses were brought ashore in the early 1600s.","zh":"牛和馬在十七世紀初被帶上岸。"},{"en":"To be brought ashore means to be carried from a ship onto land.","zh":"be brought ashore 指從船上被帶到陸地。"},{"en":"Supplies may be brought ashore after a boat reaches a small island.","zh":"船抵達小島後，補給品可能被帶上岸。"},{"en":"Once animals are brought ashore, they can begin moving, feeding, and breeding on land.","zh":"動物一旦被帶上岸，就可以開始在陸地移動、覓食和繁殖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arrival from sea to land.","zh":"這個短語描述由海上到陸地的到達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the early 1600s","meaning":"十七世紀初","examples":[{"en":"Cattle and horses arrived in North America in the early 1600s.","zh":"牛和馬在十七世紀初抵達北美洲。"},{"en":"The early 1600s means the first part of the seventeenth century, roughly the years soon after 1600.","zh":"the early 1600s 指十七世紀的早期，大約是 1600 年後不久的年代。"},{"en":"A history teacher may place early colonial events in the early 1600s.","zh":"歷史老師可能把早期殖民事件放在十七世紀初。"},{"en":"Dates like the early 1600s help readers understand the sequence of settlement and ecological change.","zh":"像十七世紀初這樣的日期幫助讀者理解定居和生態變化的先後次序。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate historical period.","zh":"這個短語給出大約的歷史時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hospitable climate and terrain","meaning":"適宜的氣候和地形","examples":[{"en":"Horses found hospitable climate and terrain in North America.","zh":"馬在北美洲找到適宜的氣候和地形。"},{"en":"Hospitable climate and terrain means weather and land conditions that help living things survive and spread.","zh":"hospitable climate and terrain 指有助生物生存和擴散的天氣與土地條件。"},{"en":"A crop may grow well where there is hospitable climate and terrain, such as good rainfall and suitable soil.","zh":"作物可能在有適宜氣候和地形的地方生長良好，例如雨量充足和土壤合適。"},{"en":"When animals find hospitable conditions, their numbers may increase quickly.","zh":"當動物找到適宜條件，其數量可能迅速增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an environment that is welcoming for survival.","zh":"這個短語描述有利於生存的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"wander free","meaning":"自由遊蕩","examples":[{"en":"Many horses wandered free after arriving in North America.","zh":"許多馬抵達北美洲後自由遊蕩。"},{"en":"To wander free means to move around without being tightly controlled or confined.","zh":"wander free 指在沒有嚴格控制或限制下四處移動。"},{"en":"A dog may wander free in a village if no one keeps it behind a gate.","zh":"如果沒有人把狗關在門後，牠可能在村中自由遊蕩。"},{"en":"Animals that wander free can spread into new areas and damage crops.","zh":"自由遊蕩的動物可以擴散到新地區並破壞農作物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uncontrolled movement.","zh":"這個短語描述不受控制的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"little more evidence of","meaning":"幾乎沒有更多……證據","examples":[{"en":"Some animals had little more evidence of human ownership than collars.","zh":"有些動物除了頸圈外，幾乎沒有更多人類擁有的證據。"},{"en":"Little more evidence of something than another thing means almost no proof except that one small sign.","zh":"little more evidence of something than another thing 指除了某個小跡象外，幾乎沒有證明。"},{"en":"The lost bicycle had little more evidence of ownership than a name sticker.","zh":"那架失物單車除了姓名貼紙外，幾乎沒有更多擁有權證據。"},{"en":"If livestock had only collars, people could barely tell who owned them.","zh":"如果牲畜只有頸圈，人們幾乎無法分辨牠們屬於誰。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses how limited the proof was.","zh":"這個短語強調證據非常有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"connection to humanity","meaning":"與人類的聯繫","examples":[{"en":"The collars showed their connection to humanity.","zh":"頸圈顯示牠們與人類的聯繫。"},{"en":"Connection to humanity means a link with human control, care, ownership, or activity.","zh":"connection to humanity 指與人類控制、照料、擁有或活動之間的連繫。"},{"en":"A tag on a stray dog may show its connection to humanity through a former owner.","zh":"流浪狗身上的牌子可能透過前主人顯示牠與人類的聯繫。"},{"en":"Animals can appear wild, but small signs may reveal human involvement.","zh":"動物可能看似野生，但小跡象可以揭示人類參與。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence that something is linked to people.","zh":"這個短語描述某物與人類相連的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"collars with a hook","meaning":"帶鉤的頸圈","examples":[{"en":"The animals wore collars with a hook at the bottom.","zh":"這些動物戴着底部有鉤的頸圈。"},{"en":"Collars with a hook are neck bands fitted with a hooked part that can catch on objects.","zh":"collars with a hook 指裝有鉤形部分、可勾住物件的頸圈。"},{"en":"A farmer might use collars with a hook to stop animals from jumping over fences easily.","zh":"農民可能使用帶鉤的頸圈，以阻止動物輕易跳過圍欄。"},{"en":"If the hook catches on a fence, the animal may be stopped before reaching crops.","zh":"如果鉤勾住圍欄，動物可能在到達農作物前被阻止。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical device used to control livestock movement.","zh":"這個短語描述用來控制牲畜移動的實用裝置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"catch on fences","meaning":"勾住圍欄","examples":[{"en":"The hook could catch on fences when the animals jumped.","zh":"當動物跳起時，鉤可能勾住圍欄。"},{"en":"To catch on fences means to become stuck or hooked on the fence structure.","zh":"catch on fences 指卡住或勾在圍欄結構上。"},{"en":"A schoolbag strap may catch on a fence if a student climbs over it carelessly.","zh":"如果學生不小心爬過圍欄，書包帶可能勾住圍欄。"},{"en":"If an animal’s collar catches on a fence, it may be unable to cross.","zh":"如果動物頸圈勾住圍欄，牠可能無法越過。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something getting hooked or trapped on a barrier.","zh":"這個短語描述某物被屏障勾住或困住。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"leap over","meaning":"跳過","examples":[{"en":"Animals tried to leap over fences to reach crops.","zh":"動物試圖跳過圍欄去接近農作物。"},{"en":"To leap over something means to jump across or above it.","zh":"leap over something 指跳越或跳過某物。"},{"en":"A child may leap over a puddle to keep her shoes dry.","zh":"孩子可能跳過水坑，以免鞋子弄濕。"},{"en":"Animals leap over fences when they want to reach food or escape confinement.","zh":"動物想接近食物或逃離限制時，會跳過圍欄。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong jumping movement across a barrier.","zh":"這個短語描述越過障礙物的強力跳躍動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get at crops","meaning":"接近並吃到農作物","examples":[{"en":"The animals tried to get at crops beyond the fences.","zh":"動物試圖接近並吃到圍欄外的農作物。"},{"en":"To get at crops means to reach them, usually in order to eat or damage them.","zh":"get at crops 指接近農作物，通常是為了吃掉或破壞它們。"},{"en":"A farmer may build a fence so goats cannot get at crops in the vegetable field.","zh":"農民可能建圍欄，讓山羊無法接近並吃到菜田中的農作物。"},{"en":"If animals get at crops, harvests may be reduced or destroyed.","zh":"如果動物吃到農作物，收成可能減少或被摧毀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching protected food plants.","zh":"這個短語描述到達受保護的食用植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"keeping livestock in","meaning":"把牲畜困在裏面","examples":[{"en":"The fences were not mainly for keeping livestock in.","zh":"圍欄主要不是為了把牲畜困在裏面。"},{"en":"Keeping livestock in means preventing farm animals from leaving an enclosed area.","zh":"keeping livestock in 指防止農場動物離開封閉區域。"},{"en":"A farmer repairs a gate because keeping livestock in protects roads and neighbours’ gardens.","zh":"農民修理大門，因為把牲畜困在裏面能保護道路和鄰居花園。"},{"en":"If fences fail at keeping livestock in, animals may wander into dangerous places.","zh":"如果圍欄無法把牲畜困在裏面，動物可能遊蕩到危險地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes confinement of farm animals inside a space.","zh":"這個短語描述把農場動物限制在某空間內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"keeping livestock out","meaning":"把牲畜擋在外面","examples":[{"en":"The fences were for keeping livestock out of fields.","zh":"圍欄是為了把牲畜擋在田地外面。"},{"en":"Keeping livestock out means stopping farm animals from entering a place.","zh":"keeping livestock out 指阻止農場動物進入某地方。"},{"en":"Gardeners may build low fences for keeping livestock out of vegetable beds.","zh":"園丁可能建矮圍欄，把牲畜擋在菜圃外面。"},{"en":"If animals are kept out of fields, crops have a better chance to grow.","zh":"如果動物被擋在田地外，作物較有機會生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protection from animals entering an area.","zh":"這個短語描述防止動物進入某區域的保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Native American resistance","meaning":"美洲原住民的抵抗","examples":[{"en":"Native American resistance to Europeans was ineffective.","zh":"美洲原住民對歐洲人的抵抗是無效的。"},{"en":"Native American resistance means actions by Indigenous peoples to oppose European control, settlement, or expansion.","zh":"Native American resistance 指原住民族反對歐洲控制、定居或擴張的行動。"},{"en":"Resistance can include fighting, refusing cooperation, moving away, or protecting land and culture.","zh":"抵抗可以包括戰鬥、拒絕合作、遷離，或保護土地和文化。"},{"en":"Disease, weapons, land loss, and political pressure made resistance much harder.","zh":"疾病、武器、土地流失和政治壓力令抵抗困難得多。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to Indigenous opposition in the context of colonisation.","zh":"這個短語指殖民語境中的原住民反抗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ineffective","meaning":"無效的","examples":[{"en":"Their resistance was ineffective against European expansion.","zh":"他們對歐洲擴張的抵抗是無效的。"},{"en":"Ineffective means not producing the intended result.","zh":"ineffective 指未能產生預期結果。"},{"en":"A warning sign is ineffective if drivers ignore it and continue speeding.","zh":"如果司機無視警告牌並繼續超速，該警告牌就是無效的。"},{"en":"Resistance may become ineffective when disease and hunger weaken a community first.","zh":"當疾病和飢餓先削弱一個社群，抵抗可能變得無效。"},{"en":"This word describes an action that fails to work well.","zh":"這個詞描述未能有效發揮作用的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Indigenous peoples","meaning":"原住民族","examples":[{"en":"Indigenous peoples suffered greatly after European arrival.","zh":"歐洲人到來後，原住民族遭受巨大苦難。"},{"en":"Indigenous peoples are the original peoples of a land, with long-standing cultural, historical, and spiritual ties to it.","zh":"Indigenous peoples 指一片土地的原本民族，與該地有長久的文化、歷史和精神連繫。"},{"en":"Indigenous peoples may protect traditional languages, land knowledge, and community practices.","zh":"原住民族可能保護傳統語言、土地知識和社群做法。"},{"en":"Colonisation often harmed Indigenous peoples through disease, violence, and land loss.","zh":"殖民常透過疾病、暴力和土地流失傷害原住民族。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to native communities connected deeply to their ancestral lands.","zh":"這個短語指與祖傳土地有深厚連繫的本土社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"suffer from","meaning":"遭受……","examples":[{"en":"Indigenous peoples suffered from violence and disease.","zh":"原住民族遭受暴力和疾病之苦。"},{"en":"To suffer from something means to be harmed by an illness, problem, or difficult condition.","zh":"suffer from something 指受到疾病、問題或困難情況傷害。"},{"en":"Students may suffer from stress when they face too many tests at once.","zh":"當學生同時面對太多測驗，他們可能遭受壓力。"},{"en":"Communities can suffer from disease, poverty, violence, or loss of land.","zh":"社群可能遭受疾病、貧窮、暴力或土地流失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being negatively affected by something.","zh":"這個短語描述受到某事負面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"white brutality","meaning":"白人的殘暴行為","examples":[{"en":"White brutality was one factor in Indigenous suffering.","zh":"白人的殘暴行為是原住民族受苦的一個因素。"},{"en":"White brutality means cruel violence or harsh treatment by European colonists or white settlers.","zh":"white brutality 指歐洲殖民者或白人定居者的殘酷暴力或嚴苛對待。"},{"en":"Historical accounts of forced removal can show white brutality toward Indigenous communities.","zh":"關於強迫遷移的歷史記載可以顯示對原住民社群的白人殘暴行為。"},{"en":"Brutality can destroy families, weaken resistance, and leave long-term trauma.","zh":"殘暴行為可以摧毀家庭、削弱抵抗並留下長期創傷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes violent colonial treatment in blunt moral terms.","zh":"這個短語以直接道德語氣描述殖民暴力對待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"alcoholism","meaning":"酗酒問題","examples":[{"en":"Alcoholism contributed to the damage suffered by Indigenous communities.","zh":"酗酒問題加深了原住民社群所受的傷害。"},{"en":"Alcoholism is a serious condition in which a person becomes dependent on alcohol.","zh":"alcoholism 指一個人對酒精產生依賴的嚴重狀況。"},{"en":"A family may suffer when alcoholism leads to poor health, lost income, and conflict at home.","zh":"當酗酒導致健康變差、收入流失和家庭衝突，家庭可能受苦。"},{"en":"In damaged communities, alcoholism can worsen existing social and emotional problems.","zh":"在受創社群中，酗酒問題可以加劇既有社會和情感問題。"},{"en":"This word describes harmful dependence on alcohol, not simply occasional drinking.","zh":"這個詞描述有害的酒精依賴，而不只是偶爾喝酒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"driving off of game","meaning":"驅趕獵物","examples":[{"en":"The killing and driving off of game harmed Indigenous livelihoods.","zh":"獵物被殺和被驅趕傷害了原住民生計。"},{"en":"Driving off of game means forcing wild animals away from an area where people hunt them for food.","zh":"driving off of game 指把人們用來狩獵取食的野生動物趕離某地。"},{"en":"If construction drives off deer from a forest, hunters may lose an important food source.","zh":"如果建設工程把鹿趕離森林，獵人可能失去重要食物來源。"},{"en":"When game is driven off, communities that depend on hunting may face hunger and hardship.","zh":"當獵物被驅趕，依賴狩獵的社群可能面對飢餓和困苦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes loss of wild animals through disturbance or force.","zh":"這個短語描述野生動物因干擾或力量而流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"expropriation of farmland","meaning":"侵佔農地","examples":[{"en":"The expropriation of farmland weakened Indigenous communities.","zh":"侵佔農地削弱了原住民社群。"},{"en":"Expropriation of farmland means taking farmland away from its users or owners, often by authority or force.","zh":"expropriation of farmland 指通常由權力或武力把農地從使用者或擁有人手中取走。"},{"en":"If a village loses farmland to a development project, families may lose food and income.","zh":"如果村莊因發展項目失去農地，家庭可能失去食物和收入。"},{"en":"Taking farmland can weaken communities because land supports work, food, and identity.","zh":"奪走農地可以削弱社群，因為土地支撐工作、食物和身份。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the forced or official removal of land rights.","zh":"這個短語描述被迫或官方地移除土地權利。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"insufficient to explain","meaning":"不足以解釋","examples":[{"en":"These factors were insufficient to explain the degree of defeat.","zh":"這些因素不足以解釋他們敗亡的程度。"},{"en":"Insufficient to explain means not enough to fully account for why something happened.","zh":"insufficient to explain 指不足以完整說明某事為何發生。"},{"en":"Low marks alone are insufficient to explain why a student has lost confidence.","zh":"低分本身不足以解釋學生為何失去信心。"},{"en":"If several causes still do not explain the full result, another major factor may be missing.","zh":"如果幾個原因仍不能解釋完整結果，可能缺少另一個主要因素。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an explanation is incomplete.","zh":"這個短語顯示解釋並不完整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"degree of their defeat","meaning":"他們敗亡的程度","examples":[{"en":"Germs help explain the degree of their defeat.","zh":"病菌有助解釋他們敗亡的程度。"},{"en":"The degree of their defeat means how severe or complete their loss was.","zh":"degree of their defeat 指他們失敗有多嚴重或多徹底。"},{"en":"In a sports match, the score can show the degree of a team’s defeat.","zh":"在體育比賽中，比分可以顯示一隊敗北的程度。"},{"en":"In history, disease can make defeat more severe by weakening people before conflict begins.","zh":"在歷史中，疾病可以在衝突開始前削弱人群，使敗亡更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the extent of loss, not just the fact that loss happened.","zh":"這個短語著重失敗的程度，而不只是失敗這個事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the crucial factor","meaning":"關鍵因素","examples":[{"en":"The crucial factor was germs.","zh":"關鍵因素是病菌。"},{"en":"The crucial factor is the most important cause or element in a situation.","zh":"crucial factor 指某情況中最重要的原因或元素。"},{"en":"In a student’s improvement, the crucial factor may be regular feedback rather than longer study hours.","zh":"在學生進步中，關鍵因素可能是定期回饋，而不是更長學習時間。"},{"en":"When one factor changes the whole result, it is crucial.","zh":"當一個因素改變整個結果，它就是關鍵的。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main reason something happened.","zh":"這個短語指出某事發生的主要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"infectious diseases","meaning":"傳染病","examples":[{"en":"Infectious diseases devastated Native American populations.","zh":"傳染病摧毀了美洲原住民人口。"},{"en":"Infectious diseases are illnesses that can spread from one person, animal, or environment to another.","zh":"infectious diseases 指可以由一個人、動物或環境傳到另一方的疾病。"},{"en":"Flu and measles are infectious diseases because they can pass between people.","zh":"流感和麻疹是傳染病，因為它們可以在人與人之間傳播。"},{"en":"When infectious diseases enter a population with little immunity, deaths can rise quickly.","zh":"當傳染病進入免疫力低的人群，死亡人數可以迅速上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes diseases that spread through contact, carriers, or surroundings.","zh":"這個短語描述透過接觸、載體或環境傳播的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mow down","meaning":"大量殺死；摧毀","examples":[{"en":"Smallpox mowed down Native Americans.","zh":"天花大量殺死了美洲原住民。"},{"en":"To mow down people means to kill or defeat many of them quickly and brutally.","zh":"mow down people 指迅速而殘酷地殺死或擊敗大量人。"},{"en":"A deadly epidemic can mow down a village if people have no protection or medicine.","zh":"如果人們沒有保護或藥物，致命流行病可以摧毀整個村莊。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a force cutting through people as if cutting grass.","zh":"這個短語暗示一股力量像割草一樣掃過人群。"},{"en":"It is a strong expression used for severe destruction.","zh":"它是用於嚴重破壞的強烈表達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"first recorded pandemic","meaning":"首次有記錄的大流行病","examples":[{"en":"The first recorded pandemic occurred in the early 1630s.","zh":"首次有記錄的大流行病發生於十七世紀三十年代初。"},{"en":"The first recorded pandemic means the earliest large disease outbreak documented in written records.","zh":"first recorded pandemic 指書面記錄中最早的大型疾病爆發。"},{"en":"A historian may study the first recorded pandemic in a region by reading letters and official reports.","zh":"歷史學家可能透過閱讀書信和官方報告，研究某地首次有記錄的大流行病。"},{"en":"Written records help show when a disease spread widely and whom it affected.","zh":"書面記錄有助顯示疾病何時廣泛傳播及影響誰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the earliest known documented widespread outbreak.","zh":"這個短語描述已知最早、有文獻記載的廣泛疫情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"detonate among","meaning":"在……之中爆發","examples":[{"en":"The disease detonated among the Algonquin of Massachusetts.","zh":"這種疾病在麻省的阿爾岡昆人之中爆發。"},{"en":"To detonate among a group means to break out suddenly and violently within that group.","zh":"detonate among a group 指在某群體中突然且猛烈地爆發。"},{"en":"A rumour can detonate among students if it spreads quickly through social media.","zh":"如果謠言透過社交媒體迅速傳播，它可以在學生之中爆發。"},{"en":"When a disease detonates among people with no immunity, it can cause sudden mass suffering.","zh":"當疾病在沒有免疫力的人群中爆發，它可以造成突然而大規模的苦難。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an explosive image of rapid spread.","zh":"這個短語以爆炸意象描寫快速擴散。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Algonquin","meaning":"阿爾岡昆人","examples":[{"en":"The pandemic spread among the Algonquin of Massachusetts.","zh":"這場大流行病在麻省的阿爾岡昆人之中傳播。"},{"en":"The Algonquin were Indigenous peoples connected with parts of northeastern North America.","zh":"Algonquin 指與北美東北部部分地區有關的原住民族群。"},{"en":"A history lesson may mention the Algonquin when discussing early contact between Europeans and Native peoples.","zh":"歷史課討論歐洲人與原住民早期接觸時，可能提及阿爾岡昆人。"},{"en":"Diseases introduced by outsiders severely harmed many Indigenous groups, including Algonquin communities.","zh":"外來者帶來的疾病嚴重傷害許多原住民族群，包括阿爾岡昆社群。"},{"en":"This word refers to a Native people in the historical context of North America.","zh":"這個詞在北美歷史語境中指一個原住民族。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Plymouth Plantation","meaning":"普利茅斯殖民地","examples":[{"en":"William Bradford of Plymouth Plantation described the disease.","zh":"普利茅斯殖民地的 William Bradford 描述了這種疾病。"},{"en":"Plymouth Plantation was an early English settlement in North America.","zh":"Plymouth Plantation 是北美早期英國殖民聚落。"},{"en":"A historian may use writings from Plymouth Plantation to understand early colonial life.","zh":"歷史學家可能使用普利茅斯殖民地的文字記錄來理解早期殖民生活。"},{"en":"Accounts from settlements can record disease, conflict, farming, and contact with Indigenous peoples.","zh":"殖民聚落的記載可以記錄疾病、衝突、農業和與原住民的接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase names a historical colonial community and source of records.","zh":"這個短語命名一個歷史殖民社群和記錄來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"victims","meaning":"受害者","examples":[{"en":"The victims were unable to help one another.","zh":"受害者無法互相幫助。"},{"en":"Victims are people who are harmed by disease, violence, accidents, or unfair treatment.","zh":"victims 指受到疾病、暴力、意外或不公平對待傷害的人。"},{"en":"After a flood, victims may need food, shelter, medicine, and emotional support.","zh":"水災後，受害者可能需要食物、住所、藥物和情感支援。"},{"en":"When many victims are sick at once, communities may struggle to care for them.","zh":"當許多受害者同時患病，社群可能難以照顧他們。"},{"en":"This word focuses on people who suffer harm.","zh":"這個詞著重受傷害的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not able to help one another","meaning":"無法互相幫助","examples":[{"en":"The victims were not able to help one another.","zh":"受害者無法互相幫助。"},{"en":"Not able to help one another means people cannot give each other support because they are all too weak, busy, or affected.","zh":"not able to help one another 指人們因全都太虛弱、忙亂或受影響而不能互相支援。"},{"en":"During a serious flu outbreak, family members may not be able to help one another if everyone is sick.","zh":"在嚴重流感爆發期間，如果每個人都生病，家庭成員可能無法互相幫助。"},{"en":"When mutual help collapses, a crisis becomes much more dangerous.","zh":"當互助崩潰，危機會變得危險得多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a situation where shared suffering prevents support.","zh":"這個短語描述共同受苦令人無法提供支援的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"bury the dead","meaning":"埋葬死者","examples":[{"en":"Some communities could not even bury the dead.","zh":"有些社群甚至無法埋葬死者。"},{"en":"To bury the dead means to place dead bodies in the ground or give them funeral treatment.","zh":"bury the dead 指把遺體埋入地下或進行喪葬處理。"},{"en":"After a disaster, volunteers may help families bury the dead with dignity.","zh":"災難後，義工可能幫助家庭有尊嚴地埋葬死者。"},{"en":"If disease kills too many people at once, even burial can become impossible.","zh":"如果疾病一次殺死太多人，甚至埋葬也可能變得不可能。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the extreme seriousness of a crisis.","zh":"這個短語顯示危機的極端嚴重性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"missionaries and traders","meaning":"傳教士和商人","examples":[{"en":"Missionaries and traders told the same story about smallpox.","zh":"傳教士和商人講述了關於天花的同一個故事。"},{"en":"Missionaries and traders are people who travel to spread religion or conduct business.","zh":"missionaries and traders 指為傳播宗教或做生意而旅行的人。"},{"en":"Missionaries may record local conditions, while traders may report what they see along trade routes.","zh":"傳教士可能記錄本地情況，而商人可能報告他們在貿易路線上看到的事情。"},{"en":"Because they travelled widely, missionaries and traders often carried news from one place to another.","zh":"因為他們廣泛旅行，傳教士和商人常把消息從一地帶到另一地。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to two travelling groups who could report events from the interior.","zh":"這個短語指能從內陸報告事件的兩類旅行群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"venture into","meaning":"冒險進入","examples":[{"en":"They ventured into the American interior.","zh":"他們冒險進入美洲內陸。"},{"en":"To venture into a place means to go there despite difficulty, distance, or risk.","zh":"venture into a place 指儘管有困難、距離或風險仍前往某地。"},{"en":"Hikers may venture into a remote forest only after preparing maps, food, and water.","zh":"遠足者可能在準備地圖、食物和水後，才冒險進入偏遠森林。"},{"en":"People who venture into unknown areas may discover new information but also face danger.","zh":"冒險進入未知地區的人可能發現新資料，但也面對危險。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests bold or risky movement into a place.","zh":"這個短語暗示大膽或帶風險地進入某地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"American interior","meaning":"美洲內陸","examples":[{"en":"Diseases spread into the American interior.","zh":"疾病傳入美洲內陸。"},{"en":"The American interior means the inland parts of the Americas away from the coast.","zh":"American interior 指遠離海岸的美洲內陸地區。"},{"en":"Traders moving away from ports could carry goods and diseases into the American interior.","zh":"離開港口的商人可能把貨物和疾病帶入美洲內陸。"},{"en":"Once disease entered the interior, communities far from the coast could still be affected.","zh":"一旦疾病進入內陸，遠離海岸的社群仍可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts inland regions with coastal settlements.","zh":"這個短語把內陸地區與沿海聚落作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"appalling story","meaning":"令人震驚的故事","examples":[{"en":"They told the same appalling story about disease and death.","zh":"他們講述了同一個關於疾病和死亡的令人震驚的故事。"},{"en":"An appalling story is a shocking and deeply upsetting account of something terrible.","zh":"appalling story 指對可怕事情的震撼且令人極度不安的描述。"},{"en":"A report about children lacking clean water can be an appalling story of neglect.","zh":"一份關於兒童缺乏潔淨食水的報告，可以是忽視造成的令人震驚故事。"},{"en":"Appalling stories often force readers to face suffering they might otherwise ignore.","zh":"令人震驚的故事常迫使讀者面對他們本可能忽視的苦難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a story that shocks because the harm is severe.","zh":"這個短語描述因傷害嚴重而令人震驚的故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"indigenes","meaning":"原住民","examples":[{"en":"Smallpox devastated the indigenes of North America.","zh":"天花摧毀了北美洲原住民。"},{"en":"Indigenes are the native people originally belonging to a place.","zh":"indigenes 指原本屬於某地的本土人民。"},{"en":"In historical writing, indigenes may refer to Indigenous communities before colonisation.","zh":"在歷史寫作中，indigenes 可指殖民前的原住民社群。"},{"en":"When outsiders arrive with disease and weapons, indigenes may suffer severe losses.","zh":"當外來者帶着疾病和武器到來，原住民可能遭受嚴重損失。"},{"en":"This word is a formal term for native inhabitants.","zh":"這個詞是指本土居民的正式用語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"epidemic","meaning":"流行病","examples":[{"en":"The epidemic destroyed large parts of several communities.","zh":"這場流行病摧毀了幾個社群的大部分。"},{"en":"An epidemic is a disease outbreak that spreads quickly among many people in a region.","zh":"epidemic 指在某地區大量人口之間迅速傳播的疾病爆發。"},{"en":"Schools may close during an epidemic to reduce contact among students.","zh":"在流行病期間，學校可能停課以減少學生之間的接觸。"},{"en":"An epidemic can overwhelm families, hospitals, and burial practices.","zh":"流行病可以壓垮家庭、醫院和喪葬做法。"},{"en":"This word describes a serious spread of disease within a population.","zh":"這個詞描述疾病在人群中的嚴重傳播。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"destroy half the Cherokee","meaning":"摧毀一半切羅基人","examples":[{"en":"The epidemic destroyed half the Cherokee in 1738.","zh":"這場流行病在 1738 年摧毀了一半切羅基人。"},{"en":"To destroy half the Cherokee means to kill or wipe out around half of the Cherokee people in that context.","zh":"destroy half the Cherokee 指在該語境中殺死或消滅約一半切羅基人。"},{"en":"A disease that destroys half a village leaves almost every family grieving.","zh":"摧毀半個村莊人口的疾病，會令幾乎每個家庭都陷入悲痛。"},{"en":"Losing half a population can break leadership, farming, defence, and family life.","zh":"失去一半人口可以破壞領導、農業、防衛和家庭生活。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the extreme demographic damage caused by disease.","zh":"這個短語顯示疾病造成的極端人口傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"entire population","meaning":"全部人口","examples":[{"en":"The disease may have killed half the entire population in some regions.","zh":"這種疾病可能在某些地區殺死了全部人口的一半。"},{"en":"Entire population means all the people living in a particular place or group.","zh":"entire population 指生活在某地方或群體中的所有人。"},{"en":"A city survey may count the entire population, not only schoolchildren or workers.","zh":"城市調查可能統計全部人口，而不只是學童或工人。"},{"en":"When a disease affects the entire population, no household may be untouched.","zh":"當疾病影響全部人口，可能沒有家庭能置身事外。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the whole group is being considered.","zh":"這個短語強調正在考慮整個群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"high plains","meaning":"高原地區","examples":[{"en":"Smallpox spread among people of the high plains.","zh":"天花在高原地區的人群中傳播。"},{"en":"High plains are broad, flat or gently rolling areas of land at relatively high elevation.","zh":"high plains 指海拔較高、廣闊平坦或微微起伏的土地。"},{"en":"Communities on high plains may depend on grazing, hunting, or farming suited to open land.","zh":"高原地區社群可能依賴適合開闊土地的放牧、狩獵或農業。"},{"en":"Disease can spread across high plains through travel, trade, and contact between groups.","zh":"疾病可以透過旅行、貿易和群體接觸在高原地區傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to elevated open land rather than mountains or coasts.","zh":"這個短語指高海拔開闊土地，而不是山脈或海岸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"export of native animals","meaning":"本土動物輸出","examples":[{"en":"The export of America’s native animals had limited impact.","zh":"美洲本土動物輸出的影響有限。"},{"en":"Export of native animals means sending animals originally from one region to other parts of the world.","zh":"export of native animals 指把原本來自某地區的動物送往世界其他地方。"},{"en":"A country may control the export of native animals to protect endangered species.","zh":"一個國家可能管制本土動物輸出，以保護瀕危物種。"},{"en":"If exported animals do not spread widely, their impact on new ecosystems may be small.","zh":"如果輸出的動物沒有廣泛擴散，它們對新生態系統的影響可能很小。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the movement of local animals outward.","zh":"這個短語描述本地動物向外移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"revolutionise agriculture","meaning":"徹底改變農業","examples":[{"en":"American animals did not revolutionise Old World agriculture.","zh":"美洲動物沒有徹底改變舊世界農業。"},{"en":"To revolutionise agriculture means to change farming completely and dramatically.","zh":"revolutionise agriculture 指完全而劇烈地改變農業。"},{"en":"Irrigation systems can revolutionise agriculture in dry regions by making crops possible.","zh":"灌溉系統可以在乾旱地區使種植成為可能，從而徹底改變農業。"},{"en":"A new crop or animal revolutionises farming only if it changes production on a large scale.","zh":"新作物或動物只有在大規模改變生產時，才算徹底改變農業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major transformation in farming.","zh":"這個短語描述農業上的重大轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ecosystems","meaning":"生態系統","examples":[{"en":"The export of American animals did not transform Old World ecosystems.","zh":"美洲動物輸出沒有改造舊世界生態系統。"},{"en":"Ecosystems are communities of living things and the physical environments they interact with.","zh":"ecosystems 指生物群落及其互動的物理環境。"},{"en":"A pond ecosystem includes fish, plants, insects, water, sunlight, and mud.","zh":"池塘生態系統包括魚、植物、昆蟲、水、陽光和泥。"},{"en":"When a new species enters an ecosystem, it can affect food chains and habitats.","zh":"當新物種進入生態系統，它可以影響食物鏈和棲息地。"},{"en":"This word describes connected natural systems, not isolated organisms.","zh":"這個詞描述互相連接的自然系統，而不是孤立生物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"introduction of European animals","meaning":"歐洲動物的引入","examples":[{"en":"The introduction of European animals changed the New World greatly.","zh":"歐洲動物的引入極大改變了新世界。"},{"en":"Introduction of European animals means bringing animals from Europe or the Old World into a new region.","zh":"introduction of European animals 指把來自歐洲或舊世界的動物帶入新地區。"},{"en":"The introduction of horses changed transport, hunting, and warfare in parts of the Americas.","zh":"馬的引入改變了美洲部分地區的交通、狩獵和戰爭。"},{"en":"Imported animals can transform landscapes by grazing, trampling, breeding, and spreading.","zh":"外來動物可以透過放牧、踩踏、繁殖和擴散改變地貌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the arrival and establishment of foreign animals.","zh":"這個短語描述外來動物的到來和定居。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"establish themselves","meaning":"站穩腳跟；定居繁衍","examples":[{"en":"Some American animals established themselves outside the Americas.","zh":"有些美洲動物在美洲以外站穩腳跟。"},{"en":"To establish themselves means to survive, reproduce, and become settled in a new place.","zh":"establish themselves 指在新地方生存、繁殖並穩定下來。"},{"en":"A small business establishes itself when local customers begin to trust and use it regularly.","zh":"當本地顧客開始信任並經常光顧，小企業就站穩腳跟。"},{"en":"Animals establish themselves if the climate, food, and predators allow them to survive.","zh":"如果氣候、食物和捕食者條件容許，動物便能定居繁衍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming successfully rooted in a new environment.","zh":"這個短語描述在新環境中成功紮根。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"east of the Atlantic","meaning":"大西洋以東","examples":[{"en":"Some American animals established themselves east of the Atlantic.","zh":"有些美洲動物在大西洋以東站穩腳跟。"},{"en":"East of the Atlantic means on the European, African, or Old World side of the Atlantic Ocean.","zh":"east of the Atlantic 指在大西洋東側，即歐洲、非洲或舊世界一邊。"},{"en":"Crops that moved east of the Atlantic entered farms and kitchens in Europe and Africa.","zh":"移到大西洋以東的作物進入了歐洲和非洲的農田與廚房。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show direction in exchanges between the Americas and the Old World.","zh":"這個短語有助顯示美洲與舊世界交換中的方向。"},{"en":"This expression locates something on the eastern side of the Atlantic world.","zh":"這個表達定位於大西洋世界的東側。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"west of the Pacific","meaning":"太平洋以西","examples":[{"en":"Some American animals spread west of the Pacific.","zh":"有些美洲動物擴散到太平洋以西。"},{"en":"West of the Pacific means in regions on the western side of the Pacific Ocean, such as parts of Asia or Oceania depending on context.","zh":"west of the Pacific 指在太平洋西側地區，例如視乎語境可指亞洲或大洋洲部分地區。"},{"en":"Goods moving west of the Pacific may reach Asian ports after long sea journeys.","zh":"移往太平洋以西的貨物，可能經長途海上旅程抵達亞洲港口。"},{"en":"Directional phrases like this help track global movement across oceans.","zh":"這類方向短語幫助追蹤跨海洋的全球移動。"},{"en":"This phrase places movement beyond the Pacific toward its western side.","zh":"這個短語把移動定位於越過太平洋往其西側。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"not make much of a difference","meaning":"沒有造成太大分別","examples":[{"en":"The spread of these animals did not make much of a difference.","zh":"這些動物的擴散沒有造成太大分別。"},{"en":"To not make much of a difference means to have little real effect on the result.","zh":"not make much of a difference 指對結果沒有多少實質影響。"},{"en":"Buying one extra notebook may not make much of a difference if the student still does not study.","zh":"如果學生仍不學習，多買一本筆記簿可能沒有造成太大分別。"},{"en":"A change matters only if it affects behaviour, outcomes, or conditions noticeably.","zh":"只有當改變明顯影響行為、結果或條件，它才算重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited impact.","zh":"這個短語描述有限影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be raised in","meaning":"在……被飼養","examples":[{"en":"Some American domesticated animals are raised in the Old World.","zh":"有些美洲馴養動物在舊世界被飼養。"},{"en":"To be raised in a place means to be kept, cared for, and grown there.","zh":"be raised in a place 指在某地被飼養、照料並長大。"},{"en":"Chickens may be raised in small farms, large farms, or family yards.","zh":"雞可能在小農場、大農場或家庭院子中被飼養。"},{"en":"Animals raised in a new region may become part of local farming or food culture.","zh":"在新地區被飼養的動物，可能成為本地農業或飲食文化的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where animals are reared.","zh":"這個短語描述動物在哪裡被飼養。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"displace chickens and geese","meaning":"取代雞和鵝","examples":[{"en":"Turkeys have not displaced chickens and geese.","zh":"火雞沒有取代雞和鵝。"},{"en":"To displace chickens and geese means to replace them as the main birds people raise or eat.","zh":"displace chickens and geese 指取代雞和鵝成為人們主要飼養或食用的禽鳥。"},{"en":"A new product displaces an old one when customers stop buying the old version.","zh":"當顧客停止購買舊版本，新產品就取代舊產品。"},{"en":"Turkeys may become popular, but they did not remove chickens and geese from ordinary farming.","zh":"火雞可能變得受歡迎，但並沒有把雞和鵝從一般農業中移走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes replacement, not simple addition.","zh":"這個短語描述取代，而不是簡單加入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"prove useful in laboratories","meaning":"在實驗室證明有用","examples":[{"en":"Guinea pigs have proved useful in laboratories.","zh":"天竺鼠已在實驗室證明有用。"},{"en":"To prove useful in laboratories means to show practical value for scientific experiments or research.","zh":"prove useful in laboratories 指顯示出對科學實驗或研究有實際價值。"},{"en":"A simple measuring tool can prove useful in laboratories if it gives reliable results.","zh":"如果簡單量度工具能給出可靠結果，它可以在實驗室證明有用。"},{"en":"Animals used in research may help scientists study medicine, disease, or biology.","zh":"研究中使用的動物可能幫助科學家研究藥物、疾病或生物學。"},{"en":"This phrase describes usefulness confirmed by scientific work.","zh":"這個短語描述由科學工作證實的用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"usurp rabbits","meaning":"取代兔子","examples":[{"en":"Guinea pigs have not usurped rabbits in butcher shops.","zh":"天竺鼠沒有在肉店取代兔子。"},{"en":"To usurp rabbits means to take the place or role that rabbits used to have.","zh":"usurp rabbits 指奪取或取代兔子原本的位置或角色。"},{"en":"A new team leader may usurp an old leader’s influence if everyone starts following the new person.","zh":"如果大家開始跟隨新領袖，新組長可能取代舊領袖的影響力。"},{"en":"Guinea pigs may be used in laboratories, but they did not replace rabbits as common meat.","zh":"天竺鼠可能用於實驗室，但沒有取代兔子成為常見肉類。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking over another thing’s position.","zh":"這個短語描述接管另一事物的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"butcher shops","meaning":"肉店","examples":[{"en":"Guinea pigs did not replace rabbits in butcher shops.","zh":"天竺鼠沒有在肉店取代兔子。"},{"en":"Butcher shops are shops that sell meat, often cut and prepared by a butcher.","zh":"butcher shops 指售賣肉類的店舖，通常由屠夫切割和處理肉類。"},{"en":"A family may buy beef, pork, chicken, or rabbit from butcher shops.","zh":"家庭可能在肉店購買牛肉、豬肉、雞肉或兔肉。"},{"en":"What is sold in butcher shops reflects local eating habits and food supply.","zh":"肉店售賣甚麼，反映本地飲食習慣和食物供應。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to meat-selling shops, not general grocery stores.","zh":"這個短語指售賣肉類的店，而不是一般雜貨店。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"great contribution to","meaning":"對……的重大貢獻","examples":[{"en":"The New World’s great contribution to the Old was in crop plants.","zh":"新世界對舊世界的重大貢獻在於農作物植物。"},{"en":"A great contribution to something is an important benefit, gift, or influence given to it.","zh":"great contribution to something 指給予某事的重要好處、禮物或影響。"},{"en":"Public libraries make a great contribution to education by giving everyone access to books.","zh":"公共圖書館讓人人接觸書本，對教育作出重大貢獻。"},{"en":"New crops made a great contribution because they changed food supply and population growth.","zh":"新作物作出重大貢獻，因為它們改變了食物供應和人口增長。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a major positive impact.","zh":"這個短語突出重大正面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"crop plants","meaning":"農作物植物","examples":[{"en":"Crop plants were the New World’s greatest contribution.","zh":"農作物植物是新世界最大的貢獻。"},{"en":"Crop plants are plants grown by people for food, fibre, medicine, or other practical use.","zh":"crop plants 指人類為食物、纖維、藥物或其他實際用途而種植的植物。"},{"en":"Rice, maize, potatoes, cotton, and beans are crop plants.","zh":"稻米、粟米、馬鈴薯、棉花和豆都是農作物植物。"},{"en":"When crop plants spread to new regions, they can change farming and diets.","zh":"當農作物植物傳到新地區，它們可以改變農業和飲食。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to cultivated plants that people depend on.","zh":"這個短語指人們依賴的栽培植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"become essentials in","meaning":"成為……的必需品","examples":[{"en":"New World crops became essentials in many diets.","zh":"新世界作物成為許多飲食中的必需品。"},{"en":"To become essentials in something means to become necessary or central parts of it.","zh":"become essentials in something 指成為其中必要或核心部分。"},{"en":"Rice has become an essential in many family meals across Asia.","zh":"稻米已成為亞洲許多家庭膳食中的必需品。"},{"en":"A crop becomes essential when people depend on it for daily food.","zh":"當人們依賴某作物作日常食物，它就成為必需品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something moving from optional to necessary.","zh":"這個短語描述某物由可選變成必要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"diets of hundreds of millions","meaning":"數以億計人口的飲食","examples":[{"en":"These crops entered the diets of hundreds of millions of people.","zh":"這些作物進入數以億計人口的飲食。"},{"en":"Diets of hundreds of millions means the regular food eaten by extremely large numbers of people.","zh":"diets of hundreds of millions 指極大量人口日常食用的食物。"},{"en":"Potatoes entering the diets of hundreds of millions shows how one crop can change global eating habits.","zh":"馬鈴薯進入數以億計人口的飲食，顯示一種作物如何改變全球飲食習慣。"},{"en":"When a food becomes common in many diets, farming and trade also change.","zh":"當一種食物在許多飲食中變得常見，農業和貿易也會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the massive scale of dietary change.","zh":"這個短語強調飲食變化的巨大規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Europeans, Africans, and Asians","meaning":"歐洲人、非洲人和亞洲人","examples":[{"en":"New World crops changed the diets of Europeans, Africans, and Asians.","zh":"新世界作物改變了歐洲人、非洲人和亞洲人的飲食。"},{"en":"Europeans, Africans, and Asians refers to people living in Europe, Africa, and Asia.","zh":"Europeans, Africans, and Asians 指生活在歐洲、非洲和亞洲的人。"},{"en":"A global crop can affect Europeans, Africans, and Asians differently depending on local climate and food habits.","zh":"全球作物可以因本地氣候和飲食習慣不同，而對歐洲人、非洲人和亞洲人產生不同影響。"},{"en":"When one exchange changes three continents, its historical importance is very large.","zh":"當一次交換改變三個大洲，其歷史重要性就非常大。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the broad Old World population affected by the exchange.","zh":"這個短語突出受交換影響的廣泛舊世界人口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"influence on","meaning":"對……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Their influence on Old World peoples was enormous.","zh":"它們對舊世界人民的影響巨大。"},{"en":"Influence on something means the effect or power one thing has over another.","zh":"influence on something 指一件事物對另一方產生的效果或力量。"},{"en":"A good teacher can have a strong influence on a student’s confidence.","zh":"好老師可以對學生信心有強大影響。"},{"en":"New foods can influence population growth when they provide more reliable nutrition.","zh":"當新食物提供更可靠營養，它們可以影響人口增長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the effect one factor has on a person, group, or situation.","zh":"這個短語描述一個因素對人、群體或情況的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"go far to explain","meaning":"很大程度上解釋","examples":[{"en":"These crops go far to explain global population growth.","zh":"這些作物很大程度上解釋了全球人口增長。"},{"en":"To go far to explain something means to explain a large part of it, though perhaps not all of it.","zh":"go far to explain something 指解釋某事的大部分，雖然未必全部。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep may go far to explain why a student cannot concentrate in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可能很大程度上解釋學生為何無法在課堂集中。"},{"en":"A strong food supply can go far to explain why populations increase.","zh":"穩定食物供應可以很大程度上解釋人口為何增加。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a factor is very important but not necessarily the only cause.","zh":"這個短語顯示某因素非常重要，但不一定是唯一原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"global population explosion","meaning":"全球人口爆炸","examples":[{"en":"Crop exchange helped cause the global population explosion.","zh":"作物交換有助造成全球人口爆炸。"},{"en":"Global population explosion means a very rapid increase in the number of people worldwide.","zh":"global population explosion 指全球人口數量非常迅速地增加。"},{"en":"Better food supply, medicine, and sanitation can contribute to a global population explosion.","zh":"更好的食物供應、醫療和衞生可以促成全球人口爆炸。"},{"en":"When more people survive and food becomes more available, population can rise sharply.","zh":"當更多人存活且食物更充足，人口可以急劇上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large-scale demographic growth across the world.","zh":"這個短語描述全球範圍的大規模人口增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"indispensable factor","meaning":"不可或缺的因素","examples":[{"en":"The Columbian Exchange was an indispensable factor in demographic growth.","zh":"哥倫布大交換是人口增長中不可或缺的因素。"},{"en":"An indispensable factor is a cause or element so important that the result could not be fully explained without it.","zh":"indispensable factor 指重要到沒有它就無法完整解釋結果的原因或元素。"},{"en":"Practice is an indispensable factor in learning a musical instrument.","zh":"練習是學習樂器不可或缺的因素。"},{"en":"If a factor is indispensable, removing it would change the whole explanation.","zh":"如果某因素不可或缺，移除它會改變整個解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something essential, not merely helpful.","zh":"這個短語描述必要事物，而不只是有幫助的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"demographic explosion","meaning":"人口爆炸","examples":[{"en":"The exchange contributed to a demographic explosion.","zh":"這場交換促成了人口爆炸。"},{"en":"A demographic explosion is a very rapid increase in population size.","zh":"demographic explosion 指人口數量非常迅速增加。"},{"en":"A town may experience a demographic explosion if new jobs attract many young families.","zh":"如果新工作吸引許多年輕家庭，一個城鎮可能經歷人口爆炸。"},{"en":"More food and lower death rates can lead to demographic explosion.","zh":"更多食物和較低死亡率可以導致人口爆炸。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on sudden or dramatic population growth.","zh":"這個短語著重突然或劇烈的人口增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"superiority or inferiority","meaning":"優越或劣等","examples":[{"en":"The issue was not about superiority or inferiority of biosystems.","zh":"這個問題並不是關於生物系統的優越或劣等。"},{"en":"Superiority or inferiority means being better or worse than something else.","zh":"superiority or inferiority 指比其他事物更好或更差。"},{"en":"Comparing languages should not become a question of superiority or inferiority.","zh":"比較語言不應變成優越或劣等的問題。"},{"en":"The writer suggests the outcome came from environment, not from one biosystem being better.","zh":"作者指出結果來自環境，而不是某一生物系統更優越。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when rejecting a simple ranking of better and worse.","zh":"這個短語用於拒絕簡單的高低排序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"biosystems","meaning":"生物系統","examples":[{"en":"The passage compares different biosystems without ranking them.","zh":"文章比較不同生物系統，但沒有把它們排序。"},{"en":"Biosystems are living systems made up of organisms and their relationships with one another and the environment.","zh":"biosystems 指由生物及其彼此和環境之間關係組成的生命系統。"},{"en":"A rainforest, a farm, and a grassland can each be understood as a biosystem.","zh":"雨林、農場和草原都可以被理解為一個生物系統。"},{"en":"Different biosystems may respond differently when new species or diseases arrive.","zh":"當新物種或疾病到來，不同生物系統可能有不同反應。"},{"en":"This word describes biological systems, not political or economic systems.","zh":"這個詞描述生物系統，而不是政治或經濟系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in any absolute sense","meaning":"在任何絕對意義上","examples":[{"en":"The writer rejects superiority in any absolute sense.","zh":"作者拒絕在任何絕對意義上的優越性。"},{"en":"In any absolute sense means in a complete, universal, or unconditional way.","zh":"in any absolute sense 指以完全、普遍或無條件的方式。"},{"en":"No teaching method is best in any absolute sense because students and goals differ.","zh":"沒有一種教學方法在任何絕對意義上都是最佳，因為學生和目標不同。"},{"en":"A system may work better in one environment but not be superior everywhere.","zh":"一個系統可能在某環境中運作較好，但並非在任何地方都優越。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against making total and simple judgements.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要作全面而簡單的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"environmental contrasts","meaning":"環境差異","examples":[{"en":"The outcome had to do with environmental contrasts.","zh":"這個結果與環境差異有關。"},{"en":"Environmental contrasts are differences in climate, land, plants, animals, diseases, and living conditions between places.","zh":"environmental contrasts 指地方之間在氣候、土地、植物、動物、疾病和生活條件上的差異。"},{"en":"The contrast between a dry region and a wet region can shape what crops survive.","zh":"乾旱地區與潮濕地區之間的差異，可以塑造甚麼作物能存活。"},{"en":"Environmental contrasts can explain why one species succeeds in one place but fails in another.","zh":"環境差異可以解釋為何一個物種在某地成功，卻在另一地失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase points to differences in surroundings rather than differences in value.","zh":"這個短語指向周遭環境差別，而不是價值高低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be accustomed to","meaning":"習慣於……","examples":[{"en":"Amerindians were accustomed to one kind of environment.","zh":"美洲原住民習慣於某一種環境。"},{"en":"To be accustomed to something means to be used to it because of long experience.","zh":"be accustomed to something 指因長期經驗而習慣某事。"},{"en":"Students accustomed to small classes may feel nervous in a large lecture hall.","zh":"習慣小班教學的學生，可能在大型演講廳感到緊張。"},{"en":"People and species cope better with conditions they are already accustomed to.","zh":"人和物種對已經習慣的條件較能應對。"},{"en":"This phrase describes familiarity built through time.","zh":"這個短語描述透過時間建立的熟悉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"one particular kind of environment","meaning":"某一特定環境","examples":[{"en":"Amerindians lived in one particular kind of environment.","zh":"美洲原住民生活在某一特定環境中。"},{"en":"One particular kind of environment means one specific set of natural and social conditions.","zh":"one particular kind of environment 指一組特定自然和社會條件。"},{"en":"A child raised in a quiet village is used to one particular kind of environment.","zh":"在安靜村莊長大的孩子習慣於某一特定環境。"},{"en":"When people move to a very different environment, old skills may not work as well.","zh":"當人們移到非常不同的環境，舊技能可能不再那麼有效。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights that an environment is specific, not universal.","zh":"這個短語突出環境是特定的，而非普遍適用的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"create a kind of environment","meaning":"創造一種環境","examples":[{"en":"Old World peoples created a kind of environment familiar to them.","zh":"舊世界人民創造了一種他們熟悉的環境。"},{"en":"To create a kind of environment means to shape surroundings so they have certain conditions.","zh":"create a kind of environment 指塑造周遭條件，使其具有某些特徵。"},{"en":"A teacher can create a calm environment by setting clear routines and speaking gently.","zh":"老師可以透過設定清楚常規和溫和說話來創造安靜環境。"},{"en":"Settlers created familiar environments by planting known crops and bringing familiar animals.","zh":"定居者透過種植熟悉作物和帶來熟悉動物，創造熟悉環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes actively shaping conditions around people or species.","zh":"這個短語描述主動塑造人或物種周圍的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be already adapted to","meaning":"已經適應……","examples":[{"en":"Europeans were already adapted to the environment they created.","zh":"歐洲人已經適應他們所創造的環境。"},{"en":"To be already adapted to something means to have traits, habits, or experience that fit that condition before facing it again.","zh":"be already adapted to something 指在再次面對某條件前，已具備適合它的特徵、習慣或經驗。"},{"en":"A student already adapted to online learning may manage remote lessons more easily.","zh":"已經適應網上學習的學生，可能較容易應付遙距課堂。"},{"en":"Species already adapted to grazing may survive better when livestock are present.","zh":"已經適應放牧的物種，在有牲畜存在時可能更能存活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes prior readiness for a condition.","zh":"這個短語描述對某條件已有準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"increase in number","meaning":"數量增加","examples":[{"en":"Old World peoples increased in number after arriving in America.","zh":"舊世界人民抵達美洲後數量增加。"},{"en":"To increase in number means to become more numerous.","zh":"increase in number 指數量變多。"},{"en":"A school club may increase in number after students see an exciting performance.","zh":"學生看過精彩表演後，學校社團人數可能增加。"},{"en":"Populations increase in number when births, survival, or immigration exceed deaths and departures.","zh":"當出生、生存或移入超過死亡和離開，人口數量會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes numerical growth.","zh":"這個短語描述數量上的增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"initially plunge","meaning":"起初急劇下降","examples":[{"en":"Amerindian numbers initially plunged after exposure to European germs.","zh":"接觸歐洲病菌後，美洲原住民人口起初急劇下降。"},{"en":"To initially plunge means to fall sharply at the beginning of a process.","zh":"initially plunge 指在一個過程開始時急劇下降。"},{"en":"A shop’s sales may initially plunge after a new competitor opens nearby.","zh":"新競爭者在附近開業後，商店銷售可能起初急劇下降。"},{"en":"Populations can initially plunge when disease spreads before recovery or adaptation begins.","zh":"當疾病在恢復或適應開始前擴散，人口可能起初急劇下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sudden early drop.","zh":"這個短語描述早期突然下跌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"decline has reversed","meaning":"下降趨勢已逆轉","examples":[{"en":"That decline has reversed in our time.","zh":"那種下降趨勢在我們這個時代已逆轉。"},{"en":"A decline has reversed when a downward trend stops and begins to move upward again.","zh":"decline has reversed 指下降趨勢停止，並再次開始向上。"},{"en":"A school’s reading scores may reverse their decline after a strong support programme begins.","zh":"強大支援計劃開始後，學校閱讀分數的下降趨勢可能逆轉。"},{"en":"Reversal does not erase past damage, but it shows a change in direction.","zh":"逆轉不會抹去過去傷害，但它顯示方向改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recovery after a period of decrease.","zh":"這個短語描述一段下降後的恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"in our time","meaning":"在我們這個時代","examples":[{"en":"Amerindian populations have recovered somewhat in our time.","zh":"美洲原住民人口在我們這個時代已有某程度恢復。"},{"en":"In our time means during the present age or the period close to our own lives.","zh":"in our time 指在當今年代，或接近我們生活的時期。"},{"en":"In our time, digital tools have changed how students learn and communicate.","zh":"在我們這個時代，數碼工具改變了學生學習和溝通的方式。"},{"en":"Using this phrase connects historical trends with the modern world.","zh":"使用這個短語可把歷史趨勢與現代世界連接起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing past conditions with present developments.","zh":"它適合用於比較過去情況和現今發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"environmental influence","meaning":"環境影響","examples":[{"en":"Amerindian populations adapted to Old World environmental influence.","zh":"美洲原住民人口適應了舊世界的環境影響。"},{"en":"Environmental influence means the effect that surroundings, climate, species, or diseases have on people or organisms.","zh":"environmental influence 指周遭環境、氣候、物種或疾病對人或生物產生的影響。"},{"en":"City noise can have an environmental influence on sleep and concentration.","zh":"城市噪音可以對睡眠和專注造成環境影響。"},{"en":"When new animals, plants, and diseases arrive, environmental influence can change survival patterns.","zh":"當新動物、植物和疾病到來，環境影響可以改變生存模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the power of surroundings to shape life.","zh":"這個短語描述周遭環境塑造生命的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"demographic triumph","meaning":"人口上的勝利","examples":[{"en":"The demographic triumph of the invaders still stands.","zh":"入侵者人口上的勝利仍然存在。"},{"en":"Demographic triumph means victory shown through population growth, survival, or numerical dominance.","zh":"demographic triumph 指透過人口增長、生存或數量優勢顯示的勝利。"},{"en":"A group may achieve demographic triumph if its population grows while another group declines.","zh":"如果一個群體人口增加，而另一群體下降，前者可能取得人口上的勝利。"},{"en":"In colonisation, demographic triumph can result from disease, settlement, and environmental advantage.","zh":"在殖民中，人口上的勝利可能來自疾病、定居和環境優勢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes population-based success, not moral superiority.","zh":"這個短語描述人口層面的成功，而不是道德優越。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"invaders","meaning":"入侵者","examples":[{"en":"The invaders gained a lasting demographic advantage.","zh":"入侵者取得持久的人口優勢。"},{"en":"Invaders are people who enter a place by force or without the agreement of those already living there.","zh":"invaders 指以武力或在原居民不同意下進入某地的人。"},{"en":"In history, invaders may bring soldiers, settlers, animals, crops, and diseases.","zh":"在歷史中，入侵者可能帶來士兵、定居者、動物、作物和疾病。"},{"en":"Invaders can change land ownership, population patterns, and local ecosystems.","zh":"入侵者可以改變土地擁有權、人口模式和本地生態系統。"},{"en":"This word describes outsiders entering aggressively or destructively.","zh":"這個詞描述以侵略性或破壞性方式進入的外來者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"spectacular feature","meaning":"顯著特徵","examples":[{"en":"The demographic triumph was a spectacular feature of the invasion.","zh":"人口上的勝利是這場入侵的一個顯著特徵。"},{"en":"A spectacular feature is a striking or highly noticeable part of something.","zh":"spectacular feature 指某事中引人注目或非常明顯的部分。"},{"en":"A glass roof may be the spectacular feature of a new library.","zh":"玻璃屋頂可能是新圖書館的顯著特徵。"},{"en":"In history, a spectacular feature is something so important that readers cannot ignore it.","zh":"在歷史中，顯著特徵是重要到讀者不能忽視的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a major and attention-grabbing characteristic.","zh":"這個短語指出重大而吸引注意的特點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"still stands","meaning":"仍然存在","examples":[{"en":"The demographic triumph of the invaders still stands.","zh":"入侵者人口上的勝利仍然存在。"},{"en":"Still stands means still remains true, present, or valid after time has passed.","zh":"still stands 指時間過去後仍然真實、存在或有效。"},{"en":"The school rule still stands even though some students dislike it.","zh":"即使有些學生不喜歡，校規仍然有效。"},{"en":"A historical result may still stand if its effects continue into the present.","zh":"如果歷史結果的影響延續至現在，它可能仍然存在。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that has not disappeared or been overturned.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有消失或被推翻的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"which paragraph contains","meaning":"哪一段包含","examples":[{"en":"Students must identify which paragraph contains the information.","zh":"學生必須識別哪一段包含該資料。"},{"en":"Which paragraph contains asks readers to locate the paragraph where a specific detail appears.","zh":"which paragraph contains 要求讀者找出某具體細節出現在哪一段。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students scan the passage to find which paragraph contains a date or example.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生會掃讀文章，找出哪一段包含日期或例子。"},{"en":"This task tests location skills rather than only general understanding.","zh":"這項任務測試定位能力，而不只是整體理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in IELTS-style matching questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 IELTS 類型的配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"following information","meaning":"以下資料","examples":[{"en":"The questions ask students to locate the following information.","zh":"題目要求學生定位以下資料。"},{"en":"Following information means the details listed immediately after the instruction.","zh":"following information 指指示後面立即列出的細節。"},{"en":"Students should read the following information carefully before searching the passage.","zh":"學生在搜尋文章前，應仔細閱讀以下資料。"},{"en":"If the following information includes names or dates, they can become useful keywords.","zh":"如果以下資料包括姓名或日期，它們可以成為有用關鍵詞。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the information that comes next in the question.","zh":"這個短語指題目中接下來出現的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"imported species","meaning":"外來物種","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to an imported species named after English colonists.","zh":"題目提到一種以英國殖民者命名的外來物種。"},{"en":"An imported species is a plant, animal, or organism brought into a place from another region.","zh":"imported species 指從另一地區帶入某地的植物、動物或生物。"},{"en":"A fish released from an aquarium can become an imported species in a local river.","zh":"從水族箱放生的魚，可以成為本地河流中的外來物種。"},{"en":"Imported species may spread quickly if local predators or competitors do not control them.","zh":"如果本地捕食者或競爭者無法控制，外來物種可能迅速擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organisms introduced from outside.","zh":"這個短語描述由外地引入的生物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"named after","meaning":"以……命名","examples":[{"en":"The plant was named after the English colonists.","zh":"這種植物以英國殖民者命名。"},{"en":"Named after means given the same name as a person, group, place, or event.","zh":"named after 指以某人、群體、地方或事件的名稱來命名。"},{"en":"A school hall may be named after a former principal who helped build the school.","zh":"學校禮堂可能以一位幫助建校的前校長命名。"},{"en":"Names can preserve memory, admiration, criticism, or historical observation.","zh":"名稱可以保存記憶、敬意、批評或歷史觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the source or inspiration of a name.","zh":"這個短語解釋名稱的來源或靈感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"English colonists","meaning":"英國殖民者","examples":[{"en":"English colonists introduced many plants to the New World.","zh":"英國殖民者把許多植物引入新世界。"},{"en":"English colonists were settlers from England who established colonies in other lands.","zh":"English colonists 指來自英格蘭、在其他土地建立殖民地的定居者。"},{"en":"English colonists brought crops, animals, tools, laws, and religious practices with them.","zh":"英國殖民者隨身帶來作物、動物、工具、法律和宗教做法。"},{"en":"Their settlement could change local ecosystems and Indigenous communities.","zh":"他們的定居可以改變本地生態系統和原住民社群。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to English settlers in the context of colonisation.","zh":"這個短語在殖民語境中指英國定居者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"population growth","meaning":"人口增長","examples":[{"en":"The question asks why both worlds experienced population growth.","zh":"題目問為何兩個世界都經歷人口增長。"},{"en":"Population growth means an increase in the number of people living in a place or group.","zh":"population growth 指某地方或群體中的人口數量增加。"},{"en":"A town may experience population growth when new jobs attract families.","zh":"當新工作吸引家庭，一個城鎮可能經歷人口增長。"},{"en":"Better food supply, lower death rates, and migration can lead to population growth.","zh":"更好的食物供應、較低死亡率和移民可以導致人口增長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people becoming more numerous.","zh":"這個短語描述人數變多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"formation of new continents","meaning":"新大陸的形成","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to the formation of new continents.","zh":"題目提到新大陸的形成。"},{"en":"Formation of new continents means the geological process by which landmasses take shape or separate over time.","zh":"formation of new continents 指陸塊隨時間成形或分離的地質過程。"},{"en":"A science lesson may discuss continent formation when explaining plate movement.","zh":"科學課解釋板塊移動時，可能討論大陸形成。"},{"en":"Continental formation can separate species and lead to different evolutionary paths.","zh":"大陸形成可以分隔物種，並導致不同演化路徑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large-scale Earth history, not modern political borders.","zh":"這個短語描述大尺度地球歷史，而不是現代政治邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"indigenous population","meaning":"原住民人口","examples":[{"en":"The indigenous population declined after European arrival.","zh":"歐洲人到來後，原住民人口下降。"},{"en":"Indigenous population means the native people living in a place before outside settlement or colonisation.","zh":"indigenous population 指外來定居或殖民前生活在某地的本土人民。"},{"en":"Disease, war, and land loss can reduce an indigenous population.","zh":"疾病、戰爭和土地流失可以減少原住民人口。"},{"en":"When an indigenous population declines sharply, languages and cultural knowledge may also be threatened.","zh":"當原住民人口急劇下降，語言和文化知識也可能受威脅。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the size and condition of native communities.","zh":"這個短語指本土社群的人口規模和狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"an overview of","meaning":"……的概述","examples":[{"en":"The paragraph gives an overview of species absent from each world.","zh":"該段概述了每個世界所沒有的物種。"},{"en":"An overview of something is a general summary of its main points.","zh":"overview of something 指對某事主要重點的一般總結。"},{"en":"A teacher may give an overview of a chapter before students read the details.","zh":"老師可能在學生閱讀細節前，先給出章節概述。"},{"en":"An overview helps readers understand the big picture before studying examples.","zh":"概述幫助讀者在研究例子前理解大圖像。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broad introduction rather than a detailed analysis.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛介紹，而不是詳細分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"species absent from","meaning":"……所沒有的物種","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes species absent from the Old World and New World.","zh":"文章描述舊世界和新世界所沒有的物種。"},{"en":"Species absent from a place are plants, animals, or organisms not naturally found there.","zh":"species absent from a place 指某地自然不存在的植物、動物或生物。"},{"en":"Before contact, horses were species absent from much of the New World.","zh":"接觸之前，馬是新世界大部分地區所沒有的物種。"},{"en":"When absent species are introduced, they may fill new roles or disrupt existing ecosystems.","zh":"當原本不存在的物種被引入，它們可能填補新角色或打亂既有生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what a region lacked before exchange.","zh":"這個短語描述某地區在交換前缺乏甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"little effect on","meaning":"對……影響甚微","examples":[{"en":"Some animal species had little effect on the Old World.","zh":"有些動物物種對舊世界影響甚微。"},{"en":"Little effect on something means only a small influence or change.","zh":"little effect on something 指只有很小影響或變化。"},{"en":"Changing the classroom poster may have little effect on students’ exam performance.","zh":"更換課室海報可能對學生考試表現影響甚微。"},{"en":"A species has little effect if it does not spread widely or change farming and food habits.","zh":"如果某物種沒有廣泛擴散，也沒有改變農業和飲食習慣，它影響甚微。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a weak or limited impact.","zh":"這個短語描述微弱或有限影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"overall explanation","meaning":"整體解釋","examples":[{"en":"The final paragraph gives an overall explanation of the invasion’s success.","zh":"最後一段給出對入侵成功的整體解釋。"},{"en":"An overall explanation is a broad account that brings together the main causes of something.","zh":"overall explanation 指把某事主要成因整合起來的廣泛說明。"},{"en":"A teacher may give an overall explanation of a poor exam result by discussing sleep, revision, and question skills together.","zh":"老師可能透過一起討論睡眠、溫習和答題技巧，對考試成績差給出整體解釋。"},{"en":"Overall explanations help readers see how several factors connect.","zh":"整體解釋幫助讀者看見多個因素如何連接。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a general explanation of the whole situation.","zh":"這個短語描述對整個情況的一般解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"species invasion","meaning":"物種入侵","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains the success of the Old World species invasion.","zh":"文章解釋了舊世界物種入侵的成功。"},{"en":"Species invasion means the spread of plants, animals, or organisms into a new region where they were not previously established.","zh":"species invasion 指植物、動物或生物擴散到之前未曾定居的新地區。"},{"en":"An imported weed spreading across farmland can be a species invasion.","zh":"外來雜草擴散到農田，可以是一種物種入侵。"},{"en":"Species invasion can occur when humans carry organisms across natural barriers.","zh":"當人類把生物帶過天然屏障，物種入侵就可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ecological takeover or spread by introduced life forms.","zh":"這個短語描述外來生命形式在生態上的接管或擴散。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"take root in","meaning":"在……紮根","examples":[{"en":"European animals took root in the New World.","zh":"歐洲動物在新世界紮根。"},{"en":"To take root in a place means to become established and begin to grow, spread, or succeed there.","zh":"take root in a place 指在某地站穩腳跟並開始成長、擴散或成功。"},{"en":"A new community library may take root in a neighbourhood if families use it often.","zh":"如果家庭經常使用，新的社區圖書館可能在社區中紮根。"},{"en":"Species take root when the environment allows them to survive and reproduce.","zh":"當環境容許物種生存和繁殖，物種便會紮根。"},{"en":"This phrase describes successful establishment after arrival.","zh":"這個短語描述抵達後成功定居。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"agree with the claims","meaning":"與作者說法相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements agree with the writer’s claims.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與作者說法相符。"},{"en":"To agree with the claims means to match what the writer says or argues.","zh":"agree with the claims 指與作者所說或所主張的內容一致。"},{"en":"In a reading test, a statement agrees with the claims only if the passage supports it clearly.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，只有當文章清楚支持某陳述，它才與作者說法相符。"},{"en":"Students should not choose TRUE just because a statement sounds reasonable.","zh":"學生不應只因陳述聽起來合理就選 TRUE。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for checking agreement with the writer’s stated ideas.","zh":"這個短語用於檢查是否與作者明確觀點一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文本內容相反的東西。"},{"en":"If the passage says crops travelled east, an answer saying they travelled west may contradict the information.","zh":"如果文章說作物向東傳播，而答案說它們向西傳播，就可能與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"In reading tests, contradiction must be based on the passage, not outside knowledge.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，矛盾必須基於文章，而不是外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a direct conflict with the text.","zh":"這個短語描述與文本直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no information about this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Write Not Given if there is no information about this.","zh":"如果沒有相關資料，寫 Not Given。"},{"en":"No information about this means the passage does not provide enough detail to decide whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"no information about this 指文章沒有提供足夠細節來判斷陳述是真是假。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions a writer’s age, there is no information about this.","zh":"如果文章從未提及作者年齡，就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when there is no information about a point.","zh":"當某點沒有相關資料時，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a NOT GIVEN situation in reading tasks.","zh":"這個短語表示閱讀題中的 NOT GIVEN 情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"keep cattle and horses inside","meaning":"把牛和馬困在裏面","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether fences kept cattle and horses inside.","zh":"這個陳述問圍欄是否把牛和馬困在裏面。"},{"en":"To keep cattle and horses inside means to prevent these animals from leaving an enclosed area.","zh":"keep cattle and horses inside 指防止這些動物離開封閉區域。"},{"en":"A rancher may build strong fences to keep cattle and horses inside at night.","zh":"牧場主人可能建堅固圍欄，在夜間把牛和馬困在裏面。"},{"en":"If animals are not kept inside, they may wander onto roads or into crop fields.","zh":"如果動物沒有被困在裏面，牠們可能走到道路或農田中。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on holding livestock within boundaries.","zh":"這個短語著重把牲畜留在邊界內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be brutally killed by","meaning":"被……殘暴殺害","examples":[{"en":"The statement says Indigenous people were brutally killed by European colonists.","zh":"該陳述說原住民被歐洲殖民者殘暴殺害。"},{"en":"To be brutally killed by someone means to be killed in a cruel and violent way by that person or group.","zh":"be brutally killed by someone 指被某人或某群體以殘酷暴力方式殺害。"},{"en":"Civilians may be brutally killed by invading soldiers during a war.","zh":"戰爭期間，平民可能被入侵士兵殘暴殺害。"},{"en":"Brutal killing creates fear, trauma, and long-lasting anger in affected communities.","zh":"殘暴殺害會在受影響社群中造成恐懼、創傷和長久憤怒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extreme violence and moral wrongdoing.","zh":"這個短語描述極端暴力和道德錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"become popular in","meaning":"在……變得受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether American animals became popular in the Old World.","zh":"題目問美洲動物是否在舊世界變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"To become popular in a place means to be liked, used, or accepted by many people there.","zh":"become popular in a place 指在某地被許多人喜歡、使用或接受。"},{"en":"Bubble tea became popular in many cities because young people enjoyed its flavours and style.","zh":"珍珠奶茶因年輕人喜歡其味道和風格，在許多城市變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"An animal or crop becomes popular when people find it useful, tasty, or profitable.","zh":"當人們覺得某動物或作物有用、美味或有利可圖，它就會變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase describes widespread acceptance in a particular place.","zh":"這個短語描述在某地方被廣泛接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"play a major role in","meaning":"在……中扮演重要角色","examples":[{"en":"Crop exchange played a major role in world population growth.","zh":"作物交換在世界人口增長中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"To play a major role in something means to be one of the most important factors affecting it.","zh":"play a major role in something 指成為影響某事的最重要因素之一。"},{"en":"Good sleep can play a major role in students’ memory and concentration.","zh":"良好睡眠可以在學生記憶和專注中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"A factor plays a major role when the result would be very different without it.","zh":"當沒有某因素結果會非常不同，它就扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights strong influence.","zh":"這個短語突出強大影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"answer the questions below","meaning":"回答以下問題","examples":[{"en":"Students must answer the questions below using words from the passage.","zh":"學生必須使用文章中的詞語回答以下問題。"},{"en":"Answer the questions below is an instruction telling students to respond to the questions that follow.","zh":"answer the questions below 是指示學生回答接下來問題的說法。"},{"en":"In an exam, students should read the instructions before answering the questions below.","zh":"在考試中，學生在回答以下問題前應先閱讀指示。"},{"en":"The instruction may also limit how many words can be used.","zh":"該指示也可能限制可使用的字數。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a set of reading-comprehension answers.","zh":"這個短語引入一組閱讀理解答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不超過三個詞","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than three words.","zh":"每個答案應不超過三個詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must use three words or fewer.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案必須使用三個或更少的詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “infectious diseases,” it fits because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “infectious diseases”，它符合要求，因為它有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing four words may make the answer wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫四個詞也可能令答案錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語在考試指示中給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"from the passage","meaning":"從文章中","examples":[{"en":"The answers should be taken from the passage.","zh":"答案應從文章中選取。"},{"en":"From the passage means the answer must come directly from the reading text.","zh":"from the passage 指答案必須直接來自閱讀文本。"},{"en":"Students should copy the exact words from the passage if the instruction requires it.","zh":"如果指示要求，學生應複製文章中的原字。"},{"en":"Outside knowledge should not replace information from the passage in this task.","zh":"在這項任務中，外部知識不應取代文章資料。"},{"en":"This phrase tells students where the answer source is.","zh":"這個短語告訴學生答案來源在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"which groups reported","meaning":"哪些群體報告了","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which groups reported the same story.","zh":"題目問哪些群體報告了同一個故事。"},{"en":"Which groups reported asks readers to identify the people or organisations who gave the information.","zh":"which groups reported 要求讀者識別哪些人或組織提供了資料。"},{"en":"A reading question may ask which groups reported rising prices in a city.","zh":"閱讀題可能問哪些群體報告了城市物價上升。"},{"en":"Identifying reporting groups helps students connect evidence with its source.","zh":"識別報告群體幫助學生把證據與來源連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on who gave or recorded the information.","zh":"這個短語著重誰提供或記錄了資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"European diseases","meaning":"歐洲疾病","examples":[{"en":"European diseases spread among Indigenous people.","zh":"歐洲疾病在原住民之間傳播。"},{"en":"European diseases are diseases brought by Europeans or associated with Old World populations.","zh":"European diseases 指由歐洲人帶來或與舊世界人口有關的疾病。"},{"en":"Smallpox and measles are often discussed as European diseases in the context of the Americas.","zh":"在美洲語境中，天花和麻疹常被討論為歐洲疾病。"},{"en":"When European diseases reached people without immunity, they caused severe population loss.","zh":"當歐洲疾病傳到沒有免疫力的人群，它們造成嚴重人口損失。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to diseases introduced through European contact.","zh":"這個短語指透過歐洲接觸引入的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"among Indigenous people","meaning":"在原住民之中","examples":[{"en":"The diseases spread among Indigenous people in the interior.","zh":"這些疾病在內陸原住民之中傳播。"},{"en":"Among Indigenous people means within or throughout native communities.","zh":"among Indigenous people 指在原住民社群內或遍及原住民社群。"},{"en":"A health programme may work among Indigenous people by respecting local languages and customs.","zh":"健康計劃可能透過尊重本地語言和習俗，在原住民之中推行。"},{"en":"Disease spreading among Indigenous people can affect families, elders, and cultural knowledge.","zh":"疾病在原住民之中傳播，可以影響家庭、長者和文化知識。"},{"en":"This phrase places an action inside Indigenous communities.","zh":"這個短語把行動放在原住民社群內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"enduring feature","meaning":"持久存在的特徵","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about an enduring feature of the invasion.","zh":"題目問這場入侵的一個持久存在的特徵。"},{"en":"An enduring feature is a characteristic that lasts for a long time.","zh":"enduring feature 指持續很久的特徵。"},{"en":"A school’s caring atmosphere can be an enduring feature if it continues through many principals.","zh":"如果一所學校的關懷氣氛經歷多任校長仍延續，它可以是持久存在的特徵。"},{"en":"In history, an enduring feature matters because its effects remain after the original event.","zh":"在歷史中，持久特徵重要，因為其影響在原事件後仍存在。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something lasting and still important.","zh":"這個短語描述持久而仍重要的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"remains","meaning":"仍然存在","examples":[{"en":"The demographic triumph remains after the Old World’s invasion.","zh":"舊世界入侵後，人口上的勝利仍然存在。"},{"en":"Remains means continues to exist, stay true, or be present.","zh":"remains 指繼續存在、仍然屬實或仍在場。"},{"en":"The old market remains important because local families still shop there every morning.","zh":"舊街市仍然重要，因為本地家庭每天早上仍在那裡購物。"},{"en":"A historical effect remains when later generations still live with its consequences.","zh":"當後代仍生活在某歷史影響的後果中，該影響就仍然存在。"},{"en":"This word describes something that has not disappeared.","zh":"這個詞描述沒有消失的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 32 - The Columbian Exchange.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 33":[{"front":"travel beyond their own societies","meaning":"到自己的社會以外旅行","examples":[{"en":"There are many reasons why individuals have travelled beyond their own societies.","zh":"人們到自己的社會以外旅行有許多原因。"},{"en":"To travel beyond one’s own society means to go outside the community, culture, or country one normally belongs to.","zh":"travel beyond one’s own society 指離開自己通常所屬的社群、文化或國家，到外面去。"},{"en":"A student may travel beyond her own society when she joins an exchange programme in another country.","zh":"學生參加另一個國家的交流計劃時，可能就是到自己的社會以外旅行。"},{"en":"Travelling beyond one’s own society can expose people to different customs, beliefs, and ways of organising daily life.","zh":"到自己的社會以外旅行可以令人接觸不同習俗、信念和日常生活組織方式。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses crossing social and cultural boundaries, not only physical distance.","zh":"這個短語強調跨越社會和文化界線，而不只是身體距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"satisfy curiosity about","meaning":"滿足對……的好奇心","examples":[{"en":"Some travellers simply desired to satisfy curiosity about the larger world.","zh":"有些旅行者只是希望滿足對更廣闊世界的好奇心。"},{"en":"To satisfy curiosity about something means to find out more because one wants to know and understand it.","zh":"satisfy curiosity about something 指因想知道和理解某事而了解更多。"},{"en":"A child may read books about space to satisfy curiosity about the planets.","zh":"孩子可能閱讀關於太空的書，以滿足對行星的好奇心。"},{"en":"Curiosity can lead people to travel, ask questions, read, or observe carefully.","zh":"好奇心可以令人旅行、提問、閱讀或仔細觀察。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a desire for knowledge, not a practical need.","zh":"這個短語描述對知識的渴望，而不是實際需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the larger world","meaning":"更廣闊的世界","examples":[{"en":"Some travellers were curious about the larger world.","zh":"有些旅行者對更廣闊的世界感到好奇。"},{"en":"The larger world means the wider world outside one’s own home, community, region, or society.","zh":"the larger world 指自己家庭、社區、地區或社會以外更廣大的世界。"},{"en":"Reading international news helps students understand the larger world beyond their school and family.","zh":"閱讀國際新聞幫助學生理解學校和家庭以外更廣闊的世界。"},{"en":"People become more open-minded when they realise their own experience is only one small part of the larger world.","zh":"當人們明白自己的經驗只是更廣闊世界中的一小部分，就會變得更開明。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a broader human, cultural, or geographical context.","zh":"這個短語暗示更廣泛的人類、文化或地理背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"until recent times","meaning":"直到近代","examples":[{"en":"Until recent times, travellers did not begin journeys solely out of curiosity.","zh":"直到近代，旅行者並不會純粹出於好奇而開始旅程。"},{"en":"Until recent times means before the modern or relatively recent period.","zh":"until recent times 指在現代或較近期之前。"},{"en":"Until recent times, many families repaired old objects instead of replacing them quickly.","zh":"直到近代，許多家庭會修理舊物，而不是很快更換。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare older habits with modern behaviour.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較較早期習慣與現代行為。"},{"en":"It usually introduces something that has changed over time.","zh":"它通常引入隨時間改變了的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"solely out of curiosity","meaning":"純粹出於好奇","examples":[{"en":"Travellers did not start their journeys solely out of curiosity.","zh":"旅行者並不是純粹出於好奇而開始旅程。"},{"en":"Solely out of curiosity means only because one wants to know, not because of money, duty, religion, or other practical reasons.","zh":"solely out of curiosity 指只因想知道，而不是因金錢、責任、宗教或其他實際原因。"},{"en":"A student may visit a science exhibition solely out of curiosity, even if it is not required for school.","zh":"學生可能純粹出於好奇去參觀科學展覽，即使學校沒有要求。"},{"en":"If people act solely out of curiosity, their main motive is learning or discovery.","zh":"如果人們純粹出於好奇行動，他們的主要動機就是學習或發現。"},{"en":"The phrase excludes other motives and focuses on pure interest.","zh":"這個短語排除其他動機，集中於純粹興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"travellers’ accounts","meaning":"旅行者的記述","examples":[{"en":"Travellers’ accounts give valuable information on foreign lands.","zh":"旅行者的記述提供關於異地的寶貴資料。"},{"en":"Travellers’ accounts are written or spoken records of what travellers saw, heard, and experienced.","zh":"travellers’ accounts 指旅行者把自己所見、所聞和所經歷寫下或說出的記錄。"},{"en":"A traveller’s account may describe local food, roads, temples, markets, and social customs.","zh":"旅行者的記述可能描述本地食物、道路、寺廟、市場和社會習俗。"},{"en":"Such accounts help later readers understand places they may never visit themselves.","zh":"這類記述幫助後來讀者理解他們可能永遠不會親身到訪的地方。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to records of travel experience, not bank accounts.","zh":"這個短語指旅行經驗記錄，而不是銀行戶口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"give valuable information on","meaning":"提供關於……的寶貴資料","examples":[{"en":"Travel accounts give valuable information on foreign lands.","zh":"旅行記述提供關於異地的寶貴資料。"},{"en":"To give valuable information on something means to provide useful and important knowledge about it.","zh":"give valuable information on something 指提供關於某事有用而重要的知識。"},{"en":"A school survey can give valuable information on students’ sleep habits and stress levels.","zh":"學校調查可以提供關於學生睡眠習慣和壓力水平的寶貴資料。"},{"en":"Valuable information helps people make better decisions, ask better questions, or understand a situation more clearly.","zh":"寶貴資料幫助人們作出更好決定、提出更好問題，或更清楚理解情況。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses usefulness and importance.","zh":"這個短語強調有用性和重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"foreign lands","meaning":"外國；異地","examples":[{"en":"Travel accounts describe foreign lands and local societies.","zh":"旅行記述描述外國和本地社會。"},{"en":"Foreign lands are countries or regions outside one’s own country or familiar society.","zh":"foreign lands 指自己國家或熟悉社會以外的國家或地區。"},{"en":"Old maps often showed foreign lands as mysterious places filled with unknown people and goods.","zh":"古地圖常把外國描繪成充滿未知人群和貨品的神秘地方。"},{"en":"Travelling to foreign lands can challenge assumptions because daily life may work very differently there.","zh":"到異地旅行可以挑戰假設，因為當地日常生活可能運作得很不同。"},{"en":"The phrase is literary and usually means distant or unfamiliar places.","zh":"這個短語較具文學色彩，通常指遙遠或陌生地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"provide a window into","meaning":"讓人了解……","examples":[{"en":"Travel accounts provide a window into local cultures and histories.","zh":"旅行記述讓人了解本地文化和歷史。"},{"en":"To provide a window into something means to help people see, understand, or learn about it.","zh":"provide a window into something 指幫助人看見、理解或認識某事。"},{"en":"A documentary can provide a window into the lives of workers who are usually ignored.","zh":"紀錄片可以讓人了解平時被忽視的工人生活。"},{"en":"Personal stories provide a window into history because they show how large events affected ordinary people.","zh":"個人故事讓人了解歷史，因為它們顯示重大事件如何影響普通人。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests giving access to something normally hidden or distant.","zh":"這個短語暗示提供通往平時隱藏或遙遠事物的入口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"local cultures and histories","meaning":"本地文化和歷史","examples":[{"en":"These accounts provide a window into local cultures and histories.","zh":"這些記述讓人了解本地文化和歷史。"},{"en":"Local cultures and histories are the customs, stories, values, events, and memories of particular communities or places.","zh":"local cultures and histories 指特定社群或地方的習俗、故事、價值、事件和記憶。"},{"en":"A museum exhibition may teach visitors about local cultures and histories through photographs and personal objects.","zh":"博物館展覽可能透過照片和個人物件教訪客認識本地文化和歷史。"},{"en":"Understanding local cultures and histories helps travellers avoid judging a place too quickly.","zh":"理解本地文化和歷史幫助旅客避免太快判斷一個地方。"},{"en":"The phrase combines how people live with what happened to them in the past.","zh":"這個短語結合人們如何生活，以及他們過去經歷了甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a mirror for","meaning":"反映……的一面鏡子","examples":[{"en":"Travel writing can also be a mirror for the travellers themselves.","zh":"旅行寫作也可以成為反映旅行者自身的一面鏡子。"},{"en":"A mirror for someone means something that reflects their own values, assumptions, fears, or identity back to them.","zh":"mirror for someone 指能反映某人自身價值觀、假設、恐懼或身份的事物。"},{"en":"Studying abroad can become a mirror for students because they notice habits from home more clearly.","zh":"留學可以成為學生的一面鏡子，因為他們更清楚注意到來自家鄉的習慣。"},{"en":"Travel writing reflects not only foreign places but also what the traveller chooses to notice or criticise.","zh":"旅行寫作不只反映外地，也反映旅行者選擇注意或批評甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes self-understanding through comparison.","zh":"這個短語描述透過比較產生的自我理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have a better understanding of","meaning":"更了解……","examples":[{"en":"These accounts help travellers have a better understanding of themselves.","zh":"這些記述幫助旅行者更了解自己。"},{"en":"To have a better understanding of something means to know it more clearly, deeply, or accurately.","zh":"have a better understanding of something 指更清楚、更深入或更準確地認識某事。"},{"en":"After receiving feedback, a student may have a better understanding of her writing weaknesses.","zh":"收到回饋後，學生可能更了解自己的寫作弱點。"},{"en":"Comparing cultures can help people understand their own habits because differences become clearer.","zh":"比較文化可以幫助人理解自己的習慣，因為差異會變得更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improved knowledge or insight.","zh":"這個短語描述知識或洞察有所提升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"records of foreign travel","meaning":"外國旅行記錄","examples":[{"en":"Records of foreign travel appeared soon after the invention of writing.","zh":"外國旅行記錄在文字發明後不久便出現。"},{"en":"Records of foreign travel are written accounts that describe journeys to other lands.","zh":"records of foreign travel 指描述前往異地旅程的文字記錄。"},{"en":"A traveller’s diary can become a record of foreign travel if it describes routes, people, and customs abroad.","zh":"如果旅行者日記描述海外路線、人群和習俗，它可以成為外國旅行記錄。"},{"en":"Such records survive because writing allows experiences to be stored and shared across time.","zh":"這類記錄能保存下來，因為文字讓經驗得以跨時間儲存和分享。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to documented journeys beyond one’s own society.","zh":"這個短語指被記錄下來、超越自己社會的旅程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"soon after","meaning":"在……之後不久","examples":[{"en":"Records of foreign travel appeared soon after the invention of writing.","zh":"外國旅行記錄在文字發明後不久便出現。"},{"en":"Soon after means not long after an event happens.","zh":"soon after 指某事件發生後不久。"},{"en":"Soon after the school opened, parents began asking for more language classes.","zh":"學校開辦後不久，家長便開始要求更多語言課程。"},{"en":"When a new technology appears, new uses often develop soon after.","zh":"當新科技出現，新用途通常在不久後發展出來。"},{"en":"The phrase connects two events that happen close together in time.","zh":"這個短語連接時間上相距很近的兩件事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the invention of writing","meaning":"文字的發明","examples":[{"en":"Travel records appeared soon after the invention of writing.","zh":"旅行記錄在文字發明後不久便出現。"},{"en":"The invention of writing is the development of systems for recording language with marks or symbols.","zh":"invention of writing 指用符號或記號記錄語言的系統發展出來。"},{"en":"The invention of writing allowed laws, stories, trade records, and travel experiences to be preserved.","zh":"文字的發明讓法律、故事、貿易記錄和旅行經驗得以保存。"},{"en":"Once people could write, information no longer depended only on memory and speech.","zh":"一旦人們能書寫，資訊就不再只依靠記憶和口頭傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to one of the major turning points in human communication.","zh":"這個短語指人類溝通的一個重大轉捩點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fragmentary travel accounts","meaning":"零散的旅行記述","examples":[{"en":"Fragmentary travel accounts appeared in Mesopotamia and Egypt in ancient times.","zh":"零散的旅行記述在古代美索不達米亞和埃及出現。"},{"en":"Fragmentary travel accounts are incomplete or broken records of journeys.","zh":"fragmentary travel accounts 指不完整或殘缺的旅行記錄。"},{"en":"An old notebook with only a few surviving pages may be a fragmentary travel account.","zh":"只有幾頁保存下來的舊筆記本，可能是一份零散的旅行記述。"},{"en":"Fragmentary records can still be useful because even small details may reveal routes, goods, or customs.","zh":"零散記錄仍然有用，因為即使細小細節也可能揭示路線、貨品或習俗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes travel writing that survives only in pieces.","zh":"這個短語描述只以碎片形式保存的旅行寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ancient times","meaning":"古代","examples":[{"en":"Fragmentary travel accounts appeared in ancient times.","zh":"零散的旅行記述在古代出現。"},{"en":"Ancient times means a very early period of human history, especially before the Middle Ages.","zh":"ancient times 指人類歷史中非常早期的時代，尤其是中世紀以前。"},{"en":"In ancient times, people used clay tablets, papyrus, or stone inscriptions to record information.","zh":"在古代，人們使用泥板、紙草或石刻來記錄資訊。"},{"en":"Studying ancient times helps us understand how early societies traded, worshipped, and governed.","zh":"研究古代幫助我們理解早期社會如何貿易、崇拜和治理。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a distant historical past.","zh":"這個短語指遙遠的歷史過去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the formation of","meaning":"……的形成","examples":[{"en":"Travel accounts grew after the formation of large, imperial states.","zh":"大型帝國國家形成後，旅行記述增加。"},{"en":"The formation of something is the process by which it is created or comes into existence.","zh":"formation of something 指某事物被創造或開始存在的過程。"},{"en":"The formation of a student council can give students a voice in school decisions.","zh":"學生會的形成可以讓學生在學校決策中有聲音。"},{"en":"The formation of large states created a need for information about roads, peoples, and resources.","zh":"大型國家的形成造成對道路、人民和資源資訊的需要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the creation or development of an organised thing.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織事物的創立或發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"large, imperial states","meaning":"大型帝國國家","examples":[{"en":"Large, imperial states encouraged interest in useful travel information.","zh":"大型帝國國家促進了人們對實用旅行資訊的興趣。"},{"en":"Large, imperial states are powerful political systems that control extensive territories and often many peoples.","zh":"large, imperial states 指控制廣闊領土、通常包括多個民族的強大政治體系。"},{"en":"Ancient empires needed officials, soldiers, and messengers to understand distant regions.","zh":"古代帝國需要官員、士兵和信使了解遙遠地區。"},{"en":"Imperial states valued travel information because rulers needed to govern, tax, trade, and defend their lands.","zh":"帝國國家重視旅行資訊，因為統治者需要治理、徵稅、貿易和保衛土地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes big empires rather than small local communities.","zh":"這個短語描述大型帝國，而不是小型本地社區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the classical world","meaning":"古典世界","examples":[{"en":"Travel accounts became important in the classical world.","zh":"旅行記述在古典世界變得重要。"},{"en":"The classical world usually refers to ancient Greek and Roman civilisation and related cultures.","zh":"classical world 通常指古希臘、古羅馬文明及相關文化。"},{"en":"Students study the classical world to learn about early history, philosophy, politics, and literature.","zh":"學生研究古典世界，以了解早期歷史、哲學、政治和文學。"},{"en":"Travel writing mattered in the classical world because empires needed knowledge of distant peoples and places.","zh":"旅行寫作在古典世界重要，因為帝國需要了解遙遠的人群和地方。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a major ancient cultural period.","zh":"這個短語指出一個重要古代文化時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"emerged as","meaning":"逐漸成為","examples":[{"en":"Travel accounts emerged as a prominent literary genre.","zh":"旅行記述逐漸成為重要的文學體裁。"},{"en":"To emerge as something means to gradually become recognised as that thing.","zh":"emerge as something 指逐漸被認為是某種事物。"},{"en":"Online learning emerged as a major teaching method during school closures.","zh":"停課期間，網上學習逐漸成為主要教學方法。"},{"en":"A small habit can emerge as a serious problem if it grows over time.","zh":"如果小習慣隨時間擴大，它可以逐漸成為嚴重問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual development into a clear role or status.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步發展成清楚角色或地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a prominent literary genre","meaning":"重要的文學體裁","examples":[{"en":"Travel accounts emerged as a prominent literary genre in many lands.","zh":"旅行記述在許多地方逐漸成為重要的文學體裁。"},{"en":"A prominent literary genre is an important and widely recognised type of writing.","zh":"prominent literary genre 指重要且被廣泛認可的寫作類型。"},{"en":"Detective fiction became a prominent literary genre because readers enjoyed solving mysteries.","zh":"偵探小說成為重要的文學體裁，因為讀者喜歡解開謎團。"},{"en":"A genre becomes prominent when many writers produce it and many readers value it.","zh":"當許多作家創作、許多讀者重視，一種體裁就會變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a major category of literature.","zh":"這個短語描述文學中的主要類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hold strong appeal for","meaning":"對……有很大吸引力","examples":[{"en":"Travel accounts held strong appeal for rulers.","zh":"旅行記述對統治者有很大吸引力。"},{"en":"To hold strong appeal for someone means to be very attractive or interesting to that person or group.","zh":"hold strong appeal for someone 指對某人或某群體非常吸引或有趣。"},{"en":"Practical internship programmes hold strong appeal for students who want job experience.","zh":"實用實習計劃對想取得工作經驗的學生有很大吸引力。"},{"en":"Travel information appealed to rulers because it could help them control territory and plan policy.","zh":"旅行資訊吸引統治者，因為它可以幫助他們控制領土和制定政策。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why something attracts attention.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物為何吸引注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"desire useful knowledge about","meaning":"渴望獲得關於……的實用知識","examples":[{"en":"Rulers desired useful knowledge about their realms.","zh":"統治者渴望獲得關於自己領土的實用知識。"},{"en":"To desire useful knowledge about something means to strongly want practical information about it.","zh":"desire useful knowledge about something 指強烈想得到關於某事的實用資訊。"},{"en":"A school principal may desire useful knowledge about why students are often late.","zh":"校長可能渴望獲得關於學生為何經常遲到的實用知識。"},{"en":"Useful knowledge helps leaders manage problems instead of making decisions blindly.","zh":"實用知識幫助領導者處理問題，而不是盲目作決定。"},{"en":"The phrase connects curiosity with practical purpose.","zh":"這個短語把好奇心與實際目的連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"their realms","meaning":"他們的領土；國土","examples":[{"en":"Rulers wanted useful knowledge about their realms.","zh":"統治者想獲得關於自己領土的實用知識。"},{"en":"Their realms means the lands, peoples, and territories ruled by kings, emperors, or governments.","zh":"their realms 指由國王、皇帝或政府統治的土地、人民和領土。"},{"en":"A medieval king needed information about villages, roads, and farms in his realm.","zh":"中世紀國王需要了解其國土中的村莊、道路和農場。"},{"en":"Rulers studied their realms because better knowledge made taxation, defence, and administration easier.","zh":"統治者研究自己的領土，因為更好知識令徵稅、防衛和行政更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to territory under political control.","zh":"這個短語指受政治控制的領土。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reported on his travels","meaning":"記述自己的旅行","examples":[{"en":"Herodotus reported on his travels in Egypt and Anatolia.","zh":"Herodotus 記述了自己在埃及和安納托利亞的旅行。"},{"en":"To report on one’s travels means to describe or record what one saw and learned while travelling.","zh":"report on one’s travels 指描述或記錄自己旅行時所見所學。"},{"en":"A student may report on her travels after visiting a rural village for a school project.","zh":"學生為學校項目到訪鄉村後，可能記述自己的旅行。"},{"en":"Travel reports help others learn from one person’s observations.","zh":"旅行報告幫助其他人從一個人的觀察中學習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes turning travel experience into information for readers or listeners.","zh":"這個短語描述把旅行經驗變成給讀者或聽眾的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"while researching","meaning":"在研究……期間","examples":[{"en":"Herodotus reported on his travels while researching the Persian Wars.","zh":"Herodotus 在研究波斯戰爭期間記述自己的旅行。"},{"en":"While researching means during the process of studying a topic carefully.","zh":"while researching 指在仔細研究某主題的過程中。"},{"en":"A student may discover old family photographs while researching local history.","zh":"學生在研究本地歷史期間，可能發現舊家庭照片。"},{"en":"Research often leads to unexpected findings because people follow evidence into new areas.","zh":"研究常帶來意外發現，因為人們會順着證據走向新領域。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an activity with an ongoing investigation.","zh":"這個短語把一項活動與進行中的調查連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Persian Wars","meaning":"波斯戰爭","examples":[{"en":"Herodotus researched the history of the Persian Wars.","zh":"Herodotus 研究波斯戰爭的歷史。"},{"en":"The Persian Wars were conflicts between the Persian Empire and Greek city-states in the fifth century BCE.","zh":"Persian Wars 指公元前五世紀波斯帝國與希臘城邦之間的衝突。"},{"en":"History students may study the Persian Wars to understand ancient politics, empire, and warfare.","zh":"歷史學生可能研究波斯戰爭，以理解古代政治、帝國和戰爭。"},{"en":"Researching wars often requires travel accounts because writers describe peoples and places involved in conflict.","zh":"研究戰爭常需要旅行記述，因為作者會描述參與衝突的人群和地方。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major subject of ancient historical writing.","zh":"這個短語命名古代歷史寫作中的一個重要主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as far west as","meaning":"向西遠至","examples":[{"en":"Zhang Qian described Central Asia as far west as Bactria.","zh":"張騫描述中亞，向西遠至大夏。"},{"en":"As far west as a place means reaching that westernmost point.","zh":"as far west as a place 指到達西方最遠至某地。"},{"en":"A delivery company may serve towns as far west as the coast.","zh":"速遞公司可能服務城鎮，向西遠至海岸。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show the geographical range of a journey or description.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示旅程或描述的地理範圍。"},{"en":"It stresses distance in a western direction.","zh":"它強調向西方向的距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"modern-day Afghanistan","meaning":"現今的阿富汗","examples":[{"en":"Bactria was located in modern-day Afghanistan.","zh":"大夏位於現今的阿富汗。"},{"en":"Modern-day Afghanistan means the area that is now the country of Afghanistan.","zh":"modern-day Afghanistan 指現在屬於阿富汗這個國家的地區。"},{"en":"Ancient place names are often explained by connecting them with modern-day countries.","zh":"古地名通常透過連接現今國家來解釋。"},{"en":"Saying “modern-day Afghanistan” helps readers locate an old region on a present map.","zh":"說「現今的阿富汗」幫助讀者在現代地圖上定位古老地區。"},{"en":"The phrase links ancient geography with today’s political geography.","zh":"這個短語把古代地理與今日政治地理連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on the basis of","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"Zhang Qian described Central Asia on the basis of his travels.","zh":"張騫根據自己的旅行描述中亞。"},{"en":"On the basis of something means using it as the evidence, reason, or foundation for a statement or decision.","zh":"on the basis of something 指以某事作為陳述或決定的證據、理由或基礎。"},{"en":"A teacher may grade an essay on the basis of content, grammar, organisation, and vocabulary.","zh":"老師可能根據內容、文法、組織和詞彙為作文評分。"},{"en":"Good conclusions should be made on the basis of evidence, not guesses.","zh":"好結論應根據證據作出，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase shows what supports an idea.","zh":"這個短語顯示某想法由甚麼支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"undertake travels","meaning":"進行旅行","examples":[{"en":"Zhang Qian undertook travels in the first century BCE.","zh":"張騫在公元前一世紀進行旅行。"},{"en":"To undertake travels means to make or carry out journeys, often with a serious purpose.","zh":"undertake travels 指進行或展開旅程，通常帶有嚴肅目的。"},{"en":"A researcher may undertake travels to villages in order to interview local people.","zh":"研究人員可能進行到各村落的旅行，以訪問本地人。"},{"en":"People undertake difficult journeys when the goal is important enough.","zh":"當目標足夠重要，人們會進行艱難旅程。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds more formal than simply “travel”.","zh":"這個短語比單純 “travel” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in search of allies","meaning":"為尋找盟友","examples":[{"en":"Zhang Qian travelled in search of allies for the Han dynasty.","zh":"張騫為漢朝尋找盟友而旅行。"},{"en":"In search of allies means trying to find people, groups, or states that will support one’s side.","zh":"in search of allies 指嘗試尋找會支持自己一方的人、團體或國家。"},{"en":"A student leader may speak to different clubs in search of allies for a charity project.","zh":"學生領袖可能與不同學會交談，為慈善項目尋找盟友。"},{"en":"States seek allies when they need military, political, or economic support.","zh":"國家在需要軍事、政治或經濟支持時會尋找盟友。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a purposeful search for partners.","zh":"這個短語描述有目的地尋找合作伙伴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the Han dynasty","meaning":"漢朝","examples":[{"en":"Zhang Qian searched for allies for the Han dynasty.","zh":"張騫為漢朝尋找盟友。"},{"en":"The Han dynasty was a major Chinese dynasty that ruled for several centuries in ancient China.","zh":"Han dynasty 指古代中國一個統治數個世紀的重要朝代。"},{"en":"Students studying Chinese history often learn about the Han dynasty’s government, trade, and expansion.","zh":"學習中國歷史的學生常認識漢朝的政府、貿易和擴張。"},{"en":"Diplomatic travel during the Han dynasty helped China learn about Central Asia.","zh":"漢朝時期的外交旅行幫助中國了解中亞。"},{"en":"The phrase names an important period in Chinese imperial history.","zh":"這個短語命名中國帝國歷史中的重要時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"relied on","meaning":"依靠；依賴","examples":[{"en":"Roman geographers relied on their own travels and other reports.","zh":"羅馬地理學家依靠自己的旅行和其他報告。"},{"en":"To rely on something means to depend on it for support, information, or success.","zh":"rely on something 指依賴某物以獲得支持、資訊或成功。"},{"en":"Students often rely on dictionaries when reading difficult articles.","zh":"學生閱讀困難文章時常依靠字典。"},{"en":"Researchers rely on evidence because memory and opinion alone may be unreliable.","zh":"研究人員依靠證據，因為單靠記憶和意見可能不可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase shows dependence on a source or tool.","zh":"這個短語顯示對來源或工具的依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"compile vast compendia of","meaning":"編纂大量……彙編","examples":[{"en":"Geographers compiled vast compendia of geographical knowledge.","zh":"地理學家編纂大量地理知識彙編。"},{"en":"To compile vast compendia of something means to collect and organise large bodies of information into written collections.","zh":"compile vast compendia of something 指收集並整理大量資訊成為文字彙編。"},{"en":"A school library may compile a compendium of student writing from the whole year.","zh":"學校圖書館可能把全年學生作品編纂成一本文集。"},{"en":"Compendia are useful because scattered information becomes easier to search and compare.","zh":"彙編很有用，因為零散資訊會變得更容易搜尋和比較。"},{"en":"The phrase describes large-scale collection and organisation of knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述大規模收集和整理知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"geographical knowledge","meaning":"地理知識","examples":[{"en":"Ptolemy and Strabo helped compile geographical knowledge.","zh":"Ptolemy 和 Strabo 協助編纂地理知識。"},{"en":"Geographical knowledge is information about places, regions, distances, maps, climates, peoples, and landscapes.","zh":"geographical knowledge 指關於地方、地區、距離、地圖、氣候、人群和景觀的資訊。"},{"en":"Drivers need geographical knowledge to choose routes and understand traffic patterns.","zh":"司機需要地理知識來選擇路線和理解交通模式。"},{"en":"Empires valued geographical knowledge because it helped with trade, taxation, and military planning.","zh":"帝國重視地理知識，因為它有助貿易、徵稅和軍事規劃。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to knowledge about the physical and human world across space.","zh":"這個短語指關於空間中的自然和人文世界的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the post-classical era","meaning":"後古典時代","examples":[{"en":"Trade and pilgrimage became major incentives during the post-classical era.","zh":"貿易和朝聖在後古典時代成為主要誘因。"},{"en":"The post-classical era refers broadly to the historical period after the classical age and before the modern era.","zh":"post-classical era 大致指古典時代之後、現代以前的歷史時期。"},{"en":"In world history classes, the post-classical era often includes growing trade networks and religious travel.","zh":"在世界歷史課中，後古典時代通常包括不斷增長的貿易網絡和宗教旅行。"},{"en":"Travel increased in this era because merchants and pilgrims moved across long-distance routes.","zh":"這個時代旅行增加，因為商人和朝聖者沿長途路線移動。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a period between ancient and modern history.","zh":"這個短語指出古代與現代之間的一個時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"trade and pilgrimage","meaning":"貿易和朝聖","examples":[{"en":"Trade and pilgrimage emerged as major incentives for travel.","zh":"貿易和朝聖成為旅行的主要誘因。"},{"en":"Trade and pilgrimage mean travel for buying and selling goods and travel for religious devotion.","zh":"trade and pilgrimage 指為買賣貨品而旅行，以及為宗教虔敬而旅行。"},{"en":"A medieval town could grow rich when both traders and pilgrims passed through it.","zh":"當商人和朝聖者都經過，中世紀城鎮可能變得富裕。"},{"en":"Trade brings people to markets, while pilgrimage brings believers to sacred places.","zh":"貿易把人帶到市場，而朝聖把信徒帶到聖地。"},{"en":"The phrase combines economic and religious motives for travel.","zh":"這個短語結合旅行的經濟和宗教動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"emerge as major incentives for","meaning":"成為……的主要誘因","examples":[{"en":"Trade and pilgrimage emerged as major incentives for foreign travel.","zh":"貿易和朝聖成為外國旅行的主要誘因。"},{"en":"To emerge as major incentives for something means to gradually become important reasons that encourage it.","zh":"emerge as major incentives for something 指逐漸成為鼓勵某事的重要原因。"},{"en":"Flexible hours may emerge as a major incentive for workers to stay in a company.","zh":"彈性工時可能成為員工留在公司的主要誘因。"},{"en":"When trade routes became profitable, trade emerged as a powerful reason for travel.","zh":"當貿易路線變得有利可圖，貿易便成為旅行的強大原因。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how motives become important over time.","zh":"這個短語解釋動機如何隨時間變得重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Muslim merchants","meaning":"穆斯林商人","examples":[{"en":"Muslim merchants sought trading opportunities across the eastern hemisphere.","zh":"穆斯林商人在東半球各地尋找貿易機會。"},{"en":"Muslim merchants were traders from Islamic societies who bought, sold, and transported goods.","zh":"Muslim merchants 指來自伊斯蘭社會、買賣和運送貨品的商人。"},{"en":"Muslim merchants might carry spices, textiles, books, or precious metals along sea and land routes.","zh":"穆斯林商人可能沿海陸路線運送香料、紡織品、書籍或貴金屬。"},{"en":"Merchants often became sources of information because trade required knowledge of distant markets.","zh":"商人常成為資訊來源，因為貿易需要了解遙遠市場。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies traders by both religion and commercial role.","zh":"這個短語同時以宗教和商業角色識別商人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"seek trading opportunities","meaning":"尋找貿易機會","examples":[{"en":"Muslim merchants sought trading opportunities throughout the eastern hemisphere.","zh":"穆斯林商人在東半球大部分地區尋找貿易機會。"},{"en":"To seek trading opportunities means to look for chances to buy, sell, or exchange goods profitably.","zh":"seek trading opportunities 指尋找能有利可圖地買賣或交換貨品的機會。"},{"en":"A small business owner may visit a trade fair to seek trading opportunities with suppliers.","zh":"小企業主可能參觀貿易展，以尋找與供應商合作的貿易機會。"},{"en":"Merchants travel when new markets promise profit, rare goods, or better prices.","zh":"當新市場帶來利潤、稀有貨品或更好價格，商人就會旅行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the business motive for travel.","zh":"這個短語描述旅行的商業動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"throughout much of","meaning":"遍及……大部分地區","examples":[{"en":"Muslim merchants travelled throughout much of the eastern hemisphere.","zh":"穆斯林商人遍及東半球大部分地區旅行。"},{"en":"Throughout much of a place means across a large part of that area.","zh":"throughout much of a place 指遍佈某地大部分區域。"},{"en":"Heavy rain fell throughout much of the city, causing delays in many districts.","zh":"大雨遍及城市大部分地區，導致多區延誤。"},{"en":"A religion, product, or language can spread throughout much of a region through trade and migration.","zh":"宗教、產品或語言可以透過貿易和遷徙傳遍某地大部分地區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad but not necessarily complete coverage.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛但不一定完全的覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the eastern hemisphere","meaning":"東半球","examples":[{"en":"Muslim merchants travelled widely across the eastern hemisphere.","zh":"穆斯林商人在東半球廣泛旅行。"},{"en":"The eastern hemisphere is the half of the Earth that includes much of Europe, Africa, Asia, and Australia.","zh":"eastern hemisphere 指地球的一半，包括歐洲、非洲、亞洲和澳洲的大部分地區。"},{"en":"Ancient trade routes connected many parts of the eastern hemisphere through land and sea travel.","zh":"古代貿易路線透過陸路和海路旅行連接東半球許多地方。"},{"en":"Travel across the eastern hemisphere allowed goods, religions, and ideas to move between societies.","zh":"橫跨東半球的旅行使貨物、宗教和思想在社會之間流動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a very large geographical half of the world.","zh":"這個短語指世界非常廣闊的一個地理半球。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"commercial products","meaning":"商業產品；商品","examples":[{"en":"Muslim merchants described the commercial products of the Indian Ocean basin.","zh":"穆斯林商人描述印度洋盆地的商品。"},{"en":"Commercial products are goods that are bought, sold, or traded in markets.","zh":"commercial products 指在市場上買賣或交易的貨品。"},{"en":"Coffee, cloth, spices, and smartphones are all commercial products.","zh":"咖啡、布料、香料和智能手機都是商品。"},{"en":"Travellers recorded commercial products because goods showed what a region produced and valued.","zh":"旅行者記錄商品，因為貨品顯示某地區生產和重視甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on marketable goods rather than private possessions.","zh":"這個短語重點是可在市場交易的貨品，而不是私人財物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the Indian Ocean basin","meaning":"印度洋盆地","examples":[{"en":"They described societies around the Indian Ocean basin.","zh":"他們描述印度洋盆地周圍的社會。"},{"en":"The Indian Ocean basin is the large region connected by the Indian Ocean and its surrounding coasts and seas.","zh":"Indian Ocean basin 指由印度洋及其周邊海岸和海域連接起來的廣大地區。"},{"en":"Ports around the Indian Ocean basin traded spices, textiles, metals, and religious ideas.","zh":"印度洋盆地周圍的港口交易香料、紡織品、金屬和宗教思想。"},{"en":"Sea travel made the Indian Ocean basin a major zone of contact between Africa, Arabia, India, and Southeast Asia.","zh":"海上旅行令印度洋盆地成為非洲、阿拉伯、印度和東南亞之間的重要接觸地帶。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to both the ocean and the connected coastal world.","zh":"這個短語同時指海洋和與其連接的沿海世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"supply the first written accounts of","meaning":"提供關於……的首批文字記錄","examples":[{"en":"Muslim merchants supplied the first written accounts of societies in sub-Saharan West Africa.","zh":"穆斯林商人提供了關於撒哈拉以南西非社會的首批文字記錄。"},{"en":"To supply the first written accounts of something means to provide the earliest surviving written descriptions of it.","zh":"supply the first written accounts of something 指提供關於某事最早保存下來的文字描述。"},{"en":"Early visitors may supply the first written accounts of a village before local records begin.","zh":"在本地記錄開始前，早期訪客可能提供關於某村落的首批文字記錄。"},{"en":"First written accounts are important because they may be the earliest outside evidence about a society.","zh":"首批文字記錄很重要，因為它們可能是關於某社會最早的外部證據。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both priority and documentation.","zh":"這個短語同時強調最早性和文獻記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sub-Saharan West Africa","meaning":"撒哈拉以南的西非","examples":[{"en":"The merchants wrote about societies in sub-Saharan West Africa.","zh":"商人撰寫關於撒哈拉以南西非社會的記述。"},{"en":"Sub-Saharan West Africa refers to the western part of Africa south of the Sahara Desert.","zh":"sub-Saharan West Africa 指撒哈拉沙漠以南的非洲西部。"},{"en":"Historians study sub-Saharan West Africa to understand trade, kingdoms, languages, and religious change.","zh":"歷史學家研究撒哈拉以南的西非，以理解貿易、王國、語言和宗教變化。"},{"en":"Travel accounts from this region helped outsiders learn about societies not well known in Mediterranean writing.","zh":"來自這一地區的旅行記述，幫助外人認識在地中海文字中不太為人所知的社會。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a broad African region by geography.","zh":"這個短語以地理方式指出一個廣闊非洲地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"set out in search of","meaning":"出發尋找……","examples":[{"en":"Merchants set out in search of trade and profit.","zh":"商人出發尋找貿易和利潤。"},{"en":"To set out in search of something means to begin a journey or effort to find it.","zh":"set out in search of something 指開始一段旅程或努力去尋找某物。"},{"en":"A graduate may set out in search of her first full-time job after university.","zh":"大學畢業生可能出發尋找第一份全職工作。"},{"en":"People set out in search of opportunities when they believe better chances exist elsewhere.","zh":"當人們相信其他地方有更好機會，就會出發尋找機會。"},{"en":"The phrase combines beginning a journey with a clear goal.","zh":"這個短語把開始旅程與清晰目標結合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"trade and profit","meaning":"貿易和利潤","examples":[{"en":"Merchants travelled in search of trade and profit.","zh":"商人為尋找貿易和利潤而旅行。"},{"en":"Trade and profit refer to buying and selling goods and earning money from those exchanges.","zh":"trade and profit 指買賣貨品，以及從交換中賺取金錢。"},{"en":"A shop owner visits wholesalers because trade and profit depend on finding good products at good prices.","zh":"店主拜訪批發商，因為貿易和利潤取決於以好價格找到好產品。"},{"en":"When trade is profitable, merchants may travel farther and take greater risks.","zh":"當貿易有利可圖，商人可能走得更遠並承擔更大風險。"},{"en":"The phrase explains a commercial motive for movement.","zh":"這個短語解釋移動的商業動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"devout Muslims","meaning":"虔誠的穆斯林","examples":[{"en":"Devout Muslims travelled as pilgrims to Mecca.","zh":"虔誠的穆斯林以朝聖者身分前往麥加。"},{"en":"Devout Muslims are Muslims who are deeply committed to their religious faith and practices.","zh":"devout Muslims 指深切投入伊斯蘭信仰和宗教實踐的穆斯林。"},{"en":"Devout believers may arrange daily life around prayer, fasting, charity, and worship.","zh":"虔誠信徒可能圍繞祈禱、齋戒、施捨和敬拜安排日常生活。"},{"en":"Devotion can motivate long and difficult journeys to sacred places.","zh":"虔誠可以推動人們展開漫長而艱難的聖地之旅。"},{"en":"The phrase describes religious seriousness and commitment.","zh":"這個短語描述宗教上的認真和投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"travel as pilgrims to","meaning":"以朝聖者身分前往……","examples":[{"en":"Devout Muslims travelled as pilgrims to Mecca.","zh":"虔誠的穆斯林以朝聖者身分前往麥加。"},{"en":"To travel as pilgrims to a place means to go there for religious devotion or sacred duty.","zh":"travel as pilgrims to a place 指為宗教虔敬或神聖責任前往某地。"},{"en":"Christians may travel as pilgrims to Jerusalem to visit sites connected with their faith.","zh":"基督徒可能以朝聖者身分前往耶路撒冷，參觀與信仰相關的地點。"},{"en":"Pilgrims often travel because the journey itself has spiritual meaning.","zh":"朝聖者通常旅行，因為旅程本身具有精神意義。"},{"en":"The phrase describes religious travel, not ordinary sightseeing.","zh":"這個短語描述宗教旅行，而不是普通觀光。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"perform the hajj","meaning":"履行朝覲","examples":[{"en":"Muslim pilgrims travelled to Mecca to perform the hajj.","zh":"穆斯林朝聖者前往麥加履行朝覲。"},{"en":"To perform the hajj means to complete the Islamic pilgrimage to Mecca according to religious practice.","zh":"perform the hajj 指按照宗教做法完成前往麥加的伊斯蘭朝聖。"},{"en":"A Muslim family may save money for years so an elder can perform the hajj.","zh":"穆斯林家庭可能多年儲錢，讓長者能履行朝覲。"},{"en":"The hajj brings Muslims from many societies together in a shared act of worship.","zh":"朝覲把來自許多社會的穆斯林聚集在共同敬拜行動中。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a specific Islamic religious duty.","zh":"這個短語指一項特定伊斯蘭宗教義務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"holy sites of Islam","meaning":"伊斯蘭教聖地","examples":[{"en":"Pilgrims visited the holy sites of Islam.","zh":"朝聖者到訪伊斯蘭教聖地。"},{"en":"Holy sites of Islam are places considered sacred or especially important in the Islamic faith.","zh":"holy sites of Islam 指在伊斯蘭信仰中被視為神聖或特別重要的地方。"},{"en":"Mecca and Medina are among the most important holy sites of Islam.","zh":"麥加和麥地那屬於最重要的伊斯蘭教聖地。"},{"en":"Pilgrimage to holy sites can strengthen religious identity and connect believers with history.","zh":"到聖地朝聖可以加強宗教身份，並把信徒與歷史連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to places with spiritual meaning for Muslims.","zh":"這個短語指對穆斯林具有精神意義的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"original pilgrimage to","meaning":"首次前往……朝聖","examples":[{"en":"The Prophet Muhammad’s original pilgrimage to Mecca inspired later pilgrims.","zh":"先知穆罕默德首次前往麥加朝聖啟發了後來的朝聖者。"},{"en":"An original pilgrimage to a place is the first or earliest important religious journey connected with a tradition.","zh":"original pilgrimage to a place 指與某傳統相關的第一次或最早重要宗教旅程。"},{"en":"A founder’s original visit to a sacred site may become a model for later believers.","zh":"創始人首次到訪聖地，可能成為後來信徒的榜樣。"},{"en":"Later pilgrims follow earlier examples because those journeys carry spiritual authority.","zh":"後來朝聖者仿效早期例子，因為那些旅程帶有精神權威。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a first journey that later becomes meaningful for others.","zh":"這個短語指出後來對他人有意義的首次旅程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"untold millions of","meaning":"數以百萬計的；無數的","examples":[{"en":"Untold millions of Muslims have followed his example.","zh":"無數穆斯林仿效了他的榜樣。"},{"en":"Untold millions of people means countless millions, too many to count exactly.","zh":"untold millions of people 指數以百萬計、難以精確點算的人。"},{"en":"Untold millions of viewers have watched major sports events on television.","zh":"無數觀眾曾在電視上觀看大型體育賽事。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when the number is extremely large and exact counting is difficult or unnecessary.","zh":"當數量極大而精確點算困難或沒有必要時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It adds a sense of scale and historical weight.","zh":"它增加規模感和歷史重量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"follow someone’s example","meaning":"仿效某人","examples":[{"en":"Many Muslims followed the Prophet Muhammad’s example.","zh":"許多穆斯林仿效先知穆罕默德。"},{"en":"To follow someone’s example means to do what that person did because it is respected or seen as a model.","zh":"follow someone’s example 指因尊重某人或視其為榜樣而做同樣事情。"},{"en":"Younger students may follow a senior student’s example and volunteer for community service.","zh":"低年級學生可能仿效高年級學生，參與社區服務。"},{"en":"People follow examples when they trust the person or value the meaning behind the action.","zh":"當人們信任某人或重視行動背後意義，就會仿效其榜樣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes imitation based on respect.","zh":"這個短語描述基於尊重的模仿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hajj accounts","meaning":"朝覲記述","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of hajj accounts related the pilgrims’ experiences.","zh":"數以千計的朝覲記述記載了朝聖者的經歷。"},{"en":"Hajj accounts are written descriptions of Muslim pilgrims’ journeys to Mecca.","zh":"hajj accounts 指穆斯林朝聖者前往麥加旅程的文字描述。"},{"en":"A hajj account may describe the route, hardships, prayers, crowds, and emotions of pilgrimage.","zh":"朝覲記述可能描述路線、艱辛、祈禱、人群和朝聖情感。"},{"en":"These accounts helped later pilgrims prepare and helped readers understand Islamic devotion.","zh":"這些記述幫助後來朝聖者準備，也幫助讀者理解伊斯蘭虔敬。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to travel writing centred on the hajj.","zh":"這個短語指以朝覲為中心的旅行寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"relate experiences","meaning":"記述經歷","examples":[{"en":"Hajj accounts related the experiences of Muslim pilgrims.","zh":"朝覲記述記載穆斯林朝聖者的經歷。"},{"en":"To relate experiences means to tell or describe what happened to someone.","zh":"relate experiences 指講述或描述某人經歷了甚麼。"},{"en":"A student may relate her experience of volunteering during a class presentation.","zh":"學生可能在課堂匯報中記述自己的義工經歷。"},{"en":"Relating experiences helps listeners understand events through a personal viewpoint.","zh":"記述經歷幫助聽眾透過個人視角理解事件。"},{"en":"The phrase is more formal than simply saying “tell stories”.","zh":"這個短語比單純說 “tell stories” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not quite so prominent as","meaning":"不及……那麼突出","examples":[{"en":"East Asian travellers were not quite so prominent as Muslims.","zh":"東亞旅行者不及穆斯林那麼突出。"},{"en":"Not quite so prominent as means not as important, visible, or influential as another group.","zh":"not quite so prominent as 指不如另一群體那麼重要、顯眼或有影響力。"},{"en":"In a school project, one student may be not quite so prominent as the team leader but still do important work.","zh":"在學校項目中，一名學生可能不及組長那麼突出，但仍做重要工作。"},{"en":"A group may be less prominent if fewer records survive or fewer people wrote about them.","zh":"如果保存下來的記錄較少，或較少人書寫某群體，該群體可能較不突出。"},{"en":"The phrase makes a careful comparison without saying the group is unimportant.","zh":"這個短語作出謹慎比較，而不是說該群體不重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"highways and sea lanes","meaning":"陸路和海上航線","examples":[{"en":"East Asian travellers followed many highways and sea lanes.","zh":"東亞旅行者沿着許多陸路和海上航線前進。"},{"en":"Highways and sea lanes are major land routes and ocean routes used for travel and trade.","zh":"highways and sea lanes 指用於旅行和貿易的主要陸上路線和海上路線。"},{"en":"Modern delivery networks depend on highways and sea lanes to move goods between cities and countries.","zh":"現代配送網絡依靠陸路和海上航線在城市和國家之間運送貨物。"},{"en":"Long-distance travel became easier when reliable routes connected markets, ports, and religious sites.","zh":"當可靠路線連接市場、港口和宗教地點，長途旅行變得更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase combines overland and maritime routes.","zh":"這個短語結合陸上和海上路線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"occasionally venture to","meaning":"偶爾冒險前往……","examples":[{"en":"Chinese merchants occasionally ventured to East Africa.","zh":"中國商人偶爾冒險前往東非。"},{"en":"To occasionally venture to a place means to sometimes travel there, often despite distance or risk.","zh":"occasionally venture to a place 指有時前往某地，通常儘管路途遙遠或有風險。"},{"en":"A small business owner may occasionally venture to overseas fairs to meet suppliers.","zh":"小企業主可能偶爾冒險前往海外展覽會見供應商。"},{"en":"People venture far from home when they believe the opportunity is worth the difficulty.","zh":"當人們相信機會值得承受困難，就會冒險遠離家鄉。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests irregular but bold travel.","zh":"這個短語暗示不定期但大膽的旅行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"undertake distant pilgrimages","meaning":"進行遠程朝聖","examples":[{"en":"Devout East Asian Buddhists undertook distant pilgrimages.","zh":"虔誠的東亞佛教徒進行遠程朝聖。"},{"en":"To undertake distant pilgrimages means to make long religious journeys to sacred places.","zh":"undertake distant pilgrimages 指前往聖地進行長途宗教旅程。"},{"en":"A believer may undertake a distant pilgrimage to a temple connected with a respected teacher.","zh":"信徒可能前往與受尊敬老師有關的寺廟進行遠程朝聖。"},{"en":"Distant pilgrimages require faith, resources, and physical endurance.","zh":"遠程朝聖需要信念、資源和體力耐力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious long-distance religious travel.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴肅的長途宗教旅行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"study with Buddhist teachers","meaning":"跟佛教老師學習","examples":[{"en":"Chinese Buddhists travelled to India to study with Buddhist teachers.","zh":"中國佛教徒前往印度跟佛教老師學習。"},{"en":"To study with Buddhist teachers means to learn religious teachings, texts, or practices from Buddhist masters.","zh":"study with Buddhist teachers 指向佛教大師學習宗教教義、經文或修行方法。"},{"en":"A student may travel to a monastery to study with Buddhist teachers during a summer retreat.","zh":"學生可能在暑期靜修期間前往寺院跟佛教老師學習。"},{"en":"Travellers sought teachers because personal instruction could explain difficult sacred texts.","zh":"旅行者尋找老師，因為親身指導可以解釋困難聖典。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning directly from religious authorities.","zh":"這個短語描述直接向宗教權威學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"collect sacred texts","meaning":"收集神聖經文","examples":[{"en":"Chinese Buddhists travelled to India to collect sacred texts.","zh":"中國佛教徒前往印度收集神聖經文。"},{"en":"To collect sacred texts means to obtain holy writings for study, copying, translation, or worship.","zh":"collect sacred texts 指取得聖典，用於研究、抄寫、翻譯或敬拜。"},{"en":"A library may collect sacred texts from different religions for academic study.","zh":"圖書館可能收集不同宗教的神聖經文作學術研究。"},{"en":"Pilgrims collected texts because religious knowledge could be carried home and shared with others.","zh":"朝聖者收集經文，因為宗教知識可以帶回家並與他人分享。"},{"en":"The phrase links travel with religious learning and preservation.","zh":"這個短語把旅行與宗教學習和保存連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"record the experiences of","meaning":"記錄……的經歷","examples":[{"en":"Written accounts recorded the experiences of many pilgrims.","zh":"文字記述記錄了許多朝聖者的經歷。"},{"en":"To record the experiences of people means to write down what they saw, felt, did, and learned.","zh":"record the experiences of people 指寫下他們所見、所感、所做和所學。"},{"en":"A school magazine may record the experiences of students who joined an exchange trip.","zh":"校刊可能記錄參加交流團學生的經歷。"},{"en":"Recording experiences preserves personal memories and helps later readers understand the event.","zh":"記錄經歷保存個人記憶，並幫助後來讀者理解事件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes turning lived experience into a record.","zh":"這個短語描述把生活經驗變成記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not so numerous as","meaning":"數量不及……多","examples":[{"en":"Buddhists from Japan and Korea were not so numerous as the Chinese pilgrims.","zh":"來自日本和韓國的佛教徒數量不及中國朝聖者多。"},{"en":"Not so numerous as means fewer in number than another group.","zh":"not so numerous as 指數量比另一群體少。"},{"en":"In a school club, new members may be not so numerous as returning members.","zh":"在學校學會中，新會員數量可能不及舊會員多。"},{"en":"A group may be less numerous because travel is costly, dangerous, or less common in that society.","zh":"某群體數量較少，可能因旅行昂貴、危險，或在該社會較不常見。"},{"en":"The phrase compares quantity.","zh":"這個短語比較數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"venture abroad","meaning":"前往外地；出國冒險","examples":[{"en":"Buddhists from Japan and Korea also ventured abroad.","zh":"來自日本和韓國的佛教徒也前往外地。"},{"en":"To venture abroad means to travel to another country, often with some risk, uncertainty, or purpose.","zh":"venture abroad 指前往另一個國家，通常帶有某種風險、不確定性或目的。"},{"en":"A young entrepreneur may venture abroad to find customers for a new product.","zh":"年輕創業者可能出國尋找新產品的顧客。"},{"en":"People venture abroad when they believe the learning, profit, or spiritual value is worth the effort.","zh":"當人們相信學習、利潤或精神價值值得付出努力，就會前往外地。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests going overseas with courage or uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語暗示帶着勇氣或不確定性出國。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in the interests of","meaning":"為了……的利益；出於……目的","examples":[{"en":"Some Buddhists travelled abroad in the interests of spiritual enlightenment.","zh":"有些佛教徒為了精神啟迪而到外地旅行。"},{"en":"In the interests of something means for the purpose of helping, achieving, or protecting it.","zh":"in the interests of something 指為了幫助、達成或保護某事。"},{"en":"A school may ban phones during exams in the interests of fairness.","zh":"學校可能為了公平而在考試期間禁止手機。"},{"en":"People accept inconvenience when it serves a larger goal they value.","zh":"當某事服務於人們重視的更大目標，他們會接受不便。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the reason or purpose behind an action.","zh":"這個短語給出行動背後的原因或目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"spiritual enlightenment","meaning":"精神啟迪；覺悟","examples":[{"en":"Buddhists travelled in the interests of spiritual enlightenment.","zh":"佛教徒為了精神啟迪而旅行。"},{"en":"Spiritual enlightenment is a deeper religious or inner understanding of truth, life, or liberation.","zh":"spiritual enlightenment 指對真理、生命或解脫有更深層的宗教或內在理解。"},{"en":"A person may seek spiritual enlightenment through meditation, study, service, or pilgrimage.","zh":"一個人可能透過冥想、學習、服務或朝聖尋求精神啟迪。"},{"en":"Religious journeys can support enlightenment by connecting believers with teachers, texts, and sacred places.","zh":"宗教旅程可以透過把信徒與老師、經文和聖地連起來支持覺悟。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to inner awakening rather than ordinary knowledge.","zh":"這個短語指內在覺醒，而不是普通知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"medieval Europeans","meaning":"中世紀歐洲人","examples":[{"en":"Medieval Europeans travelled less often than their Muslim counterparts.","zh":"中世紀歐洲人旅行次數少於其穆斯林同類群體。"},{"en":"Medieval Europeans were people living in Europe during the Middle Ages.","zh":"medieval Europeans 指生活在中世紀歐洲的人。"},{"en":"Medieval Europeans included farmers, nobles, monks, merchants, and pilgrims.","zh":"中世紀歐洲人包括農民、貴族、修士、商人和朝聖者。"},{"en":"Their travel patterns were shaped by religion, trade, war, roads, and political conditions.","zh":"他們的旅行模式受宗教、貿易、戰爭、道路和政治情況塑造。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a historical group from a particular period and region.","zh":"這個短語指出特定時期和地區的歷史群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"take to the roads","meaning":"踏上旅途","examples":[{"en":"Medieval Europeans did not take to the roads in very large numbers.","zh":"中世紀歐洲人並沒有大量踏上旅途。"},{"en":"To take to the roads means to begin travelling, especially overland.","zh":"take to the roads 指開始旅行，尤其是經陸路旅行。"},{"en":"Families take to the roads during long holidays, causing traffic jams near popular beaches.","zh":"長假期間，許多家庭踏上旅途，令熱門海灘附近出現交通擠塞。"},{"en":"People take to the roads when travel becomes safer, cheaper, or more necessary.","zh":"當旅行變得更安全、更便宜或更必要，人們便會踏上旅途。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement by many travellers.","zh":"這個短語描述大量旅行者的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in as large numbers as","meaning":"數量與……一樣多","examples":[{"en":"Europeans did not travel in as large numbers as their Muslim counterparts.","zh":"歐洲人旅行的人數並不及其穆斯林同類群體那麼多。"},{"en":"In as large numbers as means in the same quantity or scale as another group.","zh":"in as large numbers as 指數量或規模與另一群體一樣大。"},{"en":"Fewer students joined the hiking club this year; they did not participate in as large numbers as last year.","zh":"今年較少學生加入遠足學會；他們參與的人數不及去年那麼多。"},{"en":"Comparing numbers helps show which group was more active or visible.","zh":"比較數量有助顯示哪個群體更活躍或更顯眼。"},{"en":"The phrase is used for numerical comparison between groups.","zh":"這個短語用於群體之間的數量比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"counterparts","meaning":"對應的人；同類群體","examples":[{"en":"Medieval Europeans travelled less than their Muslim and East Asian counterparts.","zh":"中世紀歐洲人旅行少於其穆斯林和東亞同類群體。"},{"en":"Counterparts are people or things in another place or group that have a similar role or position.","zh":"counterparts 指另一地方或群體中具有相似角色或位置的人或事物。"},{"en":"A school principal may meet her counterparts from other schools to discuss exam policies.","zh":"校長可能與其他學校的對應人員會面，討論考試政策。"},{"en":"Comparing counterparts helps show similarities and differences between societies.","zh":"比較同類群體有助顯示不同社會之間的相似與差異。"},{"en":"The word means equivalent people or groups, not opponents.","zh":"這個詞指對應的人或群體，不是對手。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"gradually increasing crowds of","meaning":"逐漸增加的人群","examples":[{"en":"Gradually increasing crowds of Christian pilgrims travelled to holy sites.","zh":"逐漸增加的基督教朝聖者人群前往聖地。"},{"en":"Gradually increasing crowds of people means groups that become larger little by little over time.","zh":"gradually increasing crowds of people 指隨時間一點點變大的群體。"},{"en":"Gradually increasing crowds of shoppers appeared after the new market opened.","zh":"新市場開業後，逐漸增加的購物人群出現。"},{"en":"Crowds grow gradually when more people hear about a place, trust it, or can afford to go there.","zh":"當更多人聽說某地、信任某地或負擔得起前往，人群會逐漸增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow but steady growth in numbers.","zh":"這個短語描述人數緩慢但穩定增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Christian pilgrims","meaning":"基督教朝聖者","examples":[{"en":"Christian pilgrims travelled to Jerusalem, Rome, and Santiago de Compostela.","zh":"基督教朝聖者前往耶路撒冷、羅馬和聖地亞哥－德孔波斯特拉。"},{"en":"Christian pilgrims are Christians who travel to sacred places for religious reasons.","zh":"Christian pilgrims 指因宗教原因前往聖地的基督徒。"},{"en":"Christian pilgrims may walk long routes while praying, reflecting, and visiting churches.","zh":"基督教朝聖者可能一邊祈禱、反思和參觀教堂，一邊步行長途路線。"},{"en":"Pilgrimage can strengthen faith because travellers connect physical journey with spiritual purpose.","zh":"朝聖可以加強信仰，因為旅行者把身體旅程與精神目的連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies religious travellers in the Christian tradition.","zh":"這個短語指出基督教傳統中的宗教旅行者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"flow to","meaning":"湧向……","examples":[{"en":"Christian pilgrims flowed to Jerusalem and Rome.","zh":"基督教朝聖者湧向耶路撒冷和羅馬。"},{"en":"To flow to a place means many people or things move there continuously or in large numbers.","zh":"flow to a place 指許多人或事物持續或大量移向某地。"},{"en":"Customers flowed to the new bakery after people praised it online.","zh":"人們在網上稱讚新麵包店後，顧客湧向那裏。"},{"en":"People flow to important cities, markets, or sacred sites when those places offer meaning or opportunity.","zh":"當重要城市、市場或聖地提供意義或機會，人們會湧向那些地方。"},{"en":"The phrase compares human movement to the movement of water.","zh":"這個短語把人群移動比作水流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"after the 12th century","meaning":"十二世紀以後","examples":[{"en":"After the 12th century, European merchants and missionaries travelled widely.","zh":"十二世紀以後，歐洲商人和傳教士廣泛旅行。"},{"en":"After the 12th century means during the period following the years 1101 to 1200.","zh":"after the 12th century 指在1101年至1200年之後的時期。"},{"en":"After the 12th century, many changes in trade and religion affected European travel.","zh":"十二世紀以後，貿易和宗教的許多變化影響歐洲旅行。"},{"en":"Time phrases like this help readers place events in historical sequence.","zh":"這類時間短語幫助讀者把事件放入歷史順序。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a point after which travel patterns changed.","zh":"這個短語標示旅行模式發生變化之後的一個時間點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"travel widely","meaning":"廣泛旅行","examples":[{"en":"Merchants, pilgrims, and missionaries from medieval Europe travelled widely.","zh":"來自中世紀歐洲的商人、朝聖者和傳教士廣泛旅行。"},{"en":"To travel widely means to visit many places or cover a broad geographical area.","zh":"travel widely 指到訪許多地方或覆蓋廣闊地理範圍。"},{"en":"A business consultant may travel widely to meet clients in different cities.","zh":"商業顧問可能廣泛旅行，與不同城市的客戶會面。"},{"en":"People who travel widely often gather more comparisons and stories than those who stay in one place.","zh":"廣泛旅行的人通常比留在一地的人收集更多比較和故事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad travel, not just one journey.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛旅行，而不只是一次旅程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"leave numerous travel accounts","meaning":"留下大量旅行記述","examples":[{"en":"Medieval European travellers left numerous travel accounts.","zh":"中世紀歐洲旅行者留下大量旅行記述。"},{"en":"To leave numerous travel accounts means to produce many written records that survive for later readers.","zh":"leave numerous travel accounts 指產生許多保存給後來讀者的文字記錄。"},{"en":"A famous explorer may leave numerous travel accounts in letters, diaries, and published books.","zh":"著名探險家可能在信件、日記和出版書籍中留下大量旅行記述。"},{"en":"Many records matter because they allow historians to compare different travellers’ observations.","zh":"大量記錄很重要，因為它們讓歷史學家比較不同旅行者的觀察。"},{"en":"The phrase connects writing with historical survival.","zh":"這個短語把寫作與歷史保存連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"travels and sojourn in","meaning":"在……的旅行和逗留","examples":[{"en":"Marco Polo described his travels and sojourn in China.","zh":"Marco Polo 描述了自己在中國的旅行和逗留。"},{"en":"Travels and sojourn in a place means journeys to different areas and a temporary stay there.","zh":"travels and sojourn in a place 指前往不同地區的旅程，以及在該地的短期停留。"},{"en":"A researcher may write about her travels and sojourn in a mountain village after living there for six months.","zh":"研究人員在山村生活六個月後，可能撰寫自己在那裏的旅行和逗留。"},{"en":"A sojourn gives deeper observation than a quick visit because the traveller spends more time in one place.","zh":"逗留比快速到訪帶來更深入觀察，因為旅行者在同一地方花更多時間。"},{"en":"The phrase combines movement with temporary residence.","zh":"這個短語結合移動與短期居住。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the best known","meaning":"最廣為人知的","examples":[{"en":"Marco Polo’s description is the best known.","zh":"Marco Polo 的描述是最廣為人知的。"},{"en":"The best known means the most famous or most widely recognised.","zh":"the best known 指最著名或最廣泛被認識的。"},{"en":"Among school poems, the one used in exams is often the best known.","zh":"在學校詩歌中，考試使用的那一首通常最廣為人知。"},{"en":"A text becomes best known when it is copied, taught, translated, or discussed for a long time.","zh":"當文本長期被抄寫、教授、翻譯或討論，它就會變得最廣為人知。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to public familiarity, not necessarily accuracy.","zh":"這個短語指公眾熟悉度，而不一定是準確性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"become familiar with","meaning":"熟悉……","examples":[{"en":"European peoples became familiar with the larger world of the eastern hemisphere.","zh":"歐洲民族逐漸熟悉東半球更廣闊的世界。"},{"en":"To become familiar with something means to gradually know and recognise it better.","zh":"become familiar with something 指逐漸更認識並能辨認某事。"},{"en":"New students become familiar with the school after they learn the timetable and classroom locations.","zh":"新生學會時間表和課室位置後，會逐漸熟悉學校。"},{"en":"Repeated reading and travel accounts can make distant places feel less strange.","zh":"反覆閱讀和旅行記述可以令遙遠地方感覺較不陌生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving from unfamiliarity toward understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述由陌生走向理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"profitable commercial opportunities","meaning":"有利可圖的商業機會","examples":[{"en":"Europeans learned about profitable commercial opportunities in Asia and Africa.","zh":"歐洲人了解到亞洲和非洲有利可圖的商業機會。"},{"en":"Profitable commercial opportunities are chances to make money through trade, business, or investment.","zh":"profitable commercial opportunities 指透過貿易、商業或投資賺錢的機會。"},{"en":"A bakery may see profitable commercial opportunities when a new housing estate opens nearby.","zh":"新屋苑在附近落成時，麵包店可能看到有利可圖的商業機會。"},{"en":"Travellers reported business opportunities because merchants wanted to know where profit could be made.","zh":"旅行者報告商業機會，因為商人想知道哪裏可以賺取利潤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes economic chances that can bring financial gain.","zh":"這個短語描述能帶來財務收益的經濟機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"work to find","meaning":"努力尋找","examples":[{"en":"European peoples worked to find more direct routes to markets.","zh":"歐洲民族努力尋找通往市場的更直接路線。"},{"en":"To work to find something means to make sustained effort to discover or obtain it.","zh":"work to find something 指持續努力去發現或取得某物。"},{"en":"A teacher may work to find better examples when students do not understand a phrase.","zh":"當學生不理解某短語，老師可能努力尋找更好例子。"},{"en":"People work to find solutions when existing methods are slow, expensive, or ineffective.","zh":"當現有方法緩慢、昂貴或無效，人們會努力尋找解決方案。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses effort and purpose.","zh":"這個短語強調努力和目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"more direct routes to","meaning":"通往……更直接的路線","examples":[{"en":"Europeans searched for more direct routes to Asian and African markets.","zh":"歐洲人尋找通往亞洲和非洲市場的更直接路線。"},{"en":"More direct routes to a place are shorter, faster, or less complicated ways to reach it.","zh":"more direct routes to a place 指到達某地更短、更快或較不複雜的方法。"},{"en":"A commuter may look for a more direct route to work to avoid changing trains twice.","zh":"通勤者可能尋找通往工作的更直接路線，以避免轉兩次車。"},{"en":"Direct routes reduce time, cost, and risk, so merchants value them highly.","zh":"直接路線減少時間、成本和風險，所以商人非常重視它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improved paths to a destination.","zh":"這個短語描述通往目的地的改良路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Asian and African markets","meaning":"亞洲和非洲市場","examples":[{"en":"European peoples wanted new routes to Asian and African markets.","zh":"歐洲民族想要通往亞洲和非洲市場的新路線。"},{"en":"Asian and African markets are places or trading networks in Asia and Africa where goods are bought and sold.","zh":"Asian and African markets 指亞洲和非洲買賣貨品的地方或貿易網絡。"},{"en":"European merchants wanted Asian and African markets because they offered spices, textiles, metals, and other valuable goods.","zh":"歐洲商人想進入亞洲和非洲市場，因為那裏提供香料、紡織品、金屬和其他貴重貨品。"},{"en":"Access to distant markets could create profit and political power.","zh":"進入遙遠市場可以創造利潤和政治力量。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to commercial opportunities in two large regions.","zh":"這個短語指兩大地區中的商業機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"efforts took them to","meaning":"他們的努力令他們到達……","examples":[{"en":"Their efforts took them to the Americas and Oceania.","zh":"他們的努力令他們到達美洲和大洋洲。"},{"en":"If efforts take people to a place, their attempts or searches eventually lead them there.","zh":"efforts take people to a place 指他們的嘗試或尋找最終把他們帶到某地。"},{"en":"A student’s search for better education may take her to a university overseas.","zh":"學生尋找更好教育的努力，可能令她到達海外大學。"},{"en":"Trying to solve one problem can unexpectedly take people to new places or discoveries.","zh":"嘗試解決一個問題，可以意外地把人帶到新地方或新發現。"},{"en":"The phrase links purposeful effort with an eventual destination.","zh":"這個短語把有目的的努力與最終目的地連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not only…, but eventually…","meaning":"不但……，最終還……","examples":[{"en":"Their efforts took them not only to the eastern hemisphere, but eventually to the Americas and Oceania.","zh":"他們的努力不但令他們到達東半球，最終還到達美洲和大洋洲。"},{"en":"Not only A, but eventually B means first A happened, and later the process extended to B as well.","zh":"not only A, but eventually B 指先發生 A，後來過程也擴展至 B。"},{"en":"Online learning spread not only to universities, but eventually to primary schools.","zh":"網上學習不但傳到大學，最終還傳到小學。"},{"en":"The structure shows expansion from one result to a later, wider result.","zh":"這個結構顯示由一個結果擴展到後來更廣泛的結果。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing historical development over time.","zh":"它適合描述隨時間出現的歷史發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the Americas and Oceania","meaning":"美洲和大洋洲","examples":[{"en":"European voyages eventually reached the Americas and Oceania.","zh":"歐洲航行最終到達美洲和大洋洲。"},{"en":"The Americas and Oceania refer to the continents and regions of North and South America and the Pacific island world including Australia and nearby islands.","zh":"Americas and Oceania 指北美洲、南美洲，以及包括澳洲和附近島嶼在內的太平洋島嶼世界。"},{"en":"World history classes study the Americas and Oceania to understand exploration, colonisation, and cultural exchange.","zh":"世界歷史課研究美洲和大洋洲，以理解探索、殖民和文化交流。"},{"en":"European travel to these regions changed global trade, migration, and political power.","zh":"歐洲到這些地區的旅行改變了全球貿易、遷徙和政治力量。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies large regions outside the old Afro-Eurasian travel world.","zh":"這個短語指出舊亞非歐旅行世界以外的大型地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dominate travel and travel writing","meaning":"主導旅行和旅行寫作","examples":[{"en":"Muslim and Chinese peoples dominated travel and travel writing in post-classical times.","zh":"穆斯林和中國人在後古典時代主導旅行和旅行寫作。"},{"en":"To dominate travel and travel writing means to be the most active or influential group in travelling and producing travel accounts.","zh":"dominate travel and travel writing 指在旅行和產生旅行記述方面成為最活躍或最有影響力的群體。"},{"en":"A country can dominate scientific publishing if its researchers produce the largest share of important papers.","zh":"如果某國研究者產出最多重要論文，它可以主導科學出版。"},{"en":"Groups dominate a field when they travel more, write more, or shape what others know.","zh":"當某群體旅行更多、書寫更多或塑造他人所知，就會主導某領域。"},{"en":"The phrase describes leadership or strong influence in both movement and written records.","zh":"這個短語描述在移動和文字記錄兩方面的領導或強大影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take centre stage","meaning":"成為焦點；佔據主導地位","examples":[{"en":"European explorers and missionaries took centre stage during the early modern era.","zh":"歐洲探險家和傳教士在近代早期成為焦點。"},{"en":"To take centre stage means to become the main focus of attention or activity.","zh":"take centre stage 指成為注意力或活動的主要焦點。"},{"en":"During a school concert, the choir may take centre stage after weeks of practice.","zh":"在學校音樂會中，合唱團可能在數週練習後成為焦點。"},{"en":"A group takes centre stage when its actions become more visible or important than others’.","zh":"當某群體的行動比其他人更顯眼或重要，它就會佔據主導地位。"},{"en":"The phrase comes from theatre and means becoming central.","zh":"這個短語來自劇場，意思是變得居中重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the early modern era","meaning":"近代早期","examples":[{"en":"European travel expanded during the early modern era.","zh":"歐洲旅行在近代早期擴展。"},{"en":"The early modern era is the historical period after the Middle Ages and before the modern industrial age.","zh":"early modern era 指中世紀之後、現代工業時代之前的歷史時期。"},{"en":"Historians often connect the early modern era with exploration, empire, printing, and global trade.","zh":"歷史學家常把近代早期與探索、帝國、印刷和全球貿易連起來。"},{"en":"Travel writing expanded in this period because more voyages were recorded and printed.","zh":"這一時期旅行寫作擴展，因為更多航行被記錄和印刷。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a major transition period in world history.","zh":"這個短語指出世界歷史中的重要過渡時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"by no means","meaning":"絕不；完全不是","examples":[{"en":"Muslim and Chinese travel by no means came to a halt.","zh":"穆斯林和中國旅行絕沒有停止。"},{"en":"By no means means definitely not or in no way.","zh":"by no means 指絕對不是或完全不。"},{"en":"A difficult exam is by no means impossible if students prepare carefully.","zh":"如果學生仔細準備，困難考試絕非不可能。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly rejects a possible misunderstanding.","zh":"這個短語強烈否定一種可能誤解。"},{"en":"It is more formal and emphatic than simply saying “not”.","zh":"它比單純說 “not” 更正式和強調。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"come to a halt","meaning":"停止","examples":[{"en":"Muslim and Chinese travel did not come to a halt in early modern times.","zh":"穆斯林和中國旅行在近代早期並沒有停止。"},{"en":"To come to a halt means to stop moving, developing, or continuing.","zh":"come to a halt 指停止移動、發展或持續。"},{"en":"Traffic came to a halt when an accident blocked the tunnel.","zh":"當意外堵塞隧道，交通便停止了。"},{"en":"A tradition does not come to a halt just because another culture becomes more visible.","zh":"傳統不會只因另一種文化變得更顯眼就停止。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stopping completely.","zh":"這個短語描述完全停止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"venture to distant corners of","meaning":"冒險前往……的遙遠角落","examples":[{"en":"European peoples ventured to distant corners of the globe.","zh":"歐洲民族冒險前往全球的遙遠角落。"},{"en":"To venture to distant corners of a place means to travel boldly to remote or faraway parts of it.","zh":"venture to distant corners of a place 指大膽前往某地偏遠或遙遠部分。"},{"en":"A photographer may venture to distant corners of a country to capture rare landscapes.","zh":"攝影師可能冒險前往一個國家的遙遠角落，拍攝罕見景觀。"},{"en":"People venture far when they are driven by trade, mission, knowledge, or ambition.","zh":"當人們受貿易、使命、知識或野心推動，就會冒險遠行。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests risky travel to remote places.","zh":"這個短語暗示前往偏遠地方的冒險旅行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the globe","meaning":"全球；世界","examples":[{"en":"European travellers described distant corners of the globe.","zh":"歐洲旅行者描述全球遙遠角落。"},{"en":"The globe means the whole world or the Earth.","zh":"the globe 指整個世界或地球。"},{"en":"News can now travel around the globe within minutes.","zh":"新聞現在可以在數分鐘內傳遍全球。"},{"en":"Travel writing helped readers imagine parts of the globe they had never seen.","zh":"旅行寫作幫助讀者想像自己從未見過的世界各地。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used when discussing worldwide movement or knowledge.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論全球範圍的移動或知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"printing presses churned out","meaning":"印刷機大量出版","examples":[{"en":"European printing presses churned out thousands of travel accounts.","zh":"歐洲印刷機大量出版數以千計的旅行記述。"},{"en":"If printing presses churn out books, they produce large numbers of printed works quickly.","zh":"printing presses churn out books 指印刷機快速生產大量印刷作品。"},{"en":"During exam season, photocopiers may churn out hundreds of worksheets for students.","zh":"考試季節期間，影印機可能大量印出數百份學生工作紙。"},{"en":"Printing technology increased the spread of travel writing because books could be produced in quantity.","zh":"印刷技術增加旅行寫作的傳播，因為書籍可以大量生產。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests mass production.","zh":"這個短語暗示大規模生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a reading public","meaning":"閱讀大眾","examples":[{"en":"Travel accounts were written for a reading public.","zh":"旅行記述是為閱讀大眾而寫的。"},{"en":"A reading public is a group of people who regularly read and buy written material.","zh":"reading public 指定期閱讀和購買文字材料的一群人。"},{"en":"Newspapers grew when a reading public became large enough to support daily publication.","zh":"當閱讀大眾大到足以支持每日出版，報紙便發展起來。"},{"en":"Writers publish more when there is a reading public eager for stories or information.","zh":"當有渴望故事或資訊的閱讀大眾，作者便會出版更多。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an audience of readers.","zh":"這個短語描述讀者群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"apparently insatiable appetite for","meaning":"對……似乎有無窮的興趣","examples":[{"en":"The reading public had an apparently insatiable appetite for news about the larger world.","zh":"閱讀大眾對更廣闊世界的消息似乎有無窮的興趣。"},{"en":"An apparently insatiable appetite for something is a desire that seems impossible to satisfy.","zh":"apparently insatiable appetite for something 指對某事的渴望似乎無法被滿足。"},{"en":"Many teenagers have an apparently insatiable appetite for short videos on their phones.","zh":"許多青少年對手機短片似乎有無窮的興趣。"},{"en":"When people constantly demand more information, publishers produce more to meet that appetite.","zh":"當人們持續要求更多資訊，出版商就會生產更多以滿足這種渴望。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly describes intense and continuing interest.","zh":"這個短語強烈描述 intense 而持續的興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the volume of travel literature","meaning":"旅行文學的數量","examples":[{"en":"The volume of travel literature was extremely great.","zh":"旅行文學的數量極其龐大。"},{"en":"The volume of travel literature means the total amount of travel writing produced or available.","zh":"volume of travel literature 指旅行寫作被生產或可取得的總量。"},{"en":"The volume of online study materials can be overwhelming for students before exams.","zh":"考試前，網上學習材料的數量可能令學生不知所措。"},{"en":"A high volume of travel literature shows strong public interest and active publishing.","zh":"大量旅行文學顯示公眾興趣強烈，出版活動活躍。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to quantity, not loudness.","zh":"這個短語指數量，而不是音量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"assemble numerous travel accounts","meaning":"彙編大量旅行記述","examples":[{"en":"Several editors assembled numerous travel accounts.","zh":"幾位編者彙編了大量旅行記述。"},{"en":"To assemble numerous travel accounts means to collect many travel writings and put them together.","zh":"assemble numerous travel accounts 指收集許多旅行寫作並把它們放在一起。"},{"en":"A teacher may assemble numerous student essays into a class writing booklet.","zh":"老師可能把大量學生作文彙編成一本班級寫作小冊子。"},{"en":"Editors assemble accounts so readers can access many journeys in one organised collection.","zh":"編者彙編記述，讓讀者能在一個有組織文集中接觸許多旅程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gathering and arranging many texts.","zh":"這個短語描述收集並整理大量文本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make something available in","meaning":"以……形式提供某物","examples":[{"en":"Editors made travel accounts available in enormous published collections.","zh":"編者以龐大出版文集形式提供旅行記述。"},{"en":"To make something available in a form means to provide it so people can access it through that form.","zh":"make something available in a form 指以某形式提供某物，讓人們可以取得。"},{"en":"A school may make worksheets available in an online folder for absent students.","zh":"學校可能把工作紙放在網上資料夾，以供缺席學生使用。"},{"en":"Making information available increases its audience and usefulness.","zh":"提供資訊可以增加其受眾和用途。"},{"en":"The phrase describes providing access.","zh":"這個短語描述提供取得途徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"published collections","meaning":"出版文集","examples":[{"en":"Travel accounts appeared in enormous published collections.","zh":"旅行記述出現在龐大的出版文集中。"},{"en":"Published collections are books or volumes that gather many writings and make them available to readers.","zh":"published collections 指收集許多作品並提供給讀者的書籍或卷冊。"},{"en":"A poetry club may create a published collection of members’ best poems.","zh":"詩社可能製作一本成員最佳詩作的出版文集。"},{"en":"Collections preserve writing because individual pieces are less easily lost when printed together.","zh":"文集保存寫作，因為個別作品一起印刷後較不容易遺失。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised printed works.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的印刷作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make one’s way to","meaning":"前往……","examples":[{"en":"European travellers made their way to the interior regions of Africa and the Americas.","zh":"歐洲旅行者前往非洲和美洲的內陸地區。"},{"en":"To make one’s way to a place means to travel there, often gradually or with effort.","zh":"make one’s way to a place 指前往某地，通常是逐步或費力地去。"},{"en":"After school, students make their way to the bus stop through crowded streets.","zh":"放學後，學生穿過擁擠街道前往巴士站。"},{"en":"Travellers make their way to remote regions when roads are difficult and progress is slow.","zh":"當道路困難且進展緩慢，旅行者會費力前往偏遠地區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reaching a place through movement and effort.","zh":"這個短語描述透過移動和努力到達某地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"interior regions","meaning":"內陸地區","examples":[{"en":"European travellers explored interior regions of Africa and the Americas.","zh":"歐洲旅行者探索非洲和美洲的內陸地區。"},{"en":"Interior regions are inland areas far from coasts, borders, or major ports.","zh":"interior regions 指遠離海岸、邊界或主要港口的內陸地區。"},{"en":"A country’s interior regions may have villages, forests, mountains, and rivers that tourists rarely see.","zh":"一個國家的內陸地區可能有遊客較少看見的村莊、森林、山脈和河流。"},{"en":"Travelling into interior regions can be harder because transport and supplies may be limited.","zh":"前往內陸地區可能較困難，因為交通和補給可能有限。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts inland areas with coastal or outer areas.","zh":"這個短語把內陸地區與沿海或外圍地區作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"generate a fresh round of","meaning":"帶來新一輪……","examples":[{"en":"European travel generated a fresh round of travel writing.","zh":"歐洲旅行帶來新一輪旅行寫作。"},{"en":"To generate a fresh round of something means to cause a new wave or new period of that activity.","zh":"generate a fresh round of something 指造成某活動的新一波或新時期。"},{"en":"A new education policy may generate a fresh round of debate among teachers and parents.","zh":"新教育政策可能在老師和家長之間帶來新一輪辯論。"},{"en":"New journeys create new stories, which can lead to more writing and publishing.","zh":"新旅程創造新故事，繼而帶來更多寫作和出版。"},{"en":"The phrase describes causing renewed activity.","zh":"這個短語描述引發 renewed 活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"meanwhile","meaning":"與此同時","examples":[{"en":"Meanwhile, colonial administrators wrote about colonial societies.","zh":"與此同時，殖民地行政官員撰寫關於殖民地社會的作品。"},{"en":"Meanwhile means at the same time, or while another event is happening.","zh":"meanwhile 指同時，或在另一事件發生期間。"},{"en":"The students practised speaking; meanwhile, the teacher prepared feedback sheets.","zh":"學生練習口語；與此同時，老師準備回饋表。"},{"en":"The word helps writers show parallel developments.","zh":"這個詞幫助作者顯示並行發展。"},{"en":"It connects two events occurring during the same general period.","zh":"它連接同一大致時期內發生的兩件事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"colonial administrators","meaning":"殖民地行政官員","examples":[{"en":"Colonial administrators devoted numerous writings to colonial subjects.","zh":"殖民地行政官員撰寫大量關於殖民地臣民的作品。"},{"en":"Colonial administrators were officials who governed or managed colonies for imperial powers.","zh":"colonial administrators 指為帝國勢力治理或管理殖民地的官員。"},{"en":"A colonial administrator might write reports about local laws, taxes, resources, and people.","zh":"殖民地行政官員可能撰寫關於本地法律、稅收、資源和人民的報告。"},{"en":"Their writings can reveal both useful information and the biases of colonial rule.","zh":"他們的作品可以揭示有用資訊，也可以揭示殖民統治的偏見。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies government officials within colonial systems.","zh":"這個短語指出殖民制度中的政府官員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"devote writings to","meaning":"撰寫大量關於……的作品","examples":[{"en":"Colonial administrators devoted numerous writings to the societies of their colonial subjects.","zh":"殖民地行政官員撰寫大量關於其殖民地臣民社會的作品。"},{"en":"To devote writings to a topic means to write a lot about it or focus written work on it.","zh":"devote writings to a topic 指大量書寫某主題，或把文字工作集中於該主題。"},{"en":"A historian may devote several chapters to the lives of ordinary workers.","zh":"歷史學家可能用幾章撰寫關於普通工人生活的內容。"},{"en":"Writers devote attention to a topic when they think it is important, useful, or politically necessary.","zh":"當作者認為某主題重要、有用或在政治上必要，就會把注意力投入其中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes focused written effort.","zh":"這個短語描述集中的文字努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"colonial subjects","meaning":"殖民地臣民；殖民地人民","examples":[{"en":"Administrators wrote about the societies of their colonial subjects.","zh":"行政官員撰寫關於其殖民地人民社會的作品。"},{"en":"Colonial subjects were people living under colonial rule rather than self-government.","zh":"colonial subjects 指生活在殖民統治下，而非自治的人。"},{"en":"Colonial subjects often had little power over the laws and policies imposed on them.","zh":"殖民地臣民通常對施加於他們的法律和政策缺乏權力。"},{"en":"Writings about colonial subjects may reflect the viewpoint of rulers more than local people themselves.","zh":"關於殖民地人民的作品，可能更多反映統治者觀點，而不是本地人自己。"},{"en":"The phrase describes people governed by a colonial power.","zh":"這個短語描述受殖民勢力管治的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"colonies they established","meaning":"他們建立的殖民地","examples":[{"en":"European powers wrote about Asian and African colonies they established.","zh":"歐洲列強撰寫關於他們在亞洲和非洲建立的殖民地。"},{"en":"Colonies they established are territories that powerful states created and controlled outside their own homeland.","zh":"colonies they established 指強國在自己本土以外建立並控制的領土。"},{"en":"A history textbook may discuss colonies established by European empires in Africa and Asia.","zh":"歷史教科書可能討論歐洲帝國在非洲和亞洲建立的殖民地。"},{"en":"Colonies were established for trade, resources, strategy, settlement, or political power.","zh":"殖民地因貿易、資源、戰略、定居或政治權力而建立。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies territories created under imperial control.","zh":"這個短語指出在帝國控制下建立的領土。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"by mid-century","meaning":"到十九世紀中葉","examples":[{"en":"By mid-century, attention was flowing in the other direction.","zh":"到十九世紀中葉，注意力正流向相反方向。"},{"en":"By mid-century means by the middle of a particular century.","zh":"by mid-century 指到某一個世紀的中期為止。"},{"en":"By mid-century, many cities may need new transport systems if populations keep growing.","zh":"如果人口持續增長，到本世紀中葉，許多城市可能需要新交通系統。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a time marker for when a change had happened.","zh":"這個短語提供變化已經發生的時間標記。"},{"en":"It is often used in historical or future projections.","zh":"它常用於歷史或未來預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"flow in the other direction","meaning":"流向相反方向","examples":[{"en":"By mid-century, attention was also flowing in the other direction.","zh":"到十九世紀中葉，注意力也開始流向相反方向。"},{"en":"To flow in the other direction means to move or shift the opposite way from before.","zh":"flow in the other direction 指朝與之前相反的方向移動或轉移。"},{"en":"At first students copied foreign styles; later, influence began to flow in the other direction.","zh":"起初學生模仿外國風格；後來，影響開始流向相反方向。"},{"en":"Cultural attention shifts when one side becomes curious about the other side’s power or knowledge.","zh":"當一方對另一方的力量或知識感到好奇，文化注意力便會轉向。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reversal in movement, influence, or interest.","zh":"這個短語描述移動、影響或興趣的逆轉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be painfully aware of","meaning":"深切意識到……","examples":[{"en":"Asian travellers were painfully aware of European military and technological prowess.","zh":"亞洲旅行者深切意識到歐洲的軍事和科技實力。"},{"en":"To be painfully aware of something means to know it very clearly, often with discomfort, worry, or humiliation.","zh":"be painfully aware of something 指非常清楚知道某事，通常帶有不安、憂慮或羞辱感。"},{"en":"A student who fails a mock exam may become painfully aware of her weak grammar.","zh":"模擬試不合格的學生可能深切意識到自己的文法弱點。"},{"en":"People are painfully aware of a problem when it directly affects their confidence or safety.","zh":"當問題直接影響信心或安全，人們會深切意識到它。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests knowledge that is sharp and unpleasant.","zh":"這個短語暗示清楚但令人不舒服的認知。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"military and technological prowess","meaning":"軍事和科技實力","examples":[{"en":"Asian travellers observed the military and technological prowess of Europe.","zh":"亞洲旅行者觀察到歐洲的軍事和科技實力。"},{"en":"Military and technological prowess means great skill, strength, or superiority in warfare and technology.","zh":"military and technological prowess 指在戰爭和科技方面的高超能力、力量或優勢。"},{"en":"A country may show technological prowess through advanced trains, hospitals, or communication systems.","zh":"一個國家可能透過先進火車、醫院或通訊系統展示科技實力。"},{"en":"Observing another society’s prowess can push reformers to ask how their own society should change.","zh":"觀察另一社會的實力，可以推動改革者思考自己社會應如何改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes impressive power and capability.","zh":"這個短語描述令人印象深刻的力量和能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Euro-American societies","meaning":"歐洲及歐美社會","examples":[{"en":"Asian travellers visited European and Euro-American societies.","zh":"亞洲旅行者到訪歐洲及歐美社會。"},{"en":"Euro-American societies are societies shaped by European and American political, economic, and cultural systems.","zh":"Euro-American societies 指受歐洲和美國政治、經濟及文化制度塑造的社會。"},{"en":"Asian reformers studied Euro-American societies to understand schools, parliaments, factories, and armies.","zh":"亞洲改革者研究歐美社會，以理解學校、議會、工廠和軍隊。"},{"en":"Visiting such societies helped travellers compare institutions and identify possible reforms at home.","zh":"到訪這類社會幫助旅行者比較制度，並找出本國可能改革之處。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to Europe and societies in the Americas influenced by Europe.","zh":"這個短語指歐洲，以及受歐洲影響的美洲社會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in hopes of discovering","meaning":"希望發現……","examples":[{"en":"Asian travellers visited the West in hopes of discovering useful principles.","zh":"亞洲旅行者到訪西方，希望發現有用原則。"},{"en":"In hopes of discovering something means with the aim of finding or learning it.","zh":"in hopes of discovering something 指帶着尋找或學習某事的目的。"},{"en":"A student may join a summer programme in hopes of discovering what career suits her.","zh":"學生可能參加暑期計劃，希望發現適合自己的職業。"},{"en":"Travellers visit foreign societies when they hope to discover ideas that can solve problems at home.","zh":"當旅行者希望發現能解決本國問題的想法，便會到訪外國社會。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a hopeful purpose for action.","zh":"這個短語給出帶希望的行動目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"principles useful for","meaning":"對……有用的原則","examples":[{"en":"They hoped to discover principles useful for the organisation of their societies.","zh":"他們希望發現對自己社會組織方式有用的原則。"},{"en":"Principles useful for something are basic ideas or rules that can help achieve that purpose.","zh":"principles useful for something 指能幫助達成某目的的基本想法或規則。"},{"en":"A teacher may look for principles useful for managing a noisy classroom fairly.","zh":"老師可能尋找對公平管理嘈雜課室有用的原則。"},{"en":"Societies study foreign systems when they want principles that can guide reform.","zh":"當社會想要能指導改革的原則，就會研究外國制度。"},{"en":"The phrase connects general ideas with practical use.","zh":"這個短語把一般想法與實際用途連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the organisation of their own societies","meaning":"自己社會的組織方式","examples":[{"en":"Asian travellers studied principles for the organisation of their own societies.","zh":"亞洲旅行者研究適用於自己社會組織方式的原則。"},{"en":"The organisation of their own societies means the way their societies are structured, governed, educated, and managed.","zh":"organisation of their own societies 指他們自己的社會如何被組織、治理、教育和管理。"},{"en":"A reformer may study schools abroad to improve the organisation of education in her own society.","zh":"改革者可能研究外國學校，以改善自己社會的教育組織方式。"},{"en":"Understanding organisation helps leaders decide how laws, institutions, and public services should work.","zh":"理解組織方式幫助領導者決定法律、制度和公共服務應如何運作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to social structure and systems.","zh":"這個短語指社會結構和制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"among the most prominent of","meaning":"屬於最著名的……之一","examples":[{"en":"Sun Yat-sen was among the most prominent of these travellers.","zh":"孫中山屬於這些旅行者中最著名的人物之一。"},{"en":"Among the most prominent of a group means one of the most famous, important, or noticeable members of that group.","zh":"among the most prominent of a group 指某群體中最著名、最重要或最顯眼的成員之一。"},{"en":"In a class debate, one speaker may be among the most prominent because her argument is clear and persuasive.","zh":"在班級辯論中，一名講者可能因論點清楚而有說服力，成為最突出者之一。"},{"en":"Prominent figures are remembered because their actions or writings have wider influence.","zh":"重要人物被記住，因為他們的行動或作品有更廣泛影響。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies someone as especially important within a group.","zh":"這個短語指出某人在群體中特別重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make extensive use of","meaning":"廣泛運用……","examples":[{"en":"Fukuzawa Yukichi made extensive use of his overseas observations.","zh":"福澤諭吉廣泛運用自己的海外觀察。"},{"en":"To make extensive use of something means to use it a lot and in many ways.","zh":"make extensive use of something 指大量並以多種方式使用某物。"},{"en":"A teacher may make extensive use of real student mistakes when preparing grammar lessons.","zh":"老師準備文法課時，可能廣泛運用真實學生錯誤。"},{"en":"Travellers make extensive use of observations when they turn experience into reform ideas or books.","zh":"旅行者把經驗轉化為改革思想或書籍時，會廣泛運用觀察。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses frequent and serious use.","zh":"這個短語強調頻繁而認真的使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"overseas observations and experiences","meaning":"海外觀察和經驗","examples":[{"en":"These writers used their overseas observations and experiences in their writings.","zh":"這些作者在作品中使用自己的海外觀察和經驗。"},{"en":"Overseas observations and experiences are things people notice, learn, and live through while abroad.","zh":"overseas observations and experiences 指人們在海外注意到、學到和親身經歷的事情。"},{"en":"A student may use overseas observations and experiences when writing an essay about education systems.","zh":"學生寫關於教育制度的文章時，可能使用海外觀察和經驗。"},{"en":"First-hand experience can make writing richer because it includes details from real life.","zh":"第一手經驗可以令寫作更豐富，因為它包括真實生活細節。"},{"en":"The phrase combines what travellers saw with what they personally went through.","zh":"這個短語結合旅行者所見和親身經歷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Japanese reformer","meaning":"日本改革家","examples":[{"en":"Fukuzawa Yukichi was a Japanese reformer.","zh":"福澤諭吉是一位日本改革家。"},{"en":"A Japanese reformer is a person from Japan who works to change and improve society, government, education, or culture.","zh":"Japanese reformer 指來自日本、致力改變和改善社會、政府、教育或文化的人。"},{"en":"A reformer may study foreign systems to decide which ideas could help his own country.","zh":"改革家可能研究外國制度，以決定哪些想法能幫助自己的國家。"},{"en":"Reformers often travel because seeing other societies gives them models for change.","zh":"改革家常旅行，因為觀察其他社會能給他們改革模式。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies both nationality and role.","zh":"這個短語同時指出國籍和角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Chinese revolutionary","meaning":"中國革命家","examples":[{"en":"Sun Yat-sen was a Chinese revolutionary.","zh":"孫中山是一位中國革命家。"},{"en":"A Chinese revolutionary is a Chinese person who works to overthrow or radically change an existing political system.","zh":"Chinese revolutionary 指致力推翻或徹底改變現有政治制度的中國人。"},{"en":"A revolutionary may travel abroad to seek support, learn ideas, or organise movements.","zh":"革命家可能到海外尋求支持、學習思想或組織運動。"},{"en":"Revolutionary travel can connect political change at home with ideas and networks overseas.","zh":"革命性的旅行可以把本國政治變革與海外思想和網絡連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a person involved in major political transformation.","zh":"這個短語指出參與重大政治轉型的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"inexpensive and reliable means of","meaning":"廉宜而可靠的……方式","examples":[{"en":"The development of inexpensive and reliable means of mass transport changed travel.","zh":"廉宜而可靠的大眾交通方式的發展改變了旅行。"},{"en":"Inexpensive and reliable means of something are cheap and dependable ways to do it.","zh":"inexpensive and reliable means of something 指做某事既便宜又可靠的方法。"},{"en":"Online payment became popular when people found inexpensive and reliable means of transferring money.","zh":"當人們找到廉宜而可靠的轉帳方式，網上支付便變得流行。"},{"en":"Travel expands when transport becomes affordable and predictable.","zh":"當交通變得負擔得起且可預測，旅行便會擴展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes methods that are both low-cost and trustworthy.","zh":"這個短語描述低成本且可信賴的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"mass transport","meaning":"大眾交通運輸","examples":[{"en":"Mass transport made long-distance travel easier.","zh":"大眾交通運輸令長途旅行更容易。"},{"en":"Mass transport is transport that carries large numbers of people, such as trains, buses, ships, and planes.","zh":"mass transport 指運載大量人群的交通，例如火車、巴士、船和飛機。"},{"en":"A city needs good mass transport so workers and students can travel without relying only on cars.","zh":"城市需要良好大眾交通，讓工人和學生不必只依賴私家車出行。"},{"en":"Mass transport lowers the cost of travel because many passengers share the system.","zh":"大眾交通降低旅行成本，因為許多乘客共同使用系統。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to public or large-scale transport systems.","zh":"這個短語指公共或大規模交通系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"witness explosions both in… and in…","meaning":"見證……和……的急速增長","examples":[{"en":"The twentieth century witnessed explosions both in long-distance travel and in travel writing.","zh":"二十世紀見證長途旅行和旅行寫作的急速增長。"},{"en":"To witness explosions both in A and in B means to see rapid growth in two areas.","zh":"witness explosions both in A and in B 指見證兩個範疇快速增長。"},{"en":"The internet age witnessed explosions both in online shopping and in digital advertising.","zh":"互聯網時代見證網上購物和數碼廣告的急速增長。"},{"en":"When technology lowers cost, related activities can grow quickly together.","zh":"當科技降低成本，相關活動可以一起快速增長。"},{"en":"The phrase uses “explosions” metaphorically to mean sudden large increases.","zh":"這個短語以 “explosions” 作比喻，意思是突然大幅增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the frequency of","meaning":"……的頻率","examples":[{"en":"The frequency of long-distance travel increased in the twentieth century.","zh":"長途旅行的頻率在二十世紀增加。"},{"en":"The frequency of something is how often it happens.","zh":"frequency of something 指某事發生得有多頻密。"},{"en":"A teacher may measure the frequency of late homework to see whether a class needs more support.","zh":"老師可能量度遲交功課的頻率，以了解班級是否需要更多支援。"},{"en":"When transport becomes cheaper, the frequency of travel usually rises.","zh":"當交通變得較便宜，旅行頻率通常上升。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how often an event occurs.","zh":"這個短語重點是事件發生的頻密程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"long-distance travel","meaning":"長途旅行","examples":[{"en":"Long-distance travel became much more common in the twentieth century.","zh":"長途旅行在二十世紀變得常見得多。"},{"en":"Long-distance travel is travel over a great distance, often between regions, countries, or continents.","zh":"long-distance travel 指跨越很大距離的旅行，通常在地區、國家或大洲之間。"},{"en":"A student may make long-distance travel to attend university in another country.","zh":"學生可能進行長途旅行，到另一個國家升讀大學。"},{"en":"Better trains, ships, and planes made long-distance travel faster and more affordable.","zh":"更好的火車、船和飛機令長途旅行更快且更負擔得起。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts extended journeys with short local trips.","zh":"這個短語把長途旅程與短程本地出行作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the volume of","meaning":"……的數量","examples":[{"en":"The volume of travel writing also increased.","zh":"旅行寫作的數量也增加。"},{"en":"The volume of something is the total amount or quantity of it.","zh":"volume of something 指某事物的總量或數量。"},{"en":"The volume of homework may rise before final exams.","zh":"期末考試前，功課數量可能上升。"},{"en":"When more people travel, the volume of travel writing can also increase because more experiences are recorded.","zh":"當更多人旅行，旅行寫作的數量也可能增加，因為更多經驗被記錄。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to amount, not sound level in this context.","zh":"在這個語境中，這個短語指數量，而不是音量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a great deal of","meaning":"大量的……","examples":[{"en":"A great deal of travel took place for business and diplomacy.","zh":"大量旅行是為了商業和外交而發生。"},{"en":"A great deal of something means a large amount of it.","zh":"a great deal of something 指大量某事物。"},{"en":"A great deal of preparation is needed before a public speaking competition.","zh":"公開演說比賽前需要大量準備。"},{"en":"When business expands, a great deal of travel may be needed to meet partners and clients.","zh":"當商業擴張，可能需要大量旅行來會見合作伙伴和客戶。"},{"en":"The phrase is used with uncountable nouns or general activities.","zh":"這個短語用於不可數名詞或一般活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take place for reasons of","meaning":"因……原因而發生","examples":[{"en":"Travel took place for reasons of business, administration, and diplomacy.","zh":"旅行因商業、行政和外交原因而發生。"},{"en":"To take place for reasons of something means to happen because of those purposes or motives.","zh":"take place for reasons of something 指因那些目的或動機而發生。"},{"en":"A meeting may take place for reasons of safety after a serious accident.","zh":"嚴重事故後，會議可能因安全原因而舉行。"},{"en":"Travel happens for different reasons, such as profit, religious duty, government work, or leisure.","zh":"旅行因不同原因而發生，例如利潤、宗教責任、政府工作或休閒。"},{"en":"The phrase formally explains why an activity occurs.","zh":"這個短語正式解釋某活動為何發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"administration and diplomacy","meaning":"行政和外交","examples":[{"en":"Some travel took place for administration and diplomacy.","zh":"有些旅行是為了行政和外交。"},{"en":"Administration and diplomacy refer to government management and official relations between states or groups.","zh":"administration and diplomacy 指政府管理，以及國家或群體之間的官方關係。"},{"en":"Officials may travel for administration and diplomacy when they inspect provinces or meet foreign leaders.","zh":"官員巡視省份或會見外國領袖時，可能為行政和外交而旅行。"},{"en":"Governments need such travel because rules, reports, and negotiations often require direct contact.","zh":"政府需要這類旅行，因為規則、報告和談判常需要直接接觸。"},{"en":"The phrase combines internal governance with external relations.","zh":"這個短語結合內部治理和外部關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"missionary work","meaning":"傳教工作","examples":[{"en":"Missionary work remained a reason for travel.","zh":"傳教工作仍然是旅行的原因。"},{"en":"Missionary work is religious work aimed at spreading faith, teaching, serving communities, or converting people.","zh":"missionary work 指旨在傳播信仰、教學、服務社區或使人改信宗教的宗教工作。"},{"en":"Missionaries may travel to distant places to build schools, translate texts, or preach.","zh":"傳教士可能前往遙遠地方建學校、翻譯文本或講道。"},{"en":"Missionary work led to travel because religious goals often required contact with new communities.","zh":"傳教工作導致旅行，因為宗教目標常需要接觸新社群。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to religion-based service and outreach.","zh":"這個短語指以宗教為基礎的服務和外展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as in ages past","meaning":"一如過往時代","examples":[{"en":"People still travelled for pilgrimage, as in ages past.","zh":"人們仍然為朝聖而旅行，一如過往時代。"},{"en":"As in ages past means in the same way as people did in earlier periods of history.","zh":"as in ages past 指如較早歷史時期的人那樣。"},{"en":"Families still gather for festivals, as in ages past, even if the celebrations now include modern music.","zh":"家庭仍為節日聚集，一如過往時代，即使慶祝現在包括現代音樂。"},{"en":"The phrase shows continuity between the present and the past.","zh":"這個短語顯示現在與過去之間的延續。"},{"en":"It is slightly literary and often used in historical writing.","zh":"它略帶文學色彩，常用於歷史寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"effective modes of mass transport","meaning":"有效的大眾交通方式","examples":[{"en":"Effective modes of mass transport made new kinds of travel possible.","zh":"有效的大眾交通方式令新型旅行成為可能。"},{"en":"Effective modes of mass transport are reliable ways of carrying many people over distance.","zh":"effective modes of mass transport 指能可靠地運載大量人群跨越距離的方法。"},{"en":"High-speed trains and affordable flights are effective modes of mass transport for modern travellers.","zh":"高速鐵路和廉價航班是現代旅行者有效的大眾交通方式。"},{"en":"When transport becomes effective, more people can travel for work, study, worship, or leisure.","zh":"當交通變得有效，更多人能為工作、學習、敬拜或休閒而旅行。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to transport systems that work well at large scale.","zh":"這個短語指能在大規模下良好運作的交通系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"make it possible for","meaning":"令……成為可能","examples":[{"en":"Mass transport made it possible for new kinds of travel to flourish.","zh":"大眾交通令新型旅行得以蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"To make it possible for something to happen means to create the conditions that allow it to happen.","zh":"make it possible for something to happen 指創造條件，讓某事能夠發生。"},{"en":"Online platforms make it possible for students in small towns to learn from teachers far away.","zh":"網上平台令小鎮學生可以向遠方老師學習成為可能。"},{"en":"Cheap transport made tourism possible for ordinary people, not only the rich.","zh":"廉價交通令普通人也能旅遊，而不只是富人。"},{"en":"The phrase shows what enables a change.","zh":"這個短語顯示甚麼促成改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"flourish","meaning":"蓬勃發展","examples":[{"en":"New kinds of travel began to flourish.","zh":"新型旅行開始蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"To flourish means to grow strongly, develop successfully, or become active and popular.","zh":"flourish 指強勁成長、成功發展或變得活躍和受歡迎。"},{"en":"A school debate club may flourish when students receive good coaching and enough practice time.","zh":"當學生得到良好指導和足夠練習時間，學校辯論學會可能蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"Tourism flourishes when transport is affordable and people have money and free time.","zh":"當交通負擔得起，而人們有金錢和空閒時間，旅遊便會蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"The word describes healthy growth and success.","zh":"這個詞描述健康增長和成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the most distinctive of","meaning":"最具特色的……","examples":[{"en":"The most distinctive of these new forms was mass tourism.","zh":"這些新形式中最具特色的是大眾旅遊。"},{"en":"The most distinctive of a group means the one that stands out most clearly because it is special or different.","zh":"most distinctive of a group 指因特別或不同而最清楚突出的那一項。"},{"en":"The most distinctive of the school’s traditions is its annual night concert.","zh":"學校傳統中最具特色的是年度夜間音樂會。"},{"en":"Something becomes distinctive when its features separate it clearly from other examples.","zh":"當某事的特徵令它與其他例子清楚分開，它就變得具特色。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the most recognisable item in a set.","zh":"這個短語指出一組事物中最易識別的一項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"mass tourism","meaning":"大眾旅遊","examples":[{"en":"Mass tourism emerged as a major form of consumption.","zh":"大眾旅遊逐漸成為主要消費形式。"},{"en":"Mass tourism is large-scale tourism involving many ordinary travellers visiting popular destinations.","zh":"mass tourism 指大量普通旅客到訪熱門目的地的大規模旅遊。"},{"en":"Package tours and cruise holidays are common examples of mass tourism.","zh":"旅行團和郵輪假期是大眾旅遊的常見例子。"},{"en":"Mass tourism grows when transport becomes cheap and people have more leisure time.","zh":"當交通變得便宜，人們有更多閒暇時間，大眾旅遊便會增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes tourism as a widespread consumer activity.","zh":"這個短語描述作為普遍消費活動的旅遊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a major form of consumption","meaning":"主要消費形式","examples":[{"en":"Tourism emerged as a major form of consumption in wealthy societies.","zh":"旅遊在富裕社會中逐漸成為主要消費形式。"},{"en":"A major form of consumption is an important way people spend money to buy goods or experiences.","zh":"major form of consumption 指人們花錢購買貨品或體驗的重要方式。"},{"en":"Streaming subscriptions have become a major form of consumption for many young people.","zh":"對許多年輕人來說，串流訂閱已成為主要消費形式。"},{"en":"Tourism became consumption because people bought travel, hotels, food, entertainment, and experiences.","zh":"旅遊成為消費，因為人們購買交通、酒店、食物、娛樂和體驗。"},{"en":"The phrase treats travel as part of consumer behaviour.","zh":"這個短語把旅行視為消費行為的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"wealthy societies","meaning":"富裕社會","examples":[{"en":"Mass tourism grew among individuals living in wealthy societies.","zh":"大眾旅遊在生活於富裕社會的人之間增長。"},{"en":"Wealthy societies are communities or countries where many people have enough money for comfort, leisure, and extra spending.","zh":"wealthy societies 指許多人有足夠金錢享受舒適、休閒和額外消費的社區或國家。"},{"en":"In wealthy societies, families may spend money on holidays, hobbies, and private lessons.","zh":"在富裕社會中，家庭可能花錢在假期、興趣和私人課程上。"},{"en":"Tourism grows in wealthy societies because people have disposable income and paid leave.","zh":"旅遊在富裕社會增長，因為人們有可支配收入和有薪假期。"},{"en":"The phrase describes societies with high material resources.","zh":"這個短語描述物質資源豐富的社會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"enable consumers to","meaning":"使消費者能夠……","examples":[{"en":"Tourism enabled consumers to get away from home.","zh":"旅遊使消費者能夠離家外遊。"},{"en":"To enable consumers to do something means to make it possible for buyers or ordinary people to do it.","zh":"enable consumers to do something 指令買家或普通人能夠做某事。"},{"en":"Budget airlines enable consumers to visit other countries more cheaply.","zh":"廉價航空使消費者能夠更便宜地到訪其他國家。"},{"en":"Technology enables consumers to compare prices before buying.","zh":"科技使消費者能夠在購買前比較價格。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a service or product with what people can now do.","zh":"這個短語把服務或產品與人們現在能做的事連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"get away from home","meaning":"離家外遊；離開日常生活","examples":[{"en":"Tourism enabled consumers to get away from home.","zh":"旅遊使消費者能夠離家外遊。"},{"en":"To get away from home means to leave one’s normal home environment for rest, change, or enjoyment.","zh":"get away from home 指離開平時的家庭環境，以休息、轉換或享受。"},{"en":"A busy parent may want to get away from home for a weekend to relax.","zh":"忙碌家長可能想週末離家外遊以放鬆。"},{"en":"People travel for leisure because distance from daily routines can feel refreshing.","zh":"人們為休閒而旅行，因為離開日常慣例會令人感到清新。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests escape from ordinary life, not permanent migration.","zh":"這個短語暗示逃離平常生活，而不是永久移民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"see the sights","meaning":"觀光","examples":[{"en":"Tourists travelled to Rome to see the sights.","zh":"遊客前往羅馬觀光。"},{"en":"To see the sights means to visit famous or interesting places in a city or region.","zh":"see the sights 指到訪城市或地區中著名或有趣的地方。"},{"en":"A family visiting London may see the sights, such as museums, bridges, and historic buildings.","zh":"到倫敦旅行的家庭可能觀光，例如參觀博物館、橋樑和歷史建築。"},{"en":"Sightseeing becomes easier when guidebooks, maps, and transport are available.","zh":"當有旅遊指南、地圖和交通，觀光會變得更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to tourism focused on places worth seeing.","zh":"這個短語指以值得觀看的地點為中心的旅遊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"take a cruise through","meaning":"乘郵輪遊覽……","examples":[{"en":"Some tourists took a cruise through the Caribbean.","zh":"有些遊客乘郵輪遊覽加勒比海。"},{"en":"To take a cruise through a region means to travel by ship for pleasure through that area.","zh":"take a cruise through a region 指乘船為娛樂目的遊覽該地區。"},{"en":"Retired couples may take a cruise through several Mediterranean ports.","zh":"退休夫婦可能乘郵輪遊覽幾個地中海港口。"},{"en":"Cruises became popular because travellers can sleep, eat, and move between destinations on one vessel.","zh":"郵輪變得受歡迎，因為旅客可以在同一艘船上睡覺、進食並在目的地之間移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes leisure travel by ship.","zh":"這個短語描述乘船休閒旅行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"walk the Great Wall of China","meaning":"遊覽中國長城","examples":[{"en":"Tourists travelled to China to walk the Great Wall of China.","zh":"遊客前往中國遊覽中國長城。"},{"en":"To walk the Great Wall of China means to visit and walk along parts of the famous historic wall in northern China.","zh":"walk the Great Wall of China 指到訪並沿中國北方著名歷史城牆部分路段步行。"},{"en":"A traveller may walk the Great Wall of China to experience both history and landscape.","zh":"旅行者可能遊覽中國長城，以體驗歷史和景觀。"},{"en":"Famous landmarks attract tourists because they turn history into something people can physically experience.","zh":"著名地標吸引遊客，因為它們把歷史變成人們能親身體驗的事物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a specific sightseeing activity.","zh":"這個短語描述一項具體觀光活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"visit wineries in","meaning":"參觀……的酒莊","examples":[{"en":"Some tourists visited wineries in Bordeaux.","zh":"有些遊客參觀波爾多的酒莊。"},{"en":"To visit wineries in a place means to go to places where wine is made, stored, or tasted in that region.","zh":"visit wineries in a place 指到訪該地區製造、儲存或品嚐葡萄酒的地方。"},{"en":"Adults may visit wineries in a countryside area to learn about grapes and local farming.","zh":"成年人可能參觀鄉郊地區的酒莊，以了解葡萄和本地農業。"},{"en":"Winery tourism connects food, agriculture, culture, and regional identity.","zh":"酒莊旅遊把食物、農業、文化和地區身份連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a specialised form of leisure travel.","zh":"這個短語描述一種專門的休閒旅行形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"go on safari","meaning":"參加野生動物觀察旅行","examples":[{"en":"Tourists could go on safari in Kenya.","zh":"遊客可以在肯尼亞參加野生動物觀察旅行。"},{"en":"To go on safari means to travel, usually in Africa, to observe wild animals in their natural environment.","zh":"go on safari 指旅行，通常在非洲，觀察自然環境中的野生動物。"},{"en":"A family may go on safari to see elephants, lions, giraffes, and birds.","zh":"家庭可能參加 safari 去看大象、獅子、長頸鹿和鳥類。"},{"en":"Safaris can support conservation when local communities benefit and animals are protected.","zh":"當本地社區受益且動物受保護，野生動物觀察旅行可以支持保育。"},{"en":"The phrase describes wildlife-viewing travel, not hunting in this context.","zh":"在這個語境中，這個短語描述野生動物觀察旅行，而不是狩獵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a peculiar variant of","meaning":"……的一種特殊變體","examples":[{"en":"A peculiar variant of the travel account arose for tourists.","zh":"一種旅行記述的特殊變體為遊客而出現。"},{"en":"A peculiar variant of something is an unusual form or version of it.","zh":"peculiar variant of something 指某物不尋常的形式或版本。"},{"en":"A comic strip can be a peculiar variant of storytelling because it uses both pictures and words.","zh":"漫畫可以是敘事的一種特殊變體，因為它同時使用圖像和文字。"},{"en":"New social needs can create new variants of older forms of writing.","zh":"新社會需要可以創造舊寫作形式的新變體。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an odd or distinctive version.","zh":"這個短語描述奇特或具特色的版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"arise to meet the needs of","meaning":"出現以滿足……的需要","examples":[{"en":"The guidebook arose to meet the needs of tourists.","zh":"旅遊指南出現，以滿足遊客的需要。"},{"en":"To arise to meet the needs of someone means to develop because those people require help or information.","zh":"arise to meet the needs of someone 指因那些人需要幫助或資訊而發展出來。"},{"en":"Online booking apps arose to meet the needs of travellers who wanted quick hotel comparisons.","zh":"網上訂房應用程式出現，以滿足想快速比較酒店的旅客需要。"},{"en":"New products often arise when everyday problems become common enough.","zh":"當日常問題變得足夠普遍，新產品往往會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase connects emergence with practical demand.","zh":"這個短語把出現與實際需求連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"guidebook","meaning":"旅遊指南","examples":[{"en":"A guidebook offers practical advice for tourists.","zh":"旅遊指南為遊客提供實用建議。"},{"en":"A guidebook is a book or digital resource that gives travellers information about places, routes, costs, food, lodging, and customs.","zh":"guidebook 指為旅行者提供關於地方、路線、費用、食物、住宿和習俗資訊的書或數碼資源。"},{"en":"A visitor may use a guidebook to decide which museum to visit first.","zh":"訪客可能使用旅遊指南決定先參觀哪間博物館。"},{"en":"Guidebooks reduce uncertainty because tourists can plan before arriving.","zh":"旅遊指南減少不確定性，因為遊客可以在到達前規劃。"},{"en":"The word refers to practical travel information, not a personal diary.","zh":"這個詞指實用旅行資訊，而不是個人日記。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"offer advice on","meaning":"就……提供建議","examples":[{"en":"Guidebooks offer advice on food, lodging, and local customs.","zh":"旅遊指南就食物、住宿和本地習俗提供建議。"},{"en":"To offer advice on something means to give suggestions or guidance about that topic.","zh":"offer advice on something 指就某主題給予建議或指導。"},{"en":"A doctor may offer advice on sleep, exercise, and diet.","zh":"醫生可能就睡眠、運動和飲食提供建議。"},{"en":"Advice helps travellers avoid mistakes, save money, and behave respectfully.","zh":"建議幫助旅客避免錯誤、節省金錢並有禮地行事。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the subject of guidance.","zh":"這個短語引入指導的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lodging","meaning":"住宿","examples":[{"en":"Guidebooks include advice on food and lodging.","zh":"旅遊指南包括關於食物和住宿的建議。"},{"en":"Lodging means a place to stay while travelling, such as a hotel, guesthouse, hostel, or rented room.","zh":"lodging 指旅行時暫住的地方，例如酒店、民宿、青年旅舍或租住房間。"},{"en":"Students on a field trip need safe lodging near the research site.","zh":"參加實地考察的學生需要靠近研究地點的安全住宿。"},{"en":"Travellers choose lodging based on cost, location, cleanliness, and comfort.","zh":"旅客根據費用、地點、清潔和舒適程度選擇住宿。"},{"en":"The word refers to temporary accommodation.","zh":"這個詞指臨時住所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"local customs","meaning":"本地習俗","examples":[{"en":"Guidebooks often explain local customs.","zh":"旅遊指南常解釋本地習俗。"},{"en":"Local customs are accepted behaviours, traditions, and social rules in a particular community or place.","zh":"local customs 指某特定社區或地方中被接受的行為、傳統和社交規則。"},{"en":"A guidebook may explain local customs about tipping, dress, greetings, or temple visits.","zh":"旅遊指南可能解釋關於小費、衣着、打招呼或參觀寺廟的本地習俗。"},{"en":"Understanding local customs helps travellers avoid causing offence by accident.","zh":"理解本地習俗幫助旅客避免無意中冒犯他人。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to everyday cultural rules and traditions.","zh":"這個短語指日常文化規則和傳統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"should not miss seeing","meaning":"不應錯過參觀","examples":[{"en":"Guidebooks list the sights that visitors should not miss seeing.","zh":"旅遊指南列出訪客不應錯過參觀的景點。"},{"en":"Should not miss seeing something means it is worth visiting or looking at because it is important, beautiful, or special.","zh":"should not miss seeing something 指某物因重要、美麗或特別而值得到訪或觀看。"},{"en":"Visitors to the city should not miss seeing the old harbour at sunset.","zh":"到訪該城市的人不應錯過在日落時參觀舊港口。"},{"en":"Guidebooks use this phrase to help tourists choose when time is limited.","zh":"當時間有限，旅遊指南使用這個短語幫助遊客選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights recommended attractions.","zh":"這個短語突出推薦景點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"massive economic impact","meaning":"巨大的經濟影響","examples":[{"en":"Tourism has had a massive economic impact throughout the world.","zh":"旅遊在全世界產生了巨大的經濟影響。"},{"en":"A massive economic impact is a very large effect on jobs, income, businesses, prices, or public finances.","zh":"massive economic impact 指對職位、收入、企業、價格或公共財政造成非常大的影響。"},{"en":"A new airport can have a massive economic impact on nearby hotels, restaurants, and taxi drivers.","zh":"新機場可以對附近酒店、餐廳和的士司機產生巨大經濟影響。"},{"en":"Tourism creates economic impact because travellers spend money on transport, lodging, food, shopping, and entertainment.","zh":"旅遊產生經濟影響，因為旅客在交通、住宿、食物、購物和娛樂上花錢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large financial effect on society.","zh":"這個短語描述對社會的大型財務影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"considerable influence","meaning":"相當大的影響","examples":[{"en":"Other new forms of travel have also had considerable influence.","zh":"其他新型旅行也產生了相當大的影響。"},{"en":"Considerable influence means a strong or noticeable effect on people, behaviour, society, or events.","zh":"considerable influence 指對人、行為、社會或事件有強烈或明顯影響。"},{"en":"A popular teacher can have considerable influence on students’ confidence and subject choices.","zh":"受歡迎的老師可以對學生信心和選科有相當大的影響。"},{"en":"Travel has influence because it changes what people see, buy, believe, and write about.","zh":"旅行有影響，因為它改變人們看見、購買、相信和書寫的內容。"},{"en":"The phrase means more than a small effect but not necessarily total control.","zh":"這個短語意思是不小的影響，但不一定是完全控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contemporary times","meaning":"當代","examples":[{"en":"New forms of travel have influenced society in contemporary times.","zh":"新型旅行在當代影響了社會。"},{"en":"Contemporary times means the present period or recent modern era.","zh":"contemporary times 指現時時期或近期現代。"},{"en":"In contemporary times, many people use smartphones to plan transport and holidays.","zh":"在當代，許多人使用智能手機規劃交通和假期。"},{"en":"Travel changes in contemporary times because technology, income, and global connections have changed.","zh":"當代旅行有所改變，因為科技、收入和全球連結已經改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the world of today or the near present.","zh":"這個短語指今日或接近現在的世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each multiple-choice question.","zh":"學生為每條選擇題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the option label that matches the right answer.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇與正確答案相配的選項字母。"},{"en":"If answer C matches the passage, students should write C clearly in the box.","zh":"如果 C 答案符合文章，學生應在方格內清楚寫 C。"},{"en":"Careless copying can make a correct answer wrong even when the student understands the passage.","zh":"即使學生理解文章，粗心抄寫也可以令正確答案變錯。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"write your answers in boxes","meaning":"把答案填寫在方格內","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write their answers in boxes on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生把答案填寫在答題紙上的方格內。"},{"en":"To write your answers in boxes means to place each answer inside the marked spaces provided.","zh":"write your answers in boxes 指把每個答案填在指定標示空格內。"},{"en":"In a public exam, students must write answers in boxes so markers can find them easily.","zh":"在公開考試中，學生必須把答案填寫在方格內，方便評卷員尋找。"},{"en":"Following layout instructions prevents lost marks caused by unclear answer placement.","zh":"跟從版面指示可以避免因答案位置不清而失分。"},{"en":"The phrase is an instruction about answer format.","zh":"這個短語是關於答案格式的指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in the early days","meaning":"在早期","examples":[{"en":"The question asks why most people travelled in the early days.","zh":"題目問大多數人在早期為何旅行。"},{"en":"In the early days means during the beginning period of a development, practice, or history.","zh":"in the early days 指某發展、做法或歷史的開始時期。"},{"en":"In the early days of mobile phones, many people used them only for calls and text messages.","zh":"在手機早期，許多人只用它來打電話和發短訊。"},{"en":"Early patterns often differ from later ones because technology, money, and social needs change.","zh":"早期模式通常與後來不同，因為科技、金錢和社會需要會改變。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the first stage of a historical process.","zh":"這個短語指歷史過程的第一階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"record one’s own experiences","meaning":"記錄自己的經歷","examples":[{"en":"Travellers often record their own experiences in travel writing.","zh":"旅行者常在旅行寫作中記錄自己的經歷。"},{"en":"To record one’s own experiences means to write down, film, or otherwise preserve what one personally went through.","zh":"record one’s own experiences 指寫下、拍攝或以其他方式保存自己親身經歷的事情。"},{"en":"A student may record her own experiences during an internship in a daily journal.","zh":"學生可能在日記中記錄自己的實習經歷。"},{"en":"Recording experiences helps people remember details and share lessons with others.","zh":"記錄經歷幫助人記住細節並與他人分享教訓。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on personal first-hand experience.","zh":"這個短語重點是個人的第一手經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reflect upon","meaning":"反思……","examples":[{"en":"Travel writing may lead travellers to reflect upon their own society and life.","zh":"旅行寫作可能引導旅行者反思自己的社會和生活。"},{"en":"To reflect upon something means to think carefully and deeply about it.","zh":"reflect upon something 指仔細而深入地思考某事。"},{"en":"After receiving exam results, a student may reflect upon her study habits.","zh":"收到考試成績後，學生可能反思自己的學習習慣。"},{"en":"Travel encourages reflection because unfamiliar places make normal habits seem visible.","zh":"旅行鼓勵反思，因為陌生地方會令平常習慣變得可見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes thoughtful self-examination.","zh":"這個短語描述有思想深度的自我檢視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be related to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Travel writing is related to the development of human society.","zh":"旅行寫作與人類社會發展有關。"},{"en":"To be related to something means to have a connection with it.","zh":"be related to something 指與某事有聯繫。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is related to weak concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足與課堂專注力弱有關。"},{"en":"Travel writing is related to social development because it spreads knowledge about other peoples and places.","zh":"旅行寫作與社會發展有關，因為它傳播關於其他民族和地方的知識。"},{"en":"The phrase shows connection, not necessarily direct cause.","zh":"這個短語顯示聯繫，不一定是直接原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the table below","meaning":"完成下表","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the table below with words from the passage.","zh":"考生用文章中的字詞完成下表。"},{"en":"Complete the table below means fill the empty spaces in the table that follows.","zh":"complete the table below 指填寫下方表格中的空格。"},{"en":"Students should complete the table below by checking headings, grammar, and exact wording.","zh":"學生應透過檢查標題、文法和準確字詞來完成下表。"},{"en":"Table completion tests whether students can locate details and fit them into a structure.","zh":"表格填充測試學生能否定位細節並把它們放入結構中。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案應包含不多於兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must use one or two words only.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案只能使用一個或兩個英文詞。"},{"en":"If the correct answer is “mass tourism”, it follows the rule because it has two words.","zh":"如果正確答案是 “mass tourism”，它符合規則，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Exceeding the word limit can make an answer wrong even when the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，超出字數限制也可以令答案錯。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語設定嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"destination","meaning":"目的地","examples":[{"en":"The destination tells us where the traveller went.","zh":"目的地告訴我們旅行者去了哪裏。"},{"en":"A destination is the place someone is travelling to.","zh":"destination 指某人前往的地方。"},{"en":"A family’s holiday destination may be a beach town, a mountain village, or a historic city.","zh":"家庭假期目的地可能是海邊小鎮、山村或歷史城市。"},{"en":"Knowing the destination helps readers understand the route, purpose, and difficulty of a journey.","zh":"知道目的地幫助讀者理解旅程路線、目的和難度。"},{"en":"The word refers to the end point or target place of travel.","zh":"這個詞指旅行的終點或目標地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"purpose of travel","meaning":"旅行目的","examples":[{"en":"The table asks for the purpose of travel.","zh":"表格要求填寫旅行目的。"},{"en":"Purpose of travel means the reason why someone makes a journey.","zh":"purpose of travel 指某人進行旅程的原因。"},{"en":"A person’s purpose of travel may be study, work, worship, trade, family, or leisure.","zh":"一個人的旅行目的可能是學習、工作、敬拜、貿易、探親或休閒。"},{"en":"Understanding purpose helps explain why travellers choose certain routes, places, and records.","zh":"理解目的有助解釋旅行者為何選擇某些路線、地方和記錄。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on motive.","zh":"這個短語重點是動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"gather information for","meaning":"為……收集資料","examples":[{"en":"Herodotus gathered information for the study of history.","zh":"Herodotus 為歷史研究收集資料。"},{"en":"To gather information for something means to collect facts, observations, or evidence to support that work.","zh":"gather information for something 指收集事實、觀察或證據以支持某項工作。"},{"en":"A student may gather information for a school project by interviewing neighbours.","zh":"學生可能透過訪問鄰居，為學校項目收集資料。"},{"en":"Good research depends on gathering information before forming conclusions.","zh":"好研究取決於先收集資料，再形成結論。"},{"en":"The phrase connects information collection with a purpose.","zh":"這個短語把資料收集與目的連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"seek allies","meaning":"尋求盟友","examples":[{"en":"Zhang Qian travelled west to seek allies.","zh":"張騫向西旅行以尋求盟友。"},{"en":"To seek allies means to look for people, groups, or states that will support one’s aims.","zh":"seek allies 指尋找會支持自己目標的人、團體或國家。"},{"en":"A student council may seek allies among teachers before proposing a new school rule.","zh":"學生會提出新校規前，可能在老師之中尋求盟友。"},{"en":"Groups seek allies when they cannot achieve a goal alone.","zh":"當群體無法單獨達成目標，就會尋求盟友。"},{"en":"The phrase describes searching for support.","zh":"這個短語描述尋找支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"acquire knowledge","meaning":"獲取知識","examples":[{"en":"Roman geographers travelled to acquire knowledge about the Mediterranean.","zh":"羅馬地理學家旅行，以獲取關於地中海的知識。"},{"en":"To acquire knowledge means to gain information, understanding, or skill through study or experience.","zh":"acquire knowledge 指透過學習或經驗獲得資訊、理解或技能。"},{"en":"Students acquire knowledge by reading, practising, asking questions, and making mistakes.","zh":"學生透過閱讀、練習、提問和犯錯獲取知識。"},{"en":"Travel helps people acquire knowledge because they can observe places directly.","zh":"旅行幫助人們獲取知識，因為他們可以直接觀察地方。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gaining knowledge over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間取得知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"for trading and pilgrimage","meaning":"為了貿易和朝聖","examples":[{"en":"Many Muslims travelled for trading and pilgrimage.","zh":"許多穆斯林為了貿易和朝聖而旅行。"},{"en":"For trading and pilgrimage means for the purposes of commerce and religious travel.","zh":"for trading and pilgrimage 指為商業和宗教旅行目的。"},{"en":"A port city may attract visitors for trading and pilgrimage if it has both markets and holy sites.","zh":"如果港口城市同時有市場和聖地，它可能吸引人為了貿易和朝聖而來。"},{"en":"These two motives often created long-distance travel networks.","zh":"這兩種動機常創造長途旅行網絡。"},{"en":"The phrase combines economic and spiritual purposes.","zh":"這個短語結合經濟和精神目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"collect Buddhist texts","meaning":"收集佛教經文","examples":[{"en":"Chinese Buddhists travelled to India to collect Buddhist texts.","zh":"中國佛教徒前往印度收集佛教經文。"},{"en":"To collect Buddhist texts means to obtain Buddhist writings for study, translation, copying, or religious use.","zh":"collect Buddhist texts 指取得佛教文字，用於研究、翻譯、抄寫或宗教用途。"},{"en":"A monastery may collect Buddhist texts to preserve teachings for future students.","zh":"寺院可能收集佛教經文，以為未來學生保存教義。"},{"en":"Text collection mattered because written teachings could travel farther than one teacher’s voice.","zh":"收集經文很重要，因為文字教義能比一位老師的聲音傳得更遠。"},{"en":"The phrase links travel with religious knowledge.","zh":"這個短語把旅行與宗教知識連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"satisfy public curiosity about","meaning":"滿足公眾對……的好奇心","examples":[{"en":"Travel books helped satisfy public curiosity about the New World.","zh":"旅遊書幫助滿足公眾對新大陸的好奇心。"},{"en":"To satisfy public curiosity about something means to answer many people’s desire to know more about it.","zh":"satisfy public curiosity about something 指回應許多人想了解更多的願望。"},{"en":"A news report may satisfy public curiosity about how a new train line will work.","zh":"新聞報道可能滿足公眾對新鐵路線如何運作的好奇心。"},{"en":"Publishers produce popular books when public curiosity creates demand for information.","zh":"當公眾好奇心創造資訊需求，出版商便會生產受歡迎書籍。"},{"en":"The phrase connects widespread interest with information supply.","zh":"這個短語把廣泛興趣與資訊供應連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the New World","meaning":"新大陸","examples":[{"en":"European explorers wrote about the New World.","zh":"歐洲探險家撰寫關於新大陸的作品。"},{"en":"The New World is a historical term used by Europeans to refer to the Americas after they became known to Europe.","zh":"New World 是歐洲人得知美洲後，用來稱呼美洲的歷史用語。"},{"en":"Travel accounts about the New World described lands, peoples, plants, animals, and resources unfamiliar to European readers.","zh":"關於新大陸的旅行記述描述歐洲讀者不熟悉的土地、人民、植物、動物和資源。"},{"en":"The term reflects a European viewpoint, because the Americas were not new to the peoples already living there.","zh":"這個詞反映歐洲視角，因為對已居住在那裏的人而言，美洲並不是新的。"},{"en":"The phrase is historically important but should be understood critically.","zh":"這個短語具有歷史重要性，但應批判地理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"provide information for","meaning":"為……提供資料","examples":[{"en":"Colonial administrators wrote to provide information for the colonies they set up.","zh":"殖民地行政官員寫作，是為他們建立的殖民地提供資料。"},{"en":"To provide information for someone or something means to give useful details that support their work or understanding.","zh":"provide information for someone or something 指提供有用細節，以支持其工作或理解。"},{"en":"A school report may provide information for parents about students’ progress and behaviour.","zh":"學校報告可能為家長提供關於學生進度和行為的資料。"},{"en":"Governments collect information because policies are harder to make without accurate details.","zh":"政府收集資訊，因為沒有準確細節就較難制定政策。"},{"en":"The phrase describes supplying knowledge for a practical purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述為實際目的提供知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"set up","meaning":"建立；設立","examples":[{"en":"European powers set up colonies in Asia and Africa.","zh":"歐洲列強在亞洲和非洲建立殖民地。"},{"en":"To set up something means to establish, create, or organise it.","zh":"set up something 指建立、創立或組織某事物。"},{"en":"Students may set up a reading club after noticing many classmates enjoy novels.","zh":"學生發現許多同學喜歡小說後，可能設立閱讀學會。"},{"en":"Organisations set up new offices or systems when they want to expand control or service.","zh":"組織想擴大控制或服務時，會建立新辦公室或系統。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating something that did not exist before.","zh":"這個短語描述創造之前不存在的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"by the mid-nineteenth century","meaning":"到十九世紀中葉","examples":[{"en":"By the mid-nineteenth century, Asian travellers were visiting Europe and the United States.","zh":"到十九世紀中葉，亞洲旅行者正在到訪歐洲和美國。"},{"en":"By the mid-nineteenth century means by around the middle of the 1800s.","zh":"by the mid-nineteenth century 指到十九世紀中期左右。"},{"en":"By the mid-nineteenth century, steamships and railways were changing how people travelled.","zh":"到十九世紀中葉，蒸汽船和鐵路正在改變人們旅行的方式。"},{"en":"This time phrase helps place Asian travel to the West within a specific historical period.","zh":"這個時間短語幫助把亞洲人前往西方的旅行放在特定歷史時期中。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a development that had appeared by that time.","zh":"這個短語標示某發展到那時已經出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"study the organisation of","meaning":"研究……的組織方式","examples":[{"en":"Asian travellers studied the organisation of European societies.","zh":"亞洲旅行者研究歐洲社會的組織方式。"},{"en":"To study the organisation of a society means to examine how its government, economy, education, military, and institutions are arranged.","zh":"study the organisation of a society 指考察其政府、經濟、教育、軍事和制度如何安排。"},{"en":"A policymaker may study the organisation of another country’s healthcare system before reforming hospitals at home.","zh":"政策制定者在改革本國醫院前，可能研究另一國醫療制度的組織方式。"},{"en":"Studying organisation helps reformers see which systems might be adapted to their own society.","zh":"研究組織方式幫助改革者看出哪些制度可以被改造並用於本國社會。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on social structure and institutional design.","zh":"這個短語重點是社會結構和制度設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"entertainment and pleasure","meaning":"娛樂和消遣","examples":[{"en":"Mass tourism often involves travel for entertainment and pleasure.","zh":"大眾旅遊通常涉及為娛樂和消遣而旅行。"},{"en":"Entertainment and pleasure mean enjoyment, relaxation, amusement, and fun rather than duty or work.","zh":"entertainment and pleasure 指享受、放鬆、娛樂和樂趣，而不是責任或工作。"},{"en":"Families may travel for entertainment and pleasure during summer holidays.","zh":"家庭可能在暑假為娛樂和消遣而旅行。"},{"en":"As incomes rise, more people can spend money on experiences that are not necessary for survival.","zh":"隨着收入上升，更多人可以花錢在非生存必需的體驗上。"},{"en":"The phrase describes leisure motives for travel.","zh":"這個短語描述旅行的休閒動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a popular pastime","meaning":"受歡迎的消遣","examples":[{"en":"Reading travel stories became a popular pastime for many people.","zh":"閱讀旅行故事成為許多人的受歡迎消遣。"},{"en":"A popular pastime is an activity many people enjoy doing in their free time.","zh":"popular pastime 指許多人在空閒時間喜歡做的活動。"},{"en":"Watching dramas on streaming platforms is a popular pastime for many families.","zh":"在串流平台觀看劇集是許多家庭受歡迎的消遣。"},{"en":"Travel stories became popular because they let readers imagine distant places without leaving home.","zh":"旅行故事變得受歡迎，因為它們讓讀者不用離家也能想像遙遠地方。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common leisure activity.","zh":"這個短語描述常見休閒活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"truthful rather than fictional","meaning":"真實而非虛構的","examples":[{"en":"Some readers regarded travel accounts as truthful rather than fictional.","zh":"有些讀者把旅行記述視為真實而非虛構的。"},{"en":"Truthful rather than fictional means based on real events or observations, not invented stories.","zh":"truthful rather than fictional 指基於真實事件或觀察，而不是編造故事。"},{"en":"A diary is usually read as truthful rather than fictional, although it may still be selective.","zh":"日記通常被視為真實而非虛構的，雖然它仍可能有選擇性。"},{"en":"Readers trusted travel accounts because they seemed to report actual journeys and places.","zh":"讀者信任旅行記述，因為它們看似報道實際旅程和地方。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts fact-based writing with imagined writing.","zh":"這個短語把基於事實的寫作與想像寫作作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"play an important role in","meaning":"在……中扮演重要角色","examples":[{"en":"Travel books played an important role in literature.","zh":"旅遊書在文學中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"To play an important role in something means to be a significant part of how it develops or works.","zh":"play an important role in something 指在某事的發展或運作中佔有重要位置。"},{"en":"Parents play an important role in children’s reading habits.","zh":"家長在孩子閱讀習慣中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"Travel books influenced literature by mixing observation, storytelling, geography, and cultural comparison.","zh":"旅遊書透過結合觀察、敘事、地理和文化比較來影響文學。"},{"en":"The phrase describes meaningful contribution.","zh":"這個短語描述有意義的貢獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"knowledge of their empire","meaning":"對自己帝國的認識","examples":[{"en":"Imperial rulers desired knowledge of their empire.","zh":"帝國統治者渴望對自己帝國的認識。"},{"en":"Knowledge of their empire means information about the lands, peoples, resources, roads, and conditions under imperial rule.","zh":"knowledge of their empire 指關於帝國統治下的土地、人民、資源、道路和情況的資訊。"},{"en":"A ruler who lacks knowledge of his empire may not know where taxes, soldiers, or roads are needed.","zh":"缺乏對自己帝國認識的統治者，可能不知道哪裏需要稅收、士兵或道路。"},{"en":"Empires need knowledge because distant territories are difficult to govern blindly.","zh":"帝國需要知識，因為遙遠領土難以盲目治理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical political and geographical understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述實用的政治和地理理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the largest number of records","meaning":"最多記錄","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which group produced the largest number of records.","zh":"題目問哪個群體產生最多記錄。"},{"en":"The largest number of records means the greatest quantity of written accounts or documents.","zh":"largest number of records 指最大數量的文字記述或文件。"},{"en":"A school may ask which class produced the largest number of reading logs in one term.","zh":"學校可能詢問哪一班在一個學期內產生最多閱讀記錄。"},{"en":"Comparing record numbers helps identify which group left the most evidence for historians.","zh":"比較記錄數量有助識別哪個群體為歷史學家留下最多證據。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on quantity of surviving documents.","zh":"這個短語重點是保存文件的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"spiritual journeys","meaning":"精神旅程；朝聖旅程","examples":[{"en":"Pilgrims produced many records of spiritual journeys.","zh":"朝聖者產生了許多精神旅程的記錄。"},{"en":"Spiritual journeys are travels undertaken for religious growth, devotion, reflection, or sacred duty.","zh":"spiritual journeys 指為宗教成長、虔敬、反思或神聖責任而進行的旅行。"},{"en":"A person may describe meditation retreat as a spiritual journey even if it is not physically far away.","zh":"一個人可能把冥想靜修描述為精神旅程，即使身體距離並不遠。"},{"en":"Pilgrimage accounts record spiritual journeys because the inner meaning matters as much as the route.","zh":"朝聖記述記錄精神旅程，因為內在意義與路線同樣重要。"},{"en":"The phrase can refer to both physical travel and inner transformation.","zh":"這個短語可以指身體旅行，也可以指內在轉化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"meet the public’s interest","meaning":"迎合公眾興趣","examples":[{"en":"Travel books were published to meet the public’s interest.","zh":"旅遊書被出版以迎合公眾興趣。"},{"en":"To meet the public’s interest means to satisfy what many people want to know, read, or experience.","zh":"meet the public’s interest 指滿足許多人想知道、閱讀或體驗的事情。"},{"en":"A museum may extend an exhibition to meet the public’s interest in local history.","zh":"博物館可能延長展覽，以迎合公眾對本地歷史的興趣。"},{"en":"Publishers respond to public interest because demand can create a market for books.","zh":"出版商回應公眾興趣，因為需求可以創造書籍市場。"},{"en":"The phrase connects audience demand with supply.","zh":"這個短語把受眾需求與供應連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"explore new business opportunities","meaning":"探索新的商機","examples":[{"en":"Some travellers explored new business opportunities overseas.","zh":"有些旅行者在海外探索新的商機。"},{"en":"To explore new business opportunities means to investigate possible ways to earn money, trade, invest, or expand.","zh":"explore new business opportunities 指研究可能賺錢、貿易、投資或擴展的方法。"},{"en":"A restaurant owner may explore new business opportunities by testing online delivery.","zh":"餐廳老闆可能透過測試網上外賣來探索新的商機。"},{"en":"Travel helps businesspeople discover markets, partners, resources, and customer needs.","zh":"旅行幫助商人發現市場、合作伙伴、資源和顧客需要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes looking for commercial possibilities.","zh":"這個短語描述尋找商業可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the main theme of","meaning":"……的主題","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the main theme of the passage.","zh":"題目問文章的主題。"},{"en":"The main theme of a text is its central idea or overall message.","zh":"main theme of a text 指文本的中心思想或整體訊息。"},{"en":"The main theme of a story may be friendship, courage, inequality, or change.","zh":"故事的主題可能是友誼、勇氣、不平等或改變。"},{"en":"Finding the main theme helps students avoid focusing only on small details.","zh":"找出主題幫助學生避免只集中於小細節。"},{"en":"The phrase asks what the whole text is mainly about.","zh":"這個短語詢問整篇文本主要關於甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the production of travel books","meaning":"旅遊書的出版","examples":[{"en":"The production of travel books increased after printing became widespread.","zh":"印刷變得普及後，旅遊書的出版增加。"},{"en":"The production of travel books means the writing, printing, and publication of books about travel.","zh":"production of travel books 指關於旅行書籍的寫作、印刷和出版。"},{"en":"A publisher may increase the production of travel books when many people start planning holidays.","zh":"當許多人開始計劃假期，出版商可能增加旅遊書的出版。"},{"en":"Printing technology made production faster, cheaper, and able to reach more readers.","zh":"印刷技術令生產更快、更便宜，並能接觸更多讀者。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on making and publishing travel-related books.","zh":"這個短語重點是製作和出版旅行相關書籍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"literary status","meaning":"文學地位","examples":[{"en":"The passage mentions the literary status of travel accounts.","zh":"文章提到旅行記述的文學地位。"},{"en":"Literary status means the recognised position or importance of a type of writing within literature.","zh":"literary status 指某種寫作在文學中被認可的位置或重要性。"},{"en":"A poem may gain literary status when critics, teachers, and readers continue to value it.","zh":"當評論家、老師和讀者持續重視一首詩，它可能獲得文學地位。"},{"en":"Travel accounts gained literary status when they became widely read and treated as a serious genre.","zh":"當旅行記述被廣泛閱讀並被視為嚴肅體裁，它便獲得文學地位。"},{"en":"The phrase concerns cultural and literary importance.","zh":"這個短語關乎文化和文學重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"historical significance","meaning":"歷史意義","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains the historical significance of travel books.","zh":"文章解釋旅遊書的歷史意義。"},{"en":"Historical significance means the importance of something for understanding the past or its effects on later events.","zh":"historical significance 指某事對理解過去或其對後來事件影響的重要性。"},{"en":"A small diary may have historical significance if it records ordinary life during a war.","zh":"如果一本小日記記錄戰爭期間的普通生活，它可能具有歷史意義。"},{"en":"Travel books are historically significant because they preserve contact between societies and changing views of the world.","zh":"旅遊書具有歷史意義，因為它們保存社會之間的接觸和世界觀的變化。"},{"en":"The phrase asks why something matters in history.","zh":"這個短語詢問某事在歷史中為何重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the development of travel books","meaning":"旅遊書的發展","examples":[{"en":"The development of travel books is traced across different periods.","zh":"旅遊書的發展被追溯到不同時期。"},{"en":"The development of travel books means how travel writing changed, grew, and took new forms over time.","zh":"development of travel books 指旅行寫作如何隨時間改變、增長並形成新形式。"},{"en":"A teacher may trace the development of travel books from handwritten accounts to printed guidebooks and online blogs.","zh":"老師可能追溯旅遊書從手寫記述到印刷指南和網誌的發展。"},{"en":"Studying development shows how changing technology, transport, and readers shaped travel writing.","zh":"研究發展顯示科技、交通和讀者的變化如何塑造旅行寫作。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on historical change in a writing form.","zh":"這個短語重點是某種寫作形式的歷史變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 33 - Travel Books.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 34":[{"front":"mechanisms of linguistic change","meaning":"語言變化的機制","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains several mechanisms of linguistic change.","zh":"文章解釋了幾種語言變化的機制。"},{"en":"Mechanisms of linguistic change are the processes that explain how languages alter over time.","zh":"語言變化的機制是解釋語言如何隨時間改變的過程。"},{"en":"Borrowing foreign words is one mechanism of linguistic change because it adds new vocabulary to a language.","zh":"借用外來詞是一種語言變化的機制，因為它為語言加入新詞彙。"},{"en":"If many speakers simplify a difficult sound, that mechanism may gradually change pronunciation.","zh":"如果許多說話者簡化一個困難音，這種機制可能逐漸改變發音。"},{"en":"The phrase helps us study language change as a process, not as random mistakes.","zh":"這個短語幫助我們把語言變化視為過程，而不是隨機錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cause disagreement","meaning":"引起分歧","examples":[{"en":"Changes in pronunciation have caused the most disagreement among scholars.","zh":"發音變化在學者之間引起最多分歧。"},{"en":"To cause disagreement means to make people hold different opinions about an issue.","zh":"「cause disagreement」意思是令人在某議題上持有不同意見。"},{"en":"A new school rule may cause disagreement if students think it is unfair but teachers think it is necessary.","zh":"如果學生認為新校規不公平，而老師認為有必要，新校規可能引起分歧。"},{"en":"If evidence can be interpreted in several ways, it often causes disagreement among experts.","zh":"如果證據可以有多種解讀，它常會在專家之間引起分歧。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the result of a topic being debatable or uncertain.","zh":"這個短語描述某話題具爭議或不確定所造成的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sources of evidence for","meaning":"關於……的證據來源","examples":[{"en":"We have various sources of evidence for the pronunciations of earlier times.","zh":"我們有各種關於早期發音的證據來源。"},{"en":"Sources of evidence for something are materials or clues that help prove or explain it.","zh":"關於某事的證據來源，是幫助證明或解釋它的材料或線索。"},{"en":"Old letters, recordings, and newspapers can be sources of evidence for how people lived.","zh":"舊信件、錄音和報紙可以是關於人們如何生活的證據來源。"},{"en":"If one source is unclear, researchers look for other sources of evidence to support the conclusion.","zh":"如果一項來源不清楚，研究人員會尋找其他證據來源來支持結論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where proof or clues come from.","zh":"這個短語描述證據或線索從哪裡來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pronunciations of earlier times","meaning":"早期的發音","examples":[{"en":"Spellings can help us understand the pronunciations of earlier times.","zh":"拼寫可以幫助我們理解早期的發音。"},{"en":"Pronunciations of earlier times are the ways words were spoken in the past.","zh":"「pronunciations of earlier times」是過去人們說出詞語的方式。"},{"en":"Old poems can give clues about pronunciations of earlier times because rhyming words may reveal old sounds.","zh":"舊詩可以提供早期發音的線索，因為押韻詞可能顯示舊音。"},{"en":"If spelling no longer matches speech, it may preserve evidence of an older pronunciation.","zh":"如果拼寫不再符合現代說話方式，它可能保存較舊發音的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to historical speech sounds, not modern accents.","zh":"這個短語指歷史語音，而不是現代口音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the treatment of borrowed words","meaning":"對外來詞的處理","examples":[{"en":"The treatment of borrowed words can provide clues about historical pronunciation.","zh":"對外來詞的處理可以提供關於歷史發音的線索。"},{"en":"The treatment of borrowed words means how a language adopts, spells, and pronounces words taken from another language.","zh":"「the treatment of borrowed words」意思是一種語言如何接收、拼寫和讀出從另一語言借入的詞。"},{"en":"English may change a French word’s sound so it fits English pronunciation habits.","zh":"英語可能改變法語詞的音，使它符合英語發音習慣。"},{"en":"If a borrowed word is spelled in an unusual way, it may reveal how people heard it at the time.","zh":"如果外來詞拼寫方式不尋常，它可能顯示當時人們如何聽到該詞。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on what happens to foreign words after they enter a language.","zh":"這個短語集中於外來詞進入一種語言後發生甚麼事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"words borrowed from other languages","meaning":"從其他語言借入的詞","examples":[{"en":"Words borrowed from other languages may preserve older sound patterns.","zh":"從其他語言借入的詞可能保存較舊的語音模式。"},{"en":"Words borrowed from other languages are words taken from another language and used in a new one.","zh":"「words borrowed from other languages」是從另一語言取來並在新語言中使用的詞。"},{"en":"English borrowed words such as café, piano, and kindergarten from other languages.","zh":"英語從其他語言借入 café、piano 和 kindergarten 等詞。"},{"en":"When borrowed words enter a language, their sounds may change to fit local pronunciation.","zh":"當外來詞進入一種語言，其發音可能會改變以配合本地發音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes vocabulary that crosses language boundaries.","zh":"這個短語描述跨越語言界線的詞彙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be borrowed by other languages","meaning":"被其他語言借用","examples":[{"en":"Some English words were borrowed by other languages.","zh":"有些英語詞被其他語言借用。"},{"en":"To be borrowed by other languages means to be taken into another language and used by its speakers.","zh":"「be borrowed by other languages」意思是被另一種語言接收並由其說話者使用。"},{"en":"The word “computer” has been borrowed by many languages because the technology spread worldwide.","zh":"“computer” 這個詞被許多語言借用，因為該科技傳遍全球。"},{"en":"If a word is borrowed by other languages, its pronunciation may change in each language.","zh":"如果一個詞被其他語言借用，它在每種語言中的發音可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes vocabulary moving outward from one language to others.","zh":"這個短語描述詞彙由一種語言向其他語言傳播。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"contemporary grammarians","meaning":"同時代的語法學家","examples":[{"en":"Contemporary grammarians described how people spoke in their own period.","zh":"同時代的語法學家描述了他們所處時期人們如何說話。"},{"en":"Contemporary grammarians are grammar experts who lived at the same time as the language stage being studied.","zh":"「contemporary grammarians」是與所研究語言階段同時代的語法專家。"},{"en":"A contemporary grammarian in the seventeenth century might record how educated speakers pronounced English.","zh":"十七世紀的同時代語法學家可能記錄受教育人士如何讀英語。"},{"en":"If such writers describe speech directly, their notes become valuable historical evidence.","zh":"如果這些作者直接描述說話方式，他們的筆記就成為珍貴歷史證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to grammar writers from the same historical period.","zh":"這個短語指來自同一歷史時期的語法作者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"spelling-reformers","meaning":"拼寫改革者","examples":[{"en":"Spelling-reformers tried to improve the writing system of English.","zh":"拼寫改革者試圖改善英語書寫系統。"},{"en":"Spelling-reformers are people who want spelling to match pronunciation more clearly or logically.","zh":"「spelling-reformers」是希望拼寫更清楚或更合邏輯地符合發音的人。"},{"en":"A spelling-reformer might argue that silent letters make reading harder for children.","zh":"拼寫改革者可能主張不發音字母令兒童閱讀更困難。"},{"en":"If reformers record how words should be spelled, they may reveal how words were pronounced.","zh":"如果改革者記錄詞語應如何拼寫，他們可能揭示詞語當時如何發音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes people who try to change spelling rules.","zh":"這個短語描述試圖改變拼寫規則的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"modern pronunciations","meaning":"現代發音","examples":[{"en":"Modern pronunciations in related languages can give useful evidence.","zh":"相關語言中的現代發音可以提供有用證據。"},{"en":"Modern pronunciations are the ways words are spoken by present-day speakers.","zh":"「modern pronunciations」是現代說話者讀出詞語的方式。"},{"en":"Comparing modern pronunciations in English and related dialects can reveal older sound patterns.","zh":"比較英語和相關方言中的現代發音，可以揭示較舊的語音模式。"},{"en":"If a sound survives in one modern dialect, it may help reconstruct an older form.","zh":"如果某個音保留在一種現代方言中，它可能幫助重建較舊形式。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to present-day speech sounds.","zh":"這個短語指現今的說話聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"languages and dialects concerned","meaning":"相關的語言和方言","examples":[{"en":"Researchers compare the languages and dialects concerned.","zh":"研究人員比較相關的語言和方言。"},{"en":"The languages and dialects concerned are the particular languages and regional varieties relevant to the study.","zh":"「languages and dialects concerned」是與研究相關的特定語言和地區變體。"},{"en":"A researcher studying English history may compare Scots, Irish English, and older English dialects concerned.","zh":"研究英語歷史的人可能比較蘇格蘭語、愛爾蘭英語和相關古英語方言。"},{"en":"If the wrong dialect is compared, the evidence may become misleading.","zh":"如果比較了錯誤方言，證據可能變得誤導。"},{"en":"The phrase means the specific language varieties involved.","zh":"這個短語指涉及的特定語言變體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"from the middle of the sixteenth century onward","meaning":"從十六世紀中葉起","examples":[{"en":"From the middle of the sixteenth century onward, writers began to describe English pronunciation more carefully.","zh":"從十六世紀中葉起，作者開始更仔細地描述英語發音。"},{"en":"From the middle of the sixteenth century onward means starting around the mid-1500s and continuing after that.","zh":"「from the middle of the sixteenth century onward」意思是從十六世紀中期左右開始並持續往後。"},{"en":"From the middle of the school year onward, the class kept weekly reading records.","zh":"從學年中段起，班上開始每週記錄閱讀情況。"},{"en":"If evidence becomes richer from a certain point onward, historians can study that later period more confidently.","zh":"如果證據從某時點起變得更豐富，歷史學家就能更有信心研究之後時期。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a starting point and continues forward in time.","zh":"這個短語提供起點，並表示時間向後延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"describe the position of","meaning":"描述……的位置","examples":[{"en":"Writers attempted to describe the position of the speech-organs.","zh":"作者試圖描述發音器官的位置。"},{"en":"To describe the position of something means to explain where it is placed or how it is arranged.","zh":"「describe the position of」某物，意思是解釋它放在哪裡或如何排列。"},{"en":"A science teacher may describe the position of the tongue when teaching pronunciation.","zh":"科學老師教發音時，可能描述舌頭的位置。"},{"en":"If we know the position of the lips and tongue, we can understand how a sound is made.","zh":"如果我們知道嘴唇和舌頭的位置，就能理解某個音如何產生。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when explaining physical arrangement.","zh":"這個短語適用於解釋身體或物件排列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"speech-organs","meaning":"發音器官","examples":[{"en":"Speech-organs are used in the production of speech sounds.","zh":"發音器官用於產生語音。"},{"en":"Speech-organs are body parts such as the tongue, lips, teeth, palate, and vocal cords used for speaking.","zh":"「speech-organs」是用於說話的身體部位，例如舌頭、嘴唇、牙齒、顎和聲帶。"},{"en":"When students pronounce /p/, their two lips are important speech-organs.","zh":"當學生發 /p/ 音時，雙唇是重要發音器官。"},{"en":"If speech-organs move differently, the sound produced may also change.","zh":"如果發音器官移動方式不同，產生的音也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the physical parts involved in speech.","zh":"這個短語指參與說話的身體部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the production of English phonemes","meaning":"英語音位的產生","examples":[{"en":"Writers described the position of the speech-organs for the production of English phonemes.","zh":"作者描述發音器官在產生英語音位時的位置。"},{"en":"The production of English phonemes means the physical making of the basic sound units of English.","zh":"「the production of English phonemes」意思是身體實際產生英語基本語音單位。"},{"en":"To produce the phoneme /t/, the tongue touches the teeth-ridge and then releases air.","zh":"要產生 /t/ 這個音位，舌頭接觸齒齦，然後釋放氣流。"},{"en":"If the speech-organs are placed differently, one English phoneme may sound like another.","zh":"如果發音器官位置不同，一個英語音位可能聽起來像另一個。"},{"en":"The phrase connects English sounds with how the mouth makes them.","zh":"這個短語把英語語音與口腔如何製造它們連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in effect","meaning":"實際上；其實","examples":[{"en":"Some writers invented what were, in effect, systems of phonetic symbols.","zh":"有些作者發明的其實是音標符號系統。"},{"en":"In effect means in reality or in practical terms, even if not officially named that way.","zh":"「in effect」意思是實際上或就實際功能而言，即使沒有正式如此命名。"},{"en":"The class monitor became, in effect, the organiser of the whole event.","zh":"班長實際上成為整個活動的組織者。"},{"en":"If a system works like phonetic symbols, it is in effect a phonetic alphabet.","zh":"如果一套系統像音標符號一樣運作，它其實就是音標字母表。"},{"en":"The phrase clarifies what something really functions as.","zh":"這個短語說明某事真正發揮的功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"systems of phonetic symbols","meaning":"音標符號系統","examples":[{"en":"Early writers invented systems of phonetic symbols.","zh":"早期作者發明了音標符號系統。"},{"en":"Systems of phonetic symbols are sets of written signs used to represent speech sounds.","zh":"「systems of phonetic symbols」是用來代表語音的一套書寫符號。"},{"en":"Dictionaries use phonetic symbols to show how difficult words should be pronounced.","zh":"字典使用音標符號顯示困難詞語應如何發音。"},{"en":"If spelling is confusing, phonetic symbols can show the actual sound more clearly.","zh":"如果拼寫令人困惑，音標符號可以更清楚顯示實際聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes writing systems for pronunciation.","zh":"這個短語描述用於發音的書寫系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"combined with","meaning":"結合……","examples":[{"en":"Different kinds of evidence, combined with knowledge of speech-production, can clarify older pronunciation.","zh":"不同種類的證據結合發音產生知識，可以釐清較舊發音。"},{"en":"Combined with means joined together with something else to create a stronger result.","zh":"「combined with」意思是與另一事物結合，以產生更強效果。"},{"en":"Good teaching, combined with regular practice, helps students improve faster.","zh":"良好教學結合規律練習，可以幫助學生進步更快。"},{"en":"If old spellings are combined with phonetic knowledge, pronunciation history becomes clearer.","zh":"如果舊拼寫結合語音知識，發音歷史就更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that two sources work together.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩種來源共同發揮作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"mechanisms of speech-production","meaning":"發音產生的機制","examples":[{"en":"Knowledge of the mechanisms of speech-production helps researchers interpret sound changes.","zh":"關於發音產生機制的知識幫助研究人員解讀音變。"},{"en":"Mechanisms of speech-production are the physical processes by which the mouth, throat, and lungs create speech sounds.","zh":"「mechanisms of speech-production」是口腔、喉嚨和肺部製造語音的身體過程。"},{"en":"Students understand /m/ better when they learn that both lips close during its production.","zh":"當學生知道 /m/ 的產生需要雙唇閉合，他們會更理解這個音。"},{"en":"If researchers know how sounds are made, they can judge which sound changes are likely.","zh":"如果研究人員知道聲音如何產生，就能判斷哪些音變較可能發生。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the body’s process of making speech.","zh":"這個短語指身體製造語音的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"give us a very good idea of","meaning":"令我們對……有相當清楚的了解","examples":[{"en":"The evidence can give us a very good idea of the pronunciation of an earlier age.","zh":"這些證據可以令我們對某個早期時代的發音有相當清楚的了解。"},{"en":"To give us a very good idea of something means to help us understand it quite clearly, though not perfectly.","zh":"「give us a very good idea of」某事，意思是幫助我們相當清楚理解它，但不是完全確定。"},{"en":"A student’s draft can give the teacher a very good idea of what the student understands.","zh":"學生的草稿可以令老師相當清楚了解學生明白甚麼。"},{"en":"If several sources agree, they can give researchers a good idea of past pronunciation.","zh":"如果多項來源一致，它們可以令研究人員對過去發音有清楚了解。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests strong but not absolute understanding.","zh":"這個短語暗示強而有力但非絕對的理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the pronunciation of an earlier age","meaning":"某個早期時代的發音","examples":[{"en":"Researchers can often reconstruct the pronunciation of an earlier age.","zh":"研究人員常常能重建某個早期時代的發音。"},{"en":"The pronunciation of an earlier age means how people spoke words during a past historical period.","zh":"「the pronunciation of an earlier age」意思是人們在過去某歷史時期如何讀詞。"},{"en":"Old rhymes can help scholars guess the pronunciation of an earlier age.","zh":"舊押韻可以幫助學者推測某個早期時代的發音。"},{"en":"If a word once rhymed with another word, it may reveal how both were pronounced then.","zh":"如果某詞曾與另一詞押韻，它可能揭示兩者當時如何發音。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to historical pronunciation at a particular time.","zh":"這個短語指特定時期的歷史發音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"absolute certainty is never possible","meaning":"絕對確定是不可能的","examples":[{"en":"Absolute certainty is never possible when studying earlier pronunciation.","zh":"研究早期發音時，絕對確定是不可能的。"},{"en":"Absolute certainty is never possible means we can be strongly confident but cannot know something with perfect proof.","zh":"「absolute certainty is never possible」意思是我們可以非常有信心，但不能以完美證據知道某事。"},{"en":"Historians may know a great deal about an event, but absolute certainty is never possible for every detail.","zh":"歷史學家可能對一件事件知道很多，但每個細節都絕對確定是不可能的。"},{"en":"If there are no recordings, scholars must rely on indirect clues rather than complete certainty.","zh":"如果沒有錄音，學者必須依靠間接線索，而不是完全確定。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against claiming perfect knowledge.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要聲稱擁有完美知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"over any period of a few generations or more","meaning":"在幾代人或更長時間內","examples":[{"en":"Pronunciation can change over any period of a few generations or more.","zh":"發音可以在幾代人或更長時間內改變。"},{"en":"Over any period of a few generations or more means across several generations or a longer time span.","zh":"「over any period of a few generations or more」意思是跨越幾代人或更長時間。"},{"en":"Family stories can change over a few generations as people retell them differently.","zh":"家族故事在幾代人之間可能因人們不同講述而改變。"},{"en":"If pronunciation changes slowly, it may only become obvious after grandparents and grandchildren are compared.","zh":"如果發音慢慢改變，可能要比較祖父母和孫輩後才明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes change across long human time.","zh":"這個短語描述跨越長人類時間的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"large-scale regularities","meaning":"大規模的規律性","examples":[{"en":"Large-scale regularities can be found in pronunciation changes.","zh":"發音變化中可以找到大規模的規律性。"},{"en":"Large-scale regularities are broad patterns that happen repeatedly across many examples.","zh":"「large-scale regularities」是在許多例子中反覆出現的廣泛模式。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice large-scale regularities in students’ grammar mistakes after marking many essays.","zh":"老師批改許多文章後，可能注意到學生文法錯誤中的大規模規律性。"},{"en":"If many vowels shift in the same direction, that is not random but a pattern.","zh":"如果許多元音朝同一方向轉變，那就不是隨機，而是模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated patterns across a large set.","zh":"這個短語描述大量例子中的反覆模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"over a certain period of time","meaning":"在某段時間內","examples":[{"en":"Over a certain period of time, many vowels may change in the same direction.","zh":"在某段時間內，許多元音可能朝同一方向改變。"},{"en":"Over a certain period of time means during a particular length of time.","zh":"「over a certain period of time」意思是在某一段特定時間內。"},{"en":"Over a certain period of time, a student’s handwriting may become neater with practice.","zh":"在某段時間內，學生的字跡可能透過練習變得更工整。"},{"en":"If a sound changes gradually over time, people may not notice it immediately.","zh":"如果一個音隨時間逐漸改變，人們未必立即注意到。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a time frame for change.","zh":"這個短語提供變化的時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"long vowels","meaning":"長元音","examples":[{"en":"Long vowels may change into different long vowels over time.","zh":"長元音可能隨時間變成不同的長元音。"},{"en":"Long vowels are vowel sounds that are held longer or have a length distinction in a language.","zh":"「long vowels」是發音時間較長，或在語言中有長短區別的元音。"},{"en":"In some languages, changing a short vowel to a long vowel can change the meaning of a word.","zh":"在某些語言中，把短元音變成長元音可以改變詞義。"},{"en":"If long vowels shift systematically, many words may be pronounced differently.","zh":"如果長元音系統性轉變，許多詞的發音可能不同。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a type of vowel sound in phonology.","zh":"這個短語指音系學中的一類元音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in a certain position","meaning":"在某個特定位置","examples":[{"en":"A consonant may change when it appears in a certain position.","zh":"輔音在某個特定位置出現時可能改變。"},{"en":"In a certain position means in a specific place within a word or sentence.","zh":"「in a certain position」意思是在詞語或句子中的特定位置。"},{"en":"A sound may be pronounced differently at the beginning of a word than at the end.","zh":"一個音在詞首和詞尾的發音可能不同。"},{"en":"If a consonant changes only before another sound, its position matters.","zh":"如果輔音只在另一個音前改變，它的位置就很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase helps explain where a rule applies.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋規則在哪裡適用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at the end of a word","meaning":"在詞尾","examples":[{"en":"A consonant at the end of a word may be pronounced differently.","zh":"在詞尾的輔音可能讀法不同。"},{"en":"At the end of a word means in the final sound or letter position of a word.","zh":"「at the end of a word」意思是在詞語最後的音或字母位置。"},{"en":"In English, some letters at the end of a word may become weak or silent.","zh":"在英語中，有些詞尾字母可能變弱或不發音。"},{"en":"If a sound is hard to pronounce at the end, speakers may simplify or drop it.","zh":"如果某個音在詞尾難發，說話者可能簡化或省略它。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the final position in a word.","zh":"這個短語指出詞語最後位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sound laws","meaning":"語音規律；音變規律","examples":[{"en":"Regular pronunciation changes are often called sound laws.","zh":"規律的發音變化常被稱為語音規律。"},{"en":"Sound laws are regular patterns of sound change in a language during a particular period.","zh":"「sound laws」是在某語言某時期中的規律音變模式。"},{"en":"A sound law may explain why the same consonant changed in many related words.","zh":"語音規律可能解釋為何同一輔音在許多相關詞中改變。"},{"en":"If a change follows a sound law, it happens systematically rather than randomly.","zh":"如果變化遵循語音規律，它就是系統性發生，而不是隨機發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes regular rules of historical pronunciation change.","zh":"這個短語描述歷史發音變化中的規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"universal sound laws","meaning":"普遍語音規律","examples":[{"en":"There are no universal sound laws that apply to all languages.","zh":"沒有適用於所有語言的普遍語音規律。"},{"en":"Universal sound laws would be sound-change rules that work in every language.","zh":"「universal sound laws」是理論上可在每種語言中運作的音變規則。"},{"en":"A rule may explain English history well but fail when applied to Chinese or Arabic.","zh":"某規則可能很好地解釋英語歷史，但套用到中文或阿拉伯語時失效。"},{"en":"If languages change differently, no single sound law can explain all of them.","zh":"如果語言以不同方式改變，就沒有單一語音規律能解釋所有語言。"},{"en":"The phrase describes general rules that would apply everywhere, though the passage rejects them.","zh":"這個短語描述本應普遍適用的規則，但文章否定其存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reflect universal tendencies","meaning":"反映普遍趨勢","examples":[{"en":"Sound laws often reflect universal tendencies in speech.","zh":"語音規律常反映說話中的普遍趨勢。"},{"en":"To reflect universal tendencies means to show patterns that are common in human speech generally.","zh":"「reflect universal tendencies」意思是顯示人類語音中普遍常見的模式。"},{"en":"Many languages simplify difficult sound combinations, reflecting a common human tendency toward easier pronunciation.","zh":"許多語言會簡化困難音組，反映人類傾向較容易發音的普遍趨勢。"},{"en":"If speakers everywhere prefer easier mouth movements, similar sound changes may appear in different languages.","zh":"如果各地說話者都偏好較容易的口腔動作，不同語言中可能出現相似音變。"},{"en":"The phrase means a specific rule may reveal a broader human pattern.","zh":"這個短語意思是特定規則可能揭示更廣泛的人類模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a given language","meaning":"某一種語言","examples":[{"en":"A sound law applies to a given language at a given period.","zh":"語音規律適用於某一種語言在某一段時期。"},{"en":"A given language means one particular language being discussed.","zh":"「a given language」意思是正在討論的某一種特定語言。"},{"en":"A grammar rule may work in a given language but not in another language.","zh":"某文法規則可能在某一種語言中適用，但在另一語言中不適用。"},{"en":"If a sound change belongs to a given language, researchers should not assume it applies everywhere.","zh":"如果音變屬於某一種語言，研究人員不應假設它處處適用。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows discussion to one specific language.","zh":"這個短語把討論收窄到一種特定語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a given period","meaning":"某一段時期","examples":[{"en":"A particular sound law belongs to a given period in a language.","zh":"某一語音規律屬於某一種語言中的某一段時期。"},{"en":"A given period means one specific time span being discussed.","zh":"「a given period」意思是正在討論的一段特定時間。"},{"en":"A school policy may work well during a given period but become outdated later.","zh":"學校政策可能在某一段時期有效，但之後變得過時。"},{"en":"If a sound law belongs to a given period, it may stop applying after the language changes again.","zh":"如果語音規律屬於某一段時期，在語言再次改變後可能不再適用。"},{"en":"The phrase limits a statement to a particular time.","zh":"這個短語把說法限制在特定時間內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"play a part in","meaning":"在……中起作用","examples":[{"en":"Fashion may play a part in the process of pronunciation change.","zh":"潮流可能在發音變化過程中起作用。"},{"en":"To play a part in something means to contribute to it or have some influence on it.","zh":"「play a part in」某事，意思是促成它或對它有一定影響。"},{"en":"Sleep can play a part in how well students remember new vocabulary.","zh":"睡眠可以在學生記住新詞彙方面起作用。"},{"en":"If prestige affects imitation, social fashion can play a part in language change.","zh":"如果威望影響模仿，社會潮流就能在語言變化中起作用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one factor among several.","zh":"這個短語描述多個因素中的其中一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the process of change","meaning":"變化的過程","examples":[{"en":"Fashion may influence the process of change in pronunciation.","zh":"潮流可能影響發音變化的過程。"},{"en":"The process of change means the steps or stages through which something becomes different.","zh":"「the process of change」意思是某事變得不同所經歷的步驟或階段。"},{"en":"The process of change in a school policy may include discussion, trial, feedback, and revision.","zh":"學校政策變化的過程可能包括討論、試行、回饋和修訂。"},{"en":"If pronunciation changes slowly, the process may begin in one group and spread later.","zh":"如果發音慢慢改變，過程可能先在一個群體開始，之後傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how change happens over time.","zh":"這個短語集中於變化如何隨時間發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the spread of change","meaning":"變化的傳播","examples":[{"en":"Fashion certainly plays a part in the spread of change.","zh":"潮流確實在變化的傳播中起作用。"},{"en":"The spread of change means the movement of a new habit, form, or practice from one group to others.","zh":"「the spread of change」意思是新習慣、形式或做法由一個群體傳到其他群體。"},{"en":"A new slang word may spread from one school to many schools through social media.","zh":"新潮語可能透過社交媒體由一間學校傳到許多學校。"},{"en":"If high-status speakers use a pronunciation, others may copy it and spread the change.","zh":"如果高地位說話者使用某種發音，其他人可能模仿並傳播該變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how change travels through a community.","zh":"這個短語描述變化如何在社群中流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"people with the most prestige","meaning":"最有威望的人","examples":[{"en":"People with the most prestige are most likely to be imitated.","zh":"最有威望的人最可能被模仿。"},{"en":"People with the most prestige are those who are most respected, admired, or socially influential.","zh":"「people with the most prestige」是最受尊重、羨慕或具社會影響力的人。"},{"en":"In a school, popular senior students may have prestige, so younger students copy their speech.","zh":"在學校中，受歡迎的高年級學生可能有威望，因此低年級學生模仿他們說話。"},{"en":"If prestigious speakers change pronunciation, that change may spread more quickly.","zh":"如果有威望的說話者改變發音，該變化可能更快傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase describes socially powerful models of imitation.","zh":"這個短語描述具社會力量的模仿對象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be likely to be imitated","meaning":"很可能被模仿","examples":[{"en":"Prestigious speakers are likely to be imitated by others.","zh":"有威望的說話者很可能被其他人模仿。"},{"en":"To be likely to be imitated means others will probably copy that person’s behaviour, style, or speech.","zh":"「be likely to be imitated」意思是其他人很可能模仿該人的行為、風格或說話方式。"},{"en":"A confident presenter may be imitated by classmates who want to sound professional.","zh":"有自信的匯報者可能被想聽起來專業的同學模仿。"},{"en":"If a pronunciation is associated with successful people, it may be copied widely.","zh":"如果某發音與成功人士有關，它可能被廣泛模仿。"},{"en":"The phrase describes probable copying.","zh":"這個短語描述很可能出現的模仿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take place in","meaning":"在……中發生","examples":[{"en":"A change that takes place in one social group may spread to another.","zh":"在一個社會群體中發生的變化，可能傳到另一個群體。"},{"en":"To take place in a group or location means to happen there.","zh":"「take place in」某群體或地點，意思是在那裡發生。"},{"en":"A new fashion may take place first in cities before spreading to smaller towns.","zh":"新潮流可能先在城市中發生，再傳到較小城鎮。"},{"en":"If a pronunciation change takes place in a powerful group, other groups may notice it.","zh":"如果發音變化在有權勢的群體中發生，其他群體可能注意到它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where something happens.","zh":"這個短語描述某事發生在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"social group","meaning":"社會群體","examples":[{"en":"A pronunciation change may begin in one social group.","zh":"發音變化可能始於一個社會群體。"},{"en":"A social group is a set of people who share status, age, job, class, interests, or community identity.","zh":"「social group」是共享地位、年齡、工作、階級、興趣或社群身份的一群人。"},{"en":"Teenagers, office workers, and university students can each form a social group.","zh":"青少年、辦公室員工和大學生都可以各自形成社會群體。"},{"en":"If one social group uses a new pronunciation, other groups may later copy it.","zh":"如果一個社會群體使用新發音，其他群體之後可能模仿。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people connected by social features.","zh":"這個短語指由社會特徵連繫起來的人群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"more or less accurately","meaning":"或多或少準確地","examples":[{"en":"Speakers may imitate a pronunciation more or less accurately.","zh":"說話者可能或多或少準確地模仿某種發音。"},{"en":"More or less accurately means with some degree of correctness, but not perfectly.","zh":"「more or less accurately」意思是有一定程度準確，但並不完美。"},{"en":"A student may repeat a teacher’s accent more or less accurately after hearing it many times.","zh":"學生聽過很多次後，可能或多或少準確地模仿老師的口音。"},{"en":"If imitation is not exact, small pronunciation differences may appear.","zh":"如果模仿並不完全準確，就可能出現小發音差異。"},{"en":"The phrase describes imperfect but recognisable copying.","zh":"這個短語描述不完美但可辨認的模仿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rise or fall in status","meaning":"地位上升或下降","examples":[{"en":"When a social group rises or falls in status, its pronunciation may gain or lose prestige.","zh":"當一個社會群體地位上升或下降，其發音可能獲得或失去威望。"},{"en":"To rise or fall in status means to become more or less respected or powerful in society.","zh":"「rise or fall in status」意思是在社會中變得更受尊重或較不受尊重、更有權或較無權。"},{"en":"A profession may rise in status when society begins to value its skills more highly.","zh":"當社會開始更重視某職業技能，該職業地位可能上升。"},{"en":"If a group falls in status, people may stop copying its speech.","zh":"如果一個群體地位下降，人們可能停止模仿其說話方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes social movement in respect or rank.","zh":"這個短語描述尊重或階級上的社會變動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"gain or lose prestige","meaning":"獲得或失去威望","examples":[{"en":"A pronunciation may gain or lose prestige over time.","zh":"一種發音可能隨時間獲得或失去威望。"},{"en":"To gain or lose prestige means to become more or less respected or socially desirable.","zh":"「gain or lose prestige」意思是變得更受尊重或更不受尊重、更受歡迎或更不受歡迎。"},{"en":"A hairstyle may gain prestige if celebrities wear it, then lose prestige when it looks outdated.","zh":"如果名人留某種髮型，它可能獲得威望；當它顯得過時，又可能失去威望。"},{"en":"If an accent gains prestige, people may try to copy it.","zh":"如果某口音獲得威望，人們可能嘗試模仿它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing social value.","zh":"這個短語描述社會價值的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"formerly considered desirable","meaning":"以往被認為理想的","examples":[{"en":"A Russian pronunciation formerly considered desirable later became undesirable.","zh":"一種以往被認為理想的俄語發音後來變得不受歡迎。"},{"en":"Formerly considered desirable means once thought to be attractive, proper, or high-status.","zh":"「formerly considered desirable」意思是曾經被認為吸引、正確或有高地位。"},{"en":"A school uniform style formerly considered desirable may later seem old-fashioned.","zh":"以往被認為理想的校服款式後來可能顯得過時。"},{"en":"If social values change, a once-admired accent may lose its appeal.","zh":"如果社會價值改變，曾受欣賞的口音可能失去吸引力。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts past approval with later change.","zh":"這個短語對比過去認可與後來改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"an undesirable accent","meaning":"不受歡迎的口音","examples":[{"en":"People tried to disguise a pronunciation that had become an undesirable accent.","zh":"人們試圖掩飾一種已變成不受歡迎口音的發音。"},{"en":"An undesirable accent is an accent that people judge negatively or consider low-status.","zh":"「an undesirable accent」是被人負面評價或視為低地位的口音。"},{"en":"A worker may feel embarrassed if colleagues treat their regional accent as undesirable.","zh":"如果同事把某人的地區口音視為不受歡迎，那位員工可能感到尷尬。"},{"en":"If an accent becomes undesirable, speakers may try to hide it in formal situations.","zh":"如果一種口音變得不受歡迎，說話者可能在正式場合嘗試隱藏它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes social judgement, not linguistic inferiority.","zh":"這個短語描述社會評價，而不是語言本身低劣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"try to disguise","meaning":"試圖掩飾","examples":[{"en":"Speakers tried to disguise an accent that had lost prestige.","zh":"說話者試圖掩飾一種已失去威望的口音。"},{"en":"To try to disguise something means to attempt to hide it or make it less noticeable.","zh":"「try to disguise」某事，意思是嘗試隱藏它或令它較不明顯。"},{"en":"A nervous student may try to disguise their anxiety by speaking more slowly.","zh":"緊張的學生可能試圖透過說慢一點來掩飾焦慮。"},{"en":"If an accent is judged negatively, speakers may try to disguise it to avoid prejudice.","zh":"如果某口音被負面評價，說話者可能試圖掩飾它以避免偏見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deliberate hiding or masking.","zh":"這個短語描述有意隱藏或遮掩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"accepted English pronunciation","meaning":"公認英語發音","examples":[{"en":"Accepted English pronunciation changed during the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries.","zh":"公認英語發音在十七和十八世紀期間發生變化。"},{"en":"Accepted English pronunciation means the form of English pronunciation regarded as correct, educated, or socially approved at a time.","zh":"「accepted English pronunciation」是在某時期被視為正確、受教育或社會認可的英語發音。"},{"en":"A student may learn accepted pronunciation for public speaking, even if they use a regional accent at home.","zh":"學生可能為公開演講學習公認發音，即使在家使用地區口音。"},{"en":"If society changes, accepted pronunciation may change with it.","zh":"如果社會改變，公認發音也可能跟着改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes socially recognised pronunciation standards.","zh":"這個短語描述受社會認可的發音標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"consist in","meaning":"在於；表現為","examples":[{"en":"Some pronunciation changes consist in the replacement of one style by another.","zh":"有些發音變化在於以一種風格取代另一種。"},{"en":"To consist in something means to have that thing as the main feature or essential nature.","zh":"「consist in」某事，意思是以該事作為主要特徵或本質。"},{"en":"Good revision does not consist in reading notes once; it involves testing and correction.","zh":"良好溫習不在於只讀一次筆記；它涉及測試和修正。"},{"en":"If a change consists in replacement, the new form takes the place of the old one.","zh":"如果變化表現為取代，新形式就取代舊形式。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what something mainly involves.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事主要涉及甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the replacement of one style by another","meaning":"以一種風格取代另一種風格","examples":[{"en":"The change involved the replacement of one style of pronunciation by another.","zh":"這種變化涉及以一種發音風格取代另一種。"},{"en":"The replacement of one style by another means one way of doing something takes over from a previous way.","zh":"「the replacement of one style by another」意思是一種做法取代先前另一種做法。"},{"en":"In schools, the replacement of chalkboards by smartboards changed classroom teaching.","zh":"在學校中，智慧白板取代黑板改變了課堂教學。"},{"en":"If one pronunciation style becomes prestigious, it may replace another style over time.","zh":"如果一種發音風格變得有威望，它可能隨時間取代另一種風格。"},{"en":"The phrase describes substitution between two styles.","zh":"這個短語描述兩種風格之間的替換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an already existing style","meaning":"已經存在的風格","examples":[{"en":"An already existing style of pronunciation replaced another style.","zh":"一種已經存在的發音風格取代了另一種風格。"},{"en":"An already existing style is a style that was already present before it became dominant.","zh":"「an already existing style」是在成為主導前已經存在的風格。"},{"en":"A school may adopt an already existing teaching method instead of inventing a new one.","zh":"學校可能採用已經存在的教學方法，而不是發明新方法。"},{"en":"If a pronunciation style already exists in one group, it can later spread to another group.","zh":"如果一種發音風格已存在於某群體中，它之後可以傳到另一群體。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the new dominant form was not newly created.","zh":"這個短語顯示新的主導形式並非新創造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be a result of","meaning":"是……的結果","examples":[{"en":"Such substitutions were probably a result of great social changes.","zh":"這些替換很可能是巨大社會變遷的結果。"},{"en":"To be a result of something means to happen because of it.","zh":"「be a result of」某事，意思是因為它而發生。"},{"en":"A student’s better grades may be a result of regular feedback and practice.","zh":"學生成績改善可能是規律回饋和練習的結果。"},{"en":"If society changes greatly, speech patterns may change as a result.","zh":"如果社會大幅改變，說話模式可能因此改變。"},{"en":"The phrase explains cause and effect.","zh":"這個短語解釋因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"great social changes","meaning":"巨大的社會變遷","examples":[{"en":"Great social changes affected English pronunciation in that period.","zh":"巨大的社會變遷影響了那個時期的英語發音。"},{"en":"Great social changes are major shifts in class, power, wealth, values, or social structure.","zh":"「great social changes」是階級、權力、財富、價值或社會結構上的重大轉變。"},{"en":"Industrialisation brought great social changes as people moved from farms to cities.","zh":"工業化帶來巨大社會變遷，因為人們由農村搬到城市。"},{"en":"If social classes mix differently, speech habits may also shift.","zh":"如果社會階級以不同方式混合，說話習慣也可能轉變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes large changes in how society is organised.","zh":"這個短語描述社會組織方式的大型改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"increased power and wealth","meaning":"權力和財富增加","examples":[{"en":"The increased power and wealth of the middle classes influenced speech patterns.","zh":"中產階級權力和財富增加影響了說話模式。"},{"en":"Increased power and wealth means a group has gained more influence, money, and social importance.","zh":"「increased power and wealth」意思是一個群體獲得更多影響力、金錢和社會重要性。"},{"en":"A business group may gain power and wealth when trade expands quickly.","zh":"當貿易迅速擴張，某商業群體可能獲得更多權力和財富。"},{"en":"If a class becomes richer and more powerful, its habits may become more fashionable.","zh":"如果一個階級變得更富有和更有權力，其習慣可能變得更時尚。"},{"en":"The phrase links economic and social strength.","zh":"這個短語連結經濟和社會力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the middle classes","meaning":"中產階級","examples":[{"en":"The middle classes became more powerful and wealthy.","zh":"中產階級變得更有權力和財富。"},{"en":"The middle classes are social groups between the working class and the upper class, often linked with education, business, or professions.","zh":"「the middle classes」是介乎工人階級與上流階級之間的社會群體，常與教育、商業或專業有關。"},{"en":"Teachers, shop owners, and office managers may belong to the middle classes in some societies.","zh":"在某些社會中，老師、店主和辦公室經理可能屬於中產階級。"},{"en":"If the middle classes rise socially, their speech may gain influence.","zh":"如果中產階級社會地位上升，其說話方式可能獲得影響力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a broad social class, not one single group.","zh":"這個短語指廣泛社會階級，而不是單一群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"steady infiltration upwards into","meaning":"穩步向上滲入……","examples":[{"en":"The middle classes’ steady infiltration upwards into higher social ranks affected pronunciation.","zh":"中產階級穩步向上滲入較高社會階層，影響了發音。"},{"en":"Steady infiltration upwards into a group means gradual movement into a higher social level.","zh":"「steady infiltration upwards into」某群體，意思是逐漸進入較高社會層級。"},{"en":"Talented workers may move steadily upwards into management positions over many years.","zh":"有才能的員工可能多年來穩步向上進入管理層職位。"},{"en":"If middle-class people enter higher ranks, they may carry their speech habits with them.","zh":"如果中產人士進入較高階層，他們可能把自己的說話習慣帶進去。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow upward social movement.","zh":"這個短語描述緩慢的向上社會流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the ranks of the landed gentry","meaning":"擁有土地的鄉紳階層","examples":[{"en":"The middle classes moved upwards into the ranks of the landed gentry.","zh":"中產階級向上進入擁有土地的鄉紳階層。"},{"en":"The ranks of the landed gentry are the social class of land-owning gentlemen and families.","zh":"「the ranks of the landed gentry」是擁有土地的紳士和家族所屬社會階層。"},{"en":"In older Britain, the landed gentry had social prestige because they owned land.","zh":"在舊英國，擁有土地的鄉紳因擁有土地而具社會威望。"},{"en":"If new wealthy families enter the landed gentry, older class boundaries become less fixed.","zh":"如果新富家庭進入鄉紳階層，舊階級界線就變得較不固定。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a historical upper social group based on landownership.","zh":"這個短語指以土地擁有為基礎的歷史上層社會群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"carry elements of something into","meaning":"把……的元素帶入……","examples":[{"en":"Social mobility carried elements of middle-class pronunciation into upper-class speech.","zh":"社會流動把中產階級發音的元素帶入上流階層說話方式。"},{"en":"To carry elements of something into another area means to bring parts of it there.","zh":"「carry elements of something into」另一範圍，意思是把其中部分帶到那裡。"},{"en":"Migrants may carry elements of their home culture into a new city through food and festivals.","zh":"移民可能透過食物和節日，把家鄉文化元素帶入新城市。"},{"en":"If people move socially, they may bring speech habits from one class into another.","zh":"如果人們在社會上流動，他們可能把一個階級的說話習慣帶入另一階級。"},{"en":"The phrase describes transfer of features from one context to another.","zh":"這個短語描述特徵由一個語境轉移到另一語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"upper-class speech","meaning":"上流階層的說話方式","examples":[{"en":"Middle-class pronunciation influenced upper-class speech.","zh":"中產階級發音影響了上流階層的說話方式。"},{"en":"Upper-class speech is the way of speaking associated with the highest social class.","zh":"「upper-class speech」是與最高社會階層相關的說話方式。"},{"en":"In some societies, upper-class speech is treated as more formal or prestigious.","zh":"在某些社會中，上流階層說話方式被視為較正式或有威望。"},{"en":"If upper-class speech adopts middle-class features, social change is reflected in language.","zh":"如果上流階層說話方式吸收中產特徵，社會變化就反映在語言中。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to speech linked with high social status.","zh":"這個短語指與高社會地位相關的說話方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a less specific variant of","meaning":"較籠統的論點變體","examples":[{"en":"A less specific variant of the argument focuses on imperfect imitation.","zh":"該論點的較籠統變體集中於不完美模仿。"},{"en":"A less specific variant of an argument is a broader or less detailed version of that argument.","zh":"「a less specific variant of」某論點，是該論點較廣泛或較不詳細的版本。"},{"en":"A teacher may give a less specific variant of an explanation before adding technical details.","zh":"老師可能先給出較籠統的解釋，再加入技術細節。"},{"en":"If an argument becomes less specific, it may cover more cases but explain fewer details.","zh":"如果論點變得較籠統，它可能涵蓋更多個案，但解釋較少細節。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broader version of an idea.","zh":"這個短語描述一個想法的較廣泛版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"children’s imitation","meaning":"兒童的模仿","examples":[{"en":"Children’s imitation of adult speech is often imperfect.","zh":"兒童對成人說話方式的模仿常常不完美。"},{"en":"Children’s imitation means children copying the words, sounds, habits, or behaviour of others.","zh":"「children’s imitation」意思是兒童模仿他人的詞語、聲音、習慣或行為。"},{"en":"A child may imitate a parent’s accent after hearing it every day at home.","zh":"孩子每天在家聽到父母口音後，可能模仿該口音。"},{"en":"If children copy adult speech imperfectly in a similar direction, pronunciation may slowly change.","zh":"如果兒童以相似方向不完美地模仿成人說話，發音可能慢慢改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how children learn by copying.","zh":"這個短語描述兒童如何透過模仿學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"imperfect imitation","meaning":"不完美的模仿","examples":[{"en":"Imperfect imitation may help explain some pronunciation changes.","zh":"不完美的模仿可能幫助解釋某些發音變化。"},{"en":"Imperfect imitation means copying something with small differences or mistakes.","zh":"「imperfect imitation」意思是帶有小差異或錯誤地模仿某事。"},{"en":"A student may imitate a teacher’s pronunciation imperfectly and create a slightly different sound.","zh":"學生可能不完美地模仿老師發音，產生略為不同的聲音。"},{"en":"If many children imitate the same sound imperfectly in the same way, the language may change.","zh":"如果許多兒童以同一方式不完美地模仿同一個音，語言可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes copying that is close but not exact.","zh":"這個短語描述接近但不完全準確的模仿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"copy their parents’ speech","meaning":"模仿父母的說話方式","examples":[{"en":"Children copy their parents’ speech but do not reproduce it exactly.","zh":"兒童模仿父母的說話方式，但不會完全準確重現。"},{"en":"To copy their parents’ speech means to learn and repeat the way parents pronounce words and use language.","zh":"「copy their parents’ speech」意思是學習並重複父母讀詞和使用語言的方式。"},{"en":"A child may copy their parents’ speech by using the same local expressions at home.","zh":"孩子可能透過在家使用同一本地說法來模仿父母的說話方式。"},{"en":"If children copy speech imperfectly, small differences can enter the next generation.","zh":"如果兒童不完美地模仿說話方式，小差異可能進入下一代。"},{"en":"The phrase describes language learning through family imitation.","zh":"這個短語描述透過家庭模仿學習語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"reproduce it exactly","meaning":"完全準確地重現","examples":[{"en":"Children copy adult speech but never reproduce it exactly.","zh":"兒童模仿成人說話方式，但從不完全準確地重現。"},{"en":"To reproduce it exactly means to copy something with no difference at all.","zh":"「reproduce it exactly」意思是毫無差異地複製某事。"},{"en":"A student may copy a diagram carefully but still fail to reproduce it exactly.","zh":"學生可能仔細抄畫圖表，但仍未能完全準確地重現。"},{"en":"If children do not reproduce adult speech exactly, minor pronunciation differences appear.","zh":"如果兒童沒有完全準確地重現成人說話方式，小發音差異就會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes perfect copying, which is difficult in real life.","zh":"這個短語描述完美複製，而這在現實中很困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"deviations from adult speech","meaning":"偏離成人說話方式的情況","examples":[{"en":"Deviations from adult speech are usually corrected in later childhood.","zh":"偏離成人說話方式的情況通常在兒童期後期被糾正。"},{"en":"Deviations from adult speech are differences between how children speak and how adults around them speak.","zh":"「deviations from adult speech」是兒童說話方式與身邊成人說話方式之間的差異。"},{"en":"A child who says “wabbit” instead of “rabbit” shows a deviation from adult speech.","zh":"孩子把 “rabbit” 說成 “wabbit”，就是偏離成人說話方式。"},{"en":"If adults correct these deviations, many childhood pronunciations disappear.","zh":"如果成人糾正這些偏差，許多兒童期發音就會消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes child speech forms that differ from adult models.","zh":"這個短語描述與成人模式不同的兒童說話形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in later childhood","meaning":"在兒童期後期","examples":[{"en":"Many pronunciation deviations are corrected in later childhood.","zh":"許多發音偏差在兒童期後期被糾正。"},{"en":"In later childhood means during the later years of childhood, before adolescence.","zh":"「in later childhood」意思是在青春期前的較後兒童年歲。"},{"en":"A child may become better at reading aloud in later childhood.","zh":"孩子可能在兒童期後期更擅長朗讀。"},{"en":"If speech errors are corrected in later childhood, they may not enter adult speech.","zh":"如果語音錯誤在兒童期後期被糾正，它們可能不會進入成人說話方式。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a developmental time period.","zh":"這個短語提供發展時間段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a certain amount of random variation","meaning":"一定程度的隨機變異","examples":[{"en":"Adults show a certain amount of random variation in pronunciation.","zh":"成人在發音上顯示一定程度的隨機變異。"},{"en":"A certain amount of random variation means some small unpredictable differences.","zh":"「a certain amount of random variation」意思是一些小而不可預測的差異。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice a certain amount of random variation in students’ handwriting from day to day.","zh":"老師可能注意到學生每天字跡有一定程度的隨機變異。"},{"en":"If variation is random, it may not lead to a stable language change.","zh":"如果變異是隨機的，它未必導致穩定語言變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limited but irregular difference.","zh":"這個短語描述有限但不規則的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a given phoneme","meaning":"某一個音位","examples":[{"en":"A speaker may vary in the pronunciation of a given phoneme.","zh":"說話者在某一個音位的發音上可能有所變化。"},{"en":"A given phoneme means one particular sound unit in a language.","zh":"「a given phoneme」意思是一種語言中的某個特定語音單位。"},{"en":"The English phoneme /t/ may be pronounced differently in “top” and “water”.","zh":"英語音位 /t/ 在 “top” 和 “water” 中可能讀法不同。"},{"en":"If one phoneme varies in predictable ways, linguists can study the pattern.","zh":"如果一個音位以可預測方式變化，語言學家就能研究該模式。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a specific speech sound being discussed.","zh":"這個短語指出正在討論的特定語音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the phonetic context","meaning":"語音環境","examples":[{"en":"The phonetic context may be kept unchanged in the example.","zh":"例子中的語音環境可能保持不變。"},{"en":"The phonetic context is the surrounding sound environment of a speech sound.","zh":"「the phonetic context」是某語音周圍的聲音環境。"},{"en":"The sound /n/ may change depending on the phonetic context before /p/ or /t/.","zh":"/n/ 音可能因位於 /p/ 或 /t/ 前的語音環境不同而改變。"},{"en":"If the surrounding sounds stay the same, researchers can compare pronunciation more fairly.","zh":"如果周圍聲音保持相同，研究人員就能更公平地比較發音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the sound environment around a phoneme.","zh":"這個短語描述音位周圍的聲音環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be kept unchanged","meaning":"保持不變","examples":[{"en":"The phonetic context is kept unchanged during the comparison.","zh":"比較期間，語音環境保持不變。"},{"en":"To be kept unchanged means to remain the same while other things are compared or tested.","zh":"「be kept unchanged」意思是在比較或測試其他事物時保持相同。"},{"en":"In a science experiment, the amount of water may be kept unchanged while light is varied.","zh":"在科學實驗中，水量可能保持不變，而光線有所變化。"},{"en":"If context is kept unchanged, any difference is easier to identify.","zh":"如果語境保持不變，任何差異就更容易識別。"},{"en":"The phrase describes controlled sameness.","zh":"這個短語描述受控的不變狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"explain changes in pronunciation","meaning":"解釋發音變化","examples":[{"en":"Random variation alone cannot explain changes in pronunciation.","zh":"單靠隨機變異不能解釋發音變化。"},{"en":"To explain changes in pronunciation means to show why speech sounds become different over time.","zh":"「explain changes in pronunciation」意思是顯示語音為何隨時間變得不同。"},{"en":"Linguists may use social status, imitation, and ease of articulation to explain pronunciation changes.","zh":"語言學家可能用社會地位、模仿和發音省力來解釋發音變化。"},{"en":"If a theory cannot explain a systematic pattern, it is incomplete.","zh":"如果一個理論不能解釋系統性模式，它就是不完整的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving reasons for sound change.","zh":"這個短語描述為音變提供原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"systematic trend","meaning":"系統性趨勢","examples":[{"en":"A systematic trend in imitation errors could lead to pronunciation change.","zh":"模仿錯誤中的系統性趨勢可能導致發音變化。"},{"en":"A systematic trend is a repeated pattern that moves in the same direction.","zh":"「systematic trend」是朝同一方向反覆出現的模式。"},{"en":"If many students make the same grammar mistake, the teacher sees a systematic trend, not random errors.","zh":"如果許多學生犯同一文法錯誤，老師看到的是系統性趨勢，而不是隨機錯誤。"},{"en":"If children repeatedly simplify the same sound, the trend may become part of the language.","zh":"如果兒童反覆簡化同一個音，這種趨勢可能成為語言的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised, repeated movement in data or behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述數據或行為中有組織、反覆的變動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"failures of imitation","meaning":"模仿失準","examples":[{"en":"Failures of imitation must show a systematic trend to affect the language.","zh":"模仿失準必須顯示系統性趨勢，才會影響語言。"},{"en":"Failures of imitation are cases where someone tries to copy speech but does not copy it exactly.","zh":"「failures of imitation」是某人嘗試模仿說話但未能完全準確複製的情況。"},{"en":"A child’s failure to imitate /r/ may produce a different sound for several years.","zh":"孩子未能模仿 /r/ 音，可能多年都發出另一個音。"},{"en":"If failures of imitation are random, they usually disappear; if patterned, they may spread.","zh":"如果模仿失準是隨機的，它們通常會消失；如果有模式，可能會傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase describes imperfect copying that may influence language.","zh":"這個短語描述可能影響語言的不完美複製。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"merely random deviations","meaning":"純粹隨機的偏差","examples":[{"en":"Merely random deviations will cancel one another out.","zh":"純粹隨機的偏差會互相抵消。"},{"en":"Merely random deviations are small differences with no clear direction or pattern.","zh":"「merely random deviations」是沒有清楚方向或模式的小差異。"},{"en":"If students make different spelling mistakes every time, they may be merely random deviations.","zh":"如果學生每次都犯不同拼寫錯誤，它們可能只是純粹隨機的偏差。"},{"en":"Random deviations usually do not create lasting change because they do not move together.","zh":"隨機偏差通常不會造成持久變化，因為它們不會一起朝同方向移動。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts accidental variation with systematic change.","zh":"這個短語對比偶然變異與系統性變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cancel one another out","meaning":"互相抵消","examples":[{"en":"Random deviations will cancel one another out over time.","zh":"隨機偏差會隨時間互相抵消。"},{"en":"To cancel one another out means two or more effects balance each other so there is no overall result.","zh":"「cancel one another out」意思是兩個或多個效果互相平衡，因此沒有整體結果。"},{"en":"If one student arrives five minutes early and another five minutes late, the average may cancel the difference out.","zh":"如果一名學生早到五分鐘，另一名遲到五分鐘，平均數可能互相抵消差異。"},{"en":"If pronunciation errors move in opposite directions, they may not change the language overall.","zh":"如果發音錯誤朝相反方向移動，它們可能不會整體改變語言。"},{"en":"The phrase describes effects neutralising each other.","zh":"這個短語描述效果互相中和。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"net change","meaning":"淨變化","examples":[{"en":"If deviations cancel out, there will be no net change in the language.","zh":"如果偏差互相抵消，語言就不會有淨變化。"},{"en":"Net change is the overall change left after opposite effects have been balanced.","zh":"「net change」是在相反效果平衡後留下的整體變化。"},{"en":"A class may gain two students and lose two students, producing no net change in class size.","zh":"一班增加兩名學生又失去兩名學生，班級人數就沒有淨變化。"},{"en":"If random pronunciation differences balance out, the language as a whole stays the same.","zh":"如果隨機發音差異互相平衡，整體語言就保持不變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the final overall effect.","zh":"這個短語描述最終整體效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be often invoked","meaning":"經常被援引","examples":[{"en":"The principle of ease is often invoked to explain sound change.","zh":"省力原則經常被援引用來解釋音變。"},{"en":"To be often invoked means to be frequently mentioned or used as an explanation.","zh":"「be often invoked」意思是經常被提及或用作解釋。"},{"en":"Stress is often invoked to explain why students make careless mistakes.","zh":"壓力經常被援引用來解釋學生為何犯粗心錯誤。"},{"en":"If a principle explains many cases, scholars may invoke it repeatedly.","zh":"如果某原則能解釋許多個案，學者可能反覆援引它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an idea being regularly used in argument or explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述某想法經常被用於論證或解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the principle of ease","meaning":"省力原則","examples":[{"en":"The principle of ease is also called minimisation of effort.","zh":"省力原則又稱為減少用力。"},{"en":"The principle of ease is the idea that speakers tend to prefer easier or less effortful pronunciation.","zh":"「the principle of ease」是說話者傾向選擇較容易或較省力發音的想法。"},{"en":"People may shorten “going to” to “gonna” in casual speech because it is easier to say.","zh":"人們在口語中可能把 “going to” 縮成 “gonna”，因為較容易說。"},{"en":"If a difficult sound combination becomes easier, the principle of ease may be involved.","zh":"如果困難音組變得較容易，省力原則可能參與其中。"},{"en":"The phrase explains sound change through reduced effort.","zh":"這個短語透過減少用力來解釋音變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"minimisation of effort","meaning":"減少用力；省力","examples":[{"en":"Minimisation of effort may influence pronunciation.","zh":"減少用力可能影響發音。"},{"en":"Minimisation of effort means reducing the physical or mental work needed to do something.","zh":"「minimisation of effort」意思是減少做某事所需的身體或心理工作量。"},{"en":"People use shortcuts in typing because minimisation of effort saves time and energy.","zh":"人們打字時使用捷徑，因為減少用力可以節省時間和精力。"},{"en":"If speakers can pronounce a word with less mouth movement, the easier version may spread.","zh":"如果說話者能用較少口腔動作讀出詞語，較容易版本可能傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the tendency to make actions easier.","zh":"這個短語描述把動作變得更容易的傾向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the change from X to Y","meaning":"從 X 變成 Y 的變化","examples":[{"en":"The change from fussy to fuzzy is an example of assimilation.","zh":"從 fussy 變成 fuzzy 的變化是同化的例子。"},{"en":"The change from X to Y means one form becomes another form.","zh":"「the change from X to Y」意思是一種形式變成另一種形式。"},{"en":"The change from handwritten notices to online messages altered how parents receive school information.","zh":"從手寫通告變成網上訊息的變化，改變了家長接收學校資訊的方式。"},{"en":"If one sound changes into another under nearby influence, linguists describe the change from X to Y.","zh":"如果一個音在鄰近音影響下變成另一個音，語言學家會描述從 X 到 Y 的變化。"},{"en":"The phrase names the starting form and the resulting form.","zh":"這個短語指出起始形式和結果形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be an example of","meaning":"是……的例子","examples":[{"en":"The change from fussy to fuzzy is an example of assimilation.","zh":"從 fussy 變成 fuzzy 是同化的例子。"},{"en":"To be an example of something means to show or illustrate that category or idea.","zh":"「be an example of」某事，意思是顯示或說明該類別或想法。"},{"en":"Forgetting a silent letter in spelling can be an example of sound influencing writing.","zh":"拼寫中忘記不發音字母可以是聲音影響文字的例子。"},{"en":"If one case clearly shows a rule, it can help students understand the rule.","zh":"如果一個個案清楚顯示規則，它可以幫助學生理解該規則。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a specific case of a broader concept.","zh":"這個短語引入較廣概念中的具體個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"assimilation","meaning":"同化","examples":[{"en":"Assimilation is a very common kind of sound change.","zh":"同化是一種非常常見的音變。"},{"en":"Assimilation happens when one sound becomes more like a nearby sound.","zh":"「assimilation」發生於一個音變得更像附近另一個音時。"},{"en":"In fast speech, “handbag” may sound closer to “hambag” because /n/ moves toward /b/.","zh":"在快速說話中，“handbag” 可能聽起來較像 “hambag”，因為 /n/ 向 /b/ 靠近。"},{"en":"If a sound changes to match its neighbour, pronunciation becomes easier.","zh":"如果一個音改變以配合鄰近音，發音就變得較容易。"},{"en":"The word describes sound change through influence from nearby sounds.","zh":"這個詞描述受鄰近音影響而出現的音變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"under the influence of","meaning":"在……的影響下","examples":[{"en":"A sound may change under the influence of a neighbouring sound.","zh":"一個音可能在鄰近音的影響下改變。"},{"en":"Under the influence of something means affected or shaped by it.","zh":"「under the influence of」某事，意思是受其影響或塑造。"},{"en":"A student’s writing may improve under the influence of careful teacher feedback.","zh":"在老師仔細回饋的影響下，學生寫作可能進步。"},{"en":"If one sound is close to another, it may change under that sound’s influence.","zh":"如果一個音靠近另一個音，它可能在該音影響下改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one thing being affected by another.","zh":"這個短語描述一事物受另一事物影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a neighbouring sound","meaning":"鄰近音","examples":[{"en":"Assimilation occurs when a sound is influenced by a neighbouring sound.","zh":"當一個音受鄰近音影響時，就會發生同化。"},{"en":"A neighbouring sound is a sound that comes directly before or after another sound.","zh":"「a neighbouring sound」是在另一個音前面或後面直接出現的音。"},{"en":"In “input”, the /n/ may sound like /m/ because the neighbouring /p/ is made with the lips.","zh":"在 “input” 中，/n/ 可能聽起來像 /m/，因為鄰近的 /p/ 由雙唇發出。"},{"en":"If a neighbouring sound is easier to match, speakers may adjust pronunciation.","zh":"如果配合鄰近音較容易，說話者可能調整發音。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to nearby sounds in a word or phrase.","zh":"這個短語指詞語或短語中的附近聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"greater efficiency","meaning":"更高效率","examples":[{"en":"Greater efficiency has been achieved in the pronunciation of scant.","zh":"scant 的發音達到了更高效率。"},{"en":"Greater efficiency means doing something with less effort, time, or movement.","zh":"「greater efficiency」意思是以較少力氣、時間或動作完成某事。"},{"en":"A student achieves greater efficiency by organising notes before revising.","zh":"學生在溫習前整理筆記，可以達到更高效率。"},{"en":"If two sounds are made in the same place, the mouth uses less movement.","zh":"如果兩個音在同一位置發出，口腔就使用較少動作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a more economical way of doing something.","zh":"這個短語描述更省力的做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be articulated in the same place","meaning":"在同一發音部位發出","examples":[{"en":"The sounds /n/ and /t/ are articulated in the same place.","zh":"/n/ 和 /t/ 兩個音在同一發音部位發出。"},{"en":"To be articulated in the same place means two sounds are produced using the same part of the mouth.","zh":"「be articulated in the same place」意思是兩個音使用口腔同一部位產生。"},{"en":"/t/ and /d/ are articulated in the same place, but they differ in voicing.","zh":"/t/ 和 /d/ 在同一發音部位發出，但濁音性不同。"},{"en":"If two sounds share the same place of articulation, moving between them is easier.","zh":"如果兩個音共享同一發音部位，在它們之間轉換會較容易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where sounds are physically made.","zh":"這個短語描述聲音在身體哪裡產生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the tip of the tongue","meaning":"舌尖","examples":[{"en":"The sound is made with the tip of the tongue against the teeth-ridge.","zh":"這個音是用舌尖抵住齒齦發出的。"},{"en":"The tip of the tongue is the front end of the tongue.","zh":"「the tip of the tongue」是舌頭最前端。"},{"en":"When pronouncing /t/, many speakers place the tip of the tongue near the teeth-ridge.","zh":"發 /t/ 音時，許多說話者把舌尖放近齒齦。"},{"en":"If the tongue tip touches a different place, the sound may change.","zh":"如果舌尖接觸不同位置，聲音可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase names an important speech-organ part.","zh":"這個短語指出重要發音器官部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the teeth-ridge","meaning":"齒齦","examples":[{"en":"The tip of the tongue touches the teeth-ridge when producing certain sounds.","zh":"產生某些音時，舌尖會接觸齒齦。"},{"en":"The teeth-ridge is the hard ridge just behind the upper front teeth.","zh":"「the teeth-ridge」是上排門牙後方的硬脊。"},{"en":"English /t/, /d/, and /n/ are often made with the tongue near the teeth-ridge.","zh":"英語 /t/、/d/ 和 /n/ 常以舌頭靠近齒齦發出。"},{"en":"If the tongue moves from the teeth-ridge to the lips, the sound changes completely.","zh":"如果舌頭由齒齦移到嘴唇，聲音會完全改變。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific place of articulation.","zh":"這個短語指出特定發音部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"whereas","meaning":"然而；而","examples":[{"en":"/n/ is articulated at the teeth-ridge, whereas /m/ is articulated with the two lips.","zh":"/n/ 在齒齦發音，而 /m/ 用雙唇發音。"},{"en":"Whereas is used to contrast two facts or situations.","zh":"「whereas」用來對比兩個事實或情況。"},{"en":"Some students prefer visual notes, whereas others learn better by listening.","zh":"有些學生喜歡視覺筆記，而另一些透過聆聽學得更好。"},{"en":"If one sound uses the tongue whereas another uses the lips, their articulation differs.","zh":"如果一個音用舌頭，而另一個音用嘴唇，它們的發音方式就不同。"},{"en":"The word clearly marks a difference between two things.","zh":"這個詞清楚標示兩件事之間的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be articulated elsewhere","meaning":"在其他位置發音","examples":[{"en":"/m/ is articulated elsewhere, with the two lips.","zh":"/m/ 在其他位置發音，即用雙唇發出。"},{"en":"To be articulated elsewhere means to be produced at a different place in the mouth.","zh":"「be articulated elsewhere」意思是在口腔中不同位置產生。"},{"en":"A sound made with the tongue may change if it is articulated elsewhere with the lips.","zh":"用舌頭發出的音，如果改在雙唇等其他位置發音，就可能改變。"},{"en":"If a sound moves to a different place of articulation, listeners may hear a different phoneme.","zh":"如果聲音移到不同發音部位，聽者可能聽到不同音位。"},{"en":"The phrase compares one sound’s place of production with another.","zh":"這個短語比較一個音與另一個音的發音位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"with the two lips","meaning":"用雙唇","examples":[{"en":"The sound /m/ is articulated with the two lips.","zh":"/m/ 音用雙唇發出。"},{"en":"With the two lips means using both lips to make a sound.","zh":"「with the two lips」意思是使用上下雙唇發出聲音。"},{"en":"The sounds /p/, /b/, and /m/ are made with the two lips.","zh":"/p/、/b/ 和 /m/ 都用雙唇發出。"},{"en":"If a sound before /p/ changes to /m/, it may be because both use the lips.","zh":"如果 /p/ 前的音變成 /m/，可能因為兩者都使用嘴唇。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a bilabial way of pronouncing a sound.","zh":"這個短語描述雙唇發音方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the place of articulation","meaning":"發音部位","examples":[{"en":"The place of articulation of the nasal consonant has changed.","zh":"鼻音輔音的發音部位已經改變。"},{"en":"The place of articulation is the part of the mouth where a sound is produced.","zh":"「the place of articulation」是聲音在口腔中產生的位置。"},{"en":"The place of articulation for /p/ is the two lips, while /t/ uses the teeth-ridge area.","zh":"/p/ 的發音部位是雙唇，而 /t/ 使用齒齦附近。"},{"en":"If the place of articulation changes, the sound may become easier near a neighbouring sound.","zh":"如果發音部位改變，該音在鄰近音旁可能變得較容易發出。"},{"en":"The phrase names where a speech sound is made.","zh":"這個短語指出語音在哪裡產生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"nasal consonant","meaning":"鼻音輔音","examples":[{"en":"The nasal consonant changes to match the following sound.","zh":"鼻音輔音改變以配合後面的聲音。"},{"en":"A nasal consonant is a consonant made with air passing through the nose, such as /m/, /n/, or /ŋ/.","zh":"「nasal consonant」是氣流經鼻腔發出的輔音，例如 /m/、/n/ 或 /ŋ/。"},{"en":"In “sing”, the final sound is a nasal consonant.","zh":"在 “sing” 中，最後一個音是鼻音輔音。"},{"en":"If a nasal consonant comes before /p/, it may change toward /m/ because both use the lips.","zh":"如果鼻音輔音出現在 /p/ 前，它可能向 /m/ 改變，因為兩者都用嘴唇。"},{"en":"The phrase names a type of consonant produced through the nose.","zh":"這個短語指出經鼻腔發出的輔音類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"conform with","meaning":"與……一致；配合","examples":[{"en":"The nasal consonant changes to conform with the following plosive.","zh":"鼻音輔音改變以配合後面的爆破音。"},{"en":"To conform with something means to become similar to it or follow its pattern.","zh":"「conform with」某事，意思是變得與它相似或跟從其模式。"},{"en":"A school uniform must conform with the school’s dress code.","zh":"校服必須符合學校服裝規定。"},{"en":"If one sound conforms with the next sound, pronunciation becomes smoother.","zh":"如果一個音配合下一個音，發音就變得更順。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adjustment to match a rule, pattern, or neighbour.","zh":"這個短語描述調整以符合規則、模式或鄰近事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"following plosive","meaning":"後面的爆破音","examples":[{"en":"The nasal consonant conforms with the following plosive.","zh":"鼻音輔音與後面的爆破音一致。"},{"en":"A following plosive is a stop consonant that comes immediately after another sound.","zh":"「following plosive」是緊接在另一個音後面的塞音輔音。"},{"en":"In a word like “input”, the /p/ is the following plosive after the nasal sound.","zh":"在 “input” 這類詞中，/p/ 是鼻音後面的爆破音。"},{"en":"If a nasal sound adjusts to a following plosive, assimilation has occurred.","zh":"如果鼻音調整以配合後面的爆破音，就發生了同化。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the next stop sound in pronunciation.","zh":"這個短語指出發音中的下一個塞音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a more recent example","meaning":"較近期的例子","examples":[{"en":"A more recent example is the common pronunciation of football as foopball.","zh":"較近期的例子是把 football 常讀成 foopball。"},{"en":"A more recent example is an example from a later or more modern period.","zh":"「a more recent example」是來自較後或較現代時期的例子。"},{"en":"A more recent example of online learning is students attending live video classes.","zh":"網上學習的較近期例子是學生參加即時視像課堂。"},{"en":"If an old sound process still appears today, a recent example makes it easier to understand.","zh":"如果舊音變過程今天仍然出現，近期例子會令它更容易理解。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a newer illustration of the same idea.","zh":"這個短語引入同一想法的較新例證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the common pronunciation of","meaning":"……的常見發音","examples":[{"en":"The common pronunciation of football as foopball shows a similar process.","zh":"把 football 常讀成 foopball 顯示類似過程。"},{"en":"The common pronunciation of a word is the way many speakers usually say it.","zh":"「the common pronunciation of」某詞，是許多說話者通常讀出它的方式。"},{"en":"The common pronunciation of “often” may differ depending on whether the /t/ is pronounced.","zh":"“often” 的常見發音可能因 /t/ 是否讀出而不同。"},{"en":"If a pronunciation becomes common, it may influence how future speakers learn the word.","zh":"如果一種發音變得常見，它可能影響未來說話者如何學習該詞。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to ordinary everyday speech.","zh":"這個短語指普通日常說話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pronunciation of football as foopball","meaning":"把 football 讀成 foopball 的發音","examples":[{"en":"The pronunciation of football as foopball is an example of assimilation.","zh":"把 football 讀成 foopball 的發音是同化的例子。"},{"en":"The pronunciation of football as foopball means saying the /t/ sound more like /p/ because of the nearby /b/.","zh":"「pronunciation of football as foopball」意思是因附近 /b/ 音影響，把 /t/ 音讀得更像 /p/。"},{"en":"In fast speech, people may say football in a way that sounds closer to foopball.","zh":"在快速說話中，人們讀 football 時可能聽起來較接近 foopball。"},{"en":"If a sound changes to become more like the next sound, the word becomes easier to pronounce quickly.","zh":"如果一個音改變得更像下一個音，該詞快速發音時就更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a concrete example of assimilation in everyday speech.","zh":"這個短語提供日常說話中同化的具體例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not the only way in which","meaning":"並不是……的唯一方式","examples":[{"en":"Assimilation is not the only way in which pronunciation changes.","zh":"同化並不是發音變化的唯一方式。"},{"en":"Not the only way in which means there are other methods, causes, or processes besides this one.","zh":"「not the only way in which」意思是除了這一種之外，還有其他方法、原因或過程。"},{"en":"Reading is not the only way in which students learn vocabulary; speaking and listening also help.","zh":"閱讀並不是學生學習詞彙的唯一方式；說話和聆聽也有幫助。"},{"en":"If assimilation is only one process, linguists must also study deletion and simplification.","zh":"如果同化只是其中一個過程，語言學家也必須研究省略和簡化。"},{"en":"The phrase prevents an explanation from sounding complete when it is only partial.","zh":"這個短語防止一個解釋在只是部分時聽起來像全部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in order to increase efficiency","meaning":"為了提高效率","examples":[{"en":"Speakers may change pronunciation in order to increase efficiency.","zh":"說話者可能為了提高效率而改變發音。"},{"en":"In order to increase efficiency means for the purpose of making an action easier, faster, or less effortful.","zh":"「in order to increase efficiency」意思是為了令行動更容易、更快或更省力。"},{"en":"A student may use a timetable in order to increase efficiency during revision.","zh":"學生可能為了提高溫習效率而使用時間表。"},{"en":"If a sound is hard to produce quickly, speakers may simplify it to save effort.","zh":"如果某個音難以快速發出，說話者可能簡化它以節省力氣。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the purpose behind a change.","zh":"這個短語解釋改變背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be lost at the end of a word","meaning":"在詞尾消失","examples":[{"en":"Consonants are often lost at the end of a word.","zh":"輔音常在詞尾消失。"},{"en":"To be lost at the end of a word means a sound that was once pronounced in final position disappears.","zh":"「be lost at the end of a word」意思是一個原本在詞尾讀出的音消失。"},{"en":"A final consonant may be lost in casual speech if it is difficult to say quickly.","zh":"如果詞尾輔音快速說話時難發，它可能在口語中消失。"},{"en":"If a sound is repeatedly dropped at word endings, the pronunciation of many words may change.","zh":"如果一個音反覆在詞尾被省略，許多詞的發音可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deletion of a final sound.","zh":"這個短語描述詞尾音的脫落。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Middle English","meaning":"中古英語","examples":[{"en":"In Middle English, word-final [-n] was often lost in unstressed syllables.","zh":"在中古英語中，詞尾 [-n] 常在非重讀音節中消失。"},{"en":"Middle English is the stage of English used roughly between Old English and Early Modern English.","zh":"「Middle English」是大約位於古英語和早期現代英語之間的英語階段。"},{"en":"Students reading Chaucer meet Middle English, which looks and sounds different from modern English.","zh":"學生閱讀 Chaucer 時會遇到中古英語，它看起來和聽起來都與現代英語不同。"},{"en":"If a sound change happened in Middle English, it may explain why modern spellings look unusual.","zh":"如果某音變發生於中古英語，它可能解釋為何現代拼寫看起來不尋常。"},{"en":"The phrase names a historical period of the English language.","zh":"這個短語指出英語的一個歷史時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"word-final","meaning":"詞尾的","examples":[{"en":"Word-final [-n] was often lost in unstressed syllables.","zh":"詞尾的 [-n] 常在非重讀音節中消失。"},{"en":"Word-final means appearing at the end of a word.","zh":"「word-final」意思是出現在詞語結尾的。"},{"en":"The /t/ in “cat” is a word-final consonant.","zh":"“cat” 中的 /t/ 是詞尾輔音。"},{"en":"If word-final sounds are weak, they may disappear over time.","zh":"如果詞尾音較弱，它們可能隨時間消失。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the final position in a word.","zh":"這個短語指出詞語最後位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"unstressed syllables","meaning":"非重讀音節","examples":[{"en":"Word-final sounds were often lost in unstressed syllables.","zh":"詞尾音常在非重讀音節中消失。"},{"en":"Unstressed syllables are syllables pronounced with less force or emphasis.","zh":"「unstressed syllables」是發音力量或重點較弱的音節。"},{"en":"In the word “banana”, some syllables are weaker than others.","zh":"在 “banana” 這個詞中，有些音節比其他音節弱。"},{"en":"If a sound occurs in an unstressed syllable, speakers may reduce or drop it.","zh":"如果一個音出現在非重讀音節中，說話者可能弱化或省略它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to weakly pronounced syllables.","zh":"這個短語指發音較弱的音節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"consonant clusters","meaning":"輔音叢","examples":[{"en":"Consonant clusters are often simplified.","zh":"輔音叢常被簡化。"},{"en":"Consonant clusters are groups of two or more consonants that appear together without a vowel between them.","zh":"「consonant clusters」是兩個或以上輔音連在一起，中間沒有元音。"},{"en":"The word “street” begins with a consonant cluster: /str/.","zh":"“street” 這個詞以輔音叢 /str/ 開始。"},{"en":"If a cluster is difficult to pronounce, speakers may drop one consonant.","zh":"如果輔音叢難以發音，說話者可能省略其中一個輔音。"},{"en":"The phrase names a sequence of consonant sounds.","zh":"這個短語指出一串輔音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be simplified","meaning":"被簡化","examples":[{"en":"Consonant clusters are often simplified in pronunciation.","zh":"輔音叢在發音中常被簡化。"},{"en":"To be simplified means to be made easier, usually by removing or reducing something.","zh":"「be simplified」意思是被變得更容易，通常透過移除或減少某些部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may simplify a difficult grammar rule by using a clear example.","zh":"老師可能透過清楚例子簡化困難文法規則。"},{"en":"If a sound sequence is simplified, pronunciation becomes quicker or easier.","zh":"如果一串聲音被簡化，發音就變得更快或更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making something less complex.","zh":"這個短語描述令某事較不複雜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at one time","meaning":"曾經；一度","examples":[{"en":"At one time there was a [t] in words like castle and Christmas.","zh":"castle 和 Christmas 這類詞曾經有 [t] 音。"},{"en":"At one time means formerly or during an earlier period.","zh":"「at one time」意思是以往或在較早時期。"},{"en":"At one time, many students wrote essays entirely by hand.","zh":"曾經，許多學生完全用手寫作文。"},{"en":"If a sound existed at one time, spelling may preserve it even after pronunciation changes.","zh":"如果某音曾經存在，即使發音改變，拼寫也可能保存它。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a past situation that may no longer be true.","zh":"這個短語引入過去情況，而該情況可能已不再真實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an initial [k]","meaning":"詞首 [k] 音","examples":[{"en":"There was once an initial [k] in words like knight and know.","zh":"knight 和 know 這類詞曾經有詞首 [k] 音。"},{"en":"An initial [k] is a /k/ sound at the beginning of a word.","zh":"「an initial [k]」是在詞語開頭的 /k/ 音。"},{"en":"The word “cat” has an initial /k/ sound in modern English pronunciation.","zh":"“cat” 在現代英語發音中有詞首 /k/ 音。"},{"en":"If an initial [k] becomes silent, spelling may still show that it once existed.","zh":"如果詞首 [k] 變成不發音，拼寫可能仍顯示它曾經存在。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a beginning sound in a word.","zh":"這個短語指出詞語開頭的聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a whole syllable","meaning":"整個音節","examples":[{"en":"Sometimes a whole syllable is dropped out.","zh":"有時整個音節會被省略。"},{"en":"A whole syllable is an entire beat or sound unit in a word.","zh":"「a whole syllable」是詞語中完整的一拍或聲音單位。"},{"en":"The word “family” may be pronounced with fewer syllables in casual speech.","zh":"“family” 在口語中可能被讀成較少音節。"},{"en":"If a whole syllable is dropped, the word becomes shorter and easier to say.","zh":"如果整個音節被省略，詞語就變得更短、更容易說。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the loss of an entire syllable, not just one sound.","zh":"這個短語指整個音節消失，而不只是一個音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be dropped out","meaning":"被省略","examples":[{"en":"A whole syllable may be dropped out when two successive syllables begin with the same consonant.","zh":"當兩個連續音節以同一輔音開始時，整個音節可能被省略。"},{"en":"To be dropped out means to be omitted or left out from pronunciation.","zh":"「be dropped out」意思是在發音中被省略或漏掉。"},{"en":"In casual speech, a sound may be dropped out because the speaker is talking quickly.","zh":"在口語中，說話者講得快時，一個音可能被省略。"},{"en":"If repeated syllables are hard to say, one may be dropped out.","zh":"如果重複音節難讀，其中一個可能被省略。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a sound or syllable disappearing from speech.","zh":"這個短語描述聲音或音節從說話中消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"two successive syllables","meaning":"兩個連續音節","examples":[{"en":"Two successive syllables may begin with the same consonant.","zh":"兩個連續音節可能以同一輔音開始。"},{"en":"Two successive syllables are two syllables that come one immediately after the other.","zh":"「two successive syllables」是彼此緊接出現的兩個音節。"},{"en":"In a long word, two successive syllables may sound very similar and cause simplification.","zh":"在長詞中，兩個連續音節可能聽起來很相似，並造成簡化。"},{"en":"If two successive syllables begin alike, speakers may accidentally drop one.","zh":"如果兩個連續音節開頭相同，說話者可能意外省略其中一個。"},{"en":"The phrase describes neighbouring syllables in a word.","zh":"這個短語描述詞語中相鄰音節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"begin with the same consonant","meaning":"以同一個輔音開始","examples":[{"en":"The two syllables begin with the same consonant.","zh":"這兩個音節以同一個輔音開始。"},{"en":"To begin with the same consonant means two syllables or words start with the same consonant sound.","zh":"「begin with the same consonant」意思是兩個音節或詞以同一輔音開頭。"},{"en":"“Peter Piper” begins with repeated /p/ sounds.","zh":"“Peter Piper” 以重複 /p/ 音開始。"},{"en":"If two nearby syllables begin with the same consonant, one may be easier to drop.","zh":"如果兩個鄰近音節以同一輔音開始，其中一個可能較容易被省略。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies repeated initial consonant sounds.","zh":"這個短語指出重複的詞首輔音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"haplology","meaning":"重複音節脫落","examples":[{"en":"Haplology occurs when a syllable is dropped from a word.","zh":"當一個音節從詞中被省略時，就會出現重複音節脫落。"},{"en":"Haplology is the loss of one of two similar or repeated syllables in pronunciation.","zh":"「haplology」是發音中兩個相似或重複音節之一消失。"},{"en":"Speakers may shorten a long word when two syllables sound too alike.","zh":"當兩個音節聽起來太相似，說話者可能縮短長詞。"},{"en":"If “probably” is pronounced with fewer syllables in casual speech, it shows a similar simplification tendency.","zh":"如果 “probably” 在口語中被讀成較少音節，它顯示類似簡化傾向。"},{"en":"The word names a specific type of syllable loss.","zh":"這個詞命名一種特定音節脫落。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be pronounced as if it were","meaning":"發音像是……一樣","examples":[{"en":"Temporary is often pronounced as if it were tempory.","zh":"temporary 常被讀得像 tempory 一樣。"},{"en":"To be pronounced as if it were another form means to be said in a way that sounds like that shorter or different form.","zh":"「be pronounced as if it were」另一形式，意思是讀起來像那個較短或不同形式。"},{"en":"In fast speech, “library” may be pronounced as if it were “libry” by some speakers.","zh":"在快速說話中，有些人可能把 “library” 讀得像 “libry” 一樣。"},{"en":"If a word is pronounced as if a syllable is missing, haplology or simplification may be involved.","zh":"如果詞語讀起來像少了一個音節，可能涉及重複音節脫落或簡化。"},{"en":"The phrase compares actual spelling with spoken form.","zh":"這個短語比較實際拼寫與口語形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"complete the summary below","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates are asked to complete the summary below.","zh":"考生被要求完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary below means to fill in the missing words in the short passage that follows.","zh":"「complete the summary below」意思是填寫下方短文中的缺失詞語。"},{"en":"Students should read the summary first so they know what information to find.","zh":"學生應先閱讀摘要，這樣才知道要尋找甚麼資料。"},{"en":"If the summary follows the passage order, candidates can locate answers more easily.","zh":"如果摘要跟隨文章順序，考生可以更容易定位答案。"},{"en":"The phrase is an exam instruction for gap-filling tasks.","zh":"這個短語是填空題的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"choose no more than three words","meaning":"選擇不多於三個詞","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should choose no more than three words from the passage.","zh":"考生應從文章中選擇不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"Choose no more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"「choose no more than three words」意思是答案必須包含三個詞或更少。"},{"en":"If the answer is “sound laws”, it follows the rule because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “sound laws”，它符合規則，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"If students write four words, the answer may be wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"如果學生寫四個詞，即使意思正確，答案也可能錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit for answers.","zh":"這個短語為答案設定嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a living language","meaning":"活語言；仍在使用的語言","examples":[{"en":"The pronunciation of a living language changes over time.","zh":"活語言的發音會隨時間改變。"},{"en":"A living language is a language that people still use in everyday communication.","zh":"「a living language」是人們仍在日常溝通中使用的語言。"},{"en":"English is a living language because speakers keep creating, borrowing, and changing words.","zh":"英語是活語言，因為說話者不斷創造、借用和改變詞語。"},{"en":"If a language is living, its pronunciation and vocabulary may continue to evolve.","zh":"如果一種語言仍在使用，其發音和詞彙可能繼續演變。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts active languages with dead or no-longer-used languages.","zh":"這個短語對比活躍語言與死亡或不再使用的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"over thousands of years","meaning":"經過數千年","examples":[{"en":"The pronunciation of a living language changes over thousands of years.","zh":"活語言的發音經過數千年會改變。"},{"en":"Over thousands of years means across a very long historical period.","zh":"「over thousands of years」意思是跨越非常漫長的歷史時期。"},{"en":"Over thousands of years, farming, cities, and writing systems changed human society.","zh":"經過數千年，農業、城市和書寫系統改變了人類社會。"},{"en":"If pronunciation changes over such a long time, modern speech may sound very different from ancient speech.","zh":"如果發音經過如此漫長時間改變，現代說話可能與古代說話非常不同。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extremely long-term change.","zh":"這個短語描述極長期變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"large-scale regular changes","meaning":"大規模的規律變化","examples":[{"en":"Large-scale regular changes are usually called sound laws.","zh":"大規模的規律變化通常被稱為語音規律。"},{"en":"Large-scale regular changes are broad changes that happen repeatedly and systematically across many examples.","zh":"「large-scale regular changes」是在許多例子中反覆而系統地發生的廣泛變化。"},{"en":"If many words lose the same final sound, that may be a large-scale regular change.","zh":"如果許多詞都失去同一詞尾音，那可能是大規模的規律變化。"},{"en":"Such changes allow linguists to identify patterns rather than isolated accidents.","zh":"這類變化讓語言學家識別模式，而不是孤立意外。"},{"en":"The phrase describes systematic change across many words or sounds.","zh":"這個短語描述跨越許多詞或聲音的系統性變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"contribute to","meaning":"導致；促成","examples":[{"en":"Three factors contribute to these changes.","zh":"三個因素促成這些變化。"},{"en":"To contribute to something means to help cause it or add to its development.","zh":"「contribute to」某事，意思是幫助造成它或推動其發展。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can contribute to poor concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致課堂專注力差。"},{"en":"If imitation, fashion, and ease all contribute to sound change, no single cause is enough.","zh":"如果模仿、潮流和省力都促成音變，單一原因就不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one factor helping to produce a result.","zh":"這個短語描述其中一個因素幫助產生結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"an element of","meaning":"……的成分","examples":[{"en":"Imitation involves an element of fashion.","zh":"模仿涉及潮流的成分。"},{"en":"An element of something is one part or feature of it.","zh":"「an element of」某事，是其中一部分或特徵。"},{"en":"A good lesson includes an element of fun so students stay engaged.","zh":"好課堂包含趣味成分，讓學生保持投入。"},{"en":"If imitation contains an element of fashion, people copy speech partly because it seems stylish or prestigious.","zh":"如果模仿包含潮流成分，人們模仿說話部分是因為它看起來時尚或有威望。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies one component within a larger process.","zh":"這個短語指出較大過程中的其中一個組成部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"adult speech","meaning":"成人說話方式","examples":[{"en":"Children’s imitations of adult speech may be imperfect.","zh":"兒童對成人說話方式的模仿可能不完美。"},{"en":"Adult speech is the way grown people pronounce words and use language.","zh":"「adult speech」是成年人發音和使用語言的方式。"},{"en":"Children learn language partly by listening to adult speech at home and school.","zh":"兒童部分透過在家中和學校聆聽成人說話來學習語言。"},{"en":"If children copy adult speech imperfectly, small differences may enter the next generation.","zh":"如果兒童不完美地模仿成人說話方式，小差異可能進入下一代。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to adult models of speaking.","zh":"這個短語指成人的說話模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"systematic ones","meaning":"系統性的情況","examples":[{"en":"Systematic ones may contribute to language change.","zh":"系統性的情況可能促成語言變化。"},{"en":"Systematic ones means examples that follow a regular pattern rather than happening randomly.","zh":"「systematic ones」意思是遵循規律模式、而不是隨機發生的例子。"},{"en":"A teacher ignores one random spelling error but studies systematic ones that many students repeat.","zh":"老師可能不理會一個隨機拼寫錯誤，但會研究許多學生重複犯的系統性錯誤。"},{"en":"If imitation errors are systematic, they can spread and become part of the language.","zh":"如果模仿錯誤是系統性的，它們可能傳播並成為語言的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to patterned cases, not random cases.","zh":"這個短語回指有模式的情況，而不是隨機情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reflect the principle of ease","meaning":"反映省力原則","examples":[{"en":"Random variations in pronunciation may reflect the principle of ease.","zh":"發音中的隨機變異可能反映省力原則。"},{"en":"To reflect the principle of ease means to show the tendency to use less effort in speaking.","zh":"「reflect the principle of ease」意思是顯示說話時傾向減少用力。"},{"en":"Saying “gonna” instead of “going to” may reflect the principle of ease in casual speech.","zh":"在口語中把 “going to” 說成 “gonna” 可能反映省力原則。"},{"en":"If a pronunciation becomes shorter or smoother, it may reflect speakers’ wish to save effort.","zh":"如果發音變得更短或更順，它可能反映說話者想省力。"},{"en":"The phrase connects sound change with easier articulation.","zh":"這個短語把音變與較容易發音連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Some statements agree with the information given in the passage.","zh":"有些陳述與文章所給資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"「agree with the information given」意思是與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the passage says sound laws are not universal, a statement saying the same thing agrees with the information given.","zh":"如果文章說語音規律不是普遍的，而陳述說同樣意思，就與所給資料一致。"},{"en":"If a statement adds something not mentioned, it may not agree or contradict clearly.","zh":"如果陳述加入文中沒有提及的內容，它未必清楚一致或矛盾。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個短語用於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement is false if it contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"如果陳述與文章資料相矛盾，它就是錯的。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"「contradict the information」意思是說出與文章相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says a sound was lost but the statement says it remained, the statement contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說某音消失了，而陳述說它保留了，該陳述就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"If an answer contradicts evidence, it should be marked false.","zh":"如果答案與證據矛盾，就應判為 false。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct conflict with the text.","zh":"這個短語描述與文本直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"Write “NOT GIVEN” if there is no information on this in the passage.","zh":"如果文章沒有這方面的資料，就寫 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not say enough to decide.","zh":"「there is no information on this」意思是文章沒有提供足夠資料讓人判斷。"},{"en":"If a passage discusses pronunciation but not the writer’s age, there is no information on the writer’s age.","zh":"如果文章討論發音但沒有提及作者年齡，就沒有關於作者年齡的資料。"},{"en":"If evidence is missing, students should not guess from general knowledge.","zh":"如果證據缺失，學生不應憑常識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the NOT GIVEN answer type.","zh":"這個短語解釋 NOT GIVEN 答案類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"determine the pronunciation of","meaning":"確定……的發音","examples":[{"en":"Modern people try to determine the pronunciation of words in an earlier age.","zh":"現代人嘗試確定早期時代詞語的發音。"},{"en":"To determine the pronunciation of something means to find out how it was or should be spoken.","zh":"「determine the pronunciation of」某物，意思是找出它過去或應該如何發音。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a dictionary to determine the pronunciation of a difficult word.","zh":"老師可能使用字典確定困難詞的發音。"},{"en":"If there are no recordings, researchers determine old pronunciation from spelling, rhymes, and descriptions.","zh":"如果沒有錄音，研究人員會從拼寫、押韻和描述確定舊發音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes working out how words sound.","zh":"這個短語描述推斷詞語如何發聲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be related to changes in","meaning":"與……的變化有關","examples":[{"en":"A change in pronunciation may be related to changes in social status.","zh":"發音變化可能與社會地位的變化有關。"},{"en":"To be related to changes in something means to be connected with shifts in that area.","zh":"「be related to changes in」某事，意思是與該方面的轉變有關。"},{"en":"Falling school attendance may be related to changes in transport or family routines.","zh":"學校出席率下降可能與交通或家庭日常的變化有關。"},{"en":"If a social group rises in status, its speech may become more prestigious.","zh":"如果一個社會群體地位上升，其說話方式可能變得更有威望。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a connection between two kinds of change.","zh":"這個短語描述兩類變化之間的關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"casual inaccuracies in pronunciation","meaning":"隨意的發音誤差","examples":[{"en":"Casual inaccuracies in pronunciation may not influence language change.","zh":"隨意的發音誤差可能不會影響語言變化。"},{"en":"Casual inaccuracies in pronunciation are small, accidental, unsystematic mistakes in speech.","zh":"「casual inaccuracies in pronunciation」是說話中小型、偶然、非系統性的錯誤。"},{"en":"A student may mispronounce one word once because they are tired; that is a casual inaccuracy.","zh":"學生可能因疲倦而一次讀錯某詞；那就是隨意誤差。"},{"en":"If mistakes are casual and random, they usually do not spread through the language.","zh":"如果錯誤是隨意且隨機的，它們通常不會在語言中傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts occasional errors with systematic sound change.","zh":"這個短語對比偶然錯誤與系統性音變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have a major influence on","meaning":"對……有重大影響","examples":[{"en":"Random pronunciation errors may not have a major influence on language change.","zh":"隨機發音錯誤可能不會對語言變化有重大影響。"},{"en":"To have a major influence on something means to affect it strongly.","zh":"「have a major influence on」某事，意思是強烈影響它。"},{"en":"A good teacher can have a major influence on a student’s confidence.","zh":"好老師可以對學生信心有重大影響。"},{"en":"If errors are random, they may have little influence even if they happen often.","zh":"如果錯誤是隨機的，即使常發生，也可能影響很小。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong impact.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be pronounced more easily than","meaning":"比……更容易發音","examples":[{"en":"Scant can be pronounced more easily than skamt.","zh":"scant 比 skamt 更容易發音。"},{"en":"To be pronounced more easily than another form means to require less effort or simpler mouth movement.","zh":"「be pronounced more easily than」另一形式，意思是需要較少力氣或較簡單口腔動作。"},{"en":"A short nickname may be pronounced more easily than a long formal name.","zh":"短暱稱可能比正式長名更容易發音。"},{"en":"If two sounds are made in the same place, the word may be easier to say quickly.","zh":"如果兩個音在同一位置發出，該詞快速說出時可能較容易。"},{"en":"The phrase compares ease of articulation.","zh":"這個短語比較發音難易。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"silent [g]","meaning":"不發音的 [g]","examples":[{"en":"The word gnat contains a silent [g] in its spelling.","zh":"gnat 這個詞的拼寫中包含不發音的 [g]。"},{"en":"A silent [g] is the letter g written in a word but not pronounced.","zh":"「silent [g]」是寫在詞中但不讀出的字母 g。"},{"en":"The word “gnome” also has a silent g at the beginning.","zh":"“gnome” 這個詞開頭也有不發音的 g。"},{"en":"If a silent letter remains in spelling, it may show an older pronunciation.","zh":"如果不發音字母保留在拼寫中，它可能顯示較舊發音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a written letter that has no sound in modern speech.","zh":"這個短語描述在現代說話中沒有聲音的書寫字母。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"eventually disappear from","meaning":"最終從……消失","examples":[{"en":"A silent letter may eventually disappear from spelling.","zh":"不發音字母可能最終從拼寫中消失。"},{"en":"To eventually disappear from something means to be removed or lost after a period of time.","zh":"「eventually disappear from」某事，意思是在一段時間後被移除或消失。"},{"en":"A school rule may eventually disappear from practice if nobody follows it anymore.","zh":"如果沒有人再遵守某校規，它可能最終從實際做法中消失。"},{"en":"If a sound is not pronounced for centuries, its letter may later disappear from spelling.","zh":"如果一個音數百年都不讀，其字母之後可能從拼寫中消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual loss from a system.","zh":"這個短語描述從一個系統中逐漸失去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reflect its full spelling","meaning":"反映其完整拼寫","examples":[{"en":"The pronunciation of temporary does not always reflect its full spelling.","zh":"temporary 的發音不一定反映其完整拼寫。"},{"en":"To reflect its full spelling means to pronounce all the sounds suggested by the written form.","zh":"「reflect its full spelling」意思是讀出書寫形式所暗示的所有聲音。"},{"en":"The word “Wednesday” is not pronounced in a way that fully reflects its spelling.","zh":"“Wednesday” 的發音並不完全反映其拼寫。"},{"en":"If speakers drop a syllable, pronunciation no longer matches the complete written form.","zh":"如果說話者省略一個音節，發音就不再符合完整書寫形式。"},{"en":"The phrase compares speech with spelling.","zh":"這個短語比較說話與拼寫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"match each statement with","meaning":"將每個陳述與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match each statement with the correct sentence.","zh":"考生將每個陳述與正確句子配對。"},{"en":"To match each statement with something means to connect every statement to the item that best fits it.","zh":"「match each statement with」某事，意思是把每個陳述連接到最合適的項目。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may match each statement with the paragraph containing the evidence.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能把每個陳述與包含證據的段落配對。"},{"en":"If candidates understand the meaning of each statement, they can find the correct match faster.","zh":"如果考生理解每個陳述的意思，就能更快找到正確配對。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a matching task.","zh":"這個短語描述配對任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the correct sentence","meaning":"正確句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct sentence from the list.","zh":"考生從列表中選擇正確句子。"},{"en":"The correct sentence is the sentence that accurately matches the meaning or evidence required.","zh":"「the correct sentence」是準確符合所需意思或證據的句子。"},{"en":"If a question describes assimilation, the correct sentence should mention one sound changing because of a neighbour.","zh":"如果題目描述同化，正確句子應提到一個音因鄰近音而改變。"},{"en":"Choosing the wrong sentence usually means the evidence has been misunderstood.","zh":"選錯句子通常代表證據被誤解。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the exact answer in a sentence-matching task.","zh":"這個短語指出句子配對題中的確切答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as a consequence","meaning":"因此；結果","examples":[{"en":"As a consequence, one sound may be pronounced differently.","zh":"因此，一個音可能被讀得不同。"},{"en":"As a consequence means as a result of what has just been described.","zh":"「as a consequence」意思是作為剛才所描述事情的結果。"},{"en":"The school bus arrived late; as a consequence, several students missed the first lesson.","zh":"校巴遲到；結果，幾名學生錯過第一課。"},{"en":"If the tongue moves to an easier position, a sound may change as a consequence.","zh":"如果舌頭移到較容易的位置，一個音可能因此改變。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a result.","zh":"這個短語引入結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be pronounced as","meaning":"被讀成……","examples":[{"en":"In one context, ‘b’ may be pronounced as ‘p’.","zh":"在一個語境中，‘b’ 可能被讀成 ‘p’。"},{"en":"To be pronounced as another sound means to be spoken so that it sounds like that sound.","zh":"「be pronounced as」另一個音，意思是說出來時聽起來像該音。"},{"en":"In some accents, one vowel may be pronounced as a different vowel.","zh":"在某些口音中，一個元音可能被讀成另一個元音。"},{"en":"If a letter is pronounced as another sound, spelling and speech no longer match simply.","zh":"如果一個字母被讀成另一個音，拼寫和說話就不再簡單一致。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how a written form is actually spoken.","zh":"這個短語描述書寫形式實際如何被讀出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the omission of","meaning":"……的省略","examples":[{"en":"The omission of ‘t’ from Christmas is an example of pronunciation simplification.","zh":"Christmas 中 ‘t’ 的省略是發音簡化的例子。"},{"en":"The omission of something means leaving it out or not including it.","zh":"「the omission of」某事，意思是把它漏掉或不包括它。"},{"en":"The omission of a student’s name from the list may cause confusion on registration day.","zh":"如果學生姓名從名單中省略，登記日可能造成混亂。"},{"en":"If a difficult consonant is omitted, the word may become easier to pronounce.","zh":"如果困難輔音被省略，詞語可能更容易發音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something being removed or left unspoken.","zh":"這個短語描述某物被移除或沒有被讀出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 34 - Mechanisms of Linguistic Change.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 35":[{"front":"honeybees in trouble","meaning":"陷入困境的蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"The passage is about honeybees in trouble and the search for alternative pollinators.","zh":"文章是關於陷入困境的蜜蜂，以及尋找替代授粉者。"},{"en":"Honeybees in trouble means honeybees are facing serious problems that threaten their survival or usefulness.","zh":"陷入困境的蜜蜂，指蜜蜂正面對威脅其生存或用途的嚴重問題。"},{"en":"A farmer may worry about honeybees in trouble if fewer bees visit the orchard in spring.","zh":"如果春天較少蜜蜂到訪果園，農民可能會擔心蜜蜂陷入困境。"},{"en":"If honeybees are in trouble, crops that need pollination may produce less fruit.","zh":"如果蜜蜂陷入困境，需要授粉的農作物可能結出較少果實。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a problem that affects both insects and agriculture.","zh":"這個短語暗示一個同時影響昆蟲和農業的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"native pollinators","meaning":"本土授粉者","examples":[{"en":"Native pollinators may be able to fill part of the gap left by declining honeybees.","zh":"本土授粉者或許能填補蜜蜂減少後留下的部分空缺。"},{"en":"Native pollinators are local animals or insects that naturally pollinate plants in a region.","zh":"本土授粉者，是某地區自然為植物授粉的本地動物或昆蟲。"},{"en":"Butterflies, wild bees, flies, and beetles can be native pollinators in some places.","zh":"在某些地方，蝴蝶、野生蜜蜂、蒼蠅和甲蟲都可以是本土授粉者。"},{"en":"If native pollinators are protected, farms may depend less on imported honeybees.","zh":"如果本土授粉者受到保護，農場可能較少依賴外來蜜蜂。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to local species that help plants reproduce.","zh":"這個短語指幫助植物繁殖的本地物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fill the gap","meaning":"填補空缺","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are asking whether native pollinators can fill the gap.","zh":"研究人員正在問本土授粉者是否能填補空缺。"},{"en":"To fill the gap means to provide what is missing or replace what has been lost.","zh":"填補空缺，指提供缺少的東西，或取代已失去的角色。"},{"en":"If a teacher is absent, another teacher may fill the gap for the lesson.","zh":"如果老師缺席，另一位老師可能會填補該課堂的空缺。"},{"en":"If honeybees decline, other insects may fill the gap by pollinating some crops.","zh":"如果蜜蜂減少，其他昆蟲可能透過為部分農作物授粉來填補空缺。"},{"en":"The phrase describes solving a shortage or missing role.","zh":"這個短語描述解決短缺或缺失角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ominous headlines","meaning":"不祥的新聞標題","examples":[{"en":"Ominous headlines have described a mysterious problem affecting honeybees.","zh":"不祥的新聞標題描述了一個影響蜜蜂的神秘問題。"},{"en":"Ominous headlines are news titles that sound worrying and suggest something bad may happen.","zh":"不祥的新聞標題，是聽起來令人擔心並暗示壞事可能發生的新聞標題。"},{"en":"A headline about empty reservoirs before summer can feel ominous.","zh":"關於夏季前水庫空置的標題，可能令人感到不祥。"},{"en":"If headlines are ominous, readers may expect danger, crisis, or serious loss.","zh":"如果標題不祥，讀者可能預期危險、危機或嚴重損失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a threatening tone in the news.","zh":"這個短語描述新聞中的威脅性語氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a mysterious ailment","meaning":"神秘疾病","examples":[{"en":"Colony collapse disorder is described as a mysterious ailment.","zh":"蜂群崩壞失調症被描述為一種神秘疾病。"},{"en":"A mysterious ailment is an illness or disorder whose cause is not clearly understood.","zh":"神秘疾病，是原因未被清楚理解的疾病或失調。"},{"en":"Doctors may investigate a mysterious ailment when patients share symptoms but tests are unclear.","zh":"當病人有相似症狀但測試不清楚，醫生可能調查神秘疾病。"},{"en":"If an ailment is mysterious, scientists need time to identify its causes.","zh":"如果疾病很神秘，科學家需要時間找出成因。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests illness plus uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語暗示疾病和不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"colony collapse disorder","meaning":"蜂群崩壞失調症","examples":[{"en":"Colony collapse disorder is wiping out many honeybee colonies.","zh":"蜂群崩壞失調症正在令許多蜜蜂蜂群大量死亡。"},{"en":"Colony collapse disorder is a serious problem in which worker bees disappear from a hive.","zh":"蜂群崩壞失調症，是工蜂從蜂箱中消失的嚴重問題。"},{"en":"A beekeeper may suspect colony collapse disorder when a hive suddenly becomes almost empty.","zh":"當蜂箱突然幾乎空了，養蜂人可能懷疑是蜂群崩壞失調症。"},{"en":"If colony collapse disorder spreads, farmers may struggle to find enough bees for pollination.","zh":"如果蜂群崩壞失調症蔓延，農民可能難以找到足夠蜜蜂授粉。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific honeybee crisis.","zh":"這個短語命名一場特定的蜜蜂危機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"wipe out","meaning":"消滅；令……大量死亡","examples":[{"en":"A serious disorder is wiping out honeybees that pollinate many crops.","zh":"一種嚴重失調症正在令為多種農作物授粉的蜜蜂大量死亡。"},{"en":"To wipe out something means to destroy it completely or kill a very large number of it.","zh":"消滅某物，指完全摧毀它，或令其大量死亡。"},{"en":"A flood can wipe out a small village if houses are built too close to the river.","zh":"如果房屋建得太近河邊，洪水可能摧毀一個小村莊。"},{"en":"If disease wipes out bees, farms may lose important pollination services.","zh":"如果疾病令蜜蜂大量死亡，農場可能失去重要授粉服務。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests severe destruction, not a small decline.","zh":"這個短語暗示嚴重破壞，而不是小幅下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pollinate many crops","meaning":"為多種農作物授粉","examples":[{"en":"Honeybees pollinate many crops in modern agriculture.","zh":"蜜蜂在現代農業中為多種農作物授粉。"},{"en":"To pollinate many crops means to carry pollen between flowers so different plants can produce fruit or seeds.","zh":"為多種農作物授粉，指在花之間傳送花粉，使不同植物能結果或產生種子。"},{"en":"Bees pollinate apples, almonds, melons, and many other crops.","zh":"蜜蜂為蘋果、杏仁、瓜類和許多其他農作物授粉。"},{"en":"If insects do not pollinate crops, farmers may harvest less food.","zh":"如果昆蟲不為農作物授粉，農民可能收穫較少食物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an important biological service for farming.","zh":"這個短語描述農業中的重要生物服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"without honeybees","meaning":"沒有蜜蜂的話","examples":[{"en":"Without honeybees, some people fear that food production would suffer.","zh":"沒有蜜蜂的話，有些人擔心食物生產會受損。"},{"en":"Without honeybees means if honeybees were absent or unavailable.","zh":"沒有蜜蜂的話，指如果蜜蜂不存在或無法使用。"},{"en":"Without buses, many students would have difficulty getting to school.","zh":"沒有巴士的話，許多學生上學會有困難。"},{"en":"Without honeybees, farmers may need other pollinators or costly manual methods.","zh":"沒有蜜蜂的話，農民可能需要其他授粉者或昂貴的人手方法。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a situation where an important support is missing.","zh":"這個短語引入重要支援缺失的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the story goes","meaning":"據說；人們常說","examples":[{"en":"Without honeybees, the story goes, fields will be sterile and food will be scarce.","zh":"人們常說，沒有蜜蜂的話，田地將無法結果，食物也會短缺。"},{"en":"The story goes means people commonly say or repeat a particular account.","zh":"據說或人們常說，指人們普遍說或重複某種說法。"},{"en":"The story goes that the old building is haunted, although no one has proof.","zh":"據說那座舊建築鬧鬼，雖然沒有人有證據。"},{"en":"If a writer uses this phrase, they may be questioning a popular version of events.","zh":"如果作者使用這個短語，可能是在質疑一種流行說法。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a widely repeated claim, not necessarily proven fact.","zh":"這個短語暗示被廣泛重複的主張，而不一定是已證實事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fields will be sterile","meaning":"田地將無法結果","examples":[{"en":"Some reports warn that fields will be sterile without enough pollinators.","zh":"一些報道警告，如果沒有足夠授粉者，田地將無法結果。"},{"en":"Fields will be sterile means crops may not produce fruit or seeds because fertilisation fails.","zh":"田地將無法結果，指因受精失敗，農作物可能不能結出果實或種子。"},{"en":"A garden may seem sterile if flowers bloom but never turn into fruit.","zh":"如果花開了卻從不結果，花園可能看似無法結果。"},{"en":"If pollinators disappear, some fields may produce leaves and flowers but little harvest.","zh":"如果授粉者消失，一些田地可能長出葉和花，但幾乎沒有收成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes farmland that cannot reproduce crops successfully.","zh":"這個短語描述不能成功繁殖農作物的農地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"economies will collapse","meaning":"經濟將會崩潰","examples":[{"en":"Some accounts suggest that economies will collapse if honeybees disappear.","zh":"一些說法暗示，如果蜜蜂消失，經濟將會崩潰。"},{"en":"Economies will collapse means financial systems, businesses, and jobs may fail on a large scale.","zh":"經濟將會崩潰，指金融系統、企業和職位可能大規模失敗。"},{"en":"A town’s economy may collapse if its only major factory closes suddenly.","zh":"如果一個城鎮唯一的大型工廠突然關閉，其經濟可能崩潰。"},{"en":"If crop production falls sharply, farmers, food companies, and shops may all suffer.","zh":"如果農作物生產大幅下降，農民、食品公司和商店都可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an extreme economic breakdown.","zh":"這個短語描述極端的經濟瓦解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"food will be scarce","meaning":"食物將會短缺","examples":[{"en":"Food may become scarce if crop pollination fails.","zh":"如果農作物授粉失敗，食物可能變得短缺。"},{"en":"Food will be scarce means there will not be enough food available for people.","zh":"食物將會短缺，指沒有足夠食物供人使用。"},{"en":"After a typhoon, fresh vegetables may be scarce in local markets.","zh":"颱風後，本地街市的新鮮蔬菜可能短缺。"},{"en":"If pollination fails across many farms, some fruits and nuts may become harder to find.","zh":"如果許多農場授粉失敗，某些水果和堅果可能更難找到。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shortage, not just higher prices.","zh":"這個短語描述短缺，而不只是價格上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what few accounts acknowledge","meaning":"很少報道承認的是","examples":[{"en":"What few accounts acknowledge is that the current system is not entirely natural.","zh":"很少報道承認的是，目前的系統並不完全自然。"},{"en":"What few accounts acknowledge means something important that only a small number of reports admit.","zh":"很少報道承認的是，指只有少數報道承認的重要事情。"},{"en":"What few school reports acknowledge is that homework stress often affects family life too.","zh":"很少學校報告承認的是，功課壓力也常影響家庭生活。"},{"en":"If few accounts acknowledge a fact, readers may receive an incomplete picture.","zh":"如果很少報道承認某事實，讀者可能得到不完整圖像。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an overlooked truth.","zh":"這個短語引入被忽略的真相。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what is at risk","meaning":"面臨風險的事物","examples":[{"en":"What is at risk is not itself a natural state of affairs.","zh":"面臨風險的事物本身並不是自然狀態。"},{"en":"What is at risk means the thing that may be harmed, lost, or damaged.","zh":"面臨風險的事物，指可能受害、失去或受損的東西。"},{"en":"If a library closes, what is at risk is not only books but also a quiet place to study.","zh":"如果圖書館關閉，面臨風險的不只是書，還有安靜溫習的地方。"},{"en":"If pollination systems fail, what is at risk includes food supply and farm income.","zh":"如果授粉系統失敗，面臨風險的包括食物供應和農場收入。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what could be lost.","zh":"這個短語指出可能失去甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a natural state of affairs","meaning":"自然狀態；自然情況","examples":[{"en":"The dependence on honeybees is not a natural state of affairs.","zh":"對蜜蜂的依賴並不是自然狀態。"},{"en":"A natural state of affairs is a situation that exists naturally without heavy human organisation.","zh":"自然狀態，是沒有大量人為組織下自然存在的情況。"},{"en":"A forest with many wild insects is closer to a natural state of affairs than a single-crop field.","zh":"有許多野生昆蟲的森林，比單一作物田地更接近自然狀態。"},{"en":"If farming depends on transported hives, the system is industrial rather than purely natural.","zh":"如果農業依賴運送蜂箱，該系統就是工業化而非純自然。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how things would be without artificial control.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有人工控制時事情的樣子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"for one thing","meaning":"首先；其中一點是","examples":[{"en":"For one thing, honeybees are not native to the United States.","zh":"首先，蜜蜂並不是美國本土物種。"},{"en":"For one thing introduces one reason or example among several possible points.","zh":"首先或其中一點是，用來引入幾個可能觀點中的一個理由或例子。"},{"en":"I prefer studying in the library; for one thing, it is much quieter than home.","zh":"我較喜歡在圖書館溫習；其中一點是，那裡比家中安靜得多。"},{"en":"If a writer says “for one thing,” more supporting reasons may follow.","zh":"如果作者說 “for one thing”，之後可能還有更多支持理由。"},{"en":"The phrase helps begin an explanation or argument.","zh":"這個短語幫助開始解釋或論證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"first reported","meaning":"首次被報告","examples":[{"en":"Colony collapse disorder was first reported in the United States.","zh":"蜂群崩壞失調症首次在美國被報告。"},{"en":"First reported means officially noticed or described for the first time.","zh":"首次被報告，指第一次被正式注意或描述。"},{"en":"A new illness may be first reported in a hospital before scientists study it widely.","zh":"新疾病可能先在醫院首次被報告，之後科學家才廣泛研究。"},{"en":"If a disorder is first reported in one country, it may later be found elsewhere.","zh":"如果一種失調症首次在一個國家被報告，日後可能在其他地方也被發現。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the earliest known report.","zh":"這個短語標示最早已知報告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have its greatest impacts","meaning":"造成最大影響","examples":[{"en":"Colony collapse disorder has had its greatest impacts in the United States.","zh":"蜂群崩壞失調症在美國造成最大影響。"},{"en":"To have its greatest impacts somewhere means to cause the strongest effects there.","zh":"在某地造成最大影響，指在那裡造成最強烈效果。"},{"en":"A storm may have its greatest impacts in low-lying coastal towns.","zh":"風暴可能在低窪沿岸城鎮造成最大影響。"},{"en":"If a bee disorder has its greatest impacts in one country, that country’s farms may suffer most.","zh":"如果蜜蜂失調症在某國造成最大影響，該國農場可能受害最深。"},{"en":"The phrase compares where effects are strongest.","zh":"這個短語比較影響在哪裡最強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a native species","meaning":"本土物種","examples":[{"en":"Honeybees are not a native species in the United States.","zh":"蜜蜂在美國並不是本土物種。"},{"en":"A native species is a plant or animal that naturally belongs to a place.","zh":"本土物種，是自然屬於某地的植物或動物。"},{"en":"A local wildflower can be a native species if it grew there before people introduced it.","zh":"如果本地野花在人們引入前已在當地生長，它可以是本土物種。"},{"en":"If a species is not native, it may have been brought by humans from elsewhere.","zh":"如果一個物種不是本土物種，它可能由人類從其他地方帶來。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies natural origin in a region.","zh":"這個短語指出某地區的自然來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pollination in modern agriculture","meaning":"現代農業中的授粉","examples":[{"en":"Pollination in modern agriculture is organised like an industry.","zh":"現代農業中的授粉像產業一樣被組織。"},{"en":"Pollination in modern agriculture means the managed movement of pollen to help crops produce food.","zh":"現代農業中的授粉，指受管理地傳送花粉，以幫助農作物生產食物。"},{"en":"Farmers may rent beehives as part of pollination in modern agriculture.","zh":"農民可能租用蜂箱作為現代農業授粉的一部分。"},{"en":"If pollination is industrially organised, farms may depend on scheduled bee transport.","zh":"如果授粉以工業方式組織，農場可能依賴按時間表運送蜜蜂。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a natural process with modern farming systems.","zh":"這個短語把自然過程與現代農業系統連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not alchemy but industry","meaning":"不是煉金術，而是產業","examples":[{"en":"Pollination in modern agriculture is not alchemy but industry.","zh":"現代農業中的授粉不是煉金術，而是產業。"},{"en":"Not alchemy but industry means the process is not magical or mysterious, but organised and commercial.","zh":"不是煉金術，而是產業，指過程不是神奇或神秘，而是有組織和商業化。"},{"en":"Modern food delivery is not luck but industry, with drivers, apps, warehouses, and schedules.","zh":"現代送餐不是靠運氣，而是產業，有司機、應用程式、倉庫和時間表。"},{"en":"If pollination is an industry, bees become part of a managed production system.","zh":"如果授粉是一個產業，蜜蜂就成為受管理生產系統的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts mystery with organised business.","zh":"這個短語把神秘與有組織商業作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the total number of hives","meaning":"蜂箱總數","examples":[{"en":"The total number of hives involved in US crop pollination is very large.","zh":"參與美國農作物授粉的蜂箱總數非常龐大。"},{"en":"The total number of hives means all the beehives counted together.","zh":"蜂箱總數，指把所有蜂箱合計起來的數目。"},{"en":"A beekeeper may record the total number of hives before moving them to farms.","zh":"養蜂人可能在把蜂箱運往農場前記錄蜂箱總數。"},{"en":"If the total number of hives falls, fewer bees may be available for pollination.","zh":"如果蜂箱總數下降，可供授粉的蜜蜂可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a combined count of beehives.","zh":"這個短語給出蜂箱的合計數目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be involved in","meaning":"參與；涉及","examples":[{"en":"Millions of hives are involved in the US pollination industry.","zh":"數以百萬計的蜂箱參與美國授粉產業。"},{"en":"To be involved in something means to take part in it or be connected with it.","zh":"參與某事或涉及某事，指加入其中或與它有關。"},{"en":"Parents may be involved in a school charity event by helping sell tickets.","zh":"家長可能透過幫忙售票參與學校慈善活動。"},{"en":"If many hives are involved in crop pollination, the process is large and organised.","zh":"如果許多蜂箱參與農作物授粉，該過程就是龐大而有組織的。"},{"en":"The phrase shows participation or connection.","zh":"這個短語顯示參與或關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the pollination industry","meaning":"授粉產業","examples":[{"en":"The US pollination industry uses millions of honeybee hives.","zh":"美國授粉產業使用數以百萬計的蜜蜂蜂箱。"},{"en":"The pollination industry is the business of providing pollinators to help crops reproduce.","zh":"授粉產業，是提供授粉者幫助農作物繁殖的商業活動。"},{"en":"A farmer may pay the pollination industry to bring bees during flowering season.","zh":"農民可能在開花季節付款請授粉產業帶來蜜蜂。"},{"en":"If the pollination industry is disrupted, crop production may become less reliable.","zh":"如果授粉產業被擾亂，農作物生產可能變得較不可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase treats pollination as a commercial service.","zh":"這個短語把授粉視為商業服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"somewhere between","meaning":"大約介乎……之間","examples":[{"en":"The number of hives has been somewhere between 2.5 million and 3 million.","zh":"蜂箱數目大約介乎二百五十萬至三百萬之間。"},{"en":"Somewhere between two numbers means approximately within that range.","zh":"大約介乎兩個數字之間，指大致在該範圍內。"},{"en":"The trip may take somewhere between thirty and forty minutes.","zh":"旅程可能需時大約三十至四十分鐘之間。"},{"en":"If hive numbers are somewhere between two figures, the exact count may vary by year.","zh":"如果蜂箱數目介乎兩個數字之間，準確數目可能按年份而變。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate range.","zh":"這個短語給出約略範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in recent years","meaning":"近年來","examples":[{"en":"The number of hives has remained high in recent years.","zh":"近年來，蜂箱數目一直維持高位。"},{"en":"In recent years means during the last few years or relatively near the present.","zh":"近年來，指過去幾年或相對接近現在的時期。"},{"en":"In recent years, more students have used online dictionaries.","zh":"近年來，更多學生使用網上字典。"},{"en":"If a problem has grown in recent years, it may need updated research.","zh":"如果問題近年來變大，就可能需要最新研究。"},{"en":"The phrase places a trend close to the present time.","zh":"這個短語把趨勢放在接近現時的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"large quantities of","meaning":"大量的","examples":[{"en":"American farmers began using large quantities of insecticides.","zh":"美國農民開始使用大量殺蟲劑。"},{"en":"Large quantities of something means a great amount of it.","zh":"大量的某物，指數量很多。"},{"en":"A school canteen may prepare large quantities of rice for lunch.","zh":"學校飯堂可能為午餐準備大量米飯。"},{"en":"If farms use large quantities of chemicals, insects may be harmed along with pests.","zh":"如果農場使用大量化學品，昆蟲可能和害蟲一起受害。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses amount or scale.","zh":"這個短語強調數量或規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"organophosphate insecticides","meaning":"有機磷殺蟲劑","examples":[{"en":"Organophosphate insecticides can harm native bees.","zh":"有機磷殺蟲劑可以傷害本土蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Organophosphate insecticides are chemical pesticides used to kill insects.","zh":"有機磷殺蟲劑，是用來殺死昆蟲的化學農藥。"},{"en":"Farmers may use organophosphate insecticides to control pests on crops.","zh":"農民可能使用有機磷殺蟲劑控制農作物害蟲。"},{"en":"If these insecticides kill pollinators too, crop production can suffer indirectly.","zh":"如果這些殺蟲劑也殺死授粉者，農作物生產會間接受損。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a specific class of agricultural chemicals.","zh":"這個短語指一類特定農業化學品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"large-scale crop monocultures","meaning":"大規模單一作物種植","examples":[{"en":"Large-scale crop monocultures have changed the agricultural landscape.","zh":"大規模單一作物種植改變了農業景觀。"},{"en":"Large-scale crop monocultures are huge farms or areas growing only one crop.","zh":"大規模單一作物種植，是只種植一種農作物的大型農場或地區。"},{"en":"A valley planted only with corn for miles is a large-scale crop monoculture.","zh":"一個山谷連綿數英里都只種粟米，就是大規模單一作物種植。"},{"en":"If farms become monocultures, wild insects may lose varied food and habitat.","zh":"如果農場變成單一作物種植，野生昆蟲可能失去多樣食物和棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes farming that is big but biologically simple.","zh":"這個短語描述規模大但生物上簡單的農業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"clean-farming practices","meaning":"清耕做法","examples":[{"en":"Clean-farming practices removed many plants from field edges.","zh":"清耕做法從田地邊緣移除了許多植物。"},{"en":"Clean-farming practices are methods that keep fields very tidy by removing weeds and extra vegetation.","zh":"清耕做法，是透過移除雜草和額外植被來保持田地非常整潔的方法。"},{"en":"A farmer may clear field edges to make machinery easier to use.","zh":"農民可能清理田邊，使機械更容易使用。"},{"en":"If clean farming removes wild flowers, pollinators may lose food and nesting places.","zh":"如果清耕移除野花，授粉者可能失去食物和築巢地點。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds positive, but it can harm biodiversity.","zh":"這個短語聽起來正面，但可能傷害生物多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"scrub native vegetation from","meaning":"清除……的本土植被","examples":[{"en":"Clean farming scrubbed native vegetation from field margins and roadsides.","zh":"清耕從田地邊緣和路邊地帶清除本土植被。"},{"en":"To scrub native vegetation from a place means to remove local plants thoroughly from it.","zh":"從某地清除本土植被，指徹底移除當地原生植物。"},{"en":"A housing project may scrub native vegetation from a hillside before construction.","zh":"住宅工程可能在施工前從山坡清除本土植被。"},{"en":"If native plants are scrubbed from farm edges, wild bees lose shelter and food.","zh":"如果本土植物從農田邊緣被清除，野生蜜蜂會失去庇護和食物。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests forceful and complete removal.","zh":"這個短語暗示強力而全面的移除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"native vegetation","meaning":"本土植被","examples":[{"en":"Native vegetation provides habitat and food for wild pollinators.","zh":"本土植被為野生授粉者提供棲息地和食物。"},{"en":"Native vegetation is the local plant life that naturally grows in a region.","zh":"本土植被，是某地區自然生長的本地植物。"},{"en":"Native vegetation beside a road may include shrubs, grasses, and wild flowers.","zh":"道路旁的本土植被可能包括灌木、草和野花。"},{"en":"If native vegetation disappears, local insects and birds may lose important resources.","zh":"如果本土植被消失，本地昆蟲和鳥類可能失去重要資源。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to natural local plants.","zh":"這個短語指自然存在的本地植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"field margins","meaning":"田地邊緣","examples":[{"en":"Native vegetation was removed from field margins.","zh":"本土植被被從田地邊緣移除。"},{"en":"Field margins are the edges or borders around farm fields.","zh":"田地邊緣，是農田周圍的邊界或邊緣。"},{"en":"Bees may nest or feed in flowers growing along field margins.","zh":"蜜蜂可能在田地邊緣生長的花中築巢或覓食。"},{"en":"If field margins are cleared completely, farmland becomes less friendly to wildlife.","zh":"如果田地邊緣被完全清理，農田就變得較不適合野生生物。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the outer edges of fields.","zh":"這個短語指農田外圍邊緣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"roadsides","meaning":"路邊地帶","examples":[{"en":"Clean farming removed native vegetation from roadsides.","zh":"清耕從路邊地帶移除了本土植被。"},{"en":"Roadsides are the strips of land along the sides of roads.","zh":"路邊地帶，是道路兩旁的一條土地。"},{"en":"Wild flowers on roadsides can provide food for bees and butterflies.","zh":"路邊地帶的野花可以為蜜蜂和蝴蝶提供食物。"},{"en":"If roadsides are sprayed with chemicals, pollinators may lose safe feeding areas.","zh":"如果路邊地帶被噴灑化學品，授粉者可能失去安全覓食地。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to land beside roads.","zh":"這個短語指道路旁的土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"kill something outright","meaning":"直接殺死某物","examples":[{"en":"These practices killed many native bees outright.","zh":"這些做法直接殺死了許多本土蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To kill something outright means to kill it immediately or completely.","zh":"直接殺死某物，指立即或完全殺死它。"},{"en":"A strong poison can kill insects outright within minutes.","zh":"強力毒藥可以在幾分鐘內直接殺死昆蟲。"},{"en":"If pesticides kill bees outright, pollination services may disappear quickly.","zh":"如果殺蟲劑直接殺死蜜蜂，授粉服務可能迅速消失。"},{"en":"The phrase shows direct and severe harm.","zh":"這個短語顯示直接而嚴重的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be vulnerable to","meaning":"容易受到……傷害","examples":[{"en":"Native bees are vulnerable to insecticides.","zh":"本土蜜蜂容易受到殺蟲劑傷害。"},{"en":"To be vulnerable to something means to be easily harmed or affected by it.","zh":"容易受到某事傷害，指容易被它傷害或影響。"},{"en":"Elderly people may be vulnerable to extreme heat during summer.","zh":"長者在夏天可能容易受到極端高溫傷害。"},{"en":"If bees are vulnerable to chemicals, spraying fields can damage pollinator populations.","zh":"如果蜜蜂容易受化學品傷害，噴灑田地可能損害授粉者種群。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weakness in the face of a threat.","zh":"這個短語描述面對威脅時的脆弱性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"agricultural pests","meaning":"農業害蟲","examples":[{"en":"Native bees are as vulnerable to insecticides as agricultural pests are.","zh":"本土蜜蜂和農業害蟲一樣容易受到殺蟲劑傷害。"},{"en":"Agricultural pests are insects or animals that damage crops or farm products.","zh":"農業害蟲，是破壞農作物或農產品的昆蟲或動物。"},{"en":"Caterpillars can be agricultural pests when they eat vegetable leaves.","zh":"當毛蟲吃掉蔬菜葉時，就可能成為農業害蟲。"},{"en":"If pesticides target agricultural pests, they may also harm useful insects.","zh":"如果殺蟲劑針對農業害蟲，也可能傷害有益昆蟲。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to farm-damaging organisms.","zh":"這個短語指破壞農業的生物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the agricultural landscape","meaning":"農業景觀；農田環境","examples":[{"en":"Modern farming has made the agricultural landscape less friendly to native bees.","zh":"現代農業令農業景觀對本土蜜蜂較不友善。"},{"en":"The agricultural landscape is the visible farmland environment, including fields, field edges, crops, roads, and hedges.","zh":"農業景觀，是可見的農田環境，包括田地、田邊、農作物、道路和樹籬。"},{"en":"A mixed agricultural landscape may include farms, wild strips, ponds, and small woods.","zh":"混合式農業景觀可能包括農場、野生植物帶、池塘和小林地。"},{"en":"If the agricultural landscape becomes too uniform, wildlife may lose places to live.","zh":"如果農業景觀變得太單一，野生生物可能失去棲身之處。"},{"en":"The phrase describes farmland as an environment.","zh":"這個短語把農地描述為一種環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"inhospitable to","meaning":"不適合……生存","examples":[{"en":"The agricultural landscape became inhospitable to many native bees.","zh":"農業景觀變得不適合許多本土蜜蜂生存。"},{"en":"Inhospitable to something means difficult or unsuitable for it to live, grow, or survive.","zh":"不適合某物生存，指對它生活、生長或存活來說困難或不合適。"},{"en":"A classroom with no air conditioning may be inhospitable to students during a heatwave.","zh":"熱浪期間，沒有冷氣的課室可能不適合學生長時間停留。"},{"en":"If farms lack flowers and nesting sites, they become inhospitable to wild bees.","zh":"如果農場缺少花和築巢地點，就會變得不適合野生蜜蜂生存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an unfriendly environment.","zh":"這個短語描述不友善環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"those that remained","meaning":"剩下的那些","examples":[{"en":"The landscape became inhospitable to the native bees that remained.","zh":"該景觀變得不適合剩下的本土蜜蜂生存。"},{"en":"Those that remained means the ones still left after others had disappeared or been removed.","zh":"剩下的那些，指其他已消失或被移除後仍留下的個體。"},{"en":"After many shops closed, those that remained had to serve more customers.","zh":"許多商店關閉後，剩下的那些商店要服務更多顧客。"},{"en":"If many bees die, those that remain may still struggle in a poor habitat.","zh":"如果許多蜜蜂死亡，剩下的那些仍可能在惡劣棲息地中掙扎。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to survivors or leftovers.","zh":"這個短語指倖存者或留下的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"concern about","meaning":"對……的憂慮","examples":[{"en":"Concern about these farming practices is not new.","zh":"對這些耕作方式的憂慮並不新。"},{"en":"Concern about something means worry or unease about it.","zh":"對某事的憂慮，指對它感到擔心或不安。"},{"en":"Parents may express concern about children spending too much time online.","zh":"家長可能表達對孩子花太多時間上網的憂慮。"},{"en":"If concern about pesticides grows, farmers may look for safer methods.","zh":"如果對殺蟲劑的憂慮增加，農民可能尋找較安全方法。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a worry people have.","zh":"這個短語引入人們的擔心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"effects on pollinators","meaning":"對授粉者的影響","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have long worried about the effects of farming practices on pollinators.","zh":"研究人員長期擔心耕作方式對授粉者的影響。"},{"en":"Effects on pollinators are the ways a change harms, helps, or alters animals that pollinate plants.","zh":"對授粉者的影響，是某種變化如何傷害、幫助或改變為植物授粉的動物。"},{"en":"A new pesticide may have negative effects on pollinators if bees visit sprayed flowers.","zh":"如果蜜蜂到訪被噴灑過的花，新殺蟲劑可能對授粉者有負面影響。"},{"en":"If farming removes wild plants, the effects on pollinators may include hunger and habitat loss.","zh":"如果農業移除野生植物，對授粉者的影響可能包括飢餓和棲息地喪失。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how pollinating species are affected.","zh":"這個短語強調授粉物種如何受影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ecological alarm cry","meaning":"生態警號","examples":[{"en":"Silent Spring was an ecological alarm cry.","zh":"《寂靜的春天》是一個生態警號。"},{"en":"An ecological alarm cry is a strong warning about danger to nature or ecosystems.","zh":"生態警號，是關於自然或生態系統危險的強烈警告。"},{"en":"A report on dying coral reefs can act as an ecological alarm cry.","zh":"關於珊瑚礁死亡的報告可以成為生態警號。"},{"en":"If an ecological alarm cry is ignored, damage may continue until it becomes harder to reverse.","zh":"如果生態警號被忽視，破壞可能持續到更難逆轉。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests urgent environmental warning.","zh":"這個短語暗示緊急環境警告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"warn of","meaning":"警告可能出現……","examples":[{"en":"Rachel Carson warned of a possible “Fruitless Fall”.","zh":"Rachel Carson 警告可能出現「無果的秋天」。"},{"en":"To warn of something means to tell people that a danger may happen.","zh":"警告可能出現某事，指告訴人們某種危險可能發生。"},{"en":"Weather reports may warn of heavy rain before a typhoon arrives.","zh":"天氣報告可能在颱風到達前警告可能有大雨。"},{"en":"If scientists warn of pollinator loss, farmers and governments may need to respond.","zh":"如果科學家警告授粉者流失，農民和政府可能需要回應。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a predicted danger.","zh":"這個短語引入預測中的危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a Fruitless Fall","meaning":"無果的秋天","examples":[{"en":"Rachel Carson warned of a “Fruitless Fall” caused by the loss of insect pollinators.","zh":"Rachel Carson 警告失去昆蟲授粉者可能造成「無果的秋天」。"},{"en":"A Fruitless Fall means an autumn with few fruits because pollination has failed.","zh":"無果的秋天，指因授粉失敗而幾乎沒有果實的秋季。"},{"en":"An orchard owner would fear a fruitless fall if flowers bloom but no apples grow.","zh":"如果花開了但蘋果沒有長出來，果園主人會害怕無果的秋天。"},{"en":"If insect pollinators disappear, fruit trees may fail to produce a normal harvest.","zh":"如果昆蟲授粉者消失，果樹可能無法產生正常收成。"},{"en":"The phrase is a memorable image of failed pollination.","zh":"這個短語以令人難忘的圖像描述授粉失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"result from","meaning":"由……引起","examples":[{"en":"A “Fruitless Fall” could result from the disappearance of insect pollinators.","zh":"「無果的秋天」可能由昆蟲授粉者消失引起。"},{"en":"To result from something means to be caused by it.","zh":"由某事引起，指由它造成。"},{"en":"Poor exam results may result from lack of sleep and weak revision habits.","zh":"考試成績差可能由睡眠不足和溫習習慣薄弱引起。"},{"en":"If crop failure results from pollinator loss, protecting insects becomes essential.","zh":"如果農作物失收由授粉者流失引起，保護昆蟲就變得必要。"},{"en":"The phrase links an effect to its cause.","zh":"這個短語把結果與原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the disappearance of","meaning":"……的消失","examples":[{"en":"Carson warned about the disappearance of insect pollinators.","zh":"Carson 警告昆蟲授粉者的消失。"},{"en":"The disappearance of something means it is no longer present or has been lost.","zh":"某物的消失，指它不再存在或已經失去。"},{"en":"The disappearance of a local bus route can make life harder for elderly residents.","zh":"本地巴士路線的消失可能令長者生活更困難。"},{"en":"If pollinators disappear, plants that depend on them may reproduce poorly.","zh":"如果授粉者消失，依賴牠們的植物可能繁殖不良。"},{"en":"The phrase describes loss or absence.","zh":"這個短語描述失去或不存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"insect pollinators","meaning":"昆蟲授粉者","examples":[{"en":"The disappearance of insect pollinators could seriously affect crops.","zh":"昆蟲授粉者的消失可能嚴重影響農作物。"},{"en":"Insect pollinators are insects that move pollen between flowers.","zh":"昆蟲授粉者，是在花之間傳送花粉的昆蟲。"},{"en":"Bees, butterflies, moths, flies, and beetles can be insect pollinators.","zh":"蜜蜂、蝴蝶、蛾、蒼蠅和甲蟲都可以是昆蟲授粉者。"},{"en":"If insect pollinators decline, some fruits and vegetables may become less abundant.","zh":"如果昆蟲授粉者減少，某些水果和蔬菜可能變得較少。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies insects that help plants reproduce.","zh":"這個短語指出幫助植物繁殖的昆蟲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"has not yet occurred","meaning":"尚未發生","examples":[{"en":"The feared “Fruitless Fall” has not yet occurred.","zh":"人們害怕的「無果的秋天」尚未發生。"},{"en":"Has not yet occurred means has not happened up to the present time.","zh":"尚未發生，指直到目前仍未發生。"},{"en":"The predicted storm has not yet occurred, but residents remain prepared.","zh":"預測中的風暴尚未發生，但居民仍保持準備。"},{"en":"If a disaster has not yet occurred, prevention may still be possible.","zh":"如果災難尚未發生，預防可能仍然可行。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something expected or feared has not happened so far.","zh":"這個短語顯示預期或恐懼的事情到目前仍未發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"largely thanks to","meaning":"很大程度上歸功於","examples":[{"en":"The crisis may have been avoided largely thanks to the honeybee.","zh":"這場危機可能很大程度上歸功於蜜蜂才得以避免。"},{"en":"Largely thanks to means mostly because of someone or something helpful.","zh":"很大程度上歸功於，指主要因為某人或某事提供幫助。"},{"en":"The school event succeeded largely thanks to volunteers who stayed late.","zh":"學校活動成功，很大程度上歸功於留下來幫忙到很晚的義工。"},{"en":"If food supply remains stable largely thanks to honeybees, their role is very important.","zh":"如果食物供應穩定很大程度上歸功於蜜蜂，牠們的角色就非常重要。"},{"en":"The phrase gives major credit to a cause.","zh":"這個短語把主要功勞歸於某原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"turn to","meaning":"轉而依靠","examples":[{"en":"Farmers turned to honeybees as wild pollinators declined.","zh":"隨着野生授粉者減少，農民轉而依靠蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To turn to something means to start using it for help or support.","zh":"轉而依靠某物，指開始使用它作為幫助或支援。"},{"en":"A student may turn to a dictionary when they cannot understand a word.","zh":"學生不明白一個詞時，可能轉而查字典。"},{"en":"If wild bees decline, farmers may turn to managed honeybees for pollination.","zh":"如果野生蜜蜂減少，農民可能轉而依靠受管理蜜蜂授粉。"},{"en":"The phrase shows choosing a new source of help.","zh":"這個短語顯示選擇新的幫助來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"wild pollinators","meaning":"野生授粉者","examples":[{"en":"The ability of wild pollinators to service crops has declined.","zh":"野生授粉者為農作物提供授粉服務的能力已經下降。"},{"en":"Wild pollinators are unmanaged animals or insects that naturally pollinate plants.","zh":"野生授粉者，是不受人管理、自然為植物授粉的動物或昆蟲。"},{"en":"Wild pollinators may live in hedges, forests, gardens, and field edges.","zh":"野生授粉者可能生活在樹籬、森林、花園和田邊。"},{"en":"If wild pollinators decline, farms may depend more heavily on managed bees.","zh":"如果野生授粉者減少，農場可能更高度依賴受管理蜜蜂。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to natural pollinating species outside human control.","zh":"這個短語指人類控制以外的自然授粉物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"service crops","meaning":"為農作物提供授粉服務","examples":[{"en":"Wild pollinators help service crops by pollinating them.","zh":"野生授粉者透過授粉幫助為農作物提供服務。"},{"en":"To service crops means to provide an important function that helps crops grow or produce food.","zh":"為農作物提供服務，指提供幫助農作物生長或生產食物的重要功能。"},{"en":"Irrigation systems service crops by bringing water to dry fields.","zh":"灌溉系統透過把水帶到乾燥田地來服務農作物。"},{"en":"If insects service crops through pollination, farmers benefit from their natural work.","zh":"如果昆蟲透過授粉服務農作物，農民就受益於牠們的自然工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes useful support given to farming.","zh":"這個短語描述對農業有用的支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"decline","meaning":"下降；衰退","examples":[{"en":"The ability of wild pollinators to service crops has declined.","zh":"野生授粉者服務農作物的能力已經下降。"},{"en":"To decline means to become smaller, weaker, or less common.","zh":"下降或衰退，指變得較少、較弱或較不常見。"},{"en":"A student’s energy may decline after several nights of poor sleep.","zh":"學生連續幾晚睡得不好後，精力可能下降。"},{"en":"If wild pollinators decline, crops may receive fewer flower visits.","zh":"如果野生授粉者衰退，農作物可能得到較少訪花次數。"},{"en":"The word describes a downward change.","zh":"這個詞描述向下的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"semi-domesticated","meaning":"半馴化的","examples":[{"en":"The honeybee has been semi-domesticated since ancient times.","zh":"蜜蜂自古以來已經是半馴化的。"},{"en":"Semi-domesticated means partly controlled by humans but not completely tame like many farm animals.","zh":"半馴化的，指部分受人類控制，但不像許多農場動物般完全馴服。"},{"en":"A semi-domesticated animal may live near people but still behave partly like a wild animal.","zh":"半馴化動物可能生活在人附近，但仍部分像野生動物般行動。"},{"en":"If honeybees are semi-domesticated, humans can manage hives but cannot control every bee.","zh":"如果蜜蜂是半馴化的，人類可以管理蜂箱，但不能控制每一隻蜜蜂。"},{"en":"The word describes a middle state between wild and fully domesticated.","zh":"這個詞描述野生和完全馴化之間的中間狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the ancient Egyptians","meaning":"古埃及人","examples":[{"en":"Honeybees have been semi-domesticated since the time of the ancient Egyptians.","zh":"蜜蜂自古埃及人時代以來已經半馴化。"},{"en":"The ancient Egyptians were people who lived in ancient Egypt thousands of years ago.","zh":"古埃及人，是數千年前生活在古埃及的人。"},{"en":"The ancient Egyptians are known for pyramids, writing, farming, and religious practices.","zh":"古埃及人以金字塔、文字、農業和宗教習俗聞名。"},{"en":"If honeybee keeping goes back to the ancient Egyptians, it has a very long history.","zh":"如果養蜜蜂可追溯至古埃及人，它就有非常悠久的歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an early civilisation in Egypt.","zh":"這個短語指埃及的一個早期文明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"it was not just familiarity that","meaning":"並不只是因為熟悉才……","examples":[{"en":"It was not just familiarity that made farmers choose honeybees.","zh":"農民選擇蜜蜂並不只是因為熟悉。"},{"en":"It was not just familiarity that means another deeper reason existed besides people already knowing something.","zh":"並不只是因為熟悉，指除了人們已認識某物之外，還有另一個更深原因。"},{"en":"It was not just familiarity that made students choose the library; it was also quiet and safe.","zh":"學生選擇圖書館並不只是因為熟悉，也因為它安靜和安全。"},{"en":"If farmers chose honeybees for biological reasons too, habit was not the only cause.","zh":"如果農民也因生物原因選擇蜜蜂，習慣就不是唯一原因。"},{"en":"The phrase rejects an overly simple explanation.","zh":"這個短語否定過分簡單的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"determine this choice","meaning":"決定這個選擇","examples":[{"en":"Biology helped determine the choice of honeybees for agriculture.","zh":"生物學因素幫助決定農業中選擇蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To determine this choice means to influence or decide which option is selected.","zh":"決定這個選擇，指影響或決定選取哪個選項。"},{"en":"A student’s budget may determine the choice of restaurant.","zh":"學生的預算可能決定選擇哪間餐廳。"},{"en":"If honeybee biology fits industrial farms, it helps explain why farmers selected them.","zh":"如果蜜蜂生物特性適合工業化農場，就有助解釋農民為何選擇牠們。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a reason with a decision.","zh":"這個短語把原因與決定連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be suited to","meaning":"適合……","examples":[{"en":"Honeybees are suited to modern agricultural systems.","zh":"蜜蜂適合現代農業系統。"},{"en":"To be suited to something means to fit it well or be appropriate for it.","zh":"適合某事，指與它配合良好或對它合適。"},{"en":"Online lessons are suited to students who live far from school.","zh":"網上課堂適合住得離學校很遠的學生。"},{"en":"If honeybees can be moved and managed easily, they are suited to industrial farming.","zh":"如果蜜蜂容易被搬運和管理，牠們就適合工業化農業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical fit.","zh":"這個短語描述實際配合度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the kind of agricultural system","meaning":"……那種農業系統","examples":[{"en":"Honeybees suited the kind of agricultural system that was emerging.","zh":"蜜蜂適合當時正在出現的那種農業系統。"},{"en":"The kind of agricultural system means the particular type or model of farming being discussed.","zh":"那種農業系統，指正在討論的特定農業類型或模式。"},{"en":"A small village farm and a large industrial farm are different kinds of agricultural systems.","zh":"小村莊農場和大型工業農場是不同種類的農業系統。"},{"en":"If a new agricultural system needs mobile pollinators, honeybees may fit it well.","zh":"如果新農業系統需要可移動授粉者，蜜蜂可能很適合。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a specific farming model.","zh":"這個短語指出特定農業模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be emerging","meaning":"正在出現","examples":[{"en":"A new kind of agricultural system was emerging.","zh":"一種新的農業系統正在出現。"},{"en":"To be emerging means to be beginning to appear or develop.","zh":"正在出現，指開始出現或發展。"},{"en":"A new fashion trend may be emerging when many young people start wearing the same style.","zh":"當許多年輕人開始穿同一風格，新時裝潮流可能正在出現。"},{"en":"If industrial farming was emerging, new pollination methods also became necessary.","zh":"如果工業化農業正在出現，新的授粉方法也變得必要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something coming into existence.","zh":"這個短語描述某事正在形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be closed up","meaning":"被關起來；被封起來","examples":[{"en":"Honeybee hives can be closed up before pesticides are applied.","zh":"蜜蜂蜂箱可以在施用殺蟲劑前被封起來。"},{"en":"To be closed up means to be shut so that nothing can easily enter or leave.","zh":"被關起來或封起來，指被關上，使東西不容易進出。"},{"en":"A shop may be closed up at night to keep goods safe.","zh":"商店晚上可能被關起來，以保護貨物安全。"},{"en":"If hives are closed up during pesticide use, bees may be protected temporarily.","zh":"如果蜂箱在使用殺蟲劑期間被封起來，蜜蜂可能暫時受到保護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sealing or shutting something.","zh":"這個短語描述封閉或關上某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"moved out of the way","meaning":"被移離；移開","examples":[{"en":"Honeybee hives can be moved out of the way when farmers use pesticides.","zh":"農民使用殺蟲劑時，蜜蜂蜂箱可以被移開。"},{"en":"Moved out of the way means relocated so they are no longer in danger or blocking something.","zh":"被移開，指被搬到另一處，使其不再有危險或不再阻礙某事。"},{"en":"Chairs are moved out of the way before students play indoor games.","zh":"學生玩室內遊戲前，椅子會被移開。"},{"en":"If hives are moved away from sprayed fields, bees may avoid direct chemical exposure.","zh":"如果蜂箱被移離噴灑田地，蜜蜂可能避免直接接觸化學品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes removing something from a risky or inconvenient place.","zh":"這個短語描述把某物從危險或不方便位置移走。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pesticides are applied to","meaning":"殺蟲劑被施用於……","examples":[{"en":"Honeybee hives can be moved when pesticides are applied to a field.","zh":"當殺蟲劑被施用於田地時，蜜蜂蜂箱可以被移開。"},{"en":"When pesticides are applied to a place, chemicals are put or sprayed there to kill pests.","zh":"殺蟲劑被施用於某地，指化學品被放置或噴灑在那裡以殺死害蟲。"},{"en":"Workers may leave a park temporarily when pesticides are applied to the grass.","zh":"當殺蟲劑被施用於草地時，工人可能暫時離開公園。"},{"en":"If pesticides are applied to flowering crops, pollinators may be exposed to danger.","zh":"如果殺蟲劑被施用於開花農作物，授粉者可能暴露於危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using pest-killing chemicals on a surface or area.","zh":"這個短語描述在表面或區域使用殺蟲化學品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"generalist pollinators","meaning":"廣泛型授粉者","examples":[{"en":"Honeybees are generalist pollinators that can pollinate many crops.","zh":"蜜蜂是能為多種農作物授粉的廣泛型授粉者。"},{"en":"Generalist pollinators are pollinators that can work with many different plant species.","zh":"廣泛型授粉者，是能為許多不同植物物種授粉的授粉者。"},{"en":"A generalist worker in an office can handle many tasks instead of only one.","zh":"辦公室中的廣泛型員工可以處理多項工作，而不只一項。"},{"en":"If a pollinator is generalist, farmers can use it for several crops.","zh":"如果授粉者屬於廣泛型，農民可以把它用於幾種農作物。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts broad usefulness with narrow specialisation.","zh":"這個短語把廣泛用途與狹窄專門化作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"many different crops","meaning":"多種不同農作物","examples":[{"en":"Honeybees can be used to pollinate many different crops.","zh":"蜜蜂可以用來為多種不同農作物授粉。"},{"en":"Many different crops means several kinds of farm plants grown for food or products.","zh":"多種不同農作物，指為食物或產品而種植的幾種農場植物。"},{"en":"A market garden may grow many different crops, such as tomatoes, peppers, and melons.","zh":"市場菜園可能種植多種不同農作物，例如番茄、甜椒和瓜類。"},{"en":"If one pollinator can serve many crops, it becomes useful to large farming systems.","zh":"如果一種授粉者能服務多種農作物，它就對大型農業系統很有用。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses variety in agriculture.","zh":"這個短語強調農業中的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the most efficient pollinator","meaning":"最高效的授粉者","examples":[{"en":"Honeybees are not the most efficient pollinator of every crop.","zh":"蜜蜂並不是每一種農作物最高效的授粉者。"},{"en":"The most efficient pollinator is the species that pollinates a plant with the least waste of time or effort.","zh":"最高效的授粉者，是以最少時間或努力為植物授粉的物種。"},{"en":"A machine is most efficient when it finishes the job quickly with little energy.","zh":"當機器用少量能量快速完成工作，它就是最高效的。"},{"en":"If another bee visits flowers more effectively, honeybees may not be the best choice for that crop.","zh":"如果另一種蜜蜂更有效到訪花朵，蜜蜂未必是該農作物的最佳選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase asks which pollinator works best.","zh":"這個短語問哪種授粉者最有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have strength in numbers","meaning":"以數量取勝","examples":[{"en":"Honeybees have strength in numbers because many bees live in one hive.","zh":"蜜蜂以數量取勝，因為許多蜜蜂住在同一個蜂箱。"},{"en":"To have strength in numbers means to be powerful because there are many individuals working together.","zh":"以數量取勝，指因有許多個體一起工作而強大。"},{"en":"Volunteers have strength in numbers when many people help clean a beach.","zh":"當許多人幫忙清潔海灘，義工就以數量取勝。"},{"en":"If one hive contains thousands of bees, the colony can pollinate many flowers quickly.","zh":"如果一個蜂箱有數以千計蜜蜂，蜂群可以快速為許多花授粉。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the power of large numbers.","zh":"這個短語突出龐大數量的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a single hive","meaning":"單一蜂箱","examples":[{"en":"Up to 100,000 bees can live in a single hive.","zh":"多達十萬隻蜜蜂可以住在單一蜂箱中。"},{"en":"A single hive means one beehive, not a group of many hives.","zh":"單一蜂箱，指一個蜂箱，而不是一組蜂箱。"},{"en":"A beekeeper may inspect a single hive before checking the whole row.","zh":"養蜂人可能先檢查單一蜂箱，再檢查整排蜂箱。"},{"en":"If a single hive contains many bees, it can provide a large workforce for pollination.","zh":"如果單一蜂箱含有許多蜜蜂，它就可以提供龐大授粉工作力。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on one hive as a unit.","zh":"這個短語強調一個蜂箱作為單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"without a doubt","meaning":"毫無疑問","examples":[{"en":"Without a doubt, honeybees are extremely useful in agriculture.","zh":"毫無疑問，蜜蜂在農業中極其有用。"},{"en":"Without a doubt means certainly or unquestionably.","zh":"毫無疑問，指確定地或無可置疑地。"},{"en":"Without a doubt, regular practice helps students improve speaking confidence.","zh":"毫無疑問，定期練習幫助學生提升說話信心。"},{"en":"If evidence is strong, a writer may use this phrase to show certainty.","zh":"如果證據有力，作者可能用這個短語顯示肯定。"},{"en":"The phrase strengthens a clear opinion.","zh":"這個短語加強清楚意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the US Department of Agriculture","meaning":"美國農業部","examples":[{"en":"Jim Cane works for the US Department of Agriculture.","zh":"Jim Cane 任職於美國農業部。"},{"en":"The US Department of Agriculture is a government department concerned with farming, food, and rural issues in the United States.","zh":"美國農業部，是美國負責農業、食物和鄉郊議題的政府部門。"},{"en":"A farmer may read guidance from the US Department of Agriculture before choosing new crop methods.","zh":"農民可能在選擇新種植方法前閱讀美國農業部的指引。"},{"en":"If a researcher works there, their work is connected with national agricultural concerns.","zh":"如果研究人員在那裡工作，其工作就與國家農業問題有關。"},{"en":"The phrase names an official American agricultural institution.","zh":"這個短語命名美國官方農業機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in other words","meaning":"換言之","examples":[{"en":"In other words, the honeybee has become crucial to modern agriculture.","zh":"換言之，蜜蜂已變得對現代農業至關重要。"},{"en":"In other words introduces the same idea in a clearer or simpler way.","zh":"換言之，用較清楚或較簡單方式引入同一個想法。"},{"en":"This grammar rule is about time; in other words, tense matters.","zh":"這條文法規則關於時間；換言之，時態很重要。"},{"en":"If a sentence is complex, “in other words” helps restate the meaning.","zh":"如果句子複雜，“in other words” 有助重新說明意思。"},{"en":"The phrase signals explanation or rephrasing.","zh":"這個短語表示解釋或改述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a crucial cog in","meaning":"……中的關鍵一環","examples":[{"en":"The honeybee has become a crucial cog in industrial agriculture.","zh":"蜜蜂已成為工業化農業中的關鍵一環。"},{"en":"A crucial cog in a system is a small but essential part that helps the whole system work.","zh":"系統中的關鍵一環，是幫助整個系統運作的細小但必要部分。"},{"en":"A school secretary can be a crucial cog in the daily running of a school.","zh":"學校文員可以是學校日常運作中的關鍵一環。"},{"en":"If honeybees stop working, the larger agricultural machine may slow down.","zh":"如果蜜蜂停止發揮作用，更大的農業機器可能慢下來。"},{"en":"The phrase compares a person or thing to an important machine part.","zh":"這個短語把人或物比作重要機件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"industrial agriculture","meaning":"工業化農業","examples":[{"en":"Honeybees play an important role in industrial agriculture.","zh":"蜜蜂在工業化農業中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"Industrial agriculture is large-scale farming organised like a modern production system.","zh":"工業化農業，是像現代生產系統一樣組織的大規模農業。"},{"en":"Industrial agriculture may use machines, chemicals, monocultures, and long-distance transport.","zh":"工業化農業可能使用機器、化學品、單一作物和長途運輸。"},{"en":"If agriculture becomes highly industrial, it can produce more food but also become more fragile.","zh":"如果農業高度工業化，它可以生產更多食物，但也可能變得更脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes farming as a large organised industry.","zh":"這個短語把農業描述為大型有組織產業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"deliver more food","meaning":"提供更多食物","examples":[{"en":"The modern agricultural system delivers more food to more places.","zh":"現代農業系統向更多地方提供更多食物。"},{"en":"To deliver more food means to produce and supply a greater amount of food.","zh":"提供更多食物，指生產和供應更大量食物。"},{"en":"A larger delivery network can deliver more food to homes during bad weather.","zh":"較大的送貨網絡可以在惡劣天氣中向住戶提供更多食物。"},{"en":"If farms become more efficient, they may deliver more food to cities and export markets.","zh":"如果農場變得更有效率，它們可能向城市和出口市場提供更多食物。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on supply and distribution.","zh":"這個短語強調供應和分配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"more cheaply than ever before","meaning":"比以往任何時候都更便宜","examples":[{"en":"Food can now be delivered more cheaply than ever before.","zh":"現在食物可以比以往任何時候都更便宜地被送達。"},{"en":"More cheaply than ever before means at a lower cost than at any earlier time.","zh":"比以往任何時候都更便宜，指成本低於過去任何時間。"},{"en":"Online calls allow families abroad to communicate more cheaply than ever before.","zh":"網上通話讓海外家庭能比以往任何時候都更便宜地溝通。"},{"en":"If industrial farming lowers costs, consumers may buy food at lower prices.","zh":"如果工業化農業降低成本，消費者可能以較低價格買到食物。"},{"en":"The phrase compares present cost with the whole past.","zh":"這個短語把現時成本與整個過去作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be vulnerable","meaning":"容易受衝擊","examples":[{"en":"The industrial agricultural system is also vulnerable.","zh":"工業化農業系統也容易受衝擊。"},{"en":"To be vulnerable means to be easily harmed, damaged, or disrupted.","zh":"容易受衝擊，指容易被傷害、破壞或擾亂。"},{"en":"A computer system is vulnerable if one password can open every account.","zh":"如果一個密碼可以開啟所有帳戶，電腦系統就是脆弱的。"},{"en":"If agriculture depends on one pollinator, disease in that species can threaten the whole system.","zh":"如果農業依賴一種授粉者，該物種的疾病可以威脅整個系統。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weakness under pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述在壓力下的弱點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the photosynthetic equivalent of","meaning":"相當於進行光合作用的……","examples":[{"en":"A farm field can become the photosynthetic equivalent of a factory floor.","zh":"農田可以變成相當於進行光合作用的工廠車間。"},{"en":"The photosynthetic equivalent of something means a plant-based version that works like that thing.","zh":"相當於進行光合作用的某物，指以植物為基礎、運作像該物的版本。"},{"en":"A greenhouse full of identical lettuce can be the plant-growing equivalent of an assembly line.","zh":"滿是相同生菜的溫室，可以是植物生長版的流水線。"},{"en":"If a field is treated like a factory floor, nature is organised for production above diversity.","zh":"如果田地被當成工廠車間，自然就被組織成重生產而非多樣性。"},{"en":"The phrase uses comparison to show industrial-style farming.","zh":"這個短語用比較展示工業化農業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a factory floor","meaning":"工廠車間","examples":[{"en":"The writer compares a farm field to a factory floor.","zh":"作者把農田比作工廠車間。"},{"en":"A factory floor is the main working area in a factory where goods are made.","zh":"工廠車間，是工廠中製造貨品的主要工作區域。"},{"en":"Workers on a factory floor may repeat the same task many times.","zh":"工廠車間中的工人可能多次重複同一項任務。"},{"en":"If farmland is compared to a factory floor, the writer stresses efficiency and repetition.","zh":"如果農地被比作工廠車間，作者就是強調效率和重複。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests industrial production.","zh":"這個短語暗示工業生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a series of","meaning":"一連串的","examples":[{"en":"Pollination has become a series of long-distance operations.","zh":"授粉已變成一連串長距離操作。"},{"en":"A series of something means several related events or actions happening one after another.","zh":"一連串的某事，指幾個相關事件或行動一個接一個發生。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students a series of short quizzes before the exam.","zh":"老師可能在考試前給學生一連串小測。"},{"en":"If pollination becomes a series of operations, it is planned and repeated like a business process.","zh":"如果授粉變成一連串操作，它就是像商業流程般被規劃和重複。"},{"en":"The phrase describes connected steps.","zh":"這個短語描述互相連接的步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"continent-long assembly lines","meaning":"橫跨大陸的流水作業線","examples":[{"en":"Industrial pollination can resemble continent-long assembly lines.","zh":"工業化授粉可能像橫跨大陸的流水作業線。"},{"en":"Continent-long assembly lines means production-like systems stretching across very large distances.","zh":"橫跨大陸的流水作業線，指延伸非常遠距離、像生產線般的系統。"},{"en":"A delivery network from farms to cities can feel like a country-wide assembly line.","zh":"從農場到城市的配送網絡，可能感覺像全國性的流水線。"},{"en":"If beehives move across a continent to pollinate crops, agriculture resembles a giant factory system.","zh":"如果蜂箱橫跨大陸移動來為農作物授粉，農業就像巨大工廠系統。"},{"en":"The phrase uses an industrial image to show scale.","zh":"這個短語用工業圖像展示規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"leach out","meaning":"削弱；流失","examples":[{"en":"Industrial farming can leach out the resilience of natural ecosystems.","zh":"工業化農業可以削弱自然生態系統的韌性。"},{"en":"To leach out something means to slowly remove or drain it away.","zh":"削弱或流失某物，指慢慢移除或耗走它。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can leach nutrients out of soil.","zh":"大雨可以把土壤中的營養沖走。"},{"en":"If farming removes diversity year after year, it may leach out natural resilience.","zh":"如果農業一年又一年移除多樣性，就可能削弱自然韌性。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests gradual loss.","zh":"這個短語暗示逐漸流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"resilience","meaning":"韌性；恢復力","examples":[{"en":"Natural ecosystems have resilience that industrial systems may lack.","zh":"自然生態系統有工業系統可能缺乏的韌性。"},{"en":"Resilience is the ability to recover after stress, damage, or change.","zh":"韌性，是在壓力、損害或變化後恢復的能力。"},{"en":"A student shows resilience when they improve after failing a test.","zh":"學生考試失敗後進步，就是展現韌性。"},{"en":"If an ecosystem has resilience, it can survive shocks such as drought or disease.","zh":"如果生態系統有韌性，就能承受乾旱或疾病等衝擊。"},{"en":"The word means recovery strength.","zh":"這個詞指恢復能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"natural ecosystems","meaning":"自然生態系統","examples":[{"en":"Natural ecosystems are often more resilient than overspecialised agricultural systems.","zh":"自然生態系統通常比過度專門化的農業系統更有韌性。"},{"en":"Natural ecosystems are communities of living things interacting with their environment without being fully controlled by humans.","zh":"自然生態系統，是不完全受人類控制、與環境互動的生物群落。"},{"en":"A forest, wetland, or coral reef can be a natural ecosystem.","zh":"森林、濕地或珊瑚礁都可以是自然生態系統。"},{"en":"If natural ecosystems contain many species, they may recover better from disturbance.","zh":"如果自然生態系統包含許多物種，就可能更好地從擾動中恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to connected living systems in nature.","zh":"這個短語指自然中互相連繫的生命系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"point out that","meaning":"指出","examples":[{"en":"Breno Freitas pointed out that specialisation can be risky.","zh":"Breno Freitas 指出，專門化可能有風險。"},{"en":"To point out that means to mention or explain something important.","zh":"指出，指提及或解釋重要事情。"},{"en":"A teacher may point out that an essay needs clearer topic sentences.","zh":"老師可能指出文章需要更清楚的主題句。"},{"en":"If an expert points out a risk, readers should pay attention to the warning.","zh":"如果專家指出風險，讀者應留意警告。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a highlighted observation.","zh":"這個短語引入被突出強調的觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in nature","meaning":"在自然界中","examples":[{"en":"In nature, a high degree of specialisation can be dangerous.","zh":"在自然界中，高度專門化可能很危險。"},{"en":"In nature means in the natural world, outside purely human-made systems.","zh":"在自然界中，指在自然世界裡，而不是純人造系統中。"},{"en":"In nature, different plants and animals often depend on one another.","zh":"在自然界中，不同植物和動物常互相依賴。"},{"en":"If a species is too specialised in nature, one small change can threaten it.","zh":"如果一個物種在自然界中過度專門化，一個小變化就可能威脅它。"},{"en":"The phrase places the idea in the natural world.","zh":"這個短語把想法放在自然世界中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a high degree of specialisation","meaning":"高度專門化","examples":[{"en":"A high degree of specialisation can become a dangerous game.","zh":"高度專門化可能變成危險的做法。"},{"en":"A high degree of specialisation means depending on one narrow skill, role, or relationship.","zh":"高度專門化，指依賴一種狹窄技能、角色或關係。"},{"en":"A worker with only one very specific skill may face risk if that job disappears.","zh":"如果工人只有一項非常特定技能，該工作消失時就可能面臨風險。"},{"en":"If agriculture depends on one pollinator, a disease affecting it can threaten many crops.","zh":"如果農業依賴一種授粉者，影響它的疾病可以威脅許多農作物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes narrow dependence.","zh":"這個短語描述狹窄依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a dangerous game","meaning":"危險的做法","examples":[{"en":"Relying on one pollinator species can be a dangerous game.","zh":"依靠單一授粉物種可能是危險的做法。"},{"en":"A dangerous game is a risky strategy that may fail badly if conditions change.","zh":"危險的做法，是情況改變時可能嚴重失敗的高風險策略。"},{"en":"Spending all your savings on one business idea can be a dangerous game.","zh":"把所有積蓄投放在一個商業想法上，可能是危險的做法。"},{"en":"If one bee species collapses, a single-pollinator strategy can damage food production.","zh":"如果一種蜜蜂崩潰，單一授粉者策略可能損害食物生產。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against risky dependence.","zh":"這個短語警告不要冒險依賴單一事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in equilibrium","meaning":"處於平衡狀態","examples":[{"en":"Specialisation works well while everything is in equilibrium.","zh":"當一切處於平衡狀態時，專門化運作良好。"},{"en":"In equilibrium means in a balanced and stable state.","zh":"處於平衡狀態，指處於平衡而穩定的狀態。"},{"en":"A student’s schedule is in equilibrium when study, sleep, and rest are all balanced.","zh":"當學習、睡眠和休息都平衡時，學生的時間表就處於平衡狀態。"},{"en":"If an ecosystem is in equilibrium, one species does not suddenly dominate or disappear.","zh":"如果生態系統處於平衡狀態，某一物種不會突然支配或消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes balance.","zh":"這個短語描述平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lead to extinction","meaning":"導致滅絕","examples":[{"en":"A slight imbalance can quickly lead to extinction.","zh":"輕微不平衡可以迅速導致滅絕。"},{"en":"To lead to extinction means to cause a species to disappear completely.","zh":"導致滅絕，指造成某物種完全消失。"},{"en":"Habitat loss can lead to extinction if animals have nowhere else to live.","zh":"如果動物沒有其他地方可住，棲息地喪失可以導致滅絕。"},{"en":"If a specialised species loses the one plant it needs, extinction may become possible.","zh":"如果專門化物種失去唯一需要的植物，滅絕可能變成可能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a cause ending in total species loss.","zh":"這個短語描述導向物種完全消失的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the slightest imbalance","meaning":"最輕微的不平衡","examples":[{"en":"Specialisation can become dangerous at the slightest imbalance.","zh":"專門化在最輕微的不平衡下都可能變得危險。"},{"en":"The slightest imbalance means even a very small loss of balance.","zh":"最輕微的不平衡，指即使非常小的失衡。"},{"en":"A tightrope walker can fall because of the slightest imbalance.","zh":"走鋼線的人可能因最輕微的不平衡而跌倒。"},{"en":"If a system is too specialised, even a small change may cause serious failure.","zh":"如果系統過度專門化，即使小變化也可能造成嚴重失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses extreme sensitivity.","zh":"這個短語強調極高敏感度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in effect","meaning":"實際上","examples":[{"en":"In effect, humans have become dangerously overspecialised.","zh":"實際上，人類在使用蜜蜂方面已變得危險地過度專門化。"},{"en":"In effect means in practical reality, even if not officially or obviously.","zh":"實際上，指在實際現實中，即使不是正式或明顯如此。"},{"en":"If a student does all the group work alone, in effect they are working without a team.","zh":"如果學生獨自完成所有小組工作，實際上他是在沒有團隊下工作。"},{"en":"If agriculture relies on one pollinator, in effect it has narrowed its safety options.","zh":"如果農業依賴一種授粉者，實際上它已縮窄安全選項。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the real practical meaning.","zh":"這個短語引入真正的實際意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be heavily reliant on","meaning":"高度依賴……","examples":[{"en":"Modern agriculture is heavily reliant on a single pollinator species.","zh":"現代農業高度依賴單一授粉物種。"},{"en":"To be heavily reliant on something means to depend on it very strongly.","zh":"高度依賴某物，指非常強烈地依靠它。"},{"en":"A student who cannot study without a phone dictionary is heavily reliant on technology.","zh":"如果學生沒有手機字典就不能溫習，就是高度依賴科技。"},{"en":"If farms are heavily reliant on honeybees, honeybee disease becomes a major risk.","zh":"如果農場高度依賴蜜蜂，蜜蜂疾病就成為重大風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong dependence.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a single pollinator species","meaning":"單一授粉物種","examples":[{"en":"Depending on a single pollinator species makes agriculture fragile.","zh":"依賴單一授粉物種令農業變得脆弱。"},{"en":"A single pollinator species means only one kind of animal or insect used for pollination.","zh":"單一授粉物種，指只使用一種動物或昆蟲進行授粉。"},{"en":"A farm that uses only honeybees depends on a single pollinator species.","zh":"只使用蜜蜂的農場，就是依賴單一授粉物種。"},{"en":"If that species suffers disease, the whole pollination system may be affected.","zh":"如果該物種受疾病影響，整個授粉系統可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights lack of diversity.","zh":"這個短語突出缺乏多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dangerously overspecialised","meaning":"危險地過度專門化","examples":[{"en":"Humans have become dangerously overspecialised in their use of honeybees.","zh":"人類在使用蜜蜂方面已變得危險地過度專門化。"},{"en":"Dangerously overspecialised means relying too narrowly on one method, species, or system in a risky way.","zh":"危險地過度專門化，指以有風險的方式過度狹窄地依賴一種方法、物種或系統。"},{"en":"A company is dangerously overspecialised if it can only sell one product to one customer.","zh":"如果公司只能向一個客戶出售一種產品，就是危險地過度專門化。"},{"en":"If honeybees fail, overspecialised agriculture may not have enough alternatives.","zh":"如果蜜蜂失效，過度專門化的農業可能沒有足夠替代方案。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that narrow efficiency can create fragility.","zh":"這個短語警告狹窄效率可能造成脆弱性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the human-honeybee relationship","meaning":"人類與蜜蜂的關係","examples":[{"en":"Colony collapse disorder has disrupted the human-honeybee relationship.","zh":"蜂群崩壞失調症擾亂了人類與蜜蜂的關係。"},{"en":"The human-honeybee relationship is the long connection between people and honeybees through beekeeping and agriculture.","zh":"人類與蜜蜂的關係，是人們透過養蜂和農業與蜜蜂建立的長期連繫。"},{"en":"Beekeepers show the human-honeybee relationship when they manage hives for honey and crop pollination.","zh":"養蜂人管理蜂箱以取得蜂蜜和為農作物授粉，展現了人類與蜜蜂的關係。"},{"en":"If honeybee colonies collapse, this relationship becomes unstable and costly.","zh":"如果蜜蜂蜂群崩潰，這種關係就變得不穩定而昂貴。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how humans depend on and manage bees.","zh":"這個短語描述人類如何依賴和管理蜜蜂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be disrupted by","meaning":"被……擾亂","examples":[{"en":"The human-honeybee relationship has been disrupted by colony collapse disorder.","zh":"人類與蜜蜂的關係被蜂群崩壞失調症擾亂。"},{"en":"To be disrupted by something means to be interrupted, damaged, or made less stable by it.","zh":"被某事擾亂，指被它打斷、破壞或變得較不穩定。"},{"en":"A train service may be disrupted by heavy rain.","zh":"火車服務可能被大雨擾亂。"},{"en":"If pollination is disrupted by bee disease, farmers may lose reliable crop support.","zh":"如果授粉被蜜蜂疾病擾亂，農民可能失去可靠農作物支援。"},{"en":"The phrase describes disturbance caused by a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述問題造成的干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"become clear","meaning":"變得明顯","examples":[{"en":"The vulnerability of the agricultural system begins to become clear.","zh":"農業系統的脆弱性開始變得明顯。"},{"en":"To become clear means to become easy to understand or see.","zh":"變得明顯，指變得容易理解或看見。"},{"en":"A grammar rule becomes clear when the teacher gives simple examples.","zh":"當老師給出簡單例子，文法規則就變得明顯。"},{"en":"If honeybees decline, agriculture’s dependence on one pollinator becomes clear.","zh":"如果蜜蜂減少，農業對單一授粉者的依賴就變得明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something previously hidden becoming obvious.","zh":"這個短語描述先前隱藏的事情變得清楚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, a few wild bees are already being managed for crop pollination.","zh":"事實上，少數野生蜜蜂已經被管理用於農作物授粉。"},{"en":"In fact introduces information that is true and often surprising or stronger than expected.","zh":"事實上，引入真實資料，且通常令人意外或比預期更有力。"},{"en":"Many students think grammar is impossible; in fact, clear patterns can make it manageable.","zh":"許多學生以為文法不可能學懂；事實上，清楚模式可以令它變得可處理。"},{"en":"If wild bees are already managed, alternatives to honeybees are not just theoretical.","zh":"如果野生蜜蜂已被管理，蜜蜂替代方案就不只是理論。"},{"en":"The phrase adds factual clarification.","zh":"這個短語加入事實性澄清。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"wild bees","meaning":"野生蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"Wild bees can sometimes be effective crop pollinators.","zh":"野生蜜蜂有時可以是有效的農作物授粉者。"},{"en":"Wild bees are bee species that live naturally without being kept in managed hives.","zh":"野生蜜蜂，是自然生活而非被養在受管理蜂箱中的蜜蜂物種。"},{"en":"Wild bees may nest in soil, old wood, stems, or field edges.","zh":"野生蜜蜂可能在泥土、舊木、莖或田地邊緣築巢。"},{"en":"If wild bees are protected, they can support both crops and natural plants.","zh":"如果野生蜜蜂受到保護，牠們可以支持農作物和自然植物。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to unmanaged bee species.","zh":"這個短語指不受管理的蜜蜂物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be successfully managed for","meaning":"被成功管理以用於……","examples":[{"en":"A few wild bees are already being successfully managed for crop pollination.","zh":"少數野生蜜蜂已經被成功管理以用於農作物授粉。"},{"en":"To be successfully managed for a purpose means to be controlled or supported well enough to serve that purpose.","zh":"被成功管理以用於某目的，指被妥善控制或支援，足以服務該目的。"},{"en":"A school garden can be successfully managed for science lessons if students water it regularly.","zh":"如果學生定期澆水，學校花園可以被成功管理以用於科學課。"},{"en":"If wild bees are successfully managed, farmers can use them without relying only on honeybees.","zh":"如果野生蜜蜂被成功管理，農民就能使用牠們，而不只依賴蜜蜂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes effective human support for a practical goal.","zh":"這個短語描述為實際目標提供有效人為支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"crop pollination","meaning":"農作物授粉","examples":[{"en":"Some native bees can be used for crop pollination.","zh":"一些本土蜜蜂可以用於農作物授粉。"},{"en":"Crop pollination is the transfer of pollen that helps farm plants produce fruit, seeds, or nuts.","zh":"農作物授粉，是傳送花粉，幫助農場植物產生果實、種子或堅果。"},{"en":"Apple orchards need crop pollination before apples can develop properly.","zh":"蘋果果園需要農作物授粉，蘋果才能正常發育。"},{"en":"If crop pollination is weak, harvest size and quality may fall.","zh":"如果農作物授粉不足，收成數量和品質可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to pollination in farming.","zh":"這個短語指農業中的授粉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"provide native bees in adequate numbers","meaning":"提供足夠數量的本土蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"The challenge is to provide native bees in adequate numbers.","zh":"挑戰是提供足夠數量的本土蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To provide native bees in adequate numbers means to make enough local bees available for the job.","zh":"提供足夠數量的本土蜜蜂，指令有足夠本地蜜蜂可供完成工作。"},{"en":"A school canteen must provide lunch in adequate numbers so every student can eat.","zh":"學校飯堂必須提供足夠數量的午餐，讓每位學生都有得吃。"},{"en":"If farms need millions of flowers pollinated, only a few bees will not be enough.","zh":"如果農場需要為數以百萬計的花授粉，只有少量蜜蜂並不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on supplying enough bees.","zh":"這個短語強調供應足夠蜜蜂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"on a reliable basis","meaning":"以可靠方式","examples":[{"en":"Farmers need native bees on a reliable basis.","zh":"農民需要以可靠方式獲得本土蜜蜂。"},{"en":"On a reliable basis means regularly and dependably, not just once or by chance.","zh":"以可靠方式，指定期而可靠地，而不是只一次或靠運氣。"},{"en":"Students need feedback on a reliable basis if they want to improve writing.","zh":"如果學生想改善寫作，就需要以可靠方式獲得回饋。"},{"en":"If farmers cannot obtain bees reliably, crop pollination becomes risky.","zh":"如果農民不能可靠地取得蜜蜂，農作物授粉就變得有風險。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses dependable availability.","zh":"這個短語強調可靠供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in a fairly short number of years","meaning":"在相當短的幾年內","examples":[{"en":"Researchers hope to provide native bees in a fairly short number of years.","zh":"研究人員希望在相當短的幾年內提供本土蜜蜂。"},{"en":"In a fairly short number of years means within a relatively limited period of several years.","zh":"在相當短的幾年內，指在相對有限的數年時間中。"},{"en":"A student can improve greatly in a fairly short number of years with steady practice.","zh":"如果持續練習，學生可以在相當短的幾年內大幅進步。"},{"en":"If researchers act quickly, alternative pollination systems may become available soon.","zh":"如果研究人員快速行動，替代授粉系統可能不久後可用。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a goal that may be achieved in the near future.","zh":"這個短語暗示可能在不遠將來達成的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in order to","meaning":"為了","examples":[{"en":"Native bees must be provided in adequate numbers in order to service crops.","zh":"為了服務農作物，必須提供足夠數量的本土蜜蜂。"},{"en":"In order to means for the purpose of doing something.","zh":"為了，指以做某事為目的。"},{"en":"Students revise vocabulary in order to answer reading questions more accurately.","zh":"學生為了更準確回答閱讀題而溫習詞彙。"},{"en":"If farms want good harvests, they need enough pollinators in order to fertilise flowers.","zh":"如果農場想有好收成，就需要足夠授粉者為了令花受精。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces purpose.","zh":"這個短語引入目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"millions of flowers per acre","meaning":"每英畝數以百萬計的花","examples":[{"en":"Some crops produce millions of flowers per acre.","zh":"一些農作物每英畝產生數以百萬計的花。"},{"en":"Millions of flowers per acre means an extremely high number of flowers in each acre of farmland.","zh":"每英畝數以百萬計的花，指每英畝農地有極大量花朵。"},{"en":"A large orchard can have millions of flowers when trees bloom at the same time.","zh":"當樹木同時開花，大型果園可以有數以百萬計的花。"},{"en":"If crops produce so many flowers, pollinators must work quickly during flowering season.","zh":"如果農作物產生這麼多花，授粉者必須在花期快速工作。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the scale of pollination needed.","zh":"這個短語顯示所需授粉規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a two- to three-week time frame","meaning":"兩至三星期的時限","examples":[{"en":"Many crops need pollination within a two- to three-week time frame.","zh":"許多農作物需要在兩至三星期的時限內完成授粉。"},{"en":"A two- to three-week time frame is a period lasting about two or three weeks.","zh":"兩至三星期的時限，是大約持續兩或三星期的期間。"},{"en":"A school project may need to be finished within a two- to three-week time frame.","zh":"學校項目可能需要在兩至三星期的時限內完成。"},{"en":"If flowers are ready only for a short time, pollination must happen quickly.","zh":"如果花只有短時間適合授粉，授粉就必須快速發生。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a limited period for action.","zh":"這個短語給出有限行動時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"On the other hand, native bees can be more efficient for certain crops.","zh":"另一方面，本土蜜蜂對某些農作物可能更有效率。"},{"en":"On the other hand introduces a contrasting or balancing point.","zh":"另一方面，引入相反或平衡的觀點。"},{"en":"Online lessons are convenient; on the other hand, students may miss face-to-face discussion.","zh":"網上課堂很方便；另一方面，學生可能錯過面對面討論。"},{"en":"If honeybees are useful, on the other hand native bees may still be better for some crops.","zh":"如果蜜蜂有用，另一方面，本土蜜蜂對某些農作物仍可能更好。"},{"en":"The phrase signals contrast.","zh":"這個短語表示對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"certain crops","meaning":"某些農作物","examples":[{"en":"Native bees can be more efficient pollinators of certain crops.","zh":"本土蜜蜂可以是某些農作物更有效率的授粉者。"},{"en":"Certain crops means some particular crops, not all crops.","zh":"某些農作物，指一些特定農作物，而不是所有農作物。"},{"en":"Certain crops, such as apples or almonds, may need special pollination conditions.","zh":"某些農作物，例如蘋果或杏仁，可能需要特殊授粉條件。"},{"en":"If a native bee works well with certain crops, farmers may use it selectively.","zh":"如果一種本土蜜蜂對某些農作物效果好，農民可能選擇性使用牠。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows a claim to specific examples.","zh":"這個短語把主張限制在特定例子上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"do the job","meaning":"完成工作","examples":[{"en":"Fewer native bees may be needed to do the job.","zh":"可能需要較少本土蜜蜂就能完成工作。"},{"en":"To do the job means to complete the necessary task successfully.","zh":"完成工作，指成功完成所需任務。"},{"en":"One good calculator can do the job if students only need basic arithmetic.","zh":"如果學生只需要基本算術，一部好計算機就能完成工作。"},{"en":"If native bees are efficient, fewer of them may pollinate the same area.","zh":"如果本土蜜蜂效率高，較少數量也能為同一地區授粉。"},{"en":"The phrase means accomplish the required work.","zh":"這個短語指完成所需工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"blue orchard bees","meaning":"藍果園蜂","examples":[{"en":"Blue orchard bees can pollinate apples and almonds efficiently.","zh":"藍果園蜂可以有效為蘋果和杏仁授粉。"},{"en":"Blue orchard bees are a type of native bee known for pollinating orchard crops well.","zh":"藍果園蜂，是一種以善於為果園農作物授粉聞名的本土蜜蜂。"},{"en":"A fruit grower may use blue orchard bees during apple blossom season.","zh":"果農可能在蘋果花季使用藍果園蜂。"},{"en":"If blue orchard bees pollinate efficiently, fewer bees may be needed than honeybees.","zh":"如果藍果園蜂授粉效率高，所需數量可能少於蜜蜂。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific bee species used in crop pollination.","zh":"這個短語命名一種用於農作物授粉的特定蜜蜂物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pollinate a hectare of","meaning":"為一公頃的……授粉","examples":[{"en":"About 750 blue orchard bees can pollinate a hectare of apples.","zh":"大約750隻藍果園蜂可以為一公頃蘋果授粉。"},{"en":"To pollinate a hectare of a crop means to provide pollination across an area of one hectare.","zh":"為一公頃農作物授粉，指為一公頃範圍內的農作物提供授粉。"},{"en":"A team of workers may water a hectare of vegetables in one morning.","zh":"一隊工人可能在一個早上為一公頃蔬菜澆水。"},{"en":"If fewer bees can pollinate a hectare, the species is highly efficient.","zh":"如果較少蜜蜂就能為一公頃授粉，該物種就非常高效。"},{"en":"The phrase links pollination with land area.","zh":"這個短語把授粉與土地面積連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a task that would require","meaning":"一項需要……的任務","examples":[{"en":"This is a task that would require many more honeybees.","zh":"這是一項需要更多蜜蜂的任務。"},{"en":"A task that would require something is a job that needs that resource to be completed.","zh":"一項需要某物的任務，指完成該工作需要該資源。"},{"en":"Moving a piano is a task that would require several strong people.","zh":"搬鋼琴是一項需要幾個強壯人士的任務。"},{"en":"If one crop needs many honeybees, a more efficient native bee can reduce the number required.","zh":"如果一種農作物需要許多蜜蜂，更高效的本土蜜蜂可以減少所需數量。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what a job needs.","zh":"這個短語解釋一項工作需要甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"roughly","meaning":"大約","examples":[{"en":"The same task would require roughly 50,000 to 150,000 honeybees.","zh":"同一項任務大約需要五萬至十五萬隻蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Roughly means approximately, not exactly.","zh":"大約，指約略，而不是完全準確。"},{"en":"The walk from school to the station takes roughly ten minutes.","zh":"從學校步行到車站大約需要十分鐘。"},{"en":"If a number is given roughly, small differences are acceptable.","zh":"如果數字是大約給出的，小差異可以接受。"},{"en":"The word signals an estimate.","zh":"這個詞表示估算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"bee tinkerers","meaning":"蜜蜂應用實驗者","examples":[{"en":"Bee tinkerers are engaged in similar work around the world.","zh":"蜜蜂應用實驗者在世界各地從事類似工作。"},{"en":"Bee tinkerers are people who experiment with ways to use, manage, or improve bees for pollination.","zh":"蜜蜂應用實驗者，是試驗如何使用、管理或改善蜜蜂授粉的人。"},{"en":"A bee tinkerer may test different nest boxes to see which wild bees prefer.","zh":"蜜蜂應用實驗者可能測試不同巢箱，看看野生蜜蜂較喜歡哪種。"},{"en":"If bee tinkerers find better methods, farmers may gain new pollination options.","zh":"如果蜜蜂應用實驗者找到更好方法，農民可能得到新的授粉選項。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests practical experimenters rather than only formal scientists.","zh":"這個短語暗示實用實驗者，而不只是正式科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be engaged in similar work","meaning":"從事類似工作","examples":[{"en":"Researchers in many countries are engaged in similar work.","zh":"許多國家的研究人員正在從事類似工作。"},{"en":"To be engaged in similar work means to be actively doing related tasks or research.","zh":"從事類似工作，指積極進行相關任務或研究。"},{"en":"Two schools may be engaged in similar work if both are developing reading programmes.","zh":"如果兩間學校都在發展閱讀計劃，它們就是從事類似工作。"},{"en":"If scientists around the world study native bees, progress may happen faster.","zh":"如果世界各地科學家都研究本土蜜蜂，進展可能更快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active involvement in related activity.","zh":"這個短語描述積極參與相關活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in many corners of the world","meaning":"在世界各地","examples":[{"en":"Bee researchers are working in many corners of the world.","zh":"蜜蜂研究人員正在世界各地工作。"},{"en":"In many corners of the world means in many different places around the world.","zh":"在世界各地，指在全球許多不同地方。"},{"en":"People use mobile phones in many corners of the world.","zh":"世界各地的人都使用手機。"},{"en":"If researchers in many regions study native bees, solutions may suit different climates.","zh":"如果許多地區的研究者都研究本土蜜蜂，解決方案可能適合不同氣候。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises wide global spread.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛全球分佈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"native pollinator of","meaning":"……的本土授粉者","examples":[{"en":"Centris tarsata is the native pollinator of wild cashew.","zh":"Centris tarsata 是野生腰果的本土授粉者。"},{"en":"The native pollinator of a plant is the local species that naturally pollinates it.","zh":"某植物的本土授粉者，是自然為它授粉的本地物種。"},{"en":"A local bee may be the native pollinator of a wild flower in a forest.","zh":"本地蜜蜂可能是森林中某種野花的本土授粉者。"},{"en":"If a crop has a native pollinator, farmers may support that species instead of importing bees.","zh":"如果一種農作物有本土授粉者，農民可能支持該物種，而不是引入蜜蜂。"},{"en":"The phrase connects one local pollinator with one plant.","zh":"這個短語把一種本地授粉者與一種植物連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"wild cashew","meaning":"野生腰果","examples":[{"en":"Centris tarsata naturally pollinates wild cashew.","zh":"Centris tarsata 自然為野生腰果授粉。"},{"en":"Wild cashew is a naturally growing cashew plant that is not mainly cultivated as a commercial crop.","zh":"野生腰果，是自然生長、並非主要作商業農作物種植的腰果植物。"},{"en":"Scientists may study wild cashew to understand how its natural pollinators work.","zh":"科學家可能研究野生腰果，以了解其天然授粉者如何運作。"},{"en":"If wild cashew depends on a native bee, commercial cashew farms may learn from that relationship.","zh":"如果野生腰果依賴一種本土蜜蜂，商業腰果農場可能從這種關係學習。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to cashew in its non-domesticated or natural form.","zh":"這個短語指未馴化或自然狀態的腰果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"commercial cashew orchards","meaning":"商業腰果果園","examples":[{"en":"Centris tarsata can survive in commercial cashew orchards.","zh":"Centris tarsata 能在商業腰果果園中生存。"},{"en":"Commercial cashew orchards are farms where cashew trees are grown to sell the crop.","zh":"商業腰果果園，是種植腰果樹以出售收成的農場。"},{"en":"A commercial cashew orchard needs reliable pollination to produce nuts for market.","zh":"商業腰果果園需要可靠授粉，以生產可出售的堅果。"},{"en":"If native bees survive in commercial orchards, farmers may use them for crop pollination.","zh":"如果本土蜜蜂能在商業果園中生存，農民可能使用牠們授粉。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to business-focused cashew farms.","zh":"這個短語指以商業為目的的腰果農場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"growers provide","meaning":"種植者提供","examples":[{"en":"Native pollinators can survive if growers provide the right resources.","zh":"如果種植者提供合適資源，本土授粉者就能生存。"},{"en":"Growers provide something means farmers or plant producers supply what is needed.","zh":"種植者提供某物，指農民或植物生產者供應所需東西。"},{"en":"Vegetable growers provide water, fertiliser, and shelter to help crops grow.","zh":"蔬菜種植者提供水、肥料和保護，幫助農作物生長。"},{"en":"If growers provide flowers and nesting sites, pollinators may remain near farms.","zh":"如果種植者提供花和築巢地點，授粉者可能留在農場附近。"},{"en":"The phrase describes farmers supplying support.","zh":"這個短語描述農民提供支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a source of floral oils","meaning":"花油來源","examples":[{"en":"Growers can provide a source of floral oils for native bees.","zh":"種植者可以為本土蜜蜂提供花油來源。"},{"en":"A source of floral oils is a plant or flower that supplies oils collected by certain bees.","zh":"花油來源，是供應某些蜜蜂收集的油分的植物或花。"},{"en":"Some bees need floral oils just as other insects need nectar or pollen.","zh":"一些蜜蜂需要花油，就像其他昆蟲需要花蜜或花粉。"},{"en":"If growers plant oil-producing flowers, certain native bees may survive in orchards.","zh":"如果種植者種植產油花卉，某些本土蜜蜂可能在果園中生存。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a special food resource for bees.","zh":"這個短語指出蜜蜂的一種特殊食物資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"interplant something with","meaning":"將……與……間種","examples":[{"en":"Growers can interplant cashew trees with Caribbean cherry.","zh":"種植者可以將腰果樹與加勒比櫻桃間種。"},{"en":"To interplant one crop with another means to grow them together in the same area.","zh":"將一種作物與另一種間種，指在同一地區一起種植它們。"},{"en":"A gardener may interplant vegetables with herbs to save space and attract insects.","zh":"園丁可能將蔬菜與香草間種，以節省空間並吸引昆蟲。"},{"en":"If cashew is interplanted with flowers, pollinators may find more food nearby.","zh":"如果腰果與花卉間種，授粉者可能在附近找到更多食物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mixed planting.","zh":"這個短語描述混合種植。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Caribbean cherry","meaning":"加勒比櫻桃","examples":[{"en":"Caribbean cherry can provide floral oils for native pollinators.","zh":"加勒比櫻桃可以為本土授粉者提供花油。"},{"en":"Caribbean cherry is a plant mentioned as a companion plant that can support certain bees.","zh":"加勒比櫻桃，是文中提到可支援某些蜜蜂的伴生植物。"},{"en":"A farmer may plant Caribbean cherry near cashew trees to provide extra bee resources.","zh":"農民可能在腰果樹附近種植加勒比櫻桃，以提供額外蜜蜂資源。"},{"en":"If Caribbean cherry supplies floral oils, native bees may remain in the orchard.","zh":"如果加勒比櫻桃供應花油，本土蜜蜂可能留在果園中。"},{"en":"The phrase names a plant used to support pollinators.","zh":"這個短語命名一種用來支援授粉者的植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in certain places","meaning":"在某些地方","examples":[{"en":"In certain places, native bees may already be important pollinators.","zh":"在某些地方，本土蜜蜂可能已經是重要授粉者。"},{"en":"In certain places means in some specific locations, not everywhere.","zh":"在某些地方，指在一些特定地點，而不是所有地方。"},{"en":"In certain places, buses arrive every five minutes, while rural areas have fewer services.","zh":"在某些地方，巴士每五分鐘一班，而鄉郊地區服務較少。"},{"en":"If native bees work well in certain places, local conditions may be important.","zh":"如果本土蜜蜂在某些地方表現良好，本地條件可能很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase limits a claim to particular locations.","zh":"這個短語把主張限制在特定地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"get credit for","meaning":"獲得應有認可","examples":[{"en":"Native bees may be doing more than they are getting credit for.","zh":"本土蜜蜂可能做得比牠們獲得的認可更多。"},{"en":"To get credit for something means to receive recognition for doing it.","zh":"因某事獲得認可，指因做了該事而得到承認。"},{"en":"A quiet student may not get credit for helping the group finish the project.","zh":"安靜的學生幫助小組完成項目，卻可能沒有獲得應有認可。"},{"en":"If wild bees pollinate many crops unnoticed, their importance may be underestimated.","zh":"如果野生蜜蜂默默為許多農作物授粉，其重要性可能被低估。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on recognition or appreciation.","zh":"這個短語強調認可或欣賞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lead a team","meaning":"帶領團隊","examples":[{"en":"Rachael Winfree led a team that studied crop pollination.","zh":"Rachael Winfree 帶領一個研究農作物授粉的團隊。"},{"en":"To lead a team means to guide and organise a group of people working together.","zh":"帶領團隊，指指導和組織一群一起工作的人。"},{"en":"A student may lead a team during a science project by dividing tasks fairly.","zh":"學生可能在科學項目中透過公平分工帶領團隊。"},{"en":"If a researcher leads a team, they coordinate the study and help interpret results.","zh":"如果研究者帶領團隊，他們會協調研究並幫助解讀結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes responsibility for group direction.","zh":"這個短語描述負責群體方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"look at pollination of","meaning":"研究……的授粉情況","examples":[{"en":"The team looked at pollination of four summer crops.","zh":"團隊研究四種夏季農作物的授粉情況。"},{"en":"To look at pollination of crops means to study how those crops are pollinated.","zh":"研究農作物的授粉情況，指研究那些農作物如何被授粉。"},{"en":"A biology class may look at pollination of flowers in the school garden.","zh":"生物課可能研究學校花園中花朵的授粉情況。"},{"en":"If researchers look at pollination carefully, they can identify which insects do the work.","zh":"如果研究人員仔細研究授粉，就能辨認哪些昆蟲完成工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes studying a pollination process.","zh":"這個短語描述研究授粉過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"summer crops","meaning":"夏季農作物","examples":[{"en":"The study focused on four summer crops.","zh":"該研究集中於四種夏季農作物。"},{"en":"Summer crops are crops grown or harvested mainly during the summer season.","zh":"夏季農作物，是主要在夏季種植或收成的農作物。"},{"en":"Watermelons and peppers can be summer crops in warm regions.","zh":"在溫暖地區，西瓜和甜椒可以是夏季農作物。"},{"en":"If summer crops flower during hot months, drought and pollinator activity both matter.","zh":"如果夏季農作物在炎熱月份開花，乾旱和授粉者活動都很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies crops by season.","zh":"這個短語按季節指出農作物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"watermelon","meaning":"西瓜","examples":[{"en":"Watermelon was one of the crops in Winfree’s study.","zh":"西瓜是 Winfree 研究中的農作物之一。"},{"en":"Watermelon is a large sweet fruit with watery flesh and seeds.","zh":"西瓜，是有多汁果肉和種子的大型甜水果。"},{"en":"Families often buy watermelon in summer because it is refreshing.","zh":"家庭常在夏天買西瓜，因為它清爽解渴。"},{"en":"If watermelon flowers are not pollinated, the fruit may not develop properly.","zh":"如果西瓜花沒有被授粉，果實可能不能正常發育。"},{"en":"The word names a crop that depends on successful pollination.","zh":"這個詞命名一種依賴成功授粉的農作物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"peppers","meaning":"甜椒；辣椒","examples":[{"en":"Peppers were included in the study of summer crops.","zh":"甜椒／辣椒被包括在夏季農作物研究中。"},{"en":"Peppers are vegetables or fruits used in cooking, including sweet peppers and hot peppers.","zh":"甜椒或辣椒，是用於烹調的蔬果，包括甜椒和辣椒。"},{"en":"A lunchbox may include peppers in a salad or stir-fry.","zh":"午餐盒可能在沙律或炒菜中加入甜椒。"},{"en":"If pepper plants receive better pollination, fruit quality may improve.","zh":"如果椒類植物得到更好授粉，果實品質可能改善。"},{"en":"The word refers to a common crop with many varieties.","zh":"這個詞指有許多品種的常見農作物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"muskmelon","meaning":"甜瓜","examples":[{"en":"Muskmelon was one of the crops examined by the research team.","zh":"甜瓜是研究團隊考察的農作物之一。"},{"en":"Muskmelon is a sweet melon crop with fragrant flesh.","zh":"甜瓜，是果肉香甜的瓜類農作物。"},{"en":"A fruit shop may sell muskmelon beside watermelon and honeydew.","zh":"水果店可能在西瓜和蜜瓜旁邊售賣甜瓜。"},{"en":"If muskmelon flowers are well pollinated, the fruit can develop more successfully.","zh":"如果甜瓜花授粉良好，果實可以更成功發育。"},{"en":"The word names a melon crop studied for pollination.","zh":"這個詞命名一種被研究授粉情況的瓜類農作物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in the region of","meaning":"在……地區","examples":[{"en":"The farms were in the region of New Jersey and Pennsylvania.","zh":"這些農場位於新澤西州和賓夕凡尼亞州地區。"},{"en":"In the region of a place means in or around that geographical area.","zh":"在某地區，指在該地理區域內或周圍。"},{"en":"A weather warning may cover the region of Hong Kong and nearby coastal cities.","zh":"天氣警告可能涵蓋香港及附近沿岸城市地區。"},{"en":"If farms are in one region, their landscape and climate may shape pollinator activity.","zh":"如果農場位於同一地區，其景觀和氣候可能塑造授粉者活動。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies approximate location.","zh":"這個短語指出約略位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"identify species of","meaning":"辨認……的物種","examples":[{"en":"The team identified 54 species of wild bees.","zh":"團隊辨認出54種野生蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To identify species of something means to recognise and name different biological types.","zh":"辨認某物的物種，指認出並命名不同生物類型。"},{"en":"Students may identify species of trees by looking at leaves and bark.","zh":"學生可能透過觀察葉和樹皮辨認樹木物種。"},{"en":"If researchers identify many bee species, they can measure pollinator diversity.","zh":"如果研究人員辨認出許多蜜蜂物種，就能量度授粉者多樣性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes scientific recognition and classification.","zh":"這個短語描述科學上的辨認和分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"visit these crops","meaning":"到訪這些農作物","examples":[{"en":"Many wild bees visited these crops.","zh":"許多野生蜜蜂到訪這些農作物。"},{"en":"To visit these crops means to land on or move among their flowers, often for food.","zh":"到訪這些農作物，指降落在或穿梭於其花朵之間，通常為了覓食。"},{"en":"Bees visit garden flowers when they collect nectar and pollen.","zh":"蜜蜂收集花蜜和花粉時會到訪花園中的花。"},{"en":"If bees visit crops often, pollination is more likely to happen.","zh":"如果蜜蜂經常到訪農作物，授粉就更可能發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pollinator activity on crop flowers.","zh":"這個短語描述授粉者在農作物花上的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the most important pollinators","meaning":"最重要的授粉者","examples":[{"en":"Wild bees were the most important pollinators in the system.","zh":"野生蜜蜂是該系統中最重要的授粉者。"},{"en":"The most important pollinators are the species that contribute most to pollination.","zh":"最重要的授粉者，是對授粉貢獻最大的物種。"},{"en":"In a small garden, butterflies may be attractive, but bees may be the most important pollinators.","zh":"在小花園中，蝴蝶可能吸引人，但蜜蜂可能是最重要的授粉者。"},{"en":"If wild bees make most flower visits, they may matter more than managed honeybees.","zh":"如果野生蜜蜂佔最多訪花次數，牠們可能比受管理蜜蜂更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main pollination contributors.","zh":"這個短語指出主要授粉貢獻者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"managed honeybees","meaning":"受管理的蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"Managed honeybees were present on many farms.","zh":"受管理的蜜蜂出現在許多農場。"},{"en":"Managed honeybees are honeybees kept and controlled by people in hives.","zh":"受管理的蜜蜂，是由人類在蜂箱中飼養和控制的蜜蜂。"},{"en":"A beekeeper may move managed honeybees to an orchard during blossom season.","zh":"養蜂人可能在花季把受管理的蜜蜂移到果園。"},{"en":"If managed honeybees are used widely, farmers may depend on beekeepers for pollination.","zh":"如果受管理蜜蜂被廣泛使用，農民可能依賴養蜂人授粉。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts kept honeybees with wild pollinators.","zh":"這個短語把人類飼養的蜜蜂與野生授粉者作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be present on","meaning":"出現在……；存在於……","examples":[{"en":"Managed honeybees were present on many of the farms.","zh":"受管理的蜜蜂存在於許多農場。"},{"en":"To be present on a place means to exist or be found there.","zh":"出現在某地，指存在於或可在那裡找到。"},{"en":"Security guards may be present on campus during a school event.","zh":"學校活動期間，保安員可能出現在校園內。"},{"en":"If honeybees are present on farms, they may help pollinate crops there.","zh":"如果蜜蜂出現在農場，牠們可能幫助當地農作物授粉。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being there.","zh":"這個短語描述在某處存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be responsible for","meaning":"負責；佔……","examples":[{"en":"Wild bees were responsible for 62 per cent of flower visits.","zh":"野生蜜蜂負責百分之六十二的訪花次數。"},{"en":"To be responsible for a share means to account for or cause that part of the total.","zh":"負責某比例，指佔總數中的那一部分或造成那部分。"},{"en":"One class may be responsible for half of the recycling collected at school.","zh":"一個班級可能佔學校回收物的一半。"},{"en":"If wild bees are responsible for most visits, they play a major role in pollination.","zh":"如果野生蜜蜂佔大多數訪花次數，牠們在授粉中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"The phrase can mean “account for,” not only “be guilty of.”","zh":"這個短語可以解作「佔」，不只是「要負責任」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"flower visits","meaning":"訪花次數","examples":[{"en":"Wild bees accounted for many flower visits in the study.","zh":"在研究中，野生蜜蜂佔許多訪花次數。"},{"en":"Flower visits are occasions when insects land on or enter flowers.","zh":"訪花次數，是昆蟲降落或進入花朵的次數。"},{"en":"A student counting bees in a garden may record each flower visit in a notebook.","zh":"學生在花園數蜜蜂時，可能在筆記本記錄每次訪花。"},{"en":"If flower visits increase, pollination may improve.","zh":"如果訪花次數增加，授粉可能改善。"},{"en":"The phrase measures pollinator activity.","zh":"這個短語量度授粉者活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"focus specifically on","meaning":"專門聚焦於","examples":[{"en":"Another study focused specifically on watermelon.","zh":"另一項研究專門聚焦於西瓜。"},{"en":"To focus specifically on something means to study or discuss that one thing in particular.","zh":"專門聚焦於某事，指特別研究或討論該一件事。"},{"en":"A teacher may focus specifically on articles if students often misuse “a” and “the.”","zh":"如果學生常誤用 “a” 和 “the”，老師可能專門聚焦於冠詞。"},{"en":"If researchers focus on one crop, they can measure pollination more precisely.","zh":"如果研究人員聚焦於一種農作物，就能更準確量度授粉。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows attention to a specific subject.","zh":"這個短語把注意力收窄到特定主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"colleagues","meaning":"同事；研究伙伴","examples":[{"en":"Winfree and her colleagues studied watermelon pollination.","zh":"Winfree 和她的同事研究西瓜授粉。"},{"en":"Colleagues are people who work with you, usually in the same organisation or project.","zh":"同事，是與你一起工作的人，通常在同一機構或項目中。"},{"en":"A teacher may discuss lesson plans with colleagues after school.","zh":"老師可能放學後與同事討論教案。"},{"en":"If researchers and colleagues share data, a study can become more reliable.","zh":"如果研究人員和同事共享數據，研究可以變得更可靠。"},{"en":"The word refers to work partners.","zh":"這個詞指工作伙伴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"calculate that","meaning":"計算出；估算出","examples":[{"en":"The researchers calculated that native bees alone could provide sufficient pollination.","zh":"研究人員計算出單靠本土蜜蜂就可以提供足夠授粉。"},{"en":"To calculate that means to work something out using numbers, evidence, or data.","zh":"計算出某事，指使用數字、證據或數據推算出來。"},{"en":"A student may calculate that they need 70 marks to reach their target grade.","zh":"學生可能計算出自己需要70分才能達到目標等級。"},{"en":"If researchers calculate pollination levels, they can judge whether bees are enough.","zh":"如果研究人員計算授粉水平，就能判斷蜜蜂是否足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a data-based estimate.","zh":"這個短語引入基於數據的估算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"native bees alone","meaning":"單靠本土蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"Native bees alone could provide sufficient pollination at many farms.","zh":"單靠本土蜜蜂就可以在許多農場提供足夠授粉。"},{"en":"Native bees alone means only native bees, without help from honeybees or other managed pollinators.","zh":"單靠本土蜜蜂，指只靠本土蜜蜂，不靠蜜蜂或其他受管理授粉者。"},{"en":"A student may finish homework alone if no group help is needed.","zh":"如果不需要小組幫助，學生可以單獨完成功課。"},{"en":"If native bees alone are enough, farmers may not need to rent honeybee hives.","zh":"如果單靠本土蜜蜂已足夠，農民可能不需要租用蜜蜂蜂箱。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses independence from other pollinators.","zh":"這個短語強調不依賴其他授粉者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"provide sufficient pollination","meaning":"提供足夠授粉","examples":[{"en":"Native bees could provide sufficient pollination at 90 per cent of the farms studied.","zh":"本土蜜蜂能在研究中百分之九十的農場提供足夠授粉。"},{"en":"To provide sufficient pollination means to give enough pollination for crops to produce normally.","zh":"提供足夠授粉，指給予足夠授粉，使農作物正常生產。"},{"en":"A garden with many bees may provide sufficient pollination for tomatoes and cucumbers.","zh":"有許多蜜蜂的花園，可能為番茄和青瓜提供足夠授粉。"},{"en":"If pollination is sufficient, farmers may get a normal harvest.","zh":"如果授粉足夠，農民可能得到正常收成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes enough pollination, not necessarily maximum pollination.","zh":"這個短語描述足夠授粉，而不一定是最大授粉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"by contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"By contrast, honeybees alone were sufficient at fewer farms.","zh":"相比之下，單靠蜜蜂在較少農場已足夠。"},{"en":"By contrast introduces a clear difference between two facts.","zh":"相比之下，引入兩個事實之間的清楚差異。"},{"en":"The first class finished early; by contrast, the second class needed extra time.","zh":"第一班很早完成；相比之下，第二班需要額外時間。"},{"en":"If native bees were sufficient at more farms, by contrast honeybees performed less well in that comparison.","zh":"如果本土蜜蜂在更多農場已足夠，相比之下，蜜蜂在該比較中表現較弱。"},{"en":"The phrase signals comparison and difference.","zh":"這個短語表示比較和差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"at only 78 per cent of farms","meaning":"只在百分之七十八的農場","examples":[{"en":"Honeybees alone could provide sufficient pollination at only 78 per cent of farms.","zh":"單靠蜜蜂只在百分之七十八的農場能提供足夠授粉。"},{"en":"At only 78 per cent of farms means in just 78 out of every 100 farms.","zh":"只在百分之七十八的農場，指每一百個農場中只有七十八個。"},{"en":"If a service works at only 78 per cent of schools, many students are still not covered.","zh":"如果一項服務只在百分之七十八的學校有效，仍有許多學生未被覆蓋。"},{"en":"If honeybees alone are sufficient at fewer farms than native bees, wild pollinators may be more important than expected.","zh":"如果單靠蜜蜂足夠的農場比本土蜜蜂少，野生授粉者可能比預期更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a limited percentage.","zh":"這個短語給出有限百分比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"not typical of","meaning":"並非……的典型例子","examples":[{"en":"The region is not typical of the way most food is produced.","zh":"該地區並非大部分食物生產方式的典型例子。"},{"en":"Not typical of something means not representative of the usual pattern.","zh":"並非某事的典型例子，指不能代表一般模式。"},{"en":"A quiet Saturday is not typical of a busy shopping mall.","zh":"安靜的星期六並不是繁忙商場的典型情況。"},{"en":"If one study area is unusual, its results may not apply everywhere.","zh":"如果一個研究地區不尋常，其結果未必適用於所有地方。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against overgeneralising.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要過度概括。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the way most food is produced","meaning":"大部分食物的生產方式","examples":[{"en":"Winfree says the region is not typical of the way most food is produced.","zh":"Winfree 說，該地區並非大部分食物生產方式的典型例子。"},{"en":"The way most food is produced means the common methods used to grow, process, and supply food.","zh":"大部分食物的生產方式，指種植、加工和供應食物的常見方法。"},{"en":"In many places, most food is produced through large farms and long supply chains.","zh":"在許多地方，大部分食物是透過大型農場和長供應鏈生產。"},{"en":"If a study region uses smaller mixed farms, it may differ from mainstream food production.","zh":"如果研究地區使用較小型混合農場，它可能不同於主流食物生產方式。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the normal food-production system.","zh":"這個短語指一般食物生產系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"admit","meaning":"承認","examples":[{"en":"Winfree admits that her study region is unusual.","zh":"Winfree 承認她的研究地區不尋常。"},{"en":"To admit something means to accept or acknowledge that it is true.","zh":"承認某事，指接受或承認它是真的。"},{"en":"A student may admit that they did not revise enough before the test.","zh":"學生可能承認自己測驗前溫習不足。"},{"en":"If a researcher admits a limitation, their argument becomes more honest.","zh":"如果研究者承認限制，其論點會變得更誠實。"},{"en":"The word often introduces a concession.","zh":"這個詞常引入讓步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the Delaware Valley","meaning":"特拉華河谷","examples":[{"en":"Many farms in the Delaware Valley are relatively small.","zh":"特拉華河谷的許多農場相對較小。"},{"en":"The Delaware Valley is a region around the Delaware River in the eastern United States.","zh":"特拉華河谷，是美國東部特拉華河周圍的地區。"},{"en":"A geography class may study the Delaware Valley to compare farms, towns, and suburbs.","zh":"地理課可能研究特拉華河谷，以比較農場、城鎮和郊區。"},{"en":"If farms there are small and mixed with suburbs, pollinator habitats may be more varied.","zh":"如果當地農場較小並與郊區混合，授粉者棲息地可能更多樣。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific regional landscape.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定地區景觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"relatively small","meaning":"相對較小","examples":[{"en":"Most farms and farm fields in the region are relatively small.","zh":"該地區大多數農場和農田相對較小。"},{"en":"Relatively small means small compared with other examples or the usual size.","zh":"相對較小，指與其他例子或一般大小相比較小。"},{"en":"A classroom may feel relatively small compared with a school hall.","zh":"與學校禮堂相比，課室可能感覺相對較小。"},{"en":"If farm fields are relatively small, wild bees may reach crops more easily from nearby habitats.","zh":"如果農田相對較小，野生蜜蜂可能更容易從附近棲息地到達農作物。"},{"en":"The phrase compares size, not absolute measurement.","zh":"這個短語比較大小，而不是絕對量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a variety of crops","meaning":"多種農作物","examples":[{"en":"Each farmer typically grows a variety of crops.","zh":"每位農民通常種植多種農作物。"},{"en":"A variety of crops means several different kinds of crops.","zh":"多種農作物，指幾種不同農作物。"},{"en":"A small farm may grow a variety of crops, such as beans, tomatoes, melons, and herbs.","zh":"小農場可能種植多種農作物，例如豆、番茄、瓜類和香草。"},{"en":"If farms grow varied crops, pollinators may find flowers at different times.","zh":"如果農場種植多樣作物，授粉者可能在不同時間找到花。"},{"en":"The phrase describes agricultural diversity.","zh":"這個短語描述農業多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be interspersed with","meaning":"與……交錯分佈","examples":[{"en":"Farms are interspersed with suburbs and other types of land use.","zh":"農場與郊區和其他土地用途交錯分佈。"},{"en":"To be interspersed with something means to be mixed or scattered among it.","zh":"與某物交錯分佈，指與它混合或散佈在其中。"},{"en":"Shops may be interspersed with homes along a busy street.","zh":"商店可能與住宅在繁忙街道上交錯分佈。"},{"en":"If farms are interspersed with gardens and woodlots, bees may find more habitats.","zh":"如果農場與花園和小林地交錯分佈，蜜蜂可能找到更多棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a mixed pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述混合模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"suburbs","meaning":"郊區","examples":[{"en":"Farms in the region are interspersed with suburbs.","zh":"該地區的農場與郊區交錯分佈。"},{"en":"Suburbs are residential areas outside or around a city.","zh":"郊區，是城市外圍或周圍的住宅地區。"},{"en":"Many families live in suburbs and travel to the city for work.","zh":"許多家庭住在郊區，並到城市工作。"},{"en":"If suburbs include gardens and trees, they may provide resources for wild bees.","zh":"如果郊區有花園和樹木，它們可能為野生蜜蜂提供資源。"},{"en":"The word refers to outer residential communities.","zh":"這個詞指城市外圍住宅社區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"types of land use","meaning":"土地用途類型","examples":[{"en":"Different types of land use can affect bee conservation.","zh":"不同土地用途類型可以影響蜜蜂保育。"},{"en":"Types of land use are ways land is used, such as farming, housing, parks, roads, or woodland.","zh":"土地用途類型，是土地被使用的方式，例如農業、住宅、公園、道路或林地。"},{"en":"A city map may show different types of land use in different colours.","zh":"城市地圖可能用不同顏色顯示不同土地用途類型。"},{"en":"If land use is mixed, wildlife may find more varied habitats.","zh":"如果土地用途混合，野生生物可能找到更多樣棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the functions assigned to land.","zh":"這個短語描述土地被賦予的功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"opportunities for homeowners to","meaning":"讓業主有機會去","examples":[{"en":"The landscape creates opportunities for homeowners to get involved in bee conservation.","zh":"該景觀讓業主有機會參與蜜蜂保育。"},{"en":"Opportunities for homeowners to do something are chances for house owners to take action.","zh":"讓業主有機會做某事，指給房屋擁有人採取行動的機會。"},{"en":"A recycling scheme creates opportunities for homeowners to reduce waste.","zh":"回收計劃讓業主有機會減少廢物。"},{"en":"If gardens can support bees, homeowners have a role in conservation.","zh":"如果花園能支援蜜蜂，業主就在保育中有角色。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how ordinary residents can participate.","zh":"這個短語顯示普通居民如何參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"get involved in","meaning":"參與","examples":[{"en":"Homeowners can get involved in bee conservation.","zh":"業主可以參與蜜蜂保育。"},{"en":"To get involved in something means to take part in it actively.","zh":"參與某事，指積極加入其中。"},{"en":"Students can get involved in a school charity event by designing posters.","zh":"學生可以透過設計海報參與學校慈善活動。"},{"en":"If residents get involved in conservation, small gardens can become useful habitats.","zh":"如果居民參與保育，小花園可以變成有用棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active participation.","zh":"這個短語描述積極參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"bee conservation","meaning":"蜜蜂保育","examples":[{"en":"Bee conservation can involve farmers and homeowners.","zh":"蜜蜂保育可以涉及農民和業主。"},{"en":"Bee conservation is the protection and support of bee populations and habitats.","zh":"蜜蜂保育，是保護和支援蜜蜂種群及棲息地。"},{"en":"Planting wild flowers in a garden can be part of bee conservation.","zh":"在花園種植野花可以是蜜蜂保育的一部分。"},{"en":"If bee conservation succeeds, pollination services may become more reliable.","zh":"如果蜜蜂保育成功，授粉服務可能變得更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to actions that help bees survive.","zh":"這個短語指幫助蜜蜂生存的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a bee-friendly patchwork","meaning":"有利蜜蜂生存的拼合式景觀","examples":[{"en":"The landscape is a bee-friendly patchwork.","zh":"該景觀是有利蜜蜂生存的拼合式景觀。"},{"en":"A bee-friendly patchwork is a mixed landscape with different small habitats and food sources useful to bees.","zh":"有利蜜蜂生存的拼合式景觀，是有不同小棲息地和食物來源、對蜜蜂有用的混合景觀。"},{"en":"Gardens, field edges, woodlots, and fallow fields can form a bee-friendly patchwork.","zh":"花園、田邊、小林地和休耕田可以形成有利蜜蜂生存的拼合式景觀。"},{"en":"If bees can move among these patches, they may find food and nesting places.","zh":"如果蜜蜂能在這些小區塊之間移動，就可能找到食物和築巢地點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a varied landscape that supports bees.","zh":"這個短語描述支援蜜蜂的多樣景觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"nesting habitat","meaning":"築巢棲息地","examples":[{"en":"The landscape provides a variety of nesting habitat.","zh":"該景觀提供多種築巢棲息地。"},{"en":"Nesting habitat is the place where animals can build nests or raise young.","zh":"築巢棲息地，是動物可以築巢或養育幼體的地方。"},{"en":"Birds may use trees as nesting habitat, while some bees use soil or hollow stems.","zh":"鳥類可能使用樹木作築巢棲息地，而一些蜜蜂使用泥土或空心莖。"},{"en":"If nesting habitat disappears, pollinator populations may fall even when flowers remain.","zh":"如果築巢棲息地消失，即使花仍存在，授粉者種群也可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to places suitable for reproduction.","zh":"這個短語指適合繁殖的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"floral resources","meaning":"花卉資源","examples":[{"en":"Wild bees need floral resources as food.","zh":"野生蜜蜂需要花卉資源作為食物。"},{"en":"Floral resources are flowers and flower products such as nectar, pollen, or oils that animals use.","zh":"花卉資源，是花和花產品，例如動物使用的花蜜、花粉或花油。"},{"en":"A garden with many flowering plants provides floral resources for bees.","zh":"有許多開花植物的花園為蜜蜂提供花卉資源。"},{"en":"If floral resources are available through the season, pollinators can survive longer.","zh":"如果整個季節都有花卉資源，授粉者可以生存更久。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to food supplied by flowers.","zh":"這個短語指由花提供的食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"distributed among","meaning":"分佈於……之間","examples":[{"en":"Nesting habitat and floral resources are distributed among different land types.","zh":"築巢棲息地和花卉資源分佈於不同土地類型之間。"},{"en":"Distributed among means spread across or shared between several places or groups.","zh":"分佈於……之間，指散佈在幾個地方或群體之間。"},{"en":"Homework tasks may be distributed among group members to make the project fair.","zh":"功課任務可能分配在小組成員之間，使項目公平。"},{"en":"If bee resources are distributed among gardens, fields, and woodlots, bees can use the whole landscape.","zh":"如果蜜蜂資源分佈於花園、田地和小林地之間，蜜蜂就能使用整個景觀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes spread across different locations.","zh":"這個短語描述分散在不同地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"weedy field margins","meaning":"長有雜草的田邊","examples":[{"en":"Weedy field margins can support wild bees.","zh":"長有雜草的田邊可以支援野生蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Weedy field margins are field edges where wild plants and weeds grow.","zh":"長有雜草的田邊，是野生植物和雜草生長的田地邊緣。"},{"en":"A farmer may leave weedy field margins instead of clearing every plant.","zh":"農民可能保留長有雜草的田邊，而不是清除每一株植物。"},{"en":"If weedy field margins contain flowers, bees can feed near crops.","zh":"如果長有雜草的田邊有花，蜜蜂就能在農作物附近覓食。"},{"en":"The phrase describes untidy but ecologically useful field edges.","zh":"這個短語描述不整潔但具生態價值的田邊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"fallow fields","meaning":"休耕田","examples":[{"en":"Fallow fields can provide habitat for pollinators.","zh":"休耕田可以為授粉者提供棲息地。"},{"en":"Fallow fields are fields left unplanted for a period so the land can rest.","zh":"休耕田，是暫時不種植、讓土地休息的田地。"},{"en":"A farmer may leave one field fallow while using another for vegetables.","zh":"農民可能讓一塊田休耕，同時用另一塊田種蔬菜。"},{"en":"If fallow fields grow wild flowers, they can support bees and other insects.","zh":"如果休耕田長出野花，就能支援蜜蜂和其他昆蟲。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to resting farmland.","zh":"這個短語指正在休息的農地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"suburban neighborhoods","meaning":"郊區社區","examples":[{"en":"Suburban neighborhoods can provide resources for bees.","zh":"郊區社區可以為蜜蜂提供資源。"},{"en":"Suburban neighborhoods are residential areas outside or around a city.","zh":"郊區社區，是城市外圍或周圍的住宅區。"},{"en":"A suburban neighborhood may have gardens, trees, lawns, and small parks.","zh":"郊區社區可能有花園、樹木、草坪和小公園。"},{"en":"If residents plant flowers, suburban neighborhoods can become useful pollinator habitats.","zh":"如果居民種花，郊區社區可以成為有用的授粉者棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to communities in the suburbs.","zh":"這個短語指郊區中的社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"semi-natural habitat","meaning":"半自然棲息地","examples":[{"en":"Semi-natural habitat helps support wild pollinators.","zh":"半自然棲息地有助支援野生授粉者。"},{"en":"Semi-natural habitat is land that is partly natural but still influenced by human activity.","zh":"半自然棲息地，是部分自然但仍受人類活動影響的土地。"},{"en":"A field edge with wild plants beside a farm can be semi-natural habitat.","zh":"農場旁長有野生植物的田邊可以是半自然棲息地。"},{"en":"If semi-natural habitat remains near crops, wild bees may survive there.","zh":"如果半自然棲息地留在農作物附近，野生蜜蜂可能在那裡生存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a habitat between fully wild and fully managed.","zh":"這個短語描述介乎完全野生和完全管理之間的棲息地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"old woodlots","meaning":"舊小林地","examples":[{"en":"Old woodlots can provide habitat for wild bees.","zh":"舊小林地可以為野生蜜蜂提供棲息地。"},{"en":"Old woodlots are small areas of old trees or woodland.","zh":"舊小林地，是有老樹或林木的小片林地。"},{"en":"A farm with old woodlots nearby may support birds, insects, and bees.","zh":"附近有舊小林地的農場可能支援鳥類、昆蟲和蜜蜂。"},{"en":"If old woodlots are removed, wild bees may lose nesting places.","zh":"如果舊小林地被移除，野生蜜蜂可能失去築巢地點。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to small established wooded areas.","zh":"這個短語指已存在一段時間的小型林地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"at a relatively small scale","meaning":"以相對小的規模","examples":[{"en":"The bee-friendly landscape exists at a relatively small scale.","zh":"這種有利蜜蜂的景觀以相對小的規模存在。"},{"en":"At a relatively small scale means in a limited size or local area compared with larger systems.","zh":"以相對小的規模，指與更大系統相比，大小或本地範圍有限。"},{"en":"A school garden works at a relatively small scale compared with a city park.","zh":"與城市公園相比，學校花園以相對小的規模運作。"},{"en":"If conservation works at a small scale, homeowners and small farmers can participate.","zh":"如果保育能以小規模運作，業主和小農民就可以參與。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limited but meaningful scope.","zh":"這個短語描述有限但有意義的範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"pollinator-friendly farming practices","meaning":"有利授粉者的耕作方式","examples":[{"en":"Pollinator-friendly farming practices can support both crops and wild species.","zh":"有利授粉者的耕作方式可以支援農作物和野生物種。"},{"en":"Pollinator-friendly farming practices are farming methods that help bees and other pollinators survive.","zh":"有利授粉者的耕作方式，是幫助蜜蜂和其他授粉者生存的農業方法。"},{"en":"Farmers may plant wildflower strips as a pollinator-friendly farming practice.","zh":"農民可能種植野花帶，作為有利授粉者的耕作方式。"},{"en":"If farms reduce pesticide harm and provide habitat, pollination may improve.","zh":"如果農場減少殺蟲劑傷害並提供棲息地，授粉可能改善。"},{"en":"The phrase describes farming that supports useful insects.","zh":"這個短語描述支援有益昆蟲的農業方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"aid pollination","meaning":"幫助授粉","examples":[{"en":"These practices would aid pollination of agricultural crops.","zh":"這些做法會幫助農作物授粉。"},{"en":"To aid pollination means to help pollen move between flowers so plants can reproduce.","zh":"幫助授粉，指協助花粉在花之間傳送，使植物能繁殖。"},{"en":"Planting flowers near vegetables can aid pollination in a home garden.","zh":"在蔬菜附近種花可以幫助家庭花園授粉。"},{"en":"If pollination is aided, crops may produce more fruit or seeds.","zh":"如果授粉得到幫助，農作物可能產生更多果實或種子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes helping the pollination process.","zh":"這個短語描述協助授粉過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agricultural crops","meaning":"農作物","examples":[{"en":"Pollinator-friendly practices can aid pollination of agricultural crops.","zh":"有利授粉者的做法可以幫助農作物授粉。"},{"en":"Agricultural crops are plants grown on farms for food, fibre, oil, or other products.","zh":"農作物，是在農場種植、用於食物、纖維、油或其他產品的植物。"},{"en":"Wheat, apples, cotton, and almonds are agricultural crops.","zh":"小麥、蘋果、棉花和杏仁都是農作物。"},{"en":"If agricultural crops lack pollination, harvests may decline.","zh":"如果農作物缺乏授粉，收成可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to farm-grown plants.","zh":"這個短語指農場種植的植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"serve as a key element in","meaning":"成為……的關鍵元素","examples":[{"en":"Pollinator-friendly farming can serve as a key element in conservation strategy.","zh":"有利授粉者的耕作可以成為保育策略的關鍵元素。"},{"en":"To serve as a key element in something means to be an important part of it.","zh":"成為某事的關鍵元素，指成為它的重要部分。"},{"en":"Clear communication can serve as a key element in a successful group project.","zh":"清楚溝通可以成為成功小組項目的關鍵元素。"},{"en":"If farms support pollinators, they become part of a wider conservation plan.","zh":"如果農場支援授粉者，它們就成為更廣泛保育計劃的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies an important role within a larger system.","zh":"這個短語指出較大系統中的重要角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"overall conservation strategy","meaning":"整體保育策略","examples":[{"en":"Wild pollinators need an overall conservation strategy.","zh":"野生授粉者需要整體保育策略。"},{"en":"An overall conservation strategy is a broad plan for protecting species and habitats.","zh":"整體保育策略，是保護物種和棲息地的廣泛計劃。"},{"en":"A city may create an overall conservation strategy for parks, trees, wetlands, and wildlife.","zh":"城市可能為公園、樹木、濕地和野生生物制定整體保育策略。"},{"en":"If pollinators face many threats, one small action may not be enough.","zh":"如果授粉者面對許多威脅，單一小行動可能不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a complete protection plan.","zh":"這個短語描述完整保護計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"wild pollinators","meaning":"野生授粉者","examples":[{"en":"Pollinator-friendly farming can help conserve wild pollinators.","zh":"有利授粉者的耕作可以幫助保育野生授粉者。"},{"en":"Wild pollinators are unmanaged animals or insects that pollinate plants in natural or farm settings.","zh":"野生授粉者，是在自然或農場環境中為植物授粉的不受管理動物或昆蟲。"},{"en":"Wild pollinators may include bees, butterflies, flies, moths, and beetles.","zh":"野生授粉者可能包括蜜蜂、蝴蝶、蒼蠅、蛾和甲蟲。"},{"en":"If wild pollinators are conserved, both crops and wild plants may benefit.","zh":"如果野生授粉者受到保育，農作物和野生植物都可能受益。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to pollinators living outside managed systems.","zh":"這個短語指生活在受管理系統以外的授粉者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"aid other wild species","meaning":"也幫助其他野生物種","examples":[{"en":"Pollinator-friendly practices often aid other wild species as well.","zh":"有利授粉者的做法通常也幫助其他野生物種。"},{"en":"To aid other wild species means to help other animals or plants that live naturally in the area.","zh":"幫助其他野生物種，指支援當地自然生活的其他動物或植物。"},{"en":"Planting hedges may aid birds, insects, and small mammals.","zh":"種植樹籬可能幫助鳥類、昆蟲和小型哺乳動物。"},{"en":"If farms provide habitat for bees, they may also support other wildlife.","zh":"如果農場為蜜蜂提供棲息地，也可能支援其他野生生物。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one conservation action can have wider benefits.","zh":"這個短語顯示一項保育行動可以有更廣泛好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"implement these practices","meaning":"實施這些做法","examples":[{"en":"Not all farmers will be able to implement these practices.","zh":"並非所有農民都能實施這些做法。"},{"en":"To implement these practices means to put these methods into action.","zh":"實施這些做法，指把這些方法付諸行動。"},{"en":"A school may implement new reading practices by changing homework and lesson routines.","zh":"學校可能透過改變功課和課堂常規來實施新的閱讀做法。"},{"en":"If farmers lack money or land, they may struggle to implement pollinator-friendly methods.","zh":"如果農民缺乏金錢或土地，可能難以實施有利授粉者的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving from idea to action.","zh":"這個短語描述由想法走向行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"suggest a shift to","meaning":"建議轉向","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are suggesting a shift to a more diverse agricultural system.","zh":"研究人員建議轉向更 多元的農業系統。"},{"en":"To suggest a shift to something means to recommend changing direction toward it.","zh":"建議轉向某事，指建議改變方向朝向它。"},{"en":"A doctor may suggest a shift to healthier meals and regular exercise.","zh":"醫生可能建議轉向較健康飲食和定期運動。"},{"en":"If one pollinator system is risky, researchers may suggest a shift to diversity.","zh":"如果單一授粉者系統有風險，研究人員可能建議轉向多樣化。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a recommended change.","zh":"這個短語引入建議中的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a polyglot agricultural system","meaning":"多元混合農業系統","examples":[{"en":"Researchers suggest a polyglot agricultural system using different bee species.","zh":"研究人員建議使用不同蜜蜂物種的多元混合農業系統。"},{"en":"A polyglot agricultural system is a mixed system that uses several pollinator species rather than only one.","zh":"多元混合農業系統，是使用幾種授粉物種而不是只用一種的混合系統。"},{"en":"A multilingual school is similar because it uses more than one language.","zh":"多語學校也類似，因為它使用多於一種語言。"},{"en":"If agriculture uses different bees for different crops, it may become more resilient.","zh":"如果農業為不同農作物使用不同蜜蜂，它可能更有韌性。"},{"en":"The phrase uses “polyglot” to mean diverse and mixed.","zh":"這個短語用 “polyglot” 表示多樣和混合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"small-scale farms","meaning":"小規模農場","examples":[{"en":"Native bees may be enough for some small-scale farms.","zh":"對一些小規模農場來說，本土蜜蜂可能已經足夠。"},{"en":"Small-scale farms are farms that operate on a limited size or with modest production.","zh":"小規模農場，是以有限規模或中小產量運作的農場。"},{"en":"A family-run vegetable farm can be a small-scale farm.","zh":"家庭經營的蔬菜農場可以是小規模農場。"},{"en":"If a farm is small and mixed, local wild bees may pollinate enough crops.","zh":"如果農場小而混合，本地野生蜜蜂可能足以為農作物授粉。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts smaller farms with large industrial operations.","zh":"這個短語把較小農場與大型工業化經營作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"all that is needed","meaning":"所需要的全部","examples":[{"en":"For some farms, native bees may be all that is needed.","zh":"對一些農場來說，本土蜜蜂可能就是所需要的全部。"},{"en":"All that is needed means everything necessary, with nothing more required.","zh":"所需要的全部，指一切必要東西，無需更多。"},{"en":"For a short homework task, a pencil may be all that is needed.","zh":"對短功課來說，一支鉛筆可能就是所需要的全部。"},{"en":"If native bees provide enough pollination, extra managed hives may not be necessary.","zh":"如果本土蜜蜂提供足夠授粉，額外受管理蜂箱可能沒有必要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses sufficiency.","zh":"這個短語強調足夠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"larger operations","meaning":"較大型的農業經營","examples":[{"en":"Larger operations may need several types of managed bees.","zh":"較大型的農業經營可能需要幾種受管理蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Larger operations are bigger businesses or farms with greater scale and production needs.","zh":"較大型經營，是規模和生產需要較大的企業或農場。"},{"en":"A larger restaurant operation may need more staff than a small café.","zh":"較大型餐廳經營可能比小咖啡店需要更多員工。"},{"en":"If a farm covers many fields, it may need more planned pollination support.","zh":"如果農場覆蓋許多田地，就可能需要更多有計劃的授粉支援。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to larger-scale agricultural businesses.","zh":"這個短語指較大規模的農業企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a suite of managed bees","meaning":"一組受管理的蜂種","examples":[{"en":"Larger farms may use a suite of managed bees.","zh":"較大型農場可能使用一組受管理的蜂種。"},{"en":"A suite of managed bees means a set of different bee species controlled or supported by people.","zh":"一組受管理的蜂種，指由人類控制或支援的幾種不同蜜蜂物種。"},{"en":"A hospital may use a suite of tools to diagnose a patient, not just one test.","zh":"醫院可能使用一組工具診斷病人，而不只是一項測試。"},{"en":"If farms use a suite of bees, each species can serve different crops or conditions.","zh":"如果農場使用一組蜜蜂，每種物種都可服務不同農作物或條件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a grouped set of managed pollinators.","zh":"這個短語描述一組受管理授粉者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"fill the generalist role","meaning":"擔當廣泛授粉者的角色","examples":[{"en":"Honeybees can fill the generalist role in crop pollination.","zh":"蜜蜂可以在農作物授粉中擔當廣泛授粉者的角色。"},{"en":"To fill the generalist role means to take the broad, flexible job of serving many different crops.","zh":"擔當廣泛角色，指承擔服務許多不同農作物的寬泛而靈活工作。"},{"en":"In a small office, one assistant may fill the generalist role by handling many tasks.","zh":"在小辦公室中，一名助理可能透過處理多項任務來擔當廣泛角色。"},{"en":"If honeybees pollinate many crops, they can support the wide part of the system.","zh":"如果蜜蜂為許多農作物授粉，就能支援系統中較廣泛的部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes taking a broad, multi-purpose role.","zh":"這個短語描述承擔廣泛、多用途角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"pollinate specific crops","meaning":"為特定農作物授粉","examples":[{"en":"Other native bees can pollinate specific crops.","zh":"其他本土蜜蜂可以為特定農作物授粉。"},{"en":"To pollinate specific crops means to provide pollination for particular crop types.","zh":"為特定農作物授粉，指為某些特定農作物類型提供授粉。"},{"en":"A specialist tutor may help students with specific exam papers rather than every subject.","zh":"專科補習老師可能幫助學生處理特定試卷，而不是所有科目。"},{"en":"If a native bee works especially well on apples, it can pollinate that crop efficiently.","zh":"如果一種本土蜜蜂特別適合蘋果，它就能有效為該作物授粉。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts specialised pollination with general pollination.","zh":"這個短語把專門授粉與廣泛授粉作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be augmented by","meaning":"由……補充；由……加強","examples":[{"en":"Managed bees could be augmented by free pollination services from wild pollinators.","zh":"受管理蜜蜂可以由野生授粉者的免費授粉服務補充。"},{"en":"To be augmented by something means to be strengthened, increased, or supported by it.","zh":"由某物補充或加強，指被它增強、增加或支援。"},{"en":"Classroom teaching can be augmented by online practice exercises.","zh":"課堂教學可以由網上練習題補充。"},{"en":"If managed bees are augmented by wild pollinators, the whole system becomes less fragile.","zh":"如果受管理蜜蜂由野生授粉者補充，整個系統就較不脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adding support to improve something.","zh":"這個短語描述加入支援以改善某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"free pollination services","meaning":"免費授粉服務","examples":[{"en":"Wild pollinators can provide free pollination services.","zh":"野生授粉者可以提供免費授粉服務。"},{"en":"Free pollination services are pollination benefits provided naturally without direct payment.","zh":"免費授粉服務，是自然提供、無需直接付款的授粉好處。"},{"en":"Bees in a garden provide free pollination services when they help fruit trees produce fruit.","zh":"花園中的蜜蜂幫助果樹結果時，就是提供免費授粉服務。"},{"en":"If farms protect wild pollinators, they may receive useful pollination without renting hives.","zh":"如果農場保護野生授粉者，就可能不用租蜂箱也得到有用授粉。"},{"en":"The phrase treats natural pollination as a valuable service.","zh":"這個短語把自然授粉視為有價值服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"resurgent wild pollinators","meaning":"重新興盛的野生授粉者","examples":[{"en":"Resurgent wild pollinators could support agricultural systems.","zh":"重新興盛的野生授粉者可以支援農業系統。"},{"en":"Resurgent wild pollinators are wild pollinator populations that are recovering or becoming strong again.","zh":"重新興盛的野生授粉者，是正在恢復或重新變強的野生授粉者種群。"},{"en":"A resurgent local bird population may return after parks restore trees.","zh":"公園恢復樹木後，本地鳥類種群可能重新興盛。"},{"en":"If wild pollinators become resurgent, farms may gain more natural pollination support.","zh":"如果野生授粉者重新興盛，農場可能得到更多自然授粉支援。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests recovery after decline.","zh":"這個短語暗示衰退後的恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"have an opportunity to","meaning":"有機會去","examples":[{"en":"Farmers still have an opportunity to build a more resilient system.","zh":"農民仍有機會建立更有韌性的系統。"},{"en":"To have an opportunity to do something means to have a chance to do it.","zh":"有機會做某事，指有做該事的機會。"},{"en":"Students have an opportunity to improve when teachers give clear feedback.","zh":"當老師給清楚回饋，學生就有機會改善。"},{"en":"If farmers act before pollination systems fail, they can build better alternatives.","zh":"如果農民在授粉系統失敗前行動，就能建立更好的替代方案。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a chance for positive action.","zh":"這個短語暗示正面行動的機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"replace something with","meaning":"以……取代……","examples":[{"en":"Researchers want to replace a risky monoculture with a diverse system.","zh":"研究人員想以多元系統取代高風險單一化模式。"},{"en":"To replace something with another thing means to remove the first and use the second instead.","zh":"以某物取代另一物，指移除第一個，改用第二個。"},{"en":"A school may replace paper notices with online messages.","zh":"學校可能以網上信息取代紙本通告。"},{"en":"If agriculture replaces one-pollinator dependence with diversity, it may become safer.","zh":"如果農業以多樣性取代單一授粉者依賴，就可能變得更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes substitution.","zh":"這個短語描述替換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a risky monoculture","meaning":"高風險單一化模式","examples":[{"en":"Dependence on one pollinator creates a risky monoculture.","zh":"依賴一種授粉者造成高風險單一化模式。"},{"en":"A risky monoculture is a system that depends too heavily on one crop, species, or method.","zh":"高風險單一化模式，是過度依賴一種作物、物種或方法的系統。"},{"en":"A farm growing only one crop may become a risky monoculture if disease attacks that crop.","zh":"如果疾病攻擊單一作物，只種一種作物的農場可能成為高風險單一化模式。"},{"en":"If pollination depends on one bee species, the system has little backup.","zh":"如果授粉依賴一種蜜蜂物種，系統就幾乎沒有後備。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that lack of diversity creates danger.","zh":"這個短語警告缺乏多樣性會造成危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"diverse, resilient, and robust","meaning":"多元、有韌性且穩健","examples":[{"en":"A better agricultural system would be diverse, resilient, and robust.","zh":"更好的農業系統會是多元、有韌性且穩健的。"},{"en":"Diverse, resilient, and robust means varied, able to recover, and strong under pressure.","zh":"多元、有韌性且穩健，指多樣、能恢復，並在壓力下強健。"},{"en":"A good study plan is diverse, resilient, and robust if it includes reading, writing, rest, and backup time.","zh":"如果學習計劃包括閱讀、寫作、休息和後備時間，就是多元、有韌性且穩健。"},{"en":"If farming uses many pollinators and habitats, it can better survive disease or climate shocks.","zh":"如果農業使用多種授粉者和棲息地，就能更好承受疾病或氣候衝擊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong system built on variety.","zh":"這個短語描述建立在多樣性上的強大系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"agree with the claims of","meaning":"與……的主張一致","examples":[{"en":"Students must decide whether the statements agree with the claims of the writer.","zh":"學生必須判斷陳述是否與作者的主張一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the claims of the writer means to match what the writer says or argues.","zh":"與作者的主張一致，指與作者所說或論證的內容相符。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students should check the passage before saying a statement agrees.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先檢查文章，再說陳述一致。"},{"en":"If a statement changes the writer’s meaning, it does not agree with the claim.","zh":"如果陳述改變作者意思，就不符合主張。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in questions about the writer’s view.","zh":"這個短語用於關於作者觀點的題目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the views of the writer","meaning":"作者的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The answer depends on the views of the writer.","zh":"答案取決於作者的觀點。"},{"en":"The views of the writer are the opinions, beliefs, or arguments expressed by the author.","zh":"作者的觀點，是作者表達的意見、信念或論點。"},{"en":"Students identify the views of the writer by noticing words like “should,” “dangerous,” or “important.”","zh":"學生可以透過留意 “should”、“dangerous” 或 “important” 等詞辨認作者觀點。"},{"en":"If the passage gives no clear view, students should not guess from outside knowledge.","zh":"如果文章沒有給出清楚觀點，學生不應靠外部知識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on author opinion.","zh":"這個短語強調作者意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the views of the writer.","zh":"一項陳述可能與作者的觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to express the opposite of what that person argues.","zh":"與某人的觀點相矛盾，指表達與該人論點相反的內容。"},{"en":"If a writer supports bee conservation, saying it is unnecessary may contradict the writer’s view.","zh":"如果作者支持蜜蜂保育，說它不必要可能與作者觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"In exam questions, contradiction means the statement is not just absent but opposite.","zh":"在考試題中，矛盾指陳述不只是缺失，而是相反。"},{"en":"The phrase describes conflict with an opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述與意見衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Students write “NOT GIVEN” if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"如果無法判斷作者想法，學生寫 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"無法判斷，指沒有足夠資料作決定。"},{"en":"If an article never mentions a farmer’s age, it is impossible to say whether he is young or old.","zh":"如果文章從未提到農民年齡，就無法判斷他年輕還是年老。"},{"en":"In reading tests, missing evidence should not be replaced by personal guesswork.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，不應用個人猜測取代缺失證據。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the text does not support a clear answer.","zh":"這個短語表示文本不支持清楚答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"on your answer sheet","meaning":"在答題紙上","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write their answers on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生在答題紙上寫下答案。"},{"en":"On your answer sheet means in the official place where exam answers are recorded.","zh":"在答題紙上，指在考試答案被記錄的正式位置。"},{"en":"A student may solve a question on rough paper but must copy the final answer onto the answer sheet.","zh":"學生可能在草稿紙上解題，但必須把最終答案抄到答題紙上。"},{"en":"If answers are not written on the answer sheet, they may not be marked.","zh":"如果答案沒有寫在答題紙上，可能不會被批改。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an exam instruction about where to write.","zh":"這個短語給出關於書寫位置的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"on a large scale","meaning":"大規模地","examples":[{"en":"Farmers have used honeybees on a large scale in recent years.","zh":"近年來，農民大規模地使用蜜蜂。"},{"en":"On a large scale means involving a big area, number, or amount.","zh":"大規模地，指涉及大範圍、大數量或大量。"},{"en":"A city may recycle on a large scale if every district joins the programme.","zh":"如果每個地區都加入計劃，城市就可以大規模地回收。"},{"en":"If honeybees are used on a large scale, disease can affect many farms at once.","zh":"如果蜜蜂被大規模使用，疾病可能同時影響許多農場。"},{"en":"The phrase describes big scope or size.","zh":"這個短語描述範圍或規模大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be harmful to","meaning":"對……有害","examples":[{"en":"Some farming practices may be harmful to native bees.","zh":"一些耕作方式可能對本土蜜蜂有害。"},{"en":"To be harmful to something means to damage it or make it less healthy.","zh":"對某物有害，指傷害它或令它較不健康。"},{"en":"Too much screen time may be harmful to a student’s sleep.","zh":"過多螢幕時間可能對學生睡眠有害。"},{"en":"If pesticides are harmful to pollinators, they can indirectly reduce crop production.","zh":"如果殺蟲劑對授粉者有害，就可能間接減少農作物生產。"},{"en":"The phrase describes negative effect or damage.","zh":"這個短語描述負面影響或損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"farmers’ health","meaning":"農民健康","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether clean-farming practices would be harmful to farmers’ health.","zh":"該陳述問清耕做法是否會對農民健康有害。"},{"en":"Farmers’ health means the physical and mental well-being of people who work in farming.","zh":"農民健康，指從事農業工作的人的身體和心理健康。"},{"en":"Farmers’ health can be affected by long working hours, chemicals, heat, and stress.","zh":"農民健康可能受長工時、化學品、高溫和壓力影響。"},{"en":"If farming practices expose workers to dangerous sprays, farmers’ health may suffer.","zh":"如果耕作方式令工人暴露於危險噴劑，農民健康可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the well-being of agricultural workers.","zh":"這個短語強調農業工作者的福祉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"for every crop","meaning":"對每一種農作物而言","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether one bee is the most efficient pollinator for every crop.","zh":"題目問一種蜜蜂是否對每一種農作物而言都是最高效授粉者。"},{"en":"For every crop means for all types of crops without exception.","zh":"對每一種農作物而言，指對所有農作物類型都適用，沒有例外。"},{"en":"One study method does not work best for every student.","zh":"一種學習方法不會對每個學生都最有效。"},{"en":"If honeybees are not best for every crop, native bees may be better in some cases.","zh":"如果蜜蜂不是對每一種農作物都最好，本土蜜蜂在某些情況可能更好。"},{"en":"The phrase tests whether a claim applies universally.","zh":"這個短語測試某主張是否普遍適用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be beneficial to","meaning":"對……有益","examples":[{"en":"Protecting native bees can be beneficial to other local creatures.","zh":"保護本土蜜蜂可以對其他本地生物有益。"},{"en":"To be beneficial to something means to help it or have a good effect on it.","zh":"對某物有益，指幫助它或對它有好影響。"},{"en":"Regular exercise is beneficial to physical health and mood.","zh":"定期運動對身體健康和情緒有益。"},{"en":"If bee habitats include flowers and trees, other insects and birds may benefit too.","zh":"如果蜜蜂棲息地包括花和樹，其他昆蟲和鳥類也可能受益。"},{"en":"The phrase describes positive effect.","zh":"這個短語描述正面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"local creatures","meaning":"本地生物","examples":[{"en":"Pollinator-friendly farming can benefit local creatures.","zh":"有利授粉者的耕作可以惠及本地生物。"},{"en":"Local creatures are animals and insects that live naturally in a particular area.","zh":"本地生物，是自然生活在特定地區的動物和昆蟲。"},{"en":"Local creatures in a garden may include birds, bees, butterflies, lizards, and frogs.","zh":"花園中的本地生物可能包括鳥、蜜蜂、蝴蝶、蜥蜴和青蛙。"},{"en":"If farms protect flowers and shelter, local creatures may gain food and habitat.","zh":"如果農場保護花和庇護處，本地生物可能得到食物和棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to nearby wildlife.","zh":"這個短語指附近的野生生物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"protect native bees","meaning":"保護本土蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"Farmers and homeowners can help protect native bees.","zh":"農民和業主可以幫助保護本土蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To protect native bees means to keep local bee species safe from harm and habitat loss.","zh":"保護本土蜜蜂，指使本地蜜蜂物種免受傷害和棲息地喪失。"},{"en":"Gardeners can protect native bees by planting flowers and avoiding unnecessary pesticides.","zh":"園丁可以透過種花和避免不必要殺蟲劑來保護本土蜜蜂。"},{"en":"If native bees are protected, farms may gain more stable pollination.","zh":"如果本土蜜蜂受到保護，農場可能得到更穩定授粉。"},{"en":"The phrase describes conservation action for local bees.","zh":"這個短語描述針對本地蜜蜂的保育行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"考生為每條問題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option that matches the evidence.","zh":"選出正確字母，指選擇與證據相符的答案選項。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice question, the correct letter may be A, B, C, or D.","zh":"在選擇題中，正確字母可能是 A、B、C 或 D。"},{"en":"If students read only one sentence, they may choose the wrong letter.","zh":"如果學生只讀一句，可能選錯字母。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"underline the writer’s point","meaning":"突顯作者的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The example of the “Fruitless Fall” underlines the writer’s point about pollinators.","zh":"「無果的秋天」這個例子突顯作者關於授粉者的觀點。"},{"en":"To underline the writer’s point means to emphasise or make the writer’s argument clearer.","zh":"突顯作者的觀點，指強調或令作者論點更清楚。"},{"en":"A real accident case can underline a teacher’s point about laboratory safety.","zh":"一個真實意外案例可以突顯老師關於實驗室安全的觀點。"},{"en":"If an example shows serious crop loss, it strengthens the argument about pollinator importance.","zh":"如果例子顯示嚴重農作物損失，它就加強授粉者重要性的論點。"},{"en":"The phrase means highlight an argument.","zh":"這個短語指突出一個論點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the need to use pesticides","meaning":"使用殺蟲劑的需要","examples":[{"en":"One option refers to the need to use pesticides.","zh":"一個選項提到使用殺蟲劑的需要。"},{"en":"The need to use pesticides means the necessity of using chemicals to control pests.","zh":"使用殺蟲劑的需要，指使用化學品控制害蟲的必要性。"},{"en":"A farmer may discuss the need to use pesticides when insects are destroying crops.","zh":"當昆蟲正在破壞農作物時，農民可能討論使用殺蟲劑的需要。"},{"en":"If pesticides harm bees, the need to use them must be balanced against pollinator protection.","zh":"如果殺蟲劑傷害蜜蜂，使用它們的需要就必須與保護授粉者平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on whether chemical control is necessary.","zh":"這個短語強調是否有必要使用化學控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"impacts of losing insect pollinators","meaning":"失去昆蟲授粉者的影響","examples":[{"en":"The “Fruitless Fall” highlights the impacts of losing insect pollinators.","zh":"「無果的秋天」突顯失去昆蟲授粉者的影響。"},{"en":"Impacts of losing insect pollinators are the effects caused when pollinating insects disappear.","zh":"失去昆蟲授粉者的影響，是授粉昆蟲消失時造成的後果。"},{"en":"Losing bees and butterflies may reduce fruit in gardens and farms.","zh":"失去蜜蜂和蝴蝶可能減少花園和農場中的果實。"},{"en":"If insect pollinators are lost, food supply and ecosystems may both suffer.","zh":"如果昆蟲授粉者消失，食物供應和生態系統都可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes consequences of pollinator decline.","zh":"這個短語描述授粉者減少的後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"vulnerabilities of native bees","meaning":"本土蜜蜂的脆弱性","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the vulnerabilities of native bees in modern farmland.","zh":"文章討論本土蜜蜂在現代農田中的脆弱性。"},{"en":"Vulnerabilities of native bees are weaknesses or risks that make local bees easy to harm.","zh":"本土蜜蜂的脆弱性，是令本地蜜蜂容易受傷害的弱點或風險。"},{"en":"Pesticides and loss of wild flowers are vulnerabilities for many native bees.","zh":"殺蟲劑和野花消失是許多本土蜜蜂的脆弱因素。"},{"en":"If these vulnerabilities are ignored, native bee populations may decline further.","zh":"如果這些脆弱性被忽視，本土蜜蜂種群可能進一步下降。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on why native bees need protection.","zh":"這個短語強調本土蜜蜂為何需要保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the benefits of building","meaning":"建立……的好處","examples":[{"en":"One option mentions the benefits of building more pollination industries.","zh":"一個選項提到建立更多授粉產業的好處。"},{"en":"The benefits of building something are the advantages gained from creating or developing it.","zh":"建立某事的好處，是創造或發展它所帶來的優點。"},{"en":"The benefits of building a new library include more study space and community programmes.","zh":"建立新圖書館的好處包括更多溫習空間和社區活動。"},{"en":"If more pollination industries are built, farms may gain services but nature may not become healthier.","zh":"如果建立更多授粉產業，農場可能得到服務，但自然未必變得更健康。"},{"en":"The phrase asks what good results development may bring.","zh":"這個短語詢問發展可能帶來甚麼好結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"pollination industries","meaning":"授粉產業","examples":[{"en":"Modern agriculture has created large pollination industries.","zh":"現代農業創造了大型授粉產業。"},{"en":"Pollination industries are businesses that provide pollinators or pollination services to farms.","zh":"授粉產業，是向農場提供授粉者或授粉服務的商業活動。"},{"en":"Beekeepers who rent hives to orchards are part of pollination industries.","zh":"把蜂箱租給果園的養蜂人是授粉產業的一部分。"},{"en":"If farming depends on such industries, pollination becomes a paid service.","zh":"如果農業依賴這類產業，授粉就成為付費服務。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to commercial systems built around pollination.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞授粉建立的商業系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"adapt to the modern agricultural system","meaning":"適應現代農業系統","examples":[{"en":"Honeybees can adapt to the modern agricultural system.","zh":"蜜蜂可以適應現代農業系統。"},{"en":"To adapt to the modern agricultural system means to fit or adjust to today’s organised farming methods.","zh":"適應現代農業系統，指配合或調整至今天有組織的耕作方法。"},{"en":"Farmers adapt to new school lunch demand by growing vegetables that can be supplied regularly.","zh":"農民透過種植能定期供應的蔬菜，適應新的學校午餐需求。"},{"en":"If honeybee hives can be moved and managed, they fit industrial agriculture better than many wild bees.","zh":"如果蜜蜂蜂箱能被移動和管理，牠們比許多野生蜜蜂更適合工業化農業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical adjustment to modern farming.","zh":"這個短語描述對現代農業的實際調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"since ancient times","meaning":"自古以來","examples":[{"en":"Honeybees have been semi-domesticated since ancient times.","zh":"蜜蜂自古以來已經半馴化。"},{"en":"Since ancient times means from a very old period in human history until now.","zh":"自古以來，指從人類歷史中很久遠的時期直到現在。"},{"en":"People have used herbs as medicine since ancient times.","zh":"人們自古以來使用草藥作醫藥。"},{"en":"If a practice has existed since ancient times, it has a long cultural history.","zh":"如果一種做法自古以來存在，它就有悠久文化歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights great historical depth.","zh":"這個短語突出深厚歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be moved away from","meaning":"從……移開","examples":[{"en":"Honeybee hives can be moved away from pesticides.","zh":"蜜蜂蜂箱可以從殺蟲劑附近移開。"},{"en":"To be moved away from something means to be relocated so that it is not near a danger or object.","zh":"從某物移開，指被搬離，使其不靠近危險或物件。"},{"en":"Children may be moved away from a broken window for safety.","zh":"為安全起見，孩子可能被從破窗旁移開。"},{"en":"If hives are moved away from pesticides, bees may avoid direct poisoning.","zh":"如果蜂箱從殺蟲劑附近移開，蜜蜂可能避免直接中毒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes protective relocation.","zh":"這個短語描述保護性搬移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"illustrate one drawback of","meaning":"說明……的一個缺點","examples":[{"en":"The factory comparison illustrates one drawback of industrial agriculture.","zh":"工廠比較說明工業化農業的一個缺點。"},{"en":"To illustrate one drawback of something means to show one disadvantage clearly through an example.","zh":"說明某事的一個缺點，指透過例子清楚展示一個劣勢。"},{"en":"A long queue illustrates one drawback of having too few staff.","zh":"長隊伍說明員工太少的一個缺點。"},{"en":"If a farm resembles a factory, the example may show loss of ecological resilience.","zh":"如果農場像工廠，該例子可能顯示生態韌性流失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes explaining a weakness with an example.","zh":"這個短語描述用例子解釋弱點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"industrialised agricultural system","meaning":"工業化農業系統","examples":[{"en":"The writer criticises the vulnerability of the industrialised agricultural system.","zh":"作者批評工業化農業系統的脆弱性。"},{"en":"An industrialised agricultural system is a farming system organised like large-scale industry.","zh":"工業化農業系統，是像大規模工業一樣組織的農業系統。"},{"en":"It may use machines, chemicals, monocultures, long supply chains, and specialised services.","zh":"它可能使用機器、化學品、單一作物、長供應鏈和專門服務。"},{"en":"If such a system relies on one pollinator, it can become efficient but fragile.","zh":"如果這類系統依賴一種授粉者，它可以高效但脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes modern farming as an industrial structure.","zh":"這個短語把現代農業描述為工業結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"low cost in modern agriculture","meaning":"現代農業中的低成本","examples":[{"en":"One option refers to the low cost in modern agriculture.","zh":"一個選項提到現代農業中的低成本。"},{"en":"Low cost in modern agriculture means food or farming services can be produced cheaply.","zh":"現代農業中的低成本，指食物或農業服務可以便宜地生產。"},{"en":"Large machines may create low cost in modern agriculture by reducing labour needs.","zh":"大型機器可能透過減少勞動力需求，創造現代農業中的低成本。"},{"en":"If low cost depends on fragile systems, cheap food may hide environmental risk.","zh":"如果低成本依賴脆弱系統，廉價食物可能隱藏環境風險。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on economic efficiency.","zh":"這個短語強調經濟效率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"high yields achieved by","meaning":"由……達到的高產量","examples":[{"en":"Industrial agriculture is often associated with high yields achieved at large scale.","zh":"工業化農業常與大規模達到的高產量有關。"},{"en":"High yields achieved by something are large harvests produced through a particular method or system.","zh":"由某事達到的高產量，是透過特定方法或系統生產的大量收成。"},{"en":"High yields achieved by improved seeds can increase farm income.","zh":"由改良種子達到的高產量可以增加農場收入。"},{"en":"If high yields depend on one pollinator, the system may still be risky.","zh":"如果高產量依賴一種授粉者，系統仍可能有風險。"},{"en":"The phrase links strong production results with their cause.","zh":"這個短語把強勁產量與其原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"prove that","meaning":"證明","examples":[{"en":"Winfree’s research helps prove that wild bees can be important pollinators.","zh":"Winfree 的研究有助證明野生蜜蜂可以是重要授粉者。"},{"en":"To prove that means to show with evidence that something is true.","zh":"證明，指用證據顯示某事為真。"},{"en":"A student can prove that an answer is correct by quoting the passage.","zh":"學生可以透過引用文章證明答案正確。"},{"en":"If research proves wild bees matter, conservation becomes more urgent.","zh":"如果研究證明野生蜜蜂重要，保育就變得更迫切。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence-based confirmation.","zh":"這個短語引入基於證據的確認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"various crops","meaning":"各種農作物","examples":[{"en":"Honeybees and wild bees can pollinate various crops.","zh":"蜜蜂和野生蜜蜂可以為各種農作物授粉。"},{"en":"Various crops means several different kinds of farm plants.","zh":"各種農作物，指幾種不同農場植物。"},{"en":"A farmer may grow various crops to reduce risk if one crop fails.","zh":"農民可能種植各種農作物，以減少某一作物失收的風險。"},{"en":"If different bees pollinate various crops, the system becomes more flexible.","zh":"如果不同蜜蜂為各種農作物授粉，系統就變得更靈活。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses crop diversity.","zh":"這個短語強調農作物多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"types of wild bees","meaning":"野生蜜蜂種類","examples":[{"en":"The study identified many types of wild bees as pollinators.","zh":"該研究辨認出許多野生蜜蜂種類作為授粉者。"},{"en":"Types of wild bees are different species or groups of bees living outside managed hives.","zh":"野生蜜蜂種類，是生活在受管理蜂箱以外的不同蜜蜂物種或群體。"},{"en":"Some types of wild bees nest in soil, while others use hollow wood or plant stems.","zh":"一些野生蜜蜂種類在泥土中築巢，另一些使用空心木或植物莖。"},{"en":"If many types of wild bees visit crops, pollination does not depend on one species alone.","zh":"如果許多野生蜜蜂種類到訪農作物，授粉就不只依賴單一物種。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights bee diversity.","zh":"這個短語突出蜜蜂多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"increase crop yields","meaning":"提高農作物產量","examples":[{"en":"Effective pollination can help increase crop yields.","zh":"有效授粉可以幫助提高農作物產量。"},{"en":"To increase crop yields means to raise the amount of crops produced from a field or farm.","zh":"提高農作物產量，指增加一片田或農場生產的農作物數量。"},{"en":"Better irrigation can increase crop yields during dry seasons.","zh":"更好的灌溉可以在乾季提高農作物產量。"},{"en":"If bees pollinate more flowers, more fruit or seeds may develop.","zh":"如果蜜蜂為更多花授粉，就可能有更多果實或種子發育。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improving farm output.","zh":"這個短語描述改善農業產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"in certain cases","meaning":"在某些情況下","examples":[{"en":"Wild bees can work more efficiently than honeybees in certain cases.","zh":"在某些情況下，野生蜜蜂可以比蜜蜂工作更有效率。"},{"en":"In certain cases means in some specific situations, but not always.","zh":"在某些情況下，指在一些特定情況中，但不是永遠如此。"},{"en":"In certain cases, studying with music helps students concentrate.","zh":"在某些情況下，邊聽音樂邊溫習有助學生集中。"},{"en":"If wild bees are better for one crop, they may not be better for every crop.","zh":"如果野生蜜蜂對一種農作物較好，也不代表對每種農作物都較好。"},{"en":"The phrase limits a claim to particular situations.","zh":"這個短語把主張限制在特定情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the last paragraph","meaning":"最後一段","examples":[{"en":"The last paragraph suggests a more diverse approach to pollination.","zh":"最後一段建議採取更 多元的授粉方法。"},{"en":"The last paragraph is the final paragraph of a passage or article.","zh":"最後一段，是文章或篇章的最終段落。"},{"en":"In reading tests, the last paragraph often gives the writer’s conclusion or future direction.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，最後一段常給出作者結論或未來方向。"},{"en":"If the last paragraph suggests diversity, it may summarise the main solution.","zh":"如果最後一段建議多樣化，它可能總結主要解決方案。"},{"en":"The phrase points readers to the ending section.","zh":"這個短語把讀者指向結尾部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"use different bee species","meaning":"使用不同蜜蜂物種","examples":[{"en":"Researchers suggest using different bee species in agricultural systems.","zh":"研究人員建議在農業系統中使用不同蜜蜂物種。"},{"en":"To use different bee species means to rely on more than one kind of bee.","zh":"使用不同蜜蜂物種，指依靠多於一種蜜蜂。"},{"en":"A school uses different teaching methods when students learn in different ways.","zh":"當學生有不同學習方式，學校會使用不同教學方法。"},{"en":"If farms use different bee species, each crop may receive a better pollinator.","zh":"如果農場使用不同蜜蜂物種，每種農作物可能得到更合適授粉者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pollination diversity.","zh":"這個短語描述授粉多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"agricultural systems of various sizes","meaning":"不同規模的農業系統","examples":[{"en":"Different agricultural systems of various sizes may need different pollination strategies.","zh":"不同規模的農業系統可能需要不同授粉策略。"},{"en":"Agricultural systems of various sizes are farms or farming operations that range from small to large.","zh":"不同規模的農業系統，是由小到大的農場或農業經營。"},{"en":"A family garden and a huge fruit plantation are agricultural systems of very different sizes.","zh":"家庭花園和巨大水果種植園是規模非常不同的農業系統。"},{"en":"If farm size changes, the best pollination strategy may also change.","zh":"如果農場規模改變，最佳授粉策略也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase links farming scale with farming needs.","zh":"這個短語把農業規模與農業需要連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"intensive and extensive agricultural systems","meaning":"集約式與粗放式農業系統","examples":[{"en":"One option compares intensive and extensive agricultural systems.","zh":"一個選項比較集約式與粗放式農業系統。"},{"en":"Intensive agricultural systems use high inputs on smaller areas, while extensive systems use larger areas with lower inputs.","zh":"集約式農業系統在較小面積使用高投入，而粗放式系統在較大面積使用較低投入。"},{"en":"A greenhouse vegetable farm may be intensive, while open grazing land may be extensive.","zh":"溫室蔬菜農場可能是集約式，而開闊牧地可能是粗放式。"},{"en":"If farming systems differ, their pollination needs may differ too.","zh":"如果農業系統不同，其授粉需要也可能不同。"},{"en":"The phrase compares two broad farming styles.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種廣泛農業方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"rely on native pollinators","meaning":"依靠本土授粉者","examples":[{"en":"Some farmers may be able to rely on native pollinators.","zh":"一些農民可能能夠依靠本土授粉者。"},{"en":"To rely on native pollinators means to depend on local pollinating species for crop pollination.","zh":"依靠本土授粉者，指依賴本地授粉物種為農作物授粉。"},{"en":"A gardener may rely on native pollinators instead of hand-pollinating flowers.","zh":"園丁可能依靠本土授粉者，而不是手工為花授粉。"},{"en":"If native pollinators are abundant, farmers may need fewer rented hives.","zh":"如果本土授粉者數量充足，農民可能需要較少租用蜂箱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes depending on local natural pollination.","zh":"這個短語描述依賴本地自然授粉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"complete each sentence with","meaning":"用……完成每句","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete each sentence with the correct ending.","zh":"考生用正確結尾完成每句。"},{"en":"To complete each sentence with something means to choose words that finish the sentence correctly.","zh":"用某物完成每句，指選擇能正確完成句子的字詞。"},{"en":"Students complete each sentence with a verb that matches the grammar pattern.","zh":"學生用符合文法模式的動詞完成每句。"},{"en":"If the ending does not match the meaning, the sentence becomes wrong.","zh":"如果結尾不符合意思，句子就會錯。"},{"en":"The phrase is a reading or grammar task instruction.","zh":"這個短語是閱讀或文法題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the correct ending","meaning":"正確結尾","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct ending for each sentence.","zh":"學生為每句選擇正確結尾。"},{"en":"The correct ending is the answer choice that finishes a sentence accurately.","zh":"正確結尾，是能準確完成句子的答案選項。"},{"en":"In a sentence-completion task, the correct ending must fit both grammar and meaning.","zh":"在句子完成題中，正確結尾必須同時符合文法和意思。"},{"en":"If a sentence begins with a cause, the correct ending may describe the result.","zh":"如果句子以原因開頭，正確結尾可能描述結果。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the best sentence finish.","zh":"這個短語指最佳句尾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"severe consequences","meaning":"嚴重後果","examples":[{"en":"The loss of honeybees could cause severe consequences.","zh":"失去蜜蜂可能造成嚴重後果。"},{"en":"Severe consequences are very serious results or effects.","zh":"嚴重後果，是非常嚴重的結果或影響。"},{"en":"Ignoring a fire alarm can have severe consequences for everyone in a building.","zh":"忽視火警鐘可能對建築物內所有人造成嚴重後果。"},{"en":"If pollination fails, the severe consequences may include crop loss and higher food prices.","zh":"如果授粉失敗，嚴重後果可能包括農作物損失和食物價格上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious outcomes.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"both commerce and agriculture","meaning":"商業和農業兩方面","examples":[{"en":"Pollinator loss could affect both commerce and agriculture.","zh":"授粉者流失可能影響商業和農業兩方面。"},{"en":"Both commerce and agriculture means business activity as well as farming.","zh":"商業和農業兩方面，指商業活動以及農業。"},{"en":"A fruit shortage can affect both commerce and agriculture because farmers sell less and shops have fewer products.","zh":"水果短缺可以影響商業和農業兩方面，因為農民賣得較少，商店產品也較少。"},{"en":"If bees decline, farms, food companies, supermarkets, and consumers may all be affected.","zh":"如果蜜蜂減少，農場、食品公司、超市和消費者都可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase joins economic trade with food production.","zh":"這個短語把經濟貿易與食物生產連在一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"cannot be bred","meaning":"不能被繁殖","examples":[{"en":"One option claims that honeybees cannot be bred.","zh":"一個選項聲稱蜜蜂不能被繁殖。"},{"en":"Cannot be bred means cannot be raised or reproduced by humans in controlled conditions.","zh":"不能被繁殖，指不能由人類在受控條件下飼養或繁殖。"},{"en":"Some wild animals cannot be bred easily in zoos because they need special habitats.","zh":"一些野生動物不能輕易在動物園繁殖，因為牠們需要特殊棲息地。"},{"en":"If bees cannot be bred reliably, farmers cannot simply increase their numbers when needed.","zh":"如果蜜蜂不能可靠繁殖，農民就不能在需要時簡單增加其數量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes difficulty in human-controlled reproduction.","zh":"這個短語描述人為控制繁殖上的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"a specific plant is supplied","meaning":"提供某種特定植物時","examples":[{"en":"Native pollinators may survive when a specific plant is supplied.","zh":"提供某種特定植物時，本土授粉者可能生存。"},{"en":"When a specific plant is supplied means when a particular useful plant is provided.","zh":"提供某種特定植物時，指提供某種特別有用的植物。"},{"en":"A butterfly species may survive in a garden when its specific host plant is supplied.","zh":"當花園提供特定寄主植物時，某種蝴蝶可能生存。"},{"en":"If bees need floral oils, supplying the right plant may keep them in the orchard.","zh":"如果蜜蜂需要花油，提供合適植物可能令牠們留在果園。"},{"en":"The phrase links survival with providing the correct plant resource.","zh":"這個短語把生存與提供正確植物資源連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be fragile when relying on","meaning":"在依賴……時變得脆弱","examples":[{"en":"An agricultural system is fragile when relying on a single pollinator.","zh":"農業系統在依賴單一授粉者時變得脆弱。"},{"en":"To be fragile when relying on something means to become weak because of depending too much on it.","zh":"在依賴某事時變得脆弱，指因過度依靠它而變弱。"},{"en":"A student’s study plan is fragile when relying on only one night of revision.","zh":"如果學生只依賴一晚溫習，其學習計劃就很脆弱。"},{"en":"If one pollinator fails, a system with no alternatives may break down.","zh":"如果一種授粉者失效，沒有替代方案的系統可能崩潰。"},{"en":"The phrase warns about risky dependence.","zh":"這個短語警告有風險的依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"Freitas’s observations show that","meaning":"Freitas 的觀察顯示","examples":[{"en":"Freitas’s observations show that native pollinators can survive with suitable resources.","zh":"Freitas 的觀察顯示，本土授粉者有合適資源時可以生存。"},{"en":"Freitas’s observations show that means his recorded findings provide evidence for a claim.","zh":"Freitas 的觀察顯示，指他記錄到的發現為某主張提供證據。"},{"en":"A teacher’s observations may show that students learn better with examples.","zh":"老師的觀察可能顯示學生透過例子學得更好。"},{"en":"If field observations show bees using certain plants, farmers can design better habitats.","zh":"如果野外觀察顯示蜜蜂使用某些植物，農民就能設計更好棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence from what a researcher noticed.","zh":"這個短語引入研究者觀察所得的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"examples of blue orchard bees","meaning":"藍果園蜂的例子","examples":[{"en":"Examples of blue orchard bees show that fewer native bees may be needed.","zh":"藍果園蜂的例子顯示，可能需要較少本土蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Examples of blue orchard bees are cases showing how this bee species works in pollination.","zh":"藍果園蜂的例子，是顯示這種蜜蜂如何授粉的個案。"},{"en":"A teacher may use examples of successful students to show how revision habits matter.","zh":"老師可能使用成功學生的例子來顯示溫習習慣的重要性。"},{"en":"If blue orchard bees pollinate efficiently, they illustrate the value of native pollinators.","zh":"如果藍果園蜂授粉效率高，它們就說明本土授粉者的價值。"},{"en":"The phrase uses one bee species as evidence.","zh":"這個短語用一種蜜蜂物種作為證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be mentioned to exemplify that","meaning":"被提及以說明","examples":[{"en":"Centris tarsata is mentioned to exemplify that native pollinators can survive in orchards.","zh":"Centris tarsata 被提及以說明本土授粉者可以在果園中生存。"},{"en":"To be mentioned to exemplify that means to be named as an example showing a point.","zh":"被提及以說明某事，指被列名作為展示某觀點的例子。"},{"en":"A school may mention one successful project to exemplify that teamwork matters.","zh":"學校可能提及一個成功項目，以說明團隊合作重要。"},{"en":"If a bee species is mentioned as an example, it helps make the general claim concrete.","zh":"如果一種蜜蜂物種被作為例子提及，它有助令一般主張具體。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why an example is included.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何包括某例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"one finding of the research","meaning":"研究的一項發現","examples":[{"en":"One finding of the research in the Delaware Valley is that some landscapes support wild bees.","zh":"特拉華河谷研究的一項發現是，一些景觀支援野生蜜蜂。"},{"en":"One finding of the research is one result or conclusion produced by a study.","zh":"研究的一項發現，是一項研究產生的一個結果或結論。"},{"en":"One finding of a school survey may be that students need quieter study areas.","zh":"學校調查的一項發現可能是學生需要更安靜的溫習區。"},{"en":"If a finding shows mixed landscapes support bees, conservation can include homes and farms.","zh":"如果發現顯示混合景觀支援蜜蜂，保育就可以包括住宅和農場。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a specific research result.","zh":"這個短語引入一個具體研究結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be favourable for supporting","meaning":"有利於支持……","examples":[{"en":"Some agricultural landscapes are favourable for supporting wild bees.","zh":"一些農業景觀有利於支持野生蜜蜂生存。"},{"en":"To be favourable for supporting something means to provide good conditions that help it survive or succeed.","zh":"有利於支持某事，指提供幫助它生存或成功的良好條件。"},{"en":"A quiet classroom is favourable for supporting students who need concentration.","zh":"安靜課室有利於支持需要集中精神的學生。"},{"en":"If a farm has flowers, nesting places, and limited pesticide use, it may support wild bees well.","zh":"如果農場有花、築巢地點和有限殺蟲劑使用，就可能很好地支援野生蜜蜂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes helpful conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述有幫助的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"supporting wild bees","meaning":"支持野生蜜蜂生存","examples":[{"en":"Mixed landscapes can be favourable for supporting wild bees.","zh":"混合景觀可以有利於支持野生蜜蜂生存。"},{"en":"Supporting wild bees means helping wild bee populations survive, feed, nest, and reproduce.","zh":"支持野生蜜蜂生存，指幫助野生蜜蜂種群存活、覓食、築巢和繁殖。"},{"en":"A homeowner can support wild bees by planting native flowers and leaving some bare soil.","zh":"業主可以透過種植本土花卉和保留一些裸露泥土來支持野生蜜蜂。"},{"en":"If more people support wild bees, farms may receive more natural pollination.","zh":"如果更多人支持野生蜜蜂，農場可能得到更多自然授粉。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical help for wild bee survival.","zh":"這個短語描述對野生蜜蜂生存的實際幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 35 - Honey bees in trouble.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 36":[{"front":"Internal Market","meaning":"內部市場","examples":[{"en":"Internal marketing treats employees as an important internal market.","zh":"內部市場推廣把員工視為一個重要的內部市場。"},{"en":"An internal market means employees are treated as people who also need to understand and accept the company’s message.","zh":"Internal market 指員工也被視為需要理解並接受公司訊息的人。"},{"en":"A school has an internal market when teachers must first believe in a new learning policy before students accept it.","zh":"當老師必須先相信新的學習政策，學生才會接受時，學校也有一個內部市場。"},{"en":"If the internal market is ignored, employees may not support what the company tells customers.","zh":"如果內部市場被忽略，員工可能不支持公司對顧客所說的內容。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that persuasion inside a company can be as important as persuasion outside it.","zh":"這個片語提醒我們，公司內部的說服可以和對外說服同樣重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Selling the Inside","meaning":"對內推廣；向內部推銷理念","examples":[{"en":"The article explains the idea of selling the inside before selling to customers.","zh":"文章解釋在向顧客推銷前先向內部推銷理念。"},{"en":"Selling the inside means persuading employees to believe in a message before presenting it to the public.","zh":"Selling the inside 指在向公眾展示訊息前，先說服員工相信它。"},{"en":"A restaurant should sell the inside first by making sure staff understand a new service promise.","zh":"餐廳應先對內推廣，確保員工理解新的服務承諾。"},{"en":"If employees do not accept the message, customers may receive a weak or confusing experience.","zh":"如果員工不接受訊息，顧客可能得到薄弱或混亂的體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes internal persuasion before external marketing.","zh":"這個片語描述對外市場推廣前的內部說服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"when you think of","meaning":"當你想到……時","examples":[{"en":"When you think of marketing, you probably think of customers first.","zh":"當你想到市場推廣時，你很可能先想到顧客。"},{"en":"When you think of something means when that idea comes into your mind.","zh":"When you think of something 指當某個想法進入你的腦海時。"},{"en":"When you think of exams, you may immediately think of pressure and revision.","zh":"當你想到考試時，你可能立刻想到壓力和溫習。"},{"en":"If people think of marketing only as advertising, they may miss its internal role.","zh":"如果人們只把市場推廣想成廣告，他們可能忽略其內部作用。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the first idea people commonly associate with a topic.","zh":"這個片語引出人們通常首先聯想到某主題的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"more than likely","meaning":"很可能","examples":[{"en":"People more than likely associate marketing with selling to customers.","zh":"人們很可能把市場推廣與向顧客銷售聯繫起來。"},{"en":"More than likely means very probably or almost certainly.","zh":"More than likely 指非常可能或幾乎肯定。"},{"en":"If a student has not slept, they are more than likely to lose focus in class.","zh":"如果學生沒有睡覺，他很可能在課堂上失去專注。"},{"en":"If staff hear nothing about a new campaign, they will more than likely feel confused.","zh":"如果員工完全沒有聽過新推廣活動，他們很可能感到困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a strong probability without sounding completely absolute.","zh":"這個片語表達很高可能性，但語氣不至於完全絕對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"marketing to your customers","meaning":"向顧客進行市場推廣","examples":[{"en":"Most people think of marketing to their customers before marketing to employees.","zh":"大多數人先想到向顧客進行市場推廣，而不是向員工推廣。"},{"en":"Marketing to your customers means promoting products, services, or ideas to the people who buy from you.","zh":"Marketing to your customers 指向購買者推廣產品、服務或理念。"},{"en":"A shop markets to customers when it advertises discounts and explains product benefits.","zh":"商店宣傳折扣並解釋產品好處時，就是向顧客進行市場推廣。"},{"en":"If a company markets to customers but forgets staff training, service may not match the advertisement.","zh":"如果公司向顧客推廣卻忘記員工培訓，服務可能與廣告不一致。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the usual outward-facing side of marketing.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於市場推廣通常面向外部的一面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"persuade more people to","meaning":"說服更多人去……","examples":[{"en":"Companies try to persuade more people to buy what they sell.","zh":"公司嘗試說服更多人購買它們所銷售的東西。"},{"en":"To persuade more people to do something means to make a larger number of people willing to do it.","zh":"To persuade more people to do something 指令更多人願意做某事。"},{"en":"A school may persuade more students to read by showing books connected to their interests.","zh":"學校可以透過展示與學生興趣相關的書，說服更多學生閱讀。"},{"en":"If an advertisement is clear and trustworthy, it may persuade more people to try a product.","zh":"如果廣告清晰且可信，它可能說服更多人嘗試某產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing acceptance through explanation, emotion, or evidence.","zh":"這個片語描述透過解釋、情感或證據增加接受度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what you sell","meaning":"你所銷售的東西","examples":[{"en":"Marketing aims to persuade people to buy what you sell.","zh":"市場推廣旨在說服人們購買你所銷售的東西。"},{"en":"What you sell means the products, services, or ideas a business offers.","zh":"What you sell 指企業提供的產品、服務或理念。"},{"en":"A tutor may sell lessons, but what they really sell is confidence and improvement.","zh":"補習老師可能銷售課堂，但真正銷售的是信心和進步。"},{"en":"If employees do not understand what you sell, they cannot explain its value well.","zh":"如果員工不理解你所銷售的東西，他們就不能好好解釋其價值。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to both physical products and less visible services.","zh":"這個片語既可指實體產品，也可指較不明顯的服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"another market","meaning":"另一個市場","examples":[{"en":"Employees can be seen as another market for the company’s message.","zh":"員工可以被視為公司訊息的另一個市場。"},{"en":"Another market means an additional group of people who must be persuaded or served.","zh":"Another market 指另一個需要被說服或服務的人群。"},{"en":"Parents can be another market for a school’s new learning programme.","zh":"家長可以是學校新學習計劃的另一個市場。"},{"en":"If a message matters to staff as well as customers, employees become another market.","zh":"如果訊息對員工和顧客同樣重要，員工就成為另一個市場。"},{"en":"This phrase expands marketing beyond the usual customer audience.","zh":"這個片語把市場推廣擴展到一般顧客以外的受眾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"just as important","meaning":"同樣重要","examples":[{"en":"The internal market is just as important as the customer market.","zh":"內部市場與顧客市場同樣重要。"},{"en":"Just as important means equally important.","zh":"Just as important 指同等重要。"},{"en":"In education, feedback is just as important as final marks.","zh":"在教育中，回饋與最終分數同樣重要。"},{"en":"If employee belief is just as important as customer awareness, companies must invest in both.","zh":"如果員工信念與顧客認知同樣重要，公司就必須投資兩者。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two things and says neither should be treated as secondary.","zh":"這個片語比較兩件事，並表示兩者都不應被視為次要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the very people who","meaning":"正正是那些……的人","examples":[{"en":"Employees are the very people who can make the brand real for customers.","zh":"員工正正是那些能令品牌對顧客而言變得真實的人。"},{"en":"The very people who means exactly the people who are most directly involved.","zh":"The very people who 指正正是最直接相關的那些人。"},{"en":"Nurses are the very people who understand patients’ daily worries best.","zh":"護士正正是那些最了解病人日常憂慮的人。"},{"en":"If staff serve customers every day, they are the very people who shape the brand experience.","zh":"如果員工每天服務顧客，他們正正是塑造品牌體驗的人。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly identifies a group as especially important.","zh":"這個片語強烈指出某群體特別重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"make the brand come alive","meaning":"令品牌變得鮮活","examples":[{"en":"Employees can make the brand come alive for customers.","zh":"員工可以令品牌對顧客而言變得鮮活。"},{"en":"To make the brand come alive means to turn a brand promise into a real experience.","zh":"To make the brand come alive 指把品牌承諾變成真實體驗。"},{"en":"A hotel receptionist makes the brand come alive when warm service matches the advertisement.","zh":"當酒店接待員的親切服務配合廣告時，他就令品牌變得鮮活。"},{"en":"If employees act with care and skill, customers feel the brand is more than a logo.","zh":"如果員工有關懷和技巧地行事，顧客會覺得品牌不只是標誌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing an abstract brand into something customers can feel.","zh":"這個片語描述把抽象品牌變成顧客能感受到的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for your customers","meaning":"對你的顧客而言","examples":[{"en":"Employees help the brand come alive for your customers.","zh":"員工幫助品牌對你的顧客而言變得鮮活。"},{"en":"For your customers means from the point of view or experience of the people who buy from you.","zh":"For your customers 指從購買者的角度或體驗來看。"},{"en":"A clear return policy makes shopping easier for your customers.","zh":"清晰退貨政策令購物對你的顧客而言更容易。"},{"en":"If employees are confused, the service may feel inconsistent for your customers.","zh":"如果員工困惑，服務對你的顧客而言可能感覺不一致。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the customer’s experience rather than the company’s intention.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於顧客體驗，而不是公司的意圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"executives","meaning":"企業高層；行政人員","examples":[{"en":"The writers help executives develop branding campaigns.","zh":"作者幫助企業高層制定品牌推廣活動。"},{"en":"Executives are senior managers who make important decisions in an organisation.","zh":"Executives 是在組織中作重要決定的高級管理人員。"},{"en":"School executives may decide whether to open a new campus or change the curriculum.","zh":"學校高層可能決定是否開設新校舍或改變課程。"},{"en":"If executives ignore employees, their branding decisions may fail in daily service.","zh":"如果企業高層忽略員工，他們的品牌決定可能在日常服務中失敗。"},{"en":"This word usually refers to people with high-level responsibility.","zh":"這個詞通常指擁有高層責任的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"develop and carry out","meaning":"制定並執行","examples":[{"en":"Executives need to develop and carry out effective branding campaigns.","zh":"企業高層需要制定並執行有效的品牌推廣活動。"},{"en":"To develop and carry out something means to design it and then put it into action.","zh":"To develop and carry out something 指設計某事，然後把它付諸行動。"},{"en":"A school may develop and carry out a reading programme for weaker students.","zh":"學校可能為能力較弱學生制定並執行閱讀計劃。"},{"en":"If a plan is developed but not carried out well, it remains only an idea.","zh":"如果計劃制定了但沒有好好執行，它仍只是一個想法。"},{"en":"This phrase joins planning with practical execution.","zh":"這個片語把規劃與實際執行結合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"branding campaigns","meaning":"品牌推廣活動","examples":[{"en":"The writers help companies carry out branding campaigns.","zh":"作者幫助公司執行品牌推廣活動。"},{"en":"Branding campaigns are planned activities that shape how people see and feel about a brand.","zh":"Branding campaigns 是有計劃地塑造人們如何看待和感受品牌的活動。"},{"en":"A café may run a branding campaign to show that it is local, friendly, and sustainable.","zh":"咖啡店可能推行品牌推廣活動，顯示自己本地、親切且可持續。"},{"en":"If a branding campaign promises care but staff act coldly, the message loses power.","zh":"如果品牌推廣活動承諾關懷，但員工態度冷淡，訊息就會失去力量。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised efforts to build a brand image.","zh":"這個片語指有組織地建立品牌形象的努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"very often ignore","meaning":"很經常忽略","examples":[{"en":"Companies very often ignore their employees during branding campaigns.","zh":"公司在品牌推廣活動中很經常忽略員工。"},{"en":"Very often ignore means frequently fail to notice or consider something important.","zh":"Very often ignore 指經常未能注意或考慮重要事物。"},{"en":"Schools very often ignore quiet students because louder students demand more attention.","zh":"學校很經常忽略安靜學生，因為較吵的學生要求更多注意。"},{"en":"If companies often ignore employees, internal support for new ideas becomes weak.","zh":"如果公司經常忽略員工，內部對新理念的支持就會薄弱。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises a repeated pattern of neglect.","zh":"這個片語批評一種反覆出現的忽視模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"critical constituency","meaning":"關鍵群體；重要持份者群體","examples":[{"en":"Employees are a critical constituency in any branding campaign.","zh":"員工是任何品牌推廣活動中的關鍵群體。"},{"en":"A critical constituency is an important group whose support matters greatly.","zh":"Critical constituency 是支持非常重要的群體。"},{"en":"Parents are a critical constituency when a school changes homework policy.","zh":"當學校改變功課政策時，家長是一個關鍵群體。"},{"en":"If a critical constituency is ignored, a plan may face resistance or fail.","zh":"如果關鍵群體被忽略，計劃可能面對抗拒或失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a group that must not be left out of decision-making.","zh":"這個片語描述決策中不可被排除的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"internal marketing","meaning":"內部市場推廣","examples":[{"en":"Internal marketing helps employees understand and believe in the brand.","zh":"內部市場推廣幫助員工理解並相信品牌。"},{"en":"Internal marketing is marketing directed at employees inside an organisation.","zh":"Internal marketing 是針對組織內員工的市場推廣。"},{"en":"A hospital uses internal marketing when it explains a new patient-care promise to nurses and clerks.","zh":"醫院向護士和文員解釋新的病人照顧承諾時，就是在做內部市場推廣。"},{"en":"If internal marketing works, employees can deliver the public message more naturally.","zh":"如果內部市場推廣奏效，員工可以更自然地實現對外訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase treats employees as an audience that must be informed and persuaded.","zh":"這個片語把員工視為必須被告知和說服的受眾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a powerful emotional connection","meaning":"強烈的情感連繫","examples":[{"en":"Employees need a powerful emotional connection to the products and services they sell.","zh":"員工需要與自己銷售的產品和服務有強烈的情感連繫。"},{"en":"A powerful emotional connection is a strong feeling of belief, pride, or attachment.","zh":"Powerful emotional connection 是強烈的信念、自豪或依附感。"},{"en":"Teachers may work harder when they feel an emotional connection to their school’s mission.","zh":"當老師對學校使命有情感連繫時，他們可能工作更努力。"},{"en":"If employees feel emotionally connected, they may represent the brand more sincerely.","zh":"如果員工有情感連繫，他們可能更真誠地代表品牌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes motivation that comes from feeling, not only instruction.","zh":"這個片語描述來自感受，而不只是指示的動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"products and services","meaning":"產品和服務","examples":[{"en":"Employees should feel connected to the products and services they sell.","zh":"員工應該與自己銷售的產品和服務有連繫。"},{"en":"Products and services are the goods and help that a business provides.","zh":"Products and services 是企業提供的貨品和幫助。"},{"en":"A phone shop sells products like phones and services like repairs or data plans.","zh":"電話店銷售手機等產品，也提供維修或數據計劃等服務。"},{"en":"If staff understand both products and services, they can answer customers more clearly.","zh":"如果員工理解產品和服務，他們就能更清楚回答顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both physical items and useful actions offered to customers.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋實體物品和提供給顧客的有用行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"without that connection","meaning":"沒有那種連繫的話","examples":[{"en":"Without that connection, employees may weaken the brand promise.","zh":"沒有那種連繫的話，員工可能削弱品牌承諾。"},{"en":"Without that connection means if the emotional or practical link is missing.","zh":"Without that connection 指如果缺少情感或實際連繫。"},{"en":"Without a connection to the school’s values, teachers may treat new policies as empty slogans.","zh":"如果老師與學校價值沒有連繫，他們可能把新政策視為空洞口號。"},{"en":"If staff do not feel connected, they may serve customers mechanically.","zh":"如果員工沒有連繫感，他們可能機械式地服務顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the negative result of a missing link.","zh":"這個片語引出缺少連繫帶來的負面結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be likely to","meaning":"很可能會","examples":[{"en":"Employees are likely to undermine advertising promises if they feel no connection.","zh":"如果員工沒有連繫感，他們很可能會削弱廣告承諾。"},{"en":"To be likely to do something means to have a strong chance of doing it.","zh":"To be likely to do something 指有很大機會做某事。"},{"en":"A tired student is likely to make careless mistakes during a test.","zh":"疲倦的學生很可能在測驗中犯粗心錯誤。"},{"en":"If employees feel ignored, they are more likely to resist change.","zh":"如果員工感到被忽視，他們更可能抗拒改變。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses probability, not certainty.","zh":"這個片語表達可能性，而不是確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"undermine the expectations","meaning":"削弱……期望","examples":[{"en":"Disengaged employees may undermine the expectations set by advertising.","zh":"缺乏投入感的員工可能削弱廣告所建立的期望。"},{"en":"To undermine the expectations means to weaken or disappoint what people were led to expect.","zh":"To undermine the expectations 指削弱或令先前建立的期待落空。"},{"en":"A hotel advertisement may create high expectations, but rude service can undermine them.","zh":"酒店廣告可能建立高期望，但粗魯服務可以削弱這些期望。"},{"en":"If staff behaviour conflicts with a promise, customer trust may fall.","zh":"如果員工行為與承諾衝突，顧客信任可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damaging the hopes or standards created earlier.","zh":"這個片語描述破壞早前建立的希望或標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"expectations set by","meaning":"由……建立的期望","examples":[{"en":"Employees can undermine the expectations set by company advertising.","zh":"員工可以削弱由公司廣告建立的期望。"},{"en":"Expectations set by something are the hopes or standards created by it.","zh":"Expectations set by something 是由某事創造的希望或標準。"},{"en":"A school brochure sets expectations about teaching quality and support.","zh":"學校簡介冊會建立關於教學質素和支援的期望。"},{"en":"If reality falls below expectations set by marketing, customers may feel cheated.","zh":"如果現實低於由市場推廣建立的期望，顧客可能感到受騙。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the source of people’s expectations.","zh":"這個片語指出人們期望的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in some cases","meaning":"在某些情況下","examples":[{"en":"In some cases, employees do not understand what the company has promised.","zh":"在某些情況下，員工不理解公司承諾了甚麼。"},{"en":"In some cases means in certain situations, but not always.","zh":"In some cases 指在某些情況中，但不是每一次。"},{"en":"In some cases, students fail not because they are lazy but because they do not understand the question.","zh":"在某些情況下，學生失敗不是因為懶惰，而是因為不理解題目。"},{"en":"If a writer uses this phrase, they are limiting the claim to particular examples.","zh":"如果作者使用這個片語，他是在把說法限制於特定例子。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids saying that something happens every time.","zh":"這個片語避免說某事每次都發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what you have promised the public","meaning":"你向公眾作出的承諾","examples":[{"en":"Employees may not understand what the company has promised the public.","zh":"員工可能不理解公司向公眾作出了甚麼承諾。"},{"en":"What you have promised the public means the claims or commitments made openly to customers or society.","zh":"What you have promised the public 指公開向顧客或社會作出的聲稱或承諾。"},{"en":"A school must train staff if it has promised the public safer classrooms.","zh":"如果學校向公眾承諾更安全的課室，就必須培訓員工。"},{"en":"If public promises are unclear internally, employees cannot deliver them properly.","zh":"如果對外承諾在內部不清晰，員工就不能妥善實現它們。"},{"en":"This phrase connects external promises with internal responsibility.","zh":"這個片語把對外承諾與內部責任連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"end up doing something","meaning":"最終做某事","examples":[{"en":"Employees may end up working against the company’s message.","zh":"員工可能最終做出與公司訊息相反的事。"},{"en":"To end up doing something means to finally do something, often unintentionally.","zh":"To end up doing something 指最後做了某事，通常不是原本有意如此。"},{"en":"A student who delays revision may end up studying all night before the exam.","zh":"拖延溫習的學生可能最終在考試前通宵讀書。"},{"en":"If employees are not guided, they may end up damaging the brand without meaning to.","zh":"如果員工沒有得到引導，他們可能無意中最終損害品牌。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows an unexpected or unwanted final result.","zh":"這個片語常顯示意料之外或不想要的最終結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"work at cross-purposes","meaning":"目標互相衝突；各行其是","examples":[{"en":"Employees can end up working at cross-purposes with the advertising campaign.","zh":"員工最終可能與廣告活動目標互相衝突。"},{"en":"To work at cross-purposes means to act in ways that conflict with each other’s goals.","zh":"To work at cross-purposes 指行動方式彼此目標衝突。"},{"en":"A teacher and parent work at cross-purposes if one encourages rest while the other demands more drilling.","zh":"如果老師鼓勵休息，而家長要求更多操練，兩者就是目標互相衝突。"},{"en":"If marketing promises speed but staff are told to cut service time, the messages may conflict.","zh":"如果市場推廣承諾速度，但員工被要求削減服務時間，訊息可能衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people or plans pulling in different directions.","zh":"這個片語描述人或計劃朝不同方向拉扯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in other cases","meaning":"在另一些情況下","examples":[{"en":"In other cases, employees may not believe in the brand.","zh":"在另一些情況下，員工可能不相信品牌。"},{"en":"In other cases means in different situations from the ones just mentioned.","zh":"In other cases 指在剛才提到情況以外的另一些情況中。"},{"en":"Some students struggle because of grammar; in other cases, the problem is confidence.","zh":"有些學生因文法而吃力；在另一些情況下，問題是信心。"},{"en":"This phrase helps a writer present another type of example.","zh":"這個片語幫助作者提出另一類例子。"},{"en":"It shows that a problem can appear in more than one form.","zh":"它顯示問題可以以不止一種形式出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"believe in the brand","meaning":"相信品牌","examples":[{"en":"Employees need to believe in the brand they represent.","zh":"員工需要相信自己所代表的品牌。"},{"en":"To believe in the brand means to trust its values, promises, and purpose.","zh":"To believe in the brand 指信任其價值、承諾和目的。"},{"en":"A teacher believes in a school brand when they genuinely support its learning philosophy.","zh":"當老師真心支持學校的學習理念時，他就是相信學校品牌。"},{"en":"If employees believe in the brand, their service sounds more sincere.","zh":"如果員工相信品牌，他們的服務聽起來會更真誠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inner trust, not just knowledge of a logo.","zh":"這個片語描述內在信任，而不只是知道一個標誌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"feel disengaged","meaning":"感到抽離；缺乏投入感","examples":[{"en":"Some employees feel disengaged when they do not believe in the brand.","zh":"有些員工不相信品牌時會感到抽離。"},{"en":"To feel disengaged means to feel mentally or emotionally disconnected from work.","zh":"To feel disengaged 指在精神或情感上與工作脫節。"},{"en":"A student may feel disengaged if every lesson seems unrelated to real life.","zh":"如果每堂課似乎都與現實生活無關，學生可能感到抽離。"},{"en":"If employees feel disengaged, they may do only the minimum required.","zh":"如果員工缺乏投入感，他們可能只做最低要求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes low involvement and weak emotional connection.","zh":"這個片語描述低參與度和薄弱情感連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hostile toward","meaning":"對……懷有敵意","examples":[{"en":"Some employees may even feel hostile toward the company.","zh":"有些員工甚至可能對公司懷有敵意。"},{"en":"To be hostile toward someone means to feel angry, unfriendly, or opposed to them.","zh":"To be hostile toward someone 指對某人感到憤怒、不友善或反對。"},{"en":"Residents may become hostile toward a project if they feel ignored by planners.","zh":"如果居民覺得被規劃者忽視，他們可能對項目懷有敵意。"},{"en":"If employees feel cheated, hostility can replace loyalty.","zh":"如果員工覺得被欺騙，敵意可能取代忠誠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active negative feeling, not simple disagreement.","zh":"這個片語描述主動的負面感受，而不只是不同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"care about","meaning":"關心；在乎","examples":[{"en":"Employees work harder when they care about the brand.","zh":"當員工在乎品牌時，他們會更努力工作。"},{"en":"To care about something means to feel that it matters.","zh":"To care about something 指覺得某事重要。"},{"en":"Students write better essays when they care about the topic.","zh":"當學生在乎題目時，他們會寫出更好的作文。"},{"en":"If employees care about customers, they may solve problems more patiently.","zh":"如果員工關心顧客，他們可能更有耐性地解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional concern that can affect behaviour.","zh":"這個片語描述會影響行為的情感關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be motivated to","meaning":"有動力去……","examples":[{"en":"Employees are motivated to work harder when they believe in the brand.","zh":"當員工相信品牌時，他們會有動力更努力工作。"},{"en":"To be motivated to do something means to feel willing and driven to do it.","zh":"To be motivated to do something 指感到願意並受推動去做某事。"},{"en":"A student is motivated to practise speaking when they see real improvement.","zh":"當學生看見真實進步時，他會有動力練習說話。"},{"en":"If workers believe their effort matters, they may be motivated to do more.","zh":"如果員工相信自己的努力重要，他們可能有動力做更多。"},{"en":"This phrase links inner desire with action.","zh":"這個片語把內在欲望與行動連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"loyalty to the company","meaning":"對公司的忠誠","examples":[{"en":"Employees’ loyalty to the company increases when they believe in the brand.","zh":"當員工相信品牌時，他們對公司的忠誠會增加。"},{"en":"Loyalty to the company means commitment and faithfulness to the organisation.","zh":"Loyalty to the company 指對組織的投入和忠誠。"},{"en":"Workers may show loyalty to the company by staying during difficult periods.","zh":"員工在困難時期仍留下來，可能是對公司表現忠誠。"},{"en":"If employees feel respected, their loyalty may become stronger.","zh":"如果員工感到受尊重，他們的忠誠可能更強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a long-term bond between employees and an employer.","zh":"這個片語描述員工與僱主之間的長期連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be united and inspired by","meaning":"因……而團結並受到鼓舞","examples":[{"en":"Employees are united and inspired by a common purpose.","zh":"員工因共同目標而團結並受到鼓舞。"},{"en":"To be united and inspired by something means to feel joined together and encouraged by it.","zh":"To be united and inspired by something 指因某事感到連結並受到鼓勵。"},{"en":"A class can be united and inspired by a shared goal to raise money for charity.","zh":"班級可以因為共同為慈善籌款的目標而團結並受到鼓舞。"},{"en":"If staff share a meaningful purpose, teamwork may become stronger.","zh":"如果員工共享有意義的目標，團隊合作可能更強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both togetherness and motivation.","zh":"這個片語同時描述團結和動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a common sense of purpose","meaning":"共同的目標感","examples":[{"en":"A strong brand can give employees a common sense of purpose.","zh":"強大的品牌可以給員工共同的目標感。"},{"en":"A common sense of purpose is a shared feeling that everyone is working toward the same meaningful goal.","zh":"Common sense of purpose 是大家都朝同一個有意義目標努力的共同感覺。"},{"en":"A school team gains a common sense of purpose when teachers agree that every student can improve.","zh":"當老師同意每位學生都能進步時，學校團隊會獲得共同目標感。"},{"en":"If workers share a purpose, daily tasks feel less random.","zh":"如果員工共享目標，日常任務就不會感覺那麼零散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shared direction and meaning.","zh":"這個片語描述共同方向和意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a sense of identity","meaning":"身份認同感","examples":[{"en":"Internal marketing can give employees a stronger sense of identity.","zh":"內部市場推廣可以給員工更強的身份認同感。"},{"en":"A sense of identity is the feeling of knowing who you are and what group you belong to.","zh":"Sense of identity 是知道自己是誰以及屬於哪個群體的感覺。"},{"en":"Students may gain a sense of identity from their school house, club, or language group.","zh":"學生可能從社、學會或語言群體中獲得身份認同感。"},{"en":"If employees identify with the company, they may represent it more proudly.","zh":"如果員工認同公司，他們可能更自豪地代表它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes belonging and self-understanding.","zh":"這個片語描述歸屬和自我理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"done poorly","meaning":"做得差","examples":[{"en":"In many companies, internal marketing is done poorly.","zh":"在許多公司，內部市場推廣做得差。"},{"en":"Done poorly means carried out badly or ineffectively.","zh":"Done poorly 指執行得差或無效。"},{"en":"A lesson is done poorly if students leave without understanding the main idea.","zh":"如果學生離開課堂時仍不理解主旨，這堂課就是做得差。"},{"en":"If internal communication is done poorly, employees may feel confused or excluded.","zh":"如果內部溝通做得差，員工可能感到困惑或被排除。"},{"en":"This phrase judges the quality of execution.","zh":"這個片語判斷執行質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"if at all","meaning":"即使有做的話","examples":[{"en":"Internal marketing is often done poorly, if at all.","zh":"內部市場推廣經常做得差，即使有做的話。"},{"en":"If at all means if it happens at all, suggesting it may not happen.","zh":"If at all 指如果真的有發生，暗示它可能根本沒有發生。"},{"en":"Some students revise only briefly, if at all, before a small test.","zh":"有些學生在小測前只短暫溫習，即使有溫習的話。"},{"en":"If staff training happens rarely, if at all, employees cannot support new campaigns.","zh":"如果員工培訓很少發生，甚至根本沒有，員工就不能支持新推廣活動。"},{"en":"This phrase adds doubt about whether something even exists or happens.","zh":"這個片語加入對某事是否存在或發生的懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"recognise the need to","meaning":"意識到有需要……","examples":[{"en":"Executives recognise the need to keep employees informed.","zh":"企業高層意識到有需要讓員工知道最新情況。"},{"en":"To recognise the need to do something means to understand that it is necessary.","zh":"To recognise the need to do something 指明白某事是必要的。"},{"en":"A teacher may recognise the need to explain exam instructions more clearly.","zh":"老師可能意識到有需要更清楚解釋考試指示。"},{"en":"If managers recognise the need for communication, fewer rumours may spread.","zh":"如果管理者意識到有需要溝通，謠言可能較少擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase shows awareness of a necessary action.","zh":"這個片語顯示對必要行動的意識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"keep people informed about","meaning":"讓人知道……","examples":[{"en":"Managers should keep people informed about the company’s strategy.","zh":"管理者應讓人知道公司的策略。"},{"en":"To keep people informed about something means to give them updated information about it.","zh":"To keep people informed about something 指向人們提供關於某事的最新資訊。"},{"en":"A school keeps parents informed about exam dates through notices and messages.","zh":"學校透過通告和訊息讓家長知道考試日期。"},{"en":"If employees are kept informed, they can adjust their work more confidently.","zh":"如果員工獲得資訊，他們可以更有信心地調整工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regular and clear communication.","zh":"這個片語描述定期而清晰的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"strategy and direction","meaning":"策略和方向","examples":[{"en":"Employees should understand the company’s strategy and direction.","zh":"員工應理解公司的策略和方向。"},{"en":"Strategy and direction means the plan a company follows and where it intends to go.","zh":"Strategy and direction 指公司遵循的計劃以及它打算走向哪裏。"},{"en":"A school’s strategy and direction may focus on stronger reading and better student support.","zh":"學校的策略和方向可能集中於提升閱讀和改善學生支援。"},{"en":"If staff do not know the direction, their work may become scattered.","zh":"如果員工不知道方向，他們的工作可能變得分散。"},{"en":"This phrase combines planning with future movement.","zh":"這個片語把規劃與未來走向結合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"convince employees of","meaning":"令員工相信……","examples":[{"en":"Companies need to convince employees of the brand’s power.","zh":"公司需要令員工相信品牌的力量。"},{"en":"To convince employees of something means to make them believe it is true or valuable.","zh":"To convince employees of something 指令員工相信某事是真實或有價值的。"},{"en":"A principal must convince teachers of the value of a new teaching method.","zh":"校長必須令老師相信新教學方法的價值。"},{"en":"If employees are not convinced, they may repeat the message without energy.","zh":"如果員工不被說服，他們可能沒有熱情地重複訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes internal persuasion based on trust and evidence.","zh":"這個片語描述基於信任和證據的內部說服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the brand’s power","meaning":"品牌的力量","examples":[{"en":"Some executives fail to convince employees of the brand’s power.","zh":"一些企業高層未能令員工相信品牌的力量。"},{"en":"The brand’s power is its ability to influence feelings, trust, choices, and loyalty.","zh":"Brand’s power 是品牌影響感受、信任、選擇和忠誠的能力。"},{"en":"A strong school brand may make parents feel safe sending their children there.","zh":"強大的學校品牌可能令家長放心把孩子送到那裏。"},{"en":"If employees see the brand’s power, they may take customer service more seriously.","zh":"如果員工看見品牌的力量，他們可能更認真看待顧客服務。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the real influence a brand can have.","zh":"這個片語指品牌能產生的真實影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take something as a given","meaning":"視……為理所當然","examples":[{"en":"Many executives take employees’ belief in the brand as a given.","zh":"許多企業高層把員工相信品牌視為理所當然。"},{"en":"To take something as a given means to assume it is already true without checking.","zh":"To take something as a given 指未經查證就假設某事已經是真的。"},{"en":"A teacher should not take students’ understanding as a given after one explanation.","zh":"老師不應在解釋一次後，就把學生理解視為理所當然。"},{"en":"If managers assume employees already believe the brand, they may skip necessary communication.","zh":"如果管理者假設員工已相信品牌，他們可能跳過必要溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against careless assumptions.","zh":"這個片語提醒人不要作草率假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"send out messages to","meaning":"向……發出訊息","examples":[{"en":"Companies should send out consistent messages to employees and customers.","zh":"公司應向員工和顧客發出一致訊息。"},{"en":"To send out messages to people means to communicate information or ideas to them.","zh":"To send out messages to people 指向人們傳達資訊或理念。"},{"en":"A school sends out messages to parents when exam arrangements change.","zh":"當考試安排改變，學校會向家長發出訊息。"},{"en":"If different groups receive different messages, confusion may grow.","zh":"如果不同群體收到不同訊息，混亂可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes spreading information to an audience.","zh":"這個片語描述向受眾傳播資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the marketplace","meaning":"市場；顧客市場","examples":[{"en":"Employees need to hear the same messages that companies send to the marketplace.","zh":"員工需要聽到公司傳達給市場的同一訊息。"},{"en":"The marketplace means the public world of customers, competitors, and buyers.","zh":"Marketplace 指由顧客、競爭者和買家組成的公眾商業世界。"},{"en":"A new product enters the marketplace when customers can buy it and compare it with others.","zh":"當顧客可以購買並與其他產品比較時，新產品就進入市場。"},{"en":"If employees hear a different message from the marketplace, trust may weaken.","zh":"如果員工聽到與顧客市場不同的訊息，信任可能削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the external business environment.","zh":"這個片語指外部商業環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"internal and external communications","meaning":"內外溝通","examples":[{"en":"Internal and external communications are often mismatched.","zh":"內外溝通經常不一致。"},{"en":"Internal and external communications are messages sent inside the organisation and to the public outside it.","zh":"Internal and external communications 是發給組織內部和外部公眾的訊息。"},{"en":"A school’s internal emails and public notices should explain the same policy consistently.","zh":"學校的內部電郵和公開通告應一致地解釋同一政策。"},{"en":"If internal and external communication conflict, employees may question leadership honesty.","zh":"如果內外溝通衝突，員工可能質疑領導層誠信。"},{"en":"This phrase compares inside messaging with outside messaging.","zh":"這個片語比較內部訊息與外部訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be mismatched","meaning":"不一致；不配合","examples":[{"en":"Messages to employees and customers may be mismatched.","zh":"給員工和顧客的訊息可能不一致。"},{"en":"To be mismatched means to not fit together properly.","zh":"To be mismatched 指彼此不能恰當配合。"},{"en":"A lesson is mismatched if the exercise is too hard for beginners.","zh":"如果練習對初學者太難，課堂內容就是不配合。"},{"en":"If staff are told one thing and customers hear another, the messages are mismatched.","zh":"如果員工被告知一套說法，而顧客聽到另一套，訊息就是不一致。"},{"en":"This phrase describes poor fit or inconsistency.","zh":"這個片語描述不配合或不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"threaten someone’s perceptions of","meaning":"威脅某人對……的看法","examples":[{"en":"Mixed messages threaten employees’ perceptions of the company’s integrity.","zh":"混亂訊息威脅員工對公司誠信的看法。"},{"en":"To threaten someone’s perceptions of something means to damage how they see or judge it.","zh":"To threaten someone’s perceptions of something 指損害某人如何看待或判斷某事。"},{"en":"A school’s unfair punishment may threaten parents’ perception of its fairness.","zh":"學校不公平懲罰可能威脅家長對其公平性的看法。"},{"en":"If employees see inconsistency, they may stop seeing the company as honest.","zh":"如果員工看見不一致，他們可能不再視公司為誠實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harm to people’s trust or impression.","zh":"這個片語描述對信任或印象的損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"company integrity","meaning":"公司誠信","examples":[{"en":"Conflicting messages can damage employees’ view of company integrity.","zh":"衝突訊息可以損害員工對公司誠信的看法。"},{"en":"Company integrity means the honesty, consistency, and moral reliability of a company.","zh":"Company integrity 指公司的誠實、一致性和道德可靠性。"},{"en":"A company shows integrity when it treats staff fairly even during difficult times.","zh":"公司在困難時期仍公平對待員工，就是展現誠信。"},{"en":"If public promises differ from internal actions, company integrity may be questioned.","zh":"如果公開承諾與內部行動不同，公司誠信可能受到質疑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes whether a company can be trusted.","zh":"這個片語描述公司是否值得信任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be told one thing by","meaning":"被……告知一套說法","examples":[{"en":"Employees may be told one thing by management and hear another in public.","zh":"員工可能被管理層告知一套說法，卻在公眾面前聽到另一套。"},{"en":"To be told one thing by someone means to receive one version of information from that person or group.","zh":"To be told one thing by someone 指從某人或某群體收到一個版本的資訊。"},{"en":"Students feel confused if they are told one thing by one teacher and another by another teacher.","zh":"如果學生被一位老師告知一套說法，卻被另一位老師告知另一套，他們會困惑。"},{"en":"If employees are told one message internally but see a different public message, trust may fall.","zh":"如果員工在內部被告知一個訊息，卻看到不同公開訊息，信任可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces inconsistency in communication.","zh":"這個片語常引出溝通上的不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"management","meaning":"管理層","examples":[{"en":"Employees are told one thing by management but see another public message.","zh":"員工被管理層告知一套說法，卻看見另一個公開訊息。"},{"en":"Management means the people responsible for directing and controlling an organisation.","zh":"Management 指負責指導和控制組織的人。"},{"en":"School management decides timetables, staffing, budgets, and major policies.","zh":"學校管理層決定時間表、人手、預算和主要政策。"},{"en":"If management communicates badly, employees may misunderstand priorities.","zh":"如果管理層溝通差，員工可能誤解優先事項。"},{"en":"This word refers to the leadership group, not ordinary staff.","zh":"這個詞指領導群體，而不是普通員工。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"observe that","meaning":"留意到；觀察到","examples":[{"en":"Employees observe that a different message is being sent to the public.","zh":"員工留意到另一個不同訊息正在傳達給公眾。"},{"en":"To observe that means to notice or point out that something is happening.","zh":"To observe that 指注意到或指出某事正在發生。"},{"en":"A teacher may observe that students become quieter before exams.","zh":"老師可能觀察到學生在考試前變得更安靜。"},{"en":"If workers observe a gap between words and actions, confidence may decline.","zh":"如果員工留意到言行之間有差距，信心可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what someone notices from evidence or experience.","zh":"這個片語引出某人從證據或經驗中注意到的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a different message","meaning":"不同的訊息","examples":[{"en":"A different message may be sent to customers and employees.","zh":"顧客和員工可能收到不同的訊息。"},{"en":"A different message means information or meaning that does not match another message.","zh":"A different message 指與另一訊息不一致的資訊或意思。"},{"en":"A school sends a different message if it praises balance publicly but pressures students privately.","zh":"如果學校公開讚揚平衡，私下卻給學生壓力，它就是發出不同訊息。"},{"en":"If different audiences hear different messages, the organisation may seem dishonest.","zh":"如果不同受眾聽到不同訊息，組織可能顯得不誠實。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights inconsistency in communication.","zh":"這個片語突出溝通上的不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be sent to the public","meaning":"被傳達給公眾","examples":[{"en":"A different message was being sent to the public.","zh":"不同的訊息正在被傳達給公眾。"},{"en":"To be sent to the public means to be communicated openly to customers or society.","zh":"To be sent to the public 指公開傳達給顧客或社會。"},{"en":"A safety warning is sent to the public when a product may be dangerous.","zh":"當產品可能有危險時，安全警告會被傳達給公眾。"},{"en":"If public communication differs from internal instructions, employees may feel misled.","zh":"如果公開溝通與內部指示不同，員工可能感到被誤導。"},{"en":"This phrase describes outward communication beyond the company.","zh":"這個片語描述公司以外的對外溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"For instance, one health insurance company sent conflicting messages.","zh":"例如，一間醫療保險公司發出了互相衝突的訊息。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"For instance 指例如。"},{"en":"Many habits affect learning; for instance, poor sleep can weaken memory.","zh":"許多習慣影響學習；例如，睡眠不足可以削弱記憶。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to make a general point clearer with a specific case.","zh":"作者使用這個片語，以具體個案令一般觀點更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an example that supports the previous idea.","zh":"這個片語引出支持前文想法的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"health insurance company","meaning":"醫療保險公司","examples":[{"en":"A health insurance company advertised that patients were its top priority.","zh":"一間醫療保險公司宣傳病人是其首要任務。"},{"en":"A health insurance company sells plans that help people pay medical costs.","zh":"Health insurance company 銷售幫助人支付醫療費用的計劃。"},{"en":"Families may buy cover from a health insurance company to reduce hospital bills.","zh":"家庭可能向醫療保險公司購買保障，以減少住院費用。"},{"en":"If a health insurance company claims to care about patients, its internal targets should support that claim.","zh":"如果醫療保險公司聲稱關心病人，其內部目標應支持這說法。"},{"en":"This phrase names a business connected to healthcare financing.","zh":"這個片語命名與醫療融資相關的企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the welfare of patients","meaning":"病人的福祉","examples":[{"en":"The company advertised that the welfare of patients was its number one priority.","zh":"公司宣傳病人的福祉是其首要任務。"},{"en":"The welfare of patients means patients’ health, safety, comfort, and overall well-being.","zh":"Welfare of patients 指病人的健康、安全、舒適和整體福祉。"},{"en":"A hospital protects the welfare of patients by keeping wards clean and medicine accurate.","zh":"醫院透過保持病房清潔和藥物準確來保障病人福祉。"},{"en":"If cost cutting harms care, patient welfare may suffer.","zh":"如果削減成本傷害護理，病人福祉可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what is good for patients, not just company profit.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於對病人有益的事，而不只是公司利潤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"number one priority","meaning":"首要任務","examples":[{"en":"The welfare of patients was presented as the company’s number one priority.","zh":"病人的福祉被呈現為公司的首要任務。"},{"en":"Number one priority means the most important concern before all others.","zh":"Number one priority 指比所有其他事情更重要的首要關注。"},{"en":"During a fire drill, student safety is the number one priority.","zh":"在火警演習期間，學生安全是首要任務。"},{"en":"If a company says customers are its top priority, its actions must prove it.","zh":"如果公司說顧客是首要任務，其行動必須證明這一點。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the thing that should come first.","zh":"這個片語指出最應優先處理的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"stock options","meaning":"股票期權","examples":[{"en":"Employees were told to increase the value of their stock options.","zh":"員工被告知要提高其股票期權的價值。"},{"en":"Stock options are rights that allow employees to buy company shares at a set price.","zh":"Stock options 是讓員工可以按指定價格購買公司股票的權利。"},{"en":"A start-up may offer stock options when it cannot yet pay very high salaries.","zh":"初創公司在未能支付很高薪金時，可能提供股票期權。"},{"en":"If a company’s share price rises, stock options may become more valuable.","zh":"如果公司股價上升，股票期權可能變得更有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to employee rewards and financial incentives.","zh":"這個片語屬於員工獎勵和金錢誘因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cost reductions","meaning":"削減成本","examples":[{"en":"Employees were encouraged to increase value through cost reductions.","zh":"員工被鼓勵透過削減成本來增加價值。"},{"en":"Cost reductions are actions that lower the amount of money a company spends.","zh":"Cost reductions 是降低公司開支的行動。"},{"en":"A school may seek cost reductions by saving electricity and printing less paper.","zh":"學校可能透過節省電力和減少打印來尋求削減成本。"},{"en":"If cost reductions go too far, service quality may decline.","zh":"如果削減成本過度，服務質素可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cutting expenses, sometimes with risks.","zh":"這個片語描述減少開支，有時帶有風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"financial services institution","meaning":"金融服務機構","examples":[{"en":"A major financial services institution changed its public message.","zh":"一間大型金融服務機構改變了其公開訊息。"},{"en":"A financial services institution is an organisation such as a bank, insurer, or investment company.","zh":"Financial services institution 是銀行、保險公司或投資公司等組織。"},{"en":"A bank is a financial services institution because it handles savings, loans, and advice.","zh":"銀行是金融服務機構，因為它處理存款、貸款和建議。"},{"en":"If such an institution changes its role, employees must understand the new customer promise.","zh":"如果這類機構改變角色，員工必須理解新的顧客承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase names an organisation in the finance industry.","zh":"這個片語命名金融業中的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make a major shift in focus","meaning":"在重點上作出重大轉變","examples":[{"en":"The company made a major shift in focus from retailing to advising.","zh":"公司在重點上作出重大轉變，從零售轉向顧問服務。"},{"en":"To make a major shift in focus means to change the main area of attention or business direction.","zh":"To make a major shift in focus 指改變主要關注範圍或業務方向。"},{"en":"A school may make a major shift in focus from exam drilling to reading confidence.","zh":"學校可能在重點上作出重大轉變，從考試操練轉向閱讀信心。"},{"en":"If focus changes but staff behaviour does not, customers may not notice the new direction.","zh":"如果重點改變但員工行為沒有改變，顧客可能察覺不到新方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a significant change in priorities.","zh":"這個片語描述優先事項上的重大改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"from being…to…","meaning":"從……變成……","examples":[{"en":"The company shifted from being a financial retailer to a financial adviser.","zh":"公司從金融零售商變成金融顧問。"},{"en":"From being A to B shows a change from one identity or role to another.","zh":"From being A to B 顯示從一種身份或角色轉變成另一種。"},{"en":"A student may move from being quiet in class to becoming a confident speaker.","zh":"學生可能從課堂上安靜的人變成自信的發言者。"},{"en":"If a company changes from being a seller to an adviser, staff need new skills.","zh":"如果公司從銷售者變成顧問，員工需要新技能。"},{"en":"This structure clearly shows transformation.","zh":"這個結構清楚顯示轉化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"financial retailer","meaning":"金融零售商","examples":[{"en":"The company wanted to move away from being a financial retailer.","zh":"公司想擺脫金融零售商的角色。"},{"en":"A financial retailer sells financial products such as accounts, loans, insurance, or investments.","zh":"Financial retailer 銷售戶口、貸款、保險或投資等金融產品。"},{"en":"A bank branch acts as a financial retailer when staff mainly process products and transactions.","zh":"當銀行分行員工主要處理產品和交易時，它就是金融零售商。"},{"en":"If customers need advice, a pure retailer role may feel too limited.","zh":"如果顧客需要建議，純零售角色可能顯得太有限。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sales-focused role in finance.","zh":"這個片語描述金融業中以銷售為主的角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"financial adviser","meaning":"金融顧問","examples":[{"en":"The institution wanted to become a financial adviser.","zh":"該機構想成為金融顧問。"},{"en":"A financial adviser helps people make decisions about money, savings, insurance, or investments.","zh":"Financial adviser 幫助人們就金錢、儲蓄、保險或投資作決定。"},{"en":"A family may consult a financial adviser before buying insurance or planning retirement.","zh":"家庭在購買保險或規劃退休前，可能諮詢金融顧問。"},{"en":"If staff become advisers, they must listen and guide rather than simply process transactions.","zh":"如果員工成為顧問，他們必須聆聽和引導，而不只是處理交易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a guidance-based financial role.","zh":"這個片語描述以指導為本的金融角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"customer experience","meaning":"顧客體驗","examples":[{"en":"Research showed that the customer experience had not changed.","zh":"研究顯示顧客體驗沒有改變。"},{"en":"Customer experience means what customers feel, see, and receive when dealing with a company.","zh":"Customer experience 指顧客與公司接觸時感到、看見和得到的東西。"},{"en":"A café’s customer experience includes waiting time, staff attitude, taste, and payment ease.","zh":"咖啡店的顧客體驗包括等候時間、員工態度、味道和付款方便程度。"},{"en":"If branding changes but customer experience stays the same, the campaign may fail.","zh":"如果品牌改變但顧客體驗不變，推廣活動可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on reality from the customer’s side.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於顧客一方的現實感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"it turned out that","meaning":"結果發現","examples":[{"en":"It turned out that company leaders had not sold the change internally.","zh":"結果發現，公司領導層沒有向內部推廣這項變革。"},{"en":"It turned out that means the truth was discovered later.","zh":"It turned out that 指後來發現真相是如此。"},{"en":"It turned out that the student failed because they had misunderstood the question.","zh":"結果發現，學生失敗是因為誤解了題目。"},{"en":"If a campaign fails, it may turn out that staff were never properly trained.","zh":"如果推廣活動失敗，結果可能發現員工從未得到適當培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a later discovery, often surprising.","zh":"這個片語引出後來發現的事情，通常帶有意外感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"make an effort to","meaning":"努力去……","examples":[{"en":"Leaders had not made an effort to sell the change internally.","zh":"領導層沒有努力向內部推廣這項變革。"},{"en":"To make an effort to do something means to try seriously to do it.","zh":"To make an effort to do something 指認真嘗試做某事。"},{"en":"A student makes an effort to improve pronunciation by recording and listening to their speech.","zh":"學生透過錄音和聆聽自己的說話，努力改善發音。"},{"en":"If managers make no effort to explain change, employees may resist it.","zh":"如果管理者沒有努力解釋變革，員工可能抗拒它。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses active trying, not passive hope.","zh":"這個片語強調主動嘗試，而不是被動希望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sell the change internally","meaning":"向內部推廣變革","examples":[{"en":"The company failed to sell the change internally.","zh":"公司未能向內部推廣變革。"},{"en":"To sell the change internally means to persuade employees to understand and support a change.","zh":"To sell the change internally 指說服員工理解並支持變革。"},{"en":"A school must sell a new homework policy internally before teachers can explain it to parents.","zh":"學校必須先向內部推廣新功課政策，老師才能向家長解釋。"},{"en":"If change is not sold internally, staff may continue old habits.","zh":"如果變革沒有向內部推廣，員工可能繼續舊習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes winning employee support for a new direction.","zh":"這個片語描述為新方向爭取員工支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"churn out transactions","meaning":"機械式大量處理交易","examples":[{"en":"Employees were still churning out transactions.","zh":"員工仍在機械式大量處理交易。"},{"en":"To churn out transactions means to process many financial actions quickly and mechanically.","zh":"To churn out transactions 指快速而機械地處理大量金融操作。"},{"en":"A clerk may churn out forms all day without explaining anything to customers.","zh":"文員可能整天機械式處理表格，而不向顧客解釋任何事情。"},{"en":"If employees only churn out transactions, customers do not feel advised or cared for.","zh":"如果員工只大量處理交易，顧客不會感到得到建議或照顧。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests repetitive work with little personal guidance.","zh":"這個片語暗示重複工作，缺乏個人化指導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"change their behaviour","meaning":"改變行為","examples":[{"en":"Employees had not changed their behaviour to match the new role.","zh":"員工沒有改變行為以配合新角色。"},{"en":"To change their behaviour means to act differently from before.","zh":"To change their behaviour 指以不同於以往的方式行動。"},{"en":"Students change their behaviour when they start asking questions instead of staying silent.","zh":"當學生開始提問而不是沉默時，他們就是改變行為。"},{"en":"If employees do not change behaviour, a new brand message may remain empty.","zh":"如果員工不改變行為，新品牌訊息可能仍然空洞。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on visible action, not just attitude.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於可見行動，而不只是態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"match their new role","meaning":"配合新的角色","examples":[{"en":"Employees had to change their behaviour to match their new adviser role.","zh":"員工必須改變行為，以配合新的顧問角色。"},{"en":"To match their new role means to act in a way that fits new responsibilities.","zh":"To match their new role 指以符合新責任的方式行動。"},{"en":"A student leader must match their new role by helping others, not only speaking loudly.","zh":"學生領袖必須透過幫助他人，而不只是大聲說話，來配合新角色。"},{"en":"If staff move from selling to advising, their behaviour must match the new role.","zh":"如果員工從銷售轉向顧問服務，他們的行為必須配合新角色。"},{"en":"This phrase connects behaviour with changed expectations.","zh":"這個片語把行為與改變後的期望連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"adviser role","meaning":"顧問角色","examples":[{"en":"The new adviser role required employees to behave differently.","zh":"新的顧問角色要求員工以不同方式行事。"},{"en":"An adviser role is a role focused on guiding, explaining, and helping people make decisions.","zh":"Adviser role 是集中於引導、解釋和幫助人作決定的角色。"},{"en":"A teacher takes an adviser role when helping students choose subjects.","zh":"老師幫助學生選科時，就是擔當顧問角色。"},{"en":"If employees take an adviser role, they must listen carefully before recommending products.","zh":"如果員工擔當顧問角色，他們必須先仔細聆聽，再推薦產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a role based on trust and guidance.","zh":"這個片語描述以信任和指導為本的角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"enable employees to","meaning":"使員工能夠……","examples":[{"en":"Companies should enable employees to deliver on customer expectations.","zh":"公司應使員工能夠實現顧客期望。"},{"en":"To enable employees to do something means to give them the tools, training, or authority to do it.","zh":"To enable employees to do something 指給員工工具、培訓或權力去做某事。"},{"en":"A school enables teachers to teach better by giving resources and planning time.","zh":"學校透過提供資源和備課時間，使老師能更好教學。"},{"en":"If employees lack training, they cannot deliver even a good brand promise.","zh":"如果員工缺乏培訓，即使品牌承諾好，他們也不能實現它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows support that makes action possible.","zh":"這個片語顯示令行動成為可能的支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"deliver on customer expectations","meaning":"實現顧客期望","examples":[{"en":"Employees need to deliver on customer expectations.","zh":"員工需要實現顧客期望。"},{"en":"To deliver on customer expectations means to provide the experience customers were led to expect.","zh":"To deliver on customer expectations 指提供顧客被引導期待的體驗。"},{"en":"A delivery company delivers on expectations when parcels arrive safely and on time.","zh":"當速遞公司安全準時送達包裹時，它就是實現顧客期望。"},{"en":"If advertising promises friendly service, staff must make that promise real.","zh":"如果廣告承諾友善服務，員工必須令該承諾成真。"},{"en":"This phrase connects customer promises with actual performance.","zh":"這個片語把顧客承諾與實際表現連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"of course","meaning":"當然","examples":[{"en":"Delivering on customer expectations is important, of course.","zh":"實現顧客期望當然重要。"},{"en":"Of course means naturally, obviously, or as expected.","zh":"Of course 指自然地、明顯地或理所當然地。"},{"en":"Of course, students need practice, but they also need feedback.","zh":"當然，學生需要練習，但他們也需要回饋。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to accept a point before adding another idea.","zh":"作者使用這個片語來先接受一點，再加入另一個想法。"},{"en":"This phrase often softens the move from agreement to a new argument.","zh":"這個片語常用來柔化從同意轉向新論點的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not the only reason","meaning":"並非唯一原因","examples":[{"en":"Customer expectations are not the only reason for internal marketing.","zh":"顧客期望並非內部市場推廣的唯一原因。"},{"en":"Not the only reason means there are other reasons as well.","zh":"Not the only reason 指還有其他原因。"},{"en":"Better marks are not the only reason to read; reading also builds confidence and imagination.","zh":"更好成績並非閱讀的唯一原因；閱讀也建立信心和想像力。"},{"en":"If a company trains staff only for customers, it may miss internal culture benefits.","zh":"如果公司只為顧客而培訓員工，它可能錯過內部文化好處。"},{"en":"This phrase widens the explanation beyond one cause.","zh":"這個片語把解釋擴展到單一原因之外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"match internal and external messages","meaning":"使內外訊息一致","examples":[{"en":"A company needs to match internal and external messages.","zh":"公司需要使內外訊息一致。"},{"en":"To match internal and external messages means to make messages to employees and the public consistent.","zh":"To match internal and external messages 指令傳給員工和公眾的訊息一致。"},{"en":"A school should match what it tells teachers with what it tells parents.","zh":"學校應使告訴老師的內容與告訴家長的內容一致。"},{"en":"If internal and external messages match, employees are less likely to feel misled.","zh":"如果內外訊息一致，員工較不可能感到被誤導。"},{"en":"This phrase describes communication alignment across audiences.","zh":"這個片語描述跨受眾的溝通一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"push the company to achieve","meaning":"推動公司達成……","examples":[{"en":"Internal marketing can push the company to achieve difficult goals.","zh":"內部市場推廣可以推動公司達成困難目標。"},{"en":"To push the company to achieve something means to drive it toward reaching a target.","zh":"To push the company to achieve something 指推動公司朝目標前進。"},{"en":"A public promise can push a school to improve support for weaker students.","zh":"公開承諾可以推動學校改善對能力較弱學生的支援。"},{"en":"If employees share the goal, pressure can become motivation rather than fear.","zh":"如果員工共享目標，壓力可以變成動力而不是恐懼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes encouragement or pressure toward achievement.","zh":"這個片語描述朝成就而來的鼓勵或壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"otherwise be out of reach","meaning":"否則可能難以達到","examples":[{"en":"Some goals might otherwise be out of reach.","zh":"有些目標否則可能難以達到。"},{"en":"Otherwise be out of reach means would be impossible or very difficult without that support or condition.","zh":"Otherwise be out of reach 指如果沒有某種支援或條件，就會不可能或很難達到。"},{"en":"A scholarship can make university possible for a student who would otherwise be unable to afford it.","zh":"獎學金可以令原本負擔不起大學的學生有機會入讀。"},{"en":"If employees unite around a goal, difficult change may become achievable.","zh":"如果員工圍繞目標團結起來，困難變革可能變得可達成。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something becomes possible only because of an extra factor.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事因額外因素才變得可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"launch a campaign","meaning":"推出推廣活動","examples":[{"en":"IBM launched its e-business campaign in 1997.","zh":"IBM 在 1997 年推出其電子商務推廣活動。"},{"en":"To launch a campaign means to start an organised effort to promote an idea, product, or goal.","zh":"To launch a campaign 指開始一個有組織地推廣理念、產品或目標的行動。"},{"en":"A school may launch a reading campaign to encourage students to borrow more books.","zh":"學校可能推出閱讀推廣活動，鼓勵學生借更多書。"},{"en":"If a campaign is launched without preparation, people may ignore it.","zh":"如果推廣活動沒有準備就推出，人們可能忽視它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the formal beginning of a planned promotion.","zh":"這個片語描述有計劃推廣的正式開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"e-business campaign","meaning":"電子商務推廣活動","examples":[{"en":"IBM’s e-business campaign helped change the company’s image.","zh":"IBM 的電子商務推廣活動幫助改變公司形象。"},{"en":"An e-business campaign promotes the idea that business can be done through Internet-based systems.","zh":"E-business campaign 推廣商業可以透過互聯網系統進行的理念。"},{"en":"A bank may run an e-business campaign to encourage customers to use online services.","zh":"銀行可能推行電子商務推廣活動，鼓勵顧客使用網上服務。"},{"en":"If employees understand the digital message, they can help customers trust the change.","zh":"如果員工理解數碼訊息，他們可以幫助顧客信任這項改變。"},{"en":"This phrase names a campaign centred on electronic or online business.","zh":"這個片語命名以電子或網上商務為中心的推廣活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be widely credited for","meaning":"被廣泛認為有功於……","examples":[{"en":"The campaign was widely credited for turning around IBM’s image.","zh":"這項推廣活動被廣泛認為有功於扭轉 IBM 的形象。"},{"en":"To be widely credited for something means many people believe it caused or helped achieve it.","zh":"To be widely credited for something 指許多人相信某事造成或幫助達成某結果。"},{"en":"A teacher may be widely credited for improving a school’s writing results.","zh":"老師可能被廣泛認為有功於改善學校寫作成績。"},{"en":"If many people link success to one action, that action receives public credit.","zh":"如果很多人把成功與某行動連接，該行動就得到公開認可。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad recognition for a positive result.","zh":"這個片語描述因正面成果而得到廣泛承認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"turn around the company’s image","meaning":"扭轉公司形象","examples":[{"en":"The campaign helped turn around the company’s image.","zh":"這項推廣活動幫助扭轉公司形象。"},{"en":"To turn around a company’s image means to change public opinion about it from negative or outdated to positive.","zh":"To turn around a company’s image 指把公眾對公司的看法由負面或過時轉為正面。"},{"en":"A restaurant may turn around its image by improving hygiene and service.","zh":"餐廳可能透過改善衛生和服務來扭轉形象。"},{"en":"If a campaign changes how customers and staff see the company, its image may recover.","zh":"如果推廣活動改變顧客和員工如何看公司，其形象可能恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major improvement in reputation.","zh":"這個片語描述聲譽上的重大改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"choose to ignore","meaning":"選擇忽視","examples":[{"en":"IBM chose to ignore research suggesting consumers were unprepared.","zh":"IBM 選擇忽視顯示消費者未準備好的研究。"},{"en":"To choose to ignore something means to decide not to follow or consider it.","zh":"To choose to ignore something 指決定不跟隨或不考慮某事。"},{"en":"A student may choose to ignore advice and keep using a weak study method.","zh":"學生可能選擇忽視建議，繼續使用薄弱的學習方法。"},{"en":"If leaders ignore warning signs, they take a risk.","zh":"如果領袖忽視警號，他們就在冒險。"},{"en":"This phrase shows deliberate disregard, not simple forgetting.","zh":"這個片語顯示刻意不理，而不是單純忘記。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"research that suggested","meaning":"顯示……的研究","examples":[{"en":"IBM ignored research that suggested consumers were unprepared.","zh":"IBM 忽視了顯示消費者未準備好的研究。"},{"en":"Research that suggested something is evidence pointing toward a possible conclusion.","zh":"Research that suggested something 是指向某個可能結論的證據。"},{"en":"A school may review research that suggests students learn better with shorter homework.","zh":"學校可能檢視顯示學生透過較短功課學得更好的研究。"},{"en":"If research suggests danger, decision-makers should explain why they still proceed.","zh":"如果研究顯示危險，決策者應解釋為何仍繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces evidence behind a claim.","zh":"這個片語引出某主張背後的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be unprepared to","meaning":"未準備好去……","examples":[{"en":"Consumers were unprepared to see IBM as an e-business leader.","zh":"消費者未準備好把 IBM 視為電子商務領導者。"},{"en":"To be unprepared to do something means to not be ready to accept, do, or understand it.","zh":"To be unprepared to do something 指未準備好接受、做或理解某事。"},{"en":"A student may be unprepared to answer if they have not read the passage.","zh":"如果學生沒有讀篇章，他可能未準備好回答問題。"},{"en":"If customers are unprepared for a new brand position, the company must educate them.","zh":"如果顧客未準備好接受新品牌定位，公司就必須教育他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lack of readiness.","zh":"這個片語描述缺乏準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"embrace something as","meaning":"接納……為","examples":[{"en":"Consumers were unprepared to embrace IBM as a leader in e-business.","zh":"消費者未準備好接納 IBM 為電子商務領導者。"},{"en":"To embrace something as a role or identity means to accept it warmly or fully in that way.","zh":"To embrace something as a role or identity 指熱切或完全接受某事具有該角色或身份。"},{"en":"Parents may embrace a school as a caring community when teachers communicate well.","zh":"當老師溝通良好，家長可能接納學校為關懷社群。"},{"en":"If customers do not embrace a company as innovative, its campaign may struggle.","zh":"如果顧客不接納公司為創新者，其推廣活動可能吃力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong acceptance of an identity or idea.","zh":"這個片語描述對身份或理念的強烈接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a leader in","meaning":"……方面的領導者","examples":[{"en":"IBM wanted consumers to see it as a leader in e-business.","zh":"IBM 希望消費者把它視為電子商務方面的領導者。"},{"en":"A leader in a field is a person or organisation seen as one of the best or most advanced in that area.","zh":"Leader in a field 是在某範疇中被視為最好或最先進之一的人或組織。"},{"en":"A school may become a leader in inclusive education if other schools learn from its methods.","zh":"如果其他學校向某校的方法學習，該校可能成為融合教育方面的領導者。"},{"en":"If a company wants to be seen as a leader, its employees must act with confidence and expertise.","zh":"如果公司想被視為領導者，員工必須自信且專業地行事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognised strength in a particular field.","zh":"這個片語描述在特定範疇中被認可的實力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"to the outside world","meaning":"對外界而言","examples":[{"en":"To the outside world, the campaign looked like external marketing.","zh":"對外界而言，這項推廣活動看起來像對外市場推廣。"},{"en":"To the outside world means from the view of people outside the organisation.","zh":"To the outside world 指從組織以外人士的角度來看。"},{"en":"To the outside world, a school may look calm even when teachers are managing many problems internally.","zh":"對外界而言，學校可能看似平靜，即使老師在內部處理許多問題。"},{"en":"If a campaign has an internal purpose, outsiders may still see only the public advertisement.","zh":"如果推廣活動有內部目的，外人仍可能只看見公開廣告。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts external appearance with internal reality.","zh":"這個片語對比外部表象與內部現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"external marketing effort","meaning":"對外市場推廣工作","examples":[{"en":"The campaign looked like an external marketing effort.","zh":"這項推廣活動看起來像對外市場推廣工作。"},{"en":"An external marketing effort is a campaign aimed at customers or the public outside the company.","zh":"External marketing effort 是針對公司外顧客或公眾的推廣活動。"},{"en":"A poster campaign for a new course is an external marketing effort by a school.","zh":"學校為新課程推出海報宣傳，就是一項對外市場推廣工作。"},{"en":"If an external effort also influences employees, it can serve two purposes.","zh":"如果對外工作同時影響員工，它可以服務兩個目的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes outward-facing promotion.","zh":"這個片語描述面向外部的推廣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"align employees around","meaning":"使員工圍繞……保持一致","examples":[{"en":"IBM used the campaign to align employees around a new idea.","zh":"IBM 利用這項推廣活動，使員工圍繞一個新理念保持一致。"},{"en":"To align employees around something means to make staff share the same direction or belief.","zh":"To align employees around something 指使員工共享同一方向或信念。"},{"en":"A principal may align teachers around a new reading goal before changing lessons.","zh":"校長可能在改變課堂前，使老師圍繞新的閱讀目標保持一致。"},{"en":"If employees are aligned around a vision, they are more likely to act consistently.","zh":"如果員工圍繞願景一致，他們較可能一致行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating shared focus inside an organisation.","zh":"這個片語描述在組織內創造共同焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the future of technology","meaning":"科技的未來","examples":[{"en":"The Internet was presented as the future of technology.","zh":"互聯網被呈現為科技的未來。"},{"en":"The future of technology means the direction in which technology is expected to develop.","zh":"Future of technology 指科技預計會發展的方向。"},{"en":"Schools may see artificial intelligence as part of the future of technology in learning.","zh":"學校可能把人工智能視為學習科技未來的一部分。"},{"en":"If employees believe they are working on the future of technology, they may feel more purposeful.","zh":"如果員工相信自己正在參與科技的未來，他們可能更有目標感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a forward-looking technological vision.","zh":"這個片語描述面向未來的科技願景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"change the way someone thinks about","meaning":"改變某人對……的想法","examples":[{"en":"The campaign changed the way employees thought about their work.","zh":"這項推廣活動改變了員工對自己工作的想法。"},{"en":"To change the way someone thinks about something means to alter their understanding or attitude toward it.","zh":"To change the way someone thinks about something 指改變某人對某事的理解或態度。"},{"en":"A teacher’s feedback can change the way a student thinks about mistakes.","zh":"老師的回饋可以改變學生對錯誤的想法。"},{"en":"If employees see their work as part of a bigger mission, their behaviour may change.","zh":"如果員工把工作視為更大使命的一部分，他們的行為可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift in mindset.","zh":"這個片語描述思維方式的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"from how…to how…","meaning":"從如何……到如何……","examples":[{"en":"The campaign affected everything from how products were named to how sales were approached.","zh":"這項推廣活動影響一切，從產品如何命名到銷售如何處理。"},{"en":"From how A to how B shows a wide range of areas affected.","zh":"From how A to how B 顯示受影響範圍廣泛。"},{"en":"A new school policy may affect everything from how homework is set to how parents are contacted.","zh":"新校政可能影響一切，從功課如何設置到家長如何聯絡。"},{"en":"If a campaign changes many daily details, it has deep organisational impact.","zh":"如果推廣活動改變許多日常細節，它就有深層組織影響。"},{"en":"This structure shows that change is broad, not narrow.","zh":"這個結構顯示改變很廣，而不是很窄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"name products","meaning":"為產品命名","examples":[{"en":"The campaign changed how employees named products.","zh":"這項推廣活動改變了員工如何為產品命名。"},{"en":"To name products means to choose names for goods or services.","zh":"To name products 指為貨品或服務選擇名稱。"},{"en":"A bakery may name products after local streets to make them feel familiar.","zh":"麵包店可能用本地街道為產品命名，令它們感覺親切。"},{"en":"If product names match a brand message, customers may understand the offer faster.","zh":"如果產品名稱配合品牌訊息，顧客可能更快理解其定位。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one small but important part of branding.","zh":"這個片語描述品牌建立中細小但重要的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"organise staff","meaning":"組織人手；安排職員","examples":[{"en":"The campaign changed how IBM organised staff.","zh":"這項推廣活動改變了 IBM 如何組織人手。"},{"en":"To organise staff means to arrange employees into teams, roles, or working structures.","zh":"To organise staff 指把員工安排進團隊、角色或工作架構。"},{"en":"A school organises staff differently during exam season to cover supervision duties.","zh":"學校在考試季節會不同地安排職員，以覆蓋監考職責。"},{"en":"If staff are organised around a new strategy, work may become more focused.","zh":"如果員工圍繞新策略被組織，工作可能更集中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how people inside an organisation are arranged.","zh":"這個片語描述組織內的人員如何被安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"approach selling","meaning":"處理銷售的方法","examples":[{"en":"The campaign changed how employees approached selling.","zh":"這項推廣活動改變了員工處理銷售的方法。"},{"en":"To approach selling means to handle the process of persuading customers to buy.","zh":"To approach selling 指處理說服顧客購買的過程。"},{"en":"A salesperson may approach selling by first asking what the customer actually needs.","zh":"銷售員可能先詢問顧客真正需要甚麼，再處理銷售。"},{"en":"If a company moves toward advising, selling becomes more about trust than pressure.","zh":"如果公司轉向顧問服務，銷售就更關乎信任，而不是壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the method or attitude used in sales.","zh":"這個片語描述銷售中使用的方法或態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"successful largely because","meaning":"成功主要是因為","examples":[{"en":"The campaign was successful largely because it gave employees direction.","zh":"這項推廣活動成功主要是因為它給了員工方向。"},{"en":"Successful largely because means successful mainly for a particular reason.","zh":"Successful largely because 指成功主要源於某個特定原因。"},{"en":"A class project may be successful largely because every student has a clear role.","zh":"班級專題可能成功主要是因為每位學生都有清晰角色。"},{"en":"If employees gain direction from a campaign, they may act more confidently.","zh":"如果員工從推廣活動中獲得方向，他們可能更有信心地行動。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main reason for success.","zh":"這個片語指出成功的主要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a sense of direction","meaning":"方向感","examples":[{"en":"The campaign gave employees a sense of direction.","zh":"這項推廣活動給了員工方向感。"},{"en":"A sense of direction is the feeling of knowing where to go or what to work toward.","zh":"Sense of direction 是知道往哪裏走或朝甚麼努力的感覺。"},{"en":"A student gains a sense of direction when a teacher explains the next study steps clearly.","zh":"當老師清楚解釋下一步學習方向，學生就獲得方向感。"},{"en":"If employees lack direction, they may waste effort on conflicting priorities.","zh":"如果員工缺乏方向，他們可能把努力浪費在互相衝突的優先事項上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clarity about future action.","zh":"這個片語描述對未來行動的清晰感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"which in turn","meaning":"而這又","examples":[{"en":"The campaign gave employees purpose, which in turn restored confidence.","zh":"這項推廣活動給員工目標，而這又恢復了信心。"},{"en":"Which in turn means and this then caused the next result.","zh":"Which in turn 指而這接着造成下一個結果。"},{"en":"Better sleep improves concentration, which in turn helps students learn faster.","zh":"更好睡眠改善專注，而這又幫助學生學得更快。"},{"en":"If internal marketing builds belief, this in turn can improve customer service.","zh":"如果內部市場推廣建立信念，而這又可以改善顧客服務。"},{"en":"This phrase links one result to another result in a chain.","zh":"這個片語把一個結果與另一個結果連成因果鏈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"restore someone’s confidence in","meaning":"恢復某人對……的信心","examples":[{"en":"The campaign restored employees’ confidence in IBM’s future.","zh":"這項推廣活動恢復了員工對 IBM 未來的信心。"},{"en":"To restore someone’s confidence in something means to help them trust it again.","zh":"To restore someone’s confidence in something 指幫助某人重新信任某事。"},{"en":"A good mock result can restore a student’s confidence in their exam preparation.","zh":"好的模擬試成績可以恢復學生對考試準備的信心。"},{"en":"If employees see a clear plan, their confidence in leadership may return.","zh":"如果員工看見清晰計劃，他們對領導層的信心可能恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rebuilding lost trust.","zh":"這個片語描述重建失去的信任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ability to predict the future","meaning":"預測未來的能力","examples":[{"en":"Employees regained confidence in IBM’s ability to predict the future.","zh":"員工重新獲得對 IBM 預測未來能力的信心。"},{"en":"Ability to predict the future means the skill or power to foresee what will become important.","zh":"Ability to predict the future 指預見甚麼將變得重要的技能或能力。"},{"en":"A school shows this ability when it prepares students for digital skills before they are required.","zh":"當學校在數碼技能被要求前先培養學生，它就展現這種能力。"},{"en":"If a company predicts future technology correctly, employees may trust its direction.","zh":"如果公司正確預測未來科技，員工可能信任其方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes confidence in foresight.","zh":"這個片語描述對遠見的信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lead the technology industry","meaning":"引領科技行業","examples":[{"en":"IBM wanted to lead the technology industry.","zh":"IBM 希望引領科技行業。"},{"en":"To lead the technology industry means to be among the companies shaping its future direction.","zh":"To lead the technology industry 指成為塑造該行業未來方向的公司之一。"},{"en":"A company may lead an industry by inventing tools others later copy.","zh":"公司可能透過發明後來被其他人模仿的工具來引領行業。"},{"en":"If employees believe their company can lead, they may feel more pride in their work.","zh":"如果員工相信公司能引領行業，他們可能對工作更自豪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being at the front of technological change.","zh":"這個片語描述走在科技變革前沿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"four times more likely to","meaning":"可能性高四倍","examples":[{"en":"People are four times more likely to associate e-business with IBM.","zh":"人們把電子商務與 IBM 聯繫起來的可能性高四倍。"},{"en":"Four times more likely to means the chance is four times higher than another comparison point.","zh":"Four times more likely to 指機會比另一比較點高四倍。"},{"en":"A student who practises daily may be four times more likely to remember new words than one who never reviews.","zh":"每日練習的學生記住新詞的可能性，可能比從不重溫的學生高四倍。"},{"en":"If a campaign strongly links a term to a company, public association may increase sharply.","zh":"如果推廣活動強烈把某詞與公司連接，公眾聯想可能大幅增加。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a numerical comparison of likelihood.","zh":"這個片語用數字比較可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"associate the term with","meaning":"將某個詞與……聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"Many people associate the term “e-business” with IBM.","zh":"許多人將 “e-business” 這個詞與 IBM 聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To associate the term with something means to connect a word or idea with it in the mind.","zh":"To associate the term with something 指在腦海中把某詞或概念與某事連接。"},{"en":"Students often associate the term “revision” with exams and stress.","zh":"學生常把 “revision” 這個詞與考試和壓力聯繫起來。"},{"en":"If customers associate a term with one company, that company gains brand strength.","zh":"如果顧客把某詞與一間公司聯繫起來，該公司就得到品牌力量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental connection between a word and an organisation or idea.","zh":"這個片語描述詞語與組織或想法之間的心理連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"nearest competitor","meaning":"最接近的競爭對手","examples":[{"en":"People associate e-business with IBM more than with its nearest competitor.","zh":"人們把電子商務與 IBM 聯繫起來，多於與其最接近的競爭對手聯繫起來。"},{"en":"A nearest competitor is the rival most similar or closest in market position.","zh":"Nearest competitor 是市場定位最相似或最接近的競爭者。"},{"en":"A café’s nearest competitor may be another café on the same street with similar prices.","zh":"咖啡店最接近的競爭對手可能是同一條街上價格相近的另一間咖啡店。"},{"en":"If a brand is remembered more than its nearest competitor, its campaign has worked well.","zh":"如果品牌比最接近的競爭對手更容易被記住，其推廣活動就做得好。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a company with its closest rival.","zh":"這個片語把公司與最接近的對手比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take employees into account","meaning":"考慮員工因素","examples":[{"en":"A company should take employees into account when creating a brand message.","zh":"公司在創造品牌訊息時應考慮員工因素。"},{"en":"To take employees into account means to consider their views, feelings, and role.","zh":"To take employees into account 指考慮員工的看法、感受和角色。"},{"en":"A school should take teachers into account before changing the timetable.","zh":"學校改變時間表前應考慮老師因素。"},{"en":"If employees are not considered, they may reject a campaign designed for customers.","zh":"如果員工沒有被考慮，他們可能拒絕一個為顧客設計的推廣活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes including staff in planning.","zh":"這個片語描述在規劃中包括員工。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"avoid creating","meaning":"避免創造；避免製造","examples":[{"en":"Companies should avoid creating messages that alienate staff.","zh":"公司應避免創造令員工疏離的訊息。"},{"en":"To avoid creating something means to prevent oneself from making it happen.","zh":"To avoid creating something 指防止自己造成某事。"},{"en":"A teacher should avoid creating confusion by giving clear instructions.","zh":"老師應透過清晰指示避免製造混亂。"},{"en":"If a slogan insults employees, it may create resistance rather than support.","zh":"如果口號侮辱員工，它可能製造抗拒而不是支持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preventing a harmful result before it appears.","zh":"這個片語描述在有害結果出現前加以防止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"resonate with staff","meaning":"引起員工共鳴","examples":[{"en":"A brand message should resonate with staff.","zh":"品牌訊息應引起員工共鳴。"},{"en":"To resonate with staff means to feel meaningful, believable, or emotionally relevant to employees.","zh":"To resonate with staff 指對員工而言有意義、可信或情感相關。"},{"en":"A school motto resonates with teachers if it reflects what they actually do every day.","zh":"如果校訓反映老師每天真正做的事，它就會引起老師共鳴。"},{"en":"If a message resonates, staff are more likely to repeat it sincerely.","zh":"如果訊息引起共鳴，員工較可能真誠地重複它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a message that connects emotionally.","zh":"這個片語描述能建立情感連接的訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"build resentment","meaning":"引起怨氣；造成不滿","examples":[{"en":"A poorly chosen message may build resentment among employees.","zh":"選擇不當的訊息可能在員工之間造成不滿。"},{"en":"To build resentment means to create or increase hidden anger over time.","zh":"To build resentment 指隨時間製造或增加隱藏憤怒。"},{"en":"A school rule may build resentment if students feel it is unfairly enforced.","zh":"如果學生覺得校規被不公平執行，該規則可能引起怨氣。"},{"en":"If a campaign blames staff for industry problems, employee anger may grow.","zh":"如果推廣活動把行業問題歸咎於員工，員工怒氣可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow growth of bitterness.","zh":"這個片語描述苦澀不滿慢慢增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"shelve a slogan","meaning":"擱置口號","examples":[{"en":"United Airlines shelved its famous slogan.","zh":"United Airlines 擱置了其著名口號。"},{"en":"To shelve a slogan means to stop using it, usually because it no longer works.","zh":"To shelve a slogan 指停止使用某口號，通常因它不再有效。"},{"en":"A school may shelve a slogan if students and teachers find it empty.","zh":"如果學生和老師覺得口號空洞，學校可能擱置該口號。"},{"en":"If a slogan creates resentment, the company may remove it from advertising.","zh":"如果口號引起怨氣，公司可能把它從廣告中移除。"},{"en":"This phrase describes putting aside a public message.","zh":"這個片語描述把公開訊息擱置不用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be presented with","meaning":"獲提供；看到","examples":[{"en":"United Airlines was presented with a survey about customer resentment.","zh":"United Airlines 看到一項關於顧客不滿的調查。"},{"en":"To be presented with something means to be given or shown it formally.","zh":"To be presented with something 指被正式給予或展示某物。"},{"en":"A teacher may be presented with exam data showing students need more reading practice.","zh":"老師可能看到顯示學生需要更多閱讀練習的考試數據。"},{"en":"If leaders are presented with strong evidence, they should respond carefully.","zh":"如果領袖獲提供有力證據，他們應謹慎回應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving information for consideration.","zh":"這個片語描述收到資訊以供考慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"reveal the depth of","meaning":"揭示……的嚴重程度","examples":[{"en":"The survey revealed the depth of customer resentment.","zh":"調查揭示了顧客不滿的嚴重程度。"},{"en":"To reveal the depth of something means to show how serious or strong it really is.","zh":"To reveal the depth of something 指顯示某事真正有多嚴重或強烈。"},{"en":"A student survey may reveal the depth of exam anxiety in a school.","zh":"學生調查可能揭示學校中考試焦慮的嚴重程度。"},{"en":"If data reveal deep dissatisfaction, leaders can no longer ignore the problem.","zh":"如果數據揭示深層不滿，領袖就不能再忽視問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a hidden problem is more serious than expected.","zh":"這個片語顯示隱藏問題比預期更嚴重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"customer resentment toward","meaning":"顧客對……的不滿","examples":[{"en":"The survey revealed customer resentment toward the airline industry.","zh":"調查揭示顧客對航空業的不滿。"},{"en":"Customer resentment toward something is anger or bitterness customers feel about it.","zh":"Customer resentment toward something 是顧客對某事感到的憤怒或怨氣。"},{"en":"Customers may develop resentment toward a company after repeated hidden charges.","zh":"顧客在反覆遇到隱藏收費後，可能對公司產生不滿。"},{"en":"If resentment is strong, a polite advertisement may not be enough to rebuild trust.","zh":"如果不滿強烈，禮貌廣告未必足以重建信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes negative customer feeling directed at a business or industry.","zh":"這個片語描述顧客針對企業或行業的負面感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in an effort to","meaning":"為了……","examples":[{"en":"United changed its campaign in an effort to acknowledge industry problems.","zh":"United 改變推廣活動，為了承認行業問題。"},{"en":"In an effort to means in order to try to do something.","zh":"In an effort to 指為了嘗試做某事。"},{"en":"A school may reduce homework in an effort to improve students’ sleep.","zh":"學校可能減少功課，為了改善學生睡眠。"},{"en":"If a company admits problems in an effort to seem honest, employees must support the message.","zh":"如果公司為了顯得誠實而承認問題，員工必須支持該訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the purpose behind an action.","zh":"這個片語引出行動背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"own up to","meaning":"承認；坦承","examples":[{"en":"United tried to own up to the industry’s shortcomings.","zh":"United 嘗試坦承行業不足之處。"},{"en":"To own up to something means to admit it honestly, especially a mistake or weakness.","zh":"To own up to something 指誠實承認某事，尤其是錯誤或弱點。"},{"en":"A student should own up to copying homework instead of blaming a friend.","zh":"學生應承認抄功課，而不是怪朋友。"},{"en":"If a company owns up to poor service, it must also show how it will improve.","zh":"如果公司承認服務欠佳，它也必須顯示會如何改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes honest admission of fault.","zh":"這個片語描述誠實承認過失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"industry shortcomings","meaning":"行業不足之處","examples":[{"en":"The campaign acknowledged the airline industry’s shortcomings.","zh":"這項推廣活動承認航空業的不足之處。"},{"en":"Industry shortcomings are weaknesses or problems common in a whole industry.","zh":"Industry shortcomings 是整個行業普遍存在的弱點或問題。"},{"en":"Long waiting times may be a shortcoming of public healthcare systems.","zh":"輪候時間長可能是公共醫療系統的不足之處。"},{"en":"If an industry shortcoming affects customers badly, one company may try to stand apart.","zh":"如果行業不足嚴重影響顧客，一間公司可能嘗試與眾不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shared weaknesses beyond one company.","zh":"這個片語描述超越單一公司的共同弱點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"seek to differentiate itself","meaning":"試圖令自己與眾不同","examples":[{"en":"United sought to differentiate itself by admitting poor service.","zh":"United 試圖透過承認服務欠佳來令自己與眾不同。"},{"en":"To seek to differentiate itself means to try to show how it is different from competitors.","zh":"To seek to differentiate itself 指嘗試顯示自己與競爭對手有何不同。"},{"en":"A small café may differentiate itself by using local ingredients and personal service.","zh":"小咖啡店可能透過使用本地食材和個人化服務來令自己與眾不同。"},{"en":"If all companies sound the same, differentiation becomes harder.","zh":"如果所有公司聽起來都一樣，差異化就變得更難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trying to stand out in a market.","zh":"這個片語描述在市場中嘗試突圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"acknowledge poor service","meaning":"承認服務欠佳","examples":[{"en":"The campaign acknowledged poor service in the airline industry.","zh":"這項推廣活動承認航空業服務欠佳。"},{"en":"To acknowledge poor service means to admit that customers have not been treated well enough.","zh":"To acknowledge poor service 指承認顧客沒有得到足夠好的對待。"},{"en":"A restaurant may acknowledge poor service by apologising and retraining staff.","zh":"餐廳可能透過道歉和重新培訓員工來承認服務欠佳。"},{"en":"If a company admits poor service but changes nothing, customers may become angrier.","zh":"如果公司承認服務欠佳卻沒有改變，顧客可能更憤怒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognising a service problem openly.","zh":"這個片語描述公開承認服務問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"incremental improvements","meaning":"漸進式改善","examples":[{"en":"United promised incremental improvements such as better meals.","zh":"United 承諾漸進式改善，例如更好的餐膳。"},{"en":"Incremental improvements are small, gradual improvements made step by step.","zh":"Incremental improvements 是一步一步作出的細小、逐步改善。"},{"en":"A student can improve writing through incremental improvements in grammar, planning, and vocabulary.","zh":"學生可以透過文法、規劃和詞彙上的漸進式改善來提升寫作。"},{"en":"If small improvements continue, the final result may become meaningful over time.","zh":"如果小改善持續，最終結果可能隨時間變得有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes progress by small stages rather than sudden transformation.","zh":"這個片語描述分階段進步，而不是突然轉化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a logical premise","meaning":"合理的前提","examples":[{"en":"The campaign had a logical premise at the time.","zh":"這項推廣活動在當時有一個合理的前提。"},{"en":"A logical premise is a reasonable starting idea on which an argument or plan is based.","zh":"Logical premise 是論點或計劃所建基的合理起點。"},{"en":"A school’s reading plan may begin from the logical premise that practice improves fluency.","zh":"學校閱讀計劃可能建基於練習能提升流暢度這個合理前提。"},{"en":"If the premise ignores employees, even a logical campaign may fail.","zh":"如果前提忽略員工，即使合邏輯的推廣活動也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the reasoning foundation of an idea.","zh":"這個片語描述想法的推理基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"given the tenor of the times","meaning":"考慮到當時的氣氛","examples":[{"en":"The campaign seemed logical given the tenor of the times.","zh":"考慮到當時的氣氛，這項推廣活動似乎合乎邏輯。"},{"en":"Given the tenor of the times means considering the general mood or attitude of that period.","zh":"Given the tenor of the times 指考慮到某時期的一般氣氛或態度。"},{"en":"Given the tenor of the times, a school may focus more on mental health after a difficult year.","zh":"考慮到當時的氣氛，學校在艱難一年後可能更重視心理健康。"},{"en":"If customers strongly dislike flying, an honest campaign may seem sensible at that moment.","zh":"如果顧客非常反感飛行，誠實的推廣活動在當時可能顯得合理。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why an idea made sense in its historical context.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何某想法在其歷史背景中合理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"customers’ distaste for","meaning":"顧客對……的反感","examples":[{"en":"The campaign focused on customers’ distaste for flying.","zh":"這項推廣活動聚焦於顧客對飛行的反感。"},{"en":"Customers’ distaste for something means customers’ dislike or negative feeling toward it.","zh":"Customers’ distaste for something 指顧客對某事的不喜歡或負面感覺。"},{"en":"A restaurant must notice customers’ distaste for long waiting times.","zh":"餐廳必須留意顧客對長時間等候的反感。"},{"en":"If a campaign mentions customers’ dislikes too strongly, staff may feel insulted.","zh":"如果推廣活動過度強調顧客不滿，員工可能感到被侮辱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a negative customer attitude.","zh":"這個片語描述顧客的負面態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"deeply discouraging to","meaning":"令……深感沮喪","examples":[{"en":"The campaign was deeply discouraging to the staff.","zh":"這項推廣活動令員工深感沮喪。"},{"en":"Deeply discouraging to someone means making them feel very disappointed or demotivated.","zh":"Deeply discouraging to someone 指令某人非常失望或失去動力。"},{"en":"Harsh comments can be deeply discouraging to a student who has tried hard.","zh":"對努力過的學生而言，嚴厲評語可以令人深感沮喪。"},{"en":"If a campaign suggests staff are part of the problem, morale may collapse.","zh":"如果推廣活動暗示員工是問題一部分，士氣可能崩潰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong negative effect on motivation.","zh":"這個片語描述對動機的強烈負面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"employee resentment","meaning":"員工怨氣","examples":[{"en":"Employee resentment made the campaign difficult to deliver.","zh":"員工怨氣令推廣活動難以實現。"},{"en":"Employee resentment is anger or bitterness felt by staff, often because they feel unfairly treated.","zh":"Employee resentment 是員工感到的憤怒或怨氣，通常因覺得受到不公平對待。"},{"en":"A sudden pay cut can create employee resentment if managers do not explain it clearly.","zh":"如果管理者沒有清楚解釋，突然減薪可以造成員工怨氣。"},{"en":"If resentment grows, employees may stop supporting company promises.","zh":"如果怨氣增加，員工可能停止支持公司承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hidden or open staff anger.","zh":"這個片語描述隱藏或公開的員工怒氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make it impossible for someone to","meaning":"令某人無法……","examples":[{"en":"Employee resentment made it impossible for United to deliver improvements.","zh":"員工怨氣令 United 無法實現改善。"},{"en":"To make it impossible for someone to do something means to prevent them from being able to do it.","zh":"To make it impossible for someone to do something 指阻止某人能夠做某事。"},{"en":"Poor internet can make it impossible for students to join an online lesson.","zh":"網絡差可以令學生無法參加網上課堂。"},{"en":"If employees refuse to support a campaign, the company cannot fulfil its promise.","zh":"如果員工拒絕支持推廣活動，公司就不能履行承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a condition that blocks success completely.","zh":"這個片語描述完全阻礙成功的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"deliver the improvements","meaning":"實現改善","examples":[{"en":"United could not deliver the improvements it was promising.","zh":"United 無法實現它所承諾的改善。"},{"en":"To deliver the improvements means to actually provide the better conditions or service promised.","zh":"To deliver the improvements 指真正提供所承諾的更好條件或服務。"},{"en":"A school must deliver promised improvements if it says classes will become smaller.","zh":"如果學校說班級會變小，它就必須實現承諾的改善。"},{"en":"If employees do not cooperate, promised service improvements may not happen.","zh":"如果員工不合作，承諾的服務改善可能不會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase connects promises with real delivery.","zh":"這個片語把承諾與實際交付連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"undermine the pledge","meaning":"削弱承諾","examples":[{"en":"Employee resentment undermined the “Rising” pledge.","zh":"員工怨氣削弱了 “Rising” 這個承諾。"},{"en":"To undermine the pledge means to weaken a promise so it no longer seems believable.","zh":"To undermine the pledge 指削弱某項承諾，使它不再顯得可信。"},{"en":"A school’s promise of fairness is undermined if rules are applied differently to rich and poor students.","zh":"如果校規對貧富學生執行不同，學校公平承諾就會被削弱。"},{"en":"If staff do not support a pledge, customers may not experience it.","zh":"如果員工不支持承諾，顧客可能體驗不到它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damaging the credibility of a promise.","zh":"這個片語描述破壞承諾的可信性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"employee opposition","meaning":"員工反對","examples":[{"en":"United decided that employee opposition was undermining its success.","zh":"United 認為員工反對正在削弱其成功。"},{"en":"Employee opposition is resistance or disagreement from staff.","zh":"Employee opposition 是來自員工的抗拒或不同意。"},{"en":"A new timetable may face employee opposition if teachers were not consulted.","zh":"如果老師沒有被諮詢，新時間表可能面對員工反對。"},{"en":"If opposition becomes strong, a campaign may have to be changed or withdrawn.","zh":"如果反對變得強烈，推廣活動可能必須改變或撤回。"},{"en":"This phrase describes staff pushing back against a decision.","zh":"這個片語描述員工對決定作出反抗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"pull the campaign","meaning":"撤回推廣活動","examples":[{"en":"United pulled the campaign after employee opposition weakened it.","zh":"United 在員工反對削弱推廣活動後撤回了它。"},{"en":"To pull the campaign means to stop or withdraw it from use.","zh":"To pull the campaign 指停止或撤回使用某推廣活動。"},{"en":"A company may pull an advertisement if customers find it offensive.","zh":"如果顧客覺得廣告冒犯，公司可能撤回廣告。"},{"en":"If a campaign damages staff morale, leaders may decide to remove it.","zh":"如果推廣活動損害員工士氣，領導層可能決定移除它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ending a campaign before continuing causes more harm.","zh":"這個片語描述在造成更多傷害前終止推廣活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"move to","meaning":"轉向；改用","examples":[{"en":"United moved to a more inclusive brand message.","zh":"United 轉向更具包容性的品牌訊息。"},{"en":"To move to something means to change from one approach to another.","zh":"To move to something 指從一種方法改為另一種。"},{"en":"A school may move to online notices instead of printed letters.","zh":"學校可能改用網上通告，而不是印刷信件。"},{"en":"If one message fails, a company may move to a more suitable one.","zh":"如果一個訊息失敗，公司可能轉向更合適的訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift in approach or position.","zh":"這個片語描述方法或立場上的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"inclusive brand message","meaning":"更具包容性的品牌訊息","examples":[{"en":"United later adopted a more inclusive brand message.","zh":"United 後來採用更具包容性的品牌訊息。"},{"en":"An inclusive brand message is a message that different audiences can accept and feel part of.","zh":"Inclusive brand message 是不同受眾都能接受並感到自己被包括的訊息。"},{"en":"A school motto is inclusive if students, parents, and teachers can all believe in it.","zh":"如果學生、家長和老師都能相信校訓，它就是具包容性的。"},{"en":"If a brand message includes employees as well as customers, it may gain stronger support.","zh":"如果品牌訊息包括員工和顧客，它可能獲得更強支持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a message that does not alienate important groups.","zh":"這個片語描述不會令重要群體疏離的訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"both audiences can embrace","meaning":"兩類受眾都能接受","examples":[{"en":"The new message was one that both audiences could embrace.","zh":"新訊息是兩類受眾都能接受的訊息。"},{"en":"Both audiences can embrace means two groups can both accept and support the message.","zh":"Both audiences can embrace 指兩個群體都能接受並支持該訊息。"},{"en":"A school policy works better when both teachers and parents can embrace it.","zh":"當老師和家長都能接受一項校政時，它會更有效。"},{"en":"If customers like a promise but employees hate it, both audiences cannot embrace it.","zh":"如果顧客喜歡某承諾但員工討厭它，兩類受眾就不能都接受。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses shared acceptance across groups.","zh":"這個片語強調跨群體的共同接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a fundamental principle of","meaning":"……的基本原則","examples":[{"en":"The campaign followed a fundamental principle of advertising.","zh":"這項推廣活動遵循廣告的一項基本原則。"},{"en":"A fundamental principle of something is a basic rule or idea that guides it.","zh":"Fundamental principle of something 是指引某領域的基本規則或理念。"},{"en":"A fundamental principle of teaching is that students need to understand before they memorise.","zh":"教學的一項基本原則是學生需要先理解，然後才記憶。"},{"en":"If a campaign ignores a basic principle, it may fail even with a large budget.","zh":"如果推廣活動忽略基本原則，即使預算很大也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase names an important foundation of a field.","zh":"這個片語命名某領域的重要基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"find and address","meaning":"找出並處理","examples":[{"en":"Advertisers often try to find and address a customer concern.","zh":"廣告人經常嘗試找出並處理顧客關注的問題。"},{"en":"To find and address a problem means to identify it and then deal with it.","zh":"To find and address a problem 指識別問題，然後處理它。"},{"en":"A teacher should find and address the reason students keep making the same grammar mistake.","zh":"老師應找出並處理學生不斷犯同一文法錯誤的原因。"},{"en":"If a company finds a customer concern but does not address it, trust will not improve.","zh":"如果公司找出顧客關注卻不處理，信任不會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase combines diagnosis with action.","zh":"這個片語把診斷與行動結合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"customer concern","meaning":"顧客關注的問題","examples":[{"en":"United tried to address a customer concern about flying.","zh":"United 嘗試處理顧客對飛行的關注問題。"},{"en":"A customer concern is a worry, complaint, or need that customers have.","zh":"Customer concern 是顧客擁有的憂慮、投訴或需要。"},{"en":"Long delivery time is a common customer concern for online shops.","zh":"送貨時間長是網店常見的顧客關注問題。"},{"en":"If a company understands customer concerns, it can design better service.","zh":"如果公司理解顧客關注，就能設計更好服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what customers care or worry about.","zh":"這個片語描述顧客在乎或擔心的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"fail someone","meaning":"令某人失敗；對某人不奏效","examples":[{"en":"The advertising principle failed United because it ignored employees.","zh":"這項廣告原則對 United 不奏效，因為它忽略員工。"},{"en":"To fail someone means to not work for them or not give them the result they need.","zh":"To fail someone 指對某人不起作用，或不能給他需要的結果。"},{"en":"A study method may fail a student if it only teaches memorisation.","zh":"如果學習方法只教記憶，它可能對學生不奏效。"},{"en":"If a principle ignores a key group, it may fail the company using it.","zh":"如果一項原則忽略關鍵群體，它可能令使用它的公司失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something being ineffective for a particular person or organisation.","zh":"這個片語描述某事對特定人士或組織無效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"consider the internal market","meaning":"考慮內部市場","examples":[{"en":"United’s campaign failed because it did not consider the internal market.","zh":"United 的推廣活動失敗，因為它沒有考慮內部市場。"},{"en":"To consider the internal market means to think about employees as an audience for the brand message.","zh":"To consider the internal market 指把員工視為品牌訊息的受眾來思考。"},{"en":"A school should consider teachers before announcing a new public promise.","zh":"學校在宣布新的公開承諾前，應先考慮老師。"},{"en":"If the internal market is ignored, staff may resist what customers are being promised.","zh":"如果內部市場被忽略，員工可能抗拒公司對顧客的承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes including employee response in marketing decisions.","zh":"這個片語描述在市場決策中包括員工反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"when it comes to","meaning":"談到……時","examples":[{"en":"When it comes to execution, companies need to link both campaigns.","zh":"談到執行時，公司需要連繫兩種推廣活動。"},{"en":"When it comes to something means when discussing or dealing with that particular area.","zh":"When it comes to something 指談論或處理某特定範疇時。"},{"en":"When it comes to exams, clear instructions are as important as knowledge.","zh":"談到考試時，清晰指示和知識同樣重要。"},{"en":"This phrase helps narrow the discussion to one aspect of a larger topic.","zh":"這個片語幫助把討論收窄到較大主題的一個方面。"},{"en":"It often introduces the practical part of an issue.","zh":"它常引出問題的實際部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"execution","meaning":"執行","examples":[{"en":"Execution is important when linking internal and external marketing.","zh":"連繫內外市場推廣時，執行很重要。"},{"en":"Execution means putting a plan into practical action.","zh":"Execution 指把計劃付諸實際行動。"},{"en":"A school event may have a good idea, but poor execution can make it chaotic.","zh":"學校活動可能理念很好，但執行差會令它混亂。"},{"en":"If execution is weak, even a clever strategy may fail.","zh":"如果執行薄弱，即使策略聰明也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This word focuses on how well something is carried out.","zh":"這個詞聚焦於某事實行得有多好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"link internal and external marketing campaigns","meaning":"連繫內外市場推廣活動","examples":[{"en":"Companies can link internal and external marketing campaigns through advertising.","zh":"公司可以透過廣告連繫內外市場推廣活動。"},{"en":"To link internal and external marketing campaigns means to connect messages for employees with messages for customers.","zh":"To link internal and external marketing campaigns 指把給員工的訊息和給顧客的訊息連接起來。"},{"en":"A school may link internal and external communication by training teachers before sending parent notices.","zh":"學校可能先培訓老師，再發家長通告，以連繫內外溝通。"},{"en":"If both campaigns support each other, employees can help deliver the public promise.","zh":"如果兩種推廣活動互相支持，員工可以幫助實現公開承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes coordination between inside and outside marketing.","zh":"這個片語描述內部與外部市場推廣之間的協調。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"external advertising","meaning":"對外廣告","examples":[{"en":"External advertising can also target employees.","zh":"對外廣告也可以針對員工。"},{"en":"External advertising is public advertising aimed at customers or people outside the company.","zh":"External advertising 是針對顧客或公司外人士的公開廣告。"},{"en":"A bus advertisement for a new school course is external advertising.","zh":"巴士上的新課程廣告就是對外廣告。"},{"en":"If employees see the same public message, external advertising can also build internal belief.","zh":"如果員工看見同一公開訊息，對外廣告也可以建立內部信念。"},{"en":"This phrase describes advertising visible beyond the organisation.","zh":"這個片語描述組織以外也可見的廣告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"target both audiences","meaning":"針對兩類受眾","examples":[{"en":"Some external advertising targets both customers and employees.","zh":"有些對外廣告同時針對顧客和員工兩類受眾。"},{"en":"To target both audiences means to design a message for two groups at the same time.","zh":"To target both audiences 指同時為兩個群體設計訊息。"},{"en":"A school notice may target both parents and students if both need to act.","zh":"如果家長和學生都需要行動，學校通告可能針對兩類受眾。"},{"en":"If both audiences understand the same message, consistency improves.","zh":"如果兩類受眾理解同一訊息，一致性會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes communication aimed at two important groups.","zh":"這個片語描述針對兩個重要群體的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"use this tactic effectively","meaning":"有效運用這種策略","examples":[{"en":"IBM used this tactic effectively in its e-business campaign.","zh":"IBM 在電子商務推廣活動中有效運用這種策略。"},{"en":"To use this tactic effectively means to apply this method successfully.","zh":"To use this tactic effectively 指成功應用這種方法。"},{"en":"A teacher uses questioning effectively when students begin thinking more deeply.","zh":"當學生開始更深入思考時，老師就是有效運用提問策略。"},{"en":"If a tactic supports both employees and customers, it can have a stronger impact.","zh":"如果策略同時支持員工和顧客，它可以有更強影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes successful use of a chosen method.","zh":"這個片語描述成功使用某種方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take out an ad","meaning":"刊登廣告","examples":[{"en":"IBM took out an eight-page ad in the Wall Street Journal.","zh":"IBM 在《華爾街日報》刊登了一則八頁廣告。"},{"en":"To take out an ad means to pay for and place an advertisement in a publication or media channel.","zh":"To take out an ad 指付費在刊物或媒體渠道刊登廣告。"},{"en":"A tutoring centre may take out an ad in a local magazine before exam season.","zh":"補習中心可能在考試季前於本地雜誌刊登廣告。"},{"en":"If a company takes out a large advertisement, it signals seriousness and visibility.","zh":"如果公司刊登大型廣告，它會顯示認真和可見度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes buying advertising space.","zh":"這個片語描述購買廣告空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"eight-page ad","meaning":"八頁廣告","examples":[{"en":"IBM used an eight-page ad to declare its new vision.","zh":"IBM 使用八頁廣告來宣布其新願景。"},{"en":"An eight-page ad is a large advertisement spread across eight pages.","zh":"Eight-page ad 是橫跨八頁的大型廣告。"},{"en":"A company would use such a large ad only when it wants strong public attention.","zh":"公司只有在想引起強烈公眾注意時，才會使用如此大型廣告。"},{"en":"If an advertisement is unusually long, it may signal a major change or announcement.","zh":"如果廣告異常長，它可能顯示重大改變或宣布。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the size and seriousness of the advertisement.","zh":"這個片語描述廣告的規模和嚴肅性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"declare a new vision","meaning":"宣布新願景","examples":[{"en":"The advertisement declared IBM’s new vision.","zh":"這則廣告宣布了 IBM 的新願景。"},{"en":"To declare a new vision means to publicly announce a new future direction or goal.","zh":"To declare a new vision 指公開宣布新的未來方向或目標。"},{"en":"A school may declare a new vision focused on creativity and student well-being.","zh":"學校可能宣布以創意和學生福祉為中心的新願景。"},{"en":"If a vision is declared publicly, employees may feel pressure to live up to it.","zh":"如果願景被公開宣布，員工可能感到壓力去達成它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a formal announcement of future identity.","zh":"這個片語描述對未來身份的正式宣布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be directed at","meaning":"針對……","examples":[{"en":"The message was directed at both customers and internal stakeholders.","zh":"該訊息針對顧客和內部持份者。"},{"en":"To be directed at someone means to be aimed at that person or group.","zh":"To be directed at someone 指針對某人或某群體。"},{"en":"A notice about homework is directed at students, while a fee notice is directed at parents.","zh":"關於功課的通告針對學生，而收費通告針對家長。"},{"en":"If a campaign is directed at employees too, they should understand their role in it.","zh":"如果推廣活動也針對員工，他們應理解自己在其中的角色。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the intended audience.","zh":"這個片語指出預期受眾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"internal stakeholders","meaning":"內部持份者","examples":[{"en":"The advertisement was also directed at internal stakeholders.","zh":"這則廣告也針對內部持份者。"},{"en":"Internal stakeholders are people inside an organisation who are affected by its decisions.","zh":"Internal stakeholders 是組織內受其決定影響的人。"},{"en":"Teachers, clerks, and school leaders are internal stakeholders in a school policy change.","zh":"老師、文員和學校領導層都是校政改變中的內部持份者。"},{"en":"If internal stakeholders are ignored, implementation may become difficult.","zh":"如果內部持份者被忽略，實施可能變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes important people inside the organisation.","zh":"這個片語描述組織內的重要人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"capture attention","meaning":"吸引注意","examples":[{"en":"The expensive advertisement helped capture attention.","zh":"這則昂貴廣告幫助吸引注意。"},{"en":"To capture attention means to make people notice and focus on something.","zh":"To capture attention 指令人注意並集中於某事。"},{"en":"A strong opening story can capture students’ attention in a lesson.","zh":"強而有力的開場故事可以在課堂中吸引學生注意。"},{"en":"If a company wants change to feel important, a visible message can capture attention quickly.","zh":"如果公司想令變革感覺重要，可見訊息可以迅速吸引注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes drawing people’s focus.","zh":"這個片語描述吸引人們焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"used sparingly","meaning":"謹慎地少量使用","examples":[{"en":"This tactic is powerful if it is used sparingly.","zh":"如果這種策略謹慎地少量使用，它會很有力量。"},{"en":"Used sparingly means used only occasionally and not too much.","zh":"Used sparingly 指只偶爾使用，而不是過度使用。"},{"en":"A teacher may use dramatic music sparingly so it remains effective.","zh":"老師可能謹慎少量使用戲劇性音樂，讓它保持效果。"},{"en":"If a company makes huge announcements too often, people may stop paying attention.","zh":"如果公司太常作重大宣布，人們可能不再留意。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that overuse can reduce impact.","zh":"這個片語提醒過度使用會減低影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"powerful form of communication","meaning":"強而有力的溝通方式","examples":[{"en":"External advertising can be a powerful form of communication.","zh":"對外廣告可以是一種強而有力的溝通方式。"},{"en":"A powerful form of communication is a method that strongly delivers a message.","zh":"Powerful form of communication 是能強烈傳達訊息的方法。"},{"en":"A personal story can be a powerful form of communication in a health campaign.","zh":"個人故事可以成為健康宣傳中強而有力的溝通方式。"},{"en":"If advertising reaches both staff and customers, it may influence behaviour on both sides.","zh":"如果廣告同時接觸員工和顧客，它可能影響雙方行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes communication with strong effect.","zh":"這個片語描述有強大效果的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"symbolic advantage","meaning":"象徵性的優勢","examples":[{"en":"Advertising to both audiences has a symbolic advantage.","zh":"向兩類受眾做廣告有象徵性的優勢。"},{"en":"A symbolic advantage is a benefit created by what an action represents, not only what it directly does.","zh":"Symbolic advantage 是由行動所代表的意義創造的好處，而不只是直接作用。"},{"en":"A principal visiting classrooms has symbolic advantage because it shows learning matters.","zh":"校長走訪課室有象徵性優勢，因為它顯示學習重要。"},{"en":"If the same message is public and internal, it symbolises openness and seriousness.","zh":"如果同一訊息同時公開和內部傳達，它象徵開放和認真。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the meaning behind an action.","zh":"這個片語描述行動背後的意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"signal that","meaning":"顯示；傳遞出……","examples":[{"en":"The tactic signals that the company takes its pledge seriously.","zh":"這種策略顯示公司認真看待其承諾。"},{"en":"To signal that means to show or communicate something indirectly or clearly.","zh":"To signal that 指間接或清楚顯示或傳達某事。"},{"en":"A teacher arriving early signals that the lesson matters.","zh":"老師早到顯示這堂課很重要。"},{"en":"If leaders invest money in a public promise, they signal seriousness.","zh":"如果領袖為公開承諾投入金錢，他們就是傳遞出認真態度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sending a message through action.","zh":"這個片語描述透過行動傳達訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"take its pledge seriously","meaning":"認真看待其承諾","examples":[{"en":"The advertisement showed that IBM was taking its pledge seriously.","zh":"這則廣告顯示 IBM 正認真看待其承諾。"},{"en":"To take its pledge seriously means to treat a promise as real and important.","zh":"To take its pledge seriously 指把承諾視為真實且重要。"},{"en":"A school takes its safety pledge seriously when it repairs dangerous stairs quickly.","zh":"當學校迅速維修危險樓梯，就是認真看待其安全承諾。"},{"en":"If a company makes a promise but invests nothing, people may doubt its seriousness.","zh":"如果公司作出承諾卻毫無投入，人們可能懷疑其認真程度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes honouring a commitment through action.","zh":"這個片語描述透過行動履行承諾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"signal transparency","meaning":"顯示透明度","examples":[{"en":"The same message to both audiences signals transparency.","zh":"向兩類受眾傳達同一訊息顯示透明度。"},{"en":"To signal transparency means to show openness and honesty.","zh":"To signal transparency 指顯示開放和誠實。"},{"en":"A school signals transparency when it shares exam policies with both teachers and parents.","zh":"當學校向老師和家長都分享考試政策，就是顯示透明度。"},{"en":"If employees and customers hear the same promise, the company appears more open.","zh":"如果員工和顧客聽到同一承諾，公司就顯得更開放。"},{"en":"This phrase describes communication that builds trust through openness.","zh":"這個片語描述透過開放建立信任的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the same message going out to","meaning":"同一訊息傳達給……","examples":[{"en":"Transparency comes from the same message going out to both audiences.","zh":"透明度來自同一訊息傳達給兩類受眾。"},{"en":"The same message going out to people means identical information being communicated to them.","zh":"The same message going out to people 指相同資訊被傳達給他們。"},{"en":"A school avoids confusion by sending the same message to students and parents about exam rules.","zh":"學校向學生和家長傳達同一考試規則訊息，可以避免混亂。"},{"en":"If different audiences receive the same message, trust and consistency increase.","zh":"如果不同受眾收到同一訊息，信任和一致性會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses uniform communication.","zh":"這個片語強調統一溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"senior executives","meaning":"高級行政人員","examples":[{"en":"Senior executives at Nike also act as Corporate Storytellers.","zh":"Nike 的高級行政人員也擔任企業故事講述者。"},{"en":"Senior executives are high-ranking leaders in a company.","zh":"Senior executives 是公司的高級領導人。"},{"en":"A senior executive may decide company strategy, budgets, and major partnerships.","zh":"高級行政人員可能決定公司策略、預算和主要合作。"},{"en":"If senior executives tell company stories, employees may see culture as important.","zh":"如果高級行政人員講述公司故事，員工可能視文化為重要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to top-level decision-makers.","zh":"這個片語指高層決策者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"hold the additional title of","meaning":"兼任……的職銜","examples":[{"en":"Some Nike executives hold the additional title of Corporate Storyteller.","zh":"一些 Nike 行政人員兼任企業故事講述者的職銜。"},{"en":"To hold the additional title of something means to have another official role name besides one’s main title.","zh":"To hold the additional title of something 指除了主要職銜外，還有另一個正式角色名稱。"},{"en":"A teacher may hold the additional title of student mentor.","zh":"老師可能兼任學生導師的職銜。"},{"en":"If a leader has an extra title, it signals that the role is formally recognised.","zh":"如果領袖有額外職銜，這顯示該角色被正式認可。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an extra named responsibility.","zh":"這個片語描述額外命名的責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Corporate Storyteller","meaning":"企業故事講述者","examples":[{"en":"Nike uses Corporate Storytellers to reinforce its company spirit.","zh":"Nike 使用企業故事講述者來強化公司精神。"},{"en":"A Corporate Storyteller is a person who tells company stories to pass on values and identity.","zh":"Corporate Storyteller 是講述公司故事以傳遞價值和身份的人。"},{"en":"A school storyteller might share stories of former students to teach younger students resilience.","zh":"學校故事講述者可能分享舊生故事，以教年輕學生堅毅。"},{"en":"If company stories are repeated well, employees may remember the culture more deeply.","zh":"如果公司故事被好好重複，員工可能更深入記住文化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes storytelling as a formal business role.","zh":"這個片語描述把講故事視為正式商業角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"deliberately avoid","meaning":"刻意避免","examples":[{"en":"Nike’s storytellers deliberately avoid stories of financial success.","zh":"Nike 的故事講述者刻意避免財務成功的故事。"},{"en":"To deliberately avoid something means to choose not to do or mention it on purpose.","zh":"To deliberately avoid something 指有意選擇不做或不提某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may deliberately avoid difficult vocabulary when explaining a new idea to beginners.","zh":"老師向初學者解釋新概念時，可能刻意避免困難詞彙。"},{"en":"If storytellers avoid financial success stories, they may keep attention on values instead of money.","zh":"如果故事講述者避免財務成功故事，他們可能把焦點放在價值而不是金錢上。"},{"en":"This phrase shows intentional choice, not accident.","zh":"這個片語顯示有意識的選擇，而非意外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"financial successes","meaning":"財務上的成功","examples":[{"en":"The storytellers avoid stories of financial successes.","zh":"故事講述者避免講述財務上的成功。"},{"en":"Financial successes are achievements measured by money, profit, sales, or business growth.","zh":"Financial successes 是以金錢、利潤、銷售或業務增長量度的成就。"},{"en":"A company may celebrate financial success after a profitable year.","zh":"公司在盈利年度後可能慶祝財務成功。"},{"en":"If culture stories focus only on money, employees may miss deeper values.","zh":"如果文化故事只聚焦金錢，員工可能錯過更深層價值。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to business success in financial terms.","zh":"這個片語指財務層面的商業成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"concentrate on","meaning":"集中於……","examples":[{"en":"They concentrate on parables of just doing it.","zh":"他們集中於關於「Just Do It」精神的寓言式故事。"},{"en":"To concentrate on something means to give main attention to it.","zh":"To concentrate on something 指把主要注意力放在某事上。"},{"en":"A student may concentrate on grammar before improving style.","zh":"學生可能先集中於文法，再改善風格。"},{"en":"If stories concentrate on innovation, employees learn what the company values most.","zh":"如果故事集中於創新，員工會學到公司最重視甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes focusing attention on one main area.","zh":"這個片語描述把注意力集中在一個主要範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"parables of","meaning":"關於……的寓言式故事","examples":[{"en":"Nike uses parables of innovation to teach company values.","zh":"Nike 使用關於創新的寓言式故事來教授公司價值。"},{"en":"Parables of something are simple stories that teach a lesson about that idea.","zh":"Parables of something 是教授某理念教訓的簡單故事。"},{"en":"A teacher may tell parables of honesty to help children understand trust.","zh":"老師可能講述關於誠實的寓言式故事，幫助孩子理解信任。"},{"en":"If a company uses parables, values become easier to remember than abstract rules.","zh":"如果公司使用寓言式故事，價值會比抽象規則更容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lesson-carrying stories.","zh":"這個片語描述承載教訓的故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reflecting and reinforcing","meaning":"反映並強化","examples":[{"en":"The stories reflect and reinforce Nike’s advertising campaigns.","zh":"這些故事反映並強化 Nike 的廣告活動。"},{"en":"Reflecting and reinforcing means showing the same idea and making it stronger.","zh":"Reflecting and reinforcing 指展示同一理念並令它更強。"},{"en":"A school’s assemblies can reflect and reinforce the values taught in class.","zh":"學校早會可以反映並強化課堂所教的價值。"},{"en":"If internal stories reinforce external ads, employees and customers hear a consistent message.","zh":"如果內部故事強化對外廣告，員工和顧客會聽到一致訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeating a message in a way that strengthens it.","zh":"這個片語描述以加強效果的方式重複訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"ad campaigns","meaning":"廣告活動","examples":[{"en":"The company stories reinforce Nike’s ad campaigns.","zh":"公司故事強化 Nike 的廣告活動。"},{"en":"Ad campaigns are organised sets of advertisements with a shared message.","zh":"Ad campaigns 是具有共同訊息的一系列有組織廣告。"},{"en":"A public health ad campaign may encourage people to wash hands during flu season.","zh":"公共健康廣告活動可能鼓勵人們在流感季節洗手。"},{"en":"If an ad campaign promises innovation, company stories should support that message.","zh":"如果廣告活動承諾創新，公司故事應支持該訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to planned advertising efforts.","zh":"這個片語指有計劃的廣告工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"one tale recalls how","meaning":"有一個故事講述","examples":[{"en":"One tale recalls how Bill Bowerman created a shoe prototype.","zh":"有一個故事講述 Bill Bowerman 如何創造鞋的原型。"},{"en":"One tale recalls how means one story remembers or retells the way something happened.","zh":"One tale recalls how 指有一個故事記述或重述某事如何發生。"},{"en":"One school tale recalls how a teacher helped a struggling student become a leader.","zh":"有一個學校故事講述一位老師如何幫助吃力的學生成為領袖。"},{"en":"If stories recall company origins, employees may feel connected to its values.","zh":"如果故事記述公司起源，員工可能感到與其價值有連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a memorable example from the past.","zh":"這個片語引出過去一個令人記得的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"legendary coach","meaning":"傳奇教練","examples":[{"en":"Bill Bowerman was a legendary coach and Nike co-founder.","zh":"Bill Bowerman 是一位傳奇教練，也是 Nike 聯合創辦人。"},{"en":"A legendary coach is a coach remembered as highly respected, influential, or almost mythical.","zh":"Legendary coach 是被記住為極受尊重、有影響力或近乎神話般的教練。"},{"en":"A legendary school coach may be remembered for shaping students’ character, not only winning games.","zh":"傳奇學校教練可能因塑造學生品格而被記住，而不只是贏比賽。"},{"en":"If a company connects itself to a legendary figure, its story gains emotional power.","zh":"如果公司把自己與傳奇人物連接，故事會獲得情感力量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone whose reputation has become famous over time.","zh":"這個片語描述聲譽隨時間變得著名的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"Nike co-founder","meaning":"Nike 聯合創辦人","examples":[{"en":"Bill Bowerman was a Nike co-founder.","zh":"Bill Bowerman 是 Nike 聯合創辦人。"},{"en":"A co-founder is one of the people who starts an organisation or company.","zh":"Co-founder 是共同創立組織或公司的人之一。"},{"en":"A school club may have two co-founders who first planned its purpose and activities.","zh":"學校學會可能有兩位聯合創辦人，最初規劃其目的和活動。"},{"en":"If a co-founder’s story is repeated, employees may remember the company’s origins.","zh":"如果聯合創辦人的故事被重複，員工可能記住公司的起源。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies one of the original creators of Nike.","zh":"這個片語指出 Nike 的原始創建者之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"in an effort to build","meaning":"為了製造……","examples":[{"en":"Bowerman experimented in an effort to build a better shoe.","zh":"Bowerman 為了製造更好的鞋而進行實驗。"},{"en":"In an effort to build something means while trying to create or improve it.","zh":"In an effort to build something 指為了創造或改善某物而嘗試。"},{"en":"A teacher may test new activities in an effort to build students’ confidence.","zh":"老師可能測試新活動，為了建立學生信心。"},{"en":"If someone experiments to build something better, failure can become part of innovation.","zh":"如果有人為製造更好事物而實驗，失敗可以成為創新一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase shows purposeful trying toward creation.","zh":"這個片語顯示朝創造而來的有目的嘗試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"pour rubber into","meaning":"把橡膠倒進……","examples":[{"en":"Bowerman poured rubber into the family waffle iron.","zh":"Bowerman 把橡膠倒進家用窩夫機。"},{"en":"To pour rubber into something means to put liquid or softened rubber into a container or mould.","zh":"To pour rubber into something 指把液態或軟化橡膠倒進容器或模具。"},{"en":"A science teacher may pour wax into a mould to show how shapes are formed.","zh":"科學老師可能把蠟倒進模具，展示形狀如何形成。"},{"en":"If material is poured into an unusual tool, a surprising prototype may result.","zh":"如果材料被倒進不尋常工具，可能產生令人意外的原型。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical action used in making something.","zh":"這個片語描述製作某物時的實體動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"waffle iron","meaning":"窩夫機","examples":[{"en":"The prototype was created using a family waffle iron.","zh":"原型是用家用窩夫機創造出來的。"},{"en":"A waffle iron is a kitchen tool used to cook waffles in a patterned shape.","zh":"Waffle iron 是用來烹調帶有格紋形狀窩夫的廚房工具。"},{"en":"A family may use a waffle iron at breakfast to make crisp patterned waffles.","zh":"家庭可能在早餐時使用窩夫機製作香脆格紋窩夫。"},{"en":"If a sports-shoe sole is inspired by a waffle iron, the story becomes easy to remember.","zh":"如果運動鞋鞋底受窩夫機啟發，故事會容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase names an ordinary household tool used in an inventive way.","zh":"這個片語命名一件被創意使用的普通家庭工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"give birth to","meaning":"催生；孕育出","examples":[{"en":"The experiment gave birth to the prototype of Nike’s Waffle Sole.","zh":"這次實驗催生了 Nike Waffle Sole 的原型。"},{"en":"To give birth to something means to create or lead to the beginning of it.","zh":"To give birth to something 指創造或導致某事開始。"},{"en":"A small classroom idea can give birth to a school-wide reading programme.","zh":"一個小課堂想法可以孕育出全校閱讀計劃。"},{"en":"If an experiment succeeds, it may give birth to a new product.","zh":"如果實驗成功，它可能催生新產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the origin of something new.","zh":"這個片語描述新事物的起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"prototype","meaning":"原型","examples":[{"en":"The experiment produced the prototype of Nike’s famous Waffle Sole.","zh":"這次實驗產生了 Nike 著名 Waffle Sole 的原型。"},{"en":"A prototype is an early model used to test an idea before final production.","zh":"Prototype 是在最終生產前用來測試想法的早期模型。"},{"en":"Students may build a cardboard prototype before making a final design project.","zh":"學生可能先製作紙板原型，再完成最終設計項目。"},{"en":"If a prototype works, designers can improve it into a real product.","zh":"如果原型有效，設計師可以把它改善成真正產品。"},{"en":"This word describes a first version for testing.","zh":"這個詞描述用於測試的第一版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"Waffle Sole","meaning":"Waffle Sole 鞋底","examples":[{"en":"The prototype became Nike’s famous Waffle Sole.","zh":"該原型成為 Nike 著名的 Waffle Sole 鞋底。"},{"en":"Waffle Sole refers to a Nike shoe sole design inspired by the pattern of a waffle iron.","zh":"Waffle Sole 指受窩夫機格紋啟發的 Nike 鞋底設計。"},{"en":"A trainer’s sole can affect grip, comfort, and running performance.","zh":"運動鞋鞋底可以影響抓地力、舒適度和跑步表現。"},{"en":"If a product has a memorable origin story, employees may use it to explain company innovation.","zh":"如果產品有令人記得的起源故事，員工可能用它解釋公司創新。"},{"en":"This phrase names a product feature connected to Nike’s innovation story.","zh":"這個片語命名與 Nike 創新故事相關的產品特色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"inventive moves","meaning":"創新的舉動","examples":[{"en":"Nike talks about inventive moves to keep innovation alive.","zh":"Nike 談論創新的舉動，以保持創新精神。"},{"en":"Inventive moves are creative actions or decisions that lead to new solutions.","zh":"Inventive moves 是帶來新解決方案的創意行動或決定。"},{"en":"A teacher makes an inventive move when turning grammar practice into a game.","zh":"老師把文法練習變成遊戲，就是作出創新的舉動。"},{"en":"If a company encourages inventive moves, employees may feel safe to experiment.","zh":"如果公司鼓勵創新舉動，員工可能感到可以安全地實驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical creativity in action.","zh":"這個片語描述行動中的實用創意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the spirit of innovation","meaning":"創新精神","examples":[{"en":"The company wants to keep the spirit of innovation alive.","zh":"公司想保持創新精神。"},{"en":"The spirit of innovation is the attitude of trying new ideas and improving old methods.","zh":"Spirit of innovation 是嘗試新想法和改善舊方法的態度。"},{"en":"A school shows the spirit of innovation when teachers test better ways to support students.","zh":"當老師測試更好方法支援學生時，學校就展現創新精神。"},{"en":"If staff fear mistakes, the spirit of innovation may disappear.","zh":"如果員工害怕犯錯，創新精神可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the culture behind creative improvement.","zh":"這個片語描述創意改善背後的文化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"alive and well","meaning":"仍然充滿活力","examples":[{"en":"Nike wants the spirit of innovation to remain alive and well.","zh":"Nike 希望創新精神仍然充滿活力。"},{"en":"Alive and well means still existing and strong.","zh":"Alive and well 指仍然存在而且強健。"},{"en":"Traditional music can remain alive and well if young people continue to perform it.","zh":"如果年輕人繼續演奏，傳統音樂可以仍然充滿活力。"},{"en":"If a company keeps telling innovation stories, its founding values may stay alive and well.","zh":"如果公司持續講述創新故事，其創辦價值可能保持活力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something continuing healthily.","zh":"這個片語描述某事健康地延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"characterise its ad campaigns","meaning":"成為其廣告活動的特色","examples":[{"en":"Innovation characterises Nike’s ad campaigns.","zh":"創新成為 Nike 廣告活動的特色。"},{"en":"To characterise something means to be a typical or defining feature of it.","zh":"To characterise something 指成為某事的典型或定義性特徵。"},{"en":"Warm humour may characterise a teacher’s lessons.","zh":"溫暖幽默可能成為一位老師課堂的特色。"},{"en":"If innovation characterises a brand’s advertising, customers expect creativity from the company.","zh":"如果創新成為品牌廣告特色，顧客會期待公司有創意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what strongly marks or defines something.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈標誌或定義某事的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"messages must be aligned","meaning":"訊息必須一致","examples":[{"en":"Internal and external messages must be aligned.","zh":"內部和外部訊息必須一致。"},{"en":"Messages must be aligned means different communications should support the same idea.","zh":"Messages must be aligned 指不同溝通應支持同一想法。"},{"en":"A school’s classroom rules and parent notices must be aligned.","zh":"學校的課室規則和家長通告必須一致。"},{"en":"If messages are not aligned, people may doubt the organisation’s honesty.","zh":"如果訊息不一致，人們可能懷疑組織誠信。"},{"en":"This phrase describes necessary consistency in communication.","zh":"這個片語描述溝通中必要的一致性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"external promises","meaning":"對外承諾","examples":[{"en":"Companies should keep external promises slightly ahead of internal realities.","zh":"公司應讓對外承諾稍微領先於內部現實。"},{"en":"External promises are commitments made publicly to customers or society.","zh":"External promises 是公開向顧客或社會作出的承諾。"},{"en":"A hospital’s public promise of faster service is an external promise.","zh":"醫院公開承諾更快服務，就是對外承諾。"},{"en":"If external promises are too ambitious, employees may be unable to deliver them.","zh":"如果對外承諾太有野心，員工可能無法實現它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what an organisation tells the outside world it will do.","zh":"這個片語描述組織對外界說自己會做甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"internal realities","meaning":"內部現實情況","examples":[{"en":"External promises should not move too far ahead of internal realities.","zh":"對外承諾不應太超前於內部現實情況。"},{"en":"Internal realities are the actual conditions, abilities, and limitations inside an organisation.","zh":"Internal realities 是組織內實際條件、能力和限制。"},{"en":"A school may promise small classes, but its internal reality may be limited classroom space.","zh":"學校可能承諾小班教學，但其內部現實可能是課室空間有限。"},{"en":"If promises ignore internal realities, employees may feel pressured and customers disappointed.","zh":"如果承諾忽視內部現實，員工可能感到受壓，顧客可能失望。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts public claims with what is actually possible inside.","zh":"這個片語對比公開聲稱與內部實際可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a little ahead of","meaning":"稍微領先於……","examples":[{"en":"External promises can be kept a little ahead of internal realities.","zh":"對外承諾可以稍微領先於內部現實。"},{"en":"A little ahead of means slightly beyond but not too far beyond something.","zh":"A little ahead of 指稍微超出某事，但不是太超前。"},{"en":"A teacher may set a reading target a little ahead of a student’s current level.","zh":"老師可能把閱讀目標設定得稍微高於學生當前水平。"},{"en":"If a promise is only slightly ahead of reality, it can motivate improvement without destroying trust.","zh":"如果承諾只稍微領先現實，它可以激勵改善而不破壞信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small, manageable gap.","zh":"這個片語描述細小且可管理的差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"provide incentives for","meaning":"為……提供誘因","examples":[{"en":"Promises provide incentives for employees.","zh":"承諾為員工提供誘因。"},{"en":"To provide incentives for someone means to give them reasons or motivation to act.","zh":"To provide incentives for someone 指給某人行動的理由或動力。"},{"en":"A school prize can provide incentives for students to read more books.","zh":"學校獎項可以為學生閱讀更多書提供誘因。"},{"en":"If a company makes a public promise, employees may feel pushed to meet it.","zh":"如果公司作出公開承諾，員工可能感到被推動去達成它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving motivation through reward, pressure, or purpose.","zh":"這個片語描述透過獎勵、壓力或目標提供動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"live up to","meaning":"達到；不辜負","examples":[{"en":"Employees need something to live up to.","zh":"員工需要一些可以努力達到的東西。"},{"en":"To live up to something means to meet a standard, promise, or expectation.","zh":"To live up to something 指達到某標準、承諾或期望。"},{"en":"A student tries to live up to a teacher’s trust by preparing carefully.","zh":"學生透過仔細準備，努力不辜負老師的信任。"},{"en":"If a company promises excellent service, staff need support to live up to it.","zh":"如果公司承諾優質服務，員工需要支援去達到它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching the level expected.","zh":"這個片語描述達到被期望的水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"rallying cry","meaning":"動員口號","examples":[{"en":"Ford turned an internal rallying cry into a consumer slogan.","zh":"Ford 把內部動員口號變成消費者口號。"},{"en":"A rallying cry is a short phrase that brings people together around a goal.","zh":"Rallying cry 是把人們圍繞目標凝聚起來的短語。"},{"en":"A school team may use “one more try” as a rallying cry before a competition.","zh":"學校隊伍可能在比賽前用「再試一次」作為動員口號。"},{"en":"If a rallying cry is repeated often, it can shape group energy.","zh":"如果動員口號經常重複，它可以塑造群體能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a slogan used to motivate and unite people.","zh":"這個片語描述用來激勵和團結人們的口號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"consumer slogan","meaning":"消費者口號","examples":[{"en":"“Quality Is Job 1” became a consumer slogan.","zh":"“Quality Is Job 1” 成為消費者口號。"},{"en":"A consumer slogan is a short public phrase aimed at customers.","zh":"Consumer slogan 是針對顧客的簡短公開口號。"},{"en":"A supermarket may use a consumer slogan to promise freshness and low prices.","zh":"超級市場可能用消費者口號承諾新鮮和低價。"},{"en":"If a consumer slogan comes from an internal value, employees may support it more easily.","zh":"如果消費者口號來自內部價值，員工可能更容易支持它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a memorable message for buyers.","zh":"這個片語描述給買家的易記訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in response to","meaning":"回應……","examples":[{"en":"Ford used the slogan in response to Japanese competition.","zh":"Ford 使用該口號來回應日本競爭。"},{"en":"In response to means as a reaction to something.","zh":"In response to 指作為對某事的反應。"},{"en":"A school may add counselling services in response to rising student stress.","zh":"學校可能因學生壓力上升而增加輔導服務。"},{"en":"If competitors become stronger, a company may change its message in response.","zh":"如果競爭對手變得更強，公司可能作出回應並改變訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase links an action to the situation that caused it.","zh":"這個片語把行動與造成該行動的情況連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the threat from","meaning":"來自……的威脅","examples":[{"en":"Ford faced the threat from cheaper and more reliable Japanese cars.","zh":"Ford 面對來自更便宜且更可靠的日本汽車的威脅。"},{"en":"The threat from something is the danger or pressure caused by it.","zh":"Threat from something 是由某事造成的危險或壓力。"},{"en":"Small shops may face the threat from online shopping platforms.","zh":"小店可能面對來自網購平台的威脅。"},{"en":"If a threat becomes serious, companies may need to improve quickly.","zh":"如果威脅變得嚴重，公司可能需要迅速改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes competitive or external danger.","zh":"這個片語描述競爭或外部危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"more reliable","meaning":"更可靠","examples":[{"en":"Japanese cars were seen as cheaper and more reliable.","zh":"日本汽車被視為更便宜且更可靠。"},{"en":"More reliable means more able to work well and be trusted over time.","zh":"More reliable 指更能長期良好運作並值得信任。"},{"en":"A bus service becomes more reliable when it arrives on time every day.","zh":"如果巴士服務每天準時到達，它就變得更可靠。"},{"en":"If a product is more reliable, customers may trust the brand more.","zh":"如果產品更可靠，顧客可能更信任品牌。"},{"en":"This phrase compares dependability.","zh":"這個片語比較可靠程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"before the claim was fully justified","meaning":"在說法完全有根據之前","examples":[{"en":"Ford made the claim before it was fully justified.","zh":"Ford 在這個說法完全有根據之前就提出了它。"},{"en":"Before the claim was fully justified means before there was enough evidence to prove the statement completely.","zh":"Before the claim was fully justified 指在有足夠證據完全證明說法之前。"},{"en":"A school should not claim success before exam results fully justify it.","zh":"學校不應在考試結果完全支持前聲稱成功。"},{"en":"If a promise is made too early, employees must work hard to make it true.","zh":"如果承諾太早提出，員工必須努力令它成真。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a claim that is slightly ahead of proof.","zh":"這個片語描述稍微超前於證據的說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"place something in the public arena","meaning":"把……放到公眾領域","examples":[{"en":"Ford placed its quality promise in the public arena.","zh":"Ford 把其品質承諾放到公眾領域。"},{"en":"To place something in the public arena means to make it visible and open to public judgement.","zh":"To place something in the public arena 指使某事公開可見並接受公眾判斷。"},{"en":"A school places a promise in the public arena when it publishes targets on its website.","zh":"學校在網站公布目標時，就是把承諾放到公眾領域。"},{"en":"If a claim is public, people can test whether the organisation lives up to it.","zh":"如果聲稱是公開的，人們可以檢驗組織是否做到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a commitment publicly visible.","zh":"這個片語描述令承諾公開可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"give employees an incentive to","meaning":"給員工誘因去……","examples":[{"en":"The slogan gave employees an incentive to improve quality.","zh":"這個口號給員工誘因去改善品質。"},{"en":"To give employees an incentive to do something means to give them a reason to act.","zh":"To give employees an incentive to do something 指給員工行動的理由。"},{"en":"A bonus may give employees an incentive to finish a project early.","zh":"花紅可能給員工誘因去提早完成項目。"},{"en":"If a promise is public, employees may feel motivated to meet it.","zh":"如果承諾是公開的，員工可能感到有動力去達成它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating a reason for staff action.","zh":"這個片語描述為員工行動創造理由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"match the Japanese","meaning":"追上日本企業","examples":[{"en":"Ford employees were encouraged to match the Japanese.","zh":"Ford 員工被鼓勵去追上日本企業。"},{"en":"To match the Japanese means to reach the same standard as Japanese competitors in that context.","zh":"To match the Japanese 在此語境中指達到日本競爭對手的同等標準。"},{"en":"A local restaurant may try to match a famous chain’s speed while keeping its own taste.","zh":"本地餐廳可能嘗試追上著名連鎖店的速度，同時保持自身味道。"},{"en":"If competitors are more reliable, a company must improve quality to match them.","zh":"如果競爭對手更可靠，公司必須改善品質才能追上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trying to equal a strong rival’s standard.","zh":"這個片語描述嘗試達到強大對手的標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"push something too far ahead","meaning":"把……推得太超前","examples":[{"en":"A promise loses credibility if it is pushed too far ahead.","zh":"如果承諾被推得太超前，它會失去可信性。"},{"en":"To push something too far ahead means to make a promise or claim much more advanced than reality.","zh":"To push something too far ahead 指令承諾或聲稱遠遠超前於現實。"},{"en":"A school pushes a claim too far ahead if it promises perfect results before improving teaching.","zh":"如果學校在改善教學前承諾完美成績，就是把說法推得太超前。"},{"en":"If public promises are too distant from reality, people may stop believing them.","zh":"如果公開承諾與現實距離太遠，人們可能不再相信。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against overpromising.","zh":"這個片語提醒人不要過度承諾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"lose credibility","meaning":"失去可信性","examples":[{"en":"A promise loses credibility if it is too far from reality.","zh":"如果承諾與現實距離太遠，它會失去可信性。"},{"en":"To lose credibility means to become less believable or trustworthy.","zh":"To lose credibility 指變得較不可信或不值得信任。"},{"en":"A student loses credibility if they often make excuses that prove false.","zh":"如果學生經常找藉口而後來被證明不真實，他會失去可信性。"},{"en":"If a company promises more than it can deliver, customers may stop trusting it.","zh":"如果公司承諾超出自己能做到的範圍，顧客可能不再信任它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the weakening of trust.","zh":"這個片語描述信任削弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"beleaguered","meaning":"陷入困境的","examples":[{"en":"British Rail was a beleaguered company when it launched the campaign.","zh":"British Rail 推出推廣活動時，是一間陷入困境的公司。"},{"en":"Beleaguered means under serious pressure from problems, criticism, or attacks.","zh":"Beleaguered 指受到問題、批評或攻擊嚴重壓迫。"},{"en":"A beleaguered school may face falling enrolment, staff shortages, and parent complaints.","zh":"陷入困境的學校可能面對收生下降、人手短缺和家長投訴。"},{"en":"If a company is already beleaguered, a badly timed campaign can worsen its troubles.","zh":"如果公司已陷入困境，時機不佳的推廣活動可能令問題惡化。"},{"en":"This word describes an organisation surrounded by difficulties.","zh":"這個詞描述被困難包圍的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"service improvements","meaning":"服務改善","examples":[{"en":"British Rail announced service improvements too early.","zh":"British Rail 太早宣布服務改善。"},{"en":"Service improvements are changes that make service better for customers or users.","zh":"Service improvements 是令顧客服務或用戶服務變得更好的改變。"},{"en":"A clinic may introduce service improvements such as shorter waiting times and clearer booking.","zh":"診所可能推出服務改善，例如縮短等候時間和更清晰預約。"},{"en":"If improvements are promised before they are real, customers may become more critical.","zh":"如果改善在尚未成真前就被承諾，顧客可能變得更批評。"},{"en":"This phrase describes better service quality or delivery.","zh":"這個片語描述服務質素或提供方式的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"under the banner","meaning":"以……為口號；在……旗號下","examples":[{"en":"The campaign was launched under the banner “We’re Getting There.”","zh":"這項推廣活動以 “We’re Getting There” 為口號推出。"},{"en":"Under the banner means using a slogan, name, or theme to represent an effort.","zh":"Under the banner 指使用某口號、名稱或主題代表某項行動。"},{"en":"A school may run activities under the banner “Read Every Day.”","zh":"學校可能以 “Read Every Day” 為口號舉辦活動。"},{"en":"If a campaign banner sounds too confident, people may compare it with reality closely.","zh":"如果推廣口號聽起來太有信心，人們可能仔細把它與現實比較。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the public label of a campaign or movement.","zh":"這個片語描述推廣活動或運動的公開標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"prematurely","meaning":"過早地","examples":[{"en":"British Rail launched the campaign prematurely.","zh":"British Rail 過早地推出推廣活動。"},{"en":"Prematurely means too early, before the right time or before preparation is complete.","zh":"Prematurely 指太早，在適當時間前或準備完成前。"},{"en":"A student may submit an essay prematurely before checking grammar and structure.","zh":"學生可能在檢查文法和結構前過早地提交作文。"},{"en":"If a company announces improvements prematurely, the public may notice the unfinished reality.","zh":"如果公司過早宣布改善，公眾可能注意到未完成的現實。"},{"en":"This word warns that timing was too early.","zh":"這個詞提醒時機太早。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"draw attention to","meaning":"使人注意到……","examples":[{"en":"The campaign drew attention to the gap between promise and reality.","zh":"這項推廣活動使人注意到承諾與現實之間的差距。"},{"en":"To draw attention to something means to make people notice it.","zh":"To draw attention to something 指令人注意某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may draw attention to common grammar mistakes before students write again.","zh":"老師可能在學生再次寫作前，使他們注意常見文法錯誤。"},{"en":"If a campaign promises improvement too early, it may make weaknesses more visible.","zh":"如果推廣活動太早承諾改善，它可能令弱點更明顯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making an issue noticeable.","zh":"這個片語描述令議題變得可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the gap between","meaning":"……之間的差距","examples":[{"en":"The campaign highlighted the gap between the promise and the reality.","zh":"這項推廣活動突出了承諾與現實之間的差距。"},{"en":"The gap between two things is the difference or distance between them.","zh":"The gap between two things 是兩者之間的差異或距離。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice the gap between a student’s speaking confidence and writing accuracy.","zh":"老師可能注意到學生說話信心與寫作準確度之間的差距。"},{"en":"If the gap between promise and reality is large, credibility falls.","zh":"如果承諾與現實之間的差距很大，可信性會下降。"},{"en":"This phrase compares what is said with what actually exists.","zh":"這個片語比較所說的與實際存在的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"prompt destructive press coverage","meaning":"引發負面傳媒報道","examples":[{"en":"The campaign prompted destructive press coverage.","zh":"這項推廣活動引發負面傳媒報道。"},{"en":"To prompt destructive press coverage means to cause newspapers or media to report in a damaging way.","zh":"To prompt destructive press coverage 指導致報紙或媒體以有損害的方式報道。"},{"en":"A school scandal may prompt negative press coverage if leaders respond badly.","zh":"如果領導層回應差，學校醜聞可能引發負面傳媒報道。"},{"en":"If media coverage attacks a campaign, staff morale and public trust may fall.","zh":"如果媒體報道攻擊推廣活動，員工士氣和公眾信任可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a campaign causing harmful media attention.","zh":"這個片語描述推廣活動造成有害媒體關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"in turn","meaning":"繼而；反過來","examples":[{"en":"Negative press coverage, in turn, demoralised staff.","zh":"負面傳媒報道繼而令員工士氣低落。"},{"en":"In turn means as the next result in a chain of cause and effect.","zh":"In turn 指作為因果鏈中的下一個結果。"},{"en":"Poor sleep reduces concentration, which in turn affects exam performance.","zh":"睡眠不足削弱專注，繼而影響考試表現。"},{"en":"If bad publicity hurts staff morale, service may then become worse.","zh":"如果負面宣傳傷害員工士氣，服務之後可能變得更差。"},{"en":"This phrase connects one consequence to another.","zh":"這個片語把一個後果與另一個後果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"demoralise staff","meaning":"令員工士氣低落","examples":[{"en":"The press coverage demoralised staff.","zh":"傳媒報道令員工士氣低落。"},{"en":"To demoralise staff means to make employees lose confidence, hope, or motivation.","zh":"To demoralise staff 指令員工失去信心、希望或動力。"},{"en":"Constant criticism can demoralise teachers who are already working hard.","zh":"持續批評可以令本來已努力工作的老師士氣低落。"},{"en":"If staff are demoralised, they may stop trying to improve service.","zh":"如果員工士氣低落，他們可能停止嘗試改善服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damage to employee morale.","zh":"這個片語描述對員工士氣的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be legitimately proud of","meaning":"有充分理由為……自豪","examples":[{"en":"Staff had been legitimately proud of the service advances they had made.","zh":"員工有充分理由為自己作出的服務進步感到自豪。"},{"en":"To be legitimately proud of something means to have a fair and reasonable reason to feel proud.","zh":"To be legitimately proud of something 指有公平而合理的理由感到自豪。"},{"en":"A student is legitimately proud of improving after months of practice.","zh":"學生經過數月練習後進步，有充分理由感到自豪。"},{"en":"If employees make real progress, negative publicity can feel especially unfair.","zh":"如果員工取得真實進步，負面宣傳可能顯得特別不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pride that is deserved, not empty.","zh":"這個片語描述應得的自豪，而不是空洞自滿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"service advances","meaning":"服務上的進步","examples":[{"en":"Employees were proud of the service advances they had made.","zh":"員工為自己作出的服務進步感到自豪。"},{"en":"Service advances are improvements or progress in the quality of service.","zh":"Service advances 是服務質素上的改善或進展。"},{"en":"A clinic may make service advances by adding online booking and shorter waiting times.","zh":"診所可能透過增加網上預約和縮短等候時間來取得服務進步。"},{"en":"If service advances are ignored, staff may feel their effort is not recognised.","zh":"如果服務進步被忽視，員工可能覺得努力沒有被認可。"},{"en":"This phrase describes real progress in how customers or users are served.","zh":"這個片語描述顧客或用戶服務方式上的真正進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"complete each sentence with","meaning":"用……完成每句","examples":[{"en":"Students complete each sentence with the correct ending.","zh":"學生用正確句尾完成每句。"},{"en":"To complete each sentence with something means to finish the sentence using the required word or phrase.","zh":"To complete each sentence with something 指用所需字詞或片語完成句子。"},{"en":"In reading exams, students complete sentences with information from the passage.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生用文章資料完成句子。"},{"en":"If the ending does not fit the grammar, the answer is likely wrong.","zh":"如果句尾不符合文法，答案很可能錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the correct ending","meaning":"正確的句尾；正確結尾","examples":[{"en":"The task asks students to choose the correct ending.","zh":"題目要求學生選擇正確句尾。"},{"en":"The correct ending is the option that completes the sentence accurately and grammatically.","zh":"Correct ending 是準確且符合文法地完成句子的選項。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole sentence before choosing the correct ending.","zh":"學生應先讀完整句，再選擇正確句尾。"},{"en":"If an ending changes the meaning of the passage, it is not correct.","zh":"如果句尾改變文章意思，它就不正確。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the right sentence completion.","zh":"這個片語指正確的句子完成部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"write the correct letter","meaning":"寫上正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students write the correct letter in the answer boxes.","zh":"學生在答案框寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"To write the correct letter means to record the option letter that matches the answer.","zh":"To write the correct letter 指記下符合答案的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a matching task, students may write A, B, or C instead of a full phrase.","zh":"在配對題中，學生可能寫 A、B 或 C，而不是完整片語。"},{"en":"If students choose the right idea but write the wrong letter, they may lose the mark.","zh":"如果學生選對意思卻寫錯字母，可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is a standard instruction in reading exams.","zh":"這個片語是閱讀考試的標準指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"more than once","meaning":"不止一次","examples":[{"en":"The same letter can be used more than once.","zh":"同一字母可以使用不止一次。"},{"en":"More than once means two or more times.","zh":"More than once 指兩次或更多次。"},{"en":"A paragraph may be used more than once if it contains several pieces of information.","zh":"如果一段包含幾項資料，它可能被使用不止一次。"},{"en":"If an answer option fits two questions, students should not assume it can only be used once.","zh":"如果一個選項適合兩題，學生不應假設它只能用一次。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that repetition may be allowed.","zh":"這個片語提醒重複使用可能被允許。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"alienate employees","meaning":"令員工疏離；令員工反感","examples":[{"en":"A campaign can alienate employees if it ignores their feelings.","zh":"如果推廣活動忽略員工感受，它可以令員工疏離。"},{"en":"To alienate employees means to make staff feel excluded, offended, or distant from the company.","zh":"To alienate employees 指令員工感到被排除、被冒犯或與公司疏遠。"},{"en":"A school policy can alienate teachers if it blames them without listening.","zh":"如果校政不聆聽老師就責怪他們，它可以令老師反感。"},{"en":"If employees feel alienated, they may resist the brand message.","zh":"如果員工感到疏離，他們可能抗拒品牌訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating emotional distance from staff.","zh":"這個片語描述與員工製造情感距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"apologetic branding campaign","meaning":"帶有道歉意味的品牌推廣活動","examples":[{"en":"An apologetic branding campaign may discourage staff.","zh":"帶有道歉意味的品牌推廣活動可能令員工氣餒。"},{"en":"An apologetic branding campaign is a campaign that admits problems or says sorry as part of its message.","zh":"Apologetic branding campaign 是把承認問題或道歉作為訊息一部分的推廣活動。"},{"en":"A company may use an apologetic campaign after customers complain about poor service.","zh":"顧客投訴服務差後，公司可能使用帶有道歉意味的推廣活動。"},{"en":"If the apology sounds like it blames staff, employees may feel discouraged.","zh":"如果道歉聽起來像責怪員工，員工可能感到氣餒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a brand message built around apology or admission.","zh":"這個片語描述以道歉或承認為核心的品牌訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"attract negative publicity","meaning":"招致負面宣傳","examples":[{"en":"A poorly timed campaign can attract negative publicity.","zh":"時機不佳的推廣活動可以招致負面宣傳。"},{"en":"To attract negative publicity means to draw unfavourable public or media attention.","zh":"To attract negative publicity 指吸引不利的公眾或媒體注意。"},{"en":"A school may attract negative publicity if it announces a fee rise without explanation.","zh":"如果學校不作解釋就宣布加學費，可能招致負面宣傳。"},{"en":"If a campaign highlights a company’s weaknesses, journalists may criticise it.","zh":"如果推廣活動突出公司弱點，記者可能批評它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming known for bad reasons.","zh":"這個片語描述因壞理由而被人注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"advertising campaign","meaning":"廣告活動","examples":[{"en":"The company attracted negative publicity through its advertising campaign.","zh":"公司透過其廣告活動招致負面宣傳。"},{"en":"An advertising campaign is a planned series of advertisements with one main message.","zh":"Advertising campaign 是帶有同一主要訊息的一系列有計劃廣告。"},{"en":"A charity may run an advertising campaign to encourage donations.","zh":"慈善機構可能推行廣告活動以鼓勵捐款。"},{"en":"If an advertising campaign does not match reality, it may damage trust.","zh":"如果廣告活動與現實不符，它可能損害信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised public promotion through ads.","zh":"這個片語描述透過廣告進行的有組織公開推廣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"conflicting image","meaning":"矛盾的形象","examples":[{"en":"The company produced a conflicting image for employees and the public.","zh":"公司為員工和公眾製造了矛盾的形象。"},{"en":"A conflicting image is an impression that contains mixed or contradictory messages.","zh":"Conflicting image 是包含混亂或互相矛盾訊息的印象。"},{"en":"A school creates a conflicting image if it says it values rest but gives excessive homework.","zh":"如果學校說重視休息卻給過量功課，它就製造矛盾形象。"},{"en":"If employees and customers see different images, brand trust may weaken.","zh":"如果員工和顧客看見不同形象，品牌信任可能削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a confused or inconsistent public identity.","zh":"這個片語描述混亂或不一致的公開身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the general public","meaning":"一般大眾","examples":[{"en":"The campaign sent one message to employees and another to the general public.","zh":"推廣活動向員工發出一個訊息，向一般大眾發出另一個訊息。"},{"en":"The general public means ordinary people as a whole, not a specialised group.","zh":"General public 指普通人整體，而不是專門群體。"},{"en":"A health warning is written for the general public, so it should avoid technical language.","zh":"健康警告是寫給一般大眾的，所以應避免技術語言。"},{"en":"If the general public hears one promise while employees hear another, confusion may result.","zh":"如果一般大眾聽到一個承諾，而員工聽到另一個，可能造成混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes society at large.","zh":"這個片語描述整體社會大眾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"successfully use something to inspire","meaning":"成功利用……去激勵","examples":[{"en":"A company can successfully use advertising to inspire employees.","zh":"公司可以成功利用廣告去激勵員工。"},{"en":"To successfully use something to inspire means to apply it in a way that motivates people.","zh":"To successfully use something to inspire 指有效運用某物來激勵人。"},{"en":"A teacher can successfully use real stories to inspire students to read more.","zh":"老師可以成功利用真實故事去激勵學生多閱讀。"},{"en":"If advertising gives employees pride and direction, it can inspire them internally.","zh":"如果廣告給員工自豪和方向，它可以在內部激勵他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes effective use of a tool for motivation.","zh":"這個片語描述有效使用工具來產生動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"inspire employees","meaning":"激勵員工","examples":[{"en":"IBM used its campaign to inspire employees.","zh":"IBM 利用其推廣活動激勵員工。"},{"en":"To inspire employees means to make workers feel motivated, hopeful, or proud.","zh":"To inspire employees 指令員工感到有動力、有希望或自豪。"},{"en":"A manager can inspire employees by explaining how their work helps real customers.","zh":"管理者可以透過解釋員工工作如何幫助真實顧客來激勵員工。"},{"en":"If employees are inspired, they may put more energy into difficult tasks.","zh":"如果員工受到激勵，他們可能把更多精力投入困難任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lifting staff motivation emotionally.","zh":"這個片語描述在情感上提升員工動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"draw on","meaning":"借鑑；取材自","examples":[{"en":"Nike’s storytelling draws on the legends of the company spirit.","zh":"Nike 的故事講述取材自公司精神中的傳奇。"},{"en":"To draw on something means to use it as a source of ideas, strength, or material.","zh":"To draw on something 指把某事用作想法、力量或材料來源。"},{"en":"A student can draw on personal experience when writing an argumentative essay.","zh":"學生寫議論文時可以借鑑個人經驗。"},{"en":"If a company draws on its history, it can make values feel more real.","zh":"如果公司取材自自身歷史，它可以令價值更真實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using an existing source to support something new.","zh":"這個片語描述使用現有來源來支持新內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"company spirit","meaning":"公司精神","examples":[{"en":"Nike’s stories help preserve the company spirit.","zh":"Nike 的故事幫助保存公司精神。"},{"en":"Company spirit is the shared attitude, values, and energy that define a company.","zh":"Company spirit 是定義公司的共同態度、價值和能量。"},{"en":"A school’s spirit may include care, hard work, humour, and pride.","zh":"學校精神可能包括關懷、勤奮、幽默和自豪。"},{"en":"If company spirit is strong, employees may feel part of something larger than a job.","zh":"如果公司精神強，員工可能感到自己屬於比工作更大的事物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the emotional culture of an organisation.","zh":"這個片語描述組織的情感文化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"sport shoe company","meaning":"運動鞋公司","examples":[{"en":"A sport shoe company used stories to reinforce its brand values.","zh":"一間運動鞋公司使用故事來強化其品牌價值。"},{"en":"A sport shoe company designs, makes, or sells shoes for sports and exercise.","zh":"Sport shoe company 設計、製造或銷售運動和鍛煉用鞋。"},{"en":"A running-shoe brand may test soles with athletes before selling them.","zh":"跑鞋品牌可能在銷售前與運動員測試鞋底。"},{"en":"If a sport shoe company tells strong innovation stories, customers may trust its products more.","zh":"如果運動鞋公司講述有力的創新故事，顧客可能更信任其產品。"},{"en":"This phrase names a business in the athletic footwear market.","zh":"這個片語命名運動鞋市場中的企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"railway company","meaning":"鐵路公司","examples":[{"en":"A railway company attracted negative publicity through its campaign.","zh":"一間鐵路公司透過其推廣活動招致負面宣傳。"},{"en":"A railway company operates trains, stations, or rail services.","zh":"Railway company 營運火車、車站或鐵路服務。"},{"en":"A railway company must manage timetables, safety, staff, and passenger complaints.","zh":"鐵路公司必須管理時間表、安全、人手和乘客投訴。"},{"en":"If a railway company promises better service too early, passengers may criticise it.","zh":"如果鐵路公司太早承諾更好服務，乘客可能批評它。"},{"en":"This phrase names a transport organisation.","zh":"這個片語命名一種交通運輸組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"agree with the claims of","meaning":"符合……的主張","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements agree with the claims of the writer.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否符合作者的主張。"},{"en":"To agree with the claims of the writer means to match what the writer argues.","zh":"To agree with the claims of the writer 指符合作者所主張的內容。"},{"en":"In reading tasks, students must use the passage, not outside knowledge, to judge this.","zh":"在閱讀題中，學生必須用文章而非外部知識來判斷。"},{"en":"If a statement changes the writer’s meaning, it does not agree with the claim.","zh":"如果陳述改變作者意思，它就不符合主張。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in YES, NO, NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於 YES、NO、NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the claims of the writer","meaning":"作者的主張","examples":[{"en":"The task asks about the claims of the writer, not outside facts.","zh":"題目問的是作者的主張，而不是外部事實。"},{"en":"The claims of the writer are the ideas, arguments, or opinions the writer presents.","zh":"Claims of the writer 是作者提出的想法、論點或意見。"},{"en":"A student should separate the writer’s claims from examples mentioned only for contrast.","zh":"學生應把作者主張與只作對比的例子分開。"},{"en":"If the writer does not state or imply something, it should not be treated as a claim.","zh":"如果作者沒有明說或暗示某事，就不應把它視為主張。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the author’s position inside the text.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於文本內作者的立場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the views of the writer.","zh":"陳述可能與作者的觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of that person’s view.","zh":"To contradict the views of someone 指說出與某人觀點相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the writer says employees matter, a statement saying employees do not matter contradicts the view.","zh":"如果作者說員工重要，而陳述說員工不重要，就是與觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should choose NO only when the meaning is clearly opposite.","zh":"學生只有在意思清楚相反時，才應選 NO。"},{"en":"This phrase describes conflict between a statement and an opinion.","zh":"這個片語描述陳述與觀點之間的衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"It is impossible to say if the passage gives no clear information.","zh":"如果文章沒有提供清晰資料，就無法判斷。"},{"en":"To be impossible to say means there is not enough evidence to decide.","zh":"To be impossible to say 指沒有足夠證據作決定。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions staff salaries, it is impossible to say whether they increased.","zh":"如果文章從未提及員工薪酬，就無法判斷薪酬是否增加。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when the text gives no support.","zh":"當文本沒有支持時，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when neither agreement nor contradiction can be proven.","zh":"這個片語用於不能證明一致或矛盾的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"a strong conviction in","meaning":"對……的堅定信念","examples":[{"en":"A strong conviction in the brand can improve employees’ motivation.","zh":"對品牌的堅定信念可以改善員工動機。"},{"en":"A strong conviction in something is a firm belief that it is true, valuable, or right.","zh":"Strong conviction in something 是堅定相信某事真實、有價值或正確。"},{"en":"A teacher with a strong conviction in reading will encourage students even when progress is slow.","zh":"對閱讀有堅定信念的老師，即使學生進步慢也會鼓勵他們。"},{"en":"If employees strongly believe in a brand, they may defend and promote it sincerely.","zh":"如果員工強烈相信品牌，他們可能真誠地捍衛並推廣它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep belief, not casual agreement.","zh":"這個片語描述深層信念，而不是隨便同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"contribute to","meaning":"有助於；促成","examples":[{"en":"Belief in the brand can contribute to higher job performance.","zh":"相信品牌可以有助於更高工作表現。"},{"en":"To contribute to something means to help cause or support it.","zh":"To contribute to something 指幫助造成或支持某事。"},{"en":"Regular sleep can contribute to better concentration in class.","zh":"規律睡眠可以有助於課堂上更好專注。"},{"en":"If internal marketing increases motivation, it may contribute to better service.","zh":"如果內部市場推廣增加動機，它可能促成更好服務。"},{"en":"This phrase links one factor to a result.","zh":"這個片語把一個因素與結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"higher job performance","meaning":"更高的工作表現","examples":[{"en":"Motivated employees may achieve higher job performance.","zh":"有動力的員工可能達到更高的工作表現。"},{"en":"Higher job performance means better quality, productivity, or effectiveness at work.","zh":"Higher job performance 指工作上的更好質素、生產力或效果。"},{"en":"A nurse shows higher job performance when care becomes safer and more efficient.","zh":"當護理更安全和更有效率時，護士就展現更高工作表現。"},{"en":"If employees believe in the brand, they may serve customers with greater effort.","zh":"如果員工相信品牌，他們可能更努力服務顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improved work results.","zh":"這個片語描述改善了的工作成果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"overlook the necessity for","meaning":"忽略……的必要性","examples":[{"en":"Companies often overlook the necessity for internal communication.","zh":"公司經常忽略內部溝通的必要性。"},{"en":"To overlook the necessity for something means to fail to realise that it is needed.","zh":"To overlook the necessity for something 指未能意識到某事是需要的。"},{"en":"A student may overlook the necessity for planning before writing an essay.","zh":"學生寫作文前可能忽略規劃的必要性。"},{"en":"If companies overlook internal communication, staff may not understand the brand promise.","zh":"如果公司忽略內部溝通，員工可能不理解品牌承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes missing something essential.","zh":"這個片語描述錯過必要之事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"internal communication","meaning":"內部溝通","examples":[{"en":"Internal communication is essential for successful branding.","zh":"內部溝通對成功品牌建立至關重要。"},{"en":"Internal communication is the sharing of information inside an organisation.","zh":"Internal communication 是組織內部資訊分享。"},{"en":"A school uses internal communication when teachers receive clear updates before parents are informed.","zh":"當老師在家長獲通知前先收到清晰更新，學校就是在進行內部溝通。"},{"en":"If internal communication is weak, employees may hear rumours instead of facts.","zh":"如果內部溝通薄弱，員工可能聽到謠言而不是事實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how an organisation speaks to its own people.","zh":"這個片語描述組織如何與自己的人溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be ready to view something as","meaning":"準備好將……視為","examples":[{"en":"Consumers were not ready to view IBM as an e-business leader.","zh":"消費者尚未準備好將 IBM 視為電子商務領導者。"},{"en":"To be ready to view something as something means to be prepared to accept it in that role or identity.","zh":"To be ready to view something as something 指準備好接受某事具有該角色或身份。"},{"en":"Parents may not be ready to view online lessons as equal to classroom learning.","zh":"家長可能未準備好將網上課堂視為等同面授學習。"},{"en":"If customers are not ready to accept a new image, marketing must build belief gradually.","zh":"如果顧客尚未準備好接受新形象，市場推廣必須逐步建立信念。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental readiness to accept a new identity.","zh":"這個片語描述接受新身份的心理準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"due to","meaning":"由於；因為","examples":[{"en":"The campaign’s failure was not described as being due to agency advice.","zh":"文章沒有把推廣活動失敗描述為由於廣告公司建議。"},{"en":"Due to means because of.","zh":"Due to 指因為。"},{"en":"The school picnic was cancelled due to heavy rain.","zh":"學校野餐由於大雨而取消。"},{"en":"If a campaign fails due to poor internal support, better advertising alone may not solve it.","zh":"如果推廣活動由於內部支持差而失敗，單靠更好廣告未必能解決。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the reason for a result.","zh":"這個片語引出結果的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"bad advice","meaning":"錯誤建議","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not say the airline failed because of bad advice.","zh":"文章沒有說航空公司失敗是因為錯誤建議。"},{"en":"Bad advice is guidance that is wrong, unsuitable, or harmful.","zh":"Bad advice 是錯誤、不合適或有害的指引。"},{"en":"A student may waste time if they follow bad advice about memorising whole essays.","zh":"如果學生聽從整篇背誦作文的錯誤建議，可能浪費時間。"},{"en":"If a company follows bad advice, it may choose the wrong message or timing.","zh":"如果公司聽從錯誤建議，可能選錯訊息或時機。"},{"en":"This phrase describes guidance that leads people in the wrong direction.","zh":"這個片語描述把人帶向錯誤方向的指引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"advertising agency","meaning":"廣告公司","examples":[{"en":"An advertising agency may advise companies on branding campaigns.","zh":"廣告公司可能就品牌推廣活動向公司提供建議。"},{"en":"An advertising agency is a business that creates advertisements and marketing plans for clients.","zh":"Advertising agency 是為客戶創造廣告和市場推廣計劃的企業。"},{"en":"A small shop may hire an advertising agency to design posters and online ads.","zh":"小店可能聘請廣告公司設計海報和網上廣告。"},{"en":"If an agency understands customers but not employees, its campaign may still fail.","zh":"如果廣告公司理解顧客但不理解員工，其推廣活動仍可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase names a professional marketing service company.","zh":"這個片語命名專業市場推廣服務公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"branding campaign","meaning":"品牌建立活動；品牌推廣活動","examples":[{"en":"A branding campaign should connect with both customers and employees.","zh":"品牌推廣活動應同時與顧客和員工建立連繫。"},{"en":"A branding campaign is a planned effort to shape how people understand a brand.","zh":"Branding campaign 是有計劃地塑造人們如何理解品牌的努力。"},{"en":"A university may run a branding campaign to show it is practical, global, and student-centred.","zh":"大學可能推行品牌推廣活動，顯示自己實用、國際化且以學生為中心。"},{"en":"If employees cannot support the brand message, the campaign may feel false.","zh":"如果員工不能支持品牌訊息，推廣活動可能感覺虛假。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised work to build brand identity.","zh":"這個片語描述有組織地建立品牌身份的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"boost its image","meaning":"提升形象","examples":[{"en":"A company may launch a campaign to boost its image.","zh":"公司可能推出推廣活動來提升形象。"},{"en":"To boost its image means to improve how the public sees the company.","zh":"To boost its image 指改善公眾如何看待公司。"},{"en":"A school may boost its image by showing student achievements and community service.","zh":"學校可能透過展示學生成就和社區服務來提升形象。"},{"en":"If image improves but service does not, the improvement may not last.","zh":"如果形象改善但服務沒有改善，這種改善可能不持久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strengthening reputation.","zh":"這個片語描述加強聲譽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"as a result of","meaning":"因為；由於","examples":[{"en":"The campaign was pulled as a result of employee opposition.","zh":"這項推廣活動因員工反對而被撤回。"},{"en":"As a result of means because of something that happened.","zh":"As a result of 指因為某事發生。"},{"en":"A lesson may be delayed as a result of a fire drill.","zh":"課堂可能由於火警演習而延遲。"},{"en":"If employee opposition becomes strong, leaders may cancel the campaign as a result.","zh":"如果員工反對變得強烈，領袖可能因此取消推廣活動。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the cause of a consequence.","zh":"這個片語引出後果的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"market research","meaning":"市場研究","examples":[{"en":"Market research can reveal how customers feel about a brand.","zh":"市場研究可以揭示顧客如何看待品牌。"},{"en":"Market research is the collection of information about customers, competitors, and demand.","zh":"Market research 是收集關於顧客、競爭者和需求的資訊。"},{"en":"A café may use market research to learn whether customers want healthier drinks.","zh":"咖啡店可能使用市場研究來了解顧客是否想要更健康飲品。"},{"en":"If market research is ignored, a company may misunderstand its audience.","zh":"如果市場研究被忽視，公司可能誤解其受眾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence-gathering for business decisions.","zh":"這個片語描述為商業決策收集證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"launch its new campaign","meaning":"推出新的推廣活動","examples":[{"en":"IBM launched its new campaign despite unfavourable research.","zh":"IBM 儘管有不利研究，仍推出新的推廣活動。"},{"en":"To launch its new campaign means to start its new organised promotion.","zh":"To launch its new campaign 指開始其新的有組織推廣。"},{"en":"A school may launch its new campaign for reading week on Monday morning.","zh":"學校可能在星期一早上推出閱讀周的新推廣活動。"},{"en":"If a campaign is launched despite doubts, leaders may be taking a strategic risk.","zh":"如果在有疑慮下仍推出推廣活動，領袖可能正在承擔策略風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of a new promotional effort.","zh":"這個片語描述新推廣工作的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"an expensive mistake","meaning":"昂貴的錯誤","examples":[{"en":"An advertising campaign can become an expensive mistake if it damages credibility.","zh":"如果廣告活動損害可信性，它可能成為昂貴的錯誤。"},{"en":"An expensive mistake is an error that costs a lot of money, trust, or effort.","zh":"Expensive mistake 是代價很高的錯誤，可以是金錢、信任或努力上的代價。"},{"en":"Buying the wrong school software can become an expensive mistake if teachers cannot use it.","zh":"如果老師不能使用，買錯學校軟件可能成為昂貴的錯誤。"},{"en":"If a campaign fails publicly, the company may lose both budget and reputation.","zh":"如果推廣活動公開失敗，公司可能同時失去預算和聲譽。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a costly wrong decision.","zh":"這個片語描述代價高昂的錯誤決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"employees claimed that","meaning":"員工聲稱","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not state that Nike employees claimed they were inspired.","zh":"文章沒有說 Nike 員工聲稱自己受到激勵。"},{"en":"Employees claimed that means staff said or reported something, whether or not it is proven.","zh":"Employees claimed that 指員工說出或報稱某事，不論是否已證實。"},{"en":"Employees claimed that the new system saved time, but managers still checked the data.","zh":"員工聲稱新系統節省時間，但管理者仍檢查數據。"},{"en":"If a passage does not mention a claim, students should not assume it is true.","zh":"如果文章沒有提及某聲稱，學生不應假設它是真的。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what employees reportedly said.","zh":"這個片語引出員工據稱說過的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"be inspired by","meaning":"受……啟發；受……激勵","examples":[{"en":"Employees may be inspired by company stories.","zh":"員工可能受公司故事啟發。"},{"en":"To be inspired by something means to feel encouraged, motivated, or given ideas by it.","zh":"To be inspired by something 指因某事感到受鼓勵、有動力或得到想法。"},{"en":"A student may be inspired by a teacher’s story of overcoming failure.","zh":"學生可能受老師克服失敗的故事啟發。"},{"en":"If employees are inspired by a founder’s example, they may copy that spirit at work.","zh":"如果員工受創辦人的例子啟發，他們可能在工作中效法那種精神。"},{"en":"This phrase describes positive influence on feeling or action.","zh":"這個片語描述對感受或行動的正面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"company stories","meaning":"公司故事","examples":[{"en":"Nike uses company stories to reinforce its culture.","zh":"Nike 使用公司故事來強化其文化。"},{"en":"Company stories are stories about a company’s history, people, values, or important moments.","zh":"Company stories 是關於公司歷史、人物、價值或重要時刻的故事。"},{"en":"A school may tell stories about former students to pass on its spirit.","zh":"學校可能講述舊生故事來傳承其精神。"},{"en":"If company stories are meaningful, employees may remember values better than rules.","zh":"如果公司故事有意義，員工可能比記規則更容易記住價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes storytelling used to preserve organisational culture.","zh":"這個片語描述用來保存組織文化的故事講述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"a slight difference between","meaning":"……之間的輕微差距","examples":[{"en":"A slight difference between promises and realities can motivate employees.","zh":"承諾與現實之間的輕微差距可以激勵員工。"},{"en":"A slight difference between two things is a small gap or difference.","zh":"Slight difference between two things 是兩者之間的小差距或小不同。"},{"en":"A slight difference between a student’s current level and target level can create healthy challenge.","zh":"學生當前水平與目標水平之間的輕微差距，可以創造健康挑戰。"},{"en":"If the difference is slight, employees may feel the promise is achievable.","zh":"如果差距輕微，員工可能覺得承諾可達成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small, manageable gap.","zh":"這個片語描述細小而可管理的差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"create a sense of purpose","meaning":"建立目標感","examples":[{"en":"External promises can create a sense of purpose for employees.","zh":"對外承諾可以為員工建立目標感。"},{"en":"To create a sense of purpose means to make people feel their work has direction and meaning.","zh":"To create a sense of purpose 指令人覺得自己的工作有方向和意義。"},{"en":"A teacher can create a sense of purpose by showing students how English helps real communication.","zh":"老師可以透過展示英語如何幫助真實溝通，為學生建立目標感。"},{"en":"If employees see how their work supports a public promise, they may feel more motivated.","zh":"如果員工看見自己的工作如何支持公開承諾，他們可能更有動力。"},{"en":"This phrase connects meaning with action and direction.","zh":"這個片語把意義與行動和方向連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 36 - Internal Market - Selling the inside.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 37":[{"front":"living dunes","meaning":"有生命力的沙丘","examples":[{"en":"Living dunes can grow, move and even produce sound.","zh":"有生命力的沙丘可以生長、移動，甚至發出聲音。"},{"en":"Living dunes are sand dunes that behave like active natural structures rather than dead piles of sand.","zh":"living dunes 指像活躍自然結構般運作，而不是死寂沙堆的沙丘。"},{"en":"Visitors may be surprised to learn that living dunes can slowly cross roads and cover buildings.","zh":"遊客可能驚訝地知道，有生命力的沙丘可以慢慢橫越道路並覆蓋建築物。"},{"en":"Wind, loose sand and little vegetation allow living dunes to change position over time.","zh":"風、鬆散沙粒和稀少植被使有生命力的沙丘能隨時間改變位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when sand dunes are described as active, changing and almost creature-like.","zh":"當沙丘被描述為活躍、會變化、幾乎像生物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sand dune","meaning":"沙丘","examples":[{"en":"A sand dune is not just a lifeless pile of sand.","zh":"沙丘不只是一堆毫無生命的沙。"},{"en":"A sand dune is a hill or ridge of sand formed by wind.","zh":"sand dune 指由風形成的沙山或沙脊。"},{"en":"Children may see a sand dune on a beach and climb up its steep side.","zh":"孩子可能在海灘看見沙丘，然後爬上它陡峭的一邊。"},{"en":"Sand dunes form when wind drops sand around an obstacle such as a rock or plant.","zh":"當風吹動沙粒，並在石頭或植物等障礙物附近沉積，沙丘就會形成。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing deserts, beaches and wind-shaped landforms.","zh":"討論沙漠、海灘和由風塑造的地貌時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"picture something as","meaning":"把某物想像成……","examples":[{"en":"Many people picture a sand dune as a barren pile of sand.","zh":"許多人把沙丘想像成一堆荒蕪的沙。"},{"en":"Picture something as means imagine or think of something in a particular way.","zh":"picture something as 指以某種方式想像或看待某物。"},{"en":"Some students picture exams as a disaster, even when they have prepared well.","zh":"有些學生即使準備充足，仍把考試想像成災難。"},{"en":"If people picture deserts as empty places, they may overlook the life and movement there.","zh":"如果人們把沙漠想像成空無一物的地方，他們可能忽略那裏的生命和變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing how people imagine something.","zh":"描述人們如何想像某事物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a barren pile of lifeless sand","meaning":"一堆荒蕪、毫無生氣的沙","examples":[{"en":"People often picture dunes as a barren pile of lifeless sand.","zh":"人們常把沙丘想像成一堆荒蕪、毫無生氣的沙。"},{"en":"A barren pile of lifeless sand is a dry, empty-looking mass of sand with no obvious life.","zh":"a barren pile of lifeless sand 指看起來乾燥、空洞、沒有明顯生命的一大堆沙。"},{"en":"From far away, a desert hill may look like a barren pile of lifeless sand.","zh":"從遠處看，一座沙漠小丘可能像一堆荒蕪、毫無生氣的沙。"},{"en":"This image can be misleading because dunes may move, grow and contain living creatures.","zh":"這種想像可能有誤導性，因為沙丘可能移動、生長，並藏有生物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting appearance with hidden activity.","zh":"對比外觀與隱藏活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dynamic natural structures","meaning":"動態自然結構","examples":[{"en":"Sand dunes are dynamic natural structures.","zh":"沙丘是動態自然結構。"},{"en":"Dynamic natural structures are natural forms that change, move or develop over time.","zh":"dynamic natural structures 指會隨時間改變、移動或發展的自然形態。"},{"en":"Rivers, glaciers and sand dunes are dynamic natural structures because they reshape land slowly.","zh":"河流、冰川和沙丘都是動態自然結構，因為它們會慢慢重塑土地。"},{"en":"Wind and water can make dynamic natural structures look different from year to year.","zh":"風和水可以令動態自然結構每年看起來不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when nature is active rather than fixed.","zh":"當自然不是固定不變，而是活躍變動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"grow, shift and travel","meaning":"生長、移動和遷移","examples":[{"en":"Sand dunes can grow, shift and travel.","zh":"沙丘可以生長、移動和遷移。"},{"en":"Grow, shift and travel means become larger, change position and move across land.","zh":"grow, shift and travel 指變大、改變位置並橫越土地。"},{"en":"A small dune may grow, shift and travel after months of strong wind.","zh":"經過數月強風，小沙丘可能會生長、移動和遷移。"},{"en":"Loose sand allows dunes to grow, shift and travel instead of staying in one place.","zh":"鬆散沙粒使沙丘能生長、移動和遷移，而不是停留在原地。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing gradual movement and change.","zh":"描述逐步移動和改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"crawl with living things","meaning":"佈滿爬行生物","examples":[{"en":"Some sand dunes crawl with living things.","zh":"有些沙丘佈滿爬行生物。"},{"en":"Crawl with living things means be full of small animals, insects or other life moving around.","zh":"crawl with living things 指充滿四處活動的小動物、昆蟲或其他生命。"},{"en":"A garden log may crawl with living things after rain.","zh":"雨後，花園裏的木頭可能佈滿爬行生物。"},{"en":"Even dry places can crawl with living things if small creatures have adapted to them.","zh":"即使乾燥地方，只要小生物適應了環境，也可以佈滿生命。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a place looks empty but is actually full of life.","zh":"當某地看似空曠但其實充滿生命時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"no more than","meaning":"不過是；僅僅是","examples":[{"en":"Although dunes may seem no more than wind-blown sand, they can be dangerous.","zh":"雖然沙丘可能看似不過是被風吹積的沙，但它們可以很危險。"},{"en":"No more than means only or nothing beyond that.","zh":"no more than 指只是、僅僅是，沒有更多。"},{"en":"A short message may seem no more than a few words, but it can change someone’s mood.","zh":"一則短訊息可能看似不過是幾個字，但可以改變某人的心情。"},{"en":"When people think dunes are no more than sand, they may underestimate their power.","zh":"當人們以為沙丘不過是沙，他們可能低估其力量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when correcting an overly simple view.","zh":"修正過度簡化的看法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"wind-blown sand","meaning":"被風吹積的沙","examples":[{"en":"A dune is made of wind-blown sand.","zh":"沙丘由被風吹積的沙組成。"},{"en":"Wind-blown sand is sand that has been moved, carried or piled up by wind.","zh":"wind-blown sand 指被風吹動、搬運或堆積起來的沙。"},{"en":"After a storm, wind-blown sand may cover a seaside road.","zh":"暴風後，被風吹積的沙可能覆蓋海邊道路。"},{"en":"Wind-blown sand can build dunes when it settles around rocks, plants or other obstacles.","zh":"當被風吹積的沙在石頭、植物或其他障礙物附近沉積，就能形成沙丘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how wind shapes land.","zh":"解釋風如何塑造土地時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"roll over","meaning":"輾過","examples":[{"en":"Dunes can roll over trees and buildings.","zh":"沙丘可以輾過樹木和建築物。"},{"en":"Roll over means move across and cover or crush something.","zh":"roll over 指移動並覆蓋或壓過某物。"},{"en":"A slow-moving wave of snow can roll over a mountain road after heavy snowfall.","zh":"大雪後，緩慢移動的雪浪可能輾過山路。"},{"en":"When dunes roll over objects, they may bury them under sand.","zh":"當沙丘輾過物件，它們可能把物件埋在沙下。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a large moving mass passes over something.","zh":"當大型移動物體越過某物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"march relentlessly across","meaning":"無情地不斷穿越……","examples":[{"en":"Dunes can march relentlessly across highways.","zh":"沙丘可以無情地不斷穿越公路。"},{"en":"March relentlessly across means move steadily across an area without stopping.","zh":"march relentlessly across 指不停地、穩定地橫越某地。"},{"en":"Floodwater may march relentlessly across fields during a long storm.","zh":"長時間暴風雨期間，洪水可能無情地不斷穿越農田。"},{"en":"A dune marches relentlessly when wind keeps pushing sand in the same direction.","zh":"當風持續把沙推向同一方向，沙丘就會無情地移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when movement feels slow but unstoppable.","zh":"當移動緩慢但似乎無法阻止時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"devour vehicles in their path","meaning":"吞噬路徑上的車輛","examples":[{"en":"Some dunes devour vehicles in their path.","zh":"有些沙丘會吞噬路徑上的車輛。"},{"en":"Devour vehicles in their path means completely cover or swallow vehicles that stand where the dunes move.","zh":"devour vehicles in their path 指完全覆蓋或吞沒位於沙丘移動路徑上的車輛。"},{"en":"A fast landslide can devour cars in its path if people cannot escape in time.","zh":"如果人們不能及時逃離，快速山泥傾瀉可能吞噬路徑上的汽車。"},{"en":"Dunes devour vehicles when sand keeps piling up around and over them.","zh":"當沙粒不斷在車輛周圍和上方堆積，沙丘就會吞噬車輛。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when nature is described as swallowing objects dramatically.","zh":"當自然被戲劇化地描寫成吞沒物件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"threaten crops and factories","meaning":"威脅農作物和工廠","examples":[{"en":"Dunes can threaten crops and factories in dry regions.","zh":"沙丘可以威脅乾旱地區的農作物和工廠。"},{"en":"Threaten crops and factories means create danger for farmland, food production and industrial buildings.","zh":"threaten crops and factories 指對農田、糧食生產和工業建築造成危險。"},{"en":"Flooding can threaten crops and factories if water covers fields and enters workshops.","zh":"如果洪水淹沒田地並進入工場，就可能威脅農作物和工廠。"},{"en":"Moving sand threatens crops by burying plants and threatens factories by blocking access.","zh":"移動中的沙會透過掩埋植物威脅農作物，並透過阻塞通道威脅工廠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when natural processes endanger farming and industry.","zh":"當自然過程危及農業和工業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"killer dunes","meaning":"殺手沙丘","examples":[{"en":"Killer dunes can swallow up entire towns.","zh":"殺手沙丘可以吞沒整座城鎮。"},{"en":"Killer dunes are dangerous moving dunes that can bury roads, homes or settlements.","zh":"killer dunes 指能掩埋道路、房屋或聚居地的危險移動沙丘。"},{"en":"Villagers may fear killer dunes if sand keeps moving closer to their houses each year.","zh":"如果沙每年都更接近房屋，村民可能害怕殺手沙丘。"},{"en":"Killer dunes become dangerous when wind pushes huge amounts of sand toward human areas.","zh":"當風把大量沙推向人類居住區，殺手沙丘就會變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when dunes are presented as a serious threat.","zh":"當沙丘被呈現為嚴重威脅時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"roll in","meaning":"滾滾而來","examples":[{"en":"In some places, killer dunes roll in and cover towns.","zh":"在某些地方，殺手沙丘滾滾而來並覆蓋城鎮。"},{"en":"Roll in means move into an area steadily, often in a large mass.","zh":"roll in 指大量地、穩定地移入某區域。"},{"en":"Dark clouds may roll in before a heavy storm.","zh":"暴雨前，烏雲可能滾滾而來。"},{"en":"When dunes roll in, sand slowly enters and covers places where people live or work.","zh":"當沙丘滾滾而來，沙會慢慢進入並覆蓋人們生活或工作的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something arrives gradually but powerfully.","zh":"當某物逐漸但有力地到來時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"swallow up towns","meaning":"吞沒城鎮","examples":[{"en":"Killer dunes can swallow up towns.","zh":"殺手沙丘可以吞沒城鎮。"},{"en":"Swallow up towns means cover towns so completely that buildings and streets disappear under sand.","zh":"swallow up towns 指完全覆蓋城鎮，使建築物和街道消失在沙下。"},{"en":"A huge flood can swallow up villages when water rises above rooftops.","zh":"當水位升至屋頂以上，巨大洪水可以吞沒村莊。"},{"en":"Dunes swallow up towns when sand keeps advancing faster than people can remove it.","zh":"當沙推進速度快於人們清除速度，沙丘就會吞沒城鎮。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing total coverage or destruction.","zh":"描述完全覆蓋或破壞時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"entire villages","meaning":"整條村莊","examples":[{"en":"Entire villages have disappeared under the sand.","zh":"整條村莊已消失在沙下。"},{"en":"Entire villages means whole villages, not just a few houses.","zh":"entire villages 指整條村，而不只是幾間房屋。"},{"en":"A typhoon may damage entire villages if many homes are built near the coast.","zh":"如果許多房屋建在海邊，颱風可能破壞整條村莊。"},{"en":"When entire villages are affected, the problem becomes a community disaster.","zh":"當整條村莊受影響，問題就變成社區災難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when emphasising the full scale of damage.","zh":"強調破壞的完整規模時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"disappear under the sand","meaning":"消失在沙下","examples":[{"en":"Some villages have disappeared under the sand.","zh":"有些村莊已消失在沙下。"},{"en":"Disappear under the sand means become buried until people can no longer see something.","zh":"disappear under the sand 指被沙掩埋至人們再也看不見。"},{"en":"A lost toy may disappear under the sand at the beach.","zh":"遺失的玩具可能在海灘消失在沙下。"},{"en":"Villages disappear under the sand when dunes move over them for years.","zh":"當沙丘多年來移過村莊，村莊就會消失在沙下。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when sand completely covers objects or places.","zh":"當沙完全覆蓋物件或地方時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in a few instances","meaning":"在少數情況下","examples":[{"en":"In a few instances, governments built new villages for displaced residents.","zh":"在少數情況下，政府為流離失所的居民興建新村。"},{"en":"In a few instances means in a small number of cases.","zh":"in a few instances 指在少數個案中。"},{"en":"In a few instances, students may need extra time because of illness or family problems.","zh":"在少數情況下，學生可能因疾病或家庭問題需要額外時間。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something happened, but not often.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事曾經發生，但並不常見。"},{"en":"It is useful when an example is limited rather than common.","zh":"當例子有限而非普遍時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"displaced","meaning":"流離失所的","examples":[{"en":"The government built new villages for displaced people.","zh":"政府為流離失所的人興建新村。"},{"en":"Displaced means forced to leave one’s home because of danger, disaster or conflict.","zh":"displaced 指因危險、災難或衝突而被迫離開家園。"},{"en":"Families may become displaced after a flood destroys their houses.","zh":"洪水摧毀房屋後，家庭可能變得流離失所。"},{"en":"Displaced people need housing, food, documents and support to rebuild their lives.","zh":"流離失所的人需要住房、食物、文件和支援來重建生活。"},{"en":"This word is useful when people lose their homes through forces beyond their control.","zh":"當人們因不能控制的力量失去家園時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be buried several years later","meaning":"數年後被掩埋","examples":[{"en":"The new villages were buried several years later.","zh":"這些新村數年後被掩埋。"},{"en":"Be buried several years later means become covered by sand after a number of years have passed.","zh":"be buried several years later 指經過若干年後被沙覆蓋。"},{"en":"A road built near moving dunes may be buried several years later if no barrier is built.","zh":"如果沒有建屏障，建在移動沙丘附近的道路可能數年後被掩埋。"},{"en":"This can happen when the original danger continues after people relocate.","zh":"當人們遷移後原有危險仍持續，這種情況就可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a problem returns after a delay.","zh":"當問題延遲後再次出現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"prevent something from overwhelming","meaning":"防止某物淹沒……","examples":[{"en":"Authorities try to prevent sand dunes from overwhelming cities.","zh":"當局嘗試防止沙丘淹沒城市。"},{"en":"Prevent something from overwhelming means stop it from covering, defeating or becoming too much for a place or group.","zh":"prevent something from overwhelming 指阻止某物覆蓋、擊垮或壓倒某地或某群體。"},{"en":"Extra teachers can prevent paperwork from overwhelming a small school office.","zh":"額外老師可以防止文書工作壓垮小型校務處。"},{"en":"Barriers and vegetation may prevent dunes from overwhelming roads and farmland.","zh":"屏障和植被可能防止沙丘淹沒道路和農田。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when action is needed before a force becomes uncontrollable.","zh":"當需要在某力量失控前採取行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"agricultural areas","meaning":"農業地區","examples":[{"en":"Sand dunes can threaten agricultural areas.","zh":"沙丘可以威脅農業地區。"},{"en":"Agricultural areas are places used for farming crops or raising animals.","zh":"agricultural areas 指用來種植農作物或飼養動物的地方。"},{"en":"A village may depend on nearby agricultural areas for vegetables and grain.","zh":"村莊可能依靠附近農業地區供應蔬菜和穀物。"},{"en":"If sand covers agricultural areas, farmers may lose both land and income.","zh":"如果沙覆蓋農業地區，農民可能失去土地和收入。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing farming land.","zh":"討論農地時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"become a priority","meaning":"成為優先事項","examples":[{"en":"Preventing dunes from overwhelming cities has become a priority.","zh":"防止沙丘淹沒城市已成為優先事項。"},{"en":"Become a priority means become one of the most important things that must be dealt with first.","zh":"become a priority 指成為必須優先處理的最重要事項之一。"},{"en":"If many students are falling behind, reading support may become a priority for the school.","zh":"如果許多學生落後，閱讀支援可能成為學校的優先事項。"},{"en":"A problem becomes a priority when delay would cause greater damage.","zh":"當拖延會造成更大損害，問題就會成為優先事項。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something moves to the top of an agenda.","zh":"當某事上升為首要議程時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the United Nations Environment Programme","meaning":"聯合國環境規劃署","examples":[{"en":"The United Nations Environment Programme treats dune control as a priority.","zh":"聯合國環境規劃署把沙丘控制視為優先事項。"},{"en":"The United Nations Environment Programme is a UN body that works on environmental protection and policy.","zh":"the United Nations Environment Programme 指負責環境保護和政策工作的聯合國機構。"},{"en":"Governments may follow advice from the United Nations Environment Programme on desertification.","zh":"政府可能跟隨聯合國環境規劃署關於沙漠化的建議。"},{"en":"International organisations become involved when environmental problems cross local boundaries.","zh":"當環境問題超越本地界限，國際機構就會介入。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing global environmental action.","zh":"討論全球環境行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"significant experimental measurements","meaning":"重要的實驗測量","examples":[{"en":"Bagnold made significant experimental measurements on sand movement.","zh":"Bagnold 對沙粒移動作出重要的實驗測量。"},{"en":"Significant experimental measurements are important data collected through controlled tests.","zh":"significant experimental measurements 指透過受控測試收集的重要數據。"},{"en":"A science class may take significant experimental measurements of plant growth each week.","zh":"科學課可能每週對植物生長作重要的實驗測量。"},{"en":"Measurements become significant when they help explain how a natural process works.","zh":"當測量有助解釋自然過程如何運作，它們就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research uses data from experiments.","zh":"當研究使用實驗數據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sand movement","meaning":"沙粒移動","examples":[{"en":"Bagnold studied sand movement before World War II.","zh":"Bagnold 在第二次世界大戰前研究沙粒移動。"},{"en":"Sand movement is the way sand grains are carried, dropped or shifted by wind or water.","zh":"sand movement 指沙粒被風或水搬運、沉積或移動的方式。"},{"en":"Sand movement on a beach may cover footprints within minutes.","zh":"海灘上的沙粒移動可能在幾分鐘內覆蓋腳印。"},{"en":"Understanding sand movement helps people predict where dunes may travel.","zh":"理解沙粒移動有助人們預測沙丘可能移往哪裏。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when studying how sand changes position.","zh":"研究沙粒如何改變位置時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be performed by","meaning":"由……進行","examples":[{"en":"The measurements were performed by Ralph Bagnold.","zh":"這些測量由 Ralph Bagnold 進行。"},{"en":"Be performed by means be carried out or done by a particular person or group.","zh":"be performed by 指由某特定人物或群體執行或完成。"},{"en":"The safety inspection was performed by trained engineers.","zh":"安全檢查由受訓工程師進行。"},{"en":"Knowing who performed an experiment helps readers judge its source and reliability.","zh":"知道誰進行實驗，有助讀者判斷其來源和可靠性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying who carried out an action.","zh":"識別由誰執行某行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a British engineer","meaning":"英國工程師","examples":[{"en":"Ralph Bagnold was a British engineer who worked in Egypt.","zh":"Ralph Bagnold 是一位曾在埃及工作的英國工程師。"},{"en":"A British engineer is an engineer from Britain or trained within a British context.","zh":"a British engineer 指來自英國或在英國背景下受訓的工程師。"},{"en":"A British engineer may work overseas on bridges, railways or environmental projects.","zh":"英國工程師可能在海外參與橋樑、鐵路或環境項目。"},{"en":"Engineers contribute to science when they measure physical processes carefully.","zh":"工程師仔細測量物理過程時，可以對科學作出貢獻。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying a person by profession and nationality.","zh":"以職業和國籍識別人物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prior to","meaning":"在……之前","examples":[{"en":"Bagnold worked in Egypt prior to World War II.","zh":"Bagnold 在第二次世界大戰之前曾於埃及工作。"},{"en":"Prior to means before a particular time or event.","zh":"prior to 指在某特定時間或事件之前。"},{"en":"Students should review key vocabulary prior to the reading test.","zh":"學生應在閱讀測驗之前重溫關鍵詞彙。"},{"en":"Work done prior to a crisis can later become important evidence or preparation.","zh":"危機前完成的工作，後來可能成為重要證據或準備。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in formal writing about time order.","zh":"在正式寫作中說明時間次序時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"investigate the physics of","meaning":"探究……的物理原理","examples":[{"en":"Bagnold investigated the physics of particles moved by wind.","zh":"Bagnold 探究被風吹動粒子的物理原理。"},{"en":"Investigate the physics of something means study the forces, motion and physical rules behind it.","zh":"investigate the physics of something 指研究某事物背後的力量、運動和物理規律。"},{"en":"Students can investigate the physics of a rolling ball by measuring speed and slope.","zh":"學生可以透過測量速度和斜坡來探究滾動球的物理原理。"},{"en":"Scientists investigate the physics of sand to understand why dunes form and move.","zh":"科學家探究沙的物理原理，以理解沙丘為何形成和移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when studying the physical mechanism behind a process.","zh":"研究某過程背後的物理機制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"particles moving through the atmosphere","meaning":"在大氣中移動的粒子","examples":[{"en":"He studied particles moving through the atmosphere.","zh":"他研究在大氣中移動的粒子。"},{"en":"Particles moving through the atmosphere are tiny pieces of matter carried in the air.","zh":"particles moving through the atmosphere 指在空氣中被搬運的微小物質。"},{"en":"Dust, pollen and smoke are examples of particles moving through the atmosphere.","zh":"灰塵、花粉和煙都是在大氣中移動的粒子例子。"},{"en":"Wind speed affects how far particles moving through the atmosphere can travel.","zh":"風速影響在大氣中移動的粒子能走多遠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing airborne material.","zh":"討論空氣中物質時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"deposited by wind","meaning":"被風吹沉積","examples":[{"en":"Sand particles can be deposited by wind.","zh":"沙粒可以被風吹沉積。"},{"en":"Deposited by wind means dropped or left in a place after being carried by wind.","zh":"deposited by wind 指被風搬運後落下或留在某處。"},{"en":"Leaves may be deposited by wind in a corner of a playground.","zh":"樹葉可能被風吹沉積在操場角落。"},{"en":"Sand is deposited by wind when the wind slows down near an obstacle.","zh":"當風在障礙物附近減慢，沙粒就會被風吹沉積。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how loose material collects.","zh":"解釋鬆散物質如何聚集時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"recognise two basic types","meaning":"識別兩種基本類型","examples":[{"en":"Bagnold recognised two basic types of dune.","zh":"Bagnold 識別了兩種基本沙丘類型。"},{"en":"Recognise two basic types means identify and classify something into two main categories.","zh":"recognise two basic types 指把某物識別並分類為兩個主要類別。"},{"en":"A teacher may recognise two basic types of grammar mistakes in students’ essays.","zh":"老師可能在學生作文中識別兩種基本文法錯誤。"},{"en":"Classification helps people understand a complex subject more clearly.","zh":"分類幫助人們更清楚理解複雜主題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing a simple category system.","zh":"引入簡單分類系統時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"crescentic dune","meaning":"新月形沙丘","examples":[{"en":"The crescentic dune is shaped like a crescent moon.","zh":"新月形沙丘形狀像新月。"},{"en":"A crescentic dune is a curved sand dune with pointed ends.","zh":"crescentic dune 指有彎曲形狀和尖端的沙丘。"},{"en":"From above, a crescentic dune may look like a thin moon lying on the desert floor.","zh":"從上方看，新月形沙丘可能像一彎月亮躺在沙漠地面上。"},{"en":"Crescentic dunes often form where wind blows mainly from one direction.","zh":"新月形沙丘常在風主要從一個方向吹來的地方形成。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a curved dune type.","zh":"描述彎曲沙丘類型時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"barchan","meaning":"巴爾漢沙丘","examples":[{"en":"Bagnold called the crescentic dune a barchan.","zh":"Bagnold 把新月形沙丘稱為巴爾漢沙丘。"},{"en":"A barchan is a crescent-shaped dune with two pointed arms.","zh":"barchan 指有兩個尖臂的新月形沙丘。"},{"en":"Desert researchers may measure how quickly a barchan moves across open sand.","zh":"沙漠研究人員可能量度巴爾漢沙丘在開闊沙地上移動得多快。"},{"en":"A barchan can travel when wind pushes sand over its crest and down its slip face.","zh":"當風把沙推過沙丘頂部並滑下滑落面，巴爾漢沙丘就能移動。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing technical names for dune types.","zh":"討論沙丘類型的技術名稱時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"linear dune","meaning":"線形沙丘","examples":[{"en":"The linear dune is straighter than the crescentic dune.","zh":"線形沙丘比新月形沙丘更直。"},{"en":"A linear dune is a long, narrow dune that stretches like a line.","zh":"linear dune 指像線一樣延伸的狹長沙丘。"},{"en":"On a map, a linear dune may appear as a long ridge across the desert.","zh":"在地圖上，線形沙丘可能像橫跨沙漠的長沙脊。"},{"en":"Linear dunes can become very long when winds shape them over great distances.","zh":"當風在長距離上塑造沙丘，線形沙丘可以變得非常長。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing dune shapes.","zh":"比較沙丘形狀時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"longitudinal dune","meaning":"縱向沙丘","examples":[{"en":"Bagnold also called the linear dune a longitudinal dune.","zh":"Bagnold 也把線形沙丘稱為縱向沙丘。"},{"en":"A longitudinal dune is a long dune that usually lies parallel to the main wind direction.","zh":"longitudinal dune 指通常與主要風向平行的長形沙丘。"},{"en":"Pilots flying over deserts may see longitudinal dunes running across the landscape.","zh":"飛越沙漠的機師可能看見縱向沙丘橫跨地貌。"},{"en":"These dunes form patterns when winds keep shaping sand along a long line.","zh":"當風持續沿着長線塑造沙粒，這些沙丘就形成圖案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when using the scientific name for a linear dune.","zh":"使用線形沙丘的科學名稱時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"seif","meaning":"賽夫沙丘；劍狀沙丘","examples":[{"en":"The word seif is Arabic for “sword”.","zh":"seif 這個詞在阿拉伯語中意為「劍」。"},{"en":"Seif is another name for a long, sword-like linear dune.","zh":"seif 是長而像劍的線形沙丘的另一名稱。"},{"en":"A desert guide may point to a seif stretching far across the sand.","zh":"沙漠導遊可能指向一條遠遠延伸穿過沙地的賽夫沙丘。"},{"en":"The name makes sense because the dune can look long and narrow like a blade.","zh":"這個名稱合理，因為沙丘可以看起來像刀刃般又長又窄。"},{"en":"This word is useful when learning special names for dune forms.","zh":"學習沙丘形態的特殊名稱時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"as its name suggests","meaning":"顧名思義","examples":[{"en":"As its name suggests, the crescentic dune is shaped like a crescent moon.","zh":"顧名思義，新月形沙丘形狀像新月。"},{"en":"As its name suggests means the name itself gives a clue about the meaning or appearance.","zh":"as its name suggests 指名稱本身已提示其意思或外觀。"},{"en":"As its name suggests, a touchscreen is a screen that users can touch to control.","zh":"顧名思義，觸控螢幕就是使用者可以觸摸來控制的螢幕。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers connect a term with its obvious feature.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者把術語與其明顯特徵連接起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when the name explains the thing clearly.","zh":"當名稱清楚解釋事物時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be shaped like","meaning":"形狀像……","examples":[{"en":"The dune is shaped like a crescent moon.","zh":"這個沙丘形狀像新月。"},{"en":"Be shaped like means have a form similar to something else.","zh":"be shaped like 指形狀與另一事物相似。"},{"en":"A classroom table may be shaped like a circle so students can face one another.","zh":"課室桌子可能形狀像圓形，讓學生能面向彼此。"},{"en":"Shape comparisons help people imagine something they have not seen.","zh":"形狀比較幫助人們想像未見過的事物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing appearance through familiar objects.","zh":"透過熟悉物件描述外觀時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"crescent moon","meaning":"新月","examples":[{"en":"A barchan dune is shaped like a crescent moon.","zh":"巴爾漢沙丘形狀像新月。"},{"en":"A crescent moon is the thin curved shape of the moon when only part of it is visible.","zh":"crescent moon 指月亮只有一部分可見時呈現的細彎形狀。"},{"en":"Children may draw a crescent moon beside stars in a night-sky picture.","zh":"孩子可能在夜空圖畫中，在星星旁畫一彎新月。"},{"en":"The crescent moon shape helps explain why a barchan has curved arms.","zh":"新月形狀有助解釋為何巴爾漢沙丘有彎曲的兩臂。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing curved shapes.","zh":"描述彎曲形狀時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"points at each end","meaning":"兩端呈尖角","examples":[{"en":"The crescentic dune has points at each end.","zh":"新月形沙丘兩端呈尖角。"},{"en":"Points at each end are sharp or narrow tips on both sides of a shape.","zh":"points at each end 指形狀兩側有尖細或狹窄的端點。"},{"en":"A leaf may have points at each end if it is long and narrow.","zh":"如果葉子又長又窄，它可能兩端呈尖角。"},{"en":"These pointed ends help make the dune look like a crescent.","zh":"這些尖端使沙丘看起來像新月。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the ends of a curved shape.","zh":"描述彎曲形狀的兩端時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"wider than it is long","meaning":"寬度大於長度","examples":[{"en":"A barchan dune is usually wider than it is long.","zh":"巴爾漢沙丘通常寬度大於長度。"},{"en":"Wider than it is long means the width is greater than the length.","zh":"wider than it is long 指寬度比長度更大。"},{"en":"A short classroom table may be wider than it is long if it is designed for group work.","zh":"如果短課室桌子是為小組工作設計，它可能寬度大於長度。"},{"en":"This shape helps distinguish a barchan from a long linear dune.","zh":"這種形狀幫助區分巴爾漢沙丘和長形線形沙丘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing dimensions.","zh":"比較尺寸時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"desert surfaces","meaning":"沙漠表面","examples":[{"en":"Some barchan dunes move quickly over desert surfaces.","zh":"有些巴爾漢沙丘會快速移過沙漠表面。"},{"en":"Desert surfaces are the exposed ground areas in deserts, often covered with sand, rock or dry soil.","zh":"desert surfaces 指沙漠中外露的地面，常覆蓋沙、岩石或乾土。"},{"en":"Tyre tracks can remain visible on desert surfaces until wind covers them.","zh":"車胎痕可能留在沙漠表面，直到風把它們覆蓋。"},{"en":"Smooth desert surfaces allow some dunes to travel more easily.","zh":"平滑沙漠表面讓某些沙丘更容易移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing land conditions in deserts.","zh":"討論沙漠地面情況時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"prominent feature","meaning":"突出特徵","examples":[{"en":"Ridges are the prominent feature of linear dunes.","zh":"沙脊是線形沙丘的突出特徵。"},{"en":"A prominent feature is the most noticeable or important part of something.","zh":"prominent feature 指某物最明顯或最重要的部分。"},{"en":"Large windows are a prominent feature of the new school library.","zh":"大窗戶是新學校圖書館的突出特徵。"},{"en":"Prominent features help people recognise and classify objects quickly.","zh":"突出特徵幫助人們快速識別和分類物件。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying what stands out most.","zh":"識別最突出的地方時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"unlike","meaning":"與……不同","examples":[{"en":"Unlike crescentic dunes, linear dunes are longer than they are wide.","zh":"與新月形沙丘不同，線形沙丘長度大於寬度。"},{"en":"Unlike means different from or in contrast to.","zh":"unlike 指不同於，或與……形成對比。"},{"en":"Unlike buses, trains usually run on fixed tracks.","zh":"與巴士不同，火車通常在固定軌道上行駛。"},{"en":"This word helps readers compare two things clearly.","zh":"這個詞幫助讀者清楚比較兩件事。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing an important difference.","zh":"顯示重要差異時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"more than 100 miles long","meaning":"長逾一百英里","examples":[{"en":"Some linear dunes are more than 100 miles long.","zh":"有些線形沙丘長逾一百英里。"},{"en":"More than 100 miles long means longer than 100 miles from one end to the other.","zh":"more than 100 miles long 指從一端到另一端長度超過一百英里。"},{"en":"A railway line more than 100 miles long can connect several towns.","zh":"一條長逾一百英里的鐵路可以連接幾個城鎮。"},{"en":"This length shows that some dunes are not small hills but huge landforms.","zh":"這個長度顯示有些沙丘不是小山，而是巨大的地貌。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when emphasising great distance.","zh":"強調很長距離時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be composed of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"Complex dunes are composed of smaller dunes of different types.","zh":"複合沙丘由不同類型的小沙丘組成。"},{"en":"Be composed of means be made up of several parts or materials.","zh":"be composed of 指由幾個部分或材料組成。"},{"en":"A balanced meal may be composed of rice, vegetables, meat and soup.","zh":"均衡一餐可能由米飯、蔬菜、肉類和湯組成。"},{"en":"Understanding what something is composed of helps people understand how it works.","zh":"理解某物由甚麼組成，有助人們理解它如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing structure or ingredients.","zh":"描述結構或成分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"complex dunes","meaning":"複合沙丘","examples":[{"en":"Dunes composed of smaller dunes are called complex dunes.","zh":"由較小沙丘組成的沙丘稱為複合沙丘。"},{"en":"Complex dunes are dunes made up of several smaller dunes or mixed dune types.","zh":"complex dunes 指由幾個較小沙丘或混合沙丘類型組成的沙丘。"},{"en":"A desert landscape may contain complex dunes that look confusing from the ground.","zh":"沙漠地貌可能包含從地面看很複雜的複合沙丘。"},{"en":"Complex dunes form when wind patterns and sand supplies create overlapping shapes.","zh":"當風的模式和沙源形成重疊形狀，複合沙丘就會形成。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when dunes have more than one simple form.","zh":"當沙丘有多於一種簡單形態時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"complicated dynamics","meaning":"複雜動態","examples":[{"en":"Dune formation involves complicated dynamics.","zh":"沙丘形成涉及複雜動態。"},{"en":"Complicated dynamics are complex interactions of forces, movement and change.","zh":"complicated dynamics 指力量、運動和變化之間的複雜互動。"},{"en":"Traffic flow has complicated dynamics because drivers, lights and road design affect one another.","zh":"交通流量有複雜動態，因為司機、交通燈和道路設計互相影響。"},{"en":"Dune dynamics are complicated because wind, sand size, slope and obstacles all interact.","zh":"沙丘動態很複雜，因為風、沙粒大小、坡度和障礙物全部互相作用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a process changes through many connected factors.","zh":"當過程透過許多相連因素改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dune formation","meaning":"沙丘形成","examples":[{"en":"Bagnold studied the dynamics of dune formation.","zh":"Bagnold 研究沙丘形成的動態。"},{"en":"Dune formation is the process by which sand dunes are created and shaped.","zh":"dune formation 指沙丘被創造和塑造的過程。"},{"en":"Students can model dune formation by blowing sand around a small stone in a tray.","zh":"學生可以在托盤中向小石頭周圍吹沙，模擬沙丘形成。"},{"en":"Dune formation happens when wind moves sand and drops it where it loses speed.","zh":"當風移動沙粒，並在失速位置把沙沉積，沙丘形成就會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how dunes begin and develop.","zh":"解釋沙丘如何開始和發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"generally need something to form","meaning":"一般需要某物才會形成","examples":[{"en":"A sand dune generally needs three things to form.","zh":"沙丘一般需要三樣東西才會形成。"},{"en":"Generally need something to form means usually require certain conditions before it can be created.","zh":"generally need something to form 指通常需要某些條件才可以形成。"},{"en":"A club generally needs members, a purpose and a meeting place to form.","zh":"學會一般需要會員、目的和聚會地點才會成立。"},{"en":"Dunes cannot form everywhere because they need sand, wind and a place for sand to settle.","zh":"沙丘不能在任何地方形成，因為它們需要沙、風和讓沙沉積的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining necessary conditions.","zh":"解釋必要條件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a large amount of loose sand","meaning":"大量鬆散沙粒","examples":[{"en":"A dune needs a large amount of loose sand.","zh":"沙丘需要大量鬆散沙粒。"},{"en":"A large amount of loose sand means many sand grains that are not fixed by plants, water or hard ground.","zh":"a large amount of loose sand 指大量未被植物、水或硬地固定的沙粒。"},{"en":"A dry riverbed may contain a large amount of loose sand after water disappears.","zh":"水消失後，乾河床可能含有大量鬆散沙粒。"},{"en":"Loose sand is needed because wind cannot build a dune from sand that is stuck firmly in place.","zh":"鬆散沙粒是必要的，因為風不能用牢牢固定的沙建成沙丘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the material needed for dune formation.","zh":"解釋沙丘形成所需材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"little vegetation","meaning":"植被稀少","examples":[{"en":"Dunes often form in areas with little vegetation.","zh":"沙丘常在植被稀少的地區形成。"},{"en":"Little vegetation means few plants growing in an area.","zh":"little vegetation 指某地區生長的植物很少。"},{"en":"A dry hillside with little vegetation may lose soil more easily in heavy rain.","zh":"植被稀少的乾山坡在大雨中可能更容易流失泥土。"},{"en":"Little vegetation allows wind to move sand because plant roots are not holding it down.","zh":"植被稀少使風能移動沙粒，因為沒有植物根部固定沙。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when plant cover is low.","zh":"當植物覆蓋少時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a dried-up river","meaning":"乾涸的河流","examples":[{"en":"Loose sand may collect in a dried-up river.","zh":"鬆散沙粒可能聚集在乾涸的河流中。"},{"en":"A dried-up river is a riverbed where the water has disappeared.","zh":"dried-up river 指水已消失的河床。"},{"en":"Children may walk across a dried-up river during a long dry season.","zh":"在漫長旱季中，孩子可能步行穿過乾涸的河流。"},{"en":"A dried-up river can supply loose sand because flowing water once carried sediment there.","zh":"乾涸的河流可以提供鬆散沙粒，因為流水曾把沉積物帶到那裏。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing dry former waterways.","zh":"討論乾涸舊水道時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lake or seabed","meaning":"湖床或海床","examples":[{"en":"Dunes may form in a dried-up lake or seabed.","zh":"沙丘可能在乾涸的湖床或海床形成。"},{"en":"A lake or seabed is the ground at the bottom of a lake or sea, even after water has disappeared.","zh":"lake or seabed 指湖或海底部的地面，即使水已消失也可如此稱呼。"},{"en":"A dried lakebed can become a dusty plain when the climate becomes very dry.","zh":"當氣候變得很乾，乾涸湖床可能變成多塵平原。"},{"en":"These beds may provide fine sand for wind to move and shape into dunes.","zh":"這些底床可能提供細沙，讓風移動並塑造成沙丘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining where sand sources may come from.","zh":"解釋沙源可能來自哪裏時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a wind or breeze","meaning":"風或微風","examples":[{"en":"A wind or breeze is needed to move the grains of sand.","zh":"需要風或微風來移動沙粒。"},{"en":"A wind or breeze is moving air, either strong or gentle.","zh":"a wind or breeze 指流動的空氣，可以強或弱。"},{"en":"A light breeze can move dry leaves across a playground.","zh":"輕微微風可以把乾葉吹過操場。"},{"en":"Without wind or breeze, loose sand would not travel far enough to build dunes.","zh":"沒有風或微風，鬆散沙粒就不能移動得足夠遠以形成沙丘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining what provides movement.","zh":"解釋甚麼提供移動力量時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"grains of sand","meaning":"沙粒","examples":[{"en":"Wind moves the grains of sand.","zh":"風移動沙粒。"},{"en":"Grains of sand are tiny individual pieces of sand.","zh":"grains of sand 指一粒粒細小的沙。"},{"en":"A child may feel grains of sand stuck between their toes after leaving the beach.","zh":"孩子離開海灘後，可能感到腳趾之間黏着沙粒。"},{"en":"The size and weight of grains of sand affect how easily wind can move them.","zh":"沙粒的大小和重量影響風能多容易移動它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when focusing on the small pieces that make up sand.","zh":"聚焦組成沙的細小單位時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lose momentum","meaning":"失去動量；失去動力","examples":[{"en":"An obstacle causes the sand to lose momentum.","zh":"障礙物令沙失去動量。"},{"en":"Lose momentum means slow down or lose the force that keeps something moving.","zh":"lose momentum 指減速或失去使某物繼續移動的力量。"},{"en":"A rolling ball may lose momentum when it reaches thick grass.","zh":"滾動的球到達厚草地時可能失去動量。"},{"en":"Sand loses momentum when wind slows near an obstacle, so the grains settle.","zh":"當風在障礙物附近減慢，沙就失去動量，因此沙粒沉積。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when movement becomes weaker.","zh":"當移動力量變弱時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"settle","meaning":"沉積下來","examples":[{"en":"The sand loses momentum and settles.","zh":"沙失去動量並沉積下來。"},{"en":"Settle means stop moving and come to rest in a place.","zh":"settle 指停止移動並停留在某處。"},{"en":"Dust may settle on a desk if the room is not cleaned for several days.","zh":"如果房間幾天沒有清潔，灰塵可能沉積在書桌上。"},{"en":"Sand settles when the wind can no longer carry it forward.","zh":"當風不能再把沙向前搬運，沙就會沉積下來。"},{"en":"This word is useful when particles stop moving and collect somewhere.","zh":"當粒子停止移動並聚集在某處時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"variables merge","meaning":"各項變數匯合","examples":[{"en":"Where these three variables merge, a sand dune forms.","zh":"當這三項變數匯合，沙丘就會形成。"},{"en":"Variables merge means several factors come together in the same place or situation.","zh":"variables merge 指幾個因素在同一地方或情況中結合。"},{"en":"A good lesson happens when clear explanation, practice and feedback merge.","zh":"當清楚解釋、練習和回饋匯合，好課堂就會出現。"},{"en":"A dune forms when sand, wind and an obstacle merge in the right conditions.","zh":"當沙、風和障礙物在合適條件下匯合，沙丘就會形成。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when several causes combine to produce a result.","zh":"當幾個原因結合產生結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pick up the sand","meaning":"捲起沙粒","examples":[{"en":"The wind picks up the sand and moves it forward.","zh":"風捲起沙粒並把它向前移動。"},{"en":"Pick up the sand means lift sand grains from the ground and carry them.","zh":"pick up the sand 指把沙粒從地面提起並搬運。"},{"en":"A strong breeze may pick up sand from a beach and blow it onto towels.","zh":"強微風可能從海灘捲起沙粒並吹到毛巾上。"},{"en":"Wind picks up sand more easily when the grains are dry and loose.","zh":"當沙粒乾燥而鬆散，風更容易捲起沙粒。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how sand begins to move.","zh":"解釋沙如何開始移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"above the ground","meaning":"離地面","examples":[{"en":"The sand usually travels only an inch or two above the ground.","zh":"沙通常只在離地面一兩吋的位置移動。"},{"en":"Above the ground means higher than the surface of the land or floor.","zh":"above the ground 指高於土地或地板表面。"},{"en":"A low fence may stand only a few centimetres above the ground.","zh":"低矮圍欄可能只高於地面幾厘米。"},{"en":"Sand travels close to the ground because most grains are too heavy to stay high in the air.","zh":"沙粒靠近地面移動，因為大多數沙粒太重，不能長時間留在高空。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing height or position.","zh":"描述高度或位置時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cause something to stop","meaning":"令某物停下來","examples":[{"en":"An obstacle causes the moving sand to stop.","zh":"障礙物令移動中的沙停下來。"},{"en":"Cause something to stop means make something end its movement or activity.","zh":"cause something to stop 指使某物停止移動或活動。"},{"en":"A red traffic light causes cars to stop at a junction.","zh":"紅色交通燈令汽車在路口停下來。"},{"en":"Obstacles cause sand to stop by reducing wind speed and movement.","zh":"障礙物透過降低風速和移動力量令沙停下來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why motion ends.","zh":"解釋為何運動停止時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the heaviest grains","meaning":"最重的沙粒","examples":[{"en":"The heaviest grains settle against the obstacle.","zh":"最重的沙粒沉積在障礙物旁。"},{"en":"The heaviest grains are the sand particles with the greatest weight.","zh":"the heaviest grains 指重量最大的沙粒。"},{"en":"In a jar of mixed seeds, the heaviest grains may fall to the bottom first.","zh":"在混合種子的瓶中，最重的顆粒可能先落到底部。"},{"en":"Heavier grains settle sooner because wind has less power to carry them forward.","zh":"較重沙粒較早沉積，因為風較難把它們向前搬運。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing particles by weight.","zh":"按重量比較粒子時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"settle against","meaning":"沉積在……旁","examples":[{"en":"The heaviest grains settle against the obstacle.","zh":"最重的沙粒沉積在障礙物旁。"},{"en":"Settle against means come to rest beside or touching something.","zh":"settle against 指停留在某物旁邊或貼着某物。"},{"en":"Fallen leaves may settle against a garden wall after a windy day.","zh":"大風天後，落葉可能沉積在花園牆邊。"},{"en":"Sand settles against obstacles because wind slows there.","zh":"沙會沉積在障礙物旁，因為風在那裏減慢。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when loose material collects beside something.","zh":"當鬆散物質聚集在某物旁時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a small ridge or bump","meaning":"小沙脊或隆起","examples":[{"en":"A small ridge or bump forms near the obstacle.","zh":"一條小沙脊或隆起在障礙物附近形成。"},{"en":"A small ridge or bump is a low raised line or mound on a surface.","zh":"small ridge or bump 指表面上的低矮凸起線條或小丘。"},{"en":"A small ridge of soil may form beside a garden path after rain.","zh":"雨後，花園小徑旁可能形成一條小泥脊。"},{"en":"A small ridge or bump can become the starting point of a larger dune.","zh":"小沙脊或隆起可以成為較大沙丘的起點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the first raised shape in a surface.","zh":"描述表面最初出現的凸起形狀時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the lighter grains","meaning":"較輕的沙粒","examples":[{"en":"The lighter grains are deposited on the other side of the obstacle.","zh":"較輕的沙粒沉積在障礙物另一邊。"},{"en":"The lighter grains are sand particles with less weight.","zh":"the lighter grains 指重量較小的沙粒。"},{"en":"When children shake a box of mixed grains, the lighter grains may stay near the top.","zh":"孩子搖晃一盒混合穀粒時，較輕的顆粒可能留在較上層。"},{"en":"Lighter grains can travel farther because wind can carry them more easily.","zh":"較輕沙粒能移動更遠，因為風較容易搬運它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining particle movement by weight.","zh":"以重量解釋粒子移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be deposited on","meaning":"沉積在……上","examples":[{"en":"The lighter grains are deposited on the other side.","zh":"較輕的沙粒沉積在另一邊。"},{"en":"Be deposited on means be dropped and left on a surface.","zh":"be deposited on 指落下並留在某表面上。"},{"en":"Dust may be deposited on windowsills when the wind blows through an open window.","zh":"當風從開着的窗吹入，灰塵可能沉積在窗台上。"},{"en":"Sand is deposited on the sheltered side when wind loses enough force.","zh":"當風失去足夠力量，沙就會沉積在背風一側。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when material settles onto a surface.","zh":"當物質沉落在表面上時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"so steep that","meaning":"陡峭到……","examples":[{"en":"The pile becomes so steep that it collapses.","zh":"沙堆變得陡峭到坍塌。"},{"en":"So steep that means steep enough to cause a particular result.","zh":"so steep that 指陡峭程度足以造成某結果。"},{"en":"The hill was so steep that the children had to walk slowly.","zh":"那座山陡峭到孩子們必須慢慢走。"},{"en":"When sand becomes so steep that gravity pulls it down, the slope collapses.","zh":"當沙堆陡峭到重力把它拉下，斜坡就會坍塌。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when degree leads to consequence.","zh":"當程度導致後果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"collapse under its own weight","meaning":"因自身重量而坍塌","examples":[{"en":"The pile collapses under its own weight.","zh":"沙堆因自身重量而坍塌。"},{"en":"Collapse under its own weight means fall down because it is too heavy or unstable to support itself.","zh":"collapse under its own weight 指因太重或太不穩而無法支撐自己，於是倒塌。"},{"en":"A wet cardboard box may collapse under its own weight when filled with books.","zh":"裝滿書的濕紙箱可能因自身重量而坍塌。"},{"en":"A sand pile collapses when its slope becomes too steep for the grains to hold.","zh":"當沙堆斜坡太陡，沙粒無法支撐，就會坍塌。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an object fails because of its own mass.","zh":"當物件因自身重量而失效時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"come to rest","meaning":"停下來","examples":[{"en":"The collapsing sand comes to rest at the right steepness.","zh":"坍塌中的沙在適當坡度停下來。"},{"en":"Come to rest means stop moving after movement or falling.","zh":"come to rest 指移動或下跌後停止。"},{"en":"A rolling pencil may come to rest at the edge of a desk.","zh":"滾動的鉛筆可能在書桌邊停下來。"},{"en":"Sand comes to rest when the slope becomes stable enough.","zh":"當斜坡變得足夠穩定，沙就會停下來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when motion gradually stops.","zh":"當動作逐漸停止時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the right steepness","meaning":"適當的坡度","examples":[{"en":"The sand reaches the right steepness to keep the dune stable.","zh":"沙達到適當的坡度，以使沙丘保持穩定。"},{"en":"The right steepness is the angle that is steep enough to form a slope but not so steep that it collapses.","zh":"right steepness 指角度足夠形成斜坡，但不至於陡峭到坍塌。"},{"en":"A wheelchair ramp needs the right steepness so users can move safely.","zh":"輪椅斜道需要適當坡度，讓使用者安全移動。"},{"en":"Sand needs the right steepness because too much slope causes sliding.","zh":"沙需要適當坡度，因為斜度太大會造成滑落。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stability depends on angle.","zh":"當穩定性取決於角度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"keep the dune stable","meaning":"使沙丘保持穩定","examples":[{"en":"The right steepness keeps the dune stable.","zh":"適當坡度使沙丘保持穩定。"},{"en":"Keep the dune stable means prevent the dune from collapsing or changing suddenly.","zh":"keep the dune stable 指防止沙丘突然坍塌或改變。"},{"en":"Plant roots can help keep a small slope stable after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，植物根部可以幫助小斜坡保持穩定。"},{"en":"A dune stays stable when its sand slope reaches a balance between gravity and friction.","zh":"當沙坡在重力和摩擦力之間達到平衡，沙丘就保持穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why a landform holds its shape.","zh":"解釋地貌為何能保持形狀時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"repeating cycle","meaning":"反覆循環","examples":[{"en":"The repeating cycle allows the dune to move forward.","zh":"反覆循環讓沙丘向前移動。"},{"en":"A repeating cycle is a process that happens again and again in the same order.","zh":"repeating cycle 指同一過程按相同次序一次又一次發生。"},{"en":"Study, practise, receive feedback and revise can become a repeating cycle for improvement.","zh":"學習、練習、得到回饋和修改可以成為進步的反覆循環。"},{"en":"Dunes move because sand climbs, collapses and settles in a repeating cycle.","zh":"沙丘會移動，是因為沙上移、坍塌和沉積形成反覆循環。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when repeated steps create gradual change.","zh":"當重複步驟造成逐步改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"inch up","meaning":"緩慢向上移動","examples":[{"en":"Sand inches up the windward side of the dune.","zh":"沙粒沿着沙丘迎風面緩慢向上移動。"},{"en":"Inch up means move upward very slowly and little by little.","zh":"inch up 指非常慢地、一點一點向上移動。"},{"en":"A nervous student may inch up the stage steps before giving a speech.","zh":"緊張的學生演講前可能緩慢走上舞台階梯。"},{"en":"Sand inches up because each gust of wind moves grains only a short distance.","zh":"沙粒緩慢向上移動，因為每陣風只把沙粒移動一小段距離。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when movement is extremely slow.","zh":"當移動極慢時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"windward side","meaning":"迎風面","examples":[{"en":"Sand moves up the windward side of the dune.","zh":"沙沿着沙丘迎風面向上移動。"},{"en":"The windward side is the side facing the direction from which the wind blows.","zh":"windward side 指面向風來方向的一面。"},{"en":"On a windy day, the windward side of a building feels colder.","zh":"在大風天，建築物的迎風面感覺較冷。"},{"en":"Sand collects and moves up the windward side before sliding down the other side.","zh":"沙會先在迎風面聚集並向上移動，然後滑下另一邊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining wind direction and surfaces.","zh":"解釋風向和表面時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dune crest","meaning":"沙丘頂部","examples":[{"en":"Sand travels up to the dune crest.","zh":"沙移動到沙丘頂部。"},{"en":"A dune crest is the highest ridge or top line of a dune.","zh":"dune crest 指沙丘最高的脊線或頂部線。"},{"en":"Hikers may stand on a dune crest to see across the desert.","zh":"遠足者可能站在沙丘頂部，眺望沙漠。"},{"en":"When sand reaches the dune crest, it may fall down the slip face.","zh":"當沙到達沙丘頂部，它可能滑下滑落面。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing parts of a dune.","zh":"描述沙丘部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"slip face","meaning":"滑落面","examples":[{"en":"Sand slips down the dune’s slip face.","zh":"沙從沙丘的滑落面滑下。"},{"en":"A slip face is the steep side of a dune where sand slides down.","zh":"slip face 指沙丘上沙向下滑落的陡峭一面。"},{"en":"The slip face may look smooth because fresh sand has recently fallen over it.","zh":"滑落面可能看起來平滑，因為新沙剛剛滑落其上。"},{"en":"Dunes move forward when sand crosses the crest and slides down the slip face.","zh":"當沙越過頂部並滑下滑落面，沙丘就會向前移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how dunes migrate.","zh":"解釋沙丘如何遷移時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"inch forward","meaning":"緩慢向前移動","examples":[{"en":"The repeating cycle allows the dune to inch forward.","zh":"反覆循環讓沙丘緩慢向前移動。"},{"en":"Inch forward means move ahead very slowly.","zh":"inch forward 指非常慢地向前移動。"},{"en":"Cars may inch forward in a traffic jam during rush hour.","zh":"繁忙時間塞車時，汽車可能緩慢向前移動。"},{"en":"A dune inches forward as sand repeatedly climbs one side and falls down the other.","zh":"當沙反覆爬上一邊並滑下另一邊，沙丘就緩慢向前移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when progress or movement is tiny but continuous.","zh":"當進展或移動細小但持續時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"migrate in the direction","meaning":"朝……方向遷移","examples":[{"en":"The dune migrates in the direction the wind blows.","zh":"沙丘朝風吹的方向遷移。"},{"en":"Migrate in the direction means move gradually toward a particular direction.","zh":"migrate in the direction 指逐漸朝某一方向移動。"},{"en":"Birds may migrate in the direction of warmer regions before winter.","zh":"冬天前，鳥類可能朝較溫暖地區的方向遷移。"},{"en":"Dunes migrate in the direction of the wind because wind carries sand forward.","zh":"沙丘朝風的方向遷移，因為風把沙向前搬運。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when gradual movement follows a force or route.","zh":"當逐漸移動跟隨某力量或路線時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"depending on","meaning":"取決於","examples":[{"en":"Dune shape changes depending on the speed and direction of the wind.","zh":"沙丘形狀會取決於風速和風向而改變。"},{"en":"Depending on means being affected or decided by another factor.","zh":"depending on 指受另一因素影響或由另一因素決定。"},{"en":"Students may walk or take the bus depending on the weather.","zh":"學生可能步行或搭巴士，取決於天氣。"},{"en":"Dunes develop differently depending on wind, sand weight and local obstacles.","zh":"沙丘會取決於風、沙粒重量和本地障礙物而不同地發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an outcome changes with conditions.","zh":"當結果隨條件而改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the speed and direction of the wind","meaning":"風速和風向","examples":[{"en":"The speed and direction of the wind affect dune shape.","zh":"風速和風向影響沙丘形狀。"},{"en":"The speed and direction of the wind means how fast the wind blows and where it blows toward.","zh":"speed and direction of the wind 指風有多快，以及吹向哪個方向。"},{"en":"Sailors check the speed and direction of the wind before leaving harbour.","zh":"水手離開港口前會檢查風速和風向。"},{"en":"Strong steady wind can build different dunes from gentle shifting wind.","zh":"強而穩定的風會形成不同於柔和多變風的沙丘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when wind conditions explain natural movement.","zh":"當風的條件解釋自然移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the weight of the local sand","meaning":"當地沙粒的重量","examples":[{"en":"The weight of the local sand affects the size of a dune.","zh":"當地沙粒的重量影響沙丘大小。"},{"en":"The weight of the local sand means how heavy the sand grains in that area are.","zh":"weight of the local sand 指該地區沙粒有多重。"},{"en":"Heavier local sand may be harder for wind to lift and move.","zh":"較重的當地沙粒可能較難被風吹起和移動。"},{"en":"Sand weight affects dune size because lighter grains can travel farther and pile differently.","zh":"沙粒重量影響沙丘大小，因為較輕沙粒可以走更遠並以不同方式堆積。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when local material properties matter.","zh":"當本地材料特性很重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"develop into","meaning":"發展成；形成","examples":[{"en":"Dunes develop into different shapes and sizes.","zh":"沙丘會發展成不同形狀和大小。"},{"en":"Develop into means gradually become a particular form, condition or result.","zh":"develop into 指逐漸變成某種形式、狀態或結果。"},{"en":"A small class discussion can develop into a full debate.","zh":"一場小型課堂討論可以發展成完整辯論。"},{"en":"Dunes develop into different forms when wind and sand conditions change.","zh":"當風和沙的條件改變，沙丘會發展成不同形態。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something changes gradually into something else.","zh":"當某物逐漸變成另一物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"different shapes and sizes","meaning":"不同形狀和大小","examples":[{"en":"Dunes develop into different shapes and sizes.","zh":"沙丘會形成不同形狀和大小。"},{"en":"Different shapes and sizes means various forms and measurements.","zh":"different shapes and sizes 指各種不同形式和尺寸。"},{"en":"School bags come in different shapes and sizes for children of different ages.","zh":"書包有不同形狀和大小，以配合不同年齡的孩子。"},{"en":"Dunes have different shapes and sizes because wind, sand and obstacles vary by place.","zh":"沙丘有不同形狀和大小，因為風、沙和障礙物因地而異。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when variety in form is important.","zh":"當形態多樣性重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stronger winds tend to","meaning":"較強的風往往會……","examples":[{"en":"Stronger winds tend to make taller dunes.","zh":"較強的風往往會形成較高的沙丘。"},{"en":"Stronger winds tend to means stronger winds usually or often cause a certain result.","zh":"stronger winds tend to 指較強的風通常或常常造成某結果。"},{"en":"Stronger winds tend to make umbrellas turn inside out.","zh":"較強的風往往會把雨傘吹反。"},{"en":"Stronger winds can carry more sand, so they tend to build higher dunes.","zh":"較強的風可以搬運更多沙，所以往往形成較高沙丘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a common tendency, not an absolute rule.","zh":"描述常見傾向而非絕對規則時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"taller dunes","meaning":"較高的沙丘","examples":[{"en":"Stronger winds tend to make taller dunes.","zh":"較強的風往往會形成較高的沙丘。"},{"en":"Taller dunes are dunes with greater height than others.","zh":"taller dunes 指高度比其他沙丘更高的沙丘。"},{"en":"Tourists may find taller dunes harder to climb than low beach dunes.","zh":"遊客可能覺得較高的沙丘比低矮海灘沙丘更難攀爬。"},{"en":"Stronger winds can pile more sand upward, creating taller dunes over time.","zh":"較強的風能把更多沙向上堆積，隨時間形成較高沙丘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing dune height.","zh":"比較沙丘高度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"gentler winds","meaning":"較柔和的風","examples":[{"en":"Gentler winds tend to spread dunes out.","zh":"較柔和的風往往會使沙丘延展分散。"},{"en":"Gentler winds are softer, weaker winds that blow with less force.","zh":"gentler winds 指較柔和、較弱、力量較小的風。"},{"en":"Gentler winds may move leaves slowly rather than tearing branches from trees.","zh":"較柔和的風可能慢慢移動樹葉，而不是把樹枝吹斷。"},{"en":"Because gentler winds carry sand less forcefully, they may spread it across a wider area.","zh":"因為較柔和的風搬運沙粒力量較小，它們可能把沙分散到更闊範圍。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when wind is mild rather than strong.","zh":"當風較溫和而非強烈時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"spread them out","meaning":"使其分散；使其延展","examples":[{"en":"Gentler winds tend to spread dunes out.","zh":"較柔和的風往往會使沙丘分散。"},{"en":"Spread them out means make them cover a wider area instead of being concentrated in one place.","zh":"spread them out 指使它們覆蓋更闊範圍，而不是集中在一處。"},{"en":"A teacher may spread desks out so students have more room to work.","zh":"老師可能把書桌分散擺放，讓學生有更多工作空間。"},{"en":"Wind can spread dunes out when it moves sand gently across a broad surface.","zh":"當風輕柔地把沙移過廣闊表面，它可以使沙丘延展分散。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something becomes less compact and more widely distributed.","zh":"當某物變得較不集中、分布更廣時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"generally remains the same","meaning":"一般保持不變","examples":[{"en":"If the wind direction generally remains the same, dunes shift in that direction.","zh":"如果風向一般保持不變，沙丘會朝那方向移動。"},{"en":"Generally remains the same means usually stays unchanged over time.","zh":"generally remains the same 指通常隨時間保持不變。"},{"en":"If a student’s study routine generally remains the same, progress becomes easier to track.","zh":"如果學生的學習規律一般保持不變，進步較容易追蹤。"},{"en":"Dunes move predictably when the wind direction generally remains the same.","zh":"當風向一般保持不變，沙丘的移動較可預測。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stability over time affects results.","zh":"當長期穩定性影響結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"gradually shift","meaning":"逐漸移動","examples":[{"en":"Dunes gradually shift in the direction of the wind.","zh":"沙丘會朝風的方向逐漸移動。"},{"en":"Gradually shift means slowly change position over time.","zh":"gradually shift 指隨時間慢慢改變位置。"},{"en":"A family’s spending habits may gradually shift after prices rise.","zh":"價格上升後，家庭消費習慣可能逐漸轉變。"},{"en":"Dunes gradually shift because each movement of sand is small but repeated many times.","zh":"沙丘逐漸移動，因為每次沙的移動都很小，但反覆發生很多次。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when change is slow and continuous.","zh":"當變化緩慢而持續時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a curiously dynamic creature","meaning":"奇妙地充滿動態的事物","examples":[{"en":"Farouk El-Baz described a dune as a curiously dynamic creature.","zh":"Farouk El-Baz 把沙丘描述為奇妙地充滿動態的事物。"},{"en":"A curiously dynamic creature means something that seems surprisingly alive, active and changeable.","zh":"curiously dynamic creature 指某物出乎意料地像有生命般活躍和多變。"},{"en":"A busy city can feel like a curiously dynamic creature because it grows and changes every day.","zh":"繁忙城市可以像奇妙地充滿動態的事物，因為它每天都生長和改變。"},{"en":"The phrase makes dunes sound alive because they move, grow and produce new forms.","zh":"這個短語令沙丘聽起來像有生命，因為它們會移動、生長和產生新形態。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a non-living thing behaves in an active, almost living way.","zh":"當無生命事物表現得活躍、近乎有生命時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"once formed","meaning":"一旦形成","examples":[{"en":"Once formed, a dune can grow and change shape.","zh":"一旦形成，沙丘可以生長並改變形狀。"},{"en":"Once formed means after something has come into existence.","zh":"once formed 指某物出現或形成之後。"},{"en":"Once formed, a study group may meet every Friday after school.","zh":"一旦成立，學習小組可能每逢星期五放學後聚會。"},{"en":"Once a dune is formed, wind can continue shaping and moving it.","zh":"一旦沙丘形成，風可以繼續塑造和移動它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining what happens after a process begins.","zh":"解釋過程開始後會發生甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"change shape","meaning":"改變形狀","examples":[{"en":"A dune can grow, change shape and move with the wind.","zh":"沙丘可以生長、改變形狀並隨風移動。"},{"en":"Change shape means become a different form or outline.","zh":"change shape 指變成不同形態或輪廓。"},{"en":"A soft clay model can change shape when children press it.","zh":"當孩子按壓軟黏土模型，它可以改變形狀。"},{"en":"Dunes change shape when wind removes sand from one side and deposits it on another.","zh":"當風從一邊移走沙並在另一邊沉積，沙丘就會改變形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing changing form.","zh":"描述形態改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"move with the wind","meaning":"隨風移動","examples":[{"en":"A dune can move with the wind.","zh":"沙丘可以隨風移動。"},{"en":"Move with the wind means travel in the direction pushed by wind.","zh":"move with the wind 指朝風推動的方向移動。"},{"en":"A plastic bag may move with the wind across a street.","zh":"膠袋可能隨風橫過街道。"},{"en":"Dunes move with the wind because wind carries sand grains forward.","zh":"沙丘隨風移動，因為風把沙粒向前搬運。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when wind controls movement.","zh":"當風控制移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"breed new dunes","meaning":"繁衍出新沙丘","examples":[{"en":"A dune can even breed new dunes.","zh":"沙丘甚至可以繁衍出新沙丘。"},{"en":"Breed new dunes means produce smaller new dunes from or around an existing dune.","zh":"breed new dunes 指從既有沙丘或其周圍產生較小的新沙丘。"},{"en":"A successful business can breed new businesses when former workers start their own shops.","zh":"成功企業可以在前員工開設自己的店舖時孕育出新企業。"},{"en":"Dunes may breed new dunes when parts of sand break away and move downwind.","zh":"當部分沙脫離並順風移動，沙丘可能繁衍出新沙丘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when natural forms are described as reproducing.","zh":"當自然形態被描述為繁殖時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"offspring","meaning":"後代","examples":[{"en":"Some offspring are carried on the back of the mother dune.","zh":"有些後代被帶在母沙丘背上。"},{"en":"Offspring usually means children or young produced by a parent, but here it means new smaller dunes.","zh":"offspring 通常指父母產生的孩子或幼體，但這裏指新的較小沙丘。"},{"en":"A plant’s offspring may grow near the parent plant after seeds fall nearby.","zh":"種子落在附近後，植物的後代可能在母株旁生長。"},{"en":"Calling new dunes offspring makes the dune seem like a living parent.","zh":"把新沙丘稱為後代，令沙丘看起來像有生命的母體。"},{"en":"This word is useful when new forms come from an older source.","zh":"當新形態來自較舊來源時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be carried on the back of","meaning":"被帶在……背上","examples":[{"en":"Some new dunes are carried on the back of the mother dune.","zh":"有些新沙丘被帶在母沙丘背上。"},{"en":"Be carried on the back of means be located or moved on the upper surface of something larger.","zh":"be carried on the back of 指位於或被移動在較大事物的上方表面。"},{"en":"A child may be carried on the back of a parent during a hike.","zh":"遠足時，孩子可能被父母背在背上。"},{"en":"Smaller dunes can ride on larger dunes when wind moves sand across their surface.","zh":"當風把沙移過較大沙丘表面，較小沙丘可以像被帶着移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one thing is supported or transported by another.","zh":"當一物由另一物支撐或運送時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"mother dune","meaning":"母沙丘","examples":[{"en":"Some smaller dunes are carried on the back of the mother dune.","zh":"有些較小沙丘被帶在母沙丘背上。"},{"en":"A mother dune is the larger original dune from which smaller dunes seem to develop.","zh":"mother dune 指較大的原始沙丘，較小沙丘似乎從它發展而來。"},{"en":"Scientists may call a large dune a mother dune when smaller dunes form around it.","zh":"當較小沙丘在大型沙丘周圍形成，科學家可能稱大型沙丘為母沙丘。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that dunes can produce new forms like living organisms.","zh":"這個短語暗示沙丘可以像生物一樣產生新形態。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing parent-like natural structures.","zh":"描述像母體般的自然結構時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"race downwind","meaning":"順風快速移動","examples":[{"en":"Other new dunes are born and race downwind.","zh":"其他新沙丘形成後會順風快速移動。"},{"en":"Race downwind means move quickly in the same direction as the wind.","zh":"race downwind 指朝風向快速移動。"},{"en":"A paper cup may race downwind across a playground during a storm.","zh":"暴風期間，紙杯可能順風快速穿過操場。"},{"en":"Small dunes can race downwind faster than larger dunes because they contain less sand.","zh":"小沙丘可比大沙丘更快順風移動，因為它們含沙較少。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when wind-driven movement is fast.","zh":"當由風推動的移動很快時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"outpace their parents","meaning":"超越其母體","examples":[{"en":"Some new dunes outpace their parents.","zh":"有些新沙丘會超越其母體。"},{"en":"Outpace their parents means move faster than the larger dunes from which they came.","zh":"outpace their parents 指比它們源自的較大沙丘移動得更快。"},{"en":"A young athlete may outpace their parent during a family run.","zh":"年輕運動員可能在家庭跑步中超越父母。"},{"en":"Smaller dunes may outpace their parents because they need less sand movement to advance.","zh":"較小沙丘可能超越母沙丘，因為它們前進所需的沙粒移動較少。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a newer or younger thing moves ahead faster than its source.","zh":"當較新或較年輕事物比其來源前進更快時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be heard singing","meaning":"被聽見發出歌聲","examples":[{"en":"Sand dunes can be heard singing in many locations.","zh":"在許多地點都可聽見沙丘發出歌聲。"},{"en":"Be heard singing means produce a sound that people can hear, like a musical or humming noise.","zh":"be heard singing 指發出人們能聽見、像音樂或嗡鳴的聲音。"},{"en":"Pipes in an old building may be heard singing when strong wind passes through them.","zh":"強風吹過舊建築的管道時，可能聽見管道像在唱歌。"},{"en":"Dunes can be heard singing when moving sand grains vibrate together.","zh":"當移動沙粒一起振動，就可能聽見沙丘發出歌聲。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a non-living thing produces a strange sound.","zh":"當無生命物體發出奇怪聲音時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"locations worldwide","meaning":"全球各地點","examples":[{"en":"Singing dunes exist in more than 30 locations worldwide.","zh":"會發聲的沙丘存在於全球三十多個地點。"},{"en":"Locations worldwide means places in many different parts of the world.","zh":"locations worldwide 指世界許多不同地方的地點。"},{"en":"A popular coffee chain may have shops in thousands of locations worldwide.","zh":"受歡迎咖啡連鎖店可能在全球數千個地點有分店。"},{"en":"Finding the same phenomenon in locations worldwide shows it is not a local accident.","zh":"在全球各地點發現同一現象，顯示它不是本地偶然事件。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something appears across the globe.","zh":"當某事物出現在全球不同地方時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"characteristic frequency","meaning":"特有頻率","examples":[{"en":"Each singing dune has its own characteristic frequency.","zh":"每個會發聲的沙丘都有自己的特有頻率。"},{"en":"A characteristic frequency is the particular sound frequency that something naturally produces.","zh":"characteristic frequency 指某物自然產生的特定聲音頻率。"},{"en":"A musical instrument has a characteristic frequency that helps create its recognisable tone.","zh":"樂器有特有頻率，幫助形成可辨認的音色。"},{"en":"A dune’s characteristic frequency helps explain why different dunes produce different notes.","zh":"沙丘的特有頻率有助解釋為何不同沙丘產生不同音調。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when sound is linked to physical properties.","zh":"當聲音與物理特性相關時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the thirteenth-century explorer","meaning":"十三世紀探險家","examples":[{"en":"The thirteenth-century explorer Marco Polo heard singing dunes.","zh":"十三世紀探險家馬可孛羅曾聽見會發聲的沙丘。"},{"en":"The thirteenth-century explorer means a traveller or explorer active in the 1200s.","zh":"thirteenth-century explorer 指活躍於十三世紀的旅行者或探險家。"},{"en":"A history teacher may describe Marco Polo as a thirteenth-century explorer who travelled far from Europe.","zh":"歷史老師可能把馬可孛羅描述為遠離歐洲旅行的十三世紀探險家。"},{"en":"Mentioning an old explorer shows that singing dunes have fascinated people for centuries.","zh":"提及古代探險家顯示會發聲的沙丘幾個世紀以來一直令人着迷。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying historical figures by time period and role.","zh":"以時代和角色識別歷史人物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"encounter noises","meaning":"遇到聲音","examples":[{"en":"Marco Polo encountered strange noises made by desert sand dunes.","zh":"馬可孛羅遇到由沙漠沙丘發出的奇怪聲音。"},{"en":"Encounter noises means hear or come across sounds, especially unexpected ones.","zh":"encounter noises 指聽見或遇上聲音，尤其是意想不到的聲音。"},{"en":"Campers may encounter noises at night when animals move near their tents.","zh":"露營者夜晚可能因動物在帳篷附近活動而遇到聲音。"},{"en":"Unexpected noises can make people search for explanations, especially in unfamiliar places.","zh":"意外聲音會令人尋找解釋，尤其在陌生地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone experiences strange sounds.","zh":"當某人經歷奇怪聲音時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"weird and wonderful noises","meaning":"奇異而奇妙的聲音","examples":[{"en":"Marco Polo heard weird and wonderful noises from desert dunes.","zh":"馬可孛羅從沙漠沙丘聽到奇異而奇妙的聲音。"},{"en":"Weird and wonderful noises are strange but fascinating sounds.","zh":"weird and wonderful noises 指奇怪但令人着迷的聲音。"},{"en":"Children may hear weird and wonderful noises when they visit a science museum.","zh":"孩子參觀科學博物館時，可能聽到奇異而奇妙的聲音。"},{"en":"Such noises attract attention because they feel both mysterious and interesting.","zh":"這類聲音吸引注意，因為它們既神秘又有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when sounds are unusual in an exciting way.","zh":"當聲音以令人興奮的方式不尋常時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"attribute something to","meaning":"把某事歸因於……","examples":[{"en":"Marco Polo attributed the noises to evil spirits.","zh":"馬可孛羅把那些聲音歸因於惡靈。"},{"en":"Attribute something to means say that something is caused by a particular source or reason.","zh":"attribute something to 指認為某事由某特定來源或原因造成。"},{"en":"A teacher may attribute a student’s tiredness to lack of sleep.","zh":"老師可能把學生疲倦歸因於睡眠不足。"},{"en":"People often attribute strange events to supernatural causes when they lack scientific explanations.","zh":"當人們缺乏科學解釋，常把奇怪事件歸因於超自然原因。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining what someone thinks caused something.","zh":"解釋某人認為某事由甚麼造成時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"evil spirits","meaning":"惡靈","examples":[{"en":"Marco Polo thought the noises came from evil spirits.","zh":"馬可孛羅認為那些聲音來自惡靈。"},{"en":"Evil spirits are supernatural beings believed to cause fear, harm or misfortune.","zh":"evil spirits 指被認為會造成恐懼、傷害或不幸的超自然存在。"},{"en":"In old stories, villagers may blame illness or strange sounds on evil spirits.","zh":"在古老故事中，村民可能把疾病或奇怪聲音歸咎於惡靈。"},{"en":"Belief in evil spirits can arise when people cannot explain frightening natural events.","zh":"當人們無法解釋可怕自然事件，惡靈信念可能產生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing superstition or old beliefs.","zh":"討論迷信或古老信念時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"unearthly","meaning":"不似人間的；超自然般的","examples":[{"en":"The sound of singing dunes is unearthly.","zh":"會發聲沙丘的聲音不似人間。"},{"en":"Unearthly means strange, mysterious and not like ordinary sounds or experiences on Earth.","zh":"unearthly 指奇怪、神秘，且不像地球上普通聲音或經驗。"},{"en":"A lonely wind through an empty tunnel can sound unearthly at night.","zh":"夜晚穿過空隧道的孤風，可能聽起來不似人間。"},{"en":"A sound feels unearthly when people cannot see where it comes from.","zh":"當人們看不到聲音來源，聲音就可能感覺超自然。"},{"en":"This word is useful when something feels supernatural or beyond normal life.","zh":"當某物感覺超自然或超出正常生活時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"unnerving","meaning":"令人不安的","examples":[{"en":"The volume of the sound is unnerving.","zh":"那聲音的音量令人不安。"},{"en":"Unnerving means making someone feel anxious, frightened or uncomfortable.","zh":"unnerving 指令人感到焦慮、害怕或不舒服。"},{"en":"A sudden alarm in a quiet library can be unnerving.","zh":"安靜圖書館中突然響起的警鐘可能令人不安。"},{"en":"Loud mysterious dune sounds are unnerving because listeners cannot easily locate the source.","zh":"神秘而響亮的沙丘聲令人不安，因為聽者難以確定來源。"},{"en":"This word is useful when something creates unease.","zh":"當某物造成不安時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"otherworldliness","meaning":"超現實感；異世界感","examples":[{"en":"The tone’s otherworldliness makes the sound more mysterious.","zh":"那音調的異世界感使聲音更神秘。"},{"en":"Otherworldliness is the quality of seeming to come from another world or reality.","zh":"otherworldliness 指某物似乎來自另一個世界或現實的特質。"},{"en":"A misty forest at dawn may have a sense of otherworldliness.","zh":"黎明時霧氣籠罩的森林可能帶有超現實感。"},{"en":"The otherworldliness of singing dunes comes from their strange tone and hidden source.","zh":"會發聲沙丘的異世界感來自其奇怪音調和隱藏來源。"},{"en":"This word is useful when describing a mysterious atmosphere.","zh":"描述神秘氣氛時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the inability to","meaning":"無法……","examples":[{"en":"The inability to localise the source adds to the mystery.","zh":"無法確定來源增加了神秘感。"},{"en":"The inability to do something means not being able to do it.","zh":"inability to do something 指不能做某事。"},{"en":"A student’s inability to concentrate may come from tiredness rather than laziness.","zh":"學生無法集中精神可能源於疲倦，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"The inability to find a sound’s source can make the sound feel frightening.","zh":"無法找出聲音來源會令聲音感覺可怕。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when lack of ability creates a problem.","zh":"當缺乏能力造成問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"localise the source of","meaning":"確定……的來源位置","examples":[{"en":"The human ear cannot easily localise the source of the noise.","zh":"人耳不容易確定噪音的來源位置。"},{"en":"Localise the source of means identify exactly where something comes from.","zh":"localise the source of 指準確識別某物來自哪裏。"},{"en":"A mechanic tries to localise the source of a strange sound in a car engine.","zh":"機械師會嘗試確定汽車引擎中奇怪聲音的來源位置。"},{"en":"If people cannot localise the source of a sound, they may feel confused or alarmed.","zh":"如果人們無法確定聲音來源，他們可能感到困惑或驚慌。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when finding the exact origin of something.","zh":"尋找某事物的確切來源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"research agency","meaning":"研究機構","examples":[{"en":"CNRS is a French national research agency.","zh":"CNRS 是法國國家研究機構。"},{"en":"A research agency is an organisation that supports, funds or carries out scientific studies.","zh":"research agency 指支援、資助或進行科學研究的組織。"},{"en":"A public health research agency may study how diseases spread in cities.","zh":"公共衛生研究機構可能研究疾病如何在城市中傳播。"},{"en":"Research agencies help gather evidence that individuals could not collect alone.","zh":"研究機構幫助收集個人無法獨自收集的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing organisations behind scientific work.","zh":"討論科學工作背後的機構時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"colleagues","meaning":"同事；研究夥伴","examples":[{"en":"Douady and his colleagues studied dunes in several countries.","zh":"Douady 和他的同事在幾個國家研究沙丘。"},{"en":"Colleagues are people who work with you, usually in the same organisation or field.","zh":"colleagues 指與你一起工作的人，通常在同一機構或領域。"},{"en":"A teacher may discuss lesson plans with colleagues after school.","zh":"老師可能放學後與同事討論教案。"},{"en":"Colleagues can combine skills and evidence to solve difficult research problems.","zh":"同事可以結合技能和證據來解決困難研究問題。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing teamwork in professional settings.","zh":"討論專業環境中的團隊合作時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"delve deeper into","meaning":"深入研究","examples":[{"en":"Douady has been delving deeper into the mystery of singing dunes.","zh":"Douady 一直深入研究會發聲沙丘的奧秘。"},{"en":"Delve deeper into means study or investigate something more thoroughly.","zh":"delve deeper into 指更徹底地研究或探究某事。"},{"en":"Students may delve deeper into a poem after first understanding its basic meaning.","zh":"學生初步理解詩意後，可能深入研究詩作。"},{"en":"Researchers delve deeper when simple explanations are not enough.","zh":"當簡單解釋不足夠，研究人員就會深入研究。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when investigation becomes more detailed.","zh":"當調查變得更詳細時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the exact mechanism behind","meaning":"……背後的確切機制","examples":[{"en":"Researchers want to explain the exact mechanism behind the sound.","zh":"研究人員想解釋聲音背後的確切機制。"},{"en":"The exact mechanism behind something is the precise process that causes it to happen.","zh":"exact mechanism behind something 指造成某事發生的精確過程。"},{"en":"Doctors try to understand the exact mechanism behind a new disease symptom.","zh":"醫生嘗試理解新疾病症狀背後的確切機制。"},{"en":"Knowing the mechanism behind dune sounds helps scientists move beyond superstition.","zh":"了解沙丘聲音背後的機制，幫助科學家超越迷信。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how something really works.","zh":"解釋某事真正如何運作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"acoustic phenomenon","meaning":"聲學現象","examples":[{"en":"Singing dunes are an acoustic phenomenon.","zh":"會發聲沙丘是一種聲學現象。"},{"en":"An acoustic phenomenon is an event or effect related to sound.","zh":"acoustic phenomenon 指與聲音有關的事件或效果。"},{"en":"An echo in a tunnel is a simple acoustic phenomenon.","zh":"隧道中的回音是一種簡單的聲學現象。"},{"en":"Singing dunes are acoustic because their mystery depends on how sound is produced and heard.","zh":"會發聲沙丘屬於聲學現象，因為其奧秘取決於聲音如何產生和被聽見。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing scientific explanations of sound.","zh":"討論聲音的科學解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"haul something back to","meaning":"把某物運回……","examples":[{"en":"The group hauled sand back to the laboratory.","zh":"團隊把沙運回實驗室。"},{"en":"Haul something back to means carry or transport something, often heavy, back to a place.","zh":"haul something back to 指把某物，通常是重物，搬運回某地。"},{"en":"Students may haul sports equipment back to the storeroom after PE lessons.","zh":"體育課後，學生可能把運動器材運回儲物室。"},{"en":"Researchers hauled sand back so they could test it under controlled conditions.","zh":"研究人員把沙運回去，以便在受控條件下測試。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when moving material for study or work.","zh":"為研究或工作搬運材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the laboratory","meaning":"實驗室","examples":[{"en":"The researchers tested singing sand in the laboratory.","zh":"研究人員在實驗室測試會發聲的沙。"},{"en":"The laboratory is a place where scientific experiments and tests are carried out.","zh":"laboratory 指進行科學實驗和測試的地方。"},{"en":"Students wear goggles in the laboratory when handling chemicals.","zh":"學生在實驗室處理化學品時會戴護目鏡。"},{"en":"The laboratory allows researchers to control conditions more carefully than in the desert.","zh":"實驗室讓研究人員比在沙漠中更仔細控制條件。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing scientific testing.","zh":"討論科學測試時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"set something up in channels","meaning":"把某物放置在槽道中","examples":[{"en":"The researchers set the sand up in channels.","zh":"研究人員把沙放置在槽道中。"},{"en":"Set something up in channels means arrange material inside long narrow paths or containers for testing.","zh":"set something up in channels 指把材料安排在狹長通道或容器中作測試。"},{"en":"A science teacher may set water up in channels to show how rivers erode soil.","zh":"科學老師可能把水放在槽道中，以展示河流如何侵蝕泥土。"},{"en":"Channels help researchers control how sand moves during the experiment.","zh":"槽道幫助研究人員控制實驗中沙如何移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when material is arranged in a test structure.","zh":"當材料被安排在測試結構中時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"automated pushing plates","meaning":"自動推板","examples":[{"en":"The sand was tested with automated pushing plates.","zh":"沙以自動推板進行測試。"},{"en":"Automated pushing plates are machine-controlled plates that push material in a repeated way.","zh":"automated pushing plates 指由機器控制、以重複方式推動材料的板。"},{"en":"A factory may use automated pushing plates to move products along a production line.","zh":"工廠可能使用自動推板把產品沿生產線移動。"},{"en":"Automated plates help experiments because they repeat the same movement consistently.","zh":"自動推板有助實驗，因為它們能一致地重複相同動作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when machines create controlled motion in tests.","zh":"當機器在測試中創造受控運動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"prove that","meaning":"證明","examples":[{"en":"The experiment proved that the dune itself was not needed.","zh":"實驗證明沙丘本身並非必要。"},{"en":"Prove that means show with evidence that something is true.","zh":"prove that 指用證據顯示某事為真。"},{"en":"A science project can prove that plants grow faster with enough sunlight.","zh":"科學專題可以證明植物在足夠陽光下生長得更快。"},{"en":"Experiments prove claims by testing them under controlled conditions.","zh":"實驗透過在受控條件下測試聲稱來證明它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence confirms an idea.","zh":"當證據確認某想法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"act as","meaning":"充當；作為","examples":[{"en":"The dune itself was not needed to act as a resonating body.","zh":"沙丘本身並不需要充當共鳴體。"},{"en":"Act as means serve the function of something.","zh":"act as 指發揮某物的功能。"},{"en":"A large table can act as a temporary desk during a group project.","zh":"小組專題期間，大桌子可以充當臨時書桌。"},{"en":"In the experiment, sand alone could act as the sound-producing material.","zh":"在實驗中，沙本身可以作為產生聲音的材料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one thing performs the role of another.","zh":"當一物發揮另一物角色時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a resonating body","meaning":"共鳴體","examples":[{"en":"The dune was not needed as a resonating body for the sound.","zh":"沙丘並不需要作為聲音的共鳴體。"},{"en":"A resonating body is an object or structure that vibrates and helps make sound louder or fuller.","zh":"resonating body 指會振動並幫助聲音變大或更飽滿的物體或結構。"},{"en":"The wooden body of a guitar acts as a resonating body.","zh":"結他的木製琴身充當共鳴體。"},{"en":"Researchers tested whether the dune itself amplified the sound like an instrument body.","zh":"研究人員測試沙丘本身是否像樂器琴身般放大聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining sound production.","zh":"解釋聲音產生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as some researchers had theorised","meaning":"正如一些研究人員曾推測的那樣","examples":[{"en":"The dune was not necessary, as some researchers had theorised.","zh":"沙丘並非必要，這與一些研究人員曾推測的不同。"},{"en":"As some researchers had theorised means according to what some researchers had previously suggested as an explanation.","zh":"as some researchers had theorised 指根據一些研究人員先前提出的解釋。"},{"en":"The new data did not support the cause, as some researchers had theorised earlier.","zh":"新數據並不支持先前一些研究人員曾推測的成因。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a previous scientific idea is being compared with new evidence.","zh":"這個短語顯示先前科學想法正與新證據比較。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing whether a theory was right or wrong.","zh":"討論理論是否正確時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"booming sound","meaning":"低沉轟鳴聲","examples":[{"en":"Singing dunes can produce a booming sound.","zh":"會發聲沙丘可以產生低沉轟鳴聲。"},{"en":"A booming sound is a deep, loud and powerful noise.","zh":"booming sound 指低沉、響亮而有力的聲音。"},{"en":"Thunder can make a booming sound during a storm.","zh":"雷暴期間，雷聲可以發出低沉轟鳴聲。"},{"en":"Dunes produce a booming sound when many sand grains move together in rhythm.","zh":"當許多沙粒有節奏地一起移動，沙丘會產生低沉轟鳴聲。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing low, strong sounds.","zh":"描述低沉而強烈的聲音時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a small range of sizes","meaning":"尺寸範圍較小","examples":[{"en":"The grains must be of a small range of sizes.","zh":"沙粒尺寸範圍必須較小。"},{"en":"A small range of sizes means the grains are similar in size, not very mixed.","zh":"small range of sizes 指顆粒大小相近，而不是非常混雜。"},{"en":"A box of beads has a small range of sizes if most beads are nearly the same size.","zh":"如果一盒珠子大多大小相近，就有較小的尺寸範圍。"},{"en":"Similar grain sizes may help sand move together and produce a clear sound.","zh":"相似沙粒大小可能幫助沙一起移動並產生清晰聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when uniform size matters.","zh":"當大小一致性重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"alike in shape","meaning":"形狀相似","examples":[{"en":"The grains have to be alike in shape.","zh":"沙粒形狀必須相似。"},{"en":"Alike in shape means similar in form or outline.","zh":"alike in shape 指形態或輪廓相似。"},{"en":"Puzzle pieces are not alike in shape because each one must fit a different place.","zh":"拼圖塊形狀並不相似，因為每塊要配合不同位置。"},{"en":"Sand grains that are alike in shape may slide and vibrate together more evenly.","zh":"形狀相似的沙粒可能更均勻地滑動和振動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing physical form.","zh":"比較實體形態時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"well-rounded","meaning":"圓滑的","examples":[{"en":"Singing sand grains are usually well-rounded.","zh":"會發聲的沙粒通常是圓滑的。"},{"en":"Well-rounded means smooth and round rather than sharp or angular.","zh":"well-rounded 指光滑而圓，不尖銳或有棱角。"},{"en":"Pebbles on a beach often become well-rounded after waves rub them for years.","zh":"海灘上的小石經海浪多年摩擦後，常變得圓滑。"},{"en":"Well-rounded grains may move more smoothly over one another.","zh":"圓滑沙粒可能更順暢地互相滑過。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing particles shaped by rubbing or erosion.","zh":"描述受摩擦或侵蝕塑造的粒子時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"key discovery","meaning":"重要發現","examples":[{"en":"Douady’s key discovery concerned the size of the grains.","zh":"Douady 的重要發現涉及沙粒大小。"},{"en":"A key discovery is an important finding that helps explain a problem.","zh":"key discovery 指有助解釋問題的重要發現。"},{"en":"A doctor’s key discovery may explain why many patients had the same symptoms.","zh":"醫生的重要發現可能解釋為何許多病人有相同症狀。"},{"en":"Key discoveries matter because they change the direction of research.","zh":"重要發現很重要，因為它們會改變研究方向。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one finding is especially important.","zh":"當某一發現特別重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"synchronised frequency","meaning":"同步頻率","examples":[{"en":"The synchronised frequency determines the tone of the sound.","zh":"同步頻率決定聲音的音調。"},{"en":"Synchronised frequency means a shared vibration rate produced when many particles move together.","zh":"synchronised frequency 指許多粒子一起移動時產生的共同振動率。"},{"en":"A choir sounds clearer when singers keep a synchronised rhythm.","zh":"當歌手保持同步節奏，合唱聽起來更清晰。"},{"en":"Sand grains can create sound when their movements become synchronised.","zh":"當沙粒的移動變得同步，它們就能產生聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when many small movements combine into one sound.","zh":"當許多小動作結合成一種聲音時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"determine the tone of","meaning":"決定……的音調","examples":[{"en":"Grain size determines the tone of the sound.","zh":"沙粒大小決定聲音的音調。"},{"en":"Determine the tone of means decide or control how high, low or distinctive a sound is.","zh":"determine the tone of 指決定或控制聲音有多高、多低或多獨特。"},{"en":"The length of a guitar string can determine the tone of the note.","zh":"結他弦的長度可以決定音符的音調。"},{"en":"Larger sand grains may determine a lower sound, while smaller grains may create a higher one.","zh":"較大沙粒可能決定較低聲音，而較小沙粒可能產生較高聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining what controls sound quality.","zh":"解釋甚麼控制聲音質素時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the result of","meaning":"是……的結果","examples":[{"en":"The frequency is the result of the grain size.","zh":"頻率是沙粒大小的結果。"},{"en":"The result of means caused by or produced from something.","zh":"the result of 指由某事造成或產生。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may be the result of regular practice and supportive feedback.","zh":"學生的信心可能是定期練習和支持性回饋的結果。"},{"en":"The dune’s note is the result of physical features in the sand.","zh":"沙丘的音調是沙的物理特徵所造成的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining cause and effect.","zh":"解釋因果關係時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"grain size","meaning":"沙粒大小","examples":[{"en":"The tone of the sound depends on grain size.","zh":"聲音的音調取決於沙粒大小。"},{"en":"Grain size means how large or small individual grains of sand are.","zh":"grain size 指單個沙粒有多大或多小。"},{"en":"Soil with large grain size may drain water faster than fine clay soil.","zh":"沙粒較大的土壤可能比細黏土排水更快。"},{"en":"Grain size affects dune sound because different-sized grains vibrate differently.","zh":"沙粒大小影響沙丘聲音，因為不同大小的沙粒振動方式不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when particle size changes a natural process.","zh":"當粒子大小改變自然過程時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the larger…, the lower…","meaning":"越……，就越低……","examples":[{"en":"The larger the grain, the lower the key.","zh":"沙粒越大，音調就越低。"},{"en":"The larger…, the lower… shows that when one thing increases, another thing decreases.","zh":"the larger…, the lower… 顯示一件事增加時，另一件事降低。"},{"en":"The larger the class, the lower the amount of individual attention each student may receive.","zh":"班級越大，每個學生可能得到的個別關注就越少。"},{"en":"In singing sand, larger grains tend to produce lower notes.","zh":"在會發聲的沙中，較大沙粒往往產生較低音調。"},{"en":"This structure is useful when comparing two linked changes.","zh":"比較兩個相連變化時，這個結構很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lower the key","meaning":"音調越低","examples":[{"en":"The larger the grain, the lower the key.","zh":"沙粒越大，音調越低。"},{"en":"Lower the key means produce a lower musical note or pitch.","zh":"lower the key 指產生較低的音符或音高。"},{"en":"A singer may lower the key of a song if the original note is too high.","zh":"如果原本音太高，歌手可能把歌曲降調。"},{"en":"Larger grains lower the key because their vibration produces a deeper tone.","zh":"較大沙粒使音調降低，因為它們的振動產生較深聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing pitch in music or sound.","zh":"討論音樂或聲音中的音高時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"successfully predict","meaning":"成功預測","examples":[{"en":"Douady successfully predicted the notes emitted by dunes.","zh":"Douady 成功預測沙丘發出的音調。"},{"en":"Successfully predict means correctly say what will happen or what something will be before checking it.","zh":"successfully predict 指在檢查前正確說出會發生甚麼或某物會是怎樣。"},{"en":"A teacher may successfully predict which grammar point students will find difficult.","zh":"老師可能成功預測學生會覺得哪個文法點困難。"},{"en":"Scientists can successfully predict dune notes when they understand the link between grain size and sound.","zh":"當科學家理解沙粒大小和聲音之間的關係，就能成功預測沙丘音調。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a prediction is confirmed by evidence.","zh":"當預測被證據確認時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"notes emitted by","meaning":"由……發出的音調","examples":[{"en":"He predicted the notes emitted by dunes in several countries.","zh":"他預測了幾個國家沙丘發出的音調。"},{"en":"Notes emitted by means musical sounds produced by something.","zh":"notes emitted by 指由某物產生的音樂性聲音。"},{"en":"A tuner can measure the notes emitted by a violin string.","zh":"調音器可以量度小提琴弦發出的音調。"},{"en":"Dunes emit notes when moving grains vibrate together at a shared frequency.","zh":"當移動沙粒以共同頻率一起振動，沙丘就會發出音調。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something produces distinct musical sounds.","zh":"當某物產生明確音樂聲時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"simply by measuring","meaning":"只需透過測量……","examples":[{"en":"He predicted the notes simply by measuring the grains.","zh":"他只需透過測量沙粒，就預測了音調。"},{"en":"Simply by measuring means by doing only the act of measuring, without needing many other steps.","zh":"simply by measuring 指只透過測量這個動作，而不需要許多其他步驟。"},{"en":"A tailor can estimate clothing size simply by measuring a person’s shoulders and waist.","zh":"裁縫只需透過測量人的肩膀和腰圍，就能估計衣服尺寸。"},{"en":"If grain size controls sound, scientists can predict tone simply by measuring grains.","zh":"如果沙粒大小控制聲音，科學家只需測量沙粒就能預測音調。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a simple action gives enough information.","zh":"當簡單動作已提供足夠資訊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"smooth, varnish-like coating","meaning":"光滑、像清漆般的塗層","examples":[{"en":"The singing grains had a smooth, varnish-like coating.","zh":"會發聲的沙粒有光滑、像清漆般的塗層。"},{"en":"A smooth, varnish-like coating is a shiny, polished surface layer similar to varnish.","zh":"smooth, varnish-like coating 指類似清漆的閃亮、拋光表面層。"},{"en":"Old wooden furniture may have a smooth, varnish-like coating after being polished.","zh":"舊木家具拋光後可能有光滑、像清漆般的塗層。"},{"en":"The coating may affect how sand grains slide, rub or vibrate.","zh":"這層塗層可能影響沙粒如何滑動、摩擦或振動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a thin shiny surface layer.","zh":"描述薄而閃亮的表面層時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"minerals such as","meaning":"例如……等礦物","examples":[{"en":"The coating contains minerals such as silicon, iron and manganese.","zh":"塗層含有硅、鐵和錳等礦物。"},{"en":"Minerals such as introduces examples of natural substances found in rocks, soil or sand.","zh":"minerals such as 用來引出在岩石、土壤或沙中發現的天然物質例子。"},{"en":"Foods can contain minerals such as calcium, iron and potassium.","zh":"食物可以含有鈣、鐵和鉀等礦物。"},{"en":"Listing minerals helps explain what the coating is made of.","zh":"列出礦物有助解釋塗層由甚麼組成。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving examples from a larger group.","zh":"從較大類別中舉例時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"silicon, iron and manganese","meaning":"硅、鐵和錳","examples":[{"en":"The coating contains silicon, iron and manganese.","zh":"塗層含有硅、鐵和錳。"},{"en":"Silicon, iron and manganese are minerals or elements that can occur in natural materials.","zh":"silicon, iron and manganese 是可出現在天然材料中的礦物或元素。"},{"en":"A science teacher may mention iron when explaining why some rocks look reddish.","zh":"科學老師解釋為何有些岩石呈紅色時，可能提到鐵。"},{"en":"These substances may form part of the coating on singing sand grains.","zh":"這些物質可能構成會發聲沙粒塗層的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying the materials in a mineral layer.","zh":"識別礦物層中的材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lie beneath","meaning":"位於……之下","examples":[{"en":"The dunes once lay beneath an ancient ocean.","zh":"這些沙丘曾位於古代海洋之下。"},{"en":"Lie beneath means be located under something.","zh":"lie beneath 指位於某物之下。"},{"en":"Old pipes may lie beneath a city street.","zh":"舊水管可能位於城市街道之下。"},{"en":"If dunes once lay beneath an ocean, minerals from water may have affected the sand.","zh":"如果沙丘曾位於海洋之下，水中的礦物可能影響沙粒。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing something hidden below a surface.","zh":"描述某物隱藏在表面下時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"an ancient ocean","meaning":"古代海洋","examples":[{"en":"The mineral coating formed when the dunes lay beneath an ancient ocean.","zh":"礦物塗層在沙丘位於古代海洋之下時形成。"},{"en":"An ancient ocean is a sea that existed in the distant geological past.","zh":"ancient ocean 指存在於遙遠地質過去的海洋。"},{"en":"Fossils in rocks can show that an ancient ocean once covered an area.","zh":"岩石中的化石可以顯示古代海洋曾覆蓋某地區。"},{"en":"Ancient oceans can leave mineral traces that remain long after the water disappears.","zh":"古代海洋可以留下礦物痕跡，即使水消失很久仍存在。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing geological history.","zh":"討論地質歷史時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"muted grains","meaning":"不發聲的沙粒","examples":[{"en":"Muted grains had lost their mineral coating.","zh":"不發聲的沙粒已失去礦物塗層。"},{"en":"Muted grains are sand grains that no longer produce the singing sound.","zh":"muted grains 指不再產生歌聲般聲音的沙粒。"},{"en":"A bell can sound muted if cloth covers it and reduces its vibration.","zh":"如果布蓋住鐘並減少其振動，鐘聲會變得沉悶。"},{"en":"Sand grains may become muted when the surface coating needed for sound is worn away.","zh":"當產生聲音所需的表面塗層被磨掉，沙粒可能變得不發聲。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when sound is reduced or absent.","zh":"當聲音被降低或消失時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be worn away","meaning":"被磨掉；被磨蝕","examples":[{"en":"The coating had been worn away from the muted grains.","zh":"不發聲沙粒上的塗層已被磨掉。"},{"en":"Be worn away means be gradually removed by rubbing, wind, water or use.","zh":"be worn away 指因摩擦、風、水或使用而逐漸被移除。"},{"en":"The paint on a school desk may be worn away after years of use.","zh":"學校書桌上的油漆可能在多年使用後被磨掉。"},{"en":"A mineral coating can be worn away when grains rub against one another.","zh":"當沙粒互相摩擦，礦物塗層可能被磨蝕。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a surface slowly disappears.","zh":"當表面慢慢消失時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"explain why","meaning":"解釋為何","examples":[{"en":"The worn coating explains why only some dunes can sing.","zh":"被磨掉的塗層解釋為何只有部分沙丘會發聲。"},{"en":"Explain why means give the reason for something.","zh":"explain why 指給出某事的原因。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain why a grammar answer is wrong, not just mark it with a cross.","zh":"老師可能解釋為何文法答案錯誤，而不只是打交叉。"},{"en":"Understanding the coating may explain why some sand produces sound and other sand does not.","zh":"理解塗層可能解釋為何有些沙會發聲，而其他沙不會。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving causes or reasons.","zh":"給出原因或理由時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"admit that","meaning":"承認","examples":[{"en":"Douady admits that he is unsure about the coating’s role.","zh":"Douady 承認自己不確定塗層的作用。"},{"en":"Admit that means honestly say something is true, especially when it shows uncertainty or weakness.","zh":"admit that 指誠實地說某事為真，尤其是顯示不確定或不足時。"},{"en":"A student may admit that they do not understand the question.","zh":"學生可能承認自己不明白題目。"},{"en":"Scientists admit uncertainty when evidence is not yet strong enough.","zh":"當證據尚未足夠有力，科學家會承認不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone is honest about limits in knowledge.","zh":"當某人誠實說明知識限制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"what role something plays","meaning":"某物所起的作用","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are unsure what role the coating plays.","zh":"研究人員不確定塗層所起的作用。"},{"en":"What role something plays means what function or importance it has in a process.","zh":"what role something plays 指某物在過程中有甚麼功能或重要性。"},{"en":"Teachers may ask what role sleep plays in students’ learning.","zh":"老師可能問睡眠在學生學習中起甚麼作用。"},{"en":"Scientists want to know whether the coating helps create sound or merely appears with singing sand.","zh":"科學家想知道塗層是否幫助產生聲音，還是只與會發聲的沙同時出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying a factor’s function.","zh":"識別某因素的功能時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"produce the noise","meaning":"產生聲音","examples":[{"en":"The coating may play a role in producing the noise.","zh":"塗層可能在產生聲音方面起作用。"},{"en":"Produce the noise means create or cause the sound.","zh":"produce the noise 指創造或造成聲音。"},{"en":"Loose metal parts in a bicycle may produce a noise when the bike moves.","zh":"單車上的鬆脫金屬零件可能在車移動時產生聲音。"},{"en":"Sand grains may produce the noise when their movement becomes synchronised.","zh":"當沙粒移動變得同步，它們可能產生聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the source of a sound.","zh":"解釋聲音來源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"give up all of their secrets","meaning":"透露所有秘密","examples":[{"en":"The mysterious dunes are not ready to give up all of their secrets.","zh":"這些神秘沙丘還未準備透露所有秘密。"},{"en":"Give up all of their secrets means reveal everything that is still unknown or hidden.","zh":"give up all of their secrets 指揭示所有仍未知或隱藏的事情。"},{"en":"An old family photo may not give up all of its secrets until relatives explain the people in it.","zh":"舊家庭照片可能要等親戚解釋相中人物後，才透露所有秘密。"},{"en":"Nature often does not give up all of its secrets after one experiment.","zh":"大自然常不會在一次實驗後就透露所有秘密。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when mystery remains after research.","zh":"當研究後仍有謎團存在時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct heading for each paragraph.","zh":"考生為每段選出正確標題。"},{"en":"Choose the correct heading means select the title that best summarises a paragraph.","zh":"choose the correct heading 指選擇最能概括段落的標題。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole paragraph before choosing the correct heading.","zh":"學生應先閱讀整段，再選出正確標題。"},{"en":"A correct heading matches the main idea, not just one repeated word.","zh":"正確標題符合主旨，而不只是符合一個重複字眼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in IELTS-style reading tasks.","zh":"這個短語適用於 IELTS 式閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The list of headings contains possible paragraph summaries.","zh":"標題列表包含可能的段落摘要。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a set of titles that candidates choose from.","zh":"list of headings 指考生可從中選擇的一組標題。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students compare each paragraph with the list of headings.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生把每段與標題列表比較。"},{"en":"A heading list can include tempting wrong answers that mention minor details.","zh":"標題列表可能包括提到細節的誘人錯誤答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining matching-headings questions.","zh":"解釋配對標題題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"shaping and reforming","meaning":"塑造和重新塑造","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes the shaping and reforming of dunes.","zh":"文章描述沙丘的塑造和重新塑造。"},{"en":"Shaping and reforming means forming something and then changing its form again.","zh":"shaping and reforming 指形成某物，然後再次改變其形狀。"},{"en":"A river’s shaping and reforming of land can create bends, banks and islands.","zh":"河流對土地的塑造和重新塑造可以形成河彎、河岸和島嶼。"},{"en":"Wind causes the shaping and reforming of dunes by moving sand from one place to another.","zh":"風透過把沙從一處移到另一處，造成沙丘的塑造和重新塑造。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a natural form changes repeatedly.","zh":"當自然形態反覆改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"causes of desertification","meaning":"沙漠化的成因","examples":[{"en":"The heading refers to the causes of desertification.","zh":"這個標題提及沙漠化的成因。"},{"en":"Causes of desertification are reasons why land becomes more desert-like and less productive.","zh":"causes of desertification 指土地變得更像沙漠、產量更低的原因。"},{"en":"Overgrazing and drought can be causes of desertification in dry regions.","zh":"過度放牧和乾旱可以是乾旱地區沙漠化的成因。"},{"en":"Understanding the causes of desertification helps governments protect farmland.","zh":"理解沙漠化的成因有助政府保護農地。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing why land becomes degraded and dry.","zh":"討論土地為何退化和乾旱時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"potential threat to","meaning":"對……的潛在威脅","examples":[{"en":"Dunes can be a potential threat to industry and transport.","zh":"沙丘可以成為對工業和交通的潛在威脅。"},{"en":"A potential threat to something is a possible danger that may harm it later.","zh":"potential threat to something 指日後可能傷害某事物的危險。"},{"en":"Heavy traffic is a potential threat to children’s safety near schools.","zh":"嚴重交通是學校附近兒童安全的潛在威脅。"},{"en":"Moving dunes become a potential threat when they approach roads, farms or buildings.","zh":"當移動沙丘接近道路、農田或建築物，它們就成為潛在威脅。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when danger is possible but not yet fully realised.","zh":"當危險可能存在但尚未完全發生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"industry and communication","meaning":"工業及交通聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Dunes may threaten industry and communication routes.","zh":"沙丘可能威脅工業及交通聯繫路線。"},{"en":"Industry and communication refers to factories, economic activity and transport or connection routes.","zh":"industry and communication 指工廠、經濟活動以及交通或連接路線。"},{"en":"A storm can damage industry and communication by closing factories and blocking roads.","zh":"暴風可以透過令工廠關閉和道路受阻來損害工業及交通聯繫。"},{"en":"Dunes threaten communication when roads or highways are buried by sand.","zh":"當道路或公路被沙掩埋，沙丘就威脅交通聯繫。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when natural hazards affect work and transport links.","zh":"當自然災害影響工作和交通連接時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"an old superstition demystified","meaning":"古老迷信被破解","examples":[{"en":"Science has demystified an old superstition about singing dunes.","zh":"科學破解了關於會發聲沙丘的古老迷信。"},{"en":"An old superstition demystified means an ancient belief has been explained by facts instead of mystery.","zh":"an old superstition demystified 指古老信念被事實解釋，而不再神秘。"},{"en":"Lightning was once feared as anger from gods, but science demystified that old superstition.","zh":"閃電曾被視為神明憤怒，但科學破解了這種古老迷信。"},{"en":"Research demystifies singing dunes by showing that the sound comes from sand grains.","zh":"研究透過顯示聲音來自沙粒，破解了會發聲沙丘的神秘感。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when science explains a mysterious old belief.","zh":"當科學解釋神秘古老信念時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"differences and similarities","meaning":"異同","examples":[{"en":"The passage compares the differences and similarities between dune types.","zh":"文章比較不同沙丘類型之間的異同。"},{"en":"Differences and similarities are the ways things are unlike and alike.","zh":"differences and similarities 指事物不同和相似之處。"},{"en":"Students compare differences and similarities between city schools and village schools.","zh":"學生比較城市學校和鄉村學校的異同。"},{"en":"Comparing dune types helps readers understand what features classify them.","zh":"比較沙丘類型幫助讀者理解哪些特徵用來分類它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when two or more things are being compared.","zh":"比較兩個或多個事物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a continuous cycling process","meaning":"持續循環過程","examples":[{"en":"Dune movement depends on a continuous cycling process.","zh":"沙丘移動依賴持續循環過程。"},{"en":"A continuous cycling process is a repeated process that keeps going without stopping.","zh":"continuous cycling process 指不斷重複、持續進行的過程。"},{"en":"Water heating, evaporating and falling as rain is part of a continuous cycling process.","zh":"水受熱、蒸發並以雨形式落下，是持續循環過程的一部分。"},{"en":"Sand dunes move because sand repeatedly climbs, falls and settles.","zh":"沙丘移動是因為沙反覆上移、滑落和沉積。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when repeated natural steps create ongoing change.","zh":"當重複自然步驟造成持續變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"habitat for rare species","meaning":"珍稀物種的棲息地","examples":[{"en":"A dune can serve as a habitat for rare species.","zh":"沙丘可以成為珍稀物種的棲息地。"},{"en":"A habitat for rare species is a place where uncommon plants or animals live and survive.","zh":"habitat for rare species 指罕見植物或動物生活和生存的地方。"},{"en":"A wetland may be a habitat for rare species of birds.","zh":"濕地可能是珍稀鳥類的棲息地。"},{"en":"Protecting habitats matters because rare species may disappear if their living places are damaged.","zh":"保護棲息地很重要，因為如果生活地方受損，珍稀物種可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing conservation.","zh":"討論保育時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"rare species","meaning":"珍稀物種","examples":[{"en":"Some headings refer to rare species, but the passage focuses mainly on dunes.","zh":"有些標題提到珍稀物種，但文章主要集中於沙丘。"},{"en":"Rare species are plants or animals that are uncommon or have small populations.","zh":"rare species 指不常見或種群數量很小的植物或動物。"},{"en":"A rare species of frog may live only in one mountain stream.","zh":"某種珍稀青蛙可能只生活在一條山溪中。"},{"en":"Rare species are vulnerable because losing one habitat can threaten the whole population.","zh":"珍稀物種很脆弱，因為失去一個棲息地可能威脅整個種群。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing biodiversity and conservation.","zh":"討論生物多樣性和保育時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"replicate the process","meaning":"重現過程","examples":[{"en":"The scientists replicated the process in the laboratory.","zh":"科學家在實驗室中重現了這個過程。"},{"en":"Replicate the process means repeat or recreate the same process under controlled conditions.","zh":"replicate the process 指在受控條件下重複或重建同一過程。"},{"en":"A student may replicate the process of seed growth in a classroom experiment.","zh":"學生可能在課室實驗中重現種子生長過程。"},{"en":"Scientists replicate a natural process to test which parts are necessary.","zh":"科學家重現自然過程，以測試哪些部分是必要的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when researchers recreate events for study.","zh":"當研究人員重建事件以便研究時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"in the laboratory","meaning":"在實驗室裏","examples":[{"en":"The sound-producing process was replicated in the laboratory.","zh":"產生聲音的過程在實驗室裏被重現。"},{"en":"In the laboratory means in a controlled scientific testing place.","zh":"in the laboratory 指在受控的科學測試場所中。"},{"en":"Students test water samples in the laboratory during science lessons.","zh":"學生在科學課中於實驗室裏測試水樣本。"},{"en":"Testing in the laboratory helps researchers separate important factors from background noise.","zh":"在實驗室測試幫助研究人員把重要因素與背景干擾分開。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when experiments happen under controlled conditions.","zh":"當實驗在受控條件下進行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the most common type of dune","meaning":"最常見的沙丘類型","examples":[{"en":"The barchan is the most common type of dune.","zh":"巴爾漢沙丘是最常見的沙丘類型。"},{"en":"The most common type of dune means the dune form found most often.","zh":"most common type of dune 指最常被找到的沙丘形態。"},{"en":"In a park, grassland may be the most common type of open space.","zh":"在公園中，草地可能是最常見的開放空間類型。"},{"en":"Knowing the most common type helps students start with the most typical example.","zh":"知道最常見類型幫助學生從最典型例子開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when ranking categories by frequency.","zh":"按出現頻率排列類別時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"complete the sentences below","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the sentences below with words from the passage.","zh":"考生用文章中的詞語完成以下句子。"},{"en":"Complete the sentences below means fill in missing words in the sentences that follow.","zh":"complete the sentences below 指填入下方句子中的缺失詞語。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete the sentences below by copying exact words from the text.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過從文本抄出準確詞語來完成以下句子。"},{"en":"This task checks whether students can locate information and fit it grammatically.","zh":"這個任務檢查學生能否定位資訊並在文法上配合句子。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"one word only","meaning":"只填一個字","examples":[{"en":"The instructions say that each answer should use one word only.","zh":"指示說每個答案只應使用一個字。"},{"en":"One word only means the answer must contain exactly one word and no extra words.","zh":"one word only 指答案必須剛好包含一個詞，不能有額外詞語。"},{"en":"If the answer is “sand”, students should not write “the sand” in a one-word-only task.","zh":"如果答案是 “sand”，在只填一個字的任務中，學生不應寫 “the sand”。"},{"en":"Word limits matter because extra words can make an answer wrong.","zh":"字數限制很重要，因為額外詞語可能令答案錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in IELTS-style completion tasks.","zh":"這個短語適用於 IELTS 式填空題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be said to have","meaning":"據說有","examples":[{"en":"The linear dune is said to have long ridges.","zh":"線形沙丘據說有長長的沙脊。"},{"en":"Be said to have means people describe or report something as having a particular feature.","zh":"be said to have 指人們描述或報告某物有某特徵。"},{"en":"The old library is said to have a hidden reading room.","zh":"那座舊圖書館據說有一間隱藏閱讀室。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when information is reported rather than directly observed by the speaker.","zh":"當資訊是被報告出來，而不是說話者直接觀察時，常用這個短語。"},{"en":"It is useful in formal descriptions and reading passages.","zh":"它適用於正式描述和閱讀文章。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"long ridges","meaning":"長長的沙脊","examples":[{"en":"The linear dune has long ridges.","zh":"線形沙丘有長長的沙脊。"},{"en":"Long ridges are raised narrow lines that stretch across a surface for a long distance.","zh":"long ridges 指在表面上長距離延伸的狹長凸起線條。"},{"en":"Long ridges of soil may appear in a field after ploughing.","zh":"耕地後，田裏可能出現長長的泥脊。"},{"en":"In dunes, long ridges help identify linear or longitudinal forms.","zh":"在沙丘中，長沙脊有助識別線形或縱向形態。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing raised land patterns.","zh":"描述凸起地貌圖案時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"extend hundreds of miles","meaning":"延伸數百英里","examples":[{"en":"Some ridges can extend hundreds of miles.","zh":"有些沙脊可以延伸數百英里。"},{"en":"Extend hundreds of miles means stretch across a very long distance.","zh":"extend hundreds of miles 指橫跨非常長的距離。"},{"en":"A railway can extend hundreds of miles across a country.","zh":"鐵路可以延伸數百英里，穿過一個國家。"},{"en":"Dune ridges that extend hundreds of miles show how large desert landforms can be.","zh":"延伸數百英里的沙脊顯示沙漠地貌可以有多巨大。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when emphasising extreme length.","zh":"強調極長距離時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"spiritual phenomenon","meaning":"靈異現象","examples":[{"en":"Douady believes the singing of dunes is not a spiritual phenomenon.","zh":"Douady 認為沙丘發聲不是靈異現象。"},{"en":"A spiritual phenomenon is an event believed to come from spirits or supernatural forces.","zh":"spiritual phenomenon 指被認為來自靈體或超自然力量的事件。"},{"en":"In the past, people may have treated strange natural sounds as spiritual phenomena.","zh":"過去，人們可能把奇怪自然聲音視為靈異現象。"},{"en":"Science challenges this view by showing physical causes behind the sound.","zh":"科學透過顯示聲音背後的物理原因來挑戰這種看法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting superstition with scientific explanation.","zh":"對比迷信與科學解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"purely acoustic","meaning":"純粹是聲學上的","examples":[{"en":"Douady believes the singing of dunes is purely acoustic.","zh":"Douady 認為沙丘發聲純粹是聲學上的。"},{"en":"Purely acoustic means entirely related to sound, not spirits or magic.","zh":"purely acoustic 指完全與聲音有關，而不是與靈體或魔法有關。"},{"en":"An echo in a hall is a purely acoustic effect caused by sound reflection.","zh":"大堂中的回音是由聲音反射造成的純聲學效果。"},{"en":"Calling dune singing purely acoustic means the explanation lies in vibration and sound waves.","zh":"說沙丘發聲純粹是聲學上的，意思是解釋在於振動和聲波。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when sound has a scientific, not supernatural, explanation.","zh":"當聲音有科學而非超自然解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"complete the summary below","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the summary below using words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的詞語完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"Complete the summary below means fill missing words in a short overview of the text.","zh":"complete the summary below 指在文本簡短概述中填入缺失詞語。"},{"en":"Students complete the summary below after identifying the main facts in the paragraph.","zh":"學生識別段落主要事實後，完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"Summary completion tests both understanding and accurate word choice.","zh":"摘要填空同時測試理解和準確用詞。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading-comprehension instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於閱讀理解指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"most commonly found","meaning":"最常見於","examples":[{"en":"Two types of dunes are most commonly found in deserts.","zh":"兩種沙丘最常見於沙漠。"},{"en":"Most commonly found means found most often or in the greatest number of cases.","zh":"most commonly found 指最常被發現，或在最多情況中出現。"},{"en":"Smartphones are most commonly found in students’ bags today.","zh":"今日，智能手機最常見於學生書包中。"},{"en":"Knowing what is most commonly found helps learners focus on typical examples first.","zh":"知道甚麼最常見，有助學習者先集中於典型例子。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing frequency.","zh":"描述頻率時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"throughout the world","meaning":"世界各地","examples":[{"en":"These dunes are found in deserts throughout the world.","zh":"這些沙丘可在世界各地的沙漠中找到。"},{"en":"Throughout the world means in many countries or regions across the whole world.","zh":"throughout the world 指遍及全世界許多國家或地區。"},{"en":"English is studied in schools throughout the world.","zh":"英語在世界各地的學校中被學習。"},{"en":"A feature found throughout the world is not limited to one local area.","zh":"在世界各地都能找到的特徵並不限於一個本地區域。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something has global distribution.","zh":"當某物有全球分布時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"sometimes also known as","meaning":"有時亦稱為","examples":[{"en":"The barchan dune is sometimes also known as the crescentic dune.","zh":"巴爾漢沙丘有時亦稱為新月形沙丘。"},{"en":"Sometimes also known as means sometimes called by another name.","zh":"sometimes also known as 指有時被稱為另一名稱。"},{"en":"A lift is sometimes also known as an elevator in American English.","zh":"lift 在美式英語中有時亦稱為 elevator。"},{"en":"Knowing alternative names helps students recognise the same thing in different texts.","zh":"知道替代名稱幫助學生在不同文本中認出同一事物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a term has more than one name.","zh":"當術語有多於一個名稱時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"it has long been known that","meaning":"人們早已知道","examples":[{"en":"It has long been known that some dunes can sing.","zh":"人們早已知道有些沙丘會發聲。"},{"en":"It has long been known that means people have understood or reported something for a long time.","zh":"it has long been known that 指人們很久以來已理解或報告某事。"},{"en":"It has long been known that sleep affects learning and memory.","zh":"人們早已知道睡眠影響學習和記憶。"},{"en":"Old knowledge can still need modern research to explain the mechanism behind it.","zh":"舊知識仍可能需要現代研究來解釋其背後機制。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an observation is old but its explanation may be new.","zh":"當觀察很早已有，但解釋可能是新的時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the answer lies in","meaning":"答案在於……","examples":[{"en":"The answer lies in the sand itself.","zh":"答案在於沙本身。"},{"en":"The answer lies in means the explanation or solution can be found in a particular place or factor.","zh":"the answer lies in 指解釋或解決方法可在某地方或因素中找到。"},{"en":"If students keep making the same mistake, the answer may lie in unclear instructions.","zh":"如果學生一直犯同一錯誤，答案可能在於指示不清。"},{"en":"For singing dunes, the answer lies in the grains rather than in spirits.","zh":"對會發聲沙丘而言，答案在於沙粒，而不是靈體。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when pointing to the true source of an explanation.","zh":"指出解釋的真正來源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"singing sand","meaning":"會發聲的沙","examples":[{"en":"Scientists produced singing sand in the laboratory.","zh":"科學家在實驗室中製造出會發聲的沙。"},{"en":"Singing sand is sand that can produce a musical or booming sound when it moves.","zh":"singing sand 指移動時能產生音樂般或轟鳴聲的沙。"},{"en":"Visitors may hear singing sand when they slide down a special dune.","zh":"遊客從特殊沙丘滑下時，可能聽見會發聲的沙。"},{"en":"Singing sand requires grains with suitable size, shape and surface features.","zh":"會發聲的沙需要有合適大小、形狀和表面特徵的沙粒。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when sand itself produces sound.","zh":"當沙本身產生聲音時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"similar shapes","meaning":"相似形狀","examples":[{"en":"The grains must have similar shapes.","zh":"沙粒必須有相似形狀。"},{"en":"Similar shapes means forms that are alike or nearly alike.","zh":"similar shapes 指相同或近乎相同的形態。"},{"en":"A box of buttons with similar shapes is easier to organise than a mixed box.","zh":"一盒形狀相似的鈕扣比混合鈕扣盒更容易整理。"},{"en":"Similar shapes may help sand grains move together smoothly.","zh":"相似形狀可能幫助沙粒順暢地一起移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when matching physical form matters.","zh":"當實體形態配合很重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"affect the tone of","meaning":"影響……的音調","examples":[{"en":"The size of the grains can affect the tone of the sound.","zh":"沙粒大小可以影響聲音的音調。"},{"en":"Affect the tone of means influence whether a sound is high, low, deep or sharp.","zh":"affect the tone of 指影響聲音是高、低、深沉還是尖銳。"},{"en":"The size of a drum can affect the tone of the music it produces.","zh":"鼓的大小可以影響它產生的音樂音調。"},{"en":"Grain size affects tone because different grains vibrate at different frequencies.","zh":"沙粒大小影響音調，因為不同沙粒以不同頻率振動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining what changes sound quality.","zh":"解釋甚麼改變聲音質素時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"varnish composed of","meaning":"由……構成的清漆狀塗層","examples":[{"en":"The function of the varnish composed of minerals remains unclear.","zh":"由礦物構成的清漆狀塗層的功能仍不清楚。"},{"en":"Varnish composed of means a smooth coating made up of particular materials.","zh":"varnish composed of 指由特定材料組成的光滑塗層。"},{"en":"A table may have a varnish composed of protective chemicals to make it shiny.","zh":"桌子可能有由保護性化學物質構成的清漆，使它發亮。"},{"en":"On singing sand, the mineral varnish may affect friction, movement or sound.","zh":"在會發聲的沙上，礦物清漆狀塗層可能影響摩擦、移動或聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing what a coating is made from.","zh":"描述塗層由甚麼構成時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a mixture of minerals","meaning":"礦物混合物","examples":[{"en":"The varnish contains a mixture of minerals.","zh":"清漆狀塗層含有礦物混合物。"},{"en":"A mixture of minerals is a combination of different natural mineral substances.","zh":"mixture of minerals 指不同天然礦物質的組合。"},{"en":"Soil may contain a mixture of minerals that affects plant growth.","zh":"土壤可能含有影響植物生長的礦物混合物。"},{"en":"The mineral mixture on sand grains may help explain why only some dunes sing.","zh":"沙粒上的礦物混合物可能有助解釋為何只有部分沙丘會發聲。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when several minerals appear together.","zh":"當幾種礦物一起出現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"remain puzzling","meaning":"仍然令人費解","examples":[{"en":"The function of the varnish still remains puzzling.","zh":"清漆狀塗層的功能仍然令人費解。"},{"en":"Remain puzzling means continue to be difficult to understand or explain.","zh":"remain puzzling 指仍然難以理解或解釋。"},{"en":"A student’s sudden drop in marks may remain puzzling until the teacher learns about sleep problems.","zh":"學生成績突然下降可能仍然令人費解，直到老師知道其睡眠問題。"},{"en":"Even after experiments, some parts of singing dunes remain puzzling.","zh":"即使經過實驗，會發聲沙丘的某些部分仍令人費解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when questions are still unanswered.","zh":"當問題仍未有答案時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 37 - Living Dunes.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 38":[{"front":"accidental scientists","meaning":"偶然作出發現的科學家","examples":[{"en":"Accidental scientists sometimes make discoveries while looking for something else.","zh":"偶然作出發現的科學家有時會在尋找其他東西時作出發現。"},{"en":"Accidental scientists are people who discover something important without originally planning to find it.","zh":"Accidental scientists 是指原本並沒有計劃找到某物，卻發現重要東西的人。"},{"en":"A student may become an accidental scientist when a failed experiment reveals a strange new result.","zh":"當一次失敗實驗揭示奇怪的新結果，學生可能成為偶然作出發現的科學家。"},{"en":"Accidental scientists still need knowledge, because they must recognise that an unexpected result matters.","zh":"偶然作出發現的科學家仍然需要知識，因為他們必須認出意外結果的重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that discovery can involve both chance and careful attention.","zh":"這個片語顯示發現可以同時涉及機遇和細心觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a paradox lies close to the heart of","meaning":"一個悖論接近……的核心","examples":[{"en":"A paradox lies close to the heart of scientific discovery.","zh":"一個悖論接近科學發現的核心。"},{"en":"A paradox lies close to the heart of something means a deep contradiction sits near the centre of that issue.","zh":"A paradox lies close to the heart of something 指一個深層矛盾位於某議題核心附近。"},{"en":"A paradox lies close to the heart of education: students need guidance, but they also need independence.","zh":"教育的核心附近有一個悖論：學生需要指導，但也需要獨立。"},{"en":"When two opposite ideas are both partly true, a paradox may shape the whole problem.","zh":"當兩個相反想法都部分正確時，一個悖論可能塑造整個問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for introducing a central tension in an argument.","zh":"這個片語適合用來引出論點中的核心張力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"scientific discovery","meaning":"科學發現","examples":[{"en":"A paradox lies close to the heart of scientific discovery.","zh":"一個悖論接近科學發現的核心。"},{"en":"Scientific discovery means finding new knowledge about nature, people, technology, or the universe through careful investigation.","zh":"Scientific discovery 指透過仔細研究，找到關於自然、人類、科技或宇宙的新知識。"},{"en":"A child’s simple question about why plants bend toward light can lead to scientific discovery.","zh":"孩子問植物為何向光彎曲這個簡單問題，可能引向科學發現。"},{"en":"Scientific discovery often begins when results do not match what researchers expected.","zh":"科學發現常在結果與研究人員預期不符時開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of finding something previously unknown in science.","zh":"這個片語描述在科學中找到先前未知事物的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"just what you are looking for","meaning":"正正是你正在尋找的東西","examples":[{"en":"If you know just what you are looking for, finding it can hardly count as a discovery.","zh":"如果你知道正正是你正在尋找的東西，找到它便很難算作發現。"},{"en":"Just what you are looking for means exactly the thing you expected or wanted to find.","zh":"Just what you are looking for 指完全是你預期或想找到的東西。"},{"en":"If a student searches a dictionary for one word and finds that word, it is just what they are looking for.","zh":"如果學生在字典中查一個字並找到那個字，那就是正正是他正在尋找的東西。"},{"en":"When the result is already expected, the surprise and discovery are reduced.","zh":"當結果早已被預期，驚喜和發現感便會減少。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses exact expectation, not accidental finding.","zh":"這個片語強調精確預期，而不是偶然找到。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"can hardly count as","meaning":"很難算作……","examples":[{"en":"If the result was fully anticipated, it can hardly count as a discovery.","zh":"如果結果完全預料之中，它很難算作發現。"},{"en":"Can hardly count as means it is difficult to regard something as belonging to that category.","zh":"Can hardly count as 指很難把某事視為屬於某類別。"},{"en":"Copying a model answer can hardly count as original writing.","zh":"抄襲範文很難算作原創寫作。"},{"en":"If no new understanding is gained, the work can hardly count as real research.","zh":"如果沒有獲得新理解，該工作很難算作真正研究。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to challenge whether something truly qualifies as what people claim.","zh":"這個片語常用來質疑某事是否真的符合人們所聲稱的類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fully anticipated","meaning":"完全預料之中","examples":[{"en":"The discovery can hardly count as a discovery if it was fully anticipated.","zh":"如果某發現完全預料之中，它很難算作發現。"},{"en":"Fully anticipated means completely expected before it happened.","zh":"Fully anticipated 指在發生之前已被完全預期。"},{"en":"If rain was fully anticipated, students would bring umbrellas before leaving home.","zh":"如果下雨完全預料之中，學生離家前就會帶雨傘。"},{"en":"When an experiment gives a fully anticipated result, it confirms an idea rather than surprises researchers.","zh":"當實驗得出完全預料之中的結果，它是在確認想法，而不是令研究人員驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that has already been completely predicted.","zh":"這個片語描述已被完全預測到的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"On the other hand, if you have no notion of what you are looking for, discovery is impossible.","zh":"另一方面，如果你對自己正在尋找甚麼毫無概念，發現就是不可能的。"},{"en":"On the other hand introduces a contrasting point or another side of an argument.","zh":"On the other hand 用來引出對比點或論點的另一面。"},{"en":"Practice is useful; on the other hand, students also need clear explanation before practising.","zh":"練習很有用；另一方面，學生在練習前也需要清楚解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers balance one idea with an opposite or limiting idea.","zh":"這個片語幫助作者用相反或限制性的想法平衡前一點。"},{"en":"It is often used when both sides of an issue contain some truth.","zh":"當議題雙方都有部分道理時，它常被使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have no notion of","meaning":"對……毫無概念","examples":[{"en":"If you have no notion of what you are looking for, you cannot know when you have found it.","zh":"如果你對自己正在尋找甚麼毫無概念，你就無法知道自己何時已找到它。"},{"en":"To have no notion of something means to have no idea or understanding of it.","zh":"To have no notion of something 指對某事沒有任何想法或理解。"},{"en":"A new student may have no notion of how the school timetable works on the first day.","zh":"新學生在第一天可能對學校時間表如何運作毫無概念。"},{"en":"If people have no notion of the problem, they cannot choose the right solution.","zh":"如果人們對問題毫無概念，他們就無法選擇正確解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete lack of understanding or awareness.","zh":"這個片語描述完全缺乏理解或意識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"know when you have found it","meaning":"知道自己何時已找到它","examples":[{"en":"You cannot know when you have found it if you have no idea what you are seeking.","zh":"如果你不知道自己正在尋找甚麼，就無法知道自己何時已找到它。"},{"en":"To know when you have found it means to recognise that the thing discovered is the right or important one.","zh":"To know when you have found it 指能認出被發現的東西是正確或重要的。"},{"en":"If a student does not know what evidence is needed, they may not know when they have found it.","zh":"如果學生不知道需要甚麼證據，他可能不知道自己何時已找到它。"},{"en":"Clear goals help people recognise useful information when it appears.","zh":"清楚目標幫助人們在有用資訊出現時認出它。"},{"en":"This phrase links discovery with recognition, not just searching.","zh":"這個片語把發現與辨認連接起來，而不只是搜尋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"discovery, as such","meaning":"嚴格來說的發現","examples":[{"en":"Discovery, as such, is out of the question when you have no notion of what you seek.","zh":"當你對自己尋找甚麼毫無概念時，嚴格來說的發現是不可能的。"},{"en":"Discovery, as such means discovery in the strict or proper sense of the word.","zh":"Discovery, as such 指嚴格或真正意義上的發現。"},{"en":"Guessing an answer by luck is not learning, as such, because no understanding has been built.","zh":"靠運氣猜中答案嚴格來說不是學習，因為沒有建立理解。"},{"en":"If someone cannot recognise what matters, discovery as such cannot really occur.","zh":"如果某人無法認出重要之處，嚴格來說的發現就不能真正發生。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows a word to its exact meaning.","zh":"這個片語把某個詞限制在其確切意思上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"out of the question","meaning":"不可能；不在考慮之列","examples":[{"en":"Discovery is out of the question if you cannot recognise what you have found.","zh":"如果你不能辨認自己找到了甚麼，發現就是不可能的。"},{"en":"Out of the question means impossible or not acceptable as an option.","zh":"Out of the question 指不可能或不可接受為選項。"},{"en":"Joining a school trip is out of the question if a student has a serious fever.","zh":"如果學生發高燒，參加學校旅行就是不可能的。"},{"en":"If there is no evidence, making a confident conclusion is out of the question.","zh":"如果沒有證據，作出肯定結論是不在考慮之列的。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly rejects a possibility.","zh":"這個片語強烈否定某種可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the philosophy of science","meaning":"科學哲學","examples":[{"en":"In the philosophy of science, these extremes map onto deductivism and inductivism.","zh":"在科學哲學中，這些極端對應於演繹主義和歸納主義。"},{"en":"The philosophy of science is the study of how science works, what counts as evidence, and how knowledge is justified.","zh":"The philosophy of science 是研究科學如何運作、甚麼算作證據，以及知識如何被證成的學問。"},{"en":"A student studying the philosophy of science may ask whether experiments can ever be completely objective.","zh":"研究科學哲學的學生可能會問實驗是否能完全客觀。"},{"en":"This field helps people think about the assumptions behind scientific methods.","zh":"這個領域幫助人思考科學方法背後的假設。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to thinking about science itself, not doing a laboratory experiment.","zh":"這個片語指思考科學本身，而不是進行實驗室實驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"these extremes","meaning":"這些極端","examples":[{"en":"These extremes map onto the purist forms of deductivism and inductivism.","zh":"這些極端對應於演繹主義和歸納主義的純粹形式。"},{"en":"These extremes means the two opposite and very strong positions just mentioned.","zh":"These extremes 指剛提到的兩個相反而非常強烈的立場。"},{"en":"In education, memorising everything and never memorising anything are both extremes.","zh":"在教育中，背誦一切和完全不背誦都是極端。"},{"en":"When people focus only on extremes, they may miss a balanced solution.","zh":"當人們只專注於極端，他們可能錯過平衡解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to two very different ends of an argument.","zh":"這個片語回指論點中兩個非常不同的端點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"map onto","meaning":"對應於……","examples":[{"en":"These extremes map onto two opposing views of scientific discovery.","zh":"這些極端對應於兩種相反的科學發現觀點。"},{"en":"To map onto something means to correspond to it or match it in a meaningful way.","zh":"To map onto something 指與某事有意義地對應或配合。"},{"en":"In a school timetable, lesson times map onto the daily routine of teachers and students.","zh":"在學校時間表中，課堂時間對應於老師和學生的日常流程。"},{"en":"If two categories map onto real differences, they can help explain a problem clearly.","zh":"如果兩個類別對應於真實差異，它們可以幫助清楚解釋問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one set of ideas matches another set.","zh":"這個片語顯示一組想法與另一組想法相配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"purist forms of","meaning":"純粹形式的……","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the purist forms of deductivism and inductivism.","zh":"文章討論演繹主義和歸納主義的純粹形式。"},{"en":"Purist forms of something are the strictest and least mixed versions of an idea or approach.","zh":"Purist forms of something 是某想法或方法最嚴格、最不混合的版本。"},{"en":"A purist form of grammar teaching may allow no games, only rules and drills.","zh":"純粹形式的文法教學可能不容許遊戲，只容許規則和操練。"},{"en":"Purist forms can be clear in theory but difficult to use in real life.","zh":"純粹形式在理論上可能清晰，但在現實中難以使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an extreme, uncompromising version of a belief.","zh":"這個片語描述一種信念的極端、不妥協版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"deductivism","meaning":"演繹主義","examples":[{"en":"In deductivism, the outcome is supposed to be logically contained in the premises.","zh":"在演繹主義中，結果理應在邏輯上包含於前提之中。"},{"en":"Deductivism is the view that conclusions follow logically from starting assumptions or premises.","zh":"Deductivism 是認為結論由起始假設或前提在邏輯上推出的觀點。"},{"en":"In a maths proof, deductivism appears when each step follows from earlier accepted statements.","zh":"在數學證明中，當每一步都由先前接受的陳述推出，演繹主義便出現。"},{"en":"If everything is already contained in the premises, the final answer may feel less like a surprise.","zh":"如果一切早已包含在前提中，最終答案可能較不像驚喜。"},{"en":"This term contrasts planned logical reasoning with open-ended discovery.","zh":"這個術語把有計劃的邏輯推理與開放式發現作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"inductivism","meaning":"歸納主義","examples":[{"en":"In inductivism, researchers are told to begin with no expectations.","zh":"在歸納主義中，研究人員被告知一開始不要抱任何期望。"},{"en":"Inductivism is the view that researchers should observe facts first and build general ideas from them.","zh":"Inductivism 是認為研究人員應先觀察事實，再由事實建立一般想法的觀點。"},{"en":"A student using inductivism may collect many examples before forming a grammar rule.","zh":"使用歸納主義的學生可能先收集許多例子，再形成文法規則。"},{"en":"If researchers begin with no expectations at all, they may struggle to recognise what matters.","zh":"如果研究人員一開始完全沒有期望，他們可能難以認出甚麼重要。"},{"en":"This term contrasts observation-first research with theory-first reasoning.","zh":"這個術語把先觀察的研究與先理論的推理作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in the former","meaning":"在前者之中","examples":[{"en":"In the former, the outcome is supposed to be contained in the premises.","zh":"在前者之中，結果理應包含於前提之中。"},{"en":"In the former means in the first of two things just mentioned.","zh":"In the former 指在剛剛提到的兩者中的第一個之中。"},{"en":"Some students choose online classes or face-to-face classes; in the former, they need more self-discipline.","zh":"有些學生選擇網上課或面授課；在前者之中，他們需要更多自律。"},{"en":"This phrase helps avoid repeating the first item in a pair.","zh":"這個片語幫助避免重複一對選項中的第一項。"},{"en":"It is useful only when two choices have already been clearly stated.","zh":"只有在兩個選項已清楚說明時，這個片語才有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in the latter","meaning":"在後者之中","examples":[{"en":"In the latter, researchers are recommended to start with no expectations.","zh":"在後者之中，研究人員被建議一開始不抱任何期望。"},{"en":"In the latter means in the second of two things just mentioned.","zh":"In the latter 指在剛剛提到的兩者中的第二個之中。"},{"en":"Students may choose group work or individual work; in the latter, they must manage all tasks alone.","zh":"學生可能選擇小組工作或個人工作；在後者之中，他們必須獨自處理所有任務。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to the second item in a pair.","zh":"這個片語回指一對選項中的第二項。"},{"en":"It helps writers compare two ideas without repeating both names.","zh":"它幫助作者比較兩個想法，而不用重複兩者名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the outcome is supposed to","meaning":"結果理應……","examples":[{"en":"In deductivism, the outcome is supposed to be logically contained in the premises.","zh":"在演繹主義中，結果理應在邏輯上包含於前提之中。"},{"en":"The outcome is supposed to means the result is expected or assumed to happen in a particular way.","zh":"The outcome is supposed to 指結果被預期或假定會以某種方式發生。"},{"en":"In a recipe, the outcome is supposed to be a soft cake if the steps are followed correctly.","zh":"在食譜中，如果步驟正確完成，結果理應是一個鬆軟蛋糕。"},{"en":"If the outcome is already supposed to follow from the starting point, little room is left for surprise.","zh":"如果結果理應已由起點推出，驚喜空間便很少。"},{"en":"This phrase shows expectation about a final result.","zh":"這個片語顯示對最終結果的預期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"logically contained in","meaning":"在邏輯上包含於……","examples":[{"en":"The outcome is supposed to be logically contained in the premises.","zh":"結果理應在邏輯上包含於前提之中。"},{"en":"Logically contained in means already implied by the starting statements if the reasoning is valid.","zh":"Logically contained in 指如果推理有效，某事已由起始陳述暗含。"},{"en":"In maths, the answer may be logically contained in the formula and numbers given.","zh":"在數學中，答案可能在邏輯上包含於所給公式和數字之中。"},{"en":"If a conclusion is logically contained in the premises, it should follow without adding new information.","zh":"如果結論在邏輯上包含於前提中，它應該不需加入新資訊便能推出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strict relationship between assumptions and conclusion.","zh":"這個片語描述假設與結論之間的嚴格關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the premises you start with","meaning":"你一開始採用的前提","examples":[{"en":"The outcome is supposed to be contained in the premises you start with.","zh":"結果理應包含於你一開始採用的前提之中。"},{"en":"The premises you start with are the first assumptions, facts, or claims used in reasoning.","zh":"The premises you start with 是推理中首先使用的假設、事實或主張。"},{"en":"In an essay, the argument becomes weak if the premises you start with are false.","zh":"在文章中，如果你一開始採用的前提是錯的，論點就會變弱。"},{"en":"If the starting premises are too narrow, the conclusion may also be narrow.","zh":"如果起始前提太狹窄，結論也可能太狹窄。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the foundation of an argument or investigation.","zh":"這個片語指論證或研究的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"start with no expectations whatsoever","meaning":"一開始完全不抱任何期望","examples":[{"en":"Inductivism recommends that researchers start with no expectations whatsoever.","zh":"歸納主義建議研究人員一開始完全不抱任何期望。"},{"en":"To start with no expectations whatsoever means to begin without any prediction about what will happen.","zh":"To start with no expectations whatsoever 指開始時對會發生甚麼完全沒有預測。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to observe a plant experiment and start with no expectations whatsoever.","zh":"老師可能要求學生觀察植物實驗，並一開始完全不抱任何期望。"},{"en":"Starting with no expectations can reduce bias, but it may also make results harder to interpret.","zh":"一開始不抱任何期望可以減少偏見，但也可能令結果較難解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a completely open beginning.","zh":"這個片語描述完全開放的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"no expectations whatsoever","meaning":"完全沒有任何期望","examples":[{"en":"The researcher is recommended to start with no expectations whatsoever.","zh":"研究人員被建議一開始完全沒有任何期望。"},{"en":"No expectations whatsoever means absolutely no expectations at all.","zh":"No expectations whatsoever 指絕對沒有任何期望。"},{"en":"If students enter a new club with no expectations whatsoever, they may be open to many experiences.","zh":"如果學生加入新學會時完全沒有任何期望，他們可能對許多經驗保持開放。"},{"en":"Having no expectations can prevent disappointment, but it may also make goals unclear.","zh":"沒有期望可以避免失望，但也可能令目標不清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises the complete absence of expectation.","zh":"這個片語強烈強調完全沒有期望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"see what turns up","meaning":"看看會出現甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Inductivism recommends starting with no expectations and seeing what turns up.","zh":"歸納主義建議一開始不抱任何期望，看看會出現甚麼。"},{"en":"To see what turns up means to wait and observe what appears or happens.","zh":"To see what turns up 指等待並觀察甚麼會出現或發生。"},{"en":"A student may search old family photos to see what turns up for a history project.","zh":"學生可能翻找舊家庭照片，看看會為歷史專題出現甚麼資料。"},{"en":"If researchers see what turns up without a plan, they may find surprises but also confusion.","zh":"如果研究人員沒有計劃地看看會出現甚麼，他們可能找到驚喜，也可能感到混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes open-ended searching or observation.","zh":"這個片語描述開放式搜尋或觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as in so many things","meaning":"正如很多事情一樣","examples":[{"en":"As in so many things, the ideal position lies somewhere in between.","zh":"正如很多事情一樣，理想立場處於兩者之間某處。"},{"en":"As in so many things means as happens in many other situations too.","zh":"As in so many things 指正如許多其他情況中也會發生一樣。"},{"en":"As in so many things, learning English needs both discipline and enjoyment.","zh":"正如很多事情一樣，學英語既需要紀律，也需要樂趣。"},{"en":"This phrase connects one issue to a common pattern in life.","zh":"這個片語把一個議題連接到生活中的常見模式。"},{"en":"It often prepares readers for a balanced or middle-ground answer.","zh":"它常為讀者準備一個平衡或中間立場的答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the ideal position","meaning":"理想立場","examples":[{"en":"The ideal position is widely supposed to reside somewhere between two extremes.","zh":"理想立場普遍被認為處於兩個極端之間某處。"},{"en":"The ideal position means the best or most reasonable stance in a debate.","zh":"The ideal position 指辯論中最好或最合理的立場。"},{"en":"In homework policy, the ideal position may be enough practice but not so much that students lose sleep.","zh":"在功課政策上，理想立場可能是有足夠練習，但不多到令學生失眠。"},{"en":"If two extremes are unrealistic, the ideal position may lie between them.","zh":"如果兩個極端都不現實，理想立場可能位於兩者之間。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the balanced view the writer favours.","zh":"這個片語指出作者較支持的平衡觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"widely supposed to","meaning":"普遍被認為會……","examples":[{"en":"The ideal position is widely supposed to lie between two extremes.","zh":"理想立場普遍被認為會位於兩個極端之間。"},{"en":"Widely supposed to means generally believed or assumed by many people.","zh":"Widely supposed to 指被許多人普遍相信或假定。"},{"en":"Good sleep is widely supposed to improve concentration and memory.","zh":"良好睡眠普遍被認為會改善專注力和記憶。"},{"en":"If something is widely supposed to be true, people may accept it without much argument.","zh":"如果某事普遍被認為是真實的，人們可能不太爭論便接受它。"},{"en":"This phrase reports a common belief rather than a proven fact.","zh":"這個片語報告常見信念，而不是已證明事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reside somewhere in between","meaning":"處於兩者之間某處","examples":[{"en":"The ideal position is thought to reside somewhere in between the two extremes.","zh":"理想立場被認為處於兩個極端之間某處。"},{"en":"To reside somewhere in between means to be located in the middle area between two opposite positions.","zh":"To reside somewhere in between 指位於兩個相反立場之間的中間區域。"},{"en":"The best study plan may reside somewhere in between strict scheduling and total freedom.","zh":"最佳學習計劃可能處於嚴格時間表和完全自由之間某處。"},{"en":"If both extremes fail, a workable answer often sits between them.","zh":"如果兩個極端都失敗，可行答案通常位於兩者之間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a middle-ground solution.","zh":"這個片語描述中間路線的解決方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"impossible-to-realise extremes","meaning":"無法實現的極端","examples":[{"en":"The two views are described as impossible-to-realise extremes.","zh":"這兩種觀點被描述為無法實現的極端。"},{"en":"Impossible-to-realise extremes are very strict positions that cannot realistically be achieved.","zh":"Impossible-to-realise extremes 是現實中無法達成的非常嚴格立場。"},{"en":"A plan to study every minute or never study at all would be impossible-to-realise extremes.","zh":"每分鐘都讀書或完全不讀書的計劃，都是無法實現的極端。"},{"en":"When theories are too extreme, real people cannot follow them in daily life.","zh":"當理論太極端，真實的人無法在日常生活中跟從。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises ideas that are too pure to be practical.","zh":"這個片語批評太純粹而不實際的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"good enough idea of","meaning":"對……有足夠清楚的概念","examples":[{"en":"You need a good enough idea of what you are looking for to be surprised.","zh":"你需要對自己正在尋找甚麼有足夠清楚的概念，才能感到驚訝。"},{"en":"A good enough idea of something means sufficient understanding to recognise what is relevant.","zh":"A good enough idea of something 指有足夠理解去辨認甚麼相關。"},{"en":"A student needs a good enough idea of the essay question before choosing examples.","zh":"學生在選例子前，需要對作文題目有足夠清楚的概念。"},{"en":"If you understand the goal partly, you can notice when a result is unexpected.","zh":"如果你部分理解目標，就能注意到結果何時出乎意料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes useful but not perfect knowledge.","zh":"這個片語描述有用但不完美的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be surprised when","meaning":"當……時感到驚訝","examples":[{"en":"You need to be surprised when you find something else of value.","zh":"當你找到其他有價值的東西時，你需要感到驚訝。"},{"en":"To be surprised when something happens means to notice that it is different from what you expected.","zh":"To be surprised when something happens 指注意到某事與你預期不同。"},{"en":"A teacher may be surprised when a quiet student gives the strongest answer.","zh":"當一位安靜學生給出最有力答案時，老師可能感到驚訝。"},{"en":"Surprise can signal that something important has broken the usual pattern.","zh":"驚訝可以顯示某件重要事情打破了平常模式。"},{"en":"This phrase connects unexpected events with recognition.","zh":"這個片語把意外事件與辨認連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"something else of value","meaning":"其他有價值的東西","examples":[{"en":"A scientist may find something else of value during research.","zh":"科學家可能在研究期間找到其他有價值的東西。"},{"en":"Something else of value means another useful or important thing, different from the original goal.","zh":"Something else of value 指不同於原本目標的另一個有用或重要事物。"},{"en":"A student searching for one quote may find something else of value, such as a better argument.","zh":"學生尋找一句引文時，可能找到其他有價值的東西，例如更好的論點。"},{"en":"Unexpected useful findings can change the direction of a project.","zh":"意外而有用的發現可以改變項目的方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unplanned but worthwhile result.","zh":"這個片語描述未經計劃但值得重視的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ignorant enough of","meaning":"對……不夠確定","examples":[{"en":"You need to be ignorant enough of your end point to entertain alternative outcomes.","zh":"你需要對自己的最終目標不夠確定，才能考慮其他可能結果。"},{"en":"Ignorant enough of something means not knowing it so completely that other possibilities remain open.","zh":"Ignorant enough of something 指並非完全知道某事，因此仍能開放其他可能性。"},{"en":"A designer may be ignorant enough of the final product to explore several different ideas.","zh":"設計師可能對最終產品不夠確定，因此能探索幾個不同想法。"},{"en":"If researchers are too certain, they may reject unexpected evidence too quickly.","zh":"如果研究人員太肯定，他們可能太快拒絕意外證據。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that limited ignorance can make discovery possible.","zh":"這個片語暗示有限的無知可以令發現成為可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"end point","meaning":"最終目標；終點","examples":[{"en":"A scientist should not be too certain of the end point.","zh":"科學家不應對最終目標太肯定。"},{"en":"An end point is the final result, destination, or goal of a process.","zh":"End point 是某過程的最終結果、目的地或目標。"},{"en":"In a school project, the end point may be a presentation, report, or exhibition.","zh":"在學校專題中，終點可能是一場匯報、一份報告或一個展覽。"},{"en":"If the end point is fixed too early, people may miss better possibilities.","zh":"如果終點太早被固定，人們可能錯過更好的可能性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where an activity is expected to finish.","zh":"這個片語描述活動預期在哪裏結束。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"entertain alternative outcomes","meaning":"考慮其他可能結果","examples":[{"en":"Scientists need to entertain alternative outcomes during discovery.","zh":"科學家在發現過程中需要考慮其他可能結果。"},{"en":"To entertain alternative outcomes means to consider other possible results seriously.","zh":"To entertain alternative outcomes 指認真考慮其他可能結果。"},{"en":"A student should entertain alternative outcomes when evidence does not support the first answer.","zh":"當證據不支持第一個答案時，學生應考慮其他可能結果。"},{"en":"Considering alternatives can prevent people from forcing facts into a wrong theory.","zh":"考慮其他可能性可以防止人們把事實硬塞進錯誤理論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes open-minded thinking during investigation.","zh":"這個片語描述研究期間開放心態的思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"accidental aspect","meaning":"偶然的一面","examples":[{"en":"Scientific discovery should have an accidental aspect.","zh":"科學發現應有偶然的一面。"},{"en":"An accidental aspect is a part of something that happens by chance rather than by plan.","zh":"Accidental aspect 是某事中由機遇而非計劃造成的一部分。"},{"en":"A recipe mistake may have an accidental aspect if it creates a better taste unexpectedly.","zh":"如果食譜錯誤意外創造更好味道，它就有偶然的一面。"},{"en":"In research, chance can reveal results that planning alone would not produce.","zh":"在研究中，機遇可以揭示單靠規劃不會產生的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that accident is one part of a process, not the whole process.","zh":"這個片語顯示偶然只是過程的一部分，而不是整個過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not too much of one","meaning":"但又不能太多","examples":[{"en":"Scientific discovery should have an accidental aspect, but not too much of one.","zh":"科學發現應有偶然的一面，但又不能太多。"},{"en":"Not too much of one means the element should exist, but only within limits.","zh":"Not too much of one 指某元素應該存在，但只應在限度之內。"},{"en":"A lesson can include humour, but not too much of it, or students may lose focus.","zh":"課堂可以有幽默，但又不能太多，否則學生可能失去焦點。"},{"en":"If research relies too much on accident, it may become aimless rather than scientific.","zh":"如果研究過分依賴偶然，它可能變得漫無目的，而不是科學。"},{"en":"This phrase balances acceptance with caution.","zh":"這個片語在接受與謹慎之間取得平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"expresses a position","meaning":"表達一種立場","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity expresses a position between total planning and total accident.","zh":"Serendipity 表達一種介乎完全規劃與完全偶然之間的立場。"},{"en":"To express a position means to communicate a particular view or stance.","zh":"To express a position 指傳達某種觀點或立場。"},{"en":"A school policy may express a position on discipline and student freedom.","zh":"學校政策可能表達一種關於紀律和學生自由的立場。"},{"en":"When a word expresses a position, it carries an argument, not just a definition.","zh":"當一個詞表達一種立場，它承載的是論點，而不只是定義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how language can show a viewpoint.","zh":"這個片語描述語言如何顯示觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"something like that","meaning":"類似那樣的東西","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity expresses a position something like that.","zh":"Serendipity 表達一種大概類似那樣的立場。"},{"en":"Something like that means approximately that idea, though not exactly or fully defined.","zh":"Something like that 指大約是那個意思，但不是完全精確或完整定義。"},{"en":"A teacher might say, “Good writing needs clarity, logic, confidence, something like that.”","zh":"老師可能說：「好寫作需要清晰、邏輯、自信，類似那樣的東西。」"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the speaker is giving a rough explanation.","zh":"當說話者給出粗略解釋時，這個片語很有用。"},{"en":"It signals approximation rather than precise definition.","zh":"它表示近似，而不是精確定義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the father of the sociology of science","meaning":"科學社會學之父","examples":[{"en":"Robert King Merton was called the father of the sociology of science.","zh":"Robert King Merton 被稱為科學社會學之父。"},{"en":"The father of a field means a person regarded as one of its most important founders.","zh":"The father of a field 指被視為某領域最重要創立者之一的人。"},{"en":"A scholar may be called the father of a subject if later researchers build on his ideas.","zh":"如果後來研究者建立在某學者的想法之上，他可能被稱為某學科之父。"},{"en":"Such a title gives authority, but it also simplifies the work of many other contributors.","zh":"這樣的稱號賦予權威，但也簡化了許多其他貢獻者的工作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows high historical importance in an academic field.","zh":"這個片語顯示某人在學術領域中的高度歷史重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"liked it well enough to","meaning":"十分喜歡……以致","examples":[{"en":"Merton liked the word well enough to compose its biography.","zh":"Merton 十分喜歡這個詞，以致為它撰寫傳記。"},{"en":"Liked it well enough to means liked something so much that it led to a further action.","zh":"Liked it well enough to 指十分喜歡某事，以致進一步採取行動。"},{"en":"A student liked the poem well enough to memorise it after class.","zh":"學生十分喜歡那首詩，以致課後把它背下來。"},{"en":"If someone likes an idea strongly, they may spend time researching and explaining it.","zh":"如果某人非常喜歡一個想法，他可能花時間研究和解釋它。"},{"en":"This phrase connects strong interest with action.","zh":"這個片語把強烈興趣與行動連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"compose its biography","meaning":"為它撰寫傳記","examples":[{"en":"Merton liked the word serendipity enough to compose its biography.","zh":"Merton 十分喜歡 serendipity 這個詞，以致為它撰寫傳記。"},{"en":"To compose its biography means to write the history of how a word, person, or idea developed.","zh":"To compose its biography 指撰寫某個詞、人物或想法如何發展的歷史。"},{"en":"A language teacher may compose the biography of a slang word by tracing where it first appeared.","zh":"語言老師可能透過追溯俚語首次出現的位置，為它撰寫傳記。"},{"en":"Writing a word’s biography can show how meanings change over time.","zh":"撰寫一個詞的傳記可以顯示意義如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"This phrase treats a word almost like a living thing with a life story.","zh":"這個片語把詞語幾乎視為有生命故事的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"assisted by","meaning":"在……協助下","examples":[{"en":"Merton was assisted by the French cultural historian Elinor Barber.","zh":"Merton 在法國文化史學家 Elinor Barber 協助下完成工作。"},{"en":"Assisted by someone means helped or supported by that person.","zh":"Assisted by someone 指由某人幫助或支援。"},{"en":"A teacher may be assisted by senior students during a school open day.","zh":"老師在學校開放日可能由高年級學生協助。"},{"en":"Assistance can make a difficult project more accurate and easier to complete.","zh":"協助可以令困難項目更準確，也更容易完成。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the person who helped with the work.","zh":"這個片語指出協助工作的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cultural historian","meaning":"文化史學家","examples":[{"en":"Elinor Barber was a French cultural historian.","zh":"Elinor Barber 是一位法國文化史學家。"},{"en":"A cultural historian studies how beliefs, customs, language, art, and daily life change over time.","zh":"Cultural historian 研究信念、習俗、語言、藝術和日常生活如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"A cultural historian may study how a festival changed after people moved from villages to cities.","zh":"文化史學家可能研究某節日在人們由鄉村搬到城市後如何改變。"},{"en":"Cultural historians help explain why words and ideas carry different meanings in different periods.","zh":"文化史學家幫助解釋為何詞語和想法在不同時期帶有不同意義。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a historian who focuses on culture, not only politics or wars.","zh":"這個片語指專注文化而不只是政治或戰爭的歷史學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"did not appear in","meaning":"沒有出現在……之中","examples":[{"en":"The word did not appear in the published literature until the early 19th century.","zh":"這個詞直到十九世紀初才出現在已出版文獻中。"},{"en":"Did not appear in means was not found, printed, or recorded in a particular place.","zh":"Did not appear in 指沒有在某個地方被找到、印出或記錄。"},{"en":"A student’s name did not appear in the attendance list because it was typed wrongly.","zh":"學生的名字因打錯而沒有出現在出席名單中。"},{"en":"If a term does not appear in earlier texts, it may have become common only later.","zh":"如果某術語沒有出現在較早文本中，它可能只是後來才變得常見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes absence from a record or source.","zh":"這個片語描述在紀錄或來源中缺席。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"published literature","meaning":"已出版文獻","examples":[{"en":"The word serendipity did not appear in published literature until the early 19th century.","zh":"Serendipity 這個詞直到十九世紀初才出現在已出版文獻中。"},{"en":"Published literature means written works that have been formally printed or made public.","zh":"Published literature 指已正式印刷或公開的書面作品。"},{"en":"A researcher checks published literature before claiming that an idea is new.","zh":"研究人員在聲稱某想法是新的之前，會查閱已出版文獻。"},{"en":"If a word appears in published literature, there is evidence that people used it at that time.","zh":"如果一個詞出現在已出版文獻中，就有證據顯示當時有人使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to public written records, not private notes.","zh":"這個片語指公開書面紀錄，而不是私人筆記。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the early 19th century","meaning":"十九世紀初","examples":[{"en":"The word first appeared in published literature in the early 19th century.","zh":"這個詞最早在十九世紀初出現在已出版文獻中。"},{"en":"The early 19th century means the first part of the 1800s.","zh":"The early 19th century 指十九世紀的早期，即一八零零年代初。"},{"en":"A historian may study newspapers from the early 19th century to understand social change.","zh":"歷史學家可能研究十九世紀初的報紙，以理解社會變化。"},{"en":"If a word became visible in the early 19th century, its public history is relatively recent.","zh":"如果一個詞在十九世紀初才變得可見，其公共歷史相對較近。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a historical period near the beginning of the 1800s.","zh":"這個片語指出十九世紀開端附近的歷史時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"well enough known to","meaning":"變得廣為人知至可以……","examples":[{"en":"The word did not become well enough known to use without explanation until later.","zh":"這個詞直到後來才變得廣為人知至可以不加解釋便使用。"},{"en":"Well enough known to do something means familiar enough that people can use it without extra explanation.","zh":"Well enough known to do something 指熟悉到人們可以不需額外解釋便使用。"},{"en":"A school rule may become well enough known to follow without reminders after several weeks.","zh":"幾星期後，校規可能變得廣為人知至學生不用提醒也會遵守。"},{"en":"If a term is not well known enough, writers must define it for readers.","zh":"如果術語不夠廣為人知，作者就必須為讀者定義它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a level of public familiarity.","zh":"這個片語描述公眾熟悉程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"use without explanation","meaning":"不加解釋便使用","examples":[{"en":"The word was not common enough to use without explanation.","zh":"這個詞並不常見到可以不加解釋便使用。"},{"en":"To use without explanation means to use a word or idea without defining it first.","zh":"To use without explanation 指不先定義便使用某個詞或想法。"},{"en":"A teacher should not use “photosynthesis” without explanation in a beginner class.","zh":"老師不應在初學班不加解釋便使用 “photosynthesis”。"},{"en":"If readers may not know a term, using it without explanation can confuse them.","zh":"如果讀者可能不知道某術語，不加解釋便使用它會令他們困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes assuming that the audience already understands something.","zh":"這個片語描述假設受眾已理解某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the first third of the 20th century","meaning":"二十世紀首三分之一時期","examples":[{"en":"The word became familiar sometime in the first third of the 20th century.","zh":"這個詞在二十世紀首三分之一時期某個時間變得熟悉。"},{"en":"The first third of the 20th century means roughly the period from 1900 to the early 1930s.","zh":"The first third of the 20th century 指大約由一九零零年至一九三零年代初的時期。"},{"en":"A historian might study films from the first third of the 20th century to understand early cinema.","zh":"歷史學家可能研究二十世紀首三分之一時期的電影，以理解早期電影。"},{"en":"If a word became common then, it may reflect changes in modern intellectual culture.","zh":"如果一個詞在那時變得常見，它可能反映現代知識文化的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the early portion of the twentieth century.","zh":"這個片語指出二十世紀早段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a happy accident","meaning":"幸運的意外","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity means a happy accident or pleasant surprise.","zh":"Serendipity 指幸運的意外或令人愉快的驚喜。"},{"en":"A happy accident is an unexpected event that produces a good result.","zh":"Happy accident 是產生好結果的意外事件。"},{"en":"A cook may create a new dessert by a happy accident after mixing the wrong ingredients.","zh":"廚師可能在混錯材料後，因幸運的意外創造新甜品。"},{"en":"Happy accidents matter only when someone notices their usefulness.","zh":"幸運的意外只有在有人注意到其用處時才重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes good luck that brings value.","zh":"這個片語描述帶來價值的好運。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pleasant surprise","meaning":"令人愉快的驚喜","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity can mean a pleasant surprise.","zh":"Serendipity 可以指令人愉快的驚喜。"},{"en":"A pleasant surprise is something unexpected that makes people happy or interested.","zh":"Pleasant surprise 是令人快樂或感興趣的意外事情。"},{"en":"Finding an old photo inside a second-hand book can be a pleasant surprise.","zh":"在二手書中找到一張舊照片，可以是令人愉快的驚喜。"},{"en":"Pleasant surprises can change a normal day into a memorable one.","zh":"令人愉快的驚喜可以把普通一天變成值得記住的一天。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unexpected good news or discovery.","zh":"這個片語描述意想不到的好消息或發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"specifically","meaning":"具體來說","examples":[{"en":"Specifically, serendipity refers to finding something useful without looking for it.","zh":"具體來說，serendipity 指並非刻意尋找，卻找到有用的東西。"},{"en":"Specifically means more exactly or in more detailed terms.","zh":"Specifically 指更準確或以更詳細方式來說。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “You need to revise grammar; specifically, verb tenses and articles.”","zh":"老師可能說：「你需要溫習文法；具體來說，是動詞時態和冠詞。」"},{"en":"This word helps move from a general idea to a clearer explanation.","zh":"這個詞幫助由一般想法轉向更清楚解釋。"},{"en":"It is useful when the writer wants to narrow the meaning.","zh":"當作者想縮窄意思時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"finding something good or useful","meaning":"找到好或有用的東西","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity involves finding something good or useful without looking for it.","zh":"Serendipity 涉及並非刻意尋找，卻找到好或有用的東西。"},{"en":"Finding something good or useful means discovering something valuable, helpful, or beneficial.","zh":"Finding something good or useful 指發現有價值、有幫助或有益的東西。"},{"en":"A student may find something good or useful when old notes reveal an idea for a new essay.","zh":"當舊筆記揭示新文章想法時，學生可能找到好或有用的東西。"},{"en":"Unexpected usefulness can make a small event important.","zh":"意想不到的用處可以令小事件變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the positive value of what is discovered.","zh":"這個片語集中於被發現事物的正面價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"without looking for it","meaning":"並非刻意尋找它","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity means finding something useful without looking for it.","zh":"Serendipity 指並非刻意尋找，卻找到有用的東西。"},{"en":"Without looking for it means without intentionally searching for that specific thing.","zh":"Without looking for it 指沒有刻意搜尋那個特定東西。"},{"en":"A reader may learn a useful phrase without looking for it while reading a novel.","zh":"讀者閱讀小說時，可能並非刻意尋找，卻學到有用片語。"},{"en":"If someone finds value without looking for it, chance has played a role.","zh":"如果某人並非刻意尋找卻找到價值，機遇就發揮了作用。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights accidental discovery rather than planned search.","zh":"這個片語突出偶然發現，而不是有計劃搜尋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the first noted use of","meaning":"首次有記載的用法","examples":[{"en":"The first noted use of “serendipity” in English was by Horace Walpole.","zh":"“Serendipity” 在英語中首次有記載的用法出自 Horace Walpole。"},{"en":"The first noted use of a word means the earliest recorded example scholars have identified.","zh":"The first noted use of a word 指學者找到的最早記錄例子。"},{"en":"A dictionary may list the first noted use of a slang word in newspapers or letters.","zh":"字典可能列出俚語在報紙或信件中的首次有記載用法。"},{"en":"Knowing the first noted use helps trace how a word entered public language.","zh":"知道首次有記載用法，有助追溯詞語如何進入公共語言。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on historical evidence of usage.","zh":"這個片語集中於用法的歷史證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the English language","meaning":"在英語中","examples":[{"en":"The first noted use of the word in the English language was by Horace Walpole.","zh":"這個詞在英語中首次有記載的用法出自 Horace Walpole。"},{"en":"In the English language means within English as a system of words and usage.","zh":"In the English language 指在英語這個詞語和用法系統之內。"},{"en":"Some words in the English language come from French, Latin, Arabic, or Hindi.","zh":"英語中的一些詞來自法語、拉丁語、阿拉伯語或印地語。"},{"en":"If a term enters the English language, speakers can begin using it in new contexts.","zh":"如果一個術語進入英語，說話者便可以在新語境中使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the language in which a word appears.","zh":"這個片語指出詞語出現在哪種語言中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"came from","meaning":"來自……","examples":[{"en":"Walpole explained that the word came from a fairy tale.","zh":"Walpole 解釋這個詞來自一個童話故事。"},{"en":"Came from means originated in or was taken from a particular source.","zh":"Came from 指起源於或取自某個來源。"},{"en":"A family recipe may have come from a grandmother’s handwritten notebook.","zh":"家庭食譜可能來自祖母的手寫筆記本。"},{"en":"Knowing where an idea came from can help explain its meaning.","zh":"知道一個想法來自哪裏，可以幫助解釋其意思。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies origin or source.","zh":"這個片語指出起源或來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fairy tale","meaning":"童話故事","examples":[{"en":"The word serendipity came from a fairy tale.","zh":"Serendipity 這個詞來自一個童話故事。"},{"en":"A fairy tale is a traditional story often involving magic, princes, strange journeys, or moral lessons.","zh":"Fairy tale 是常涉及魔法、王子、奇異旅程或道德教訓的傳統故事。"},{"en":"Children may learn courage or kindness through a fairy tale told at bedtime.","zh":"孩子可能透過睡前童話故事學到勇氣或善良。"},{"en":"Fairy tales can preserve old cultural values while entertaining listeners.","zh":"童話故事可以在娛樂聽眾的同時保存古老文化價值。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to imaginative traditional stories, not factual history.","zh":"這個片語指富想像力的傳統故事，而不是真實歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the ancient name for","meaning":"……的古名","examples":[{"en":"Serendip was the ancient name for Ceylon.","zh":"Serendip 是 Ceylon 的古名。"},{"en":"The ancient name for a place means the old name used for it in earlier times.","zh":"The ancient name for a place 指某地方在較早時期使用的舊名稱。"},{"en":"A history teacher may explain that Edo was the ancient name for Tokyo.","zh":"歷史老師可能解釋 Edo 是東京的古名。"},{"en":"Ancient names can reveal how places were known before political or cultural changes.","zh":"古名可以揭示地方在政治或文化變化前如何被稱呼。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a modern place with its older name.","zh":"這個片語把現代地方與其舊名稱連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"present-day","meaning":"現今的……","examples":[{"en":"Ceylon is present-day Sri Lanka.","zh":"Ceylon 是現今的 Sri Lanka。"},{"en":"Present-day means the modern name, form, or situation of something now.","zh":"Present-day 指某事物現在的現代名稱、形式或情況。"},{"en":"Ancient Rome was located partly in present-day Italy.","zh":"古羅馬部分位於現今的意大利。"},{"en":"Using present-day names helps readers connect history with modern geography.","zh":"使用現今名稱幫助讀者把歷史與現代地理連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase links the past with the current world.","zh":"這個片語把過去與當前世界連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"by accidents and sagacity","meaning":"憑藉意外和敏銳判斷","examples":[{"en":"The heroes made discoveries by accidents and sagacity.","zh":"英雄們憑藉意外和敏銳判斷作出發現。"},{"en":"By accidents and sagacity means through chance events combined with wise judgement.","zh":"By accidents and sagacity 指透過偶然事件加上明智判斷。"},{"en":"A doctor may notice a strange symptom by accident and use sagacity to understand its meaning.","zh":"醫生可能偶然注意到奇怪症狀，並運用敏銳判斷理解其意義。"},{"en":"Accident alone is not enough if no one has the insight to interpret it.","zh":"如果沒有人有洞察力去解讀，單靠意外是不夠的。"},{"en":"This phrase combines luck with intelligence.","zh":"這個片語結合運氣與智慧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sagacity","meaning":"智慧；敏銳判斷力","examples":[{"en":"The princes made discoveries by accidents and sagacity.","zh":"王子們憑藉意外和敏銳判斷作出發現。"},{"en":"Sagacity means wisdom, sharp judgement, and the ability to understand what is important.","zh":"Sagacity 指智慧、敏銳判斷，以及理解甚麼重要的能力。"},{"en":"A teacher shows sagacity when she notices that a quiet student is confused but afraid to ask.","zh":"當老師注意到一位安靜學生困惑但不敢提問時，她展現出敏銳判斷力。"},{"en":"Sagacity helps people turn small clues into useful understanding.","zh":"敏銳判斷力幫助人把小線索轉化成有用理解。"},{"en":"This word describes intelligent judgement, not just knowledge.","zh":"這個詞描述聰明判斷，而不只是知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not in quest of","meaning":"並非正在尋找的","examples":[{"en":"The princes discovered things which they were not in quest of.","zh":"王子們發現了他們並非正在尋找的東西。"},{"en":"Not in quest of means not actively searching for that thing.","zh":"Not in quest of 指沒有主動尋找某物。"},{"en":"A student may find an excellent quote while not in quest of it but while checking another source.","zh":"學生可能在查另一個來源時，找到一句自己並非正在尋找的精彩引文。"},{"en":"If you are not in quest of something, finding it can feel accidental.","zh":"如果你並非正在尋找某物，找到它就會感覺偶然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes discovery outside the original search.","zh":"這個片語描述在原本搜尋以外的發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"antiquarians","meaning":"古物研究者；古物收藏家","examples":[{"en":"Antiquarians found the word serendipity useful.","zh":"古物研究者覺得 serendipity 這個詞有用。"},{"en":"Antiquarians are people who study, collect, or search for old objects, books, or historical curiosities.","zh":"Antiquarians 是研究、收藏或搜尋舊物、舊書或歷史奇珍的人。"},{"en":"An antiquarian may spend weekends looking through old maps and coins in a market.","zh":"古物收藏家可能週末在市場翻找舊地圖和硬幣。"},{"en":"Because antiquarians often find unexpected objects, serendipity describes their work well.","zh":"因為古物研究者常找到意想不到的物件，serendipity 很好地描述了他們的工作。"},{"en":"This word refers to people interested in old and rare things.","zh":"這個詞指對古老和稀有事物感興趣的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"following Walpole","meaning":"跟隨華波爾之後","examples":[{"en":"Antiquarians, following Walpole, found the word useful.","zh":"古物研究者跟隨華波爾之後，覺得這個詞有用。"},{"en":"Following Walpole means after Walpole’s example or influence.","zh":"Following Walpole 指在 Walpole 的例子或影響之後。"},{"en":"Following a teacher’s advice, a student may rewrite the introduction before changing the whole essay.","zh":"學生跟隨老師建議後，可能先重寫引言，再改整篇文章。"},{"en":"When people follow an influential writer, his words and ideas spread further.","zh":"當人們跟隨有影響力的作者，他的詞語和想法會傳得更遠。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that later users adopted an earlier person’s lead.","zh":"這個片語顯示後來使用者採納較早人物的引導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"found it useful","meaning":"覺得它有用","examples":[{"en":"Antiquarians found the word useful because they often discovered curiosities.","zh":"古物研究者覺得這個詞有用，因為他們常發現奇珍異物。"},{"en":"Found it useful means considered it helpful for explaining, doing, or understanding something.","zh":"Found it useful 指認為某事有助於解釋、完成或理解某事。"},{"en":"Students found the checklist useful because it reminded them to check grammar before submitting essays.","zh":"學生覺得檢查清單有用，因為它提醒他們交作文前檢查文法。"},{"en":"If a word describes an experience clearly, people are likely to find it useful.","zh":"如果一個詞清楚描述某種經驗，人們就很可能覺得它有用。"},{"en":"This phrase shows practical value from the user’s point of view.","zh":"這個片語從使用者角度顯示實際價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rummaging about for","meaning":"翻找；四處搜尋","examples":[{"en":"Antiquarians were always rummaging about for curiosities.","zh":"古物研究者總是在翻找奇珍異物。"},{"en":"Rummaging about for something means searching through many things in a slightly messy or informal way.","zh":"Rummaging about for something 指以有點凌亂或非正式的方式在許多東西中搜尋。"},{"en":"A student may rummage about for old notes before an exam.","zh":"學生考試前可能翻找舊筆記。"},{"en":"Rummaging about can lead to unexpected finds because the search is not perfectly controlled.","zh":"翻找可能帶來意想不到的發現，因為搜尋不是完全受控的。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active but somewhat untidy searching.","zh":"這個片語暗示主動但有點凌亂的搜尋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"curiosities","meaning":"奇珍異物","examples":[{"en":"Antiquarians often rummaged about for curiosities.","zh":"古物研究者常四處搜尋奇珍異物。"},{"en":"Curiosities are unusual, interesting, or rare objects that attract attention.","zh":"Curiosities 是不尋常、有趣或稀有而吸引注意的物件。"},{"en":"A flea market may be full of curiosities such as old postcards, coins, and broken clocks.","zh":"跳蚤市場可能充滿奇珍異物，例如舊明信片、硬幣和壞鐘。"},{"en":"Curiosities make people look more closely because they do not fit ordinary categories.","zh":"奇珍異物令人更仔細觀看，因為它們不符合普通類別。"},{"en":"This word describes strange or interesting things people may want to collect or study.","zh":"這個詞描述人們可能想收藏或研究的奇怪有趣東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"unexpected but pleasant surprises","meaning":"意想不到但令人愉快的驚喜","examples":[{"en":"Unexpected but pleasant surprises were not unknown to antiquarians.","zh":"意想不到但令人愉快的驚喜對古物研究者來說並不陌生。"},{"en":"Unexpected but pleasant surprises are good events or discoveries that people did not predict.","zh":"Unexpected but pleasant surprises 是人們沒有預測到的好事件或發現。"},{"en":"Finding a forgotten birthday card inside an old book can be an unexpected but pleasant surprise.","zh":"在舊書中找到一張被遺忘的生日卡，可以是意想不到但令人愉快的驚喜。"},{"en":"Such surprises feel rewarding because they arrive without being planned.","zh":"這類驚喜令人覺得有回報，因為它們並非經計劃而來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes chance events that bring enjoyment or value.","zh":"這個片語描述帶來快樂或價值的偶然事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not unknown to","meaning":"對……來說並不陌生","examples":[{"en":"Unexpected surprises were not unknown to antiquarians.","zh":"意外驚喜對古物研究者來說並不陌生。"},{"en":"Not unknown to someone means something has been experienced or recognised by that person or group before.","zh":"Not unknown to someone 指某人或某群體以前曾經經歷或認出某事。"},{"en":"Stress before exams is not unknown to hardworking students.","zh":"考試前壓力對勤奮學生來說並不陌生。"},{"en":"If a problem is not unknown to a team, they may already have ways to deal with it.","zh":"如果某問題對團隊來說並不陌生，他們可能已有處理方法。"},{"en":"This phrase means familiar to some degree, but in a formal style.","zh":"這個片語以正式風格表示某事有一定熟悉度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have a knack for","meaning":"有……的本領；有……的天賦","examples":[{"en":"Some people seemed to have a knack for making such discoveries.","zh":"有些人似乎有作出這類發現的本領。"},{"en":"To have a knack for something means to have a natural or practised ability to do it well.","zh":"To have a knack for something 指有自然或練習得來的能力，能把某事做好。"},{"en":"A teacher may have a knack for explaining difficult grammar in simple examples.","zh":"老師可能有用簡單例子解釋困難文法的本領。"},{"en":"People with a knack for noticing details often find clues others miss.","zh":"有注意細節本領的人，常找到其他人錯過的線索。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a special ability that may look effortless.","zh":"這個片語描述一種看似輕鬆的特殊能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"that sort of thing","meaning":"那類事情","examples":[{"en":"Some people seemed to have a knack for that sort of thing.","zh":"有些人似乎有做那類事情的本領。"},{"en":"That sort of thing means that kind of activity, event, skill, or situation.","zh":"That sort of thing 指那一類活動、事件、技能或情況。"},{"en":"Some students are good at organising notes, planning revision, and that sort of thing.","zh":"有些學生擅長整理筆記、規劃溫習和那類事情。"},{"en":"This phrase groups similar examples without listing every one.","zh":"這個片語把相似例子歸在一起，而不用逐一列出。"},{"en":"It is common in informal explanation when the exact category is already clear.","zh":"當準確類別已清楚時，它常見於非正式解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"special capacity","meaning":"特殊能力","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity was used to express that special capacity.","zh":"Serendipity 被用來表達那種特殊能力。"},{"en":"A special capacity is an unusual ability or power to do something.","zh":"Special capacity 是做某事的不尋常能力或力量。"},{"en":"A nurse may have a special capacity for calming frightened patients.","zh":"護士可能有安撫受驚病人的特殊能力。"},{"en":"If someone repeatedly notices useful accidents, people may think they possess a special capacity.","zh":"如果某人反覆注意到有用的意外，人們可能認為他擁有特殊能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an ability that seems different from ordinary skill.","zh":"這個片語描述一種似乎不同於普通技能的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"came to dwell on","meaning":"開始深入思考；開始重視","examples":[{"en":"Scientists also came to dwell on serendipity.","zh":"科學家也開始深入思考 serendipity。"},{"en":"To come to dwell on something means to begin thinking about it deeply or repeatedly.","zh":"To come to dwell on something 指開始深入或反覆思考某事。"},{"en":"After failing an exam, a student may come to dwell on how they studied, not just on the score.","zh":"考試失敗後，學生可能開始深入思考自己如何溫習，而不只是分數。"},{"en":"When an idea seems important, people may return to it again and again.","zh":"當一個想法似乎重要，人們可能反覆回到它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growing attention to a topic.","zh":"這個片語描述對某題目的關注增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"say something important about","meaning":"表達關於……的重要事情","examples":[{"en":"Scientists used serendipity to say something important about their practice.","zh":"科學家使用 serendipity 來表達關於其實踐的重要事情。"},{"en":"To say something important about something means to reveal a meaningful point about it.","zh":"To say something important about something 指揭示關於某事的有意義重點。"},{"en":"A student’s mistake may say something important about how the class understands a grammar rule.","zh":"學生的錯誤可能表達關於全班如何理解某文法規則的重要事情。"},{"en":"If one word explains a whole attitude, it can say something important about a culture.","zh":"如果一個詞解釋了整種態度，它可以表達關於某文化的重要事情。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a statement or idea that reveals deeper meaning.","zh":"這個片語描述揭示深層意義的陳述或想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"scientific practice","meaning":"科學實踐","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity said something important about scientific practice.","zh":"Serendipity 表達了關於科學實踐的重要事情。"},{"en":"Scientific practice means what scientists actually do when they design, conduct, and interpret research.","zh":"Scientific practice 指科學家在設計、進行和解釋研究時實際做的事情。"},{"en":"Careful note-taking is part of scientific practice because unexpected details may matter later.","zh":"仔細記錄是科學實踐的一部分，因為意外細節日後可能重要。"},{"en":"Scientific practice includes planning, observing, doubting, testing, and revising ideas.","zh":"科學實踐包括規劃、觀察、懷疑、測試和修正想法。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on science as real work, not only abstract method.","zh":"這個片語集中於科學作為真實工作，而不只是抽象方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cut to the heart of the matter","meaning":"觸及問題核心","examples":[{"en":"Scientific uses of the word cut to the heart of the matter.","zh":"這個詞在科學上的用法觸及問題核心。"},{"en":"To cut to the heart of the matter means to reach the central issue directly.","zh":"To cut to the heart of the matter 指直接到達核心議題。"},{"en":"A teacher cuts to the heart of the matter when she asks why students cannot use grammar in real writing.","zh":"當老師問學生為何不能在真實寫作中使用文法時，她就觸及問題核心。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when an idea avoids surface details and reaches the main problem.","zh":"當一個想法避開表面細節並到達主要問題時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It suggests directness, clarity, and importance.","zh":"它暗示直接、清晰和重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"vigorously contested","meaning":"受到激烈爭論","examples":[{"en":"The meaning of serendipity was often vigorously contested.","zh":"Serendipity 的意思常受到激烈爭論。"},{"en":"Vigorously contested means strongly argued about by people with different views.","zh":"Vigorously contested 指由持不同觀點的人強烈爭論。"},{"en":"A school’s phone ban may be vigorously contested by parents, teachers, and students.","zh":"學校禁用手機的政策可能受到家長、老師和學生激烈爭論。"},{"en":"When a word affects authority or status, its meaning can become fiercely debated.","zh":"當一個詞影響權威或地位，其意思可能變得備受激烈討論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intense disagreement.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"physiologist","meaning":"生理學家","examples":[{"en":"Walter Cannon was a Harvard physiologist.","zh":"Walter Cannon 是哈佛大學的生理學家。"},{"en":"A physiologist is a scientist who studies how living bodies and their organs work.","zh":"Physiologist 是研究生命體及其器官如何運作的科學家。"},{"en":"A physiologist may study how the heart responds when a person exercises.","zh":"生理學家可能研究人運動時心臟如何反應。"},{"en":"Physiologists help explain bodily processes such as breathing, stress, and digestion.","zh":"生理學家幫助解釋呼吸、壓力和消化等身體過程。"},{"en":"This word refers to a scientist focused on body functions.","zh":"這個詞指專注身體功能的科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"immunologist","meaning":"免疫學家","examples":[{"en":"Peter Medawar was a British immunologist.","zh":"Peter Medawar 是英國免疫學家。"},{"en":"An immunologist is a scientist or doctor who studies the immune system.","zh":"Immunologist 是研究免疫系統的科學家或醫生。"},{"en":"An immunologist may investigate why some people react badly to certain vaccines or allergens.","zh":"免疫學家可能研究為何某些人對特定疫苗或致敏原反應不良。"},{"en":"Immunologists help explain how the body fights disease.","zh":"免疫學家幫助解釋身體如何對抗疾病。"},{"en":"This word refers to an expert in immunity and disease defence.","zh":"這個詞指免疫和疾病防禦方面的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"liked to emphasise","meaning":"喜歡強調","examples":[{"en":"Many scientists liked to emphasise the accidental nature of discovery.","zh":"許多科學家喜歡強調發現的偶然性。"},{"en":"Liked to emphasise means often chose to stress or highlight a particular point.","zh":"Liked to emphasise 指常選擇強調或突出某個重點。"},{"en":"A teacher may like to emphasise planning because students often start essays too quickly.","zh":"老師可能喜歡強調規劃，因為學生常太快開始寫作文。"},{"en":"If people emphasise one idea repeatedly, they want others to remember its importance.","zh":"如果人們反覆強調一個想法，他們希望別人記住其重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a preferred focus in explanation.","zh":"這個片語顯示解釋中的偏好焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"unplanned and even accidental","meaning":"未經計劃甚至偶然的","examples":[{"en":"They emphasised that much scientific discovery was unplanned and even accidental.","zh":"他們強調許多科學發現是未經計劃甚至偶然的。"},{"en":"Unplanned and even accidental means not arranged in advance and sometimes happening by chance.","zh":"Unplanned and even accidental 指不是事先安排，有時是靠機遇發生。"},{"en":"A useful friendship may be unplanned and even accidental when two classmates sit together by chance.","zh":"當兩位同學偶然坐在一起，一段有用友誼可能是未經計劃甚至偶然的。"},{"en":"If discoveries are unplanned, strict methods cannot explain everything about science.","zh":"如果發現是未經計劃的，嚴格方法就無法解釋科學的一切。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that chance may play a real role.","zh":"這個片語強調機遇可能真的發揮作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"discovery of electromagnetism","meaning":"電磁學的發現","examples":[{"en":"Ørsted’s discovery of electromagnetism is given as an example.","zh":"Ørsted 的電磁學發現被作為例子。"},{"en":"The discovery of electromagnetism means the finding that electricity and magnetism are connected.","zh":"The discovery of electromagnetism 指發現電與磁之間有聯繫。"},{"en":"A physics teacher may use the discovery of electromagnetism to show how observation can change science.","zh":"物理老師可能用電磁學的發現來展示觀察如何改變科學。"},{"en":"This discovery became important because it helped later technologies such as motors and generators develop.","zh":"這項發現變得重要，因為它幫助後來的馬達和發電機等技術發展。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a major scientific finding about electric currents and magnetic effects.","zh":"這個片語指關於電流和磁效應的重要科學發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"unintentionally brought","meaning":"無意中把……帶到","examples":[{"en":"Ørsted unintentionally brought a current-carrying wire near a magnetic needle.","zh":"Ørsted 無意中把一條載有電流的電線帶近一支磁針。"},{"en":"Unintentionally brought means moved or placed something somewhere without planning that effect.","zh":"Unintentionally brought 指沒有計劃該效果而移動或放置某物到某處。"},{"en":"A student may unintentionally bring the wrong notebook to class and discover useful old notes inside.","zh":"學生可能無意中把錯誤筆記簿帶到課堂，卻在裏面發現有用舊筆記。"},{"en":"Unintentional actions can matter when they create unexpected results.","zh":"當無意行動產生意外結果，它就可能重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accidental action rather than deliberate choice.","zh":"這個片語描述偶然行動，而不是刻意選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"current-carrying wire","meaning":"載有電流的電線","examples":[{"en":"Ørsted used a current-carrying wire in his experiment.","zh":"Ørsted 在實驗中使用了一條載有電流的電線。"},{"en":"A current-carrying wire is a wire through which electric current is flowing.","zh":"Current-carrying wire 是有電流流過的電線。"},{"en":"In a school physics lab, a current-carrying wire may be placed near a compass to show magnetic effects.","zh":"在學校物理實驗室中，載有電流的電線可能被放在指南針附近，以展示磁效應。"},{"en":"If current flows through a wire, it can create a magnetic field around it.","zh":"如果電流流過電線，它可以在周圍產生磁場。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a wire that is actively carrying electricity.","zh":"這個片語描述正在傳導電力的電線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"parallel to","meaning":"與……平行","examples":[{"en":"The wire was brought parallel to a magnetic needle.","zh":"電線被帶到與磁針平行的位置。"},{"en":"Parallel to means lying or moving in the same direction while staying the same distance apart.","zh":"Parallel to 指位於或移動於相同方向，同時保持相同距離。"},{"en":"Two desks are parallel to each other if their edges run in the same direction.","zh":"如果兩張書桌邊緣朝同一方向延伸，它們就是彼此平行。"},{"en":"In experiments, placing objects parallel to each other can change what researchers observe.","zh":"在實驗中，把物件放成彼此平行可能改變研究人員觀察到的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase describes alignment or direction.","zh":"這個片語描述排列或方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"magnetic needle","meaning":"磁針","examples":[{"en":"The current-carrying wire was placed near a magnetic needle.","zh":"載有電流的電線被放在磁針附近。"},{"en":"A magnetic needle is a small magnetised pointer, like the needle in a compass.","zh":"Magnetic needle 是一支小型磁化指針，例如指南針內的指針。"},{"en":"A magnetic needle can move when it is affected by a magnetic field.","zh":"磁針受到磁場影響時可以移動。"},{"en":"If a nearby wire changes the needle’s direction, the observer may suspect a link between electricity and magnetism.","zh":"如果附近電線改變磁針方向，觀察者可能懷疑電與磁之間有聯繫。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a tool used to detect magnetic effects.","zh":"這個片語指用來偵測磁效應的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the rhetoric about","meaning":"關於……的漂亮說辭","examples":[{"en":"The rhetoric about the sufficiency of the rational method was so much hot air.","zh":"關於理性方法充分性的漂亮說辭只是空話。"},{"en":"The rhetoric about something means the impressive-sounding language used to discuss or defend it.","zh":"The rhetoric about something 指用來討論或捍衛某事的聽起來有氣勢的語言。"},{"en":"The rhetoric about school reform may sound attractive, but students need real support.","zh":"關於教育改革的漂亮說辭可能聽起來吸引，但學生需要真正支援。"},{"en":"If rhetoric hides weak evidence, people may mistake words for truth.","zh":"如果修辭掩蓋薄弱證據，人們可能把說話誤當真理。"},{"en":"This phrase can criticise language that sounds grand but lacks substance.","zh":"這個片語可批評聽起來宏大但缺乏實質的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the sufficiency of","meaning":"……的充分性","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists questioned the sufficiency of the rational method.","zh":"一些科學家質疑理性方法的充分性。"},{"en":"The sufficiency of something means whether it is enough for the purpose.","zh":"The sufficiency of something 指某事是否足以達到目的。"},{"en":"A teacher may question the sufficiency of one mock exam to prepare students for the real test.","zh":"老師可能質疑一次模擬考是否足以讓學生準備真實考試。"},{"en":"If a method cannot explain accidents, its sufficiency is doubtful.","zh":"如果方法不能解釋偶然事件，其充分性就令人懷疑。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether something alone is adequate.","zh":"這個片語集中於某事單靠自身是否足夠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rational method","meaning":"理性方法","examples":[{"en":"Medawar rejected the idea that discovery follows one rational method.","zh":"Medawar 拒絕發現遵循單一理性方法的想法。"},{"en":"A rational method is a logical, orderly way of solving problems or reaching conclusions.","zh":"Rational method 是用邏輯、有條理方式解決問題或得出結論。"},{"en":"A student uses a rational method when they test each answer against evidence.","zh":"學生把每個答案與證據對照時，就是使用理性方法。"},{"en":"Rational methods are useful, but they may not capture every surprise in discovery.","zh":"理性方法有用，但未必能捕捉發現中的每個驚喜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised reasoning rather than luck or feeling.","zh":"這個片語描述有組織推理，而不是運氣或感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"so much hot air","meaning":"空話；誇誇其談","examples":[{"en":"The claim about a single rational method was so much hot air.","zh":"關於單一理性方法的說法只是空話。"},{"en":"So much hot air means empty talk that sounds important but has little real value.","zh":"So much hot air 指聽起來重要但實際價值很少的空話。"},{"en":"A company’s promise to care about workers is so much hot air if wages remain unfair.","zh":"如果工資仍然不公平，公司聲稱關心工人的承諾就是空話。"},{"en":"If grand words are not matched by evidence or action, they become hot air.","zh":"如果宏大說話沒有證據或行動配合，它們就變成空話。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly criticises meaningless talk.","zh":"這個片語強烈批評無意義說話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"insisted","meaning":"堅稱","examples":[{"en":"Medawar insisted that there was no such thing as The Scientific Method.","zh":"Medawar 堅稱根本沒有「科學方法」這回事。"},{"en":"Insisted means stated firmly and refused to soften the claim.","zh":"Insisted 指堅定地陳述，並拒絕淡化該主張。"},{"en":"A teacher insisted that students show their working, not just the final answer.","zh":"老師堅稱學生必須展示步驟，而不只是最終答案。"},{"en":"If someone insists on a point, they believe it matters and should not be ignored.","zh":"如果某人堅持某點，他相信它重要且不應被忽視。"},{"en":"This word shows firmness and strong belief.","zh":"這個詞顯示堅定和強烈信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"no such thing as","meaning":"根本沒有……這回事","examples":[{"en":"Medawar argued that there was no such thing as The Scientific Method.","zh":"Medawar 認為根本沒有「科學方法」這回事。"},{"en":"No such thing as means that the thing named does not really exist in the claimed form.","zh":"No such thing as 指所說的事物並不以人們聲稱的形式真正存在。"},{"en":"There is no such thing as perfect revision if a student never sleeps.","zh":"如果學生從不睡覺，根本沒有完美溫習這回事。"},{"en":"If people say there is no such thing as one fixed method, they reject over-simple rules.","zh":"如果人們說根本沒有單一固定方法這回事，他們是在拒絕過分簡化的規則。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly denies the existence of a claimed idea or object.","zh":"這個片語強烈否定某個被聲稱的想法或物件存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"The Scientific Method","meaning":"科學方法","examples":[{"en":"Medawar denied that there was one fixed Scientific Method.","zh":"Medawar 否認存在一套固定的科學方法。"},{"en":"The Scientific Method usually refers to an organised way of asking questions, testing ideas, and using evidence.","zh":"The Scientific Method 通常指一種有組織地提出問題、測試想法和使用證據的方法。"},{"en":"In school, students may learn The Scientific Method as observation, hypothesis, experiment, and conclusion.","zh":"在學校，學生可能把科學方法學成觀察、假設、實驗和結論。"},{"en":"Medawar’s point was that real discovery may not follow one neat set of steps.","zh":"Medawar 的重點是，真實發現未必遵循一套整齊步驟。"},{"en":"This phrase represents the idea of a single orderly method for science.","zh":"這個片語代表科學有單一有序方法的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"systematising the process of discovery","meaning":"將發現過程系統化","examples":[{"en":"Medawar saw no way of systematising the process of discovery.","zh":"Medawar 看不到有方法將發現過程系統化。"},{"en":"Systematising the process of discovery means turning discovery into a fixed, organised procedure.","zh":"Systematising the process of discovery 指把發現變成固定、有組織的程序。"},{"en":"A school may systematise essay writing by giving students planning steps, but creativity still matters.","zh":"學校可能透過給學生規劃步驟來把寫作系統化，但創意仍然重要。"},{"en":"If discovery depends on surprise, it cannot be fully reduced to a system.","zh":"如果發現依賴驚喜，它就不能完全被化約為一套系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trying to make discovery follow a formal method.","zh":"這個片語描述嘗試令發現遵循正式方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the process of discovery","meaning":"發現的過程","examples":[{"en":"The process of discovery cannot always be systematised.","zh":"發現的過程不能總是被系統化。"},{"en":"The process of discovery is the way new knowledge, ideas, or facts are found and recognised.","zh":"The process of discovery 是新知識、想法或事實被找到並辨認的方式。"},{"en":"In a science project, the process of discovery may include mistakes, questions, tests, and surprises.","zh":"在科學專題中，發現的過程可能包括錯誤、問題、測試和驚喜。"},{"en":"If researchers record the process carefully, they can learn from unexpected results.","zh":"如果研究人員仔細記錄過程，他們可以從意外結果中學習。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how discovery happens, not only what is found.","zh":"這個片語集中於發現如何發生，而不只是發現了甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"had a way of showing up","meaning":"往往會出現","examples":[{"en":"Important discoveries had a way of showing up unexpectedly.","zh":"重要發現往往會意外出現。"},{"en":"Had a way of showing up means tended to appear or happen, often in a noticeable pattern.","zh":"Had a way of showing up 指往往會出現或發生，常帶有可注意到的模式。"},{"en":"Problems have a way of showing up when people rush and skip checking.","zh":"當人們匆忙並跳過檢查，問題往往會出現。"},{"en":"If useful ideas show up unexpectedly, researchers must be ready to notice them.","zh":"如果有用想法意外出現，研究人員必須準備好注意它們。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a repeated tendency rather than a strict rule.","zh":"這個片語暗示反覆傾向，而不是嚴格規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"when they had a mind to do so","meaning":"在它們自己似乎想出現的時候","examples":[{"en":"Important discoveries appeared when they had a mind to do so.","zh":"重要發現會在它們自己似乎想出現的時候出現。"},{"en":"When they had a mind to do so means when they seemed ready or willing to appear, as if they had their own intention.","zh":"When they had a mind to do so 指在它們似乎準備好或願意出現的時候，好像它們有自己的意願。"},{"en":"A writer may jokingly say ideas come only when they have a mind to do so.","zh":"作家可能開玩笑說，靈感只在它自己似乎想出現的時候才來。"},{"en":"This phrase personifies events by making them seem independent of human planning.","zh":"這個片語把事件擬人化，使它們看似不受人類規劃控制。"},{"en":"It suggests that discovery cannot be fully controlled.","zh":"它暗示發現不能被完全控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not when you were looking for them","meaning":"而不是在你尋找它們的時候","examples":[{"en":"Important discoveries often appeared when researchers were not looking for them.","zh":"重要發現常在研究人員不是正在尋找它們時出現。"},{"en":"Not when you were looking for them means not during the planned search for that specific thing.","zh":"Not when you were looking for them 指不是在有計劃尋找那個特定事物期間。"},{"en":"A student may find a useful example while not looking for it, but while reading for another topic.","zh":"學生可能不是在尋找有用例子時，而是在閱讀另一題目時找到它。"},{"en":"If something appears outside the intended search, it may feel accidental.","zh":"如果某事出現在原定搜尋之外，它可能感覺偶然。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the gap between intention and result.","zh":"這個片語突出意圖與結果之間的落差。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"book collectors","meaning":"藏書家","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists may have a happy knack, like some book collectors.","zh":"有些科學家可能像某些藏書家一樣，有幸運的本領。"},{"en":"Book collectors are people who search for, buy, preserve, or study books, often rare or old ones.","zh":"Book collectors 是搜尋、購買、保存或研究書籍的人，通常尤其關注稀有或舊書。"},{"en":"Book collectors may find a valuable first edition in a small second-hand shop.","zh":"藏書家可能在小型二手書店找到珍貴初版書。"},{"en":"Because book collectors often search widely, chance can reward their patience.","zh":"因為藏書家常廣泛搜尋，機遇可以回報他們的耐心。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people who collect books as a serious interest.","zh":"這個片語指把收藏書籍作為認真興趣的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a happy knack","meaning":"幸運的本領","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists may have a happy knack for discovery.","zh":"有些科學家可能有作出發現的幸運本領。"},{"en":"A happy knack is a fortunate talent for doing something well, often without seeming to try hard.","zh":"Happy knack 是一種幸運的天賦，能把某事做好，而且看似不太費力。"},{"en":"A teacher may have a happy knack for making shy students speak.","zh":"老師可能有令害羞學生開口說話的幸運本領。"},{"en":"If someone repeatedly turns accidents into success, people may say they have a happy knack.","zh":"如果某人反覆把意外變成成功，人們可能說他有幸運的本領。"},{"en":"This phrase describes useful talent mixed with luck.","zh":"這個片語描述混合了有用才能和運氣的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"personal skill or capacity","meaning":"個人技巧或能力","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity may describe a situation rather than a personal skill or capacity.","zh":"Serendipity 可能描述一種情況，而不是個人技巧或能力。"},{"en":"Personal skill or capacity means an ability that belongs to an individual person.","zh":"Personal skill or capacity 指屬於個人的能力。"},{"en":"Good pronunciation is a personal skill, while a lucky seating arrangement is a situation.","zh":"良好發音是個人技巧，而幸運座位安排是一種情況。"},{"en":"If discovery depends on circumstances, it may not be purely a personal capacity.","zh":"如果發現取決於環境，它可能不純粹是個人能力。"},{"en":"This phrase helps distinguish individual ability from external conditions.","zh":"這個片語幫助區分個人能力與外部條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"meant to stress","meaning":"意在強調","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists used the word to stress accidental situations.","zh":"一些科學家使用這個詞，意在強調偶然情況。"},{"en":"Meant to stress means intended to emphasise a particular point.","zh":"Meant to stress 指意圖強調某個特定重點。"},{"en":"A teacher’s red underline may be meant to stress one serious grammar problem.","zh":"老師的紅線可能意在強調一個嚴重文法問題。"},{"en":"If writers stress accident, they want readers to notice that planning is not everything.","zh":"如果作者強調偶然，他們希望讀者注意到規劃不是一切。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose behind a word or action.","zh":"這個片語解釋某個詞或行動背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"belonging to the situation","meaning":"屬於情況本身","examples":[{"en":"Some accidents belong to the situation rather than the scientist.","zh":"有些意外屬於情況本身，而不是屬於科學家。"},{"en":"Belonging to the situation means caused by the circumstances, not by a person’s special ability.","zh":"Belonging to the situation 指由環境造成，而不是由某人的特殊能力造成。"},{"en":"A quiet classroom may help concentration because of the situation, not because every student is naturally focused.","zh":"安靜課室可能因情況本身而幫助專注，而不是因為每個學生天生專注。"},{"en":"If a result belongs to the situation, we should not give all credit to one person.","zh":"如果結果屬於情況本身，我們不應把所有功勞都歸給一人。"},{"en":"This phrase shifts attention from individual talent to surrounding conditions.","zh":"這個片語把注意力由個人才能轉向周圍條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"treated serendipity as","meaning":"將……視為","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists treated serendipity as a personal capacity.","zh":"一些科學家將 serendipity 視為個人能力。"},{"en":"To treat something as something means to understand, regard, or handle it in that way.","zh":"To treat something as something 指以某種方式理解、看待或處理某事。"},{"en":"A school may treat punctuality as part of respect, not just a rule.","zh":"學校可能將準時視為尊重的一部分，而不只是規則。"},{"en":"If scientists treat serendipity as skill, they give more importance to the individual researcher.","zh":"如果科學家將 serendipity 視為技巧，他們就更重視個別研究人員。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how people interpret a concept.","zh":"這個片語描述人們如何解讀概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"exploited the ambiguity of","meaning":"利用……的含糊性","examples":[{"en":"Many scientists exploited the ambiguity of the notion.","zh":"許多科學家利用這個概念的含糊性。"},{"en":"To exploit the ambiguity of something means to take advantage of its unclear meaning.","zh":"To exploit the ambiguity of something 指利用某事意思不清楚之處。"},{"en":"A politician may exploit the ambiguity of a promise so different voters hear different things.","zh":"政治人物可能利用承諾的含糊性，令不同選民聽到不同意思。"},{"en":"If a word has several meanings, people may use that flexibility to support their own view.","zh":"如果一個詞有幾個意思，人們可能利用這種彈性支持自己的觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using unclear meaning strategically.","zh":"這個片語描述策略性地使用不清楚的意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the ambiguity of the notion","meaning":"這個概念的含糊性","examples":[{"en":"The ambiguity of the notion allowed different interpretations.","zh":"這個概念的含糊性容許不同解釋。"},{"en":"The ambiguity of the notion means the idea is unclear enough to be understood in several ways.","zh":"The ambiguity of the notion 指該想法不夠清楚，以致可用幾種方式理解。"},{"en":"The ambiguity of the word “fair” can cause arguments in a classroom rule.","zh":"“公平”一詞的含糊性可以在課室規則中引起爭論。"},{"en":"When a notion is ambiguous, people may agree on the word but disagree on its meaning.","zh":"當概念含糊，人們可能同意使用同一詞，卻不同意其意思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unclear conceptual boundaries.","zh":"這個片語描述概念邊界不清。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"what X took as Y","meaning":"某人視作……的東西","examples":[{"en":"What Cannon and Medawar took as harmless, other scientists found dangerous.","zh":"Cannon 和 Medawar 視作無害的東西，其他科學家卻認為危險。"},{"en":"What X took as Y means what one person regarded as a certain thing.","zh":"What X took as Y 指某人把某事視為某種東西。"},{"en":"What one teacher took as creative freedom, another teacher saw as poor discipline.","zh":"一位老師視作創作自由的東西，另一位老師視為紀律差。"},{"en":"This structure compares different interpretations of the same thing.","zh":"這個結構比較對同一事物的不同解讀。"},{"en":"It is useful when one group sees safety where another sees risk.","zh":"當一群人看見安全，而另一群人看見風險時，這個結構很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"benign nose-thumbing at","meaning":"對……的善意嘲弄","examples":[{"en":"Some saw serendipity as a benign nose-thumbing at rigid methods.","zh":"有些人把 serendipity 視為對僵化方法的善意嘲弄。"},{"en":"Benign nose-thumbing at something means a harmless, playful act of disrespect toward it.","zh":"Benign nose-thumbing at something 指對某事作出無害、帶玩笑意味的不敬。"},{"en":"A student’s funny cartoon may be a benign nose-thumbing at overly strict school rules.","zh":"學生的有趣漫畫可能是對過分嚴格校規的善意嘲弄。"},{"en":"If criticism is benign, it mocks without seriously attacking.","zh":"如果批評是善意的，它會嘲弄但不嚴重攻擊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gentle defiance rather than dangerous rebellion.","zh":"這個片語描述溫和反抗，而不是危險叛亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Dreams of Method","meaning":"對「方法夢想」的迷信","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity challenged Dreams of Method.","zh":"Serendipity 挑戰了對「方法夢想」的迷信。"},{"en":"Dreams of Method means the belief or hope that a perfect method can control discovery.","zh":"Dreams of Method 指相信或希望有一套完美方法可以控制發現。"},{"en":"A teacher may criticise students’ dreams of method if they expect one formula to solve every essay.","zh":"如果學生期望一條公式解決所有作文，老師可能批評他們對方法夢想的迷信。"},{"en":"If real work involves uncertainty, dreams of method may be unrealistic.","zh":"如果真實工作涉及不確定性，對方法的夢想可能不切實際。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises overconfidence in fixed procedures.","zh":"這個片語批評對固定程序的過度自信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"found incendiary","meaning":"認為……具煽動性","examples":[{"en":"Other scientists found the idea of serendipity incendiary.","zh":"其他科學家認為 serendipity 這個想法具煽動性。"},{"en":"Found incendiary means considered something likely to cause anger, conflict, or strong reaction.","zh":"Found incendiary 指認為某事可能引起憤怒、衝突或強烈反應。"},{"en":"A proposal to remove all exams may be found incendiary by parents and teachers.","zh":"取消所有考試的提案可能被家長和老師認為具煽動性。"},{"en":"If an idea threatens authority, people may find it incendiary.","zh":"如果一個想法威脅權威，人們可能認為它具煽動性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a view seen as dangerously provocative.","zh":"這個片語描述被視為危險挑釁的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a significant serendipitous aspect","meaning":"重要的偶然發現成分","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists said science had a significant serendipitous aspect.","zh":"一些科學家說科學有重要的偶然發現成分。"},{"en":"A significant serendipitous aspect means an important element of useful accidental discovery.","zh":"Significant serendipitous aspect 指有用偶然發現中的重要元素。"},{"en":"A school project may have a significant serendipitous aspect when a mistake reveals a better question.","zh":"當錯誤揭示更好問題時，學校專題可能有重要的偶然發現成分。"},{"en":"If science includes such an aspect, not every discovery can be planned in advance.","zh":"如果科學包含這種成分，不是每項發現都能事先規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important role played by chance and recognition.","zh":"這個片語描述機遇和辨認所發揮的重要角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"taken by some as","meaning":"被一些人視為……","examples":[{"en":"The idea was taken by some as dangerous denigration.","zh":"這個想法被一些人視為危險的貶低。"},{"en":"Taken by some as means understood or interpreted by some people as a particular thing.","zh":"Taken by some as 指被某些人理解或解讀為某種東西。"},{"en":"A teacher’s strict comment may be taken by some as helpful honesty and by others as criticism.","zh":"老師嚴格的評語可能被一些人視為有幫助的誠實，也被另一些人視為批評。"},{"en":"Different audiences can take the same statement in very different ways.","zh":"不同受眾可以非常不同地理解同一句話。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that interpretation depends on the listener or reader.","zh":"這個片語顯示解讀取決於聽者或讀者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"dangerous denigration","meaning":"危險的貶低","examples":[{"en":"Some regarded serendipity as dangerous denigration of science.","zh":"有些人把 serendipity 視為對科學的危險貶低。"},{"en":"Dangerous denigration means harmful belittling or lowering of someone’s value or authority.","zh":"Dangerous denigration 指有害地貶低某人的價值或權威。"},{"en":"Calling all teachers useless would be dangerous denigration because it damages trust in education.","zh":"說所有老師都無用會是危險的貶低，因為它破壞對教育的信任。"},{"en":"If chance is overemphasised, some fear it may make scientific expertise seem unimportant.","zh":"如果過分強調機遇，有些人擔心它會令科學專業知識顯得不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes criticism seen as damaging and unfair.","zh":"這個片語描述被視為有害且不公平的批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"expert authority","meaning":"專家權威","examples":[{"en":"If discovery were accidental, expert authority would be weakened.","zh":"如果發現是偶然的，專家權威就會被削弱。"},{"en":"Expert authority is the respect and influence given to people with special knowledge or skill.","zh":"Expert authority 是給予擁有特殊知識或技能人士的尊重和影響力。"},{"en":"A doctor’s expert authority comes from training, experience, and evidence-based judgement.","zh":"醫生的專家權威來自培訓、經驗和基於證據的判斷。"},{"en":"If a result seems based only on luck, people may question the expert’s role.","zh":"如果結果看似只基於運氣，人們可能質疑專家的角色。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the power professionals gain from expertise.","zh":"這個片語指專業人士因專業知識而獲得的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in this connection","meaning":"在這方面","examples":[{"en":"In this connection, Pasteur’s aphorism was often quoted.","zh":"在這方面，Pasteur 的格言常被引用。"},{"en":"In this connection means in relation to the point just being discussed.","zh":"In this connection 指與剛正在討論的重點有關。"},{"en":"A teacher may discuss exam pressure; in this connection, sleep habits are also important.","zh":"老師可能討論考試壓力；在這方面，睡眠習慣也很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase links the next example or idea to the current argument.","zh":"這個片語把下一個例子或想法與當前論點連接起來。"},{"en":"It is a formal way to say “on this related point”.","zh":"這是表示「在這個相關點上」的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the aphorism of choice","meaning":"最常引用的格言","examples":[{"en":"The aphorism of choice came from Louis Pasteur.","zh":"最常引用的格言來自 Louis Pasteur。"},{"en":"The aphorism of choice means the short saying most often selected or preferred for a particular point.","zh":"Aphorism of choice 指為表達某個重點而最常被選用或偏好的短句。"},{"en":"For exam preparation, the aphorism of choice might be “practise makes progress”.","zh":"對考試準備而言，最常引用的格言可能是「練習帶來進步」。"},{"en":"If a saying is repeatedly quoted, it becomes the preferred way to express an idea.","zh":"如果一句話反覆被引用，它就成為表達某想法的首選方式。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the favourite quotation used in an argument.","zh":"這個片語指出論證中最受偏好的引用語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"no less an authority than","meaning":"正是來自……這位權威","examples":[{"en":"The quotation came from no less an authority than Louis Pasteur.","zh":"這句引文正是來自 Louis Pasteur 這位權威。"},{"en":"No less an authority than someone means the person cited is highly respected and impressive.","zh":"No less an authority than someone 指所引用的人非常受尊重且令人信服。"},{"en":"A grammar point may be supported by no less an authority than a leading dictionary.","zh":"某文法點可能由正是來自權威字典的說法支持。"},{"en":"This phrase strengthens an argument by stressing the importance of the source.","zh":"這個片語透過強調來源重要性來加強論點。"},{"en":"It suggests that the cited person is difficult to dismiss.","zh":"它暗示被引用的人很難被輕易否定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"chance favours the prepared mind","meaning":"機遇偏愛有準備的頭腦","examples":[{"en":"Pasteur argued that chance favours the prepared mind.","zh":"Pasteur 認為機遇偏愛有準備的頭腦。"},{"en":"Chance favours the prepared mind means lucky opportunities are most useful to people who are ready to recognise them.","zh":"Chance favours the prepared mind 指幸運機會對準備好辨認它們的人最有用。"},{"en":"A student who reads widely may notice a perfect essay example by chance because their mind is prepared.","zh":"廣泛閱讀的學生可能偶然注意到完美作文例子，因為他的頭腦已有準備。"},{"en":"Preparation turns accident into opportunity by helping people understand what they see.","zh":"準備透過幫助人理解所見，把意外轉化為機會。"},{"en":"This saying balances luck with knowledge and readiness.","zh":"這句話平衡了運氣、知識和準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"unplanned and unforeseen","meaning":"未經計劃且無法預見的","examples":[{"en":"Events may turn up unplanned and unforeseen.","zh":"事件可能未經計劃且無法預見地出現。"},{"en":"Unplanned and unforeseen means not arranged in advance and not predicted.","zh":"Unplanned and unforeseen 指並非事先安排，也沒有被預測。"},{"en":"A school trip may face unplanned and unforeseen problems, such as sudden transport delays.","zh":"學校旅行可能面對未經計劃且無法預見的問題，例如突然交通延誤。"},{"en":"If events are unforeseen, flexible planning becomes important.","zh":"如果事件無法預見，彈性規劃就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes things that happen outside expectation and preparation.","zh":"這個片語描述發生在預期和準備之外的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as one is looking for something else","meaning":"當某人正在尋找其他東西時","examples":[{"en":"Unexpected events may occur as one is looking for something else.","zh":"意外事件可能在某人正在尋找其他東西時發生。"},{"en":"As one is looking for something else means while a person is searching for a different thing.","zh":"As one is looking for something else 指當某人正在搜尋另一樣東西時。"},{"en":"A student may find a useful article as they are looking for a dictionary definition.","zh":"學生可能在尋找字典定義時，找到一篇有用文章。"},{"en":"Searching for one thing can accidentally open the door to another discovery.","zh":"尋找一樣東西可能偶然打開另一項發現的大門。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights discovery during a different task.","zh":"這個片語突出在不同任務期間出現的發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the ability to notice","meaning":"察覺……的能力","examples":[{"en":"The ability to notice unexpected events comes from preparation.","zh":"察覺意外事件的能力來自準備。"},{"en":"The ability to notice means the skill of seeing or recognising something important.","zh":"The ability to notice 指看見或辨認重要事物的能力。"},{"en":"A nurse’s ability to notice small changes in a patient can prevent serious problems.","zh":"護士察覺病人細微變化的能力可以防止嚴重問題。"},{"en":"Training improves attention, so people can notice clues that others miss.","zh":"訓練改善注意力，使人能察覺其他人錯過的線索。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises recognition, not just eyesight.","zh":"這個片語強調辨認，而不只是視力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"potential bearing and meaning","meaning":"潛在關聯和意義","examples":[{"en":"Scientists must see the potential bearing and meaning of unexpected events.","zh":"科學家必須看見意外事件的潛在關聯和意義。"},{"en":"Potential bearing and meaning means the possible relevance, importance, or significance of something.","zh":"Potential bearing and meaning 指某事可能具有的相關性、重要性或意義。"},{"en":"A teacher may see the potential meaning of repeated mistakes in students’ essays.","zh":"老師可能看見學生作文中反覆錯誤的潛在意義。"},{"en":"If an event has bearing on a problem, it may help explain or solve that problem.","zh":"如果某事件與問題有關聯，它可能幫助解釋或解決該問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes why an unexpected detail may matter.","zh":"這個片語描述意外細節為何可能重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"exploit their occurrence","meaning":"利用它們的出現","examples":[{"en":"Prepared scientists can exploit the occurrence of unexpected events.","zh":"有準備的科學家可以利用意外事件的出現。"},{"en":"To exploit their occurrence means to make useful use of the fact that they happened.","zh":"To exploit their occurrence 指善用它們已經發生這一事實。"},{"en":"A teacher may exploit a student’s interesting mistake to explain a grammar point to the class.","zh":"老師可能利用學生一個有趣錯誤的出現，向全班解釋文法點。"},{"en":"If people notice unexpected events but do not use them, the opportunity may be lost.","zh":"如果人們注意到意外事件卻不利用它們，機會可能流失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes turning an event into an advantage.","zh":"這個片語描述把事件轉化為優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make constructive use of","meaning":"善用；作建設性運用","examples":[{"en":"Scientists can make constructive use of accidents.","zh":"科學家可以善用意外。"},{"en":"To make constructive use of something means to use it in a positive and productive way.","zh":"To make constructive use of something 指以正面而有成效的方式使用某事。"},{"en":"A student can make constructive use of criticism by rewriting weak paragraphs.","zh":"學生可以透過重寫薄弱段落，建設性地運用批評。"},{"en":"If mistakes are used constructively, they become sources of improvement.","zh":"如果錯誤被建設性地使用，它們會成為改善來源。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on turning something imperfect into something useful.","zh":"這個片語集中於把不完美事物轉化為有用事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"systematic mental preparation","meaning":"系統性的心理準備","examples":[{"en":"These abilities are the result of systematic mental preparation.","zh":"這些能力是系統性的心理準備的結果。"},{"en":"Systematic mental preparation means organised training of the mind before facing a task.","zh":"Systematic mental preparation 指在面對任務前有組織地訓練頭腦。"},{"en":"A student uses systematic mental preparation when they practise past papers, review mistakes, and plan answers.","zh":"學生練習歷屆試題、檢討錯誤並規劃答案時，就是使用系統性的心理準備。"},{"en":"Preparation helps people respond better when unexpected problems appear.","zh":"準備幫助人們在意外問題出現時作出更好反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disciplined thinking built before the important moment.","zh":"這個片語描述在重要時刻前建立的有紀律思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"on closer inspection","meaning":"仔細審視之下","examples":[{"en":"On closer inspection, accident dissolves into sagacity.","zh":"仔細審視之下，偶然變成敏銳判斷。"},{"en":"On closer inspection means after looking at something more carefully.","zh":"On closer inspection 指在更仔細查看某事之後。"},{"en":"On closer inspection, a student’s “careless” mistake may reveal a deeper grammar problem.","zh":"仔細審視之下，學生的「粗心」錯誤可能揭示更深層文法問題。"},{"en":"Careful examination can change how people interpret a situation.","zh":"仔細檢查可以改變人們如何解讀情況。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a revised judgement after deeper analysis.","zh":"這個片語引出深入分析後修正的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"accident dissolves into sagacity","meaning":"偶然變成敏銳判斷","examples":[{"en":"On closer inspection, accident dissolves into sagacity.","zh":"仔細審視之下，偶然變成敏銳判斷。"},{"en":"Accident dissolves into sagacity means what first looks like luck turns out to involve wise judgement.","zh":"Accident dissolves into sagacity 指最初看似運氣的事，原來涉及明智判斷。"},{"en":"A coach’s “lucky” decision may dissolve into sagacity when we see how carefully he read the game.","zh":"當我們看見教練如何仔細閱讀比賽，他的「幸運」決定可能變成敏銳判斷。"},{"en":"If preparation helps someone use chance well, accident is no longer pure accident.","zh":"如果準備幫助某人善用機遇，偶然就不再是純粹偶然。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that luck and intelligence can be difficult to separate.","zh":"這個片語顯示運氣和智慧可能難以分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the context in which","meaning":"……所在的背景","examples":[{"en":"The context in which serendipity was most contested was planned science.","zh":"Serendipity 最受爭議的背景是有計劃的科學研究。"},{"en":"The context in which something happens means the situation or background where it occurs.","zh":"The context in which something happens 指某事發生的情況或背景。"},{"en":"The context in which a student makes a mistake can explain whether it is careless or conceptual.","zh":"學生出錯所在的背景可以解釋它是粗心還是概念問題。"},{"en":"Understanding context helps people interpret words and actions more fairly.","zh":"理解背景幫助人們更公平地解讀言語和行動。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the setting that gives meaning to an issue.","zh":"這個片語引出賦予議題意義的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"most contested","meaning":"最受爭議的","examples":[{"en":"Scientific serendipity was most contested in debates about planned science.","zh":"科學中的 serendipity 在關於有計劃科學的辯論中最受爭議。"},{"en":"Most contested means argued about most strongly or frequently.","zh":"Most contested 指最強烈或最頻繁受到爭論。"},{"en":"In school policy, homework load may be the most contested issue among parents.","zh":"在學校政策中，功課量可能是家長之間最受爭議的議題。"},{"en":"A topic becomes most contested when it affects power, money, or identity.","zh":"當題目影響權力、金錢或身份，它會變得最受爭議。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the area of greatest disagreement.","zh":"這個片語指出最大分歧所在的範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"had its greatest resonance","meaning":"引起最大共鳴","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity had its greatest resonance in discussions of planned science.","zh":"Serendipity 在有計劃科學的討論中引起最大共鳴。"},{"en":"Had its greatest resonance means had the strongest meaning, influence, or emotional force in a particular context.","zh":"Had its greatest resonance 指在某特定背景中有最強意義、影響或情感力量。"},{"en":"A story about poverty may have its greatest resonance among students who have seen inequality directly.","zh":"關於貧窮的故事可能在親眼見過不平等的學生之中引起最大共鳴。"},{"en":"If an idea resonates strongly, people feel that it explains something important.","zh":"如果一個想法引起強烈共鳴，人們會覺得它解釋了重要事情。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where an idea matters most.","zh":"這個片語描述某想法在哪裏最重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"connected with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The debate was connected with the idea of planned science.","zh":"這場辯論與有計劃科學這個想法有關。"},{"en":"Connected with means related to or associated with something.","zh":"Connected with 指與某事相關或有聯繫。"},{"en":"Student stress may be connected with sleep, homework, exams, and family pressure.","zh":"學生壓力可能與睡眠、功課、考試和家庭壓力有關。"},{"en":"If two issues are connected, changing one may affect the other.","zh":"如果兩個議題有關，改變其中一個可能影響另一個。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a relationship between ideas or events.","zh":"這個片語描述想法或事件之間的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"planned science","meaning":"有計劃的科學研究","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity was strongly debated in the context of planned science.","zh":"Serendipity 在有計劃的科學研究背景中受到強烈辯論。"},{"en":"Planned science means scientific research directed by clear goals, organised programmes, and often institutional or industrial planning.","zh":"Planned science 指由清楚目標、有組織計劃，並常由機構或工業規劃引導的科學研究。"},{"en":"A government-funded vaccine project is an example of planned science because goals and resources are set in advance.","zh":"政府資助的疫苗項目是有計劃科學的例子，因為目標和資源事先設定。"},{"en":"If research is heavily planned, accidental discovery may seem harder to explain.","zh":"如果研究高度受規劃，偶然發現可能更難解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts organised research with spontaneous discovery.","zh":"這個片語把有組織研究與自發發現作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"serendipitists","meaning":"相信偶然發現重要性的人","examples":[{"en":"The serendipitists were not all inhabitants of academic ivory towers.","zh":"相信偶然發現重要性的人並不全都是學術象牙塔裏的人。"},{"en":"Serendipitists are people who believe serendipity plays an important role in discovery.","zh":"Serendipitists 是相信偶然發現在發現過程中扮演重要角色的人。"},{"en":"A researcher who defends accidental discovery may be called a serendipitist.","zh":"捍衛偶然發現的研究人員可能被稱為 serendipitist。"},{"en":"Serendipitists argue that planning should leave room for unexpected results.","zh":"相信偶然發現重要性的人認為規劃應為意外結果留下空間。"},{"en":"This word describes supporters of chance-based discovery.","zh":"這個詞描述支持以機遇為基礎的發現的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"inhabitants of academic ivory towers","meaning":"學術象牙塔裏的人","examples":[{"en":"The supporters of serendipity were not all inhabitants of academic ivory towers.","zh":"Serendipity 的支持者並不全都是學術象牙塔裏的人。"},{"en":"Inhabitants of academic ivory towers are academics seen as isolated from practical life.","zh":"Inhabitants of academic ivory towers 是被視為與實際生活隔離的學者。"},{"en":"A businessperson may accuse university theorists of being inhabitants of academic ivory towers if their advice ignores real customers.","zh":"如果大學理論家的建議忽視真實顧客，商人可能指他們是學術象牙塔裏的人。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises scholars who appear disconnected from ordinary work.","zh":"這個片語批評看似脫離普通工作的學者。"},{"en":"It contrasts academic isolation with practical experience.","zh":"它把學術隔離與實務經驗作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"academic ivory towers","meaning":"學術象牙塔","examples":[{"en":"The debate was not limited to academic ivory towers.","zh":"這場辯論並不限於學術象牙塔。"},{"en":"Academic ivory towers are university or scholarly settings seen as remote from real-world concerns.","zh":"Academic ivory towers 是被視為遠離現實問題的大學或學術環境。"},{"en":"A theory may sound elegant in academic ivory towers but fail in a busy workplace.","zh":"某理論在學術象牙塔中可能聽起來優雅，但在繁忙職場中失敗。"},{"en":"If an issue reaches industry, it is no longer trapped inside academic ivory towers.","zh":"如果議題進入工業界，它就不再被困在學術象牙塔內。"},{"en":"This phrase often criticises isolated academic thinking.","zh":"這個片語常批評與現實隔離的學術思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"pioneers of industrial research","meaning":"工業研究先驅","examples":[{"en":"Whitney and Langmuir were pioneers of industrial research.","zh":"Whitney 和 Langmuir 是工業研究先驅。"},{"en":"Pioneers of industrial research are early leaders who helped develop research inside companies or industries.","zh":"Pioneers of industrial research 是幫助在公司或工業內發展研究的早期領導者。"},{"en":"A pioneer of industrial research may build a laboratory where scientists solve practical product problems.","zh":"工業研究先驅可能建立實驗室，讓科學家解決實際產品問題。"},{"en":"Pioneers shape later practice because others copy their methods and institutions.","zh":"先驅會塑造後來實踐，因為其他人會模仿他們的方法和機構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes influential early figures in research for industry.","zh":"這個片語描述工業研究中有影響力的早期人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"made much play of","meaning":"大力強調；充分利用","examples":[{"en":"Whitney and Langmuir made much play of serendipity.","zh":"Whitney 和 Langmuir 大力強調 serendipity。"},{"en":"To make much play of something means to emphasise it strongly or use it repeatedly in an argument.","zh":"To make much play of something 指在論證中強烈強調或反覆利用某事。"},{"en":"A school may make much play of its exam results when advertising to parents.","zh":"學校向家長宣傳時，可能大力強調其考試成績。"},{"en":"If speakers make much play of chance, they want it to seem important to the debate.","zh":"如果說話者大力強調機遇，他們想令它在辯論中顯得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deliberate emphasis.","zh":"這個片語描述有意識的強調。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in the course of","meaning":"在……過程中","examples":[{"en":"They discussed serendipity in the course of arguing against rigid planning.","zh":"他們在反對僵化規劃的過程中討論 serendipity。"},{"en":"In the course of means during the process of doing something.","zh":"In the course of 指在做某事的過程中。"},{"en":"A student may learn useful vocabulary in the course of preparing a presentation.","zh":"學生可能在準備匯報的過程中學到有用詞彙。"},{"en":"Important ideas can appear while people are working on a different task.","zh":"重要想法可以在人們處理另一項任務時出現。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something happens as part of a larger process.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事作為較大過程的一部分發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"arguing against","meaning":"反對……時","examples":[{"en":"They used serendipity while arguing against overly rigid research planning.","zh":"他們在反對過於僵化的研究規劃時使用 serendipity。"},{"en":"Arguing against something means giving reasons to oppose it.","zh":"Arguing against something 指提出理由反對某事。"},{"en":"A student may argue against a school rule if it unfairly affects poorer classmates.","zh":"如果校規不公平地影響較貧窮同學，學生可能提出理由反對。"},{"en":"If people argue against rigid planning, they may support flexibility and judgement.","zh":"如果人們反對僵化規劃，他們可能支持彈性和判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active opposition through reasons.","zh":"這個片語描述透過理由作出的主動反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"overly rigid research planning","meaning":"過於僵化的研究規劃","examples":[{"en":"Langmuir argued against overly rigid research planning.","zh":"Langmuir 反對過於僵化的研究規劃。"},{"en":"Overly rigid research planning means research planning that is too fixed, strict, and unable to adapt.","zh":"Overly rigid research planning 指過分固定、嚴格且不能適應的研究規劃。"},{"en":"A school project becomes overly rigid if students cannot change their question after finding better evidence.","zh":"如果學生找到更好證據後仍不能改變題目，學校專題就變得過於僵化。"},{"en":"Overly rigid planning can cause researchers to ignore unexpected but valuable results.","zh":"過於僵化的規劃可能令研究人員忽視意外但有價值的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises planning that leaves no room for discovery.","zh":"這個片語批評不為發現留下空間的規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"misconceptions about","meaning":"對……的誤解","examples":[{"en":"Langmuir criticised misconceptions about the research process.","zh":"Langmuir 批評對研究過程的誤解。"},{"en":"Misconceptions about something are wrong or misleading ideas about it.","zh":"Misconceptions about something 是關於某事的錯誤或誤導性想法。"},{"en":"Students may have misconceptions about grammar if they think every long sentence is advanced.","zh":"如果學生以為每個長句都是高級句，他們可能對文法有誤解。"},{"en":"Misconceptions can lead to poor decisions because people solve the wrong problem.","zh":"誤解可以導致差劣決定，因為人們在解決錯誤問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes false beliefs that need correction.","zh":"這個片語描述需要修正的錯誤信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"certainty and rationality","meaning":"確定性和理性","examples":[{"en":"Misconceptions about certainty and rationality can damage research.","zh":"對確定性和理性的誤解可能損害研究。"},{"en":"Certainty and rationality mean confidence in clear knowledge and logical thinking.","zh":"Certainty and rationality 指對清楚知識和邏輯思考的信心。"},{"en":"A teacher values rationality when students support answers with evidence rather than guesses.","zh":"當學生用證據而不是猜測支持答案時，老師重視的是理性。"},{"en":"Too much certainty can be dangerous if it prevents people from noticing new evidence.","zh":"如果過多確定性阻止人們注意新證據，它可能很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to two ideals often associated with science and planning.","zh":"這個片語指常與科學和規劃相關的兩個理想。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the research process","meaning":"研究過程","examples":[{"en":"Misconceptions about the research process did much harm.","zh":"對研究過程的誤解造成很大傷害。"},{"en":"The research process is the series of steps, decisions, observations, and revisions involved in doing research.","zh":"Research process 是進行研究時涉及的一系列步驟、決定、觀察和修正。"},{"en":"In a school project, the research process may include choosing a question, collecting data, and checking evidence.","zh":"在學校專題中，研究過程可能包括選題、收集數據和檢查證據。"},{"en":"If people misunderstand the process, they may expect research to be cleaner than it really is.","zh":"如果人們誤解過程，他們可能期望研究比實際更整齊。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how research is actually carried out.","zh":"這個片語集中於研究實際如何進行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"did much harm","meaning":"造成很大傷害","examples":[{"en":"Langmuir thought these misconceptions did much harm.","zh":"Langmuir 認為這些誤解造成很大傷害。"},{"en":"Did much harm means caused serious damage or negative effects.","zh":"Did much harm 指造成嚴重損害或負面影響。"},{"en":"A false rumour can do much harm to a student’s confidence and friendships.","zh":"虛假謠言可以對學生信心和友誼造成很大傷害。"},{"en":"Misunderstanding science can harm policy by encouraging unrealistic expectations.","zh":"誤解科學可以透過鼓勵不切實際期望而損害政策。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong negative impact.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈負面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"mature acceptance of uncertainty","meaning":"成熟地接受不確定性","examples":[{"en":"A mature acceptance of uncertainty may lead to better research policies.","zh":"成熟地接受不確定性可能帶來更好的研究政策。"},{"en":"Mature acceptance of uncertainty means calmly recognising that not everything can be predicted or controlled.","zh":"Mature acceptance of uncertainty 指冷靜承認不是一切都能被預測或控制。"},{"en":"A student shows mature acceptance of uncertainty when they prepare well but accept that exam questions may surprise them.","zh":"當學生準備充分，但接受考題可能令人意外，他就是成熟地接受不確定性。"},{"en":"Accepting uncertainty can lead people to plan flexibly rather than rigidly.","zh":"接受不確定性可以令人體現彈性規劃，而不是僵化規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wisdom about limits in knowledge and control.","zh":"這個片語描述對知識和控制限制的智慧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"far more likely to result in","meaning":"更有可能導致……","examples":[{"en":"Accepting uncertainty was far more likely to result in productive research policies.","zh":"接受不確定性更有可能導致有成效的研究政策。"},{"en":"Far more likely to result in means much more probably leading to a particular outcome.","zh":"Far more likely to result in 指更大可能導致某特定結果。"},{"en":"Regular practice is far more likely to result in fluency than last-minute memorisation.","zh":"定期練習比臨急背誦更有可能導致流利。"},{"en":"If a method is more realistic, it is more likely to produce useful results.","zh":"如果方法較現實，它更可能產生有用結果。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly compares the probability of outcomes.","zh":"這個片語強烈比較結果出現的可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"productive research policies","meaning":"有成效的研究政策","examples":[{"en":"Accepting uncertainty can result in productive research policies.","zh":"接受不確定性可以導致有成效的研究政策。"},{"en":"Productive research policies are rules or plans that help research produce useful, valuable, or creative results.","zh":"Productive research policies 是幫助研究產生有用、有價值或有創意結果的規則或計劃。"},{"en":"A university may create productive research policies by giving scientists time to explore unexpected findings.","zh":"大學可能透過給科學家時間探索意外發現，制定有成效的研究政策。"},{"en":"If policies are too rigid, research may become less productive.","zh":"如果政策太僵化，研究可能變得較少成果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes policies that help research work well.","zh":"這個片語描述幫助研究良好運作的政策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"for his own part","meaning":"就他本人而言","examples":[{"en":"For his own part, Langmuir said that outcomes occurred as if by accident.","zh":"就 Langmuir 本人而言，他說結果好像是偶然發生的。"},{"en":"For his own part means speaking for himself or giving his own view.","zh":"For his own part 指就他自己而言，或提出他自己的觀點。"},{"en":"For her own part, the teacher believed that students needed more practice, not more rules.","zh":"就那位老師本人而言，她認為學生需要更多練習，而不是更多規則。"},{"en":"This phrase separates one person’s opinion from the wider debate.","zh":"這個片語把某人的個人意見與更廣泛辯論分開。"},{"en":"It is useful when introducing an individual stance.","zh":"當引入個人立場時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"satisfactory outcomes","meaning":"令人滿意的結果","examples":[{"en":"Langmuir said satisfactory outcomes occurred as though they were drifting with the wind.","zh":"Langmuir 說令人滿意的結果好像隨風漂流般出現。"},{"en":"Satisfactory outcomes are results that are good enough, useful, or pleasing.","zh":"Satisfactory outcomes 是足夠好、有用或令人滿意的結果。"},{"en":"A student may get satisfactory outcomes from revision if they understand mistakes and improve steadily.","zh":"如果學生理解錯誤並穩步改善，溫習可能帶來令人滿意的結果。"},{"en":"Satisfactory outcomes do not always come from strict planning; sometimes flexibility helps.","zh":"令人滿意的結果不一定來自嚴格規劃；有時彈性會有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes results that meet expectations or needs.","zh":"這個片語描述符合期望或需要的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"as though","meaning":"好像；彷彿","examples":[{"en":"The outcomes occurred as though the researchers were drifting with the wind.","zh":"結果出現時，好像研究人員正在隨風漂流。"},{"en":"As though means as if, used to describe how something seems.","zh":"As though 指好像、彷彿，用來描述某事看起來如何。"},{"en":"A student spoke as though they had practised the presentation many times.","zh":"學生說話時，好像已經練習匯報很多次。"},{"en":"This phrase compares reality with an imagined situation to explain a feeling or appearance.","zh":"這個片語把現實與想像情況比較，以解釋感覺或外觀。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing how something looks, sounds, or feels.","zh":"它適合描述某事看起來、聽起來或感覺如何。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"drifting with the wind","meaning":"隨風漂流","examples":[{"en":"Langmuir described research as drifting with the wind.","zh":"Langmuir 把研究描述為隨風漂流。"},{"en":"Drifting with the wind means moving without a fixed direction, guided by outside forces.","zh":"Drifting with the wind 指沒有固定方向地移動，受外部力量引導。"},{"en":"A student without a study plan may feel like they are drifting with the wind before exams.","zh":"沒有學習計劃的學生在考試前可能感覺自己像隨風漂流。"},{"en":"If research drifts too much, it may lack focus; if it never drifts, it may miss surprises.","zh":"如果研究過分漂流，它可能缺乏焦點；如果完全不漂流，它可能錯過驚喜。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests movement shaped by uncertainty rather than strict control.","zh":"這個片語暗示受不確定性而非嚴格控制塑造的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"came about by accident","meaning":"偶然發生","examples":[{"en":"Langmuir said these things came about by accident.","zh":"Langmuir 說這些事情是偶然發生的。"},{"en":"Came about by accident means happened by chance rather than by deliberate planning.","zh":"Came about by accident 指因機遇而非刻意規劃發生。"},{"en":"A useful classroom game may come about by accident when a teacher changes a task quickly.","zh":"當老師快速改變任務時，一個有用課堂遊戲可能偶然發生。"},{"en":"If something comes about by accident, its value may only become clear later.","zh":"如果某事偶然發生，其價值可能只是後來才變得清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accidental origin.","zh":"這個片語描述偶然起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"determinate relationship between","meaning":"……之間的確定關係","examples":[{"en":"Langmuir doubted that research had a determinate relationship between cause and effect.","zh":"Langmuir 懷疑研究在因與果之間有確定關係。"},{"en":"A determinate relationship between two things is a fixed, clear, and predictable connection.","zh":"Determinate relationship between two things 是兩者之間固定、清楚且可預測的聯繫。"},{"en":"In simple maths, there is a determinate relationship between adding more items and increasing the total.","zh":"在簡單數學中，加入更多物件與總數增加之間有確定關係。"},{"en":"Research may be difficult to plan if cause and effect are not fully determinate.","zh":"如果因果並非完全確定，研究可能難以規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a precise and reliable connection.","zh":"這個片語描述精確可靠的聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"cause and effect","meaning":"因果關係","examples":[{"en":"Research may not have a simple relationship between cause and effect.","zh":"研究未必有簡單的因果關係。"},{"en":"Cause and effect means the connection between what makes something happen and what happens as a result.","zh":"Cause and effect 指造成某事的原因與結果之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"If a student sleeps late and feels tired in class, that may show cause and effect.","zh":"如果學生睡得晚並在課堂上疲倦，這可能顯示因果關係。"},{"en":"In complex research, one cause may produce many effects, and one effect may have many causes.","zh":"在複雜研究中，一個原因可能產生多個結果，一個結果也可能有多個原因。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the logic of why things happen.","zh":"這個片語描述事情為何發生的邏輯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"does not get us very far","meaning":"不能帶我們走得很遠；幫助有限","examples":[{"en":"If cause and effect are uncertain, planning does not get us very far.","zh":"如果因果關係不確定，規劃就不能帶我們走得很遠。"},{"en":"Does not get us very far means does not help us make much progress.","zh":"Does not get us very far 指不能幫助我們取得太多進展。"},{"en":"Memorising model essays does not get students very far if they cannot answer new questions.","zh":"如果學生不能回答新題目，背誦範文不能帶他們走得很遠。"},{"en":"A method that ignores uncertainty may help at first but fail later.","zh":"忽視不確定性的方法起初可能有幫助，但之後會失效。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises limited usefulness.","zh":"這個片語批評某事用處有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"from within the bowels of","meaning":"從……內部深處","examples":[{"en":"Arguments for scientific autonomy came from within the bowels of corporate capitalism.","zh":"支持科學自主的論據來自企業資本主義內部深處。"},{"en":"From within the bowels of something means from deep inside a large system or organisation.","zh":"From within the bowels of something 指來自大型系統或組織深處。"},{"en":"Criticism of exam pressure may come from within the bowels of the education system itself.","zh":"對考試壓力的批評可能來自教育制度本身的內部深處。"},{"en":"If a challenge comes from inside a system, it is harder to dismiss as outside attack.","zh":"如果挑戰來自制度內部，就較難被視為外部攻擊而忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses an origin deep within an unexpected place.","zh":"這個片語強調來源位於意想不到地方的深處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"corporate capitalism","meaning":"企業資本主義","examples":[{"en":"Arguments for scientific spontaneity came from within corporate capitalism.","zh":"支持科學自發性的論據來自企業資本主義內部。"},{"en":"Corporate capitalism is an economic system in which large companies play a major role in production, research, and profit-making.","zh":"Corporate capitalism 是大型公司在生產、研究和賺取利潤中扮演主要角色的經濟制度。"},{"en":"A large technology company operating global laboratories is part of corporate capitalism.","zh":"經營全球實驗室的大型科技公司是企業資本主義的一部分。"},{"en":"If corporate capitalism supports scientific freedom, the relationship between business and science is more complex than expected.","zh":"如果企業資本主義支持科學自由，商業與科學的關係就比預期更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to capitalism organised around powerful corporations.","zh":"這個片語指圍繞強大企業組織起來的資本主義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"powerful arguments","meaning":"強而有力的論據","examples":[{"en":"Industrial researchers made powerful arguments for scientific autonomy.","zh":"工業研究人員提出支持科學自主的強而有力論據。"},{"en":"Powerful arguments are strong reasons that can persuade people or change a debate.","zh":"Powerful arguments 是能說服人或改變辯論的強大理由。"},{"en":"A student makes powerful arguments when every claim is supported by clear evidence.","zh":"當學生每個主張都有清楚證據支持，他就是提出強而有力的論據。"},{"en":"Powerful arguments can force critics to rethink their position.","zh":"強而有力的論據可以迫使批評者重新思考立場。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reasoning that has real persuasive force.","zh":"這個片語描述具有真正說服力的推理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"by way of","meaning":"通過……；藉由","examples":[{"en":"They argued for autonomy by way of serendipity.","zh":"他們藉由 serendipity 為自主辯護。"},{"en":"By way of means through, by using, or by means of something.","zh":"By way of 指通過、使用或憑藉某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain grammar by way of simple stories rather than abstract rules.","zh":"老師可能藉由簡單故事而不是抽象規則來解釋文法。"},{"en":"If an idea is defended by way of examples, the examples become part of the argument.","zh":"如果一個想法通過例子被捍衛，那些例子就成為論證的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the route used to make a point.","zh":"這個片語顯示用來提出觀點的途徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"scientific spontaneity","meaning":"科學上的自發性","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity supported arguments for scientific spontaneity.","zh":"Serendipity 支持了科學上的自發性的論點。"},{"en":"Scientific spontaneity means allowing science to develop through flexible, unexpected, and not fully planned activity.","zh":"Scientific spontaneity 指容許科學透過靈活、意外且未完全規劃的活動發展。"},{"en":"A research team shows scientific spontaneity when it follows an unexpected result into a new question.","zh":"當研究團隊跟隨意外結果走向新問題，它就展現科學上的自發性。"},{"en":"Too little spontaneity can make research rigid and blind to surprises.","zh":"太少自發性可以令研究僵化，並對驚喜視而不見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes freedom and openness in scientific work.","zh":"這個片語描述科學工作中的自由和開放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"scientific autonomy","meaning":"科學自主","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity supported arguments for scientific autonomy.","zh":"Serendipity 支持了科學自主的論點。"},{"en":"Scientific autonomy means the freedom of scientists to choose questions, methods, and directions without excessive outside control.","zh":"Scientific autonomy 指科學家在沒有過度外部控制下選擇問題、方法和方向的自由。"},{"en":"A laboratory has scientific autonomy when researchers can follow unexpected findings without immediate commercial pressure.","zh":"當研究人員能在沒有即時商業壓力下追隨意外發現，實驗室就有科學自主。"},{"en":"Scientific autonomy can help discovery because not every valuable result can be planned in advance.","zh":"科學自主可以幫助發現，因為不是每個有價值結果都能事先規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes independence in scientific decision-making.","zh":"這個片語描述科學決策中的獨立性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the notion that","meaning":"……這個觀念","examples":[{"en":"The notion that industry always regimented science does not wash.","zh":"工業總是嚴格管制科學這個觀念說不通。"},{"en":"The notion that means the idea or belief that something is true.","zh":"The notion that 指某事為真的想法或信念。"},{"en":"The notion that all students learn best in the same way is too simple.","zh":"所有學生都以同一方式學得最好這個觀念太簡單。"},{"en":"If evidence contradicts a notion, people should be willing to revise it.","zh":"如果證據與某觀念相矛盾，人們應願意修正它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an idea that may be questioned or defended.","zh":"這個片語引出可能被質疑或捍衛的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"invariably committed to","meaning":"總是致力於……","examples":[{"en":"Industry was not invariably committed to rigid research control.","zh":"工業界並非總是致力於僵化的研究控制。"},{"en":"Invariably committed to means always dedicated to or fixed on doing something.","zh":"Invariably committed to 指總是投入或固定要做某事。"},{"en":"A school is not invariably committed to exams if it also values projects and interviews.","zh":"如果學校也重視專題和面試，它就不是總是致力於考試。"},{"en":"If an organisation is not invariably committed to control, it may sometimes allow freedom.","zh":"如果組織並非總是致力於控制，它有時可能容許自由。"},{"en":"This phrase describes whether a commitment is constant and unchanging.","zh":"這個片語描述承諾是否持續不變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"regimentation of scientific research","meaning":"對科學研究的嚴格管制","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe industry supports the regimentation of scientific research.","zh":"有些人相信工業界支持對科學研究的嚴格管制。"},{"en":"Regimentation of scientific research means strict control and organisation of research activities.","zh":"Regimentation of scientific research 指對研究活動作出嚴格控制和組織。"},{"en":"A company may impose regimentation if every experiment must follow a fixed commercial plan.","zh":"如果每個實驗都必須跟隨固定商業計劃，公司可能實施嚴格管制。"},{"en":"Too much regimentation can reduce creativity and discourage unexpected discoveries.","zh":"過多嚴格管制可以減少創意，並削弱意外發現。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises research controlled like a rigid system.","zh":"這個片語批評像僵化制度般受控制的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"just doesn’t wash","meaning":"說不通；站不住腳","examples":[{"en":"The notion that industry always controls research just doesn’t wash.","zh":"工業界總是控制研究這個觀念說不通。"},{"en":"Just doesn’t wash means does not sound convincing, logical, or believable.","zh":"Just doesn’t wash 指聽起來不令人信服、不合邏輯或不可信。"},{"en":"The excuse that a student forgot homework every day for a month just doesn’t wash.","zh":"學生連續一個月每天都忘記功課這個藉口說不通。"},{"en":"If evidence shows many exceptions, a simple claim may not wash.","zh":"如果證據顯示許多例外，簡單說法可能站不住腳。"},{"en":"This informal phrase rejects an explanation as weak.","zh":"這個非正式片語把某解釋視為薄弱而拒絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"represented the keystone in the arch of","meaning":"是……的核心支柱","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity represented the keystone in the arch of Merton’s work.","zh":"Serendipity 是 Merton 研究工作的核心支柱。"},{"en":"Represented the keystone in the arch of something means formed the central supporting idea in a larger structure.","zh":"Represented the keystone in the arch of something 指構成較大結構中的核心支撐想法。"},{"en":"Clear feedback may represent the keystone in the arch of effective teaching.","zh":"清楚回饋可能是有效教學的核心支柱。"},{"en":"If the keystone is removed, the whole argument or system may become weaker.","zh":"如果核心支柱被移除，整個論點或制度可能變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase uses an architectural image to describe a central support.","zh":"這個片語使用建築意象來描述中心支撐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"social scientific work","meaning":"社會科學研究","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity was central to Merton’s social scientific work.","zh":"Serendipity 是 Merton 社會科學研究的核心。"},{"en":"Social scientific work is research that studies society, human behaviour, institutions, and social relationships.","zh":"Social scientific work 是研究社會、人類行為、制度和社會關係的工作。"},{"en":"A study of how families respond to unemployment is social scientific work.","zh":"關於家庭如何應對失業的研究就是社會科學研究。"},{"en":"Social scientific work often deals with uncertainty because human behaviour is complex.","zh":"社會科學研究常處理不確定性，因為人類行為複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to research in the social sciences.","zh":"這個片語指社會科學中的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a seminal essay on","meaning":"關於……的開創性文章","examples":[{"en":"Merton wrote a seminal essay on unanticipated consequences.","zh":"Merton 寫了一篇關於未預料後果的開創性文章。"},{"en":"A seminal essay on something is an influential early piece of writing that shapes later thinking about that topic.","zh":"Seminal essay on something 是一篇有影響力的早期文章，能塑造後來對該題目的思考。"},{"en":"A seminal essay on education may change how teachers understand learning.","zh":"關於教育的開創性文章可能改變老師如何理解學習。"},{"en":"If an essay becomes seminal, later writers often refer back to it.","zh":"如果一篇文章成為開創性文章，後來作者常回頭引用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a highly important and influential article.","zh":"這個片語描述非常重要且有影響力的文章。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"unanticipated consequences","meaning":"未預料到的後果","examples":[{"en":"Merton studied the unanticipated consequences of purposive social action.","zh":"Merton 研究有目的社會行動的未預料到的後果。"},{"en":"Unanticipated consequences are results that people did not expect when they acted.","zh":"Unanticipated consequences 是人們行動時沒有預期到的結果。"},{"en":"A school phone ban may have the unanticipated consequence of making students talk more during breaks.","zh":"學校禁用手機可能有一個未預料到的後果，就是學生在小息時交談更多。"},{"en":"Even careful plans can create results that no one predicted.","zh":"即使周詳計劃也可以產生沒有人預測到的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unexpected outcomes of intentional actions.","zh":"這個片語描述有意行動帶來的意外結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"purposive social action","meaning":"有目的的社會行動","examples":[{"en":"Merton wrote about purposive social action.","zh":"Merton 撰寫關於有目的的社會行動的文章。"},{"en":"Purposive social action is action taken by people or groups with a clear aim in society.","zh":"Purposive social action 是人或群體在社會中帶着明確目的採取的行動。"},{"en":"A government campaign to reduce smoking is a form of purposive social action.","zh":"政府減少吸煙的宣傳活動是一種有目的的社會行動。"},{"en":"Even purposive action can lead to unexpected results because society is complex.","zh":"即使有目的行動也可能導致意外結果，因為社會很複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intentional action within social life.","zh":"這個片語描述社會生活中的有意行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the nature of social action","meaning":"社會行動的本質","examples":[{"en":"Merton argued that uncertainty is part of the nature of social action.","zh":"Merton 認為不確定性是社會行動本質的一部分。"},{"en":"The nature of social action means the basic character of how people act within society.","zh":"The nature of social action 指人們在社會中行動方式的基本特質。"},{"en":"The nature of classroom discussion includes disagreement, negotiation, and changing opinions.","zh":"課堂討論的本質包括分歧、協商和意見改變。"},{"en":"If uncertainty belongs to social action, even rational plans may produce surprising results.","zh":"如果不確定性屬於社會行動，即使理性計劃也可能產生驚人結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the essential features of social behaviour.","zh":"這個片語描述社會行為的核心特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"what one intends is rarely what one gets","meaning":"人們想得到的往往不是最終得到的","examples":[{"en":"Merton argued that what one intends is rarely what one gets.","zh":"Merton 認為人們想得到的往往不是最終得到的。"},{"en":"What one intends is rarely what one gets means people often receive results different from their original aims.","zh":"What one intends is rarely what one gets 指人們常得到不同於原本目標的結果。"},{"en":"A school may introduce longer homework to improve grades but end up increasing stress instead.","zh":"學校可能引入更多功課來提高成績，結果卻增加壓力。"},{"en":"Intentions do not guarantee outcomes because other people and conditions intervene.","zh":"意圖不保證結果，因為其他人和條件會介入。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that planned actions can produce unexpected effects.","zh":"這個片語提醒有計劃行動也可能產生意外效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"intending to provide resources for","meaning":"意圖為……提供資源","examples":[{"en":"Some thinkers intended to provide resources for buttressing religion.","zh":"一些思想家意圖為鞏固宗教提供資源。"},{"en":"Intending to provide resources for something means planning to supply support, evidence, or tools for that purpose.","zh":"Intending to provide resources for something 指計劃為某目的提供支持、證據或工具。"},{"en":"A teacher may design notes intending to provide resources for weaker students.","zh":"老師可能設計筆記，意圖為較弱學生提供資源。"},{"en":"Plans can have unexpected outcomes even when the original intention is clear.","zh":"即使原本意圖清楚，計劃也可能有意外結果。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose behind an action.","zh":"這個片語解釋行動背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"buttressing","meaning":"支持；鞏固","examples":[{"en":"Natural philosophers tried to buttress the Christian religion.","zh":"自然哲學家嘗試鞏固基督教。"},{"en":"Buttressing means supporting or strengthening something, especially an argument, belief, or institution.","zh":"Buttressing 指支持或強化某事，尤其是論點、信念或制度。"},{"en":"A student can buttress an essay argument by adding clear evidence and examples.","zh":"學生可以透過加入清楚證據和例子來鞏固文章論點。"},{"en":"If evidence is weak, extra examples may be needed to buttress the claim.","zh":"如果證據薄弱，就可能需要額外例子來支持主張。"},{"en":"This word describes giving support so something stands more firmly.","zh":"這個詞描述給予支持，使某事更穩固。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the Christian religion","meaning":"基督教","examples":[{"en":"Natural philosophers hoped to support the Christian religion.","zh":"自然哲學家希望支持基督教。"},{"en":"The Christian religion is the faith based on the life and teachings of Jesus Christ.","zh":"The Christian religion 是以耶穌基督的生平和教導為基礎的信仰。"},{"en":"A historian may study how the Christian religion shaped education, art, and politics in Europe.","zh":"歷史學家可能研究基督教如何塑造歐洲的教育、藝術和政治。"},{"en":"Religious ideas can influence science, society, and culture in complex ways.","zh":"宗教思想可以以複雜方式影響科學、社會和文化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to Christianity as a religious tradition.","zh":"這個片語指基督教這一宗教傳統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"natural philosophers","meaning":"自然哲學家","examples":[{"en":"Natural philosophers of the Scientific Revolution helped lay the groundwork for secularism.","zh":"科學革命時期的自然哲學家幫助為世俗主義奠定基礎。"},{"en":"Natural philosophers were early thinkers who studied nature before modern science became a separate profession.","zh":"Natural philosophers 是在現代科學成為獨立專業前研究自然的早期思想家。"},{"en":"A natural philosopher might study motion, light, plants, or the heavens using observation and reasoning.","zh":"自然哲學家可能使用觀察和推理研究運動、光、植物或天體。"},{"en":"Their work helped create modern science, even when their intentions were different.","zh":"他們的工作幫助創造現代科學，即使其意圖不同。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to early scientists in historical language.","zh":"這個片語以歷史語言指早期科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the Scientific Revolution","meaning":"科學革命","examples":[{"en":"The Scientific Revolution had consequences that were not fully intended.","zh":"科學革命帶來了並非完全有意造成的後果。"},{"en":"The Scientific Revolution was a major historical period when new methods and discoveries transformed ideas about nature.","zh":"Scientific Revolution 是一個重要歷史時期，新方法和發現改變了人們對自然的想法。"},{"en":"Students study the Scientific Revolution to understand how observation and mathematics changed knowledge.","zh":"學生研究科學革命，以理解觀察和數學如何改變知識。"},{"en":"Its consequences reached beyond science into religion, politics, and society.","zh":"它的後果超越科學，進入宗教、政治和社會。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a major turning point in the history of science.","zh":"這個片語指科學史上的重大轉折點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"laid the groundwork for","meaning":"為……奠定基礎","examples":[{"en":"Natural philosophers laid the groundwork for secularism.","zh":"自然哲學家為世俗主義奠定基礎。"},{"en":"To lay the groundwork for something means to create the basic conditions that make it possible later.","zh":"To lay the groundwork for something 指創造基本條件，使某事日後成為可能。"},{"en":"Early reading habits can lay the groundwork for strong writing skills.","zh":"早期閱讀習慣可以為強大寫作能力奠定基礎。"},{"en":"Actions may prepare the way for results that people did not originally intend.","zh":"行動可能為人們原本沒有打算的結果鋪路。"},{"en":"This phrase describes building a foundation for future development.","zh":"這個片語描述為未來發展建立基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"secularism","meaning":"世俗主義","examples":[{"en":"The work of natural philosophers helped lay the groundwork for secularism.","zh":"自然哲學家的工作幫助為世俗主義奠定基礎。"},{"en":"Secularism is the idea that public life, knowledge, or government can be separate from religious authority.","zh":"Secularism 是認為公共生活、知識或政府可以與宗教權威分開的想法。"},{"en":"A secular school system may teach religion as a subject but not be controlled by one religion.","zh":"世俗學校制度可能把宗教作為科目教授，但不受單一宗教控制。"},{"en":"Scientific thinking helped secularism grow by offering explanations outside church authority.","zh":"科學思維透過提供教會權威以外的解釋，幫助世俗主義發展。"},{"en":"This word describes a separation between religious authority and public or intellectual life.","zh":"這個詞描述宗教權威與公共或知識生活之間的分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"wind up","meaning":"最終……；結果……","examples":[{"en":"People wanting to be alone with nature may wind up crowding one another.","zh":"想獨自親近自然的人，結果可能彼此擠在一起。"},{"en":"To wind up means to finally end in a particular situation, often unexpectedly.","zh":"To wind up 指最終落入某種情況，常帶意外意味。"},{"en":"A student who delays revision may wind up studying all night before the exam.","zh":"拖延溫習的學生最終可能在考試前通宵讀書。"},{"en":"People may intend one result but wind up creating the opposite.","zh":"人們可能意圖得到一個結果，結果卻創造相反效果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an eventual outcome, often different from the plan.","zh":"這個片語描述最終結果，常與原計劃不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"crowding one another","meaning":"彼此擠在一起","examples":[{"en":"Visitors to Yosemite Valley may wind up crowding one another.","zh":"前往 Yosemite Valley 的遊客結果可能彼此擠在一起。"},{"en":"Crowding one another means being packed together so closely that people disturb each other.","zh":"Crowding one another 指人們擠得太近，以致互相打擾。"},{"en":"Students crowd one another when too many people try to leave a classroom through one door.","zh":"當太多學生試圖從同一道門離開課室，他們就會彼此擠在一起。"},{"en":"When many people seek quiet in the same place, the place may become crowded instead.","zh":"當許多人在同一地方尋找寧靜，那地方反而可能變得擁擠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people unintentionally reducing each other’s space.","zh":"這個片語描述人們無意中減少彼此空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"know enough to ensure","meaning":"知道得足以確保……","examples":[{"en":"We do not know enough to ensure that the past guides the future.","zh":"我們知道得不足以確保過去能指引未來。"},{"en":"To know enough to ensure something means to have sufficient knowledge to guarantee it.","zh":"To know enough to ensure something 指擁有足夠知識去保證某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may not know enough to ensure every student will succeed after one lesson.","zh":"老師可能知道得不足以確保每個學生一堂課後都會成功。"},{"en":"If conditions change, past experience may not be enough to guarantee future results.","zh":"如果條件改變，過去經驗可能不足以保證未來結果。"},{"en":"This phrase questions whether knowledge is sufficient for certainty.","zh":"這個片語質疑知識是否足以帶來確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the past is an adequate guide to the future","meaning":"過去足以指引未來","examples":[{"en":"The past is not always an adequate guide to the future.","zh":"過去並不總是足以指引未來。"},{"en":"The past is an adequate guide to the future means previous experience can reliably help predict what will happen next.","zh":"The past is an adequate guide to the future 指過往經驗能可靠地幫助預測接下來會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"A student may think past papers are an adequate guide to the future exam, but new questions can still appear.","zh":"學生可能認為歷屆試題足以指引未來考試，但新題目仍可能出現。"},{"en":"If the world changes quickly, the past may guide us only partly.","zh":"如果世界快速改變，過去可能只能部分指引我們。"},{"en":"This phrase questions whether history can reliably predict future outcomes.","zh":"這個片語質疑歷史是否能可靠預測未來結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"uncertainty about outcomes","meaning":"對結果的不確定性","examples":[{"en":"Uncertainty about outcomes is endemic.","zh":"對結果的不確定性是普遍存在的。"},{"en":"Uncertainty about outcomes means not knowing what results an action will finally produce.","zh":"Uncertainty about outcomes 指不知道某行動最終會產生甚麼結果。"},{"en":"A school may face uncertainty about outcomes when introducing a new teaching method.","zh":"學校引入新教學方法時，可能面對對結果的不確定性。"},{"en":"If outcomes are uncertain, careful monitoring and flexibility become important.","zh":"如果結果不確定，仔細監察和彈性就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doubt about final results.","zh":"這個片語描述對最終結果的疑問。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"best-laid plans","meaning":"最周詳的計劃","examples":[{"en":"Even our best-laid plans have uncertain consequences.","zh":"即使我們最周詳的計劃，其後果也不確定。"},{"en":"Best-laid plans are the most careful and well-prepared plans people make.","zh":"Best-laid plans 是人們作出的最仔細、最充分準備的計劃。"},{"en":"A family’s best-laid travel plans can fail if a storm cancels all flights.","zh":"如果暴風雨取消所有航班，家庭最周詳的旅行計劃也可能失敗。"},{"en":"Even careful planning cannot remove all uncertainty.","zh":"即使仔細規劃也不能消除所有不確定性。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that strong preparation still does not guarantee results.","zh":"這個片語提醒充分準備仍不保證結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"endemic","meaning":"普遍存在的；根深蒂固的","examples":[{"en":"Uncertainty is endemic in social action.","zh":"不確定性在社會行動中普遍存在。"},{"en":"Endemic means deeply present, widespread, and built into a situation or system.","zh":"Endemic 指深深存在、廣泛存在並內嵌於某情況或制度中。"},{"en":"Exam stress may be endemic in a school culture that values marks above everything else.","zh":"在一個把分數置於一切之上的學校文化中，考試壓力可能根深蒂固。"},{"en":"If uncertainty is endemic, it cannot be removed by one simple rule.","zh":"如果不確定性是根深蒂固的，它不能由一條簡單規則移除。"},{"en":"This word describes a problem or feature that is rooted in a system.","zh":"這個詞描述植根於制度中的問題或特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"undertaken with the best evidence","meaning":"以最佳證據進行的","examples":[{"en":"Some social action is undertaken with the best evidence.","zh":"一些社會行動是以最佳證據進行的。"},{"en":"Undertaken with the best evidence means carried out using the strongest available information.","zh":"Undertaken with the best evidence 指使用可取得的最強資訊來進行。"},{"en":"A school reform may be undertaken with the best evidence from student surveys and research.","zh":"學校改革可能以來自學生問卷和研究的最佳證據進行。"},{"en":"Even evidence-based action can produce unexpected results.","zh":"即使以證據為基礎的行動也可以產生意外結果。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that good evidence improves decisions but does not guarantee outcomes.","zh":"這個片語顯示好證據能改善決策，但不保證結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"formulated according to","meaning":"根據……制定","examples":[{"en":"Social action may be formulated according to rational criteria.","zh":"社會行動可能根據理性準則制定。"},{"en":"Formulated according to means designed or planned based on particular rules, standards, or principles.","zh":"Formulated according to 指根據特定規則、標準或原則設計或規劃。"},{"en":"A school timetable may be formulated according to room availability and students’ needs.","zh":"學校時間表可能根據課室可用情況和學生需要制定。"},{"en":"If a plan is formulated according to good criteria, it is more reasonable but still not certain.","zh":"如果計劃根據良好準則制定，它會更合理，但仍不一定確定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the basis used to create a plan.","zh":"這個片語描述制定計劃所依據的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"rational criteria","meaning":"理性準則","examples":[{"en":"Even action based on rational criteria can have uncertain consequences.","zh":"即使基於理性準則的行動也可能有不確定後果。"},{"en":"Rational criteria are logical standards used to judge, plan, or decide something.","zh":"Rational criteria 是用來判斷、規劃或決定某事的邏輯標準。"},{"en":"A teacher may use rational criteria such as clarity, evidence, and grammar to mark essays.","zh":"老師可能使用清晰度、證據和文法等理性準則來批改作文。"},{"en":"Rational criteria improve decision-making, but they cannot remove every unexpected result.","zh":"理性準則改善決策，但不能移除每個意外結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reasonable standards for judgement.","zh":"這個片語描述判斷中的合理標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"uncertain in its consequences","meaning":"其後果是不確定的","examples":[{"en":"All social action is uncertain in its consequences.","zh":"所有社會行動的後果都是不確定的。"},{"en":"Uncertain in its consequences means the final effects cannot be fully predicted.","zh":"Uncertain in its consequences 指最終影響不能被完全預測。"},{"en":"A new school policy may be uncertain in its consequences until students actually experience it.","zh":"新學校政策在學生真正經歷之前，其後果可能是不確定的。"},{"en":"If consequences are uncertain, leaders should check results and be ready to adjust.","zh":"如果後果不確定，領導者應檢查結果並準備調整。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unpredictability after an action is taken.","zh":"這個片語描述行動採取後的不可預測性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"choose the most suitable heading","meaning":"選出最合適的標題","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the most suitable heading for each paragraph.","zh":"學生為每段選出最合適的標題。"},{"en":"To choose the most suitable heading means to select the title that best summarises the main idea.","zh":"To choose the most suitable heading 指選擇最能概括主旨的標題。"},{"en":"In reading practice, students should choose the most suitable heading after understanding the whole paragraph.","zh":"在閱讀練習中，學生應理解整段後才選出最合適的標題。"},{"en":"If a heading matches only one detail, it may not be the best answer.","zh":"如果標題只符合一個細節，它可能不是最佳答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in IELTS-style heading-matching tasks.","zh":"這個片語常見於 IELTS 式標題配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The list of headings contains more choices than needed.","zh":"標題列表包含比所需更多的選項。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a set of possible paragraph titles in a reading task.","zh":"List of headings 是閱讀任務中一組可能的段落標題。"},{"en":"Students should compare each heading with the paragraph’s main idea, not just one repeated word.","zh":"學生應把每個標題與段落主旨比較，而不只是看一個重複字。"},{"en":"Extra headings make the task harder because some choices will not be used.","zh":"額外標題令題目更困難，因為有些選項不會被使用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the answer options in a heading-matching exercise.","zh":"這個片語指標題配對練習中的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"write the appropriate number","meaning":"寫上合適的編號","examples":[{"en":"Students write the appropriate number on their answer sheet.","zh":"學生在答題紙上寫上合適的編號。"},{"en":"To write the appropriate number means to record the correct numbered answer for a question.","zh":"To write the appropriate number 指為問題記下正確的編號答案。"},{"en":"In a matching exercise, students must write the appropriate number beside each paragraph letter.","zh":"在配對練習中，學生必須在每個段落字母旁寫上合適的編號。"},{"en":"If students copy the wrong number, they may lose marks even when they understand the text.","zh":"如果學生抄錯編號，即使理解文章也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how answers are entered in a test.","zh":"這個片語描述考試中如何填寫答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"in boxes on your answer sheet","meaning":"在答題紙方格內","examples":[{"en":"Students write their answers in boxes on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生在答題紙方格內寫下答案。"},{"en":"In boxes on your answer sheet means in the marked spaces provided for answers.","zh":"In boxes on your answer sheet 指在提供作答的標示空格內。"},{"en":"In IELTS practice, students must write answers in boxes on the answer sheet, not in the question paper margin.","zh":"在 IELTS 練習中，學生必須在答題紙方格內寫答案，而不是寫在試卷邊位。"},{"en":"If answers are written in the wrong place, they may not be counted.","zh":"如果答案寫在錯誤位置，它們可能不被計算。"},{"en":"This phrase gives practical instructions for recording exam answers.","zh":"這個片語提供記錄考試答案的實際指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"contradiction of views on","meaning":"對……看法的矛盾","examples":[{"en":"The heading refers to a contradiction of views on scientific discovery.","zh":"該標題指對科學發現看法的矛盾。"},{"en":"A contradiction of views on something means two or more opinions about it conflict with each other.","zh":"Contradiction of views on something 指關於某事的兩個或多個意見互相衝突。"},{"en":"There may be a contradiction of views on homework if parents want more practice but students need more rest.","zh":"如果家長想要更多練習，但學生需要更多休息，對功課的看法可能出現矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradictory views can create debate because both sides cannot be fully true at the same time.","zh":"矛盾觀點可以引發辯論，因為雙方不能同時完全正確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes opposition between ideas about one topic.","zh":"這個片語描述同一題目上想法之間的對立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"resolving the contradiction","meaning":"解決矛盾","examples":[{"en":"One heading concerns resolving the contradiction in scientific discovery.","zh":"其中一個標題涉及解決科學發現中的矛盾。"},{"en":"Resolving the contradiction means finding a way to explain or settle two conflicting ideas.","zh":"Resolving the contradiction 指找到方法解釋或處理兩個衝突想法。"},{"en":"A teacher resolves a contradiction when she shows students how grammar can be both rule-based and flexible.","zh":"當老師向學生展示文法既有規則又可靈活使用時，她就解決了一個矛盾。"},{"en":"If a contradiction is resolved, the argument becomes clearer and more balanced.","zh":"如果矛盾被解決，論點會變得更清楚和更平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes solving a tension between opposing views.","zh":"這個片語描述解決相反觀點之間的張力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"came into being","meaning":"形成；出現","examples":[{"en":"One heading asks how the word came into being.","zh":"其中一個標題問這個詞如何形成。"},{"en":"Came into being means began to exist or was created.","zh":"Came into being 指開始存在或被創造。"},{"en":"A school club came into being when several students asked for a place to practise debate.","zh":"當幾個學生要求有地方練習辯論，一個學校學會便形成了。"},{"en":"Understanding how a word came into being helps explain its original meaning.","zh":"理解一個詞如何形成，有助解釋其原本意思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes origin or creation.","zh":"這個片語描述起源或創造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"illustration of","meaning":"對……的說明；例證","examples":[{"en":"The paragraph gives an illustration of serendipity in the business sector.","zh":"該段提供 serendipity 在商界中的例證。"},{"en":"An illustration of something is an example that helps explain it.","zh":"Illustration of something 是幫助解釋某事的例子。"},{"en":"A teacher may give an illustration of teamwork by describing how nurses cooperate in a hospital.","zh":"老師可能透過描述護士如何在醫院合作，提供團隊合作的例證。"},{"en":"If an abstract idea is difficult, an illustration makes it easier to understand.","zh":"如果抽象想法困難，例證會令它更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an example used for explanation.","zh":"這個片語指用於解釋的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"business sector","meaning":"商界；商業領域","examples":[{"en":"Industrial research provides an example from the business sector.","zh":"工業研究提供了來自商界的例子。"},{"en":"The business sector means the part of society made up of companies and commercial organisations.","zh":"Business sector 指由公司和商業組織組成的社會部分。"},{"en":"Students may enter the business sector after studying marketing, finance, or management.","zh":"學生學習市場學、金融或管理後，可能進入商業領域。"},{"en":"If an idea appears in the business sector, it is not limited to universities.","zh":"如果一個想法出現在商界，它就不限於大學。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the world of companies and commerce.","zh":"這個片語指公司和商業的世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter from the options.","zh":"學生從選項中選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer choice that best matches the question.","zh":"To choose the correct letter 指選擇最符合題目的答案選項。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should choose the correct letter only after checking the relevant paragraph.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應在檢查相關段落後才選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Similar options can be traps, so meaning matters more than repeated words.","zh":"相似選項可以是陷阱，所以意思比重複字更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is a standard multiple-choice instruction.","zh":"這個片語是標準多項選擇指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"means","meaning":"意思是","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what “inductivism” means in paragraph A.","zh":"題目問 paragraph A 中 “inductivism” 的意思是甚麼。"},{"en":"Means introduces the definition or explanation of a word, phrase, or idea.","zh":"Means 用來引出詞語、片語或想法的定義或解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask what “evaluate” means before students answer an essay question.","zh":"老師可能在學生回答作文題前，先問 “evaluate” 的意思是甚麼。"},{"en":"If students misunderstand what a key word means, they may choose the wrong answer.","zh":"如果學生誤解關鍵詞的意思，他們可能選錯答案。"},{"en":"This word is used when explaining meaning.","zh":"這個詞用於解釋意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"anticipate results","meaning":"預期結果","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers may anticipate results from the beginning.","zh":"一些研究人員可能從一開始就預期結果。"},{"en":"To anticipate results means to expect or predict outcomes before they happen.","zh":"To anticipate results 指在結果發生前預期或預測它們。"},{"en":"A student may anticipate results in a science experiment by guessing which plant will grow fastest.","zh":"學生可能在科學實驗中預期結果，猜測哪棵植物會長得最快。"},{"en":"Anticipating results can guide research, but it can also create bias.","zh":"預期結果可以引導研究，但也可能造成偏見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes expecting outcomes in advance.","zh":"這個片語描述事先期待結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"from the beginning","meaning":"從一開始","examples":[{"en":"The question option refers to anticipating results from the beginning.","zh":"該題目選項提到從一開始就預期結果。"},{"en":"From the beginning means from the very start of a process or activity.","zh":"From the beginning 指從過程或活動最初開始。"},{"en":"A student who plans from the beginning is less likely to rush the essay at the end.","zh":"從一開始就規劃的學生，較不可能在最後匆忙寫作文。"},{"en":"If expectations exist from the beginning, they may shape what people notice later.","zh":"如果從一開始就有期望，它們可能塑造人們之後注意到的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the starting point of a process.","zh":"這個片語標示過程的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"work from prepared premises","meaning":"從既定前提出發","examples":[{"en":"Deductivism can involve working from prepared premises.","zh":"演繹主義可以涉及從既定前提出發。"},{"en":"To work from prepared premises means to begin reasoning from assumptions already chosen in advance.","zh":"To work from prepared premises 指從事先選定的假設開始推理。"},{"en":"A student working from prepared premises may build an argument from two fixed claims.","zh":"從既定前提出發的學生可能由兩個固定主張建立論證。"},{"en":"Prepared premises can make reasoning orderly, but they may limit surprise.","zh":"既定前提可以令推理有序，但可能限制驚喜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes starting with established assumptions.","zh":"這個片語描述由已建立假設開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"accept chance discoveries","meaning":"接受偶然發現","examples":[{"en":"Some approaches accept chance discoveries as part of science.","zh":"一些方法接受偶然發現是科學的一部分。"},{"en":"To accept chance discoveries means to recognise that accidental findings can be valuable.","zh":"To accept chance discoveries 指承認偶然發現可以有價值。"},{"en":"A teacher may accept a student’s unexpected observation as a useful starting point for discussion.","zh":"老師可能接受學生意外觀察作為討論的有用起點。"},{"en":"If researchers accept chance discoveries, they are more likely to investigate surprising results.","zh":"如果研究人員接受偶然發現，他們更可能調查令人驚訝的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes openness to useful accidents.","zh":"這個片語描述對有用意外保持開放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"discoveries tend to happen unplanned","meaning":"發現往往未經計劃地發生","examples":[{"en":"Medawar believed that discoveries tend to happen unplanned.","zh":"Medawar 相信發現往往未經計劃地發生。"},{"en":"Discoveries tend to happen unplanned means new findings often appear without being fully arranged in advance.","zh":"Discoveries tend to happen unplanned 指新發現常在沒有完全事先安排下出現。"},{"en":"A useful classroom activity may happen unplanned when students ask an unexpected question.","zh":"當學生提出意外問題，一個有用課堂活動可能未經計劃地發生。"},{"en":"If discoveries often happen unplanned, researchers need flexibility as well as method.","zh":"如果發現常未經計劃地發生，研究人員既需要方法，也需要彈性。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the accidental side of discovery.","zh":"這個片語強調發現的偶然一面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"a determined mind","meaning":"堅定的頭腦","examples":[{"en":"Some answer options refer to discoveries made by people with a determined mind.","zh":"一些答案選項提到由具有堅定頭腦的人作出的發現。"},{"en":"A determined mind is a mindset that keeps trying despite difficulty or uncertainty.","zh":"Determined mind 是在困難或不確定中仍持續嘗試的心態。"},{"en":"A student with a determined mind may keep revising after several weak essays.","zh":"具有堅定頭腦的學生可能在幾篇作文表現薄弱後仍繼續修改。"},{"en":"Determination can help people continue, but it does not guarantee discovery.","zh":"決心可以幫助人持續下去，但不保證發現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental persistence and focus.","zh":"這個片語描述心理上的堅持和專注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"personal skill","meaning":"個人技巧","examples":[{"en":"The question contrasts serendipity as a situation with serendipity as a personal skill.","zh":"題目把 serendipity 作為情況與作為個人技巧作對比。"},{"en":"A personal skill is an ability that belongs to an individual and can often be practised or improved.","zh":"Personal skill 是屬於個人的能力，通常可以練習或改善。"},{"en":"Public speaking is a personal skill that improves when students receive feedback.","zh":"公開演說是一種個人技巧，學生收到回饋後會進步。"},{"en":"If serendipity is a personal skill, some people may be better at using accidents than others.","zh":"如果 serendipity 是個人技巧，有些人可能比其他人更善於利用意外。"},{"en":"This phrase describes individual ability rather than external circumstance.","zh":"這個片語描述個人能力，而不是外部情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"devalues scientific expertise","meaning":"貶低科學專業知識","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists fear that serendipity devalues scientific expertise.","zh":"一些科學家擔心 serendipity 會貶低科學專業知識。"},{"en":"To devalue scientific expertise means to make specialised scientific knowledge seem less important or less respected.","zh":"To devalue scientific expertise 指令專門科學知識顯得較不重要或較不受尊重。"},{"en":"Saying that medical success is only luck would devalue doctors’ training and judgement.","zh":"說醫療成功只是運氣，會貶低醫生的訓練和判斷。"},{"en":"If chance is overemphasised, experts may worry that their preparation is being ignored.","zh":"如果過分強調機遇，專家可能擔心自己的準備被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing the perceived value of expert knowledge.","zh":"這個片語描述降低專家知識的被認知價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"beyond their comprehension","meaning":"超出他們的理解","examples":[{"en":"One option suggests that serendipity is beyond some scientists’ comprehension.","zh":"一個選項暗示 serendipity 超出一些科學家的理解。"},{"en":"Beyond their comprehension means too difficult or strange for them to understand.","zh":"Beyond their comprehension 指對他們來說太難或太奇怪，以致不能理解。"},{"en":"Advanced physics may be beyond a young child’s comprehension without simple examples.","zh":"如果沒有簡單例子，高階物理可能超出小孩的理解。"},{"en":"If an idea is beyond someone’s comprehension, they may reject it too quickly.","zh":"如果一個想法超出某人的理解，他可能太快拒絕它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the limit of someone’s understanding.","zh":"這個片語描述某人理解能力的界限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"accepting uncertainty","meaning":"接受不確定性","examples":[{"en":"Accepting uncertainty can help produce positive results in research.","zh":"接受不確定性可以幫助研究產生正面結果。"},{"en":"Accepting uncertainty means recognising that not everything can be predicted or controlled.","zh":"Accepting uncertainty 指承認不是一切都能被預測或控制。"},{"en":"A student accepts uncertainty when they prepare well but know the exam may still contain surprises.","zh":"當學生準備充分，但知道考試仍可能有驚喜時，他就是接受不確定性。"},{"en":"Accepting uncertainty encourages flexible planning and careful observation.","zh":"接受不確定性鼓勵彈性規劃和仔細觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a realistic attitude toward unknown outcomes.","zh":"這個片語描述對未知結果的現實態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"positive results","meaning":"正面結果","examples":[{"en":"Accepting uncertainty can help researchers produce positive results.","zh":"接受不確定性可以幫助研究人員產生正面結果。"},{"en":"Positive results are useful, successful, or beneficial outcomes.","zh":"Positive results 是有用、成功或有益的成果。"},{"en":"A school may see positive results when students receive regular feedback and practise more.","zh":"當學生收到定期回饋並多加練習，學校可能看見正面結果。"},{"en":"Positive results often come from both planning and adjustment.","zh":"正面結果常來自規劃和調整兩者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes outcomes that help rather than harm.","zh":"這個片語描述有幫助而非有害的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"conflict between reality and expectation","meaning":"現實與期望之間的衝突","examples":[{"en":"The Yosemite example shows a conflict between reality and expectation.","zh":"Yosemite 的例子顯示現實與期望之間的衝突。"},{"en":"A conflict between reality and expectation happens when what actually occurs differs from what people hoped or predicted.","zh":"Conflict between reality and expectation 發生於實際情況與人們希望或預測不同時。"},{"en":"A student may expect university to be easy but face a conflict between reality and expectation after heavy assignments.","zh":"學生可能期望大學很容易，但在大量功課後面對現實與期望之間的衝突。"},{"en":"Such conflict can reveal the unanticipated consequences of human action.","zh":"這種衝突可以揭示人類行動的未預料後果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mismatch between plans and actual outcomes.","zh":"這個片語描述計劃與實際結果之間的不配合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"systematic planning","meaning":"系統性規劃","examples":[{"en":"One option contrasts uncertainty with systematic planning.","zh":"一個選項把不確定性與系統性規劃作對比。"},{"en":"Systematic planning means organised preparation using clear steps, evidence, and goals.","zh":"Systematic planning 指使用清楚步驟、證據和目標作有組織準備。"},{"en":"A student uses systematic planning when they divide revision into weekly tasks.","zh":"當學生把溫習分成每週任務，他就是使用系統性規劃。"},{"en":"Systematic planning reduces confusion, but it cannot remove every surprise.","zh":"系統性規劃減少混亂，但不能移除每個驚喜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful organised preparation.","zh":"這個片語描述仔細而有組織的準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"the power of anticipation","meaning":"預期的力量","examples":[{"en":"The question option refers to the power of anticipation.","zh":"該題目選項提到預期的力量。"},{"en":"The power of anticipation means the influence that expectations have on how people think, notice, or act.","zh":"The power of anticipation 指期望對人們如何思考、注意或行動的影響。"},{"en":"A student who expects a listening test may pay more attention to pronunciation during practice.","zh":"預期有聆聽測驗的學生，可能在練習中更留意發音。"},{"en":"Anticipation can guide attention, but it can also make people miss unexpected evidence.","zh":"預期可以引導注意力，但也可能令人錯過意外證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how expecting something can shape behaviour.","zh":"這個片語描述期待某事如何塑造行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"answer the questions below","meaning":"回答以下問題","examples":[{"en":"Students answer the questions below using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞回答以下問題。"},{"en":"To answer the questions below means to respond to the listed questions that follow the instruction.","zh":"To answer the questions below 指回應指示之後列出的問題。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should answer the questions below only after locating the relevant lines.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應在找到相關行文後才回答以下問題。"},{"en":"If students answer from memory instead of the passage, they may choose unsupported answers.","zh":"如果學生憑記憶而不是文章作答，他們可能選擇沒有支持的答案。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a direct exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語給出直接考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should use no more than two words from the passage.","zh":"每個答案應使用文章中不多於兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must contain two words or fewer.","zh":"No more than two words 指答案必須包含兩個字或更少。"},{"en":"If the correct idea is “fairy tale”, students can write it because it has two words.","zh":"如果正確意思是 “fairy tale”，學生可以寫它，因為它有兩個字。"},{"en":"Writing three words may lose marks even if the meaning is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫三個字也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a strict word limit in completion questions.","zh":"這個片語在填充題中設定嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"from the passage","meaning":"來自文章","examples":[{"en":"The answer must be taken from the passage.","zh":"答案必須來自文章。"},{"en":"From the passage means the words or information must come directly from the reading text.","zh":"From the passage 指字詞或資料必須直接來自閱讀文章。"},{"en":"Students should copy the answer from the passage, not invent their own synonym.","zh":"學生應從文章中抄出答案，而不是自創同義詞。"},{"en":"If the question says “from the passage”, outside knowledge should not be used.","zh":"如果題目說 “from the passage”，就不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase tells students where the evidence or wording must come from.","zh":"這個片語告訴學生證據或措辭必須來自哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"the person who first used","meaning":"首位使用……的人","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for the person who first used the word.","zh":"題目問首位使用該詞的人。"},{"en":"The person who first used something is the earliest known user recorded in the evidence.","zh":"The person who first used something 是證據中記錄的最早已知使用者。"},{"en":"A dictionary may name the person who first used a term in a letter or book.","zh":"字典可能指出在信件或書中首位使用某術語的人。"},{"en":"Knowing the first user can help trace the history of a word.","zh":"知道首位使用者可以幫助追溯詞語歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for an individual connected with an origin.","zh":"這個片語詢問與起源有關的個人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"what kind of story","meaning":"哪一類故事","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what kind of story the word comes from.","zh":"題目問這個詞來自哪一類故事。"},{"en":"What kind of story asks for the type or genre of a story.","zh":"What kind of story 詢問故事的類型或體裁。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask what kind of story students are reading: a myth, a fairy tale, or a biography.","zh":"老師可能問學生正在讀哪一類故事：神話、童話還是傳記。"},{"en":"Identifying the story type can help explain tone, purpose, and meaning.","zh":"辨認故事類型可以幫助解釋語氣、目的和意義。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for classification, not the whole plot.","zh":"這個片語問的是分類，而不是整個情節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"the present name of","meaning":"……的現今名稱","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for the present name of Serendip.","zh":"題目問 Serendip 的現今名稱。"},{"en":"The present name of a place means the name used for it today.","zh":"The present name of a place 指該地方今天使用的名稱。"},{"en":"A history teacher may ask for the present name of an ancient city to connect past and modern maps.","zh":"歷史老師可能要求學生說出古城的現今名稱，以連接古代和現代地圖。"},{"en":"If old names change, present names help readers locate places in the current world.","zh":"如果舊名稱改變，現今名稱幫助讀者在當前世界定位地方。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for the modern equivalent of an older name.","zh":"這個片語詢問舊名稱的現代對應名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 38 - Accidental Scientists.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 39":[{"front":"mental functions","meaning":"心智能力","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe all mental functions are localised in the brain.","zh":"有些人相信所有心智能力都定位於大腦中。"},{"en":"Mental functions are abilities of the mind, such as memory, attention, language, emotion, and decision-making.","zh":"mental functions 指心智的能力，例如記憶、注意力、語言、情緒和決策。"},{"en":"A student uses several mental functions when reading a passage, remembering details, and choosing an answer.","zh":"學生閱讀文章、記住細節並選擇答案時，會使用多種心智能力。"},{"en":"If a mental function is damaged after brain injury, a person may lose one ability while keeping others.","zh":"如果某種心智能力在腦傷後受損，一個人可能失去一種能力，但保留其他能力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what the mind does, not just what the body does.","zh":"這個片語指心智所做的事情，而不只是身體所做的動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a missed educational opportunity","meaning":"錯失的教育機會","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer sees this as a missed educational opportunity.","zh":"評論者認為這是一個錯失的教育機會。"},{"en":"A missed educational opportunity is a chance to teach or explain something useful that was not taken.","zh":"missed educational opportunity 指一個本可教授或解釋有用知識、但沒有把握的機會。"},{"en":"If a teacher marks an essay but gives no feedback, it may be a missed educational opportunity.","zh":"如果老師批改文章但沒有給回饋，這可能是錯失的教育機會。"},{"en":"When a book describes strange cases but does not explain their wider meaning, readers may lose a chance to learn more deeply.","zh":"當一本書描述奇特個案卻不解釋其更廣泛意義，讀者可能失去更深入學習的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises the failure to turn information into learning.","zh":"這個片語批評未能把資訊轉化為學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"another conclusion one could draw","meaning":"另一個可得出的結論是","examples":[{"en":"Another conclusion one could draw is that there are no clear cures.","zh":"另一個可得出的結論是，目前沒有清楚療法。"},{"en":"Another conclusion one could draw means another reasonable idea that can be inferred from the evidence.","zh":"another conclusion one could draw 指從證據中可推論出的另一個合理想法。"},{"en":"If several students fail the same question, another conclusion one could draw is that the instruction was unclear.","zh":"如果幾位學生答錯同一道題，另一個可得出的結論是指示不清楚。"},{"en":"When the same evidence supports more than one explanation, careful writers should mention the possible conclusions.","zh":"當同一證據支持多於一種解釋，細心作者應提及可能結論。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an additional interpretation.","zh":"這個片語引出額外詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"neurological problems","meaning":"神經系統問題","examples":[{"en":"There seem to be no cures for neurological problems involving music.","zh":"涉及音樂的神經系統問題似乎沒有明確療法。"},{"en":"Neurological problems are medical problems connected with the brain, nerves, or nervous system.","zh":"neurological problems 指與大腦、神經或神經系統有關的醫學問題。"},{"en":"Memory loss, seizures, unusual movement, and speech difficulty can all be neurological problems.","zh":"記憶喪失、癲癇發作、異常動作和說話困難都可以是神經系統問題。"},{"en":"If a neurological problem affects music, a person may hear sounds normally but process music strangely.","zh":"如果神經系統問題影響音樂，一個人可能正常聽到聲音，卻奇怪地處理音樂。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to problems rooted in the nervous system.","zh":"這個片語指根源於神經系統的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"involving music","meaning":"涉及音樂的","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses neurological problems involving music.","zh":"這本書討論涉及音樂的神經系統問題。"},{"en":"Involving music means connected with music or including music as an important part.","zh":"involving music 指與音樂有關，或把音樂作為重要部分包括在內。"},{"en":"A school project involving music may ask students to compare rhythm, emotion, and memory.","zh":"涉及音樂的學校專題可能要求學生比較節奏、情感和記憶。"},{"en":"If a medical case involves music, doctors may study hearing, movement, memory, or emotion together.","zh":"如果醫學個案涉及音樂，醫生可能同時研究聽覺、動作、記憶或情緒。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that music is part of the situation being discussed.","zh":"這個片語顯示音樂是所討論情況的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"alleviate a symptom","meaning":"紓緩症狀","examples":[{"en":"A drug can alleviate a symptom in one patient.","zh":"一種藥物可以在一名病人身上紓緩症狀。"},{"en":"Alleviate a symptom means make a sign of illness less severe or easier to bear.","zh":"alleviate a symptom 指令某個疾病徵狀變得較輕或較容易承受。"},{"en":"Rest and water may alleviate a headache caused by tiredness.","zh":"休息和喝水可能紓緩由疲倦造成的頭痛。"},{"en":"A treatment may alleviate one symptom without curing the underlying condition.","zh":"治療可以紓緩一種症狀，但未必治癒根本病症。"},{"en":"The phrase means reduce suffering, not necessarily remove the illness completely.","zh":"這個片語意思是減少痛苦，而不一定完全消除疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"aggravate a symptom","meaning":"加重症狀","examples":[{"en":"The same drug can aggravate a symptom in another patient.","zh":"同一種藥物可以在另一名病人身上加重症狀。"},{"en":"Aggravate a symptom means make a symptom worse or more difficult to manage.","zh":"aggravate a symptom 指令某個症狀惡化或更難處理。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can aggravate anxiety before an important exam.","zh":"睡眠不足可以加重重要考試前的焦慮。"},{"en":"If a medication aggravates a symptom, doctors may need to change the dose or try another treatment.","zh":"如果藥物加重症狀，醫生可能需要改變劑量或嘗試另一種治療。"},{"en":"The phrase describes worsening, not improvement.","zh":"這個片語描述惡化，而不是改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"positive and negative effects","meaning":"正面及負面影響","examples":[{"en":"A drug can have both positive and negative effects.","zh":"一種藥物可以同時有正面及負面影響。"},{"en":"Positive and negative effects are helpful results and harmful or unwanted results.","zh":"positive and negative effects 指有幫助的結果，以及有害或不想要的結果。"},{"en":"Social media can have positive effects on communication but negative effects on concentration.","zh":"社交媒體可以對溝通有正面影響，但對專注力有負面影響。"},{"en":"If a treatment has both positive and negative effects, doctors must weigh benefit against risk.","zh":"如果一種治療同時有正面及負面影響，醫生必須權衡好處與風險。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds readers that one action can bring mixed outcomes.","zh":"這個片語提醒讀者，同一行動可以帶來混合結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"almost exclusively","meaning":"幾乎全都是","examples":[{"en":"The treatments mentioned are almost exclusively antiepileptic medications.","zh":"所提到的治療幾乎全都是抗癲癇藥物。"},{"en":"Almost exclusively means nearly only one type, with very few exceptions.","zh":"almost exclusively 指幾乎只有一種類型，例外很少。"},{"en":"A café that sells almost exclusively coffee may offer only one or two small snacks.","zh":"一間幾乎全都賣咖啡的咖啡店，可能只提供一兩款小食。"},{"en":"If a book discusses almost exclusively one treatment, readers may wonder whether other options were ignored.","zh":"如果一本書幾乎只討論一種治療，讀者可能會想其他選項是否被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a very narrow focus.","zh":"這個片語強調焦點非常狹窄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"antiepileptic medications","meaning":"抗癲癇藥物","examples":[{"en":"The treatments mentioned are mostly antiepileptic medications.","zh":"所提到的治療大多是抗癲癇藥物。"},{"en":"Antiepileptic medications are drugs used to reduce or prevent seizures and abnormal brain excitability.","zh":"antiepileptic medications 指用來減少或預防癲癇發作及異常大腦興奮性的藥物。"},{"en":"A patient with epilepsy may take antiepileptic medications every day under medical supervision.","zh":"癲癇病人可能在醫生監督下每天服用抗癲癇藥物。"},{"en":"If such drugs affect brain excitability generally, they may help one symptom but disturb another.","zh":"如果這類藥物整體影響大腦興奮性，它們可能幫助一種症狀，卻干擾另一種。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a class of medicines, not a general cure for all brain disorders.","zh":"這個片語指一類藥物，而不是所有大腦疾病的通用療法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"damp down","meaning":"減弱；抑制","examples":[{"en":"These medications damp down the excitability of the brain.","zh":"這些藥物會抑制大腦興奮性。"},{"en":"Damp down means reduce, calm, or suppress something that is too strong or active.","zh":"damp down 指減少、平息或抑制過強或過度活躍的東西。"},{"en":"A teacher may damp down a noisy class by lowering their voice and giving clear instructions.","zh":"老師可能透過降低聲線並給出清楚指示，平息嘈吵班級。"},{"en":"If a drug damps down brain activity too broadly, useful functions may also be affected.","zh":"如果藥物過於廣泛地抑制大腦活動，有用功能也可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests reducing intensity.","zh":"這個片語暗示降低強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"excitability of the brain","meaning":"大腦興奮性","examples":[{"en":"Antiepileptic medications reduce the excitability of the brain.","zh":"抗癲癇藥物會降低大腦興奮性。"},{"en":"Excitability of the brain means how easily brain cells become active or fire signals.","zh":"excitability of the brain 指腦細胞有多容易變得活躍或發出訊號。"},{"en":"Doctors may worry about high brain excitability if a patient is prone to seizures.","zh":"如果病人容易癲癇發作，醫生可能會擔心大腦興奮性過高。"},{"en":"Reducing brain excitability can help prevent abnormal activity, but the effect may not be perfectly targeted.","zh":"降低大腦興奮性可以幫助防止異常活動，但效果未必完全精準。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the brain’s tendency to become electrically active.","zh":"這個片語指大腦變得電活動活躍的傾向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in general","meaning":"整體而言；一般來說","examples":[{"en":"These medications affect the brain in general.","zh":"這些藥物整體而言會影響大腦。"},{"en":"In general means broadly, overall, or in most cases rather than in one precise situation.","zh":"in general 指廣泛地、整體上或在大多數情況下，而不是指一個精確情況。"},{"en":"In general, students learn better when examples are clear and connected to daily life.","zh":"一般來說，當例子清楚並連接日常生活，學生會學得更好。"},{"en":"If a medicine acts on the brain in general, it may not target only one small function.","zh":"如果藥物整體作用於大腦，它可能不只針對一個細小功能。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a broad statement rather than a detailed exception.","zh":"這個片語給出概括陳述，而不是詳細例外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"effectiveness varies widely","meaning":"成效差異很大","examples":[{"en":"The effectiveness of these treatments varies widely.","zh":"這些治療的成效差異很大。"},{"en":"Effectiveness varies widely means something works very differently across people, cases, or situations.","zh":"effectiveness varies widely 指某事在不同人、個案或情況中效果非常不同。"},{"en":"A study method may work well for one student but poorly for another, so its effectiveness varies widely.","zh":"一種溫習方法可能對一名學生很有效，對另一名學生很差，所以成效差異很大。"},{"en":"If a treatment’s effectiveness varies widely, doctors must observe each patient carefully.","zh":"如果治療成效差異很大，醫生必須仔細觀察每位病人。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses inconsistent results.","zh":"這個片語強調結果不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in many of the cases described","meaning":"在所描述的許多個案中","examples":[{"en":"In many of the cases described, patients had normal EEG results.","zh":"在所描述的許多個案中，病人的腦電圖結果正常。"},{"en":"In many of the cases described means in a large number of the examples discussed in the text.","zh":"in many of the cases described 指在文本討論的大量例子中。"},{"en":"In many of the cases described in a school report, stress was linked to sleep loss.","zh":"在學校報告所描述的許多個案中，壓力與睡眠不足有關。"},{"en":"If many described cases show the same pattern, the writer may be pointing to a broader problem.","zh":"如果許多被描述的個案顯示同一模式，作者可能正在指出更廣泛問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to repeated examples within the material.","zh":"這個片語指材料中反覆出現的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"music-brain symptoms","meaning":"音樂與大腦相關症狀","examples":[{"en":"Patients with music-brain symptoms sometimes have normal EEG results.","zh":"有音樂與大腦相關症狀的病人，有時腦電圖結果正常。"},{"en":"Music-brain symptoms are unusual signs or experiences involving both music and brain function.","zh":"music-brain symptoms 指同時涉及音樂和大腦功能的不尋常徵狀或經驗。"},{"en":"Hearing music that is not playing may be a music-brain symptom if it comes from neurological change.","zh":"如果聽到不存在的音樂來自神經變化，這可能是音樂與大腦相關症狀。"},{"en":"If music-brain symptoms appear despite normal basic tests, more sensitive methods may be needed.","zh":"如果基本測試正常但仍出現音樂與大腦相關症狀，就可能需要更靈敏方法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to symptoms at the link between music and the nervous system.","zh":"這個片語指音樂與神經系統連結處的症狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"EEG results","meaning":"腦電圖結果","examples":[{"en":"Many patients were reported to have normal EEG results.","zh":"許多病人被報告有正常腦電圖結果。"},{"en":"EEG results are the findings from a test that records electrical activity in the brain.","zh":"EEG results 指記錄大腦電活動的測試所得結果。"},{"en":"A doctor may compare EEG results with a patient’s symptoms before deciding what to do next.","zh":"醫生可能把腦電圖結果與病人症狀比較，再決定下一步。"},{"en":"Normal EEG results do not always mean there is no subtle brain problem.","zh":"正常腦電圖結果不一定代表沒有細微大腦問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the recorded outcome of brain-wave testing.","zh":"這個片語指腦電波測試的記錄結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"recognise the existence of","meaning":"承認……的存在","examples":[{"en":"Sacks recognises the existence of new technologies.","zh":"Sacks 承認新科技的存在。"},{"en":"Recognise the existence of means acknowledge that something exists or is real.","zh":"recognise the existence of 指承認某事物存在或是真實的。"},{"en":"A school must recognise the existence of online bullying before it can deal with it properly.","zh":"學校必須先承認網絡欺凌的存在，才能妥善處理它。"},{"en":"If a writer recognises new technology but does not use it, readers may still question their approach.","zh":"如果作者承認新科技存在但不使用它，讀者仍可能質疑其方法。"},{"en":"The phrase means admitting something is there, not necessarily supporting it strongly.","zh":"這個片語意思是承認某事存在，而不一定強烈支持它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"far more sensitive ways to","meaning":"靈敏得多的……方法","examples":[{"en":"There are far more sensitive ways to analyse brain waves.","zh":"現在有靈敏得多的方法去分析腦電波。"},{"en":"Far more sensitive ways to do something are methods that can detect much smaller details than older methods.","zh":"far more sensitive ways to do something 指比舊方法能偵測細小得多細節的方法。"},{"en":"Modern cameras offer far more sensitive ways to study tiny movements in sports training.","zh":"現代攝影機提供靈敏得多的方法，去研究運動訓練中的細微動作。"},{"en":"If newer tools are far more sensitive, they may reveal problems missed by standard tests.","zh":"如果較新工具靈敏得多，它們可能揭示標準測試錯過的問題。"},{"en":"The phrase compares a newer or better method with a less precise one.","zh":"這個片語比較較新或較好方法與較不精準方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"analyse brain waves","meaning":"分析腦電波","examples":[{"en":"New technologies can analyse brain waves more sensitively.","zh":"新科技可以更靈敏地分析腦電波。"},{"en":"Analyse brain waves means study patterns of electrical activity in the brain.","zh":"analyse brain waves 指研究大腦電活動的模式。"},{"en":"Doctors may analyse brain waves to investigate seizures, sleep problems, or unusual experiences.","zh":"醫生可能分析腦電波，以研究癲癇、睡眠問題或不尋常經驗。"},{"en":"If brain waves are analysed with better tools, subtle abnormalities may become visible.","zh":"如果用更好工具分析腦電波，細微異常可能變得可見。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to examining the brain’s electrical signals.","zh":"這個片語指檢視大腦的電訊號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"standard neurological EEG test","meaning":"標準神經科腦電圖測試","examples":[{"en":"The standard neurological EEG test may not be sensitive enough.","zh":"標準神經科腦電圖測試可能不夠靈敏。"},{"en":"A standard neurological EEG test is a usual medical test for recording brain electrical activity.","zh":"standard neurological EEG test 指常用於記錄大腦電活動的醫學測試。"},{"en":"A hospital may use a standard EEG test first because it is familiar and widely available.","zh":"醫院可能先使用標準腦電圖測試，因為它常見且普遍可用。"},{"en":"If a standard test misses subtle symptoms, doctors may need newer or more specialised methods.","zh":"如果標準測試錯過細微症狀，醫生可能需要較新或較專門的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the ordinary clinical brain-wave test.","zh":"這個片語指普通臨床腦電波測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"call for their use","meaning":"呼籲使用它們","examples":[{"en":"Sacks does not call for the use of newer technologies.","zh":"Sacks 沒有呼籲使用較新的科技。"},{"en":"Call for their use means publicly recommend or demand that those methods or tools should be used.","zh":"call for their use 指公開建議或要求使用那些方法或工具。"},{"en":"After repeated accidents, parents may call for the use of safer school buses.","zh":"在多次意外後，家長可能呼籲使用更安全的校巴。"},{"en":"If an expert recognises new tests but does not call for their use, the reviewer may see a lack of urgency.","zh":"如果專家承認新測試但不呼籲使用它們，評論者可能認為缺乏迫切感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes asking others to adopt something.","zh":"這個片語描述要求他人採用某事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"exhibit compassion for","meaning":"對……表現出同情","examples":[{"en":"Sacks exhibits great compassion for patients.","zh":"Sacks 對病人表現出極大同情。"},{"en":"Exhibit compassion for means show deep care, sympathy, and concern for someone’s suffering.","zh":"exhibit compassion for 指對某人的痛苦表現出深切關懷、同情和關注。"},{"en":"A good nurse exhibits compassion for patients by listening patiently and explaining treatment gently.","zh":"好護士透過耐心聆聽和溫和解釋治療，對病人表現出同情。"},{"en":"If a writer shows compassion for patients, case studies feel humane rather than cold.","zh":"如果作者對病人表現出同情，個案研究會顯得有人性，而不是冰冷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visible kindness toward people in difficulty.","zh":"這個片語描述對困境中的人展現出可見的仁慈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"convey no sense of urgency","meaning":"沒有傳達出迫切感","examples":[{"en":"He conveys no sense of urgency about new diagnostic methods.","zh":"他對新的診斷方法沒有傳達出迫切感。"},{"en":"Convey no sense of urgency means fail to show that something needs immediate attention or action.","zh":"convey no sense of urgency 指未能顯示某事需要即時關注或行動。"},{"en":"A school notice conveys no sense of urgency if it mentions a safety problem casually and gives no deadline.","zh":"如果學校通告隨便提到安全問題且沒有期限，就沒有傳達出迫切感。"},{"en":"If a doctor writes without urgency about better tests, readers may feel progress is not being pushed strongly enough.","zh":"如果醫生對更好測試寫得毫無迫切感，讀者可能覺得進步沒有被強力推動。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises a calmness that may seem too passive.","zh":"這個片語批評一種可能顯得太被動的平靜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the pursuit of","meaning":"對……的追求","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer wants more urgency in the pursuit of new avenues.","zh":"評論者希望在追求新途徑方面有更多迫切感。"},{"en":"The pursuit of something means the active effort to find, achieve, or develop it.","zh":"pursuit of something 指積極努力尋找、達成或發展某事。"},{"en":"A student’s pursuit of better writing may include reading models, practising daily, and asking for feedback.","zh":"學生對更好寫作的追求可能包括閱讀範文、每日練習和尋求回饋。"},{"en":"If researchers are serious in the pursuit of new treatments, they must test ideas carefully.","zh":"如果研究人員認真追求新療法，就必須仔細測試想法。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses active searching or striving.","zh":"這個片語強調主動尋找或努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"new avenues","meaning":"新途徑；新方向","examples":[{"en":"The field needs new avenues in diagnosis and treatment.","zh":"這個領域在診斷與治療方面需要新途徑。"},{"en":"New avenues are new possible ways, methods, or directions for progress.","zh":"new avenues 指新的可能方法、途徑或進步方向。"},{"en":"Online platforms opened new avenues for students who could not attend lessons in person.","zh":"網上平台為無法親身上課的學生開啟新途徑。"},{"en":"If old methods do not solve a problem, researchers must search for new avenues.","zh":"如果舊方法不能解決問題，研究人員就必須尋找新方向。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests fresh paths for investigation or action.","zh":"這個片語暗示調查或行動的新道路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"diagnosis and treatment","meaning":"診斷與治療","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer wants progress in the diagnosis and treatment of music-brain disorders.","zh":"評論者希望音樂與大腦障礙的診斷與治療有所進展。"},{"en":"Diagnosis and treatment mean identifying a medical problem and then trying to manage or cure it.","zh":"diagnosis and treatment 指找出醫學問題，然後嘗試處理或治癒它。"},{"en":"Good diagnosis and treatment require both accurate tests and careful listening to the patient.","zh":"良好診斷與治療需要準確測試，也需要仔細聆聽病人。"},{"en":"If diagnosis is weak, treatment may target the wrong problem.","zh":"如果診斷薄弱，治療可能針對錯誤問題。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both finding the condition and helping the patient.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋找出病症和幫助病人兩方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"absence echoes","meaning":"這種缺失呼應了……","examples":[{"en":"This absence echoes the book’s preface.","zh":"這種缺失呼應了該書的前言。"},{"en":"Absence echoes means a missing element repeats or reflects an earlier idea.","zh":"absence echoes 指某個缺少的元素重複或反映較早的想法。"},{"en":"If a school report talks about student voice but includes no student comments, that absence echoes the problem it describes.","zh":"如果學校報告談學生聲音，卻沒有學生評論，這種缺失就呼應它所描述的問題。"},{"en":"When a book worries that technology may replace observation but then avoids new technology, the absence becomes meaningful.","zh":"當一本書擔心科技會取代觀察，卻又避開新科技，這種缺失就變得有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how something missing can still connect with a theme.","zh":"這個片語顯示缺少的東西也可以與主題相連。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"express fear that","meaning":"表達對……的擔憂","examples":[{"en":"Sacks expresses fear that observation may be lost.","zh":"Sacks 表達對觀察可能失傳的擔憂。"},{"en":"Express fear that means openly state worry that something bad may happen.","zh":"express fear that 指公開表示擔心某件壞事可能發生。"},{"en":"Parents may express fear that too much phone use will harm children’s sleep.","zh":"家長可能表達對過度使用手機會損害孩子睡眠的擔憂。"},{"en":"If a doctor expresses fear that observation may disappear, they are warning against overreliance on machines.","zh":"如果醫生表達對觀察可能消失的擔憂，他是在警告不要過分依賴機器。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a stated concern.","zh":"這個片語引出明確說出的憂慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be lost","meaning":"消失；失傳","examples":[{"en":"Sacks fears that the art of observation may be lost.","zh":"Sacks 擔心觀察的藝術可能失傳。"},{"en":"Be lost means disappear, be forgotten, or no longer be practised.","zh":"be lost 指消失、被遺忘或不再被實踐。"},{"en":"A local dialect may be lost if young people stop using it at home.","zh":"如果年輕人在家中停止使用本地方言，它可能失傳。"},{"en":"If careful observation is lost in medicine, important human details may be ignored.","zh":"如果醫學中的細心觀察消失，重要的人性細節可能被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe the disappearance of a skill, habit, object, or tradition.","zh":"這個片語可以描述技能、習慣、物件或傳統的消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rely too much on","meaning":"過分依賴","examples":[{"en":"Sacks worries that doctors may rely too much on new technologies.","zh":"Sacks 擔心醫生可能過分依賴新科技。"},{"en":"Rely too much on means depend excessively on something and neglect other useful methods.","zh":"rely too much on 指過度依靠某事，並忽略其他有用方法。"},{"en":"Students may rely too much on translation apps and stop learning how sentences work.","zh":"學生可能過分依賴翻譯應用程式，因而停止學習句子如何運作。"},{"en":"If doctors rely too much on scans, they may overlook what patients say and feel.","zh":"如果醫生過分依賴掃描，可能忽略病人所說和所感受的事情。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against overdependence.","zh":"這個片語提醒不要過度依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"call for both approaches","meaning":"呼籲同時採用兩種方法","examples":[{"en":"Sacks calls for both observation and technology.","zh":"Sacks 呼籲同時採用觀察和科技兩種方法。"},{"en":"Call for both approaches means argue that two methods should be used together.","zh":"call for both approaches 指主張兩種方法應一起使用。"},{"en":"A teacher may call for both grammar explanation and speaking practice in language lessons.","zh":"老師可能呼籲在語言課中同時採用文法解釋和口語練習。"},{"en":"If observation and technology are combined, doctors may gain both human detail and scientific precision.","zh":"如果觀察與科技結合，醫生可能同時獲得人的細節和科學精確性。"},{"en":"The phrase rejects a false choice between two useful methods.","zh":"這個片語拒絕在兩種有用方法之間作虛假的二選一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"neurological community","meaning":"神經學界","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer hopes the neurological community will respond.","zh":"評論者希望神經學界會作出回應。"},{"en":"The neurological community is the group of doctors, scientists, researchers, and professionals working on brain and nervous-system issues.","zh":"neurological community 指研究大腦和神經系統問題的醫生、科學家、研究人員和專業人士群體。"},{"en":"The neurological community may debate new treatments for stroke, epilepsy, or movement disorders.","zh":"神經學界可能討論中風、癲癇或運動障礙的新療法。"},{"en":"If the neurological community responds to new evidence, diagnosis and treatment may improve.","zh":"如果神經學界回應新證據，診斷與治療可能改善。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a professional field as a whole.","zh":"這個片語指整個專業領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students must choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生必須為每題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choose the correct letter means select the option letter that matches the right answer.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇與正確答案相符的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students choose the correct letter after comparing all the options with the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生把所有選項與文章比較後選出正確字母。"},{"en":"If two options look similar, students must check the exact wording before choosing.","zh":"如果兩個選項看起來相似，學生在選擇前必須檢查準確措辭。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction in multiple-choice questions.","zh":"這個片語是多項選擇題中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mixed feelings about","meaning":"對……感受複雜","examples":[{"en":"The question asks why the writer has mixed feelings about the book.","zh":"題目問為何作者對這本書感受複雜。"},{"en":"Mixed feelings about something are both positive and negative feelings toward it.","zh":"mixed feelings about something 指對某事同時有正面和負面感受。"},{"en":"A student may have mixed feelings about online lessons because they are convenient but lonely.","zh":"學生可能對網上課堂感受複雜，因為它方便但孤單。"},{"en":"If a reviewer has mixed feelings about a book, the review may include both praise and criticism.","zh":"如果評論者對一本書感受複雜，評論可能同時有讚賞和批評。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a reaction is not simply good or bad.","zh":"這個片語顯示反應不是單純好或壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cause this reaction","meaning":"引起這種反應","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what caused the writer’s reaction.","zh":"題目問甚麼引起作者這種反應。"},{"en":"Cause this reaction means make someone respond or feel in a particular way.","zh":"cause this reaction 指令某人以某種方式回應或感受。"},{"en":"A harsh comment from a teacher may cause a nervous reaction in a shy student.","zh":"老師一句嚴厲評論可能在害羞學生身上引起緊張反應。"},{"en":"If high expectations are not fully met, disappointment may cause a mixed reaction.","zh":"如果很高期望沒有完全被滿足，失望可能引起複雜反應。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a reason with an emotional or intellectual response.","zh":"這個片語把原因與情緒或思想反應連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"expect something to be better than","meaning":"期望……比實際更好","examples":[{"en":"The writer expected the book to be better than it was.","zh":"作者期望這本書比實際更好。"},{"en":"Expect something to be better than it was means believe beforehand that something would be of higher quality than it actually turned out to be.","zh":"expect something to be better than it was 指事前相信某事質素會比實際結果更高。"},{"en":"A student may expect a film to be better than it was because all their friends praised it.","zh":"學生可能因朋友全都讚賞某電影，而期望它比實際更好。"},{"en":"When expectations are too high, even a decent result can feel disappointing.","zh":"當期望太高，即使結果不錯，也可能令人失望。"},{"en":"The phrase explains disappointment caused by a gap between expectation and reality.","zh":"這個片語解釋期望與現實之間落差造成的失望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fail to include","meaning":"未能包括","examples":[{"en":"The option says that Sacks failed to include personal stories.","zh":"該選項說 Sacks 未能包括個人故事。"},{"en":"Fail to include means leave something out, often when it should have been included.","zh":"fail to include 指漏掉某事，通常是本應包括卻沒有包括。"},{"en":"A student may lose marks if they fail to include evidence in an argumentative essay.","zh":"如果學生在議論文中未能包括證據，可能會失分。"},{"en":"If a science book fails to include recent research, readers may question its completeness.","zh":"如果科學書未能包括近期研究，讀者可能質疑其完整性。"},{"en":"The phrase points to an omission.","zh":"這個片語指出遺漏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"personal stories","meaning":"個人故事","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to personal stories in the book.","zh":"題目提到書中的個人故事。"},{"en":"Personal stories are real experiences from a person’s life, told in a personal or autobiographical way.","zh":"personal stories 指某人生活中的真實經歷，以個人化或自傳式方式講述。"},{"en":"A teacher may use personal stories to make a difficult lesson feel more human.","zh":"老師可能使用個人故事，令困難課堂更有人情味。"},{"en":"If a medical book includes personal stories, patients may feel less like abstract cases.","zh":"如果醫學書包含個人故事，病人就較不會像抽象個案。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to lived experience rather than only theory.","zh":"這個片語指親身經驗，而不只是理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tone of voice","meaning":"語氣；寫作聲音","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the tone of voice of the book.","zh":"題目問這本書的語氣。"},{"en":"Tone of voice means the attitude or feeling expressed through writing or speech.","zh":"tone of voice 指透過寫作或說話表達出的態度或感覺。"},{"en":"A teacher’s tone of voice can make criticism sound helpful or hurtful.","zh":"老師的語氣可以令批評聽起來有幫助或傷人。"},{"en":"If a book’s tone is calm and erudite, readers may trust the author’s judgement.","zh":"如果一本書語氣平靜而博學，讀者可能信任作者判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to how something sounds emotionally and intellectually.","zh":"這個片語指某事在情感和思想上聽起來如何。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"autobiographical description","meaning":"自傳式描述","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions autobiographical description in the book.","zh":"題目提到書中的自傳式描述。"},{"en":"Autobiographical description is writing in which the author describes events, feelings, or memories from their own life.","zh":"autobiographical description 指作者描述自己人生中的事件、感受或記憶的寫作。"},{"en":"A memoir uses autobiographical description when the writer explains childhood experiences in detail.","zh":"當作家詳細解釋童年經歷，回憶錄就是在使用自傳式描述。"},{"en":"If a scientific book includes autobiographical description, it may feel warmer and more personal.","zh":"如果科學書包含自傳式描述，它可能感覺更溫暖、更個人化。"},{"en":"The phrase connects self-writing with descriptive detail.","zh":"這個片語把自我書寫與描述細節連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"come to terms with","meaning":"接受並適應","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Sacks tried to come to terms with new technologies.","zh":"題目問 Sacks 是否嘗試接受並適應新科技。"},{"en":"Come to terms with means accept, understand, and adjust to something difficult or new.","zh":"come to terms with 指接受、理解並適應困難或新的事物。"},{"en":"A student may need time to come to terms with moving to a new school.","zh":"學生可能需要時間接受並適應轉到新學校。"},{"en":"If doctors come to terms with new technology, they learn how to use it without losing older skills.","zh":"如果醫生接受並適應新科技，他們會學習如何使用它，而不失去舊技能。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests acceptance after tension or uncertainty.","zh":"這個片語暗示在緊張或不確定後的接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"do away with","meaning":"廢除；摒棄","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that Sacks wanted to do away with simple observation.","zh":"該選項暗示 Sacks 想摒棄簡單觀察。"},{"en":"Do away with means remove, abolish, or stop using something.","zh":"do away with 指移除、廢除或停止使用某事物。"},{"en":"A school may do away with paper notices and send messages through an app instead.","zh":"學校可能廢除紙本通告，改用應用程式發訊息。"},{"en":"If doctors do away with observation completely, they may lose important human details.","zh":"如果醫生完全摒棄觀察，可能失去重要的人性細節。"},{"en":"The phrase describes getting rid of something.","zh":"這個片語描述把某事物除去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"determine the cause of","meaning":"確定……的成因","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Cicoria can determine the cause of his musicality.","zh":"題目問 Cicoria 是否能確定其音樂才能的成因。"},{"en":"Determine the cause of means find out the reason why something happened.","zh":"determine the cause of 指找出某事發生的原因。"},{"en":"A doctor may run tests to determine the cause of a patient’s headaches.","zh":"醫生可能進行測試，以確定病人頭痛的成因。"},{"en":"If Cicoria refuses further tests, it becomes harder to determine the cause of his sudden musical ability.","zh":"如果 Cicoria 拒絕進一步測試，就更難確定其突然音樂能力的成因。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on identifying the reason behind a change or problem.","zh":"這個片語集中於找出改變或問題背後的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sudden musicality","meaning":"突然出現的音樂才能","examples":[{"en":"Cicoria’s sudden musicality followed a lightning strike.","zh":"Cicoria 突然出現的音樂才能是在雷擊後出現的。"},{"en":"Sudden musicality means musical ability or musical passion that appears unexpectedly and quickly.","zh":"sudden musicality 指意想不到且快速出現的音樂能力或音樂熱情。"},{"en":"A person with sudden musicality may begin composing songs despite having little previous training.","zh":"突然有音樂才能的人，可能即使以前很少受訓，也開始作曲。"},{"en":"If sudden musicality appears after an accident, scientists may suspect a neurological change.","zh":"如果突然出現的音樂才能發生在意外後，科學家可能懷疑神經變化。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the surprising speed of a new musical ability.","zh":"這個片語突出新音樂能力出現得令人驚訝地快速。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"further tests","meaning":"進一步測試","examples":[{"en":"Cicoria refuses to have further tests.","zh":"Cicoria 拒絕接受進一步測試。"},{"en":"Further tests are additional tests done after earlier ones, usually to gather more information.","zh":"further tests 指在早前測試後進行的額外測試，通常為取得更多資料。"},{"en":"A doctor may order further tests if a patient’s symptoms continue despite normal results.","zh":"如果病人症狀持續但結果正常，醫生可能安排進一步測試。"},{"en":"If further tests are refused, the cause of a condition may remain uncertain.","zh":"如果進一步測試被拒絕，病症成因可能仍不確定。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to extra investigation beyond the first test.","zh":"這個片語指首次測試以外的額外調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lightning strike","meaning":"雷擊","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to Cicoria’s lightning strike.","zh":"題目提到 Cicoria 的雷擊事件。"},{"en":"A lightning strike is an event in which lightning hits a person, object, or place.","zh":"lightning strike 指閃電擊中人、物件或地方的事件。"},{"en":"A lightning strike can damage trees, power systems, buildings, or the human body.","zh":"雷擊可以損害樹木、電力系統、建築物或人體。"},{"en":"If unusual symptoms follow a lightning strike, doctors may study whether the electrical injury affected the brain.","zh":"如果雷擊後出現不尋常症狀，醫生可能研究電擊傷害是否影響大腦。"},{"en":"The phrase names the sudden electrical event.","zh":"這個片語指出突然的電擊事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"agree with the views of","meaning":"符合……的看法","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements agree with the views of the writer.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否符合作者的看法。"},{"en":"Agree with the views of means match what someone thinks or argues.","zh":"agree with the views of 指與某人的想法或論點相符。"},{"en":"In reading questions, a statement agrees with the writer’s view only if the writer clearly supports that idea.","zh":"在閱讀題中，只有當作者清楚支持某想法，陳述才符合作者看法。"},{"en":"If students confuse facts with the writer’s opinion, they may choose the wrong answer.","zh":"如果學生混淆事實和作者意見，可能會選錯答案。"},{"en":"The phrase asks students to compare statements with the writer’s attitude.","zh":"這個片語要求學生把陳述與作者態度比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的看法相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the views of the writer.","zh":"陳述可能與作者的看法相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradict the views of means say the opposite of what someone thinks or argues.","zh":"contradict the views of 指說出與某人想法或論點相反的內容。"},{"en":"If a writer supports music therapy, a statement saying the writer rejects it would contradict the writer’s views.","zh":"如果作者支持音樂治療，而陳述說作者拒絕它，就與作者看法相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should choose NO only when the statement clearly goes against the writer’s opinion.","zh":"只有當陳述清楚違反作者意見時，學生才應選 NO。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct conflict with someone’s viewpoint.","zh":"這個片語描述與某人觀點直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Students write NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"如果無法判斷作者怎樣想，學生寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide confidently.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資訊作出有信心的判斷。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions a patient’s age, it is impossible to say whether the patient was young or old.","zh":"如果文章從未提及病人年齡，就無法判斷病人是年輕還是年老。"},{"en":"In reading tests, impossible to say does not mean unlikely; it means unsupported by the text.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，無法判斷不是指不可能，而是指文本沒有支持。"},{"en":"The phrase warns students not to guess beyond the evidence.","zh":"這個片語提醒學生不要超出證據猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"highly reputable writer","meaning":"聲譽很高的作家","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to Sacks as a highly reputable writer.","zh":"該陳述把 Sacks 稱為聲譽很高的作家。"},{"en":"A highly reputable writer is a writer widely respected for quality, reliability, or influence.","zh":"highly reputable writer 指因質素、可靠性或影響力而廣受尊重的作家。"},{"en":"A highly reputable writer may be trusted because they have produced careful work for many years.","zh":"聲譽很高的作家可能因多年來創作細心作品而受到信任。"},{"en":"If a reviewer criticises a highly reputable writer, they may feel the need to explain their judgement carefully.","zh":"如果評論者批評聲譽很高的作家，可能需要仔細解釋其判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong professional or public respect.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈的專業或公眾尊重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"less than favourable review","meaning":"不太正面的評論","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer gives a less than favourable review of some parts of the book.","zh":"評論者對書中某些部分作出不太正面的評論。"},{"en":"A less than favourable review is a review that is partly negative or not very approving.","zh":"less than favourable review 指部分負面或不太認可的評論。"},{"en":"A restaurant may receive a less than favourable review if the food is good but the service is slow.","zh":"如果餐廳食物不錯但服務很慢，可能收到不太正面的評論。"},{"en":"If a review is less than favourable, it may still contain some praise.","zh":"如果評論不太正面，它仍可能包含一些讚賞。"},{"en":"The phrase is a polite way to say the review is not very positive.","zh":"這個片語是較禮貌地表示評論不太正面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be a good treatment for","meaning":"是……的良好治療方法","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Beethoven’s sonata is a good treatment for musical disorders.","zh":"該陳述問貝多芬奏鳴曲是否是音樂障礙的良好治療方法。"},{"en":"Be a good treatment for means be an effective way to improve or manage a condition.","zh":"be a good treatment for 指是改善或處理某病症的有效方法。"},{"en":"Gentle exercise may be a good treatment for some back pain, but not for every injury.","zh":"溫和運動可能是某些背痛的良好治療方法，但不適合每種傷患。"},{"en":"If a treatment helps one patient, it is not automatically a good treatment for all similar conditions.","zh":"如果一種治療幫到一名病人，不代表它自動是所有相似病症的良好療法。"},{"en":"The phrase asks whether something has real therapeutic value.","zh":"這個片語詢問某事是否有真正治療價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"technological methods","meaning":"科技方法","examples":[{"en":"The question compares technological methods with observation.","zh":"題目把科技方法與觀察作比較。"},{"en":"Technological methods are ways of studying or solving problems using machines, tools, or advanced systems.","zh":"technological methods 指使用機器、工具或先進系統研究或解決問題的方法。"},{"en":"Hospitals use technological methods such as scans and digital monitors to collect medical information.","zh":"醫院使用掃描和數碼監察器等科技方法收集醫療資料。"},{"en":"If technological methods replace observation completely, human context may be lost.","zh":"如果科技方法完全取代觀察，人文背景可能會消失。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts tool-based methods with direct human noticing.","zh":"這個片語把工具式方法與直接人類觀察作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"studying his patients","meaning":"研究他的病人","examples":[{"en":"Sacks uses observation when studying his patients.","zh":"Sacks 在研究他的病人時使用觀察。"},{"en":"Studying his patients means carefully observing, describing, and trying to understand the people he treats.","zh":"studying his patients 指仔細觀察、描述並嘗試理解他所治療的人。"},{"en":"A doctor studying a patient may listen to symptoms, watch movement, and ask about daily life.","zh":"醫生研究病人時，可能聆聽症狀、觀察動作並詢問日常生活。"},{"en":"If Sacks studies patients closely, his case descriptions can become rich and humane.","zh":"如果 Sacks 仔細研究病人，他的個案描述可以變得豐富而有人性。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to clinical investigation, not treating people as objects.","zh":"這個片語指臨床調查，而不是把人當成物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"music therapy is undervalued","meaning":"音樂治療被低估","examples":[{"en":"The passage suggests that music therapy is undervalued.","zh":"文章暗示音樂治療被低估。"},{"en":"Music therapy is undervalued means people do not give it enough respect, attention, or support.","zh":"music therapy is undervalued 指人們沒有給予音樂治療足夠尊重、關注或支持。"},{"en":"School counselling may be undervalued if people notice exam results more than emotional recovery.","zh":"如果人們比情緒復原更注意考試成績，學校輔導可能被低估。"},{"en":"If music therapy is undervalued, useful treatments may receive too little funding or research.","zh":"如果音樂治療被低估，有用療法可能得到太少資金或研究。"},{"en":"The phrase means the field deserves more appreciation than it gets.","zh":"這個片語意思是該領域值得比目前更多欣賞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have more scepticism about","meaning":"對……有更多懷疑精神","examples":[{"en":"The writer thinks Sacks should have more scepticism about theories and findings.","zh":"作者認為 Sacks 應對理論和發現有更多懷疑精神。"},{"en":"Have more scepticism about means question something more carefully instead of accepting it too easily.","zh":"have more scepticism about 指更仔細質疑某事，而不是太容易接受。"},{"en":"Students should have more scepticism about online answers that give no evidence.","zh":"學生應對沒有證據的網上答案有更多懷疑精神。"},{"en":"If a writer has more scepticism about scientific claims, the discussion may become more balanced.","zh":"如果作者對科學主張有更多懷疑精神，討論可能變得更平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase praises careful doubt rather than blind rejection.","zh":"這個片語讚賞細心懷疑，而不是盲目否定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"testing methods","meaning":"測試方法","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to Sacks’s attitude toward new testing methods.","zh":"該陳述提到 Sacks 對新測試方法的態度。"},{"en":"Testing methods are procedures or tools used to measure, check, or investigate something.","zh":"testing methods 指用來量度、檢查或研究某事的程序或工具。"},{"en":"Schools use testing methods such as quizzes, essays, and oral exams to assess learning.","zh":"學校使用小測、文章和口試等測試方法來評估學習。"},{"en":"If old testing methods miss subtle problems, newer methods may be needed.","zh":"如果舊測試方法錯過細微問題，就可能需要較新方法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to ways of gathering evidence through tests.","zh":"這個片語指透過測試收集證據的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dissociations between harmony and melody","meaning":"和聲與旋律之間的功能分離","examples":[{"en":"Dissociations between harmony and melody reveal how music is processed.","zh":"和聲與旋律之間的功能分離揭示音樂如何被處理。"},{"en":"Dissociations between harmony and melody are separations showing that a person may lose one ability while keeping the other.","zh":"dissociations between harmony and melody 指顯示一個人可能失去其中一種能力但保留另一種能力的分離現象。"},{"en":"A patient may understand melody but fail to hear harmony, showing that these abilities can separate.","zh":"病人可能理解旋律卻無法聽出和聲，顯示這些能力可以分離。"},{"en":"If harmony and melody can dissociate, the brain probably does not process music as one simple unit.","zh":"如果和聲和旋律可以功能分離，大腦大概不是把音樂當成一個簡單整體處理。"},{"en":"The phrase helps explain separate components of music comprehension.","zh":"這個片語有助解釋音樂理解能力中的分開組成部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the study of treatments","meaning":"對療法的研究","examples":[{"en":"The study of treatments shows that medication can have varied results.","zh":"對療法的研究顯示藥物可以有不同結果。"},{"en":"The study of treatments means research into how different therapies or medicines work.","zh":"study of treatments 指研究不同治療或藥物如何發揮作用。"},{"en":"The study of treatments for anxiety may compare counselling, exercise, and medication.","zh":"對焦慮療法的研究可能比較輔導、運動和藥物。"},{"en":"If treatment studies show varied results, doctors must avoid assuming one method works for everyone.","zh":"如果療法研究顯示結果各異，醫生必須避免假設一種方法適合所有人。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to systematic investigation of medical or therapeutic help.","zh":"這個片語指對醫學或治療幫助的系統性研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"EEG scans","meaning":"腦電圖掃描","examples":[{"en":"EEG scans of Sacks’s patients often appeared normal.","zh":"Sacks 病人的腦電圖掃描常看起來正常。"},{"en":"EEG scans are recordings or tests of the brain’s electrical activity.","zh":"EEG scans 指對大腦電活動的記錄或測試。"},{"en":"A doctor may order EEG scans when a patient reports seizures or unusual sensory experiences.","zh":"當病人報告癲癇或不尋常感覺經驗，醫生可能安排腦電圖掃描。"},{"en":"If EEG scans appear normal but symptoms continue, the problem may be too subtle for standard testing.","zh":"如果腦電圖掃描正常但症狀持續，問題可能太細微，標準測試無法發現。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to brain-wave examinations.","zh":"這個片語指腦電波檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"testing based on new technologies","meaning":"基於新科技的測試","examples":[{"en":"Testing based on new technologies should not be used in isolation.","zh":"基於新科技的測試不應被單獨使用。"},{"en":"Testing based on new technologies means using modern tools or machines to examine a problem.","zh":"testing based on new technologies 指使用現代工具或機器來檢查問題。"},{"en":"A hospital may use testing based on new technologies to find details that older methods miss.","zh":"醫院可能使用基於新科技的測試，找出舊方法錯過的細節。"},{"en":"If new testing is used without observation, doctors may get data but miss the patient’s lived experience.","zh":"如果新測試沒有配合觀察，醫生可能得到數據，卻錯過病人的親身經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights technology-based assessment.","zh":"這個片語突出以科技為基礎的評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be used in isolation","meaning":"被單獨使用","examples":[{"en":"New technologies should not be used in isolation.","zh":"新科技不應被單獨使用。"},{"en":"Be used in isolation means be used alone, without support from other methods or context.","zh":"be used in isolation 指單獨使用，而沒有其他方法或語境支援。"},{"en":"A grammar rule should not be taught in isolation if students never see it in real sentences.","zh":"如果學生從未在真實句子中看到文法規則，該規則就不應被孤立教授。"},{"en":"If brain scans are used in isolation, the patient’s story may be ignored.","zh":"如果腦掃描被單獨使用，病人的故事可能被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that one method alone may be incomplete.","zh":"這個片語提醒單一方法可能不完整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"medication can have varied results","meaning":"藥物可產生不同效果","examples":[{"en":"The passage indicates that medication can have varied results.","zh":"文章顯示藥物可產生不同效果。"},{"en":"Medication can have varied results means the same medicine may affect different people in different ways.","zh":"medication can have varied results 指同一藥物可能對不同人產生不同影響。"},{"en":"One student may feel sleepy after a medicine, while another feels no side effect at all.","zh":"一名學生服藥後可能感到困倦，另一名學生則完全沒有副作用。"},{"en":"If medication has varied results, treatment should be monitored carefully.","zh":"如果藥物效果不同，治療就應被仔細監察。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that medical response is not always predictable.","zh":"這個片語強調醫療反應不一定可預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"unravel the mysteries","meaning":"解開謎團","examples":[{"en":"New research may help the neurological community unravel the mysteries.","zh":"新研究可能幫助神經學界解開謎團。"},{"en":"Unravel the mysteries means gradually solve or explain things that are confusing or unknown.","zh":"unravel the mysteries 指逐步解決或解釋令人困惑或未知的事情。"},{"en":"A detective tries to unravel the mysteries behind a strange disappearance.","zh":"偵探嘗試解開一宗奇怪失蹤案背後的謎團。"},{"en":"If scientists gather better evidence, they may unravel mysteries that once seemed impossible to explain.","zh":"如果科學家收集更好證據，就可能解開曾經看似無法解釋的謎團。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests patient investigation leading to understanding.","zh":"這個片語暗示耐心調查帶來理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be localised in the brain","meaning":"定位於大腦某一區域","examples":[{"en":"The passage questions whether music is localised in one area of the brain.","zh":"文章質疑音樂是否定位於大腦某一區域。"},{"en":"Be localised in the brain means be located or mainly controlled in a particular brain area.","zh":"be localised in the brain 指位於或主要受控於某個特定大腦區域。"},{"en":"Some language functions are partly localised in the brain, but real communication uses many systems together.","zh":"有些語言功能部分定位於大腦中，但真正溝通會同時使用許多系統。"},{"en":"If music is not localised in one area, damage to different regions may affect different musical abilities.","zh":"如果音樂不是定位於單一區域，不同區域受損可能影響不同音樂能力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the idea that a mental function has a specific brain location.","zh":"這個片語指某種心智能力有特定大腦位置的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 39 - Musical Maladies.pdf","sourcePage":7}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 40":[{"front":"high-speed photography","meaning":"高速攝影","examples":[{"en":"High-speed photography can capture events that are too fast for the human eye.","zh":"高速攝影可以捕捉快得肉眼看不清的事件。"},{"en":"High-speed photography is a technique that records very fast movement so people can study it slowly.","zh":"高速攝影是一種記錄極快動作的技術，讓人可以慢慢研究它。"},{"en":"A science teacher may use high-speed photography to show how a balloon bursts.","zh":"科學老師可能使用高速攝影展示氣球如何爆破。"},{"en":"Because it freezes or slows rapid action, high-speed photography helps scientists see details they would normally miss.","zh":"由於高速攝影能定格或放慢快速動作，它幫助科學家看見平時會錯過的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to photography that reveals extremely quick events.","zh":"這個短語指能揭示極快速事件的攝影技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"attract the interest of","meaning":"引起……的興趣","examples":[{"en":"Photography attracted the interest of many scientists and artists from its inception.","zh":"攝影自創立以來就引起許多科學家和藝術家的興趣。"},{"en":"To attract the interest of someone means to make that person curious or keen to learn more.","zh":"引起某人的興趣，是指令那人感到好奇或想了解更多。"},{"en":"A new school robot may attract the interest of students who enjoy technology.","zh":"新的學校機械人可能引起喜歡科技的學生的興趣。"},{"en":"If a topic attracts the interest of both scientists and artists, it probably has both practical and creative value.","zh":"如果一個主題同時引起科學家和藝術家的興趣，它很可能同時有實用和創意價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something drawing attention from a person or group.","zh":"這個短語描述某事吸引某人或某群體注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"from its inception","meaning":"從一開始；自創立以來","examples":[{"en":"Photography attracted scientific and artistic interest from its inception.","zh":"攝影自創立以來就引起科學和藝術方面的興趣。"},{"en":"From its inception means from the very beginning of something’s existence.","zh":"從一開始，是指從某事存在的最初階段起。"},{"en":"The school debate club welcomed younger students from its inception.","zh":"學校辯論學會自創立以來就歡迎低年級學生。"},{"en":"If an idea has been popular from its inception, people supported it right from the start.","zh":"如果一個想法從一開始就受歡迎，表示人們由最初已支持它。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights what was true at the beginning.","zh":"這個短語強調某事在開端時已經如此。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"record and study movements","meaning":"記錄和研究動作","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have used photography to record and study movements.","zh":"科學家一直使用攝影來記錄和研究動作。"},{"en":"To record and study movements means to capture actions so they can be examined carefully later.","zh":"記錄和研究動作，是指捕捉行動，以便之後仔細分析。"},{"en":"A sports coach may record and study a runner’s movements to improve technique.","zh":"運動教練可能記錄和研究跑手的動作，以改善技巧。"},{"en":"When movements are recorded, people can slow them down and notice mistakes or hidden patterns.","zh":"當動作被記錄下來，人們就可以放慢觀看，注意錯誤或隱藏模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using evidence to analyse how something moves.","zh":"這個短語描述使用證據分析某物如何移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"human and animal locomotion","meaning":"人類和動物的移動方式","examples":[{"en":"Eadweard Muybridge studied human and animal locomotion in 1887.","zh":"Eadweard Muybridge 在 1887 年研究人類和動物的移動方式。"},{"en":"Human and animal locomotion means the way people and animals move from one place to another.","zh":"人類和動物的移動方式，是指人和動物如何從一處移到另一處。"},{"en":"A biology lesson may compare human and animal locomotion by looking at walking, running and jumping.","zh":"生物課可能透過觀察步行、奔跑和跳躍，比較人類和動物的移動方式。"},{"en":"Studying locomotion helps scientists understand muscles, balance and movement patterns.","zh":"研究移動方式有助科學家理解肌肉、平衡和動作模式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to movement such as walking, running, flying or crawling.","zh":"這個短語指步行、奔跑、飛行或爬行等移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be equally interested in","meaning":"對……同樣感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Artists are equally interested in the movement-related aspects of photography.","zh":"藝術家對攝影中與動作相關的方面同樣感興趣。"},{"en":"To be equally interested in something means to have the same level of interest as another person or group.","zh":"對某事同樣感興趣，是指與另一人或另一群體有相同程度的興趣。"},{"en":"Teachers and parents may be equally interested in a child’s progress.","zh":"老師和父母可能對孩子的進步同樣感興趣。"},{"en":"If artists are equally interested in movement, photography is not only scientific but also creative.","zh":"如果藝術家也同樣關注動作，攝影就不只是科學，也具有創意。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two sides care about the same thing.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩方都關心同一件事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"these aspects","meaning":"這些方面","examples":[{"en":"Artists are interested in these aspects of photography as well.","zh":"藝術家也對攝影的這些方面感興趣。"},{"en":"These aspects means the particular parts or features already mentioned.","zh":"這些方面，是指前面已提到的特定部分或特徵。"},{"en":"A school may improve lighting, seating and sound; students may notice these aspects immediately.","zh":"學校可能改善燈光、座位和音響；學生可能立即注意到這些方面。"},{"en":"When these aspects are important, people should not look only at the whole topic.","zh":"當這些方面很重要，人們不應只看整個主題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to specific features under discussion.","zh":"這個短語回指正在討論的具體特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"explore avenues other than","meaning":"探索……以外的途徑","examples":[{"en":"Artists try to explore avenues other than the mechanical recording of reality.","zh":"藝術家嘗試探索機械式記錄現實以外的途徑。"},{"en":"To explore avenues other than something means to look for different methods or possibilities beyond it.","zh":"探索某事以外的途徑，是指尋找超越它的不同方法或可能性。"},{"en":"A student may explore avenues other than memorising by using diagrams and practice questions.","zh":"學生可能探索死記硬背以外的途徑，例如使用圖表和練習題。"},{"en":"Exploring other avenues can lead to more creative or effective solutions.","zh":"探索其他途徑可以帶來更有創意或更有效的解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes looking beyond the usual or obvious path.","zh":"這個短語描述超越慣常或明顯道路去尋找方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"photo-mechanical representation of reality","meaning":"對現實的攝影機械式再現","examples":[{"en":"Some artists moved beyond the photo-mechanical representation of reality.","zh":"有些藝術家超越了對現實的攝影機械式再現。"},{"en":"Photo-mechanical representation of reality means using photography mainly to reproduce what the camera sees.","zh":"對現實的攝影機械式再現，是指主要使用攝影重現相機所看見的東西。"},{"en":"A passport photo is a simple example of photo-mechanical representation because it records appearance directly.","zh":"證件相是攝影機械式再現的簡單例子，因為它直接記錄外貌。"},{"en":"Artists may reject pure mechanical realism when they want photography to express mood or imagination.","zh":"當藝術家想用攝影表達氣氛或想像時，可能會拒絕純粹機械式寫實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes photography as a machine-like copy of the real world.","zh":"這個短語描述攝影像機器般複製真實世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pictorialist movement","meaning":"畫意攝影運動","examples":[{"en":"The pictorialist movement explored photography as an artistic form.","zh":"畫意攝影運動探索攝影作為藝術形式。"},{"en":"The pictorialist movement was an approach that treated photography as art rather than only mechanical recording.","zh":"畫意攝影運動是一種把攝影視為藝術，而不只是機械記錄的方法。"},{"en":"A pictorialist photographer might soften focus to make a photo look more like a painting.","zh":"畫意攝影師可能柔化焦點，令相片看起來更像繪畫。"},{"en":"This movement mattered because it helped people see photography as creative expression.","zh":"這個運動重要，因為它幫助人們把攝影視為創意表達。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an artistic movement in photography.","zh":"這個短語指攝影中的一場藝術運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"military, police, and security forces","meaning":"軍隊、警方和保安部隊","examples":[{"en":"Military, police, and security forces use photography for practical purposes.","zh":"軍隊、警方和保安部隊把攝影用於實際目的。"},{"en":"Military, police, and security forces are organisations that protect order, safety and national defence.","zh":"軍隊、警方和保安部隊是保護秩序、安全和國防的組織。"},{"en":"Police may use photographs to identify suspects or record evidence.","zh":"警方可能使用相片識別疑犯或記錄證據。"},{"en":"These forces use photography because visual records can support investigation and protection.","zh":"這些部隊使用攝影，因為視覺記錄可以支援調查和保護工作。"},{"en":"This phrase groups together organisations concerned with security and public safety.","zh":"這個短語把與安全和公共保護有關的組織集合起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"surveillance, recognition and data storage","meaning":"監察、識別和資料儲存","examples":[{"en":"Photography is used for surveillance, recognition and data storage.","zh":"攝影被用於監察、識別和資料儲存。"},{"en":"Surveillance, recognition and data storage mean watching, identifying and keeping information for later use.","zh":"監察、識別和資料儲存，是指觀看、辨認和保存資訊以供日後使用。"},{"en":"A building camera may provide surveillance, face recognition and stored video records.","zh":"大廈攝影機可能提供監察、人臉識別和儲存影片記錄。"},{"en":"These uses are practical because photos can preserve information more accurately than memory.","zh":"這些用途很實際，因為相片可以比記憶更準確保存資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes security and information-related uses of photography.","zh":"這個短語描述攝影在安全和資訊方面的用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"preserve memories","meaning":"保存回憶","examples":[{"en":"Amateurs use photography to preserve memories.","zh":"業餘愛好者使用攝影保存回憶。"},{"en":"To preserve memories means to keep reminders of past events, people or places.","zh":"保存回憶，是指保留過去事件、人物或地方的紀念。"},{"en":"A family may take photos at a birthday party to preserve memories of the day.","zh":"家人可能在生日派對拍照，以保存當天的回憶。"},{"en":"Photos help preserve memories because people can look back at moments long after they have passed.","zh":"相片有助保存回憶，因為人們可在時刻過去很久後回看。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping personal history alive.","zh":"這個短語描述保存個人歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"capture special moments","meaning":"捕捉特別時刻","examples":[{"en":"People use cameras to capture special moments.","zh":"人們使用相機捕捉特別時刻。"},{"en":"To capture special moments means to record important or memorable events in photos or video.","zh":"捕捉特別時刻，是指用相片或影片記錄重要或值得記住的事件。"},{"en":"Parents may capture special moments when their child performs on stage for the first time.","zh":"孩子第一次上台表演時，父母可能捕捉這個特別時刻。"},{"en":"Capturing moments matters because the event itself may last only a few seconds.","zh":"捕捉時刻很重要，因為事件本身可能只持續幾秒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recording meaningful experiences before they pass.","zh":"這個短語描述在有意義經歷流逝前把它記錄下來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tell stories","meaning":"講述故事","examples":[{"en":"Photography can be used to tell stories.","zh":"攝影可以用來講述故事。"},{"en":"To tell stories means to communicate events, feelings or ideas in a narrative form.","zh":"講述故事，是指以敘事形式傳達事件、感受或想法。"},{"en":"A photo essay about a village can tell stories of daily work, family life and change.","zh":"關於村莊的相片文章可以講述日常工作、家庭生活和變化的故事。"},{"en":"Photographs tell stories when they show people, actions and details that suggest what happened.","zh":"當相片展示人物、行動和暗示事件的細節，它們就在講述故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using images to communicate a narrative.","zh":"這個短語描述使用影像傳達敘事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"send messages","meaning":"傳遞訊息","examples":[{"en":"Photographs can send messages without words.","zh":"相片可以不用文字傳遞訊息。"},{"en":"To send messages means to communicate ideas, feelings or warnings to others.","zh":"傳遞訊息，是指向他人傳達想法、感受或警告。"},{"en":"A poster showing polluted water can send a message about environmental protection.","zh":"展示受污染水源的海報可以傳遞環保訊息。"},{"en":"Images can send messages quickly because viewers understand visual signs almost immediately.","zh":"影像可以快速傳遞訊息，因為觀眾幾乎即時理解視覺符號。"},{"en":"This phrase describes communication through signs, words or images.","zh":"這個短語描述透過標誌、文字或影像進行溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a source of entertainment","meaning":"娛樂來源","examples":[{"en":"Photography is also used as a source of entertainment.","zh":"攝影也被用作娛樂來源。"},{"en":"A source of entertainment is something that gives people enjoyment or amusement.","zh":"娛樂來源是給人享受或消遣的東西。"},{"en":"Funny family photos can be a source of entertainment at a reunion dinner.","zh":"有趣的家庭相片可以成為團年飯上的娛樂來源。"},{"en":"Photography entertains people when images are beautiful, surprising or emotionally engaging.","zh":"當影像美麗、令人驚訝或牽動情感，攝影就能娛樂人們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that provides enjoyment.","zh":"這個短語描述提供樂趣的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"technological improvements","meaning":"技術改良","examples":[{"en":"Technological improvements have changed what cameras can show.","zh":"技術改良改變了相機能展示的東西。"},{"en":"Technological improvements are advances that make tools or systems work better.","zh":"技術改良是令工具或系統運作得更好的進步。"},{"en":"Better phone cameras are technological improvements that help people take clearer photos.","zh":"更好的手機相機是技術改良，幫助人拍攝更清晰相片。"},{"en":"As technology improves, cameras can capture faster, smaller or darker events.","zh":"隨着科技改善，相機可以捕捉更快、更小或更暗的事件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes progress in technology.","zh":"這個短語描述科技上的進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"make it possible to","meaning":"令……成為可能","examples":[{"en":"New techniques have made it possible to visualise hidden events.","zh":"新技術令將隱藏事件視覺化成為可能。"},{"en":"To make it possible to do something means to create the conditions that allow it to happen.","zh":"令做某事成為可能，是指創造容許它發生的條件。"},{"en":"Online platforms make it possible to attend lessons from home.","zh":"網上平台令在家上課成為可能。"},{"en":"New tools can make impossible tasks possible by removing earlier limitations.","zh":"新工具可以透過移除早期限制，令不可能的任務成為可能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes enabling an action.","zh":"這個短語描述使某行動得以實現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"visualise events","meaning":"將事件視覺化","examples":[{"en":"Photography can visualise events that the human eye cannot follow.","zh":"攝影可以將肉眼無法追蹤的事件視覺化。"},{"en":"To visualise events means to make events visible or easier to see and understand.","zh":"將事件視覺化，是指令事件可見或更容易觀看和理解。"},{"en":"A chart can visualise a student’s progress over the school year.","zh":"圖表可以將學生一整年的進步視覺化。"},{"en":"When cameras visualise hidden events, people can study processes they normally cannot observe.","zh":"當相機把隱藏事件視覺化，人們就能研究平常無法觀察的過程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes turning something difficult to see into a visual form.","zh":"這個短語描述把難以看見的東西轉化成視覺形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"too fast or too slow for","meaning":"對……來說太快或太慢","examples":[{"en":"Some events are too fast or too slow for the human eye.","zh":"有些事件對肉眼來說太快或太慢。"},{"en":"Too fast or too slow for someone means outside that person’s ability to notice clearly.","zh":"對某人來說太快或太慢，是指超出那人清楚察覺的能力。"},{"en":"A spinning fan may be too fast for a child to see each blade clearly.","zh":"旋轉風扇可能對孩子來說太快，無法清楚看見每片扇葉。"},{"en":"A plant growing may be too slow for people to notice from moment to moment.","zh":"植物生長可能對人們來說太慢，無法逐刻察覺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement beyond normal perception.","zh":"這個短語描述超越正常感知的動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the human eye","meaning":"肉眼","examples":[{"en":"Some movements are invisible to the human eye.","zh":"有些動作對肉眼來說不可見。"},{"en":"The human eye means ordinary human sight without special instruments.","zh":"肉眼是指沒有特殊儀器輔助的普通人類視力。"},{"en":"Dust in the air may be too small for the human eye to see clearly.","zh":"空氣中的灰塵可能太細小，肉眼無法清楚看見。"},{"en":"Cameras can reveal details that the human eye misses.","zh":"相機可以揭示肉眼錯過的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to natural eyesight.","zh":"這個短語指自然視力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"one such technique","meaning":"其中一種這樣的技巧","examples":[{"en":"One such technique is called fast motion.","zh":"其中一種這樣的技巧稱為快動作。"},{"en":"One such technique means one example of the kind of technique just mentioned.","zh":"其中一種這樣的技巧，是指剛提到那類技巧中的一個例子。"},{"en":"Schools use many ways to support reading; one such technique is guided reading.","zh":"學校使用許多方法支援閱讀；其中一種技巧是導讀。"},{"en":"This phrase helps move from a general category to a specific example.","zh":"這個短語幫助由一般類別轉到具體例子。"},{"en":"It refers back to a type already discussed.","zh":"它回指已討論的某一類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fast motion","meaning":"快動作；縮時效果","examples":[{"en":"Fast motion is professionally known as time-lapse photography.","zh":"快動作在專業上稱為縮時攝影。"},{"en":"Fast motion is a visual effect in which a slow process appears to happen quickly.","zh":"快動作是一種視覺效果，令緩慢過程看起來快速發生。"},{"en":"A video of clouds moving across the sky may use fast motion to show several hours in seconds.","zh":"雲朵移過天空的影片可能使用快動作，在數秒內展示數小時。"},{"en":"Fast motion helps viewers notice slow changes that would otherwise be boring or invisible.","zh":"快動作幫助觀眾注意到否則會沉悶或看不見的緩慢變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes time being compressed on screen.","zh":"這個短語描述螢幕上的時間被壓縮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"professionally known as","meaning":"專業上稱為","examples":[{"en":"Fast motion is professionally known as time-lapse photography.","zh":"快動作在專業上稱為縮時攝影。"},{"en":"Professionally known as means called by that formal or technical name in a profession.","zh":"專業上稱為，是指在某專業中以該正式或技術名稱稱呼。"},{"en":"A heart attack is professionally known as a myocardial infarction in medicine.","zh":"心臟病發在醫學上專業稱為 myocardial infarction。"},{"en":"A professional term may be more precise than an everyday name.","zh":"專業術語可能比日常名稱更精確。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the technical name for something.","zh":"這個短語引入某事物的技術名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"time-lapse photography","meaning":"縮時攝影","examples":[{"en":"Time-lapse photography shows slow processes at a faster speed.","zh":"縮時攝影以較快速度展示緩慢過程。"},{"en":"Time-lapse photography is a method of taking photos at intervals and playing them back quickly.","zh":"縮時攝影是一種每隔一段時間拍照，然後快速播放的方法。"},{"en":"A gardener may use time-lapse photography to show a flower opening over several hours.","zh":"園丁可能使用縮時攝影展示花朵在數小時內盛開。"},{"en":"Because the images are played quickly, slow changes appear much faster.","zh":"因為影像被快速播放，緩慢變化看起來快得多。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to photography that compresses long periods of time.","zh":"這個短語指壓縮長時間過程的攝影。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the perfect technique for","meaning":"用於……的理想技巧","examples":[{"en":"Time-lapse photography is the perfect technique for capturing slow natural events.","zh":"縮時攝影是捕捉緩慢自然事件的理想技巧。"},{"en":"The perfect technique for something is the most suitable method for doing it.","zh":"用於某事的理想技巧，是做該事最合適的方法。"},{"en":"Flashcards may be the perfect technique for memorising short vocabulary lists.","zh":"抽認卡可能是記短詞彙表的理想技巧。"},{"en":"A technique is perfect for a task when it solves the main difficulty of that task.","zh":"當一種技巧解決任務的主要困難，它就很適合該任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a method that fits a purpose extremely well.","zh":"這個短語描述非常符合目的的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"capture events and movements","meaning":"捕捉事件和動作","examples":[{"en":"The technique captures events and movements in the natural world.","zh":"這項技巧捕捉自然界中的事件和動作。"},{"en":"To capture events and movements means to record actions or changes in photos or video.","zh":"捕捉事件和動作，是指用相片或影片記錄行動或變化。"},{"en":"A wildlife camera can capture events and movements around a pond at night.","zh":"野外相機可以捕捉夜間池塘附近的事件和動作。"},{"en":"Capturing movement allows people to study what happened after the moment has passed.","zh":"捕捉動作讓人在時刻過去後仍能研究發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recording visible change or action.","zh":"這個短語描述記錄可見變化或行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the natural world","meaning":"自然界","examples":[{"en":"Many slow processes in the natural world can be filmed with time-lapse photography.","zh":"自然界中許多緩慢過程可以用縮時攝影拍攝。"},{"en":"The natural world means plants, animals, weather, landscapes and other parts of nature.","zh":"自然界是指植物、動物、天氣、景觀和其他自然部分。"},{"en":"Students may study the natural world by observing insects in a school garden.","zh":"學生可能透過觀察校園花園中的昆蟲來研究自然界。"},{"en":"Photography helps people see changes in nature that are normally too slow or hidden.","zh":"攝影幫助人們看見自然中通常太慢或隱藏的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes nature rather than human-made environments.","zh":"這個短語描述自然，而不是人造環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"occur over a timescale","meaning":"在某個時間尺度上發生","examples":[{"en":"Some natural changes occur over a timescale too slow for us to notice.","zh":"有些自然變化在慢得我們難以察覺的時間尺度上發生。"},{"en":"To occur over a timescale means to happen across a particular length of time.","zh":"在某個時間尺度上發生，是指在某段特定時間長度中發生。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement in writing may occur over a timescale of several months.","zh":"學生寫作能力的進步可能在數月的時間尺度上發生。"},{"en":"If a process occurs over a long timescale, people may need recordings to see the change.","zh":"如果一個過程在很長時間尺度上發生，人們可能需要錄影才能看見變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the period over which something happens.","zh":"這個短語描述某事發生所跨越的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"human perception","meaning":"人類感知","examples":[{"en":"The process is too slow for human perception to follow.","zh":"這個過程太慢，人類感知難以追蹤。"},{"en":"Human perception is the ability of people to notice and understand things through the senses.","zh":"人類感知是人透過感官注意和理解事物的能力。"},{"en":"A very quiet sound may be below the level of human perception.","zh":"非常微弱的聲音可能低於人類感知水平。"},{"en":"Cameras can extend human perception by showing things we cannot normally see.","zh":"相機可以透過展示我們通常看不到的東西來延伸人類感知。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what people can sense and notice.","zh":"這個短語描述人能感覺和察覺的範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"too slow for human perception to follow","meaning":"慢得人類感知難以追蹤","examples":[{"en":"The growth of a mushroom is too slow for human perception to follow.","zh":"蘑菇的生長慢得人類感知難以追蹤。"},{"en":"Too slow for human perception to follow means changing so gradually that people cannot notice the movement directly.","zh":"慢得人類感知難以追蹤，是指變化太逐漸，人們不能直接察覺其動作。"},{"en":"A child’s height increase is too slow for human perception to follow day by day.","zh":"孩子的身高增長每日都慢得人類感知難以追蹤。"},{"en":"Time-lapse photography helps because it compresses slow change into a visible sequence.","zh":"縮時攝影有幫助，因為它把緩慢變化壓縮成可見序列。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement that is real but not easily perceived in real time.","zh":"這個短語描述真實存在但難以即時感知的動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"life cycle","meaning":"生命週期","examples":[{"en":"The life cycle of a mushroom can be shown through time-lapse photography.","zh":"蘑菇的生命週期可以透過縮時攝影展示。"},{"en":"A life cycle is the series of stages a living thing goes through from beginning to end.","zh":"生命週期是生物由開始到結束所經歷的一系列階段。"},{"en":"Students may learn the life cycle of a butterfly from egg to caterpillar to adult.","zh":"學生可能學習蝴蝶由卵到毛蟲再到成蟲的生命週期。"},{"en":"Time-lapse photography can show a life cycle clearly because it speeds up slow growth.","zh":"縮時攝影可以清楚展示生命週期，因為它加速緩慢生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the full development process of a living thing.","zh":"這個短語描述生物的完整發展過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"too gradual for the human eye to follow","meaning":"逐漸得肉眼難以察覺","examples":[{"en":"The life cycle of a mushroom is too gradual for the human eye to follow.","zh":"蘑菇的生命週期逐漸得肉眼難以察覺。"},{"en":"Too gradual for the human eye to follow means changing too slowly for people to see directly.","zh":"逐漸得肉眼難以察覺，是指變化太慢，人們無法直接看見。"},{"en":"The opening of a flower may be too gradual for the human eye to follow in real time.","zh":"花朵盛開在實時中可能逐漸得肉眼難以察覺。"},{"en":"Slow change becomes visible when photography compresses many hours into seconds.","zh":"當攝影把數小時壓縮成數秒，緩慢變化就變得可見。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why time-lapse photography is useful.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何縮時攝影有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the principle used to","meaning":"用作……的原理","examples":[{"en":"The principle used to present the mushroom’s growth is simple.","zh":"用作呈現蘑菇生長的原理很簡單。"},{"en":"The principle used to do something is the basic idea or rule behind the method.","zh":"用作做某事的原理，是該方法背後的基本想法或規則。"},{"en":"The principle used to teach spelling may be repeated practice with feedback.","zh":"用作教拼字的原理可能是反覆練習加回饋。"},{"en":"Understanding the principle helps students apply the method to new examples.","zh":"理解原理有助學生把方法應用到新例子。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the basic rule behind an action.","zh":"這個短語指出行動背後的基本規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a series of photographs","meaning":"一系列相片","examples":[{"en":"A series of photographs is taken at regular intervals.","zh":"一系列相片每隔固定時間被拍攝。"},{"en":"A series of photographs is a set of photos taken one after another.","zh":"一系列相片，是一組按先後拍攝的相片。"},{"en":"A parent may take a series of photographs of a child building a sandcastle.","zh":"父母可能拍下一系列相片，記錄孩子堆沙堡。"},{"en":"When photos are taken in order, they can show change over time.","zh":"當相片按順序拍攝，它們可以展示隨時間發生的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes multiple photos forming a sequence.","zh":"這個短語描述多張相片形成序列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at regular intervals","meaning":"每隔固定時間","examples":[{"en":"The photographs are taken at regular intervals.","zh":"這些相片每隔固定時間被拍攝。"},{"en":"At regular intervals means repeatedly after equal or planned periods of time.","zh":"每隔固定時間，是指在相等或預定時間後反覆進行。"},{"en":"A nurse may check a patient’s temperature at regular intervals.","zh":"護士可能每隔固定時間檢查病人體溫。"},{"en":"Regular intervals help create a smooth record of change.","zh":"固定時間間隔有助建立連貫的變化記錄。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated timing pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述重複的時間模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be arranged as","meaning":"被排列成","examples":[{"en":"The photographs are arranged as a moving-image film.","zh":"這些相片被排列成動態影像影片。"},{"en":"To be arranged as something means to be organised into that form.","zh":"被排列成某物，是指被整理成該形式。"},{"en":"A teacher may arrange students’ photos as a class memory book.","zh":"老師可能把學生相片排列成班級紀念冊。"},{"en":"When still photos are arranged as film frames, they can create the effect of movement.","zh":"當靜態相片被排列成影片幀，就可以產生動作效果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organising materials into a new format.","zh":"這個短語描述把材料整理成新格式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a moving-image film","meaning":"動態影像影片","examples":[{"en":"The photographs are arranged as a moving-image film.","zh":"這些相片被排列成動態影像影片。"},{"en":"A moving-image film is a sequence of images played so that they appear to move.","zh":"動態影像影片是一連串影像被播放後看起來像在移動。"},{"en":"A simple animation is a moving-image film made from many drawings.","zh":"簡單動畫是由許多圖畫製成的動態影像影片。"},{"en":"Movement appears when separate images are shown quickly in sequence.","zh":"當分開的影像按順序快速顯示，動作就會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to film or video rather than a single still picture.","zh":"這個短語指影片或錄像，而不是單張靜態圖片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"played back at normal speed","meaning":"以正常速度播放","examples":[{"en":"When played back at normal speed, the sequence appears continuous.","zh":"以正常速度播放時，序列看起來連貫。"},{"en":"Played back at normal speed means shown at the usual speed for film or video.","zh":"以正常速度播放，是指以影片或錄像的一般速度顯示。"},{"en":"A recording of a speech sounds natural when it is played back at normal speed.","zh":"演講錄音以正常速度播放時聽起來自然。"},{"en":"In time-lapse work, normal playback speed can make slow events appear fast.","zh":"在縮時攝影中，正常播放速度可以令緩慢事件看起來很快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how recorded material is shown to viewers.","zh":"這個短語描述錄製材料如何展示給觀眾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the sequence appears continuous","meaning":"序列看起來連貫","examples":[{"en":"The sequence appears continuous when the film is played normally.","zh":"影片正常播放時，序列看起來連貫。"},{"en":"The sequence appears continuous means the separate images look like one smooth movement.","zh":"序列看起來連貫，是指分開影像看起來像一個流暢動作。"},{"en":"A flipbook works because each page changes slightly, so the sequence appears continuous.","zh":"翻頁小書有效，是因為每頁略有變化，所以序列看起來連貫。"},{"en":"When gaps between images are small enough, viewers perceive motion instead of separate pictures.","zh":"當影像之間的間隔足夠小，觀眾感知到的是動作，而不是分開圖片。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the visual effect of smooth flow.","zh":"這個短語描述流暢連續的視覺效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sped up","meaning":"被加速","examples":[{"en":"The sequence appears continuous and sped up.","zh":"這個序列看起來連貫並被加速。"},{"en":"Sped up means made to happen or appear faster.","zh":"被加速，是指被令其發生或看起來更快。"},{"en":"A cooking video may be sped up so viewers do not watch ten minutes of stirring.","zh":"烹飪影片可能被加速，這樣觀眾不用看十分鐘攪拌。"},{"en":"When slow events are sped up, changes become easier and quicker to understand.","zh":"當緩慢事件被加速，變化就更容易、更快速理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increased speed in playback or action.","zh":"這個短語描述播放或行動速度增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"put simply","meaning":"簡單來說","examples":[{"en":"Put simply, time-lapse photography shrinks time.","zh":"簡單來說，縮時攝影縮短時間。"},{"en":"Put simply means explained in a clear and easy way.","zh":"簡單來說，是指用清楚容易的方式解釋。"},{"en":"Put simply, saving money means spending less than you earn.","zh":"簡單來說，儲錢就是花得比賺得少。"},{"en":"This phrase helps introduce a simple version of a more technical idea.","zh":"這個短語幫助引入較技術概念的簡單版本。"},{"en":"It signals that the next explanation will be easy to understand.","zh":"它表示下一個解釋會容易理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"shrink time","meaning":"縮短時間","examples":[{"en":"Time-lapse photography can shrink time.","zh":"縮時攝影可以縮短時間。"},{"en":"To shrink time means to make a long process appear much shorter on screen.","zh":"縮短時間，是指令一個漫長過程在螢幕上看起來短得多。"},{"en":"A video can shrink time by showing a whole school day in thirty seconds.","zh":"影片可以透過在三十秒內展示整個上學日來縮短時間。"},{"en":"When time is shrunk, viewers can see the full process without waiting for hours or months.","zh":"當時間被壓縮，觀眾不用等數小時或數月就能看完整個過程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes compressing time visually.","zh":"這個短語描述以視覺方式壓縮時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"viewed to completion","meaning":"完整觀看至結束","examples":[{"en":"Events that normally take months can be viewed to completion in seconds.","zh":"通常需時數月的事件可以在數秒內完整觀看至結束。"},{"en":"Viewed to completion means watched from beginning to end.","zh":"完整觀看至結束，是指由開始看到完結。"},{"en":"A long art project can be viewed to completion in a short video.","zh":"一個長時間藝術項目可以在短片中完整觀看至結束。"},{"en":"Time-lapse allows viewers to see the whole process rather than only one moment.","zh":"縮時攝影讓觀眾看到整個過程，而不只是某一刻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes watching the full development of something.","zh":"這個短語描述觀看某事的完整發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in seconds","meaning":"在數秒內","examples":[{"en":"Long events can be viewed to completion in seconds.","zh":"漫長事件可以在數秒內完整觀看至結束。"},{"en":"In seconds means within only a few seconds.","zh":"在數秒內，是指只在幾秒鐘之內。"},{"en":"A phone can take and send a photo in seconds.","zh":"手機可以在數秒內拍攝並傳送相片。"},{"en":"Time-lapse photography turns long waiting into a viewing experience that lasts only seconds.","zh":"縮時攝影把漫長等待變成只持續數秒的觀看經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises very short time.","zh":"這個短語強調非常短的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be sped up by factors of","meaning":"以……倍數加速","examples":[{"en":"Slow events can be sped up by factors of tens to millions.","zh":"緩慢事件可以以數十倍至數百萬倍加速。"},{"en":"To be sped up by factors of something means to be made faster by those multiples.","zh":"以某倍數加速，是指速度被提高到那些倍數。"},{"en":"A plant-growth video may be sped up by a factor of hundreds so days appear as seconds.","zh":"植物生長影片可能以數百倍加速，使數天看起來像數秒。"},{"en":"The larger the factor, the more time is compressed.","zh":"倍數越大，時間被壓縮得越多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mathematical levels of speed increase.","zh":"這個短語描述速度增加的數學程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"factors of tens to millions","meaning":"數十倍至數百萬倍","examples":[{"en":"Time-lapse photography can speed up events by factors of tens to millions.","zh":"縮時攝影可以把事件加速數十倍至數百萬倍。"},{"en":"Factors of tens to millions means speed increases ranging from ten times to millions of times.","zh":"數十倍至數百萬倍，是指由十倍到數百萬倍不等的加速。"},{"en":"A cloud video may need only tens of times speed, but a plant life cycle may need thousands.","zh":"雲朵影片可能只需數十倍速度，但植物生命週期可能需要數千倍。"},{"en":"Different events need different speed factors depending on how slowly they naturally happen.","zh":"不同事件需要不同加速倍數，取決於它們自然發生得有多慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very wide range of acceleration.","zh":"這個短語描述非常廣泛的加速範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"commonly used technique","meaning":"常用技巧","examples":[{"en":"High-speed photography is another commonly used technique.","zh":"高速攝影是另一種常用技巧。"},{"en":"A commonly used technique is a method that many people use often.","zh":"常用技巧是許多人經常使用的方法。"},{"en":"Highlighting key words is a commonly used technique in reading exams.","zh":"標示關鍵字是閱讀考試中的常用技巧。"},{"en":"A technique becomes common when it reliably solves a frequent problem.","zh":"當一種技巧能可靠解決常見問題，它就會變得常用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a familiar and widely used method.","zh":"這個短語描述熟悉且廣泛使用的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the science of taking pictures of","meaning":"拍攝……的科學","examples":[{"en":"High-speed photography is the science of taking pictures of very fast phenomena.","zh":"高速攝影是拍攝極快速現象的科學。"},{"en":"The science of taking pictures of something means the systematic study and technical method of photographing it.","zh":"拍攝某物的科學，是指有系統研究並以技術方法拍攝它。"},{"en":"Medical imaging is the science of taking pictures of the inside of the body.","zh":"醫學影像是拍攝身體內部的科學。"},{"en":"Calling it a science suggests that accurate equipment, timing and method are required.","zh":"把它稱為科學，暗示需要準確設備、時間控制和方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes photography as a technical and research-based practice.","zh":"這個短語描述攝影作為技術和研究為本的實踐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"very fast phenomena","meaning":"極快速的現象","examples":[{"en":"High-speed photography records very fast phenomena.","zh":"高速攝影記錄極快速的現象。"},{"en":"Very fast phenomena are events or actions that happen extremely quickly.","zh":"極快速的現象，是發生得非常快的事件或動作。"},{"en":"A bursting bubble and a bird’s wingbeat are very fast phenomena.","zh":"爆破的泡泡和鳥類拍翼都是極快速的現象。"},{"en":"People need special cameras because very fast phenomena happen too quickly for normal sight.","zh":"人們需要特殊相機，因為極快速現象發生得太快，普通視力看不清。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rapid events that require special observation.","zh":"這個短語描述需要特殊觀察的快速事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be considered the opposite of","meaning":"可被視為……的相反","examples":[{"en":"High-speed photography can be considered the opposite of time-lapse photography.","zh":"高速攝影可被視為縮時攝影的相反。"},{"en":"To be considered the opposite of something means to be seen as working in the reverse way.","zh":"可被視為某事的相反，是指被看作以相反方式運作。"},{"en":"Saving money can be considered the opposite of spending freely.","zh":"儲錢可被視為隨意花錢的相反。"},{"en":"High-speed photography slows fast events, while time-lapse photography speeds slow events.","zh":"高速攝影放慢快速事件，而縮時攝影加速緩慢事件。"},{"en":"This phrase explains contrast between two methods.","zh":"這個短語解釋兩種方法之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"one of the many applications","meaning":"眾多應用之一","examples":[{"en":"One of the many applications of high-speed photography is biological research.","zh":"高速攝影的眾多應用之一是生物學研究。"},{"en":"One of the many applications means one use among several possible uses.","zh":"眾多應用之一，是指多種可能用途中的一種。"},{"en":"One of the many applications of smartphones is online learning.","zh":"智能手機的眾多應用之一是網上學習。"},{"en":"A technology is valuable when it has many applications across different fields.","zh":"當一項技術在不同領域有多種應用，它就很有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces one example of how something can be used.","zh":"這個短語引入某事物可如何使用的一個例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"biological research into","meaning":"對……的生物學研究","examples":[{"en":"High-speed photography is used in biological research into birds and bats.","zh":"高速攝影被用於對鳥類和蝙蝠的生物學研究。"},{"en":"Biological research into something means scientific study of living things or life processes.","zh":"對某事的生物學研究，是對生命體或生命過程的科學研究。"},{"en":"Scientists may conduct biological research into how insects move and feed.","zh":"科學家可能對昆蟲如何移動和進食進行生物學研究。"},{"en":"High-speed cameras help biological research because many animal movements are too fast to see.","zh":"高速攝影機有助生物學研究，因為許多動物動作太快，肉眼看不清。"},{"en":"This phrase describes scientific investigation of living organisms.","zh":"這個短語描述對生物的科學調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"spider silk","meaning":"蜘蛛絲","examples":[{"en":"Scientists use high-speed photography to study spider silk.","zh":"科學家使用高速攝影研究蜘蛛絲。"},{"en":"Spider silk is the strong thread produced by spiders.","zh":"蜘蛛絲是蜘蛛產生的強韌絲線。"},{"en":"A biology class may study spider silk to understand how webs catch insects.","zh":"生物課可能研究蜘蛛絲，以了解蜘蛛網如何捕捉昆蟲。"},{"en":"High-speed photography can show how spider silk stretches, snaps or catches prey.","zh":"高速攝影可以展示蜘蛛絲如何拉伸、斷裂或捕捉獵物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the natural fibre made by spiders.","zh":"這個短語指由蜘蛛製造的天然纖維。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a hummingbird hovering","meaning":"一隻蜂鳥懸停","examples":[{"en":"Imagine a hummingbird hovering almost completely still in the air.","zh":"想像一隻蜂鳥在空中幾乎完全靜止地懸停。"},{"en":"A hummingbird hovering is a tiny bird staying in one place in the air by beating its wings quickly.","zh":"一隻蜂鳥懸停，是指細小鳥類透過快速拍動翅膀停留在空中同一位置。"},{"en":"A photographer may try to capture a hummingbird hovering near a flower.","zh":"攝影師可能嘗試捕捉一隻蜂鳥在花朵附近懸停。"},{"en":"Hovering is possible because the bird’s wings move extremely fast and control lift precisely.","zh":"懸停之所以可能，是因為鳥翼移動極快並精確控制升力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a bird remaining in the air without moving forward much.","zh":"這個短語描述鳥停留在空中而幾乎不向前移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"almost completely still","meaning":"幾乎完全靜止","examples":[{"en":"The hummingbird stays almost completely still in the air.","zh":"蜂鳥在空中幾乎完全靜止。"},{"en":"Almost completely still means nearly not moving, though small movements may still happen.","zh":"幾乎完全靜止，是指幾乎不動，雖然仍可能有小動作。"},{"en":"A dancer may stand almost completely still before starting a performance.","zh":"舞者在開始表演前可能幾乎完全靜止地站着。"},{"en":"The hummingbird looks still because its body stays in place while its wings move rapidly.","zh":"蜂鳥看起來靜止，是因為其身體停在原位，而翅膀快速移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes near-total stillness.","zh":"這個短語描述接近完全靜止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"feed on nectar","meaning":"吸食花蜜","examples":[{"en":"The hummingbird hovers while feeding on nectar.","zh":"蜂鳥一邊懸停，一邊吸食花蜜。"},{"en":"To feed on nectar means to eat or drink the sweet liquid produced by flowers.","zh":"吸食花蜜，是指吃或喝花朵產生的甜液。"},{"en":"Bees and butterflies often feed on nectar in a garden.","zh":"蜜蜂和蝴蝶經常在花園中吸食花蜜。"},{"en":"Hummingbirds hover near flowers because nectar is their food source.","zh":"蜂鳥在花朵附近懸停，因為花蜜是牠們的食物來源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how certain animals get food from flowers.","zh":"這個短語描述某些動物如何從花朵獲取食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"with every flap","meaning":"每拍動一次","examples":[{"en":"With every flap, the bird’s wings bend and change shape.","zh":"每拍動一次，鳥翼都會彎曲和變形。"},{"en":"With every flap means each time the wings move up or down.","zh":"每拍動一次，是指翅膀每次上下移動。"},{"en":"With every flap of a paper fan, cool air moves toward the child’s face.","zh":"紙扇每扇動一次，涼風就吹向孩子的臉。"},{"en":"Repeated flaps create continuous movement and control.","zh":"反覆拍動會產生連續動作和控制。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what happens each time wings beat.","zh":"這個短語聚焦翅膀每次拍動時發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bend, flex and change shape","meaning":"彎曲、屈伸和變形","examples":[{"en":"The hummingbird’s wings bend, flex and change shape.","zh":"蜂鳥的翅膀會彎曲、屈伸和變形。"},{"en":"To bend, flex and change shape means to curve, move and alter form during action.","zh":"彎曲、屈伸和變形，是指在動作中彎曲、移動並改變形態。"},{"en":"A gymnast’s body may bend, flex and change shape during a jump.","zh":"體操運動員跳躍時，身體可能彎曲、屈伸和變形。"},{"en":"Flexible movement helps wings control air and generate lift.","zh":"靈活動作幫助翅膀控制空氣並產生升力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complex physical movement, not a fixed shape.","zh":"這個短語描述複雜身體動作，而不是固定形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"subtle movements","meaning":"細微動作","examples":[{"en":"These subtle movements control the lift of the wings.","zh":"這些細微動作控制翅膀的升力。"},{"en":"Subtle movements are small, slight movements that may be difficult to notice.","zh":"細微動作是小而輕微、可能難以察覺的動作。"},{"en":"A musician’s subtle finger movements can change the sound of a note.","zh":"音樂家的細微手指動作可以改變音符聲音。"},{"en":"Small movements can create big effects when they control balance or direction.","zh":"當小動作控制平衡或方向時，它們可以產生巨大效果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fine and delicate movement.","zh":"這個短語描述精細而微妙的動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"precisely control","meaning":"精確控制","examples":[{"en":"The wing movements precisely control the lift they generate.","zh":"翅膀動作精確控制它們產生的升力。"},{"en":"To precisely control something means to manage it very accurately.","zh":"精確控制某物，是指非常準確地掌控它。"},{"en":"A surgeon must precisely control hand movements during an operation.","zh":"外科醫生在手術中必須精確控制手部動作。"},{"en":"Precise control allows small changes to produce the desired result.","zh":"精確控制使小變化能產生想要的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accurate and careful control.","zh":"這個短語描述準確而仔細的控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"generate lift","meaning":"產生升力","examples":[{"en":"The hummingbird’s wings generate lift as they move.","zh":"蜂鳥的翅膀在移動時產生升力。"},{"en":"To generate lift means to create upward force that helps something stay in the air.","zh":"產生升力，是指創造幫助某物留在空中的向上力量。"},{"en":"An aeroplane’s wings generate lift when air flows over them.","zh":"飛機機翼在氣流流過時產生升力。"},{"en":"Without enough lift, a flying animal or aircraft cannot remain airborne.","zh":"沒有足夠升力，飛行動物或飛機就不能留在空中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes producing the upward force needed for flight.","zh":"這個短語描述產生飛行所需的向上力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"an excellent hoverer","meaning":"擅長懸停的動物","examples":[{"en":"The hummingbird is an excellent hoverer.","zh":"蜂鳥是一種擅長懸停的動物。"},{"en":"An excellent hoverer is an animal or machine that can stay in one place in the air very well.","zh":"擅長懸停的動物或機器，是能很好地停留在空中同一位置的動物或機器。"},{"en":"A drone is an excellent hoverer if it can remain steady while filming.","zh":"如果無人機拍攝時能保持穩定，它就是擅長懸停的機器。"},{"en":"Hummingbirds are excellent hoverers because their wings beat extremely fast and flexibly.","zh":"蜂鳥擅長懸停，因為牠們的翅膀拍動極快且靈活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong ability to hover.","zh":"這個短語描述強大的懸停能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"flap its wings","meaning":"拍動翅膀","examples":[{"en":"A hummingbird can flap its wings up to 80 times every second.","zh":"蜂鳥每秒可以拍動翅膀多達 80 次。"},{"en":"To flap its wings means to move the wings up and down repeatedly.","zh":"拍動翅膀，是指反覆上下移動翅膀。"},{"en":"A bird may flap its wings quickly before taking off.","zh":"鳥起飛前可能快速拍動翅膀。"},{"en":"Fast wing flapping helps hummingbirds stay in the air and feed from flowers.","zh":"快速拍翼幫助蜂鳥停留在空中並從花朵吸食花蜜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated wing movement.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆的翅膀動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"up to 80 times every second","meaning":"每秒多達80次","examples":[{"en":"A hummingbird flaps its wings up to 80 times every second.","zh":"蜂鳥每秒拍動翅膀多達 80 次。"},{"en":"Up to 80 times every second means as many as 80 times in each second.","zh":"每秒多達 80 次，是指每秒最多可達 80 次。"},{"en":"A fast camera may take up to 100 photos every second.","zh":"快速相機可能每秒拍攝多達 100 張相片。"},{"en":"Such high frequency explains why normal eyes cannot clearly follow each movement.","zh":"如此高頻率解釋了為何普通肉眼不能清楚追蹤每個動作。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a very high maximum rate.","zh":"這個短語表達非常高的最高頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"truly capture this motion","meaning":"真正捕捉這個動作","examples":[{"en":"Only special cameras can truly capture this motion.","zh":"只有特殊相機能真正捕捉這個動作。"},{"en":"To truly capture this motion means to record the movement clearly and accurately.","zh":"真正捕捉這個動作，是指清楚而準確地記錄該動作。"},{"en":"A phone camera may not truly capture a tennis ball moving at high speed.","zh":"手機相機可能無法真正捕捉高速移動的網球。"},{"en":"Special cameras are needed when motion is too fast for ordinary recording.","zh":"當動作對普通錄影來說太快，就需要特殊相機。"},{"en":"This phrase describes capturing movement with enough detail to study it.","zh":"這個短語描述以足夠細節捕捉動作以供研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in effect","meaning":"實際上","examples":[{"en":"High-speed cameras, in effect, slow down time.","zh":"高速攝影機實際上放慢了時間。"},{"en":"In effect means in practical result, even if not literally.","zh":"實際上，是指在實際效果上如此，即使不是字面上如此。"},{"en":"A clear timetable, in effect, reduces stress because students know what to do next.","zh":"清楚時間表實際上會減少壓力，因為學生知道下一步做甚麼。"},{"en":"High-speed cameras do not really change time, but they make fast action appear slower.","zh":"高速攝影機並不真正改變時間，但它們令快速動作看起來更慢。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the practical effect of something.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事的實際效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"slow down time","meaning":"放慢時間","examples":[{"en":"High-speed cameras slow down time for the viewer.","zh":"高速攝影機為觀眾放慢時間。"},{"en":"To slow down time means to make events appear to happen more slowly on screen.","zh":"放慢時間，是指令事件在螢幕上看起來更慢發生。"},{"en":"A sports replay can slow down time so viewers can see whether the ball crossed the line.","zh":"體育重播可以放慢時間，讓觀眾看清球是否越過界線。"},{"en":"Slowing down time helps people notice details in fast action.","zh":"放慢時間幫助人們注意快速動作中的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visual effect, not a real change in time itself.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺效果，而不是真正改變時間本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a longer sequence of film","meaning":"較長的影片序列","examples":[{"en":"A longer sequence of film is captured at a high frame rate.","zh":"較長的影片序列以高幀率被捕捉。"},{"en":"A longer sequence of film means more recorded frames showing a short event in greater detail.","zh":"較長的影片序列，是指更多錄影片格，以更詳細方式展示短暫事件。"},{"en":"A coach may use a longer sequence of film to study a golfer’s swing.","zh":"教練可能使用較長的影片序列研究高爾夫球手揮桿。"},{"en":"More frames allow fast movement to be replayed smoothly and slowly.","zh":"更多幀讓快速動作能順暢而慢速地重播。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extended recorded footage.","zh":"這個短語描述較長的錄影片段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"high sampling frequency","meaning":"高採樣頻率","examples":[{"en":"The film is captured at a high sampling frequency.","zh":"影片以高採樣頻率被拍攝。"},{"en":"High sampling frequency means recording many measurements or frames in a short time.","zh":"高採樣頻率，是指在短時間內記錄很多測量值或畫格。"},{"en":"A sound recorder with high sampling frequency can capture fine details in music.","zh":"具有高採樣頻率的錄音機可以捕捉音樂中的細節。"},{"en":"Higher sampling frequency gives more data, so rapid changes become easier to study.","zh":"較高採樣頻率提供更多資料，因此快速變化更容易研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frequent recording of information.","zh":"這個短語描述頻繁記錄資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"frame rate","meaning":"幀率","examples":[{"en":"The camera records movement at a high frame rate.","zh":"相機以高幀率記錄動作。"},{"en":"Frame rate is the number of image frames recorded or shown per second.","zh":"幀率是每秒記錄或顯示的影像幀數。"},{"en":"A video game may look smoother when it has a higher frame rate.","zh":"電子遊戲在較高幀率下可能看起來更順暢。"},{"en":"A high frame rate captures more stages of a fast movement.","zh":"高幀率捕捉快速動作中的更多階段。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how many pictures are recorded each second.","zh":"這個短語描述每秒記錄多少張影像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be projected on screen","meaning":"被投射到螢幕上","examples":[{"en":"The film is later projected on screen at a lower speed.","zh":"影片之後以較低速度被投射到螢幕上。"},{"en":"To be projected on screen means to be shown on a screen for viewers.","zh":"被投射到螢幕上，是指被顯示在螢幕上給觀眾觀看。"},{"en":"A teacher may project a science video on screen during class.","zh":"老師可能在課堂上把科學影片投射到螢幕上。"},{"en":"Projection makes recorded material visible to an audience.","zh":"投影令錄製材料能被觀眾看見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes showing film or images on a screen.","zh":"這個短語描述把影片或影像顯示在螢幕上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"replayed at normal speed","meaning":"以正常速度重播","examples":[{"en":"When replayed at normal speed, time appears slower.","zh":"以正常速度重播時，時間看起來變慢。"},{"en":"Replayed at normal speed means played again at the usual viewing speed.","zh":"以正常速度重播，是指以一般觀看速度再次播放。"},{"en":"A slow-motion sports clip may be recorded very fast but replayed at normal speed.","zh":"慢動作體育片段可能以高速拍攝，但以正常速度重播。"},{"en":"When high-frame footage is replayed normally, the original action appears slowed down.","zh":"當高幀率片段以正常速度重播，原本動作看起來被放慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how recorded footage is shown after filming.","zh":"這個短語描述拍攝後影片如何被播放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be slowed down proportionately","meaning":"按比例放慢","examples":[{"en":"The movement is slowed down proportionately when replayed.","zh":"動作重播時會按比例放慢。"},{"en":"To be slowed down proportionately means to be reduced in speed according to the recording and playback rates.","zh":"按比例放慢，是指根據拍攝和播放速度的比例降低速度。"},{"en":"If footage is recorded ten times faster than normal, movement may be slowed down proportionately in playback.","zh":"如果片段以正常速度十倍拍攝，動作在播放時可能按比例放慢。"},{"en":"Proportional slowdown keeps the motion smooth rather than random or uneven.","zh":"按比例放慢能保持動作順暢，而不是隨機或不均。"},{"en":"This phrase describes speed reduction by a matching ratio.","zh":"這個短語描述按相應比例降低速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"become such a mainstay of","meaning":"成為……的重要工具","examples":[{"en":"High-speed cameras have become such a mainstay of biology.","zh":"高速攝影機已成為生物學的重要工具。"},{"en":"To become such a mainstay of something means to become a very important and regularly used part of it.","zh":"成為某領域的重要工具，是指成為其中非常重要且經常使用的一部分。"},{"en":"Online dictionaries have become a mainstay of language learning for many students.","zh":"網上字典已成為許多學生語言學習的重要工具。"},{"en":"A tool becomes a mainstay when experts rely on it again and again.","zh":"當專家反覆依賴某工具，它就會成為重要支柱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something becoming central and dependable.","zh":"這個短語描述某物變得核心且可靠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in common usage","meaning":"在一般用法中","examples":[{"en":"In common usage, high-speed photography can also mean freezing motion.","zh":"在一般用法中，高速攝影也可以指定格動作。"},{"en":"In common usage means in the way ordinary people usually use a word or phrase.","zh":"在一般用法中，是指普通人通常使用某詞或短語的方式。"},{"en":"In common usage, “phone” often means a smartphone rather than only a device for calls.","zh":"在一般用法中，“phone” 常指智能手機，而不只是打電話的裝置。"},{"en":"Common usage may be less technical than professional usage.","zh":"一般用法可能比專業用法較不技術化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes everyday meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述日常意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"指；表示","examples":[{"en":"High-speed photography can refer to the use of high-speed cameras.","zh":"高速攝影可以指使用高速攝影機。"},{"en":"To refer to something means to mean, describe or point to it.","zh":"指某事，是指表示、描述或指向它。"},{"en":"In school, “PE” usually refers to physical education.","zh":"在學校，“PE” 通常指體育課。"},{"en":"A word can refer to different things depending on context.","zh":"一個詞可以因語境不同而指不同事物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what a term is used to mean.","zh":"這個短語描述術語被用來表示甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"high-speed cameras","meaning":"高速攝影機","examples":[{"en":"High-speed cameras can freeze motion and reduce blur.","zh":"高速攝影機可以定格動作並減少模糊。"},{"en":"High-speed cameras are cameras that record very rapid movement using many frames per second.","zh":"高速攝影機是以每秒大量幀數記錄極快速動作的相機。"},{"en":"A laboratory may use high-speed cameras to study how glass cracks.","zh":"實驗室可能使用高速攝影機研究玻璃如何破裂。"},{"en":"Because they capture fast motion clearly, high-speed cameras are useful in science and sport.","zh":"因為高速攝影機能清楚捕捉快速動作，它們在科學和體育中很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to cameras designed for rapid events.","zh":"這個短語指為快速事件而設計的相機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"freeze motion","meaning":"定格動作","examples":[{"en":"A high-speed camera can freeze motion in a photograph.","zh":"高速攝影機可以在相片中定格動作。"},{"en":"To freeze motion means to capture a moving object so sharply that it appears still.","zh":"定格動作，是指清晰捕捉移動物體，使它看起來靜止。"},{"en":"A sports photographer may freeze motion when a footballer kicks the ball.","zh":"體育攝影師可能在足球員踢球時定格動作。"},{"en":"Fast shutter speeds freeze motion by reducing the time the sensor records light.","zh":"快速快門透過縮短感光元件記錄光線的時間來定格動作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making movement look still in an image.","zh":"這個短語描述令動作在影像中看起來靜止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reduce motion blur","meaning":"減少動態模糊","examples":[{"en":"A fast shutter can reduce motion blur.","zh":"快速快門可以減少動態模糊。"},{"en":"To reduce motion blur means to make moving objects look clearer and less smeared.","zh":"減少動態模糊，是指令移動物體看起來更清楚、不拖影。"},{"en":"A parent may use sports mode to reduce motion blur when photographing a running child.","zh":"父母拍攝奔跑中的孩子時，可能使用運動模式減少動態模糊。"},{"en":"Motion blur decreases when the camera captures the image very quickly.","zh":"當相機非常快速捕捉影像，動態模糊就會減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making movement appear sharper in a photo.","zh":"這個短語描述令相片中的動作更清晰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"good sensitivity","meaning":"良好感光度","examples":[{"en":"The camera requires a sensor with good sensitivity.","zh":"相機需要具有良好感光度的感光元件。"},{"en":"Good sensitivity means the sensor can respond well to light, even in difficult conditions.","zh":"良好感光度，是指感光元件即使在困難環境中也能對光線有良好反應。"},{"en":"A camera with good sensitivity can take clearer photos in a dark classroom.","zh":"具良好感光度的相機可以在昏暗課室中拍出較清晰相片。"},{"en":"Good sensitivity matters because high-speed shooting often allows very little light into the camera.","zh":"良好感光度很重要，因為高速拍攝通常只讓很少光線進入相機。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sensor’s ability to detect light effectively.","zh":"這個短語描述感光元件有效偵測光線的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"shuttering system","meaning":"快門系統","examples":[{"en":"High-speed photography needs a very good shuttering system.","zh":"高速攝影需要非常好的快門系統。"},{"en":"A shuttering system controls how and when light reaches the camera sensor.","zh":"快門系統控制光線如何以及何時到達相機感光元件。"},{"en":"A camera with a poor shuttering system may miss the exact moment a water drop splashes.","zh":"快門系統差的相機可能錯過水滴濺起的準確瞬間。"},{"en":"Good shutter control helps freeze fast movement clearly.","zh":"良好快門控制有助清楚定格快速動作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the camera mechanism that controls exposure timing.","zh":"這個短語指控制曝光時間的相機機制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fast strobe light","meaning":"快速頻閃燈","examples":[{"en":"A fast strobe light can help freeze rapid motion.","zh":"快速頻閃燈可以幫助定格快速動作。"},{"en":"A fast strobe light is a light that flashes very quickly for photographing fast action.","zh":"快速頻閃燈是為拍攝快速動作而非常快速閃光的燈。"},{"en":"A photographer may use a fast strobe light to capture a dancer mid-jump.","zh":"攝影師可能使用快速頻閃燈捕捉舞者跳起的一刻。"},{"en":"The quick flash provides enough light for a very short exposure.","zh":"快速閃光為極短曝光提供足夠光線。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lighting used to freeze motion.","zh":"這個短語描述用來定格動作的燈光。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"National Geographic footage","meaning":"《國家地理》影片片段","examples":[{"en":"The National Geographic footage showed a cheetah in super slow motion.","zh":"《國家地理》影片片段以超慢動作展示獵豹。"},{"en":"National Geographic footage means video material produced or shown by National Geographic.","zh":"《國家地理》影片片段，是由《國家地理》製作或播放的影片材料。"},{"en":"Students may watch National Geographic footage to learn about animals in the wild.","zh":"學生可能觀看《國家地理》影片片段，以了解野外動物。"},{"en":"Such footage can educate viewers because it combines clear images with real natural behaviour.","zh":"這類片段可以教育觀眾，因為它結合清晰影像和真實自然行為。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to documentary-style video material.","zh":"這個短語指紀錄片風格的影片材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"an intensive three-day shoot","meaning":"密集的三天拍攝","examples":[{"en":"The footage was captured during an intensive three-day shoot.","zh":"這段影片是在密集的三天拍攝期間捕捉的。"},{"en":"An intensive three-day shoot is a concentrated filming period lasting three days.","zh":"密集的三天拍攝，是持續三天的集中拍攝期。"},{"en":"A school drama team may have an intensive two-day shoot to finish a short film.","zh":"學校戲劇隊可能進行密集的兩天拍攝，以完成短片。"},{"en":"Intensive shoots require planning because much work must be done in limited time.","zh":"密集拍攝需要規劃，因為大量工作必須在有限時間內完成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a short but demanding filming session.","zh":"這個短語描述短暫但要求高的拍攝過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"unprecedented in its clarity and detail","meaning":"清晰度和細節前所未有","examples":[{"en":"The footage was unprecedented in its clarity and detail.","zh":"這段影片的清晰度和細節前所未有。"},{"en":"Unprecedented in its clarity and detail means never before seen with such sharpness and amount of information.","zh":"清晰度和細節前所未有，是指從未以如此清晰和豐富資訊被看見。"},{"en":"A new microscope image may be unprecedented in its clarity and detail.","zh":"新顯微鏡影像的清晰度和細節可能前所未有。"},{"en":"Clearer detail can change understanding because viewers notice things that were hidden before.","zh":"更清楚的細節可以改變理解，因為觀眾會注意到以前隱藏的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a level of visual quality never achieved before.","zh":"這個短語描述從未達到過的視覺質素水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"founder of","meaning":"……的創辦人","examples":[{"en":"Cathryn Hilker is the founder of the zoo’s Cat Ambassador Program.","zh":"Cathryn Hilker 是該動物園貓科動物大使計劃的創辦人。"},{"en":"The founder of something is the person who started or created it.","zh":"某事的創辦人，是開始或創立它的人。"},{"en":"The founder of a school club may write its first rules and recruit its first members.","zh":"學校學會的創辦人可能撰寫第一套規則並招募首批成員。"},{"en":"Founders often shape the purpose and early direction of a project.","zh":"創辦人通常塑造項目的目的和早期方向。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who began an organisation or programme.","zh":"這個短語指出誰開始了一個組織或計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"super slow-motion video","meaning":"超慢動作影片","examples":[{"en":"The super slow-motion video revealed details she had never seen before.","zh":"超慢動作影片揭示了她以前從未見過的細節。"},{"en":"A super slow-motion video shows action much more slowly than it happened in real life.","zh":"超慢動作影片以比現實中慢得多的速度展示動作。"},{"en":"A coach may use super slow-motion video to analyse a gymnast’s landing.","zh":"教練可能使用超慢動作影片分析體操運動員落地。"},{"en":"Slowing the action greatly helps viewers see tiny changes in movement.","zh":"大幅放慢動作幫助觀眾看見動作中的微小變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes video that makes rapid motion extremely slow.","zh":"這個短語描述把快速動作變得極慢的影片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the slow-motion video is entrancing","meaning":"慢動作影片令人著迷","examples":[{"en":"The slow-motion video is entrancing to watch.","zh":"慢動作影片看起來令人著迷。"},{"en":"If a slow-motion video is entrancing, it is so beautiful or interesting that viewers keep watching.","zh":"如果慢動作影片令人著迷，表示它美麗或有趣得令觀眾一直觀看。"},{"en":"A slow-motion video of raindrops hitting a pond can be entrancing.","zh":"雨滴落在池塘上的慢動作影片可以令人著迷。"},{"en":"Slow motion can be entrancing because it reveals grace and detail hidden in fast movement.","zh":"慢動作可以令人著迷，因為它揭示快速動作中隱藏的優雅和細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a video that strongly holds attention.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈吸引注意力的影片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sprinting cat’s anatomy","meaning":"奔跑中的貓科動物身體結構","examples":[{"en":"The video shows every part of the sprinting cat’s anatomy.","zh":"影片展示奔跑中的貓科動物身體結構的每一部分。"},{"en":"A sprinting cat’s anatomy means the body structure of a cat-like animal while it is running very fast.","zh":"奔跑中的貓科動物身體結構，是指貓科動物高速奔跑時的身體構造。"},{"en":"A biology teacher may use such footage to show how muscles and bones work during running.","zh":"生物老師可能使用這類片段展示奔跑時肌肉和骨骼如何運作。"},{"en":"Watching anatomy in motion helps scientists understand speed and balance.","zh":"觀看運動中的身體結構幫助科學家理解速度和平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the body parts of a fast-running cat-like animal.","zh":"這個短語描述快速奔跑的貓科動物身體部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"supple limbs","meaning":"柔韌的四肢","examples":[{"en":"The cheetah’s supple limbs help it run at great speed.","zh":"獵豹柔韌的四肢幫助牠高速奔跑。"},{"en":"Supple limbs are flexible arms or legs that bend and move easily.","zh":"柔韌的四肢，是容易彎曲和移動的手臂或腿。"},{"en":"A dancer needs supple limbs to move smoothly and gracefully.","zh":"舞者需要柔韌的四肢，才能流暢優雅地移動。"},{"en":"Flexible limbs help animals stretch further and move more efficiently.","zh":"靈活四肢幫助動物伸展得更遠並更有效率地移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes body parts that are flexible rather than stiff.","zh":"這個短語描述靈活而不是僵硬的身體部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rippling muscles","meaning":"起伏的肌肉","examples":[{"en":"The video reveals the cheetah’s rippling muscles.","zh":"影片揭示獵豹起伏的肌肉。"},{"en":"Rippling muscles are muscles that visibly move in waves under the skin.","zh":"起伏的肌肉，是皮膚下可見像波浪般移動的肌肉。"},{"en":"A slow-motion sports video may show a runner’s rippling muscles during a sprint.","zh":"慢動作體育影片可能展示短跑運動員衝刺時起伏的肌肉。"},{"en":"Rippling muscles make strength and movement easier to see.","zh":"起伏的肌肉令力量和動作更容易看見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible waves of muscular motion.","zh":"這個短語描述可見的肌肉波動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hyperflexible spine","meaning":"超柔韌的脊椎","examples":[{"en":"The cheetah has a hyperflexible spine.","zh":"獵豹有超柔韌的脊椎。"},{"en":"A hyperflexible spine is a backbone that can bend and stretch extremely well.","zh":"超柔韌的脊椎，是能極度彎曲和伸展的脊骨。"},{"en":"A gymnast’s back may look highly flexible during a bridge pose.","zh":"體操運動員做橋式時，背部可能看起來非常柔韌。"},{"en":"A cheetah’s flexible spine helps lengthen each stride while running.","zh":"獵豹柔韌的脊椎幫助牠在奔跑時延長每一步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unusually flexible backbone.","zh":"這個短語描述異常靈活的脊骨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"work together in","meaning":"在……中協同運作","examples":[{"en":"The cheetah’s body parts work together in a symphony of speed.","zh":"獵豹的身體部位在速度的交響中協同運作。"},{"en":"To work together in something means to cooperate as parts of one larger action or effect.","zh":"在某事中協同運作，是指作為一個更大行動或效果的部分互相配合。"},{"en":"In a school play, actors, lighting and music work together in one performance.","zh":"在學校話劇中，演員、燈光和音樂在一場演出中協同運作。"},{"en":"When body parts work together, movement becomes smoother and more powerful.","zh":"當身體部位協同運作，動作就更流暢有力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes coordinated action within a larger whole.","zh":"這個短語描述較大整體中的協調行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a symphony of speed","meaning":"速度的交響","examples":[{"en":"The cheetah’s body moves in a symphony of speed.","zh":"獵豹的身體以速度的交響方式移動。"},{"en":"A symphony of speed is a poetic way to describe many movements working together beautifully and quickly.","zh":"速度的交響，是用詩意方式描述許多動作美麗而快速地協同運作。"},{"en":"A relay team running perfectly together can look like a symphony of speed.","zh":"接力隊完美合作奔跑時，看起來可以像速度的交響。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests not just speed, but coordinated and graceful speed.","zh":"這個短語暗示的不只是速度，還有協調而優雅的速度。"},{"en":"This phrase uses music as a metaphor for smooth movement.","zh":"這個短語用音樂比喻流暢動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reveal the fluid grace of","meaning":"展現……的流暢優雅","examples":[{"en":"The footage reveals the fluid grace of the world’s fastest land animal.","zh":"這段影片展現世界上最快陸上動物的流暢優雅。"},{"en":"To reveal the fluid grace of something means to show its smooth and beautiful movement clearly.","zh":"展現某物的流暢優雅，是指清楚展示其平滑而美麗的動作。"},{"en":"Slow-motion video can reveal the fluid grace of a dancer’s jump.","zh":"慢動作影片可以展現舞者跳躍的流暢優雅。"},{"en":"High-speed footage reveals grace by slowing movement enough for viewers to see each part.","zh":"高速影片透過把動作放慢到觀眾看得見每部分來展現優雅。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making smooth beauty visible.","zh":"這個短語描述令平滑美感變得可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the world’s fastest land animal","meaning":"世界上最快的陸上動物","examples":[{"en":"The cheetah is the world’s fastest land animal.","zh":"獵豹是世界上最快的陸上動物。"},{"en":"The world’s fastest land animal is the animal that can run faster on land than any other animal.","zh":"世界上最快的陸上動物，是在陸地上跑得比任何其他動物都快的動物。"},{"en":"Children often learn that the cheetah is the world’s fastest land animal in science class.","zh":"孩子常在科學課學到獵豹是世界上最快的陸上動物。"},{"en":"Its speed comes from body features such as long legs, strong muscles and a flexible spine.","zh":"牠的速度來自身體特徵，例如長腿、強壯肌肉和柔韌脊椎。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the cheetah by its exceptional running speed.","zh":"這個短語以獵豹非凡的奔跑速度來識別牠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"become even more complicated","meaning":"變得更加複雜","examples":[{"en":"Things become even more complicated when filming a frog catching prey.","zh":"拍攝青蛙捕食時，事情變得更加複雜。"},{"en":"To become even more complicated means to become harder, with more problems or details involved.","zh":"變得更加複雜，是指變得更困難，涉及更多問題或細節。"},{"en":"Planning a school trip becomes even more complicated when the weather is uncertain.","zh":"當天氣不確定，規劃學校旅行會變得更加複雜。"},{"en":"Filming fast animal behaviour becomes complicated because timing and camera settings must be exact.","zh":"拍攝快速動物行為會變得複雜，因為時間和相機設定必須準確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a situation becoming more difficult than before.","zh":"這個短語描述情況比之前更困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"catch its prey","meaning":"捕捉獵物","examples":[{"en":"The frog catches its prey with an elastic tongue.","zh":"青蛙用有彈性的舌頭捕捉獵物。"},{"en":"To catch its prey means to capture the animal it eats.","zh":"捕捉獵物，是指捕獲牠所吃的動物。"},{"en":"A spider catches its prey when an insect becomes trapped in its web.","zh":"當昆蟲被困在蜘蛛網中，蜘蛛就捕捉到獵物。"},{"en":"Predators need quick movements or clever methods to catch prey successfully.","zh":"捕食者需要快速動作或巧妙方法才能成功捕捉獵物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an animal obtaining food by capturing another animal.","zh":"這個短語描述動物透過捕獲另一動物來獲取食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"snatch up prey","meaning":"迅速捕捉獵物","examples":[{"en":"Frogs can snatch up prey in a few thousandths of a second.","zh":"青蛙可以在幾千分之一秒內迅速捕捉獵物。"},{"en":"To snatch up prey means to grab food suddenly and quickly.","zh":"迅速捕捉獵物，是指突然快速抓住食物。"},{"en":"A bird may snatch up an insect from the ground before it escapes.","zh":"鳥可能在昆蟲逃走前從地上迅速捕捉牠。"},{"en":"The action must be fast because prey animals often move away quickly.","zh":"這個動作必須很快，因為獵物通常會迅速逃開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sudden capture of food by an animal.","zh":"這個短語描述動物突然捕獲食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a few thousandths of a second","meaning":"幾千分之一秒","examples":[{"en":"The frog strikes in a few thousandths of a second.","zh":"青蛙在幾千分之一秒內出擊。"},{"en":"A few thousandths of a second means only a tiny fraction of one second.","zh":"幾千分之一秒，是一秒中極小的一部分。"},{"en":"A camera flash may last only a few thousandths of a second.","zh":"相機閃光可能只持續幾千分之一秒。"},{"en":"Movements this fast require high-speed cameras because normal eyes cannot separate the stages.","zh":"如此快速的動作需要高速攝影機，因為普通肉眼無法分辨各階段。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an extremely short time.","zh":"這個短語描述極短時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"strike out with","meaning":"用……出擊","examples":[{"en":"Frogs strike out with elastic tongues.","zh":"青蛙用有彈性的舌頭出擊。"},{"en":"To strike out with something means to shoot or extend it quickly toward a target.","zh":"用某物出擊，是指把它快速伸向目標或射向目標。"},{"en":"A boxer may strike out with a quick punch during a match.","zh":"拳擊手可能在比賽中用快速一拳出擊。"},{"en":"Frogs strike out with their tongues because insects must be caught before they escape.","zh":"青蛙用舌頭出擊，因為昆蟲必須在逃走前被捉住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sudden attacking movement using a body part or tool.","zh":"這個短語描述使用身體部位或工具進行突然攻擊動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"elastic tongues","meaning":"有彈性的舌頭","examples":[{"en":"Frogs catch insects with elastic tongues.","zh":"青蛙用有彈性的舌頭捕捉昆蟲。"},{"en":"Elastic tongues are tongues that can stretch and spring back quickly.","zh":"有彈性的舌頭，是能伸展並快速彈回的舌頭。"},{"en":"A rubber band is elastic because it stretches and returns to shape.","zh":"橡筋有彈性，因為它能伸展並回復形狀。"},{"en":"Frogs need elastic tongues to reach prey quickly and pull it back.","zh":"青蛙需要有彈性的舌頭，才能快速觸及獵物並把牠拉回。"},{"en":"This phrase describes flexible tongues used for catching food.","zh":"這個短語描述用來捕食的靈活舌頭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"roll out","meaning":"伸展出來","examples":[{"en":"Biologists want to see how a frog’s tongue rolls out.","zh":"生物學家想看青蛙的舌頭如何伸展出來。"},{"en":"To roll out means to unfold, extend or move outward smoothly.","zh":"伸展出來，是指展開、伸出或平滑向外移動。"},{"en":"A teacher may roll out a poster across the classroom floor.","zh":"老師可能把海報在課室地板上展開。"},{"en":"A frog’s tongue rolls out quickly so it can reach prey at a distance.","zh":"青蛙的舌頭快速伸展出來，以便觸及遠處獵物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something extending outward.","zh":"這個短語描述某物向外延伸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"adhere to prey","meaning":"黏住獵物","examples":[{"en":"The frog’s tongue adheres to prey before returning to its mouth.","zh":"青蛙的舌頭在回到口中前會黏住獵物。"},{"en":"To adhere to prey means to stick to the animal being caught.","zh":"黏住獵物，是指黏附正在被捕捉的動物。"},{"en":"Sticky tape adheres to paper when pressed down.","zh":"膠紙按下後會黏住紙張。"},{"en":"A frog’s tongue must adhere to prey so the insect is pulled back instead of escaping.","zh":"青蛙的舌頭必須黏住獵物，昆蟲才會被拉回而不是逃走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sticking firmly to captured food.","zh":"這個短語描述牢牢黏住捕獲的食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"roll back into","meaning":"捲回……裏","examples":[{"en":"The tongue rolls back into the frog’s mouth.","zh":"舌頭捲回青蛙口中。"},{"en":"To roll back into something means to return inward by folding or moving back.","zh":"捲回某處，是指透過摺回或移回而返回內部。"},{"en":"A tape measure rolls back into its case after use.","zh":"捲尺使用後會捲回盒子裏。"},{"en":"The frog’s tongue rolls back into its mouth to bring the prey with it.","zh":"青蛙的舌頭捲回口中，把獵物一同帶回。"},{"en":"This phrase describes returning into an original place.","zh":"這個短語描述回到原本位置裏面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"50 times faster than","meaning":"比……快50倍","examples":[{"en":"The action is 50 times faster than an eye blink.","zh":"這個動作比眨眼快 50 倍。"},{"en":"50 times faster than something means happening at fifty times the speed of that thing.","zh":"比某事快 50 倍，是指以該事 50 倍的速度發生。"},{"en":"A computer may process a task 50 times faster than an old machine.","zh":"一部電腦處理任務可能比舊機器快 50 倍。"},{"en":"When something is 50 times faster than a blink, people cannot see it clearly without special equipment.","zh":"當某事比眨眼快 50 倍，人們沒有特殊設備就無法看清。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a strong speed comparison.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈速度比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"an eye blink","meaning":"眨眼","examples":[{"en":"The frog’s strike is much faster than an eye blink.","zh":"青蛙出擊比眨眼快得多。"},{"en":"An eye blink is the quick closing and opening of the eyelids.","zh":"眨眼是眼瞼快速合上和張開。"},{"en":"A camera can take a photo in less time than an eye blink.","zh":"相機可以在比眨眼更短的時間內拍照。"},{"en":"Comparing an action to a blink helps readers understand how fast it is.","zh":"把動作與眨眼比較，幫助讀者理解它有多快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very short natural action.","zh":"這個短語描述非常短暫的自然動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in slow motion","meaning":"以慢動作","examples":[{"en":"A high-speed camera can show the movement in slow motion.","zh":"高速攝影機可以以慢動作展示這個動作。"},{"en":"In slow motion means shown more slowly than it happened in real life.","zh":"以慢動作，是指以比現實發生速度更慢的方式展示。"},{"en":"A sports replay in slow motion can show whether a player touched the line.","zh":"體育慢動作重播可以顯示球員是否碰到界線。"},{"en":"Slow motion helps viewers see details hidden in quick actions.","zh":"慢動作幫助觀眾看見快速行動中隱藏的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slowed playback.","zh":"這個短語描述放慢播放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"one problem still remains","meaning":"仍有一個問題","examples":[{"en":"One problem still remains when viewers watch too much slow motion.","zh":"當觀眾看太多慢動作時，仍有一個問題。"},{"en":"One problem still remains means there is still an issue that has not been solved.","zh":"仍有一個問題，是指仍然有一個未解決的議題。"},{"en":"After the school repairs the roof, one problem still remains: the classrooms are too hot.","zh":"學校修好屋頂後，仍有一個問題：課室太熱。"},{"en":"A solution may fix one difficulty while leaving another difficulty behind.","zh":"一個解決方法可能處理了一項困難，卻留下另一項困難。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an unresolved problem.","zh":"這個短語引入尚未解決的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"become bored if","meaning":"如果……就會感到沉悶","examples":[{"en":"Viewers would become bored if the frog swam in slow motion for too long.","zh":"如果青蛙游泳的畫面以慢動作播放太久，觀眾就會感到沉悶。"},{"en":"Become bored if means start feeling uninterested when a certain condition happens.","zh":"如果某情況發生就會感到沉悶，是指在該條件下開始失去興趣。"},{"en":"Students may become bored if a video repeats the same point for ten minutes.","zh":"如果影片重複同一重點十分鐘，學生可能會感到沉悶。"},{"en":"Slow motion is useful, but too much of it can reduce interest.","zh":"慢動作有用，但太多會降低興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase links a condition with loss of attention.","zh":"這個短語把條件與注意力流失連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"for too long","meaning":"太久","examples":[{"en":"The swimming scene should not be shown in slow motion for too long.","zh":"游泳場面不應以慢動作展示太久。"},{"en":"For too long means for a longer time than is useful, comfortable or interesting.","zh":"太久，是指時間長到超出有用、舒服或有趣的程度。"},{"en":"If a teacher explains one example for too long, students may lose focus.","zh":"如果老師解釋一個例子太久，學生可能失去專注。"},{"en":"Even good techniques can become ineffective when used for too long.","zh":"即使是好技巧，使用太久也可能變得無效。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that excessive duration can create problems.","zh":"這個短語提醒過長時間會造成問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"how can this be avoided","meaning":"怎樣避免這種情況","examples":[{"en":"The editor must decide how this can be avoided.","zh":"剪接師必須決定怎樣避免這種情況。"},{"en":"How can this be avoided asks what can be done to prevent a problem.","zh":"怎樣避免這種情況，是問可以做甚麼來防止問題。"},{"en":"If students keep making the same grammar mistake, the teacher may ask how this can be avoided.","zh":"如果學生不斷犯同一文法錯誤，老師可能會問怎樣避免這種情況。"},{"en":"The question shifts attention from the problem to the solution.","zh":"這個問題把注意力由問題轉向解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when looking for prevention.","zh":"這個短語用於尋找預防方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the solution is a simple one","meaning":"解決方法很簡單","examples":[{"en":"The solution is a simple one: adjust the playback speed.","zh":"解決方法很簡單：調整播放速度。"},{"en":"The solution is a simple one means the answer to the problem is easy or straightforward.","zh":"解決方法很簡單，是指問題的答案容易或直接。"},{"en":"If students forget deadlines, the solution is a simple one: use a shared calendar.","zh":"如果學生忘記截止日期，解決方法很簡單：使用共享日曆。"},{"en":"A simple solution can work well when the problem is caused by one clear factor.","zh":"當問題由一個清楚因素造成，簡單解決方法可以很有效。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an uncomplicated answer.","zh":"這個短語引入不複雜的答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"adjust the playback speed","meaning":"調整播放速度","examples":[{"en":"The editor can adjust the playback speed to keep the film interesting.","zh":"剪接師可以調整播放速度，使影片保持有趣。"},{"en":"To adjust the playback speed means to change how fast or slow a recording is shown.","zh":"調整播放速度，是指改變錄像顯示得快或慢。"},{"en":"A student may adjust the playback speed of a lecture video to review difficult parts slowly.","zh":"學生可能調整講座影片的播放速度，以慢速重溫困難部分。"},{"en":"Changing playback speed helps viewers focus on the important moments.","zh":"改變播放速度幫助觀眾專注於重要時刻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlling viewing speed after recording.","zh":"這個短語描述錄製後控制觀看速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"film speed adjustment","meaning":"影片速度調整","examples":[{"en":"Film speed adjustment helps viewers focus on the important action.","zh":"影片速度調整幫助觀眾專注於重要動作。"},{"en":"Film speed adjustment means changing the speed of video playback or edited footage.","zh":"影片速度調整，是改變影片播放或剪接片段的速度。"},{"en":"An editor may use film speed adjustment to slow down a goal and speed up the celebration.","zh":"剪接師可能使用影片速度調整，把入球放慢，把慶祝加快。"},{"en":"Adjusting speed keeps a video informative without making boring parts last too long.","zh":"調整速度能令影片有資訊量，同時避免沉悶部分持續太久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes editing the pace of a film.","zh":"這個短語描述剪接影片節奏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be shot at a high frame rate","meaning":"以高幀率拍攝","examples":[{"en":"The film is originally shot at a high frame rate.","zh":"影片原本以高幀率拍攝。"},{"en":"To be shot at a high frame rate means to be filmed with many frames recorded each second.","zh":"以高幀率拍攝，是指每秒記錄大量畫格來拍攝。"},{"en":"A skateboarding trick may be shot at a high frame rate so the landing can be studied.","zh":"滑板技巧可能以高幀率拍攝，以便研究落地動作。"},{"en":"High-frame-rate footage can later be slowed down smoothly.","zh":"高幀率片段之後可以順暢地放慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a filming method for capturing fast movement.","zh":"這個短語描述捕捉快速動作的拍攝方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"frames per second","meaning":"每秒幀數","examples":[{"en":"The frog footage may be shot at 300 frames per second.","zh":"青蛙影片可能以每秒 300 幀拍攝。"},{"en":"Frames per second means the number of individual images recorded or shown each second.","zh":"每秒幀數，是每秒記錄或顯示的個別影像數量。"},{"en":"A video recorded at 60 frames per second looks smoother than one recorded at 15.","zh":"每秒 60 幀的影片比每秒 15 幀的影片看起來更順暢。"},{"en":"More frames per second make fast movement easier to slow down and analyse.","zh":"每秒幀數越多，快速動作越容易放慢和分析。"},{"en":"This phrase measures recording or playback rate.","zh":"這個短語量度錄製或播放速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be converted to","meaning":"被轉換成","examples":[{"en":"High frame-rate footage can be converted to lower frame rates.","zh":"高幀率片段可以被轉換成較低幀率。"},{"en":"To be converted to something means to be changed into another form or setting.","zh":"被轉換成某物，是指被改變成另一形式或設定。"},{"en":"A Word document can be converted to a PDF for easier sharing.","zh":"Word 文件可以被轉換成 PDF，以便分享。"},{"en":"Footage is converted when editors need a different speed or format.","zh":"當剪接師需要不同速度或格式時，片段會被轉換。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing one form into another.","zh":"這個短語描述把一種形式改成另一種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"much lower frame rates","meaning":"低得多的幀率","examples":[{"en":"The footage can be converted to much lower frame rates.","zh":"影片可以被轉換成低得多的幀率。"},{"en":"Much lower frame rates means far fewer frames per second than before.","zh":"低得多的幀率，是指每秒幀數比之前少很多。"},{"en":"A high-speed video may be changed to much lower frame rates for normal viewing.","zh":"高速影片可能被改成低得多的幀率，以便正常觀看。"},{"en":"Lowering the frame rate can change how fast the action appears.","zh":"降低幀率可以改變動作看起來的速度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large decrease in frames per second.","zh":"這個短語描述每秒幀數大幅下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"without major issues","meaning":"沒有重大問題","examples":[{"en":"The footage can be converted without major issues.","zh":"影片可以在沒有重大問題下被轉換。"},{"en":"Without major issues means without serious problems or difficulties.","zh":"沒有重大問題，是指沒有嚴重問題或困難。"},{"en":"The school trip ended without major issues, although the bus was late.","zh":"學校旅行雖然巴士遲到，但沒有重大問題地結束。"},{"en":"If footage converts without major issues, editors can work smoothly.","zh":"如果影片轉換沒有重大問題，剪接師就能順利工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a process happening without serious trouble.","zh":"這個短語描述過程沒有嚴重麻煩地進行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"at a later editing stage","meaning":"在後期剪接階段","examples":[{"en":"The speed is adjusted at a later editing stage.","zh":"速度在後期剪接階段被調整。"},{"en":"At a later editing stage means during a later part of the process of editing the film.","zh":"在後期剪接階段，是指在影片剪接過程的較後部分。"},{"en":"A school video may have music added at a later editing stage.","zh":"學校影片可能在後期剪接階段加入音樂。"},{"en":"Some decisions are not made during filming but during editing afterward.","zh":"有些決定不是在拍攝時作出，而是在之後剪接時作出。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a later step in post-production.","zh":"這個短語指後期製作中的較後步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be preserved for","meaning":"為……保留","examples":[{"en":"The high frame rate is preserved for the prey-catching part.","zh":"高幀率為捕食部分保留。"},{"en":"To be preserved for something means to be kept for that particular use or section.","zh":"為某事保留，是指為該特定用途或部分保存。"},{"en":"The best photos may be preserved for the school magazine cover.","zh":"最好的相片可能為學校雜誌封面保留。"},{"en":"Editors preserve slow motion for important action so viewers see the crucial detail.","zh":"剪接師會為重要動作保留慢動作，讓觀眾看見關鍵細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes saving something for a specific purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述把某物留作特定用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"prey-catching part","meaning":"捕食部分","examples":[{"en":"The prey-catching part remains in slow motion.","zh":"捕食部分保持慢動作。"},{"en":"The prey-catching part is the section showing an animal capturing its food.","zh":"捕食部分是展示動物捕捉食物的片段。"},{"en":"In a frog video, the prey-catching part may show the tongue shooting out.","zh":"在青蛙影片中，捕食部分可能展示舌頭射出的畫面。"},{"en":"This part is kept slow because it contains the fastest and most important movement.","zh":"這部分保持慢速，因為它包含最快且最重要的動作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the section focused on catching prey.","zh":"這個短語描述聚焦捕捉獵物的片段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be converted to normal speed","meaning":"被轉換成正常速度","examples":[{"en":"The swimming part is converted to normal speed.","zh":"游泳部分被轉換成正常速度。"},{"en":"To be converted to normal speed means to be changed so it plays at ordinary speed.","zh":"被轉換成正常速度，是指被改成以普通速度播放。"},{"en":"An editor may convert a walking scene to normal speed after showing a jump in slow motion.","zh":"剪接師可能在慢動作展示跳躍後，把步行場面轉換成正常速度。"},{"en":"Normal speed keeps unimportant parts from feeling too long.","zh":"正常速度避免不重要部分感覺太長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing footage back to ordinary playback.","zh":"這個短語描述把片段改回普通播放速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sit back and enjoy","meaning":"輕鬆坐下來欣賞","examples":[{"en":"The scientists can sit back and enjoy the video.","zh":"科學家可以輕鬆坐下來欣賞影片。"},{"en":"To sit back and enjoy means to relax and watch or experience something with pleasure.","zh":"輕鬆坐下來欣賞，是指放鬆觀看或享受某事。"},{"en":"After finishing a difficult project, students can sit back and enjoy their presentation video.","zh":"完成困難專題後，學生可以輕鬆坐下來欣賞自己的匯報影片。"},{"en":"Once editing removes boring waiting time, viewers can enjoy the important action easily.","zh":"一旦剪接移除沉悶等待時間，觀眾就能輕鬆欣賞重要動作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relaxed enjoyment after work or preparation.","zh":"這個短語描述工作或準備後的放鬆享受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"go through the pain of","meaning":"忍受……的痛苦","examples":[{"en":"Viewers do not have to go through the pain of waiting.","zh":"觀眾不用忍受等待的痛苦。"},{"en":"To go through the pain of something means to suffer an unpleasant or boring experience.","zh":"忍受某事的痛苦，是指經歷不愉快或沉悶的事情。"},{"en":"Students may go through the pain of rewriting an essay if they ignored the question.","zh":"如果學生忽略題目，可能要忍受重寫文章的痛苦。"},{"en":"Editing can remove unnecessary waiting so viewers avoid a frustrating experience.","zh":"剪接可以移除不必要等待，讓觀眾避免令人沮喪的經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes enduring something unpleasant.","zh":"這個短語描述承受不愉快的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"shooting a good film","meaning":"拍攝一部好影片","examples":[{"en":"Shooting a good film is not just about technology.","zh":"拍攝一部好影片不只是關於科技。"},{"en":"Shooting a good film means filming a video or movie successfully and skilfully.","zh":"拍攝一部好影片，是指成功而有技巧地拍攝影片或電影。"},{"en":"Students shooting a good film need a clear story, steady camera work and patient editing.","zh":"學生拍攝一部好影片需要清楚故事、穩定鏡頭和耐心剪接。"},{"en":"Good equipment helps, but planning and patience often decide the final quality.","zh":"好設備有幫助，但規劃和耐性往往決定最終質素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of making a good video or movie.","zh":"這個短語描述製作好影片或電影的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"not just about","meaning":"不只是關於……","examples":[{"en":"Good photography is not just about technology.","zh":"好攝影不只是關於科技。"},{"en":"Not just about something means not limited to that one factor.","zh":"不只是關於某事，是指不只限於那一個因素。"},{"en":"Good writing is not just about vocabulary; it also needs clear ideas and organisation.","zh":"好寫作不只是關於詞彙；它也需要清楚想法和組織。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that a topic has more than one important element.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者一個主題有不止一個重要元素。"},{"en":"It introduces a broader understanding of something.","zh":"它引入對某事更廣泛的理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as in the case of","meaning":"正如……的情況","examples":[{"en":"Patience is required, as in the case of bats.","zh":"需要耐性，正如拍攝蝙蝠的情況。"},{"en":"As in the case of something means as shown by that particular example.","zh":"正如某事的情況，是指由該特定例子所顯示的一樣。"},{"en":"Good planning matters in exams, as in the case of IELTS writing.","zh":"良好規劃在考試中很重要，正如 IELTS 寫作的情況。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an example that supports the general point.","zh":"這個短語引入支持一般重點的例子。"},{"en":"It means the example shows the same idea.","zh":"它表示該例子顯示同一想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"small and dark-coloured","meaning":"體型細小且顏色深","examples":[{"en":"Bats are small and dark-coloured.","zh":"蝙蝠體型細小且顏色深。"},{"en":"Small and dark-coloured means little in size and having a dark appearance.","zh":"體型細小且顏色深，是指大小小而外觀顏色深。"},{"en":"A small and dark-coloured bird may be difficult to see at night.","zh":"體型細小且顏色深的鳥在夜間可能難以看見。"},{"en":"Bats are hard to film because their size and colour make them less visible.","zh":"蝙蝠難以拍攝，因為牠們的體型和顏色令牠們較不顯眼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical features that affect visibility.","zh":"這個短語描述影響可見度的身體特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"active only at night","meaning":"只在夜間活動","examples":[{"en":"Bats are active only at night.","zh":"蝙蝠只在夜間活動。"},{"en":"Active only at night means moving, feeding or hunting during nighttime rather than daytime.","zh":"只在夜間活動，是指在晚上而非白天移動、進食或捕獵。"},{"en":"Some animals are active only at night to avoid heat and predators.","zh":"有些動物只在夜間活動，以避開高溫和捕食者。"},{"en":"Night activity makes filming harder because there is less light.","zh":"夜間活動令拍攝更困難，因為光線較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes nocturnal behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述夜行行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"capture bats on film","meaning":"將蝙蝠拍攝下來","examples":[{"en":"Photographers need special equipment to capture bats on film.","zh":"攝影師需要特殊設備將蝙蝠拍攝下來。"},{"en":"To capture bats on film means to record bats in photographs or video.","zh":"將蝙蝠拍攝下來，是指用相片或影片記錄蝙蝠。"},{"en":"A wildlife researcher may capture bats on film as they leave a cave.","zh":"野生動物研究員可能在蝙蝠離開洞穴時將牠們拍攝下來。"},{"en":"Special equipment is needed because bats are fast, small and active in darkness.","zh":"需要特殊設備，因為蝙蝠快速、細小，而且在黑暗中活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes filming or photographing bats.","zh":"這個短語描述拍攝或錄影蝙蝠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"camera-triggering device","meaning":"相機觸發裝置","examples":[{"en":"A camera-triggering device can take pictures automatically.","zh":"相機觸發裝置可以自動拍照。"},{"en":"A camera-triggering device is equipment that makes a camera take a photo when something happens.","zh":"相機觸發裝置是在某事發生時令相機拍照的設備。"},{"en":"A wildlife camera may use a triggering device when an animal passes in front of it.","zh":"野外相機可能在動物經過前方時使用觸發裝置。"},{"en":"Triggering devices help photographers capture animals without standing there all night.","zh":"觸發裝置幫助攝影師捕捉動物，而不用整晚站在那裡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a tool that activates a camera.","zh":"這個短語描述啟動相機的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"place a camera near","meaning":"將相機放在……附近","examples":[{"en":"Photographers place a camera near the bat cave.","zh":"攝影師將相機放在蝙蝠洞附近。"},{"en":"To place a camera near something means to put it close to that location for filming or photography.","zh":"將相機放在某物附近，是指把相機放近該位置以拍攝或錄影。"},{"en":"A teacher may place a camera near the experiment table to record the reaction.","zh":"老師可能將相機放在實驗桌附近，記錄反應。"},{"en":"Correct placement matters because the subject must pass within the camera’s view.","zh":"正確位置很重要，因為拍攝對象必須經過相機視野。"},{"en":"This phrase describes positioning a camera close to a target area.","zh":"這個短語描述把相機放近目標區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"bat cave","meaning":"蝙蝠洞","examples":[{"en":"The camera is placed near the bat cave.","zh":"相機被放在蝙蝠洞附近。"},{"en":"A bat cave is a cave where bats live or gather.","zh":"蝙蝠洞是蝙蝠居住或聚集的洞穴。"},{"en":"Researchers may visit a bat cave at sunset to observe bats leaving to feed.","zh":"研究員可能在日落時到蝙蝠洞觀察蝙蝠外出覓食。"},{"en":"A bat cave is a good filming location because many bats pass through the entrance.","zh":"蝙蝠洞是良好拍攝地點，因為許多蝙蝠會經過入口。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a natural shelter used by bats.","zh":"這個短語指蝙蝠使用的自然庇護處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"on the path of","meaning":"在……的路徑上","examples":[{"en":"The camera is placed on the path of the flying bats.","zh":"相機被放在飛行蝙蝠的路徑上。"},{"en":"On the path of something means in the route where it is expected to move.","zh":"在某物的路徑上，是指位於它預期移動的路線上。"},{"en":"A photographer may stand on the path of a parade to take better photos.","zh":"攝影師可能站在巡遊路徑上，以拍攝更好相片。"},{"en":"Placing a camera on the animal’s path increases the chance of capturing it.","zh":"把相機放在動物路徑上，會增加捕捉牠的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being positioned along a route.","zh":"這個短語描述位於某條路線之上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be hard-wired to","meaning":"以線路連接到……","examples":[{"en":"The camera must be hard-wired to a triggering device.","zh":"相機必須以線路連接到觸發裝置。"},{"en":"To be hard-wired to something means to be physically connected to it with wires.","zh":"以線路連接到某物，是指用電線與它實體連接。"},{"en":"A school alarm may be hard-wired to the main security system.","zh":"學校警報器可能以線路連接到主要保安系統。"},{"en":"A wired connection can make the trigger faster and more reliable.","zh":"有線連接可以令觸發更快、更可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a direct electrical connection.","zh":"這個短語描述直接電線連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"triggering device","meaning":"觸發裝置","examples":[{"en":"The triggering device activates the camera automatically.","zh":"觸發裝置會自動啟動相機。"},{"en":"A triggering device is a tool that starts another device when a signal is detected.","zh":"觸發裝置是在偵測到信號時啟動另一裝置的工具。"},{"en":"A shop door may use a triggering device to open when a customer approaches.","zh":"商店門可能使用觸發裝置，在顧客接近時打開。"},{"en":"Triggering devices are useful when timing must be exact.","zh":"當時間必須準確，觸發裝置很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes equipment that causes an action to start.","zh":"這個短語描述引發行動開始的設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"break the triggering beam","meaning":"打斷觸發光束","examples":[{"en":"The camera fires when a bat breaks the triggering beam.","zh":"當蝙蝠打斷觸發光束時，相機就會拍攝。"},{"en":"To break the triggering beam means to pass through a light or sensor beam and interrupt it.","zh":"打斷觸發光束，是指穿過一束光或感應光束並中斷它。"},{"en":"A shop entrance sensor may activate when a customer breaks the beam.","zh":"當顧客打斷光束，商店入口感應器可能會啟動。"},{"en":"Breaking the beam tells the system that something has passed the target point.","zh":"打斷光束會告訴系統，有東西經過目標點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes interrupting a sensor signal.","zh":"這個短語描述中斷感應信號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the camera fires","meaning":"相機觸發拍攝","examples":[{"en":"The camera fires whenever a bat passes through the beam.","zh":"每當蝙蝠穿過光束，相機就會觸發拍攝。"},{"en":"The camera fires means the camera takes a photo or starts capturing an image.","zh":"相機觸發拍攝，是指相機拍照或開始捕捉影像。"},{"en":"At a finish line, the camera fires as soon as the runner crosses it.","zh":"在終點線上，跑手一越過終點，相機就會觸發拍攝。"},{"en":"Automatic firing is useful when the photographer cannot press the button at exactly the right moment.","zh":"當攝影師不能在準確時刻按下按鈕，自動觸發拍攝很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the camera being triggered to shoot.","zh":"這個短語描述相機被觸發進行拍攝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"keep doing so","meaning":"持續這樣做","examples":[{"en":"The camera will keep doing so through the night.","zh":"相機會整晚持續這樣做。"},{"en":"Keep doing so means continue doing the same action.","zh":"持續這樣做，是指繼續做同一個動作。"},{"en":"If students answer carefully and get good results, they should keep doing so.","zh":"如果學生仔細答題並取得好成績，他們應該持續這樣做。"},{"en":"The camera keeps taking pictures as long as bats continue to trigger it.","zh":"只要蝙蝠繼續觸發相機，相機就會持續拍照。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating the full action again.","zh":"這個短語避免再次重複完整動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"through the night","meaning":"整晚","examples":[{"en":"The camera continues shooting through the night.","zh":"相機整晚持續拍攝。"},{"en":"Through the night means during the whole night or for most of the night.","zh":"整晚，是指整個晚上或大部分晚上期間。"},{"en":"Nurses may monitor a patient through the night after surgery.","zh":"手術後，護士可能整晚監察病人。"},{"en":"Night-long recording is useful when animals are active while people sleep.","zh":"當動物在人睡覺時活動，整晚記錄就很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an action continuing overnight.","zh":"這個短語描述行動持續一整夜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the battery runs out","meaning":"電池耗盡","examples":[{"en":"The camera stops when the battery runs out.","zh":"電池耗盡時，相機就會停止。"},{"en":"The battery runs out means the battery has no power left.","zh":"電池耗盡，是指電池沒有剩餘電力。"},{"en":"A student’s phone may turn off if the battery runs out during a field trip.","zh":"學生在考察期間如果手機電池耗盡，手機可能關機。"},{"en":"When the battery runs out, automatic filming cannot continue.","zh":"當電池耗盡，自動拍攝就不能繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a device losing power.","zh":"這個短語描述裝置失去電力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"advanced triggering devices","meaning":"先進觸發裝置","examples":[{"en":"Advanced triggering devices allow unmanned shooting.","zh":"先進觸發裝置容許無人操作拍攝。"},{"en":"Advanced triggering devices are sophisticated tools that automatically activate cameras at the right moment.","zh":"先進觸發裝置是在正確時刻自動啟動相機的精密工具。"},{"en":"A wildlife team may use advanced triggering devices to film animals without disturbing them.","zh":"野生動物團隊可能使用先進觸發裝置，在不打擾動物的情況下拍攝牠們。"},{"en":"Better triggering devices reduce the need for human timing and constant attention.","zh":"較好的觸發裝置減少對人工掌握時機和長時間注意的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes high-level automatic camera controls.","zh":"這個短語描述高階自動相機控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"unmanned shooting","meaning":"無人操作拍攝","examples":[{"en":"Modern devices allow unmanned shooting.","zh":"現代裝置容許無人操作拍攝。"},{"en":"Unmanned shooting means filming or photographing without a person directly operating the camera.","zh":"無人操作拍攝，是指沒有人直接操作相機的拍攝或錄影。"},{"en":"A security camera uses unmanned shooting when it records an empty hallway overnight.","zh":"保安攝影機整晚記錄空走廊時，就是使用無人操作拍攝。"},{"en":"Unmanned shooting is useful when people cannot safely or patiently stay near the subject.","zh":"當人不能安全或耐心地留在拍攝對象附近，無人操作拍攝很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes automatic recording without human presence.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有人在場的自動記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"take several nights to","meaning":"可能需要幾晚去……","examples":[{"en":"It may take several nights to get a high-quality film.","zh":"取得高質素影片可能需要幾晚。"},{"en":"Take several nights to do something means need more than one night to finish or achieve it.","zh":"需要幾晚去做某事，是指需要超過一晚才能完成或達成它。"},{"en":"It may take several nights to observe a shy animal in the wild.","zh":"在野外觀察害羞動物可能需要幾晚。"},{"en":"Difficult filming can require repeated attempts before the right moment is captured.","zh":"困難拍攝可能需要反覆嘗試，才能捕捉正確瞬間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a task that needs multiple nights.","zh":"這個短語描述需要多個晚上完成的任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a truly high-quality film","meaning":"真正高質素的影片","examples":[{"en":"Photographers may need several nights to get a truly high-quality film.","zh":"攝影師可能需要幾晚才能取得真正高質素的影片。"},{"en":"A truly high-quality film is a film with clear images, good timing and useful content.","zh":"真正高質素的影片，是有清晰影像、良好時機和有用內容的影片。"},{"en":"A student project becomes a high-quality film when the sound, lighting and story all work well.","zh":"當聲音、燈光和故事都配合得好，學生專題就成為高質素影片。"},{"en":"Quality takes time because the best scenes may not happen on the first attempt.","zh":"質素需要時間，因為最佳場面未必第一次嘗試就出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a film that is genuinely well made.","zh":"這個短語描述真正製作良好的影片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"first pioneered","meaning":"最初被開創","examples":[{"en":"The technique was first pioneered around two hundred years ago.","zh":"這項技術大約二百年前最初被開創。"},{"en":"First pioneered means first developed or introduced by early innovators.","zh":"最初被開創，是指最早由創新者發展或引入。"},{"en":"Online learning was first pioneered by small groups before becoming common.","zh":"網上學習最初由小群體開創，後來才變得普遍。"},{"en":"A technique may look modern even if its basic idea was pioneered long ago.","zh":"一項技術可能看起來現代，即使其基本想法很久以前已被開創。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the earliest development of an idea or method.","zh":"這個短語描述想法或方法的最早發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"around two hundred years ago","meaning":"大約二百年前","examples":[{"en":"Photography was first pioneered around two hundred years ago.","zh":"攝影大約二百年前最初被開創。"},{"en":"Around two hundred years ago means approximately two centuries in the past.","zh":"大約二百年前，是指約兩個世紀以前。"},{"en":"A school building built around two hundred years ago may now be a heritage site.","zh":"大約二百年前建成的校舍現在可能是歷史建築。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate time, not an exact date.","zh":"這個短語給出近似時間，而不是精確日期。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rough historical period.","zh":"這個短語描述粗略歷史時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"develop to a state where","meaning":"發展到……的程度","examples":[{"en":"Photography has developed to a state where it is almost unrecognisable.","zh":"攝影已發展到幾乎難以辨認的程度。"},{"en":"To develop to a state where something happens means to change until that condition is reached.","zh":"發展到某種程度，是指逐漸改變直到達到該狀態。"},{"en":"A small school club may develop to a state where it becomes a city-wide competition.","zh":"小型學校學會可能發展到成為全市比賽的程度。"},{"en":"Long-term development can transform something so much that it no longer looks like its early form.","zh":"長期發展可以大幅改變某事，使它不再像早期形式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching a new condition through gradual change.","zh":"這個短語描述透過逐步變化達到新狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"almost unrecognisable","meaning":"幾乎難以辨認；面目全非","examples":[{"en":"Modern photography is almost unrecognisable compared with its early form.","zh":"與早期形式相比，現代攝影幾乎難以辨認。"},{"en":"Almost unrecognisable means changed so much that it is difficult to identify as the same thing.","zh":"幾乎難以辨認，是指改變太大，難以看出是同一事物。"},{"en":"After years of renovation, the old classroom looked almost unrecognisable.","zh":"經過多年翻新，舊課室看起來幾乎難以辨認。"},{"en":"Technology can change a field so deeply that its modern form looks completely different.","zh":"科技可以深刻改變一個領域，使其現代形式看起來完全不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extreme transformation.","zh":"這個短語描述極大轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be nothing like","meaning":"完全不像……","examples":[{"en":"The future of photography may be nothing like what we imagine.","zh":"攝影的未來可能完全不像我們所想像的。"},{"en":"To be nothing like something means to be completely different from it.","zh":"完全不像某事，是指與它完全不同。"},{"en":"University life may be nothing like what a secondary school student expects.","zh":"大學生活可能完全不像中學生所預期。"},{"en":"Fast technological change can make the future very different from today’s predictions.","zh":"快速科技變化可以令未來與今天的預測非常不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong contrast between expectation and reality.","zh":"這個短語描述期望與現實之間的強烈對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"what we imagine it to be","meaning":"我們想像中的樣子","examples":[{"en":"The future may be different from what we imagine it to be.","zh":"未來可能不同於我們想像中的樣子。"},{"en":"What we imagine it to be means the way we picture or expect something in our minds.","zh":"我們想像中的樣子，是我們在腦中描繪或預期某事的方式。"},{"en":"A new job may not be what we imagine it to be before starting.","zh":"新工作在開始前，可能並不是我們想像中的樣子。"},{"en":"Imagination can be wrong when new information or technology changes the situation.","zh":"當新資訊或科技改變情況，想像可能出錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes our mental expectation of something.","zh":"這個短語描述我們對某事的心理預期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"no matter what future it may hold","meaning":"不論它將來會怎樣","examples":[{"en":"No matter what future it may hold, photography will continue to develop.","zh":"不論攝影將來會怎樣，它都會繼續發展。"},{"en":"No matter what future it may hold means whatever happens to it in the future.","zh":"不論它將來會怎樣，是指無論未來發生甚麼。"},{"en":"No matter what future online learning may hold, students will still need discipline.","zh":"不論網上學習將來會怎樣，學生仍需要自律。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the main statement remains true despite uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語顯示即使未來不確定，主要說法仍成立。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing an unpredictable future.","zh":"它適合討論難以預測的未來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"continue to develop","meaning":"繼續發展","examples":[{"en":"Photography will continue to develop.","zh":"攝影會繼續發展。"},{"en":"To continue to develop means to keep changing, improving or becoming more advanced.","zh":"繼續發展，是指持續改變、改善或變得更先進。"},{"en":"A student’s writing will continue to develop if they read and practise regularly.","zh":"如果學生定期閱讀和練習，寫作會繼續發展。"},{"en":"A field continues to develop when new tools, ideas and needs appear.","zh":"當新工具、想法和需求出現，一個領域就會繼續發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing growth or progress.","zh":"這個短語描述持續成長或進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"repeatedly demonstrated","meaning":"反覆證明","examples":[{"en":"Photography has repeatedly demonstrated its value in our lives.","zh":"攝影已反覆證明它在我們生活中的價值。"},{"en":"Repeatedly demonstrated means shown many times through examples or results.","zh":"反覆證明，是指透過例子或結果多次顯示。"},{"en":"A student who improves in every test has repeatedly demonstrated hard work.","zh":"每次測驗都有進步的學生反覆證明了自己的努力。"},{"en":"When a tool is useful in many situations, its value is demonstrated again and again.","zh":"當工具在許多情況中有用，它的價值就一次又一次被證明。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence shown more than once.","zh":"這個短語描述不止一次顯示出來的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"in many aspects of our lives","meaning":"在我們生活的許多方面","examples":[{"en":"Photography is useful in many aspects of our lives.","zh":"攝影在我們生活的許多方面都有用。"},{"en":"In many aspects of our lives means in many different parts of daily life.","zh":"在我們生活的許多方面，是指在日常生活中許多不同部分。"},{"en":"Mobile phones are useful in many aspects of our lives, including communication, travel and study.","zh":"手機在我們生活的許多方面都有用，包括溝通、出行和學習。"},{"en":"Photography matters because it supports memory, science, art, security and entertainment.","zh":"攝影重要，因為它支援記憶、科學、藝術、安全和娛樂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad usefulness across life areas.","zh":"這個短語描述跨生活領域的廣泛用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a picture is worth a thousand words","meaning":"一圖勝千言","examples":[{"en":"The saying reminds us that a picture is worth a thousand words.","zh":"這句話提醒我們，一圖勝千言。"},{"en":"A picture is worth a thousand words means one image can communicate a lot of meaning quickly.","zh":"一圖勝千言，是指一張影像可以快速傳達大量意思。"},{"en":"A photo of a flooded street may explain the damage better than a long report.","zh":"一張水浸街道的相片，可能比長篇報告更能說明損害。"},{"en":"Images can be powerful because they show details and emotions immediately.","zh":"影像很有力量，因為它們能即時展示細節和情感。"},{"en":"This phrase praises the communicative power of images.","zh":"這個短語讚揚影像的傳意力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"look at the following organisms","meaning":"查看以下生物","examples":[{"en":"Students look at the following organisms and match them with features.","zh":"學生查看以下生物，並把它們與特徵配對。"},{"en":"Look at the following organisms means examine the list of living things given below.","zh":"查看以下生物，是指檢視下面列出的生命體。"},{"en":"In a biology task, students may look at the following organisms: frog, bat and hummingbird.","zh":"在生物題中，學生可能查看以下生物：青蛙、蝙蝠和蜂鳥。"},{"en":"Students need to read each organism carefully before matching it to the correct information.","zh":"學生需要仔細閱讀每種生物，再配對正確資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"list of features","meaning":"特徵列表","examples":[{"en":"The question provides a list of features.","zh":"題目提供一個特徵列表。"},{"en":"A list of features is a set of characteristics or details to choose from.","zh":"特徵列表是一組可選擇的特徵或細節。"},{"en":"A reading question may give a list of features such as “fast wings” and “elastic tongue”.","zh":"閱讀題可能提供特徵列表，例如「快速翅膀」和「有彈性的舌頭」。"},{"en":"Students must compare each feature with the passage before choosing an answer.","zh":"學生必須先把每項特徵與篇章比較，然後才選答案。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the answer options in a matching task.","zh":"這個短語指配對題中的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"match each organism with","meaning":"將每種生物與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Students must match each organism with the correct feature.","zh":"學生必須將每種生物與正確特徵配對。"},{"en":"To match each organism with something means to connect every living thing to the right description.","zh":"將每種生物與某物配對，是指把每種生命體連接到正確描述。"},{"en":"A student may match “frog” with “elastic tongue” after reading the passage.","zh":"學生讀完篇章後，可能把「青蛙」與「有彈性的舌頭」配對。"},{"en":"Matching requires checking details rather than guessing from general knowledge.","zh":"配對需要檢查細節，而不是憑常識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a classification task.","zh":"這個短語描述分類任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the correct feature","meaning":"正確特徵","examples":[{"en":"Each organism should be matched with the correct feature.","zh":"每種生物應與正確特徵配對。"},{"en":"The correct feature is the characteristic that accurately belongs to the organism.","zh":"正確特徵，是準確屬於該生物的特徵。"},{"en":"If the passage says bats are active at night, “active only at night” is the correct feature.","zh":"如果篇章說蝙蝠只在夜間活動，「只在夜間活動」就是正確特徵。"},{"en":"Choosing the correct feature shows that the student understood the specific detail.","zh":"選擇正確特徵顯示學生理解了具體細節。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the right descriptive characteristic.","zh":"這個短語指正確的描述性特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"too fast to be perceived","meaning":"快得無法被察覺","examples":[{"en":"Some movements are too fast to be perceived.","zh":"有些動作快得無法被察覺。"},{"en":"Too fast to be perceived means happening so quickly that people cannot notice it clearly.","zh":"快得無法被察覺，是指發生得太快，人們不能清楚注意到。"},{"en":"A frog’s tongue strike may be too fast to be perceived without a high-speed camera.","zh":"青蛙舌頭出擊若沒有高速攝影機，可能快得無法被察覺。"},{"en":"When movement is too fast to be perceived, special recording makes it visible.","zh":"當動作快得無法被察覺，特殊錄影能令它變得可見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes motion beyond normal human perception.","zh":"這個短語描述超越正常人類感知的動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"position the camera where","meaning":"將相機放在……的位置","examples":[{"en":"Photographers position the camera where the animal will pass.","zh":"攝影師將相機放在動物會經過的位置。"},{"en":"To position the camera where something will happen means to place it in the best location for recording.","zh":"將相機放在某事會發生的位置，是指把它放在最適合記錄的地點。"},{"en":"A teacher may position the camera where all students can be seen during a performance.","zh":"老師可能將相機放在能看見所有學生表演的位置。"},{"en":"Good positioning increases the chance of capturing the right moment.","zh":"良好位置增加捕捉正確瞬間的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing the camera’s location carefully.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細選擇相機位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"too slow to be visible to human eyes","meaning":"慢得肉眼看不見","examples":[{"en":"Some processes are too slow to be visible to human eyes.","zh":"有些過程慢得肉眼看不見。"},{"en":"Too slow to be visible to human eyes means changing so gradually that people cannot see it directly.","zh":"慢得肉眼看不見，是指變化太逐漸，人們不能直接看見。"},{"en":"A seed growing into a plant is too slow to be visible to human eyes moment by moment.","zh":"種子長成植物的過程逐刻來看慢得肉眼看不見。"},{"en":"Time-lapse photography helps by making slow change appear faster.","zh":"縮時攝影透過令緩慢變化看起來更快來幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual processes that ordinary sight cannot follow.","zh":"這個短語描述普通視力無法追蹤的逐漸過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"adjust the filming speed","meaning":"調整拍攝或影片速度","examples":[{"en":"Editors adjust the filming speed to make the video interesting.","zh":"剪接師調整影片速度，使影片更有趣。"},{"en":"To adjust the filming speed means to change how fast the footage appears in the final video.","zh":"調整拍攝或影片速度，是指改變最終影片中片段看起來的快慢。"},{"en":"A student editor may adjust the filming speed so a long experiment does not feel boring.","zh":"學生剪接師可能調整影片速度，令長實驗不會顯得沉悶。"},{"en":"Speed adjustment helps viewers focus on important actions while skipping unnecessary waiting.","zh":"速度調整幫助觀眾專注重要動作，同時跳過不必要等待。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing video pace for clarity or interest.","zh":"這個短語描述為清晰或趣味而改變影片節奏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the summary below","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary below with words from the passage.","zh":"學生用篇章中的字詞完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"Complete the summary below means fill in the missing parts of a short summary.","zh":"完成以下摘要，是指填上短摘要中的缺失部分。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete the summary by finding exact words in the text.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過在文本中找出準確字詞來完成摘要。"},{"en":"This task checks whether students understand both meaning and wording.","zh":"這項任務檢查學生是否理解意思和措辭。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不超過三個字","examples":[{"en":"Students should write no more than three words for each answer.","zh":"學生每個答案應寫不超過三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"不超過三個字，是指答案必須包含三個或以下英文詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “high frame rate,” it follows the rule because it has three words.","zh":"如果答案是 “high frame rate”，它符合規則，因為有三個詞。"},{"en":"Writing four words may be marked wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫四個詞也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the most common techniques of","meaning":"最常見的……技巧","examples":[{"en":"Fast motion and slow motion are among the most common techniques of photography.","zh":"快動作和慢動作是攝影中最常見的技巧之一。"},{"en":"The most common techniques of something are the methods most often used in that field.","zh":"最常見的某種技巧，是該領域中最常使用的方法。"},{"en":"Skimming and scanning are among the most common techniques of reading exams.","zh":"略讀和掃讀是閱讀考試中最常見的技巧之一。"},{"en":"Common techniques become popular because they solve frequent problems effectively.","zh":"常見技巧會流行，是因為它們有效解決常見問題。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces widely used methods in a subject.","zh":"這個短語引入某學科中廣泛使用的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"present a naturally slow process","meaning":"呈現自然緩慢的過程","examples":[{"en":"Photographers use time-lapse photography to present a naturally slow process.","zh":"攝影師使用縮時攝影呈現自然緩慢的過程。"},{"en":"To present a naturally slow process means to show a process that normally happens gradually.","zh":"呈現自然緩慢的過程，是指展示通常逐漸發生的過程。"},{"en":"A science video may present a naturally slow process, such as bread rising.","zh":"科學影片可能呈現自然緩慢的過程，例如麵包發酵膨脹。"},{"en":"Time-lapse makes slow processes easier to understand by speeding them up.","zh":"縮時攝影透過加速緩慢過程，使它們更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes showing gradual change clearly.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚展示逐漸變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"shown on screen in sequence","meaning":"按順序在螢幕上播放","examples":[{"en":"The pictures are shown on screen in sequence.","zh":"這些圖片按順序在螢幕上播放。"},{"en":"Shown on screen in sequence means displayed one after another in the correct order.","zh":"按順序在螢幕上播放，是指以正確次序一張接一張顯示。"},{"en":"A slideshow of a school trip may be shown on screen in sequence from morning to evening.","zh":"學校旅行投影片可能按順序在螢幕上播放，從早上到晚上。"},{"en":"Correct sequence helps viewers understand how an event develops over time.","zh":"正確次序幫助觀眾理解事件如何隨時間發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordered visual presentation.","zh":"這個短語描述有順序的視覺呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"normal motion picture rate","meaning":"正常電影播放速度","examples":[{"en":"The images are shown at a normal motion picture rate.","zh":"這些影像以正常電影播放速度顯示。"},{"en":"Normal motion picture rate means the usual speed at which film frames are shown.","zh":"正常電影播放速度，是電影畫格顯示的一般速度。"},{"en":"A cinema film is usually shown at a normal motion picture rate so movement looks natural.","zh":"電影院電影通常以正常電影播放速度播放，使動作看起來自然。"},{"en":"When time-lapse photos are shown at this rate, slow events appear faster than real life.","zh":"當縮時相片以這個速度顯示，緩慢事件會看起來比現實更快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the standard playback speed for film.","zh":"這個短語描述電影的標準播放速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"faster than what it naturally is","meaning":"比自然狀態更快","examples":[{"en":"The process appears faster than what it naturally is.","zh":"這個過程看起來比自然狀態更快。"},{"en":"Faster than what it naturally is means quicker on screen than in real life.","zh":"比自然狀態更快，是指在螢幕上比現實生活中更快。"},{"en":"A flower opening may appear faster than what it naturally is in a time-lapse video.","zh":"花朵盛開在縮時影片中可能看起來比自然狀態更快。"},{"en":"This effect happens because long intervals are compressed into a short sequence.","zh":"這種效果出現，是因為長時間間隔被壓縮成短序列。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an artificial increase in apparent speed.","zh":"這個短語描述表面速度被人為提高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"On the other hand, high-speed photography shows fast movement slowly.","zh":"另一方面，高速攝影以慢速展示快速動作。"},{"en":"On the other hand introduces a contrasting point or different side of an issue.","zh":"另一方面，用來引入對比重點或事情的另一面。"},{"en":"Time-lapse speeds slow events; on the other hand, high-speed photography slows fast ones.","zh":"縮時攝影加速慢事件；另一方面，高速攝影放慢快事件。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers compare two opposite techniques.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者比較兩種相反技巧。"},{"en":"It signals contrast.","zh":"它表示對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"demonstrate how fast things move","meaning":"展示事物移動得有多快","examples":[{"en":"High-speed photography can demonstrate how fast things move.","zh":"高速攝影可以展示事物移動得有多快。"},{"en":"To demonstrate how fast things move means to show the speed of movement clearly.","zh":"展示事物移動得有多快，是指清楚顯示動作速度。"},{"en":"A science video can demonstrate how fast a rubber band snaps back.","zh":"科學影片可以展示橡筋彈回得有多快。"},{"en":"Slow-motion replay makes speed easier to understand because viewers can see each stage.","zh":"慢動作重播令速度更容易理解，因為觀眾可以看見每個階段。"},{"en":"This phrase describes showing movement speed through evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述透過證據展示動作速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be exposed on","meaning":"曝光於；拍攝在……上","examples":[{"en":"The movement is exposed on a longer sequence of film.","zh":"這個動作被拍攝在較長的影片序列上。"},{"en":"To be exposed on film means to be recorded by light reaching the camera film or sensor.","zh":"曝光於影片上，是指由光線到達相機底片或感光元件而被記錄。"},{"en":"A moving car may be exposed on several frames during a high-speed recording.","zh":"一輛移動中的汽車可能在高速錄影中被拍攝在多個畫格上。"},{"en":"More exposure frames allow movement to be stretched out in playback.","zh":"更多曝光畫格使動作能在播放時被拉長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement being captured in recorded images.","zh":"這個短語描述動作被捕捉在錄製影像中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"normal playback speed","meaning":"正常播放速度","examples":[{"en":"The film is projected at normal playback speed.","zh":"影片以正常播放速度投射。"},{"en":"Normal playback speed is the usual speed used when showing recorded video.","zh":"正常播放速度，是展示錄像時使用的一般速度。"},{"en":"A lecture recording at normal playback speed sounds like the teacher’s real speaking speed.","zh":"講座錄影以正常播放速度播放時，聽起來像老師真實說話速度。"},{"en":"High-speed footage shown at normal playback speed makes fast events appear slower.","zh":"高速片段以正常播放速度顯示，會令快速事件看起來更慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordinary viewing speed after recording.","zh":"這個短語描述錄製後的普通觀看速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"contain the following information","meaning":"包含以下資料","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which paragraph contains the following information.","zh":"學生辨認哪一段包含以下資料。"},{"en":"To contain the following information means to include the details listed below.","zh":"包含以下資料，是指包括下面列出的細節。"},{"en":"A paragraph may contain the following information about why bats are difficult to film.","zh":"某一段可能包含關於蝙蝠為何難拍攝的以下資料。"},{"en":"This task requires students to locate ideas, not just match exact words.","zh":"這項任務要求學生定位想法，而不只是配對完全相同的字。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in paragraph-matching questions.","zh":"這個短語用於段落配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"photography’s application in various fields","meaning":"攝影在不同領域的應用","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes photography’s application in various fields.","zh":"篇章描述攝影在不同領域的應用。"},{"en":"Photography’s application in various fields means the ways photography is used in different areas of life or work.","zh":"攝影在不同領域的應用，是指攝影在生活或工作不同範疇中的使用方式。"},{"en":"Photography has applications in education, science, medicine, security and family life.","zh":"攝影在教育、科學、醫學、安全和家庭生活中都有應用。"},{"en":"A tool becomes valuable when it can be applied across many fields.","zh":"當工具能應用於許多領域，它就變得有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad practical uses of photography.","zh":"這個短語描述攝影廣泛的實際用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"have a significant role in","meaning":"在……中有重要作用","examples":[{"en":"High-speed photography has a significant role in biology.","zh":"高速攝影在生物學中有重要作用。"},{"en":"To have a significant role in something means to be important in that area or process.","zh":"在某事中有重要作用，是指在該範疇或過程中很重要。"},{"en":"Practice has a significant role in improving speaking fluency.","zh":"練習在改善口語流暢度中有重要作用。"},{"en":"High-speed photography is important in biology because it reveals movement that scientists cannot otherwise study clearly.","zh":"高速攝影在生物學中重要，因為它揭示科學家否則無法清楚研究的動作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaningful importance within a field.","zh":"這個短語描述在某領域中的有意義重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"traditional wisdom","meaning":"傳統智慧；老話","examples":[{"en":"The passage ends with a piece of traditional wisdom about pictures.","zh":"篇章以一句關於圖像的傳統智慧作結。"},{"en":"Traditional wisdom is an old saying or widely accepted idea passed down over time.","zh":"傳統智慧是流傳下來的老話或廣泛接受的想法。"},{"en":"“Practice makes perfect” is a piece of traditional wisdom often used in schools.","zh":"「熟能生巧」是學校常用的一句傳統智慧。"},{"en":"Traditional wisdom can make a conclusion memorable because readers already recognise it.","zh":"傳統智慧能令結論令人難忘，因為讀者已熟悉它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a familiar old belief or saying.","zh":"這個短語描述熟悉的古老信念或說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"assure readers of","meaning":"令讀者相信……","examples":[{"en":"The saying assures readers of the prospects of photography.","zh":"這句話令讀者相信攝影的前景。"},{"en":"To assure readers of something means to make readers feel confident about it.","zh":"令讀者相信某事，是指使讀者對它有信心。"},{"en":"A school report may assure parents of the safety of a new campus plan.","zh":"學校報告可能令家長相信新校園計劃的安全性。"},{"en":"Writers assure readers by giving a strong conclusion or familiar example.","zh":"作者透過強而有力的結論或熟悉例子令讀者安心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving confidence or reassurance.","zh":"這個短語描述給予信心或保證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the prospects of photography","meaning":"攝影的前景","examples":[{"en":"The final paragraph discusses the prospects of photography.","zh":"最後一段討論攝影的前景。"},{"en":"The prospects of photography means the future possibilities and likely development of photography.","zh":"攝影的前景，是指攝影未來的可能性和可能發展。"},{"en":"A technology magazine may discuss the prospects of photography in medicine and education.","zh":"科技雜誌可能討論攝影在醫學和教育中的前景。"},{"en":"New cameras and editing tools suggest photography will keep changing.","zh":"新相機和剪接工具顯示攝影會繼續變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what photography may become in the future.","zh":"這個短語描述攝影未來可能變成甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be processed before final release","meaning":"在正式發佈前經過處理","examples":[{"en":"The film is processed before final release.","zh":"影片在正式發佈前經過處理。"},{"en":"To be processed before final release means to be edited, adjusted or prepared before being shown publicly.","zh":"在正式發佈前經過處理，是指在公開展示前被剪接、調整或準備。"},{"en":"A school video may be processed before final release so mistakes can be removed.","zh":"學校影片可能在正式發佈前經過處理，以移除錯誤。"},{"en":"Processing improves quality by correcting speed, sound, colour or sequence.","zh":"處理可以透過修正速度、聲音、顏色或次序來提升質素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparation before publication or viewing.","zh":"這個短語描述出版或觀看前的準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"filming without human effort","meaning":"無需人手操作的拍攝","examples":[{"en":"Advanced devices make filming without human effort possible.","zh":"先進裝置令無需人手操作的拍攝成為可能。"},{"en":"Filming without human effort means recording video automatically without a person controlling each shot.","zh":"無需人手操作的拍攝，是指自動錄影，而不用人控制每個鏡頭。"},{"en":"A security camera films without human effort when it records movement at night.","zh":"保安攝影機夜間記錄動作時，就是無需人手操作地拍攝。"},{"en":"Automatic filming is useful when the subject appears unpredictably or at inconvenient times.","zh":"當拍攝對象不可預測或在不方便時間出現，自動拍攝很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes camera work done by devices rather than by direct human action.","zh":"這個短語描述由裝置而非人直接操作完成的拍攝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 40 - High speed photography.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 41":[{"front":"source of knowledge","meaning":"知識來源","examples":[{"en":"Medicine is used as an example to explore different sources of knowledge.","zh":"醫學被用作例子，以探討不同知識來源。"},{"en":"A source of knowledge is where information, understanding, or evidence comes from.","zh":"source of knowledge 是資訊、理解或證據的來源。"},{"en":"A student’s source of knowledge may be a textbook, a teacher, an experiment, or personal experience.","zh":"學生的知識來源可以是教科書、老師、實驗或個人經驗。"},{"en":"Different sources of knowledge can lead people to trust some claims more than others.","zh":"不同知識來源可以令人較信任某些說法，而較不信任另一些。"},{"en":"The phrase helps students ask where a belief comes from and why it should be trusted.","zh":"這個短語幫助學生追問一個信念從何而來，以及為何值得信任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what counts as knowledge","meaning":"甚麼算是知識","examples":[{"en":"The passage asks what counts as knowledge in the field of medicine.","zh":"文章問在醫學領域中甚麼算是知識。"},{"en":"What counts as knowledge means what should be accepted as real, reliable knowledge.","zh":"what counts as knowledge 指甚麼應被接受為真正可靠的知識。"},{"en":"In science class, students ask what counts as knowledge when they compare guesses with experiment results.","zh":"在科學課中，學生比較猜測和實驗結果時，就是在問甚麼算是知識。"},{"en":"A claim may not count as knowledge if it has no evidence behind it.","zh":"如果一項聲稱背後沒有證據，它可能不算是知識。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when people are deciding whether information is trustworthy enough.","zh":"當人們判斷資訊是否足夠可信時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the status of","meaning":"……的地位","examples":[{"en":"The passage explores the status of different kinds of knowledge.","zh":"文章探討不同種類知識的地位。"},{"en":"The status of something is its level of importance, authority, or acceptance.","zh":"the status of 某事，是它的重要性、權威性或被接受程度。"},{"en":"In a school, the status of exam results may be higher than casual comments from classmates.","zh":"在學校中，考試結果的地位可能高於同學的隨口評論。"},{"en":"A source gains status when people believe it is accurate and professionally recognised.","zh":"當人們相信某來源準確且受專業認可，它的地位就會提高。"},{"en":"The phrase helps compare how seriously different things are treated.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較不同事物被多認真看待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"different kinds of knowledge","meaning":"不同種類的知識","examples":[{"en":"Different kinds of knowledge may have different levels of authority.","zh":"不同種類的知識可能有不同權威程度。"},{"en":"Different kinds of knowledge are different ways of knowing, such as personal experience, expert training, or scientific evidence.","zh":"different kinds of knowledge 是不同的認知方式，例如個人經驗、專家訓練或科學證據。"},{"en":"A patient’s pain is one kind of knowledge, while a doctor’s test result is another.","zh":"病人的疼痛是一種知識，而醫生的檢查結果是另一種。"},{"en":"People may disagree because they rely on different kinds of knowledge.","zh":"人們可能因依賴不同種類的知識而意見不合。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds students that not all knowledge comes from the same place.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生，不是所有知識都來自同一地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"explore these questions","meaning":"探討這些問題","examples":[{"en":"The passage explores these questions through the example of medicine.","zh":"文章透過醫學這個例子探討這些問題。"},{"en":"To explore these questions means to examine them carefully from different angles.","zh":"explore these questions 指從不同角度仔細檢視這些問題。"},{"en":"A teacher may explore these questions by asking students to compare personal opinion with evidence.","zh":"老師可能透過要求學生比較個人意見與證據，探討這些問題。"},{"en":"Exploring questions can reveal that a simple issue is more complicated than it first seems.","zh":"探討問題可以揭示一個簡單議題比起初看來更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious investigation rather than quick answering.","zh":"這個短語描述認真的探究，而不是快速回答。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"集中於；聚焦於","examples":[{"en":"The writer focuses on one particular area of knowledge.","zh":"作者聚焦於某一特定知識範疇。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give attention mainly to that thing.","zh":"focus on 某事，指主要把注意力放在該事上。"},{"en":"A student may focus on grammar first if sentence mistakes are hurting her writing score.","zh":"如果句子錯誤影響寫作分數，學生可能先集中於文法。"},{"en":"Focusing on one area can make a discussion clearer and more detailed.","zh":"聚焦於一個範疇可以令討論更清楚、更詳細。"},{"en":"The phrase describes narrowing attention to a chosen topic.","zh":"這個短語描述把注意力收窄到選定主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one particular area of knowledge","meaning":"某一特定知識範疇","examples":[{"en":"Medicine is one particular area of knowledge discussed in the passage.","zh":"醫學是文章中討論的某一特定知識範疇。"},{"en":"One particular area of knowledge means one specific field where people study, learn, or make claims.","zh":"one particular area of knowledge 指人們研究、學習或提出主張的一個特定領域。"},{"en":"History is one particular area of knowledge, while biology is another.","zh":"歷史是一個特定知識範疇，而生物學是另一個。"},{"en":"Choosing one particular area of knowledge helps writers avoid discussing everything at once.","zh":"選擇某一特定知識範疇，可以幫助作者避免一次討論所有事情。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a focused field rather than knowledge in general.","zh":"這個短語指向一個聚焦領域，而不是泛指知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"medicine","meaning":"醫學","examples":[{"en":"Medicine is used to examine how people know they are ill.","zh":"醫學被用來檢視人們如何知道自己生病。"},{"en":"Medicine is the field concerned with health, illness, diagnosis, treatment, and prevention.","zh":"medicine 是關於健康、疾病、診斷、治療和預防的領域。"},{"en":"A student may study medicine if she wants to become a doctor and treat patients.","zh":"如果學生想成為醫生並治療病人，她可能修讀醫學。"},{"en":"Medicine relies on both scientific evidence and practical experience with patients.","zh":"醫學同時依賴科學證據和處理病人的實際經驗。"},{"en":"The word can refer to the medical field, not only to pills or drugs.","zh":"這個詞可以指醫學領域，而不只是藥丸或藥物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"seem to be an absurd question","meaning":"似乎是荒謬的問題","examples":[{"en":"Asking how you know when you are ill may seem to be an absurd question.","zh":"問你如何知道自己生病，似乎是荒謬的問題。"},{"en":"To seem to be an absurd question means to appear silly, pointless, or too obvious to ask.","zh":"seem to be an absurd question 指看起來愚蠢、無意義或太明顯而不用問。"},{"en":"Asking why people need sleep may seem to be an absurd question until science explains how complex sleep is.","zh":"問人為何需要睡眠可能似乎是荒謬的問題，直到科學解釋睡眠有多複雜。"},{"en":"A question can seem absurd at first but become useful when people examine it carefully.","zh":"一個問題起初可以看似荒謬，但仔細檢視後可能變得有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an idea that looks foolish before deeper thinking begins.","zh":"這個短語描述一個在深入思考前看似愚蠢的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"feel ill","meaning":"感到不適；覺得自己病了","examples":[{"en":"You may believe you are ill because you feel ill.","zh":"你可能因為感到不適而相信自己生病。"},{"en":"To feel ill means to feel physically unwell or sick.","zh":"feel ill 指感到身體不舒服或生病。"},{"en":"A student may feel ill after waking up with a headache and sore throat.","zh":"學生早上醒來頭痛和喉嚨痛後，可能感到不適。"},{"en":"Feeling ill often leads people to rest, seek advice, or visit a doctor.","zh":"感到不適常會令人休息、尋求意見或看醫生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a personal bodily feeling, not a confirmed diagnosis.","zh":"這個短語描述個人的身體感覺，而不是已確認的診斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"your body tells you that","meaning":"你的身體告訴你……","examples":[{"en":"Your body tells you that something may be wrong.","zh":"你的身體告訴你可能有些地方出問題。"},{"en":"Your body tells you that means physical feelings give you a sign or warning.","zh":"your body tells you that 指身體感覺給你一個信號或警告。"},{"en":"If your body tells you that you are exhausted, you may need sleep rather than more coffee.","zh":"如果你的身體告訴你已筋疲力盡，你可能需要睡眠，而不是更多咖啡。"},{"en":"People often notice illness first because the body sends signals such as pain or tiredness.","zh":"人們常最先因身體發出疼痛或疲倦等信號而注意到疾病。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bodily experience acting like information.","zh":"這個短語描述身體經驗像資訊一樣發揮作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pain or discomfort","meaning":"疼痛或不適","examples":[{"en":"You may know that you feel pain or discomfort.","zh":"你可能知道自己感到疼痛或不適。"},{"en":"Pain or discomfort means physical suffering, soreness, pressure, or an unpleasant bodily feeling.","zh":"pain or discomfort 指身體痛楚、酸痛、壓迫感或令人不舒服的身體感覺。"},{"en":"A worker may feel pain or discomfort after sitting at a desk for too many hours.","zh":"工人坐在書桌前太多小時後，可能感到疼痛或不適。"},{"en":"Pain or discomfort can push people to change habits or seek medical advice.","zh":"疼痛或不適可以促使人改變習慣或尋求醫療意見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bodily signs that something may not be right.","zh":"這個短語描述身體可能有問題的跡象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a little more complex","meaning":"稍為複雜","examples":[{"en":"Knowing that you are ill is a little more complex.","zh":"知道自己生病這件事稍為複雜。"},{"en":"A little more complex means slightly harder to understand than it first appears.","zh":"a little more complex 指比起初看來稍微更難理解。"},{"en":"Choosing a school is a little more complex than simply picking the nearest one.","zh":"選擇學校比單純選最近的一間稍為複雜。"},{"en":"A situation becomes more complex when several causes or types of evidence are involved.","zh":"當涉及多個原因或多種證據時，情況會變得更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase gently warns readers that the issue is not as simple as it seems.","zh":"這個短語溫和地提醒讀者，問題並沒有表面看來那麼簡單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at times","meaning":"有時候","examples":[{"en":"At times, people experience symptoms without having a serious illness.","zh":"有時候，人們會出現症狀，但並沒有嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"At times means sometimes or on some occasions.","zh":"at times 指有時或在某些情況下。"},{"en":"At times, students feel stressed even when they have prepared well.","zh":"有時候，即使準備充分，學生仍會感到壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something happens occasionally, not always.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事偶爾發生，而不是永遠發生。"},{"en":"It helps writers avoid making an overgeneralised statement.","zh":"它幫助作者避免作出過度概括的陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"experience symptoms of illness","meaning":"出現疾病症狀","examples":[{"en":"People may experience symptoms of illness when they are simply tired.","zh":"人們只是疲倦時，也可能出現疾病症狀。"},{"en":"To experience symptoms of illness means to feel signs that seem connected with being sick.","zh":"experience symptoms of illness 指感到似乎與生病有關的跡象。"},{"en":"A person may experience symptoms of illness such as coughing, fever, or unusual tiredness.","zh":"一個人可能出現咳嗽、發燒或異常疲倦等疾病症狀。"},{"en":"Symptoms may lead someone to worry, but they do not always prove a serious disease.","zh":"症狀可能令人擔心，但不一定證明有嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"The phrase describes feeling bodily signs that may need interpretation.","zh":"這個短語描述出現需要詮釋的身體跡象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, they may simply be tired or overworked.","zh":"事實上，他們可能只是疲倦或工作過勞。"},{"en":"In fact introduces information that corrects, clarifies, or strengthens the previous idea.","zh":"in fact 引出修正、澄清或加強前一想法的資訊。"},{"en":"A student may think she is bad at English; in fact, she may just need more reading practice.","zh":"學生可能以為自己英文差；事實上，她可能只是需要更多閱讀練習。"},{"en":"Writers use in fact when the next sentence gives a more accurate explanation.","zh":"當下一句給出更準確解釋，作者會使用 in fact。"},{"en":"The phrase often shows that the truth is different from the first guess.","zh":"這個短語常顯示真相與最初猜測不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tired or overworked","meaning":"疲倦或工作過勞","examples":[{"en":"Some people feel ill because they are tired or overworked.","zh":"有些人因疲倦或工作過勞而覺得自己病了。"},{"en":"Tired or overworked means physically or mentally exhausted because of too much activity, study, or work.","zh":"tired or overworked 指因太多活動、學習或工作而身心疲憊。"},{"en":"A nurse may feel tired or overworked after several long night shifts.","zh":"護士連續幾個漫長夜班後，可能感到疲倦或工作過勞。"},{"en":"Being tired or overworked can create symptoms that resemble illness.","zh":"疲倦或工作過勞可以造成像疾病一樣的症狀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes exhaustion rather than necessarily a disease.","zh":"這個短語描述疲憊，而不一定是疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have a hangover","meaning":"宿醉","examples":[{"en":"Some people may feel unwell because they have a hangover.","zh":"有些人可能因宿醉而感到不適。"},{"en":"To have a hangover means to feel ill after drinking too much alcohol, often with headache or nausea.","zh":"have a hangover 指飲酒過量後感到不舒服，常伴有頭痛或噁心。"},{"en":"A person may have a hangover the morning after a party.","zh":"一個人可能在派對翌日早上宿醉。"},{"en":"A hangover can make someone mistake temporary discomfort for a more serious illness.","zh":"宿醉可以令人把暫時不適誤以為是較嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the after-effect of alcohol, not a medical diagnosis by itself.","zh":"這個短語描述酒精帶來的後續反應，本身不是醫學診斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"suffer from a disease","meaning":"患上疾病","examples":[{"en":"People may suffer from a disease without realising it immediately.","zh":"人們可能患上疾病而沒有立即意識到。"},{"en":"To suffer from a disease means to have an illness that affects the body or mind.","zh":"suffer from a disease 指患有影響身體或心理的疾病。"},{"en":"A person may suffer from diabetes for some time before noticing clear signs.","zh":"一個人可能患糖尿病一段時間後才注意到明顯跡象。"},{"en":"Some diseases develop quietly, so people may not know they are ill at first.","zh":"有些疾病靜靜發展，所以人們起初未必知道自己生病。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being affected by a medical condition.","zh":"這個短語描述受某醫療狀況影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fail to become aware of","meaning":"未能察覺……","examples":[{"en":"Some patients fail to become aware of the illness until later.","zh":"有些病人直到後來才未能察覺疾病。"},{"en":"To fail to become aware of something means not to notice or understand it when it first happens.","zh":"fail to become aware of 某事，指在它起初發生時沒有注意到或理解它。"},{"en":"A student may fail to become aware of a deadline if she does not check school email.","zh":"如果學生不查看學校電郵，可能未能察覺截止日期。"},{"en":"People may fail to notice illness when symptoms are mild or easy to explain away.","zh":"當症狀輕微或容易用其他原因解釋，人們可能未能察覺疾病。"},{"en":"The phrase describes delayed awareness.","zh":"這個短語描述延遲察覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reach a late stage","meaning":"發展到晚期","examples":[{"en":"An illness may reach a late stage before the patient notices it.","zh":"疾病可能在病人注意到之前已發展到晚期。"},{"en":"To reach a late stage means to develop to an advanced point in a process.","zh":"reach a late stage 指發展到某過程的後期或高級階段。"},{"en":"A building problem may reach a late stage before anyone sees cracks in the wall.","zh":"建築問題可能在牆上出現裂縫前已發展到晚期。"},{"en":"If a disease reaches a late stage, treatment may become more difficult.","zh":"如果疾病發展到晚期，治療可能變得更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a process that has progressed far.","zh":"這個短語描述一個過程已進展得很遠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in its development","meaning":"在其發展過程中","examples":[{"en":"The disease may reach a late stage in its development.","zh":"疾病可能在其發展過程中達到晚期。"},{"en":"In its development means during the process by which something grows, changes, or progresses.","zh":"in its development 指在某事成長、改變或進展的過程中。"},{"en":"A project may face problems early in its development before the team has clear routines.","zh":"項目在其發展初期可能遇到問題，因為團隊尚未有清晰常規。"},{"en":"Understanding where something is in its development helps people decide what action is needed.","zh":"理解某事在其發展過程中的位置，有助人決定需要甚麼行動。"},{"en":"The phrase places an event within a process of change.","zh":"這個短語把事件放在變化過程之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"feel unwell","meaning":"感到身體不適","examples":[{"en":"You feel unwell and decide to visit the doctor.","zh":"你感到身體不適，並決定去看醫生。"},{"en":"To feel unwell means to feel physically not right, sick, weak, or uncomfortable.","zh":"feel unwell 指身體感覺不對勁、生病、虛弱或不舒服。"},{"en":"A worker may feel unwell after a night of poor sleep and a long commute.","zh":"工人一晚睡得差再長途通勤後，可能感到身體不適。"},{"en":"Feeling unwell can lead someone to rest, cancel plans, or seek medical advice.","zh":"感到身體不適可以令人休息、取消計劃或尋求醫療意見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a personal feeling that may or may not be serious.","zh":"這個短語描述個人感覺，可能嚴重，也可能不嚴重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have a bad cough","meaning":"咳得很厲害","examples":[{"en":"You have a bad cough and always seem to be tired.","zh":"你咳得很厲害，而且總是似乎很疲倦。"},{"en":"To have a bad cough means to cough often, strongly, or for a worrying length of time.","zh":"have a bad cough 指經常、強烈或持續令人擔心地咳嗽。"},{"en":"A student with a bad cough may stay home to avoid spreading germs.","zh":"咳得很厲害的學生可能留在家中，以免傳播病菌。"},{"en":"A bad cough can disturb sleep and make a person feel exhausted.","zh":"嚴重咳嗽可以干擾睡眠，令人感到筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a noticeable symptom that may need medical attention.","zh":"這個短語描述明顯症狀，可能需要醫療注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"seem to be tired","meaning":"似乎很疲倦","examples":[{"en":"You always seem to be tired, even after resting.","zh":"即使休息後，你仍總是似乎很疲倦。"},{"en":"To seem to be tired means to appear exhausted, low in energy, or sleepy.","zh":"seem to be tired 指看起來筋疲力盡、沒有精神或想睡。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice that a usually active student seems to be tired in class.","zh":"老師可能注意到一名平時活躍的學生在課堂上似乎很疲倦。"},{"en":"Someone may seem tired because of stress, illness, poor sleep, or overwork.","zh":"某人看似疲倦，可能因壓力、疾病、睡眠不足或工作過勞。"},{"en":"The phrase describes appearance, not necessarily the confirmed cause.","zh":"這個短語描述外表，而不一定是已確認的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stress at work","meaning":"工作壓力","examples":[{"en":"The symptoms could be caused by stress at work.","zh":"這些症狀可能由工作壓力引起。"},{"en":"Stress at work means pressure, worry, or strain caused by job demands.","zh":"stress at work 指由工作要求造成的壓力、擔憂或緊張。"},{"en":"An accountant may feel stress at work near the end of the financial year.","zh":"會計師在財政年度結束前可能感到工作壓力。"},{"en":"Work stress can affect sleep, mood, appetite, and physical comfort.","zh":"工作壓力可以影響睡眠、心情、食慾和身體舒適度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pressure from the workplace as a possible cause of problems.","zh":"這個短語描述來自工作場所的壓力，作為問題的可能原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"give up smoking","meaning":"戒煙","examples":[{"en":"The patient thinks that perhaps he should give up smoking.","zh":"病人認為也許自己應該戒煙。"},{"en":"To give up smoking means to stop smoking cigarettes or tobacco.","zh":"give up smoking 指停止吸香煙或煙草。"},{"en":"A father may decide to give up smoking after his child develops breathing problems.","zh":"父親在孩子出現呼吸問題後，可能決定戒煙。"},{"en":"Giving up smoking can improve health, reduce coughing, and lower long-term disease risks.","zh":"戒煙可以改善健康、減少咳嗽，並降低長期疾病風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stopping a harmful habit.","zh":"這個短語描述停止一種有害習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"visit the doctor","meaning":"看醫生","examples":[{"en":"You visit the doctor because your symptoms get worse.","zh":"你因症狀惡化而去看醫生。"},{"en":"To visit the doctor means to go to a medical professional for advice, examination, or treatment.","zh":"visit the doctor 指前往醫療專業人士處尋求意見、檢查或治療。"},{"en":"A student may visit the doctor if a fever lasts for several days.","zh":"如果發燒持續幾天，學生可能去看醫生。"},{"en":"Visiting the doctor can turn personal worry into a clearer medical explanation.","zh":"看醫生可以把個人擔憂轉化為較清楚的醫學解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes seeking professional medical help.","zh":"這個短語描述尋求專業醫療協助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"listen to your chest and heart","meaning":"聽診胸部和心臟","examples":[{"en":"The doctor listens to your chest and heart.","zh":"醫生聽診你的胸部和心臟。"},{"en":"To listen to your chest and heart means to use a stethoscope to check breathing and heartbeat sounds.","zh":"listen to your chest and heart 指用聽診器檢查呼吸和心跳聲音。"},{"en":"A doctor may listen to a child’s chest and heart when the child has a cough and fever.","zh":"當孩子咳嗽和發燒時，醫生可能會聽診他的胸部和心臟。"},{"en":"Unusual sounds can give the doctor clues about infection or heart problems.","zh":"不尋常聲音可以給醫生關於感染或心臟問題的線索。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a basic physical examination.","zh":"這個短語描述基本身體檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"take your temperature and blood pressure","meaning":"量體溫和血壓","examples":[{"en":"The doctor takes your temperature and blood pressure.","zh":"醫生量你的體溫和血壓。"},{"en":"To take your temperature and blood pressure means to measure body heat and the force of blood moving through the arteries.","zh":"take your temperature and blood pressure 指量度身體熱度和血液在動脈中流動的壓力。"},{"en":"A nurse may take your temperature and blood pressure before you see the doctor.","zh":"護士可能在你見醫生前先量你的體溫和血壓。"},{"en":"These measurements help medical staff decide whether there are signs of fever or circulation problems.","zh":"這些量度幫助醫護人員判斷是否有發燒或循環問題跡象。"},{"en":"The phrase describes routine medical checks.","zh":"這個短語描述常規醫療檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"blood pressure","meaning":"血壓","examples":[{"en":"High blood pressure can be an important medical sign.","zh":"高血壓可以是一個重要醫學徵象。"},{"en":"Blood pressure is the force of blood pushing against the walls of the blood vessels.","zh":"blood pressure 是血液推向血管壁的壓力。"},{"en":"A doctor may check blood pressure during a routine health examination.","zh":"醫生可能在常規健康檢查中量血壓。"},{"en":"High blood pressure can increase the risk of heart disease if it is not controlled.","zh":"如果不受控制，高血壓可以增加心臟病風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a key measurement of cardiovascular health.","zh":"這個短語描述心血管健康的重要量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"prescribe antibiotics for","meaning":"為……處方抗生素","examples":[{"en":"The doctor prescribes antibiotics for your cough.","zh":"醫生為你的咳嗽處方抗生素。"},{"en":"To prescribe antibiotics for a condition means to officially give medicine used to treat bacterial infections.","zh":"prescribe antibiotics for 某病況，指正式開出用來治療細菌感染的藥物。"},{"en":"A doctor may prescribe antibiotics for a throat infection if bacteria are suspected.","zh":"如果懷疑是細菌感染，醫生可能為喉嚨感染處方抗生素。"},{"en":"Antibiotics should be used carefully because unnecessary use can reduce their effectiveness.","zh":"抗生素應小心使用，因為不必要使用會降低其效力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a doctor giving a specific medical treatment.","zh":"這個短語描述醫生給予特定醫療治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"antibiotics","meaning":"抗生素","examples":[{"en":"Antibiotics may be prescribed when a bacterial infection is suspected.","zh":"當懷疑有細菌感染時，可能會處方抗生素。"},{"en":"Antibiotics are medicines used to kill bacteria or stop them from growing.","zh":"antibiotics 是用來殺死細菌或阻止細菌生長的藥物。"},{"en":"A patient may take antibiotics for a chest infection if the doctor thinks bacteria are involved.","zh":"如果醫生認為涉及細菌，病人可能因胸腔感染服用抗生素。"},{"en":"Antibiotics do not treat ordinary viral colds, so doctors must choose carefully.","zh":"抗生素不能治療普通病毒性感冒，所以醫生必須小心選擇。"},{"en":"The word refers to a specific group of infection-fighting medicines.","zh":"這個詞指一類特定的抗感染藥物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"things do not improve","meaning":"情況沒有改善","examples":[{"en":"Things do not improve after the first visit to the doctor.","zh":"第一次看醫生後，情況沒有改善。"},{"en":"Things do not improve means the situation stays bad or does not get better.","zh":"things do not improve 指情況仍然不好，沒有變好。"},{"en":"If a student studies harder but things do not improve, she may need a different method.","zh":"如果學生更努力溫習但情況沒有改善，她可能需要不同方法。"},{"en":"When symptoms do not improve, people often return for further advice.","zh":"當症狀沒有改善，人們常會再次尋求意見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a lack of progress.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"struggle on","meaning":"勉強撐下去","examples":[{"en":"You struggle on, hoping that work will become easier soon.","zh":"你勉強撐下去，希望工作很快會變得容易些。"},{"en":"To struggle on means to continue despite difficulty, tiredness, or pain.","zh":"struggle on 指即使困難、疲倦或疼痛仍繼續下去。"},{"en":"A worker may struggle on through a busy week because the team is short of staff.","zh":"工人可能因團隊人手不足而在繁忙一週中勉強撐下去。"},{"en":"Struggling on can help someone finish a task, but it may worsen health if rest is needed.","zh":"勉強撐下去可以幫人完成任務，但如果需要休息，可能會令健康變差。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pushing through difficulty rather than stopping.","zh":"這個短語描述在困難中硬撐，而不是停下來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pull yourself together","meaning":"振作起來","examples":[{"en":"You think that you should pull yourself together.","zh":"你認為自己應該振作起來。"},{"en":"To pull yourself together means to control your emotions or behaviour and act normally again.","zh":"pull yourself together 指控制自己的情緒或行為，重新正常地行動。"},{"en":"A nervous student may tell herself to pull herself together before an oral exam.","zh":"緊張學生可能在口試前告訴自己要振作起來。"},{"en":"This phrase can encourage action, but it may be unfair if the problem is real illness.","zh":"這個短語可以鼓勵行動，但如果問題是真正疾病，這樣說可能不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase describes trying to regain self-control.","zh":"這個短語描述嘗試恢復自我控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ease off","meaning":"減輕；緩和","examples":[{"en":"You hope that the pressure at work will ease off soon.","zh":"你希望工作上的壓力很快會減輕。"},{"en":"To ease off means to become less strong, intense, or demanding.","zh":"ease off 指變得沒那麼強烈、緊張或繁重。"},{"en":"Traffic may ease off after the morning rush hour.","zh":"早上繁忙時間後，交通可能會緩和。"},{"en":"If pain does not ease off, a person may need medical advice.","zh":"如果疼痛沒有減輕，一個人可能需要醫療意見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pressure, pain, or difficulty becoming lighter.","zh":"這個短語描述壓力、疼痛或困難變輕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a return visit to","meaning":"再次求診","examples":[{"en":"A return visit to the doctor shocks the patient.","zh":"再次求診令病人震驚。"},{"en":"A return visit to a place is a second or later visit after an earlier one.","zh":"return visit to 某處，是在較早一次之後的第二次或之後的探訪。"},{"en":"A return visit to the dentist may be needed if tooth pain continues.","zh":"如果牙痛持續，可能需要再次去看牙醫。"},{"en":"Return visits help professionals check whether the first treatment worked.","zh":"再次求診幫助專業人士檢查第一次治療是否有效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes going back for follow-up.","zh":"這個短語描述回去跟進。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"drawing on","meaning":"憑藉；運用","examples":[{"en":"The doctor makes a diagnosis, drawing on years of training and experience.","zh":"醫生憑藉多年的訓練和經驗作出診斷。"},{"en":"Drawing on something means using it as a source of knowledge, skill, or support.","zh":"drawing on 某物，指把它用作知識、技能或支援來源。"},{"en":"A teacher may solve a classroom problem by drawing on past experience with similar students.","zh":"老師可能憑藉過往與相似學生相處的經驗，解決課室問題。"},{"en":"Professionals make better decisions when they draw on both training and real cases.","zh":"專業人士同時運用訓練和真實個案時，會作出更好決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using what one already knows.","zh":"這個短語描述使用自己已有的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"years of training and experience","meaning":"多年的訓練和經驗","examples":[{"en":"The doctor draws on years of training and experience.","zh":"醫生運用多年的訓練和經驗。"},{"en":"Years of training and experience means a long period of formal learning and practical work.","zh":"years of training and experience 指長時間的正式學習和實際工作。"},{"en":"A senior nurse uses years of training and experience when judging whether a patient needs urgent care.","zh":"資深護士判斷病人是否需要緊急護理時，會運用多年的訓練和經驗。"},{"en":"Long experience helps professionals notice details beginners may miss.","zh":"長期經驗幫助專業人士注意到初學者可能錯過的細節。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why expert judgement carries authority.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何專家判斷具有權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"diagnose pneumonia","meaning":"診斷出肺炎","examples":[{"en":"The doctor diagnoses pneumonia after examining the patient again.","zh":"醫生再次檢查病人後診斷出肺炎。"},{"en":"To diagnose pneumonia means to identify pneumonia as the illness causing the patient’s symptoms.","zh":"diagnose pneumonia 指確認肺炎是造成病人症狀的疾病。"},{"en":"A doctor may diagnose pneumonia after hearing unusual chest sounds and checking test results.","zh":"醫生可能在聽到不尋常胸音並檢查測試結果後，診斷出肺炎。"},{"en":"Diagnosis changes treatment because pneumonia may require rest, medicine, and careful monitoring.","zh":"診斷會改變治療，因為肺炎可能需要休息、藥物和仔細監察。"},{"en":"The phrase describes naming a specific lung infection medically.","zh":"這個短語描述在醫學上命名一種特定肺部感染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pneumonia","meaning":"肺炎","examples":[{"en":"Pneumonia can require bed rest and time off work.","zh":"肺炎可能需要臥床休息和請假不上班。"},{"en":"Pneumonia is a lung infection that can cause coughing, fever, chest pain, and difficulty breathing.","zh":"pneumonia 是一種肺部感染，可以引起咳嗽、發燒、胸痛和呼吸困難。"},{"en":"An elderly person with pneumonia may need hospital care if breathing becomes difficult.","zh":"患肺炎的長者如果呼吸變得困難，可能需要住院護理。"},{"en":"Pneumonia can be serious because it affects the lungs’ ability to work properly.","zh":"肺炎可以很嚴重，因為它影響肺部正常運作的能力。"},{"en":"The word refers to a specific illness, not just an ordinary cough.","zh":"這個詞指特定疾病，而不只是普通咳嗽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bed rest","meaning":"臥床休息","examples":[{"en":"The patient needs bed rest after being diagnosed with pneumonia.","zh":"病人被診斷患上肺炎後需要臥床休息。"},{"en":"Bed rest means staying in bed to recover from illness or injury.","zh":"bed rest 指留在床上，以便從疾病或受傷中恢復。"},{"en":"A doctor may advise bed rest if a patient has a high fever and severe weakness.","zh":"如果病人高燒和嚴重虛弱，醫生可能建議臥床休息。"},{"en":"Bed rest reduces physical demand on the body so it can recover.","zh":"臥床休息減少身體負擔，讓身體可以康復。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rest as part of medical recovery.","zh":"這個短語描述作為醫療康復一部分的休息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a considerable amount of","meaning":"相當多的……","examples":[{"en":"The patient needs a considerable amount of time off work.","zh":"病人需要相當多的請假不上班時間。"},{"en":"A considerable amount of something means quite a large amount of it.","zh":"considerable amount of 某物，指數量相當大。"},{"en":"A school project may require a considerable amount of planning before students begin filming.","zh":"學校項目在學生開始拍攝前，可能需要相當多的規劃。"},{"en":"If an illness needs a considerable amount of recovery time, normal work may have to stop.","zh":"如果疾病需要相當多的康復時間，正常工作可能要暫停。"},{"en":"The phrase describes more than a small or minor amount.","zh":"這個短語描述多於少量或輕微數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"time off work","meaning":"請假不上班的時間","examples":[{"en":"The illness requires a considerable amount of time off work.","zh":"這場病需要相當多請假不上班的時間。"},{"en":"Time off work means time when a person is allowed not to work, often because of illness, rest, or personal reasons.","zh":"time off work 指一個人獲准不上班的時間，常因疾病、休息或私人原因。"},{"en":"An employee may take time off work after surgery.","zh":"員工手術後可能請假不上班。"},{"en":"Serious illness can require time off work so the person can recover properly.","zh":"嚴重疾病可能需要請假不上班，讓人妥善康復。"},{"en":"The phrase describes absence from work with a reason.","zh":"這個短語描述有原因的工作缺席。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the scenario is transformed","meaning":"情況徹底改變","examples":[{"en":"The scenario is transformed after the doctor diagnoses pneumonia.","zh":"醫生診斷出肺炎後，情況徹底改變。"},{"en":"The scenario is transformed means the situation changes completely in meaning or seriousness.","zh":"scenario is transformed 指情況在意義或嚴重程度上完全改變。"},{"en":"A missed deadline is transformed into a serious problem when it causes a client to cancel a contract.","zh":"當錯過截止日期導致客戶取消合約，它就由小事變成嚴重問題。"},{"en":"New evidence can transform a situation by changing how people understand it.","zh":"新證據可以透過改變人們的理解來徹底改變情況。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a major shift in how a case is viewed.","zh":"這個短語描述人們看待事件方式的重大轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be caused by","meaning":"由……引起","examples":[{"en":"The symptoms are no longer thought to be caused by work pressure.","zh":"這些症狀不再被認為由工作壓力引起。"},{"en":"To be caused by something means to happen because of that reason or source.","zh":"be caused by 某事，指因該原因或來源而發生。"},{"en":"A headache may be caused by lack of sleep, dehydration, or stress.","zh":"頭痛可能由睡眠不足、缺水或壓力引起。"},{"en":"Finding what symptoms are caused by helps doctors choose the right treatment.","zh":"找出症狀由甚麼引起，有助醫生選擇正確治療。"},{"en":"The phrase links an effect to its cause.","zh":"這個短語把結果與原因連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pressure at work","meaning":"工作上的壓力","examples":[{"en":"The patient first thinks the symptoms are caused by pressure at work.","zh":"病人起初認為症狀由工作上的壓力引起。"},{"en":"Pressure at work means stress or demands that come from a job.","zh":"pressure at work 指來自工作的壓力或要求。"},{"en":"A manager may feel pressure at work when several deadlines arrive in the same week.","zh":"當幾個截止日期在同一週到來，經理可能感到工作上的壓力。"},{"en":"Work pressure can make people blame tiredness or illness on their job.","zh":"工作壓力可以令人把疲倦或疾病歸咎於工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes job-related strain.","zh":"這個短語描述與工作有關的緊張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have proof that","meaning":"有證據證明……","examples":[{"en":"The patient now has proof that he is ill.","zh":"病人現在有證據證明自己生病。"},{"en":"To have proof that something is true means to have evidence showing it is true.","zh":"have proof that 某事為真，指有證據顯示它是真實的。"},{"en":"A student has proof that she submitted homework if the online system records the time.","zh":"如果網上系統記錄了時間，學生就有證據證明自己已提交功課。"},{"en":"Proof changes a belief into something others are more likely to accept.","zh":"證據會把一個信念變成他人較可能接受的東西。"},{"en":"The phrase describes having evidence strong enough to support a claim.","zh":"這個短語描述有足夠支持一項主張的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the result of combining A with B","meaning":"結合A與B的結果","examples":[{"en":"The diagnosis is the result of combining personal experience with medical expertise.","zh":"診斷是結合個人經驗與醫學專業知識的結果。"},{"en":"The result of combining A with B means the outcome produced when two things are brought together.","zh":"the result of combining A with B 指把兩事物結合後產生的結果。"},{"en":"A good presentation may be the result of combining clear research with confident speaking.","zh":"好匯報可能是結合清晰研究與自信演說的結果。"},{"en":"Combining personal feelings with expert judgement can create a fuller understanding of illness.","zh":"結合個人感受與專家判斷，可以創造對疾病更完整的理解。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how two sources produce one outcome.","zh":"這個短語解釋兩個來源如何產生一個結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"subjective experience","meaning":"主觀經驗","examples":[{"en":"The patient’s subjective experience is combined with the doctor’s diagnosis.","zh":"病人的主觀經驗與醫生的診斷結合起來。"},{"en":"Subjective experience means a person’s own feelings, perceptions, or personal view of what is happening.","zh":"subjective experience 指一個人自己的感覺、知覺或對事情的個人看法。"},{"en":"Pain level is partly subjective experience because only the patient knows how it feels.","zh":"疼痛程度部分屬於主觀經驗，因為只有病人知道那感覺如何。"},{"en":"Subjective experience is important, but it may need expert interpretation.","zh":"主觀經驗很重要，但可能需要專家詮釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes knowledge from inside the person’s own experience.","zh":"這個短語描述來自個人內在經驗的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"medical expert","meaning":"醫學專家","examples":[{"en":"The doctor has the status of a medical expert.","zh":"醫生具有醫學專家的地位。"},{"en":"A medical expert is a person with specialised training and authority in medicine.","zh":"medical expert 是在醫學方面有專門訓練和權威的人。"},{"en":"A hospital may ask a medical expert to explain a difficult diagnosis to a family.","zh":"醫院可能請醫學專家向家庭解釋困難診斷。"},{"en":"Medical experts are trusted because they combine education, evidence, and clinical experience.","zh":"醫學專家受到信任，因為他們結合教育、證據和臨床經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to someone whose medical judgement carries authority.","zh":"這個短語指醫學判斷具有權威的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"medically authenticated diagnosis","meaning":"經醫學確認的診斷","examples":[{"en":"The patient receives a medically authenticated diagnosis.","zh":"病人得到經醫學確認的診斷。"},{"en":"A medically authenticated diagnosis is a diagnosis confirmed by a recognised medical professional.","zh":"medically authenticated diagnosis 是由受認可醫療專業人士確認的診斷。"},{"en":"An employer may accept a medically authenticated diagnosis when considering sick leave.","zh":"僱主考慮病假時，可能接受經醫學確認的診斷。"},{"en":"Such a diagnosis gives the patient’s illness social and official recognition.","zh":"這種診斷給病人的疾病社會和官方認可。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a health claim validated by medicine.","zh":"這個短語描述由醫學驗證的健康聲稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"seriously ill","meaning":"病得嚴重","examples":[{"en":"The diagnosis shows that the patient is seriously ill.","zh":"診斷顯示病人病得嚴重。"},{"en":"Seriously ill means having a medical condition that is important, dangerous, or not minor.","zh":"seriously ill 指患有重要、危險或非輕微的醫療狀況。"},{"en":"A patient with breathing difficulty and high fever may be seriously ill.","zh":"有呼吸困難和高燒的病人可能病得嚴重。"},{"en":"If someone is seriously ill, they may need rest, treatment, and time away from work.","zh":"如果某人病得嚴重，可能需要休息、治療和暫時不上班。"},{"en":"The phrase describes illness that should not be ignored.","zh":"這個短語描述不應被忽視的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"evidence on which to base","meaning":"可作為……基礎的證據","examples":[{"en":"The patient has evidence on which to base this knowledge.","zh":"病人有可作為這種知識基礎的證據。"},{"en":"Evidence on which to base something means facts or information that support a belief or decision.","zh":"evidence on which to base 某事，指支持信念或決定的事實或資訊。"},{"en":"A school needs evidence on which to base a decision about changing the timetable.","zh":"學校需要可作為改時間表決定基礎的證據。"},{"en":"Without evidence, a conclusion may be only a guess.","zh":"沒有證據，結論可能只是猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a foundation for knowledge or judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述知識或判斷的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"base knowledge on evidence","meaning":"以證據作為知識基礎","examples":[{"en":"People usually base medical knowledge on evidence.","zh":"人們通常以證據作為醫學知識基礎。"},{"en":"To base knowledge on evidence means to build what we know from facts, observations, or reliable data.","zh":"base knowledge on evidence 指把我們所知建立在事實、觀察或可靠數據之上。"},{"en":"A doctor bases knowledge on evidence when she checks symptoms, test results, and medical history.","zh":"醫生檢查症狀、測試結果和病歷時，就是以證據作為知識基礎。"},{"en":"Evidence-based knowledge is stronger than guesses or rumours.","zh":"以證據為基礎的知識比猜測或謠言更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes grounding belief in supportable information.","zh":"這個短語描述把信念建立在可支持資訊上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"different sources of knowledge","meaning":"不同知識來源","examples":[{"en":"The scenario shows many different sources of knowledge.","zh":"這個情境顯示許多不同知識來源。"},{"en":"Different sources of knowledge are the various places from which people get information or understanding.","zh":"different sources of knowledge 是人們取得資訊或理解的各種來源。"},{"en":"In a health decision, sources may include symptoms, family advice, medical tests, and a doctor’s judgement.","zh":"在健康決定中，來源可以包括症狀、家人意見、醫學檢查和醫生判斷。"},{"en":"Different sources can support or challenge one another.","zh":"不同來源可以互相支持或挑戰。"},{"en":"The phrase helps explain why knowledge is often built from several kinds of evidence.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋為何知識常由多種證據建立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"consult the doctor","meaning":"諮詢醫生；求醫","examples":[{"en":"The patient decides to consult the doctor because he feels unwell.","zh":"病人因感到不適而決定諮詢醫生。"},{"en":"To consult the doctor means to ask a doctor for medical advice or examination.","zh":"consult the doctor 指向醫生尋求醫療意見或檢查。"},{"en":"A parent may consult the doctor if a child’s cough lasts more than a week.","zh":"如果孩子咳嗽超過一星期，父母可能求醫。"},{"en":"Consulting a doctor can help turn unclear symptoms into a more reliable diagnosis.","zh":"諮詢醫生可以幫助把不清楚的症狀轉化為較可靠診斷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes seeking professional medical guidance.","zh":"這個短語描述尋求專業醫療指引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the first place","meaning":"最初；一開始","examples":[{"en":"The patient consults the doctor in the first place because he feels unwell.","zh":"病人最初求醫，是因為他感到不適。"},{"en":"In the first place means at the beginning or as the original reason.","zh":"in the first place 指在開始時，或作為最初原因。"},{"en":"A student joined the club in the first place because she wanted to make friends.","zh":"學生一開始加入學會，是因為她想交朋友。"},{"en":"The phrase helps explain why an action started before later events changed the situation.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋後來事件改變情況前，某行動為何開始。"},{"en":"It points back to the original cause or starting point.","zh":"它回指原本原因或起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"personal knowledge about","meaning":"關於……的個人知識","examples":[{"en":"Feeling unwell is personal knowledge about your own body.","zh":"感到不適是關於你自己身體的個人知識。"},{"en":"Personal knowledge about something is knowledge gained through one’s own direct experience.","zh":"personal knowledge about 某事，是透過自己直接經驗獲得的知識。"},{"en":"A runner has personal knowledge about how her knees feel after long training.","zh":"跑手對長時間訓練後自己膝蓋的感覺有個人知識。"},{"en":"Personal knowledge can be valuable, but others may not be able to verify it immediately.","zh":"個人知識可以有價值，但別人未必能立即驗證。"},{"en":"The phrase describes knowledge that belongs to the person experiencing it.","zh":"這個短語描述屬於經歷者本人的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"your own body","meaning":"你自己的身體","examples":[{"en":"You have personal knowledge about your own body.","zh":"你對你自己的身體有個人知識。"},{"en":"Your own body means the body you personally live in and experience directly.","zh":"your own body 指你親自生活於其中並直接經驗的身體。"},{"en":"You may know your own body well enough to notice when normal tiredness becomes unusual.","zh":"你可能足夠了解自己的身體，能注意到普通疲倦何時變得不尋常。"},{"en":"Knowledge of your own body helps you decide when to rest or seek help.","zh":"對自己身體的了解幫助你決定何時休息或尋求幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses direct personal experience of health and feeling.","zh":"這個短語強調對健康和感覺的直接個人經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"expert diagnosis","meaning":"專家診斷","examples":[{"en":"The doctor’s expert diagnosis is based on training and experience.","zh":"醫生的專家診斷以訓練和經驗為基礎。"},{"en":"An expert diagnosis is a professional judgement about illness made by someone with specialised medical knowledge.","zh":"expert diagnosis 是由具有專門醫學知識的人對疾病作出的專業判斷。"},{"en":"A patient may need an expert diagnosis before receiving treatment for a complicated condition.","zh":"病人在接受複雜病況治療前，可能需要專家診斷。"},{"en":"Expert diagnosis carries authority because it is supported by training, evidence, and practice.","zh":"專家診斷具有權威，因為它由訓練、證據和實踐支持。"},{"en":"The phrase describes medical judgement made by a qualified professional.","zh":"這個短語描述由合資格專業人士作出的醫學判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be based on experience and training","meaning":"以經驗和訓練為基礎","examples":[{"en":"The doctor’s diagnosis is based on experience and training.","zh":"醫生的診斷以經驗和訓練為基礎。"},{"en":"To be based on experience and training means to depend on practical work and formal learning.","zh":"be based on experience and training 指依賴實際工作和正式學習。"},{"en":"A pilot’s decision in bad weather is based on experience and training.","zh":"飛行員在惡劣天氣下的決定以經驗和訓練為基礎。"},{"en":"Decisions based on experience and training are usually more reliable than guesses.","zh":"以經驗和訓練為基礎的決定通常比猜測更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why professional judgement deserves attention.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何專業判斷值得重視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as diverse as","meaning":"多樣至包括……","examples":[{"en":"The doctor’s knowledge comes from sources as diverse as textbooks and laboratory reports.","zh":"醫生的知識來自多樣至包括教科書和化驗報告等來源。"},{"en":"As diverse as means including very different examples or types.","zh":"as diverse as 指包括非常不同的例子或種類。"},{"en":"A student’s learning tools may be as diverse as books, videos, field trips, and interviews.","zh":"學生的學習工具可以多樣至包括書本、影片、實地考察和訪問。"},{"en":"Diverse sources can make understanding broader because each source gives different evidence.","zh":"多樣來源可以令理解更廣闊，因為每個來源提供不同證據。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights variety within a group.","zh":"這個短語突出一個群體內的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"laboratory reports","meaning":"化驗報告","examples":[{"en":"Laboratory reports can be a source of medical knowledge.","zh":"化驗報告可以是醫學知識來源。"},{"en":"Laboratory reports are written results from scientific tests carried out in a lab.","zh":"laboratory reports 是在實驗室進行科學測試後寫成的結果。"},{"en":"A doctor may read laboratory reports to check blood, urine, or infection results.","zh":"醫生可能閱讀化驗報告，以檢查血液、尿液或感染結果。"},{"en":"Lab reports can support or challenge a doctor’s first guess about an illness.","zh":"化驗報告可以支持或挑戰醫生對疾病的最初猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to test-based documents used in medical decision-making.","zh":"這個短語指用於醫療決策的測試文件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"medical textbooks","meaning":"醫學教科書","examples":[{"en":"Medical textbooks are one source of a doctor’s knowledge.","zh":"醫學教科書是醫生知識的一個來源。"},{"en":"Medical textbooks are books that explain diseases, treatments, anatomy, and medical principles.","zh":"medical textbooks 是解釋疾病、治療、解剖和醫學原則的書。"},{"en":"A medical student studies textbooks to learn how symptoms connect with possible illnesses.","zh":"醫學生研讀教科書，以學習症狀如何與可能疾病相連。"},{"en":"Textbooks give doctors shared professional knowledge beyond personal experience.","zh":"教科書給醫生超越個人經驗的共同專業知識。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to formal written medical learning.","zh":"這個短語指正式的書面醫學學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"years of experience","meaning":"多年經驗","examples":[{"en":"Years of experience help doctors make better diagnoses.","zh":"多年經驗幫助醫生作出更好診斷。"},{"en":"Years of experience means knowledge gained from doing something for a long time.","zh":"years of experience 指長時間做某事而獲得的知識。"},{"en":"A teacher with years of experience may quickly recognise why a class is losing focus.","zh":"有多年經驗的老師可能很快看出班級為何失去專注。"},{"en":"Experience helps professionals notice patterns that are difficult to learn from books alone.","zh":"經驗幫助專業人士注意到單靠書本難以學會的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical knowledge built over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間建立的實踐知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the experience of our own bodies","meaning":"對自身身體的經驗","examples":[{"en":"The experience of our own bodies is one source of knowledge.","zh":"對自身身體的經驗是一種知識來源。"},{"en":"The experience of our own bodies means what we feel directly through pain, energy, weakness, or comfort.","zh":"experience of our own bodies 指我們透過疼痛、精力、虛弱或舒適直接感受到的東西。"},{"en":"A person knows from the experience of her own body when exercise leaves her unusually breathless.","zh":"一個人透過對自身身體的經驗，知道運動後異常氣喘。"},{"en":"Bodily experience can alert us to problems before formal tests are done.","zh":"身體經驗可以在正式檢查前提醒我們有問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes personal physical awareness as knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述把個人身體覺察視為知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"changes that might be significant","meaning":"可能有重要意義的變化","examples":[{"en":"People notice changes that might be significant.","zh":"人們注意到可能有重要意義的變化。"},{"en":"Changes that might be significant are differences that could be important or worth attention.","zh":"changes that might be significant 是可能重要或值得注意的差異。"},{"en":"Sudden weight loss, unusual tiredness, or a persistent cough may be changes that might be significant.","zh":"體重突然下降、異常疲倦或持續咳嗽，可能是有重要意義的變化。"},{"en":"Noticing important changes early can lead people to seek help sooner.","zh":"及早注意重要變化可以令人更早尋求幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase describes possible warning signs.","zh":"這個短語描述可能的警號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"physical distress","meaning":"身體不適；身體痛苦","examples":[{"en":"Physical distress may lead someone to seek medical advice.","zh":"身體不適可能促使某人尋求醫療意見。"},{"en":"Physical distress means bodily pain, discomfort, weakness, or suffering.","zh":"physical distress 指身體疼痛、不適、虛弱或痛苦。"},{"en":"A person with chest pain may experience physical distress and call a doctor.","zh":"胸痛的人可能經歷身體痛苦並致電醫生。"},{"en":"Physical distress can interrupt sleep, work, and ordinary daily tasks.","zh":"身體不適可以打斷睡眠、工作和普通日常任務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bodily suffering that demands attention.","zh":"這個短語描述需要注意的身體痛苦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be mediated by","meaning":"受……中介；受……影響","examples":[{"en":"Personal experience is mediated by other forms of knowledge.","zh":"個人經驗受其他形式的知識中介。"},{"en":"To be mediated by something means to be shaped, filtered, or influenced by it.","zh":"be mediated by 某事，指被它塑造、過濾或影響。"},{"en":"A student’s view of a school may be mediated by friends’ comments and online reviews.","zh":"學生對一所學校的看法可能受朋友評論和網上評價影響。"},{"en":"Personal feelings are not always direct because language and culture affect how we interpret them.","zh":"個人感受不一定是直接的，因為語言和文化會影響我們如何詮釋它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something passing through another influence before being understood.","zh":"這個短語描述某事在被理解前經過另一種影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"other forms of knowledge","meaning":"其他形式的知識","examples":[{"en":"Personal experience is shaped by other forms of knowledge.","zh":"個人經驗由其他形式的知識塑造。"},{"en":"Other forms of knowledge are additional ways of knowing beyond one main source.","zh":"other forms of knowledge 是主要來源以外的其他認知方式。"},{"en":"A patient’s feelings may be shaped by other forms of knowledge, such as family advice or media reports.","zh":"病人的感受可能受到其他形式的知識影響，例如家人意見或傳媒報道。"},{"en":"These forms can help explain symptoms, but they may also mislead people.","zh":"這些形式可以幫助解釋症狀，但也可能誤導人。"},{"en":"The phrase points to knowledge outside the immediate personal experience.","zh":"這個短語指個人直接經驗以外的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the words available to describe","meaning":"可用來描述……的詞語","examples":[{"en":"Our symptoms are shaped by the words available to describe them.","zh":"我們的症狀受到可用來描述它們的詞語影響。"},{"en":"The words available to describe something are the language choices people have for explaining it.","zh":"words available to describe 某事，是人們用來解釋它的語言選擇。"},{"en":"A child may struggle to describe anxiety if she has no words available to describe the feeling.","zh":"如果孩子沒有可用來描述焦慮的詞語，她可能難以表達那種感覺。"},{"en":"If people learn better words for symptoms, they can explain health problems more clearly.","zh":"如果人們學會更好的症狀詞語，就能更清楚解釋健康問題。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that language affects understanding.","zh":"這個短語顯示語言會影響理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"common sense","meaning":"常識","examples":[{"en":"The common sense of family and friends may influence our judgement.","zh":"家人和朋友的常識可能影響我們的判斷。"},{"en":"Common sense is ordinary practical judgement based on everyday experience rather than specialist study.","zh":"common sense 是基於日常經驗，而非專門研究的普通實用判斷。"},{"en":"Common sense may tell someone to rest when they have a fever.","zh":"常識可能告訴某人發燒時要休息。"},{"en":"Common sense can be useful, but it may not be enough for serious medical problems.","zh":"常識可以有用，但對嚴重醫療問題可能不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes everyday practical understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述日常實用理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ideas drawn from popular culture","meaning":"來自流行文化的觀念","examples":[{"en":"Ideas drawn from popular culture shape how people explain illness.","zh":"來自流行文化的觀念塑造人們如何解釋疾病。"},{"en":"Ideas drawn from popular culture are beliefs taken from media, films, magazines, social trends, or everyday public discussion.","zh":"ideas drawn from popular culture 是取自傳媒、電影、雜誌、社會潮流或日常公共討論的信念。"},{"en":"A person may blame stress for every headache because that idea is common in popular culture.","zh":"一個人可能把每次頭痛都歸咎於壓力，因為這種觀念在流行文化中常見。"},{"en":"Popular ideas can help people name problems, but they may oversimplify medical causes.","zh":"流行觀念可以幫助人命名問題，但也可能過分簡化醫學原因。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cultural explanations borrowed from everyday society.","zh":"這個短語描述從日常社會借來的文化解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"over the past decade","meaning":"在過去十年間","examples":[{"en":"Over the past decade, stress-related illness has received attention in Western culture.","zh":"在過去十年間，與壓力有關的疾病在西方文化中受到關注。"},{"en":"Over the past decade means during the last ten years.","zh":"over the past decade 指在過去十年期間。"},{"en":"Over the past decade, many schools have used more digital learning tools.","zh":"在過去十年間，許多學校使用了更多數碼學習工具。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show that a change has happened across a recent ten-year period.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示某變化在最近十年間發生。"},{"en":"It places a trend in time.","zh":"它把一個趨勢放入時間之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Western culture","meaning":"西方文化","examples":[{"en":"Western culture has placed emphasis on stress-related illness.","zh":"西方文化重視與壓力有關的疾病。"},{"en":"Western culture refers broadly to the values, habits, media, and institutions common in many European and North American societies.","zh":"Western culture 廣泛指許多歐洲和北美社會中常見的價值觀、習慣、媒體和制度。"},{"en":"Ideas about work-life balance are often discussed in Western culture.","zh":"工作與生活平衡的觀念常在西方文化中被討論。"},{"en":"Cultural context affects how people explain health, success, stress, and responsibility.","zh":"文化背景會影響人們如何解釋健康、成功、壓力和責任。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broad cultural background, not one single country.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛文化背景，而不是單一國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"place significant emphasis on","meaning":"非常重視……","examples":[{"en":"The media have placed significant emphasis on stress-related illness.","zh":"傳媒非常重視與壓力有關的疾病。"},{"en":"To place significant emphasis on something means to give it a lot of attention and importance.","zh":"place significant emphasis on 某事，指給予它大量注意和重要性。"},{"en":"Schools may place significant emphasis on reading because it supports every subject.","zh":"學校可能非常重視閱讀，因為它支持每個科目。"},{"en":"When the media emphasise one issue strongly, people may use it to explain many experiences.","zh":"當傳媒強烈重視某議題，人們可能用它解釋許多經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving strong focus to a topic.","zh":"這個短語描述對某主題給予強烈焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stress-related illness","meaning":"與壓力有關的疾病","examples":[{"en":"Stress-related illness is often discussed in the media.","zh":"與壓力有關的疾病常在傳媒中被討論。"},{"en":"Stress-related illness means health problems that are caused or worsened by stress.","zh":"stress-related illness 指由壓力造成或加劇的健康問題。"},{"en":"Headaches, poor sleep, and stomach discomfort may sometimes be linked to stress-related illness.","zh":"頭痛、睡眠差和胃部不適有時可能與壓力相關疾病有關。"},{"en":"Talking about stress-related illness can help people take mental pressure seriously.","zh":"討論與壓力有關的疾病，可以幫助人認真看待心理壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase connects health problems with stress as a possible cause.","zh":"這個短語把健康問題與壓力這個可能原因連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the media","meaning":"在傳媒中","examples":[{"en":"Stress-related illness has been discussed widely in the media.","zh":"與壓力有關的疾病已在傳媒中被廣泛討論。"},{"en":"In the media means in newspapers, television, radio, websites, social platforms, or other public information channels.","zh":"in the media 指在報章、電視、電台、網站、社交平台或其他公共資訊渠道中。"},{"en":"A new health warning may spread quickly in the media.","zh":"新健康警告可能在傳媒中迅速傳播。"},{"en":"When a topic appears often in the media, people may start using its language in daily life.","zh":"當一個主題常在傳媒中出現，人們可能開始在日常生活中使用其語言。"},{"en":"The phrase describes public communication channels.","zh":"這個短語描述公共傳播渠道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reference to","meaning":"提及……","examples":[{"en":"Reference to being stressed out has become common.","zh":"提及壓力很大已變得常見。"},{"en":"Reference to something means a mention of it in speech, writing, or discussion.","zh":"reference to 某事，指在說話、寫作或討論中提到它。"},{"en":"A teacher may make reference to a previous lesson before introducing a new topic.","zh":"老師在介紹新主題前，可能提及上一課。"},{"en":"Frequent references to stress can make people see stress as a common explanation for discomfort.","zh":"頻繁提及壓力可以令人把壓力視為不適的常見解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mentioning an idea or topic.","zh":"這個短語描述提到某個想法或主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stressed out","meaning":"壓力很大","examples":[{"en":"Many people describe themselves as stressed out at work.","zh":"許多人形容自己在工作中壓力很大。"},{"en":"Stressed out means feeling under strong mental or emotional pressure.","zh":"stressed out 指感到強烈心理或情緒壓力。"},{"en":"A student may feel stressed out when homework, tests, and family duties happen at the same time.","zh":"當功課、測驗和家庭責任同時出現，學生可能感到壓力很大。"},{"en":"Feeling stressed out can affect sleep, patience, concentration, and health.","zh":"感到壓力很大可以影響睡眠、耐性、專注力和健康。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in everyday conversation about pressure.","zh":"這個短語常見於關於壓力的日常對話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a common response","meaning":"常見回應","examples":[{"en":"Saying that one is stressed out has become a common response.","zh":"說自己壓力很大已成為常見回應。"},{"en":"A common response is a usual reaction or answer in a particular situation.","zh":"common response 是在特定情況下通常出現的反應或答案。"},{"en":"Saying “I’m tired” is a common response when someone asks why a student is quiet.","zh":"當有人問學生為何安靜，說「我很累」是常見回應。"},{"en":"Common responses show what explanations people are used to giving.","zh":"常見回應顯示人們習慣給出甚麼解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a reaction that many people share.","zh":"這個短語描述許多人共有的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"daily workplace exchanges","meaning":"日常職場交流","examples":[{"en":"References to stress are common in daily workplace exchanges.","zh":"提及壓力在日常職場交流中很常見。"},{"en":"Daily workplace exchanges are ordinary conversations or interactions that happen at work each day.","zh":"daily workplace exchanges 是每天在工作中發生的普通對話或互動。"},{"en":"Colleagues may mention deadlines, tiredness, or meetings in daily workplace exchanges.","zh":"同事可能在日常職場交流中提到截止日期、疲倦或會議。"},{"en":"Repeated workplace talk can shape how people explain their health and mood.","zh":"反覆的職場談話可以塑造人們如何解釋健康和心情。"},{"en":"The phrase describes everyday communication at work.","zh":"這個短語描述工作中的日常溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"popular common-sense knowledge","meaning":"大眾常識","examples":[{"en":"Stress has become part of popular common-sense knowledge.","zh":"壓力已成為大眾常識的一部分。"},{"en":"Popular common-sense knowledge is what many ordinary people believe or accept in daily life.","zh":"popular common-sense knowledge 是許多普通人在日常生活中相信或接受的東西。"},{"en":"The idea that sleep affects mood is part of popular common-sense knowledge.","zh":"睡眠會影響心情這個想法，是大眾常識的一部分。"},{"en":"Such knowledge can be useful, but it may simplify complex problems too much.","zh":"這種知識可以有用，但也可能過分簡化複雜問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes widely shared everyday understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛共享的日常理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"it is therefore not surprising that","meaning":"因此……並不令人意外","examples":[{"en":"It is therefore not surprising that people may explain symptoms as stress.","zh":"因此，人們可能把症狀解釋為壓力，並不令人意外。"},{"en":"It is therefore not surprising that means the result is understandable because of the reason just given.","zh":"it is therefore not surprising that 指由於剛提到的原因，結果是可以理解的。"},{"en":"The lesson was very difficult; it is therefore not surprising that many students asked for extra help.","zh":"課堂很困難；因此許多學生要求額外幫助並不令人意外。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with an expected result.","zh":"這個短語把原因與預期結果連起來。"},{"en":"It helps writers show that a conclusion follows logically.","zh":"它幫助作者顯示結論合乎邏輯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"seek an explanation for","meaning":"為……尋找解釋","examples":[{"en":"People may seek an explanation for physical symptoms of discomfort.","zh":"人們可能為身體不適的症狀尋找解釋。"},{"en":"To seek an explanation for something means to try to find out why it happened.","zh":"seek an explanation for 某事，指嘗試找出它為何發生。"},{"en":"A parent may seek an explanation for a child’s sudden refusal to go to school.","zh":"家長可能為孩子突然拒絕上學尋找解釋。"},{"en":"When people feel pain or confusion, they often look for a cause that makes sense.","zh":"當人感到疼痛或困惑，他們常尋找合理原因。"},{"en":"The phrase describes actively trying to understand a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述主動嘗試理解問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"physical symptoms of discomfort","meaning":"身體不適的症狀","examples":[{"en":"Stress may be used to explain physical symptoms of discomfort.","zh":"壓力可能被用來解釋身體不適的症狀。"},{"en":"Physical symptoms of discomfort are bodily signs such as pain, tiredness, nausea, or tightness.","zh":"physical symptoms of discomfort 是疼痛、疲倦、噁心或繃緊等身體跡象。"},{"en":"A person may notice physical symptoms of discomfort after several weeks of poor sleep.","zh":"一個人在幾星期睡眠不足後，可能注意到身體不適的症狀。"},{"en":"Such symptoms may have emotional, physical, or medical causes.","zh":"這些症狀可能有情緒、身體或醫學原因。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bodily signs that feel unpleasant and need interpretation.","zh":"這個短語描述令人不舒服並需要詮釋的身體跡象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rely on","meaning":"依賴；依靠","examples":[{"en":"We might rely on the observations of others who know us.","zh":"我們可能依賴認識我們的人的觀察。"},{"en":"To rely on something means to depend on it for help, support, or information.","zh":"rely on 某事，指依靠它取得幫助、支援或資訊。"},{"en":"A student may rely on a teacher’s feedback to improve an essay.","zh":"學生可能依靠老師回饋來改善文章。"},{"en":"People rely on others when their own judgement may be incomplete.","zh":"當自己的判斷可能不完整，人們會依賴他人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes depending on a source.","zh":"這個短語描述依靠某來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the observations of others","meaning":"他人的觀察","examples":[{"en":"The observations of others can be another source of knowledge.","zh":"他人的觀察可以是另一種知識來源。"},{"en":"The observations of others are things other people notice about us or a situation.","zh":"observations of others 是其他人注意到關於我們或某情況的事情。"},{"en":"A friend may notice that you look pale before you realise you are unwell.","zh":"朋友可能在你意識到自己不適前，注意到你面色蒼白。"},{"en":"Other people’s observations can confirm or challenge our own feelings.","zh":"他人的觀察可以確認或挑戰我們自己的感覺。"},{"en":"The phrase describes knowledge gained from what others see.","zh":"這個短語描述從別人所見中獲得的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"comments from friends and family","meaning":"朋友和家人的評語","examples":[{"en":"Comments from friends and family may influence how we understand illness.","zh":"朋友和家人的評語可能影響我們如何理解疾病。"},{"en":"Comments from friends and family are remarks or advice given by people close to us.","zh":"comments from friends and family 是親近的人給出的說話或意見。"},{"en":"A sister may say your cough sounds worse than last week, and that comment may make you see a doctor.","zh":"姐姐可能說你的咳嗽比上星期更嚴重，而這句評語可能令你去看醫生。"},{"en":"Such comments can be helpful because close people notice changes in our behaviour.","zh":"這些評語可以有幫助，因為親近的人會注意到我們行為上的變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes informal knowledge from personal relationships.","zh":"這個短語描述來自人際關係的非正式知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"complementary health practices","meaning":"輔助醫療療法","examples":[{"en":"Complementary health practices produce their own bodies of knowledge.","zh":"輔助醫療療法產生自己的知識體系。"},{"en":"Complementary health practices are health approaches used alongside or outside conventional medicine.","zh":"complementary health practices 是與常規醫學並行或在其以外使用的健康方法。"},{"en":"Acupuncture, massage therapy, and herbal advice may be treated as complementary health practices.","zh":"針灸、按摩治療和草藥建議可能被視為輔助醫療療法。"},{"en":"People may turn to these practices when they want additional ways to understand or manage health.","zh":"當人們想用額外方式理解或管理健康時，可能轉向這些療法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes non-mainstream health methods that may accompany medical care.","zh":"這個短語描述可配合醫療護理的非主流健康方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"holistic medicine","meaning":"整全醫學","examples":[{"en":"Holistic medicine may influence how people understand their health.","zh":"整全醫學可能影響人們如何理解自己的健康。"},{"en":"Holistic medicine is an approach that considers the whole person, including body, mind, lifestyle, and environment.","zh":"holistic medicine 是考慮整個人的方法，包括身體、心理、生活方式和環境。"},{"en":"A holistic practitioner may ask about sleep, stress, diet, and relationships, not only symptoms.","zh":"整全治療師可能詢問睡眠、壓力、飲食和關係，而不只是症狀。"},{"en":"Holistic medicine can make people connect illness with wider life patterns.","zh":"整全醫學可以令人把疾病與更廣泛的生活模式連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a whole-person approach to health.","zh":"這個短語描述以整個人為中心的健康方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"bodies of knowledge","meaning":"知識體系","examples":[{"en":"Different health practices produce their own bodies of knowledge.","zh":"不同健康療法產生自己的知識體系。"},{"en":"Bodies of knowledge are organised sets of ideas, methods, facts, and explanations in a field.","zh":"bodies of knowledge 是某領域中有組織的一套想法、方法、事實和解釋。"},{"en":"Law, medicine, and education each have their own body of knowledge.","zh":"法律、醫學和教育各有自己的知識體系。"},{"en":"A body of knowledge gives people shared language and methods for understanding problems.","zh":"知識體系給人共同語言和方法去理解問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a structured collection of knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述有結構的知識集合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"draw on","meaning":"借鑑；利用","examples":[{"en":"People may draw on different bodies of knowledge when deciding how ill they are.","zh":"人們判斷自己病得多嚴重時，可能借鑑不同知識體系。"},{"en":"To draw on something means to use it as a resource for thinking, deciding, or acting.","zh":"draw on 某物，指把它用作思考、決定或行動的資源。"},{"en":"A student may draw on class notes and personal experience when writing an essay.","zh":"學生寫文章時，可能利用課堂筆記和個人經驗。"},{"en":"Drawing on several sources can make a judgement richer but also more complicated.","zh":"借鑑多個來源可以令判斷更豐富，但也更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using available knowledge or experience.","zh":"這個短語描述使用可用知識或經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the nature and degree of","meaning":"……的性質和程度","examples":[{"en":"People consider the nature and degree of their ill health.","zh":"人們考慮自己病況的性質和程度。"},{"en":"The nature and degree of something means what kind it is and how serious or strong it is.","zh":"nature and degree of 某事，指它是甚麼種類，以及有多嚴重或強烈。"},{"en":"A teacher considers the nature and degree of a student’s mistake before deciding how to help.","zh":"老師在決定如何幫助學生前，會考慮錯誤的性質和程度。"},{"en":"In medicine, knowing the type and seriousness of a problem guides treatment.","zh":"在醫學中，知道問題的種類和嚴重程度會指引治療。"},{"en":"The phrase helps describe both quality and severity.","zh":"這個短語幫助同時描述性質和嚴重性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ill health","meaning":"健康欠佳；病況","examples":[{"en":"People draw on different knowledge when judging their ill health.","zh":"人們判斷自己的健康欠佳情況時，會借鑑不同知識。"},{"en":"Ill health means a poor or weakened state of physical or mental health.","zh":"ill health 指身體或心理健康欠佳或變弱的狀態。"},{"en":"Long working hours can contribute to ill health if people do not rest enough.","zh":"如果人們沒有足夠休息，長工時可以導致健康欠佳。"},{"en":"Judging ill health may require both personal feeling and professional advice.","zh":"判斷病況可能需要個人感覺和專業意見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes health problems in a general way.","zh":"這個短語以概括方式描述健康問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"possible treatments","meaning":"可能的治療方法","examples":[{"en":"Patients may consider possible treatments after judging their symptoms.","zh":"病人判斷症狀後，可能考慮可能的治療方法。"},{"en":"Possible treatments are the different ways a health problem might be managed or cured.","zh":"possible treatments 是處理或治癒健康問題的不同可能方法。"},{"en":"Possible treatments for a cough may include rest, medicine, further tests, or lifestyle changes.","zh":"咳嗽的可能治療方法可能包括休息、藥物、進一步檢查或生活方式改變。"},{"en":"Doctors compare treatments by considering cause, risk, cost, and likely benefit.","zh":"醫生會考慮原因、風險、成本和可能好處來比較治療方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes medical options that may be considered.","zh":"這個短語描述可被考慮的醫療選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"influential and authoritative","meaning":"有影響力且具權威性","examples":[{"en":"The doctor is an influential and authoritative source of knowledge.","zh":"醫生是有影響力且具權威性的知識來源。"},{"en":"Influential and authoritative means powerful in shaping people’s beliefs and trusted as a recognised authority.","zh":"influential and authoritative 指能強烈塑造人們信念，並被視為受認可權威。"},{"en":"A senior judge’s opinion may be influential and authoritative in a legal debate.","zh":"在法律辯論中，資深法官的意見可能有影響力且具權威性。"},{"en":"A source becomes influential when people act on it, and authoritative when society recognises its expertise.","zh":"當人們根據某來源行動，它就有影響力；當社會承認其專業，它就具權威性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong social and professional power.","zh":"這個短語描述強大的社會和專業力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"authoritative source of knowledge","meaning":"權威知識來源","examples":[{"en":"Medical knowledge is often treated as an authoritative source of knowledge.","zh":"醫學知識常被視為權威知識來源。"},{"en":"An authoritative source of knowledge is a source people trust because it has recognised expertise or official status.","zh":"authoritative source of knowledge 是人們因其受認可專業或官方地位而信任的來源。"},{"en":"A government health guideline may be an authoritative source of knowledge during a public health campaign.","zh":"在公共健康宣傳中，政府健康指引可能是權威知識來源。"},{"en":"Authoritative sources can influence decisions because people believe they are reliable.","zh":"權威來源可以影響決定，因為人們相信它們可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes knowledge that carries recognised authority.","zh":"這個短語描述帶有受認可權威的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"medical knowledge provided by","meaning":"由……提供的醫學知識","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses medical knowledge provided by the general practitioner.","zh":"文章討論由普通科醫生提供的醫學知識。"},{"en":"Medical knowledge provided by someone means health-related information, judgement, or explanation given by that person.","zh":"medical knowledge provided by 某人，指由該人給出的健康相關資訊、判斷或解釋。"},{"en":"Medical knowledge provided by a nurse may help a family understand how to care for a wound.","zh":"由護士提供的醫學知識可能幫助家庭了解如何護理傷口。"},{"en":"Such knowledge can guide treatment, rest, medication, or further testing.","zh":"這種知識可以指引治療、休息、用藥或進一步檢查。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who supplies the medical understanding.","zh":"這個短語指出誰提供醫學理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"general practitioner","meaning":"普通科醫生","examples":[{"en":"The general practitioner provides influential medical knowledge.","zh":"普通科醫生提供有影響力的醫學知識。"},{"en":"A general practitioner is a doctor who treats common health problems and refers patients to specialists when needed.","zh":"general practitioner 是治療常見健康問題，並在需要時轉介病人給專科醫生的醫生。"},{"en":"A patient with a cough, fever, or tiredness may first see a general practitioner.","zh":"有咳嗽、發燒或疲倦的病人可能先看普通科醫生。"},{"en":"General practitioners often know a patient’s medical history and can judge whether symptoms need further tests.","zh":"普通科醫生常了解病人病歷，並能判斷症狀是否需要進一步檢查。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a family doctor or primary-care doctor.","zh":"這個短語指家庭醫生或基層醫療醫生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have access to expert knowledge","meaning":"能接觸專業知識","examples":[{"en":"We expect the doctor to have access to expert knowledge.","zh":"我們期望醫生能接觸專業知識。"},{"en":"To have access to expert knowledge means to be able to use specialised information, training, or professional resources.","zh":"have access to expert knowledge 指能夠使用專門資訊、訓練或專業資源。"},{"en":"A lawyer has access to expert knowledge about legal rules that ordinary clients may not understand.","zh":"律師能接觸普通客戶未必理解的法律規則專業知識。"},{"en":"Access to expert knowledge helps professionals make decisions beyond common sense.","zh":"能接觸專業知識幫助專業人士作出超越常識的決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being able to draw on specialised understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述能運用專門理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"socially sanctioned","meaning":"得到社會認可的","examples":[{"en":"The doctor’s authority is socially sanctioned.","zh":"醫生的權威得到社會認可。"},{"en":"Socially sanctioned means accepted, approved, or supported by society.","zh":"socially sanctioned 指被社會接受、批准或支持。"},{"en":"A teacher’s right to assess homework is socially sanctioned by the school system.","zh":"老師評改功課的權利由學校制度給予社會認可。"},{"en":"When authority is socially sanctioned, people usually accept it as legitimate.","zh":"當權威得到社會認可，人們通常接受它是正當的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes approval given by social rules or institutions.","zh":"這個短語描述由社會規則或制度給予的認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"it would not be acceptable to","meaning":"……是不被接受的","examples":[{"en":"It would not be acceptable to miss work without proper medical evidence.","zh":"在沒有適當醫學證據下缺勤是不被接受的。"},{"en":"It would not be acceptable to means people would not consider the action proper, fair, or allowed.","zh":"it would not be acceptable to 指人們不會認為某行動恰當、公平或被容許。"},{"en":"It would not be acceptable to submit an assignment copied from the internet.","zh":"提交從網上抄來的功課是不被接受的。"},{"en":"A behaviour becomes unacceptable when it breaks expected rules or responsibilities.","zh":"當行為違反預期規則或責任，它就變得不被接受。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an action society or an institution would reject.","zh":"這個短語引出社會或機構會拒絕的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"notify our employer","meaning":"通知僱主","examples":[{"en":"We may need to notify our employer when we are too ill to work.","zh":"當我們病得不能工作時，可能需要通知僱主。"},{"en":"To notify our employer means to formally tell the person or organisation we work for.","zh":"notify our employer 指正式告知我們工作的那個人或機構。"},{"en":"An employee should notify the employer if illness prevents them from attending work.","zh":"如果疾病使員工不能上班，他應通知僱主。"},{"en":"Notification helps the workplace arrange cover and keep records.","zh":"通知有助工作場所安排替補和保存記錄。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving official information to a workplace.","zh":"這個短語描述向工作場所提供正式資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"turn up for work","meaning":"上班；出現於工作崗位","examples":[{"en":"A sick employee may be unable to turn up for work.","zh":"生病員工可能無法上班。"},{"en":"To turn up for work means to arrive at the workplace as expected.","zh":"turn up for work 指按預期到達工作場所。"},{"en":"A bus driver must turn up for work on time because passengers depend on the service.","zh":"巴士司機必須準時上班，因為乘客依賴該服務。"},{"en":"If someone cannot turn up for work, the employer may need evidence or notice.","zh":"如果某人不能上班，僱主可能需要證據或通知。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physically attending work.","zh":"這個短語描述親身出現在工作崗位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"faith healer","meaning":"信仰治療師","examples":[{"en":"A faith healer is not normally accepted as a source of workplace medical proof.","zh":"信仰治療師通常不被接受為職場醫學證明來源。"},{"en":"A faith healer is someone who claims to heal illness through religious belief or spiritual power.","zh":"faith healer 是聲稱透過宗教信念或精神力量治病的人。"},{"en":"A person may visit a faith healer for comfort, but an employer may still require a doctor’s certificate.","zh":"一個人可能為了安慰而找信仰治療師，但僱主仍可能要求醫生證明。"},{"en":"Faith healing may matter to some people personally, but it lacks the same official status as medical diagnosis.","zh":"信仰治療對某些人個人上可能重要，但它沒有醫學診斷同等官方地位。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a religious or spiritual healer rather than a conventional medical doctor.","zh":"這個短語描述宗教或精神治療者，而不是常規醫生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"astrologer","meaning":"占星師","examples":[{"en":"An astrologer’s opinion would not usually justify sick leave.","zh":"占星師的意見通常不能為病假提供理由。"},{"en":"An astrologer is someone who interprets the positions of stars and planets to give advice or predictions.","zh":"astrologer 是解讀星體和行星位置，以給予建議或預測的人。"},{"en":"A person might ask an astrologer about luck or relationships, but not normally for medical certification.","zh":"一個人可能向占星師詢問運氣或關係，但通常不會要求醫療證明。"},{"en":"Society does not usually treat astrology as an official source of medical knowledge.","zh":"社會通常不把占星視為官方醫學知識來源。"},{"en":"The word refers to a person connected with astrology, not astronomy.","zh":"這個詞指與占星術有關的人，而不是天文學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"therapist","meaning":"治療師","examples":[{"en":"A therapist may offer support, but the employer may still require medical certification.","zh":"治療師可能提供支援，但僱主仍可能要求醫療證明。"},{"en":"A therapist is a professional who helps people with mental, emotional, physical, or behavioural problems.","zh":"therapist 是幫助人處理心理、情緒、身體或行為問題的專業人士。"},{"en":"A person may see a therapist to manage anxiety after a stressful period at work.","zh":"一個人在工作壓力大的一段時間後，可能見治療師處理焦慮。"},{"en":"A therapist’s support can be valuable, but workplace rules may still require formal medical documents.","zh":"治療師的支援可以很有價值，但職場規則仍可能要求正式醫療文件。"},{"en":"The word describes a helping professional, though the exact role depends on the field.","zh":"這個詞描述提供幫助的專業人士，但具體角色視領域而定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"priest","meaning":"神父；牧師","examples":[{"en":"A priest’s advice would not usually replace a medical diagnosis.","zh":"神父或牧師的建議通常不能取代醫學診斷。"},{"en":"A priest is a religious leader who performs spiritual duties and gives religious guidance.","zh":"priest 是履行宗教職責並給予宗教指引的宗教領袖。"},{"en":"A patient may speak to a priest for comfort during serious illness.","zh":"病人在嚴重疾病期間，可能向神父或牧師尋求安慰。"},{"en":"Spiritual advice may help emotionally, but it normally does not count as medical proof.","zh":"精神上的建議可能在情緒上有幫助，但通常不算醫學證明。"},{"en":"The word refers to a religious figure, not a medical expert.","zh":"這個詞指宗教人物，而不是醫學專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"expert medical diagnosis","meaning":"專業醫學診斷","examples":[{"en":"An expert medical diagnosis is needed for extended sick leave.","zh":"長期病假需要專業醫學診斷。"},{"en":"An expert medical diagnosis is a professional judgement about illness made by a qualified medical expert.","zh":"expert medical diagnosis 是由合資格醫學專家作出的疾病專業判斷。"},{"en":"A worker may need an expert medical diagnosis before taking several weeks away from work.","zh":"工人在請幾星期假前，可能需要專業醫學診斷。"},{"en":"Such a diagnosis helps institutions distinguish serious illness from ordinary tiredness.","zh":"這種診斷幫助機構區分嚴重疾病與普通疲倦。"},{"en":"The phrase describes medical confirmation with professional authority.","zh":"這個短語描述具有專業權威的醫學確認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"obtain the necessary certificate","meaning":"取得所需證明書","examples":[{"en":"Patients may need to obtain the necessary certificate for time off work.","zh":"病人可能需要取得請假不上班所需的證明書。"},{"en":"To obtain the necessary certificate means to get the official document required for a purpose.","zh":"obtain the necessary certificate 指取得某目的所需的官方文件。"},{"en":"An employee may need to obtain the necessary certificate after several days of sick leave.","zh":"員工請病假幾天後，可能需要取得所需證明書。"},{"en":"Without the certificate, an employer may not accept the absence as properly supported.","zh":"沒有證明書，僱主可能不接受缺勤有適當支持。"},{"en":"The phrase describes getting required official proof.","zh":"這個短語描述取得所需官方證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"statutory self-certification period","meaning":"法定自我申報病假期","examples":[{"en":"The patient may need a certificate after the statutory self-certification period.","zh":"病人可能在法定自我申報病假期後需要證明書。"},{"en":"A statutory self-certification period is a legally defined time when employees can declare their own sickness without a doctor’s certificate.","zh":"statutory self-certification period 是法律規定員工可自行申報病假而毋須醫生證明的時期。"},{"en":"After this period, a worker may need medical proof to continue sick leave.","zh":"過了這段時期，工人可能需要醫學證明才能繼續病假。"},{"en":"The rule balances trust in employees with employers’ need for official evidence.","zh":"這條規則平衡對員工的信任與僱主對官方證據的需要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a legally recognised sickness-reporting period.","zh":"這個短語描述法律認可的病假申報期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"medical sciences","meaning":"醫學科學","examples":[{"en":"The knowledge of the medical sciences is privileged in contemporary Western culture.","zh":"醫學科學的知識在當代西方文化中享有特殊地位。"},{"en":"Medical sciences are scientific fields that study health, disease, treatment, the body, and medical evidence.","zh":"medical sciences 是研究健康、疾病、治療、身體和醫學證據的科學領域。"},{"en":"Biology, pathology, pharmacology, and clinical research all contribute to the medical sciences.","zh":"生物學、病理學、藥理學和臨床研究都對醫學科學有貢獻。"},{"en":"Medical sciences gain authority because they use research, testing, and professional training.","zh":"醫學科學因使用研究、測試和專業訓練而取得權威。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to scientific knowledge connected with medicine.","zh":"這個短語指與醫學相關的科學知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be privileged in this respect","meaning":"在這方面享有特殊地位","examples":[{"en":"Medical knowledge is privileged in this respect in Western culture.","zh":"醫學知識在西方文化中，在這方面享有特殊地位。"},{"en":"To be privileged in this respect means to be given special authority or higher status in this particular way.","zh":"be privileged in this respect 指在這個特定方面獲給予特殊權威或較高地位。"},{"en":"In exams, written evidence may be privileged in this respect over personal memory.","zh":"在考試中，書面證據在這方面可能比個人記憶享有特殊地位。"},{"en":"A type of knowledge becomes privileged when institutions trust it more than other sources.","zh":"當制度比其他來源更信任某類知識，它就會享有特殊地位。"},{"en":"The phrase describes special social or institutional status.","zh":"這個短語描述特殊的社會或制度地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"contemporary Western culture","meaning":"當代西方文化","examples":[{"en":"Medical sciences are privileged in contemporary Western culture.","zh":"醫學科學在當代西方文化中享有特殊地位。"},{"en":"Contemporary Western culture means present-day culture in many Western societies.","zh":"contemporary Western culture 指許多西方社會中的現代文化。"},{"en":"Contemporary Western culture often values scientific evidence, professional credentials, and official documents.","zh":"當代西方文化常重視科學證據、專業資格和官方文件。"},{"en":"Cultural values affect which kinds of knowledge people treat as reliable.","zh":"文化價值會影響人們把哪些知識視為可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the modern Western social context.","zh":"這個短語描述現代西方社會語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"medical practitioners","meaning":"醫生；醫療從業員","examples":[{"en":"Medical practitioners have the authority to prescribe drugs.","zh":"醫療從業員有權處方藥物。"},{"en":"Medical practitioners are trained healthcare professionals who diagnose, treat, or care for patients.","zh":"medical practitioners 是受過訓練、診斷、治療或照顧病人的醫療專業人士。"},{"en":"Doctors and some other qualified health professionals are medical practitioners.","zh":"醫生和某些其他合資格健康專業人士都是醫療從業員。"},{"en":"Medical practitioners are trusted because society recognises their training and legal responsibilities.","zh":"醫療從業員受到信任，因為社會承認他們的訓練和法律責任。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people officially practising medicine or healthcare.","zh":"這個短語指正式從事醫學或醫療護理的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be seen as having","meaning":"被視為擁有……","examples":[{"en":"Doctors are seen as having expert knowledge.","zh":"醫生被視為擁有專業知識。"},{"en":"To be seen as having something means to be regarded or treated as possessing it.","zh":"be seen as having 某物，指被認為或被看待為擁有它。"},{"en":"A headteacher may be seen as having authority over school rules.","zh":"校長可能被視為擁有管理校規的權威。"},{"en":"When people are seen as having expertise, others are more likely to follow their advice.","zh":"當人被視為擁有專業知識，別人較可能跟從其建議。"},{"en":"The phrase describes public or social perception.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾或社會看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"legally prescribe","meaning":"合法處方","examples":[{"en":"Doctors can legally prescribe drugs and treatments.","zh":"醫生可以合法處方藥物和治療方法。"},{"en":"To legally prescribe something means to officially order or provide it within the law.","zh":"legally prescribe 某物，指在法律範圍內正式開出或提供它。"},{"en":"A doctor can legally prescribe antibiotics if the patient needs them.","zh":"如果病人需要，醫生可以合法處方抗生素。"},{"en":"Legal permission protects patients because powerful medicines must be controlled.","zh":"法律許可保護病人，因為強效藥物必須受控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes medical prescribing allowed by law.","zh":"這個短語描述法律容許的醫療處方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"drugs and treatments","meaning":"藥物和治療方法","examples":[{"en":"Patients may not otherwise have access to certain drugs and treatments.","zh":"病人否則可能無法取得某些藥物和治療方法。"},{"en":"Drugs and treatments are medicines, procedures, therapies, or medical actions used to manage illness.","zh":"drugs and treatments 是用來處理疾病的藥物、程序、療法或醫療行動。"},{"en":"A patient with pneumonia may receive drugs and treatments such as antibiotics, rest, and monitoring.","zh":"患肺炎的病人可能接受抗生素、休息和監察等藥物和治療方法。"},{"en":"Some drugs and treatments require professional approval because they can affect the body strongly.","zh":"有些藥物和治療方法需要專業批准，因為它們可以強烈影響身體。"},{"en":"The phrase describes medical options used to treat health problems.","zh":"這個短語描述用於治療健康問題的醫療選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"would not otherwise have access to","meaning":"否則無法取得……","examples":[{"en":"Patients would not otherwise have access to some treatments.","zh":"病人否則無法取得某些治療方法。"},{"en":"Would not otherwise have access to means would not be able to get or use something without a particular condition.","zh":"would not otherwise have access to 指如果沒有某個條件，就無法取得或使用某物。"},{"en":"A student may not otherwise have access to expensive textbooks without a school library.","zh":"如果沒有學校圖書館，學生可能否則無法取得昂貴教科書。"},{"en":"Medical approval can give patients access to treatments they cannot obtain alone.","zh":"醫學批准可以讓病人取得自己無法獲得的治療。"},{"en":"The phrase explains that access depends on another factor.","zh":"這個短語解釋取得某物取決於另一因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a range of different knowledge","meaning":"一系列不同知識","examples":[{"en":"People draw on a range of different knowledge about health.","zh":"人們借鑑一系列關於健康的不同知識。"},{"en":"A range of different knowledge means several types of information, experience, or understanding.","zh":"range of different knowledge 指幾種類型的資訊、經驗或理解。"},{"en":"A patient may use a range of different knowledge, including symptoms, family advice, and medical tests.","zh":"病人可能使用一系列不同知識，包括症狀、家人意見和醫學檢查。"},{"en":"Using a range of knowledge can improve judgement, but it can also create conflicting explanations.","zh":"使用一系列知識可以改善判斷，但也可能造成互相衝突的解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broad set of knowledge sources.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛的知識來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make decisions about","meaning":"就……作出決定","examples":[{"en":"People make decisions about their own state of health.","zh":"人們就自己的健康狀況作出決定。"},{"en":"To make decisions about something means to choose what to believe or do concerning it.","zh":"make decisions about 某事，指就它選擇相信甚麼或做甚麼。"},{"en":"A parent may make decisions about a child’s diet after reading medical advice.","zh":"家長閱讀醫療建議後，可能就孩子飲食作出決定。"},{"en":"Decisions about health can affect treatment, rest, work, and family responsibilities.","zh":"關於健康的決定可以影響治療、休息、工作和家庭責任。"},{"en":"The phrase describes choosing a course of action or judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇行動方向或判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"state of health","meaning":"健康狀況","examples":[{"en":"People use different sources of knowledge to judge their state of health.","zh":"人們使用不同知識來源來判斷自己的健康狀況。"},{"en":"State of health means a person’s overall condition of being healthy, ill, weak, or recovering.","zh":"state of health 指一個人整體處於健康、生病、虛弱或康復的狀態。"},{"en":"A doctor may ask questions about sleep, appetite, pain, and energy to judge a patient’s state of health.","zh":"醫生可能詢問睡眠、食慾、疼痛和精力，以判斷病人的健康狀況。"},{"en":"A person’s state of health can change gradually or suddenly.","zh":"一個人的健康狀況可以逐漸或突然改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes someone’s general health condition.","zh":"這個短語描述某人的整體健康情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"existing knowledge","meaning":"既有知識","examples":[{"en":"The story involves more than existing knowledge.","zh":"這個故事涉及的不只是既有知識。"},{"en":"Existing knowledge is knowledge that is already available before a new case or situation appears.","zh":"existing knowledge 是新個案或情況出現前已經可用的知識。"},{"en":"A doctor uses existing knowledge from textbooks and past patients when meeting a new patient.","zh":"醫生面對新病人時，會使用來自教科書和過往病人的既有知識。"},{"en":"New cases can test, extend, or change existing knowledge.","zh":"新個案可以測試、擴展或改變既有知識。"},{"en":"The phrase describes knowledge that already exists before new interpretation begins.","zh":"這個短語描述新詮釋開始前已存在的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"new knowledge is constructed","meaning":"新知識被建構出來","examples":[{"en":"New knowledge is constructed through diagnosis and interpretation.","zh":"新知識透過診斷和詮釋被建構出來。"},{"en":"New knowledge is constructed means new understanding is built through thinking, evidence, and explanation.","zh":"new knowledge is constructed 指透過思考、證據和解釋建立新的理解。"},{"en":"A teacher constructs new knowledge about a student after observing how she learns in class.","zh":"老師觀察學生如何在課堂中學習後，會建構出關於該學生的新知識。"},{"en":"Diagnosis creates knowledge by connecting symptoms, evidence, and professional judgement.","zh":"診斷透過連接症狀、證據和專業判斷來創造知識。"},{"en":"The phrase describes knowledge being actively built, not simply found.","zh":"這個短語描述知識被主動建立，而不是單純被發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"medical training and background","meaning":"醫學訓練和背景","examples":[{"en":"The doctor’s medical training and background shape her hypothesis.","zh":"醫生的醫學訓練和背景塑造她的假設。"},{"en":"Medical training and background mean the doctor’s education, professional preparation, and past clinical experience.","zh":"medical training and background 指醫生的教育、專業準備和過往臨床經驗。"},{"en":"A doctor’s medical training and background help her recognise patterns in symptoms.","zh":"醫生的醫學訓練和背景幫助她辨認症狀中的模式。"},{"en":"This background affects which illness she considers likely and which evidence she checks.","zh":"這種背景影響她認為哪種疾病較可能，以及她檢查哪些證據。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what supports professional medical judgement.","zh":"這個短語解釋甚麼支持專業醫學判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"hypothesise","meaning":"提出假設","examples":[{"en":"The doctor may hypothesise that the patient has pneumonia.","zh":"醫生可能提出假設，認為病人患上肺炎。"},{"en":"To hypothesise means to suggest a possible explanation that still needs evidence.","zh":"hypothesise 指提出仍需要證據支持的可能解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may hypothesise that poor test results were caused by unclear instructions.","zh":"老師可能提出假設，認為測驗成績差是由指示不清造成。"},{"en":"A hypothesis guides what evidence people look for next.","zh":"假設會引導人們下一步尋找甚麼證據。"},{"en":"The word describes forming a testable explanation.","zh":"這個詞描述形成可測試的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"look for evidence","meaning":"尋找證據","examples":[{"en":"The doctor looks for evidence to support or reject the hypothesis.","zh":"醫生尋找證據來支持或否定該假設。"},{"en":"To look for evidence means to search for facts, signs, or data that help judge a claim.","zh":"look for evidence 指尋找幫助判斷某主張的事實、跡象或數據。"},{"en":"A student should look for evidence in the passage before choosing a reading answer.","zh":"學生在選擇閱讀答案前，應在文章中尋找證據。"},{"en":"Evidence can confirm a first idea or show that it needs to be changed.","zh":"證據可以確認最初想法，或顯示它需要改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the search for support before deciding.","zh":"這個短語描述在決定前尋找支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"observations and instruments","meaning":"觀察和儀器","examples":[{"en":"The doctor uses observations and instruments to assess the evidence.","zh":"醫生使用觀察和儀器來評估證據。"},{"en":"Observations and instruments are what the doctor notices directly and the tools used to measure signs.","zh":"observations and instruments 是醫生直接注意到的東西，以及用來量度徵象的工具。"},{"en":"A thermometer, stethoscope, and blood pressure monitor are instruments that support medical observation.","zh":"體溫計、聽診器和血壓計都是支援醫學觀察的儀器。"},{"en":"Combining observation with instruments can make judgement more reliable.","zh":"把觀察與儀器結合，可以令判斷更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both human noticing and technical measurement.","zh":"這個短語描述人的注意和技術量度兩者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"assess the evidence","meaning":"評估證據","examples":[{"en":"The doctor assesses the evidence before making a diagnosis.","zh":"醫生作出診斷前評估證據。"},{"en":"To assess the evidence means to examine information carefully and judge what it shows.","zh":"assess the evidence 指仔細檢視資訊並判斷它顯示甚麼。"},{"en":"A teacher assesses the evidence before deciding whether a student has improved.","zh":"老師在判斷學生是否進步前，會評估證據。"},{"en":"Careful assessment reduces the risk of jumping to the wrong conclusion.","zh":"仔細評估可以降低貿然得出錯誤結論的風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evaluating evidence before making a judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述在作出判斷前評價證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"critically","meaning":"關鍵地；審慎地","examples":[{"en":"The doctor must critically interpret the evidence.","zh":"醫生必須審慎地詮釋證據。"},{"en":"Critically means carefully, thoughtfully, and with attention to possible errors or weaknesses.","zh":"critically 指仔細、深思熟慮，並注意可能錯誤或弱點。"},{"en":"Students should critically read online health advice before trusting it.","zh":"學生在相信網上健康建議前，應審慎閱讀。"},{"en":"Thinking critically helps people avoid accepting the first explanation too quickly.","zh":"批判性思考幫助人避免太快接受第一個解釋。"},{"en":"The word describes careful judgement rather than simple criticism.","zh":"這個詞描述仔細判斷，而不只是批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"interpret it in the light of","meaning":"根據……來詮釋","examples":[{"en":"The doctor interprets the evidence in the light of her training and experience.","zh":"醫生根據自己的訓練和經驗來詮釋證據。"},{"en":"To interpret something in the light of something else means to understand it using that background or information.","zh":"interpret something in the light of 其他東西，指使用該背景或資訊來理解某事。"},{"en":"A teacher interprets a student’s silence in the light of knowing the student is usually shy.","zh":"老師知道學生平時害羞，因此根據這一背景來詮釋學生的沉默。"},{"en":"The same evidence can mean different things when interpreted through different background knowledge.","zh":"同一證據透過不同背景知識詮釋，可以有不同意思。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using context to explain evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述使用語境來解釋證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"training and experience","meaning":"訓練和經驗","examples":[{"en":"The doctor interprets evidence through training and experience.","zh":"醫生透過訓練和經驗詮釋證據。"},{"en":"Training and experience mean formal learning plus practical knowledge gained from real work.","zh":"training and experience 指正式學習加上從實際工作獲得的實用知識。"},{"en":"A firefighter uses training and experience to decide how to enter a burning building safely.","zh":"消防員使用訓練和經驗，決定如何安全進入燃燒中的建築物。"},{"en":"Professional judgement becomes stronger when training is tested by experience.","zh":"當訓練被經驗檢驗，專業判斷會變得更強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the two foundations of skilled decision-making.","zh":"這個短語描述熟練決策的兩個基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"create new knowledge","meaning":"創造新知識","examples":[{"en":"The diagnosis creates new knowledge for both the patient and the doctor.","zh":"診斷為病人和醫生都創造新知識。"},{"en":"To create new knowledge means to produce new understanding that did not exist before.","zh":"create new knowledge 指產生以前不存在的新理解。"},{"en":"A classroom experiment can create new knowledge when students discover why plants grow better in light.","zh":"當學生發現植物為何在光照下長得更好，課堂實驗就能創造新知識。"},{"en":"New knowledge can come from connecting evidence with expert interpretation.","zh":"新知識可以來自把證據與專家詮釋連接起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes knowledge being produced through inquiry.","zh":"這個短語描述知識透過探究被產生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be added to","meaning":"被加入……","examples":[{"en":"The case may be added to the doctor’s medical knowledge.","zh":"這個個案可能被加入醫生的醫學知識中。"},{"en":"To be added to something means to become part of a larger collection or body of information.","zh":"be added to 某物，指成為較大集合或資訊體系的一部分。"},{"en":"A new example may be added to a teacher’s notes after a student asks a useful question.","zh":"學生提出有用問題後，老師筆記中可能加入一個新例子。"},{"en":"Each case can add to experience and help future judgement.","zh":"每個個案都可以增加經驗，並幫助日後判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one piece joining a wider set.","zh":"這個短語描述一部分加入更廣闊集合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"future diagnoses","meaning":"日後的診斷","examples":[{"en":"The new knowledge may help in future diagnoses of pneumonia.","zh":"新知識可能有助日後的肺炎診斷。"},{"en":"Future diagnoses are medical judgements that will be made in later cases.","zh":"future diagnoses 是在後來個案中作出的醫學判斷。"},{"en":"A doctor’s experience with one unusual patient may help future diagnoses of similar symptoms.","zh":"醫生處理一名不尋常病人的經驗，可能幫助日後對相似症狀的診斷。"},{"en":"Learning from past cases can improve later medical decisions.","zh":"從過往個案中學習，可以改善後來醫療決定。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to diagnoses made in the future.","zh":"這個短語指將來作出的診斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"diagnoses of pneumonia","meaning":"肺炎診斷","examples":[{"en":"The case may help the doctor make future diagnoses of pneumonia.","zh":"這個個案可能幫助醫生日後作出肺炎診斷。"},{"en":"Diagnoses of pneumonia are medical decisions identifying pneumonia as the patient’s illness.","zh":"diagnoses of pneumonia 是確認肺炎為病人疾病的醫學決定。"},{"en":"A doctor may compare a new cough case with earlier diagnoses of pneumonia.","zh":"醫生可能把新的咳嗽個案與以往肺炎診斷作比較。"},{"en":"More experience with pneumonia can help doctors recognise warning signs faster.","zh":"更多處理肺炎的經驗，可以幫助醫生更快辨認警號。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cases where pneumonia is medically identified.","zh":"這個短語描述在醫學上確認肺炎的個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"contain the following information","meaning":"包含以下資料","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which paragraph contains the following information.","zh":"學生辨認哪一段包含以下資料。"},{"en":"Contain the following information means include the details listed in the question.","zh":"contain the following information 指包括題目列出的細節。"},{"en":"A reading question may ask which paragraph contains information about the patient’s diagnosis.","zh":"閱讀題可能問哪一段包含關於病人診斷的資料。"},{"en":"Students should scan for meaning, not just identical words.","zh":"學生應搜尋意思，而不只是相同字眼。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction for matching paragraphs to information.","zh":"這個短語是把段落與資料配對的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the contrast between","meaning":"……之間的對比","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the contrast between personal judgement and medical diagnosis.","zh":"題目問個人判斷與醫學診斷之間的對比。"},{"en":"The contrast between two things means the clear difference between them.","zh":"contrast between 兩事物，指它們之間清楚的差異。"},{"en":"The contrast between a student’s guess and the teacher’s answer can show where misunderstanding begins.","zh":"學生猜測與老師答案之間的對比，可以顯示誤解從哪裏開始。"},{"en":"Contrast helps readers understand why two ideas should not be treated as the same.","zh":"對比幫助讀者理解為何兩個想法不應被視為相同。"},{"en":"The phrase describes comparison through difference.","zh":"這個短語描述透過差異進行比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"personal judgement","meaning":"個人判斷","examples":[{"en":"Personal judgement may differ from a doctor’s diagnosis.","zh":"個人判斷可能與醫生診斷不同。"},{"en":"Personal judgement is an opinion or decision based on one’s own experience, feelings, or reasoning.","zh":"personal judgement 是基於自己的經驗、感受或推理作出的意見或決定。"},{"en":"A worker may personally judge that tiredness is caused by overtime, not illness.","zh":"工人可能個人判斷疲倦由加班造成，而不是疾病。"},{"en":"Personal judgement can be useful, but it may lack professional evidence.","zh":"個人判斷可以有用，但可能缺乏專業證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes individual interpretation rather than expert confirmation.","zh":"這個短語描述個人詮釋，而不是專家確認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a doctor’s diagnosis","meaning":"醫生的診斷","examples":[{"en":"A doctor’s diagnosis has a different status from personal judgement.","zh":"醫生的診斷與個人判斷有不同地位。"},{"en":"A doctor’s diagnosis is a professional medical identification of an illness or condition.","zh":"doctor’s diagnosis 是對疾病或狀況的專業醫學確認。"},{"en":"A patient may feel tired, but a doctor’s diagnosis can show whether the cause is infection, stress, or something else.","zh":"病人可能感到疲倦，但醫生的診斷可以顯示原因是感染、壓力還是其他問題。"},{"en":"A doctor’s diagnosis often carries official weight in workplaces and institutions.","zh":"醫生的診斷在工作場所和機構中常具有官方分量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes medically recognised judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述受醫學認可的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a reference to","meaning":"提及……","examples":[{"en":"The task asks for a reference to cultural ideas about stress.","zh":"題目要求找出提及關於壓力的文化觀念。"},{"en":"A reference to something is a mention of that thing in speech or writing.","zh":"reference to 某事，是在說話或寫作中提到該事。"},{"en":"A reading question may ask for a reference to the patient’s first visit to the doctor.","zh":"閱讀題可能要求找出提及病人第一次看醫生的地方。"},{"en":"Finding a reference often requires noticing a paraphrase, not the exact same words.","zh":"找出提及某事之處常需要注意改寫，而不是完全相同字眼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a point in the text where something is mentioned.","zh":"這個短語描述文本中提到某事的一點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"cultural ideas about stress","meaning":"關於壓力的文化觀念","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses cultural ideas about stress.","zh":"文章討論關於壓力的文化觀念。"},{"en":"Cultural ideas about stress are beliefs a society shares about what stress is and how it affects people.","zh":"cultural ideas about stress 是一個社會共同持有、關於壓力是甚麼及如何影響人的信念。"},{"en":"A culture may teach people to see tiredness as stress rather than illness.","zh":"一種文化可能教人把疲倦視為壓力，而不是疾病。"},{"en":"Cultural ideas can influence how people explain symptoms and seek help.","zh":"文化觀念可以影響人們如何解釋症狀和尋求幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase describes society’s shared understanding of stress.","zh":"這個短語描述社會對壓力的共同理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"sick leave","meaning":"病假","examples":[{"en":"Sick leave may require a professional medical diagnosis.","zh":"病假可能需要專業醫學診斷。"},{"en":"Sick leave is authorised time away from work because of illness.","zh":"sick leave 是因疾病而獲准暫時不上班的時間。"},{"en":"An employee may take sick leave when pneumonia makes it impossible to work safely.","zh":"當肺炎使員工無法安全工作，他可能請病假。"},{"en":"Workplaces often require rules for sick leave so absence can be recorded fairly.","zh":"工作場所常需要病假規則，以便公平記錄缺勤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes illness-related absence from work.","zh":"這個短語描述與疾病有關的工作缺席。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be permitted without","meaning":"在沒有……的情況下獲准","examples":[{"en":"Sick leave may not be permitted without professional diagnosis.","zh":"病假在沒有專業診斷的情況下可能不獲准。"},{"en":"To be permitted without something means to be allowed even though that thing is absent.","zh":"be permitted without 某物，指即使沒有該物仍被允許。"},{"en":"Students may not be permitted without a signed form to join a school trip.","zh":"學生在沒有簽署表格的情況下，可能不獲准參加學校旅行。"},{"en":"Institutions often require proof before they permit special arrangements.","zh":"機構常在允許特別安排前要求證明。"},{"en":"The phrase describes permission depending on a required condition.","zh":"這個短語描述許可取決於所需條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"professional diagnosis","meaning":"專業診斷","examples":[{"en":"An employer may require a professional diagnosis for sick leave.","zh":"僱主可能要求病假有專業診斷。"},{"en":"A professional diagnosis is a health judgement made by a qualified medical professional.","zh":"professional diagnosis 是由合資格醫療專業人士作出的健康判斷。"},{"en":"A patient’s own feeling may start the process, but a professional diagnosis gives official confirmation.","zh":"病人的個人感覺可能開始整個過程，但專業診斷提供官方確認。"},{"en":"Workplaces may rely on professional diagnosis to decide whether extended leave is justified.","zh":"工作場所可能依賴專業診斷來決定長期病假是否有理據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes diagnosis with recognised professional authority.","zh":"這個短語描述具有受認可專業權威的診斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be regarded in society","meaning":"在社會中被看待","examples":[{"en":"The question asks how doctors’ opinions are regarded in society.","zh":"題目問醫生的意見在社會中如何被看待。"},{"en":"To be regarded in society means to be viewed, valued, or treated by the wider community.","zh":"be regarded in society 指被更廣泛社群如何看待、重視或對待。"},{"en":"Teachers are often regarded in society as responsible for children’s learning and behaviour.","zh":"老師在社會中常被看作負責孩子學習和行為的人。"},{"en":"How something is regarded affects how much authority it has.","zh":"某事如何被看待，會影響它有多少權威。"},{"en":"The phrase describes social perception and status.","zh":"這個短語描述社會看法和地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"contribute to new knowledge","meaning":"有助產生新知識","examples":[{"en":"A patient’s illness can contribute to new knowledge.","zh":"病人的疾病可以有助產生新知識。"},{"en":"To contribute to new knowledge means to help create or add to understanding.","zh":"contribute to new knowledge 指幫助創造或增加理解。"},{"en":"A classroom experiment can contribute to new knowledge when it reveals why students make the same mistake.","zh":"課堂實驗如果揭示學生為何犯同一錯誤，就能有助產生新知識。"},{"en":"Individual cases can teach professionals patterns they may use later.","zh":"個別個案可以教專業人士日後可能使用的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes helping knowledge grow.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助知識增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"non-specialised sources","meaning":"非專業來源","examples":[{"en":"Some knowledge is drawn from non-specialised sources.","zh":"有些知識來自非專業來源。"},{"en":"Non-specialised sources are sources that do not come from trained experts or formal professional fields.","zh":"non-specialised sources 是不來自受訓專家或正式專業領域的來源。"},{"en":"Friends, family, media stories, and common sense can be non-specialised sources.","zh":"朋友、家人、傳媒故事和常識都可以是非專業來源。"},{"en":"These sources may be helpful, but they may not have the same authority as expert evidence.","zh":"這些來源可能有幫助，但未必有專家證據同等權威。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ordinary, informal sources of knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述普通、非正式的知識來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"other than personal knowledge","meaning":"個人知識以外的","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to sources other than personal knowledge.","zh":"題目指個人知識以外的來源。"},{"en":"Other than personal knowledge means apart from what someone knows through direct experience.","zh":"other than personal knowledge 指除了某人透過直接經驗知道的東西以外。"},{"en":"A patient may use sources other than personal knowledge, such as test results or a doctor’s advice.","zh":"病人可能使用個人知識以外的來源，例如檢查結果或醫生建議。"},{"en":"Looking beyond personal knowledge can reduce mistakes caused by subjective feeling alone.","zh":"超越個人知識可以減少只靠主觀感覺造成的錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase separates personal experience from other sources.","zh":"這個短語把個人經驗與其他來源分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"combine personal experience with","meaning":"將個人經驗與……結合","examples":[{"en":"The example combines personal experience with a professional diagnosis.","zh":"這個例子將個人經驗與專業診斷結合。"},{"en":"To combine personal experience with something means to bring one’s own feelings together with another source of knowledge.","zh":"combine personal experience with 某物，指把自己的感覺與另一種知識來源放在一起。"},{"en":"A patient combines personal experience with medical advice when she explains pain and then listens to the doctor’s assessment.","zh":"病人解釋疼痛再聽醫生評估時，就是將個人經驗與醫療建議結合。"},{"en":"Combining these sources can create a fuller understanding than either source alone.","zh":"結合這些來源可以產生比單一來源更完整的理解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes joining subjective experience with another form of evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述把主觀經驗與另一種證據結合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"professional diagnosis","meaning":"專業診斷","examples":[{"en":"The patient’s experience is combined with a professional diagnosis.","zh":"病人的經驗與專業診斷結合起來。"},{"en":"A professional diagnosis is a medical judgement made by someone qualified to assess illness.","zh":"professional diagnosis 是由有資格評估疾病的人作出的醫學判斷。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may feel personal, but a professional diagnosis may show an infection.","zh":"學生的疲倦可能是個人感覺，但專業診斷可能顯示感染。"},{"en":"Professional diagnosis can turn uncertain symptoms into a recognised medical condition.","zh":"專業診斷可以把不確定症狀轉化為受認可的醫療狀況。"},{"en":"The phrase describes expert confirmation of illness.","zh":"這個短語描述對疾病的專家確認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"realise they are ill","meaning":"意識到自己生病","examples":[{"en":"Some people do not realise they are ill until the disease has progressed.","zh":"有些人直到疾病已經進展後才意識到自己生病。"},{"en":"To realise they are ill means to become aware that they have a sickness or medical condition.","zh":"realise they are ill 指察覺自己患有疾病或醫療狀況。"},{"en":"A person may not realise they are ill if symptoms feel like ordinary tiredness.","zh":"如果症狀感覺像普通疲倦，一個人可能沒有意識到自己生病。"},{"en":"Late realisation can delay treatment and make recovery harder.","zh":"太遲察覺可以延誤治療並令康復更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes becoming aware of illness.","zh":"這個短語描述對疾病產生覺察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"complete the notes below","meaning":"完成以下筆記","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the notes below using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成以下筆記。"},{"en":"Complete the notes below means fill in missing information in the notes under the question.","zh":"complete the notes below 指填寫題目下方筆記中的缺失資料。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students complete notes by finding the exact part of the passage that gives the answer.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過找出文章中提供答案的準確部分來完成筆記。"},{"en":"Checking grammar around each blank helps prevent wrong word forms.","zh":"檢查每個空格周圍的文法，有助避免錯誤詞形。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction for note-completion tasks.","zh":"這個短語是筆記填充題中的常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個詞","examples":[{"en":"The instruction says to choose no more than three words from the passage.","zh":"指示說要從文章中選擇不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案必須包含三個詞或以下。"},{"en":"“Professional medical diagnosis” has three words, so it fits this instruction.","zh":"“professional medical diagnosis” 有三個詞，所以符合這個指示。"},{"en":"Writing four words may lose marks even if the meaning is close.","zh":"即使意思接近，寫四個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit for exam answers.","zh":"這個短語為考試答案設定嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"from the passage","meaning":"來自文章","examples":[{"en":"The answers must be taken from the passage.","zh":"答案必須來自文章。"},{"en":"From the passage means the answer must come directly from the reading text, not from personal knowledge.","zh":"from the passage 指答案必須直接來自閱讀文本，而不是來自個人知識。"},{"en":"A student should copy the correct word from the passage if the question gives a word limit.","zh":"如果題目有字數限制，學生應從文章中抄出正確字詞。"},{"en":"Using outside knowledge can be wrong if the passage does not support it.","zh":"如果文章不支持，使用外部知識可能是錯的。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds candidates to rely on textual evidence.","zh":"這個短語提醒考生依賴文本證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"personal experience","meaning":"個人經驗","examples":[{"en":"Personal experience is one source of knowledge about illness.","zh":"個人經驗是關於疾病的一種知識來源。"},{"en":"Personal experience is what someone learns from their own feelings, actions, or events.","zh":"personal experience 是某人從自己的感覺、行動或事件中學到的東西。"},{"en":"A patient’s personal experience of pain helps the doctor understand what the test results cannot show alone.","zh":"病人對疼痛的個人經驗，幫助醫生理解單靠檢查結果無法顯示的內容。"},{"en":"Personal experience can start a search for knowledge, but it may need expert confirmation.","zh":"個人經驗可以開始尋找知識，但可能需要專家確認。"},{"en":"The phrase describes knowledge gained directly by the individual.","zh":"這個短語描述由個人直接獲得的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"symptoms of","meaning":"……的症狀","examples":[{"en":"A bad cough and tiredness can be symptoms of illness.","zh":"嚴重咳嗽和疲倦可以是疾病的症狀。"},{"en":"Symptoms of something are signs or feelings that may show a condition is present.","zh":"symptoms of 某事，是可能顯示某狀況存在的跡象或感覺。"},{"en":"Fever and sore throat can be symptoms of an infection.","zh":"發燒和喉嚨痛可以是感染的症狀。"},{"en":"Symptoms help people notice a problem, but they need interpretation before diagnosis.","zh":"症狀幫助人注意到問題，但在診斷前需要詮釋。"},{"en":"The phrase links visible or felt signs to a possible cause.","zh":"這個短語把可見或可感覺的跡象與可能原因連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"doctor’s measurements","meaning":"醫生的量度數據","examples":[{"en":"The doctor’s measurements include temperature and blood pressure.","zh":"醫生的量度數據包括體溫和血壓。"},{"en":"Doctor’s measurements are the numbers or observations a doctor records during an examination.","zh":"doctor’s measurements 是醫生在檢查中記錄的數字或觀察。"},{"en":"A doctor’s measurements may include pulse, temperature, weight, and blood pressure.","zh":"醫生的量度數據可能包括脈搏、體溫、體重和血壓。"},{"en":"Measurements can provide evidence beyond what the patient feels subjectively.","zh":"量度數據可以提供超越病人主觀感覺的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recorded medical data from an examination.","zh":"這個短語描述來自檢查的醫療記錄數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"common judgement from","meaning":"來自……的一般判斷","examples":[{"en":"Common judgement from people around you may shape your view of illness.","zh":"來自你身邊人的一般判斷可能塑造你對疾病的看法。"},{"en":"Common judgement from a group means ordinary practical opinions given by that group.","zh":"common judgement from 某群體，指由該群體給出的普通實用意見。"},{"en":"Common judgement from family may tell a patient that a cough has lasted too long to ignore.","zh":"來自家人的一般判斷可能告訴病人，咳嗽已持續太久，不能忽視。"},{"en":"Such judgement can influence whether someone rests, works, or visits a doctor.","zh":"這種判斷可以影響某人是否休息、工作或看醫生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes everyday advice from non-experts.","zh":"這個短語描述來自非專家的日常建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"people around you","meaning":"你身邊的人","examples":[{"en":"People around you may notice signs of illness before you do.","zh":"你身邊的人可能比你更早注意到疾病跡象。"},{"en":"People around you are the friends, family members, colleagues, or others who regularly see you.","zh":"people around you 是經常見到你的朋友、家人、同事或其他人。"},{"en":"A colleague may notice that you look tired every morning and suggest seeing a doctor.","zh":"同事可能注意到你每天早上看起來很疲倦，並建議你看醫生。"},{"en":"People around you can provide outside observations that you may miss yourself.","zh":"你身邊的人可以提供你自己可能錯過的外部觀察。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to those close enough to observe your behaviour.","zh":"這個短語指那些足夠接近而能觀察你行為的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"scientific evidence","meaning":"科學證據","examples":[{"en":"Scientific evidence is an important source of medical knowledge.","zh":"科學證據是醫學知識的重要來源。"},{"en":"Scientific evidence is information gathered through observation, testing, measurement, and careful research.","zh":"scientific evidence 是透過觀察、測試、量度和仔細研究收集的資訊。"},{"en":"Blood test results and clinical studies can provide scientific evidence for a diagnosis.","zh":"血液檢查結果和臨床研究可以為診斷提供科學證據。"},{"en":"Scientific evidence helps reduce reliance on guesswork or personal belief alone.","zh":"科學證據幫助減少只依賴猜測或個人信念。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence produced through scientific methods.","zh":"這個短語描述透過科學方法產生的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"medical hypothesis","meaning":"醫學假設","examples":[{"en":"A doctor may examine a medical hypothesis using evidence.","zh":"醫生可能使用證據檢驗醫學假設。"},{"en":"A medical hypothesis is a possible medical explanation that needs to be tested against evidence.","zh":"medical hypothesis 是需要用證據測試的可能醫學解釋。"},{"en":"A doctor may form a medical hypothesis that a cough is caused by pneumonia.","zh":"醫生可能形成一個醫學假設，認為咳嗽由肺炎造成。"},{"en":"The hypothesis guides which questions, observations, and tests the doctor uses next.","zh":"假設會引導醫生接下來使用哪些問題、觀察和檢查。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a testable medical explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述可測試的醫學解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"examine the hypothesis","meaning":"檢驗假設","examples":[{"en":"The doctor examines the hypothesis through observations and instruments.","zh":"醫生透過觀察和儀器檢驗假設。"},{"en":"To examine the hypothesis means to test whether a possible explanation is supported by evidence.","zh":"examine the hypothesis 指測試某個可能解釋是否得到證據支持。"},{"en":"A scientist examines the hypothesis by comparing results from different groups.","zh":"科學家透過比較不同組別的結果來檢驗假設。"},{"en":"Examining a hypothesis helps people avoid accepting the first explanation too quickly.","zh":"檢驗假設幫助人避免太快接受第一個解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes checking a possible explanation carefully.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細檢查可能解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"previous training and experience","meaning":"以往的訓練和經驗","examples":[{"en":"The doctor uses previous training and experience to interpret evidence.","zh":"醫生使用以往的訓練和經驗來詮釋證據。"},{"en":"Previous training and experience are the learning and practical work someone has gained before the present situation.","zh":"previous training and experience 是某人在目前情況前已獲得的學習和實際工作經驗。"},{"en":"A teacher uses previous training and experience to understand why a student keeps making the same grammar mistake.","zh":"老師使用以往的訓練和經驗，理解學生為何反覆犯同一文法錯誤。"},{"en":"Past preparation helps professionals interpret new evidence more accurately.","zh":"過往準備幫助專業人士更準確地詮釋新證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes earlier professional learning used in current judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述在目前判斷中使用的早前專業學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 41 - Source of Knowledge.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 42":[{"front":"e-training","meaning":"電子培訓；網上培訓","examples":[{"en":"E-training can reduce costs and make staff training more flexible.","zh":"電子培訓可以降低成本，並令員工培訓更靈活。"},{"en":"E-training is training delivered through computers, the Internet, or digital platforms.","zh":"電子培訓是透過電腦、互聯網或數碼平台提供的培訓。"},{"en":"A company may use e-training so new employees can learn safety rules before coming to the office.","zh":"公司可能使用電子培訓，讓新員工到辦公室前先學習安全規則。"},{"en":"E-training can save money because workers do not always need to travel to a classroom.","zh":"電子培訓可以節省金錢，因為員工不一定需要前往課室。"},{"en":"E-training is useful for clear skills, but it may not replace face-to-face practice for every topic.","zh":"電子培訓適合清晰技能，但未必能取代每個課題的面對面練習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"e-learning","meaning":"電子學習","examples":[{"en":"E-learning is an umbrella term for several forms of technology-based learning.","zh":"電子學習是幾種科技化學習形式的總稱。"},{"en":"E-learning means learning that uses digital tools such as websites, videos, apps, or online courses.","zh":"電子學習指使用網站、影片、應用程式或網上課程等數碼工具來學習。"},{"en":"A student may use e-learning to revise grammar at home after school.","zh":"學生可能放學後在家使用電子學習來溫習文法。"},{"en":"E-learning can make education more flexible because learners can study at different times.","zh":"電子學習可以令教育更靈活，因為學習者可以在不同時間學習。"},{"en":"E-learning works best when the learner has enough motivation, equipment, and support.","zh":"當學習者有足夠動機、設備和支援時，電子學習最有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an umbrella term for","meaning":"……的總稱","examples":[{"en":"E-learning is an umbrella term for online learning, web-based training and technology-delivered instruction.","zh":"電子學習是網上學習、網上培訓和透過科技提供的教學的總稱。"},{"en":"An umbrella term for something is a general word or phrase that covers several related types.","zh":"an umbrella term for something 指涵蓋幾種相關類型的總稱。"},{"en":"“Public transport” is an umbrella term for buses, trains, trams, and ferries.","zh":"「公共交通」是巴士、火車、電車和渡輪的總稱。"},{"en":"Using an umbrella term helps people talk about many related things together.","zh":"使用總稱有助人們把許多相關事物一起討論。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one category includes several smaller categories.","zh":"當一個類別包含幾個較小類別時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"online learning","meaning":"網上學習","examples":[{"en":"Online learning allows employees to study without going to a classroom.","zh":"網上學習讓員工不用去課室也能學習。"},{"en":"Online learning is learning that takes place through the Internet.","zh":"網上學習是透過互聯網進行的學習。"},{"en":"A student may use online learning to watch a recorded maths lesson at home.","zh":"學生可能使用網上學習，在家觀看錄影數學課。"},{"en":"Online learning saves travel time, but learners still need discipline and a quiet space.","zh":"網上學習節省交通時間，但學習者仍需要自律和安靜空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning through a connected device rather than a physical classroom.","zh":"這個短語描述透過連網裝置而不是實體課室學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"web-based training","meaning":"網上培訓","examples":[{"en":"Web-based training can be delivered through an Internet-connected computer.","zh":"網上培訓可以透過可連接互聯網的電腦提供。"},{"en":"Web-based training is training provided through websites or online platforms.","zh":"網上培訓是透過網站或網上平台提供的培訓。"},{"en":"A shop may use web-based training to teach staff how to use a new payment system.","zh":"商店可能使用網上培訓，教員工如何使用新的付款系統。"},{"en":"Web-based training allows the same materials to reach many workers in different locations.","zh":"網上培訓讓同一套教材接觸到不同地點的許多員工。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on training that is accessed through the web.","zh":"這個短語集中於透過網頁存取的培訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"technology-delivered instruction","meaning":"透過科技提供的教學","examples":[{"en":"Technology-delivered instruction can be useful for large corporations.","zh":"透過科技提供的教學對大型企業可能有用。"},{"en":"Technology-delivered instruction is teaching provided through digital tools rather than only by a teacher in a room.","zh":"technology-delivered instruction 指透過數碼工具提供教學，而不只是由老師在課室教授。"},{"en":"A hospital may use technology-delivered instruction to teach staff new hygiene procedures.","zh":"醫院可能使用透過科技提供的教學，教職員新的衞生程序。"},{"en":"This method can reach many learners quickly when the same message must be delivered clearly.","zh":"當同一訊息必須清楚傳達時，這種方法可以快速接觸許多學習者。"},{"en":"It is useful for standard information, but personal coaching may still need human interaction.","zh":"它適合標準資訊，但個人指導仍可能需要人際互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"greatly benefit corporations","meaning":"令企業大大受益","examples":[{"en":"E-learning can greatly benefit corporations that need to train many employees.","zh":"電子學習可以令需要培訓大量員工的企業大大受益。"},{"en":"To greatly benefit corporations means to bring companies large advantages or savings.","zh":"greatly benefit corporations 指為公司帶來巨大好處或節省。"},{"en":"A delivery company may greatly benefit from online driver training if staff work in many cities.","zh":"如果員工分布在許多城市，物流公司可能從網上司機培訓中大大受益。"},{"en":"Digital training can benefit corporations by reducing travel, classroom rental, and instructor costs.","zh":"數碼培訓可以透過減少差旅、課室租金和導師成本，令企業受益。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the advantage is large, not minor.","zh":"這個短語顯示好處很大，而不是輕微。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"IBM, for instance, introduced an e-training programme for new managers.","zh":"例如，IBM 為新任經理推出了一項電子培訓計劃。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance 指例如。"},{"en":"Some school tasks can be done online; for instance, students can submit essays through a learning platform.","zh":"有些學校任務可以在網上完成；例如，學生可以透過學習平台提交作文。"},{"en":"Writers use “for instance” to give a concrete case after a general point.","zh":"作者使用 “for instance” 在一般觀點後給出具體例子。"},{"en":"This phrase helps make an idea clearer by showing one example.","zh":"這個短語透過展示一個例子，幫助令想法更清楚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the introduction of","meaning":"……的引入","examples":[{"en":"The introduction of Basic Blue saved IBM a large amount of money.","zh":"Basic Blue 的引入為 IBM 節省了大量金錢。"},{"en":"The introduction of something means the act of starting, launching, or bringing it into use.","zh":"the introduction of something 指開始、推出或使用某事物。"},{"en":"The introduction of a new timetable can change when students eat lunch.","zh":"新時間表的引入可以改變學生吃午飯的時間。"},{"en":"When a company introduces a new system, costs and routines may change.","zh":"當公司引入新系統，成本和日常程序可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the moment a new idea, policy, or tool begins to be used.","zh":"這個短語集中於新想法、政策或工具開始被使用的一刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"e-training programme","meaning":"電子培訓計劃","examples":[{"en":"IBM introduced an e-training programme to train new managers.","zh":"IBM 推出了一項電子培訓計劃來培訓新任經理。"},{"en":"An e-training programme is a planned digital course or system used to train people.","zh":"e-training programme 指用來培訓人員的有計劃數碼課程或系統。"},{"en":"A bank may create an e-training programme to teach staff new fraud-prevention rules.","zh":"銀行可能建立電子培訓計劃，教員工新的防詐騙規則。"},{"en":"Such a programme can train many employees consistently across different branches.","zh":"這類計劃可以在不同分行一致地培訓大量員工。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a structured online training plan, not just one random video.","zh":"這個短語描述有結構的網上培訓計劃，而不只是一條隨機影片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"train new managers","meaning":"培訓新任經理","examples":[{"en":"The purpose of Basic Blue was to train new managers.","zh":"Basic Blue 的目的是培訓新任經理。"},{"en":"To train new managers means to teach newly appointed managers the skills, rules, and responsibilities of their role.","zh":"train new managers 指教授新上任經理其職位所需的技能、規則和責任。"},{"en":"A company may train new managers in communication, scheduling, and staff evaluation.","zh":"公司可能在溝通、排班和員工評估方面培訓新任經理。"},{"en":"Good training helps new managers avoid mistakes that could affect the whole team.","zh":"良好培訓幫助新任經理避免可能影響整個團隊的錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparing people for leadership duties.","zh":"這個短語描述為領導職責作準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"save the company about","meaning":"為公司節省約……","examples":[{"en":"The programme saved the company about $200 million in 1999.","zh":"該計劃在1999年為公司節省約二億美元。"},{"en":"To save the company about an amount means to reduce its costs by approximately that amount.","zh":"save the company about an amount 指為公司減少大約某個金額的成本。"},{"en":"A new energy system may save the school about ten thousand dollars a year.","zh":"新能源系統可能每年為學校節省約一萬美元。"},{"en":"Cost-saving programmes help organisations use money for other priorities.","zh":"節省成本的計劃幫助機構把金錢用於其他優先事項。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate financial saving.","zh":"這個短語給出大約的財政節省。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"travel expenses","meaning":"差旅開支","examples":[{"en":"Cutting travel expenses produced most of the savings.","zh":"削減差旅開支帶來了大部分節省。"},{"en":"Travel expenses are costs related to transport, hotels, meals, or trips for work or training.","zh":"travel expenses 指與交通、酒店、膳食或工作及培訓出差有關的成本。"},{"en":"A company pays travel expenses when staff fly to another city for a meeting.","zh":"當員工飛往另一城市開會，公司會支付差旅開支。"},{"en":"Reducing travel expenses can save money quickly if many employees usually travel.","zh":"如果許多員工通常需要出差，減少差旅開支可以快速省錢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the money spent on moving people from one place to another.","zh":"這個短語描述把人從一地移到另一地所花的錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be required to","meaning":"需要……","examples":[{"en":"Travel expenses were required to bring employees and instructors together.","zh":"把員工和導師聚在一起需要差旅開支。"},{"en":"To be required to do something means to be needed or officially expected to do it.","zh":"be required to do something 指需要或被正式要求做某事。"},{"en":"Students may be required to wear safety glasses in a science lab.","zh":"學生在科學實驗室可能需要戴安全眼鏡。"},{"en":"If travel is required, the company must pay for transport and accommodation.","zh":"如果需要出差，公司必須支付交通和住宿費用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something necessary or demanded.","zh":"這個短語描述某事是必要或被要求的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"bring employees and instructors to","meaning":"把員工和導師帶到……","examples":[{"en":"Companies used to bring employees and instructors to a central classroom.","zh":"公司過去常把員工和導師帶到集中上課的課室。"},{"en":"To bring employees and instructors to a place means to arrange for both groups to gather there.","zh":"bring employees and instructors to a place 指安排員工和導師一起到某地方。"},{"en":"A hotel may bring staff and trainers to one conference room for customer-service training.","zh":"酒店可能把員工和培訓導師帶到同一會議室進行客服培訓。"},{"en":"Bringing people together can improve interaction, but it also creates travel and time costs.","zh":"把人聚在一起可以改善互動，但也會產生交通和時間成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physically gathering learners and teachers in one place.","zh":"這個短語描述把學習者和老師實體聚集在同一地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a central classroom","meaning":"集中上課的課室","examples":[{"en":"Traditional training often required everyone to gather in a central classroom.","zh":"傳統培訓通常要求所有人聚集在集中上課的課室。"},{"en":"A central classroom is one shared teaching room where learners from different places meet.","zh":"central classroom 指來自不同地方的學習者共同上課的一個課室。"},{"en":"A company may ask staff from many branches to attend a course in a central classroom.","zh":"公司可能要求多間分行的員工到集中課室參加課程。"},{"en":"Central classrooms can make teaching consistent, but they require travel and scheduling.","zh":"集中課室可以令教學一致，但需要交通和時間安排。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one physical training location for many learners.","zh":"這個短語描述供許多學習者使用的一個實體培訓地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"account for the lion’s share of","meaning":"佔……的最大部分","examples":[{"en":"Cutting travel expenses accounts for the lion’s share of the savings.","zh":"削減差旅開支佔節省費用的最大部分。"},{"en":"To account for the lion’s share of something means to make up the largest part of it.","zh":"account for the lion’s share of something 指構成某事中最大的一部分。"},{"en":"Rent may account for the lion’s share of a small shop’s monthly costs.","zh":"租金可能佔小店每月成本的最大部分。"},{"en":"If one expense is the lion’s share, reducing it can create major savings.","zh":"如果某項開支佔最大部分，減少它可以帶來重大節省。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the biggest portion, not a small contribution.","zh":"這個短語強調最大比例，而不是小貢獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the savings","meaning":"節省下來的費用","examples":[{"en":"The savings came mainly from reducing travel expenses.","zh":"節省下來的費用主要來自減少差旅開支。"},{"en":"The savings are the money kept or not spent because costs have been reduced.","zh":"the savings 指因成本降低而保留下來或沒有花掉的金錢。"},{"en":"A family may use the savings from eating at home to pay for a holiday.","zh":"家庭可能用在家吃飯節省下來的費用去支付旅行。"},{"en":"When a company reduces unnecessary travel, the savings can be invested in better training materials.","zh":"當公司減少不必要差旅，節省下來的費用可以投資於更好的培訓材料。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to money saved after a change.","zh":"這個短語指改變後省下的金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an online course","meaning":"網上課程","examples":[{"en":"With an online course, employees can learn from almost anywhere.","zh":"有了網上課程，員工幾乎可以在任何地方學習。"},{"en":"An online course is a structured class or training programme delivered through the Internet.","zh":"online course 指透過互聯網提供的有結構課堂或培訓計劃。"},{"en":"A student may take an online course in English writing during the summer holiday.","zh":"學生可能在暑假修讀英文寫作網上課程。"},{"en":"Online courses allow learners to study without being in the same room as the teacher.","zh":"網上課程讓學習者不用與老師在同一房間也能學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised learning delivered digitally.","zh":"這個短語描述以數碼方式提供的有組織學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Internet-connected PC","meaning":"可連接互聯網的個人電腦","examples":[{"en":"Employees can learn from any Internet-connected PC.","zh":"員工可以透過任何可連接互聯網的個人電腦學習。"},{"en":"An Internet-connected PC is a personal computer that can access the Internet.","zh":"Internet-connected PC 指可以連上互聯網的個人電腦。"},{"en":"A worker may complete training on an Internet-connected PC at home or in the office.","zh":"員工可能在家中或辦公室用可連接互聯網的個人電腦完成培訓。"},{"en":"If a PC is not connected to the Internet, online materials may be unavailable.","zh":"如果個人電腦不能連接互聯網，網上材料可能無法使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the basic equipment needed for many online courses.","zh":"這個短語描述許多網上課程所需的基本設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"anywhere in the world","meaning":"世界任何地方","examples":[{"en":"Employees can take an online course anywhere in the world.","zh":"員工可以在世界任何地方修讀網上課程。"},{"en":"Anywhere in the world means in any country or location globally.","zh":"anywhere in the world 指全球任何國家或地點。"},{"en":"A student with Internet access can join a language class anywhere in the world.","zh":"有互聯網的學生可以在世界任何地方參加語言課。"},{"en":"Global access makes online learning useful for companies with international offices.","zh":"全球存取令網上學習對有國際辦公室的公司很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that location is no longer a major limit.","zh":"這個短語強調地點不再是主要限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reduce training costs by","meaning":"將培訓成本減少……","examples":[{"en":"Ernst & Young reduced training costs by 35 per cent.","zh":"Ernst & Young 將培訓成本減少了百分之三十五。"},{"en":"To reduce training costs by an amount means to lower the money spent on training by that amount.","zh":"reduce training costs by an amount 指把培訓開支降低某個幅度。"},{"en":"A school may reduce printing costs by 20 per cent if it uses digital worksheets.","zh":"如果學校使用數碼工作紙，可能將印刷成本減少百分之二十。"},{"en":"Reducing training costs can free money for better software, trainers, or learner support.","zh":"減少培訓成本可以釋放資金，用於更好的軟件、導師或學習支援。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the size of a cost reduction.","zh":"這個短語給出成本降低的幅度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"improve consistency","meaning":"提高一致性","examples":[{"en":"The company reduced costs while improving consistency.","zh":"公司在降低成本的同時提高一致性。"},{"en":"To improve consistency means to make quality, content, or delivery more uniform and reliable.","zh":"improve consistency 指令質素、內容或傳達方式更統一和可靠。"},{"en":"A restaurant improves consistency when every branch serves food at the same standard.","zh":"當餐廳每間分店都以相同標準出餐，就是提高一致性。"},{"en":"Consistent training reduces confusion because employees receive the same message.","zh":"一致的培訓減少混亂，因為員工收到相同訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making results less uneven.","zh":"這個短語描述令結果較不參差。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"improve scalability","meaning":"提高擴展能力","examples":[{"en":"E-learning helped the company improve scalability.","zh":"電子學習幫助公司提高擴展能力。"},{"en":"To improve scalability means to make a system easier to expand for more users without losing quality.","zh":"improve scalability 指令系統更容易擴大給更多使用者，而不失去質素。"},{"en":"A school improves scalability when one online lesson can serve many classes at once.","zh":"當一堂網上課可以同時服務許多班級，學校就是提高擴展能力。"},{"en":"Scalable training helps companies grow without rebuilding the course for every new employee.","zh":"可擴展的培訓幫助公司增長，而不用為每名新員工重新建立課程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making something easier to enlarge.","zh":"這個短語描述令某事更容易擴大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"consistency and scalability","meaning":"一致性和擴展能力","examples":[{"en":"Ernst & Young improved consistency and scalability through e-learning.","zh":"Ernst & Young 透過電子學習提高了一致性和擴展能力。"},{"en":"Consistency and scalability mean stable quality and the ability to expand to more learners.","zh":"consistency and scalability 指穩定質素和擴展至更多學習者的能力。"},{"en":"A tutoring centre needs consistency and scalability if it wants all branches to teach the same course well.","zh":"如果補習中心希望所有分校都把同一課程教好，就需要一致性和擴展能力。"},{"en":"E-learning can support both because one course can be delivered repeatedly to many people.","zh":"電子學習可以支援兩者，因為一門課程可以反覆傳送給許多人。"},{"en":"This phrase combines reliability with growth potential.","zh":"這個短語結合可靠性和增長潛力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in addition to","meaning":"除……之外","examples":[{"en":"In addition to economic benefits, e-learning offers several practical advantages.","zh":"除經濟效益之外，電子學習還提供幾項實際好處。"},{"en":"In addition to means besides or as well as.","zh":"in addition to 指除了某事之外，也包括其他事。"},{"en":"In addition to grammar, students need ideas and examples for strong writing.","zh":"除了文法之外，學生還需要想法和例子才能寫出有力文章。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another point to an argument.","zh":"這個短語為論點加入另一點。"},{"en":"It shows that the discussion is not limited to one benefit or reason.","zh":"它顯示討論不只限於一個好處或原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"positive economic benefits","meaning":"正面的經濟效益","examples":[{"en":"E-learning can produce positive economic benefits for corporations.","zh":"電子學習可以為企業帶來正面的經濟效益。"},{"en":"Positive economic benefits are financial advantages such as savings, efficiency, or higher returns.","zh":"positive economic benefits 指節省、效率提升或更高回報等財政好處。"},{"en":"A company gains positive economic benefits when online training reduces travel and hotel costs.","zh":"當網上培訓減少交通和酒店費用，公司就獲得正面的經濟效益。"},{"en":"Economic benefits can make a training method easier to justify to managers.","zh":"經濟效益可以令培訓方法更容易向管理層解釋其合理性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes money-related gains.","zh":"這個短語描述與金錢有關的收益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"other advantages such as","meaning":"其他好處，例如……","examples":[{"en":"E-learning offers other advantages such as convenience and flexibility.","zh":"電子學習提供其他好處，例如便利性和靈活性。"},{"en":"Other advantages such as means additional benefits, for example the ones named after the phrase.","zh":"other advantages such as 指額外好處，例如短語後列出的那些。"},{"en":"Public libraries offer other advantages such as quiet study space and free Internet access.","zh":"公共圖書館提供其他好處，例如安靜自修空間和免費互聯網。"},{"en":"Listing examples helps readers understand what kind of benefits are meant.","zh":"列出例子幫助讀者理解所指的是哪類好處。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces extra examples of positive points.","zh":"這個短語引出額外正面例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"convenience","meaning":"便利性","examples":[{"en":"Convenience has made e-learning attractive to many companies.","zh":"便利性令電子學習對許多公司有吸引力。"},{"en":"Convenience means being easy to use, access, or fit into daily life.","zh":"convenience 指容易使用、容易取得或容易融入日常生活。"},{"en":"A shop near a train station offers convenience because commuters can buy things quickly.","zh":"位於火車站附近的商店具便利性，因為通勤者可以快速購物。"},{"en":"Convenient training reduces stress because employees can learn without long travel.","zh":"方便的培訓減少壓力，因為員工不用長途出行也能學習。"},{"en":"This word describes practical ease.","zh":"這個字描述實際上的方便。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"standardised delivery","meaning":"標準化傳授","examples":[{"en":"Standardised delivery helps companies provide the same training to many employees.","zh":"標準化傳授幫助公司向許多員工提供相同培訓。"},{"en":"Standardised delivery means presenting the same content in the same way to different learners.","zh":"standardised delivery 指以相同方式向不同學習者呈現相同內容。"},{"en":"A school uses standardised delivery when all classes receive the same exam instructions.","zh":"當所有班級收到相同考試指示，學校就是使用標準化傳達。"},{"en":"This can reduce mistakes because everyone hears the same message.","zh":"這可以減少錯誤，因為每個人都聽到相同訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes consistency in how training is provided.","zh":"這個短語描述培訓提供方式的一致性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"self-paced learning","meaning":"按自己步伐學習","examples":[{"en":"Self-paced learning allows employees to study at a suitable speed.","zh":"按自己步伐學習讓員工以合適速度學習。"},{"en":"Self-paced learning means learners can move through materials at their own speed.","zh":"self-paced learning 指學習者可以按自己的速度完成教材。"},{"en":"A student may pause a video lesson and replay a difficult grammar point.","zh":"學生可以暫停影片課堂，重播困難文法點。"},{"en":"Learning at one’s own pace helps slower learners review and faster learners move ahead.","zh":"按自己步伐學習幫助較慢的學習者重溫，也讓較快的學習者前進。"},{"en":"This phrase describes flexible progress controlled by the learner.","zh":"這個短語描述由學習者控制進度的靈活學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"available content","meaning":"可用內容","examples":[{"en":"The variety of available content has made e-learning a high priority.","zh":"可用內容的多樣性令電子學習成為高度優先事項。"},{"en":"Available content is the learning material that people can access and use.","zh":"available content 指人們可以取得和使用的學習材料。"},{"en":"A language app with videos, quizzes, and articles has a wide range of available content.","zh":"有影片、測驗和文章的語言應用程式有大量可用內容。"},{"en":"More available content gives learners more choices and helps suit different needs.","zh":"更多可用內容給學習者更多選擇，並幫助配合不同需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accessible materials, not hidden or unavailable resources.","zh":"這個短語描述可取得材料，而不是隱藏或不可用資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a high priority for","meaning":"……的高度優先事項","examples":[{"en":"E-learning has become a high priority for many corporations.","zh":"電子學習已成為許多企業的高度優先事項。"},{"en":"A high priority for someone is something they consider very important and deal with early.","zh":"a high priority for someone 指某人認為非常重要並會優先處理的事。"},{"en":"Student safety is a high priority for every school.","zh":"學生安全是每間學校的高度優先事項。"},{"en":"If training becomes a high priority, companies may spend more time and money on it.","zh":"如果培訓成為高度優先事項，公司可能花更多時間和金錢在其上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something placed near the top of a decision list.","zh":"這個短語描述在決策清單中排得很前的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be widely believed to","meaning":"被普遍認為","examples":[{"en":"E-learning is widely believed to offer flexible learning.","zh":"電子學習被普遍認為能提供靈活學習。"},{"en":"To be widely believed to do something means many people think it does that thing.","zh":"be widely believed to do something 指許多人認為某事物會做到某事。"},{"en":"Exercise is widely believed to improve mood and physical health.","zh":"運動被普遍認為能改善情緒和身體健康。"},{"en":"A widely believed idea may still need evidence before it becomes certain.","zh":"被普遍相信的想法在確定前仍可能需要證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common belief, not necessarily a proven fact.","zh":"這個短語描述常見看法，而不一定是已證實事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"offer flexible learning","meaning":"提供靈活學習","examples":[{"en":"E-learning can offer flexible learning at any time and in any place.","zh":"電子學習可以隨時隨地提供靈活學習。"},{"en":"To offer flexible learning means to allow learners more choice over time, place, or pace.","zh":"offer flexible learning 指讓學習者在時間、地點或步伐上有更多選擇。"},{"en":"A working parent may need flexible learning because they can only study after their child sleeps.","zh":"在職家長可能需要靈活學習，因為他們只能在孩子睡後學習。"},{"en":"Flexible learning helps people fit education around work, family, and travel.","zh":"靈活學習幫助人把教育配合工作、家庭和旅行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning that adapts to the learner’s situation.","zh":"這個短語描述能適應學習者情況的學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"any time, any place learning","meaning":"隨時隨地學習","examples":[{"en":"Many corporations value any time, any place learning.","zh":"許多企業重視隨時隨地學習。"},{"en":"Any time, any place learning means learners can study whenever and wherever they have access.","zh":"any time, any place learning 指學習者只要能登入，就可在任何時間和地點學習。"},{"en":"A salesperson travelling between cities can use any time, any place learning on a laptop.","zh":"在城市之間出差的銷售員可以用手提電腦隨時隨地學習。"},{"en":"This kind of learning reduces the need for everyone to meet at one fixed time.","zh":"這種學習減少所有人在固定時間聚集的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses maximum flexibility in time and location.","zh":"這個短語強調時間和地點上的最大靈活性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"valid in principle","meaning":"原則上成立","examples":[{"en":"The claim for any place learning is valid in principle.","zh":"隨地學習這個說法原則上成立。"},{"en":"Valid in principle means the idea is basically reasonable, even if there may be practical problems.","zh":"valid in principle 指想法基本合理，即使實際上可能有問題。"},{"en":"Letting students choose their own projects is valid in principle, but teachers still need to guide them.","zh":"讓學生選擇自己的專題原則上成立，但老師仍需要指導。"},{"en":"A plan can be valid in principle but difficult to carry out in real life.","zh":"一個計劃可以原則上成立，但在現實中難以執行。"},{"en":"This phrase separates the basic idea from practical details.","zh":"這個短語把基本想法與實際細節分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"engage with","meaning":"接觸；參與","examples":[{"en":"Learners can engage with rich learning materials online.","zh":"學習者可以在網上接觸並投入豐富的學習材料。"},{"en":"To engage with something means to actively use, think about, or respond to it.","zh":"engage with something 指主動使用、思考或回應某事。"},{"en":"Students engage with a text when they ask questions, highlight ideas, and discuss meaning.","zh":"當學生提問、標示重點和討論意思時，就是在投入文本。"},{"en":"Better engagement can lead to deeper understanding and stronger memory.","zh":"更高投入度可以帶來更深入理解和更強記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active involvement, not passive looking.","zh":"這個短語描述主動參與，而不是被動觀看。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rich learning materials","meaning":"豐富的學習材料","examples":[{"en":"E-learning gives many people access to rich learning materials.","zh":"電子學習讓許多人接觸到豐富的學習材料。"},{"en":"Rich learning materials are varied, detailed, and useful resources that help people learn deeply.","zh":"rich learning materials 指多樣、詳細且有用、能幫助人深入學習的資源。"},{"en":"A course with videos, diagrams, quizzes, and real cases has rich learning materials.","zh":"有影片、圖解、測驗和真實案例的課程擁有豐富學習材料。"},{"en":"Rich materials can support different learners because some learn better through sound, text, or images.","zh":"豐富材料可以支援不同學習者，因為有人較適合透過聲音、文字或圖像學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning resources with depth and variety.","zh":"這個短語描述有深度和多樣性的學習資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"simply unavailable","meaning":"根本無法取得","examples":[{"en":"Some learning materials were simply unavailable in the past.","zh":"有些學習材料在過去根本無法取得。"},{"en":"Simply unavailable means completely not accessible or not possible to obtain.","zh":"simply unavailable 指完全無法接觸或無法取得。"},{"en":"Before the Internet, many rare books were simply unavailable to students in small towns.","zh":"在互聯網出現前，許多稀有書籍對小鎮學生而言根本無法取得。"},{"en":"If materials are unavailable, learners cannot benefit from them no matter how motivated they are.","zh":"如果材料無法取得，學習者再有動機也不能受益。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that access was impossible, not just inconvenient.","zh":"這個短語強調不是不方便，而是無法取得。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"an era of","meaning":"……的年代","examples":[{"en":"Rich online materials were unavailable in an era of paper-based distance learning.","zh":"在紙本遙距學習的年代，豐富網上材料無法取得。"},{"en":"An era of something is a period of time strongly associated with that thing.","zh":"an era of something 指一段與某事物密切相關的時期。"},{"en":"We now live in an era of mobile communication, where phones shape daily life.","zh":"我們現在生活在流動通訊的年代，手機塑造日常生活。"},{"en":"Each era creates different limits and possibilities for learning.","zh":"每個年代都為學習創造不同限制和可能性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a historical period defined by a major feature.","zh":"這個短語描述由主要特徵定義的歷史時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"paper-based distance learning","meaning":"紙本遙距學習","examples":[{"en":"Paper-based distance learning offered fewer interactive learning materials.","zh":"紙本遙距學習提供較少互動學習材料。"},{"en":"Paper-based distance learning is remote study using printed materials sent to learners.","zh":"paper-based distance learning 指使用寄給學習者的印刷材料進行遙距學習。"},{"en":"In the past, students might receive lessons by post and send written work back to teachers.","zh":"過去，學生可能透過郵寄收到課程，並把書面功課寄回老師。"},{"en":"Paper-based learning can reach distant learners, but it offers limited audio, video, and interaction.","zh":"紙本學習可以接觸遠方學習者，但音訊、影片和互動有限。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an older form of learning from far away.","zh":"這個短語描述較舊形式的遙距學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"broadcast distance learning","meaning":"廣播式遙距學習","examples":[{"en":"Broadcast distance learning was less flexible than modern e-learning.","zh":"廣播式遙距學習不如現代電子學習靈活。"},{"en":"Broadcast distance learning is remote teaching delivered through television, radio, or scheduled broadcasts.","zh":"broadcast distance learning 指透過電視、電台或定時廣播提供的遙距教學。"},{"en":"A student might once have watched a lesson on television at a fixed time.","zh":"學生過去可能在固定時間觀看電視課堂。"},{"en":"Broadcast learning can reach many people, but learners cannot easily pause, replay, or ask questions.","zh":"廣播式學習可以接觸很多人，但學習者不容易暫停、重播或提問。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distance learning through one-way broadcast media.","zh":"這個短語描述透過單向廣播媒體進行的遙距學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"specific information and skills","meaning":"特定資料和技能","examples":[{"en":"E-training can teach specific information and skills effectively.","zh":"電子培訓可以有效教授特定資料和技能。"},{"en":"Specific information and skills are clear facts and practical abilities that learners need for a task.","zh":"specific information and skills 指學習者完成任務所需的清晰事實和實用能力。"},{"en":"A cashier may learn specific information and skills such as refund rules and payment procedures.","zh":"收銀員可能學習退貨規則和付款程序等特定資料和技能。"},{"en":"Clear skills are easier to teach online because the goals can be shown step by step.","zh":"清晰技能較容易在網上教授，因為目標可以逐步展示。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to focused learning content, not broad personal development.","zh":"這個短語指聚焦的學習內容，而不是廣泛個人成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hold great promise","meaning":"很有前景","examples":[{"en":"For teaching specific skills, e-training holds great promise.","zh":"在教授特定技能方面，電子培訓很有前景。"},{"en":"To hold great promise means to show strong potential for future success.","zh":"hold great promise 指顯示出未來成功的強大潛力。"},{"en":"A new reading app holds great promise if early users improve quickly.","zh":"如果早期使用者進步很快，一個新的閱讀應用程式就很有前景。"},{"en":"Something may hold promise before it is perfect because early results are encouraging.","zh":"某事即使未完美，也可能因早期結果令人鼓舞而有前景。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong hope based on potential.","zh":"這個短語描述基於潛力的強烈希望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be especially effective at","meaning":"在……方面尤其有效","examples":[{"en":"E-training can be especially effective at preparing employees for certification.","zh":"電子培訓在幫助員工準備認證方面尤其有效。"},{"en":"To be especially effective at something means to work particularly well for that purpose.","zh":"be especially effective at something 指對某目的特別有效。"},{"en":"Practice tests are especially effective at helping students understand exam timing.","zh":"模擬試在幫助學生理解考試時間安排方面尤其有效。"},{"en":"E-training is effective when content is clear, repeatable, and easy to test.","zh":"當內容清晰、可重複並容易測試時，電子培訓很有效。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a situation where a method works very well.","zh":"這個短語突出某方法特別有效的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"prepare for","meaning":"為……作準備","examples":[{"en":"E-learning can help employees prepare for IT certification programmes.","zh":"電子學習可以幫助員工為資訊科技認證課程作準備。"},{"en":"To prepare for something means to get ready for it through study, practice, or planning.","zh":"prepare for something 指透過學習、練習或計劃為某事作準備。"},{"en":"Students prepare for a speaking exam by practising answers aloud.","zh":"學生透過大聲練習答案來為口試作準備。"},{"en":"Good preparation can reduce anxiety and improve performance.","zh":"良好準備可以減少焦慮並改善表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes getting ready before an important task.","zh":"這個短語描述在重要任務前作準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"IT certification programmes","meaning":"資訊科技認證課程","examples":[{"en":"Employees may use e-training to prepare for IT certification programmes.","zh":"員工可能使用電子培訓來準備資訊科技認證課程。"},{"en":"IT certification programmes are courses or exams that prove a person has certain technology skills.","zh":"IT certification programmes 指證明某人具備特定科技技能的課程或考試。"},{"en":"A worker may complete an IT certification programme to show they can manage networks safely.","zh":"員工可能完成資訊科技認證課程，以顯示自己能安全管理網絡。"},{"en":"Certifications can help employees qualify for new technical roles.","zh":"認證可以幫助員工符合新技術職位資格。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal proof of information-technology ability.","zh":"這個短語指資訊科技能力的正式證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"effectively address topics","meaning":"有效處理某些課題","examples":[{"en":"E-learning can effectively address topics with clear objectives.","zh":"電子學習可以有效處理有清晰目標的課題。"},{"en":"To effectively address topics means to deal with subjects in a useful and successful way.","zh":"effectively address topics 指以有用而成功的方式處理某些主題。"},{"en":"A workshop can effectively address exam stress if it teaches practical planning and relaxation skills.","zh":"如果工作坊教授實用規劃和放鬆技巧，就可以有效處理考試壓力。"},{"en":"Clear topics are easier to address because learners know exactly what they must understand.","zh":"清晰課題較容易處理，因為學習者知道自己必須理解甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes handling a subject well.","zh":"這個短語描述妥善處理某主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sexual harassment education","meaning":"性騷擾教育","examples":[{"en":"E-learning can be used for sexual harassment education.","zh":"電子學習可以用於性騷擾教育。"},{"en":"Sexual harassment education teaches people what harassment is, how to prevent it, and how to report it.","zh":"sexual harassment education 教人甚麼是性騷擾、如何預防，以及如何舉報。"},{"en":"A company may require all staff to complete sexual harassment education during onboarding.","zh":"公司可能要求所有員工入職時完成性騷擾教育。"},{"en":"Clear training can reduce harmful behaviour because employees understand rules and consequences.","zh":"清晰培訓可以減少有害行為，因為員工明白規則和後果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes workplace education about respect, boundaries, and safety.","zh":"這個短語描述關於尊重、界線和安全的職場教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"safety training","meaning":"安全培訓","examples":[{"en":"Safety training is one area where clear objectives can be identified.","zh":"安全培訓是一個可以識別清晰目標的範疇。"},{"en":"Safety training teaches people how to avoid accidents, injuries, and dangerous behaviour.","zh":"safety training 教人如何避免意外、受傷和危險行為。"},{"en":"Factory workers may complete safety training before using heavy machinery.","zh":"工廠工人使用重型機械前可能要完成安全培訓。"},{"en":"Good safety training can prevent injuries and reduce workplace accidents.","zh":"良好安全培訓可以防止受傷並減少工作場所意外。"},{"en":"This phrase describes training that protects people from harm.","zh":"這個短語描述保護人免受傷害的培訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"management training","meaning":"管理培訓","examples":[{"en":"Management training can sometimes be delivered effectively online.","zh":"管理培訓有時可以有效地在網上提供。"},{"en":"Management training teaches people how to lead teams, make decisions, and organise work.","zh":"management training 教人如何帶領團隊、作決策和組織工作。"},{"en":"A new supervisor may receive management training on giving feedback to staff.","zh":"新任主管可能接受關於如何向員工給予回饋的管理培訓。"},{"en":"Some management skills can be taught online, but role-play may still need live practice.","zh":"有些管理技能可以在網上教授，但角色扮演仍可能需要即時練習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes training for leadership and organisation.","zh":"這個短語描述領導和組織方面的培訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a clear set of objectives","meaning":"一套清晰目標","examples":[{"en":"E-learning works well when a clear set of objectives can be identified.","zh":"當能夠識別一套清晰目標時，電子學習效果良好。"},{"en":"A clear set of objectives is a list of specific goals learners are expected to achieve.","zh":"clear set of objectives 指學習者被期望達成的一系列具體目標。"},{"en":"A writing course may have objectives such as improving structure, grammar, and argument.","zh":"寫作課程可能有改善結構、文法和論證等目標。"},{"en":"Clear objectives help teachers design lessons and help students measure progress.","zh":"清晰目標幫助老師設計課堂，也幫助學生量度進步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes well-defined learning targets.","zh":"這個短語描述明確定義的學習目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"training experts","meaning":"培訓專家","examples":[{"en":"Training experts recommend using different methods when necessary.","zh":"培訓專家建議在有需要時使用不同方法。"},{"en":"Training experts are people with specialist knowledge about how to design and deliver effective training.","zh":"training experts 指對如何設計和提供有效培訓有專門知識的人。"},{"en":"A company may ask training experts to improve a weak staff-development programme.","zh":"公司可能請培訓專家改善成效不佳的員工發展計劃。"},{"en":"Experts can choose methods based on the learners, topic, budget, and goals.","zh":"專家可以根據學習者、課題、預算和目標選擇方法。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to specialists in teaching adults or employees.","zh":"這個短語指專門教授成人或員工的人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"recommend a blended approach","meaning":"建議採用混合模式","examples":[{"en":"Training experts recommend a blended approach to corporate training.","zh":"培訓專家建議企業培訓採用混合模式。"},{"en":"To recommend a blended approach means to suggest combining more than one training method.","zh":"recommend a blended approach 指建議結合多於一種培訓方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may recommend a blended approach that includes videos, worksheets, and live discussion.","zh":"老師可能建議採用混合模式，包括影片、工作紙和即時討論。"},{"en":"Blending methods can help because different skills may need different learning environments.","zh":"混合方法有幫助，因為不同技能可能需要不同學習環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes advice to mix methods rather than rely on one only.","zh":"這個短語描述建議混合方法，而不是只依靠單一方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a blended approach","meaning":"混合模式","examples":[{"en":"A blended approach combines online and in-person training.","zh":"混合模式結合網上和面授培訓。"},{"en":"A blended approach is a method that mixes two or more learning formats.","zh":"blended approach 指混合兩種或以上學習形式的方法。"},{"en":"A school may use a blended approach by assigning videos at home and discussions in class.","zh":"學校可能透過在家觀看影片、在課堂討論來使用混合模式。"},{"en":"Blended learning can use online materials for facts and face-to-face time for practice.","zh":"混合學習可以用網上材料學事實，用面對面時間練習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a combined method.","zh":"這個短語描述結合式方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"online and in-person training","meaning":"網上和面授培訓","examples":[{"en":"The approach combines online and in-person training as the subject requires.","zh":"這種模式視乎科目需要結合網上和面授培訓。"},{"en":"Online and in-person training means digital learning combined with face-to-face sessions.","zh":"online and in-person training 指數碼學習與面對面課節結合。"},{"en":"A company may teach rules online but practise difficult conversations in person.","zh":"公司可能在網上教授規則，但面對面練習困難對話。"},{"en":"This mix helps learners get both flexible content and human interaction.","zh":"這種混合幫助學習者同時得到靈活內容和人際互動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using both remote and physical training formats.","zh":"這個短語描述同時使用遙距和實體培訓形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as the subject requires","meaning":"視乎科目需要","examples":[{"en":"Training should combine different methods as the subject requires.","zh":"培訓應視乎科目需要結合不同方法。"},{"en":"As the subject requires means according to what the topic needs.","zh":"as the subject requires 指按照課題本身的需要。"},{"en":"A science lesson may use experiments as the subject requires, while history may use documents.","zh":"科學課可視乎科目需要使用實驗，而歷史課可能使用文獻。"},{"en":"Different subjects need different teaching methods because skills and goals vary.","zh":"不同科目需要不同教學方法，因為技能和目標各有不同。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the method should fit the topic.","zh":"這個短語顯示方法應配合課題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a universal solution","meaning":"萬能解決方案","examples":[{"en":"E-learning is not a universal solution for every training need.","zh":"電子學習不是每種培訓需要的萬能解決方案。"},{"en":"A universal solution is one answer that works for every situation.","zh":"universal solution 指適用於所有情況的一個答案。"},{"en":"More homework is not a universal solution because some students need feedback, not extra tasks.","zh":"更多功課不是萬能解決方案，因為有些學生需要回饋，而不是額外任務。"},{"en":"If one method cannot solve every problem, teachers must choose tools carefully.","zh":"如果一種方法不能解決所有問題，老師就必須小心選擇工具。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against treating one idea as perfect for all cases.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要把一個想法視為適合所有情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"windowless classrooms","meaning":"沒有窗的課室","examples":[{"en":"E-learning may reduce the number of windowless classrooms.","zh":"電子學習可能減少沒有窗的課室數量。"},{"en":"Windowless classrooms are classrooms with no windows, often feeling closed and uncomfortable.","zh":"windowless classrooms 指沒有窗戶、通常感覺封閉和不舒服的課室。"},{"en":"Workers may dislike training in windowless classrooms because the room feels dark and tiring.","zh":"員工可能不喜歡在沒有窗的課室培訓，因為房間感覺昏暗和疲累。"},{"en":"Replacing some classroom training with online learning can reduce time spent in such rooms.","zh":"以網上學習取代部分課室培訓，可以減少待在這類房間的時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to make traditional training sound dull or unpleasant.","zh":"這個短語用來令傳統培訓聽起來沉悶或不舒服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"filled with","meaning":"充滿……","examples":[{"en":"Some classrooms are filled with bored or sleepy students.","zh":"有些課室充滿感到沉悶或昏昏欲睡的學生。"},{"en":"Filled with means containing a lot of something or many people.","zh":"filled with 指包含大量某物或許多人。"},{"en":"A library may be filled with students before a major exam.","zh":"大考前，圖書館可能充滿學生。"},{"en":"If a room is filled with tired learners, teaching becomes less effective.","zh":"如果房間充滿疲倦學習者，教學會較低效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a space containing many things or people.","zh":"這個短語描述某空間包含許多事物或人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"snoring students","meaning":"打鼻鼾的學生","examples":[{"en":"The writer jokes about classrooms filled with snoring students.","zh":"作者開玩笑說課室充滿打鼻鼾的學生。"},{"en":"Snoring students are students who are so sleepy that they fall asleep and make snoring sounds.","zh":"snoring students 指睏到睡着並發出鼻鼾聲的學生。"},{"en":"A long lecture after lunch may leave the back row full of snoring students.","zh":"午飯後的長講座可能令後排坐滿打鼻鼾的學生。"},{"en":"If students are snoring, the lesson is probably failing to keep them engaged.","zh":"如果學生在打鼻鼾，課堂很可能未能令他們投入。"},{"en":"This phrase humorously suggests that a class is boring or learners are exhausted.","zh":"這個短語幽默地暗示課堂沉悶或學習者非常疲倦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have its advantages","meaning":"有其好處","examples":[{"en":"E-learning definitely has its advantages when it reduces costs.","zh":"當電子學習能降低成本時，它確實有其好處。"},{"en":"To have its advantages means to have some clear benefits, even if it also has weaknesses.","zh":"have its advantages 指有一些清楚好處，即使也有弱點。"},{"en":"Studying at home has its advantages because students save travel time.","zh":"在家學習有其好處，因為學生節省交通時間。"},{"en":"A method can have advantages without being perfect for every situation.","zh":"一種方法可以有好處，但不代表適合每個情況。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a balanced positive comment.","zh":"這個短語給出平衡的正面評價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"implementing e-learning","meaning":"推行電子學習","examples":[{"en":"Much of the discussion about implementing e-learning has focused on technology.","zh":"關於推行電子學習的許多討論都聚焦於科技。"},{"en":"Implementing e-learning means putting online learning systems into actual use.","zh":"implementing e-learning 指把網上學習系統實際投入使用。"},{"en":"A school implementing e-learning must train teachers and prepare students.","zh":"推行電子學習的學校必須培訓老師並讓學生作好準備。"},{"en":"Implementation can fail if people focus only on software and ignore learner needs.","zh":"如果人們只聚焦於軟件而忽視學習者需要，推行可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the practical process of introducing e-learning.","zh":"這個短語描述引入電子學習的實際過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"focus on the technology","meaning":"聚焦於科技","examples":[{"en":"Many discussions of e-learning focus on the technology.","zh":"許多關於電子學習的討論都聚焦於科技。"},{"en":"To focus on the technology means to pay most attention to the tools, software, and systems used.","zh":"focus on the technology 指主要注意所使用的工具、軟件和系統。"},{"en":"A school may focus on the technology and forget that teachers need training too.","zh":"學校可能聚焦於科技，卻忘記老師也需要培訓。"},{"en":"If planning focuses only on technology, human problems may remain unsolved.","zh":"如果規劃只聚焦於科技，人為問題可能仍未解決。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attention being directed mainly to digital tools.","zh":"這個短語描述注意力主要放在數碼工具上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be not just about","meaning":"不只是關於……","examples":[{"en":"E-learning is not just about technology.","zh":"電子學習不只是關於科技。"},{"en":"To be not just about something means that the topic includes more than that one element.","zh":"be not just about something 指某主題包含的不止那一個元素。"},{"en":"Good teaching is not just about exam marks; it is also about confidence and thinking skills.","zh":"好教學不只是關於考試分數；也關於信心和思考能力。"},{"en":"If e-learning is not just about technology, managers must consider motivation and support.","zh":"如果電子學習不只是關於科技，管理者必須考慮動機和支援。"},{"en":"This phrase expands a narrow view into a broader one.","zh":"這個短語把狹窄看法擴展成較廣泛看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"human factors","meaning":"人為因素","examples":[{"en":"E-learning also involves many human factors.","zh":"電子學習也涉及許多人為因素。"},{"en":"Human factors are people-related issues such as motivation, habits, confidence, and communication.","zh":"human factors 指與人有關的問題，例如動機、習慣、信心和溝通。"},{"en":"A new school app may fail because of human factors, even if the software is good.","zh":"即使軟件很好，新學校應用程式也可能因人為因素失敗。"},{"en":"Training succeeds when designers consider how real people learn, feel, and behave.","zh":"當設計者考慮真人如何學習、感受和行動，培訓才會成功。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that people matter as much as technology.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，人和科技同樣重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a capable manager","meaning":"有能力的經理","examples":[{"en":"A capable manager knows that employee training is important.","zh":"有能力的經理知道員工培訓很重要。"},{"en":"A capable manager is a manager who can organise people, solve problems, and make good decisions.","zh":"capable manager 指能組織人員、解決問題和作出良好決策的經理。"},{"en":"A capable manager notices when staff need new skills before mistakes become serious.","zh":"有能力的經理會在錯誤變嚴重前注意到員工需要新技能。"},{"en":"Good managers improve performance by giving workers clear training and support.","zh":"好經理透過給員工清晰培訓和支援來改善表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone competent in leadership and daily operations.","zh":"這個短語描述在領導和日常營運方面有能力的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"teach employees new skills","meaning":"教授員工新技能","examples":[{"en":"Teaching employees new skills is critical to a successful business.","zh":"教授員工新技能對成功企業至關重要。"},{"en":"To teach employees new skills means to help workers learn abilities they need for their jobs.","zh":"teach employees new skills 指幫助員工學習工作所需的新能力。"},{"en":"A café may teach employees new skills when it introduces a new coffee machine.","zh":"當咖啡店引入新咖啡機時，可能要教授員工新技能。"},{"en":"New skills help employees adapt when technology, customers, or company rules change.","zh":"新技能幫助員工在科技、顧客或公司規則改變時適應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes workplace learning that improves staff ability.","zh":"這個短語描述改善員工能力的職場學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be critical to","meaning":"對……至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Teaching employees new skills is critical to a smoothly running business.","zh":"教授員工新技能對運作順暢的企業至關重要。"},{"en":"To be critical to something means to be extremely important for its success or operation.","zh":"be critical to something 指對某事成功或運作極其重要。"},{"en":"Clear instructions are critical to student safety during a science experiment.","zh":"清楚指示對科學實驗中的學生安全至關重要。"},{"en":"If training is critical to a business, ignoring it can create serious problems.","zh":"如果培訓對企業至關重要，忽視它可能造成嚴重問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is necessary, not optional.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事是必要的，而不是可有可無。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a smoothly running business","meaning":"運作順暢的企業","examples":[{"en":"Effective training is critical to a smoothly running business.","zh":"有效培訓對運作順暢的企業至關重要。"},{"en":"A smoothly running business is a company that operates efficiently with few delays or mistakes.","zh":"smoothly running business 指高效運作、少延誤和少錯誤的公司。"},{"en":"A shop with trained staff, clear duties, and reliable systems is a smoothly running business.","zh":"有受訓員工、清晰職責和可靠系統的商店就是運作順暢的企業。"},{"en":"When a business runs smoothly, customers receive better service and workers feel less confused.","zh":"當企業運作順暢，顧客得到更好服務，員工也較少混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an organisation that works well day to day.","zh":"這個短語描述日常運作良好的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"having said that","meaning":"話雖如此","examples":[{"en":"Having said that, classroom instruction can be expensive and ineffective.","zh":"話雖如此，課堂教學可能昂貴且低效。"},{"en":"Having said that means although the previous point is true, another contrasting point should be considered.","zh":"having said that 指雖然前面的觀點成立，但仍應考慮另一個對比點。"},{"en":"Online learning is flexible; having said that, some students still need face-to-face help.","zh":"網上學習很靈活；話雖如此，有些學生仍需要面對面幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers give a balanced argument.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者提出平衡論證。"},{"en":"It introduces a qualification or contrast after agreement.","zh":"它在同意後引出修正或對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the traditional route of","meaning":"傳統的……途徑","examples":[{"en":"The traditional route of classroom instruction has several drawbacks.","zh":"傳統的課堂教學途徑有幾個缺點。"},{"en":"The traditional route of something means the usual older way of doing it.","zh":"traditional route of something 指做某事的一般舊方法。"},{"en":"The traditional route of job hunting involved printed résumés and newspaper advertisements.","zh":"傳統求職途徑包括印刷履歷和報紙廣告。"},{"en":"Traditional routes may be familiar, but they can become slow or costly.","zh":"傳統途徑可能熟悉，但可以變得緩慢或昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts older methods with newer alternatives.","zh":"這個短語把舊方法與新替代方案作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"classroom instruction","meaning":"課堂教學","examples":[{"en":"Classroom instruction can take employees away from their jobs.","zh":"課堂教學會令員工離開工作崗位。"},{"en":"Classroom instruction is teaching that happens in a physical classroom with an instructor present.","zh":"classroom instruction 指在實體課室中由導師現場進行的教學。"},{"en":"A company may use classroom instruction for role-play and group discussion.","zh":"公司可能使用課堂教學進行角色扮演和小組討論。"},{"en":"It can help interaction, but it may require travel and time away from work.","zh":"它可以幫助互動，但可能需要交通並令員工離開工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes traditional face-to-face teaching.","zh":"這個短語描述傳統面對面教學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"run the risk of","meaning":"冒着……的風險","examples":[{"en":"Classroom instruction runs the risk of being expensive and slow.","zh":"課堂教學冒着昂貴和緩慢的風險。"},{"en":"To run the risk of something means to face the possibility of a negative result.","zh":"run the risk of something 指面對某個負面結果的可能性。"},{"en":"A student who starts revision too late runs the risk of forgetting important topics.","zh":"太遲開始溫習的學生冒着忘記重要課題的風險。"},{"en":"If training is poorly planned, it runs the risk of wasting time and money.","zh":"如果培訓規劃不佳，它會冒着浪費時間和金錢的風險。"},{"en":"This phrase warns about possible danger or disadvantage.","zh":"這個短語警告可能出現危險或缺點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"expensive, slow and ineffective","meaning":"昂貴、緩慢而低效","examples":[{"en":"Traditional classroom instruction can be expensive, slow and ineffective.","zh":"傳統課堂教學可能昂貴、緩慢而低效。"},{"en":"Expensive, slow and ineffective means costly, time-consuming, and not producing good results.","zh":"expensive, slow and ineffective 指成本高、耗時長，而且不能產生好結果。"},{"en":"A badly organised meeting can be expensive, slow and ineffective if many staff attend but no decisions are made.","zh":"如果許多員工參加卻沒有作出決定，一場組織差劣的會議可能昂貴、緩慢而低效。"},{"en":"Training becomes ineffective when learners are bored or cannot apply what they learn.","zh":"當學習者感到沉悶或不能應用所學，培訓就會低效。"},{"en":"This phrase gives three serious weaknesses together.","zh":"這個短語一次列出三個嚴重弱點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"greatest disadvantage","meaning":"最大缺點","examples":[{"en":"The classroom’s greatest disadvantage is that it takes employees out of their jobs.","zh":"課堂教學的最大缺點是它令員工離開工作崗位。"},{"en":"The greatest disadvantage is the most serious weakness of something.","zh":"greatest disadvantage 指某事最嚴重的弱點。"},{"en":"The greatest disadvantage of living far from school may be the long travel time.","zh":"住得離學校遠的最大缺點可能是交通時間很長。"},{"en":"Identifying the greatest disadvantage helps people decide whether an option is worth choosing.","zh":"找出最大缺點有助人決定某選項是否值得選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the main problem.","zh":"這個短語指出主要問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"take employees out of their jobs","meaning":"令員工離開工作崗位","examples":[{"en":"Classroom training takes employees out of their jobs.","zh":"課堂培訓令員工離開工作崗位。"},{"en":"To take employees out of their jobs means to remove workers from their normal duties for a period of time.","zh":"take employees out of their jobs 指在一段時間內令員工離開正常職責。"},{"en":"A full-day workshop may take nurses out of their jobs and leave fewer staff on the ward.","zh":"全日工作坊可能令護士離開工作崗位，病房人手變少。"},{"en":"When many employees leave work for training, daily operations may slow down.","zh":"當許多員工離開工作去培訓，日常營運可能變慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the work disruption caused by training.","zh":"這個短語描述培訓造成的工作干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"training session","meaning":"培訓課節","examples":[{"en":"Every minute in a training session is a minute away from work.","zh":"培訓課節中的每一分鐘，都是離開工作的每一分鐘。"},{"en":"A training session is a scheduled period when people learn or practise work-related skills.","zh":"training session 指一段安排好的時間，讓人學習或練習與工作有關的技能。"},{"en":"A supermarket may hold a training session on how to handle customer complaints.","zh":"超級市場可能舉辦關於如何處理顧客投訴的培訓課節。"},{"en":"Training sessions can be useful, but they also take time from normal duties.","zh":"培訓課節可以有用，但也會佔用正常工作時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one organised unit of training.","zh":"這個短語描述一個有組織的培訓單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"out on the floor working","meaning":"在前線工作","examples":[{"en":"Employees in a classroom are not out on the floor working.","zh":"在課室中的員工並不是在前線工作。"},{"en":"Out on the floor working means doing the actual job in the workplace, especially in shops, factories, or service areas.","zh":"out on the floor working 指在工作場所實際工作，尤其在商店、工廠或服務區。"},{"en":"A retail worker out on the floor is helping customers, arranging products, or checking shelves.","zh":"在前線工作的零售員正在幫助顧客、整理貨品或檢查貨架。"},{"en":"If too many workers attend training at once, fewer people are out on the floor working.","zh":"如果太多員工同時參加培訓，在前線工作的人就會變少。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts real work duties with time spent in training.","zh":"這個短語對比實際工作職責與培訓時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"it looks as if","meaning":"看來似乎","examples":[{"en":"It looks as if e-training can avoid some traditional drawbacks.","zh":"看來似乎電子培訓可以避開一些傳統缺點。"},{"en":"It looks as if means it seems that something is true based on available evidence.","zh":"it looks as if 指根據現有證據，看起來某事是真的。"},{"en":"It looks as if the lesson worked because students can now answer the questions correctly.","zh":"看來這堂課有效，因為學生現在能正確回答問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a reasonable impression, not absolute certainty.","zh":"這個短語表示合理印象，而不是絕對肯定。"},{"en":"It is useful when drawing a cautious conclusion.","zh":"它適合用於作出謹慎結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a way to circumvent","meaning":"避開……的方法","examples":[{"en":"E-training offers a way to circumvent traditional training drawbacks.","zh":"電子培訓提供了一種避開傳統培訓缺點的方法。"},{"en":"A way to circumvent something is a method for avoiding a problem or obstacle.","zh":"a way to circumvent something 指避開某問題或障礙的方法。"},{"en":"Online payment offers a way to circumvent long queues at a ticket office.","zh":"網上付款提供了一種避開售票處長隊的方法。"},{"en":"If a method circumvents a problem, it does not remove the problem directly but works around it.","zh":"如果一種方法避開某問題，它不是直接消除問題，而是繞過它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical workaround.","zh":"這個短語描述實用的替代路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"traditional training drawbacks","meaning":"傳統培訓的缺點","examples":[{"en":"E-training may reduce traditional training drawbacks.","zh":"電子培訓可能減少傳統培訓的缺點。"},{"en":"Traditional training drawbacks are the weaknesses of older classroom-based training methods.","zh":"traditional training drawbacks 指較舊課堂式培訓方法的弱點。"},{"en":"Travel time, high costs, and missed work can be traditional training drawbacks.","zh":"交通時間、高成本和耽誤工作都可以是傳統培訓的缺點。"},{"en":"Reducing these drawbacks makes training easier to fit into daily work.","zh":"減少這些缺點，會令培訓更容易融入日常工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the disadvantages of older training systems.","zh":"這個短語描述舊式培訓系統的劣勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"effective teaching techniques","meaning":"有效的教學技巧","examples":[{"en":"E-training promises more effective teaching techniques.","zh":"電子培訓承諾提供更有效的教學技巧。"},{"en":"Effective teaching techniques are methods that help learners understand, remember, and use what they learn.","zh":"effective teaching techniques 指幫助學習者理解、記住並使用所學的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher uses effective techniques when she gives examples, practice, and feedback.","zh":"當老師給例子、練習和回饋時，就是使用有效教學技巧。"},{"en":"Better techniques can raise motivation and improve test performance.","zh":"更好的技巧可以提升動機並改善測驗表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes teaching methods that actually help learning happen.","zh":"這個短語描述真正幫助學習發生的教學方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"integrate audio and video","meaning":"結合音訊和影片","examples":[{"en":"E-training can integrate audio and video with interactive materials.","zh":"電子培訓可以把音訊和影片與互動教材結合。"},{"en":"To integrate audio and video means to combine sound and moving images with other learning resources.","zh":"integrate audio and video 指把聲音和動態影像與其他學習資源結合。"},{"en":"A language course may integrate audio and video so students can hear pronunciation and see context.","zh":"語言課程可能結合音訊和影片，讓學生聽到發音並看到語境。"},{"en":"Combining media can make lessons clearer because learners receive information in different ways.","zh":"結合不同媒體可以令課堂更清楚，因為學習者以不同方式接收資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mixing sound and visual material into a course.","zh":"這個短語描述把聲音和視覺材料混入課程中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"animation and text","meaning":"動畫和文字","examples":[{"en":"The course integrates animation and text with other learning materials.","zh":"課程把動畫和文字與其他學習材料結合。"},{"en":"Animation and text means moving images combined with written words.","zh":"animation and text 指動態影像與書面文字的結合。"},{"en":"A science lesson may use animation and text to explain how blood moves through the heart.","zh":"科學課可能使用動畫和文字解釋血液如何流經心臟。"},{"en":"Animation can show movement, while text can explain key terms clearly.","zh":"動畫可以展示動作，而文字可以清楚解釋關鍵詞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two media types often used together in digital learning.","zh":"這個短語描述數碼學習中常一起使用的兩種媒體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"interactive materials","meaning":"互動教材","examples":[{"en":"Interactive materials can help students learn at their own pace.","zh":"互動教材可以幫助學生按自己的步伐學習。"},{"en":"Interactive materials are learning resources that require learners to click, answer, choose, practise, or respond.","zh":"interactive materials 指要求學習者點擊、回答、選擇、練習或回應的學習資源。"},{"en":"An online quiz with instant feedback is an interactive material.","zh":"有即時回饋的網上測驗是一種互動教材。"},{"en":"Interaction keeps learners active and can show them mistakes immediately.","zh":"互動令學習者保持主動，並可以即時顯示錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes materials that learners use actively, not just read passively.","zh":"這個短語描述學習者主動使用，而不只是被動閱讀的教材。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"with the intention of","meaning":"旨在；以……為目的","examples":[{"en":"The materials are designed with the intention of teaching each student individually.","zh":"這些材料的設計旨在個別教授每名學生。"},{"en":"With the intention of doing something means with the purpose or aim of doing it.","zh":"with the intention of doing something 指以做某事為目的。"},{"en":"A teacher may group students with the intention of letting stronger students support weaker ones.","zh":"老師可能把學生分組，旨在讓較強學生支援較弱學生。"},{"en":"When materials are designed with a clear intention, their activities usually fit the goal better.","zh":"當材料設計有清晰意圖，其活動通常更配合目標。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the planned purpose behind an action.","zh":"這個短語解釋行動背後的計劃目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at one’s own pace","meaning":"按自己的步伐","examples":[{"en":"E-training allows each student to learn at his or her own pace.","zh":"電子培訓讓每名學生按自己的步伐學習。"},{"en":"At one’s own pace means at a speed that suits that person.","zh":"at one’s own pace 指以適合自己的速度。"},{"en":"A beginner may learn grammar at her own pace by repeating difficult lessons.","zh":"初學者可以透過重複困難課堂，按自己的步伐學習文法。"},{"en":"Learning at one’s own pace can reduce pressure and improve understanding.","zh":"按自己的步伐學習可以減少壓力並改善理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes flexible speed controlled by the learner.","zh":"這個短語描述由學習者控制的靈活速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"higher performance results","meaning":"更高的表現成果","examples":[{"en":"E-training can lead to higher performance results.","zh":"電子培訓可以帶來更高的表現成果。"},{"en":"Higher performance results are better outcomes in tests, work, or practical tasks.","zh":"higher performance results 指在測驗、工作或實務任務中有更好結果。"},{"en":"A sales team may achieve higher performance results after practising customer conversations online.","zh":"銷售團隊在網上練習顧客對話後，可能取得更高的表現成果。"},{"en":"Better training can improve performance because learners practise more and receive clearer feedback.","zh":"更好培訓可以改善表現，因為學習者練習更多並得到更清楚回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improved measurable results.","zh":"這個短語描述可量度結果的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"immediate benefits to","meaning":"對……的即時好處","examples":[{"en":"There are immediate benefits to students who learn online.","zh":"網上學習對學生有即時好處。"},{"en":"Immediate benefits to someone are advantages that help that person quickly or directly.","zh":"immediate benefits to someone 指快速或直接幫助某人的好處。"},{"en":"A quiet classroom gives immediate benefits to students who need to concentrate.","zh":"安靜課室對需要專注的學生有即時好處。"},{"en":"Online learning may immediately benefit learners by saving travel time and allowing replay.","zh":"網上學習可以透過節省交通時間和容許重播，立即讓學習者受益。"},{"en":"This phrase describes advantages that appear quickly.","zh":"這個短語描述很快出現的好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"increased time on task","meaning":"更長的專注學習時間","examples":[{"en":"E-learning can produce increased time on task.","zh":"電子學習可以帶來更長的專注學習時間。"},{"en":"Increased time on task means learners spend more time actively working on the learning activity.","zh":"increased time on task 指學習者花更多時間主動進行學習活動。"},{"en":"A reading app may increase time on task by giving students short daily exercises.","zh":"閱讀應用程式可能透過每日短練習增加學生專注學習時間。"},{"en":"More time on task usually gives learners more practice and more chances to improve.","zh":"更多專注學習時間通常給學習者更多練習和改善機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes longer active learning time.","zh":"這個短語描述更長的主動學習時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"higher levels of motivation","meaning":"更高的學習動機","examples":[{"en":"Some learners show higher levels of motivation in e-learning.","zh":"有些學習者在電子學習中顯示更高的學習動機。"},{"en":"Higher levels of motivation mean stronger willingness and energy to learn or complete tasks.","zh":"higher levels of motivation 指更強的學習或完成任務意願和能量。"},{"en":"Students may show higher motivation when lessons include games, goals, and immediate feedback.","zh":"當課堂包括遊戲、目標和即時回饋，學生可能顯示更高動機。"},{"en":"Motivation can increase effort, attention, and persistence.","zh":"動機可以增加努力、注意力和堅持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learners being more willing to keep learning.","zh":"這個短語描述學習者更願意持續學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reduced test anxiety","meaning":"減少考試焦慮","examples":[{"en":"E-learning may lead to reduced test anxiety for many learners.","zh":"電子學習可能令許多學習者減少考試焦慮。"},{"en":"Reduced test anxiety means less fear or nervousness before or during tests.","zh":"reduced test anxiety 指考試前或考試期間較少恐懼或緊張。"},{"en":"Practice quizzes can reduce test anxiety because students know what to expect.","zh":"練習測驗可以減少考試焦慮，因為學生知道可以預期甚麼。"},{"en":"When anxiety is lower, learners may think more clearly and perform better.","zh":"當焦慮較低，學習者可能思考更清晰並表現更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decrease in exam-related stress.","zh":"這個短語描述考試相關壓力下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"perform better than","meaning":"表現比……好","examples":[{"en":"E-learners performed better than traditional learners in one study.","zh":"在一項研究中，電子學習者表現比傳統學習者好。"},{"en":"To perform better than someone means to achieve stronger results than that person or group.","zh":"perform better than someone 指取得比某人或某群體更好的結果。"},{"en":"A student who practises daily may perform better than one who only revises the night before.","zh":"每天練習的學生，可能比只在考試前一晚溫習的學生表現更好。"},{"en":"Better performance may come from more practice, clearer feedback, or stronger motivation.","zh":"更好表現可能來自更多練習、更清楚回饋或更強動機。"},{"en":"This phrase compares achievement between two groups.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個群體之間的成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"traditional learners","meaning":"傳統學習者","examples":[{"en":"E-learners performed 20 per cent better than traditional learners.","zh":"電子學習者的表現比傳統學習者好百分之二十。"},{"en":"Traditional learners are learners who study mainly through face-to-face classroom methods.","zh":"traditional learners 指主要透過面對面課堂方法學習的人。"},{"en":"Traditional learners may attend lectures, take paper notes, and ask questions in class.","zh":"傳統學習者可能聽講座、做紙本筆記並在課堂提問。"},{"en":"Comparing traditional learners with online learners helps researchers evaluate teaching methods.","zh":"比較傳統學習者和網上學習者，有助研究人員評估教學方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learners in older or classroom-based systems.","zh":"這個短語描述在較舊或課堂式系統中的學習者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a significant difference between","meaning":"……之間的顯著差異","examples":[{"en":"Nelson reported a significant difference between the mean grades of two groups.","zh":"Nelson 報告兩組平均成績之間有顯著差異。"},{"en":"A significant difference between two things is a clear and important difference that is unlikely to be ignored.","zh":"significant difference between two things 指兩者之間清楚且重要、不應被忽略的差異。"},{"en":"A teacher may see a significant difference between students who revise weekly and those who do not.","zh":"老師可能看見每週溫習的學生與不溫習的學生之間有顯著差異。"},{"en":"Significant differences can suggest that one method may be more effective than another.","zh":"顯著差異可以暗示一種方法可能比另一種更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when comparing research results.","zh":"這個短語常用於比較研究結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"mean grades","meaning":"平均成績","examples":[{"en":"The study compared the mean grades earned by university students.","zh":"該研究比較大學生取得的平均成績。"},{"en":"Mean grades are average grades calculated from a group of students’ scores.","zh":"mean grades 指由一組學生分數計算出的平均成績。"},{"en":"A teacher may compare mean grades before and after a new revision programme.","zh":"老師可能比較新溫習計劃前後的平均成績。"},{"en":"Mean grades help researchers see the overall performance of a class or group.","zh":"平均成績幫助研究人員看見班級或群體的整體表現。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to average results, not one student’s mark.","zh":"這個短語指平均結果，而不是某一名學生的分數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"traditional and distance-education classes","meaning":"傳統課堂和遙距教育課堂","examples":[{"en":"The study compared students in traditional and distance-education classes.","zh":"該研究比較傳統課堂和遙距教育課堂中的學生。"},{"en":"Traditional and distance-education classes are classroom-based courses and courses studied from a distance.","zh":"traditional and distance-education classes 指課室式課程和遙距學習課程。"},{"en":"A university may offer both traditional and distance-education classes for working adults.","zh":"大學可能為在職成人提供傳統課堂和遙距教育課堂。"},{"en":"Comparing the two formats helps schools decide which methods suit which learners.","zh":"比較兩種形式有助學校決定哪些方法適合哪些學習者。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts physical classroom learning with remote learning.","zh":"這個短語對比實體課堂學習和遙距學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"distance learners","meaning":"遙距學習者","examples":[{"en":"Distance learners outperformed traditional learners in Nelson’s report.","zh":"在 Nelson 的報告中，遙距學習者表現優於傳統學習者。"},{"en":"Distance learners are students who study remotely rather than attending regular face-to-face classes.","zh":"distance learners 指遙距學習，而不是定期參加面對面課堂的學生。"},{"en":"A parent with a full-time job may become a distance learner to study at night.","zh":"有全職工作的家長可能成為遙距學習者，在晚上學習。"},{"en":"Distance learners need self-discipline because teachers are not physically beside them.","zh":"遙距學習者需要自律，因為老師不是實體在旁邊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people learning from another location.","zh":"這個短語描述在另一地點學習的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"outperform traditional learners","meaning":"表現優於傳統學習者","examples":[{"en":"Distance learners may outperform traditional learners in some studies.","zh":"在一些研究中，遙距學習者可能表現優於傳統學習者。"},{"en":"To outperform traditional learners means to achieve better results than learners in classroom-based courses.","zh":"outperform traditional learners 指取得比課室式學習者更好的結果。"},{"en":"Online students may outperform traditional learners if they replay lessons and practise more often.","zh":"如果網上學生重播課堂並更常練習，可能表現優於傳統學習者。"},{"en":"Higher performance may depend on course design, learner motivation, and support.","zh":"較高表現可能取決於課程設計、學習動機和支援。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the success of remote learners with classroom learners.","zh":"這個短語比較遙距學習者與課室學習者的成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"On the other hand, e-training technology can be expensive.","zh":"另一方面，電子培訓科技可能很昂貴。"},{"en":"On the other hand introduces a contrasting point or another side of an argument.","zh":"on the other hand 引出對比觀點或論點的另一面。"},{"en":"Online learning is flexible; on the other hand, some students miss classroom interaction.","zh":"網上學習很靈活；另一方面，有些學生懷念課堂互動。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers build balanced discussion.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者建立平衡討論。"},{"en":"It signals that the next idea may challenge or limit the previous one.","zh":"它表示下一個想法可能挑戰或限制前一個想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"e-training technology","meaning":"電子培訓科技","examples":[{"en":"E-training technology is not always cheap to develop.","zh":"電子培訓科技並不總是便宜開發。"},{"en":"E-training technology includes the software, platforms, media tools, and systems used for online training.","zh":"e-training technology 包括用於網上培訓的軟件、平台、媒體工具和系統。"},{"en":"A company may need e-training technology to host videos, quizzes, and learner records.","zh":"公司可能需要電子培訓科技來托管影片、測驗和學習者紀錄。"},{"en":"The technology can improve training, but development and maintenance may be costly.","zh":"這種科技可以改善培訓，但開發和維護可能昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the technical tools behind digital training.","zh":"這個短語指數碼培訓背後的技術工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"service providers","meaning":"服務供應商","examples":[{"en":"E-training service providers charge high fees for online instruction.","zh":"電子培訓服務供應商為網上教學收取高昂費用。"},{"en":"Service providers are companies or people that supply a particular service to clients.","zh":"service providers 指向客戶提供特定服務的公司或人士。"},{"en":"An Internet service provider gives homes and offices access to the Internet.","zh":"互聯網服務供應商為家庭和辦公室提供上網服務。"},{"en":"When companies lack internal skills, they may hire service providers to build training courses.","zh":"當公司缺乏內部技能時，可能聘請服務供應商建立培訓課程。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to outside organisations that deliver a service.","zh":"這個短語指提供服務的外部機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"on average","meaning":"平均而言","examples":[{"en":"Service providers, on average, charge large sums for online instruction.","zh":"服務供應商平均而言為網上教學收取大筆費用。"},{"en":"On average means when the total is divided across all examples or cases.","zh":"on average 指把總數分配到所有例子或個案後得出的水平。"},{"en":"Students in the class read, on average, twenty pages a week.","zh":"這班學生平均而言每星期閱讀二十頁。"},{"en":"Averages help describe the general level, even though individual cases may vary.","zh":"平均數幫助描述一般水平，即使個別情況可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a typical amount rather than an exact amount for every case.","zh":"這個短語給出典型數量，而不是每個個案的精確數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"charge between…and…","meaning":"收取介乎……至……的費用","examples":[{"en":"Providers may charge between $10,000 and $60,000 for one hour of online instruction.","zh":"供應商可能為一小時網上教學收取介乎一萬至六萬美元的費用。"},{"en":"To charge between A and B means to ask for a price within that range.","zh":"charge between A and B 指要求某個範圍內的價格。"},{"en":"A tutor may charge between 300 and 500 dollars per lesson depending on experience.","zh":"導師可能視乎經驗每堂收取介乎三百至五百元的費用。"},{"en":"A wide price range may reflect different levels of complexity and quality.","zh":"價格範圍很大，可能反映不同複雜程度和質素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a minimum and maximum price.","zh":"這個短語描述最低和最高價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"develop one hour of online instruction","meaning":"製作一小時網上教學內容","examples":[{"en":"It can be expensive to develop one hour of online instruction.","zh":"製作一小時網上教學內容可能很昂貴。"},{"en":"To develop one hour of online instruction means to create enough digital teaching material for one hour of learning.","zh":"develop one hour of online instruction 指製作足夠一小時學習用的數碼教學材料。"},{"en":"A designer may need scripts, videos, quizzes, graphics, and testing to develop one online lesson.","zh":"設計者可能需要講稿、影片、測驗、圖像和測試，才能製作一堂網上課。"},{"en":"Development takes time because online materials must work technically and teach clearly.","zh":"製作需要時間，因為網上材料必須技術上可運作並能清楚教學。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the production work behind a digital course hour.","zh":"這個短語描述一小時數碼課程背後的製作工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"online instruction","meaning":"網上教學","examples":[{"en":"The cost of online instruction depends on the topic and media used.","zh":"網上教學的成本取決於課題和所使用的媒體。"},{"en":"Online instruction is teaching delivered through the Internet.","zh":"online instruction 指透過互聯網提供的教學。"},{"en":"A teacher may provide online instruction through video lessons and live chat.","zh":"老師可能透過影片課堂和即時聊天提供網上教學。"},{"en":"Online instruction can be cheap if simple, but expensive if it uses video, animation, and testing systems.","zh":"如果形式簡單，網上教學可以便宜；如果使用影片、動畫和測試系統，則可能昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes Internet-based teaching.","zh":"這個短語描述以互聯網為基礎的教學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"vary depending on","meaning":"視乎……而有所不同","examples":[{"en":"The price varies depending on the complexity of the training topic.","zh":"價格視乎培訓課題的複雜程度而有所不同。"},{"en":"To vary depending on something means to change according to that factor.","zh":"vary depending on something 指根據某因素而改變。"},{"en":"Travel time varies depending on traffic, weather, and transport choice.","zh":"交通時間視乎交通、天氣和交通工具選擇而有所不同。"},{"en":"If prices vary depending on complexity, harder topics usually cost more to develop.","zh":"如果價格視乎複雜程度而不同，較難課題通常開發成本更高。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why something is not fixed.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何某事並非固定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the complexity of","meaning":"……的複雜程度","examples":[{"en":"The price depends on the complexity of the training topic.","zh":"價格取決於培訓課題的複雜程度。"},{"en":"The complexity of something means how difficult, detailed, or complicated it is.","zh":"complexity of something 指某事有多困難、詳細或複雜。"},{"en":"The complexity of a maths problem affects how long students need to solve it.","zh":"數學題的複雜程度會影響學生需要多久才能解答。"},{"en":"More complex training may require more examples, media, practice, and expert review.","zh":"較複雜的培訓可能需要更多例子、媒體、練習和專家審閱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the level of difficulty within a subject or task.","zh":"這個短語描述主題或任務內部的難度水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"training topic","meaning":"培訓課題","examples":[{"en":"A complex training topic costs more to develop.","zh":"複雜的培訓課題開發成本更高。"},{"en":"A training topic is the subject or skill that a course teaches.","zh":"training topic 指課程教授的主題或技能。"},{"en":"Fire safety, customer service, and data privacy can all be training topics.","zh":"消防安全、客戶服務和資料私隱都可以是培訓課題。"},{"en":"Clear topics are cheaper to teach because objectives and examples are easier to design.","zh":"清晰課題較便宜，因為目標和例子較容易設計。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what the training is about.","zh":"這個短語描述培訓關於甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the media used","meaning":"所使用的媒體","examples":[{"en":"The cost depends partly on the media used.","zh":"成本部分取決於所使用的媒體。"},{"en":"The media used are the types of content, such as text, audio, video, animation, or interactive quizzes.","zh":"media used 指內容形式，例如文字、音訊、影片、動畫或互動測驗。"},{"en":"A course using only text costs less than one using filmed scenes and voice acting.","zh":"只使用文字的課程比使用拍攝場景和配音的課程成本低。"},{"en":"More advanced media can make learning richer but also increase production costs.","zh":"更先進媒體可以令學習更豐富，但也會增加製作成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the communication formats chosen for a course.","zh":"這個短語描述課程所選擇的傳達形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"HTML pages","meaning":"HTML 網頁","examples":[{"en":"HTML pages are cheaper to develop than streaming-video presentations.","zh":"HTML 網頁比串流影片簡報更便宜開發。"},{"en":"HTML pages are basic web pages made with code that displays text, images, and links.","zh":"HTML pages 指用程式碼製作、顯示文字、圖片和連結的基本網頁。"},{"en":"A simple company policy course may be delivered through HTML pages with short quizzes.","zh":"簡單公司政策課程可能透過 HTML 網頁和短測驗提供。"},{"en":"They cost less because they require less filming, editing, and technical production.","zh":"它們成本較低，因為需要較少拍攝、剪接和技術製作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple web-based content format.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單的網頁式內容格式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"streaming-video presentations","meaning":"串流影片簡報","examples":[{"en":"Streaming-video presentations cost more to develop.","zh":"串流影片簡報開發成本更高。"},{"en":"Streaming-video presentations are online video lessons or talks that play through the Internet.","zh":"streaming-video presentations 指透過互聯網播放的網上影片課堂或講解。"},{"en":"A company may use streaming-video presentations to show a trainer explaining a new product.","zh":"公司可能使用串流影片簡報，展示培訓員講解新產品。"},{"en":"They can be engaging, but filming, editing, hosting, and bandwidth can raise costs.","zh":"它們可以吸引人，但拍攝、剪接、寄存和頻寬都會增加成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes video-based online teaching material.","zh":"這個短語描述以影片為基礎的網上教學材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Flash animations","meaning":"Flash 動畫","examples":[{"en":"Flash animations are more expensive than simple HTML pages.","zh":"Flash 動畫比簡單 HTML 網頁更昂貴。"},{"en":"Flash animations are animated digital materials, formerly common on websites and online courses.","zh":"Flash animations 指動畫式數碼材料，過去常見於網站和網上課程。"},{"en":"A training course might use animations to show how a machine works step by step.","zh":"培訓課程可能使用動畫逐步展示機器如何運作。"},{"en":"Animation can make difficult processes clearer, but it usually costs more to design.","zh":"動畫可以令困難過程更清楚，但通常設計成本更高。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to animated online content rather than plain text pages.","zh":"這個短語指動畫式網上內容，而不是純文字網頁。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"course content","meaning":"課程內容","examples":[{"en":"Course content is only the starting point for costs.","zh":"課程內容只是成本的起點。"},{"en":"Course content is the actual material taught in a course, such as lessons, readings, videos, and quizzes.","zh":"course content 指課程中實際教授的材料，例如課堂、閱讀、影片和測驗。"},{"en":"A grammar course’s content may include tense rules, examples, exercises, and answer explanations.","zh":"文法課程內容可能包括時態規則、例子、練習和答案解釋。"},{"en":"Content is necessary, but platforms, support, and delivery systems also cost money.","zh":"內容是必要的，但平台、支援和傳送系統也要花錢。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to what learners study inside a course.","zh":"這個短語指學習者在課程中學習的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the starting point for","meaning":"……的起點","examples":[{"en":"Course content is just the starting point for costs.","zh":"課程內容只是成本的起點。"},{"en":"The starting point for something is the first stage or basic beginning of a larger process.","zh":"starting point for something 指較大過程的第一階段或基本開始。"},{"en":"Choosing a topic is the starting point for writing a research essay.","zh":"選擇題目是撰寫研究文章的起點。"},{"en":"After the starting point, many extra steps may still be needed.","zh":"起點之後，可能仍需要許多額外步驟。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that one thing begins the process but does not complete it.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者，一件事開啟過程，但不代表完成過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a complete e-learning solution","meaning":"完整的電子學習方案","examples":[{"en":"A complete e-learning solution includes more than course content.","zh":"完整的電子學習方案不只包括課程內容。"},{"en":"A complete e-learning solution is a full system that includes content, platform, access, tracking, and support.","zh":"complete e-learning solution 指包含內容、平台、存取、追蹤和支援的完整系統。"},{"en":"A company needs a complete solution if thousands of employees must take and record training.","zh":"如果數千名員工必須接受並記錄培訓，公司需要完整方案。"},{"en":"Without a full solution, learners may have materials but no reliable way to access or complete them.","zh":"沒有完整方案，學習者可能有材料，卻沒有可靠方式存取或完成它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the whole package needed for online learning to work.","zh":"這個短語描述網上學習能運作所需的整體配套。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"technology platform","meaning":"科技平台","examples":[{"en":"The technology platform delivers the online courses.","zh":"科技平台傳送網上課程。"},{"en":"A technology platform is the digital system that hosts, manages, and delivers online services or content.","zh":"technology platform 指寄存、管理和提供網上服務或內容的數碼系統。"},{"en":"A school may use a technology platform where students watch videos and submit homework.","zh":"學校可能使用科技平台，讓學生觀看影片和提交功課。"},{"en":"A good platform makes learning easier because materials, records, and communication stay organised.","zh":"好平台令學習更容易，因為材料、紀錄和溝通都保持有組織。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the technical base of an online course system.","zh":"這個短語描述網上課程系統的技術基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"network connections","meaning":"網絡連線","examples":[{"en":"Network connections are part of the technology platform.","zh":"網絡連線是科技平台的一部分。"},{"en":"Network connections are the links that allow computers and devices to communicate with each other or the Internet.","zh":"network connections 指讓電腦和裝置彼此或與互聯網溝通的連接。"},{"en":"A weak network connection can make an online lesson freeze or disconnect.","zh":"網絡連線弱可能令網上課堂畫面停頓或斷線。"},{"en":"Good network connections are necessary when many employees stream videos at the same time.","zh":"當許多員工同時串流影片時，良好網絡連線是必要的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the communication links behind online learning.","zh":"這個短語描述網上學習背後的通訊連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"deliver the courses","meaning":"傳送課程","examples":[{"en":"The platform is used to deliver the courses.","zh":"該平台用來傳送課程。"},{"en":"To deliver the courses means to provide the lessons and materials to learners.","zh":"deliver the courses 指把課堂和材料提供給學習者。"},{"en":"A university may deliver the courses through a learning management system.","zh":"大學可能透過學習管理系統傳送課程。"},{"en":"If delivery fails, students may not receive lessons even if the content is good.","zh":"如果傳送失敗，即使內容很好，學生也可能收不到課堂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making courses available to learners.","zh":"這個短語描述讓學習者能取得課程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"learning management system","meaning":"學習管理系統","examples":[{"en":"A learning management system is used to deliver and manage courses.","zh":"學習管理系統用來傳送和管理課程。"},{"en":"A learning management system is software that organises online courses, learners, records, and assessments.","zh":"learning management system 指管理網上課程、學習者、紀錄和評估的軟件。"},{"en":"A school may use a learning management system to track homework submission and quiz scores.","zh":"學校可能使用學習管理系統追蹤功課提交和測驗分數。"},{"en":"It helps organisations manage training because progress can be recorded automatically.","zh":"它幫助機構管理培訓，因為進度可以自動記錄。"},{"en":"This phrase is often shortened to LMS.","zh":"這個短語常簡稱為 LMS。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be installed on site","meaning":"安裝在現場","examples":[{"en":"The learning management system can be installed on site.","zh":"學習管理系統可以安裝在現場。"},{"en":"To be installed on site means to be set up physically or locally at the organisation’s own location.","zh":"be installed on site 指在機構自己的地點實體或本地設定。"},{"en":"A company may install software on site if it wants direct control over its data.","zh":"如果公司想直接控制資料，可能把軟件安裝在現場。"},{"en":"On-site installation can give control, but it may require technical staff and maintenance.","zh":"現場安裝可以提供控制權，但可能需要技術人員和維護。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts local setup with using an outside service.","zh":"這個短語把本地設定與使用外部服務作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be outsourced","meaning":"外判","examples":[{"en":"The learning management system can be outsourced.","zh":"學習管理系統可以外判。"},{"en":"To be outsourced means to be handled by an outside company rather than internally.","zh":"be outsourced 指由外部公司而不是內部處理。"},{"en":"A small business may outsource payroll because it lacks accounting staff.","zh":"小企業可能外判薪酬工作，因為缺乏會計員工。"},{"en":"Outsourcing can save internal effort, but the company may depend more on a provider.","zh":"外判可以節省內部工作量，但公司可能更依賴供應商。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving work to an external specialist.","zh":"這個短語描述把工作交給外部專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"necessary investments in","meaning":"在……方面的必要投資","examples":[{"en":"Companies must make necessary investments in network bandwidth.","zh":"公司必須在網絡頻寬方面作必要投資。"},{"en":"Necessary investments in something are required spending needed for a system to work properly.","zh":"necessary investments in something 指為了系統正常運作而必須花費的開支。"},{"en":"A school may make necessary investments in tablets before launching digital textbooks.","zh":"學校推出數碼教科書前，可能需要在平板電腦方面作必要投資。"},{"en":"Without necessary investments, a new training system may fail even if the content is good.","zh":"沒有必要投資，即使內容很好，新培訓系統也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes spending that is required, not optional.","zh":"這個短語描述必需而非可選的開支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"network bandwidth","meaning":"網絡頻寬","examples":[{"en":"Network bandwidth is needed to deliver multimedia courses.","zh":"傳送多媒體課程需要網絡頻寬。"},{"en":"Network bandwidth is the amount of data a network can carry at one time.","zh":"network bandwidth 指網絡同一時間可以傳送的資料量。"},{"en":"A video call needs more network bandwidth than a plain text email.","zh":"視像通話比純文字電郵需要更多網絡頻寬。"},{"en":"If bandwidth is low, videos may freeze and online lessons may become frustrating.","zh":"如果頻寬低，影片可能停頓，網上課堂可能令人沮喪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the capacity of an Internet connection.","zh":"這個短語描述互聯網連線的容量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"deliver multimedia courses","meaning":"傳送多媒體課程","examples":[{"en":"Companies need sufficient bandwidth to deliver multimedia courses.","zh":"公司需要足夠頻寬來傳送多媒體課程。"},{"en":"To deliver multimedia courses means to provide courses containing video, audio, animation, images, and text.","zh":"deliver multimedia courses 指提供包含影片、音訊、動畫、圖像和文字的課程。"},{"en":"A university may need a strong platform to deliver multimedia courses to thousands of students.","zh":"大學可能需要強大平台，向數千名學生傳送多媒體課程。"},{"en":"Multimedia courses require more technical support because files are larger and more complex.","zh":"多媒體課程需要更多技術支援，因為檔案較大且較複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sending rich digital course materials to learners.","zh":"這個短語描述把豐富數碼課程材料傳送給學習者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be left holding one heck of a bill","meaning":"最後要承擔一筆驚人帳單","examples":[{"en":"After all the extra costs, a company may be left holding one heck of a bill.","zh":"加上所有額外成本後，公司最後可能要承擔一筆驚人帳單。"},{"en":"To be left holding one heck of a bill means to end up responsible for a surprisingly large cost.","zh":"be left holding one heck of a bill 指最後要負責一筆令人意外的高昂費用。"},{"en":"A family may be left holding one heck of a bill after ignoring hidden renovation costs.","zh":"如果家庭忽視裝修隱藏成本，最後可能要承擔一筆驚人帳單。"},{"en":"Extra platform, support, and bandwidth expenses can make an online project much more costly than expected.","zh":"額外平台、支援和頻寬開支可以令網上項目比預期昂貴得多。"},{"en":"This informal phrase warns that the final cost may be shocking.","zh":"這個非正式短語警告最終成本可能令人震驚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"LMS infrastructure","meaning":"學習管理系統基建","examples":[{"en":"LMS infrastructure can be very expensive in the first year.","zh":"學習管理系統基建在第一年可能非常昂貴。"},{"en":"LMS infrastructure is the technical foundation needed to run a learning management system.","zh":"LMS infrastructure 指運行學習管理系統所需的技術基礎。"},{"en":"It may include servers, software licences, user accounts, security, and support staff.","zh":"它可能包括伺服器、軟件授權、用戶帳戶、安全系統和支援人員。"},{"en":"Building this infrastructure costs money before many learners even start the course.","zh":"建立這些基建在許多學習者開始課程前已要花錢。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the background system that supports online training.","zh":"這個短語指支援網上培訓的背景系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a dozen or so","meaning":"大約十多個","examples":[{"en":"A company may buy a dozen or so online courses.","zh":"公司可能購買大約十多個網上課程。"},{"en":"A dozen or so means about twelve, but not necessarily exactly twelve.","zh":"a dozen or so 指大約十二個，但不一定剛好十二個。"},{"en":"A teacher may prepare a dozen or so practice questions for a short quiz.","zh":"老師可能為短測準備大約十多條練習題。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate number when exact counting is not important.","zh":"當精確數字不重要時，這個短語給出大約數量。"},{"en":"It is useful for informal estimates.","zh":"它適合用於非正式估算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"costs can top","meaning":"成本可超過……","examples":[{"en":"Costs can top $500,000 in the first year.","zh":"第一年的成本可超過五十萬美元。"},{"en":"Costs can top an amount means costs can rise above that amount.","zh":"costs can top an amount 指成本可以高於某個金額。"},{"en":"The cost of renovating an old school building can top several million dollars.","zh":"翻新舊校舍的成本可超過數百萬元。"},{"en":"When costs top expectations, managers may need to cut other spending.","zh":"當成本超出預期，管理者可能需要削減其他開支。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that expenses may exceed a high figure.","zh":"這個短語警告開支可能超過一個高數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in the first year","meaning":"在第一年","examples":[{"en":"Costs can be especially high in the first year.","zh":"成本在第一年可能尤其高。"},{"en":"In the first year means during the first twelve months after something begins.","zh":"in the first year 指某事開始後的首十二個月期間。"},{"en":"A new restaurant may spend heavily in the first year on equipment and decoration.","zh":"新餐廳在第一年可能在設備和裝修上大量花費。"},{"en":"First-year costs are often high because systems must be built from the beginning.","zh":"第一年成本通常較高，因為系統必須從頭建立。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the early stage of a project.","zh":"這個短語指出項目的早期階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"custom e-training","meaning":"度身訂造的電子培訓","examples":[{"en":"Custom e-training is currently suitable mainly for large organisations.","zh":"度身訂造的電子培訓目前主要適合大型機構。"},{"en":"Custom e-training is online training specially designed for one organisation’s needs.","zh":"custom e-training 指為某一機構需要特別設計的網上培訓。"},{"en":"A bank may build custom e-training to teach its own security rules and internal software.","zh":"銀行可能建立度身訂造的電子培訓，教授自己的安全規則和內部軟件。"},{"en":"Custom courses cost more because they must be planned, written, designed, and tested specially.","zh":"度身訂造課程成本較高，因為必須特別規劃、撰寫、設計和測試。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts tailored training with ready-made courses.","zh":"這個短語對比量身訂造培訓和現成課程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"for the time being","meaning":"暫時","examples":[{"en":"For the time being, custom e-training is mainly an option for large organisations.","zh":"暫時，度身訂造的電子培訓主要是大型機構的選項。"},{"en":"For the time being means for now, though the situation may change later.","zh":"for the time being 指目前暫時如此，但之後情況可能改變。"},{"en":"For the time being, the library will close early because of renovation work.","zh":"暫時，圖書館因裝修工程會提早關門。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a temporary situation, not a permanent rule.","zh":"這個短語暗示臨時情況，而不是永久規則。"},{"en":"It is useful when present conditions may change in the future.","zh":"當現在情況將來可能改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"an option only for","meaning":"只適合……的選項","examples":[{"en":"Custom e-training is an option only for large organisations.","zh":"度身訂造的電子培訓只是大型機構的選項。"},{"en":"An option only for a group is a choice that is realistically available only to that group.","zh":"option only for a group 指實際上只有某群體能選擇的方案。"},{"en":"Private tutoring abroad may be an option only for families with enough money.","zh":"海外私人補習可能只是有足夠金錢家庭的選項。"},{"en":"High cost can make a useful method available only to large or wealthy users.","zh":"高成本可以令有用方法只適合大型或富裕使用者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a choice limited to certain people or organisations.","zh":"這個短語描述只限某些人或機構的選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"large organisations","meaning":"大型機構","examples":[{"en":"Large organisations are more able to afford custom e-training.","zh":"大型機構更有能力負擔度身訂造的電子培訓。"},{"en":"Large organisations are big companies, institutions, or bodies with many employees and resources.","zh":"large organisations 指有許多員工和資源的大公司、機構或團體。"},{"en":"A multinational bank is a large organisation with offices in many countries.","zh":"跨國銀行是大型機構，在許多國家都有辦公室。"},{"en":"Large organisations can spread training costs across many learners.","zh":"大型機構可以把培訓成本分攤到許多學習者身上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organisations with enough size and money to support major systems.","zh":"這個短語描述有足夠規模和金錢支援大型系統的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"large enough staff","meaning":"足夠龐大的員工隊伍","examples":[{"en":"Companies with large enough staff may find that e-training pays for itself.","zh":"擁有足夠龐大員工隊伍的公司可能發現電子培訓值回成本。"},{"en":"Large enough staff means a workforce big enough to justify the cost of a system.","zh":"large enough staff 指員工規模大到足以支持某系統成本。"},{"en":"A company with only five workers may not have large enough staff for a custom training platform.","zh":"只有五名員工的公司，可能沒有足夠龐大的員工隊伍去使用度身訂造培訓平台。"},{"en":"When many employees use the same course, the cost per person falls.","zh":"當許多員工使用同一課程，每人成本就會下降。"},{"en":"This phrase links staff size with whether an investment makes sense.","zh":"這個短語把員工規模與投資是否合理連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"pay for itself","meaning":"值回成本","examples":[{"en":"For large companies, the e-training concept pays for itself.","zh":"對大型公司而言，電子培訓概念可以值回成本。"},{"en":"To pay for itself means to save or earn enough money to cover its own cost.","zh":"pay for itself 指節省或賺取足夠金錢來抵消自身成本。"},{"en":"A new coffee machine pays for itself if it saves a café more money than it costs.","zh":"如果新咖啡機為咖啡店節省的錢超過其成本，它就值回成本。"},{"en":"E-training pays for itself when savings from travel and time exceed development costs.","zh":"當差旅和時間節省超過開發成本，電子培訓就值回成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an investment becoming financially worthwhile.","zh":"這個短語描述投資在財政上變得值得。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"aware of this fact","meaning":"意識到這一點","examples":[{"en":"Aware of this fact, large companies are investing heavily in online training.","zh":"意識到這一點，大型公司正大量投資於網上培訓。"},{"en":"Aware of this fact means knowing this information and acting with it in mind.","zh":"aware of this fact 指知道這項資料，並在行動時把它考慮在內。"},{"en":"Aware of rising electricity prices, a school may invest in solar panels.","zh":"意識到電費上升，學校可能投資太陽能板。"},{"en":"When managers are aware of cost savings, they may support new training systems.","zh":"當管理者意識到成本節省，他們可能支持新培訓系統。"},{"en":"This phrase connects knowledge with action.","zh":"這個短語把知識與行動連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"invest heavily in","meaning":"大量投資於……","examples":[{"en":"Large companies are investing heavily in online training.","zh":"大型公司正大量投資於網上培訓。"},{"en":"To invest heavily in something means to spend a large amount of money, time, or effort on it.","zh":"invest heavily in something 指在某事上投入大量金錢、時間或努力。"},{"en":"A school may invest heavily in teacher training when exam results are falling.","zh":"當考試成績下降，學校可能大量投資於教師培訓。"},{"en":"Heavy investment shows that an organisation sees something as important for the future.","zh":"大量投資顯示機構認為某事對未來重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong commitment of resources.","zh":"這個短語描述對資源的強力投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"online training","meaning":"網上培訓","examples":[{"en":"Many large companies now invest heavily in online training.","zh":"許多大型公司現在大量投資於網上培訓。"},{"en":"Online training is job-related learning delivered through the Internet.","zh":"online training 指透過互聯網提供的工作相關學習。"},{"en":"A company may use online training to teach staff data privacy rules.","zh":"公司可能使用網上培訓教員工資料私隱規則。"},{"en":"It can train people in different offices without bringing everyone to one classroom.","zh":"它可以培訓不同辦公室的人，而不用把所有人帶到同一課室。"},{"en":"This phrase describes work training provided digitally.","zh":"這個短語描述以數碼方式提供的工作培訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"400-plus courses","meaning":"四百多個課程","examples":[{"en":"Rockwell Collins offers 400-plus courses to its clients.","zh":"Rockwell Collins 向客戶提供四百多個課程。"},{"en":"400-plus courses means more than four hundred courses.","zh":"400-plus courses 指超過四百個課程。"},{"en":"A university with 400-plus courses gives students many subject choices.","zh":"擁有四百多個課程的大學給學生許多科目選擇。"},{"en":"A large course catalogue can serve different job roles and skill levels.","zh":"大型課程目錄可以服務不同職位和技能水平。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate number above 400.","zh":"這個短語給出超過四百的大約數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be delivered instantly to","meaning":"即時傳送給……","examples":[{"en":"Many courses are delivered instantly to clients in an e-learning format.","zh":"許多課程以電子學習形式即時傳送給客戶。"},{"en":"To be delivered instantly to someone means to be sent or made available to them immediately.","zh":"be delivered instantly to someone 指立即傳送或提供給某人。"},{"en":"An online receipt is delivered instantly to a customer after payment.","zh":"顧客付款後，網上收據會即時傳送給他。"},{"en":"Instant delivery reduces waiting time and helps learners start sooner.","zh":"即時傳送減少等待時間，並幫助學習者更快開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes immediate electronic access.","zh":"這個短語描述即時電子存取。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"clients","meaning":"客戶","examples":[{"en":"Rockwell Collins delivers many courses instantly to its clients.","zh":"Rockwell Collins 向其客戶即時傳送許多課程。"},{"en":"Clients are customers who buy services or professional support from a business.","zh":"clients 指從企業購買服務或專業支援的顧客。"},{"en":"A design company’s clients may include schools, restaurants, and small shops.","zh":"設計公司的客戶可能包括學校、餐廳和小店。"},{"en":"Companies try to serve clients well because satisfied clients may return or recommend them.","zh":"公司努力服務客戶，因為滿意客戶可能再次光顧或推薦。"},{"en":"This word often refers to business customers rather than casual shoppers.","zh":"這個字通常指商業客戶，而不是普通購物者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"e-learning format","meaning":"電子學習形式","examples":[{"en":"Over half of the courses are delivered in an e-learning format.","zh":"超過一半課程以電子學習形式提供。"},{"en":"An e-learning format is a digital form of course delivery through online platforms or computer systems.","zh":"e-learning format 指透過網上平台或電腦系統提供課程的數碼形式。"},{"en":"A safety course in e-learning format may include videos, quizzes, and progress tracking.","zh":"以電子學習形式提供的安全課程可能包括影片、測驗和進度追蹤。"},{"en":"Delivering courses in this format can make access faster and more flexible.","zh":"以這種形式提供課程可以令存取更快和更靈活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how the course is packaged and delivered digitally.","zh":"這個短語描述課程如何以數碼方式包裝和傳送。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"annual training costs","meaning":"每年培訓成本","examples":[{"en":"The change reduced Rockwell Collins’s annual training costs by 40 per cent.","zh":"這項改變將 Rockwell Collins 每年培訓成本減少了百分之四十。"},{"en":"Annual training costs are the total amount spent on training in one year.","zh":"annual training costs 指一年內花在培訓上的總金額。"},{"en":"A company may review annual training costs before deciding next year’s budget.","zh":"公司可能在決定下一年預算前檢視每年培訓成本。"},{"en":"Reducing annual training costs can make a programme easier to maintain long term.","zh":"減少每年培訓成本可以令計劃更容易長期維持。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to yearly spending on employee learning.","zh":"這個短語指員工學習方面的年度開支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"success stories","meaning":"成功個案","examples":[{"en":"Many other e-learning success stories exist.","zh":"還有許多其他電子學習成功個案。"},{"en":"Success stories are examples of people or organisations achieving good results.","zh":"success stories 指人或機構取得好結果的例子。"},{"en":"A school may share success stories about students who improved through extra reading.","zh":"學校可能分享透過額外閱讀而進步的學生成功個案。"},{"en":"Success stories encourage others because they show that a method can work.","zh":"成功個案鼓勵其他人，因為它們顯示某方法可以有效。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to positive real cases, not just theory.","zh":"這個短語指正面的真實例子，而不只是理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be expected to","meaning":"預期會……","examples":[{"en":"E-learning is not expected to replace the classroom entirely.","zh":"電子學習預期不會完全取代課堂。"},{"en":"To be expected to do something means people think or predict that it will do that thing.","zh":"be expected to do something 指人們認為或預測某事會做某事。"},{"en":"Students are expected to submit homework before the deadline.","zh":"學生被期望在截止日期前提交功課。"},{"en":"If something is not expected to happen, experts do not think it is likely.","zh":"如果某事不被預期會發生，專家並不認為它很可能。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe predictions or requirements depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可按語境描述預測或要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"replace the classroom entirely","meaning":"完全取代課堂","examples":[{"en":"E-learning is not expected to replace the classroom entirely.","zh":"電子學習預期不會完全取代課堂。"},{"en":"To replace the classroom entirely means to take over all classroom teaching completely.","zh":"replace the classroom entirely 指完全接管所有課堂教學。"},{"en":"Online videos may support learning, but they do not replace the classroom entirely for young children.","zh":"網上影片可以支援學習，但對幼童而言並不能完全取代課堂。"},{"en":"Some skills still need discussion, teamwork, and real-time feedback.","zh":"有些技能仍需要討論、團隊合作和即時回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes total substitution, not partial support.","zh":"這個短語描述完全替代，而不是部分支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"for one thing","meaning":"其中一個原因是","examples":[{"en":"For one thing, bandwidth limitations remain a problem.","zh":"其中一個原因是，頻寬限制仍然是一個問題。"},{"en":"For one thing means one reason is this, especially when more reasons may follow.","zh":"for one thing 指其中一個原因是這樣，尤其暗示後面可能還有其他原因。"},{"en":"I prefer studying in the library; for one thing, it is quieter than home.","zh":"我較喜歡在圖書館溫習；其中一個原因是它比家裡安靜。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the first supporting reason in an explanation.","zh":"這個短語引出解釋中的第一個支持理由。"},{"en":"It helps organise a multi-reason argument.","zh":"它幫助組織有多個原因的論點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"bandwidth limitations","meaning":"頻寬限制","examples":[{"en":"Bandwidth limitations are still an issue for online multimedia.","zh":"頻寬限制對網上多媒體仍然是問題。"},{"en":"Bandwidth limitations are restrictions caused by an Internet connection not being able to carry enough data quickly.","zh":"bandwidth limitations 指互聯網連線無法快速傳送足夠資料所造成的限制。"},{"en":"A student with bandwidth limitations may hear broken audio during a live lesson.","zh":"有頻寬限制的學生在直播課中可能聽到斷續音訊。"},{"en":"Limited bandwidth makes video and animation harder to deliver smoothly.","zh":"有限頻寬令影片和動畫較難順暢傳送。"},{"en":"This phrase describes technical limits on online content delivery.","zh":"這個短語描述網上內容傳送的技術限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"still an issue","meaning":"仍然是問題","examples":[{"en":"Bandwidth limitations are still an issue in e-learning.","zh":"頻寬限制在電子學習中仍然是問題。"},{"en":"Still an issue means the problem has not disappeared and remains important.","zh":"still an issue 指問題尚未消失，並仍然重要。"},{"en":"Noise is still an issue in the classroom even after the windows were repaired.","zh":"即使窗戶已修好，噪音在課室中仍然是問題。"},{"en":"If a problem is still an issue, planners must continue to deal with it.","zh":"如果某問題仍然存在，規劃者必須繼續處理它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a difficulty continues.","zh":"這個短語顯示困難持續存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"present multimedia over the Internet","meaning":"透過互聯網展示多媒體內容","examples":[{"en":"It can be difficult to present multimedia over the Internet.","zh":"透過互聯網展示多媒體內容可能很困難。"},{"en":"To present multimedia over the Internet means to deliver video, audio, animation, and images online.","zh":"present multimedia over the Internet 指在網上提供影片、音訊、動畫和圖像。"},{"en":"A teacher may struggle to present multimedia over the Internet if students have weak connections.","zh":"如果學生網絡連線弱，老師可能難以透過互聯網展示多媒體內容。"},{"en":"Multimedia requires more data, so poor bandwidth can make lessons slow or unstable.","zh":"多媒體需要更多資料量，因此頻寬差可以令課堂變慢或不穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes online delivery of rich media content.","zh":"這個短語描述在網上傳送豐富媒體內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be suited to","meaning":"適合……","examples":[{"en":"E-training is not suited to every mode of instruction.","zh":"電子培訓並不適合每種教學模式。"},{"en":"To be suited to something means to be appropriate or useful for it.","zh":"be suited to something 指對某事合適或有用。"},{"en":"Group discussion is suited to topics where students need to share opinions.","zh":"小組討論適合需要學生分享意見的課題。"},{"en":"If a method is not suited to a task, learners may struggle even if the technology is good.","zh":"如果方法不適合任務，即使科技很好，學習者也可能吃力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes whether something fits a purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述某事是否配合某目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"every mode of instruction","meaning":"每種教學模式","examples":[{"en":"E-training is not suited to every mode of instruction.","zh":"電子培訓並不適合每種教學模式。"},{"en":"Every mode of instruction means every way of teaching or delivering learning.","zh":"every mode of instruction 指每一種教學或提供學習的方式。"},{"en":"Lectures, workshops, role-play, online modules, and field trips are different modes of instruction.","zh":"講座、工作坊、角色扮演、網上單元和實地考察都是不同教學模式。"},{"en":"Some modes suit factual learning, while others suit teamwork or practical skills.","zh":"有些模式適合事實學習，另一些適合團隊合作或實用技能。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to all possible teaching methods.","zh":"這個短語指所有可能的教學方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"For instance, e-training may not be good for building teams.","zh":"例如，電子培訓可能不適合建立團隊。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance 指例如。"},{"en":"Some skills need face-to-face practice; for instance, conflict management often benefits from role-play.","zh":"有些技能需要面對面練習；例如，衝突管理通常受益於角色扮演。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to give a clear example of a general claim.","zh":"作者使用這個短語為一般說法提供清晰例子。"},{"en":"It helps readers see how an idea applies in real life.","zh":"它幫助讀者看見想法如何應用於現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be ineffective at","meaning":"在……方面無效","examples":[{"en":"E-training is ineffective at imparting cultural values.","zh":"電子培訓在傳遞文化價值方面無效。"},{"en":"To be ineffective at something means not to work well for that purpose.","zh":"be ineffective at something 指對某目的效果不好。"},{"en":"Memorising model answers is ineffective at building real speaking confidence.","zh":"背誦範文答案在建立真正口語信心方面無效。"},{"en":"A method can be effective for facts but ineffective for attitudes or teamwork.","zh":"一種方法可以對事實有效，但對態度或團隊合作無效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weak performance for a particular task.","zh":"這個短語描述在特定任務上的低效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"impart cultural values","meaning":"傳遞文化價值","examples":[{"en":"E-training is ineffective at imparting cultural values.","zh":"電子培訓在傳遞文化價值方面無效。"},{"en":"To impart cultural values means to pass on beliefs, attitudes, and ways of behaving that belong to an organisation or community.","zh":"impart cultural values 指傳承屬於機構或社群的信念、態度和行為方式。"},{"en":"A school imparts cultural values when older students model respect and responsibility for younger ones.","zh":"當高年級學生為低年級學生示範尊重和責任，學校就在傳遞文化價值。"},{"en":"Cultural values are often learned through interaction, observation, and shared experience.","zh":"文化價值通常透過互動、觀察和共同經驗學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes teaching values, not just facts.","zh":"這個短語描述教授價值觀，而不只是事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"build teams","meaning":"建立團隊","examples":[{"en":"Group training sessions may be better for building teams.","zh":"小組培訓課節可能更適合建立團隊。"},{"en":"To build teams means to help people work together with trust, communication, and shared goals.","zh":"build teams 指幫助人以信任、溝通和共同目標一起工作。"},{"en":"A manager may build teams through group projects and problem-solving activities.","zh":"經理可能透過小組專案和解難活動建立團隊。"},{"en":"Team-building works best when people interact, listen, and solve tasks together.","zh":"當人們互動、聆聽並一起解決任務時，團隊建立效果最好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating stronger cooperation among workers.","zh":"這個短語描述在員工之間建立更強合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"unique corporate culture","meaning":"獨特企業文化","examples":[{"en":"A unique corporate culture is difficult to convey through a computer.","zh":"獨特企業文化很難透過電腦傳達。"},{"en":"Unique corporate culture is the special set of values, habits, language, and working style of a company.","zh":"unique corporate culture 指公司特有的一套價值、習慣、語言和工作風格。"},{"en":"A start-up may have a unique corporate culture built around speed, openness, and experimentation.","zh":"初創公司可能有圍繞速度、開放和實驗建立的獨特企業文化。"},{"en":"Culture is hard to teach online because new staff often need to observe real workplace behaviour.","zh":"文化很難在網上教授，因為新員工通常需要觀察真實職場行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what makes a company’s internal way of working distinctive.","zh":"這個短語描述令公司內部工作方式獨特的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"convey something to","meaning":"向……傳達某事","examples":[{"en":"It is difficult to convey a unique culture to first-time employees online.","zh":"在網上向新入職員工傳達獨特文化是困難的。"},{"en":"To convey something to someone means to communicate or pass it on to them.","zh":"convey something to someone 指向某人傳達或傳遞某事。"},{"en":"A teacher conveys confidence to students by giving clear feedback and encouragement.","zh":"老師透過清楚回饋和鼓勵向學生傳達信心。"},{"en":"Some ideas are easier to convey through stories and examples than through rules alone.","zh":"有些想法透過故事和例子比單靠規則更容易傳達。"},{"en":"This phrase describes passing meaning, values, or information to another person.","zh":"這個短語描述把意思、價值或資訊傳給另一個人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"first-time employees","meaning":"新入職員工","examples":[{"en":"First-time employees may need face-to-face training to understand company culture.","zh":"新入職員工可能需要面對面培訓來理解公司文化。"},{"en":"First-time employees are people who are new to a workplace or role.","zh":"first-time employees 指剛加入工作場所或職位的人。"},{"en":"A first-time employee may need help understanding office routines, dress codes, and reporting lines.","zh":"新入職員工可能需要幫助來理解辦公室常規、衣着規定和匯報關係。"},{"en":"New workers learn faster when someone explains both rules and unwritten expectations.","zh":"當有人解釋規則和不成文期望，新員工會學得更快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes employees entering a company or job for the first time.","zh":"這個短語描述第一次進入某公司或職位的員工。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"through a computer monitor","meaning":"透過電腦屏幕","examples":[{"en":"Corporate culture is difficult to convey through a computer monitor.","zh":"企業文化很難透過電腦屏幕傳達。"},{"en":"Through a computer monitor means by using a screen rather than meeting in person.","zh":"through a computer monitor 指透過螢幕，而不是親身見面。"},{"en":"A manager may explain rules through a computer monitor, but trust may still need real interaction.","zh":"經理可能透過電腦屏幕解釋規則，但信任仍可能需要真實互動。"},{"en":"Screens can deliver information, but they may not fully show tone, atmosphere, and relationships.","zh":"螢幕可以傳送資訊，但未必能完全顯示語氣、氣氛和關係。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts online communication with face-to-face experience.","zh":"這個短語對比網上溝通和面對面經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"group training sessions","meaning":"小組培訓課節","examples":[{"en":"Group training sessions are more suitable for building teams.","zh":"小組培訓課節更適合建立團隊。"},{"en":"Group training sessions are training periods where several learners work together at the same time.","zh":"group training sessions 指幾名學習者同時一起學習的培訓時段。"},{"en":"A company may use group training sessions for leadership games and team discussions.","zh":"公司可能使用小組培訓課節進行領導力遊戲和團隊討論。"},{"en":"Group sessions help people practise communication and learn from each other.","zh":"小組課節幫助人練習溝通並互相學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes training that depends on interaction among learners.","zh":"這個短語描述依賴學習者互動的培訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be suitable for","meaning":"適合……","examples":[{"en":"Group training sessions are suitable for building teams.","zh":"小組培訓課節適合建立團隊。"},{"en":"To be suitable for something means to be appropriate or useful for that purpose.","zh":"be suitable for something 指對某目的合適或有用。"},{"en":"A quiet room is suitable for reading because it has few distractions.","zh":"安靜房間適合閱讀，因為干擾較少。"},{"en":"A method is suitable when it matches the task, learners, and goal.","zh":"當方法配合任務、學習者和目標，它就是合適的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a good fit between method and purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述方法與目的之間的配合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"for these purposes","meaning":"為了這些目的","examples":[{"en":"Group training sessions are more suitable for these purposes.","zh":"小組培訓課節為了這些目的更合適。"},{"en":"For these purposes means for the aims or goals just mentioned.","zh":"for these purposes 指為了剛才提到的目標或目的。"},{"en":"If the aim is teamwork, online quizzes may not be enough for these purposes.","zh":"如果目標是團隊合作，網上測驗為了這些目的可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase points back to earlier goals in the discussion.","zh":"這個短語指回討論中較早提到的目標。"},{"en":"It helps avoid repeating the same purpose again.","zh":"它有助避免再次重複同一目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a perceived loss of","meaning":"被認為損失了……","examples":[{"en":"There is a perceived loss of research time in online teaching.","zh":"網上教學被認為損失了研究時間。"},{"en":"A perceived loss of something is a loss that people believe or feel is happening.","zh":"perceived loss of something 指人們相信或感覺正在失去某事。"},{"en":"Teachers may feel a perceived loss of personal contact when lessons move online.","zh":"當課堂轉到網上，老師可能感到被認為失去了個人接觸。"},{"en":"A perceived loss may affect attitudes even if the actual loss is difficult to measure.","zh":"即使實際損失難以量度，被感知的損失也可能影響態度。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights how people understand or experience a change.","zh":"這個短語突出人們如何理解或經歷改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"research time","meaning":"研究時間","examples":[{"en":"Online teaching may involve a perceived loss of research time.","zh":"網上教學可能涉及被認為損失了研究時間。"},{"en":"Research time is time available for studying, investigating, writing, or producing academic work.","zh":"research time 指可用於研究、調查、寫作或產出學術工作的時間。"},{"en":"A university lecturer may lose research time when administrative work increases.","zh":"當行政工作增加，大學講師可能失去研究時間。"},{"en":"If online courses take many hours to prepare, instructors may have less time for research.","zh":"如果網上課程需要許多小時準備，導師可能有較少時間做研究。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to time used for academic investigation.","zh":"這個短語指用於學術探究的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the work involved in","meaning":"……所涉及的工作","examples":[{"en":"The work involved in developing online classes can be considerable.","zh":"開發網上課堂所涉及的工作可能相當多。"},{"en":"The work involved in something means the tasks, effort, and time needed to do it.","zh":"work involved in something 指完成某事所需的任務、努力和時間。"},{"en":"The work involved in organising a school fair includes booking stalls, contacting parents, and planning safety.","zh":"組織學校嘉年華所涉及的工作包括預訂攤位、聯絡家長和規劃安全。"},{"en":"A project may seem simple until people see all the work involved in it.","zh":"一個項目在看到所有相關工作前可能看似簡單。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the effort behind a task.","zh":"這個短語集中於任務背後的努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"online classes","meaning":"網上課堂","examples":[{"en":"Developing and teaching online classes takes time.","zh":"開發和教授網上課堂需要時間。"},{"en":"Online classes are lessons taught through the Internet rather than in a physical classroom.","zh":"online classes 指透過互聯網而不是實體課室教授的課堂。"},{"en":"A teacher may run online classes with video calls, slides, quizzes, and discussion boards.","zh":"老師可能用視像通話、投影片、測驗和討論區進行網上課堂。"},{"en":"Online classes require planning because students may need clearer instructions and digital support.","zh":"網上課堂需要規劃，因為學生可能需要更清楚指示和數碼支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lessons delivered remotely through digital tools.","zh":"這個短語描述透過數碼工具遙距提供的課堂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"estimate that","meaning":"估計","examples":[{"en":"Professor Wallin estimated that the course required hundreds of person-hours.","zh":"Wallin 教授估計該課程需要數百個人時。"},{"en":"To estimate that something is true means to make a careful approximate judgement.","zh":"estimate that something is true 指作出小心的大約判斷。"},{"en":"A school may estimate that a renovation will take three months.","zh":"學校可能估計裝修需時三個月。"},{"en":"Estimates help people plan budgets and schedules before exact numbers are known.","zh":"在確切數字未知道前，估計幫助人規劃預算和時間表。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making an informed approximation.","zh":"這個短語描述作出有根據的約略判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"person-hours","meaning":"人時","examples":[{"en":"The course required between 500 and 1,000 person-hours.","zh":"該課程需要五百至一千個人時。"},{"en":"Person-hours measure work by multiplying the number of people by the hours they spend.","zh":"person-hours 透過人數乘以工作小時來量度工作量。"},{"en":"If five teachers work for ten hours, the project uses fifty person-hours.","zh":"如果五名老師工作十小時，該項目就使用五十個人時。"},{"en":"Person-hours help organisations estimate the labour needed for a project.","zh":"人時幫助機構估計項目所需人力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes total human work time.","zh":"這個短語描述人力工作的總時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the appropriate level of","meaning":"適當水平的……","examples":[{"en":"The course had to be kept at the appropriate level of currency and usefulness.","zh":"該課程必須保持適當水平的時效性和實用性。"},{"en":"The appropriate level of something is the right amount, quality, or standard for the situation.","zh":"appropriate level of something 指適合該情況的正確數量、質素或標準。"},{"en":"A teacher should set homework at the appropriate level of difficulty for the class.","zh":"老師應為班級設定適當難度水平的功課。"},{"en":"If the level is too high or too low, learners may become confused or bored.","zh":"如果水平太高或太低，學習者可能困惑或沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a suitable standard.","zh":"這個短語描述合適標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"currency and usefulness","meaning":"時效性和實用性","examples":[{"en":"Online courses require work to maintain their currency and usefulness.","zh":"網上課程需要工作來維持其時效性和實用性。"},{"en":"Currency and usefulness mean being up to date and practically helpful.","zh":"currency and usefulness 指內容保持最新並具有實際幫助。"},{"en":"A law course must maintain currency and usefulness because rules change over time.","zh":"法律課程必須維持時效性和實用性，因為規則會隨時間改變。"},{"en":"If content becomes outdated, learners may study information they cannot apply.","zh":"如果內容過時，學習者可能學到不能應用的資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase combines freshness with practical value.","zh":"這個短語結合新近程度和實際價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"distance learning instructors","meaning":"遙距學習導師","examples":[{"en":"Distance learning instructors often need technical skills.","zh":"遙距學習導師通常需要技術技能。"},{"en":"Distance learning instructors are teachers or trainers who teach learners remotely.","zh":"distance learning instructors 指遙距教授學習者的老師或培訓員。"},{"en":"An online English tutor is a distance learning instructor when teaching by video call.","zh":"網上英文導師透過視像通話教學時，就是遙距學習導師。"},{"en":"These instructors need to manage both teaching and technology.","zh":"這些導師需要同時管理教學和科技。"},{"en":"This phrase describes educators working outside the traditional classroom setting.","zh":"這個短語描述在傳統課室以外工作的教育者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"technical skills","meaning":"技術技能","examples":[{"en":"Online instructors often need technical skills.","zh":"網上導師通常需要技術技能。"},{"en":"Technical skills are practical abilities related to using tools, systems, software, or equipment.","zh":"technical skills 指使用工具、系統、軟件或設備的實用能力。"},{"en":"A teacher needs technical skills to upload videos and manage online quizzes.","zh":"老師需要技術技能來上載影片和管理網上測驗。"},{"en":"Without technical skills, an instructor may waste time solving platform problems during class.","zh":"沒有技術技能，導師可能在課堂中浪費時間解決平台問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hands-on ability with technology or specialised tools.","zh":"這個短語描述操作科技或專門工具的實務能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"courseware system","meaning":"課件系統","examples":[{"en":"Technical skills may be needed even with an advanced courseware system.","zh":"即使有先進課件系統，也可能需要技術技能。"},{"en":"A courseware system is software used to create, organise, and deliver digital learning materials.","zh":"courseware system 指用來製作、組織和提供數碼學習材料的軟件。"},{"en":"A company may use a courseware system to build staff training modules.","zh":"公司可能使用課件系統建立員工培訓單元。"},{"en":"Even advanced systems require users to upload content, manage settings, and fix problems.","zh":"即使系統先進，使用者仍需要上載內容、管理設定和解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes software for making and running courses.","zh":"這個短語描述製作和運行課程的軟件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"amount to","meaning":"相當於","examples":[{"en":"The preparation time may amount to half of a person-year.","zh":"準備時間可能相當於半個人年。"},{"en":"To amount to something means to add up to that total or be equal to it.","zh":"amount to something 指加起來達到某總數或等同於某數值。"},{"en":"Ten hours a week for a year can amount to a large amount of study time.","zh":"每星期十小時持續一年，可以相當於大量學習時間。"},{"en":"Small tasks can amount to a heavy workload when repeated many times.","zh":"小任務重複許多次後，可以相當於沉重工作量。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the final total or equivalent value.","zh":"這個短語顯示最終總數或等值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a quarter of a person-year","meaning":"四分之一個人年","examples":[{"en":"The work may amount to a quarter of a person-year.","zh":"這項工作可能相當於四分之一個人年。"},{"en":"A quarter of a person-year means the amount of work one person would do in about three months full-time.","zh":"quarter of a person-year 指一個人全職工作約三個月的工作量。"},{"en":"A project requiring a quarter of a person-year is not small, even if it sounds simple.","zh":"需要四分之一個人年的項目並不小，即使聽起來簡單。"},{"en":"This measurement helps managers understand the labour cost behind online course design.","zh":"這種量度幫助管理者理解網上課程設計背後的人力成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a substantial amount of work time.","zh":"這個短語描述相當多的工作時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"half of a person-year","meaning":"半個人年","examples":[{"en":"The work may amount to half of a person-year.","zh":"這項工作可能相當於半個人年。"},{"en":"Half of a person-year means the amount of work one person would do in about six months full-time.","zh":"half of a person-year 指一個人全職工作約六個月的工作量。"},{"en":"Building a detailed online course may take half of a person-year if videos and quizzes are included.","zh":"如果包括影片和測驗，建立詳細網上課程可能需要半個人年。"},{"en":"Such a large time investment explains why online courses can be expensive to develop.","zh":"如此大的時間投資解釋了為何網上課程開發成本可以很高。"},{"en":"This phrase measures workload in terms of full-time human effort.","zh":"這個短語用全職人力努力來量度工作量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"computer literacy","meaning":"電腦知識；電腦素養","examples":[{"en":"Teaching materials require computer literacy.","zh":"教學材料需要電腦知識。"},{"en":"Computer literacy is the ability to use computers and digital tools confidently enough for basic tasks.","zh":"computer literacy 指能有信心地使用電腦和數碼工具完成基本任務的能力。"},{"en":"A student with computer literacy can open files, use email, and join online classes.","zh":"具備電腦素養的學生可以開啟檔案、使用電郵和參加網上課堂。"},{"en":"Without computer literacy, learners may struggle before they even reach the course content.","zh":"沒有電腦素養，學習者可能在接觸課程內容前已感到困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes basic confidence and ability with computers.","zh":"這個短語描述對電腦的基本信心和能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"access to equipment","meaning":"使用設備的機會","examples":[{"en":"Students need access to equipment to join an e-learning programme.","zh":"學生需要有使用設備的機會，才能參加電子學習計劃。"},{"en":"Access to equipment means being able to use the tools or devices needed for a task.","zh":"access to equipment 指能夠使用完成任務所需的工具或裝置。"},{"en":"A student without access to a laptop may struggle to complete online homework.","zh":"沒有手提電腦可用的學生，可能難以完成網上功課。"},{"en":"Access affects fairness because learners cannot benefit from digital courses without the right tools.","zh":"使用設備的機會影響公平，因為沒有合適工具，學習者不能從數碼課程受益。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical availability of equipment.","zh":"這個短語描述設備在實際上是否可用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"basic equipment","meaning":"基本設備","examples":[{"en":"Any e-learning system involves basic equipment.","zh":"任何電子學習系統都涉及基本設備。"},{"en":"Basic equipment means the simple tools needed before something can be done.","zh":"basic equipment 指做某事前所需的簡單工具。"},{"en":"For online learning, basic equipment may include a device, Internet access, headphones, and a charger.","zh":"對網上學習而言，基本設備可能包括裝置、互聯網、耳機和充電器。"},{"en":"If basic equipment is missing, even a good course becomes hard to use.","zh":"如果缺少基本設備，即使課程很好也會難以使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the minimum physical tools required.","zh":"這個短語描述最低限度所需的實體工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a minimum level of","meaning":"最低程度的……","examples":[{"en":"Students need a minimum level of computer knowledge.","zh":"學生需要最低程度的電腦知識。"},{"en":"A minimum level of something is the lowest amount or standard needed.","zh":"minimum level of something 指所需的最低數量或標準。"},{"en":"A driver needs a minimum level of eyesight to drive safely.","zh":"司機需要最低程度的視力才能安全駕駛。"},{"en":"If learners lack the minimum level, they may need support before starting the course.","zh":"如果學習者缺乏最低水平，他們可能在開始課程前需要支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the basic requirement for participation.","zh":"這個短語描述參與所需的基本要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"computer knowledge","meaning":"電腦知識","examples":[{"en":"A minimum level of computer knowledge is required for e-learning.","zh":"電子學習需要最低程度的電腦知識。"},{"en":"Computer knowledge is understanding of how to use computers, software, files, and online tools.","zh":"computer knowledge 指懂得如何使用電腦、軟件、檔案和網上工具。"},{"en":"A worker with computer knowledge can log in, download materials, and submit forms online.","zh":"有電腦知識的員工可以登入、下載材料和網上提交表格。"},{"en":"Without this knowledge, technical problems may block learning.","zh":"沒有這些知識，技術問題可能阻礙學習。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical understanding of digital tools.","zh":"這個短語指對數碼工具的實用理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"in order to perform","meaning":"為了執行……","examples":[{"en":"Students need computer knowledge in order to perform the required tasks.","zh":"學生需要電腦知識，為了執行所需任務。"},{"en":"In order to perform something means so that someone can carry out or complete it.","zh":"in order to perform something 指為了能夠進行或完成某事。"},{"en":"Students need a calculator in order to perform certain maths calculations.","zh":"學生需要計算機，為了執行某些數學計算。"},{"en":"Skills and tools are often necessary before a task can be done properly.","zh":"在任務能正確完成前，技能和工具通常是必要的。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose of having a skill or resource.","zh":"這個短語解釋擁有技能或資源的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the tasks required by","meaning":"由……要求的任務","examples":[{"en":"Students must perform the tasks required by the system.","zh":"學生必須執行系統要求的任務。"},{"en":"The tasks required by something are the actions that the system or situation asks users to complete.","zh":"tasks required by something 指系統或情況要求使用者完成的行動。"},{"en":"An online course may require tasks such as logging in, watching videos, and submitting quizzes.","zh":"網上課程可能要求登入、觀看影片和提交測驗等任務。"},{"en":"If students cannot complete the required tasks, they may not finish the course successfully.","zh":"如果學生不能完成所需任務，可能無法成功完成課程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes required actions set by a system.","zh":"這個短語描述由系統設定的必要行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"possess these skills","meaning":"具備這些技能","examples":[{"en":"A student who does not possess these skills may fail online.","zh":"不具備這些技能的學生可能在網上學習中失敗。"},{"en":"To possess these skills means to have the abilities being discussed.","zh":"possess these skills 指擁有正在討論的那些能力。"},{"en":"A worker must possess basic computer skills to complete digital training.","zh":"員工必須具備基本電腦技能，才能完成數碼培訓。"},{"en":"If learners do not possess the required skills, support or beginner training may be needed.","zh":"如果學習者不具備所需技能，可能需要支援或初階培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes having necessary abilities.","zh":"這個短語描述擁有必要能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"have access to","meaning":"可以使用……","examples":[{"en":"Students must have access to the necessary tools.","zh":"學生必須可以使用必要工具。"},{"en":"To have access to something means to be able to use or obtain it.","zh":"have access to something 指能夠使用或取得某物。"},{"en":"A student without access to the Internet may struggle with online homework.","zh":"沒有互聯網可用的學生可能難以完成網上功課。"},{"en":"Access to tools affects whether learners can participate fairly.","zh":"能否使用工具會影響學習者是否能公平參與。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical availability.","zh":"這個短語描述實際可得性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"succeed in","meaning":"在……取得成功","examples":[{"en":"Students need equipment and skills to succeed in an e-learning programme.","zh":"學生需要設備和技能，才能在電子學習計劃中取得成功。"},{"en":"To succeed in something means to achieve a good result in it.","zh":"succeed in something 指在某事上取得好結果。"},{"en":"A student may succeed in a speaking exam by practising regularly and receiving feedback.","zh":"學生可能透過定期練習和取得回饋，在口試中取得成功。"},{"en":"Success often requires both effort and the right resources.","zh":"成功通常需要努力和合適資源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes achieving the desired outcome.","zh":"這個短語描述達成預期成果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"debate the obvious advantages of","meaning":"爭論……的明顯好處","examples":[{"en":"Few people debate the obvious advantages of e-learning.","zh":"很少人爭論電子學習的明顯好處。"},{"en":"To debate the obvious advantages of something means to argue about benefits that already seem clear.","zh":"debate the obvious advantages of something 指爭論已經看來清楚的好處。"},{"en":"Few people debate the obvious advantages of clean drinking water.","zh":"很少人會爭論清潔食水的明顯好處。"},{"en":"When advantages are obvious, discussion often moves to cost, fairness, or limitations.","zh":"當好處明顯時，討論通常轉向成本、公平或限制。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the benefits are widely accepted.","zh":"這個短語暗示好處已被廣泛接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"systematic research","meaning":"系統性研究","examples":[{"en":"Systematic research is needed to evaluate e-learning.","zh":"需要系統性研究來評估電子學習。"},{"en":"Systematic research is careful, organised investigation using clear methods.","zh":"systematic research 指使用清晰方法進行的小心、有組織調查。"},{"en":"A school may conduct systematic research before changing its homework policy.","zh":"學校在改變功課政策前可能進行系統性研究。"},{"en":"Without systematic research, people may rely only on stories or personal impressions.","zh":"沒有系統性研究，人們可能只依賴故事或個人印象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes structured evidence-gathering.","zh":"這個短語描述有結構的證據收集。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"confirm that","meaning":"確認","examples":[{"en":"Research is needed to confirm that learners are acquiring the skills.","zh":"需要研究來確認學習者正在掌握這些技能。"},{"en":"To confirm that something is true means to check and show that it is true.","zh":"confirm that something is true 指檢查並顯示某事是真的。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a quiz to confirm that students understand the lesson.","zh":"老師可能用測驗確認學生理解課堂。"},{"en":"Confirmation is important because confidence alone does not prove learning happened.","zh":"確認很重要，因為單靠信心不能證明學習已發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes verifying a claim with evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述用證據核實某主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"acquire and use skills","meaning":"掌握並運用技能","examples":[{"en":"Researchers need to know whether learners acquire and use skills taught online.","zh":"研究人員需要知道學習者是否掌握並運用網上教授的技能。"},{"en":"To acquire and use skills means to learn abilities and apply them in real situations.","zh":"acquire and use skills 指學會能力並在真實情況中應用。"},{"en":"A student acquires grammar skills when they understand the rules and uses them in writing.","zh":"當學生理解文法規則並在寫作中使用，就是掌握並運用文法技能。"},{"en":"Training is successful only if learners can use the skill after the course.","zh":"只有學習者能在課程後使用技能，培訓才算成功。"},{"en":"This phrase connects learning with practical application.","zh":"這個短語把學習與實際應用連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be taught online","meaning":"在網上教授","examples":[{"en":"Some skills are being taught online in corporate training.","zh":"有些技能正在企業培訓中透過網上教授。"},{"en":"To be taught online means to be delivered through Internet-based lessons or digital materials.","zh":"be taught online 指透過互聯網課堂或數碼材料提供教學。"},{"en":"Basic Excel skills can be taught online with videos and practice files.","zh":"基本 Excel 技能可以透過影片和練習檔案在網上教授。"},{"en":"Skills taught online should include feedback so learners know whether they are improving.","zh":"在網上教授的技能應包括回饋，讓學習者知道自己是否進步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes digital delivery of instruction.","zh":"這個短語描述教學的數碼傳送。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the best way to achieve","meaning":"達成……的最佳方法","examples":[{"en":"Research should show whether e-learning is the best way to achieve the outcomes.","zh":"研究應顯示電子學習是否是達成成果的最佳方法。"},{"en":"The best way to achieve something is the most effective method for reaching a goal.","zh":"best way to achieve something 指達到目標的最有效方法。"},{"en":"For some students, regular feedback is the best way to achieve writing improvement.","zh":"對有些學生而言，定期回饋是達成寫作進步的最佳方法。"},{"en":"A method is best only if it reaches the goal better than realistic alternatives.","zh":"只有當某方法比現實替代方案更能達標，它才算最佳。"},{"en":"This phrase compares methods by their results.","zh":"這個短語根據結果比較方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"achieve the outcomes","meaning":"達成成果","examples":[{"en":"Companies need to know whether e-learning can achieve the desired outcomes.","zh":"公司需要知道電子學習能否達成預期成果。"},{"en":"To achieve the outcomes means to reach the results that were planned or hoped for.","zh":"achieve the outcomes 指達到計劃或期望中的結果。"},{"en":"A school programme achieves the outcomes if students actually read more and write better.","zh":"如果學生真的閱讀更多並寫得更好，學校計劃就達成成果。"},{"en":"Training should be judged by results, not only by how modern the platform looks.","zh":"培訓應按結果評估，而不只是看平台有多現代。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching intended results.","zh":"這個短語描述達到預期結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a corporate environment","meaning":"企業環境","examples":[{"en":"E-learning must be evaluated in a corporate environment.","zh":"電子學習必須在企業環境中評估。"},{"en":"A corporate environment is a business setting with employees, managers, policies, and workplace goals.","zh":"corporate environment 指有員工、經理、政策和工作目標的商業環境。"},{"en":"Training that works in a university may not work the same way in a corporate environment.","zh":"在大學有效的培訓，在企業環境中未必以同樣方式有效。"},{"en":"Corporate environments often care about cost, efficiency, performance, and compliance.","zh":"企業環境通常重視成本、效率、表現和合規。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the workplace context of companies.","zh":"這個短語描述公司的工作場所語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"blended-learning approach","meaning":"混合學習模式","examples":[{"en":"A blended-learning approach is gaining popularity.","zh":"混合學習模式正越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"A blended-learning approach combines online learning with face-to-face teaching or other learning methods.","zh":"blended-learning approach 指把網上學習與面對面教學或其他學習方法結合。"},{"en":"A school may use a blended-learning approach by giving videos at home and discussion in class.","zh":"學校可能透過在家觀看影片、在課堂討論來使用混合學習模式。"},{"en":"Blended learning can balance flexibility with human interaction.","zh":"混合學習可以平衡靈活性和人際互動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mixed learning method.","zh":"這個短語描述混合式學習方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"指的是","examples":[{"en":"Blended learning refers to a mix of different learning environments.","zh":"混合學習指的是不同學習環境的組合。"},{"en":"To refer to something means to mean it, describe it, or point to it.","zh":"refer to something 指意思是、描述或指向某事。"},{"en":"In this lesson, “staff” refers to the people working for a company.","zh":"在這堂課中，“staff” 指的是為公司工作的人。"},{"en":"Clear reference helps learners understand exactly what a term means.","zh":"清楚指稱有助學習者準確理解術語意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when defining vocabulary.","zh":"這個短語常用於定義詞彙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a mix of different learning environments","meaning":"不同學習環境的組合","examples":[{"en":"Blended learning uses a mix of different learning environments.","zh":"混合學習使用不同學習環境的組合。"},{"en":"A mix of different learning environments means a combination of places or formats for learning.","zh":"mix of different learning environments 指不同學習地點或形式的結合。"},{"en":"A course may mix classroom lessons, online videos, group projects, and workplace practice.","zh":"課程可能混合課室課堂、網上影片、小組專案和職場實習。"},{"en":"Different environments help because some tasks need flexibility while others need interaction.","zh":"不同環境有幫助，因為有些任務需要靈活性，另一些需要互動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning that happens in more than one setting.","zh":"這個短語描述在多於一種環境中發生的學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"gain popularity","meaning":"越來越受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The blended-learning approach is gaining popularity.","zh":"混合學習模式正越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"To gain popularity means to become more widely liked, used, or accepted.","zh":"gain popularity 指變得更受喜愛、更常被使用或更被接受。"},{"en":"Online booking gained popularity because people could reserve seats quickly.","zh":"網上訂位因為可以快速預留座位而越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"A method gains popularity when more people see that it solves a real problem.","zh":"當更多人看見某方法解決真實問題，它就會越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growing public or professional acceptance.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾或專業界接受度上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"traditional face-to-face classroom methods","meaning":"傳統面對面課堂方法","examples":[{"en":"The approach combines traditional face-to-face classroom methods with technology.","zh":"這種模式把傳統面對面課堂方法與科技結合。"},{"en":"Traditional face-to-face classroom methods are older teaching methods where teachers and learners meet in the same room.","zh":"traditional face-to-face classroom methods 指老師和學習者在同一房間見面的較舊教學方法。"},{"en":"Lectures, group discussion, and live role-play are traditional face-to-face methods.","zh":"講座、小組討論和即時角色扮演都是傳統面對面方法。"},{"en":"These methods support immediate questions and human interaction.","zh":"這些方法支援即時提問和人際互動。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts physical classroom teaching with technology-based learning.","zh":"這個短語把實體課室教學與科技化學習作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"computer-mediated activities","meaning":"以電腦為媒介的活動","examples":[{"en":"Blended learning includes computer-mediated activities.","zh":"混合學習包括以電腦為媒介的活動。"},{"en":"Computer-mediated activities are learning tasks carried out through computers or digital platforms.","zh":"computer-mediated activities 指透過電腦或數碼平台進行的學習任務。"},{"en":"Online quizzes, discussion boards, and simulation tasks are computer-mediated activities.","zh":"網上測驗、討論區和模擬任務都是以電腦為媒介的活動。"},{"en":"These activities can record progress and give learners flexible practice.","zh":"這些活動可以記錄進度並給學習者靈活練習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes activities where computers help connect learners with content or people.","zh":"這個短語描述電腦幫助學習者接觸內容或他人的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"according to its proponents","meaning":"據其支持者所說","examples":[{"en":"According to its proponents, blended learning creates a more integrated approach.","zh":"據其支持者所說，混合學習創造更整合的方法。"},{"en":"According to its proponents means according to the people who support or argue for it.","zh":"according to its proponents 指根據支持或主張某事的人所說。"},{"en":"According to its proponents, homework helps students practise independently.","zh":"據其支持者所說，功課幫助學生獨立練習。"},{"en":"This phrase reports supporters’ views without saying everyone agrees.","zh":"這個短語報告支持者的看法，而不是說人人同意。"},{"en":"It is useful when presenting one side of a debate.","zh":"它適合用於呈現爭議中的一方觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"a more integrated approach","meaning":"更整合的方法","examples":[{"en":"Blended learning creates a more integrated approach for instructors and learners.","zh":"混合學習為導師和學習者創造更整合的方法。"},{"en":"A more integrated approach is a method whose parts work together more smoothly.","zh":"more integrated approach 指各部分更順暢地配合的方法。"},{"en":"A school may use a more integrated approach by linking reading, writing, speaking, and projects.","zh":"學校可能透過連繫閱讀、寫作、口語和專案，使用更整合的方法。"},{"en":"Integration helps learners see how different activities support the same goal.","zh":"整合幫助學習者看見不同活動如何支援同一目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a more connected and unified method.","zh":"這個短語描述更連貫和統一的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"instructors and learners","meaning":"導師和學習者","examples":[{"en":"The approach benefits both instructors and learners.","zh":"這種方法同時惠及導師和學習者。"},{"en":"Instructors and learners are the people who teach and the people who study.","zh":"instructors and learners 指教學的人和學習的人。"},{"en":"Instructors need clear tools, while learners need accessible materials and feedback.","zh":"導師需要清楚工具，而學習者需要可取得的材料和回饋。"},{"en":"A good course design helps both sides communicate and work more effectively.","zh":"好課程設計幫助雙方更有效溝通和工作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the two main groups in education.","zh":"這個短語指教育中的兩個主要群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"technology-based materials","meaning":"科技教材","examples":[{"en":"Technology-based materials formerly played a supporting role.","zh":"科技教材以前起輔助作用。"},{"en":"Technology-based materials are learning resources delivered through digital tools or devices.","zh":"technology-based materials 指透過數碼工具或裝置提供的學習資源。"},{"en":"Slides, online quizzes, videos, and interactive exercises are technology-based materials.","zh":"投影片、網上測驗、影片和互動練習都是科技教材。"},{"en":"These materials can support face-to-face teaching by adding practice and visual explanation.","zh":"這些材料可以透過加入練習和視覺解釋來支援面對面教學。"},{"en":"This phrase describes digital resources used in learning.","zh":"這個短語描述學習中使用的數碼資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"play a supporting role to","meaning":"對……起輔助作用","examples":[{"en":"Technology-based materials used to play a supporting role to face-to-face instruction.","zh":"科技教材過去對面對面教學起輔助作用。"},{"en":"To play a supporting role to something means to help it rather than become the main method.","zh":"play a supporting role to something 指幫助某事，而不是成為主要方法。"},{"en":"Practice worksheets play a supporting role to classroom teaching.","zh":"練習工作紙對課堂教學起輔助作用。"},{"en":"Support tools can strengthen the main lesson without replacing the teacher.","zh":"輔助工具可以強化主要課堂，而不取代老師。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a secondary but helpful function.","zh":"這個短語描述次要但有幫助的功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"face-to-face instruction","meaning":"面對面教學","examples":[{"en":"Technology used to support face-to-face instruction.","zh":"科技過去用來支援面對面教學。"},{"en":"Face-to-face instruction is teaching where instructors and learners meet in person.","zh":"face-to-face instruction 指導師和學習者親身見面的教學。"},{"en":"A speaking class often needs face-to-face instruction so students can practise interaction.","zh":"口語課通常需要面對面教學，讓學生練習互動。"},{"en":"This method allows immediate feedback, body language, and group discussion.","zh":"這種方法容許即時回饋、肢體語言和小組討論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes traditional in-person teaching.","zh":"這個短語描述傳統親身教學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"through a blended learning approach","meaning":"透過混合學習模式","examples":[{"en":"Through a blended learning approach, technology becomes more important.","zh":"透過混合學習模式，科技變得更重要。"},{"en":"Through a blended learning approach means by using a mixture of online and face-to-face learning.","zh":"through a blended learning approach 指透過混合網上和面對面學習。"},{"en":"Through a blended learning approach, students may watch videos before class and practise in class.","zh":"透過混合學習模式，學生可能課前觀看影片，課堂上練習。"},{"en":"This approach can make technology part of the main course design rather than only an extra tool.","zh":"這種模式可以令科技成為主要課程設計的一部分，而不只是額外工具。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the method by which learning is organised.","zh":"這個短語描述學習如何被組織的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to choose the correct heading for each paragraph.","zh":"考生需要為每段選出正確標題。"},{"en":"To choose the correct heading means to select the title that best matches a paragraph’s main idea.","zh":"choose the correct heading 指選擇最符合段落主旨的標題。"},{"en":"Candidates should read the whole paragraph before choosing a heading.","zh":"考生選標題前應讀完整段。"},{"en":"A heading that matches only one small detail is usually not the correct one.","zh":"只符合一個小細節的標題通常不是正確答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"from the list below","meaning":"從下列列表中","examples":[{"en":"The correct heading should be chosen from the list below.","zh":"正確標題應從下列列表中選出。"},{"en":"From the list below means using only the options printed underneath the instruction.","zh":"from the list below 指只使用指示下方列出的選項。"},{"en":"Students should not invent their own answer if the question says to choose from the list below.","zh":"如果題目要求從下列列表中選擇，學生不應自己創作答案。"},{"en":"This phrase tells candidates where the answer choices are located.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生答案選項在哪裡。"},{"en":"It limits answers to the given options.","zh":"它把答案限制於已給選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"write the correct number","meaning":"寫上正確編號","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the correct number on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生在答題紙上寫上正確編號。"},{"en":"To write the correct number means to record the number that matches the chosen option.","zh":"write the correct number 指記下與所選選項相符的編號。"},{"en":"If heading vi is correct, candidates should write vi, not the words of the heading.","zh":"如果標題 vi 正確，考生應寫 vi，而不是寫出標題文字。"},{"en":"Correct format matters because wrong numbering can lose marks.","zh":"正確格式很重要，因為寫錯編號可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an instruction about how to record an answer.","zh":"這個短語給出如何記錄答案的指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"on your answer sheet","meaning":"在答題紙上","examples":[{"en":"Answers should be written on your answer sheet.","zh":"答案應寫在答題紙上。"},{"en":"On your answer sheet means in the official place where exam answers must be recorded.","zh":"on your answer sheet 指在考試答案必須記錄的正式位置。"},{"en":"A student may know the answer but lose marks if it is not written on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生可能知道答案，但如果沒有寫在答題紙上，仍可能失分。"},{"en":"Exam instructions often separate working space from the official answer area.","zh":"考試指示通常把草稿位置與正式答案區分開。"},{"en":"This phrase tells candidates where to put final answers.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生最終答案應放在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"overview of the benefits of","meaning":"概述……的好處","examples":[{"en":"One heading gives an overview of the benefits of e-training.","zh":"其中一個標題概述電子培訓的好處。"},{"en":"An overview of the benefits of something is a general summary of its main advantages.","zh":"overview of the benefits of something 指對某事主要優點的一般總結。"},{"en":"A brochure may give an overview of the benefits of joining a library.","zh":"小冊子可能概述加入圖書館的好處。"},{"en":"An overview helps readers understand the big picture before studying details.","zh":"概述幫助讀者在研究細節前理解大方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broad summary of positive points.","zh":"這個短語描述對正面要點的廣泛總結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"successful training choice","meaning":"成功的培訓選擇","examples":[{"en":"The heading refers to IBM’s successful training choice.","zh":"該標題指 IBM 成功的培訓選擇。"},{"en":"A successful training choice is a training method that achieves good results.","zh":"successful training choice 指能取得好結果的培訓方法。"},{"en":"A company makes a successful training choice when staff learn faster and costs fall.","zh":"當員工學得更快且成本下降，公司就作出了成功的培訓選擇。"},{"en":"Successful choices are judged by results, not only by whether the method looks modern.","zh":"成功選擇按結果判斷，而不只是看方法是否現代。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a training decision that works well.","zh":"這個短語描述有效的培訓決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"future direction","meaning":"未來方向","examples":[{"en":"The final paragraph discusses a possible future direction in teaching.","zh":"最後一段討論教學中可能的未來方向。"},{"en":"A future direction is the way something may develop later.","zh":"future direction 指某事將來可能發展的方向。"},{"en":"A school’s future direction may include more digital learning and smaller group teaching.","zh":"學校的未來方向可能包括更多數碼學習和較小組教學。"},{"en":"Discussing future direction helps readers understand where current changes may lead.","zh":"討論未來方向幫助讀者理解目前變化可能通向哪裡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible path of development.","zh":"這個短語描述可能的發展路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"a new style of teaching","meaning":"新的教學方式","examples":[{"en":"Blended learning may become a new style of teaching.","zh":"混合學習可能成為新的教學方式。"},{"en":"A new style of teaching is a fresh method or approach to helping people learn.","zh":"new style of teaching 指幫助人學習的新方法或新取向。"},{"en":"Flipped classrooms became a new style of teaching when students watched videos before class.","zh":"當學生課前觀看影片，翻轉課堂就成為新的教學方式。"},{"en":"New styles often appear when technology or learner needs change.","zh":"當科技或學習者需要改變，新教學方式通常會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a different way of organising lessons.","zh":"這個短語描述組織課堂的不同方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"learners’ achievement","meaning":"學習者的成就","examples":[{"en":"One heading focuses on learners’ achievement.","zh":"其中一個標題集中於學習者的成就。"},{"en":"Learners’ achievement means the results or progress made by students or trainees.","zh":"learners’ achievement 指學生或受訓者取得的結果或進步。"},{"en":"A teacher may measure learners’ achievement through tests, projects, and class participation.","zh":"老師可能透過測驗、專題和課堂參與量度學習者的成就。"},{"en":"Higher achievement suggests that a course may be helping learners improve.","zh":"較高成就顯示課程可能正在幫助學習者進步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what learners successfully accomplish.","zh":"這個短語描述學習者成功完成的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"advanced teaching materials","meaning":"先進教學材料","examples":[{"en":"E-training can use advanced teaching materials such as audio and animation.","zh":"電子培訓可以使用音訊和動畫等先進教學材料。"},{"en":"Advanced teaching materials are modern or sophisticated resources that support learning.","zh":"advanced teaching materials 指支援學習的現代或較精細資源。"},{"en":"A science course may use advanced teaching materials like simulations and 3D diagrams.","zh":"科學課程可能使用模擬和 3D 圖解等先進教學材料。"},{"en":"Advanced materials can make difficult ideas easier to see, hear, and practise.","zh":"先進材料可以令困難想法更容易觀看、聆聽和練習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes richer learning resources than simple notes.","zh":"這個短語描述比簡單筆記更豐富的學習資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"limitations of e-training","meaning":"電子培訓的限制","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the limitations of e-training.","zh":"文章討論電子培訓的限制。"},{"en":"Limitations of e-training are the weaknesses or situations where online training does not work well.","zh":"limitations of e-training 指網上培訓的弱點或效果不佳的情況。"},{"en":"E-training may have limitations when learners need teamwork, cultural understanding, or practical coaching.","zh":"當學習者需要團隊合作、文化理解或實務指導時，電子培訓可能有局限。"},{"en":"Recognising limitations helps companies choose blended methods instead of relying on one tool.","zh":"認清限制幫助公司選擇混合方法，而不是只依靠單一工具。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what e-training cannot easily do.","zh":"這個短語描述電子培訓不容易做到的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"E-training has both advantages and limitations compared with traditional classes.","zh":"與傳統課堂相比，電子培訓既有優點也有限制。"},{"en":"Compared with means judged beside another thing to show similarities or differences.","zh":"compared with 指把某事與另一事並列判斷，以顯示相似或差異。"},{"en":"Compared with paper notes, digital notes are easier to search and edit.","zh":"與紙本筆記相比，數碼筆記較容易搜尋和編輯。"},{"en":"Comparison helps people decide which method fits a particular need.","zh":"比較幫助人決定哪種方法適合特定需要。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the standard used for comparison.","zh":"這個短語引出比較標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"traditional classes","meaning":"傳統課堂","examples":[{"en":"Traditional classes may still be useful for some purposes.","zh":"傳統課堂對某些目的仍可能有用。"},{"en":"Traditional classes are lessons taught in a physical classroom with a teacher and students present.","zh":"traditional classes 指老師和學生在實體課室中進行的課堂。"},{"en":"Speaking practice and team activities may work better in traditional classes.","zh":"口語練習和團隊活動可能在傳統課堂中效果更好。"},{"en":"Traditional classes allow immediate questions, body language, and social interaction.","zh":"傳統課堂容許即時提問、肢體語言和社交互動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes familiar classroom-based learning.","zh":"這個短語描述熟悉的課室式學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"a major financial burden","meaning":"重大財政負擔","examples":[{"en":"Technology can be a major financial burden for companies.","zh":"科技對公司而言可能是重大財政負擔。"},{"en":"A major financial burden is a large cost that creates pressure on a budget.","zh":"major financial burden 指對預算造成壓力的大筆開支。"},{"en":"Buying laptops for every student may be a major financial burden for a small school.","zh":"為每名學生購買手提電腦可能對小學校構成重大財政負擔。"},{"en":"When costs are too high, organisations may delay or reduce a project.","zh":"當成本太高，機構可能延遲或縮減項目。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious money pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重金錢壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"economic considerations","meaning":"經濟方面的考慮","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses advantages beyond economic considerations.","zh":"文章討論超出經濟方面考慮的好處。"},{"en":"Economic considerations are money-related factors such as cost, savings, profit, or budget.","zh":"economic considerations 指與金錢有關的因素，例如成本、節省、利潤或預算。"},{"en":"A family choosing a school may consider economic factors like fees and transport costs.","zh":"家庭選學校時，可能考慮學費和交通費等經濟因素。"},{"en":"Decisions often include economic considerations, but quality and human needs also matter.","zh":"決策通常包括經濟方面的考慮，但質素和人的需要也重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes financial points in decision-making.","zh":"這個短語描述決策中的財政因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"training delivered through computers","meaning":"透過電腦提供的培訓","examples":[{"en":"E-learning can be described as training delivered through computers.","zh":"電子學習可以被描述為透過電腦提供的培訓。"},{"en":"Training delivered through computers means instruction provided using digital devices and systems.","zh":"training delivered through computers 指使用數碼裝置和系統提供的教學。"},{"en":"A company may offer training delivered through computers so staff can complete modules at their desks.","zh":"公司可能提供透過電腦提供的培訓，讓員工在辦公桌完成單元。"},{"en":"Computer delivery allows courses to be repeated, tracked, and updated more easily.","zh":"電腦傳送讓課程更容易重複、追蹤和更新。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the basic idea behind e-learning.","zh":"這個短語描述電子學習背後的基本概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"which paragraph contains","meaning":"哪一段包含……","examples":[{"en":"Candidates identify which paragraph contains specific information.","zh":"考生辨認哪一段包含特定資料。"},{"en":"Which paragraph contains something asks where that information appears in the passage.","zh":"which paragraph contains something 問該資料出現在文章哪一段。"},{"en":"A reading question may ask which paragraph contains an example of cost savings.","zh":"閱讀題可能問哪一段包含成本節省的例子。"},{"en":"Students should scan for key words and then read carefully around them.","zh":"學生應掃讀關鍵字，然後仔細閱讀其前後內容。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in information-matching questions.","zh":"這個短語用於資料配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"the following information","meaning":"以下資料","examples":[{"en":"The question asks candidates to find the following information in the passage.","zh":"題目要求考生在文章中找出以下資料。"},{"en":"The following information means the details listed after the instruction.","zh":"following information 指指示之後列出的細節。"},{"en":"Students should read the following information before scanning the passage.","zh":"學生掃讀文章前應先閱讀以下資料。"},{"en":"This phrase tells readers that a list of details is about to appear.","zh":"這個短語告訴讀者接下來會出現一列細節。"},{"en":"It is common in reading tests and worksheets.","zh":"它常見於閱讀測驗和工作紙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"highly successful","meaning":"非常成功","examples":[{"en":"Project Basic Blue at IBM was highly successful.","zh":"IBM 的 Basic Blue 項目非常成功。"},{"en":"Highly successful means very effective or achieving very good results.","zh":"highly successful 指非常有效或取得很好結果。"},{"en":"A study plan is highly successful if students improve quickly and feel more confident.","zh":"如果學生進步很快並更有信心，學習計劃就是非常成功。"},{"en":"A successful project often saves money, solves problems, or improves performance.","zh":"成功項目通常能節省金錢、解決問題或改善表現。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses strong positive results.","zh":"這個短語強調強烈正面結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"because of its flexibility","meaning":"由於其靈活性","examples":[{"en":"E-learning is a priority for many corporations because of its flexibility.","zh":"電子學習由於其靈活性，成為許多企業的優先事項。"},{"en":"Because of its flexibility means because it can adapt to different times, places, or needs.","zh":"because of its flexibility 指因為它能適應不同時間、地點或需要。"},{"en":"Online tutoring is popular because of its flexibility for students with busy schedules.","zh":"網上補習因其靈活性而受忙碌學生歡迎。"},{"en":"Flexibility helps companies train employees without stopping normal work completely.","zh":"靈活性幫助公司培訓員工，而不用完全停止正常工作。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the reason something is valued.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事受重視的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"the combination of","meaning":"……的結合","examples":[{"en":"The combination of traditional and e-training environments may become common.","zh":"傳統和電子培訓環境的結合可能變得常見。"},{"en":"The combination of two things means using them together.","zh":"combination of two things 指把兩件事一起使用。"},{"en":"The combination of practice questions and teacher feedback can improve exam writing.","zh":"練習題和老師回饋的結合可以改善考試寫作。"},{"en":"Combining methods can work better because each method covers different needs.","zh":"結合方法可能更有效，因為每種方法滿足不同需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bringing two elements together.","zh":"這個短語描述把兩個元素放在一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"may prevail","meaning":"可能會流行；可能會佔優","examples":[{"en":"A blended approach may prevail in corporate training.","zh":"混合模式可能在企業培訓中流行或佔優。"},{"en":"May prevail means may become the most common, accepted, or successful option.","zh":"may prevail 指可能成為最常見、最被接受或最成功的選項。"},{"en":"Online booking may prevail because it is faster than phone reservations.","zh":"網上預訂可能會流行，因為它比電話預訂更快。"},{"en":"A method prevails when enough people find it practical and effective.","zh":"當足夠多人覺得某方法實用且有效，它就會佔優。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible future winner or dominant trend.","zh":"這個短語描述可能的未來贏家或主導趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"rapid electronic delivery","meaning":"快速電子傳送","examples":[{"en":"The passage gives an example of rapid electronic delivery to clients.","zh":"文章給出向客戶快速電子傳送的例子。"},{"en":"Rapid electronic delivery means sending digital products or materials quickly through online systems.","zh":"rapid electronic delivery 指透過網上系統快速傳送數碼產品或材料。"},{"en":"A school can use rapid electronic delivery to send exam notices to all students at once.","zh":"學校可以使用快速電子傳送，同時向所有學生發送考試通知。"},{"en":"Fast digital delivery reduces waiting time and printing costs.","zh":"快速數碼傳送減少等待時間和印刷成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quick online transfer of information or products.","zh":"這個短語描述資訊或產品的快速網上轉移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"products to customers","meaning":"給客戶的產品","examples":[{"en":"Some companies deliver training products to customers electronically.","zh":"有些公司以電子方式向客戶傳送培訓產品。"},{"en":"Products to customers means goods, services, or materials supplied to the people who buy them.","zh":"products to customers 指供應給購買者的貨品、服務或材料。"},{"en":"A software company may send digital products to customers by download link.","zh":"軟件公司可能透過下載連結把數碼產品送到客戶手上。"},{"en":"Electronic delivery helps customers receive products faster and with less physical handling.","zh":"電子傳送幫助客戶更快收到產品，並減少實物處理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the movement of business offerings to buyers.","zh":"這個短語描述企業提供物如何送到買家手中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"choose THREE letters","meaning":"選出三個字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to choose three letters from the options.","zh":"考生需要從選項中選出三個字母。"},{"en":"Choose THREE letters means select exactly three answer options marked by letters.","zh":"choose THREE letters 指準確選出三個以字母標示的答案選項。"},{"en":"If the correct answers are A, D, and F, students must write all three letters.","zh":"如果正確答案是 A、D 和 F，學生必須寫出三個字母。"},{"en":"Choosing too many or too few letters can make the answer wrong.","zh":"選太多或太少字母都可能令答案錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict multiple-answer instruction.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格的多答案指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"technical facilities","meaning":"技術設施","examples":[{"en":"Technical facilities may be necessary for e-learning.","zh":"電子學習可能需要技術設施。"},{"en":"Technical facilities are the equipment, systems, and connections needed for technology to work.","zh":"technical facilities 指科技運作所需的設備、系統和連線。"},{"en":"A computer room, stable Wi-Fi, and support staff are technical facilities for online learning.","zh":"電腦室、穩定 Wi-Fi 和支援人員都是網上學習的技術設施。"},{"en":"Without these facilities, learners may not be able to access digital courses.","zh":"沒有這些設施，學習者可能無法存取數碼課程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the technical resources behind e-learning.","zh":"這個短語描述電子學習背後的技術資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"difficult to obtain","meaning":"難以取得","examples":[{"en":"Some facilities may be difficult to obtain for certain learners.","zh":"某些設施對某些學習者而言可能難以取得。"},{"en":"Difficult to obtain means hard to get, access, or secure.","zh":"difficult to obtain 指難以獲得、使用或確保取得。"},{"en":"A quiet study space may be difficult to obtain for students living in crowded homes.","zh":"對住在擠迫家庭的學生而言，安靜自修空間可能難以取得。"},{"en":"If equipment is difficult to obtain, online learning may become unfair.","zh":"如果設備難以取得，網上學習可能變得不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited access.","zh":"這個短語描述有限存取。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"be restricted due to","meaning":"由於……而受限制","examples":[{"en":"Multimedia delivery may be restricted due to bandwidth limitations.","zh":"多媒體傳送可能由於頻寬限制而受限制。"},{"en":"To be restricted due to something means to be limited because of that reason.","zh":"be restricted due to something 指因某原因而被限制。"},{"en":"A school trip may be restricted due to bad weather.","zh":"學校旅行可能由於惡劣天氣而受限制。"},{"en":"If Internet capacity is limited, video lessons may be restricted or reduced in quality.","zh":"如果互聯網容量有限，影片課堂可能受限制或降低質素。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the cause of a limitation.","zh":"這個短語解釋限制的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"unique corporate values","meaning":"獨特企業價值","examples":[{"en":"E-training may be ineffective at imparting unique corporate values.","zh":"電子培訓在傳遞獨特企業價值方面可能無效。"},{"en":"Unique corporate values are the special beliefs and principles that guide a particular company.","zh":"unique corporate values 指指導某一公司的特有信念和原則。"},{"en":"A company may value honesty, customer care, speed, or teamwork in a distinctive way.","zh":"公司可能以獨特方式重視誠實、客戶關懷、速度或團隊合作。"},{"en":"Such values are often learned through real workplace behaviour, not only written rules.","zh":"這些價值通常透過真實職場行為學習，而不只是書面規則。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the values that make one company’s culture different.","zh":"這個短語描述令某公司文化不同的價值觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"new employees","meaning":"新員工","examples":[{"en":"New employees may need face-to-face training to understand company culture.","zh":"新員工可能需要面對面培訓來理解公司文化。"},{"en":"New employees are people who have recently joined a company or organisation.","zh":"new employees 指最近加入公司或機構的人。"},{"en":"New employees often need help with rules, software, colleagues, and workplace expectations.","zh":"新員工通常需要在規則、軟件、同事和職場期望方面得到幫助。"},{"en":"Good onboarding helps new employees become confident and productive faster.","zh":"良好入職培訓幫助新員工更快變得有信心和有生產力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes staff at the beginning of their job.","zh":"這個短語描述剛開始工作的員工。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"spend long periods away from","meaning":"長時間離開……","examples":[{"en":"Employees may spend long periods away from their jobs to attend training.","zh":"員工可能長時間離開工作去參加培訓。"},{"en":"To spend long periods away from something means to be absent from it for a long time.","zh":"spend long periods away from something 指長時間不在某地方或不做某事。"},{"en":"A student who spends long periods away from school may fall behind in lessons.","zh":"長時間離開學校的學生可能在課業上落後。"},{"en":"Long absences from work can slow normal operations and increase pressure on colleagues.","zh":"長時間離開工作可以拖慢正常營運並增加同事壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being away for a significant amount of time.","zh":"這個短語描述離開相當長時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"attend training","meaning":"參加培訓","examples":[{"en":"Employees sometimes need to attend training away from their normal work.","zh":"員工有時需要離開正常工作去參加培訓。"},{"en":"To attend training means to take part in a planned learning session or course.","zh":"attend training 指參與有計劃的學習課節或課程。"},{"en":"A nurse may attend training to learn how to use new medical equipment.","zh":"護士可能參加培訓，學習如何使用新醫療設備。"},{"en":"Training attendance helps workers update skills, but it may take time from daily duties.","zh":"參加培訓幫助員工更新技能，但可能佔用日常職責時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes going to or participating in workplace learning.","zh":"這個短語描述前往或參與職場學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"preparation time","meaning":"準備時間","examples":[{"en":"More preparation time may be needed for online courses.","zh":"網上課程可能需要更多準備時間。"},{"en":"Preparation time is the time spent planning, designing, writing, and organising before something begins.","zh":"preparation time 指某事開始前用於規劃、設計、撰寫和組織的時間。"},{"en":"A teacher needs preparation time before giving a new grammar lesson.","zh":"老師教授新文法課前需要準備時間。"},{"en":"Online courses require preparation because materials must be clear without constant face-to-face explanation.","zh":"網上課程需要準備，因為材料必須在沒有持續面對面解釋下仍然清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the time needed before delivery.","zh":"這個短語描述正式提供前所需的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"a suitable level","meaning":"合適水平","examples":[{"en":"Online courses must be kept at a suitable level of usefulness.","zh":"網上課程必須保持合適水平的實用性。"},{"en":"A suitable level is the right degree or standard for a particular need.","zh":"suitable level 指適合特定需要的程度或標準。"},{"en":"A teacher should keep examples at a suitable level for the class, not too easy or too hard.","zh":"老師應把例子保持在適合班級的水平，不太易也不太難。"},{"en":"If online materials are not kept at a suitable level, learners may stop using them.","zh":"如果網上材料沒有保持合適水平，學習者可能停止使用它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an appropriate standard.","zh":"這個短語描述恰當標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 42 - E-training.pdf","sourcePage":25}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 43":[{"front":"the significant role of","meaning":"……的重要作用","examples":[{"en":"Mother tongues play a significant role in education.","zh":"母語在教育中發揮重要作用。"},{"en":"The significant role of something means its important influence on a result or process.","zh":"the significant role of something 指某事對結果或過程的重要影響。"},{"en":"The significant role of sleep in learning is clear when tired students cannot concentrate.","zh":"睡眠在學習中的重要作用，在疲倦學生無法集中時很清楚。"},{"en":"When a factor plays a significant role, ignoring it can lead to poor decisions.","zh":"當某因素發揮重要作用，忽視它可能導致錯誤決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why something should not be treated as minor.","zh":"這個短語適合用於解釋為何某事不應被視為次要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mother tongue","meaning":"母語","examples":[{"en":"A child’s mother tongue can support educational development.","zh":"兒童的母語可以支持教育發展。"},{"en":"A mother tongue is the first language a child learns at home or in the family.","zh":"mother tongue 指孩子在家中或家庭中最先學會的語言。"},{"en":"A student may speak Cantonese as her mother tongue while learning English at school.","zh":"學生可能以廣東話為母語，同時在學校學習英語。"},{"en":"A strong mother tongue can help children understand new ideas more clearly.","zh":"穩固的母語能力可以幫助孩子更清楚理解新概念。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a child’s home language, not necessarily the language used in school.","zh":"這個短語指孩子的家庭語言，不一定是學校使用的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"population mobility","meaning":"人口流動","examples":[{"en":"Population mobility has increased diversity within schools.","zh":"人口流動增加了學校內的多元性。"},{"en":"Population mobility means people moving between countries, cities, or communities to live, work, or study.","zh":"population mobility 指人們為生活、工作或學習而在國家、城市或社區之間移動。"},{"en":"A city may experience population mobility when many migrant families move into the area.","zh":"當許多移民家庭搬入某區，城市可能經歷人口流動。"},{"en":"Population mobility can make classrooms more multilingual and culturally diverse.","zh":"人口流動可以令課室變得更多語言和文化多元。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement of people and the social changes it creates.","zh":"這個短語描述人口移動及其帶來的社會變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one consequence of","meaning":"……的一個後果","examples":[{"en":"One consequence of population mobility is increasing diversity in schools.","zh":"人口流動的一個後果是學校內多元性增加。"},{"en":"One consequence of something means one result or effect that happens because of it.","zh":"one consequence of something 指由某事造成的一個結果或影響。"},{"en":"One consequence of poor sleep is that students find it harder to remember new words.","zh":"睡眠不足的一個後果是學生較難記住新詞。"},{"en":"When people move into new communities, one consequence may be greater language diversity.","zh":"當人們搬入新社區，一個後果可能是語言多樣性增加。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining cause and effect.","zh":"這個短語適合用於解釋因果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"increasing diversity within schools","meaning":"學校內日益增加的多元性","examples":[{"en":"Many countries are experiencing increasing diversity within schools.","zh":"許多國家正在經歷學校內日益增加的多元性。"},{"en":"Increasing diversity within schools means schools have more students from different languages, cultures, and backgrounds.","zh":"increasing diversity within schools 指學校有更多來自不同語言、文化和背景的學生。"},{"en":"A school may see increasing diversity when children from many countries join the same classes.","zh":"當來自多個國家的孩子加入同一批班級，學校可能看見日益增加的多元性。"},{"en":"Increasing diversity can enrich learning, but it also requires careful language support.","zh":"日益增加的多元性可以豐富學習，但也需要仔細的語言支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growing variety inside school communities.","zh":"這個短語描述學校社群內不斷增加的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"to illustrate","meaning":"舉例說明","examples":[{"en":"To illustrate, many kindergarten pupils in Toronto do not speak English at home.","zh":"舉例說明，多倫多許多幼稚園學生在家中不說英語。"},{"en":"To illustrate means to give an example that makes an idea clearer.","zh":"to illustrate 指給出例子，使一個想法更清楚。"},{"en":"To illustrate, a teacher may show two student answers before explaining what makes one stronger.","zh":"舉例說明，老師可能先展示兩份學生答案，再解釋哪一份較強。"},{"en":"Examples help readers understand a general point through a real situation.","zh":"例子透過真實情況幫助讀者理解一般觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when moving from explanation to example.","zh":"這個短語適合用於由解釋轉向例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"kindergarten pupils","meaning":"幼稚園學生","examples":[{"en":"Many kindergarten pupils come from homes where English is not the usual language.","zh":"許多幼稚園學生來自英語並非日常語言的家庭。"},{"en":"Kindergarten pupils are young children who attend the first stage of formal schooling.","zh":"kindergarten pupils 指就讀正式學校教育最初階段的年幼兒童。"},{"en":"Kindergarten pupils may learn letters, numbers, songs, and basic classroom routines.","zh":"幼稚園學生可能學習字母、數字、歌曲和基本課堂常規。"},{"en":"If kindergarten pupils speak another language at home, teachers may need to support both languages.","zh":"如果幼稚園學生在家說另一種語言，老師可能需要支援兩種語言。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to very young schoolchildren.","zh":"這個短語指非常年幼的學童。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"come from homes where","meaning":"來自……家庭","examples":[{"en":"Many pupils come from homes where English is not the usual language.","zh":"許多學生來自英語不是日常語言的家庭。"},{"en":"Come from homes where means to live in families or households with a particular condition.","zh":"come from homes where 指來自具有某種情況的家庭或住戶。"},{"en":"Some students come from homes where grandparents take care of them after school.","zh":"有些學生來自放學後由祖父母照顧的家庭。"},{"en":"A child’s home background can affect language use, confidence, and learning support.","zh":"孩子的家庭背景可以影響語言使用、自信和學習支援。"},{"en":"This phrase connects students’ school life with their family environment.","zh":"這個短語把學生的學校生活與家庭環境連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the usual language of communication","meaning":"日常溝通語言","examples":[{"en":"English is not the usual language of communication in many pupils’ homes.","zh":"在許多學生家中，英語不是日常溝通語言。"},{"en":"The usual language of communication is the language people normally use to talk to one another.","zh":"usual language of communication 指人們通常用來彼此交談的語言。"},{"en":"In some families, Cantonese is the usual language of communication even when children study in English.","zh":"在有些家庭中，即使孩子用英語上學，廣東話仍是日常溝通語言。"},{"en":"The language used at home shapes how children express feelings and understand family stories.","zh":"家中使用的語言塑造孩子如何表達感受和理解家庭故事。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to everyday spoken language in a particular setting.","zh":"這個短語指特定環境中的日常口語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"educational policies and practices","meaning":"教育政策和做法","examples":[{"en":"Educational policies and practices vary widely between countries.","zh":"教育政策和做法在國家之間差異很大。"},{"en":"Educational policies and practices are the rules, plans, and classroom methods used in education systems.","zh":"educational policies and practices 指教育制度中使用的規則、計劃和課堂方法。"},{"en":"A school’s educational practices may include homework rules, language support, and assessment methods.","zh":"學校的教育做法可能包括功課規則、語言支援和評估方法。"},{"en":"Policies affect what schools are allowed or expected to do.","zh":"政策影響學校被允許或被期望做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to both official decisions and everyday teaching actions.","zh":"這個短語同時指官方決定和日常教學行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"vary widely between","meaning":"在……之間差異很大","examples":[{"en":"Educational policies vary widely between countries.","zh":"教育政策在國家之間差異很大。"},{"en":"To vary widely between things means to be very different from one case to another.","zh":"vary widely between things 指不同個案之間非常不同。"},{"en":"School lunch rules vary widely between families, schools, and cultures.","zh":"學校午餐規則在家庭、學校和文化之間差異很大。"},{"en":"When policies vary widely, students may have very different learning experiences.","zh":"當政策差異很大，學生可能有非常不同的學習經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights large differences across groups or places.","zh":"這個短語突出不同群體或地方之間的巨大差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"political parties and groups","meaning":"政黨和團體","examples":[{"en":"Some political parties and groups search for ways to solve the problem.","zh":"有些政黨和團體尋找方法解決問題。"},{"en":"Political parties and groups are organisations that try to influence public decisions and government policy.","zh":"political parties and groups 指嘗試影響公共決策和政府政策的組織。"},{"en":"Political parties and groups may debate how schools should teach migrant children.","zh":"政黨和團體可能辯論學校應如何教育移民兒童。"},{"en":"Their views can shape laws, funding, and public attitudes.","zh":"他們的觀點可以塑造法律、資金和公眾態度。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised political actors, not individual voters only.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的政治行動者，而不只是個別選民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"search for ways to","meaning":"尋找方法去……","examples":[{"en":"Policy-makers search for ways to integrate diverse communities.","zh":"政策制定者尋找方法去融合多元社群。"},{"en":"To search for ways to do something means to look for possible methods or solutions.","zh":"search for ways to do something 指尋找可行方法或解決方案。"},{"en":"Teachers may search for ways to help quiet students speak more confidently.","zh":"老師可能尋找方法去幫助安靜學生更自信地發言。"},{"en":"Searching for ways to solve a problem often begins with understanding its real causes.","zh":"尋找方法解決問題，通常由理解真正成因開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active problem-solving.","zh":"這個短語描述主動解難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"diverse communities","meaning":"多元社群","examples":[{"en":"Schools must respond to the needs of diverse communities.","zh":"學校必須回應多元社群的需要。"},{"en":"Diverse communities are groups of people with different languages, cultures, religions, or social backgrounds.","zh":"diverse communities 指由不同語言、文化、宗教或社會背景的人組成的群體。"},{"en":"A city with immigrants, local families, and international workers contains diverse communities.","zh":"一個有移民、本地家庭和國際工人的城市包含多元社群。"},{"en":"Diverse communities need services that respect different identities and practical needs.","zh":"多元社群需要尊重不同身份和實際需要的服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes communities made up of varied groups.","zh":"這個短語描述由多樣群體組成的社區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"integration in schools and society","meaning":"融入學校和社會","examples":[{"en":"Some groups focus on the integration of children in schools and society.","zh":"有些團體集中於兒童融入學校和社會。"},{"en":"Integration in schools and society means helping people become included in education and public life.","zh":"integration in schools and society 指幫助人們被納入教育和公共生活。"},{"en":"A new student may need language support for integration in school and friendship groups.","zh":"新學生可能需要語言支援，以融入學校和朋友圈。"},{"en":"Good integration allows children to participate without losing their home identity.","zh":"良好融合讓孩子能參與，同時不失去家庭身份。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to inclusion, not forced cultural erasure.","zh":"這個短語指包容，而不是被迫抹去文化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"positive consequences for","meaning":"對……的正面影響","examples":[{"en":"Some people see few positive consequences for the host society.","zh":"有些人認為對接收社會幾乎沒有正面影響。"},{"en":"Positive consequences for something are good effects or benefits that it receives.","zh":"positive consequences for something 指某事物所得到的良好效果或好處。"},{"en":"Bilingual education can have positive consequences for schools by improving communication with families.","zh":"雙語教育可以透過改善與家庭的溝通，對學校產生正面影響。"},{"en":"When diversity is well supported, it can create positive consequences for the whole community.","zh":"當多元性得到良好支援，它可以對整個社區產生正面影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes beneficial results for a particular group or place.","zh":"這個短語描述對特定群體或地方有益的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the host society","meaning":"接收社會；東道社會","examples":[{"en":"Some groups worry that diversity threatens the host society.","zh":"有些團體擔心多元性威脅接收社會。"},{"en":"The host society is the country or community that receives newcomers, migrants, or minority groups.","zh":"host society 指接收新來者、移民或少數群體的國家或社區。"},{"en":"Immigrant children may learn the language of the host society at school.","zh":"移民兒童可能在學校學習接收社會的語言。"},{"en":"A host society benefits when newcomers are supported rather than excluded.","zh":"當新來者得到支援而不是被排斥，接收社會會受益。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the receiving society, not the migrants themselves.","zh":"這個短語指接收一方的社會，而不是移民本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"threaten the identity of","meaning":"威脅……的身份認同","examples":[{"en":"They worry that diversity threatens the identity of the host society.","zh":"他們擔心多元性威脅接收社會的身份認同。"},{"en":"To threaten the identity of a group means to seem to endanger its shared culture, values, or sense of belonging.","zh":"threaten the identity of a group 指看似危害該群體共同文化、價值或歸屬感。"},{"en":"Some people wrongly think that new languages threaten the identity of a city.","zh":"有些人錯誤地認為新語言會威脅城市的身份認同。"},{"en":"Fear of identity loss can lead to unfair policies against minority children.","zh":"對身份流失的恐懼可以導致針對少數族裔兒童的不公平政策。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a perceived danger to collective identity.","zh":"這個短語描述對集體身份的被感知威脅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"consequently","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"Consequently, some groups promote unfortunate educational policies.","zh":"因此，有些團體推動不理想的教育政策。"},{"en":"Consequently means as a result of what has just been mentioned.","zh":"consequently 指因為剛提及的事情，所以出現某結果。"},{"en":"The school ignored language support; consequently, some students fell behind.","zh":"學校忽視語言支援；因此，有些學生落後了。"},{"en":"This word links a cause with a following result.","zh":"這個詞把原因與隨後結果連接起來。"},{"en":"It is useful in formal writing when explaining consequences.","zh":"它在正式寫作中解釋後果時很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"promote educational policies","meaning":"推動教育政策","examples":[{"en":"Some political groups promote educational policies that reduce linguistic diversity.","zh":"有些政治團體推動減少語言多元性的教育政策。"},{"en":"To promote educational policies means to support, argue for, or push forward rules about education.","zh":"promote educational policies 指支持、主張或推進關於教育的規則。"},{"en":"A parents’ group may promote educational policies that give more reading support to young children.","zh":"家長團體可能推動為年幼兒童提供更多閱讀支援的教育政策。"},{"en":"Policies promoted by political groups can affect classroom language, textbooks, and funding.","zh":"政治團體推動的政策可以影響課堂語言、教科書和資金。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active support for education-related decisions.","zh":"這個短語描述對教育相關決策的主動支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"unfortunate educational policies","meaning":"不理想的教育政策","examples":[{"en":"Unfortunate educational policies may discourage children from using their mother tongue.","zh":"不理想的教育政策可能令兒童不敢使用母語。"},{"en":"Unfortunate educational policies are school rules or government decisions that create harmful or unfair results.","zh":"unfortunate educational policies 指造成有害或不公平結果的學校規則或政府決定。"},{"en":"A policy that punishes children for speaking their home language would be unfortunate.","zh":"懲罰孩子說家庭語言的政策會是不理想的政策。"},{"en":"Such policies can weaken family communication and reduce children’s confidence.","zh":"這類政策可以削弱家庭溝通並降低兒童信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes education policies with negative consequences.","zh":"這個短語描述帶有負面後果的教育政策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make the problem disappear","meaning":"令問題消失","examples":[{"en":"Some policies try to make the problem disappear rather than solve it fairly.","zh":"有些政策試圖令問題消失，而不是公平地解決它。"},{"en":"To make the problem disappear means to hide, remove, or silence the visible issue without truly solving it.","zh":"make the problem disappear 指隱藏、移除或壓下表面的問題，而沒有真正解決它。"},{"en":"A school may make a bullying problem disappear on paper by ignoring reports.","zh":"學校可能透過忽視報告，在紙面上令欺凌問題消失。"},{"en":"Hiding a problem can make people feel unheard and may create deeper harm.","zh":"隱藏問題可以令人感到不被聆聽，並可能造成更深傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase often criticises superficial solutions.","zh":"這個短語常用來批評表面解決方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"retain their culture and language","meaning":"保留自己的文化和語言","examples":[{"en":"Students may retain their culture and language while learning the mainstream language.","zh":"學生可以在學習主流語言的同時，保留自己的文化和語言。"},{"en":"To retain their culture and language means to keep their traditions, identity, and home language alive.","zh":"retain their culture and language 指保留自己的傳統、身份和家庭語言。"},{"en":"Migrant children can retain their culture and language through family stories and weekend classes.","zh":"移民兒童可以透過家庭故事和週末課堂保留自己的文化和語言。"},{"en":"Retaining culture and language can strengthen confidence and family relationships.","zh":"保留文化和語言可以增強信心和家庭關係。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that learning a new language does not require losing the old one.","zh":"這個短語顯示學習新語言不需要失去舊語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be viewed as","meaning":"被視為","examples":[{"en":"Students who retain their language are sometimes viewed as less capable.","zh":"保留自己語言的學生有時被視為能力較弱。"},{"en":"To be viewed as something means to be seen or judged in a particular way.","zh":"be viewed as something 指被以某種方式看待或判斷。"},{"en":"A quiet student may be viewed as shy, even if she is simply thinking carefully.","zh":"安靜的學生可能被視為害羞，即使她只是正在仔細思考。"},{"en":"How people are viewed can affect how they are treated.","zh":"人們如何被看待，可以影響他們如何被對待。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on perception, not necessarily truth.","zh":"這個短語著重觀感，而不一定是真相。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"less capable of","meaning":"較缺乏能力去……","examples":[{"en":"Some students are viewed as less capable of identifying with the mainstream culture.","zh":"有些學生被視為較缺乏能力去認同主流文化。"},{"en":"Less capable of doing something means having less ability or being seen as having less ability to do it.","zh":"less capable of doing something 指較沒有能力，或被看成較沒有能力去做某事。"},{"en":"A child may be wrongly seen as less capable of learning English because she uses another language at home.","zh":"孩子可能因在家使用另一種語言，而被錯誤視為較缺乏能力學英文。"},{"en":"Such judgements can lower expectations and harm confidence.","zh":"這類判斷可以降低期望並傷害信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reduced ability or perceived reduced ability.","zh":"這個短語描述能力較低或被認為能力較低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"identify with","meaning":"認同……","examples":[{"en":"Children can identify with the mainstream culture without losing their mother tongue.","zh":"兒童可以認同主流文化，而不失去母語。"},{"en":"To identify with something means to feel connected to it and see it as part of who you are.","zh":"identify with something 指感到與某事有連繫，並把它視為自身一部分。"},{"en":"A student may identify with her school community when she feels respected there.","zh":"當學生在學校感到被尊重，她可能會認同學校社群。"},{"en":"Children can identify with more than one culture if both are valued.","zh":"如果兩種文化都被重視，兒童可以認同多於一種文化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional and cultural connection.","zh":"這個短語描述情感和文化上的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mainstream culture","meaning":"主流文化","examples":[{"en":"Schools often expect students to identify with the mainstream culture.","zh":"學校常期望學生認同主流文化。"},{"en":"Mainstream culture is the dominant or most widely accepted culture in a society.","zh":"mainstream culture 指社會中佔主導或最廣泛被接受的文化。"},{"en":"In many schools, mainstream culture appears in festivals, language use, textbooks, and classroom expectations.","zh":"在許多學校中，主流文化出現在節日、語言使用、教科書和課堂期望中。"},{"en":"If mainstream culture is treated as the only valuable culture, minority students may feel excluded.","zh":"如果主流文化被視為唯一有價值的文化，少數族裔學生可能感到被排除。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the culture with the strongest public influence.","zh":"這個短語指最具公共影響力的文化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mainstream language","meaning":"主流語言","examples":[{"en":"Students are expected to learn the mainstream language of society.","zh":"學生被期望學習社會的主流語言。"},{"en":"The mainstream language is the language most commonly used in public life, schools, or official communication.","zh":"mainstream language 指公共生活、學校或官方溝通中最常使用的語言。"},{"en":"Immigrant children often need the mainstream language to follow lessons and make friends.","zh":"移民兒童通常需要主流語言來跟上課堂和交朋友。"},{"en":"Learning the mainstream language can help integration, but it should not require losing the mother tongue.","zh":"學習主流語言可以幫助融入，但不應要求失去母語。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the socially dominant language.","zh":"這個短語指社會上佔主導地位的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the challenge for","meaning":"對……來說的挑戰","examples":[{"en":"The challenge for educators is to respect the rights of all children.","zh":"對教育工作者來說，挑戰是尊重所有兒童的權利。"},{"en":"The challenge for someone means the difficult task or problem that person must deal with.","zh":"the challenge for someone 指某人必須處理的困難任務或問題。"},{"en":"The challenge for teachers is to support weak students without slowing the whole class too much.","zh":"對老師來說，挑戰是在支援較弱學生的同時，不過度拖慢全班進度。"},{"en":"A challenge often involves balancing two important needs.","zh":"挑戰通常涉及平衡兩項重要需要。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the main difficulty faced by a group.","zh":"這個短語引入某群體所面對的主要困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"educators and policy-makers","meaning":"教育工作者和政策制定者","examples":[{"en":"Educators and policy-makers must respond to linguistic diversity.","zh":"教育工作者和政策制定者必須回應語言多元性。"},{"en":"Educators and policy-makers are teachers, school leaders, officials, and decision-makers who shape education.","zh":"educators and policy-makers 指塑造教育的老師、學校領袖、官員和決策者。"},{"en":"Educators and policy-makers may decide whether schools provide bilingual support.","zh":"教育工作者和政策制定者可能決定學校是否提供雙語支援。"},{"en":"Their decisions can affect children’s confidence, achievement, and family communication.","zh":"他們的決定可以影響兒童的信心、成就和家庭溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to both classroom professionals and people who design education policy.","zh":"這個短語同時指課堂專業人士和設計教育政策的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"shape the evolution of","meaning":"塑造……的演變","examples":[{"en":"Policy-makers can shape the evolution of national identity.","zh":"政策制定者可以塑造國民身份認同的演變。"},{"en":"To shape the evolution of something means to influence how it gradually develops over time.","zh":"shape the evolution of something 指影響某事如何隨時間逐步發展。"},{"en":"Schools can shape the evolution of students’ values by what they teach and celebrate.","zh":"學校可以透過所教授和慶祝的內容，塑造學生價值觀的演變。"},{"en":"Language policy can shape national identity by deciding whose language is recognised.","zh":"語言政策可以透過決定誰的語言被承認，塑造國民身份。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-term influence on development.","zh":"這個短語描述對發展的長期影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"national identity","meaning":"國民身份認同","examples":[{"en":"Education can influence the development of national identity.","zh":"教育可以影響國民身份認同的發展。"},{"en":"National identity is the shared sense of belonging people feel toward a country.","zh":"national identity 指人們對一個國家共同感到的歸屬感。"},{"en":"Language, history lessons, public holidays, and symbols can all shape national identity.","zh":"語言、歷史課、公眾假期和象徵都可以塑造國民身份認同。"},{"en":"If national identity includes many cultures, more citizens may feel respected.","zh":"如果國民身份認同包括多種文化，更多公民可能感到被尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to how people understand themselves as members of a nation.","zh":"這個短語指人們如何理解自己作為國家成員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in such a way that","meaning":"以……的方式","examples":[{"en":"Policy should be shaped in such a way that all citizens’ rights are respected.","zh":"政策應以尊重所有公民權利的方式塑造。"},{"en":"In such a way that means in a manner that produces a particular result.","zh":"in such a way that 指以能產生某特定結果的方式。"},{"en":"A teacher should explain rules in such a way that students understand both the rule and the reason.","zh":"老師應以讓學生理解規則和原因的方式解釋規則。"},{"en":"If a policy is designed carefully, it can protect diversity and unity at the same time.","zh":"如果政策設計仔細，它可以同時保護多元和團結。"},{"en":"This phrase links a method with the result it aims to create.","zh":"這個短語把方法與其想達成的結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the rights of all citizens","meaning":"所有公民的權利","examples":[{"en":"The rights of all citizens should be respected in education.","zh":"所有公民的權利在教育中都應受到尊重。"},{"en":"The rights of all citizens are the basic protections and freedoms that every member of a country should have.","zh":"rights of all citizens 指一個國家每位成員都應享有的基本保障和自由。"},{"en":"Schools respect the rights of all citizens when children from different backgrounds are treated fairly.","zh":"當來自不同背景的孩子受到公平對待，學校就在尊重所有公民的權利。"},{"en":"Ignoring minority languages may make some citizens feel that their rights are less valued.","zh":"忽視少數語言可能令部分公民覺得自己的權利較不受重視。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses fairness for everyone, not only the majority.","zh":"這個短語強調對每個人的公平，而不只是對多數人的公平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"including schoolchildren","meaning":"包括學童","examples":[{"en":"The rights of all citizens, including schoolchildren, should be respected.","zh":"所有公民的權利，包括學童，都應受到尊重。"},{"en":"Including schoolchildren means school-age children are part of the group being discussed.","zh":"including schoolchildren 指正在討論的群體也包括學齡兒童。"},{"en":"Public transport rules should consider all users, including schoolchildren who travel alone.","zh":"公共交通規則應考慮所有使用者，包括獨自乘車的學童。"},{"en":"Including children in rights discussions reminds adults that young people also deserve respect.","zh":"在權利討論中包括兒童，提醒成年人年輕人也應受到尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase adds schoolchildren as an important example within a larger group.","zh":"這個短語把學童作為較大群體中的重要例子加入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cultural, linguistic and economic resources","meaning":"文化、語言和經濟資源","examples":[{"en":"A nation should maximise its cultural, linguistic and economic resources.","zh":"一個國家應充分發揮其文化、語言和經濟資源。"},{"en":"Cultural, linguistic and economic resources are a society’s traditions, languages, skills, money, and productive strengths.","zh":"cultural, linguistic and economic resources 指社會的傳統、語言、技能、金錢和生產力量。"},{"en":"A multilingual community has linguistic resources that can help trade, education, and public services.","zh":"多語社群擁有可幫助貿易、教育和公共服務的語言資源。"},{"en":"When schools ignore children’s languages, they waste resources that could benefit society.","zh":"當學校忽視孩子的語言，就是浪費本可令社會受益的資源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes valuable assets a country can use and develop.","zh":"這個短語描述一個國家可以使用和發展的寶貴資產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"maximise resources","meaning":"充分發揮資源","examples":[{"en":"Good education policies help maximise national resources.","zh":"良好的教育政策幫助充分發揮國家資源。"},{"en":"To maximise resources means to use available strengths, skills, money, or materials as fully as possible.","zh":"maximise resources 指盡可能充分使用現有優勢、技能、金錢或材料。"},{"en":"A school maximises resources when it uses bilingual parents to support language events.","zh":"學校讓雙語家長支援語言活動，就是在充分發揮資源。"},{"en":"Maximising resources can reduce waste and create more opportunities.","zh":"充分發揮資源可以減少浪費並創造更多機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making the best possible use of what is available.","zh":"這個短語描述盡量善用現有資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"waste the resources of","meaning":"浪費……的資源","examples":[{"en":"Discouraging children from using their mother tongues wastes the resources of the nation.","zh":"阻止兒童使用母語是在浪費國家的資源。"},{"en":"To waste the resources of a group means to fail to use its valuable abilities, knowledge, or assets properly.","zh":"waste the resources of a group 指未能妥善使用該群體寶貴的能力、知識或資產。"},{"en":"A company wastes the resources of its staff if it ignores their language skills.","zh":"如果公司忽視員工的語言能力，就是浪費員工資源。"},{"en":"Wasting resources can reduce creativity, productivity, and social trust.","zh":"浪費資源可以降低創意、生產力和社會信任。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises the careless loss of something valuable.","zh":"這個短語批評對寶貴事物的粗心流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"discourage someone from doing something","meaning":"阻止某人做某事；令某人打消……念頭","examples":[{"en":"Schools should not discourage children from developing their mother tongues.","zh":"學校不應阻止兒童發展自己的母語。"},{"en":"To discourage someone from doing something means to make them less willing or confident to do it.","zh":"discourage someone from doing something 指令某人較不願意或較沒有信心做某事。"},{"en":"Harsh correction can discourage students from speaking English in class.","zh":"嚴厲糾正可以令學生打消在課堂說英語的念頭。"},{"en":"If children are discouraged from using their home language, they may feel ashamed of it.","zh":"如果孩子被阻止使用家庭語言，他們可能會為此感到羞愧。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing someone’s motivation to act.","zh":"這個短語描述降低某人行動動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"develop their mother tongues","meaning":"發展自己的母語能力","examples":[{"en":"Children should be encouraged to develop their mother tongues.","zh":"兒童應被鼓勵發展自己的母語能力。"},{"en":"To develop their mother tongues means to improve their ability to speak, read, write, and think in their home languages.","zh":"develop their mother tongues 指提升他們用家庭語言說、讀、寫和思考的能力。"},{"en":"Parents can help children develop their mother tongues by reading stories and discussing daily events.","zh":"父母可以透過閱讀故事和討論日常事情，幫助孩子發展自己的母語能力。"},{"en":"Strong mother-tongue development can support learning in other languages.","zh":"強大的母語發展可以支援其他語言的學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes building deeper ability in the first language.","zh":"這個短語描述建立更深入的第一語言能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"quite simply unintelligent","meaning":"簡直是不明智的","examples":[{"en":"Wasting children’s linguistic resources is quite simply unintelligent.","zh":"浪費兒童的語言資源簡直是不明智的。"},{"en":"Quite simply unintelligent means plainly unwise or lacking good judgement.","zh":"quite simply unintelligent 指明顯不明智或缺乏良好判斷。"},{"en":"Throwing away useful textbooks while students still need them is quite simply unintelligent.","zh":"在學生仍需要課本時把有用課本丟掉，簡直是不明智的。"},{"en":"A policy may be unintelligent if it wastes talent instead of developing it.","zh":"如果政策浪費人才而不是發展人才，它可能是不明智的。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses strong criticism in a direct way.","zh":"這個短語以直接方式表達強烈批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"from the point of view of","meaning":"從……角度來看","examples":[{"en":"This policy is unintelligent from the point of view of national self-interest.","zh":"從國家自身利益角度來看，這項政策是不明智的。"},{"en":"From the point of view of means when considered from a particular perspective or interest.","zh":"from the point of view of 指從某特定角度或利益來考慮。"},{"en":"From the point of view of students, clear instructions are more useful than long warnings.","zh":"從學生角度來看，清楚指示比長篇警告更有用。"},{"en":"A policy may look efficient from one point of view but unfair from another.","zh":"一項政策從某角度看可能有效率，但從另一角度看可能不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase shows whose perspective is being used.","zh":"這個短語顯示正在使用誰的角度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"national self-interest","meaning":"國家自身利益","examples":[{"en":"Supporting mother tongues can serve national self-interest.","zh":"支持母語可以服務國家自身利益。"},{"en":"National self-interest is what benefits a country’s long-term strength, stability, and development.","zh":"national self-interest 指有利於國家長遠力量、穩定和發展的事情。"},{"en":"Training multilingual citizens may serve national self-interest by improving trade and public services.","zh":"培養多語公民可以透過改善貿易和公共服務，服務國家自身利益。"},{"en":"Ignoring children’s language skills can weaken a country’s future resources.","zh":"忽視兒童語言能力可以削弱國家未來資源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to what is good for the nation itself.","zh":"這個短語指對國家本身有利的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a first step in","meaning":"……的第一步","examples":[{"en":"A first step in providing better education is to examine existing research.","zh":"提供更好教育的第一步是檢視現有研究。"},{"en":"A first step in doing something is an early action that begins the process.","zh":"a first step in doing something 指開始某過程的早期行動。"},{"en":"A first step in improving writing is to find the student’s most common grammar mistakes.","zh":"改善寫作的第一步，是找出學生最常見的文法錯誤。"},{"en":"Starting with research helps schools avoid decisions based only on fear or opinion.","zh":"由研究開始，幫助學校避免只基於恐懼或意見作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the beginning of a solution.","zh":"這個短語引入解決方案的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"provide an appropriate education for","meaning":"為……提供合適教育","examples":[{"en":"Schools should provide an appropriate education for diverse children.","zh":"學校應為多元兒童提供合適教育。"},{"en":"To provide an appropriate education for children means to offer teaching that fits their needs, backgrounds, and abilities.","zh":"provide an appropriate education for children 指提供符合孩子需要、背景和能力的教學。"},{"en":"A school provides an appropriate education when it supports both new language learners and advanced students.","zh":"當學校同時支援新語言學習者和高能力學生，就是在提供合適教育。"},{"en":"If education is not appropriate, children may feel lost or unfairly judged.","zh":"如果教育不合適，孩子可能感到迷失或被不公平評價。"},{"en":"This phrase describes suitable and fair educational support.","zh":"這個短語描述合適而公平的教育支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"culturally and linguistically diverse children","meaning":"文化和語言背景多元的兒童","examples":[{"en":"Teachers need to support culturally and linguistically diverse children.","zh":"老師需要支援文化和語言背景多元的兒童。"},{"en":"Culturally and linguistically diverse children are children from different cultural backgrounds and language communities.","zh":"culturally and linguistically diverse children 指來自不同文化背景和語言社群的兒童。"},{"en":"A class may include culturally and linguistically diverse children who speak Arabic, Cantonese, Spanish, or Urdu at home.","zh":"一班可能包括在家說阿拉伯語、廣東話、西班牙語或烏爾都語的文化和語言背景多元兒童。"},{"en":"These children may need support that respects both school learning and home identity.","zh":"這些兒童可能需要既尊重學校學習，也尊重家庭身份的支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes students with varied cultural and language backgrounds.","zh":"這個短語描述具有多樣文化和語言背景的學生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"existing research","meaning":"現有研究","examples":[{"en":"Existing research shows the value of children’s mother tongues.","zh":"現有研究顯示兒童母語的價值。"},{"en":"Existing research is the body of studies and evidence already available on a topic.","zh":"existing research 指某主題上已經存在的一批研究和證據。"},{"en":"A teacher may read existing research before choosing a new reading programme.","zh":"老師可能在選擇新閱讀計劃前閱讀現有研究。"},{"en":"Using existing research helps people avoid repeating old mistakes.","zh":"使用現有研究幫助人們避免重複舊錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to what researchers have already found.","zh":"這個短語指研究人員已經發現的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the role of","meaning":"……的作用","examples":[{"en":"Researchers examine the role of mother tongues in education.","zh":"研究人員檢視母語在教育中的作用。"},{"en":"The role of something is the part it plays in a process or result.","zh":"role of something 指某事在過程或結果中所扮演的部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may examine the role of feedback in improving student writing.","zh":"老師可能檢視回饋在改善學生寫作中的作用。"},{"en":"Understanding a factor’s role helps people decide whether to support or change it.","zh":"理解某因素的作用，幫助人們決定是否支援或改變它。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what contribution something makes.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事作出甚麼貢獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"educational development","meaning":"教育發展","examples":[{"en":"Mother tongues play an important role in children’s educational development.","zh":"母語在兒童教育發展中發揮重要作用。"},{"en":"Educational development is the growth of a child’s learning, thinking, language, and academic skills.","zh":"educational development 指兒童學習、思考、語言和學業技能的成長。"},{"en":"Reading at home can support a child’s educational development before formal schooling begins.","zh":"在家閱讀可以在正式上學前支援孩子的教育發展。"},{"en":"Strong language ability helps children understand lessons and express ideas.","zh":"強大的語言能力幫助孩子理解課堂並表達想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes progress in learning and schooling.","zh":"這個短語描述學習和求學上的進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, the research is very clear.","zh":"事實上，研究非常清楚。"},{"en":"In fact means actually, especially when giving a stronger or clearer truth.","zh":"in fact 指事實上，尤其用於提出更強或更清楚的真相。"},{"en":"Some people think bilingualism confuses children; in fact, it can support learning.","zh":"有些人認為雙語會令孩子混亂；事實上，它可以支援學習。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to correct or strengthen a point.","zh":"作者使用這個短語來修正或加強重點。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces evidence that challenges a common belief.","zh":"這個短語常引入挑戰常見信念的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"continue to develop","meaning":"繼續發展","examples":[{"en":"Children should continue to develop their abilities in more than one language.","zh":"兒童應繼續發展使用多於一種語言的能力。"},{"en":"To continue to develop means to keep improving over time.","zh":"continue to develop 指隨時間持續進步。"},{"en":"Students should continue to develop their reading skills after they can read basic stories.","zh":"學生能閱讀基本故事後，仍應繼續發展閱讀能力。"},{"en":"If language development stops too early, children may lose confidence or fluency.","zh":"如果語言發展太早停止，孩子可能失去信心或流暢度。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that growth should not stop at an early stage.","zh":"這個短語強調成長不應在早期階段停止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"abilities in two or more languages","meaning":"使用兩種或以上語言的能力","examples":[{"en":"Children can develop abilities in two or more languages.","zh":"兒童可以發展使用兩種或以上語言的能力。"},{"en":"Abilities in two or more languages are skills in understanding, speaking, reading, or writing multiple languages.","zh":"abilities in two or more languages 指理解、說、讀或寫多種語言的技能。"},{"en":"A child may use one language with grandparents and another language at school.","zh":"孩子可能與祖父母使用一種語言，而在學校使用另一種語言。"},{"en":"Developing abilities in several languages can improve communication across family and society.","zh":"發展多種語言能力可以改善家庭和社會之間的溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to multilingual language skills.","zh":"這個短語指多語能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"throughout their primary-school years","meaning":"在整個小學階段","examples":[{"en":"Children develop language abilities throughout their primary-school years.","zh":"兒童在整個小學階段發展語言能力。"},{"en":"Throughout their primary-school years means during the whole period of primary education.","zh":"throughout their primary-school years 指在整個小學教育期間。"},{"en":"Children build reading habits throughout their primary-school years, not only in the first year.","zh":"兒童在整個小學階段建立閱讀習慣，而不只是在第一年。"},{"en":"Continuous support matters because language growth takes many years.","zh":"持續支援很重要，因為語言成長需要多年。"},{"en":"This phrase describes development across the full primary-school period.","zh":"這個短語描述貫穿整個小學階段的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"gain a deeper understanding of","meaning":"對……有更深入的了解","examples":[{"en":"Bilingual children gain a deeper understanding of language.","zh":"雙語兒童對語言有更深入的了解。"},{"en":"To gain a deeper understanding of something means to understand it more fully and thoughtfully.","zh":"gain a deeper understanding of something 指更完整和更深入地理解某事。"},{"en":"Students gain a deeper understanding of history when they read personal stories, not only dates.","zh":"當學生閱讀個人故事，而不只是日期，他們會對歷史有更深入的了解。"},{"en":"Comparing two languages can help children notice how grammar and meaning work.","zh":"比較兩種語言可以幫助孩子注意文法和意思如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving beyond surface knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述超越表面知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"use it effectively","meaning":"有效地運用它","examples":[{"en":"Children learn how to use language effectively.","zh":"兒童學會如何有效地運用語言。"},{"en":"To use it effectively means to use something in a way that achieves the intended purpose well.","zh":"use it effectively 指以能良好達成目的的方式使用某物。"},{"en":"A student uses language effectively when she explains an idea clearly to classmates.","zh":"當學生清楚向同學解釋想法，她就是有效地運用語言。"},{"en":"Effective language use helps children ask questions, solve problems, and build relationships.","zh":"有效運用語言幫助孩子提問、解難和建立關係。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on successful practical use.","zh":"這個短語著重成功的實際使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have more practice in","meaning":"有更多練習去……","examples":[{"en":"Bilingual children have more practice in processing language.","zh":"雙語兒童有更多練習去處理語言。"},{"en":"To have more practice in something means to get more repeated experience doing it.","zh":"have more practice in something 指在做某事上有更多反覆經驗。"},{"en":"Students have more practice in speaking when lessons include pair discussion.","zh":"當課堂包括二人討論，學生就有更多練習去說話。"},{"en":"More practice can make a skill faster, stronger, and more flexible.","zh":"更多練習可以令技能更快、更強和更靈活。"},{"en":"This phrase connects repeated use with improvement.","zh":"這個短語把反覆使用與進步連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"process language","meaning":"處理語言","examples":[{"en":"Children process language in different ways when they use two languages.","zh":"兒童使用兩種語言時，會以不同方式處理語言。"},{"en":"To process language means to understand, interpret, and use words, sounds, and grammar mentally.","zh":"process language 指在腦中理解、詮釋和使用詞語、聲音和文法。"},{"en":"A student processes language when she listens to a question and decides how to answer.","zh":"當學生聽問題並決定如何回答時，她就是在處理語言。"},{"en":"Using two languages gives children more chances to compare sounds and meanings.","zh":"使用兩種語言給孩子更多機會比較聲音和意思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the mental work involved in language use.","zh":"這個短語描述語言使用所涉及的心理工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"develop literacy in","meaning":"培養……的讀寫能力","examples":[{"en":"Children benefit when they develop literacy in both languages.","zh":"當兒童培養兩種語言的讀寫能力，他們會受益。"},{"en":"To develop literacy in a language means to build reading and writing ability in that language.","zh":"develop literacy in a language 指建立該語言的閱讀和寫作能力。"},{"en":"A child may develop literacy in Chinese through storybooks and in English through school lessons.","zh":"孩子可能透過故事書培養中文讀寫能力，並透過學校課堂培養英文讀寫能力。"},{"en":"Literacy in one language can support reading strategies in another language.","zh":"一種語言的讀寫能力可以支援另一種語言中的閱讀策略。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to growing reading and writing skills.","zh":"這個短語指閱讀和寫作能力的成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"research studies","meaning":"研究","examples":[{"en":"More than 150 research studies support the importance of bilingualism.","zh":"超過 150 項研究支持雙語能力的重要性。"},{"en":"Research studies are organised investigations that collect evidence to answer questions.","zh":"research studies 指有組織地收集證據以回答問題的研究。"},{"en":"Research studies on education may use tests, interviews, classroom observations, or school records.","zh":"關於教育的研究可能使用測驗、訪談、課堂觀察或學校紀錄。"},{"en":"Many studies together can give stronger support than a single opinion.","zh":"多項研究合起來可以比單一意見提供更強支持。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal pieces of research.","zh":"這個短語指正式研究作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"conducted during","meaning":"在……期間進行","examples":[{"en":"Many research studies were conducted during the past 25 years.","zh":"許多研究在過去 25 年期間進行。"},{"en":"Conducted during means carried out within a particular period of time.","zh":"conducted during 指在某段特定時間內進行。"},{"en":"A survey conducted during the school year may reflect students’ real workload.","zh":"在學年期間進行的調查可能反映學生真實工作量。"},{"en":"The time when research is conducted can affect its results.","zh":"研究進行的時間可以影響其結果。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an activity with its time period.","zh":"這個短語把活動與其時間段連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"strongly support","meaning":"強烈支持","examples":[{"en":"Research studies strongly support Goethe’s view of language learning.","zh":"研究強烈支持 Goethe 對語言學習的看法。"},{"en":"To strongly support something means to provide clear and powerful evidence or agreement for it.","zh":"strongly support something 指為某事提供清楚而有力的證據或同意。"},{"en":"Exam results and classroom observations may strongly support a new reading programme.","zh":"考試結果和課堂觀察可能強烈支持一項新閱讀計劃。"},{"en":"Strong support makes an argument more convincing than opinion alone.","zh":"強力支持令論點比單靠意見更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that evidence is firm, not weak.","zh":"這個短語顯示證據有力，而不是薄弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"eighteenth-century German philosopher","meaning":"十八世紀德國哲學家","examples":[{"en":"Goethe was a famous eighteenth-century German philosopher.","zh":"Goethe 是一位著名的十八世紀德國哲學家。"},{"en":"An eighteenth-century German philosopher is a thinker from Germany who lived and wrote in the 1700s.","zh":"eighteenth-century German philosopher 指生活並著述於十八世紀的德國思想家。"},{"en":"A history lesson may mention an eighteenth-century German philosopher when discussing European ideas.","zh":"歷史課討論歐洲思想時，可能提及十八世紀德國哲學家。"},{"en":"Naming a respected philosopher can lend authority to an argument.","zh":"引用受尊敬的哲學家可以加強論點權威。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a person by time period, nationality, and intellectual role.","zh":"這個短語以時代、國籍和思想角色識別人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"truly know","meaning":"真正了解","examples":[{"en":"A person who knows only one language may not truly know that language.","zh":"只懂一種語言的人，可能並不真正了解那種語言。"},{"en":"To truly know something means to understand it deeply, not only use it on the surface.","zh":"truly know something 指深入理解某事，而不只是表面使用。"},{"en":"Students may not truly know a grammar rule until they can use it in their own writing.","zh":"學生要到能在自己的寫作中使用文法規則，才可能真正了解它。"},{"en":"Comparing languages can make learners notice features they once took for granted.","zh":"比較語言可以令學習者注意到自己曾視為理所當然的特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses deep understanding rather than basic familiarity.","zh":"這個短語強調深入理解，而不是基本熟悉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"research suggests that","meaning":"研究顯示","examples":[{"en":"Research suggests that bilingual children may develop flexible thinking.","zh":"研究顯示雙語兒童可能發展靈活思維。"},{"en":"Research suggests that means studies provide evidence pointing toward a conclusion.","zh":"research suggests that 指研究提供指向某結論的證據。"},{"en":"Research suggests that regular reading improves vocabulary growth.","zh":"研究顯示定期閱讀能改善詞彙增長。"},{"en":"This phrase is careful because it presents evidence without overstating certainty.","zh":"這個短語較謹慎，因為它呈現證據而不過度肯定。"},{"en":"It is useful in academic writing when summarising findings.","zh":"它適合在學術寫作中總結研究結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"bilingual children","meaning":"雙語兒童","examples":[{"en":"Bilingual children may develop more flexibility in their thinking.","zh":"雙語兒童可能發展出更靈活的思維。"},{"en":"Bilingual children are children who use or are learning two languages.","zh":"bilingual children 指使用或正在學習兩種語言的兒童。"},{"en":"A bilingual child may speak one language with grandparents and another with teachers.","zh":"雙語兒童可能與祖父母說一種語言，與老師說另一種語言。"},{"en":"Bilingual children often learn to switch between languages depending on the situation.","zh":"雙語兒童常學會按情境在兩種語言之間切換。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to children with experience in two languages.","zh":"這個短語指有兩種語言經驗的兒童。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"flexibility in their thinking","meaning":"思維上的靈活性","examples":[{"en":"Bilingual children may develop more flexibility in their thinking.","zh":"雙語兒童可能發展出更多思維上的靈活性。"},{"en":"Flexibility in thinking is the ability to shift between ideas, viewpoints, or ways of solving problems.","zh":"flexibility in thinking 指在想法、角度或解難方式之間轉換的能力。"},{"en":"A student shows flexibility in thinking when she solves a maths problem in two different ways.","zh":"學生用兩種不同方法解數學題時，就顯示思維上的靈活性。"},{"en":"Using two languages may train children to notice different patterns and meanings.","zh":"使用兩種語言可能訓練兒童注意不同模式和意思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental adaptability.","zh":"這個短語描述心智適應能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as a result of","meaning":"由於；作為……的結果","examples":[{"en":"Children may become more flexible as a result of processing two languages.","zh":"兒童可能由於處理兩種語言而變得更靈活。"},{"en":"As a result of means because of something that happened or existed.","zh":"as a result of 指因為某事發生或存在。"},{"en":"A student may gain confidence as a result of regular speaking practice.","zh":"學生可能由於定期口語練習而建立信心。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links a cause with its effect.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接原因和結果。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining why a change happens.","zh":"它適合用於解釋變化為何發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"process information through","meaning":"透過……處理資料","examples":[{"en":"Bilingual children process information through two different languages.","zh":"雙語兒童透過兩種不同語言處理資料。"},{"en":"To process information through something means to understand or organise ideas using that system or language.","zh":"process information through something 指使用某系統或語言理解或組織想法。"},{"en":"A child may process information through her home language before answering in the school language.","zh":"孩子可能先透過家庭語言處理資料，再用學校語言回答。"},{"en":"Processing information through two languages can strengthen comparison and mental flexibility.","zh":"透過兩種語言處理資料可以加強比較和心智靈活性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how the mind handles information using a particular channel.","zh":"這個短語描述大腦如何透過特定渠道處理資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the level of development of","meaning":"……的發展程度","examples":[{"en":"The level of development of children’s mother tongue predicts second language development.","zh":"兒童母語的發展程度能預測第二語言發展。"},{"en":"The level of development of something means how advanced or strong it has become.","zh":"level of development of something 指某事已變得多高階或多強。"},{"en":"Teachers may check the level of development of a child’s reading before choosing books.","zh":"老師可能先檢查孩子閱讀能力的發展程度，再選擇書本。"},{"en":"A stronger first language can support learning in a second language.","zh":"較強的第一語言可以支援第二語言學習。"},{"en":"This phrase measures how far a skill has grown.","zh":"這個短語量度技能已發展到甚麼程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a strong predictor of","meaning":"……的有力預測因素","examples":[{"en":"Mother-tongue development is a strong predictor of second language development.","zh":"母語發展是第二語言發展的有力預測因素。"},{"en":"A strong predictor of something is a factor that gives a good indication of what is likely to happen.","zh":"strong predictor of something 指能很好顯示某事可能發生的因素。"},{"en":"Regular attendance is a strong predictor of better school performance.","zh":"定期出席是較佳學業表現的有力預測因素。"},{"en":"If one factor strongly predicts another, it should be taken seriously in planning.","zh":"如果一個因素能強力預測另一個結果，規劃時就應認真對待。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a factor that helps forecast an outcome.","zh":"這個短語描述有助預測結果的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"second language development","meaning":"第二語言發展","examples":[{"en":"A strong mother tongue supports second language development.","zh":"強大的母語支援第二語言發展。"},{"en":"Second language development is the growth of ability in a language learned after the first language.","zh":"second language development 指在第一語言之後學習的語言能力成長。"},{"en":"A child learning English at school after speaking Urdu at home is experiencing second language development.","zh":"在家說烏爾都語、在學校學英語的孩子，正在經歷第二語言發展。"},{"en":"Skills in the first language can help children understand grammar, meaning, and reading in the second language.","zh":"第一語言中的技能可以幫助孩子理解第二語言的文法、意思和閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to progress in an additional language.","zh":"這個短語指額外語言的進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"come to school with","meaning":"帶着……入學","examples":[{"en":"Some children come to school with a solid foundation in their mother tongue.","zh":"有些兒童帶着穩固的母語基礎入學。"},{"en":"To come to school with something means to arrive at school already having that ability, background, or experience.","zh":"come to school with something 指入學時已經具有某能力、背景或經驗。"},{"en":"Some children come to school with strong storytelling skills from family conversations.","zh":"有些兒童帶着來自家庭對話的強大說故事能力入學。"},{"en":"What children bring from home can support learning if teachers recognise it.","zh":"如果老師承認孩子從家庭帶來的東西，它可以支援學習。"},{"en":"This phrase connects home experience with school learning.","zh":"這個短語把家庭經驗與學校學習連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a solid foundation in","meaning":"在……方面有穩固基礎","examples":[{"en":"Children need a solid foundation in their mother tongue.","zh":"兒童需要在母語方面有穩固基礎。"},{"en":"A solid foundation in something is a strong basic understanding or skill that later learning can build on.","zh":"solid foundation in something 指日後學習可建基其上的強大基本理解或技能。"},{"en":"A student needs a solid foundation in grammar before writing complex essays.","zh":"學生在寫複雜作文前，需要在文法方面有穩固基礎。"},{"en":"Without a solid foundation, later learning may become confusing and unstable.","zh":"沒有穩固基礎，之後的學習可能變得混亂和不穩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong basics that support future progress.","zh":"這個短語描述支援未來進步的強大基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stronger literacy abilities","meaning":"較強的讀寫能力","examples":[{"en":"Children with a solid mother-tongue foundation develop stronger literacy abilities.","zh":"有穩固母語基礎的兒童會發展出較強的讀寫能力。"},{"en":"Stronger literacy abilities mean better reading, writing, and understanding of written language.","zh":"stronger literacy abilities 指較好的閱讀、寫作和理解書面語能力。"},{"en":"A child who reads stories in her home language may develop stronger literacy abilities later at school.","zh":"在家庭語言中閱讀故事的孩子，日後在學校可能發展較強的讀寫能力。"},{"en":"Strong literacy helps students understand textbooks and express ideas clearly.","zh":"強大的讀寫能力幫助學生理解教科書並清楚表達想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improved reading and writing skills.","zh":"這個短語描述改善了的閱讀和寫作技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the school language","meaning":"學校教學語言","examples":[{"en":"Children use the school language for learning in class.","zh":"兒童在課堂學習中使用學校教學語言。"},{"en":"The school language is the main language used for teaching, learning, and classroom communication.","zh":"school language 指用於教學、學習和課堂溝通的主要語言。"},{"en":"A child may speak Punjabi at home but use English as the school language.","zh":"孩子可能在家說旁遮普語，但以英語作為學校教學語言。"},{"en":"If children do not understand the school language well, they may struggle with every subject.","zh":"如果兒童不能好好理解學校語言，他們可能在每一科都吃力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the language of instruction in school.","zh":"這個短語指學校中的教學語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"parents and other caregivers","meaning":"父母及其他照顧者","examples":[{"en":"Parents and other caregivers can support children’s language development.","zh":"父母及其他照顧者可以支援兒童語言發展。"},{"en":"Parents and other caregivers are the adults who look after children and help them grow.","zh":"parents and other caregivers 指照顧孩子並幫助他們成長的成年人。"},{"en":"Grandparents, relatives, and childminders can be other caregivers besides parents.","zh":"除父母外，祖父母、親戚和保姆都可以是其他照顧者。"},{"en":"Caregivers support language by talking, reading, listening, and explaining daily experiences.","zh":"照顧者透過交談、閱讀、聆聽和解釋日常經驗支援語言。"},{"en":"This phrase includes both parents and other people who care for children.","zh":"這個短語包括父母和其他照顧孩子的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"spend time with","meaning":"花時間陪伴……","examples":[{"en":"Caregivers should spend time with children and talk to them.","zh":"照顧者應花時間陪伴兒童並與他們交談。"},{"en":"To spend time with someone means to be with them and give them attention.","zh":"spend time with someone 指與某人在一起並給予關注。"},{"en":"Parents spend time with children when they read together before bed.","zh":"父母睡前與孩子一起閱讀，就是花時間陪伴孩子。"},{"en":"Time spent talking with adults helps children build vocabulary and confidence.","zh":"與成年人交談的時間幫助孩子建立詞彙和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes personal attention, not just physical presence.","zh":"這個短語描述個人關注，而不只是身體在場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"discuss issues with","meaning":"與……討論議題","examples":[{"en":"Parents can discuss issues with children in their mother tongue.","zh":"父母可以用母語與兒童討論議題。"},{"en":"To discuss issues with someone means to talk about important topics or problems together.","zh":"discuss issues with someone 指與某人一起談論重要主題或問題。"},{"en":"A parent may discuss school pressure with a child after a difficult test.","zh":"在困難測驗後，家長可能與孩子討論學業壓力。"},{"en":"Discussing issues in the mother tongue can let children express feelings more fully.","zh":"用母語討論議題可以讓孩子更完整地表達感受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaningful conversation about matters that need thought.","zh":"這個短語描述就需要思考的事情進行有意義對話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in a way that","meaning":"以……的方式","examples":[{"en":"Adults can speak with children in a way that develops their mother tongue.","zh":"成年人可以以發展兒童母語的方式與他們交談。"},{"en":"In a way that means in a manner that produces a particular effect or result.","zh":"in a way that 指以能產生某特定效果或結果的方式。"},{"en":"Teachers can correct mistakes in a way that protects students’ confidence.","zh":"老師可以以保護學生信心的方式糾正錯誤。"},{"en":"The way adults speak can either develop or limit children’s language.","zh":"成年人的說話方式可以發展或限制兒童語言。"},{"en":"This phrase links a method with its intended effect.","zh":"這個短語把方法與其預期效果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"well-prepared to","meaning":"已準備好去……","examples":[{"en":"Children who develop their mother tongue are well-prepared to learn the school language.","zh":"發展母語能力的兒童已準備好去學習學校語言。"},{"en":"To be well-prepared to do something means to have the skills, knowledge, or confidence needed for it.","zh":"well-prepared to do something 指具備做某事所需的技能、知識或信心。"},{"en":"A student who reads every week is well-prepared to write better essays.","zh":"每週閱讀的學生已準備好去寫更好的作文。"},{"en":"Strong first-language skills can prepare children for learning another language.","zh":"強大的第一語言技能可以為兒童學習另一種語言作好準備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes readiness for a future task.","zh":"這個短語描述對未來任務的準備程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"succeed educationally","meaning":"在學業上取得成功","examples":[{"en":"Children with strong language support are more likely to succeed educationally.","zh":"有強大語言支援的兒童較有可能在學業上取得成功。"},{"en":"To succeed educationally means to do well in learning, school progress, and academic development.","zh":"succeed educationally 指在學習、學校進展和學術發展上表現良好。"},{"en":"Students succeed educationally when they understand lessons, complete work, and grow in confidence.","zh":"當學生理解課堂、完成功課並建立信心，他們就在學業上取得成功。"},{"en":"Language support can help children succeed because they can access classroom content.","zh":"語言支援可以幫助孩子成功，因為他們能接觸課堂內容。"},{"en":"This phrase describes success in education, not only exam scores.","zh":"這個短語描述教育上的成功，而不只是考試分數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"knowledge and skills","meaning":"知識和技能","examples":[{"en":"Children’s knowledge and skills can transfer across languages.","zh":"兒童的知識和技能可以在不同語言之間轉移。"},{"en":"Knowledge and skills are what people know and what they are able to do.","zh":"knowledge and skills 指人們知道的東西和能做的事情。"},{"en":"A student’s knowledge and skills may include reading strategies, vocabulary, and problem-solving.","zh":"學生的知識和技能可能包括閱讀策略、詞彙和解難能力。"},{"en":"When knowledge and skills transfer, learning in one area can support another area.","zh":"當知識和技能轉移，一個範疇的學習可以支援另一個範疇。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to both understanding and practical ability.","zh":"這個短語同時指理解和實際能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"transfer across languages","meaning":"在不同語言之間轉移","examples":[{"en":"Children’s knowledge and skills transfer across languages.","zh":"兒童的知識和技能會在不同語言之間轉移。"},{"en":"To transfer across languages means to move or be applied from one language to another.","zh":"transfer across languages 指從一種語言轉到另一種語言，或被應用於另一種語言。"},{"en":"A child who learns how to find the main idea in Chinese can use that skill in English reading.","zh":"孩子在中文中學會找主旨後，可以在英文閱讀中使用這項技能。"},{"en":"Transfer across languages helps explain why mother-tongue development supports school-language learning.","zh":"語言之間的轉移有助解釋為何母語發展支援學校語言學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning that carries over between languages.","zh":"這個短語描述能在語言之間延伸的學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"two-way","meaning":"雙向的","examples":[{"en":"Transfer across languages can be two-way.","zh":"語言之間的轉移可以是雙向的。"},{"en":"Two-way means moving or working in both directions, not only one direction.","zh":"two-way 指在兩個方向移動或運作，而不只是一個方向。"},{"en":"Communication between school and parents should be two-way so both sides can listen and respond.","zh":"學校和家長之間的溝通應是雙向的，讓雙方都能聆聽和回應。"},{"en":"If language transfer is two-way, each language can support the other.","zh":"如果語言轉移是雙向的，每種語言都可以支援另一種語言。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mutual influence.","zh":"這個短語描述互相影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"nurture each other","meaning":"互相滋養；互相促進","examples":[{"en":"Both languages nurture each other when children can use both.","zh":"當兒童能使用兩種語言，兩種語言會互相滋養。"},{"en":"To nurture each other means to support and help each other grow.","zh":"nurture each other 指互相支持並幫助彼此成長。"},{"en":"Reading in the mother tongue can nurture school-language reading by building thinking skills.","zh":"母語閱讀可以透過建立思考能力來促進學校語言閱讀。"},{"en":"When two skills nurture each other, progress in one strengthens the other.","zh":"當兩項技能互相促進，一方面的進步會加強另一方面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mutual support and growth.","zh":"這個短語描述互相支援和成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"educational environment","meaning":"教育環境","examples":[{"en":"The educational environment should permit access to both languages.","zh":"教育環境應容許接觸兩種語言。"},{"en":"An educational environment is the school setting, teaching approach, resources, and relationships that shape learning.","zh":"educational environment 指塑造學習的學校環境、教學方法、資源和關係。"},{"en":"A supportive educational environment includes patient teachers, clear materials, and safe classroom routines.","zh":"支援性的教育環境包括有耐性的老師、清楚教材和安全課堂常規。"},{"en":"The environment affects whether children feel free to use and develop their languages.","zh":"環境會影響兒童是否感到可以自由使用和發展自己的語言。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the conditions surrounding learning.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞學習的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"permit access to","meaning":"容許接觸……","examples":[{"en":"A good school environment permits children access to both languages.","zh":"良好的學校環境容許兒童接觸兩種語言。"},{"en":"To permit access to something means to allow people to use, reach, or take part in it.","zh":"permit access to something 指容許人們使用、接觸或參與某事。"},{"en":"A library permits access to books, computers, and quiet study spaces.","zh":"圖書館容許使用書本、電腦和安靜自修空間。"},{"en":"When schools permit access to both languages, children can build on what they already know.","zh":"當學校容許接觸兩種語言，兒童可以建基於已有知識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes allowing meaningful use or availability.","zh":"這個短語描述容許有意義的使用或接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"mother-tongue-based teaching programmes","meaning":"以母語為本的教學課程","examples":[{"en":"Some parents are suspicious of mother-tongue-based teaching programmes.","zh":"有些家長對以母語為本的教學課程抱有懷疑。"},{"en":"Mother-tongue-based teaching programmes use children’s home language as part of classroom teaching.","zh":"mother-tongue-based teaching programmes 指把兒童家庭語言作為課堂教學一部分的課程。"},{"en":"A school may teach science concepts first through pupils’ mother tongue before introducing the school language.","zh":"學校可能先透過學生母語教授科學概念，再引入學校語言。"},{"en":"Such programmes can support understanding if they are well planned and well implemented.","zh":"如果規劃和推行良好，這類課程可以支援理解。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to education that builds on children’s first language.","zh":"這個短語指建基於兒童第一語言的教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be suspicious of","meaning":"對……抱有懷疑","examples":[{"en":"Some educators are suspicious of bilingual programmes.","zh":"有些教育工作者對雙語課程抱有懷疑。"},{"en":"To be suspicious of something means to doubt it or worry that it may cause problems.","zh":"be suspicious of something 指懷疑某事，或擔心它可能造成問題。"},{"en":"Parents may be suspicious of a new exam system if schools do not explain it clearly.","zh":"如果學校沒有清楚解釋新考試制度，家長可能對它抱有懷疑。"},{"en":"Suspicion often grows when people lack information or hear frightening claims.","zh":"當人們缺乏資訊或聽到令人害怕的說法，懷疑常會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doubt or mistrust.","zh":"這個短語描述疑慮或不信任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take time away from","meaning":"佔用原本用於……的時間","examples":[{"en":"Some people worry that mother-tongue teaching takes time away from the majority language.","zh":"有些人擔心母語教學會佔用原本用於主流語言的時間。"},{"en":"To take time away from something means to reduce the time available for it.","zh":"take time away from something 指減少可用於某事的時間。"},{"en":"A long school assembly may take time away from regular lessons.","zh":"長時間學校集會可能佔用原本用於正常課堂的時間。"},{"en":"People may fear that one activity harms another by using limited time.","zh":"人們可能擔心一項活動因使用有限時間而傷害另一項活動。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses concern about competition for time.","zh":"這個短語表達對時間競爭的憂慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the majority language","meaning":"多數人使用的語言；主流語言","examples":[{"en":"Children also need to develop the majority language.","zh":"兒童也需要發展主流語言。"},{"en":"The majority language is the language used by most people in a society or school system.","zh":"majority language 指一個社會或學校制度中大多數人使用的語言。"},{"en":"In an English-speaking country, English is often the majority language.","zh":"在英語國家，英語通常是主流語言。"},{"en":"Children need the majority language to access public life, but their mother tongue can still be valuable.","zh":"兒童需要主流語言來接觸公共生活，但母語仍然有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the socially dominant language.","zh":"這個短語指社會上佔主導地位的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"spend time teaching through","meaning":"花時間以……作為教學語言","examples":[{"en":"Teachers may spend time teaching through children’s home language.","zh":"老師可能花時間以兒童的家庭語言作為教學語言。"},{"en":"To spend time teaching through a language means to use that language as the medium for instruction.","zh":"spend time teaching through a language 指使用該語言作為教學媒介。"},{"en":"A teacher may spend time teaching through Cantonese before asking students to explain the idea in English.","zh":"老師可能先花時間以廣東話教學，再要求學生用英文解釋概念。"},{"en":"Teaching through a familiar language can make difficult concepts easier to understand.","zh":"透過熟悉語言教學可以令困難概念較容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using a language to deliver teaching.","zh":"這個短語描述使用某語言來進行教學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"children’s home language","meaning":"兒童的家庭語言","examples":[{"en":"A bilingual programme may teach through children’s home language.","zh":"雙語課程可能透過兒童的家庭語言教學。"},{"en":"Children’s home language is the language children commonly use with family at home.","zh":"children’s home language 指兒童在家中通常與家人使用的語言。"},{"en":"A child’s home language may be different from the language used in school textbooks.","zh":"兒童的家庭語言可能不同於學校課本使用的語言。"},{"en":"Valuing the home language can help children feel respected and understood.","zh":"重視家庭語言可以幫助兒童感到被尊重和理解。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the language of family life.","zh":"這個短語指家庭生活中的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"progress as far in","meaning":"在……方面進步到同等程度","examples":[{"en":"Some people worry that children will not progress as far in the majority language.","zh":"有些人擔心兒童在主流語言方面不會進步到同等程度。"},{"en":"To progress as far in something means to reach the same level of development or achievement in it.","zh":"progress as far in something 指在某方面達到相同發展或成就水平。"},{"en":"A parent may worry that a child will not progress as far in maths if too much time is spent on other subjects.","zh":"家長可能擔心如果花太多時間在其他科目上，孩子在數學方面不會進步到同等程度。"},{"en":"Research may show whether this fear is reasonable or not.","zh":"研究可以顯示這種擔心是否合理。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how much progress is made in one area.","zh":"這個短語比較某方面取得多少進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"one of the most strongly established findings","meaning":"最有力確立的研究結果之一","examples":[{"en":"This is one of the most strongly established findings of educational research.","zh":"這是教育研究中最有力確立的研究結果之一。"},{"en":"One of the most strongly established findings is a conclusion supported by a large amount of reliable evidence.","zh":"one of the most strongly established findings 指由大量可靠證據支持的結論之一。"},{"en":"That regular reading improves vocabulary is one of the strongly established findings in language learning.","zh":"定期閱讀能改善詞彙，是語言學習中有力確立的研究結果之一。"},{"en":"Strongly established findings should influence policy more than fear or assumption.","zh":"有力確立的研究結果應比恐懼或假設更能影響政策。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence that is especially firm.","zh":"這個短語描述尤其穩固的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"well-implemented bilingual programmes","meaning":"推行良好的雙語課程","examples":[{"en":"Well-implemented bilingual programmes can promote literacy in a minority language.","zh":"推行良好的雙語課程可以促進少數語言的讀寫能力。"},{"en":"Well-implemented bilingual programmes are carefully planned and effectively run programmes using two languages.","zh":"well-implemented bilingual programmes 指經仔細規劃並有效執行、使用兩種語言的課程。"},{"en":"A school has a well-implemented bilingual programme when teachers are trained and materials are suitable.","zh":"當老師受過培訓而教材合適，學校就有推行良好的雙語課程。"},{"en":"Good implementation matters because a poor programme may fail even if the idea is strong.","zh":"良好推行很重要，因為即使理念很好，差劣課程也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bilingual programmes that are properly put into practice.","zh":"這個短語描述被妥善實踐的雙語課程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"promote literacy","meaning":"促進讀寫能力","examples":[{"en":"Bilingual programmes can promote literacy in a minority language.","zh":"雙語課程可以促進少數語言的讀寫能力。"},{"en":"To promote literacy means to help people improve reading and writing ability.","zh":"promote literacy 指幫助人們提升閱讀和寫作能力。"},{"en":"Libraries promote literacy by giving children access to books and reading activities.","zh":"圖書館透過讓兒童接觸書本和閱讀活動來促進讀寫能力。"},{"en":"Promoting literacy in the mother tongue can strengthen children’s overall language development.","zh":"促進母語讀寫能力可以加強兒童整體語言發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes actions that build reading and writing skills.","zh":"這個短語描述建立閱讀和寫作技能的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"subject-matter knowledge","meaning":"學科知識","examples":[{"en":"Students can gain subject-matter knowledge through a minority language.","zh":"學生可以透過少數語言獲得學科知識。"},{"en":"Subject-matter knowledge is knowledge of school subjects such as science, history, mathematics, or geography.","zh":"subject-matter knowledge 指科學、歷史、數學或地理等學校科目的知識。"},{"en":"A child can learn subject-matter knowledge about plants in her home language before learning the English terms.","zh":"孩子可以先用家庭語言學習關於植物的學科知識，再學英文術語。"},{"en":"Understanding the concept matters even if the language later changes.","zh":"即使之後語言改變，理解概念才是重要的。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to knowledge of academic content.","zh":"這個短語指學術內容知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"minority language","meaning":"少數族裔語言；少數語言","examples":[{"en":"Students can learn subject content through a minority language.","zh":"學生可以透過少數語言學習學科內容。"},{"en":"A minority language is a language spoken by a smaller group within a wider society.","zh":"minority language 指在較大社會中由較小群體使用的語言。"},{"en":"In some cities, Urdu, Somali, or Polish may be minority languages in schools.","zh":"在有些城市，烏爾都語、索馬里語或波蘭語可能是學校中的少數語言。"},{"en":"Supporting a minority language can help children maintain family communication and identity.","zh":"支援少數語言可以幫助兒童維持家庭溝通和身份認同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a language used by a smaller community, not a less valuable language.","zh":"這個短語描述較小社群使用的語言，而不是較低價值的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"without any negative effects on","meaning":"對……沒有任何負面影響","examples":[{"en":"Bilingual programmes can support one language without any negative effects on another.","zh":"雙語課程可以支援一種語言，而對另一種語言沒有任何負面影響。"},{"en":"Without any negative effects on something means without harming or weakening it.","zh":"without any negative effects on something 指沒有傷害或削弱某事。"},{"en":"A student can learn music without any negative effects on her academic study if time is managed well.","zh":"如果時間管理得好，學生可以學音樂，而對學業沒有任何負面影響。"},{"en":"Research may show that mother-tongue teaching does not damage majority-language development.","zh":"研究可能顯示母語教學不會損害主流語言發展。"},{"en":"This phrase directly answers a fear about harmful side effects.","zh":"這個短語直接回應對有害副作用的憂慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"children’s development in","meaning":"兒童在……方面的發展","examples":[{"en":"Good bilingual programmes do not harm children’s development in the majority language.","zh":"良好的雙語課程不會傷害兒童在主流語言方面的發展。"},{"en":"Children’s development in something is children’s growth or progress in that skill or area.","zh":"children’s development in something 指兒童在某技能或範疇上的成長或進步。"},{"en":"Teachers may track children’s development in reading from year to year.","zh":"老師可能逐年追蹤兒童在閱讀方面的發展。"},{"en":"A good programme supports one area without slowing development in another.","zh":"良好課程會支援一個範疇，而不拖慢另一範疇的發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes progress in a specific part of learning.","zh":"這個短語描述學習某一部分的進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"within Europe","meaning":"在歐洲範圍內","examples":[{"en":"Within Europe, the Foyer programme illustrates the benefits of multilingual education.","zh":"在歐洲範圍內，Foyer 課程說明多語教育的好處。"},{"en":"Within Europe means inside European countries or across the European region.","zh":"within Europe 指在歐洲國家內或整個歐洲地區中。"},{"en":"Within Europe, schools may use very different approaches to migrant children’s languages.","zh":"在歐洲範圍內，學校可能對移民兒童語言採用非常不同的方法。"},{"en":"Examples within one region can show how policies differ even among neighbouring countries.","zh":"同一地區內的例子可以顯示即使是鄰近國家，政策也不同。"},{"en":"This phrase locates an example geographically.","zh":"這個短語以地理方式定位例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"speaking and literacy abilities","meaning":"說話和讀寫能力","examples":[{"en":"The Foyer programme develops children’s speaking and literacy abilities.","zh":"Foyer 課程發展兒童的說話和讀寫能力。"},{"en":"Speaking and literacy abilities are skills in oral communication, reading, and writing.","zh":"speaking and literacy abilities 指口語溝通、閱讀和寫作能力。"},{"en":"A child develops speaking abilities through conversation and literacy abilities through books and writing.","zh":"孩子透過對話發展說話能力，透過書本和寫作發展讀寫能力。"},{"en":"Programmes that support both can help children communicate in everyday and academic settings.","zh":"同時支援兩者的課程可以幫助孩子在日常和學術環境中溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both spoken language and written language skills.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋口語和書面語技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in three languages","meaning":"以三種語言","examples":[{"en":"Some programmes develop children’s abilities in three languages.","zh":"有些課程以三種語言發展兒童的能力。"},{"en":"In three languages means using or developing skills across three different languages.","zh":"in three languages 指跨三種不同語言使用或發展能力。"},{"en":"A child may learn to speak at home in one language and read at school in two others.","zh":"孩子可能在家用一種語言說話，並在學校以另外兩種語言閱讀。"},{"en":"Learning in three languages requires careful support so each language has a clear role.","zh":"以三種語言學習需要仔細支援，使每種語言都有清楚角色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trilingual language development.","zh":"這個短語描述三語發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"illustrate the benefits of","meaning":"說明……的好處","examples":[{"en":"The Foyer programme illustrates the benefits of bilingual education.","zh":"Foyer 課程說明雙語教育的好處。"},{"en":"To illustrate the benefits of something means to show clearly what good effects it can have.","zh":"illustrate the benefits of something 指清楚展示某事可以帶來甚麼良好效果。"},{"en":"A successful reading club can illustrate the benefits of giving children access to books.","zh":"成功的閱讀會可以說明讓兒童接觸書本的好處。"},{"en":"Real examples help people understand benefits more clearly than theory alone.","zh":"真實例子比單靠理論更能幫助人理解好處。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces evidence of positive results.","zh":"這個短語引入正面結果的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"bilingual and trilingual education","meaning":"雙語和三語教育","examples":[{"en":"The programme shows the benefits of bilingual and trilingual education.","zh":"該課程顯示雙語和三語教育的好處。"},{"en":"Bilingual and trilingual education uses two or three languages as part of teaching and learning.","zh":"bilingual and trilingual education 指把兩種或三種語言作為教學和學習一部分的教育。"},{"en":"A trilingual programme may help children learn through their home language, the national language, and an international language.","zh":"三語課程可能幫助兒童透過家庭語言、國家語言和國際語言學習。"},{"en":"These forms of education can support identity while expanding communication skills.","zh":"這些教育形式可以支援身份認同，同時擴展溝通能力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to education built around multiple languages.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞多種語言建立的教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"it is easy to understand how","meaning":"不難理解……如何發生","examples":[{"en":"It is easy to understand how language transfer happens.","zh":"不難理解語言轉移如何發生。"},{"en":"It is easy to understand how means the explanation is clear and not difficult to follow.","zh":"it is easy to understand how 指解釋清楚，不難跟上。"},{"en":"It is easy to understand how practice improves pronunciation when students repeat sounds every day.","zh":"當學生每天重複聲音，不難理解練習如何改善發音。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces a simple explanation after a complex idea.","zh":"這個短語常在複雜想法後引入簡單解釋。"},{"en":"It helps make an argument feel logical and accessible.","zh":"它幫助令論點感覺合乎邏輯且容易理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"learn through","meaning":"透過……學習","examples":[{"en":"Children can learn through a minority language.","zh":"兒童可以透過少數語言學習。"},{"en":"To learn through a language means to use that language as the medium for understanding subject content.","zh":"learn through a language 指使用該語言作為理解學科內容的媒介。"},{"en":"A child may learn science through Spanish before learning the same terms in English.","zh":"孩子可能先透過西班牙語學習科學，再學同一概念的英語術語。"},{"en":"Learning through a familiar language can make new concepts easier to grasp.","zh":"透過熟悉語言學習可以令新概念較容易掌握。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the language used as the teaching channel.","zh":"這個短語描述用作教學渠道的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"learn concepts and intellectual skills","meaning":"學習概念和智力技能","examples":[{"en":"Children learn concepts and intellectual skills through their mother tongue.","zh":"兒童透過母語學習概念和智力技能。"},{"en":"To learn concepts and intellectual skills means to understand ideas and develop thinking abilities.","zh":"learn concepts and intellectual skills 指理解想法並發展思考能力。"},{"en":"Children learn concepts like time, size, and cause before they learn all the school-language words for them.","zh":"兒童在學會所有學校語言詞彙前，已學習時間、大小和因果等概念。"},{"en":"Once a child understands a concept, only the label may need to change in another language.","zh":"一旦孩子理解概念，在另一種語言中可能只需要改變標籤。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to learning ideas and thinking tools, not only vocabulary.","zh":"這個短語指學習想法和思考工具，而不只是詞彙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"tell the time","meaning":"看懂時間；說出時間","examples":[{"en":"Pupils who can tell the time in one language understand the concept.","zh":"能用一種語言說出時間的學生，已理解該概念。"},{"en":"To tell the time means to read a clock and say what time it is.","zh":"tell the time 指看懂時鐘並說出現在是甚麼時間。"},{"en":"A child can tell the time when she says, “It is half past three.”","zh":"當孩子說「現在是三點半」時，她就是能說出時間。"},{"en":"Once children understand clocks, they do not need to relearn the whole idea in another language.","zh":"一旦兒童理解時鐘，他們不需要在另一種語言中重新學整個概念。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to understanding and saying clock time.","zh":"這個短語指理解並說出時鐘時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"understand the concept of","meaning":"理解……的概念","examples":[{"en":"Pupils understand the concept of telling the time.","zh":"學生理解說出時間的概念。"},{"en":"To understand the concept of something means to grasp the idea behind it, not just memorise words.","zh":"understand the concept of something 指掌握某事背後的想法，而不只是背誦詞語。"},{"en":"A student understands the concept of division when she can share objects equally.","zh":"當學生能把物件平均分配，她就理解除法的概念。"},{"en":"Understanding a concept in one language can help when learning another language’s terms.","zh":"在一種語言中理解概念，可以幫助學習另一種語言的術語。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on idea-level understanding.","zh":"這個短語著重概念層面的理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in order to","meaning":"為了","examples":[{"en":"In order to tell the time in another language, pupils do not need to relearn the concept.","zh":"為了用另一種語言說出時間，學生不需要重新學習該概念。"},{"en":"In order to means for the purpose of doing something.","zh":"in order to 指為了做某事。"},{"en":"Students practise examples in order to use new phrases naturally.","zh":"學生練習例句，是為了自然地使用新短語。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly connects an action with its purpose.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接行動與目的。"},{"en":"It is common in formal explanation and exam writing.","zh":"它常見於正式解釋和考試寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"relearn the concept","meaning":"重新學習概念","examples":[{"en":"Children do not need to relearn the concept in the majority language.","zh":"兒童不需要用主流語言重新學習該概念。"},{"en":"To relearn the concept means to learn the same idea again from the beginning.","zh":"relearn the concept 指從頭再次學習同一個想法。"},{"en":"A child who already understands subtraction does not need to relearn the concept when the lesson uses English words.","zh":"已理解減法的孩子，在課堂使用英文詞語時，不需要重新學習概念。"},{"en":"If concepts transfer, students only need new language labels, not new thinking.","zh":"如果概念可以轉移，學生只需要新的語言標籤，而不是新的思考。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning an already understood idea again.","zh":"這個短語描述再次學習已理解的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"similarly","meaning":"同樣地","examples":[{"en":"Similarly, other skills can transfer across languages.","zh":"同樣地，其他技能可以在不同語言之間轉移。"},{"en":"Similarly means in a similar way or for a similar reason.","zh":"similarly 指以相似方式或基於相似原因。"},{"en":"A child can use reading strategies in Chinese; similarly, she can apply them in English.","zh":"孩子可以在中文中使用閱讀策略；同樣地，她可以在英文中應用它們。"},{"en":"This word connects two ideas that follow the same pattern.","zh":"這個詞連接兩個遵循同一模式的想法。"},{"en":"It is useful when adding another example of the same principle.","zh":"它適合用於加入同一原則的另一個例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at more advanced stages","meaning":"在較高階段","examples":[{"en":"At more advanced stages, reading skills can transfer across languages.","zh":"在較高階段，閱讀技能可以在不同語言之間轉移。"},{"en":"At more advanced stages means at later or higher levels of learning or development.","zh":"at more advanced stages 指在學習或發展的較後期或較高水平。"},{"en":"At more advanced stages, students can analyse tone, evidence, and argument structure.","zh":"在較高階段，學生可以分析語氣、證據和論點結構。"},{"en":"Advanced stages often involve abstract thinking rather than simple recognition.","zh":"較高階段通常涉及抽象思考，而不是簡單辨認。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a higher level in a learning process.","zh":"這個短語描述學習過程中的較高水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"distinguish the main idea from","meaning":"區分主要意思和……","examples":[{"en":"Students learn to distinguish the main idea from supporting details.","zh":"學生學會區分主要意思和支持細節。"},{"en":"To distinguish the main idea from something means to tell the central message apart from less central information.","zh":"distinguish the main idea from something 指把中心訊息與較次要資料分辨開來。"},{"en":"In a reading passage, students distinguish the main idea from examples, dates, and minor facts.","zh":"在閱讀文章中，學生會把主旨與例子、日期和次要事實區分開。"},{"en":"This skill helps readers avoid treating every sentence as equally important.","zh":"這項技能幫助讀者避免把每句句子都視為同等重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes separating the central point from supporting information.","zh":"這個短語描述把中心重點與支援資料分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"supporting details","meaning":"支持細節","examples":[{"en":"Good readers identify the main idea and supporting details.","zh":"良好讀者會識別主要意思和支持細節。"},{"en":"Supporting details are examples, facts, reasons, or explanations that help prove or explain the main idea.","zh":"supporting details 指幫助證明或解釋主旨的例子、事實、原因或解釋。"},{"en":"In an essay, supporting details may include statistics, stories, and expert comments.","zh":"在作文中，支持細節可能包括統計、故事和專家評論。"},{"en":"Without supporting details, a main idea can sound empty or unconvincing.","zh":"沒有支持細節，主旨可能顯得空泛或缺乏說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to information that backs up a central point.","zh":"這個短語指支持中心觀點的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a written passage","meaning":"一篇文章","examples":[{"en":"Students analyse the main idea of a written passage.","zh":"學生分析一篇文章的主旨。"},{"en":"A written passage is a section of text, usually used for reading, study, or examination.","zh":"written passage 指一段文字，通常用於閱讀、學習或考試。"},{"en":"A written passage may be an article, story, report, or textbook extract.","zh":"一篇文章可以是文章、故事、報告或教科書摘錄。"},{"en":"Understanding a written passage requires reading both the main idea and details.","zh":"理解一篇文章需要閱讀主旨和細節。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a piece of written text.","zh":"這個短語指一段書面文本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"distinguish fact from opinion","meaning":"區分事實與意見","examples":[{"en":"Students learn to distinguish fact from opinion.","zh":"學生學會區分事實與意見。"},{"en":"To distinguish fact from opinion means to tell proven information apart from personal belief or judgement.","zh":"distinguish fact from opinion 指把已證實資料與個人信念或判斷分辨開來。"},{"en":"“The school starts at eight” is a fact, while “the school starts too early” is an opinion.","zh":"「學校八點開始」是事實，而「學校開始得太早」是意見。"},{"en":"This skill helps students read arguments more critically.","zh":"這項技能幫助學生更批判地閱讀論點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes separating objective information from subjective views.","zh":"這個短語描述把客觀資料與主觀看法分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"secondary school pupils","meaning":"中學生","examples":[{"en":"Studies of secondary school pupils provide interesting findings.","zh":"關於中學生的研究提供有趣的研究結果。"},{"en":"Secondary school pupils are students who attend school after primary school, usually during the teenage years.","zh":"secondary school pupils 指小學後就讀學校的學生，通常處於青少年階段。"},{"en":"Secondary school pupils may face more academic language demands than younger children.","zh":"中學生可能面對比年幼兒童更高的學術語言要求。"},{"en":"Their reading strategies can show whether skills transfer across languages.","zh":"他們的閱讀策略可以顯示技能是否在語言之間轉移。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to students in the middle or high school stage.","zh":"這個短語指中學階段的學生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"provide interesting findings","meaning":"提供有趣的研究結果","examples":[{"en":"Studies of secondary school pupils provide interesting findings.","zh":"關於中學生的研究提供有趣的研究結果。"},{"en":"To provide interesting findings means to offer results that are useful, surprising, or worth examining.","zh":"provide interesting findings 指提供有用、令人意外或值得檢視的結果。"},{"en":"A school survey may provide interesting findings about why students avoid reading.","zh":"學校調查可能提供關於學生為何避免閱讀的有趣研究結果。"},{"en":"Interesting findings can lead to new questions and better teaching decisions.","zh":"有趣的研究結果可以帶來新問題和更好的教學決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research results that deserve attention.","zh":"這個短語描述值得注意的研究結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in this area","meaning":"在這方面","examples":[{"en":"More research is needed in this area.","zh":"在這方面需要更多研究。"},{"en":"In this area means in this subject, field, or part of a topic.","zh":"in this area 指在這個主題、領域或議題部分中。"},{"en":"More research is needed in this area if schools want to understand language loss better.","zh":"如果學校想更了解語言流失，在這方面需要更多研究。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a specific topic that still needs study.","zh":"這個短語指出仍需要研究的特定主題。"},{"en":"It is often used when discussing gaps in knowledge.","zh":"它常用於討論知識空白。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be worth extending","meaning":"值得擴展","examples":[{"en":"This research would be worth extending.","zh":"這項研究值得擴展。"},{"en":"To be worth extending means to deserve being continued, expanded, or developed further.","zh":"be worth extending 指值得繼續、擴大或進一步發展。"},{"en":"A small study on homework stress may be worth extending to more schools.","zh":"一項關於功課壓力的小型研究可能值得擴展至更多學校。"},{"en":"Extending research can test whether the same findings appear in other groups.","zh":"擴展研究可以測試相同結果是否出現在其他群體中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research or work that should be taken further.","zh":"這個短語描述應進一步推展的研究或工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"many people marvel at","meaning":"很多人驚訝於……","examples":[{"en":"Many people marvel at how quickly bilingual children learn conversational skills.","zh":"很多人驚訝於雙語兒童學會日常會話能力的速度。"},{"en":"To marvel at something means to feel surprised and impressed by it.","zh":"marvel at something 指對某事感到驚訝和讚嘆。"},{"en":"Parents may marvel at how fast children copy new songs and phrases.","zh":"父母可能驚訝於孩子多快模仿新歌曲和短語。"},{"en":"People often marvel at quick progress while overlooking slower academic development.","zh":"人們常驚訝於快速進步，卻忽略較慢的學術發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes surprised admiration.","zh":"這個短語描述帶有欣賞的驚訝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"pick up","meaning":"學會；掌握","examples":[{"en":"Bilingual children often pick up conversational skills quickly.","zh":"雙語兒童常迅速學會日常會話能力。"},{"en":"To pick up a skill means to learn it naturally or without long formal instruction.","zh":"pick up a skill 指自然地或不經長期正式教學而學會某技能。"},{"en":"Children may pick up new slang from classmates after only a few weeks.","zh":"孩子可能只用幾星期便從同學那裡學會新俚語。"},{"en":"People can pick up everyday speech faster than academic language.","zh":"人們可以比學術語言更快掌握日常說話。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning something informally or gradually.","zh":"這個短語描述非正式或逐步學會某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"conversational skills","meaning":"日常會話能力","examples":[{"en":"Bilingual children may acquire conversational skills quickly.","zh":"雙語兒童可能迅速獲得日常會話能力。"},{"en":"Conversational skills are the ability to speak, listen, respond, and keep everyday communication going.","zh":"conversational skills 指說話、聆聽、回應並維持日常溝通的能力。"},{"en":"A child uses conversational skills when chatting with classmates during lunch.","zh":"孩子午飯時與同學聊天，就是在使用日常會話能力。"},{"en":"These skills may develop faster than the language needed for textbooks and essays.","zh":"這些能力可能比教科書和作文所需語言更快發展。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to everyday speaking ability.","zh":"這個短語指日常口語能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the majority language at school","meaning":"在學校使用的主流語言","examples":[{"en":"Children often learn the majority language at school.","zh":"兒童常在學校學習主流語言。"},{"en":"The majority language at school is the dominant language used for lessons, classmates, and school routines.","zh":"majority language at school 指用於課堂、同學交流和學校常規的主要語言。"},{"en":"A child may speak Turkish at home but learn the majority language at school every day.","zh":"孩子可能在家說土耳其語，但每天在學校學習主流語言。"},{"en":"School exposure can build everyday speaking skills in the majority language quickly.","zh":"學校接觸可以迅速建立主流語言的日常說話能力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the main school language children encounter.","zh":"這個短語指兒童在學校接觸到的主要語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"take much longer for someone to","meaning":"某人需要更長時間去……","examples":[{"en":"It takes much longer for children to develop academic language skills.","zh":"兒童需要更長時間去發展學術語言能力。"},{"en":"It takes much longer for someone to do something means that person needs far more time to achieve it.","zh":"it takes much longer for someone to do something 指某人需要多得多時間才能做到某事。"},{"en":"It takes much longer for students to write strong essays than to answer simple questions.","zh":"學生需要更長時間去寫出有力作文，而不是回答簡單問題。"},{"en":"Some skills develop slowly because they require vocabulary, thinking, and practice.","zh":"有些技能發展緩慢，因為它們需要詞彙、思考和練習。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that a process is not quick.","zh":"這個短語強調過程並不快速。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"catch up with","meaning":"追上……","examples":[{"en":"Bilingual children may need time to catch up with native speakers.","zh":"雙語兒童可能需要時間追上母語人士。"},{"en":"To catch up with someone means to reach the same level after being behind.","zh":"catch up with someone 指在落後後達到相同水平。"},{"en":"A student who missed two weeks of school may need extra help to catch up with classmates.","zh":"缺課兩星期的學生可能需要額外幫助來追上同學。"},{"en":"Catching up takes time when the gap involves academic language, not only daily speech.","zh":"當差距涉及學術語言而不只是日常說話，追上需要時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes closing a gap in progress or ability.","zh":"這個短語描述縮小進度或能力差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"native speakers","meaning":"母語人士","examples":[{"en":"Children may take years to catch up with native speakers academically.","zh":"兒童可能需要多年才在學術上追上母語人士。"},{"en":"Native speakers are people who have spoken a language from early childhood as their first language.","zh":"native speakers 指從幼年起把某語言作為第一語言使用的人。"},{"en":"A child learning English at school may compare herself with native speakers in the same class.","zh":"在學校學英語的孩子可能把自己與同班母語人士比較。"},{"en":"Native speakers usually have a larger everyday vocabulary because of years of exposure.","zh":"母語人士通常因多年接觸而有較大日常詞彙量。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to first-language users of a language.","zh":"這個短語指某語言的第一語言使用者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"academic language skills","meaning":"學術語言能力","examples":[{"en":"Academic language skills take longer to develop than conversational skills.","zh":"學術語言能力比日常會話能力需要更長時間發展。"},{"en":"Academic language skills are the reading, writing, speaking, and thinking skills needed for school subjects.","zh":"academic language skills 指學校科目所需的閱讀、寫作、說話和思考語言能力。"},{"en":"Explaining a science experiment requires more academic language skills than chatting with friends.","zh":"解釋科學實驗比與朋友聊天需要更多學術語言能力。"},{"en":"These skills take time because they involve abstract vocabulary and complex sentences.","zh":"這些能力需要時間，因為它們涉及抽象詞彙和複雜句子。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to language needed for learning and study.","zh":"這個短語指學習和研習所需語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be much less aware of","meaning":"對……認識少得多","examples":[{"en":"Educators are often much less aware of mother-tongue loss.","zh":"教育工作者對母語流失的認識常少得多。"},{"en":"To be much less aware of something means to know or notice it far less clearly.","zh":"be much less aware of something 指對某事知道或注意得遠遠較少。"},{"en":"Parents may be much less aware of online bullying if children do not talk about it.","zh":"如果孩子不談網上欺凌，家長可能對它認識少得多。"},{"en":"If teachers are less aware of language loss, they may not act until the problem is serious.","zh":"如果老師較少意識到語言流失，可能到問題嚴重才行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lack of attention or understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏關注或理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lose their ability to","meaning":"失去……的能力","examples":[{"en":"Children can quickly lose their ability to use their mother tongue.","zh":"兒童可能迅速失去使用母語的能力。"},{"en":"To lose their ability to do something means to no longer be able to do it well.","zh":"lose their ability to do something 指不再能好好做某事。"},{"en":"A child may lose her ability to write Chinese if she stops using it for many years.","zh":"如果孩子多年停止使用中文，她可能失去寫中文的能力。"},{"en":"Language ability can weaken when children stop practising it daily.","zh":"當孩子停止日常練習語言，語言能力可能削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a skill becoming weaker or disappearing.","zh":"這個短語描述技能變弱或消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the home context","meaning":"家庭環境","examples":[{"en":"Some children stop using their mother tongue even in the home context.","zh":"有些兒童即使在家庭環境中也停止使用母語。"},{"en":"The home context is the family setting where children live, speak, and interact with relatives.","zh":"home context 指兒童生活、說話和與親人互動的家庭環境。"},{"en":"A child may behave differently in the home context than in the classroom.","zh":"孩子在家庭環境中的表現可能不同於課室。"},{"en":"If the mother tongue disappears even at home, family communication may weaken.","zh":"如果母語甚至在家中也消失，家庭溝通可能削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the situation and environment of family life.","zh":"這個短語指家庭生活的情況和環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the extent and rapidity of","meaning":"……的程度和速度","examples":[{"en":"The extent and rapidity of language loss vary between communities.","zh":"語言流失的程度和速度在社群之間有所不同。"},{"en":"The extent and rapidity of something mean how much it happens and how quickly it happens.","zh":"extent and rapidity of something 指某事發生的程度以及速度。"},{"en":"Teachers may study the extent and rapidity of reading decline after a long holiday.","zh":"老師可能研究長假後閱讀能力下降的程度和速度。"},{"en":"A problem can be serious because it spreads widely, quickly, or both.","zh":"一個問題可能因為範圍廣、速度快，或兩者兼有而嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase measures both size and speed.","zh":"這個短語同時量度規模和速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"language loss","meaning":"語言流失","examples":[{"en":"Language loss can happen quickly after children start school.","zh":"兒童開始上學後，語言流失可能很快發生。"},{"en":"Language loss is the weakening or disappearance of a person’s ability to use a language.","zh":"language loss 指一個人使用某語言的能力削弱或消失。"},{"en":"A child may experience language loss if she stops speaking her home language after entering school.","zh":"如果孩子入學後停止說家庭語言，她可能經歷語言流失。"},{"en":"Language loss can reduce communication with grandparents and weaken cultural connection.","zh":"語言流失可以減少與祖父母的溝通，並削弱文化連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes losing active ability in a language.","zh":"這個短語描述失去一種語言的主動能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"vary according to","meaning":"根據……而有所不同","examples":[{"en":"Language loss varies according to the concentration of families in a neighbourhood.","zh":"語言流失根據鄰近地區家庭的集中程度而有所不同。"},{"en":"To vary according to something means to change depending on that factor.","zh":"vary according to something 指隨某因素而改變。"},{"en":"Students’ travel time varies according to where they live.","zh":"學生上學交通時間根據他們住在哪裡而有所不同。"},{"en":"If language use varies according to neighbourhood, community support matters.","zh":"如果語言使用根據鄰近社區而不同，社區支援就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what a difference depends on.","zh":"這個短語解釋差異取決於甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the concentration of families","meaning":"家庭的集中程度","examples":[{"en":"The concentration of families from the same linguistic group affects language loss.","zh":"來自同一語言群體的家庭集中程度會影響語言流失。"},{"en":"The concentration of families means how many similar families live close together in one area.","zh":"concentration of families 指相似家庭有多少聚居在同一地區。"},{"en":"A high concentration of families from the same language group can help children keep using that language.","zh":"同一語言群體家庭高度集中，可以幫助兒童繼續使用該語言。"},{"en":"When families are scattered, children may have fewer chances to use their mother tongue outside home.","zh":"當家庭分散，兒童在家外使用母語的機會可能較少。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to how densely a group is located in a neighbourhood.","zh":"這個短語指一個群體在社區中聚居的密度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a particular linguistic group","meaning":"特定語言群體","examples":[{"en":"Children may belong to a particular linguistic group.","zh":"兒童可能屬於某個特定語言群體。"},{"en":"A particular linguistic group is a specific community of people who share a language.","zh":"particular linguistic group 指共享某種語言的特定社群。"},{"en":"Cantonese-speaking families in a city may form a particular linguistic group.","zh":"城市中的廣東話家庭可能形成一個特定語言群體。"},{"en":"Children from the same linguistic group can support one another’s language use.","zh":"來自同一語言群體的兒童可以互相支持語言使用。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific language community.","zh":"這個短語識別某一特定語言社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in the neighbourhood","meaning":"在社區內；在鄰近地區","examples":[{"en":"Language use depends partly on the community in the neighbourhood.","zh":"語言使用部分取決於鄰近地區中的社群。"},{"en":"In the neighbourhood means in the local area where people live near one another.","zh":"in the neighbourhood 指在人們彼此住得近的本地區域中。"},{"en":"Children may hear their mother tongue in the neighbourhood if many families speak it nearby.","zh":"如果附近有許多家庭說同一語言，兒童可能在社區內聽到母語。"},{"en":"A supportive neighbourhood gives children more chances to use their home language.","zh":"有支援的社區給兒童更多機會使用家庭語言。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the surrounding local community.","zh":"這個短語指周圍的本地社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be used extensively","meaning":"被廣泛使用","examples":[{"en":"The mother tongue may be used extensively in the community.","zh":"母語可能在社區中被廣泛使用。"},{"en":"To be used extensively means to be used widely, often, and in many situations.","zh":"be used extensively 指在許多情況中廣泛而頻繁地使用。"},{"en":"A language is used extensively when shops, neighbours, families, and community centres all use it.","zh":"當商店、鄰居、家庭和社區中心都使用某語言，它就是被廣泛使用。"},{"en":"Extensive use helps children keep the language active and natural.","zh":"廣泛使用幫助兒童保持該語言活躍而自然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad and frequent use.","zh":"這個短語描述範圍廣且頻密的使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in the community","meaning":"在社區中","examples":[{"en":"Children retain their mother tongue more easily when it is used in the community.","zh":"當母語在社區中被使用，兒童較容易保留母語。"},{"en":"In the community means among people living or interacting in the same local area or social group.","zh":"in the community 指在同一本地區域或社會群體中生活或互動的人之間。"},{"en":"Children may practise their home language in the community at shops, festivals, or religious centres.","zh":"兒童可能在商店、節日或宗教中心於社區中練習家庭語言。"},{"en":"Community use gives children more real reasons to keep speaking the language.","zh":"社區使用給孩子更多真正理由繼續說該語言。"},{"en":"This phrase places language use beyond the home and school.","zh":"這個短語把語言使用放在家庭和學校以外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"not concentrated in","meaning":"並不集中於……","examples":[{"en":"Some language communities are not concentrated in particular neighbourhoods.","zh":"有些語言社群並不集中於特定鄰近地區。"},{"en":"Not concentrated in means not gathered closely together in one area.","zh":"not concentrated in 指沒有緊密聚集在某一地區。"},{"en":"If families are not concentrated in one district, children may rarely meet peers who speak the same language.","zh":"如果家庭並不集中於同一區，兒童可能很少遇到說同一語言的同輩。"},{"en":"Scattered communities may find it harder to maintain language use.","zh":"分散社群可能較難維持語言使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a group being spread out rather than clustered.","zh":"這個短語描述群體分散，而不是聚集。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"communicate in","meaning":"以……溝通","examples":[{"en":"Children may lose their ability to communicate in their mother tongue.","zh":"兒童可能失去以母語溝通的能力。"},{"en":"To communicate in a language means to use that language to speak, listen, read, or write with others.","zh":"communicate in a language 指使用該語言與他人說、聽、讀或寫。"},{"en":"A child may communicate in English at school but in Arabic with grandparents.","zh":"孩子可能在學校以英語溝通，但與祖父母以阿拉伯語溝通。"},{"en":"If children stop communicating in their mother tongue, family relationships may become harder.","zh":"如果兒童停止以母語溝通，家庭關係可能變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using a language for interaction.","zh":"這個短語描述使用某語言互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"within two to three years of","meaning":"在……後兩至三年內","examples":[{"en":"Children may lose their mother tongue within two to three years of starting school.","zh":"兒童可能在開始上學後兩至三年內失去母語。"},{"en":"Within two to three years of something means before two or three years have passed after that event.","zh":"within two to three years of something 指在某事件後未超過兩三年的時間內。"},{"en":"Some students become fluent in daily school language within two to three years of arrival.","zh":"有些學生在抵達後兩至三年內，日常學校語言變得流利。"},{"en":"Rapid language change can surprise families because it happens within only a few years.","zh":"快速語言變化會令家庭驚訝，因為它只在幾年內發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a time limit after a starting point.","zh":"這個短語描述某起點後的時間限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"retain receptive skills","meaning":"保留理解能力","examples":[{"en":"Children may retain receptive skills in their mother tongue.","zh":"兒童可能保留母語的理解能力。"},{"en":"To retain receptive skills means to keep the ability to understand a language when listening or reading.","zh":"retain receptive skills 指保留聆聽或閱讀時理解某語言的能力。"},{"en":"A child may understand grandparents’ speech but answer in the school language.","zh":"孩子可能聽得懂祖父母說話，但用學校語言回答。"},{"en":"Receptive skills can remain even after active speaking ability becomes weaker.","zh":"即使主動說話能力變弱，理解能力仍可能保留。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping understanding ability, not necessarily speaking ability.","zh":"這個短語描述保留理解能力，不一定是說話能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"use the majority language in speaking with","meaning":"與……說話時使用主流語言","examples":[{"en":"Children may use the majority language in speaking with their peers.","zh":"兒童可能與同輩說話時使用主流語言。"},{"en":"To use the majority language in speaking with someone means to talk to that person in the dominant social or school language.","zh":"use the majority language in speaking with someone 指與某人交談時使用社會或學校中的主導語言。"},{"en":"A child may use English in speaking with classmates but use Polish at home.","zh":"孩子可能與同學說話時使用英語，但在家使用波蘭語。"},{"en":"Peer pressure can make children switch to the majority language even outside lessons.","zh":"朋輩壓力可以令孩子即使在課堂外也轉用主流語言。"},{"en":"This phrase describes language choice in conversation.","zh":"這個短語描述對話中的語言選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"peers and siblings","meaning":"同輩和兄弟姊妹","examples":[{"en":"Children may use the majority language with peers and siblings.","zh":"兒童可能與同輩和兄弟姊妹使用主流語言。"},{"en":"Peers and siblings are children of similar age and brothers or sisters in the family.","zh":"peers and siblings 指年齡相近的同伴，以及家庭中的兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"A child may speak one language with parents but another with peers and siblings.","zh":"孩子可能與父母說一種語言，但與同輩和兄弟姊妹說另一種語言。"},{"en":"Language used with peers and siblings can influence which language feels natural.","zh":"與同輩和兄弟姊妹使用的語言，可以影響哪種語言感覺自然。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to friends of similar age and brothers or sisters.","zh":"這個短語指年齡相近的朋友和兄弟姊妹。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"respond to their parents","meaning":"回應父母","examples":[{"en":"Some children use the majority language when responding to their parents.","zh":"有些兒童在回應父母時使用主流語言。"},{"en":"To respond to their parents means to answer or react to what their parents say.","zh":"respond to their parents 指回答或回應父母所說的話。"},{"en":"A child may understand her mother’s question in Cantonese but respond to her parents in English.","zh":"孩子可能聽懂母親用廣東話提出的問題，但用英文回應父母。"},{"en":"This pattern can show that receptive ability remains while active speaking changes.","zh":"這種模式可以顯示理解能力仍在，但主動說話改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a child’s reply or reaction to parents.","zh":"這個短語描述孩子對父母的回答或反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"by the time","meaning":"到……的時候","examples":[{"en":"By the time children become adolescents, the language gap may be serious.","zh":"到兒童成為青少年時，語言差距可能已很嚴重。"},{"en":"By the time means when a certain later point is reached.","zh":"by the time 指到達某個較後時間點時。"},{"en":"By the time students reach secondary school, weak reading habits may already affect several subjects.","zh":"到學生升上中學時，薄弱閱讀習慣可能已影響幾個科目。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows that a change has happened before a later stage arrives.","zh":"這個短語常顯示變化在較後階段到來前已經發生。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing development over time.","zh":"它適合描述隨時間出現的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"become adolescents","meaning":"成為青少年","examples":[{"en":"Children may lose their mother tongue by the time they become adolescents.","zh":"兒童到成為青少年時，可能已失去母語。"},{"en":"To become adolescents means to enter the teenage stage between childhood and adulthood.","zh":"become adolescents 指進入兒童期與成年期之間的青少年階段。"},{"en":"Children become adolescents when they begin secondary school and face new social pressures.","zh":"兒童升上中學並面對新社交壓力時，就成為青少年。"},{"en":"Language habits formed earlier may become harder to change during adolescence.","zh":"早期形成的語言習慣在青春期可能較難改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to growing into the teenage years.","zh":"這個短語指成長至青少年時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"linguistic division","meaning":"語言隔閡","examples":[{"en":"A linguistic division can develop between parents and children.","zh":"父母與子女之間可能形成語言隔閡。"},{"en":"A linguistic division is a language gap that makes communication harder between groups or people.","zh":"linguistic division 指令群體或人之間溝通更困難的語言差距。"},{"en":"A family may experience a linguistic division when children answer in English but parents prefer their mother tongue.","zh":"當孩子用英文回答，而父母較喜歡母語，家庭可能經歷語言隔閡。"},{"en":"Language gaps can create emotional distance as well as practical misunderstanding.","zh":"語言差距可以造成情感距離，也可以造成實際誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes separation caused by language difference.","zh":"這個短語描述由語言差異造成的分隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"emotional chasm","meaning":"情感鴻溝","examples":[{"en":"The linguistic division may become an emotional chasm.","zh":"語言隔閡可能變成情感鴻溝。"},{"en":"An emotional chasm is a deep emotional gap between people.","zh":"emotional chasm 指人與人之間深深的情感距離。"},{"en":"A teenager may feel an emotional chasm from parents if they cannot discuss feelings in the same language.","zh":"如果青少年不能用同一語言與父母談感受，可能感到與父母之間有情感鴻溝。"},{"en":"Language loss can turn practical communication problems into family distance.","zh":"語言流失可以把實際溝通問題變成家庭距離。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious emotional separation.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重的情感分隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"become alienated from","meaning":"與……疏離","examples":[{"en":"Some pupils become alienated from the cultures of both home and school.","zh":"有些學生與家庭和學校兩方面的文化變得疏離。"},{"en":"To become alienated from something means to feel disconnected, distant, or no longer belonging to it.","zh":"become alienated from something 指感到與某事斷開、疏遠或不再屬於它。"},{"en":"A student may become alienated from school if teachers never recognise her background.","zh":"如果老師從不承認學生背景，學生可能與學校疏離。"},{"en":"Losing connection with both home and school can damage identity and confidence.","zh":"與家庭和學校都失去連繫，可以傷害身份認同和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social or emotional disconnection.","zh":"這個短語描述社交或情感上的疏離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the cultures of both home and school","meaning":"家庭和學校兩方面的文化","examples":[{"en":"Some adolescents feel disconnected from the cultures of both home and school.","zh":"有些青少年感到與家庭和學校兩方面的文化脫節。"},{"en":"The cultures of both home and school are the values, languages, habits, and expectations in family life and school life.","zh":"cultures of both home and school 指家庭生活和學校生活中的價值、語言、習慣和期望。"},{"en":"A child may feel caught between home culture and school culture if the two are never connected.","zh":"如果家庭文化和學校文化從不連接，孩子可能感到夾在兩者之間。"},{"en":"When neither culture feels fully welcoming, young people may feel lost.","zh":"當兩種文化都不令人完全感到被接納，年輕人可能感到迷失。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the two main cultural worlds children live in.","zh":"這個短語比較兒童生活中的兩個主要文化世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"predictable results","meaning":"可預見的結果","examples":[{"en":"Alienation can lead to predictable results.","zh":"疏離可以導致可預見的結果。"},{"en":"Predictable results are outcomes that can be expected because the causes are clear.","zh":"predictable results 指因為成因清楚而可以預期的結果。"},{"en":"If students feel ignored for years, low motivation is a predictable result.","zh":"如果學生多年感到被忽視，低動機就是可預見的結果。"},{"en":"When language loss creates family distance, emotional problems may follow.","zh":"當語言流失造成家庭距離，情緒問題可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes results that are not surprising.","zh":"這個短語描述並不令人意外的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"考生應為每題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option labelled with the right letter.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選出以正確字母標示的答案選項。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice question, candidates choose A, B, C, or D after reading carefully.","zh":"在多項選擇題中，考生仔細閱讀後選擇 A、B、C 或 D。"},{"en":"Choosing the correct letter requires matching the option with the passage, not just guessing.","zh":"選出正確字母需要把選項與文章配對，而不只是猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common examination instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"write the correct letter in boxes","meaning":"把正確字母填寫在方格內","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the correct letter in boxes on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生把正確字母填寫在答題紙的方格內。"},{"en":"To write the correct letter in boxes means to put the chosen answer letter into the numbered spaces provided.","zh":"write the correct letter in boxes 指把所選答案字母寫入提供的編號空格。"},{"en":"Candidates must write the correct letter in boxes clearly so markers can read it.","zh":"考生必須清楚地把正確字母填寫在方格內，讓評卷員能讀懂。"},{"en":"Writing in the wrong box can make a correct answer appear incorrect.","zh":"寫錯方格可以令正確答案看似錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how to record answers in an exam.","zh":"這個短語描述考試中如何記錄答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"make a point","meaning":"提出觀點","examples":[{"en":"The writer makes a point about the value of mother tongues.","zh":"作者提出關於母語價值的觀點。"},{"en":"To make a point means to express an important idea or argument.","zh":"make a point 指表達重要想法或論點。"},{"en":"A teacher may make a point about why examples matter in vocabulary learning.","zh":"老師可能提出例子為何對詞彙學習重要的觀點。"},{"en":"Writers make points to guide readers toward a particular understanding.","zh":"作者提出觀點，引導讀者走向某種理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes presenting a meaningful argument.","zh":"這個短語描述提出有意義的論點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"current studies","meaning":"近期研究","examples":[{"en":"Some answer options refer to current studies on children’s mother tongues.","zh":"有些答案選項提及關於兒童母語的近期研究。"},{"en":"Current studies are recent or present-day research works on a topic.","zh":"current studies 指關於某主題的近期或當代研究。"},{"en":"Current studies on bilingual education may examine children in multilingual classrooms today.","zh":"關於雙語教育的近期研究可能檢視今天多語課室中的兒童。"},{"en":"Current studies can update older assumptions when social conditions change.","zh":"當社會情況改變，近期研究可以更新舊假設。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to research that is modern or recently available.","zh":"這個短語指現代或最近可得的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be misleading","meaning":"具誤導性","examples":[{"en":"Some current studies may be misleading if they are interpreted wrongly.","zh":"如果被錯誤解讀，有些近期研究可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"To be misleading means to give a false or wrong impression.","zh":"be misleading 指給人錯誤或不真實的印象。"},{"en":"A high test score may be misleading if the test was too easy.","zh":"如果測驗太容易，高分可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"Misleading information can lead people to make poor decisions.","zh":"具誤導性的資料可以令人作出差劣決定。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that something may seem to show one thing but actually mean another.","zh":"這個短語提醒某事看似顯示一件事，但實際可能是另一回事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"culturally rich education programme","meaning":"文化豐富的教育課程","examples":[{"en":"A culturally rich education programme can support diverse learners.","zh":"文化豐富的教育課程可以支援多元學習者。"},{"en":"A culturally rich education programme includes different languages, histories, stories, traditions, and identities in learning.","zh":"culturally rich education programme 指在學習中包括不同語言、歷史、故事、傳統和身份的課程。"},{"en":"A school creates a culturally rich programme when students read stories from many communities.","zh":"當學生閱讀來自許多社群的故事，學校就在創造文化豐富的課程。"},{"en":"Such a programme can help children feel represented and respected.","zh":"這類課程可以幫助孩子感到被代表和被尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes education that values cultural variety.","zh":"這個短語描述重視文化多樣性的教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"benefit some children more than others","meaning":"對某些兒童較其他兒童更有益","examples":[{"en":"Some programmes may benefit some children more than others.","zh":"有些課程可能對某些兒童較其他兒童更有益。"},{"en":"To benefit some children more than others means to help certain children more strongly than other groups.","zh":"benefit some children more than others 指對某些孩子的幫助比對其他群體更大。"},{"en":"An English-only programme may benefit fluent English speakers more than new arrivals.","zh":"只用英語的課程可能對英語流利者較新來學生更有益。"},{"en":"Unequal benefits can widen learning gaps if schools do not adjust support.","zh":"如果學校不調整支援，不平均的好處可以擴大學習差距。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uneven effects across students.","zh":"這個短語描述對學生有不均等影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"make a valuable contribution to","meaning":"對……作出寶貴貢獻","examples":[{"en":"Bilingual children can make a valuable contribution to society.","zh":"雙語兒童可以對社會作出寶貴貢獻。"},{"en":"To make a valuable contribution to something means to add something useful or important to it.","zh":"make a valuable contribution to something 指為某事加入有用或重要的東西。"},{"en":"Students who speak several languages can make a valuable contribution to school events for new families.","zh":"會說幾種語言的學生，可以對為新家庭舉辦的學校活動作出寶貴貢獻。"},{"en":"Valuing children’s languages can turn diversity into a social strength.","zh":"重視兒童語言可以把多元性轉化成社會力量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving something beneficial to a group or system.","zh":"這個短語描述為群體或系統提供有益事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the wealth of a country","meaning":"一個國家的財富","examples":[{"en":"Linguistic resources can contribute to the wealth of a country.","zh":"語言資源可以貢獻於一個國家的財富。"},{"en":"The wealth of a country includes not only money, but also skills, knowledge, culture, and human potential.","zh":"wealth of a country 不只包括金錢，也包括技能、知識、文化和人的潛力。"},{"en":"A multilingual workforce can add to the wealth of a country by improving trade and services.","zh":"多語勞動人口可以透過改善貿易和服務，增加一個國家的財富。"},{"en":"Education policies can waste or develop a country’s human resources.","zh":"教育政策可以浪費或發展一個國家的人力資源。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to broad national value, not only financial wealth.","zh":"這個短語可以指廣義國家價值，而不只是金錢財富。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"mother-tongue use at school","meaning":"在學校使用母語","examples":[{"en":"The law on mother-tongue use at school may be debated.","zh":"關於在學校使用母語的法律可能受到爭論。"},{"en":"Mother-tongue use at school means allowing or encouraging children to use their home language in the school setting.","zh":"mother-tongue use at school 指容許或鼓勵兒童在學校環境中使用家庭語言。"},{"en":"Mother-tongue use at school may include reading, discussion, translation, or bilingual support.","zh":"在學校使用母語可能包括閱讀、討論、翻譯或雙語支援。"},{"en":"Debates arise when people disagree about how much space home languages should have in school.","zh":"當人們不同意家庭語言在學校應有多少空間，爭論就會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to using the first language within education.","zh":"這個短語指在教育中使用第一語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be strengthened","meaning":"被加強","examples":[{"en":"Some people think the law should be strengthened.","zh":"有些人認為法律應被加強。"},{"en":"To be strengthened means to be made stronger, clearer, or more effective.","zh":"be strengthened 指被變得更強、更清楚或更有效。"},{"en":"School safety rules may be strengthened after repeated accidents.","zh":"反覆發生意外後，學校安全規則可能被加強。"},{"en":"A strengthened law can give stronger protection to children’s language rights.","zh":"被加強的法律可以給兒童語言權利更強保護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making something more powerful or secure.","zh":"這個短語描述使某事更有力或更穩固。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"提及；引用","examples":[{"en":"The writer refers to Goethe to support his argument.","zh":"作者提及 Goethe 來支持其論點。"},{"en":"To refer to someone or something means to mention or use it as part of an explanation.","zh":"refer to someone or something 指提及或使用某人某事作為解釋的一部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may refer to a student’s earlier essay to show improvement.","zh":"老師可能提及學生較早的作文，以顯示進步。"},{"en":"Writers refer to experts when they want to support a claim.","zh":"作者想支持聲稱時，會引用專家。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mentioning a source, example, or person.","zh":"這個短語描述提及來源、例子或人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"lend weight to","meaning":"加強……的說服力","examples":[{"en":"A quotation can lend weight to an argument.","zh":"引文可以加強論點的說服力。"},{"en":"To lend weight to an argument means to make it stronger or more convincing.","zh":"lend weight to an argument 指令論點更強或更有說服力。"},{"en":"Research evidence can lend weight to a teacher’s request for more language support.","zh":"研究證據可以加強老師要求更多語言支援的說服力。"},{"en":"A respected expert’s view can make a claim sound more serious.","zh":"受尊敬專家的觀點可以令聲稱聽起來更嚴肅。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding authority or force to an argument.","zh":"這個短語描述為論點增加權威或力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradict research","meaning":"與研究相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"An example may contradict research if it says the opposite.","zh":"如果例子說的是相反內容，它可能與研究相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict research means to go against what studies have found.","zh":"contradict research 指與研究發現相反。"},{"en":"A claim that bilingualism always harms children would contradict research on language development.","zh":"聲稱雙語能力總是傷害兒童，會與語言發展研究相矛盾。"},{"en":"If an opinion contradicts research, it needs very strong evidence to be accepted.","zh":"如果意見與研究相矛盾，它需要非常強的證據才會被接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes conflict between a claim and evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述聲稱與證據之間的衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"introduce a new concept","meaning":"引入新概念","examples":[{"en":"A writer may use a quotation to introduce a new concept.","zh":"作者可能用引文引入新概念。"},{"en":"To introduce a new concept means to bring in an idea that readers may not have considered before.","zh":"introduce a new concept 指帶入讀者可能未曾考慮過的想法。"},{"en":"A teacher may introduce a new concept by starting with a simple real-life example.","zh":"老師可能透過一個簡單生活例子引入新概念。"},{"en":"New concepts are easier to learn when they are connected to familiar experiences.","zh":"當新概念與熟悉經驗連接，它們較容易學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes presenting a fresh idea.","zh":"這個短語描述提出新想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"update current thinking","meaning":"更新現時看法","examples":[{"en":"New research can update current thinking about bilingual education.","zh":"新研究可以更新關於雙語教育的現時看法。"},{"en":"To update current thinking means to change or improve existing ideas using newer evidence.","zh":"update current thinking 指使用較新證據改變或改善現有想法。"},{"en":"Recent studies may update current thinking about how much homework children need.","zh":"近期研究可能更新關於兒童需要多少功課的現時看法。"},{"en":"Updated thinking helps schools avoid relying on old assumptions.","zh":"更新看法幫助學校避免依賴舊假設。"},{"en":"This phrase describes revising beliefs in light of new information.","zh":"這個短語描述根據新資訊修訂信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"have a firm grasp of","meaning":"牢固掌握……","examples":[{"en":"Children with a firm grasp of their mother tongue learn more effectively.","zh":"牢固掌握母語的兒童學習得更有效。"},{"en":"To have a firm grasp of something means to understand or control it well.","zh":"have a firm grasp of something 指很好地理解或掌握某事。"},{"en":"A student with a firm grasp of basic grammar can write more accurate sentences.","zh":"牢固掌握基本文法的學生可以寫出更準確句子。"},{"en":"A firm grasp of the first language can support learning in another language.","zh":"牢固掌握第一語言可以支援另一種語言的學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong understanding or command.","zh":"這個短語描述強大的理解或掌控能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"go on to do much better","meaning":"繼而表現更好","examples":[{"en":"Children with strong language foundations may go on to do much better at school.","zh":"有強大語言基礎的兒童可能繼而在學校表現更好。"},{"en":"To go on to do much better means to later perform more successfully after an earlier stage.","zh":"go on to do much better 指在較早階段之後，日後表現更成功。"},{"en":"A student who builds good reading habits early may go on to do much better in secondary school.","zh":"早早建立良好閱讀習慣的學生，可能繼而在中學表現更好。"},{"en":"Early language support can lead to stronger later academic performance.","zh":"早期語言支援可以帶來較強的後期學業表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes later improvement following a foundation.","zh":"這個短語描述在基礎之後出現的日後進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"throughout their time at school","meaning":"在整個求學階段","examples":[{"en":"Language skills can support children throughout their time at school.","zh":"語言技能可以在整個求學階段支援兒童。"},{"en":"Throughout their time at school means during the whole period when children are students.","zh":"throughout their time at school 指在兒童作為學生的整個期間。"},{"en":"Good reading skills help students throughout their time at school, from primary lessons to public exams.","zh":"良好閱讀能力在整個求學階段都幫助學生，從小學課堂到公開考試。"},{"en":"Long-term language support matters because school demands become more complex over time.","zh":"長期語言支援很重要，因為學校要求會隨時間變得更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes support across the full school journey.","zh":"這個短語描述貫穿整個求學旅程的支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"cultural background","meaning":"文化背景","examples":[{"en":"Children may read stories about their cultural background.","zh":"兒童可能閱讀關於自己文化背景的故事。"},{"en":"Cultural background is the traditions, language, values, history, and family experiences a person comes from.","zh":"cultural background 指一個人所來自的傳統、語言、價值、歷史和家庭經驗。"},{"en":"A child’s cultural background may include festivals, food, stories, and religious practices.","zh":"孩子的文化背景可能包括節日、食物、故事和宗教做法。"},{"en":"When schools recognise cultural background, students may feel more respected.","zh":"當學校承認文化背景，學生可能感到更受尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the cultural roots that shape a person.","zh":"這個短語指塑造一個人的文化根源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"stronger relationships with","meaning":"與……建立更緊密的關係","examples":[{"en":"Language can help children build stronger relationships with family members.","zh":"語言可以幫助兒童與家人建立更緊密的關係。"},{"en":"Stronger relationships with someone are closer, more trusting, and more meaningful connections with them.","zh":"stronger relationships with someone 指與某人有更親近、更信任和更有意義的連繫。"},{"en":"A child may build stronger relationships with grandparents by speaking their shared language.","zh":"孩子可以透過說共同語言，與祖父母建立更緊密的關係。"},{"en":"When communication improves, family trust and emotional support can also improve.","zh":"當溝通改善，家庭信任和情感支援也可以改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deeper human connection.","zh":"這個短語描述更深的人際連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be suspicious about","meaning":"對……抱有懷疑","examples":[{"en":"Some people are suspicious about mother-tongue-based teaching programmes.","zh":"有些人對以母語為本的教學課程抱有懷疑。"},{"en":"To be suspicious about something means to feel doubtful, cautious, or mistrustful toward it.","zh":"be suspicious about something 指對某事感到懷疑、謹慎或不信任。"},{"en":"Parents may be suspicious about a new policy if they do not understand how it works.","zh":"如果家長不了解新政策如何運作，可能對它抱有懷疑。"},{"en":"Suspicion can decrease when schools explain evidence clearly.","zh":"當學校清楚解釋證據，懷疑可以減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doubt or worry about something.","zh":"這個短語描述對某事的疑慮或擔心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be slow to learn to read","meaning":"學習閱讀進度緩慢","examples":[{"en":"Some parents worry that children will be slow to learn to read.","zh":"有些家長擔心兒童學習閱讀進度緩慢。"},{"en":"To be slow to learn to read means to take longer than expected to develop reading ability.","zh":"be slow to learn to read 指需要比預期更長時間發展閱讀能力。"},{"en":"A child may be slow to learn to read if she lacks books, support, or confidence.","zh":"如果孩子缺乏書本、支援或信心，她學習閱讀可能進度緩慢。"},{"en":"Slow reading development does not always mean low intelligence.","zh":"閱讀發展緩慢不一定代表智力低。"},{"en":"This phrase describes delayed progress in reading.","zh":"這個短語描述閱讀進展延遲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"confuse words in","meaning":"混淆……中的詞語","examples":[{"en":"Some people think bilingual children will confuse words in two languages.","zh":"有些人認為雙語兒童會混淆兩種語言中的詞語。"},{"en":"To confuse words in two languages means to mix them up or use the wrong one by mistake.","zh":"confuse words in two languages 指把兩種語言中的詞語混在一起或誤用。"},{"en":"A young child may confuse words in English and Spanish while still learning both.","zh":"年幼孩子在仍在學兩種語言時，可能混淆英文和西班牙文中的詞語。"},{"en":"Occasional mixing does not necessarily mean bilingualism is harmful.","zh":"偶爾混用不一定代表雙語有害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fear about mixing vocabulary across languages.","zh":"這個短語描述對跨語言混淆詞彙的擔心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be less interested in","meaning":"對……較不感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Some people fear children will be less interested in their lessons.","zh":"有些人擔心兒童會對課堂較不感興趣。"},{"en":"To be less interested in something means to feel less curious, motivated, or engaged with it.","zh":"be less interested in something 指對某事較少好奇、動機或投入。"},{"en":"Students may be less interested in a lesson if they cannot understand the language used.","zh":"如果學生不理解課堂使用的語言，他們可能對課堂較不感興趣。"},{"en":"Interest often increases when lessons connect with students’ lives and backgrounds.","zh":"當課堂與學生生活和背景連接，興趣通常會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reduced motivation or attention.","zh":"這個短語描述動機或注意力減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"use up valuable time","meaning":"用去寶貴時間","examples":[{"en":"Some critics fear that bilingual programmes will use up valuable time.","zh":"有些批評者擔心雙語課程會用去寶貴時間。"},{"en":"To use up valuable time means to spend limited time on one thing so less remains for another.","zh":"use up valuable time 指把有限時間花在一件事上，以致另一件事所剩時間較少。"},{"en":"A long announcement may use up valuable lesson time before students start writing.","zh":"長篇公告可能在學生開始寫作前用去寶貴課堂時間。"},{"en":"Critics may worry that one language programme leaves too little time for another language.","zh":"批評者可能擔心一種語言課程令另一種語言時間太少。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses concern about wasting or consuming important time.","zh":"這個短語表達對浪費或消耗重要時間的憂慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the summary using the list of words.","zh":"考生使用詞語列表完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill gaps in a shortened version of the passage.","zh":"complete the summary 指在文章的簡短版本中填補空格。"},{"en":"Students complete the summary by choosing words that fit both meaning and grammar.","zh":"學生透過選擇意思和文法都合適的詞語完成摘要。"},{"en":"This task tests understanding of main ideas, details, and sentence structure.","zh":"這項任務測試對主旨、細節和句子結構的理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"using the list of words","meaning":"使用所提供的詞語列表","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using the list of words provided.","zh":"學生使用所提供的詞語列表完成摘要。"},{"en":"Using the list of words means choosing answers only from the words given in the question.","zh":"using the list of words 指只從題目提供的詞語中選擇答案。"},{"en":"In this task, students should not invent their own answers if a word list is provided.","zh":"在這類任務中，如果提供詞語列表，學生不應自行創作答案。"},{"en":"The list limits the possible answers and helps students focus.","zh":"詞語列表限制可能答案並幫助學生集中。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the source of the answers.","zh":"這個短語解釋答案來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"acquire the ability to","meaning":"獲得……的能力","examples":[{"en":"Bilingual children can acquire the ability to converse in the majority language.","zh":"雙語兒童可以獲得以主流語言交談的能力。"},{"en":"To acquire the ability to do something means to gradually gain the skill to do it.","zh":"acquire the ability to do something 指逐漸獲得做某事的技能。"},{"en":"Students acquire the ability to write essays by reading models and practising often.","zh":"學生透過閱讀範文和經常練習，獲得寫作文的能力。"},{"en":"Ability is acquired through exposure, practice, feedback, and time.","zh":"能力是透過接觸、練習、回饋和時間獲得的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gaining a skill.","zh":"這個短語描述獲得技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"converse in","meaning":"以……交談","examples":[{"en":"Many children quickly learn to converse in the majority language.","zh":"許多兒童很快學會以主流語言交談。"},{"en":"To converse in a language means to have ordinary spoken conversations in that language.","zh":"converse in a language 指用該語言進行普通口語對話。"},{"en":"A child may converse in English with classmates but in Korean with grandparents.","zh":"孩子可能與同學以英語交談，但與祖父母以韓語交談。"},{"en":"Conversing in a language helps children build fluency and social confidence.","zh":"以某語言交談幫助兒童建立流暢度和社交信心。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to speaking with others in a language.","zh":"這個短語指用某語言與他人說話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"remarkably quickly","meaning":"異常迅速地","examples":[{"en":"Bilingual children may acquire conversational skills remarkably quickly.","zh":"雙語兒童可能異常迅速地獲得日常會話能力。"},{"en":"Remarkably quickly means surprisingly fast or faster than expected.","zh":"remarkably quickly 指令人驚訝地快，或快於預期。"},{"en":"A new student may learn classroom routines remarkably quickly after a few friendly explanations.","zh":"經過幾次友善解釋後，新學生可能異常迅速地學會課堂常規。"},{"en":"Quick progress in conversation can hide slower progress in academic language.","zh":"會話上的快速進步可能掩蓋學術語言較慢的進展。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights unusually fast development.","zh":"這個短語突出異常快速的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"competence in","meaning":"在……方面的能力","examples":[{"en":"Competence in the mother tongue can be lost quickly.","zh":"母語方面的能力可能迅速流失。"},{"en":"Competence in something means practical ability or skill in that area.","zh":"competence in something 指在某範疇的實際能力或技能。"},{"en":"A student may have strong competence in speaking but weaker competence in writing.","zh":"學生可能在說話方面能力強，但在寫作方面能力較弱。"},{"en":"Language competence can weaken if the language is no longer used actively.","zh":"如果語言不再被主動使用，語言能力可能削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ability in a specific skill or language.","zh":"這個短語描述在某項技能或語言方面的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"at a similar rate","meaning":"以相若速度","examples":[{"en":"Mother-tongue ability can be lost at a similar rate.","zh":"母語能力可以以相若速度流失。"},{"en":"At a similar rate means at about the same speed or pace.","zh":"at a similar rate 指以大約相同速度或步伐。"},{"en":"Two students may improve at a similar rate if they practise for the same amount of time.","zh":"如果兩名學生練習時間相同，他們可能以相若速度進步。"},{"en":"Skills can be gained quickly and sometimes lost at a similar rate without practice.","zh":"技能可以迅速獲得，也有時在沒有練習時以相若速度流失。"},{"en":"This phrase compares speed of change.","zh":"這個短語比較變化速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"this phenomenon","meaning":"這種現象","examples":[{"en":"This phenomenon depends partly on the local community.","zh":"這種現象部分取決於本地社區。"},{"en":"This phenomenon means this observable event, pattern, or situation.","zh":"this phenomenon 指這個可觀察到的事件、模式或情況。"},{"en":"The phenomenon of students switching languages during recess can reveal social pressure.","zh":"學生在小息時轉換語言這種現象，可以揭示社交壓力。"},{"en":"A phenomenon may have several causes, so researchers must examine context carefully.","zh":"一種現象可能有幾個成因，因此研究人員必須仔細檢視情境。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a situation already discussed.","zh":"這個短語回指已討論的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"to a certain extent","meaning":"在某程度上","examples":[{"en":"Language loss depends, to a certain extent, on the local neighbourhood.","zh":"語言流失在某程度上取決於本地鄰近社區。"},{"en":"To a certain extent means partly, but not completely.","zh":"to a certain extent 指部分地，但不是完全地。"},{"en":"Exam performance depends, to a certain extent, on sleep and confidence.","zh":"考試表現在某程度上取決於睡眠和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor matters, but it is not the only factor.","zh":"這個短語顯示某因素重要，但不是唯一因素。"},{"en":"It is useful when making a balanced statement.","zh":"它適合用於作出平衡陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the proportion of","meaning":"……的比例","examples":[{"en":"The proportion of families from the same background affects language maintenance.","zh":"來自同一背景的家庭比例會影響語言維持。"},{"en":"The proportion of something is the part or percentage of a whole group.","zh":"proportion of something 指整體群體中的部分或百分比。"},{"en":"A school may check the proportion of students who speak more than one language at home.","zh":"學校可能檢查在家說多於一種語言的學生比例。"},{"en":"A higher proportion of same-language families can create more chances to use that language.","zh":"同語言家庭比例較高，可以創造更多使用該語言的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to share, part, or percentage.","zh":"這個短語指份額、部分或百分比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"linguistic background","meaning":"語言背景","examples":[{"en":"Children from the same linguistic background may support one another.","zh":"來自相同語言背景的兒童可以互相支持。"},{"en":"Linguistic background is a person’s language history, home language, and experience with languages.","zh":"linguistic background 指一個人的語言歷史、家庭語言和語言經驗。"},{"en":"Two students from the same linguistic background may help each other understand school instructions.","zh":"兩名來自相同語言背景的學生，可能互相幫助理解學校指示。"},{"en":"Linguistic background affects how children learn new words and connect with peers.","zh":"語言背景影響兒童如何學新詞和與同輩建立連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the language side of a person’s background.","zh":"這個短語指一個人背景中的語言部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"settle in","meaning":"定居於……","examples":[{"en":"Families from the same linguistic group may settle in a particular area.","zh":"來自同一語言群體的家庭可能定居於某一特定地區。"},{"en":"To settle in a place means to begin living there and become part of the local community.","zh":"settle in a place 指開始在某地生活並成為本地社區一部分。"},{"en":"New families may settle in a neighbourhood because relatives already live there.","zh":"新家庭可能因親戚已住在某區而定居於該社區。"},{"en":"When families settle close together, children hear their mother tongue more often.","zh":"當家庭聚居，兒童會更常聽到母語。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a new place one’s home.","zh":"這個短語描述把新地方變成自己的家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a particular area","meaning":"某一特定地區","examples":[{"en":"Language maintenance can depend on the community in a particular area.","zh":"語言維持可能取決於某一特定地區中的社群。"},{"en":"A particular area is a specific place, neighbourhood, district, or region.","zh":"particular area 指某個特定地方、鄰近社區、地區或區域。"},{"en":"A school may serve a particular area where many families share the same language.","zh":"學校可能服務某一特定地區，該區許多家庭共享同一語言。"},{"en":"The people living in one area can shape the languages children hear every day.","zh":"居住在某區的人可以塑造兒童每天聽到的語言。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to one specific location.","zh":"這個短語指某個具體位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"active use of","meaning":"主動使用……","examples":[{"en":"Children may lose the active use of their mother tongue.","zh":"兒童可能失去主動使用母語的能力。"},{"en":"Active use of a language means speaking or writing it, not only understanding it.","zh":"active use of a language 指說或寫該語言，而不只是理解它。"},{"en":"A teenager may understand a home language but lose active use of it if he always replies in English.","zh":"如果青少年總是用英文回答，他可能理解家庭語言，但失去主動使用它的能力。"},{"en":"Active use keeps a language strong because the speaker practises producing it.","zh":"主動使用令語言保持強大，因為說話者練習產出語言。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to using a language actively, not passively.","zh":"這個短語指主動而非被動地使用語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"no longer employ","meaning":"不再使用","examples":[{"en":"Children may no longer employ their mother tongue at home.","zh":"兒童可能不再在家使用母語。"},{"en":"No longer employ means no longer use.","zh":"no longer employ 指不再使用。"},{"en":"A student may no longer employ a dictionary if she relies only on translation apps.","zh":"如果學生只依賴翻譯應用程式，她可能不再使用字典。"},{"en":"When children no longer employ the home language, speaking ability can fade quickly.","zh":"當兒童不再使用家庭語言，說話能力可以迅速減退。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal way to say something has stopped being used.","zh":"這個短語是表示某物停止被使用的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"although they may still understand it","meaning":"雖然他們可能仍然明白它","examples":[{"en":"Children may stop speaking their mother tongue, although they may still understand it.","zh":"兒童可能停止說母語，雖然他們可能仍然明白它。"},{"en":"Although they may still understand it means even if they can still comprehend the language.","zh":"although they may still understand it 指即使他們仍能理解該語言。"},{"en":"A child may answer in English although she may still understand her grandmother’s Cantonese.","zh":"孩子可能用英文回答，雖然她可能仍然明白祖母的廣東話。"},{"en":"Understanding can remain after active speaking becomes weak.","zh":"主動說話變弱後，理解能力仍可能存在。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts passive understanding with active use.","zh":"這個短語把被動理解與主動使用作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"it follows that","meaning":"因此可見","examples":[{"en":"It follows that language loss can affect children emotionally.","zh":"因此可見，語言流失可以在情感上影響兒童。"},{"en":"It follows that means the next idea is a logical result of what has just been explained.","zh":"it follows that 指下一個想法是剛解釋內容的邏輯結果。"},{"en":"If children cannot speak easily with parents, it follows that family closeness may suffer.","zh":"如果孩子不能輕鬆與父母交談，因此可見家庭親密感可能受損。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to show a conclusion follows from evidence.","zh":"作者使用這個短語顯示結論來自證據。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a logical consequence.","zh":"這個短語引入邏輯後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"in these circumstances","meaning":"在這些情況下","examples":[{"en":"In these circumstances, adolescents may feel culturally disconnected.","zh":"在這些情況下，青少年可能感到文化上脫節。"},{"en":"In these circumstances means under these conditions or in this situation.","zh":"in these circumstances 指在這些條件下或在這種情況中。"},{"en":"If students cannot understand lessons or talk easily at home, in these circumstances they may feel isolated.","zh":"如果學生不能理解課堂，也不能在家輕鬆交談，在這些情況下，他們可能感到孤立。"},{"en":"The phrase links a response to the conditions that caused it.","zh":"這個短語把回應與造成它的條件連接起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining why a result is understandable.","zh":"它適合用於解釋為何某結果可以理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a sense of dislocation","meaning":"失落感；無所適從的感覺","examples":[{"en":"Some adolescents experience a sense of dislocation.","zh":"有些青少年經歷一種失落感。"},{"en":"A sense of dislocation is a feeling of not fully belonging anywhere.","zh":"sense of dislocation 指感到自己不完全屬於任何地方。"},{"en":"A teenager may feel a sense of dislocation if she feels too different at school and too distant from home culture.","zh":"如果青少年覺得自己在學校太不同、又與家庭文化太疏遠，她可能感到無所適從。"},{"en":"Language loss can make young people feel separated from both family and classmates.","zh":"語言流失可以令年輕人感到與家庭和同學都分離。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional and cultural unsettlement.","zh":"這個短語描述情感和文化上的不安定感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"in relation to","meaning":"關於；就……而言","examples":[{"en":"Some pupils feel dislocation in relation to home and school life.","zh":"有些學生就家庭和學校生活而言感到無所適從。"},{"en":"In relation to means connected with or concerning a particular thing.","zh":"in relation to 指與某特定事物有關或關於某事。"},{"en":"A student may feel anxious in relation to exams but confident in daily classwork.","zh":"學生可能就考試而言感到焦慮，但在日常課堂功課中有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase helps specify which area or topic is being discussed.","zh":"這個短語幫助明確正在討論哪個範疇或主題。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing how something connects to a wider issue.","zh":"它適合用於描述某事如何連接到更廣泛議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"aspects of their lives","meaning":"生活的各方面","examples":[{"en":"Language loss can affect many aspects of children’s lives.","zh":"語言流失可以影響兒童生活的各方面。"},{"en":"Aspects of their lives are different parts of how people live, such as family, school, friendship, and identity.","zh":"aspects of their lives 指人們生活的不同部分，例如家庭、學校、友誼和身份。"},{"en":"A child’s language affects many aspects of her life, from homework to talking with grandparents.","zh":"孩子的語言影響她生活的各方面，從功課到與祖父母交談。"},{"en":"When one important aspect changes, other parts of life may change too.","zh":"當一個重要方面改變，生活其他部分也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to different areas of a person’s life.","zh":"這個短語指一個人生活中的不同範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所提供資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether statements agree with the information given in the passage.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與文章所提供資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"A TRUE answer agrees with the information given, while a FALSE answer says the opposite.","zh":"TRUE 答案與所提供資料一致，而 FALSE 答案則說相反內容。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge if the task asks about the passage only.","zh":"如果題目只問文章內容，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading-comprehension instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀理解指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the views of the writer.","zh":"陳述可能與作者的觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what that person thinks or argues.","zh":"contradict the views of someone 指說出與某人想法或論點相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the writer supports bilingual education, a statement against all bilingual programmes may contradict the writer’s views.","zh":"如果作者支持雙語教育，反對所有雙語課程的陳述可能與作者觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be based on the text, not on a reader’s personal opinion.","zh":"矛盾必須基於文本，而不是讀者個人意見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disagreement with a stated viewpoint.","zh":"這個短語描述與已表達觀點不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"If there is not enough information, it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"如果資料不足，就無法判斷作者的想法。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough evidence to make a clear judgement.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠證據作出清楚判斷。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions cost, it is impossible to say whether the writer thinks the programme is expensive.","zh":"如果文章從未提及成本，就無法判斷作者是否認為該課程昂貴。"},{"en":"In reading tests, this often leads to a NOT GIVEN answer.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，這通常導向 NOT GIVEN 答案。"},{"en":"This phrase warns students not to guess beyond the text.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生不要超出文本猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"attend kindergarten","meaning":"就讀幼稚園","examples":[{"en":"Many children who attend kindergarten in Toronto do not speak English at home.","zh":"在多倫多就讀幼稚園的許多兒童在家不說英語。"},{"en":"To attend kindergarten means to go to kindergarten as a pupil.","zh":"attend kindergarten 指作為學生上幼稚園。"},{"en":"Children who attend kindergarten learn routines such as lining up, sharing, and listening to stories.","zh":"就讀幼稚園的兒童會學習排隊、分享和聽故事等常規。"},{"en":"Kindergarten attendance may expose children to a school language different from their home language.","zh":"就讀幼稚園可能令兒童接觸不同於家庭語言的學校語言。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to being enrolled in early childhood schooling.","zh":"這個短語指入讀早期兒童教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"have English as their mother tongue","meaning":"以英語為母語","examples":[{"en":"Less than half of the children have English as their mother tongue.","zh":"少於一半兒童以英語為母語。"},{"en":"To have English as their mother tongue means English is the first or home language they learned.","zh":"have English as their mother tongue 指英語是他們最先學會或家中使用的語言。"},{"en":"A child may have English as her mother tongue even if she later learns French at school.","zh":"即使孩子後來在學校學法語，她仍可能以英語為母語。"},{"en":"If fewer children have English as their mother tongue, schools may need stronger language support.","zh":"如果較少兒童以英語為母語，學校可能需要更強語言支援。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies English as a child’s first language.","zh":"這個短語指出英語是孩子的第一語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"host-country language","meaning":"所在國家的語言","examples":[{"en":"Learning the host-country language is important for immigrant children.","zh":"學習所在國家的語言對移民兒童很重要。"},{"en":"The host-country language is the main language used in the country where newcomers live.","zh":"host-country language 指新來者所居住國家使用的主要語言。"},{"en":"A child moving to Canada may need to learn English or French as the host-country language.","zh":"搬到加拿大的孩子可能需要學英語或法語作為所在國家的語言。"},{"en":"Learning the host-country language helps children access school, services, and friendships.","zh":"學習所在國家的語言幫助孩子接觸學校、服務和友誼。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the language of the receiving country.","zh":"這個短語指接收國的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"have an adverse effect on","meaning":"對……有不良影響","examples":[{"en":"Some people worry that school language learning may have an adverse effect on the mother tongue.","zh":"有些人擔心學校語言學習可能對母語有不良影響。"},{"en":"To have an adverse effect on something means to harm it or influence it negatively.","zh":"have an adverse effect on something 指傷害某事或對其造成負面影響。"},{"en":"Too much screen time may have an adverse effect on sleep and concentration.","zh":"過多螢幕時間可能對睡眠和專注力有不良影響。"},{"en":"People may fear that one language will weaken another, though research may not support that fear.","zh":"人們可能害怕一種語言會削弱另一種語言，雖然研究未必支持這種恐懼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a negative impact.","zh":"這個短語描述負面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be accepted by","meaning":"被……接受","examples":[{"en":"A programme may be accepted by an education system.","zh":"課程可能被教育制度接受。"},{"en":"To be accepted by a group or system means to be approved, recognised, or allowed by it.","zh":"be accepted by a group or system 指被某群體或制度批准、承認或容許。"},{"en":"A new teaching method may be accepted by a school after a successful trial.","zh":"新教學方法在成功試行後，可能被學校接受。"},{"en":"Acceptance by an education system can affect whether a programme receives funding.","zh":"被教育制度接受可以影響課程是否獲得資金。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official or social approval.","zh":"這個短語描述官方或社會上的接納。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"education system","meaning":"教育制度","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to the French education system.","zh":"該陳述指的是法國教育制度。"},{"en":"An education system is the organised structure of schools, policies, exams, and teaching in a country or region.","zh":"education system 指一個國家或地區中學校、政策、考試和教學的組織結構。"},{"en":"An education system decides what languages are taught and how students are assessed.","zh":"教育制度決定教授哪些語言，以及如何評估學生。"},{"en":"If an education system values only one language, minority students may need extra support.","zh":"如果教育制度只重視一種語言，少數語言學生可能需要額外支援。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the whole organised arrangement of education.","zh":"這個短語指整個有組織的教育安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be taught to","meaning":"被教導去……","examples":[{"en":"Children may be taught to tell the time in school.","zh":"兒童可能在學校被教導去說出時間。"},{"en":"To be taught to do something means to be shown or instructed how to do it.","zh":"be taught to do something 指被展示或指導如何做某事。"},{"en":"Students are taught to underline keywords before answering reading questions.","zh":"學生被教導在回答閱讀題前劃下關鍵詞。"},{"en":"What children are taught in one language can often help them in another language.","zh":"兒童在一種語言中學到的東西，通常可以幫助他們使用另一種語言。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving instruction.","zh":"這個短語描述接受教導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"monolingual children","meaning":"單語兒童","examples":[{"en":"The question compares bilingual children with monolingual children.","zh":"題目比較雙語兒童與單語兒童。"},{"en":"Monolingual children are children who use or know mainly one language.","zh":"monolingual children 指主要使用或懂得一種語言的兒童。"},{"en":"A monolingual child may speak only English at home and at school.","zh":"單語兒童可能在家和學校都只說英語。"},{"en":"Comparing monolingual and bilingual children can show how language experience affects learning.","zh":"比較單語和雙語兒童，可以顯示語言經驗如何影響學習。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to children with one main language.","zh":"這個短語指有一種主要語言的兒童。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"apply reading comprehension strategies","meaning":"應用閱讀理解策略","examples":[{"en":"Bilingual children can apply reading comprehension strategies across languages.","zh":"雙語兒童可以跨語言應用閱讀理解策略。"},{"en":"To apply reading comprehension strategies means to use methods for understanding texts, such as finding the main idea or identifying supporting details.","zh":"apply reading comprehension strategies 指使用理解文本的方法，例如找主旨或識別支持細節。"},{"en":"A student may apply reading comprehension strategies learned in Chinese when reading an English article.","zh":"學生可能在閱讀英文文章時，應用在中文中學到的閱讀理解策略。"},{"en":"Strategy transfer helps children use existing skills in new language contexts.","zh":"策略轉移幫助兒童在新語言情境中使用已有技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using reading methods to understand texts.","zh":"這個短語描述使用閱讀方法來理解文本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"acquired in one language","meaning":"在一種語言中習得的","examples":[{"en":"Skills acquired in one language can transfer to another.","zh":"在一種語言中習得的技能可以轉移到另一種語言。"},{"en":"Acquired in one language means learned or developed through using that language.","zh":"acquired in one language 指透過使用某一種語言而學會或發展。"},{"en":"A reading strategy acquired in Chinese may help a child understand English passages.","zh":"在中文中習得的閱讀策略，可能幫助孩子理解英文文章。"},{"en":"When skills are acquired in one language, children do not always need to learn them again from zero.","zh":"當技能在一種語言中習得，兒童未必需要從零再學一次。"},{"en":"This phrase describes skills gained through a particular language.","zh":"這個短語描述透過某特定語言獲得的技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"when reading in the other","meaning":"在閱讀另一種語言時","examples":[{"en":"Children can use the same strategy when reading in the other language.","zh":"兒童在閱讀另一種語言時可以使用同一策略。"},{"en":"When reading in the other language means while reading in a second or different language.","zh":"when reading in the other language 指在閱讀第二種或另一種語言時。"},{"en":"A child who finds topic sentences in Chinese can use the same method when reading in English.","zh":"能在中文中找主題句的孩子，在閱讀英文時可以使用同一方法。"},{"en":"Reading strategies can transfer because the thinking skill is similar even when the words change.","zh":"閱讀策略可以轉移，因為即使詞語改變，思考技能仍相似。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to applying a skill while reading another language.","zh":"這個短語指在閱讀另一種語言時應用某項技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 43 - The Significant Role of Mother Tongue in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 44":[{"front":"blast through","meaning":"吹襲；猛吹過","examples":[{"en":"An east wind blasts through a gap in the Cordillera de Tilarán.","zh":"東風猛烈吹過 Cordillera de Tilarán 山脈的一個缺口。"},{"en":"To blast through a place means to move through it very forcefully, usually with wind, air, sound, or energy.","zh":"blast through a place 指風、空氣、聲音或能量非常猛烈地穿過某處。"},{"en":"During the storm, cold air blasted through the open classroom windows.","zh":"暴風雨期間，冷空氣猛烈吹過打開的課室窗戶。"},{"en":"Strong wind can blast through narrow streets because buildings create a tunnel effect.","zh":"強風可以猛烈吹過狹窄街道，因為建築物會造成隧道效應。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests power and speed, not a gentle breeze.","zh":"這個短語暗示力量和速度，而不是柔和微風。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a rugged mountain range","meaning":"崎嶇的山脈","examples":[{"en":"The Cordillera de Tilarán is a rugged mountain range in northern Costa Rica.","zh":"Cordillera de Tilarán 是哥斯達黎加北部一條崎嶇的山脈。"},{"en":"A rugged mountain range is a line of mountains with rough, steep, uneven land.","zh":"rugged mountain range 指一列地勢粗糙、陡峭而不平坦的山。"},{"en":"Hikers need strong shoes when walking through a rugged mountain range.","zh":"徒步者穿越崎嶇山脈時需要穿堅固的鞋。"},{"en":"Rugged mountain ranges can make travel difficult because roads must twist around cliffs and valleys.","zh":"崎嶇山脈可以令交通困難，因為道路必須繞過懸崖和山谷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mountains that are wild, rough, and physically challenging.","zh":"這個短語描述野性、粗糙而具身體挑戰的山地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"split something in half","meaning":"把……分成兩半","examples":[{"en":"The mountain range splits northern Costa Rica in half.","zh":"這條山脈把哥斯達黎加北部分成兩半。"},{"en":"To split something in half means to divide it into two parts.","zh":"split something in half 指把某物分成兩部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may split the class in half for a debate activity.","zh":"老師可能把全班分成兩半來進行辯論活動。"},{"en":"A river can split a town in half, making bridges important for daily travel.","zh":"一條河可以把城鎮分成兩半，使橋樑對日常交通十分重要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a clear division into two sides or sections.","zh":"這個短語強調清楚分成兩邊或兩部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a female mantled howler monkey","meaning":"一隻雌性披毛吼猴","examples":[{"en":"A female mantled howler monkey moves through the forest canopy.","zh":"一隻雌性披毛吼猴在森林樹冠層中移動。"},{"en":"A female mantled howler monkey is a female monkey of a species known for loud calls and a dark mantle of fur.","zh":"female mantled howler monkey 指一種以響亮叫聲和深色披毛聞名的雌性猴子。"},{"en":"A researcher may watch a female mantled howler monkey to study how it feeds and cares for its young.","zh":"研究人員可能觀察一隻雌性披毛吼猴，以研究牠如何覓食和照顧幼猴。"},{"en":"Female monkeys are important to population growth because they give birth and raise infants.","zh":"雌性猴子對種群增長重要，因為牠們會生育和撫養幼猴。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies both the sex and species of the animal.","zh":"這個短語同時指出動物的性別和物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"swaying trees","meaning":"搖曳的樹木","examples":[{"en":"The monkey moves through the swaying trees.","zh":"那隻猴子穿過搖曳的樹木。"},{"en":"Swaying trees are trees moving slowly from side to side, usually because of wind.","zh":"swaying trees 指通常因風而左右慢慢擺動的樹木。"},{"en":"Children may see swaying trees outside the window before a heavy rainstorm.","zh":"暴雨前，孩子可能在窗外看見搖曳的樹木。"},{"en":"Strong wind makes branches unstable, so animals moving through swaying trees need balance.","zh":"強風令樹枝不穩，所以在搖曳樹木中移動的動物需要平衡力。"},{"en":"The phrase creates an image of movement in the forest.","zh":"這個短語營造森林中有動態的畫面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the forest canopy","meaning":"森林樹冠層","examples":[{"en":"The monkey moves through the forest canopy.","zh":"那隻猴子在森林樹冠層中移動。"},{"en":"The forest canopy is the upper layer of a forest formed by the branches and leaves of tall trees.","zh":"forest canopy 指由高大樹木的樹枝和樹葉形成的森林上層。"},{"en":"Birds, insects, and monkeys may live high in the forest canopy.","zh":"鳥類、昆蟲和猴子可能生活在高高的森林樹冠層。"},{"en":"The canopy protects animals from some predators but can be dangerous when branches are weak.","zh":"樹冠層能保護動物免受某些捕食者威脅，但樹枝脆弱時也可能危險。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the treetop layer, not the forest floor.","zh":"這個短語指樹頂層，而不是森林地面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"primatologist","meaning":"靈長類動物學家","examples":[{"en":"Ken Glander is a primatologist from Duke University.","zh":"Ken Glander 是來自杜克大學的靈長類動物學家。"},{"en":"A primatologist is a scientist who studies primates, such as monkeys, apes, and lemurs.","zh":"primatologist 指研究猴子、猿、狐猴等靈長類動物的科學家。"},{"en":"A primatologist may spend months in a forest recording how monkeys feed, move, and communicate.","zh":"靈長類動物學家可能在森林中花數月記錄猴子如何覓食、移動和溝通。"},{"en":"Primatologists help conservation because they explain what primates need to survive.","zh":"靈長類動物學家有助保育，因為他們解釋靈長類動物生存所需。"},{"en":"The word refers to a specialist in primate behaviour, ecology, or evolution.","zh":"這個詞指研究靈長類行為、生態或演化的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"gaze into","meaning":"凝視……","examples":[{"en":"Glander gazes into the canopy while tracking the monkey.","zh":"Glander 追蹤那隻猴子時，凝視着樹冠層。"},{"en":"To gaze into something means to look steadily and carefully into it for some time.","zh":"gaze into something 指長時間穩定而仔細地看進某處。"},{"en":"A student may gaze into a microscope to see tiny cells clearly.","zh":"學生可能凝視顯微鏡，以清楚看見細胞。"},{"en":"Scientists gaze into the forest canopy because small movements can reveal where an animal is hiding.","zh":"科學家凝視森林樹冠層，因為細小動作可以揭示動物藏身位置。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests careful attention, not a quick glance.","zh":"這個短語暗示仔細注意，而不是快速一瞥。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"track someone’s movements","meaning":"追蹤某人的動向","examples":[{"en":"He tracks the female monkey’s movements in the canopy.","zh":"他追蹤那隻雌性猴子在樹冠層中的動向。"},{"en":"To track someone’s movements means to follow or record where they go and how they move.","zh":"track someone’s movements 指跟蹤或記錄某人去了哪裏和如何移動。"},{"en":"A parent may track a child’s movements on a school trip for safety.","zh":"家長可能在學校旅行中追蹤孩子的動向，以確保安全。"},{"en":"Researchers track animal movements to understand feeding patterns, territory, and social behaviour.","zh":"研究人員追蹤動物動向，以了解覓食模式、領域和社交行為。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful observation over time.","zh":"這個短語描述長時間仔細觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dart gun","meaning":"飛鏢槍；麻醉鏢槍","examples":[{"en":"Glander holds a dart gun as he waits for the right moment.","zh":"Glander 拿着麻醉鏢槍，等待適當時機。"},{"en":"A dart gun is a device that shoots a small dart, often carrying a sedative, to safely capture or examine animals.","zh":"dart gun 指發射小飛鏢的裝置，通常飛鏢帶有鎮靜劑，用來安全捕捉或檢查動物。"},{"en":"Wildlife vets may use a dart gun to treat a sick animal that cannot be approached by hand.","zh":"野生動物獸醫可能使用麻醉鏢槍治療無法徒手接近的病獸。"},{"en":"Dart guns reduce danger because researchers can keep distance from frightened or powerful animals.","zh":"麻醉鏢槍減少危險，因為研究人員可以與受驚或強壯動物保持距離。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a scientific tool, not a weapon for ordinary hunting.","zh":"這個短語指科學工具，而不是普通狩獵武器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"with infinite patience","meaning":"以無比耐性","examples":[{"en":"He waits with infinite patience for the right moment to shoot.","zh":"他以無比耐性等待射擊的適當時機。"},{"en":"With infinite patience means with extremely great patience and without rushing.","zh":"with infinite patience 指以極大的耐性、不急躁地做事。"},{"en":"A good teacher may explain the same grammar point with infinite patience until students understand.","zh":"好老師可能以無比耐性解釋同一個文法點，直到學生明白。"},{"en":"Wildlife research often needs infinite patience because animals do not behave on a human schedule.","zh":"野生動物研究通常需要無比耐性，因為動物不會按人類時間表行動。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises calm persistence over a long wait.","zh":"這個短語強調長時間等待中的冷靜堅持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the right moment to","meaning":"做……的適當時機","examples":[{"en":"He waits for the right moment to fire the dart.","zh":"他等待發射飛鏢的適當時機。"},{"en":"The right moment to do something is the best or safest time to do it.","zh":"the right moment to do something 指做某事的最佳或最安全時間。"},{"en":"A student should choose the right moment to ask a question, such as after the teacher finishes explaining.","zh":"學生應選擇適當時機發問，例如在老師解釋完之後。"},{"en":"Acting at the wrong moment can cause failure, danger, or misunderstanding.","zh":"在錯誤時機行動可以造成失敗、危險或誤會。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses timing and judgement.","zh":"這個短語強調時機和判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"with great care","meaning":"非常小心地","examples":[{"en":"With great care, Glander aims and fires.","zh":"Glander 非常小心地瞄準並射擊。"},{"en":"With great care means very carefully, with attention to safety and accuracy.","zh":"with great care 指非常小心，注意安全和準確。"},{"en":"A nurse handles a newborn baby with great care.","zh":"護士非常小心地抱起初生嬰兒。"},{"en":"Dangerous or delicate tasks require great care because small mistakes can cause harm.","zh":"危險或精細任務需要非常小心，因為小錯誤可以造成傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests slow, precise, and responsible action.","zh":"這個短語暗示緩慢、精準和負責任的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"aim and fire","meaning":"瞄準並射擊","examples":[{"en":"Glander aims and fires at the monkey.","zh":"Glander 向那隻猴子瞄準並射擊。"},{"en":"To aim and fire means to point a gun, camera, or similar device at a target and then release a shot.","zh":"aim and fire 指把槍、相機或類似裝置對準目標，然後發射。"},{"en":"A photographer may aim and fire the camera quickly when a bird opens its wings.","zh":"當鳥張開翅膀時，攝影師可能快速瞄準並拍攝。"},{"en":"A researcher must aim carefully before firing a dart so the animal is not injured unnecessarily.","zh":"研究人員發射麻醉鏢前必須仔細瞄準，避免不必要地傷害動物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes two actions: targeting first, then shooting.","zh":"這個短語描述兩個動作：先對準，再射擊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"wobble","meaning":"搖晃；蹣跚","examples":[{"en":"After being hit by the dart, the monkey wobbles.","zh":"被飛鏢射中後，那隻猴子搖晃起來。"},{"en":"To wobble means to move unsteadily from side to side, as if about to fall.","zh":"wobble 指不穩地左右搖動，好像快要跌倒。"},{"en":"A child may wobble on a bicycle when learning to ride for the first time.","zh":"孩子第一次學踩單車時可能會搖晃。"},{"en":"Sedation can make an animal wobble because its muscles and balance are affected.","zh":"鎮靜劑會令動物搖晃，因為肌肉和平衡受到影響。"},{"en":"The word describes unsteady movement, not smooth walking.","zh":"這個詞描述不穩定動作，而不是平穩走路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"belong to a population","meaning":"屬於某個種群","examples":[{"en":"This howler belongs to a population that has lived at the ranch for decades.","zh":"這隻吼猴屬於一個已在該牧場生活數十年的種群。"},{"en":"To belong to a population means to be part of a group of the same species living in a particular area.","zh":"belong to a population 指屬於生活在某特定地區的同一物種群體。"},{"en":"A bird tagged in the park may belong to a local population that nests there every year.","zh":"在公園被標記的鳥可能屬於每年在那裏築巢的本地種群。"},{"en":"Scientists study populations because group size and health show whether a species is surviving well.","zh":"科學家研究種群，因為群體大小和健康顯示某物種是否生存良好。"},{"en":"The phrase connects one individual animal with a wider group.","zh":"這個短語把單一個體動物與更大的群體連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"for decades","meaning":"數十年來","examples":[{"en":"The howler population has lived at Hacienda La Pacifica for decades.","zh":"吼猴種群數十年來一直生活在 Hacienda La Pacifica。"},{"en":"For decades means for many tens of years.","zh":"for decades 指持續許多個十年。"},{"en":"A family shop may serve the same neighbourhood for decades.","zh":"一間家庭小店可能數十年來服務同一社區。"},{"en":"If animals survive in one area for decades, the habitat must provide enough food and shelter.","zh":"如果動物在同一地區生存數十年，該棲息地必須提供足夠食物和庇護。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a long period, not just a few years.","zh":"這個短語顯示很長時期，而不只是幾年。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a working cattle ranch","meaning":"仍在營運的牧牛場","examples":[{"en":"Hacienda La Pacifica is a working cattle ranch in Guanacaste province.","zh":"Hacienda La Pacifica 是 Guanacaste 省一個仍在營運的牧牛場。"},{"en":"A working cattle ranch is an active farm where cattle are raised for meat, milk, or other agricultural purposes.","zh":"working cattle ranch 指正在運作、飼養牛隻以供肉類、牛奶或其他農業用途的農場。"},{"en":"Visitors to a working cattle ranch may see fences, pasture, workers, and herds of cows.","zh":"到訪仍在營運的牧牛場，遊客可能看到圍欄、牧草地、工人和牛群。"},{"en":"A working ranch can still support wildlife if some trees and habitat remain.","zh":"如果仍保留一些樹木和棲息地，營運中的牧場也可以支持野生動物。"},{"en":"The phrase means the ranch is still operating, not just preserved as a tourist site.","zh":"這個短語表示牧場仍在運作，而不只是作為旅遊景點保存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"native primates","meaning":"本土靈長類動物","examples":[{"en":"Other native primates were once common in the area.","zh":"其他本土靈長類動物曾經在該地區很常見。"},{"en":"Native primates are primate species that naturally live in a region rather than being introduced by humans.","zh":"native primates 指自然生活在某地區，而不是由人類引入的靈長類物種。"},{"en":"A national park may protect native primates such as monkeys that evolved in that forest.","zh":"國家公園可能保護在該森林演化的猴子等本土靈長類動物。"},{"en":"When native primates disappear, the local ecosystem can lose seed dispersers and important animal interactions.","zh":"當本土靈長類動物消失，本地生態系統可能失去種子傳播者和重要動物互動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to original local primate species.","zh":"這個短語指原本屬於當地的靈長類物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"white-faced capuchin monkeys","meaning":"白面卷尾猴","examples":[{"en":"White-faced capuchin monkeys were once common in this area.","zh":"白面卷尾猴曾經在這個地區很常見。"},{"en":"White-faced capuchin monkeys are small Central American monkeys with pale faces and dark bodies.","zh":"white-faced capuchin monkeys 指臉部較白、身體較深色的中美洲小型猴子。"},{"en":"A tourist may recognise white-faced capuchin monkeys because they are active, clever, and often visible in trees.","zh":"遊客可能認出白面卷尾猴，因為牠們活躍、聰明，而且常在樹上可見。"},{"en":"These monkeys need suitable forest because they often feed on fruit, insects, and small animals.","zh":"這些猴子需要合適森林，因為牠們常吃水果、昆蟲和小動物。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific monkey species.","zh":"這個短語命名一種特定猴子物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"spider monkeys","meaning":"蜘蛛猴","examples":[{"en":"Spider monkeys also vanished from the surrounding area.","zh":"蜘蛛猴也從周邊地區消失了。"},{"en":"Spider monkeys are long-limbed monkeys that move through trees with great agility.","zh":"spider monkeys 指四肢修長、能非常靈活地在樹間移動的猴子。"},{"en":"In a rainforest, spider monkeys may swing from branch to branch while searching for fruit.","zh":"在雨林中，蜘蛛猴可能在尋找水果時從一根樹枝盪到另一根樹枝。"},{"en":"Spider monkeys are vulnerable when forests are broken into small pieces because they need large home ranges.","zh":"當森林被分割成小片，蜘蛛猴會變得脆弱，因為牠們需要大活動範圍。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a primate species adapted to life high in trees.","zh":"這個短語指適應高樹生活的靈長類物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"once common","meaning":"曾經很常見","examples":[{"en":"Several native primates were once common in this area.","zh":"幾種本土靈長類動物曾經在這個地區很常見。"},{"en":"Once common means something used to be found often, but may no longer be common now.","zh":"once common 指某事物過去常見，但現在可能已不常見。"},{"en":"Public phone booths were once common in cities before mobile phones spread.","zh":"手提電話普及前，公共電話亭曾經在城市中很常見。"},{"en":"A species that was once common may disappear if its habitat is destroyed.","zh":"如果棲息地被破壞，曾經很常見的物種也可能消失。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the past with the present.","zh":"這個短語比較過去與現在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"vanish after","meaning":"在……之後消失","examples":[{"en":"The capuchin monkeys and spider monkeys vanished after the highway was built nearby.","zh":"白面卷尾猴和蜘蛛猴在附近公路建成後消失了。"},{"en":"To vanish after something means to disappear following that event.","zh":"vanish after something 指在某事件之後消失。"},{"en":"Small shops may vanish after a large shopping mall opens nearby.","zh":"大型商場在附近開業後，小店可能消失。"},{"en":"Animals may vanish after road building if the road cuts their habitat into pieces.","zh":"如果道路把棲息地切碎，動物可能在道路建設後消失。"},{"en":"The phrase links disappearance with a later cause or event.","zh":"這個短語把消失與後來的原因或事件連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"surrounding land","meaning":"周邊土地","examples":[{"en":"Most of the surrounding land was clear-cut for pasture.","zh":"大部分周邊土地被砍清作牧草地。"},{"en":"Surrounding land is the land around a particular place.","zh":"surrounding land 指某地點周圍的土地。"},{"en":"A school’s surrounding land may include roads, shops, parks, and housing estates.","zh":"學校的周邊土地可能包括道路、商店、公園和屋苑。"},{"en":"Changes to surrounding land can affect animals even if a small forest patch remains.","zh":"即使仍保留一小片森林，周邊土地的改變也可以影響動物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the area around the main location.","zh":"這個短語描述主要地點周圍的區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be clear-cut for pasture","meaning":"被砍清作牧草地","examples":[{"en":"Most of the surrounding land was clear-cut for pasture.","zh":"大部分周邊土地被砍清作牧草地。"},{"en":"To be clear-cut for pasture means trees are completely removed so the land can be used for grazing animals.","zh":"be clear-cut for pasture 指樹木被完全清除，以便土地用作動物放牧。"},{"en":"A forest may be clear-cut for pasture when farmers want more land for cattle.","zh":"當農民想要更多土地養牛，森林可能被砍清作牧草地。"},{"en":"Clear-cutting removes food, shelter, and pathways for forest animals.","zh":"砍清森林會移除森林動物的食物、庇護和移動通道。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a major land-use change from forest to grazing land.","zh":"這個短語描述由森林變成放牧地的重大土地用途改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"persist at","meaning":"在……繼續生存","examples":[{"en":"Howlers persist at La Pacifica because they are leaf-eaters.","zh":"吼猴在 La Pacifica 繼續生存，因為牠們是食葉動物。"},{"en":"To persist at a place means to continue surviving or remaining there despite difficulties.","zh":"persist at a place 指儘管有困難，仍在某地繼續生存或存在。"},{"en":"Some small shops persist in old neighbourhoods because loyal customers keep returning.","zh":"有些小店因忠實顧客持續回來，而能在舊社區繼續存在。"},{"en":"A species may persist in a damaged habitat if it can use whatever food remains.","zh":"如果物種能利用剩餘食物，牠可能在受破壞棲息地中繼續生存。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests survival under pressure.","zh":"這個短語暗示在壓力下存活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"leaf-eaters","meaning":"食葉動物","examples":[{"en":"Howlers are leaf-eaters that can survive on leaves.","zh":"吼猴是能靠樹葉生存的食葉動物。"},{"en":"Leaf-eaters are animals that feed mainly or partly on leaves.","zh":"leaf-eaters 指主要或部分以葉子為食的動物。"},{"en":"Caterpillars, koalas, and some monkeys are leaf-eaters.","zh":"毛蟲、樹熊和一些猴子都是食葉動物。"},{"en":"Leaf-eaters need ways to digest tough plant material and handle plant chemicals.","zh":"食葉動物需要方法消化堅韌植物材料並處理植物化學物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes animals by what they eat.","zh":"這個短語按飲食描述動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"depend on","meaning":"依賴……","examples":[{"en":"Howlers do not depend on large areas of fruiting trees.","zh":"吼猴不依賴大片結果實的樹木。"},{"en":"To depend on something means to need it in order to live, work, or succeed.","zh":"depend on something 指需要某物才能生活、工作或成功。"},{"en":"Students may depend on public transport if they live far from school.","zh":"如果學生住得離學校很遠，可能依賴公共交通。"},{"en":"Animals that depend on one food source become vulnerable when that food disappears.","zh":"依賴單一食物來源的動物，在該食物消失時會變得脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase shows reliance or need.","zh":"這個短語顯示依靠或需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"large areas of fruiting trees","meaning":"大片結果實的樹木","examples":[{"en":"Capuchin and spider monkeys depend on large areas of fruiting trees.","zh":"卷尾猴和蜘蛛猴依賴大片結果實的樹木。"},{"en":"Large areas of fruiting trees are wide forest spaces where many trees produce fruit.","zh":"large areas of fruiting trees 指有許多樹木結果實的廣闊森林空間。"},{"en":"Birds may gather in large areas of fruiting trees during the season when berries are ripe.","zh":"在漿果成熟季節，鳥類可能聚集在大片結果實的樹木中。"},{"en":"Animals that need fruit require bigger habitats because fruit appears in different places at different times.","zh":"需要水果的動物需要更大棲息地，因為果實在不同時間出現在不同地方。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a food-rich forest area.","zh":"這個短語描述食物豐富的森林區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"half a dozen trees","meaning":"半打樹；六棵左右的樹","examples":[{"en":"Howlers can survive anywhere with half a dozen trees.","zh":"只要有六棵左右的樹，吼猴幾乎在哪裏都能生存。"},{"en":"Half a dozen trees means about six trees.","zh":"half a dozen trees 指大約六棵樹。"},{"en":"A small garden with half a dozen trees can already provide shade for several families.","zh":"有六棵左右樹的小花園，已經可以為幾個家庭提供遮蔭。"},{"en":"If a monkey can survive with only half a dozen trees, it can live in smaller habitat patches.","zh":"如果猴子只需六棵左右的樹就能生存，牠就可以生活在較小棲息地斑塊中。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate small number, not an exact count.","zh":"這個短語給出大約的小數量，而不是精確計算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"eating habits","meaning":"飲食習慣","examples":[{"en":"Their eating habits are highly flexible.","zh":"牠們的飲食習慣非常靈活。"},{"en":"Eating habits are the usual patterns of what, when, and how a person or animal eats.","zh":"eating habits 指人或動物通常吃甚麼、何時吃和如何吃的模式。"},{"en":"A student’s eating habits may change during exams if she skips breakfast and eats late at night.","zh":"如果學生不吃早餐、深夜進食，她的飲食習慣可能在考試期間改變。"},{"en":"Flexible eating habits help animals survive when one type of food becomes scarce.","zh":"靈活的飲食習慣幫助動物在某種食物變少時生存。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to regular food behaviour.","zh":"這個短語指規律性的進食行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be flexible","meaning":"有彈性；靈活","examples":[{"en":"Howlers survive because their eating habits are flexible.","zh":"吼猴能生存，因為牠們的飲食習慣很靈活。"},{"en":"To be flexible means to be able to change or adapt when conditions change.","zh":"be flexible 指當情況改變時能夠改變或適應。"},{"en":"A teacher is flexible when she changes the lesson plan because students need more practice.","zh":"當學生需要更多練習，老師改變課堂計劃，就是靈活。"},{"en":"Flexibility helps animals survive in damaged habitats because they can use different foods or spaces.","zh":"靈活性幫助動物在受破壞棲息地中生存，因為牠們能使用不同食物或空間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adaptability, not physical bending only.","zh":"這個短語描述適應力，而不只是身體能彎曲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"an arms race between","meaning":"……之間的攻防競賽","examples":[{"en":"In forests, life is an arms race between trees and leaf-eating creatures.","zh":"在森林中，生命是樹木與食葉生物之間的攻防競賽。"},{"en":"An arms race between two sides is a continuing competition in which each side develops new ways to beat the other.","zh":"arms race between two sides 指雙方持續競爭，各自發展新方法來擊敗對方。"},{"en":"Computer security is an arms race between hackers and software companies.","zh":"電腦安全是黑客與軟件公司之間的攻防競賽。"},{"en":"Trees evolve toxins, so leaf-eaters evolve ways to tolerate or avoid those toxins.","zh":"樹木演化出毒素，所以食葉動物演化出忍受或避開這些毒素的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a back-and-forth struggle, not only military competition.","zh":"這個短語描述來回較量，而不只是軍事競爭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"myriad creatures","meaning":"無數生物","examples":[{"en":"Myriad creatures feed on leaves in the forest.","zh":"森林中有無數生物以樹葉為食。"},{"en":"Myriad creatures means a very large number of different living things.","zh":"myriad creatures 指數量非常多、種類各異的生物。"},{"en":"A pond may contain myriad creatures, from tiny insects to small fish.","zh":"池塘可能有無數生物，從細小昆蟲到小魚都有。"},{"en":"When many creatures depend on leaves, plants face constant pressure to defend themselves.","zh":"當許多生物依賴樹葉，植物就面對持續防禦壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses great number and variety.","zh":"這個短語強調數量和種類都很多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"feed on leaves","meaning":"以樹葉為食","examples":[{"en":"Many forest creatures feed on leaves.","zh":"許多森林生物以樹葉為食。"},{"en":"To feed on leaves means to eat leaves as food.","zh":"feed on leaves 指吃樹葉作為食物。"},{"en":"Caterpillars often feed on leaves in a school garden.","zh":"毛蟲常在學校花園中以樹葉為食。"},{"en":"Animals that feed on leaves need digestive systems that can handle tough plant fibres.","zh":"以樹葉為食的動物需要能處理堅韌植物纖維的消化系統。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a feeding habit.","zh":"這個短語描述一種覓食習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"evolve a variety of","meaning":"演化出各式各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"Plants have evolved a variety of chemical defences.","zh":"植物已演化出各式各樣的化學防禦機制。"},{"en":"To evolve a variety of something means to gradually develop many different forms of it over time.","zh":"evolve a variety of something 指隨時間逐漸發展出許多不同形式的某物。"},{"en":"Schools may evolve a variety of teaching methods as students’ needs change.","zh":"隨着學生需要改變，學校可能演化出各式各樣的教學方法。"},{"en":"Plants evolve different defences because different animals attack them in different ways.","zh":"植物演化出不同防禦，因為不同動物以不同方式攻擊它們。"},{"en":"The phrase shows slow development of many types of solutions.","zh":"這個短語顯示許多類型方案的緩慢發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"chemical defences","meaning":"化學防禦機制","examples":[{"en":"Plants use chemical defences against leaf-eating animals.","zh":"植物使用化學防禦機制對抗食葉動物。"},{"en":"Chemical defences are substances produced by living things to protect themselves from being eaten or harmed.","zh":"chemical defences 指生物產生、用來保護自己免被吃掉或傷害的物質。"},{"en":"Some plants use bitter chemicals as chemical defences so insects avoid them.","zh":"有些植物使用苦味化學物作為化學防禦，使昆蟲避開它們。"},{"en":"Chemical defences can reduce damage because animals learn that certain leaves taste bad or are toxic.","zh":"化學防禦機制可以減少傷害，因為動物會學到某些葉子味道差或有毒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes protection through chemicals, not physical barriers.","zh":"這個短語描述透過化學物保護，而不是物理屏障。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ranging from X to Y","meaning":"由 X 到 Y 不等","examples":[{"en":"Plant defences range from bad-tasting tannins to deadly poisons.","zh":"植物防禦機制由味道難聞的單寧到致命毒素不等。"},{"en":"Ranging from X to Y means including many types between one example and another.","zh":"ranging from X to Y 指包括由一個例子到另一個例子之間的許多類型。"},{"en":"School activities may range from quiet reading to outdoor sports.","zh":"學校活動可能由安靜閱讀到戶外運動不等。"},{"en":"The phrase shows variety by giving a lower or simpler example and a stronger or more extreme one.","zh":"這個短語透過給出較低或較簡單例子，以及較強或較極端例子來顯示多樣性。"},{"en":"It helps readers understand the full spread of possibilities.","zh":"它幫助讀者理解可能性的完整範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"bad-tasting tannins","meaning":"味道難聞的單寧","examples":[{"en":"Bad-tasting tannins can make leaves harder to digest.","zh":"味道難聞的單寧可以令葉子較難消化。"},{"en":"Bad-tasting tannins are bitter plant chemicals that can discourage animals from eating leaves.","zh":"bad-tasting tannins 指苦味植物化學物，可以阻止動物吃葉子。"},{"en":"Tea can taste bitter partly because it contains tannins.","zh":"茶有時帶苦味，部分原因是它含有單寧。"},{"en":"Tannins protect plants because animals may avoid leaves that taste unpleasant or reduce digestion.","zh":"單寧保護植物，因為動物可能避開味道差或降低消化的葉子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one type of plant chemical defence.","zh":"這個短語描述一種植物化學防禦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"bind with","meaning":"與……結合","examples":[{"en":"Tannins bind with plant-produced nutrients.","zh":"單寧與植物產生的營養物質結合。"},{"en":"To bind with something means to attach or combine chemically with it.","zh":"bind with something 指以化學方式附着或結合於某物。"},{"en":"In cooking, some ingredients bind with water and make a sauce thicker.","zh":"在烹飪中，有些材料會與水結合，使醬汁變稠。"},{"en":"When tannins bind with nutrients, animals may not be able to digest those nutrients well.","zh":"當單寧與營養物質結合，動物可能無法好好消化那些營養。"},{"en":"The phrase describes joining together at a chemical or physical level.","zh":"這個短語描述在化學或物理層面結合在一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"plant-produced nutrients","meaning":"植物產生的營養物質","examples":[{"en":"Tannins bind with plant-produced nutrients in leaves.","zh":"單寧與葉子中植物產生的營養物質結合。"},{"en":"Plant-produced nutrients are useful substances made by plants that animals may eat and absorb.","zh":"plant-produced nutrients 指植物製造、動物可能進食和吸收的有用物質。"},{"en":"Fruit, seeds, and leaves all contain plant-produced nutrients.","zh":"果實、種子和葉子都含有植物產生的營養物質。"},{"en":"If chemicals make plant-produced nutrients hard to digest, leaf-eaters get less benefit from eating leaves.","zh":"如果化學物令植物產生的營養物質難以消化，食葉動物從葉子中得到的好處就較少。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to nutrients created by the plant itself.","zh":"這個短語指由植物本身製造的營養。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"render something indigestible","meaning":"令……不能被消化","examples":[{"en":"Tannins render some plant nutrients indigestible.","zh":"單寧令某些植物營養物質不能被消化。"},{"en":"To render something indigestible means to make it impossible or difficult for the body to digest.","zh":"render something indigestible 指令某物變得無法或難以被身體消化。"},{"en":"Overcooking food can sometimes render it less pleasant, but toxins can render nutrients indigestible.","zh":"過度烹調食物有時會令它較不好吃，但毒素可以令營養不能被消化。"},{"en":"When plant chemicals render nutrients indigestible, animals must eat more or choose different leaves.","zh":"當植物化學物令營養不能被消化，動物就必須吃更多或選擇其他葉子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing something into a form the body cannot use easily.","zh":"這個短語描述把某物變成身體不易使用的形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"deadly poisons","meaning":"致命毒素","examples":[{"en":"Some plants produce deadly poisons such as alkaloids and cyanide.","zh":"有些植物產生生物鹼和氰化物等致命毒素。"},{"en":"Deadly poisons are substances that can kill living things if taken in enough quantity.","zh":"deadly poisons 指如果攝入足夠份量就能殺死生物的物質。"},{"en":"A warning label may tell children not to touch bottles that contain deadly poisons.","zh":"警告標籤可能提醒孩子不要觸碰含有致命毒素的瓶子。"},{"en":"Plants produce deadly poisons to stop animals from eating them.","zh":"植物產生致命毒素，以阻止動物吃掉它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extremely dangerous toxic substances.","zh":"這個短語描述極危險的有毒物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"alkaloids and cyanide","meaning":"生物鹼和氰化物","examples":[{"en":"Alkaloids and cyanide are examples of plant poisons.","zh":"生物鹼和氰化物是植物毒素的例子。"},{"en":"Alkaloids and cyanide are chemicals that some plants produce and that can be toxic to animals.","zh":"alkaloids and cyanide 指一些植物會產生、並可能對動物有毒的化學物。"},{"en":"A science lesson may discuss alkaloids and cyanide when explaining how plants defend themselves.","zh":"科學課解釋植物如何防禦自己時，可能討論生物鹼和氰化物。"},{"en":"Such chemicals can discourage feeding because animals may become sick or die after eating them.","zh":"這類化學物可以阻止進食，因為動物吃下後可能生病或死亡。"},{"en":"The phrase names two kinds of chemical plant defence.","zh":"這個短語命名兩種植物化學防禦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have some ability to","meaning":"有一定能力去……","examples":[{"en":"All primates have some ability to handle plant toxins.","zh":"所有靈長類動物都有一定能力處理植物毒素。"},{"en":"To have some ability to do something means to be partly capable of doing it, though not perfectly.","zh":"have some ability to do something 指有部分能力做某事，但未必完美。"},{"en":"A beginner may have some ability to read English signs even if she cannot understand long articles.","zh":"初學者可能有一定能力閱讀英文標誌，即使不能理解長文章。"},{"en":"Some ability can make survival possible, but stronger ability gives a clearer advantage.","zh":"一定能力可以令生存成為可能，但更強能力帶來更明顯優勢。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests limited but real capacity.","zh":"這個短語暗示有限但真實的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"handle plant toxins","meaning":"處理植物毒素","examples":[{"en":"Primates have some ability to handle plant toxins.","zh":"靈長類動物有一定能力處理植物毒素。"},{"en":"To handle plant toxins means to tolerate, break down, or reduce the harm of poisonous plant chemicals.","zh":"handle plant toxins 指忍受、分解或減低有毒植物化學物的傷害。"},{"en":"Some animals handle plant toxins by eating only small amounts of certain leaves.","zh":"有些動物透過只吃少量某些葉子來處理植物毒素。"},{"en":"If an animal cannot handle plant toxins, it may become sick after feeding.","zh":"如果動物不能處理植物毒素，牠進食後可能生病。"},{"en":"The phrase describes biological tolerance and detoxification.","zh":"這個短語描述生物耐受力和解毒能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"detoxify a dangerous poison","meaning":"為危險毒物解毒","examples":[{"en":"Humans can detoxify a dangerous poison known as caffeine.","zh":"人類能為一種被稱為咖啡因的危險毒物解毒。"},{"en":"To detoxify a dangerous poison means to change or break down a harmful substance so it becomes less harmful.","zh":"detoxify a dangerous poison 指改變或分解有害物質，使其變得較不有害。"},{"en":"The liver helps people detoxify many substances that enter the body.","zh":"肝臟幫助人類為許多進入身體的物質解毒。"},{"en":"If an animal can detoxify a poison, it may eat plants that other animals avoid.","zh":"如果動物能為毒物解毒，牠可能吃其他動物避開的植物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reducing toxicity inside the body.","zh":"這個短語描述在身體內降低毒性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"known as","meaning":"被稱為……","examples":[{"en":"Humans can detoxify a dangerous poison known as caffeine.","zh":"人類能為一種被稱為咖啡因的危險毒物解毒。"},{"en":"Known as means called by a particular name.","zh":"known as 指以某個特定名稱稱呼。"},{"en":"The city is known as a financial centre because many banks are based there.","zh":"該城市被稱為金融中心，因為許多銀行都設於那裏。"},{"en":"Scientific names help people identify substances, animals, or places more precisely.","zh":"科學名稱幫助人們更精確識別物質、動物或地方。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the name by which something is recognised.","zh":"這個短語引入某事物被認識的名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be deadly to","meaning":"對……致命","examples":[{"en":"Caffeine is deadly to many animals.","zh":"咖啡因對許多動物致命。"},{"en":"To be deadly to something means to be able to kill it.","zh":"be deadly to something 指能夠殺死某生物。"},{"en":"Chocolate can be deadly to dogs if they eat too much of it.","zh":"如果狗吃太多朱古力，朱古力可能對狗致命。"},{"en":"A substance that is safe for humans may still be deadly to smaller animals.","zh":"對人類安全的物質，仍可能對較小動物致命。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a serious danger to life.","zh":"這個短語描述對生命的嚴重危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"long-term exposure to","meaning":"長期接觸……","examples":[{"en":"Long-term exposure to a plant toxin can improve a leaf-eater’s tolerance.","zh":"長期接觸植物毒素可以改善食葉動物的耐受力。"},{"en":"Long-term exposure to something means repeated or continuous contact with it over a long period.","zh":"long-term exposure to something 指長時間反覆或持續接觸某物。"},{"en":"Long-term exposure to loud noise can damage a worker’s hearing.","zh":"長期接觸巨大噪音可以損害工人的聽力。"},{"en":"Repeated exposure can sometimes help the body adapt, but it can also cause harm depending on the substance.","zh":"反覆接觸有時可以幫助身體適應，但也可能造成傷害，視乎物質而定。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses duration and repeated contact.","zh":"這個短語強調持續時間和反覆接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a specific plant toxin","meaning":"某種特定植物毒素","examples":[{"en":"Leaf-eaters may adapt to a specific plant toxin.","zh":"食葉動物可能適應某種特定植物毒素。"},{"en":"A specific plant toxin is one particular poisonous chemical produced by a plant.","zh":"specific plant toxin 指植物產生的某一種特定有毒化學物。"},{"en":"A scientist may test whether an insect can survive after eating a specific plant toxin.","zh":"科學家可能測試昆蟲吃下某種特定植物毒素後能否生存。"},{"en":"Animals may tolerate one toxin but still be harmed by another.","zh":"動物可能能忍受一種毒素，但仍受另一種毒素傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows the meaning to one exact plant poison.","zh":"這個短語把意思收窄到一種確切植物毒物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"increase someone’s ability to","meaning":"提升某人……的能力","examples":[{"en":"Exposure can increase a monkey’s ability to neutralise the poison.","zh":"接觸可以提升猴子中和毒素的能力。"},{"en":"To increase someone’s ability to do something means to make that person or animal better able to do it.","zh":"increase someone’s ability to do something 指令某人或動物更能做到某事。"},{"en":"Regular speaking practice can increase a student’s ability to answer questions naturally.","zh":"定期口語練習可以提升學生自然回答問題的能力。"},{"en":"Repeated experience can increase ability because the body or mind learns to respond better.","zh":"反覆經驗可以提升能力，因為身體或頭腦學會更好回應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improvement in capacity.","zh":"這個短語描述能力提升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"neutralise the poison","meaning":"中和毒素","examples":[{"en":"Leaf-eaters can neutralise the poison and absorb nutrients.","zh":"食葉動物可以中和毒素並吸收營養。"},{"en":"To neutralise the poison means to reduce or remove its harmful effect.","zh":"neutralise the poison 指減少或消除毒素的有害作用。"},{"en":"Doctors may give treatment to neutralise poison after a patient swallows something toxic.","zh":"病人吞下有毒物質後，醫生可能給予治療來中和毒素。"},{"en":"If animals can neutralise a plant poison, they can use food that would harm other species.","zh":"如果動物能中和植物毒素，牠們就能使用會傷害其他物種的食物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a poison less dangerous.","zh":"這個短語描述令毒素較不危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"absorb the leaf nutrients","meaning":"吸收樹葉中的營養","examples":[{"en":"Some monkeys can absorb the leaf nutrients after neutralising toxins.","zh":"有些猴子在中和毒素後能吸收樹葉中的營養。"},{"en":"To absorb the leaf nutrients means to take useful substances from leaves into the body.","zh":"absorb the leaf nutrients 指把葉子中的有用物質吸收到身體裏。"},{"en":"Children absorb nutrients from food after the digestive system breaks it down.","zh":"消化系統分解食物後，孩子從食物中吸收營養。"},{"en":"If toxins block digestion, animals cannot absorb the leaf nutrients effectively.","zh":"如果毒素阻礙消化，動物就不能有效吸收樹葉中的營養。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gaining useful food value from leaves.","zh":"這個短語描述從葉子中取得有用食物價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"regenerating forests","meaning":"正在再生的森林","examples":[{"en":"The leaves in regenerating forests are more howler-friendly.","zh":"正在再生的森林中的葉子較適合吼猴。"},{"en":"Regenerating forests are forests growing back after damage, clearing, farming, or fire.","zh":"regenerating forests 指在破壞、砍伐、耕作或火災後重新生長的森林。"},{"en":"A hillside can become a regenerating forest when farmers stop cutting trees and young plants return.","zh":"當農民停止砍樹、幼植物重新出現，山坡可以變成正在再生的森林。"},{"en":"Regenerating forests often have young trees, which may produce leaves with fewer toxins.","zh":"正在再生的森林通常有年輕樹木，而這些樹可能產生毒素較少的葉子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes forest recovery.","zh":"這個短語描述森林恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"howler-friendly","meaning":"較適合吼猴的","examples":[{"en":"Young forest leaves are more howler-friendly than leaves from old-growth trees.","zh":"年輕森林的葉子比老林樹木的葉子更適合吼猴。"},{"en":"Howler-friendly means suitable or helpful for howler monkeys.","zh":"howler-friendly 指適合或有利於吼猴。"},{"en":"A farm with shade trees may become more howler-friendly if monkeys can find safe branches and edible leaves.","zh":"如果猴子能找到安全樹枝和可吃葉子，有遮蔭樹的農場可能變得較適合吼猴。"},{"en":"Younger leaves may be howler-friendly because they contain fewer toxins and are easier to digest.","zh":"較年輕葉子可能較適合吼猴，因為它們含有較少毒素並較易消化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes conditions that support howler survival.","zh":"這個短語描述支持吼猴生存的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"undisturbed, centuries-old trees","meaning":"未受干擾、已有數百年歷史的樹木","examples":[{"en":"Undisturbed, centuries-old trees produce leaves with higher toxin levels.","zh":"未受干擾、已有數百年歷史的樹木會產生毒素水平較高的葉子。"},{"en":"Undisturbed, centuries-old trees are very old trees that have grown for hundreds of years without major human damage.","zh":"undisturbed, centuries-old trees 指已生長數百年且沒有受到重大人為破壞的古老樹木。"},{"en":"A protected forest may contain undisturbed, centuries-old trees that shelter many species.","zh":"受保護森林可能有未受干擾、已有數百年歷史的樹木，為許多物種提供庇護。"},{"en":"Old trees may invest more energy in chemical defence because they are well established.","zh":"老樹可能把更多能量投放在化學防禦上，因為它們根基穩固。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests age, stability, and little human interference.","zh":"這個短語暗示年齡、穩定性和很少人類干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the Amazon Basin","meaning":"亞馬遜盆地","examples":[{"en":"The Amazon Basin contains undisturbed, centuries-old trees.","zh":"亞馬遜盆地有未受干擾、已有數百年歷史的樹木。"},{"en":"The Amazon Basin is the large region drained by the Amazon River and its tributaries in South America.","zh":"Amazon Basin 指南美洲由亞馬遜河及其支流排水形成的廣大地區。"},{"en":"Scientists study the Amazon Basin because it contains huge forests and extraordinary biodiversity.","zh":"科學家研究亞馬遜盆地，因為它有巨大森林和非凡生物多樣性。"},{"en":"Forest loss in the Amazon Basin can affect climate, wildlife, and local communities.","zh":"亞馬遜盆地的森林流失可以影響氣候、野生動物和本地社區。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a major tropical region, not just the river itself.","zh":"這個短語指主要熱帶地區，而不只是河流本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put energy into","meaning":"把能量投放於……","examples":[{"en":"Younger trees put most of their limited energy into growth.","zh":"年輕樹木把大部分有限能量投放於生長。"},{"en":"To put energy into something means to use effort, resources, or biological energy for that purpose.","zh":"put energy into something 指把努力、資源或生物能量用於某目的。"},{"en":"A student may put energy into vocabulary review before a speaking exam.","zh":"學生可能在口試前把精力投放於詞彙溫習。"},{"en":"Young trees put energy into growth because becoming taller helps them reach sunlight.","zh":"年輕樹木把能量投放於生長，因為長高能幫助它們接觸陽光。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where effort or resources are directed.","zh":"這個短語描述努力或資源被導向哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"limited energy","meaning":"有限的能量","examples":[{"en":"Young trees have limited energy for both growth and chemical defence.","zh":"年輕樹木沒有足夠能量同時用於生長和化學防禦。"},{"en":"Limited energy means there is not enough energy to do everything fully.","zh":"limited energy 指沒有足夠能量完全做所有事情。"},{"en":"A student with limited energy after school may choose one important task instead of five small ones.","zh":"放學後精力有限的學生，可能選擇做一項重要任務，而不是五項小任務。"},{"en":"If trees have limited energy, spending more on growth may mean spending less on toxins.","zh":"如果樹木能量有限，把更多用於生長可能意味較少用於毒素。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the need to make trade-offs.","zh":"這個短語突出需要作出取捨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"produce lower levels of toxin","meaning":"產生較低水平的毒素","examples":[{"en":"Younger trees produce much lower levels of toxin.","zh":"年輕樹木產生低得多的毒素水平。"},{"en":"To produce lower levels of toxin means to make a smaller amount of poisonous chemicals.","zh":"produce lower levels of toxin 指製造較少量的有毒化學物。"},{"en":"Some food plants produce lower levels of bitter chemicals when they are young and tender.","zh":"有些食用植物在年輕柔嫩時產生較低水平的苦味化學物。"},{"en":"Lower toxin levels make leaves easier for animals to eat and digest.","zh":"較低毒素水平令葉子較易被動物吃下和消化。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the amount of harmful substances produced.","zh":"這個短語比較有害物質的產生量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"well-established, old-growth trees","meaning":"根基穩固的老林樹木","examples":[{"en":"Well-established, old-growth trees produce more toxins.","zh":"根基穩固的老林樹木會產生更多毒素。"},{"en":"Well-established, old-growth trees are mature trees in old forests that have had a long time to grow strong.","zh":"well-established, old-growth trees 指老林中成熟、已有長時間長得強壯的樹木。"},{"en":"A national park may protect well-established, old-growth trees because they support many animals.","zh":"國家公園可能保護根基穩固的老林樹木，因為它們支持許多動物。"},{"en":"Such trees may invest more in defence because they have already reached a stable size.","zh":"這類樹可能把更多能量投放於防禦，因為它們已達穩定大小。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mature, long-standing forest trees.","zh":"這個短語描述成熟、長期存在的森林樹木。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"maturing forests","meaning":"逐漸成熟的森林","examples":[{"en":"The importance of maturing forests to primates is studied at Santa Rosa National Park.","zh":"逐漸成熟的森林對靈長類動物的重要性，正在 Santa Rosa 國家公園被研究。"},{"en":"Maturing forests are forests that are growing older and gradually becoming more developed.","zh":"maturing forests 指正在變老並逐漸發展成熟的森林。"},{"en":"A former farm can become a maturing forest after young trees grow for many years.","zh":"年輕樹木生長多年後，昔日農地可以變成逐漸成熟的森林。"},{"en":"As forests mature, branches become stronger and food resources may change.","zh":"隨着森林成熟，樹枝變得更強壯，食物資源也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes forests between young regrowth and old-growth forest.","zh":"這個短語描述介乎年輕再生林和老林之間的森林。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a subject of study","meaning":"研究課題","examples":[{"en":"Maturing forests are a subject of study at Santa Rosa National Park.","zh":"逐漸成熟的森林是 Santa Rosa 國家公園的一個研究課題。"},{"en":"A subject of study is a topic that researchers examine carefully.","zh":"subject of study 指研究人員仔細考察的主題。"},{"en":"Student stress has become a subject of study in many schools.","zh":"學生壓力已成為許多學校的研究課題。"},{"en":"A topic becomes a subject of study when people need evidence rather than guesses.","zh":"當人們需要證據而不是猜測，某主題就會成為研究課題。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what researchers are investigating.","zh":"這個短語指出研究人員正在調查甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"host populations of","meaning":"擁有……的種群","examples":[{"en":"The park hosts populations of several monkey species.","zh":"該公園擁有幾種猴子的種群。"},{"en":"To host populations of animals means to provide a place where groups of those animals live.","zh":"host populations of animals 指提供某些動物群體生活的地方。"},{"en":"A wetland may host populations of frogs, birds, and insects.","zh":"濕地可能擁有青蛙、鳥類和昆蟲的種群。"},{"en":"Protected areas host wildlife populations because they offer food, space, and reduced human disturbance.","zh":"保護區擁有野生動物種群，因為它們提供食物、空間和較少人類干擾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an area supporting living groups of species.","zh":"這個短語描述某地支持物種群體生存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not only...but also","meaning":"不但……而且……","examples":[{"en":"The park hosts populations not only of howlers but also of capuchins and spider monkeys.","zh":"該公園不但擁有吼猴種群，而且也有卷尾猴和蜘蛛猴種群。"},{"en":"Not only A but also B means both A and B are true or included.","zh":"not only A but also B 指 A 和 B 都是真的或都包括在內。"},{"en":"A good school supports not only exam results but also students’ mental health.","zh":"好學校不但支持考試成績，而且也支持學生心理健康。"},{"en":"This structure adds emphasis by showing that the second point is also important.","zh":"這個結構透過顯示第二點同樣重要來加強語氣。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful for connecting two related facts.","zh":"這個短語適合連接兩個相關事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reborn forests","meaning":"重生的森林","examples":[{"en":"Capuchins were the first monkeys to use the reborn forests.","zh":"卷尾猴是首批使用重生森林的猴子。"},{"en":"Reborn forests are forests that have grown back after being damaged, cleared, or abandoned.","zh":"reborn forests 指在受破壞、被砍清或被棄置後重新長回來的森林。"},{"en":"A hillside covered with young trees after years of farming can become a reborn forest.","zh":"經過多年耕作後長滿年輕樹木的山坡，可以成為重生的森林。"},{"en":"Reborn forests can offer new habitat as trees return and animals move back in.","zh":"隨着樹木回歸和動物遷回，重生森林可以提供新棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase presents forest recovery as a kind of new life.","zh":"這個短語把森林恢復呈現為一種新生命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as young as","meaning":"年齡低至……","examples":[{"en":"The trees were as young as 14 years when capuchins began using them.","zh":"當卷尾猴開始使用這些樹時，樹木年齡低至14年。"},{"en":"As young as a certain age means only that age, which may be younger than expected.","zh":"as young as a certain age 指只有該年齡，可能比預期年輕。"},{"en":"Children as young as five may learn basic coding through simple games.","zh":"年齡低至五歲的孩子，可能透過簡單遊戲學習基本編程。"},{"en":"If monkeys use forests as young as 14 years, early forest recovery may already provide useful habitat.","zh":"如果猴子使用低至14年的森林，早期森林恢復可能已提供有用棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a surprisingly low age.","zh":"這個短語突出令人意外的低年齡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"larger and heavier than","meaning":"比……更大、更重","examples":[{"en":"Howlers are larger and heavier than capuchins.","zh":"吼猴比卷尾猴更大、更重。"},{"en":"Larger and heavier than means bigger in size and greater in weight than another thing.","zh":"larger and heavier than 指比另一物體體型更大、重量更重。"},{"en":"A school bus is larger and heavier than a private car.","zh":"校巴比私家車更大、更重。"},{"en":"Heavier animals need stronger branches, so forest structure affects where they can move.","zh":"較重的動物需要更強壯的樹枝，所以森林結構影響牠們能在哪裏移動。"},{"en":"The phrase compares both body size and weight.","zh":"這個短語同時比較體型和重量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"limbs that can support","meaning":"能支撐……的樹枝","examples":[{"en":"Howlers need limbs that can support their body weight.","zh":"吼猴需要能支撐其體重的樹枝。"},{"en":"Limbs that can support something are branches strong enough to hold that weight.","zh":"limbs that can support something 指強壯到能承托該重量的樹枝。"},{"en":"A child should not climb a tree unless the limbs can support her safely.","zh":"除非樹枝能安全支撐孩子，否則孩子不應爬樹。"},{"en":"If branches cannot support a monkey’s weight, the animal may fall or avoid that tree.","zh":"如果樹枝不能支撐猴子的重量，動物可能跌下或避開該樹。"},{"en":"The phrase describes structural strength needed for movement.","zh":"這個短語描述移動所需的結構強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"greater body weight","meaning":"較大的體重","examples":[{"en":"Older trees can support the howlers’ greater body weight.","zh":"較老的樹能支撐吼猴較大的體重。"},{"en":"Greater body weight means a heavier body compared with another animal or group.","zh":"greater body weight 指與另一動物或群體相比更重的身體重量。"},{"en":"A larger dog has greater body weight than a small cat, so it needs a stronger leash.","zh":"大型狗比小貓有較大的體重，所以需要更堅固的牽繩。"},{"en":"Greater body weight affects how animals move, feed, and choose resting places.","zh":"較大的體重影響動物如何移動、覓食和選擇休息地點。"},{"en":"The phrase compares weight and its practical effects.","zh":"這個短語比較重量及其實際影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"conditions observed at","meaning":"在……觀察到的情況","examples":[{"en":"Conditions observed at Hacienda La Pacifica help explain the population boom.","zh":"在 Hacienda La Pacifica 觀察到的情況有助解釋種群激增。"},{"en":"Conditions observed at a place are the features or facts researchers notice there.","zh":"conditions observed at a place 指研究人員在某地注意到的特徵或事實。"},{"en":"Conditions observed at a school, such as class size and homework load, can explain student stress.","zh":"在學校觀察到的情況，例如班級大小和功課量，可以解釋學生壓力。"},{"en":"Scientists use observed conditions to connect evidence with patterns in animal populations.","zh":"科學家使用觀察到的情況，把證據與動物種群模式連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes findings based on direct observation.","zh":"這個短語描述基於直接觀察的發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"help explain","meaning":"有助解釋","examples":[{"en":"The ranch conditions help explain the howler population boom in Santa Rosa.","zh":"牧場情況有助解釋 Santa Rosa 的吼猴種群激增。"},{"en":"To help explain something means to provide part of the reason for understanding it.","zh":"help explain something 指提供部分原因，使人更能理解某事。"},{"en":"A student’s lack of sleep may help explain why her test score fell.","zh":"學生睡眠不足可能有助解釋她測驗成績下降。"},{"en":"Evidence often helps explain a pattern without being the only cause.","zh":"證據通常有助解釋某模式，但不一定是唯一原因。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something gives useful support to an explanation.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事為解釋提供有用支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"population boom","meaning":"種群激增","examples":[{"en":"Howlers experienced a population boom in Santa Rosa.","zh":"吼猴在 Santa Rosa 經歷種群激增。"},{"en":"A population boom is a rapid increase in the number of individuals in a group or species.","zh":"population boom 指某群體或物種個體數量快速增加。"},{"en":"A town may experience a population boom after a new railway station opens nearby.","zh":"新火車站在附近開通後，城鎮可能經歷人口激增。"},{"en":"Animal population booms happen when food, shelter, and reproduction conditions improve.","zh":"當食物、庇護和繁殖條件改善，動物種群可能激增。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fast growth in numbers.","zh":"這個短語描述數量快速增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be more resilient than","meaning":"比……更具適應力","examples":[{"en":"Howlers are more resilient than capuchins and spider monkeys.","zh":"吼猴比卷尾猴和蜘蛛猴更具適應力。"},{"en":"To be more resilient than another species means to recover, adapt, or survive better under difficult conditions.","zh":"be more resilient than another species 指在困難情況下更能恢復、適應或生存。"},{"en":"Some students are more resilient than others because they ask for help after failure.","zh":"有些學生比其他人更具抗逆力，因為失敗後會尋求幫助。"},{"en":"Howlers are more resilient because they can eat leaves, use small areas, and reproduce quickly.","zh":"吼猴更具適應力，因為牠們能吃葉、使用小範圍並快速繁殖。"},{"en":"The phrase compares ability to cope with stress or change.","zh":"這個短語比較應對壓力或改變的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"live within a small home range","meaning":"在細小活動範圍內生活","examples":[{"en":"Howlers can live within a small home range.","zh":"吼猴可以在細小活動範圍內生活。"},{"en":"To live within a small home range means to survive in a limited area where an animal normally moves, feeds, and rests.","zh":"live within a small home range 指在動物通常移動、覓食和休息的有限區域中生存。"},{"en":"A city cat may live within a small home range around one block and a garden.","zh":"城市貓可能在一個街區和一個花園附近的小活動範圍內生活。"},{"en":"Animals with small home ranges can survive better when forests are fragmented.","zh":"活動範圍小的動物，在森林破碎化時較能生存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limited space needs.","zh":"這個短語描述對空間需求有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as long as","meaning":"只要……","examples":[{"en":"Howlers can live within a small home range as long as the trees have the right food.","zh":"只要樹木有合適食物，吼猴就能在細小活動範圍內生活。"},{"en":"As long as means provided that or if this condition is met.","zh":"as long as 指只要某條件被滿足。"},{"en":"Students can use phones in class as long as they are using them for learning.","zh":"只要學生把手機用於學習，他們就可以在課堂中使用手機。"},{"en":"A small habitat can support monkeys as long as it contains enough safe food.","zh":"只要小型棲息地含有足夠安全食物，就能支持猴子。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the condition that makes something possible.","zh":"這個短語引入令某事成為可能的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"Spider monkeys, on the other hand, occupy a huge home range.","zh":"另一方面，蜘蛛猴佔用很大的活動範圍。"},{"en":"On the other hand introduces a contrasting point.","zh":"on the other hand 引入對比重點。"},{"en":"Some students like group work; on the other hand, others prefer studying alone.","zh":"有些學生喜歡小組工作；另一方面，其他學生較喜歡獨自學習。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare two different situations or opinions clearly.","zh":"這個短語幫助清楚比較兩種不同情況或意見。"},{"en":"It signals that the next idea is different from the previous one.","zh":"它表示下一個想法與前一個不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"occupy a huge home range","meaning":"佔用很大的活動範圍","examples":[{"en":"Spider monkeys occupy a huge home range.","zh":"蜘蛛猴佔用很大的活動範圍。"},{"en":"To occupy a huge home range means to use a very large area for feeding, moving, and living.","zh":"occupy a huge home range 指使用非常大的區域來覓食、移動和生活。"},{"en":"A wild dog pack may occupy a huge home range if prey is spread out.","zh":"如果獵物分布分散，野狗群可能佔用很大的活動範圍。"},{"en":"Animals with huge home ranges suffer when roads and farms cut their habitat into small pieces.","zh":"活動範圍很大的動物，在道路和農地把棲息地切成小塊時會受害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a species’ need for large space.","zh":"這個短語描述物種對大空間的需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make it in fragmented habitat","meaning":"在破碎化棲息地生存下來","examples":[{"en":"Spider monkeys cannot make it in fragmented habitat.","zh":"蜘蛛猴無法在破碎化棲息地生存下來。"},{"en":"To make it in a habitat means to survive successfully there.","zh":"make it in a habitat 指在某棲息地成功生存。"},{"en":"A small shop may not make it in an expensive district if rent is too high.","zh":"如果租金太高，小店可能無法在昂貴地區生存下來。"},{"en":"Fragmented habitat makes survival hard because animals cannot move easily between food sources.","zh":"破碎化棲息地令生存困難，因為動物不能輕易在食物來源之間移動。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and means manage to survive.","zh":"這個短語較口語，意思是設法生存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reproduce faster than","meaning":"比……繁殖得更快","examples":[{"en":"Howlers reproduce faster than other monkey species in the area.","zh":"吼猴比該地區其他猴子物種繁殖得更快。"},{"en":"To reproduce faster than another species means to have babies more often or at a younger age.","zh":"reproduce faster than another species 指比另一物種更頻繁或更早生育後代。"},{"en":"Some insects reproduce faster than birds because they lay many eggs in a short time.","zh":"有些昆蟲比鳥類繁殖得更快，因為牠們短時間內產下許多卵。"},{"en":"Faster reproduction helps a species recover after losses or expand when conditions improve.","zh":"較快繁殖幫助物種在損失後恢復，或在條件改善時擴張。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the speed of population growth.","zh":"這個短語比較種群增長速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bear their first young","meaning":"首次產仔","examples":[{"en":"Capuchins do not bear their first young until about seven years old.","zh":"卷尾猴直到約七歲才首次產仔。"},{"en":"To bear their first young means to give birth to their first baby or offspring.","zh":"bear their first young 指生下第一個嬰兒或後代。"},{"en":"Some animals bear their first young only after they reach full physical maturity.","zh":"有些動物只有在身體完全成熟後才首次產仔。"},{"en":"Species that bear their first young late may recover slowly when numbers fall.","zh":"較遲首次產仔的物種，在數量下降時可能恢復較慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the first reproductive event in an animal’s life.","zh":"這個短語描述動物生命中的第一次繁殖事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"do so even later","meaning":"更遲才這樣做","examples":[{"en":"Spider monkeys do so even later than capuchins.","zh":"蜘蛛猴甚至比卷尾猴更遲才這樣做。"},{"en":"Do so even later means perform the same action at an even later time.","zh":"do so even later 指在更遲時間做同一件事。"},{"en":"Some students start revision late, and others do so even later, just before the exam.","zh":"有些學生很遲才開始溫習，而其他人更遲才這樣做，直到考試前才開始。"},{"en":"If a species reproduces later, its population may grow more slowly.","zh":"如果物種較遲繁殖，其種群可能增長較慢。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to a previously mentioned action.","zh":"這個短語指回前文提及的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"give birth for the first time","meaning":"首次生育","examples":[{"en":"Howlers give birth for the first time at about 3.5 years of age.","zh":"吼猴約在3.5歲首次生育。"},{"en":"To give birth for the first time means to have one’s first baby or offspring.","zh":"give birth for the first time 指生下第一個嬰兒或後代。"},{"en":"A vet may record when an animal gives birth for the first time to understand its breeding cycle.","zh":"獸醫可能記錄動物首次生育的時間，以了解其繁殖週期。"},{"en":"Earlier first birth can increase population growth because females start reproducing sooner.","zh":"較早首次生育可以增加種群增長，因為雌性更早開始繁殖。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the beginning of reproduction.","zh":"這個短語標示繁殖的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"well-fed howlers","meaning":"營養充足的吼猴","examples":[{"en":"Well-fed howlers can produce an infant every two years.","zh":"營養充足的吼猴可以每兩年誕下一隻幼猴。"},{"en":"Well-fed howlers are howler monkeys that receive enough food and nutrition.","zh":"well-fed howlers 指獲得足夠食物和營養的吼猴。"},{"en":"Well-fed students are more likely to concentrate in class than hungry ones.","zh":"營養充足的學生比飢餓學生較能在課堂上專心。"},{"en":"When animals are well-fed, they often reproduce more successfully.","zh":"當動物營養充足，牠們通常能更成功繁殖。"},{"en":"The phrase connects good nutrition with health and reproduction.","zh":"這個短語把良好營養與健康和繁殖連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"produce an infant every two years","meaning":"每兩年誕下一隻幼猴","examples":[{"en":"Well-fed howlers can produce an infant every two years.","zh":"營養充足的吼猴可以每兩年誕下一隻幼猴。"},{"en":"To produce an infant every two years means to have one baby roughly once in a two-year period.","zh":"produce an infant every two years 指大約每兩年生下一隻幼猴。"},{"en":"A breeding programme may record whether an animal produces an infant every two years or less often.","zh":"繁殖計劃可能記錄動物是否每兩年誕下一隻幼獸，或繁殖較不頻密。"},{"en":"Frequent births help a population grow faster when enough food is available.","zh":"當有足夠食物，頻繁生育幫助種群更快增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reproductive rate.","zh":"這個短語描述繁殖率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hold plenty of water","meaning":"含有大量水分","examples":[{"en":"The leaves howlers eat hold plenty of water.","zh":"吼猴所吃的葉子含有大量水分。"},{"en":"To hold plenty of water means to contain a large amount of water.","zh":"hold plenty of water 指含有大量水。"},{"en":"Watermelon holds plenty of water, so it feels refreshing on a hot day.","zh":"西瓜含有大量水分，所以在熱天吃起來很清爽。"},{"en":"Leaves with high water content help animals survive when streams dry up.","zh":"含水量高的葉子幫助動物在溪流乾涸時生存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes water stored inside food or material.","zh":"這個短語描述食物或材料內儲存的水分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"survive away from","meaning":"遠離……仍能生存","examples":[{"en":"Howlers can survive away from open streams and waterholes.","zh":"吼猴遠離露天溪流和水坑仍能生存。"},{"en":"To survive away from something means to continue living without being close to it.","zh":"survive away from something 指不靠近某物也能繼續生活。"},{"en":"Some workers can survive away from the office if they have internet and a quiet room.","zh":"如果有互聯網和安靜房間，有些員工遠離辦公室仍能工作。"},{"en":"Animals that get water from food can survive away from rivers during dry periods.","zh":"能從食物中取得水分的動物，在乾旱時期能遠離河流仍然生存。"},{"en":"The phrase shows independence from a nearby resource.","zh":"這個短語顯示不依賴附近資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"open streams and waterholes","meaning":"露天溪流和水坑","examples":[{"en":"Howlers can live away from open streams and waterholes.","zh":"吼猴可以遠離露天溪流和水坑生活。"},{"en":"Open streams and waterholes are exposed sources of water that animals can drink from.","zh":"open streams and waterholes 指暴露在外、動物可以飲用的水源。"},{"en":"During a school hike, students may see open streams and waterholes along the trail.","zh":"學生在學校遠足期間，可能沿路看到露天溪流和水坑。"},{"en":"Animals that rely on open streams and waterholes suffer when drought dries them up.","zh":"依賴露天溪流和水坑的動物，在乾旱令它們乾涸時會受苦。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to visible natural water sources.","zh":"這個短語指可見的自然水源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"give someone a real advantage over","meaning":"令某人比……有明顯優勢","examples":[{"en":"This ability gives howlers a real advantage over other monkeys.","zh":"這種能力令吼猴比其他猴子有明顯優勢。"},{"en":"To give someone a real advantage over others means to make them clearly better able to succeed than others.","zh":"give someone a real advantage over others 指令某人明顯比其他人更有能力成功。"},{"en":"Good pronunciation gives a job applicant a real advantage over others in a speaking interview.","zh":"良好發音令求職者在口語面試中比其他人有明顯優勢。"},{"en":"Getting water from leaves gives howlers an advantage when streams are dry.","zh":"從葉子取得水分令吼猴在溪流乾涸時有優勢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a meaningful competitive benefit.","zh":"這個短語描述有意義的競爭好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"suffer during","meaning":"在……期間受苦；受影響","examples":[{"en":"Capuchins and spider monkeys have suffered during the drought.","zh":"卷尾猴和蜘蛛猴在乾旱期間受苦。"},{"en":"To suffer during a period means to experience hardship, harm, or difficulty at that time.","zh":"suffer during a period 指在某段時間經歷艱難、傷害或困難。"},{"en":"Small shops may suffer during roadworks because customers cannot reach them easily.","zh":"道路工程期間，小店可能受影響，因為顧客不容易到達。"},{"en":"Animals suffer during drought when food and water become scarce.","zh":"當食物和水變得稀少，動物在乾旱期間會受苦。"},{"en":"The phrase connects difficulty with a particular time or event.","zh":"這個短語把困難與特定時間或事件連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"long, ongoing drought","meaning":"長期持續的乾旱","examples":[{"en":"The long, ongoing drought in Guanacaste has affected some monkey species.","zh":"Guanacaste 長期持續的乾旱已影響一些猴子物種。"},{"en":"A long, ongoing drought is a dry period that has lasted a long time and is still continuing.","zh":"long, ongoing drought 指已持續很久並仍在繼續的乾旱時期。"},{"en":"Farmers may lose crops during a long, ongoing drought because the soil stays dry for months.","zh":"在長期持續的乾旱期間，農民可能失去作物，因為泥土數月保持乾燥。"},{"en":"Ongoing drought reduces waterholes and can force animals to change their feeding areas.","zh":"持續乾旱減少水坑，並可能迫使動物改變覓食區域。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both duration and continuation.","zh":"這個短語同時強調持續時間和仍在進行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"human population pressures","meaning":"人類人口壓力","examples":[{"en":"Growing human population pressures have led to forest destruction.","zh":"不斷增加的人類人口壓力導致森林破壞。"},{"en":"Human population pressures are demands on land, food, water, housing, and jobs caused by more people living in an area.","zh":"human population pressures 指某地人口增加對土地、食物、水、住房和工作造成的需求。"},{"en":"A small town may face human population pressures when many families move in quickly.","zh":"當許多家庭快速遷入，小鎮可能面對人類人口壓力。"},{"en":"Population pressure can lead to forest clearing because people need farmland, roads, and homes.","zh":"人口壓力可以導致森林砍伐，因為人們需要農地、道路和房屋。"},{"en":"The phrase links human growth with environmental stress.","zh":"這個短語把人類增長與環境壓力連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Central and South America","meaning":"中美洲和南美洲","examples":[{"en":"Forests in Central and South America face human population pressures.","zh":"中美洲和南美洲的森林面對人類人口壓力。"},{"en":"Central and South America refers to the region including countries between southern North America and the southern tip of the American continent.","zh":"Central and South America 指包括北美洲南部與美洲大陸南端之間多個國家的地區。"},{"en":"Many rainforests, farms, cities, and wildlife habitats are found in Central and South America.","zh":"中美洲和南美洲有許多雨林、農場、城市和野生動物棲息地。"},{"en":"Forest loss in this region affects monkeys, birds, rivers, and local communities.","zh":"這一地區的森林流失影響猴子、鳥類、河流和本地社區。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a broad geographic region.","zh":"這個短語指出一個廣闊地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lead to persistent destruction of","meaning":"導致……持續被破壞","examples":[{"en":"Population pressures have led to persistent destruction of forests.","zh":"人口壓力導致森林持續被破壞。"},{"en":"To lead to persistent destruction of something means to cause continuing damage to it over time.","zh":"lead to persistent destruction of something 指造成某物隨時間持續受損。"},{"en":"Illegal dumping can lead to persistent destruction of a beach if no one removes the waste.","zh":"如果無人清理垃圾，非法傾倒可以導致海灘持續被破壞。"},{"en":"Repeated forest clearing causes long-term habitat loss because trees cannot recover quickly.","zh":"反覆砍伐森林造成長期棲息地流失，因為樹木不能快速恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase links a cause with ongoing damage.","zh":"這個短語把原因與持續傷害連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"about 1.1 million acres of","meaning":"約一百一十萬英畝的……","examples":[{"en":"About 1.1 million acres of Central American forest were felled yearly.","zh":"中美洲森林每年約一百一十萬英畝被砍伐。"},{"en":"About 1.1 million acres of something means approximately that large an area.","zh":"about 1.1 million acres of something 指面積大約為一百一十萬英畝。"},{"en":"A government report may say about 1,000 acres of farmland were flooded after heavy rain.","zh":"政府報告可能說暴雨後約一千英畝農地被淹。"},{"en":"Giving an area figure helps readers understand the scale of environmental loss.","zh":"給出面積數字幫助讀者理解環境損失的規模。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate measurement of land area.","zh":"這個短語給出土地面積的大約量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be felled yearly","meaning":"每年被砍伐","examples":[{"en":"Large areas of Central American forest were felled yearly.","zh":"大片中美洲森林每年被砍伐。"},{"en":"To be felled yearly means to be cut down every year, especially trees or forests.","zh":"be felled yearly 指每年被砍倒，尤其指樹木或森林。"},{"en":"If hundreds of roadside trees are felled yearly, the city may become hotter and less shaded.","zh":"如果每年有數百棵路邊樹被砍伐，城市可能變得更熱、遮蔭更少。"},{"en":"Forests felled yearly cannot easily support animals that need continuous tree cover.","zh":"每年被砍伐的森林不容易支持需要連續樹冠覆蓋的動物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated annual cutting.","zh":"這個短語描述每年反覆砍伐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ecologist","meaning":"生態學家","examples":[{"en":"Alejandro Estrada is an ecologist in Veracruz, Mexico.","zh":"Alejandro Estrada 是墨西哥 Veracruz 的生態學家。"},{"en":"An ecologist is a scientist who studies how living things interact with each other and their environment.","zh":"ecologist 指研究生物如何彼此互動，以及如何與環境互動的科學家。"},{"en":"An ecologist may study how birds, insects, trees, and farms affect one another.","zh":"生態學家可能研究鳥類、昆蟲、樹木和農場如何互相影響。"},{"en":"Ecologists help solve conservation problems by showing how ecosystems work.","zh":"生態學家透過顯示生態系統如何運作，幫助解決保育問題。"},{"en":"The word refers to a scientist focused on relationships in nature.","zh":"這個詞指專注研究自然界關係的科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"explore how","meaning":"探討……如何","examples":[{"en":"Estrada has been exploring how monkeys survive in human-shaped landscapes.","zh":"Estrada 一直在探討猴子如何在人類塑造的景觀中生存。"},{"en":"To explore how something happens means to investigate the process or reason behind it.","zh":"explore how something happens 指研究某事發生的過程或原因。"},{"en":"A teacher may explore how students use dictionaries during writing lessons.","zh":"老師可能探討學生在寫作課中如何使用字典。"},{"en":"Researchers explore how animals survive in changed habitats to design better conservation plans.","zh":"研究人員探討動物如何在改變後的棲息地中生存，以設計更好保育計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an investigation into method or mechanism.","zh":"這個短語引入對方法或機制的調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a landscape increasingly shaped by humans","meaning":"日益受人類塑造的景觀","examples":[{"en":"Monkeys survive in a landscape increasingly shaped by humans.","zh":"猴子在日益受人類塑造的景觀中生存。"},{"en":"A landscape increasingly shaped by humans is an environment more and more changed by farming, roads, towns, or other human activities.","zh":"landscape increasingly shaped by humans 指越來越受農業、道路、城鎮或其他人類活動改變的環境。"},{"en":"A village edge with farms, houses, and remaining trees is a landscape increasingly shaped by humans.","zh":"有農田、房屋和剩餘樹木的村邊，就是日益受人類塑造的景觀。"},{"en":"Animals in such landscapes must adapt because natural habitats are altered or broken apart.","zh":"在這類景觀中的動物必須適應，因為自然棲息地被改變或分割。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a place where human influence is growing.","zh":"這個短語描述人類影響日益增加的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"study the ecology of","meaning":"研究……的生態","examples":[{"en":"Researchers studied the ecology of mantled howler monkeys.","zh":"研究人員研究披毛吼猴的生態。"},{"en":"To study the ecology of a species means to examine how it lives, feeds, reproduces, and interacts with its environment.","zh":"study the ecology of a species 指研究某物種如何生活、覓食、繁殖並與環境互動。"},{"en":"Scientists may study the ecology of urban birds to understand why they nest near people.","zh":"科學家可能研究城市鳥類的生態，以了解牠們為何在人類附近築巢。"},{"en":"Studying ecology helps explain why some animals survive in altered habitats while others disappear.","zh":"研究生態有助解釋為何有些動物能在改變後的棲息地生存，而另一些會消失。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on life relationships within an environment.","zh":"這個短語重點是環境中的生命關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"thrive in a habitat","meaning":"在某棲息地繁盛生長","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys thrive in a habitat completely altered by humans.","zh":"這些猴子在人類完全改變的棲息地中繁盛生長。"},{"en":"To thrive in a habitat means to live, grow, and reproduce successfully there.","zh":"thrive in a habitat 指在某棲息地中成功生活、成長和繁殖。"},{"en":"Some plants thrive in city parks because they tolerate pollution and poor soil.","zh":"有些植物在城市公園中繁盛生長，因為它們能忍受污染和貧瘠土壤。"},{"en":"Animals thrive when a habitat provides enough food, shelter, and safety.","zh":"當棲息地提供足夠食物、庇護和安全，動物就會繁盛。"},{"en":"The phrase means doing well, not merely surviving.","zh":"這個短語意思是生活得好，而不只是生存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be completely altered by humans","meaning":"被人類完全改變","examples":[{"en":"The cacao plantation was completely altered by humans.","zh":"可可種植園被人類完全改變。"},{"en":"To be completely altered by humans means to be changed very greatly by human activity.","zh":"be completely altered by humans 指被人類活動大幅改變。"},{"en":"A wetland may be completely altered by humans if it is drained and turned into housing.","zh":"如果濕地被排乾並變成房屋，它就可能被人類完全改變。"},{"en":"Completely altered habitats can still support some species if useful trees or food sources remain.","zh":"如果仍保留有用樹木或食物來源，完全改變的棲息地仍可支持某些物種。"},{"en":"The phrase describes major human-caused environmental change.","zh":"這個短語描述由人類造成的重大環境改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cacao plantation","meaning":"可可種植園","examples":[{"en":"A cacao plantation in Tabasco supports a group of howler monkeys.","zh":"Tabasco 的一個可可種植園支持一群吼猴。"},{"en":"A cacao plantation is farmland where cacao trees are grown to produce cocoa beans.","zh":"cacao plantation 指種植可可樹以生產可可豆的農地。"},{"en":"Workers on a cacao plantation may harvest pods that later become chocolate products.","zh":"可可種植園的工人可能收割日後製成朱古力產品的豆莢。"},{"en":"If a cacao plantation keeps shade trees, it may also provide habitat for wildlife.","zh":"如果可可種植園保留遮蔭樹，它也可能為野生動物提供棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to agricultural land used for growing cacao.","zh":"這個短語指用於種植可可的農業土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"varieties of coffee","meaning":"多個咖啡品種","examples":[{"en":"Many varieties of coffee need shade to grow.","zh":"多個咖啡品種需要遮蔭才能生長。"},{"en":"Varieties of coffee are different types or cultivated forms of coffee plants.","zh":"varieties of coffee 指咖啡植物的不同類型或栽培品種。"},{"en":"A café may sell several varieties of coffee with different flavours and origins.","zh":"咖啡店可能出售幾個味道和產地不同的咖啡品種。"},{"en":"Some varieties grow better under shade, so farmers plant tall trees above them.","zh":"有些品種在遮蔭下長得更好，所以農民在其上方種植高樹。"},{"en":"The phrase describes different kinds within one crop.","zh":"這個短語描述同一作物內的不同種類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"need shade to grow","meaning":"需要遮蔭才能生長","examples":[{"en":"Cacao plants need shade to grow.","zh":"可可植物需要遮蔭才能生長。"},{"en":"To need shade to grow means to require protection from direct sunlight in order to develop well.","zh":"need shade to grow 指需要避開直射陽光的保護，才能良好發展。"},{"en":"Some young garden plants need shade to grow because strong sun dries them out.","zh":"有些年幼園藝植物需要遮蔭才能生長，因為強烈陽光會令它們乾枯。"},{"en":"Farmers plant tall trees over cacao because shade protects the crop and improves growing conditions.","zh":"農民在可可上方種植高樹，因為遮蔭保護作物並改善生長條件。"},{"en":"The phrase connects plant growth with reduced sunlight.","zh":"這個短語把植物生長與減少陽光照射連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"landowners","meaning":"地主；土地擁有人","examples":[{"en":"The landowners planted tall trees to protect their crop.","zh":"土地擁有人種植高樹來保護作物。"},{"en":"Landowners are people or organisations that own land.","zh":"landowners 指擁有土地的人或組織。"},{"en":"Landowners may rent fields to farmers or decide how forests on their land are managed.","zh":"土地擁有人可能把田地租給農民，或決定如何管理其土地上的森林。"},{"en":"Landowners affect wildlife because their decisions shape what happens to trees, crops, and rivers.","zh":"土地擁有人影響野生動物，因為他們的決定塑造樹木、作物和河流的情況。"},{"en":"The word identifies those with legal control over land.","zh":"這個詞指出對土地有法律控制權的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"form a protective canopy over","meaning":"在……上方形成保護性樹冠","examples":[{"en":"Tall trees form a protective canopy over the cacao crop.","zh":"高樹在可可作物上方形成保護性樹冠。"},{"en":"To form a protective canopy over something means to create a covering layer of branches and leaves above it.","zh":"form a protective canopy over something 指在某物上方形成由樹枝和樹葉構成的覆蓋層。"},{"en":"Trees along a school path can form a protective canopy over students walking in the sun.","zh":"學校小路旁的樹可以在陽光下為行走的學生形成保護性樹冠。"},{"en":"A protective canopy helps crops by reducing heat, direct sunlight, and wind damage.","zh":"保護性樹冠透過減少熱力、直射陽光和風害來幫助作物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes natural cover from above.","zh":"這個短語描述來自上方的自然覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"move in","meaning":"遷入；搬進來","examples":[{"en":"The howlers moved in after nearby forests were cut.","zh":"附近森林被砍伐後，吼猴遷入了。"},{"en":"To move in means to come and start living in a place.","zh":"move in 指來到某地並開始居住。"},{"en":"A new family may move in next door during the summer holiday.","zh":"暑假期間，一個新家庭可能搬到隔壁。"},{"en":"Animals may move in when a farm or garden provides food and trees similar to their old habitat.","zh":"當農場或花園提供類似舊棲息地的食物和樹木，動物可能遷入。"},{"en":"The phrase describes settling in a new living place.","zh":"這個短語描述在新居住地安頓下來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a hodgepodge of","meaning":"混雜的一堆……","examples":[{"en":"The habitat is a hodgepodge of cultivated native and exotic plants.","zh":"該棲息地是人工栽種的本土及外來植物混雜的一堆。"},{"en":"A hodgepodge of things is a mixed collection of different items that do not form a neat pattern.","zh":"hodgepodge of things 指由不同東西組成、沒有整齊模式的混合體。"},{"en":"A student’s desk may be a hodgepodge of books, snacks, cables, and old worksheets.","zh":"學生書桌可能是書本、零食、電線和舊工作紙混雜的一堆。"},{"en":"Mixed habitats can support some animals because they provide many kinds of food and cover.","zh":"混合棲息地可以支持某些動物，因為它們提供多種食物和遮蔽。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a messy mixture.","zh":"這個短語暗示雜亂混合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cultivated native and exotic plants","meaning":"人工栽種的本土及外來植物","examples":[{"en":"The plantation contains cultivated native and exotic plants.","zh":"該種植園包含人工栽種的本土及外來植物。"},{"en":"Cultivated native and exotic plants are planted species that include both local plants and plants originally from elsewhere.","zh":"cultivated native and exotic plants 指人工種植的物種，包括本地植物和原產外地的植物。"},{"en":"A community garden may grow cultivated native and exotic plants, such as local herbs and imported flowers.","zh":"社區花園可能種植人工栽種的本土及外來植物，例如本地香草和進口花卉。"},{"en":"Mixed planting can change habitat by giving animals new foods and shelter.","zh":"混合種植可以透過提供新食物和庇護改變棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a planted mixture of local and non-local species.","zh":"這個短語描述由本地和非本地物種組成的人工種植混合體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"support about as many monkeys as","meaning":"容納的猴子數量約與……一樣多","examples":[{"en":"The strange habitat supports about as many monkeys as a same-sized wild forest.","zh":"這個奇特棲息地容納的猴子數量，約與同等大小的野生森林一樣多。"},{"en":"To support about as many monkeys as another place means to provide enough food and space for roughly the same number of monkeys.","zh":"support about as many monkeys as another place 指提供足夠食物和空間，容納大約同樣數量的猴子。"},{"en":"A small park may support about as many birds as a larger garden if it has more trees and water.","zh":"如果小公園有更多樹木和水，它容納的鳥類數量可能約與較大花園一樣多。"},{"en":"If farms support many monkeys, they may help conservation as well as agriculture.","zh":"如果農場能支持許多猴子，它們可能同時幫助保育和農業。"},{"en":"The phrase compares carrying capacity between two habitats.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個棲息地的承載能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a same-sized patch of wild forest","meaning":"同等大小的一片野生森林","examples":[{"en":"The plantation supports as many monkeys as a same-sized patch of wild forest.","zh":"該種植園支持的猴子數量與同等大小的一片野生森林一樣多。"},{"en":"A same-sized patch of wild forest is a natural forest area equal in size to the place being compared.","zh":"same-sized patch of wild forest 指面積與被比較地方相同的一片天然森林。"},{"en":"A researcher may compare a school garden with a same-sized patch of wild forest to count insects.","zh":"研究人員可能把學校花園與同等大小的一片野生森林比較，以點算昆蟲。"},{"en":"Same-sized comparisons are useful because they make habitat quality easier to judge.","zh":"同等大小比較很有用，因為它令棲息地質素較易判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a fair size-based comparison.","zh":"這個短語提供基於面積的公平比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"shade trees","meaning":"遮蔭樹","examples":[{"en":"The howlers eat the leaves and fruit of the shade trees.","zh":"吼猴吃遮蔭樹的葉子和果實。"},{"en":"Shade trees are trees planted or kept to provide cover from direct sunlight.","zh":"shade trees 指被種植或保留下來、用來遮擋直射陽光的樹木。"},{"en":"A school playground may have shade trees so students can rest out of the sun.","zh":"學校操場可能有遮蔭樹，讓學生避開陽光休息。"},{"en":"Shade trees help crops like cacao by cooling the area and protecting plants from strong light.","zh":"遮蔭樹透過降低溫度和保護植物免受強光照射，幫助可可等作物。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to trees used for shelter and shade.","zh":"這個短語指用於庇護和遮蔭的樹木。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"leave something alone","meaning":"不碰；不干擾……","examples":[{"en":"The howlers leave the valuable cacao pods alone.","zh":"吼猴不碰那些有價值的可可豆莢。"},{"en":"To leave something alone means not to touch, disturb, damage, or use it.","zh":"leave something alone 指不觸碰、不干擾、不破壞或不使用某物。"},{"en":"Children should leave a hot stove alone because touching it is dangerous.","zh":"孩子應該不要碰熱爐，因為觸碰它很危險。"},{"en":"Farmers tolerate monkeys more easily if the animals leave valuable crops alone.","zh":"如果動物不碰有價值作物，農民較容易容忍牠們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deliberate non-interference.","zh":"這個短語描述有意不干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cacao pods","meaning":"可可豆莢","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys do not eat the valuable cacao pods.","zh":"猴子不吃那些有價值的可可豆莢。"},{"en":"Cacao pods are large fruit pods from cacao trees that contain beans used to make chocolate.","zh":"cacao pods 指可可樹的大果莢，裏面含有用來製造朱古力的豆。"},{"en":"Farmers harvest cacao pods and remove the beans inside for processing.","zh":"農民收割可可豆莢，並取出裏面的豆作加工。"},{"en":"If monkeys damaged cacao pods, farmers would lose income and might chase them away.","zh":"如果猴子破壞可可豆莢，農民會損失收入，並可能趕走牠們。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the economically valuable fruit of cacao trees.","zh":"這個短語指可可樹具經濟價值的果實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tolerate them","meaning":"容忍牠們","examples":[{"en":"The farmers tolerate the howler monkeys because they leave the cacao pods alone.","zh":"農民容忍吼猴，因為牠們不碰可可豆莢。"},{"en":"To tolerate them means to allow them to remain even if they may be inconvenient or unwanted.","zh":"tolerate them 指即使牠們可能不方便或不受歡迎，也容許牠們留下。"},{"en":"A shop owner may tolerate street performers if they attract customers and do not block the entrance.","zh":"如果街頭表演者吸引顧客且不阻塞入口，店主可能容忍他們。"},{"en":"Farmers tolerate wildlife when the benefits seem greater than the damage.","zh":"當好處看似大於損害，農民會容忍野生動物。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests acceptance, not necessarily affection.","zh":"這個短語暗示接受，而不一定是喜愛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"underappreciated benefits","meaning":"被低估的好處","examples":[{"en":"Estrada believes the monkeys bring underappreciated benefits to farms.","zh":"Estrada 認為猴子為農場帶來被低估的好處。"},{"en":"Underappreciated benefits are advantages that people do not notice or value enough.","zh":"underappreciated benefits 指人們沒有充分注意或重視的好處。"},{"en":"Cleaning staff provide underappreciated benefits because a safe school depends on their work.","zh":"清潔員提供被低估的好處，因為安全學校依賴他們的工作。"},{"en":"Monkeys may benefit farms by spreading seeds and fertilising soil, even if farmers first see them as pests.","zh":"猴子可能透過傳播種子和為土壤施肥而有利於農場，即使農民起初把牠們視為害獸。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights hidden or undervalued positive effects.","zh":"這個短語突出隱藏或被低估的正面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"disperse the seeds of","meaning":"傳播……的種子","examples":[{"en":"Howler monkeys disperse the seeds of fig and other shade trees.","zh":"吼猴傳播無花果和其他遮蔭樹的種子。"},{"en":"To disperse the seeds of a plant means to spread its seeds to new places.","zh":"disperse the seeds of a plant 指把某植物的種子傳播到新地方。"},{"en":"Birds disperse the seeds of berries when they eat the fruit and drop seeds elsewhere.","zh":"鳥類吃下漿果並在別處排出種子時，就是傳播漿果植物的種子。"},{"en":"Seed dispersal helps forests regenerate because young plants can grow away from the parent tree.","zh":"種子傳播幫助森林再生，因為幼植物可以在母樹以外生長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how animals help plants spread.","zh":"這個短語描述動物如何幫助植物擴散。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fertilise the soil","meaning":"為土壤施肥","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys fertilise the soil with faeces.","zh":"猴子用糞便為土壤施肥。"},{"en":"To fertilise the soil means to add nutrients that help plants grow.","zh":"fertilise the soil 指加入能幫助植物生長的營養物質。"},{"en":"Gardeners fertilise the soil with compost before planting vegetables.","zh":"園丁在種菜前用堆肥為土壤施肥。"},{"en":"Animal droppings can fertilise soil because they return nutrients to the ground.","zh":"動物糞便可以為土壤施肥，因為它們把營養送回地面。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improving soil fertility.","zh":"這個短語描述改善土壤肥力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"faeces","meaning":"糞便","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys’ faeces help fertilise the soil.","zh":"猴子的糞便有助為土壤施肥。"},{"en":"Faeces are solid waste passed out of the body after digestion.","zh":"faeces 指消化後從身體排出的固體廢物。"},{"en":"Farmers may use animal faeces as manure after treating it safely.","zh":"農民可能在安全處理後使用動物糞便作肥料。"},{"en":"Faeces can return nutrients to soil, but they can also spread disease if handled badly.","zh":"糞便可以把營養送回土壤，但若處理不當也可能傳播疾病。"},{"en":"The word is the formal term for animal or human waste.","zh":"這個詞是動物或人類排泄物的正式名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"point out that","meaning":"指出","examples":[{"en":"Estrada points out that howler monkeys live in shade plantations in several countries.","zh":"Estrada 指出，吼猴生活在幾個國家的遮蔭種植園中。"},{"en":"To point out that something is true means to mention it clearly because it is important or may be overlooked.","zh":"point out that something is true 指清楚提及某事，因為它重要或可能被忽略。"},{"en":"A teacher may point out that a wrong answer still uses the correct grammar pattern.","zh":"老師可能指出錯誤答案仍使用了正確文法模式。"},{"en":"Researchers point out evidence to change how people understand a problem.","zh":"研究人員指出證據，以改變人們如何理解問題。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a clear observation or reminder.","zh":"這個短語引入清楚觀察或提醒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"shade coffee and cacao plantations","meaning":"遮蔭咖啡及可可種植園","examples":[{"en":"Howler monkeys live in shade coffee and cacao plantations.","zh":"吼猴生活在遮蔭咖啡及可可種植園中。"},{"en":"Shade coffee and cacao plantations are farms where coffee or cacao grows under taller trees.","zh":"shade coffee and cacao plantations 指咖啡或可可在較高樹木下生長的農場。"},{"en":"Shade coffee plantations may support birds because the tall trees provide nesting places.","zh":"遮蔭咖啡種植園可能支持鳥類，因為高樹提供築巢地方。"},{"en":"Shade plantations can be more wildlife-friendly than open fields because they keep some tree cover.","zh":"遮蔭種植園比開闊田地更有利於野生動物，因為它們保留一些樹木覆蓋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes farms that mix crops with shade trees.","zh":"這個短語描述把作物與遮蔭樹混合的農場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"forage in","meaning":"在……覓食","examples":[{"en":"Spider monkeys also forage in such plantations.","zh":"蜘蛛猴也在這類種植園中覓食。"},{"en":"To forage in a place means to search there for food.","zh":"forage in a place 指在某地尋找食物。"},{"en":"Birds may forage in a school garden after students leave crumbs on the ground.","zh":"學生把麵包屑留在地上後，鳥類可能在學校花園覓食。"},{"en":"Animals forage where food is available, even if the place is not a natural forest.","zh":"動物會在有食物的地方覓食，即使該地方不是天然森林。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active searching for food.","zh":"這個短語描述主動尋找食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in the long term","meaning":"長遠而言","examples":[{"en":"Spider monkeys need nearby forest to survive in the long term.","zh":"長遠而言，蜘蛛猴需要附近森林才能生存。"},{"en":"In the long term means over a long period, not just immediately.","zh":"in the long term 指在長時間內，而不只是即時。"},{"en":"Eating instant noodles saves time today, but in the long term a balanced diet is healthier.","zh":"今天吃即食麵節省時間，但長遠而言均衡飲食較健康。"},{"en":"A habitat may support animals briefly but fail in the long term if breeding areas are missing.","zh":"如果缺少繁殖地，棲息地可能短暫支持動物，但長遠而言會失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on future sustainability.","zh":"這個短語重點是未來可持續性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"see the advantages of","meaning":"看到……的好處","examples":[{"en":"Estrada hopes farmers will see the advantages of coexisting with wild monkeys.","zh":"Estrada 希望農民會看到與野生猴子共存的好處。"},{"en":"To see the advantages of something means to recognise its benefits.","zh":"see the advantages of something 指認識到某事的好處。"},{"en":"Parents may see the advantages of online homework when they can check progress easily.","zh":"當家長能輕易查看進度，可能會看到網上功課的好處。"},{"en":"Farmers may protect monkeys if they see advantages such as seed dispersal and ecotourism income.","zh":"如果農民看到種子傳播和生態旅遊收入等好處，他們可能保護猴子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change in understanding from doubt to appreciation.","zh":"這個短語描述由懷疑轉向欣賞的理解變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"coexist with","meaning":"與……共存","examples":[{"en":"Farmers may learn to coexist with wild monkeys.","zh":"農民可能學會與野生猴子共存。"},{"en":"To coexist with another living thing means to live in the same area without destroying or driving it away.","zh":"coexist with another living thing 指與另一種生物生活在同一地區，而不消滅或驅趕它。"},{"en":"City residents coexist with street cats by feeding them responsibly and controlling waste.","zh":"城市居民可以透過負責任地餵飼和控制垃圾，與街貓共存。"},{"en":"Coexistence becomes easier when both human needs and wildlife needs are considered.","zh":"當人類需要和野生動物需要都被考慮，共存會較容易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sharing space peacefully or practically.","zh":"這個短語描述和平或實際地共享空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"potential ecotourism projects","meaning":"具潛力的生態旅遊項目","examples":[{"en":"Wild monkeys may support potential ecotourism projects.","zh":"野生猴子可能支持具潛力的生態旅遊項目。"},{"en":"Potential ecotourism projects are possible travel activities based on nature and conservation.","zh":"potential ecotourism projects 指以自然和保育為基礎、可能發展的旅遊活動。"},{"en":"A village with rare birds may develop potential ecotourism projects such as guided forest walks.","zh":"擁有稀有鳥類的村落可能發展導賞森林步行等具潛力的生態旅遊項目。"},{"en":"Ecotourism can bring income if wildlife is protected rather than chased away.","zh":"如果野生動物受到保護而不是被驅趕，生態旅遊可以帶來收入。"},{"en":"The phrase describes tourism ideas that could develop in the future.","zh":"這個短語描述未來可能發展的旅遊構想。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be viewed as a conflict between","meaning":"被視為……之間的衝突","examples":[{"en":"Conservation is often viewed as a conflict between farming and nature.","zh":"保育常被視為農業與大自然之間的衝突。"},{"en":"To be viewed as a conflict between two things means people see them as opposing each other.","zh":"be viewed as a conflict between two things 指人們把兩者看作互相對立。"},{"en":"Homework is sometimes viewed as a conflict between study and rest.","zh":"功課有時被視為學習與休息之間的衝突。"},{"en":"If farming and nature are seen only as enemies, people may miss solutions that help both.","zh":"如果農業和自然只被視為敵人，人們可能錯過能同時幫助兩者的方案。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a way of seeing a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述看待問題的一種方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"agricultural practices","meaning":"農業做法","examples":[{"en":"Conservation is often discussed alongside agricultural practices.","zh":"保育常與農業做法一起討論。"},{"en":"Agricultural practices are the methods farmers use to grow crops, raise animals, and manage land.","zh":"agricultural practices 指農民種植作物、飼養動物和管理土地的方法。"},{"en":"Using shade trees in cacao farms is one agricultural practice that may support wildlife.","zh":"在可可農場使用遮蔭樹，是可能支持野生動物的一種農業做法。"},{"en":"Agricultural practices affect soil, water, forests, and animal habitats.","zh":"農業做法影響土壤、水、森林和動物棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to farming methods and routines.","zh":"這個短語指農耕方法和慣例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"preserve nature","meaning":"保護大自然","examples":[{"en":"Conservation involves the need to preserve nature.","zh":"保育涉及保護大自然的需要。"},{"en":"To preserve nature means to protect natural places, plants, animals, and ecological processes.","zh":"preserve nature 指保護自然地方、植物、動物和生態過程。"},{"en":"A community can preserve nature by keeping rivers clean and protecting old trees.","zh":"社區可以透過保持河流清潔和保護老樹來保護大自然。"},{"en":"Preserving nature helps people too because clean water, shade, and soil depend on healthy ecosystems.","zh":"保護大自然也幫助人類，因為清潔食水、遮蔭和土壤都依賴健康生態系統。"},{"en":"The phrase describes protecting the natural world for the future.","zh":"這個短語描述為未來保護自然世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"move away from that vision","meaning":"擺脫那種看法","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are moving away from that vision of conflict.","zh":"研究人員正在擺脫那種衝突看法。"},{"en":"To move away from that vision means to stop accepting that way of seeing the issue.","zh":"move away from that vision 指停止接受那種看待問題的方式。"},{"en":"A school may move away from the vision that strict punishment is the only way to manage students.","zh":"學校可能擺脫嚴厲懲罰是管理學生唯一方法的看法。"},{"en":"Researchers move away from old views when new evidence shows better possibilities.","zh":"當新證據顯示更好可能性，研究人員會擺脫舊觀點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing perspective.","zh":"這個短語描述觀點轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"consider ways in which","meaning":"考慮……的方式","examples":[{"en":"They consider ways in which farming can support primate conservation.","zh":"他們考慮農業可以支持靈長類動物保育的方式。"},{"en":"To consider ways in which something can happen means to think carefully about possible methods or paths.","zh":"consider ways in which something can happen 指仔細思考某事可以發生的可能方法或途徑。"},{"en":"A teacher may consider ways in which group work can help shy students speak more.","zh":"老師可能考慮小組活動可以幫助害羞學生多說話的方式。"},{"en":"Considering different ways can reveal solutions that are not obvious at first.","zh":"考慮不同方式可以揭示一開始不明顯的解決方案。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces careful thinking about practical possibilities.","zh":"這個短語引入對實際可能性的仔細思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a tool for the conservation of primates","meaning":"保護靈長類動物的工具","examples":[{"en":"Agricultural activities may become a tool for the conservation of primates.","zh":"農業活動可能成為保護靈長類動物的工具。"},{"en":"A tool for the conservation of primates is something that helps protect monkeys, apes, and related animals.","zh":"tool for the conservation of primates 指有助保護猴子、猿和相關動物的事物。"},{"en":"Shade plantations can be a tool for the conservation of primates if they provide food and safe movement routes.","zh":"如果遮蔭種植園提供食物和安全移動路線，它們可以成為保護靈長類動物的工具。"},{"en":"Farming becomes useful for conservation when it keeps trees instead of removing all habitat.","zh":"當農業保留樹木而不是移除所有棲息地，它就能對保育有用。"},{"en":"The phrase presents agriculture as part of the solution, not only a threat.","zh":"這個短語把農業呈現為解決方案的一部分，而不只是威脅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"human-modified landscapes","meaning":"經人類改造的景觀","examples":[{"en":"Primates may survive in human-modified landscapes.","zh":"靈長類動物可能在經人類改造的景觀中生存。"},{"en":"Human-modified landscapes are environments changed by people through farming, roads, buildings, or other activities.","zh":"human-modified landscapes 指透過農業、道路、建築或其他活動被人類改變的環境。"},{"en":"A countryside with farms, villages, and small forest patches is a human-modified landscape.","zh":"有農場、村落和小片森林的鄉郊，就是經人類改造的景觀。"},{"en":"Some animals can survive in human-modified landscapes if enough food and cover remain.","zh":"如果仍有足夠食物和遮蔽，有些動物可以在經人類改造的景觀中生存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes nature altered by human activity.","zh":"這個短語描述被人類活動改變的大自然。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"contains the following information","meaning":"包含以下資料","examples":[{"en":"Each paragraph contains different information about monkeys and forests.","zh":"每一段都包含關於猴子和森林的不同資料。"},{"en":"Contains the following information means includes the details listed in the question or instruction.","zh":"contains the following information 指包括題目或指示中列出的細節。"},{"en":"A report may contain the following information: cost, deadline, risks, and expected benefits.","zh":"報告可能包含以下資料：成本、限期、風險和預期好處。"},{"en":"In reading tasks, students scan paragraphs to find which one contains the required information.","zh":"在閱讀任務中，學生掃讀段落，找出哪一段包含所需資料。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to connect a text section with specific details.","zh":"這個短語用來把文本部分與特定細節連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a reference to","meaning":"提及……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for a reference to the rate of forest loss.","zh":"題目要求找出提及森林流失速度的地方。"},{"en":"A reference to something is a mention of that topic or detail.","zh":"reference to something 指提到某主題或細節。"},{"en":"A passage about education may include a reference to homework stress in one paragraph.","zh":"關於教育的文章可能在某一段提及功課壓力。"},{"en":"Finding references helps students locate answers without reading every sentence equally slowly.","zh":"找出提及內容幫助學生定位答案，而不必同樣慢速閱讀每句。"},{"en":"The phrase means a mention, not necessarily a long explanation.","zh":"這個短語意思是提到，不一定是長篇解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the rate of reduction in forest habitats","meaning":"森林棲息地減少的速度","examples":[{"en":"The passage gives the rate of reduction in forest habitats.","zh":"文章給出森林棲息地減少的速度。"},{"en":"The rate of reduction in forest habitats is how quickly forest living areas are decreasing.","zh":"rate of reduction in forest habitats 指森林生活區域正在以多快速度減少。"},{"en":"A conservation report may measure the rate of reduction in wetlands each year.","zh":"保育報告可能量度每年濕地減少的速度。"},{"en":"Knowing the rate of habitat loss helps governments decide how urgent protection must be.","zh":"知道棲息地流失速度，幫助政府決定保護工作有多迫切。"},{"en":"The phrase combines speed of loss with natural living space.","zh":"這個短語結合流失速度與自然生活空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"only one species of monkey survived","meaning":"只有一種猴子存活下來","examples":[{"en":"Only one species of monkey survived in the area after the others vanished.","zh":"其他猴子消失後，該地區只有一種猴子存活下來。"},{"en":"Only one species of monkey survived means all other monkey species disappeared from the area, but one remained.","zh":"only one species of monkey survived 指所有其他猴子物種從該地區消失，但有一種留下。"},{"en":"After a severe disease outbreak, only one species of bird survived on the island.","zh":"嚴重疾病爆發後，島上只有一種鳥類存活下來。"},{"en":"When only one species survives, scientists ask what special traits helped it cope.","zh":"當只有一種物種存活，科學家會問甚麼特徵幫助它應對。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights selective survival.","zh":"這個短語突出選擇性生存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a reason why","meaning":"……的原因","examples":[{"en":"The passage gives a reason why howler monkeys prefer younger leaves.","zh":"文章給出吼猴偏好較年輕葉子的原因。"},{"en":"A reason why something happens is an explanation for it.","zh":"reason why something happens 指某事發生的解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask for a reason why a student chose one answer instead of another.","zh":"老師可能要求學生說明為何選擇一個答案而不是另一個的原因。"},{"en":"Reasons help readers move from facts to understanding causes.","zh":"原因幫助讀者由事實走向理解成因。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an explanation.","zh":"這個短語引入解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"choose new leaves as food over old ones","meaning":"選擇新葉而非老葉作食物","examples":[{"en":"Howler monkeys may choose new leaves as food over old ones.","zh":"吼猴可能選擇新葉而非老葉作食物。"},{"en":"To choose A over B means to prefer A instead of B.","zh":"choose A over B 指偏好 A 而不是 B。"},{"en":"A student may choose a quiet library over a noisy café when preparing for exams.","zh":"準備考試時，學生可能選擇安靜圖書館而非嘈雜咖啡店。"},{"en":"Howlers choose young leaves over old leaves because younger leaves may contain fewer toxins.","zh":"吼猴選擇幼葉而非老葉，因為幼葉可能含較少毒素。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly shows preference between two options.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示兩個選項之間的偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"diet and eating habits","meaning":"飲食和飲食習慣","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes the howlers’ diet and eating habits.","zh":"文章描述吼猴的飲食和飲食習慣。"},{"en":"Diet and eating habits refer to what an animal or person eats and how regularly they eat it.","zh":"diet and eating habits 指動物或人吃甚麼，以及通常如何進食。"},{"en":"A doctor may ask about a patient’s diet and eating habits before giving health advice.","zh":"醫生在給健康建議前，可能詢問病人的飲食和飲食習慣。"},{"en":"Flexible diet and eating habits help howlers survive in small or damaged habitats.","zh":"靈活的飲食和飲食習慣幫助吼猴在細小或受破壞棲息地中生存。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both food types and feeding behaviour.","zh":"這個短語同時涵蓋食物類型和進食行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"changing farmers’ attitudes toward wildlife","meaning":"農民對野生動物態度的轉變","examples":[{"en":"The final paragraph discusses changing farmers’ attitudes toward wildlife.","zh":"最後一段討論農民對野生動物態度的轉變。"},{"en":"Changing farmers’ attitudes toward wildlife means helping farmers think differently about wild animals, often from seeing them as pests to seeing them as useful.","zh":"changing farmers’ attitudes toward wildlife 指幫助農民改變對野生動物的想法，通常由視牠們為害獸轉為視牠們有用。"},{"en":"A workshop may change farmers’ attitudes toward birds by showing how they eat crop pests.","zh":"工作坊可能透過展示鳥類如何吃害蟲，改變農民對鳥類的態度。"},{"en":"Attitudes change when people see practical benefits such as soil fertility, tourism, or seed dispersal.","zh":"當人們看到土壤肥力、旅遊或種子傳播等實際好處，態度就會改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shift in how farmers view wild animals.","zh":"這個短語描述農民看待野生動物方式的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ability to live in a fragmented habitat","meaning":"在破碎化棲息地生活的能力","examples":[{"en":"Howler monkeys have an ability to live in a fragmented habitat.","zh":"吼猴有在破碎化棲息地生活的能力。"},{"en":"The ability to live in a fragmented habitat is the capacity to survive in small, separated pieces of natural habitat.","zh":"ability to live in a fragmented habitat 指在細小、分隔開的自然棲息地碎片中生存的能力。"},{"en":"Some city birds have the ability to live in fragmented habitat such as parks, gardens, and roadside trees.","zh":"有些城市鳥類有在公園、花園和路邊樹等破碎化棲息地生活的能力。"},{"en":"This ability helps a species survive when farms, roads, or towns break forests apart.","zh":"當農田、道路或城鎮把森林分割，這種能力幫助物種生存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adaptation to broken landscapes.","zh":"這個短語描述對破碎景觀的適應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"look at the following places","meaning":"查看以下地方","examples":[{"en":"Candidates look at the following places and match them with descriptions.","zh":"考生查看以下地方，並把它們與描述配對。"},{"en":"Look at the following places means read or examine the place names listed below.","zh":"look at the following places 指閱讀或查看下方列出的地名。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should look at the following places before scanning the passage for details.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先查看以下地方，再掃讀文章找細節。"},{"en":"Checking the list first helps students know what names to search for.","zh":"先檢查列表幫助學生知道要搜尋哪些名稱。"},{"en":"The phrase is an instruction for a matching task.","zh":"這個短語是配對題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the list of descriptions below","meaning":"以下描述列表","examples":[{"en":"Candidates use the list of descriptions below to answer the questions.","zh":"考生使用以下描述列表作答。"},{"en":"The list of descriptions below means the set of description options printed after the instruction.","zh":"list of descriptions below 指指示後印出的描述選項集合。"},{"en":"Students should read the list of descriptions below before deciding which paragraph or place matches each one.","zh":"學生應先閱讀以下描述列表，再決定哪一段或哪個地方與每項相配。"},{"en":"The list helps organise possible answers and reduces guessing.","zh":"該列表幫助組織可能答案並減少猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase points to answer options that follow.","zh":"這個短語指向接下來的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"match each description with","meaning":"把每項描述與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match each description with the correct place.","zh":"考生把每項描述與正確地方配對。"},{"en":"To match each description with something means to connect every description to the option it correctly describes.","zh":"match each description with something 指把每項描述連接到它正確描述的選項。"},{"en":"Students may match each description with a character after reading a story.","zh":"學生閱讀故事後，可能把每項描述與人物配對。"},{"en":"Matching tasks require careful checking because several options may look similar.","zh":"配對題需要仔細檢查，因為幾個選項可能看似相似。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pairing information accurately.","zh":"這個短語描述準確配對資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"benefit local agriculture","meaning":"令本地農業受益","examples":[{"en":"Howler monkeys can benefit local agriculture by spreading seeds.","zh":"吼猴可以透過傳播種子令本地農業受益。"},{"en":"To benefit local agriculture means to help farming in the nearby area.","zh":"benefit local agriculture 指幫助附近地區的農業。"},{"en":"Bees benefit local agriculture by pollinating fruit trees and vegetable crops.","zh":"蜜蜂透過為果樹和蔬菜作物授粉，令本地農業受益。"},{"en":"Wildlife can benefit farms when it improves soil, spreads useful trees, or attracts visitors.","zh":"當野生動物改善土壤、傳播有用樹木或吸引遊客，它們可以令農場受益。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a positive effect on farming.","zh":"這個短語描述對農業的正面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the original home of","meaning":"……原本的棲息地","examples":[{"en":"The area was the original home of all three native monkey species.","zh":"該地區是所有三種本土猴子物種原本的棲息地。"},{"en":"The original home of a species is the place where it naturally lived before later changes.","zh":"original home of a species 指某物種在後來變化前自然生活的地方。"},{"en":"A river valley may be the original home of a fish species before dams changed the water flow.","zh":"在水壩改變水流前，河谷可能是某魚類原本的棲息地。"},{"en":"Knowing an animal’s original home helps conservationists understand what habitat it needs.","zh":"知道動物原本的棲息地，有助保育人士理解牠需要甚麼棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to natural historic habitat.","zh":"這個短語指自然歷史棲息地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a better habitat","meaning":"較好的棲息地","examples":[{"en":"Capuchin monkeys found a better habitat in the reborn forests.","zh":"卷尾猴在重生森林中找到較好的棲息地。"},{"en":"A better habitat is a place that provides more suitable food, shelter, space, or safety for a species.","zh":"better habitat 指為某物種提供更合適食物、庇護、空間或安全的地方。"},{"en":"A classroom with good light and less noise is a better learning habitat for young children.","zh":"光線良好、噪音較少的課室，是幼兒較好的學習棲息地。"},{"en":"Animals move to better habitats when old areas become too dry, crowded, or dangerous.","zh":"當舊地區變得太乾、太擠或太危險，動物會遷往較好棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase compares how suitable different places are for living.","zh":"這個短語比較不同地方對生活的適合程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete the sentences below","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the sentences below using words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成以下句子。"},{"en":"Complete the sentences below means fill in the missing words in the sentences that follow.","zh":"complete the sentences below 指填寫下方句子中缺漏的字詞。"},{"en":"Students should complete the sentences below by checking grammar and locating exact words in the text.","zh":"學生應透過檢查文法並在文本中定位準確字詞來完成以下句子。"},{"en":"This task tests whether candidates understand both meaning and word limits.","zh":"這項任務測試考生是否理解意思和字數限制。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"choose no more than two words","meaning":"選擇不多於兩個詞","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose no more than two words from the passage.","zh":"考生從文章中選擇不多於兩個詞。"},{"en":"Choose no more than two words means the answer must contain one or two words, not three or more.","zh":"choose no more than two words 指答案必須包含一個或兩個英文詞，而不是三個或更多。"},{"en":"If the answer is “plant toxins”, it uses two words and follows the instruction.","zh":"如果答案是 “plant toxins”，它有兩個詞，符合指示。"},{"en":"Ignoring the word limit can make a correct idea wrong in an exam.","zh":"忽略字數限制可以令正確意思在考試中變錯。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a strict answer length.","zh":"這個短語設定嚴格答案長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"survive better in the region","meaning":"在該地區生存得較好","examples":[{"en":"Howler monkeys survive better in the region than the other two species.","zh":"吼猴在該地區比另外兩個物種生存得較好。"},{"en":"To survive better in the region means to cope more successfully with the local conditions than others do.","zh":"survive better in the region 指比其他物種更成功應對本地條件。"},{"en":"Some shops survive better in a neighbourhood because they understand local customers.","zh":"有些商店在某社區生存得較好，因為它們理解本地顧客。"},{"en":"Howlers survive better because their diet, water needs, and reproduction give them advantages.","zh":"吼猴生存得較好，因為其飲食、水分需要和繁殖給牠們優勢。"},{"en":"The phrase compares local survival success.","zh":"這個短語比較本地生存成功程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"not easily found","meaning":"不容易找到","examples":[{"en":"Fruit is not easily found in some fragmented habitats.","zh":"在某些破碎化棲息地中，水果不容易找到。"},{"en":"Not easily found means difficult to locate or obtain.","zh":"not easily found 指難以找到或取得。"},{"en":"Quiet study spaces are not easily found in a crowded home.","zh":"在擠迫家庭中，安靜自修空間不容易找到。"},{"en":"If fruit is not easily found, animals that depend on fruit must travel farther or suffer.","zh":"如果水果不容易找到，依賴水果的動物就必須走更遠或受苦。"},{"en":"The phrase shows scarcity or difficulty of access.","zh":"這個短語顯示稀少或取得困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"have a better ability to tolerate","meaning":"有較強能力忍受……","examples":[{"en":"Howlers have a better ability to tolerate plant toxins.","zh":"吼猴有較強能力忍受植物毒素。"},{"en":"To have a better ability to tolerate something means to be more capable of enduring it without serious harm.","zh":"have a better ability to tolerate something 指更能承受某事而不受嚴重傷害。"},{"en":"Some people have a better ability to tolerate spicy food because they eat it often.","zh":"有些人因經常吃辣，較能忍受辛辣食物。"},{"en":"Better toxin tolerance allows howlers to eat leaves that other monkeys may avoid.","zh":"較強毒素耐受力讓吼猴能吃其他猴子可能避開的葉子。"},{"en":"The phrase compares biological or practical endurance.","zh":"這個短語比較生物或實際承受力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"protect themselves","meaning":"保護自己","examples":[{"en":"Old and young trees use toxins to protect themselves.","zh":"老樹和年輕樹木使用毒素來保護自己。"},{"en":"To protect themselves means to defend their own bodies, safety, or survival.","zh":"protect themselves 指保護自身身體、安全或生存。"},{"en":"Students protect themselves from sunburn by wearing hats during outdoor activities.","zh":"學生在戶外活動時戴帽，以保護自己免被曬傷。"},{"en":"Plants protect themselves with chemicals because they cannot run away from animals.","zh":"植物用化學物保護自己，因為它們不能逃離動物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes self-defence.","zh":"這個短語描述自我防禦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reproductive rate","meaning":"繁殖率","examples":[{"en":"Howlers have a faster reproductive rate than the other monkeys.","zh":"吼猴的繁殖率比其他猴子更快。"},{"en":"Reproductive rate is how quickly or often a species produces offspring.","zh":"reproductive rate 指物種產生後代的速度或頻率。"},{"en":"Insects usually have a high reproductive rate because they lay many eggs.","zh":"昆蟲通常繁殖率高，因為牠們產下許多卵。"},{"en":"A faster reproductive rate helps a population recover after losses.","zh":"較快繁殖率幫助種群在損失後恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase measures speed of reproduction.","zh":"這個短語量度繁殖速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"about once every two years","meaning":"約每兩年一次","examples":[{"en":"Well-fed howlers can have a baby about once every two years.","zh":"營養充足的吼猴約每兩年可生一隻幼猴。"},{"en":"About once every two years means roughly one time in each two-year period.","zh":"about once every two years 指大約每兩年一次。"},{"en":"A school may review its curriculum about once every two years.","zh":"學校可能約每兩年檢討一次課程。"},{"en":"If a species gives birth about once every two years, its population can grow faster than species that reproduce later.","zh":"如果物種約每兩年生育一次，其種群可以比更遲繁殖的物種增長更快。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate frequency.","zh":"這個短語給出大約頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contain plenty of","meaning":"含有大量……","examples":[{"en":"The leaves contain plenty of water.","zh":"葉子含有大量水分。"},{"en":"To contain plenty of something means to have a large amount of it inside.","zh":"contain plenty of something 指內部有大量某物。"},{"en":"Oranges contain plenty of juice, so they are refreshing in hot weather.","zh":"橙含有大量果汁，所以在熱天很清爽。"},{"en":"Leaves that contain plenty of water help animals survive where drinking water is scarce.","zh":"含有大量水分的葉子幫助動物在飲用水稀少的地方生存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes abundance inside an object or food.","zh":"這個短語描述物件或食物內部含量豐富。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"resist the continuous drought","meaning":"抵禦持續乾旱","examples":[{"en":"Water-rich leaves help howlers resist the continuous drought.","zh":"含水豐富的葉子幫助吼猴抵禦持續乾旱。"},{"en":"To resist the continuous drought means to survive or cope with a long dry period without being badly harmed.","zh":"resist the continuous drought 指在長期乾旱中生存或應對，而不受嚴重傷害。"},{"en":"Farmers plant drought-resistant crops to resist continuous drought in dry regions.","zh":"農民在乾旱地區種植抗旱作物，以抵禦持續乾旱。"},{"en":"Howlers resist drought better because their food also supplies water.","zh":"吼猴更能抵禦乾旱，因為牠們的食物也提供水分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes coping with ongoing lack of rain.","zh":"這個短語描述應對持續缺雨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 44 - Monkeys and Forests.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 45":[{"front":"stealth forces","meaning":"隱性力量；暗中起作用的因素","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the stealth forces involved in weight loss.","zh":"文章討論減重過程中涉及的隱性力量。"},{"en":"Stealth forces are hidden influences that affect a situation without being obvious.","zh":"「stealth forces」是暗中影響情況、但不容易被看見的因素。"},{"en":"In a classroom, peer pressure can be a stealth force that changes how students behave.","zh":"在課室中，同儕壓力可以是改變學生行為的隱性力量。"},{"en":"If people ignore stealth forces, they may blame the wrong cause of a problem.","zh":"如果人們忽視隱性力量，就可能把問題歸咎於錯誤原因。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that some powerful factors work quietly in the background.","zh":"這個短語暗示有些強大因素在背景中悄悄運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"weight loss","meaning":"減重；減肥","examples":[{"en":"The field of weight loss is more complicated than many people think.","zh":"減重這個領域比許多人想像中更複雜。"},{"en":"Weight loss means reducing body weight, often through changes in diet, activity, health, or lifestyle.","zh":"「weight loss」意思是減少體重，通常透過飲食、活動、健康或生活方式改變。"},{"en":"A person may seek weight loss after a doctor warns that high blood pressure is becoming serious.","zh":"醫生警告高血壓變得嚴重後，一個人可能尋求減重。"},{"en":"If weight loss is too rapid, it may be hard to maintain and may affect health.","zh":"如果減重太快，可能難以維持，也可能影響健康。"},{"en":"The phrase is about losing weight, but the causes and methods can be complex.","zh":"這個短語關於體重下降，但成因和方法可以很複雜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the field of","meaning":"……的領域","examples":[{"en":"The field of weight loss includes research from many different disciplines.","zh":"減重領域包括來自許多不同學科的研究。"},{"en":"The field of something means the area of study, work, or professional activity connected with it.","zh":"「the field of」某事，意思是與它相關的研究、工作或專業活動範圍。"},{"en":"The field of education includes teaching, assessment, curriculum design, and child development.","zh":"教育領域包括教學、評估、課程設計和兒童發展。"},{"en":"If a field is complex, experts from different backgrounds may study it in different ways.","zh":"如果一個領域很複雜，來自不同背景的專家可能以不同方式研究它。"},{"en":"The phrase helps name a broad professional or academic area.","zh":"這個短語有助指出一個廣泛的專業或學術範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ancient fable","meaning":"古老寓言","examples":[{"en":"The writer compares weight-loss research to an ancient fable.","zh":"作者把減重研究比作一則古老寓言。"},{"en":"An ancient fable is an old short story that teaches a lesson, often through animals or symbolic characters.","zh":"「ancient fable」是古老短故事，通常透過動物或象徵人物教導道理。"},{"en":"Teachers may use an ancient fable to explain why people should not judge too quickly.","zh":"老師可能用古老寓言解釋為何人不應太快下判斷。"},{"en":"If a writer uses a fable, difficult ideas can become easier to understand.","zh":"如果作者使用寓言，困難概念可以變得更容易理解。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an old teaching story, not just any old tale.","zh":"這個短語指古老的教訓故事，而不只是任何舊故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the blind men and the elephant","meaning":"盲人摸象","examples":[{"en":"The field of weight loss is like the fable of the blind men and the elephant.","zh":"減重領域就像盲人摸象的寓言。"},{"en":"The blind men and the elephant is a story about people understanding only part of a larger truth.","zh":"「the blind men and the elephant」是一個關於人只理解較大真相其中一部分的故事。"},{"en":"In a group project, each student may see only one part of the problem, like the blind men and the elephant.","zh":"在小組專題中，每個學生可能只看見問題一部分，就像盲人摸象。"},{"en":"If experts study only one side of obesity, their findings may seem to disagree.","zh":"如果專家只研究肥胖的一面，他們的發現可能看似互相矛盾。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that partial knowledge can create confusion.","zh":"這個短語提醒人，片面知識會造成混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"investigate a different part of","meaning":"研究……的不同部分","examples":[{"en":"Each man investigates a different part of the animal.","zh":"每個人研究這隻動物的不同部分。"},{"en":"To investigate a different part of something means to study one separate section rather than the whole thing.","zh":"「investigate a different part of」某事，意思是研究其中一個獨立部分，而不是整體。"},{"en":"In a school project, one student may investigate the causes of pollution while another studies its effects.","zh":"在學校專題中，一名學生可能研究污染成因，另一名研究其影響。"},{"en":"If each expert investigates a different part of a problem, their conclusions may not match at first.","zh":"如果每位專家研究問題的不同部分，他們的結論起初可能不吻合。"},{"en":"The phrase describes divided research into separate areas.","zh":"這個短語描述把研究分成不同範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"report back","meaning":"匯報；報告結果","examples":[{"en":"Each man investigates the animal and reports back.","zh":"每個人研究那隻動物後回來匯報。"},{"en":"To report back means to return with information after checking, researching, or completing a task.","zh":"「report back」意思是在檢查、研究或完成任務後帶着資料回來匯報。"},{"en":"A student may interview classmates and report back to the group with the results.","zh":"學生可能訪問同學後，向小組匯報結果。"},{"en":"If staff report back clearly, the team can decide what to do next.","zh":"如果員工清楚匯報，團隊就能決定下一步。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving findings after an investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述調查後報告發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"only to discover that","meaning":"結果卻發現","examples":[{"en":"Each man reports back, only to discover that his finding conflicts with the others.","zh":"每個人回來匯報，結果卻發現自己的發現與其他人的相衝突。"},{"en":"Only to discover that means someone does something and then unexpectedly finds out a surprising result.","zh":"「only to discover that」意思是某人做完某事後，意外發現令人驚訝的結果。"},{"en":"A student may study one chapter carefully, only to discover that the test covers another chapter.","zh":"學生可能很仔細溫習一章，結果卻發現測驗考另一章。"},{"en":"If researchers expect agreement but find conflict, the result can be confusing.","zh":"如果研究人員預期一致，卻發現衝突，結果可能令人困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase often introduces an unexpected or disappointing discovery.","zh":"這個短語常引入意外或令人失望的發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"bafflingly incompatible with","meaning":"令人費解地與……不相容","examples":[{"en":"His finding is bafflingly incompatible with those of the others.","zh":"他的發現令人費解地與其他人的發現不相容。"},{"en":"Bafflingly incompatible with means confusingly unable to fit or agree with something else.","zh":"「bafflingly incompatible with」意思是令人困惑地無法與另一事物配合或一致。"},{"en":"Two witnesses may give stories that are bafflingly incompatible with each other.","zh":"兩名目擊者可能給出彼此令人費解地不相容的說法。"},{"en":"If research findings are incompatible, scientists must check methods, samples, and assumptions.","zh":"如果研究發現不相容，科學家就必須檢查方法、樣本和假設。"},{"en":"The phrase describes disagreement that is difficult to explain.","zh":"這個短語描述難以解釋的不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"various findings","meaning":"各種研究結果","examples":[{"en":"Various findings about obesity come from many different experts.","zh":"關於肥胖的各種研究結果來自許多不同專家。"},{"en":"Various findings are different results or conclusions discovered through research.","zh":"「various findings」是透過研究發現的不同結果或結論。"},{"en":"A school survey may produce various findings about homework, sleep, and stress.","zh":"學校調查可能產生關於功課、睡眠和壓力的各種研究結果。"},{"en":"If various findings point in different directions, a problem may be more complex than expected.","zh":"如果各種研究結果指向不同方向，問題可能比預期更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights multiple pieces of research evidence.","zh":"這個短語突出多項研究證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"public-health experts","meaning":"公共衞生專家","examples":[{"en":"Public-health experts have produced findings about weight loss.","zh":"公共衞生專家提出了關於減重的研究結果。"},{"en":"Public-health experts study the health of whole populations, not just individual patients.","zh":"「public-health experts」研究整體人口的健康，而不只是個別病人。"},{"en":"Public-health experts may study smoking, vaccination, obesity, and air pollution.","zh":"公共衞生專家可能研究吸煙、疫苗接種、肥胖和空氣污染。"},{"en":"If a health problem affects millions of people, public-health experts look for social patterns and prevention strategies.","zh":"如果健康問題影響數百萬人，公共衞生專家會尋找社會模式和預防策略。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to specialists in population health.","zh":"這個短語指人口健康方面的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"physicians","meaning":"醫生","examples":[{"en":"Physicians often study the medical causes of obesity.","zh":"醫生常研究肥胖的醫學成因。"},{"en":"Physicians are medical doctors who diagnose, treat, and advise patients.","zh":"「physicians」是診斷、治療和建議病人的醫生。"},{"en":"A physician may check blood pressure, blood sugar, and family history during a health visit.","zh":"醫生在健康檢查中可能檢查血壓、血糖和家族病史。"},{"en":"If a patient gains weight suddenly, a physician may look for medical explanations.","zh":"如果病人體重突然增加，醫生可能尋找醫學解釋。"},{"en":"The word refers to doctors, especially in formal or medical writing.","zh":"這個詞指醫生，尤其用於正式或醫學寫作中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"psychologists","meaning":"心理學家","examples":[{"en":"Psychologists examine the behavioural side of weight loss.","zh":"心理學家研究減重的行為層面。"},{"en":"Psychologists study thoughts, emotions, behaviour, and mental processes.","zh":"「psychologists」研究思想、情緒、行為和心理過程。"},{"en":"A psychologist may help a student manage stress before important exams.","zh":"心理學家可能幫助學生在重要考試前管理壓力。"},{"en":"If eating habits are linked to anxiety, psychologists can help explain the pattern.","zh":"如果飲食習慣與焦慮有關，心理學家可以幫助解釋這種模式。"},{"en":"The word refers to experts in the mind and behaviour.","zh":"這個詞指研究心理和行為的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"geneticists","meaning":"遺傳學家","examples":[{"en":"Geneticists study how genes may affect body weight.","zh":"遺傳學家研究基因如何可能影響體重。"},{"en":"Geneticists are scientists who study genes, heredity, and inherited traits.","zh":"「geneticists」是研究基因、遺傳和遺傳特徵的科學家。"},{"en":"A geneticist may study why some diseases run in families.","zh":"遺傳學家可能研究為何某些疾病會在家族中出現。"},{"en":"If body weight is partly influenced by genes, geneticists can help explain biological risk.","zh":"如果體重部分受基因影響，遺傳學家可以幫助解釋生物風險。"},{"en":"The word refers to experts in genetic inheritance.","zh":"這個詞指遺傳方面的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"molecular biologists","meaning":"分子生物學家","examples":[{"en":"Molecular biologists investigate biological processes related to obesity.","zh":"分子生物學家研究與肥胖相關的生物過程。"},{"en":"Molecular biologists study life at the level of cells, genes, proteins, and molecules.","zh":"「molecular biologists」在細胞、基因、蛋白質和分子層面研究生命。"},{"en":"A molecular biologist may study how a hormone sends signals inside the body.","zh":"分子生物學家可能研究荷爾蒙如何在體內傳遞訊號。"},{"en":"If obesity involves cell-level processes, molecular biology can reveal hidden mechanisms.","zh":"如果肥胖涉及細胞層面的過程，分子生物學可以揭示隱藏機制。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to scientists who study the smallest working parts of life.","zh":"這個短語指研究生命最小運作部分的科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"nutritionists","meaning":"營養學家","examples":[{"en":"Nutritionists study how diet affects body weight.","zh":"營養學家研究飲食如何影響體重。"},{"en":"Nutritionists are experts who study food, nutrients, eating habits, and health.","zh":"「nutritionists」是研究食物、營養素、飲食習慣和健康的專家。"},{"en":"A nutritionist may help a family plan meals with more vegetables and less sugar.","zh":"營養學家可能幫助家庭規劃更多蔬菜、較少糖分的餐單。"},{"en":"If a person eats poorly, a nutritionist can suggest practical changes.","zh":"如果一個人飲食不佳，營養學家可以建議實際改變。"},{"en":"The word refers to specialists in diet and nutrition.","zh":"這個詞指飲食和營養方面的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"about as similar as","meaning":"相似程度就像……與……一樣","examples":[{"en":"The various findings are about as similar as an elephant’s tusk is to its tail.","zh":"各種研究結果的相似程度就像象牙與象尾一樣。"},{"en":"About as similar as means almost not similar at all, often used humorously or critically.","zh":"「about as similar as」意思是幾乎完全不相似，常帶幽默或批評語氣。"},{"en":"Saying those two plans are alike is about as similar as a bicycle is to a bus.","zh":"說那兩個計劃相似，就像說單車和巴士相似一樣。"},{"en":"If two explanations differ greatly, this phrase stresses the contrast sharply.","zh":"如果兩個解釋差異很大，這個短語會強烈突出對比。"},{"en":"The phrase uses comparison to show strong difference.","zh":"這個短語用比較顯示強烈差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an elephant’s tusk","meaning":"象牙","examples":[{"en":"An elephant’s tusk is very different from its tail.","zh":"象牙與象尾非常不同。"},{"en":"An elephant’s tusk is the long hard ivory tooth that grows from an elephant’s mouth.","zh":"「an elephant’s tusk」是從大象口部長出的長而硬的象牙。"},{"en":"In a picture book, children may recognise an elephant by its trunk, ears, and tusks.","zh":"在圖畫書中，孩子可能透過象鼻、耳朵和象牙認出大象。"},{"en":"If someone compares a tusk with a tail, they are stressing how different two things are.","zh":"如果有人把象牙與象尾比較，他是在強調兩件事非常不同。"},{"en":"The phrase is used here as part of a vivid contrast.","zh":"這個短語在這裡用作鮮明對比的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be largely predetermined by","meaning":"很大程度上由……預先決定","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers say obesity is largely predetermined by our genes and biology.","zh":"有些研究人員說肥胖很大程度上由我們的基因和生理因素預先決定。"},{"en":"To be largely predetermined by something means to be mostly decided in advance by that factor.","zh":"「be largely predetermined by」某事，意思是很大程度上由該因素事先決定。"},{"en":"A plant’s maximum height may be largely predetermined by its species and genetics.","zh":"植物的最高高度可能很大程度上由其品種和基因預先決定。"},{"en":"If weight is partly predetermined by biology, personal choice is not the whole explanation.","zh":"如果體重部分由生理因素預先決定，個人選擇就不是全部解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that hidden earlier factors strongly shape the outcome.","zh":"這個短語暗示較早的隱藏因素強烈塑造結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"genes and biology","meaning":"基因和生理因素","examples":[{"en":"Genes and biology may strongly influence obesity.","zh":"基因和生理因素可能強烈影響肥胖。"},{"en":"Genes and biology refer to inherited information and the body’s natural physical processes.","zh":"「genes and biology」指遺傳資訊和身體自然生理過程。"},{"en":"A person’s height is shaped by genes and biology as well as nutrition.","zh":"一個人的身高受基因和生理因素影響，也受營養影響。"},{"en":"If genes and biology affect weight, people may respond differently to the same diet.","zh":"如果基因和生理因素影響體重，人們對同一飲食可能有不同反應。"},{"en":"The phrase points to internal body factors, not just lifestyle.","zh":"這個短語指身體內在因素，而不只是生活方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"attribute something to","meaning":"將……歸因於","examples":[{"en":"Some experts attribute obesity to an overabundance of unhealthy food and screen time.","zh":"有些專家將肥胖歸因於過量不健康食物和屏幕時間。"},{"en":"To attribute something to a cause means to say that the cause explains it.","zh":"「attribute something to」某原因，意思是說該原因解釋了某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may attribute poor test results to lack of sleep and weak revision.","zh":"老師可能將測驗成績差歸因於睡眠不足和溫習薄弱。"},{"en":"If experts attribute weight gain only to laziness, they may miss biological causes.","zh":"如果專家只將體重增加歸因於懶惰，他們可能忽略生物成因。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when explaining why something happens.","zh":"這個短語用於解釋某事為何發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an overabundance of","meaning":"過量的……","examples":[{"en":"Some people attribute obesity to an overabundance of fries and soda.","zh":"有些人將肥胖歸因於過量薯條和汽水。"},{"en":"An overabundance of something means too much of it is available.","zh":"「an overabundance of」某物，意思是該物供應過多。"},{"en":"An overabundance of cheap snacks near schools may encourage unhealthy eating.","zh":"學校附近有過量廉價小食，可能鼓勵不健康飲食。"},{"en":"If people are surrounded by too much high-calorie food, making healthy choices becomes harder.","zh":"如果人們被太多高熱量食物包圍，作出健康選擇就更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes excessive availability.","zh":"這個短語描述過度供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fries and soda","meaning":"薯條和汽水","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers blame obesity partly on fries and soda.","zh":"有些研究人員部分把肥胖歸咎於薯條和汽水。"},{"en":"Fries and soda are common fast-food items often high in calories, fat, sugar, or salt.","zh":"「fries and soda」是常見快餐食品，通常熱量、脂肪、糖分或鹽分較高。"},{"en":"A teenager who buys fries and soda every day may consume more calories than expected.","zh":"每天買薯條和汽水的青少年，可能攝取比預期更多卡路里。"},{"en":"If these foods replace balanced meals, health problems may become more likely.","zh":"如果這些食物取代均衡膳食，健康問題可能更容易出現。"},{"en":"The phrase stands for unhealthy convenience food in the passage.","zh":"這個短語在文章中代表不健康方便食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"screen-sucking","meaning":"過度使用屏幕；長時間對着屏幕","examples":[{"en":"Screen-sucking may contribute to a less active lifestyle.","zh":"過度使用屏幕可能導致較少活動的生活方式。"},{"en":"Screen-sucking means spending too much time absorbed in screens such as phones, computers, or television.","zh":"「screen-sucking」意思是過多時間沉迷於手機、電腦或電視等屏幕。"},{"en":"A child who spends the whole afternoon gaming may have little time for outdoor play.","zh":"整個下午打機的孩子可能很少有時間戶外玩耍。"},{"en":"If screen time replaces movement, daily energy use can decrease.","zh":"如果屏幕時間取代活動，每日能量消耗可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and critical, suggesting unhealthy attachment to screens.","zh":"這個短語較口語且帶批評意味，暗示不健康地依附屏幕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"viral infection","meaning":"病毒感染","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers think obesity may be linked to viral infection.","zh":"有些研究人員認為肥胖可能與病毒感染有關。"},{"en":"A viral infection happens when a virus enters the body and begins to multiply.","zh":"「viral infection」是病毒進入身體並開始繁殖時發生的感染。"},{"en":"Flu is a common viral infection that can cause fever, tiredness, and coughing.","zh":"流感是一種常見病毒感染，可引起發燒、疲倦和咳嗽。"},{"en":"If a virus affects metabolism, it might influence body weight in unexpected ways.","zh":"如果病毒影響新陳代謝，它可能以意想不到的方式影響體重。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to illness caused by a virus.","zh":"這個短語指由病毒造成的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"insulin","meaning":"胰島素","examples":[{"en":"Insulin may play a role in how the body stores fat.","zh":"胰島素可能在身體如何儲存脂肪方面發揮作用。"},{"en":"Insulin is a hormone that helps move sugar from the blood into body cells.","zh":"「insulin」是一種幫助把糖分從血液移入身體細胞的荷爾蒙。"},{"en":"People with diabetes often need to monitor how their body uses insulin.","zh":"糖尿病患者常需要監測身體如何使用胰島素。"},{"en":"If insulin levels are high after meals, the body may store more energy as fat.","zh":"如果餐後胰島素水平高，身體可能把更多能量以脂肪形式儲存。"},{"en":"The word refers to an important hormone in blood-sugar control.","zh":"這個詞指血糖控制中的重要荷爾蒙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"metabolic conditions","meaning":"代謝狀況","examples":[{"en":"Some experts focus on metabolic conditions encountered before birth.","zh":"有些專家集中研究出生前遇到的代謝狀況。"},{"en":"Metabolic conditions are body conditions related to how energy, sugar, and nutrients are processed.","zh":"「metabolic conditions」是與身體如何處理能量、糖分和營養有關的狀況。"},{"en":"A doctor may examine metabolic conditions when a patient gains weight without eating more.","zh":"如果病人沒有吃更多卻增重，醫生可能檢查代謝狀況。"},{"en":"If metabolic conditions are shaped early in life, later health may be affected.","zh":"如果代謝狀況在生命早期被塑造，日後健康可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the body’s energy-processing environment.","zh":"這個短語指身體處理能量的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"encounter in the womb","meaning":"在子宮內遇到；在胎內經歷","examples":[{"en":"Some metabolic conditions are encountered in the womb.","zh":"有些代謝狀況是在子宮內遇到的。"},{"en":"To encounter something in the womb means to experience it before birth inside the mother’s body.","zh":"「encounter something in the womb」意思是在出生前於母體內經歷某事。"},{"en":"A baby may be affected by nutrients, hormones, or blood-sugar levels encountered in the womb.","zh":"嬰兒可能受在子宮內遇到的營養、荷爾蒙或血糖水平影響。"},{"en":"If early conditions influence development, health risks may begin before birth.","zh":"如果早期狀況影響發展，健康風險可能在出生前已開始。"},{"en":"The phrase describes prenatal exposure.","zh":"這個短語描述產前接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"subscribe to a theory","meaning":"認同某種理論","examples":[{"en":"Everyone seems to subscribe to their own little theory about obesity.","zh":"每個人似乎都認同自己那套關於肥胖的小理論。"},{"en":"To subscribe to a theory means to believe or support that explanation.","zh":"「subscribe to a theory」意思是相信或支持某種解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may subscribe to the theory that students learn best through active practice.","zh":"老師可能認同學生透過主動練習學得最好的理論。"},{"en":"If every expert supports a different theory, the public may feel confused.","zh":"如果每位專家支持不同理論，公眾可能感到困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes accepting an idea as true or useful.","zh":"這個短語描述接受某想法為真或有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"medical director","meaning":"醫學總監","examples":[{"en":"Robert Berkowitz is the medical director of a weight and eating disorders centre.","zh":"Robert Berkowitz 是一間體重與進食失調中心的醫學總監。"},{"en":"A medical director is a senior doctor responsible for medical standards, services, or programmes.","zh":"「medical director」是負責醫療標準、服務或項目的高級醫生。"},{"en":"A hospital’s medical director may decide how patient care should be organised.","zh":"醫院的醫學總監可能決定病人護理如何組織。"},{"en":"If a centre treats complex disorders, a medical director helps guide its professional work.","zh":"如果中心治療複雜疾病，醫學總監會指導其專業工作。"},{"en":"The phrase names a leadership role in healthcare.","zh":"這個短語指出醫療保健中的領導職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"eating disorders","meaning":"進食失調","examples":[{"en":"The centre studies weight and eating disorders.","zh":"該中心研究體重和進食失調。"},{"en":"Eating disorders are health conditions involving harmful patterns of eating, food control, or body image.","zh":"「eating disorders」是涉及有害飲食模式、食物控制或身體形象的健康狀況。"},{"en":"A teenager with an eating disorder may skip meals even when hungry.","zh":"有進食失調的青少年即使肚餓，也可能跳過正餐。"},{"en":"If eating disorders are not treated, they can damage both physical and mental health.","zh":"如果進食失調沒有被治療，可能損害身心健康。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to serious medical and psychological conditions.","zh":"這個短語指嚴重醫學和心理狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be programmed to","meaning":"被設定去；天生傾向於","examples":[{"en":"Human bodies may be programmed to hang onto fat.","zh":"人體可能天生傾向於保留脂肪。"},{"en":"To be programmed to do something means to be naturally set up or strongly inclined to do it.","zh":"「be programmed to」做某事，意思是自然上被設定或強烈傾向做該事。"},{"en":"Babies seem programmed to cry when they need food, comfort, or sleep.","zh":"嬰兒似乎天生會在需要食物、安撫或睡眠時哭。"},{"en":"If the body is programmed to save energy, weight loss may become harder.","zh":"如果身體被設定去節省能量，減重可能變得更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a built-in tendency.","zh":"這個短語暗示內在傾向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hang onto fat","meaning":"保留脂肪；不輕易消耗脂肪","examples":[{"en":"We may be programmed to hang onto the fat we have.","zh":"我們可能天生傾向於保留已有脂肪。"},{"en":"To hang onto fat means to keep body fat rather than burn it easily.","zh":"「hang onto fat」意思是保留身體脂肪，而不是輕易燃燒它。"},{"en":"Some people exercise regularly but still hang onto fat around the waist.","zh":"有些人規律運動，但腰部仍會保留脂肪。"},{"en":"If the body senses food shortage, it may slow metabolism and conserve fat.","zh":"如果身體感覺食物不足，它可能減慢新陳代謝並保存脂肪。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that the body resists losing stored energy.","zh":"這個短語暗示身體抗拒失去儲存能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be predisposed to","meaning":"天生較易……","examples":[{"en":"Some people are predisposed to create and carry more fat.","zh":"有些人天生較易形成並積存更多脂肪。"},{"en":"To be predisposed to something means to have a natural tendency or higher risk for it.","zh":"「be predisposed to」某事，意思是對它有自然傾向或較高風險。"},{"en":"Some children are predisposed to allergies because they run in the family.","zh":"有些孩子因家族遺傳而天生較易有過敏。"},{"en":"If a person is predisposed to weight gain, the same diet may affect them more strongly.","zh":"如果一個人天生較易增重，同一飲食可能對他影響更強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes biological or early-life tendency.","zh":"這個短語描述生物或早期生命傾向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"create and carry more fat","meaning":"形成並積存更多脂肪","examples":[{"en":"Some people are biologically predisposed to create and carry more fat.","zh":"有些人在生理上天生較易形成並積存更多脂肪。"},{"en":"To create and carry more fat means to form and store more body fat over time.","zh":"「create and carry more fat」意思是隨時間形成並儲存更多身體脂肪。"},{"en":"A person may create and carry more fat if energy intake repeatedly exceeds energy use.","zh":"如果能量攝取反覆超過能量消耗，一個人可能形成並積存更多脂肪。"},{"en":"If the body stores energy efficiently, it may carry more fat even under ordinary conditions.","zh":"如果身體有效率地儲存能量，即使在普通情況下也可能積存更多脂肪。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both producing fat and keeping it in the body.","zh":"這個短語同時描述產生脂肪和把脂肪留在體內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"diet and exercise","meaning":"飲食和運動","examples":[{"en":"Diet and exercise can help with weight loss.","zh":"飲食和運動可以幫助減重。"},{"en":"Diet and exercise refer to what a person eats and how physically active they are.","zh":"「diet and exercise」指一個人吃甚麼，以及身體活動量如何。"},{"en":"A person may improve diet and exercise by eating more vegetables and walking daily.","zh":"一個人可以透過多吃蔬菜和每日步行來改善飲食和運動。"},{"en":"If diet changes but exercise does not, health may improve only partly.","zh":"如果飲食改變但運動沒有改變，健康可能只部分改善。"},{"en":"The phrase names two common lifestyle tools for health management.","zh":"這個短語指出健康管理中的兩種常見生活方式工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the end","meaning":"到頭來；最終","examples":[{"en":"In the end, the solution to obesity is likely to be complicated.","zh":"到頭來，肥胖的解決方法很可能是複雜的。"},{"en":"In the end means finally or after considering everything.","zh":"「in the end」意思是最終，或在考慮所有事情後。"},{"en":"In the end, the team chose the simpler plan because it was cheaper and safer.","zh":"到頭來，團隊選擇較簡單的計劃，因為它較便宜和安全。"},{"en":"If many causes are involved, the final answer may not be simple.","zh":"如果涉及許多成因，最終答案可能不簡單。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a final conclusion.","zh":"這個短語引入最終結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"more complicated than","meaning":"比……更複雜","examples":[{"en":"The solution is more complicated than eating less and walking more.","zh":"解決方法比少吃和多走路更複雜。"},{"en":"More complicated than means not as simple as another explanation or action.","zh":"「more complicated than」意思是比另一種解釋或行動更不簡單。"},{"en":"Learning a language is more complicated than memorising a word list.","zh":"學習語言比背詞表更複雜。"},{"en":"If biology, habits, and environment all matter, weight loss is more complicated than willpower alone.","zh":"如果生理、習慣和環境都重要，減重就比單靠意志力更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase compares a complex reality with a simple idea.","zh":"這個短語比較複雜現實與簡單想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"push away the plate","meaning":"少吃；把食物推開","examples":[{"en":"Weight loss is more complicated than simply pushing away the plate.","zh":"減重比單純少吃更複雜。"},{"en":"To push away the plate means to stop eating or eat less, often used figuratively.","zh":"「push away the plate」意思是停止進食或吃少些，常作比喻使用。"},{"en":"A person may push away the plate when they feel full, even if food remains.","zh":"即使還有食物，一個人覺得飽時可能把碟推開。"},{"en":"If hunger hormones increase after dieting, simply eating less may not be easy.","zh":"如果節食後飢餓荷爾蒙上升，單純少吃可能並不容易。"},{"en":"The phrase represents the idea that weight loss is just about refusing food.","zh":"這個短語代表減重只是拒絕食物這種想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"it is not as simple as","meaning":"並不是簡單到……","examples":[{"en":"It is not as simple as saying that people are overweight because they are lazy.","zh":"事情並不是簡單到說人們超重是因為懶惰。"},{"en":"It is not as simple as means the explanation is more complex than that statement suggests.","zh":"「it is not as simple as」意思是解釋比那句話所暗示的更複雜。"},{"en":"School failure is not as simple as saying students do not try hard enough.","zh":"學業失敗並不是簡單到說學生不夠努力。"},{"en":"If many hidden factors shape behaviour, blaming one cause is unfair.","zh":"如果許多隱藏因素塑造行為，歸咎單一原因並不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase challenges an oversimplified explanation.","zh":"這個短語挑戰過分簡化的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"willpower","meaning":"意志力","examples":[{"en":"Willpower is not only possessed by thin people.","zh":"意志力並非只有瘦的人才擁有。"},{"en":"Willpower is the ability to control one’s actions and continue despite temptation or difficulty.","zh":"「willpower」是控制自己行動並在誘惑或困難中堅持的能力。"},{"en":"A student needs willpower to revise when friends are playing games online.","zh":"當朋友在網上打機時，學生需要意志力去溫習。"},{"en":"If hunger becomes constant, willpower alone may not be enough.","zh":"如果飢餓感變得持續，單靠意志力可能不足夠。"},{"en":"The word refers to mental self-control, not magic strength.","zh":"這個詞指心理自控力，而不是神奇力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a prerogative of","meaning":"……的特權","examples":[{"en":"Willpower is not a prerogative of thin people.","zh":"意志力不是瘦的人的特權。"},{"en":"A prerogative of a group is a special right or quality that belongs only to that group.","zh":"「a prerogative of」某群體，是只屬於該群體的特別權利或特質。"},{"en":"Good ideas are not a prerogative of senior staff; junior workers can have them too.","zh":"好想法不是高級員工的特權；初級員工也可以有。"},{"en":"If willpower is not a prerogative of thin people, overweight people should not be judged as weak.","zh":"如果意志力不是瘦人的特權，就不應把超重人士判斷為軟弱。"},{"en":"The phrase means something is not an exclusive possession.","zh":"這個短語意思是某事不是某群體獨有的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"thin people","meaning":"瘦的人","examples":[{"en":"The passage rejects the idea that only thin people have willpower.","zh":"文章反對只有瘦的人才有意志力這種想法。"},{"en":"Thin people are people whose bodies have little visible fat or a low body weight.","zh":"「thin people」是身體可見脂肪較少或體重較低的人。"},{"en":"Thin people may still have health problems, just as heavier people may be fit.","zh":"瘦的人仍可能有健康問題，就像較重的人也可能體能良好。"},{"en":"If society assumes thin people are always disciplined, it may judge bodies unfairly.","zh":"如果社會假設瘦的人一定有紀律，就可能不公平地評價身體。"},{"en":"The phrase describes body size, not moral worth.","zh":"這個短語描述身形，而不是道德價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be distributed equally","meaning":"平均分佈","examples":[{"en":"Willpower is distributed equally among people.","zh":"意志力在人群之間平均分佈。"},{"en":"To be distributed equally means to be shared fairly or evenly across a group.","zh":"「be distributed equally」意思是在一個群體中公平或平均地分配。"},{"en":"In a fair classroom, resources should be distributed equally among students.","zh":"在公平課室中，資源應在學生之間平均分佈。"},{"en":"If willpower is distributed equally, body weight cannot simply prove character.","zh":"如果意志力平均分佈，體重就不能簡單證明品格。"},{"en":"The phrase describes even sharing or spread.","zh":"這個短語描述平均分享或分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"years away from","meaning":"距離……仍有多年","examples":[{"en":"Science may still be years away from a miracle formula for fat loss.","zh":"科學距離減脂神奇方法可能仍有多年。"},{"en":"Years away from something means still needing many years before reaching or achieving it.","zh":"「years away from」某事，意思是仍需要多年才到達或達成它。"},{"en":"A small company may be years away from selling its product worldwide.","zh":"小公司距離把產品賣到全球可能仍有多年。"},{"en":"If science is years away from a cure, people should be careful about exaggerated promises.","zh":"如果科學距離療法仍有多年，人們應小心誇大承諾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something not yet close.","zh":"這個短語描述某事仍未接近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a miracle formula for","meaning":"……的神奇方法","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have not yet found a miracle formula for fat loss.","zh":"科學家尚未找到減脂的神奇方法。"},{"en":"A miracle formula for something is a perfect, easy solution that seems almost magical.","zh":"「a miracle formula for」某事，是看似近乎神奇、完美又簡單的解決方法。"},{"en":"There is no miracle formula for exam success; students need practice, feedback, and time.","zh":"考試成功沒有神奇方法；學生需要練習、回饋和時間。"},{"en":"If an advertisement promises a miracle formula, consumers should be cautious.","zh":"如果廣告承諾神奇方法，消費者應該小心。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests an unrealistic quick fix.","zh":"這個短語常暗示不切實際的快速解決方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fat loss","meaning":"減脂","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are still studying the science of fat loss.","zh":"研究人員仍在研究減脂科學。"},{"en":"Fat loss means reducing the amount of fat stored in the body.","zh":"「fat loss」意思是減少身體儲存的脂肪量。"},{"en":"A person may lose water weight quickly but achieve fat loss more slowly.","zh":"一個人可能很快減掉水分重量，但減脂較慢。"},{"en":"If fat loss is maintained, health risks may decrease over time.","zh":"如果減脂成果能維持，健康風險可能隨時間下降。"},{"en":"The phrase is more specific than general weight loss.","zh":"這個短語比一般減重更具體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the hormone leptin","meaning":"瘦素這種荷爾蒙","examples":[{"en":"The hormone leptin is important in the brain’s weight-control system.","zh":"瘦素這種荷爾蒙在大腦體重控制系統中很重要。"},{"en":"The hormone leptin is a chemical messenger involved in appetite, fat storage, and energy balance.","zh":"「the hormone leptin」是一種與食慾、脂肪儲存和能量平衡有關的化學訊使。"},{"en":"Doctors may study leptin when trying to understand why hunger changes after dieting.","zh":"醫生嘗試理解節食後飢餓感為何改變時，可能研究瘦素。"},{"en":"If leptin signals fall, the brain may think the body needs more food.","zh":"如果瘦素訊號下降，大腦可能以為身體需要更多食物。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific hormone linked to body weight.","zh":"這個短語指出與體重相關的特定荷爾蒙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a crucial player in","meaning":"……中的關鍵角色","examples":[{"en":"Leptin is a crucial player in the brain’s weight-management circuitry.","zh":"瘦素是大腦體重管理迴路中的關鍵角色。"},{"en":"A crucial player in something is an important factor or participant that strongly affects the result.","zh":"「a crucial player in」某事，是強烈影響結果的重要因素或參與者。"},{"en":"Sleep is a crucial player in memory because the brain processes learning during rest.","zh":"睡眠是記憶中的關鍵角色，因為大腦在休息時處理學習內容。"},{"en":"If leptin changes after weight loss, it may strongly affect hunger and metabolism.","zh":"如果瘦素在減重後改變，它可能強烈影響飢餓感和新陳代謝。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights an important role in a system.","zh":"這個短語突出某系統中的重要作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"weight-management circuitry","meaning":"體重管理迴路","examples":[{"en":"Leptin affects the brain’s weight-management circuitry.","zh":"瘦素影響大腦的體重管理迴路。"},{"en":"Weight-management circuitry refers to the body and brain systems that help regulate hunger, energy use, and body weight.","zh":"「weight-management circuitry」指幫助調節飢餓、能量使用和體重的身體及大腦系統。"},{"en":"The brain’s control system may tell a person to eat more when energy stores seem low.","zh":"當能量儲備看似偏低時，大腦控制系統可能叫人多吃。"},{"en":"If this circuitry becomes disrupted, weight control can become harder.","zh":"如果這個迴路被打亂，控制體重就可能更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a biological control network.","zh":"這個短語描述生物控制網絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"produce too little","meaning":"產生太少……","examples":[{"en":"Some people produce too little leptin.","zh":"有些人產生太少瘦素。"},{"en":"To produce too little of something means the body or system makes less than needed.","zh":"「produce too little」某物，意思是身體或系統製造的量少於所需。"},{"en":"If a printer produces too little ink, the words on the page look faint.","zh":"如果打印機產生太少墨水，頁面上的文字會很淡。"},{"en":"If the body produces too little of a hormone, normal signals may not work properly.","zh":"如果身體產生太少某種荷爾蒙，正常訊號可能不能正常運作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an insufficient amount being made.","zh":"這個短語描述製造量不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"become desensitised to","meaning":"對……變得不敏感","examples":[{"en":"Some people become desensitised to leptin.","zh":"有些人對瘦素變得不敏感。"},{"en":"To become desensitised to something means to become less responsive to it over time.","zh":"「become desensitised to」某物，意思是隨時間對它反應變弱。"},{"en":"A person may become desensitised to loud traffic noise after living near a busy road for years.","zh":"一個人住在繁忙道路附近多年後，可能對交通噪音變得不敏感。"},{"en":"If the body becomes desensitised to a hormone, the signal may no longer work strongly.","zh":"如果身體對某荷爾蒙變得不敏感，訊號可能不再有力運作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reduced sensitivity.","zh":"這個短語描述敏感度下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"obese people","meaning":"肥胖人士","examples":[{"en":"Obese people may experience biological changes after losing weight.","zh":"肥胖人士在減重後可能經歷生物變化。"},{"en":"Obese people are people whose body fat level is high enough to raise health concerns.","zh":"「obese people」是身體脂肪水平高到引起健康關注的人。"},{"en":"A doctor may advise obese people to check blood pressure, blood sugar, and heart health.","zh":"醫生可能建議肥胖人士檢查血壓、血糖和心臟健康。"},{"en":"If obese people lose weight, their bodies may respond with stronger hunger signals.","zh":"如果肥胖人士減重，他們的身體可能以更強飢餓訊號作反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a medical weight category, not a person’s character.","zh":"這個短語描述醫學體重類別，而不是人的品格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"leptin levels plummet","meaning":"瘦素水平急跌","examples":[{"en":"When obese people lose weight, their leptin levels plummet.","zh":"當肥胖人士減重時，他們的瘦素水平會急跌。"},{"en":"Leptin levels plummet means the amount of leptin drops very quickly and sharply.","zh":"「leptin levels plummet」意思是瘦素數量非常快速而大幅下降。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may plummet after repeated criticism.","zh":"學生在反覆批評後，自信可能急跌。"},{"en":"If leptin levels plummet, the body may increase hunger and slow energy use.","zh":"如果瘦素水平急跌，身體可能增加飢餓感並減慢能量使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a sudden steep fall.","zh":"這個短語描述突然大幅下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"along with","meaning":"與……一起；連同","examples":[{"en":"Leptin levels plummet along with metabolism.","zh":"瘦素水平連同新陳代謝一起急跌。"},{"en":"Along with means together with or at the same time as something else.","zh":"「along with」意思是與某事一起或同時。"},{"en":"A school notice may be sent along with a consent form.","zh":"學校通告可能連同同意書一起發出。"},{"en":"If one health marker changes along with another, the two may be connected.","zh":"如果一項健康指標與另一項一起改變，兩者可能有關。"},{"en":"The phrase shows things happening or being considered together.","zh":"這個短語顯示事情一同發生或被一同考慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"metabolism","meaning":"新陳代謝","examples":[{"en":"A person’s metabolism may slow down after weight loss.","zh":"一個人的新陳代謝在減重後可能減慢。"},{"en":"Metabolism is the process by which the body uses food and energy to stay alive and active.","zh":"「metabolism」是身體使用食物和能量以維持生命與活動的過程。"},{"en":"Exercise, muscle mass, hormones, and age can all affect metabolism.","zh":"運動、肌肉量、荷爾蒙和年齡都可以影響新陳代謝。"},{"en":"If metabolism slows, the body may burn fewer calories than before.","zh":"如果新陳代謝減慢，身體可能比以前消耗較少卡路里。"},{"en":"The word refers to the body’s energy-processing system.","zh":"這個詞指身體處理能量的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"efficient at using fuel","meaning":"更有效率地使用能量","examples":[{"en":"The body becomes more efficient at using fuel after weight loss.","zh":"身體在減重後變得更有效率地使用能量。"},{"en":"Efficient at using fuel means able to use energy with less waste.","zh":"「efficient at using fuel」意思是能以較少浪費使用能量。"},{"en":"A car that is efficient at using fuel can travel farther with less petrol.","zh":"更有效率地使用燃料的汽車，可以用較少汽油行駛更遠。"},{"en":"If the body becomes more efficient, it may need fewer calories for the same activity.","zh":"如果身體變得更有效率，同樣活動可能需要較少卡路里。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using energy economically.","zh":"這個短語描述節省地使用能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"conserve fat","meaning":"保存脂肪","examples":[{"en":"The body may become better at conserving fat.","zh":"身體可能變得更擅長保存脂肪。"},{"en":"To conserve fat means to save or preserve stored fat instead of burning it.","zh":"「conserve fat」意思是保存或保留已儲存脂肪，而不是燃燒它。"},{"en":"During a food shortage, the body may conserve energy to protect survival.","zh":"在食物短缺期間，身體可能保存能量以保護生存。"},{"en":"If the body conserves fat after dieting, keeping weight off becomes harder.","zh":"如果身體在節食後保存脂肪，維持減重成果就更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the body protecting stored energy.","zh":"這個短語描述身體保護已儲存能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make it tough to","meaning":"令……變得困難","examples":[{"en":"Lower leptin levels make it tough to keep the weight off.","zh":"較低瘦素水平令保持減重成果變得困難。"},{"en":"To make it tough to do something means to make that action difficult.","zh":"「make it tough to」做某事，意思是令該行動變得困難。"},{"en":"Noisy neighbours can make it tough to sleep before an exam.","zh":"嘈吵鄰居可能令考試前睡覺變得困難。"},{"en":"If hunger increases after dieting, it becomes harder to maintain the new weight.","zh":"如果節食後飢餓感增加，維持新體重就變得更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how one factor creates difficulty.","zh":"這個短語解釋某因素如何造成困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"keep the weight off","meaning":"保持減重成果；不反彈","examples":[{"en":"Many people find it difficult to keep the weight off.","zh":"許多人發現保持減重成果很困難。"},{"en":"To keep the weight off means to maintain weight loss and avoid regaining the lost weight.","zh":"「keep the weight off」意思是維持減重成果，避免重新增加已減去的體重。"},{"en":"A person may lose weight before summer but struggle to keep it off during winter.","zh":"一個人可能在夏天前減重，但在冬天難以保持不反彈。"},{"en":"If metabolism slows after dieting, keeping the weight off may require long-term habits.","zh":"如果節食後新陳代謝減慢，保持減重成果可能需要長期習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on maintenance after weight loss.","zh":"這個短語集中於減重後的維持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"go into a state of","meaning":"進入……狀態","examples":[{"en":"Obese dieters’ bodies can go into a state of chronic hunger.","zh":"肥胖節食者的身體可能進入長期飢餓狀態。"},{"en":"To go into a state of something means to enter a particular condition or mode.","zh":"「go into a state of」某事，意思是進入某種狀況或模式。"},{"en":"A phone may go into a state of low power when the battery is almost empty.","zh":"手機電量快耗盡時，可能進入低電量狀態。"},{"en":"If the body enters a hunger state, it may push the person to eat more.","zh":"如果身體進入飢餓狀態，它可能推動人吃更多。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shift into a condition.","zh":"這個短語描述轉入某種狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"chronic hunger","meaning":"長期飢餓感","examples":[{"en":"Some dieters experience chronic hunger after losing weight.","zh":"有些節食者在減重後經歷長期飢餓感。"},{"en":"Chronic hunger is a long-lasting feeling of hunger that does not go away easily.","zh":"「chronic hunger」是持續很久、不易消失的飢餓感。"},{"en":"A person with chronic hunger may think about food even after eating a normal meal.","zh":"有長期飢餓感的人，即使吃了一頓正常餐後，仍可能想着食物。"},{"en":"If chronic hunger continues for months, maintaining a diet becomes extremely hard.","zh":"如果長期飢餓感持續數月，維持飲食計劃會變得極其困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes persistent hunger, not a short appetite.","zh":"這個短語描述持續飢餓，而不是短暫食慾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"compare something to","meaning":"將……比作","examples":[{"en":"Rudolph Leibel compares chronic hunger to thirst.","zh":"Rudolph Leibel 將長期飢餓感比作口渴。"},{"en":"To compare something to another thing means to show their similarity to help people understand.","zh":"「compare something to」另一事物，意思是顯示兩者相似之處以幫助理解。"},{"en":"A teacher may compare grammar to building blocks because both create structure.","zh":"老師可能將文法比作積木，因為兩者都建立結構。"},{"en":"If hunger is compared to thirst, readers understand it as a strong physical drive.","zh":"如果飢餓感被比作口渴，讀者就會把它理解為強烈生理驅動。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an analogy.","zh":"這個短語引入類比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tolerate chronic thirst","meaning":"忍受長期口渴","examples":[{"en":"Few people could tolerate chronic thirst for long.","zh":"很少人能長時間忍受長期口渴。"},{"en":"To tolerate chronic thirst means to endure a constant need to drink water over a long time.","zh":"「tolerate chronic thirst」意思是長期忍受持續喝水需求。"},{"en":"A hiker without enough water may struggle to tolerate thirst even for a few hours.","zh":"沒有足夠水的遠足者可能連幾小時口渴也難以忍受。"},{"en":"If chronic hunger feels like chronic thirst, expecting people to ignore it is unrealistic.","zh":"如果長期飢餓感像長期口渴，期望人們忽視它就不切實際。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how hard a constant physical urge can be to bear.","zh":"這個短語顯示持續生理衝動有多難承受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the majority","meaning":"大多數人","examples":[{"en":"The majority of people could not stand chronic thirst.","zh":"大多數人受不了長期口渴。"},{"en":"The majority means more than half of a group.","zh":"「the majority」意思是一個群體中超過一半的人。"},{"en":"The majority of students chose to revise in the library rather than at home.","zh":"大多數學生選擇在圖書館溫習，而不是在家中。"},{"en":"If the majority cannot tolerate a condition, it is probably very difficult.","zh":"如果大多數人不能忍受某狀況，它很可能非常困難。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to most people in a group.","zh":"這個短語指一個群體中的大部分人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cannot stand it","meaning":"受不了","examples":[{"en":"Most people cannot stand a constant feeling of hunger.","zh":"大多數人受不了持續飢餓感。"},{"en":"Cannot stand it means cannot tolerate or endure something because it is too unpleasant.","zh":"「cannot stand it」意思是因為某事太不愉快而無法忍受。"},{"en":"Some students cannot stand loud noise when they are trying to read.","zh":"有些學生在嘗試閱讀時受不了嘈吵聲。"},{"en":"If hunger becomes constant, a person may eventually abandon the diet.","zh":"如果飢餓感變得持續，一個人最終可能放棄節食。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses strong difficulty in tolerating something.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈的難以忍受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a behavioural problem","meaning":"行為問題","examples":[{"en":"Leibel questions whether chronic hunger is really a behavioural problem.","zh":"Leibel 質疑長期飢餓感是否真的是行為問題。"},{"en":"A behavioural problem is a difficulty caused mainly by actions, habits, or conduct.","zh":"「a behavioural problem」是主要由行動、習慣或行為造成的困難。"},{"en":"Talking loudly in class may be treated as a behavioural problem.","zh":"在課堂大聲說話可能被視為行為問題。"},{"en":"If hunger is biological, calling it a behavioural problem may be unfair.","zh":"如果飢餓感是生理性的，把它稱為行為問題可能不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase separates behaviour-based causes from physical causes.","zh":"這個短語把行為成因與身體成因區分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lack of willpower","meaning":"缺乏意志力","examples":[{"en":"Chronic hunger is not simply a lack of willpower.","zh":"長期飢餓感不只是缺乏意志力。"},{"en":"Lack of willpower means not having enough self-control to continue or resist temptation.","zh":"「lack of willpower」意思是沒有足夠自控力去堅持或抵抗誘惑。"},{"en":"Forgetting homework once is not always a lack of willpower; the student may be exhausted.","zh":"偶爾忘記功課不一定是缺乏意志力；學生可能太疲倦。"},{"en":"If biology creates strong hunger, failure to diet should not be blamed only on weak self-control.","zh":"如果生理因素造成強烈飢餓，節食失敗就不應只歸咎於自控力弱。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used to criticise, but it can oversimplify problems.","zh":"這個短語常用於批評，但可能過分簡化問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"espouse moderate daily exercise","meaning":"支持溫和日常運動","examples":[{"en":"The government has long espoused moderate daily exercise.","zh":"政府長期支持溫和日常運動。"},{"en":"To espouse moderate daily exercise means to publicly support regular, not extreme, physical activity.","zh":"「espouse moderate daily exercise」意思是公開支持規律而不極端的身體活動。"},{"en":"A school may espouse daily walking because it is simple and safe for most students.","zh":"學校可能支持每日步行，因為對大多數學生來說簡單又安全。"},{"en":"If health authorities espouse moderate exercise, they encourage habits many people can maintain.","zh":"如果衞生當局支持溫和運動，它們鼓勵許多人能維持的習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes official support for a health recommendation.","zh":"這個短語描述官方支持健康建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"moderate daily exercise","meaning":"溫和日常運動","examples":[{"en":"Moderate daily exercise may not produce major weight loss.","zh":"溫和日常運動可能不會造成大幅減重。"},{"en":"Moderate daily exercise is regular physical activity that is not too intense, such as walking or taking stairs.","zh":"「moderate daily exercise」是規律但不太劇烈的身體活動，例如步行或行樓梯。"},{"en":"A person may do moderate daily exercise by walking to the bus stop and using stairs at work.","zh":"一個人可以透過步行到巴士站和在工作地點行樓梯來做溫和日常運動。"},{"en":"If exercise is moderate, it may improve heart health even if weight changes little.","zh":"如果運動屬於溫和，它可能改善心臟健康，即使體重變化不大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes manageable everyday activity.","zh":"這個短語描述可維持的日常活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"of the evening-walk variety","meaning":"屬於散步一類的","examples":[{"en":"The advice is often of the evening-walk or take-the-stairs variety.","zh":"這項建議通常屬於晚上散步或行樓梯一類。"},{"en":"Of the evening-walk variety means belonging to the simple, light, everyday type of exercise.","zh":"「of the evening-walk variety」意思是屬於簡單、輕量、日常運動那一類。"},{"en":"Advice of the “drink more water” variety is easy to follow but may not solve every health problem.","zh":"「多喝水」一類建議容易跟從，但未必能解決所有健康問題。"},{"en":"If an exercise plan is of this variety, it is gentle rather than intense.","zh":"如果運動計劃屬於這一類，它是溫和而不是劇烈。"},{"en":"The phrase classifies something as a familiar, modest example.","zh":"這個短語把某事歸類為熟悉而溫和的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take the stairs","meaning":"行樓梯","examples":[{"en":"Taking the stairs is a common example of moderate daily exercise.","zh":"行樓梯是溫和日常運動的常見例子。"},{"en":"To take the stairs means to walk up or down stairs instead of using a lift or escalator.","zh":"「take the stairs」意思是步行上落樓梯，而不是使用升降機或扶手電梯。"},{"en":"An office worker may take the stairs to add movement to a busy day.","zh":"辦公室員工可能行樓梯，為忙碌一天增加活動量。"},{"en":"If people take the stairs regularly, they may improve fitness slightly over time.","zh":"如果人們規律地行樓梯，長遠可能略為改善體能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small everyday activity choice.","zh":"這個短語描述日常生活中的小活動選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"budge the needle on the scale","meaning":"令磅上的數字有明顯變化","examples":[{"en":"Moderate exercise may not do much to budge the needle on the scale.","zh":"溫和運動可能不足以令磅上的數字有明顯變化。"},{"en":"To budge the needle on the scale means to make body weight change noticeably.","zh":"「budge the needle on the scale」意思是令體重出現可見變化。"},{"en":"Skipping one biscuit may not budge the needle on the scale by the next morning.","zh":"少吃一塊餅乾未必能在翌日早上令磅上的數字有明顯變化。"},{"en":"If a habit burns only a few calories, weight may change very slowly.","zh":"如果一個習慣只消耗少量卡路里，體重可能變化很慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a visible change in weight measurement.","zh":"這個短語描述體重測量上的可見改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"burn calories","meaning":"消耗卡路里","examples":[{"en":"A 150-pound person burns about 150 calories on a half-hour walk.","zh":"一個150磅的人半小時步行大約消耗150卡路里。"},{"en":"To burn calories means to use energy from food through movement or body processes.","zh":"「burn calories」意思是透過活動或身體過程使用來自食物的能量。"},{"en":"A person burns calories while walking, cleaning, studying, and even sleeping.","zh":"一個人在步行、清潔、學習甚至睡覺時都會消耗卡路里。"},{"en":"If exercise burns fewer calories than expected, weight loss may be slower.","zh":"如果運動消耗的卡路里比預期少，減重可能較慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes energy use.","zh":"這個短語描述能量使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a half-hour walk","meaning":"半小時步行","examples":[{"en":"A half-hour walk burns the equivalent of about two apples.","zh":"半小時步行消耗的熱量大約相當於兩個蘋果。"},{"en":"A half-hour walk is a walk lasting thirty minutes.","zh":"「a half-hour walk」是持續三十分鐘的步行。"},{"en":"A student may take a half-hour walk after dinner to relax before studying.","zh":"學生可能晚飯後半小時步行，在溫習前放鬆。"},{"en":"If a walk lasts only half an hour, it may improve health but not burn many calories.","zh":"如果步行只持續半小時，它可能改善健康，但不會消耗很多卡路里。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a short, manageable exercise activity.","zh":"這個短語描述短而可做到的運動活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the equivalent of","meaning":"相當於","examples":[{"en":"The calories burned are the equivalent of two apples.","zh":"消耗的卡路里相當於兩個蘋果。"},{"en":"The equivalent of something means equal in value, amount, effect, or meaning.","zh":"「the equivalent of」某物，意思是在價值、數量、效果或意思上相等。"},{"en":"One hour of focused tutoring may be the equivalent of several hours of confused self-study.","zh":"一小時專注補習可能相當於數小時混亂自學。"},{"en":"If exercise burns the equivalent of a small snack, eating extra food can cancel the effect.","zh":"如果運動消耗的熱量只相當於一份小食，額外進食可能抵消效果。"},{"en":"The phrase explains one thing by comparing it to another.","zh":"這個短語透過另一事物解釋某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"good for the heart","meaning":"對心臟有益","examples":[{"en":"A short walk is good for the heart.","zh":"短途步行對心臟有益。"},{"en":"Good for the heart means beneficial to heart health and circulation.","zh":"「good for the heart」意思是對心臟健康和血液循環有好處。"},{"en":"Regular walking, enough sleep, and less smoking are good for the heart.","zh":"規律步行、充足睡眠和少吸煙都對心臟有益。"},{"en":"If an activity is good for the heart, it may still not cause large weight loss.","zh":"如果一項活動對心臟有益，它仍未必造成大幅減重。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a health benefit to the cardiovascular system.","zh":"這個短語描述對心血管系統的健康好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"less so for","meaning":"對……則較少","examples":[{"en":"A short walk is good for the heart, but less so for weight loss.","zh":"短途步行對心臟有益，但對減重則較少。"},{"en":"Less so for something means it is less effective, less true, or less useful for that purpose.","zh":"「less so for」某事，意思是對該目的較不有效、較不真確或較不有用。"},{"en":"Flashcards are useful for vocabulary, but less so for learning essay structure.","zh":"單詞卡對詞彙有用，但對學習文章結構則較少。"},{"en":"If walking burns few calories, it may help health more than fat loss.","zh":"如果步行消耗卡路里少，它可能對健康幫助大於對減脂幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase compares usefulness across two purposes.","zh":"這個短語比較對兩種目的的有用程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"radical changes","meaning":"徹底改變","examples":[{"en":"Deirdre Barrett says radical changes are necessary.","zh":"Deirdre Barrett 說徹底改變是必要的。"},{"en":"Radical changes are major changes that go far beyond small adjustments.","zh":"「radical changes」是遠超小修小補的重大改變。"},{"en":"A student who always fails may need radical changes in sleep, study time, and phone use.","zh":"經常不及格的學生可能需要在睡眠、溫習時間和手機使用上作徹底改變。"},{"en":"If small habits do not work, a person may need deeper changes to routine and environment.","zh":"如果小習慣無效，一個人可能需要對日常和環境作更深層改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes large, serious changes.","zh":"這個短語描述巨大而嚴肅的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"take a cue from","meaning":"參考；借鑑","examples":[{"en":"Barrett suggests taking a cue from successful weight-losers.","zh":"Barrett 建議參考成功減重人士。"},{"en":"To take a cue from someone means to learn from their example or follow their useful approach.","zh":"「take a cue from」某人，意思是從其例子學習或跟隨其有用做法。"},{"en":"New students can take a cue from organised classmates who prepare books the night before.","zh":"新生可以參考有條理同學的做法，在前一晚準備書本。"},{"en":"If some people maintain weight loss successfully, others may learn practical habits from them.","zh":"如果有些人成功維持減重，其他人可向他們學習實際習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using another person’s behaviour as guidance.","zh":"這個短語描述以他人行為作指引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"successful weight-losers","meaning":"成功減重人士","examples":[{"en":"The National Weight Control Registry includes successful weight-losers.","zh":"國家體重控制登記處包括成功減重人士。"},{"en":"Successful weight-losers are people who have lost weight and managed to maintain the loss.","zh":"「successful weight-losers」是已減重並成功維持成果的人。"},{"en":"A successful weight-loser may keep regular meal routines and monitor progress honestly.","zh":"成功減重人士可能保持規律用餐並誠實監察進展。"},{"en":"If researchers study successful weight-losers, they may find habits that work in real life.","zh":"如果研究人員研究成功減重人士，可能找到現實中有效的習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on people who both lose weight and keep it off.","zh":"這個短語集中於既減重又保持成果的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a self-selected group of","meaning":"自行選擇參加的一群……","examples":[{"en":"The registry is a self-selected group of successful weight-losers.","zh":"該登記處是一群自行選擇參加的成功減重人士。"},{"en":"A self-selected group is made up of people who choose to join rather than being randomly chosen.","zh":"「a self-selected group」是由自願加入、而非隨機挑選的人組成。"},{"en":"A survey of volunteers is a self-selected group, so it may not represent everyone.","zh":"由義工填寫的調查是一個自行選擇參加的群體，所以未必代表所有人。"},{"en":"If a group is self-selected, researchers must be careful about drawing broad conclusions.","zh":"如果群體是自行選擇參加的，研究人員下廣泛結論時必須小心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how participants entered a study or registry.","zh":"這個短語描述參加者如何進入研究或登記處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"shed an average of","meaning":"平均減掉","examples":[{"en":"Registry members have shed an average of 66 pounds.","zh":"登記處成員平均減掉66磅。"},{"en":"To shed an average of a certain amount means to lose that typical amount, especially of weight.","zh":"「shed an average of」某數量，意思是平均減去該數量，尤其指體重。"},{"en":"Participants in a walking programme may shed an average of three kilograms after six months.","zh":"步行計劃參加者六個月後可能平均減掉三公斤。"},{"en":"If members shed a large average amount, their methods attract research attention.","zh":"如果成員平均減掉大量體重，他們的方法會引起研究關注。"},{"en":"The phrase reports typical weight lost by a group.","zh":"這個短語報告一個群體典型減去的體重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"keep it off","meaning":"維持成果；沒有反彈","examples":[{"en":"Many registry members lost weight and kept it off for years.","zh":"許多登記處成員減了重並多年沒有反彈。"},{"en":"To keep it off means to prevent lost weight from returning.","zh":"「keep it off」意思是防止已減掉的體重回來。"},{"en":"A person may lose weight before a wedding but struggle to keep it off afterward.","zh":"一個人可能在婚禮前減重，但之後難以維持成果。"},{"en":"If habits disappear after dieting, the weight may come back.","zh":"如果節食後習慣消失，體重可能回升。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses long-term maintenance after weight loss.","zh":"這個短語強調減重後的長期維持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"low-carb diets","meaning":"低碳水化合物飲食","examples":[{"en":"Some registry members lost weight using low-carb diets.","zh":"有些登記處成員使用低碳水化合物飲食減重。"},{"en":"Low-carb diets are eating plans that reduce foods high in carbohydrates, such as bread, rice, pasta, and sugar.","zh":"「low-carb diets」是減少高碳水化合物食物的飲食計劃，例如麵包、米飯、意粉和糖。"},{"en":"A person on a low-carb diet may choose eggs and vegetables instead of noodles for breakfast.","zh":"採用低碳水飲食的人早餐可能選雞蛋和蔬菜，而不是麵。"},{"en":"If carbohydrates are reduced, total calorie intake may also fall.","zh":"如果碳水化合物減少，總卡路里攝取也可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one type of weight-loss diet.","zh":"這個短語描述一種減重飲食方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"low-fat diets","meaning":"低脂飲食","examples":[{"en":"Some people lost weight by following low-fat diets.","zh":"有些人透過遵循低脂飲食減重。"},{"en":"Low-fat diets are eating plans that reduce foods high in fat, such as fried food, butter, and fatty meat.","zh":"「low-fat diets」是減少高脂食物的飲食計劃，例如油炸食物、牛油和肥肉。"},{"en":"A person on a low-fat diet may choose grilled fish instead of fried chicken.","zh":"採用低脂飲食的人可能選烤魚，而不是炸雞。"},{"en":"If high-fat foods are reduced, calorie intake may decrease.","zh":"如果高脂食物減少，卡路里攝取可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a diet based on limiting fat.","zh":"這個短語描述以限制脂肪為基礎的飲食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"eliminate refined foods","meaning":"戒掉精製食品","examples":[{"en":"Other successful dieters eliminated refined foods.","zh":"其他成功節食者戒掉精製食品。"},{"en":"To eliminate refined foods means to stop eating highly processed foods such as white bread, sweets, or sugary cereals.","zh":"「eliminate refined foods」意思是停止進食高度加工食物，例如白麵包、糖果或含糖穀物。"},{"en":"A family may eliminate refined foods by replacing biscuits with fruit and nuts.","zh":"家庭可能用水果和果仁代替餅乾，以戒掉精製食品。"},{"en":"If refined foods are removed, people may eat more whole foods and feel fuller.","zh":"如果精製食品被移除，人們可能吃更多原型食物並感到更飽。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cutting out processed foods from the diet.","zh":"這個短語描述從飲食中戒掉加工食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"do it on their own","meaning":"靠自己完成","examples":[{"en":"Some registry members lost weight on their own.","zh":"有些登記處成員靠自己減重成功。"},{"en":"To do it on their own means to achieve something without formal help from others.","zh":"「do it on their own」意思是不靠正式他人幫助而達成某事。"},{"en":"A student may learn basic video editing on their own by practising at home.","zh":"學生可能透過在家練習，靠自己學會基本影片剪接。"},{"en":"If someone loses weight on their own, they may rely on personal planning and discipline.","zh":"如果某人靠自己減重，可能依賴個人規劃和紀律。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses independence.","zh":"這個短語強調獨立完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rely on counselling","meaning":"依靠輔導","examples":[{"en":"Others relied on counselling to lose weight.","zh":"其他人依靠輔導來減重。"},{"en":"To rely on counselling means to depend on professional guidance, conversation, and support.","zh":"「rely on counselling」意思是依靠專業指導、對話和支援。"},{"en":"A student may rely on counselling after bullying affects confidence and sleep.","zh":"學生被欺凌影響信心和睡眠後，可能依靠輔導。"},{"en":"If eating habits are emotional, counselling may help people understand triggers.","zh":"如果飲食習慣與情緒有關，輔導可能幫助人理解誘因。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using guided support rather than handling the problem alone.","zh":"這個短語描述使用指導支援，而不是獨自處理問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"that said","meaning":"話雖如此","examples":[{"en":"That said, not everyone can lose 66 pounds.","zh":"話雖如此，並不是每個人都能減掉66磅。"},{"en":"That said means despite what has just been said, another point must also be considered.","zh":"「that said」意思是儘管剛才那樣說，仍有另一點需要考慮。"},{"en":"The new app is useful; that said, it still cannot replace a good teacher.","zh":"這個新應用程式很有用；話雖如此，它仍不能取代好老師。"},{"en":"If successful cases are impressive, we still need to remember they may not apply to everyone.","zh":"如果成功個案令人印象深刻，我們仍要記得它們未必適用於每個人。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a balancing or limiting point.","zh":"這個短語引入平衡或限制性的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not everyone can","meaning":"不是每個人都能","examples":[{"en":"Not everyone can lose a large amount of weight.","zh":"不是每個人都能減掉大量體重。"},{"en":"Not everyone can means some people are unable to do it, even if others can.","zh":"「not everyone can」意思是有些人做不到，即使其他人做得到。"},{"en":"Not everyone can study well in a noisy café.","zh":"不是每個人都能在嘈雜咖啡店中好好學習。"},{"en":"If bodies respond differently, not everyone can achieve the same result with the same plan.","zh":"如果身體反應不同，不是每個人都能用同一計劃達到同一結果。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds us to avoid unrealistic expectations.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們避免不切實際期望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not everyone needs to","meaning":"不是每個人都需要","examples":[{"en":"Not everyone needs to lose 66 pounds.","zh":"不是每個人都需要減掉66磅。"},{"en":"Not everyone needs to means the action is unnecessary for some people.","zh":"「not everyone needs to」意思是對某些人而言，該行動並非必要。"},{"en":"Not everyone needs to buy a new laptop; some only need better study habits.","zh":"不是每個人都需要買新手提電腦；有些人只需要更好學習習慣。"},{"en":"If health improves after small weight loss, a huge change may not be necessary.","zh":"如果小幅減重後健康改善，巨大改變未必必要。"},{"en":"The phrase separates need from possibility.","zh":"這個短語把需要與可能性區分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the goal should not be","meaning":"目標不應該是","examples":[{"en":"The goal should not be getting thin, but getting healthy.","zh":"目標不應該是變瘦，而是變得健康。"},{"en":"The goal should not be means the main aim ought not to focus on that thing.","zh":"「the goal should not be」意思是主要目標不應集中於該事。"},{"en":"The goal should not be memorising answers, but understanding how to think.","zh":"目標不應該是背答案，而是理解如何思考。"},{"en":"If the goal is only appearance, people may ignore long-term health.","zh":"如果目標只是外表，人們可能忽略長遠健康。"},{"en":"The phrase corrects a mistaken target.","zh":"這個短語修正錯誤目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"getting thin","meaning":"變瘦","examples":[{"en":"The goal should not simply be getting thin.","zh":"目標不應只是變瘦。"},{"en":"Getting thin means becoming slimmer or weighing less, often mainly in appearance.","zh":"「getting thin」意思是變得較瘦或體重較低，通常主要指外表。"},{"en":"A person may focus on getting thin but still eat poorly and feel weak.","zh":"一個人可能集中於變瘦，但仍然飲食不佳並感到虛弱。"},{"en":"If getting thin becomes the only goal, health and confidence may suffer.","zh":"如果變瘦成為唯一目標，健康和信心可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes appearance-focused weight reduction.","zh":"這個短語描述以外表為重點的體重下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"getting healthy","meaning":"變得健康","examples":[{"en":"The real goal should be getting healthy.","zh":"真正目標應該是變得健康。"},{"en":"Getting healthy means improving physical and mental health, not just changing appearance.","zh":"「getting healthy」意思是改善身體和心理健康，而不只是改變外表。"},{"en":"A person may get healthy by sleeping better, moving more, and eating balanced meals.","zh":"一個人可以透過睡得更好、多活動和吃均衡餐來變得健康。"},{"en":"If someone becomes healthier, blood pressure and energy may improve even before major weight loss.","zh":"如果某人變得更健康，即使尚未大幅減重，血壓和精力也可能改善。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on health outcomes rather than looks.","zh":"這個短語集中於健康結果，而不是外貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"whittle your weight down","meaning":"逐步減低體重","examples":[{"en":"It may be enough to whittle your weight down to the low end of your set range.","zh":"逐步把體重減到設定範圍的低端可能已經足夠。"},{"en":"To whittle your weight down means to reduce weight gradually, bit by bit.","zh":"「whittle your weight down」意思是一點一點逐步減低體重。"},{"en":"A student may whittle a large assignment down by writing one paragraph each day.","zh":"學生可能每天寫一段，逐步完成大型作業。"},{"en":"If weight is reduced slowly, the change may feel more manageable.","zh":"如果體重慢慢下降，改變可能感覺更可管理。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests gradual reduction rather than sudden loss.","zh":"這個短語暗示逐步減少，而不是突然下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the low end of","meaning":"……的低端","examples":[{"en":"Friedman suggests aiming for the low end of your set range.","zh":"Friedman 建議以你的設定體重範圍低端為目標。"},{"en":"The low end of a range means the lower part or minimum side of that range.","zh":"「the low end of」某範圍，意思是該範圍的較低部分或最低一邊。"},{"en":"If a course fee is between $300 and $500, $300 is at the low end of the range.","zh":"如果課程收費介乎300至500元，300元就是該範圍的低端。"},{"en":"If a person aims for the low end of a healthy range, the goal may be realistic but still beneficial.","zh":"如果一個人以健康範圍的低端為目標，目標可能既實際又有益。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the lower boundary of a range.","zh":"這個短語描述範圍的較低界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"your set range","meaning":"你的設定體重範圍","examples":[{"en":"Your body may have a genetically influenced set range for weight.","zh":"你的身體可能有一個受基因影響的設定體重範圍。"},{"en":"Your set range means the weight range your body tends to maintain naturally.","zh":"「your set range」意思是你的身體自然傾向維持的體重範圍。"},{"en":"Some people find their weight stays within a narrow range even when routines change slightly.","zh":"有些人發現即使日常略有改變，體重仍停留在狹窄範圍內。"},{"en":"If a body defends a set range, extreme weight loss may be difficult to maintain.","zh":"如果身體守住某設定範圍，極端減重可能難以維持。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a biologically influenced weight zone.","zh":"這個短語暗示受生物因素影響的體重區間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"vastly decrease your risk of","meaning":"大幅降低……的風險","examples":[{"en":"Losing even 10 pounds can vastly decrease your risk of disease.","zh":"即使只減掉10磅，也可以大幅降低你患病的風險。"},{"en":"To vastly decrease your risk of something means to greatly lower the chance that it will happen.","zh":"「vastly decrease your risk of」某事，意思是大大降低它發生的機會。"},{"en":"Wearing a seat belt can vastly decrease your risk of serious injury in a crash.","zh":"繫安全帶可以大幅降低車禍中嚴重受傷的風險。"},{"en":"If modest weight loss reduces disease risk, health gains can matter more than appearance.","zh":"如果適度減重能降低疾病風險，健康得益可以比外表更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large reduction in danger.","zh":"這個短語描述危險大幅下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"diabetes","meaning":"糖尿病","examples":[{"en":"Losing weight can reduce the risk of diabetes.","zh":"減重可以降低糖尿病風險。"},{"en":"Diabetes is a disease in which the body has difficulty controlling blood sugar.","zh":"「diabetes」是一種身體難以控制血糖的疾病。"},{"en":"A person with diabetes may need to monitor diet, exercise, medication, and blood sugar levels.","zh":"糖尿病患者可能需要監察飲食、運動、藥物和血糖水平。"},{"en":"If obesity increases diabetes risk, weight management may improve long-term health.","zh":"如果肥胖增加糖尿病風險，體重管理可能改善長遠健康。"},{"en":"The word refers to a serious metabolic disease.","zh":"這個詞指嚴重代謝疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"heart disease","meaning":"心臟病","examples":[{"en":"Weight loss can lower the risk of heart disease.","zh":"減重可以降低心臟病風險。"},{"en":"Heart disease refers to medical conditions that affect the heart and blood vessels.","zh":"「heart disease」指影響心臟和血管的醫學狀況。"},{"en":"High blood pressure, smoking, and poor diet can increase the risk of heart disease.","zh":"高血壓、吸煙和不良飲食都可以增加心臟病風險。"},{"en":"If weight loss improves blood pressure, the heart may face less strain.","zh":"如果減重改善血壓，心臟可能承受較少壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a major category of cardiovascular illness.","zh":"這個短語指一大類心血管疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"high blood pressure","meaning":"高血壓","examples":[{"en":"Losing weight can reduce the risk of high blood pressure.","zh":"減重可以降低高血壓風險。"},{"en":"High blood pressure means the force of blood against artery walls is too high over time.","zh":"「high blood pressure」意思是血液長期對動脈壁造成過高壓力。"},{"en":"A nurse may check high blood pressure during a routine health screening.","zh":"護士可能在例行健康檢查中檢查高血壓。"},{"en":"If blood pressure stays high, the heart and blood vessels may be damaged.","zh":"如果血壓持續偏高，心臟和血管可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a common but serious health risk.","zh":"這個短語指常見但嚴重的健康風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the point is to","meaning":"重點是","examples":[{"en":"The point is to not give up because your body does not look perfect.","zh":"重點是不要因為身體看起來不完美就放棄。"},{"en":"The point is to do something means the main purpose or lesson is that action.","zh":"「the point is to」做某事，意思是主要目的或教訓就是該行動。"},{"en":"The point is to learn from mistakes, not to feel ashamed of them.","zh":"重點是從錯誤中學習，而不是為錯誤感到羞恥。"},{"en":"If the point is health, people should not quit just because they do not look like models.","zh":"如果重點是健康，人們不應只因不像模特兒就放棄。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main message.","zh":"這個短語指出主要訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"give up","meaning":"放棄","examples":[{"en":"People should not give up just because they are not thin.","zh":"人們不應只因自己不瘦就放棄。"},{"en":"To give up means to stop trying or abandon an effort.","zh":"「give up」意思是停止嘗試或放棄努力。"},{"en":"A student should not give up on English after one bad speaking test.","zh":"學生不應因一次口試差就放棄英語。"},{"en":"If progress is slow, giving up may stop a person from receiving long-term benefits.","zh":"如果進展緩慢，放棄可能令一個人失去長遠得益。"},{"en":"The phrase describes quitting before the goal is fully reached.","zh":"這個短語描述在完全達標前停止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a swimsuit model","meaning":"泳裝模特兒","examples":[{"en":"The point is not to give up just because you do not look like a swimsuit model.","zh":"重點不是只因你不像泳裝模特兒就放棄。"},{"en":"A swimsuit model is a model photographed or shown wearing swimwear, often representing an unrealistic beauty ideal.","zh":"「a swimsuit model」是穿着泳裝拍攝或展示的模特兒，常代表不切實際的美貌標準。"},{"en":"Many ordinary people cannot and do not need to look like swimsuit models to be healthy.","zh":"許多普通人不能、也不需要看起來像泳裝模特兒才算健康。"},{"en":"If health goals are compared with model images, people may feel discouraged unfairly.","zh":"如果健康目標被拿來與模特兒形象比較，人們可能不公平地感到氣餒。"},{"en":"The phrase is used here to criticise appearance-based standards.","zh":"這個短語在這裡用來批評以外表為本的標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the negotiation between","meaning":"……之間的相互作用","examples":[{"en":"The negotiation between your genes and the environment begins very early.","zh":"你的基因與環境之間的相互作用很早便開始。"},{"en":"The negotiation between two forces means their ongoing interaction or influence on each other.","zh":"「the negotiation between」兩種力量，意思是它們持續互動或互相影響。"},{"en":"A student’s success may depend on the negotiation between natural ability and daily practice.","zh":"學生成功可能取決於天生能力與日常練習之間的相互作用。"},{"en":"If genes and environment interact, neither side alone explains the final result.","zh":"如果基因和環境互動，任何一方都不能單獨解釋最終結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a back-and-forth influence, not a formal meeting.","zh":"這個短語描述來回影響，而不是正式談判會議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"genes and the environment","meaning":"基因與環境","examples":[{"en":"Genes and the environment interact to influence weight.","zh":"基因與環境互相作用以影響體重。"},{"en":"Genes and the environment refer to inherited biology and surrounding conditions such as food, family, stress, and activity.","zh":"「genes and the environment」指遺傳生理因素和周遭條件，例如食物、家庭、壓力和活動量。"},{"en":"A child’s height may be shaped by genes and the environment, including nutrition and illness.","zh":"孩子的身高可能受基因與環境塑造，包括營養和疾病。"},{"en":"If both genes and environment matter, health advice must consider more than personal choice.","zh":"如果基因與環境都重要，健康建議就必須考慮個人選擇以外的因素。"},{"en":"The phrase combines internal and external influences.","zh":"這個短語結合內在和外在影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"begin on day one","meaning":"從一開始便開始","examples":[{"en":"The negotiation between genes and the environment begins on day one.","zh":"基因與環境之間的相互作用從一開始便開始。"},{"en":"Begin on day one means start from the very beginning.","zh":"「begin on day one」意思是從最開始便開始。"},{"en":"Good classroom habits should begin on day one of the school year.","zh":"良好課室習慣應在學年第一天就開始。"},{"en":"If weight-related influences begin on day one, early life conditions matter greatly.","zh":"如果體重相關影響從一開始便開始，早期生命條件就非常重要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that something starts immediately.","zh":"這個短語強調某事立即開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"optimal weight","meaning":"最理想體重","examples":[{"en":"Your optimal weight may be shaped before birth.","zh":"你的最理想體重可能在出生前已被塑造。"},{"en":"Optimal weight means the weight range that is healthiest or most suitable for a person’s body.","zh":"「optimal weight」意思是對某人身體最健康或最合適的體重範圍。"},{"en":"An athlete’s optimal weight may differ from that of an office worker of the same height.","zh":"運動員的最理想體重可能與同身高辦公室員工不同。"},{"en":"If optimal weight is about health, it should not be confused with looking very thin.","zh":"如果最理想體重關乎健康，就不應與看起來很瘦混淆。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a suitable health-based weight.","zh":"這個短語描述以健康為基礎的合適體重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"written by your genes","meaning":"由你的基因寫定","examples":[{"en":"Your optimal weight is partly written by your genes.","zh":"你的最理想體重部分由你的基因寫定。"},{"en":"Written by your genes means strongly influenced by inherited biological information.","zh":"「written by your genes」意思是強烈受遺傳生物資訊影響。"},{"en":"Eye colour is largely written by your genes.","zh":"眼睛顏色很大程度上由你的基因寫定。"},{"en":"If body weight is partly written by genes, people may have different natural ranges.","zh":"如果體重部分由基因寫定，人們可能有不同自然範圍。"},{"en":"The phrase is figurative and means genetically influenced.","zh":"這個短語是比喻用法，意思是受基因影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get edited early on","meaning":"在早期被修正","examples":[{"en":"Your weight range appears to get edited early on.","zh":"你的體重範圍似乎在早期被修正。"},{"en":"To get edited early on means to be adjusted or shaped at an early stage.","zh":"「get edited early on」意思是在早期階段被調整或塑造。"},{"en":"A student’s pronunciation may get edited early on if a teacher corrects mistakes gently.","zh":"如果老師溫和糾正錯誤，學生的發音可能在早期被修正。"},{"en":"If weight range is edited before birth, later biology may carry that early influence.","zh":"如果體重範圍在出生前被修正，日後生理可能帶着那種早期影響。"},{"en":"The phrase uses “edited” figuratively to mean changed or adjusted.","zh":"這個短語把 “edited” 作比喻，意思是被改變或調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"before birth","meaning":"出生前","examples":[{"en":"Some conditions before birth may influence later weight.","zh":"出生前某些狀況可能影響日後體重。"},{"en":"Before birth means during the period before a baby is born.","zh":"「before birth」意思是在嬰兒出生之前的期間。"},{"en":"A baby’s development before birth can be affected by nutrition and maternal health.","zh":"嬰兒出生前的發展可能受營養和母體健康影響。"},{"en":"If risk factors begin before birth, prevention may need to start during pregnancy.","zh":"如果風險因素在出生前開始，預防可能需要從懷孕期間開始。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the prenatal period.","zh":"這個短語指產前時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"inside the womb","meaning":"在子宮內","examples":[{"en":"Weight-related conditions may begin inside the womb.","zh":"與體重相關的狀況可能在子宮內開始。"},{"en":"Inside the womb means within the mother’s uterus before birth.","zh":"「inside the womb」意思是在出生前母親的子宮內。"},{"en":"A baby receives oxygen and nutrients while developing inside the womb.","zh":"嬰兒在子宮內發育時接收氧氣和營養。"},{"en":"If conditions inside the womb affect metabolism, early development may shape later health.","zh":"如果子宮內狀況影響代謝，早期發展可能塑造日後健康。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the baby’s environment before birth.","zh":"這個短語描述嬰兒出生前的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"blood-sugar levels","meaning":"血糖水平","examples":[{"en":"A pregnant woman’s blood-sugar levels may affect her child’s weight risk.","zh":"孕婦的血糖水平可能影響孩子的體重風險。"},{"en":"Blood-sugar levels are the amount of glucose present in the blood.","zh":"「blood-sugar levels」是血液中葡萄糖的含量。"},{"en":"People with diabetes often check blood-sugar levels before or after meals.","zh":"糖尿病患者常在飯前或飯後檢查血糖水平。"},{"en":"If blood sugar stays high during pregnancy, it may affect the baby’s development.","zh":"如果懷孕期間血糖持續偏高，可能影響嬰兒發展。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a measurable health indicator.","zh":"這個短語指可量度的健康指標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"while pregnant","meaning":"懷孕期間","examples":[{"en":"High blood sugar while pregnant may increase a child’s obesity risk.","zh":"懷孕期間血糖高可能增加孩子的肥胖風險。"},{"en":"While pregnant means during the time when a woman is carrying a baby before birth.","zh":"「while pregnant」意思是女性在出生前懷着嬰兒的期間。"},{"en":"A woman may need extra medical check-ups while pregnant.","zh":"女性懷孕期間可能需要額外身體檢查。"},{"en":"If health problems appear while pregnant, they can affect both mother and child.","zh":"如果健康問題在懷孕期間出現，可能同時影響母親和孩子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the pregnancy period.","zh":"這個短語描述懷孕時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"more likely to be","meaning":"更有可能","examples":[{"en":"Children may be more likely to be overweight if their mothers have high blood sugar.","zh":"如果母親血糖高，孩子更有可能超重。"},{"en":"More likely to be means having a higher chance of being in a certain condition.","zh":"「more likely to be」意思是處於某狀況的機會較高。"},{"en":"Students who sleep too little are more likely to be tired in class.","zh":"睡眠太少的學生更有可能在課堂上疲倦。"},{"en":"If a risk factor is present, a result may become more probable but not guaranteed.","zh":"如果存在風險因素，某結果可能變得更有可能，但並非必然。"},{"en":"The phrase describes increased probability.","zh":"這個短語描述可能性增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"overweight or obese","meaning":"超重或肥胖","examples":[{"en":"Children of mothers with high blood sugar are more likely to be overweight or obese.","zh":"母親血糖高的孩子更有可能超重或肥胖。"},{"en":"Overweight or obese means having a body weight or body fat level above the healthy range.","zh":"「overweight or obese」意思是體重或身體脂肪水平高於健康範圍。"},{"en":"A doctor may use height, weight, and health markers to assess whether a person is overweight or obese.","zh":"醫生可能用身高、體重和健康指標評估一個人是否超重或肥胖。"},{"en":"If a child becomes overweight or obese, early lifestyle support may help reduce future risk.","zh":"如果孩子變得超重或肥胖，早期生活方式支援可能幫助降低未來風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weight categories linked to health concern.","zh":"這個短語描述與健康關注相關的體重類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"according to a study of","meaning":"根據一項關於……的研究","examples":[{"en":"According to a study of almost 10,000 mother-child pairs, maternal health may affect a child’s weight.","zh":"根據一項關於近10,000對母子配對的研究，母體健康可能影響孩子體重。"},{"en":"According to a study of something means based on research examining that group or topic.","zh":"「according to a study of」某事，意思是根據研究該群體或主題所得。"},{"en":"According to a study of teenagers, sleep affects concentration and mood.","zh":"根據一項關於青少年的研究，睡眠會影響專注力和心情。"},{"en":"If a claim is based on a large study, it may seem more reliable than personal opinion.","zh":"如果主張基於大型研究，它可能比個人意見更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces research evidence.","zh":"這個短語引入研究證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mother-child pairs","meaning":"母子配對","examples":[{"en":"The study examined almost 10,000 mother-child pairs.","zh":"研究檢視了近10,000對母子配對。"},{"en":"Mother-child pairs are matched sets consisting of a mother and her child.","zh":"「mother-child pairs」是由一位母親和其孩子組成的配對組合。"},{"en":"A health study may follow mother-child pairs to see how pregnancy affects later development.","zh":"健康研究可能追蹤母子配對，以觀察懷孕如何影響日後發展。"},{"en":"If many mother-child pairs are studied, researchers can look for family patterns.","zh":"如果研究許多母子配對，研究人員可以尋找家庭模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes paired participants in research.","zh":"這個短語描述研究中的配對參加者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"maternal diabetes","meaning":"母體糖尿病","examples":[{"en":"Maternal diabetes may influence a child’s obesity risk.","zh":"母體糖尿病可能影響孩子的肥胖風險。"},{"en":"Maternal diabetes means diabetes in the mother, especially during or before pregnancy.","zh":"「maternal diabetes」意思是母親患有糖尿病，尤其是在懷孕期間或之前。"},{"en":"Doctors may monitor maternal diabetes carefully to protect both mother and baby.","zh":"醫生可能仔細監察母體糖尿病，以保護母親和嬰兒。"},{"en":"If maternal diabetes affects the womb environment, the child’s metabolism may be influenced.","zh":"如果母體糖尿病影響子宮環境，孩子的新陳代謝可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a mother’s health with a child’s later risk.","zh":"這個短語把母親健康與孩子日後風險連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"influence obesity risk","meaning":"影響肥胖風險","examples":[{"en":"Maternal diabetes may influence a child’s obesity risk.","zh":"母體糖尿病可能影響孩子的肥胖風險。"},{"en":"To influence obesity risk means to change the chance that someone will become obese.","zh":"「influence obesity risk」意思是改變某人成為肥胖的機會。"},{"en":"Family diet, sleep, stress, and activity can influence obesity risk over time.","zh":"家庭飲食、睡眠、壓力和活動量都可以隨時間影響肥胖風險。"},{"en":"If early biological conditions influence obesity risk, prevention may need to begin early.","zh":"如果早期生物狀況影響肥胖風險，預防可能需要早早開始。"},{"en":"The phrase describes factors that affect future likelihood of obesity.","zh":"這個短語描述影響未來肥胖可能性的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"through a process called","meaning":"透過一個稱為……的過程","examples":[{"en":"This may happen through a process called metabolic imprinting.","zh":"這可能透過一個稱為代謝印記的過程發生。"},{"en":"Through a process called something means by means of a mechanism with that name.","zh":"「through a process called」某事，意思是透過一個具有該名稱的機制。"},{"en":"Plants make food through a process called photosynthesis.","zh":"植物透過一個稱為光合作用的過程製造食物。"},{"en":"If scientists name a process, they can discuss how it works more precisely.","zh":"如果科學家為過程命名，就能更精確討論其運作。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the mechanism behind a result.","zh":"這個短語引入結果背後的機制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"metabolic imprinting","meaning":"代謝印記","examples":[{"en":"Metabolic imprinting may help explain how maternal diabetes affects children.","zh":"代謝印記可能幫助解釋母體糖尿病如何影響孩子。"},{"en":"Metabolic imprinting is an early biological influence that may shape later metabolism and weight risk.","zh":"「metabolic imprinting」是一種早期生物影響，可能塑造日後新陳代謝和體重風險。"},{"en":"A baby’s body may learn certain energy patterns before birth through metabolic imprinting.","zh":"嬰兒身體可能透過代謝印記在出生前學到某些能量模式。"},{"en":"If metabolic imprinting occurs, early conditions can leave long-term effects.","zh":"如果出現代謝印記，早期狀況可以留下長遠影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to lasting metabolic influence from early development.","zh":"這個短語指早期發展帶來的持久代謝影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"endocrinologist","meaning":"內分泌學家","examples":[{"en":"Teresa Hillier is an endocrinologist who studies obesity risk.","zh":"Teresa Hillier 是研究肥胖風險的內分泌學家。"},{"en":"An endocrinologist is a doctor who specialises in hormones and related body systems.","zh":"「endocrinologist」是專門研究荷爾蒙和相關身體系統的醫生。"},{"en":"An endocrinologist may treat diabetes, thyroid problems, or hormone disorders.","zh":"內分泌學家可能治療糖尿病、甲狀腺問題或荷爾蒙失調。"},{"en":"If hormones affect weight, an endocrinologist can help explain the medical side.","zh":"如果荷爾蒙影響體重，內分泌學家可以幫助解釋醫學層面。"},{"en":"The word names a hormone specialist.","zh":"這個詞指荷爾蒙專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lead author","meaning":"主要作者","examples":[{"en":"Teresa Hillier was the study’s lead author.","zh":"Teresa Hillier 是該研究的主要作者。"},{"en":"The lead author is the main researcher or writer responsible for a study or paper.","zh":"「lead author」是研究或論文中主要負責的研究人員或撰寫者。"},{"en":"In a group report, the lead author may organise evidence and write the final version.","zh":"在小組報告中，主要作者可能整理證據並撰寫最終版本。"},{"en":"If a scientist is the lead author, they usually play a central role in the research.","zh":"如果科學家是主要作者，他們通常在研究中發揮核心作用。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main named contributor.","zh":"這個短語指出主要具名貢獻者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the implication is clear","meaning":"其含義很清楚","examples":[{"en":"The implication is clear: weight may be established very early.","zh":"其含義很清楚：體重可能在很早期已確立。"},{"en":"The implication is clear means the meaning or conclusion suggested by the evidence is easy to see.","zh":"「the implication is clear」意思是證據所暗示的意思或結論很容易看出。"},{"en":"If students sleep less and perform worse, the implication is clear: rest matters.","zh":"如果學生睡得較少而表現較差，其含義很清楚：休息很重要。"},{"en":"When evidence points strongly in one direction, the hidden message becomes obvious.","zh":"當證據強烈指向一個方向，隱含訊息就變得明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an important conclusion drawn from evidence.","zh":"這個短語引入由證據得出的重要結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be established very early","meaning":"在很早期已確立","examples":[{"en":"Weight may be established very early in life.","zh":"體重可能在人生很早期已確立。"},{"en":"To be established very early means to be set or shaped near the beginning of development.","zh":"「be established very early」意思是在發展初期已被設定或塑造。"},{"en":"Reading habits can be established very early if parents read with children every night.","zh":"如果父母每晚與孩子閱讀，閱讀習慣可以在很早期已確立。"},{"en":"If weight patterns are established early, later change may require more effort.","zh":"如果體重模式早期已確立，日後改變可能需要更多努力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes early formation of a pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述模式早期形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be passed from mother to child","meaning":"由母親傳給孩子","examples":[{"en":"Obesity is often passed from mother to child.","zh":"肥胖常由母親傳給孩子。"},{"en":"To be passed from mother to child means to be transmitted or influenced across generations through biology, environment, or habits.","zh":"「be passed from mother to child」意思是透過生理、環境或習慣跨代傳遞或影響。"},{"en":"Some family traditions are passed from mother to child through cooking and storytelling.","zh":"有些家庭傳統透過煮食和講故事由母親傳給孩子。"},{"en":"If health risks are passed from mother to child, prevention may involve the whole family.","zh":"如果健康風險由母親傳給孩子，預防可能涉及整個家庭。"},{"en":"The phrase describes transfer across generations.","zh":"這個短語描述跨代傳遞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"numerous studies","meaning":"大量研究","examples":[{"en":"Numerous studies have linked a mother’s obesity with a child’s weight gain.","zh":"大量研究把母親肥胖與孩子體重增加連繫起來。"},{"en":"Numerous studies means many research studies.","zh":"「numerous studies」意思是許多研究。"},{"en":"Numerous studies show that sleep affects learning and memory.","zh":"大量研究顯示睡眠會影響學習和記憶。"},{"en":"If numerous studies reach similar conclusions, the evidence becomes harder to ignore.","zh":"如果大量研究得出相似結論，證據就更難被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises a large body of research.","zh":"這個短語強調大量研究證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in both animals and humans","meaning":"在動物和人類身上","examples":[{"en":"Studies in both animals and humans show a link between maternal obesity and child weight gain.","zh":"在動物和人類身上的研究都顯示母體肥胖與孩子體重增加有關。"},{"en":"In both animals and humans means the finding appears in animal research and human research.","zh":"「in both animals and humans」意思是該發現同時出現在動物研究和人類研究中。"},{"en":"A medicine may be tested in both animals and humans before doctors fully understand its effects.","zh":"藥物可能在動物和人類身上測試後，醫生才全面理解其效果。"},{"en":"If a pattern appears in both animals and humans, scientists may take it more seriously.","zh":"如果模式同時出現在動物和人類身上，科學家可能更重視它。"},{"en":"The phrase compares evidence across species.","zh":"這個短語比較跨物種證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"directly increase","meaning":"直接增加","examples":[{"en":"A mother’s obesity can directly increase her child’s risk for weight gain.","zh":"母親肥胖可以直接增加孩子體重增加的風險。"},{"en":"To directly increase something means to raise it in a clear and immediate way, not through a distant link.","zh":"「directly increase」某事，意思是以清楚而直接的方式提高它，而不是透過遙遠關聯。"},{"en":"Adding more sugary drinks can directly increase a child’s daily calorie intake.","zh":"增加含糖飲品可以直接增加孩子每日卡路里攝取。"},{"en":"If one factor directly increases risk, reducing that factor may help prevention.","zh":"如果某因素直接增加風險，減少該因素可能有助預防。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong causal effect.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈因果影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"risk for weight gain","meaning":"體重增加的風險","examples":[{"en":"A child may have a higher risk for weight gain if the mother is obese.","zh":"如果母親肥胖，孩子體重增加的風險可能較高。"},{"en":"Risk for weight gain means the chance that a person will gain weight in the future.","zh":"「risk for weight gain」意思是某人日後增加體重的機會。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep, stress, and high-calorie snacks can increase risk for weight gain.","zh":"睡眠不足、壓力和高熱量小食都可以增加體重增加的風險。"},{"en":"If risk is identified early, families may change habits before problems become serious.","zh":"如果風險早早被識別，家庭可以在問題嚴重前改變習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes future likelihood, not guaranteed weight gain.","zh":"這個短語描述未來可能性，而不是保證會增重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"mothers-to-be","meaning":"準媽媽","examples":[{"en":"The advice for mothers-to-be is to get fit before pregnancy.","zh":"給準媽媽的建議是在懷孕前改善體能。"},{"en":"Mothers-to-be are women who are pregnant or planning to become mothers soon.","zh":"「mothers-to-be」是正在懷孕或計劃很快成為母親的女性。"},{"en":"Hospitals may offer nutrition classes for mothers-to-be.","zh":"醫院可能為準媽媽提供營養課程。"},{"en":"If mothers-to-be improve health before birth, children may benefit later.","zh":"如果準媽媽在孩子出生前改善健康，孩子日後可能受益。"},{"en":"The phrase is a gentle way to refer to future mothers.","zh":"這個短語是指未來母親的溫和說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"get fit","meaning":"改善體能；保持健康體態","examples":[{"en":"Mothers-to-be should try to get fit before pregnancy.","zh":"準媽媽應嘗試在懷孕前改善體能。"},{"en":"To get fit means to improve physical health, strength, stamina, and general condition.","zh":"「get fit」意思是改善身體健康、力量、耐力和整體狀態。"},{"en":"A worker may get fit by walking daily and doing simple strength exercises.","zh":"工人可以透過每日步行和做簡單力量訓練改善體能。"},{"en":"If someone gets fit before pregnancy, health risks may decrease.","zh":"如果某人在懷孕前改善體能，健康風險可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on improving fitness, not simply becoming thin.","zh":"這個短語集中於改善體能，而不只是變瘦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"get pregnant","meaning":"懷孕","examples":[{"en":"Women are advised to get fit before they get pregnant.","zh":"女性被建議在懷孕前改善體能。"},{"en":"To get pregnant means to become pregnant and begin carrying a developing baby.","zh":"「get pregnant」意思是開始懷孕並孕育發育中的嬰兒。"},{"en":"A couple may speak to a doctor before trying to get pregnant.","zh":"夫婦可能在嘗試懷孕前先諮詢醫生。"},{"en":"If a woman improves health before she gets pregnant, pregnancy may be safer.","zh":"如果女性在懷孕前改善健康，懷孕過程可能更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the start of pregnancy.","zh":"這個短語描述懷孕開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reduce your risk of","meaning":"降低……的風險","examples":[{"en":"Getting fit can reduce your risk of complications during pregnancy.","zh":"改善體能可以降低懷孕期間併發症的風險。"},{"en":"To reduce your risk of something means to lower the chance that it will happen.","zh":"「reduce your risk of」某事，意思是降低它發生的機會。"},{"en":"Wearing a helmet can reduce your risk of head injury while cycling.","zh":"踩單車時戴頭盔可以降低頭部受傷風險。"},{"en":"If fitness improves, some pregnancy-related health risks may become lower.","zh":"如果體能改善，某些懷孕相關健康風險可能降低。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lowering danger or probability.","zh":"這個短語描述降低危險或可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"complications during pregnancy","meaning":"懷孕期間的併發症","examples":[{"en":"Fitness may reduce complications during pregnancy.","zh":"體能良好可能減少懷孕期間的併發症。"},{"en":"Complications during pregnancy are health problems that arise while a woman is pregnant.","zh":"「complications during pregnancy」是在女性懷孕期間出現的健康問題。"},{"en":"Doctors monitor blood pressure and blood sugar to prevent complications during pregnancy.","zh":"醫生會監測血壓和血糖，以預防懷孕期間的併發症。"},{"en":"If complications occur, both mother and baby may need extra care.","zh":"如果出現併發症，母親和嬰兒可能都需要額外照顧。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to pregnancy-related medical problems.","zh":"這個短語指與懷孕相關的醫療問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"increase your chances of","meaning":"增加……的機會","examples":[{"en":"Getting fit can increase your chances of having a normal-weight child.","zh":"改善體能可以增加你生下正常體重孩子的機會。"},{"en":"To increase your chances of something means to make that result more likely.","zh":"「increase your chances of」某事，意思是令該結果更有可能發生。"},{"en":"Practising speaking every day can increase your chances of doing well in an oral exam.","zh":"每日練習說話可以增加你口試表現好的機會。"},{"en":"If mothers improve health before pregnancy, the chance of a healthier outcome may rise.","zh":"如果母親在懷孕前改善健康，較健康結果的機會可能上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improving probability.","zh":"這個短語描述提高可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"normal-weight child","meaning":"正常體重的孩子","examples":[{"en":"Healthy mothers may have a better chance of having a normal-weight child.","zh":"健康母親可能有較大機會生下正常體重的孩子。"},{"en":"A normal-weight child is a child whose weight falls within a healthy range for age and size.","zh":"「normal-weight child」是體重符合其年齡和身形健康範圍的孩子。"},{"en":"Doctors check children’s growth charts to see whether weight is developing normally.","zh":"醫生會查看兒童生長圖表，以了解體重是否正常發展。"},{"en":"If a child is normal-weight, disease risk may be lower, though health still depends on many factors.","zh":"如果孩子體重正常，疾病風險可能較低，但健康仍取決於許多因素。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a healthy weight category for children.","zh":"這個短語描述兒童的健康體重類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the $64,000 question","meaning":"關鍵難題；最重要的問題","examples":[{"en":"The $64,000 question is which diets actually work.","zh":"關鍵難題是哪些飲食方法真正有效。"},{"en":"The $64,000 question means the most important or difficult question.","zh":"「the $64,000 question」意思是最重要或最難回答的問題。"},{"en":"For students, the $64,000 question before exams is how to revise effectively.","zh":"對學生而言，考試前最重要的問題是如何有效溫習。"},{"en":"If many diets exist, the key question is which one works for which person.","zh":"如果有許多飲食方法，關鍵問題就是哪種方法適合哪類人。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the central problem everyone wants answered.","zh":"這個短語突出人人都想得到答案的核心問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"which diets work","meaning":"哪些飲食方法有效","examples":[{"en":"Researchers continue to ask which diets work best.","zh":"研究人員繼續追問哪些飲食方法最有效。"},{"en":"Which diets work means which eating plans actually produce the desired results.","zh":"「which diets work」意思是哪些飲食計劃真正產生期望結果。"},{"en":"A doctor may ask which diets work for patients with diabetes and high blood pressure.","zh":"醫生可能詢問哪些飲食方法對糖尿病和高血壓患者有效。"},{"en":"If different bodies respond differently, no single diet may work for everyone.","zh":"如果不同身體反應不同，可能沒有一種飲食方法適合所有人。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on effectiveness, not popularity.","zh":"這個短語集中於效果，而不是受歡迎程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a better way to","meaning":"更好的……方法","examples":[{"en":"The study asks whether there is a better way to diet.","zh":"該研究詢問是否有更好的節食方法。"},{"en":"A better way to do something means a more effective, safer, or more suitable method.","zh":"「a better way to」做某事，意思是更有效、更安全或更合適的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may look for a better way to explain grammar to weaker students.","zh":"老師可能尋找更好的方法向較弱學生解釋文法。"},{"en":"If the old method fails, researchers search for a better way.","zh":"如果舊方法失敗，研究人員就會尋找更好的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces improvement in method.","zh":"這個短語引入方法上的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"seem to offer an answer","meaning":"似乎提供答案","examples":[{"en":"A study seemed to offer an answer to the diet question.","zh":"一項研究似乎為飲食問題提供答案。"},{"en":"To seem to offer an answer means to appear to provide a possible explanation or solution.","zh":"「seem to offer an answer」意思是看起來提供可能的解釋或解決方案。"},{"en":"A new survey may seem to offer an answer to why students are tired.","zh":"新調查可能似乎為學生為何疲倦提供答案。"},{"en":"If evidence is early or limited, an answer may look promising but still need confirmation.","zh":"如果證據仍早期或有限，答案可能看似有希望，但仍需確認。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a possible, not final, answer.","zh":"這個短語暗示可能答案，而不是最終答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"compare two groups of","meaning":"比較兩組……","examples":[{"en":"The paper compared two groups of adults.","zh":"該論文比較兩組成年人。"},{"en":"To compare two groups of people means to examine similarities and differences between them.","zh":"「compare two groups of」人，意思是檢視兩組之間的相似和差異。"},{"en":"A teacher may compare two groups of students who used different revision methods.","zh":"老師可能比較使用不同溫習方法的兩組學生。"},{"en":"If two groups respond differently, researchers can learn which factor matters.","zh":"如果兩組反應不同，研究人員可以了解哪個因素重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common research method.","zh":"這個短語描述常見研究方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"secrete high levels of","meaning":"分泌高水平的……","examples":[{"en":"Some adults secrete high levels of insulin after eating.","zh":"有些成年人進食後分泌高水平胰島素。"},{"en":"To secrete high levels of something means the body releases a large amount of a substance.","zh":"「secrete high levels of」某物，意思是身體釋放大量某種物質。"},{"en":"The body may secrete high levels of stress hormones before a frightening event.","zh":"在可怕事件前，身體可能分泌高水平壓力荷爾蒙。"},{"en":"If a person secretes high levels of insulin, their body may store energy differently.","zh":"如果一個人分泌高水平胰島素，其身體儲存能量的方式可能不同。"},{"en":"The phrase describes biological release of a substance.","zh":"這個短語描述身體釋放某物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"sweep blood sugar out of","meaning":"將血糖從……帶走","examples":[{"en":"Insulin sweeps blood sugar out of the bloodstream.","zh":"胰島素將血糖從血液循環中帶走。"},{"en":"To sweep blood sugar out of the bloodstream means to move sugar from the blood into cells or storage.","zh":"「sweep blood sugar out of the bloodstream」意思是把糖分從血液移入細胞或儲存處。"},{"en":"After a meal, insulin helps clear sugar from the blood so cells can use it.","zh":"飯後，胰島素幫助清除血液中的糖，讓細胞使用。"},{"en":"If blood sugar is removed quickly, the body may store some of it as fat.","zh":"如果血糖被快速移走，身體可能把其中一部分以脂肪形式儲存。"},{"en":"The phrase uses “sweep” figuratively to describe rapid removal.","zh":"這個短語用 “sweep” 作比喻，描述快速移除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the bloodstream","meaning":"血液循環","examples":[{"en":"Insulin removes blood sugar from the bloodstream.","zh":"胰島素將血糖從血液循環中移走。"},{"en":"The bloodstream is the flow of blood moving through the body’s blood vessels.","zh":"「the bloodstream」是流經身體血管的血液流動系統。"},{"en":"Medicine enters the bloodstream after being absorbed by the body.","zh":"藥物被身體吸收後會進入血液循環。"},{"en":"If sugar stays too high in the bloodstream, health problems can develop.","zh":"如果血糖在血液循環中長期過高，可能出現健康問題。"},{"en":"The word refers to the body’s circulating blood system.","zh":"這個詞指身體循環中的血液系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"promote storage as fat","meaning":"促進以脂肪形式儲存","examples":[{"en":"Insulin promotes the storage of blood sugar as fat.","zh":"胰島素促進血糖以脂肪形式儲存。"},{"en":"To promote storage as fat means to encourage the body to keep extra energy in the form of fat.","zh":"「promote storage as fat」意思是促使身體把額外能量以脂肪形式保存。"},{"en":"If a person regularly consumes more energy than needed, the body may store the surplus as fat.","zh":"如果一個人經常攝取多於所需的能量，身體可能把多餘部分儲存為脂肪。"},{"en":"When insulin is high, some nutrients may be directed toward storage.","zh":"當胰島素偏高時，一些營養可能被導向儲存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how energy can be stored in the body.","zh":"這個短語描述能量如何在身體中被儲存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"within each group","meaning":"在每組之內","examples":[{"en":"Within each group, half the participants followed a low-fat diet.","zh":"在每組之內，一半參加者採用低脂飲食。"},{"en":"Within each group means inside or among the members of each separate group.","zh":"「within each group」意思是在每個獨立組別的成員之中。"},{"en":"Within each class, half the students used flashcards and half used mind maps.","zh":"在每班之內，一半學生使用單詞卡，一半使用思維導圖。"},{"en":"If treatment is divided within each group, researchers can compare effects more carefully.","zh":"如果在每組之內再分配處理方法，研究人員可以更仔細比較效果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes subdivision inside groups.","zh":"這個短語描述組內細分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be put on a diet","meaning":"被安排採用某種飲食","examples":[{"en":"Half of each group was put on a low-fat diet.","zh":"每組一半人被安排採用低脂飲食。"},{"en":"To be put on a diet means to be assigned or instructed to follow a particular eating plan.","zh":"「be put on a diet」意思是被安排或指示遵循某種飲食計劃。"},{"en":"A doctor may put a patient on a low-salt diet to control blood pressure.","zh":"醫生可能安排病人採用低鹽飲食，以控制血壓。"},{"en":"If participants are put on different diets, researchers can compare results.","zh":"如果參加者被安排採用不同飲食，研究人員就能比較結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being given a diet plan to follow.","zh":"這個短語描述被給予飲食計劃並跟從。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a low-glycemic-load diet","meaning":"低升糖負荷飲食","examples":[{"en":"Some participants followed a low-glycemic-load diet.","zh":"有些參加者採用低升糖負荷飲食。"},{"en":"A low-glycemic-load diet is an eating plan that limits foods causing large rises in blood sugar.","zh":"「a low-glycemic-load diet」是限制會令血糖大幅上升食物的飲食計劃。"},{"en":"A person on this diet may choose beans, vegetables, and whole grains instead of sugary cereal.","zh":"採用這種飲食的人可能選豆類、蔬菜和全穀物，而不是含糖早餐穀物。"},{"en":"If blood sugar rises more slowly, insulin responses may also change.","zh":"如果血糖上升較慢，胰島素反應也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a diet focused on blood-sugar impact.","zh":"這個短語描述集中於血糖影響的飲食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"on average","meaning":"平均而言","examples":[{"en":"On average, the low-insulin-secreting group lost nearly 10 pounds.","zh":"平均而言，低胰島素分泌組減掉接近10磅。"},{"en":"On average means considering the typical result across a group.","zh":"「on average」意思是從整個群體看典型結果。"},{"en":"On average, students in the class read for twenty minutes each night.","zh":"平均而言，班上學生每晚閱讀二十分鐘。"},{"en":"If an average is reported, individual results may still vary widely.","zh":"如果報告的是平均數，個別結果仍可能差異很大。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a general group-level result.","zh":"這個短語提供群體層面的概括結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"low-insulin-secreting group","meaning":"低胰島素分泌組","examples":[{"en":"The low-insulin-secreting group fared the same on both diets.","zh":"低胰島素分泌組在兩種飲食上效果相若。"},{"en":"A low-insulin-secreting group is a group of people whose bodies release relatively little insulin after eating.","zh":"「low-insulin-secreting group」是進食後身體釋放相對較少胰島素的一組人。"},{"en":"Researchers may compare low-insulin-secreting people with high-insulin-secreting people.","zh":"研究人員可能比較低胰島素分泌者和高胰島素分泌者。"},{"en":"If this group responds similarly to two diets, insulin level may not change their outcome much.","zh":"如果這組人對兩種飲食反應相似，胰島素水平可能不太改變其結果。"},{"en":"The phrase names a research group based on insulin response.","zh":"這個短語指出根據胰島素反應分類的研究組別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"fare the same on","meaning":"在……上效果相若","examples":[{"en":"The low-insulin-secreting group fared the same on both diets.","zh":"低胰島素分泌組在兩種飲食上效果相若。"},{"en":"To fare the same on something means to have similar results or performance under different conditions.","zh":"「fare the same on」某事，意思是在不同條件下有相似結果或表現。"},{"en":"Two students may fare the same on paper tests and online tests.","zh":"兩名學生可能在紙本測驗和網上測驗上表現相若。"},{"en":"If a group fares the same on two diets, neither diet gives them a clear advantage.","zh":"如果一組人在兩種飲食上效果相若，任何一種飲食都沒有明顯優勢。"},{"en":"The phrase compares outcomes.","zh":"這個短語比較結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in the first six months","meaning":"在首六個月","examples":[{"en":"Participants lost nearly 10 pounds in the first six months.","zh":"參加者在首六個月減掉接近10磅。"},{"en":"In the first six months means during the initial half-year period.","zh":"「in the first six months」意思是在最初半年的期間。"},{"en":"In the first six months of university, students often learn how to manage time.","zh":"在大學首六個月，學生常學會如何管理時間。"},{"en":"If weight loss happens early, researchers still need to see whether it lasts.","zh":"如果減重在早期發生，研究人員仍需觀察它是否持續。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a specific early time frame.","zh":"這個短語提供特定早期時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"gain half of it back","meaning":"反彈約一半","examples":[{"en":"Many participants gained about half of the lost weight back.","zh":"許多參加者反彈了約一半已減掉的體重。"},{"en":"To gain half of it back means to regain about half of what was lost.","zh":"「gain half of it back」意思是重新增加已失去部分的大約一半。"},{"en":"A student may save $1,000, spend $500, and effectively gain half the savings back as expenses.","zh":"學生可能儲了1,000元，花掉500元，即等於花回一半儲蓄。"},{"en":"If people regain half the weight, the diet helped but maintenance was difficult.","zh":"如果人們反彈一半體重，飲食方法曾有效，但維持成果困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes partial regain after loss.","zh":"這個短語描述失去後部分回升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"by the end of","meaning":"到……結束時","examples":[{"en":"Some participants regained weight by the end of the study.","zh":"有些參加者到研究結束時體重回升。"},{"en":"By the end of something means before or at the time when it finishes.","zh":"「by the end of」某事，意思是在它結束前或結束時。"},{"en":"By the end of the term, students should have completed three essays.","zh":"到學期結束時，學生應已完成三篇文章。"},{"en":"If weight returns by the end of a study, early success may not last.","zh":"如果體重到研究結束時回升，早期成功可能沒有維持。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the final point of a period.","zh":"這個短語標示一段時間的終點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"do as well on","meaning":"在……上表現一樣好","examples":[{"en":"The high-insulin group did not do as well on the low-fat plan.","zh":"高胰島素組在低脂計劃上的表現沒有那麼好。"},{"en":"To do as well on something means to achieve an equally good result with that method or condition.","zh":"「do as well on」某事，意思是在該方法或條件下取得同樣好的結果。"},{"en":"Some students do as well on oral exams as on written exams, but others do not.","zh":"有些學生在口試上表現與筆試一樣好，但有些不是。"},{"en":"If one group does not do as well on a diet, that diet may not suit their biology.","zh":"如果一組人在某飲食上表現不一樣好，那種飲食可能不適合他們的生理。"},{"en":"The phrase compares performance or success.","zh":"這個短語比較表現或成效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"low-fat plan","meaning":"低脂計劃","examples":[{"en":"The high-insulin group had poorer results on the low-fat plan.","zh":"高胰島素組在低脂計劃上的結果較差。"},{"en":"A low-fat plan is a diet plan that reduces fat intake.","zh":"「low-fat plan」是減少脂肪攝取的飲食計劃。"},{"en":"A low-fat plan may include steamed food, lean meat, and less oil.","zh":"低脂計劃可能包括蒸煮食物、瘦肉和較少油分。"},{"en":"If someone replaces fat with sugary snacks, a low-fat plan may not work well.","zh":"如果某人用含糖小食取代脂肪，低脂計劃可能效果不佳。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a structured diet based on reducing fat.","zh":"這個短語描述以減少脂肪為基礎的結構化飲食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the most successful","meaning":"最成功的","examples":[{"en":"The most successful participants were high-insulin secretors on the low-glycemic-load diet.","zh":"最成功的參加者是採用低升糖負荷飲食的高胰島素分泌者。"},{"en":"The most successful means the group or people who achieved the best results.","zh":"「the most successful」意思是取得最佳結果的人或群體。"},{"en":"The most successful students were not always the fastest, but the most consistent.","zh":"最成功的學生不一定最快，而往往最穩定。"},{"en":"If one group loses more weight and maintains it better, researchers call them the most successful.","zh":"如果一組人減重更多並維持得更好，研究人員會稱他們為最成功。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the strongest performers.","zh":"這個短語指出表現最強的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"high-insulin secretors","meaning":"高胰島素分泌者","examples":[{"en":"High-insulin secretors did best on a low-glycemic-load diet.","zh":"高胰島素分泌者在低升糖負荷飲食上效果最好。"},{"en":"High-insulin secretors are people whose bodies release high levels of insulin after eating.","zh":"「high-insulin secretors」是進食後身體釋放高水平胰島素的人。"},{"en":"A researcher may test blood samples to identify high-insulin secretors.","zh":"研究人員可能測試血液樣本來識別高胰島素分泌者。"},{"en":"If high-insulin secretors respond better to certain diets, diet advice may need to be personalised.","zh":"如果高胰島素分泌者對某些飲食反應更好，飲食建議可能需要個人化。"},{"en":"The phrase names people according to insulin response.","zh":"這個短語根據胰島素反應命名一類人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"caused not by…, but by…","meaning":"不是由……引起，而是由……引起","examples":[{"en":"Some fat may be caused not by diet or genes, but by germs.","zh":"有些脂肪可能不是由飲食或基因引起，而是由病菌引起。"},{"en":"Caused not by A, but by B means A is not the real cause; B is.","zh":"「caused not by A, but by B」意思是 A 不是真正原因，B 才是。"},{"en":"The student’s poor marks were caused not by laziness, but by months of poor sleep.","zh":"學生成績差不是由懶惰引起，而是由數月睡眠不足引起。"},{"en":"If obesity is caused not only by diet but also by infection, treatment ideas may change.","zh":"如果肥胖不只由飲食引起，也由感染引起，治療想法可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase makes a strong contrast between false and real causes.","zh":"這個短語在錯誤原因與真正原因之間作強烈對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"germs","meaning":"病菌","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers suggest that germs may play a role in obesity.","zh":"有些研究人員提出病菌可能在肥胖中發揮作用。"},{"en":"Germs are tiny organisms or agents, such as bacteria or viruses, that can cause disease.","zh":"「germs」是可引起疾病的微小生物或因子，例如細菌或病毒。"},{"en":"Washing hands before eating can reduce the spread of germs.","zh":"進食前洗手可以減少病菌傳播。"},{"en":"If germs affect body weight, obesity may have an infectious dimension.","zh":"如果病菌影響體重，肥胖可能有感染層面。"},{"en":"The word refers to disease-causing microscopic agents in everyday language.","zh":"這個詞在日常語言中指致病微小因子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"say, a virus","meaning":"例如病毒","examples":[{"en":"Obesity might be linked to germs, say, a virus.","zh":"肥胖可能與病菌有關，例如病毒。"},{"en":"Say, a virus means for example, a virus.","zh":"「say, a virus」意思是例如病毒。"},{"en":"A school may need emergency supplies, say, masks, water, and first-aid kits.","zh":"學校可能需要應急用品，例如口罩、水和急救箱。"},{"en":"If an author says “say”, they are giving one possible example, not the only one.","zh":"如果作者使用 “say”，他是在給出一個可能例子，而不是唯一例子。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an example casually.","zh":"這個短語以隨意方式引入例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"sound like","meaning":"聽起來像","examples":[{"en":"The idea sounds like a sci-fi horror movie.","zh":"這個想法聽起來像科幻恐怖電影。"},{"en":"To sound like something means to seem similar to it when described.","zh":"「sound like」某物，意思是被描述時似乎與它相似。"},{"en":"A plan to live on Mars may sound like science fiction to young students.","zh":"在火星生活的計劃對年幼學生來說可能聽起來像科幻小說。"},{"en":"If a medical idea sounds strange, research may still show it deserves attention.","zh":"如果醫學想法聽起來奇怪，研究仍可能顯示它值得注意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the impression created by an idea.","zh":"這個短語描述想法造成的印象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a sci-fi horror movie","meaning":"科幻恐怖電影","examples":[{"en":"The idea of virus-related obesity sounds like a sci-fi horror movie.","zh":"與病毒相關的肥胖概念聽起來像科幻恐怖電影。"},{"en":"A sci-fi horror movie is a frightening film based on science-fiction ideas.","zh":"「a sci-fi horror movie」是基於科幻概念的驚嚇電影。"},{"en":"A story about a virus changing human behaviour may feel like a sci-fi horror movie.","zh":"關於病毒改變人類行為的故事可能感覺像科幻恐怖電影。"},{"en":"If research sounds like this kind of film, readers may find it strange or alarming.","zh":"如果研究聽起來像這類電影，讀者可能覺得奇怪或不安。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests something dramatic, futuristic, and unsettling.","zh":"這個短語暗示戲劇化、未來感和令人不安。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"new research suggests","meaning":"新研究顯示","examples":[{"en":"New research suggests that some obesity may be attributable to infection.","zh":"新研究顯示，有些肥胖可能可歸因於感染。"},{"en":"New research suggests means recent studies indicate a possible conclusion.","zh":"「new research suggests」意思是近期研究指出一個可能結論。"},{"en":"New research suggests that sleep quality may affect memory more than students expect.","zh":"新研究顯示，睡眠質素對記憶的影響可能比學生預期更大。"},{"en":"If research suggests something, it is evidence-based but may still need more confirmation.","zh":"如果研究顯示某事，它有證據基礎，但可能仍需更多確認。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a recent scientific possibility.","zh":"這個短語引入近期科學可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"some dimension of","meaning":"……的某個層面","examples":[{"en":"Some dimension of the obesity epidemic may be linked to viruses.","zh":"肥胖流行問題的某個層面可能與病毒有關。"},{"en":"Some dimension of something means one aspect, layer, or part of a larger issue.","zh":"「some dimension of」某事，意思是較大議題中的一個方面、層面或部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may examine the emotional dimension of exam stress, not only study habits.","zh":"老師可能研究考試壓力的情緒層面，而不只是學習習慣。"},{"en":"If one dimension of obesity is infectious, the overall problem becomes more complex.","zh":"如果肥胖其中一個層面與感染有關，整體問題就更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights one part of a broad problem.","zh":"這個短語突出廣泛問題中的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the obesity epidemic","meaning":"肥胖流行問題","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are studying possible causes of the obesity epidemic.","zh":"研究人員正在研究肥胖流行問題的可能成因。"},{"en":"The obesity epidemic refers to the widespread and increasing problem of obesity in a population.","zh":"「the obesity epidemic」指一個人口中肥胖問題廣泛且日益增加。"},{"en":"Public-health experts may call obesity an epidemic when rates rise across many communities.","zh":"當肥胖率在許多社區上升時，公共衞生專家可能稱它為流行問題。"},{"en":"If an epidemic has many causes, solutions must address food, activity, biology, and environment.","zh":"如果流行問題有許多成因，解決方法就必須處理食物、活動、生理和環境。"},{"en":"The phrase describes obesity as a large-scale public-health problem.","zh":"這個短語把肥胖描述為大型公共衞生問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be attributable to","meaning":"可歸因於","examples":[{"en":"Some obesity may be attributable to infection by common viruses.","zh":"有些肥胖可能可歸因於常見病毒感染。"},{"en":"To be attributable to something means to be caused or explained by it.","zh":"「be attributable to」某事，意思是由它造成或可由它解釋。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be attributable to late-night phone use.","zh":"學生疲倦可能可歸因於深夜使用手機。"},{"en":"If weight gain is attributable to infection, the cause is not just personal behaviour.","zh":"如果體重增加可歸因於感染，成因就不只是個人行為。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to explain cause.","zh":"這個短語是解釋原因的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"infection by common viruses","meaning":"由常見病毒引起的感染","examples":[{"en":"Some obesity may be linked to infection by common viruses.","zh":"有些肥胖可能與由常見病毒引起的感染有關。"},{"en":"Infection by common viruses means illness or biological change caused by viruses that many people may encounter.","zh":"「infection by common viruses」意思是由許多人可能遇到的病毒造成的疾病或生物變化。"},{"en":"A cold can result from infection by common viruses spread through coughs and touch.","zh":"感冒可能由咳嗽和接觸傳播的常見病毒感染引起。"},{"en":"If common viruses affect fat cells, ordinary infections may have unexpected effects.","zh":"如果常見病毒影響脂肪細胞，普通感染可能有意想不到的效果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes viral infection from widespread viruses.","zh":"這個短語描述由廣泛病毒引起的病毒感染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the idea of infectobesity","meaning":"感染性肥胖的概念","examples":[{"en":"The idea of infectobesity came to Dhurandhar 20 years ago.","zh":"感染性肥胖的概念在20年前浮現在 Dhurandhar 腦海。"},{"en":"The idea of infectobesity is the concept that infection may contribute to obesity.","zh":"「the idea of infectobesity」是感染可能促成肥胖的概念。"},{"en":"A scientist may develop a new idea after noticing an unusual pattern in animals.","zh":"科學家可能在注意到動物中的異常模式後發展新想法。"},{"en":"If infectobesity is real, some weight gain may have an infectious cause.","zh":"如果感染性肥胖是真實的，有些體重增加可能有感染成因。"},{"en":"The phrase names a theory linking infection and obesity.","zh":"這個短語命名一種把感染與肥胖連繫起來的理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"come to someone","meaning":"被某人想到；浮現在某人腦海","examples":[{"en":"The idea came to him when he was a young doctor in Bombay.","zh":"這個想法在他還是孟買年輕醫生時浮現在他腦海。"},{"en":"When an idea comes to someone, it suddenly appears in that person’s mind.","zh":"當一個想法 comes to someone，意思是它突然出現在那個人的腦中。"},{"en":"A solution may come to a student while they are walking home after class.","zh":"解決方法可能在學生放學走回家時浮現在腦海。"},{"en":"If an idea comes unexpectedly, it may begin a long research journey.","zh":"如果想法意外出現，它可能開始一段漫長研究旅程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a thought arriving in someone’s mind.","zh":"這個短語描述念頭進入某人腦海。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"treat obesity","meaning":"治療肥胖","examples":[{"en":"Dhurandhar was treating obesity in Bombay.","zh":"Dhurandhar 當時在孟買治療肥胖。"},{"en":"To treat obesity means to help reduce or manage obesity through medical, dietary, behavioural, or lifestyle methods.","zh":"「treat obesity」意思是透過醫療、飲食、行為或生活方式方法幫助減少或管理肥胖。"},{"en":"A clinic may treat obesity by offering nutrition advice, exercise support, and medical monitoring.","zh":"診所可能透過營養建議、運動支援和醫療監察治療肥胖。"},{"en":"If obesity has many causes, treatment may need several approaches.","zh":"如果肥胖有許多成因，治療可能需要多種方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes professional care for obesity.","zh":"這個短語描述對肥胖的專業照護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"local avian virus","meaning":"本地鳥類病毒","examples":[{"en":"He discovered that a local avian virus affected chickens.","zh":"他發現一種本地鳥類病毒影響雞隻。"},{"en":"A local avian virus is a bird-related virus found in a particular area.","zh":"「local avian virus」是在特定地區發現、與鳥類相關的病毒。"},{"en":"Farmers may worry about a local avian virus if many chickens suddenly become ill.","zh":"如果許多雞突然生病，農民可能擔心本地鳥類病毒。"},{"en":"If an avian virus changes animal weight, researchers may ask whether similar viruses affect humans.","zh":"如果鳥類病毒改變動物體重，研究人員可能追問類似病毒是否影響人類。"},{"en":"The phrase names a bird virus from a local setting.","zh":"這個短語指出來自本地環境的鳥類病毒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"become ill with","meaning":"患上……；因……生病","examples":[{"en":"Chickens became ill with organ damage.","zh":"雞隻因器官損傷而生病。"},{"en":"To become ill with something means to develop sickness or a health problem.","zh":"「become ill with」某事，意思是患上疾病或出現健康問題。"},{"en":"A child may become ill with flu after classmates cough around them.","zh":"如果同學在身邊咳嗽，孩子可能患上流感。"},{"en":"If animals become ill with organ damage, the disease is serious.","zh":"如果動物患上器官損傷，疾病就很嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase describes developing a particular illness or condition.","zh":"這個短語描述出現特定疾病或狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"organ damage","meaning":"器官損傷","examples":[{"en":"The virus caused chickens to suffer organ damage.","zh":"該病毒導致雞隻出現器官損傷。"},{"en":"Organ damage means harm to important body parts such as the liver, heart, kidneys, or lungs.","zh":"「organ damage」意思是肝、心、腎或肺等重要身體器官受損。"},{"en":"Severe infection can sometimes lead to organ damage if it is not treated quickly.","zh":"如果沒有迅速治療，嚴重感染有時可導致器官損傷。"},{"en":"If a virus causes organ damage, it can threaten survival.","zh":"如果病毒造成器官損傷，它可能威脅生命。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious internal injury.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重內部傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"abdominal fat","meaning":"腹部脂肪","examples":[{"en":"The chickens developed large amounts of abdominal fat.","zh":"雞隻形成大量腹部脂肪。"},{"en":"Abdominal fat is fat stored around the belly area.","zh":"「abdominal fat」是儲存在腹部周圍的脂肪。"},{"en":"A doctor may measure waist size to estimate abdominal fat and health risk.","zh":"醫生可能量度腰圍，以估計腹部脂肪和健康風險。"},{"en":"If abdominal fat increases, risk for diabetes and heart disease may also rise.","zh":"如果腹部脂肪增加，糖尿病和心臟病風險也可能上升。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to fat around the abdomen.","zh":"這個短語指腹部周圍的脂肪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"before they died","meaning":"在死亡前","examples":[{"en":"The chickens developed abdominal fat before they died.","zh":"雞隻在死亡前形成腹部脂肪。"},{"en":"Before they died means during the period before death occurred.","zh":"「before they died」意思是在死亡發生之前的期間。"},{"en":"The old trees dropped many seeds before they died in the drought.","zh":"老樹在乾旱中死亡前掉下許多種子。"},{"en":"If symptoms appear before animals die, researchers can study the disease process.","zh":"如果症狀在動物死亡前出現，研究人員可以研究疾病過程。"},{"en":"The phrase gives timing before death.","zh":"這個短語提供死亡前的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in experiments","meaning":"在實驗中","examples":[{"en":"In experiments, infected chickens became obese.","zh":"在實驗中，受感染雞隻變得肥胖。"},{"en":"In experiments means under controlled research conditions designed to test an idea.","zh":"「in experiments」意思是在用來測試想法的受控研究條件下。"},{"en":"In experiments, students may compare how plants grow with and without sunlight.","zh":"在實驗中，學生可能比較植物在有陽光和沒有陽光下如何生長。"},{"en":"If an effect appears in experiments, researchers may test whether it also appears in real life.","zh":"如果某效果在實驗中出現，研究人員可能測試它是否也在現實中出現。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence from scientific testing.","zh":"這個短語引入科學測試證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"SMAM-1-infected chickens","meaning":"感染 SMAM-1 的雞","examples":[{"en":"SMAM-1-infected chickens became obese on the same diet as other chickens.","zh":"感染 SMAM-1 的雞在與其他雞吃同樣飲食下變得肥胖。"},{"en":"SMAM-1-infected chickens are chickens that have been infected with the SMAM-1 virus.","zh":"「SMAM-1-infected chickens」是感染了 SMAM-1 病毒的雞。"},{"en":"Researchers compare infected chickens with uninfected ones to see whether the virus changes weight.","zh":"研究人員比較感染雞與未感染雞，以觀察病毒是否改變體重。"},{"en":"If infected chickens gain fat on the same diet, the virus may be influencing metabolism.","zh":"如果感染雞在相同飲食下增加脂肪，病毒可能正在影響代謝。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a group of animals by infection status.","zh":"這個短語根據感染狀態指出一組動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"on the same diet as","meaning":"與……吃同樣的飲食","examples":[{"en":"The infected chickens became obese on the same diet as uninfected ones.","zh":"受感染雞隻與未感染雞吃同樣飲食卻變得肥胖。"},{"en":"On the same diet as means eating the same food pattern as another group.","zh":"「on the same diet as」意思是與另一組吃同樣飲食模式。"},{"en":"Two students may perform differently even on the same study schedule as each other.","zh":"兩名學生即使用同樣溫習時間表，表現也可能不同。"},{"en":"If animals gain weight on the same diet, another factor besides food may be involved.","zh":"如果動物在同樣飲食下增重，食物以外可能有其他因素參與。"},{"en":"The phrase helps control comparison.","zh":"這個短語幫助控制比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"uninfected ones","meaning":"未受感染的那些","examples":[{"en":"The uninfected ones stayed thin on the same diet.","zh":"未受感染的那些在相同飲食下保持瘦削。"},{"en":"Uninfected ones are individuals or animals that do not have the infection being studied.","zh":"「uninfected ones」是沒有研究中所指感染的個體或動物。"},{"en":"Researchers compare infected mice with uninfected ones to see what a virus changes.","zh":"研究人員比較受感染老鼠和未受感染老鼠，以觀察病毒改變了甚麼。"},{"en":"If uninfected ones stay healthy, infection may explain the difference.","zh":"如果未受感染的那些保持健康，感染可能解釋差異。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the comparison group without infection.","zh":"這個短語指沒有感染的比較組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"stay svelte","meaning":"保持苗條","examples":[{"en":"The uninfected chickens stayed svelte.","zh":"未受感染雞隻保持苗條。"},{"en":"To stay svelte means to remain slim, lean, or slender.","zh":"「stay svelte」意思是保持纖瘦、精瘦或苗條。"},{"en":"A dancer may stay svelte through regular training and careful eating.","zh":"舞蹈員可能透過規律訓練和注意飲食保持苗條。"},{"en":"If uninfected animals stay svelte while infected ones gain weight, researchers suspect infection matters.","zh":"如果未感染動物保持苗條，而感染動物增重，研究人員會懷疑感染有影響。"},{"en":"The phrase is a stylish way to say “remain slim”.","zh":"這個短語是 “remain slim” 的較有風格說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"move to the US","meaning":"移居美國","examples":[{"en":"Dhurandhar later moved to the US to continue his research.","zh":"Dhurandhar 後來移居美國繼續研究。"},{"en":"To move to the US means to relocate and live or work in the United States.","zh":"「move to the US」意思是搬遷到美國生活或工作。"},{"en":"A scientist may move to the US to join a university laboratory.","zh":"科學家可能移居美國加入大學實驗室。"},{"en":"If researchers move countries, they may gain access to new equipment and collaborators.","zh":"如果研究人員移居他國，可能獲得新設備和合作者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes relocation to the United States.","zh":"這個短語描述遷往美國。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"bona fide human virus","meaning":"真正的人類病毒","examples":[{"en":"He began studying a bona fide human virus.","zh":"他開始研究一種真正的人類病毒。"},{"en":"A bona fide human virus is a genuine virus known to infect humans.","zh":"「bona fide human virus」是真正已知會感染人類的病毒。"},{"en":"A researcher needs strong evidence before calling a virus a bona fide human virus.","zh":"研究人員需要有力證據，才會稱一種病毒為真正的人類病毒。"},{"en":"If a virus truly infects humans, its health effects become more relevant to medicine.","zh":"如果病毒確實感染人類，其健康影響就與醫學更相關。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the virus is real and human-related.","zh":"這個短語強調病毒是真實且與人類相關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"adenovirus 36","meaning":"腺病毒 36","examples":[{"en":"Adenovirus 36 is a human virus linked to weight gain in the research.","zh":"腺病毒36是在研究中與體重增加有關的人類病毒。"},{"en":"Adenovirus 36 is a specific type of adenovirus studied for possible links with obesity.","zh":"「adenovirus 36」是一種特定腺病毒，因可能與肥胖有關而被研究。"},{"en":"Scientists may test blood samples to see whether people have been exposed to adenovirus 36.","zh":"科學家可能測試血液樣本，以了解人們是否接觸過腺病毒36。"},{"en":"If adenovirus 36 affects fat cells, it could change how researchers view some obesity.","zh":"如果腺病毒36影響脂肪細胞，它可能改變研究人員對某些肥胖的看法。"},{"en":"The phrase names the specific virus in the study.","zh":"這個短語指出研究中的特定病毒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in the lab","meaning":"在實驗室中","examples":[{"en":"In the lab, animals infected with the virus became obese.","zh":"在實驗室中，受該病毒感染的動物變得肥胖。"},{"en":"In the lab means in a laboratory setting under research conditions.","zh":"「in the lab」意思是在實驗室環境和研究條件下。"},{"en":"In the lab, students can test how different liquids affect plant growth.","zh":"在實驗室中，學生可以測試不同液體如何影響植物生長。"},{"en":"If a result appears in the lab, scientists still need to test how it applies outside the lab.","zh":"如果結果在實驗室中出現，科學家仍需測試它如何適用於實驗室外。"},{"en":"The phrase describes controlled scientific testing.","zh":"這個短語描述受控科學測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"every species of animal","meaning":"每一種動物","examples":[{"en":"Every species of animal infected with the virus became obese.","zh":"每一種受該病毒感染的動物都變得肥胖。"},{"en":"Every species of animal means each kind of animal in the study, without exception.","zh":"「every species of animal」意思是研究中的每一種動物，沒有例外。"},{"en":"A zoo vet must understand that every species of animal may need different food and care.","zh":"動物園獸醫必須明白每一種動物可能需要不同食物和照顧。"},{"en":"If every tested species shows the same effect, the finding becomes more striking.","zh":"如果每一種測試動物都顯示同一效果，發現就更引人注目。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses broad consistency across animal types.","zh":"這個短語強調不同動物種類之間的一致性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"rhesus monkeys","meaning":"恒河猴","examples":[{"en":"Even rhesus monkeys gained weight after exposure to the virus.","zh":"甚至恒河猴接觸該病毒後也增加體重。"},{"en":"Rhesus monkeys are a species of monkey often used in biological and medical research.","zh":"「rhesus monkeys」是一種常用於生物和醫學研究的猴子。"},{"en":"Researchers may study rhesus monkeys when they need animal models closer to humans than mice.","zh":"當研究人員需要比老鼠更接近人類的動物模型時，可能研究恒河猴。"},{"en":"If rhesus monkeys gain weight after infection, the result may seem more relevant to humans.","zh":"如果恒河猴感染後增加體重，結果可能看起來與人類更相關。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific primate species.","zh":"這個短語指出一種特定靈長類動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"pick up the virus","meaning":"感染病毒","examples":[{"en":"Rhesus monkeys picked up the virus from the environment.","zh":"恒河猴從環境中感染病毒。"},{"en":"To pick up the virus means to become infected with it through contact or exposure.","zh":"「pick up the virus」意思是透過接觸或暴露而感染該病毒。"},{"en":"A child may pick up a virus at school if many classmates are sick.","zh":"如果許多同學生病，孩子可能在學校感染病毒。"},{"en":"If animals pick up a virus naturally, infection may happen outside controlled experiments.","zh":"如果動物自然感染病毒，感染可能在受控實驗之外發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes catching or acquiring a virus.","zh":"這個短語描述感染或獲得病毒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"from the environment","meaning":"從環境中","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys picked up the virus from the environment.","zh":"猴子從環境中感染病毒。"},{"en":"From the environment means from surrounding conditions, surfaces, air, animals, or places.","zh":"「from the environment」意思是來自周遭條件、表面、空氣、動物或地方。"},{"en":"Children may pick up germs from the environment when they touch shared toys.","zh":"孩子接觸共用玩具時，可能從環境中沾上病菌。"},{"en":"If a virus comes from the environment, exposure may not require direct contact with a sick person.","zh":"如果病毒來自環境，接觸不一定需要直接接觸病人。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the surrounding source.","zh":"這個短語指出周遭來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"gain body weight","meaning":"增加體重","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys gained 15 per cent of their body weight.","zh":"猴子增加了自身體重的百分之十五。"},{"en":"To gain body weight means to become heavier.","zh":"「gain body weight」意思是變得更重。"},{"en":"A child may gain body weight during puberty as the body grows quickly.","zh":"孩子在青春期可能因身體快速成長而增加體重。"},{"en":"If animals gain body weight after viral exposure, researchers investigate the biological cause.","zh":"如果動物在病毒接觸後增加體重，研究人員會調查生物成因。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an increase in overall weight.","zh":"這個短語描述整體體重增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"upon exposure","meaning":"接觸後","examples":[{"en":"The animals gained weight upon exposure to the virus.","zh":"動物接觸該病毒後增加體重。"},{"en":"Upon exposure means immediately after or as a result of coming into contact with something.","zh":"「upon exposure」意思是在接觸某物之後立即或因此發生。"},{"en":"Some people sneeze upon exposure to dust or pollen.","zh":"有些人接觸塵埃或花粉後會打噴嚏。"},{"en":"If animals change upon exposure to a virus, contact with the virus may be important.","zh":"如果動物接觸病毒後出現變化，接觸該病毒可能很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase connects contact with a following effect.","zh":"這個短語把接觸與隨後效果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"isolate a gene","meaning":"分離出一個基因","examples":[{"en":"Dhurandhar has isolated a gene linked to the virus’s fattening power.","zh":"Dhurandhar 已分離出一個與該病毒致肥能力相關的基因。"},{"en":"To isolate a gene means to identify and separate a specific gene for study.","zh":"「isolate a gene」意思是識別並分離某個特定基因以作研究。"},{"en":"Scientists may isolate a gene to understand why a plant resists disease.","zh":"科學家可能分離出一個基因，以理解植物為何能抵抗疾病。"},{"en":"If a gene is isolated, researchers can test what it does.","zh":"如果基因被分離出來，研究人員就能測試它的作用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes finding a specific genetic factor.","zh":"這個短語描述找出特定遺傳因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be blocked from expressing itself","meaning":"被阻止表達","examples":[{"en":"When the gene is blocked from expressing itself, the virus loses its fattening power.","zh":"當該基因被阻止表達時，病毒失去其致肥能力。"},{"en":"A gene is blocked from expressing itself when it is prevented from producing its usual biological effect.","zh":"當基因被阻止表達時，意思是它被阻止產生通常的生物效果。"},{"en":"Scientists may block a gene from expressing itself to see whether a disease process stops.","zh":"科學家可能阻止某基因表達，以觀察疾病過程是否停止。"},{"en":"If a gene cannot express itself, the trait or effect it controls may not appear.","zh":"如果基因不能表達，它控制的特徵或效果可能不會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stopping a gene from becoming active.","zh":"這個短語描述阻止基因變得活躍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"turn off","meaning":"關掉；使……停止運作","examples":[{"en":"Blocking the gene seems to turn off the virus’s fattening power.","zh":"阻截該基因似乎會關掉病毒的致肥能力。"},{"en":"To turn off an effect means to stop it from working or becoming active.","zh":"「turn off」某效果，意思是阻止它運作或變得活躍。"},{"en":"A teacher may turn off classroom notifications so students can focus.","zh":"老師可能關掉課室通知，讓學生專心。"},{"en":"If blocking a gene turns off an effect, that gene may be essential.","zh":"如果阻截基因會關掉某效果，該基因可能是必要的。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used figuratively to mean stopping a function.","zh":"這個短語常作比喻使用，意思是停止某功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"fattening power","meaning":"致肥能力","examples":[{"en":"The virus’s fattening power may depend on a specific gene.","zh":"該病毒的致肥能力可能取決於一個特定基因。"},{"en":"Fattening power means the ability to cause weight gain or fat formation.","zh":"「fattening power」意思是造成體重增加或脂肪形成的能力。"},{"en":"A snack’s fattening power may come from high sugar, oil, and portion size.","zh":"小食的致肥能力可能來自高糖、高油和份量大。"},{"en":"If a virus has fattening power, it may change how cells store energy.","zh":"如果病毒具有致肥能力，它可能改變細胞儲存能量的方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the capacity to make something fatter.","zh":"這個短語描述令某物變肥的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"stem cells","meaning":"幹細胞","examples":[{"en":"Stem cells exposed to AD-36 can turn into fat cells.","zh":"接觸 AD-36 的幹細胞可以變成脂肪細胞。"},{"en":"Stem cells are early cells that can develop into different types of specialised cells.","zh":"「stem cells」是早期細胞，可以發展成不同種類的專門細胞。"},{"en":"Scientists study stem cells because they may help repair damaged tissues one day.","zh":"科學家研究幹細胞，因為它們有一天可能幫助修復受損組織。"},{"en":"If stem cells turn into fat cells after viral exposure, the virus may affect cell development.","zh":"如果幹細胞在接觸病毒後變成脂肪細胞，病毒可能影響細胞發展。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to flexible cells with developmental potential.","zh":"這個短語指具有發展潛力的靈活細胞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"extracted from fat cells","meaning":"從脂肪細胞提取","examples":[{"en":"Stem cells were extracted from fat cells and exposed to the virus.","zh":"幹細胞從脂肪細胞提取出來，並接觸該病毒。"},{"en":"Extracted from fat cells means taken out of fat tissue or fat-related cells for study.","zh":"「extracted from fat cells」意思是從脂肪組織或脂肪相關細胞取出以作研究。"},{"en":"Scientists may extract cells from a sample to examine them under a microscope.","zh":"科學家可能從樣本中提取細胞，在顯微鏡下檢查。"},{"en":"If stem cells are extracted carefully, researchers can test how they respond to a virus.","zh":"如果幹細胞被小心提取，研究人員可以測試它們如何回應病毒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes removing biological material from fat tissue.","zh":"這個短語描述從脂肪組織移出生物材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be exposed to","meaning":"接觸到……","examples":[{"en":"Stem cells were exposed to AD-36 in the lab.","zh":"幹細胞在實驗室中接觸到 AD-36。"},{"en":"To be exposed to something means to come into contact with it.","zh":"「be exposed to」某物，意思是接觸到它。"},{"en":"A person exposed to smoke every day may develop breathing problems.","zh":"每日接觸煙霧的人可能出現呼吸問題。"},{"en":"If cells are exposed to a virus, scientists can observe whether they change.","zh":"如果細胞接觸到病毒，科學家可以觀察它們是否改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes contact with a factor or substance.","zh":"這個短語描述接觸某因素或物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"reliably blossom into","meaning":"穩定地發展成","examples":[{"en":"The stem cells reliably blossom into fat cells after exposure to AD-36.","zh":"幹細胞在接觸 AD-36 後穩定地發展成脂肪細胞。"},{"en":"To reliably blossom into something means to consistently develop into that form.","zh":"「reliably blossom into」某物，意思是穩定而一致地發展成該形態。"},{"en":"With enough practice, a shy student may blossom into a confident speaker.","zh":"經過足夠練習，害羞學生可能發展成有自信的演講者。"},{"en":"If stem cells reliably become fat cells after exposure, the effect is repeated and predictable.","zh":"如果幹細胞在接觸後穩定地變成脂肪細胞，效果就是可重複且可預測的。"},{"en":"The phrase uses “blossom” figuratively to mean develop.","zh":"這個短語以 “blossom” 作比喻，意思是發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"fat cells","meaning":"脂肪細胞","examples":[{"en":"The exposed stem cells became fat cells.","zh":"接觸病毒的幹細胞變成脂肪細胞。"},{"en":"Fat cells are body cells that store fat and energy.","zh":"「fat cells」是儲存脂肪和能量的身體細胞。"},{"en":"When people gain weight, fat cells may grow larger or increase in number.","zh":"當人們增加體重，脂肪細胞可能變大或數量增加。"},{"en":"If a virus encourages stem cells to become fat cells, it may contribute to fat storage.","zh":"如果病毒促使幹細胞變成脂肪細胞，它可能促成脂肪儲存。"},{"en":"The phrase names the cells involved in storing body fat.","zh":"這個短語指出負責儲存身體脂肪的細胞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the key gene","meaning":"關鍵基因","examples":[{"en":"The key gene appears to control the virus’s fattening effect.","zh":"關鍵基因似乎控制病毒的致肥效果。"},{"en":"The key gene is the most important gene involved in a particular effect or process.","zh":"「the key gene」是涉及某特定效果或過程的最重要基因。"},{"en":"Scientists may look for the key gene behind a plant’s ability to survive drought.","zh":"科學家可能尋找植物能在乾旱中存活背後的關鍵基因。"},{"en":"If a key gene is blocked and the effect disappears, the gene is likely central.","zh":"如果關鍵基因被阻截後效果消失，該基因很可能十分核心。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the gene that matters most.","zh":"這個短語指出最重要的基因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be inhibited","meaning":"被抑制","examples":[{"en":"When the key gene is inhibited, the stem cells do not become fat cells.","zh":"當關鍵基因被抑制時，幹細胞不會變成脂肪細胞。"},{"en":"To be inhibited means to be slowed, blocked, or prevented from working.","zh":"「be inhibited」意思是被減慢、阻截或阻止運作。"},{"en":"A medicine may inhibit a virus by stopping it from multiplying.","zh":"藥物可能透過阻止病毒繁殖來抑制病毒。"},{"en":"If a gene is inhibited and fat-cell formation stops, the gene may be necessary.","zh":"如果基因被抑制而脂肪細胞形成停止，該基因可能是必要的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes biological activity being held back.","zh":"這個短語描述生物活動被壓制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"differentiate","meaning":"分化","examples":[{"en":"The stem cells do not differentiate when the key gene is inhibited.","zh":"當關鍵基因被抑制時，幹細胞不會分化。"},{"en":"To differentiate means for cells to develop into a more specialised type.","zh":"「differentiate」意思是細胞發展成較專門的類型。"},{"en":"In biology, stem cells can differentiate into muscle, nerve, or blood cells.","zh":"在生物學中，幹細胞可以分化成肌肉、神經或血液細胞。"},{"en":"If cells fail to differentiate, they do not become the specialised cells expected.","zh":"如果細胞未能分化，它們就不會變成預期的專門細胞。"},{"en":"The word describes a key process in cell development.","zh":"這個詞描述細胞發展中的關鍵過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"necessary and sufficient","meaning":"必要且充分","examples":[{"en":"The gene appears to be necessary and sufficient to trigger AD-36-related obesity.","zh":"該基因似乎對引發與 AD-36 相關的肥胖而言是必要且充分的。"},{"en":"Necessary and sufficient means required for an effect and enough by itself to cause that effect.","zh":"「necessary and sufficient」意思是某事既是效果所必需，又單靠它已足以造成效果。"},{"en":"A password may be necessary and sufficient to enter a simple online account.","zh":"對簡單網上帳戶而言，密碼可能是登入所必要且充分的條件。"},{"en":"If a gene is necessary and sufficient, blocking it may stop the whole process.","zh":"如果某基因是必要且充分的，阻截它可能停止整個過程。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to show strong causal importance.","zh":"這個短語用來顯示強烈因果重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"trigger obesity","meaning":"引發肥胖","examples":[{"en":"The gene may trigger obesity related to AD-36.","zh":"該基因可能引發與 AD-36 相關的肥胖。"},{"en":"To trigger obesity means to start or set off processes that lead to obesity.","zh":"「trigger obesity」意思是啟動導致肥胖的過程。"},{"en":"Long-term stress may trigger overeating in some people.","zh":"長期壓力可能引發某些人過量進食。"},{"en":"If a gene triggers fat-cell formation, it may increase body weight over time.","zh":"如果基因引發脂肪細胞形成，它可能隨時間增加體重。"},{"en":"The phrase describes starting a chain of events leading to obesity.","zh":"這個短語描述啟動導致肥胖的一連串事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"AD-36-related obesity","meaning":"與 AD-36 相關的肥胖","examples":[{"en":"Researchers hope to understand AD-36-related obesity.","zh":"研究人員希望理解與 AD-36 相關的肥胖。"},{"en":"AD-36-related obesity means obesity that may be connected to the adenovirus 36 virus.","zh":"「AD-36-related obesity」意思是可能與腺病毒36有關的肥胖。"},{"en":"Doctors would need strong evidence before treating AD-36-related obesity differently.","zh":"醫生需要有力證據，才會以不同方式治療與 AD-36 相關的肥胖。"},{"en":"If obesity is related to a virus, prevention may involve more than diet and exercise.","zh":"如果肥胖與病毒有關，預防可能不只涉及飲食和運動。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a possible virus-linked form of obesity.","zh":"這個短語指出可能與病毒相關的一種肥胖形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the goal is to","meaning":"目標是","examples":[{"en":"The goal is to use the research to create an obesity vaccine.","zh":"目標是利用這項研究創造肥胖疫苗。"},{"en":"The goal is to do something means the main aim is that action or result.","zh":"「the goal is to」做某事，意思是主要目的就是該行動或結果。"},{"en":"The goal is to help students speak naturally, not only pass exams.","zh":"目標是幫助學生自然說話，而不只是通過考試。"},{"en":"If the goal is to create a vaccine, researchers need to identify the virus mechanism clearly.","zh":"如果目標是創造疫苗，研究人員需要清楚識別病毒機制。"},{"en":"The phrase states the purpose of a plan.","zh":"這個短語說明計劃目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a sort of","meaning":"某種；一類","examples":[{"en":"The research may lead to a sort of obesity vaccine.","zh":"這項研究可能帶來某種肥胖疫苗。"},{"en":"A sort of something means a kind of it, often not an exact or traditional version.","zh":"「a sort of」某物，意思是某一類東西，通常不是完全標準或傳統版本。"},{"en":"A study timetable can act as a sort of map for exam preparation.","zh":"溫習時間表可以充當某種考試準備地圖。"},{"en":"If a treatment prevents virus-related weight gain, it may be a sort of obesity vaccine.","zh":"如果一種治療能防止病毒相關體重增加，它可能是某種肥胖疫苗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an approximate type.","zh":"這個短語描述大概類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"obesity vaccine","meaning":"肥胖疫苗","examples":[{"en":"The researchers hope to create an obesity vaccine.","zh":"研究人員希望創造肥胖疫苗。"},{"en":"An obesity vaccine would be a vaccine intended to prevent a form of obesity, especially if infection is involved.","zh":"「obesity vaccine」是旨在預防某種肥胖的疫苗，尤其在感染參與其中時。"},{"en":"A vaccine normally trains the body to resist a disease-causing agent.","zh":"疫苗通常訓練身體抵抗致病因子。"},{"en":"If obesity can be triggered by a virus, a vaccine might help prevent that specific pathway.","zh":"如果肥胖可以由病毒引發，疫苗可能幫助預防該特定路徑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a possible future medical solution.","zh":"這個短語描述可能的未來醫學解決方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"Reading Passage 3 has seven sections","meaning":"第三篇閱讀文章有七個部分","examples":[{"en":"Reading Passage 3 has seven sections.","zh":"第三篇閱讀文章有七個部分。"},{"en":"This sentence means the third reading text is divided into seven parts.","zh":"這句話意思是第三篇閱讀文本被分成七部分。"},{"en":"In IELTS Reading, a passage may have sections labelled A to G.","zh":"在 IELTS Reading 中，文章可能有標為 A 至 G 的部分。"},{"en":"If a passage has seven sections, matching questions may ask where information appears.","zh":"如果文章有七個部分，配對題可能要求找出資料出現在哪裡。"},{"en":"The phrase gives structural information about the reading text.","zh":"這個短語提供閱讀文本的結構資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"contain the following information","meaning":"包含以下資料","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which section contains the following information.","zh":"學生識別哪一部分包含以下資料。"},{"en":"To contain the following information means to include the details listed below.","zh":"「contain the following information」意思是包括下方列出的細節。"},{"en":"A paragraph may contain the following information about causes, examples, or results.","zh":"段落可能包含以下關於成因、例子或結果的資料。"},{"en":"If students scan for key words, they can find where the information is contained.","zh":"如果學生掃讀關鍵詞，就能找出資料被包含在哪裡。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in paragraph-matching tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於段落配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"write the correct letter","meaning":"寫上正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the correct letter in the answer boxes.","zh":"考生在答案框中寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"To write the correct letter means to choose the letter that matches the answer and record it.","zh":"「write the correct letter」意思是選擇與答案相符的字母並寫下來。"},{"en":"If the answer is section C, candidates should write C, not the whole paragraph.","zh":"如果答案是 C 段，考生應寫 C，而不是整段。"},{"en":"If the wrong letter is written, the answer will not match the evidence.","zh":"如果寫錯字母，答案就不能與證據相符。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a precise exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語給出精確考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"use any letter more than once","meaning":"可重複使用任何字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates may use any letter more than once.","zh":"考生可重複使用任何字母。"},{"en":"Use any letter more than once means the same section or option can be chosen for more than one answer.","zh":"「use any letter more than once」意思是同一部分或選項可以用於多於一個答案。"},{"en":"In a matching task, section B may answer two different questions.","zh":"在配對題中，B 段可能回答兩條不同問題。"},{"en":"If students assume each letter can be used only once, they may make avoidable mistakes.","zh":"如果學生以為每個字母只能用一次，就可能犯可避免的錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase removes a common exam restriction.","zh":"這個短語取消一種常見考試限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"an evaluation of","meaning":"對……的評估","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for an evaluation of the effect of weight loss on different diets.","zh":"題目要求對不同飲食中減重效果作評估。"},{"en":"An evaluation of something is a judgement or assessment based on evidence.","zh":"「an evaluation of」某事，是基於證據作出的判斷或評估。"},{"en":"A teacher may write an evaluation of a student’s essay after checking content and grammar.","zh":"老師可能在檢查內容和文法後，為學生文章寫評估。"},{"en":"If research evaluates different diets, it compares their results and usefulness.","zh":"如果研究評估不同飲食，它會比較其結果和實用性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful assessment.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the effect of weight loss on","meaning":"減重對……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The study compares the effect of weight loss on different kinds of diets.","zh":"該研究比較減重對不同種類飲食方法的影響。"},{"en":"The effect of weight loss on something means how weight loss changes or influences that thing.","zh":"「the effect of weight loss on」某事，意思是減重如何改變或影響該事。"},{"en":"A doctor may study the effect of weight loss on blood pressure.","zh":"醫生可能研究減重對血壓的影響。"},{"en":"If weight loss affects hormones, hunger and metabolism may change afterward.","zh":"如果減重影響荷爾蒙，之後飢餓感和新陳代謝可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase connects weight loss with its result or impact.","zh":"這個短語把減重與其結果或影響連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"different kinds of diets","meaning":"不同種類的飲食方法","examples":[{"en":"Researchers compared different kinds of diets.","zh":"研究人員比較不同種類的飲食方法。"},{"en":"Different kinds of diets means various eating plans with different rules or goals.","zh":"「different kinds of diets」意思是具有不同規則或目標的各種飲食計劃。"},{"en":"A clinic may compare low-carb, low-fat, and Mediterranean diets.","zh":"診所可能比較低碳水、低脂和地中海飲食。"},{"en":"If different diets work for different people, one-size-fits-all advice may fail.","zh":"如果不同飲食適合不同人，一刀切建議可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes variety in eating approaches.","zh":"這個短語描述飲食方法的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"research involving","meaning":"涉及……的研究","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to research involving participants’ relatives.","zh":"題目指涉及參加者親屬的研究。"},{"en":"Research involving someone or something includes that person, group, or factor in the study.","zh":"「research involving」某人或某事，意思是研究包括該人、群體或因素。"},{"en":"A school study involving parents may ask how homework affects family life.","zh":"涉及家長的學校研究可能詢問功課如何影響家庭生活。"},{"en":"If research involves relatives, it may explore family patterns or inherited risk.","zh":"如果研究涉及親屬，它可能探討家庭模式或遺傳風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes who or what is included in research.","zh":"這個短語描述研究包括誰或甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"participants’ relatives","meaning":"參加者的親屬","examples":[{"en":"The study involved participants’ relatives, especially mothers and children.","zh":"該研究涉及參加者的親屬，尤其是母親和孩子。"},{"en":"Participants’ relatives are family members of the people taking part in a study.","zh":"「participants’ relatives」是參加研究者的家庭成員。"},{"en":"Researchers may ask participants’ relatives about family medical history.","zh":"研究人員可能詢問參加者的親屬有關家族病史。"},{"en":"If relatives are studied, scientists can examine patterns across generations.","zh":"如果親屬被納入研究，科學家可以檢視跨代模式。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to family members connected to research participants.","zh":"這個短語指與研究參加者相關的家庭成員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"immediately regain weight","meaning":"立即反彈","examples":[{"en":"Some people did not immediately regain weight after weight loss.","zh":"有些人在減重後沒有立即反彈。"},{"en":"To immediately regain weight means to put lost weight back on very soon after losing it.","zh":"「immediately regain weight」意思是在減重後很快重新增加已減去的體重。"},{"en":"A dieter may immediately regain weight if they return to old eating habits after a crash diet.","zh":"如果節食者在極端節食後回到舊飲食習慣，可能立即反彈。"},{"en":"If weight is not regained immediately, researchers still need to check long-term maintenance.","zh":"如果體重沒有立即反彈，研究人員仍需檢查長期維持情況。"},{"en":"The phrase describes quick rebound after weight loss.","zh":"這個短語描述減重後快速回升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"after weight loss","meaning":"減重後","examples":[{"en":"Maintaining a lower weight after weight loss can be difficult.","zh":"減重後維持較低體重可能很困難。"},{"en":"After weight loss means during the period following a reduction in weight.","zh":"「after weight loss」意思是在體重下降之後的期間。"},{"en":"After weight loss, a person may need new habits to maintain progress.","zh":"減重後，一個人可能需要新習慣來維持進展。"},{"en":"If hormones change after weight loss, hunger may increase.","zh":"如果荷爾蒙在減重後改變，飢餓感可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the maintenance stage after losing weight.","zh":"這個短語集中於減重後的維持階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"long-term hunger","meaning":"長期飢餓感","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether long-term hunger is tolerable.","zh":"題目問長期飢餓感是否可以忍受。"},{"en":"Long-term hunger is a persistent feeling of hunger that continues for a long period.","zh":"「long-term hunger」是長時間持續的飢餓感。"},{"en":"A person who feels hungry every day after dieting may struggle with long-term hunger.","zh":"節食後每天都感到肚餓的人，可能受長期飢餓感困擾。"},{"en":"If long-term hunger is severe, willpower alone may not solve the problem.","zh":"如果長期飢餓感嚴重，單靠意志力可能不能解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ongoing hunger, not a short moment before lunch.","zh":"這個短語描述持續飢餓，而不是午餐前一刻的短暫飢餓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be tolerable","meaning":"可以忍受","examples":[{"en":"Long-term hunger may not be tolerable for most people.","zh":"對大多數人而言，長期飢餓感可能不可忍受。"},{"en":"To be tolerable means to be bearable or possible to endure.","zh":"「be tolerable」意思是可以承受或可以忍受。"},{"en":"A little noise may be tolerable, but constant drilling can be unbearable.","zh":"一點噪音可能可以忍受，但持續鑽牆聲可能令人受不了。"},{"en":"If hunger is not tolerable, people may abandon a weight-loss plan.","zh":"如果飢餓感不可忍受，人們可能放棄減重計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase describes whether something can be endured.","zh":"這個短語描述某事是否能被承受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"weight-loss programme","meaning":"減重計劃","examples":[{"en":"Long-term hunger can make a weight-loss programme difficult.","zh":"長期飢餓感可以令減重計劃變得困難。"},{"en":"A weight-loss programme is a planned system designed to help people lose weight.","zh":"「weight-loss programme」是旨在幫助人減重的有計劃系統。"},{"en":"A clinic’s weight-loss programme may include meal plans, exercise, counselling, and check-ups.","zh":"診所的減重計劃可能包括餐單、運動、輔導和檢查。"},{"en":"If a programme ignores hunger and biology, participants may struggle to continue.","zh":"如果計劃忽視飢餓感和生理因素，參加者可能難以繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an organised plan for losing weight.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的減重方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"ongoing research","meaning":"正在進行的研究","examples":[{"en":"Ongoing research may lead to a new practical solution.","zh":"正在進行的研究可能帶來新的實際解決方法。"},{"en":"Ongoing research is research that is still continuing and has not fully finished.","zh":"「ongoing research」是仍在繼續、尚未完全完成的研究。"},{"en":"Ongoing research into sleep may change how schools design timetables.","zh":"正在進行的睡眠研究可能改變學校如何設計時間表。"},{"en":"If research is ongoing, conclusions may become clearer as more evidence appears.","zh":"如果研究仍在進行，隨着更多證據出現，結論可能更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continuing investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述持續調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"導致；帶來","examples":[{"en":"The research may lead to an obesity vaccine.","zh":"這項研究可能帶來肥胖疫苗。"},{"en":"To lead to something means to cause it or result in it.","zh":"「lead to」某事，意思是造成它或帶來它。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can lead to weaker concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致課堂專注力較弱。"},{"en":"If a gene discovery leads to a vaccine, basic research becomes practical medicine.","zh":"如果基因發現帶來疫苗，基礎研究就變成實用醫學。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a cause or process with an outcome.","zh":"這個短語把原因或過程與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"a practical solution","meaning":"實際解決方法","examples":[{"en":"Scientists hope to find a practical solution to virus-related obesity.","zh":"科學家希望找到病毒相關肥胖的實際解決方法。"},{"en":"A practical solution is a method that can actually be used to solve a real problem.","zh":"「a practical solution」是可以真正用來解決現實問題的方法。"},{"en":"A school may need a practical solution to late homework, such as a clear reminder system.","zh":"學校可能需要一個處理遲交功課的實際解決方法，例如清楚提醒系統。"},{"en":"If a solution is too expensive or unrealistic, it may not help ordinary people.","zh":"如果解決方法太昂貴或不切實際，可能幫不到普通人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a workable answer.","zh":"這個短語描述可行答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"other than","meaning":"除……以外","examples":[{"en":"The research may lead to a solution other than diet or genetic intervention.","zh":"研究可能帶來飲食或基因干預以外的解決方法。"},{"en":"Other than means different from or apart from the thing mentioned.","zh":"「other than」意思是不同於或除所提及事物之外。"},{"en":"A student may need help other than extra homework, such as sleep support or counselling.","zh":"學生可能需要額外功課以外的幫助，例如睡眠支援或輔導。"},{"en":"If obesity can involve infection, solutions other than diet may become possible.","zh":"如果肥胖可以涉及感染，飲食以外的解決方法可能變得可行。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an alternative.","zh":"這個短語引入替代方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"genetic intervention","meaning":"基因干預","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions a solution other than diet or genetic intervention.","zh":"題目提到飲食或基因干預以外的解決方法。"},{"en":"Genetic intervention means changing, blocking, or influencing genes to affect a biological outcome.","zh":"「genetic intervention」意思是改變、阻截或影響基因，以影響生物結果。"},{"en":"Scientists may discuss genetic intervention when studying inherited diseases.","zh":"科學家研究遺傳病時，可能討論基因干預。"},{"en":"If a problem can be solved without genetic intervention, treatment may be simpler or safer.","zh":"如果問題不用基因干預也能解決，治療可能更簡單或更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct action on genes.","zh":"這個短語描述對基因的直接行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"match each researcher with","meaning":"將每位研究人員與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match each researcher with the correct finding.","zh":"學生將每位研究人員與正確研究發現配對。"},{"en":"To match each researcher with something means to connect each person to the idea or result they are associated with.","zh":"「match each researcher with」某事，意思是把每個人與其相關想法或結果連起來。"},{"en":"In a reading exercise, students may match each scientist with their discovery.","zh":"在閱讀練習中，學生可能把每位科學家與其發現配對。"},{"en":"If students recognise names and evidence, matching becomes faster.","zh":"如果學生認出姓名和證據，配對就更快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a person-to-idea matching task.","zh":"這個短語描述人物與想法的配對任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"the correct finding","meaning":"正確研究發現","examples":[{"en":"Each researcher must be matched with the correct finding.","zh":"每位研究人員必須與正確研究發現配對。"},{"en":"The correct finding is the research result that accurately belongs to a particular researcher.","zh":"「the correct finding」是準確屬於某位研究人員的研究結果。"},{"en":"If a scientist studied hormones, the correct finding may mention leptin or insulin.","zh":"如果科學家研究荷爾蒙，正確研究發現可能提到瘦素或胰島素。"},{"en":"If candidates confuse two findings, they may match the wrong researcher.","zh":"如果考生混淆兩項發現，可能配對錯誤研究人員。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the accurate research result in a matching task.","zh":"這個短語指出配對題中的準確研究結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be predetermined by","meaning":"由……預先決定","examples":[{"en":"A person’s weight may be partly predetermined by biology.","zh":"一個人的體重可能部分由生理因素預先決定。"},{"en":"To be predetermined by something means to be decided in advance by that factor.","zh":"「be predetermined by」某事，意思是由該因素事先決定。"},{"en":"A plant’s flower colour may be predetermined by its genes.","zh":"植物花色可能由其基因預先決定。"},{"en":"If weight is partly predetermined, personal effort still matters but is not the whole story.","zh":"如果體重部分預先決定，個人努力仍然重要，但不是全部故事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes influence that exists before personal choice.","zh":"這個短語描述在個人選擇之前已存在的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"the interaction of","meaning":"……之間的相互作用","examples":[{"en":"A person’s weight may be shaped by the interaction of DNA and the environment.","zh":"一個人的體重可能由 DNA 與環境之間的相互作用塑造。"},{"en":"The interaction of two things means the way they affect each other.","zh":"「the interaction of」兩件事，意思是它們互相影響的方式。"},{"en":"Learning depends on the interaction of teaching, practice, feedback, and sleep.","zh":"學習取決於教學、練習、回饋和睡眠之間的相互作用。"},{"en":"If DNA and environment interact, neither one alone fully explains the outcome.","zh":"如果 DNA 與環境互動，任何一方都不能單獨完全解釋結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes combined influence.","zh":"這個短語描述共同影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"DNA and the environment","meaning":"DNA 與環境","examples":[{"en":"DNA and the environment can both influence body weight.","zh":"DNA 與環境都可以影響體重。"},{"en":"DNA and the environment means inherited genetic information plus outside conditions and experiences.","zh":"「DNA and the environment」意思是遺傳資訊加上外在條件和經歷。"},{"en":"A child’s health may be shaped by DNA and the environment, including food, stress, and activity.","zh":"孩子的健康可能由 DNA 與環境塑造，包括食物、壓力和活動。"},{"en":"If both influence weight, people with similar diets may still have different outcomes.","zh":"如果兩者都影響體重，飲食相似的人仍可能有不同結果。"},{"en":"The phrase combines inherited and external factors.","zh":"這個短語結合遺傳和外在因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"overweight pregnant mothers","meaning":"超重孕婦","examples":[{"en":"Overweight pregnant mothers may increase the risk of weight gain in their children.","zh":"超重孕婦可能增加孩子體重增加的風險。"},{"en":"Overweight pregnant mothers are pregnant women whose weight is above a healthy range.","zh":"「overweight pregnant mothers」是體重高於健康範圍的孕婦。"},{"en":"Doctors may monitor overweight pregnant mothers for blood sugar and blood pressure problems.","zh":"醫生可能監測超重孕婦的血糖和血壓問題。"},{"en":"If maternal weight affects the womb environment, the child’s later health may be influenced.","zh":"如果母體體重影響子宮環境，孩子日後健康可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a pregnancy-related health risk group.","zh":"這個短語描述與懷孕相關的健康風險群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"increase the risk of","meaning":"增加……的風險","examples":[{"en":"Maternal obesity may increase the risk of weight gain in children.","zh":"母體肥胖可能增加孩子體重增加的風險。"},{"en":"To increase the risk of something means to make it more likely to happen.","zh":"「increase the risk of」某事，意思是令它更有可能發生。"},{"en":"Smoking can increase the risk of lung disease.","zh":"吸煙可以增加肺病風險。"},{"en":"If a risk factor increases the chance of weight gain, early prevention may help.","zh":"如果風險因素增加體重上升機會，早期預防可能有幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase describes raising probability, not guaranteeing the result.","zh":"這個短語描述提高可能性，而不是保證結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"health rather than appearance","meaning":"健康而不是外表","examples":[{"en":"The aim of losing weight should be health rather than appearance.","zh":"減重目標應是健康而不是外表。"},{"en":"Health rather than appearance means the main concern should be physical well-being, not looks.","zh":"「health rather than appearance」意思是主要關注應是身體健康，而不是外貌。"},{"en":"Exercise should help students feel stronger, rather than only make them look slimmer.","zh":"運動應幫助學生感覺更強壯，而不是只令他們看起來更瘦。"},{"en":"If weight loss focuses on health, small improvements can still be meaningful.","zh":"如果減重集中於健康，小改善仍可以有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts medical benefit with visual image.","zh":"這個短語對比醫學益處與視覺形象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"small lifestyle changes","meaning":"小幅生活方式改變","examples":[{"en":"Small lifestyle changes may not result in much weight loss.","zh":"小幅生活方式改變可能不會帶來大幅減重。"},{"en":"Small lifestyle changes are minor adjustments to daily habits, such as walking more or eating fewer snacks.","zh":"「small lifestyle changes」是對日常習慣作出小調整，例如多走路或少吃零食。"},{"en":"A student may make small lifestyle changes by sleeping earlier and drinking less soda.","zh":"學生可以透過早睡和少喝汽水作出小幅生活方式改變。"},{"en":"If the changes are too small, health may improve slightly but weight may not shift much.","zh":"如果改變太小，健康可能略有改善，但體重未必大幅改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes modest changes in daily routine.","zh":"這個短語描述日常的小幅改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"result in","meaning":"導致；帶來","examples":[{"en":"Small changes may not result in significant weight loss.","zh":"小改變可能不會帶來顯著減重。"},{"en":"To result in something means to cause it or lead to it.","zh":"「result in」某事，意思是造成它或導致它。"},{"en":"Careless planning can result in missed deadlines.","zh":"粗心規劃可能導致錯過截止日期。"},{"en":"If moderate exercise burns few calories, it may not result in major weight change.","zh":"如果溫和運動消耗卡路里少，它可能不會帶來重大體重變化。"},{"en":"The phrase connects cause with outcome.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"much weight loss","meaning":"大幅減重","examples":[{"en":"Small lifestyle changes may not produce much weight loss.","zh":"小幅生活方式改變可能不會產生大幅減重。"},{"en":"Much weight loss means a large or noticeable reduction in body weight.","zh":"「much weight loss」意思是體重有大幅或明顯下降。"},{"en":"A short walk after dinner may improve mood but may not produce much weight loss.","zh":"晚飯後短步行可能改善心情，但未必產生大幅減重。"},{"en":"If calorie intake remains high, small exercise changes may not cause major loss.","zh":"如果卡路里攝取仍高，小幅運動改變可能不會造成重大下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a substantial amount of lost weight.","zh":"這個短語描述大量體重下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"different perspectives on","meaning":"對……的不同觀點","examples":[{"en":"Different researchers support different perspectives on weight loss.","zh":"不同研究人員支持對減重的不同觀點。"},{"en":"Different perspectives on something are different ways of understanding or explaining it.","zh":"「different perspectives on」某事，是理解或解釋它的不同方式。"},{"en":"Teachers and parents may have different perspectives on homework load.","zh":"老師和家長可能對功課量有不同觀點。"},{"en":"If experts have different perspectives on obesity, the field may need combined explanations.","zh":"如果專家對肥胖有不同觀點，該領域可能需要綜合解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes varied viewpoints.","zh":"這個短語描述多樣觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the summary using words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的詞語完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill missing words in a shortened version of the passage.","zh":"「complete the summary」意思是在文章縮短版本中填入缺失詞語。"},{"en":"Students complete the summary by matching gaps with evidence in the text.","zh":"學生透過把空格與文本證據配對來完成摘要。"},{"en":"If a summary uses exact passage order, scanning becomes easier.","zh":"如果摘要按文章順序，掃讀會較容易。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"no more than one word","meaning":"不超過一個字","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose no more than one word from the passage for each answer.","zh":"考生每個答案從文章中選擇不超過一個字。"},{"en":"No more than one word means each answer must be a single word only.","zh":"「no more than one word」意思是每個答案只能是一個詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “virus”, it follows the instruction; “a virus” does not.","zh":"如果答案是 “virus”，它符合指示；“a virus” 則不符合。"},{"en":"If candidates write two words, the answer may be marked wrong even if the meaning is correct.","zh":"如果考生寫兩個詞，即使意思正確，答案也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict one-word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格的一詞限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"develop the concept of","meaning":"提出……的概念","examples":[{"en":"Dhurandhar developed the concept of infectobesity.","zh":"Dhurandhar 提出了感染性肥胖的概念。"},{"en":"To develop the concept of something means to form and explain a new idea clearly.","zh":"「develop the concept of」某事，意思是形成並清楚解釋一個新想法。"},{"en":"A teacher may develop the concept of “growth mindset” through examples and class routines.","zh":"老師可能透過例子和課堂常規提出「成長心態」的概念。"},{"en":"If a scientist develops a concept, later research can test and refine it.","zh":"如果科學家提出一個概念，後來研究可以測試和完善它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating a structured idea.","zh":"這個短語描述創造有結構的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"experiment on","meaning":"在……身上做實驗","examples":[{"en":"The researcher experimented on chickens before studying human viruses.","zh":"研究人員在研究人類病毒前，先在雞身上做實驗。"},{"en":"To experiment on something means to test ideas using that subject in research.","zh":"「experiment on」某物，意思是在研究中用該對象測試想法。"},{"en":"Students may experiment on plants to see how water affects growth.","zh":"學生可能在植物身上做實驗，以觀察水如何影響生長。"},{"en":"If researchers experiment on animals, they can observe biological effects under controlled conditions.","zh":"如果研究人員在動物身上做實驗，就能在受控條件下觀察生物效果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes testing through scientific study.","zh":"這個短語描述透過科學研究進行測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"identify a new virus","meaning":"識別出一種新病毒","examples":[{"en":"After moving to the United States, he identified a new virus.","zh":"移居美國後，他識別出一種新病毒。"},{"en":"To identify a new virus means to recognise and name a virus that was not previously known in that context.","zh":"「identify a new virus」意思是辨認並命名一種在該語境中以前未知的病毒。"},{"en":"Scientists may identify a new virus by analysing samples from infected patients.","zh":"科學家可能透過分析受感染病人的樣本來識別出新病毒。"},{"en":"If a new virus is identified, researchers can study how it spreads and what it does.","zh":"如果新病毒被識別出來，研究人員就能研究它如何傳播和造成甚麼影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes scientific recognition of a virus.","zh":"這個短語描述科學上辨認病毒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"induce weight gain","meaning":"引發體重增加","examples":[{"en":"The virus appeared to induce weight gain in animals.","zh":"該病毒似乎會在動物身上引發體重增加。"},{"en":"To induce weight gain means to cause or trigger an increase in body weight.","zh":"「induce weight gain」意思是造成或引發體重增加。"},{"en":"Some medicines may induce weight gain as a side effect.","zh":"有些藥物可能以副作用形式引發體重增加。"},{"en":"If a virus induces weight gain, infection may be part of the cause.","zh":"如果病毒引發體重增加，感染可能是成因之一。"},{"en":"The phrase describes causing weight to increase.","zh":"這個短語描述造成體重上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"currently no way to","meaning":"目前沒有方法去","examples":[{"en":"There is currently no way to eliminate the virus.","zh":"目前沒有方法消除該病毒。"},{"en":"Currently no way to do something means no method exists at the present time.","zh":"「currently no way to」做某事，意思是目前沒有方法做到。"},{"en":"There is currently no way to predict every student’s exam result perfectly.","zh":"目前沒有方法完全準確預測每位學生的考試成績。"},{"en":"If there is currently no way to remove a virus, prevention and research become important.","zh":"如果目前沒有方法清除病毒，預防和研究就變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes present limitation.","zh":"這個短語描述當前限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"eliminate the virus","meaning":"消除病毒","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have not yet found a way to eliminate the virus.","zh":"研究人員尚未找到消除該病毒的方法。"},{"en":"To eliminate the virus means to remove, destroy, or stop it completely.","zh":"「eliminate the virus」意思是完全移除、摧毀或阻止該病毒。"},{"en":"Hospitals use cleaning procedures to eliminate viruses from surfaces.","zh":"醫院使用清潔程序來消除表面病毒。"},{"en":"If scientists cannot eliminate a virus, they may try to block its harmful effects.","zh":"如果科學家不能消除病毒，他們可能嘗試阻截其有害效果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes complete removal or destruction of a virus.","zh":"這個短語描述完全移除或摧毀病毒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"be isolated and blocked","meaning":"被分離並阻截","examples":[{"en":"A gene can be isolated and blocked to reduce the virus’s effects.","zh":"一個基因可以被分離並阻截，以減低病毒影響。"},{"en":"To be isolated and blocked means to be identified separately and then prevented from working.","zh":"「be isolated and blocked」意思是先被單獨識別出來，然後被阻止運作。"},{"en":"Scientists may isolate and block a harmful signal to see whether symptoms improve.","zh":"科學家可能分離並阻截有害訊號，以觀察症狀是否改善。"},{"en":"If a gene is isolated and blocked, researchers can test its role in disease.","zh":"如果基因被分離並阻截，研究人員就能測試它在疾病中的角色。"},{"en":"The phrase describes two research steps: finding and stopping.","zh":"這個短語描述兩個研究步驟：找出和停止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"reduce its effects","meaning":"減低其影響","examples":[{"en":"Blocking the gene may reduce the virus’s effects.","zh":"阻截該基因可能減低病毒的影響。"},{"en":"To reduce its effects means to make its impact weaker or less serious.","zh":"「reduce its effects」意思是令其影響較弱或較不嚴重。"},{"en":"Wearing sunscreen can reduce the sun’s effects on the skin.","zh":"塗防曬可以減低陽光對皮膚的影響。"},{"en":"If a gene is blocked, the virus may still exist but cause less harm.","zh":"如果基因被阻截，病毒可能仍存在，但造成較少傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weakening an impact rather than removing the cause completely.","zh":"這個短語描述削弱影響，而不是完全移除原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"aim to develop","meaning":"旨在研發","examples":[{"en":"The doctor aims to develop a vaccine.","zh":"這位醫生旨在研發疫苗。"},{"en":"To aim to develop something means to plan or intend to create it through work and research.","zh":"「aim to develop」某物，意思是計劃或打算透過工作和研究創造它。"},{"en":"A school may aim to develop a reading programme for weaker students.","zh":"學校可能旨在為較弱學生研發閱讀計劃。"},{"en":"If researchers aim to develop a vaccine, they need evidence, testing, and safety checks.","zh":"如果研究人員旨在研發疫苗，他們需要證據、測試和安全檢查。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a planned goal.","zh":"這個短語描述有計劃的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"combat the virus","meaning":"對抗病毒","examples":[{"en":"A vaccine could help combat the virus.","zh":"疫苗可以幫助對抗病毒。"},{"en":"To combat the virus means to fight against it or reduce its ability to cause harm.","zh":"「combat the virus」意思是對抗病毒，或減低它造成傷害的能力。"},{"en":"Doctors combat viruses through vaccination, hygiene, treatment, and public education.","zh":"醫生透過疫苗、衛生、治療和公共教育對抗病毒。"},{"en":"If a vaccine helps the body recognise a virus, it can combat infection more effectively.","zh":"如果疫苗幫助身體識別病毒，它就能更有效對抗感染。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active effort against a harmful virus.","zh":"這個短語描述主動對抗有害病毒的努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 45 - Stealth Forces in weight Loss.pdf","sourcePage":24}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 46":[{"front":"Global Warming in New Zealand","meaning":"新西蘭的全球暖化","examples":[{"en":"Global warming in New Zealand affects farming, glaciers, coastlines and wildlife.","zh":"新西蘭的全球暖化影響農業、冰川、海岸線和野生動物。"},{"en":"Global warming in New Zealand means the rise in temperature and climate-related changes affecting the country.","zh":"新西蘭的全球暖化，指影響該國的氣溫上升和氣候相關變化。"},{"en":"A student may study global warming in New Zealand by looking at farms, glaciers, beaches, and animals.","zh":"學生可以透過研究農場、冰川、海灘和動物來了解新西蘭的全球暖化。"},{"en":"If temperatures continue to rise, global warming in New Zealand may affect both the economy and nature.","zh":"如果氣溫持續上升，新西蘭的全球暖化可能影響經濟和自然環境。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how a worldwide climate problem appears in one specific country.","zh":"這個短語強調全球氣候問題如何出現在一個特定國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"environmentalists","meaning":"環保人士","examples":[{"en":"Many environmentalists believe that the world is getting warmer.","zh":"許多環保人士相信世界正在變暖。"},{"en":"Environmentalists are people who care about protecting nature and reducing damage to the environment.","zh":"環保人士，是關心保護自然和減少環境破壞的人。"},{"en":"Environmentalists may organise beach clean-ups, tree planting, or campaigns against pollution.","zh":"環保人士可能組織清潔海灘、植樹或反污染運動。"},{"en":"If environmentalists gather evidence about climate change, they may push governments to act.","zh":"如果環保人士收集氣候變化證據，他們可能推動政府行動。"},{"en":"The word refers to people concerned with the health of the natural world.","zh":"這個詞指關心自然世界健康的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"seem to be getting warmer","meaning":"似乎正在變暖","examples":[{"en":"The world seems to be getting warmer.","zh":"世界似乎正在變暖。"},{"en":"To seem to be getting warmer means to appear to be gradually increasing in temperature.","zh":"似乎正在變暖，指看起來氣溫正逐漸上升。"},{"en":"A city may seem to be getting warmer if winters become shorter and summers feel longer.","zh":"如果一個城市冬天變短、夏天感覺更長，它可能似乎正在變暖。"},{"en":"If the world keeps getting warmer, farms, coastlines, and wildlife may face new risks.","zh":"如果世界持續變暖，農場、海岸線和野生動物可能面臨新風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an observed trend, not one single hot day.","zh":"這個短語描述觀察到的趨勢，而不是單一炎熱日子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one of the countries nearest to","meaning":"最接近……的國家之一","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand is one of the countries nearest to the South Polar Region.","zh":"新西蘭是最接近南極地區的國家之一。"},{"en":"One of the countries nearest to a place means among the countries located closest to that area.","zh":"最接近某地的國家之一，指位於最靠近該地區的國家之中。"},{"en":"Japan is one of the countries nearest to Korea, so travel between them can be short.","zh":"日本是最接近韓國的國家之一，因此兩地之間旅程可以很短。"},{"en":"If a country is near a polar region, changes in polar climate may matter to it.","zh":"如果一個國家接近極地地區，極地氣候變化可能對它重要。"},{"en":"The phrase compares distance between countries and a specific region.","zh":"這個短語比較國家與特定地區之間的距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the South Polar Region","meaning":"南極地區","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand is located near the South Polar Region.","zh":"新西蘭位於南極地區附近。"},{"en":"The South Polar Region is the area around the South Pole, including Antarctica and nearby oceans.","zh":"南極地區，是南極點周圍的區域，包括南極洲和附近海洋。"},{"en":"Scientists travel to the South Polar Region to study ice, climate, and wildlife.","zh":"科學家前往南極地區研究冰、氣候和野生動物。"},{"en":"If the South Polar Region warms quickly, nearby countries may notice climate effects.","zh":"如果南極地區迅速變暖，附近國家可能會察覺氣候影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the polar area at the southern end of the Earth.","zh":"這個短語指地球南端的極地區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"maintain an upward trend","meaning":"維持上升趨勢","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand has maintained an upward trend in its average temperature.","zh":"新西蘭平均氣溫一直維持上升趨勢。"},{"en":"To maintain an upward trend means to continue rising over time.","zh":"維持上升趨勢，指隨時間持續上升。"},{"en":"A student’s marks maintain an upward trend if each test result is higher than the last.","zh":"如果學生每次測驗分數都比上一次高，成績就是維持上升趨勢。"},{"en":"If temperature maintains an upward trend, people can expect more climate pressure in future.","zh":"如果氣溫維持上升趨勢，人們可以預期未來有更多氣候壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a continuing increase, not a temporary jump.","zh":"這個短語描述持續增加，而不是暫時跳升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"average temperature","meaning":"平均氣溫","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand’s average temperature has risen in recent years.","zh":"新西蘭近年的平均氣溫已經上升。"},{"en":"Average temperature is the general temperature calculated from many temperature readings.","zh":"平均氣溫，是由許多氣溫讀數計算出來的一般氣溫。"},{"en":"A city’s average temperature may be higher in July than in January.","zh":"一個城市七月的平均氣溫可能高於一月。"},{"en":"If average temperature rises, crops, water supply, and human comfort may be affected.","zh":"如果平均氣溫上升，農作物、水供應和人類舒適度可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an overall climate measure, not the temperature at one moment.","zh":"這個短語指整體氣候量度，而不是某一刻的氣溫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rise by 4°C","meaning":"上升攝氏四度","examples":[{"en":"The temperature in New Zealand may rise by 4°C in the next century.","zh":"新西蘭氣溫在下一個世紀可能上升攝氏四度。"},{"en":"To rise by 4°C means to increase by four degrees Celsius.","zh":"上升攝氏四度，指增加四個攝氏度。"},{"en":"If a classroom temperature rises by 4°C, students may feel much hotter.","zh":"如果課室氣溫上升攝氏四度，學生可能會覺得熱很多。"},{"en":"If a country’s average temperature rises by 4°C, farming and ecosystems may change seriously.","zh":"如果一個國家的平均氣溫上升攝氏四度，農業和生態系統可能嚴重改變。"},{"en":"The phrase states the amount of increase.","zh":"這個短語說明升幅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the next century","meaning":"在下一個世紀","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand’s temperature may rise by 4°C in the next century.","zh":"新西蘭氣溫在下一個世紀可能上升攝氏四度。"},{"en":"In the next century means during the next one hundred years.","zh":"在下一個世紀，指在未來一百年之內。"},{"en":"A city may need new transport plans in the next century as its population grows.","zh":"隨着人口增長，一個城市在下一個世紀可能需要新的交通規劃。"},{"en":"If climate effects are expected in the next century, governments must plan early.","zh":"如果氣候影響預計在下一個世紀出現，政府就必須及早規劃。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a long future time period.","zh":"這個短語指一段很長的未來時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the polar region","meaning":"極地地區","examples":[{"en":"The temperature in the polar region may rise by more than 6°C.","zh":"極地地區的氣溫可能上升超過攝氏六度。"},{"en":"The polar region is the area around the North Pole or South Pole.","zh":"極地地區，是北極或南極周圍的區域。"},{"en":"Animals in the polar region often depend on ice and cold conditions.","zh":"極地地區的動物常依賴冰和寒冷環境。"},{"en":"If the polar region warms quickly, ice loss may affect sea levels and wildlife.","zh":"如果極地地區迅速變暖，冰量流失可能影響海平面和野生動物。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to extremely cold regions near the poles.","zh":"這個短語指靠近兩極的極寒地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lower projected increase","meaning":"較低的預計升幅","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand’s lower projected increase is due to the surrounding ocean.","zh":"新西蘭較低的預計升幅是由於周邊海洋。"},{"en":"A lower projected increase is a predicted rise that is smaller than another predicted rise.","zh":"較低的預計升幅，是比另一個預測升幅更小的預測上升。"},{"en":"A school may have a lower projected increase in enrolment if fewer families move nearby.","zh":"如果較少家庭搬到附近，學校收生的預計增幅可能較低。"},{"en":"If surrounding oceans cool the land, the projected temperature rise may be lower.","zh":"如果周邊海洋冷卻陸地，預計氣溫升幅可能較低。"},{"en":"The phrase compares predicted growth or rise.","zh":"這個短語比較預測中的增長或上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be due to","meaning":"由於；因……所致","examples":[{"en":"The lower projected increase is due to the surrounding ocean.","zh":"較低的預計升幅是由於周邊海洋。"},{"en":"To be due to something means to be caused by it.","zh":"由於某事，指由它造成。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be due to lack of sleep.","zh":"學生疲倦可能是由於睡眠不足。"},{"en":"If a temperature change is due to ocean influence, geography helps explain the pattern.","zh":"如果氣溫變化是由海洋影響所致，地理就有助解釋該模式。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the cause of a result.","zh":"這個短語引入結果的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"surrounding ocean","meaning":"周邊海洋","examples":[{"en":"The surrounding ocean helps limit New Zealand’s temperature rise.","zh":"周邊海洋有助限制新西蘭的氣溫上升。"},{"en":"The surrounding ocean is the sea around a land area or country.","zh":"周邊海洋，是陸地或國家周圍的海域。"},{"en":"An island’s surrounding ocean can affect its weather and transport.","zh":"島嶼的周邊海洋可以影響其天氣和交通。"},{"en":"If the surrounding ocean absorbs heat, nearby land may warm more slowly.","zh":"如果周邊海洋吸收熱量，附近陸地可能升溫較慢。"},{"en":"The phrase connects geography with climate influence.","zh":"這個短語把地理與氣候影響連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"act like","meaning":"發揮像……一樣的作用","examples":[{"en":"The ocean acts like an air conditioner for New Zealand.","zh":"海洋對新西蘭發揮像冷氣機一樣的作用。"},{"en":"To act like something means to function in a similar way to it.","zh":"發揮像某物一樣的作用，指以與它相似的方式運作。"},{"en":"A thick curtain can act like a blanket by keeping heat inside a room.","zh":"厚窗簾可以像毛氈一樣，把熱力留在房間內。"},{"en":"If the ocean acts like an air conditioner, it helps cool or moderate nearby land.","zh":"如果海洋像冷氣機一樣運作，它有助冷卻或調節附近陸地。"},{"en":"The phrase explains a function through comparison.","zh":"這個短語透過比較解釋功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an air conditioner","meaning":"冷氣機","examples":[{"en":"The surrounding ocean acts like an air conditioner.","zh":"周邊海洋發揮像冷氣機一樣的作用。"},{"en":"An air conditioner is a machine that cools indoor air.","zh":"冷氣機，是冷卻室內空氣的機器。"},{"en":"Offices often use an air conditioner during hot summer afternoons.","zh":"辦公室在炎熱夏日下午常使用冷氣機。"},{"en":"If the ocean acts like an air conditioner, it reduces extreme heat near the coast.","zh":"如果海洋像冷氣機一樣運作，它會減少沿岸極端高溫。"},{"en":"The phrase is used here as a simple comparison for cooling effect.","zh":"這個短語在此用作冷卻效果的簡單比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"comparatively fortunate","meaning":"相對幸運","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand is comparatively fortunate because of the surrounding ocean.","zh":"新西蘭因周邊海洋而相對幸運。"},{"en":"Comparatively fortunate means luckier or in a better position than others when compared.","zh":"相對幸運，指與其他人或地方相比更幸運或處境較好。"},{"en":"A student with a quiet study space is comparatively fortunate before exams.","zh":"考試前有安靜溫習空間的學生相對幸運。"},{"en":"If a country warms more slowly than polar regions, it may be comparatively fortunate.","zh":"如果一個國家比極地地區升溫較慢，它可能相對幸運。"},{"en":"The phrase describes relative advantage, not complete safety.","zh":"這個短語描述相對優勢，而不是完全安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"scientifically speaking","meaning":"從科學角度來說","examples":[{"en":"Scientifically speaking, this phenomenon is linked to SAM.","zh":"從科學角度來說，這個現象與 SAM 有關。"},{"en":"Scientifically speaking means from a scientific point of view or according to scientific explanation.","zh":"從科學角度來說，指從科學觀點或根據科學解釋而言。"},{"en":"Scientifically speaking, sleep helps memory because the brain processes information during rest.","zh":"從科學角度來說，睡眠有助記憶，因為大腦在休息時處理資訊。"},{"en":"If a claim is explained scientifically, it should be supported by evidence and mechanisms.","zh":"如果一個主張以科學方式解釋，就應由證據和機制支持。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a more technical explanation.","zh":"這個短語引入更技術性的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"temperature phenomenon","meaning":"氣溫現象","examples":[{"en":"This temperature phenomenon is associated with SAM.","zh":"這個氣溫現象與 SAM 有關。"},{"en":"A temperature phenomenon is an observable pattern or event involving temperature.","zh":"氣溫現象，是涉及氣溫的可觀察模式或事件。"},{"en":"A heatwave is a temperature phenomenon that can affect health and electricity use.","zh":"熱浪是一種氣溫現象，會影響健康和用電量。"},{"en":"If a temperature phenomenon repeats over years, scientists may study its causes.","zh":"如果氣溫現象多年重複，科學家可能研究其原因。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a pattern in temperature behaviour.","zh":"這個短語指氣溫變化中的模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be associated with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The temperature phenomenon is associated with SAM.","zh":"這個氣溫現象與 SAM 有關。"},{"en":"To be associated with something means to be connected with it in some way.","zh":"與某事有關，指以某種方式與它連繫。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is often associated with lower concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足常與課堂專注力較低有關。"},{"en":"If drought is associated with wind changes, weather patterns may explain crop problems.","zh":"如果乾旱與風向變化有關，天氣模式可能解釋農作物問題。"},{"en":"The phrase shows connection, not always direct cause.","zh":"這個短語顯示關聯，但不一定是直接原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"researchers call","meaning":"研究人員稱之為","examples":[{"en":"Researchers call this pattern the Southern Annular Mode.","zh":"研究人員稱這種模式為南半球環狀模態。"},{"en":"Researchers call something a name when they use that term to identify or describe it.","zh":"研究人員稱某物為某名稱，指他們使用該術語來識別或描述它。"},{"en":"Doctors call high blood pressure hypertension.","zh":"醫生稱高血壓為 hypertension。"},{"en":"If researchers give a pattern a name, it becomes easier to discuss and study.","zh":"如果研究人員給某模式命名，它就更容易被討論和研究。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a technical name used by experts.","zh":"這個短語引入專家使用的技術名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Southern Annular Mode","meaning":"南半球環狀模態","examples":[{"en":"The Southern Annular Mode affects winds around New Zealand and Antarctica.","zh":"南半球環狀模態影響新西蘭和南極洲周圍的風。"},{"en":"The Southern Annular Mode is a climate pattern involving a belt of winds in the Southern Hemisphere.","zh":"南半球環狀模態，是涉及南半球風帶的氣候模式。"},{"en":"A geography lesson may explain the Southern Annular Mode when discussing New Zealand’s rainfall.","zh":"地理課討論新西蘭降雨時，可能解釋南半球環狀模態。"},{"en":"If the Southern Annular Mode changes, rainfall and moisture patterns may also change.","zh":"如果南半球環狀模態改變，降雨和水分模式也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase names a scientific climate pattern.","zh":"這個短語命名一種科學氣候模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"指的是","examples":[{"en":"SAM refers to the wind belt around the Southern Ocean.","zh":"SAM 指的是環繞南大洋的風帶。"},{"en":"To refer to something means to mean, describe, or point to it.","zh":"指的是某物，意思是表示、描述或指向該物。"},{"en":"In grammar, “subject” refers to the person or thing doing the action.","zh":"在文法中，“subject” 指的是做出動作的人或物。"},{"en":"If a term refers to a wind belt, students should not confuse it with one single storm.","zh":"如果某術語指的是風帶，學生不應把它誤解成單一風暴。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what a word or name means.","zh":"這個短語解釋某個詞或名稱的意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"wind belt","meaning":"風帶","examples":[{"en":"SAM refers to the wind belt that circles the Southern Ocean.","zh":"SAM 指的是環繞南大洋的風帶。"},{"en":"A wind belt is a large band of moving air that follows a regular path around the Earth.","zh":"風帶，是沿固定路徑環繞地球移動的大型空氣帶。"},{"en":"Sailors may study wind belts to understand ocean travel routes.","zh":"水手可能研究風帶，以了解海上航行路線。"},{"en":"If a wind belt shifts, rainfall and temperature patterns may change.","zh":"如果風帶移動，降雨和氣溫模式可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broad pattern of winds.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛的風向模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"circle the Southern Ocean","meaning":"環繞南大洋","examples":[{"en":"The wind belt circles the Southern Ocean.","zh":"風帶環繞南大洋。"},{"en":"To circle the Southern Ocean means to go around it in a ring-like path.","zh":"環繞南大洋，指以像圓環般的路徑圍繞它。"},{"en":"A road may circle a lake, allowing drivers to see it from every side.","zh":"一條道路可能環繞湖泊，讓司機從各方向看見它。"},{"en":"If winds circle an ocean, they can influence weather across nearby regions.","zh":"如果風環繞一片海洋，它們可以影響附近地區的天氣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement around a large area.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞大型區域的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Southern Ocean","meaning":"南大洋","examples":[{"en":"The Southern Ocean surrounds Antarctica.","zh":"南大洋圍繞南極洲。"},{"en":"The Southern Ocean is the ocean around Antarctica in the far south of the Earth.","zh":"南大洋，是位於地球最南端、圍繞南極洲的海洋。"},{"en":"Scientists study the Southern Ocean because it affects global climate and marine life.","zh":"科學家研究南大洋，因為它影響全球氣候和海洋生物。"},{"en":"If winds change over the Southern Ocean, countries nearby may experience rainfall changes.","zh":"如果南大洋上空的風改變，附近國家可能經歷降雨變化。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major ocean region near Antarctica.","zh":"這個短語命名靠近南極洲的重要海洋區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Antarctica","meaning":"南極洲","examples":[{"en":"The wind belt circles the ocean around New Zealand and Antarctica.","zh":"風帶環繞新西蘭和南極洲周圍的海洋。"},{"en":"Antarctica is the icy continent around the South Pole.","zh":"南極洲，是位於南極點周圍的冰封大陸。"},{"en":"Researchers travel to Antarctica to study ice sheets, penguins, and climate records.","zh":"研究人員前往南極洲研究冰蓋、企鵝和氣候記錄。"},{"en":"If Antarctica loses ice, sea levels around the world may be affected.","zh":"如果南極洲流失冰量，全球海平面都可能受影響。"},{"en":"The word refers to the southern polar continent.","zh":"這個詞指地球南方的極地大陸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"recent work has revealed that","meaning":"近期研究顯示","examples":[{"en":"Recent work has revealed that SAM affects rainfall patterns.","zh":"近期研究顯示 SAM 影響降雨模式。"},{"en":"Recent work has revealed that means new research has shown something previously less clear.","zh":"近期研究顯示，指新研究揭示了先前較不清楚的事情。"},{"en":"Recent work has revealed that students remember vocabulary better when examples are concrete.","zh":"近期研究顯示，例子具體時學生更容易記住詞彙。"},{"en":"If recent work reveals a climate link, older explanations may need updating.","zh":"如果近期研究揭示氣候關聯，舊解釋可能需要更新。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a new research finding.","zh":"這個短語引入新的研究發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"changes in","meaning":"……的變化","examples":[{"en":"Changes in SAM have affected New Zealand’s climate.","zh":"SAM 的變化已影響新西蘭氣候。"},{"en":"Changes in something are differences or shifts in its condition, pattern, or behaviour.","zh":"某事的變化，是其狀況、模式或行為上的差異或轉變。"},{"en":"Changes in school rules can affect how students use phones.","zh":"校規的變化可以影響學生如何使用手機。"},{"en":"If changes in wind patterns occur, rainfall and drought may also change.","zh":"如果風向模式出現變化，降雨和乾旱也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the area where change happens.","zh":"這個短語指出變化發生的範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"result in a reduction in","meaning":"導致……減少","examples":[{"en":"Changes in SAM have resulted in a reduction in summer moisture.","zh":"SAM 的變化導致夏季水分減少。"},{"en":"To result in a reduction in something means to cause it to become smaller or less.","zh":"導致某物減少，指造成它變小或變少。"},{"en":"Cutting bus services may result in a reduction in transport options for students.","zh":"削減巴士服務可能導致學生交通選擇減少。"},{"en":"If winds carry less moisture, crops may receive less water during hot months.","zh":"如果風帶來較少水分，農作物在炎熱月份可能得到較少水。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a cause leading to a decrease.","zh":"這個短語顯示原因導致下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"moisture carried by winds","meaning":"由風帶來的水分","examples":[{"en":"There is less moisture carried by winds during summer.","zh":"夏季由風帶來的水分較少。"},{"en":"Moisture carried by winds is water vapour or dampness transported through the air.","zh":"由風帶來的水分，是透過空氣運送的水蒸氣或濕氣。"},{"en":"Coastal winds may bring moisture that makes laundry dry more slowly.","zh":"海岸風可能帶來水分，令衣物乾得較慢。"},{"en":"If winds carry less moisture, the soil may dry out faster.","zh":"如果風帶來較少水分，土壤可能更快變乾。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how air movement can transport water.","zh":"這個短語解釋空氣流動如何運送水分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"more rainfall in other seasons","meaning":"其他季節更多降雨","examples":[{"en":"SAM may bring more rainfall in other seasons.","zh":"SAM 可能在其他季節帶來更多降雨。"},{"en":"More rainfall in other seasons means extra rain outside the season being discussed.","zh":"其他季節更多降雨，指正在討論的季節之外有額外雨量。"},{"en":"A region may have dry summers but more rainfall in other seasons such as autumn or winter.","zh":"一個地區可能夏季乾旱，但在秋季或冬季等其他季節有更多降雨。"},{"en":"If rain comes after crops need it most, it may not prevent harvest damage.","zh":"如果雨在農作物最需要水之後才來，可能無法防止收成受損。"},{"en":"The phrase compares rainfall across seasons.","zh":"這個短語比較不同季節的降雨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"may turn out to be","meaning":"可能最終會是","examples":[{"en":"A bigger problem may turn out to be severe agricultural droughts.","zh":"更大的問題可能最終會是嚴重農業乾旱。"},{"en":"May turn out to be means may eventually prove to be true or important.","zh":"可能最終會是，指最終可能證明是真實或重要的事情。"},{"en":"A small leak may turn out to be a serious plumbing problem.","zh":"小漏水可能最終會是嚴重水管問題。"},{"en":"If drought becomes worse than expected, it may turn out to be the main climate danger for farms.","zh":"如果乾旱比預期更嚴重，它可能最終會成為農場的主要氣候危險。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a possible final result after time passes.","zh":"這個短語顯示時間過去後可能出現的最終結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"severe agricultural droughts","meaning":"嚴重農業乾旱","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand may face more severe agricultural droughts.","zh":"新西蘭可能面對更嚴重的農業乾旱。"},{"en":"Severe agricultural droughts are serious periods of dry weather that harm farming.","zh":"嚴重農業乾旱，是傷害農業的嚴重乾燥天氣時期。"},{"en":"A severe agricultural drought can leave fields cracked and crops unable to grow.","zh":"嚴重農業乾旱可以令田地龜裂，農作物無法生長。"},{"en":"If droughts become severe, farmers may lose income and food supply may fall.","zh":"如果乾旱變得嚴重，農民可能失去收入，食物供應也可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to droughts judged by their impact on agriculture.","zh":"這個短語指按其對農業影響來判斷的乾旱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"increased water loss","meaning":"水分流失增加","examples":[{"en":"Increased water loss from the soil can damage harvests.","zh":"土壤水分流失增加會損害收成。"},{"en":"Increased water loss means more water is being lost than before.","zh":"水分流失增加，指比以前失去更多水分。"},{"en":"A plant pot placed in strong sun may experience increased water loss.","zh":"放在強烈陽光下的盆栽可能出現水分流失增加。"},{"en":"If soil loses more water, plants may not have enough moisture to grow well.","zh":"如果土壤失去更多水分，植物可能沒有足夠濕氣良好生長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a rise in water disappearing from a system.","zh":"這個短語描述水分從某系統中消失的情況增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"water loss from the soil","meaning":"土壤水分流失","examples":[{"en":"Water loss from the soil may lead to poorer harvests.","zh":"土壤水分流失可能導致收成較差。"},{"en":"Water loss from the soil means moisture leaving the ground through heat, wind, or plant use.","zh":"土壤水分流失，指水分因高溫、風或植物吸收而離開地面。"},{"en":"Garden soil can suffer water loss when it is exposed to strong sun all day.","zh":"花園土壤整天暴露在強烈陽光下時，可能出現水分流失。"},{"en":"If soil loses water during the growing season, crops may produce less food.","zh":"如果土壤在生長季節流失水分，農作物可能產出較少食物。"},{"en":"The phrase connects dry ground with plant stress.","zh":"這個短語把乾燥土地與植物壓力連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"result in poorer harvests","meaning":"導致收成較差","examples":[{"en":"Dry soil can result in poorer harvests.","zh":"乾燥土壤可以導致收成較差。"},{"en":"To result in poorer harvests means to cause farmers to grow or collect fewer crops.","zh":"導致收成較差，指造成農民種出或收集到較少農作物。"},{"en":"A lack of rain can result in poorer harvests for rice farmers.","zh":"缺雨可以導致稻農收成較差。"},{"en":"If harvests become poorer, food prices may rise and farmers may earn less.","zh":"如果收成變差，食物價格可能上升，農民收入可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase shows farming loss as an outcome.","zh":"這個短語顯示農業損失作為結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"winter rainfall","meaning":"冬季降雨","examples":[{"en":"Winter rainfall may arrive too late to save crops.","zh":"冬季降雨可能來得太遲而無法挽救農作物。"},{"en":"Winter rainfall is rain that falls during the winter season.","zh":"冬季降雨，是在冬季降下的雨。"},{"en":"A city may depend on winter rainfall to refill reservoirs before summer.","zh":"一個城市可能依靠冬季降雨在夏季前補充水庫。"},{"en":"If crops need water in spring or summer, winter rainfall may not help enough.","zh":"如果農作物在春季或夏季需要水，冬季降雨可能幫助不夠。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies rain by season.","zh":"這個短語按季節指出降雨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"arrive too late to save","meaning":"來得太遲而無法挽救","examples":[{"en":"Winter rainfall may arrive too late to save the harvests.","zh":"冬季降雨可能來得太遲而無法挽救收成。"},{"en":"To arrive too late to save something means to come after the time when help is still useful.","zh":"來得太遲而無法挽救某事，指在幫助仍有效的時間之後才到來。"},{"en":"Medicine may arrive too late to save a patient if treatment is delayed for too long.","zh":"如果治療延誤太久，藥物可能來得太遲而無法挽救病人。"},{"en":"If rain arrives after crops have died, it cannot repair the lost harvest.","zh":"如果雨在農作物死亡後才來，就不能修復失去的收成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes help that comes after the critical moment.","zh":"這個短語描述在關鍵時刻之後才到來的幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"among all the problems caused by","meaning":"在由……造成的所有問題之中","examples":[{"en":"Among all the problems caused by drought, moisture deficit is the most serious.","zh":"在由乾旱造成的所有問題之中，水分虧缺是最嚴重的。"},{"en":"Among all the problems caused by something means compared with all the difficulties that it creates.","zh":"在由某事造成的所有問題之中，指與它造成的所有困難相比。"},{"en":"Among all the problems caused by poor sleep, low concentration may be the most obvious in class.","zh":"在由睡眠不足造成的所有問題之中，專注力低可能在課堂中最明顯。"},{"en":"If drought creates many problems, identifying the most serious one helps planning.","zh":"如果乾旱造成許多問題，找出最嚴重的一個有助規劃。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces comparison within a group of effects.","zh":"這個短語引入在一組影響中的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"drought","meaning":"乾旱；旱災","examples":[{"en":"Drought can cause serious problems for crops.","zh":"乾旱會對農作物造成嚴重問題。"},{"en":"Drought is a long period with little or no rain, causing water shortage.","zh":"乾旱，是長時間少雨或無雨，導致缺水的情況。"},{"en":"A village may face drought when wells dry up and fields turn brown.","zh":"當水井乾涸、田地變黃，村莊可能面臨旱災。"},{"en":"If drought lasts through the growing season, farmers may lose much of their harvest.","zh":"如果乾旱持續整個生長季節，農民可能失去大量收成。"},{"en":"The word describes a serious lack of water in the environment.","zh":"這個詞描述環境中嚴重缺水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"moisture deficit","meaning":"水分虧缺","examples":[{"en":"Moisture deficit is the most serious problem caused by drought.","zh":"水分虧缺是乾旱造成的最嚴重問題。"},{"en":"Moisture deficit means there is not enough water available for plants compared with what they need.","zh":"水分虧缺，指與植物所需相比，可用水分不足。"},{"en":"A garden has a moisture deficit when soil is dry and leaves begin to wilt.","zh":"當土壤乾燥、葉子開始枯萎，花園就有水分虧缺。"},{"en":"If moisture deficit occurs during a key growth stage, crop yield may fall sharply.","zh":"如果水分虧缺發生在關鍵生長階段，農作物產量可能大幅下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shortage of useful water for plants.","zh":"這個短語描述植物可用水分不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the gap between","meaning":"……之間的差距","examples":[{"en":"Moisture deficit is the gap between the water plants need and the water available.","zh":"水分虧缺是植物所需水分與可用水分之間的差距。"},{"en":"The gap between two things is the difference or distance between them.","zh":"兩者之間的差距，是它們之間的差異或距離。"},{"en":"The gap between a student’s current score and target score shows how much improvement is needed.","zh":"學生目前分數與目標分數之間的差距，顯示需要改善多少。"},{"en":"If the gap between needed water and available water grows, crops suffer more stress.","zh":"如果所需水分與可用水分之間的差距擴大，農作物承受更大壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase compares two amounts or situations.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個數量或情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the water plants need","meaning":"植物所需的水分","examples":[{"en":"Moisture deficit measures the gap between the water plants need and the water available.","zh":"水分虧缺量度植物所需水分與可用水分之間的差距。"},{"en":"The water plants need means the amount of water required for healthy growth.","zh":"植物所需的水分，指植物健康生長所需要的水量。"},{"en":"Tomato plants may need more water during hot weather than during cool weather.","zh":"番茄植物在炎熱天氣可能比涼快天氣需要更多水。"},{"en":"If the soil cannot provide the water plants need, leaves may wilt and fruit may be smaller.","zh":"如果土壤不能提供植物所需水分，葉子可能枯萎，果實可能較小。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on plant demand for water.","zh":"這個短語強調植物對水的需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"growing season","meaning":"生長季節","examples":[{"en":"Plants need enough water during the growing season.","zh":"植物在生長季節需要足夠水分。"},{"en":"The growing season is the period of the year when crops or plants actively grow.","zh":"生長季節，是一年中農作物或植物活躍生長的時期。"},{"en":"Farmers often work hardest during the growing season because crops need care every day.","zh":"農民在生長季節通常最忙，因為農作物每天都需要照顧。"},{"en":"If drought happens during the growing season, harvests may be seriously reduced.","zh":"如果乾旱發生在生長季節，收成可能嚴重減少。"},{"en":"The phrase links plant growth with a particular time of year.","zh":"這個短語把植物生長與一年中特定時間連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"available from the soil","meaning":"可從土壤獲得的","examples":[{"en":"Moisture deficit compares plant needs with water available from the soil.","zh":"水分虧缺比較植物需要與可從土壤獲得的水分。"},{"en":"Available from the soil means obtainable by plants from the ground around their roots.","zh":"可從土壤獲得的，指植物可以從根部周圍地面取得的。"},{"en":"Nutrients available from the soil help vegetables grow stronger.","zh":"可從土壤獲得的營養有助蔬菜長得更強壯。"},{"en":"If little water is available from the soil, plants may stop growing even if rain comes later.","zh":"如果可從土壤獲得的水很少，即使之後下雨，植物也可能停止生長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what the soil can supply.","zh":"這個短語描述土壤能供應甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"measures of","meaning":"……的量度指標","examples":[{"en":"Measures of moisture deficit were at their highest since the 1970s.","zh":"水分虧缺的量度指標達到自二十世紀七十年代以來最高。"},{"en":"Measures of something are ways of calculating, recording, or showing its level.","zh":"某事的量度指標，是計算、記錄或顯示其水平的方法。"},{"en":"Test scores are measures of student performance, but they do not show everything.","zh":"測驗分數是學生表現的量度指標，但不能顯示一切。"},{"en":"If measures of drought rise, officials may warn farmers earlier.","zh":"如果乾旱量度指標上升，官員可能更早警告農民。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to indicators used to assess a condition.","zh":"這個短語指用來評估狀況的指標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at their highest since","meaning":"達到自……以來最高","examples":[{"en":"Moisture deficit levels were at their highest since the 1970s.","zh":"水分虧缺水平達到自二十世紀七十年代以來最高。"},{"en":"At their highest since a time means reaching the greatest level recorded after that time.","zh":"達到自某時以來最高，指達到該時間之後記錄到的最高水平。"},{"en":"School applications may be at their highest since 2010 if many families move nearby.","zh":"如果許多家庭搬到附近，學校申請人數可能達到自2010年以來最高。"},{"en":"If drought measures are at their highest since the 1970s, the situation is historically serious.","zh":"如果乾旱指標達到自七十年代以來最高，情況在歷史上相當嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the present level with a long period of past records.","zh":"這個短語把現時水平與長期過去記錄作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the 1970s","meaning":"二十世紀七十年代","examples":[{"en":"Moisture deficit was at its highest level since the 1970s.","zh":"水分虧缺達到自二十世紀七十年代以來最高水平。"},{"en":"The 1970s means the years from 1970 to 1979.","zh":"二十世紀七十年代，指1970年至1979年。"},{"en":"Music, clothing, and technology from the 1970s often look very different from today’s.","zh":"二十世紀七十年代的音樂、服裝和科技常與今天很不同。"},{"en":"If a climate record is compared with the 1970s, scientists are using a long historical frame.","zh":"如果氣候記錄與七十年代相比，科學家就是使用較長歷史框架。"},{"en":"The phrase names a decade in the twentieth century.","zh":"這個短語指出二十世紀的一個十年。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"meanwhile","meaning":"與此同時","examples":[{"en":"Meanwhile, ecological analyses show different effects at different growth stages.","zh":"與此同時，生態分析顯示不同生長階段有不同影響。"},{"en":"Meanwhile means at the same time or in another related development.","zh":"與此同時，指在同一時間或另一個相關發展中。"},{"en":"The students prepared the posters; meanwhile, the teacher booked the hall.","zh":"學生準備海報；與此同時，老師預訂禮堂。"},{"en":"If one study discusses rainfall, meanwhile another analysis may show crop effects.","zh":"如果一項研究討論降雨，與此同時另一項分析可能顯示農作物影響。"},{"en":"The word connects two things happening in parallel.","zh":"這個詞連接兩件並行發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ecological analyses","meaning":"生態分析","examples":[{"en":"Ecological analyses show that moisture deficit affects crops differently.","zh":"生態分析顯示水分虧缺對農作物有不同影響。"},{"en":"Ecological analyses are studies of how living things interact with their environment.","zh":"生態分析，是研究生物如何與環境互動的分析。"},{"en":"Ecological analyses may examine how fish, water quality, and temperature affect one another.","zh":"生態分析可能研究魚類、水質和溫度如何互相影響。"},{"en":"If ecological analyses include crop stages, they can show when plants are most vulnerable.","zh":"如果生態分析包括農作物階段，就能顯示植物何時最脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to scientific studies of environmental relationships.","zh":"這個短語指研究環境關係的科學分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"clearly show that","meaning":"清楚顯示","examples":[{"en":"Ecological analyses clearly show that timing matters for crop growth.","zh":"生態分析清楚顯示時間對農作物生長很重要。"},{"en":"To clearly show that means to demonstrate something in a way that is easy to understand.","zh":"清楚顯示，指以容易理解的方式證明某事。"},{"en":"A falling attendance record clearly shows that students are losing interest.","zh":"下降的出席紀錄清楚顯示學生正在失去興趣。"},{"en":"If data clearly show a risk, people should not ignore the warning.","zh":"如果數據清楚顯示風險，人們不應忽視警告。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces strong and understandable evidence.","zh":"這個短語引入有力而易明的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have different effects at","meaning":"在……有不同影響","examples":[{"en":"Moisture deficit has different effects at different stages of crop growth.","zh":"水分虧缺在農作物不同生長階段有不同影響。"},{"en":"To have different effects at different times means to influence things differently depending on the stage.","zh":"在不同時間有不同影響，指視乎階段而以不同方式影響事情。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep has different effects at school and during sports practice.","zh":"睡眠不足在學校和運動練習時有不同影響。"},{"en":"If water shortage happens during flowering, it may harm crops more than at another stage.","zh":"如果缺水發生在開花期，它對農作物的傷害可能大於其他階段。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights that timing changes impact.","zh":"這個短語突出時間會改變影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stages of crop growth","meaning":"農作物生長階段","examples":[{"en":"Moisture deficit affects different stages of crop growth.","zh":"水分虧缺影響農作物不同生長階段。"},{"en":"Stages of crop growth are the steps plants pass through as they develop.","zh":"農作物生長階段，是植物發展時經過的步驟。"},{"en":"Crop growth stages may include germination, leaf growth, flowering, and grain formation.","zh":"農作物生長階段可能包括發芽、葉片生長、開花和穀粒形成。"},{"en":"If drought hits a sensitive growth stage, the harvest may be badly damaged.","zh":"如果乾旱打擊敏感生長階段，收成可能嚴重受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the development timeline of farm plants.","zh":"這個短語描述農場植物的發展時間線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"occur around","meaning":"發生在……左右","examples":[{"en":"Damage is greater if moisture deficit occurs around a crucial growth stage.","zh":"如果水分虧缺發生在關鍵生長階段左右，損害會更大。"},{"en":"To occur around a time means to happen near that period.","zh":"發生在某時間左右，指在該時期附近發生。"},{"en":"Exam stress often occurs around the final weeks of a school term.","zh":"考試壓力常發生在學期最後幾週左右。"},{"en":"If drought occurs around flowering, the crop may produce fewer seeds.","zh":"如果乾旱發生在開花期左右，農作物可能產生較少種子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes timing near an important point.","zh":"這個短語描述接近重要時間點的時機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a crucial growth stage","meaning":"關鍵生長階段","examples":[{"en":"Moisture deficit can be serious around a crucial growth stage.","zh":"水分虧缺在關鍵生長階段左右可能很嚴重。"},{"en":"A crucial growth stage is a very important period in plant development.","zh":"關鍵生長階段，是植物發展中非常重要的時期。"},{"en":"For many crops, flowering is a crucial growth stage because it affects final yield.","zh":"對許多農作物來說，開花是關鍵生長階段，因為它影響最終產量。"},{"en":"If plants lack water at a crucial growth stage, later rain may not repair the damage.","zh":"如果植物在關鍵生長階段缺水，後來下雨也可能無法修復損害。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a key moment in crop development.","zh":"這個短語指出農作物發展中的關鍵時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"reduce grain yield by","meaning":"令穀物產量減少……","examples":[{"en":"Moisture deficit can reduce grain yield by about 22 per cent.","zh":"水分虧缺可以令穀物產量減少約百分之二十二。"},{"en":"To reduce grain yield by an amount means to lower the crop output by that amount.","zh":"令穀物產量減少某幅度，指使農作物產出降低該數量。"},{"en":"A disease may reduce grain yield by half if farmers cannot control it.","zh":"如果農民不能控制病害，病害可能令穀物產量減少一半。"},{"en":"If drought reduces yield, farmers harvest less grain from the same field.","zh":"如果乾旱令產量減少，農民就從同一片田收得較少穀物。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the measured loss in crop production.","zh":"這個短語顯示農作物生產中的量化損失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"grain yield","meaning":"穀物產量","examples":[{"en":"Moisture deficit can reduce grain yield.","zh":"水分虧缺可以降低穀物產量。"},{"en":"Grain yield is the amount of grain produced from a field or crop.","zh":"穀物產量，是一片田或一種農作物產出的穀物數量。"},{"en":"Farmers measure grain yield to know how successful a harvest has been.","zh":"農民量度穀物產量，以知道收成有多成功。"},{"en":"If grain yield falls, food supply and farm income may both decline.","zh":"如果穀物產量下降，食物供應和農場收入都可能下跌。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the output of grain crops.","zh":"這個短語指穀物作物的產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"about 22 per cent","meaning":"約百分之二十二","examples":[{"en":"The deficit can reduce grain yield by about 22 per cent.","zh":"這種虧缺可以令穀物產量減少約百分之二十二。"},{"en":"About 22 per cent means approximately twenty-two out of every hundred.","zh":"約百分之二十二，指每一百個中大約二十二個。"},{"en":"If a class of 100 students loses about 22 per cent of its members, 22 students have left.","zh":"如果一班100名學生流失約百分之二十二，即有22名學生離開。"},{"en":"If yield falls by about 22 per cent, the loss is large enough to affect farmers seriously.","zh":"如果產量下降約百分之二十二，損失大到足以嚴重影響農民。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate percentage.","zh":"這個短語給出約略百分比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"The effect is greater compared with a deficit during the vegetative phase.","zh":"與營養生長期的水分虧缺相比，其影響更大。"},{"en":"Compared with means judged against another thing or situation.","zh":"與某事相比，指與另一事物或情況作比較來判斷。"},{"en":"Compared with last year, this year’s class has more students.","zh":"與去年相比，今年的班級有更多學生。"},{"en":"If one drought timing is worse compared with another, farmers must know which stage is most sensitive.","zh":"如果某個乾旱時機比另一個更糟，農民必須知道哪個階段最敏感。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces comparison.","zh":"這個短語引入比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"vegetative phase","meaning":"營養生長期","examples":[{"en":"A deficit during the vegetative phase may be less damaging.","zh":"營養生長期中的水分虧缺可能傷害較小。"},{"en":"The vegetative phase is the plant growth stage focused on leaves, stems, and roots rather than flowers or seeds.","zh":"營養生長期，是植物生長中集中於葉、莖和根，而非花或種子的階段。"},{"en":"A vegetable plant may grow many leaves during its vegetative phase.","zh":"蔬菜植物在營養生長期可能長出許多葉子。"},{"en":"If drought happens during a less sensitive phase, the crop may recover more easily.","zh":"如果乾旱發生在較不敏感階段，農作物可能較容易恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase names one stage of plant development.","zh":"這個短語命名植物發展的一個階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not only affecting","meaning":"不只影響","examples":[{"en":"Global warming is not only affecting agricultural production.","zh":"全球暖化不只影響農業生產。"},{"en":"Not only affecting something means it affects that thing and also other areas.","zh":"不只影響某事，指它影響該事，並同時影響其他範圍。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is not only affecting a student’s grades; it also affects mood and health.","zh":"睡眠不足不只影響學生的成績，也影響情緒和健康。"},{"en":"If climate change affects farms and glaciers, the problem is broader than agriculture.","zh":"如果氣候變化影響農場和冰川，問題就比農業更廣。"},{"en":"The phrase prepares readers for additional effects.","zh":"這個短語讓讀者準備理解額外影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"agricultural production","meaning":"農業生產","examples":[{"en":"Global warming is affecting agricultural production.","zh":"全球暖化正在影響農業生產。"},{"en":"Agricultural production is the growing, raising, and harvesting of food and farm products.","zh":"農業生產，是種植、飼養和收穫食物及農產品。"},{"en":"Rice, wheat, milk, fruit, and vegetables are all part of agricultural production.","zh":"稻米、小麥、牛奶、水果和蔬菜都是農業生產的一部分。"},{"en":"If drought reduces agricultural production, food prices and farmer income may be affected.","zh":"如果乾旱降低農業生產，食物價格和農民收入可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the output of farming.","zh":"這個短語指農業的產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"snowpack","meaning":"積雪層","examples":[{"en":"The country’s snowpack is melting because of global warming.","zh":"該國的積雪層因全球暖化而融化。"},{"en":"Snowpack is the layer of accumulated snow on mountains or land.","zh":"積雪層，是山上或地面累積起來的一層雪。"},{"en":"Mountain snowpack can store water that melts slowly into rivers.","zh":"山區積雪層可以儲存水分，並慢慢融化流入河流。"},{"en":"If snowpack melts earlier, water may be available at the wrong time for farms and towns.","zh":"如果積雪層更早融化，水可能在錯誤時間供應給農場和城鎮。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to stored snow, not just falling snow.","zh":"這個短語指儲存起來的雪，而不只是正在降下的雪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"glaciers","meaning":"冰川","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand’s glaciers are melting at an alarming rate.","zh":"新西蘭的冰川正以驚人速度融化。"},{"en":"Glaciers are large, slow-moving masses of ice formed from compacted snow.","zh":"冰川，是由壓實積雪形成的大型、緩慢移動冰體。"},{"en":"Tourists may visit mountain glaciers to see blue ice and deep valleys.","zh":"遊客可能到山區冰川觀看藍色冰體和深谷。"},{"en":"If glaciers melt quickly, they can change rivers, lakes, and sea levels.","zh":"如果冰川快速融化，就可能改變河流、湖泊和海平面。"},{"en":"The word refers to long-lasting bodies of ice.","zh":"這個詞指長期存在的冰體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"melt at an alarming rate","meaning":"以驚人速度融化","examples":[{"en":"Glaciers are melting at an alarming rate.","zh":"冰川正以驚人速度融化。"},{"en":"To melt at an alarming rate means to melt so quickly that people become worried.","zh":"以驚人速度融化，指融化得非常快，令人擔心。"},{"en":"Ice cream left in strong sun can melt at an alarming rate.","zh":"放在強烈陽光下的雪糕可以以驚人速度融化。"},{"en":"If glaciers melt at an alarming rate, scientists and local communities may need urgent plans.","zh":"如果冰川以驚人速度融化，科學家和本地社區可能需要緊急計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase combines speed with concern.","zh":"這個短語結合速度和憂慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"due to global warming","meaning":"由於全球暖化","examples":[{"en":"Snowpack and glaciers are melting due to global warming.","zh":"積雪層和冰川由於全球暖化而融化。"},{"en":"Due to global warming means because of the long-term rise in global temperatures.","zh":"由於全球暖化，指因全球氣溫長期上升而造成。"},{"en":"Some coastal towns may face higher flood risk due to global warming.","zh":"一些沿岸城鎮可能由於全球暖化而面臨更高水浸風險。"},{"en":"If ice melts due to global warming, the change is linked to wider climate trends.","zh":"如果冰因全球暖化而融化，該變化就與更廣泛氣候趨勢有關。"},{"en":"The phrase gives climate change as the cause.","zh":"這個短語把氣候變化作為原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"place additional strain on","meaning":"對……造成額外壓力","examples":[{"en":"Melting snow and ice place additional strain on local areas.","zh":"融化的雪和冰對本地地區造成額外壓力。"},{"en":"To place additional strain on something means to add extra pressure or difficulty to it.","zh":"對某事造成額外壓力，指給它增加額外負擔或困難。"},{"en":"A flu outbreak can place additional strain on hospitals.","zh":"流感爆發可以對醫院造成額外壓力。"},{"en":"If climate change damages roads, farms, and water systems, local areas face greater pressure.","zh":"如果氣候變化損害道路、農場和水系統，本地地區就面對更大壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extra burden.","zh":"這個短語描述額外負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"local areas","meaning":"本地地區","examples":[{"en":"Climate change places additional strain on local areas.","zh":"氣候變化對本地地區造成額外壓力。"},{"en":"Local areas are nearby communities, districts, or regions affected by an issue.","zh":"本地地區，是受某問題影響的附近社區、區域或地區。"},{"en":"Local areas may include small towns, farming districts, and coastal villages.","zh":"本地地區可能包括小鎮、農業區和沿岸村莊。"},{"en":"If global warming affects local areas differently, each community may need its own plan.","zh":"如果全球暖化對不同本地地區有不同影響，每個社區可能需要自己的計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase brings a large issue down to specific places.","zh":"這個短語把大問題帶回具體地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be accompanied by","meaning":"伴隨着……","examples":[{"en":"Global warming may be accompanied by a rising snow line.","zh":"全球暖化可能伴隨着雪線上升。"},{"en":"To be accompanied by something means to happen together with it.","zh":"伴隨着某事，指與它同時發生。"},{"en":"A fever may be accompanied by a headache and tiredness.","zh":"發燒可能伴隨頭痛和疲倦。"},{"en":"If warming is accompanied by a rising snow line, ski resorts may lose lower snow areas.","zh":"如果變暖伴隨雪線上升，滑雪度假村可能失去較低處雪地。"},{"en":"The phrase links one event with another related event.","zh":"這個短語把一件事與另一件相關事件連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a rising snow line","meaning":"雪線上升","examples":[{"en":"A rising snow line creates problems for ski resorts.","zh":"雪線上升為滑雪度假村造成問題。"},{"en":"A rising snow line means the lowest level where snow remains is moving higher up mountains.","zh":"雪線上升，指能保持積雪的最低高度正向山上移動。"},{"en":"A mountain town may notice a rising snow line when snow no longer reaches old ski fields.","zh":"當雪不再到達舊滑雪場，山區城鎮可能注意到雪線上升。"},{"en":"If the snow line rises, winter tourism may have to move to higher altitudes.","zh":"如果雪線上升，冬季旅遊可能要移向更高海拔。"},{"en":"The phrase describes snow becoming limited to higher places.","zh":"這個短語描述雪變得只限於較高地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"local ski industry","meaning":"本地滑雪業","examples":[{"en":"The local ski industry faces a crisis as snow melts earlier.","zh":"隨着雪更早融化，本地滑雪業面臨危機。"},{"en":"The local ski industry includes ski resorts, instructors, equipment shops, hotels, and tourism services in an area.","zh":"本地滑雪業包括某地的滑雪度假村、教練、器材店、酒店和旅遊服務。"},{"en":"A mountain village may depend on its local ski industry for winter jobs.","zh":"山區村莊可能依賴本地滑雪業提供冬季工作。"},{"en":"If snow becomes unreliable, the local ski industry may lose visitors and income.","zh":"如果降雪變得不可靠，本地滑雪業可能失去遊客和收入。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to businesses connected with skiing in a particular place.","zh":"這個短語指特定地方與滑雪相關的商業活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"face a crisis","meaning":"面臨危機","examples":[{"en":"The local ski industry may face a crisis.","zh":"本地滑雪業可能面臨危機。"},{"en":"To face a crisis means to deal with a serious and difficult situation.","zh":"面臨危機，指要處理嚴重而困難的情況。"},{"en":"A school may face a crisis if many teachers leave at the same time.","zh":"如果許多老師同時離職，學校可能面臨危機。"},{"en":"If ski resorts lose snow, they may face a crisis in income and employment.","zh":"如果滑雪度假村失去積雪，就可能在收入和就業方面面臨危機。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being confronted by a major problem.","zh":"這個短語描述面對重大問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"move up","meaning":"向上移","examples":[{"en":"The snow line may move up as the temperature rises.","zh":"隨着氣溫上升，雪線可能向上移。"},{"en":"To move up means to shift to a higher position.","zh":"向上移，指移到更高位置。"},{"en":"Students may move up to the next level after passing a language test.","zh":"學生通過語言測試後可能升到下一級。"},{"en":"If the snow line moves up, lower slopes may no longer have enough snow.","zh":"如果雪線向上移，較低斜坡可能不再有足夠積雪。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe physical movement or progress to a higher level.","zh":"這個短語可以描述身體位置移動或升到更高水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"melt earlier","meaning":"更早融化","examples":[{"en":"The snow at the bottom may melt earlier.","zh":"底部的雪可能更早融化。"},{"en":"To melt earlier means to turn from snow or ice into water sooner than usual.","zh":"更早融化，指雪或冰比平常更早變成水。"},{"en":"Ice cubes melt earlier if they are left near a sunny window.","zh":"如果冰塊放在陽光充足的窗邊，就會更早融化。"},{"en":"If mountain snow melts earlier, ski seasons may become shorter.","zh":"如果山上積雪更早融化，滑雪季節可能變短。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change in timing.","zh":"這個短語描述時間上的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"increased snowfall","meaning":"降雪量增加","examples":[{"en":"Increased snowfall in some areas may help the ski industry.","zh":"某些地區降雪量增加可能幫助滑雪業。"},{"en":"Increased snowfall means more snow falling than before or than usual.","zh":"降雪量增加，指比以前或平常有更多雪降下。"},{"en":"A mountain town may welcome increased snowfall because tourists come to ski.","zh":"山區小鎮可能歡迎降雪量增加，因為遊客會來滑雪。"},{"en":"If increased snowfall happens only in high areas, low ski fields may still struggle.","zh":"如果降雪量增加只發生在高地，低海拔滑雪場仍可能困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a rise in snow amount.","zh":"這個短語描述雪量上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"help someone through difficult periods","meaning":"幫助某人渡過困難時期","examples":[{"en":"Increased snowfall may help the local ski industry through difficult periods.","zh":"降雪量增加可能幫助本地滑雪業渡過困難時期。"},{"en":"To help someone through difficult periods means to support them while they face hard times.","zh":"幫助某人渡過困難時期，指在他們面對艱難時提供支持。"},{"en":"Extra tutoring can help a student through a difficult exam period.","zh":"額外補習可以幫助學生渡過困難考試期。"},{"en":"If more snow arrives in some seasons, ski businesses may survive years with poorer snow.","zh":"如果某些季節有更多雪，滑雪企業可能捱過雪況較差的年份。"},{"en":"The phrase describes support during hardship.","zh":"這個短語描述在困境中提供支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"glacier regions","meaning":"冰川地區","examples":[{"en":"Climate change is reflected in the glacier regions of southern New Zealand.","zh":"氣候變化反映於新西蘭南部的冰川地區。"},{"en":"Glacier regions are areas where glaciers are found.","zh":"冰川地區，是有冰川存在的區域。"},{"en":"Tourists may visit glacier regions to see ice, mountains, lakes, and valleys.","zh":"遊客可能參觀冰川地區，觀看冰、山、湖和山谷。"},{"en":"If glacier regions lose ice, nearby rivers and tourism may also change.","zh":"如果冰川地區流失冰量，附近河流和旅遊業也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to places shaped by glaciers.","zh":"這個短語指受冰川塑造的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"respond to","meaning":"對……作出反應","examples":[{"en":"Glacier regions respond to climate change in complex ways.","zh":"冰川地區以複雜方式對氣候變化作出反應。"},{"en":"To respond to something means to react to it or change because of it.","zh":"對某事作出反應，指因它而有反應或改變。"},{"en":"Students respond to feedback by correcting mistakes in later essays.","zh":"學生透過在之後作文中改正錯誤來回應回饋。"},{"en":"If glaciers respond slowly to climate change, their changes may appear over many years.","zh":"如果冰川對氣候變化反應緩慢，其變化可能多年後才出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reaction or adjustment.","zh":"這個短語描述反應或調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"climate change","meaning":"氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"Climate change affects New Zealand’s glaciers, farms and coastlines.","zh":"氣候變化影響新西蘭的冰川、農場和海岸線。"},{"en":"Climate change means long-term changes in temperature, rainfall, storms, and other climate patterns.","zh":"氣候變化，指氣溫、降雨、風暴和其他氣候模式的長期改變。"},{"en":"A community may discuss climate change when floods become more frequent.","zh":"當水浸變得更頻繁，社區可能討論氣候變化。"},{"en":"If climate change worsens droughts, farmers may need new crops and water plans.","zh":"如果氣候變化令乾旱惡化，農民可能需要新作物和用水計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long-term environmental change, not daily weather.","zh":"這個短語描述長期環境改變，而不是每日天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be reflected in","meaning":"反映於……","examples":[{"en":"Climate change is reflected in the glacier regions.","zh":"氣候變化反映於冰川地區。"},{"en":"To be reflected in something means to be shown or made visible through it.","zh":"反映於某事，指透過它顯示或變得可見。"},{"en":"A student’s hard work is reflected in improved writing and clearer answers.","zh":"學生的努力反映於改善了的寫作和更清楚答案。"},{"en":"If warming is reflected in glaciers, melting ice becomes evidence of climate change.","zh":"如果變暖反映於冰川，融化的冰就成為氣候變化的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how a larger change appears in a specific sign.","zh":"這個短語描述較大變化如何出現在具體跡象中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"southern New Zealand","meaning":"新西蘭南部","examples":[{"en":"Glacier regions in southern New Zealand are covered by ice and snow.","zh":"新西蘭南部的冰川地區被冰雪覆蓋。"},{"en":"Southern New Zealand means the southern part of New Zealand.","zh":"新西蘭南部，指新西蘭的南方部分。"},{"en":"Travellers may visit southern New Zealand for mountains, lakes, and cold landscapes.","zh":"旅客可能到新西蘭南部遊覽山脈、湖泊和寒冷景觀。"},{"en":"If southern New Zealand loses ice, the change may affect tourism and water systems.","zh":"如果新西蘭南部流失冰量，該變化可能影響旅遊和水系統。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a geographic part of the country.","zh":"這個短語指出該國的地理部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be covered by ice and snow","meaning":"被冰雪覆蓋","examples":[{"en":"Some land in southern New Zealand is covered by ice and snow.","zh":"新西蘭南部一些土地被冰雪覆蓋。"},{"en":"To be covered by ice and snow means to have ice and snow lying over the surface.","zh":"被冰雪覆蓋，指表面上有冰和雪。"},{"en":"A mountain road may be covered by ice and snow after a winter storm.","zh":"冬季風暴後，山路可能被冰雪覆蓋。"},{"en":"If land is covered by ice and snow, rising temperatures can change its appearance quickly.","zh":"如果土地被冰雪覆蓋，氣溫上升可以很快改變其外觀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a frozen surface.","zh":"這個短語描述冰凍表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the reaction of something to","meaning":"……對……的反應","examples":[{"en":"The reaction of a glacier to climate change is complex.","zh":"冰川對氣候變化的反應很複雜。"},{"en":"The reaction of something to a change means how it responds when that change happens.","zh":"某物對某變化的反應，指該變化發生時它如何回應。"},{"en":"A plant’s reaction to less water may include yellow leaves and slower growth.","zh":"植物對水分減少的反應可能包括葉子變黃和生長變慢。"},{"en":"If a glacier reacts slowly, its full change may not be visible immediately.","zh":"如果冰川反應緩慢，其完整變化可能不會立即可見。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on response to a cause.","zh":"這個短語強調對原因的回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"climatic change","meaning":"氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"A glacier’s reaction to climatic change involves several processes.","zh":"冰川對氣候變化的反應涉及幾個過程。"},{"en":"Climatic change means long-term change in climate conditions such as temperature and rainfall.","zh":"氣候變化，指氣溫和降雨等氣候狀況的長期改變。"},{"en":"Farmers notice climatic change when planting seasons no longer match old experience.","zh":"當播種季節不再符合舊經驗，農民就會注意到氣候變化。"},{"en":"If climatic change affects ice and water, communities may need new plans.","zh":"如果氣候變化影響冰和水，社區可能需要新計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to say climate change.","zh":"這個短語是 climate change 的較正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"involve a complex chain of processes","meaning":"涉及一連串複雜過程","examples":[{"en":"The reaction of a glacier involves a complex chain of processes.","zh":"冰川的反應涉及一連串複雜過程。"},{"en":"To involve a complex chain of processes means to include many connected steps that influence one another.","zh":"涉及一連串複雜過程，指包括許多互相影響的連接步驟。"},{"en":"Applying for university can involve a complex chain of processes, from forms to interviews.","zh":"申請大學可能涉及一連串複雜過程，由填表到面試。"},{"en":"If glacier change involves many processes, a simple temperature reading cannot explain everything.","zh":"如果冰川變化涉及許多過程，單一氣溫讀數不能解釋一切。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights linked stages and complexity.","zh":"這個短語突出互相連接的階段和複雜性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"over periods ranging from…to…","meaning":"在由……至……不等的期間","examples":[{"en":"Changes occur over periods ranging from years to several decades.","zh":"變化會在由數年至數十年不等的期間發生。"},{"en":"Over periods ranging from A to B means across time spans from one length to another.","zh":"在由 A 至 B 不等的期間，指跨越由一種長度到另一種長度的時間跨度。"},{"en":"Language improvement can happen over periods ranging from months to years.","zh":"語言進步可以在由數月至數年不等的期間發生。"},{"en":"If glacier changes range from years to decades, scientists need long-term records.","zh":"如果冰川變化由數年到數十年不等，科學家需要長期記錄。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a range of time lengths.","zh":"這個短語給出時間長度範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"several decades","meaning":"數十年","examples":[{"en":"Some glacier changes occur over several decades.","zh":"一些冰川變化會在數十年間發生。"},{"en":"Several decades means a period of many tens of years.","zh":"數十年，指許多個十年的時間。"},{"en":"A school building may serve a community for several decades.","zh":"一座校舍可能服務社區數十年。"},{"en":"If environmental change takes several decades, people may not notice it from one year to the next.","zh":"如果環境變化需時數十年，人們可能不會從一年到下一年明顯察覺。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a long time span.","zh":"這個短語指很長的時間跨度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cumulative changes","meaning":"累積變化","examples":[{"en":"Cumulative changes in mass balance affect glacier size.","zh":"質量平衡的累積變化影響冰川大小。"},{"en":"Cumulative changes are changes that build up gradually over time.","zh":"累積變化，是隨時間逐漸積累起來的變化。"},{"en":"Small daily savings can create cumulative changes in a family budget.","zh":"每天小額儲蓄可以在家庭預算中造成累積變化。"},{"en":"If a glacier loses a little mass each year, the cumulative change can become large.","zh":"如果冰川每年流失少量質量，累積變化可以變得很大。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on effects that accumulate.","zh":"這個短語強調會積聚的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"mass balance","meaning":"質量平衡","examples":[{"en":"Glacier mass balance is a direct signal of atmospheric conditions.","zh":"冰川質量平衡是大氣狀況的直接信號。"},{"en":"Mass balance is the difference between how much ice a glacier gains and how much it loses.","zh":"質量平衡，是冰川獲得多少冰與失去多少冰之間的差異。"},{"en":"A budget is similar: balance depends on money coming in and money going out.","zh":"預算也類似：平衡取決於收入和支出。"},{"en":"If a glacier loses more ice than it gains, its mass balance becomes negative.","zh":"如果冰川失去的冰多於得到的冰，其質量平衡就變成負數。"},{"en":"The phrase measures whether a glacier is growing or shrinking.","zh":"這個短語量度冰川正在增長還是縮小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"volume and thickness changes","meaning":"體積和厚度變化","examples":[{"en":"Cumulative changes cause volume and thickness changes.","zh":"累積變化造成體積和厚度變化。"},{"en":"Volume and thickness changes are alterations in how much space something takes up and how thick it is.","zh":"體積和厚度變化，是某物佔據空間多少及厚度上的改變。"},{"en":"A sponge shows volume and thickness changes when it absorbs water.","zh":"海綿吸水時會出現體積和厚度變化。"},{"en":"If a glacier loses volume and thickness, its shape and movement may change.","zh":"如果冰川失去體積和厚度，其形狀和移動可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical changes in size and depth.","zh":"這個短語描述大小和深度上的物理變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"affect the flow of ice","meaning":"影響冰流","examples":[{"en":"Volume and thickness changes affect the flow of ice.","zh":"體積和厚度變化影響冰流。"},{"en":"To affect the flow of ice means to change how ice moves.","zh":"影響冰流，指改變冰的移動方式。"},{"en":"A blocked pipe affects the flow of water through a building.","zh":"堵塞的水管會影響水在建築物中的流動。"},{"en":"If glacier thickness changes, ice may slide or deform differently.","zh":"如果冰川厚度改變，冰可能以不同方式滑動或變形。"},{"en":"The phrase connects glacier shape with glacier movement.","zh":"這個短語把冰川形狀與冰川移動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"via","meaning":"透過；經由","examples":[{"en":"Ice flow changes via altered internal deformation and basal sliding.","zh":"冰流透過改變了的內部變形和基底滑動而改變。"},{"en":"Via means through or by means of a particular route, method, or process.","zh":"透過或經由，指通過特定路線、方法或過程。"},{"en":"Students may submit homework via an online platform.","zh":"學生可能透過網上平台提交功課。"},{"en":"If glacier movement changes via internal processes, the cause is not only surface melting.","zh":"如果冰川移動透過內部過程改變，原因就不只是表面融化。"},{"en":"The word introduces the method or pathway.","zh":"這個詞引入方法或路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"altered internal deformation","meaning":"改變了的內部變形","examples":[{"en":"Altered internal deformation affects the flow of ice.","zh":"改變了的內部變形影響冰流。"},{"en":"Altered internal deformation means changed bending or reshaping inside the glacier.","zh":"改變了的內部變形，指冰川內部彎曲或重塑方式改變。"},{"en":"A mattress changes shape internally when someone lies on it for years.","zh":"床褥在人長年躺在上面後，內部形狀會改變。"},{"en":"If a glacier deforms differently inside, the whole ice mass may move differently.","zh":"如果冰川內部以不同方式變形，整個冰體可能以不同方式移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a changed process within the ice.","zh":"這個短語描述冰內部已改變的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"basal sliding","meaning":"基底滑動","examples":[{"en":"Basal sliding is part of the glacier’s dynamic response.","zh":"基底滑動是冰川動態反應的一部分。"},{"en":"Basal sliding is the movement of a glacier along its base over the ground beneath it.","zh":"基底滑動，是冰川沿其底部在下方地面上滑動。"},{"en":"A heavy box slides more easily if the floor beneath it becomes wet.","zh":"如果下面地板濕了，沉重箱子會較容易滑動。"},{"en":"If melting water reaches the glacier base, basal sliding may increase.","zh":"如果融水到達冰川底部，基底滑動可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement at the bottom of a glacier.","zh":"這個短語描述冰川底部的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dynamic response","meaning":"動態反應","examples":[{"en":"The glacier’s dynamic response leads to changes in length.","zh":"冰川的動態反應導致長度變化。"},{"en":"A dynamic response is a changing physical reaction to forces or conditions.","zh":"動態反應，是對力量或環境狀況產生的變化性物理反應。"},{"en":"A bridge has a dynamic response when it moves slightly under heavy traffic and wind.","zh":"橋樑在繁忙交通和風下輕微移動，就是有動態反應。"},{"en":"If a glacier’s dynamic response changes, its front may advance or retreat.","zh":"如果冰川的動態反應改變，其前緣可能前進或後退。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active movement-based reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述以移動為基礎的主動反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lead to changes in","meaning":"導致……的變化","examples":[{"en":"The dynamic response leads to changes in glacier length.","zh":"動態反應導致冰川長度的變化。"},{"en":"To lead to changes in something means to cause that thing to become different.","zh":"導致某事的變化，指使該事變得不同。"},{"en":"A new timetable may lead to changes in students’ sleep habits.","zh":"新時間表可能導致學生睡眠習慣的變化。"},{"en":"If ice movement changes, it may lead to changes in the glacier’s shape and length.","zh":"如果冰的移動改變，可能導致冰川形狀和長度變化。"},{"en":"The phrase shows cause and resulting change.","zh":"這個短語顯示原因和結果性變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"glacier length","meaning":"冰川長度","examples":[{"en":"The glacier’s dynamic response changes glacier length.","zh":"冰川的動態反應改變冰川長度。"},{"en":"Glacier length is the distance from the upper part of a glacier to its front end.","zh":"冰川長度，是冰川上部到其前端之間的距離。"},{"en":"Scientists may measure glacier length every year to see whether it is retreating.","zh":"科學家可能每年量度冰川長度，以觀察它是否正在後退。"},{"en":"If glacier length decreases, the glacier is usually shrinking or retreating.","zh":"如果冰川長度減少，冰川通常正在縮小或後退。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the measured length of an ice body.","zh":"這個短語指冰體被量度的長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"advance or retreat","meaning":"前進或後退","examples":[{"en":"Climate change may cause the advance or retreat of glacier tongues.","zh":"氣候變化可能造成冰舌前進或後退。"},{"en":"Advance or retreat means move forward or move backward.","zh":"前進或後退，指向前移動或向後移動。"},{"en":"A sports team may advance or retreat depending on whether it is attacking or defending.","zh":"運動隊伍可能視乎進攻或防守而前進或後退。"},{"en":"If a glacier gains ice, its front may advance; if it loses ice, it may retreat.","zh":"如果冰川增加冰量，其前端可能前進；如果失去冰量，就可能後退。"},{"en":"The phrase describes opposite directions of movement.","zh":"這個短語描述相反方向的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"glacier tongues","meaning":"冰舌","examples":[{"en":"The advance or retreat of glacier tongues changes glacier length.","zh":"冰舌的前進或後退改變冰川長度。"},{"en":"Glacier tongues are long, narrow lower parts of glaciers that extend down valleys.","zh":"冰舌，是冰川向山谷延伸的狹長下部。"},{"en":"On a map, a glacier tongue may look like a strip of ice reaching into a valley.","zh":"在地圖上，冰舌可能像一條伸入山谷的冰帶。"},{"en":"If glacier tongues retreat, lakes may form where ice once covered the land.","zh":"如果冰舌後退，原本被冰覆蓋的地方可能形成湖泊。"},{"en":"The phrase names the extended front parts of glaciers.","zh":"這個短語命名冰川延伸的前部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"undoubtedly","meaning":"毫無疑問","examples":[{"en":"Undoubtedly, glacier mass balance is a direct climate signal.","zh":"毫無疑問，冰川質量平衡是直接氣候信號。"},{"en":"Undoubtedly means without doubt or certainly.","zh":"毫無疑問，指沒有疑問或肯定地。"},{"en":"Undoubtedly, regular practice helps students improve pronunciation.","zh":"毫無疑問，定期練習有助學生改善發音。"},{"en":"If evidence is very strong, a writer may use undoubtedly to show confidence.","zh":"如果證據非常強，作者可能使用「毫無疑問」來顯示信心。"},{"en":"The word strengthens a statement.","zh":"這個詞加強陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a more direct signal of","meaning":"……更直接的信號","examples":[{"en":"Glacier mass balance is a more direct signal of annual atmospheric conditions.","zh":"冰川質量平衡是年度大氣狀況更直接的信號。"},{"en":"A more direct signal of something is evidence that shows it more closely or immediately.","zh":"某事更直接的信號，是更密切或即時顯示它的證據。"},{"en":"A fever is a more direct signal of illness than simply feeling tired.","zh":"發燒比只是感到疲倦更能直接顯示疾病。"},{"en":"If mass balance responds to yearly weather, it can reveal climate conditions clearly.","zh":"如果質量平衡回應年度天氣，它就能清楚揭示氣候狀況。"},{"en":"The phrase compares how clearly something shows evidence.","zh":"這個短語比較某物顯示證據的清晰程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"annual atmospheric conditions","meaning":"年度大氣狀況","examples":[{"en":"Glacier mass balance reflects annual atmospheric conditions.","zh":"冰川質量平衡反映年度大氣狀況。"},{"en":"Annual atmospheric conditions are the weather and air conditions over a year.","zh":"年度大氣狀況，是一年中的天氣和空氣狀況。"},{"en":"Farmers review annual atmospheric conditions to understand rainfall, heat, and wind patterns.","zh":"農民檢視年度大氣狀況，以了解降雨、高溫和風向模式。"},{"en":"If annual atmospheric conditions change, glaciers may gain or lose different amounts of ice.","zh":"如果年度大氣狀況改變，冰川可能增加或失去不同冰量。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to yearly climate-related air conditions.","zh":"這個短語指每年的氣候相關空氣狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the latest research from","meaning":"來自……的最新研究","examples":[{"en":"The latest research from NIWA shows further ice loss.","zh":"來自 NIWA 的最新研究顯示進一步冰量流失。"},{"en":"The latest research from an organisation means the newest study or findings produced by it.","zh":"來自某機構的最新研究，指由該機構產生的最新研究或發現。"},{"en":"The latest research from a university may change how doctors treat a disease.","zh":"來自大學的最新研究可能改變醫生治療疾病的方法。"},{"en":"If the latest research shows ice loss, older maps may no longer reflect reality.","zh":"如果最新研究顯示冰量流失，舊地圖可能不再反映現實。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces recent evidence from a named source.","zh":"這個短語引入來自具名來源的近期證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"National Institute of Water and Atmospheric Research","meaning":"國家水與大氣研究所","examples":[{"en":"The National Institute of Water and Atmospheric Research studies climate and water systems.","zh":"國家水與大氣研究所研究氣候和水系統。"},{"en":"The National Institute of Water and Atmospheric Research is an organisation focused on water, weather, climate, and atmospheric science.","zh":"國家水與大氣研究所，是專注於水、天氣、氣候和大氣科學的機構。"},{"en":"A student might cite the National Institute of Water and Atmospheric Research in a report on New Zealand climate.","zh":"學生在新西蘭氣候報告中可能引用國家水與大氣研究所。"},{"en":"If such an institute publishes glacier data, it gives scientific support to the discussion.","zh":"如果這類研究所發表冰川數據，就為討論提供科學支持。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specialist research organisation.","zh":"這個短語命名一個專門研究機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"keep moving up","meaning":"持續上移","examples":[{"en":"The glacier line keeps moving up because of global warming.","zh":"冰川線因全球暖化而持續上移。"},{"en":"To keep moving up means to continue shifting to a higher position.","zh":"持續上移，指繼續向較高位置移動。"},{"en":"Rent may keep moving up if housing demand stays high.","zh":"如果住屋需求保持高企，租金可能持續上升。"},{"en":"If a glacier line keeps moving up, ice is disappearing from lower areas.","zh":"如果冰川線持續上移，較低地區的冰正在消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continued upward movement.","zh":"這個短語描述持續向上移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the impacts of global warming","meaning":"全球暖化的影響","examples":[{"en":"The glacier line keeps moving up because of the impacts of global warming.","zh":"冰川線因全球暖化的影響而持續上移。"},{"en":"The impacts of global warming are the effects caused by rising global temperatures.","zh":"全球暖化的影響，是全球氣溫上升造成的後果。"},{"en":"The impacts of global warming can include heatwaves, melting ice, droughts, and sea-level rise.","zh":"全球暖化的影響可以包括熱浪、冰融化、乾旱和海平面上升。"},{"en":"If the impacts of global warming worsen, communities may need stronger adaptation plans.","zh":"如果全球暖化的影響惡化，社區可能需要更強的適應計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to consequences, not the cause itself.","zh":"這個短語指後果，而不是原因本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"further ice loss","meaning":"進一步冰量流失","examples":[{"en":"Further ice loss is evident in the Mount Cook region.","zh":"進一步冰量流失在庫克山地區明顯可見。"},{"en":"Further ice loss means additional melting or reduction of ice beyond what has already happened.","zh":"進一步冰量流失，指在已發生的情況之外，冰繼續融化或減少。"},{"en":"A freezer with a broken door may show further ice loss each day.","zh":"冰箱門壞掉時，可能每天出現進一步冰量流失。"},{"en":"If further ice loss continues in a glacier region, lakes may expand and landscapes may change.","zh":"如果冰川地區持續進一步流失冰量，湖泊可能擴大，景觀也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continued loss of ice.","zh":"這個短語描述冰量持續減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be evident in","meaning":"在……明顯可見","examples":[{"en":"Further ice loss is evident in the Mount Cook region.","zh":"進一步冰量流失在庫克山地區明顯可見。"},{"en":"To be evident in something means to be clearly visible or shown there.","zh":"在某處明顯可見，指在那裡清楚可見或顯示出來。"},{"en":"A student’s progress is evident in clearer writing and fewer grammar mistakes.","zh":"學生的進步在更清楚的寫作和更少文法錯誤中明顯可見。"},{"en":"If ice loss is evident in a region, the physical landscape shows the change.","zh":"如果冰量流失在某地區明顯可見，實際景觀就顯示出變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visible evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述可見證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Mount Cook region","meaning":"庫克山地區","examples":[{"en":"Further ice loss is evident in the Mount Cook region.","zh":"進一步冰量流失在庫克山地區明顯可見。"},{"en":"The Mount Cook region is the area around Mount Cook in New Zealand.","zh":"庫克山地區，是新西蘭庫克山周圍的區域。"},{"en":"Tourists visit the Mount Cook region for mountains, glaciers, and alpine scenery.","zh":"遊客到庫克山地區欣賞山脈、冰川和高山景色。"},{"en":"If glaciers shrink in the Mount Cook region, tourism and local water systems may be affected.","zh":"如果庫克山地區的冰川縮小，旅遊和本地水系統可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a specific mountain area.","zh":"這個短語指出特定山區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a 14-km-long sector of","meaning":"一段長十四公里的……","examples":[{"en":"A 14-km-long sector of the glacier had melted by 1996.","zh":"到1996年，一段長十四公里的冰川已經融化。"},{"en":"A 14-km-long sector of something is a section measuring fourteen kilometres in length.","zh":"一段長十四公里的某物，是長度達十四公里的一部分。"},{"en":"A 14-km-long sector of a road may close after a storm damages it.","zh":"暴風雨損壞道路後，一段長十四公里的道路可能關閉。"},{"en":"If a 14-km-long part of a glacier melts, the loss is large enough to reshape the area.","zh":"如果一段長十四公里的冰川融化，損失足以重塑該地區。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a precise length for one section.","zh":"這個短語為某一部分給出準確長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"form a melt lake","meaning":"形成融水湖","examples":[{"en":"The melted glacier formed a melt lake called Hooker Lake.","zh":"融化的冰川形成一個名為胡克湖的融水湖。"},{"en":"To form a melt lake means to create a lake from water produced by melting ice.","zh":"形成融水湖，指由冰融化產生的水形成湖泊。"},{"en":"Snow on a roof can form a small pool of meltwater when the sun returns.","zh":"太陽再出現時，屋頂上的雪可以形成一小灘融水。"},{"en":"If a glacier melts back, water may collect and form a lake at its front.","zh":"如果冰川向後融退，水可能聚集並在其前方形成湖泊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lake creation from ice melt.","zh":"這個短語描述由融冰形成湖泊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"melt lake","meaning":"融水湖","examples":[{"en":"Hooker Lake is a melt lake formed by glacier melting.","zh":"胡克湖是由冰川融化形成的融水湖。"},{"en":"A melt lake is a lake created by water from melting ice or snow.","zh":"融水湖，是由冰或雪融化後的水形成的湖泊。"},{"en":"A small melt lake may appear on top of ice during warm weather.","zh":"暖天時，冰面上可能出現小型融水湖。"},{"en":"If melt lakes grow, they can show that ice is disappearing quickly.","zh":"如果融水湖擴大，就可以顯示冰正在迅速消失。"},{"en":"The phrase names a lake formed from melted ice.","zh":"這個短語命名由融冰形成的湖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Hooker Lake","meaning":"胡克湖","examples":[{"en":"Hooker Lake formed after part of the glacier melted.","zh":"胡克湖在部分冰川融化後形成。"},{"en":"Hooker Lake is a named lake in the Mount Cook region formed from glacier meltwater.","zh":"胡克湖，是庫克山地區由冰川融水形成的具名湖泊。"},{"en":"A geography student may use Hooker Lake as an example of glacier retreat.","zh":"地理學生可能使用胡克湖作為冰川後退的例子。"},{"en":"If Hooker Lake continues to grow, it may show ongoing ice loss nearby.","zh":"如果胡克湖繼續擴大，可能顯示附近冰量持續流失。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific melt lake.","zh":"這個短語命名一個具體融水湖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"glacier front","meaning":"冰川前緣","examples":[{"en":"The glacier front is melting at a rate of 40 metres per year.","zh":"冰川前緣正以每年四十米的速度融化。"},{"en":"The glacier front is the lower or leading edge of a glacier.","zh":"冰川前緣，是冰川下方或前方的邊緣。"},{"en":"Scientists photograph the glacier front to see whether it is retreating.","zh":"科學家拍攝冰川前緣，以觀察它是否正在後退。"},{"en":"If the glacier front melts quickly, a lake in front of it may expand.","zh":"如果冰川前緣快速融化，其前方湖泊可能擴大。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the visible end of a glacier.","zh":"這個短語指冰川可見的末端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at a rate of","meaning":"以……的速度","examples":[{"en":"The glacier front is melting at a rate of 40 metres per year.","zh":"冰川前緣正以每年四十米的速度融化。"},{"en":"At a rate of means at a measured speed or amount over time.","zh":"以某速度，指按一個可量度的速度或時間內的數量。"},{"en":"A car may travel at a rate of 60 kilometres per hour.","zh":"汽車可能以每小時六十公里的速度行駛。"},{"en":"If a glacier melts at a fast rate, its retreat can be measured year by year.","zh":"如果冰川以快速速度融化，其後退可以逐年量度。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the speed or pace of change.","zh":"這個短語給出變化速度或步伐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"retreat at a uniform rate","meaning":"以均勻速度後退","examples":[{"en":"The glacier may retreat at a rather uniform rate.","zh":"冰川可能以相當均勻的速度後退。"},{"en":"To retreat at a uniform rate means to move back at a steady and regular speed.","zh":"以均勻速度後退，指以穩定而規律的速度向後移。"},{"en":"A tide line may retreat at a uniform rate as water slowly drains away.","zh":"當水慢慢退去，潮水線可能以均勻速度後退。"},{"en":"If a glacier retreats uniformly, scientists can estimate where its front may be later.","zh":"如果冰川均勻後退，科學家可以估計其前緣日後位置。"},{"en":"The phrase describes steady backward movement.","zh":"這個短語描述穩定的向後移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"continue to grow","meaning":"繼續擴大","examples":[{"en":"The lake will continue to grow as the glacier retreats.","zh":"隨着冰川後退，湖泊會繼續擴大。"},{"en":"To continue to grow means to keep increasing in size, number, or amount.","zh":"繼續擴大，指在大小、數量或數額上持續增加。"},{"en":"A school club may continue to grow if new students join every year.","zh":"如果每年都有新學生加入，學校學會可能繼續擴大。"},{"en":"If a glacier melts into a lake, the lake may continue to grow until the ice stops retreating.","zh":"如果冰川融化成湖泊，湖泊可能繼續擴大，直到冰停止後退。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ongoing increase.","zh":"這個短語描述持續增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"reach the glacier bed","meaning":"到達冰川床","examples":[{"en":"The lake will grow until it reaches the glacier bed.","zh":"湖泊會擴大，直到到達冰川床。"},{"en":"To reach the glacier bed means to extend to the bottom surface beneath the glacier.","zh":"到達冰川床，指延伸至冰川下方的底部表面。"},{"en":"Water in a sink rises until it reaches the overflow hole.","zh":"洗手盆中的水會上升，直到到達溢水孔。"},{"en":"If a melt lake reaches the glacier bed, the shape of the glacier basin may control its size.","zh":"如果融水湖到達冰川床，冰川盆地形狀可能控制其大小。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reaching a lower boundary under the ice.","zh":"這個短語描述到達冰下的較低邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a direct result of","meaning":"……的直接結果","examples":[{"en":"A direct result of melting glaciers is a change in high tides.","zh":"冰川融化的直接結果是潮汐高位變化。"},{"en":"A direct result of something is an effect caused clearly by it.","zh":"某事的直接結果，是由它清楚造成的影響。"},{"en":"A direct result of missing many lessons may be weaker exam performance.","zh":"缺席許多課堂的直接結果可能是考試表現較弱。"},{"en":"If melting glaciers add water to oceans, sea-level effects may follow directly.","zh":"如果冰川融化向海洋增加水量，海平面影響可能直接隨之而來。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a clear consequence.","zh":"這個短語指出清楚後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"melting glaciers","meaning":"冰川融化","examples":[{"en":"Melting glaciers contribute to sea-level rise.","zh":"冰川融化促成海平面上升。"},{"en":"Melting glaciers are glaciers that are losing ice as it turns into water.","zh":"冰川融化，是冰川的冰變成水而流失。"},{"en":"Photographs taken years apart can show melting glaciers retreating up a valley.","zh":"相隔多年拍攝的照片可以顯示冰川融化並沿山谷後退。"},{"en":"If melting glaciers release large amounts of water, oceans may rise gradually.","zh":"如果冰川融化釋放大量水，海洋可能逐漸上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ice loss from glaciers.","zh":"這個短語描述冰川的冰量流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a change in high tides","meaning":"潮汐高位變化","examples":[{"en":"A change in high tides is linked to sea-level rise.","zh":"潮汐高位變化與海平面上升有關。"},{"en":"A change in high tides means the highest sea level reached by the tide becomes different.","zh":"潮汐高位變化，指潮水達到的最高海水水平變得不同。"},{"en":"A coastal town may notice a change in high tides when water reaches roads more often.","zh":"當海水更常到達道路，沿岸城鎮可能注意到潮汐高位變化。"},{"en":"If high tides become higher, flooding risk can increase along the coast.","zh":"如果潮汐高位變高，沿岸水浸風險可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to changes in the upper level of tidal water.","zh":"這個短語指潮汐水位上限的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a major factor in","meaning":"……的主要因素","examples":[{"en":"Melting glaciers are a major factor in sea-level rise.","zh":"冰川融化是海平面上升的主要因素。"},{"en":"A major factor in something is an important cause or influence.","zh":"某事的主要因素，是重要原因或影響。"},{"en":"Sleep is a major factor in a student’s concentration.","zh":"睡眠是學生專注力的主要因素。"},{"en":"If melting glaciers are a major factor, reducing warming can help limit future sea-level rise.","zh":"如果冰川融化是主要因素，減少暖化就有助限制未來海平面上升。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies one important contributor.","zh":"這個短語指出一個重要貢獻因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sea-level rise","meaning":"海平面上升","examples":[{"en":"Sea-level rise threatens coastal and groundwater systems.","zh":"海平面上升威脅沿岸和地下水系統。"},{"en":"Sea-level rise is the increase in the average level of the ocean.","zh":"海平面上升，是海洋平均水位增加。"},{"en":"A fishing village may worry about sea-level rise if waves reach homes more often.","zh":"如果海浪更常到達民居，漁村可能擔心海平面上升。"},{"en":"If sea level rises, salt water may move into coastal land and groundwater.","zh":"如果海平面上升，鹹水可能進入沿岸土地和地下水。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to rising ocean height over time.","zh":"這個短語指海洋高度隨時間上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the trend of rising sea levels","meaning":"海平面上升趨勢","examples":[{"en":"The trend of rising sea levels threatens groundwater.","zh":"海平面上升趨勢威脅地下水。"},{"en":"The trend of rising sea levels means the continuing pattern of oceans getting higher.","zh":"海平面上升趨勢，指海洋水位持續變高的模式。"},{"en":"Coastal planners watch the trend of rising sea levels when deciding where homes can be built.","zh":"沿岸規劃者決定住宅可在哪裡建造時，會留意海平面上升趨勢。"},{"en":"If the trend continues, flood defences may need to be raised.","zh":"如果該趨勢持續，防洪設施可能需要加高。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the long-term direction of sea-level change.","zh":"這個短語強調海平面變化的長期方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"threaten the groundwater system","meaning":"威脅地下水系統","examples":[{"en":"Rising sea levels threaten the groundwater system.","zh":"海平面上升威脅地下水系統。"},{"en":"To threaten the groundwater system means to put underground water supplies at risk.","zh":"威脅地下水系統，指令地下水供應面臨風險。"},{"en":"Chemical waste can threaten the groundwater system if it leaks into the soil.","zh":"如果化學廢料滲入土壤，就可能威脅地下水系統。"},{"en":"If salty seawater enters groundwater, farms and towns may lose fresh water sources.","zh":"如果鹹海水進入地下水，農場和城鎮可能失去淡水來源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes danger to underground water.","zh":"這個短語描述對地下水的危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"groundwater system","meaning":"地下水系統","examples":[{"en":"The groundwater system may become hypersaline.","zh":"地下水系統可能變得鹽度過高。"},{"en":"A groundwater system is the underground supply and movement of water stored in soil and rock.","zh":"地下水系統，是儲存在土壤和岩石中的地下水供應及流動。"},{"en":"Wells often depend on the groundwater system for clean water.","zh":"水井常依靠地下水系統提供清潔食水。"},{"en":"If the groundwater system becomes polluted or salty, agriculture and drinking water may suffer.","zh":"如果地下水系統受污染或變鹹，農業和飲用水可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to water below the ground.","zh":"這個短語指地底下的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make groundwater hypersaline","meaning":"令地下水鹽度過高","examples":[{"en":"Rising sea levels may make groundwater hypersaline.","zh":"海平面上升可能令地下水鹽度過高。"},{"en":"To make groundwater hypersaline means to cause underground water to become extremely salty.","zh":"令地下水鹽度過高，指使地下水變得極鹹。"},{"en":"If seawater enters a coastal well, it can make the groundwater too salty to drink.","zh":"如果海水進入沿岸水井，就可能令地下水鹹到不能飲用。"},{"en":"If groundwater becomes hypersaline, crops may grow poorly or die.","zh":"如果地下水鹽度過高，農作物可能生長不良或死亡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes salt contamination of underground water.","zh":"這個短語描述地下水受鹽分污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reduce agricultural production","meaning":"降低農業產量","examples":[{"en":"Hypersaline groundwater may reduce agricultural production.","zh":"鹽度過高的地下水可能降低農業產量。"},{"en":"To reduce agricultural production means to lower the amount of food or crops produced by farming.","zh":"降低農業產量，指減少農業生產的食物或農作物數量。"},{"en":"Plant disease can reduce agricultural production if it spreads across many fields.","zh":"如果植物疾病蔓延到許多田地，就可能降低農業產量。"},{"en":"If irrigation water becomes salty, farms may produce fewer crops.","zh":"如果灌溉水變鹹，農場可能產出較少農作物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a fall in farming output.","zh":"這個短語描述農業產出下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"counter this trend","meaning":"應對這趨勢","examples":[{"en":"Experts believe New Zealand must counter this trend.","zh":"專家認為新西蘭必須應對這趨勢。"},{"en":"To counter this trend means to take action against a developing pattern or direction.","zh":"應對這趨勢，指採取行動抵抗正在發展的模式或方向。"},{"en":"A school may counter a trend of late homework by offering study support after class.","zh":"學校可能透過課後學習支援，應對遲交功課的趨勢。"},{"en":"If sea levels are rising, communities may counter the trend with planning and coastal protection.","zh":"如果海平面正在上升，社區可能透過規劃和海岸保護應對這趨勢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active response to an unwanted development.","zh":"這個短語描述對不想見到的發展作出主動回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take a longer-term view of","meaning":"對……採取較長遠的看法","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand may need to take a longer-term view of sea-level change.","zh":"新西蘭可能需要對海平面變化採取較長遠的看法。"},{"en":"To take a longer-term view of something means to think about its effects over many years.","zh":"對某事採取較長遠的看法，指思考它多年後的影響。"},{"en":"Families take a longer-term view of money when they save for education or retirement.","zh":"家庭為教育或退休儲蓄時，就是對金錢採取較長遠的看法。"},{"en":"If coastal change happens slowly, short-term planning may not be enough.","zh":"如果海岸變化緩慢發生，短期規劃可能不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase encourages planning beyond immediate problems.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵超越即時問題作規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sea-level change","meaning":"海平面變化","examples":[{"en":"Experts recommend a longer-term view of sea-level change.","zh":"專家建議對海平面變化採取較長遠看法。"},{"en":"Sea-level change means change in the height of the ocean over time.","zh":"海平面變化，指海洋高度隨時間改變。"},{"en":"Coastal engineers study sea-level change before designing flood barriers.","zh":"沿岸工程師設計防洪屏障前會研究海平面變化。"},{"en":"If sea-level change continues, old coastal maps may become less useful.","zh":"如果海平面變化持續，舊海岸地圖可能變得較不實用。"},{"en":"The phrase can refer to rising, falling, or shifting sea levels.","zh":"這個短語可以指海平面上升、下降或轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"coastal boundaries","meaning":"海岸邊界","examples":[{"en":"Coastal boundaries need to be upgraded and redefined.","zh":"海岸邊界需要被升級並重新界定。"},{"en":"Coastal boundaries are the lines or limits used to mark coastal land and sea-related zones.","zh":"海岸邊界，是用來標示沿岸土地和海洋相關區域的界線或限制。"},{"en":"A town may review coastal boundaries before allowing houses near the beach.","zh":"城鎮可能在准許海灘附近建屋前檢討海岸邊界。"},{"en":"If sea levels rise, old coastal boundaries may no longer protect people or property.","zh":"如果海平面上升，舊海岸邊界可能不再能保護人和財產。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to official limits along the coast.","zh":"這個短語指沿岸的官方界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be upgraded and redefined","meaning":"被升級並重新界定","examples":[{"en":"The coastal boundaries need to be upgraded and redefined.","zh":"海岸邊界需要被升級並重新界定。"},{"en":"To be upgraded and redefined means to be improved and given a new or clearer meaning or limit.","zh":"被升級並重新界定，指被改善，並被賦予新的或更清楚的意思或界限。"},{"en":"A school safety policy may be upgraded and redefined after a serious accident.","zh":"嚴重意外後，學校安全政策可能被升級並重新界定。"},{"en":"If coastal risks change, boundaries may need better standards and new definitions.","zh":"如果沿岸風險改變，邊界可能需要更好標準和新定義。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improvement plus clarification.","zh":"這個短語描述改善加澄清。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"There is no doubt that","meaning":"毫無疑問","examples":[{"en":"There is no doubt that global warming has affected New Zealand.","zh":"毫無疑問，全球暖化已影響新西蘭。"},{"en":"There is no doubt that means something is certain or strongly accepted.","zh":"毫無疑問，指某事是確定或被強烈接受的。"},{"en":"There is no doubt that regular reading improves vocabulary over time.","zh":"毫無疑問，定期閱讀會隨時間改善詞彙。"},{"en":"If evidence from farms, glaciers, and coastlines all points the same way, doubt becomes difficult.","zh":"如果來自農場、冰川和海岸線的證據都指向同一方向，就很難懷疑。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a confident statement.","zh":"這個短語引入有信心的陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in many aspects","meaning":"在許多方面","examples":[{"en":"Global warming has affected New Zealand in many aspects.","zh":"全球暖化在許多方面影響了新西蘭。"},{"en":"In many aspects means in many different ways or areas.","zh":"在許多方面，指以許多不同方式或在許多範圍內。"},{"en":"A new phone policy may affect school life in many aspects, including study, discipline, and communication.","zh":"新手機政策可能在學習、紀律和溝通等許多方面影響校園生活。"},{"en":"If warming affects farming, tourism, water, and wildlife, its influence is broad.","zh":"如果暖化影響農業、旅遊、水和野生動物，其影響就是廣泛的。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the effect is not limited to one area.","zh":"這個短語顯示影響不限於一個範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the response to","meaning":"對……的應對","examples":[{"en":"The response to global warming should involve local people and experts.","zh":"對全球暖化的應對應包括本地居民和專家。"},{"en":"The response to something is the action taken to deal with it.","zh":"對某事的應對，是為處理它而採取的行動。"},{"en":"A school’s response to bullying may include counselling, rules, and parent meetings.","zh":"學校對欺凌的應對可能包括輔導、規則和家長會議。"},{"en":"If global warming affects local areas differently, the response must include local knowledge.","zh":"如果全球暖化對不同本地地區有不同影響，應對就必須包括本地知識。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on action after a problem is recognised.","zh":"這個短語強調問題被認識後的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"以……為基礎","examples":[{"en":"The response should be based on joint efforts.","zh":"應對應以共同努力為基礎。"},{"en":"To be based on something means to use it as the foundation or main support.","zh":"以某事為基礎，指用它作為根基或主要支持。"},{"en":"A good essay should be based on clear evidence and logical explanation.","zh":"好文章應以清楚證據和合邏輯解釋為基礎。"},{"en":"If climate policy is based on joint efforts, more people can share responsibility.","zh":"如果氣候政策以共同努力為基礎，更多人就可以分擔責任。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the foundation of an idea or action.","zh":"這個短語指出想法或行動的根基。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"joint efforts","meaning":"共同努力","examples":[{"en":"The response should be based on the joint efforts of local people and experts.","zh":"應對應以本地居民和專家的共同努力為基礎。"},{"en":"Joint efforts are actions done together by different people or groups.","zh":"共同努力，是不同人或群體一起做出的行動。"},{"en":"A clean-up campaign succeeds through the joint efforts of students, teachers, and parents.","zh":"清潔運動透過學生、老師和家長的共同努力而成功。"},{"en":"If climate problems are complex, joint efforts can combine local experience with scientific knowledge.","zh":"如果氣候問題複雜，共同努力可以結合本地經驗和科學知識。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses cooperation.","zh":"這個短語強調合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"local people and experts","meaning":"本地居民和專家","examples":[{"en":"Local people and experts need to work together.","zh":"本地居民和專家需要合作。"},{"en":"Local people and experts means community members and trained specialists.","zh":"本地居民和專家，指社區成員和受過訓練的專業人士。"},{"en":"Local people may know which roads flood first, while experts may explain the climate data.","zh":"本地居民可能知道哪些道路最先水浸，而專家可能解釋氣候數據。"},{"en":"If both groups cooperate, solutions can be practical and scientifically informed.","zh":"如果兩個群體合作，解決方案就可以既實際又有科學根據。"},{"en":"The phrase combines lived experience with specialist knowledge.","zh":"這個短語結合生活經驗與專業知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"address difficult conditions","meaning":"應對困難情況","examples":[{"en":"The joint effort aims to address difficult conditions.","zh":"共同努力旨在應對困難情況。"},{"en":"To address difficult conditions means to deal with challenging situations directly.","zh":"應對困難情況，指直接處理具挑戰性的處境。"},{"en":"A school may address difficult conditions by offering support to students after a typhoon.","zh":"颱風後，學校可能透過提供支援來應對困難情況。"},{"en":"If farmers face drought and salty water, they need plans that address both problems.","zh":"如果農民面對乾旱和鹹水，就需要能同時處理兩個問題的計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase means respond to problems actively.","zh":"這個短語指主動回應問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"take a long-term approach","meaning":"採取長遠方法","examples":[{"en":"Farmers are taking a long-term approach to climate change.","zh":"農民正在對氣候變化採取長遠方法。"},{"en":"To take a long-term approach means to plan for future years, not only immediate needs.","zh":"採取長遠方法，指為未來多年規劃，而不只處理即時需要。"},{"en":"A student takes a long-term approach to English by reading every day for several years.","zh":"學生透過多年每天閱讀，對英語採取長遠方法。"},{"en":"If climate change continues, farmers need strategies that work beyond one season.","zh":"如果氣候變化持續，農民需要不只適用於一季的策略。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses future-focused planning.","zh":"這個短語強調面向未來的規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"multigenerational approach","meaning":"跨世代方法","examples":[{"en":"Farmers are taking a multigenerational approach to changing temperatures.","zh":"農民正在對不斷變化的氣溫採取跨世代方法。"},{"en":"A multigenerational approach considers the needs of several generations, not only people alive today.","zh":"跨世代方法，考慮幾代人的需要，而不只是今天活着的人。"},{"en":"A family business uses a multigenerational approach when it trains children to continue the work responsibly.","zh":"家族企業培訓子女負責任地延續事業時，就是使用跨世代方法。"},{"en":"If farms must survive future climate shifts, planning may need to cover children and grandchildren.","zh":"如果農場必須在未來氣候轉變中生存，規劃可能需要涵蓋子女和孫輩。"},{"en":"The phrase describes thinking across generations.","zh":"這個短語描述跨越世代思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"adjust breeds and species","meaning":"調整品種和物種","examples":[{"en":"Farmers adjust breeds and species to changing temperatures.","zh":"農民因應不斷變化的氣溫調整品種和物種。"},{"en":"To adjust breeds and species means to choose or change the kinds of animals or plants being raised or grown.","zh":"調整品種和物種，指選擇或改變飼養或種植的動植物種類。"},{"en":"A farmer may choose heat-tolerant crop species if summers become hotter.","zh":"如果夏季變得更熱，農民可能選擇耐熱農作物品種。"},{"en":"If temperatures change, old breeds may no longer grow or survive as well.","zh":"如果氣溫改變，舊品種可能不再同樣容易生長或生存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adapting farming choices.","zh":"這個短語描述調整農業選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"changing temperatures","meaning":"不斷變化的氣溫","examples":[{"en":"Farmers need to adapt to changing temperatures.","zh":"農民需要適應不斷變化的氣溫。"},{"en":"Changing temperatures are temperatures that are rising, falling, or becoming less predictable over time.","zh":"不斷變化的氣溫，是隨時間上升、下降或變得較難預測的氣溫。"},{"en":"Schools may change outdoor activity plans because of changing temperatures.","zh":"學校可能因不斷變化的氣溫而改變戶外活動安排。"},{"en":"If temperatures change during growing seasons, farmers may need new planting schedules.","zh":"如果氣溫在生長季節改變，農民可能需要新的播種時間表。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to temperature patterns that do not stay stable.","zh":"這個短語指不穩定的氣溫模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"agriculturists","meaning":"農學家","examples":[{"en":"Agriculturists are finding ways to protect the soil.","zh":"農學家正在尋找保護土壤的方法。"},{"en":"Agriculturists are experts who study or work in farming and crop production.","zh":"農學家，是研究或從事農業和農作物生產的專家。"},{"en":"Agriculturists may advise farmers on soil, irrigation, seeds, and pests.","zh":"農學家可能就土壤、灌溉、種子和害蟲向農民提供建議。"},{"en":"If climate change creates new farm problems, agriculturists help design practical solutions.","zh":"如果氣候變化帶來新的農業問題，農學家會幫助設計實際解決方案。"},{"en":"The word refers to agricultural specialists.","zh":"這個詞指農業專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"find ways to tackle","meaning":"找方法處理","examples":[{"en":"Agriculturists find ways to tackle climate-related soil problems.","zh":"農學家找方法處理與氣候有關的土壤問題。"},{"en":"To find ways to tackle something means to look for methods to deal with it.","zh":"找方法處理某事，指尋找處理它的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may find ways to tackle students’ fear of speaking English.","zh":"老師可能找方法處理學生害怕說英語的問題。"},{"en":"If soil dries out more often, experts must find ways to tackle water loss.","zh":"如果土壤更常乾涸，專家必須找方法處理水分流失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes searching for practical solutions.","zh":"這個短語描述尋找實際解決方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"problems climate change may cause","meaning":"氣候變化可能造成的問題","examples":[{"en":"Agriculturists study the problems climate change may cause for the soil.","zh":"農學家研究氣候變化可能對土壤造成的問題。"},{"en":"Problems climate change may cause are difficulties that may result from changing climate conditions.","zh":"氣候變化可能造成的問題，是由氣候狀況改變可能導致的困難。"},{"en":"Schools may discuss problems climate change may cause, such as heat stress and flooding.","zh":"學校可能討論氣候變化可能造成的問題，例如熱壓力和水浸。"},{"en":"If soil problems are caused by climate change, normal farming methods may need revision.","zh":"如果土壤問題由氣候變化造成，普通農業方法可能需要修訂。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies possible future effects of climate change.","zh":"這個短語指出氣候變化可能帶來的未來影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in broad terms","meaning":"概括而言","examples":[{"en":"In broad terms, the ecosystem’s resilience is expected to continue.","zh":"概括而言，生態系統的復原力預期會持續。"},{"en":"In broad terms means speaking generally, without going into small details.","zh":"概括而言，指一般地說，不深入細小細節。"},{"en":"In broad terms, a healthy diet includes enough vegetables, protein, and water.","zh":"概括而言，健康飲食包括足夠蔬菜、蛋白質和水。"},{"en":"If a writer uses this phrase, they are giving the big picture first.","zh":"如果作者使用這個短語，就是先給出大局。"},{"en":"The phrase signals a general summary.","zh":"這個短語表示一般總結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"going forward","meaning":"展望未來","examples":[{"en":"Going forward, the ecosystem’s resilience is expected to continue.","zh":"展望未來，生態系統的復原力預期會持續。"},{"en":"Going forward means from now into the future.","zh":"展望未來，指由現在開始到未來。"},{"en":"Going forward, the class will practise speaking every Friday.","zh":"展望未來，班級會每逢星期五練習口語。"},{"en":"If climate pressure continues going forward, ecosystems will need to adapt.","zh":"如果氣候壓力未來持續，生態系統就需要適應。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces future direction.","zh":"這個短語引入未來方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"ecosystem","meaning":"生態系統","examples":[{"en":"The ecosystem’s long-established resilience is expected to continue.","zh":"生態系統長期形成的復原力預期會持續。"},{"en":"An ecosystem is a community of living things interacting with one another and their environment.","zh":"生態系統，是生物群落與彼此及環境互動形成的系統。"},{"en":"A pond ecosystem includes fish, insects, plants, water, sunlight, and soil.","zh":"池塘生態系統包括魚、昆蟲、植物、水、陽光和土壤。"},{"en":"If one part of an ecosystem changes, other parts may also be affected.","zh":"如果生態系統的一部分改變，其他部分也可能受影響。"},{"en":"The word refers to a connected natural system.","zh":"這個詞指互相連繫的自然系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"long-established resilience","meaning":"長期形成的復原力","examples":[{"en":"The ecosystem has long-established resilience.","zh":"生態系統有長期形成的復原力。"},{"en":"Long-established resilience means the ability to recover has developed and lasted for a long time.","zh":"長期形成的復原力，指恢復能力已經發展並持續很久。"},{"en":"A community with long-established resilience can recover after storms because people know how to help one another.","zh":"有長期形成復原力的社區，在風暴後可以恢復，因為人們知道如何互相幫助。"},{"en":"If an ecosystem has resilience, it may absorb some climate pressure without immediate collapse.","zh":"如果生態系統有復原力，它可能承受部分氣候壓力而不立即崩潰。"},{"en":"The phrase describes old and proven recovery strength.","zh":"這個短語描述已存在很久並經證明的恢復力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be expected to continue","meaning":"預期會持續","examples":[{"en":"The ecosystem’s resilience is expected to continue.","zh":"生態系統的復原力預期會持續。"},{"en":"To be expected to continue means people believe something will keep happening or existing.","zh":"預期會持續，指人們相信某事會繼續發生或存在。"},{"en":"Rain is expected to continue through the weekend if the forecast is correct.","zh":"如果天氣預報正確，雨預期會持續到週末。"},{"en":"If resilience is expected to continue, experts think the system can still cope for now.","zh":"如果復原力預期會持續，專家認為該系統目前仍能應付。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a predicted continuation.","zh":"這個短語描述預測中的延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"animals’ responses","meaning":"動物的反應","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are studying animals’ responses to global warming.","zh":"科學家正在研究動物對全球暖化的反應。"},{"en":"Animals’ responses are the ways animals react or adapt to a change.","zh":"動物的反應，是動物對變化作出回應或適應的方式。"},{"en":"Birds moving to cooler areas can be one of animals’ responses to rising temperatures.","zh":"鳥類移到較涼地方，可以是動物對氣溫上升的反應之一。"},{"en":"If animals’ responses are unusual, scientists may learn how climate affects behaviour.","zh":"如果動物反應不尋常，科學家可能了解氣候如何影響行為。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on animal reactions.","zh":"這個短語強調動物反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"adapt to global warming","meaning":"適應全球暖化","examples":[{"en":"Animals can adapt to global warming in unusual ways.","zh":"動物可以以不尋常的方式適應全球暖化。"},{"en":"To adapt to global warming means to change behaviour, timing, location, or biology in response to warming.","zh":"適應全球暖化，指因應變暖而改變行為、時間、地點或生理。"},{"en":"Farmers may adapt to global warming by planting crops that tolerate heat.","zh":"農民可能透過種植耐熱作物來適應全球暖化。"},{"en":"If animals cannot adapt quickly enough, their survival may be threatened.","zh":"如果動物不能足夠快地適應，其生存可能受威脅。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adjustment to rising temperatures.","zh":"這個短語描述對氣溫上升的調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in unusual ways","meaning":"以不尋常的方式","examples":[{"en":"Animals may respond to climate change in unusual ways.","zh":"動物可能以不尋常的方式回應氣候變化。"},{"en":"In unusual ways means in ways that are not common or expected.","zh":"以不尋常的方式，指以不常見或不預期的方式。"},{"en":"A student may remember vocabulary in unusual ways, such as drawing cartoons for each word.","zh":"學生可能以不尋常方式記詞彙，例如為每個詞畫漫畫。"},{"en":"If animals adapt in unusual ways, scientists may need to study them carefully.","zh":"如果動物以不尋常方式適應，科學家可能需要仔細研究牠們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unexpected methods or behaviours.","zh":"這個短語描述意想不到的方法或行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a study has examined","meaning":"一項研究考察了","examples":[{"en":"A study has examined sea turtles on northern beaches.","zh":"一項研究考察了北部海灘上的海龜。"},{"en":"A study has examined something means researchers have investigated or looked closely at it.","zh":"一項研究考察了某事，指研究者已調查或仔細觀察它。"},{"en":"A study has examined how homework time affects sleep among teenagers.","zh":"一項研究考察了功課時間如何影響青少年睡眠。"},{"en":"If a study examines turtles, it may collect data on nests, temperature, and hatchlings.","zh":"如果研究考察海龜，可能收集巢穴、溫度和幼龜數據。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a research topic.","zh":"這個短語引入研究主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"sea turtles","meaning":"海龜","examples":[{"en":"Sea turtles may be affected by rising nest temperatures.","zh":"海龜可能受到巢穴溫度上升影響。"},{"en":"Sea turtles are marine reptiles that live in the ocean and lay eggs on beaches.","zh":"海龜，是生活在海洋並在海灘產卵的海洋爬行動物。"},{"en":"Volunteers may protect sea turtle nests from people, dogs, and bright lights.","zh":"義工可能保護海龜巢穴免受人、狗和強光影響。"},{"en":"If beach temperatures rise, sea turtle hatchlings may be affected before they reach the sea.","zh":"如果海灘溫度上升，海龜幼體在到達海洋前就可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to turtles adapted to ocean life.","zh":"這個短語指適應海洋生活的龜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"northern beaches","meaning":"北部海灘","examples":[{"en":"The study examined sea turtles on northern beaches in New Zealand.","zh":"該研究考察了新西蘭北部海灘上的海龜。"},{"en":"Northern beaches are beaches located in the northern part of a place or country.","zh":"北部海灘，是位於某地方或國家北部的海灘。"},{"en":"Families may visit northern beaches because they are warmer and sunnier.","zh":"家庭可能到北部海灘，因為那裡較溫暖和陽光充足。"},{"en":"If northern beaches become warmer, turtle nests there may show climate effects first.","zh":"如果北部海灘變暖，當地海龜巢穴可能最先顯示氣候影響。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies coastal locations by direction.","zh":"這個短語按方向指出沿岸地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"become male or female","meaning":"變成雄性或雌性","examples":[{"en":"Sea turtles become male or female depending on nest temperature.","zh":"海龜視乎巢穴溫度而變成雄性或雌性。"},{"en":"To become male or female means to develop into one sex rather than the other.","zh":"變成雄性或雌性，指發展成其中一種性別。"},{"en":"Some animals’ sex is influenced by temperature while they develop in the egg.","zh":"一些動物在蛋中發育時，性別受溫度影響。"},{"en":"If nest temperature rises, the balance between males and females may change.","zh":"如果巢穴溫度上升，雄性與雌性之間的平衡可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sex development in young animals.","zh":"這個短語描述幼年動物的性別發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"depending on","meaning":"視乎；取決於","examples":[{"en":"Sea turtles become male or female depending on the nest temperature.","zh":"海龜變成雄性或雌性取決於巢穴溫度。"},{"en":"Depending on means determined by or affected by a particular condition.","zh":"取決於，指由某特定條件決定或受其影響。"},{"en":"Students may wear sports clothes or uniforms depending on the school schedule.","zh":"學生可能視乎學校時間表穿運動服或校服。"},{"en":"If turtle sex depends on temperature, warming beaches may affect population balance.","zh":"如果海龜性別取決於溫度，變暖的海灘可能影響種群平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the condition that controls the result.","zh":"這個短語引入控制結果的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"nest temperature","meaning":"巢穴溫度","examples":[{"en":"Nest temperature determines the sex of sea turtle hatchlings.","zh":"巢穴溫度決定海龜幼體的性別。"},{"en":"Nest temperature is the temperature inside or around an animal’s nest.","zh":"巢穴溫度，是動物巢穴內部或周圍的溫度。"},{"en":"Bird eggs may fail to develop if nest temperature becomes too low or too high.","zh":"如果巢穴溫度太低或太高，鳥蛋可能無法發育。"},{"en":"If sea turtle nest temperature rises, more hatchlings may develop as one sex.","zh":"如果海龜巢穴溫度上升，更多幼體可能發展成某一性別。"},{"en":"The phrase connects the nesting environment with animal development.","zh":"這個短語把築巢環境與動物發展連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"further research","meaning":"進一步研究","examples":[{"en":"Further research will examine how rising temperatures affect sea turtles.","zh":"進一步研究會考察不斷上升的氣溫如何影響海龜。"},{"en":"Further research means additional study done after earlier research.","zh":"進一步研究，指在早期研究之後進行的額外研究。"},{"en":"Further research may be needed when a first experiment gives mixed results.","zh":"當第一次實驗結果混雜，可能需要進一步研究。"},{"en":"If scientists do further research, they can confirm or correct earlier findings.","zh":"如果科學家做進一步研究，就可以確認或修正早期發現。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that investigation is continuing.","zh":"這個短語顯示調查仍在繼續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"find out how","meaning":"查明……如何","examples":[{"en":"Further research will find out how rising temperatures affect sex ratio.","zh":"進一步研究會查明不斷上升的氣溫如何影響性別比例。"},{"en":"To find out how something happens means to discover the process or method behind it.","zh":"查明某事如何發生，指發現其背後的過程或方法。"},{"en":"A student may do an experiment to find out how light affects plant growth.","zh":"學生可能做實驗，查明光線如何影響植物生長。"},{"en":"If scientists find out how temperature affects turtles, they can predict future risks better.","zh":"如果科學家查明溫度如何影響海龜，就能更好預測未來風險。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on discovering an explanation.","zh":"這個短語強調發現解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"rising temperatures","meaning":"不斷上升的氣溫","examples":[{"en":"Rising temperatures may affect the sex ratio of sea turtles.","zh":"不斷上升的氣溫可能影響海龜的性別比例。"},{"en":"Rising temperatures are temperatures that are increasing over time.","zh":"不斷上升的氣溫，是隨時間增加的氣溫。"},{"en":"Rising temperatures can make outdoor sports more dangerous during summer.","zh":"不斷上升的氣溫可以令夏季戶外運動更危險。"},{"en":"If temperatures rise around turtle nests, the sex of hatchlings may be affected.","zh":"如果海龜巢穴周圍氣溫上升，幼體性別可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a warming trend.","zh":"這個短語描述變暖趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"sex ratio","meaning":"性別比例","examples":[{"en":"Scientists want to know how rising temperatures affect the sex ratio.","zh":"科學家想知道不斷上升的氣溫如何影響性別比例。"},{"en":"Sex ratio is the balance or proportion of males and females in a group.","zh":"性別比例，是一個群體中雄性和雌性或男性和女性的平衡或比例。"},{"en":"A class with 15 boys and 15 girls has an equal sex ratio.","zh":"一班有15名男生和15名女生，就是性別比例相等。"},{"en":"If climate change shifts the sex ratio of turtles, future breeding may be affected.","zh":"如果氣候變化改變海龜的性別比例，未來繁殖可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the male-female balance.","zh":"這個短語指雌雄或男女平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"determine the sex of","meaning":"決定……的性別","examples":[{"en":"Nest temperature determines the sex of hatchlings.","zh":"巢穴溫度決定幼體的性別。"},{"en":"To determine the sex of an animal means to decide or control whether it becomes male or female.","zh":"決定某動物的性別，指決定或控制它變成雄性還是雌性。"},{"en":"In some reptiles, egg temperature can determine the sex of the young.","zh":"在一些爬行動物中，蛋的溫度可以決定幼體性別。"},{"en":"If heat determines sex, warmer beaches may change future animal populations.","zh":"如果熱力決定性別，較暖海灘可能改變未來動物種群。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what controls sex development.","zh":"這個短語描述控制性別發展的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"hatchlings","meaning":"剛孵化的幼體；幼龜","examples":[{"en":"The temperature of the nest determines the sex of hatchlings.","zh":"巢穴溫度決定剛孵化幼體的性別。"},{"en":"Hatchlings are young animals that have just come out of eggs.","zh":"剛孵化的幼體，是剛從蛋中出來的年幼動物。"},{"en":"Sea turtle hatchlings crawl from the beach to the ocean after leaving the nest.","zh":"海龜幼體離開巢穴後，會從海灘爬向海洋。"},{"en":"If hatchlings face high temperatures or predators, fewer may survive.","zh":"如果幼體面對高溫或捕食者，存活數量可能較少。"},{"en":"The word refers to newly hatched young animals.","zh":"這個詞指剛孵化的年幼動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"tackling the problems of","meaning":"處理……的問題","examples":[{"en":"Tackling the problems of global warming is never easy.","zh":"處理全球暖化的問題從來都不容易。"},{"en":"Tackling the problems of something means actively dealing with the difficulties it creates.","zh":"處理某事的問題，指主動應對它造成的困難。"},{"en":"A school may tackle the problems of bullying by setting rules and offering counselling.","zh":"學校可能透過制定規則和提供輔導處理欺凌問題。"},{"en":"If global warming creates many local problems, tackling them requires different strategies.","zh":"如果全球暖化造成許多本地問題，處理它們就需要不同策略。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical problem-solving.","zh":"這個短語描述實際解難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"never easy","meaning":"從來都不容易","examples":[{"en":"Tackling global warming is never easy in New Zealand.","zh":"在新西蘭處理全球暖化從來都不容易。"},{"en":"Never easy means always difficult or not simple at any time.","zh":"從來都不容易，指一直困難或任何時候都不簡單。"},{"en":"Learning a new language is never easy if students never practise outside class.","zh":"如果學生從不在課外練習，學習新語言從來都不容易。"},{"en":"If a problem involves science, money, and local communities, solving it is rarely simple.","zh":"如果問題涉及科學、金錢和本地社區，解決它很少會簡單。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses continuing difficulty.","zh":"這個短語強調持續困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"records show that","meaning":"記錄顯示","examples":[{"en":"Records show that global warming has different regional impacts.","zh":"記錄顯示全球暖化有不同地區影響。"},{"en":"Records show that means documented information provides evidence for something.","zh":"記錄顯示，指有記錄的資料為某事提供證據。"},{"en":"School records show that attendance improves after breakfast support begins.","zh":"學校記錄顯示，早餐支援開始後出席率改善。"},{"en":"If climate records show regional differences, one national average may hide local problems.","zh":"如果氣候記錄顯示地區差異，單一全國平均值可能隱藏本地問題。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence from recorded data.","zh":"這個短語引入來自記錄數據的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the slow process of","meaning":"……的緩慢過程","examples":[{"en":"The slow process of global warming may affect regions differently.","zh":"全球暖化的緩慢過程可能對不同地區有不同影響。"},{"en":"The slow process of something is a gradual development that takes a long time.","zh":"某事的緩慢過程，是需時很長的逐漸發展。"},{"en":"The slow process of learning pronunciation requires repeated listening and practice.","zh":"學習發音的緩慢過程需要反覆聆聽和練習。"},{"en":"If warming happens slowly, people may not notice its danger until effects accumulate.","zh":"如果暖化緩慢發生，人們可能直到影響累積後才注意到危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual change over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間逐步出現的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"different impacts on","meaning":"對……有不同影響","examples":[{"en":"Global warming may have different impacts on various regions.","zh":"全球暖化可能對各個地區有不同影響。"},{"en":"Different impacts on something means effects that vary depending on the place, group, or situation.","zh":"對某事有不同影響，指效果會按地點、群體或情況而不同。"},{"en":"Online learning has different impacts on confident students and shy students.","zh":"網上學習對自信學生和害羞學生有不同影響。"},{"en":"If climate change has different impacts on regions, national policy must allow local flexibility.","zh":"如果氣候變化對不同地區有不同影響，國家政策必須容許本地彈性。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights unequal effects.","zh":"這個短語突出影響不均。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"various regions","meaning":"各個地區","examples":[{"en":"Global warming may affect various regions in different ways.","zh":"全球暖化可能以不同方式影響各個地區。"},{"en":"Various regions means several different areas or parts of a country or world.","zh":"各個地區，指一個國家或世界中的幾個不同區域或部分。"},{"en":"A textbook may compare various regions by climate, population, and economy.","zh":"教科書可能按氣候、人口和經濟比較各個地區。"},{"en":"If various regions face different risks, one solution may not work everywhere.","zh":"如果各個地區面對不同風險，一個解決方案未必到處適用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to more than one geographic area.","zh":"這個短語指多於一個地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"account for only","meaning":"只佔","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand accounts for only 0.5 per cent of global carbon dioxide emissions.","zh":"新西蘭只佔全球二氧化碳排放的百分之零點五。"},{"en":"To account for only a percentage means to make up just that small share of the total.","zh":"只佔某百分比，指只構成總數中的那一小部分。"},{"en":"One student may account for only a small part of a class’s total absences.","zh":"一名學生可能只佔全班缺席總數的一小部分。"},{"en":"If a country accounts for only a small share of emissions, global cooperation is still needed.","zh":"如果一個國家只佔排放的一小部分，仍需要全球合作。"},{"en":"The phrase shows limited proportion.","zh":"這個短語顯示有限比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"carbon dioxide emissions","meaning":"二氧化碳排放","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand produces a small share of the world’s carbon dioxide emissions.","zh":"新西蘭產生全球二氧化碳排放中的一小部分。"},{"en":"Carbon dioxide emissions are releases of carbon dioxide gas into the air.","zh":"二氧化碳排放，是二氧化碳氣體被釋放到空氣中。"},{"en":"Cars, factories, and power stations can produce carbon dioxide emissions.","zh":"汽車、工廠和發電站都可能產生二氧化碳排放。"},{"en":"If carbon dioxide emissions increase, global warming can become worse.","zh":"如果二氧化碳排放增加，全球暖化可能惡化。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to climate-related gas pollution.","zh":"這個短語指與氣候相關的氣體污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"meet government standards","meaning":"符合政府標準","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand’s emissions meet government standards.","zh":"新西蘭的排放符合政府標準。"},{"en":"To meet government standards means to satisfy official rules or required levels set by the government.","zh":"符合政府標準，指滿足政府制定的官方規則或要求水平。"},{"en":"A restaurant must meet government standards for food safety.","zh":"餐廳必須符合食品安全的政府標準。"},{"en":"If emissions meet standards, they are legally acceptable, but the wider climate problem may remain.","zh":"如果排放符合標準，它們在法律上可以接受，但更廣泛氣候問題可能仍存在。"},{"en":"The phrase describes compliance with official rules.","zh":"這個短語描述遵守官方規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the tip of the iceberg","meaning":"冰山一角","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand’s efforts are only the tip of the iceberg.","zh":"新西蘭的努力只是冰山一角。"},{"en":"The tip of the iceberg is the small visible part of a much larger problem or situation.","zh":"冰山一角，是一個更大問題或情況中可見的小部分。"},{"en":"A few late homework cases may be the tip of the iceberg if many students are struggling silently.","zh":"如果許多學生默默掙扎，幾宗遲交功課可能只是冰山一角。"},{"en":"If one country acts alone, its efforts may reveal only a small part of the global work needed.","zh":"如果一個國家單獨行動，其努力可能只顯示全球所需工作的很小部分。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests there is much more beneath the surface.","zh":"這個短語暗示表面之下還有更多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"remain a global issue","meaning":"仍然是全球議題","examples":[{"en":"Global warming remains a global issue.","zh":"全球暖化仍然是全球議題。"},{"en":"To remain a global issue means to continue being a problem affecting the whole world.","zh":"仍然是全球議題，指繼續是一個影響全世界的問題。"},{"en":"Plastic pollution remains a global issue because oceans connect many countries.","zh":"塑膠污染仍然是全球議題，因為海洋連接許多國家。"},{"en":"If one country reduces emissions but others do not, the problem still crosses borders.","zh":"如果一個國家減排而其他國家沒有，問題仍會跨越邊界。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the issue is not only local.","zh":"這個短語強調該議題不只是本地問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"uncertain future","meaning":"不明朗的未來","examples":[{"en":"Global warming remains a global issue with an uncertain future.","zh":"全球暖化仍是一個有不明朗未來的全球議題。"},{"en":"An uncertain future is a future that cannot be predicted clearly.","zh":"不明朗的未來，是不能清楚預測的未來。"},{"en":"A student may face an uncertain future when choosing between several career paths.","zh":"學生在幾條職業路徑之間選擇時，可能面對不明朗的未來。"},{"en":"If climate outcomes depend on human action, the future remains uncertain.","zh":"如果氣候結果取決於人類行動，未來仍然不明朗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lack of clear prediction.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏清晰預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生為每條問題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the option letter that matches the right answer.","zh":"選出正確字母，指選擇與正確答案相符的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice question, students may choose A, B, C, or D.","zh":"在選擇題中，學生可能選 A、B、C 或 D。"},{"en":"If students find evidence in the passage first, they can choose the correct letter more accurately.","zh":"如果學生先在文章中找到證據，就能更準確選出正確字母。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"write the correct letter in boxes","meaning":"在方格內寫上正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students write the correct letter in boxes on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生在答題紙方格內寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"To write the correct letter in boxes means to put the chosen option letter in the official answer spaces.","zh":"在方格內寫上正確字母，指把所選選項字母填入正式答案位置。"},{"en":"A student should write “C” in the box if option C is correct.","zh":"如果選項 C 正確，學生應在方格內寫 “C”。"},{"en":"If the letter is written in the wrong box, the answer may be marked incorrectly.","zh":"如果字母寫在錯誤方格，答案可能被錯誤評分。"},{"en":"The phrase tells students exactly where to record answers.","zh":"這個短語清楚告訴學生在哪裡記錄答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the main idea of","meaning":"……的主要意思","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for the main idea of the first paragraph.","zh":"題目問第一段的主要意思。"},{"en":"The main idea of a paragraph is its central message or most important point.","zh":"某段的主要意思，是其核心信息或最重要觀點。"},{"en":"The main idea of a story may be that friendship requires honesty.","zh":"一個故事的主要意思可能是友誼需要誠實。"},{"en":"If students understand the main idea, details become easier to organise.","zh":"如果學生理解主要意思，細節就更容易整理。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for the big point, not a small example.","zh":"這個短語問的是大重點，而不是小例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"increase less than","meaning":"增幅少於……","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand’s temperature may increase less than that of other regions.","zh":"新西蘭氣溫增幅可能少於其他地區。"},{"en":"To increase less than something means to rise by a smaller amount.","zh":"增幅少於某事，指上升幅度較小。"},{"en":"A student’s expenses may increase less than their friend’s if they live at home.","zh":"如果學生住在家中，其開支增幅可能少於朋友。"},{"en":"If New Zealand warms less than polar areas, the surrounding ocean may be a reason.","zh":"如果新西蘭升溫少於極地地區，周邊海洋可能是原因。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the size of increases.","zh":"這個短語比較增幅大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"close location to","meaning":"接近……的位置","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand’s close location to the polar region affects its climate.","zh":"新西蘭接近極地地區的位置影響其氣候。"},{"en":"Close location to a place means being geographically near that place.","zh":"接近某地的位置，指地理上靠近該地。"},{"en":"A shop’s close location to a school may bring many student customers.","zh":"商店接近學校的位置可能帶來許多學生顧客。"},{"en":"If a country has a close location to polar areas, polar climate patterns may influence it.","zh":"如果一個國家位置接近極地地區，極地氣候模式可能影響它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes nearness in position.","zh":"這個短語描述位置上的接近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"high air quality","meaning":"高空氣質素","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions high air quality as a possible answer choice.","zh":"題目提到高空氣質素作為可能答案選項。"},{"en":"High air quality means the air is clean and contains low levels of harmful pollution.","zh":"高空氣質素，指空氣清潔，含有較低水平的有害污染。"},{"en":"A park with few cars nearby may have high air quality.","zh":"附近車輛很少的公園可能有高空氣質素。"},{"en":"If air quality is high, people may find it easier to breathe and exercise outdoors.","zh":"如果空氣質素高，人們可能更容易在戶外呼吸和運動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes clean and healthy air conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述清潔健康的空氣狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be surrounded by sea","meaning":"被海洋包圍","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand is surrounded by sea.","zh":"新西蘭被海洋包圍。"},{"en":"To be surrounded by sea means to have ocean water on all or most sides.","zh":"被海洋包圍，指四周或大部分周邊都有海水。"},{"en":"An island is surrounded by sea, so travel often depends on boats or planes.","zh":"島嶼被海洋包圍，因此交通常依靠船或飛機。"},{"en":"If a country is surrounded by sea, the ocean can strongly influence its climate.","zh":"如果一個國家被海洋包圍，海洋可以強烈影響其氣候。"},{"en":"The phrase describes island-like geography.","zh":"這個短語描述島嶼式地理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"one effect of","meaning":"……的一個影響","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about one effect of the wind belt.","zh":"題目問風帶的一個影響。"},{"en":"One effect of something means one result or consequence caused by it.","zh":"某事的一個影響，指由它造成的一個結果或後果。"},{"en":"One effect of heavy rain is slower traffic.","zh":"大雨的一個影響是交通較慢。"},{"en":"If the wind belt changes rainfall, that is one effect of the climate pattern.","zh":"如果風帶改變降雨，那就是該氣候模式的一個影響。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for a single result among several possible results.","zh":"這個短語要求在多個可能結果中找出一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contain more moisture","meaning":"含有更多水分","examples":[{"en":"Winds may contain more moisture in some seasons.","zh":"某些季節的風可能含有更多水分。"},{"en":"To contain more moisture means to hold a larger amount of water vapour or dampness.","zh":"含有更多水分，指含有較大量水蒸氣或濕氣。"},{"en":"Warm bathroom air can contain more moisture after a hot shower.","zh":"熱水澡後，浴室暖空氣可以含有更多水分。"},{"en":"If winds contain more moisture, they may bring more rain to nearby land.","zh":"如果風含有更多水分，就可能為附近陸地帶來更多雨。"},{"en":"The phrase describes water held in air.","zh":"這個短語描述空氣中所含的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"hotter months of the year","meaning":"一年中較熱的月份","examples":[{"en":"Droughts may become more serious in the hotter months of the year.","zh":"乾旱在一年中較熱的月份可能變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"The hotter months of the year are the parts of the year when temperatures are higher.","zh":"一年中較熱的月份，是氣溫較高的時期。"},{"en":"In many places, July and August are hotter months of the year.","zh":"在許多地方，七月和八月是一年中較熱的月份。"},{"en":"If drought happens during hotter months, water evaporates faster and crops suffer more.","zh":"如果乾旱發生在較熱月份，水分蒸發更快，農作物受害更大。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the warmer season by temperature.","zh":"這個短語按氣溫指出較暖季節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"as a result of","meaning":"由於；因為","examples":[{"en":"Agricultural production may fall as a result of drought.","zh":"農業生產可能由於乾旱而下降。"},{"en":"As a result of means because of something or as its consequence.","zh":"由於某事，指因它或作為它的後果。"},{"en":"A student may miss school as a result of illness.","zh":"學生可能因病缺課。"},{"en":"If crops fail as a result of drought, food supply and income may fall.","zh":"如果農作物因乾旱失收，食物供應和收入可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the cause of a result.","zh":"這個短語引入結果的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"recorded its lowest productivity","meaning":"錄得最低生產力","examples":[{"en":"The soil was described as having recorded its lowest productivity.","zh":"土壤被描述為錄得最低生產力。"},{"en":"To record its lowest productivity means to reach the lowest measured level of output or usefulness.","zh":"錄得最低生產力，指達到量度到的最低產出或效用水平。"},{"en":"A factory may record its lowest productivity if machines break down for several days.","zh":"如果機器故障數天，工廠可能錄得最低生產力。"},{"en":"If soil productivity reaches a low point, farmers may need to improve moisture and nutrients.","zh":"如果土壤生產力降至低點，農民可能需要改善水分和營養。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a measured minimum performance.","zh":"這個短語描述量度到的最低表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"ski resort","meaning":"滑雪度假村","examples":[{"en":"A ski resort may be affected by a rising snow line.","zh":"滑雪度假村可能受到雪線上升影響。"},{"en":"A ski resort is a place where people go skiing, usually with slopes, lifts, hotels, and equipment services.","zh":"滑雪度假村，是供人滑雪的地方，通常有雪坡、纜車、酒店和器材服務。"},{"en":"Families may visit a ski resort during winter holidays.","zh":"家庭可能在寒假到滑雪度假村。"},{"en":"If snow melts earlier, a ski resort may have fewer visitors and shorter seasons.","zh":"如果雪更早融化，滑雪度假村可能有較少遊客和較短季節。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a tourism site built around skiing.","zh":"這個短語指以滑雪為中心的旅遊地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"skiing altitude","meaning":"滑雪高度","examples":[{"en":"A rising snow line can affect the skiing altitude.","zh":"雪線上升可以影響滑雪高度。"},{"en":"Skiing altitude is the height above sea level where skiing can take place.","zh":"滑雪高度，是可以進行滑雪的海拔高度。"},{"en":"A resort at a higher skiing altitude may keep snow longer than a lower resort.","zh":"滑雪高度較高的度假村，可能比低海拔度假村更長時間保有積雪。"},{"en":"If warming raises the snow line, suitable skiing altitude may move higher.","zh":"如果暖化令雪線上升，適合滑雪的高度可能移向更高地方。"},{"en":"The phrase connects skiing with mountain height.","zh":"這個短語把滑雪與山地高度連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"make a profit","meaning":"賺取利潤","examples":[{"en":"Some ski resorts may struggle to make a profit.","zh":"一些滑雪度假村可能難以賺取利潤。"},{"en":"To make a profit means to earn more money than the cost of running a business.","zh":"賺取利潤，指賺得比營運企業成本更多的金錢。"},{"en":"A small shop makes a profit when sales are higher than rent, wages, and stock costs.","zh":"當小店銷售額高於租金、工資和貨品成本時，就能賺取利潤。"},{"en":"If a ski resort loses visitors, it may not make enough money to survive.","zh":"如果滑雪度假村失去遊客，可能賺不到足夠金錢生存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes financial success in business.","zh":"這個短語描述商業上的財務成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"cumulative changes over a long period of time","meaning":"長時間累積的變化","examples":[{"en":"Cumulative changes over a long period of time can alter glaciers.","zh":"長時間累積的變化可以改變冰川。"},{"en":"Cumulative changes over a long period of time are small changes that build up across many years.","zh":"長時間累積的變化，是多年中逐漸積聚的小變化。"},{"en":"Saving a little money every week creates cumulative changes over a long period of time.","zh":"每星期儲一點錢會形成長時間累積的變化。"},{"en":"If glaciers lose a little ice each year, long-term cumulative change can become dramatic.","zh":"如果冰川每年失去一點冰，長期累積變化可以變得巨大。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses gradual but powerful accumulation.","zh":"這個短語強調漸進但有力的累積。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"alterations in","meaning":"……的改變","examples":[{"en":"Cumulative changes may lead to alterations in glacier volume and thickness.","zh":"累積變化可能導致冰川體積和厚度的改變。"},{"en":"Alterations in something are changes made to or occurring in it.","zh":"某事的改變，是對它作出的或在它身上發生的變化。"},{"en":"Alterations in a school timetable can affect transport and lunch arrangements.","zh":"學校時間表的改變可以影響交通和午餐安排。"},{"en":"If glacier volume changes, alterations in ice movement may follow.","zh":"如果冰川體積改變，冰流的改變可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to say changes in.","zh":"這個短語是 changes in 的較正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"volume and thickness","meaning":"體積和厚度","examples":[{"en":"Changes in volume and thickness affect the flow of ice.","zh":"體積和厚度的變化影響冰流。"},{"en":"Volume and thickness mean how much space something occupies and how deep or thick it is.","zh":"體積和厚度，指某物佔據多少空間以及有多深或多厚。"},{"en":"A cake’s volume and thickness change when it rises in the oven.","zh":"蛋糕在焗爐中膨脹時，其體積和厚度會改變。"},{"en":"If a glacier loses volume and thickness, it may move and melt differently.","zh":"如果冰川失去體積和厚度，它可能以不同方式移動和融化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes two physical measurements.","zh":"這個短語描述兩種物理量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"mention NIWA","meaning":"提及 NIWA","examples":[{"en":"The writer mentions NIWA to support the discussion of glacier melting.","zh":"作者提及 NIWA，以支持關於冰川融化的討論。"},{"en":"To mention NIWA means to refer to that research organisation by name.","zh":"提及 NIWA，指以名稱提到該研究機構。"},{"en":"A student may mention a university study to support an argument in an essay.","zh":"學生可能提及大學研究，以支持文章中的論點。"},{"en":"If a writer mentions a scientific institute, the evidence may seem more credible.","zh":"如果作者提及科學研究所，證據可能看起來更可信。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using a named source in discussion.","zh":"這個短語描述在討論中使用具名來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a particular example","meaning":"一個具體例子","examples":[{"en":"The Mount Cook region is used as a particular example of ice loss.","zh":"庫克山地區被用作冰量流失的一個具體例子。"},{"en":"A particular example is one specific case used to illustrate a general idea.","zh":"一個具體例子，是用來說明一般想法的一個特定個案。"},{"en":"A teacher may use one student’s sentence as a particular example of a grammar mistake.","zh":"老師可能用一名學生的句子作為文法錯誤的具體例子。"},{"en":"If a general problem feels abstract, a particular example makes it easier to understand.","zh":"如果一般問題感覺抽象，具體例子會令它更容易理解。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a concrete case.","zh":"這個短語指出一個具體個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the effects of glacier melting","meaning":"冰川融化的影響","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains the effects of glacier melting.","zh":"文章解釋冰川融化的影響。"},{"en":"The effects of glacier melting are the results caused when glaciers lose ice.","zh":"冰川融化的影響，是冰川失去冰量時造成的結果。"},{"en":"The effects of glacier melting may include growing lakes, changing rivers, and rising sea levels.","zh":"冰川融化的影響可能包括湖泊擴大、河流改變和海平面上升。"},{"en":"If glaciers melt quickly, both local landscapes and global oceans may be affected.","zh":"如果冰川快速融化，本地景觀和全球海洋都可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on consequences of ice loss.","zh":"這個短語強調冰量流失的後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"emphasise the severity of","meaning":"強調……的嚴重性","examples":[{"en":"The example may emphasise the severity of ice loss.","zh":"這個例子可能強調冰量流失的嚴重性。"},{"en":"To emphasise the severity of something means to stress how serious it is.","zh":"強調某事的嚴重性，指突出它有多嚴重。"},{"en":"A doctor may show X-ray images to emphasise the severity of an injury.","zh":"醫生可能展示 X 光片來強調傷勢的嚴重性。"},{"en":"If a writer gives precise figures, they can emphasise how serious the problem is.","zh":"如果作者給出準確數字，就可以強調問題有多嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses attention on seriousness.","zh":"這個短語把注意力集中於嚴重程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"alert the reader to","meaning":"提醒讀者注意","examples":[{"en":"The data can alert the reader to the speed of glacier melting.","zh":"數據可以提醒讀者注意冰川融化的速度。"},{"en":"To alert the reader to something means to make the reader notice or become aware of it.","zh":"提醒讀者注意某事，指令讀者注意或意識到它。"},{"en":"A warning sign alerts drivers to a sharp bend ahead.","zh":"警告標誌提醒司機注意前方急彎。"},{"en":"If data alert readers to a rapid change, they may take the issue more seriously.","zh":"如果數據提醒讀者注意快速變化，他們可能更認真看待該議題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes drawing attention to an important point.","zh":"這個短語描述把注意力引向重要重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a uniform rate","meaning":"均勻速度","examples":[{"en":"The glacier may retreat at a uniform rate.","zh":"冰川可能以均勻速度後退。"},{"en":"A uniform rate is a steady speed that stays roughly the same over time.","zh":"均勻速度，是隨時間大致保持相同的穩定速度。"},{"en":"A machine fills bottles at a uniform rate if each bottle takes the same time.","zh":"如果機器每瓶所需時間相同，就是以均勻速度裝瓶。"},{"en":"If a glacier retreats at a uniform rate, future retreat may be easier to estimate.","zh":"如果冰川以均勻速度後退，未來後退情況可能較容易估計。"},{"en":"The phrase describes regular, even movement or change.","zh":"這個短語描述規律、平均的移動或變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill missing words in a shortened version of the passage.","zh":"完成摘要，指在文章的縮短版本中填入缺少的字詞。"},{"en":"Students complete a summary by reading the sentences before and after each gap.","zh":"學生透過閱讀每個空格前後的句子來完成摘要。"},{"en":"If answers must come from the passage, students should copy the exact words needed.","zh":"如果答案必須來自文章，學生應抄寫所需的準確字詞。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個詞","examples":[{"en":"The instructions say to use no more than two words.","zh":"指示說使用不多於兩個詞。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must contain one or two words only.","zh":"不多於兩個詞，指答案只能包含一個或兩個詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “sea level,” students should not write extra words around it.","zh":"如果答案是 “sea level”，學生不應在周圍加入額外詞語。"},{"en":"If students write three words, the answer may be wrong even when the idea is correct.","zh":"如果學生寫三個詞，即使意思正確，答案也可能錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"research data show that","meaning":"研究數據顯示","examples":[{"en":"Research data show that sea level is connected with climate change.","zh":"研究數據顯示海平面與氣候變化有關。"},{"en":"Research data show that means collected evidence indicates something.","zh":"研究數據顯示，指收集到的證據表明某事。"},{"en":"Research data show that students remember vocabulary better when they review it regularly.","zh":"研究數據顯示，學生定期複習詞彙時記得更好。"},{"en":"If data show a connection, the claim becomes stronger than personal opinion.","zh":"如果數據顯示某關聯，該主張就比個人意見更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence-based information.","zh":"這個短語引入以證據為基礎的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a close relationship with","meaning":"與……有密切關係","examples":[{"en":"Sea level has a close relationship with climate change.","zh":"海平面與氣候變化有密切關係。"},{"en":"A close relationship with something means a strong connection with it.","zh":"與某事有密切關係，指與它有強烈連繫。"},{"en":"Sleep has a close relationship with memory and mood.","zh":"睡眠與記憶和情緒有密切關係。"},{"en":"If sea level has a close relationship with climate change, warming can affect coastal risk.","zh":"如果海平面與氣候變化有密切關係，暖化就可以影響沿岸風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong connection.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the major reason for","meaning":"……的主要原因","examples":[{"en":"The major reason for sea-level rise is connected with melting glaciers.","zh":"海平面上升的主要原因與冰川融化有關。"},{"en":"The major reason for something is the main cause or explanation.","zh":"某事的主要原因，是最主要的原因或解釋。"},{"en":"The major reason for a student’s improvement may be regular practice.","zh":"學生進步的主要原因可能是定期練習。"},{"en":"If melting glaciers are the major reason, climate action must address ice loss.","zh":"如果冰川融化是主要原因，氣候行動就必須處理冰量流失。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the most important cause.","zh":"這個短語指出最重要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be connected with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Sea-level rise is connected with climate change.","zh":"海平面上升與氣候變化有關。"},{"en":"To be connected with something means to be related to it in some way.","zh":"與某事有關，指以某種方式與它相關。"},{"en":"A student’s stress may be connected with exams and lack of sleep.","zh":"學生壓力可能與考試和睡眠不足有關。"},{"en":"If sea-level rise is connected with warming, coastal planning must consider climate trends.","zh":"如果海平面上升與暖化有關，沿岸規劃就必須考慮氣候趨勢。"},{"en":"The phrase shows relationship or association.","zh":"這個短語顯示關係或關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"lead to a reduction in","meaning":"導致……減少","examples":[{"en":"Damage to groundwater may lead to a reduction in agricultural production.","zh":"地下水受損可能導致農業生產減少。"},{"en":"To lead to a reduction in something means to cause it to become smaller or lower.","zh":"導致某事減少，指造成它變小或降低。"},{"en":"Fewer buses may lead to a reduction in transport options for students.","zh":"巴士減少可能導致學生交通選擇減少。"},{"en":"If groundwater becomes salty, crop output may fall.","zh":"如果地下水變鹹，農作物產量可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a cause producing a decrease.","zh":"這個短語顯示原因造成下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"in the long run","meaning":"長遠而言","examples":[{"en":"In the long run, coastal boundaries may need to be upgraded.","zh":"長遠而言，海岸邊界可能需要被升級。"},{"en":"In the long run means over a long period of time, not immediately.","zh":"長遠而言，指在很長時間內，而不是立即。"},{"en":"Exercise may feel tiring now, but in the long run it improves health.","zh":"運動現在可能令人疲倦，但長遠而言會改善健康。"},{"en":"If sea levels keep rising, long-term coastal planning becomes necessary.","zh":"如果海平面持續上升，長期海岸規劃就變得必要。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on future consequences.","zh":"這個短語強調未來後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"reduce the effects of","meaning":"減少……的影響","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand may need to reduce the effects of changing sea levels.","zh":"新西蘭可能需要減少海平面變化的影響。"},{"en":"To reduce the effects of something means to make its impact smaller or less harmful.","zh":"減少某事的影響，指令其影響變小或較少有害。"},{"en":"Sunscreen can reduce the effects of strong sunlight on the skin.","zh":"防曬霜可以減少強烈陽光對皮膚的影響。"},{"en":"If coastal walls reduce flood effects, communities may be safer.","zh":"如果海堤減少水浸影響，社區可能更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limiting damage rather than removing the cause completely.","zh":"這個短語描述限制損害，而不是完全移除原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"agree with the claims of","meaning":"符合……的主張","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the claims of the writer.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否符合作者的主張。"},{"en":"To agree with the claims of someone means to match what that person says or argues.","zh":"符合某人的主張，指與該人所說或所論證的內容一致。"},{"en":"In a reading test, an answer agrees with the writer if it reflects the passage accurately.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，如果答案準確反映文章，它就符合作者觀點。"},{"en":"If a statement changes the writer’s meaning, it does not agree with the claim.","zh":"如果陳述改變作者意思，就不符合主張。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in reading questions about viewpoints.","zh":"這個短語用於關於觀點的閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the views of the writer.","zh":"一項陳述可能與作者的觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what they believe or argue.","zh":"與某人的觀點相矛盾，指說出與其信念或論點相反的內容。"},{"en":"If a passage supports public transport, saying cars are the only solution may contradict the writer’s view.","zh":"如果文章支持公共交通，說私家車是唯一方案可能與作者觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"If a statement contradicts the passage, the answer may be “No” or “False.”","zh":"如果陳述與文章矛盾，答案可能是 “No” 或 “False”。"},{"en":"The phrase describes conflict with an opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述與意見衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"It is impossible to say if the passage gives no clear evidence.","zh":"如果文章沒有提供清楚證據，就無法判斷。"},{"en":"To be impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"無法判斷，指沒有足夠資料作決定。"},{"en":"If a text never mentions price, it is impossible to say whether a product is expensive.","zh":"如果文本從未提到價格，就無法判斷產品是否昂貴。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students should not guess when the evidence is missing.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，當證據缺失時，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the answer cannot be judged from the text.","zh":"這個短語表示答案不能從文本判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"respond less to","meaning":"對……反應較少","examples":[{"en":"The statement compares how farmers and experts respond to climate change.","zh":"該陳述比較農民和專家如何回應氣候變化。"},{"en":"To respond less to something means to react to it less strongly or less actively than another person or group.","zh":"對某事反應較少，指比另一人或群體較不強烈或較不積極地回應它。"},{"en":"Some students respond less to written feedback than to face-to-face explanation.","zh":"有些學生對書面回饋的反應，少於面對面解釋。"},{"en":"If one group responds less to climate change, its preparation may be weaker.","zh":"如果某群體對氣候變化反應較少，其準備可能較弱。"},{"en":"The phrase compares levels of reaction.","zh":"這個短語比較反應程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"agricultural experts","meaning":"農業專家","examples":[{"en":"Agricultural experts study the effects of climate change on farming.","zh":"農業專家研究氣候變化對農業的影響。"},{"en":"Agricultural experts are specialists who understand crops, soil, livestock, and farm systems.","zh":"農業專家，是了解農作物、土壤、牲畜和農場系統的專門人士。"},{"en":"Farmers may ask agricultural experts which crop variety suits a dry season.","zh":"農民可能詢問農業專家哪種作物品種適合乾季。"},{"en":"If climate risks increase, agricultural experts can help design adaptation plans.","zh":"如果氣候風險增加，農業專家可以幫助設計適應計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to specialists in farming science and practice.","zh":"這個短語指農業科學和實務方面的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"agricultural sector","meaning":"農業界","examples":[{"en":"The agricultural sector must adapt to climate change.","zh":"農業界必須適應氣候變化。"},{"en":"The agricultural sector is the part of the economy involved in farming and food production.","zh":"農業界，是經濟中涉及農業和食物生產的部分。"},{"en":"The agricultural sector includes farms, farm workers, suppliers, and food-processing businesses.","zh":"農業界包括農場、農場工人、供應商和食品加工企業。"},{"en":"If the agricultural sector suffers, food supply and rural jobs may be affected.","zh":"如果農業界受損，食物供應和鄉郊就業可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the farming part of society and the economy.","zh":"這個短語指社會和經濟中的農業部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"resistant to dealing with","meaning":"抗拒處理……","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether the sector is resistant to dealing with climate change.","zh":"該陳述問農業界是否抗拒處理氣候變化。"},{"en":"To be resistant to dealing with something means to be unwilling to face or handle it.","zh":"抗拒處理某事，指不願面對或處理它。"},{"en":"A student may be resistant to dealing with grammar mistakes because correction feels uncomfortable.","zh":"學生可能抗拒處理文法錯誤，因為改正令人不舒服。"},{"en":"If an industry resists dealing with climate change, adaptation may be delayed.","zh":"如果某行業抗拒處理氣候變化，適應工作可能被延誤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reluctance to handle a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述不願處理問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"vulnerable to climate change","meaning":"容易受氣候變化影響","examples":[{"en":"Sea turtles may be vulnerable to climate change.","zh":"海龜可能容易受氣候變化影響。"},{"en":"Vulnerable to climate change means easily harmed or affected by changes in climate.","zh":"容易受氣候變化影響，指容易被氣候改變傷害或影響。"},{"en":"Coastal homes are vulnerable to climate change if storms and sea levels rise.","zh":"如果風暴和海平面上升，沿岸住宅就容易受氣候變化影響。"},{"en":"If turtle sex depends on temperature, warming nests make them vulnerable.","zh":"如果海龜性別取決於溫度，變暖的巢穴就令牠們脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes exposure to climate-related harm.","zh":"這個短語描述暴露於氣候相關傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"progress slowly","meaning":"緩慢推進","examples":[{"en":"Global warming may progress slowly but still have serious effects.","zh":"全球暖化可能緩慢推進，但仍有嚴重影響。"},{"en":"To progress slowly means to develop or move forward gradually over time.","zh":"緩慢推進，指隨時間逐漸發展或向前移動。"},{"en":"A student’s speaking skill may progress slowly if they practise only once a month.","zh":"如果學生每月只練習一次，口語能力可能緩慢進步。"},{"en":"If a problem progresses slowly, people may underestimate it until damage becomes visible.","zh":"如果問題緩慢推進，人們可能低估它，直到損害變得可見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual development.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"cut carbon dioxide emissions","meaning":"減少二氧化碳排放","examples":[{"en":"Countries may need to cut carbon dioxide emissions.","zh":"各國可能需要減少二氧化碳排放。"},{"en":"To cut carbon dioxide emissions means to reduce the amount of carbon dioxide released into the air.","zh":"減少二氧化碳排放，指降低釋放到空氣中的二氧化碳數量。"},{"en":"A city can cut carbon dioxide emissions by improving public transport and saving energy.","zh":"城市可以透過改善公共交通和節省能源來減少二氧化碳排放。"},{"en":"If emissions are cut, the pressure causing global warming may be reduced.","zh":"如果排放被減少，造成全球暖化的壓力可能降低。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lowering climate-related pollution.","zh":"這個短語描述降低與氣候有關的污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"solve the problem of","meaning":"解決……的問題","examples":[{"en":"Cutting emissions alone may not solve the problem of global warming.","zh":"單靠減排可能無法解決全球暖化的問題。"},{"en":"To solve the problem of something means to find a way to deal with it successfully.","zh":"解決某事的問題，指找到方法成功處理它。"},{"en":"A school may solve the problem of late homework by offering clearer deadlines and study support.","zh":"學校可能透過提供更清楚限期和學習支援來解決遲交功課問題。"},{"en":"If a problem has many causes, one action alone may not solve it completely.","zh":"如果問題有許多原因，單一行動未必能完全解決它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes finding an effective solution to a difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述為困難找到有效解決方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 46 - Global Warming in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":21}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 47":[{"front":"motivating drives","meaning":"動機驅動力","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses four motivating drives that influence employees’ behaviour.","zh":"文章討論四種影響員工行為的動機驅動力。"},{"en":"Motivating drives are deep needs or forces that push people to act.","zh":"Motivating drives 是推動人採取行動的深層需要或力量。"},{"en":"A student’s motivating drive may be the wish to improve, gain approval, or understand a subject.","zh":"學生的動機驅動力可能是想進步、獲得認可或理解某科目。"},{"en":"If managers ignore motivating drives, rewards may fail to change behaviour.","zh":"如果管理者忽視動機驅動力，獎勵可能未能改變行為。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the inner forces behind effort, choice, and persistence.","zh":"這個片語解釋努力、選擇和堅持背後的內在力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ways to motivate employees","meaning":"激勵員工的方法","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have been researching ways to motivate employees for many years.","zh":"科學家多年來一直研究激勵員工的方法。"},{"en":"Ways to motivate employees are methods used to increase workers’ energy, commitment, and effort.","zh":"Ways to motivate employees 是用來提升員工精力、投入和努力的方法。"},{"en":"A manager may motivate employees by giving clear goals, fair praise, and growth opportunities.","zh":"管理者可以透過清晰目標、公平讚賞和成長機會來激勵員工。"},{"en":"If employees feel ignored, even higher pay may not fully motivate them.","zh":"如果員工感到被忽視，即使加薪也未必能完全激勵他們。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical methods for improving workplace motivation.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於提升職場動機的實用方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for many years","meaning":"多年來","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have studied employee motivation for many years.","zh":"研究人員多年來一直研究員工動機。"},{"en":"For many years means over a long period of time.","zh":"For many years 指經過很長一段時間。"},{"en":"A teacher may use the same reading strategy for many years because it works well.","zh":"老師可能多年來使用同一種閱讀策略，因為它很有效。"},{"en":"If a problem has existed for many years, one quick solution may not be enough.","zh":"如果問題已存在多年，一個快速解決方案可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights duration and long-term attention.","zh":"這個片語強調持續時間和長期關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"much of this work","meaning":"這方面的大部分研究","examples":[{"en":"Much of this work focuses on relationships in organisations.","zh":"這方面的大部分研究聚焦於組織中的關係。"},{"en":"Much of this work means a large part of the research, effort, or writing being discussed.","zh":"Much of this work 指正在討論的研究、努力或寫作中的大部分。"},{"en":"Much of this work in education examines how students learn from feedback.","zh":"教育方面的大部分研究會探討學生如何從回饋中學習。"},{"en":"If much of this work ignores emotions, the explanation may be incomplete.","zh":"如果這方面的大部分研究忽略情緒，解釋可能不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a major share of a larger body of work.","zh":"這個片語指較大研究或工作中的主要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"focus on relationships","meaning":"聚焦於關係","examples":[{"en":"Much of the research focuses on relationships between employees and organisations.","zh":"大部分研究聚焦於員工與組織之間的關係。"},{"en":"To focus on relationships means to pay special attention to how people or groups connect.","zh":"To focus on relationships 指特別留意人或群體如何連繫。"},{"en":"A school counsellor may focus on relationships between classmates when solving bullying problems.","zh":"學校輔導員處理欺凌問題時，可能聚焦於同學之間的關係。"},{"en":"If workplace relationships are poor, employees may feel less loyal and less motivated.","zh":"如果職場關係欠佳，員工可能較不忠誠、較缺乏動力。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights connection, trust, and interaction between people or groups.","zh":"這個片語突出人或群體之間的連繫、信任和互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"seek to build","meaning":"旨在建立；嘗試建立","examples":[{"en":"The research seeks to build a comprehensive model for further study.","zh":"這項研究旨在建立一個供進一步研究的全面模型。"},{"en":"To seek to build something means to try or aim to create it.","zh":"To seek to build something 指嘗試或旨在創造某物。"},{"en":"A school may seek to build a stronger reading culture through daily reading time.","zh":"學校可能透過每日閱讀時間，旨在建立更強的閱讀文化。"},{"en":"If researchers seek to build a model, they collect evidence to explain a pattern.","zh":"如果研究人員嘗試建立模型，他們會收集證據來解釋模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an intentional effort to develop something.","zh":"這個片語描述有意識地發展某物的努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a comprehensive model","meaning":"全面模型","examples":[{"en":"Researchers want to build a comprehensive model of employee motivation.","zh":"研究人員想建立一個員工動機的全面模型。"},{"en":"A comprehensive model is a broad explanation that includes all major parts of a topic.","zh":"Comprehensive model 是包含某主題所有主要部分的廣泛解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may build a comprehensive model of writing by including ideas, grammar, structure, and tone.","zh":"老師可能透過包括想法、文法、結構和語氣，建立寫作的全面模型。"},{"en":"If a model leaves out important causes, it cannot explain the problem fully.","zh":"如果模型漏掉重要成因，它就不能完整解釋問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a complete framework rather than a narrow idea.","zh":"這個片語描述完整框架，而不是狹窄想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for further study","meaning":"供進一步研究","examples":[{"en":"The model is intended for further study of motivation.","zh":"這個模型旨在供進一步研究動機之用。"},{"en":"For further study means for more research, examination, or learning later.","zh":"For further study 指之後作更多研究、檢視或學習。"},{"en":"A teacher may mark difficult vocabulary for further study after class.","zh":"老師可能在課後標記困難詞彙，供進一步學習。"},{"en":"If an experiment raises new questions, researchers may keep the topic for further study.","zh":"如果實驗提出新問題，研究人員可能保留該題目供進一步研究。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the work is not finished yet.","zh":"這個片語顯示工作尚未完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"especially important when","meaning":"在……時尤其重要","examples":[{"en":"This research is especially important when teams are unmotivated.","zh":"當團隊缺乏動力時，這項研究尤其重要。"},{"en":"Especially important when means particularly necessary in a specific situation.","zh":"Especially important when 指在某特定情況下特別必要。"},{"en":"Clear instructions are especially important when students are doing a new task.","zh":"當學生做新任務時，清晰指示尤其重要。"},{"en":"If a team has low morale, understanding motivation becomes more urgent.","zh":"如果團隊士氣低落，理解動機就變得更迫切。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the situation in which something matters most.","zh":"這個片語突出某事最重要的情境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the business goal","meaning":"商業目標","examples":[{"en":"The business goal may be to turn unmotivated teams into productive ones.","zh":"商業目標可能是將缺乏動力的團隊轉化為高效團隊。"},{"en":"The business goal is the practical result an organisation wants to achieve.","zh":"Business goal 是組織想達成的實際結果。"},{"en":"A shop’s business goal may be to serve customers faster without lowering quality.","zh":"商店的商業目標可能是在不降低質素下更快服務顧客。"},{"en":"If a company’s goal is clear, managers can choose better methods to reach it.","zh":"如果公司目標清晰，管理者可以選擇更好方法達成它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the commercial or organisational target behind an action.","zh":"這個片語指行動背後的商業或組織目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"turn unmotivated teams into productive ones","meaning":"將缺乏動力的團隊轉化為高效團隊","examples":[{"en":"Managers may want to turn unmotivated teams into productive ones.","zh":"管理者可能想將缺乏動力的團隊轉化為高效團隊。"},{"en":"To turn unmotivated teams into productive ones means to help low-energy teams become effective and active.","zh":"To turn unmotivated teams into productive ones 指幫助低能量團隊變得有效而主動。"},{"en":"A coach may turn a discouraged sports team into a focused one through clear training and encouragement.","zh":"教練可能透過清晰訓練和鼓勵，把沮喪的運動隊轉化為專注團隊。"},{"en":"If workers understand their goals and feel valued, productivity may improve.","zh":"如果員工理解目標並感到被重視，生產力可能改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing poor team energy into useful performance.","zh":"這個片語描述把低落團隊能量轉化為有用表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"productive teams","meaning":"高效團隊","examples":[{"en":"Productive teams are valuable to any organisation.","zh":"高效團隊對任何組織都有價值。"},{"en":"Productive teams are groups that complete useful work efficiently and reliably.","zh":"Productive teams 是能高效且可靠地完成有用工作的群體。"},{"en":"A productive class project team divides tasks clearly and finishes before the deadline.","zh":"高效的班級專題小組會清晰分工，並在限期前完成。"},{"en":"If a team communicates well, it can waste less time and produce better results.","zh":"如果團隊溝通良好，它可以少浪費時間並產生更好結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes teams that turn effort into real outcomes.","zh":"這個片語描述能把努力轉化為實際成果的團隊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"such research has limitations","meaning":"這類研究有局限","examples":[{"en":"Such research has limitations because it may ignore deeper causes.","zh":"這類研究有局限，因為它可能忽略更深層成因。"},{"en":"Such research has limitations means this kind of study cannot explain everything.","zh":"Such research has limitations 指這類研究不能解釋所有事情。"},{"en":"A survey about student grades has limitations if it ignores sleep, family stress, and teaching quality.","zh":"如果關於學生成績的調查忽略睡眠、家庭壓力和教學質素，它就有局限。"},{"en":"If research looks only at rewards, it may miss emotional needs.","zh":"如果研究只看獎勵，就可能錯過情緒需要。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a study is useful but incomplete.","zh":"這個片語提醒研究有用但不完整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be like studying","meaning":"就像研究……","examples":[{"en":"Studying motivation without drives can be like studying a car without its engine.","zh":"研究動機卻不研究驅動力，就像研究汽車卻不研究引擎。"},{"en":"Be like studying means to compare one type of investigation with another similar one.","zh":"Be like studying 指把一種研究與另一種相似研究作比較。"},{"en":"Studying grammar without examples is like studying cooking without tasting food.","zh":"學文法卻沒有例子，就像學烹飪卻不試味。"},{"en":"If researchers miss the central mechanism, their study may feel incomplete.","zh":"如果研究人員錯過核心機制，其研究可能顯得不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase uses comparison to show what is missing.","zh":"這個片語用比較來顯示缺少了甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"without examining","meaning":"沒有檢視……","examples":[{"en":"Studying a car’s movement without examining its engine gives an incomplete picture.","zh":"研究汽車移動卻沒有檢視其引擎，只會得到不完整畫面。"},{"en":"Without examining means not looking closely at something important.","zh":"Without examining 指沒有仔細查看重要事物。"},{"en":"A teacher cannot understand poor marks without examining attendance and homework habits.","zh":"老師沒有檢視出席和功課習慣，就不能理解成績差的原因。"},{"en":"If managers judge performance without examining motivation, they may blame the wrong cause.","zh":"如果管理者判斷表現時沒有檢視動機，他們可能怪錯原因。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that careful investigation is missing.","zh":"這個片語顯示缺少仔細調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"drives people to succeed","meaning":"推動人們成功","examples":[{"en":"Motivation is what drives people to succeed.","zh":"動機就是推動人們成功的東西。"},{"en":"What drives people to succeed means the force that pushes them to work hard and reach goals.","zh":"What drives people to succeed 指推動人努力工作並達成目標的力量。"},{"en":"A student’s wish to help their family may drive them to succeed in school.","zh":"學生想幫助家人的願望可能推動他在學校成功。"},{"en":"If people have a strong reason to continue, they may persist through difficulty.","zh":"如果人有強烈理由繼續，他們可能在困難中堅持。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the inner push behind achievement.","zh":"這個片語解釋成就背後的內在推力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"play a vital role in","meaning":"在……中扮演關鍵角色","examples":[{"en":"Motivation plays a vital role in organisational development.","zh":"動機在組織發展中扮演關鍵角色。"},{"en":"To play a vital role in something means to be extremely important in making it happen.","zh":"To play a vital role in something 指對某事發生極其重要。"},{"en":"Sleep plays a vital role in students’ memory and concentration.","zh":"睡眠在學生記憶和專注中扮演關鍵角色。"},{"en":"If communication plays a vital role in teamwork, poor communication can weaken results.","zh":"如果溝通在團隊合作中扮演關鍵角色，溝通欠佳就會削弱成果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a factor that is central, not minor.","zh":"這個片語描述核心而非次要因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"enhancing organisational development","meaning":"促進組織發展","examples":[{"en":"Motivation plays a vital role in enhancing organisational development.","zh":"動機在促進組織發展中扮演關鍵角色。"},{"en":"Enhancing organisational development means improving how an organisation grows, learns, and performs.","zh":"Enhancing organisational development 指改善組織成長、學習和表現的方式。"},{"en":"Training can enhance organisational development by giving staff better skills.","zh":"培訓可以透過提升員工技能來促進組織發展。"},{"en":"If employees are motivated, they may share ideas and improve the company faster.","zh":"如果員工有動機，他們可能分享想法並令公司更快進步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strengthening an organisation’s long-term progress.","zh":"這個片語描述加強組織長期進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"study the motivation of employees","meaning":"研究員工的動機","examples":[{"en":"It is important to study the motivation of employees.","zh":"研究員工的動機很重要。"},{"en":"To study the motivation of employees means to examine why workers try, commit, or give up.","zh":"To study the motivation of employees 指研究員工為何努力、投入或放棄。"},{"en":"A manager may study motivation by asking staff what makes work meaningful.","zh":"管理者可能透過詢問員工甚麼令工作有意義來研究動機。"},{"en":"If a company understands motivation, it can design better jobs and rewards.","zh":"如果公司理解動機，它可以設計更好的工作和獎勵。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on understanding the reasons behind employee behaviour.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於理解員工行為背後的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be related to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Employee motivation is related to emotions and behaviour.","zh":"員工動機與情緒和行為有關。"},{"en":"To be related to something means to have a connection with it.","zh":"To be related to something 指與某事有連繫。"},{"en":"A student’s concentration may be related to sleep quality.","zh":"學生專注力可能與睡眠質素有關。"},{"en":"If motivation is related to emotions, managers should not treat workers like machines.","zh":"如果動機與情緒有關，管理者就不應把員工當成機器。"},{"en":"This phrase shows connection, though not always direct cause.","zh":"這個片語顯示關聯，但不一定是直接因果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"emotions and behaviour","meaning":"情緒和行為","examples":[{"en":"Motivation is closely connected to employees’ emotions and behaviour.","zh":"動機與員工的情緒和行為密切相關。"},{"en":"Emotions and behaviour means how people feel and how they act.","zh":"Emotions and behaviour 指人們的感受和行動方式。"},{"en":"A student’s emotions and behaviour may change before an important exam.","zh":"學生在重要考試前，情緒和行為可能改變。"},{"en":"If workers feel unfairly treated, their behaviour may become less cooperative.","zh":"如果員工覺得受到不公平對待，他們的行為可能變得較不合作。"},{"en":"This phrase links inner feelings with outward actions.","zh":"這個片語把內在感受與外在行動連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"recent studies","meaning":"近期研究","examples":[{"en":"Recent studies have identified four motivational drives.","zh":"近期研究識別出四種動機驅動力。"},{"en":"Recent studies are research projects completed or published not long ago.","zh":"Recent studies 是不久前完成或發表的研究項目。"},{"en":"Recent studies on sleep suggest that teenagers often need more rest than they get.","zh":"近期關於睡眠的研究顯示，青少年通常需要比實際得到更多的休息。"},{"en":"If recent studies show new evidence, older theories may need to change.","zh":"如果近期研究顯示新證據，舊理論可能需要改變。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces newer research findings.","zh":"這個片語引出較新的研究發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"identify four motivational drives","meaning":"識別出四種動機驅動力","examples":[{"en":"Recent studies have identified four motivational drives in employees.","zh":"近期研究在員工身上識別出四種動機驅動力。"},{"en":"To identify four motivational drives means to recognise and name four forces that motivate people.","zh":"To identify four motivational drives 指認出並命名四種推動人的力量。"},{"en":"A teacher may identify three common reasons students avoid speaking English.","zh":"老師可能識別出學生避免說英語的三個常見原因。"},{"en":"If researchers identify key drives, managers can design more suitable policies.","zh":"如果研究人員識別出關鍵驅動力，管理者可以設計更合適政策。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finding and naming important causes of motivation.","zh":"這個片語描述找出並命名動機的重要成因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"motivational drives","meaning":"動機驅動力","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains four motivational drives.","zh":"文章解釋四種動機驅動力。"},{"en":"Motivational drives are basic forces that shape what people want and how hard they try.","zh":"Motivational drives 是塑造人想要甚麼和有多努力的基本力量。"},{"en":"In school, curiosity, belonging, achievement, and safety can all act as motivational drives.","zh":"在學校，好奇心、歸屬感、成就和安全感都可以成為動機驅動力。"},{"en":"If a task satisfies several drives, people may work with more energy.","zh":"如果任務滿足幾種驅動力，人們可能更有精力工作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the deep reasons behind motivation.","zh":"這個片語指動機背後的深層原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the drive to acquire","meaning":"獲取的驅動力","examples":[{"en":"The drive to acquire is one of the four motivational drives.","zh":"獲取的驅動力是四種動機驅動力之一。"},{"en":"The drive to acquire is the desire to gain rewards, status, resources, or achievement.","zh":"The drive to acquire 是取得獎勵、地位、資源或成就的欲望。"},{"en":"A student may study hard because they want a scholarship or a high grade.","zh":"學生可能因想得到獎學金或高分而努力學習。"},{"en":"If workers see no chance of reward or progress, this drive may not be satisfied.","zh":"如果員工看不到獎勵或進步機會，這種驅動力可能得不到滿足。"},{"en":"This phrase explains motivation based on gaining something valued.","zh":"這個片語解釋基於取得有價值事物的動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the drive to bond","meaning":"建立連繫的驅動力","examples":[{"en":"The drive to bond helps employees feel connected to others.","zh":"建立連繫的驅動力幫助員工感到與他人連接。"},{"en":"The drive to bond is the need to form relationships and feel part of a group.","zh":"The drive to bond 是建立關係並感到屬於群體的需要。"},{"en":"A new student may feel motivated when classmates invite them to join a project.","zh":"當同學邀請新生加入專題時，新生可能感到更有動力。"},{"en":"If workers feel isolated, their loyalty and commitment may fall.","zh":"如果員工感到孤立，他們的忠誠和投入可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase explains motivation based on connection and belonging.","zh":"這個片語解釋基於連繫和歸屬的動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the drive to comprehend","meaning":"理解的驅動力","examples":[{"en":"The drive to comprehend motivates employees to understand and grow.","zh":"理解的驅動力激勵員工理解和成長。"},{"en":"The drive to comprehend is the desire to make sense of work, learn, and solve problems.","zh":"The drive to comprehend 是理解工作、學習和解決問題的欲望。"},{"en":"A student may enjoy science because experiments help them understand how things work.","zh":"學生可能喜歡科學，因為實驗幫助他理解事物如何運作。"},{"en":"If a job is meaningful and challenging, this drive can become stronger.","zh":"如果工作有意義且具挑戰性，這種驅動力可以變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase explains motivation based on learning and understanding.","zh":"這個片語解釋基於學習和理解的動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the drive to defend","meaning":"防衛的驅動力","examples":[{"en":"The drive to defend is linked to justice, fairness, and self-expression.","zh":"防衛的驅動力與公義、公平和自我表達有關。"},{"en":"The drive to defend is the need to protect oneself, one’s group, and what feels fair.","zh":"The drive to defend 是保護自己、群體以及自己認為公平之事的需要。"},{"en":"A worker may speak up if promotion decisions seem unfair.","zh":"如果晉升決定看似不公平，員工可能會發聲。"},{"en":"If people feel threatened or silenced, they may resist management decisions.","zh":"如果人們感到受威脅或被壓制，他們可能抗拒管理決定。"},{"en":"This phrase explains motivation based on protection, fairness, and voice.","zh":"這個片語解釋基於保護、公平和發聲的動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"must be met","meaning":"必須得到滿足","examples":[{"en":"The drive to acquire must be met to improve performance.","zh":"獲取的驅動力必須得到滿足，才能改善表現。"},{"en":"Must be met means a need or condition has to be satisfied.","zh":"Must be met 指需要或條件必須得到滿足。"},{"en":"A student’s need for rest must be met before they can concentrate well.","zh":"學生對休息的需要必須得到滿足，才能好好專注。"},{"en":"If employees’ basic drives are not met, motivation may remain weak.","zh":"如果員工的基本驅動力沒有得到滿足，動機可能仍然薄弱。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is necessary, not optional.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事是必要，而不是可選。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"optimise acquisition and achievement","meaning":"優化獲取與成就","examples":[{"en":"The drive to acquire must be met to optimise acquisition and achievement.","zh":"獲取的驅動力必須得到滿足，以優化獲取與成就。"},{"en":"To optimise acquisition and achievement means to help people gain rewards and perform at their best.","zh":"To optimise acquisition and achievement 指幫助人獲得獎勵並發揮最佳表現。"},{"en":"A school can optimise achievement by giving students clear targets and useful feedback.","zh":"學校可以透過清晰目標和有用回饋來優化成就。"},{"en":"If rewards match effort, employees may work harder and aim higher.","zh":"如果獎勵配合努力，員工可能更努力並追求更高目標。"},{"en":"This phrase connects motivation with gaining results and reaching goals.","zh":"這個片語把動機與取得成果和達成目標連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"acquisition and achievement","meaning":"獲取與成就","examples":[{"en":"Rewards can support both acquisition and achievement.","zh":"獎勵可以同時支持獲取與成就。"},{"en":"Acquisition and achievement means gaining something valuable and successfully reaching a goal.","zh":"Acquisition and achievement 指取得有價值的東西並成功達成目標。"},{"en":"A student may value both acquisition of knowledge and achievement in exams.","zh":"學生可能同時重視知識獲取和考試成就。"},{"en":"If a workplace recognises achievement, employees may feel their effort is worthwhile.","zh":"如果職場認可成就，員工可能覺得自己的努力值得。"},{"en":"This phrase combines getting rewards with accomplishing meaningful results.","zh":"這個片語把取得獎勵與完成有意義成果結合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"outstanding performance","meaning":"出色表現","examples":[{"en":"Outstanding performance should be recognised by organisations.","zh":"組織應認可出色表現。"},{"en":"Outstanding performance is work that is much better than normal or expected.","zh":"Outstanding performance 是遠高於一般或預期的工作表現。"},{"en":"A student shows outstanding performance when they improve greatly and help classmates too.","zh":"當學生大幅進步並幫助同學時，他展現出色表現。"},{"en":"If outstanding performance is ignored, high achievers may feel discouraged.","zh":"如果出色表現被忽視，高表現者可能感到氣餒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes excellent work that deserves attention.","zh":"這個片語描述值得關注的優秀工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be recognised","meaning":"得到認可","examples":[{"en":"Employees are motivated when outstanding performance is recognised.","zh":"當出色表現得到認可，員工會更有動力。"},{"en":"To be recognised means to be noticed, valued, or officially acknowledged.","zh":"To be recognised 指被注意、重視或正式承認。"},{"en":"A student’s effort should be recognised even if the final mark is not perfect.","zh":"即使最終分數不完美，學生的努力也應得到認可。"},{"en":"If good work is recognised, people are more likely to keep trying.","zh":"如果好工作得到認可，人們較可能繼續努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving acknowledgement for value or effort.","zh":"這個片語描述因價值或努力而獲得承認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"benefits and career opportunities","meaning":"福利和事業發展機會","examples":[{"en":"Employees value benefits and career opportunities.","zh":"員工重視福利和事業發展機會。"},{"en":"Benefits and career opportunities are workplace rewards such as insurance, leave, promotion, and growth paths.","zh":"Benefits and career opportunities 是保險、假期、晉升和成長路徑等職場獎勵。"},{"en":"A graduate may choose a company because it offers training and promotion opportunities.","zh":"畢業生可能因公司提供培訓和晉升機會而選擇它。"},{"en":"If benefits are poor and growth is blocked, workers may leave.","zh":"如果福利差且成長受阻，員工可能離開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical rewards beyond basic salary.","zh":"這個片語描述基本薪酬以外的實際獎勵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be provided","meaning":"被提供","examples":[{"en":"Career opportunities should be provided to high-performing employees.","zh":"事業發展機會應被提供給高表現員工。"},{"en":"To be provided means to be given or made available.","zh":"To be provided 指被給予或可供使用。"},{"en":"Students learn better when clear examples are provided before an exercise.","zh":"如果練習前提供清晰例子，學生會學得更好。"},{"en":"If support is provided at the right time, people can perform more confidently.","zh":"如果支援在適當時間被提供，人們可以更有信心地表現。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on making something available to someone.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於讓某物可供某人使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a written letter of appreciation","meaning":"書面感謝信","examples":[{"en":"A written letter of appreciation can motivate employees strongly.","zh":"書面感謝信可以強烈激勵員工。"},{"en":"A written letter of appreciation is a formal note thanking someone for good work.","zh":"Written letter of appreciation 是正式感謝某人良好工作的信件。"},{"en":"A teacher may give a student a letter of appreciation after they help organise an event.","zh":"學生協助籌辦活動後，老師可能給他一封書面感謝信。"},{"en":"If appreciation is personal and specific, it can feel more meaningful than a small reward.","zh":"如果感謝具個人化且具體，它可能比小獎勵更有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognition expressed in writing.","zh":"這個片語描述以書面形式表達的認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"generate more motivation than","meaning":"比……產生更多動力","examples":[{"en":"A letter of appreciation may generate more motivation than a cheque.","zh":"一封感謝信可能比一張支票產生更多動力。"},{"en":"To generate more motivation than something means to create a stronger desire to act than that other thing.","zh":"To generate more motivation than something 指比另一事物創造更強的行動欲望。"},{"en":"Honest praise may generate more motivation than a generic prize.","zh":"真誠讚賞可能比普通獎品產生更多動力。"},{"en":"If people value respect, recognition can motivate them more than money alone.","zh":"如果人們重視尊重，認可可以比單靠金錢更能激勵他們。"},{"en":"This phrase compares which factor creates stronger motivation.","zh":"這個片語比較哪個因素產生更強動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a thousand-dollar cheque","meaning":"一張一千美元的支票","examples":[{"en":"A written letter of appreciation may be more motivating than a thousand-dollar cheque.","zh":"書面感謝信可能比一張一千美元的支票更能激勵人。"},{"en":"A thousand-dollar cheque is a written payment worth one thousand dollars.","zh":"Thousand-dollar cheque 是價值一千美元的書面付款。"},{"en":"A worker may appreciate a cheque, but still want personal recognition for effort.","zh":"員工可能欣賞支票，但仍希望努力得到個人認可。"},{"en":"If money is given without respect, it may not create lasting motivation.","zh":"如果金錢在沒有尊重下給予，它可能不能創造持久動機。"},{"en":"This phrase is used as a concrete example of a financial reward.","zh":"這個片語被用作金錢獎勵的具體例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"act as an invisible force","meaning":"作為一股無形力量","examples":[{"en":"Appreciation can act as an invisible force in the workplace.","zh":"感謝可以在職場中作為一股無形力量。"},{"en":"To act as an invisible force means to influence people strongly even though it cannot be seen.","zh":"To act as an invisible force 指雖然看不見，卻強烈影響人。"},{"en":"Trust can act as an invisible force that helps a class work together smoothly.","zh":"信任可以作為一股無形力量，幫助班級順利合作。"},{"en":"If employees feel appreciated, that feeling may quietly guide their effort.","zh":"如果員工感到被欣賞，這種感覺可能默默引導他們的努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hidden influence on behaviour.","zh":"這個片語描述對行為的隱藏影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"boost engagement","meaning":"提升投入感","examples":[{"en":"Recognition can boost employee engagement.","zh":"認可可以提升員工投入感。"},{"en":"To boost engagement means to increase people’s interest, involvement, and commitment.","zh":"To boost engagement 指增加人的興趣、參與和投入。"},{"en":"A teacher can boost engagement by using real-life examples instead of abstract notes.","zh":"老師可以透過使用生活例子而不是抽象筆記來提升投入感。"},{"en":"If staff feel their work matters, they may participate more actively.","zh":"如果員工覺得自己的工作重要，他們可能更主動參與。"},{"en":"This phrase describes raising people’s level of involvement.","zh":"這個片語描述提高人的投入程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"successful organisations and leaders","meaning":"成功的組織和領袖","examples":[{"en":"Successful organisations and leaders understand different sources of motivation.","zh":"成功的組織和領袖理解不同動機來源。"},{"en":"Successful organisations and leaders are companies and managers that achieve goals and support people effectively.","zh":"Successful organisations and leaders 是能達成目標並有效支持人的公司和管理者。"},{"en":"A successful school leader knows that students need both discipline and encouragement.","zh":"成功的學校領袖知道學生既需要紀律，也需要鼓勵。"},{"en":"If leaders understand motivation, they can build stronger teams.","zh":"如果領袖理解動機，他們可以建立更強團隊。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to effective organisations and the people who guide them.","zh":"這個片語指有效的組織以及引導它們的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"focus not only on…, but also on…","meaning":"不但聚焦於……，也聚焦於……","examples":[{"en":"Leaders should focus not only on material rewards, but also on other motivators.","zh":"領袖不但應聚焦於物質獎勵，也應聚焦於其他激勵因素。"},{"en":"Focus not only on A, but also on B means give attention to both things, not just the first one.","zh":"Focus not only on A, but also on B 指同時留意兩件事，而不只是第一件。"},{"en":"Students should focus not only on grammar, but also on ideas and organisation.","zh":"學生不但應聚焦於文法，也應聚焦於想法和組織。"},{"en":"If managers focus only on money, they may miss belonging, meaning, and fairness.","zh":"如果管理者只聚焦於金錢，他們可能錯過歸屬、意義和公平。"},{"en":"This structure helps show a wider and more balanced view.","zh":"這個結構幫助表達更廣泛和平衡的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"material rewards","meaning":"物質獎勵","examples":[{"en":"Material rewards alone may not be enough to motivate employees.","zh":"單靠物質獎勵可能不足以激勵員工。"},{"en":"Material rewards are physical or financial benefits such as money, gifts, or bonuses.","zh":"Material rewards 是金錢、禮物或花紅等實體或財務好處。"},{"en":"A student may receive a book voucher as a material reward for good attendance.","zh":"學生可能因出席良好而收到書券作為物質獎勵。"},{"en":"If workers need respect and meaning, money alone may not satisfy them.","zh":"如果員工需要尊重和意義，單靠金錢可能不能滿足他們。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts tangible rewards with emotional or social motivators.","zh":"這個片語把有形獎勵與情感或社會動機作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"organisational levers","meaning":"組織槓桿；組織推動因素","examples":[{"en":"Successful leaders use organisational levers to drive motivation.","zh":"成功領袖使用組織槓桿來推動動機。"},{"en":"Organisational levers are tools or systems a company can adjust to influence behaviour.","zh":"Organisational levers 是公司可調整以影響行為的工具或制度。"},{"en":"Training, rewards, job design, and communication can all be organisational levers.","zh":"培訓、獎勵、工作設計和溝通都可以是組織推動因素。"},{"en":"If the right lever is used, employees may feel more motivated and supported.","zh":"如果使用正確槓桿，員工可能感到更有動力和支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes management tools that can move people’s behaviour.","zh":"這個片語描述可以推動人行為的管理工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"drive motivation","meaning":"推動動機","examples":[{"en":"Different organisational levers can drive motivation.","zh":"不同組織槓桿可以推動動機。"},{"en":"To drive motivation means to create or strengthen people’s desire to act.","zh":"To drive motivation 指創造或加強人們行動的欲望。"},{"en":"Clear feedback can drive motivation because students know how to improve.","zh":"清晰回饋可以推動動機，因為學生知道如何改善。"},{"en":"If a reward system feels fair, it may drive stronger effort.","zh":"如果獎勵制度感覺公平，它可能推動更強努力。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what increases motivation.","zh":"這個片語解釋甚麼會增加動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"key to driving motivation","meaning":"推動動機的關鍵","examples":[{"en":"The drive to bond is key to driving motivation.","zh":"建立連繫的驅動力是推動動機的關鍵。"},{"en":"Key to driving motivation means especially important for increasing people’s willingness to act.","zh":"Key to driving motivation 指對增加人們行動意願尤其重要。"},{"en":"In a classroom, belonging may be key to driving motivation among shy students.","zh":"在課室中，歸屬感可能是推動害羞學生動機的關鍵。"},{"en":"If people feel accepted, they may try harder and stay longer.","zh":"如果人們感到被接納，他們可能更努力並留得更久。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a central factor behind motivation.","zh":"這個片語指出動機背後的核心因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bonds between people","meaning":"人與人之間的連繫","examples":[{"en":"There are many kinds of bonds between people.","zh":"人與人之間有許多種連繫。"},{"en":"Bonds between people are emotional connections such as trust, friendship, loyalty, or care.","zh":"Bonds between people 是信任、友誼、忠誠或關心等情感連接。"},{"en":"Team activities can build bonds between classmates who rarely speak to one another.","zh":"團隊活動可以建立平時少說話的同學之間的連繫。"},{"en":"If bonds are strong, people may help one another during pressure.","zh":"如果連繫強，人們可能在壓力下互相幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes human connections that hold groups together.","zh":"這個片語描述把群體凝聚起來的人際連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"friendship and family ties","meaning":"友誼和家庭紐帶","examples":[{"en":"Friendship and family ties are examples of bonds between people.","zh":"友誼和家庭紐帶是人與人之間連繫的例子。"},{"en":"Friendship and family ties are close relationships formed through friends and relatives.","zh":"Friendship and family ties 是透過朋友和親人形成的親密關係。"},{"en":"A student may rely on friendship and family ties when facing exam stress.","zh":"學生面對考試壓力時，可能依靠友誼和家庭紐帶。"},{"en":"If people move far from home, these ties may become harder to maintain.","zh":"如果人們搬到離家很遠，這些紐帶可能較難維持。"},{"en":"This phrase names two familiar forms of emotional connection.","zh":"這個片語命名兩種熟悉的情感連繫形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"within a company","meaning":"在公司內部","examples":[{"en":"Within a company, employees want to feel that they belong.","zh":"在公司內部，員工希望感到自己有歸屬感。"},{"en":"Within a company means inside the organisation or among its employees.","zh":"Within a company 指在組織內或員工之間。"},{"en":"Within a school, teachers and students may follow shared rules and routines.","zh":"在學校內部，老師和學生可能遵守共同規則和常規。"},{"en":"If communication is weak within a company, misunderstanding may spread quickly.","zh":"如果公司內部溝通薄弱，誤解可能迅速擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to what happens inside an organisation.","zh":"這個片語指組織內發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"feel that they belong","meaning":"感到自己有歸屬感","examples":[{"en":"Employees want to feel that they belong to the organisation.","zh":"員工希望感到自己屬於組織。"},{"en":"To feel that they belong means to feel accepted, included, and part of a group.","zh":"To feel that they belong 指感到被接納、被包括，並是群體一部分。"},{"en":"New students feel that they belong when classmates remember their names and invite them to join.","zh":"當同學記得新生名字並邀請他加入時，新生會感到自己有歸屬感。"},{"en":"If workers feel excluded, their commitment may weaken.","zh":"如果員工感到被排除，他們的投入可能減弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional inclusion and group identity.","zh":"這個片語描述情感上的融入和群體身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an essential part of","meaning":"……的重要一部分","examples":[{"en":"Employees want to feel that they are an essential part of the organisation.","zh":"員工希望感到自己是組織的重要一部分。"},{"en":"An essential part of something is a necessary and important part of it.","zh":"An essential part of something 是某事必要且重要的一部分。"},{"en":"Clear examples are an essential part of a good vocabulary lesson.","zh":"清晰例子是優質詞彙課的重要一部分。"},{"en":"If employees feel essential, they may take greater responsibility for results.","zh":"如果員工感到自己重要，他們可能對成果承擔更大責任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that is not optional or minor.","zh":"這個片語描述並非可有可無或次要的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sense of belonging","meaning":"歸屬感","examples":[{"en":"A sense of belonging can motivate employees.","zh":"歸屬感可以激勵員工。"},{"en":"A sense of belonging is the feeling that one is accepted and valued by a group.","zh":"Sense of belonging 是感到被群體接納和重視的感覺。"},{"en":"A student with a strong sense of belonging may be more willing to speak in class.","zh":"有強烈歸屬感的學生可能更願意在課堂發言。"},{"en":"If people lack belonging, they may withdraw from group activities.","zh":"如果人們缺乏歸屬感，他們可能退出群體活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the feeling of being part of a community.","zh":"這個片語描述成為社群一部分的感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"show the greatest commitment","meaning":"表現出最大的投入","examples":[{"en":"Employees show the greatest commitment when internal motivation guides them.","zh":"當內在動機引導員工時，他們會表現出最大的投入。"},{"en":"To show the greatest commitment means to display the strongest loyalty, effort, or dedication.","zh":"To show the greatest commitment 指展現最強忠誠、努力或奉獻。"},{"en":"A volunteer may show the greatest commitment when the cause feels personally meaningful.","zh":"當義工覺得使命對自己有意義時，他可能表現出最大的投入。"},{"en":"If employees believe in their work, they may stay engaged even during difficulties.","zh":"如果員工相信自己的工作，他們即使在困難中也可能保持投入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the highest level of dedication.","zh":"這個片語描述最高程度的奉獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"internal motivation","meaning":"內在動機","examples":[{"en":"Internal motivation can influence employees’ decisions and behaviour.","zh":"內在動機可以影響員工的決定和行為。"},{"en":"Internal motivation is motivation that comes from personal interest, values, or meaning.","zh":"Internal motivation 是來自個人興趣、價值或意義的動機。"},{"en":"A student may study history because they truly enjoy understanding the past.","zh":"學生可能因真正喜歡理解過去而學習歷史。"},{"en":"If internal motivation is strong, people may continue even without immediate rewards.","zh":"如果內在動機強，人們即使沒有即時獎勵也可能繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts inner drive with outside pressure or rewards.","zh":"這個片語把內在推動力與外在壓力或獎勵作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"influence the direction of","meaning":"影響……的方向","examples":[{"en":"Internal motivation influences the direction of employees’ decisions.","zh":"內在動機影響員工決定的方向。"},{"en":"To influence the direction of something means to affect where it goes or what choice it takes.","zh":"To influence the direction of something 指影響某事走向哪裏或採取甚麼選擇。"},{"en":"A teacher’s advice can influence the direction of a student’s career plan.","zh":"老師的建議可以影響學生職業規劃的方向。"},{"en":"If motivation changes, people may choose different goals and actions.","zh":"如果動機改變，人們可能選擇不同目標和行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shaping the path something takes.","zh":"這個片語描述塑造某事的路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"intensity and persistence","meaning":"強度和持續性","examples":[{"en":"Motivation affects the direction, intensity, and persistence of behaviour.","zh":"動機影響行為的方向、強度和持續性。"},{"en":"Intensity and persistence mean how strongly and how long someone keeps doing something.","zh":"Intensity and persistence 指某人做某事有多強烈以及維持多久。"},{"en":"A student with high intensity studies hard, while persistence keeps them working over months.","zh":"有高強度的學生會努力學習，而持續性令他持續數月工作。"},{"en":"If motivation is weak, effort may be low and short-lived.","zh":"如果動機薄弱，努力可能低且短暫。"},{"en":"This phrase measures both strength and staying power.","zh":"這個片語同時量度力度和持久力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"decisions and behaviour","meaning":"決定和行為","examples":[{"en":"Employee motivation influences decisions and behaviour within the company.","zh":"員工動機影響公司內部的決定和行為。"},{"en":"Decisions and behaviour means what people choose and how they act.","zh":"Decisions and behaviour 指人們選擇甚麼以及如何行動。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence can affect their decisions and behaviour during a speaking exam.","zh":"學生的信心可以影響他在口試中的決定和行為。"},{"en":"If workers feel trusted, they may choose to help others more often.","zh":"如果員工感到被信任，他們可能更常選擇幫助他人。"},{"en":"This phrase connects thinking, choosing, and acting.","zh":"這個片語把思考、選擇和行動連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"higher performance","meaning":"更高表現","examples":[{"en":"The drive to comprehend can motivate employees to higher performance.","zh":"理解的驅動力可以激勵員工達至更高表現。"},{"en":"Higher performance means better results, stronger effort, or improved quality of work.","zh":"Higher performance 指更好成果、更強努力或更高工作質素。"},{"en":"A student may reach higher performance after receiving clear feedback on mistakes.","zh":"學生在收到清晰錯誤回饋後，可能達至更高表現。"},{"en":"If work feels meaningful, employees may concentrate more and produce better results.","zh":"如果工作感覺有意義，員工可能更專注並產生更好成果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improvement beyond the usual level.","zh":"這個片語描述超越一般水平的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"setting stretch goals","meaning":"訂立挑戰性目標","examples":[{"en":"Setting stretch goals can have a major impact on performance.","zh":"訂立挑戰性目標可以對表現有重大影響。"},{"en":"Setting stretch goals means creating targets that are challenging but still possible.","zh":"Setting stretch goals 指訂立具挑戰性但仍可達成的目標。"},{"en":"A teacher may set a stretch goal for a student to write 300 words instead of 200.","zh":"老師可能為學生訂立挑戰性目標，要求寫300字而不是200字。"},{"en":"If goals are too easy, people may not grow; if too hard, they may give up.","zh":"如果目標太容易，人們可能不會成長；如果太難，則可能放棄。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using ambitious targets to push improvement.","zh":"這個片語描述用具野心的目標推動進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have a major impact on","meaning":"對……有重大影響","examples":[{"en":"Stretch goals can have a major impact on performance.","zh":"挑戰性目標可以對表現有重大影響。"},{"en":"To have a major impact on something means to strongly affect it.","zh":"To have a major impact on something 指強烈影響某事。"},{"en":"A good teacher can have a major impact on a student’s confidence.","zh":"好老師可以對學生信心有重大影響。"},{"en":"If work design changes motivation, it may also change productivity.","zh":"如果工作設計改變動機，它也可能改變生產力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong and noticeable effect.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈且明顯的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ensure that","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Organisations need to ensure that job roles are stimulating.","zh":"組織需要確保工作角色有刺激性。"},{"en":"To ensure that means to make certain that something happens or is true.","zh":"To ensure that 指確保某事發生或屬實。"},{"en":"A teacher should ensure that students understand the instructions before starting.","zh":"老師應確保學生在開始前明白指示。"},{"en":"If managers ensure that roles are clear, employees may feel less confused.","zh":"如果管理者確保角色清晰，員工可能較少困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces something that must be made secure or certain.","zh":"這個片語引出必須被保障或確定的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"various job roles","meaning":"各種工作角色","examples":[{"en":"Various job roles should provide employees with stimulation.","zh":"各種工作角色應為員工提供刺激和挑戰。"},{"en":"Various job roles means different positions or types of work within an organisation.","zh":"Various job roles 指組織內不同職位或工作類型。"},{"en":"In a school, various job roles include teachers, clerks, counsellors, and cleaners.","zh":"在學校中，各種工作角色包括老師、文員、輔導員和清潔工。"},{"en":"If job roles are too narrow, employees may feel bored or trapped.","zh":"如果工作角色太狹窄，員工可能感到沉悶或被困。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the different kinds of work people do.","zh":"這個片語描述人們所做的不同工作種類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"provide employees with stimulation","meaning":"為員工提供刺激和挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Good job roles provide employees with stimulation.","zh":"好的工作角色為員工提供刺激和挑戰。"},{"en":"To provide employees with stimulation means to give workers interesting challenges that keep them mentally active.","zh":"To provide employees with stimulation 指給員工有趣挑戰，使他們保持思考活躍。"},{"en":"A teacher provides students with stimulation by asking questions that make them think.","zh":"老師透過提出令人思考的問題，為學生提供刺激和挑戰。"},{"en":"If work is stimulating, employees may learn more and stay engaged longer.","zh":"如果工作具刺激性，員工可能學得更多並保持更長投入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping people interested through challenge and variety.","zh":"這個片語描述透過挑戰和變化令人保持興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"challenge someone","meaning":"挑戰某人","examples":[{"en":"Work should challenge employees or allow them to grow.","zh":"工作應挑戰員工，或讓他們成長。"},{"en":"To challenge someone means to push them to use more skill, effort, or thought.","zh":"To challenge someone 指推動某人運用更多技能、努力或思考。"},{"en":"A difficult reading passage can challenge students without being impossible.","zh":"困難閱讀篇章可以挑戰學生，但不至於不可能完成。"},{"en":"If tasks never challenge workers, they may stop improving.","zh":"如果任務從不挑戰員工，他們可能停止進步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pressure that can help growth when it is reasonable.","zh":"這個片語描述合理時能幫助成長的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"allow someone to grow","meaning":"讓某人成長","examples":[{"en":"Meaningful work allows employees to grow.","zh":"有意義的工作讓員工成長。"},{"en":"To allow someone to grow means to give them chances to learn, improve, and become more capable.","zh":"To allow someone to grow 指給某人學習、進步和變得更有能力的機會。"},{"en":"A club leadership role may allow a shy student to grow in confidence.","zh":"學會領袖角色可能讓害羞學生在信心上成長。"},{"en":"If a job offers no learning, employees may look elsewhere.","zh":"如果工作沒有學習機會，員工可能另覓去處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating space for personal development.","zh":"這個片語描述為個人成長創造空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"meaningless things","meaning":"沒有意義的事情","examples":[{"en":"Employees do not want to do meaningless things.","zh":"員工不想做沒有意義的事情。"},{"en":"Meaningless things are tasks that feel useless, empty, or unconnected to any real purpose.","zh":"Meaningless things 是感覺無用、空洞或與真正目的無關的任務。"},{"en":"A student may dislike copying notes if they do not understand why it helps.","zh":"如果學生不明白抄筆記有何幫助，他可能不喜歡這樣做。"},{"en":"If workers spend days on tasks no one uses, motivation may fall.","zh":"如果員工花很多天做沒有人使用的任務，動機可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes work that lacks purpose or value.","zh":"這個片語描述缺乏目的或價值的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"monotonous jobs","meaning":"單調乏味的工作","examples":[{"en":"Employees may lose motivation in monotonous jobs.","zh":"員工在單調乏味的工作中可能失去動機。"},{"en":"Monotonous jobs are jobs that are repetitive, dull, and lacking variety.","zh":"Monotonous jobs 是重複、沉悶且缺乏變化的工作。"},{"en":"A worker who scans the same item all day may find the job monotonous.","zh":"整天掃描同一類物品的員工可能覺得工作單調。"},{"en":"If a job is too monotonous, employees may feel bored and mentally tired.","zh":"如果工作太單調，員工可能感到沉悶和精神疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase describes work that feels the same every day.","zh":"這個片語描述每天感覺一樣的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"personal meaning and fulfilment","meaning":"個人意義和滿足感","examples":[{"en":"A job should provide personal meaning and fulfilment.","zh":"一份工作應提供個人意義和滿足感。"},{"en":"Personal meaning and fulfilment are the feelings that work matters and helps a person grow.","zh":"Personal meaning and fulfilment 是感到工作重要並幫助個人成長的感覺。"},{"en":"A nurse may feel fulfilment when patients recover and thank the team.","zh":"當病人康復並感謝團隊時，護士可能感到滿足。"},{"en":"If work has no personal meaning, salary alone may not keep employees motivated.","zh":"如果工作沒有個人意義，單靠薪金可能不能保持員工動力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional satisfaction from purposeful work.","zh":"這個片語描述從有目的工作中得到的情感滿足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"leave the company","meaning":"離開公司","examples":[{"en":"Employees may leave the company if their work feels meaningless.","zh":"如果工作感覺沒有意義，員工可能離開公司。"},{"en":"To leave the company means to stop working for that organisation.","zh":"To leave the company 指停止為該組織工作。"},{"en":"A worker may leave the company after finding a role with better training.","zh":"員工找到有更好培訓的職位後，可能離開公司。"},{"en":"If many employees leave, the company may lose experience and spend more on hiring.","zh":"如果許多員工離開，公司可能失去經驗並花更多錢招聘。"},{"en":"This phrase describes resignation or departure from an employer.","zh":"這個片語描述辭職或離開僱主。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the hardest lever to pull","meaning":"最難運用的槓桿","examples":[{"en":"The drive to defend is often the hardest lever to pull.","zh":"防衛的驅動力往往是最難運用的槓桿。"},{"en":"The hardest lever to pull means the most difficult tool or method to use effectively.","zh":"The hardest lever to pull 指最難有效使用的工具或方法。"},{"en":"For a teacher, changing a student’s confidence may be the hardest lever to pull.","zh":"對老師而言，改變學生信心可能是最難運用的槓桿。"},{"en":"If fairness is involved, one poor decision can damage trust quickly.","zh":"如果涉及公平，一個差劣決定可以迅速破壞信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the most difficult management factor to handle.","zh":"這個片語描述最難處理的管理因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"manifest itself as","meaning":"表現為","examples":[{"en":"The drive to defend manifests itself as a quest for justice.","zh":"防衛的驅動力表現為對公義的追求。"},{"en":"To manifest itself as something means to appear or show itself in that form.","zh":"To manifest itself as something 指以某種形式出現或展現。"},{"en":"Stress may manifest itself as headaches, anger, or poor sleep.","zh":"壓力可能表現為頭痛、憤怒或睡眠差。"},{"en":"If people feel treated unfairly, their defensive drive may appear as complaints or resistance.","zh":"如果人們覺得受到不公平對待，防衛驅動力可能表現為投訴或抗拒。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how an inner force becomes visible.","zh":"這個片語解釋內在力量如何變得可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a quest to","meaning":"對……的追求","examples":[{"en":"The drive to defend is a quest to create and promote fairness.","zh":"防衛的驅動力是對建立並促進公平的追求。"},{"en":"A quest to do something is a serious search or effort to achieve it.","zh":"A quest to do something 是為達成某事而作出的認真尋求或努力。"},{"en":"A student may begin a quest to improve English by reading every day.","zh":"學生可能透過每日閱讀，開始對改善英語的追求。"},{"en":"If workers want justice, they may push for clearer rules and fair treatment.","zh":"如果員工想要公義，他們可能推動更清晰規則和公平待遇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a determined pursuit of a goal.","zh":"這個片語描述對目標的堅定追求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"create and promote justice","meaning":"建立並促進公義","examples":[{"en":"Employees want organisations to create and promote justice.","zh":"員工希望組織建立並促進公義。"},{"en":"To create and promote justice means to build fair systems and actively support them.","zh":"To create and promote justice 指建立公平制度並積極支持它們。"},{"en":"A school can create and promote justice by applying rules equally to all students.","zh":"學校可以透過平等執行規則來建立並促進公義。"},{"en":"If promotion decisions are transparent, employees may trust the organisation more.","zh":"如果晉升決定透明，員工可能更信任組織。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making fairness real, not just talking about it.","zh":"這個片語描述令公平真正落實，而不只是談論公平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"justice and fairness","meaning":"公義和公平","examples":[{"en":"The drive to defend is linked to justice and fairness.","zh":"防衛的驅動力與公義和公平有關。"},{"en":"Justice and fairness mean people are treated properly, equally, and according to reasonable rules.","zh":"Justice and fairness 指人們受到恰當、平等並根據合理規則的對待。"},{"en":"Students expect justice and fairness when teachers mark assignments.","zh":"老師批改功課時，學生期待公義和公平。"},{"en":"If employees see unfair treatment, trust in management may fall.","zh":"如果員工看見不公平待遇，他們對管理層的信任可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a moral need for proper treatment.","zh":"這個片語描述對恰當對待的道德需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"express ourselves freely","meaning":"自由表達自己","examples":[{"en":"Employees value the ability to express themselves freely.","zh":"員工重視自由表達自己的能力。"},{"en":"To express ourselves freely means to share thoughts, concerns, or identity without fear.","zh":"To express ourselves freely 指在沒有恐懼下分享想法、憂慮或身份。"},{"en":"Students learn better when they can express themselves freely during discussion.","zh":"當學生能在討論中自由表達自己，他們會學得更好。"},{"en":"If workers cannot speak honestly, problems may stay hidden until they become serious.","zh":"如果員工不能誠實發聲，問題可能一直被隱藏直到變嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes open and safe self-expression.","zh":"這個片語描述開放且安全的自我表達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"organisational lever","meaning":"組織槓桿；組織推動因素","examples":[{"en":"Resource allocation is an organisational lever for the drive to defend.","zh":"資源分配是防衛驅動力的一個組織槓桿。"},{"en":"An organisational lever is a policy, system, or practice that leaders can adjust to influence employees.","zh":"Organisational lever 是領袖可調整以影響員工的政策、制度或做法。"},{"en":"A school timetable is an organisational lever because it shapes how teachers and students use time.","zh":"學校時間表是一種組織槓桿，因為它塑造老師和學生如何使用時間。"},{"en":"If leaders adjust the right lever, motivation and trust may improve.","zh":"如果領袖調整正確槓桿，動機和信任可能改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical tool for managing behaviour.","zh":"這個片語描述管理行為的實用工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"basic human motivator","meaning":"基本人類動機","examples":[{"en":"The drive to defend is a basic human motivator.","zh":"防衛的驅動力是一種基本人類動機。"},{"en":"A basic human motivator is a deep force that influences people across many situations.","zh":"Basic human motivator 是在多種情境中影響人的深層力量。"},{"en":"The wish to be safe is a basic human motivator in families, schools, and workplaces.","zh":"想要安全是在家庭、學校和職場中的基本人類動機。"},{"en":"If a basic motivator is threatened, people may react strongly.","zh":"如果基本動機受到威脅，人們可能強烈反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fundamental reason people act.","zh":"這個片語描述人們行動的根本原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"resource allocation","meaning":"資源分配","examples":[{"en":"Resource allocation can affect employees’ sense of fairness.","zh":"資源分配可以影響員工的公平感。"},{"en":"Resource allocation means deciding how money, time, staff, equipment, or opportunities are distributed.","zh":"Resource allocation 指決定金錢、時間、人手、設備或機會如何分配。"},{"en":"A school’s resource allocation affects which classes receive new computers first.","zh":"學校的資源分配會影響哪些班級先獲得新電腦。"},{"en":"If resources are allocated unfairly, people may feel ignored or angry.","zh":"如果資源分配不公平，人們可能感到被忽視或憤怒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how limited resources are shared.","zh":"這個片語描述有限資源如何被分享。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be met through","meaning":"透過……得到滿足","examples":[{"en":"The drive to defend is also met through connection to a company.","zh":"防衛的驅動力也可透過與公司的連繫得到滿足。"},{"en":"To be met through something means to be satisfied by means of it.","zh":"To be met through something 指透過某方式得到滿足。"},{"en":"A student’s need for confidence may be met through regular encouragement.","zh":"學生對信心的需要可能透過定期鼓勵得到滿足。"},{"en":"If employees feel connected to the company, their defensive concerns may lessen.","zh":"如果員工感到與公司有連繫，他們的防衛性憂慮可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the method by which a need is satisfied.","zh":"這個片語解釋需要透過甚麼方法得到滿足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sense of connection to","meaning":"對……的連繫感","examples":[{"en":"Employees may need a sense of connection to their company.","zh":"員工可能需要對公司的連繫感。"},{"en":"A sense of connection to something is the feeling of being linked to it emotionally or practically.","zh":"Sense of connection to something 是感到在情感或實際上與某事有連繫。"},{"en":"Students may feel a sense of connection to a school when teachers know them personally.","zh":"當老師親自認識學生時，學生可能對學校有連繫感。"},{"en":"If workers feel no connection to the company, they may leave more easily.","zh":"如果員工對公司沒有連繫感，他們可能更容易離開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes belonging and attachment to an organisation.","zh":"這個片語描述對組織的歸屬和依附。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"merge with another company","meaning":"與另一間公司合併","examples":[{"en":"Employees may worry if their company merges with another company.","zh":"如果公司與另一間公司合併，員工可能會擔心。"},{"en":"To merge with another company means two companies join together to become one larger organisation.","zh":"To merge with another company 指兩間公司結合成一個更大的組織。"},{"en":"A small tutoring centre may merge with another company to share teachers and resources.","zh":"小型補習中心可能與另一間公司合併，以共享老師和資源。"},{"en":"If a merger changes jobs and culture, employees may feel uncertain.","zh":"如果合併改變工作和文化，員工可能感到不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major organisational joining.","zh":"這個片語描述重大的組織結合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"show concern","meaning":"表示憂慮","examples":[{"en":"Employees may show concern during a company merger.","zh":"員工可能在公司合併期間表示憂慮。"},{"en":"To show concern means to express worry, care, or unease about something.","zh":"To show concern 指表達擔心、關心或不安。"},{"en":"Parents may show concern if a child suddenly stops enjoying school.","zh":"如果孩子突然不再喜歡上學，家長可能表示憂慮。"},{"en":"If staff show concern early, leaders can answer questions before fear spreads.","zh":"如果員工及早表示憂慮，領袖可以在恐懼擴散前回答問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible worry or care.","zh":"這個片語描述可見的擔憂或關心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"examine the relationships between","meaning":"檢視……之間的關係","examples":[{"en":"Two studies examined the relationships between the four drives and motivation.","zh":"兩項研究檢視四種驅動力與動機之間的關係。"},{"en":"To examine the relationships between things means to study how they are connected.","zh":"To examine the relationships between things 指研究它們如何連接。"},{"en":"A teacher may examine the relationship between homework habits and exam results.","zh":"老師可能檢視功課習慣與考試成績之間的關係。"},{"en":"If two factors move together, researchers may investigate whether one influences the other.","zh":"如果兩個因素一同變化，研究人員可能調查其中一個是否影響另一個。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful study of connections.","zh":"這個片語描述對關聯的仔細研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an article based on","meaning":"一篇以……為基礎的文章","examples":[{"en":"An article based on the studies was later published.","zh":"一篇以這些研究為基礎的文章後來被發表。"},{"en":"An article based on something is a written piece built from that information or research.","zh":"Article based on something 是由該資訊或研究建立而成的文章。"},{"en":"A student may write a report based on interviews with classmates.","zh":"學生可能寫一份以同學訪問為基礎的報告。"},{"en":"If an article is based on strong evidence, readers may trust it more.","zh":"如果文章建基於有力證據，讀者可能更信任它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the source or foundation of a written work.","zh":"這個片語顯示書面作品的來源或基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be published in","meaning":"刊登於","examples":[{"en":"The article was published in Harvard Business Review.","zh":"這篇文章刊登於《哈佛商業評論》。"},{"en":"To be published in a place means to appear formally in a magazine, journal, website, or book.","zh":"To be published in a place 指正式出現在雜誌、期刊、網站或書籍中。"},{"en":"A student’s poem may be published in the school magazine.","zh":"學生的詩可能刊登於校刊。"},{"en":"If research is published in a respected journal, more people may read and discuss it.","zh":"如果研究刊登於受尊重的期刊，更多人可能閱讀和討論它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal release of written work.","zh":"這個片語描述書面作品的正式發布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Harvard Business Review","meaning":"《哈佛商業評論》","examples":[{"en":"The article was published in Harvard Business Review.","zh":"這篇文章刊登於《哈佛商業評論》。"},{"en":"Harvard Business Review is a well-known publication about management, leadership, and business ideas.","zh":"Harvard Business Review 是關於管理、領導和商業理念的知名刊物。"},{"en":"Managers may read Harvard Business Review to learn about workplace strategy.","zh":"管理者可能閱讀《哈佛商業評論》來學習職場策略。"},{"en":"If an idea appears in a respected business publication, it may reach many leaders.","zh":"如果某想法出現在受尊重的商業刊物，它可能接觸許多領袖。"},{"en":"This phrase names a source associated with business and management discussion.","zh":"這個片語命名與商業和管理討論相關的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"emphasise four-drive theory","meaning":"強調四驅力理論","examples":[{"en":"The authors emphasised four-drive theory and empirical investigation.","zh":"作者強調四驅力理論和實證研究。"},{"en":"To emphasise four-drive theory means to give special importance to the idea that four drives shape motivation.","zh":"To emphasise four-drive theory 指特別重視四種驅動力塑造動機的想法。"},{"en":"A teacher may emphasise grammar patterns when students repeatedly make the same mistakes.","zh":"當學生反覆犯同一錯誤，老師可能強調文法模式。"},{"en":"If researchers emphasise a theory, they use it to organise their explanation.","zh":"如果研究人員強調一種理論，他們會用它來組織解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the main theoretical focus of the article.","zh":"這個片語顯示文章的主要理論焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"empirical investigation","meaning":"實證研究","examples":[{"en":"The article emphasised four-drive theory and empirical investigation.","zh":"這篇文章強調四驅力理論和實證研究。"},{"en":"Empirical investigation is research based on observation, data, surveys, or experiments.","zh":"Empirical investigation 是以觀察、數據、調查或實驗為基礎的研究。"},{"en":"A school may use empirical investigation by comparing test results before and after a new programme.","zh":"學校可能透過比較新計劃前後的測驗結果來進行實證研究。"},{"en":"If a theory is tested with data, it becomes more than just an idea.","zh":"如果理論用數據測試，它就不只是想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence-based research.","zh":"這個片語描述以證據為基礎的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"surveys of employees","meaning":"員工調查","examples":[{"en":"The article used surveys of employees at several companies.","zh":"這篇文章使用了幾間公司的員工調查。"},{"en":"Surveys of employees are questionnaires or interviews that collect workers’ views and experiences.","zh":"Surveys of employees 是收集員工看法和經驗的問卷或訪問。"},{"en":"A company may use employee surveys to learn why staff feel stressed.","zh":"公司可能使用員工調查來了解員工為何感到壓力。"},{"en":"If many workers report low trust, leaders know where improvement is needed.","zh":"如果許多員工報告信任度低，領袖就知道哪裏需要改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collecting information directly from staff.","zh":"這個片語描述直接向員工收集資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Fortune 500 companies","meaning":"財富 500 強公司","examples":[{"en":"The surveys included employees at Fortune 500 companies.","zh":"調查包括財富 500 強公司的員工。"},{"en":"Fortune 500 companies are large companies listed among the highest-revenue firms in the United States.","zh":"Fortune 500 companies 是美國收入最高公司名單中的大型公司。"},{"en":"A business student may study Fortune 500 companies to understand large-scale management.","zh":"商科學生可能研究財富 500 強公司，以理解大規模管理。"},{"en":"If research includes large companies, its findings may interest many managers.","zh":"如果研究包括大型公司，其發現可能引起許多管理者興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to major corporations with very high revenue.","zh":"這個片語指收入很高的大企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"global businesses","meaning":"全球性企業","examples":[{"en":"The research also examined employees at two global businesses.","zh":"研究也檢視兩間全球性企業的員工。"},{"en":"Global businesses are companies that operate in many countries or serve international markets.","zh":"Global businesses 是在多個國家營運或服務國際市場的公司。"},{"en":"A global business may need managers who understand different cultures and laws.","zh":"全球性企業可能需要理解不同文化和法律的管理者。"},{"en":"If a company operates worldwide, employee motivation may vary across regions.","zh":"如果公司全球營運，員工動機可能因地區而異。"},{"en":"This phrase describes businesses with international reach.","zh":"這個片語描述具有國際覆蓋的企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"independent drives","meaning":"獨立驅動力","examples":[{"en":"The article explains how independent drives influence behaviour.","zh":"文章解釋獨立驅動力如何影響行為。"},{"en":"Independent drives are separate motivational forces that can each affect people’s actions.","zh":"Independent drives 是可以各自影響人行動的不同動機力量。"},{"en":"A student may want both good grades and friendship, but these are different drives.","zh":"學生可能同時想要好成績和友誼，但這些是不同驅動力。"},{"en":"If one drive is satisfied but another is ignored, motivation may still be incomplete.","zh":"如果一種驅動力得到滿足但另一種被忽略，動機可能仍不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase describes drives that work separately but may interact.","zh":"這個片語描述各自運作但可能互相影響的驅動力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"influence employees’ behaviour","meaning":"影響員工行為","examples":[{"en":"Independent drives can influence employees’ behaviour.","zh":"獨立驅動力可以影響員工行為。"},{"en":"To influence employees’ behaviour means to affect how workers act, decide, or respond.","zh":"To influence employees’ behaviour 指影響員工如何行動、決定或回應。"},{"en":"A fair reward system may influence employees’ behaviour by encouraging stronger effort.","zh":"公平獎勵制度可能透過鼓勵更強努力來影響員工行為。"},{"en":"If workers feel disconnected, they may cooperate less and leave sooner.","zh":"如果員工感到缺乏連繫，他們可能較少合作並更早離開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes forces that shape workplace actions.","zh":"這個片語描述塑造職場行動的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"boost employee motivation","meaning":"提升員工動機","examples":[{"en":"Organisational levers can boost employee motivation.","zh":"組織槓桿可以提升員工動機。"},{"en":"To boost employee motivation means to increase workers’ willingness and energy to work.","zh":"To boost employee motivation 指增加員工工作的意願和精力。"},{"en":"A company may boost motivation by offering training and recognising good work.","zh":"公司可能透過提供培訓和認可好工作來提升動機。"},{"en":"If motivation rises, employees may show more effort and commitment.","zh":"如果動機上升，員工可能展現更多努力和投入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strengthening the desire to perform.","zh":"這個片語描述加強表現欲望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be strongly associated with","meaning":"與……有密切關聯","examples":[{"en":"The drive to bond is strongly associated with commitment.","zh":"建立連繫的驅動力與投入有密切關聯。"},{"en":"To be strongly associated with something means to have a close connection with it.","zh":"To be strongly associated with something 指與某事有緊密連繫。"},{"en":"Regular practice is strongly associated with improvement in language learning.","zh":"定期練習與語言學習進步有密切關聯。"},{"en":"If belonging and commitment rise together, researchers may study their link.","zh":"如果歸屬感和投入一起上升，研究人員可能研究它們的連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a strong relationship, not necessarily direct cause.","zh":"這個片語顯示強烈關係，但不一定是直接因果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"commitment","meaning":"投入；承諾","examples":[{"en":"The drive to bond is most strongly associated with commitment.","zh":"建立連繫的驅動力與投入最密切相關。"},{"en":"Commitment is a strong willingness to continue supporting or working for something.","zh":"Commitment 是繼續支持或為某事努力的強烈意願。"},{"en":"A student shows commitment by practising regularly even when progress is slow.","zh":"即使進步慢，學生仍定期練習，就是展現投入。"},{"en":"If employees feel connected to a team, their commitment may become stronger.","zh":"如果員工感到與團隊有連繫，他們的投入可能更強。"},{"en":"This word describes loyalty, dedication, and continued effort.","zh":"這個詞描述忠誠、奉獻和持續努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be most related to","meaning":"與……最相關","examples":[{"en":"The drive to comprehend is most related to employees’ effort.","zh":"理解的驅動力與員工努力最相關。"},{"en":"To be most related to something means to have the strongest connection with it among several factors.","zh":"To be most related to something 指在幾個因素中與某事有最強關聯。"},{"en":"In writing, planning may be most related to clear organisation.","zh":"在寫作中，規劃可能與清晰組織最相關。"},{"en":"If understanding work gives people energy, it may be closely linked to effort.","zh":"如果理解工作給人能量，它可能與努力密切相關。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the strongest relationship among options.","zh":"這個片語指出多個選項中的最強關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"devote effort to work","meaning":"投入精力於工作","examples":[{"en":"The drive to comprehend affects how much effort employees devote to work.","zh":"理解的驅動力影響員工投入多少精力於工作。"},{"en":"To devote effort to work means to put energy, attention, and persistence into a job.","zh":"To devote effort to work 指把精力、注意力和持續性投入工作。"},{"en":"A student devotes effort to an essay when they plan, write, and revise carefully.","zh":"學生仔細規劃、寫作和修改作文時，就是投入精力於作文。"},{"en":"If work feels meaningful, employees may devote more effort to it.","zh":"如果工作感覺有意義，員工可能投入更多精力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes investing real energy in a task.","zh":"這個片語描述把真正能量投入任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be satisfied by","meaning":"可透過……得到滿足","examples":[{"en":"The drive to acquire can be satisfied by a reward system.","zh":"獲取的驅動力可透過獎勵制度得到滿足。"},{"en":"To be satisfied by something means to have a need or desire fulfilled through it.","zh":"To be satisfied by something 指某需要或欲望透過某事得到滿足。"},{"en":"A child’s curiosity may be satisfied by a clear explanation and a hands-on experiment.","zh":"孩子的好奇心可能透過清晰解釋和動手實驗得到滿足。"},{"en":"If a reward system is fair, it may satisfy the desire for achievement.","zh":"如果獎勵制度公平，它可能滿足對成就的欲望。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what fulfils a need.","zh":"這個片語解釋甚麼滿足某種需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"reward system","meaning":"獎勵制度","examples":[{"en":"A reward system can help satisfy the drive to acquire.","zh":"獎勵制度可以幫助滿足獲取的驅動力。"},{"en":"A reward system is a set of rules for giving pay, praise, bonuses, promotion, or benefits.","zh":"Reward system 是給予薪酬、讚賞、花紅、晉升或福利的一套規則。"},{"en":"A school may use a reward system to recognise effort, kindness, and improvement.","zh":"學校可能使用獎勵制度來認可努力、善良和進步。"},{"en":"If the reward system feels unfair, employees may lose trust.","zh":"如果獎勵制度感覺不公平，員工可能失去信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how an organisation gives recognition and benefits.","zh":"這個片語描述組織如何給予認可和好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tie rewards to performance","meaning":"將獎勵與表現掛鈎","examples":[{"en":"A good reward system ties rewards to performance.","zh":"好的獎勵制度將獎勵與表現掛鈎。"},{"en":"To tie rewards to performance means to connect benefits directly with the quality or results of work.","zh":"To tie rewards to performance 指把好處直接與工作質素或成果連接。"},{"en":"A teacher may tie extra credit to clear improvement rather than natural ability.","zh":"老師可能把額外分數與清晰進步掛鈎，而不是與天生能力掛鈎。"},{"en":"If rewards are not linked to performance, hardworking employees may feel cheated.","zh":"如果獎勵沒有與表現掛鈎，努力工作的員工可能感到被欺騙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fair connection between effort and reward.","zh":"這個片語描述努力與獎勵之間的公平連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"opportunities for advancement","meaning":"晉升機會；發展機會","examples":[{"en":"The best people should receive opportunities for advancement.","zh":"最優秀的人應獲得晉升機會。"},{"en":"Opportunities for advancement are chances to move into better, higher, or more responsible roles.","zh":"Opportunities for advancement 是進入更好、更高或更有責任職位的機會。"},{"en":"A junior employee may stay with a company if they see real promotion opportunities.","zh":"如果初級員工看見真正晉升機會，他可能留在公司。"},{"en":"If advancement is blocked, talented workers may leave for another organisation.","zh":"如果發展受阻，有才能的員工可能轉到另一組織。"},{"en":"This phrase describes chances for career growth.","zh":"這個片語描述事業成長機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the merger of","meaning":"……的合併","examples":[{"en":"The study examined the merger of P company and H company.","zh":"研究檢視 P 公司和 H 公司的合併。"},{"en":"The merger of two companies is the joining of them into one organisation.","zh":"The merger of two companies 是兩間公司結合成一個組織。"},{"en":"The merger of two schools may require new timetables, uniforms, and leadership roles.","zh":"兩間學校的合併可能需要新時間表、校服和領導角色。"},{"en":"If a merger is managed badly, staff may worry about jobs and culture.","zh":"如果合併管理不善，員工可能擔心職位和文化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a formal joining of organisations.","zh":"這個片語描述組織的正式結合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the former company","meaning":"前者公司","examples":[{"en":"Employees in the former company showed an unusually cooperative attitude.","zh":"前者公司的員工在合併期間表現出異常合作的態度。"},{"en":"The former company means the first company mentioned out of two.","zh":"The former company 指兩間公司中先提到的那一間。"},{"en":"If A School and B School merge, the former school means A School.","zh":"如果 A 學校和 B 學校合併，前者學校指 A 學校。"},{"en":"This phrase helps avoid repeating a name when comparing two organisations.","zh":"這個片語在比較兩個組織時幫助避免重複名稱。"},{"en":"The former refers to the first item, while the latter refers to the second.","zh":"The former 指第一項，而 the latter 指第二項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an unusually cooperative attitude","meaning":"異常合作的態度","examples":[{"en":"Employees showed an unusually cooperative attitude during the merger.","zh":"員工在合併期間表現出異常合作的態度。"},{"en":"An unusually cooperative attitude is a level of helpfulness and teamwork stronger than expected.","zh":"Unusually cooperative attitude 是比預期更強的幫助和團隊合作程度。"},{"en":"A class may show an unusually cooperative attitude when preparing for a school fair.","zh":"班級籌備學校嘉年華時，可能表現出異常合作的態度。"},{"en":"If employees feel secure and respected, they may cooperate more during change.","zh":"如果員工感到安全和受尊重，他們在變革期間可能更合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes surprisingly strong willingness to work together.","zh":"這個片語描述令人意外地強的合作意願。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the key to","meaning":"……的關鍵","examples":[{"en":"The key to successfully motivating employees is to meet all drives.","zh":"成功激勵員工的關鍵是滿足所有驅動力。"},{"en":"The key to something is the most important factor needed to achieve it.","zh":"The key to something 是達成某事所需的最重要因素。"},{"en":"The key to better writing is clear thinking before sentence decoration.","zh":"寫作進步的關鍵是在修飾句子前先有清晰思考。"},{"en":"If managers know the key to motivation, they can avoid wasting effort on weak solutions.","zh":"如果管理者知道動機的關鍵，就能避免把努力浪費在薄弱方案上。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the central condition for success.","zh":"這個片語指出成功的核心條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"successfully motivating employees","meaning":"成功激勵員工","examples":[{"en":"Meeting all four drives is the key to successfully motivating employees.","zh":"滿足所有四種驅動力是成功激勵員工的關鍵。"},{"en":"Successfully motivating employees means helping workers feel willing, energised, and committed to work.","zh":"Successfully motivating employees 指幫助員工願意、有精力並投入工作。"},{"en":"A manager successfully motivates employees when staff work hard without constant pressure.","zh":"當員工不用持續壓力也努力工作，管理者就是成功激勵員工。"},{"en":"If motivation is successful, performance and morale may improve together.","zh":"如果激勵成功，表現和士氣可能一起改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes effective workplace encouragement.","zh":"這個片語描述有效的職場鼓勵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"meet all drives","meaning":"滿足所有驅動力","examples":[{"en":"Organisations need to meet all drives to motivate employees effectively.","zh":"組織需要滿足所有驅動力，才能有效激勵員工。"},{"en":"To meet all drives means to satisfy all the major motivational needs people have.","zh":"To meet all drives 指滿足人們所有主要動機需要。"},{"en":"A school may need to meet students’ need for safety, friendship, challenge, and recognition.","zh":"學校可能需要滿足學生對安全、友誼、挑戰和認可的需要。"},{"en":"If one drive is ignored, motivation may remain incomplete.","zh":"如果一種驅動力被忽視，動機可能仍不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses balanced motivation, not a single solution.","zh":"這個片語強調平衡激勵，而不是單一解決方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"if we are to understand","meaning":"如果我們要理解……","examples":[{"en":"Each drive is important if we are to understand employee motivation.","zh":"如果我們要理解員工動機，每種驅動力都很重要。"},{"en":"If we are to understand means if we want to understand properly.","zh":"If we are to understand 指如果我們想正確理解。"},{"en":"If we are to understand a student’s poor marks, we must look at sleep, stress, and teaching.","zh":"如果我們要理解學生低分，就必須看睡眠、壓力和教學。"},{"en":"If managers want real answers, they must study causes, not just symptoms.","zh":"如果管理者想得到真正答案，就必須研究成因，而不只是症狀。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a necessary condition for understanding something.","zh":"這個片語引出理解某事所需的必要條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not necessarily the only","meaning":"未必是唯一的","examples":[{"en":"These four drives are not necessarily the only human drives.","zh":"這四種驅動力未必是唯一的人類驅動力。"},{"en":"Not necessarily the only means there may be others besides the ones mentioned.","zh":"Not necessarily the only 指除了所提到的，可能還有其他。"},{"en":"Exams are not necessarily the only reason students feel stressed.","zh":"考試未必是學生感到壓力的唯一原因。"},{"en":"If a theory names four causes, it may still leave room for additional causes.","zh":"如果理論列出四個成因，它仍可能為額外成因留有空間。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids making an absolute claim.","zh":"這個片語避免作出絕對聲稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"human drives","meaning":"人類驅動力","examples":[{"en":"The four drives are central to understanding modern human life.","zh":"這四種驅動力對理解現代人類生活至關重要。"},{"en":"Human drives are deep needs or forces that shape human behaviour.","zh":"Human drives 是塑造人類行為的深層需要或力量。"},{"en":"The need for safety, belonging, achievement, and meaning can all be human drives.","zh":"對安全、歸屬、成就和意義的需要都可以是人類驅動力。"},{"en":"If human drives are ignored, policies may fail even when they look logical.","zh":"如果人類驅動力被忽視，政策即使看似合理也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes basic forces behind how people act.","zh":"這個片語描述人類行動背後的基本力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be central to","meaning":"對……至關重要","examples":[{"en":"The four drives are central to a unified understanding of modern life.","zh":"這四種驅動力對現代生活的統一理解至關重要。"},{"en":"To be central to something means to be extremely important to it.","zh":"To be central to something 指對某事極其重要。"},{"en":"Clear examples are central to effective vocabulary teaching.","zh":"清晰例子對有效詞彙教學至關重要。"},{"en":"If motivation is central to performance, managers must take it seriously.","zh":"如果動機對表現至關重要，管理者必須認真看待它。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies something as a core element.","zh":"這個片語指出某物是核心元素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a unified understanding of","meaning":"對……的統一理解","examples":[{"en":"The theory offers a unified understanding of modern human life.","zh":"這個理論提供對現代人類生活的統一理解。"},{"en":"A unified understanding of something is a single explanation that connects many parts together.","zh":"Unified understanding of something 是把多個部分連接起來的單一解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students a unified understanding of writing by linking ideas, structure, and language.","zh":"老師可能透過連接想法、結構和語言，給學生對寫作的統一理解。"},{"en":"If different facts are organised under one model, the topic becomes easier to understand.","zh":"如果不同事實被組織在一個模型下，主題會更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a complete and connected explanation.","zh":"這個片語描述完整而連貫的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"modern human life","meaning":"現代人類生活","examples":[{"en":"The four drives help explain modern human life.","zh":"這四種驅動力幫助解釋現代人類生活。"},{"en":"Modern human life means the way people live, work, relate, and make choices today.","zh":"Modern human life 指今天人們如何生活、工作、建立關係和作選擇。"},{"en":"Mobile phones, workplaces, schools, and family pressure all shape modern human life.","zh":"手提電話、職場、學校和家庭壓力都塑造現代人類生活。"},{"en":"If motivation theories explain work and relationships, they help us understand daily life today.","zh":"如果動機理論解釋工作和關係，它們就幫助我們理解今天的日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to present-day human experience.","zh":"這個片語指當代人類經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"考生為每題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option that best matches the passage.","zh":"To choose the correct letter 指選出最符合文章的答案選項。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should read all options before choosing the correct letter.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先閱讀所有選項，再選出正確字母。"},{"en":"If two options look similar, evidence from the text should decide the answer.","zh":"如果兩個選項看似相似，文章證據應決定答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction for multiple-choice questions.","zh":"這個片語是選擇題中的常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"according to the passage","meaning":"根據文章","examples":[{"en":"Students answer the question according to the passage.","zh":"學生根據文章回答問題。"},{"en":"According to the passage means based only on information given in the text.","zh":"According to the passage 指只根據文中提供的資訊。"},{"en":"A student should not use outside knowledge if the answer must be according to the passage.","zh":"如果答案必須根據文章，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"If the passage gives no evidence, the answer should not be guessed from common sense.","zh":"如果文章沒有證據，答案不應靠常識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds students to rely on the text.","zh":"這個片語提醒學生依賴文本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"what are we told about","meaning":"我們得知關於……甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what we are told about the study of motivation.","zh":"題目問我們得知關於動機研究甚麼。"},{"en":"What are we told about means what information the passage gives us about a topic.","zh":"What are we told about 指文章給了我們關於某主題的甚麼資訊。"},{"en":"In an exam, students must find what they are told about a person, event, or idea.","zh":"在考試中，學生必須找出文章告訴我們關於人物、事件或想法的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage states only one clear fact, students should not add extra assumptions.","zh":"如果文章只陳述一個清晰事實，學生不應加入額外假設。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for text-based information, not personal opinion.","zh":"這個片語要求文本資訊，而不是個人意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the study of motivation","meaning":"動機研究","examples":[{"en":"The study of motivation has attracted attention for many years.","zh":"動機研究多年來一直受到關注。"},{"en":"The study of motivation is research into why people act, persist, or give effort.","zh":"The study of motivation 是研究人們為何行動、堅持或付出努力。"},{"en":"Teachers study motivation when they ask why some students keep practising after failure.","zh":"當老師詢問為何一些學生失敗後仍繼續練習時，就是在研究動機。"},{"en":"If researchers understand motivation, they can suggest better ways to support people.","zh":"如果研究人員理解動機，他們可以建議更好方法支持人們。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to academic investigation of human drive and effort.","zh":"這個片語指對人類驅動力和努力的學術研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"attract attention in organisations","meaning":"在組織中受到關注","examples":[{"en":"Motivation theory has attracted attention in organisations.","zh":"動機理論在組織中受到關注。"},{"en":"To attract attention in organisations means to become noticed and discussed by companies or institutions.","zh":"To attract attention in organisations 指被公司或機構注意和討論。"},{"en":"Online learning attracted attention in schools when remote lessons became necessary.","zh":"當遙距課堂變得必要時，網上學習在學校中受到關注。"},{"en":"If a theory helps improve performance, organisations may become interested in it.","zh":"如果一個理論有助改善表現，組織可能對它感興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an idea becoming important inside workplaces or institutions.","zh":"這個片語描述想法在職場或機構內變得重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"motivate their subordinates","meaning":"激勵下屬","examples":[{"en":"Managers need to know how to motivate their subordinates.","zh":"管理者需要知道如何激勵下屬。"},{"en":"To motivate their subordinates means to encourage the people working under them to perform well.","zh":"To motivate their subordinates 指鼓勵在自己之下工作的員工有良好表現。"},{"en":"A team leader motivates subordinates by explaining goals and recognising effort.","zh":"團隊領袖透過解釋目標和認可努力來激勵下屬。"},{"en":"If managers fail to motivate staff, productivity and morale may fall.","zh":"如果管理者未能激勵員工，生產力和士氣可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes leadership directed at lower-ranking employees.","zh":"這個片語描述針對較低職級員工的領導行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be related to employees’ salaries","meaning":"與員工薪酬有關","examples":[{"en":"Some people think motivation is related to employees’ salaries.","zh":"有些人認為動機與員工薪酬有關。"},{"en":"To be related to employees’ salaries means to have a connection with how much workers are paid.","zh":"To be related to employees’ salaries 指與員工獲支付多少薪金有關。"},{"en":"A worker may feel more motivated after a fair pay rise.","zh":"員工在公平加薪後可能感到更有動力。"},{"en":"If salary is the only focus, other needs such as meaning and belonging may be ignored.","zh":"如果只聚焦於薪金，意義和歸屬等其他需要可能被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase connects motivation with pay, but not always completely.","zh":"這個片語把動機與薪酬連接，但不一定完全如此。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"tend to be too theoretical","meaning":"傾向過於理論化","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers may tend to be too theoretical in their studies.","zh":"一些研究人員的研究可能傾向過於理論化。"},{"en":"To tend to be too theoretical means to focus too much on ideas and not enough on practical reality.","zh":"To tend to be too theoretical 指過度聚焦想法，而不足夠關注實際現實。"},{"en":"A writing lesson may be too theoretical if students never practise real essays.","zh":"如果學生從不練習真實作文，寫作課可能過於理論化。"},{"en":"If research is too theoretical, managers may struggle to apply it at work.","zh":"如果研究過於理論化，管理者可能難以在工作中應用。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises ideas that are not practical enough.","zh":"這個片語批評不夠實用的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"increase the profits of","meaning":"增加……的利潤","examples":[{"en":"One possible goal of employee motivation is to increase the profits of organisations.","zh":"員工激勵的一個可能目標是增加組織利潤。"},{"en":"To increase the profits of something means to raise the money left after costs are paid.","zh":"To increase the profits of something 指提高扣除成本後剩下的金錢。"},{"en":"A shop may increase profits by reducing waste and improving customer service.","zh":"商店可能透過減少浪費和改善顧客服務來增加利潤。"},{"en":"If motivated workers serve customers better, sales may rise and costs may fall.","zh":"如果有動力的員工更好地服務顧客，銷售可能上升而成本可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improving financial results.","zh":"這個片語描述改善財務成果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"what can be inferred from","meaning":"從……可以推斷出甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Students decide what can be inferred from the passage.","zh":"學生判斷從文章可以推斷出甚麼。"},{"en":"What can be inferred from something means what conclusion can be reasonably drawn from the evidence.","zh":"What can be inferred from something 指可以從證據合理得出的結論。"},{"en":"If a student is always tired in morning lessons, a teacher may infer that sleep is a problem.","zh":"如果學生在早上課堂總是疲倦，老師可能推斷睡眠是問題。"},{"en":"If the passage suggests but does not state something directly, students must read carefully.","zh":"如果文章暗示但沒有直接說明某事，學生必須仔細閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for a logical conclusion, not a wild guess.","zh":"這個片語要求邏輯結論，而不是胡亂猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"people’s drives","meaning":"人們的驅動力","examples":[{"en":"The passage analyses people’s drives in the workplace.","zh":"文章分析人們在職場中的驅動力。"},{"en":"People’s drives are the needs or desires that push people to act.","zh":"People’s drives 是推動人行動的需要或欲望。"},{"en":"A teenager’s drive to belong may influence which friends they choose.","zh":"青少年對歸屬的驅動力可能影響他選擇哪些朋友。"},{"en":"If leaders understand people’s drives, they can design better support systems.","zh":"如果領袖理解人們的驅動力，他們可以設計更好的支援制度。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the inner forces behind behaviour.","zh":"這個片語指行為背後的內在力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"satisfying employees’ drives","meaning":"滿足員工的驅動力","examples":[{"en":"Satisfying employees’ drives can affect their behaviour.","zh":"滿足員工的驅動力可以影響他們的行為。"},{"en":"Satisfying employees’ drives means meeting workers’ deep needs for reward, connection, meaning, or fairness.","zh":"Satisfying employees’ drives 指滿足員工對獎勵、連繫、意義或公平的深層需要。"},{"en":"A company may satisfy the drive to bond by building supportive teams.","zh":"公司可能透過建立支援性團隊來滿足建立連繫的驅動力。"},{"en":"If employees’ drives are satisfied, they may become more committed and energetic.","zh":"如果員工的驅動力得到滿足，他們可能更投入和有活力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meeting the needs that motivate workers.","zh":"這個片語描述滿足激勵員工的需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lead to positive changes","meaning":"帶來正面改變","examples":[{"en":"Satisfying employees’ drives can lead to positive changes in behaviour.","zh":"滿足員工的驅動力可以帶來行為上的正面改變。"},{"en":"To lead to positive changes means to cause improvements.","zh":"To lead to positive changes 指造成改善。"},{"en":"Better sleep can lead to positive changes in a student’s mood and concentration.","zh":"更好睡眠可以帶來學生心情和專注上的正面改變。"},{"en":"If employees feel valued, they may cooperate more and complain less.","zh":"如果員工感到被重視，他們可能更合作並較少抱怨。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with beneficial results.","zh":"這個片語把原因與有益結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"negatively affect","meaning":"對……造成負面影響","examples":[{"en":"Ignoring employees’ drives may negatively affect their emotions.","zh":"忽視員工的驅動力可能對他們的情緒造成負面影響。"},{"en":"To negatively affect something means to harm it or make it worse.","zh":"To negatively affect something 指傷害某事或令它變差。"},{"en":"Poor lighting can negatively affect students’ ability to read comfortably.","zh":"照明差可以對學生舒適閱讀的能力造成負面影響。"},{"en":"If managers ignore fairness, workplace trust may decline.","zh":"如果管理者忽視公平，職場信任可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a harmful influence.","zh":"這個片語描述有害影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"increase companies’ production","meaning":"提高公司的產量","examples":[{"en":"Motivated employees may help increase companies’ production.","zh":"有動力的員工可能幫助提高公司的產量。"},{"en":"To increase companies’ production means to raise the amount of goods or services companies produce.","zh":"To increase companies’ production 指提高公司生產的產品或服務數量。"},{"en":"A factory may increase production when workers are trained and machines work smoothly.","zh":"當工人受過培訓且機器順利運作，工廠可能提高產量。"},{"en":"If employees are more motivated, they may complete more work with fewer delays.","zh":"如果員工更有動力，他們可能完成更多工作並減少延誤。"},{"en":"This phrase connects motivation with higher output.","zh":"這個片語把動機與更高產出連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"result in outstanding performance","meaning":"帶來出色表現","examples":[{"en":"Strong motivation may result in outstanding performance.","zh":"強烈動機可能帶來出色表現。"},{"en":"To result in outstanding performance means to produce excellent work as an outcome.","zh":"To result in outstanding performance 指結果產生優秀工作表現。"},{"en":"Regular practice and clear feedback can result in outstanding performance in writing.","zh":"定期練習和清晰回饋可以帶來寫作上的出色表現。"},{"en":"If workers feel motivated and supported, their work quality may rise sharply.","zh":"如果員工感到有動力和受支援，他們的工作質素可能大幅上升。"},{"en":"This phrase links cause and excellent result.","zh":"這個片語把原因與優秀結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"optimise employees’ performance","meaning":"優化員工表現","examples":[{"en":"Recognition and opportunities can help optimise employees’ performance.","zh":"認可和機會可以幫助優化員工表現。"},{"en":"To optimise employees’ performance means to help workers perform as well as possible.","zh":"To optimise employees’ performance 指幫助員工盡可能表現得好。"},{"en":"A teacher optimises student performance by giving clear models and useful correction.","zh":"老師透過提供清晰範例和有用修正來優化學生表現。"},{"en":"If employees receive fair rewards and meaningful work, they may reach higher standards.","zh":"如果員工獲得公平獎勵和有意義工作，他們可能達到更高標準。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improving performance to its best practical level.","zh":"這個片語描述把表現改善到實際上最佳水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the achievement element","meaning":"成就元素","examples":[{"en":"The achievement element is part of the drive to acquire.","zh":"成就元素是獲取驅動力的一部分。"},{"en":"The achievement element is the part of motivation connected with reaching goals and proving ability.","zh":"Achievement element 是與達成目標和證明能力相關的動機部分。"},{"en":"A student’s achievement element may push them to aim for a higher band score.","zh":"學生的成就元素可能推動他追求更高等級分數。"},{"en":"If people never see progress, their sense of achievement may weaken.","zh":"如果人們從看不到進步，他們的成就感可能減弱。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the goal-reaching side of motivation.","zh":"這個片語突出動機中達成目標的一面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"career fulfilment","meaning":"事業滿足感","examples":[{"en":"Employees may seek career fulfilment as well as financial rewards.","zh":"員工可能追求事業滿足感以及金錢獎勵。"},{"en":"Career fulfilment is the satisfaction people feel when their work matches their abilities, values, and goals.","zh":"Career fulfilment 是當工作符合能力、價值和目標時，人們感到的滿足。"},{"en":"A teacher may feel career fulfilment when former students return to say thank you.","zh":"當畢業學生回來道謝，老師可能感到事業滿足感。"},{"en":"If a job pays well but feels empty, career fulfilment may be low.","zh":"如果工作薪金高但感覺空洞，事業滿足感可能低。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep satisfaction from one’s working life.","zh":"這個片語描述來自工作人生的深層滿足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"financial incentive","meaning":"金錢誘因","examples":[{"en":"A financial incentive can motivate employees, but it is not the only lever.","zh":"金錢誘因可以激勵員工，但它不是唯一槓桿。"},{"en":"A financial incentive is money offered to encourage a particular action or performance.","zh":"Financial incentive 是為鼓勵特定行動或表現而提供的金錢。"},{"en":"A shop may give staff a bonus as a financial incentive for excellent service.","zh":"商店可能給員工花紅，作為優質服務的金錢誘因。"},{"en":"If money is the only incentive, employees may still feel unvalued.","zh":"如果金錢是唯一誘因，員工仍可能感到不被重視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes motivation created through payment or monetary reward.","zh":"這個片語描述透過付款或金錢獎勵創造的動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"how does something help someone","meaning":"……如何幫助某人","examples":[{"en":"The question asks how the drive to comprehend helps employees perform better.","zh":"題目問理解的驅動力如何幫助員工表現更好。"},{"en":"How does something help someone asks for the way one thing supports or benefits a person.","zh":"How does something help someone 要求說明某事如何支持或有益於某人。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask how planning helps students write clearer essays.","zh":"老師可能問規劃如何幫助學生寫出更清晰作文。"},{"en":"If students answer this question, they should explain the process, not just repeat the result.","zh":"學生回答這題時，應解釋過程，而不只是重複結果。"},{"en":"This phrase guides students to explain cause and benefit.","zh":"這個片語引導學生解釋原因和好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"perform better","meaning":"表現更好","examples":[{"en":"Meaningful work can help employees perform better.","zh":"有意義的工作可以幫助員工表現更好。"},{"en":"To perform better means to do a task with improved quality, speed, or effectiveness.","zh":"To perform better 指以更好質素、速度或效果完成任務。"},{"en":"A student may perform better after practising past papers and checking mistakes.","zh":"學生在練習歷屆試題並檢查錯誤後，可能表現更好。"},{"en":"If employees understand the purpose of their work, they may make better decisions.","zh":"如果員工理解工作目的，他們可能作出更好決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improvement in actual results.","zh":"這個片語描述實際結果上的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"better understand the development of","meaning":"更了解……的發展","examples":[{"en":"Employees may want to better understand the development of their organisations.","zh":"員工可能想更了解其組織的發展。"},{"en":"To better understand the development of something means to understand more clearly how it grows or changes.","zh":"To better understand the development of something 指更清楚理解某事如何成長或改變。"},{"en":"Students better understand the development of a story when they trace how the main character changes.","zh":"學生追蹤主角如何改變時，會更了解故事的發展。"},{"en":"If workers understand where a company is going, they may feel more involved.","zh":"如果員工理解公司走向，他們可能感到更有參與感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deeper understanding of change over time.","zh":"這個片語描述對隨時間變化的更深理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"feel that their work is meaningful","meaning":"感到自己的工作有意義","examples":[{"en":"Employees perform better when they feel that their work is meaningful.","zh":"當員工感到自己的工作有意義，他們會表現更好。"},{"en":"To feel that their work is meaningful means to believe their job has purpose and value.","zh":"To feel that their work is meaningful 指相信自己的工作有目的和價值。"},{"en":"A hospital cleaner may feel their work is meaningful because it protects patients from infection.","zh":"醫院清潔工可能因工作保護病人免受感染而感到自己的工作有意義。"},{"en":"If people see how their work helps others, they may put in more effort.","zh":"如果人們看見自己的工作如何幫助他人，他們可能投入更多努力。"},{"en":"This phrase connects meaning with motivation and performance.","zh":"這個片語把意義與動機和表現連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"set higher goals","meaning":"訂立更高目標","examples":[{"en":"Stretch goals can encourage employees to set higher goals.","zh":"挑戰性目標可以鼓勵員工訂立更高目標。"},{"en":"To set higher goals means to choose more ambitious targets than before.","zh":"To set higher goals 指選擇比以前更有野心的目標。"},{"en":"A student may set higher goals after seeing clear improvement in mock exams.","zh":"學生在模擬試看見明顯進步後，可能訂立更高目標。"},{"en":"If goals are raised gradually, people may improve without feeling overwhelmed.","zh":"如果目標逐步提高，人們可能進步而不感到不勝負荷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes aiming beyond the previous level.","zh":"這個片語描述追求高於之前水平的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"repetitive tasks","meaning":"重複性工作","examples":[{"en":"Employees may become bored by repetitive tasks.","zh":"員工可能因重複性工作而感到沉悶。"},{"en":"Repetitive tasks are tasks that are done again and again in the same way.","zh":"Repetitive tasks 是以同一方式一再重複完成的任務。"},{"en":"Copying the same sentence fifty times can feel like a repetitive task.","zh":"抄同一句子五十次可能感覺像重複性工作。"},{"en":"If work is too repetitive, employees may lose concentration and interest.","zh":"如果工作太重複，員工可能失去專注和興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes work that lacks variety.","zh":"這個片語描述缺乏變化的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"which of the following is true about","meaning":"以下哪項關於……是正確的","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which statement is true about the drive to defend.","zh":"題目問以下哪項關於防衛的驅動力是正確的。"},{"en":"Which of the following is true about asks students to choose the accurate statement from several options.","zh":"Which of the following is true about 要求學生從幾個選項中選出準確陳述。"},{"en":"In a reading exam, students must check each option against the passage.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生必須用文章核對每個選項。"},{"en":"If one option sounds reasonable but is not supported, it should not be chosen.","zh":"如果一個選項聽起來合理但沒有支持，就不應選。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a fact-checking multiple-choice question.","zh":"這個片語引出查核事實的選擇題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"difficult to allocate","meaning":"難以分配","examples":[{"en":"Organisational resources may be difficult to allocate fairly.","zh":"組織資源可能難以公平分配。"},{"en":"Difficult to allocate means hard to divide or distribute properly.","zh":"Difficult to allocate 指難以適當劃分或分配。"},{"en":"A teacher may find classroom time difficult to allocate when some students need extra help.","zh":"當一些學生需要額外幫助，老師可能覺得課堂時間難以分配。"},{"en":"If resources are limited, every allocation decision may create disagreement.","zh":"如果資源有限，每個分配決定都可能造成分歧。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the challenge of fair distribution.","zh":"這個片語描述公平分配的挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"more difficult to implement than","meaning":"比……更難實施","examples":[{"en":"The drive to defend may be more difficult to implement than other drives.","zh":"防衛的驅動力可能比其他驅動力更難實施。"},{"en":"More difficult to implement than means harder to put into practice compared with something else.","zh":"More difficult to implement than 指相比另一事物更難付諸實行。"},{"en":"A school rule about kindness may be more difficult to implement than a rule about uniforms.","zh":"關於善待他人的校規可能比校服規則更難實施。"},{"en":"If fairness depends on many people’s perceptions, implementation becomes complex.","zh":"如果公平取決於許多人的感受，實施就會變得複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase compares practical difficulty between ideas or policies.","zh":"這個片語比較理念或政策之間的實行難度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"voice their own opinions","meaning":"表達自己的意見","examples":[{"en":"Employees think it is important to voice their own opinions.","zh":"員工認為表達自己的意見很重要。"},{"en":"To voice their own opinions means to express their views openly.","zh":"To voice their own opinions 指公開表達自己的看法。"},{"en":"Students should be allowed to voice their own opinions during class discussions.","zh":"學生應被容許在課堂討論中表達自己的意見。"},{"en":"If workers cannot voice opinions, useful warnings may never reach managers.","zh":"如果員工不能表達意見，有用警告可能永遠傳不到管理者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes speaking up rather than staying silent.","zh":"這個片語描述發聲，而不是保持沉默。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"feel connected to a company","meaning":"感到與公司有連繫","examples":[{"en":"Employees may want to feel connected to a company after a merger.","zh":"合併後，員工可能想感到與公司有連繫。"},{"en":"To feel connected to a company means to feel linked to its people, purpose, and future.","zh":"To feel connected to a company 指感到與公司的員工、目的和未來有連繫。"},{"en":"New staff may feel connected to a company when colleagues welcome them warmly.","zh":"當同事熱情歡迎新員工，新員工可能感到與公司有連繫。"},{"en":"If employees feel no connection after a merger, they may resist the new organisation.","zh":"如果員工在合併後沒有連繫感，他們可能抗拒新組織。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional attachment to the workplace.","zh":"這個片語描述對職場的情感依附。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"after a merger","meaning":"合併後","examples":[{"en":"Employees may show concern after a merger.","zh":"合併後，員工可能表示憂慮。"},{"en":"After a merger means following the joining of two companies or organisations.","zh":"After a merger 指兩間公司或組織合併之後。"},{"en":"After a merger, staff may need new job titles and reporting lines.","zh":"合併後，員工可能需要新的職銜和匯報線。"},{"en":"If communication is poor after a merger, rumours may spread quickly.","zh":"如果合併後溝通欠佳，謠言可能迅速擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the period following organisational combination.","zh":"這個片語描述組織結合後的時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"choose three letters","meaning":"選出三個字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose three letters from the answer options.","zh":"考生從答案選項中選出三個字母。"},{"en":"To choose three letters means to select three correct options, usually from a list.","zh":"To choose three letters 指通常從列表中選出三個正確選項。"},{"en":"Students should check whether the question allows answers in any order.","zh":"學生應檢查題目是否容許答案以任何次序排列。"},{"en":"If only two answers are chosen, one mark may be lost even if both are correct.","zh":"如果只選兩個答案，即使兩個都正確，也可能失去一分。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in multiple-answer reading tasks.","zh":"這個片語是多答案閱讀題中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the following statements","meaning":"以下陳述","examples":[{"en":"Students decide which of the following statements are true.","zh":"學生判斷以下陳述哪些是正確的。"},{"en":"The following statements are the sentences listed after the instruction.","zh":"The following statements 是指示後列出的句子。"},{"en":"Students should read the following statements before scanning the passage.","zh":"學生應先閱讀以下陳述，再掃讀文章。"},{"en":"If a statement changes one key word, it may become false.","zh":"如果陳述改變一個關鍵字，它可能變成錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the claims students must judge.","zh":"這個片語引出學生必須判斷的說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be true of","meaning":"對……而言屬實","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which statements are true of the study of drives.","zh":"題目問哪些陳述對驅動力研究而言屬實。"},{"en":"To be true of something means to be correct about that thing.","zh":"To be true of something 指對某事而言是正確的。"},{"en":"It is true of many students that they learn better with examples.","zh":"許多學生透過例子學得更好，這對他們而言屬實。"},{"en":"If a statement is not supported by the passage, it is not true of the topic.","zh":"如果陳述沒有文章支持，它就不對該主題而言屬實。"},{"en":"This phrase checks whether a claim accurately describes something.","zh":"這個片語檢查某說法是否準確描述某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"feel that they belong to","meaning":"感到自己屬於……","examples":[{"en":"Employees are more motivated if they feel that they belong to the company.","zh":"如果員工感到自己屬於公司，他們會更有動力。"},{"en":"To feel that they belong to something means to feel accepted as part of it.","zh":"To feel that they belong to something 指感到被接納為某事物的一部分。"},{"en":"A student may feel they belong to a class when classmates listen to their ideas.","zh":"當同學聆聽學生想法時，他可能感到自己屬於班級。"},{"en":"If employees belong emotionally to a company, they may be more loyal.","zh":"如果員工在情感上屬於公司，他們可能更忠誠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes feeling included in a group or organisation.","zh":"這個片語描述感到被納入群體或組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"training and development programme","meaning":"培訓及發展計劃","examples":[{"en":"A training and development programme may enhance employee motivation.","zh":"培訓及發展計劃可能提升員工動機。"},{"en":"A training and development programme is a planned set of activities that helps people learn and grow professionally.","zh":"Training and development programme 是幫助人專業學習和成長的一套計劃活動。"},{"en":"A new teacher may join a development programme to improve classroom management.","zh":"新老師可能參加發展計劃，以改善課堂管理。"},{"en":"If employees gain skills through training, they may feel more confident and valued.","zh":"如果員工透過培訓獲得技能，他們可能感到更有信心和被重視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised learning for career growth.","zh":"這個片語描述為事業成長而設的有組織學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be enhanced","meaning":"得到提升","examples":[{"en":"Employees’ motivation may be enhanced by suitable opportunities.","zh":"員工動機可能透過合適機會得到提升。"},{"en":"To be enhanced means to be improved, strengthened, or made better.","zh":"To be enhanced 指得到改善、加強或變得更好。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence can be enhanced by clear praise and useful feedback.","zh":"學生信心可以透過清晰讚賞和有用回饋得到提升。"},{"en":"If job roles become more meaningful, motivation may be enhanced.","zh":"如果工作角色變得更有意義，動機可能得到提升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improvement in quality or strength.","zh":"這個片語描述質素或強度上的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"working goals","meaning":"工作目標","examples":[{"en":"Employees’ working goals may affect their motivation.","zh":"員工的工作目標可能影響他們的動機。"},{"en":"Working goals are targets employees aim to achieve in their jobs.","zh":"Working goals 是員工在工作中想達成的目標。"},{"en":"A teacher’s working goal may be to help every student improve one writing level.","zh":"老師的工作目標可能是幫助每位學生提升一個寫作水平。"},{"en":"If goals are unclear, workers may not know what effort matters most.","zh":"如果目標不清晰，員工可能不知道哪種努力最重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes job-related targets that guide effort.","zh":"這個片語描述引導努力的工作相關目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be aligned with","meaning":"與……一致","examples":[{"en":"Employees may be more motivated when their goals are aligned with organisational objectives.","zh":"當員工目標與組織目標一致，他們可能更有動力。"},{"en":"To be aligned with something means to match or support it.","zh":"To be aligned with something 指與某事相配或支持某事。"},{"en":"A student’s revision plan should be aligned with the exam requirements.","zh":"學生的溫習計劃應與考試要求一致。"},{"en":"If personal goals match company goals, employees may feel their work has direction.","zh":"如果個人目標與公司目標相配，員工可能覺得工作有方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes agreement between two aims or systems.","zh":"這個片語描述兩個目標或系統之間的一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"organisational objectives","meaning":"組織目標","examples":[{"en":"Working goals should be aligned with organisational objectives.","zh":"工作目標應與組織目標一致。"},{"en":"Organisational objectives are the goals an organisation wants to achieve.","zh":"Organisational objectives 是組織想達成的目標。"},{"en":"A school’s organisational objectives may include better attendance and stronger exam results.","zh":"學校的組織目標可能包括更好出席率和更強考試成績。"},{"en":"If employees do not understand the organisation’s objectives, their effort may be scattered.","zh":"如果員工不理解組織目標，他們的努力可能分散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the official goals of a company or institution.","zh":"這個片語描述公司或機構的正式目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be reinforced","meaning":"得到加強","examples":[{"en":"Motivation can be reinforced when employees understand their goals.","zh":"當員工理解目標時，動機可以得到加強。"},{"en":"To be reinforced means to be strengthened or supported.","zh":"To be reinforced 指得到強化或支持。"},{"en":"A student’s good habit can be reinforced by praise and visible progress.","zh":"學生的好習慣可以透過讚賞和可見進步得到加強。"},{"en":"If workers see clear results from their effort, motivation may become stronger.","zh":"如果員工看見努力帶來清晰成果，動機可能變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making something stronger over time.","zh":"這個片語描述隨時間令某事更強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"as their first priority","meaning":"作為首要任務","examples":[{"en":"Companies should not always treat salary increases as their first priority.","zh":"公司不應總是把加薪作為首要任務。"},{"en":"As their first priority means as the most important thing to deal with first.","zh":"As their first priority 指作為最重要且最先處理的事情。"},{"en":"A student with poor sleep may need rest as their first priority before extra tutoring.","zh":"睡眠差的學生可能需要把休息作為首要任務，而不是額外補習。"},{"en":"If pay is treated as the only priority, deeper motivation problems may remain.","zh":"如果薪酬被視為唯一優先事項，更深層動機問題可能仍存在。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what comes before other concerns.","zh":"這個片語指出甚麼先於其他關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"insufficiently challenging","meaning":"挑戰性不足","examples":[{"en":"Employees may leave if their work is insufficiently challenging.","zh":"如果工作挑戰性不足，員工可能離開。"},{"en":"Insufficiently challenging means not difficult or interesting enough to encourage growth.","zh":"Insufficiently challenging 指不夠困難或有趣，未能鼓勵成長。"},{"en":"A strong student may become bored if every exercise is insufficiently challenging.","zh":"如果每個練習都挑戰性不足，能力強的學生可能感到沉悶。"},{"en":"If a job offers no challenge, employees may feel their skills are being wasted.","zh":"如果工作沒有挑戰，員工可能覺得技能被浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes tasks that are too easy or unstimulating.","zh":"這個片語描述太容易或缺乏刺激的任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"agree with the claims of","meaning":"與……的主張一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements agree with the claims of the writer.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與作者的主張一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the claims of someone means to match what that person argues or states.","zh":"To agree with the claims of someone 指符合某人提出或陳述的看法。"},{"en":"In reading tests, an answer agrees with the writer only if the passage supports it.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，答案只有在文章支持時才與作者一致。"},{"en":"If a statement changes the writer’s meaning, it does not agree with the claim.","zh":"如果陳述改變作者意思，它就不與主張一致。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in YES, NO, NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個片語用於 YES、NO、NOT GIVEN 題型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the views of the writer","meaning":"作者的觀點","examples":[{"en":"Students must compare each statement with the views of the writer.","zh":"學生必須把每項陳述與作者的觀點比較。"},{"en":"The views of the writer are the opinions or arguments expressed by the author.","zh":"The views of the writer 是作者表達的意見或論點。"},{"en":"A student should separate the writer’s views from examples given only for discussion.","zh":"學生應把作者觀點與只作討論的例子分開。"},{"en":"If the writer presents two sides but supports one, students must identify that position.","zh":"如果作者呈現兩方但支持其中一方，學生必須辨認該立場。"},{"en":"This phrase asks students to understand the author’s stance.","zh":"這個片語要求學生理解作者立場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A “NO” answer means the statement contradicts the views of the writer.","zh":"“NO” 答案表示陳述與作者的觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what that person believes or argues.","zh":"To contradict the views of someone 指說出與某人相信或主張相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the writer says rewards matter, a statement saying rewards never matter would contradict the view.","zh":"如果作者說獎勵重要，而陳述說獎勵從不重要，就與觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should look for direct opposition, not just missing information.","zh":"學生應尋找直接相反，而不只是沒有資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes conflict between a statement and an opinion.","zh":"這個片語描述陳述與觀點之間的衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Students choose “NOT GIVEN” if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"如果無法判斷作者想法，學生選擇 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"Impossible to say 指沒有足夠資訊作決定。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions salary levels, it is impossible to say whether salaries increased.","zh":"如果文章從未提及薪酬水平，就無法判斷薪酬是否上升。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when the evidence is missing.","zh":"證據缺失時，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when the text does not support either YES or NO.","zh":"這個片語用於文本不支持 YES 或 NO 的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"increasing pay","meaning":"加薪","examples":[{"en":"Increasing pay may lead to higher motivation in some situations.","zh":"在某些情況下，加薪可能帶來更高動機。"},{"en":"Increasing pay means raising employees’ salary, wages, or financial rewards.","zh":"Increasing pay 指提高員工薪金、工資或金錢獎勵。"},{"en":"A company may increase pay to keep experienced staff from leaving.","zh":"公司可能加薪以留住有經驗員工。"},{"en":"If pay was previously unfair, increasing it may improve trust and morale.","zh":"如果薪酬之前不公平，加薪可能改善信任和士氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using money as one possible motivation tool.","zh":"這個片語描述把金錢作為一種可能激勵工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"high work motivation","meaning":"高工作動機","examples":[{"en":"Recognition and rewards can contribute to high work motivation.","zh":"認可和獎勵可以促成高工作動機。"},{"en":"High work motivation means a strong desire to put effort into one’s job.","zh":"High work motivation 指把努力投入工作的強烈欲望。"},{"en":"A teacher with high work motivation prepares lessons carefully even after a long day.","zh":"有高工作動機的老師即使長日工作後也會仔細備課。"},{"en":"If employees have high motivation, they may solve problems more actively.","zh":"如果員工有高動機，他們可能更主動解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong energy and willingness at work.","zh":"這個片語描述工作中的強烈能量和意願。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"local companies","meaning":"本地公司","examples":[{"en":"The question compares local companies with global companies.","zh":"題目把本地公司與全球性公司作比較。"},{"en":"Local companies are businesses that operate mainly in one area, city, or country.","zh":"Local companies 是主要在某一地區、城市或國家營運的企業。"},{"en":"A local company may know neighbourhood customers better than a multinational chain.","zh":"本地公司可能比跨國連鎖更了解社區顧客。"},{"en":"If research includes only local companies, its findings may not apply everywhere.","zh":"如果研究只包括本地公司，其發現未必適用於所有地方。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts smaller regional businesses with international ones.","zh":"這個片語把較小的地區企業與國際企業作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"benefit more than","meaning":"比……得益更多","examples":[{"en":"One statement asks whether local companies benefit more than global companies.","zh":"一項陳述問本地公司是否比全球性公司得益更多。"},{"en":"To benefit more than someone means to gain a greater advantage than they do.","zh":"To benefit more than someone 指比對方獲得更大好處。"},{"en":"Small shops may benefit more than large chains from a local street festival.","zh":"本地街道節慶可能令小店比大型連鎖得益更多。"},{"en":"If one group receives more support, it may benefit more than another group.","zh":"如果一個群體得到更多支援，它可能比另一群體得益更多。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the size of advantage between groups.","zh":"這個片語比較群體之間好處大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"global companies","meaning":"全球性公司","examples":[{"en":"The studies included employees from global companies.","zh":"研究包括來自全球性公司的員工。"},{"en":"Global companies are businesses that operate across countries and international markets.","zh":"Global companies 是跨國家和國際市場營運的企業。"},{"en":"A global company may have offices in Asia, Europe, and North America.","zh":"全球性公司可能在亞洲、歐洲和北美都有辦公室。"},{"en":"If a policy works in global companies, it may still need local adjustment.","zh":"如果政策在全球性公司有效，它仍可能需要本地調整。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to large internationally active businesses.","zh":"這個片語指大型且活躍於國際的企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"achieve the greatest commitment","meaning":"達到最高投入程度","examples":[{"en":"Employees achieve the greatest commitment when the drive to bond is met.","zh":"當建立連繫的驅動力得到滿足，員工達到最高投入程度。"},{"en":"To achieve the greatest commitment means to reach the highest level of loyalty and dedication.","zh":"To achieve the greatest commitment 指達到最高程度的忠誠和奉獻。"},{"en":"A student may achieve strong commitment to a club when they feel trusted and included.","zh":"當學生感到被信任和被包括，他可能對學會達到很高投入。"},{"en":"If belonging is satisfied, people may stay with a group through difficulty.","zh":"如果歸屬得到滿足，人們可能在困難中仍留在群體中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching maximum dedication.","zh":"這個片語描述達到最大奉獻程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"an unusual attitude","meaning":"不尋常的態度","examples":[{"en":"Employees in the former company showed an unusual attitude during the merger.","zh":"前者公司的員工在合併期間表現出不尋常的態度。"},{"en":"An unusual attitude is a way of thinking or behaving that is not normally expected.","zh":"Unusual attitude 是不太符合一般預期的思考或行為方式。"},{"en":"A class may show an unusual attitude if students volunteer for extra homework.","zh":"如果學生自願做額外功課，班級可能表現出不尋常的態度。"},{"en":"If workers are unusually cooperative during a stressful merger, managers may look for the reason.","zh":"如果員工在壓力大的合併期間異常合作，管理者可能尋找原因。"},{"en":"This phrase describes behaviour or thinking that stands out.","zh":"這個片語描述突出的行為或想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"during the merger","meaning":"在合併期間","examples":[{"en":"Employees showed cooperation during the merger of two companies.","zh":"員工在兩間公司合併期間表現出合作。"},{"en":"During the merger means while two organisations were joining together.","zh":"During the merger 指兩個組織正在結合期間。"},{"en":"During the merger, staff may need new contracts and reporting lines.","zh":"在合併期間，員工可能需要新合約和匯報線。"},{"en":"If leaders communicate clearly during the merger, fear may be reduced.","zh":"如果領袖在合併期間清晰溝通，恐懼可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the time period when a merger is happening.","zh":"這個片語描述合併正在發生的時間段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be conducted to analyse","meaning":"為分析……而進行","examples":[{"en":"The two studies were conducted to analyse the relationship between drives and motivation.","zh":"兩項研究為分析驅動力與動機之間的關係而進行。"},{"en":"To be conducted to analyse something means to be carried out in order to study it carefully.","zh":"To be conducted to analyse something 指為仔細研究某事而進行。"},{"en":"A survey may be conducted to analyse why students skip homework.","zh":"調查可能為分析學生為何不做功課而進行。"},{"en":"If research is conducted carefully, its findings may be more reliable.","zh":"如果研究仔細進行，其發現可能更可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose of a study.","zh":"這個片語解釋研究目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"natural drives","meaning":"自然驅動力","examples":[{"en":"The studies examined natural drives that influence employees.","zh":"研究檢視影響員工的自然驅動力。"},{"en":"Natural drives are basic human forces that arise from normal needs and instincts.","zh":"Natural drives 是來自正常需要和本能的基本人類力量。"},{"en":"The need to belong is a natural drive seen in children and adults.","zh":"歸屬需要是在兒童和成年人身上都可見的自然驅動力。"},{"en":"If natural drives are ignored, workplace systems may feel artificial and ineffective.","zh":"如果自然驅動力被忽視，職場制度可能感覺人為且無效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes motivation rooted in human nature.","zh":"這個片語描述扎根於人性的動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"employees’ attitudes","meaning":"員工態度","examples":[{"en":"The studies looked at how drives relate to employees’ attitudes.","zh":"研究檢視驅動力如何與員工態度有關。"},{"en":"Employees’ attitudes are workers’ feelings, beliefs, and opinions about their work and organisation.","zh":"Employees’ attitudes 是員工對工作和組織的感受、信念和意見。"},{"en":"A company may survey employees’ attitudes after introducing a new timetable.","zh":"公司引入新時間表後，可能調查員工態度。"},{"en":"If attitudes become negative, cooperation and performance may fall.","zh":"如果態度變得負面，合作和表現可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how workers think and feel about their workplace.","zh":"這個片語描述員工如何看待和感受自己的職場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"cause a company to lose profits","meaning":"導致公司失去利潤","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether a reward system causes a company to lose profits.","zh":"該陳述問獎勵制度是否導致公司失去利潤。"},{"en":"To cause a company to lose profits means to make its earnings fall after costs are counted.","zh":"To cause a company to lose profits 指令公司扣除成本後的收益下降。"},{"en":"Poor customer service can cause a shop to lose profits when customers stop returning.","zh":"當顧客不再回來，差劣顧客服務可以導致商店失去利潤。"},{"en":"If rewards are too expensive and do not improve performance, they may damage profit.","zh":"如果獎勵太昂貴且沒有改善表現，它們可能損害利潤。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a business decision with financial loss.","zh":"這個片語把商業決定與財務損失連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 47 - Motivating Drives.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 48":[{"front":"Improving Patient Safety","meaning":"改善病人安全","examples":[{"en":"Improving patient safety requires better design of medicine packaging.","zh":"改善病人安全需要更好的藥物包裝設計。"},{"en":"Improving patient safety means reducing mistakes, confusion, and avoidable harm in healthcare.","zh":"improving patient safety 指減少醫療中的錯誤、混亂和可避免傷害。"},{"en":"A hospital can improve patient safety by checking medicine names carefully before giving drugs.","zh":"醫院可以透過給藥前仔細核對藥名來改善病人安全。"},{"en":"Clear labels improve patient safety because patients are less likely to take the wrong medicine.","zh":"清晰標籤可以改善病人安全，因為病人較不容易服錯藥。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing changes that protect patients from preventable danger.","zh":"討論保護病人免受可避免危險的改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"patient safety","meaning":"病人安全","examples":[{"en":"Good packaging design can improve patient safety.","zh":"良好的包裝設計可以改善病人安全。"},{"en":"Patient safety means protecting patients from mistakes, accidents, or unnecessary harm during healthcare.","zh":"patient safety 指在醫療過程中保護病人免受錯誤、意外或不必要傷害。"},{"en":"Nurses support patient safety when they confirm a patient’s name before treatment.","zh":"護士在治療前確認病人姓名，就是在支援病人安全。"},{"en":"Poor communication can damage patient safety because important warnings may be missed.","zh":"溝通不良會損害病人安全，因為重要警告可能被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how healthcare can become safer.","zh":"討論醫療如何變得更安全時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"drug packaging","meaning":"藥物包裝","examples":[{"en":"Drug packaging is a major design issue in pharmacy.","zh":"藥物包裝是藥劑業中的主要設計問題。"},{"en":"Drug packaging is the box, bottle, label, foil, or leaflet used to contain and explain medicine.","zh":"drug packaging 指用來盛載和說明藥物的盒、瓶、標籤、鋁箔或單張。"},{"en":"A pharmacist checks drug packaging to make sure the right medicine is being given.","zh":"藥劑師會檢查藥物包裝，以確保派發的是正確藥物。"},{"en":"Bad drug packaging can cause errors if two boxes look too similar.","zh":"如果兩個盒子看起來太相似，不良藥物包裝可能造成錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing medicine safety and design.","zh":"討論藥物安全和設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"patient information leaflets","meaning":"病人資料單張","examples":[{"en":"Patient information leaflets should be clear, legible and easy to use.","zh":"病人資料單張應清晰、易讀和易用。"},{"en":"Patient information leaflets are printed sheets that explain how to use a medicine safely.","zh":"patient information leaflets 指解釋如何安全使用藥物的印刷單張。"},{"en":"A patient may read patient information leaflets to check side effects or dosage instructions.","zh":"病人可能閱讀病人資料單張，以查看副作用或劑量指示。"},{"en":"If leaflets are badly organised, patients may miss important safety warnings.","zh":"如果單張組織差劣，病人可能錯過重要安全警告。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing written medicine information.","zh":"討論書面藥物資料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"PILs","meaning":"病人資料單張","examples":[{"en":"PILs give patients important information about their medicines.","zh":"PILs 向病人提供關於藥物的重要資料。"},{"en":"PILs are patient information leaflets included with medicines.","zh":"PILs 是隨藥物附上的病人資料單張。"},{"en":"A patient should read PILs before taking a new medicine for the first time.","zh":"病人第一次服用新藥前應閱讀病人資料單張。"},{"en":"Clear PILs can prevent misuse because patients understand warnings and instructions.","zh":"清晰的病人資料單張可以防止誤用，因為病人明白警告和指示。"},{"en":"This abbreviation is useful in pharmacy and healthcare writing.","zh":"這個縮寫常用於藥劑和醫療寫作。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"prominent design issues","meaning":"重要的設計問題","examples":[{"en":"Drug packaging is one of the most prominent design issues in pharmacy.","zh":"藥物包裝是藥劑業中最重要的設計問題之一。"},{"en":"Prominent design issues are important design problems that are easy to notice and widely discussed.","zh":"prominent design issues 指容易被注意到並被廣泛討論的重要設計問題。"},{"en":"In a school, unclear signs can become prominent design issues if visitors keep getting lost.","zh":"在學校中，如果訪客經常迷路，不清晰標誌可成為重要設計問題。"},{"en":"A design issue becomes prominent when it affects many users or creates safety risks.","zh":"當設計問題影響許多使用者或造成安全風險，它就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a design problem deserves serious attention.","zh":"當設計問題值得認真關注時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in pharmacy","meaning":"在藥劑業中","examples":[{"en":"Packaging is a major safety concern in pharmacy.","zh":"包裝是藥劑業中的主要安全關注。"},{"en":"In pharmacy means in the field or practice of preparing, dispensing, and advising on medicines.","zh":"in pharmacy 指在準備、派發和提供藥物建議的專業領域中。"},{"en":"In pharmacy, clear handwriting and accurate labels can prevent serious mistakes.","zh":"在藥劑業中，清晰字跡和準確標籤可以防止嚴重錯誤。"},{"en":"Small design problems matter in pharmacy because medicines affect health directly.","zh":"在藥劑業中，小設計問題也很重要，因為藥物直接影響健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing medicine-related professional work.","zh":"討論與藥物相關的專業工作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"letters pages","meaning":"讀者來信版","examples":[{"en":"Many complaints have appeared in The Journal’s letters pages.","zh":"許多投訴曾出現在 The Journal 的讀者來信版。"},{"en":"Letters pages are parts of a newspaper or journal where readers’ letters are published.","zh":"letters pages 指報章或期刊中刊登讀者來信的部分。"},{"en":"Teachers may write to the letters pages when they want to comment on education policy.","zh":"老師想評論教育政策時，可能寫信到讀者來信版。"},{"en":"Repeated complaints in letters pages show that a problem worries many readers.","zh":"讀者來信版中反覆出現投訴，顯示問題令許多讀者擔心。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing public professional feedback.","zh":"討論公開專業回饋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"over the years","meaning":"多年來","examples":[{"en":"Many pharmacists have written about packaging problems over the years.","zh":"多年來，許多藥劑師寫過關於包裝問題的文章。"},{"en":"Over the years means during a long period of time.","zh":"over the years 指在一段長時間之中。"},{"en":"Over the years, a teacher may collect many examples of common grammar mistakes.","zh":"多年來，老師可能收集到許多常見文法錯誤例子。"},{"en":"When a problem continues over the years, it is probably not a one-time accident.","zh":"當問題多年來持續，它可能不是一次性意外。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing repeated experience across time.","zh":"描述跨時間的反覆經驗時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pharmacists","meaning":"藥劑師","examples":[{"en":"Pharmacists are often concerned about unsafe medicine packaging.","zh":"藥劑師常關注不安全藥物包裝。"},{"en":"Pharmacists are trained professionals who prepare, check, and give advice about medicines.","zh":"pharmacists 指受過訓練、負責準備、核對和提供藥物建議的專業人士。"},{"en":"A pharmacist may explain to an elderly patient how often to take each tablet.","zh":"藥劑師可能向年長病人解釋每種藥片應多久服用一次。"},{"en":"Pharmacists help prevent harm because they check medicine names, doses, and instructions.","zh":"藥劑師透過核對藥名、劑量和指示來幫助防止傷害。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing medicine safety and healthcare advice.","zh":"討論藥物安全和醫療建議時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be dismayed at","meaning":"對……感到震驚或失望","examples":[{"en":"Pharmacists were dismayed at the poor design of some medicine packaging.","zh":"藥劑師對某些藥物包裝的不良設計感到震驚和失望。"},{"en":"Be dismayed at means feel shocked, disappointed, or worried about something bad.","zh":"be dismayed at 指對壞事感到震驚、失望或憂慮。"},{"en":"A teacher may be dismayed at a student’s unsafe behaviour in the laboratory.","zh":"老師可能對學生在實驗室的不安全行為感到震驚。"},{"en":"People feel dismayed when a preventable problem keeps causing harm.","zh":"當可避免問題持續造成傷害，人們會感到震驚和失望。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when disappointment includes concern.","zh":"當失望同時包含憂慮時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"accidents waiting to happen","meaning":"遲早會出事的隱患","examples":[{"en":"Some packaging designs are accidents waiting to happen.","zh":"有些包裝設計是遲早會出事的隱患。"},{"en":"Accidents waiting to happen are dangerous situations that are likely to cause trouble sooner or later.","zh":"accidents waiting to happen 指遲早可能造成麻煩的危險情況。"},{"en":"A wet staircase with no warning sign is an accident waiting to happen.","zh":"沒有警告標誌的濕樓梯是遲早會出事的隱患。"},{"en":"If medicine boxes look almost identical, they can become accidents waiting to happen.","zh":"如果藥盒看起來幾乎一樣，它們可能成為遲早會出事的隱患。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when warning that danger is predictable.","zh":"警告危險可以預見時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pharmaceutical industry","meaning":"製藥業","examples":[{"en":"Packaging design is important in the pharmaceutical industry.","zh":"包裝設計在製藥業中很重要。"},{"en":"The pharmaceutical industry is the business of developing, making, testing, and selling medicines.","zh":"pharmaceutical industry 指研發、製造、測試和銷售藥物的行業。"},{"en":"The pharmaceutical industry must follow strict rules because its products affect health.","zh":"製藥業必須遵守嚴格規則，因為其產品影響健康。"},{"en":"Poor decisions in the pharmaceutical industry can lead to patient harm or loss of trust.","zh":"製藥業中的差劣決定可能導致病人受害或失去信任。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing medicine companies and drug production.","zh":"討論藥廠和藥物生產時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be handled by","meaning":"由……處理","examples":[{"en":"Packaging design is handled by in-house teams or design agencies.","zh":"包裝設計由內部團隊或設計公司處理。"},{"en":"Be handled by means be managed, dealt with, or done by someone.","zh":"be handled by 指由某人管理、處理或完成。"},{"en":"School timetable changes may be handled by the office staff.","zh":"學校時間表更改可能由辦公室職員處理。"},{"en":"A task is done better when it is handled by people with the right training.","zh":"當任務由受過合適訓練的人處理，通常會做得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining responsibility.","zh":"解釋責任由誰負責時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in-house teams","meaning":"內部團隊","examples":[{"en":"Some packaging designs are handled by in-house teams.","zh":"有些包裝設計由內部團隊處理。"},{"en":"In-house teams are groups of workers employed within the same company or organisation.","zh":"in-house teams 指同一公司或機構內受僱的工作團隊。"},{"en":"A school may use an in-house team to design posters for open day.","zh":"學校可能使用內部團隊設計開放日海報。"},{"en":"In-house teams know company rules well, but they may need outside opinions for fresh ideas.","zh":"內部團隊熟悉公司規則，但可能需要外部意見帶來新想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when work is done internally.","zh":"當工作在機構內部完成時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"design agencies","meaning":"設計公司","examples":[{"en":"Design agencies are often commissioned to design over-the-counter medicines.","zh":"設計公司常被委託設計非處方藥。"},{"en":"Design agencies are outside companies hired to create visual designs, packaging, branding, or layouts.","zh":"design agencies 指受聘創造視覺設計、包裝、品牌或版面的外部公司。"},{"en":"A restaurant may hire a design agency to create a new menu and logo.","zh":"餐廳可能聘請設計公司製作新餐牌和標誌。"},{"en":"Design agencies can bring fresh ideas because they are not part of the company’s daily routine.","zh":"設計公司能帶來新想法，因為它們不屬於公司的日常流程。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when outside specialists create designs.","zh":"當外部專家創作設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"over-the-counter medicines","meaning":"非處方藥","examples":[{"en":"Over-the-counter medicines are usually designed with customers in mind.","zh":"非處方藥通常以顧客為設計考慮。"},{"en":"Over-the-counter medicines are medicines people can buy without a doctor’s prescription.","zh":"over-the-counter medicines 指不需要醫生處方即可購買的藥物。"},{"en":"Cough syrup and simple painkillers are often over-the-counter medicines.","zh":"咳藥水和普通止痛藥常是非處方藥。"},{"en":"Their packaging must be clear because customers may choose them without professional help.","zh":"它們的包裝必須清晰，因為顧客可能在沒有專業協助下自行選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing medicines sold directly to the public.","zh":"討論直接售予公眾的藥物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"characteristics such as","meaning":"……等特點","examples":[{"en":"Characteristics such as attractiveness and distinguishability are regarded as significant.","zh":"吸引力和可辨識度等特點被視為重要。"},{"en":"Characteristics such as means features like the examples that follow.","zh":"characteristics such as 指例如後面所列的特徵。"},{"en":"Schools value characteristics such as honesty, curiosity, and responsibility in students.","zh":"學校重視學生的誠實、好奇心和責任感等特點。"},{"en":"Listing characteristics helps readers understand what qualities matter in a situation.","zh":"列出特點幫助讀者理解在某情況中哪些品質重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving examples of important features.","zh":"舉出重要特徵例子時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"attractiveness","meaning":"吸引力","examples":[{"en":"Attractiveness is important in the design of over-the-counter medicines.","zh":"吸引力在非處方藥設計中很重要。"},{"en":"Attractiveness means the quality of looking pleasant, appealing, or interesting.","zh":"attractiveness 指看起來令人愉快、吸引或有趣的特質。"},{"en":"A shop display needs attractiveness if it is meant to catch customers’ attention.","zh":"如果商店陳列要吸引顧客注意，就需要吸引力。"},{"en":"Attractive packaging can help a product stand out, but safety information must remain clear.","zh":"吸引人的包裝可以幫助產品突出，但安全資訊仍必須清楚。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing visual appeal.","zh":"討論視覺吸引力時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"distinguishability","meaning":"可辨識度；可區分性","examples":[{"en":"Distinguishability helps consumers tell one product from another.","zh":"可辨識度幫助消費者分辨一種產品和另一種產品。"},{"en":"Distinguishability means how easily one thing can be recognised as different from another.","zh":"distinguishability 指某物有多容易被辨認為不同於另一物。"},{"en":"School uniforms need distinguishability if different teams wear similar colours.","zh":"如果不同隊伍穿相似顏色，校服就需要可辨識度。"},{"en":"Low distinguishability can cause mistakes when people choose quickly.","zh":"可區分性低會在人們快速選擇時造成錯誤。"},{"en":"This word is useful when similar items must be clearly separated.","zh":"當相似物品必須清楚分開時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be regarded as significant","meaning":"被視為重要","examples":[{"en":"Attractiveness and distinguishability are regarded as significant.","zh":"吸引力和可辨識度被視為重要。"},{"en":"Be regarded as significant means be considered important or worth attention.","zh":"be regarded as significant 指被認為重要或值得注意。"},{"en":"Clear pronunciation is regarded as significant in speaking exams.","zh":"清晰發音在口語考試中被視為重要。"},{"en":"A feature is regarded as significant when it affects decisions, safety, or results.","zh":"當某特點影響決定、安全或結果，它就會被視為重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining what people value.","zh":"解釋人們重視甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be commissioned from","meaning":"委託……製作","examples":[{"en":"Designs for over-the-counter medicines are often commissioned from design agencies.","zh":"非處方藥的設計常委託設計公司製作。"},{"en":"Be commissioned from means be officially requested and paid for from an outside person or company.","zh":"be commissioned from 指正式向外部人士或公司要求並付費製作。"},{"en":"A school may commission a new mural from a local artist.","zh":"學校可能委託本地藝術家製作新壁畫。"},{"en":"Work is commissioned when an organisation needs specialist skills it does not have internally.","zh":"當機構需要內部沒有的專業技能，工作就會被委託出去。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when outside experts are hired to produce work.","zh":"當外部專家受聘製作作品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"marketing team","meaning":"市場推廣團隊","examples":[{"en":"A marketing team prepares a brief for the designers.","zh":"市場推廣團隊為設計師準備設計簡介。"},{"en":"A marketing team is a group responsible for promoting products and understanding customers.","zh":"marketing team 指負責推廣產品和了解顧客的團隊。"},{"en":"A marketing team may study what colours attract young shoppers.","zh":"市場推廣團隊可能研究哪些顏色吸引年輕購物者。"},{"en":"The marketing team influences design because it knows how customers may react.","zh":"市場推廣團隊會影響設計，因為它知道顧客可能如何反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing business promotion and product planning.","zh":"討論商業推廣和產品規劃時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prepare a brief","meaning":"準備設計簡介","examples":[{"en":"The marketing team prepares a brief before designers create possible designs.","zh":"市場推廣團隊在設計師創作可能設計前準備設計簡介。"},{"en":"Prepare a brief means write clear instructions, aims, and requirements for a project.","zh":"prepare a brief 指為項目寫下清楚指示、目標和要求。"},{"en":"A teacher may prepare a brief before students begin a group presentation.","zh":"老師可能在學生開始小組匯報前準備簡介。"},{"en":"A good brief prevents confusion because everyone knows the goal and limits.","zh":"良好簡介可以防止混亂，因為每個人都知道目標和限制。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when planning creative or professional work.","zh":"規劃創意或專業工作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"come up with","meaning":"想出；提出","examples":[{"en":"Designers may come up with six or seven designs.","zh":"設計師可能想出六至七個設計。"},{"en":"Come up with means think of or produce an idea, plan, or solution.","zh":"come up with 指想到或提出想法、計劃或解決方法。"},{"en":"Students may come up with several titles before choosing the best one for an essay.","zh":"學生可能先想出幾個標題，然後選最適合作文的一個。"},{"en":"Teams often come up with more ideas when they understand the problem clearly.","zh":"當團隊清楚理解問題，他們通常能提出更多想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing idea generation.","zh":"描述產生想法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"whittle something down to","meaning":"將……篩選至","examples":[{"en":"The designs are whittled down to two or three options.","zh":"這些設計被篩選至兩三個選項。"},{"en":"Whittle something down to means gradually reduce a larger number to a smaller, better selection.","zh":"whittle something down to 指逐步把較多數量減少至較小而更好的選擇。"},{"en":"A student may whittle ten essay ideas down to three strong ones.","zh":"學生可能把十個作文想法篩選至三個較強的想法。"},{"en":"Selection helps teams focus time and money on the most promising choices.","zh":"篩選幫助團隊把時間和金錢集中在最有希望的選擇上。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when many options must be narrowed.","zh":"當許多選項必須被縮小範圍時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be tested on","meaning":"在……身上測試","examples":[{"en":"The final designs may be tested on a consumer group.","zh":"最終設計可能在消費者小組身上測試。"},{"en":"Be tested on means be tried with a person or group to see how well it works.","zh":"be tested on 指讓某人或某群體試用，以了解其效果。"},{"en":"A new school app may be tested on a small class before the whole school uses it.","zh":"新學校應用程式可能先在小班身上測試，再全校使用。"},{"en":"Testing reveals problems that designers may not notice by themselves.","zh":"測試能揭示設計師自己未必注意到的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a product is checked with real users.","zh":"當產品以真實使用者檢查時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"consumer group","meaning":"消費者小組","examples":[{"en":"The designs may be tested on a consumer group.","zh":"這些設計可能在消費者小組身上測試。"},{"en":"A consumer group is a selected group of customers used to test opinions, reactions, or understanding.","zh":"consumer group 指被選出用來測試意見、反應或理解的一組顧客。"},{"en":"A supermarket may ask a consumer group to taste a new drink before selling it.","zh":"超市可能請消費者小組試飲新飲品，然後才出售。"},{"en":"Consumer groups help companies see whether ordinary people understand a product.","zh":"消費者小組幫助公司了解普通人是否理解產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when designs are tested with potential buyers.","zh":"當設計以潛在買家測試時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"In contrast, prescription-only products are usually designed in-house.","zh":"相比之下，處方藥產品通常由內部設計。"},{"en":"In contrast means on the other hand, showing a clear difference from the previous point.","zh":"in contrast 指另一方面，用來顯示與前一點清楚不同。"},{"en":"Some students enjoy group work; in contrast, others prefer quiet individual study.","zh":"有些學生喜歡小組工作；相比之下，其他學生較喜歡安靜獨自學習。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers notice a shift between two different situations.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者注意兩種不同情況之間的轉變。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing opposite or different practices.","zh":"比較相反或不同做法時，它很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prescription-only products","meaning":"處方藥產品","examples":[{"en":"Most prescription-only products are created in-house.","zh":"大多數處方藥產品由內部製作。"},{"en":"Prescription-only products are medicines that patients can get only with a doctor’s prescription.","zh":"prescription-only products 指病人只能憑醫生處方取得的藥物。"},{"en":"Strong antibiotics are often prescription-only products because they must be used carefully.","zh":"強效抗生素常是處方藥產品，因為必須小心使用。"},{"en":"These products need accurate packaging because mistakes may be serious.","zh":"這些產品需要準確包裝，因為錯誤可能很嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing medicines controlled by prescription.","zh":"討論受處方管制的藥物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be created in-house","meaning":"由內部製作","examples":[{"en":"Prescription-only packaging is often created in-house.","zh":"處方藥包裝常由內部製作。"},{"en":"Be created in-house means be designed or produced by people inside the company.","zh":"be created in-house 指由公司內部人員設計或製作。"},{"en":"A school newsletter may be created in-house by teachers and office staff.","zh":"學校通訊可能由老師和辦公室職員內部製作。"},{"en":"In-house creation can save money, but it may limit outside perspectives.","zh":"內部製作可以省錢，但可能限制外部觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when work is not outsourced.","zh":"當工作沒有外判時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in some cases","meaning":"在某些情況下","examples":[{"en":"In some cases, the design simply applies the company’s house design.","zh":"在某些情況下，設計只是套用公司的統一設計風格。"},{"en":"In some cases means in certain situations, but not all situations.","zh":"in some cases 指在某些情況中，但不是所有情況。"},{"en":"In some cases, students need extra speaking practice before they can join group discussions confidently.","zh":"在某些情況下，學生需要額外口語練習，才可有信心參與小組討論。"},{"en":"This phrase prevents overgeneralisation because it shows the point is not always true.","zh":"這個短語防止過度概括，因為它顯示某點並非總是正確。"},{"en":"It is useful when a statement applies only sometimes.","zh":"當陳述只在部分情況適用時，它很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"involve applying","meaning":"涉及套用","examples":[{"en":"The process may involve applying a company’s house design.","zh":"這個過程可能涉及套用公司的統一設計風格。"},{"en":"Involve applying means include the action of using or putting something into practice.","zh":"involve applying 指包括使用或實踐某事物這個動作。"},{"en":"A school project may involve applying research skills to a real community problem.","zh":"學校專題可能涉及把研究技能應用到真實社區問題。"},{"en":"Applying an existing design can save time but may reduce product distinction.","zh":"套用既有設計可以省時間，但可能降低產品區分度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one action forms part of a larger process.","zh":"當某動作是一個較大過程的一部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"house design","meaning":"公司統一設計風格","examples":[{"en":"A company’s house design includes its logo, colour and font.","zh":"公司的統一設計風格包括其標誌、顏色和字體。"},{"en":"House design is a company’s standard visual style used across its products or documents.","zh":"house design 指公司在產品或文件中使用的標準視覺風格。"},{"en":"A school may have a house design for notices, using the same logo and colours each time.","zh":"學校可能有通告的統一設計風格，每次使用相同標誌和顏色。"},{"en":"A consistent house design builds recognition, but it can make different products look too similar.","zh":"一致的統一設計風格建立辨識度，但也可能令不同產品看起來太相似。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing brand style.","zh":"討論品牌風格時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"logo, colour and font","meaning":"標誌、顏色和字體","examples":[{"en":"The house design includes the logo, colour and font.","zh":"統一設計風格包括標誌、顏色和字體。"},{"en":"Logo, colour and font are visual elements that help people recognise a brand or organisation.","zh":"logo, colour and font 指幫助人們識別品牌或機構的視覺元素。"},{"en":"A school poster looks more professional when its logo, colour and font are consistent.","zh":"當學校海報的標誌、顏色和字體一致，它看起來更專業。"},{"en":"Consistent visual elements build trust, but confusing ones can make information harder to read.","zh":"一致的視覺元素建立信任，但混亂的元素會令資訊更難閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing visual identity.","zh":"討論視覺身份時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"and so on","meaning":"等等","examples":[{"en":"The design includes the logo, colour, font and so on.","zh":"設計包括標誌、顏色、字體等等。"},{"en":"And so on means and other similar things.","zh":"and so on 指以及其他類似事物。"},{"en":"Students should bring pens, pencils, rulers and so on for the exam.","zh":"學生應帶備筆、鉛筆、間尺等等參加考試。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids listing every item when the remaining examples are easy to guess.","zh":"當餘下例子容易猜到，這個短語可避免列出每一項。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving a short, incomplete list.","zh":"給出簡短且未完整列出的清單時，它很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"chosen design","meaning":"選定的設計","examples":[{"en":"The chosen design is handed over to design engineers.","zh":"選定的設計被交給設計工程師。"},{"en":"The chosen design is the option selected after comparing different possible designs.","zh":"chosen design 指在比較不同可能設計後被選出的選項。"},{"en":"After students vote on three poster ideas, the chosen design is printed for the school event.","zh":"學生為三個海報想法投票後，選定的設計會被印作學校活動海報。"},{"en":"A chosen design moves to the next stage because decision-makers believe it works best.","zh":"選定的設計進入下一階段，因為決策者相信它最合適。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one design is selected from several options.","zh":"當一個設計從多個選項中被選出時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"hand something over to","meaning":"將某物交給……","examples":[{"en":"The chosen design is handed over to design engineers.","zh":"選定的設計被交給設計工程師。"},{"en":"Hand something over to means pass responsibility or control of something to another person or group.","zh":"hand something over to 指把某物的責任或控制權交給另一人或團隊。"},{"en":"A teacher may hand a class project over to the student leaders after explaining the rules.","zh":"老師解釋規則後，可能把班級專題交給學生領袖。"},{"en":"Handover matters because the next team must understand what has already been decided.","zh":"交接很重要，因為下一個團隊必須明白已決定的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when work moves from one person or stage to another.","zh":"當工作由一個人或階段轉到另一個時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"design engineers","meaning":"設計工程師","examples":[{"en":"Design engineers work out how the packaging will be produced.","zh":"設計工程師制定包裝將如何生產。"},{"en":"Design engineers are professionals who turn design ideas into practical, manufacturable products.","zh":"design engineers 指把設計想法變成實際可製造產品的專業人士。"},{"en":"A design engineer may adjust a bottle shape so machines can fill it safely.","zh":"設計工程師可能調整瓶子形狀，讓機器能安全灌裝。"},{"en":"Without design engineers, a beautiful design may be impossible or too costly to produce.","zh":"沒有設計工程師，美觀設計可能無法生產或成本太高。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing technical product development.","zh":"討論技術產品開發時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"work out how","meaning":"制定如何；弄清楚如何","examples":[{"en":"Design engineers work out how the packaging will be produced.","zh":"設計工程師制定包裝將如何生產。"},{"en":"Work out how means find a practical method or solution.","zh":"work out how 指找出實際方法或解決方案。"},{"en":"Students may work out how to divide a group project fairly.","zh":"學生可能弄清楚如何公平分配小組專題工作。"},{"en":"Working out how to do something prevents confusion when the plan becomes real.","zh":"制定如何做某事，可以在計劃實行時防止混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when solving practical problems.","zh":"解決實際問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Design considerations","meaning":"設計考慮因素","examples":[{"en":"Design considerations include how medicines are used in real situations.","zh":"設計考慮因素包括藥物在真實情況中如何使用。"},{"en":"Design considerations are factors that designers must think about before making a product.","zh":"design considerations 指設計師製作產品前必須思考的因素。"},{"en":"For a school bag, design considerations include weight, size, comfort, and durability.","zh":"對書包而言，設計考慮因素包括重量、大小、舒適度和耐用性。"},{"en":"Ignoring design considerations can create products that look good but fail in daily use.","zh":"忽視設計考慮因素會創造出看起來好但日常使用失敗的產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when listing what designers must take into account.","zh":"列出設計師必須考慮的事情時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"recently published","meaning":"最近出版的","examples":[{"en":"Thea Swayne is the author of a recently published book on patient safety.","zh":"Thea Swayne 是一本最近出版的病人安全書籍的作者。"},{"en":"Recently published means made available to readers not long ago.","zh":"recently published 指不久前出版並可供讀者閱讀。"},{"en":"A recently published report may contain newer evidence than an old textbook.","zh":"最近出版的報告可能比舊教科書包含更新證據。"},{"en":"Recent publications can influence professional practice if they highlight urgent problems.","zh":"如果近期出版物突顯迫切問題，它們可以影響專業實踐。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when referring to new books, reports, or studies.","zh":"提及新書、報告或研究時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"information design","meaning":"資料設計","examples":[{"en":"Information design can affect patient safety.","zh":"資料設計可以影響病人安全。"},{"en":"Information design is the way information is organised, written, and shown so people can understand it.","zh":"information design 指組織、撰寫和展示資訊的方式，使人能理解。"},{"en":"A bus timetable needs good information design so passengers can find times quickly.","zh":"巴士時間表需要良好資料設計，讓乘客快速找到時間。"},{"en":"Poor information design causes mistakes when users cannot see what matters most.","zh":"當使用者看不到最重要內容，不良資料設計會造成錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing clarity in labels, forms, and instructions.","zh":"討論標籤、表格和指示的清晰度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"track the journey of","meaning":"追蹤……的流程","examples":[{"en":"Thea Swayne tracked the journey of a medicine from the factory to patients’ homes.","zh":"Thea Swayne 追蹤一種藥物由工廠到病人家中的流程。"},{"en":"Track the journey of something means follow its movement through each stage.","zh":"track the journey of something 指跟隨某物在每個階段的移動。"},{"en":"A delivery company tracks the journey of a parcel from warehouse to doorstep.","zh":"速遞公司追蹤包裹由倉庫到家門的流程。"},{"en":"Tracking a journey reveals where errors, delays, or safety risks may appear.","zh":"追蹤流程能揭示錯誤、延誤或安全風險可能出現的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when studying a process step by step.","zh":"逐步研究一個過程時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"manufacturing plant","meaning":"生產廠房","examples":[{"en":"The journey of a medicine begins at a manufacturing plant.","zh":"藥物的流程始於生產廠房。"},{"en":"A manufacturing plant is a factory where products are made on a large scale.","zh":"manufacturing plant 指大規模製造產品的工廠。"},{"en":"A manufacturing plant may produce tablets, bottles, or packaging materials.","zh":"生產廠房可能製造藥片、瓶子或包裝材料。"},{"en":"Safety must begin at the manufacturing plant because later users depend on correct production.","zh":"安全必須從生產廠房開始，因為後來使用者依賴正確生產。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing where goods are made.","zh":"討論貨品在哪裏製造時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"distribution warehouses","meaning":"配送倉庫","examples":[{"en":"Medicines pass through distribution warehouses before reaching pharmacies.","zh":"藥物到達藥房前會經過配送倉庫。"},{"en":"Distribution warehouses are storage centres where goods are kept before being sent to shops or users.","zh":"distribution warehouses 指貨品送到商店或使用者前存放的倉儲中心。"},{"en":"A supermarket chain uses distribution warehouses to send food to different branches.","zh":"連鎖超市使用配送倉庫把食物送到不同分店。"},{"en":"Good warehouse systems prevent products from being lost, delayed, or mixed up.","zh":"良好倉庫系統可以防止產品遺失、延誤或混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing supply chains.","zh":"討論供應鏈時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hospital wards","meaning":"醫院病房","examples":[{"en":"Medicines are used in pharmacies, hospital wards and patients’ homes.","zh":"藥物在藥房、醫院病房和病人家中使用。"},{"en":"Hospital wards are areas in hospitals where patients stay and receive care.","zh":"hospital wards 指醫院中病人留院並接受護理的區域。"},{"en":"Nurses in hospital wards must read medicine labels quickly and accurately.","zh":"醫院病房中的護士必須快速而準確地閱讀藥物標籤。"},{"en":"Clear packaging matters in hospital wards because staff may work under pressure.","zh":"清晰包裝在醫院病房中很重要，因為員工可能在壓力下工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing care inside hospitals.","zh":"討論醫院內護理時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"patients’ homes","meaning":"病人家中","examples":[{"en":"Packaging should be safe enough for use in patients’ homes.","zh":"包裝應足夠安全，可在病人家中使用。"},{"en":"Patients’ homes are the places where patients live and manage their own medicines.","zh":"patients’ homes 指病人居住並自行管理藥物的地方。"},{"en":"In patients’ homes, medicines may be taken by tired parents, elderly people, or busy carers.","zh":"在病人家中，藥物可能由疲倦家長、長者或忙碌照顧者服用或處理。"},{"en":"Packaging must work at home because no pharmacist is standing beside the patient.","zh":"包裝必須能在家中有效，因為沒有藥劑師站在病人旁邊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing real-life medicine use outside hospitals.","zh":"討論醫院外真實用藥情況時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"highlight a multitude of","meaning":"突顯大量……","examples":[{"en":"The book highlights a multitude of design problems with current packaging.","zh":"這本書突顯現有包裝中的大量設計問題。"},{"en":"Highlight a multitude of means draw attention to a large number of things.","zh":"highlight a multitude of 指引起人們注意大量事情。"},{"en":"A school survey may highlight a multitude of problems with homework, lunch, and classroom space.","zh":"學校調查可能突顯功課、午餐和課室空間中的大量問題。"},{"en":"Highlighting many problems helps people see that change is needed across a system.","zh":"突顯許多問題幫助人們看見整個系統都需要改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a report points out many issues.","zh":"當報告指出許多議題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a multitude of","meaning":"大量；眾多","examples":[{"en":"There are a multitude of design problems in current medicine packaging.","zh":"現有藥物包裝中有大量設計問題。"},{"en":"A multitude of means a very large number of something.","zh":"a multitude of 指非常多的某事物。"},{"en":"A new teacher may face a multitude of small questions in the first week of school.","zh":"新老師在開學第一週可能面對大量小問題。"},{"en":"A multitude of minor problems can create one serious overall risk.","zh":"大量小問題可以形成一個嚴重整體風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when there are many examples, not just one or two.","zh":"當例子很多，而不只是一兩個時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"current packaging","meaning":"現有包裝","examples":[{"en":"Current packaging can create safety problems for patients and pharmacists.","zh":"現有包裝可能為病人和藥劑師造成安全問題。"},{"en":"Current packaging means the packaging that is being used now.","zh":"current packaging 指目前正在使用的包裝。"},{"en":"A company may review current packaging if customers complain that instructions are hard to read.","zh":"如果顧客投訴指示難讀，公司可能檢討現有包裝。"},{"en":"Current packaging may need redesign when it no longer fits real user needs.","zh":"當現有包裝不再符合真實使用者需要，它可能需要重新設計。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing existing product design.","zh":"討論既有產品設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"look-alikes and sound-alikes","meaning":"外觀相似及讀音相似的項目","examples":[{"en":"Look-alikes and sound-alikes can increase the risk of medicine errors.","zh":"外觀相似及讀音相似的項目會增加藥物錯誤風險。"},{"en":"Look-alikes and sound-alikes are items or names that look or sound very similar.","zh":"look-alikes and sound-alikes 指外觀或讀音非常相似的項目或名稱。"},{"en":"Two medicines with similar names can become sound-alikes in a noisy pharmacy.","zh":"兩種名稱相似的藥物在嘈雜藥房中可能變成讀音相似的項目。"},{"en":"Similar appearance or pronunciation can cause mistakes when people work quickly.","zh":"外觀或發音相似會在人們快速工作時造成錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when similarity creates safety risk.","zh":"當相似性造成安全風險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"small type sizes","meaning":"細小字體","examples":[{"en":"Small type sizes can make medicine labels difficult to read.","zh":"細小字體會令藥物標籤難以閱讀。"},{"en":"Small type sizes are very small printed letters or numbers.","zh":"small type sizes 指非常細小的印刷字母或數字。"},{"en":"Elderly patients may struggle with small type sizes on instruction leaflets.","zh":"年長病人可能難以閱讀指示單張上的細小字體。"},{"en":"If type is too small, users may miss dosage instructions or warnings.","zh":"如果字體太小，使用者可能錯過劑量指示或警告。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing readability.","zh":"討論易讀性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"glare on blister foils","meaning":"泡罩包裝鋁箔上的反光","examples":[{"en":"Glare on blister foils can make information harder to read.","zh":"泡罩包裝鋁箔上的反光會令資料更難閱讀。"},{"en":"Glare on blister foils is reflected light from shiny medicine foil that reduces visibility.","zh":"glare on blister foils 指有光從閃亮藥物鋁箔反射，降低可見度。"},{"en":"Under bright bathroom lighting, glare on blister foils may hide the tablet name.","zh":"在明亮浴室燈光下，泡罩包裝鋁箔上的反光可能遮住藥名。"},{"en":"Glare creates risk because users may turn the pack around or misread details.","zh":"反光造成風險，因為使用者可能要轉動包裝或誤讀細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing visual problems in medicine packaging.","zh":"討論藥物包裝中的視覺問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"blister foils","meaning":"泡罩包裝鋁箔","examples":[{"en":"Blister foils can create glare that reduces legibility.","zh":"泡罩包裝鋁箔可能產生反光，降低易讀性。"},{"en":"Blister foils are thin sheets used to seal tablets inside blister packs.","zh":"blister foils 指用來密封泡罩包裝內藥片的薄鋁箔。"},{"en":"A patient pushes a tablet through blister foil before taking it.","zh":"病人服藥前會把藥片從泡罩包裝鋁箔推出。"},{"en":"Shiny blister foils can protect medicine, but they may also make printed words hard to see.","zh":"閃亮鋁箔可以保護藥物，但也可能令印刷字難看見。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing tablet packaging.","zh":"討論藥片包裝時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"situations in which","meaning":"……的情況","examples":[{"en":"Designers should consider situations in which medicines are actually used.","zh":"設計師應考慮藥物實際使用的情況。"},{"en":"Situations in which means circumstances where something happens.","zh":"situations in which 指某事發生的情況或場合。"},{"en":"Teachers should consider situations in which students may need to use English outside class.","zh":"老師應考慮學生在課外可能需要使用英語的情況。"},{"en":"Design improves when creators understand the real situations in which users act.","zh":"當創作者理解使用者行動的真實情況，設計就會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when connecting actions to real contexts.","zh":"把行動與真實語境連接時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cough medicine","meaning":"咳藥水","examples":[{"en":"A parent may give cough medicine to a child in the middle of the night.","zh":"家長可能在半夜給孩子服用咳藥水。"},{"en":"Cough medicine is medicine used to relieve coughing or related throat symptoms.","zh":"cough medicine 指用來紓緩咳嗽或相關喉嚨症狀的藥物。"},{"en":"Parents should check the dose carefully before giving cough medicine to children.","zh":"家長給孩子服用咳藥水前，應仔細檢查劑量。"},{"en":"Poor labels on cough medicine can cause mistakes when a parent is tired.","zh":"當家長疲倦時，咳藥水上的差劣標籤可能造成錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing common household medicines.","zh":"討論常見家用藥物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the middle of the night","meaning":"在半夜","examples":[{"en":"A parent may need to read medicine packaging in the middle of the night.","zh":"家長可能需要在半夜閱讀藥物包裝。"},{"en":"In the middle of the night means very late at night, when people are usually tired or asleep.","zh":"in the middle of the night 指很晚的夜裏，通常人們疲倦或睡着時。"},{"en":"A sick child may wake a parent in the middle of the night.","zh":"生病孩子可能在半夜叫醒家長。"},{"en":"Instructions must be clear because people make more mistakes when tired at night.","zh":"指示必須清楚，因為人在夜晚疲倦時更容易犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing difficult late-night situations.","zh":"描述困難深夜情況時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"busy pharmacist","meaning":"忙碌的藥劑師","examples":[{"en":"A busy pharmacist may have to select one box from hundreds.","zh":"忙碌的藥劑師可能要從數以百計的盒子中選一盒。"},{"en":"A busy pharmacist is a pharmacist working under time pressure with many customers or prescriptions.","zh":"busy pharmacist 指在時間壓力下處理許多顧客或處方的藥劑師。"},{"en":"A busy pharmacist may answer questions, check prescriptions, and prepare medicines at the same time.","zh":"忙碌的藥劑師可能同時回答問題、核對處方和準備藥物。"},{"en":"Busy conditions increase risk because similar packages may be confused.","zh":"忙碌情況會增加風險，因為相似包裝可能被混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing pressure in pharmacies.","zh":"討論藥房壓力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"select one box from hundreds","meaning":"從數以百計的盒子中選一盒","examples":[{"en":"A busy pharmacist may select one box from hundreds of similar packages.","zh":"忙碌的藥劑師可能從數以百計的相似包裝中選一盒。"},{"en":"Select one box from hundreds means choose a single correct package from a very large number.","zh":"select one box from hundreds 指從非常大量物件中選出一個正確包裝。"},{"en":"A librarian may select one book from hundreds when a student asks for a specific title.","zh":"當學生要求某本特定書，圖書館員可能從數百本書中選一本。"},{"en":"If many items look similar, selecting the right one becomes harder.","zh":"如果許多物品看起來相似，選對一件會更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when choice is difficult because there are many options.","zh":"當選擇因選項太多而困難時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be designed for","meaning":"為……而設計","examples":[{"en":"Medicine packaging should be designed for real-life moments of use.","zh":"藥物包裝應為真實生活中的使用時刻而設計。"},{"en":"Be designed for means be made with a particular user, purpose, or situation in mind.","zh":"be designed for 指以特定使用者、目的或情況為考慮而製作。"},{"en":"Children’s scissors are designed for small hands and safer cutting.","zh":"兒童剪刀是為小手和較安全剪裁而設計的。"},{"en":"Good products work better when they are designed for real users, not ideal conditions.","zh":"當產品為真實使用者而非理想情況設計，它們會更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the intended purpose of a design.","zh":"解釋設計的預期目的時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"moments such as these","meaning":"這類時刻","examples":[{"en":"Packaging should be designed for moments such as these.","zh":"包裝應為這類時刻而設計。"},{"en":"Moments such as these means situations like the examples just mentioned.","zh":"moments such as these 指像剛提到的例子那樣的情況。"},{"en":"Schools need clear emergency plans for moments such as these, when students must leave quickly.","zh":"學校需要清晰緊急計劃，以應付這類學生必須快速離開的時刻。"},{"en":"Real examples help designers imagine moments when users are tired, rushed, or confused.","zh":"真實例子幫助設計師想像使用者疲倦、匆忙或混亂的時刻。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when referring back to specific situations.","zh":"回指特定情況時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be aware of","meaning":"意識到","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers may not be aware of the complex situations in which medicines are used.","zh":"製造商可能沒有意識到藥物使用時的複雜情況。"},{"en":"Be aware of means know about or notice something.","zh":"be aware of 指知道或注意到某事。"},{"en":"Students should be aware of the deadline before starting a project.","zh":"學生在開始專題前應意識到截止日期。"},{"en":"If designers are not aware of user difficulties, they may create unsafe products.","zh":"如果設計師沒有意識到使用者困難，他們可能創造不安全產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when knowledge or attention affects decisions.","zh":"當知識或注意力影響決定時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"complex situations","meaning":"複雜情況","examples":[{"en":"Medicines are often used in complex situations.","zh":"藥物常在複雜情況中使用。"},{"en":"Complex situations are circumstances with many factors, pressures, or possible problems.","zh":"complex situations 指包含許多因素、壓力或可能問題的情況。"},{"en":"A teacher faces complex situations when students have different levels, needs, and emotions.","zh":"當學生有不同程度、需要和情緒，老師就面對複雜情況。"},{"en":"In complex situations, simple instructions must be especially clear.","zh":"在複雜情況中，簡單指示尤其必須清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a situation is not straightforward.","zh":"當情況不直接簡單時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"what is supposed to happen","meaning":"理應發生的事","examples":[{"en":"Designers are interested not only in what is supposed to happen in hospitals.","zh":"設計師感興趣的不只是醫院中理應發生的事。"},{"en":"What is supposed to happen means what should happen according to the official plan or rules.","zh":"what is supposed to happen 指根據正式計劃或規則應該發生的事。"},{"en":"In school, what is supposed to happen is that students submit homework before the deadline.","zh":"在學校中，理應發生的事是學生在截止日期前交功課。"},{"en":"Real life may differ from what is supposed to happen when people are tired or rushed.","zh":"當人們疲倦或匆忙，現實可能不同於理應發生的事。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing theory with reality.","zh":"比較理論與現實時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the real world","meaning":"在現實世界中","examples":[{"en":"Designers need to understand what happens in the real world.","zh":"設計師需要理解現實世界中發生的事。"},{"en":"In the real world means in actual daily life, not in theory or ideal conditions.","zh":"in the real world 指在實際日常生活中，而非理論或理想情況中。"},{"en":"In the real world, students may forget grammar rules when speaking under pressure.","zh":"在現實世界中，學生在壓力下說話時可能忘記文法規則。"},{"en":"Designs improve when they match real-world behaviour rather than perfect behaviour.","zh":"當設計配合真實行為而非完美行為，它們會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting practical reality with planned assumptions.","zh":"對比實際現實與計劃假設時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"incidents in which","meaning":"……的事故","examples":[{"en":"There have been incidents in which vincristine was injected incorrectly.","zh":"曾有事故中長春新鹼被錯誤注射。"},{"en":"Incidents in which means events or cases where a particular thing happened.","zh":"incidents in which 指某特定事情發生的事件或個案。"},{"en":"Schools record incidents in which students are injured during sports activities.","zh":"學校會記錄學生在體育活動中受傷的事故。"},{"en":"Studying incidents helps people understand what went wrong and how to prevent it.","zh":"研究事故幫助人理解出了甚麼錯，以及如何預防。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when referring to specific accident cases.","zh":"指涉特定意外個案時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"vincristine","meaning":"長春新鹼","examples":[{"en":"Vincristine must be administered safely to avoid serious harm.","zh":"長春新鹼必須安全給藥，以避免嚴重傷害。"},{"en":"Vincristine is a powerful medicine used in cancer treatment that must be handled with great care.","zh":"vincristine 是用於癌症治療的強效藥物，必須非常小心處理。"},{"en":"A hospital team must check the route carefully before giving vincristine.","zh":"醫院團隊給予長春新鹼前，必須仔細核對給藥途徑。"},{"en":"A mistake involving vincristine can be extremely dangerous because the medicine is powerful.","zh":"涉及長春新鹼的錯誤可能極其危險，因為該藥物很強效。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing medicine errors and high-risk drugs.","zh":"討論藥物錯誤和高風險藥物時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be injected intrathecally","meaning":"被鞘內注射","examples":[{"en":"Vincristine has sometimes been injected intrathecally by mistake.","zh":"長春新鹼有時曾被錯誤地鞘內注射。"},{"en":"Be injected intrathecally means be injected into the space around the spinal cord.","zh":"be injected intrathecally 指被注射入脊髓周圍的空間。"},{"en":"Only certain medicines are meant to be injected intrathecally, so labels must be very clear.","zh":"只有某些藥物適合鞘內注射，所以標籤必須非常清楚。"},{"en":"If the wrong medicine is injected intrathecally, the result can be catastrophic.","zh":"如果錯誤藥物被鞘內注射，結果可能是災難性的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing medical route errors.","zh":"討論醫療給藥途徑錯誤時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rather than intravenously","meaning":"而不是靜脈注射","examples":[{"en":"Vincristine was injected intrathecally rather than intravenously.","zh":"長春新鹼被鞘內注射，而不是靜脈注射。"},{"en":"Rather than intravenously means instead of being injected into a vein.","zh":"rather than intravenously 指而不是注射入靜脈。"},{"en":"Some medicines must be taken by mouth rather than intravenously because the route affects safety.","zh":"有些藥物必須口服，而不是靜脈注射，因為給藥途徑影響安全。"},{"en":"Wrong route errors happen when people confuse how a medicine should enter the body.","zh":"當人們混淆藥物應如何進入身體，就會發生錯誤途徑事故。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting two medical routes.","zh":"對比兩種醫療給藥途徑時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"classic examples of","meaning":"……的典型例子","examples":[{"en":"These incidents are classic examples of poor design contributing to harm.","zh":"這些事故是不良設計導致傷害的典型例子。"},{"en":"Classic examples of something are clear, typical cases that show the problem well.","zh":"classic examples of something 指能清楚、典型地顯示問題的個案。"},{"en":"A slippery floor without a warning sign is a classic example of poor safety management.","zh":"沒有警告標誌的濕滑地板，是安全管理不善的典型例子。"},{"en":"Classic examples help students understand a general problem through a concrete case.","zh":"典型例子幫助學生透過具體個案理解一般問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an example strongly illustrates a point.","zh":"當例子強烈說明某點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"poor design","meaning":"不良設計","examples":[{"en":"Poor design can contribute to harm.","zh":"不良設計可能造成傷害。"},{"en":"Poor design means a product, system, or layout is badly planned and difficult or unsafe to use.","zh":"poor design 指產品、系統或版面規劃差劣，使用起來困難或不安全。"},{"en":"A door handle that is hard to grip is poor design for elderly users.","zh":"難以握住的門柄對長者使用者來說是不良設計。"},{"en":"Poor design causes problems when real users cannot understand or operate something safely.","zh":"當真實使用者不能安全理解或操作某物，不良設計就會造成問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when design creates practical danger or inconvenience.","zh":"當設計造成實際危險或不便時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"contribute to harm","meaning":"造成傷害；導致傷害","examples":[{"en":"Poor typography can contribute to harm.","zh":"欠佳的字體排印可能導致傷害。"},{"en":"Contribute to harm means help cause injury, danger, or damage, even if it is not the only cause.","zh":"contribute to harm 指有份造成傷害、危險或損害，即使它不是唯一原因。"},{"en":"A confusing road sign can contribute to harm if drivers choose the wrong lane.","zh":"如果司機選錯行車線，混亂路牌可能造成傷害。"},{"en":"Small design mistakes can contribute to harm when people are under pressure.","zh":"當人們在壓力下，小設計錯誤也可能導致傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one factor plays a part in causing danger.","zh":"當某因素有份造成危險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"investigations following","meaning":"隨後對……的調查","examples":[{"en":"Investigations following these tragedies blamed poor typography in part.","zh":"隨後對這些悲劇的調查把部分責任歸咎於欠佳字體排印。"},{"en":"Investigations following an event are official or careful inquiries made after it happens.","zh":"investigations following an event 指事件發生後進行的正式或仔細調查。"},{"en":"Investigations following a school bus accident may examine driver training and road conditions.","zh":"隨後對校巴意外的調查可能檢視司機培訓和道路情況。"},{"en":"Post-incident investigations help identify causes and prevent similar events.","zh":"事後調查幫助找出原因並預防類似事件。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when studying what happened after a serious incident.","zh":"研究嚴重事故後發生甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"attribute some blame to","meaning":"將部分責任歸咎於……","examples":[{"en":"Investigations attributed some blame to poor typography.","zh":"調查將部分責任歸咎於欠佳字體排印。"},{"en":"Attribute some blame to means say that someone or something was partly responsible for a problem.","zh":"attribute some blame to 指認為某人或某事對問題負有部分責任。"},{"en":"A report may attribute some blame to poor training after a workplace accident.","zh":"工作場所意外後，報告可能將部分責任歸咎於培訓不足。"},{"en":"Partial blame shows that several factors may have caused the same incident.","zh":"部分責任顯示同一事故可能由多個因素造成。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when responsibility is shared.","zh":"當責任是共同承擔時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"poor typography","meaning":"欠佳的字體排印","examples":[{"en":"Poor typography can make medicine information unsafe.","zh":"欠佳的字體排印會令藥物資料不安全。"},{"en":"Poor typography means bad choices in font, spacing, size, layout, or printed style.","zh":"poor typography 指字體、間距、大小、版面或印刷風格選擇不佳。"},{"en":"A worksheet with tiny letters and crowded lines has poor typography.","zh":"字很細且行距擁擠的工作紙有欠佳的字體排印。"},{"en":"Poor typography makes reading harder and increases the chance of misunderstanding.","zh":"欠佳字體排印令閱讀更困難，並增加誤解機會。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when printed design affects clarity.","zh":"當印刷設計影響清晰度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Safety and compliance","meaning":"安全與依從性","examples":[{"en":"Safety and compliance can both be improved through better design.","zh":"安全與依從性都可以透過更好設計改善。"},{"en":"Safety and compliance means protecting users and helping them follow instructions correctly.","zh":"safety and compliance 指保護使用者，並幫助他們正確遵從指示。"},{"en":"A medicine app can support safety and compliance by reminding patients when to take tablets.","zh":"藥物應用程式可以透過提醒病人何時服藥來支援安全與依從性。"},{"en":"Clear packaging improves compliance because people understand what they must do.","zh":"清晰包裝改善依從性，因為人們明白自己必須做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when design helps people use products safely and correctly.","zh":"當設計幫助人們安全且正確使用產品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"child protection","meaning":"兒童保護","examples":[{"en":"Child protection is another area where designers can improve safety.","zh":"兒童保護是設計師可以改善安全的另一個範疇。"},{"en":"Child protection means actions or designs that keep children safe from harm.","zh":"child protection 指保護兒童免受傷害的行動或設計。"},{"en":"Child protection in a home may include locked cupboards and covered electrical sockets.","zh":"家中的兒童保護可能包括上鎖櫃和有保護蓋的插座。"},{"en":"Medicine packaging supports child protection when it is difficult for young children to open.","zh":"當藥物包裝令幼童難以打開，它就支援兒童保護。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when children’s safety is the main concern.","zh":"當兒童安全是主要關注時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"give designers opportunities to","meaning":"給設計師機會去……","examples":[{"en":"Child protection gives designers opportunities to improve safety.","zh":"兒童保護給設計師機會去改善安全。"},{"en":"Give designers opportunities to means create chances for designers to do something useful.","zh":"give designers opportunities to 指創造機會讓設計師做有用的事。"},{"en":"A new school building gives architects opportunities to improve lighting and movement.","zh":"新校舍給建築師機會去改善照明和人流動線。"},{"en":"Problems give designers opportunities when they reveal where better solutions are needed.","zh":"當問題揭示哪裏需要更好解決方案，它們就給設計師機會。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when challenges become chances for improvement.","zh":"當挑戰變成改善機會時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"improve safety","meaning":"改善安全","examples":[{"en":"Better packaging can improve safety for children and older people.","zh":"更好的包裝可以改善兒童和長者的安全。"},{"en":"Improve safety means make something less dangerous and reduce the chance of harm.","zh":"improve safety 指令某事物較不危險，並減少傷害機會。"},{"en":"Adding handrails can improve safety on a staircase.","zh":"加裝扶手可以改善樓梯安全。"},{"en":"Safety improves when design prevents mistakes before they happen.","zh":"當設計在錯誤發生前預防它們，安全就會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing practical ways to reduce risk.","zh":"討論減低風險的實際方法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Child Accident Prevention Trust","meaning":"兒童意外預防信託","examples":[{"en":"The Child Accident Prevention Trust has reported on suspected child poisoning.","zh":"兒童意外預防信託曾就兒童疑似中毒作出報告。"},{"en":"The Child Accident Prevention Trust is an organisation concerned with preventing accidents involving children.","zh":"Child Accident Prevention Trust 是關注預防兒童意外的機構。"},{"en":"Such an organisation may publish advice for parents on safe storage of medicines.","zh":"這類機構可能發布給家長的安全存放藥物建議。"},{"en":"Accident-prevention groups collect data to show where children face avoidable risks.","zh":"意外預防組織收集數據，以顯示兒童在哪裏面對可避免風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when referring to a child-safety organisation.","zh":"提及兒童安全機構時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"seven out of ten","meaning":"十個之中有七個","examples":[{"en":"Seven out of ten children admitted with suspected poisoning had swallowed medicines.","zh":"十個因疑似中毒入院的兒童中，有七個曾吞下藥物。"},{"en":"Seven out of ten means seven people or things in every group of ten.","zh":"seven out of ten 指每十個人或物中有七個。"},{"en":"If seven out of ten students pass a test, most students have succeeded.","zh":"如果十個學生中有七個通過測驗，即大多數學生成功。"},{"en":"This expression makes statistics easier to understand than percentages alone.","zh":"這種表達比單純百分比更容易理解統計數字。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing that a problem affects the majority.","zh":"顯示問題影響大多數時，它很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be admitted to hospital","meaning":"入院","examples":[{"en":"Some children are admitted to hospital with suspected poisoning.","zh":"有些兒童因疑似中毒入院。"},{"en":"Be admitted to hospital means be officially accepted into hospital for medical care.","zh":"be admitted to hospital 指正式被醫院接收以接受醫療護理。"},{"en":"An elderly person may be admitted to hospital after a serious fall.","zh":"長者嚴重跌倒後可能入院。"},{"en":"Hospital admission usually shows that a condition may need close observation or treatment.","zh":"入院通常顯示情況可能需要密切觀察或治療。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing serious health situations.","zh":"討論嚴重健康情況時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"suspected poisoning","meaning":"懷疑中毒","examples":[{"en":"Children may be admitted to hospital with suspected poisoning.","zh":"兒童可能因懷疑中毒入院。"},{"en":"Suspected poisoning means doctors think someone may have swallowed or absorbed a harmful substance.","zh":"suspected poisoning 指醫生認為某人可能吞下或吸收了有害物質。"},{"en":"A child with suspected poisoning may need urgent checks after drinking unknown liquid.","zh":"孩子喝下不明液體後，如懷疑中毒，可能需要緊急檢查。"},{"en":"Quick action matters because poisoning can become dangerous before symptoms are clear.","zh":"快速行動很重要，因為中毒可能在症狀清楚前變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when harm is possible but not yet confirmed.","zh":"當傷害可能存在但尚未確認時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"swallow medicines","meaning":"吞下藥物","examples":[{"en":"Many children with suspected poisoning have swallowed medicines.","zh":"許多懷疑中毒的兒童曾吞下藥物。"},{"en":"Swallow medicines means take medicines into the body through the mouth.","zh":"swallow medicines 指透過口腔把藥物吞進身體。"},{"en":"A child may swallow medicines accidentally if tablets look like sweets.","zh":"如果藥片看起來像糖果，孩子可能意外吞下藥物。"},{"en":"Safe storage prevents children from swallowing medicines that are not meant for them.","zh":"安全存放可以防止兒童吞下不應給他們服用的藥物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing medicine intake and poisoning risk.","zh":"討論服藥和中毒風險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"child-resistant closures","meaning":"兒童安全瓶蓋","examples":[{"en":"Child-resistant closures have reduced the number of incidents.","zh":"兒童安全瓶蓋已減少事故數目。"},{"en":"Child-resistant closures are caps or lids designed to be difficult for young children to open.","zh":"child-resistant closures 指設計成讓幼童難以打開的瓶蓋或蓋子。"},{"en":"A medicine bottle may use a child-resistant closure that must be pushed and turned.","zh":"藥瓶可能使用需要按下再扭開的兒童安全瓶蓋。"},{"en":"These closures reduce accidents, but adults must still store medicines safely.","zh":"這些瓶蓋能減少意外，但成年人仍必須安全存放藥物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing safer medicine containers.","zh":"討論較安全藥物容器時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reduce the number of incidents","meaning":"減少事故數目","examples":[{"en":"Child-resistant closures have reduced the number of incidents.","zh":"兒童安全瓶蓋已減少事故數目。"},{"en":"Reduce the number of incidents means make accidents or problem cases happen less often.","zh":"reduce the number of incidents 指令意外或問題個案較少發生。"},{"en":"Speed bumps can reduce the number of incidents near a school gate.","zh":"減速帶可以減少校門附近的事故數目。"},{"en":"Better design reduces incidents by stopping mistakes before people make them.","zh":"更好設計透過在人們犯錯前阻止錯誤來減少事故。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing prevention.","zh":"討論預防時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not fully child-proof","meaning":"並非完全防兒童開啟","examples":[{"en":"Child-resistant closures are not fully child-proof.","zh":"兒童安全瓶蓋並非完全防兒童開啟。"},{"en":"Not fully child-proof means not completely impossible for a child to open or use dangerously.","zh":"not fully child-proof 指並非完全不可能被兒童打開或危險使用。"},{"en":"A safety lock may be helpful but not fully child-proof if an older child learns how it works.","zh":"如果年紀較大的孩子學會如何操作，安全鎖可能有幫助但並非完全防兒童。"},{"en":"Calling something child-resistant is more realistic than saying it removes all risk.","zh":"說某物防兒童開啟，比說它消除所有風險更現實。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a safety design reduces danger but does not eliminate it.","zh":"當安全設計減低危險但不能消除危險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the definition of","meaning":"……的定義","examples":[{"en":"The definition of a child-resistant closure is based on how many children can open it.","zh":"兒童安全瓶蓋的定義以有多少兒童能打開它為基礎。"},{"en":"The definition of something is the explanation of what it means.","zh":"definition of something 指對某事物意思的解釋。"},{"en":"The definition of plagiarism helps students understand what counts as copying.","zh":"抄襲的定義幫助學生理解甚麼算是複製。"},{"en":"Clear definitions matter because people need to know exactly what a term includes.","zh":"清晰定義很重要，因為人們需要確切知道術語包括甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining technical terms.","zh":"解釋技術術語時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not more than","meaning":"不超過","examples":[{"en":"Not more than 15 per cent of young children should be able to open the closure.","zh":"不超過百分之十五的幼童應能打開該瓶蓋。"},{"en":"Not more than means no greater than a stated number or amount.","zh":"not more than 指不大於某個指定數字或數量。"},{"en":"In the quiz, students should write not more than three words for each answer.","zh":"在測驗中，學生每個答案應寫不超過三個詞。"},{"en":"A limit helps make testing fair and easy to judge.","zh":"限制有助令測試公平並容易判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving a maximum.","zh":"給出最高上限時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"aged between…and…","meaning":"年齡介乎……至……","examples":[{"en":"The test involves children aged between 42 and 51 months.","zh":"這項測試涉及年齡介乎42至51個月的兒童。"},{"en":"Aged between…and… means having an age within two stated limits.","zh":"aged between…and… 指年齡在兩個指定界限之間。"},{"en":"A summer camp may accept children aged between 8 and 12.","zh":"暑期營可能接受年齡介乎8至12歲的兒童。"},{"en":"Age limits are used when ability, safety, or development level matters.","zh":"當能力、安全或發展程度重要時，就會使用年齡限制。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing age groups.","zh":"描述年齡群組時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"within five minutes","meaning":"在五分鐘內","examples":[{"en":"Not more than 15 per cent of children should be able to open it within five minutes.","zh":"不超過百分之十五的兒童應能在五分鐘內打開它。"},{"en":"Within five minutes means before five minutes have passed.","zh":"within five minutes 指在五分鐘過去之前。"},{"en":"Students should arrive at the meeting place within five minutes after the bell.","zh":"學生應在鐘聲響後五分鐘內到達集合地點。"},{"en":"A time limit shows how quickly a task can or cannot be done.","zh":"時間限制顯示任務能否被快速完成，或有多困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when measuring speed or difficulty.","zh":"量度速度或難度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"there is scope for improving","meaning":"仍有改善空間","examples":[{"en":"There is scope for improving child-resistant packaging.","zh":"兒童安全包裝仍有改善空間。"},{"en":"There is scope for improving means there is still room or possibility to make something better.","zh":"there is scope for improving 指仍有空間或可能性令某事物變得更好。"},{"en":"There is scope for improving school lunches if students keep leaving food uneaten.","zh":"如果學生一直剩飯，學校午餐仍有改善空間。"},{"en":"Noticing room for improvement helps organisations avoid becoming satisfied too soon.","zh":"注意到改善空間幫助機構避免太早滿足於現狀。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a system works partly but could be better.","zh":"當系統部分有效但仍可更好時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"currently available","meaning":"目前可用的","examples":[{"en":"There is scope for improving what is currently available.","zh":"目前可用的東西仍有改善空間。"},{"en":"Currently available means able to be used or bought now.","zh":"currently available 指現在可以使用或購買的。"},{"en":"A teacher may choose from the textbooks currently available in the school library.","zh":"老師可能從學校圖書館目前可用的教科書中選擇。"},{"en":"Existing products may be useful but still need redesign when users struggle.","zh":"既有產品可能有用，但當使用者遇到困難時仍需重新設計。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing present options.","zh":"討論現有選項時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"freelance product designer","meaning":"自由身產品設計師","examples":[{"en":"Richard Mawle is a freelance product designer.","zh":"Richard Mawle 是自由身產品設計師。"},{"en":"A freelance product designer is an independent designer hired for projects rather than employed full-time by one company.","zh":"freelance product designer 指以項目形式受聘，而非全職受僱於一間公司的獨立產品設計師。"},{"en":"A start-up may hire a freelance product designer to improve a new water bottle.","zh":"初創公司可能聘請自由身產品設計師改善新水樽。"},{"en":"Freelancers can bring outside experience from different clients and industries.","zh":"自由工作者能帶來來自不同客戶和行業的外部經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing independent design professionals.","zh":"討論獨立設計專業人士時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be based on strength","meaning":"以力度為基礎","examples":[{"en":"Many child-resistant packs are based on strength.","zh":"許多兒童安全包裝以力度為基礎。"},{"en":"Be based on strength means depend on physical force to make something work or prevent access.","zh":"be based on strength 指依靠體力來運作或阻止接觸。"},{"en":"A heavy door lock may be based on strength if users must push hard to open it.","zh":"如果使用者必須用力推才可打開，厚重門鎖可能是以力度為基礎。"},{"en":"Strength-based designs can exclude people who are weak, elderly, or disabled.","zh":"以力度為基礎的設計可能排除體弱、年長或殘疾人士。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when physical force is the main design principle.","zh":"當體力是主要設計原則時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not necessarily","meaning":"不一定","examples":[{"en":"Child-resistant packs do not necessarily prevent children from gaining access.","zh":"兒童安全包裝不一定能防止兒童取得藥物。"},{"en":"Not necessarily means not always or not in every case.","zh":"not necessarily 指不總是，或不是在每種情況都如此。"},{"en":"A high score does not necessarily mean a student understands the topic deeply.","zh":"高分不一定代表學生深入理解該主題。"},{"en":"This phrase helps avoid overclaiming when there are exceptions.","zh":"這個短語在有例外時幫助避免過度聲稱。"},{"en":"It is useful when something may be true sometimes but not always.","zh":"當某事有時可能為真但不總是如此時，它很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"prevent someone from doing something","meaning":"阻止某人做某事","examples":[{"en":"Some closures may prevent people with disabilities from opening them.","zh":"有些瓶蓋可能阻止殘疾人士打開它們。"},{"en":"Prevent someone from doing something means stop someone from being able to do it.","zh":"prevent someone from doing something 指阻止某人能夠做某事。"},{"en":"Heavy rain may prevent students from playing football outside.","zh":"大雨可能阻止學生在戶外踢足球。"},{"en":"A design should prevent danger without preventing legitimate users from using the product.","zh":"設計應防止危險，而不是阻止合法使用者使用產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something blocks an action.","zh":"當某事阻擋某行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"gain access","meaning":"取得；進入","examples":[{"en":"A child may still gain access to medicines in some child-resistant packs.","zh":"在某些兒童安全包裝中，兒童仍可能取得藥物。"},{"en":"Gain access means get into or reach something that may be restricted.","zh":"gain access 指進入或接觸到可能受限制的事物。"},{"en":"Students need a password to gain access to the online learning platform.","zh":"學生需要密碼才能進入網上學習平台。"},{"en":"If children gain access to medicines, accidental poisoning can happen.","zh":"如果兒童取得藥物，可能會發生意外中毒。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing entry, use, or reach.","zh":"討論進入、使用或接觸時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"people with disabilities","meaning":"殘疾人士","examples":[{"en":"Some child-resistant packs are difficult for people with disabilities to open.","zh":"有些兒童安全包裝對殘疾人士來說很難打開。"},{"en":"People with disabilities are people who have physical, sensory, mental, or other conditions that affect daily activities.","zh":"people with disabilities 指有身體、感官、精神或其他影響日常活動狀況的人。"},{"en":"A person with weak hand movement may struggle to open a tight medicine cap.","zh":"手部活動能力弱的人可能難以打開緊密藥瓶蓋。"},{"en":"Good design should include people with disabilities rather than make products harder for them.","zh":"良好設計應包括殘疾人士，而不是令產品對他們更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing accessibility and inclusion.","zh":"討論無障礙和共融時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"legal requirements","meaning":"法律要求","examples":[{"en":"The legal requirements exist for a good reason.","zh":"法律要求存在是有充分理由的。"},{"en":"Legal requirements are rules that the law says people or companies must follow.","zh":"legal requirements 指法律規定人或公司必須遵守的規則。"},{"en":"Food labels have legal requirements so customers know ingredients and allergy risks.","zh":"食品標籤有法律要求，讓顧客知道成分和過敏風險。"},{"en":"Legal requirements can protect the public, but they may still need practical testing.","zh":"法律要求可以保護公眾，但仍可能需要實際測試。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when rules are set by law.","zh":"當規則由法律訂定時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"for a good reason","meaning":"有充分理由","examples":[{"en":"The legal requirements are there for a good reason.","zh":"法律要求存在是有充分理由的。"},{"en":"For a good reason means because there is a sensible or important purpose behind it.","zh":"for a good reason 指背後有合理或重要目的。"},{"en":"Students must wear goggles in the laboratory for a good reason: chemicals can hurt their eyes.","zh":"學生必須在實驗室戴護目鏡是有充分理由的：化學品可能傷害眼睛。"},{"en":"Rules are easier to accept when people understand the reason behind them.","zh":"當人們理解規則背後原因，規則較容易被接受。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why a rule is justified.","zh":"解釋規則為何合理時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not good enough in terms of","meaning":"就……而言未夠好","examples":[{"en":"Current designs are not good enough in terms of users.","zh":"現有設計就使用者而言未夠好。"},{"en":"Not good enough in terms of means inadequate when judged by a particular standard or group.","zh":"not good enough in terms of 指按某標準或群體判斷時不足夠。"},{"en":"A classroom may be beautiful but not good enough in terms of wheelchair access.","zh":"課室可能很漂亮，但就輪椅通道而言未夠好。"},{"en":"A product fails users when it meets legal rules but not real human needs.","zh":"當產品符合安全規則但不符合真實人類需要，它就未能服務使用者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the area where something is weak.","zh":"解釋某事物在哪方面不足時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"older people","meaning":"長者","examples":[{"en":"Older people may struggle with child-resistant closures.","zh":"長者可能難以使用兒童安全瓶蓋。"},{"en":"Older people are elderly adults, often with changing strength, eyesight, or movement.","zh":"older people 指年長成年人，常有力度、視力或活動能力變化。"},{"en":"Older people may need larger print on medicine labels.","zh":"長者可能需要藥物標籤上有較大字體。"},{"en":"Design that ignores older people can make everyday health tasks difficult.","zh":"忽視長者的設計會令日常健康任務變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing age-friendly design.","zh":"討論長者友善設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"arthritis","meaning":"關節炎","examples":[{"en":"People with arthritis may find some closures difficult to open.","zh":"關節炎患者可能覺得有些瓶蓋難以打開。"},{"en":"Arthritis is a condition that causes pain, swelling, or stiffness in the joints.","zh":"arthritis 指令關節疼痛、腫脹或僵硬的疾病。"},{"en":"Someone with arthritis in the hands may struggle to grip a small bottle cap.","zh":"手部有關節炎的人可能難以握住細小瓶蓋。"},{"en":"Arthritis affects packaging design because twisting and pressing can be painful.","zh":"關節炎影響包裝設計，因為扭動和按壓可能令人疼痛。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing health conditions that affect hand use.","zh":"討論影響手部使用的健康狀況時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the same level of strength as","meaning":"與……有相同力度","examples":[{"en":"Older people may have the same level of strength as a child.","zh":"長者可能與兒童有相同力度。"},{"en":"The same level of strength as means equal physical power compared with another person or group.","zh":"the same level of strength as 指與另一人或群體相比有相同體力。"},{"en":"After an illness, an adult may have the same level of strength as a much younger person.","zh":"病後，成年人可能與年幼許多的人有相同力度。"},{"en":"If packaging assumes adult strength, it may fail users who are weaker.","zh":"如果包裝假設使用者有成人力度，它可能不適合較弱使用者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing physical ability.","zh":"比較體能時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rely on cognitive skills","meaning":"依賴認知能力","examples":[{"en":"Better designs could rely on cognitive skills instead of strength.","zh":"更好的設計可以依賴認知能力，而不是力度。"},{"en":"Rely on cognitive skills means depend on thinking, understanding, memory, or problem-solving rather than physical force.","zh":"rely on cognitive skills 指依靠思考、理解、記憶或解難，而不是體力。"},{"en":"A puzzle-style lock may rely on cognitive skills more than hand strength.","zh":"拼圖式鎖可能比起手部力度更依賴認知能力。"},{"en":"Cognitive designs can keep children out while helping weaker adults open containers.","zh":"認知型設計可以阻止兒童開啟，同時幫助較弱成年人打開容器。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when mental ability is used as a design feature.","zh":"當心理能力被用作設計特徵時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cognitive skills","meaning":"認知能力","examples":[{"en":"Cognitive skills may help make child-resistant packaging safer.","zh":"認知能力可能有助令兒童安全包裝更安全。"},{"en":"Cognitive skills are mental abilities such as understanding instructions, remembering steps, and solving problems.","zh":"cognitive skills 指理解指示、記住步驟和解決問題等心智能力。"},{"en":"Reading a map uses cognitive skills because the user must understand symbols and directions.","zh":"閱讀地圖需要認知能力，因為使用者必須理解符號和方向。"},{"en":"Designs based on cognitive skills can be safer if children lack the required understanding.","zh":"如果兒童缺乏所需理解，以認知能力為基礎的設計可以更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when thinking ability matters more than physical strength.","zh":"當思考能力比體力更重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"three-step process","meaning":"三步程序","examples":[{"en":"The opening of a container could be made a three-step process.","zh":"打開容器可被設計成三步程序。"},{"en":"A three-step process is a method that requires three separate actions to complete.","zh":"three-step process 指需要三個分開動作才能完成的方法。"},{"en":"A safe medicine cap may require users to press, turn, and lift as a three-step process.","zh":"安全藥瓶蓋可能要求使用者按、扭、提，成為三步程序。"},{"en":"More steps can prevent accidental opening if children cannot understand the sequence.","zh":"如果兒童不能理解次序，更多步驟可以防止意外打開。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining a simple ordered procedure.","zh":"解釋簡單有序程序時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"physical size of hands","meaning":"手掌的實際大小","examples":[{"en":"Some designs could be based on the physical size of hands.","zh":"有些設計可以以手掌的實際大小為基礎。"},{"en":"Physical size of hands means the actual measurement or shape of a person’s hands.","zh":"physical size of hands 指一個人雙手的實際尺寸或形狀。"},{"en":"Children’s hands are usually smaller, so a cap can be designed around hand size.","zh":"兒童的手通常較小，因此瓶蓋可圍繞手掌大小設計。"},{"en":"Using hand size may help adults open containers while keeping small children out.","zh":"使用手掌大小可能幫助成年人打開容器，同時防止幼童打開。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when body size affects product design.","zh":"當身體大小影響產品設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"improve compliance through design","meaning":"透過設計提升用藥依從性","examples":[{"en":"Richard Mawle worked on a project to improve compliance through design.","zh":"Richard Mawle 參與一個透過設計提升用藥依從性的項目。"},{"en":"Improve compliance through design means help people follow instructions better by changing the product or information layout.","zh":"improve compliance through design 指透過改變產品或資訊版面，幫助人們更好遵從指示。"},{"en":"A pill box can improve compliance through design by showing morning and evening doses clearly.","zh":"藥盒可以透過清楚顯示早晚劑量來透過設計提升依從性。"},{"en":"When design makes the correct action easier, people are more likely to follow treatment properly.","zh":"當設計令正確行動更容易，人們就更可能正確跟隨治療。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when design supports correct behaviour.","zh":"當設計支援正確行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"apply one’s skills to","meaning":"將某人的技能應用於……","examples":[{"en":"He applied his skills to packaging and patient information leaflets.","zh":"他將自己的技能應用於包裝和病人資料單張。"},{"en":"Apply one’s skills to something means use one’s abilities in a particular task or field.","zh":"apply one’s skills to something 指把某人的能力用於特定任務或領域。"},{"en":"A graphic designer may apply her skills to school posters and safety signs.","zh":"平面設計師可能把技能應用於學校海報和安全標誌。"},{"en":"Skills become valuable when they are used to solve real problems.","zh":"當技能被用來解決真實問題，它就變得有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when ability is transferred into practical work.","zh":"當能力轉化成實際工作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"commenting on","meaning":"評論……時","examples":[{"en":"Commenting on the information presented, he criticised the order of information.","zh":"評論所呈現的資料時，他批評資料次序。"},{"en":"Commenting on something means giving an opinion or observation about it.","zh":"commenting on something 指對某事發表意見或觀察。"},{"en":"Commenting on a student’s essay, the teacher praised the ideas but corrected the grammar.","zh":"評論學生文章時，老師稱讚想法但糾正文法。"},{"en":"Comments can reveal problems that the original writer did not notice.","zh":"評論可以揭示原作者未注意到的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone responds to a text, design, or situation.","zh":"當某人回應文本、設計或情況時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"information presented","meaning":"所呈現的資料","examples":[{"en":"The information presented in leaflets may not be in the most useful order.","zh":"單張中所呈現的資料未必以最有用次序排列。"},{"en":"Information presented means the facts, warnings, or instructions shown to the reader.","zh":"information presented 指展示給讀者的事實、警告或指示。"},{"en":"In a timetable, the information presented must help passengers find routes quickly.","zh":"在時間表中，所呈現的資料必須幫助乘客快速找到路線。"},{"en":"Even correct information can fail if it is presented in a confusing order.","zh":"即使資料正確，如果呈現次序混亂，也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how information is shown.","zh":"討論資訊如何展示時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"an awful lot of junk","meaning":"大量雜亂或低價值資料","examples":[{"en":"There can be an awful lot of junk at the beginning of PILs.","zh":"病人資料單張開頭可能有大量雜亂或低價值資料。"},{"en":"An awful lot of junk means a large amount of unnecessary or low-value information.","zh":"an awful lot of junk 指大量不必要或低價值資料。"},{"en":"A school notice has an awful lot of junk if the key date is hidden after long introductions.","zh":"如果關鍵日期藏在長篇引言後，學校通告就有大量雜亂資料。"},{"en":"Too much junk at the beginning can stop readers from finding urgent information.","zh":"開頭太多雜亂資訊會阻礙讀者找到緊急資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and useful when criticising cluttered writing.","zh":"這個短語較口語，適合批評雜亂文字。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at the beginning of","meaning":"在……開頭","examples":[{"en":"Company details often appear at the beginning of leaflets.","zh":"公司資料常出現在單張開頭。"},{"en":"At the beginning of means at the start of something.","zh":"at the beginning of 指在某事物的開始部分。"},{"en":"At the beginning of a lesson, a teacher may review the previous topic.","zh":"在課堂開頭，老師可能重溫上一個主題。"},{"en":"What appears at the beginning often affects what readers notice first.","zh":"出現在開頭的內容常影響讀者首先注意甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing order and structure.","zh":"討論次序和結構時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"company details","meaning":"公司資料","examples":[{"en":"Company details may be less important than safety warnings.","zh":"公司資料可能不及安全警告重要。"},{"en":"Company details are information about a company, such as its name, address, or contact information.","zh":"company details 指關於公司的資料，例如名稱、地址或聯絡資訊。"},{"en":"A leaflet may include company details at the end so readers can contact the manufacturer.","zh":"單張可能在結尾包括公司資料，讓讀者可聯絡製造商。"},{"en":"If company details appear before urgent warnings, patients may not find what they need quickly.","zh":"如果公司資料出現在緊急警告之前，病人可能不能快速找到所需內容。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing business information on documents.","zh":"討論文件上的商業資料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"listed towards the beginning of","meaning":"列於……較前部分","examples":[{"en":"Company details are often listed towards the beginning of a leaflet.","zh":"公司資料常列於單張較前部分。"},{"en":"Listed towards the beginning of means placed near the start of a written document.","zh":"listed towards the beginning of 指放在書面文件接近開首的位置。"},{"en":"In a school newsletter, important dates should be listed towards the beginning.","zh":"在學校通訊中，重要日期應列於較前部分。"},{"en":"Placing less important details too early can waste the reader’s attention.","zh":"太早放置較不重要細節可能浪費讀者注意力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing information order.","zh":"討論資訊次序時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"what might be more important","meaning":"可能更重要的是","examples":[{"en":"What might be more important is whether the medicine can be taken with alcohol.","zh":"可能更重要的是該藥物能否與酒精同服。"},{"en":"What might be more important introduces a point that deserves greater attention.","zh":"what might be more important 用來引入更值得注意的一點。"},{"en":"In a study plan, what might be more important is not time spent, but whether practice is focused.","zh":"在學習計劃中，可能更重要的不是花了多少時間，而是練習是否集中。"},{"en":"This phrase helps shift attention from a less important detail to a more practical concern.","zh":"這個短語幫助把注意力從較不重要細節轉向更實際關注。"},{"en":"It is useful when correcting priorities.","zh":"修正優先次序時，它很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be taken with alcohol","meaning":"與酒精同服","examples":[{"en":"Some medicines should not be taken with alcohol.","zh":"有些藥物不應與酒精同服。"},{"en":"Be taken with alcohol means be used or swallowed while also drinking alcohol.","zh":"be taken with alcohol 指在飲酒同時使用或吞服藥物。"},{"en":"A patient should ask a pharmacist whether antibiotics can be taken with alcohol.","zh":"病人應詢問藥劑師抗生素能否與酒精同服。"},{"en":"Mixing alcohol with some medicines can reduce effectiveness or increase side effects.","zh":"把酒精與某些藥物混合，可能降低藥效或增加副作用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing medicine warnings.","zh":"討論藥物警告時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Design principles and guidelines","meaning":"設計原則與指引","examples":[{"en":"Design principles and guidelines can help reduce packaging errors.","zh":"設計原則與指引可以幫助減少包裝錯誤。"},{"en":"Design principles and guidelines are rules or recommendations that help designers make better choices.","zh":"design principles and guidelines 指幫助設計師作出更好選擇的規則或建議。"},{"en":"A school may use design guidelines so all safety posters are easy to read.","zh":"學校可能使用設計指引，令所有安全海報容易閱讀。"},{"en":"Clear guidelines reduce errors because designers do not have to guess what works.","zh":"清晰指引能減少錯誤，因為設計師不用猜測甚麼有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing standards for good design.","zh":"討論良好設計標準時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"look-alike boxes","meaning":"外觀相似的盒子","examples":[{"en":"Look-alike boxes present a risk of selection errors.","zh":"外觀相似的盒子構成選取錯誤風險。"},{"en":"Look-alike boxes are packages that look so similar that people may confuse them.","zh":"look-alike boxes 指看起來非常相似、令人可能混淆的包裝盒。"},{"en":"Two cereal boxes with almost identical colours can be look-alike boxes for a tired shopper.","zh":"兩個顏色幾乎一樣的穀物盒，對疲倦購物者來說可以是外觀相似的盒子。"},{"en":"In pharmacies, look-alike boxes can cause serious mistakes because medicines may be mixed up.","zh":"在藥房中，外觀相似的盒子可能造成嚴重錯誤，因為藥物可能被混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when similar packaging creates danger.","zh":"當相似包裝造成危險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"present a risk of","meaning":"構成……風險","examples":[{"en":"Look-alike boxes present a risk of selection errors.","zh":"外觀相似的盒子構成選取錯誤風險。"},{"en":"Present a risk of means create or carry the possibility of a harmful problem.","zh":"present a risk of 指造成或帶有某種有害問題的可能性。"},{"en":"Wet floors present a risk of falls in a busy school corridor.","zh":"濕地板在繁忙學校走廊構成跌倒風險。"},{"en":"A risk must be considered even if the accident has not happened yet.","zh":"即使意外尚未發生，風險也必須被考慮。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when warning about possible harm.","zh":"警告可能傷害時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"selection errors","meaning":"選取錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Poor packaging can lead to selection errors.","zh":"包裝不良可能導致選取錯誤。"},{"en":"Selection errors are mistakes made when choosing the wrong item from several options.","zh":"selection errors 指從多個選項中選錯物品的錯誤。"},{"en":"A shopper may make a selection error if two sauce bottles have nearly identical labels.","zh":"如果兩瓶醬料標籤幾乎一樣，購物者可能出現選取錯誤。"},{"en":"In medicine, selection errors can harm patients because the wrong drug may be supplied.","zh":"在藥物方面，選取錯誤可能傷害病人，因為可能供應錯藥。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the mistake happens at the choosing stage.","zh":"當錯誤發生在選擇階段時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"obvious solution","meaning":"明顯的解決方法","examples":[{"en":"An obvious solution would be to use colours to highlight different strengths.","zh":"明顯的解決方法是用顏色突出不同劑量強度。"},{"en":"An obvious solution is an answer that seems clear and natural at first.","zh":"obvious solution 指初看起來清楚而自然的答案。"},{"en":"If students keep forgetting homework, an obvious solution is to write reminders on the board.","zh":"如果學生常忘記功課，明顯的解決方法是在黑板寫提醒。"},{"en":"Obvious solutions can be useful, but they still need careful testing.","zh":"明顯解決方法可以有用，但仍需要仔細測試。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a first answer seems simple and direct.","zh":"當第一個答案看似簡單直接時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"use colours to highlight","meaning":"用顏色突出……","examples":[{"en":"Designers can use colours to highlight different strengths.","zh":"設計師可以用顏色突出不同劑量強度。"},{"en":"Use colours to highlight means make information stand out by using colour.","zh":"use colours to highlight 指透過顏色令資訊更突出。"},{"en":"A teacher may use colours to highlight verbs, nouns, and adjectives on a worksheet.","zh":"老師可能用顏色在工作紙上突出動詞、名詞和形容詞。"},{"en":"Colours guide attention quickly, but users must still read the words carefully.","zh":"顏色能快速引導注意力，但使用者仍必須仔細閱讀文字。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when colour helps organise information.","zh":"當顏色幫助組織資訊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"different strengths","meaning":"不同劑量強度","examples":[{"en":"Medicine boxes may show different strengths through colour contrasts.","zh":"藥盒可能透過顏色對比顯示不同劑量強度。"},{"en":"Different strengths are different dose levels or concentrations of the same medicine.","zh":"different strengths 指同一藥物的不同劑量水平或濃度。"},{"en":"A painkiller may come in different strengths for adults and children.","zh":"止痛藥可能有成人和兒童適用的不同劑量強度。"},{"en":"Confusing different strengths can lead to underdosing or overdosing.","zh":"混淆不同劑量強度可能導致劑量不足或過量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when medicine dosage levels must be separated clearly.","zh":"當藥物劑量水平必須清楚分開時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"colour differentiation","meaning":"顏色區分","examples":[{"en":"Colour differentiation needs to be approached with care.","zh":"顏色區分需要小心處理。"},{"en":"Colour differentiation means using different colours to separate or identify different items.","zh":"colour differentiation 指使用不同顏色來分開或識別不同項目。"},{"en":"A school timetable may use colour differentiation to separate subjects.","zh":"學校時間表可能使用顏色區分不同科目。"},{"en":"Colour differentiation helps quickly, but it can fail for colour-blind users or careless readers.","zh":"顏色區分能快速幫助識別，但對色盲使用者或粗心讀者可能失效。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when colour is used as a distinguishing tool.","zh":"當顏色被用作區分工具時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be approached with care","meaning":"需要小心處理","examples":[{"en":"Colour differentiation needs to be approached with care.","zh":"顏色區分需要小心處理。"},{"en":"Be approached with care means be handled carefully because mistakes may cause problems.","zh":"be approached with care 指必須謹慎處理，因為錯誤可能造成問題。"},{"en":"Giving feedback to a sensitive student should be approached with care.","zh":"向敏感學生提供回饋需要小心處理。"},{"en":"A solution that seems simple may still create new risks if used carelessly.","zh":"看似簡單的解決方法若粗心使用，仍可能造成新風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when warning that caution is needed.","zh":"警告需要謹慎時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"strong colour contrasts","meaning":"強烈色彩對比","examples":[{"en":"Strong colour contrasts should be used in packaging design.","zh":"包裝設計應使用強烈色彩對比。"},{"en":"Strong colour contrasts are clear differences between colours, such as black on white or dark blue on yellow.","zh":"strong colour contrasts 指顏色之間有清楚差異，例如白底黑字或黃底深藍字。"},{"en":"Road signs use strong colour contrasts so drivers can read them quickly.","zh":"道路標誌使用強烈色彩對比，讓司機快速閱讀。"},{"en":"Strong contrast improves visibility, especially for tired users or people with weak eyesight.","zh":"強烈對比改善可見度，尤其對疲倦使用者或視力較弱人士有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing readable visual design.","zh":"討論易讀視覺設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"designate a colour to","meaning":"將某種顏色指定給……","examples":[{"en":"Designating a colour to a particular strength is not recommended.","zh":"不建議將某種顏色指定給特定劑量強度。"},{"en":"Designate a colour to something means assign one colour to represent that item or category.","zh":"designate a colour to something 指指定一種顏色代表某項目或類別。"},{"en":"A teacher may designate red to grammar mistakes and blue to vocabulary mistakes.","zh":"老師可能將紅色指定給文法錯誤，藍色指定給詞彙錯誤。"},{"en":"Colour assignment can help users, but it may also make them ignore written details.","zh":"顏色指定可以幫助使用者，但也可能令他們忽略書面細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when colour is used as a code.","zh":"當顏色被用作編碼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"particular strength","meaning":"特定劑量強度","examples":[{"en":"Colour coding should not be tied too simply to a particular strength.","zh":"顏色編碼不應太簡單地與某一特定劑量強度綁定。"},{"en":"A particular strength is one specific dose level of a medicine.","zh":"particular strength 指某一個特定藥物劑量水平。"},{"en":"A box may contain a particular strength of 50 mg, while another contains 100 mg.","zh":"一個盒子可能含有50毫克的特定劑量強度，另一盒則含有100毫克。"},{"en":"If users rely only on colour, they may confuse one particular strength with another.","zh":"如果使用者只依賴顏色，他們可能混淆一個特定劑量強度和另一個。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing specific medicine doses.","zh":"討論特定藥物劑量時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"colour coding","meaning":"顏色編碼","examples":[{"en":"Colour coding is not recommended if it stops users reading the text.","zh":"如果顏色編碼令使用者不閱讀文字，就不建議使用。"},{"en":"Colour coding means using colours to represent categories, instructions, or meanings.","zh":"colour coding 指使用顏色代表類別、指示或意思。"},{"en":"A school timetable may use colour coding for different subjects.","zh":"學校時間表可能用顏色編碼不同科目。"},{"en":"Colour coding can speed up recognition, but it becomes risky if people stop checking words.","zh":"顏色編碼可以加快識別，但如果人們停止核對文字，它就會變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when colours are used to organise information.","zh":"當顏色用來組織資訊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be not recommended","meaning":"不建議","examples":[{"en":"Colour coding is not recommended in some medicine packaging.","zh":"某些藥物包裝不建議使用顏色編碼。"},{"en":"Be not recommended means experts advise against using or doing something.","zh":"be not recommended 指專家建議不要使用或做某事。"},{"en":"Cramming all night before an exam is not recommended because tiredness harms performance.","zh":"考試前通宵死記不建議，因為疲倦會損害表現。"},{"en":"Something may be not recommended when its risks are greater than its benefits.","zh":"當某事風險大於好處，它可能不被建議。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving professional advice against an action.","zh":"給出反對某行動的專業建議時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"Colour coding could lead to the user not reading the text.","zh":"顏色編碼可能導致使用者不閱讀文字。"},{"en":"Lead to means cause or result in something.","zh":"lead to 指造成或導致某結果。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can lead to mistakes in class the next day.","zh":"睡眠不足可能導致翌日上課時犯錯。"},{"en":"A small design choice can lead to a serious problem if users behave differently from expected.","zh":"如果使用者行為不同於預期，小設計選擇可能導致嚴重問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining cause and effect.","zh":"解釋因果關係時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"read the text on a box","meaning":"閱讀盒上的文字","examples":[{"en":"Users should still read the text on a box carefully.","zh":"使用者仍應仔細閱讀盒上的文字。"},{"en":"Read the text on a box means look at and understand the printed words on the packaging.","zh":"read the text on a box 指查看並理解包裝盒上的印刷文字。"},{"en":"A shopper should read the text on a box before buying medicine for a child.","zh":"購物者為孩子買藥前應閱讀盒上的文字。"},{"en":"Reading the box matters because colour and shape alone may be misleading.","zh":"閱讀盒子很重要，因為單靠顏色和形狀可能有誤導性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when written package information must be checked.","zh":"當必須核對包裝文字資料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"design features","meaning":"設計特點","examples":[{"en":"Design features can provide the basis for lengthy debates.","zh":"設計特點可以為冗長討論提供基礎。"},{"en":"Design features are specific parts or qualities of a design, such as colour, shape, size, or layout.","zh":"design features 指設計中的特定部分或特質，例如顏色、形狀、大小或版面。"},{"en":"A phone’s button size and screen brightness are design features.","zh":"手機的按鈕大小和螢幕亮度都是設計特點。"},{"en":"Small design features can create big disagreements when safety is involved.","zh":"當涉及安全，小設計特點也可能引起重大分歧。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing individual parts of a design.","zh":"討論設計的個別部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"provide the basis for","meaning":"為……提供基礎","examples":[{"en":"Design features can provide the basis for lengthy debates.","zh":"設計特點可以為冗長討論提供基礎。"},{"en":"Provide the basis for means give the foundation or starting point for something.","zh":"provide the basis for 指為某事提供基礎或起點。"},{"en":"Survey results can provide the basis for a school improvement plan.","zh":"調查結果可以為學校改善計劃提供基礎。"},{"en":"A strong basis helps people discuss a problem with evidence rather than guesses.","zh":"堅實基礎幫助人們以證據而非猜測討論問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one thing supports later discussion or action.","zh":"當某事支撐後續討論或行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lengthy debates","meaning":"冗長討論","examples":[{"en":"Packaging design features can lead to lengthy debates.","zh":"包裝設計特點可能導致冗長討論。"},{"en":"Lengthy debates are long discussions with different opinions and no quick agreement.","zh":"lengthy debates 指包含不同意見且不能快速達成共識的長時間討論。"},{"en":"A school may have lengthy debates about whether phones should be allowed in class.","zh":"學校可能就課堂是否容許手機進行冗長討論。"},{"en":"Debates become lengthy when the issue affects safety, cost, and user needs at the same time.","zh":"當議題同時影響安全、成本和使用者需要，討論就會變得冗長。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when decisions take a long time to discuss.","zh":"當決定需要長時間討論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"one argument is that","meaning":"其中一個論點是","examples":[{"en":"One argument is that black-and-white packaging would force people to read carefully.","zh":"其中一個論點是黑白包裝會迫使人仔細閱讀。"},{"en":"One argument is that introduces one possible opinion or reason in a debate.","zh":"one argument is that 用來引入辯論中的一種可能意見或理由。"},{"en":"One argument is that homework teaches discipline, but others say it creates stress.","zh":"其中一個論點是功課教導自律，但其他人說它造成壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase helps present a view without saying everyone agrees with it.","zh":"這個短語幫助呈現一種看法，而不表示所有人都同意。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining different sides of an issue.","zh":"解釋議題不同立場時，它很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"black lettering","meaning":"黑色字體","examples":[{"en":"Some people argue that all packaging should be white with black lettering.","zh":"有些人主張所有包裝都應是白底黑色字體。"},{"en":"Black lettering means printed words written in black ink or black type.","zh":"black lettering 指以黑色墨水或黑色字體印出的文字。"},{"en":"A white sign with black lettering is often easy to read from a distance.","zh":"白底黑字標誌通常從遠處也容易閱讀。"},{"en":"Clear black lettering can improve legibility, especially on important instructions.","zh":"清晰黑色字體可以改善易讀性，尤其在重要指示上。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing printed text design.","zh":"討論印刷文字設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have no choice but to","meaning":"別無選擇，只能","examples":[{"en":"If all boxes looked similar, people would have no choice but to read them carefully.","zh":"如果所有盒子看起來相似，人們就別無選擇，只能仔細閱讀。"},{"en":"Have no choice but to means be forced to do something because there is no other reasonable option.","zh":"have no choice but to 指因沒有其他合理選項而被迫做某事。"},{"en":"If the lift breaks down, students may have no choice but to use the stairs.","zh":"如果升降機壞了，學生可能別無選擇，只能走樓梯。"},{"en":"Removing easy shortcuts can force people to check information more carefully.","zh":"移除簡單捷徑可以迫使人更仔細核對資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when only one action is possible.","zh":"當只有一個行動可行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"read every box carefully","meaning":"仔細閱讀每個盒子","examples":[{"en":"People would have to read every box carefully.","zh":"人們將不得不仔細閱讀每個盒子。"},{"en":"Read every box carefully means check all printed information on each package before choosing or using it.","zh":"read every box carefully 指在選擇或使用前核對每個包裝上的所有印刷資料。"},{"en":"A pharmacist should read every box carefully when several medicines have similar names.","zh":"當幾種藥物名稱相似，藥劑師應仔細閱讀每個盒子。"},{"en":"Careful reading reduces errors because visual shortcuts may be misleading.","zh":"仔細閱讀能減少錯誤，因為視覺捷徑可能有誤導性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when accuracy matters more than speed.","zh":"當準確比速度重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"few trials have examined","meaning":"很少試驗研究過","examples":[{"en":"Few trials have examined drug-packaging design.","zh":"很少試驗研究過藥物包裝設計。"},{"en":"Few trials have examined means only a small number of studies have tested or investigated something.","zh":"few trials have examined 指只有少數研究測試或調查某事。"},{"en":"Few trials have examined whether shorter homework improves learning for younger students.","zh":"很少試驗研究過較短功課是否改善低年級學生學習。"},{"en":"When few trials exist, strong claims should be made carefully.","zh":"當試驗很少，強烈聲稱應謹慎提出。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence is limited.","zh":"當證據有限時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"drug-packaging design","meaning":"藥物包裝設計","examples":[{"en":"Few trials have examined drug-packaging design directly.","zh":"很少試驗直接研究過藥物包裝設計。"},{"en":"Drug-packaging design is the planning of medicine containers, labels, colours, shapes, and information layout.","zh":"drug-packaging design 指藥物容器、標籤、顏色、形狀和資訊版面的規劃。"},{"en":"Good drug-packaging design helps pharmacists choose the right box quickly.","zh":"良好藥物包裝設計幫助藥劑師快速選對盒子。"},{"en":"Poor design can cause confusion, especially when medicines have similar names.","zh":"不良設計會造成混亂，尤其當藥物名稱相似時。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the visual and practical design of medicine packages.","zh":"討論藥物包裝的視覺和實用設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"legibility and comprehensibility","meaning":"易讀性和可理解性","examples":[{"en":"Most studies focus on legibility and comprehensibility in other settings.","zh":"大多數研究集中於其他環境中的易讀性和可理解性。"},{"en":"Legibility and comprehensibility mean how easy something is to read and understand.","zh":"legibility and comprehensibility 指某內容有多容易閱讀和理解。"},{"en":"A school notice needs legibility and comprehensibility so parents can act correctly.","zh":"學校通告需要易讀性和可理解性，讓家長能正確行動。"},{"en":"Text that is easy to see but hard to understand still fails users.","zh":"看得清但難理解的文字仍然未能服務使用者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when both reading clarity and meaning matter.","zh":"當閱讀清晰度和意思同樣重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"road traffic signs","meaning":"道路交通標誌","examples":[{"en":"Many legibility studies concern road traffic signs.","zh":"許多易讀性研究涉及道路交通標誌。"},{"en":"Road traffic signs are signs on roads that guide, warn, or instruct drivers and pedestrians.","zh":"road traffic signs 指道路上引導、警告或指示司機和行人的標誌。"},{"en":"A red stop sign is one of the most familiar road traffic signs.","zh":"紅色停車標誌是最熟悉的道路交通標誌之一。"},{"en":"Road signs must be legible because drivers may have only seconds to react.","zh":"道路標誌必須易讀，因為司機可能只有幾秒反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing public safety design.","zh":"討論公共安全設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"visual display units","meaning":"視覺顯示裝置","examples":[{"en":"Some studies of comprehensibility concern visual display units.","zh":"有些可理解性研究涉及視覺顯示裝置。"},{"en":"Visual display units are screens or electronic displays that show information.","zh":"visual display units 指顯示資訊的螢幕或電子顯示器。"},{"en":"A computer monitor in an office is a visual display unit.","zh":"辦公室中的電腦顯示器是一種視覺顯示裝置。"},{"en":"Poor screen layout can reduce understanding even when the information is correct.","zh":"即使資訊正確，差劣螢幕版面也會降低理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how information appears on screens.","zh":"討論資訊如何出現在螢幕上時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take results into account","meaning":"將結果納入考慮","examples":[{"en":"Some designers take results from such studies into account.","zh":"有些設計師會將這類研究結果納入考慮。"},{"en":"Take results into account means consider findings when making a decision.","zh":"take results into account 指在作決定時考慮研究發現或結果。"},{"en":"A teacher may take test results into account when planning revision lessons.","zh":"老師規劃溫習課時，可能將測驗結果納入考慮。"},{"en":"Decisions improve when evidence is considered instead of ignored.","zh":"當證據被考慮而非被忽視，決策會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research influences practice.","zh":"當研究影響實踐時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"prove that","meaning":"證明","examples":[{"en":"It can be difficult to prove that a particular feature is beneficial.","zh":"要證明某項特定特點有益可能很困難。"},{"en":"Prove that means show with strong evidence that something is true.","zh":"prove that 指用有力證據顯示某事為真。"},{"en":"A student must prove that an argument is valid by using examples and evidence.","zh":"學生必須用例子和證據證明論點有效。"},{"en":"It is hard to prove a design works unless real users are tested.","zh":"除非以真實使用者測試，否則很難證明設計有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence is needed to support a claim.","zh":"當需要證據支持聲稱時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a particular feature","meaning":"某項特定特點","examples":[{"en":"A particular feature may be helpful, but this can be hard to prove.","zh":"某項特定特點可能有幫助，但這可能難以證明。"},{"en":"A particular feature is one specific part or quality of a product, system, or design.","zh":"particular feature 指產品、系統或設計中的某一具體部分或特質。"},{"en":"A phone’s fingerprint lock is a particular feature that improves security.","zh":"手機的指紋鎖是一項提升安全性的特定特點。"},{"en":"Testing one feature separately helps designers know whether it truly helps users.","zh":"分開測試一項特點，幫助設計師知道它是否真的幫助使用者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when focusing on one detail.","zh":"聚焦某一細節時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be beneficial","meaning":"有益；有幫助","examples":[{"en":"It is difficult to prove that a feature is beneficial.","zh":"要證明某特點有益是困難的。"},{"en":"Be beneficial means be helpful or produce a good effect.","zh":"be beneficial 指有幫助或產生良好效果。"},{"en":"Daily reading is beneficial for students because it builds vocabulary and confidence.","zh":"每日閱讀對學生有益，因為它建立詞彙和信心。"},{"en":"A design is beneficial only if it helps real users, not just designers.","zh":"設計只有在幫助真實使用者時才算有益，而不只是設計師覺得好。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing positive effects.","zh":"描述正面效果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"EU legislation","meaning":"歐盟法例","examples":[{"en":"EU legislation requires medicine names to appear in Braille.","zh":"歐盟法例規定藥物名稱要以盲文出現。"},{"en":"EU legislation means laws or rules made by the European Union.","zh":"EU legislation 指由歐盟制定的法律或規則。"},{"en":"EU legislation may affect how companies label food, medicine, or electronic products.","zh":"歐盟法例可能影響公司如何標示食品、藥物或電子產品。"},{"en":"Such legislation can change design because companies must follow legal requirements.","zh":"這類法例可以改變設計，因為公司必須遵守法律要求。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing European legal rules.","zh":"討論歐洲法律規則時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"require that","meaning":"規定","examples":[{"en":"EU legislation requires that packaging include the medicine name in Braille.","zh":"歐盟法例規定包裝須以盲文包括藥物名稱。"},{"en":"Require that means officially say that something must happen.","zh":"require that 指正式規定某事必須發生。"},{"en":"School rules may require that students wear safety glasses in science lessons.","zh":"校規可能規定學生在科學課必須戴安全眼鏡。"},{"en":"Requirements create standards that everyone must follow.","zh":"規定會建立所有人必須遵守的標準。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when expressing formal rules.","zh":"表達正式規則時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"include the name of the medicine","meaning":"包括藥物名稱","examples":[{"en":"Packaging must include the name of the medicine in Braille.","zh":"包裝必須以盲文包括藥物名稱。"},{"en":"Include the name of the medicine means show the medicine’s name clearly on the package or document.","zh":"include the name of the medicine 指在包裝或文件上清楚顯示藥物名稱。"},{"en":"A pill bottle should include the name of the medicine so patients can check it before use.","zh":"藥瓶應包括藥物名稱，讓病人使用前核對。"},{"en":"Naming the medicine clearly prevents confusion between similar-looking products.","zh":"清楚標出藥物名稱可以防止與外觀相似產品混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing essential label information.","zh":"討論標籤必要資料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Braille","meaning":"盲文","examples":[{"en":"The name of the medicine must now appear in Braille.","zh":"藥物名稱現在必須以盲文出現。"},{"en":"Braille is a system of raised dots that blind or visually impaired people can read by touch.","zh":"Braille 指由凸起點組成、讓盲人或視障人士以觸摸閱讀的系統。"},{"en":"Lift buttons often include Braille so blind users can identify floors.","zh":"升降機按鈕常包括盲文，讓盲人使用者識別樓層。"},{"en":"Braille on packaging can improve access, but it must fit safely with printed text.","zh":"包裝上的盲文可以改善無障礙使用，但必須與印刷文字安全配合。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing accessibility for blind readers.","zh":"討論盲人讀者的無障礙設計時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"visually impaired patients","meaning":"視障病人","examples":[{"en":"It is not clear how much visually impaired patients will benefit.","zh":"尚不清楚視障病人會受益多少。"},{"en":"Visually impaired patients are patients whose eyesight is limited or seriously reduced.","zh":"visually impaired patients 指視力有限或嚴重下降的病人。"},{"en":"Visually impaired patients may need large print, Braille, or audio instructions.","zh":"視障病人可能需要大字體、盲文或語音指示。"},{"en":"If packaging ignores visual impairment, patients may struggle to identify medicines safely.","zh":"如果包裝忽視視障，病人可能難以安全識別藥物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing accessible healthcare information.","zh":"討論無障礙醫療資訊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"benefit from","meaning":"從……受益","examples":[{"en":"Visually impaired patients may benefit from Braille on packaging.","zh":"視障病人可能從包裝上的盲文受益。"},{"en":"Benefit from means gain help, advantage, or improvement from something.","zh":"benefit from 指從某事物得到幫助、好處或改善。"},{"en":"Students benefit from clear examples because they can understand grammar faster.","zh":"學生從清楚例子受益，因為他們能更快理解文法。"},{"en":"A design feature is valuable only if real users benefit from it.","zh":"只有當真實使用者從中受益，設計特點才有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something produces a positive effect.","zh":"當某事物產生正面效果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"sighted patients","meaning":"視力正常的病人","examples":[{"en":"Designers do not know whether sighted patients will be impaired by Braille.","zh":"設計師不知道視力正常的病人是否會受盲文影響。"},{"en":"Sighted patients are patients who can see, especially compared with blind or visually impaired patients.","zh":"sighted patients 指能看見的病人，尤其是與盲人或視障病人相比。"},{"en":"Sighted patients usually read printed labels rather than Braille.","zh":"視力正常的病人通常閱讀印刷標籤，而不是盲文。"},{"en":"A design must help visually impaired users without making reading harder for sighted patients.","zh":"設計必須幫助視障使用者，而不令視力正常病人閱讀更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing users with and without visual impairment.","zh":"比較有視障和無視障使用者時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be impaired","meaning":"受影響；受損","examples":[{"en":"The reading of sighted patients may be impaired.","zh":"視力正常病人的閱讀可能受影響。"},{"en":"Be impaired means be made weaker, worse, or less effective.","zh":"be impaired 指變弱、變差或變得較無效。"},{"en":"A student’s concentration may be impaired by lack of sleep.","zh":"學生的專注力可能因睡眠不足而受損。"},{"en":"A design intended to help one group should not impair another group’s use.","zh":"旨在幫助一個群體的設計不應損害另一群體的使用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is negatively affected.","zh":"當某事受到負面影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"more evidence","meaning":"更多證據","examples":[{"en":"More evidence about packaging design may soon be available.","zh":"關於包裝設計的更多證據可能很快會有。"},{"en":"More evidence means additional information or proof that helps people judge a claim.","zh":"more evidence 指額外資訊或證明，幫助人判斷某聲稱。"},{"en":"Teachers need more evidence before deciding whether a new homework policy works.","zh":"老師需要更多證據，才決定新功課政策是否有效。"},{"en":"More evidence can turn guesses into better decisions.","zh":"更多證據可以把猜測變成更好決策。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when current knowledge is not enough.","zh":"當目前知識不足夠時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"soon be available","meaning":"可能很快會有","examples":[{"en":"More evidence may soon be available.","zh":"更多證據可能很快會有。"},{"en":"Soon be available means likely to be accessible or ready in the near future.","zh":"soon be available 指很可能在不久將來可取得或準備好。"},{"en":"A new library booking system may soon be available after testing finishes.","zh":"新圖書館預約系統完成測試後可能很快會有。"},{"en":"When information soon becomes available, people may delay final decisions until then.","zh":"當資訊很快會有，人們可能延遲最終決定直到那時。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is expected shortly.","zh":"當某物預期很快出現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"reflect consultations with","meaning":"反映與……的諮詢","examples":[{"en":"PILs must reflect consultations with target patient groups.","zh":"病人資料單張必須反映與目標病人群體的諮詢。"},{"en":"Reflect consultations with means show that advice or feedback from a group has been considered.","zh":"reflect consultations with 指顯示已考慮某群體的建議或回饋。"},{"en":"A school policy should reflect consultations with teachers, students, and parents.","zh":"學校政策應反映與老師、學生和家長的諮詢。"},{"en":"Consultation matters because real users often notice problems experts miss.","zh":"諮詢很重要，因為真實使用者常注意到專家錯過的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when feedback should influence a final document or design.","zh":"當回饋應影響最終文件或設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"target patient groups","meaning":"目標病人群體","examples":[{"en":"Patient information leaflets should be tested with target patient groups.","zh":"病人資料單張應與目標病人群體一起測試。"},{"en":"Target patient groups are the specific types of patients a medicine or leaflet is meant for.","zh":"target patient groups 指某藥物或單張面向的特定病人類型。"},{"en":"A leaflet for asthma medicine may be tested with target patient groups such as teenagers and parents.","zh":"哮喘藥物單張可能與青少年和家長等目標病人群體測試。"},{"en":"Testing with the right group reveals whether the information fits real users.","zh":"與正確群體測試能揭示資料是否適合真實使用者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when healthcare information is designed for particular patients.","zh":"當醫療資訊為特定病人設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ensure that","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Consultations help ensure that leaflets are legible, clear and easy to use.","zh":"諮詢有助確保單張易讀、清晰而易用。"},{"en":"Ensure that means make certain that something happens or is true.","zh":"ensure that 指確保某事發生或為真。"},{"en":"A teacher checks instructions to ensure that students know what to do.","zh":"老師檢查指示，以確保學生知道要做甚麼。"},{"en":"Extra checking ensures that small errors do not become bigger problems.","zh":"額外檢查確保小錯誤不會變成更大問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing how people make a result more certain.","zh":"描述人們如何令結果更確定時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"legible, clear and easy to use","meaning":"易讀、清晰而易用","examples":[{"en":"PILs should be legible, clear and easy to use.","zh":"病人資料單張應易讀、清晰而易用。"},{"en":"Legible, clear and easy to use means readable, understandable, and practical for ordinary users.","zh":"legible, clear and easy to use 指可閱讀、可理解，並對普通使用者實用。"},{"en":"A school form should be legible, clear and easy to use so parents can complete it correctly.","zh":"學校表格應易讀、清晰而易用，讓家長能正確填寫。"},{"en":"If information is not clear, users may avoid it or make mistakes.","zh":"如果資訊不清楚，使用者可能避開它或犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when judging whether information design works well.","zh":"判斷資訊設計是否有效時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"imply that","meaning":"意味着","examples":[{"en":"The new requirement implies that industry will have to start conducting tests.","zh":"新要求意味着業界將不得不開始進行測試。"},{"en":"Imply that means suggest or show something indirectly.","zh":"imply that 指間接暗示或顯示某事。"},{"en":"If a teacher gives extra practice, it may imply that the exam will be difficult.","zh":"如果老師提供額外練習，這可能意味着考試會困難。"},{"en":"Implication matters because a rule can create duties even if it does not state them directly.","zh":"含意很重要，因為規則即使沒有直接說明，也可能產生責任。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining hidden meaning or consequence.","zh":"解釋隱含意思或後果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"conduct tests","meaning":"進行測試","examples":[{"en":"The pharmaceutical industry will have to conduct tests on leaflets and packaging.","zh":"製藥業將必須對單張和包裝進行測試。"},{"en":"Conduct tests means carry out checks or experiments to see how well something works.","zh":"conduct tests 指進行檢查或實驗，以了解某物運作得如何。"},{"en":"A school may conduct tests to see whether students understand a new reading method.","zh":"學校可能進行測試，以了解學生是否理解新的閱讀方法。"},{"en":"Testing helps find problems before a product reaches many users.","zh":"測試幫助在產品到達大量使用者前找出問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evaluating safety, quality, or understanding.","zh":"評估安全、質素或理解時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"readability studies","meaning":"易讀性研究","examples":[{"en":"Dr van der Waarde has performed readability studies for industry.","zh":"van der Waarde 博士曾為業界進行易讀性研究。"},{"en":"Readability studies are investigations into how easily people can read and understand written material.","zh":"readability studies 指研究人們有多容易閱讀和理解書面材料。"},{"en":"A company may run readability studies before printing instructions for elderly users.","zh":"公司可能在印刷給長者使用的指示前進行易讀性研究。"},{"en":"Such studies reveal whether real readers can find and understand key information.","zh":"這類研究揭示真實讀者是否能找到並理解關鍵資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when testing written communication.","zh":"測試書面溝通時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"typical study","meaning":"典型研究","examples":[{"en":"A typical study involves testing a leaflet or package on a small group.","zh":"典型研究涉及在小組身上測試單張或包裝。"},{"en":"A typical study is a normal or common kind of research in a particular field.","zh":"typical study 指某領域中正常或常見的研究類型。"},{"en":"A typical study in education may compare two groups of students over several weeks.","zh":"教育方面的典型研究可能在數週內比較兩組學生。"},{"en":"Typical studies help people understand standard research practice.","zh":"典型研究幫助人們理解標準研究做法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing what usually happens in research.","zh":"描述研究中通常會發生甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"involve showing","meaning":"涉及展示","examples":[{"en":"A typical study involves showing a leaflet or package to a small group.","zh":"典型研究涉及向小組展示單張或包裝。"},{"en":"Involve showing means include the action of presenting something for people to see or use.","zh":"involve showing 指包括展示某物給人觀看或使用這個動作。"},{"en":"A design test may involve showing two posters to students and asking which is clearer.","zh":"設計測試可能涉及向學生展示兩張海報，並詢問哪一張更清楚。"},{"en":"Showing materials to users helps researchers observe real reactions.","zh":"向使用者展示材料幫助研究者觀察真實反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one step in a study is presentation.","zh":"當研究中的一步是展示時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"test understanding","meaning":"測試理解","examples":[{"en":"Researchers ask questions to test understanding.","zh":"研究人員會提問以測試理解。"},{"en":"Test understanding means check whether someone has correctly understood information.","zh":"test understanding 指檢查某人是否正確理解資訊。"},{"en":"A teacher asks short questions after a lesson to test understanding.","zh":"老師課後問簡短問題來測試理解。"},{"en":"Testing understanding matters because people may read words without grasping the meaning.","zh":"測試理解很重要，因為人們可能讀了文字卻未掌握意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when checking comprehension.","zh":"檢查理解時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"results and comments","meaning":"結果和意見","examples":[{"en":"Results and comments are used to modify the material.","zh":"結果和意見被用來修改材料。"},{"en":"Results and comments are the test findings and user feedback collected during a study.","zh":"results and comments 指研究期間收集的測試發現和使用者回饋。"},{"en":"A teacher may use students’ results and comments to improve a worksheet.","zh":"老師可能使用學生的結果和意見來改善工作紙。"},{"en":"Feedback helps designers know not only what failed but also why it failed.","zh":"回饋幫助設計師知道不只甚麼失敗，也知道為何失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence and opinions guide revision.","zh":"當證據和意見指引修改時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"modify the material","meaning":"修改材料","examples":[{"en":"Researchers use comments to modify the material.","zh":"研究人員使用意見來修改材料。"},{"en":"Modify the material means change the document, package, or design to improve it.","zh":"modify the material 指改變文件、包裝或設計以改善它。"},{"en":"A teacher may modify the material after students say the instructions are confusing.","zh":"學生表示指示混亂後，老師可能修改材料。"},{"en":"Materials improve when real feedback leads to concrete changes.","zh":"當真實回饋帶來具體改變，材料就會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when written or visual content is revised.","zh":"當書面或視覺內容被修訂時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a larger group","meaning":"較大的小組","examples":[{"en":"The modified material is then tested on a larger group.","zh":"修改後的材料接着在較大的小組身上測試。"},{"en":"A larger group means more people than the first test group.","zh":"larger group 指比第一個測試小組更多人。"},{"en":"A school may test a new timetable with one class first and then with a larger group.","zh":"學校可能先用一班測試新時間表，然後再用較大的小組測試。"},{"en":"Larger groups reveal problems that small early tests may miss.","zh":"較大小組能揭示小型早期測試可能錯過的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when testing expands to more users.","zh":"當測試擴展至更多使用者時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a third group","meaning":"第三組","examples":[{"en":"A third group is used to show that further changes are improvements.","zh":"第三組被用來顯示進一步修改是改善。"},{"en":"A third group is another separate group used after the first two groups in testing.","zh":"third group 指在第一和第二組之後使用的另一個獨立小組。"},{"en":"Researchers may use a third group to check whether a revised form is truly clearer.","zh":"研究者可能使用第三組來檢查修訂表格是否真的更清楚。"},{"en":"Testing with another group helps confirm that changes work beyond the first users.","zh":"用另一組測試有助確認改變不只對第一批使用者有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research has several testing stages.","zh":"當研究有幾個測試階段時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"further changes","meaning":"進一步修改","examples":[{"en":"Further changes must be shown to be improvements.","zh":"必須顯示進一步修改是改善。"},{"en":"Further changes are additional modifications made after earlier changes.","zh":"further changes 指在早前修改後作出的額外改動。"},{"en":"A teacher may make further changes to a worksheet after a second class still finds it confusing.","zh":"如果第二班學生仍覺得工作紙混亂，老師可能作進一步修改。"},{"en":"More changes are useful only if they make the material clearer or safer.","zh":"只有當更多改動令材料更清楚或更安全，它們才有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when revision continues after an initial improvement.","zh":"當初步改善後仍繼續修訂時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be sceptical about","meaning":"對……持懷疑態度","examples":[{"en":"Dr van der Waarde is sceptical about the legal requirements.","zh":"van der Waarde 博士對法律要求持懷疑態度。"},{"en":"Be sceptical about means doubt whether something is true, useful, or effective.","zh":"be sceptical about 指懷疑某事是否真實、有用或有效。"},{"en":"A parent may be sceptical about an expensive course that promises instant fluency.","zh":"家長可能對承諾即時流利的昂貴課程持懷疑態度。"},{"en":"Scepticism can be useful when evidence is weak or practical problems remain.","zh":"當證據薄弱或實際問題仍存在，懷疑態度可以有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone questions a claim or policy.","zh":"當某人質疑聲稱或政策時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"regulatory authorities","meaning":"監管機構","examples":[{"en":"Regulatory authorities may not have enough resources to handle packaging information properly.","zh":"監管機構可能沒有足夠資源妥善處理包裝資料。"},{"en":"Regulatory authorities are official bodies that check whether companies follow rules and standards.","zh":"regulatory authorities 指檢查公司是否遵守規則和標準的官方機構。"},{"en":"Food safety departments are regulatory authorities for restaurants and food factories.","zh":"食物安全部門是餐廳和食品工廠的監管機構。"},{"en":"If authorities lack resources, unsafe designs may not be examined deeply enough.","zh":"如果監管機構缺乏資源，不安全設計可能不會被深入檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing official control and inspection.","zh":"討論官方管制和檢查時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"have the resources to","meaning":"有資源去……","examples":[{"en":"Many authorities do not have the resources to handle packaging information properly.","zh":"許多監管機構沒有資源妥善處理包裝資料。"},{"en":"Have the resources to means have enough money, staff, time, tools, or expertise to do something.","zh":"have the resources to 指有足夠金錢、人手、時間、工具或專業知識去做某事。"},{"en":"A small school may not have the resources to offer every advanced subject.","zh":"小型學校可能沒有資源開設每一科高階科目。"},{"en":"Even good rules fail if organisations lack the resources to enforce them.","zh":"即使規則良好，如果機構缺乏資源執行，規則也會失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when ability depends on available support.","zh":"當能力取決於可用支援時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"handle packaging information properly","meaning":"妥善處理包裝資料","examples":[{"en":"Regulatory authorities may not handle packaging information properly.","zh":"監管機構可能未能妥善處理包裝資料。"},{"en":"Handle packaging information properly means examine, organise, and judge package information in a careful practical way.","zh":"handle packaging information properly 指以仔細而實際的方式檢查、組織和判斷包裝資料。"},{"en":"A company must handle allergy information properly so customers can avoid unsafe food.","zh":"公司必須妥善處理過敏資料，讓顧客避免不安全食品。"},{"en":"Poor handling of information can allow unclear warnings to remain on products.","zh":"資訊處理不善可能令不清楚警告繼續留在產品上。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when information management affects safety.","zh":"當資訊管理影響安全時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in a practical context","meaning":"在實際情境中","examples":[{"en":"Authorities may not examine packaging in a practical context.","zh":"監管機構可能沒有在實際情境中檢查包裝。"},{"en":"In a practical context means in a real-life situation where something will actually be used.","zh":"in a practical context 指在某物實際使用的真實生活情況中。"},{"en":"A school rule should be tested in a practical context, not only discussed in a meeting.","zh":"校規應在實際情境中測試，而不只是會議中討論。"},{"en":"Practical context reveals problems that look invisible on paper.","zh":"實際情境會揭示紙面上看不到的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when real use matters more than theory.","zh":"當真實使用比理論重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"one box at a time","meaning":"每次只看一盒","examples":[{"en":"Authorities often see one box at a time.","zh":"監管機構常每次只看一盒。"},{"en":"One box at a time means examining a single package separately rather than comparing several together.","zh":"one box at a time 指分開檢查單一包裝，而不是把幾個一起比較。"},{"en":"A teacher checking one essay at a time may miss patterns across the whole class.","zh":"老師每次只看一篇文章，可能錯過全班共同模式。"},{"en":"Looking at one item alone can hide confusion caused by similar items nearby.","zh":"單獨看一件物品可能隱藏附近相似物品造成的混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when separate review may miss real-world problems.","zh":"當分開審查可能錯過現實問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"several together","meaning":"多盒一起","examples":[{"en":"Pharmacists often see several medicine boxes together.","zh":"藥劑師常看到多盒藥物一起放着。"},{"en":"Several together means more than one item placed, viewed, or considered at the same time.","zh":"several together 指多於一件物品同時被放置、觀看或考慮。"},{"en":"A shopper may compare several cereal boxes together before choosing one.","zh":"購物者可能把幾盒穀物早餐一起比較後才選一盒。"},{"en":"Seeing several together reveals similarities that are not obvious when each item is alone.","zh":"多件一起看會揭示單獨看時不明顯的相似性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparison matters.","zh":"當比較很重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"as pharmacists would do","meaning":"像藥劑師那樣","examples":[{"en":"Authorities should examine packaging as pharmacists would do.","zh":"監管機構應像藥劑師那樣檢查包裝。"},{"en":"As pharmacists would do means in the same way pharmacists experience or handle medicines in practice.","zh":"as pharmacists would do 指以藥劑師在實務中經歷或處理藥物的方式。"},{"en":"A designer should test labels as real users would do, not only under perfect lighting.","zh":"設計師應像真實使用者那樣測試標籤，而不只在完美燈光下測試。"},{"en":"Following professional practice helps reveal risks that office review may miss.","zh":"跟隨專業實務有助揭示辦公室審查可能錯過的風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when experts’ real working conditions should guide testing.","zh":"當專家真實工作情況應指導測試時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"Innovations","meaning":"創新","examples":[{"en":"Innovations can make medicine packaging safer and more user-friendly.","zh":"創新可以令藥物包裝更安全和更易用。"},{"en":"Innovations are new ideas, products, or methods that improve how something works.","zh":"innovations 指改善某事運作方式的新想法、產品或方法。"},{"en":"Online booking was an innovation that made clinic appointments easier for many patients.","zh":"網上預約是一項創新，令許多病人更容易預約診所。"},{"en":"Innovations matter when old methods create avoidable problems.","zh":"當舊方法造成可避免問題，創新就很重要。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing practical new solutions.","zh":"討論實用新解決方案時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"innovation exhibition","meaning":"創新展覽","examples":[{"en":"The RCA innovation exhibition revealed several new healthcare designs.","zh":"RCA 創新展覽展示了幾項新的醫療設計。"},{"en":"An innovation exhibition is an event where new ideas, designs, or inventions are publicly shown.","zh":"innovation exhibition 指公開展示新想法、設計或發明的活動。"},{"en":"A school innovation exhibition may show students’ robots, apps, and environmental projects.","zh":"學校創新展覽可能展示學生的機械人、應用程式和環保項目。"},{"en":"Exhibitions help new ideas gain attention from users, companies, and researchers.","zh":"展覽幫助新想法吸引使用者、公司和研究者注意。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing public displays of new designs.","zh":"討論新設計的公開展示時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reveal designs for","meaning":"展出……的設計","examples":[{"en":"The exhibition revealed designs for innovative objects.","zh":"展覽展出了創新物件的設計。"},{"en":"Reveal designs for means show new plans or prototypes for particular products.","zh":"reveal designs for 指展示某些產品的新計劃或原型。"},{"en":"A company may reveal designs for a new electric bus before production begins.","zh":"公司可能在生產開始前展出新電動巴士的設計。"},{"en":"Revealing designs lets people discuss strengths and weaknesses early.","zh":"展出設計讓人們及早討論優點和弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when new product ideas are shown publicly.","zh":"當新產品想法公開展示時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"innovative objects","meaning":"創新物件","examples":[{"en":"The exhibition showed innovative objects for patients.","zh":"展覽展示了供病人使用的創新物件。"},{"en":"Innovative objects are new or clever items designed to solve problems in better ways.","zh":"innovative objects 指以新的或聰明方式解決問題的物品。"},{"en":"A spoon with a special handle for shaky hands is an innovative object.","zh":"為手抖人士設計、帶特別手柄的匙羹是一件創新物件。"},{"en":"Such objects are useful when they make everyday tasks safer or easier.","zh":"當這類物件令日常任務更安全或更容易，它們就有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing practical inventions.","zh":"討論實用發明時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"The popper","meaning":"The popper（設計名稱）","examples":[{"en":"The popper aims to help arthritis sufferers remove tablets from blister packs.","zh":"The popper 旨在幫助關節炎患者從泡罩包裝中取出藥片。"},{"en":"The popper is a design name for a tool that helps push tablets out of blister packs.","zh":"The popper 是一種工具的設計名稱，用來幫助把藥片從泡罩包裝推出。"},{"en":"A person with painful fingers may use The popper instead of pressing foil by hand.","zh":"手指疼痛的人可能使用 The popper，而不是用手按壓鋁箔。"},{"en":"The tool improves access because it reduces the force needed to remove tablets.","zh":"這個工具改善可及性，因為它減少取出藥片所需力度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing a named healthcare design.","zh":"討論具名稱的醫療設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"aim to help","meaning":"旨在幫助","examples":[{"en":"The popper aims to help arthritis sufferers.","zh":"The popper 旨在幫助關節炎患者。"},{"en":"Aim to help means be designed or intended to assist someone.","zh":"aim to help 指被設計或意圖用來協助某人。"},{"en":"A school reading programme aims to help students who struggle with long passages.","zh":"學校閱讀計劃旨在幫助難以閱讀長篇文章的學生。"},{"en":"A clear aim helps designers focus on the real user problem.","zh":"清晰目標幫助設計師集中於真實使用者問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the purpose of a product or project.","zh":"解釋產品或項目的目的時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"arthritis sufferers","meaning":"關節炎患者","examples":[{"en":"Arthritis sufferers may find blister packs difficult to use.","zh":"關節炎患者可能覺得泡罩包裝難以使用。"},{"en":"Arthritis sufferers are people who have joint pain, stiffness, or swelling caused by arthritis.","zh":"arthritis sufferers 指因關節炎而有關節疼痛、僵硬或腫脹的人。"},{"en":"Arthritis sufferers may struggle with small buttons, tight lids, or blister foils.","zh":"關節炎患者可能難以使用細小按鈕、緊瓶蓋或泡罩鋁箔。"},{"en":"Packaging design must consider arthritis sufferers because hand pain affects medicine use.","zh":"包裝設計必須考慮關節炎患者，因為手痛會影響用藥。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing users with joint problems.","zh":"討論有關節問題的使用者時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"remove tablets from","meaning":"從……取出藥片","examples":[{"en":"The popper helps users remove tablets from blister packs.","zh":"The popper 幫助使用者從泡罩包裝中取出藥片。"},{"en":"Remove tablets from means take pills out of a package or container.","zh":"remove tablets from 指把藥片從包裝或容器中取出。"},{"en":"A patient may need help to remove tablets from a foil pack if their fingers are weak.","zh":"如果手指無力，病人可能需要幫助才能從鋁箔包裝取出藥片。"},{"en":"Easy removal matters because medicine is useless if patients cannot access it.","zh":"容易取出很重要，因為如果病人無法取得藥物，藥物就沒有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing medicine packaging usability.","zh":"討論藥物包裝易用性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"blister packs","meaning":"泡罩包裝","examples":[{"en":"Blister packs can be difficult for arthritis sufferers to open.","zh":"泡罩包裝對關節炎患者來說可能難以打開。"},{"en":"Blister packs are medicine packages where tablets sit in small plastic pockets sealed with foil.","zh":"blister packs 指藥片放在小塑膠格內並以鋁箔密封的藥物包裝。"},{"en":"Many tablets are sold in blister packs so each dose stays separate and protected.","zh":"許多藥片以泡罩包裝出售，使每一劑分開並受保護。"},{"en":"Blister packs protect medicine, but they can be hard to open for people with weak hands.","zh":"泡罩包裝保護藥物，但對手部無力人士可能難以打開。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing tablet packaging.","zh":"討論藥片包裝時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"pluspoint","meaning":"pluspoint（設計名稱）","examples":[{"en":"Pluspoint is an adrenaline auto-injector designed to be easier to carry.","zh":"Pluspoint 是一款設計成較易攜帶的腎上腺素自動注射器。"},{"en":"Pluspoint is a design name for a smaller, more portable emergency injection device.","zh":"Pluspoint 是一種較小、更便攜的緊急注射裝置的設計名稱。"},{"en":"A patient with severe allergies may be more willing to carry Pluspoint in a bag.","zh":"有嚴重過敏的病人可能更願意把 Pluspoint 放在袋中攜帶。"},{"en":"A portable design helps because emergency medicine only works if it is with the patient.","zh":"便攜設計有幫助，因為緊急藥物只有在病人身邊才有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing a named healthcare innovation.","zh":"討論具名稱的醫療創新時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"adrenaline auto-injector","meaning":"腎上腺素自動注射器","examples":[{"en":"Pluspoint is an adrenaline auto-injector.","zh":"Pluspoint 是腎上腺素自動注射器。"},{"en":"An adrenaline auto-injector is a device that quickly injects adrenaline during a severe allergic reaction.","zh":"adrenaline auto-injector 指在嚴重過敏反應時快速注射腎上腺素的裝置。"},{"en":"A person with a dangerous food allergy may carry an adrenaline auto-injector every day.","zh":"有危險食物過敏的人可能每天攜帶腎上腺素自動注射器。"},{"en":"Auto-injectors must be easy to carry because emergencies can happen anywhere.","zh":"自動注射器必須容易攜帶，因為緊急情況可在任何地方發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing emergency allergy treatment.","zh":"討論過敏緊急治療時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"aim to overcome","meaning":"旨在克服","examples":[{"en":"Pluspoint aims to overcome the problem of prohibitive size.","zh":"Pluspoint 旨在克服尺寸大得令人卻步的問題。"},{"en":"Aim to overcome means be designed or intended to solve a difficulty.","zh":"aim to overcome 指被設計或意圖用來解決困難。"},{"en":"A school breakfast programme aims to overcome hunger before morning lessons.","zh":"學校早餐計劃旨在克服早課前學生肚餓的問題。"},{"en":"Designs improve when they target a specific barrier that stops people using a product.","zh":"當設計針對阻止人使用產品的特定障礙，它會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a solution is created to remove a problem.","zh":"當解決方案為消除問題而創造時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the fact that","meaning":"……這一事實","examples":[{"en":"The design addresses the fact that many patients do not carry their auto-injectors.","zh":"這項設計處理許多病人不攜帶自動注射器這一事實。"},{"en":"The fact that introduces a real situation or truth that must be considered.","zh":"the fact that 用來引入必須考慮的真實情況或事實。"},{"en":"A school policy must consider the fact that some students travel more than an hour to school.","zh":"學校政策必須考慮有些學生上學路程超過一小時這一事實。"},{"en":"Good design starts with the fact that real users do not always behave ideally.","zh":"良好設計始於一個事實：真實使用者並不總是理想地行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when pointing to an important reality.","zh":"指出重要現實時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"carry their auto-injectors","meaning":"攜帶自動注射器","examples":[{"en":"Many patients do not carry their auto-injectors because they are too large.","zh":"許多病人因為自動注射器太大而不攜帶它們。"},{"en":"Carry their auto-injectors means keep emergency injection devices with them when they go out.","zh":"carry their auto-injectors 指外出時把緊急注射裝置帶在身邊。"},{"en":"A student with a severe allergy should carry their auto-injector during school trips.","zh":"有嚴重過敏的學生在學校旅行期間應攜帶自動注射器。"},{"en":"If patients do not carry their auto-injectors, they may be unprotected during emergencies.","zh":"如果病人不攜帶自動注射器，緊急情況中可能沒有保護。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing portable emergency medicine.","zh":"討論便攜式緊急藥物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"due to","meaning":"由於","examples":[{"en":"Many patients do not carry auto-injectors due to their prohibitive size.","zh":"許多病人由於自動注射器尺寸大得令人卻步而不攜帶它們。"},{"en":"Due to means because of.","zh":"due to 指因為或由於。"},{"en":"The sports day was cancelled due to heavy rain.","zh":"運動會由於大雨而取消。"},{"en":"This phrase links a result to its cause.","zh":"這個短語把結果與原因連接起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining why something happens.","zh":"解釋事情為何發生時，它很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"prohibitive size","meaning":"大得令人卻步的尺寸","examples":[{"en":"Some auto-injectors are not carried because of their prohibitive size.","zh":"有些自動注射器因尺寸大得令人卻步而不被攜帶。"},{"en":"Prohibitive size means a size so large or inconvenient that it stops people from using or carrying something.","zh":"prohibitive size 指大到或不便到阻止人使用或攜帶某物的尺寸。"},{"en":"A textbook with prohibitive size may be left at home because students cannot fit it in their bags.","zh":"一本尺寸大得令人卻步的教科書可能被學生留在家中，因為放不進書包。"},{"en":"If medical devices are too large, patients may not keep them nearby when needed.","zh":"如果醫療裝置太大，病人可能在需要時沒有把它們放在身邊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when size becomes a practical barrier.","zh":"當尺寸成為實際障礙時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the aim of good design","meaning":"良好設計的目的","examples":[{"en":"The aim of good design is to make things more user-friendly and safer.","zh":"良好設計的目的是令事物更易用和更安全。"},{"en":"The aim of good design means the main purpose of designing something well.","zh":"the aim of good design 指把某物設計得好的主要目的。"},{"en":"The aim of good design in a school chair is comfort, safety, and easy movement.","zh":"學校椅子的良好設計目的，是舒適、安全和容易移動。"},{"en":"Good design solves real problems rather than simply making products look attractive.","zh":"良好設計解決真實問題，而不是只令產品看起來吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining what design should achieve.","zh":"解釋設計應達到甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"inclusive design","meaning":"共融設計","examples":[{"en":"Roger Coleman is a professor of inclusive design.","zh":"Roger Coleman 是共融設計教授。"},{"en":"Inclusive design is design that considers many types of users, including older people and people with disabilities.","zh":"inclusive design 指考慮多種使用者，包括長者和殘疾人士的設計。"},{"en":"A lift with buttons, audio announcements, and Braille is an example of inclusive design.","zh":"有按鈕、語音提示和盲文的升降機是共融設計例子。"},{"en":"Inclusive design reduces exclusion because more people can use the product safely.","zh":"共融設計減少排除，因為更多人能安全使用產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing design for diverse users.","zh":"討論為多元使用者而設的設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"user-friendly","meaning":"易用；方便用家","examples":[{"en":"Good design should make products more user-friendly.","zh":"良好設計應令產品更易用。"},{"en":"User-friendly means easy for ordinary people to understand and use.","zh":"user-friendly 指普通人容易理解和使用。"},{"en":"A user-friendly website has clear buttons, simple language, and logical steps.","zh":"易用網站有清晰按鈕、簡單語言和合理步驟。"},{"en":"A product becomes more user-friendly when users can complete tasks without help.","zh":"當使用者不用協助也能完成任務，產品就更易用。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing practical ease of use.","zh":"討論實際易用性時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"as well as safer","meaning":"以及更安全","examples":[{"en":"Good design should make products more user-friendly as well as safer.","zh":"良好設計應令產品更易用以及更安全。"},{"en":"As well as safer means in addition to being safer.","zh":"as well as safer 指除了更安全之外，還有另一好處。"},{"en":"A school gate should be easier to open as well as safer during emergencies.","zh":"學校大門在緊急情況中應更容易打開，以及更安全。"},{"en":"Good solutions often improve convenience and safety at the same time.","zh":"好解決方案常同時改善便利性和安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when adding safety to another benefit.","zh":"在另一好處之外加入安全時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"patient-centred health system","meaning":"以病人為本的醫療系統","examples":[{"en":"A patient-centred health system should value good design.","zh":"以病人為本的醫療系統應重視良好設計。"},{"en":"A patient-centred health system is a healthcare system that focuses on patients’ needs, safety, comfort, and understanding.","zh":"patient-centred health system 指集中於病人需要、安全、舒適和理解的醫療系統。"},{"en":"A patient-centred clinic explains treatment choices in language patients can understand.","zh":"以病人為本的診所會用病人能理解的語言解釋治療選擇。"},{"en":"Patient-centred systems reduce harm because they consider real people, not only medical procedures.","zh":"以病人為本的系統減少傷害，因為它們考慮真實的人，而不只是醫療程序。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when healthcare is organised around patients.","zh":"當醫療圍繞病人組織時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"can only be a good thing","meaning":"只會是好事","examples":[{"en":"In a patient-centred health system, safer design can only be a good thing.","zh":"在以病人為本的醫療系統中，更安全的設計只會是好事。"},{"en":"Can only be a good thing means must be positive and unlikely to cause harm.","zh":"can only be a good thing 指必定正面且不太可能造成傷害。"},{"en":"Clearer school notices can only be a good thing for busy parents.","zh":"更清晰的學校通告對忙碌家長來說只會是好事。"},{"en":"When a change improves safety without reducing access, it is hard to oppose.","zh":"當改變改善安全而不降低可及性，就很難反對。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when strongly approving a positive change.","zh":"強烈認可正面改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"not intended to be mandatory","meaning":"並非旨在成為強制性規定","examples":[{"en":"Information Design for Patient Safety is not intended to be mandatory.","zh":"《病人安全資料設計》並非旨在成為強制性規定。"},{"en":"Not intended to be mandatory means not meant to be a compulsory rule.","zh":"not intended to be mandatory 指並非打算成為必須遵守的規則。"},{"en":"A school handbook may give advice that is not intended to be mandatory for every teacher.","zh":"學校手冊可能提供建議，但並非旨在對每位老師成為強制性規定。"},{"en":"Non-mandatory guidance can still influence behaviour if people respect it.","zh":"非強制性指引如果受人尊重，仍可影響行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when guidance is recommended but not legally required.","zh":"當指引被建議但非法律要求時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"rather","meaning":"而是","examples":[{"en":"Rather, its purpose is to create a basic design standard.","zh":"而是，它的目的是建立基本設計標準。"},{"en":"Rather means instead or more accurately, used to correct or clarify a previous idea.","zh":"rather 指而是或更準確地說，用來修正或澄清前一個想法。"},{"en":"This lesson is not about memorising rules; rather, it is about using grammar naturally.","zh":"這堂課不是關於背誦規則；而是關於自然使用文法。"},{"en":"The word helps writers replace one possible understanding with a better one.","zh":"這個詞幫助寫作者用更好理解取代一個可能理解。"},{"en":"This word is useful when correcting direction in an explanation.","zh":"在解釋中修正方向時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"its purpose is to","meaning":"其目的是","examples":[{"en":"Its purpose is to create a basic design standard and stimulate innovation.","zh":"其目的是建立基本設計標準並推動創新。"},{"en":"Its purpose is to means its main aim or function is to do something.","zh":"its purpose is to 指其主要目標或功能是做某事。"},{"en":"The purpose of a fire drill is to teach students how to leave safely.","zh":"火警演習的目的是教學生如何安全離開。"},{"en":"A clear purpose helps people judge whether a project has succeeded.","zh":"清晰目的幫助人們判斷項目是否成功。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why something exists.","zh":"解釋某物為何存在時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"basic design standard","meaning":"基本設計標準","examples":[{"en":"The book aims to create a basic design standard.","zh":"這本書旨在建立基本設計標準。"},{"en":"A basic design standard is a minimum level of design quality that products should meet.","zh":"basic design standard 指產品應達到的最低設計質素水平。"},{"en":"A school may set a basic design standard for notices so all parents can read them easily.","zh":"學校可能為通告設定基本設計標準，讓所有家長都容易閱讀。"},{"en":"Standards help prevent poor design by giving everyone a clear starting point.","zh":"標準透過給所有人清晰起點來幫助防止不良設計。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing minimum acceptable design quality.","zh":"討論最低可接受設計質素時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"stimulate innovation","meaning":"推動創新","examples":[{"en":"The design standard aims to stimulate innovation.","zh":"設計標準旨在推動創新。"},{"en":"Stimulate innovation means encourage people to create new and better ideas or products.","zh":"stimulate innovation 指鼓勵人創造新的和更好的想法或產品。"},{"en":"A science competition can stimulate innovation among students.","zh":"科學比賽可以推動學生創新。"},{"en":"Clear standards can stimulate innovation because designers know the basic safety level they must exceed.","zh":"清晰標準可以推動創新，因為設計師知道必須超越的基本安全水平。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when rules or challenges encourage creativity.","zh":"當規則或挑戰鼓勵創意時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the challenge for","meaning":"……面對的挑戰","examples":[{"en":"The challenge for the pharmaceutical industry is to adopt such a standard.","zh":"製藥業面對的挑戰是採納這類標準。"},{"en":"The challenge for someone is the difficult task or problem they must deal with.","zh":"the challenge for someone 指某人必須處理的困難任務或問題。"},{"en":"The challenge for new teachers is to manage the class while building trust.","zh":"新老師面對的挑戰是在建立信任的同時管理課堂。"},{"en":"A challenge becomes harder when it requires many people to change old habits.","zh":"當挑戰要求許多人改變舊習慣，它會更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying who must solve a difficult problem.","zh":"識別誰必須解決困難問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"as a whole","meaning":"整體而言","examples":[{"en":"The pharmaceutical industry as a whole needs to adopt better standards.","zh":"製藥業整體而言需要採納更好標準。"},{"en":"As a whole means considered as one complete group or system.","zh":"as a whole 指作為一個完整群體或系統來考慮。"},{"en":"A school as a whole improves when teachers, students, and parents work together.","zh":"當老師、學生和家長合作，學校整體而言會改善。"},{"en":"System-wide change matters when individual effort is not enough.","zh":"當個別努力不足夠，系統層面的改變就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing an entire group rather than one part.","zh":"討論整個群體而非其中一部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"adopt such a standard","meaning":"採納這類標準","examples":[{"en":"The pharmaceutical industry should adopt such a standard.","zh":"製藥業應採納這類標準。"},{"en":"Adopt such a standard means accept and start using that rule or level of quality.","zh":"adopt such a standard 指接受並開始使用該規則或質素水平。"},{"en":"A school may adopt a clear writing standard for all notices sent to parents.","zh":"學校可能採納清晰寫作標準，用於所有給家長的通告。"},{"en":"Standards only improve practice when organisations actually adopt them.","zh":"標準只有在機構真正採納時，才會改善實踐。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when moving from advice to real use.","zh":"從建議轉向實際使用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"look at the following statements","meaning":"查看以下陳述","examples":[{"en":"Students look at the following statements and match them with the correct source.","zh":"學生查看以下陳述，並將它們與正確來源配對。"},{"en":"Look at the following statements means read the sentences listed below carefully.","zh":"look at the following statements 指仔細閱讀下方列出的句子。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should look at the following statements before searching for evidence.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先查看以下陳述，再搜尋證據。"},{"en":"Careful reading of statements prevents students from matching only by keywords.","zh":"仔細閱讀陳述可以防止學生只憑關鍵詞配對。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於考試指示。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the list of people or organisations","meaning":"人物或機構列表","examples":[{"en":"The task gives a list of people or organisations.","zh":"任務給出人物或機構列表。"},{"en":"The list of people or organisations means the names that students must choose from in a matching task.","zh":"list of people or organisations 指學生在配對題中必須選擇的名稱。"},{"en":"A history worksheet may provide a list of people or organisations connected with a reform movement.","zh":"歷史工作紙可能提供與改革運動相關的人物或機構列表。"},{"en":"A clear list helps students know all possible answer choices.","zh":"清晰列表幫助學生知道所有可能答案選項。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in matching-question instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於配對題指示。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"match each statement with","meaning":"將每項陳述與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match each statement with the correct person or organisation.","zh":"學生將每項陳述與正確人物或機構配對。"},{"en":"Match each statement with means connect every sentence to the answer it belongs to.","zh":"match each statement with 指把每句話連接到其所屬答案。"},{"en":"Students may match each statement with the speaker who made that opinion in the passage.","zh":"學生可能將每項陳述與文章中提出該意見的說話者配對。"},{"en":"Good matching requires understanding meaning, not just spotting repeated words.","zh":"良好配對需要理解意思，而不只是找重複字眼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading-comprehension tasks.","zh":"這個短語適用於閱讀理解任務。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the correct person or organisation","meaning":"正確人物或機構","examples":[{"en":"Each statement should be matched with the correct person or organisation.","zh":"每項陳述應與正確人物或機構配對。"},{"en":"The correct person or organisation is the source that best matches the statement.","zh":"correct person or organisation 指最符合該陳述的來源。"},{"en":"If a doctor made a claim in the passage, that doctor is the correct person for the matching item.","zh":"如果一位醫生在文章中提出某聲稱，該醫生就是該配對項目的正確人物。"},{"en":"Students must check evidence carefully because several people may discuss similar topics.","zh":"學生必須仔細核對證據，因為幾個人可能討論相似主題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in source-matching exercises.","zh":"這個短語適用於來源配對練習。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"you may use any letter more than once","meaning":"可使用任何字母多於一次","examples":[{"en":"The instructions say that students may use any letter more than once.","zh":"指示說學生可使用任何字母多於一次。"},{"en":"You may use any letter more than once means the same answer option can be chosen for several questions.","zh":"you may use any letter more than once 指同一答案選項可被用於多條題目。"},{"en":"In a matching task, one paragraph letter may answer two different questions.","zh":"在配對題中，同一段落字母可能回答兩條不同問題。"},{"en":"This instruction prevents students from wrongly using each option only once.","zh":"這個指示防止學生錯誤地每個選項只用一次。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in exam tasks where answers can repeat.","zh":"這個短語適用於答案可以重複的考試任務。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"have the same difficulty as","meaning":"與……有同樣困難","examples":[{"en":"Elderly people may have the same difficulty as children when opening some containers.","zh":"長者打開某些容器時，可能與兒童有同樣困難。"},{"en":"Have the same difficulty as means experience a similar problem or level of struggle.","zh":"have the same difficulty as 指經歷相似問題或相同程度困難。"},{"en":"A new student may have the same difficulty as a younger child when using a complicated school app.","zh":"新學生使用複雜學校應用程式時，可能與較年幼孩子有同樣困難。"},{"en":"If two groups have the same difficulty, a solution should help both groups.","zh":"如果兩個群體有同樣困難，解決方案應幫助兩者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing user problems.","zh":"比較使用者問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"lids of containers","meaning":"容器蓋","examples":[{"en":"The lids of containers may require too much strength to open.","zh":"容器蓋可能需要太大力度才能打開。"},{"en":"Lids of containers are the covers on bottles, jars, boxes, or other containers.","zh":"lids of containers 指瓶、罐、盒或其他容器上的蓋子。"},{"en":"The lids of jam jars can be hard to open if they are sealed tightly.","zh":"如果果醬瓶密封很緊，容器蓋可能很難打開。"},{"en":"Lid design affects access because users must remove the lid before reaching the contents.","zh":"蓋子設計影響可及性，因為使用者必須先移除蓋子才能取得內容物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing packaging and accessibility.","zh":"討論包裝和可及性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"require too much strength to open","meaning":"需要太大力度才能打開","examples":[{"en":"Some lids require too much strength to open.","zh":"有些蓋子需要太大力度才能打開。"},{"en":"Require too much strength to open means need more physical force than many users can comfortably use.","zh":"require too much strength to open 指需要超過許多使用者能舒適使用的體力。"},{"en":"A water bottle may require too much strength to open for a child or elderly person.","zh":"一個水樽對兒童或長者來說，可能需要太大力度才能打開。"},{"en":"If packaging needs too much force, users may avoid the product or use unsafe tools.","zh":"如果包裝需要太大力度，使用者可能避用產品或使用不安全工具。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when physical effort becomes a barrier.","zh":"當體力要求成為障礙時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"adapting packaging for the blind","meaning":"為盲人改良包裝","examples":[{"en":"Adapting packaging for the blind may disadvantage sighted people.","zh":"為盲人改良包裝可能對視力正常人士不利。"},{"en":"Adapting packaging for the blind means changing packaging so blind users can identify or use it more easily.","zh":"adapting packaging for the blind 指改變包裝，令盲人使用者更容易識別或使用。"},{"en":"Adding Braille is one way of adapting packaging for the blind.","zh":"加入盲文是為盲人改良包裝的一種方法。"},{"en":"Accessibility changes should help blind users without reducing clarity for other users.","zh":"無障礙改變應幫助盲人使用者，而不降低其他使用者的清晰度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing inclusive packaging design.","zh":"討論共融包裝設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"disadvantage sighted people","meaning":"對視力正常人士不利","examples":[{"en":"Some design changes may disadvantage sighted people.","zh":"有些設計改變可能對視力正常人士不利。"},{"en":"Disadvantage sighted people means make something harder or less convenient for people who can see.","zh":"disadvantage sighted people 指令能看見的人使用時更困難或較不方便。"},{"en":"Raised marks on a label may disadvantage sighted people if they cover printed words.","zh":"如果標籤上的凸起標記遮住印刷文字，可能對視力正常人士不利。"},{"en":"Inclusive design should avoid solving one problem by creating another for a different group.","zh":"共融設計應避免透過解決一個問題而為另一群體創造新問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when accessibility changes must be balanced.","zh":"當無障礙改變需要平衡時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"specially designed lids","meaning":"特別設計的瓶蓋","examples":[{"en":"Specially designed lids cannot eliminate every risk.","zh":"特別設計的瓶蓋不能消除所有風險。"},{"en":"Specially designed lids are caps made for a specific safety or usability purpose.","zh":"specially designed lids 指為特定安全或易用目的製作的蓋子。"},{"en":"A medicine bottle may use specially designed lids that children find harder to open.","zh":"藥瓶可能使用令兒童較難打開的特別設計瓶蓋。"},{"en":"Special design can reduce danger, but it cannot replace careful storage.","zh":"特別設計可以降低危險，但不能取代小心存放。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing safety-focused container design.","zh":"討論以安全為重點的容器設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"eliminate the possibility of","meaning":"消除……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"Specially designed lids cannot eliminate the possibility of accidental poisoning.","zh":"特別設計的瓶蓋不能消除意外中毒的可能性。"},{"en":"Eliminate the possibility of means completely remove the chance of something happening.","zh":"eliminate the possibility of 指完全移除某事發生的機會。"},{"en":"Locking the cupboard reduces risk, but it may not eliminate the possibility of accidents.","zh":"鎖上櫃子會降低風險，但未必能消除意外的可能性。"},{"en":"Many safety designs reduce risk rather than remove it completely.","zh":"許多安全設計是降低風險，而不是完全消除風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing whether danger can be fully removed.","zh":"討論危險能否完全移除時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"swallowing pills accidentally","meaning":"意外吞下藥丸","examples":[{"en":"Children may still swallow pills accidentally.","zh":"兒童仍可能意外吞下藥丸。"},{"en":"Swallowing pills accidentally means taking tablets into the body by mistake, without intending to.","zh":"swallowing pills accidentally 指在無意中錯誤吞下藥片。"},{"en":"A child may swallow pills accidentally if they find tablets on a bedside table.","zh":"如果孩子在床頭櫃找到藥片，可能意外吞下藥丸。"},{"en":"Accidental swallowing can happen quickly, so storage and packaging both matter.","zh":"意外吞服可能很快發生，所以存放和包裝都很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing poisoning prevention.","zh":"討論中毒預防時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"container design","meaning":"容器設計","examples":[{"en":"Container design should consider how medicines are used at home.","zh":"容器設計應考慮藥物在家中如何使用。"},{"en":"Container design is the shape, lid, opening method, and usability of a container.","zh":"container design 指容器的形狀、蓋子、打開方法和易用性。"},{"en":"A shampoo bottle’s container design affects whether people can open it with wet hands.","zh":"洗頭水瓶的容器設計影響人能否用濕手打開它。"},{"en":"Good container design balances safety, convenience, strength, and accessibility.","zh":"良好容器設計平衡安全、便利、力度和可及性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how packages physically work.","zh":"討論包裝實際如何運作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"drug being used at home","meaning":"藥物在家中使用","examples":[{"en":"Packaging should consider a drug being used at home.","zh":"包裝應考慮藥物在家中使用的情況。"},{"en":"A drug being used at home means a medicine handled by patients or carers outside professional settings.","zh":"drug being used at home 指病人或照顧者在專業環境以外處理藥物。"},{"en":"A parent giving fever medicine at night is an example of a drug being used at home.","zh":"家長夜晚給孩子退燒藥，是藥物在家中使用的例子。"},{"en":"Home use creates risk because lighting, tiredness, and stress may affect reading.","zh":"家中使用會造成風險，因為光線、疲倦和壓力可能影響閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when medicine use happens outside hospitals or pharmacies.","zh":"當用藥發生在醫院或藥房以外時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"investigate multiple medicine containers together","meaning":"一併檢視多個藥物容器","examples":[{"en":"Authorities should investigate multiple medicine containers together.","zh":"監管機構應一併檢視多個藥物容器。"},{"en":"Investigate multiple medicine containers together means examine several packages at the same time to see whether they may be confused.","zh":"investigate multiple medicine containers together 指同時檢查幾個包裝，以了解它們是否可能被混淆。"},{"en":"A pharmacist may compare several medicine containers together before arranging shelves.","zh":"藥劑師在整理貨架前，可能一併比較多個藥物容器。"},{"en":"Looking at many containers together reveals look-alike risks that single-box review misses.","zh":"多個容器一起看，能揭示單盒審查錯過的外觀相似風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when package comparison affects safety.","zh":"當包裝比較影響安全時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"rather than individually","meaning":"而不是逐個地","examples":[{"en":"Packaging should be examined together rather than individually.","zh":"包裝應一併檢查，而不是逐個地檢查。"},{"en":"Rather than individually means instead of looking at each item separately.","zh":"rather than individually 指而不是分開查看每件物品。"},{"en":"Teachers may review common class mistakes together rather than individually when many students make the same error.","zh":"當許多學生犯同一錯誤，老師可能一起檢討全班常見錯誤，而不是逐個地處理。"},{"en":"Studying items together can reveal patterns that separate review hides.","zh":"一起研究物件可以揭示分開審查隱藏的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when group comparison is better than isolated checking.","zh":"當整體比較比分開檢查更好時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"appear in the most useful order","meaning":"以最有用的次序出現","examples":[{"en":"Information in a leaflet may not appear in the most useful order.","zh":"單張中的資料未必以最有用的次序出現。"},{"en":"Appear in the most useful order means be arranged so readers can find the most important information first.","zh":"appear in the most useful order 指以讓讀者最先找到最重要資訊的方式排列。"},{"en":"A school notice should put the date, time, and place in the most useful order.","zh":"學校通告應以最有用的次序放置日期、時間和地點。"},{"en":"Poor order makes readers work harder and may hide urgent warnings.","zh":"次序差劣會令讀者更費力，並可能隱藏緊急警告。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing information structure.","zh":"討論資訊結構時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"complete the notes","meaning":"完成筆記","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the notes using the list of words.","zh":"學生使用詞語列表完成筆記。"},{"en":"Complete the notes means fill missing words into a set of short organised points.","zh":"complete the notes 指把缺少的詞填入一組簡短、有組織的要點。"},{"en":"In a reading exercise, students complete the notes after finding exact words in the text.","zh":"在閱讀練習中，學生找到文本中的準確詞語後完成筆記。"},{"en":"Note completion checks whether students can identify key information quickly.","zh":"筆記填空檢查學生能否快速識別關鍵資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in IELTS-style reading instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於 IELTS 式閱讀指示。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"using the list of words","meaning":"使用詞語列表","examples":[{"en":"The notes should be completed using the list of words.","zh":"筆記應使用詞語列表完成。"},{"en":"Using the list of words means choosing answers only from the words provided.","zh":"using the list of words 指只從提供的詞語中選擇答案。"},{"en":"Students should not invent new answers if the task says using the list of words.","zh":"如果任務說使用詞語列表，學生不應自行創作新答案。"},{"en":"A word list limits choices and helps test exact understanding.","zh":"詞語列表限制選擇，並幫助測試準確理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in controlled completion tasks.","zh":"這個短語適用於受控填空任務。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"Packaging in the Pharmaceutical Industry","meaning":"製藥業中的包裝","examples":[{"en":"The notes summarise packaging in the pharmaceutical industry.","zh":"筆記概述製藥業中的包裝。"},{"en":"Packaging in the pharmaceutical industry refers to how medicines are contained, labelled, and presented.","zh":"packaging in the pharmaceutical industry 指藥物如何被盛載、標籤和呈現。"},{"en":"A training course may teach pharmacists about packaging in the pharmaceutical industry.","zh":"培訓課程可能教藥劑師了解製藥業中的包裝。"},{"en":"Safe packaging matters because drug packages guide both professionals and patients.","zh":"安全包裝很重要，因為藥物包裝指引專業人士和病人。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing medicine packaging as an industry issue.","zh":"把藥物包裝作為行業議題討論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"designs for over-the-counter medicines","meaning":"非處方藥的設計","examples":[{"en":"Designs for over-the-counter medicines are often created by external designers.","zh":"非處方藥的設計常由外部設計師創作。"},{"en":"Designs for over-the-counter medicines are the packaging and visual plans for medicines sold without prescription.","zh":"designs for over-the-counter medicines 指無需處方出售的藥物包裝和視覺方案。"},{"en":"A cold remedy box may need an attractive design because customers choose it from a shelf.","zh":"感冒藥盒可能需要吸引設計，因為顧客從貨架上選擇它。"},{"en":"These designs must balance marketing appeal with clear safety information.","zh":"這些設計必須平衡市場吸引力和清晰安全資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing consumer-facing medicine packaging.","zh":"討論面向消費者的藥物包裝時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"prepare the proposal","meaning":"準備提案","examples":[{"en":"Marketing teams prepare the proposal before designers begin their work.","zh":"市場推廣團隊在設計師開始工作前準備提案。"},{"en":"Prepare the proposal means write or organise the plan that explains what should be designed.","zh":"prepare the proposal 指撰寫或整理說明應設計甚麼的計劃。"},{"en":"A student team may prepare the proposal before asking teachers to approve an event.","zh":"學生團隊可能先準備提案，再請老師批准活動。"},{"en":"A good proposal gives the next group clear aims, limits, and expected results.","zh":"好提案為下一組人提供清晰目標、限制和預期結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when planning work before action begins.","zh":"在行動開始前規劃工作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"pass it to","meaning":"將其交給","examples":[{"en":"The proposal is passed to designers.","zh":"提案被交給設計師。"},{"en":"Pass it to means give or send something to another person or team.","zh":"pass it to 指把某物給予或傳送給另一人或團隊。"},{"en":"A teacher may pass a student’s question to the subject coordinator.","zh":"老師可能將學生問題交給科目統籌。"},{"en":"Work moves smoothly when information is passed to the right people at the right time.","zh":"當資訊在正確時間交給正確人員，工作會順暢推進。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when responsibility or information moves forward.","zh":"當責任或資訊向前移交時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be tested by","meaning":"由……測試","examples":[{"en":"Some designs are tested by consumers.","zh":"有些設計由消費者測試。"},{"en":"Be tested by means be tried or evaluated by a particular person or group.","zh":"be tested by 指由特定人士或群體試用或評估。"},{"en":"A new school lunch menu may be tested by students before it is adopted.","zh":"新學校午餐餐單在採用前可能由學生測試。"},{"en":"Testing by real users shows whether a design works outside the designer’s office.","zh":"由真實使用者測試能顯示設計在設計師辦公室外是否有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when users evaluate a product.","zh":"當使用者評估產品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"prescription-only medicines","meaning":"處方藥","examples":[{"en":"Prescription-only medicines usually have packaging designed in-house.","zh":"處方藥通常有由內部設計的包裝。"},{"en":"Prescription-only medicines are drugs that can be supplied only with a doctor’s prescription.","zh":"prescription-only medicines 指只能憑醫生處方供應的藥物。"},{"en":"Some heart medicines are prescription-only medicines because incorrect use may be dangerous.","zh":"有些心臟藥是處方藥，因為錯誤使用可能危險。"},{"en":"Their packaging must be reliable because patients may depend on them for serious conditions.","zh":"它們的包裝必須可靠，因為病人可能因嚴重疾病依賴它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing controlled medicines.","zh":"討論受管制藥物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be created by","meaning":"由……創作","examples":[{"en":"The design is created by an in-house team.","zh":"這個設計由內部團隊創作。"},{"en":"Be created by means be made, designed, or produced by someone.","zh":"be created by 指由某人製作、設計或生產。"},{"en":"A school website may be created by students in a technology club.","zh":"學校網站可能由科技學會學生創作。"},{"en":"Knowing who created a design can explain its style, limits, and assumptions.","zh":"知道誰創作設計，可以解釋其風格、限制和假設。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying the maker.","zh":"識別製作者時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生為每條題目選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choose the correct letter means select the letter that matches the right answer.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇與正確答案相配的字母。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice question, students may choose the correct letter after eliminating wrong options.","zh":"在多項選擇題中，學生可排除錯誤選項後選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Careful reading matters because one wrong letter can change the answer completely.","zh":"仔細閱讀很重要，因為一個錯字母可以完全改變答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於考試指示。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"design feature","meaning":"設計特點","examples":[{"en":"A design feature may cause an accident involving medicine containers.","zh":"某項設計特點可能造成涉及藥物容器的意外。"},{"en":"A design feature is one specific part or quality of a product’s design.","zh":"design feature 指產品設計中的一個特定部分或特質。"},{"en":"A bottle’s cap shape is a design feature that affects how easy it is to open.","zh":"瓶蓋形狀是一項影響打開難易度的設計特點。"},{"en":"A small design feature can create large safety risks if users misunderstand it.","zh":"如果使用者誤解，小設計特點可能造成巨大安全風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing details that affect product use.","zh":"討論影響產品使用的細節時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"cause an accident","meaning":"造成意外","examples":[{"en":"Poor typography can cause an accident involving medicine containers.","zh":"欠佳字體排印可能造成涉及藥物容器的意外。"},{"en":"Cause an accident means make an unexpected harmful event happen.","zh":"cause an accident 指令意外且有害的事件發生。"},{"en":"A loose cable across a classroom floor can cause an accident.","zh":"橫跨課室地板的鬆散電線可能造成意外。"},{"en":"Accidents often happen when design, behaviour, and pressure combine badly.","zh":"意外常在設計、行為和壓力不良結合時發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying what creates danger.","zh":"識別甚麼造成危險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"involving medicine containers","meaning":"涉及藥物容器","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about an accident involving medicine containers.","zh":"題目問一宗涉及藥物容器的意外。"},{"en":"Involving medicine containers means connected with bottles, boxes, blister packs, or other medicine packages.","zh":"involving medicine containers 指與瓶、盒、泡罩包裝或其他藥物包裝有關。"},{"en":"A mistake involving medicine containers may happen when two bottles look alike.","zh":"當兩個瓶子看起來相似，可能發生涉及藥物容器的錯誤。"},{"en":"Such accidents are serious because the container affects which medicine is chosen.","zh":"這類意外很嚴重，因為容器影響哪種藥物被選中。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the package itself is part of the problem.","zh":"當包裝本身是問題一部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"print error","meaning":"印刷錯誤","examples":[{"en":"A print error on medicine packaging can be dangerous.","zh":"藥物包裝上的印刷錯誤可能很危險。"},{"en":"A print error is a mistake in printed text, numbers, symbols, or layout.","zh":"print error 指印刷文字、數字、符號或版面上的錯誤。"},{"en":"A wrong date on a school notice is a print error that can confuse parents.","zh":"學校通告上的錯誤日期是一個會令家長混亂的印刷錯誤。"},{"en":"On medicine packaging, print errors may cause wrong dosage or wrong medicine use.","zh":"在藥物包裝上，印刷錯誤可能造成錯誤劑量或錯誤用藥。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when printed mistakes affect safety.","zh":"當印刷錯誤影響安全時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"style of print","meaning":"印刷字體風格","examples":[{"en":"The style of print may affect whether medicine information is read correctly.","zh":"印刷字體風格可能影響藥物資料是否被正確閱讀。"},{"en":"Style of print means the font, size, spacing, boldness, and layout of printed words.","zh":"style of print 指印刷文字的字體、大小、間距、粗幼和版面。"},{"en":"A form with a clear style of print is easier for parents to complete.","zh":"印刷字體風格清晰的表格較容易讓家長填寫。"},{"en":"If the print style is crowded or tiny, readers may miss key details.","zh":"如果印刷風格擁擠或細小，讀者可能錯過關鍵細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing typography and readability.","zh":"討論字體排印和易讀性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"wrong label","meaning":"錯誤標籤","examples":[{"en":"A wrong label can create a serious patient-safety risk.","zh":"錯誤標籤可能造成嚴重病人安全風險。"},{"en":"A wrong label is a label that gives incorrect information about a product.","zh":"wrong label 指提供產品錯誤資訊的標籤。"},{"en":"A food item with a wrong label may hide an ingredient that causes allergies.","zh":"有錯誤標籤的食品可能隱藏會引起過敏的成分。"},{"en":"On medicine, a wrong label can lead to wrong use, wrong dose, or wrong patient instructions.","zh":"在藥物上，錯誤標籤可能導致錯誤使用、錯誤劑量或錯誤病人指示。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when labelling mistakes create danger.","zh":"當標籤錯誤造成危險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"shape of the bottle","meaning":"瓶子的形狀","examples":[{"en":"The shape of the bottle may affect how easily a medicine is used.","zh":"瓶子的形狀可能影響藥物使用的難易度。"},{"en":"Shape of the bottle means the physical form of the bottle, including its size, grip, and neck.","zh":"shape of the bottle 指瓶子的實體形狀，包括大小、握持位置和瓶口。"},{"en":"A bottle with a narrow neck may be hard for elderly people to pour from.","zh":"瓶口狹窄的瓶子可能令長者難以倒出液體。"},{"en":"Bottle shape affects safety because it changes how users hold, open, and control the medicine.","zh":"瓶子形狀影響安全，因為它改變使用者如何握住、打開和控制藥物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing container design.","zh":"討論容器設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"one view of","meaning":"對……的一種看法","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about one view of black-and-white packaging.","zh":"題目問對黑白包裝的一種看法。"},{"en":"One view of something is one opinion or interpretation about it.","zh":"one view of something 指對某事的一種意見或詮釋。"},{"en":"One view of homework is that it builds discipline; another is that it creates stress.","zh":"對功課的一種看法是它建立自律；另一種是它造成壓力。"},{"en":"Showing one view helps students understand that an issue may have several sides.","zh":"展示一種看法幫助學生理解議題可能有幾個角度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing opinions in a text.","zh":"討論文本中的意見時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"black and white","meaning":"黑白","examples":[{"en":"Some people argue that packaging should be printed only in black and white.","zh":"有些人主張包裝應只以黑白印刷。"},{"en":"Black and white means using only black and white colours, without other colours.","zh":"black and white 指只使用黑色和白色，不使用其他顏色。"},{"en":"A black-and-white worksheet may be cheaper to print than a full-colour one.","zh":"黑白工作紙可能比全彩工作紙印刷成本更低。"},{"en":"Black and white can improve contrast, but it may make products harder to distinguish.","zh":"黑白可以改善對比度，但可能令產品更難區分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing simple visual design.","zh":"討論簡單視覺設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"pay more attention to","meaning":"更加留意","examples":[{"en":"Black-and-white packaging may make people pay more attention to the information.","zh":"黑白包裝可能令人更加留意資訊。"},{"en":"Pay more attention to means focus more carefully on something.","zh":"pay more attention to 指更仔細地集中於某事。"},{"en":"Students should pay more attention to articles when writing English sentences.","zh":"學生寫英文句子時應更加留意冠詞。"},{"en":"People may notice warnings better when there are fewer distracting design elements.","zh":"當干擾性的設計元素較少，人們可能更注意警告。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone needs to focus more carefully.","zh":"當某人需要更仔細集中時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"make all products look alike","meaning":"令所有產品看起來相似","examples":[{"en":"Using only black and white may make all products look alike.","zh":"只使用黑白可能令所有產品看起來相似。"},{"en":"Make all products look alike means cause different items to appear too similar.","zh":"make all products look alike 指令不同物品外觀看起來太相似。"},{"en":"If every school notice uses the same layout, it may make all notices look alike.","zh":"如果每張學校通告都使用同一版面，可能令所有通告看起來相似。"},{"en":"When products look alike, users must depend more on reading details.","zh":"當產品看起來相似，使用者必須更依賴閱讀細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when uniform design reduces distinguishability.","zh":"當統一設計降低可辨識度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"container design has made progress","meaning":"容器設計已有進展","examples":[{"en":"The examples show that container design has made some progress.","zh":"這些例子顯示容器設計已有一些進展。"},{"en":"Container design has made progress means the design of containers has improved over time.","zh":"container design has made progress 指容器設計隨時間已有改善。"},{"en":"Water bottles with easier caps show that container design has made progress for everyday users.","zh":"有更易開瓶蓋的水樽顯示容器設計已為日常使用者取得進展。"},{"en":"Progress happens when designers respond to real user difficulties.","zh":"當設計師回應真實使用者困難，進展就會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing improvement in packaging or product design.","zh":"討論包裝或產品設計改善時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"inappropriate design","meaning":"不合適的設計","examples":[{"en":"Inappropriate design can lead to accidents.","zh":"不合適的設計可能導致意外。"},{"en":"Inappropriate design means design that does not fit the user, purpose, or situation.","zh":"inappropriate design 指不適合使用者、目的或情況的設計。"},{"en":"A tiny font on a senior-centre notice is inappropriate design.","zh":"長者中心通告使用細小字體是不合適的設計。"},{"en":"Inappropriate design causes problems when real users cannot use a product safely or comfortably.","zh":"當真實使用者不能安全或舒適地使用產品，不合適設計就造成問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when design is unsuitable.","zh":"當設計不適合時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"lead to accidents","meaning":"導致意外","examples":[{"en":"Poor packaging can lead to accidents.","zh":"包裝不良可能導致意外。"},{"en":"Lead to accidents means cause or increase the chance of harmful unexpected events.","zh":"lead to accidents 指造成或增加有害意外事件發生的機會。"},{"en":"Loose floor mats can lead to accidents in a busy corridor.","zh":"鬆脫地墊可能在繁忙走廊導致意外。"},{"en":"In medicine, unclear packaging can lead to accidents because users may choose wrongly.","zh":"在藥物方面，不清晰包裝可能導致意外，因為使用者可能選錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining safety consequences.","zh":"解釋安全後果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"need further improvement","meaning":"仍需進一步改善","examples":[{"en":"The industry still needs further improvement in packaging design.","zh":"該行業在包裝設計上仍需進一步改善。"},{"en":"Need further improvement means still require more changes to become good enough.","zh":"need further improvement 指仍需要更多改變才能足夠好。"},{"en":"A student’s essay may need further improvement even after grammar mistakes are corrected.","zh":"即使文法錯誤已被糾正，學生文章可能仍需進一步改善。"},{"en":"Improvement is needed when existing solutions reduce problems but do not solve them fully.","zh":"當現有解決方案減少問題但未完全解決，仍需要改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when progress has begun but remains incomplete.","zh":"當進展已開始但仍未完成時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"be better informed","meaning":"獲得更充分資料","examples":[{"en":"Consumers should be better informed about medicine safety.","zh":"消費者應獲得關於藥物安全的更充分資料。"},{"en":"Be better informed means have clearer, fuller, and more useful information before making decisions.","zh":"be better informed 指在作決定前有更清楚、更完整和更有用的資訊。"},{"en":"Parents are better informed when school notices explain both the rule and the reason behind it.","zh":"當學校通告解釋規則及其原因，家長就獲得更充分資料。"},{"en":"Better-informed patients are more likely to use medicines correctly and ask useful questions.","zh":"獲得更充分資料的病人更可能正確用藥並提出有用問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when improved information leads to safer choices.","zh":"當改善資訊帶來更安全選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"SuperFast FlPassage 3 Flash Cards 48 - Improving Patient Safetyash Card Export System - Sheet1-10.pdf","sourcePage":24}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 49":[{"front":"theory or practice","meaning":"理論還是實踐","examples":[{"en":"The passage asks whether business-school research should focus on theory or practice.","zh":"文章探問商學院研究應專注於理論還是實踐。"},{"en":"Theory or practice means the choice between abstract ideas and real-world action.","zh":"Theory or practice 指在抽象理念與現實行動之間作選擇。"},{"en":"A student may prefer practice when learning speaking, because real conversations reveal problems quickly.","zh":"學生學習口語時可能較喜歡實踐，因為真實對話能快速暴露問題。"},{"en":"Too much theory without practice can leave learners unable to use what they know.","zh":"太多理論而沒有實踐，可能令學習者無法使用自己知道的知識。"},{"en":"Good education often connects theory with practice, so students understand ideas and apply them.","zh":"好教育通常把理論與實踐連接起來，讓學生理解概念並能應用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the point of","meaning":"……的目的；……的意義","examples":[{"en":"The title asks about the point of research carried out by business schools.","zh":"標題探問由商學院進行的研究有甚麼目的。"},{"en":"The point of something means its purpose, value, or reason for existing.","zh":"The point of something 指某事的目的、價值或存在理由。"},{"en":"A student may ask about the point of homework if it does not help them learn.","zh":"如果功課不能幫助學習，學生可能會問做功課有甚麼意義。"},{"en":"If an activity has no clear point, people may lose motivation to do it.","zh":"如果一項活動沒有清楚目的，人們可能失去做它的動力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when questioning whether something is meaningful or useful.","zh":"這個片語適用於質疑某事是否有意義或有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"research carried out by","meaning":"由……進行的研究","examples":[{"en":"The article discusses research carried out by business schools.","zh":"文章討論由商學院進行的研究。"},{"en":"Research carried out by someone means research done, organised, or completed by that person or organisation.","zh":"Research carried out by someone 指由某人或某機構進行、組織或完成的研究。"},{"en":"Research carried out by a hospital may help doctors improve patient care.","zh":"由醫院進行的研究可能幫助醫生改善病人護理。"},{"en":"If research carried out by schools has no practical effect, people may question its value.","zh":"如果由學校進行的研究沒有實際影響，人們可能質疑其價值。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who is responsible for doing the research.","zh":"這個片語指出誰負責進行該研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"business schools","meaning":"商學院","examples":[{"en":"Business schools are judged partly by the quality of their research.","zh":"商學院部分根據其研究質素來評定。"},{"en":"Business schools are university departments or institutions that teach management, finance, marketing, and related subjects.","zh":"Business schools 是教授管理、金融、市場學及相關科目的大學學系或機構。"},{"en":"A student may attend a business school to learn accounting, leadership, and business strategy.","zh":"學生可能入讀商學院，以學習會計、領導和商業策略。"},{"en":"If business schools focus only on publications, students may not receive enough career preparation.","zh":"如果商學院只專注於出版物，學生可能得不到足夠職業準備。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to institutions that train people for business and management careers.","zh":"這個片語指培訓人們投身商業和管理事業的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"academic institutions","meaning":"學術機構","examples":[{"en":"Students go to universities and other academic institutions to prepare for their future.","zh":"學生到大學和其他學術機構，為將來作準備。"},{"en":"Academic institutions are schools, colleges, and universities that focus on education and research.","zh":"Academic institutions 是專注於教育和研究的學校、學院和大學。"},{"en":"Libraries, lecture halls, laboratories, and classrooms are common parts of academic institutions.","zh":"圖書館、演講廳、實驗室和課室都是學術機構常見部分。"},{"en":"If academic institutions ignore workplace skills, graduates may struggle after leaving school.","zh":"如果學術機構忽視職場技能，畢業生離校後可能會吃力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organisations built around learning, teaching, and scholarship.","zh":"這個片語指圍繞學習、教學和學術研究建立的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"prepare for their future","meaning":"為將來作準備","examples":[{"en":"Students attend universities to prepare for their future.","zh":"學生入讀大學，為將來作準備。"},{"en":"To prepare for their future means to build the knowledge, habits, and skills needed for later life.","zh":"To prepare for their future 指建立日後生活所需的知識、習慣和技能。"},{"en":"Students prepare for their future by learning communication, problem-solving, and self-discipline.","zh":"學生透過學習溝通、解難和自律，為將來作準備。"},{"en":"Good preparation can make the move from school to work less frightening.","zh":"充分準備可以令由學校走向職場的過程較不令人害怕。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when education is linked to long-term life or career goals.","zh":"當教育與長遠人生或事業目標相連時，常會使用這個片語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pay tuition","meaning":"繳交學費","examples":[{"en":"Many students pay tuition in the hope of finding a good career.","zh":"許多學生繳交學費，希望找到好事業。"},{"en":"To pay tuition means to pay money for lessons, courses, or university study.","zh":"To pay tuition 指為課堂、課程或大學學習付款。"},{"en":"Parents may pay tuition for a language course if they believe it will help their child.","zh":"如果家長相信語言課程能幫助孩子，他們可能為其繳交學費。"},{"en":"When tuition is expensive, students expect the education to bring real benefits.","zh":"當學費昂貴，學生會期望教育帶來真實好處。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the financial cost of formal education.","zh":"這個片語集中於正規教育的金錢成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"struggle through classes","meaning":"艱難地完成課堂","examples":[{"en":"Students may struggle through classes before entering their careers.","zh":"學生可能在投身事業前艱難地完成課堂。"},{"en":"To struggle through classes means to complete lessons with difficulty, effort, or stress.","zh":"To struggle through classes 指困難、努力或有壓力地完成課堂。"},{"en":"A tired student may struggle through an evening class after a long day at work.","zh":"疲倦學生在長時間工作後，可能艱難地完成晚間課堂。"},{"en":"If lessons feel too theoretical, students may struggle through them without seeing the purpose.","zh":"如果課堂感覺太理論化，學生可能看不到目的，只是艱難地完成。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests continuing despite difficulty rather than learning easily.","zh":"這個片語暗示在困難中繼續，而不是輕鬆學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the hope that","meaning":"希望能夠","examples":[{"en":"Students study in the hope that they can find a fulfilling career.","zh":"學生讀書，希望能夠找到一份充實的事業。"},{"en":"In the hope that means because someone wants a particular result to happen.","zh":"In the hope that 指因為某人希望某個結果發生。"},{"en":"A family may save money in the hope that they can buy a flat later.","zh":"家庭可能儲錢，希望能夠日後買樓。"},{"en":"If people act in the hope of a better future, disappointment can be strong when results do not come.","zh":"如果人們為了更好將來而行動，但結果沒有出現，失望可能很強烈。"},{"en":"This phrase connects effort with an expected or desired outcome.","zh":"這個片語把努力與預期或渴望的結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a fulfilling and exciting career","meaning":"充實而令人興奮的事業","examples":[{"en":"Many students hope to find a fulfilling and exciting career.","zh":"許多學生希望找到一份充實而令人興奮的事業。"},{"en":"A fulfilling and exciting career is a job path that feels meaningful, rewarding, and interesting.","zh":"Fulfilling and exciting career 是令人覺得有意義、有回報且有趣的職業道路。"},{"en":"A nurse may find a fulfilling and exciting career in helping patients recover.","zh":"護士可能在幫助病人康復中找到充實而令人興奮的事業。"},{"en":"If a career is fulfilling but not exciting, a person may feel stable but not challenged.","zh":"如果事業充實但不令人興奮，人可能感到穩定但缺少挑戰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes work that gives both purpose and energy.","zh":"這個片語描述同時帶來目的感和活力的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"choice of university","meaning":"大學選擇","examples":[{"en":"Your choice of university can strongly affect your future.","zh":"你的大學選擇可以強烈影響你的將來。"},{"en":"Choice of university means the decision about which university to attend.","zh":"Choice of university 指選擇入讀哪一間大學的決定。"},{"en":"A student may consider teaching quality, location, fees, and career support when making a choice of university.","zh":"學生作出大學選擇時，可能考慮教學質素、地點、學費和就業支援。"},{"en":"A poor choice may lead to stress if the programme does not fit the student’s goals.","zh":"如果課程不符合學生目標，錯誤選擇可能帶來壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an education decision with long-term consequences.","zh":"這個片語描述具有長遠後果的教育決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have a major influence on","meaning":"對……有重大影響","examples":[{"en":"Your choice of university has a major influence on your future.","zh":"你的大學選擇對你的將來有重大影響。"},{"en":"To have a major influence on something means to affect it strongly.","zh":"To have a major influence on something 指強烈影響某事。"},{"en":"A teacher’s feedback can have a major influence on a student’s confidence.","zh":"老師的回饋可以對學生自信有重大影響。"},{"en":"If a university has strong career links, it may influence students’ job opportunities.","zh":"如果大學有強大職業聯繫，它可能影響學生的工作機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a powerful effect, not a small detail.","zh":"這個片語描述強大影響，而不是小細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"best prepare someone for","meaning":"最能幫助某人為……作準備","examples":[{"en":"Students want to know which university will best prepare them for their future.","zh":"學生想知道哪間大學最能幫助他們為將來作準備。"},{"en":"To best prepare someone for something means to give them the most useful training or support for it.","zh":"To best prepare someone for something 指給某人對某事最有用的訓練或支援。"},{"en":"Speaking practice can best prepare students for real interviews because they must answer immediately.","zh":"口語練習最能幫助學生為真實面試作準備，因為他們必須即時回答。"},{"en":"If a course includes workplace tasks, it may better prepare students for employment.","zh":"如果課程包括職場任務，它可能更能幫助學生為就業作準備。"},{"en":"This phrase compares which option gives the strongest preparation.","zh":"這個片語比較哪個選項提供最強準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be judged by","meaning":"根據……來評定","examples":[{"en":"Business schools are judged by the quality of their research.","zh":"商學院根據其研究質素來評定。"},{"en":"To be judged by something means to be evaluated according to that standard.","zh":"To be judged by something 指按照某標準被評估。"},{"en":"A restaurant may be judged by its food, service, cleanliness, and price.","zh":"餐廳可能根據食物、服務、清潔和價格來評定。"},{"en":"If schools are judged only by research, teaching quality may receive less attention.","zh":"如果學校只根據研究來評定，教學質素可能較少受到關注。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the standard used to assess someone or something.","zh":"這個片語顯示用來評估某人或某事的標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"quality of the research","meaning":"研究質素","examples":[{"en":"The quality of the research affects how business schools are judged.","zh":"研究質素影響商學院如何被評定。"},{"en":"Quality of the research means how reliable, original, useful, and well-supported the research is.","zh":"Quality of the research 指研究有多可靠、原創、有用和有充分支持。"},{"en":"A science project has better research quality when its data are accurate and clearly explained.","zh":"如果數據準確並清楚解釋，科學專題的研究質素會較好。"},{"en":"Poor research quality can damage a school’s reputation even if the topic sounds impressive.","zh":"即使題目聽起來令人印象深刻，差劣研究質素也會損害學校聲譽。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how good the research is, not just how much is produced.","zh":"這個片語集中於研究有多好，而不只是產出多少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"carried out by their faculties","meaning":"由其教職員進行的","examples":[{"en":"Business schools are judged by the research carried out by their faculties.","zh":"商學院根據由其教職員進行的研究來評定。"},{"en":"Carried out by their faculties means done by the professors, lecturers, and academic staff of the school.","zh":"Carried out by their faculties 指由該學院的教授、講師和學術人員進行。"},{"en":"A university may promote projects carried out by its faculties to show academic strength.","zh":"大學可能宣傳由其教職員進行的項目，以展示學術實力。"},{"en":"If faculty research is strong, the school’s reputation may improve.","zh":"如果教職員研究強，學校聲譽可能改善。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the academic staff as the people doing the research.","zh":"這個片語指出教職員是進行研究的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"both teach and produce","meaning":"既教學又產出","examples":[{"en":"Professors must both teach students and produce original research.","zh":"教授必須既教學生又產出原創研究。"},{"en":"Both teach and produce means doing two duties: educating students and creating academic work.","zh":"Both teach and produce 指履行兩項職責：教育學生和創造學術成果。"},{"en":"A professor may teach classes during term time and produce research during the summer.","zh":"教授可能在學期中教課，並在暑假產出研究。"},{"en":"If academics must do both, time pressure can affect teaching or research quality.","zh":"如果學者必須兩者兼顧，時間壓力可能影響教學或研究質素。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the double role expected of university staff.","zh":"這個片語突出大學員工被期望承擔的雙重角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"original research","meaning":"原創研究","examples":[{"en":"Professors are expected to produce original research in their own field.","zh":"教授被期望在自己的領域內產出原創研究。"},{"en":"Original research is new academic work that adds knowledge instead of simply repeating existing ideas.","zh":"Original research 是增加知識，而不是只是重複現有想法的新學術工作。"},{"en":"A student’s project may become original research if it collects new data from real interviews.","zh":"如果學生專題從真實訪談中收集新數據，它可能成為原創研究。"},{"en":"Original research can improve a university’s reputation when it answers important questions.","zh":"當原創研究回答重要問題，它可以改善大學聲譽。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research that contributes something new.","zh":"這個片語描述作出新貢獻的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in their own field","meaning":"在自己的領域內","examples":[{"en":"Professors produce original research in their own field.","zh":"教授在自己的領域內產出原創研究。"},{"en":"In their own field means within the subject or professional area they specialise in.","zh":"In their own field 指在他們專門研究的科目或專業範疇內。"},{"en":"A doctor may publish research in their own field of heart disease.","zh":"醫生可能在自己的心臟病領域內發表研究。"},{"en":"If people work outside their own field, they may need help from specialists.","zh":"如果人們在自己領域以外工作，他們可能需要專家協助。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the area where someone has expertise.","zh":"這個片語指出某人擁有專業知識的範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be assessed by","meaning":"由……評估","examples":[{"en":"The quality of research is assessed by academic publications.","zh":"研究質素由學術出版物評估。"},{"en":"To be assessed by something means to be evaluated using that measure or evidence.","zh":"To be assessed by something 指使用某標準或證據來評估。"},{"en":"A student’s speaking ability may be assessed by fluency, pronunciation, and accuracy.","zh":"學生口語能力可能由流暢度、發音和準確度評估。"},{"en":"If research is assessed mainly by publications, practical impact may be ignored.","zh":"如果研究主要由出版物評估，實際影響可能被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the method used to judge quality.","zh":"這個片語描述用來判斷質素的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"academic publications","meaning":"學術出版物","examples":[{"en":"Academic publications are often used to assess research quality.","zh":"學術出版物常被用來評估研究質素。"},{"en":"Academic publications are articles, papers, and books written for scholarly audiences.","zh":"Academic publications 是為學術讀者撰寫的文章、論文和書籍。"},{"en":"A professor may need academic publications to gain promotion at a university.","zh":"教授可能需要學術出版物來在大學獲得晉升。"},{"en":"If academic publications are too technical, managers may not read them.","zh":"如果學術出版物太技術化，管理人員可能不會閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal scholarly writing rather than general media articles.","zh":"這個片語指正式學術寫作，而不是一般媒體文章。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"同時","examples":[{"en":"At the same time, universities have another responsibility.","zh":"同時，大學有另一項責任。"},{"en":"At the same time introduces another point that exists together with the first point.","zh":"At the same time 用來引出與第一點同時存在的另一個重點。"},{"en":"A teacher must explain clearly; at the same time, students must practise actively.","zh":"老師必須清楚講解；同時，學生必須主動練習。"},{"en":"If universities do research and teach students, both duties matter.","zh":"如果大學既做研究又教學生，兩項責任都重要。"},{"en":"This phrase helps balance two ideas that are both true.","zh":"這個片語幫助平衡兩個同時成立的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have another responsibility","meaning":"有另一項責任","examples":[{"en":"Universities have another responsibility to prepare students for the real world.","zh":"大學有另一項責任，就是讓學生為現實世界作準備。"},{"en":"To have another responsibility means to have an additional duty beyond the one already mentioned.","zh":"To have another responsibility 指除了已提及的責任外，還有額外職責。"},{"en":"Parents feed their children, but they also have another responsibility to teach values.","zh":"父母養育孩子，但他們也有另一項責任，就是教導價值觀。"},{"en":"If universities only publish research, they may neglect their responsibility to students.","zh":"如果大學只發表研究，它們可能忽略對學生的責任。"},{"en":"This phrase adds a second duty to an organisation or person.","zh":"這個片語為組織或個人加入第二項職責。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"equip students for","meaning":"使學生具備應付……的能力","examples":[{"en":"Universities should equip students for the real world.","zh":"大學應使學生具備應付現實世界的能力。"},{"en":"To equip students for something means to give them the skills, knowledge, and confidence needed for it.","zh":"To equip students for something 指給學生應付某事所需的技能、知識和信心。"},{"en":"Interview practice can equip students for job applications.","zh":"面試練習可以使學生具備應付求職的能力。"},{"en":"If students are not equipped for work, they may feel lost after graduation.","zh":"如果學生沒有具備應付工作的能力，他們畢業後可能感到迷失。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical preparation, not only academic learning.","zh":"這個片語集中於實際準備，而不只是學術學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the real world","meaning":"現實世界","examples":[{"en":"Universities are expected to equip students for the real world.","zh":"大學被期望使學生具備應付現實世界的能力。"},{"en":"The real world means life outside school or theory, where people face practical problems and consequences.","zh":"The real world 指學校或理論以外的生活，人們在其中面對實際問題和後果。"},{"en":"In the real world, workers must meet deadlines, communicate clearly, and solve unexpected problems.","zh":"在現實世界中，員工必須趕及期限、清楚溝通並解決突發問題。"},{"en":"If education ignores the real world, students may know theories but not how to use them.","zh":"如果教育忽視現實世界，學生可能知道理論，卻不知道如何使用。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts practical life with classroom or academic settings.","zh":"這個片語把實際生活與課堂或學術環境作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"however that is defined","meaning":"無論如何界定","examples":[{"en":"Universities should prepare students for the real world, however that is defined.","zh":"大學應使學生為現實世界作準備，無論現實世界如何界定。"},{"en":"However that is defined means no matter how people choose to explain or describe that idea.","zh":"However that is defined 指不論人們如何解釋或描述那個概念。"},{"en":"Schools should support student well-being, however that is defined in different communities.","zh":"學校應支持學生福祉，無論不同社區如何界定福祉。"},{"en":"This phrase accepts that a term may be interpreted in more than one way.","zh":"這個片語承認某術語可能有多於一種解讀方式。"},{"en":"It is useful when the main point remains true despite different definitions.","zh":"當主要觀點在不同定義下仍然成立時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"go into academia","meaning":"進入學術界","examples":[{"en":"Most students will not go into academia themselves.","zh":"大多數學生自己不會進入學術界。"},{"en":"To go into academia means to build a career in university teaching, research, or scholarship.","zh":"To go into academia 指在大學教學、研究或學術方面發展事業。"},{"en":"A graduate may go into academia if they enjoy research and want to become a professor.","zh":"如果畢業生喜歡研究並想成為教授，他可能進入學術界。"},{"en":"If most students do not enter academia, business schools must prepare them for other careers too.","zh":"如果大多數學生不進入學術界，商學院也必須讓他們為其他事業作準備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes joining the academic world professionally.","zh":"這個片語描述專業上加入學術世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"future careers","meaning":"未來事業","examples":[{"en":"Universities should prepare students for their future careers.","zh":"大學應幫助學生為未來事業作準備。"},{"en":"Future careers are the jobs or professional paths students may enter later in life.","zh":"Future careers 是學生日後可能投身的工作或專業道路。"},{"en":"Internships can help students understand which future careers suit their strengths.","zh":"實習可以幫助學生理解哪些未來事業適合自己的強項。"},{"en":"If a course ignores future careers, students may graduate with knowledge but little direction.","zh":"如果課程忽視未來事業，學生可能畢業時有知識但缺少方向。"},{"en":"This phrase connects education with later working life.","zh":"這個片語把教育與日後工作生活連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"whatever they may be","meaning":"不論它們是甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Professors should prepare students for future careers, whatever they may be.","zh":"教授應幫助學生為未來事業作準備，不論它們是甚麼。"},{"en":"Whatever they may be means no matter what those careers turn out to be.","zh":"Whatever they may be 指不論那些事業最終是甚麼。"},{"en":"Schools should teach communication skills, whatever students’ future jobs may be.","zh":"學校應教授溝通技能，不論學生未來工作是甚麼。"},{"en":"If career paths are uncertain, broad skills become especially useful.","zh":"如果事業道路不確定，廣泛技能就特別有用。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the statement applies across many possible outcomes.","zh":"這個片語顯示該說法適用於許多可能結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"academic research","meaning":"學術研究","examples":[{"en":"The usefulness of academic research to business practice is debated.","zh":"學術研究對商業實務的實用性備受爭議。"},{"en":"Academic research is formal study carried out to create, test, or develop knowledge.","zh":"Academic research 是為創造、測試或發展知識而進行的正式研究。"},{"en":"Academic research may involve surveys, experiments, data analysis, or theoretical arguments.","zh":"學術研究可能涉及問卷、實驗、數據分析或理論論證。"},{"en":"If academic research is too distant from practice, professionals may ignore it.","zh":"如果學術研究離實踐太遠，專業人士可能忽視它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to research produced mainly within universities or scholarly settings.","zh":"這個片語指主要在大學或學術環境中產出的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"business practice","meaning":"商業實務","examples":[{"en":"Some people question whether academic research is useful to business practice.","zh":"有些人質疑學術研究是否對商業實務有用。"},{"en":"Business practice means the real actions, decisions, and methods used in companies and workplaces.","zh":"Business practice 指公司和職場中使用的真實行動、決策和方法。"},{"en":"A manager uses business practice when hiring staff, setting prices, or handling customers.","zh":"經理聘請員工、定價或處理顧客時，就是在運用商業實務。"},{"en":"If research improves business practice, companies may become more efficient or ethical.","zh":"如果研究改善商業實務，公司可能變得更有效率或更合乎道德。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts real workplace action with academic theory.","zh":"這個片語把真實職場行動與學術理論作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"provoke vigorous arguments","meaning":"引發激烈爭論","examples":[{"en":"Questions about research can provoke vigorous arguments on campus.","zh":"關於研究的問題可以在校園內引發激烈爭論。"},{"en":"To provoke vigorous arguments means to cause strong, energetic disagreement or debate.","zh":"To provoke vigorous arguments 指造成強烈而激烈的分歧或辯論。"},{"en":"A new homework policy may provoke vigorous arguments among parents and teachers.","zh":"新功課政策可能在家長和老師之間引發激烈爭論。"},{"en":"If a proposal threatens old habits, people may argue strongly about it.","zh":"如果建議威脅舊習慣，人們可能會強烈爭論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a topic that triggers intense debate.","zh":"這個片語描述會觸發激烈辯論的題目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on campus","meaning":"在校園內","examples":[{"en":"The debate has provoked vigorous arguments on campus.","zh":"這場辯論已在校園內引發激烈爭論。"},{"en":"On campus means within the university or school grounds and community.","zh":"On campus 指在大學或學校範圍及社群內。"},{"en":"Students may join clubs, attend lectures, and meet friends on campus.","zh":"學生可能在校園內參加學會、上講座和見朋友。"},{"en":"If a policy affects teaching and research, people on campus will discuss it seriously.","zh":"如果政策影響教學和研究，校園內的人會認真討論。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to life or events inside an educational institution.","zh":"這個片語指教育機構內的生活或事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the debate","meaning":"這場辯論","examples":[{"en":"The debate about business-school research first flared during the 1950s.","zh":"關於商學院研究的這場辯論在二十世紀五十年代首次爆發。"},{"en":"The debate means the ongoing discussion or disagreement about an issue.","zh":"The debate 指圍繞某議題持續進行的討論或分歧。"},{"en":"The debate over school uniforms often involves freedom, discipline, and identity.","zh":"關於校服的辯論常涉及自由、紀律和身份。"},{"en":"A debate can continue for years if both sides have strong reasons.","zh":"如果雙方都有強烈理由，一場辯論可以持續多年。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a contested topic, not a casual conversation.","zh":"這個片語指具爭議的題目，而不是隨意對話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"first flared","meaning":"首次爆發","examples":[{"en":"The debate first flared during the 1950s.","zh":"這場辯論在二十世紀五十年代首次爆發。"},{"en":"First flared means first became intense, visible, or heated.","zh":"First flared 指首次變得激烈、明顯或熾熱。"},{"en":"Public concern about school pressure first flared after several reports on student stress.","zh":"幾份學生壓力報告發表後，公眾對學校壓力的關注首次爆發。"},{"en":"When criticism suddenly becomes loud, a debate can flare quickly.","zh":"當批評突然變得響亮，辯論可以迅速爆發。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first strong outbreak of an argument or issue.","zh":"這個片語描述爭論或議題第一次強烈爆發。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be reignited","meaning":"被重新點燃","examples":[{"en":"The debate was reignited when AACSB considered changing its evaluation methods.","zh":"當 AACSB 考慮改變評估方法時，這場辯論被重新點燃。"},{"en":"To be reignited means to become active, heated, or controversial again after a quiet period.","zh":"To be reignited 指在沉寂一段時間後再次變得活躍、激烈或具爭議。"},{"en":"A school uniform debate may be reignited when a new principal changes the rules.","zh":"當新校長改變校服規則，校服辯論可能被重新點燃。"},{"en":"If an old issue returns with new evidence, public argument may start again.","zh":"如果舊議題帶着新證據回來，公眾爭論可能再次開始。"},{"en":"This phrase compares renewed debate to a fire being lit again.","zh":"這個片語把重新出現的辯論比作火再次被點燃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"AACSB International","meaning":"國際商學院促進協會","examples":[{"en":"AACSB International is a global accrediting agency for business schools.","zh":"AACSB International 是商學院的全球認證機構。"},{"en":"AACSB International is an organisation that evaluates and accredits business schools around the world.","zh":"AACSB International 是評估並認證世界各地商學院的組織。"},{"en":"A business school may seek AACSB accreditation to show that it meets recognised standards.","zh":"商學院可能尋求 AACSB 認證，以顯示自己符合受認可標準。"},{"en":"If AACSB changes its criteria, many business schools may need to adjust their priorities.","zh":"如果 AACSB 改變準則，許多商學院可能需要調整優先事項。"},{"en":"This phrase names an organisation with influence over business-school evaluation.","zh":"這個片語命名一個對商學院評估有影響力的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"widely recognised","meaning":"廣受認可的","examples":[{"en":"AACSB is the most widely recognised global accrediting agency for business schools.","zh":"AACSB 是最廣受認可的商學院全球認證機構。"},{"en":"Widely recognised means known, accepted, or respected by many people or organisations.","zh":"Widely recognised 指被許多人或機構知道、接受或尊重。"},{"en":"A widely recognised certificate can help a job applicant prove their skills.","zh":"廣受認可的證書可以幫助求職者證明技能。"},{"en":"If an agency is widely recognised, schools may care greatly about its judgement.","zh":"如果一個機構廣受認可，學校可能非常重視它的評審。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad acceptance and reputation.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛接受和聲譽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"global accrediting agency","meaning":"全球認證機構","examples":[{"en":"AACSB is a global accrediting agency for business schools.","zh":"AACSB 是商學院的全球認證機構。"},{"en":"A global accrediting agency is an international organisation that checks whether schools meet certain standards.","zh":"Global accrediting agency 是檢查學校是否符合某些標準的國際組織。"},{"en":"A university may use approval from a global accrediting agency to attract overseas students.","zh":"大學可能使用全球認證機構的認可來吸引海外學生。"},{"en":"Accreditation can affect reputation, partnerships, and student confidence.","zh":"認證可以影響聲譽、合作和學生信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an organisation that evaluates institutions across countries.","zh":"這個片語描述跨國評估機構的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"consider changing","meaning":"考慮改變","examples":[{"en":"AACSB announced that it would consider changing the way it evaluates research.","zh":"AACSB 宣布會考慮改變其評估研究的方式。"},{"en":"To consider changing something means to think seriously about altering it.","zh":"To consider changing something 指認真思考是否改動某事。"},{"en":"A school may consider changing its timetable if students are always exhausted.","zh":"如果學生總是筋疲力盡，學校可能考慮改變時間表。"},{"en":"If an old system no longer works well, leaders may consider changing it.","zh":"如果舊制度不再有效，領導者可能考慮改變它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful thought before making a possible change.","zh":"這個片語描述在可能作出改變前的慎重思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"evaluate research","meaning":"評估研究","examples":[{"en":"AACSB considered changing how it evaluates research.","zh":"AACSB 考慮改變其評估研究的方式。"},{"en":"To evaluate research means to judge its quality, value, impact, or usefulness.","zh":"To evaluate research 指判斷研究的質素、價值、影響或實用性。"},{"en":"Teachers evaluate student research by checking evidence, reasoning, and clarity.","zh":"老師透過檢查證據、推理和清晰度來評估學生研究。"},{"en":"If evaluators include practical impact, schools may change the kind of research they reward.","zh":"如果評估者納入實際影響，學校可能改變自己獎勵的研究類型。"},{"en":"This phrase describes judging research by selected standards.","zh":"這個片語描述按所選標準判斷研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the news followed","meaning":"這消息是在……之後出現","examples":[{"en":"The news followed criticism in a 2002 study.","zh":"這消息是在一項二零零二年研究的批評之後出現。"},{"en":"The news followed means the news came after and was connected to an earlier event or comment.","zh":"The news followed 指消息在較早事件或評論之後出現，並與其有關。"},{"en":"The school’s new policy followed complaints from parents about heavy homework.","zh":"學校的新政策是在家長投訴功課繁重之後出現。"},{"en":"If news follows criticism, the criticism may have influenced the decision.","zh":"如果消息在批評後出現，該批評可能影響了決定。"},{"en":"This phrase shows sequence and possible connection between events.","zh":"這個片語顯示事件之間的先後次序和可能關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"damning criticism","meaning":"嚴厲批評","examples":[{"en":"The news followed rather damning criticism of business education.","zh":"這消息是在對商業教育相當嚴厲的批評之後出現。"},{"en":"Damning criticism is very strong criticism that seriously damages the reputation of something.","zh":"Damning criticism 是非常強烈、會嚴重損害某事聲譽的批評。"},{"en":"A restaurant may face damning criticism if inspectors find serious hygiene problems.","zh":"如果檢查員發現嚴重衛生問題，餐廳可能面對嚴厲批評。"},{"en":"If criticism is damning, leaders may be forced to defend or reform the system.","zh":"如果批評嚴厲，領導者可能被迫捍衛或改革制度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes criticism that is severe, not mild.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重批評，而不是溫和意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"question whether","meaning":"質疑是否","examples":[{"en":"The study questioned whether business education was sustainable.","zh":"該研究質疑商業教育是否可持續。"},{"en":"To question whether something is true means to doubt it and ask for evidence.","zh":"To question whether something is true 指懷疑某事是否真實並要求證據。"},{"en":"Parents may question whether expensive tutoring really improves confidence.","zh":"家長可能質疑昂貴補習是否真的提升信心。"},{"en":"If people question whether a system works, leaders may need to justify it.","zh":"如果人們質疑制度是否有效，領導者可能需要為其辯護。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces doubt about a claim or arrangement.","zh":"這個片語引出對某主張或安排的懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"business education","meaning":"商業教育","examples":[{"en":"The study criticised business education in its current form.","zh":"該研究批評目前形式的商業教育。"},{"en":"Business education means teaching people knowledge and skills for business, management, and professional work.","zh":"Business education 指教授人們商業、管理和專業工作所需的知識和技能。"},{"en":"Business education may include finance, marketing, leadership, ethics, and communication.","zh":"商業教育可能包括金融、市場學、領導、倫理和溝通。"},{"en":"If business education is too theoretical, graduates may not know how to handle real clients.","zh":"如果商業教育太理論化，畢業生可能不知道如何處理真實客戶。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to training designed for business-related careers.","zh":"這個片語指為商業相關事業而設的培訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in its current guise","meaning":"以目前的形式","examples":[{"en":"The study questioned whether business education in its current guise was sustainable.","zh":"該研究質疑商業教育以目前的形式是否可持續。"},{"en":"In its current guise means in the form or version it has at present.","zh":"In its current guise 指以現在所具有的形式或版本。"},{"en":"Online learning, in its current guise, may help revision but cannot replace all face-to-face practice.","zh":"網上學習以目前的形式，可能有助溫習，但不能取代所有面對面練習。"},{"en":"If a system in its current guise fails students, reform may be necessary.","zh":"如果一個制度以目前形式未能幫到學生，改革可能有必要。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the present form, not the whole idea forever.","zh":"這個片語集中於目前形式，而不是永遠否定整個理念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be sustainable","meaning":"可持續的","examples":[{"en":"The study questioned whether current business education was sustainable.","zh":"該研究質疑目前商業教育是否可持續。"},{"en":"To be sustainable means to be able to continue successfully over time without serious damage or failure.","zh":"To be sustainable 指能長期成功持續，而不造成嚴重損害或失敗。"},{"en":"A student’s study plan is sustainable if it allows enough sleep and regular practice.","zh":"如果學生的學習計劃容許足夠睡眠和定期練習，它就是可持續的。"},{"en":"If a school model costs too much and helps too few students, it may not be sustainable.","zh":"如果學校模式成本太高而幫到太少學生，它可能不可持續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-term workability.","zh":"這個片語描述長遠可運作性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"traditional academic models","meaning":"傳統學術模式","examples":[{"en":"Traditional academic models may not prepare students adequately.","zh":"傳統學術模式可能未能充分幫助學生作準備。"},{"en":"Traditional academic models are older university systems that emphasise lectures, theory, research, and publications.","zh":"Traditional academic models 是強調講課、理論、研究和出版物的較舊大學制度。"},{"en":"A traditional academic model may reward professors mainly for journal articles.","zh":"傳統學術模式可能主要以期刊文章獎勵教授。"},{"en":"If careers change quickly, traditional academic models may need practical updates.","zh":"如果職業快速變化，傳統學術模式可能需要實務更新。"},{"en":"This phrase describes established educational structures rather than new professional approaches.","zh":"這個片語描述既有教育架構，而不是新的專業取向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"adequately prepare students for","meaning":"充分幫助學生為……作準備","examples":[{"en":"Traditional academic models were not adequately preparing students for modern careers.","zh":"傳統學術模式未能充分幫助學生為現代事業作準備。"},{"en":"To adequately prepare students for something means to give them enough training, knowledge, and experience for it.","zh":"To adequately prepare students for something 指給學生足夠訓練、知識和經驗去應付某事。"},{"en":"Mock interviews can adequately prepare students for real job interviews if feedback is honest.","zh":"如果回饋誠實，模擬面試可以充分幫助學生為真實求職面試作準備。"},{"en":"If students lack practical skills, they may not be adequately prepared for work.","zh":"如果學生缺乏實用技能，他們可能未能充分準備好工作。"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether preparation is sufficient, not perfect.","zh":"這個片語問準備是否足夠，而不是是否完美。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the kinds of careers","meaning":"各類事業","examples":[{"en":"Students now face different kinds of careers.","zh":"學生如今面對不同類型的事業。"},{"en":"The kinds of careers means the types of jobs or professional paths people may enter.","zh":"The kinds of careers 指人們可能進入的工作類型或專業道路。"},{"en":"Today’s students may consider careers in finance, technology, healthcare, education, or media.","zh":"今天的學生可能考慮金融、科技、醫療、教育或媒體方面的事業。"},{"en":"If careers become more varied, one narrow education model may not fit everyone.","zh":"如果事業變得更多樣化，單一狹窄教育模式可能不適合所有人。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the range of possible working lives.","zh":"這個片語集中於可能工作人生的範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"face today","meaning":"現今面對","examples":[{"en":"The careers students face today are different from those in the past.","zh":"學生現今面對的事業不同於過去。"},{"en":"Face today means deal with or encounter in the present time.","zh":"Face today 指在現在處理或遇到。"},{"en":"The problems families face today may include high rents and long working hours.","zh":"家庭現今面對的問題可能包括高租金和長工時。"},{"en":"If students face new career demands today, universities must update their teaching.","zh":"如果學生現今面對新的職業要求，大學必須更新教學。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a challenge with the current situation.","zh":"這個片語把挑戰與目前情況連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"controversial recommendation","meaning":"具爭議性的建議","examples":[{"en":"The most controversial recommendation concerned how schools demonstrate research value.","zh":"最具爭議性的建議涉及學校如何展示研究價值。"},{"en":"A controversial recommendation is a suggestion that many people disagree about strongly.","zh":"Controversial recommendation 是許多人強烈不同意或爭論的建議。"},{"en":"A proposal to replace exams with interviews may be a controversial recommendation in a school.","zh":"用面試取代考試的提議，在學校可能是具爭議性的建議。"},{"en":"If a recommendation affects money, status, or jobs, it may become controversial quickly.","zh":"如果建議影響金錢、地位或工作，它可能很快變得具爭議性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes advice that triggers disagreement.","zh":"這個片語描述會引發分歧的建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"draft report","meaning":"報告草稿","examples":[{"en":"The recommendation appeared in AACSB’s draft report.","zh":"該建議出現在 AACSB 的報告草稿中。"},{"en":"A draft report is an unfinished version of a report shared for checking, comment, or revision.","zh":"Draft report 是尚未完成、用作檢查、徵詢意見或修改的報告版本。"},{"en":"A student may send a draft report to a teacher before submitting the final version.","zh":"學生可能在提交最終版本前，把報告草稿交給老師。"},{"en":"If a draft report receives strong criticism, its final version may be changed.","zh":"如果報告草稿受到強烈批評，其最終版本可能被改動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a report that is not yet final.","zh":"這個片語指尚未定稿的報告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"send something round to","meaning":"將……傳閱給","examples":[{"en":"The draft report was sent round to administrators for comment.","zh":"報告草稿被傳閱給行政人員徵詢意見。"},{"en":"To send something round to people means to circulate it so several people can read or respond to it.","zh":"To send something round to people 指傳閱某物，讓幾個人閱讀或回應。"},{"en":"A teacher may send a timetable round to colleagues before confirming it.","zh":"老師可能在確認時間表前，把它傳閱給同事。"},{"en":"If a proposal is sent round, the writer can collect feedback before making a final decision.","zh":"如果提案被傳閱，撰寫者可以在作最終決定前收集回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sharing a document with a group for review.","zh":"這個片語描述把文件分享給一群人審閱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"administrators","meaning":"行政人員","examples":[{"en":"The draft report was sent to administrators for comment.","zh":"報告草稿被傳送給行政人員徵詢意見。"},{"en":"Administrators are people who manage the practical operation of an organisation.","zh":"Administrators 是管理組織實際運作的人。"},{"en":"School administrators may handle admissions, budgets, timetables, and staff records.","zh":"學校行政人員可能處理收生、預算、時間表和員工紀錄。"},{"en":"If administrators support a policy, it may be easier to put into practice.","zh":"如果行政人員支持某政策，它可能較容易落實。"},{"en":"This word refers to people who manage systems rather than teach classes directly.","zh":"這個詞指管理制度的人，而不是直接教課的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for comment","meaning":"徵詢意見","examples":[{"en":"The draft report was circulated for comment.","zh":"報告草稿被傳閱以徵詢意見。"},{"en":"For comment means so that people can give opinions, criticism, or suggestions.","zh":"For comment 指讓人們提供意見、批評或建議。"},{"en":"A class proposal may be sent to students for comment before the teacher finalises it.","zh":"班級建議可能在老師定稿前先傳給學生徵詢意見。"},{"en":"Asking for comment can reveal problems before a decision becomes official.","zh":"徵詢意見可以在決定正式落實前揭示問題。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a draft is shared.","zh":"這個片語解釋草稿為何被分享。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be required to demonstrate","meaning":"被要求證明","examples":[{"en":"Schools should be required to demonstrate the value of their research.","zh":"學校應被要求證明其研究的價值。"},{"en":"To be required to demonstrate something means to be formally asked to show proof of it.","zh":"To be required to demonstrate something 指被正式要求展示某事的證據。"},{"en":"Students may be required to demonstrate their speaking ability in a presentation.","zh":"學生可能被要求在匯報中證明自己的口語能力。"},{"en":"If schools must demonstrate impact, they need evidence beyond publication lists.","zh":"如果學校必須證明影響，它們需要出版清單以外的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an obligation to prove something clearly.","zh":"這個片語描述清楚證明某事的義務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the value of","meaning":"……的價值","examples":[{"en":"Schools should demonstrate the value of their faculties’ research.","zh":"學校應展示其教職員研究的價值。"},{"en":"The value of something means its importance, usefulness, or benefit.","zh":"The value of something 指某事的重要性、實用性或好處。"},{"en":"A student may understand the value of grammar when writing becomes clearer.","zh":"當寫作變得更清楚，學生可能理解文法的價值。"},{"en":"If research helps companies make better decisions, its value becomes easier to see.","zh":"如果研究幫助公司作出更好決定，其價值就更容易看見。"},{"en":"This phrase asks what good something actually does.","zh":"這個片語詢問某事實際上有甚麼好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"faculties’ research","meaning":"教職員的研究","examples":[{"en":"AACSB wanted schools to demonstrate the value of their faculties’ research.","zh":"AACSB 希望學校展示其教職員研究的價值。"},{"en":"Faculties’ research means research produced by the teaching and academic staff of a school or university.","zh":"Faculties’ research 指由學校或大學的教學及學術人員產出的研究。"},{"en":"A university may showcase its faculties’ research during an open day.","zh":"大學可能在開放日展示其教職員的研究。"},{"en":"If faculties’ research does not reach students or professionals, its public value may be questioned.","zh":"如果教職員的研究沒有接觸學生或專業人士，其公共價值可能被質疑。"},{"en":"This phrase links research output to the people employed by the institution.","zh":"這個片語把研究產出與機構聘用的人連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not simply by","meaning":"不只是透過","examples":[{"en":"Research value should be shown not simply by listing journal citations.","zh":"研究價值不應只是透過列出期刊引用次數來展示。"},{"en":"Not simply by means not only through one method or measure.","zh":"Not simply by 指不只是透過一種方法或標準。"},{"en":"A student’s ability should be judged not simply by exam marks but also by effort and progress.","zh":"學生能力不應只是透過考試分數來評定，也應看努力和進步。"},{"en":"If value is shown only by citations, practical benefits may be missed.","zh":"如果價值只由引用次數展示，實際好處可能被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast between a narrow measure and a broader view.","zh":"這個片語引出狹窄標準與更廣闊看法之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"list citations in journals","meaning":"列出期刊引用次數","examples":[{"en":"Schools traditionally list citations in journals to show research value.","zh":"學校傳統上列出期刊引用次數來展示研究價值。"},{"en":"To list citations in journals means to count or show how often research is referred to in academic publications.","zh":"To list citations in journals 指計算或展示研究在學術出版物中被引用的次數。"},{"en":"A professor may list citations in journals to prove that other scholars read their work.","zh":"教授可能列出期刊引用次數，以證明其他學者閱讀其作品。"},{"en":"If schools rely only on citations, they may reward research that professionals never use.","zh":"如果學校只依賴引用次數，它們可能獎勵專業人士從不使用的研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an academic way of measuring influence.","zh":"這個片語描述一種衡量影響力的學術方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"demonstrate the impact","meaning":"展示影響","examples":[{"en":"Schools should demonstrate the impact of their research.","zh":"學校應展示其研究的影響。"},{"en":"To demonstrate the impact means to show clearly what effects or results something has produced.","zh":"To demonstrate the impact 指清楚顯示某事產生了甚麼效果或結果。"},{"en":"A charity may demonstrate the impact of donations by showing how many meals were provided.","zh":"慈善機構可能透過展示提供了多少餐食來展示捐款影響。"},{"en":"If research changes business practice, schools can use that evidence to demonstrate impact.","zh":"如果研究改變商業實務，學校可以用該證據展示影響。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on proving real-world effects.","zh":"這個片語集中於證明現實效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the professional world","meaning":"專業世界；職場世界","examples":[{"en":"AACSB wanted schools to show research impact in the professional world.","zh":"AACSB 希望學校展示研究在專業世界中的影響。"},{"en":"The professional world means workplaces and industries where people apply skills in real jobs.","zh":"The professional world 指人們在真實工作中應用技能的職場和行業。"},{"en":"In the professional world, clear communication can matter as much as technical knowledge.","zh":"在專業世界中，清晰溝通可能與技術知識同樣重要。"},{"en":"If research reaches the professional world, managers and workers may use it in decisions.","zh":"如果研究進入專業世界，管理人員和員工可能在決策中使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts practical careers with purely academic settings.","zh":"這個片語把實際事業與純學術環境作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"new criteria","meaning":"新準則","examples":[{"en":"New criteria would be considered alongside academic publications.","zh":"新準則將與學術出版物一同被考慮。"},{"en":"New criteria are new standards used to judge, compare, or evaluate something.","zh":"New criteria 是用來判斷、比較或評估某事的新標準。"},{"en":"A school may introduce new criteria for awards, such as teamwork and improvement.","zh":"學校可能為獎項引入新準則，例如團隊合作和進步。"},{"en":"If evaluation criteria change, people often change their behaviour to match them.","zh":"如果評估準則改變，人們通常會改變行為來配合。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fresh measures used in assessment.","zh":"這個片語描述評估中使用的新衡量標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"average incomes","meaning":"平均收入","examples":[{"en":"Average incomes could become a criterion for evaluating business schools.","zh":"平均收入可以成為評估商學院的準則。"},{"en":"Average incomes are the typical earnings of a group, calculated by considering many people’s pay.","zh":"Average incomes 是考慮許多人薪酬後計算出的某群體典型收入。"},{"en":"A university may study graduates’ average incomes to understand employment outcomes.","zh":"大學可能研究畢業生平均收入，以了解就業成果。"},{"en":"If average incomes are high, a school may claim that its graduates do well in the job market.","zh":"如果平均收入高，學校可能聲稱其畢業生在就業市場表現良好。"},{"en":"This phrase measures financial outcomes across a group.","zh":"這個片語衡量某群體的財務成果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"student placement","meaning":"學生就業安排","examples":[{"en":"Student placement in top firms could be used to evaluate business schools.","zh":"學生在頂尖公司的就業安排可以用來評估商學院。"},{"en":"Student placement means helping or tracking where students get jobs, internships, or professional positions.","zh":"Student placement 指幫助或追蹤學生在哪裏獲得工作、實習或專業職位。"},{"en":"A strong career office can improve student placement by connecting students with employers.","zh":"強大的就業辦公室可以透過連繫學生和僱主來改善學生就業安排。"},{"en":"If student placement is poor, graduates may struggle even after expensive study.","zh":"如果學生就業安排差，畢業生即使完成昂貴學習後也可能吃力。"},{"en":"This phrase connects education with employment results.","zh":"這個片語把教育與就業成果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"top firms","meaning":"頂尖公司","examples":[{"en":"AACSB considered student placement in top firms as a criterion.","zh":"AACSB 考慮把學生在頂尖公司的就業安排作為準則。"},{"en":"Top firms are leading companies with strong reputations, resources, and career opportunities.","zh":"Top firms 是有強大聲譽、資源和事業機會的領先公司。"},{"en":"Many business students want internships at top firms because they can learn from experienced teams.","zh":"許多商科學生想在頂尖公司實習，因為可以向有經驗團隊學習。"},{"en":"If many graduates enter top firms, a school may appear more successful professionally.","zh":"如果許多畢業生進入頂尖公司，學校在專業成果上可能顯得更成功。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to highly respected companies in an industry.","zh":"這個片語指行業中備受尊重的公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"business collaborations","meaning":"商業合作","examples":[{"en":"Business collaborations could become part of school evaluation.","zh":"商業合作可以成為學校評估的一部分。"},{"en":"Business collaborations are partnerships between schools and companies for projects, research, training, or internships.","zh":"Business collaborations 是學校與公司在項目、研究、培訓或實習方面的合作。"},{"en":"A university may build business collaborations so students can solve real company problems.","zh":"大學可能建立商業合作，讓學生解決真實公司問題。"},{"en":"If schools collaborate with firms, students may gain more practical experience.","zh":"如果學校與企業合作，學生可能獲得更多實際經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cooperation between education and industry.","zh":"這個片語描述教育與行業之間的合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"just as important as","meaning":"與……同樣重要","examples":[{"en":"Professional outcomes may become just as important as academic publications.","zh":"專業成果可能變得與學術出版物同樣重要。"},{"en":"Just as important as means equal in importance to another thing.","zh":"Just as important as 指與另一事物同等重要。"},{"en":"Clear speaking can be just as important as grammar in a job interview.","zh":"在求職面試中，清晰說話可以與文法同樣重要。"},{"en":"If career results are just as important as research papers, schools must balance both.","zh":"如果就業成果與研究論文同樣重要，學校就必須平衡兩者。"},{"en":"This phrase shows equal value between two things.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩件事具有同等價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"justify its stance","meaning":"為其立場辯護","examples":[{"en":"AACSB justifies its stance by referring to schools’ different strengths.","zh":"AACSB 透過提及學校不同強項，為其立場辯護。"},{"en":"To justify its stance means to explain why its position is reasonable or right.","zh":"To justify its stance 指解釋其立場為何合理或正確。"},{"en":"A school may justify its stance on homework by showing evidence that practice improves learning.","zh":"學校可能透過展示練習改善學習的證據，為其功課立場辯護。"},{"en":"If a proposal is controversial, the organisation behind it must justify its position clearly.","zh":"如果提案具爭議，背後組織必須清楚為其立場辯護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes defending a viewpoint with reasons.","zh":"這個片語描述用理由捍衛觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"play to their strengths","meaning":"發揮自己的強項","examples":[{"en":"AACSB wants schools and faculty to play to their strengths.","zh":"AACSB 希望學校和教職員發揮自己的強項。"},{"en":"To play to their strengths means to focus on what they do best.","zh":"To play to their strengths 指專注於自己最擅長的事情。"},{"en":"A shy student may play to their strengths by writing a strong script before speaking.","zh":"害羞學生可能先寫好強而有力的稿件，以發揮自己的強項。"},{"en":"If a school is excellent at practical training, it may focus on professional outcomes.","zh":"如果學校在實務培訓方面優秀，它可能專注於專業成果。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests using existing advantages wisely.","zh":"這個片語建議明智地利用現有優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"strengths lie in","meaning":"強項在於","examples":[{"en":"A school’s strengths may lie in teaching, practical research, or scholarship.","zh":"學校的強項可能在於教學、實務研究或學術探索。"},{"en":"Strengths lie in means the strongest abilities or advantages are found in a particular area.","zh":"Strengths lie in 指最強能力或優勢存在於某個範疇。"},{"en":"A student’s strengths may lie in speaking and explaining ideas clearly.","zh":"學生的強項可能在於說話和清楚解釋想法。"},{"en":"If a university’s strengths lie in industry links, it should use those links to help students.","zh":"如果大學強項在於業界聯繫，它應利用那些聯繫幫助學生。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where someone or something is strongest.","zh":"這個片語指出某人或某事最強之處在哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pedagogy","meaning":"教學法","examples":[{"en":"Some schools may have strengths in pedagogy.","zh":"一些學校可能在教學法方面有強項。"},{"en":"Pedagogy means the theory and practice of teaching and learning.","zh":"Pedagogy 指教與學的理論和實踐。"},{"en":"A teacher improves pedagogy by designing examples that help students understand difficult ideas.","zh":"老師透過設計幫助學生理解困難概念的例子來改善教學法。"},{"en":"Strong pedagogy can turn confusing content into clear, usable knowledge.","zh":"強大的教學法可以把令人混亂的內容變成清楚、可用的知識。"},{"en":"This word refers to how teaching is planned and delivered.","zh":"這個詞指教學如何被規劃和執行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"practical applications","meaning":"實際應用","examples":[{"en":"Some research has practical applications in business.","zh":"一些研究在商業中有實際應用。"},{"en":"Practical applications are real uses of an idea, theory, or discovery.","zh":"Practical applications 是某個想法、理論或發現的真實用途。"},{"en":"A grammar rule has practical applications when students use it to write clearer emails.","zh":"當學生用文法規則寫出更清楚電郵時，該規則就有實際應用。"},{"en":"If research has practical applications, managers may use it to improve decisions.","zh":"如果研究有實際應用，管理人員可能用它改善決策。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how knowledge can be used in real situations.","zh":"這個片語集中於知識如何在真實情況中使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"scholarly endeavour","meaning":"學術探索","examples":[{"en":"AACSB recognises scholarly endeavour as one possible strength.","zh":"AACSB 承認學術探索是一種可能的強項。"},{"en":"Scholarly endeavour means serious academic effort to create, test, or develop knowledge.","zh":"Scholarly endeavour 指為創造、測試或發展知識而作出的嚴肅學術努力。"},{"en":"A historian’s careful study of old letters is a form of scholarly endeavour.","zh":"歷史學家仔細研究舊信件就是一種學術探索。"},{"en":"Scholarly endeavour can expand knowledge even when its practical value is not immediate.","zh":"學術探索可以擴展知識，即使其實用價值未必即時出現。"},{"en":"This phrase gives academic research a formal and respectful tone.","zh":"這個片語為學術研究帶來正式而尊重的語氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"operate in a pyramid structure","meaning":"以金字塔結構運作","examples":[{"en":"Universities traditionally operate in a pyramid structure.","zh":"大學傳統上以金字塔結構運作。"},{"en":"To operate in a pyramid structure means to work through a hierarchy with many people at the bottom and fewer at the top.","zh":"To operate in a pyramid structure 指透過底層人多、頂層人少的等級制度運作。"},{"en":"A company may operate in a pyramid structure where junior staff report to managers, who report to directors.","zh":"公司可能以金字塔結構運作，初級員工向經理匯報，經理再向董事匯報。"},{"en":"If promotion depends on research output, many academics compete to move up the pyramid.","zh":"如果晉升取決於研究產出，許多學者會競爭向金字塔上層移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a hierarchical system with limited top positions.","zh":"這個片語描述頂層職位有限的等級制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"enter and remain in the system","meaning":"進入並留在體系中","examples":[{"en":"Faculty members enter and remain in the system to succeed academically.","zh":"教職員進入並留在體系中，以在學術上取得成功。"},{"en":"To enter and remain in the system means to join an institution or profession and continue working within its rules.","zh":"To enter and remain in the system 指加入一個機構或專業，並繼續在其規則內工作。"},{"en":"A young teacher may enter and remain in the school system by meeting training and performance requirements.","zh":"年輕老師可能透過符合培訓和表現要求，進入並留在學校體系中。"},{"en":"If the system rewards publications, academics must publish to stay competitive.","zh":"如果體系獎勵出版物，學者就必須發表以保持競爭力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes joining and surviving within an organised structure.","zh":"這個片語描述加入並在有組織結構中生存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in an attempt to","meaning":"為了嘗試","examples":[{"en":"Faculty members publish research in an attempt to succeed in their fields.","zh":"教職員發表研究，為了嘗試在自己的領域取得成功。"},{"en":"In an attempt to means trying to achieve a particular result.","zh":"In an attempt to 指試圖達成某個結果。"},{"en":"A student may rewrite an essay several times in an attempt to improve clarity.","zh":"學生可能多次重寫文章，為了嘗試改善清晰度。"},{"en":"If people act in an attempt to win approval, their behaviour may follow the reward system.","zh":"如果人們為了嘗試獲得認可而行動，他們的行為可能跟隨獎勵制度。"},{"en":"This phrase shows purpose, but not guaranteed success.","zh":"這個片語顯示目的，但不保證成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"succeed in their academic fields","meaning":"在學術領域取得成功","examples":[{"en":"Faculty members try to succeed in their academic fields.","zh":"教職員嘗試在學術領域取得成功。"},{"en":"To succeed in their academic fields means to gain respect, promotion, or influence in their areas of study.","zh":"To succeed in their academic fields 指在自己的研究範疇中獲得尊重、晉升或影響力。"},{"en":"A biology professor may succeed in her field by publishing useful research and training strong students.","zh":"生物學教授可能透過發表有用研究並培訓優秀學生，在自己的領域取得成功。"},{"en":"If success depends only on journals, professors may focus less on practical teaching.","zh":"如果成功只取決於期刊，教授可能較少專注於實務教學。"},{"en":"This phrase describes achievement within a scholarly discipline.","zh":"這個片語描述在學術學科內的成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"publish competitive research","meaning":"發表有競爭力的研究","examples":[{"en":"A psychology professor must publish competitive research.","zh":"心理學教授必須發表有競爭力的研究。"},{"en":"To publish competitive research means to produce research strong enough to be accepted by respected journals.","zh":"To publish competitive research 指產出足夠強、能被受尊重期刊接受的研究。"},{"en":"A young scholar may need to publish competitive research before applying for promotion.","zh":"年輕學者申請晉升前，可能需要發表有競爭力的研究。"},{"en":"If research is not original or well-supported, it may fail to compete with other papers.","zh":"如果研究不原創或支持不足，它可能無法與其他論文競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research that can survive academic comparison.","zh":"這個片語描述能經得起學術比較的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"top neuroscience journals","meaning":"頂尖神經科學期刊","examples":[{"en":"A psychology professor may need to publish in top neuroscience journals.","zh":"心理學教授可能需要在頂尖神經科學期刊發表。"},{"en":"Top neuroscience journals are leading academic publications in the study of the brain and nervous system.","zh":"Top neuroscience journals 是研究大腦和神經系統的領先學術出版物。"},{"en":"A researcher may aim for top neuroscience journals if her study uses strong evidence and new methods.","zh":"如果研究使用強證據和新方法，研究人員可能以頂尖神經科學期刊為目標。"},{"en":"Publishing in top journals can improve a professor’s reputation and career chances.","zh":"在頂尖期刊發表可以提升教授聲譽和事業機會。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to highly respected journals in a specialised academic field.","zh":"這個片語指專門學術領域中備受尊重的期刊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cultural-studies professor","meaning":"文化研究教授","examples":[{"en":"A cultural-studies professor may send students on field research expeditions.","zh":"文化研究教授可能派學生進行田野研究考察。"},{"en":"A cultural-studies professor teaches and researches culture, identity, media, communities, and social meaning.","zh":"Cultural-studies professor 教授並研究文化、身份、媒體、社群和社會意義。"},{"en":"A cultural-studies professor may ask students to interview residents about local festivals.","zh":"文化研究教授可能要求學生訪問居民有關本地節日的經驗。"},{"en":"If culture is studied only in books, students may miss how people actually live.","zh":"如果文化只在書本中研究，學生可能錯過人們實際如何生活。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an academic who studies culture as a serious subject.","zh":"這個片語指把文化作為嚴肅學科研究的學者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"graduate students","meaning":"研究生","examples":[{"en":"Graduate students may be sent on new field research expeditions.","zh":"研究生可能被派往新的田野研究考察。"},{"en":"Graduate students are students studying for advanced degrees after a bachelor’s degree.","zh":"Graduate students 是完成學士學位後攻讀更高學位的學生。"},{"en":"A graduate student may collect interview data for a research project.","zh":"研究生可能為研究項目收集訪談數據。"},{"en":"Graduate students often balance coursework, research, teaching assistance, and deadlines.","zh":"研究生常要平衡課業、研究、助教工作和期限。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to postgraduate learners in universities.","zh":"這個片語指大學中的深造學生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"field research expeditions","meaning":"田野研究考察","examples":[{"en":"Some professors send graduate students on field research expeditions.","zh":"一些教授派研究生進行田野研究考察。"},{"en":"Field research expeditions are trips made to collect information directly from real places or communities.","zh":"Field research expeditions 是前往真實地方或社群直接收集資料的考察。"},{"en":"Students may join field research expeditions to observe village markets or interview workers.","zh":"學生可能參加田野研究考察，觀察鄉村市場或訪問工人。"},{"en":"Fieldwork can reveal details that cannot be found in books or online databases.","zh":"田野研究可以揭示書本或網上資料庫找不到的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research done outside the classroom or office.","zh":"這個片語描述在課室或辦公室以外進行的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be taken seriously","meaning":"受到認真看待","examples":[{"en":"A professor must produce research to be taken seriously.","zh":"教授必須產出研究，才能受到認真看待。"},{"en":"To be taken seriously means to be respected and treated as important or credible.","zh":"To be taken seriously 指受到尊重，並被視為重要或可信。"},{"en":"A student’s complaint is more likely to be taken seriously if it includes clear evidence.","zh":"如果學生投訴包括清楚證據，就更可能受到認真看待。"},{"en":"If professors do not publish, other academics may question their authority.","zh":"如果教授不發表，其他學者可能質疑其權威。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being regarded as worthy of attention.","zh":"這個片語描述被視為值得注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the core of","meaning":"……的核心","examples":[{"en":"Research is the core of a university’s output.","zh":"研究是大學產出的核心。"},{"en":"The core of something is its central and most important part.","zh":"The core of something 是其中心和最重要部分。"},{"en":"Practice is the core of language improvement because students must use what they learn.","zh":"練習是語言進步的核心，因為學生必須使用所學。"},{"en":"If research is treated as the core, universities may spend heavily on it.","zh":"如果研究被視為核心，大學可能在其上大量花費。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what sits at the centre of a system or idea.","zh":"這個片語指出某制度或想法的中心所在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a university’s output","meaning":"大學的產出","examples":[{"en":"Research forms a major part of a university’s output.","zh":"研究構成大學產出的主要部分。"},{"en":"A university’s output means what a university produces, such as graduates, research, ideas, and public service.","zh":"University’s output 指大學產出的東西，例如畢業生、研究、想法和公共服務。"},{"en":"A school’s output may include exam results, confident students, and community projects.","zh":"學校的產出可能包括考試成績、自信學生和社區項目。"},{"en":"If output is measured only by research, student learning may be undervalued.","zh":"如果產出只由研究衡量，學生學習可能被低估。"},{"en":"This phrase looks at what an institution produces for society.","zh":"這個片語看機構為社會產出甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"research of any kind","meaning":"任何形式的研究","examples":[{"en":"Research of any kind is expensive.","zh":"任何形式的研究都很昂貴。"},{"en":"Research of any kind means all types of research, regardless of topic or method.","zh":"Research of any kind 指所有類型的研究，不論題目或方法。"},{"en":"Research of any kind may require time, staff, data, equipment, and careful analysis.","zh":"任何形式的研究都可能需要時間、人手、數據、設備和仔細分析。"},{"en":"If research costs a lot, people may ask what benefits it brings.","zh":"如果研究成本很高，人們可能會問它帶來甚麼好處。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a general statement about every form of research.","zh":"這個片語對所有研究形式作出一般說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"point out that","meaning":"指出","examples":[{"en":"AACSB points out that business schools spend large sums on research.","zh":"AACSB 指出美國商學院在研究上花費大筆金錢。"},{"en":"To point out that means to draw attention to a fact or issue.","zh":"To point out that 指把注意力引向某個事實或議題。"},{"en":"A teacher may point out that a short sentence can be clearer than a long one.","zh":"老師可能指出短句可以比長句更清楚。"},{"en":"If an organisation points out a cost, it may be preparing to question whether the cost is justified.","zh":"如果組織指出一項成本，它可能準備質疑該成本是否合理。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces information the speaker wants readers to notice.","zh":"這個片語引出說話者希望讀者注意的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"spend more than","meaning":"花費超過","examples":[{"en":"Business schools in America spend more than $320 million a year on research.","zh":"美國商學院每年在研究上花費超過三億二千萬美元。"},{"en":"To spend more than an amount means to use a larger sum of money than that figure.","zh":"To spend more than an amount 指使用比某數字更大的金額。"},{"en":"A family may spend more than expected on transport if they live far from school.","zh":"如果家庭住得離學校遠，他們在交通上可能花費超過預期。"},{"en":"If schools spend more than millions on research, the public may expect clear benefits.","zh":"如果學校在研究上花費超過數百萬，公眾可能期望清楚好處。"},{"en":"This phrase compares real spending with a stated threshold.","zh":"這個片語把實際支出與某個門檻作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a year on","meaning":"每年在……上","examples":[{"en":"Business schools spend more than $320 million a year on research.","zh":"商學院每年在研究上花費超過三億二千萬美元。"},{"en":"A year on something means each year for that particular activity or purpose.","zh":"A year on something 指每年用於某特定活動或目的。"},{"en":"A student may spend thousands of dollars a year on transport and textbooks.","zh":"學生每年可能在交通和教科書上花費數千元。"},{"en":"If an organisation spends heavily every year, the long-term cost becomes significant.","zh":"如果組織每年大量花費，長期成本會變得顯著。"},{"en":"This phrase connects annual spending with a specific area.","zh":"這個片語把年度支出與特定範疇連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"legitimate to ask","meaning":"有理由去問","examples":[{"en":"It seems legitimate to ask why such research is undertaken.","zh":"問為何進行這類研究似乎是有理由的。"},{"en":"Legitimate to ask means reasonable, fair, or acceptable to question something.","zh":"Legitimate to ask 指質疑某事是合理、公平或可接受的。"},{"en":"If a course costs a lot, it is legitimate to ask what support students will receive.","zh":"如果課程很昂貴，問學生會得到甚麼支援是有理由的。"},{"en":"When public money is spent, people have a legitimate reason to ask about results.","zh":"當公共資金被使用，人們有正當理由詢問結果。"},{"en":"This phrase gives permission to question something seriously.","zh":"這個片語容許人們認真質疑某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"for what purpose","meaning":"為了甚麼目的","examples":[{"en":"It is fair to ask for what purpose expensive research is undertaken.","zh":"問昂貴研究是為了甚麼目的而進行，是公平的。"},{"en":"For what purpose means for what reason or intended result.","zh":"For what purpose 指為了甚麼原因或預期結果。"},{"en":"A student may ask for what purpose a long assignment is given.","zh":"學生可能問一份長功課是為了甚麼目的而設。"},{"en":"If the purpose is unclear, people may see the activity as wasteful.","zh":"如果目的不清楚，人們可能把活動視為浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase directly questions the aim behind an action.","zh":"這個片語直接質疑行動背後的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be undertaken","meaning":"被進行","examples":[{"en":"Expensive research should have a clear reason for being undertaken.","zh":"昂貴研究被進行應有清楚理由。"},{"en":"To be undertaken means to be carried out, started, or done as a task.","zh":"To be undertaken 指作為任務被進行、展開或完成。"},{"en":"A survey may be undertaken before a school changes its timetable.","zh":"學校改變時間表前，可能進行一項問卷調查。"},{"en":"If a project is undertaken without clear goals, it may waste time and money.","zh":"如果項目在沒有清楚目標下被進行，它可能浪費時間和金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal way to say that work is done.","zh":"這個片語是表示工作被完成的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"choose to specialise in","meaning":"選擇專攻","examples":[{"en":"A school may choose to specialise in professional outputs.","zh":"學校可能選擇專攻專業成果。"},{"en":"To choose to specialise in something means to decide to focus mainly on one area of strength.","zh":"To choose to specialise in something 指決定主要專注於某個強項範疇。"},{"en":"A student may choose to specialise in marketing after enjoying a branding project.","zh":"學生在喜歡品牌項目後，可能選擇專攻市場學。"},{"en":"If a school specialises in career training, it may invest more in internships than research.","zh":"如果學校專攻職業培訓，它可能在實習上投資多於研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a deliberate decision to focus on a particular field.","zh":"這個片語描述有意識地決定專注於某特定領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"professional outputs","meaning":"專業成果","examples":[{"en":"Some schools may focus more on professional outputs than academic outputs.","zh":"一些學校可能比學術成果更專注於專業成果。"},{"en":"Professional outputs are practical results linked to careers, industry, employment, or workplace performance.","zh":"Professional outputs 是與事業、行業、就業或職場表現相關的實際成果。"},{"en":"Internships, employer partnerships, and graduate job placements can be professional outputs.","zh":"實習、僱主合作和畢業生就業安排都可以是專業成果。"},{"en":"If professional outputs improve, students may feel the school has prepared them well.","zh":"如果專業成果改善，學生可能覺得學校讓他們準備充分。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on real-world career results rather than academic publications.","zh":"這個片語集中於真實職業成果，而不是學術出版物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"academic outputs","meaning":"學術成果","examples":[{"en":"Traditional evaluation often values academic outputs.","zh":"傳統評估常重視學術成果。"},{"en":"Academic outputs are scholarly products such as journal articles, books, conference papers, and research reports.","zh":"Academic outputs 是期刊文章、書籍、會議論文和研究報告等學術產品。"},{"en":"A university may count academic outputs when deciding whether to promote a professor.","zh":"大學決定是否晉升教授時，可能計算學術成果。"},{"en":"If academic outputs dominate evaluation, teaching and career support may receive less attention.","zh":"如果學術成果主導評估，教學和就業支援可能較少受到關注。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to measurable scholarly work produced by academics.","zh":"這個片語指學者產出的可衡量學術工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"A school could focus on professional outputs rather than academic outputs.","zh":"學校可以專注於專業成果，而不是學術成果。"},{"en":"Rather than introduces the thing that is not chosen or not the main focus.","zh":"Rather than 用來引出沒有被選擇或不是主要焦點的事物。"},{"en":"A student may practise speaking daily rather than only memorising grammar rules.","zh":"學生可以每天練習口語，而不是只背文法規則。"},{"en":"If schools value job placement rather than journal articles alone, priorities will shift.","zh":"如果學校重視就業安排，而不是只重視期刊文章，優先事項就會轉變。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a clear contrast between two choices.","zh":"這個片語在兩個選擇之間建立清楚對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"redirect money into","meaning":"將資金重新投放到","examples":[{"en":"A school could redirect money into more fruitful programmes.","zh":"學校可以將資金重新投放到更有成效的項目。"},{"en":"To redirect money into something means to move funding from one use to another.","zh":"To redirect money into something 指把資金由一種用途轉移到另一種用途。"},{"en":"A school may redirect money into counselling if students show serious stress.","zh":"如果學生顯示嚴重壓力，學校可能將資金重新投放到輔導服務。"},{"en":"If research funding is redirected into career services, students may receive more practical support.","zh":"如果研究資金被重新投放到就業服務，學生可能得到更多實際支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing where money is spent.","zh":"這個片語描述改變金錢花在哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a large sum of money","meaning":"一大筆金錢","examples":[{"en":"Research funding can involve a large sum of money.","zh":"研究資金可以涉及一大筆金錢。"},{"en":"A large sum of money means a big amount of money.","zh":"Large sum of money 指一大筆金額。"},{"en":"Studying overseas may require a large sum of money for tuition, rent, and living costs.","zh":"到海外讀書可能需要一大筆金錢支付學費、租金和生活費。"},{"en":"If a large sum is spent, people may expect clear results and accountability.","zh":"如果花費一大筆金錢，人們可能期望清楚結果和問責。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights financial scale.","zh":"這個片語突出財務規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fruitful programmes","meaning":"更有成效的項目","examples":[{"en":"Money could be redirected into more fruitful programmes for students.","zh":"資金可以重新投放到對學生更有成效的項目。"},{"en":"Fruitful programmes are activities or schemes that produce useful, positive results.","zh":"Fruitful programmes 是產生有用、正面結果的活動或計劃。"},{"en":"A school mentoring scheme may be fruitful if younger students gain confidence and study habits.","zh":"如果學校師友計劃令低年級學生建立信心和學習習慣，它可能很有成效。"},{"en":"If a programme leads to jobs, skills, or better learning, it may be more fruitful than a symbolic project.","zh":"如果項目帶來工作、技能或更好學習，它可能比象徵性項目更有成效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes programmes that genuinely produce benefits.","zh":"這個片語描述真正帶來好處的項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"graduates employed at","meaning":"畢業生受僱於","examples":[{"en":"A business school may want more graduates employed at top financial firms.","zh":"商學院可能希望更多畢業生受僱於頂尖金融公司。"},{"en":"Graduates employed at a place are former students who have jobs there.","zh":"Graduates employed at a place 是在某處工作的畢業生。"},{"en":"A university may proudly report the number of graduates employed at hospitals, schools, or banks.","zh":"大學可能自豪地報告受僱於醫院、學校或銀行的畢業生數量。"},{"en":"If many graduates are employed at strong companies, the school can show career success.","zh":"如果許多畢業生受僱於強大公司，學校就可以展示就業成功。"},{"en":"This phrase links alumni employment to specific workplaces.","zh":"這個片語把校友就業與特定工作場所連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"top financial firms","meaning":"頂尖金融公司","examples":[{"en":"Some schools want more graduates to work at top financial firms.","zh":"一些學校希望更多畢業生到頂尖金融公司工作。"},{"en":"Top financial firms are leading companies in banking, investment, insurance, or finance.","zh":"Top financial firms 是銀行、投資、保險或金融領域中的領先公司。"},{"en":"A student may apply to top financial firms because they offer training, salary, and career growth.","zh":"學生可能申請頂尖金融公司，因為它們提供培訓、薪金和事業發展。"},{"en":"If a school sends many graduates to top financial firms, its reputation may improve.","zh":"如果學校把許多畢業生送入頂尖金融公司，其聲譽可能改善。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to highly respected companies in the finance industry.","zh":"這個片語指金融業中備受尊重的公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be better spent on","meaning":"更適合花在……上","examples":[{"en":"Money may be better spent on a career centre than on more research.","zh":"資金可能更適合花在就業輔導中心，而不是更多研究上。"},{"en":"To be better spent on something means the money would create more value if used for that purpose.","zh":"To be better spent on something 指如果金錢用於某目的，會創造更多價值。"},{"en":"A school budget may be better spent on library books than on decorative posters.","zh":"學校預算可能更適合花在圖書館書籍上，而不是裝飾海報上。"},{"en":"If students need job support, funding may be better spent on career services.","zh":"如果學生需要就業支援，資金可能更適合花在就業服務上。"},{"en":"This phrase compares which use of money is wiser.","zh":"這個片語比較金錢用在哪裏更明智。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a career centre","meaning":"就業輔導中心","examples":[{"en":"A career centre can help students build professional skills.","zh":"就業輔導中心可以幫助學生培養專業技能。"},{"en":"A career centre is a university or school service that helps students plan jobs, internships, and applications.","zh":"Career centre 是大學或學校中幫助學生規劃工作、實習和申請的服務。"},{"en":"Students may visit a career centre to practise interviews or improve their CVs.","zh":"學生可能到就業輔導中心練習面試或改善履歷。"},{"en":"If a career centre is strong, graduates may enter the job market with more confidence.","zh":"如果就業輔導中心強大，畢業生可能更有信心進入就業市場。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an office that connects education with employment.","zh":"這個片語指把教育與就業連接起來的辦公室。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"focus on building skills","meaning":"專注於培養技能","examples":[{"en":"A career centre focuses on building the skills of students.","zh":"就業輔導中心專注於培養學生的技能。"},{"en":"To focus on building skills means to concentrate on helping people develop abilities they can use.","zh":"To focus on building skills 指集中幫助人發展可以使用的能力。"},{"en":"A speaking class may focus on building skills through role-play and feedback.","zh":"口語班可能透過角色扮演和回饋，專注於培養技能。"},{"en":"If students build real skills, they become more employable and independent.","zh":"如果學生建立真實技能，他們會更具就業能力和獨立性。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises practical ability rather than passive knowledge.","zh":"這個片語強調實際能力，而不是被動知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"high-level research","meaning":"高水平研究","examples":[{"en":"Some funding is used for high-level research conducted by faculty.","zh":"一些資金用於由教職員進行的高水平研究。"},{"en":"High-level research is advanced, serious research that usually requires expert knowledge and careful methods.","zh":"High-level research 是通常需要專家知識和嚴謹方法的進階嚴肅研究。"},{"en":"A university laboratory may conduct high-level research on new medical treatments.","zh":"大學實驗室可能進行關於新醫療方法的高水平研究。"},{"en":"High-level research can improve reputation, but it may not always help students directly.","zh":"高水平研究可以改善聲譽，但未必總是直接幫助學生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research of a sophisticated academic standard.","zh":"這個片語描述具有精深學術標準的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"conducted by faculty","meaning":"由教職員進行的","examples":[{"en":"High-level research is often conducted by faculty.","zh":"高水平研究通常由教職員進行。"},{"en":"Conducted by faculty means carried out by professors, lecturers, or academic staff.","zh":"Conducted by faculty 指由教授、講師或學術人員進行。"},{"en":"A study conducted by faculty may involve students as research assistants.","zh":"由教職員進行的研究可能讓學生擔任研究助理。"},{"en":"If research is conducted by faculty, the school may use it to show academic strength.","zh":"如果研究由教職員進行，學校可能用它展示學術實力。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies academic staff as the people doing the work.","zh":"這個片語指出學術人員是進行工作的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a change in evaluation","meaning":"評估方式的改變","examples":[{"en":"A change in evaluation could alter how business schools spend money.","zh":"評估方式的改變可能改變商學院如何花錢。"},{"en":"A change in evaluation means a shift in the standards or methods used to judge something.","zh":"Change in evaluation 指用來判斷某事的標準或方法出現轉變。"},{"en":"A school may see a change in evaluation when project work becomes part of the final grade.","zh":"當專題習作成為最終成績一部分，學校可能出現評估方式的改變。"},{"en":"If evaluation changes, people often change what they prioritise.","zh":"如果評估改變，人們通常會改變自己重視的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a new way of judging performance or value.","zh":"這個片語描述判斷表現或價值的新方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"open the door to","meaning":"為……打開大門","examples":[{"en":"A change in evaluation could open the door to more professional teachers.","zh":"評估方式的改變可以為更多專業教師打開大門。"},{"en":"To open the door to something means to make it possible or easier for it to happen.","zh":"To open the door to something 指令某事變得可能或更容易發生。"},{"en":"Better English skills can open the door to overseas study and international work.","zh":"更好的英語能力可以為海外升學和國際工作打開大門。"},{"en":"If schools value practical experience, they may invite more professionals to teach.","zh":"如果學校重視實務經驗，它們可能邀請更多專業人士教學。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating new opportunities.","zh":"這個片語描述創造新機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"professionals from different fields","meaning":"來自不同領域的專業人士","examples":[{"en":"Schools could invite professionals from different fields to teach.","zh":"學校可以邀請來自不同領域的專業人士教學。"},{"en":"Professionals from different fields are experienced workers from various industries or areas of expertise.","zh":"Professionals from different fields 是來自不同行業或專業範疇的有經驗工作者。"},{"en":"A school may invite professionals from law, finance, healthcare, and design to speak to students.","zh":"學校可能邀請來自法律、金融、醫療和設計的專業人士向學生演講。"},{"en":"If students meet professionals from different fields, they can understand career options more clearly.","zh":"如果學生接觸來自不同領域的專業人士，他們可以更清楚理解事業選項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes real-world experts from more than one sector.","zh":"這個片語描述來自多於一個界別的現實世界專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"teach as adjuncts","meaning":"擔任兼任教師","examples":[{"en":"Professionals could teach as adjuncts at business schools.","zh":"專業人士可以在商學院擔任兼任教師。"},{"en":"To teach as adjuncts means to teach part-time or in a limited role while not being full permanent faculty.","zh":"To teach as adjuncts 指以兼職或有限角色教學，而不是全職永久教職員。"},{"en":"A marketing director may teach as an adjunct one evening a week.","zh":"市場總監可能每星期一晚擔任兼任教師。"},{"en":"Adjunct teachers can bring current workplace experience into the classroom.","zh":"兼任教師可以把現時職場經驗帶入課室。"},{"en":"This phrase describes professionals teaching without becoming full-time professors.","zh":"這個片語描述專業人士教學，但不成為全職教授。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"accredited courses","meaning":"獲認可課程","examples":[{"en":"Students could take accredited courses taught by professionals.","zh":"學生可以修讀由專業人士教授的獲認可課程。"},{"en":"Accredited courses are courses officially recognised as meeting certain standards.","zh":"Accredited courses 是被正式認可為符合某些標準的課程。"},{"en":"A student may prefer an accredited course because employers are more likely to trust it.","zh":"學生可能較喜歡獲認可課程，因為僱主更可能信任它。"},{"en":"If a course is accredited, its quality has been checked by an outside body or authority.","zh":"如果課程獲認可，其質素已由外部機構或權威檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to courses with formal approval.","zh":"這個片語指具有正式認可的課程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"currently working in","meaning":"目前在……工作","examples":[{"en":"Students could learn from people currently working in their dream field.","zh":"學生可以向目前在自己理想行業工作的人學習。"},{"en":"Currently working in means presently employed in a particular industry or job area.","zh":"Currently working in 指目前受僱於某個行業或工作範疇。"},{"en":"A student interested in journalism may interview someone currently working in a newsroom.","zh":"對新聞感興趣的學生可能訪問目前在新聞編輯室工作的人。"},{"en":"Learning from current professionals can show students what the job is really like now.","zh":"向現職專業人士學習，可以讓學生看見工作現在真實是怎樣。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses present, real-world experience.","zh":"這個片語強調目前的現實世界經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"dream field","meaning":"理想行業","examples":[{"en":"Students may want to learn from people in their dream field.","zh":"學生可能想向理想行業中的人學習。"},{"en":"A dream field is the industry or profession a person hopes to enter most.","zh":"Dream field 是某人最希望進入的行業或專業。"},{"en":"A student whose dream field is aviation may speak to flight attendants and pilots.","zh":"如果學生的理想行業是航空，他可能與空中服務員和機師交流。"},{"en":"If students meet people in their dream field, they can test whether the career suits them.","zh":"如果學生接觸理想行業中的人，他們可以測試該事業是否適合自己。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an ideal career area.","zh":"這個片語描述理想中的職業範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"critical component of","meaning":"……的關鍵組成部分","examples":[{"en":"AACSB asks why research is the most critical component of traditional education.","zh":"AACSB 問為何研究是傳統教育最關鍵的組成部分。"},{"en":"A critical component of something is an essential part that strongly affects the whole system.","zh":"Critical component of something 是強烈影響整個系統的必要部分。"},{"en":"Clear feedback is a critical component of language learning.","zh":"清晰回饋是語言學習的關鍵組成部分。"},{"en":"If one critical component is missing, the whole programme may become less effective.","zh":"如果缺少一個關鍵組成部分，整個課程可能變得較不有效。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a part that is not optional.","zh":"這個片語指出某部分並非可有可無。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"traditional education","meaning":"傳統教育","examples":[{"en":"AACSB questions the role of research in traditional education.","zh":"AACSB 質疑研究在傳統教育中的角色。"},{"en":"Traditional education refers to established ways of teaching and learning, often centred on classes, exams, and academic knowledge.","zh":"Traditional education 指既有的教與學方式，通常以課堂、考試和學術知識為中心。"},{"en":"Traditional education may give students strong theory but fewer chances to practise workplace tasks.","zh":"傳統教育可能給學生強大理論，但較少機會練習職場任務。"},{"en":"If society changes, traditional education may need to adapt.","zh":"如果社會改變，傳統教育可能需要適應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes older or established educational approaches.","zh":"這個片語描述較舊或既有的教育方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on one level","meaning":"從某一層面來看","examples":[{"en":"On one level, the question is simple to answer.","zh":"從某一層面來看，這個問題容易回答。"},{"en":"On one level means from one point of view or in one limited sense.","zh":"On one level 指從某個角度或某個有限意義上看。"},{"en":"On one level, exams are simply tests; on another level, they affect confidence and opportunity.","zh":"從某一層面來看，考試只是測驗；但從另一層面看，它們影響信心和機會。"},{"en":"This phrase allows a writer to give a simple answer before adding complexity.","zh":"這個片語讓作者先給簡單答案，再加入複雜性。"},{"en":"It shows that an issue can be understood in more than one way.","zh":"它顯示一個議題可以用多於一種方式理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"simple to answer","meaning":"容易回答","examples":[{"en":"The question about research value is simple to answer on one level.","zh":"從某一層面來看，關於研究價值的問題容易回答。"},{"en":"Simple to answer means easy to respond to, at least in a basic way.","zh":"Simple to answer 指至少在基本層面上容易回應。"},{"en":"The question “Why study grammar?” is simple to answer: it helps people communicate clearly.","zh":"“為何學文法？”這個問題容易回答：它幫助人清楚溝通。"},{"en":"A question can be simple to answer at first but complicated when details are considered.","zh":"一個問題起初可能容易回答，但考慮細節時會變得複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an answer that seems straightforward.","zh":"這個片語描述看似直接的答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"expanding the boundaries of knowledge","meaning":"擴展知識邊界","examples":[{"en":"Research is about expanding the boundaries of knowledge.","zh":"研究是關於擴展知識邊界。"},{"en":"Expanding the boundaries of knowledge means increasing what people understand or can explain.","zh":"Expanding the boundaries of knowledge 指增加人們理解或能解釋的範圍。"},{"en":"Medical research expands the boundaries of knowledge when it discovers a new treatment.","zh":"醫學研究發現新療法時，就是擴展知識邊界。"},{"en":"If universities stop asking new questions, knowledge may stop growing.","zh":"如果大學停止提出新問題，知識可能停止增長。"},{"en":"This phrase gives research a broad academic purpose.","zh":"這個片語給研究一個廣闊的學術目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"thrive on","meaning":"依靠……蓬勃發展","examples":[{"en":"Research thrives on answering unasked questions.","zh":"研究依靠回答未被提出的問題而蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"To thrive on something means to grow, succeed, or become stronger because of it.","zh":"To thrive on something 指因某事而成長、成功或變得更強。"},{"en":"Curious students thrive on challenging questions because they enjoy solving problems.","zh":"好奇的學生依靠具挑戰性的問題而進步，因為他們喜歡解難。"},{"en":"Research thrives when people are willing to explore what others have not yet asked.","zh":"當人們願意探索別人尚未提出的問題，研究就會蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the condition that helps something flourish.","zh":"這個片語顯示幫助某事繁盛的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"unasked questions","meaning":"未被提出的問題","examples":[{"en":"Academic research often answers unasked questions.","zh":"學術研究常回答未被提出的問題。"},{"en":"Unasked questions are questions that people have not yet thought to raise or investigate.","zh":"Unasked questions 是人們尚未想到要提出或研究的問題。"},{"en":"A good teacher may ask unasked questions that help students see a topic differently.","zh":"好老師可能提出未被提出的問題，幫助學生以不同方式看待題目。"},{"en":"If researchers only answer familiar questions, knowledge may grow slowly.","zh":"如果研究人員只回答熟悉問題，知識可能增長緩慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unexplored questions that can lead to new understanding.","zh":"這個片語描述能帶來新理解的未探索問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the pursuit of knowledge","meaning":"對知識的追求","examples":[{"en":"The pursuit of knowledge is important to the university system.","zh":"對知識的追求對大學體系很重要。"},{"en":"The pursuit of knowledge means the effort to discover, understand, and explain more about the world.","zh":"The pursuit of knowledge 指努力發現、理解和解釋更多關於世界的事。"},{"en":"A student shows the pursuit of knowledge when they read beyond the textbook out of curiosity.","zh":"當學生出於好奇閱讀教科書以外的內容，他就是在追求知識。"},{"en":"If education values only jobs, the pursuit of knowledge may receive less attention.","zh":"如果教育只重視工作，對知識的追求可能較少受到關注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning as a serious long-term aim.","zh":"這個片語描述把學習視為嚴肅長遠目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"university system","meaning":"大學體系","examples":[{"en":"The pursuit of knowledge remains important to the university system.","zh":"對知識的追求仍然對大學體系很重要。"},{"en":"The university system means the organised network of universities, rules, teaching, research, and qualifications.","zh":"University system 指由大學、規則、教學、研究和資格組成的有組織網絡。"},{"en":"The university system affects how students are admitted, taught, assessed, and awarded degrees.","zh":"大學體系影響學生如何入學、受教、評估和獲頒學位。"},{"en":"If the university system rewards only publications, professors may focus heavily on research.","zh":"如果大學體系只獎勵出版物，教授可能非常專注於研究。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to higher education as an organised structure.","zh":"這個片語指作為有組織結構的高等教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"society progresses","meaning":"社會進步","examples":[{"en":"Society progresses because people learn new ways to do things.","zh":"社會進步是因為人們學會新的做事方式。"},{"en":"Society progresses means communities become more developed, effective, fair, or knowledgeable over time.","zh":"Society progresses 指社群隨時間變得更發達、更有效、更公平或更有知識。"},{"en":"Society progresses when hospitals improve treatment and schools reach more children.","zh":"當醫院改善治療、學校接觸更多孩子，社會就會進步。"},{"en":"Research can help society progress by solving problems people once accepted as unavoidable.","zh":"研究可以透過解決人們曾認為無法避免的問題，幫助社會進步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad improvement in human life or organisation.","zh":"這個片語描述人類生活或組織的廣泛改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in new ways","meaning":"以新的方式","examples":[{"en":"Research helps society do things in new ways.","zh":"研究幫助社會以新的方式做事。"},{"en":"In new ways means using different methods, approaches, or ideas from before.","zh":"In new ways 指使用不同於以往的方法、做法或想法。"},{"en":"Teachers may explain vocabulary in new ways by using pictures, stories, and daily examples.","zh":"老師可能透過圖片、故事和日常例子，以新的方式解釋詞彙。"},{"en":"If people work in new ways, old problems may become easier to solve.","zh":"如果人們以新的方式工作，舊問題可能變得更容易解決。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights innovation and change in method.","zh":"這個片語突出方法上的創新和改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"depend heavily on","meaning":"很大程度上依賴","examples":[{"en":"Progress depends heavily on academic research.","zh":"進步很大程度上依賴學術研究。"},{"en":"To depend heavily on something means to rely on it a great deal.","zh":"To depend heavily on something 指在很大程度上依靠某事。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may depend heavily on regular practice and honest correction.","zh":"學生進步可能很大程度上依賴定期練習和誠實修正。"},{"en":"If a system depends heavily on one source of funding, it becomes vulnerable when that money disappears.","zh":"如果制度很大程度上依賴單一資金來源，當該資金消失時就會變得脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong reliance.","zh":"這個片語顯示強烈依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cannot ignore","meaning":"不能忽視","examples":[{"en":"One cannot ignore the practical uses of research publications.","zh":"人們不能忽視研究出版物的實際用途。"},{"en":"Cannot ignore means must pay attention to something because it is important.","zh":"Cannot ignore 指因某事重要而必須注意。"},{"en":"A school cannot ignore student stress if many pupils are missing classes.","zh":"如果許多學生缺課，學校不能忽視學生壓力。"},{"en":"If research brings reputation and funding, universities cannot ignore its practical benefits.","zh":"如果研究帶來聲譽和資金，大學不能忽視其實際好處。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that a point is too important to dismiss.","zh":"這個片語強調某點重要到不能置之不理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"practical uses of","meaning":"……的實際用途","examples":[{"en":"There are practical uses of research publications.","zh":"研究出版物有實際用途。"},{"en":"Practical uses of something are real purposes or benefits it can serve outside theory.","zh":"Practical uses of something 是某事在理論以外能發揮的真實目的或好處。"},{"en":"A grammar chart has practical uses if students use it to correct their writing.","zh":"如果學生用文法表修正寫作，它就有實際用途。"},{"en":"If publications help attract funding, they have practical uses for universities.","zh":"如果出版物幫助吸引資金，它們對大學就有實際用途。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how something can be useful in real life.","zh":"這個片語集中於某事在現實生活中如何有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"research publications","meaning":"研究出版物","examples":[{"en":"Research publications can improve a school’s reputation.","zh":"研究出版物可以改善學校聲譽。"},{"en":"Research publications are formal written works that report academic studies or findings.","zh":"Research publications 是報告學術研究或發現的正式書面作品。"},{"en":"A professor may list research publications when applying for a university post.","zh":"教授申請大學職位時，可能列出研究出版物。"},{"en":"Strong publications can attract attention, funding, and respect from other institutions.","zh":"強大的出版物可以吸引注意、資金和其他機構的尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to published academic work.","zh":"這個片語指已出版的學術工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cement reputations","meaning":"鞏固聲譽","examples":[{"en":"Research can help cement schools’ and professors’ reputations.","zh":"研究可以幫助鞏固學校和教授的聲譽。"},{"en":"To cement reputations means to make reputations stronger, more secure, or more widely accepted.","zh":"To cement reputations 指令聲譽更強、更穩固或更廣泛被接受。"},{"en":"A restaurant can cement its reputation by serving reliable food for many years.","zh":"餐廳多年來提供可靠食物，可以鞏固其聲譽。"},{"en":"If a professor publishes important research, it can strengthen their standing in the field.","zh":"如果教授發表重要研究，它可以強化他在領域中的地位。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a reputation firmer and harder to question.","zh":"這個片語描述令聲譽更堅固、更難被質疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"gain kudos from","meaning":"從……獲得聲望","examples":[{"en":"Schools gain kudos from their faculties’ publication records.","zh":"學校從其教職員的發表紀錄中獲得聲望。"},{"en":"To gain kudos from something means to receive praise, respect, or status because of it.","zh":"To gain kudos from something 指因某事獲得讚賞、尊重或地位。"},{"en":"A student may gain kudos from classmates after giving a clear presentation.","zh":"學生作出清楚匯報後，可能從同學中獲得聲望。"},{"en":"If a university gains kudos from publications, it may keep rewarding research output.","zh":"如果大學從出版物中獲得聲望，它可能繼續獎勵研究產出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social or professional prestige gained from achievement.","zh":"這個片語描述從成就中取得社會或專業威望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"publication records","meaning":"發表紀錄","examples":[{"en":"Publication records affect a school’s reputation.","zh":"發表紀錄影響學校聲譽。"},{"en":"Publication records are lists or histories of the research articles, books, or papers someone has published.","zh":"Publication records 是某人已發表研究文章、書籍或論文的清單或歷史。"},{"en":"A professor with a strong publication record may find it easier to get promoted.","zh":"發表紀錄強的教授可能較容易獲得晉升。"},{"en":"If schools value publication records too much, teaching quality may become secondary.","zh":"如果學校過分重視發表紀錄，教學質素可能變得次要。"},{"en":"This phrase measures academic productivity through published work.","zh":"這個片語透過已發表作品衡量學術生產力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in some cases","meaning":"在某些情況下","examples":[{"en":"In some cases, research output affects funding.","zh":"在某些情況下，研究產出會影響資金。"},{"en":"In some cases means in certain situations, but not always.","zh":"In some cases 指在某些情況中，但不是總是如此。"},{"en":"In some cases, students improve quickly after one clear explanation.","zh":"在某些情況下，學生在一次清楚解釋後進步很快。"},{"en":"If funding rules differ by country, research output may matter more in some places than others.","zh":"如果資助規則因國家而異，研究產出在某些地方可能比其他地方更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase limits a statement to particular examples or situations.","zh":"這個片語把說法限制在特定例子或情況中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"government-funded schools","meaning":"政府資助院校","examples":[{"en":"Government-funded schools in Britain may receive money based on research output.","zh":"英國政府資助院校可能根據研究產出獲得資金。"},{"en":"Government-funded schools are educational institutions that receive financial support from the government.","zh":"Government-funded schools 是從政府獲得財政支援的教育機構。"},{"en":"A government-funded school must often follow public rules on spending and reporting.","zh":"政府資助院校通常必須遵守公共開支和報告規則。"},{"en":"If public funding depends on research, schools may publish more to secure money.","zh":"如果公共資助取決於研究，學校可能發表更多作品來確保資金。"},{"en":"This phrase describes schools supported by public funds.","zh":"這個片語描述由公共資金支持的學校。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"affect how much money","meaning":"影響……獲得多少資金","examples":[{"en":"Research publications can affect how much money schools receive.","zh":"研究出版物可以影響學校獲得多少資金。"},{"en":"To affect how much money means to influence the amount of funding or income given.","zh":"To affect how much money 指影響給予的資助或收入金額。"},{"en":"A student’s scholarship result may affect how much money their family needs to pay.","zh":"學生的獎學金結果可能影響家庭需要支付多少錢。"},{"en":"If research output affects funding, universities have a strong reason to publish.","zh":"如果研究產出影響資金，大學就有強烈理由發表。"},{"en":"This phrase links a factor to the amount of money received.","zh":"這個片語把某因素與收到的金錢數額連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the mantra is often","meaning":"常見信條是","examples":[{"en":"For professors, the mantra is often “publish or perish”.","zh":"對教授來說，常見信條是「不發表，就淘汰」。"},{"en":"The mantra is often means the repeated guiding rule or belief is usually a particular phrase.","zh":"The mantra is often 指反覆出現的指導規則或信念通常是某句話。"},{"en":"For athletes, the mantra is often “train hard and recover well”.","zh":"對運動員來說，常見信條是「努力訓練，好好恢復」。"},{"en":"If a mantra is repeated often, it can shape people’s behaviour and priorities.","zh":"如果信條經常被重複，它可以塑造人們的行為和優先事項。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a common slogan or belief within a group.","zh":"這個片語引出某群體中的常見口號或信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"publish or perish","meaning":"不發表，就淘汰","examples":[{"en":"For many professors, the rule is “publish or perish”.","zh":"對許多教授來說，規則是「不發表，就淘汰」。"},{"en":"Publish or perish means academics must publish research or risk losing career progress and status.","zh":"Publish or perish 指學者必須發表研究，否則可能失去事業進展和地位。"},{"en":"A young lecturer may feel pressure to publish or perish before applying for tenure.","zh":"年輕講師申請終身教職前，可能感到不發表就淘汰的壓力。"},{"en":"If promotion depends on publications, professors may prioritise research over teaching.","zh":"如果晉升取決於出版物，教授可能把研究置於教學之上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the pressure to publish in academic life.","zh":"這個片語描述學術生活中的發表壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"careers depend on","meaning":"事業取決於","examples":[{"en":"Professors’ careers depend on being seen in the right journals.","zh":"教授的事業取決於作品出現在合適的期刊上。"},{"en":"Careers depend on something means professional progress is strongly controlled by that factor.","zh":"Careers depend on something 指職業發展很大程度受某因素控制。"},{"en":"A salesperson’s career may depend on trust, communication, and consistent results.","zh":"銷售員的事業可能取決於信任、溝通和穩定成果。"},{"en":"If academic careers depend on journal publications, professors will spend much time writing papers.","zh":"如果學術事業取決於期刊出版，教授就會花大量時間寫論文。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what strongly affects someone’s working future.","zh":"這個片語顯示甚麼強烈影響某人的工作前途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be seen in the right journals","meaning":"出現在合適的期刊上","examples":[{"en":"Professors need their work to be seen in the right journals.","zh":"教授需要自己的作品出現在合適的期刊上。"},{"en":"To be seen in the right journals means to have research published in respected publications recognised by the field.","zh":"To be seen in the right journals 指研究在該領域認可的受尊重出版物中發表。"},{"en":"A young scientist may need her article to be seen in the right journals before others notice her work.","zh":"年輕科學家可能需要文章出現在合適的期刊上，別人才會注意其作品。"},{"en":"If work appears in respected journals, it can bring status and career opportunities.","zh":"如果作品出現在受尊重期刊，它可以帶來地位和事業機會。"},{"en":"This phrase links academic visibility with prestige.","zh":"這個片語把學術可見度與聲望連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"at a certain point","meaning":"到了某個階段","examples":[{"en":"At a certain point, one has to question the purpose of the research.","zh":"到了某個階段，人們必須質疑研究的目的。"},{"en":"At a certain point means after a particular stage, time, or level has been reached.","zh":"At a certain point 指到達某個階段、時間或水平之後。"},{"en":"At a certain point, a student must stop collecting notes and start writing the essay.","zh":"到了某個階段，學生必須停止收集筆記並開始寫作文。"},{"en":"If costs keep rising, people eventually ask whether the spending is justified.","zh":"如果成本持續上升，人們最終會問支出是否合理。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the moment when rethinking becomes necessary.","zh":"這個片語標示重新思考變得必要的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"one has to wonder whether","meaning":"不禁要問是否","examples":[{"en":"One has to wonder whether research benefits students or universities.","zh":"人們不禁要問研究是惠及學生還是大學。"},{"en":"One has to wonder whether means it is natural or reasonable to ask if something is true.","zh":"One has to wonder whether 指很自然或合理地要問某事是否真實。"},{"en":"When students are exhausted every day, one has to wonder whether the timetable is healthy.","zh":"當學生每天都筋疲力盡，人們不禁要問時間表是否健康。"},{"en":"This phrase raises a doubt politely but firmly.","zh":"這個片語以禮貌但堅定的方式提出疑問。"},{"en":"It is useful when evidence makes a question difficult to avoid.","zh":"當證據令人難以避免某問題時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"for the benefit of","meaning":"為了……的利益","examples":[{"en":"Research should be done for the benefit of students as well as universities.","zh":"研究應為了學生以及大學的利益而進行。"},{"en":"For the benefit of someone means in order to help or serve that person or group.","zh":"For the benefit of someone 指為了幫助或服務某人或某群體。"},{"en":"A school may change its homework policy for the benefit of students’ mental health.","zh":"學校可能為了學生心理健康的利益而改變功課政策。"},{"en":"If research is funded by tuition, students may expect it to benefit their education.","zh":"如果研究由學費資助，學生可能期望它有益於自己的教育。"},{"en":"This phrase explains who should gain from an action.","zh":"這個片語解釋誰應從行動中受益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"aim to teach","meaning":"旨在教導","examples":[{"en":"A university aims to teach its students, not only to publish research.","zh":"大學旨在教導學生，而不只是發表研究。"},{"en":"To aim to teach means to have education as a central purpose.","zh":"To aim to teach 指把教育作為核心目的。"},{"en":"A language course should aim to teach students how to use English, not only how to pass tests.","zh":"語言課程應旨在教導學生如何使用英語，而不只是如何考試合格。"},{"en":"If a university forgets its teaching aim, students may feel ignored.","zh":"如果大學忘記其教學目的，學生可能感到被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights teaching as a deliberate goal.","zh":"這個片語突出教學是一個有意識的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"attract greater funding","meaning":"吸引更多資金","examples":[{"en":"More publications can attract greater funding.","zh":"更多出版物可以吸引更多資金。"},{"en":"To attract greater funding means to bring in more financial support.","zh":"To attract greater funding 指帶來更多財政支援。"},{"en":"A school may attract greater funding after proving that its reading programme improves results.","zh":"學校證明閱讀計劃改善成績後，可能吸引更多資金。"},{"en":"If publications raise a university’s reputation, donors or governments may provide more money.","zh":"如果出版物提升大學聲譽，捐助者或政府可能提供更多金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase connects achievement or reputation with more resources.","zh":"這個片語把成就或聲譽與更多資源連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in turn","meaning":"反過來；繼而","examples":[{"en":"Greater funding may in turn be spent on better publications.","zh":"更多資金繼而可能被花在更好的出版物上。"},{"en":"In turn means as the next result in a chain of events.","zh":"In turn 指作為一連串事件中的下一個結果。"},{"en":"Better sleep improves concentration, which in turn helps students learn faster.","zh":"更好睡眠改善專注力，繼而幫助學生學得更快。"},{"en":"If publications bring funding, and funding supports more publications, a cycle forms.","zh":"如果出版物帶來資金，而資金又支持更多出版物，就形成循環。"},{"en":"This phrase shows one result leading to another.","zh":"這個片語顯示一個結果帶來另一個結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be spent on","meaning":"被花在……上","examples":[{"en":"Funding may be spent on producing better publications.","zh":"資金可能被花在產出更好的出版物上。"},{"en":"To be spent on something means to be used to pay for that purpose.","zh":"To be spent on something 指被用來支付某目的。"},{"en":"A family’s savings may be spent on school fees, rent, or medical care.","zh":"家庭儲蓄可能被花在學費、租金或醫療上。"},{"en":"If money is spent on research rather than students, priorities may be questioned.","zh":"如果金錢被花在研究而不是學生身上，優先事項可能被質疑。"},{"en":"This phrase explains where money is used.","zh":"這個片語解釋金錢被用在哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"seek to enter careers","meaning":"尋求進入某些事業","examples":[{"en":"Many students seek to enter careers outside academia.","zh":"許多學生尋求進入學術界以外的事業。"},{"en":"To seek to enter careers means to try to begin particular working paths.","zh":"To seek to enter careers 指嘗試開始某些工作道路。"},{"en":"A business student may seek to enter careers in consulting, banking, or marketing.","zh":"商科學生可能尋求進入顧問、銀行或市場學方面的事業。"},{"en":"If students seek careers outside universities, courses should include practical preparation.","zh":"如果學生尋求大學以外的事業，課程應包括實務準備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes actively trying to start a professional life.","zh":"這個片語描述主動嘗試開始專業人生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"outside academia","meaning":"學術界以外","examples":[{"en":"Many students plan to work outside academia.","zh":"許多學生計劃在學術界以外工作。"},{"en":"Outside academia means outside universities, research institutions, or scholarly careers.","zh":"Outside academia 指在大學、研究機構或學術事業以外。"},{"en":"A graduate may work outside academia in business, government, education, or media.","zh":"畢業生可能在學術界以外的商業、政府、教育或媒體工作。"},{"en":"If most students work outside academia, purely academic training may not be enough.","zh":"如果大多數學生在學術界以外工作，純學術訓練可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts professional workplaces with scholarly institutions.","zh":"這個片語把專業職場與學術機構作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"find this cycle frustrating","meaning":"覺得這個循環令人沮喪","examples":[{"en":"Students outside academia may find this publication cycle frustrating.","zh":"學術界以外的學生可能覺得這個出版循環令人沮喪。"},{"en":"To find this cycle frustrating means to feel annoyed or discouraged by a repeating process.","zh":"To find this cycle frustrating 指對一個反覆過程感到煩惱或氣餒。"},{"en":"Students may find repeated grammar drills frustrating if they never learn how to use them in writing.","zh":"如果學生一直做文法操練，卻從未學會如何在寫作中使用，他們可能覺得這個循環令人沮喪。"},{"en":"If research funding only leads to more publications, students may feel their needs are ignored.","zh":"如果研究資金只帶來更多出版物，學生可能覺得自己的需要被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional dissatisfaction with a repeated system.","zh":"這個片語描述對重複制度的情緒不滿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the Ivory Tower","meaning":"象牙塔","examples":[{"en":"Some students see professors as part of the Ivory Tower of academia.","zh":"一些學生把教授視為學術界象牙塔的一部分。"},{"en":"The Ivory Tower means an academic world seen as separated from ordinary life and practical problems.","zh":"Ivory Tower 指被視為與普通生活和實際問題分離的學術世界。"},{"en":"A manager may criticise university theories as coming from the Ivory Tower if they ignore real workplace pressure.","zh":"如果大學理論忽視真實職場壓力，管理人員可能批評它們來自象牙塔。"},{"en":"If academics stay in the Ivory Tower, their work may not reach people who need it.","zh":"如果學者留在象牙塔中，他們的工作可能無法接觸有需要的人。"},{"en":"This phrase often criticises intellectual life that feels isolated from reality.","zh":"這個片語常批評與現實隔離的知識生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"operate in","meaning":"在……中運作","examples":[{"en":"Some academics are seen as operating in a self-contained community.","zh":"一些學者被視為在自成一體的群體中運作。"},{"en":"To operate in a place or system means to work within it and follow its rules.","zh":"To operate in a place or system 指在某地方或制度內工作並遵守其規則。"},{"en":"A small business may operate in a competitive market where prices change quickly.","zh":"小企業可能在價格快速變動的競爭市場中運作。"},{"en":"If academics operate only inside their own circle, outsiders may not understand their work.","zh":"如果學者只在自己的圈子中運作，外人可能不理解其作品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the environment in which someone works.","zh":"這個片語描述某人工作的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a self-contained community","meaning":"自成一體的群體","examples":[{"en":"Academia can appear to be a self-contained community.","zh":"學術界可能看起來像一個自成一體的群體。"},{"en":"A self-contained community is a group that mostly functions within itself and has limited contact with outsiders.","zh":"Self-contained community 是主要在內部運作，與外人接觸有限的群體。"},{"en":"A boarding school may feel like a self-contained community if students live, study, and socialise there.","zh":"如果學生在寄宿學校生活、學習和社交，該校可能感覺像自成一體的群體。"},{"en":"If academics mainly talk to other academics, their ideas may not spread outside the group.","zh":"如果學者主要與其他學者交談，其想法可能不會傳到群體以外。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests separation from the wider world.","zh":"這個片語暗示與更廣闊世界分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"have little influence on","meaning":"對……影響甚微","examples":[{"en":"Some academic work has little influence on the outside world.","zh":"一些學術作品對外面的世界影響甚微。"},{"en":"To have little influence on something means to affect it only slightly or not in any meaningful way.","zh":"To have little influence on something 指只輕微影響某事，或沒有任何有意義影響。"},{"en":"A school rule has little influence on students if no one explains or enforces it.","zh":"如果沒有人解釋或執行校規，它對學生影響甚微。"},{"en":"If managers never read a study, that study may have little influence on business practice.","zh":"如果管理人員從不閱讀某研究，該研究對商業實務可能影響甚微。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weak impact.","zh":"這個片語描述微弱影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the outside world","meaning":"外面的世界；現實世界","examples":[{"en":"Students may feel that academic research has little influence on the outside world.","zh":"學生可能覺得學術研究對外面的世界影響甚微。"},{"en":"The outside world means life beyond a particular closed group, institution, or environment.","zh":"The outside world 指某個封閉群體、機構或環境以外的生活。"},{"en":"Students in school may not fully understand the outside world until they take internships.","zh":"學生在學校中可能直到實習才充分理解外面的世界。"},{"en":"If universities ignore the outside world, their teaching may feel unrealistic.","zh":"如果大學忽視外面的世界，其教學可能感覺不切實際。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts a closed setting with broader society.","zh":"這個片語把封閉環境與更廣闊社會作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"part of the trouble","meaning":"問題的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Part of the trouble is that academic journals share a similar ethos.","zh":"問題的一部分在於學術期刊有相似理念。"},{"en":"Part of the trouble means one reason for the problem, though not the only reason.","zh":"Part of the trouble 指問題其中一個原因，但不是唯一原因。"},{"en":"Part of the trouble with poor writing is that students often rush planning.","zh":"寫作差劣的問題一部分在於學生常常匆忙規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase helps identify one cause within a larger problem.","zh":"這個片語幫助指出較大問題中的一個成因。"},{"en":"It suggests the issue has more than one contributing factor.","zh":"它暗示該問題有多於一個促成因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"labour under","meaning":"受……束縛；在……下運作","examples":[{"en":"Journals labour under a similar ethos.","zh":"期刊受相似理念束縛。"},{"en":"To labour under something means to be burdened, limited, or strongly shaped by it.","zh":"To labour under something 指受某事負擔、限制或強烈塑造。"},{"en":"Students may labour under the belief that longer sentences always sound smarter.","zh":"學生可能受「句子越長就越聰明」這個想法束縛。"},{"en":"If journals labour under narrow academic values, practical writing may be discouraged.","zh":"如果期刊受狹窄學術價值束縛，實用寫作可能被削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests being constrained by an assumption or system.","zh":"這個片語暗示受假設或制度限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a similar ethos","meaning":"相似的理念","examples":[{"en":"Academic journals often operate under a similar ethos.","zh":"學術期刊常在相似理念下運作。"},{"en":"A similar ethos means a shared set of values, beliefs, or guiding principles.","zh":"Similar ethos 指一套共同的價值、信念或指導原則。"},{"en":"Two schools may have a similar ethos if both value discipline, care, and academic effort.","zh":"如果兩間學校都重視紀律、關懷和學術努力，它們可能有相似理念。"},{"en":"If journals share a similar ethos, they may reward the same style of research.","zh":"如果期刊有相似理念，它們可能獎勵同一風格的研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common mindset across organisations.","zh":"這個片語描述組織之間的共同心態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"highly quantitative","meaning":"高度量化的","examples":[{"en":"Much academic research is highly quantitative.","zh":"許多學術研究高度量化。"},{"en":"Highly quantitative means strongly based on numbers, measurement, statistics, or data analysis.","zh":"Highly quantitative 指強烈基於數字、量度、統計或數據分析。"},{"en":"A school survey becomes highly quantitative when it focuses on scores, percentages, and charts.","zh":"當學校問卷集中於分數、百分比和圖表，它就變得高度量化。"},{"en":"Quantitative research can be powerful, but it may feel distant if readers cannot understand the numbers.","zh":"量化研究可以很有力，但如果讀者不理解數字，它可能感覺遙遠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research that relies heavily on numerical evidence.","zh":"這個片語描述高度依賴數字證據的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"hypothesis-driven","meaning":"以假設為導向的","examples":[{"en":"Many research articles are hypothesis-driven.","zh":"許多研究文章以假設為導向。"},{"en":"Hypothesis-driven means organised around testing a proposed explanation or prediction.","zh":"Hypothesis-driven 指圍繞測試一個提出的解釋或預測而組織。"},{"en":"A science project is hypothesis-driven when students first predict that sunlight affects plant growth.","zh":"當學生先預測陽光會影響植物生長，科學專題就是以假設為導向。"},{"en":"If research is hypothesis-driven, the method is designed to test whether the idea is supported.","zh":"如果研究以假設為導向，其方法會被設計來測試該想法是否得到支持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research led by a specific testable claim.","zh":"這個片語描述由具體可測試主張引導的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"esoteric","meaning":"深奧難懂的","examples":[{"en":"Much of the research is esoteric and difficult for managers to use.","zh":"很多研究深奧難懂，管理人員難以使用。"},{"en":"Esoteric means understood by only a small group of specialists and difficult for ordinary people to access.","zh":"Esoteric 指只有少數專家理解，普通人難以接觸的。"},{"en":"A grammar explanation becomes esoteric if it uses too many technical terms without examples.","zh":"如果文法解釋使用太多技術術語而沒有例子，它會變得深奧難懂。"},{"en":"If research is too esoteric, practical readers may stop reading before reaching the useful idea.","zh":"如果研究太深奧難懂，實務讀者可能未讀到有用想法就停止。"},{"en":"This word describes knowledge that feels specialised, obscure, and hard to apply.","zh":"這個詞描述感覺專門、晦澀且難以應用的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, much academic research is not read by managers.","zh":"因此，許多學術研究並沒有被管理人員閱讀。"},{"en":"As a result introduces the consequence of what has just been explained.","zh":"As a result 用來引出剛剛所解釋事情的後果。"},{"en":"The instructions were unclear; as a result, many students answered the wrong question.","zh":"指示不清楚；因此，許多學生答錯問題。"},{"en":"If research is too technical, managers may ignore it as a result.","zh":"如果研究太技術化，管理人員可能因此忽視它。"},{"en":"This phrase links cause and effect.","zh":"這個片語連接原因和結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"almost universally unread","meaning":"幾乎完全沒有人閱讀","examples":[{"en":"Academic research is almost universally unread by real-world managers.","zh":"學術研究幾乎完全不被現實職場中的管理人員閱讀。"},{"en":"Almost universally unread means hardly anyone in the relevant group reads it.","zh":"Almost universally unread 指相關群體中幾乎沒有人閱讀。"},{"en":"A school policy document may be almost universally unread if it is too long and full of jargon.","zh":"如果學校政策文件太長且充滿術語，它可能幾乎完全沒有人閱讀。"},{"en":"If research is almost universally unread, its influence outside academia will be limited.","zh":"如果研究幾乎完全沒有人閱讀，它在學術界以外的影響會有限。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly criticises writing that fails to reach its intended audience.","zh":"這個片語強烈批評未能接觸目標讀者的寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"real-world managers","meaning":"現實職場中的管理人員","examples":[{"en":"Real-world managers rarely read highly esoteric academic research.","zh":"現實職場中的管理人員很少閱讀高度深奧的學術研究。"},{"en":"Real-world managers are managers working in actual companies or organisations, not just studying management theory.","zh":"Real-world managers 是在真實公司或機構中工作的管理人員，而不只是研究管理理論的人。"},{"en":"Real-world managers need advice they can use when hiring staff, serving customers, or solving conflicts.","zh":"現實職場中的管理人員需要能用於招聘員工、服務顧客或解決衝突的建議。"},{"en":"If academic papers ignore real-world managers’ needs, those managers may not read them.","zh":"如果學術論文忽視現實職場管理人員的需要，這些管理人員可能不會閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts practising managers with academic researchers.","zh":"這個片語把實務管理人員與學術研究人員作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"published research","meaning":"已發表的研究","examples":[{"en":"Much academic research criticises other published research.","zh":"許多學術研究批評其他已發表的研究。"},{"en":"Published research is research that has appeared in journals, books, reports, or other formal outlets.","zh":"Published research 是已出現在期刊、書籍、報告或其他正式渠道的研究。"},{"en":"Students often use published research to support arguments in essays.","zh":"學生常使用已發表的研究來支持文章論點。"},{"en":"If published research only speaks to other researchers, its practical reach may be narrow.","zh":"如果已發表的研究只與其他研究者對話，其實際影響範圍可能很窄。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to research made publicly available in formal written form.","zh":"這個片語指以正式書面形式公開的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"an issue of","meaning":"某一期","examples":[{"en":"A paper appeared in an issue of Strategy & Leadership.","zh":"一篇論文出現在《策略與領導》某一期。"},{"en":"An issue of a journal means one particular published edition of that magazine or journal.","zh":"An issue of a journal 指該雜誌或期刊某一特定出版期。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to read an article from an issue of a science magazine.","zh":"老師可能要求學生閱讀科學雜誌某一期中的文章。"},{"en":"If a paper appears in a respected issue, it may receive more attention from readers.","zh":"如果論文出現在受尊重期刊的某一期，它可能得到更多讀者注意。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific edition of a publication.","zh":"這個片語指出出版物的特定一期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"Strategy & Leadership","meaning":"《策略與領導》","examples":[{"en":"The article cites Strategy & Leadership to criticise academic research.","zh":"文章引用《策略與領導》來批評學術研究。"},{"en":"Strategy & Leadership is the name of a publication discussing management, strategy, and leadership issues.","zh":"Strategy & Leadership 是一份討論管理、策略和領導議題的出版物名稱。"},{"en":"A business student may read Strategy & Leadership to understand debates in management practice.","zh":"商科學生可能閱讀《策略與領導》，以理解管理實務中的辯論。"},{"en":"Mentioning a publication can give support to an argument if the source is relevant.","zh":"如果來源相關，提及出版物可以為論點提供支持。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a named journal used as evidence in the passage.","zh":"這個片語指文章中用作證據的一份具名期刊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"comment that","meaning":"評論說","examples":[{"en":"The paper commented that research often ignores managers’ needs.","zh":"該論文評論說，研究常忽視管理人員的需要。"},{"en":"To comment that means to state an opinion, observation, or judgement.","zh":"To comment that 指陳述意見、觀察或判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher may comment that an essay has strong ideas but weak organisation.","zh":"老師可能評論說文章想法很強，但組織較弱。"},{"en":"If a paper comments on a problem, it may influence how readers understand the issue.","zh":"如果論文評論某問題，它可能影響讀者如何理解該議題。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a stated view or criticism.","zh":"這個片語引出明示觀點或批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be designed with someone’s needs in mind","meaning":"以某人的需要為出發點設計","examples":[{"en":"Research is often not designed with managers’ needs in mind.","zh":"研究通常不是以管理人員的需要為出發點設計。"},{"en":"To be designed with someone’s needs in mind means to be planned around what that person or group actually needs.","zh":"To be designed with someone’s needs in mind 指圍繞某人或某群體真正需要來規劃。"},{"en":"A language course should be designed with beginners’ needs in mind by using clear examples and simple tasks.","zh":"語言課程應以初學者的需要為出發點設計，使用清楚例子和簡單任務。"},{"en":"If research is not designed for managers, it may fail to solve workplace problems.","zh":"如果研究不是為管理人員而設計，它可能無法解決職場問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on planning something for a specific audience.","zh":"這個片語集中於為特定受眾規劃某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"nor is it communicated","meaning":"也沒有被傳達","examples":[{"en":"Research is not designed for managers, nor is it communicated in the journals they read.","zh":"研究不是為管理人員而設計，也沒有在他們閱讀的期刊中傳達。"},{"en":"Nor is it communicated means it is also not shared or presented in a way that reaches the audience.","zh":"Nor is it communicated 指它也沒有以能接觸受眾的方式分享或呈現。"},{"en":"A school rule is useless if it is not explained to students, nor is it communicated to parents.","zh":"如果校規沒有向學生解釋，也沒有傳達給家長，它就沒有用。"},{"en":"If useful ideas are not communicated clearly, they may have little practical effect.","zh":"如果有用想法沒有被清楚傳達，它們可能幾乎沒有實際效果。"},{"en":"This phrase adds a second negative point after the first one.","zh":"這個片語在第一個否定點後加入第二個否定點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"for the most part","meaning":"在大多數情況下","examples":[{"en":"For the most part, research has become a closed system.","zh":"在大多數情況下，研究已變成一個封閉系統。"},{"en":"For the most part means generally, mostly, or in most situations.","zh":"For the most part 指一般而言、大多數時候或在大多數情況下。"},{"en":"For the most part, students improve when practice is regular and feedback is clear.","zh":"在大多數情況下，當練習定期而回饋清楚，學生會進步。"},{"en":"This phrase allows a general statement while leaving room for exceptions.","zh":"這個片語容許一般說法，同時保留例外空間。"},{"en":"It is useful when a pattern is mostly true but not always true.","zh":"當某模式大致正確但不是永遠正確時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"self-referential closed system","meaning":"自我指涉的封閉系統","examples":[{"en":"The paper described research as a self-referential closed system.","zh":"該論文把研究描述為自我指涉的封閉系統。"},{"en":"A self-referential closed system is a system that mostly talks about itself and stays cut off from outside users.","zh":"Self-referential closed system 是主要談論自身並與外部使用者隔絕的系統。"},{"en":"A school committee becomes a closed system if it only writes reports for other committee members.","zh":"如果學校委員會只為其他委員撰寫報告，它就變成封閉系統。"},{"en":"If research only responds to other research, managers may find it irrelevant.","zh":"如果研究只回應其他研究，管理人員可能覺得它無關。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises work that circulates inside its own world.","zh":"這個片語批評只在自己世界內流通的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"irrelevant to corporate performance","meaning":"與企業表現無關","examples":[{"en":"Some research is criticised as irrelevant to corporate performance.","zh":"一些研究被批評為與企業表現無關。"},{"en":"Irrelevant to corporate performance means not connected to how well companies actually operate or succeed.","zh":"Irrelevant to corporate performance 指與公司實際運作或成功程度沒有關聯。"},{"en":"A theory may be irrelevant to corporate performance if managers cannot use it to improve decisions.","zh":"如果管理人員不能用某理論改善決策，它可能與企業表現無關。"},{"en":"If research does not affect profits, staff, customers, or strategy, business readers may ignore it.","zh":"如果研究不影響利潤、員工、顧客或策略，商業讀者可能忽視它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lack of practical business relevance.","zh":"這個片語描述缺乏實際商業相關性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"insist that","meaning":"堅持認為","examples":[{"en":"AACSB insists that the separation between academia and business must change.","zh":"AACSB 堅持認為學術界與商業之間的分離必須改變。"},{"en":"To insist that means to state something firmly and refuse to treat it as optional.","zh":"To insist that 指堅定陳述某事，並拒絕把它視為可有可無。"},{"en":"A teacher may insist that students explain their answers, not just choose A, B, C, or D.","zh":"老師可能堅持認為學生必須解釋答案，而不只是選 A、B、C 或 D。"},{"en":"If an organisation insists on change, it believes the current system is no longer acceptable.","zh":"如果組織堅持要求改變，它相信目前制度已不再可接受。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a strong and firm position.","zh":"這個片語顯示強烈而堅定的立場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"separation must change","meaning":"分離狀態必須改變","examples":[{"en":"AACSB argues that the separation between research and practice must change.","zh":"AACSB 認為研究與實踐之間的分離狀態必須改變。"},{"en":"Separation must change means the distance or divide between two areas should be reduced or removed.","zh":"Separation must change 指兩個範疇之間的距離或分隔應被減少或移除。"},{"en":"The separation between school learning and daily life must change if students cannot apply what they learn.","zh":"如果學生不能應用所學，學校學習與日常生活之間的分離狀態必須改變。"},{"en":"If research and practice stay separate, useful ideas may not reach workplaces.","zh":"如果研究和實踐一直分離，有用想法可能無法進入職場。"},{"en":"This phrase calls for closer connection between divided worlds.","zh":"這個片語呼籲在分隔的世界之間建立更緊密聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"higher education","meaning":"高等教育","examples":[{"en":"The future of higher education may depend on closer links with the professional world.","zh":"高等教育的未來可能取決於與專業世界更緊密的聯繫。"},{"en":"Higher education means education after secondary school, usually at universities or colleges.","zh":"Higher education 指中學後的教育，通常在大學或學院進行。"},{"en":"Higher education can include bachelor’s degrees, master’s degrees, and doctoral research.","zh":"高等教育可以包括學士學位、碩士學位和博士研究。"},{"en":"If higher education becomes too expensive, students may demand clearer career benefits.","zh":"如果高等教育變得太昂貴，學生可能要求更清楚的職業好處。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to advanced formal education beyond school level.","zh":"這個片語指學校階段以後的高階正規教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"invest thousands of dollars","meaning":"投入數千美元","examples":[{"en":"Students invest thousands of dollars in their education.","zh":"學生在教育上投入數千美元。"},{"en":"To invest thousands of dollars means to spend a large amount of money with the hope of future benefit.","zh":"To invest thousands of dollars 指花費一大筆金錢，希望日後得到好處。"},{"en":"A family may invest thousands of dollars in language lessons if they believe English will open career doors.","zh":"如果家庭相信英語會打開事業大門，他們可能在語言課程上投入數千美元。"},{"en":"If education is a major investment, students expect useful skills and opportunities in return.","zh":"如果教育是一項重大投資，學生會期望得到有用技能和機會作回報。"},{"en":"This phrase treats spending on education as a long-term investment.","zh":"這個片語把教育開支視為長期投資。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"career path","meaning":"事業道路","examples":[{"en":"Education is part of many students’ career path.","zh":"教育是許多學生事業道路的一部分。"},{"en":"A career path is the route a person takes through education, jobs, training, and promotions.","zh":"Career path 是一個人透過教育、工作、培訓和晉升走出的路線。"},{"en":"A student’s career path may begin with an internship and later lead to management.","zh":"學生的事業道路可能由實習開始，之後走向管理。"},{"en":"If universities understand students’ career paths, they can design more useful support.","zh":"如果大學理解學生的事業道路，它們可以設計更有用的支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the direction of someone’s working life over time.","zh":"這個片語描述某人工作人生隨時間發展的方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be incorporated into","meaning":"被納入","examples":[{"en":"Academics should be more fully incorporated into the professional world.","zh":"學者應更充分地被納入專業世界。"},{"en":"To be incorporated into something means to be included or integrated as part of it.","zh":"To be incorporated into something 指被包括或融入其中，成為其一部分。"},{"en":"Speaking practice should be incorporated into grammar lessons so students can use new structures.","zh":"口語練習應被納入文法課，讓學生能使用新句式。"},{"en":"If academics are incorporated into industry discussions, their research may become more relevant.","zh":"如果學者被納入業界討論，他們的研究可能變得更相關。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being brought into a larger system.","zh":"這個片語描述被帶入一個更大系統之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"professional world","meaning":"專業世界；職場世界","examples":[{"en":"Academics should become more connected with the professional world.","zh":"學者應與專業世界有更緊密聯繫。"},{"en":"The professional world means the world of real jobs, industries, clients, organisations, and workplace decisions.","zh":"Professional world 指真實工作、行業、客戶、機構和職場決策的世界。"},{"en":"Students understand the professional world better after internships and workplace visits.","zh":"學生在實習和職場參觀後，會更理解專業世界。"},{"en":"If universities connect with the professional world, teaching can become more realistic.","zh":"如果大學與專業世界連接，教學可以變得更貼近現實。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts work practice with purely academic activity.","zh":"這個片語把工作實務與純學術活動作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"focus on other strengths","meaning":"專注於其他強項","examples":[{"en":"Universities must focus on other strengths outside of research.","zh":"大學必須專注於研究以外的其他強項。"},{"en":"To focus on other strengths means to give attention to advantages besides the main or usual one.","zh":"To focus on other strengths 指關注主要或慣常強項以外的優勢。"},{"en":"A student weak in exams may focus on other strengths, such as speaking, design, or teamwork.","zh":"考試較弱的學生可能專注於其他強項，例如口語、設計或團隊合作。"},{"en":"If universities value teaching and networks as well as research, students may benefit more directly.","zh":"如果大學重視教學和人脈以及研究，學生可能更直接受益。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages a broader view of ability or value.","zh":"這個片語鼓勵對能力或價值採取更廣闊看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"outside of research","meaning":"研究以外","examples":[{"en":"Universities should develop strengths outside of research.","zh":"大學應發展研究以外的強項。"},{"en":"Outside of research means beyond academic study and publication.","zh":"Outside of research 指在學術研究和出版以外。"},{"en":"A university can build value outside of research through teaching quality, mentoring, and career support.","zh":"大學可以透過教學質素、指導和就業支援，在研究以外建立價值。"},{"en":"If schools ignore strengths outside research, students may receive a narrower education.","zh":"如果學校忽視研究以外的強項，學生可能接受較狹窄的教育。"},{"en":"This phrase points to areas beyond scholarly production.","zh":"這個片語指學術產出以外的範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"professional networks","meaning":"專業人脈網絡","examples":[{"en":"Professional networks can help universities prepare students for careers.","zh":"專業人脈網絡可以幫助大學讓學生為事業作準備。"},{"en":"Professional networks are connections with people and organisations in different industries.","zh":"Professional networks 是與不同行業人士和機構的聯繫。"},{"en":"A student may use professional networks to find internships, mentors, or job interviews.","zh":"學生可能利用專業人脈網絡尋找實習、導師或求職面試。"},{"en":"If a university has strong professional networks, students can meet employers more easily.","zh":"如果大學有強大的專業人脈網絡，學生可以更容易接觸僱主。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to relationships that support career opportunities.","zh":"這個片語指支援事業機會的人際關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"technology skills","meaning":"科技技能","examples":[{"en":"Technology skills are important for students’ future careers.","zh":"科技技能對學生未來事業很重要。"},{"en":"Technology skills are abilities related to using digital tools, software, data, and online systems effectively.","zh":"Technology skills 是有效使用數碼工具、軟件、數據和網上系統的能力。"},{"en":"Students with technology skills may manage spreadsheets, presentations, databases, or online communication better.","zh":"具有科技技能的學生可能更好地管理試算表、簡報、資料庫或網上溝通。"},{"en":"If workplaces become more digital, weak technology skills can limit career progress.","zh":"如果職場變得更數碼化，薄弱科技技能可能限制事業發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical digital abilities needed at work.","zh":"這個片語描述工作中所需的實用數碼能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"connections with","meaning":"與……的聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Universities need connections with top business firms around the world.","zh":"大學需要與世界各地頂尖商業公司建立聯繫。"},{"en":"Connections with someone means relationships, links, or contacts with them.","zh":"Connections with someone 指與某人或某機構的關係、連繫或接觸。"},{"en":"A school with connections with local hospitals may offer better healthcare internships.","zh":"與本地醫院有聯繫的學校，可能提供更好的醫療實習。"},{"en":"If students have access to industry connections, they may find career opportunities more easily.","zh":"如果學生能接觸業界聯繫，他們可能更容易找到事業機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes useful links between people or organisations.","zh":"這個片語描述人或組織之間有用的連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"top business firms","meaning":"頂尖商業公司","examples":[{"en":"Universities should build connections with top business firms.","zh":"大學應與頂尖商業公司建立聯繫。"},{"en":"Top business firms are leading companies with strong reputations, resources, and influence.","zh":"Top business firms 是具有強大聲譽、資源和影響力的領先公司。"},{"en":"Students may visit top business firms to learn how large companies solve real problems.","zh":"學生可能參觀頂尖商業公司，學習大型公司如何解決真實問題。"},{"en":"If a university partners with top firms, students may gain better internships and career advice.","zh":"如果大學與頂尖公司合作，學生可能獲得更好的實習和事業建議。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to highly respected companies in the business world.","zh":"這個片語指商業世界中備受尊重的公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"resist the report","meaning":"抵制該報告","examples":[{"en":"Many universities resisted the report.","zh":"許多大學抵制該報告。"},{"en":"To resist the report means to oppose, reject, or refuse to accept its recommendations.","zh":"To resist the report 指反對、拒絕或不接受該報告的建議。"},{"en":"Teachers may resist a new marking policy if they think it is unfair to students.","zh":"如果老師認為新評分政策對學生不公平，他們可能抵制它。"},{"en":"If a report threatens old rewards, institutions may resist it strongly.","zh":"如果報告威脅舊有獎勵方式，機構可能強烈抵制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes opposition to a document or proposal.","zh":"這個片語描述對文件或提案的反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"continue to change","meaning":"繼續變化","examples":[{"en":"Today’s world continues to change.","zh":"今天的世界繼續變化。"},{"en":"To continue to change means to keep developing or becoming different over time.","zh":"To continue to change 指隨時間持續發展或變得不同。"},{"en":"Technology continues to change how students learn, communicate, and apply for jobs.","zh":"科技繼續改變學生如何學習、溝通和求職。"},{"en":"If the world continues to change, education cannot remain fixed forever.","zh":"如果世界繼續變化，教育不能永遠固定不變。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses ongoing transformation.","zh":"這個片語強調持續轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"have little choice but to","meaning":"除了……別無選擇","examples":[{"en":"Universities have little choice but to adapt to new standards.","zh":"大學除了適應新標準外，別無選擇。"},{"en":"To have little choice but to do something means to almost have no realistic option except doing it.","zh":"To have little choice but to do something 指幾乎沒有現實選項，只能做某事。"},{"en":"If rent rises sharply, a family may have little choice but to move to a cheaper flat.","zh":"如果租金大幅上升，家庭可能除了搬到較便宜單位外，別無選擇。"},{"en":"If standards change, universities may need to adapt even if they dislike the change.","zh":"如果標準改變，大學即使不喜歡該改變，也可能需要適應。"},{"en":"This phrase shows pressure and limited options.","zh":"這個片語顯示壓力和有限選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"adapt to","meaning":"適應","examples":[{"en":"Universities must adapt to new trends and standards.","zh":"大學必須適應新趨勢和新標準。"},{"en":"To adapt to something means to change in order to deal with a new situation.","zh":"To adapt to something 指為應付新情況而改變。"},{"en":"Students adapt to online learning by managing time and using digital tools.","zh":"學生透過管理時間和使用數碼工具來適應網上學習。"},{"en":"If universities adapt to workplace changes, their graduates may be better prepared.","zh":"如果大學適應職場變化，其畢業生可能準備得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing successfully when conditions change.","zh":"這個片語描述在情況改變時成功作出改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"new trends and standards","meaning":"新趨勢和新標準","examples":[{"en":"Universities need to adapt to new trends and standards.","zh":"大學需要適應新趨勢和新標準。"},{"en":"New trends and standards are fresh patterns, expectations, or rules that people increasingly follow.","zh":"New trends and standards 是人們越來越跟隨的新模式、期望或規則。"},{"en":"Schools may adjust lessons because of new trends and standards in digital learning.","zh":"學校可能因數碼學習的新趨勢和新標準而調整課堂。"},{"en":"If universities ignore new standards, employers may see their training as outdated.","zh":"如果大學忽視新標準，僱主可能認為其培訓過時。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to changing expectations in society or industry.","zh":"這個片語指社會或行業中不斷改變的期望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"考生為每條問題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option that matches the question best.","zh":"To choose the correct letter 指選擇最符合題目的答案選項。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should read all options before choosing the correct letter.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應閱讀所有選項後才選出正確字母。"},{"en":"If two answers look similar, careful reading helps avoid choosing the wrong letter.","zh":"如果兩個答案看似相似，仔細閱讀有助避免選錯字母。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in multiple-choice questions.","zh":"這個片語是多項選擇題中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the recommendation given by","meaning":"由……提出的建議","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the recommendation given by AACSB.","zh":"題目問由 AACSB 提出的建議。"},{"en":"The recommendation given by someone means the advice or proposal that person or organisation has made.","zh":"The recommendation given by someone 指由某人或某組織作出的建議或提案。"},{"en":"Students should follow the recommendation given by the teacher if it clearly improves their essay.","zh":"如果老師提出的建議能清楚改善文章，學生應跟從。"},{"en":"If a recommendation is given by an influential agency, schools may take it seriously.","zh":"如果建議由有影響力的機構提出，學校可能認真看待。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the source of a proposal.","zh":"這個片語指出提案的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"focus only on","meaning":"只專注於","examples":[{"en":"AACSB did not want schools to focus only on journal citations.","zh":"AACSB 不希望學校只專注於期刊引用次數。"},{"en":"To focus only on something means to pay attention to that thing and ignore other important factors.","zh":"To focus only on something 指只關注某事而忽視其他重要因素。"},{"en":"Students should not focus only on vocabulary while ignoring grammar and organisation.","zh":"學生不應只專注於詞彙，而忽視文法和組織。"},{"en":"If schools focus only on citations, they may miss research impact in the workplace.","zh":"如果學校只專注於引用次數，它們可能錯過研究在職場中的影響。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against a narrow view.","zh":"這個片語提醒不要採取狹窄看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"listing citations","meaning":"列出引用次數","examples":[{"en":"Listing citations alone may not show the value of research.","zh":"單是列出引用次數未必能顯示研究價值。"},{"en":"Listing citations means recording how often a piece of research is referred to by other academic works.","zh":"Listing citations 指記錄某項研究被其他學術作品引用多少次。"},{"en":"A professor may list citations to show that many scholars have used their article.","zh":"教授可能列出引用次數，以顯示許多學者使用過自己的文章。"},{"en":"If citations are listed without practical evidence, outsiders may still not see the research’s usefulness.","zh":"如果只列出引用次數而沒有實際證據，外界仍可能看不到研究實用性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes counting academic references as a measure of influence.","zh":"這個片語描述把學術引用計數作為影響力衡量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"research papers","meaning":"研究論文","examples":[{"en":"Research papers are often used to evaluate academic output.","zh":"研究論文常被用來評估學術產出。"},{"en":"Research papers are formal academic articles that present questions, methods, evidence, and conclusions.","zh":"Research papers 是呈現問題、方法、證據和結論的正式學術文章。"},{"en":"A university student may read research papers before writing a literature review.","zh":"大學生寫文獻回顧前，可能閱讀研究論文。"},{"en":"If professors must publish many research papers, they may have less time for teaching.","zh":"如果教授必須發表許多研究論文，他們可能較少時間教學。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to written academic studies.","zh":"這個片語指書面學術研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"consider the quantity of","meaning":"考慮……的數量","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether AACSB wanted to consider the quantity of academic publications.","zh":"該選項問 AACSB 是否想考慮學術出版物的數量。"},{"en":"To consider the quantity of something means to look at how many there are.","zh":"To consider the quantity of something 指查看某事物有多少。"},{"en":"A teacher may consider the quantity of homework, not only its difficulty.","zh":"老師可能考慮功課數量，而不只是其難度。"},{"en":"If evaluation considers only quantity, quality and usefulness may be overlooked.","zh":"如果評估只考慮數量，質素和實用性可能被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on amount rather than value.","zh":"這個片語集中於數量，而不是價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"evaluate how","meaning":"評估如何","examples":[{"en":"The recommendation was to evaluate how research influences the professional world.","zh":"該建議是評估研究如何影響專業世界。"},{"en":"To evaluate how something happens means to judge the way it works or produces effects.","zh":"To evaluate how something happens 指判斷某事如何運作或產生效果。"},{"en":"A school may evaluate how a new timetable affects students’ sleep.","zh":"學校可能評估新時間表如何影響學生睡眠。"},{"en":"If evaluators study how research influences practice, they need evidence from workplaces.","zh":"如果評估者研究研究如何影響實務，他們需要來自職場的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on judging the process or effect of something.","zh":"這個片語集中於判斷某事的過程或效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"influence the field","meaning":"影響某個領域","examples":[{"en":"Research may influence a field beyond academic journals.","zh":"研究可能在學術期刊以外影響某個領域。"},{"en":"To influence the field means to change thinking, practice, or standards in a professional or academic area.","zh":"To influence the field 指改變某專業或學術範疇中的思維、實務或標準。"},{"en":"A strong medical study can influence the field by changing how doctors treat patients.","zh":"強大的醫學研究可以透過改變醫生治療病人的方式來影響該領域。"},{"en":"If business research changes management practice, it influences the field outside universities.","zh":"如果商業研究改變管理實務，它就在大學以外影響該領域。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaningful impact within an area of work or study.","zh":"這個片語描述在工作或學習範疇內的有意義影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"maintain traditional academic models","meaning":"維持傳統學術模式","examples":[{"en":"Some universities want to maintain traditional academic models.","zh":"一些大學想維持傳統學術模式。"},{"en":"To maintain traditional academic models means to keep older systems of teaching, research, and evaluation.","zh":"To maintain traditional academic models 指保留較舊的教學、研究和評估制度。"},{"en":"A school may maintain traditional exams because teachers believe they are reliable.","zh":"學校可能維持傳統考試，因為老師相信它們可靠。"},{"en":"If universities maintain old models too strictly, they may fail to meet new career needs.","zh":"如果大學過分嚴格維持舊模式，它們可能未能滿足新職業需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preserving established academic systems.","zh":"這個片語描述保留既有學術制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"put forward the recommendation","meaning":"提出該建議","examples":[{"en":"The question asks why AACSB put forward the recommendation.","zh":"題目問 AACSB 為何提出該建議。"},{"en":"To put forward a recommendation means to formally suggest an idea for people to consider.","zh":"To put forward a recommendation 指正式提出一個想法供人考慮。"},{"en":"A student council may put forward a recommendation to extend library hours.","zh":"學生會可能提出延長圖書館開放時間的建議。"},{"en":"If an organisation puts forward a recommendation, it usually wants discussion or change.","zh":"如果組織提出建議，它通常希望引發討論或改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes presenting a proposal.","zh":"這個片語描述提出提案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"make full use of","meaning":"充分利用","examples":[{"en":"AACSB wanted schools to make full use of faculty members’ strengths.","zh":"AACSB 希望學校充分利用教職員的強項。"},{"en":"To make full use of something means to use it as completely and effectively as possible.","zh":"To make full use of something 指盡可能完整而有效地使用某事物。"},{"en":"Students can make full use of feedback by correcting mistakes and rewriting weak sentences.","zh":"學生可以透過改正錯誤和重寫弱句，充分利用回饋。"},{"en":"If schools make full use of different strengths, not every school needs to follow one model.","zh":"如果學校充分利用不同強項，不是每間學校都需要跟隨同一模式。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises using available resources well.","zh":"這個片語強調善用現有資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"faculty members’ strengths","meaning":"教職員的強項","examples":[{"en":"Schools should play to faculty members’ strengths.","zh":"學校應發揮教職員的強項。"},{"en":"Faculty members’ strengths are the areas where academic staff are especially capable, such as teaching, research, or industry work.","zh":"Faculty members’ strengths 是學術人員特別擅長的範疇，例如教學、研究或業界工作。"},{"en":"A professor with strong industry experience may help students understand real business problems.","zh":"具有豐富業界經驗的教授可能幫助學生理解真實商業問題。"},{"en":"If schools ignore faculty strengths, they may waste useful talent.","zh":"如果學校忽視教職員強項，它們可能浪費有用人才。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the best abilities of teaching and research staff.","zh":"這個片語描述教學和研究人員最好的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"reinforce a structure","meaning":"加強某種結構","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether AACSB wanted to reinforce universities’ pyramid structure.","zh":"該選項問 AACSB 是否想加強大學的金字塔結構。"},{"en":"To reinforce a structure means to strengthen or support an existing system or arrangement.","zh":"To reinforce a structure 指強化或支持現有制度或安排。"},{"en":"A school may reinforce a discipline structure by giving teachers clearer rules.","zh":"學校可能透過給老師更清楚規則來加強紀律結構。"},{"en":"If evaluation still rewards only top publications, it may reinforce the old academic hierarchy.","zh":"如果評估仍只獎勵頂尖出版物，它可能加強舊有學術等級制度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a system stronger rather than changing it.","zh":"這個片語描述令制度更強，而不是改變它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"push professors to","meaning":"推動教授去","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that AACSB wanted to push professors to publish papers.","zh":"該選項暗示 AACSB 想推動教授去發表論文。"},{"en":"To push professors to do something means to pressure or encourage them strongly to do it.","zh":"To push professors to do something 指強烈施壓或鼓勵教授做某事。"},{"en":"A department may push teachers to use more technology in lessons.","zh":"學系可能推動老師在課堂中使用更多科技。"},{"en":"If promotion rules push professors to publish, teaching may become less central.","zh":"如果晉升規則推動教授去發表，教學可能變得較不核心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pressure placed on academic staff.","zh":"這個片語描述施加在學術人員身上的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"reduce costs of research","meaning":"降低研究成本","examples":[{"en":"One possible reason was to reduce costs of research in universities.","zh":"一個可能原因是降低大學的研究成本。"},{"en":"To reduce costs of research means to lower the amount of money spent on doing research.","zh":"To reduce costs of research 指減少進行研究所花費的金錢。"},{"en":"A university may reduce research costs by sharing equipment between departments.","zh":"大學可能透過學系之間共用設備來降低研究成本。"},{"en":"If research spending is questioned, schools may look for cheaper ways to produce useful work.","zh":"如果研究開支受到質疑，學校可能尋找較便宜的方法產出有用工作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on cutting research expenses.","zh":"這個片語集中於削減研究開支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"mention the journal","meaning":"提及該期刊","examples":[{"en":"The question asks why the author mentions the journal Strategy & Leadership.","zh":"題目問作者為何提及《策略與領導》這本期刊。"},{"en":"To mention the journal means to refer to a particular academic or professional publication.","zh":"To mention the journal 指提到某一本特定學術或專業出版物。"},{"en":"A student may mention a journal to show where an idea came from.","zh":"學生可能提及期刊，以顯示某想法來自哪裏。"},{"en":"If an author mentions a journal, it may be to support a claim or give an example.","zh":"如果作者提及某期刊，可能是為了支持主張或提供例子。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the purpose of naming a source.","zh":"這個片語集中於命名來源的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"characterise something as","meaning":"將……描述為","examples":[{"en":"The author uses the journal to characterise research as irrelevant to performance.","zh":"作者使用該期刊把研究描述為與表現無關。"},{"en":"To characterise something as something means to describe it as having a particular quality.","zh":"To characterise something as something 指把某事描述為具有某種特質。"},{"en":"A teacher may characterise an essay as clear but underdeveloped.","zh":"老師可能把一篇文章描述為清楚但發展不足。"},{"en":"If critics characterise research as irrelevant, they are judging its practical usefulness negatively.","zh":"如果批評者把研究描述為無關，他們是在負面評價其實用性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how someone presents or labels a thing.","zh":"這個片語描述某人如何呈現或標籤某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"company performance","meaning":"公司表現","examples":[{"en":"The article argues that some research is irrelevant to company performance.","zh":"文章認為一些研究與公司表現無關。"},{"en":"Company performance means how well a company does in areas such as profit, growth, service, and efficiency.","zh":"Company performance 指公司在利潤、增長、服務和效率等方面表現如何。"},{"en":"A manager may track company performance by looking at sales, customer complaints, and staff turnover.","zh":"經理可能透過銷售、顧客投訴和員工流失來追蹤公司表現。"},{"en":"If research improves company performance, businesses are more likely to value it.","zh":"如果研究改善公司表現，企業更可能重視它。"},{"en":"This phrase measures how effectively a company operates.","zh":"這個片語衡量公司運作得多有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"suggest that","meaning":"表示；暗示","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that managers do not read research papers.","zh":"該選項暗示管理人員不閱讀研究論文。"},{"en":"Suggest that means to indicate or imply that something may be true.","zh":"Suggest that 指顯示或暗示某事可能是真實的。"},{"en":"Falling attendance may suggest that students are losing interest in the course.","zh":"出席率下降可能暗示學生正在失去對課程的興趣。"},{"en":"If evidence suggests a problem, leaders should investigate before making conclusions.","zh":"如果證據顯示有問題，領導者應先調查再下結論。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a careful claim rather than absolute certainty.","zh":"這個片語引出謹慎主張，而不是絕對確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"students’ expectations for","meaning":"學生對……的期望","examples":[{"en":"The question includes an option about students’ expectations for universities.","zh":"題目包括一個關於學生對大學期望的選項。"},{"en":"Students’ expectations for something are what students believe it should provide or achieve.","zh":"Students’ expectations for something 是學生相信某事應提供或達成的東西。"},{"en":"Students’ expectations for a language course may include clear notes, useful practice, and feedback.","zh":"學生對語言課程的期望可能包括清楚筆記、有用練習和回饋。"},{"en":"If universities do not meet students’ expectations, students may feel their tuition is wasted.","zh":"如果大學未能滿足學生期望，學生可能覺得學費被浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what students hope or demand from an institution.","zh":"這個片語描述學生對機構的希望或要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"exemplify high-quality research papers","meaning":"舉例說明高質素研究論文","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether the journal is used to exemplify high-quality research papers.","zh":"該選項問該期刊是否用來舉例說明高質素研究論文。"},{"en":"To exemplify high-quality research papers means to serve as an example of strong academic work.","zh":"To exemplify high-quality research papers 指作為強大學術作品的例子。"},{"en":"A teacher may show one essay to exemplify clear structure and strong evidence.","zh":"老師可能展示一篇文章，以舉例說明清晰結構和有力證據。"},{"en":"If a source is used to exemplify quality, the writer is presenting it as a positive model.","zh":"如果來源被用來舉例說明質素，作者是在把它呈現為正面典範。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using something as an example of excellence.","zh":"這個片語描述用某事作為卓越例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be consistent with","meaning":"與……一致","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which statements are consistent with Pfeffer and Fong’s views.","zh":"學生辨認哪些陳述與 Pfeffer 和 Fong 的觀點一致。"},{"en":"To be consistent with something means to agree with it and not contradict it.","zh":"To be consistent with something 指與某事相符，而不相矛盾。"},{"en":"A student’s answer is consistent with the passage if it matches the writer’s meaning.","zh":"如果學生答案符合文章意思，它就與文章一致。"},{"en":"If a statement is consistent with an author’s view, it supports rather than opposes that view.","zh":"如果陳述與作者觀點一致，它就是支持而不是反對該觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading questions about opinions and claims.","zh":"這個片語常見於關於觀點和主張的閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"attend universities","meaning":"入讀大學","examples":[{"en":"Students pay tuition to attend universities.","zh":"學生繳交學費入讀大學。"},{"en":"To attend universities means to study at universities as enrolled students.","zh":"To attend universities 指以註冊學生身份在大學學習。"},{"en":"Many students attend universities to gain knowledge, qualifications, and career opportunities.","zh":"許多學生入讀大學，以獲得知識、資格和事業機會。"},{"en":"If students pay to attend universities, they may expect teaching that prepares them for work.","zh":"如果學生付費入讀大學，他們可能期望教學能讓他們為工作作準備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes participation in higher education.","zh":"這個片語描述參與高等教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"not doing its job well","meaning":"未能有效履行職責","examples":[{"en":"The study suggested that business education was not doing its job well.","zh":"該研究指出商業教育未能有效履行職責。"},{"en":"Not doing its job well means failing to perform the function it is supposed to perform.","zh":"Not doing its job well 指未能履行其應該履行的功能。"},{"en":"A timetable is not doing its job well if students are always late because lessons are too close together.","zh":"如果課堂相隔太近令學生總是遲到，時間表就是未能有效履行職責。"},{"en":"If business education does not prepare students for careers, critics may say it is failing.","zh":"如果商業教育未能讓學生為事業作準備，批評者可能說它失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises poor performance against expected duties.","zh":"這個片語批評某事未能達到預期職責。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"focus on writing papers","meaning":"專注於撰寫論文","examples":[{"en":"Some professors focus heavily on writing papers.","zh":"一些教授非常專注於撰寫論文。"},{"en":"To focus on writing papers means to spend much attention and effort producing academic articles.","zh":"To focus on writing papers 指花大量注意力和努力產出學術文章。"},{"en":"A lecturer may focus on writing papers because promotion depends on publications.","zh":"講師可能因晉升取決於出版物而專注於撰寫論文。"},{"en":"If professors focus too much on papers, students may receive less mentoring.","zh":"如果教授過分專注於論文，學生可能得到較少指導。"},{"en":"This phrase describes prioritising academic publication work.","zh":"這個片語描述把學術出版工作置於優先。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be ill-prepared for","meaning":"對……準備不足","examples":[{"en":"Students may be ill-prepared for their future careers.","zh":"學生可能對未來事業準備不足。"},{"en":"To be ill-prepared for something means to lack the skills, knowledge, or experience needed for it.","zh":"To be ill-prepared for something 指缺乏應付某事所需的技能、知識或經驗。"},{"en":"A student may be ill-prepared for an interview if they have never practised answering questions aloud.","zh":"如果學生從未練習大聲回答問題，他可能對面試準備不足。"},{"en":"If university courses ignore real business problems, graduates may feel unready for work.","zh":"如果大學課程忽視真實商業問題，畢業生可能覺得未準備好工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes poor preparation before facing a challenge.","zh":"這個片語描述面對挑戰前準備不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"recognised accrediting agency","meaning":"獲認可的認證機構","examples":[{"en":"A recognised accrediting agency can influence how schools are evaluated.","zh":"獲認可的認證機構可以影響學校如何被評估。"},{"en":"A recognised accrediting agency is an accepted organisation that officially judges whether institutions meet standards.","zh":"Recognised accrediting agency 是被接受、正式判斷機構是否符合標準的組織。"},{"en":"A university may value a recognised accrediting agency because employers and students trust its approval.","zh":"大學可能重視獲認可的認證機構，因為僱主和學生信任其認可。"},{"en":"If such an agency changes standards, schools may change their behaviour.","zh":"如果這類機構改變標準，學校可能改變行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an authoritative body that gives formal recognition.","zh":"這個片語描述給予正式認可的權威機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"evaluate research effectively","meaning":"有效評估研究","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether an accrediting agency can evaluate research effectively.","zh":"該選項問認證機構是否能有效評估研究。"},{"en":"To evaluate research effectively means to judge research in a fair, accurate, and useful way.","zh":"To evaluate research effectively 指以公平、準確而有用的方式判斷研究。"},{"en":"A teacher evaluates research effectively by checking evidence, method, originality, and relevance.","zh":"老師透過檢查證據、方法、原創性和相關性來有效評估研究。"},{"en":"If an agency evaluates research poorly, schools may chase the wrong goals.","zh":"如果機構評估研究做得差，學校可能追逐錯誤目標。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the quality of the evaluation process.","zh":"這個片語集中於評估過程的質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether statements agree with the information given.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與所給資料相符。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage states or implies.","zh":"To agree with the information given 指與文章所陳述或暗示的內容相配。"},{"en":"If a passage says research is expensive, a statement saying research costs money agrees with the information given.","zh":"如果文章說研究昂貴，陳述說研究花錢就是與所給資料相符。"},{"en":"Students should check exact meaning before deciding TRUE.","zh":"學生應在決定 TRUE 前檢查確切意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN reading tasks.","zh":"這個片語常見於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章中的資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"To contradict the information 指說出與文章內容相反的意思。"},{"en":"If a passage says most students work outside academia, a statement saying most become professors contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說大多數學生在學術界以外工作，陳述說大多數成為教授就是與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should look for direct opposition, not merely different wording.","zh":"學生應尋找直接相反，而不是僅僅不同措辭。"},{"en":"This phrase explains when an answer should be FALSE.","zh":"這個片語解釋答案何時應為 FALSE。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students choose “NOT GIVEN” when there is no information on this.","zh":"當文中沒有相關資料，學生選擇 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"There is no information on this 指文章沒有說明陳述是真是假。"},{"en":"If a passage discusses tuition but not student age, a claim about age may be NOT GIVEN.","zh":"如果文章討論學費但沒有討論學生年齡，關於年齡的說法可能是 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when the passage gives no evidence.","zh":"當文章沒有提供證據，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the logic of NOT GIVEN answers.","zh":"這個片語解釋 NOT GIVEN 答案的邏輯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"usefulness of academic research","meaning":"學術研究的實用性","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the usefulness of academic research for business practice.","zh":"文章討論學術研究對商業實務的實用性。"},{"en":"Usefulness of academic research means how much scholarly work helps people understand or solve real problems.","zh":"Usefulness of academic research 指學術作品在多大程度上幫助人理解或解決真實問題。"},{"en":"A teacher may judge the usefulness of academic research by whether it improves classroom methods.","zh":"老師可能透過研究是否改善課堂方法來判斷學術研究的實用性。"},{"en":"If managers cannot apply a study, its usefulness to business may be limited.","zh":"如果管理人員不能應用某研究，它對商業的實用性可能有限。"},{"en":"This phrase evaluates research by its practical value.","zh":"這個片語按實際價值評估研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"a recent one","meaning":"近期才出現的事情","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether the debate is a recent one.","zh":"題目問這場辯論是否是近期才出現的事情。"},{"en":"A recent one means something that began or happened not long ago.","zh":"Recent one 指不久前才開始或發生的事情。"},{"en":"Online learning is a recent one among many education debates compared with homework and exams.","zh":"與功課和考試相比，網上學習是眾多教育辯論中較近期才出現的事情。"},{"en":"If a debate began decades ago, it is not a recent one.","zh":"如果辯論數十年前已開始，它就不是近期才出現的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies whether an issue is new or longstanding.","zh":"這個片語判斷某議題是新的還是長久存在的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"be reviewed externally","meaning":"由外部審閱","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether AACSB’s draft report was reviewed externally.","zh":"該陳述問 AACSB 的報告草稿是否由外部審閱。"},{"en":"To be reviewed externally means to be checked by people outside the organisation or group that wrote it.","zh":"To be reviewed externally 指由撰寫它的組織或群體以外的人檢查。"},{"en":"A school policy may be reviewed externally by education experts before it is adopted.","zh":"學校政策在採用前，可能由教育專家作外部審閱。"},{"en":"External review can make a report more credible because outsiders may notice hidden problems.","zh":"外部審閱可以令報告更可信，因為外人可能注意到隱藏問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes review by outside people, not only internal staff.","zh":"這個片語描述由外部人士而不只是內部員工審閱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"spend yearly on","meaning":"每年花費在……上","examples":[{"en":"Business schools spend large amounts yearly on research.","zh":"商學院每年在研究上花費大量金錢。"},{"en":"To spend yearly on something means to use money for it every year.","zh":"To spend yearly on something 指每年為某事花錢。"},{"en":"A family may spend yearly on school fees, uniforms, and transport.","zh":"家庭可能每年花費在學費、校服和交通上。"},{"en":"If an institution spends heavily every year, people may question whether the spending brings results.","zh":"如果機構每年大量花費，人們可能質疑該支出是否帶來成果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regular annual spending.","zh":"這個片語描述定期年度支出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"pursue professional outputs","meaning":"追求專業成果","examples":[{"en":"Some schools may choose to pursue professional outputs.","zh":"一些學校可能選擇追求專業成果。"},{"en":"To pursue professional outputs means to actively work toward career-related results such as placements, partnerships, and practical skills.","zh":"To pursue professional outputs 指主動追求就業安排、合作和實用技能等與事業相關的成果。"},{"en":"A college may pursue professional outputs by building internships into every programme.","zh":"學院可能透過把實習納入每個課程來追求專業成果。"},{"en":"If schools pursue professional outcomes, students may see clearer links between study and work.","zh":"如果學校追求專業成果，學生可能看見學習與工作之間更清楚的聯繫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing practical career results as a goal.","zh":"這個片語描述把實際職業成果選為目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"benefit professors and students alike","meaning":"同時惠及教授和學生","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether publications benefit professors and students alike.","zh":"該陳述問出版物是否同時惠及教授和學生。"},{"en":"To benefit professors and students alike means to help both groups equally or in a similar way.","zh":"To benefit professors and students alike 指同等或以相似方式幫助兩個群體。"},{"en":"Clear course materials can benefit teachers and students alike because lessons run more smoothly.","zh":"清楚課程材料可以同時惠及老師和學生，因為課堂進行得更順利。"},{"en":"If publications help professors’ careers but not students’ learning, they do not benefit both alike.","zh":"如果出版物幫助教授事業但不幫助學生學習，它們就沒有同時惠及兩者。"},{"en":"This phrase compares whether two groups gain from the same thing.","zh":"這個片語比較兩個群體是否從同一事物中受益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"complete each sentence with","meaning":"用……完成每句","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete each sentence with the correct ending.","zh":"考生用正確結尾完成每句。"},{"en":"To complete each sentence with something means to choose or add words that finish the sentence correctly.","zh":"To complete each sentence with something 指選擇或加入字詞，使句子正確完成。"},{"en":"In a grammar exercise, students complete each sentence with the correct verb form.","zh":"在文法練習中，學生用正確動詞形式完成每句。"},{"en":"If the ending does not match the meaning, the completed sentence will be wrong.","zh":"如果結尾不符合意思，完成後的句子就會錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in sentence-completion tasks.","zh":"這個片語是句子完成題中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"the correct ending","meaning":"正確結尾","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct ending for each sentence.","zh":"學生為每句選擇正確結尾。"},{"en":"The correct ending is the option that completes a sentence logically and grammatically.","zh":"Correct ending 是能在邏輯和文法上完成句子的選項。"},{"en":"A student should check subject, meaning, and grammar before choosing the correct ending.","zh":"學生選擇正確結尾前，應檢查主語、意思和文法。"},{"en":"If two endings sound possible, the passage meaning decides which one is correct.","zh":"如果兩個結尾聽起來都可能，文章意思決定哪一個正確。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the right final part of a sentence-completion answer.","zh":"這個片語指句子完成答案中正確的最後部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"support academic research","meaning":"支持學術研究","examples":[{"en":"Most professors support academic research because their careers depend on it.","zh":"大多數教授支持學術研究，因為他們的事業取決於此。"},{"en":"To support academic research means to value, defend, fund, or take part in scholarly study.","zh":"To support academic research 指重視、捍衛、資助或參與學術研究。"},{"en":"A university may support academic research by giving professors time and grants.","zh":"大學可能透過給教授時間和資助來支持學術研究。"},{"en":"If careers depend on publications, professors have strong reasons to support research.","zh":"如果事業取決於出版物，教授就有強烈理由支持研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes backing the system of scholarly work.","zh":"這個片語描述支持學術工作制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"their jobs depend on it","meaning":"他們的工作取決於此","examples":[{"en":"Professors publish research because their jobs depend on it.","zh":"教授發表研究，因為他們的工作取決於此。"},{"en":"Their jobs depend on it means keeping or advancing their employment relies on that thing.","zh":"Their jobs depend on it 指保住或推進工作依賴某事。"},{"en":"Sales staff may study product details carefully because their jobs depend on customer trust.","zh":"銷售員可能仔細學習產品細節，因為他們的工作取決於顧客信任。"},{"en":"If professors’ jobs depend on publication records, they will prioritise publishing.","zh":"如果教授的工作取決於發表紀錄，他們會優先處理出版。"},{"en":"This phrase explains pressure created by employment requirements.","zh":"這個片語解釋由工作要求造成的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"school rankings","meaning":"學校排名","examples":[{"en":"Schools may support research because they care about school rankings.","zh":"學校可能支持研究，因為它們重視學校排名。"},{"en":"School rankings are lists that compare schools according to selected measures such as research, reputation, or graduate outcomes.","zh":"School rankings 是根據研究、聲譽或畢業生成果等所選標準比較學校的列表。"},{"en":"Parents may look at school rankings before choosing a university for their child.","zh":"家長可能在為孩子選大學前查看學校排名。"},{"en":"If rankings reward research output, schools may invest more in publications.","zh":"如果排名獎勵研究產出，學校可能在出版物上投資更多。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to comparative league tables of educational institutions.","zh":"這個片語指教育機構的比較排行榜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"government funds","meaning":"政府資金","examples":[{"en":"Some schools care about research because it affects government funds.","zh":"一些學校重視研究，因為它影響政府資金。"},{"en":"Government funds are money provided by the government to support institutions, projects, or services.","zh":"Government funds 是由政府提供，用來支持機構、項目或服務的金錢。"},{"en":"A public university may use government funds to support teaching, research, and student services.","zh":"公立大學可能使用政府資金支持教學、研究和學生服務。"},{"en":"If government funds depend on research results, universities may compete strongly for publications.","zh":"如果政府資金取決於研究結果，大學可能在出版物上激烈競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to public money given for institutional support.","zh":"這個片語指用於機構支援的公共金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"innovative ways of doing things","meaning":"做事的創新方法","examples":[{"en":"Society progresses as people learn innovative ways of doing things.","zh":"隨着人們學會做事的創新方法，社會便會進步。"},{"en":"Innovative ways of doing things are new and better methods for solving problems or completing tasks.","zh":"Innovative ways of doing things 是解決問題或完成任務的新而更好的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may use innovative ways of teaching vocabulary through stories and games.","zh":"老師可能透過故事和遊戲，使用教授詞彙的創新方法。"},{"en":"If businesses find innovative ways of serving customers, they may become more competitive.","zh":"如果企業找到服務顧客的創新方法，它們可能變得更具競爭力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical creativity in action.","zh":"這個片語描述行動中的實用創意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"resist the AACSB","meaning":"抵制 AACSB","examples":[{"en":"Universities resisting the AACSB may still need to change.","zh":"抵制 AACSB 的大學可能仍然需要改變。"},{"en":"To resist the AACSB means to oppose or refuse to accept AACSB’s proposals or standards.","zh":"To resist the AACSB 指反對或拒絕接受 AACSB 的提案或標準。"},{"en":"A school may resist an outside agency if it believes the new rules are unfair.","zh":"如果學校認為新規則不公平，它可能抵制外部機構。"},{"en":"If universities resist too strongly, they may appear unwilling to adapt.","zh":"如果大學過分強烈抵制，它們可能顯得不願適應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes opposition to an influential accrediting body.","zh":"這個片語描述對有影響力認證機構的反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"trends and standards are changing","meaning":"趨勢和標準正在改變","examples":[{"en":"Universities must adapt because trends and standards are changing.","zh":"大學必須適應，因為趨勢和標準正在改變。"},{"en":"Trends and standards are changing means common practices and evaluation expectations are becoming different.","zh":"Trends and standards are changing 指常見做法和評估期望正在變得不同。"},{"en":"Teaching methods are changing when more schools value projects, discussion, and digital skills.","zh":"當更多學校重視專題、討論和數碼技能，教學方法就正在改變。"},{"en":"If standards change, institutions that refuse to adapt may fall behind.","zh":"如果標準改變，拒絕適應的機構可能落後。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why organisations cannot rely only on old habits.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何組織不能只依賴舊習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 49 - Theory or Practice? —What is the point of research carried out by biz schools?.pdf","sourcePage":24}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 50":[{"front":"Scottish novelist, poet, essayist and travel writer","meaning":"蘇格蘭小說家、詩人、散文家及旅遊作家","examples":[{"en":"Robert Louis Stevenson was a Scottish novelist, poet, essayist and travel writer.","zh":"Robert Louis Stevenson 是蘇格蘭小說家、詩人、散文家及旅遊作家。"},{"en":"A Scottish novelist, poet, essayist and travel writer is a writer from Scotland who works across several literary forms.","zh":"Scottish novelist, poet, essayist and travel writer 指來自蘇格蘭、橫跨多種文學形式創作的作家。"},{"en":"A writer may be known as a novelist, poet and essayist if they publish fiction, poems and reflective prose.","zh":"如果一位作家出版小說、詩和抒情散文，他可能被稱為小說家、詩人和散文家。"},{"en":"When an author writes in several genres, critics may judge their talent from many different angles.","zh":"當作者創作多種體裁，評論家可能從許多不同角度評價其才華。"},{"en":"This description shows that Stevenson was not limited to one type of writing.","zh":"這個描述顯示 Stevenson 並不局限於一種寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"was born in","meaning":"出生於……","examples":[{"en":"Robert Louis Stevenson was born in Edinburgh, Scotland.","zh":"Robert Louis Stevenson 出生於蘇格蘭愛丁堡。"},{"en":"Was born in means came into the world in a particular place or year.","zh":"was born in 指在某個地方或年份出生。"},{"en":"A student may write that their grandfather was born in a small village before moving to the city.","zh":"學生可能寫自己的祖父出生於一條小村，後來搬到城市。"},{"en":"Knowing where a writer was born can help readers understand the culture that shaped them.","zh":"知道一位作家出生在哪裡，可以幫助讀者理解塑造他的文化。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to give basic biographical information.","zh":"這個片語用來提供基本傳記資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"more than a century after","meaning":"在……一個多世紀後","examples":[{"en":"More than a century after his death, Stevenson’s work continues to divide opinion.","zh":"在他去世一個多世紀後，Stevenson 的作品仍繼續令意見分歧。"},{"en":"More than a century after means over one hundred years later than a particular event.","zh":"more than a century after 指在某事件之後超過一百年。"},{"en":"More than a century after a school was founded, its old buildings may still shape its identity.","zh":"在一所學校創立一個多世紀後，其舊建築可能仍塑造其身份。"},{"en":"If a writer is still debated more than a century after death, their work has lasting influence.","zh":"如果一位作家去世一個多世紀後仍被爭論，其作品就有持久影響。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a long period of time after an event.","zh":"這個片語強調事件之後的一段很長時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"continue to divide opinion","meaning":"繼續令意見分歧","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s work continues to divide opinion among critics.","zh":"Stevenson 的作品在評論家之間繼續令意見分歧。"},{"en":"Continue to divide opinion means still cause people to hold different views.","zh":"continue to divide opinion 指仍然令人持有不同看法。"},{"en":"A new school rule may continue to divide opinion if some students see it as fair and others see it as too strict.","zh":"如果有些學生認為新校規公平，而另一些認為太嚴，它可能繼續令意見分歧。"},{"en":"When a book divides opinion, some readers praise it while others strongly criticise it.","zh":"當一本書令意見分歧，有些讀者會讚賞它，另一些則強烈批評。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that disagreement has not disappeared.","zh":"這個片語顯示分歧尚未消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on the one hand","meaning":"一方面","examples":[{"en":"On the one hand, many critics praised Stevenson’s prose and style.","zh":"一方面，許多評論家讚賞 Stevenson 的散文文筆和風格。"},{"en":"On the one hand introduces one side of an argument or comparison.","zh":"on the one hand 用來引出論點或比較中的其中一面。"},{"en":"On the one hand, online lessons are convenient; on the other hand, students may feel isolated.","zh":"一方面，網上課堂很方便；另一方面，學生可能感到孤立。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when they want to present a balanced discussion.","zh":"作者想呈現平衡討論時會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"The phrase prepares the reader for another contrasting point later.","zh":"這個片語讓讀者預期稍後會出現另一個對比點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be highly praised for","meaning":"因……而備受讚賞","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson was highly praised for his expert prose and style.","zh":"Stevenson 因其精湛的散文文筆和風格而備受讚賞。"},{"en":"Be highly praised for means receive strong approval because of a particular quality or achievement.","zh":"be highly praised for 指因某種特質或成就而獲得高度認可。"},{"en":"A student may be highly praised for a clear presentation that helps the whole class understand a topic.","zh":"學生可能因清晰演講幫助全班理解課題而備受讚賞。"},{"en":"If a writer is praised for style, critics admire not only the story but also the way it is written.","zh":"如果作家因風格受讚賞，評論家欣賞的不只是故事，還有其寫法。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the reason for strong admiration.","zh":"這個片語突出強烈欣賞的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"expert prose and style","meaning":"精湛的散文文筆和風格","examples":[{"en":"Many critics admired Stevenson’s expert prose and style.","zh":"許多評論家欣賞 Stevenson 精湛的散文文筆和風格。"},{"en":"Expert prose and style means skilful writing in sentences, rhythm, word choice and overall expression.","zh":"expert prose and style 指句子、節奏、用字和整體表達上的高超寫作技巧。"},{"en":"A teacher may praise a student’s prose and style when the essay is clear, smooth and precise.","zh":"當文章清楚、流暢而精準，老師可能讚賞學生的文筆和風格。"},{"en":"Strong prose can make even a simple story feel vivid and memorable.","zh":"強大的散文文筆可以令簡單故事也變得生動難忘。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on writing craft rather than only plot.","zh":"這個片語集中於寫作工藝，而不只是情節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"English-language critics","meaning":"英語文學評論家","examples":[{"en":"Many English-language critics praised Stevenson’s writing.","zh":"許多英語文學評論家讚賞 Stevenson 的寫作。"},{"en":"English-language critics are critics who write or work mainly in English literary culture.","zh":"English-language critics 指主要以英語文學文化寫作或工作的評論家。"},{"en":"English-language critics may review novels from Scotland, America, Canada or other English-speaking places.","zh":"英語文學評論家可能評論蘇格蘭、美國、加拿大或其他英語地區的小說。"},{"en":"If English-language critics praise a writer, the writer’s reputation may grow in English literary circles.","zh":"如果英語文學評論家讚賞一位作家，該作家在英語文學圈中的聲譽可能上升。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the language and literary community of the critics.","zh":"這個片語指出評論家的語言和文學社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"On the other hand, some critics attacked the religious themes in his works.","zh":"另一方面，有些評論家攻擊他作品中的宗教主題。"},{"en":"On the other hand introduces a contrasting point or different side of an issue.","zh":"on the other hand 用來引出對比點或議題的另一面。"},{"en":"On the other hand, a small class gives more attention, but it may cost more.","zh":"另一方面，小班教學能給予更多關注，但可能成本更高。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when two ideas are both important but pull in different directions.","zh":"當兩個想法都重要但方向不同，這個片語很有用。"},{"en":"It often follows “on the one hand” in balanced writing.","zh":"它在平衡寫作中常跟在 “on the one hand” 之後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"criticise the religious themes in","meaning":"批評……中的宗教主題","examples":[{"en":"Some critics criticised the religious themes in Stevenson’s works.","zh":"有些評論家批評 Stevenson 作品中的宗教主題。"},{"en":"To criticise the religious themes in a work means to object to or judge its treatment of religion.","zh":"criticise the religious themes in a work 指反對或評判作品對宗教的處理。"},{"en":"A parent may criticise the religious themes in a film if they feel the topic is handled unfairly.","zh":"如果家長覺得電影不公平地處理宗教題材，可能會批評其中的宗教主題。"},{"en":"If critics misunderstand a writer’s beliefs, their criticism of religious themes may be too harsh.","zh":"如果評論家誤解作家的信念，他們對宗教主題的批評可能過於嚴厲。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that criticism is aimed at the religious content of a work.","zh":"這個片語顯示批評針對作品中的宗教內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"religious beliefs","meaning":"宗教信念","examples":[{"en":"Some critics misunderstood Stevenson’s own religious beliefs.","zh":"有些評論家誤解了 Stevenson 自己的宗教信念。"},{"en":"Religious beliefs are a person’s ideas about God, faith, worship or spiritual truth.","zh":"religious beliefs 指一個人對上帝、信仰、崇拜或精神真理的看法。"},{"en":"A family’s religious beliefs may affect how they celebrate festivals or make moral decisions.","zh":"家庭的宗教信念可能影響他們如何慶祝節日或作道德決定。"},{"en":"If readers confuse a character’s words with the author’s religious beliefs, they may misread the text.","zh":"如果讀者把角色的說話混同於作者的宗教信念，就可能誤讀文本。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to personal faith or views about religion.","zh":"這個片語指個人的信仰或對宗教的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"misunderstand someone’s beliefs","meaning":"誤解某人的信念","examples":[{"en":"Some readers misunderstood Stevenson’s religious beliefs.","zh":"有些讀者誤解了 Stevenson 的宗教信念。"},{"en":"Misunderstand someone’s beliefs means wrongly interpret what a person truly thinks or values.","zh":"misunderstand someone’s beliefs 指錯誤理解某人真正的想法或價值觀。"},{"en":"A teacher may misunderstand a quiet student’s beliefs if they assume silence means agreement.","zh":"如果老師以為沉默就代表同意，可能會誤解安靜學生的信念。"},{"en":"Misunderstanding a writer’s beliefs can lead to unfair criticism of their work.","zh":"誤解作家的信念可能導致對其作品作出不公平批評。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a mistake in interpreting someone’s inner views.","zh":"這個片語顯示對某人內在觀點的錯誤理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"since his death","meaning":"自他去世以來","examples":[{"en":"Since his death, critics have disagreed about his literary legacy.","zh":"自他去世以來，評論家一直對他的文學遺產意見不一。"},{"en":"Since his death means from the time he died until the present or a later point.","zh":"since his death 指從他去世那一刻直到現在或較後時間。"},{"en":"Since her death, the school has held an annual prize in her memory.","zh":"自她去世以來，學校每年設立獎項紀念她。"},{"en":"If debate continues since an author’s death, their work still matters to later generations.","zh":"如果作家去世後爭論仍持續，其作品對後世仍然重要。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a time period beginning with someone’s death.","zh":"這個片語給出由某人死亡開始的一段時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"critics and biographers","meaning":"評論家和傳記作家","examples":[{"en":"Critics and biographers have disagreed on Stevenson’s legacy.","zh":"評論家和傳記作家對 Stevenson 的遺產意見不一。"},{"en":"Critics and biographers are people who evaluate literature and people who write accounts of someone’s life.","zh":"critics and biographers 指評價文學的人，以及撰寫某人生平記述的人。"},{"en":"Critics may focus on a writer’s books, while biographers may focus on life events and relationships.","zh":"評論家可能集中於作家的書，而傳記作家可能集中於生平事件和人際關係。"},{"en":"If critics and biographers disagree, a writer’s reputation can become complicated.","zh":"如果評論家和傳記作家意見不一，作家的聲譽就可能變得複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase brings together literary judgement and life-writing.","zh":"這個片語把文學判斷和人生書寫結合起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"disagree on","meaning":"對……意見不一","examples":[{"en":"Critics and biographers disagree on the legacy of Stevenson’s writing.","zh":"評論家和傳記作家對 Stevenson 寫作的遺產意見不一。"},{"en":"Disagree on means have different opinions about a particular matter.","zh":"disagree on 指對某個特定事項持有不同意見。"},{"en":"Parents may disagree on how much screen time a child should have.","zh":"父母可能對孩子應有多少螢幕時間意見不一。"},{"en":"When experts disagree on a book, students should examine the evidence behind each view.","zh":"當專家對一本書意見不一，學生應檢視每種看法背後的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the topic of disagreement.","zh":"這個片語指出分歧的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the legacy of","meaning":"……的遺產；……留下的影響","examples":[{"en":"Critics continue to debate the legacy of Stevenson’s writing.","zh":"評論家繼續爭論 Stevenson 寫作留下的影響。"},{"en":"The legacy of something is the lasting influence or effect it leaves behind.","zh":"legacy of something 指某事物留下的持久影響或效果。"},{"en":"The legacy of a good teacher may be students who still love reading years later.","zh":"好老師留下的遺產，可能是多年後仍熱愛閱讀的學生。"},{"en":"If a writer’s stories shape later authors, that influence becomes part of their legacy.","zh":"如果作家的故事塑造後來作者，這種影響就成為其遺產的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on what remains after a person or work is gone.","zh":"這個片語集中於人或作品離開後仍留下的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a clear focus","meaning":"清晰的重點","examples":[{"en":"Two biographers wrote a biography of Stevenson with a clear focus.","zh":"兩位傳記作家寫了一本關於 Stevenson、具有清晰重點的傳記。"},{"en":"A clear focus is a specific main direction or purpose.","zh":"clear focus 指明確的主要方向或目的。"},{"en":"A student’s essay needs a clear focus so every paragraph supports the same argument.","zh":"學生文章需要清晰重點，讓每段都支持同一論點。"},{"en":"If a biography has a clear focus, readers know what aspect of the person matters most.","zh":"如果傳記有清晰重點，讀者就知道人物哪方面最重要。"},{"en":"The phrase means the work is not scattered or confusing.","zh":"這個片語意思是作品不零散、不混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"choose not to","meaning":"選擇不去……","examples":[{"en":"The biographers chose not to criticise aspects of Stevenson’s personal life.","zh":"傳記作家選擇不去批評 Stevenson 私生活的某些方面。"},{"en":"Choose not to means deliberately decide against doing something.","zh":"choose not to 指有意識地決定不做某事。"},{"en":"A student may choose not to join a debate if they are not ready to speak publicly.","zh":"如果學生尚未準備好公開發言，可能選擇不參加辯論。"},{"en":"If writers choose not to discuss scandals, they may want readers to focus on the work itself.","zh":"如果作者選擇不討論醜聞，可能希望讀者集中於作品本身。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a conscious decision, not an accident.","zh":"這個片語顯示有意識的決定，而不是意外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"criticise aspects of","meaning":"批評……的某些方面","examples":[{"en":"They chose not to criticise aspects of Stevenson’s personal life.","zh":"他們選擇不去批評 Stevenson 私生活的某些方面。"},{"en":"Criticise aspects of something means judge or attack particular parts of it.","zh":"criticise aspects of something 指評判或攻擊某事物的特定部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may criticise aspects of an essay, such as weak evidence or unclear structure.","zh":"老師可能批評文章的某些方面，例如證據薄弱或結構不清。"},{"en":"Critics may accept a writer’s talent while still criticising aspects of their behaviour.","zh":"評論家可能承認作家的才華，同時仍批評其行為的某些方面。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses criticism on selected parts, not the whole thing.","zh":"這個片語把批評集中於部分，而不是整體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"personal life","meaning":"私生活","examples":[{"en":"Some critics focused too heavily on Stevenson’s personal life.","zh":"有些評論家過度集中於 Stevenson 的私生活。"},{"en":"Personal life means the private parts of someone’s life, such as family, relationships, health and habits.","zh":"personal life 指某人生活中的私人部分，例如家庭、關係、健康和習慣。"},{"en":"A celebrity’s personal life may attract attention even when their work is more important.","zh":"名人私生活可能吸引注意，即使其作品更重要。"},{"en":"If critics focus only on personal life, they may ignore literary skill.","zh":"如果評論家只集中於私生活，可能忽略文學技巧。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts private life with public work or professional achievement.","zh":"這個片語把私人生活與公開工作或專業成就作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"instead","meaning":"相反；而是","examples":[{"en":"Instead, the biographers focused on Stevenson’s writing.","zh":"相反，傳記作家集中於 Stevenson 的寫作。"},{"en":"Instead means as an alternative or in place of something else.","zh":"instead 指作為替代，或取代另一件事。"},{"en":"A student may skip social media and read a novel instead.","zh":"學生可能不看社交媒體，而是讀小說。"},{"en":"If one approach is unhelpful, choosing another approach instead can change the result.","zh":"如果一種方法無幫助，改用另一種方法可能改變結果。"},{"en":"The word shows replacement or contrast.","zh":"這個詞顯示取代或對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"集中於……","examples":[{"en":"The biographers focused on Stevenson’s writing and style.","zh":"傳記作家集中於 Stevenson 的寫作和風格。"},{"en":"Focus on means give most attention to a particular thing.","zh":"focus on 指把大部分注意力放在某事上。"},{"en":"A student should focus on the question before writing an essay.","zh":"學生在寫文章前應集中於題目。"},{"en":"If a biography focuses on writing style, it may discuss language more than private habits.","zh":"如果傳記集中於寫作風格，它可能較多討論語言，而非私人習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase shows where attention is directed.","zh":"這個片語顯示注意力放在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"give high praise to","meaning":"高度讚揚……","examples":[{"en":"The biographers gave high praise to Stevenson’s writing style and skill.","zh":"傳記作家高度讚揚 Stevenson 的寫作風格和技巧。"},{"en":"Give high praise to means strongly admire or approve of someone or something.","zh":"give high praise to 指強烈欣賞或認可某人或某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may give high praise to a student who improves through steady effort.","zh":"老師可能高度讚揚透過穩定努力進步的學生。"},{"en":"High praise can improve a writer’s reputation when it comes from respected critics.","zh":"當高度讚揚來自受尊重評論家，它可以提升作家聲譽。"},{"en":"The phrase shows strong positive judgement.","zh":"這個片語顯示強烈正面評價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"writing style and skill","meaning":"寫作風格和技巧","examples":[{"en":"The biography gave high praise to Stevenson’s writing style and skill.","zh":"該傳記高度讚揚 Stevenson 的寫作風格和技巧。"},{"en":"Writing style and skill refer to how well a writer uses language, structure, voice and technique.","zh":"writing style and skill 指作家使用語言、結構、聲音和技巧的能力。"},{"en":"A student’s writing style and skill improve when they learn to use clearer sentences and stronger examples.","zh":"當學生學會使用更清楚句子和更有力例子，其寫作風格和技巧就會改善。"},{"en":"If a writer has strong style and skill, even familiar stories can feel fresh.","zh":"如果作家有強大的風格和技巧，即使熟悉故事也可以感覺新鮮。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on craftsmanship in writing.","zh":"這個片語集中於寫作工藝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the literary pendulum has swung","meaning":"文學評價的風向已轉變","examples":[{"en":"The literary pendulum has since swung in different directions.","zh":"文學評價的風向自此已朝不同方向轉變。"},{"en":"The literary pendulum has swung means critical opinion has changed from one side to another over time.","zh":"the literary pendulum has swung 指文學評論意見隨時間由一方轉向另一方。"},{"en":"Public opinion about a school policy may swing when parents hear new evidence.","zh":"當家長聽到新證據，對校政的公眾意見可能轉向。"},{"en":"If the literary pendulum swings, a once-admired writer may later be attacked, or the reverse.","zh":"如果文學評價風向轉變，一位曾受讚賞的作家可能後來被攻擊，反之亦然。"},{"en":"The phrase compares changing opinion to a pendulum moving back and forth.","zh":"這個片語把意見變化比作鐘擺來回擺動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a wide variety of","meaning":"各式各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s work attracted a wide variety of negative criticism.","zh":"Stevenson 的作品招來各式各樣的負面批評。"},{"en":"A wide variety of means many different kinds of something.","zh":"a wide variety of 指許多不同種類的某物。"},{"en":"A school library should offer a wide variety of books for different ages and interests.","zh":"學校圖書館應提供各式各樣適合不同年齡和興趣的書。"},{"en":"If a writer attracts many kinds of criticism, the debate around them is complex.","zh":"如果一位作家招來多種批評，圍繞他的爭論就很複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses range and diversity.","zh":"這個片語強調範圍和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"negative criticism","meaning":"負面批評","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s work attracted negative criticism during his lifetime.","zh":"Stevenson 的作品在他在生時招來負面批評。"},{"en":"Negative criticism is unfavourable judgement that points out faults or weaknesses.","zh":"negative criticism 指指出錯誤或弱點的不利評價。"},{"en":"A student may receive negative criticism if an essay has unclear ideas and weak evidence.","zh":"如果文章想法不清、證據薄弱，學生可能收到負面批評。"},{"en":"Negative criticism can hurt, but it may also show what needs improvement.","zh":"負面批評可能令人受傷，但也可能顯示需要改善的地方。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to criticism that is mainly disapproving.","zh":"這個片語指主要帶否定性的批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"during his lifetime","meaning":"在他在生時","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s work received mixed criticism during his lifetime.","zh":"Stevenson 的作品在他在生時收到褒貶不一的批評。"},{"en":"During his lifetime means while he was alive.","zh":"during his lifetime 指在他仍活着的期間。"},{"en":"Some artists become famous during their lifetime, while others are recognised only after death.","zh":"有些藝術家在生時成名，另一些則死後才被認可。"},{"en":"If a writer is criticised during their lifetime, they may personally experience the pressure of public judgement.","zh":"如果作家在生時被批評，他可能親身承受公眾評價的壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a time period within a person’s life.","zh":"這個片語給出某人生命期間的一段時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a complete reversal of polarity","meaning":"完全反轉；徹底轉向","examples":[{"en":"The change in opinion was like a complete reversal of polarity.","zh":"這種意見轉變就像完全反轉。"},{"en":"A complete reversal of polarity means a total change from one opposite position to another.","zh":"complete reversal of polarity 指由一個立場完全轉向相反立場。"},{"en":"A student who once hated public speaking but later loved debating shows a complete reversal of attitude.","zh":"一個曾討厭公開演說、後來熱愛辯論的學生，顯示態度完全反轉。"},{"en":"If praise turns into strong criticism, the change can feel like a complete reversal.","zh":"如果讚賞變成強烈批評，這種改變就像徹底轉向。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses an extreme turnaround, not a small adjustment.","zh":"這個片語強調極端轉變，而不是小調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"from…to…","meaning":"從……到……","examples":[{"en":"Views of Stevenson shifted from highly positive to clearly negative.","zh":"對 Stevenson 的看法從高度正面轉為明顯負面。"},{"en":"From A to B shows movement, change or range between two points.","zh":"from A to B 顯示兩點之間的移動、改變或範圍。"},{"en":"A student’s grade may rise from a pass to a distinction after months of practice.","zh":"經過數月練習後，學生的成績可能從合格升到優異。"},{"en":"If opinion changes from praise to criticism, the writer’s reputation becomes unstable.","zh":"如果意見從讚賞變成批評，作家的聲譽就變得不穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful for describing change over time.","zh":"這個片語適用於描述隨時間出現的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"corrupt ethics","meaning":"腐敗的道德觀","examples":[{"en":"Some critics described Stevenson as an author with corrupt ethics.","zh":"有些評論家把 Stevenson 描述為道德觀腐敗的作者。"},{"en":"Corrupt ethics means morally wrong or damaged principles about right and wrong.","zh":"corrupt ethics 指關於對錯的原則在道德上錯誤或受破壞。"},{"en":"A company has corrupt ethics if it lies to customers and exploits workers for profit.","zh":"如果公司欺騙顧客並為利潤剝削工人，它就有腐敗的道德觀。"},{"en":"If critics accuse a writer of corrupt ethics, they are attacking the moral quality of the work or author.","zh":"如果評論家指責作家道德觀腐敗，他們是在攻擊作品或作者的道德品質。"},{"en":"The phrase is a serious moral accusation.","zh":"這個片語是嚴重的道德指控。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a lack of morality","meaning":"缺乏道德","examples":[{"en":"Critics accused Stevenson’s writing of showing a lack of morality.","zh":"評論家指責 Stevenson 的寫作顯示缺乏道德。"},{"en":"A lack of morality means an absence of clear ethical values or concern for right and wrong.","zh":"lack of morality 指缺少清楚倫理價值或對對錯的關注。"},{"en":"A story may be criticised for a lack of morality if cruel behaviour is presented as admirable.","zh":"如果故事把殘忍行為呈現為值得欣賞，可能被批評缺乏道德。"},{"en":"If readers expect literature to teach virtue, they may reject works that seem morally unclear.","zh":"如果讀者期望文學教導美德，他們可能拒絕看似道德不清的作品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a perceived moral weakness.","zh":"這個片語描述被認為存在的道德弱點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"dismiss something as","meaning":"把……貶低為","examples":[{"en":"Many critics dismissed Stevenson’s works as children’s stories or horror stories.","zh":"許多評論家把 Stevenson 的作品貶低為兒童故事或恐怖故事。"},{"en":"Dismiss something as means reject it as unimportant, low-quality or not serious.","zh":"dismiss something as 指把某事物拒斥為不重要、低質或不嚴肅。"},{"en":"A teacher should not dismiss a student’s question as silly if it reveals real confusion.","zh":"如果學生問題反映真正困惑，老師不應把它貶低為愚蠢。"},{"en":"When critics dismiss adventure fiction as entertainment only, they may ignore its deeper craft.","zh":"當評論家把冒險小說貶低為純娛樂，可能忽略其更深工藝。"},{"en":"The phrase often shows unfair or quick judgement.","zh":"這個片語常顯示不公平或倉促判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"children’s stories","meaning":"兒童故事","examples":[{"en":"Some critics dismissed his works as children’s stories.","zh":"有些評論家把他的作品貶低為兒童故事。"},{"en":"Children’s stories are stories written mainly for young readers.","zh":"children’s stories 指主要為年輕讀者而寫的故事。"},{"en":"A children’s story may use simple language but still contain courage, fear and moral choice.","zh":"兒童故事可能使用簡單語言，但仍包含勇氣、恐懼和道德選擇。"},{"en":"If critics call a serious work a children’s story, they may be suggesting it lacks adult depth.","zh":"如果評論家把嚴肅作品稱為兒童故事，可能是在暗示它缺乏成人深度。"},{"en":"The phrase can be neutral, but in criticism it may sound dismissive.","zh":"這個片語可以是中性，但在批評中可能帶貶義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"horror stories","meaning":"恐怖故事","examples":[{"en":"Some critics dismissed his works as horror stories.","zh":"有些評論家把他的作品貶低為恐怖故事。"},{"en":"Horror stories are stories designed to create fear, suspense or unease.","zh":"horror stories 指旨在製造恐懼、懸念或不安的故事。"},{"en":"A horror story may use darkness, mystery and danger to make readers feel tense.","zh":"恐怖故事可能使用黑暗、神秘和危險令讀者感到緊張。"},{"en":"If critics dismiss a work as only a horror story, they may overlook its ideas about human nature.","zh":"如果評論家把作品貶低為只是恐怖故事，可能忽略其關於人性的思想。"},{"en":"The phrase names a genre often connected with fear and shock.","zh":"這個片語指出一種常與恐懼和震撼相關的體裁。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have little social value","meaning":"社會價值不大","examples":[{"en":"Some critics believed Stevenson’s stories had little social value.","zh":"有些評論家認為 Stevenson 的故事社會價值不大。"},{"en":"Have little social value means offer little benefit to society, education or moral understanding.","zh":"have little social value 指對社會、教育或道德理解提供很少好處。"},{"en":"A TV show may be criticised as having little social value if it only encourages gossip and cruelty.","zh":"如果電視節目只鼓勵八卦和殘酷，可能被批評社會價值不大。"},{"en":"If literature is judged only by social value, entertainment and style may be undervalued.","zh":"如果文學只按社會價值判斷，娛樂性和風格可能被低估。"},{"en":"The phrase questions whether something is useful beyond enjoyment.","zh":"這個片語質疑某事是否除了享受之外還有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in an educational setting","meaning":"在教育環境中","examples":[{"en":"Critics argued that his works had little social value in an educational setting.","zh":"評論家認為他的作品在教育環境中社會價值不大。"},{"en":"In an educational setting means in a school, university, classroom or learning environment.","zh":"in an educational setting 指在學校、大學、課室或學習環境中。"},{"en":"Phones may be distracting in an educational setting if students use them for games.","zh":"如果學生用手機玩遊戲，手機在教育環境中可能令人分心。"},{"en":"If a book is used in an educational setting, teachers usually expect it to support learning goals.","zh":"如果一本書用於教育環境，老師通常期望它支持學習目標。"},{"en":"The phrase places an activity inside a learning context.","zh":"這個片語把某活動放在學習語境中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be excluded from","meaning":"被排除於……之外","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s works were often excluded from literature curricula.","zh":"Stevenson 的作品常被排除於文學課程之外。"},{"en":"Be excluded from means be left out of a group, list, place or activity.","zh":"be excluded from 指被排除在某群體、清單、地方或活動之外。"},{"en":"A student may feel hurt if they are excluded from a group project without explanation.","zh":"如果學生被無故排除於小組專題之外，可能感到受傷。"},{"en":"If a writer is excluded from a curriculum, fewer students will study their work in school.","zh":"如果作家被排除於課程之外，較少學生會在學校研讀其作品。"},{"en":"The phrase shows removal or non-inclusion.","zh":"這個片語顯示移除或不納入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"literature curricula","meaning":"文學課程","examples":[{"en":"His works were often excluded from literature curricula.","zh":"他的作品常被排除於文學課程之外。"},{"en":"Literature curricula are the planned lists of books, authors and literary skills taught in schools or universities.","zh":"literature curricula 指學校或大學中有計劃教授的書籍、作者和文學技能清單。"},{"en":"A literature curriculum may include novels, poems, drama and critical essays.","zh":"文學課程可能包括小說、詩、戲劇和評論文章。"},{"en":"If a writer enters the curriculum, their status as serious literature may improve.","zh":"如果作家進入課程，其作為嚴肅文學的地位可能提升。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised literary study.","zh":"這個片語指有組織的文學學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"controversial nature","meaning":"具爭議的性質","examples":[{"en":"The controversial nature of his works affected their place in schools.","zh":"他作品具爭議的性質影響了它們在學校中的位置。"},{"en":"Controversial nature means the quality of causing disagreement, debate or strong reactions.","zh":"controversial nature 指引起分歧、爭論或強烈反應的特質。"},{"en":"The controversial nature of a school policy may make parents demand a meeting.","zh":"一項校政具爭議的性質可能令家長要求開會。"},{"en":"If a book’s themes are controversial, teachers may hesitate to include it in class.","zh":"如果一本書的主題具爭議，老師可能猶豫是否把它納入課堂。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why something creates disagreement.","zh":"這個片語解釋某事為何引起分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"these debates remain","meaning":"這些爭論仍然存在","examples":[{"en":"These debates remain among literary critics today.","zh":"這些爭論直到今天仍存在於文學評論家之間。"},{"en":"These debates remain means these arguments or disagreements still continue.","zh":"these debates remain 指這些爭論或分歧仍然持續。"},{"en":"Debates about homework remain because teachers, parents and students value different things.","zh":"關於功課的爭論仍然存在，因為老師、家長和學生重視不同事情。"},{"en":"If debates remain for decades, the issue is probably complex and unresolved.","zh":"如果爭論持續數十年，該議題大概複雜而未解決。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that an argument has not ended.","zh":"這個片語顯示爭論尚未結束。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"assert that","meaning":"斷言；堅稱","examples":[{"en":"Many critics still assert that Stevenson’s works lack moral value.","zh":"許多評論家仍堅稱 Stevenson 的作品缺乏道德價值。"},{"en":"Assert that means state something firmly and confidently.","zh":"assert that 指堅定而自信地陳述某事。"},{"en":"A student may assert that social media harms concentration, but they should still provide evidence.","zh":"學生可能斷言社交媒體損害專注力，但仍應提供證據。"},{"en":"If critics assert a strong judgement, readers may ask whether the evidence supports it.","zh":"如果評論家提出強烈判斷，讀者可能會問證據是否支持它。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a firm claim.","zh":"這個片語引出堅定主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"despite his skill","meaning":"儘管他有技巧","examples":[{"en":"Some critics argue that, despite his skill, his works lack moral value.","zh":"有些評論家認為，儘管他有技巧，他的作品仍缺乏道德價值。"},{"en":"Despite his skill means although he was talented or technically able.","zh":"despite his skill 指雖然他有才華或技術能力。"},{"en":"Despite his skill in speaking, a student may lose marks if the answer does not address the question.","zh":"儘管學生有口語技巧，如果答案沒有回應題目，仍可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase separates talent from another weakness or criticism.","zh":"這個片語把才能與另一個弱點或批評分開。"},{"en":"It shows that one positive quality does not remove all concerns.","zh":"它顯示一項正面特質不能消除所有疑慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lack moral value","meaning":"缺乏道德價值","examples":[{"en":"Some critics argue that Stevenson’s literary works lack moral value.","zh":"有些評論家認為 Stevenson 的文學作品缺乏道德價值。"},{"en":"Lack moral value means fail to teach, support or explore clear moral principles.","zh":"lack moral value 指未能教導、支持或探索清楚道德原則。"},{"en":"A story may be said to lack moral value if selfish behaviour is rewarded without question.","zh":"如果故事毫不質疑地獎賞自私行為，可能被說成缺乏道德價值。"},{"en":"If critics believe literature should guide character, they may reject works that seem morally empty.","zh":"如果評論家相信文學應引導品格，可能拒絕看似道德空洞的作品。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to criticise the ethical usefulness of a work.","zh":"這個片語用來批評作品的倫理用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"one of the main reasons","meaning":"主要原因之一","examples":[{"en":"One of the main reasons for the criticism was the genre of his writing.","zh":"批評的主要原因之一是他的寫作體裁。"},{"en":"One of the main reasons means one important cause among several possible causes.","zh":"one of the main reasons 指幾個可能原因中的一個重要原因。"},{"en":"One of the main reasons students fail essays is that they do not answer the exact question.","zh":"學生作文失分的主要原因之一，是沒有準確回答題目。"},{"en":"If a problem has several causes, naming one main reason helps organise the explanation.","zh":"如果問題有幾個原因，指出其中一個主要原因有助組織解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an important but not necessarily only explanation.","zh":"這個片語引出重要但不一定唯一的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"literary works","meaning":"文學作品","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s literary works attracted both praise and criticism.","zh":"Stevenson 的文學作品同時招來讚賞和批評。"},{"en":"Literary works are written creations such as novels, poems, essays, plays or stories.","zh":"literary works 指小說、詩、散文、戲劇或故事等書面創作。"},{"en":"Students study literary works to understand language, themes, characters and culture.","zh":"學生研究文學作品以理解語言、主題、人物和文化。"},{"en":"If literary works are controversial, they may stay alive in debate for generations.","zh":"如果文學作品具爭議，它們可能在幾代人的爭論中保持生命力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to written texts treated as literature.","zh":"這個片語指被視為文學的書面文本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"attract criticism","meaning":"招致批評","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s adventure stories attracted criticism from some literary figures.","zh":"Stevenson 的冒險故事招致一些文學人物批評。"},{"en":"Attract criticism means draw negative comments, objections or disapproval.","zh":"attract criticism 指引來負面評論、反對或不認可。"},{"en":"A school rule may attract criticism if students think it is unfair.","zh":"如果學生認為校規不公平，它可能招致批評。"},{"en":"If a novel attracts criticism, readers may become more curious about why it is controversial.","zh":"如果小說招致批評，讀者可能更好奇它為何具爭議。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that criticism comes toward someone or something.","zh":"這個片語顯示批評向某人或某事而來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the genre of","meaning":"……的體裁","examples":[{"en":"The genre of Stevenson’s writing was one reason for the criticism.","zh":"Stevenson 寫作的體裁是批評原因之一。"},{"en":"The genre of a work is its type or category, such as adventure, romance, horror or comedy.","zh":"genre of a work 指作品的類型或分類，例如冒險、愛情、恐怖或喜劇。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to identify the genre of a film before analysing its techniques.","zh":"老師可能要求學生在分析技巧前，先辨認電影的體裁。"},{"en":"If a genre is seen as low-status, works in that genre may be unfairly dismissed.","zh":"如果某體裁被視為地位較低，該體裁中的作品可能被不公平貶低。"},{"en":"The phrase classifies a work by literary or artistic type.","zh":"這個片語按文學或藝術類型分類作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"adventure stories","meaning":"冒險故事","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson mainly wrote adventure stories.","zh":"Stevenson 主要寫冒險故事。"},{"en":"Adventure stories are stories about danger, journeys, action, discovery or risky experiences.","zh":"adventure stories 指關於危險、旅程、動作、發現或冒險經歷的故事。"},{"en":"Children often enjoy adventure stories because characters must solve problems under pressure.","zh":"孩子常喜歡冒險故事，因為角色必須在壓力下解決問題。"},{"en":"Adventure stories can entertain readers, but they can also explore courage and moral choice.","zh":"冒險故事可以娛樂讀者，但也可以探索勇氣和道德選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase names a genre built around excitement and risk.","zh":"這個片語指出以刺激和風險為核心的體裁。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a popular and entertaining genre","meaning":"受歡迎而富娛樂性的體裁","examples":[{"en":"Adventure stories were a popular and entertaining genre at the time.","zh":"冒險故事在當時是受歡迎而富娛樂性的體裁。"},{"en":"A popular and entertaining genre is a type of writing that many people enjoy reading for pleasure.","zh":"popular and entertaining genre 指許多人為樂趣而喜歡閱讀的寫作類型。"},{"en":"Detective fiction is a popular and entertaining genre because readers enjoy solving mysteries.","zh":"偵探小說是受歡迎而富娛樂性的體裁，因為讀者享受解謎。"},{"en":"If a genre is popular, serious critics may sometimes undervalue it as mere entertainment.","zh":"如果某體裁受歡迎，嚴肅評論家有時可能把它低估為純娛樂。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses public enjoyment more than academic prestige.","zh":"這個片語強調大眾享受，而不是學術聲望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"engaging characters","meaning":"吸引人的角色","examples":[{"en":"Adventure stories often offer engaging characters, action and mystery.","zh":"冒險故事常提供吸引人的角色、動作情節和神秘元素。"},{"en":"Engaging characters are characters who interest readers and make them want to continue the story.","zh":"engaging characters 指令讀者感興趣並想繼續閱讀故事的角色。"},{"en":"A film with engaging characters can hold viewers’ attention even if the plot is simple.","zh":"即使情節簡單，一部有吸引人角色的電影也能抓住觀眾注意力。"},{"en":"If readers care about the characters, danger and conflict become more exciting.","zh":"如果讀者關心角色，危險和衝突就變得更刺激。"},{"en":"The phrase describes characters that attract emotional or imaginative interest.","zh":"這個片語描述能引起情感或想像興趣的角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"action and mystery","meaning":"動作情節和神秘元素","examples":[{"en":"Adventure stories often contain action and mystery.","zh":"冒險故事常包含動作情節和神秘元素。"},{"en":"Action and mystery mean exciting events and unanswered questions that create suspense.","zh":"action and mystery 指刺激事件和未解問題，能製造懸念。"},{"en":"A detective film uses action and mystery when characters chase clues and hide secrets.","zh":"當角色追查線索並隱藏秘密，偵探電影就使用動作情節和神秘元素。"},{"en":"If a story has action but no mystery, it may feel fast but not mentally engaging.","zh":"如果故事有動作但沒有神秘元素，可能感覺很快卻不夠吸引思考。"},{"en":"The phrase names two common ingredients of exciting fiction.","zh":"這個片語指出刺激小說中的兩種常見元素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ultimately","meaning":"最終；歸根究底","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe adventure stories are exciting but ultimately lack moral depth.","zh":"有些人認為冒險故事刺激，但歸根究底缺乏道德深度。"},{"en":"Ultimately means in the end or when everything is considered.","zh":"ultimately 指最終，或在考慮所有事情後。"},{"en":"A shortcut may save time at first, but ultimately it can create more mistakes.","zh":"捷徑起初可能省時間，但最終可能造成更多錯誤。"},{"en":"Critics use “ultimately” when giving their final judgement after considering details.","zh":"評論家在考慮細節後給出最終判斷時，會使用 “ultimately”。"},{"en":"The word points to the final result or conclusion.","zh":"這個詞指向最終結果或結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"teach moral principles","meaning":"教導道德原則","examples":[{"en":"Critics argued that adventure stories could not teach moral principles.","zh":"評論家認為冒險故事不能教導道德原則。"},{"en":"Teach moral principles means help readers understand ideas about right, wrong, duty or character.","zh":"teach moral principles 指幫助讀者理解關於對錯、責任或品格的觀念。"},{"en":"A classroom story can teach moral principles by showing why honesty matters.","zh":"課堂故事可以透過展示誠實為何重要來教導道德原則。"},{"en":"If a story only entertains and never asks moral questions, some critics may see it as shallow.","zh":"如果故事只娛樂而從不提出道德問題，有些評論家可能覺得它膚淺。"},{"en":"The phrase connects literature with ethical learning.","zh":"這個片語把文學與倫理學習連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"one-dimensional plots","meaning":"單一層面的情節","examples":[{"en":"Critics claimed that the plots of adventure stories were one-dimensional.","zh":"評論家聲稱冒險故事的情節是單一層面的。"},{"en":"One-dimensional plots are simple plots that lack complexity, depth or multiple meanings.","zh":"one-dimensional plots 指缺乏複雜性、深度或多重意義的簡單情節。"},{"en":"A film with a one-dimensional plot may show only good heroes and bad villains without inner conflict.","zh":"單一層面的電影情節可能只呈現好英雄和壞反派，而沒有內心衝突。"},{"en":"If a plot is one-dimensional, readers may enjoy the action but forget the story quickly.","zh":"如果情節單一，讀者可能享受動作場面，但很快忘記故事。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises a story for being too flat or simple.","zh":"這個片語批評故事過於平面或簡單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"deeper moral meaning","meaning":"更深層的道德意義","examples":[{"en":"Some critics believed Stevenson’s stories rarely offered deeper moral meaning.","zh":"有些評論家認為 Stevenson 的故事很少提供更深層的道德意義。"},{"en":"Deeper moral meaning is ethical significance beyond surface events or entertainment.","zh":"deeper moral meaning 指超越表面事件或娛樂的倫理意義。"},{"en":"A simple story about sharing food may have deeper moral meaning about kindness and community.","zh":"一個關於分享食物的簡單故事，可能有關於仁慈和社群的更深層道德意義。"},{"en":"If readers find deeper moral meaning in adventure fiction, the genre becomes more serious than pure action.","zh":"如果讀者在冒險小說中找到更深層道德意義，該體裁就不只是純動作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to hidden or richer ethical significance.","zh":"這個片語指隱藏或更豐富的倫理意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"instead focusing on","meaning":"反而集中於……","examples":[{"en":"The stories were said to lack moral depth, instead focusing on excitement.","zh":"這些故事被指缺乏道德深度，反而集中於刺激感。"},{"en":"Instead focusing on means choosing one focus in place of another expected focus.","zh":"instead focusing on 指以某焦點取代另一個預期焦點。"},{"en":"A weak essay may ignore analysis, instead focusing on retelling the story.","zh":"薄弱文章可能忽略分析，反而集中於重述故事。"},{"en":"If a book focuses on excitement instead of moral reflection, some critics may call it shallow.","zh":"如果一本書集中於刺激而不是道德反思，有些評論家可能稱它膚淺。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a contrast between two possible priorities.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩個可能優先事項之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"plot twists","meaning":"情節轉折","examples":[{"en":"Adventure stories often use exciting and shocking plot twists.","zh":"冒險故事常使用刺激而令人震驚的情節轉折。"},{"en":"Plot twists are unexpected changes in a story that surprise the reader or viewer.","zh":"plot twists 指故事中出乎意料的變化，令讀者或觀眾驚訝。"},{"en":"A mystery film may use a plot twist when the trusted friend is revealed as the criminal.","zh":"當可信朋友被揭示為罪犯，懸疑電影就可能使用情節轉折。"},{"en":"Plot twists keep readers interested because they change what people thought was true.","zh":"情節轉折令讀者保持興趣，因為它改變人們以為真實的事情。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to sudden turns in a story’s direction.","zh":"這個片語指故事方向的突然轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"thrilling events","meaning":"驚險刺激的事件","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s stories often include thrilling events.","zh":"Stevenson 的故事常包含驚險刺激的事件。"},{"en":"Thrilling events are exciting, tense or dangerous moments that make readers feel eager or nervous.","zh":"thrilling events 指令人興奮、緊張或感到危險的時刻，使讀者期待或緊張。"},{"en":"A rescue scene during a storm can be a thrilling event in a film.","zh":"暴風雨中的救援場面可以是電影中的驚險刺激事件。"},{"en":"If a story has too many thrilling events but little reflection, some critics may see it as shallow entertainment.","zh":"如果故事有太多刺激事件但很少反思，有些評論家可能視之為膚淺娛樂。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to moments designed to create excitement.","zh":"這個片語指旨在製造興奮感的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be criticised by fellow authors","meaning":"被其他作家批評","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s works were even criticised by fellow authors.","zh":"Stevenson 的作品甚至被其他作家批評。"},{"en":"Be criticised by fellow authors means receive negative judgement from other writers.","zh":"be criticised by fellow authors 指受到其他作家的負面評價。"},{"en":"A young novelist may feel hurt if their book is criticised by writers they admire.","zh":"如果年輕小說家的書被自己欣賞的作家批評，可能感到受傷。"},{"en":"Criticism from fellow authors can be powerful because it comes from people who understand the craft.","zh":"來自同行作家的批評可能很有力，因為它來自懂得寫作工藝的人。"},{"en":"The phrase shows criticism from peers, not only from reviewers.","zh":"這個片語顯示批評來自同輩，而不只是評論員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fellow authors","meaning":"同行作家","examples":[{"en":"Some fellow authors criticised Stevenson’s work.","zh":"一些同行作家批評 Stevenson 的作品。"},{"en":"Fellow authors are other writers who work in the same broad field.","zh":"fellow authors 指在同一廣泛領域中工作的其他作家。"},{"en":"Fellow authors may praise a novelist’s style while questioning the story’s structure.","zh":"同行作家可能讚賞小說家的風格，同時質疑故事結構。"},{"en":"If fellow authors disagree about a writer, the literary debate becomes more interesting.","zh":"如果同行作家對一位作家意見不一，文學爭論就更有趣。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to peers within the writing profession.","zh":"這個片語指寫作專業中的同輩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"deeply admire","meaning":"深深欣賞","examples":[{"en":"Oscar Wilde deeply admired Stevenson’s work.","zh":"Oscar Wilde 深深欣賞 Stevenson 的作品。"},{"en":"Deeply admire means strongly respect or appreciate someone or something.","zh":"deeply admire 指強烈尊重或欣賞某人或某事。"},{"en":"A student may deeply admire a teacher who explains difficult ideas with patience.","zh":"學生可能深深欣賞一位耐心解釋難懂概念的老師。"},{"en":"If one writer deeply admires another, they may still make jokes or criticisms about their work.","zh":"即使一位作家深深欣賞另一位作家，仍可能開玩笑或批評其作品。"},{"en":"The phrase shows strong positive feeling.","zh":"這個片語顯示強烈正面感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"joke that","meaning":"開玩笑說","examples":[{"en":"Oscar Wilde joked that Stevenson might have written better works outside Scotland.","zh":"Oscar Wilde 開玩笑說 Stevenson 也許在蘇格蘭以外會寫出更好的作品。"},{"en":"Joke that means say something humorously, often not as a fully serious claim.","zh":"joke that 指以幽默方式說某事，通常不是完全嚴肅的主張。"},{"en":"A teacher may joke that the class has become professional coffee drinkers during exam season.","zh":"老師可能開玩笑說全班在考試季變成專業咖啡飲用者。"},{"en":"If a critic jokes about a writer, the comment may still reveal a real opinion underneath.","zh":"如果評論家拿作家開玩笑，評論底下仍可能透露真正看法。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a humorous statement.","zh":"這個片語引出幽默陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"would have written better works","meaning":"本可寫出更好的作品","examples":[{"en":"Wilde joked that Stevenson would have written better works if he had not been born in Scotland.","zh":"Wilde 開玩笑說，如果 Stevenson 不是出生於蘇格蘭，他本可寫出更好的作品。"},{"en":"Would have written better works imagines a different past result under different conditions.","zh":"would have written better works 指在不同條件下，想像過去會有更好的結果。"},{"en":"A teacher might say a student would have written a better essay if they had planned the argument first.","zh":"老師可能說，如果學生先規劃論點，本可寫出更好的文章。"},{"en":"This structure often suggests regret, criticism or speculation about the past.","zh":"這個結構常暗示對過去的遺憾、批評或推測。"},{"en":"The phrase uses a hypothetical past to judge what might have happened.","zh":"這個片語使用假設過去來評價本可能發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"come to someone’s defence","meaning":"為某人辯護","examples":[{"en":"Other authors came to Stevenson’s defence.","zh":"其他作家為 Stevenson 辯護。"},{"en":"Come to someone’s defence means speak or act to protect someone from criticism.","zh":"come to someone’s defence 指說話或行動保護某人免受批評。"},{"en":"A classmate may come to a student’s defence when others unfairly blame them for a group mistake.","zh":"當其他人不公平地責怪學生造成小組錯誤，同學可能為他辯護。"},{"en":"If respected writers defend an author, public opinion may become more balanced.","zh":"如果受尊重作家為某作者辯護，公眾意見可能變得更平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase shows support in response to attack or criticism.","zh":"這個片語顯示面對攻擊或批評時的支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"claim that","meaning":"聲稱；認為","examples":[{"en":"Galsworthy claimed that Stevenson was a greater writer than Thomas Hardy.","zh":"Galsworthy 認為 Stevenson 是比 Thomas Hardy 更偉大的作家。"},{"en":"Claim that means state that something is true, often with confidence but needing support.","zh":"claim that 指聲稱某事是真的，通常帶有信心但需要支持。"},{"en":"A student may claim that homework improves discipline, but the essay should explain why.","zh":"學生可能聲稱功課改善紀律，但文章應解釋原因。"},{"en":"If a critic claims one writer is greater than another, readers may compare evidence from both writers.","zh":"如果評論家聲稱一位作家比另一位更偉大，讀者可能比較兩者作品中的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an arguable statement.","zh":"這個片語引出可爭論的陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a greater writer than","meaning":"比……更偉大的作家","examples":[{"en":"Galsworthy claimed that Stevenson was a greater writer than Hardy.","zh":"Galsworthy 認為 Stevenson 是比 Hardy 更偉大的作家。"},{"en":"A greater writer than someone is a writer judged to be better or more important than another writer.","zh":"greater writer than someone 指被判斷為比另一位作家更好或更重要的作家。"},{"en":"Some students may argue that one poet is a greater writer than another because their poems feel more original.","zh":"有些學生可能認為一位詩人比另一位更偉大，因為其詩更有原創性。"},{"en":"Such comparisons often depend on style, influence, themes and personal taste.","zh":"這類比較通常取決於風格、影響、主題和個人口味。"},{"en":"The phrase makes a direct literary comparison.","zh":"這個片語作直接文學比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"despite Wilde’s criticism","meaning":"儘管 Wilde 作出批評","examples":[{"en":"Despite Wilde’s criticism, Stevenson’s Scottish identity remained central to his work.","zh":"儘管 Wilde 作出批評，Stevenson 的蘇格蘭身份仍是其作品的核心。"},{"en":"Despite Wilde’s criticism means although Wilde made a critical comment.","zh":"despite Wilde’s criticism 指雖然 Wilde 作出了批評性評論。"},{"en":"Despite a teacher’s criticism, a student may keep writing because they still love stories.","zh":"儘管老師作出批評，學生仍可能繼續寫作，因為他仍熱愛故事。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one negative view did not remove another important fact.","zh":"這個片語顯示一個負面看法沒有消除另一個重要事實。"},{"en":"It introduces contrast between criticism and continuing value.","zh":"它引出批評與持續價值之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Scottish identity","meaning":"蘇格蘭身份","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s Scottish identity was an integral part of his work.","zh":"Stevenson 的蘇格蘭身份是其作品不可或缺的一部分。"},{"en":"Scottish identity means the sense of belonging connected with Scotland’s culture, history, language and people.","zh":"Scottish identity 指與蘇格蘭文化、歷史、語言和人民相關的歸屬感。"},{"en":"A writer’s Scottish identity may appear in local speech, landscapes and social habits.","zh":"作家的蘇格蘭身份可能出現在本地語言、風景和社會習慣中。"},{"en":"If identity shapes a writer’s imagination, removing it may weaken the work’s character.","zh":"如果身份塑造作家的想像力，移除它可能削弱作品特色。"},{"en":"The phrase links personal and national background with literature.","zh":"這個片語把個人和民族背景與文學連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"an integral part of","meaning":"……不可或缺的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Scottish identity was an integral part of Stevenson’s writing.","zh":"蘇格蘭身份是 Stevenson 寫作不可或缺的一部分。"},{"en":"An integral part of something is an essential part that helps make the whole complete.","zh":"integral part of something 指幫助整體完整的必要部分。"},{"en":"Feedback is an integral part of good learning because students need to know what to improve.","zh":"回饋是良好學習不可或缺的一部分，因為學生需要知道要改善甚麼。"},{"en":"If local culture is an integral part of a novel, the story may lose meaning without it.","zh":"如果本土文化是小說不可或缺的一部分，沒有它故事可能失去意義。"},{"en":"The phrase means something is necessary, not optional.","zh":"這個片語意思是某事必要，而不是可有可無。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not popular in Scotland","meaning":"在蘇格蘭並不受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s works were not popular in Scotland when he was alive.","zh":"Stevenson 的作品在他在生時在蘇格蘭並不受歡迎。"},{"en":"Not popular in Scotland means not widely liked, accepted or celebrated by Scottish readers or critics.","zh":"not popular in Scotland 指沒有被蘇格蘭讀者或評論家廣泛喜愛、接受或讚揚。"},{"en":"A singer may be famous abroad but not popular in their own city.","zh":"歌手可能在海外成名，但在自己的城市並不受歡迎。"},{"en":"If a writer is not popular at home, their national reputation may grow only later.","zh":"如果作家在本地不受歡迎，其民族聲譽可能要到後來才增長。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts local reception with wider or later fame.","zh":"這個片語把本地接受度與更廣泛或後來名聲作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"when he was alive","meaning":"在他在生時","examples":[{"en":"His works were not widely praised in Scotland when he was alive.","zh":"他的作品在他在生時沒有在蘇格蘭受到廣泛讚揚。"},{"en":"When he was alive means during the period of his life before he died.","zh":"when he was alive 指在他去世前仍活着的期間。"},{"en":"Some painters sell very little work when they are alive but become famous later.","zh":"有些畫家在生時作品賣得很少，但後來成名。"},{"en":"If a writer is undervalued when alive, later recognition can change their literary status.","zh":"如果作家在生時被低估，後來的認可可以改變其文學地位。"},{"en":"The phrase marks judgement or events during a person’s lifetime.","zh":"這個片語標示某人生命期間的評價或事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"modern Scottish literary critics","meaning":"現代蘇格蘭文學評論家","examples":[{"en":"Modern Scottish literary critics have reassessed Stevenson’s importance.","zh":"現代蘇格蘭文學評論家重新評估了 Stevenson 的重要性。"},{"en":"Modern Scottish literary critics are present-day critics who study Scottish literature.","zh":"modern Scottish literary critics 指研究蘇格蘭文學的當代評論家。"},{"en":"Modern critics may re-read old books through new concerns about identity, class and place.","zh":"現代評論家可能透過身份、階級和地方等新關注重新閱讀舊書。"},{"en":"If modern Scottish critics value local detail, Stevenson’s reputation may improve.","zh":"如果現代蘇格蘭評論家重視本地細節，Stevenson 的聲譽可能提升。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies contemporary critics within Scottish literary studies.","zh":"這個片語指出蘇格蘭文學研究中的當代評論家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the most influential writers","meaning":"最具影響力的作家","examples":[{"en":"Many critics see Scott and Stevenson as the most influential writers in Scottish history.","zh":"許多評論家視 Scott 和 Stevenson 為蘇格蘭歷史上最具影響力的作家。"},{"en":"The most influential writers are writers whose works strongly affect later literature, culture or readers.","zh":"most influential writers 指作品強烈影響後來文學、文化或讀者的作家。"},{"en":"A writer may become influential if later authors copy their style or respond to their themes.","zh":"如果後來作者模仿某作家的風格或回應其主題，他可能變得有影響力。"},{"en":"If many critics call someone influential, they believe the writer changed more than their own generation.","zh":"如果許多評論家稱某人有影響力，他們相信該作家改變的不只是自己那一代。"},{"en":"The phrase measures impact, not only popularity.","zh":"這個片語量度影響，而不只是受歡迎程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the history of","meaning":"在……歷史上","examples":[{"en":"They are considered influential writers in the history of Scotland.","zh":"他們被視為蘇格蘭歷史上具影響力的作家。"},{"en":"In the history of means within the past development or record of a place, subject or field.","zh":"in the history of 指在某地方、主題或領域過去發展或記錄中。"},{"en":"A school may remember one principal as important in the history of its development.","zh":"學校可能記得某位校長在其發展歷史上很重要。"},{"en":"If a writer is important in the history of a country, their work may shape national culture.","zh":"如果作家在一國歷史上重要，其作品可能塑造民族文化。"},{"en":"The phrase places someone or something within a historical story.","zh":"這個片語把某人或某事放入歷史故事中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"exalt someone as","meaning":"將某人推崇為……","examples":[{"en":"Some critics exalt Sir Walter Scott as a literary genius.","zh":"有些評論家將 Sir Walter Scott 推崇為文學天才。"},{"en":"Exalt someone as means praise someone very highly and present them as important or exceptional.","zh":"exalt someone as 指高度讚揚某人，並把他呈現為重要或非凡。"},{"en":"A community may exalt a doctor as a hero after years of service to poor families.","zh":"社區可能在一位醫生多年服務貧困家庭後，將他推崇為英雄。"},{"en":"If critics exalt one writer too much, another writer may be unfairly overshadowed.","zh":"如果評論家過度推崇某作家，另一位作家可能被不公平掩蓋。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests strong admiration and elevation of status.","zh":"這個片語暗示強烈讚賞和地位提升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"literary genius","meaning":"文學天才","examples":[{"en":"Some critics regard Sir Walter Scott as a literary genius.","zh":"有些評論家視 Sir Walter Scott 為文學天才。"},{"en":"A literary genius is a writer with exceptional creative and technical ability.","zh":"literary genius 指具有非凡創作和技術能力的作家。"},{"en":"A poet may be called a literary genius if their work changes how people use language.","zh":"如果詩人的作品改變人們使用語言的方式，可能被稱為文學天才。"},{"en":"Calling someone a genius can raise expectations and make comparison with others difficult.","zh":"稱某人為天才可以提高期望，並令與其他人比較變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase gives very high praise to a writer.","zh":"這個片語給予作家極高讚賞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"technical ability","meaning":"技術能力；寫作技巧","examples":[{"en":"Scott is praised for his technical ability.","zh":"Scott 因其技術能力而受讚賞。"},{"en":"Technical ability means skill in controlling form, structure, language and method.","zh":"technical ability 指控制形式、結構、語言和方法的技巧。"},{"en":"A pianist’s technical ability shows in accurate timing, strong control and clean movement.","zh":"鋼琴家的技術能力體現在準確節奏、強控制和乾淨動作上。"},{"en":"In writing, technical ability helps an author organise plot, tone and sentence rhythm.","zh":"在寫作中，技術能力幫助作者組織情節、語氣和句子節奏。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on craft and control.","zh":"這個片語集中於工藝和控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"deserve the same recognition","meaning":"應得到同等認可","examples":[{"en":"Some critics argue that Stevenson deserves the same recognition as Scott.","zh":"有些評論家認為 Stevenson 應得到與 Scott 同等的認可。"},{"en":"Deserve the same recognition means should receive equal respect, attention or honour.","zh":"deserve the same recognition 指應獲得同等尊重、關注或榮譽。"},{"en":"A quiet team member may deserve the same recognition as the person who presents the project.","zh":"安靜的組員可能應得到與匯報者同等的認可。"},{"en":"If two writers influence literature deeply, critics may argue they deserve equal status.","zh":"如果兩位作家都深刻影響文學，評論家可能認為他們應有同等地位。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when someone is seen as undervalued.","zh":"這個片語用於某人被認為受到低估時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"natural ability","meaning":"天賦；天生能力","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson is praised for his natural ability to capture stories and characters.","zh":"Stevenson 因其捕捉故事和人物的天賦而受讚賞。"},{"en":"Natural ability is talent that seems to come easily or instinctively to someone.","zh":"natural ability 指某人似乎自然或本能地擁有的才華。"},{"en":"A child with natural ability in music may remember melodies after hearing them once.","zh":"有音樂天賦的孩子可能聽一次旋律就記住。"},{"en":"Natural ability helps, but practice is still needed to turn talent into lasting skill.","zh":"天賦有幫助，但仍需要練習才能把才華變成持久技能。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses inborn or effortless-seeming talent.","zh":"這個片語強調天生或看似毫不費力的才華。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"capture stories and characters in words","meaning":"用文字捕捉故事和人物","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson had a natural ability to capture stories and characters in words.","zh":"Stevenson 有用文字捕捉故事和人物的天賦。"},{"en":"Capture stories and characters in words means describe events and people so vividly that readers can imagine them clearly.","zh":"capture stories and characters in words 指生動描寫事件和人物，令讀者能清楚想像。"},{"en":"A good writer can capture a grandmother’s voice in words so readers feel they know her.","zh":"好作家能用文字捕捉祖母的聲音，讓讀者感覺認識她。"},{"en":"If characters are captured well, they stay in readers’ minds after the story ends.","zh":"如果人物被捕捉得好，故事完結後仍留在讀者腦海。"},{"en":"The phrase describes vivid literary representation.","zh":"這個片語描述生動的文學呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be taken more seriously as","meaning":"被更認真地視為……","examples":[{"en":"Scott’s works were taken more seriously as literature.","zh":"Scott 的作品被更認真地視為文學。"},{"en":"Be taken more seriously as means be treated with greater respect in a particular role or category.","zh":"be taken more seriously as 指在某角色或類別中受到更大尊重。"},{"en":"A student’s hobby may be taken more seriously as a career after they win a major competition.","zh":"學生在大型比賽勝出後，其興趣可能被更認真地視為職業。"},{"en":"If adventure stories are not taken seriously as literature, their artistic value may be overlooked.","zh":"如果冒險故事沒有被認真視為文學，其藝術價值可能被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a change in status or respect.","zh":"這個片語顯示地位或尊重的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"depth of tragic themes","meaning":"悲劇主題的深度","examples":[{"en":"Scott’s works were respected for the depth of their tragic themes.","zh":"Scott 的作品因其悲劇主題的深度而受尊重。"},{"en":"Depth of tragic themes means serious and complex exploration of suffering, loss, failure or fate.","zh":"depth of tragic themes 指對痛苦、失去、失敗或命運作嚴肅而複雜的探索。"},{"en":"A novel about a family losing their home may show depth if it explores grief, pride and responsibility.","zh":"關於一家人失去住所的小說，如果探索悲傷、尊嚴和責任，就可能有深度。"},{"en":"If tragic themes have depth, readers feel more than sadness; they also think about human life.","zh":"如果悲劇主題有深度，讀者感到的不只是悲傷，也會思考人生。"},{"en":"The phrase praises serious emotional and moral complexity.","zh":"這個片語讚賞嚴肅的情感和道德複雜性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fans of Stevenson","meaning":"史提芬遜的支持者","examples":[{"en":"Fans of Stevenson praise his unique style of storytelling.","zh":"Stevenson 的支持者讚賞他獨特的敍事風格。"},{"en":"Fans of Stevenson are readers or critics who admire Stevenson and support his reputation.","zh":"fans of Stevenson 指欣賞 Stevenson 並支持其聲譽的讀者或評論家。"},{"en":"Fans of a writer may recommend their books to classmates and explain why they matter.","zh":"作家的支持者可能向同學推薦其書，並解釋其重要性。"},{"en":"If fans defend a controversial writer, debate around the writer may continue.","zh":"如果支持者為具爭議作家辯護，圍繞作家的討論可能持續。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people who appreciate Stevenson’s work.","zh":"這個片語指欣賞 Stevenson 作品的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"unique style of storytelling","meaning":"獨特的敍事風格","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson is admired for his unique style of storytelling.","zh":"Stevenson 因其獨特的敍事風格而受到欣賞。"},{"en":"A unique style of storytelling is a distinctive way of creating plots, characters, voice and atmosphere.","zh":"unique style of storytelling 指創造情節、人物、聲音和氣氛的獨特方式。"},{"en":"A film director may have a unique style of storytelling if audiences recognise the rhythm and mood immediately.","zh":"如果觀眾能立即認出節奏和氣氛，電影導演可能有獨特敍事風格。"},{"en":"If a writer’s storytelling style is unique, imitation may never fully capture it.","zh":"如果作家的敍事風格獨特，模仿可能永遠無法完全捕捉它。"},{"en":"The phrase praises originality in narrative technique.","zh":"這個片語讚賞敍事技巧中的原創性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"depiction of human nature","meaning":"對人性的描寫","examples":[{"en":"Critics praise Stevenson’s depiction of human nature.","zh":"評論家讚賞 Stevenson 對人性的描寫。"},{"en":"Depiction of human nature means the way a writer shows human feelings, weaknesses, desires and behaviour.","zh":"depiction of human nature 指作家呈現人類感受、弱點、欲望和行為的方式。"},{"en":"A novel may offer a strong depiction of human nature by showing jealousy inside a friendship.","zh":"小說可以透過呈現友誼中的嫉妒，提供有力的人性描寫。"},{"en":"If human nature is depicted honestly, readers may recognise themselves in the characters.","zh":"如果人性被誠實描寫，讀者可能在人物身上認出自己。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how literature represents people.","zh":"這個片語集中於文學如何呈現人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"unlike other British authors","meaning":"不像其他英國作家","examples":[{"en":"Unlike other British authors, Stevenson captured ordinary Scottish life.","zh":"不像其他英國作家，Stevenson 捕捉了普通蘇格蘭生活。"},{"en":"Unlike other British authors means different from other writers from Britain.","zh":"unlike other British authors 指與其他英國作家不同。"},{"en":"Unlike many classmates, one student may prefer writing stories to solving maths problems.","zh":"不像許多同學，一位學生可能較喜歡寫故事而不是解數學題。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a contrast between Stevenson and a wider group of writers.","zh":"這個片語突出 Stevenson 與較大作家群體之間的對比。"},{"en":"It prepares readers to notice what makes him different.","zh":"它讓讀者注意他有何不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"distinctive day-to-day life","meaning":"獨特的日常生活","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson captured the distinctive day-to-day life of ordinary Scottish people.","zh":"Stevenson 捕捉了普通蘇格蘭人獨特的日常生活。"},{"en":"Distinctive day-to-day life means the recognisable everyday habits, speech and routines of a particular group.","zh":"distinctive day-to-day life 指某群體可辨認的日常習慣、說話方式和生活程序。"},{"en":"A documentary may show the distinctive day-to-day life of fishermen in a small coastal town.","zh":"紀錄片可能展示小型沿海城鎮漁民獨特的日常生活。"},{"en":"If literature captures daily life well, readers can understand a culture from inside.","zh":"如果文學很好地捕捉日常生活，讀者就能從內部理解一種文化。"},{"en":"The phrase values ordinary details, not only dramatic events.","zh":"這個片語重視普通細節，而不只是戲劇性事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ordinary Scottish people","meaning":"普通蘇格蘭人","examples":[{"en":"His works describe the lives of ordinary Scottish people.","zh":"他的作品描寫普通蘇格蘭人的生活。"},{"en":"Ordinary Scottish people means everyday people from Scotland, not mainly kings, heroes or elites.","zh":"ordinary Scottish people 指來自蘇格蘭的平凡人，而不主要是國王、英雄或精英。"},{"en":"A novel about ordinary people may show family meals, work worries and local speech.","zh":"關於普通人的小說可能展示家庭飯局、工作煩惱和本地說話方式。"},{"en":"If writers focus on ordinary people, literature can preserve social life that history books may ignore.","zh":"如果作家集中於普通人，文學就能保存史書可能忽略的社會生活。"},{"en":"The phrase points to common people and everyday experience.","zh":"這個片語指向一般人和日常經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"point to something as","meaning":"指出……是","examples":[{"en":"Some critics point to local detail as a flaw in his works.","zh":"有些評論家指出本地細節是他作品的缺點。"},{"en":"Point to something as means identify something as an example, cause or evidence of a judgement.","zh":"point to something as 指把某事指出為判斷中的例子、原因或證據。"},{"en":"A teacher may point to weak evidence as the main problem in an essay.","zh":"老師可能指出證據薄弱是文章的主要問題。"},{"en":"If critics point to local detail as a weakness, others may see the same detail as a strength.","zh":"如果評論家指出本地細節是弱點，其他人可能把同一細節看成優點。"},{"en":"The phrase shows what evidence someone uses for their view.","zh":"這個片語顯示某人用甚麼證據支持看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a flaw of","meaning":"……的缺點","examples":[{"en":"Some critics saw the local nature of his writing as a flaw of his works.","zh":"有些評論家把他寫作的本地性視為作品的缺點。"},{"en":"A flaw of something is a weakness, fault or imperfection in it.","zh":"flaw of something 指某事物中的弱點、錯誤或不完美。"},{"en":"A flaw of a presentation may be that the slides are attractive but the argument is unclear.","zh":"演講的缺點可能是投影片吸引，但論點不清楚。"},{"en":"If one reader sees local detail as a flaw, another may see it as authenticity.","zh":"如果一位讀者把本地細節看成缺點，另一位可能把它看成真實感。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a perceived weakness.","zh":"這個片語指出被認為存在的弱點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"According to some critics, important literature should transcend local culture.","zh":"根據一些評論家所說，重要文學應超越本土文化。"},{"en":"According to means based on what a person, text or source says.","zh":"according to 指根據某人、文本或來源所說。"},{"en":"According to the timetable, the last bus leaves at ten o’clock.","zh":"根據時間表，尾班巴士在十點開出。"},{"en":"In essays, “according to” helps show whose opinion or evidence is being used.","zh":"在文章中，“according to” 有助顯示正在使用誰的意見或證據。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a source of information or viewpoint.","zh":"這個片語引出資訊或觀點來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"truly important literature","meaning":"真正重要的文學","examples":[{"en":"Critics argued that truly important literature should transcend local culture.","zh":"評論家認為真正重要的文學應超越本土文化。"},{"en":"Truly important literature means literature judged to have deep, lasting or universal value.","zh":"truly important literature 指被判斷具有深刻、持久或普遍價值的文學。"},{"en":"Some teachers believe truly important literature should help students understand life beyond exams.","zh":"有些老師認為真正重要的文學應幫助學生理解考試以外的人生。"},{"en":"If a work remains meaningful across generations, critics may call it truly important.","zh":"如果作品跨越世代仍有意義，評論家可能稱它真正重要。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a high standard of literary value.","zh":"這個片語標示文學價值的高標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"transcend local culture","meaning":"超越本土文化","examples":[{"en":"Some critics believed literature should transcend local culture and stories.","zh":"有些評論家認為文學應超越本土文化和故事。"},{"en":"Transcend local culture means rise beyond one specific place or community to speak more universally.","zh":"transcend local culture 指超越某一特定地方或社群，表達更普遍的意義。"},{"en":"A local film may transcend local culture if its family conflicts touch viewers everywhere.","zh":"如果本地電影中的家庭衝突能觸動各地觀眾，它就可能超越本土文化。"},{"en":"If critics demand universality, they may undervalue works rooted in one region.","zh":"如果評論家要求普遍性，可能低估扎根於某地區的作品。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts universal meaning with local detail.","zh":"這個片語把普遍意義與本地細節作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"local culture and stories","meaning":"本土文化和故事","examples":[{"en":"Some critics felt that great literature should rise above local culture and stories.","zh":"有些評論家認為偉大文學應超越本土文化和故事。"},{"en":"Local culture and stories are the customs, speech, memories and narratives of a particular place or community.","zh":"local culture and stories 指某特定地方或社群的習俗、語言、記憶和敍事。"},{"en":"A village’s local culture and stories may appear in festival songs and family legends.","zh":"村莊的本土文化和故事可能出現在節日歌曲和家庭傳說中。"},{"en":"If literature preserves local culture and stories, it can protect voices that might otherwise disappear.","zh":"如果文學保存本土文化和故事，就能保護原本可能消失的聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase links place-based identity with storytelling.","zh":"這個片語把地方身份與敍事連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"local taste","meaning":"本土色彩","examples":[{"en":"Many readers praise the local taste of Stevenson’s literature.","zh":"許多讀者讚賞 Stevenson 文學中的本土色彩。"},{"en":"Local taste means the flavour of a particular place, including its speech, customs, humour and atmosphere.","zh":"local taste 指某地方的味道，包括語言、習俗、幽默和氣氛。"},{"en":"A restaurant has local taste when its food reflects the habits and ingredients of the area.","zh":"當餐廳食物反映本地習慣和食材，它就有本土色彩。"},{"en":"In literature, local taste can make a story feel rooted and authentic.","zh":"在文學中，本土色彩可以令故事感覺扎根而真實。"},{"en":"The phrase values the distinct character of a place.","zh":"這個片語重視地方的獨特特色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"to this day","meaning":"直到今天","examples":[{"en":"To this day, Stevenson’s works offer insight into Scottish life.","zh":"直到今天，Stevenson 的作品仍提供對蘇格蘭生活的了解。"},{"en":"To this day means even now, after a long time has passed.","zh":"to this day 指即使經過很長時間，直到現在仍然如此。"},{"en":"To this day, former students remember the teacher who taught them to love reading.","zh":"直到今天，舊生仍記得那位教他們愛上閱讀的老師。"},{"en":"If a book remains useful to this day, it has continuing relevance.","zh":"如果一本書直到今天仍有用，它就有持續相關性。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses lasting importance into the present.","zh":"這個片語強調持續到現在的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"provide valuable insight into","meaning":"提供對……的寶貴了解","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s works provide valuable insight into life in Scotland.","zh":"Stevenson 的作品提供對蘇格蘭生活的寶貴了解。"},{"en":"Provide valuable insight into means give useful and deeper understanding of something.","zh":"provide valuable insight into 指提供對某事有用而更深入的理解。"},{"en":"A diary can provide valuable insight into how teenagers experience exam pressure.","zh":"日記可以提供對青少年如何經歷考試壓力的寶貴了解。"},{"en":"If a novel shows daily speech and customs, it may help readers understand a society from within.","zh":"如果小說展示日常語言和習俗，它可能幫助讀者從內部理解一個社會。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights understanding gained through careful observation or evidence.","zh":"這個片語突出透過細心觀察或證據獲得的理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"life in Scotland","meaning":"蘇格蘭生活","examples":[{"en":"His works provide insight into life in Scotland during the 19th century.","zh":"他的作品提供對十九世紀蘇格蘭生活的了解。"},{"en":"Life in Scotland means the everyday experiences, culture, work and relationships of people living in Scotland.","zh":"life in Scotland 指住在蘇格蘭的人們的日常經驗、文化、工作和關係。"},{"en":"A history lesson may use letters and novels to explain life in Scotland in earlier centuries.","zh":"歷史課可能使用書信和小說解釋較早世紀的蘇格蘭生活。"},{"en":"If literature shows ordinary life well, readers can imagine how people spoke, worked and lived.","zh":"如果文學很好地呈現普通生活，讀者就能想像人們如何說話、工作和生活。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to social and cultural life in a particular place.","zh":"這個片語指某特定地方的社會和文化生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"during the 19th century","meaning":"在十九世紀期間","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s works describe Scotland during the 19th century.","zh":"Stevenson 的作品描寫十九世紀期間的蘇格蘭。"},{"en":"During the 19th century means in the years from 1801 to 1900.","zh":"during the 19th century 指在1801年至1900年期間。"},{"en":"During the 19th century, many cities changed because of industry and transport.","zh":"在十九世紀期間，許多城市因工業和交通而改變。"},{"en":"If a novel is set during the 19th century, readers may need historical context to understand it fully.","zh":"如果小說設定於十九世紀，讀者可能需要歷史背景才能完全理解。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a historical time period.","zh":"這個片語給出歷史時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"choice of subject matter","meaning":"題材選擇","examples":[{"en":"Critics debated Stevenson’s choice of subject matter.","zh":"評論家爭論 Stevenson 的題材選擇。"},{"en":"Choice of subject matter means the topics, themes or situations a writer decides to write about.","zh":"choice of subject matter 指作家決定書寫的話題、主題或情況。"},{"en":"A student’s choice of subject matter affects whether an essay feels focused and interesting.","zh":"學生的題材選擇會影響文章是否集中而有趣。"},{"en":"If a writer chooses adventure rather than social realism, critics may judge the work differently.","zh":"如果作家選擇冒險題材而非社會寫實，評論家可能以不同方式評價作品。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on what the writer writes about.","zh":"這個片語集中於作家寫甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not the only source of attention","meaning":"並非唯一受關注的來源","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s writing was not the only source of attention for critics.","zh":"Stevenson 的寫作並非評論家唯一受關注的來源。"},{"en":"Not the only source of attention means not the only thing people noticed or discussed.","zh":"not the only source of attention 指不是人們注意或討論的唯一事物。"},{"en":"In a school performance, acting may not be the only source of attention; costumes and music may also matter.","zh":"在學校表演中，演技可能並非唯一受關注來源；服裝和音樂也可能重要。"},{"en":"If a writer’s life also attracts attention, discussion may move away from the books.","zh":"如果作家的生活也吸引注意，討論可能偏離書本。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that several things drew interest.","zh":"這個片語顯示有幾件事引起興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"source of attention","meaning":"受關注的來源","examples":[{"en":"His personal life became another source of attention.","zh":"他的私生活成為另一個受關注的來源。"},{"en":"A source of attention is something that attracts interest, discussion or public focus.","zh":"source of attention 指吸引興趣、討論或公眾焦點的事物。"},{"en":"A new sports centre may become a source of attention in a neighbourhood.","zh":"新體育中心可能成為社區中受關注的來源。"},{"en":"If a writer’s travels become a source of attention, readers may treat life and work together.","zh":"如果作家的旅行成為受關注來源，讀者可能把人生和作品一起看待。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what people are focusing on.","zh":"這個片語指出人們集中注意甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fans and critics alike","meaning":"支持者和評論家同樣","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s personal life interested fans and critics alike.","zh":"Stevenson 的私生活令支持者和評論家同樣感興趣。"},{"en":"Fans and critics alike means both supporters and evaluators, even though they may have different attitudes.","zh":"fans and critics alike 指支持者和評論者兩者，即使態度可能不同。"},{"en":"A controversial film may attract fans and critics alike because everyone wants to discuss it.","zh":"具爭議電影可能吸引支持者和評論家同樣關注，因為人人都想討論。"},{"en":"If both fans and critics are interested, a writer’s life becomes part of public debate.","zh":"如果支持者和評論家都感興趣，作家生活就成為公共爭論的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that two different groups share the same interest.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩個不同群體有共同興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"personal life outshone his writing","meaning":"私生活蓋過了他的作品","examples":[{"en":"Some argued that Stevenson’s personal life outshone his writing.","zh":"有些人認為 Stevenson 的私生活蓋過了他的作品。"},{"en":"Personal life outshone his writing means his private life received more attention than his books.","zh":"personal life outshone his writing 指他的私人生活比其書本受到更多關注。"},{"en":"A celebrity’s relationships may outshine their acting if the media talks about gossip more than performances.","zh":"如果媒體談八卦多於表演，名人的感情生活可能蓋過其演技。"},{"en":"If biography replaces literary discussion, readers may remember the life more than the work.","zh":"如果傳記討論取代文學討論，讀者可能記得人生多於作品。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests personal details became more prominent than artistic achievement.","zh":"這個片語暗示私人細節比藝術成就更突出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be plagued by","meaning":"長期受……困擾","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson had been plagued by health problems his whole life.","zh":"Stevenson 一生長期受健康問題困擾。"},{"en":"Be plagued by means be repeatedly troubled or seriously affected by something unpleasant.","zh":"be plagued by 指反覆受到不愉快事情困擾或嚴重影響。"},{"en":"A school may be plagued by noise if construction continues beside it for months.","zh":"如果建築工程在旁邊持續數月，學校可能長期受噪音困擾。"},{"en":"If a writer is plagued by illness, travel and work habits may be shaped by the need to recover.","zh":"如果作家長期受疾病困擾，旅行和工作習慣可能受康復需要塑造。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a long-running problem that is hard to escape.","zh":"這個片語暗示一個長期、難以擺脫的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"health problems","meaning":"健康問題","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson suffered from health problems throughout his life.","zh":"Stevenson 一生都受健康問題困擾。"},{"en":"Health problems are illnesses, weaknesses or physical conditions that affect wellbeing.","zh":"health problems 指影響身心狀態的疾病、虛弱或身體狀況。"},{"en":"A student with health problems may need rest, medicine or a flexible school schedule.","zh":"有健康問題的學生可能需要休息、藥物或彈性上課時間。"},{"en":"Long-term health problems can influence where a person lives and how they work.","zh":"長期健康問題可以影響一個人住在哪裡和如何工作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to difficulties connected with the body or health.","zh":"這個片語指與身體或健康有關的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"his whole life","meaning":"他一生","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson was affected by illness his whole life.","zh":"Stevenson 他一生都受疾病影響。"},{"en":"His whole life means from childhood to death, or throughout all of his life.","zh":"his whole life 指從童年到死亡，或貫穿整個人生。"},{"en":"A person may love music his whole life if childhood lessons create a lasting passion.","zh":"如果童年音樂課建立持久熱情，一個人可能他一生都熱愛音樂。"},{"en":"If someone faces illness his whole life, daily choices may be shaped by health limits.","zh":"如果某人一生面對疾病，日常選擇可能受健康限制塑造。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the full length of a person’s life.","zh":"這個片語強調一個人生命的完整長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"warmer climates","meaning":"較溫暖的氣候","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson often had to live in warmer climates to recover.","zh":"Stevenson 常不得不住在較溫暖的氣候中以康復。"},{"en":"Warmer climates are places with higher temperatures and milder weather.","zh":"warmer climates 指氣溫較高、天氣較溫和的地方。"},{"en":"A person with lung problems may feel better in warmer climates than in cold, damp places.","zh":"有肺部問題的人在較溫暖氣候中可能比在寒冷潮濕地方感覺更好。"},{"en":"If climate affects health, moving to a warmer place may become a medical decision.","zh":"如果氣候影響健康，搬到較暖地方可能成為醫療決定。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to places with relatively warm weather conditions.","zh":"這個片語指天氣條件相對溫暖的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cold, dreary weather","meaning":"寒冷沉悶的天氣","examples":[{"en":"He left the cold, dreary weather of Scotland for warmer places.","zh":"他離開蘇格蘭寒冷沉悶的天氣，前往較溫暖地方。"},{"en":"Cold, dreary weather means weather that is chilly, dull, gloomy and unpleasant.","zh":"cold, dreary weather 指寒冷、陰沉、灰暗而令人不舒服的天氣。"},{"en":"Students may feel sleepy on a day of cold, dreary weather with grey skies and heavy rain.","zh":"在灰天大雨、寒冷沉悶的日子，學生可能感到昏昏欲睡。"},{"en":"If cold, dreary weather worsens illness, a warmer climate may help recovery.","zh":"如果寒冷沉悶天氣令疾病惡化，較溫暖氣候可能有助康復。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a mood of discomfort and gloom.","zh":"這個片語營造不適和陰鬱的感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in order to recover","meaning":"為了康復","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson lived in warmer climates in order to recover.","zh":"Stevenson 住在較溫暖的氣候中，是為了康復。"},{"en":"In order to recover means for the purpose of becoming healthy again.","zh":"in order to recover 指為了重新恢復健康。"},{"en":"A student may stay home in order to recover from flu before returning to school.","zh":"學生可能留在家中從流感中康復，然後才返校。"},{"en":"If someone changes their environment in order to recover, health has become the main priority.","zh":"如果某人為了康復而改變環境，健康就成為主要優先事項。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly explains the purpose of an action.","zh":"這個片語清楚解釋行動目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the South Pacific island of Samoa","meaning":"南太平洋島嶼薩摩亞","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson took his family to the South Pacific island of Samoa.","zh":"Stevenson 帶家人前往南太平洋島嶼薩摩亞。"},{"en":"The South Pacific island of Samoa refers to Samoa, an island location in the South Pacific region.","zh":"South Pacific island of Samoa 指位於南太平洋地區的島嶼薩摩亞。"},{"en":"A travel writer may describe the South Pacific through its sea, climate, communities and journeys.","zh":"旅遊作家可能透過海洋、氣候、社群和旅程描寫南太平洋。"},{"en":"Moving to a distant island can shape a writer’s life, health and imagination.","zh":"搬到遙遠島嶼可以塑造作家的生活、健康和想像力。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a specific island setting connected with Stevenson’s later life.","zh":"這個片語指出與 Stevenson 晚年生活相關的特定島嶼背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a controversial decision","meaning":"具爭議的決定","examples":[{"en":"Moving to Samoa was a controversial decision at that time.","zh":"搬到薩摩亞在當時是具爭議的決定。"},{"en":"A controversial decision is a choice that causes disagreement or strong reactions.","zh":"controversial decision 指引起分歧或強烈反應的選擇。"},{"en":"A school’s decision to ban phones may be controversial if students and parents disagree.","zh":"如果學生和家長意見不一，學校禁止手機的決定可能具爭議。"},{"en":"If a writer makes a controversial decision, their personal life may attract public attention.","zh":"如果作家作出具爭議的決定，其私生活可能吸引公眾關注。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a choice that people argue about.","zh":"這個片語描述人們會爭論的選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at that time","meaning":"在當時","examples":[{"en":"The decision to move to Samoa was controversial at that time.","zh":"搬到薩摩亞的決定在當時具爭議。"},{"en":"At that time means during the particular period being discussed.","zh":"at that time 指在所討論的特定時期。"},{"en":"At that time, students wrote essays by hand because laptops were not common.","zh":"在當時，學生用手寫文章，因為手提電腦並不普遍。"},{"en":"A decision may seem strange at that time but reasonable when later events are understood.","zh":"一個決定在當時可能看似奇怪，但了解後來事件後可能變得合理。"},{"en":"The phrase places a judgement in its historical context.","zh":"這個片語把判斷放回其歷史語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"regret the decision","meaning":"後悔這個決定","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson did not regret the decision to move to Samoa.","zh":"Stevenson 並沒有後悔搬到薩摩亞這個決定。"},{"en":"Regret the decision means feel sorry or disappointed about a choice made earlier.","zh":"regret the decision 指對早前作出的選擇感到後悔或失望。"},{"en":"A student may regret the decision to revise only one topic before an exam.","zh":"學生可能後悔考試前只溫習一個課題這個決定。"},{"en":"If someone does not regret a difficult choice, they believe the benefits were worth the cost.","zh":"如果某人不後悔一個困難選擇，就表示他相信好處值得付出代價。"},{"en":"The phrase looks back at a past choice with approval or disappointment.","zh":"這個片語回望過去選擇，帶有認同或失望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sea air","meaning":"海風；海邊空氣","examples":[{"en":"The sea air helped restore Stevenson’s health for a time.","zh":"海風有一段時間幫助 Stevenson 恢復健康。"},{"en":"Sea air is the air near the sea, often imagined as fresh, moist and healthier.","zh":"sea air 指海邊的空氣，常被想像為清新、濕潤而較健康。"},{"en":"A family may visit the coast because the sea air helps them relax after a stressful month.","zh":"家庭可能到海邊，因為海風幫助他們在壓力大的一個月後放鬆。"},{"en":"If a patient feels better near the ocean, climate and environment may affect recovery.","zh":"如果病人在海邊感覺較好，氣候和環境可能影響康復。"},{"en":"The phrase connects the seaside environment with health or refreshment.","zh":"這個片語把海邊環境與健康或恢復精神連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the thrill of adventure","meaning":"冒險的刺激感","examples":[{"en":"The thrill of adventure complemented the themes of his writing.","zh":"冒險的刺激感與他寫作的主題相配合。"},{"en":"The thrill of adventure means the excitement people feel when facing risk, travel or the unknown.","zh":"thrill of adventure 指人面對風險、旅行或未知時感到的興奮。"},{"en":"A camping trip can give students the thrill of adventure when they sleep outdoors for the first time.","zh":"當學生第一次在戶外露營，露營旅行可以帶來冒險的刺激感。"},{"en":"If a writer loves travel, the thrill of adventure may enter their stories naturally.","zh":"如果作家熱愛旅行，冒險刺激感可能自然進入其故事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes excitement created by exploration and danger.","zh":"這個片語描述由探索和危險造成的興奮感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"complement the themes of","meaning":"與……的主題相配合","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s travels complemented the themes of his writing.","zh":"Stevenson 的旅行與他寫作的主題相配合。"},{"en":"Complement the themes of means fit well with and strengthen the main ideas of something.","zh":"complement the themes of 指與某事的主要思想配合良好並加強它們。"},{"en":"A film’s music can complement the themes of loneliness and hope.","zh":"電影配樂可以與孤獨和希望的主題相配合。"},{"en":"If a writer’s lifestyle matches their literary themes, readers may connect life and work more easily.","zh":"如果作家的生活方式與其文學主題相配合，讀者可能更容易連接人生和作品。"},{"en":"The phrase shows harmony between two elements.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩個元素之間的和諧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"for a time","meaning":"有一段時間","examples":[{"en":"For a time, the sea air restored Stevenson’s health.","zh":"有一段時間，海風恢復了 Stevenson 的健康。"},{"en":"For a time means for a limited period, not permanently.","zh":"for a time 指在有限期間內，而不是永久。"},{"en":"For a time, a student may feel motivated after receiving good exam results.","zh":"有一段時間，學生收到好成績後可能感到有動力。"},{"en":"If something helps only for a time, the improvement may not last.","zh":"如果某事只幫助一段時間，改善可能不能持久。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a temporary situation.","zh":"這個片語顯示暫時情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"restore his health","meaning":"恢復他的健康","examples":[{"en":"The warmer climate helped restore his health.","zh":"較溫暖氣候幫助恢復他的健康。"},{"en":"Restore his health means help him become healthier again after illness or weakness.","zh":"restore his health 指幫助他在疾病或虛弱後重新變得健康。"},{"en":"Rest, medicine and good food can help restore a patient’s health after surgery.","zh":"休息、藥物和良好食物可以幫助手術後病人恢復健康。"},{"en":"If a place restores someone’s health, it may become emotionally important to them.","zh":"如果一個地方恢復某人的健康，它可能對那人有情感上的重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes returning to a better physical condition.","zh":"這個片語描述回到較好的身體狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"gain a love of","meaning":"培養對……的熱愛","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson gained a love of travelling in the Pacific.","zh":"Stevenson 培養了對太平洋旅行的熱愛。"},{"en":"Gain a love of means gradually develop strong enjoyment or affection for something.","zh":"gain a love of 指逐漸培養對某事的強烈喜愛或感情。"},{"en":"A student may gain a love of reading after finding one novel that feels meaningful.","zh":"學生在找到一本有意義的小說後，可能培養對閱讀的熱愛。"},{"en":"If someone gains a love of travel, new places may shape their imagination and work.","zh":"如果某人培養對旅行的熱愛，新地方可能塑造其想像力和工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a feeling that develops over time.","zh":"這個片語描述隨時間發展的感情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"wander the Pacific","meaning":"漫遊太平洋","examples":[{"en":"For nearly three years, Stevenson wandered the eastern and central Pacific.","zh":"Stevenson 近三年漫遊太平洋東部和中部。"},{"en":"Wander the Pacific means travel around parts of the Pacific region, often in an open or exploratory way.","zh":"wander the Pacific 指在太平洋部分地區旅行，通常帶有開放或探索意味。"},{"en":"A travel writer may wander a city without a fixed route in order to notice ordinary life.","zh":"旅遊作家可能沒有固定路線地漫遊城市，以注意普通生活。"},{"en":"If a writer wanders through islands and ports, the journeys may become material for stories.","zh":"如果作家漫遊島嶼和港口，這些旅程可能成為故事材料。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests movement, exploration and uncertainty.","zh":"這個片語暗示移動、探索和不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the eastern and central Pacific","meaning":"太平洋東部和中部","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson travelled through the eastern and central Pacific.","zh":"Stevenson 旅行穿越太平洋東部和中部。"},{"en":"The eastern and central Pacific refers to areas in the east and middle parts of the Pacific Ocean region.","zh":"eastern and central Pacific 指太平洋地區東部和中部的範圍。"},{"en":"A travel route through the eastern and central Pacific may include many islands and long sea journeys.","zh":"穿越太平洋東部和中部的旅程可能包括許多島嶼和長途海上航行。"},{"en":"If a writer spends years there, the ocean landscape may influence their imagination.","zh":"如果作家在那裡生活多年，海洋景觀可能影響其想像力。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a broad geographical area.","zh":"這個片語指出一個廣泛地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reflect his love of travel","meaning":"反映他對旅行的熱愛","examples":[{"en":"Much of Stevenson’s work reflected his love of travel.","zh":"Stevenson 的許多作品反映他對旅行的熱愛。"},{"en":"Reflect his love of travel means show or express his strong interest in journeys and new places.","zh":"reflect his love of travel 指顯示或表達他對旅程和新地方的強烈興趣。"},{"en":"A student’s photos may reflect their love of nature if they mostly show mountains and rivers.","zh":"如果學生照片大多展示山和河，就可能反映他對自然的熱愛。"},{"en":"If an author loves travel, their books may include movement, foreign places and adventure.","zh":"如果作者熱愛旅行，其書可能包含移動、外地和冒險。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how personal interests appear in creative work.","zh":"這個片語顯示個人興趣如何出現在創作中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the adventures he experienced","meaning":"他所經歷的冒險","examples":[{"en":"His work reflected the adventures he experienced in the Pacific islands.","zh":"他的作品反映他在太平洋島嶼所經歷的冒險。"},{"en":"The adventures he experienced are the exciting, risky or unusual events he personally went through.","zh":"adventures he experienced 指他親身經歷的刺激、有風險或不尋常事件。"},{"en":"A traveller may write stories based on the adventures they experienced on a long journey.","zh":"旅人可能根據長途旅行中所經歷的冒險寫故事。"},{"en":"If real experiences enter fiction, the story may feel more vivid and believable.","zh":"如果真實經驗進入小說，故事可能更生動可信。"},{"en":"The phrase connects lived experience with later writing.","zh":"這個片語把親身經驗與後來寫作連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Pacific islands","meaning":"太平洋島嶼","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson experienced many adventures in the Pacific islands.","zh":"Stevenson 在太平洋島嶼經歷了許多冒險。"},{"en":"Pacific islands are islands located in the Pacific Ocean region.","zh":"Pacific islands 指位於太平洋地區的島嶼。"},{"en":"A travel writer visiting Pacific islands may describe beaches, villages, boats and local customs.","zh":"造訪太平洋島嶼的旅遊作家可能描寫海灘、村莊、船隻和本地習俗。"},{"en":"If a novelist lives among island communities, the setting may influence plot and atmosphere.","zh":"如果小說家生活於島嶼社群之中，背景可能影響情節和氣氛。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the island world connected with Stevenson’s travels.","zh":"這個片語指出與 Stevenson 旅行相關的島嶼世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as a result of","meaning":"由於；因為","examples":[{"en":"As a result of biographical attention, interest in his life grew.","zh":"由於對傳記資料的關注，人們對他生活的興趣增加。"},{"en":"As a result of means because of something, or as the consequence of it.","zh":"as a result of 指因為某事，或作為其結果。"},{"en":"As a result of heavy rain, the school sports day was cancelled.","zh":"由於大雨，學校運動會取消。"},{"en":"If media attention focuses on a writer’s life, readers may become curious about biography.","zh":"如果媒體關注作家生活，讀者可能對傳記產生好奇。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly connects cause and effect.","zh":"這個片語清楚連接原因和結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"biographical attention","meaning":"對傳記資料的關注","examples":[{"en":"Biographical attention sometimes drew readers away from Stevenson’s works.","zh":"對傳記資料的關注有時把讀者從 Stevenson 的作品中拉開。"},{"en":"Biographical attention means interest in the facts and stories of a person’s life.","zh":"biographical attention 指對某人生平事實和故事的興趣。"},{"en":"A famous singer’s biography may receive attention because fans want to know their struggles.","zh":"著名歌手的傳記可能受到關注，因為粉絲想知道其掙扎。"},{"en":"If biographical attention becomes too strong, the art itself may receive less discussion.","zh":"如果對傳記資料的關注太強，藝術本身可能獲得較少討論。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to focus on life history rather than only works.","zh":"這個片語指集中於生平歷史，而不只是作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the feeling grew that","meaning":"人們逐漸覺得","examples":[{"en":"The feeling grew that interest in Stevenson’s life had replaced interest in his works.","zh":"人們逐漸覺得，對 Stevenson 生活的興趣已取代對其作品的興趣。"},{"en":"The feeling grew that means more and more people began to believe or sense something.","zh":"the feeling grew that 指越來越多人開始相信或感覺某事。"},{"en":"The feeling grew that the school rule was unfair after several students shared their experiences.","zh":"在幾位學生分享經歷後，人們逐漸覺得該校規不公平。"},{"en":"If public attention keeps moving away from books, people may start to feel biography has taken over.","zh":"如果公眾注意力持續偏離書本，人們可能開始覺得傳記已取而代之。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a belief becoming stronger over time.","zh":"這個片語描述一種信念隨時間變強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"take the place of","meaning":"取代……","examples":[{"en":"Interest in Stevenson’s life had taken the place of interest in his works.","zh":"對 Stevenson 生活的興趣已取代對其作品的興趣。"},{"en":"Take the place of means replace something or become used instead of it.","zh":"take the place of 指取代某事物，或被用來代替它。"},{"en":"Online messages may take the place of handwritten letters in many families.","zh":"在許多家庭中，網上訊息可能取代手寫信件。"},{"en":"If biography takes the place of literary discussion, the writer’s books may be neglected.","zh":"如果傳記取代文學討論，作家的書可能被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase shows replacement.","zh":"這個片語顯示替代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"whether…or…","meaning":"不論是……還是……","examples":[{"en":"Whether critics focus on his writing, his beliefs or his lifestyle, opinions differ.","zh":"不論評論家集中於他的寫作、信念還是生活方式，意見都有分歧。"},{"en":"Whether A or B means no matter which possibility is true or chosen.","zh":"whether A or B 指不管哪一種可能是真實或被選擇。"},{"en":"Whether students study at home or in the library, they need a quiet place and clear goals.","zh":"不論學生在家中還是圖書館溫習，都需要安靜地方和清楚目標。"},{"en":"This structure includes several possibilities under one general statement.","zh":"這個結構把幾種可能性納入同一概括陳述。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when the result is the same across different cases.","zh":"當結果在不同情況下相同，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"writing subjects","meaning":"寫作題材","examples":[{"en":"Some critics focus on Stevenson’s writing subjects.","zh":"有些評論家集中於 Stevenson 的寫作題材。"},{"en":"Writing subjects are the topics or themes a writer chooses to write about.","zh":"writing subjects 指作家選擇書寫的話題或主題。"},{"en":"A student’s writing subjects may include school life, family pressure and future dreams.","zh":"學生的寫作題材可能包括校園生活、家庭壓力和未來夢想。"},{"en":"If critics dislike a writer’s subjects, they may undervalue the style or language.","zh":"如果評論家不喜歡作家的題材，可能低估其風格或語言。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the content areas of writing.","zh":"這個片語指寫作的內容範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"eccentric lifestyle","meaning":"古怪不尋常的生活方式","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s eccentric lifestyle attracted public attention.","zh":"Stevenson 古怪不尋常的生活方式吸引了公眾注意。"},{"en":"An eccentric lifestyle is an unusual way of living that does not follow ordinary social expectations.","zh":"eccentric lifestyle 指不跟從普通社會期望的不尋常生活方式。"},{"en":"An artist may have an eccentric lifestyle if they travel constantly and work at night.","zh":"如果藝術家經常旅行並在晚上工作，可能有古怪不尋常的生活方式。"},{"en":"If a writer’s lifestyle is eccentric, readers may become interested in the person as much as the books.","zh":"如果作家的生活方式古怪，讀者可能對其本人和書本同樣感興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unusual personal habits or choices.","zh":"這個片語描述不尋常的個人習慣或選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"travel and adventure","meaning":"旅行和冒險","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s lifestyle was shaped by travel and adventure.","zh":"Stevenson 的生活方式受旅行和冒險塑造。"},{"en":"Travel and adventure mean journeys to different places and exciting or risky experiences.","zh":"travel and adventure 指到不同地方的旅程，以及刺激或有風險的經歷。"},{"en":"A student may develop confidence through travel and adventure during an overseas exchange.","zh":"學生可能在海外交流中的旅行和冒險中建立信心。"},{"en":"If a writer’s life includes travel and adventure, those experiences may enter their stories.","zh":"如果作家生活中包含旅行和冒險，這些經歷可能進入其故事。"},{"en":"The phrase links movement with excitement and discovery.","zh":"這個片語把移動與刺激和發現連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"past and present","meaning":"過去和現在","examples":[{"en":"People from the past and present have different opinions about Stevenson.","zh":"過去和現在的人對 Stevenson 有不同看法。"},{"en":"Past and present means earlier times and the current time.","zh":"past and present 指較早時代和當前時代。"},{"en":"A museum connects past and present by showing old objects beside modern stories.","zh":"博物館透過把舊物件與現代故事並列，連接過去和現在。"},{"en":"If views change between past and present, history can show how values develop.","zh":"如果過去和現在的看法改變，歷史就能顯示價值觀如何發展。"},{"en":"The phrase compares older and current perspectives.","zh":"這個片語比較較舊和當前角度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have different opinions about","meaning":"對……有不同看法","examples":[{"en":"Critics have different opinions about Stevenson as an author.","zh":"評論家對 Stevenson 作為作家有不同看法。"},{"en":"Have different opinions about means hold different views or judgements on the same subject.","zh":"have different opinions about 指對同一主題持有不同觀點或判斷。"},{"en":"Students may have different opinions about whether school uniforms are useful.","zh":"學生可能對校服是否有用有不同看法。"},{"en":"When people have different opinions about a writer, discussion becomes richer but less settled.","zh":"當人們對作家有不同看法，討論會更豐富但較不確定。"},{"en":"The phrase shows disagreement without necessarily implying conflict.","zh":"這個片語顯示意見不同，但不一定暗示衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"controversial yet widely popular","meaning":"具爭議但廣受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson remains a controversial yet widely popular author.","zh":"Stevenson 仍是一位具爭議但廣受歡迎的作者。"},{"en":"Controversial yet widely popular means causing disagreement but still liked by many people.","zh":"controversial yet widely popular 指引起分歧但仍受許多人喜愛。"},{"en":"A film may be controversial yet widely popular if critics attack it but audiences love it.","zh":"如果電影受評論家攻擊但觀眾喜愛，它可能具爭議但廣受歡迎。"},{"en":"If an author is both controversial and popular, public success and critical approval may not match.","zh":"如果作者既具爭議又受歡迎，公眾成功和評論認可可能不一致。"},{"en":"The phrase combines disagreement with broad appeal.","zh":"這個片語結合分歧與廣泛吸引力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a figure in Western literature","meaning":"西方文學人物","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson remains an important figure in Western literature.","zh":"Stevenson 仍是西方文學中的重要人物。"},{"en":"A figure in Western literature is a person who has a recognised place in the literary tradition of Europe and related English-language cultures.","zh":"figure in Western literature 指在歐洲及相關英語文化的文學傳統中佔有公認位置的人。"},{"en":"A writer becomes a major figure when their works are still read, debated and taught.","zh":"當作家的作品仍被閱讀、爭論和教授，他就成為重要文學人物。"},{"en":"If Stevenson remains such a figure, his influence extends beyond one country.","zh":"如果 Stevenson 仍是這樣的人物，其影響就超越單一國家。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies someone’s position in a broad literary tradition.","zh":"這個片語指出某人在廣泛文學傳統中的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生為每題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choose the correct letter means select the option letter that matches the right answer.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇與正確答案相符的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice test, students may choose the correct letter after eliminating wrong options.","zh":"在多項選擇測驗中，學生可能在排除錯項後選出正確字母。"},{"en":"If students choose a letter without reading carefully, they may miss small differences in meaning.","zh":"如果學生未仔細閱讀就選字母，可能錯過意思上的細微差異。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"write the correct letter in boxes","meaning":"在方格內寫上正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students write the correct letter in boxes on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生在答題紙方格內寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"Write the correct letter in boxes means put the chosen option letter into the marked answer spaces.","zh":"write the correct letter in boxes 指把所選選項字母寫入指定答題方格。"},{"en":"In IELTS Reading, students must write answers clearly in the correct boxes.","zh":"在 IELTS 閱讀中，學生必須在正確方格內清楚寫答案。"},{"en":"If a student writes the right letter in the wrong box, the answer may be marked wrong.","zh":"如果學生把正確字母寫在錯誤方格，答案可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a precise instruction about answer format.","zh":"這個片語給出關於答案格式的精確指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Stevenson’s biographers","meaning":"史提芬遜的傳記作家","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s biographers helped shape his reputation.","zh":"Stevenson 的傳記作家幫助塑造他的聲譽。"},{"en":"Stevenson’s biographers are writers who researched and wrote accounts of Stevenson’s life.","zh":"Stevenson’s biographers 指研究並撰寫 Stevenson 生平記述的作者。"},{"en":"Biographers can influence how readers remember an author by choosing which details to emphasise.","zh":"傳記作家可以透過選擇強調哪些細節，影響讀者如何記住作家。"},{"en":"If a biographer praises writing skill rather than scandal, the author’s reputation may improve.","zh":"如果傳記作家讚賞寫作技巧而非醜聞，作者聲譽可能改善。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to those who wrote about Stevenson’s life.","zh":"這個片語指撰寫 Stevenson 生平的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"underestimate the role played by","meaning":"低估……所起的作用","examples":[{"en":"A critic may underestimate the role played by family in a writer’s life.","zh":"評論家可能低估家庭在作家人生中所起的作用。"},{"en":"Underestimate the role played by means fail to recognise how important someone or something was.","zh":"underestimate the role played by 指未能認識某人或某事有多重要。"},{"en":"A school may underestimate the role played by sleep in students’ exam performance.","zh":"學校可能低估睡眠在學生考試表現中所起的作用。"},{"en":"If critics underestimate family influence, they may miss an important source of a writer’s ideas.","zh":"如果評論家低估家庭影響，可能錯過作家思想的重要來源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving too little importance to a factor.","zh":"這個片語描述給予某因素太少重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the role played by","meaning":"由……所起的作用","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the role played by family in Stevenson’s life.","zh":"題目問家庭在 Stevenson 人生中所起的作用。"},{"en":"The role played by something is the part or influence it has in a situation.","zh":"role played by something 指某事在情況中的部分或影響。"},{"en":"The role played by parents in study habits can be large when children are young.","zh":"孩子年幼時，父母在學習習慣中所起的作用可能很大。"},{"en":"If we identify the role played by health in Stevenson’s life, his travels become easier to understand.","zh":"如果我們找出健康在 Stevenson 人生中所起的作用，就更容易理解他的旅行。"},{"en":"The phrase asks what function or influence something had.","zh":"這個片語詢問某事有甚麼功能或影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"overestimate the importance of","meaning":"高估……的重要性","examples":[{"en":"Some readers may overestimate the importance of a writer’s personal life.","zh":"有些讀者可能高估作家私生活的重要性。"},{"en":"Overestimate the importance of means think something matters more than it really does.","zh":"overestimate the importance of 指認為某事比實際更重要。"},{"en":"Students may overestimate the importance of difficult vocabulary and forget clear ideas.","zh":"學生可能高估艱深詞彙的重要性，而忘記清楚想法。"},{"en":"If readers overestimate biography, they may undervalue the actual writing.","zh":"如果讀者高估傳記，就可能低估實際寫作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving too much weight to something.","zh":"這個片語描述給予某事過多分量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in literary history","meaning":"在文學史上","examples":[{"en":"Critics debate Stevenson’s importance in literary history.","zh":"評論家爭論 Stevenson 在文學史上的重要性。"},{"en":"In literary history means within the development and record of literature over time.","zh":"in literary history 指在文學隨時間發展的記錄中。"},{"en":"A writer’s place in literary history depends on influence, originality and continued readership.","zh":"作家在文學史上的位置取決於影響、原創性和持續讀者群。"},{"en":"If a book changes later writing, it may become important in literary history.","zh":"如果一本書改變後來寫作，它可能在文學史上變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase places a writer or work within the story of literature.","zh":"這個片語把作家或作品放入文學故事中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"exaggerate someone’s religious beliefs","meaning":"誇大某人的宗教信念","examples":[{"en":"Some critics may exaggerate a writer’s religious beliefs.","zh":"有些評論家可能誇大作家的宗教信念。"},{"en":"Exaggerate someone’s religious beliefs means make their beliefs seem stronger, stranger or more important than they really are.","zh":"exaggerate someone’s religious beliefs 指令某人的信念看似比實際更強、更奇怪或更重要。"},{"en":"A reader may exaggerate a teacher’s beliefs after hearing only one comment in class.","zh":"讀者可能只聽到老師課堂上一句話，就誇大老師的信念。"},{"en":"If critics exaggerate an author’s religion, their interpretation of the work may become unfair.","zh":"如果評論家誇大作者的宗教，其作品解讀可能變得不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase describes overstating someone’s faith or religious views.","zh":"這個片語描述誇大某人的信仰或宗教觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"enhance someone’s reputation","meaning":"提升某人的聲譽","examples":[{"en":"A favourable biography can enhance a writer’s reputation.","zh":"有利的傳記可以提升作家的聲譽。"},{"en":"Enhance someone’s reputation means improve how people judge or respect that person.","zh":"enhance someone’s reputation 指改善人們對某人的評價或尊重。"},{"en":"Winning a public speaking prize can enhance a student’s reputation at school.","zh":"贏得公開演講獎可以提升學生在學校的聲譽。"},{"en":"If critics praise a writer’s skill, they may enhance the writer’s reputation over time.","zh":"如果評論家讚賞作家技巧，他們可能隨時間提升作家聲譽。"},{"en":"The phrase shows improvement in public image or status.","zh":"這個片語顯示公眾形象或地位改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"reputation as a writer","meaning":"作為作家的聲譽","examples":[{"en":"The biographers enhanced Stevenson’s reputation as a writer.","zh":"傳記作家提升了 Stevenson 作為作家的聲譽。"},{"en":"Reputation as a writer means how people judge a person’s quality, importance or status in writing.","zh":"reputation as a writer 指人們如何評價一個人在寫作上的質素、重要性或地位。"},{"en":"A novelist’s reputation as a writer may improve after critics praise their latest book.","zh":"小說家的新書受到評論家讚賞後，其作為作家的聲譽可能提升。"},{"en":"If personal gossip dominates discussion, reputation as a writer may become harder to assess fairly.","zh":"如果私人八卦主導討論，作為作家的聲譽可能更難被公平評估。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on literary standing, not general fame.","zh":"這個片語集中於文學地位，而不是一般名氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the main point of","meaning":"……的主要意思","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for the main point of the second paragraph.","zh":"題目要求找出第二段的主要意思。"},{"en":"The main point of something is its central idea or most important message.","zh":"main point of something 指某事的中心思想或最重要訊息。"},{"en":"The main point of a lesson may be that examples should teach meaning clearly.","zh":"一課的主要意思可能是例句應清楚教出意思。"},{"en":"If students miss the main point, they may remember details but misunderstand the argument.","zh":"如果學生錯過主要意思，可能記得細節但誤解論點。"},{"en":"The phrase asks what the text is mainly trying to say.","zh":"這個片語詢問文本主要想說甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"give fairer assessments to","meaning":"對……作出較公平的評價","examples":[{"en":"The public may give fairer assessments to a writer over time.","zh":"隨時間過去，公眾可能對作家作出較公平的評價。"},{"en":"Give fairer assessments to means judge someone more reasonably and less unfairly than before.","zh":"give fairer assessments to 指比以前更合理、較不偏頗地評價某人。"},{"en":"A teacher can give fairer assessments to students by considering effort, progress and final performance.","zh":"老師可以透過考慮努力、進步和最終表現，對學生作出較公平的評價。"},{"en":"If time reduces gossip and prejudice, later critics may judge a writer’s work more fairly.","zh":"如果時間減少八卦和偏見，後來評論家可能更公平地評價作家的作品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improved judgement.","zh":"這個片語描述改善了的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"fairer assessments","meaning":"較公平的評價","examples":[{"en":"Modern critics may offer fairer assessments of Stevenson’s works.","zh":"現代評論家可能對 Stevenson 的作品提出較公平的評價。"},{"en":"Fairer assessments are judgements that are more balanced, accurate and less biased.","zh":"fairer assessments 指更平衡、準確且較少偏見的判斷。"},{"en":"A fairer assessment of a student should consider improvement, not only one bad test.","zh":"對學生較公平的評價應考慮進步，而不只是一次差測驗。"},{"en":"If critics read a work in context, their assessment may become fairer.","zh":"如果評論家在語境中閱讀作品，其評價可能變得較公平。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a move away from unfair judgement.","zh":"這個片語暗示遠離不公平判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"recent criticism","meaning":"近期批評","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether recent criticism has been justified.","zh":"題目問近期批評是否有道理。"},{"en":"Recent criticism means negative judgement made in the near past or by modern commentators.","zh":"recent criticism 指近來或由現代評論者作出的負面評價。"},{"en":"Recent criticism of a school app may focus on privacy and technical problems.","zh":"對學校應用程式的近期批評可能集中於私隱和技術問題。"},{"en":"If recent criticism is based on new evidence, old reputations may be challenged.","zh":"如果近期批評基於新證據，舊有聲譽可能受到挑戰。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to criticism from a relatively current period.","zh":"這個片語指相對近期的批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be justified","meaning":"有道理；有根據","examples":[{"en":"Some readers believe that criticism of Stevenson is justified.","zh":"有些讀者相信對 Stevenson 的批評有道理。"},{"en":"Be justified means be reasonable, fair or supported by good reasons.","zh":"be justified 指合理、公平或有充分理由支持。"},{"en":"A complaint is justified if a customer paid for a service and never received it.","zh":"如果顧客付了服務費卻從未收到服務，投訴就是有根據的。"},{"en":"If criticism is justified, evidence should show that the weakness really exists.","zh":"如果批評有道理，證據應顯示弱點確實存在。"},{"en":"The phrase asks whether a judgement has a proper basis.","zh":"這個片語詢問判斷是否有適當基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"outweigh the flaws in","meaning":"比……的缺點更重要","examples":[{"en":"Some critics think Stevenson’s style outweighs the flaws in his personal life.","zh":"有些評論家認為 Stevenson 的風格比其私生活中的缺點更重要。"},{"en":"Outweigh the flaws in means be more important than the weaknesses or faults in something.","zh":"outweigh the flaws in 指比某事中的弱點或缺點更重要。"},{"en":"A student’s clear ideas may outweigh small grammar mistakes in a speaking exam.","zh":"在口語考試中，學生清楚的想法可能比小文法錯誤更重要。"},{"en":"If literary skill outweighs personal flaws, critics may focus more on the work than the life.","zh":"如果文學技巧比個人缺點更重要，評論家可能更集中於作品而非人生。"},{"en":"The phrase compares strengths against weaknesses.","zh":"這個片語比較優點和缺點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"flaws in someone’s personal life","meaning":"某人私生活中的缺點","examples":[{"en":"Biographers may choose not to focus on flaws in a writer’s personal life.","zh":"傳記作家可能選擇不集中於作家私生活中的缺點。"},{"en":"Flaws in someone’s personal life are weaknesses, mistakes or troubling details in their private behaviour or relationships.","zh":"flaws in someone’s personal life 指其私人行為或關係中的弱點、錯誤或令人不安的細節。"},{"en":"A public figure’s flaws in personal life may attract media attention even when unrelated to their work.","zh":"公眾人物私生活中的缺點可能吸引媒體注意，即使與其工作無關。"},{"en":"If critics focus too much on private flaws, they may judge the writing unfairly.","zh":"如果評論家過度集中於私人缺點，可能不公平地評價寫作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to personal weaknesses outside the work itself.","zh":"這個片語指作品本身以外的個人弱點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"according to the author","meaning":"根據作者所說","examples":[{"en":"According to the author, adventure stories were often seen as morally limited.","zh":"根據作者所說，冒險故事常被視為道德上有限。"},{"en":"According to the author means based on what the writer of the passage says.","zh":"according to the author 指根據文章作者所說。"},{"en":"According to the author, students should not answer from memory if the passage gives no evidence.","zh":"根據作者所說，如果文章沒有證據，學生不應憑記憶作答。"},{"en":"In reading questions, this phrase tells students to use the passage writer’s view.","zh":"在閱讀題中，這個片語提醒學生使用文章作者的看法。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of the claim.","zh":"這個片語指出主張的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"cannot be used to","meaning":"不能用來……","examples":[{"en":"Some critics believed adventure stories could not be used to convey moral values.","zh":"有些評論家認為冒險故事不能用來傳達道德價值。"},{"en":"Cannot be used to means is not suitable or able to serve a particular purpose.","zh":"cannot be used to 指不適合或不能達成某特定目的。"},{"en":"A broken calculator cannot be used to check exam answers accurately.","zh":"壞了的計算機不能用來準確檢查考試答案。"},{"en":"If critics say a genre cannot be used to teach morals, they reject its educational value.","zh":"如果評論家說某體裁不能用來教導道德，他們就是拒絕其教育價值。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses inability or unsuitability for a purpose.","zh":"這個片語表達能力不足或不適合作某用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"convey moral values","meaning":"傳達道德價值","examples":[{"en":"Critics doubted whether adventure stories could convey moral values.","zh":"評論家懷疑冒險故事能否傳達道德價值。"},{"en":"Convey moral values means communicate ideas about right conduct, responsibility and character.","zh":"convey moral values 指傳達關於正確行為、責任和品格的觀念。"},{"en":"A children’s story may convey moral values by showing why lying hurts trust.","zh":"兒童故事可以透過展示說謊為何傷害信任來傳達道德價值。"},{"en":"If a story conveys moral values subtly, readers may learn without feeling lectured.","zh":"如果故事含蓄地傳達道德價值，讀者可能在不覺得被說教下學習。"},{"en":"The phrase connects storytelling with ethical meaning.","zh":"這個片語把敍事與倫理意義連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a fashionable art form","meaning":"時興的藝術形式","examples":[{"en":"Adventure fiction can become a fashionable art form.","zh":"冒險小說可以成為時興的藝術形式。"},{"en":"A fashionable art form is a type of art that becomes popular or admired at a particular time.","zh":"fashionable art form 指在某一時期變得流行或受欣賞的藝術類型。"},{"en":"Street photography became a fashionable art form when people began valuing everyday city life.","zh":"當人們開始重視日常城市生活，街頭攝影成為時興藝術形式。"},{"en":"If a genre becomes fashionable, critics may start taking it more seriously.","zh":"如果某體裁變得時興，評論家可能開始更認真看待它。"},{"en":"The phrase links artistic form with social popularity.","zh":"這個片語把藝術形式與社會流行連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be found in","meaning":"可見於……","examples":[{"en":"Adventure stories can be found in the works of many writers.","zh":"冒險故事可見於許多作家的作品中。"},{"en":"Be found in means exist or appear within something.","zh":"be found in 指存在或出現在某事物之中。"},{"en":"Strong examples can be found in many good student essays.","zh":"許多優秀學生文章中可見有力例子。"},{"en":"If a theme is found in many writers’ works, it may belong to a broader literary tradition.","zh":"如果某主題可見於許多作家的作品，它可能屬於更廣泛的文學傳統。"},{"en":"The phrase tells us where something appears.","zh":"這個片語告訴我們某事出現在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"other writers’ works","meaning":"其他作家的作品","examples":[{"en":"The question compares Stevenson’s writing with other writers’ works.","zh":"題目把 Stevenson 的寫作與其他作家的作品作比較。"},{"en":"Other writers’ works are books, poems, essays or stories written by authors besides the one being discussed.","zh":"other writers’ works 指由所討論作者以外的作家所寫的書、詩、散文或故事。"},{"en":"Students may compare a poem with other writers’ works to understand style and theme.","zh":"學生可能把一首詩與其他作家的作品比較，以理解風格和主題。"},{"en":"If Stevenson is compared with other writers’ works, critics can judge what makes him distinctive.","zh":"如果 Stevenson 與其他作家的作品比較，評論家就能判斷他有何獨特。"},{"en":"The phrase places one author’s writing beside others.","zh":"這個片語把一位作者的寫作放在其他作者旁邊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"commonly regarded as","meaning":"通常被視為","examples":[{"en":"Some critics did not commonly regard Stevenson’s stories as serious literature.","zh":"有些評論家通常不把 Stevenson 的故事視為嚴肅文學。"},{"en":"Commonly regarded as means generally seen or considered as something by many people.","zh":"commonly regarded as 指被許多人普遍看成或認為是某事。"},{"en":"A school may be commonly regarded as successful if its students are confident and well supported.","zh":"如果學生自信且獲得良好支援，一所學校可能通常被視為成功。"},{"en":"If a genre is not commonly regarded as serious, its best works may still be undervalued.","zh":"如果某體裁通常不被視為嚴肅，其最佳作品仍可能被低估。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a general public or critical view.","zh":"這個片語顯示一般公眾或評論看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"real literature","meaning":"真正文學","examples":[{"en":"Critics disagreed about whether Stevenson’s works counted as real literature.","zh":"評論家對 Stevenson 的作品是否算是真正文學意見不一。"},{"en":"Real literature means writing considered serious, valuable and worthy of study.","zh":"real literature 指被視為嚴肅、有價值且值得研究的寫作。"},{"en":"Some people wrongly assume that popular books cannot be real literature.","zh":"有些人錯誤地假設流行書籍不能是真正文學。"},{"en":"If a work has strong language, themes and influence, readers may argue it deserves literary status.","zh":"如果作品有強大語言、主題和影響，讀者可能認為它值得文學地位。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used in debates about literary value.","zh":"這個片語常用於關於文學價值的爭論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"transcend local culture and stories","meaning":"超越本土文化和故事","examples":[{"en":"Some critics argued that great literature should transcend local culture and stories.","zh":"有些評論家認為偉大文學應超越本土文化和故事。"},{"en":"Transcend local culture and stories means go beyond one place’s customs and narratives to reach wider meaning.","zh":"transcend local culture and stories 指超越某地方的習俗和敍事，以達到更廣泛意義。"},{"en":"A novel rooted in one village may transcend local culture if its emotions feel universal.","zh":"扎根於一條村的小說，如果其情感具普遍性，就可能超越本土文化。"},{"en":"If critics demand transcendence, they may disagree with readers who value local detail.","zh":"如果評論家要求超越性，他們可能不同意重視本地細節的讀者。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts universal reach with local rootedness.","zh":"這個片語把普遍觸及與本地扎根作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the lifestyle of","meaning":"……的生活方式","examples":[{"en":"The lifestyle of Stevenson attracted considerable public attention.","zh":"Stevenson 的生活方式吸引了相當多公眾注意。"},{"en":"The lifestyle of someone means the way that person lives, including habits, travel, work and choices.","zh":"lifestyle of someone 指某人的生活方式，包括習慣、旅行、工作和選擇。"},{"en":"The lifestyle of a professional athlete often includes strict training, diet and rest.","zh":"職業運動員的生活方式通常包括嚴格訓練、飲食和休息。"},{"en":"If a writer’s lifestyle is unusual, the public may discuss it as much as their books.","zh":"如果作家的生活方式不尋常，公眾可能像討論書一樣討論它。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces someone’s way of living.","zh":"這個片語引出某人的生活方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be responsible for","meaning":"對……負責；是……的原因","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Stevenson’s lifestyle was responsible for his death.","zh":"題目問 Stevenson 的生活方式是否是他死亡的原因。"},{"en":"Be responsible for means be the cause of something or have duty for it.","zh":"be responsible for 指是某事的原因，或對某事有責任。"},{"en":"Poor sleep may be responsible for a student’s weak concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可能是學生課堂專注力弱的原因。"},{"en":"If lifestyle is responsible for illness, daily habits may need serious change.","zh":"如果生活方式是疾病原因，日常習慣可能需要嚴肅改變。"},{"en":"The phrase can refer to cause or responsibility depending on context.","zh":"這個片語可根據語境指原因或責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"gain more attention from","meaning":"從……獲得更多關注","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s personal life gained more attention from some readers than his works.","zh":"Stevenson 的私生活從一些讀者那裡獲得比其作品更多的關注。"},{"en":"Gain more attention from means receive greater interest or focus from a group of people.","zh":"gain more attention from 指從某群人那裡得到更大興趣或焦點。"},{"en":"A school’s sports team may gain more attention from students after winning a championship.","zh":"學校運動隊贏得冠軍後，可能從學生那裡獲得更多關注。"},{"en":"If a writer’s life gains more attention than their books, literary discussion may become distorted.","zh":"如果作家人生比其書本獲得更多關注，文學討論可能變得扭曲。"},{"en":"The phrase compares what people choose to focus on.","zh":"這個片語比較人們選擇集中於甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"prepare someone well for","meaning":"使某人為……作好準備","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Stevenson’s life prepared him well for Samoa.","zh":"題目問 Stevenson 的人生是否使他為薩摩亞作好準備。"},{"en":"Prepare someone well for means give someone the experience, skills or strength needed for a future situation.","zh":"prepare someone well for 指給某人面對未來情況所需的經驗、技能或力量。"},{"en":"Practice interviews can prepare students well for real job interviews.","zh":"模擬面試可以使學生為真正求職面試作好準備。"},{"en":"If travel and illness prepared Stevenson for Samoa, his earlier life helped him face that move.","zh":"如果旅行和疾病使 Stevenson 為薩摩亞作好準備，他早年人生就幫助他面對那次搬遷。"},{"en":"The phrase connects past experience with later readiness.","zh":"這個片語把過去經驗與後來準備狀態連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"agree with the information given in","meaning":"符合文中資料","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the information given in the passage.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否符合文章中的資料。"},{"en":"Agree with the information given in means match what the text actually says.","zh":"agree with the information given in 指與文本實際所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the passage says Stevenson moved to Samoa, a statement saying the same thing agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說 Stevenson 搬到薩摩亞，意思相同的陳述就符合資料。"},{"en":"Students should check the passage, not answer from general knowledge.","zh":"學生應查看文章，而不是根據常識作答。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in TRUE, FALSE and NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於 TRUE、FALSE 和 NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the information in the passage.","zh":"陳述可能與文章中的資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradict the information means say the opposite of what the passage states.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章陳述相反的內容。"},{"en":"If a text says the meeting was in Kobe, an answer saying it was in Tokyo contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文本說會議在神戶舉行，而答案說在東京，就是與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should choose FALSE only when the conflict with the text is clear.","zh":"只有當與文本的衝突清楚時，學生才應選 FALSE。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct disagreement with the passage.","zh":"這個片語描述與文章直接不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"If the passage gives no evidence, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文章沒有提供證據，文中就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the text does not state whether the claim is true or false.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文本沒有說明某主張是真還是假。"},{"en":"If a passage discusses Stevenson’s writing but not his school marks, there is no information on his marks.","zh":"如果文章討論 Stevenson 的寫作但沒有討論他的學校成績，文中就沒有其成績相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when the passage gives no support.","zh":"當文章沒有支持時，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase explains when NOT GIVEN is the correct answer.","zh":"這個片語解釋何時 NOT GIVEN 是正確答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"initially encourage someone to","meaning":"最初鼓勵某人去……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Stevenson initially encouraged Wilde to write.","zh":"題目問 Stevenson 是否最初鼓勵 Wilde 去寫作。"},{"en":"Initially encourage someone to means first give someone support or confidence to do something.","zh":"initially encourage someone to 指一開始給某人支持或信心去做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may initially encourage a shy student to speak by asking one easy question.","zh":"老師可能透過問一條簡單問題，最初鼓勵害羞學生發言。"},{"en":"If someone initially encourages a writer, they may influence the beginning of that writer’s career.","zh":"如果某人最初鼓勵作家，可能影響該作家事業開端。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on early encouragement.","zh":"這個片語集中於早期鼓勵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"pay attention only to","meaning":"只注意……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether critics paid attention only to Stevenson’s subjects.","zh":"題目問評論家是否只注意 Stevenson 的題材。"},{"en":"Pay attention only to means focus on one thing and ignore other important things.","zh":"pay attention only to 指只集中於一件事，而忽略其他重要事。"},{"en":"A student who pays attention only to vocabulary may forget grammar and organisation.","zh":"只注意詞彙的學生可能忘記文法和組織。"},{"en":"If critics pay attention only to subject matter, they may miss style, structure and language.","zh":"如果評論家只注意題材，可能錯過風格、結構和語言。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against too narrow a focus.","zh":"這個片語提醒不要焦點太狹窄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete the notes","meaning":"完成筆記","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the notes using the list of words.","zh":"學生使用詞語列表完成筆記。"},{"en":"Complete the notes means fill in missing information in short study notes.","zh":"complete the notes 指填補簡短學習筆記中缺失的資料。"},{"en":"In a reading exercise, students complete the notes by choosing words that fit the meaning and grammar.","zh":"在閱讀練習中，學生透過選擇符合意思和文法的詞來完成筆記。"},{"en":"If notes are completed accurately, they show the student has understood the passage.","zh":"如果筆記準確完成，就顯示學生理解了文章。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction for summary-style tasks.","zh":"這個片語是摘要式題目的常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"using the list of words","meaning":"使用詞語列表","examples":[{"en":"The notes should be completed using the list of words.","zh":"筆記應使用詞語列表完成。"},{"en":"Using the list of words means selecting answers from the words provided, not inventing new ones.","zh":"using the list of words 指從所提供詞語中選擇答案，而不是自行創造新詞。"},{"en":"In an exam, using the list of words carefully can prevent spelling and word-form mistakes.","zh":"在考試中，仔細使用詞語列表可以避免拼字和詞形錯誤。"},{"en":"If students ignore the list, they may write an answer that is correct in meaning but not accepted.","zh":"如果學生忽略列表，可能寫出意思正確但不被接受的答案。"},{"en":"The phrase limits where the answers should come from.","zh":"這個片語限制答案應來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"Sir Walter Scott and Robert Louis Stevenson","meaning":"華特・司各特爵士與羅拔・路易斯・史提芬遜","examples":[{"en":"The notes compare Sir Walter Scott and Robert Louis Stevenson.","zh":"筆記比較華特・司各特爵士與羅拔・路易斯・史提芬遜。"},{"en":"Sir Walter Scott and Robert Louis Stevenson are two major Scottish writers often discussed in relation to literary influence.","zh":"Sir Walter Scott and Robert Louis Stevenson 是兩位常被放在文學影響角度討論的蘇格蘭重要作家。"},{"en":"A literature class may compare two writers to see how their styles and themes differ.","zh":"文學課可能比較兩位作家，以了解其風格和主題如何不同。"},{"en":"Comparing Scott and Stevenson helps students understand different forms of Scottish literary achievement.","zh":"比較 Scott 和 Stevenson 有助學生理解蘇格蘭文學成就的不同形式。"},{"en":"The phrase names the two writers being compared.","zh":"這個片語指出被比較的兩位作家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a lot of people believe that","meaning":"很多人認為","examples":[{"en":"A lot of people believe that Scott and Stevenson are key Scottish writers.","zh":"很多人認為 Scott 和 Stevenson 是關鍵蘇格蘭作家。"},{"en":"A lot of people believe that means many people hold a particular opinion.","zh":"a lot of people believe that 指許多人持有某種意見。"},{"en":"A lot of people believe that reading every day improves writing fluency.","zh":"很多人認為每日閱讀能改善寫作流暢度。"},{"en":"If many people believe a writer is important, their reputation may become more stable.","zh":"如果很多人認為某位作家重要，其聲譽可能變得更穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a common belief, not necessarily a proven fact.","zh":"這個片語引出普遍信念，而不一定是已證明事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"proficient in","meaning":"精通；擅長","examples":[{"en":"Scott is described as more proficient in technical control.","zh":"Scott 被描述為更擅長技術掌控。"},{"en":"Proficient in means skilled and capable in a particular area.","zh":"proficient in 指在某特定範疇有技巧和能力。"},{"en":"A student proficient in English can explain ideas clearly in speech and writing.","zh":"擅長英文的學生能在說話和寫作中清楚解釋想法。"},{"en":"If a writer is proficient in structure, their stories may feel carefully controlled.","zh":"如果作家擅長結構，其故事可能感覺受到仔細控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical competence.","zh":"這個片語描述實際能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"technical control","meaning":"技術掌控","examples":[{"en":"Some critics praise Scott’s technical control.","zh":"有些評論家讚賞 Scott 的技術掌控。"},{"en":"Technical control means skilful management of structure, pacing, language and artistic method.","zh":"technical control 指對結構、節奏、語言和藝術方法的熟練管理。"},{"en":"A singer shows technical control by keeping pitch, rhythm and breathing steady.","zh":"歌手透過保持音準、節奏和呼吸穩定來顯示技術掌控。"},{"en":"In writing, technical control helps a long story stay organised and balanced.","zh":"在寫作中，技術掌控幫助長篇故事保持有組織和平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on disciplined craft.","zh":"這個片語集中於有紀律的工藝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"better natural ability","meaning":"更好的天賦","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson is said to have better natural ability in storytelling.","zh":"Stevenson 被說成在敍事方面有更好的天賦。"},{"en":"Better natural ability means stronger instinctive talent than someone else in a particular area.","zh":"better natural ability 指在某範疇比別人有更強本能才華。"},{"en":"One student may have better natural ability in speaking, while another improves through practice.","zh":"一位學生可能在口語上有更好天賦，而另一位則透過練習進步。"},{"en":"If a writer has natural storytelling ability, characters and scenes may feel alive with little effort.","zh":"如果作家有敍事天賦，人物和場景可能輕易顯得生動。"},{"en":"The phrase compares inborn talent.","zh":"這個片語比較天生才華。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"illustrate depth","meaning":"展現深度","examples":[{"en":"Scott’s books illustrate depth, especially in tragedy.","zh":"Scott 的書展現深度，尤其在悲劇方面。"},{"en":"Illustrate depth means show seriousness, complexity or richness through examples or artistic treatment.","zh":"illustrate depth 指透過例子或藝術處理呈現嚴肅性、複雜性或豐富性。"},{"en":"A film may illustrate depth by showing both sides of a family conflict.","zh":"電影可以透過展示家庭衝突的雙方來展現深度。"},{"en":"If a novel illustrates depth, readers think beyond surface events.","zh":"如果小說展現深度，讀者會思考表面事件以外的東西。"},{"en":"The phrase praises a work for showing more than simple action.","zh":"這個片語讚賞作品呈現的不只是簡單動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"in terms of tragedy","meaning":"在悲劇方面","examples":[{"en":"Scott’s books show depth especially in terms of tragedy.","zh":"Scott 的書尤其在悲劇方面展現深度。"},{"en":"In terms of tragedy means when considering tragic themes, suffering or serious loss.","zh":"in terms of tragedy 指從悲劇主題、痛苦或嚴重失去的角度考慮。"},{"en":"A play may be powerful in terms of tragedy if it shows how one mistake destroys a family.","zh":"如果戲劇展示一個錯誤如何毀掉一個家庭，它在悲劇方面可能很有力。"},{"en":"If critics praise a writer in terms of tragedy, they value emotional and moral seriousness.","zh":"如果評論家在悲劇方面讚賞作家，他們重視情感和道德嚴肅性。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows the discussion to one aspect.","zh":"這個片語把討論收窄到一個方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"readers prefer","meaning":"讀者較喜歡","examples":[{"en":"Many readers prefer Stevenson’s storytelling.","zh":"許多讀者較喜歡 Stevenson 的敍事技巧。"},{"en":"Readers prefer means readers like one writer, style or work more than another.","zh":"readers prefer 指讀者比起另一位作家、風格或作品，更喜歡某一方。"},{"en":"Some readers prefer short chapters because they feel easier to finish after school.","zh":"有些讀者較喜歡短章節，因為放學後較容易讀完。"},{"en":"If readers prefer a writer’s storytelling, popularity may remain strong despite criticism.","zh":"如果讀者較喜歡某作家的敍事技巧，即使有批評，受歡迎程度仍可能強。"},{"en":"The phrase shows audience choice or taste.","zh":"這個片語顯示讀者選擇或品味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"understanding of human nature","meaning":"對人性的理解","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s understanding of human nature shaped his writing.","zh":"Stevenson 對人性的理解塑造了他的寫作。"},{"en":"Understanding of human nature means insight into how people think, feel, desire and behave.","zh":"understanding of human nature 指對人如何思考、感受、渴望和行動的洞察。"},{"en":"A good teacher needs understanding of human nature to know why students feel nervous or proud.","zh":"好老師需要對人性的理解，才能知道學生為何緊張或自豪。"},{"en":"If a writer understands human nature, characters may feel believable and complex.","zh":"如果作家理解人性，人物可能顯得可信而複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to insight into people’s inner lives.","zh":"這個片語指對人內心生活的洞察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"uniquely expressive portrayal","meaning":"獨特而富表現力的描寫","examples":[{"en":"His writing gave a uniquely expressive portrayal of Scottish people.","zh":"他的寫作對蘇格蘭人作出獨特而富表現力的描寫。"},{"en":"A uniquely expressive portrayal is a very distinctive and vivid representation of people or life.","zh":"uniquely expressive portrayal 指對人物或生活作出非常獨特而生動的呈現。"},{"en":"A painting may offer a uniquely expressive portrayal of workers through posture, colour and facial expression.","zh":"一幅畫可能透過姿勢、顏色和表情，對工人作出獨特而富表現力的描寫。"},{"en":"If a writer portrays people expressively, readers can feel their voices and emotions.","zh":"如果作家富表現力地描寫人物，讀者就能感受到他們的聲音和情緒。"},{"en":"The phrase praises both originality and vividness.","zh":"這個片語同時讚賞原創性和生動性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"portrayal of Scottish people","meaning":"對蘇格蘭人的描寫","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s work offers a vivid portrayal of Scottish people.","zh":"Stevenson 的作品對蘇格蘭人作出生動描寫。"},{"en":"Portrayal of Scottish people means the way Scottish people are represented in writing or art.","zh":"portrayal of Scottish people 指蘇格蘭人在寫作或藝術中被呈現的方式。"},{"en":"A novel’s portrayal of ordinary workers can shape how readers understand a community.","zh":"小說對普通工人的描寫可以塑造讀者如何理解一個社群。"},{"en":"If a portrayal is vivid, characters feel like real people rather than symbols.","zh":"如果描寫生動，人物就像真實的人，而不只是象徵。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on representation of a specific group.","zh":"這個片語集中於對特定群體的呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"romance","meaning":"浪漫元素；傳奇色彩","examples":[{"en":"Romance was one of the literary qualities listed in the notes.","zh":"浪漫元素是筆記列出的文學特質之一。"},{"en":"Romance can mean a literary quality involving adventure, emotion, imagination or idealised experience.","zh":"romance 可指涉及冒險、情感、想像或理想化經驗的文學特質。"},{"en":"A story may contain romance when it presents distant lands, heroic choices and strong feeling.","zh":"當故事呈現遠方土地、英雄選擇和強烈感受，就可能包含浪漫元素。"},{"en":"If a work has romance, readers may enjoy its sense of wonder and possibility.","zh":"如果作品有浪漫元素，讀者可能享受其驚奇感和可能性。"},{"en":"The word here refers to literary colour, not only love stories.","zh":"這個詞在此指文學色彩，而不只是愛情故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"colourful language","meaning":"生動多彩的語言","examples":[{"en":"Colourful language can make storytelling more vivid.","zh":"生動多彩的語言可以令敍事更鮮明。"},{"en":"Colourful language means expressive, lively and memorable wording.","zh":"colourful language 指富表現力、生動而令人難忘的用字。"},{"en":"A travel writer uses colourful language when describing markets full of noise, smell and movement.","zh":"旅遊作家描寫充滿聲音、氣味和動態的市場時，就是使用生動多彩的語言。"},{"en":"If language is colourful, readers can picture scenes more clearly.","zh":"如果語言生動多彩，讀者就能更清楚想像場景。"},{"en":"The phrase praises writing that feels vivid rather than plain.","zh":"這個片語讚賞感覺鮮活而不平淡的寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"critical acclaim","meaning":"評論界讚譽","examples":[{"en":"A writer may receive critical acclaim for literary skill.","zh":"作家可能因文學技巧獲得評論界讚譽。"},{"en":"Critical acclaim means strong praise from critics or reviewers.","zh":"critical acclaim 指來自評論家或評論者的高度讚賞。"},{"en":"A film may receive critical acclaim even if it is not a huge commercial success.","zh":"電影即使不是巨大商業成功，也可能獲得評論界讚譽。"},{"en":"If a book receives critical acclaim, schools and universities may become more likely to study it.","zh":"如果一本書獲得評論界讚譽，學校和大學可能更願意研究它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to approval from critics, not only public popularity.","zh":"這個片語指評論家的認可，而不只是大眾受歡迎程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"humour","meaning":"幽默","examples":[{"en":"Humour can be an important feature of literary style.","zh":"幽默可以是文學風格的重要特徵。"},{"en":"Humour is the quality that makes something funny, witty or amusing.","zh":"humour 指令某事有趣、機智或令人發笑的特質。"},{"en":"A teacher may use humour to make a difficult grammar point feel less frightening.","zh":"老師可能使用幽默，令困難文法點不那麼可怕。"},{"en":"If a writer uses humour well, serious ideas can become easier to accept.","zh":"如果作家善用幽默，嚴肅思想可以變得較容易接受。"},{"en":"The word refers to comic effect or the ability to make readers smile.","zh":"這個詞指喜劇效果或令讀者微笑的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"storytelling","meaning":"敍事技巧","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson is often praised for his storytelling.","zh":"Stevenson 常因其敍事技巧而受到讚賞。"},{"en":"Storytelling is the skill of shaping events, characters and details into a clear and engaging narrative.","zh":"storytelling 指把事件、人物和細節塑造成清楚而吸引人的敍事的技巧。"},{"en":"A good teacher uses storytelling to make history feel connected to real people.","zh":"好老師使用敍事技巧，令歷史感覺與真實人物相連。"},{"en":"Strong storytelling keeps readers turning pages because they want to know what happens next.","zh":"強大的敍事技巧令讀者一直翻頁，因為他們想知道接下來發生甚麼。"},{"en":"The word refers to the craft of telling stories well.","zh":"這個詞指把故事講好的工藝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"human nature","meaning":"人性","examples":[{"en":"Stevenson’s works are admired for their depiction of human nature.","zh":"Stevenson 的作品因其對人性的描寫而受到欣賞。"},{"en":"Human nature means the common feelings, desires, weaknesses and behaviours that people tend to share.","zh":"human nature 指人類常共有的感受、欲望、弱點和行為。"},{"en":"A story about jealousy between friends explores human nature because many people recognise that feeling.","zh":"關於朋友之間嫉妒的故事探索人性，因為許多人認得那種感受。"},{"en":"If literature shows human nature honestly, readers may understand themselves better.","zh":"如果文學誠實呈現人性，讀者可能更了解自己。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what people are like deep down.","zh":"這個片語指人內在深處的樣子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 50 - Robert Louis Stevenson.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 51":[{"front":"be settled into","meaning":"被安置到……","examples":[{"en":"Daniel Haworth is settled into a high chair.","zh":"Daniel Haworth 被安置到嬰兒高腳椅上。"},{"en":"To be settled into a place means to be placed there comfortably and safely.","zh":"be settled into 某處，指被舒服而安全地安置在那裏。"},{"en":"A baby may be settled into a cot before bedtime.","zh":"嬰兒可能在睡前被安置到嬰兒床上。"},{"en":"If a child is not settled into a seat properly, he may feel unsafe or restless.","zh":"如果孩子沒有被妥善安置到座位上，他可能感到不安全或坐立不安。"},{"en":"The phrase often describes someone being gently placed in a fixed position.","zh":"這個短語常描述某人被溫和地放到固定位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a high chair","meaning":"嬰兒高腳椅","examples":[{"en":"The baby is placed in a high chair for the experiment.","zh":"嬰兒為了實驗被放在嬰兒高腳椅上。"},{"en":"A high chair is a tall chair used for babies or toddlers during feeding or activities.","zh":"high chair 是嬰兒或幼兒進食或活動時使用的高身椅子。"},{"en":"Parents may put a baby in a high chair so the child can sit safely at the table.","zh":"家長可能把嬰兒放在嬰兒高腳椅上，讓孩子安全地坐在桌邊。"},{"en":"A high chair keeps the baby raised and supported, so adults can feed or observe the child more easily.","zh":"嬰兒高腳椅把嬰兒抬高並支撐住，讓成人更容易餵食或觀察孩子。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a special chair designed for very young children.","zh":"這個短語指為很年幼孩子設計的特別椅子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be wheeled behind","meaning":"被推到……後面","examples":[{"en":"Daniel is wheeled behind a black screen.","zh":"Daniel 被推到黑色屏幕後面。"},{"en":"To be wheeled behind something means to be moved on wheels to a position behind it.","zh":"be wheeled behind 某物，指被用輪子推到它後方的位置。"},{"en":"A patient may be wheeled behind a curtain before a medical check.","zh":"病人可能在檢查前被推到簾子後面。"},{"en":"Being wheeled behind a screen can hide someone from view and change what they can see.","zh":"被推到屏幕後面可以使某人從視線中消失，並改變他能看見的東西。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement by a chair, trolley, or bed with wheels.","zh":"這個短語描述透過有輪子的椅子、手推車或床移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a sudden look of worry","meaning":"突然露出擔憂的神情","examples":[{"en":"A sudden look of worry appears on Daniel’s face.","zh":"Daniel 臉上突然露出擔憂的神情。"},{"en":"A sudden look of worry is a quick facial expression showing fear, concern, or uncertainty.","zh":"sudden look of worry 是快速出現、顯示害怕、擔心或不確定的面部表情。"},{"en":"A child may show a sudden look of worry when he cannot find his parent in a shop.","zh":"孩子在商店找不到父母時，可能突然露出擔憂的神情。"},{"en":"This expression can appear when someone senses danger or feels unexpectedly alone.","zh":"當某人察覺危險或突然感到孤單，這種表情可能出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes worry that appears quickly and visibly.","zh":"這個短語描述快速而明顯出現的擔憂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"furrow someone’s brow","meaning":"使某人皺起眉頭","examples":[{"en":"A look of worry furrows Daniel’s brow.","zh":"擔憂的神情使 Daniel 皺起眉頭。"},{"en":"To furrow someone’s brow means to make lines appear on the forehead because of worry, anger, or deep thought.","zh":"furrow someone’s brow 指因擔心、憤怒或深思而使某人額頭出現皺紋。"},{"en":"A difficult maths question may furrow a student’s brow during a test.","zh":"一道困難數學題可能在測驗中使學生皺起眉頭。"},{"en":"People often furrow their brow when they are confused or trying hard to understand something.","zh":"人們困惑或努力理解某事時，常會皺起眉頭。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a visible sign of mental effort or concern.","zh":"這個短語描述思考吃力或擔心的可見跡象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"9-month-old","meaning":"九個月大的","examples":[{"en":"The 9-month-old baby takes part in the experiment.","zh":"這名九個月大的嬰兒參與實驗。"},{"en":"A 9-month-old baby is a baby who is nine months old.","zh":"9-month-old baby 是九個月大的嬰兒。"},{"en":"A 9-month-old may sit with support, reach for toys, and recognise familiar faces.","zh":"九個月大的嬰兒可能能在支撐下坐着、伸手拿玩具，並認出熟悉面孔。"},{"en":"Because a 9-month-old cannot explain feelings in words, researchers watch behaviour carefully.","zh":"因為九個月大的嬰兒不能用文字解釋感受，研究人員會仔細觀察行為。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the baby’s age precisely.","zh":"這個短語準確指出嬰兒的年齡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dart left and right","meaning":"左右快速轉動","examples":[{"en":"His eyes dart left and right in search of his mother.","zh":"他的眼睛左右快速轉動，尋找母親。"},{"en":"To dart left and right means to move quickly from one side to another.","zh":"dart left and right 指從一邊快速移到另一邊。"},{"en":"A nervous student’s eyes may dart left and right before a speaking exam.","zh":"緊張學生在口試前，眼睛可能左右快速轉動。"},{"en":"Eyes often dart left and right when someone is searching, worried, or alert.","zh":"當某人正在尋找、擔心或保持警覺，眼睛常會左右快速轉動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fast, restless movement.","zh":"這個短語描述快速而不安定的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in search of","meaning":"尋找……","examples":[{"en":"Daniel looks around in search of his mother’s face.","zh":"Daniel 四處張望，尋找母親的臉。"},{"en":"In search of means looking for someone or something.","zh":"in search of 指尋找某人或某物。"},{"en":"A student may walk around the library in search of a quiet seat.","zh":"學生可能在圖書館四處走，尋找安靜座位。"},{"en":"People move their eyes, ask questions, or check places when they are in search of something.","zh":"當人們尋找某物時，會移動視線、提問或查看不同地方。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an active attempt to find what is missing.","zh":"這個短語描述主動嘗試找回缺失的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"familiar reassurance","meaning":"熟悉的安慰","examples":[{"en":"The baby looks for the familiar reassurance of his mother’s face.","zh":"嬰兒尋找母親臉上熟悉的安慰。"},{"en":"Familiar reassurance is comfort that comes from someone or something known and trusted.","zh":"familiar reassurance 是來自熟悉而可信的人或事物的安慰。"},{"en":"A child may feel familiar reassurance when a parent waits outside the classroom door.","zh":"當父母在課室門外等候，孩子可能感到熟悉的安慰。"},{"en":"Familiar reassurance can calm fear because it reminds a person that they are safe.","zh":"熟悉的安慰可以平息恐懼，因為它提醒人自己是安全的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes comfort created by recognition and trust.","zh":"這個短語描述由認出和信任所帶來的安慰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"soothing noises","meaning":"安撫性的聲音","examples":[{"en":"His mother calls his name and makes soothing noises.","zh":"他的母親叫他的名字，並發出安撫性的聲音。"},{"en":"Soothing noises are gentle sounds that help someone feel calm or safe.","zh":"soothing noises 是幫助某人感到平靜或安全的柔和聲音。"},{"en":"A parent may make soothing noises to calm a baby who wakes up crying.","zh":"嬰兒哭醒時，父母可能發出安撫性的聲音來安慰他。"},{"en":"Soft sounds can reduce distress because they signal care and closeness.","zh":"柔和聲音可以減少痛苦，因為它們傳遞關心和親近。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sounds used to comfort rather than inform.","zh":"這個短語描述用來安慰而不是傳遞資訊的聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sense something unusual","meaning":"察覺有異樣","examples":[{"en":"Daniel senses that something unusual is happening.","zh":"Daniel 察覺有異樣正在發生。"},{"en":"To sense something unusual means to notice that a situation feels different or wrong, even without full understanding.","zh":"sense something unusual 指注意到情況感覺不同或不對勁，即使未完全理解。"},{"en":"A student may sense something unusual when a normally cheerful teacher becomes silent.","zh":"當平時開朗的老師變得沉默，學生可能察覺有異樣。"},{"en":"People can become anxious when they sense something unusual but cannot explain it.","zh":"當人察覺有異樣但不能解釋時，可能會變得焦慮。"},{"en":"The phrase describes early awareness that something is not normal.","zh":"這個短語描述對不正常情況的早期察覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"suck one’s fingers for comfort","meaning":"吮手指以求安慰","examples":[{"en":"He sucks his fingers for comfort.","zh":"他吮手指以求安慰。"},{"en":"To suck one’s fingers for comfort means to put fingers in the mouth to calm oneself.","zh":"suck one’s fingers for comfort 指把手指放入口中來安撫自己。"},{"en":"A tired toddler may suck her fingers for comfort while waiting for her mother.","zh":"疲倦幼兒等母親時，可能吮手指以求安慰。"},{"en":"Babies often use simple body actions to soothe themselves when adults are not immediately available.","zh":"當成人不在身邊時，嬰兒常用簡單身體動作安撫自己。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a self-comforting behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述一種自我安慰行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"find no solace","meaning":"得不到慰藉","examples":[{"en":"Finding no solace, Daniel begins to cry.","zh":"得不到慰藉，Daniel 開始哭。"},{"en":"To find no solace means to receive no comfort or relief from distress.","zh":"find no solace 指沒有從痛苦中得到安慰或紓緩。"},{"en":"A student may find no solace in kind words if she has just failed an important exam.","zh":"如果學生剛在重要考試中失敗，即使有人說好話，她也可能得不到慰藉。"},{"en":"When comfort does not work, sadness or fear may become stronger.","zh":"當安慰不起作用，悲傷或恐懼可能變得更強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a failure to feel better.","zh":"這個短語描述未能感到好轉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"someone’s mouth crumples","meaning":"某人的嘴扭曲起來","examples":[{"en":"His mouth crumples before he starts crying.","zh":"他開始哭之前，嘴扭曲起來。"},{"en":"Someone’s mouth crumples when their lips twist or collapse as they are about to cry.","zh":"someone’s mouth crumples 指某人的嘴唇在快要哭時扭曲或垮下來。"},{"en":"A child’s mouth may crumple when he is trying not to cry after losing a toy.","zh":"孩子失去玩具後努力不哭時，嘴可能扭曲起來。"},{"en":"This expression often appears before tears because emotion is becoming too strong to hide.","zh":"這種表情常在眼淚前出現，因為情緒強烈得難以隱藏。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a visible pre-crying facial expression.","zh":"這個短語描述哭之前可見的面部表情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"someone’s body stiffens","meaning":"某人的身體繃緊","examples":[{"en":"His body stiffens when he becomes distressed.","zh":"他感到痛苦時，身體繃緊。"},{"en":"Someone’s body stiffens when the body becomes tight and less relaxed because of fear, pain, or stress.","zh":"someone’s body stiffens 指身體因害怕、疼痛或壓力而變得緊繃、不放鬆。"},{"en":"A child’s body may stiffen when a doctor approaches with an injection.","zh":"當醫生拿着針走近時，孩子的身體可能繃緊。"},{"en":"Stiffening can show that a person is tense before they speak or cry.","zh":"身體繃緊可以顯示人在說話或哭之前已很緊張。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a physical reaction to emotional pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述對情緒壓力的身體反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"let rip","meaning":"突然發出","examples":[{"en":"The baby lets rip a loud shriek of distress.","zh":"嬰兒突然發出一聲痛苦的尖叫。"},{"en":"To let rip means to suddenly release a loud sound or strong reaction.","zh":"let rip 指突然釋放出巨大聲音或強烈反應。"},{"en":"A child may let rip a scream when a balloon bursts beside him.","zh":"當氣球在孩子身旁爆開，他可能突然發出尖叫。"},{"en":"People let rip when they can no longer hold in fear, anger, or excitement.","zh":"當人無法再忍住恐懼、憤怒或興奮時，就會突然爆發。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and describes an uncontrolled outburst.","zh":"這個短語較口語，描述失控的爆發。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an almighty shriek of distress","meaning":"一聲極大的痛苦尖叫","examples":[{"en":"Daniel lets rip an almighty shriek of distress.","zh":"Daniel 突然發出一聲極大的痛苦尖叫。"},{"en":"An almighty shriek of distress is an extremely loud cry showing fear, pain, or panic.","zh":"almighty shriek of distress 是顯示害怕、痛楚或驚慌的極大尖叫。"},{"en":"A toddler may give an almighty shriek of distress when she loses sight of her father in a crowd.","zh":"幼兒在人群中看不見父親時，可能發出一聲極大的痛苦尖叫。"},{"en":"Such a cry usually makes adults respond quickly because it signals serious upset.","zh":"這種哭叫通常令成人迅速回應，因為它表示嚴重不安。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a powerful sound of emotional suffering.","zh":"這個短語描述情緒痛苦所產生的強烈聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a common response","meaning":"常見反應","examples":[{"en":"Such distress is a common response when babies are left alone.","zh":"當嬰兒被獨自留下，這種痛苦是常見反應。"},{"en":"A common response is a reaction that many people or animals show in a similar situation.","zh":"common response 是許多人或動物在相似情況中表現出的反應。"},{"en":"Feeling nervous before an exam is a common response among students.","zh":"考試前感到緊張是學生常見反應。"},{"en":"If many babies cry when separated from a parent, crying can be seen as a common response.","zh":"如果許多嬰兒與父母分開時都會哭，哭就可視為常見反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a usual or expected reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述通常或預期中的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be left alone","meaning":"被獨自留下","examples":[{"en":"Babies often become upset when they are left alone.","zh":"嬰兒被獨自留下時常會變得不安。"},{"en":"To be left alone means to be without other people nearby or without direct attention.","zh":"be left alone 指身邊沒有其他人，或沒有直接照顧。"},{"en":"A young child may cry if she is left alone in a dark room.","zh":"幼童如果被獨自留在黑房中，可能會哭。"},{"en":"Being left alone can create fear if the person depends on others for safety or comfort.","zh":"如果一個人依賴他人提供安全或安慰，被獨自留下可能造成恐懼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical or emotional separation from others.","zh":"這個短語描述與他人在身體或情感上分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pick someone up","meaning":"抱起某人","examples":[{"en":"His mother picks him up and reassures him.","zh":"他的母親抱起他並安撫他。"},{"en":"To pick someone up means to lift them into your arms or raise them from a lower position.","zh":"pick someone up 指把某人抱入懷中，或從較低位置扶起。"},{"en":"A parent may pick a crying child up after the child falls down.","zh":"孩子跌倒後，父母可能抱起哭着的孩子。"},{"en":"Picking a baby up can calm the baby because it gives warmth, contact, and safety.","zh":"抱起嬰兒可以令他平靜，因為這提供溫暖、接觸和安全感。"},{"en":"The phrase often describes lifting a child for comfort or care.","zh":"這個短語常描述為了安慰或照顧而抱起孩子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reassure someone","meaning":"安撫某人；使某人安心","examples":[{"en":"His mother reassures Daniel after he cries.","zh":"Daniel 哭後，他的母親安撫他。"},{"en":"To reassure someone means to make them feel less worried or afraid.","zh":"reassure someone 指使某人較少擔心或害怕。"},{"en":"A teacher may reassure a nervous student before a speech.","zh":"老師可能在演講前安撫緊張學生。"},{"en":"Reassurance works best when words, tone, and actions all show that the person is safe.","zh":"當言語、語氣和行動都顯示對方安全時，安撫最有效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving comfort and confidence to someone.","zh":"這個短語描述給予某人安慰和信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"chortling and alert","meaning":"咯咯笑而且精神集中的","examples":[{"en":"A chortling and alert Daniel returns to the booth.","zh":"咯咯笑而且精神集中的 Daniel 回到小隔間。"},{"en":"Chortling and alert means laughing softly or happily while also awake, attentive, and responsive.","zh":"chortling and alert 指輕聲或開心地笑，同時清醒、專注並有反應。"},{"en":"A baby may become chortling and alert after a parent plays peekaboo.","zh":"父母玩躲貓貓後，嬰兒可能變得咯咯笑而且精神集中。"},{"en":"Comfort can quickly change a baby from crying to alert and playful.","zh":"安慰可以迅速令嬰兒由哭泣轉為清醒和愛玩。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a child who is cheerful and mentally awake.","zh":"這個短語描述開心而精神清醒的孩子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"darkened booth","meaning":"昏暗的小隔間","examples":[{"en":"Daniel returns to the darkened booth behind the screen.","zh":"Daniel 回到屏幕後方昏暗的小隔間。"},{"en":"A darkened booth is a small enclosed space made dim so people can focus on a screen or task.","zh":"darkened booth 是被調暗的小型封閉空間，讓人專注於屏幕或任務。"},{"en":"In an eye test, a patient may sit in a darkened booth to look at bright images clearly.","zh":"在眼睛檢查中，病人可能坐在昏暗的小隔間中清楚觀看明亮影像。"},{"en":"Darkness can reduce distractions and make visual responses easier to measure.","zh":"昏暗環境可以減少干擾，並令視覺反應更容易量度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small, low-light testing or viewing area.","zh":"這個短語描述小型、低光度的測試或觀看區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"submit oneself to","meaning":"接受；順從","examples":[{"en":"Daniel submits himself to BabyLab after being reassured.","zh":"Daniel 被安撫後接受 BabyLab 的安排。"},{"en":"To submit oneself to something means to accept or go through it, often because someone else has arranged it.","zh":"submit oneself to 某事，指接受或經歷某事，通常因別人已安排好。"},{"en":"A patient may submit herself to a medical scan after the doctor explains the procedure.","zh":"醫生解釋程序後，病人可能接受醫學掃描。"},{"en":"People are more willing to submit themselves to a process when they feel safe and informed.","zh":"當人感到安全並了解情況，會較願意接受某過程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes accepting an experience, test, or authority.","zh":"這個短語描述接受一種經歷、測試或權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a unit set up","meaning":"設立的單位","examples":[{"en":"BabyLab is a unit set up at the University of Manchester.","zh":"BabyLab 是曼徹斯特大學設立的單位。"},{"en":"A unit set up somewhere is an organised group or department created for a purpose.","zh":"unit set up 某處，是為某目的而成立的有組織小組或部門。"},{"en":"A school may have a counselling unit set up to support students under stress.","zh":"學校可能設立輔導單位，支援受壓學生。"},{"en":"Units are set up when an organisation needs focused work on a specific problem.","zh":"當組織需要集中處理特定問題，就會設立單位。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an officially created team or centre.","zh":"這個短語描述正式成立的團隊或中心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"investigate how babies think","meaning":"研究嬰兒如何思考","examples":[{"en":"BabyLab was set up to investigate how babies think.","zh":"BabyLab 的設立是為了研究嬰兒如何思考。"},{"en":"To investigate how babies think means to study how infants notice, learn, remember, and respond to the world.","zh":"investigate how babies think 指研究嬰兒如何注意、學習、記憶和回應世界。"},{"en":"Researchers may investigate how babies think by watching where they look during simple tasks.","zh":"研究人員可能透過觀察嬰兒在簡單任務中看向哪裏，研究嬰兒如何思考。"},{"en":"Because babies cannot speak, scientists study thinking through behaviour and attention.","zh":"因為嬰兒不能說話，科學家透過行為和注意力研究思考。"},{"en":"The phrase describes scientific study of infant cognition.","zh":"這個短語描述對嬰兒認知的科學研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"piece life together","meaning":"逐步理解生活","examples":[{"en":"Researchers watch infants piece life together.","zh":"研究人員觀察嬰兒逐步理解生活。"},{"en":"To piece life together means to gradually understand the world by connecting small experiences.","zh":"piece life together 指透過連接細小經驗，逐漸理解世界。"},{"en":"A toddler pieces life together when she learns that shoes mean going outside.","zh":"當幼兒學會鞋子代表要外出，她就是在逐步理解生活。"},{"en":"Small repeated events help children build expectations about people, objects, and routines.","zh":"細小而重複的事件幫助孩子建立對人、物件和日常程序的預期。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow learning through many little clues.","zh":"這個短語描述透過許多小線索慢慢學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"infants","meaning":"嬰兒","examples":[{"en":"BabyLab has tested only 100 infants so far.","zh":"BabyLab 到目前為止只測試了一百名嬰兒。"},{"en":"Infants are very young babies, especially before they can speak or walk well.","zh":"infants 是非常年幼的嬰兒，尤其指尚未能好好說話或走路的孩子。"},{"en":"Hospitals give special care to infants because they cannot explain pain or discomfort.","zh":"醫院會特別照顧嬰兒，因為他們不能解釋疼痛或不適。"},{"en":"Researchers use gentle methods with infants because they are small and easily upset.","zh":"研究人員對嬰兒使用溫和方法，因為他們很小且容易不安。"},{"en":"The word refers to babies in the earliest stage of life.","zh":"這個詞指人生最早階段的嬰兒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"senses, emotions and motor skills","meaning":"感官、情緒和動作技能","examples":[{"en":"Researchers study how babies’ senses, emotions and motor skills develop.","zh":"研究人員研究嬰兒的感官、情緒和動作技能如何發展。"},{"en":"Senses, emotions and motor skills are abilities involving seeing, hearing, feeling, reacting emotionally, and moving the body.","zh":"senses, emotions and motor skills 是涉及觀看、聆聽、感受、情緒反應和身體移動的能力。"},{"en":"A baby uses senses, emotions and motor skills when she sees a toy, smiles, and reaches for it.","zh":"嬰兒看見玩具、微笑並伸手去拿時，就在使用感官、情緒和動作技能。"},{"en":"These abilities develop together because babies learn through looking, feeling, moving, and responding.","zh":"這些能力一起發展，因為嬰兒透過觀看、感受、移動和回應來學習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes key areas of early child development.","zh":"這個短語描述早期兒童發展的關鍵範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"take shape","meaning":"形成；發展成形","examples":[{"en":"Babies’ senses, emotions and motor skills gradually take shape.","zh":"嬰兒的感官、情緒和動作技能逐漸形成。"},{"en":"To take shape means to develop into a clearer form over time.","zh":"take shape 指隨時間發展成更清晰的形態。"},{"en":"A student’s essay takes shape after she writes an outline and organises her ideas.","zh":"學生寫出大綱並組織想法後，文章逐漸成形。"},{"en":"Skills take shape through repeated practice, feedback, and small improvements.","zh":"技能透過反覆練習、回饋和小改進而逐漸形成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something becoming more formed and understandable.","zh":"這個短語描述某事變得更成形、更可理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a source of mystery","meaning":"神秘之源","examples":[{"en":"Infant development is a source of mystery for researchers.","zh":"嬰兒發展對研究人員來說是神秘之源。"},{"en":"A source of mystery is something that raises questions and is not yet fully understood.","zh":"source of mystery 是引起問題且尚未完全被理解的事物。"},{"en":"A child’s sudden fear of school may be a source of mystery until adults ask what happened.","zh":"孩子突然害怕上學，在成人詢問發生甚麼之前，可能是神秘之源。"},{"en":"Something becomes mysterious when people can observe it but cannot easily explain it.","zh":"當人們能觀察某事但不容易解釋，它就變得神秘。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that makes people curious and uncertain.","zh":"這個短語描述令人好奇而不確定的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"endless fascination","meaning":"無窮的吸引力","examples":[{"en":"Watching infants learn is a source of endless fascination.","zh":"觀察嬰兒學習是一種無窮的吸引力來源。"},{"en":"Endless fascination means deep interest that seems to continue without becoming boring.","zh":"endless fascination 指似乎不會變得沉悶的深厚興趣。"},{"en":"For many parents, watching a baby discover mirrors is endless fascination.","zh":"對許多父母而言，看着嬰兒發現鏡子有無窮的吸引力。"},{"en":"A subject creates endless fascination when every small detail raises a new question.","zh":"當一個主題的每個小細節都引出新問題，它就會產生無窮吸引力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lasting curiosity and interest.","zh":"這個短語描述持久的好奇和興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at least to","meaning":"至少對……來說","examples":[{"en":"Baby development is fascinating, at least to parents and psychologists.","zh":"嬰兒發展很迷人，至少對父母和心理學家來說如此。"},{"en":"At least to a group means true for that group, even if not everyone feels the same.","zh":"at least to 某群體，指至少對該群體而言是真的，即使不是每個人都這樣覺得。"},{"en":"Grammar exercises may seem interesting, at least to language teachers.","zh":"文法練習可能很有趣，至少對語言老師來說。"},{"en":"The phrase limits a statement by naming who it applies to.","zh":"這個短語透過指出適用對象來限制陳述。"},{"en":"It helps avoid claiming that everyone shares the same view.","zh":"它有助避免聲稱所有人都有同一看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"developmental psychologists","meaning":"發展心理學家","examples":[{"en":"Developmental psychologists study how children grow and learn.","zh":"發展心理學家研究孩子如何成長和學習。"},{"en":"Developmental psychologists are experts who study changes in thinking, emotion, behaviour, and ability across childhood and life.","zh":"developmental psychologists 是研究兒童及人生中思考、情緒、行為和能力變化的專家。"},{"en":"A developmental psychologist may observe how toddlers learn to share toys.","zh":"發展心理學家可能觀察幼兒如何學會分享玩具。"},{"en":"Their research helps parents and teachers understand what children can do at different ages.","zh":"他們的研究幫助家長和老師理解孩子在不同年齡能做到甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to psychologists who focus on human development.","zh":"這個短語指專注於人類發展的心理學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"decode signals of distress","meaning":"解讀痛苦信號","examples":[{"en":"Parents often try to decode their babies’ signals of distress.","zh":"父母常嘗試解讀嬰兒的痛苦信號。"},{"en":"To decode signals of distress means to interpret signs that someone is upset, afraid, or uncomfortable.","zh":"decode signals of distress 指詮釋顯示某人不安、害怕或不舒服的跡象。"},{"en":"A parent may decode a baby’s crying, stiff body, and red face as signs of hunger or tiredness.","zh":"父母可能把嬰兒哭泣、身體繃緊和臉紅解讀為飢餓或疲倦的信號。"},{"en":"Understanding these signals helps adults respond before the child becomes more upset.","zh":"理解這些信號幫助成人在孩子更不安前作出回應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reading behaviour as a message of discomfort.","zh":"這個短語描述把行為讀成不適訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"read messages into","meaning":"從……解讀出信息","examples":[{"en":"Parents may read many messages into a baby’s first smile.","zh":"父母可能從嬰兒第一次微笑中解讀出許多信息。"},{"en":"To read messages into something means to interpret it as having meaning, sometimes more meaning than it really has.","zh":"read messages into 某事，指把它解讀為有意義，有時甚至超出它真正的意思。"},{"en":"A teacher may read confidence into a student’s smile, even if the student is actually nervous.","zh":"老師可能從學生微笑中解讀出自信，即使學生其實很緊張。"},{"en":"People often read messages into small actions when they badly want to understand another person.","zh":"當人很想理解另一個人時，常會從小動作解讀出信息。"},{"en":"The phrase can suggest interpretation that may or may not be correct.","zh":"這個短語可暗示詮釋未必正確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"what is going on behind","meaning":"……背後正在發生甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Researchers ask what is going on behind babies’ innocent eyes.","zh":"研究人員問嬰兒天真眼睛背後正在發生甚麼。"},{"en":"What is going on behind something asks what hidden thoughts, feelings, or processes are happening underneath the surface.","zh":"what is going on behind 某事，是問表面之下有甚麼隱藏思想、感受或過程正在發生。"},{"en":"A teacher may wonder what is going on behind a quiet student’s silence.","zh":"老師可能想知道安靜學生的沉默背後正在發生甚麼。"},{"en":"People ask this when outward behaviour does not fully reveal inner experience.","zh":"當外在行為不能完全顯示內在經驗，人們會這樣問。"},{"en":"The phrase looks beyond appearance to hidden mental activity.","zh":"這個短語越過外表，查看隱藏的心理活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"wide, innocent eyes","meaning":"睜大的天真眼睛","examples":[{"en":"People wonder what babies know behind their wide, innocent eyes.","zh":"人們想知道嬰兒睜大的天真眼睛背後知道甚麼。"},{"en":"Wide, innocent eyes are large-looking eyes that suggest openness, youth, and lack of experience.","zh":"wide, innocent eyes 是看起來很大的眼睛，暗示開放、年幼和缺乏經驗。"},{"en":"A toddler may look at a strange dog with wide, innocent eyes.","zh":"幼兒可能用睜大的天真眼睛看着陌生的狗。"},{"en":"Such eyes can make adults feel protective because the child seems pure and vulnerable.","zh":"這種眼神可以令成人想保護孩子，因為孩子看起來純真而脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both appearance and the feeling it creates.","zh":"這個短語同時描述外表和它造成的感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"understanding of and response to","meaning":"對……的理解和反應","examples":[{"en":"Researchers study babies’ understanding of and response to the world.","zh":"研究人員研究嬰兒對世界的理解和反應。"},{"en":"Understanding of and response to something means both what someone knows about it and how they react to it.","zh":"understanding of and response to 某事，指某人對它知道甚麼，以及如何作出反應。"},{"en":"A teacher can assess students’ understanding of and response to a story by asking questions and watching discussion.","zh":"老師可以透過提問和觀察討論，評估學生對故事的理解和反應。"},{"en":"A person may understand a rule but still respond to it emotionally.","zh":"一個人可能理解規則，但仍會對它有情緒反應。"},{"en":"The phrase combines knowledge with reaction.","zh":"這個短語把知識與反應結合起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"come preloaded at birth","meaning":"出生時已預先具備","examples":[{"en":"Some abilities may come preloaded at birth.","zh":"有些能力可能出生時已預先具備。"},{"en":"To come preloaded at birth means to be present in a baby from the moment they are born.","zh":"come preloaded at birth 指從嬰兒出生一刻起已存在。"},{"en":"Some scientists think a preference for looking at faces may come preloaded at birth.","zh":"有些科學家認為偏好看人臉可能出生時已預先具備。"},{"en":"If an ability is preloaded, babies do not need long experience before showing it.","zh":"如果一項能力是預先具備的，嬰兒不需要長期經驗便會表現出來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an ability treated as built in from birth.","zh":"這個短語描述被視為出生時已內置的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be built from scratch","meaning":"從零建立","examples":[{"en":"Some knowledge may be built from scratch by experience.","zh":"有些知識可能透過經驗從零建立。"},{"en":"To be built from scratch means to be developed from nothing, without an existing base.","zh":"be built from scratch 指在沒有既有基礎下從無到有地發展。"},{"en":"A student may build essay skills from scratch if she has never written in English before.","zh":"如果學生以前從未用英語寫作，她可能要從零建立文章技巧。"},{"en":"Building knowledge from scratch takes time because each new idea must be learned through experience.","zh":"從零建立知識需要時間，因為每個新概念都必須透過經驗學習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes starting at zero and gradually creating something.","zh":"這個短語描述從零開始並逐步創造某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"by experience","meaning":"透過經驗","examples":[{"en":"Babies may build knowledge from scratch by experience.","zh":"嬰兒可能透過經驗從零建立知識。"},{"en":"By experience means through what someone sees, does, feels, or goes through directly.","zh":"by experience 指透過某人直接看見、做過、感受或經歷的事情。"},{"en":"A child learns that a cup can spill by experience after knocking one over.","zh":"孩子打翻杯子後，透過經驗學會杯子會倒瀉。"},{"en":"Experience teaches lessons more strongly when a person connects action with result.","zh":"當人把行動與結果連起來，經驗教訓會更深刻。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning through real events rather than explanation only.","zh":"這個短語描述透過真實事件，而不只是解釋來學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be explored at","meaning":"在……被探究","examples":[{"en":"Questions about infant knowledge are being explored at BabyLab.","zh":"關於嬰兒知識的問題正在 BabyLab 被探究。"},{"en":"To be explored at a place means to be studied, investigated, or examined there.","zh":"be explored at 某處，指在那裏被研究、調查或檢視。"},{"en":"Questions about sleep and memory are explored at many university laboratories.","zh":"關於睡眠與記憶的問題在許多大學實驗室被探究。"},{"en":"A research centre explores a question by designing tests and collecting evidence.","zh":"研究中心透過設計測試和收集證據來探究問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where scientific investigation takes place.","zh":"這個短語描述科學調查在哪裏進行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the facility","meaning":"設施；研究中心","examples":[{"en":"The facility has tested only 100 infants.","zh":"該研究中心只測試了一百名嬰兒。"},{"en":"The facility means the building, centre, or place equipped for a particular activity.","zh":"facility 指配備某特定活動所需設備的建築、中心或地方。"},{"en":"A sports facility may include a gym, changing rooms, and training equipment.","zh":"體育設施可能包括健身室、更衣室和訓練器材。"},{"en":"A research facility needs special tools so scientists can collect reliable data.","zh":"研究設施需要特別工具，讓科學家收集可靠數據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a practical place designed for work, study, or service.","zh":"這個短語指為工作、研究或服務而設計的實用地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"challenge current thinking","meaning":"挑戰現有看法","examples":[{"en":"BabyLab is challenging current thinking about what babies know.","zh":"BabyLab 正在挑戰關於嬰兒知道甚麼的現有看法。"},{"en":"To challenge current thinking means to question accepted ideas and test whether they are true.","zh":"challenge current thinking 指質疑已接受的想法，並測試它們是否真實。"},{"en":"New exam results may challenge current thinking about how students learn vocabulary.","zh":"新考試結果可能挑戰關於學生如何學詞彙的現有看法。"},{"en":"Research challenges thinking when it shows evidence that old explanations may be wrong.","zh":"當研究顯示舊解釋可能錯誤，它就會挑戰看法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes questioning accepted views.","zh":"這個短語描述質疑已接受觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"current thinking on","meaning":"關於……的現有看法","examples":[{"en":"The research challenges current thinking on infant knowledge.","zh":"該研究挑戰關於嬰兒知識的現有看法。"},{"en":"Current thinking on a topic means the ideas or beliefs that are widely accepted now.","zh":"current thinking on 某主題，指現在被廣泛接受的想法或信念。"},{"en":"Current thinking on homework is changing as schools pay more attention to wellbeing.","zh":"隨着學校更重視福祉，關於功課的現有看法正在改變。"},{"en":"Current thinking can change when stronger evidence appears.","zh":"當更強證據出現，現有看法可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what experts or society generally believe at present.","zh":"這個短語指專家或社會目前一般相信的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"come to know","meaning":"逐漸認識","examples":[{"en":"Researchers ask how babies come to know the world.","zh":"研究人員問嬰兒如何逐漸認識世界。"},{"en":"To come to know something means to gradually learn or understand it over time.","zh":"come to know 某事，指隨時間逐漸學會或理解它。"},{"en":"A new student comes to know the school by finding classrooms, meeting teachers, and learning routines.","zh":"新學生透過找課室、認識老師和學習日常程序，逐漸認識學校。"},{"en":"People often come to know something through repeated experience rather than one explanation.","zh":"人們常透過重複經驗，而不是一次解釋來逐漸認識某事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual discovery and understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步發現和理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be engrossed in","meaning":"全神貫注於","examples":[{"en":"Daniel is engrossed in watching video clips.","zh":"Daniel 全神貫注於觀看影片片段。"},{"en":"To be engrossed in something means to be so interested that one gives it full attention.","zh":"be engrossed in 某事，指非常感興趣，以致把全部注意力放在上面。"},{"en":"A student may be engrossed in a novel and forget the time.","zh":"學生可能全神貫注於小說，以致忘記時間。"},{"en":"When someone is engrossed, distractions around them become less noticeable.","zh":"當人全神貫注，周圍干擾會變得較不明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep concentration and interest.","zh":"這個短語描述深度專注和興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"video clips","meaning":"影片片段","examples":[{"en":"Daniel watches video clips of a toy train.","zh":"Daniel 觀看玩具火車的影片片段。"},{"en":"Video clips are short pieces of recorded moving images.","zh":"video clips 是短小的錄影片段。"},{"en":"Teachers may use video clips to show a science experiment that is hard to do in class.","zh":"老師可能使用影片片段展示課堂中難以進行的科學實驗。"},{"en":"Short clips help hold attention because they give information quickly.","zh":"短片段能幫助保持注意力，因為它們快速提供資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to brief videos rather than full programmes.","zh":"這個短語指短影片，而不是完整節目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"circular track","meaning":"圓形軌道","examples":[{"en":"The red toy train moves on a circular track.","zh":"紅色玩具火車在圓形軌道上移動。"},{"en":"A circular track is a round path that returns to its starting point.","zh":"circular track 是會回到起點的圓形路徑。"},{"en":"A toy car may move around a circular track at a children’s play centre.","zh":"玩具車可能在兒童遊樂中心沿圓形軌道行走。"},{"en":"A circular track makes movement predictable because the object keeps coming back around.","zh":"圓形軌道使移動變得可預測，因為物件會不斷繞回來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a round route used by a moving object.","zh":"這個短語描述移動物件使用的圓形路線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"disappear into","meaning":"消失於……之中","examples":[{"en":"The train disappears into a tunnel.","zh":"火車消失於隧道之中。"},{"en":"To disappear into something means to move inside it and no longer be visible.","zh":"disappear into 某物，指移入其中並不再可見。"},{"en":"A child may watch a bus disappear into a tunnel on the way home.","zh":"孩子回家途中可能看着巴士消失於隧道之中。"},{"en":"When an object disappears into a space, people may expect it to come out later.","zh":"當物件消失於某空間中，人們可能預期它之後會出來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement from visible to hidden.","zh":"這個短語描述從可見移向隱藏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"emerge on the other side","meaning":"從另一邊出現","examples":[{"en":"The train emerges on the other side of the tunnel.","zh":"火車從隧道另一邊出現。"},{"en":"To emerge on the other side means to come out from the opposite end after being hidden inside.","zh":"emerge on the other side 指在裏面被隱藏後，從相反一端出來。"},{"en":"A train may enter a mountain tunnel and emerge on the other side into bright sunlight.","zh":"火車可能進入山洞，然後從另一邊出現在明亮陽光中。"},{"en":"This phrase often follows disappear into, showing that the object has passed through.","zh":"這個短語常接在 disappear into 之後，顯示物件已穿過。"},{"en":"It describes reappearing after moving through a hidden space.","zh":"它描述穿過隱藏空間後重新出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hidden device","meaning":"隱藏裝置","examples":[{"en":"A hidden device tracks Daniel’s eyes.","zh":"一個隱藏裝置追蹤 Daniel 的目光。"},{"en":"A hidden device is a piece of equipment that is not easily seen.","zh":"hidden device 是不容易被看見的設備。"},{"en":"A shop may use a hidden device to count how many customers enter.","zh":"商店可能使用隱藏裝置計算有多少顧客進入。"},{"en":"Hidden devices can collect information without distracting the person being observed.","zh":"隱藏裝置可以在不分散被觀察者注意力的情況下收集資料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes equipment placed out of sight.","zh":"這個短語描述被放在視線外的設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"track someone’s eyes","meaning":"追蹤某人的目光","examples":[{"en":"The device tracks Daniel’s eyes as they follow the train.","zh":"裝置追蹤 Daniel 跟隨火車移動的目光。"},{"en":"To track someone’s eyes means to record where and how their eyes move.","zh":"track someone’s eyes 指記錄某人的眼睛看向哪裏和如何移動。"},{"en":"Researchers may track students’ eyes to see which part of a webpage attracts attention first.","zh":"研究人員可能追蹤學生的目光，以了解網頁哪部分最先吸引注意。"},{"en":"Eye tracking helps scientists infer interest, attention, or surprise without asking questions.","zh":"眼動追蹤幫助科學家不用提問也能推斷興趣、注意力或驚訝。"},{"en":"The phrase describes measuring eye movement.","zh":"這個短語描述量度眼睛移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"measure the diameter of","meaning":"測量……的直徑","examples":[{"en":"The device measures the diameter of Daniel’s pupils.","zh":"裝置測量 Daniel 瞳孔的直徑。"},{"en":"To measure the diameter of something means to find the distance across its widest part.","zh":"measure the diameter of 某物，指找出橫跨其最寬部分的距離。"},{"en":"A nurse may measure the diameter of a wound to record whether it is healing.","zh":"護士可能測量傷口的直徑，以記錄它是否正在癒合。"},{"en":"Measuring diameter can show changes in size over time.","zh":"測量直徑可以顯示大小隨時間的變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes taking a precise width measurement.","zh":"這個短語描述精確量度寬度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pupils","meaning":"瞳孔","examples":[{"en":"The device measures Daniel’s pupils 50 times a second.","zh":"裝置每秒五十次測量 Daniel 的瞳孔。"},{"en":"Pupils are the dark openings in the centre of the eyes that change size to control light entering.","zh":"pupils 是眼睛中央的黑色開口，會改變大小以控制進入眼睛的光。"},{"en":"A doctor may shine a small light to check whether a patient’s pupils react normally.","zh":"醫生可能照小燈，檢查病人的瞳孔是否正常反應。"},{"en":"Pupils can widen when someone is interested, frightened, or in dim light.","zh":"當人感興趣、害怕或處於暗光中，瞳孔可能擴大。"},{"en":"The word refers to eye parts, not school students, in this context.","zh":"在這個語境中，這個詞指眼睛部位，而不是學生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"50 times a second","meaning":"每秒五十次","examples":[{"en":"The device measures his pupils 50 times a second.","zh":"裝置每秒五十次測量他的瞳孔。"},{"en":"50 times a second means fifty measurements are taken every single second.","zh":"50 times a second 指每一秒進行五十次測量。"},{"en":"A fast camera may record a moving object many times a second to catch tiny changes.","zh":"高速攝影機可能每秒多次記錄移動物件，以捕捉細微變化。"},{"en":"Frequent measurement gives researchers detailed information about quick reactions.","zh":"頻密測量給研究人員關於快速反應的詳細資料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a very high rate of repeated measurement.","zh":"這個短語描述非常高頻率的反覆測量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get bored","meaning":"感到厭倦","examples":[{"en":"The child gets bored after watching the same train repeatedly.","zh":"孩子反覆看同一列火車後感到厭倦。"},{"en":"To get bored means to lose interest because something feels too familiar or unstimulating.","zh":"get bored 指因某事太熟悉或缺乏刺激而失去興趣。"},{"en":"Students may get bored if every lesson uses the same worksheet format.","zh":"如果每堂課都用同一種工作紙格式，學生可能感到厭倦。"},{"en":"Boredom can reduce attention and make people stop looking or listening carefully.","zh":"厭倦可以降低注意力，令人停止仔細觀看或聆聽。"},{"en":"The phrase describes interest fading over time.","zh":"這個短語描述興趣隨時間減退。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"become habituated","meaning":"變得習慣化","examples":[{"en":"The child becomes habituated to the repeated event.","zh":"孩子對重複事件變得習慣化。"},{"en":"To become habituated means to get used to something after repeated exposure and respond less strongly.","zh":"become habituated 指在反覆接觸後習慣某事，並反應變弱。"},{"en":"A student may become habituated to background noise after studying in the same café every day.","zh":"學生每天在同一間咖啡店溫習後，可能對背景噪音變得習慣化。"},{"en":"When people become habituated, their attention drops because the event no longer feels new.","zh":"當人變得習慣化，注意力會下降，因為事件不再新奇。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the mind becoming used to repeated stimulation.","zh":"這個短語描述心智對重複刺激變得習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as psychologists call the process","meaning":"正如心理學家稱這個過程","examples":[{"en":"The child becomes habituated, as psychologists call the process.","zh":"孩子變得習慣化，正如心理學家稱這個過程。"},{"en":"As psychologists call the process means using the technical name that psychologists give to the event.","zh":"as psychologists call the process 指使用心理學家給該事件的專門名稱。"},{"en":"A child may learn by imitation, as psychologists call the process, when she copies an adult’s words.","zh":"孩子模仿成人說話時，可能透過模仿學習，正如心理學家稱這個過程。"},{"en":"This phrase explains that an everyday behaviour has a scientific label.","zh":"這個短語解釋日常行為也有科學標籤。"},{"en":"It connects ordinary observation with specialist terminology.","zh":"它把普通觀察與專業術語連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"attention level","meaning":"注意力水平","examples":[{"en":"His attention level steadily drops as he becomes bored.","zh":"當他感到厭倦時，他的注意力水平穩步下降。"},{"en":"Attention level is how much focus or interest someone gives to something.","zh":"attention level 是某人對某事投入多少專注或興趣。"},{"en":"A student’s attention level may rise when the teacher uses a surprising example.","zh":"當老師使用令人驚訝的例子，學生的注意力水平可能上升。"},{"en":"Attention level can drop when material is repeated too often.","zh":"當材料被重複太多次，注意力水平可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the strength of someone’s focus.","zh":"這個短語描述某人專注程度的強弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"steadily drop","meaning":"穩步下降","examples":[{"en":"Daniel’s attention level steadily drops.","zh":"Daniel 的注意力水平穩步下降。"},{"en":"To steadily drop means to decrease gradually and continuously.","zh":"steadily drop 指逐漸而持續下降。"},{"en":"A student’s marks may steadily drop if she stops revising for several weeks.","zh":"如果學生幾星期停止溫習，成績可能穩步下降。"},{"en":"A steady drop shows a pattern, not one sudden change.","zh":"穩步下降顯示一種模式，而不是一次突然變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a slow but clear decline.","zh":"這個短語描述緩慢但清楚的下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pick up a little","meaning":"稍為提升","examples":[{"en":"His attention picks up a little when novelty is introduced.","zh":"當新奇事物被引入時，他的注意力稍為提升。"},{"en":"To pick up a little means to improve or increase slightly.","zh":"pick up a little 指稍微改善或增加。"},{"en":"A tired class may pick up a little when the teacher starts a game.","zh":"當老師開始遊戲，疲倦的班級可能稍為精神起來。"},{"en":"A small change can make interest pick up if students were bored before.","zh":"如果學生之前感到厭倦，小改變可以令興趣稍為提升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a modest rise, not a dramatic improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述適度上升，而不是巨大改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"novelty is introduced","meaning":"引入新奇事物","examples":[{"en":"His attention rises when novelty is introduced.","zh":"當新奇事物被引入時，他的注意力上升。"},{"en":"Novelty is introduced when something new, different, or unexpected is added.","zh":"novelty is introduced 指加入新的、不同的或出乎意料的東西。"},{"en":"A teacher introduces novelty by changing from a worksheet to a short experiment.","zh":"老師由工作紙轉為短實驗，就是引入新奇事物。"},{"en":"Novelty can increase attention because people notice changes more than repetition.","zh":"新奇事物可以提高注意力，因為人們比起重複更容易注意到變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adding something new to a familiar situation.","zh":"這個短語描述在熟悉情況中加入新東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"an impossible thing happens","meaning":"不可能的事情發生","examples":[{"en":"Sometimes an impossible thing happens in the experiment.","zh":"有時實驗中會發生不可能的事情。"},{"en":"An impossible thing happens when an event seems to break what people expect from reality or physics.","zh":"impossible thing happens 指某事件看似違反人們對現實或物理的預期。"},{"en":"In a magic show, an impossible thing seems to happen when a coin disappears from a closed hand.","zh":"在魔術表演中，硬幣從握緊的手中消失時，看似有不可能的事情發生。"},{"en":"Such events attract attention because the mind tries to explain the mismatch.","zh":"這類事件會吸引注意，因為心智嘗試解釋不匹配之處。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an event that appears not to be possible.","zh":"這個短語描述看似不可能發生的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"come out another colour","meaning":"出來時變成另一種顏色","examples":[{"en":"The train goes into the tunnel one colour and comes out another.","zh":"火車進入隧道時是一種顏色，出來時變成另一種顏色。"},{"en":"To come out another colour means to appear again with a different colour from before.","zh":"come out another colour 指再次出現時顏色與之前不同。"},{"en":"A toy car may enter a box red and come out another colour in a magic trick.","zh":"魔術中，玩具車可能紅色進入盒子，出來時變成另一種顏色。"},{"en":"A colour change can surprise a child because it breaks the repeated pattern.","zh":"顏色改變可以令孩子驚訝，因為它打破重複模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an object reappearing with changed colour.","zh":"這個短語描述物件重新出現時顏色改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"variations of experiments","meaning":"實驗的變化形式","examples":[{"en":"Variations of experiments like this have long been used in psychology.","zh":"這類實驗的變化形式長期以來已在心理學中使用。"},{"en":"Variations of experiments are different versions of a similar research design.","zh":"variations of experiments 是相似研究設計的不同版本。"},{"en":"A teacher may try variations of a vocabulary test by changing pictures, sentences, or answer choices.","zh":"老師可能透過改變圖片、句子或選項，嘗試詞彙測驗的變化形式。"},{"en":"Researchers use variations to see whether a result still appears under different conditions.","zh":"研究人員使用變化形式，以查看結果在不同條件下是否仍出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes modified forms of an experiment.","zh":"這個短語描述實驗的修改形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"examine infant attention","meaning":"研究嬰兒注意力","examples":[{"en":"The experiments examine infant attention.","zh":"這些實驗研究嬰兒注意力。"},{"en":"To examine infant attention means to study what babies look at, ignore, or notice.","zh":"examine infant attention 指研究嬰兒看甚麼、忽略甚麼或注意到甚麼。"},{"en":"Researchers may examine infant attention by measuring how long babies watch a toy.","zh":"研究人員可能透過量度嬰兒觀看玩具多久來研究嬰兒注意力。"},{"en":"Studying attention helps scientists infer what babies find new or interesting.","zh":"研究注意力幫助科學家推斷嬰兒覺得甚麼新奇或有趣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research into how babies focus.","zh":"這個短語描述關於嬰兒如何專注的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a standard tool of","meaning":"……的標準工具","examples":[{"en":"Infant-attention experiments are a standard tool of developmental psychology.","zh":"嬰兒注意力實驗是發展心理學的標準工具。"},{"en":"A standard tool of a field is a common method widely used by specialists in that field.","zh":"standard tool of 某領域，是該領域專家廣泛使用的常見方法。"},{"en":"Surveys are a standard tool of social research because they collect many people’s views.","zh":"問卷是社會研究的標準工具，因為它們收集許多人的看法。"},{"en":"A standard tool becomes common because it gives useful and repeatable information.","zh":"標準工具變得常見，是因為它提供有用且可重複的資料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an accepted research or working method.","zh":"這個短語描述被接受的研究或工作方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"developmental psychology","meaning":"發展心理學","examples":[{"en":"Jean Piaget was a pioneer of developmental psychology.","zh":"Jean Piaget 是發展心理學的先驅。"},{"en":"Developmental psychology is the study of how people grow and change in thinking, emotion, and behaviour over time.","zh":"developmental psychology 是研究人們的思考、情緒和行為如何隨時間成長和改變的學科。"},{"en":"Developmental psychology helps teachers understand why young children learn differently from teenagers.","zh":"發展心理學幫助老師理解幼童為何與青少年學習方式不同。"},{"en":"The field studies development from infancy through childhood and beyond.","zh":"這個領域研究由嬰兒期到童年及之後的發展。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the branch of psychology focused on human growth.","zh":"這個短語指專注於人類成長的心理學分支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ever since","meaning":"自從……以來","examples":[{"en":"Such experiments have been used ever since Piaget’s early work.","zh":"自從 Piaget 的早期研究以來，這類實驗一直被使用。"},{"en":"Ever since means from that time until now.","zh":"ever since 指從那個時間直到現在。"},{"en":"Ever since the school opened a library, more students have borrowed books.","zh":"自從學校開設圖書館以來，更多學生借書。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a starting point in the past with a continuing result.","zh":"這個短語把過去的起點與持續結果連起來。"},{"en":"It shows that something has continued for a long period.","zh":"它顯示某事已持續很長時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pioneer of the field","meaning":"該領域的先驅","examples":[{"en":"Jean Piaget was a Swiss pioneer of the field.","zh":"Jean Piaget 是該領域的瑞士先驅。"},{"en":"A pioneer of the field is an early and important person who helps develop an area of study or work.","zh":"pioneer of the field 是早期重要人物，幫助發展某研究或工作範疇。"},{"en":"A doctor who creates a new treatment may become a pioneer of the field.","zh":"創造新療法的醫生可能成為該領域的先驅。"},{"en":"Pioneers influence later researchers because they ask new questions and design new methods.","zh":"先驅影響後來研究者，因為他們提出新問題並設計新方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes someone who helped begin or shape a discipline.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助開創或塑造一門學科的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"experiment on","meaning":"對……進行實驗","examples":[{"en":"Piaget experimented on his own children in the 1920s.","zh":"Piaget 在1920年代對自己的孩子進行實驗。"},{"en":"To experiment on someone or something means to use them as the subject of a scientific test.","zh":"experiment on 某人或某物，指把他們作為科學測試對象。"},{"en":"Scientists may experiment on plants to see how light affects growth.","zh":"科學家可能對植物進行實驗，以了解光線如何影響生長。"},{"en":"Experiments on children require special care because they are vulnerable.","zh":"對兒童進行實驗需要特別小心，因為他們較脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes carrying out research using a particular subject.","zh":"這個短語描述使用特定對象進行研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lead someone to conclude that","meaning":"使某人得出結論認為","examples":[{"en":"Piaget’s work led him to conclude that young infants lack innate knowledge.","zh":"Piaget 的研究使他得出結論認為，年幼嬰兒缺乏先天知識。"},{"en":"To lead someone to conclude that means to cause someone to reach a belief after considering evidence.","zh":"lead someone to conclude that 指使某人在考慮證據後達成某信念。"},{"en":"Repeated low test scores may lead a teacher to conclude that students need more grammar practice.","zh":"反覆低測驗分數可能使老師得出結論認為學生需要更多文法練習。"},{"en":"Evidence can lead people to a conclusion, but the conclusion may later be challenged.","zh":"證據可以引導人得出結論，但該結論後來可能被挑戰。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence guiding someone’s judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述證據引導某人的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"innate knowledge","meaning":"先天知識","examples":[{"en":"Piaget argued that young infants have no innate knowledge of the world.","zh":"Piaget 主張年幼嬰兒沒有關於世界的先天知識。"},{"en":"Innate knowledge is knowledge that a person or animal is thought to have from birth.","zh":"innate knowledge 是被認為人或動物出生時已有的知識。"},{"en":"If babies recognise faces without much practice, some scientists may call this innate knowledge.","zh":"如果嬰兒不用太多練習就能認出人臉，有些科學家可能稱這為先天知識。"},{"en":"The debate over innate knowledge asks whether learning starts with built-in ideas or experience.","zh":"關於先天知識的爭論，是問學習是否從內置概念開始，還是從經驗開始。"},{"en":"The phrase describes knowledge treated as natural rather than learned later.","zh":"這個短語描述被視為天生而非後天學得的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"how the world works","meaning":"世界如何運作","examples":[{"en":"Piaget believed babies must learn how the world works.","zh":"Piaget 相信嬰兒必須學習世界如何運作。"},{"en":"How the world works means the basic rules or patterns of reality, such as objects falling or people returning.","zh":"how the world works 指現實的基本規則或模式，例如物件會下跌或人會回來。"},{"en":"A child learns how the world works when she discovers that hot food can burn her mouth.","zh":"當孩子發現熱食會燙到嘴，她就在學習世界如何運作。"},{"en":"Repeated experiences help children build expectations about cause and effect.","zh":"重複經驗幫助孩子建立對因果的預期。"},{"en":"The phrase describes understanding ordinary rules of life and reality.","zh":"這個短語描述理解生活和現實的普通規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"object permanence","meaning":"物體恆存概念","examples":[{"en":"Piaget argued that young infants lack a sense of object permanence.","zh":"Piaget 主張年幼嬰兒缺乏物體恆存概念。"},{"en":"Object permanence is the understanding that objects and people continue to exist when they cannot be seen.","zh":"object permanence 是理解物件和人即使看不見仍然存在。"},{"en":"A baby shows object permanence when he looks for a toy hidden under a blanket.","zh":"當嬰兒尋找藏在毛氈下的玩具，他就顯示出物體恆存概念。"},{"en":"Without object permanence, a hidden object may seem to have disappeared completely.","zh":"沒有物體恆存概念，隱藏物件可能看似完全消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a basic idea about objects continuing to exist.","zh":"這個短語描述關於物件持續存在的基本概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"still exist even when","meaning":"即使……仍然存在","examples":[{"en":"Object permanence means that people and things still exist even when they are not seen.","zh":"物體恆存概念指人和物即使看不見仍然存在。"},{"en":"Still exist even when means continue to be real or present despite a particular condition.","zh":"still exist even when 指儘管有某種情況，仍繼續真實存在或在場。"},{"en":"A friend still exists even when she moves to another country and you cannot see her daily.","zh":"朋友搬到另一個國家後，即使你不能每天見到她，她仍然存在。"},{"en":"Understanding this idea helps children feel less anxious when a parent leaves the room.","zh":"理解這個概念幫助孩子在父母離開房間時較少焦慮。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that absence from sight is not the same as non-existence.","zh":"這個短語顯示看不見不等於不存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"gradually construct","meaning":"逐步建構","examples":[{"en":"Piaget believed babies gradually construct knowledge from experience.","zh":"Piaget 相信嬰兒透過經驗逐步建構知識。"},{"en":"To gradually construct something means to build it slowly over time, piece by piece.","zh":"gradually construct 某物，指隨時間一步步慢慢建立它。"},{"en":"Students gradually construct essay skills by learning introductions, examples, and conclusions one at a time.","zh":"學生透過逐一學習引言、例子和結論，逐步建構文章技巧。"},{"en":"Knowledge becomes stronger when each new experience adds to what was learned before.","zh":"當每個新經驗都加在之前所學之上，知識會變得更強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow development through repeated building.","zh":"這個短語描述透過反覆建立而緩慢發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"construct knowledge from experience","meaning":"從經驗建構知識","examples":[{"en":"Babies must construct knowledge from experience.","zh":"嬰兒必須從經驗建構知識。"},{"en":"To construct knowledge from experience means to build understanding by learning from what happens.","zh":"construct knowledge from experience 指透過從發生的事情中學習來建立理解。"},{"en":"A child constructs knowledge from experience when she learns that glass breaks if dropped.","zh":"當孩子學會玻璃掉下會碎，她就是從經驗建構知識。"},{"en":"Repeated real-life events help children connect actions with outcomes.","zh":"重複的真實生活事件幫助孩子把行動與結果連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning by building understanding from lived events.","zh":"這個短語描述從親身經歷中建立理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"constructivist theories","meaning":"建構主義理論","examples":[{"en":"Piaget’s constructivist theories influenced many educators.","zh":"Piaget 的建構主義理論影響了許多教育家。"},{"en":"Constructivist theories say learners build knowledge actively through experience and interaction.","zh":"constructivist theories 認為學習者透過經驗和互動主動建構知識。"},{"en":"A teacher using constructivist ideas may let students discover grammar patterns from examples.","zh":"使用建構主義想法的老師，可能讓學生從例子中發現文法模式。"},{"en":"These theories influence education because they make learning more active than memorisation alone.","zh":"這些理論影響教育，因為它們令學習比單純記憶更主動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to theories about learners constructing understanding.","zh":"這個短語指關於學習者建構理解的理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"massively influential","meaning":"影響極大","examples":[{"en":"Piaget’s theories were massively influential after the war.","zh":"Piaget 的理論在戰後影響極大。"},{"en":"Massively influential means having a very large effect on people’s ideas, behaviour, or work.","zh":"massively influential 指對人們的想法、行為或工作有非常巨大影響。"},{"en":"A simple teaching method can become massively influential if many schools adopt it.","zh":"如果許多學校採用一種簡單教學方法，它可以變得影響極大。"},{"en":"Influential theories shape what teachers believe and how classrooms are organised.","zh":"有影響力的理論會塑造老師相信甚麼，以及課室如何組織。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extremely strong influence.","zh":"這個短語描述極強的影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"postwar educators","meaning":"戰後教育家","examples":[{"en":"Piaget’s theories influenced postwar educators.","zh":"Piaget 的理論影響了戰後教育家。"},{"en":"Postwar educators are teachers, researchers, or education leaders working after a war, especially after World War Two in this context.","zh":"postwar educators 是戰後工作的老師、研究者或教育領袖，在此尤其指二戰後。"},{"en":"Postwar educators often looked for new ways to rebuild schools and societies.","zh":"戰後教育家常尋找重建學校和社會的新方法。"},{"en":"Educational theories can spread quickly when educators are searching for change.","zh":"當教育工作者尋求改變，教育理論可以迅速傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies education thinkers and workers in the period after war.","zh":"這個短語指出戰後時期的教育思想家和工作者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be largely set aside","meaning":"在很大程度上被擱置","examples":[{"en":"Piaget’s theories have been largely set aside by newer psychologists.","zh":"Piaget 的理論在很大程度上被較新的心理學家擱置。"},{"en":"To be largely set aside means to be mostly no longer used, accepted, or treated as central.","zh":"be largely set aside 指大部分不再被使用、接受或視為核心。"},{"en":"An old textbook may be largely set aside when a new syllabus is introduced.","zh":"當新課程引入，舊教科書可能在很大程度上被擱置。"},{"en":"Ideas are set aside when stronger evidence or better explanations replace them.","zh":"當更強證據或更好解釋取代舊想法，舊想法就會被擱置。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something losing its former importance.","zh":"這個短語描述某事失去昔日重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a new generation of","meaning":"新一代……","examples":[{"en":"A new generation of psychologists challenged Piaget’s ideas.","zh":"新一代心理學家挑戰 Piaget 的想法。"},{"en":"A new generation of a group means younger or later members who bring fresh views or methods.","zh":"new generation of 某群體，指帶來新看法或方法的較年輕或後來成員。"},{"en":"A new generation of teachers may use technology more naturally in lessons.","zh":"新一代老師可能更自然地在課堂中使用科技。"},{"en":"New generations often question older ideas because they have new tools and evidence.","zh":"新一代常質疑舊想法，因為他們有新工具和證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a later group replacing or challenging earlier thinkers.","zh":"這個短語描述後來群體取代或挑戰早期思想家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"nativist psychologists","meaning":"天賦論心理學家","examples":[{"en":"Nativist psychologists believe babies are born with some knowledge.","zh":"天賦論心理學家相信嬰兒出生時已有某些知識。"},{"en":"Nativist psychologists are researchers who argue that some mental abilities are built in from birth.","zh":"nativist psychologists 是主張某些心理能力出生時已內置的研究者。"},{"en":"A nativist psychologist may say babies naturally expect objects to follow basic physical rules.","zh":"天賦論心理學家可能說嬰兒天生預期物件會遵從基本物理規則。"},{"en":"Their view contrasts with theories that say babies learn everything only through experience.","zh":"他們的看法與認為嬰兒只透過經驗學習一切的理論形成對比。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to psychologists who emphasise innate abilities.","zh":"這個短語指強調先天能力的心理學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cognitive scientists","meaning":"認知科學家","examples":[{"en":"Cognitive scientists study how the mind processes information.","zh":"認知科學家研究心智如何處理資訊。"},{"en":"Cognitive scientists are researchers who study thinking, memory, attention, language, and learning.","zh":"cognitive scientists 是研究思考、記憶、注意力、語言和學習的研究者。"},{"en":"A cognitive scientist may study how students remember new vocabulary.","zh":"認知科學家可能研究學生如何記住新詞彙。"},{"en":"Their research helps explain why people notice some information and ignore other information.","zh":"他們的研究幫助解釋為何人們注意某些資訊而忽略其他資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to scientists who study the mind and mental processes.","zh":"這個短語指研究心智和心理過程的科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sophisticated experiments","meaning":"更精密的實驗","examples":[{"en":"More sophisticated experiments led researchers to new theories.","zh":"更精密的實驗使研究人員走向新理論。"},{"en":"Sophisticated experiments are carefully designed, advanced experiments with more precise methods or tools.","zh":"sophisticated experiments 是設計仔細、方法或工具更精準的先進實驗。"},{"en":"A hospital may use sophisticated experiments to test whether a new treatment really works.","zh":"醫院可能使用更精密的實驗，測試新療法是否真的有效。"},{"en":"Better experiments can reveal details that simple tests miss.","zh":"更好的實驗可以揭示簡單測試錯過的細節。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research that is more advanced and carefully controlled.","zh":"這個短語描述更先進且控制更仔細的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"theorise that","meaning":"提出理論認為","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists theorise that infants arrive with built-in knowledge.","zh":"有些科學家提出理論認為，嬰兒出生時已有內置知識。"},{"en":"To theorise that means to suggest an explanation based on evidence and reasoning.","zh":"theorise that 指根據證據和推理提出解釋。"},{"en":"Teachers may theorise that students are tired because homework and exams overlap.","zh":"老師可能提出理論認為學生疲倦，是因為功課和考試重疊。"},{"en":"A theory can be tested, supported, or challenged by later evidence.","zh":"理論可以被後來證據測試、支持或挑戰。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a possible scientific explanation.","zh":"這個短語引出可能的科學解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"arrive already equipped with","meaning":"出生時已具備……","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists think infants arrive already equipped with knowledge.","zh":"有些科學家認為嬰兒出生時已具備知識。"},{"en":"To arrive already equipped with something means to begin life or a task already having it.","zh":"arrive already equipped with 某物，指開始生命或任務時已經擁有它。"},{"en":"Some children arrive at school already equipped with basic reading skills.","zh":"有些孩子入學時已具備基本閱讀能力。"},{"en":"If babies arrive equipped with knowledge, experience is not the only source of learning.","zh":"如果嬰兒出生時已具備知識，經驗就不是學習的唯一來源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes starting with something already present.","zh":"這個短語描述一開始就已經有某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the physical world","meaning":"物理世界","examples":[{"en":"Babies may have some knowledge of the physical world.","zh":"嬰兒可能對物理世界有一些知識。"},{"en":"The physical world means the world of objects, space, movement, gravity, and material things.","zh":"physical world 指由物件、空間、移動、重力和物質事物組成的世界。"},{"en":"A child learns about the physical world when she sees a ball roll down a slope.","zh":"當孩子看見球從斜坡滾下，她就在學習物理世界。"},{"en":"Understanding the physical world helps children predict what objects will do.","zh":"理解物理世界幫助孩子預測物件會如何運動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to reality as governed by physical objects and rules.","zh":"這個短語指由實體物件和規則支配的現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rudimentary programming","meaning":"初步的內置機制","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists suggest babies have rudimentary programming for mathematics and language.","zh":"有些科學家提出嬰兒有用於數學和語言的初步內置機制。"},{"en":"Rudimentary programming means very basic built-in mental mechanisms or starting abilities.","zh":"rudimentary programming 指非常基本的內置心理機制或起始能力。"},{"en":"A baby’s tendency to notice patterns may be seen as rudimentary programming for learning.","zh":"嬰兒注意模式的傾向，可能被視為學習的初步內置機制。"},{"en":"Such programming would not mean full knowledge, only a simple starting structure.","zh":"這種機制不代表完整知識，只代表簡單的起始結構。"},{"en":"The phrase describes basic internal preparation for later learning.","zh":"這個短語描述為後來學習而存在的基本內部準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"mathematics and language","meaning":"數學和語言","examples":[{"en":"Some theories claim babies have early mechanisms for mathematics and language.","zh":"有些理論聲稱嬰兒有用於數學和語言的早期機制。"},{"en":"Mathematics and language are systems for number, pattern, communication, meaning, and grammar.","zh":"mathematics and language 是關於數字、模式、溝通、意義和文法的系統。"},{"en":"Children use mathematics and language when they count toys and explain what they want.","zh":"孩子數玩具並解釋自己想要甚麼時，就在使用數學和語言。"},{"en":"Early abilities in these areas may support later school learning.","zh":"這些範疇的早期能力可能支持後來的學校學習。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to two major areas of human thinking.","zh":"這個短語指人類思考的兩大主要範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"put theories through","meaning":"對理論進行……測試","examples":[{"en":"Sirois has put smart-baby theories through rigorous tests.","zh":"Sirois 對聰明嬰兒理論進行嚴格測試。"},{"en":"To put theories through tests means to examine them carefully to see whether they hold up.","zh":"put theories through tests 指仔細檢驗理論，看它們是否站得住腳。"},{"en":"A teacher may put a new teaching idea through classroom trials before using it widely.","zh":"老師可能在廣泛使用新教學想法前，先對它進行課堂試驗。"},{"en":"Testing theories can reveal whether an explanation is strong or only attractive.","zh":"測試理論可以揭示某解釋是有力，還是只是吸引人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes subjecting ideas to careful examination.","zh":"這個短語描述讓想法接受仔細檢驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a rigorous set of tests","meaning":"一套嚴格測試","examples":[{"en":"BabyLab uses a rigorous set of tests.","zh":"BabyLab 使用一套嚴格測試。"},{"en":"A rigorous set of tests is a group of careful, strict tests designed to produce reliable evidence.","zh":"rigorous set of tests 是一組仔細、嚴格並旨在產生可靠證據的測試。"},{"en":"A school may use a rigorous set of tests to decide whether a new reading programme works.","zh":"學校可能使用一套嚴格測試，判斷新閱讀計劃是否有效。"},{"en":"Rigorous tests reduce guesswork because they control conditions and measure results closely.","zh":"嚴格測試透過控制條件和仔細量度結果來減少猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious and carefully designed testing.","zh":"這個短語描述認真而仔細設計的測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"conclusions so far","meaning":"到目前為止的結論","examples":[{"en":"Sirois’s conclusions so far are closer to Piaget’s view.","zh":"Sirois 到目前為止的結論較接近 Piaget 的看法。"},{"en":"Conclusions so far are the ideas reached at this stage, before all research is complete.","zh":"conclusions so far 是在目前階段得出的想法，研究尚未全部完成。"},{"en":"The doctor’s conclusions so far may change after more test results arrive.","zh":"醫生到目前為止的結論可能在更多檢查結果出來後改變。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that the evidence is still developing.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者證據仍在發展。"},{"en":"It describes a current but possibly unfinished judgement.","zh":"它描述目前但可能未完成的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tend to be","meaning":"往往是；傾向於","examples":[{"en":"His conclusions tend to be more Piagetian.","zh":"他的結論傾向於更皮亞傑式。"},{"en":"Tend to be means usually are or are more often in a particular way.","zh":"tend to be 指通常是或較常以某種方式存在。"},{"en":"Students tend to be more confident when they practise speaking in small groups first.","zh":"學生先在小組練習說話時，往往會更有信心。"},{"en":"A tendency is a pattern, not an absolute rule.","zh":"傾向是一種模式，不是絕對規則。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what commonly happens.","zh":"這個短語描述通常發生的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Piagetian","meaning":"皮亞傑式的","examples":[{"en":"Sirois’s conclusions are more Piagetian than nativist.","zh":"Sirois 的結論較天賦論更皮亞傑式。"},{"en":"Piagetian means related to Jean Piaget’s view that children build knowledge gradually through experience.","zh":"Piagetian 指與 Jean Piaget 的看法有關，即孩子透過經驗逐漸建構知識。"},{"en":"A Piagetian teacher may design activities that let children discover rules for themselves.","zh":"皮亞傑式老師可能設計活動，讓孩子自己發現規則。"},{"en":"Piagetian explanations often emphasise development, stages, and learning from action.","zh":"皮亞傑式解釋常強調發展、階段和從行動中學習。"},{"en":"The word identifies ideas connected with Piaget’s theory.","zh":"這個詞指出與 Piaget 理論相關的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"know nothing","meaning":"一無所知","examples":[{"en":"Sirois argues that babies know nothing at first.","zh":"Sirois 主張嬰兒一開始一無所知。"},{"en":"To know nothing means to have no knowledge about a particular thing or, in this context, to start without knowledge.","zh":"know nothing 指對某事沒有知識；在此語境中指開始時沒有知識。"},{"en":"A beginner may know nothing about piano before the first lesson.","zh":"初學者上第一堂鋼琴課前，可能對鋼琴一無所知。"},{"en":"If someone knows nothing at first, learning must happen through experience and practice.","zh":"如果某人一開始一無所知，學習就必須透過經驗和練習發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a starting point of complete ignorance.","zh":"這個短語描述完全無知的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"postgraduate assistant","meaning":"研究生助理","examples":[{"en":"Iain Jackson is Sirois’s postgraduate assistant.","zh":"Iain Jackson 是 Sirois 的研究生助理。"},{"en":"A postgraduate assistant is a graduate student who helps a researcher or lecturer with academic work.","zh":"postgraduate assistant 是協助研究人員或講師做學術工作的研究生。"},{"en":"A postgraduate assistant may collect data, prepare materials, or help run experiments.","zh":"研究生助理可能收集數據、準備材料或協助進行實驗。"},{"en":"Assistants support research by handling tasks that make the project run smoothly.","zh":"助理透過處理任務來支援研究，使項目順利進行。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a university helper who is studying at postgraduate level.","zh":"這個短語指在大學中以研究生身份協助工作的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"challenge the interpretation of","meaning":"質疑對……的詮釋","examples":[{"en":"Sirois and Jackson challenge the interpretation of classic experiments.","zh":"Sirois 和 Jackson 質疑對經典實驗的詮釋。"},{"en":"To challenge the interpretation of something means to question the meaning others have drawn from it.","zh":"challenge the interpretation of 某事，指質疑別人從中得出的意思。"},{"en":"A student may challenge the interpretation of a poem by offering evidence for another reading.","zh":"學生可能透過提出支持另一種解讀的證據，質疑對詩的詮釋。"},{"en":"People can accept the data but still disagree about what the data mean.","zh":"人們可以接受數據，但仍不同意數據代表甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes questioning an explanation rather than the event itself.","zh":"這個短語描述質疑解釋，而不是質疑事件本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a variety of","meaning":"各種各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"They challenge the interpretation of a variety of classic experiments.","zh":"他們質疑對各種經典實驗的詮釋。"},{"en":"A variety of means several different kinds of something.","zh":"a variety of 指幾種不同類型的某物。"},{"en":"A good lesson uses a variety of examples so students see the phrase in different situations.","zh":"好課堂會使用各種例子，讓學生在不同情況中看見短語。"},{"en":"Variety helps learning because one example may not be enough for every student.","zh":"多樣性有助學習，因為一個例子未必足夠所有學生理解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a range, not just one type.","zh":"這個短語描述一個範圍，而不只是單一類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"classic experiments","meaning":"經典實驗","examples":[{"en":"The researchers reconsider several classic experiments.","zh":"研究人員重新考慮幾項經典實驗。"},{"en":"Classic experiments are well-known experiments that have strongly influenced a field.","zh":"classic experiments 是在某領域中廣為人知並有重大影響的實驗。"},{"en":"Students may study classic experiments in psychology to understand how major theories developed.","zh":"學生可能研究心理學中的經典實驗，以理解主要理論如何發展。"},{"en":"Classic experiments can still be questioned when new methods or data appear.","zh":"當新方法或數據出現，經典實驗仍可以被質疑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes important older studies that remain influential.","zh":"這個短語描述仍具影響力的重要舊研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"physical events","meaning":"物理事件","examples":[{"en":"The experiments showed babies physical events.","zh":"這些實驗向嬰兒展示物理事件。"},{"en":"Physical events are happenings involving objects, movement, space, or forces such as gravity.","zh":"physical events 是涉及物件、移動、空間或重力等力量的事情。"},{"en":"A ball rolling off a table is a simple physical event.","zh":"球從桌上滾下是一個簡單物理事件。"},{"en":"Babies may look longer at physical events that break their expectations.","zh":"嬰兒可能較久注視打破其預期的物理事件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes events in the material world.","zh":"這個短語描述物質世界中的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"appear to violate","meaning":"看似違反……","examples":[{"en":"Some events appeared to violate basic physical concepts.","zh":"有些事件看似違反基本物理概念。"},{"en":"To appear to violate a rule or concept means to seem to break it, even if the appearance may be misleading.","zh":"appear to violate 規則或概念，指看似打破它，即使這種表象可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"A magic trick may appear to violate gravity when a person seems to float.","zh":"當一個人看似漂浮時，魔術可能看似違反重力。"},{"en":"Events that appear to violate expectations can attract strong attention.","zh":"看似違反預期的事件可以強烈吸引注意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something seeming to break a rule.","zh":"這個短語描述某事看似打破規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"basic concepts","meaning":"基本概念","examples":[{"en":"The events appeared to violate basic concepts such as gravity.","zh":"這些事件看似違反重力等基本概念。"},{"en":"Basic concepts are simple, important ideas needed to understand a subject.","zh":"basic concepts 是理解一個科目所需的簡單而重要的想法。"},{"en":"Addition and subtraction are basic concepts in early mathematics.","zh":"加法和減法是早期數學的基本概念。"},{"en":"If students lack basic concepts, harder lessons become confusing.","zh":"如果學生缺乏基本概念，較難課堂會變得令人困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to foundation ideas in a topic.","zh":"這個短語指某主題中的基礎想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"gravity","meaning":"重力","examples":[{"en":"Gravity is one of the basic concepts tested in the experiments.","zh":"重力是實驗中測試的基本概念之一。"},{"en":"Gravity is the force that pulls objects toward the Earth or toward another large body.","zh":"gravity 是把物件拉向地球或另一個大型天體的力量。"},{"en":"A child learns about gravity when a spoon falls from the table to the floor.","zh":"當湯匙從桌上掉到地上，孩子就在學習重力。"},{"en":"Gravity helps people predict that unsupported objects will fall rather than float.","zh":"重力幫助人預測沒有支撐的物件會下跌而不是漂浮。"},{"en":"The word describes a basic physical force.","zh":"這個詞描述一種基本物理力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"solidity","meaning":"實體性；不可穿透性","examples":[{"en":"Solidity is one of the physical concepts in the experiments.","zh":"實體性是實驗中的物理概念之一。"},{"en":"Solidity is the idea that solid objects take up space and normally cannot pass through one another.","zh":"solidity 是指實體物件佔據空間，通常不能互相穿過的概念。"},{"en":"A child learns solidity when a toy car cannot move through a closed door.","zh":"當玩具車不能穿過關上的門，孩子就在學習實體性。"},{"en":"If an object seems to pass through another solid object, it may surprise observers.","zh":"如果一個物件看似穿過另一個實體物件，可能會令觀察者驚訝。"},{"en":"The word describes the physical property of being solid and resistant.","zh":"這個詞描述物件為實體且有阻擋性的物理特性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"contiguity","meaning":"接觸性；相連性","examples":[{"en":"Contiguity was one of the basic concepts mentioned in the passage.","zh":"接觸性是文章中提及的基本概念之一。"},{"en":"Contiguity means closeness, contact, or connection between things in space or time.","zh":"contiguity 指事物在空間或時間上的接近、接觸或連繫。"},{"en":"In learning, a child may connect a sound with food if the two happen in close contiguity.","zh":"在學習中，如果聲音和食物很接近地發生，孩子可能把兩者連起來。"},{"en":"Things that happen close together are easier for the mind to link.","zh":"發生時間或位置接近的事物，較容易被心智連繫。"},{"en":"The phrase describes nearness or connection that helps association.","zh":"這個短語描述有助聯想的接近或連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in one such experiment","meaning":"在其中一個這類實驗中","examples":[{"en":"In one such experiment, a panel appeared to pass through a box.","zh":"在其中一個這類實驗中，一塊板看似穿過盒子。"},{"en":"In one such experiment means in one experiment of the kind just described.","zh":"in one such experiment 指在剛描述那類實驗中的其中一個。"},{"en":"In one such experiment, students watched a video and then answered memory questions.","zh":"在其中一個這類實驗中，學生觀看影片後回答記憶問題。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a specific example from a larger group of similar studies.","zh":"這個短語從一組相似研究中引出一個具體例子。"},{"en":"It helps move from general discussion to one concrete case.","zh":"它幫助由一般討論轉向具體個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hinged wooden panel","meaning":"裝有鉸鏈的木板","examples":[{"en":"A hinged wooden panel appeared to pass through a box.","zh":"一塊裝有鉸鏈的木板看似穿過盒子。"},{"en":"A hinged wooden panel is a flat piece of wood attached by a hinge so it can swing or rotate.","zh":"hinged wooden panel 是用鉸鏈連接、可以擺動或旋轉的平面木板。"},{"en":"A cupboard door is like a hinged wooden panel because it opens and closes on a hinge.","zh":"櫥櫃門像裝有鉸鏈的木板，因為它靠鉸鏈開合。"},{"en":"A hinged panel can move predictably, so unusual movement is easier to notice.","zh":"裝有鉸鏈的木板會以可預測方式移動，所以不尋常移動更容易被注意到。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a movable wooden board.","zh":"這個短語描述可移動的木板。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"pass right through","meaning":"直接穿過","examples":[{"en":"The panel appeared to pass right through the box.","zh":"木板看似直接穿過盒子。"},{"en":"To pass right through something means to move directly from one side to the other side of it.","zh":"pass right through 某物，指直接從它一邊移到另一邊。"},{"en":"A needle can pass right through thin cloth.","zh":"針可以直接穿過薄布。"},{"en":"A solid board passing through a solid box would seem impossible because both take up space.","zh":"實體木板穿過實體盒子會看似不可能，因為兩者都佔空間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct movement through an object or space.","zh":"這個短語描述直接穿越物件或空間的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as young as","meaning":"年僅……","examples":[{"en":"Babies as young as three and a half months looked longer at the impossible event.","zh":"年僅三個半月的嬰兒較久注視不可能事件。"},{"en":"As young as means at an age that is surprisingly young.","zh":"as young as 指年齡小得令人驚訝。"},{"en":"Children as young as four can sometimes learn simple computer coding through games.","zh":"年僅四歲的孩子有時可以透過遊戲學習簡單電腦編程。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights that an ability appears earlier than expected.","zh":"這個短語突出能力比預期更早出現。"},{"en":"It is used to stress youth or early development.","zh":"它用來強調年幼或早期發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"three and a half months","meaning":"三個半月","examples":[{"en":"Babies three and a half months old took part in the experiment.","zh":"三個半月大的嬰兒參與了實驗。"},{"en":"Three and a half months means three months plus about two more weeks.","zh":"three and a half months 指三個月再加大約兩星期。"},{"en":"A baby three and a half months old may start holding the head more steadily.","zh":"三個半月大的嬰兒可能開始較穩定地抬頭。"},{"en":"Mentioning this exact age helps readers judge how early the response appeared.","zh":"提到這個準確年齡，幫助讀者判斷反應出現得多早。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a precise age for very young infants.","zh":"這個短語為很年幼嬰兒提供精確年齡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reliably look longer at","meaning":"穩定地注視……更久","examples":[{"en":"Babies would reliably look longer at the impossible event.","zh":"嬰兒會穩定地更久注視不可能事件。"},{"en":"To reliably look longer at something means to repeatedly and consistently spend more time looking at it.","zh":"reliably look longer at 某物，指反覆而一致地花更多時間看它。"},{"en":"In a classroom study, students may reliably look longer at colourful diagrams than plain text.","zh":"在課堂研究中，學生可能穩定地更久注視彩色圖表而不是純文字。"},{"en":"If babies reliably look longer, researchers treat the pattern as more than chance.","zh":"如果嬰兒穩定地注視更久，研究人員會把該模式視為不只是偶然。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a stable attention pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述穩定的注意力模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"impossible event","meaning":"不可能事件","examples":[{"en":"Babies looked longer at the impossible event.","zh":"嬰兒較久注視不可能事件。"},{"en":"An impossible event is something that appears to break basic rules of reality or physics.","zh":"impossible event 是看似違反現實或物理基本規則的事情。"},{"en":"A toy passing through a solid wall would be an impossible event.","zh":"玩具穿過實體牆會是一個不可能事件。"},{"en":"Impossible events attract attention because they do not match ordinary expectations.","zh":"不可能事件會吸引注意，因為它們不符合普通預期。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an event that should not be able to happen.","zh":"這個短語描述不應能夠發生的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"normal event","meaning":"正常事件","examples":[{"en":"The babies compared the impossible event with the normal one.","zh":"嬰兒把不可能事件與正常事件作比較。"},{"en":"A normal event is something that happens in an expected and ordinary way.","zh":"normal event 是以預期和普通方式發生的事情。"},{"en":"A ball falling after being dropped is a normal event.","zh":"球被放手後掉下是正常事件。"},{"en":"Researchers compare normal events with unusual ones to see what attracts attention.","zh":"研究人員把正常事件與不尋常事件比較，以了解甚麼吸引注意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an event that follows expected rules.","zh":"這個短語描述遵從預期規則的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"built-in knowledge","meaning":"內置知識；先天知識","examples":[{"en":"The researchers concluded that babies have built-in knowledge.","zh":"研究人員得出結論認為，嬰兒有內置知識。"},{"en":"Built-in knowledge is knowledge thought to be present naturally, without needing to be learned from experience.","zh":"built-in knowledge 是被認為自然存在、不需要從經驗學得的知識。"},{"en":"If babies expect objects to behave in certain ways, scientists may describe this as built-in knowledge.","zh":"如果嬰兒預期物件會以某些方式行動，科學家可能把這描述為內置知識。"},{"en":"Built-in knowledge would mean babies do not begin life completely blank.","zh":"內置知識意味嬰兒並非完全空白地開始生命。"},{"en":"The phrase describes knowledge treated as part of the mind from the start.","zh":"這個短語描述被視為從一開始就存在於心智中的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"recognise that something is wrong","meaning":"意識到有問題","examples":[{"en":"The babies seemed to recognise that something was wrong.","zh":"嬰兒似乎意識到有問題。"},{"en":"To recognise that something is wrong means to notice that an event does not fit what should happen.","zh":"recognise that something is wrong 指注意到事件不符合應該發生的情況。"},{"en":"A child may recognise that something is wrong when a teacher calls the class by the wrong name.","zh":"當老師叫錯班名，孩子可能意識到有問題。"},{"en":"Recognition of wrongness can make someone stare, pause, or look confused.","zh":"意識到有問題可能令人盯着看、停下來或露出困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes noticing a mismatch or problem.","zh":"這個短語描述注意到不匹配或問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take issue with","meaning":"對……提出異議","examples":[{"en":"Sirois does not take issue with the way the experiments were conducted.","zh":"Sirois 並不對實驗進行方式提出異議。"},{"en":"To take issue with something means to disagree with it or object to it.","zh":"take issue with 某事，指不同意它或反對它。"},{"en":"A parent may take issue with a school rule if it seems unfair to younger children.","zh":"如果校規對年幼孩子看似不公平，家長可能提出異議。"},{"en":"People can take issue with an interpretation while accepting the evidence itself.","zh":"人們可以接受證據本身，但對其詮釋提出異議。"},{"en":"The phrase describes disagreement with a specific point.","zh":"這個短語描述對特定一點的不同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the way experiments were conducted","meaning":"實驗進行的方式","examples":[{"en":"Sirois accepts the way the experiments were conducted.","zh":"Sirois 接受實驗進行的方式。"},{"en":"The way experiments were conducted means the methods and procedures used to carry out the experiments.","zh":"way experiments were conducted 指進行實驗所使用的方法和程序。"},{"en":"A scientist may criticise the way an experiment was conducted if the sample was too small.","zh":"如果樣本太小，科學家可能批評實驗進行的方式。"},{"en":"Good conduct matters because poor methods can weaken results.","zh":"進行方式很重要，因為差劣方法可以削弱結果。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to how the research was actually done.","zh":"這個短語指研究實際如何完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"correct and replicable","meaning":"正確且可複製","examples":[{"en":"Sirois says the methods are correct and replicable.","zh":"Sirois 說這些方法是正確且可複製的。"},{"en":"Correct and replicable means accurate and possible for other researchers to repeat with similar results.","zh":"correct and replicable 指準確，並可由其他研究人員重複而得到相似結果。"},{"en":"A classroom study is stronger if its method is correct and replicable.","zh":"如果課堂研究的方法正確且可複製，它會更有力。"},{"en":"Replicable methods help science because findings should not depend on one researcher only.","zh":"可複製方法有助科學，因為發現不應只依賴一名研究者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research methods that are trustworthy and repeatable.","zh":"這個短語描述可信且可重複的研究方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the interpretation is the problem","meaning":"問題在於詮釋","examples":[{"en":"Sirois argues that the interpretation is the problem.","zh":"Sirois 主張問題在於詮釋。"},{"en":"The interpretation is the problem means the data may be acceptable, but the explanation of the data is questionable.","zh":"the interpretation is the problem 指數據可能可接受，但對數據的解釋有問題。"},{"en":"A teacher may say the test scores are real, but the interpretation is the problem if people blame laziness too quickly.","zh":"老師可能說測驗分數是真實的，但如果人們太快歸咎懶惰，問題就在於詮釋。"},{"en":"Evidence can be correct while the meaning drawn from it is wrong.","zh":"證據可以正確，但從中得出的意思可能錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase separates facts from the explanation of those facts.","zh":"這個短語把事實與對事實的解釋分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"critical review","meaning":"批判性評論","examples":[{"en":"Sirois and Jackson wrote a critical review of recent experiments.","zh":"Sirois 和 Jackson 撰寫了一篇關於近期實驗的批判性評論。"},{"en":"A critical review is a careful evaluation that examines strengths, weaknesses, and possible problems.","zh":"critical review 是仔細評估優點、弱點和可能問題的評論。"},{"en":"Students may write a critical review of a book by discussing both its useful ideas and weak evidence.","zh":"學生可能透過討論一本書的有用想法和薄弱證據，撰寫批判性評論。"},{"en":"Critical reviews help a field improve because they question accepted conclusions.","zh":"批判性評論透過質疑已接受結論，幫助領域進步。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious analysis, not simply negative criticism.","zh":"這個短語描述認真分析，而不只是負面批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"forthcoming issue","meaning":"即將出版的一期","examples":[{"en":"The review will appear in a forthcoming issue of the journal.","zh":"該評論將刊登於期刊即將出版的一期。"},{"en":"A forthcoming issue is a future edition of a magazine, journal, or publication.","zh":"forthcoming issue 是雜誌、期刊或刊物未來的一期。"},{"en":"A school article may appear in the forthcoming issue of the student magazine.","zh":"學校文章可能刊登在學生雜誌即將出版的一期中。"},{"en":"This phrase tells readers that something has not been published yet but is expected soon.","zh":"這個短語告訴讀者某物尚未出版，但預計很快出現。"},{"en":"It describes a coming publication.","zh":"它描述即將到來的出版物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"pour cold water over","meaning":"對……潑冷水；質疑","examples":[{"en":"The review pours cold water over claims about innate skills.","zh":"該評論對關於先天能力的聲稱潑冷水。"},{"en":"To pour cold water over a claim means to make it seem less convincing or less exciting by criticising it.","zh":"pour cold water over 某聲稱，指透過批評令它看起來較不可信或較不令人興奮。"},{"en":"A teacher may pour cold water over a shortcut method if it helps students guess but not understand.","zh":"如果捷徑方法只幫學生猜答案而不幫他們理解，老師可能會對它潑冷水。"},{"en":"Evidence can pour cold water over a popular theory when it shows the theory is too simple.","zh":"當證據顯示流行理論太簡單，它可以對該理論潑冷水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strongly questioning or dampening enthusiasm.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈質疑或削弱熱情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"claim to have observed","meaning":"聲稱觀察到","examples":[{"en":"Some experiments claim to have observed innate social cognition skills.","zh":"有些實驗聲稱觀察到先天社會認知能力。"},{"en":"To claim to have observed something means to say that one has seen or measured it.","zh":"claim to have observed 某事，指聲稱自己已看見或量度到它。"},{"en":"A study may claim to have observed better memory after students used a new app.","zh":"一項研究可能聲稱觀察到學生使用新應用程式後記憶力變好。"},{"en":"Claims need evidence because observation can be misread or overinterpreted.","zh":"聲稱需要證據，因為觀察可能被誤讀或過度詮釋。"},{"en":"The phrase reports what researchers say they found.","zh":"這個短語報告研究人員說自己發現了甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"innate skills","meaning":"先天能力","examples":[{"en":"The review questions claims about innate skills in infants.","zh":"該評論質疑關於嬰兒先天能力的聲稱。"},{"en":"Innate skills are abilities believed to be present from birth rather than learned later.","zh":"innate skills 是被認為出生時已存在，而不是後天學得的能力。"},{"en":"A baby’s ability to turn toward a human voice may be discussed as an innate skill.","zh":"嬰兒轉向人聲的能力可能被討論為先天能力。"},{"en":"Whether a skill is innate matters because it changes how scientists explain learning.","zh":"某能力是否先天很重要，因為它改變科學家如何解釋學習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes abilities treated as built in.","zh":"這個短語描述被視為內置的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"precocious social cognition skills","meaning":"早熟的社會認知能力","examples":[{"en":"The experiments claimed to show precocious social cognition skills.","zh":"這些實驗聲稱顯示早熟的社會認知能力。"},{"en":"Precocious social cognition skills are unusually early abilities to understand people or social situations.","zh":"precocious social cognition skills 是異常早出現、理解人物或社會情境的能力。"},{"en":"If a baby seems to know another person’s intention, some may call this precocious social cognition.","zh":"如果嬰兒似乎知道另一個人的意圖，有些人可能稱這為早熟社會認知。"},{"en":"Such claims are controversial because early attention may not mean deep understanding.","zh":"這類聲稱具爭議性，因為早期注意不一定代表深入理解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes social understanding that appears earlier than expected.","zh":"這個短語描述比預期更早出現的社會理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"social cognition","meaning":"社會認知","examples":[{"en":"Social cognition refers to understanding people and social situations.","zh":"社會認知指理解人物和社會情境。"},{"en":"Social cognition is the ability to think about other people’s feelings, intentions, beliefs, and actions.","zh":"social cognition 是思考他人感受、意圖、信念和行動的能力。"},{"en":"A child uses social cognition when she realises a friend is sad even without being told.","zh":"當孩子即使沒有人說也意識到朋友難過，她就在使用社會認知。"},{"en":"Social cognition helps people cooperate, apologise, and predict others’ behaviour.","zh":"社會認知幫助人合作、道歉和預測他人行為。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to mental skills used in social life.","zh":"這個短語指在社交生活中使用的心理能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"indicate that","meaning":"顯示；表明","examples":[{"en":"Sirois’s experiments indicate that babies respond to novelty.","zh":"Sirois 的實驗顯示嬰兒會對新奇事物作出反應。"},{"en":"Indicate that means show or suggest that something is true.","zh":"indicate that 指顯示或暗示某事是真實的。"},{"en":"Falling attendance may indicate that students find the course too difficult.","zh":"出席率下降可能顯示學生覺得課程太難。"},{"en":"Evidence can indicate a pattern without proving every detail completely.","zh":"證據可以顯示一種模式，而不必完全證明每個細節。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces what data seems to show.","zh":"這個短語引出數據似乎顯示的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"fascination with","meaning":"對……着迷","examples":[{"en":"A baby’s fascination with impossible events may reflect novelty.","zh":"嬰兒對不可能事件着迷，可能反映新奇感。"},{"en":"Fascination with something means strong interest in it.","zh":"fascination with 某事，指對它有強烈興趣。"},{"en":"A child’s fascination with insects may lead her to spend hours watching ants.","zh":"孩子對昆蟲着迷，可能令她花幾小時觀察螞蟻。"},{"en":"Fascination often appears when something is unusual, moving, colourful, or surprising.","zh":"當某事不尋常、會動、有色彩或令人驚訝，常會引起着迷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep attraction of attention.","zh":"這個短語描述注意力被深深吸引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"physically impossible events","meaning":"物理上不可能的事件","examples":[{"en":"Babies may look longer at physically impossible events.","zh":"嬰兒可能較久注視物理上不可能的事件。"},{"en":"Physically impossible events are events that seem to break the normal rules of the physical world.","zh":"physically impossible events 是看似違反物理世界正常規則的事件。"},{"en":"A cup floating upward without support would look like a physically impossible event.","zh":"杯子在沒有支撐下向上漂浮，看起來會像物理上不可能的事件。"},{"en":"Such events draw attention because they conflict with ordinary experience.","zh":"這類事件吸引注意，因為它們與普通經驗衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase describes events that should not happen according to physical rules.","zh":"這個短語描述根據物理規則不應發生的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"merely reflect","meaning":"只不過反映","examples":[{"en":"The response may merely reflect interest in novelty.","zh":"這種反應可能只不過反映對新奇事物的興趣。"},{"en":"Merely reflect means only show or indicate something, rather than prove a deeper explanation.","zh":"merely reflect 指只顯示或表明某事，而不是證明更深層解釋。"},{"en":"A student’s silence may merely reflect tiredness, not disagreement.","zh":"學生沉默可能只不過反映疲倦，而不是不同意。"},{"en":"Researchers must be careful because one behaviour may merely reflect attention rather than understanding.","zh":"研究人員必須小心，因為一種行為可能只反映注意力，而不是理解。"},{"en":"The phrase limits the meaning of evidence.","zh":"這個短語限制證據的意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a response to stimuli","meaning":"對刺激的反應","examples":[{"en":"The behaviour may be a response to stimuli that are novel.","zh":"這種行為可能是對新奇刺激的反應。"},{"en":"A response to stimuli is a reaction caused by sights, sounds, touches, or other things that affect the senses.","zh":"response to stimuli 是由景象、聲音、觸感或其他影響感官的事物引起的反應。"},{"en":"A baby turning toward a bell is showing a response to sound stimuli.","zh":"嬰兒轉向鈴聲，就是在顯示對聲音刺激的反應。"},{"en":"Stimuli can change attention, emotion, or movement.","zh":"刺激可以改變注意力、情緒或動作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes behaviour caused by something sensed.","zh":"這個短語描述由感受到的事物引起的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"novel stimuli","meaning":"新奇刺激","examples":[{"en":"Sirois believes babies respond strongly to novel stimuli.","zh":"Sirois 相信嬰兒會強烈回應新奇刺激。"},{"en":"Novel stimuli are new or unfamiliar things that attract attention.","zh":"novel stimuli 是吸引注意的新事物或不熟悉的事物。"},{"en":"A flashing toy may be a novel stimulus for a baby who has never seen lights change.","zh":"對從未見過燈光變化的嬰兒而言，閃燈玩具可能是新奇刺激。"},{"en":"Novel stimuli can make attention rise because the brain notices change.","zh":"新奇刺激可以令注意力上升，因為大腦注意到變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes new sensory information.","zh":"這個短語描述新的感官資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"data from the eye tracker","meaning":"來自眼動追蹤儀的數據","examples":[{"en":"Data from the eye tracker support Sirois’s argument.","zh":"來自眼動追蹤儀的數據支持 Sirois 的論點。"},{"en":"Data from the eye tracker are measurements collected by a device that records eye movement or pupil size.","zh":"data from the eye tracker 是由記錄眼球移動或瞳孔大小的裝置收集的測量資料。"},{"en":"Teachers might use reading software data to see where students pause, just as researchers use data from an eye tracker.","zh":"老師可能使用閱讀軟件數據查看學生在哪裏停頓，就像研究人員使用來自眼動追蹤儀的數據。"},{"en":"Such data help researchers move beyond guessing about attention.","zh":"這類數據幫助研究人員不只靠猜測注意力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to evidence collected by eye-tracking equipment.","zh":"這個短語指由眼動追蹤設備收集的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"measurement of the pupils","meaning":"瞳孔測量","examples":[{"en":"The measurement of the pupils shows levels of interest.","zh":"瞳孔測量顯示興趣水平。"},{"en":"Measurement of the pupils means recording how large the pupils are or how they change.","zh":"measurement of the pupils 指記錄瞳孔大小或其變化。"},{"en":"In a lab, measurement of the pupils can help researchers study attention without asking questions.","zh":"在實驗室中，瞳孔測量可以幫助研究人員不用提問也能研究注意力。"},{"en":"Pupil size may change when a person is interested, excited, or surprised.","zh":"當人感興趣、興奮或驚訝時，瞳孔大小可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using pupil changes as data.","zh":"這個短語描述把瞳孔變化用作數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"widen in response to","meaning":"因應……而擴大","examples":[{"en":"Pupils widen in response to arousal or interest.","zh":"瞳孔會因應喚醒反應或興趣而擴大。"},{"en":"To widen in response to something means to become larger because of that trigger.","zh":"widen in response to 某事，指因該刺激而變大。"},{"en":"A child’s eyes may widen in response to a surprise birthday cake.","zh":"孩子看見驚喜生日蛋糕時，眼睛可能因應驚喜而睜大。"},{"en":"The body can respond automatically before a person can explain the feeling.","zh":"身體可以在一個人能解釋感受前自動作出反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a physical change caused by a stimulus.","zh":"這個短語描述由刺激引起的身體變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"arousal or interest","meaning":"喚醒反應或興趣","examples":[{"en":"Pupils may widen because of arousal or interest.","zh":"瞳孔可能因喚醒反應或興趣而擴大。"},{"en":"Arousal or interest means a state of being mentally alert, excited, curious, or emotionally activated.","zh":"arousal or interest 指心理上警覺、興奮、好奇或情緒被啟動的狀態。"},{"en":"A student may show arousal or interest when a lesson begins with a surprising question.","zh":"當課堂以令人驚訝的問題開始，學生可能表現出喚醒反應或興趣。"},{"en":"These states can make the body react, for example through wider pupils or faster attention.","zh":"這些狀態可以令身體反應，例如瞳孔擴大或注意力加快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mental or emotional activation.","zh":"這個短語描述心理或情緒被啟動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"familiar objects","meaning":"熟悉物件","examples":[{"en":"Impossible events involving familiar objects are not always more interesting.","zh":"涉及熟悉物件的不可能事件不一定更有趣。"},{"en":"Familiar objects are things someone has seen or used before and recognises easily.","zh":"familiar objects 是某人以前看過或用過、容易認出的東西。"},{"en":"A spoon, cup, or favourite toy may be a familiar object for a young child.","zh":"湯匙、杯子或最喜歡的玩具可能是幼兒熟悉的物件。"},{"en":"Familiar objects may attract less attention because the mind already knows what to expect.","zh":"熟悉物件可能吸引較少注意，因為心智已知道該預期甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes objects that are already known.","zh":"這個短語描述已為人所知的物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"possible events","meaning":"可能事件","examples":[{"en":"Possible events involving novel objects can interest babies.","zh":"涉及新奇物件的可能事件可以令嬰兒感興趣。"},{"en":"Possible events are events that can happen according to ordinary physical rules.","zh":"possible events 是按照普通物理規則能夠發生的事件。"},{"en":"A ball rolling down a ramp is a possible event.","zh":"球從斜坡滾下是一個可能事件。"},{"en":"A possible event may still be interesting if it involves something new or surprising.","zh":"如果可能事件涉及新奇或令人驚訝的東西，它仍可能有趣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes events that do not break reality’s normal rules.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有違反現實正常規則的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"novel objects","meaning":"新奇物件","examples":[{"en":"Babies may be interested in possible events involving novel objects.","zh":"嬰兒可能對涉及新奇物件的可能事件感興趣。"},{"en":"Novel objects are new or unfamiliar things that someone has not seen before.","zh":"novel objects 是某人以前未見過的新事物或不熟悉的東西。"},{"en":"A baby may stare at a novel object, such as a shiny new toy, longer than at an old cup.","zh":"嬰兒可能較久注視閃亮新玩具等新奇物件，而不是舊杯子。"},{"en":"Novel objects attract attention because the brain has no settled expectation about them.","zh":"新奇物件吸引注意，因為大腦對它們沒有固定預期。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unfamiliar things that feel new.","zh":"這個短語描述感覺新鮮的不熟悉物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in other words","meaning":"換句話說","examples":[{"en":"In other words, novelty may matter more than impossibility.","zh":"換句話說，新奇可能比不可能性更重要。"},{"en":"In other words introduces the same idea again in a clearer or simpler way.","zh":"in other words 用更清楚或更簡單的方式再次引出同一想法。"},{"en":"The task is optional; in other words, students may choose not to do it.","zh":"任務是可選的；換句話說，學生可以選擇不做。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to restate a point so readers understand it better.","zh":"作者使用這個短語重述觀點，讓讀者更好理解。"},{"en":"The phrase signals clarification or rephrasing.","zh":"這個短語表示澄清或換個說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"stay the same colour","meaning":"保持同一顏色","examples":[{"en":"The train sometimes stayed the same colour after leaving the tunnel.","zh":"火車有時離開隧道後保持同一顏色。"},{"en":"To stay the same colour means to remain unchanged in colour.","zh":"stay the same colour 指顏色保持不變。"},{"en":"A toy car may go through a cardboard tunnel and stay the same colour when it comes out.","zh":"玩具車穿過紙板隧道後，出來時可能保持同一顏色。"},{"en":"If an object stays the same colour, it follows the expected pattern.","zh":"如果物件保持同一顏色，它就符合預期模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes no change in colour.","zh":"這個短語描述顏色沒有變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"leap to the conclusion that","meaning":"貿然得出結論認為","examples":[{"en":"Previous researchers may have leapt to the conclusion that babies understand impossibility.","zh":"以往研究人員可能貿然得出結論認為嬰兒理解不可能性。"},{"en":"To leap to the conclusion that means to decide something too quickly without enough evidence.","zh":"leap to the conclusion that 指在證據不足下太快作出判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher should not leap to the conclusion that a student copied just because two answers look similar.","zh":"老師不應只因兩個答案相似，就貿然得出結論認為學生抄襲。"},{"en":"Jumping too quickly from observation to explanation can create mistakes.","zh":"從觀察太快跳到解釋可能造成錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against hasty reasoning.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要倉促推理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"understand the concept of","meaning":"理解……的概念","examples":[{"en":"The research asks whether babies understand the concept of impossibility.","zh":"該研究問嬰兒是否理解不可能性的概念。"},{"en":"To understand the concept of something means to grasp the idea behind it, not just notice it.","zh":"understand the concept of 某事，指掌握其背後想法，而不只是注意到它。"},{"en":"A student may use division but not fully understand the concept of sharing into equal groups.","zh":"學生可能會做除法，但未完全理解平均分組的概念。"},{"en":"Understanding a concept is deeper than reacting to a single example.","zh":"理解概念比對單一例子作反應更深入。"},{"en":"The phrase describes real mental understanding of an idea.","zh":"這個短語描述對想法的真正心理理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"impossibility","meaning":"不可能性","examples":[{"en":"Sirois doubts that babies understand impossibility.","zh":"Sirois 懷疑嬰兒理解不可能性。"},{"en":"Impossibility is the idea that something cannot happen under normal rules.","zh":"impossibility 是某事在正常規則下不能發生的概念。"},{"en":"A child begins to understand impossibility when she knows a person cannot walk through a wall.","zh":"當孩子知道人不能穿過牆，她開始理解不可能性。"},{"en":"Noticing something strange is not the same as understanding impossibility.","zh":"注意到某事奇怪，不等於理解不可能性。"},{"en":"The word refers to the state of being impossible.","zh":"這個詞指不可能的狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the mere fact that","meaning":"僅僅因為……這一事實","examples":[{"en":"Researchers should not infer understanding from the mere fact that babies notice novelty.","zh":"研究人員不應僅僅因為嬰兒注意到新奇之處這一事實，就推斷他們有理解。"},{"en":"The mere fact that means only the simple fact that, without extra evidence.","zh":"the mere fact that 指僅僅某個簡單事實，而沒有額外證據。"},{"en":"The mere fact that a student is quiet does not mean she is not interested.","zh":"僅僅因為學生安靜這一事實，並不代表她沒有興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase warns readers not to overinterpret one observation.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者不要過度詮釋單一觀察。"},{"en":"It separates a basic fact from a stronger conclusion.","zh":"它把基本事實與更強結論分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"perceive novelty","meaning":"察覺新奇之處","examples":[{"en":"Babies are able to perceive novelty in an event.","zh":"嬰兒能夠察覺事件中的新奇之處。"},{"en":"To perceive novelty means to notice that something is new, different, or unfamiliar.","zh":"perceive novelty 指注意到某事是新的、不同的或不熟悉的。"},{"en":"A child may perceive novelty when a familiar classroom suddenly has new posters.","zh":"當熟悉課室突然有新海報，孩子可能察覺新奇之處。"},{"en":"Perceiving novelty can increase attention even without deep understanding.","zh":"察覺新奇之處可以增加注意力，即使沒有深入理解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes noticing newness.","zh":"這個短語描述注意到新鮮感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"bridge the gap between","meaning":"彌合……之間的差距","examples":[{"en":"Sirois asks how babies bridge the gap between knowing nothing and drawing shapes.","zh":"Sirois 問嬰兒如何彌合一無所知與畫出形狀之間的差距。"},{"en":"To bridge the gap between two things means to reduce the distance or difference between them.","zh":"bridge the gap between 兩事物，指縮小它們之間的距離或差異。"},{"en":"Extra tutoring can bridge the gap between weak grammar and confident writing.","zh":"額外補習可以彌合薄弱文法與自信寫作之間的差距。"},{"en":"Learning happens when small steps connect a starting point to a more advanced ability.","zh":"當小步驟把起點與較高能力連起來，學習就會發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes connecting two different stages or levels.","zh":"這個短語描述連接兩個不同階段或水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"knowing squat","meaning":"一無所知","examples":[{"en":"Sirois describes babies as starting from knowing squat.","zh":"Sirois 形容嬰兒從一無所知開始。"},{"en":"Knowing squat means knowing nothing at all.","zh":"knowing squat 指完全不知道任何東西。"},{"en":"A student may know squat about cooking before learning how to boil an egg.","zh":"學生在學會煮雞蛋前，可能對烹飪一無所知。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and emphasises a complete lack of knowledge.","zh":"這個短語較口語，強調完全缺乏知識。"},{"en":"It is stronger and more casual than saying “knowing very little”.","zh":"它比 “knowing very little” 更強烈、更隨意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"draw triangles","meaning":"畫三角形","examples":[{"en":"Daniel’s sister is happily drawing triangles.","zh":"Daniel 的姐姐正開心地畫三角形。"},{"en":"To draw triangles means to make three-sided shapes on paper or another surface.","zh":"draw triangles 指在紙上或其他表面畫出三邊形。"},{"en":"A child may draw triangles when learning basic shapes in kindergarten.","zh":"孩子在幼稚園學習基本形狀時，可能畫三角形。"},{"en":"Drawing shapes shows that a child can control movement and recognise simple forms.","zh":"畫形狀顯示孩子能控制動作並辨認簡單形態。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a basic early drawing task.","zh":"這個短語描述基本的早期繪畫任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"tackle a task","meaning":"處理一項任務","examples":[{"en":"Lois is happily tackling the task of drawing triangles.","zh":"Lois 正開心地處理畫三角形這項任務。"},{"en":"To tackle a task means to start working on it and try to deal with it.","zh":"tackle a task 指開始做某任務並嘗試處理它。"},{"en":"A student may tackle a difficult essay by first writing a simple outline.","zh":"學生可能先寫簡單大綱來處理一篇困難文章。"},{"en":"Breaking a task into smaller steps can make it easier to tackle.","zh":"把任務拆成較小步驟，可以令它較容易處理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes actively dealing with work or a challenge.","zh":"這個短語描述主動處理工作或挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"learn everything","meaning":"學習一切","examples":[{"en":"Sirois believes babies have to learn everything.","zh":"Sirois 相信嬰兒必須學習一切。"},{"en":"To learn everything means to acquire all knowledge and skills through learning rather than having them built in.","zh":"learn everything 指所有知識和技能都要透過學習獲得，而不是天生內置。"},{"en":"A beginner in a new country may feel she has to learn everything, from transport rules to local speech.","zh":"初到新國家的人可能覺得自己要學習一切，由交通規則到本地說話方式。"},{"en":"If babies must learn everything, experience becomes the starting point of development.","zh":"如果嬰兒必須學習一切，經驗就成為發展的起點。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises learning from the ground up.","zh":"這個短語強調從零開始學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"start with","meaning":"從……開始","examples":[{"en":"Babies start with a few primitive reflexes.","zh":"嬰兒從幾種原始反射開始。"},{"en":"To start with something means to begin from that point, resource, or ability.","zh":"start with 某物，指從該點、資源或能力開始。"},{"en":"A new English learner may start with simple greetings before learning long sentences.","zh":"新英語學習者可能先從簡單問候語開始，再學長句。"},{"en":"What people start with affects how they build later skills.","zh":"人們以甚麼開始，會影響他們如何建立後來技能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the beginning point of a process.","zh":"這個短語描述一個過程的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"primitive reflexes","meaning":"原始反射","examples":[{"en":"Babies start with a few primitive reflexes.","zh":"嬰兒從幾種原始反射開始。"},{"en":"Primitive reflexes are automatic early reactions babies show without learning them.","zh":"primitive reflexes 是嬰兒不用學習便會表現出的早期自動反應。"},{"en":"A newborn may suck when something touches the mouth because of a primitive reflex.","zh":"新生兒嘴巴被觸碰時可能會吸吮，這是因為原始反射。"},{"en":"These reflexes help babies survive and begin interacting with the world.","zh":"這些反射幫助嬰兒生存並開始與世界互動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes simple built-in bodily responses.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單的內置身體反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"get things going","meaning":"啟動整個過程","examples":[{"en":"Primitive reflexes get the learning process going.","zh":"原始反射啟動整個學習過程。"},{"en":"To get things going means to start a process or make it begin moving.","zh":"get things going 指開始一個過程或令它運作起來。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask an easy question to get discussion going.","zh":"老師可能問一條簡單問題來啟動討論。"},{"en":"Small first steps can get learning going before harder tasks appear.","zh":"小小的第一步可以在較難任務出現前啟動學習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes starting momentum.","zh":"這個短語描述開始推動事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be hardwired in the brain","meaning":"天生固定在腦內","examples":[{"en":"An instinct to look at faces is hardwired in the brain.","zh":"看人臉的本能天生固定在腦內。"},{"en":"To be hardwired in the brain means to be built into the brain naturally rather than learned later.","zh":"be hardwired in the brain 指自然內置於大腦中，而不是後天學得。"},{"en":"Some fear responses may be hardwired in the brain to protect people from danger.","zh":"有些恐懼反應可能天生固定在腦內，用來保護人免受危險。"},{"en":"If a behaviour is hardwired, it appears early and automatically.","zh":"如果某行為是內置的，它會早期且自動地出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an inborn mental tendency.","zh":"這個短語描述先天心理傾向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"instinct","meaning":"本能","examples":[{"en":"The brain has an instinct that draws a baby’s eyes to a human face.","zh":"大腦有一種本能，會把嬰兒的目光吸引到人臉上。"},{"en":"An instinct is a natural tendency to behave in a certain way without being taught.","zh":"instinct 是不用被教導便自然以某方式行動的傾向。"},{"en":"A newborn’s instinct to suck helps the baby feed.","zh":"新生兒吸吮的本能幫助嬰兒進食。"},{"en":"Instincts can guide early behaviour before a person understands the reason.","zh":"本能可以在一個人理解原因前引導早期行為。"},{"en":"The word describes natural, automatic behaviour.","zh":"這個詞描述自然、自動的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"draw someone’s eyes to","meaning":"吸引某人的目光到……","examples":[{"en":"An instinct draws a baby’s eyes to a human face.","zh":"一種本能把嬰兒的目光吸引到人臉上。"},{"en":"To draw someone’s eyes to something means to attract their attention visually.","zh":"draw someone’s eyes to 某物，指以視覺方式吸引某人的注意。"},{"en":"A bright poster may draw students’ eyes to an important announcement.","zh":"鮮艷海報可能把學生的目光吸引到重要公告上。"},{"en":"Movement, colour, and faces often draw the eyes because they stand out.","zh":"動作、顏色和人臉常吸引目光，因為它們突出。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something pulling visual attention toward it.","zh":"這個短語描述某物把視覺注意力拉向自己。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"human face","meaning":"人臉","examples":[{"en":"Babies are naturally drawn to a human face.","zh":"嬰兒自然被人臉吸引。"},{"en":"A human face is the front part of a person’s head, including the eyes, nose, mouth, and expression.","zh":"human face 是人的頭部前方部分，包括眼睛、鼻子、嘴和表情。"},{"en":"A baby may calm down when she sees a familiar human face.","zh":"嬰兒看到熟悉的人臉時，可能會平靜下來。"},{"en":"Faces carry important social information, such as emotion and attention.","zh":"人臉承載重要社交資訊，例如情緒和注意力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to one of the earliest and most important visual objects for babies.","zh":"這個短語指嬰兒最早和最重要的視覺物件之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"brain imaging studies","meaning":"腦成像研究","examples":[{"en":"Brain imaging studies show that the brain has a visual buffer.","zh":"腦成像研究顯示，大腦有視覺緩衝區。"},{"en":"Brain imaging studies are research studies that use technology to see or measure activity in the brain.","zh":"brain imaging studies 是使用科技觀察或量度大腦活動的研究。"},{"en":"Doctors may use brain imaging studies to understand which areas are affected after injury.","zh":"醫生可能使用腦成像研究，了解受傷後哪些區域受到影響。"},{"en":"These studies help scientists connect behaviour with brain activity.","zh":"這些研究幫助科學家把行為與大腦活動連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research using images or scans of the brain.","zh":"這個短語描述使用大腦影像或掃描的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"visual buffer","meaning":"視覺緩衝區","examples":[{"en":"The brain has a visual buffer that represents objects briefly.","zh":"大腦有一個短暫表徵物件的視覺緩衝區。"},{"en":"A visual buffer is a short-term mental store that keeps visual information for a brief moment.","zh":"visual buffer 是短暫保存視覺資訊的短期心理儲存區。"},{"en":"When a moving light disappears, a visual buffer may help the brain hold its image briefly.","zh":"當移動燈光消失，視覺緩衝區可能幫助大腦短暫保留其影像。"},{"en":"This buffer can make something feel present for a short time after it is gone.","zh":"這個緩衝區可以令某物在消失後短時間內仍感覺存在。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a temporary holding space for visual information.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺資訊的暫時保存空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"continue to represent","meaning":"繼續表徵","examples":[{"en":"The brain continues to represent objects after they disappear.","zh":"物件消失後，大腦繼續表徵它們。"},{"en":"To continue to represent something means to keep holding or showing a mental image of it.","zh":"continue to represent 某物，指繼續保留或呈現其心理影像。"},{"en":"After a bus passes, a child may briefly continue to represent its movement in the mind.","zh":"巴士經過後，孩子可能在腦中短暫繼續表徵其移動。"},{"en":"This short continuation helps the brain connect one moment with the next.","zh":"這種短暫延續幫助大腦把前後時刻連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mental representation lasting after the object is gone.","zh":"這個短語描述物件消失後心理表徵仍持續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be removed","meaning":"被移走","examples":[{"en":"The object is still represented after it has been removed.","zh":"物件被移走後仍被表徵。"},{"en":"To be removed means to be taken away from its place.","zh":"be removed 指從原來位置被拿走。"},{"en":"A toy may be removed from a baby’s tray during an experiment.","zh":"在實驗中，玩具可能從嬰兒托盤上被移走。"},{"en":"When something is removed, researchers can test whether the child still reacts as if it exists.","zh":"當某物被移走，研究人員可以測試孩子是否仍像它存在一樣作出反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an object being taken away.","zh":"這個短語描述物件被拿走。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"lingering perception","meaning":"殘留的知覺","examples":[{"en":"The effect is a lingering perception rather than true understanding.","zh":"這種效果是殘留的知覺，而不是真正理解。"},{"en":"Lingering perception is a sensory impression that remains briefly after the original object or event is gone.","zh":"lingering perception 是原本物件或事件消失後短暫留下的感官印象。"},{"en":"A bright light may leave a lingering perception after you close your eyes.","zh":"當你閉上眼睛後，強光可能留下殘留的知覺。"},{"en":"Lingering perception can look like knowledge, but it may only be a short sensory trace.","zh":"殘留知覺可能看似知識，但它可能只是短暫感官痕跡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a remaining impression, not deep understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述殘留印象，而不是深層理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"The buffer involves lingering perception rather than conceptual understanding.","zh":"該緩衝區涉及殘留知覺，而不是概念理解。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of, showing a contrast between two possibilities.","zh":"rather than 指而不是，用來顯示兩種可能性之間的對比。"},{"en":"A student may need real practice rather than only reading grammar rules.","zh":"學生可能需要真正練習，而不是只閱讀文法規則。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate what something is from what it is not.","zh":"這個短語幫助分清某事是甚麼和不是甚麼。"},{"en":"It is useful when the writer wants to correct a possible misunderstanding.","zh":"當作者想修正可能的誤解時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"conceptual understanding","meaning":"概念理解","examples":[{"en":"Sirois distinguishes perception from conceptual understanding.","zh":"Sirois 區分知覺和概念理解。"},{"en":"Conceptual understanding is deep understanding of the idea or rule behind something.","zh":"conceptual understanding 是對某事背後想法或規則的深入理解。"},{"en":"A student has conceptual understanding of fractions when she knows why one half equals two quarters.","zh":"當學生知道為何二分之一等於四分之二，她就有分數的概念理解。"},{"en":"Conceptual understanding is stronger than memorising an answer or noticing a pattern.","zh":"概念理解比記答案或注意到模式更強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes real grasp of meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述真正掌握意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"encounter novel events","meaning":"遇到新奇事件","examples":[{"en":"Babies pay attention when they encounter novel events.","zh":"嬰兒遇到新奇事件時會注意。"},{"en":"To encounter novel events means to come across new or unfamiliar happenings.","zh":"encounter novel events 指遇到新的或不熟悉的事情。"},{"en":"A child may encounter novel events on the first day of school, such as lining up for assembly.","zh":"孩子在開學第一天可能遇到新奇事件，例如排隊參加早會。"},{"en":"New events can increase attention because the mind has not yet learned what to expect.","zh":"新事件可以提高注意力，因為心智尚未學會該預期甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes meeting new experiences.","zh":"這個短語描述遇到新經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"unexpected events","meaning":"出乎意料的事件","examples":[{"en":"Unexpected events create a mismatch in the baby’s mind.","zh":"出乎意料的事件在嬰兒心中造成不匹配。"},{"en":"Unexpected events are things that happen differently from what someone expected.","zh":"unexpected events 是以不同於某人預期的方式發生的事情。"},{"en":"A fire alarm during a quiet lesson is an unexpected event.","zh":"安靜課堂中突然響起火警鐘，是出乎意料的事件。"},{"en":"Unexpected events attract attention because people try to understand why they happened.","zh":"出乎意料的事件吸引注意，因為人們嘗試理解它們為何發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes happenings that break prediction.","zh":"這個短語描述打破預測的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a mismatch between","meaning":"……之間的不匹配","examples":[{"en":"There is a mismatch between the buffer and the new information.","zh":"緩衝區與新資訊之間存在不匹配。"},{"en":"A mismatch between two things is a difference or conflict that prevents them from fitting together.","zh":"mismatch between 兩事物，是令它們不能配合的差異或衝突。"},{"en":"A mismatch between a student’s level and the textbook can make lessons too hard.","zh":"學生水平與教科書之間的不匹配，可以令課堂太難。"},{"en":"When there is a mismatch, the mind or system must adjust.","zh":"當出現不匹配，心智或系統必須調整。"},{"en":"The phrase describes two things not matching properly.","zh":"這個短語描述兩事物未能妥善配合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"at that moment","meaning":"在那一刻","examples":[{"en":"The baby receives new information at that moment.","zh":"嬰兒在那一刻接收新資訊。"},{"en":"At that moment means exactly then, at that specific point in time.","zh":"at that moment 指正正在那個特定時間點。"},{"en":"A student may suddenly understand a grammar rule at that moment when the teacher gives a clear example.","zh":"當老師給出清楚例子時，學生可能在那一刻突然理解文法規則。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the timing of an event or change.","zh":"這個短語突出事件或變化的時間。"},{"en":"It points to a precise instant in a sequence.","zh":"它指出一連串事件中的準確瞬間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"clear the buffer","meaning":"清空緩衝區","examples":[{"en":"The brain tries to clear the buffer when there is a mismatch.","zh":"當出現不匹配時，大腦嘗試清空緩衝區。"},{"en":"To clear the buffer means to remove old temporary information so new information can be processed.","zh":"clear the buffer 指移除舊的暫時資訊，讓新資訊可以被處理。"},{"en":"A computer clears temporary memory when it needs space for a new task.","zh":"電腦需要空間處理新任務時，會清空暫時記憶。"},{"en":"Clearing the buffer helps the brain deal with conflict between old and new information.","zh":"清空緩衝區幫助大腦處理舊資訊和新資訊之間的衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase describes removing short-term stored information.","zh":"這個短語描述移除短期儲存資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"take attention","meaning":"需要注意力","examples":[{"en":"Clearing the buffer takes attention.","zh":"清空緩衝區需要注意力。"},{"en":"To take attention means to require mental focus or use up attention.","zh":"take attention 指需要心理專注或消耗注意力。"},{"en":"Solving a new puzzle takes attention because the answer is not automatic.","zh":"解新的謎題需要注意力，因為答案不是自動出現的。"},{"en":"If a task takes too much attention, a person may ignore other things nearby.","zh":"如果一項任務需要太多注意力，人可能忽略附近其他事物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mental effort being needed.","zh":"這個短語描述需要心理努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"essentially","meaning":"本質上","examples":[{"en":"Learning is essentially the work of resolving mismatches.","zh":"學習本質上是解決不匹配的工作。"},{"en":"Essentially means basically or at its most important level.","zh":"essentially 指基本上，或在最重要層面上。"},{"en":"Good revision is essentially repeated practice with honest checking.","zh":"良好溫習本質上是反覆練習加上誠實檢查。"},{"en":"The word helps reduce a complex idea to its main point.","zh":"這個詞幫助把複雜想法縮減至主要重點。"},{"en":"It signals the core meaning of an explanation.","zh":"它表示一項解釋的核心意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the laborious business of","meaning":"費力的……過程","examples":[{"en":"Learning is the laborious business of resolving mismatches.","zh":"學習是解決不匹配這個費力的過程。"},{"en":"The laborious business of doing something means the slow, difficult, and effortful process of doing it.","zh":"laborious business of doing something 指做某事緩慢、困難且費力的過程。"},{"en":"Writing a good essay is the laborious business of planning, drafting, correcting, and rewriting.","zh":"寫好文章是規劃、起草、修正和重寫這個費力的過程。"},{"en":"Important learning often feels laborious because mistakes must be found and fixed.","zh":"重要學習常感覺費力，因為錯誤必須被找出並修正。"},{"en":"The phrase describes work that is demanding but necessary.","zh":"這個短語描述辛苦但必要的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"resolve mismatches","meaning":"解決不匹配","examples":[{"en":"Babies learn by resolving mismatches.","zh":"嬰兒透過解決不匹配來學習。"},{"en":"To resolve mismatches means to deal with differences between what is expected and what actually happens.","zh":"resolve mismatches 指處理預期與實際發生事情之間的差異。"},{"en":"A student resolves a mismatch when she realises her answer does not fit the passage and changes it.","zh":"當學生意識到自己的答案不符合文章並修改它，她就在解決不匹配。"},{"en":"Resolving mismatches helps the brain update old expectations.","zh":"解決不匹配幫助大腦更新舊預期。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fixing conflicts between ideas or information.","zh":"這個短語描述修正想法或資訊之間的衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a statistical-learning machine","meaning":"統計學習機器","examples":[{"en":"Sirois describes the brain as a statistical-learning machine.","zh":"Sirois 把大腦描述為統計學習機器。"},{"en":"A statistical-learning machine is a system that learns patterns by noticing how often things happen together.","zh":"statistical-learning machine 是透過注意事物多常一起發生來學習模式的系統。"},{"en":"A child may learn word order like a statistical-learning machine by hearing many sentences repeatedly.","zh":"孩子可能像統計學習機器一樣，透過反覆聽許多句子來學習詞序。"},{"en":"Repeated patterns help the brain predict what is likely to happen next.","zh":"重複模式幫助大腦預測接下來可能發生甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the brain as a pattern-learning system.","zh":"這個短語把大腦描述為學習模式的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"with the experiment over","meaning":"實驗結束後","examples":[{"en":"With the experiment over, Daniel picks up a plastic tiger.","zh":"實驗結束後，Daniel 拿起一隻膠老虎。"},{"en":"With the experiment over means after the experiment has finished.","zh":"with the experiment over 指在實驗完成之後。"},{"en":"With the lesson over, students began packing their bags.","zh":"課堂結束後，學生開始收拾書包。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a change from the main activity to what happens afterward.","zh":"這個短語標示由主要活動轉到之後發生的事。"},{"en":"It helps show the timing of the next action.","zh":"它幫助顯示下一個行動的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"chew thoughtfully on","meaning":"若有所思地咬着……","examples":[{"en":"Daniel chews thoughtfully on the tiger’s head.","zh":"Daniel 若有所思地咬着老虎的頭。"},{"en":"To chew thoughtfully on something means to bite or mouth it while appearing calm or reflective.","zh":"chew thoughtfully on 某物，指咬着或含着它，同時看起來平靜或像在思考。"},{"en":"A toddler may chew thoughtfully on a soft toy while watching adults talk.","zh":"幼兒可能一邊看成人說話，一邊若有所思地咬着軟玩具。"},{"en":"The phrase can suggest that the child looks as if he is thinking, even if he is simply exploring by mouth.","zh":"這個短語可以暗示孩子看似在思考，即使他其實只是用嘴探索。"},{"en":"It describes a physical action with a thoughtful-looking manner.","zh":"它描述帶有若有所思神態的身體動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"as if to agree","meaning":"彷彿表示同意","examples":[{"en":"Daniel smiles as if to agree with Sirois.","zh":"Daniel 微笑，彷彿表示同意 Sirois。"},{"en":"As if to agree means in a way that makes it seem someone is agreeing, though this may not be literally true.","zh":"as if to agree 指以看似同意的方式，雖然這未必真的字面成立。"},{"en":"A dog may wag its tail as if to agree when its owner says it is time for a walk.","zh":"當主人說是時候散步，狗可能搖尾巴，彷彿表示同意。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase playfully when behaviour appears to match a statement.","zh":"當行為看似配合一句話，作者會以玩味方式使用這個短語。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an appearance of agreement.","zh":"這個短語描述看起來像同意的表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與資料一致","examples":[{"en":"The statements may agree with the information in the passage.","zh":"這些陳述可能與文章中的資料一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the information means match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information 指符合文章所說的內容。"},{"en":"A statement agrees with the information only if the text clearly supports it.","zh":"只有文本清楚支持，陳述才算與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should check the exact lines before deciding that an answer agrees.","zh":"學生在判斷答案一致前，應檢查準確行句。"},{"en":"The phrase describes consistency between a statement and the passage.","zh":"這個短語描述陳述與文章之間的一致性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the information in the passage.","zh":"一項陳述可能與文章中的資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章內容相反的東西。"},{"en":"If the passage says Daniel cried, a statement saying he stayed calm contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說 Daniel 哭了，而陳述說他保持平靜，這就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction is different from missing information because the text clearly goes against the statement.","zh":"矛盾不同於資料缺失，因為文本清楚反對該陳述。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a direct conflict with the passage.","zh":"這個短語描述與文章直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Readers should choose this option when the passage gives no information on the point.","zh":"當文章對該點沒有相關資料，讀者應選擇這個選項。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有說明該陳述是真是假。"},{"en":"If a text describes a baby’s crying but not his favourite food, there is no information on the food.","zh":"如果文本描述嬰兒哭泣，但沒有提到他最喜歡的食物，就是沒有關於食物的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from common sense when the text gives no evidence.","zh":"當文本沒有證據時，學生不應靠常識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the logic of a Not Given answer.","zh":"這個短語解釋 Not Given 答案的邏輯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"answer sheet","meaning":"答題紙","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write their answers on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生把答案寫在答題紙上。"},{"en":"An answer sheet is the paper or form where exam candidates record their final answers.","zh":"answer sheet 是考生記錄最終答案的紙張或表格。"},{"en":"Students should copy answers carefully onto the answer sheet before time ends.","zh":"學生應在時間結束前小心把答案抄到答題紙上。"},{"en":"A correct answer in the question booklet may not count if it is missing from the answer sheet.","zh":"即使答案在題目冊上正確，如果沒有寫在答題紙上，也可能不計分。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the official place for exam answers.","zh":"這個短語指考試答案的官方位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"after being left alone","meaning":"被獨自留下後","examples":[{"en":"A baby’s behaviour after being left alone can be distressing.","zh":"嬰兒被獨自留下後的行為可能令人心痛。"},{"en":"After being left alone means following a period when no familiar person is nearby.","zh":"after being left alone 指在身邊沒有熟悉的人一段時間之後。"},{"en":"A toddler may cry after being left alone in a playroom for a few minutes.","zh":"幼兒被獨自留在遊戲室幾分鐘後可能會哭。"},{"en":"Separation can change behaviour because young children depend on adults for comfort.","zh":"分離可以改變行為，因為年幼孩子依賴成人提供安慰。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what happens after isolation or separation.","zh":"這個短語描述孤立或分離之後發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"not surprising","meaning":"不令人意外","examples":[{"en":"A baby’s distress in this situation is not surprising.","zh":"嬰兒在這種情況下痛苦並不令人意外。"},{"en":"Not surprising means expected or easy to understand in the situation.","zh":"not surprising 指在該情況中是預期之內或容易理解的。"},{"en":"It is not surprising that students feel tired after three exams in one day.","zh":"學生一天內考三個試後感到疲倦，並不令人意外。"},{"en":"A reaction is not surprising when the cause is clear and common.","zh":"當原因清楚且常見，某反應就不令人意外。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that should not shock the reader.","zh":"這個短語描述不應令讀者震驚的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"overestimate what babies know","meaning":"高估嬰兒所知道的事","examples":[{"en":"Some people may overestimate what babies know.","zh":"有些人可能高估嬰兒所知道的事。"},{"en":"To overestimate what babies know means to believe babies understand more than they really do.","zh":"overestimate what babies know 指相信嬰兒理解的東西比實際更多。"},{"en":"Parents may overestimate what a baby knows if they treat every smile as a deliberate message.","zh":"如果父母把每個微笑都視為有意識的信息，可能會高估嬰兒所知道的事。"},{"en":"Overestimation can lead adults to interpret simple attention as complex understanding.","zh":"高估可以令成人把簡單注意力解讀成複雜理解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes judging babies’ knowledge as greater than it is.","zh":"這個短語描述把嬰兒知識判斷得過高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"current theories about","meaning":"關於……的現有理論","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses current theories about infant knowledge.","zh":"文章討論關於嬰兒知識的現有理論。"},{"en":"Current theories about a topic are the explanations that researchers are discussing or accepting now.","zh":"current theories about 某主題，是研究人員目前正在討論或接受的解釋。"},{"en":"Current theories about sleep suggest that rest affects memory and mood.","zh":"關於睡眠的現有理論指出，休息會影響記憶和心情。"},{"en":"Theories can change when new experiments challenge old ideas.","zh":"當新實驗挑戰舊想法，理論可以改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to modern explanations in a field.","zh":"這個短語指某領域中的現代解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"infant knowledge","meaning":"嬰兒知識","examples":[{"en":"The article examines theories about infant knowledge.","zh":"文章檢視關於嬰兒知識的理論。"},{"en":"Infant knowledge means what babies know or understand about people, objects, and the world.","zh":"infant knowledge 指嬰兒對人、物件和世界所知道或理解的東西。"},{"en":"Researchers study infant knowledge by watching babies’ eyes, movements, and reactions.","zh":"研究人員透過觀察嬰兒的眼睛、動作和反應來研究嬰兒知識。"},{"en":"Because babies cannot explain themselves, infant knowledge is difficult to measure directly.","zh":"因為嬰兒不能解釋自己，嬰兒知識很難直接量度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes babies’ early understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述嬰兒的早期理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"infant cognition","meaning":"嬰兒認知","examples":[{"en":"Sirois’s conclusion concerns infant cognition.","zh":"Sirois 的結論涉及嬰兒認知。"},{"en":"Infant cognition is the study or process of how babies think, learn, notice, and remember.","zh":"infant cognition 是研究或指嬰兒如何思考、學習、注意和記憶的過程。"},{"en":"Eye-tracking experiments can help scientists study infant cognition.","zh":"眼動追蹤實驗可以幫助科學家研究嬰兒認知。"},{"en":"Infant cognition is difficult to study because babies cannot answer questions in words.","zh":"嬰兒認知難以研究，因為嬰兒不能用語言回答問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to babies’ mental processes.","zh":"這個短語指嬰兒的心理過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"serious flaws","meaning":"嚴重缺陷","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Sirois found serious flaws in earlier experiments.","zh":"題目問 Sirois 是否在早期實驗中發現嚴重缺陷。"},{"en":"Serious flaws are important mistakes or weaknesses that can affect the reliability of a result.","zh":"serious flaws 是可以影響結果可靠性的重要錯誤或弱點。"},{"en":"A survey has serious flaws if it asks only five people and then claims to represent the whole school.","zh":"如果問卷只問五個人，卻聲稱代表全校，它就有嚴重缺陷。"},{"en":"Serious flaws can make conclusions doubtful even if the topic is interesting.","zh":"即使題目有趣，嚴重缺陷仍可以令結論可疑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes problems that matter, not small imperfections.","zh":"這個短語描述重要問題，而不是小瑕疵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"experiments conducted by","meaning":"由……進行的實驗","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes experiments conducted by Baillargeon and Spelke.","zh":"文章描述由 Baillargeon 和 Spelke 進行的實驗。"},{"en":"Experiments conducted by someone are studies carried out by that person or research team.","zh":"experiments conducted by 某人，是由該人或研究團隊進行的研究。"},{"en":"Experiments conducted by university scientists may test how students remember new words.","zh":"由大學科學家進行的實驗可能測試學生如何記住新詞。"},{"en":"Naming who conducted the experiments helps readers know the source of the findings.","zh":"說明誰進行實驗，幫助讀者知道發現的來源。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the researchers responsible for the study.","zh":"這個短語指出負責研究的研究人員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"complete each sentence","meaning":"完成每個句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete each sentence with the correct ending.","zh":"考生用正確句尾完成每個句子。"},{"en":"Complete each sentence means fill in the missing part so the sentence becomes whole and meaningful.","zh":"complete each sentence 指填入缺失部分，使句子完整且有意思。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete each sentence by matching it with information from the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過把句子與文章資料配對來完成每個句子。"},{"en":"Checking grammar helps students choose an ending that fits both meaning and structure.","zh":"檢查文法幫助學生選擇同時符合意思和結構的句尾。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the correct ending","meaning":"正確句尾","examples":[{"en":"Each sentence should be matched with the correct ending.","zh":"每個句子應與正確句尾配對。"},{"en":"The correct ending is the sentence part that completes the meaning accurately.","zh":"correct ending 是準確完成意思的句子部分。"},{"en":"A student should choose the correct ending by checking which option matches the passage.","zh":"學生應透過檢查哪個選項符合文章，選擇正確句尾。"},{"en":"The wrong ending may sound grammatically possible but change the meaning.","zh":"錯誤句尾可能文法上看似可以，但會改變意思。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the right completion for a sentence.","zh":"這個短語指句子的正確補全部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"before they are born","meaning":"在出生之前","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists think babies have certain abilities before they are born.","zh":"有些科學家認為嬰兒在出生之前已有某些能力。"},{"en":"Before they are born means during the period before birth, while still in the womb.","zh":"before they are born 指出生前，仍在子宮中的時期。"},{"en":"Babies may respond to familiar voices before they are born.","zh":"嬰兒在出生之前可能會對熟悉聲音作出反應。"},{"en":"If an ability appears before birth, scientists may discuss whether it is innate.","zh":"如果能力在出生前出現，科學家可能討論它是否先天。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the prenatal period.","zh":"這個短語描述產前時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"learn from experience","meaning":"從經驗中學習","examples":[{"en":"Piaget believed babies learn from experience.","zh":"Piaget 相信嬰兒從經驗中學習。"},{"en":"To learn from experience means to gain knowledge by going through events directly.","zh":"learn from experience 指透過直接經歷事件來獲得知識。"},{"en":"A child learns from experience that touching a hot bowl can hurt.","zh":"孩子從經驗中學會觸摸熱碗會痛。"},{"en":"Experience helps children connect actions with results.","zh":"經驗幫助孩子把行動與結果連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning through real life rather than being told only.","zh":"這個短語描述透過真實生活，而不只是被告知來學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"after they have seen the same thing for a while","meaning":"在看同一樣東西一段時間後","examples":[{"en":"A baby’s attention may drop after they have seen the same thing for a while.","zh":"嬰兒在看同一樣東西一段時間後，注意力可能下降。"},{"en":"After they have seen the same thing for a while means after repeated exposure to one familiar object or event.","zh":"after they have seen the same thing for a while 指反覆接觸同一熟悉物件或事件之後。"},{"en":"Students may stop noticing a classroom poster after they have seen the same thing for a while.","zh":"學生在看同一張課室海報一段時間後，可能不再注意它。"},{"en":"Repetition can reduce attention because the mind no longer treats the event as new.","zh":"重複可以降低注意力，因為心智不再把事件視為新事物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the effect of familiarity over time.","zh":"這個短語描述熟悉感隨時間帶來的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"face possible and impossible events","meaning":"面對可能和不可能的事件","examples":[{"en":"Babies may react differently when they face possible and impossible events.","zh":"嬰兒面對可能和不可能的事件時，反應可能不同。"},{"en":"To face possible and impossible events means to be shown events that either follow or seem to break normal rules.","zh":"face possible and impossible events 指被展示遵從正常規則或看似打破規則的事件。"},{"en":"A child faces possible and impossible events when a toy car first rolls normally and then appears to pass through a wall.","zh":"當玩具車先正常滾動，之後看似穿過牆，孩子就是面對可能和不可能的事件。"},{"en":"Comparing reactions helps researchers see what kind of event attracts attention.","zh":"比較反應幫助研究人員了解哪類事件吸引注意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being exposed to normal and rule-breaking events.","zh":"這個短語描述接觸正常和打破規則的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"previously seen things reappear","meaning":"之前見過的東西再次出現","examples":[{"en":"Object permanence concerns whether babies know that previously seen things can reappear.","zh":"物體恆存概念涉及嬰兒是否知道之前見過的東西可以再次出現。"},{"en":"Previously seen things reappear means objects that were visible before become visible again.","zh":"previously seen things reappear 指之前可見的物件再次變得可見。"},{"en":"A baby may smile when a toy hidden under a cloth reappears.","zh":"當藏在布下的玩具再次出現，嬰兒可能會微笑。"},{"en":"Reappearance helps researchers test whether babies expect objects to continue existing.","zh":"再次出現幫助研究人員測試嬰兒是否預期物件繼續存在。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something once seen coming back into view.","zh":"這個短語描述曾經見過的東西重新進入視線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"acquire knowledge","meaning":"獲得知識","examples":[{"en":"Piaget believed babies acquire knowledge through experience.","zh":"Piaget 相信嬰兒透過經驗獲得知識。"},{"en":"To acquire knowledge means to gain or learn information and understanding over time.","zh":"acquire knowledge 指隨時間得到或學會資訊與理解。"},{"en":"Students acquire knowledge of grammar by reading examples and using rules in writing.","zh":"學生透過閱讀例子和在寫作中使用規則，獲得文法知識。"},{"en":"Knowledge is acquired more deeply when learners connect it to real situations.","zh":"當學習者把知識連到真實情況，知識會被更深入地獲得。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the process of gaining understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述獲得理解的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"mechanisms for learning language","meaning":"學習語言的機制","examples":[{"en":"Some cognitive scientists think babies have mechanisms for learning language.","zh":"有些認知科學家認為嬰兒有學習語言的機制。"},{"en":"Mechanisms for learning language are mental systems or processes that help people acquire speech and grammar.","zh":"mechanisms for learning language 是幫助人獲得說話和文法的心理系統或過程。"},{"en":"A child’s ability to notice repeated sounds may be one mechanism for learning language.","zh":"孩子注意重複聲音的能力，可能是學習語言的其中一種機制。"},{"en":"Such mechanisms help explain why children learn speech quickly despite limited instruction.","zh":"這些機制幫助解釋為何孩子在有限教導下仍能快速學會說話。"},{"en":"The phrase describes internal tools that support language learning.","zh":"這個短語描述支援語言學習的內在工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"respond to novel stimuli","meaning":"對新奇刺激作出反應","examples":[{"en":"Sirois thinks babies respond to novel stimuli.","zh":"Sirois 認為嬰兒會對新奇刺激作出反應。"},{"en":"To respond to novel stimuli means to react to things that are new or unfamiliar.","zh":"respond to novel stimuli 指對新的或不熟悉的東西作出反應。"},{"en":"A baby may respond to novel stimuli by staring longer at a new toy.","zh":"嬰兒可能透過較久注視新玩具來對新奇刺激作出反應。"},{"en":"Novel stimuli can raise attention because they break familiar patterns.","zh":"新奇刺激可以提高注意力，因為它們打破熟悉模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reaction to new sensory information.","zh":"這個短語描述對新感官資訊的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"attention level will drop","meaning":"注意力水平會下降","examples":[{"en":"A baby’s attention level will drop after repeated exposure.","zh":"嬰兒在反覆接觸後，注意力水平會下降。"},{"en":"Attention level will drop means focus or interest will decrease.","zh":"attention level will drop 指專注或興趣會降低。"},{"en":"Students’ attention level will drop if a video is played too many times without a new task.","zh":"如果影片播放太多次而沒有新任務，學生的注意力水平會下降。"},{"en":"Repeated exposure can make something feel ordinary, so attention falls.","zh":"反覆接觸可以令某事感覺普通，因此注意力下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a predictable decline in focus.","zh":"這個短語描述可預測的專注力下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"what readers can learn about","meaning":"讀者可得知關於……的事","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what readers can learn about Daniel in the third paragraph.","zh":"題目問讀者可從第三段得知關於 Daniel 的甚麼。"},{"en":"What readers can learn about someone means what information the passage gives about that person.","zh":"what readers can learn about 某人，指文章給出關於該人的甚麼資料。"},{"en":"A reading question may ask what readers can learn about a scientist’s method from one paragraph.","zh":"閱讀題可能問讀者可從某段得知關於科學家方法的甚麼。"},{"en":"Students should answer using evidence from the text, not guesses about the person.","zh":"學生應使用文本證據回答，而不是猜測該人物。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on information revealed by the passage.","zh":"這個短語聚焦文章揭示的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"attention level rose","meaning":"注意力水平上升","examples":[{"en":"Daniel’s attention level rose when novelty was introduced.","zh":"當新奇事物被引入時，Daniel 的注意力水平上升。"},{"en":"Attention level rose means focus or interest increased.","zh":"attention level rose 指專注或興趣增加。"},{"en":"A class’s attention level rose when the teacher brought in a real object instead of another worksheet.","zh":"當老師帶來真實物件，而不是另一張工作紙，班級的注意力水平上升。"},{"en":"Attention rises when something new gives the mind a reason to look again.","zh":"當新事物給心智理由再次觀看，注意力就會上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an increase in focus.","zh":"這個短語描述專注力增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be accustomed to","meaning":"習慣於……","examples":[{"en":"A child’s attention falls when he is accustomed to the changes.","zh":"當孩子習慣於這些變化時，他的注意力會下降。"},{"en":"To be accustomed to something means to be used to it because it has happened often.","zh":"be accustomed to 某事，指因它經常發生而習慣它。"},{"en":"Students become accustomed to a teacher’s accent after listening for several lessons.","zh":"學生聽了幾堂課後，會習慣老師的口音。"},{"en":"When people are accustomed to something, it may no longer attract much attention.","zh":"當人習慣某事，它可能不再吸引太多注意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes familiarity through repeated experience.","zh":"這個短語描述透過重複經驗而產生的熟悉感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"brain activity","meaning":"腦部活動","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to whether Daniel’s brain activity was monitored.","zh":"該選項提到 Daniel 的腦部活動是否被監測。"},{"en":"Brain activity means the electrical or biological processes happening in the brain.","zh":"brain activity 指大腦中正在發生的電性或生物過程。"},{"en":"Scientists may study brain activity while a person reads, listens, or solves a puzzle.","zh":"科學家可能在人閱讀、聆聽或解謎時研究腦部活動。"},{"en":"Measuring brain activity can help connect behaviour with mental processes.","zh":"量度腦部活動可以幫助把行為與心理過程連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what the brain is doing internally.","zh":"這個短語描述大腦內部正在做甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be monitored with special equipment","meaning":"用特殊設備監測","examples":[{"en":"Some responses can be monitored with special equipment.","zh":"有些反應可以用特殊設備監測。"},{"en":"To be monitored with special equipment means to be observed or measured using tools designed for that purpose.","zh":"be monitored with special equipment 指使用為該目的設計的工具觀察或量度。"},{"en":"A patient’s heart rate may be monitored with special equipment during surgery.","zh":"病人在手術期間，心跳可能用特殊設備監測。"},{"en":"Special equipment can collect data that ordinary observation cannot see.","zh":"特殊設備可以收集普通觀察看不到的數據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful measurement using technical tools.","zh":"這個短語描述使用技術工具進行仔細量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"change when it comes out","meaning":"出來時改變","examples":[{"en":"The train may change when it comes out of the tunnel.","zh":"火車從隧道出來時可能改變。"},{"en":"To change when it comes out means to appear different after leaving a hidden space.","zh":"change when it comes out 指離開隱藏空間後出現時變得不同。"},{"en":"In a magic trick, a card may change when it comes out of an envelope.","zh":"在魔術中，紙牌從信封出來時可能改變。"},{"en":"Such a change can surprise viewers because they expected the object to remain the same.","zh":"這種改變可以令觀眾驚訝，因為他們預期物件保持不變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a difference appearing after re-emergence.","zh":"這個短語描述重新出現後出現差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"explain in the paragraph","meaning":"在段落中解釋","examples":[{"en":"The writer explains a change in theories in the fourth paragraph.","zh":"作者在第四段中解釋理論的變化。"},{"en":"To explain in the paragraph means to give information or reasons within that specific paragraph.","zh":"explain in the paragraph 指在該特定段落內提供資料或原因。"},{"en":"A reading question may ask what the writer explains in the paragraph about school rules.","zh":"閱讀題可能問作者在段落中如何解釋校規。"},{"en":"Students should return to the named paragraph instead of using the whole passage loosely.","zh":"學生應回到指定段落，而不是籠統使用整篇文章。"},{"en":"The phrase directs attention to one part of the text.","zh":"這個短語把注意力指向文本的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"change over time","meaning":"隨時間改變","examples":[{"en":"Theories about what babies know have changed over time.","zh":"關於嬰兒知道甚麼的理論已隨時間改變。"},{"en":"To change over time means to become different gradually as years, evidence, or experience pass.","zh":"change over time 指隨着年份、證據或經驗過去而逐漸變得不同。"},{"en":"A student’s writing style can change over time with reading and feedback.","zh":"學生的寫作風格可以透過閱讀和回饋隨時間改變。"},{"en":"Scientific ideas change over time when new experiments challenge old explanations.","zh":"當新實驗挑戰舊解釋，科學想法會隨時間改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual development or revision.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸發展或修訂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"external environment","meaning":"外在環境","examples":[{"en":"The theory concerns babies’ knowledge of the external environment.","zh":"該理論涉及嬰兒對外在環境的知識。"},{"en":"The external environment is the world outside a person’s mind or body.","zh":"external environment 是一個人心智或身體以外的世界。"},{"en":"A baby learns about the external environment by touching toys and hearing voices.","zh":"嬰兒透過觸摸玩具和聽見聲音來學習外在環境。"},{"en":"Changes in the external environment can affect attention, mood, and behaviour.","zh":"外在環境的變化可以影響注意力、心情和行為。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to surrounding objects, people, sounds, and conditions.","zh":"這個短語指周圍的物件、人物、聲音和條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"misleading interpretations","meaning":"誤導性的詮釋","examples":[{"en":"Sirois criticises misleading interpretations of current experiments.","zh":"Sirois 批評對現時實驗的誤導性詮釋。"},{"en":"Misleading interpretations are explanations that make evidence seem to show more or something different from what it really shows.","zh":"misleading interpretations 是令證據看似顯示比實際更多或不同內容的解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may warn against misleading interpretations of exam scores if one low mark is treated as total failure.","zh":"如果一次低分被視為完全失敗，老師可能提醒不要對考試分數作誤導性詮釋。"},{"en":"Misleading interpretations can spread when people jump from observation to conclusion too quickly.","zh":"當人們太快從觀察跳到結論，誤導性詮釋就可能擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase describes explanations that guide readers in the wrong direction.","zh":"這個短語描述把讀者引向錯誤方向的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"current experiments","meaning":"現時的實驗","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses current experiments on infant cognition.","zh":"文章討論關於嬰兒認知的現時實驗。"},{"en":"Current experiments are studies being done or discussed now, using modern methods.","zh":"current experiments 是目前正在進行或討論、使用現代方法的研究。"},{"en":"Current experiments in education may test whether shorter lessons improve focus.","zh":"教育中的現時實驗可能測試較短課堂是否改善專注力。"},{"en":"Current experiments can challenge older theories because they use newer tools.","zh":"現時的實驗可以挑戰較舊理論，因為它們使用較新工具。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research from the present period.","zh":"這個短語描述現階段的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be attracted by","meaning":"被……吸引","examples":[{"en":"Babies may be attracted by novel things.","zh":"嬰兒可能被新奇事物吸引。"},{"en":"To be attracted by something means to have one’s attention or interest drawn to it.","zh":"be attracted by 某物，指注意力或興趣被它吸引。"},{"en":"Students may be attracted by a colourful book cover before reading the title.","zh":"學生可能在閱讀書名之前，先被色彩鮮艷的書封吸引。"},{"en":"New, bright, moving, or unusual things often attract attention quickly.","zh":"新的、明亮的、會動的或不尋常的東西常迅速吸引注意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes attention being pulled toward something.","zh":"這個短語描述注意力被拉向某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"all the time","meaning":"一直；任何時候","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that babies are attracted by colour changes all the time.","zh":"該選項暗示嬰兒一直被顏色變化吸引。"},{"en":"All the time means always or very frequently.","zh":"all the time 指總是或非常頻繁。"},{"en":"A student who checks her phone all the time may find it hard to focus on homework.","zh":"一直查看手機的學生可能很難專注做功課。"},{"en":"This phrase can exaggerate frequency if it is not supported by evidence.","zh":"如果沒有證據支持，這個短語可能誇大頻率。"},{"en":"It describes something happening constantly or repeatedly.","zh":"它描述某事不斷或反覆發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"novel things","meaning":"新奇事物","examples":[{"en":"Sirois suggests that novel things attract a baby’s attention.","zh":"Sirois 指出新奇事物會吸引嬰兒注意力。"},{"en":"Novel things are new, unfamiliar, or unexpected objects or events.","zh":"novel things 是新的、不熟悉的或出乎意料的物件或事件。"},{"en":"A baby may stare at novel things such as a new toy or a sudden sound.","zh":"嬰兒可能盯着新玩具或突然聲音等新奇事物。"},{"en":"Novel things attract attention because the brain has not yet become used to them.","zh":"新奇事物吸引注意，因為大腦尚未習慣它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes things that feel new and interesting.","zh":"這個短語描述感覺新鮮而有趣的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"attract a baby’s attention","meaning":"吸引嬰兒的注意力","examples":[{"en":"Novel things can attract a baby’s attention.","zh":"新奇事物可以吸引嬰兒的注意力。"},{"en":"To attract a baby’s attention means to make a baby look, listen, or respond.","zh":"attract a baby’s attention 指令嬰兒觀看、聆聽或作出反應。"},{"en":"A moving rattle can attract a baby’s attention during playtime.","zh":"玩耍時間中，會動的搖鈴可以吸引嬰兒的注意力。"},{"en":"Bright colours, faces, sounds, and movement often attract babies because they stand out.","zh":"鮮艷顏色、人臉、聲音和動作常吸引嬰兒，因為它們突出。"},{"en":"The phrase describes causing a baby to focus on something.","zh":"這個短語描述令嬰兒專注於某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 51 - What Do Babies Know?.pdf","sourcePage":22}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 52":[{"front":"respond to","meaning":"對……作出反應","examples":[{"en":"People respond to words and symbols in different ways.","zh":"人們會以不同方式對文字和符號作出反應。"},{"en":"To respond to something means to react to it through feelings, thoughts, words or actions.","zh":"對某事作出反應，是指透過感受、想法、說話或行動回應它。"},{"en":"A student may respond to praise by working harder in the next lesson.","zh":"學生可能因受到稱讚而在下一堂課更加努力。"},{"en":"If people respond strongly to a symbol, it usually means they have learned to connect it with certain ideas.","zh":"如果人們對某個符號反應強烈，通常表示他們已學會把它與某些想法連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on reaction, not just passive understanding.","zh":"這個短語強調反應，而不只是被動理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"words and symbols","meaning":"文字和符號","examples":[{"en":"We respond to words and symbols according to our learned habits.","zh":"我們會根據學得的習慣對文字和符號作出反應。"},{"en":"Words and symbols are signs that carry meaning because people have learned how to interpret them.","zh":"文字和符號是帶有意義的標記，因為人們已學會如何詮釋它們。"},{"en":"A red traffic light is a symbol that tells drivers to stop.","zh":"紅色交通燈是一個告訴司機停車的符號。"},{"en":"If a symbol is not shared by a community, people may not know how to respond to it.","zh":"如果某個符號不是社群共享的，人們可能不知道如何對它作出反應。"},{"en":"This phrase includes language, signs, flags, marks and other meaningful signals.","zh":"這個短語包括語言、標誌、旗幟、記號和其他有意義的訊號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the ways we do","meaning":"以我們現有的方式","examples":[{"en":"The passage asks why we respond to symbols in the ways we do.","zh":"篇章問我們為何以現有的方式對符號作出反應。"},{"en":"In the ways we do means in the particular ways that we actually behave or react.","zh":"以我們現有的方式，是指以我們實際行事或反應的特定方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask why students study in the ways they do before changing the lesson plan.","zh":"老師在改變教學計劃前，可能會問學生為何以現有方式學習。"},{"en":"People respond in the ways they do because past experience trains their habits.","zh":"人們以現有方式反應，是因為過往經驗訓練了他們的習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase points to our existing patterns of behaviour.","zh":"這個短語指我們已有的行為模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the end product of","meaning":"……的最終產物","examples":[{"en":"The end product of education is a pattern of possible reactions.","zh":"教育的最終產物是一套可能反應的模式。"},{"en":"The end product of something is the final result produced by a process.","zh":"某事的最終產物，是一個過程所產生的最後結果。"},{"en":"The end product of months of piano practice may be a confident performance on stage.","zh":"數月鋼琴練習的最終產物，可能是在台上自信演奏。"},{"en":"If education shapes habits over many years, its end product is not just knowledge but a way of reacting.","zh":"如果教育多年塑造習慣，其最終產物不只是知識，而是一種反應方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what a long process finally creates.","zh":"這個短語描述長期過程最後創造出來的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"total pattern of reactions","meaning":"反應的整體模式","examples":[{"en":"Education shapes the total pattern of reactions we have inside ourselves.","zh":"教育塑造我們內在擁有的反應整體模式。"},{"en":"A total pattern of reactions is the full set of ways a person tends to respond.","zh":"反應的整體模式，是一個人傾向作出回應的完整方式。"},{"en":"A child’s total pattern of reactions to criticism may be shaped by parents, teachers and classmates.","zh":"孩子對批評的反應整體模式，可能由父母、老師和同學塑造。"},{"en":"Repeated experiences build a pattern, so people may react automatically without thinking carefully.","zh":"重複經驗會建立模式，所以人可能不經仔細思考就自動反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a whole system of learned responses.","zh":"這個短語描述一整套學得的反應系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"possible reactions","meaning":"可能出現的反應","examples":[{"en":"Our possible reactions are shaped by education and experience.","zh":"我們可能出現的反應由教育和經驗塑造。"},{"en":"Possible reactions are the different responses a person may have in a situation.","zh":"可能出現的反應，是人在某情況下可能有的不同回應。"},{"en":"If a student receives a low mark, possible reactions include asking for help, giving up or studying harder.","zh":"如果學生得到低分，可能反應包括求助、放棄或更加努力溫習。"},{"en":"Education can make some reactions more likely and others less likely.","zh":"教育可以令某些反應更可能出現，另一些反應較不可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to what a person might think, feel or do.","zh":"這個短語指一個人可能想、感受或做的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have within you","meaning":"內在擁有……","examples":[{"en":"You have within you the pattern of reactions called the ability to read.","zh":"你內在擁有一套稱為閱讀能力的反應模式。"},{"en":"To have something within you means to possess it internally as a skill, habit or capacity.","zh":"內在擁有某物，是指把它作為技能、習慣或能力保存在自己內部。"},{"en":"A confident speaker has within them years of practice, correction and experience.","zh":"自信的演講者內在擁有多年練習、修正和經驗。"},{"en":"When a habit is within you, it can guide your response without conscious effort.","zh":"當習慣內在存在，它可以不經刻意思考就引導你的反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an internal ability rather than an outside object.","zh":"這個短語描述內在能力，而不是外在物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"at this moment","meaning":"此刻","examples":[{"en":"At this moment, you can read because of trained patterns of response.","zh":"此刻，你能閱讀是因為經訓練形成的反應模式。"},{"en":"At this moment means right now, at the present time.","zh":"此刻，是指現在、當下。"},{"en":"At this moment, the teacher is explaining the answer on the board.","zh":"此刻，老師正在黑板上解釋答案。"},{"en":"The phrase makes the reader notice what is happening now, not in the past or future.","zh":"這個短語令讀者注意現在發生的事情，而不是過去或未來。"},{"en":"It is often used to focus attention on the present situation.","zh":"它常用來把注意力集中在當前情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the ability to read","meaning":"閱讀能力","examples":[{"en":"The ability to read depends on a learned pattern of reactions.","zh":"閱讀能力取決於一套學得的反應模式。"},{"en":"The ability to read is the skill of understanding written words and symbols.","zh":"閱讀能力是理解書面文字和符號的技能。"},{"en":"A child develops the ability to read by connecting letters with sounds and meanings.","zh":"孩子透過把字母與聲音和意思連接起來，發展閱讀能力。"},{"en":"Without this ability, printed words may look like marks rather than meaningful language.","zh":"沒有這種能力，印刷文字可能看起來像記號，而不是有意義的語言。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a learned skill, not something people are born fully able to do.","zh":"這個短語描述學得的技能，而不是人天生完全具備的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"meaningless black marks","meaning":"無意義的黑色印記","examples":[{"en":"Without the ability to read, words would look like meaningless black marks on paper.","zh":"沒有閱讀能力，文字看起來就會像紙上無意義的黑色印記。"},{"en":"Meaningless black marks are written symbols that have no meaning to someone who cannot interpret them.","zh":"無意義的黑色印記，是對不能詮釋它們的人來說沒有意義的書面符號。"},{"en":"To a person who does not know Chinese, some characters may look like meaningless marks at first.","zh":"對不懂中文的人來說，有些漢字起初可能像無意義的記號。"},{"en":"Once a person learns the writing system, the same marks become meaningful words.","zh":"一旦人學會該書寫系統，同樣的記號就變成有意義的文字。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that meaning depends on learned interpretation.","zh":"這個短語顯示意義取決於學得的詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"because of","meaning":"由於；因為","examples":[{"en":"Because of trained patterns of response, symbols can arouse feelings.","zh":"由於經訓練形成的反應模式，符號可以激起感受。"},{"en":"Because of means as a result of something.","zh":"由於或因為，是指作為某事的結果。"},{"en":"Because of heavy rain, the school sports day was postponed.","zh":"由於大雨，學校運動會延期。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the cause behind a result.","zh":"這個短語引入結果背後的原因。"},{"en":"It helps explain why something happens.","zh":"它幫助解釋某事為何發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"trained patterns of response","meaning":"經訓練形成的反應模式","examples":[{"en":"Trained patterns of response affect how we react to words and symbols.","zh":"經訓練形成的反應模式影響我們如何對文字和符號作出反應。"},{"en":"Trained patterns of response are learned habits that guide how people react.","zh":"經訓練形成的反應模式，是引導人們反應的學得習慣。"},{"en":"A student trained to raise a hand before speaking may do so automatically in class.","zh":"被訓練發言前舉手的學生，可能在課堂上自動這樣做。"},{"en":"Repeated teaching and experience can create reactions that feel natural.","zh":"重複教導和經驗可以創造出感覺自然的反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes responses shaped by learning rather than instinct alone.","zh":"這個短語描述由學習塑造的反應，而不只是本能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be stirred to patriotism","meaning":"被激發愛國情懷","examples":[{"en":"Some people are stirred to patriotism by martial music.","zh":"有些人會被軍樂激發愛國情懷。"},{"en":"To be stirred to patriotism means to feel strong love or loyalty toward one’s country.","zh":"被激發愛國情懷，是指感到對自己國家的強烈熱愛或忠誠。"},{"en":"A national anthem may stir people to patriotism during an international sports event.","zh":"國歌可能在國際體育賽事中激發人們的愛國情懷。"},{"en":"Music can trigger patriotic feelings when people have learned to connect it with national pride.","zh":"當人們學會把音樂與民族自豪感連接，音樂就能觸發愛國情感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an emotional reaction linked to country and identity.","zh":"這個短語描述與國家和身份相關的情緒反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"patriotism","meaning":"愛國情懷","examples":[{"en":"Martial music may stir some listeners to patriotism.","zh":"軍樂可能激發某些聽眾的愛國情懷。"},{"en":"Patriotism is love for and loyalty to one’s country.","zh":"愛國情懷是對自己國家的熱愛和忠誠。"},{"en":"A person may show patriotism by serving the community during a national crisis.","zh":"一個人可能透過在國家危機中服務社區來表現愛國情懷。"},{"en":"Symbols such as flags and anthems can strengthen patriotism because people connect them with national identity.","zh":"旗幟和國歌等符號可以加強愛國情懷，因為人們把它們與國家身份連接起來。"},{"en":"This word describes emotional attachment to a country.","zh":"這個詞描述對國家的情感依附。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"martial music","meaning":"軍樂","examples":[{"en":"Martial music can stir people to patriotism.","zh":"軍樂可以激發人們的愛國情懷。"},{"en":"Martial music is music connected with soldiers, war, ceremonies or military pride.","zh":"軍樂是與士兵、戰爭、儀式或軍事榮耀有關的音樂。"},{"en":"A parade may use martial music to create a serious and patriotic mood.","zh":"巡遊可能使用軍樂來營造莊嚴和愛國氣氛。"},{"en":"Because people associate it with armies and national events, it can create strong emotional reactions.","zh":"因為人們把它與軍隊和國家事件聯繫起來，它可以產生強烈情緒反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes military-style music.","zh":"這個短語描述軍事風格的音樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"feelings of reverence","meaning":"崇敬之情","examples":[{"en":"Symbols of religion can arouse feelings of reverence.","zh":"宗教象徵可以激起崇敬之情。"},{"en":"Feelings of reverence are feelings of deep respect, honour or sacred seriousness.","zh":"崇敬之情是深深尊重、敬意或神聖莊重的感受。"},{"en":"A person may feel reverence when entering a quiet temple or church.","zh":"一個人進入安靜寺廟或教堂時，可能感到崇敬。"},{"en":"Religious symbols can create reverence because believers connect them with sacred meaning.","zh":"宗教象徵可以產生崇敬，因為信徒把它們與神聖意義連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes respectful and serious emotion.","zh":"這個短語描述尊敬而莊重的情緒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be aroused by","meaning":"被……激起","examples":[{"en":"Feelings of reverence may be aroused by religious symbols.","zh":"崇敬之情可能被宗教象徵激起。"},{"en":"To be aroused by something means to be awakened, stirred or triggered by it.","zh":"被某事激起，是指被它喚醒、觸動或觸發。"},{"en":"Memories of childhood may be aroused by an old song.","zh":"童年回憶可能被一首舊歌激起。"},{"en":"Symbols arouse feelings when people have learned to connect them with strong meanings.","zh":"當人們學會把符號與強烈意義連接，符號就會激起感受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an emotion being triggered.","zh":"這個短語描述情緒被觸發。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"symbols of your religion","meaning":"你宗教的象徵","examples":[{"en":"Your feelings may be aroused by symbols of your religion.","zh":"你的感受可能被你宗教的象徵激起。"},{"en":"Symbols of your religion are objects, signs or images that represent your faith.","zh":"你宗教的象徵，是代表你信仰的物件、標誌或圖像。"},{"en":"A cross, crescent or temple image may be a religious symbol for different believers.","zh":"十字架、新月或寺廟圖像，對不同信徒而言可能是宗教象徵。"},{"en":"Such symbols can create strong feelings because they are linked to worship, identity and memory.","zh":"這些象徵可以產生強烈感受，因為它們與崇拜、身份和記憶相連。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaningful signs within a religious tradition.","zh":"這個短語描述宗教傳統中的有意義標誌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"listen more respectfully to","meaning":"更恭敬地聆聽……","examples":[{"en":"People may listen more respectfully to someone with “MD” after his name.","zh":"人們可能更恭敬地聆聽名字後有「MD」的人。"},{"en":"To listen more respectfully to someone means to pay closer and more serious attention to what they say.","zh":"更恭敬地聆聽某人，是指更認真、更尊重地注意他所說的話。"},{"en":"Patients may listen more respectfully to a doctor than to a stranger giving the same advice.","zh":"病人可能比起陌生人，更恭敬地聆聽醫生給出的同一建議。"},{"en":"Titles can change reactions because people associate them with knowledge and authority.","zh":"頭銜可以改變反應，因為人們把它們與知識和權威聯繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes respectful attention shaped by status or trust.","zh":"這個短語描述由地位或信任塑造的尊重聆聽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"health advice","meaning":"健康建議","examples":[{"en":"People often treat health advice differently depending on who gives it.","zh":"人們通常會因給出建議的人不同，而以不同方式看待健康建議。"},{"en":"Health advice is guidance about how to protect or improve physical or mental health.","zh":"健康建議是關於如何保護或改善身心健康的指引。"},{"en":"A nurse may give health advice about sleep, diet or medicine.","zh":"護士可能給出關於睡眠、飲食或藥物的健康建議。"},{"en":"People may trust health advice more when it comes from someone with medical training.","zh":"當健康建議來自受過醫療訓練的人，人們可能更信任它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes advice related to wellbeing and medical care.","zh":"這個短語描述與福祉和醫療護理相關的建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the sum total of","meaning":"……的總和","examples":[{"en":"A pattern of reactions is the sum total of the ways we respond.","zh":"反應模式是我們回應方式的總和。"},{"en":"The sum total of something is the whole amount or complete result of many parts together.","zh":"某事的總和，是許多部分加起來的整體數量或完整結果。"},{"en":"A student’s final grade may be the sum total of homework, tests, exams and participation.","zh":"學生的最終成績可能是功課、測驗、考試和參與的總和。"},{"en":"Many small experiences can combine to form one overall pattern of response.","zh":"許多小經驗可以結合形成一個整體反應模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a complete whole made from many elements.","zh":"這個短語描述由許多元素組成的完整整體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in response to","meaning":"回應……；因應……","examples":[{"en":"We act in response to events, words and symbols.","zh":"我們會因應事件、文字和符號而行動。"},{"en":"In response to something means because of it or as a reaction to it.","zh":"因應某事，是指因它而作出反應。"},{"en":"A school may close early in response to a typhoon warning.","zh":"學校可能因應颱風警告而提早關閉。"},{"en":"People’s actions often reveal what a word or symbol means to them.","zh":"人們的行動往往揭示某個詞或符號對他們有甚麼意義。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an action with the thing that caused it.","zh":"這個短語把行動與造成該行動的事物連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reaction patterns","meaning":"反應模式","examples":[{"en":"Reaction patterns are shaped by education and experience.","zh":"反應模式由教育和經驗塑造。"},{"en":"Reaction patterns are repeated ways of responding to people, events or symbols.","zh":"反應模式是對人、事件或符號反覆出現的回應方式。"},{"en":"A child may develop a calm reaction pattern if adults usually explain problems patiently.","zh":"如果成人通常耐心解釋問題，孩子可能發展出冷靜的反應模式。"},{"en":"Repeated praise, criticism and teaching can all shape how someone reacts later.","zh":"反覆的稱讚、批評和教導都可以塑造人之後如何反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes habitual responses built over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間建立的習慣性反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"semantic habits","meaning":"語義習慣","examples":[{"en":"Our reaction patterns can also be called semantic habits.","zh":"我們的反應模式也可以稱為語義習慣。"},{"en":"Semantic habits are learned ways of reacting to meanings, words and symbols.","zh":"語義習慣是對意義、詞語和符號作出反應的學得方式。"},{"en":"A person who hears the word “exam” and immediately feels stress has a semantic habit.","zh":"一個人聽到「考試」一詞便立即感到壓力，就是有一種語義習慣。"},{"en":"These habits develop because people repeatedly connect certain words with certain feelings or actions.","zh":"這些習慣會形成，是因為人們反覆把某些詞與某些感受或行動連接。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaning-related habits of response.","zh":"這個短語描述與意義相關的反應習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"internal residue","meaning":"內在殘留影響","examples":[{"en":"Semantic habits are the internal residue of education and experience.","zh":"語義習慣是教育和經驗留下的內在殘留影響。"},{"en":"Internal residue means the lasting inner effects left behind by past experiences.","zh":"內在殘留影響，是過往經驗留下的持久內在效果。"},{"en":"A strict childhood teacher may leave an internal residue of fear toward public speaking.","zh":"嚴格的童年老師可能留下對公開演說感到害怕的內在殘留影響。"},{"en":"Even after an event is over, its effects can remain inside a person’s reactions.","zh":"即使事件已結束，其影響仍可以留在一個人的反應之中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what experience leaves within us.","zh":"這個短語描述經驗在我們內部留下的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"most important residue","meaning":"最重要的殘留影響","examples":[{"en":"Semantic habits are the most important residue of our education.","zh":"語義習慣是我們教育中最重要的殘留影響。"},{"en":"The most important residue is the most significant lasting effect left behind.","zh":"最重要的殘留影響，是留下來最重大的持久效果。"},{"en":"The most important residue of a good reading course may be a habit of asking questions.","zh":"一個良好閱讀課程最重要的殘留影響，可能是提問習慣。"},{"en":"Education matters because it leaves long-term patterns, not just facts remembered for exams.","zh":"教育重要，是因為它留下長期模式，而不只是為考試記住的事實。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the lasting effect that matters most.","zh":"這個短語強調最重要的持久效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"years of education or miseducation","meaning":"多年的教育或錯誤教育","examples":[{"en":"Our habits come from years of education or miseducation.","zh":"我們的習慣來自多年的教育或錯誤教育。"},{"en":"Years of education or miseducation means long periods of learning, whether accurate or misleading.","zh":"多年的教育或錯誤教育，是指長時間學習，不論內容準確還是誤導。"},{"en":"A person may fear mistakes after years of miseducation that treated every error as shameful.","zh":"一個人可能因多年把每個錯誤都視為羞恥的錯誤教育而害怕犯錯。"},{"en":"Long-term teaching can build helpful habits, but wrong teaching can also build harmful ones.","zh":"長期教導可以建立有益習慣，但錯誤教導也可以建立有害習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts good learning with wrong or harmful learning.","zh":"這個短語對比良好學習與錯誤或有害學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"parents’ conduct toward us","meaning":"父母對待我們的方式","examples":[{"en":"Parents’ conduct toward us in childhood affects our semantic habits.","zh":"父母在童年時期對待我們的方式影響我們的語義習慣。"},{"en":"Parents’ conduct toward us means the way our parents behave toward or treat us.","zh":"父母對待我們的方式，是指父母對我們的行為或態度。"},{"en":"If parents listen patiently, a child may learn to respond calmly during disagreements.","zh":"如果父母耐心聆聽，孩子可能學會在分歧中冷靜回應。"},{"en":"Repeated treatment from parents can shape how children react to authority, praise or criticism.","zh":"父母反覆的對待方式會塑造孩子日後對權威、稱讚或批評的反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes parental behaviour as an influence on later responses.","zh":"這個短語描述父母行為作為日後反應的影響因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in childhood","meaning":"在童年時期","examples":[{"en":"Our parents’ conduct toward us in childhood helps shape our responses.","zh":"父母在童年時期對待我們的方式幫助塑造我們的反應。"},{"en":"In childhood means during the period when a person is a child.","zh":"在童年時期，是指一個人還是孩子的階段。"},{"en":"A fear learned in childhood may remain into adulthood.","zh":"童年時期學到的恐懼可能延續到成年。"},{"en":"Early experiences matter because they can form habits before people notice them.","zh":"早期經驗很重要，因為它們可以在人還未察覺前形成習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the early years of life.","zh":"這個短語指人生早年。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"formal education","meaning":"正規教育","examples":[{"en":"Formal education is one influence on our semantic habits.","zh":"正規教育是影響我們語義習慣的因素之一。"},{"en":"Formal education is organised learning provided by schools, colleges or institutions.","zh":"正規教育是由學校、大專院校或機構提供的有組織學習。"},{"en":"Grammar lessons in school are part of formal education.","zh":"學校文法課是正規教育的一部分。"},{"en":"Formal education shapes how people read, speak, judge evidence and respond to authority.","zh":"正規教育塑造人們如何閱讀、說話、判斷證據和回應權威。"},{"en":"This phrase describes structured learning rather than informal life experience.","zh":"這個短語描述有結構的學習，而不是非正式生活經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lectures we have listened to","meaning":"我們聽過的講座","examples":[{"en":"The lectures we have listened to can affect our reaction patterns.","zh":"我們聽過的講座可以影響我們的反應模式。"},{"en":"Lectures we have listened to are talks or lessons that have influenced what we know or believe.","zh":"我們聽過的講座，是曾影響我們知識或信念的演講或課堂。"},{"en":"A student who hears many lectures about climate change may respond strongly to environmental news.","zh":"一名聽過許多氣候變化講座的學生，可能會對環境新聞反應強烈。"},{"en":"Repeated messages in lectures can shape the words and ideas we treat as important.","zh":"講座中反覆出現的訊息可以塑造我們視為重要的詞語和想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes past spoken teaching as an influence.","zh":"這個短語描述過去口頭教學作為一種影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"experienced","meaning":"經歷過；接觸過","examples":[{"en":"Radio programmes and television shows we have experienced shape our habits.","zh":"我們經歷過的電台節目和電視節目塑造我們的習慣。"},{"en":"Experienced means encountered, watched, heard or lived through.","zh":"經歷過，是指遇到、觀看、聆聽或親身經過。"},{"en":"A child who has experienced kind teaching may feel safe asking questions.","zh":"經歷過友善教學的孩子，可能會覺得提問是安全的。"},{"en":"What we experience repeatedly can become part of how we react later.","zh":"我們反覆經歷的事情會成為日後反應的一部分。"},{"en":"This word describes things we have gone through or been exposed to.","zh":"這個詞描述我們經過或接觸過的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"comic strips","meaning":"連環漫畫","examples":[{"en":"Comic strips can also influence our semantic habits.","zh":"連環漫畫也可以影響我們的語義習慣。"},{"en":"Comic strips are short series of drawings that tell a story, often with speech bubbles.","zh":"連環漫畫是一連串短圖畫，通常配有對話框來講故事。"},{"en":"A child may learn jokes, stereotypes or expressions from comic strips.","zh":"孩子可能從連環漫畫中學到笑話、刻板印象或表達方式。"},{"en":"Repeated images and words in comics can shape how readers react to certain ideas.","zh":"漫畫中反覆出現的圖像和文字可以塑造讀者對某些想法的反應。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to illustrated story panels.","zh":"這個短語指以圖格呈現的故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"conversations we have had with","meaning":"我們與……有過的對話","examples":[{"en":"Conversations we have had with friends help shape our responses.","zh":"我們與朋友有過的對話幫助塑造我們的反應。"},{"en":"Conversations we have had with someone are talks from the past that may influence us.","zh":"我們與某人有過的對話，是過去可能影響我們的談話。"},{"en":"A student’s conversations with classmates can change how they feel about an exam.","zh":"學生與同學有過的對話，可以改變他對考試的感受。"},{"en":"Repeated conversations can make certain opinions feel normal or familiar.","zh":"反覆對話可以令某些觀點感覺正常或熟悉。"},{"en":"This phrase describes past discussions as part of experience.","zh":"這個短語描述過去討論作為經驗的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"friends and associates","meaning":"朋友和同伴","examples":[{"en":"Our conversations with friends and associates affect our habits.","zh":"我們與朋友和同伴的對話影響我們的習慣。"},{"en":"Friends and associates are people we know socially or through work, study or daily life.","zh":"朋友和同伴，是我們在社交、工作、學習或日常生活中認識的人。"},{"en":"A young employee may learn workplace language from friends and associates in the office.","zh":"年輕員工可能從辦公室的朋友和同伴學到職場語言。"},{"en":"The people around us shape our reactions because we hear their views repeatedly.","zh":"身邊的人會塑造我們的反應，因為我們反覆聽到他們的看法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both close friends and people connected with us.","zh":"這個短語描述親近朋友以及與我們有連繫的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"as the result of","meaning":"作為……的結果","examples":[{"en":"Our semantic habits develop as the result of many influences.","zh":"我們的語義習慣是多種影響造成的結果。"},{"en":"As the result of something means because of it or after it has had an effect.","zh":"作為某事的結果，是指因為它或在它產生影響後。"},{"en":"A student may become more confident as the result of patient feedback.","zh":"學生可能因耐心回饋而變得更自信。"},{"en":"Habits often form as the result of repeated teaching and experience.","zh":"習慣通常是反覆教導和經驗造成的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an outcome with its causes.","zh":"這個短語把結果與原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"all these influences","meaning":"所有這些影響","examples":[{"en":"All these influences make us what we are.","zh":"所有這些影響造就今日的我們。"},{"en":"All these influences means all the experiences, teachings and contacts already mentioned.","zh":"所有這些影響，是指前面提到的所有經驗、教導和接觸。"},{"en":"Family, school, books and friends are all influences that can shape a student’s character.","zh":"家庭、學校、書本和朋友都是可以塑造學生性格的影響。"},{"en":"Many small influences combine to form a person’s habits and attitudes.","zh":"許多小影響結合起來，形成一個人的習慣和態度。"},{"en":"This phrase gathers several causes into one overall explanation.","zh":"這個短語把多個原因集合成一個整體解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"make us what we are","meaning":"造就今日的我們","examples":[{"en":"Education and experience help make us what we are.","zh":"教育和經驗幫助造就今日的我們。"},{"en":"To make us what we are means to shape our personality, habits and ways of responding.","zh":"造就今日的我們，是指塑造我們的性格、習慣和反應方式。"},{"en":"A supportive teacher may help make a shy student into a confident speaker.","zh":"支持性的老師可能幫助害羞學生成為自信演講者。"},{"en":"Repeated experiences shape people, so they become different from who they might otherwise be.","zh":"重複經驗會塑造人，使他們變成不同於原本可能成為的樣子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the forces that form a person’s identity.","zh":"這個短語描述形成個人身份的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reasonably similar to","meaning":"與……相當相似","examples":[{"en":"Our semantic habits may be reasonably similar to those of people around us.","zh":"我們的語義習慣可能與身邊人的語義習慣相當相似。"},{"en":"Reasonably similar to means fairly alike, though not exactly the same.","zh":"與某物相當相似，是指頗為相像，但不是完全一樣。"},{"en":"Students in the same class may have reasonably similar study habits.","zh":"同班學生可能有相當相似的學習習慣。"},{"en":"Shared education and culture can make people respond in similar ways.","zh":"共同教育和文化可以令人以相似方式反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moderate similarity, not perfect sameness.","zh":"這個短語描述中等程度的相似，而不是完全相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"those of most people around us","meaning":"我們身邊大多數人的……","examples":[{"en":"Our reactions may resemble those of most people around us.","zh":"我們的反應可能與身邊大多數人的反應相似。"},{"en":"Those of most people around us means the reactions, habits or views belonging to people nearby.","zh":"我們身邊大多數人的，是指附近人所擁有的反應、習慣或看法。"},{"en":"A teenager’s slang may resemble that of most classmates around them.","zh":"青少年的俚語可能與身邊大多數同學的俚語相似。"},{"en":"People often become similar to those around them because they share conversations and experiences.","zh":"人們通常會變得與身邊人相似，因為他們分享對話和經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating a noun by referring back to it.","zh":"這個短語透過回指來避免重複名詞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be regarded as","meaning":"被視為……","examples":[{"en":"People with ordinary reaction patterns are regarded as normal.","zh":"擁有普通反應模式的人被視為正常。"},{"en":"To be regarded as something means to be considered or thought of in that way.","zh":"被視為某事，是指被認為或看作那樣。"},{"en":"A student who always helps classmates may be regarded as kind and reliable.","zh":"經常幫助同學的學生可能被視為友善可靠。"},{"en":"Society often judges people by whether their reactions match common expectations.","zh":"社會通常根據人們的反應是否符合共同期望來評價他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how people are viewed by others.","zh":"這個短語描述人們如何被他人看待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"noticeably different from","meaning":"與……明顯不同","examples":[{"en":"Some people’s semantic habits are noticeably different from those of others.","zh":"有些人的語義習慣與其他人的明顯不同。"},{"en":"Noticeably different from means clearly different enough to be seen or felt.","zh":"與某物明顯不同，是指差異清楚得足以被看見或感受到。"},{"en":"A student’s handwriting may be noticeably different from their classmates’.","zh":"一個學生的字跡可能與同學的字跡明顯不同。"},{"en":"If someone reacts very differently from others, people may label them unusual or original.","zh":"如果某人的反應與他人很不同，人們可能稱他不尋常或有創見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a difference that is easy to notice.","zh":"這個短語描述容易注意到的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"individualistic","meaning":"有個人風格的；個人主義的","examples":[{"en":"People with different semantic habits may be called individualistic.","zh":"擁有不同語義習慣的人可能被稱為有個人風格。"},{"en":"Individualistic means showing a strong personal style or independent way of thinking.","zh":"有個人風格的，是指表現出強烈個人風格或獨立思考方式。"},{"en":"A student who refuses to copy everyone else’s essay style may seem individualistic.","zh":"拒絕模仿所有人文章風格的學生可能顯得有個人風格。"},{"en":"Individualistic responses may be admired as original or criticised as too different.","zh":"個人化反應可能被欣賞為有創意，也可能被批評為太不同。"},{"en":"This word describes behaviour that stands apart from the group.","zh":"這個詞描述與群體不同的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"original","meaning":"有創見的；獨特的","examples":[{"en":"People with unusual responses may be regarded as original.","zh":"擁有不尋常反應的人可能被視為有創見。"},{"en":"Original means fresh, new or showing independent thought.","zh":"有創見的，是指新鮮、新穎或表現出獨立思考。"},{"en":"A student gives an original answer when they explain a poem in a way nobody else has considered.","zh":"當學生以沒有人考慮過的方式解釋詩歌，就是給出有創見的答案。"},{"en":"Original thinking can be praised when it helps people see a problem differently.","zh":"有創見的思考如果幫助人以不同方式看問題，就可能受到稱讚。"},{"en":"This word describes creativity rather than copying.","zh":"這個詞描述創造力，而不是模仿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be disapproved of","meaning":"不被認同","examples":[{"en":"Some differences in semantic habits are disapproved of.","zh":"有些語義習慣上的差異不被認同。"},{"en":"To be disapproved of means to be criticised or not accepted by others.","zh":"不被認同，是指被他人批評或不接受。"},{"en":"Talking loudly in a library is usually disapproved of.","zh":"在圖書館大聲說話通常不被認同。"},{"en":"If a reaction breaks social expectations, people may reject or criticise it.","zh":"如果反應違反社會期望，人們可能拒絕或批評它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social judgement against something.","zh":"這個短語描述社會對某事的負面評價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"viewed with alarm","meaning":"被視為令人擔憂","examples":[{"en":"Some unusual responses are viewed with alarm.","zh":"有些不尋常反應被視為令人擔憂。"},{"en":"Viewed with alarm means seen as worrying, dangerous or disturbing.","zh":"被視為令人擔憂，是指被看作令人憂慮、危險或不安。"},{"en":"A sudden drop in school attendance may be viewed with alarm by teachers.","zh":"學校出席率突然下降可能被老師視為令人擔憂。"},{"en":"People may feel alarm when someone’s reactions seem too far outside normal expectations.","zh":"當某人的反應似乎遠遠超出正常期望，人們可能感到憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a worried reaction from observers.","zh":"這個短語描述觀察者的擔心反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"defined in dictionaries as","meaning":"在字典中被定義為……","examples":[{"en":"Semantics is sometimes defined in dictionaries as the science of meaning.","zh":"語義學有時在字典中被定義為意義的科學。"},{"en":"Defined in dictionaries as means explained by dictionaries using a particular description.","zh":"在字典中被定義為，是指字典用某種描述來解釋。"},{"en":"A word may be defined in dictionaries as a noun, but used more flexibly in conversation.","zh":"一個詞在字典中可能被定義為名詞，但在對話中使用得更靈活。"},{"en":"Dictionary definitions help, but they may not show every real-life use.","zh":"字典定義有幫助，但未必顯示所有現實用法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how dictionaries explain a term.","zh":"這個短語描述字典如何解釋術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the science of","meaning":"……的科學","examples":[{"en":"Semantics is sometimes called the science of the meaning of words.","zh":"語義學有時被稱為詞語意思的科學。"},{"en":"The science of something is the systematic study of that subject.","zh":"某事的科學，是對該主題的系統研究。"},{"en":"Biology is the science of living things.","zh":"生物學是生命體的科學。"},{"en":"Calling a field a science suggests it studies evidence, patterns and principles.","zh":"把一個領域稱為科學，暗示它研究證據、模式和原則。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an organised field of study.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的研究領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the meaning of words","meaning":"詞語的意思","examples":[{"en":"Many people think semantics is about the meaning of words.","zh":"許多人認為語義學是關於詞語的意思。"},{"en":"The meaning of words is what words communicate or make people understand.","zh":"詞語的意思，是詞語傳達或令人理解的內容。"},{"en":"A learner may ask the meaning of a word before using it in a sentence.","zh":"學習者在句子中使用一個詞之前，可能會詢問其意思。"},{"en":"Meaning is not always fixed by a dictionary because people react to words differently.","zh":"意思不一定由字典固定，因為人們對詞語有不同反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what words signify to users.","zh":"這個短語描述詞語對使用者表示甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not a bad definition","meaning":"不算差的定義","examples":[{"en":"The dictionary definition would not be a bad definition in itself.","zh":"字典定義本身不算差的定義。"},{"en":"Not a bad definition means acceptable or partly useful, though not perfect.","zh":"不算差的定義，是指可以接受或部分有用，但不完美。"},{"en":"Saying “stress is pressure on the mind” is not a bad definition for beginners.","zh":"說「壓力是心理上的負擔」對初學者來說不算差的定義。"},{"en":"A definition can be helpful at first but still incomplete for deeper study.","zh":"一個定義起初可以有幫助，但對深入研究仍可能不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase gives mild approval while leaving room for criticism.","zh":"這個短語給予輕微肯定，同時保留批評空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"assume that","meaning":"假定；以為","examples":[{"en":"People often assume that word meanings can be found in dictionaries.","zh":"人們常假定詞語意思可以在字典中找到。"},{"en":"To assume that something is true means to believe it without fully checking.","zh":"假定某事為真，是指沒有完全查證就相信它。"},{"en":"A student may assume that a short question is easy, then miss an important detail.","zh":"學生可能以為短題目很容易，然後漏看重要細節。"},{"en":"Assumptions can lead to mistakes when the situation is more complex than expected.","zh":"當情況比預期複雜，假設可能導致錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking something as true too quickly.","zh":"這個短語描述太快把某事當作真實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"begins and ends with","meaning":"以……開始並以……結束","examples":[{"en":"Some people think the search for meaning begins and ends with a dictionary.","zh":"有些人認為尋找意義以字典開始並以字典結束。"},{"en":"Begins and ends with something means depends completely on it and goes no further.","zh":"以某事開始並以某事結束，是指完全依賴它，不再深入。"},{"en":"Good essay writing does not begin and end with memorising vocabulary.","zh":"好的文章寫作並不以背詞彙開始並結束。"},{"en":"If learning begins and ends with one tool, students may miss deeper understanding.","zh":"如果學習只依賴一種工具，學生可能錯過更深理解。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises an approach that is too narrow.","zh":"這個短語批評過於狹窄的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"look something up in a dictionary","meaning":"在字典中查找……","examples":[{"en":"People often look words up in a dictionary to find their meanings.","zh":"人們常在字典中查找詞語，以找出它們的意思。"},{"en":"To look something up in a dictionary means to search for its definition in a dictionary.","zh":"在字典中查找某物，是指在字典中搜尋其定義。"},{"en":"A student may look up “reverence” in a dictionary before translating a passage.","zh":"學生可能在翻譯篇章前，在字典中查找 reverence。"},{"en":"Looking up a word can help, but examples are needed to understand how it works.","zh":"查字典可以有幫助，但仍需要例子來理解它如何使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using a dictionary to check meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述使用字典查核意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"stop to think","meaning":"停下來思考","examples":[{"en":"If one stops to think, dictionary definitions are clearly limited.","zh":"如果人停下來思考，就會清楚看見字典定義有限。"},{"en":"To stop to think means to pause and consider something carefully.","zh":"停下來思考，是指暫停並仔細考慮某事。"},{"en":"If students stop to think before answering, they may notice the question is asking for contrast.","zh":"如果學生答題前停下來思考，可能會注意到題目要求對比。"},{"en":"Careful thought can reveal problems hidden by quick assumptions.","zh":"仔細思考可以揭示快速假設所隱藏的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pausing for reflection.","zh":"這個短語描述暫停反思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for a moment","meaning":"片刻","examples":[{"en":"If one stops to think for a moment, the problem becomes clear.","zh":"如果人停下來思考片刻，問題就會變得清楚。"},{"en":"For a moment means for a short period of time.","zh":"片刻，是指一小段時間。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask the class to think for a moment before giving answers.","zh":"老師可能要求全班思考片刻，然後才給答案。"},{"en":"Even a brief pause can help people notice a problem more clearly.","zh":"即使短暫停頓，也能幫助人更清楚注意到問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a short time used for thought or action.","zh":"這個短語描述用於思考或行動的短時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"to define a word","meaning":"定義一個詞","examples":[{"en":"To define a word is to explain it with more words.","zh":"定義一個詞，就是用更多文字解釋它。"},{"en":"To define a word means to state its meaning clearly.","zh":"定義一個詞，是指清楚說出其意思。"},{"en":"A teacher may define a difficult word before asking students to use it in a sentence.","zh":"老師可能先定義一個難詞，再要求學生用它造句。"},{"en":"Definitions help learners start understanding, but examples show how the word behaves.","zh":"定義幫助學習者開始理解，而例子顯示該詞如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving a word its meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述說明詞語意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"explain something with","meaning":"用……解釋……","examples":[{"en":"A dictionary explains a word with more words.","zh":"字典用更多文字解釋一個詞。"},{"en":"To explain something with something else means to use that second thing to make the first clear.","zh":"用某物解釋某事，是指使用第二樣東西令第一件事清楚。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain grammar with simple examples rather than long theory.","zh":"老師可能用簡單例子解釋文法，而不是用長篇理論。"},{"en":"Explanations can fail if the words used are also unclear.","zh":"如果所使用的詞本身也不清楚，解釋可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the tool or method used to clarify meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述用來澄清意思的工具或方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"to be thorough about","meaning":"為了徹底做到……","examples":[{"en":"To be thorough about defining, we would need to define every word used.","zh":"為了徹底做到定義，我們需要定義所使用的每一個詞。"},{"en":"To be thorough about something means to deal with it carefully and completely.","zh":"為了徹底做到某事，是指仔細而完整地處理它。"},{"en":"To be thorough about exam preparation, students should review mistakes, vocabulary and timing.","zh":"為了徹底準備考試，學生應複習錯誤、詞彙和時間分配。"},{"en":"Complete thoroughness can take much more time than people expect.","zh":"完全徹底可能比人們預期花更多時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doing something in a full and careful way.","zh":"這個短語描述完整而仔細地做某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"and so on","meaning":"如此類推","examples":[{"en":"We would define the words in the definition, then more words, and so on.","zh":"我們會定義定義中的詞，然後再定義更多詞，如此類推。"},{"en":"And so on means the same pattern continues with other similar things.","zh":"如此類推，是指同一模式繼續套用到其他相似事物。"},{"en":"A student may pack books, pens, worksheets, and so on before school.","zh":"學生上學前可能收拾書本、筆、工作紙等等。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids listing every item when the pattern is already clear.","zh":"當模式已清楚時，這個短語避免列出每一項。"},{"en":"It suggests continuation without giving all details.","zh":"它暗示繼續下去，而不給出所有細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in short","meaning":"簡而言之","examples":[{"en":"In short, defining words with more words creates a problem.","zh":"簡而言之，用更多文字定義詞語會產生問題。"},{"en":"In short introduces a brief summary of what has just been explained.","zh":"簡而言之，用來引入對剛才解釋內容的簡短總結。"},{"en":"The lesson was noisy, rushed and confusing; in short, it did not work.","zh":"那堂課嘈雜、倉促又混亂；簡而言之，它行不通。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers reduce a complex point to a clear conclusion.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者把複雜重點壓縮成清楚結論。"},{"en":"It signals that the main message is about to be stated simply.","zh":"它表示主要訊息即將被簡單說出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at once","meaning":"立刻；馬上","examples":[{"en":"Defining words with more words gets us at once into an infinite regress.","zh":"用更多文字定義詞語會立刻使我們陷入無限倒退。"},{"en":"At once means immediately or very quickly.","zh":"立刻，是指立即或非常快。"},{"en":"If a fire alarm rings, students should leave the classroom at once.","zh":"如果火警鐘響起，學生應立即離開課室。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the problem appears as soon as the method is used.","zh":"這個短語顯示問題一使用該方法就出現。"},{"en":"It describes something happening without delay.","zh":"它描述某事毫不延遲地發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"infinite regress","meaning":"無限倒退；無限追溯","examples":[{"en":"Defining words with more words can lead to an infinite regress.","zh":"用更多文字定義詞語可能導致無限倒退。"},{"en":"An infinite regress is a chain of explanations that never reaches a final stopping point.","zh":"無限倒退，是一連串永遠到不了最終終點的解釋。"},{"en":"If every answer needs another answer before it can make sense, the discussion becomes an infinite regress.","zh":"如果每個答案都需要另一個答案才能成立，討論就會變成無限倒退。"},{"en":"Dictionary definitions can create this problem when every word in a definition also needs defining.","zh":"當定義中的每個詞也需要定義，字典定義就可能造成這個問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a never-ending backward chain of explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述永不停止地向後追溯的解釋鏈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"alternatively","meaning":"或者；另外","examples":[{"en":"Alternatively, dictionary definitions can lead to a circular runaround.","zh":"或者，字典定義可能導致繞圈式解釋。"},{"en":"Alternatively means as another possibility or choice.","zh":"alternatively 是指作為另一種可能或選擇。"},{"en":"Students can revise alone; alternatively, they can form a small study group.","zh":"學生可以獨自溫習；或者，他們可以組成小型學習小組。"},{"en":"This word introduces a different way a problem or solution may appear.","zh":"這個詞引入問題或解決方法可能出現的另一方式。"},{"en":"It signals that the writer is offering another option.","zh":"它表示作者正在提供另一個選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get us into","meaning":"使我們陷入……","examples":[{"en":"Defining words with more words can get us into an infinite regress.","zh":"用更多文字定義詞語可能使我們陷入無限倒退。"},{"en":"To get us into something means to cause us to enter or become involved in a situation.","zh":"使我們陷入某事，是指令我們進入或捲入某種情況。"},{"en":"Poor planning can get a group into trouble during a school project.","zh":"缺乏規劃可以使小組在學校專題中陷入麻煩。"},{"en":"A method that seems simple may get us into difficulty if its limits are ignored.","zh":"如果忽略限制，看似簡單的方法可能使我們陷入困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being led into a problem or situation.","zh":"這個短語描述被帶入問題或情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"runaround","meaning":"兜圈子；繞圈式解釋","examples":[{"en":"Some dictionary definitions create a kind of runaround.","zh":"有些字典定義造成一種兜圈子。"},{"en":"A runaround is a confusing circular process in which you are sent from one thing to another without real progress.","zh":"兜圈子，是一種令人困惑的循環過程，人被從一處推到另一處而沒有真正進展。"},{"en":"A customer gets a runaround when each office tells them to ask another office.","zh":"如果每個辦公室都叫顧客去問另一個辦公室，顧客就是被兜圈子。"},{"en":"Circular definitions create a runaround because one word sends you to another and then back again.","zh":"循環定義會造成兜圈子，因為一個詞把你帶到另一個詞，然後又帶回來。"},{"en":"This word describes frustrating movement without a clear answer.","zh":"這個詞描述令人沮喪且沒有清楚答案的來回。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"encounter","meaning":"遇到","examples":[{"en":"We sometimes encounter circular definitions in dictionaries.","zh":"我們有時會在字典中遇到循環定義。"},{"en":"To encounter something means to meet, find or experience it.","zh":"遇到某事，是指見到、發現或經歷它。"},{"en":"A student may encounter a difficult word while reading an article.","zh":"學生閱讀文章時可能遇到一個難詞。"},{"en":"When people encounter a problem repeatedly, they may start to question the method.","zh":"當人們反覆遇到問題，他們可能開始質疑方法。"},{"en":"This word describes coming across something.","zh":"這個詞描述碰到某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"look up","meaning":"查找","examples":[{"en":"We may look up one word and find it defined by another.","zh":"我們可能查找一個詞，卻發現它被另一個詞定義。"},{"en":"To look up a word means to search for its meaning or information about it.","zh":"查找一個詞，是指搜尋其意思或相關資料。"},{"en":"A student may look up an unfamiliar phrase before writing a summary.","zh":"學生可能在寫摘要前查找不熟悉的短語。"},{"en":"Looking up words helps, but it may not explain how people actually use them.","zh":"查找詞語有幫助，但未必能解釋人們實際如何使用它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes searching for information in a dictionary or reference source.","zh":"這個短語描述在字典或參考資料中搜尋資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"defined as","meaning":"被定義為……","examples":[{"en":"One word may be defined as another word with a similar meaning.","zh":"一個詞可能被定義為另一個意思相近的詞。"},{"en":"Defined as means explained or described as something.","zh":"被定義為，是指被解釋或描述成某物。"},{"en":"In a textbook, photosynthesis may be defined as the process by which plants make food.","zh":"在教科書中，光合作用可能被定義為植物製造食物的過程。"},{"en":"A definition is useful only if the explaining words are clear to the learner.","zh":"只有當解釋用詞對學習者清楚，定義才有用。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the wording used to explain a term.","zh":"這個短語引入用來解釋術語的說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"come to another common reaction pattern","meaning":"來到另一種常見反應模式","examples":[{"en":"Here we come to another common reaction pattern.","zh":"這裡我們來到另一種常見反應模式。"},{"en":"To come to another common reaction pattern means to arrive at another usual way people respond.","zh":"來到另一種常見反應模式，是指轉到人們另一種常見回應方式。"},{"en":"In a class discussion, the teacher may come to another common mistake after explaining the first one.","zh":"在課堂討論中，老師解釋第一個錯誤後，可能來到另一個常見錯誤。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to move from one point to the next.","zh":"作者使用這個短語由一點轉到下一點。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a transition to another repeated human response.","zh":"這個短語表示轉向另一種反覆出現的人類反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"act as if","meaning":"表現得好像……","examples":[{"en":"People often act as if words can be fully explained with more words.","zh":"人們常表現得好像詞語可以完全用更多文字解釋。"},{"en":"To act as if something is true means to behave like it is true, whether or not it really is.","zh":"表現得好像某事是真的，是指行為上像它是真的，不論實際是否如此。"},{"en":"A student may act as if homework does not matter, then worry when marks are counted.","zh":"學生可能表現得好像功課不重要，然後在計分時擔心。"},{"en":"People’s behaviour can reveal their assumptions more clearly than their explanations.","zh":"人們的行為可以比他們的解釋更清楚揭示其假設。"},{"en":"This phrase describes behaviour based on an assumed belief.","zh":"這個短語描述基於某個假定信念的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"explained fully","meaning":"被充分解釋","examples":[{"en":"Words cannot always be explained fully with more words.","zh":"詞語不一定總能用更多文字被充分解釋。"},{"en":"Explained fully means made completely clear, with nothing important missing.","zh":"被充分解釋，是指被完全說清楚，沒有遺漏重要部分。"},{"en":"A grammar rule is not explained fully if students still do not know when to use it.","zh":"如果學生仍不知道何時使用某文法規則，它就未被充分解釋。"},{"en":"Some meanings require examples, actions and context, not just more definitions.","zh":"有些意義需要例子、行動和語境，而不只是更多定義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述完整解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ask for a definition of","meaning":"要求對……作出定義","examples":[{"en":"A person once asked for a definition of jazz.","zh":"有人曾要求對爵士樂作出定義。"},{"en":"To ask for a definition of something means to request a clear explanation of its meaning.","zh":"要求對某事作出定義，是指請求清楚解釋其意思。"},{"en":"A student may ask for a definition of “semantic habits” during a reading lesson.","zh":"學生可能在閱讀課中要求對「語義習慣」作出定義。"},{"en":"Asking for a definition helps, but some things are better understood through experience.","zh":"要求定義有幫助，但有些事最好透過經驗理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes requesting a direct explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述請求直接解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be said to have replied","meaning":"據說曾回答","examples":[{"en":"Louis Armstrong is said to have replied with a famous comment.","zh":"據說 Louis Armstrong 曾以一句著名評論回答。"},{"en":"Is said to have replied means people report that someone gave a certain answer.","zh":"據說曾回答，是指人們報稱某人給出某個答案。"},{"en":"The old headmaster is said to have replied calmly during the crisis.","zh":"據說那位舊校長在危機中曾冷靜回答。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when retelling a famous story without proving every detail.","zh":"這個短語適合轉述著名故事，而不必證明每個細節。"},{"en":"It signals reported speech from tradition or memory.","zh":"它表示來自傳統或記憶的轉述說話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"get to know","meaning":"了解；認識","examples":[{"en":"Armstrong suggested that asking what jazz is may prevent people from getting to know it.","zh":"Armstrong 暗示，追問爵士樂是甚麼可能阻礙人們真正了解它。"},{"en":"To get to know something means to understand it through experience, attention or familiarity.","zh":"了解某事，是指透過經驗、注意或熟悉逐漸理解它。"},{"en":"A student gets to know a poem better by reading it aloud several times.","zh":"學生透過多次朗讀詩歌，可以更了解它。"},{"en":"Some things cannot be understood only through definitions; people must experience them.","zh":"有些事不能只透過定義理解；人們必須親身經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual understanding through contact.","zh":"這個短語描述透過接觸逐步理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"proving himself to be","meaning":"證明自己是……","examples":[{"en":"Armstrong proved himself to be an intuitive semanticist.","zh":"Armstrong 證明自己是憑直覺理解語義的人。"},{"en":"Proving himself to be something means showing through words or actions that he has that quality.","zh":"證明自己是某種人，是指透過說話或行動顯示自己有該特質。"},{"en":"A quiet student may prove herself to be a strong leader during a group project.","zh":"安靜學生可能在小組專題中證明自己是強大領袖。"},{"en":"People prove qualities through what they do, not only what they claim.","zh":"人們透過行動證明特質，而不只是透過聲稱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes demonstrating one’s nature or ability.","zh":"這個短語描述展示自己的本質或能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"intuitive semanticist","meaning":"憑直覺理解語義的人","examples":[{"en":"Armstrong was an intuitive semanticist as well as a great trumpet player.","zh":"Armstrong 不但是偉大的小號手，也是憑直覺理解語義的人。"},{"en":"An intuitive semanticist is someone who understands meaning through instinct and experience rather than formal theory.","zh":"憑直覺理解語義的人，是透過本能和經驗，而不是正式理論來理解意義的人。"},{"en":"A good storyteller may be an intuitive semanticist because they know how words affect listeners.","zh":"好說故事的人可能是憑直覺理解語義的人，因為他們知道文字如何影響聽眾。"},{"en":"Such a person senses that meaning depends on use, feeling and response.","zh":"這樣的人感覺到意義取決於使用、感受和反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical understanding of meaning without academic terminology.","zh":"這個短語描述不用學術術語也能實際理解意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"以及；也是","examples":[{"en":"Armstrong was an intuitive semanticist as well as a great musician.","zh":"Armstrong 是偉大音樂家，也是憑直覺理解語義的人。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to or also.","zh":"as well as 意思是「以及」或「也是」。"},{"en":"A good teacher needs patience as well as subject knowledge.","zh":"好老師需要耐性，也需要學科知識。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another quality without replacing the first one.","zh":"這個短語加入另一個特質，而不是取代第一個。"},{"en":"It shows that two things are true at the same time.","zh":"它顯示兩件事同時成立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"trumpet player","meaning":"小號手","examples":[{"en":"Louis Armstrong was a great trumpet player.","zh":"Louis Armstrong 是偉大的小號手。"},{"en":"A trumpet player is a musician who plays the trumpet.","zh":"小號手是演奏小號的音樂家。"},{"en":"A school band may need a trumpet player for a jazz performance.","zh":"學校樂隊可能需要小號手參與爵士樂演出。"},{"en":"A skilled trumpet player can shape mood through sound, rhythm and expression.","zh":"技巧高超的小號手可以透過聲音、節奏和表情塑造氣氛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a person who performs music on the trumpet.","zh":"這個短語描述演奏小號的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"deal with","meaning":"處理；涉及","examples":[{"en":"Semantics does not deal with meaning in the common dictionary sense.","zh":"語義學並不以一般字典意義上的方式處理意義。"},{"en":"To deal with something means to handle, study or be concerned with it.","zh":"處理或涉及某事，是指應對、研究或關注它。"},{"en":"A school counsellor deals with students’ stress and friendship problems.","zh":"學校輔導員處理學生壓力和友情問題。"},{"en":"A subject may deal with a topic in a deeper way than people expect.","zh":"一門學科可能以比人們預期更深入的方式處理某主題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the area something focuses on.","zh":"這個短語描述某事聚焦的範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as that expression is commonly understood","meaning":"按照該說法通常被理解的方式","examples":[{"en":"Semantics does not deal with meaning as that expression is commonly understood.","zh":"語義學並不按照「意義」這個說法通常被理解的方式來處理意義。"},{"en":"As that expression is commonly understood means according to the usual meaning people give to that phrase.","zh":"按照該說法通常被理解的方式，是指根據人們通常賦予該短語的意思。"},{"en":"“Success,” as that expression is commonly understood, often means money or status.","zh":"「成功」按照通常被理解的方式，常指金錢或地位。"},{"en":"A writer may challenge common understanding by giving a more precise meaning.","zh":"作者可能透過給出更精確意思來挑戰一般理解。"},{"en":"This phrase separates ordinary usage from a special or deeper meaning.","zh":"這個短語把普通用法與特殊或更深層意思分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Nobel Prize-winning physicist","meaning":"諾貝爾獎得主物理學家","examples":[{"en":"P. W. Bridgman was a Nobel Prize-winning physicist.","zh":"P. W. Bridgman 是諾貝爾獎得主物理學家。"},{"en":"A Nobel Prize-winning physicist is a scientist in physics who has received the Nobel Prize.","zh":"諾貝爾獎得主物理學家，是獲得諾貝爾獎的物理學科學家。"},{"en":"A Nobel Prize-winning physicist may be invited to speak at a university lecture.","zh":"諾貝爾獎得主物理學家可能受邀到大學演講。"},{"en":"Mentioning this title gives authority to Bridgman’s view about scientific terms.","zh":"提及這個頭銜，令 Bridgman 對科學術語的看法更具權威。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both achievement and field of expertise.","zh":"這個短語同時描述成就和專業領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the true meaning of","meaning":"……的真正意思","examples":[{"en":"Bridgman argued that the true meaning of a term is found in use.","zh":"Bridgman 認為，一個術語的真正意思可在使用中找到。"},{"en":"The true meaning of something is its real or most useful meaning, not just its surface definition.","zh":"某事的真正意思，是它真實或最有用的意思，而不只是表面定義。"},{"en":"The true meaning of “help” may be seen in what a person actually does for others.","zh":"「幫助」的真正意思，可能可從一個人實際為他人做甚麼看出來。"},{"en":"If meaning is found in use, actions matter more than dictionary wording alone.","zh":"如果意義在使用中找到，行動就比單靠字典措辭更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase asks what something really means in practice.","zh":"這個短語追問某事在實際中真正代表甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a term","meaning":"術語；用語","examples":[{"en":"The true meaning of a term is found by observing how it is used.","zh":"一個術語的真正意思可透過觀察它如何被使用找到。"},{"en":"A term is a word or phrase used with a specific meaning in a subject or situation.","zh":"術語是在某學科或情況中具有特定意思的詞語或短語。"},{"en":"“Photosynthesis” is a scientific term students learn in biology.","zh":"“Photosynthesis” 是學生在生物學中學到的科學術語。"},{"en":"Terms can be misunderstood if people know the word but not the operations behind it.","zh":"如果人們知道詞語卻不知道背後操作，就可能誤解術語。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a word or expression with a defined use.","zh":"這個短語指具有明確用法的詞語或表達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be found by observing","meaning":"透過觀察……找到","examples":[{"en":"The meaning of a term is found by observing what a person does with it.","zh":"術語的意思可透過觀察一個人如何使用它找到。"},{"en":"To be found by observing means to be discovered through watching actions or evidence.","zh":"透過觀察找到，是指透過觀看行動或證據來發現。"},{"en":"A teacher may find a student’s real understanding by observing how they solve problems.","zh":"老師可能透過觀察學生如何解題來找出其真正理解。"},{"en":"Observation can reveal meaning that verbal explanations hide.","zh":"觀察可以揭示文字解釋所隱藏的意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes discovery through watching behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述透過觀看行為來發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"what a man does with it","meaning":"一個人如何使用它","examples":[{"en":"The meaning of a term depends on what a person does with it.","zh":"一個術語的意思取決於一個人如何使用它。"},{"en":"What a man does with it means how a person uses the word in action or practice.","zh":"一個人如何使用它，是指一個人在行動或實踐中如何使用該詞。"},{"en":"If someone says “urgent” but waits a week, what they do with the word shows their meaning is weak.","zh":"如果有人說「緊急」卻等一星期才做，他如何使用這個詞顯示其意義很弱。"},{"en":"Actions can show whether a term is serious, symbolic or merely decorative.","zh":"行動可以顯示一個術語是嚴肅、象徵性，還是只是裝飾性。"},{"en":"This phrase points to use rather than explanation.","zh":"這個短語指向使用，而不是解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"what he says about it","meaning":"他對它作出的說明","examples":[{"en":"Meaning is not simply what a person says about a term.","zh":"意義不只是某人對一個術語作出的說明。"},{"en":"What he says about it means the verbal explanation someone gives.","zh":"他對它作出的說明，是指某人給出的口頭解釋。"},{"en":"A student may say they understand grammar, but their writing shows whether that is true.","zh":"學生可能說自己明白文法，但其寫作會顯示是否真的如此。"},{"en":"What people say may differ from what their actions reveal.","zh":"人們所說的可能與行動所揭示的不同。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts spoken explanation with practical use.","zh":"這個短語把口頭解釋與實際使用作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"made an enormous contribution to","meaning":"對……作出巨大貢獻","examples":[{"en":"Bridgman made an enormous contribution to science.","zh":"Bridgman 對科學作出巨大貢獻。"},{"en":"To make an enormous contribution to something means to help it greatly or add something very important.","zh":"對某事作出巨大貢獻，是指大大幫助它或加入非常重要的東西。"},{"en":"A doctor who develops a life-saving vaccine makes an enormous contribution to public health.","zh":"研發救命疫苗的醫生對公共健康作出巨大貢獻。"},{"en":"Important contributions can change how later people think and work.","zh":"重要貢獻可以改變後來人們的思考和工作方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major positive impact.","zh":"這個短語描述重大正面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"scientific term","meaning":"科學術語","examples":[{"en":"The meaning of a scientific term lies in its operations.","zh":"科學術語的意思在於其操作。"},{"en":"A scientific term is a word or phrase used with a precise meaning in science.","zh":"科學術語是在科學中以精確意思使用的詞語或短語。"},{"en":"“Mass” is a scientific term that must be measured carefully.","zh":"“Mass” 是一個必須仔細量度的科學術語。"},{"en":"Scientific terms need clear operations so researchers can test and compare results.","zh":"科學術語需要清楚操作，使研究人員能測試和比較結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes specialised vocabulary used in scientific work.","zh":"這個短語描述科學工作中使用的專門詞彙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lies in","meaning":"在於……","examples":[{"en":"The meaning of a scientific term lies in the operations that establish it.","zh":"科學術語的意思在於確立它的操作。"},{"en":"Lies in means is found in or depends on something.","zh":"在於某事，是指存在於或取決於該事。"},{"en":"The value of a good lesson lies in whether students can use what they learn.","zh":"一堂好課的價值在於學生是否能使用所學。"},{"en":"If meaning lies in action, definitions alone are not enough.","zh":"如果意義在於行動，單靠定義就不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where the real importance or meaning is located.","zh":"這個短語指出真正重要性或意義所在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"operations","meaning":"操作；實際程序","examples":[{"en":"Operations are the things done to establish the validity of a term.","zh":"操作是用來確立術語有效性的實際程序。"},{"en":"Operations are practical procedures or actions used to test, measure or define something.","zh":"操作是用來測試、量度或定義某事的實際程序或行動。"},{"en":"Measuring a desk with a ruler is an operation that checks its length.","zh":"用間尺量度書桌是一個檢查其長度的操作。"},{"en":"Operations make meanings clearer because they show exactly what must be done.","zh":"操作令意義更清楚，因為它顯示必須具體做甚麼。"},{"en":"This word refers to practical steps, not just ideas.","zh":"這個詞指實際步驟，而不只是想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"establish its validity","meaning":"確立其有效性","examples":[{"en":"Operations help establish the validity of a scientific term.","zh":"操作有助確立科學術語的有效性。"},{"en":"To establish its validity means to show that it is correct, useful or properly supported.","zh":"確立其有效性，是指顯示它正確、有用或有充分支持。"},{"en":"A survey can help establish the validity of a claim about student stress.","zh":"調查可以幫助確立關於學生壓力說法的有效性。"},{"en":"Without evidence or operations, a term may sound impressive but remain unclear.","zh":"沒有證據或操作，術語可能聽起來深奧，但仍不清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes proving that something has a reliable basis.","zh":"這個短語描述證明某事有可靠基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Meaning lies in operations rather than in verbal definitions.","zh":"意義在於操作，而不是文字定義。"},{"en":"Rather than shows contrast and means instead of.","zh":"rather than 表示對比，意思是「而不是」。"},{"en":"A good teacher explains with examples rather than only giving rules.","zh":"好老師用例子解釋，而不是只給規則。"},{"en":"The phrase helps separate what matters more from what matters less.","zh":"這個短語幫助區分較重要和較不重要的東西。"},{"en":"It clearly shows that one option is preferred or more accurate than another.","zh":"它清楚顯示一個選項比另一個更可取或更準確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"verbal definitions","meaning":"文字定義","examples":[{"en":"Bridgman emphasised operations rather than verbal definitions.","zh":"Bridgman 強調操作，而不是文字定義。"},{"en":"Verbal definitions are explanations given in words.","zh":"文字定義是用文字給出的解釋。"},{"en":"A dictionary gives verbal definitions, but a science experiment shows how a concept works.","zh":"字典給出文字定義，而科學實驗顯示概念如何運作。"},{"en":"Verbal definitions may be incomplete if they do not connect to action or evidence.","zh":"如果文字定義沒有連接行動或證據，就可能不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase describes word-based explanations.","zh":"這個短語描述以文字為基礎的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"everyday kind of example","meaning":"日常例子","examples":[{"en":"The passage gives an everyday kind of example of operational definition.","zh":"篇章給出一個操作性定義的日常例子。"},{"en":"An everyday kind of example is a simple example from ordinary life.","zh":"日常例子是來自普通生活的簡單例子。"},{"en":"Measuring a table is an everyday kind of example because anyone can understand it.","zh":"量度桌子是一個日常例子，因為任何人都能理解。"},{"en":"Simple examples help learners understand difficult abstract ideas.","zh":"簡單例子幫助學習者理解困難抽象概念。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a familiar example rather than a technical one.","zh":"這個短語描述熟悉例子，而不是技術例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"operational definition","meaning":"操作性定義","examples":[{"en":"Measuring a table provides an example of operational definition.","zh":"量度桌子提供了一個操作性定義的例子。"},{"en":"An operational definition explains meaning by showing the operation used to test or measure it.","zh":"操作性定義是透過顯示用來測試或量度的操作來解釋意思。"},{"en":"To define “late” operationally, a school may say a student is late if they arrive after 8:15.","zh":"若要操作性地定義「遲到」，學校可以說學生在 8:15 後到達就是遲到。"},{"en":"Operational definitions reduce confusion because they tell people exactly what counts.","zh":"操作性定義減少混亂，因為它告訴人們甚麼才算數。"},{"en":"This phrase describes definition through practical procedure.","zh":"這個短語描述透過實際程序作出的定義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"measures six feet in length","meaning":"長六呎","examples":[{"en":"The table measures six feet in length.","zh":"這張桌子長六呎。"},{"en":"Measures six feet in length means has a length of six feet when measured.","zh":"長六呎，是指量度後長度為六呎。"},{"en":"A classroom shelf may measure two metres in length.","zh":"課室書架可能長兩米。"},{"en":"Measurement gives a clear meaning because people can check it with a ruler.","zh":"量度給出清楚意思，因為人們可以用間尺檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the exact measured length of an object.","zh":"這個短語描述物件的精確量度長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"prove it by","meaning":"透過……證明它","examples":[{"en":"You could prove it by using a one-foot ruler.","zh":"你可以透過使用一呎長的間尺來證明它。"},{"en":"To prove it by doing something means to show it is true through that action.","zh":"透過做某事證明它，是指透過該行動顯示它是真的。"},{"en":"A student can prove an answer by showing the calculation step by step.","zh":"學生可以透過一步步顯示計算來證明答案。"},{"en":"Proof becomes stronger when others can repeat the same method.","zh":"當其他人能重複同一方法，證明就更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a claim with the action that tests it.","zh":"這個短語把主張與測試它的行動連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"one-foot ruler","meaning":"一呎長的間尺","examples":[{"en":"A one-foot ruler can be used to measure the table.","zh":"一呎長的間尺可以用來量度桌子。"},{"en":"A one-foot ruler is a ruler that is one foot long.","zh":"一呎長的間尺，是長度為一呎的間尺。"},{"en":"A student may use a one-foot ruler to measure the width of a desk.","zh":"學生可能使用一呎長的間尺量度書桌寬度。"},{"en":"Using a fixed measuring tool makes the operation clear and repeatable.","zh":"使用固定量度工具令操作清楚且可重複。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple measuring instrument.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單量度工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"performing the operation of","meaning":"進行……的操作","examples":[{"en":"You prove the measurement by performing the operation of laying the ruler end to end.","zh":"你透過進行把間尺首尾相接地放置的操作來證明量度。"},{"en":"Performing the operation of something means carrying out a specific practical procedure.","zh":"進行某事的操作，是指執行一個特定實際程序。"},{"en":"A student checks water temperature by performing the operation of placing a thermometer in the cup.","zh":"學生透過把溫度計放入杯中的操作來檢查水溫。"},{"en":"Operations make definitions testable because they show what action must be taken.","zh":"操作令定義可測試，因為它顯示必須採取甚麼行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doing a clear procedure, not just talking about it.","zh":"這個短語描述進行清楚程序，而不只是談論它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"laying it end to end","meaning":"首尾相接地放置","examples":[{"en":"The ruler is laid end to end along the table.","zh":"間尺沿着桌子首尾相接地放置。"},{"en":"Laying it end to end means placing the ruler repeatedly so each new position begins where the last one ended.","zh":"首尾相接地放置，是指反覆放置間尺，使每個新位置從上一個結束位置開始。"},{"en":"Children may measure a classroom wall by laying a ruler end to end along the floor.","zh":"孩子可能透過沿地板首尾相接地放間尺來量度課室牆身。"},{"en":"This method allows a short tool to measure a longer object.","zh":"這個方法讓短工具量度較長物件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated measuring action.","zh":"這個短語描述重複量度動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"while counting","meaning":"一邊數數","examples":[{"en":"The person measures the table while counting each ruler length.","zh":"那人一邊數每個間尺長度，一邊量度桌子。"},{"en":"While counting means at the same time as counting numbers or units.","zh":"一邊數數，是指在數數字或單位的同時做某事。"},{"en":"A child may climb stairs while counting each step.","zh":"孩子可能一邊數每級樓梯，一邊上樓。"},{"en":"Counting during an operation helps turn action into a measurable result.","zh":"在操作中數數幫助把行動變成可量度結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doing one action at the same time as counting.","zh":"這個短語描述做某事同時數數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"revolutionists","meaning":"革命者","examples":[{"en":"Revolutionists have started uprisings with claims about freedom.","zh":"革命者曾以關於自由的主張發動起義。"},{"en":"Revolutionists are people who try to overthrow or radically change a political system.","zh":"革命者是試圖推翻或徹底改變政治制度的人。"},{"en":"In a history lesson, students may study revolutionists who opposed unfair rulers.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生可能研究反對不公統治者的革命者。"},{"en":"Revolutionists often use powerful words because language can move people to action.","zh":"革命者常使用有力量的語言，因為語言可以推動人行動。"},{"en":"This word describes people who seek major political change.","zh":"這個詞描述追求重大政治改變的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"started uprisings","meaning":"發動起義","examples":[{"en":"Revolutionists have started uprisings with statements about freedom.","zh":"革命者曾以關於自由的陳述發動起義。"},{"en":"Started uprisings means began organised rebellions or protests against authority.","zh":"發動起義，是指開始有組織地反抗權威的叛亂或抗議。"},{"en":"Workers may start an uprising if they are treated violently and denied basic rights.","zh":"如果工人遭暴力對待並被剝奪基本權利，可能發動起義。"},{"en":"Strong political language can help turn anger into collective action.","zh":"強烈政治語言可以幫助把憤怒轉化為集體行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes beginning a revolt or rebellion.","zh":"這個短語描述開始反抗或叛亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"born free","meaning":"生而自由","examples":[{"en":"Some revolutionists claim that man is born free.","zh":"有些革命者聲稱人是生而自由的。"},{"en":"Born free means naturally free from birth, before society imposes limits.","zh":"生而自由，是指人從出生起天然自由，在社會施加限制之前已自由。"},{"en":"A speaker may say that every child is born free and deserves basic rights.","zh":"演講者可能說每個孩子都生而自由，應享有基本權利。"},{"en":"The phrase can inspire political action because it suggests freedom is natural, not a gift from rulers.","zh":"這個短語可以激發政治行動，因為它暗示自由是自然的，不是統治者賜予的。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses an idea about human rights and natural liberty.","zh":"這個短語表達關於人權和自然自由的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in chains","meaning":"受束縛；被枷鎖束縛","examples":[{"en":"The statement says that man is everywhere in chains.","zh":"這句話說人到處都受束縛。"},{"en":"In chains means restricted, controlled or not truly free.","zh":"受束縛，是指受到限制、控制或並非真正自由。"},{"en":"A worker trapped by debt and unfair contracts may feel in chains.","zh":"被債務和不公平合約困住的工人，可能覺得自己受束縛。"},{"en":"The phrase is powerful because it turns social limits into the image of physical imprisonment.","zh":"這個短語有力量，因為它把社會限制轉化成身體被囚的形象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes loss of freedom, often metaphorically.","zh":"這個短語描述失去自由，常以比喻方式使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"perform operations","meaning":"進行操作","examples":[{"en":"Some statements cannot easily be tested by performing operations.","zh":"有些陳述不能輕易透過進行操作來測試。"},{"en":"To perform operations means to carry out practical steps or procedures.","zh":"進行操作，是指執行實際步驟或程序。"},{"en":"Students perform operations when they measure water temperature in a science experiment.","zh":"學生在科學實驗中量度水溫時，就是在進行操作。"},{"en":"A statement is easier to test if clear operations can show whether it is true.","zh":"如果清楚操作能顯示某陳述是否為真，該陳述就較容易測試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doing practical actions to check a claim.","zh":"這個短語描述進行實際行動來檢查主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"demonstrate its accuracy or inaccuracy","meaning":"證明其準確或不準確","examples":[{"en":"It is hard to demonstrate the accuracy or inaccuracy of some statements.","zh":"有些陳述很難證明其準確或不準確。"},{"en":"To demonstrate accuracy or inaccuracy means to show whether something is correct or incorrect.","zh":"證明準確或不準確，是指顯示某事正確還是錯誤。"},{"en":"A teacher can demonstrate the accuracy of an answer by solving the problem step by step.","zh":"老師可以透過一步步解題來證明答案準確。"},{"en":"Some political statements are difficult to test because they are broad and abstract.","zh":"有些政治陳述難以測試，因為它們廣泛而抽象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes proving whether a claim is right or wrong.","zh":"這個短語描述證明一個主張對或錯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"carry this suggestion outside","meaning":"將這個建議帶到……之外","examples":[{"en":"The writer carries the suggestion of operationalism outside the physical sciences.","zh":"作者將操作主義這個建議帶到自然科學之外。"},{"en":"To carry this suggestion outside a field means to apply the idea beyond its original area.","zh":"將這個建議帶到某領域之外，是指把該想法應用到原本範圍以外。"},{"en":"A teacher may carry a study method outside English lessons and use it in history class.","zh":"老師可能把一種學習方法帶到英文課之外，並用於歷史課。"},{"en":"Ideas can become more powerful when they are tested in new contexts.","zh":"當想法在新語境中被測試，它們可能變得更有力量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extending an idea beyond where it first belonged.","zh":"這個短語描述把想法擴展到原本所屬範圍之外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"operationalism","meaning":"操作主義","examples":[{"en":"The writer applies operationalism to language and human behaviour.","zh":"作者把操作主義應用於語言和人類行為。"},{"en":"Operationalism is the idea that meanings should be understood through operations or actions.","zh":"操作主義是一種認為意義應透過操作或行動來理解的想法。"},{"en":"A school may define “attendance” operationally by counting whether students are present before 8:00.","zh":"學校可以透過計算學生是否在 8 點前到場，操作性地定義「出席」。"},{"en":"Operationalism reduces vague debate by asking what people actually do or measure.","zh":"操作主義透過追問人們實際做甚麼或量度甚麼，減少含糊爭論。"},{"en":"This word describes an approach that links meaning with practical procedures.","zh":"這個詞描述把意義與實際程序連接的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"physical sciences","meaning":"自然科學；物理科學","examples":[{"en":"Bridgman applied operationalism in the physical sciences.","zh":"Bridgman 把操作主義應用於物理科學。"},{"en":"Physical sciences are sciences that study non-living matter and energy, such as physics and chemistry.","zh":"物理科學是研究非生命物質和能量的科學，例如物理和化學。"},{"en":"Students study physical sciences when they learn about forces, heat and atoms.","zh":"學生學習力、熱和原子時，就是在學物理科學。"},{"en":"These subjects often depend on measurement, experiment and repeatable operations.","zh":"這些學科通常依賴量度、實驗和可重複操作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to scientific fields concerned with the physical world.","zh":"這個短語指關注物理世界的科學領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"applied it","meaning":"應用它","examples":[{"en":"Bridgman applied operationalism to the physical sciences.","zh":"Bridgman 把操作主義應用於物理科學。"},{"en":"Applied it means used an idea, rule or method in a particular situation.","zh":"應用它，是指在特定情況中使用某個想法、規則或方法。"},{"en":"A student learned a grammar rule and applied it in an essay.","zh":"學生學會一條文法規則，並在文章中應用它。"},{"en":"An idea becomes useful when people apply it to real examples.","zh":"當人們把想法應用到真實例子，它就變得有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes putting a concept into practice.","zh":"這個短語描述把概念付諸實踐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"observe what operations people perform","meaning":"觀察人們進行甚麼操作","examples":[{"en":"The writer asks us to observe what operations people perform after using language.","zh":"作者要求我們觀察人們使用語言後進行甚麼操作。"},{"en":"To observe what operations people perform means to watch what actions people carry out.","zh":"觀察人們進行甚麼操作，是指觀看人們實際執行甚麼行動。"},{"en":"A teacher may observe what operations students perform when solving a maths problem.","zh":"老師可能觀察學生解數學題時進行甚麼操作。"},{"en":"Actions after words can reveal what those words mean to the speaker.","zh":"說話後的行動可以揭示那些話對說話者有甚麼意思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes studying meaning through behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述透過行為研究意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as the result of","meaning":"由於；作為……的結果","examples":[{"en":"People perform operations as the result of language.","zh":"人們由於語言而進行操作。"},{"en":"As the result of something means because that thing has produced an effect.","zh":"作為某事的結果，是指因為該事產生了影響。"},{"en":"A child may apologise as the result of a parent’s reminder.","zh":"孩子可能因父母提醒而道歉。"},{"en":"Words can lead to action when they trigger learned responses.","zh":"當詞語觸發學得的反應，它們就可以導致行動。"},{"en":"This phrase connects behaviour with the cause behind it.","zh":"這個短語把行為與其背後原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the language they use","meaning":"他們使用的語言","examples":[{"en":"People’s actions are affected by the language they use.","zh":"人們的行動受他們使用的語言影響。"},{"en":"The language they use means the words, phrases and expressions people choose.","zh":"他們使用的語言，是指人們選擇的詞語、短語和表達。"},{"en":"A manager who uses respectful language may receive calmer responses from staff.","zh":"使用尊重語言的經理，可能從員工那裡得到較冷靜的回應。"},{"en":"Language can shape behaviour because words carry learned associations.","zh":"語言可以塑造行為，因為詞語帶有學得的聯想。"},{"en":"This phrase describes language as an active influence on action.","zh":"這個短語描述語言作為對行動的主動影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in communicating with","meaning":"與……溝通時","examples":[{"en":"Language affects people in communicating with one another.","zh":"語言在人們彼此溝通時影響他們。"},{"en":"In communicating with someone means while exchanging information, ideas or feelings with that person.","zh":"與某人溝通時，是指與該人交換資訊、想法或感受時。"},{"en":"Students learn politeness strategies in communicating with teachers and classmates.","zh":"學生在與老師和同學溝通時學習禮貌策略。"},{"en":"The words people choose can change how others respond during communication.","zh":"人們選擇的詞語可以改變他人在溝通中的反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what happens during interaction.","zh":"這個短語描述互動期間發生甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"personnel manager","meaning":"人事經理","examples":[{"en":"A personnel manager studies an application blank.","zh":"人事經理查看一份申請表。"},{"en":"A personnel manager is a person responsible for hiring, staff records and employee matters.","zh":"人事經理是負責招聘、員工記錄和僱員事務的人。"},{"en":"A personnel manager may decide which applicants should be invited for an interview.","zh":"人事經理可能決定哪些申請者應被邀請面試。"},{"en":"Their reactions to words on an application form can affect a candidate’s future.","zh":"他們對申請表上文字的反應可以影響候選人的未來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a staff-management role.","zh":"這個短語描述人事管理職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"application blank","meaning":"申請表","examples":[{"en":"The personnel manager studies an application blank.","zh":"人事經理查看一份申請表。"},{"en":"An application blank is a form that a person fills in when applying for a job or place.","zh":"申請表是人在申請工作或名額時填寫的表格。"},{"en":"A student may complete an application blank for a summer internship.","zh":"學生可能填寫暑期實習申請表。"},{"en":"The words written on a form can influence how the reader judges the applicant.","zh":"表格上所寫的文字可以影響讀者如何評價申請者。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an application form.","zh":"這個短語指申請表格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"come to the words","meaning":"看到……這些字","examples":[{"en":"The manager comes to the words “Education: Harvard University”.","zh":"經理看到「教育：哈佛大學」這些字。"},{"en":"To come to the words means to reach and read a particular part of a text.","zh":"看到某些字，是指讀到文本中的某個特定部分。"},{"en":"A teacher marking an essay may come to the words “in conclusion” near the final paragraph.","zh":"老師批改文章時，可能在最後一段附近看到 “in conclusion” 這些字。"},{"en":"A reader’s reaction may change when they reach certain words.","zh":"讀者看到某些字時，反應可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arriving at a specific phrase while reading.","zh":"這個短語描述閱讀時到達某個特定短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"drop something in the wastebasket","meaning":"把……丟進廢紙簍","examples":[{"en":"The manager drops the application blank in the wastebasket.","zh":"經理把申請表丟進廢紙簍。"},{"en":"To drop something in the wastebasket means to throw it away in a rubbish bin.","zh":"把某物丟進廢紙簍，是指把它丟入垃圾桶。"},{"en":"A student may drop an old worksheet in the wastebasket after the lesson.","zh":"學生可能在課後把舊工作紙丟進廢紙簍。"},{"en":"In the passage, the action shows the manager’s negative reaction to certain words.","zh":"在篇章中，這個行動顯示經理對某些字的負面反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical action that can reveal meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述能揭示意義的實際動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as he would say","meaning":"正如他會說的那樣","examples":[{"en":"As he would say if asked, he does not like Harvard men.","zh":"正如他若被問到會說的那樣，他不喜歡哈佛人。"},{"en":"As he would say means according to what he would probably explain.","zh":"正如他會說的那樣，是指按照他大概會給出的解釋。"},{"en":"As my teacher would say, examples are more useful than memorised definitions.","zh":"正如我老師會說的那樣，例子比背熟定義更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a likely explanation from the person involved.","zh":"這個短語引入當事人可能給出的解釋。"},{"en":"It connects action with the reason the person might give.","zh":"它把行動與該人可能提供的原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"an instance of","meaning":"……的一個例子","examples":[{"en":"This is an instance of meaning at work.","zh":"這是意義正在發揮作用的一個例子。"},{"en":"An instance of something is a specific example of it.","zh":"某事的一個例子，是它的一個具體個案。"},{"en":"A student helping a classmate is an instance of kindness in action.","zh":"學生幫助同學，是善意付諸行動的一個例子。"},{"en":"Particular instances help explain broad ideas by making them concrete.","zh":"具體例子透過令抽象想法具體化來幫助解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a case that shows a general concept.","zh":"這個短語引入展示一般概念的個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"meaning at work","meaning":"意義正在發揮作用","examples":[{"en":"The manager’s action is an example of meaning at work.","zh":"經理的行動是意義正在發揮作用的例子。"},{"en":"Meaning at work means meaning shown through real effects, choices or behaviour.","zh":"意義正在發揮作用，是指意義透過真實影響、選擇或行為顯示出來。"},{"en":"If the word “urgent” makes everyone stop other tasks, that is meaning at work.","zh":"如果「緊急」一詞令每個人停止其他工作，那就是意義正在發揮作用。"},{"en":"Meaning is at work when a word changes what people actually do.","zh":"當一個詞改變人們實際做甚麼，意義就在發揮作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaning operating in real life.","zh":"這個短語描述意義在現實生活中運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"found in dictionaries","meaning":"在字典中找到","examples":[{"en":"This kind of meaning cannot be found in dictionaries.","zh":"這種意義不能在字典中找到。"},{"en":"Found in dictionaries means located or explained in dictionary entries.","zh":"在字典中找到，是指在字典條目中找到或得到解釋。"},{"en":"The emotional meaning of a nickname may not be found in dictionaries.","zh":"暱稱的情感意義可能不能在字典中找到。"},{"en":"Dictionaries can define words, but they may not show each person’s private reaction.","zh":"字典可以定義詞語，但未必顯示每個人的私人反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaning available through dictionary reference.","zh":"這個短語描述可透過字典參考取得的意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"seem to be taking a long time","meaning":"似乎花了很長時間","examples":[{"en":"The writer seems to be taking a long time to explain semantics.","zh":"作者似乎花了很長時間來解釋語義學。"},{"en":"Seems to be taking a long time means appears to be using more time than expected.","zh":"似乎花了很長時間，是指看起來比預期用了更多時間。"},{"en":"A teacher may seem to be taking a long time to explain a simple grammar point.","zh":"老師可能似乎花了很長時間解釋一個簡單文法點。"},{"en":"Sometimes a long explanation is needed because the idea is deeper than it first appears.","zh":"有時需要長解釋，因為概念比表面看來更深。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the impression that something is slow or extended.","zh":"這個短語描述某事給人緩慢或拉長的印象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in the course of explanation","meaning":"在解釋過程中","examples":[{"en":"The writer introduces a way of thinking in the course of explanation.","zh":"作者在解釋過程中介紹一種思考方式。"},{"en":"In the course of explanation means while explaining something.","zh":"在解釋過程中，是指在解釋某事時。"},{"en":"In the course of explaining an essay, a teacher may also teach useful vocabulary.","zh":"老師在解釋文章過程中，可能也教有用詞彙。"},{"en":"A writer can introduce a new method while clarifying a difficult idea.","zh":"作者可以在澄清困難概念時介紹新方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something happening during an explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述某事在解釋期間發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"introduce the reader to","meaning":"向讀者介紹……","examples":[{"en":"The writer introduces the reader to a way of looking at behaviour.","zh":"作者向讀者介紹一種看待行為的方式。"},{"en":"To introduce the reader to something means to present a new idea or topic to the reader.","zh":"向讀者介紹某事，是指把新想法或主題呈現給讀者。"},{"en":"A textbook may introduce the reader to basic economics before discussing inflation.","zh":"教科書可能先向讀者介紹基礎經濟學，再討論通脹。"},{"en":"Introducing a concept gradually helps readers understand unfamiliar material.","zh":"逐步介紹概念幫助讀者理解陌生材料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes guiding readers into a new subject.","zh":"這個短語描述引導讀者進入新主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a certain way of looking at","meaning":"看待……的某種方式","examples":[{"en":"The passage presents a certain way of looking at human behaviour.","zh":"篇章提出一種看待人類行為的方式。"},{"en":"A certain way of looking at something is a particular perspective or method of understanding it.","zh":"看待某事的某種方式，是理解它的特定角度或方法。"},{"en":"A counsellor may offer a new way of looking at failure as feedback rather than shame.","zh":"輔導員可能提供一種新方式，把失敗看作回饋而不是羞恥。"},{"en":"A new perspective can change what people notice and how they interpret it.","zh":"新角度可以改變人們注意到甚麼以及如何詮釋它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific viewpoint or analytical approach.","zh":"這個短語描述特定觀點或分析方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"human behaviour","meaning":"人類行為","examples":[{"en":"Semantics offers a way of looking at human behaviour.","zh":"語義學提供一種看待人類行為的方式。"},{"en":"Human behaviour is what people do, say and how they react.","zh":"人類行為是人們做甚麼、說甚麼以及如何反應。"},{"en":"A psychologist may study human behaviour by observing how students respond to stress.","zh":"心理學家可能透過觀察學生如何回應壓力來研究人類行為。"},{"en":"Words and symbols affect behaviour because people attach meanings to them.","zh":"文字和符號會影響行為，因為人們把意義附加於它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes human actions and reactions.","zh":"這個短語描述人類的行動和反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"專注於……","examples":[{"en":"The writer focuses on human responses.","zh":"作者專注於人類反應。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give special attention to it.","zh":"專注於某事，是指特別注意它。"},{"en":"A student should focus on the main idea before answering a reading question.","zh":"學生回答閱讀題前應先專注於主旨。"},{"en":"Focusing on responses helps the writer move away from dictionary definitions alone.","zh":"專注於反應幫助作者離開單靠字典定義的做法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes concentrating attention on one topic.","zh":"這個短語描述把注意力集中在某一主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"so far as we know","meaning":"就我們所知","examples":[{"en":"So far as we know, human beings are the only creatures with this symbolic capacity.","zh":"就我們所知，人類是唯一具有這種符號能力的生物。"},{"en":"So far as we know means based on current knowledge, though future evidence could change it.","zh":"就我們所知，是指根據目前知識而言，雖然未來證據可能改變它。"},{"en":"So far as we know, no students were injured during the fire drill.","zh":"就我們所知，沒有學生在消防演習中受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a claim cautious and evidence-based.","zh":"這個短語令說法較謹慎並以證據為基礎。"},{"en":"It signals that the statement is limited by what is currently known.","zh":"它表示陳述受目前所知限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"human beings","meaning":"人類","examples":[{"en":"Human beings can manufacture symbols and systems of symbols.","zh":"人類可以製造符號和符號系統。"},{"en":"Human beings are people as a species.","zh":"人類是作為一個物種的人。"},{"en":"Human beings use language, money, flags and signs to organise society.","zh":"人類使用語言、金錢、旗幟和標誌來組織社會。"},{"en":"Their symbolic ability allows them to react to meanings that are not physically present.","zh":"他們的符號能力讓他們能對並非實際存在於眼前的意義作出反應。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to humans in a broad, general sense.","zh":"這個短語以廣泛一般方式指人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"over and above","meaning":"除了……之外；超越……","examples":[{"en":"Human beings have symbolic capacity over and above biological equipment.","zh":"人類除了生理配備之外，還有符號能力。"},{"en":"Over and above means in addition to and beyond something.","zh":"over and above 是指除了某物之外，並超越它。"},{"en":"A good teacher needs patience over and above subject knowledge.","zh":"好老師除了學科知識之外，還需要耐性。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises an extra ability added to basic physical capacities.","zh":"這個短語強調在基本身體能力之外加上的額外能力。"},{"en":"It shows that humans have more than ordinary biological functions.","zh":"它顯示人類擁有超越普通生物功能的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"biological equipment","meaning":"生物本能；生理配備","examples":[{"en":"Humans share biological equipment with other creatures.","zh":"人類與其他生物共有生理配備。"},{"en":"Biological equipment means the natural body systems and instincts living creatures have.","zh":"生理配備，是生物擁有的自然身體系統和本能。"},{"en":"Eyes, ears, muscles and nerves are part of our biological equipment.","zh":"眼睛、耳朵、肌肉和神經都是我們生理配備的一部分。"},{"en":"Humans share many body functions with animals, but symbols add another level of behaviour.","zh":"人類與動物共享許多身體功能，但符號為行為加入另一層次。"},{"en":"This phrase describes natural physical capacities.","zh":"這個短語描述自然身體能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have in common with","meaning":"與……共有","examples":[{"en":"Humans have certain biological equipment in common with other creatures.","zh":"人類與其他生物共有某些生理配備。"},{"en":"To have something in common with others means to share it with them.","zh":"與他人共有某物，是指與他們分享或同樣擁有它。"},{"en":"Students from different schools may have exam stress in common.","zh":"來自不同學校的學生可能共有考試壓力。"},{"en":"Shared features help compare humans with other living creatures.","zh":"共同特徵有助比較人類與其他生物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes similarity or shared possession.","zh":"這個短語描述相似或共同擁有。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"additional capacity for","meaning":"額外的……能力","examples":[{"en":"Humans have an additional capacity for manufacturing symbols.","zh":"人類有額外的製造符號能力。"},{"en":"An additional capacity for something is an extra ability to do it.","zh":"額外的某種能力，是做該事的附加能力。"},{"en":"A bilingual student has an additional capacity for communicating with different communities.","zh":"雙語學生有額外能力與不同社群溝通。"},{"en":"Extra capacity allows people to do more than basic survival tasks.","zh":"額外能力讓人能做超越基本生存任務的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an added ability beyond what is already present.","zh":"這個短語描述在已有能力之外增加的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"manufacturing symbols","meaning":"製造符號","examples":[{"en":"Humans have the capacity for manufacturing symbols.","zh":"人類有製造符號的能力。"},{"en":"Manufacturing symbols means creating signs, words or objects that stand for meanings.","zh":"製造符號，是創造代表意義的標誌、詞語或物件。"},{"en":"A school manufactures symbols when it creates a badge, motto and uniform colours.","zh":"學校創造校徽、校訓和制服顏色時，就是在製造符號。"},{"en":"Symbols help groups communicate ideas quickly and emotionally.","zh":"符號幫助群體快速而有情感地傳達想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the human ability to create meaningful signs.","zh":"這個短語描述人類創造有意義標誌的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"systems of symbols","meaning":"符號系統","examples":[{"en":"Human beings create systems of symbols.","zh":"人類創造符號系統。"},{"en":"Systems of symbols are organised sets of signs that work together to carry meaning.","zh":"符號系統是共同運作以承載意義的一組有組織標誌。"},{"en":"Written language is a system of symbols made from letters, words and punctuation.","zh":"書面語言是由字母、詞語和標點組成的符號系統。"},{"en":"A symbol system works only when people learn how to interpret its parts.","zh":"符號系統只有在人們學會如何詮釋其部分時才有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised networks of meaningful signs.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的有意義標誌網絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"react to a flag","meaning":"對旗幟作出反應","examples":[{"en":"When people react to a flag, they react to its symbolic meaning.","zh":"當人們對旗幟作出反應時，他們是在對其象徵意義作出反應。"},{"en":"To react to a flag means to respond emotionally or behaviourally to what the flag represents.","zh":"對旗幟作出反應，是指對旗幟所代表的東西作出情緒或行為回應。"},{"en":"People may stand quietly when a national flag is raised.","zh":"當國旗升起時，人們可能安靜站立。"},{"en":"The reaction is not to cloth alone, but to the history and identity attached to it.","zh":"反應並不是單純對布，而是對附加在它上面的歷史和身份。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how symbols can produce real human responses.","zh":"這個短語顯示符號如何產生真實人類反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"not reacting simply to","meaning":"並非單純對……作出反應","examples":[{"en":"People are not reacting simply to a piece of cloth.","zh":"人們並非單純對一塊布作出反應。"},{"en":"Not reacting simply to something means the response is not caused only by the physical object itself.","zh":"並非單純對某物作出反應，是指反應不只是由實物本身造成。"},{"en":"When students cheer for a school badge, they are not reacting simply to coloured fabric.","zh":"當學生為校徽歡呼時，他們並非單純對彩色布料作出反應。"},{"en":"Their reaction comes from the memories and values connected with the symbol.","zh":"他們的反應來自與該符號相連的記憶和價值。"},{"en":"This phrase separates physical object from symbolic meaning.","zh":"這個短語把物理物件與象徵意義分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a piece of cloth","meaning":"一塊布","examples":[{"en":"A flag is physically a piece of cloth.","zh":"旗幟在物理上是一塊布。"},{"en":"A piece of cloth is a small or specific amount of fabric.","zh":"一塊布，是一小片或特定數量的布料。"},{"en":"A tailor may use a piece of cloth to repair a torn sleeve.","zh":"裁縫可能用一塊布修補破了的袖子。"},{"en":"A flag is more than cloth because society gives it symbolic meaning.","zh":"旗幟不只是布，因為社會賦予它象徵意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the material object before meaning is added.","zh":"這個短語描述加入意義前的物質物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be symbolically endowed","meaning":"被賦予象徵意義","examples":[{"en":"A flag is symbolically endowed with meaning.","zh":"旗幟被賦予象徵意義。"},{"en":"To be symbolically endowed with something means to be given meaning through social or cultural agreement.","zh":"被賦予象徵意義，是指透過社會或文化共識被給予意義。"},{"en":"A school ring may be symbolically endowed with memories of graduation and friendship.","zh":"學校戒指可能被賦予畢業和友情回憶的象徵意義。"},{"en":"Objects become meaningful when people attach shared stories, values or loyalties to them.","zh":"當人們把共享故事、價值或忠誠附加於物件，它們就變得有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaning being added symbolically.","zh":"這個短語描述意義以象徵方式被加入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a set of sounds","meaning":"一組聲音","examples":[{"en":"A spoken word is a set of sounds.","zh":"口語詞是一組聲音。"},{"en":"A set of sounds means several sounds arranged together.","zh":"一組聲音，是幾個聲音按一定方式排列在一起。"},{"en":"A baby may hear a set of sounds before learning that it forms a word.","zh":"嬰兒可能先聽到一組聲音，後來才學到它形成一個詞。"},{"en":"Sounds become language only when people connect them with meanings.","zh":"只有當人們把聲音與意義連接起來，聲音才變成語言。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical sound form of speech.","zh":"這個短語描述說話的物理聲音形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a basic idea in","meaning":"……中的一個基本概念","examples":[{"en":"A basic idea in general semantics is that meaning is in reactions.","zh":"普通語義學中的一個基本概念是意義存在於反應中。"},{"en":"A basic idea in a subject is one of its central and simple principles.","zh":"某學科中的基本概念，是其核心而簡單的原則之一。"},{"en":"A basic idea in biology is that living things need energy.","zh":"生物學中的一個基本概念是生命體需要能量。"},{"en":"Basic ideas guide how students understand later, more difficult points.","zh":"基本概念引導學生理解後來更困難的重點。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a foundation concept in a field.","zh":"這個短語引入某領域中的基礎概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"general semantics","meaning":"普通語義學","examples":[{"en":"General semantics studies meaning through human reactions.","zh":"普通語義學透過人類反應研究意義。"},{"en":"General semantics is a field that examines how language and symbols affect human thought and behaviour.","zh":"普通語義學是一個研究語言和符號如何影響人類思想與行為的領域。"},{"en":"A class on general semantics may ask why people react strongly to certain labels.","zh":"普通語義學課堂可能追問人們為何對某些標籤反應強烈。"},{"en":"It focuses on responses because meaning is shown in what people do with words.","zh":"它專注於反應，因為意義表現在人們如何使用詞語。"},{"en":"This phrase names an approach to meaning and communication.","zh":"這個短語命名一種研究意義和溝通的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"other symbols","meaning":"其他符號","examples":[{"en":"The meaning of words or other symbols is not in the symbols themselves.","zh":"詞語或其他符號的意義並不在符號本身。"},{"en":"Other symbols are signs besides words, such as flags, numbers, logos or gestures.","zh":"其他符號是詞語以外的標誌，例如旗幟、數字、標誌或手勢。"},{"en":"A school logo is one of the other symbols students may connect with identity.","zh":"校徽是學生可能與身份連接的其他符號之一。"},{"en":"Symbols work because people learn what reactions and meanings to attach to them.","zh":"符號之所以有效，是因為人們學會把甚麼反應和意義附加於它們。"},{"en":"This phrase expands the discussion beyond spoken or written words.","zh":"這個短語把討論由口頭或書面詞語擴展出去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"not in the words","meaning":"不在詞語本身","examples":[{"en":"Meaning is not in the words themselves.","zh":"意義不在詞語本身。"},{"en":"Not in the words means not contained inside the printed or spoken forms alone.","zh":"不在詞語本身，是指並不只包含在印刷或口頭形式之內。"},{"en":"The word “home” is not meaningful only because of its letters, but because of our experiences with it.","zh":"“Home” 這個詞有意義，不只是因為它的字母，而是因為我們與它相關的經驗。"},{"en":"Words gain meaning through use, context and reaction.","zh":"詞語透過使用、語境和反應獲得意義。"},{"en":"This phrase challenges the idea that meanings sit inside words like objects.","zh":"這個短語挑戰意義像物件一樣藏在詞語裡的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"semantic reactions","meaning":"語義反應","examples":[{"en":"Meaning is found in our semantic reactions.","zh":"意義存在於我們的語義反應中。"},{"en":"Semantic reactions are the responses people have to meanings, words and symbols.","zh":"語義反應是人們對意義、詞語和符號產生的回應。"},{"en":"If a national song makes people stand up, that action is a semantic reaction.","zh":"如果國歌令人站起來，那個行動就是語義反應。"},{"en":"Studying reactions shows what symbols actually mean to people.","zh":"研究反應可以顯示符號對人們實際上有甚麼意思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaning-related responses.","zh":"這個短語描述與意義相關的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"shockingly obscene story","meaning":"令人震驚的淫褻故事","examples":[{"en":"An obscene story in an unknown language would not shock the audience.","zh":"一個用未知語言講出的淫褻故事不會震驚觀眾。"},{"en":"A shockingly obscene story is a story that would strongly offend people if they understood it.","zh":"令人震驚的淫褻故事，是如果人們理解就會強烈冒犯他們的故事。"},{"en":"A rude joke may be shocking only to people who understand its language and social meaning.","zh":"粗俗笑話可能只會震驚理解其語言和社會意義的人。"},{"en":"Without understanding, the sounds may not create embarrassment or offence.","zh":"沒有理解，那些聲音可能不會造成尷尬或冒犯。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that shock depends on interpretation, not sound alone.","zh":"這個短語顯示震驚取決於詮釋，而不是單靠聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"before an audience","meaning":"在觀眾面前","examples":[{"en":"The story is told before an audience that understands only English.","zh":"這個故事在一群只懂英語的觀眾面前講述。"},{"en":"Before an audience means in front of people who are listening or watching.","zh":"在觀眾面前，是指在聆聽或觀看的人面前。"},{"en":"A student may give a speech before an audience of classmates and teachers.","zh":"學生可能在同學和老師組成的觀眾面前演講。"},{"en":"Audience reaction depends on whether listeners understand what is being said.","zh":"觀眾反應取決於聽眾是否理解所說內容。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public presentation in front of listeners.","zh":"這個短語描述在聽眾面前公開呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"understood only English","meaning":"只懂英語","examples":[{"en":"The audience understood only English.","zh":"觀眾只懂英語。"},{"en":"Understood only English means could understand English and no other language in that situation.","zh":"只懂英語，是指在該情況下只能理解英語，不能理解其他語言。"},{"en":"If tourists understood only English, a Japanese announcement might mean nothing to them.","zh":"如果遊客只懂英語，日語廣播對他們可能沒有意義。"},{"en":"A message cannot produce its intended reaction if the audience cannot understand the language.","zh":"如果觀眾不理解語言，訊息就不能產生預期反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a limit in language comprehension.","zh":"這個短語描述語言理解能力的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no one would blush","meaning":"沒有人會臉紅","examples":[{"en":"If the audience did not understand the language, no one would blush.","zh":"如果觀眾不理解該語言，沒有人會臉紅。"},{"en":"No one would blush means nobody would become embarrassed or ashamed.","zh":"沒有人會臉紅，是指沒有人會感到尷尬或羞愧。"},{"en":"If students do not understand a rude word in another language, no one may blush.","zh":"如果學生不理解另一語言中的粗俗詞，可能沒有人會臉紅。"},{"en":"Embarrassment depends on recognising the meaning, not merely hearing sounds.","zh":"尷尬取決於認出意思，而不只是聽到聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that emotional reaction depends on understanding.","zh":"這個短語顯示情緒反應取決於理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"neither shocking nor obscene","meaning":"既不令人震驚也不淫褻","examples":[{"en":"The story would be neither shocking nor obscene to people who did not understand it.","zh":"對不理解它的人來說，這個故事既不令人震驚也不淫褻。"},{"en":"Neither shocking nor obscene means not causing shock and not seeming sexually or morally offensive.","zh":"既不令人震驚也不淫褻，是指不造成震驚，也不顯得在性或道德上冒犯。"},{"en":"A rude joke in an unknown language may be neither funny nor offensive to a listener.","zh":"未知語言中的粗俗笑話，對聽眾來說可能既不好笑也不冒犯。"},{"en":"Words lose their social effect when the audience cannot interpret them.","zh":"當觀眾不能詮釋詞語，詞語就失去其社會效果。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that meaning depends on shared understanding.","zh":"這個短語顯示意義取決於共享理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"indeed","meaning":"事實上；甚至","examples":[{"en":"Indeed, the speech would not even be a story to that audience.","zh":"事實上，對那群觀眾而言，這段說話甚至不會是一個故事。"},{"en":"Indeed emphasises or strengthens the point just made.","zh":"indeed 用來強調或加強剛才提出的重點。"},{"en":"The exam was difficult; indeed, several students could not finish it.","zh":"考試很難；事實上，有幾名學生未能完成。"},{"en":"This word adds force by showing that the situation goes even further.","zh":"這個詞透過顯示情況更進一步來加強語氣。"},{"en":"It is used when the next point confirms or intensifies the previous one.","zh":"當下一點確認或強化前一點時會使用它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"likewise","meaning":"同樣地","examples":[{"en":"Likewise, the value of money depends on shared agreement.","zh":"同樣地，金錢的價值取決於共享共識。"},{"en":"Likewise means in the same way or similarly.","zh":"likewise 意思是以同樣方式或相似地。"},{"en":"Students need practice to improve writing; likewise, they need speaking practice to improve fluency.","zh":"學生需要練習來改善寫作；同樣地，他們需要口語練習來改善流暢度。"},{"en":"This word connects two examples that follow the same logic.","zh":"這個詞連接兩個遵循同一邏輯的例子。"},{"en":"It signals that a similar principle applies to the next case.","zh":"它表示相似原則適用於下一個情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"dollar bill","meaning":"一美元紙幣","examples":[{"en":"The value of a dollar bill is not in the bill itself.","zh":"一美元紙幣的價值不在紙幣本身。"},{"en":"A dollar bill is a piece of paper money worth one dollar in the United States.","zh":"一美元紙幣是美國價值一美元的紙幣。"},{"en":"A shop accepts a dollar bill because society treats it as money.","zh":"商店接受一美元紙幣，因為社會把它視為金錢。"},{"en":"Without shared agreement, the paper itself has little practical value.","zh":"沒有共享共識，紙張本身幾乎沒有實際價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical object that functions as a symbol of value.","zh":"這個短語描述作為價值象徵運作的物質物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"social agreement","meaning":"社會共識","examples":[{"en":"The value of a dollar bill depends on social agreement.","zh":"一美元紙幣的價值取決於社會共識。"},{"en":"Social agreement is shared acceptance by members of a society.","zh":"社會共識是社會成員共享的接受。"},{"en":"People use exam grades because schools and universities share an agreement about their meaning.","zh":"人們使用考試成績，因為學校和大學對其意義有共同共識。"},{"en":"If social agreement disappears, symbols such as money or titles may lose power.","zh":"如果社會共識消失，金錢或頭銜等符號可能失去力量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaning created by collective acceptance.","zh":"這個短語描述由集體接受創造的意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"accept it as","meaning":"接受它作為……","examples":[{"en":"People accept a dollar bill as a symbol of value.","zh":"人們接受一美元紙幣作為價值的象徵。"},{"en":"To accept it as something means to treat it as having that role or meaning.","zh":"接受它作為某物，是指把它視為具有該角色或意義。"},{"en":"A school may accept a doctor’s note as proof of illness.","zh":"學校可能接受醫生紙作為生病證明。"},{"en":"When people accept a symbol as meaningful, it begins to work socially.","zh":"當人們接受某符號為有意義，它就開始在社會中運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognising a role or status.","zh":"這個短語描述承認某種角色或地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a symbol of value","meaning":"價值的象徵","examples":[{"en":"A dollar bill functions as a symbol of value.","zh":"一美元紙幣作為價值的象徵運作。"},{"en":"A symbol of value is an object or sign that represents worth because people agree it does.","zh":"價值的象徵，是因人們同意而代表價值的物件或標誌。"},{"en":"A gift voucher is a symbol of value because shops accept it for goods.","zh":"禮券是價值的象徵，因為商店接受它換取貨品。"},{"en":"Symbols of value work only when others recognise and trust them.","zh":"價值象徵只有在其他人承認並信任它時才有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that stands for economic worth.","zh":"這個短語描述代表經濟價值的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"break down","meaning":"瓦解；崩潰","examples":[{"en":"If social agreement breaks down, the dollar bill loses its value.","zh":"如果社會共識瓦解，一美元紙幣就會失去價值。"},{"en":"To break down means to fail, collapse or stop working properly.","zh":"瓦解或崩潰，是指失效、倒塌或停止正常運作。"},{"en":"Communication may break down if team members stop listening to one another.","zh":"如果團隊成員停止互相聆聽，溝通可能瓦解。"},{"en":"When agreement breaks down, shared symbols can lose their meaning.","zh":"當共識瓦解，共享符號可能失去其意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a system failing.","zh":"這個短語描述系統失效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the collapse of","meaning":"……的崩潰","examples":[{"en":"The value of money could disappear through the collapse of government.","zh":"金錢的價值可能因政府崩潰而消失。"},{"en":"The collapse of something is its sudden or serious failure.","zh":"某事的崩潰，是它突然或嚴重失效。"},{"en":"The collapse of a school computer system can stop online lessons.","zh":"學校電腦系統崩潰可以令網上課堂停止。"},{"en":"If government collapses, trust in official money may also collapse.","zh":"如果政府崩潰，對官方貨幣的信任也可能崩潰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a breakdown of an institution or system.","zh":"這個短語描述機構或系統瓦解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"scrap of paper","meaning":"一張廢紙","examples":[{"en":"Without social agreement, a dollar bill becomes only a scrap of paper.","zh":"沒有社會共識，一美元紙幣只會變成一張廢紙。"},{"en":"A scrap of paper is a small piece of paper with little or no value.","zh":"一張廢紙，是一小張幾乎沒有價值的紙。"},{"en":"A receipt may become a scrap of paper after the return period ends.","zh":"退貨期限過後，收據可能變成一張廢紙。"},{"en":"Money without social trust is just paper because nobody treats it as valuable.","zh":"沒有社會信任的金錢只是紙，因為沒有人把它視為有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the physical object with its social meaning.","zh":"這個短語把物理物件與其社會意義作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"staring at it long and hard","meaning":"長時間盯着它看","examples":[{"en":"We do not understand a dollar bill by staring at it long and hard.","zh":"我們不是透過長時間盯着一美元紙幣看來理解它。"},{"en":"Staring at it long and hard means looking at it carefully for a long time.","zh":"長時間盯着它看，是指仔細看它很久。"},{"en":"A student will not understand a poem just by staring at it long and hard without thinking about context.","zh":"學生如果不思考語境，只是長時間盯着詩歌看，也不會理解它。"},{"en":"Some meanings cannot be found by looking at the object alone.","zh":"有些意義不能單靠觀看物件本身找到。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the limits of physical inspection.","zh":"這個短語顯示物理觀察的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"with respect to","meaning":"關於；對於","examples":[{"en":"We understand money by observing how people act with respect to it.","zh":"我們透過觀察人們對金錢如何行動來理解金錢。"},{"en":"With respect to something means regarding or in relation to it.","zh":"with respect to 某事，是指關於它或就它而言。"},{"en":"With respect to homework, the school expects students to submit it on time.","zh":"關於功課，學校期望學生準時提交。"},{"en":"Observing behaviour with respect to money shows what money means socially.","zh":"觀察人們對金錢的行為，顯示金錢在社會上有甚麼意義。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the topic or relationship being considered.","zh":"這個短語引入正在考慮的主題或關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"social mechanisms","meaning":"社會機制","examples":[{"en":"Social mechanisms help keep money meaningful.","zh":"社會機制幫助金錢保持有意義。"},{"en":"Social mechanisms are social systems, rules or habits that make society work in certain ways.","zh":"社會機制是令社會以某些方式運作的制度、規則或習慣。"},{"en":"Laws, banks and shops are social mechanisms that support the use of money.","zh":"法律、銀行和商店都是支持金錢使用的社會機制。"},{"en":"These mechanisms keep symbols meaningful by making people treat them consistently.","zh":"這些機制透過令人們一致對待符號，使符號保持有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the social structures behind shared meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述共享意義背後的社會結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"loyalties","meaning":"忠誠；歸屬感","examples":[{"en":"Social mechanisms and loyalties keep money meaningful.","zh":"社會機制和忠誠使金錢保持有意義。"},{"en":"Loyalties are feelings of support, commitment or faithfulness toward a group, person or system.","zh":"忠誠是對群體、人物或制度的支持、承諾或忠實感。"},{"en":"A student may feel loyalty to their school and defend its reputation.","zh":"學生可能對學校有歸屬感，並維護其聲譽。"},{"en":"Loyalties help symbols work because people continue to trust and support them.","zh":"忠誠幫助符號運作，因為人們繼續信任和支持它們。"},{"en":"This word describes emotional commitment.","zh":"這個詞描述情感承諾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"keep it meaningful","meaning":"使它保持有意義","examples":[{"en":"Social agreement helps keep the dollar bill meaningful.","zh":"社會共識幫助一美元紙幣保持有意義。"},{"en":"To keep it meaningful means to maintain its value or significance.","zh":"使它保持有意義，是指維持其價值或重要性。"},{"en":"A school tradition stays meaningful when students and teachers continue to respect it.","zh":"當學生和老師繼續尊重學校傳統，它就保持有意義。"},{"en":"If people stop accepting a symbol, it may no longer remain meaningful.","zh":"如果人們停止接受某符號，它可能不再有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preserving meaning over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間保存意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"social study","meaning":"社會研究","examples":[{"en":"Semantics is therefore a social study.","zh":"因此，語義學是一門社會研究。"},{"en":"A social study is a field that examines people, society and human relationships.","zh":"社會研究是研究人、社會和人類關係的領域。"},{"en":"History and sociology are social studies because they look at human communities.","zh":"歷史和社會學都是社會研究，因為它們研究人類社群。"},{"en":"Semantics is social because meaning depends on shared reactions and agreements.","zh":"語義學是社會性的，因為意義取決於共享反應和共識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a study of human society rather than only isolated words.","zh":"這個短語描述對人類社會的研究，而不只是孤立詞語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"basic to","meaning":"對……而言是基礎的","examples":[{"en":"Semantics is basic to all other social studies.","zh":"語義學對所有其他社會研究而言是基礎的。"},{"en":"Basic to something means fundamental or necessary for understanding it.","zh":"對某事而言是基礎的，是指對理解它來說是根本或必要的。"},{"en":"Reading skills are basic to success in many school subjects.","zh":"閱讀能力對許多學科的成功而言是基礎的。"},{"en":"If meaning shapes human behaviour, semantics becomes important for studying society.","zh":"如果意義塑造人類行為，語義學就成為研究社會的重要基礎。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that forms a foundation.","zh":"這個短語描述構成基礎的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"all other social studies","meaning":"所有其他社會研究","examples":[{"en":"Semantics is basic to all other social studies.","zh":"語義學對所有其他社會研究而言是基礎的。"},{"en":"All other social studies means every other field that studies society and human behaviour.","zh":"所有其他社會研究，是指每一個研究社會和人類行為的其他領域。"},{"en":"Economics, history and sociology are examples of social studies.","zh":"經濟學、歷史和社會學都是社會研究的例子。"},{"en":"If language affects behaviour, many social studies must consider meaning and communication.","zh":"如果語言影響行為，許多社會研究都必須考慮意義和溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the wider group of society-focused disciplines.","zh":"這個短語指更廣泛的社會研究學科。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生為每條題目選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the option letter that matches the right answer.","zh":"選出正確字母，是指選擇與正確答案相配的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice reading question, students may choose A, B, C or D.","zh":"在多項選擇閱讀題中，學生可能選 A、B、C 或 D。"},{"en":"Students should check the passage carefully before choosing the letter.","zh":"學生在選字母前應仔細查閱篇章。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction about answer format.","zh":"這個短語是關於答案格式的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"write the correct letter","meaning":"寫上正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students write the correct letter in the boxes.","zh":"學生在方格內寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"To write the correct letter means to record the answer option in the answer space.","zh":"寫上正確字母，是指在答案位置記錄答案選項。"},{"en":"A candidate may write C in the box if option C matches the passage.","zh":"如果 C 選項符合篇章，考生可能在方格內寫 C。"},{"en":"Even if students know the answer, they must write it in the correct place.","zh":"即使學生知道答案，也必須把它寫在正確位置。"},{"en":"This phrase tells students how to put down their answer.","zh":"這個短語告訴學生如何填寫答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"on your answer sheet","meaning":"在答題紙上","examples":[{"en":"Students write their answers on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生在答題紙上寫答案。"},{"en":"On your answer sheet means in the official paper or form where exam answers are recorded.","zh":"在答題紙上，是指在記錄考試答案的正式紙張或表格上。"},{"en":"A teacher may remind students to copy their answers onto the answer sheet before time ends.","zh":"老師可能提醒學生在時間結束前把答案抄到答題紙上。"},{"en":"Answers written in the wrong place may not be marked correctly.","zh":"寫在錯誤位置的答案可能不會被正確評分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the official answer document.","zh":"這個短語指正式答案文件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"what point is made","meaning":"提出了甚麼觀點","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what point is made in the first paragraph.","zh":"題目問第一段提出了甚麼觀點。"},{"en":"What point is made means what main idea or argument is stated.","zh":"提出了甚麼觀點，是指陳述了甚麼主要想法或論點。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask what point is made by an example in a reading passage.","zh":"老師可能問閱讀篇章中的例子提出了甚麼觀點。"},{"en":"Students should identify the writer’s message, not just repeat a detail.","zh":"學生應辨認作者訊息，而不只是重複細節。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for the central idea being expressed.","zh":"這個短語詢問正在表達的中心思想。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"carries meaning","meaning":"承載意義","examples":[{"en":"Print carries meaning only to trained readers.","zh":"印刷文字只對受過訓練的讀者承載意義。"},{"en":"Carries meaning means communicates or represents meaning.","zh":"承載意義，是指傳達或代表意義。"},{"en":"A red cross on a sign carries meaning because people connect it with medical help.","zh":"標誌上的紅十字承載意義，因為人們把它與醫療幫助連接起來。"},{"en":"Marks carry meaning only when people know how to interpret them.","zh":"記號只有在人們知道如何詮釋時才承載意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a symbol communicates something.","zh":"這個短語描述符號如何傳達某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"appropriate way to respond","meaning":"適當的回應方式","examples":[{"en":"Readers need to learn an appropriate way to respond to print.","zh":"讀者需要學習對印刷文字作出適當回應的方式。"},{"en":"An appropriate way to respond is a suitable or expected reaction in a situation.","zh":"適當的回應方式，是在某情況中合適或被期望的反應。"},{"en":"In a library, an appropriate way to respond to a fire alarm is to leave calmly.","zh":"在圖書館中，對火警鐘的適當回應方式是冷靜離開。"},{"en":"Learning to read means learning how to react to printed marks as meaningful words.","zh":"學會閱讀，就是學會把印刷記號當作有意義文字來回應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the correct or suitable response.","zh":"這個短語描述正確或合適的回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"According to the second paragraph, people are judged by their responses.","zh":"根據第二段，人們會按其反應被評價。"},{"en":"According to means as stated by or based on a source.","zh":"根據，是指按照某來源所說或基於某來源。"},{"en":"According to the timetable, the exam begins at nine o’clock.","zh":"根據時間表，考試在九點開始。"},{"en":"This phrase tells readers where the information comes from.","zh":"這個短語告訴讀者資訊來源。"},{"en":"It is useful when answering reading questions based on a passage.","zh":"它適合回答基於篇章的閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be judged by","meaning":"按……被評價","examples":[{"en":"People are judged by how conventional their responses are.","zh":"人們會按其反應有多符合常規而被評價。"},{"en":"To be judged by something means to be evaluated according to it.","zh":"按某事被評價，是指根據它接受評估。"},{"en":"Students may be judged by the clarity of their writing, not only by word count.","zh":"學生可能按寫作清晰度被評價，而不只是按字數。"},{"en":"Society may judge reactions as normal or strange depending on common habits.","zh":"社會可能根據共同習慣，把反應評為正常或奇怪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the standard used for evaluation.","zh":"這個短語描述用於評估的標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"level of education","meaning":"教育程度","examples":[{"en":"One option refers to a person’s level of education.","zh":"一個選項提到一個人的教育程度。"},{"en":"Level of education means how much formal schooling or training a person has completed.","zh":"教育程度，是一個人完成了多少正規學校教育或訓練。"},{"en":"A job advertisement may require a certain level of education.","zh":"招聘廣告可能要求某一教育程度。"},{"en":"Education level can affect vocabulary, but it does not explain every reaction a person has.","zh":"教育程度可以影響詞彙，但不能解釋一個人的每種反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes educational background.","zh":"這個短語描述教育背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"variety of experience","meaning":"各種經驗","examples":[{"en":"People’s responses are shaped by a variety of experience.","zh":"人們的反應由各種經驗塑造。"},{"en":"A variety of experience means many different kinds of experiences.","zh":"各種經驗，是指許多不同種類的經驗。"},{"en":"A student who reads, travels and joins clubs gains a variety of experience.","zh":"閱讀、旅行和參加學會的學生會獲得各種經驗。"},{"en":"Different experiences create different reaction patterns.","zh":"不同經驗會創造不同反應模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broad range of life influences.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛的生活影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"conventional responses","meaning":"傳統；符合常規的反應","examples":[{"en":"People may be judged by how conventional their responses are.","zh":"人們可能按其反應有多符合常規而被評價。"},{"en":"Conventional responses are reactions that match what most people expect or consider normal.","zh":"符合常規的反應，是符合大多數人期望或視為正常的反應。"},{"en":"Saying “thank you” after receiving help is a conventional response.","zh":"接受幫助後說「謝謝」是一種符合常規的反應。"},{"en":"If someone’s response is not conventional, others may see it as strange or original.","zh":"如果某人的反應不符合常規，其他人可能覺得它奇怪或有創見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes socially expected reactions.","zh":"這個短語描述社會期望中的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"incapable of","meaning":"無法……","examples":[{"en":"Standard definitions may be incapable of defining words precisely.","zh":"標準定義可能無法準確定義詞語。"},{"en":"Incapable of doing something means unable to do it.","zh":"無法做某事，是指沒有能力做到。"},{"en":"A broken printer is incapable of producing clear documents.","zh":"壞掉的打印機無法印出清晰文件。"},{"en":"A method may be incapable of solving a problem if the problem is too complex.","zh":"如果問題太複雜，一個方法可能無法解決它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inability or limitation.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有能力或有限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"define words precisely","meaning":"準確定義詞語","examples":[{"en":"Dictionaries may not define words precisely enough.","zh":"字典可能未能足夠準確地定義詞語。"},{"en":"To define words precisely means to explain their meanings exactly and clearly.","zh":"準確定義詞語，是指精確而清楚地解釋其意思。"},{"en":"A science teacher must define “force” precisely before students solve physics problems.","zh":"科學老師必須先準確定義「力」，學生才解物理題。"},{"en":"Imprecise definitions can create confusion because learners may use words too broadly.","zh":"不精確定義會造成混亂，因為學習者可能過度寬泛地使用詞語。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving exact meanings to words.","zh":"這個短語描述給詞語準確意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"in as few words as possible","meaning":"盡可能用最少文字","examples":[{"en":"One option says a dictionary should define words in as few words as possible.","zh":"一個選項說字典應盡可能用最少文字定義詞語。"},{"en":"In as few words as possible means using the smallest number of words while still communicating the idea.","zh":"盡可能用最少文字，是指在仍能傳達想法的情況下使用最少字數。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to summarise a story in as few words as possible.","zh":"老師可能要求學生盡可能用最少文字總結故事。"},{"en":"Short definitions are efficient, but they may lose important detail.","zh":"簡短定義有效率，但可能失去重要細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extreme conciseness.","zh":"這個短語描述極度簡潔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"提及","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to Louis Armstrong’s comment about jazz.","zh":"題目提及 Louis Armstrong 關於爵士樂的評論。"},{"en":"To refer to something means to mention it or direct attention to it.","zh":"提及某事，是指提到它或把注意力引向它。"},{"en":"A reading question may refer to paragraph three and ask about an example there.","zh":"閱讀題可能提及第三段，並問那裡的一個例子。"},{"en":"Referring to a comment helps readers know which part of the passage to examine.","zh":"提及某評論幫助讀者知道要查看篇章哪一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pointing to a specific idea or source.","zh":"這個短語描述指向特定想法或來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"provide insight into","meaning":"提供對……的洞見","examples":[{"en":"Armstrong’s comment provides insight into how words are defined.","zh":"Armstrong 的評論提供對詞語如何被定義的洞見。"},{"en":"To provide insight into something means to help people understand it more deeply.","zh":"提供對某事的洞見，是指幫助人更深入理解它。"},{"en":"A student’s mistakes can provide insight into what grammar points they do not understand.","zh":"學生的錯誤可以提供對他們不理解哪些文法點的洞見。"},{"en":"A short example can sometimes reveal more than a long definition.","zh":"短例子有時比長定義揭示更多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving deeper understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述給予更深理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"how words are defined","meaning":"詞語如何被定義","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what Armstrong shows about how words are defined.","zh":"題目問 Armstrong 顯示了詞語如何被定義。"},{"en":"How words are defined means the way people explain the meanings of words.","zh":"詞語如何被定義，是指人們解釋詞語意思的方式。"},{"en":"Students learn how words are defined by comparing dictionary meanings with real examples.","zh":"學生透過比較字典意思和真實例子，學習詞語如何被定義。"},{"en":"The passage suggests that definitions by words alone may be limited.","zh":"篇章暗示單靠文字作定義可能有限。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the method of explaining word meaning.","zh":"這個短語指解釋詞義的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"intend to show","meaning":"意圖表明","examples":[{"en":"The writer intends to show that meaning cannot always be shared by others.","zh":"作者意圖表明意義不一定總能由他人共享。"},{"en":"To intend to show something means to aim to make readers understand that point.","zh":"意圖表明某事，是指旨在令讀者理解該點。"},{"en":"A teacher may intend to show that examples are necessary for learning vocabulary.","zh":"老師可能意圖表明學習詞彙需要例子。"},{"en":"Writers choose examples because they want to lead readers toward a conclusion.","zh":"作者選擇例子，是因為他們想引導讀者得出結論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the purpose behind an explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述解釋背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"personnel manager","meaning":"人事經理","examples":[{"en":"The personnel manager illustrates meaning through action.","zh":"人事經理透過行動說明意義。"},{"en":"A personnel manager is a staff manager who deals with hiring and employee matters.","zh":"人事經理是處理招聘和僱員事務的人員管理者。"},{"en":"A personnel manager may reject an application after reading one detail on the form.","zh":"人事經理可能在讀到表格上的某個細節後拒絕申請。"},{"en":"The manager’s behaviour shows how meaning can appear through action, not dictionary definition.","zh":"經理的行為顯示意義可以透過行動出現，而不是透過字典定義。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a workplace role used as an example in the passage.","zh":"這個短語指篇章中用作例子的職場角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"not necessarily","meaning":"不一定","examples":[{"en":"Harvard men are not necessarily more competitive in the job market.","zh":"哈佛人不一定在就業市場更有競爭力。"},{"en":"Not necessarily means not always or not certainly.","zh":"不一定，是指並非總是或並非必然。"},{"en":"A high score does not necessarily mean a student understands every topic deeply.","zh":"高分不一定表示學生深入理解每個主題。"},{"en":"This phrase prevents readers from assuming too much from one fact.","zh":"這個短語防止讀者從單一事實作過多假設。"},{"en":"It signals that a claim may be possible but is not guaranteed.","zh":"它表示某說法可能成立，但沒有保證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"competitive in the job market","meaning":"在就業市場有競爭力","examples":[{"en":"One option says Harvard men may not be competitive in the job market.","zh":"一個選項說哈佛人可能在就業市場沒有競爭力。"},{"en":"Competitive in the job market means able to compete successfully for jobs.","zh":"在就業市場有競爭力，是指能成功競爭工作。"},{"en":"A student with strong communication skills may be more competitive in the job market.","zh":"具備強溝通能力的學生可能在就業市場更有競爭力。"},{"en":"Qualifications can help, but employers also look at experience, attitude and skills.","zh":"資歷可以有幫助，但僱主也看經驗、態度和技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes employability compared with other applicants.","zh":"這個短語描述相對於其他申請者的就業能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"make much sense","meaning":"很有道理；說得通","examples":[{"en":"One option says operationalism may not make much sense outside science.","zh":"一個選項說操作主義在科學之外可能不太說得通。"},{"en":"To make much sense means to be understandable, reasonable or useful.","zh":"說得通，是指可以理解、合理或有用。"},{"en":"A rule does not make much sense if nobody can explain why it exists.","zh":"如果沒有人能解釋某條規則為何存在，它就不太說得通。"},{"en":"An idea may make sense in one field but seem strange in another.","zh":"一個想法在某領域可能說得通，但在另一領域顯得奇怪。"},{"en":"This phrase judges whether something is clear or reasonable.","zh":"這個短語判斷某事是否清楚或合理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"take care when","meaning":"在……時小心","examples":[{"en":"Applicants should take care when filling out forms.","zh":"申請者填寫表格時應小心。"},{"en":"To take care when doing something means to do it carefully to avoid mistakes.","zh":"在做某事時小心，是指仔細做，以避免錯誤。"},{"en":"Students should take care when copying answers onto the answer sheet.","zh":"學生把答案抄到答題紙上時應小心。"},{"en":"Careless details on a form can affect how a reader judges the applicant.","zh":"表格上粗心的細節可以影響讀者如何評價申請者。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a warning to act carefully.","zh":"這個短語提醒人謹慎行事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"filling out application forms","meaning":"填寫申請表","examples":[{"en":"Job applicants fill out application forms.","zh":"求職者填寫申請表。"},{"en":"Filling out application forms means completing forms by writing the required information.","zh":"填寫申請表，是指寫上所需資料以完成表格。"},{"en":"A student may fill out an application form for a scholarship.","zh":"學生可能填寫獎學金申請表。"},{"en":"What people write on forms can influence how others respond to them.","zh":"人們在表格上寫的內容可以影響他人如何回應他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes completing official request documents.","zh":"這個短語描述完成正式申請文件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與資料一致","examples":[{"en":"The statements may agree with the information in the passage.","zh":"這些陳述可能與篇章資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information means to match what the passage says.","zh":"與資料一致，是指符合篇章所說內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says meaning is in reactions, a statement saying the same thing agrees with the information.","zh":"如果篇章說意義存在於反應中，而陳述也這樣說，它就與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students must compare the statement with the text, not with their own opinion.","zh":"學生必須把陳述與文本比較，而不是與自己的意見比較。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"contradicts the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與篇章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradicts the information means says the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"與資料相矛盾，是指說出與篇章所說相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the text says a symbol has social meaning, a statement saying symbols never carry meaning contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文本說符號有社會意義，而陳述說符號從不承載意義，它就與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"A contradiction must be clearly shown by the passage.","zh":"矛盾必須由篇章清楚顯示。"},{"en":"This phrase helps identify a FALSE answer.","zh":"這個短語幫助辨認 FALSE 答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有關於此事的資料","examples":[{"en":"Not Given means there is no information on this in the passage.","zh":"NOT GIVEN 表示篇章沒有關於此事的資料。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not say whether the point is true or false.","zh":"沒有關於此事的資料，是指篇章沒有說明該點是真是假。"},{"en":"If the passage mentions Louis Armstrong but not his childhood school, there is no information on that school.","zh":"如果篇章提到 Louis Armstrong 但沒有提及他的童年學校，就沒有關於該學校的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from outside knowledge when the text gives no evidence.","zh":"當文本沒有證據時，學生不應依靠外部知識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase corresponds to a NOT GIVEN answer.","zh":"這個短語對應 NOT GIVEN 答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"proved or disproved","meaning":"被證明或反證","examples":[{"en":"Some statements cannot easily be proved or disproved.","zh":"有些陳述不能輕易被證明或反證。"},{"en":"Proved or disproved means shown to be true or shown to be false.","zh":"被證明或反證，是指被顯示為真或被顯示為假。"},{"en":"A maths answer can be proved or disproved by checking the calculation.","zh":"數學答案可以透過檢查計算被證明或反證。"},{"en":"Broad statements about freedom may be harder to test through simple operations.","zh":"關於自由的廣泛陳述可能較難透過簡單操作測試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes establishing truth or falsehood.","zh":"這個短語描述確立真假。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"personal to individuals","meaning":"個人獨有的","examples":[{"en":"Some meanings may be personal to individuals.","zh":"有些意義可能是個人獨有的。"},{"en":"Personal to individuals means belonging to or shaped by each person’s own experience.","zh":"個人獨有的，是指屬於或由每個人的自身經驗塑造。"},{"en":"A song may be personal to one student because it reminds them of home.","zh":"一首歌對某學生可能很個人化，因為它令他想起家。"},{"en":"Personal meanings differ because people have different memories and reactions.","zh":"個人意義會不同，因為人有不同記憶和反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaning that is not fully shared by everyone.","zh":"這個短語描述並非完全由所有人共享的意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"less worthy of study","meaning":"較不值得研究","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that personal meanings are less worthy of study.","zh":"該選項暗示個人意義較不值得研究。"},{"en":"Less worthy of study means less deserving of serious attention or research.","zh":"較不值得研究，是指較不值得認真關注或研究。"},{"en":"A teacher should not assume students’ emotional reactions are less worthy of study than grammar mistakes.","zh":"老師不應假設學生的情緒反應比文法錯誤較不值得研究。"},{"en":"If personal meaning shapes behaviour, it may be very important to study.","zh":"如果個人意義塑造行為，它可能非常值得研究。"},{"en":"This phrase judges how much attention a subject deserves.","zh":"這個短語判斷某主題值得多少關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"elicit responses","meaning":"引發反應","examples":[{"en":"Flags and words elicit responses for the same symbolic reason.","zh":"旗幟和詞語基於同一象徵原因引發反應。"},{"en":"To elicit responses means to cause or draw out reactions from people.","zh":"引發反應，是指造成或引出人們的回應。"},{"en":"A teacher’s question can elicit responses from students who want to share ideas.","zh":"老師的問題可以引發想分享想法的學生作出回應。"},{"en":"Symbols elicit responses because people have learned what they stand for.","zh":"符號會引發反應，因為人們已學會它們代表甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes producing reactions.","zh":"這個短語描述產生反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"for the same reason","meaning":"基於同一原因","examples":[{"en":"Flags and words can elicit responses for the same reason.","zh":"旗幟和詞語可以基於同一原因引發反應。"},{"en":"For the same reason means because the same cause or explanation applies.","zh":"基於同一原因，是指因為同一個原因或解釋適用。"},{"en":"Students need examples to learn vocabulary; for the same reason, they need examples to learn grammar.","zh":"學生需要例子來學詞彙；基於同一原因，他們也需要例子來學文法。"},{"en":"This phrase connects two situations with one shared explanation.","zh":"這個短語把兩種情況與同一解釋連接起來。"},{"en":"It shows that the logic behind both cases is similar.","zh":"它顯示兩個案例背後的邏輯相似。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"entertaining without being understood","meaning":"在未被理解下仍具娛樂性","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether a story can be entertaining without being understood.","zh":"該選項問一個故事能否在未被理解下仍具娛樂性。"},{"en":"Entertaining without being understood means enjoyable even when the meaning is not clear.","zh":"在未被理解下仍具娛樂性，是指即使意思不清楚仍令人享受。"},{"en":"A comedy show in a foreign language may not be entertaining without subtitles.","zh":"沒有字幕的外語喜劇節目，可能在未被理解下不具娛樂性。"},{"en":"Entertainment often depends on understanding jokes, plot and social meaning.","zh":"娛樂通常取決於理解笑話、情節和社會意義。"},{"en":"This phrase tests whether enjoyment can happen without comprehension.","zh":"這個短語測試沒有理解時是否仍能產生樂趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"complete each sentence","meaning":"完成每個句子","examples":[{"en":"Students complete each sentence with the correct ending.","zh":"學生用正確結尾完成每個句子。"},{"en":"To complete each sentence means to finish every sentence by adding the missing part.","zh":"完成每個句子，是指加入缺失部分使每句完整。"},{"en":"In a reading exercise, students may complete each sentence using endings from a list.","zh":"在閱讀練習中，學生可能使用列表中的結尾完成每個句子。"},{"en":"This task checks whether students understand how ideas connect.","zh":"這項任務檢查學生是否理解想法如何連接。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction for sentence-completion questions.","zh":"這個短語是句子完成題的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the correct ending","meaning":"正確結尾","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct ending for each sentence.","zh":"學生為每個句子選擇正確結尾。"},{"en":"The correct ending is the option that logically and accurately completes a sentence.","zh":"正確結尾，是能合邏輯且準確完成句子的選項。"},{"en":"If a sentence begins with “Because it rained,” the correct ending should show a result.","zh":"如果句子以「因為下雨」開始，正確結尾應顯示結果。"},{"en":"Choosing the ending requires both grammar and meaning.","zh":"選擇結尾需要文法和意思兩方面配合。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the right final part of a sentence.","zh":"這個短語指句子的正確最後部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"is meaningless","meaning":"是無意義的","examples":[{"en":"A story in a language the audience cannot understand is meaningless to them.","zh":"用觀眾不能理解的語言講出的故事，對他們來說是無意義的。"},{"en":"Is meaningless means has no understandable meaning or significance for someone.","zh":"是無意義的，是指對某人來說沒有可理解的意思或重要性。"},{"en":"A password made of random letters is meaningless to a person who does not know the code.","zh":"對不知道密碼規則的人來說，由隨機字母組成的密碼是無意義的。"},{"en":"Something becomes meaningful only when people can interpret it.","zh":"只有當人們能詮釋某事，它才變得有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lack of meaning for a particular audience.","zh":"這個短語描述對特定觀眾缺乏意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"lasting effects on human behaviour","meaning":"對人類行為有持久影響","examples":[{"en":"A comic strip can have lasting effects on human behaviour.","zh":"連環漫畫可以對人類行為有持久影響。"},{"en":"Lasting effects on human behaviour are long-term influences on how people act or respond.","zh":"對人類行為有持久影響，是指長期影響人們如何行動或回應。"},{"en":"A childhood story may have lasting effects on how a person sees honesty.","zh":"童年故事可能對一個人如何看待誠實有持久影響。"},{"en":"Repeated messages can shape behaviour long after the original experience is over.","zh":"反覆訊息可以在原本經驗結束很久後仍塑造行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes durable influence on actions and reactions.","zh":"這個短語描述對行動和反應的長久影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"lost its meaning","meaning":"失去其意義","examples":[{"en":"A symbol can lose its meaning when social agreement breaks down.","zh":"當社會共識瓦解，符號可以失去其意義。"},{"en":"Lost its meaning means no longer carries the significance or value it once had.","zh":"失去其意義，是指不再承載它曾經擁有的重要性或價值。"},{"en":"A school tradition may lose its meaning if students no longer understand why it exists.","zh":"如果學生不再理解學校傳統為何存在，該傳統可能失去其意義。"},{"en":"Symbols depend on shared agreement, so meaning can disappear when agreement disappears.","zh":"符號依賴共享共識，所以當共識消失，意義也可以消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaning fading or collapsing.","zh":"這個短語描述意義減退或崩塌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"social context","meaning":"社會脈絡","examples":[{"en":"A dollar bill can be understood only in its social context.","zh":"一美元紙幣只能在其社會脈絡中被理解。"},{"en":"Social context is the surrounding society, relationships and shared rules that give something meaning.","zh":"社會脈絡是賦予某事意義的周圍社會、關係和共享規則。"},{"en":"A joke may be funny in one social context but rude in another.","zh":"一個笑話在某社會脈絡中可能好笑，但在另一脈絡中可能無禮。"},{"en":"Money has value because social institutions and people agree to treat it as valuable.","zh":"金錢有價值，是因為社會機構和人們同意把它視為有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the social setting that explains meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述解釋意義的社會環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"inadequate explanation of meaning","meaning":"對意義作出不足夠的解釋","examples":[{"en":"A dictionary can provide an inadequate explanation of meaning.","zh":"字典可以對意義作出不足夠的解釋。"},{"en":"An inadequate explanation of meaning is an explanation that is not complete or clear enough.","zh":"對意義作出不足夠的解釋，是不夠完整或清楚的解釋。"},{"en":"A one-word translation may be an inadequate explanation of a difficult idiom.","zh":"對困難成語而言，單字翻譯可能是不足夠的意義解釋。"},{"en":"Learners need examples and context when a definition alone is inadequate.","zh":"當定義本身不足夠，學習者需要例子和語境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an explanation that falls short.","zh":"這個短語描述未達標的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"variability of human behaviour","meaning":"人類行為的多變性","examples":[{"en":"Semantic habits reflect the variability of human behaviour.","zh":"語義習慣反映人類行為的多變性。"},{"en":"Variability of human behaviour means the fact that people act and respond in different ways.","zh":"人類行為的多變性，是指人們以不同方式行動和回應這一事實。"},{"en":"In a classroom, the same feedback may encourage one student but upset another.","zh":"在課室中，同一回饋可能鼓勵一名學生，卻令另一名學生不安。"},{"en":"Human behaviour varies because people have different experiences, values and habits.","zh":"人類行為會有差異，因為人們有不同經驗、價值和習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes differences in how people behave.","zh":"這個短語描述人們行為方式上的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"emphasises the importance of","meaning":"強調……的重要性","examples":[{"en":"Bridgman emphasises the importance of analysing how words are used.","zh":"Bridgman 強調分析詞語如何被使用的重要性。"},{"en":"To emphasise the importance of something means to stress that it matters greatly.","zh":"強調某事的重要性，是指突出它非常重要。"},{"en":"A teacher may emphasise the importance of planning before writing an essay.","zh":"老師可能強調寫文章前規劃的重要性。"},{"en":"Emphasis guides readers toward what they should pay attention to.","zh":"強調可以引導讀者注意應該重視的內容。"},{"en":"This phrase describes highlighting something as significant.","zh":"這個短語描述突出某事的重要意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"analysing how words are used","meaning":"分析詞語如何被使用","examples":[{"en":"Operationalism involves analysing how words are used.","zh":"操作主義涉及分析詞語如何被使用。"},{"en":"Analysing how words are used means studying what people do with words in real situations.","zh":"分析詞語如何被使用，是研究人們在真實情況中如何使用詞語。"},{"en":"A teacher analyses how students use “however” by reading their essays.","zh":"老師透過閱讀學生文章，分析他們如何使用 “however”。"},{"en":"Studying actual use can reveal meaning more clearly than memorising a definition.","zh":"研究實際使用可以比背定義更清楚揭示意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes examining language in action.","zh":"這個短語描述檢視運作中的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"carry more meaning than others","meaning":"承載比其他更多的意義","examples":[{"en":"One option suggests that certain behaviours carry more meaning than others.","zh":"一個選項暗示某些行為比其他行為承載更多意義。"},{"en":"To carry more meaning than others means to communicate stronger or deeper significance than other actions.","zh":"比其他行為承載更多意義，是指傳達比其他行動更強或更深的意義。"},{"en":"A handwritten apology may carry more meaning than a quick text message.","zh":"手寫道歉信可能比快速短訊承載更多意義。"},{"en":"Behaviour carries meaning when people interpret it as showing respect, anger, care or rejection.","zh":"當人們把行為詮釋為尊重、憤怒、關心或拒絕時，行為就承載意義。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the meaningful force of different actions.","zh":"這個短語比較不同行動的意義力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 52 - What is Meaning.pdf","sourcePage":22}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 53":[{"front":"moderate or divert hurricanes","meaning":"減弱或改變颶風路徑","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have considered whether hurricanes can be moderated or diverted.","zh":"科學家曾考慮是否可以減弱或改變颶風路徑。"},{"en":"To moderate or divert hurricanes means to make hurricanes weaker or change the direction they travel.","zh":"moderate or divert hurricanes 指令颶風變弱或改變其移動方向。"},{"en":"City planners may hope future technology can moderate or divert hurricanes before they reach crowded coastal areas.","zh":"城市規劃者可能希望未來科技能在颶風到達人口稠密海岸前減弱或改變其路徑。"},{"en":"If a hurricane could be moderated or diverted, fewer homes might be destroyed and fewer people might need emergency help.","zh":"如果颶風可以被減弱或改道，較少房屋可能被摧毀，較少人需要緊急援助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlling a storm’s strength or path, not simply predicting it.","zh":"這個短語描述控制風暴強度或路徑，而不只是預測它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"massive swirling storms","meaning":"大型旋轉風暴","examples":[{"en":"Hurricanes are massive swirling storms that form over tropical oceans.","zh":"颶風是在熱帶海洋上形成的大型旋轉風暴。"},{"en":"Massive swirling storms are huge storms that rotate strongly around a centre.","zh":"massive swirling storms 指圍繞中心強烈旋轉的巨大風暴。"},{"en":"A satellite image can show massive swirling storms as spiral clouds above the sea.","zh":"衛星圖像可以把大型旋轉風暴顯示為海面上方的螺旋雲層。"},{"en":"Because these storms are so large and rotating, they can affect many towns at once.","zh":"因為這些風暴巨大且旋轉，它們可以同時影響許多城鎮。"},{"en":"This phrase helps students picture hurricanes as enormous spinning weather systems.","zh":"這個短語幫助學生把颶風想像成龐大的旋轉天氣系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"winds exceeding","meaning":"風速超過","examples":[{"en":"Some hurricanes have winds exceeding 74 miles per hour.","zh":"有些颶風的風速超過每小時74英里。"},{"en":"Winds exceeding a speed are winds that go beyond that speed.","zh":"winds exceeding a speed 指風速高於某個速度。"},{"en":"A weather warning may be issued if winds exceeding safe levels are expected near a bridge.","zh":"如果預計橋樑附近風速超過安全水平，可能會發出天氣警告。"},{"en":"When winds exceed a certain speed, trees, signs, and roofs may be damaged.","zh":"當風速超過某一水平，樹木、路牌和屋頂可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to show that wind speed is above a stated limit.","zh":"這個短語用來表示風速高於已說明的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sweep across","meaning":"橫掃","examples":[{"en":"Massive storms sweep across tropical oceans before reaching land.","zh":"大型風暴在登陸前橫掃熱帶海洋。"},{"en":"To sweep across an area means to move quickly and powerfully over a wide space.","zh":"sweep across an area 指快速而有力地掠過廣闊區域。"},{"en":"Heavy rain may sweep across a city and flood several streets within an hour.","zh":"大雨可能橫掃城市，並在一小時內令幾條街水浸。"},{"en":"When a storm sweeps across the sea, ships and coastal towns may need warnings.","zh":"當風暴橫掃海面，船隻和沿海城鎮可能需要警告。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests wide, forceful movement.","zh":"這個短語暗示廣泛而強力的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tropical oceans","meaning":"熱帶海洋","examples":[{"en":"Hurricanes usually form above warm tropical oceans.","zh":"颶風通常在溫暖的熱帶海洋上方形成。"},{"en":"Tropical oceans are warm ocean areas near the equator.","zh":"tropical oceans 指赤道附近的溫暖海洋地區。"},{"en":"Holiday islands in tropical oceans often have warm water, coral reefs, and humid weather.","zh":"熱帶海洋中的度假島嶼通常有暖水、珊瑚礁和潮濕天氣。"},{"en":"Warm tropical oceans provide the heat and moisture that help hurricanes develop.","zh":"溫暖熱帶海洋提供熱力和水分，幫助颶風發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the warm sea regions where many major storms begin.","zh":"這個短語描述許多大型風暴開始形成的溫暖海域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"strike shorelines","meaning":"襲擊海岸線","examples":[{"en":"Severe storms can strike shorelines with destructive force.","zh":"強烈風暴可以以破壞性力量襲擊海岸線。"},{"en":"To strike shorelines means to hit coastal areas directly.","zh":"strike shorelines 指直接打擊沿海地區。"},{"en":"A typhoon may strike shorelines and force fishermen to return to harbour.","zh":"颱風可能襲擊海岸線，迫使漁民返回港口。"},{"en":"When a storm strikes a shoreline, waves, floods, and strong winds can damage buildings.","zh":"當風暴襲擊海岸線，海浪、水浸和強風可以損壞建築物。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a storm reaches and attacks the coast.","zh":"這個短語用於風暴到達並打擊海岸時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"devastate vast swaths of territory","meaning":"摧毀大片地區","examples":[{"en":"Hurricanes can devastate vast swaths of territory.","zh":"颶風可以摧毀大片地區。"},{"en":"To devastate vast swaths of territory means to destroy or badly damage very large areas of land.","zh":"devastate vast swaths of territory 指摧毀或嚴重破壞非常大片土地。"},{"en":"A major flood can devastate vast swaths of farmland and leave farmers without crops.","zh":"大型洪水可以摧毀大片農地，令農民失去收成。"},{"en":"When large areas are devastated, rebuilding roads, homes, and services can take years.","zh":"當大片地區被摧毀，道路、房屋和服務的重建可能需要多年。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses both the scale and seriousness of destruction.","zh":"這個短語同時強調破壞的規模和嚴重性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"roiling tempests","meaning":"翻騰的暴風雨","examples":[{"en":"These roiling tempests can cause enormous damage.","zh":"這些翻騰的暴風雨可以造成巨大破壞。"},{"en":"Roiling tempests are violent storms full of turbulent movement.","zh":"roiling tempests 指充滿混亂翻動的猛烈風暴。"},{"en":"A sailor may describe a sea storm with crashing waves and black clouds as a roiling tempest.","zh":"水手可能把有巨浪和黑雲的海上風暴形容為翻騰的暴風雨。"},{"en":"Because roiling tempests move violently, they can damage ships, buildings, and power lines.","zh":"因為翻騰的暴風雨劇烈移動，它們可以損壞船隻、建築物和電線。"},{"en":"This phrase is more literary than “storm” and makes the violence of the weather clearer.","zh":"這個短語比 “storm” 更文學化，並更清楚表現天氣的猛烈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"densely inhabited territories","meaning":"人口稠密地區","examples":[{"en":"Hurricanes are especially dangerous when they strike densely inhabited territories.","zh":"當颶風襲擊人口稠密地區時，尤其危險。"},{"en":"Densely inhabited territories are areas where many people live close together.","zh":"densely inhabited territories 指許多人密集居住的地區。"},{"en":"A city with tall apartment blocks and crowded streets is a densely inhabited territory.","zh":"有高樓住宅和擁擠街道的城市就是人口稠密地區。"},{"en":"If a storm hits a densely inhabited territory, emergency services may need to help many people at once.","zh":"如果風暴擊中人口稠密地區，緊急服務可能需要同時幫助很多人。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on population density and risk.","zh":"這個短語集中於人口密度和風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have the power to","meaning":"有能力；足以","examples":[{"en":"Such storms have the power to kill thousands of people.","zh":"這類風暴足以奪去數千人的生命。"},{"en":"To have the power to do something means to be strong or influential enough to cause it.","zh":"have the power to do something 指有足夠力量或影響力造成某結果。"},{"en":"A careless rumour can have the power to damage a student’s reputation.","zh":"一個不負責任的謠言足以損害學生名聲。"},{"en":"When a natural event has the power to kill, governments must prepare seriously.","zh":"當自然事件足以致命，政府必須認真準備。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is capable of causing a major result.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事物有能力造成重大結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cause property damage","meaning":"造成財產損失","examples":[{"en":"Hurricanes can cause property damage worth billions of dollars.","zh":"颶風可以造成價值數十億美元的財產損失。"},{"en":"To cause property damage means to damage buildings, vehicles, equipment, or other possessions.","zh":"cause property damage 指損壞建築物、車輛、設備或其他財物。"},{"en":"A burst pipe can cause property damage if water leaks into a flat overnight.","zh":"如果水管爆裂並在夜間漏水入單位，就可能造成財產損失。"},{"en":"Strong winds cause property damage when they break windows or tear off roofs.","zh":"強風打碎窗戶或掀走屋頂時，就會造成財產損失。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to financial loss caused by damage to physical things.","zh":"這個短語指實物受損造成的金錢損失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"worth billions of dollars","meaning":"價值數十億美元","examples":[{"en":"The storm caused property damage worth billions of dollars.","zh":"這場風暴造成價值數十億美元的財產損失。"},{"en":"Worth billions of dollars means having a value or cost of several thousand million dollars.","zh":"worth billions of dollars 指價值或成本達數十億美元。"},{"en":"A large airport project may be worth billions of dollars because it includes terminals, roads, and rail links.","zh":"大型機場工程可能價值數十億美元，因為包括航站樓、道路和鐵路連接。"},{"en":"Damage worth billions of dollars can take many years and huge public funds to repair.","zh":"價值數十億美元的損失可能需要多年和巨額公帑修復。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an extremely high financial value or loss.","zh":"這個短語顯示極高的金錢價值或損失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stand in their way","meaning":"阻擋……去路","examples":[{"en":"Almost nothing stands in the way of a powerful hurricane.","zh":"幾乎沒有東西能阻擋強大颶風的去路。"},{"en":"To stand in someone’s or something’s way means to block, stop, or prevent progress.","zh":"stand in someone’s or something’s way 指阻擋、停止或防止前進。"},{"en":"A lack of money may stand in the way of a student joining an overseas exchange trip.","zh":"缺錢可能阻擋學生參加海外交流團。"},{"en":"If nothing stands in a storm’s way, it can move forward and cause wide damage.","zh":"如果沒有東西阻擋風暴去路，它可以繼續前進並造成廣泛破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an obstacle that prevents movement or success.","zh":"這個短語描述妨礙移動或成功的障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"formidable forces of nature","meaning":"令人畏懼的自然力量","examples":[{"en":"Hurricanes are formidable forces of nature.","zh":"颶風是令人畏懼的自然力量。"},{"en":"Formidable forces of nature are natural powers that are extremely strong and difficult to resist.","zh":"formidable forces of nature 指極其強大且難以抵抗的自然力量。"},{"en":"Earthquakes, tsunamis, and volcanic eruptions are formidable forces of nature.","zh":"地震、海嘯和火山爆發都是令人畏懼的自然力量。"},{"en":"Because such forces are so powerful, people often focus on preparation rather than complete control.","zh":"因為這些力量非常強大，人們通常重點準備，而不是完全控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes nature at its most dangerous and impressive.","zh":"這個短語描述自然界最危險且令人震撼的一面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"severe tropical storms","meaning":"強烈熱帶風暴","examples":[{"en":"Hurricanes are examples of severe tropical storms.","zh":"颶風是強烈熱帶風暴的例子。"},{"en":"Severe tropical storms are powerful storms that form in warm tropical regions.","zh":"severe tropical storms 指在溫暖熱帶地區形成的強大風暴。"},{"en":"Weather centres track severe tropical storms so coastal communities can prepare.","zh":"天氣中心追蹤強烈熱帶風暴，讓沿海社區可以準備。"},{"en":"These storms can bring strong winds, heavy rain, storm surge, and flooding.","zh":"這些風暴可以帶來強風、大雨、風暴潮和水浸。"},{"en":"This phrase names a dangerous type of storm linked to tropical seas.","zh":"這個短語指出與熱帶海洋有關的危險風暴類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be susceptible to","meaning":"易受……影響；可能受……影響","examples":[{"en":"Some storms may be susceptible to human intervention.","zh":"有些風暴可能受人為干預影響。"},{"en":"To be susceptible to something means to be likely to be affected by it.","zh":"be susceptible to something 指容易受某事影響。"},{"en":"Young children may be susceptible to colds when they are tired and stressed.","zh":"幼童疲倦和有壓力時，可能較容易感冒。"},{"en":"If a system is susceptible to small changes, a small input may produce a large result.","zh":"如果一個系統容易受細微改變影響，小輸入可能產生大結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes vulnerability or openness to influence.","zh":"這個短語描述脆弱性或受影響的可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"human intervention","meaning":"人為干預","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are studying whether hurricanes can be changed by human intervention.","zh":"研究人員正在研究颶風是否可以透過人為干預被改變。"},{"en":"Human intervention means deliberate action by people to change a natural or social process.","zh":"human intervention 指人有意採取行動改變自然或社會過程。"},{"en":"Planting trees in a hot city is human intervention to reduce heat.","zh":"在炎熱城市種樹是減少熱力的人為干預。"},{"en":"If human intervention changes a storm, it could protect people but also create new risks.","zh":"如果人為干預改變風暴，它可以保護人們，但也可能帶來新風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people actively stepping in instead of just observing.","zh":"這個短語描述人主動介入，而不只是觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"nature and origins","meaning":"性質與成因","examples":[{"en":"A researcher must first understand the nature and origins of hurricanes.","zh":"研究人員必須先理解颶風的性質與成因。"},{"en":"The nature and origins of something are what it is like and how it begins.","zh":"nature and origins of something 指某事的特性以及它如何開始。"},{"en":"A doctor must understand the nature and origins of a disease before choosing treatment.","zh":"醫生選擇治療前，必須理解疾病的性質與成因。"},{"en":"Understanding origins helps explain causes, while understanding nature helps explain behaviour.","zh":"理解成因有助解釋原因，而理解性質有助解釋行為。"},{"en":"This phrase asks both “What is it?” and “Where does it come from?”","zh":"這個短語同時問「它是甚麼？」和「它從何而來？」"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"grow from clusters of thunderstorms","meaning":"由雷暴群發展而成","examples":[{"en":"Hurricanes grow from clusters of thunderstorms above tropical seas.","zh":"颶風由熱帶海域上方的雷暴群發展而成。"},{"en":"To grow from clusters of thunderstorms means to develop from groups of storm clouds and thunderstorm activity.","zh":"grow from clusters of thunderstorms 指由一群風暴雲和雷暴活動發展而成。"},{"en":"A small problem in a school can grow from repeated complaints that no one solves.","zh":"學校中的小問題可以由多次未被解決的投訴發展而成。"},{"en":"When thunderstorms gather over warm seas, they may organise into a larger storm system.","zh":"當雷暴在暖海上聚集，它們可能組織成更大的風暴系統。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the starting point of hurricane formation.","zh":"這個短語解釋颶風形成的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"clusters of thunderstorms","meaning":"雷暴群","examples":[{"en":"Clusters of thunderstorms can develop into hurricanes.","zh":"雷暴群可以發展成颶風。"},{"en":"Clusters of thunderstorms are groups of thunderstorm clouds occurring close together.","zh":"clusters of thunderstorms 指彼此接近出現的一組雷暴雲。"},{"en":"A weather radar may show clusters of thunderstorms forming over the sea in the afternoon.","zh":"天氣雷達可能顯示下午海面上形成雷暴群。"},{"en":"If these clusters remain over warm water, they may grow stronger and more organised.","zh":"如果這些雷暴群停留在暖水上方，它們可能變得更強和更有組織。"},{"en":"This phrase describes several storms grouped together, not one isolated shower.","zh":"這個短語描述幾個風暴聚在一起，而不是單一陣雨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tropical seas","meaning":"熱帶海域","examples":[{"en":"Warm tropical seas provide the energy needed for hurricanes.","zh":"溫暖熱帶海域提供颶風所需的能量。"},{"en":"Tropical seas are warm ocean waters near the tropics.","zh":"tropical seas 指熱帶附近的溫暖海水區域。"},{"en":"Fishing communities near tropical seas often prepare carefully during storm season.","zh":"熱帶海域附近的漁業社區通常在風季仔細準備。"},{"en":"Warm tropical seas feed storms with heat and moisture, helping them strengthen.","zh":"溫暖熱帶海域以熱力和水分供養風暴，幫助它們增強。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the warm sea areas that can fuel hurricanes.","zh":"這個短語指可以為颶風提供能量的溫暖海域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"low-latitude areas","meaning":"低緯度地區","examples":[{"en":"Oceans in low-latitude areas release heat and moisture into the atmosphere.","zh":"低緯度地區的海洋向大氣層釋放熱力和水分。"},{"en":"Low-latitude areas are regions close to the equator.","zh":"low-latitude areas 指接近赤道的地區。"},{"en":"Countries in low-latitude areas often experience warm weather for much of the year.","zh":"位於低緯度地區的國家通常一年大部分時間天氣溫暖。"},{"en":"Because the sun is strong near the equator, oceans there can store large amounts of heat.","zh":"因為赤道附近陽光強，那裡的海洋可以儲存大量熱力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes places near the Earth’s middle, where tropical weather is common.","zh":"這個短語描述接近地球中部、常見熱帶天氣的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"release heat and moisture","meaning":"釋放熱力和水分","examples":[{"en":"Tropical oceans continuously release heat and moisture into the atmosphere.","zh":"熱帶海洋持續向大氣層釋放熱力和水分。"},{"en":"To release heat and moisture means to give off warmth and water vapour into the air.","zh":"release heat and moisture 指向空氣散發熱力和水蒸氣。"},{"en":"A hot shower releases heat and moisture into a bathroom, making mirrors foggy.","zh":"熱水澡會向浴室釋放熱力和水分，令鏡子起霧。"},{"en":"When warm seas release heat and moisture, rising air can form clouds and storms.","zh":"當暖海釋放熱力和水分，上升空氣可以形成雲和風暴。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how the ocean supplies energy to the atmosphere.","zh":"這個短語解釋海洋如何向大氣提供能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the atmosphere","meaning":"大氣層","examples":[{"en":"Heat and moisture are released into the atmosphere.","zh":"熱力和水分被釋放到大氣層中。"},{"en":"The atmosphere is the layer of gases surrounding the Earth.","zh":"the atmosphere 指圍繞地球的氣體層。"},{"en":"Clouds, winds, rain, and storms all form in the atmosphere.","zh":"雲、風、雨和風暴都在大氣層中形成。"},{"en":"When heat enters the atmosphere, air movement and weather patterns can change.","zh":"當熱力進入大氣層，氣流和天氣模式可以改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the air system around the planet.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞地球的空氣系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"warm, moist air","meaning":"溫暖潮濕的空氣","examples":[{"en":"Warm, moist air forms above the sea surface.","zh":"溫暖潮濕的空氣在海面上方形成。"},{"en":"Warm, moist air is air that is both heated and full of water vapour.","zh":"warm, moist air 指既溫暖又充滿水蒸氣的空氣。"},{"en":"A bathroom after a hot shower is filled with warm, moist air.","zh":"熱水澡後的浴室充滿溫暖潮濕的空氣。"},{"en":"When warm, moist air rises and cools, clouds and rain may form.","zh":"當溫暖潮濕的空氣上升並冷卻，雲和雨可能形成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the air that helps storms grow.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助風暴增長的空氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sea surface","meaning":"海面","examples":[{"en":"Warm air rises from the sea surface.","zh":"暖空氣從海面上升。"},{"en":"The sea surface is the top layer of ocean water that touches the air.","zh":"sea surface 指接觸空氣的海洋最上層水面。"},{"en":"Fishermen may check wind and waves at the sea surface before leaving harbour.","zh":"漁民離港前可能檢查海面的風和浪。"},{"en":"When the sea surface is warm, it can heat the air above it.","zh":"當海面溫暖，它可以加熱上方空氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the boundary where ocean and atmosphere meet.","zh":"這個短語描述海洋與大氣相接的邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"water vapour","meaning":"水蒸氣","examples":[{"en":"Water vapour condenses when warm, moist air rises.","zh":"當溫暖潮濕的空氣上升時，水蒸氣會凝結。"},{"en":"Water vapour is water in gas form in the air.","zh":"water vapour 指空氣中氣體形式的水。"},{"en":"Steam above a hot cup of tea is visible water vapour cooling in the air.","zh":"熱茶上方的蒸氣，是在空氣中冷卻的可見水蒸氣。"},{"en":"When water vapour cools, it can turn into droplets and form clouds.","zh":"當水蒸氣冷卻，它可以變成水滴並形成雲。"},{"en":"This phrase names the invisible moisture that helps create rain and storms.","zh":"這個短語指出幫助形成雨和風暴的看不見水分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"condense to form","meaning":"凝結成","examples":[{"en":"Water vapour condenses to form clouds and precipitation.","zh":"水蒸氣凝結成雲和降水。"},{"en":"To condense to form something means to cool and change into liquid droplets or ice that create it.","zh":"condense to form something 指冷卻並變成水滴或冰，從而形成某物。"},{"en":"Warm breath can condense to form mist on a cold window.","zh":"溫暖呼氣可以在冰冷窗戶上凝結成霧氣。"},{"en":"When vapour condenses in the sky, clouds may grow and rain may fall.","zh":"當水蒸氣在天空中凝結，雲可能增長，雨可能降下。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how gas turns into visible water or ice.","zh":"這個短語解釋氣體如何變成可見的水或冰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"clouds and precipitation","meaning":"雲和降水","examples":[{"en":"Rising moist air forms clouds and precipitation.","zh":"上升的潮濕空氣形成雲和降水。"},{"en":"Clouds and precipitation means cloud masses and falling water such as rain, snow, or hail.","zh":"clouds and precipitation 指雲團，以及雨、雪或冰雹等降下的水。"},{"en":"A weather report may warn that clouds and precipitation will spread across the city by evening.","zh":"天氣報告可能警告雲和降水會在傍晚前擴展至全城。"},{"en":"When moist air cools enough, clouds can form and precipitation can follow.","zh":"當潮濕空氣冷卻到足夠程度，雲可以形成，降水也可能跟隨。"},{"en":"This phrase connects what appears in the sky with what falls from it.","zh":"這個短語把天空中出現的東西與從中落下的東西連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"condensation","meaning":"凝結作用","examples":[{"en":"Condensation releases heat into the surrounding air.","zh":"凝結作用把熱力釋放到周圍空氣中。"},{"en":"Condensation is the process in which water vapour cools and becomes liquid droplets.","zh":"condensation 指水蒸氣冷卻並變成液態水滴的過程。"},{"en":"Condensation appears on a cold drink can when warm air touches its surface.","zh":"當暖空氣接觸冰冷飲品罐表面，罐外會出現凝結水珠。"},{"en":"In storms, condensation releases heat, which can make rising air even more powerful.","zh":"在風暴中，凝結作用釋放熱力，可以令上升空氣更強。"},{"en":"This word describes a physical change that helps clouds and storms develop.","zh":"這個字描述幫助雲和風暴發展的物理變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"solar heat","meaning":"太陽熱能","examples":[{"en":"Condensation releases the solar heat used to evaporate water.","zh":"凝結作用釋放用來使水分蒸發的太陽熱能。"},{"en":"Solar heat is heat energy that comes from the Sun.","zh":"solar heat 指來自太陽的熱能。"},{"en":"Solar heat warms roads, roofs, seawater, and the air above them.","zh":"太陽熱能加熱道路、屋頂、海水和其上方空氣。"},{"en":"When solar heat evaporates ocean water, that energy can later be released inside storms.","zh":"當太陽熱能使海水蒸發，該能量之後可以在風暴內釋放。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the Sun’s role as an energy source.","zh":"這個短語解釋太陽作為能量來源的角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"evaporate the water","meaning":"使水分蒸發","examples":[{"en":"Solar heat evaporates the water at the ocean surface.","zh":"太陽熱能使海面上的水分蒸發。"},{"en":"To evaporate the water means to turn liquid water into water vapour.","zh":"evaporate the water 指把液態水變成水蒸氣。"},{"en":"Sunlight can evaporate the water from wet clothes hanging outside.","zh":"陽光可以使掛在戶外的濕衣服中的水分蒸發。"},{"en":"When water evaporates from the sea, it adds moisture to the air above.","zh":"當水從海面蒸發，它會為上方空氣增加水分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first step in moving water from ocean to atmosphere.","zh":"這個短語描述水由海洋進入大氣的第一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"so-called","meaning":"所謂的","examples":[{"en":"The so-called latent heat of condensation makes the air more buoyant.","zh":"所謂的凝結潛熱令空氣更易上升。"},{"en":"So-called is used before a name or term that something is known by.","zh":"so-called 用於某事物廣為人知的名稱或術語之前。"},{"en":"The so-called smart classroom uses screens, sensors, and online tools.","zh":"所謂的智能課室使用螢幕、感應器和網上工具。"},{"en":"Writers use “so-called” to introduce a technical term or sometimes to show doubt.","zh":"作者使用 “so-called” 來引入技術術語，有時也表示懷疑。"},{"en":"In science writing, it often helps present a specialised name.","zh":"在科學寫作中，它常幫助呈現專門名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"latent heat of condensation","meaning":"凝結潛熱","examples":[{"en":"Latent heat of condensation helps a hurricane strengthen.","zh":"凝結潛熱幫助颶風增強。"},{"en":"Latent heat of condensation is heat released when water vapour changes into liquid droplets.","zh":"latent heat of condensation 指水蒸氣變成液態水滴時釋放的熱力。"},{"en":"In a steamy kitchen, condensation on a cold window releases a small amount of heat.","zh":"在充滿蒸氣的廚房中，冷窗上的凝結會釋放少量熱力。"},{"en":"In a hurricane, this released heat warms the air and helps it rise higher.","zh":"在颶風中，這些釋放出的熱力會加熱空氣並幫助它升得更高。"},{"en":"This phrase names an energy source inside storm development.","zh":"這個短語指出風暴發展內部的一種能量來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"make the air more buoyant","meaning":"令空氣更易上升","examples":[{"en":"Latent heat makes the air more buoyant.","zh":"潛熱令空氣更易上升。"},{"en":"To make the air more buoyant means to make the air lighter and more able to rise.","zh":"make the air more buoyant 指令空氣較輕、較能向上升。"},{"en":"Warm air in a hot-air balloon becomes more buoyant and lifts the balloon upward.","zh":"熱氣球內的暖空氣變得更易上升，並把熱氣球向上托起。"},{"en":"When storm air becomes more buoyant, rising motion becomes stronger.","zh":"當風暴中的空氣更易上升，上升運動會變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why heated air moves upward.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何受熱空氣會向上移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rise higher","meaning":"上升得更高","examples":[{"en":"The air rises higher in a feedback process.","zh":"空氣在反饋過程中上升得更高。"},{"en":"To rise higher means to move upward to a greater height.","zh":"rise higher 指向上移動到更高位置。"},{"en":"Smoke may rise higher when a fire becomes hotter.","zh":"當火變得更熱，煙可能上升得更高。"},{"en":"As storm air rises higher, more moisture can condense and release more heat.","zh":"隨着風暴空氣上升得更高，更多水分可以凝結並釋放更多熱力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes upward movement becoming stronger or taller.","zh":"這個短語描述向上移動變得更強或更高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"self-reinforcing feedback process","meaning":"自我強化的反饋過程","examples":[{"en":"A hurricane strengthens through a self-reinforcing feedback process.","zh":"颶風透過自我強化的反饋過程增強。"},{"en":"A self-reinforcing feedback process is a cycle in which one effect makes the next effect stronger.","zh":"self-reinforcing feedback process 指一個效果令下一個效果更強的循環。"},{"en":"A student who gains confidence may practise more, and more practice may increase confidence further.","zh":"學生建立信心後可能練習更多，而更多練習又進一步增加信心。"},{"en":"In hurricanes, rising air causes condensation, which releases heat and makes the air rise even more.","zh":"在颶風中，上升空氣造成凝結，凝結釋放熱力，令空氣升得更高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a process that strengthens itself.","zh":"這個短語描述會自我增強的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tropical depression","meaning":"熱帶低氣壓","examples":[{"en":"A tropical depression begins to form and strengthen.","zh":"熱帶低氣壓開始形成並增強。"},{"en":"A tropical depression is an early tropical weather system with organised low pressure and winds weaker than a tropical storm.","zh":"tropical depression 指早期熱帶天氣系統，具有組織化低壓和弱於熱帶風暴的風。"},{"en":"Weather reports may watch a tropical depression because it could develop into a stronger storm.","zh":"天氣報告可能監察熱帶低氣壓，因為它可能發展成更強風暴。"},{"en":"If warm water continues to feed it, a tropical depression may intensify.","zh":"如果暖水繼續供養它，熱帶低氣壓可能增強。"},{"en":"This phrase names an early stage in tropical storm development.","zh":"這個短語指出熱帶風暴發展的早期階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"form and strengthen","meaning":"形成並增強","examples":[{"en":"The tropical depression begins to form and strengthen.","zh":"熱帶低氣壓開始形成並增強。"},{"en":"To form and strengthen means to come into existence and then become more powerful.","zh":"form and strengthen 指出現並逐漸變得更強。"},{"en":"A student group may form and strengthen when members meet regularly and share goals.","zh":"當成員定期見面並有共同目標，學生小組可能形成並壯大。"},{"en":"A storm forms when weather parts organise, and it strengthens when it gains more energy.","zh":"當天氣元素組織起來，風暴就形成；當它得到更多能量，就會增強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both beginning and growing stronger.","zh":"這個短語同時描述開始和變強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the familiar eye","meaning":"熟悉的風眼","examples":[{"en":"A hurricane develops the familiar eye at its centre.","zh":"颶風在中心形成熟悉的風眼。"},{"en":"The familiar eye is the well-known calm circular centre of a mature hurricane.","zh":"familiar eye 指成熟颶風中廣為人知、較平靜的圓形中心。"},{"en":"In satellite pictures, the eye looks like a clear hole in the middle of spiral clouds.","zh":"在衛星圖片中，風眼看起來像螺旋雲中間的清晰洞口。"},{"en":"When an eye forms, the storm is usually highly organised and powerful.","zh":"當風眼形成，風暴通常高度組織化且強大。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the recognisable centre of a hurricane.","zh":"這個短語指颶風可辨認的中心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"calm central hub","meaning":"平靜的中心","examples":[{"en":"The eye is the calm central hub around which the hurricane spins.","zh":"風眼是颶風圍繞旋轉的平靜中心。"},{"en":"A calm central hub is the quiet centre around which other activity moves.","zh":"calm central hub 指其他活動圍繞它運行的安靜中心。"},{"en":"In a busy school office, the reception desk can act as a central hub for messages and visitors.","zh":"在繁忙的學校辦公室，接待處可以作為訊息和訪客的中心。"},{"en":"In a hurricane, the calm centre contrasts sharply with the violent winds around it.","zh":"在颶風中，平靜中心與周圍猛烈強風形成鮮明對比。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the eye as the storm’s quiet centre of rotation.","zh":"這個短語把風眼描述為風暴旋轉的安靜中心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"spin around","meaning":"圍繞……旋轉","examples":[{"en":"A hurricane spins around its calm central eye.","zh":"颶風圍繞其平靜中心風眼旋轉。"},{"en":"To spin around something means to rotate around it.","zh":"spin around something 指圍繞某物旋轉。"},{"en":"Children may spin around a playground pole until they feel dizzy.","zh":"孩子可能圍繞遊樂場柱子旋轉，直到感到頭暈。"},{"en":"In a hurricane, powerful winds spin around the eye in a circular pattern.","zh":"在颶風中，強風以圓形模式圍繞風眼旋轉。"},{"en":"This phrase describes circular movement around a centre.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞中心的圓形移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"reach land","meaning":"登陸；抵達陸地","examples":[{"en":"A hurricane weakens when it reaches land.","zh":"颶風登陸時會減弱。"},{"en":"To reach land means to arrive over land after moving across water.","zh":"reach land 指在水面上移動後到達陸地。"},{"en":"A boat reaches land when it arrives at the harbour after crossing the sea.","zh":"船隻橫過海面後到達港口，就是抵達陸地。"},{"en":"When a hurricane reaches land, it loses access to warm ocean water.","zh":"當颶風登陸，它會失去取得溫暖海水的途徑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the moment a sea-based storm comes ashore.","zh":"這個短語描述海上風暴到達岸上的一刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"continuous supply of","meaning":"持續供應","examples":[{"en":"The hurricane loses its continuous supply of warm water after reaching land.","zh":"颶風登陸後失去其溫暖海水的持續供應。"},{"en":"A continuous supply of something is a steady, ongoing amount that keeps coming.","zh":"continuous supply of something 指穩定而持續不斷到來的某物。"},{"en":"A hospital needs a continuous supply of clean water, electricity, and medicine.","zh":"醫院需要清潔食水、電力和藥物的持續供應。"},{"en":"If a storm loses its continuous energy supply, it begins to weaken.","zh":"如果風暴失去其持續能量供應，就會開始減弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that keeps a system working.","zh":"這個短語描述令系統持續運作的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"swiftly weaken","meaning":"迅速減弱","examples":[{"en":"Without warm water, the hurricane swiftly weakens.","zh":"沒有暖水，颶風會迅速減弱。"},{"en":"To swiftly weaken means to become weaker quickly.","zh":"swiftly weaken 指快速變弱。"},{"en":"A phone battery may swiftly weaken if many apps are running at the same time.","zh":"如果同時開啟許多應用程式，手機電量可能迅速減弱。"},{"en":"When a hurricane loses warm water, its winds and clouds can lose energy quickly.","zh":"當颶風失去暖水，其風力和雲系可以迅速失去能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rapid loss of strength.","zh":"這個短語描述力量快速下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"current research","meaning":"目前的研究","examples":[{"en":"The writer’s current research was inspired by an earlier idea.","zh":"作者目前的研究受到早期想法啟發。"},{"en":"Current research means the study or investigation being done now.","zh":"current research 指正在進行的研究或調查。"},{"en":"A doctor may use current research to choose the safest treatment for patients.","zh":"醫生可能利用目前的研究為病人選擇最安全的治療。"},{"en":"Current research can build on older ideas when new technology becomes available.","zh":"當新科技出現，目前的研究可以建立在舊想法之上。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts present study with past work.","zh":"這個短語把現時研究與過去工作作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be inspired by","meaning":"受到……啟發","examples":[{"en":"The research was inspired by an intuition about chaos theory.","zh":"這項研究受到關於混沌理論的直覺啟發。"},{"en":"To be inspired by something means to get an idea, motivation, or direction from it.","zh":"be inspired by something 指從某事得到想法、動力或方向。"},{"en":"A student’s essay may be inspired by a documentary about climate change.","zh":"學生的作文可能受到一部關於氣候變化的紀錄片啟發。"},{"en":"Inspiration can lead someone to restart a project or ask a new research question.","zh":"啟發可以令人重新開始項目或提出新研究問題。"},{"en":"This phrase explains where an idea begins emotionally or intellectually.","zh":"這個短語解釋想法在情感或思想上從何開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an intuition","meaning":"直覺；靈感","examples":[{"en":"The writer had an intuition while studying chaos theory.","zh":"作者在研究混沌理論時有一個直覺。"},{"en":"An intuition is a feeling or idea that seems right before it is fully proved.","zh":"an intuition 指在完全證明前似乎正確的感覺或想法。"},{"en":"A teacher may have an intuition that a quiet student needs help, even before seeing poor marks.","zh":"老師可能在看到低分前，就直覺覺得一名安靜學生需要幫助。"},{"en":"An intuition can start research, but evidence is needed before it becomes a conclusion.","zh":"直覺可以啟動研究，但它成為結論前仍需要證據。"},{"en":"This word describes a useful first feeling, not final proof.","zh":"這個字描述有用的初步感覺，而不是最終證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"chaos theory","meaning":"混沌理論","examples":[{"en":"The writer studied chaos theory many years ago.","zh":"作者多年前研究混沌理論。"},{"en":"Chaos theory studies systems in which small changes can lead to large and unpredictable results.","zh":"chaos theory 研究細微變化可能導致巨大且難以預測結果的系統。"},{"en":"Weather is often linked to chaos theory because tiny changes can affect later forecasts.","zh":"天氣常與混沌理論有關，因為細微變化可以影響後來的預報。"},{"en":"If a system is chaotic, exact long-term prediction becomes very difficult.","zh":"如果一個系統是混沌的，精確長期預測會變得非常困難。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why small influences may matter in complex systems.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何細微影響在複雜系統中可能很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"long-range forecasting","meaning":"長期預報","examples":[{"en":"Long-range forecasting is complicated because the atmosphere is highly sensitive.","zh":"長期預報很複雜，因為大氣層對細微影響高度敏感。"},{"en":"Long-range forecasting means predicting conditions far into the future.","zh":"long-range forecasting 指預測較遠未來的情況。"},{"en":"A farmer may check long-range forecasting before deciding what crops to plant.","zh":"農民可能在決定種植甚麼作物前查看長期預報。"},{"en":"The farther ahead a forecast looks, the more small errors can grow.","zh":"預報越向遠期推算，細小錯誤越可能擴大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes prediction over a long future period.","zh":"這個短語描述對較長未來時段的預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be complicated by","meaning":"因……而變得複雜","examples":[{"en":"Weather prediction is complicated by the atmosphere’s sensitivity.","zh":"天氣預測因大氣層的敏感性而變得複雜。"},{"en":"To be complicated by something means to become more difficult because of it.","zh":"be complicated by something 指因某事而變得更困難。"},{"en":"A school trip may be complicated by heavy rain and transport delays.","zh":"學校旅行可能因大雨和交通延誤而變得複雜。"},{"en":"When many changing factors are involved, planning becomes harder.","zh":"當涉及許多不斷變化的因素，計劃會更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the reason a task is not simple.","zh":"這個短語引出任務不簡單的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be highly sensitive to","meaning":"對……高度敏感","examples":[{"en":"The atmosphere is highly sensitive to small influences.","zh":"大氣層對細微影響高度敏感。"},{"en":"To be highly sensitive to something means to react strongly even to small changes.","zh":"be highly sensitive to something 指即使對細小變化也有強烈反應。"},{"en":"A student who is highly sensitive to noise may find it hard to study in a busy café.","zh":"對噪音高度敏感的學生可能很難在繁忙咖啡店溫習。"},{"en":"If a system is highly sensitive, tiny changes can later produce large differences.","zh":"如果一個系統高度敏感，細微變化之後可以產生巨大差異。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong responsiveness to influence.","zh":"這個短語描述對影響的強烈反應性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"small influences","meaning":"細微影響","examples":[{"en":"Small influences can affect weather-forecasting models.","zh":"細微影響可以影響天氣預報模型。"},{"en":"Small influences are minor factors that may still change a result.","zh":"small influences 指可能仍會改變結果的微小因素。"},{"en":"A small influence, such as a teacher’s praise, can improve a student’s confidence.","zh":"老師一句讚賞這類細微影響，可以提升學生信心。"},{"en":"In complex systems, small influences can grow into bigger effects over time.","zh":"在複雜系統中，細微影響可以隨時間變成更大效果。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds learners that minor causes are not always unimportant.","zh":"這個短語提醒學習者，小原因不一定不重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tiny mistakes","meaning":"微小錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Tiny mistakes can grow quickly in weather models.","zh":"微小錯誤可以在天氣模型中迅速擴大。"},{"en":"Tiny mistakes are very small errors that may seem unimportant at first.","zh":"tiny mistakes 指起初可能看似不重要的非常細小錯誤。"},{"en":"A tiny mistake in an exam answer, such as a wrong minus sign, can change the final result.","zh":"考試答案中的一個微小錯誤，例如錯誤負號，可以改變最終結果。"},{"en":"In forecasting, tiny mistakes can become larger when calculations are repeated many times.","zh":"在預測中，當計算重複多次，微小錯誤可以變大。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that small errors can matter in complex work.","zh":"這個短語顯示小錯誤在複雜工作中可能很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"compound fast","meaning":"迅速累積；迅速加劇","examples":[{"en":"Tiny mistakes can compound fast in weather-forecasting models.","zh":"微小錯誤可以在天氣預報模型中迅速累積。"},{"en":"To compound fast means to increase or build up quickly.","zh":"compound fast 指快速增加或累積。"},{"en":"If a student misses one lesson and then misses the homework, confusion can compound fast.","zh":"如果學生缺席一堂課，之後又沒有做功課，混亂可以迅速加劇。"},{"en":"When small errors compound fast, the final answer may become very different from reality.","zh":"當小錯誤迅速累積，最終答案可能與現實非常不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes problems growing quickly through accumulation.","zh":"這個短語描述問題透過累積快速變大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"weather-forecasting models","meaning":"天氣預報模型","examples":[{"en":"Tiny mistakes can affect weather-forecasting models.","zh":"微小錯誤可以影響天氣預報模型。"},{"en":"Weather-forecasting models are computer systems that use data and equations to predict future weather.","zh":"weather-forecasting models 指使用數據和方程預測未來天氣的電腦系統。"},{"en":"Meteorologists use weather-forecasting models to estimate rain, wind, temperature, and storm paths.","zh":"氣象學家使用天氣預報模型估計雨量、風力、溫度和風暴路徑。"},{"en":"If the input data are wrong, the model’s forecast may also become wrong.","zh":"如果輸入數據錯誤，模型預報也可能變錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes tools used to calculate future weather.","zh":"這個短語描述用來計算未來天氣的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"intentionally apply","meaning":"有意施加","examples":[{"en":"Researchers might intentionally apply slight inputs to a hurricane.","zh":"研究人員可能有意向颶風施加輕微輸入。"},{"en":"To intentionally apply something means to use it deliberately, not by accident.","zh":"intentionally apply something 指有意使用某物，而不是偶然。"},{"en":"A teacher may intentionally apply a new rule to reduce noise in class.","zh":"老師可能有意施行新規則，以減少課堂噪音。"},{"en":"If scientists intentionally apply a small input, they hope to create a planned effect.","zh":"如果科學家有意施加小輸入，他們希望產生計劃中的效果。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses purposeful action.","zh":"這個短語強調有目的的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"slight inputs","meaning":"輕微輸入；細微干預","examples":[{"en":"Slight inputs might create a strong influence on a hurricane.","zh":"輕微輸入可能對颶風產生強大影響。"},{"en":"Slight inputs are small changes or actions added to a system.","zh":"slight inputs 指加入系統中的小改變或小行動。"},{"en":"A slight input, such as adjusting a thermostat by one degree, can change room comfort.","zh":"輕微輸入，例如把溫度控制器調一度，可以改變房間舒適度。"},{"en":"In a sensitive system, a slight input may lead to a much larger effect later.","zh":"在敏感系統中，輕微輸入之後可能導致更大效果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small intervention that may still matter.","zh":"這個短語描述雖小但仍可能重要的干預。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"create a strong influence","meaning":"產生強大影響","examples":[{"en":"Small changes might create a strong influence on a storm.","zh":"小改變可能對風暴產生強大影響。"},{"en":"To create a strong influence means to produce a powerful effect on how something develops.","zh":"create a strong influence 指對某事發展方式產生強大效果。"},{"en":"A supportive teacher can create a strong influence on a shy student’s confidence.","zh":"支持學生的老師可以對害羞學生的信心產生強大影響。"},{"en":"In weather systems, a small change may influence the storm’s later path.","zh":"在天氣系統中，小改變可能影響風暴後來的路徑。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with a powerful effect.","zh":"這個短語把原因與強大效果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"steering it away from","meaning":"使其避開……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists might steer a hurricane away from populated areas.","zh":"科學家可能使颶風避開有人居住的地區。"},{"en":"Steering something away from a place means guiding it so it does not go there.","zh":"steer something away from a place 指引導某物不要去到某地方。"},{"en":"A parent may steer a child away from a busy road.","zh":"家長可能引導孩子避開繁忙道路。"},{"en":"If a storm is steered away from a city, fewer people may be harmed.","zh":"如果風暴被引導避開城市，較少人可能受傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing direction to avoid danger.","zh":"這個短語描述改變方向以避開危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"densely populated areas","meaning":"人口稠密地區","examples":[{"en":"Researchers hope to steer hurricanes away from densely populated areas.","zh":"研究人員希望使颶風避開人口稠密地區。"},{"en":"Densely populated areas are places where many people live close together.","zh":"densely populated areas 指許多人密集居住的地方。"},{"en":"Hong Kong’s urban districts are densely populated areas with many tall buildings.","zh":"香港市區是有許多高樓的人口稠密地區。"},{"en":"When disasters hit densely populated areas, evacuation and rescue become more difficult.","zh":"當災害襲擊人口稠密地區，疏散和救援會更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on crowded human settlement.","zh":"這個短語集中於擁擠的人類聚居地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"slow it down","meaning":"使其減速","examples":[{"en":"A slight input might slow a hurricane down.","zh":"輕微輸入可能使颶風減速。"},{"en":"To slow it down means to reduce its speed.","zh":"slow it down 指降低它的速度。"},{"en":"Speed bumps slow cars down near schools to protect children.","zh":"減速壆令學校附近車輛減速，以保護兒童。"},{"en":"If a hurricane slows down, it may stay longer in one place and bring more rain.","zh":"如果颶風減速，它可能在同一地方停留更久並帶來更多雨。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing movement speed, which may have mixed effects.","zh":"這個短語描述降低移動速度，而效果可能有好有壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"back then","meaning":"當時","examples":[{"en":"Back then, the writer could not test his ideas.","zh":"當時，作者無法測試自己的想法。"},{"en":"Back then means at that earlier time in the past.","zh":"back then 指過去較早的那個時候。"},{"en":"Back then, students used paper dictionaries more often than phone apps.","zh":"當時，學生比手機應用程式更常使用紙本字典。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts an earlier situation with what is possible now.","zh":"這個短語把早期情況與現在可能做到的事作對比。"},{"en":"It helps show how time and technology have changed.","zh":"它幫助顯示時間和科技如何改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"thanks to advances in","meaning":"多虧……方面的進步","examples":[{"en":"The writer resumed his research thanks to advances in technology.","zh":"多虧科技方面的進步，作者恢復了他的研究。"},{"en":"Thanks to advances in something means because progress in that area made something possible.","zh":"thanks to advances in something 指因某範疇的進步令某事成為可能。"},{"en":"Thanks to advances in medicine, some diseases are now easier to treat.","zh":"多虧醫學方面的進步，有些疾病現在較容易治療。"},{"en":"When technology improves, old ideas may become testable for the first time.","zh":"當科技改善，舊想法可能首次變得可測試。"},{"en":"This phrase gives credit to progress as the cause of a new possibility.","zh":"這個短語把進步視為新可能性的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"computer simulation","meaning":"電腦模擬","examples":[{"en":"Computer simulation now allows researchers to test hurricane-control ideas.","zh":"電腦模擬現在讓研究人員測試控制颶風的想法。"},{"en":"Computer simulation uses computers to model real situations and test possible outcomes.","zh":"computer simulation 指使用電腦模擬真實情況並測試可能結果。"},{"en":"A driving school may use computer simulation before students practise on real roads.","zh":"駕駛學校可能在學生上真實道路前使用電腦模擬。"},{"en":"Simulations let researchers test risky ideas without harming real people.","zh":"模擬讓研究人員測試有風險的想法，而不傷害真人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a safe digital experiment.","zh":"這個短語描述安全的數碼實驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"remote-sensing technologies","meaning":"遙感技術","examples":[{"en":"Remote-sensing technologies have improved over the last decade.","zh":"遙感技術在過去十年間已有改善。"},{"en":"Remote-sensing technologies collect information about places or objects from a distance.","zh":"remote-sensing technologies 指從遠距離收集地點或物件資料的技術。"},{"en":"Satellites use remote-sensing technologies to observe forests, oceans, clouds, and storms.","zh":"衛星使用遙感技術觀察森林、海洋、雲層和風暴。"},{"en":"Better remote sensing gives scientists more accurate data for weather models.","zh":"更好的遙感為科學家提供更準確的天氣模型數據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes tools that measure the world without direct contact.","zh":"這個短語描述無需直接接觸也能量度世界的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"renew my interest in","meaning":"重新燃起我對……的興趣","examples":[{"en":"The writer was able to renew his interest in weather control.","zh":"作者得以重新燃起對天氣控制的興趣。"},{"en":"To renew my interest in something means to become interested in it again after a period of less attention.","zh":"renew my interest in something 指一段時間較少關注後，再次對某事產生興趣。"},{"en":"A good teacher may renew a student’s interest in reading after years of boredom.","zh":"好老師可能在學生多年感到沉悶後，重新燃起他對閱讀的興趣。"},{"en":"New tools can renew interest in an old problem by making new solutions possible.","zh":"新工具可以令舊問題出現新解法，從而重新燃起興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes interest returning.","zh":"這個短語描述興趣重新回來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"large-scale weather control","meaning":"大規模天氣控制","examples":[{"en":"New technologies revived interest in large-scale weather control.","zh":"新科技重新激發了人們對大規模天氣控制的興趣。"},{"en":"Large-scale weather control means trying to influence weather systems over a wide area.","zh":"large-scale weather control 指試圖影響廣闊區域的天氣系統。"},{"en":"Cloud seeding is sometimes discussed as a small form of weather control.","zh":"人們有時把人工降雨討論為一種小型天氣控制。"},{"en":"Large-scale control would be difficult because weather systems are complex and powerful.","zh":"大規模控制會很困難，因為天氣系統複雜而強大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weather intervention beyond local or minor changes.","zh":"這個短語描述超出本地或小改變的天氣干預。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"atmospheric system","meaning":"大氣系統","examples":[{"en":"The researchers studied the sensitivity of the atmospheric system.","zh":"研究人員研究大氣系統的敏感性。"},{"en":"The atmospheric system is the connected system of air, heat, moisture, pressure, and movement around Earth.","zh":"atmospheric system 指地球周圍由空氣、熱力、水分、氣壓和運動組成的互連系統。"},{"en":"Weather lessons often explain how the atmospheric system produces clouds, winds, and storms.","zh":"天氣課通常解釋大氣系統如何產生雲、風和風暴。"},{"en":"If one part of the atmospheric system changes, other parts may also respond.","zh":"如果大氣系統的一部分改變，其他部分也可能作出反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the atmosphere as an interconnected system.","zh":"這個短語把大氣描述為互相連繫的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be exploited to","meaning":"被利用來……","examples":[{"en":"The sensitivity of the atmosphere might be exploited to adjust hurricanes.","zh":"大氣的敏感性可能被利用來調整颶風。"},{"en":"To be exploited to do something means to be used deliberately to achieve a result.","zh":"be exploited to do something 指被有意使用以達到某結果。"},{"en":"A school may exploit online tools to give students instant feedback.","zh":"學校可能利用網上工具為學生提供即時回饋。"},{"en":"If scientists exploit a system’s sensitivity, they may use small changes to create larger effects.","zh":"如果科學家利用系統的敏感性，他們可能用小改變創造較大效果。"},{"en":"This phrase can be neutral here, meaning “used strategically.”","zh":"這個短語在這裡可以是中性，意思是「被策略性使用」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"adjust atmospheric phenomena","meaning":"調整大氣現象","examples":[{"en":"Scientists explored whether they could adjust atmospheric phenomena.","zh":"科學家探索他們是否能調整大氣現象。"},{"en":"To adjust atmospheric phenomena means to change weather-related events or systems slightly.","zh":"adjust atmospheric phenomena 指稍為改變與天氣有關的事件或系統。"},{"en":"Cloud seeding attempts to adjust atmospheric phenomena by encouraging rainfall.","zh":"人工降雨試圖透過促進降雨來調整大氣現象。"},{"en":"Adjusting weather systems could reduce danger, but it may also create unexpected effects.","zh":"調整天氣系統可以減少危險，但也可能產生意想不到的效果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deliberate changes to events in the atmosphere.","zh":"這個短語描述有意改變大氣中的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"robust atmospheric phenomena","meaning":"強大的大氣現象","examples":[{"en":"Hurricanes are robust atmospheric phenomena.","zh":"颶風是強大的大氣現象。"},{"en":"Robust atmospheric phenomena are strong weather systems that can maintain themselves and resist small disturbances.","zh":"robust atmospheric phenomena 指能維持自身並抵抗小干擾的強大天氣系統。"},{"en":"A powerful storm front can be a robust atmospheric phenomenon if it continues for many hours.","zh":"如果一個強烈鋒面持續多小時，它可以是強大的大氣現象。"},{"en":"Because hurricanes are robust, changing them safely would require careful understanding.","zh":"因為颶風十分強大，要安全改變它們需要仔細理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weather events that are strong, organised, and hard to disrupt.","zh":"這個短語描述強大、有組織且難以破壞的天氣事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"research team","meaning":"研究團隊","examples":[{"en":"The research team ran computer simulations of Hurricane Iniki.","zh":"研究團隊對 Iniki 颶風進行電腦模擬。"},{"en":"A research team is a group of people working together on a study or investigation.","zh":"research team 指共同進行研究或調查的一組人。"},{"en":"A university research team may study how sleep affects exam performance.","zh":"大學研究團隊可能研究睡眠如何影響考試表現。"},{"en":"Teams allow researchers to share skills, check results, and handle complex problems.","zh":"團隊讓研究人員分享技能、核對結果並處理複雜問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the group carrying out scientific work.","zh":"這個短語描述進行科學工作的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"run simulation experiments","meaning":"進行模擬實驗","examples":[{"en":"The team ran simulation experiments on computers.","zh":"團隊在電腦上進行模擬實驗。"},{"en":"To run simulation experiments means to use models to test what might happen under different conditions.","zh":"run simulation experiments 指使用模型測試不同條件下可能發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Engineers run simulation experiments before building a new bridge.","zh":"工程師建造新橋前會進行模擬實驗。"},{"en":"Simulations can reveal possible results without creating real-world danger.","zh":"模擬可以揭示可能結果，而不造成現實危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes testing ideas in a model rather than in reality.","zh":"這個短語描述在模型中而不是現實中測試想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a hurricane named Iniki","meaning":"一個名為 Iniki 的颶風","examples":[{"en":"The researchers studied a hurricane named Iniki.","zh":"研究人員研究了一個名為 Iniki 的颶風。"},{"en":"A hurricane named Iniki means a specific hurricane that had been given the name Iniki.","zh":"a hurricane named Iniki 指一個被命名為 Iniki 的特定颶風。"},{"en":"Weather agencies give storms names so the public can follow warnings more easily.","zh":"天氣機構為風暴命名，讓公眾更容易跟進警告。"},{"en":"Studying one named hurricane helps researchers compare model results with a known real storm.","zh":"研究一個有名稱的颶風，有助研究人員把模型結果與已知真實風暴比較。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a particular storm, not hurricanes in general.","zh":"這個短語指出特定風暴，而不是泛指颶風。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"occur in","meaning":"發生於","examples":[{"en":"Hurricane Iniki occurred in 1992.","zh":"Iniki 颶風發生於1992年。"},{"en":"To occur in a time or place means to happen there or then.","zh":"occur in a time or place 指在某時間或地點發生。"},{"en":"The school concert occurred in June after final exams.","zh":"學校音樂會發生於六月期末考後。"},{"en":"When a storm occurred in the past, scientists can use records to study it later.","zh":"當風暴在過去發生，科學家可以之後利用紀錄研究它。"},{"en":"This phrase tells when or where an event happened.","zh":"這個短語說明事件在何時或何地發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"current forecasting technologies","meaning":"當時的預報技術","examples":[{"en":"Current forecasting technologies were far from perfect.","zh":"當時的預報技術遠非完美。"},{"en":"Current forecasting technologies are the weather prediction tools available at a particular time.","zh":"current forecasting technologies 指某一時間可用的天氣預測工具。"},{"en":"Current forecasting technologies may include satellites, radar, sensors, and computer models.","zh":"當時的預報技術可能包括衛星、雷達、感應器和電腦模型。"},{"en":"If forecasting tools are imperfect, storm predictions may contain uncertainty.","zh":"如果預報工具不完美，風暴預測可能含有不確定性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the level of prediction technology then available.","zh":"這個短語指當時可用的預測科技水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"far from perfect","meaning":"遠非完美","examples":[{"en":"The forecasting technologies were far from perfect.","zh":"預報技術遠非完美。"},{"en":"Far from perfect means not perfect at all, with clear weaknesses or limitations.","zh":"far from perfect 指完全不完美，並有清楚弱點或限制。"},{"en":"A first draft of an essay may be far from perfect but still useful for improvement.","zh":"作文初稿可能遠非完美，但仍有助改善。"},{"en":"If a tool is far from perfect, users must treat its results with caution.","zh":"如果工具遠非完美，使用者必須謹慎看待其結果。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly shows imperfection.","zh":"這個短語強烈表示不完美。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an immediate success","meaning":"立即成功","examples":[{"en":"The first simulation was an immediate success.","zh":"第一次模擬立即成功。"},{"en":"An immediate success is something that works well right away.","zh":"an immediate success 指一開始就運作良好或成功的事。"},{"en":"A new school app is an immediate success if students and teachers use it smoothly on the first day.","zh":"如果新學校應用程式第一天師生已能順利使用，它就是立即成功。"},{"en":"Immediate success can encourage researchers to continue testing an idea.","zh":"立即成功可以鼓勵研究人員繼續測試想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes success without a long delay.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有長時間延遲的成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"with the goal of","meaning":"以……為目標","examples":[{"en":"The team worked with the goal of altering the path of Iniki.","zh":"團隊以改變 Iniki 路徑為目標進行工作。"},{"en":"With the goal of doing something means with the purpose or aim of doing it.","zh":"with the goal of doing something 指以做某事為目的或目標。"},{"en":"A student may practise speaking daily with the goal of becoming more fluent.","zh":"學生可能每天練習口語，以變得更流利為目標。"},{"en":"Clear goals help people choose the right methods and measure progress.","zh":"清晰目標幫助人選擇正確方法並量度進度。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the intended purpose of an action.","zh":"這個短語引出行動的預期目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"alter the path of","meaning":"改變……的路徑","examples":[{"en":"The researchers wanted to alter the path of the hurricane.","zh":"研究人員想改變颶風的路徑。"},{"en":"To alter the path of something means to change the route it follows.","zh":"alter the path of something 指改變某物所跟隨的路線。"},{"en":"Roadworks may alter the path of a bus for several weeks.","zh":"道路工程可能在數星期內改變巴士路線。"},{"en":"If scientists alter a hurricane’s path, they may move danger away from one area.","zh":"如果科學家改變颶風路徑，他們可能把危險移離某一地區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing direction or route.","zh":"這個短語描述改變方向或路線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"with something in mind","meaning":"心中想着……；以……為考慮","examples":[{"en":"The researchers had a target location in mind.","zh":"研究人員心中有一個目標地點。"},{"en":"To have something in mind means to be thinking about a particular plan, idea, or target.","zh":"have something in mind 指正在考慮某個特定計劃、想法或目標。"},{"en":"A teacher may design a lesson with weaker students in mind.","zh":"老師可能以能力較弱學生為考慮來設計課堂。"},{"en":"Having a clear target in mind helps people decide what changes to make.","zh":"心中有清晰目標有助人決定要作出甚麼改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planning with a specific purpose or person considered.","zh":"這個短語描述帶着特定目的或考慮某人來計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pick the spot","meaning":"選定地點","examples":[{"en":"The team picked the spot where they wanted the storm to stop.","zh":"團隊選定他們希望風暴停下的地點。"},{"en":"To pick the spot means to choose a particular place.","zh":"pick the spot 指選擇某個特定地方。"},{"en":"A family may pick the spot for a picnic under a tree near the lake.","zh":"一家人可能在湖邊樹下選定野餐地點。"},{"en":"Choosing the right spot matters because location can affect safety and results.","zh":"選對地點很重要，因為位置會影響安全和結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes selecting an exact place for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述為某目的選擇確切地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stop after six hours","meaning":"六小時後停下","examples":[{"en":"The researchers wanted the storm to stop after six hours.","zh":"研究人員希望風暴在六小時後停下。"},{"en":"To stop after six hours means to end or come to a halt once six hours have passed.","zh":"stop after six hours 指六小時過去後結束或停下來。"},{"en":"A school event may stop after six hours so students can return home before dinner.","zh":"學校活動可能在六小時後結束，讓學生晚飯前回家。"},{"en":"In a simulation, choosing when something stops helps researchers measure the result.","zh":"在模擬中，選擇某事何時停止有助研究人員量度結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a planned end point after a set time.","zh":"這個短語描述固定時間後的計劃終點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"generate artificial observations","meaning":"產生人工觀測資料","examples":[{"en":"The target was used to generate artificial observations.","zh":"該目標被用來產生人工觀測資料。"},{"en":"To generate artificial observations means to create simulated data for a model instead of collecting it from the real world.","zh":"generate artificial observations 指為模型創造模擬數據，而不是從現實世界收集。"},{"en":"A driving simulator can generate artificial observations about how a driver reacts to danger.","zh":"駕駛模擬器可以產生關於司機如何對危險作反應的人工觀測資料。"},{"en":"Artificial observations help researchers test “what if” situations safely.","zh":"人工觀測資料幫助研究人員安全測試「如果……會怎樣」的情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making data inside a model for experimental purposes.","zh":"這個短語描述為實驗目的在模型內製造數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"put something into the model","meaning":"把……輸入模型","examples":[{"en":"The researchers put artificial observations into the computer model.","zh":"研究人員把人工觀測資料輸入電腦模型。"},{"en":"To put something into the model means to enter information or data into a simulation system.","zh":"put something into the model 指把資訊或數據輸入模擬系統。"},{"en":"A student may put different numbers into a spreadsheet model to test a budget.","zh":"學生可能把不同數字輸入試算表模型，以測試預算。"},{"en":"If the input changes, the model’s output may change as well.","zh":"如果輸入改變，模型輸出也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes feeding data into a model so it can calculate results.","zh":"這個短語描述把數據輸入模型，讓它計算結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"computer model","meaning":"電腦模型","examples":[{"en":"The team used a computer model to simulate the hurricane.","zh":"團隊使用電腦模型模擬颶風。"},{"en":"A computer model is a digital representation of a real system used for testing or prediction.","zh":"computer model 指用於測試或預測真實系統的數碼表示。"},{"en":"Architects may use a computer model to test how sunlight enters a building.","zh":"建築師可能使用電腦模型測試陽光如何進入建築物。"},{"en":"Computer models help researchers study dangerous or complex systems safely.","zh":"電腦模型幫助研究人員安全研究危險或複雜系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a digital tool for analysing real-world behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述分析現實行為的數碼工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"significant alteration","meaning":"重大改變","examples":[{"en":"The most significant alteration involved temperatures and winds.","zh":"最重大的改變涉及溫度和風。"},{"en":"A significant alteration is an important change that can affect the result.","zh":"significant alteration 指可以影響結果的重要改變。"},{"en":"A significant alteration to a school timetable may change when students eat lunch.","zh":"對學校時間表的重大改變可能改變學生吃午飯的時間。"},{"en":"In a storm model, a significant alteration can change the predicted path.","zh":"在風暴模型中，重大改變可以改變預測路徑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a meaningful change, not a tiny detail.","zh":"這個短語描述有意義的改變，而不是微小細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"turn out to be","meaning":"結果是","examples":[{"en":"The most significant alteration turned out to be the initial temperatures and winds.","zh":"最重大的改變結果是初始溫度和風。"},{"en":"To turn out to be something means to be discovered or proved to be that thing later.","zh":"turn out to be something 指後來被發現或證明是某事。"},{"en":"A difficult homework question may turn out to be simple after the teacher explains it.","zh":"老師解釋後，一條困難功課題可能結果是很簡單。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows that the final finding was different from what people expected.","zh":"這個短語常顯示最終發現與人們預期不同。"},{"en":"It introduces what something was eventually found to be.","zh":"它引出某事最終被發現是甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"initial temperatures and winds","meaning":"初始溫度和風","examples":[{"en":"The simulation changed the initial temperatures and winds.","zh":"模擬改變了初始溫度和風。"},{"en":"Initial temperatures and winds are the temperature and wind conditions at the start of a model or event.","zh":"initial temperatures and winds 指模型或事件開始時的溫度和風況。"},{"en":"A weather model needs initial temperatures and winds before it can predict tomorrow’s storm.","zh":"天氣模型需要初始溫度和風，才可以預測明天的風暴。"},{"en":"If the starting conditions change, the later forecast can also change.","zh":"如果起始條件改變，之後的預報也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning weather data used in a simulation.","zh":"這個短語描述模擬中使用的起始天氣數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"across the grid","meaning":"在網格各處","examples":[{"en":"Temperature changes across the grid were usually small.","zh":"網格各處的溫度變化通常很小。"},{"en":"Across the grid means throughout the many squares or points used in a computer model.","zh":"across the grid 指遍佈電腦模型中使用的許多格子或點。"},{"en":"A city map app may calculate traffic across a grid of streets.","zh":"城市地圖應用程式可能在街道網格各處計算交通。"},{"en":"Changes across the grid show how conditions vary from one model location to another.","zh":"網格各處的變化顯示條件如何在模型不同位置之間變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something spread through a model’s whole calculation area.","zh":"這個短語描述某事遍佈模型整個計算區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tenths of a degree","meaning":"十分之幾度","examples":[{"en":"The temperature changes were only tenths of a degree.","zh":"溫度變化只有十分之幾度。"},{"en":"Tenths of a degree are very small temperature changes less than one full degree.","zh":"tenths of a degree 指少於一整度的非常細小溫度變化。"},{"en":"A classroom temperature change of two tenths of a degree would be hard for students to notice.","zh":"課室溫度改變十分之二度，學生可能很難察覺。"},{"en":"In sensitive models, even tenths of a degree may affect later results.","zh":"在敏感模型中，即使十分之幾度也可能影響之後結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very small temperature differences.","zh":"這個短語描述非常細小的溫度差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"noteworthy change","meaning":"值得注意的變化","examples":[{"en":"The most noteworthy change was an increase of almost two degrees Celsius.","zh":"最值得注意的變化是幾乎攝氏兩度的上升。"},{"en":"A noteworthy change is a change important or unusual enough to be noticed.","zh":"noteworthy change 指重要或不尋常到值得注意的變化。"},{"en":"A student’s sudden improvement from failing to top marks is a noteworthy change.","zh":"學生突然由不合格進步到高分，是值得注意的變化。"},{"en":"Noteworthy changes help researchers identify which factors may matter most.","zh":"值得注意的變化幫助研究人員辨認哪些因素可能最重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change worth paying attention to.","zh":"這個短語描述值得留意的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an increase of","meaning":"……的增加","examples":[{"en":"The simulation produced an increase of almost two degrees Celsius.","zh":"模擬產生幾乎攝氏兩度的增加。"},{"en":"An increase of something means a rise by that amount.","zh":"an increase of something 指上升了某個數量。"},{"en":"An increase of ten students in a class may require a larger classroom.","zh":"一班增加十名學生，可能需要更大的課室。"},{"en":"When temperature increases, air movement and pressure patterns may change.","zh":"當溫度上升，氣流和氣壓模式可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the size of a rise.","zh":"這個短語給出上升幅度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"two degrees Celsius","meaning":"攝氏兩度","examples":[{"en":"The temperature rose by almost two degrees Celsius.","zh":"溫度上升了接近攝氏兩度。"},{"en":"Two degrees Celsius is a temperature difference of two units on the Celsius scale.","zh":"two degrees Celsius 指攝氏溫標上的兩度溫差。"},{"en":"A room that warms by two degrees Celsius may feel noticeably more comfortable.","zh":"房間升溫攝氏兩度，可能令人明顯感到更舒適。"},{"en":"In weather systems, a two-degree change can sometimes affect air movement.","zh":"在天氣系統中，兩度變化有時可以影響氣流。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a specific temperature amount.","zh":"這個短語給出特定溫度數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lowest model layer","meaning":"模型最底層","examples":[{"en":"The change took place in the lowest model layer.","zh":"變化發生在模型最底層。"},{"en":"The lowest model layer is the bottom level in a computer model of the atmosphere.","zh":"lowest model layer 指大氣電腦模型中的最底層。"},{"en":"A weather model may divide the atmosphere into layers from the ground upward.","zh":"天氣模型可能把大氣由地面向上分成多層。"},{"en":"Changes in the lowest layer can affect surface winds and nearby temperatures.","zh":"最底層的變化可以影響地面風和附近溫度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the bottom section of a simulation grid.","zh":"這個短語描述模擬網格的底部部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"to the west of","meaning":"在……以西","examples":[{"en":"The temperature increase occurred to the west of the storm centre.","zh":"溫度上升發生在風暴中心以西。"},{"en":"To the west of something means on the western side of it.","zh":"to the west of something 指在某物的西側。"},{"en":"A library may be located to the west of the school hall.","zh":"圖書館可能位於學校禮堂以西。"},{"en":"In weather maps, location matters because small changes on one side of a storm can affect its movement.","zh":"在天氣圖中，位置很重要，因為風暴某一側的小變化可以影響其移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direction and position.","zh":"這個短語描述方向和位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"storm centre","meaning":"風暴中心","examples":[{"en":"Winds changed near the storm centre.","zh":"風在風暴中心附近改變。"},{"en":"The storm centre is the central area around which a storm system rotates or organises.","zh":"storm centre 指風暴系統圍繞旋轉或組織起來的中心區域。"},{"en":"Weather maps often mark the storm centre so people can see where the system is strongest or most organised.","zh":"天氣圖通常標示風暴中心，讓人看見系統在哪裡最強或最有組織。"},{"en":"Changes near the storm centre can affect the storm’s structure and direction.","zh":"風暴中心附近的變化可以影響風暴結構和方向。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the core area of a storm.","zh":"這個短語指出風暴的核心區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"calculations produced","meaning":"計算得出","examples":[{"en":"The calculations produced wind-speed changes.","zh":"計算得出風速變化。"},{"en":"Calculations produced something means mathematical work or computer processing created that result.","zh":"calculations produced something 指數學運算或電腦處理產生某結果。"},{"en":"A budget spreadsheet’s calculations may produce the total cost of a school trip.","zh":"預算試算表的計算可能得出學校旅行總成本。"},{"en":"In a model, calculations turn input data into predicted changes.","zh":"在模型中，計算把輸入數據轉化成預測變化。"},{"en":"This phrase connects mathematical processing with output.","zh":"這個短語把數學處理與輸出連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"wind-speed changes","meaning":"風速變化","examples":[{"en":"The model produced wind-speed changes of two or three miles per hour.","zh":"模型產生每小時兩至三英里的風速變化。"},{"en":"Wind-speed changes are increases or decreases in how fast the wind blows.","zh":"wind-speed changes 指風有多快吹動的增加或減少。"},{"en":"A small wind-speed change may decide whether outdoor sports can continue safely.","zh":"小小風速變化可能決定戶外運動能否安全繼續。"},{"en":"In storms, wind-speed changes can affect direction, damage, and rainfall patterns.","zh":"在風暴中，風速變化可以影響方向、破壞和降雨模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changes in the force of moving air.","zh":"這個短語描述移動空氣力量的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rates shifted by","meaning":"數值改變了……","examples":[{"en":"In several spots, the rates shifted by as much as 20 miles per hour.","zh":"在幾個位置，數值改變高達每小時20英里。"},{"en":"Rates shifted by an amount means the measured speeds or levels changed by that amount.","zh":"rates shifted by an amount 指量度到的速度或水平改變了某個數量。"},{"en":"A bus arrival rate may shift by ten minutes after a road closure.","zh":"道路封閉後，巴士到達時間可能改變十分鐘。"},{"en":"When wind rates shift greatly, the storm’s behaviour may also change.","zh":"當風速數值大幅改變，風暴行為也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how much a measured value has changed.","zh":"這個短語描述量度值改變了多少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"by as much as","meaning":"高達","examples":[{"en":"Some wind speeds shifted by as much as 20 miles per hour.","zh":"有些風速變化高達每小時20英里。"},{"en":"By as much as means up to a surprisingly large amount.","zh":"by as much as 指高達一個令人意外的大數量。"},{"en":"A student’s score may improve by as much as 20 marks after steady practice.","zh":"經過穩定練習，學生分數可能提升高達二十分。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the maximum size of a change.","zh":"這個短語突出變化的最大幅度。"},{"en":"It often stresses that the change is larger than expected.","zh":"它常強調變化比預期大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"minor redirections","meaning":"輕微改向","examples":[{"en":"The wind changes were caused by minor redirections near the storm centre.","zh":"風的變化是由風暴中心附近的輕微改向造成的。"},{"en":"Minor redirections are small changes in direction.","zh":"minor redirections 指方向上的小改變。"},{"en":"A driver may make minor redirections to avoid potholes without changing the whole route.","zh":"司機可能作出輕微改向以避開路面坑洞，而不改變整條路線。"},{"en":"Even small direction changes near a storm’s centre may affect where it travels later.","zh":"即使風暴中心附近的小方向變化，也可能影響它之後前往哪裡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slight adjustments in movement.","zh":"這個短語描述移動上的輕微調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"close to","meaning":"接近……","examples":[{"en":"The wind changes occurred close to the storm’s centre.","zh":"風的變化發生在接近風暴中心的位置。"},{"en":"Close to means near in distance, time, or relationship.","zh":"close to 指在距離、時間或關係上接近。"},{"en":"A student sitting close to the teacher may hear instructions more clearly.","zh":"坐近老師的學生可能更清楚聽到指示。"},{"en":"Changes close to a storm’s centre can matter more because the core controls much of the storm’s movement.","zh":"接近風暴中心的變化可能更重要，因為核心控制風暴許多移動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows nearness.","zh":"這個短語表示接近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in terms of structure","meaning":"就結構而言","examples":[{"en":"In terms of structure, the two versions of the hurricane looked similar.","zh":"就結構而言，兩個版本的颶風看起來相似。"},{"en":"In terms of structure means when considering the shape, organisation, or arrangement of parts.","zh":"in terms of structure 指從形狀、組織或部分排列來看。"},{"en":"In terms of structure, a good essay usually has an introduction, body paragraphs, and a conclusion.","zh":"就結構而言，好文章通常有引言、主體段落和結論。"},{"en":"Two storms may look similar in structure but still move differently.","zh":"兩個風暴結構可能看起來相似，但仍以不同方式移動。"},{"en":"This phrase tells readers exactly which aspect is being compared.","zh":"這個短語清楚告訴讀者比較的是哪個方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"initial and altered versions","meaning":"初始版本和修改版本","examples":[{"en":"The initial and altered versions of Hurricane Iniki seemed almost the same.","zh":"Iniki 颶風的初始版本和修改版本看起來幾乎一樣。"},{"en":"Initial and altered versions are the original version and the changed version.","zh":"initial and altered versions 指原本版本和被改動後的版本。"},{"en":"A teacher may compare the initial and altered versions of a student’s essay to show improvement.","zh":"老師可能比較學生作文的初始版本和修改版本，以顯示進步。"},{"en":"Comparing versions helps people see whether a change has had an effect.","zh":"比較不同版本有助人看見改動是否產生效果。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the starting form with the modified form.","zh":"這個短語對比起始形式和修改後形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"seem almost the same","meaning":"看起來幾乎一樣","examples":[{"en":"The altered storm seemed almost the same as the original one.","zh":"修改後的風暴看起來與原本風暴幾乎一樣。"},{"en":"To seem almost the same means to look or appear very similar, though not completely identical.","zh":"seem almost the same 指看起來非常相似，但不完全相同。"},{"en":"Two phone models may seem almost the same until you compare the camera and battery.","zh":"兩款手機可能看起來幾乎一樣，直到你比較相機和電池。"},{"en":"Things that seem almost the same can still behave differently in important ways.","zh":"看起來幾乎一樣的事物，仍可能在重要方面有不同表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong surface similarity with possible hidden differences.","zh":"這個短語描述表面高度相似，但可能有隱藏差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"critical variables","meaning":"關鍵變量","examples":[{"en":"Changes in critical variables affected the storm’s path.","zh":"關鍵變量的變化影響了風暴路徑。"},{"en":"Critical variables are important factors that can strongly influence the result.","zh":"critical variables 指可以強烈影響結果的重要因素。"},{"en":"In exam performance, sleep, practice, and time management can be critical variables.","zh":"在考試表現中，睡眠、練習和時間管理可以是關鍵變量。"},{"en":"If a critical variable changes, the final outcome may change greatly.","zh":"如果關鍵變量改變，最終結果可能大幅改變。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the key factors in a system.","zh":"這個短語指出系統中的關鍵因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"so substantial that","meaning":"如此重大，以致","examples":[{"en":"The changes were so substantial that the storm veered west.","zh":"這些變化如此重大，以致風暴轉向西方。"},{"en":"So substantial that means so large or important that a clear result happened.","zh":"so substantial that 指大或重要到造成清楚結果。"},{"en":"The rent increase was so substantial that the shop had to close.","zh":"租金升幅如此重大，以致該商店不得不結業。"},{"en":"When a change is substantial enough, it can alter the whole direction of a situation.","zh":"當改變足夠重大，它可以改變整個情況的方向。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a strong cause-and-effect relationship.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"veer west","meaning":"轉向西方","examples":[{"en":"The altered storm veered west during the simulation.","zh":"修改後的風暴在模擬中轉向西方。"},{"en":"To veer west means to suddenly or gradually turn toward the west.","zh":"veer west 指突然或逐漸轉向西方。"},{"en":"A cyclist may veer west at an intersection to avoid roadworks.","zh":"單車手可能在路口轉向西方，以避開道路工程。"},{"en":"If a storm veers west, towns to the west may face greater risk.","zh":"如果風暴轉向西方，西面的城鎮可能面對更大風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change in direction toward the west.","zh":"這個短語描述朝西方的方向改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"travel due north","meaning":"向正北方移動","examples":[{"en":"The storm later travelled due north.","zh":"風暴後來向正北方移動。"},{"en":"To travel due north means to move directly north, not northeast or northwest.","zh":"travel due north 指直接向北移動，而不是向東北或西北。"},{"en":"A hiker may travel due north by following a compass carefully.","zh":"行山者可能小心跟隨指南針向正北方移動。"},{"en":"In storm tracking, direction matters because a small turn can change which areas are hit.","zh":"在風暴追蹤中，方向很重要，因為小轉向可以改變哪些地區被擊中。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an exact northward direction.","zh":"這個短語給出準確的北向方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"leave somewhere untouched","meaning":"令某地未受波及","examples":[{"en":"The altered storm left Kauai untouched.","zh":"修改後的風暴令 Kauai 未受波及。"},{"en":"To leave somewhere untouched means to avoid damaging or affecting that place.","zh":"leave somewhere untouched 指沒有破壞或影響某地方。"},{"en":"A fire may destroy one building but leave the nearby school untouched.","zh":"火災可能燒毀一座建築物，但令附近學校未受波及。"},{"en":"If a storm changes path, it may leave one town untouched while harming another.","zh":"如果風暴改變路徑，它可能令一個城鎮未受波及，卻傷害另一城鎮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place escaping damage.","zh":"這個短語描述某地方逃過破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"future earth-orbiting solar power stations","meaning":"未來繞地球軌道運行的太陽能發電站","examples":[{"en":"Future earth-orbiting solar power stations might help control hurricanes.","zh":"未來繞地球軌道運行的太陽能發電站可能幫助控制颶風。"},{"en":"Future earth-orbiting solar power stations are possible space-based stations that collect solar energy while orbiting Earth.","zh":"future earth-orbiting solar power stations 指可能存在於太空、繞地球運行並收集太陽能的發電站。"},{"en":"Engineers may imagine such stations supplying energy to remote areas from space.","zh":"工程師可能想像這類發電站從太空為偏遠地區供電。"},{"en":"If they could direct energy accurately, they might one day influence weather systems.","zh":"如果它們能準確引導能量，將來可能影響天氣系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a proposed future technology, not something ordinary today.","zh":"這個短語描述一種被提出的未來科技，而不是今天常見事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be equipped with","meaning":"配備有","examples":[{"en":"The power stations could be equipped with large mirrors.","zh":"發電站可以配備大型鏡子。"},{"en":"To be equipped with something means to have the tools or features needed for a purpose.","zh":"be equipped with something 指擁有為某目的所需的工具或功能。"},{"en":"A science lab is equipped with microscopes, safety glasses, and measuring tools.","zh":"科學實驗室配備顯微鏡、安全眼鏡和量度工具。"},{"en":"If a station is equipped with mirrors, it may be able to focus sunlight.","zh":"如果發電站配備鏡子，它可能能夠聚焦陽光。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what a device or place has in order to function.","zh":"這個短語描述裝置或地方為運作而擁有甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"large mirrors","meaning":"大型鏡子","examples":[{"en":"Large mirrors could focus the sun’s rays.","zh":"大型鏡子可以聚焦太陽光線。"},{"en":"Large mirrors are big reflective surfaces that can redirect light.","zh":"large mirrors 指可以重新引導光線的大型反射表面。"},{"en":"A large mirror in a shop can make the room look brighter and more spacious.","zh":"商店中的大型鏡子可以令房間看起來更明亮和更寬敞。"},{"en":"In a solar power system, mirrors can direct sunlight toward a target.","zh":"在太陽能系統中，鏡子可以把陽光引向目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a tool for reflecting and focusing light.","zh":"這個短語描述用於反射和聚焦光線的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"focus the sun’s rays","meaning":"聚焦太陽光線","examples":[{"en":"The mirrors would focus the sun’s rays.","zh":"鏡子會聚焦太陽光線。"},{"en":"To focus the sun’s rays means to direct sunlight onto a smaller or specific area.","zh":"focus the sun’s rays 指把陽光引導到較小或特定區域。"},{"en":"A magnifying glass can focus the sun’s rays onto paper and make it heat up.","zh":"放大鏡可以把太陽光線聚焦到紙上，使紙變熱。"},{"en":"Focused sunlight can carry enough energy to warm or power a target.","zh":"聚焦陽光可以帶有足夠能量去加熱或供能給目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes concentrating solar energy.","zh":"這個短語描述集中太陽能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"panels of photovoltaic cells","meaning":"光伏電池板","examples":[{"en":"The stations would use panels of photovoltaic cells to gather energy.","zh":"發電站會使用光伏電池板收集能源。"},{"en":"Panels of photovoltaic cells are flat groups of solar cells that turn sunlight into electricity.","zh":"panels of photovoltaic cells 指把陽光轉化為電力的平面太陽能電池組。"},{"en":"A school roof may have panels of photovoltaic cells to reduce electricity bills.","zh":"學校屋頂可能有光伏電池板，以減少電費。"},{"en":"When sunlight hits these panels, they produce electrical energy.","zh":"當陽光照射這些板，它們會產生電能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes solar panels used for power generation.","zh":"這個短語描述用於發電的太陽能板。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"gather and send energy","meaning":"收集並傳送能源","examples":[{"en":"The cells would gather and send energy to the Earth.","zh":"電池會收集並傳送能源到地球。"},{"en":"To gather and send energy means to collect power and transmit it somewhere else.","zh":"gather and send energy 指收集能量並把它傳送到其他地方。"},{"en":"A battery can gather and send energy to a phone when it is plugged in.","zh":"外置電池接上手機時，可以收集並傳送能源給手機。"},{"en":"If space stations gathered solar energy, they would need a way to send it safely to Earth.","zh":"如果太空站收集太陽能，它們需要方法安全地把能源傳送到地球。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both collecting and transferring power.","zh":"這個短語同時描述收集和轉移能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be adapted to","meaning":"被改裝成可以……","examples":[{"en":"The stations might be adapted to beam microwaves.","zh":"這些發電站可能被改裝成可以發射微波。"},{"en":"To be adapted to do something means to be changed so it can perform a new function.","zh":"be adapted to do something 指被改變，以便能執行新功能。"},{"en":"A classroom can be adapted to hold an exam by moving desks apart.","zh":"課室可以透過把書桌移開，被改裝成可舉行考試的地方。"},{"en":"If equipment is adapted, it can be used for a purpose it was not originally built for.","zh":"如果設備被改裝，它可以用於原本並非為其設計的目的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes modifying something for a new use.","zh":"這個短語描述為新用途修改某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"beam microwaves","meaning":"發射微波","examples":[{"en":"The power stations could beam microwaves into a storm.","zh":"發電站可以向風暴發射微波。"},{"en":"To beam microwaves means to send microwave energy in a directed beam.","zh":"beam microwaves 指以定向波束傳送微波能量。"},{"en":"A communication device may beam signals from one station to another.","zh":"通訊裝置可能把訊號從一個站點發射到另一個站點。"},{"en":"If microwaves were beamed into a storm, they could transfer energy to water vapour.","zh":"如果微波被發射進風暴，它們可以把能量轉移到水蒸氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sending energy accurately toward a target.","zh":"這個短語描述把能量準確傳向目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be absorbed by","meaning":"被……吸收","examples":[{"en":"The microwaves would be absorbed by water vapour molecules.","zh":"微波會被水蒸氣分子吸收。"},{"en":"To be absorbed by something means to be taken in by it.","zh":"be absorbed by something 指被某物吸入或接收。"},{"en":"Water is absorbed by a sponge when you wipe a wet table.","zh":"當你擦拭濕桌子，水會被海綿吸收。"},{"en":"If energy is absorbed by molecules, those molecules may heat up or vibrate.","zh":"如果能量被分子吸收，那些分子可能升溫或震動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something being taken into another substance.","zh":"這個短語描述某物被另一種物質接收進去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"water vapour molecules","meaning":"水蒸氣分子","examples":[{"en":"Water vapour molecules inside the storm would absorb microwaves.","zh":"風暴內的水蒸氣分子會吸收微波。"},{"en":"Water vapour molecules are tiny particles of water in gas form.","zh":"water vapour molecules 指氣體形式的微小水粒子。"},{"en":"Steam from a kettle contains water vapour molecules moving in the air.","zh":"水壺蒸氣含有在空氣中移動的水蒸氣分子。"},{"en":"When these molecules absorb energy, they can move faster and warm the surrounding air.","zh":"當這些分子吸收能量，它們可以移動得更快並加熱周圍空氣。"},{"en":"This phrase names the microscopic water particles in humid air.","zh":"這個短語指出潮濕空氣中的微觀水粒子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"inside or around","meaning":"在……內部或周圍","examples":[{"en":"The molecules could be inside or around the storm.","zh":"這些分子可能在風暴內部或周圍。"},{"en":"Inside or around means either within something or in the area near it.","zh":"inside or around 指在某物裡面或在其附近區域。"},{"en":"Security cameras may be placed inside or around a school building.","zh":"保安鏡頭可能安裝在校舍內部或周圍。"},{"en":"What happens inside or around a storm can influence its structure and movement.","zh":"風暴內部或周圍發生的事可以影響其結構和移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both the interior and nearby surroundings.","zh":"這個短語同時描述內部和附近環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cause something to vibrate","meaning":"令……震動","examples":[{"en":"Microwaves would cause water molecules to vibrate.","zh":"微波會令水分子震動。"},{"en":"To cause something to vibrate means to make it move rapidly back and forth.","zh":"cause something to vibrate 指令某物快速來回移動。"},{"en":"A phone alarm can cause a table to vibrate if the phone is lying on it.","zh":"如果手機放在桌上，手機鬧鐘可以令桌子震動。"},{"en":"When molecules vibrate more, they can heat the air around them.","zh":"當分子震動得更多，它們可以加熱周圍空氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making something shake at a small scale.","zh":"這個短語描述令某物在細小尺度上震動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"heat up","meaning":"使……升溫","examples":[{"en":"The vibrating molecules would heat up the surrounding air.","zh":"震動的分子會使周圍空氣升溫。"},{"en":"To heat up means to become warmer or make something warmer.","zh":"heat up 指變暖或使某物變暖。"},{"en":"A microwave oven heats up food by transferring energy to molecules.","zh":"微波爐透過把能量傳給分子來加熱食物。"},{"en":"If air heats up, it may rise and change local pressure patterns.","zh":"如果空氣升溫，它可能上升並改變局部氣壓模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increase in temperature.","zh":"這個短語描述溫度上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"surrounding air","meaning":"周圍空氣","examples":[{"en":"The microwaves would heat up the surrounding air.","zh":"微波會加熱周圍空氣。"},{"en":"Surrounding air is the air around a place, object, or system.","zh":"surrounding air 指某地方、物件或系統周圍的空氣。"},{"en":"A heater warms the surrounding air in a room.","zh":"暖爐會加熱房間中的周圍空氣。"},{"en":"When surrounding air warms, it may rise and affect nearby movement.","zh":"當周圍空氣升溫，它可能上升並影響附近運動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the air immediately around something.","zh":"這個短語描述某物緊鄰周圍的空氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"thereby causing","meaning":"從而導致","examples":[{"en":"The heated air might thereby cause the hurricane to slow down.","zh":"被加熱的空氣可能從而導致颶風減速。"},{"en":"Thereby causing means causing as a result of the action just described.","zh":"thereby causing 指因剛才描述的行動而造成。"},{"en":"A school may add more buses, thereby causing shorter queues after class.","zh":"學校可能增加更多巴士，從而令放學後排隊時間縮短。"},{"en":"This phrase links one action directly to its result.","zh":"這個短語把一個行動直接連到其結果。"},{"en":"It is a formal way to show cause and effect.","zh":"它是表示因果關係的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"move in a preferred direction","meaning":"向理想方向移動","examples":[{"en":"The hurricane might move in a preferred direction.","zh":"颶風可能向理想方向移動。"},{"en":"To move in a preferred direction means to travel in the direction people want or choose.","zh":"move in a preferred direction 指朝人們希望或選擇的方向移動。"},{"en":"A rescue team may guide people to move in a preferred direction away from danger.","zh":"救援隊可能引導人們向理想方向移動，遠離危險。"},{"en":"If a storm moves in a preferred direction, it may avoid populated areas.","zh":"如果風暴向理想方向移動，它可能避開人口稠密地區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled or desired movement.","zh":"這個短語描述受控或期望中的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"computer simulations of hurricanes","meaning":"颶風電腦模擬","examples":[{"en":"Computer simulations of hurricanes suggest that storms can be influenced.","zh":"颶風電腦模擬顯示風暴可以受影響。"},{"en":"Computer simulations of hurricanes are digital experiments that model how hurricanes form, move, or change.","zh":"computer simulations of hurricanes 指模擬颶風如何形成、移動或改變的數碼實驗。"},{"en":"Scientists can use computer simulations of hurricanes to test ideas that would be too dangerous in real life.","zh":"科學家可以使用颶風電腦模擬來測試現實中太危險的想法。"},{"en":"These simulations can show whether small temperature or wind changes might affect storm paths.","zh":"這些模擬可以顯示小溫度或風力變化是否可能影響風暴路徑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using computers to study hurricane behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述使用電腦研究颶風行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make a difference to","meaning":"對……產生影響","examples":[{"en":"Changing temperature could make a difference to a storm’s route.","zh":"改變溫度可以對風暴路徑產生影響。"},{"en":"To make a difference to something means to affect it in a meaningful way.","zh":"make a difference to something 指以有意義的方式影響某事。"},{"en":"Ten extra minutes of revision each day can make a difference to exam confidence.","zh":"每天額外溫習十分鐘可以對考試信心產生影響。"},{"en":"A small change can make a difference if the system is sensitive.","zh":"如果系統敏感，小改變也可以產生影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes having a real effect.","zh":"這個短語描述具有實際效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a storm’s route","meaning":"風暴路徑","examples":[{"en":"Air temperature changes might alter a storm’s route.","zh":"空氣溫度變化可能改變風暴路徑。"},{"en":"A storm’s route is the path or direction a storm follows as it moves.","zh":"a storm’s route 指風暴移動時所跟隨的路徑或方向。"},{"en":"Weather maps show a storm’s route so people can prepare before it arrives.","zh":"天氣圖顯示風暴路徑，讓人們在它到來前準備。"},{"en":"If a storm’s route changes, different towns may face danger.","zh":"如果風暴路徑改變，不同城鎮可能面對危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where a storm travels.","zh":"這個短語描述風暴前往哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"abate its winds","meaning":"減弱其風力","examples":[{"en":"Some interventions could abate a hurricane’s winds.","zh":"有些干預可以減弱颶風風力。"},{"en":"To abate its winds means to reduce the strength or intensity of the storm’s winds.","zh":"abate its winds 指降低風暴風力的強度。"},{"en":"Strong building designs cannot abate a storm’s winds, but they can reduce damage.","zh":"堅固建築設計不能減弱風暴風力，但可以減少破壞。"},{"en":"If a hurricane’s winds are abated, the risk to homes and people may fall.","zh":"如果颶風風力被減弱，對房屋和人命的風險可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making winds less severe.","zh":"這個短語描述使風力較不嚴重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"intervention could take many forms","meaning":"干預可以有多種形式","examples":[{"en":"Intervention could take many forms in hurricane control.","zh":"在颶風控制中，干預可以有多種形式。"},{"en":"Intervention could take many forms means there are several possible ways to step in and influence the situation.","zh":"intervention could take many forms 指可以有幾種不同方式介入並影響情況。"},{"en":"School support can take many forms, including tutoring, counselling, and extra practice.","zh":"學校支援可以有多種形式，包括補習、輔導和額外練習。"},{"en":"Different forms of intervention may have different costs, risks, and effects.","zh":"不同形式的干預可能有不同成本、風險和效果。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a range of possible methods.","zh":"這個短語引出一系列可能方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"precisely targeted clouds","meaning":"精準瞄準的雲層","examples":[{"en":"Precisely targeted clouds could be seeded with chemicals.","zh":"精準瞄準的雲層可以被播撒化學物質。"},{"en":"Precisely targeted clouds are clouds chosen very accurately for a specific intervention.","zh":"precisely targeted clouds 指為特定干預被非常準確選中的雲層。"},{"en":"Doctors use precisely targeted treatment when medicine is aimed at one problem area.","zh":"當藥物針對一個問題區域，醫生就是使用精準治療。"},{"en":"If clouds are targeted precisely, scientists hope to affect only the intended part of the storm.","zh":"如果雲層被精準瞄準，科學家希望只影響風暴中預定部分。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses accuracy in choosing where to act.","zh":"這個短語強調選擇行動位置的準確性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be seeded with","meaning":"被播撒……","examples":[{"en":"Clouds might be seeded with silver iodide.","zh":"雲層可能被播撒碘化銀。"},{"en":"To be seeded with something means to have a substance added to encourage a process, especially rainfall.","zh":"be seeded with something 指被加入某種物質，以促進某個過程，尤其是降雨。"},{"en":"A cloud may be seeded with chemicals to encourage water droplets to form.","zh":"雲層可能被播撒化學物質，以促進水滴形成。"},{"en":"If clouds are seeded, precipitation patterns may change.","zh":"如果雲層被播撒，降水模式可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding material to clouds for weather modification.","zh":"這個短語描述向雲層加入物質以改變天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"silver iodide","meaning":"碘化銀","examples":[{"en":"Silver iodide may be used as a rainfall-inducing agent.","zh":"碘化銀可被用作誘導降雨劑。"},{"en":"Silver iodide is a chemical used in some cloud-seeding methods to encourage ice or rain formation.","zh":"silver iodide 指某些人工播雲方法中用來促進冰或雨形成的化學物質。"},{"en":"Scientists may release silver iodide into certain clouds during weather-modification experiments.","zh":"科學家可能在天氣改造實驗中把碘化銀釋放到特定雲層。"},{"en":"The chemical can help tiny particles form, which may influence precipitation.","zh":"這種化學物質可以幫助微粒形成，從而可能影響降水。"},{"en":"This phrase names a substance used in cloud seeding.","zh":"這個短語指出用於人工播雲的物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rainfall-inducing agents","meaning":"誘導降雨劑","examples":[{"en":"Rainfall-inducing agents could change precipitation inside a storm.","zh":"誘導降雨劑可以改變風暴內的降水。"},{"en":"Rainfall-inducing agents are substances used to encourage rain to form.","zh":"rainfall-inducing agents 指用來促進降雨形成的物質。"},{"en":"In cloud seeding, chemicals may act as rainfall-inducing agents.","zh":"在人工播雲中，化學物質可能作為誘導降雨劑。"},{"en":"If such agents change rainfall inside a storm, they may also affect the storm’s structure.","zh":"如果這些物質改變風暴內降雨，它們也可能影響風暴結構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes materials used to trigger or increase rain.","zh":"這個短語描述用來觸發或增加降雨的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"deprive a hurricane of","meaning":"使颶風失去……","examples":[{"en":"Cloud seeding might deprive a hurricane of the water it needs.","zh":"人工播雲可能使颶風失去它所需的水分。"},{"en":"To deprive a hurricane of something means to take away something necessary for it to continue or grow.","zh":"deprive a hurricane of something 指拿走颶風持續或增強所需的東西。"},{"en":"Turning off the electricity deprives a computer lab of the power it needs.","zh":"關掉電力會使電腦室失去所需電源。"},{"en":"If a storm is deprived of moisture, it may weaken or change structure.","zh":"如果風暴失去水分，它可能減弱或改變結構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes removing a vital supply.","zh":"這個短語描述移除重要供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the water it needs to grow","meaning":"其增強所需的水分","examples":[{"en":"A hurricane needs warm water and moisture to grow.","zh":"颶風需要暖水和水分來增強。"},{"en":"The water it needs to grow means the moisture supply required for the hurricane to become stronger.","zh":"the water it needs to grow 指颶風變強所需的水分供應。"},{"en":"A plant needs water to grow, just as a hurricane needs warm ocean moisture to strengthen.","zh":"植物需要水來生長，正如颶風需要溫暖海洋水分來增強。"},{"en":"Without this water supply, the storm’s energy source is reduced.","zh":"沒有這種水分供應，風暴的能量來源會減少。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the fuel that helps a hurricane develop.","zh":"這個短語解釋幫助颶風發展的燃料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"disrupt its eyewall","meaning":"破壞其眼牆","examples":[{"en":"Cloud seeding might disrupt the hurricane’s eyewall.","zh":"人工播雲可能破壞颶風眼牆。"},{"en":"To disrupt its eyewall means to disturb or break up the ring of strongest storms around the hurricane’s eye.","zh":"disrupt its eyewall 指干擾或破壞圍繞颶風風眼的最強風暴環。"},{"en":"A loud interruption can disrupt a class discussion by breaking its flow.","zh":"大聲打斷可以破壞課堂討論，使其流程中斷。"},{"en":"If the eyewall is disrupted, the hurricane’s structure and strength may change.","zh":"如果眼牆被破壞，颶風結構和強度可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damaging the storm’s most organised inner ring.","zh":"這個短語描述破壞風暴最有組織的內圈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"formidable eyewall","meaning":"強大的眼牆","examples":[{"en":"The eyewall is a formidable part of a severe tropical storm.","zh":"眼牆是強烈熱帶風暴中強大的部分。"},{"en":"A formidable eyewall is the powerful ring of storms around a hurricane’s eye.","zh":"formidable eyewall 指圍繞颶風風眼的強大風暴環。"},{"en":"Weather experts watch the eyewall because it often contains the strongest winds.","zh":"天氣專家會監察眼牆，因為它通常包含最強風力。"},{"en":"If the formidable eyewall reaches land, damage can be severe.","zh":"如果強大的眼牆到達陸地，破壞可能很嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the hurricane’s dangerous inner wall of wind and rain.","zh":"這個短語描述颶風中危險的內部風雨牆。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"essential characteristic","meaning":"基本特徵","examples":[{"en":"The eyewall is an essential characteristic of a severe tropical storm.","zh":"眼牆是強烈熱帶風暴的基本特徵。"},{"en":"An essential characteristic is a basic feature that helps define what something is.","zh":"essential characteristic 指幫助定義某物的基本特點。"},{"en":"Clear communication is an essential characteristic of a good teacher.","zh":"清楚溝通是好老師的基本特徵。"},{"en":"If a feature is essential, removing it changes the nature of the thing.","zh":"如果一個特徵是基本的，移除它會改變事物本質。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a defining quality.","zh":"這個短語描述定義性的特質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct heading for each paragraph.","zh":"學生為每段選出正確標題。"},{"en":"To choose the correct heading means to select the title that best matches the main idea.","zh":"choose the correct heading 指選擇最符合主旨的標題。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should read the whole paragraph before choosing the heading.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生選標題前應讀完整段。"},{"en":"A wrong heading often focuses on a detail rather than the paragraph’s main point.","zh":"錯誤標題通常集中於細節，而不是段落主旨。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in IELTS-style reading tasks.","zh":"這個短語是 IELTS 式閱讀題常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The question provides a list of headings.","zh":"題目提供一個標題列表。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a set of possible paragraph titles.","zh":"list of headings 指一組可能的段落標題。"},{"en":"Students compare each paragraph with the list of headings before choosing an answer.","zh":"學生選答案前會把每段與標題列表比較。"},{"en":"Extra headings are often included to test whether students understand the main idea.","zh":"額外標題通常被加入，以測試學生是否理解主旨。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the answer choices for a matching-headings task.","zh":"這個短語描述配對標題題的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"paragraph from the list","meaning":"從列表中選出段落標題","examples":[{"en":"Students choose a heading for each paragraph from the list.","zh":"學生從列表中為每段選出一個標題。"},{"en":"From the list means using only the options already provided.","zh":"from the list 指只使用已提供的選項。"},{"en":"In an exam, students may choose a title from the list rather than write their own.","zh":"在考試中，學生可能要從列表中選標題，而不是自己寫。"},{"en":"The list limits possible answers and helps test careful comparison.","zh":"列表限制可能答案，並幫助測試仔細比較。"},{"en":"This phrase tells students where the answer must come from.","zh":"這個短語告訴學生答案必須來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"write the correct number","meaning":"寫下正確編號","examples":[{"en":"Students write the correct number in the answer box.","zh":"學生在答案框中寫下正確編號。"},{"en":"To write the correct number means to record the number that matches the chosen answer.","zh":"write the correct number 指寫下與所選答案相符的編號。"},{"en":"If heading iv matches paragraph B, students should write iv in the answer box.","zh":"如果標題 iv 配對 B 段，學生應在答案框寫 iv。"},{"en":"Careless numbering can make a correct idea become a wrong answer.","zh":"粗心寫錯編號可以令正確想法變成錯誤答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction about answer format.","zh":"這個短語是關於答案格式的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"hurricanes in history","meaning":"歷史上的颶風","examples":[{"en":"One possible heading is about hurricanes in history.","zh":"其中一個可能標題是關於歷史上的颶風。"},{"en":"Hurricanes in history are hurricanes that happened in the past and are studied through records.","zh":"hurricanes in history 指過去發生並透過紀錄被研究的颶風。"},{"en":"A documentary about hurricanes in history may compare their paths, damage, and death tolls.","zh":"關於歷史上颶風的紀錄片可能比較它們的路徑、破壞和死亡人數。"},{"en":"Studying past hurricanes helps people understand future risks.","zh":"研究過去颶風有助人們理解未來風險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to historical examples of hurricanes, not current storms.","zh":"這個短語指歷史颶風例子，而不是當前風暴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"laboratory exercise","meaning":"實驗室練習；實驗模擬","examples":[{"en":"The heading refers to a laboratory exercise that rerouted a hurricane.","zh":"該標題指一個改變颶風路線的實驗室練習。"},{"en":"A laboratory exercise is a controlled experiment or practice activity used for learning or testing.","zh":"laboratory exercise 指用於學習或測試的受控實驗或練習活動。"},{"en":"Science students may complete a laboratory exercise to test how heat affects water.","zh":"科學學生可能完成實驗室練習，測試熱力如何影響水。"},{"en":"In this context, the exercise is a simulated experiment rather than a real hurricane intervention.","zh":"在這個語境中，該練習是模擬實驗，而不是真實干預颶風。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical test carried out under controlled conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述在受控條件下進行的實用測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"reroute a hurricane","meaning":"改變颶風路線","examples":[{"en":"The simulation showed how researchers might reroute a hurricane.","zh":"模擬顯示研究人員可能如何改變颶風路線。"},{"en":"To reroute a hurricane means to change the path it follows.","zh":"reroute a hurricane 指改變颶風所跟隨的路徑。"},{"en":"Road engineers reroute traffic when a main road is blocked.","zh":"當主要道路被封，工程人員會改變交通路線。"},{"en":"If scientists could reroute a hurricane, they might move it away from a crowded coastline.","zh":"如果科學家能改變颶風路線，他們可能使它避開擁擠海岸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing a hurricane’s direction, not destroying it.","zh":"這個短語描述改變颶風方向，而不是摧毀它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"utilise future technologies","meaning":"利用未來科技","examples":[{"en":"Future technologies might be utilised to influence hurricanes.","zh":"未來科技可能被利用來影響颶風。"},{"en":"To utilise future technologies means to use new or not-yet-common technologies for a purpose.","zh":"utilise future technologies 指為某目的使用新的或尚未普及的科技。"},{"en":"Schools may utilise future technologies to create more personalised lessons.","zh":"學校可能利用未來科技創造更個人化的課堂。"},{"en":"If future technologies become powerful enough, they may open solutions that are impossible today.","zh":"如果未來科技變得足夠強大，它們可能開啟今天不可能的解決方案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using advanced tools that may exist later.","zh":"這個短語描述使用日後可能存在的先進工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be unbeatable","meaning":"無法戰勝的；無法控制的","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether hurricanes are unbeatable.","zh":"題目問颶風是否無法戰勝。"},{"en":"To be unbeatable means impossible to defeat, stop, or control.","zh":"be unbeatable 指不可能擊敗、阻止或控制。"},{"en":"A school team may seem unbeatable if it wins every match by a large margin.","zh":"如果學校隊每場比賽都大勝，它可能看似無法戰勝。"},{"en":"If hurricanes are not unbeatable, research may one day reduce their danger.","zh":"如果颶風並非無法控制，研究將來可能減低其危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that appears impossible to overcome.","zh":"這個短語描述似乎無法克服的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"revisit earlier ideas","meaning":"重新探討早期想法","examples":[{"en":"The writer revisited earlier ideas after technology improved.","zh":"科技改善後，作者重新探討早期想法。"},{"en":"To revisit earlier ideas means to return to old thoughts and examine them again.","zh":"revisit earlier ideas 指回到舊想法並再次審視它們。"},{"en":"A student may revisit earlier essay ideas after receiving new feedback from a teacher.","zh":"學生收到老師新回饋後，可能重新探討早前的作文想法。"},{"en":"Improved tools can make old ideas worth testing again.","zh":"改善了的工具可以令舊想法值得再次測試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes returning to something with fresh conditions or understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述在新條件或新理解下回到某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"save lives","meaning":"拯救生命","examples":[{"en":"Controlling hurricanes might save lives.","zh":"控制颶風可能拯救生命。"},{"en":"To save lives means to prevent people from dying.","zh":"save lives 指防止人死亡。"},{"en":"Seat belts save lives by reducing injuries during car accidents.","zh":"安全帶透過減少車禍受傷來拯救生命。"},{"en":"If storm control reduces danger, emergency teams may save more lives.","zh":"如果風暴控制減少危險，緊急隊伍可能拯救更多生命。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preventing death through action or protection.","zh":"這個短語描述透過行動或保護防止死亡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"low-tech methods","meaning":"低科技方法","examples":[{"en":"Cloud seeding is presented as a relatively low-tech method.","zh":"人工播雲被呈現為相對低科技方法。"},{"en":"Low-tech methods are simple methods that do not require very advanced technology.","zh":"low-tech methods 指不需要非常先進科技的簡單方法。"},{"en":"Opening windows for ventilation is a low-tech method of improving classroom air.","zh":"開窗通風是改善課室空氣的低科技方法。"},{"en":"Low-tech methods may be cheaper and easier to use, but they may also be less precise.","zh":"低科技方法可能較便宜和容易使用，但也可能較不精準。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts simple techniques with highly advanced technology.","zh":"這個短語把簡單技術與高度先進科技作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary with words from the passage.","zh":"學生用文章中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill missing words in a shortened version of the text.","zh":"complete the summary 指在文本的簡短版本中填入缺失字詞。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should read the whole summary before choosing answers.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生選答案前應先讀完整個摘要。"},{"en":"The correct answer must fit both the meaning and the grammar of the sentence.","zh":"正確答案必須同時符合句子的意思和文法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common exam task.","zh":"這個短語描述常見考試任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"one word only","meaning":"只限一個字詞","examples":[{"en":"The instructions require one word only from the passage.","zh":"指示要求只從文章中選一個字詞。"},{"en":"One word only means the answer must contain exactly one word.","zh":"one word only 指答案必須剛好包含一個字詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “moisture,” writing “warm moisture” would break the rule.","zh":"如果答案是 “moisture”，寫 “warm moisture” 就會違反規則。"},{"en":"Word-limit instructions are strict, so extra words can make an answer wrong.","zh":"字數限制指示很嚴格，因此額外字詞可以令答案錯。"},{"en":"This phrase tells students the maximum and exact answer length.","zh":"這個短語告訴學生答案的最大且確切長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"originate as","meaning":"起源於；由……形成","examples":[{"en":"Hurricanes originate as groups of thunderstorms.","zh":"颶風起源於雷暴群。"},{"en":"To originate as something means to begin in that form.","zh":"originate as something 指以某形式開始。"},{"en":"A school club may originate as a small group of friends sharing an interest.","zh":"學校學會可能起源於一小群有共同興趣的朋友。"},{"en":"If a hurricane originates as thunderstorms, understanding thunderstorms helps explain its development.","zh":"如果颶風由雷暴形成，理解雷暴有助解釋其發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first stage of something.","zh":"這個短語描述某事的最初階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"groups of thunderstorms","meaning":"雷暴群","examples":[{"en":"Hurricanes originate as groups of thunderstorms over tropical oceans.","zh":"颶風起源於熱帶海洋上方的雷暴群。"},{"en":"Groups of thunderstorms are several thunderstorm systems occurring close together.","zh":"groups of thunderstorms 指幾個彼此接近出現的雷暴系統。"},{"en":"Weather radar may show groups of thunderstorms gathering before a larger storm develops.","zh":"天氣雷達可能顯示雷暴群正在聚集，之後發展成更大風暴。"},{"en":"If the groups remain over warm water, they can become more organised.","zh":"如果這些雷暴群停留在暖水上方，它們可以變得更有組織。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the cluster-like beginning of a hurricane.","zh":"這個短語描述颶風像群集般的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"provide heat and moisture","meaning":"提供熱力和水分","examples":[{"en":"Low-latitude seas provide heat and moisture to the atmosphere.","zh":"低緯度海域向大氣層提供熱力和水分。"},{"en":"To provide heat and moisture means to supply warmth and water vapour.","zh":"provide heat and moisture 指供應溫暖和水蒸氣。"},{"en":"A hot shower provides heat and moisture that can fog a bathroom mirror.","zh":"熱水澡提供熱力和水分，可以令浴室鏡子起霧。"},{"en":"When seas provide heat and moisture, rising air can feed storm development.","zh":"當海洋提供熱力和水分，上升空氣可以供養風暴發展。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how warm oceans support weather systems.","zh":"這個短語解釋暖海如何支援天氣系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"humid air","meaning":"潮濕空氣","examples":[{"en":"Warm, humid air forms above the sea surface.","zh":"溫暖潮濕空氣在海面上方形成。"},{"en":"Humid air is air that contains a lot of water vapour.","zh":"humid air 指含有大量水蒸氣的空氣。"},{"en":"On a rainy summer day, humid air can make clothes feel sticky.","zh":"在下雨的夏日，潮濕空氣可以令衣服感覺黏身。"},{"en":"Humid air can form clouds when it rises and cools.","zh":"潮濕空氣上升並冷卻時，可以形成雲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moisture-rich air.","zh":"這個短語描述富含水分的空氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"ascend still higher","meaning":"繼續向上升得更高","examples":[{"en":"Buoyant air ascends still higher in the storm system.","zh":"易上升的空氣在風暴系統中繼續向上升得更高。"},{"en":"To ascend still higher means to rise even further upward.","zh":"ascend still higher 指進一步向上升。"},{"en":"Smoke from a stronger fire may ascend still higher into the sky.","zh":"更猛烈火焰產生的煙可能繼續向天空升得更高。"},{"en":"When storm air ascends higher, more condensation and heat release may occur.","zh":"當風暴空氣升得更高，可能出現更多凝結和熱力釋放。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continued upward movement.","zh":"這個短語描述持續的向上移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"begin to organise and strengthen","meaning":"開始組織並增強","examples":[{"en":"The tropical depression begins to organise and strengthen.","zh":"熱帶低氣壓開始組織並增強。"},{"en":"To begin to organise and strengthen means to start forming a clearer structure and becoming more powerful.","zh":"begin to organise and strengthen 指開始形成更清晰結構並變得更強大。"},{"en":"A student group may begin to organise and strengthen after choosing leaders and meeting regularly.","zh":"學生小組選出領袖並定期開會後，可能開始組織並壯大。"},{"en":"A storm that organises and strengthens may become more dangerous.","zh":"開始組織並增強的風暴可能變得更危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes development from weak and loose to structured and strong.","zh":"這個短語描述由弱而鬆散發展成有結構而強大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"sustaining source","meaning":"維持其力量的來源","examples":[{"en":"Warm water is the hurricane’s sustaining source of energy.","zh":"暖水是颶風維持其能量的來源。"},{"en":"A sustaining source is something that keeps a process or system going.","zh":"sustaining source 指令某過程或系統持續下去的來源。"},{"en":"Regular customers can be the sustaining source of income for a small shop.","zh":"固定顧客可以是小店維持收入的來源。"},{"en":"If the sustaining source disappears, the system may weaken or stop.","zh":"如果維持來源消失，系統可能減弱或停止。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the supply that maintains strength.","zh":"這個短語描述維持力量的供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be cut off","meaning":"被切斷","examples":[{"en":"The storm’s supply of warm water is cut off over land.","zh":"風暴在陸地上方時，暖水供應被切斷。"},{"en":"To be cut off means to be stopped or separated from a supply, route, or connection.","zh":"be cut off 指供應、路線或連接被停止或隔絕。"},{"en":"A village may be cut off after a landslide blocks the only road.","zh":"山泥傾瀉堵塞唯一道路後，村莊可能被切斷。"},{"en":"When a hurricane is cut off from warm water, it loses an important energy source.","zh":"當颶風與暖水被切斷，它會失去重要能量來源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes losing access to something necessary.","zh":"這個短語描述失去取得必要事物的途徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"rapid weakening","meaning":"迅速減弱","examples":[{"en":"The loss of warm water leads to rapid weakening.","zh":"失去暖水會導致迅速減弱。"},{"en":"Rapid weakening means becoming weaker quickly.","zh":"rapid weakening 指快速變弱。"},{"en":"A phone may show rapid weakening of battery life if its battery is old.","zh":"如果手機電池老化，電量可能迅速減弱。"},{"en":"When a storm loses its energy source, its winds may reduce quickly.","zh":"當風暴失去能量來源，其風力可能快速下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fast decline in strength.","zh":"這個短語描述力量快速衰退。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生為每題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the option marked by the right letter.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇以正確字母標示的選項。"},{"en":"If option B matches the passage, students should choose the letter B.","zh":"如果 B 選項與文章相符，學生應選字母 B。"},{"en":"Students must read carefully because wrong options may include partly true details.","zh":"學生必須仔細閱讀，因為錯誤選項可能包含部分正確細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is a standard multiple-choice instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準選擇題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"encourage someone to restart","meaning":"促使某人重新開始","examples":[{"en":"Technological advances encouraged the writer to restart his research.","zh":"科技進步促使作者重新開始他的研究。"},{"en":"To encourage someone to restart means to make someone feel able or willing to begin again.","zh":"encourage someone to restart 指令某人覺得能夠或願意再次開始。"},{"en":"A teacher’s feedback may encourage a student to restart an essay instead of giving up.","zh":"老師的回饋可能促使學生重新開始一篇作文，而不是放棄。"},{"en":"New tools can encourage researchers to restart old projects that once seemed impossible.","zh":"新工具可以促使研究人員重新開始曾經看似不可能的舊項目。"},{"en":"This phrase describes support or motivation to begin again.","zh":"這個短語描述重新開始的支持或動力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"restart researching","meaning":"重新研究","examples":[{"en":"The writer restarted researching hurricane control after technology improved.","zh":"科技改善後，作者重新研究颶風控制。"},{"en":"To restart researching means to begin studying a topic again after stopping.","zh":"restart researching 指停止後再次開始研究某題目。"},{"en":"A student may restart researching a history project after finding better sources.","zh":"學生找到更好的資料後，可能重新研究歷史專題。"},{"en":"Improved technology can make old research questions possible to investigate again.","zh":"改善了的科技可以令舊研究問題再次變得可調查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes returning to a research topic.","zh":"這個短語描述回到某個研究題目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"enormous damage","meaning":"巨大破壞","examples":[{"en":"The enormous damage caused by hurricanes motivates research into storm control.","zh":"颶風造成的巨大破壞推動了風暴控制研究。"},{"en":"Enormous damage means extremely large or serious destruction.","zh":"enormous damage 指極大或極嚴重的破壞。"},{"en":"A major earthquake can cause enormous damage to roads, schools, and hospitals.","zh":"大地震可以對道路、學校和醫院造成巨大破壞。"},{"en":"When damage is enormous, governments may spend years rebuilding communities.","zh":"當破壞巨大，政府可能花多年重建社區。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses very severe harm.","zh":"這個短語強調非常嚴重的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"advances in computer technology","meaning":"電腦科技的進步","examples":[{"en":"Advances in computer technology made new simulations possible.","zh":"電腦科技的進步使新的模擬成為可能。"},{"en":"Advances in computer technology are improvements in computer speed, software, storage, and modelling ability.","zh":"advances in computer technology 指電腦速度、軟件、儲存和建模能力的改善。"},{"en":"Advances in computer technology allow students to learn through online platforms and simulations.","zh":"電腦科技的進步讓學生透過網上平台和模擬學習。"},{"en":"Better computers can process more data and test more complicated models.","zh":"更好的電腦可以處理更多數據並測試更複雜模型。"},{"en":"This phrase describes progress that opens new digital possibilities.","zh":"這個短語描述開啟新數碼可能性的進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the requirement of","meaning":"……的要求","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to the requirement of some local people.","zh":"該選項提到某些本地人的要求。"},{"en":"The requirement of someone means something that person or group needs, requests, or demands.","zh":"requirement of someone 指某人或某群體需要、請求或要求的事。"},{"en":"The requirement of a school may include safe classrooms and enough teachers.","zh":"學校的要求可能包括安全課室和足夠教師。"},{"en":"If a project ignores local requirements, people may reject it.","zh":"如果項目忽視本地要求，人們可能拒絕它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a need or demand belonging to a person or group.","zh":"這個短語描述屬於某人或群體的需要或要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"study of chaos theory","meaning":"對混沌理論的研究","examples":[{"en":"The writer’s study of chaos theory first inspired his idea.","zh":"作者對混沌理論的研究首先啟發了他的想法。"},{"en":"Study of chaos theory means learning or researching how sensitive systems can produce unpredictable results.","zh":"study of chaos theory 指學習或研究敏感系統如何產生難以預測的結果。"},{"en":"A university course may include the study of chaos theory in weather, physics, or mathematics.","zh":"大學課程可能包括對天氣、物理或數學中混沌理論的研究。"},{"en":"This study can make researchers think differently about small causes and large effects.","zh":"這種研究可以令研究人員以不同方式思考小原因和大效果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes academic work on complex sensitive systems.","zh":"這個短語描述關於複雜敏感系統的學術工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reaction after the first experiment","meaning":"第一次實驗後的反應","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the writer’s reaction after the first experiment.","zh":"題目詢問作者第一次實驗後的反應。"},{"en":"A reaction after the first experiment is how someone feels or responds once the first test is finished.","zh":"reaction after the first experiment 指第一次測試完成後某人的感受或回應。"},{"en":"A student’s reaction after the first science experiment may be excitement if the result works.","zh":"如果結果成功，學生第一次科學實驗後的反應可能是興奮。"},{"en":"Reactions can show whether researchers feel encouraged, disappointed, surprised, or doubtful.","zh":"反應可以顯示研究人員感到受鼓舞、失望、驚訝或懷疑。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on emotional or intellectual response after a test.","zh":"這個短語集中於測試後的情感或思想回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"achieve very little","meaning":"幾乎沒有成效","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that the intervention achieved very little.","zh":"該選項暗示干預幾乎沒有成效。"},{"en":"To achieve very little means to produce almost no useful result.","zh":"achieve very little 指幾乎沒有產生有用結果。"},{"en":"A study plan may achieve very little if the student only copies notes without understanding them.","zh":"如果學生只抄筆記而不理解內容，學習計劃可能幾乎沒有成效。"},{"en":"If an intervention achieves very little, researchers may need to change the method.","zh":"如果干預幾乎沒有成效，研究人員可能需要改變方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weak or disappointing results.","zh":"這個短語描述薄弱或令人失望的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"ecstatic about","meaning":"對……欣喜若狂","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that the writer was ecstatic about the experiment’s success.","zh":"該選項暗示作者對實驗成功欣喜若狂。"},{"en":"To be ecstatic about something means to feel extremely happy and excited about it.","zh":"be ecstatic about something 指對某事感到極度高興和興奮。"},{"en":"A student may be ecstatic about receiving a scholarship after months of hard work.","zh":"學生努力數月後獲得獎學金，可能欣喜若狂。"},{"en":"People feel ecstatic when a result is better than they expected.","zh":"當結果比預期更好，人們會感到欣喜若狂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very strong happiness.","zh":"這個短語描述非常強烈的快樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"intended effect","meaning":"預期效果","examples":[{"en":"The intervention had the intended effect in the simulation.","zh":"該干預在模擬中產生了預期效果。"},{"en":"The intended effect is the result that someone wanted or planned to produce.","zh":"intended effect 指某人想要或計劃產生的結果。"},{"en":"If a reminder app helps a student submit homework on time, it has its intended effect.","zh":"如果提醒應用程式幫助學生準時交功課，它就達到預期效果。"},{"en":"Researchers compare intended effects with actual effects to see whether an experiment worked.","zh":"研究人員比較預期效果和實際效果，以判斷實驗是否成功。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the planned result of an action.","zh":"這個短語描述行動的計劃結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"regretful about","meaning":"對……感到後悔","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that the writer was regretful about the experiment’s likely success.","zh":"該選項暗示作者對實驗可能成功感到後悔。"},{"en":"To be regretful about something means to feel sorry, uneasy, or disappointed about it.","zh":"be regretful about something 指對某事感到抱歉、不安或失望。"},{"en":"A student may be regretful about missing a deadline after wasting time.","zh":"學生浪費時間後錯過截止日期，可能感到後悔。"},{"en":"People may feel regretful when a choice leads to a result they do not welcome.","zh":"當一個選擇帶來人們不想要的結果，他們可能感到後悔。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sadness or discomfort about what happened or may happen.","zh":"這個短語描述對已發生或可能發生的事感到難過或不安。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"likely success","meaning":"可能成功","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to the experiment’s likely success.","zh":"該選項提到實驗可能成功。"},{"en":"Likely success means success that seems probable but is not completely certain.","zh":"likely success 指看來可能但尚未完全確定的成功。"},{"en":"A student’s likely success in an exam may depend on steady revision and enough sleep.","zh":"學生考試可能成功，可能取決於穩定溫習和足夠睡眠。"},{"en":"If early results are promising, researchers may expect likely success in later tests.","zh":"如果早期結果有希望，研究人員可能預期之後測試會成功。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a result that seems probable.","zh":"這個短語描述看來可能發生的成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 53 - Can Hurricanes be Moderated or Diverted?.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 54":[{"front":"quantitative research in education","meaning":"教育中的定量研究","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses quantitative research in education.","zh":"文章討論教育中的定量研究。"},{"en":"Quantitative research in education uses numbers, tests, scores, and statistics to study learning.","zh":"教育中的定量研究使用數字、測驗、分數和統計來研究學習。"},{"en":"A school may use quantitative research in education to compare students’ reading scores before and after a new programme.","zh":"學校可能使用教育中的定量研究，比較新課程前後學生的閱讀分數。"},{"en":"Quantitative research in education can reveal patterns, but it may miss how students feel or interpret questions.","zh":"教育中的定量研究可以揭示模式，但可能忽略學生的感受或對問題的理解方式。"},{"en":"This kind of research is useful when researchers want measurable evidence rather than only personal stories.","zh":"當研究人員想要可量度證據，而不只是個人故事時，這類研究很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"educational researchers","meaning":"教育研究人員","examples":[{"en":"Many educational researchers study how children learn and develop.","zh":"許多教育研究人員研究兒童如何學習和發展。"},{"en":"Educational researchers are people who investigate teaching, learning, schools, and student development.","zh":"教育研究人員是研究教學、學習、學校和學生發展的人。"},{"en":"Educational researchers may observe classrooms to understand why some students participate more than others.","zh":"教育研究人員可能觀察課室，以了解為何有些學生較常參與。"},{"en":"Their findings can influence teaching methods, school policies, and assessment design.","zh":"他們的研究結果可以影響教學方法、學校政策和評估設計。"},{"en":"Educational researchers do not only count test scores; some also study classroom relationships and student experiences.","zh":"教育研究人員不只計算測驗分數；有些也研究課室關係和學生經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"used to work on the assumption that","meaning":"過去一直基於……這一假設","examples":[{"en":"Many educational researchers used to work on the assumption that children develop in phases.","zh":"許多教育研究人員過去一直基於兒童按階段發展這一假設。"},{"en":"Used to work on the assumption that means people previously based their work on a belief they accepted as true.","zh":"used to work on the assumption that 指人們過去把某個信念當成真實基礎來工作或研究。"},{"en":"Doctors used to work on the assumption that rest alone was enough for some injuries.","zh":"醫生過去可能一直基於某些傷患只需休息便足夠這一假設。"},{"en":"If researchers work on a wrong assumption, their conclusions may need to be revised later.","zh":"如果研究人員基於錯誤假設行事，他們的結論日後可能需要修訂。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces an older belief that newer evidence may question.","zh":"這個短語常引入一個較舊、可能被新證據質疑的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"work on the assumption that","meaning":"基於……這一假設行事；研究","examples":[{"en":"The researchers worked on the assumption that cognitive development occurs in stages.","zh":"研究人員基於認知發展按階段出現這一假設進行研究。"},{"en":"To work on the assumption that means to plan, judge, or research as if something is true.","zh":"work on the assumption that 指在計劃、判斷或研究時，把某事當作真實。"},{"en":"A teacher may work on the assumption that students have already learnt basic sentence structure.","zh":"老師可能基於學生已學過基本句子結構這一假設來教學。"},{"en":"If the assumption is wrong, the lesson may become too difficult or too easy.","zh":"如果假設錯誤，課堂可能變得太難或太容易。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the belief behind someone’s method or decision.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人方法或決定背後的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"experience different phases of development","meaning":"經歷不同發展階段","examples":[{"en":"Children may experience different phases of development.","zh":"兒童可能經歷不同發展階段。"},{"en":"To experience different phases of development means to go through separate periods of growth or change.","zh":"experience different phases of development 指經歷不同時期的成長或變化。"},{"en":"A teenager may experience different phases of development in confidence, independence, and social skills.","zh":"青少年可能在自信、獨立和社交能力方面經歷不同發展階段。"},{"en":"These phases can affect how children understand instructions and solve problems.","zh":"這些階段可以影響兒童如何理解指示和解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing gradual growth rather than one sudden change.","zh":"這個短語適合描述逐步成長，而不是一次突然改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"phases of development","meaning":"發展階段","examples":[{"en":"Piaget believed that children pass through phases of development.","zh":"Piaget 認為兒童會經歷不同發展階段。"},{"en":"Phases of development are stages in which a person grows or changes in ability, thinking, or behaviour.","zh":"phases of development 指人在能力、思考或行為上成長或變化的階段。"},{"en":"A baby learning to crawl, walk, and speak is moving through phases of development.","zh":"嬰兒學會爬行、走路和說話，就是在經歷不同發展階段。"},{"en":"Different phases may require different kinds of teaching and support.","zh":"不同階段可能需要不同種類的教學和支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordered periods of growth.","zh":"這個短語描述有次序的成長時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"perform complex cognitive operations","meaning":"進行複雜的認知運作","examples":[{"en":"Young children may not be able to perform complex cognitive operations.","zh":"年幼兒童可能未能進行複雜的認知運作。"},{"en":"To perform complex cognitive operations means to carry out difficult mental tasks such as comparing, reasoning, or classifying.","zh":"perform complex cognitive operations 指進行比較、推理或分類等困難心理任務。"},{"en":"A child performs complex cognitive operations when she solves a logic puzzle with several steps.","zh":"孩子解答有幾個步驟的邏輯題時，就是在進行複雜的認知運作。"},{"en":"If a task requires too much reasoning, younger students may misunderstand it.","zh":"如果任務需要太多推理，年幼學生可能會誤解它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to demanding thinking processes, not physical actions.","zh":"這個短語指要求高的思考過程，而不是身體動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cognitive operations","meaning":"認知運作","examples":[{"en":"The experiment tested children’s ability to carry out cognitive operations.","zh":"實驗測試兒童進行認知運作的能力。"},{"en":"Cognitive operations are mental actions such as remembering, comparing, reasoning, and judging.","zh":"cognitive operations 指記憶、比較、推理和判斷等心理動作。"},{"en":"Choosing the best answer in a reading test involves several cognitive operations.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中選出最佳答案涉及幾種認知運作。"},{"en":"Weak instructions can make a task look like a thinking problem when it is really a communication problem.","zh":"指示不清可以令一項任務看似是思考問題，其實是溝通問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what the mind does when solving a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述人在解難時思維所做的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"reach an advanced stage of","meaning":"達到……的高級階段","examples":[{"en":"Children cannot perform some tasks until they reach an advanced stage of development.","zh":"兒童要到達到較高級的發展階段，才能完成某些任務。"},{"en":"To reach an advanced stage of something means to develop to a high or later level.","zh":"reach an advanced stage of something 指發展到較高或較後期的水平。"},{"en":"A student may not write persuasive essays well until she reaches an advanced stage of language learning.","zh":"學生可能要到達較高級的語言學習階段，才能寫好議論文。"},{"en":"When learners reach a more advanced stage, they can handle more abstract tasks.","zh":"當學習者達到較高級階段，他們就能處理更抽象的任務。"},{"en":"This phrase connects ability with development over time.","zh":"這個短語把能力與隨時間發展連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an advanced stage of cognitive development","meaning":"認知發展的高級階段","examples":[{"en":"Piaget believed that the children had not reached an advanced stage of cognitive development.","zh":"Piaget 認為兒童尚未達到認知發展的高級階段。"},{"en":"An advanced stage of cognitive development is a later level of mental growth where children can reason more logically.","zh":"an advanced stage of cognitive development 指兒童能更有邏輯地推理的較後期心理成長水平。"},{"en":"A child at an advanced stage of cognitive development may understand that quantity stays the same even when shape changes.","zh":"處於認知發展高級階段的孩子，可能明白即使形狀改變，數量仍保持不變。"},{"en":"If children have not reached this stage, they may rely more on appearance than logic.","zh":"如果兒童尚未達到這階段，他們可能更依賴外觀而不是邏輯。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a high level of thinking ability in child development.","zh":"這個短語指兒童發展中較高水平的思考能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cognitive development","meaning":"認知發展","examples":[{"en":"The study focused on children’s cognitive development.","zh":"這項研究集中於兒童的認知發展。"},{"en":"Cognitive development is the growth of thinking, memory, reasoning, language, and problem-solving ability.","zh":"cognitive development 指思考、記憶、推理、語言和解難能力的成長。"},{"en":"Reading stories, asking questions, and solving puzzles can support cognitive development.","zh":"閱讀故事、提問和解難題都可以支持認知發展。"},{"en":"Poor sleep or stress may slow cognitive development because children cannot focus well.","zh":"睡眠不足或壓力可能拖慢認知發展，因為兒童不能好好集中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how the mind develops over time.","zh":"這個短語描述心智如何隨時間發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"conduct a well-known experiment","meaning":"進行一項著名實驗","examples":[{"en":"Jean Piaget conducted a well-known experiment with children.","zh":"Jean Piaget 與兒童進行了一項著名實驗。"},{"en":"To conduct a well-known experiment means to carry out a famous study in a careful, organised way.","zh":"conduct a well-known experiment 指以仔細、有組織的方式進行一項著名研究。"},{"en":"A psychologist may conduct a well-known experiment again to see whether the result still appears today.","zh":"心理學家可能重新進行一項著名實驗，以看看結果今天是否仍會出現。"},{"en":"Famous experiments can shape how teachers and researchers think for many years.","zh":"著名實驗可以多年影響老師和研究人員的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when describing an important research activity.","zh":"這個短語用於描述重要研究活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"compare the amount of","meaning":"比較……的數量","examples":[{"en":"Piaget asked children to compare the amount of liquid in different containers.","zh":"Piaget 要求兒童比較不同容器中液體的數量。"},{"en":"To compare the amount of something means to judge whether one quantity is larger, smaller, or the same.","zh":"compare the amount of something 指判斷某一數量是較大、較小還是相同。"},{"en":"Students compare the amount of sugar in two drinks before deciding which is healthier.","zh":"學生在決定哪款飲品較健康前，會比較兩款飲品中的糖分含量。"},{"en":"Comparing amounts can be difficult if the containers or shapes look very different.","zh":"如果容器或形狀看起來很不同，比較數量可能會變困難。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on judging quantity.","zh":"這個短語著重判斷數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"containers with different shapes","meaning":"不同形狀的容器","examples":[{"en":"The children looked at containers with different shapes.","zh":"兒童看着不同形狀的容器。"},{"en":"Containers with different shapes are objects that hold something but have different forms or outlines.","zh":"containers with different shapes 指能盛載東西但外形或輪廓不同的物件。"},{"en":"A tall glass and a wide bowl are containers with different shapes.","zh":"高玻璃杯和闊碗是不同形狀的容器。"},{"en":"Different shapes can make the same amount of liquid look larger or smaller.","zh":"不同形狀可以令相同分量的液體看起來較多或較少。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when appearance may affect judgement.","zh":"當外觀可能影響判斷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have the same capacity","meaning":"有相同容量","examples":[{"en":"The containers had the same capacity.","zh":"這些容器有相同容量。"},{"en":"To have the same capacity means to be able to hold the same amount.","zh":"have the same capacity 指能盛載相同分量。"},{"en":"Two water bottles may have the same capacity even if one is tall and the other is short.","zh":"兩個水樽即使一個高、一個矮，也可能有相同容量。"},{"en":"If containers have the same capacity, they can hold equal quantities despite looking different.","zh":"如果容器有相同容量，即使外觀不同，也可以盛載相等分量。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how much things can contain.","zh":"這個短語比較物件能容納多少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the same amount of fluid","meaning":"相同分量的液體","examples":[{"en":"The children saw the same amount of fluid poured into another container.","zh":"兒童看見相同分量的液體被倒入另一個容器。"},{"en":"The same amount of fluid means an equal quantity of liquid.","zh":"the same amount of fluid 指相等數量的液體。"},{"en":"A recipe may require the same amount of fluid in two different bowls.","zh":"食譜可能要求在兩個不同碗中放入相同分量的液體。"},{"en":"The same amount of fluid can look different when it is placed in a tall glass rather than a wide dish.","zh":"相同分量的液體放在高杯而不是闊碟中，可能看起來不同。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to equal liquid quantity.","zh":"這個短語指相等液體數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be poured between","meaning":"在……之間倒來倒去","examples":[{"en":"The fluid could be poured between the containers.","zh":"液體可以在容器之間倒來倒去。"},{"en":"To be poured between containers means to be moved as liquid from one container to another.","zh":"be poured between containers 指液體從一個容器被倒到另一個容器。"},{"en":"A teacher may pour water between two cups to show that the amount has not changed.","zh":"老師可能在兩隻杯之間倒水，以顯示分量沒有改變。"},{"en":"Pouring liquid between containers can change its appearance without changing its quantity.","zh":"在容器之間倒液體可以改變外觀，但不改變數量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the movement of liquid from one place to another.","zh":"這個短語描述液體從一處移到另一處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"contain more than","meaning":"比……裝得更多","examples":[{"en":"Some children believed that one container contained more than the other.","zh":"有些兒童相信一個容器比另一個裝得更多。"},{"en":"To contain more than something means to hold a larger amount than it.","zh":"contain more than something 指盛載比另一物更多的分量。"},{"en":"A large lunch box may contain more than a small snack box.","zh":"大飯盒可能比小零食盒裝得更多。"},{"en":"A tall container may seem to contain more than a wide one, even when the liquid is equal.","zh":"高容器可能看似比闊容器裝得更多，即使液體分量相等。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the amount held inside things.","zh":"這個短語比較物件內部盛載的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"conclude that","meaning":"得出結論認為","examples":[{"en":"Piaget concluded that the children could not perform the logical task.","zh":"Piaget 得出結論認為兒童不能完成該邏輯任務。"},{"en":"To conclude that means to decide something after considering evidence.","zh":"conclude that 指在考慮證據後作出判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher may conclude that students need more practice after checking their mistakes.","zh":"老師檢查錯誤後，可能得出結論認為學生需要更多練習。"},{"en":"Conclusions can be wrong if the evidence is incomplete or misunderstood.","zh":"如果證據不完整或被誤解，結論可能是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase links evidence with a final judgement.","zh":"這個短語把證據與最終判斷連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be incapable of","meaning":"沒有能力……","examples":[{"en":"Piaget thought the children were incapable of performing the task.","zh":"Piaget 認為兒童沒有能力完成該任務。"},{"en":"To be incapable of doing something means to be unable to do it.","zh":"be incapable of doing something 指無法做某事。"},{"en":"A beginner may be incapable of writing a full academic essay without guidance.","zh":"初學者在沒有指導下，可能沒有能力寫完整學術文章。"},{"en":"A person may seem incapable of a task if the instructions are unclear.","zh":"如果指示不清，一個人可能看似沒有能力完成任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inability, but the reason for that inability may need careful checking.","zh":"這個短語描述能力不足，但能力不足的原因可能需要仔細檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"perform the logical task of","meaning":"進行……這項邏輯任務","examples":[{"en":"The children were asked to perform the logical task of comparing equal amounts of liquid.","zh":"兒童被要求進行比較相同分量液體這項邏輯任務。"},{"en":"To perform the logical task of doing something means to carry out a reasoning activity.","zh":"perform the logical task of doing something 指進行一項推理活動。"},{"en":"Students perform the logical task of choosing the best evidence for an essay argument.","zh":"學生為作文論點選擇最佳證據時，就是在進行邏輯任務。"},{"en":"If children misunderstand the words in the question, they may fail the task even if their reasoning is sound.","zh":"如果兒童誤解題目文字，即使推理本身合理，也可能任務失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on mental reasoning required by a task.","zh":"這個短語著重任務所需的心理推理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"logical task","meaning":"邏輯任務","examples":[{"en":"The experiment involved a logical task about liquid quantity.","zh":"這項實驗涉及一項關於液體數量的邏輯任務。"},{"en":"A logical task is an activity that requires reasoning rather than guessing or copying.","zh":"logical task 指需要推理，而不是猜測或抄寫的活動。"},{"en":"Solving a timetable problem is a logical task because students must compare times and routes.","zh":"解答時間表問題是一項邏輯任務，因為學生必須比較時間和路線。"},{"en":"Logical tasks can become harder when wording, context, or instructions are confusing.","zh":"當措辭、背景或指示令人混淆，邏輯任務可能變得更難。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a task based on clear reasoning.","zh":"這個短語指基於清晰推理的任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"despite their different shapes","meaning":"儘管形狀不同","examples":[{"en":"The containers held the same amount of liquid despite their different shapes.","zh":"這些容器儘管形狀不同，仍盛載相同分量的液體。"},{"en":"Despite their different shapes means although their forms were not the same.","zh":"despite their different shapes 指雖然它們的外形不相同。"},{"en":"Two lunch boxes may hold the same amount of food despite their different shapes.","zh":"兩個飯盒儘管形狀不同，也可能盛載相同分量的食物。"},{"en":"Different shapes can mislead people even when the actual quantity is equal.","zh":"即使實際數量相等，不同形狀也可以誤導人。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights contrast between appearance and reality.","zh":"這個短語突出外觀與現實之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"critics of his work","meaning":"對其研究的批評者","examples":[{"en":"Critics of his work have questioned Piaget’s interpretation.","zh":"對其研究的批評者質疑了 Piaget 的詮釋。"},{"en":"Critics of his work are people who examine his research and point out possible problems.","zh":"critics of his work 指檢視他的研究並指出可能問題的人。"},{"en":"Critics of a school policy may ask whether it helps weaker students fairly.","zh":"對學校政策的批評者可能會問它是否公平幫助能力較弱的學生。"},{"en":"Criticism can improve research by revealing hidden assumptions or weak methods.","zh":"批評可以透過揭示隱藏假設或薄弱方法來改善研究。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people who challenge a researcher’s ideas or methods.","zh":"這個短語指挑戰研究者想法或方法的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"question this interpretation","meaning":"質疑這種詮釋","examples":[{"en":"Donaldson questioned this interpretation of the children’s answers.","zh":"Donaldson 質疑這種對兒童答案的詮釋。"},{"en":"To question this interpretation means to doubt whether this explanation is correct.","zh":"question this interpretation 指懷疑這個解釋是否正確。"},{"en":"A teacher may question the interpretation that a quiet student is lazy.","zh":"老師可能質疑安靜學生就是懶惰這種詮釋。"},{"en":"Questioning an interpretation can lead researchers to consider alternative explanations.","zh":"質疑一種詮釋可以令研究人員考慮其他解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when someone challenges the meaning given to evidence.","zh":"這個短語用於有人挑戰對證據所賦予的意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"point out the possibility that","meaning":"指出……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"Critics point out the possibility that the children misunderstood the question.","zh":"批評者指出兒童誤解問題的可能性。"},{"en":"To point out the possibility that means to mention that something may be true.","zh":"point out the possibility that 指提出某事可能是真的。"},{"en":"A parent may point out the possibility that a child failed because the instructions were unclear.","zh":"家長可能指出孩子失敗是因為指示不清的可能性。"},{"en":"Pointing out a possibility does not prove it, but it opens another line of explanation.","zh":"指出一種可能性並不等於證明它，但它開啟另一條解釋方向。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a possible reason that others may have missed.","zh":"這個短語引入其他人可能忽略的可能原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be unwilling to","meaning":"不願意……","examples":[{"en":"The children might have been unwilling to play the experimenter’s game.","zh":"兒童可能不願意按實驗者的規則配合。"},{"en":"To be unwilling to do something means not to want to do it.","zh":"be unwilling to do something 指不想做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be unwilling to answer aloud if classmates often laugh at mistakes.","zh":"如果同學常取笑錯誤，學生可能不願意大聲回答。"},{"en":"If participants are unwilling to cooperate, research results may not show their true ability.","zh":"如果參與者不願意合作，研究結果可能不能顯示其真實能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reluctance rather than inability.","zh":"這個短語描述不情願，而不是能力不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"play the experimenter’s game","meaning":"按實驗者的規則配合","examples":[{"en":"The children may have been unwilling to play the experimenter’s game.","zh":"兒童可能不願意按實驗者的規則配合。"},{"en":"To play the experimenter’s game means to follow the rules, expectations, and social situation created by the researcher.","zh":"play the experimenter’s game 指跟從研究者設下的規則、期望和社交情境。"},{"en":"A child may know the answer but refuse to play the teacher’s game if the task feels strange.","zh":"如果任務感覺奇怪，孩子可能知道答案卻拒絕按老師的規則配合。"},{"en":"In experiments, participants may respond to the situation, not only to the question itself.","zh":"在實驗中，參與者可能是在回應情境，而不只是回應問題本身。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that research tasks are also social interactions.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，研究任務也是社交互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"not quite understand","meaning":"不太明白","examples":[{"en":"The children may not have quite understood the question.","zh":"兒童可能不太明白問題。"},{"en":"To not quite understand means to understand only partly or not clearly enough.","zh":"not quite understand 指只部分理解，或理解得不夠清楚。"},{"en":"A student may not quite understand a grammar rule if she can repeat it but cannot use it.","zh":"如果學生能背出文法規則但不能使用，她可能不太明白該規則。"},{"en":"Partial misunderstanding can lead to wrong answers even when the student is thinking carefully.","zh":"部分誤解可以導致錯誤答案，即使學生正在認真思考。"},{"en":"This phrase describes incomplete understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述不完整的理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the question asked by","meaning":"由……提出的問題","examples":[{"en":"The children may not have understood the question asked by the experimenter.","zh":"兒童可能沒有理解由實驗者提出的問題。"},{"en":"The question asked by someone means the question that person put to another person.","zh":"the question asked by someone 指該人向另一人提出的問題。"},{"en":"The answer depends on the question asked by the teacher, not only on the topic.","zh":"答案取決於由老師提出的問題，而不只是主題。"},{"en":"If the question asked by the tester is unclear, the result may be unreliable.","zh":"如果由測驗者提出的問題不清楚，結果可能不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the source of a question.","zh":"這個短語指出問題的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"criticisms may be valid","meaning":"這些批評可能有道理","examples":[{"en":"These criticisms may be valid.","zh":"這些批評可能有道理。"},{"en":"Criticisms may be valid means the objections or doubts may be reasonable and worth taking seriously.","zh":"criticisms may be valid 指反對意見或疑問可能合理，值得認真對待。"},{"en":"A student’s criticism of unclear homework instructions may be valid if many classmates are also confused.","zh":"如果許多同學也感到混亂，學生對功課指示不清的批評可能有道理。"},{"en":"Valid criticisms can help improve a test, lesson, or research design.","zh":"有道理的批評可以幫助改善測驗、課堂或研究設計。"},{"en":"This phrase accepts that criticism may have real support.","zh":"這個短語承認批評可能有真實根據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"more importantly","meaning":"更重要的是","examples":[{"en":"More importantly, experiments are social situations.","zh":"更重要的是，實驗是社交情境。"},{"en":"More importantly means the next point is even more significant than the previous one.","zh":"more importantly 指下一點比前一點更重要。"},{"en":"The classroom is small; more importantly, it has no proper exit in an emergency.","zh":"課室很小；更重要的是，它在緊急情況下沒有合適出口。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to move readers toward a stronger or deeper point.","zh":"作者使用這個短語，把讀者帶向更強或更深層的重點。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the following idea deserves special attention.","zh":"這個短語表示接下來的想法特別值得注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"social situations","meaning":"社交情境","examples":[{"en":"Experiments are social situations in which people interact.","zh":"實驗是人們互動的社交情境。"},{"en":"Social situations are settings where people communicate, respond, and behave around one another.","zh":"social situations 指人們彼此溝通、回應和表現的環境。"},{"en":"A classroom discussion is a social situation because students react to the teacher and classmates.","zh":"課堂討論是社交情境，因為學生會回應老師和同學。"},{"en":"In social situations, people may act differently depending on trust, pressure, or misunderstanding.","zh":"在社交情境中，人們可能因信任、壓力或誤解而有不同表現。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that behaviour happens in context, not in isolation.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，行為是在情境中發生，而不是孤立出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"interpersonal interactions","meaning":"人際互動","examples":[{"en":"Interpersonal interactions take place during experiments.","zh":"人際互動在實驗期間發生。"},{"en":"Interpersonal interactions are exchanges between people, such as speaking, listening, reacting, or cooperating.","zh":"interpersonal interactions 指人與人之間的交流，例如說話、聆聽、反應或合作。"},{"en":"A teacher and student have interpersonal interactions when they discuss homework feedback.","zh":"老師和學生討論功課回饋時，就有人際互動。"},{"en":"These interactions can affect how comfortable a child feels during a test.","zh":"這些互動可以影響孩子在測驗中感到多自在。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on person-to-person communication.","zh":"這個短語著重人與人之間的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take place","meaning":"發生；進行","examples":[{"en":"Interpersonal interactions take place in experiments.","zh":"人際互動在實驗中發生。"},{"en":"To take place means to happen or occur.","zh":"take place 指發生或進行。"},{"en":"The school concert will take place in the hall after lunch.","zh":"學校音樂會會在午飯後於禮堂舉行。"},{"en":"When an event takes place in a formal setting, people may behave more carefully.","zh":"當事件在正式環境中進行，人們可能表現得更小心。"},{"en":"This phrase is a neutral way to say that something happens.","zh":"這個短語是表示某事發生的中性說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the implication is that","meaning":"這意味著","examples":[{"en":"The implication is that the experiment measured more than logical thought.","zh":"這意味著實驗衡量的不只是邏輯思考。"},{"en":"The implication is that means the hidden or indirect meaning is that something is true.","zh":"the implication is that 指隱含或間接意思是某事為真。"},{"en":"If a student keeps missing homework, the implication is that support may be needed, not only punishment.","zh":"如果學生不斷欠交功課，這意味著可能需要支援，而不只是懲罰。"},{"en":"Implications matter because they show what a result suggests beyond the obvious answer.","zh":"含意很重要，因為它顯示結果在明顯答案以外暗示了甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what follows from an idea or finding.","zh":"這個短語引入某想法或發現所帶出的意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"attempts to replicate","meaning":"複製……的嘗試","examples":[{"en":"Attempts to replicate Piaget’s investigation may measure several different factors.","zh":"複製 Piaget 研究的嘗試可能衡量幾個不同因素。"},{"en":"Attempts to replicate a study are efforts to repeat it to see whether the same results appear.","zh":"attempts to replicate a study 指重複某研究，以看看是否出現相同結果的努力。"},{"en":"Scientists may make attempts to replicate a famous experiment before trusting its conclusion.","zh":"科學家在相信某著名實驗結論前，可能會嘗試複製該實驗。"},{"en":"Replication can reveal whether a finding is strong or depended on one unusual situation.","zh":"複製研究可以揭示某發現是否穩健，還是取決於某個特殊情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeating research for confirmation.","zh":"這個短語描述為確認而重複研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"measure not only…but also…","meaning":"不但衡量……，也衡量……","examples":[{"en":"The experiment measured not only logical thought but also children’s understanding of instructions.","zh":"這項實驗不但衡量邏輯思考，也衡量兒童對指示的理解。"},{"en":"Measure not only…but also… means to assess two things, not just one.","zh":"measure not only…but also… 指評估兩件事，而不只是一件事。"},{"en":"A speaking test may measure not only pronunciation but also confidence and organisation.","zh":"口語測驗可能不但衡量發音，也衡量自信和組織。"},{"en":"If a test measures several abilities at once, the result may be harder to interpret.","zh":"如果測驗同時衡量幾種能力，結果可能更難詮釋。"},{"en":"This structure helps show that a situation is more complex than it first appears.","zh":"這個結構幫助顯示情況比起初看來更複雜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"capacity for logical thought","meaning":"邏輯思考能力","examples":[{"en":"The test measured children’s capacity for logical thought.","zh":"測驗衡量兒童的邏輯思考能力。"},{"en":"Capacity for logical thought is the ability to reason clearly and connect ideas in a sensible way.","zh":"capacity for logical thought 指清楚推理並合理連接想法的能力。"},{"en":"A maths puzzle can show a student’s capacity for logical thought.","zh":"數學謎題可以顯示學生的邏輯思考能力。"},{"en":"If instructions are confusing, a child’s capacity for logical thought may be underestimated.","zh":"如果指示令人混亂，孩子的邏輯思考能力可能被低估。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to reasoning ability.","zh":"這個短語指推理能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"understand the instructions","meaning":"理解指示","examples":[{"en":"The results depended partly on how well the children understood the instructions.","zh":"結果部分取決於兒童有多理解指示。"},{"en":"To understand the instructions means to know exactly what one is being asked to do.","zh":"understand the instructions 指清楚知道自己被要求做甚麼。"},{"en":"Students should understand the instructions before they start filling in an exam answer sheet.","zh":"學生在開始填寫考試答題紙前，應先理解指示。"},{"en":"If learners misunderstand instructions, wrong answers may not reflect weak knowledge.","zh":"如果學習者誤解指示，錯誤答案未必反映知識薄弱。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on comprehension of the task itself.","zh":"這個短語著重對任務本身的理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be willing to comply","meaning":"願意配合","examples":[{"en":"The results depended on how willing the children were to comply.","zh":"結果取決於兒童有多願意配合。"},{"en":"To be willing to comply means to be ready to follow rules, requests, or instructions.","zh":"be willing to comply 指準備好跟從規則、要求或指示。"},{"en":"A student may be willing to comply when the teacher explains why a rule matters.","zh":"當老師解釋規則為何重要，學生可能較願意配合。"},{"en":"If participants do not comply, research results may reflect resistance rather than ability.","zh":"如果參與者不配合，研究結果可能反映抗拒，而不是能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes readiness to cooperate.","zh":"這個短語描述合作意願。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"communicate clearly","meaning":"清楚溝通","examples":[{"en":"The results depended on how clearly the experimenters communicated.","zh":"結果取決於實驗者溝通得多清楚。"},{"en":"To communicate clearly means to express ideas or instructions in a way others can understand.","zh":"communicate clearly 指以他人能理解的方式表達想法或指示。"},{"en":"A nurse must communicate clearly when explaining how to take medicine.","zh":"護士解釋如何服藥時，必須清楚溝通。"},{"en":"Clear communication prevents mistakes, confusion, and unfair judgement.","zh":"清楚溝通可防止錯誤、混亂和不公平判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes effective explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述有效解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"motivate the children","meaning":"激勵孩子；令孩子有動機","examples":[{"en":"The experimenters had to motivate the children effectively.","zh":"實驗者必須有效地激勵孩子。"},{"en":"To motivate the children means to make them interested, willing, and ready to take part.","zh":"motivate the children 指令孩子感到有興趣、願意並準備參與。"},{"en":"A teacher may motivate the children by turning a grammar activity into a game.","zh":"老師可能透過把文法活動變成遊戲來激勵孩子。"},{"en":"If children are not motivated, they may give careless answers even when they know more.","zh":"如果孩子沒有動機，即使他們知道更多，也可能給出草率答案。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on encouraging participation.","zh":"這個短語著重鼓勵參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the same kinds of criticisms","meaning":"同類批評","examples":[{"en":"The same kinds of criticisms have been directed at educational tests.","zh":"同類批評也針對教育測驗提出。"},{"en":"The same kinds of criticisms means similar objections or doubts.","zh":"the same kinds of criticisms 指相似的反對意見或疑問。"},{"en":"The same kinds of criticisms may be made about online exams if students misunderstand the format.","zh":"如果學生誤解網上考試格式，同類批評也可能針對網上考試提出。"},{"en":"When similar problems appear in different tests, researchers should examine the testing method itself.","zh":"當相似問題出現在不同測驗中，研究人員應檢視測驗方法本身。"},{"en":"This phrase links one set of criticisms to another similar case.","zh":"這個短語把一組批評與另一個相似個案連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be directed at","meaning":"針對……","examples":[{"en":"Similar criticisms have been directed at psychological tests.","zh":"相似批評也針對心理測驗提出。"},{"en":"To be directed at something means to be aimed at or focused on it.","zh":"be directed at something 指以某事為目標或焦點。"},{"en":"Complaints were directed at the school’s new lunch system, not the teachers.","zh":"投訴針對學校的新午膳制度，而不是老師。"},{"en":"When criticism is directed at a method, the method’s design may need review.","zh":"當批評針對某方法，該方法的設計可能需要檢討。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the target of criticism, action, or attention.","zh":"這個短語顯示批評、行動或注意力的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"psychological and educational tests","meaning":"心理測驗和教育測驗","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses psychological and educational tests.","zh":"文章討論心理測驗和教育測驗。"},{"en":"Psychological and educational tests are assessments used to measure thinking, learning, language, ability, or behaviour.","zh":"psychological and educational tests 指用來衡量思考、學習、語言、能力或行為的評估。"},{"en":"A school may use educational tests to check reading level and psychological tests to understand attention problems.","zh":"學校可能使用教育測驗檢查閱讀程度，並使用心理測驗了解專注問題。"},{"en":"These tests can help, but unclear questions may produce misleading results.","zh":"這些測驗可以有幫助，但問題不清可能產生誤導結果。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal assessments of mind and learning.","zh":"這個短語指對心智和學習的正式評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"For instance, Mehan argues that children may interpret questions differently.","zh":"例如，Mehan 認為兒童可能以不同方式理解問題。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance 指例如。"},{"en":"Some school rules are hard to follow; for instance, students may not know where to put phones during exams.","zh":"有些校規很難跟從；例如，學生可能不知道考試期間應把手機放在哪裡。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to make a general point clearer with one case.","zh":"作者使用這個短語，以一個個案令一般重點更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an example.","zh":"這個短語引入例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"interpret the test questions differently","meaning":"以不同方式理解測驗問題","examples":[{"en":"Participants might interpret the test questions differently from the experimenter.","zh":"參與者可能以不同於實驗者的方式理解測驗問題。"},{"en":"To interpret the test questions differently means to understand their meaning in another way.","zh":"interpret the test questions differently 指以另一種方式理解題目的意思。"},{"en":"A child may interpret a picture question differently if the image reminds her of a familiar cartoon.","zh":"如果圖片令孩子想起熟悉的卡通，她可能會以不同方式理解圖片題。"},{"en":"Different interpretations can lead to different answers even when students are thinking logically.","zh":"不同詮釋可以導致不同答案，即使學生正在有邏輯地思考。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a wrong answer may not show weak ability.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何錯誤答案未必顯示能力薄弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the way someone intended","meaning":"按某人原意的方式","examples":[{"en":"The children may not answer in the way the experimenter intended.","zh":"兒童可能沒有按實驗者原意的方式作答。"},{"en":"The way someone intended means the manner or meaning that person expected.","zh":"the way someone intended 指某人所預期的方式或意思。"},{"en":"A student may not use a worksheet in the way the teacher intended if the instructions are vague.","zh":"如果指示含糊，學生可能沒有按老師原意的方式使用工作紙。"},{"en":"When people do not respond in the intended way, results can be misread.","zh":"當人們沒有以原定方式回應，結果可能被誤讀。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the gap between intention and actual response.","zh":"這個短語突出意圖與實際回應之間的差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"language development test","meaning":"語言發展測驗","examples":[{"en":"Mehan discusses a language development test.","zh":"Mehan 討論一項語言發展測驗。"},{"en":"A language development test is an assessment of how well a child understands or uses language.","zh":"language development test 指評估兒童理解或使用語言能力的測驗。"},{"en":"A school may use a language development test to see whether a child needs speech support.","zh":"學校可能使用語言發展測驗，看看孩子是否需要言語支援。"},{"en":"Poorly chosen pictures or words can make a language test less fair.","zh":"圖片或詞語選擇不佳，可以令語言測驗不夠公平。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a test of language growth and ability.","zh":"這個短語指測試語言成長和能力的測驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a medieval fortress","meaning":"中世紀堡壘","examples":[{"en":"The picture showed a medieval fortress.","zh":"圖片顯示一座中世紀堡壘。"},{"en":"A medieval fortress is a strong defensive building from the Middle Ages.","zh":"medieval fortress 指中世紀時期的堅固防禦建築。"},{"en":"A history textbook may show a medieval fortress with thick walls and towers.","zh":"歷史教科書可能展示有厚牆和塔樓的中世紀堡壘。"},{"en":"Children unfamiliar with castles may name the picture differently from what testers expect.","zh":"不熟悉城堡的孩子，可能以不同於測驗者預期的方式命名圖片。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an old fortified building.","zh":"這個短語指古老的防禦建築。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"complete with","meaning":"配備有；包括","examples":[{"en":"The fortress was complete with a moat, drawbridge and parapets.","zh":"這座堡壘配備有護城河、吊橋和城牆雉堞。"},{"en":"Complete with means including all the expected or important features.","zh":"complete with 指包括所有預期或重要特徵。"},{"en":"The new classroom was complete with a projector, whiteboard, and reading corner.","zh":"新課室配備有投影機、白板和閱讀角。"},{"en":"This phrase often gives a vivid list of details that make something feel full or realistic.","zh":"這個短語常給出鮮明細節清單，使事物感覺完整或真實。"},{"en":"It is used to show that something has the usual parts people expect.","zh":"它用來顯示某物具有通常預期的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a moat","meaning":"護城河","examples":[{"en":"The medieval fortress was complete with a moat.","zh":"這座中世紀堡壘配備有護城河。"},{"en":"A moat is a deep ditch, often filled with water, built around a castle for protection.","zh":"moat 指圍繞城堡而建、通常有水的深溝，用於防禦。"},{"en":"Children may see a moat in storybooks about castles and knights.","zh":"兒童可能在關於城堡和騎士的故事書中看見護城河。"},{"en":"A moat made it harder for enemies to reach the castle walls.","zh":"護城河令敵人更難接近城牆。"},{"en":"This word refers to a defensive feature around a fortress.","zh":"這個詞指堡壘周圍的防禦設施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a drawbridge","meaning":"吊橋","examples":[{"en":"The picture of the fortress included a drawbridge.","zh":"堡壘的圖片包括一座吊橋。"},{"en":"A drawbridge is a bridge that can be raised or lowered, especially at a castle entrance.","zh":"drawbridge 指可以升起或放下的橋，尤其位於城堡入口。"},{"en":"A castle may lift its drawbridge to stop enemies from entering.","zh":"城堡可能升起吊橋，以阻止敵人進入。"},{"en":"In a picture, a drawbridge helps children recognise that the building is a castle.","zh":"在圖片中，吊橋幫助兒童認出該建築是城堡。"},{"en":"This word refers to a movable bridge used for access and defence.","zh":"這個詞指用於出入和防禦的可移動橋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"parapets","meaning":"城牆雉堞；矮牆","examples":[{"en":"The picture showed a fortress with parapets.","zh":"圖片顯示一座有城牆雉堞的堡壘。"},{"en":"Parapets are low protective walls along the edge or top of a building, bridge, or castle.","zh":"parapets 指沿建築、橋或城堡邊緣或頂部而建的低防護牆。"},{"en":"Soldiers could stand behind parapets on a castle wall for protection.","zh":"士兵可以站在城牆雉堞後方獲得保護。"},{"en":"Parapets help people recognise old defensive architecture.","zh":"城牆雉堞幫助人認出古老防禦建築。"},{"en":"This word refers to raised protective edges on buildings or walls.","zh":"這個詞指建築或牆上的凸起防護邊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"alongside","meaning":"在……旁邊","examples":[{"en":"The picture was shown alongside three initial consonants.","zh":"圖片被放在三個開首輔音旁邊。"},{"en":"Alongside means next to or together with something.","zh":"alongside 指在某物旁邊或與某物一起。"},{"en":"A vocabulary list may show English words alongside Chinese meanings.","zh":"詞彙表可能把英文詞語放在中文意思旁邊。"},{"en":"Placing a picture alongside letters helps students connect visual clues with language.","zh":"把圖片放在字母旁邊，幫助學生把視覺線索與語言連接起來。"},{"en":"This word describes side-by-side presentation.","zh":"這個詞描述並排呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"initial consonants","meaning":"開首輔音","examples":[{"en":"The children had to choose one of the initial consonants.","zh":"兒童必須選擇其中一個開首輔音。"},{"en":"Initial consonants are consonant sounds or letters at the beginning of words.","zh":"initial consonants 指詞語開頭的輔音音素或字母。"},{"en":"In the word “cat,” the initial consonant is C.","zh":"在 “cat” 這個字中，開首輔音是 C。"},{"en":"If children name the picture differently, they may choose a different initial consonant.","zh":"如果兒童以不同方式命名圖片，他們可能選擇不同開首輔音。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in early reading and phonics tasks.","zh":"這個短語常用於早期閱讀和拼音任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be required to","meaning":"被要求……","examples":[{"en":"The children were required to circle the correct initial consonant.","zh":"兒童被要求圈出正確的開首輔音。"},{"en":"To be required to do something means to have to do it because of a rule or instruction.","zh":"be required to do something 指因規則或指示而必須做某事。"},{"en":"Students are required to bring their identity card to the exam.","zh":"學生被要求帶身份證參加考試。"},{"en":"When people are required to follow unclear instructions, mistakes become more likely.","zh":"當人們被要求跟從不清楚的指示，錯誤會更容易出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes obligation.","zh":"這個短語描述義務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"circle the correct initial consonant","meaning":"圈出正確的開首輔音","examples":[{"en":"The children were asked to circle the correct initial consonant for “castle”.","zh":"兒童被要求圈出 “castle” 的正確開首輔音。"},{"en":"To circle the correct initial consonant means to draw a circle around the starting sound or letter of a word.","zh":"circle the correct initial consonant 指在一個詞的起首音或字母外畫圈。"},{"en":"In a phonics exercise, a child may circle B for “ball.”","zh":"在拼音練習中，孩子可能為 “ball” 圈出 B。"},{"en":"If the child thinks the picture is Disneyland, she may circle D instead of C.","zh":"如果孩子以為圖片是 Disneyland，她可能圈出 D 而不是 C。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a basic reading-test action.","zh":"這個短語描述基本閱讀測驗動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"many children choose","meaning":"很多孩子選擇","examples":[{"en":"Many children chose D instead of C.","zh":"很多孩子選擇了 D 而不是 C。"},{"en":"Many children choose means a large number of children select a particular answer or option.","zh":"many children choose 指大量孩子選取某個答案或選項。"},{"en":"Many children choose pictures before words when they are learning a new language.","zh":"很多孩子學習新語言時，會先選擇圖片而不是文字。"},{"en":"When many children choose the same wrong answer, the question itself may be confusing.","zh":"當很多孩子選擇同一個錯誤答案，題目本身可能令人混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common response among children.","zh":"這個短語描述孩子之間常見的回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"respond with","meaning":"以……作答","examples":[{"en":"The children responded with the word “Disneyland”.","zh":"兒童以 “Disneyland” 這個詞作答。"},{"en":"To respond with something means to answer by saying, writing, or choosing it.","zh":"respond with something 指以說出、寫下或選擇某事作答。"},{"en":"A student may respond with “I don’t know” when a question feels too difficult.","zh":"當問題感覺太難，學生可能以「我不知道」作答。"},{"en":"The way people respond can show how they understood the question.","zh":"人們作答的方式可以顯示他們如何理解問題。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a question or prompt with the answer given.","zh":"這個短語把問題或提示與所給答案連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"adopt the line of reasoning","meaning":"採用……的推理思路","examples":[{"en":"The children adopted the line of reasoning expected by the experimenter.","zh":"兒童採用了實驗者所預期的推理思路。"},{"en":"To adopt the line of reasoning means to follow a particular way of thinking.","zh":"adopt the line of reasoning 指跟從某一種思考方式。"},{"en":"A student may adopt the line of reasoning that lower prices increase demand.","zh":"學生可能採用價格較低會增加需求這一推理思路。"},{"en":"If people adopt a different line of reasoning, they may reach a different answer.","zh":"如果人們採用不同推理思路，他們可能得出不同答案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using a certain logic to reach a conclusion.","zh":"這個短語描述使用某種邏輯來得出結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the line of reasoning","meaning":"推理思路","examples":[{"en":"The children followed a reasonable line of reasoning.","zh":"兒童跟從了一條合理的推理思路。"},{"en":"The line of reasoning is the sequence of ideas that leads to an answer or conclusion.","zh":"line of reasoning 指導向答案或結論的一連串想法。"},{"en":"In an essay, the line of reasoning should connect evidence to the main argument.","zh":"在作文中，推理思路應把證據連接到主要論點。"},{"en":"A wrong final answer can still come from a sensible line of reasoning.","zh":"錯誤的最終答案仍可能來自合理的推理思路。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the thinking path behind a conclusion.","zh":"這個短語著重結論背後的思考路線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"expected by","meaning":"由……所預期","examples":[{"en":"The children adopted the reasoning expected by the experimenter.","zh":"兒童採用了由實驗者所預期的推理。"},{"en":"Expected by someone means believed or predicted by that person.","zh":"expected by someone 指由某人相信會出現或預測會出現。"},{"en":"A teacher may not get the answer expected by her if students interpret the picture differently.","zh":"如果學生以不同方式理解圖片，老師可能得不到她所預期的答案。"},{"en":"Expectations affect how people judge whether a response is correct or strange.","zh":"期望會影響人們如何判斷回應是正確還是奇怪。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies whose expectation is being discussed.","zh":"這個短語指出正在討論的是誰的期望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"arrive at the wrong answer","meaning":"得出錯誤答案","examples":[{"en":"The children arrived at the wrong answer.","zh":"兒童得出了錯誤答案。"},{"en":"To arrive at the wrong answer means to reach an incorrect conclusion after thinking or choosing.","zh":"arrive at the wrong answer 指經過思考或選擇後得到不正確結論。"},{"en":"A student may arrive at the wrong answer if she uses the right formula with the wrong numbers.","zh":"如果學生用正確公式但數字錯誤，可能得出錯誤答案。"},{"en":"A wrong answer may result from misunderstanding, not from lack of intelligence.","zh":"錯誤答案可能源於誤解，而不是智力不足。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the result of reasoning.","zh":"這個短語著重推理的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"score sheet","meaning":"評分表","examples":[{"en":"The score sheet does not prove that a child lacks reasoning ability.","zh":"評分表不能證明孩子缺乏推理能力。"},{"en":"A score sheet is a form or record showing points, marks, or results.","zh":"score sheet 指顯示分數、評分或結果的表格或記錄。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a score sheet to record speaking marks for fluency and pronunciation.","zh":"老師可能使用評分表記錄口語流暢度和發音分數。"},{"en":"A score sheet records outcomes, but it may not explain why those outcomes happened.","zh":"評分表記錄結果，但未必解釋這些結果為何出現。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the written record of scores.","zh":"這個短語指分數的書面記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prove that","meaning":"證明","examples":[{"en":"The score sheet does not prove that the child cannot reason.","zh":"評分表不能證明孩子不能推理。"},{"en":"To prove that means to show clearly that something is true using evidence.","zh":"prove that 指用證據清楚顯示某事為真。"},{"en":"One low test mark does not prove that a student is lazy.","zh":"一次低測驗分數不能證明學生懶惰。"},{"en":"Strong proof requires evidence that rules out other explanations.","zh":"有力證明需要排除其他解釋的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when evidence supports a conclusion firmly.","zh":"這個短語用於證據有力支持結論時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lack reasoning ability","meaning":"缺乏推理能力","examples":[{"en":"A wrong answer does not necessarily mean that a child lacks reasoning ability.","zh":"錯誤答案不一定代表孩子缺乏推理能力。"},{"en":"To lack reasoning ability means to be unable to think logically or connect ideas properly.","zh":"lack reasoning ability 指不能有邏輯地思考或恰當連接想法。"},{"en":"A student may look as if he lacks reasoning ability if he does not understand the question language.","zh":"如果學生不理解題目語言，他可能看似缺乏推理能力。"},{"en":"Before judging ability, teachers should check whether instructions were clear.","zh":"在判斷能力前，老師應檢查指示是否清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible weakness in logical thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述邏輯思考上的可能弱點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"record only that","meaning":"只記錄到","examples":[{"en":"The score sheet records only that the child gave a different answer.","zh":"評分表只記錄到孩子給出了不同答案。"},{"en":"To record only that means to write down just one fact without explaining its cause.","zh":"record only that 指只寫下一個事實，而不解釋其原因。"},{"en":"An attendance sheet records only that a student was absent; it does not explain why.","zh":"出席表只記錄到學生缺席；它不解釋原因。"},{"en":"Limited records can make people draw conclusions too quickly.","zh":"有限記錄可以令人太快下結論。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that written data may not tell the full story.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，書面數據未必說出完整故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"give a different answer","meaning":"給出不同答案","examples":[{"en":"The child gave a different answer from the one the tester expected.","zh":"孩子給出的答案不同於測驗者所預期的答案。"},{"en":"To give a different answer means to respond with something other than the expected or standard answer.","zh":"give a different answer 指以不同於預期或標準答案的內容作答。"},{"en":"A student may give a different answer if she uses another reasonable method.","zh":"如果學生使用另一種合理方法，她可能給出不同答案。"},{"en":"Different answers can reveal misunderstanding, creativity, or a different perspective.","zh":"不同答案可以揭示誤解、創意或不同觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a response that does not match expectation.","zh":"這個短語描述不符合期望的回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"The score sheet records a different answer rather than a lack of reasoning.","zh":"評分表記錄的是不同答案，而不是缺乏推理能力。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of; it clearly contrasts two ideas.","zh":"rather than 指而不是，清楚對比兩個想法。"},{"en":"A teacher should correct the misunderstanding rather than blame the student immediately.","zh":"老師應糾正誤解，而不是立即責怪學生。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate the real issue from a wrong explanation.","zh":"這個短語幫助把真正問題與錯誤解釋分開。"},{"en":"It is useful when one thing is true and another assumed thing is not.","zh":"當一件事為真，而另一件被假設的事並非真時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the tester expected","meaning":"測驗者所預期","examples":[{"en":"The answer was not the one the tester expected.","zh":"該答案並不是測驗者所預期的答案。"},{"en":"The tester expected means the person giving the test predicted or wanted a particular response.","zh":"the tester expected 指出題或施測者預測或希望得到某特定回應。"},{"en":"A student may write an answer different from what the tester expected if the picture has several possible names.","zh":"如果圖片有幾個可能名稱，學生可能寫出不同於測驗者所預期的答案。"},{"en":"Testers’ expectations can shape how answers are judged.","zh":"測驗者的期望可以塑造答案如何被判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the expected answer from the examiner’s side.","zh":"這個短語指出考官一方所預期的答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"raise questions about","meaning":"引發關於……的疑問","examples":[{"en":"This raises questions about the validity of the measures.","zh":"這引發關於衡量方法有效性的疑問。"},{"en":"To raise questions about something means to create doubts or concerns about it.","zh":"raise questions about something 指對某事產生懷疑或關注。"},{"en":"A sudden drop in exam scores may raise questions about whether the paper was too difficult.","zh":"考試分數突然下降，可能引發關於試卷是否太難的疑問。"},{"en":"When questions are raised, people may need to review evidence or methods.","zh":"當疑問被提出，人們可能需要檢討證據或方法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces doubt or critical inquiry.","zh":"這個短語引入懷疑或批判性探究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the validity of","meaning":"……的有效性","examples":[{"en":"The example raises questions about the validity of the measures.","zh":"這個例子引發關於衡量方法有效性的疑問。"},{"en":"The validity of something is how well it measures, proves, or represents what it claims to.","zh":"validity of something 指某物能否有效衡量、證明或代表它聲稱要衡量的東西。"},{"en":"A reading test has weak validity if it mainly tests memory rather than reading ability.","zh":"如果閱讀測驗主要測試記憶而不是閱讀能力，它的有效性就弱。"},{"en":"If validity is low, the results may not support the conclusion.","zh":"如果有效性低，結果可能不能支持結論。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when judging research and assessment quality.","zh":"這個短語在判斷研究和評估質素時很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"measures","meaning":"衡量指標；測量方法","examples":[{"en":"Quantitative research findings are often based on measures.","zh":"定量研究結果常基於衡量指標。"},{"en":"Measures are tools, scores, questions, or methods used to assess something.","zh":"measures 指用來評估某事的工具、分數、問題或方法。"},{"en":"A school may use attendance, test scores, and homework completion as measures of student progress.","zh":"學校可能使用出席率、測驗分數和功課完成情況作為學生進步的衡量指標。"},{"en":"Measures must match the thing being studied, or results may be misleading.","zh":"衡量方法必須配合被研究的事物，否則結果可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"This word refers to ways of turning ideas into assessable data.","zh":"這個詞指把想法轉化成可評估數據的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"quantitative research findings","meaning":"定量研究結果","examples":[{"en":"The validity of quantitative research findings may be questioned.","zh":"定量研究結果的有效性可能受到質疑。"},{"en":"Quantitative research findings are conclusions drawn from numerical data and statistical analysis.","zh":"quantitative research findings 指從數字數據和統計分析得出的結論。"},{"en":"A study may report quantitative research findings showing that attendance improved after a new policy.","zh":"一項研究可能報告定量研究結果，顯示新政策後出席率改善。"},{"en":"These findings can look precise, but they depend on the quality of the measures used.","zh":"這些結果可以看似精確，但取決於所用衡量方法的質素。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to results from number-based research.","zh":"這個短語指基於數字研究的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"基於……","examples":[{"en":"Research findings are usually based on particular measures.","zh":"研究結果通常基於特定衡量指標。"},{"en":"To be based on something means to use it as the foundation for an idea, decision, or result.","zh":"be based on something 指以某事作為想法、決定或結果的基礎。"},{"en":"A teacher’s feedback should be based on the student’s actual writing, not personal preference.","zh":"老師的回饋應基於學生實際寫作，而不是個人偏好。"},{"en":"If research is based on weak measures, its conclusions may be weak too.","zh":"如果研究基於薄弱衡量方法，其結論也可能薄弱。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the foundation behind a claim.","zh":"這個短語顯示聲稱背後的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"some scholars such as","meaning":"某些學者，例如……","examples":[{"en":"Some scholars such as Donaldson see these as technical issues.","zh":"某些學者，例如 Donaldson，把這些視為技術性問題。"},{"en":"Some scholars such as means certain academic experts, including the person named.","zh":"some scholars such as 指某些學術專家，包括被點名的人。"},{"en":"Some scholars such as language psychologists study how children interpret classroom questions.","zh":"某些學者，例如語言心理學家，研究兒童如何理解課堂問題。"},{"en":"Naming scholars helps readers see whose view is being discussed.","zh":"指名學者幫助讀者看出正在討論誰的觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples of academic voices.","zh":"這個短語引入學術意見的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"technical issues","meaning":"技術性問題","examples":[{"en":"Donaldson considers these problems to be technical issues.","zh":"Donaldson 認為這些問題是技術性問題。"},{"en":"Technical issues are problems with method, design, wording, or procedure rather than the whole idea.","zh":"technical issues 指方法、設計、措辭或程序上的問題，而不是整個想法的問題。"},{"en":"A survey may have technical issues if the questions are unclear or the answer boxes are confusing.","zh":"如果問題不清或答案方格令人混淆，問卷可能有技術性問題。"},{"en":"Technical issues can sometimes be fixed without abandoning the entire research approach.","zh":"技術性問題有時可以修正，而不必放棄整個研究取向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical research problems that may be repairable.","zh":"這個短語描述可能可修補的實際研究問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be resolved through","meaning":"透過……解決","examples":[{"en":"Technical issues can be resolved through more rigorous experimentation.","zh":"技術性問題可以透過更嚴謹的實驗解決。"},{"en":"To be resolved through something means to be solved by using that method.","zh":"be resolved through something 指透過某方法解決。"},{"en":"A misunderstanding may be resolved through a calm conversation.","zh":"誤會可以透過冷靜對話解決。"},{"en":"Research flaws can be resolved through clearer design, better instructions, and repeated testing.","zh":"研究缺陷可以透過更清楚設計、更好指示和重複測試解決。"},{"en":"This phrase links a problem with the method used to solve it.","zh":"這個短語把問題與解決它的方法連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rigorous experimentation","meaning":"嚴謹的實驗","examples":[{"en":"Donaldson thought the flaw could be addressed through rigorous experimentation.","zh":"Donaldson 認為該缺陷可以透過嚴謹的實驗處理。"},{"en":"Rigorous experimentation means careful, controlled, and well-designed testing.","zh":"rigorous experimentation 指仔細、受控制且設計良好的測試。"},{"en":"A science teacher demonstrates rigorous experimentation by controlling variables and recording results accurately.","zh":"科學老師透過控制變項和準確記錄結果來示範嚴謹的實驗。"},{"en":"Rigorous experimentation reduces the chance that results come from confusion or chance.","zh":"嚴謹的實驗減少結果來自混亂或偶然的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes high-quality experimental method.","zh":"這個短語描述高質素實驗方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"In contrast, Mehan sees the problem as more serious.","zh":"相比之下，Mehan 認為問題更嚴重。"},{"en":"In contrast means by comparison, showing a clear difference from the previous idea.","zh":"in contrast 指相比之下，顯示與前一個想法有清楚差異。"},{"en":"One student likes group work; in contrast, another prefers studying alone.","zh":"一名學生喜歡小組活動；相比之下，另一名學生較喜歡獨自學習。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to compare two different views or situations.","zh":"作者使用這個短語來比較兩種不同觀點或情況。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a shift to an opposing or different point.","zh":"這個短語表示轉向相反或不同的重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"reckon that","meaning":"認為","examples":[{"en":"Mehan reckons that the problems may affect all research of this type.","zh":"Mehan 認為這些問題可能影響所有這類研究。"},{"en":"To reckon that means to think or believe that something is true.","zh":"reckon that 指認為或相信某事為真。"},{"en":"A teacher may reckon that students need more examples before they understand the grammar point.","zh":"老師可能認為學生需要更多例子才理解該文法點。"},{"en":"This phrase is less formal than “argue that” but still shows a view or judgement.","zh":"這個短語沒有 “argue that” 那麼正式，但仍顯示觀點或判斷。"},{"en":"It introduces someone’s opinion or conclusion.","zh":"它引入某人的意見或結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not merely with","meaning":"不僅僅在於……","examples":[{"en":"The problems are not merely with particular experiments.","zh":"問題不僅僅在於個別實驗。"},{"en":"Not merely with means not only about or limited to one thing.","zh":"not merely with 指不只是關於某事，或不只限於某事。"},{"en":"The issue is not merely with one noisy class; it may involve the whole timetable.","zh":"問題不僅僅在於某一班嘈吵；它可能涉及整個時間表。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that a problem is wider than it first appears.","zh":"這個短語暗示問題比起初看來更廣泛。"},{"en":"It helps move from a narrow explanation to a broader one.","zh":"它幫助由狹窄解釋轉向更廣泛解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"particular experiments or tests","meaning":"個別實驗或測驗","examples":[{"en":"The problem may not be limited to particular experiments or tests.","zh":"問題可能不只限於個別實驗或測驗。"},{"en":"Particular experiments or tests are specific studies or assessments, not the whole research tradition.","zh":"particular experiments or tests 指特定研究或評估，而不是整個研究傳統。"},{"en":"A mistake in one quiz is about a particular test, but repeated mistakes may reveal a system problem.","zh":"一次小測錯誤只是關於個別測驗，但反覆錯誤可能揭示制度問題。"},{"en":"If flaws appear across many tests, the issue may be deeper than one design error.","zh":"如果缺陷出現在許多測驗中，問題可能比一個設計錯誤更深。"},{"en":"This phrase points to individual research examples.","zh":"這個短語指個別研究例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"legitimately jeopardise","meaning":"有理由危及","examples":[{"en":"The problems might legitimately jeopardise the validity of this research.","zh":"這些問題可能有理由危及這項研究的有效性。"},{"en":"To legitimately jeopardise something means to give a real and reasonable reason to put it at risk.","zh":"legitimately jeopardise something 指有真實而合理原因令某事受到威脅。"},{"en":"Unclear exam instructions can legitimately jeopardise the fairness of the results.","zh":"考試指示不清可以有理由危及結果的公平性。"},{"en":"When a flaw is serious, criticism is not just complaining; it may be justified.","zh":"當缺陷嚴重時，批評不只是抱怨；它可能是有根據的。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the danger to something is reasonable, not exaggerated.","zh":"這個短語顯示對某事的威脅合理，而不是誇大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"jeopardise the validity of","meaning":"危及……的有效性","examples":[{"en":"These problems might jeopardise the validity of quantitative research.","zh":"這些問題可能危及定量研究的有效性。"},{"en":"To jeopardise the validity of something means to put its truth, accuracy, or reliability at risk.","zh":"jeopardise the validity of something 指令某事的真實性、準確性或可靠性受到威脅。"},{"en":"A badly written questionnaire can jeopardise the validity of a school survey.","zh":"寫得差劣的問卷可以危及學校調查的有效性。"},{"en":"If validity is jeopardised, people may not trust the conclusions.","zh":"如果有效性受到危及，人們可能不信任結論。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a method may no longer measure what it claims to measure.","zh":"這個短語用於某方法可能不再能衡量其聲稱要衡量之物時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"research of this type","meaning":"這類研究","examples":[{"en":"Mehan questions the validity of research of this type.","zh":"Mehan 質疑這類研究的有效性。"},{"en":"Research of this type means studies that use a similar method, assumption, or design.","zh":"research of this type 指使用相似方法、假設或設計的研究。"},{"en":"Research of this type may be useful for comparing test scores across schools.","zh":"這類研究可能有助比較不同學校的測驗分數。"},{"en":"If one type of research repeatedly misunderstands participants, its conclusions may be weakened.","zh":"如果某類研究反覆誤解參與者，其結論可能被削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase groups similar studies together.","zh":"這個短語把相似研究歸為一類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"questions regarding","meaning":"關於……的疑問","examples":[{"en":"There are also questions regarding the assumptions of quantitative research.","zh":"也有關於定量研究假設的疑問。"},{"en":"Questions regarding something are doubts or issues about that subject.","zh":"questions regarding something 指關於某主題的疑問或問題。"},{"en":"Parents may raise questions regarding the safety of a school trip.","zh":"家長可能提出關於學校旅行安全的疑問。"},{"en":"When questions regarding a method appear, researchers need to explain or revise it.","zh":"當關於某方法的疑問出現，研究人員需要解釋或修訂它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an area of concern.","zh":"這個短語引入一個令人關注的範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"identify causes","meaning":"找出成因","examples":[{"en":"Quantitative researchers often assume that causes can be identified.","zh":"定量研究人員常假設成因可以被找出。"},{"en":"To identify causes means to find the reasons why something happens.","zh":"identify causes 指找出某事發生的原因。"},{"en":"A school may try to identify causes of falling attendance before changing its policy.","zh":"學校在改變政策前，可能嘗試找出出席率下降的成因。"},{"en":"Identifying causes helps people solve problems rather than only describe them.","zh":"找出成因幫助人們解決問題，而不只是描述問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on finding reasons behind results.","zh":"這個短語著重找出結果背後的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"statistical manipulation of the variables","meaning":"對變項作統計操控","examples":[{"en":"Researchers may identify causes through statistical manipulation of the variables.","zh":"研究人員可能透過對變項作統計操控來找出成因。"},{"en":"Statistical manipulation of the variables means using statistical methods to examine how different factors relate to one another.","zh":"statistical manipulation of the variables 指使用統計方法檢視不同因素如何互相關聯。"},{"en":"A researcher may use statistical manipulation of the variables to see whether homework time predicts exam scores.","zh":"研究人員可能透過對變項作統計操控，看看功課時間是否能預測考試分數。"},{"en":"This method can reveal patterns, but it cannot always explain human meaning or context.","zh":"這種方法可以揭示模式，但未必總能解釋人的意義或情境。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to number-based analysis of research factors.","zh":"這個短語指對研究因素作基於數字的分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"physical manipulation of the variables","meaning":"對變項作物理操控","examples":[{"en":"Some research relies on physical manipulation of the variables.","zh":"有些研究依賴對變項作物理操控。"},{"en":"Physical manipulation of the variables means changing research conditions directly in the real setting.","zh":"physical manipulation of the variables 指在真實環境中直接改變研究條件。"},{"en":"A teacher may physically manipulate a variable by giving one class extra reading time and another class none.","zh":"老師可以透過給一班額外閱讀時間而另一班沒有，來對變項作物理操控。"},{"en":"Changing variables can help test causes, but it may be difficult or unfair in real classrooms.","zh":"改變變項可以幫助測試成因，但在真實課室中可能困難或不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to direct control of research conditions.","zh":"這個短語指直接控制研究條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"variables","meaning":"變項","examples":[{"en":"Quantitative research often focuses on variables.","zh":"定量研究常集中於變項。"},{"en":"Variables are factors that can change, such as age, test score, class size, or study time.","zh":"variables 指可以改變的因素，例如年齡、測驗分數、班級人數或學習時間。"},{"en":"In a school study, variables may include attendance, homework hours, and reading level.","zh":"在學校研究中，變項可能包括出席率、功課時間和閱讀程度。"},{"en":"Researchers study variables to see whether changes in one factor are linked to changes in another.","zh":"研究人員研究變項，以看一個因素的變化是否與另一因素的變化有關。"},{"en":"This word is central to quantitative research.","zh":"這個詞是定量研究的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take into consideration","meaning":"考慮到","examples":[{"en":"Critics argue that this approach does not take social life into consideration.","zh":"批評者認為這種方法沒有考慮到社會生活。"},{"en":"To take something into consideration means to include it when thinking, judging, or deciding.","zh":"take something into consideration 指在思考、判斷或決定時包括某因素。"},{"en":"A teacher should take family responsibilities into consideration when a student is often tired.","zh":"當學生經常疲倦，老師應考慮到其家庭責任。"},{"en":"If researchers ignore context, they may fail to take important human factors into consideration.","zh":"如果研究人員忽略情境，他們可能沒有考慮到重要的人為因素。"},{"en":"This phrase means not leaving an important factor out.","zh":"這個短語指不把重要因素排除在外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the nature of human social life","meaning":"人類社會生活的本質","examples":[{"en":"The criticism concerns the nature of human social life.","zh":"這項批評關乎人類社會生活的本質。"},{"en":"The nature of human social life means the basic way people interact, interpret, negotiate, and behave together.","zh":"nature of human social life 指人們互動、詮釋、協商和共同表現的基本方式。"},{"en":"A classroom shows the nature of human social life because students respond to friendship, authority, and expectations.","zh":"課室顯示人類社會生活的本質，因為學生會回應友誼、權威和期望。"},{"en":"Human social life is complex because people do not react like machines.","zh":"人類社會生活很複雜，因為人不會像機器一樣反應。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to what social life is really like.","zh":"這個短語指社會生活真正是怎樣的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be made up of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"Human social life should not be seen as being made up of mechanical relationships.","zh":"人類社會生活不應被視為由機械式關係組成。"},{"en":"To be made up of something means to consist of or be formed from it.","zh":"be made up of something 指由某些部分構成。"},{"en":"A school day is made up of lessons, breaks, lunch, and activities.","zh":"一個上學日由課堂、休息、午餐和活動組成。"},{"en":"If we say society is made up only of numbers, we may miss feelings and meanings.","zh":"如果我們說社會只由數字組成，可能會忽略感受和意義。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what something contains or consists of.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事由甚麼組成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"static relationships","meaning":"靜態關係","examples":[{"en":"Critics reject the idea that social life consists of static relationships.","zh":"批評者反對社會生活由靜態關係組成這個想法。"},{"en":"Static relationships are fixed relationships that do not change over time or context.","zh":"static relationships 指不會隨時間或情境改變的固定關係。"},{"en":"Teacher-student relationships are not static because trust can grow or weaken during the year.","zh":"師生關係不是靜態關係，因為信任可以在一年中增強或削弱。"},{"en":"Social relationships change when people talk, misunderstand, cooperate, or disagree.","zh":"當人們交談、誤解、合作或不同意，社會關係就會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts fixed links with flexible human interaction.","zh":"這個短語把固定連結與靈活的人際互動作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"mechanical causal relationships","meaning":"機械式因果關係","examples":[{"en":"Human social life cannot be reduced to mechanical causal relationships.","zh":"人類社會生活不能被簡化成機械式因果關係。"},{"en":"Mechanical causal relationships are simple cause-and-effect links that operate like a machine.","zh":"mechanical causal relationships 指像機器一樣運作的簡單因果連結。"},{"en":"In a machine, pressing a button may always produce the same result; people are less predictable.","zh":"在機器中，按下按鈕可能總會產生相同結果；人則較難預測。"},{"en":"Social behaviour cannot always be explained by one cause leading to one fixed effect.","zh":"社會行為未必總能用一個原因導致一個固定結果來解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises overly simple explanations of human life.","zh":"這個短語批評對人類生活過分簡化的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in reality","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In reality, social life includes interpretation and negotiation.","zh":"事實上，社會生活包括詮釋和協商。"},{"en":"In reality means in fact, or in the real world rather than in theory.","zh":"in reality 指事實上，或在真實世界中而非理論上。"},{"en":"A job may sound easy in an advertisement; in reality, it may require long hours and patience.","zh":"一份工作在廣告中可能聽起來容易；事實上，它可能需要長時間工作和耐性。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to correct an overly simple belief.","zh":"作者使用這個短語來更正過分簡化的信念。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts what seems true with what is actually true.","zh":"這個短語把看似真實的東西與實際真相作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"complicated procedures of","meaning":"複雜的……過程","examples":[{"en":"Social life includes complicated procedures of interpretation and negotiation.","zh":"社會生活包括複雜的詮釋和協商過程。"},{"en":"Complicated procedures of something are complex processes involving several steps or choices.","zh":"complicated procedures of something 指涉及幾個步驟或選擇的複雜過程。"},{"en":"Applying for university may involve complicated procedures of forms, interviews, and document checks.","zh":"申請大學可能涉及填表、面試和文件檢查等複雜過程。"},{"en":"Complicated procedures can make simple outcomes difficult to explain.","zh":"複雜過程可以令簡單結果變得難以解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the complexity behind an activity.","zh":"這個短語突出活動背後的複雜性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"interpretation and negotiation","meaning":"詮釋和協商","examples":[{"en":"Human social life involves interpretation and negotiation.","zh":"人類社會生活涉及詮釋和協商。"},{"en":"Interpretation and negotiation mean understanding meaning and working out shared decisions or expectations.","zh":"interpretation and negotiation 指理解意思，並協調共同決定或期望。"},{"en":"In group work, students use interpretation and negotiation when deciding what the teacher’s instructions mean.","zh":"在小組活動中，學生在決定老師指示的意思時，就是在使用詮釋和協商。"},{"en":"Misinterpretation can lead to conflict, while negotiation can help people agree on a way forward.","zh":"誤解可能導致衝突，而協商可以幫助人們同意前進方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two important parts of human interaction.","zh":"這個短語描述人際互動的兩個重要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"come with determinate results","meaning":"帶有確定結果","examples":[{"en":"Human interactions do not always come with determinate results.","zh":"人際互動並不總是帶有確定結果。"},{"en":"To come with determinate results means to produce fixed, certain, and predictable outcomes.","zh":"come with determinate results 指產生固定、確定和可預測的結果。"},{"en":"A vending machine may come with determinate results, but a classroom discussion usually does not.","zh":"自動售賣機可能帶有確定結果，但課堂討論通常不會。"},{"en":"Human behaviour is hard to predict because people interpret situations differently.","zh":"人類行為難以預測，因為人們會以不同方式詮釋情境。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts predictable outcomes with uncertain human responses.","zh":"這個短語把可預測結果與不確定的人類回應作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"from this perspective","meaning":"從這個角度看","examples":[{"en":"From this perspective, human behaviour is difficult to explain only through causes.","zh":"從這個角度看，人類行為難以只透過成因解釋。"},{"en":"From this perspective means when viewed from this particular way of thinking.","zh":"from this perspective 指從這種特定思考方式來看。"},{"en":"From this perspective, a quiet student may be careful rather than uninterested.","zh":"從這個角度看，安靜的學生可能是謹慎，而不是不感興趣。"},{"en":"Changing perspective can change what explanation seems most reasonable.","zh":"改變角度可以改變哪種解釋看來最合理。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an interpretation based on a certain viewpoint.","zh":"這個短語引入基於某一觀點的詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the pattern and mechanism behind","meaning":"……背後的模式和機制","examples":[{"en":"Researchers try to understand the pattern and mechanism behind people’s behaviour.","zh":"研究人員嘗試理解人們行為背後的模式和機制。"},{"en":"The pattern and mechanism behind something are the repeated form and the process that explains how it works.","zh":"pattern and mechanism behind something 指某事反覆出現的形式，以及解釋其如何運作的過程。"},{"en":"A teacher may study the pattern and mechanism behind repeated homework delays.","zh":"老師可能研究學生反覆遲交功課背後的模式和機制。"},{"en":"Understanding the mechanism helps people fix the cause, not only notice the result.","zh":"理解機制幫助人們修正成因，而不只是注意結果。"},{"en":"This phrase looks for both what happens regularly and why it happens.","zh":"這個短語尋找甚麼經常發生，以及為何發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"people’s behaviours","meaning":"人們的行為","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses how researchers understand people’s behaviours.","zh":"文章討論研究人員如何理解人們的行為。"},{"en":"People’s behaviours are the actions, reactions, habits, and choices people show in real situations.","zh":"people’s behaviours 指人們在真實情境中表現出的行動、反應、習慣和選擇。"},{"en":"Teachers observe people’s behaviours when they study how students work in groups.","zh":"老師研究學生如何小組合作時，會觀察人們的行為。"},{"en":"Behaviours may change when people feel watched, judged, or misunderstood.","zh":"當人們感到被觀察、被評判或被誤解，行為可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what people actually do.","zh":"這個短語著重人們實際做甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"simply in terms of","meaning":"純粹從……角度","examples":[{"en":"We cannot understand social life simply in terms of causal relationships.","zh":"我們不能純粹從因果關係角度理解社會生活。"},{"en":"Simply in terms of means only from one particular angle or explanation.","zh":"simply in terms of 指只從某一特定角度或解釋來看。"},{"en":"We should not judge a student simply in terms of exam marks.","zh":"我們不應純粹從考試分數角度評價學生。"},{"en":"Looking only at one measure can hide important context and meaning.","zh":"只看一項衡量指標，可能隱藏重要背景和意義。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against an overly narrow explanation.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要作過分狹窄的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"causal relationships","meaning":"因果關係","examples":[{"en":"Quantitative research often focuses on causal relationships.","zh":"定量研究常集中於因果關係。"},{"en":"Causal relationships are links where one thing causes or influences another.","zh":"causal relationships 指一件事導致或影響另一件事的連結。"},{"en":"A school may study the causal relationship between extra reading time and higher vocabulary scores.","zh":"學校可能研究額外閱讀時間與較高詞彙分數之間的因果關係。"},{"en":"Causal relationships are useful, but human behaviour may involve more than simple cause and effect.","zh":"因果關係有用，但人類行為可能涉及多於簡單因果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes connections of cause and result.","zh":"這個短語描述原因與結果的連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the focus of quantitative research","meaning":"定量研究的重點","examples":[{"en":"Causal relationships are the focus of quantitative research.","zh":"因果關係是定量研究的重點。"},{"en":"The focus of quantitative research is the main thing number-based studies try to measure or explain.","zh":"focus of quantitative research 指以數字為本的研究主要嘗試衡量或解釋的東西。"},{"en":"In education, the focus of quantitative research may be test scores, attendance, or learning gains.","zh":"在教育中，定量研究的重點可能是測驗分數、出席率或學習進步。"},{"en":"This focus can make patterns clearer but may reduce attention to personal meaning.","zh":"這個重點可以令模式更清楚，但可能減少對個人意義的關注。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what quantitative research mainly concentrates on.","zh":"這個短語指出定量研究主要集中於甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"it is implied that","meaning":"這暗示","examples":[{"en":"It is implied that social life is more complex than quantitative models suggest.","zh":"這暗示社會生活比定量模型所顯示的更複雜。"},{"en":"It is implied that means the idea is suggested indirectly rather than stated openly.","zh":"it is implied that 指某想法被間接暗示，而不是明確說出。"},{"en":"If a teacher says, “Please check the instructions again,” it may be implied that the student has misunderstood them.","zh":"如果老師說「請再檢查指示」，這可能暗示學生誤解了指示。"},{"en":"Implied meanings require readers to infer from context.","zh":"隱含意思需要讀者從語境推斷。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an unstated but suggested idea.","zh":"這個短語引入未明說但被暗示的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"contextually variable","meaning":"因情境而變化的","examples":[{"en":"Social life is contextually variable and complex.","zh":"社會生活是因情境而變化且複雜的。"},{"en":"Contextually variable means changing depending on the situation, setting, or social context.","zh":"contextually variable 指會因情況、環境或社交語境而改變。"},{"en":"A student may be confident at home but quiet at school, so behaviour is contextually variable.","zh":"學生可能在家自信，但在學校安靜，因此行為是因情境而變化的。"},{"en":"Because behaviour changes with context, one test may not show the whole picture.","zh":"因為行為會隨情境改變，一次測驗未必顯示完整圖像。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that shifts across different situations.","zh":"這個短語描述在不同情況中會改變的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"inspire someone to","meaning":"啟發某人去……","examples":[{"en":"Criticisms have inspired researchers to adopt qualitative methodologies.","zh":"批評啟發研究人員去採用定性研究方法。"},{"en":"To inspire someone to do something means to encourage or motivate them to take an action.","zh":"inspire someone to do something 指鼓勵或推動某人採取行動。"},{"en":"A caring teacher may inspire a student to read more outside class.","zh":"有愛心的老師可能啟發學生去課外多閱讀。"},{"en":"Strong criticism can inspire improvement when people treat it seriously.","zh":"當人們認真對待批評，有力批評可以啟發改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes motivation that leads to action.","zh":"這個短語描述導致行動的動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"adopt qualitative methodologies","meaning":"採用定性研究方法","examples":[{"en":"More educational researchers have adopted qualitative methodologies.","zh":"更多教育研究人員已採用定性研究方法。"},{"en":"To adopt qualitative methodologies means to start using research methods that explore meaning, context, and experience.","zh":"adopt qualitative methodologies 指開始使用探索意義、情境和經驗的研究方法。"},{"en":"A researcher may adopt qualitative methodologies by interviewing students about their classroom feelings.","zh":"研究人員可能透過訪問學生對課室的感受來採用定性研究方法。"},{"en":"Researchers may adopt these methods when numbers alone cannot explain behaviour.","zh":"當數字 alone 不能解釋行為時，研究人員可能採用這些方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing a non-number-centred research approach.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇非以數字為中心的研究取向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"qualitative methodologies","meaning":"定性研究方法","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative methodologies have become more common in education research.","zh":"定性研究方法在教育研究中變得更常見。"},{"en":"Qualitative methodologies are research methods that study meanings, experiences, language, and social context.","zh":"qualitative methodologies 指研究意義、經驗、語言和社會情境的方法。"},{"en":"Interviews, observations, case studies, and field notes are common qualitative methodologies.","zh":"訪談、觀察、個案研究和實地筆記都是常見定性研究方法。"},{"en":"These methods help explain why people behave as they do, not only how often behaviour occurs.","zh":"這些方法幫助解釋人們為何如此行為，而不只是行為發生得多頻密。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to research approaches based mainly on words and interpretation.","zh":"這個短語指主要基於文字和詮釋的研究取向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"over the last three or four decades","meaning":"在過去三四十年間","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative research has become more common over the last three or four decades.","zh":"在過去三四十年間，定性研究變得更常見。"},{"en":"Over the last three or four decades means during the past thirty or forty years.","zh":"over the last three or four decades 指在過去三十或四十年期間。"},{"en":"Over the last three or four decades, computers have changed how students write and research.","zh":"在過去三四十年間，電腦改變了學生寫作和研究的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a long-term trend rather than a sudden change.","zh":"這個短語顯示長期趨勢，而不是突然變化。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing developments across a generation or more.","zh":"它適合描述跨越一代或更長時間的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"steer away from","meaning":"避開；不再採用","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative researchers have steered away from manipulating variables.","zh":"定性研究人員已避開操控變項。"},{"en":"To steer away from something means to avoid it or move in a different direction.","zh":"steer away from something 指避開某事或轉向另一方向。"},{"en":"A teacher may steer away from long lectures if students learn better through discussion.","zh":"如果學生透過討論學得更好，老師可能不再採用長篇講課。"},{"en":"Researchers may steer away from a method when it does not fit their research questions.","zh":"當某方法不適合研究問題，研究人員可能避開它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deliberate avoidance or change of direction.","zh":"這個短語描述有意識的避免或方向轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"measuring and manipulating variables","meaning":"測量和操控變項","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative researchers often avoid measuring and manipulating variables.","zh":"定性研究人員通常避免測量和操控變項。"},{"en":"Measuring and manipulating variables means recording factors numerically and changing them to test effects.","zh":"measuring and manipulating variables 指以數字記錄因素，並改變它們來測試效果。"},{"en":"A researcher measures and manipulates variables when one group receives extra lessons and another group does not.","zh":"當一組學生接受額外課堂而另一組沒有時，研究人員就在測量和操控變項。"},{"en":"This approach can test cause and effect but may simplify real classroom life.","zh":"這種方法可以測試因果，但可能簡化真實課室生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a core practice of experimental quantitative research.","zh":"這個短語描述實驗性定量研究的核心做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"experimentally or statistically","meaning":"以實驗或統計方式","examples":[{"en":"Variables can be manipulated experimentally or statistically.","zh":"變項可以以實驗或統計方式被操控。"},{"en":"Experimentally or statistically means through direct experimental control or through statistical calculation.","zh":"experimentally or statistically 指透過直接實驗控制或統計計算。"},{"en":"Researchers may examine study time experimentally or statistically, depending on the design.","zh":"研究人員可能以實驗或統計方式檢視學習時間，視乎設計而定。"},{"en":"Experimental control changes conditions directly, while statistical control handles data mathematically.","zh":"實驗控制直接改變條件，而統計控制以數學方式處理數據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two different ways to handle variables.","zh":"這個短語描述處理變項的兩種不同方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"forms of qualitative research","meaning":"定性研究形式","examples":[{"en":"There are many forms of qualitative research.","zh":"定性研究有很多形式。"},{"en":"Forms of qualitative research are different ways of studying experience, meaning, and social behaviour.","zh":"forms of qualitative research 指研究經驗、意義和社會行為的不同方法。"},{"en":"Interviews, observations, case studies, and discourse analysis are forms of qualitative research.","zh":"訪談、觀察、個案研究和話語分析都是定性研究形式。"},{"en":"Different forms are chosen because different questions need different kinds of evidence.","zh":"之所以選擇不同形式，是因為不同問題需要不同證據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the various methods within qualitative study.","zh":"這個短語指定性研究內的各種方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"loosely described by","meaning":"大致以……描述","examples":[{"en":"These methods are loosely described by terms such as ethnography and case study.","zh":"這些方法大致以民族誌研究和個案研究等術語描述。"},{"en":"Loosely described by means named in a broad, not exact, way.","zh":"loosely described by 指以寬泛而非精確的方式命名。"},{"en":"A school project may be loosely described by the term “research,” even if it includes interviews and posters.","zh":"學校專題即使包括訪談和海報，也可能大致以「研究」一詞描述。"},{"en":"Loose descriptions can be useful, but they may hide important differences between methods.","zh":"寬泛描述可以有用，但可能隱藏方法之間的重要差異。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the label is approximate.","zh":"這個短語表示標籤只是大概。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ethnography","meaning":"民族誌研究","examples":[{"en":"Ethnography is one form of qualitative research.","zh":"民族誌研究是定性研究的一種形式。"},{"en":"Ethnography is a research method that studies people’s culture, behaviour, and daily life in a natural setting.","zh":"ethnography 指在自然環境中研究人們文化、行為和日常生活的研究方法。"},{"en":"A researcher may use ethnography by spending months observing students in one school.","zh":"研究人員可能透過花數月觀察一所學校的學生來進行民族誌研究。"},{"en":"Ethnography helps researchers understand what people do and what those actions mean to them.","zh":"民族誌研究幫助研究人員理解人們做甚麼，以及這些行動對他們有何意義。"},{"en":"This word refers to in-depth study of a group’s social life.","zh":"這個詞指對某群體社會生活的深入研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"case study","meaning":"個案研究","examples":[{"en":"A case study can explore one school or group in depth.","zh":"個案研究可以深入探索一所學校或一個群體。"},{"en":"A case study is a detailed investigation of one person, group, event, school, or situation.","zh":"case study 指對一個人、群體、事件、學校或情況作詳細研究。"},{"en":"A researcher may write a case study of one class that improved after a new reading programme.","zh":"研究人員可能撰寫一個班級在新閱讀計劃後進步的個案研究。"},{"en":"Case studies give rich detail, but they may not represent every school or student.","zh":"個案研究提供豐富細節，但未必代表每所學校或每名學生。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to deep study of one specific case.","zh":"這個短語指對一個特定個案作深入研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"participant observation","meaning":"參與式觀察","examples":[{"en":"Participant observation is often used in qualitative research.","zh":"參與式觀察常用於定性研究。"},{"en":"Participant observation is a method where the researcher observes a group while taking part in its activities.","zh":"participant observation 指研究人員一邊參與群體活動，一邊觀察該群體的方法。"},{"en":"A researcher may use participant observation by joining a classroom project and watching how students cooperate.","zh":"研究人員可能透過加入課堂專題，並觀察學生如何合作來使用參與式觀察。"},{"en":"Taking part can help the researcher understand meanings that outsiders may miss.","zh":"參與其中可以幫助研究人員理解外人可能忽略的意義。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to observing from inside a social setting.","zh":"這個短語指從社交環境內部進行觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"life history","meaning":"生活史研究","examples":[{"en":"Life history is one form of qualitative research.","zh":"生活史研究是定性研究的一種形式。"},{"en":"Life history is a research method that studies a person’s experiences across time.","zh":"life history 指研究一個人隨時間累積的經驗的研究方法。"},{"en":"A researcher may collect a teacher’s life history to understand how her teaching beliefs developed.","zh":"研究人員可能收集一名老師的生活史，以理解她的教學信念如何形成。"},{"en":"Life histories show how personal experiences shape choices and identity.","zh":"生活史顯示個人經驗如何塑造選擇和身份。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to research based on a person’s story over time.","zh":"這個短語指基於一個人長期故事的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"unstructured interviewing","meaning":"非結構式訪談","examples":[{"en":"Unstructured interviewing allows participants to answer freely.","zh":"非結構式訪談讓參與者自由回答。"},{"en":"Unstructured interviewing is an interview method without fixed answer choices or a strict question order.","zh":"unstructured interviewing 指沒有固定答案選項或嚴格問題次序的訪談方法。"},{"en":"A researcher may use unstructured interviewing to let students describe school stress in their own words.","zh":"研究人員可能使用非結構式訪談，讓學生用自己的說話描述學校壓力。"},{"en":"This method can reveal unexpected ideas because participants are not forced into set categories.","zh":"這種方法可以揭示意想不到的想法，因為參與者不被迫放入固定類別。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to flexible, open conversation used as research.","zh":"這個短語指作為研究的靈活開放對話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"discourse analysis","meaning":"話語分析","examples":[{"en":"Discourse analysis examines language use in social contexts.","zh":"話語分析檢視社會語境中的語言使用。"},{"en":"Discourse analysis is a research method that studies how language creates meaning, power, and relationships.","zh":"discourse analysis 指研究語言如何創造意義、權力和關係的研究方法。"},{"en":"A researcher may use discourse analysis to study how teachers praise or correct students.","zh":"研究人員可能使用話語分析，研究老師如何稱讚或糾正學生。"},{"en":"The way people speak can reveal assumptions about authority, identity, and fairness.","zh":"人們說話的方式可以揭示關於權威、身份和公平的假設。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to analysing language in real social use.","zh":"這個短語指分析真實社會使用中的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"and so on","meaning":"等等","examples":[{"en":"The passage lists ethnography, case study, participant observation and so on.","zh":"文章列出民族誌研究、個案研究、參與式觀察等等。"},{"en":"And so on means and other similar things.","zh":"and so on 指以及其他相似事物。"},{"en":"A school bag may contain books, pens, notebooks, and so on.","zh":"書包可能有書、筆、筆記簿等等。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when the reader can understand the rest of the list without every item being named.","zh":"當讀者能理解清單其餘部分而無需逐項列出，作者會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids making a list unnecessarily long.","zh":"這個短語避免令清單不必要地冗長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"generally speaking","meaning":"一般來說","examples":[{"en":"Generally speaking, qualitative research has several characteristics.","zh":"一般來說，定性研究有幾個特點。"},{"en":"Generally speaking means in most cases or as a broad statement.","zh":"generally speaking 指在大多數情況下，或作為概括說法。"},{"en":"Generally speaking, students learn better when examples are clear and familiar.","zh":"一般來說，例子清楚而熟悉時，學生學得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase allows a writer to make a general point without claiming it is always true.","zh":"這個短語讓作者提出一般重點，而不聲稱它永遠正確。"},{"en":"It is useful when introducing typical features.","zh":"它適合用於引入典型特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have an intensive focus on","meaning":"密集地專注於……","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative research has an intensive focus on exploring phenomena.","zh":"定性研究密集地專注於探索現象。"},{"en":"To have an intensive focus on something means to study or pay close attention to it in great detail.","zh":"have an intensive focus on something 指非常仔細地研究或關注某事。"},{"en":"A school counsellor may have an intensive focus on why certain students avoid group work.","zh":"學校輔導員可能密集地專注於為何某些學生避免小組活動。"},{"en":"Intensive focus produces rich detail but usually involves fewer cases.","zh":"密集關注會產生豐富細節，但通常涉及較少個案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep concentration on a particular issue.","zh":"這個短語描述對某特定問題的深入集中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"explore the nature of","meaning":"探索……的本質","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative research explores the nature of educational phenomena.","zh":"定性研究探索教育現象的本質。"},{"en":"To explore the nature of something means to investigate what it is really like and how it works.","zh":"explore the nature of something 指研究某事真正是怎樣，以及如何運作。"},{"en":"A teacher may explore the nature of exam anxiety by talking with students about their feelings.","zh":"老師可能透過與學生談感受，探索考試焦慮的本質。"},{"en":"Exploring nature means looking beyond surface results to meaning and experience.","zh":"探索本質意味看超越表面結果，進入意義和經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep investigation of a subject.","zh":"這個短語描述對主題的深入研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"certain phenomena","meaning":"某些現象","examples":[{"en":"The researchers explore certain phenomena in the field of education.","zh":"研究人員探索教育領域中的某些現象。"},{"en":"Certain phenomena are particular events, patterns, or behaviours that can be observed and studied.","zh":"certain phenomena 指可以被觀察和研究的特定事件、模式或行為。"},{"en":"Bullying, classroom silence, and exam anxiety are certain phenomena in school life.","zh":"欺凌、課室沉默和考試焦慮都是學校生活中的某些現象。"},{"en":"Researchers focus on certain phenomena because they want to understand specific problems deeply.","zh":"研究人員集中於某些現象，因為他們想深入理解特定問題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to selected things that happen or appear.","zh":"這個短語指被選定研究的事情或現象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in the field of education","meaning":"在教育領域","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses research in the field of education.","zh":"文章討論教育領域中的研究。"},{"en":"In the field of education means within the area of teaching, learning, schools, and student development.","zh":"in the field of education 指在教學、學習、學校和學生發展的範疇內。"},{"en":"People in the field of education may work as teachers, researchers, principals, or policymakers.","zh":"教育領域的人可能是老師、研究人員、校長或政策制定者。"},{"en":"Research in this field can influence classrooms, exams, and school support services.","zh":"這個領域的研究可以影響課室、考試和學校支援服務。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies education as the professional or academic area being discussed.","zh":"這個短語指出正在討論的專業或學術範疇是教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"instead of","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative research explores phenomena instead of only testing hypotheses.","zh":"定性研究探索現象，而不是只測試假設。"},{"en":"Instead of means in place of or rather than.","zh":"instead of 指取代或而不是。"},{"en":"A teacher may use discussion instead of another worksheet when students need to explain ideas.","zh":"當學生需要解釋想法時，老師可能使用討論而不是再做一張工作紙。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one method or choice replaces another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一種方法或選擇取代另一種。"},{"en":"It creates a clear contrast between two options.","zh":"它在兩個選項之間建立清楚對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"set out to","meaning":"著手；旨在","examples":[{"en":"Quantitative researchers often set out to test hypotheses.","zh":"定量研究人員通常旨在測試假設。"},{"en":"To set out to do something means to begin with the aim of doing it.","zh":"set out to do something 指一開始便以做某事為目標。"},{"en":"A student may set out to improve her vocabulary by learning ten useful phrases a day.","zh":"學生可能旨在透過每天學十個有用短語來改善詞彙。"},{"en":"The aim people set out with shapes the method they choose.","zh":"人們起初設定的目標會塑造他們選擇的方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intention at the start of an action.","zh":"這個短語描述行動開始時的意圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"test hypotheses","meaning":"測試假設","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers design studies to test hypotheses.","zh":"有些研究人員設計研究來測試假設。"},{"en":"To test hypotheses means to check whether proposed explanations are supported by evidence.","zh":"test hypotheses 指檢查提出的解釋是否得到證據支持。"},{"en":"A school may test the hypothesis that shorter homework improves sleep and concentration.","zh":"學校可能測試「較短功課可改善睡眠和專注力」這一假設。"},{"en":"Testing hypotheses helps researchers move from guesses to evidence-based conclusions.","zh":"測試假設幫助研究人員由猜測走向基於證據的結論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a central aim of many experiments.","zh":"這個短語描述許多實驗的核心目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"tend to deal with","meaning":"傾向處理","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative research tends to deal with unstructured data.","zh":"定性研究傾向處理非結構化數據。"},{"en":"To tend to deal with something means usually to handle or focus on that kind of material or issue.","zh":"tend to deal with something 指通常處理或集中於某類材料或問題。"},{"en":"A school counsellor tends to deal with emotional problems more than exam scores.","zh":"學校輔導員傾向處理情緒問題，而不是考試分數。"},{"en":"What researchers deal with affects the methods they use.","zh":"研究人員處理甚麼，會影響他們使用的方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a usual pattern, not an absolute rule.","zh":"這個短語描述通常模式，而不是絕對規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unstructured data","meaning":"非結構化數據","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative research often deals with unstructured data.","zh":"定性研究常處理非結構化數據。"},{"en":"Unstructured data are information that has not been arranged into fixed categories before collection.","zh":"unstructured data 指在收集前未被安排到固定類別中的資料。"},{"en":"Students’ interview answers, classroom conversations, and field notes can be unstructured data.","zh":"學生訪談答案、課室對話和實地筆記都可以是非結構化數據。"},{"en":"Unstructured data can reveal unexpected ideas because participants are not forced into preset boxes.","zh":"非結構化數據可以揭示意想不到的想法，因為參與者不被迫放入預設框架。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to flexible, open-ended research material.","zh":"這個短語指靈活、開放式的研究材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"指的是","examples":[{"en":"Unstructured data refers to data that have not been coded in advance.","zh":"非結構化數據指的是未預先編碼的數據。"},{"en":"To refer to something means to mean, mention, or point to it.","zh":"refer to something 指意思是、提及或指向某事。"},{"en":"In this lesson, “tone” refers to the writer’s attitude toward the topic.","zh":"在這課中，“tone” 指的是作者對主題的態度。"},{"en":"Definitions often use “refer to” to explain the meaning of a term.","zh":"定義常使用 “refer to” 來解釋術語意思。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a word or phrase with its meaning.","zh":"這個短語把詞語或短語與其意思連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be coded","meaning":"被編碼","examples":[{"en":"The data have not been coded during the collection process.","zh":"數據在收集過程中並未被編碼。"},{"en":"To be coded means to be labelled or sorted into categories for analysis.","zh":"be coded 指被標籤或分類，以便分析。"},{"en":"Survey answers may be coded as “agree,” “disagree,” or “not sure.”","zh":"問卷答案可能被編碼為「同意」、「不同意」或「不確定」。"},{"en":"Coding makes data easier to count, but it may remove some detail.","zh":"編碼令數據較容易計算，但可能移除一些細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organising data into analytical labels.","zh":"這個短語描述把數據整理成分析標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the collection process","meaning":"收集過程","examples":[{"en":"The data are not coded during the collection process.","zh":"數據在收集過程中並未被編碼。"},{"en":"The collection process is the stage when researchers gather information from participants or settings.","zh":"collection process 指研究人員從參與者或環境收集資料的階段。"},{"en":"During the collection process, a researcher may record interviews and take notes.","zh":"在收集過程中，研究人員可能錄下訪談並做筆記。"},{"en":"Decisions made during collection affect what data are available later.","zh":"收集期間作出的決定會影響之後可用的數據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the gathering stage of research.","zh":"這個短語指研究中的資料收集階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"The data are not coded according to a closed set of categories.","zh":"數據並非根據一套封閉類別被編碼。"},{"en":"According to means based on or following a particular rule, source, or system.","zh":"according to 指基於或依照某規則、來源或系統。"},{"en":"Students should answer according to the passage, not according to outside knowledge.","zh":"學生應根據文章回答，而不是根據外部知識。"},{"en":"When data are coded according to fixed categories, unexpected answers may be harder to capture.","zh":"當數據根據固定類別編碼時，意想不到的答案可能較難捕捉。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the standard or source being followed.","zh":"這個短語顯示所跟從的標準或來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a closed set of analytical categories","meaning":"一套封閉的分析類別","examples":[{"en":"Quantitative research often uses a closed set of analytical categories.","zh":"定量研究常使用一套封閉的分析類別。"},{"en":"A closed set of analytical categories is a fixed list of labels used to classify data.","zh":"closed set of analytical categories 指用來分類數據的一套固定標籤。"},{"en":"A survey may use a closed set of analytical categories such as “yes,” “no,” and “not sure.”","zh":"問卷可能使用一套封閉的分析類別，例如「是」、「否」和「不確定」。"},{"en":"Closed categories make counting easier, but they may limit what participants can express.","zh":"封閉類別令計算較容易，但可能限制參與者能表達的內容。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to fixed categories used for analysis.","zh":"這個短語指用於分析的固定類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, qualitative researchers use audio or video devices.","zh":"因此，定性研究人員使用錄音或錄影裝置。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what has just been mentioned.","zh":"as a result 指因為剛提及的事情。"},{"en":"The bus was late; as a result, several students missed the first lesson.","zh":"巴士遲到；因此，幾名學生錯過第一堂課。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to show cause and effect clearly.","zh":"作者使用這個短語清楚顯示因果。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a consequence.","zh":"這個短語引入結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"engage in observation","meaning":"進行觀察","examples":[{"en":"Researchers engage in observation to record what happens.","zh":"研究人員進行觀察以記錄發生的事情。"},{"en":"To engage in observation means to watch people, events, or settings carefully for research.","zh":"engage in observation 指為研究而仔細觀看人、事件或環境。"},{"en":"A teacher may engage in observation to see how students behave during group work.","zh":"老師可能進行觀察，以了解學生在小組活動中的表現。"},{"en":"Observation helps researchers collect real behaviour rather than only reported opinions.","zh":"觀察幫助研究人員收集真實行為，而不只是受訪者聲稱的意見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful watching as a research activity.","zh":"這個短語描述作為研究活動的仔細觀看。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"audio or video devices","meaning":"錄音或錄影裝置","examples":[{"en":"Researchers use audio or video devices to record classroom events.","zh":"研究人員使用錄音或錄影裝置記錄課室事件。"},{"en":"Audio or video devices are tools that record sound, images, or both.","zh":"audio or video devices 指記錄聲音、影像或兩者的工具。"},{"en":"A researcher may use audio or video devices during interviews so important details are not forgotten.","zh":"研究人員可能在訪談中使用錄音或錄影裝置，以免忘記重要細節。"},{"en":"Recordings allow researchers to review speech, gestures, and classroom interaction later.","zh":"錄音錄影讓研究人員日後重看說話、手勢和課室互動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to recording equipment.","zh":"這個短語指記錄設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"write detailed field notes","meaning":"撰寫詳細實地筆記","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative researchers write detailed field notes during observation.","zh":"定性研究人員在觀察期間撰寫詳細實地筆記。"},{"en":"To write detailed field notes means to record careful descriptions of what is seen, heard, and understood in the research setting.","zh":"write detailed field notes 指仔細記錄在研究場景中所見、所聞和所理解的內容。"},{"en":"A researcher may write detailed field notes about where students sit and who speaks first.","zh":"研究人員可能撰寫詳細實地筆記，記錄學生坐在哪裡以及誰先說話。"},{"en":"Detailed notes help preserve context that a simple score cannot show.","zh":"詳細筆記幫助保存簡單分數不能顯示的情境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful written observation.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細的書面觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"open-ended field notes","meaning":"開放式實地筆記","examples":[{"en":"Open-ended field notes allow researchers to record unexpected details.","zh":"開放式實地筆記讓研究人員記錄意想不到的細節。"},{"en":"Open-ended field notes are observation notes that do not force information into fixed categories.","zh":"open-ended field notes 指不強迫資料放入固定類別的觀察筆記。"},{"en":"A researcher may use open-ended field notes to record a surprising joke, silence, or gesture in class.","zh":"研究人員可能用開放式實地筆記記錄課堂中意外的笑話、沉默或手勢。"},{"en":"Open-ended notes can capture details that a checklist would miss.","zh":"開放式筆記可以捕捉檢查清單會漏掉的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to flexible notes written during observation.","zh":"這個短語指觀察期間撰寫的靈活筆記。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"code behaviour according to","meaning":"按照……將行為編碼","examples":[{"en":"Quantitative researchers may code behaviour according to fixed categories.","zh":"定量研究人員可能按照固定類別將行為編碼。"},{"en":"To code behaviour according to categories means to label actions using a set system.","zh":"code behaviour according to categories 指使用一套系統標籤行動。"},{"en":"A researcher may code behaviour according to categories such as “speaking,” “listening,” or “off-task.”","zh":"研究人員可能按照「說話」、「聆聽」或「離題」等類別將行為編碼。"},{"en":"Coding behaviour helps with counting, but it may simplify complex classroom actions.","zh":"將行為編碼有助計算，但可能簡化複雜的課室行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes classifying behaviour for analysis.","zh":"這個短語描述為分析而分類行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a predetermined set of categories","meaning":"一套預先決定的類別","examples":[{"en":"Systematic observation often uses a predetermined set of categories.","zh":"系統性觀察常使用一套預先決定的類別。"},{"en":"A predetermined set of categories is a fixed group of labels decided before data collection begins.","zh":"predetermined set of categories 指在數據收集開始前已決定的一組固定標籤。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a predetermined set of categories to mark speaking, such as fluency, accuracy, and confidence.","zh":"老師可能使用一套預先決定的類別評核口語，例如流暢度、準確度和自信。"},{"en":"Predetermined categories make comparison easier but may miss unexpected behaviour.","zh":"預先決定的類別令比較較容易，但可能漏掉意想不到的行為。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to categories chosen in advance.","zh":"這個短語指事先選定的類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"typically do","meaning":"通常會做","examples":[{"en":"This is what quantitative researchers would typically do.","zh":"這是定量研究人員通常會做的事。"},{"en":"Typically do means usually do in normal cases.","zh":"typically do 指在正常情況下通常會做。"},{"en":"Students typically do a short warm-up before the main writing task.","zh":"學生通常會在主要寫作任務前做簡短熱身。"},{"en":"What people typically do may change when the purpose or context changes.","zh":"人們通常會做的事，可能會隨目的或情境改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes normal practice, not a strict rule.","zh":"這個短語描述一般做法，而不是嚴格規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"conduct systematic observation","meaning":"進行系統性觀察","examples":[{"en":"Quantitative researchers often conduct systematic observation.","zh":"定量研究人員常進行系統性觀察。"},{"en":"To conduct systematic observation means to watch and record behaviour using a planned, organised method.","zh":"conduct systematic observation 指使用有計劃、有組織的方法觀察和記錄行為。"},{"en":"A researcher may conduct systematic observation by counting how many times students raise their hands.","zh":"研究人員可能透過計算學生舉手次數來進行系統性觀察。"},{"en":"Systematic observation makes data easier to compare across classes.","zh":"系統性觀察令不同班級的數據較容易比較。"},{"en":"This phrase describes structured watching for research.","zh":"這個短語描述用於研究的結構化觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"similarly","meaning":"同樣地","examples":[{"en":"Similarly, qualitative interviews use open-ended questions.","zh":"同樣地，定性訪談使用開放式問題。"},{"en":"Similarly means in a similar way or for a similar reason.","zh":"similarly 指以相似方式或基於相似原因。"},{"en":"One class benefits from visual examples; similarly, another class learns better with pictures than long explanations.","zh":"一班受益於視覺例子；同樣地，另一班也透過圖片比長篇解釋學得更好。"},{"en":"Writers use this word to connect two related points.","zh":"作者使用這個詞連接兩個相關重點。"},{"en":"This word shows that the next idea follows a similar pattern.","zh":"這個詞顯示下一個想法遵循相似模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"open-ended questions","meaning":"開放式問題","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative interviewers ask open-ended questions.","zh":"定性訪談者會問開放式問題。"},{"en":"Open-ended questions allow people to answer in their own words rather than choosing from fixed options.","zh":"open-ended questions 讓人用自己的話回答，而不是從固定選項中選擇。"},{"en":"“How do you feel about homework?” is an open-ended question.","zh":"「你對功課有甚麼感受？」是一條開放式問題。"},{"en":"Open-ended questions can reveal feelings, reasons, and examples that closed questions may miss.","zh":"開放式問題可以揭示封閉式問題可能漏掉的感受、原因和例子。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to questions with flexible answers.","zh":"這個短語指答案靈活的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"specific, predefined answers","meaning":"具體而預先設定的答案","examples":[{"en":"Postal questionnaires often require specific, predefined answers.","zh":"郵寄問卷通常要求具體而預先設定的答案。"},{"en":"Specific, predefined answers are fixed responses prepared before participants answer.","zh":"specific, predefined answers 指在參與者回答前已準備好的固定回應。"},{"en":"A form asking students to choose “agree,” “disagree,” or “not sure” uses specific, predefined answers.","zh":"要學生選擇「同意」、「不同意」或「不確定」的表格，使用具體而預先設定的答案。"},{"en":"These answers make data easy to count but may restrict what people can say.","zh":"這些答案令數據容易計算，但可能限制人們能說甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes closed answer choices.","zh":"這個短語描述封閉式答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"predefined answers","meaning":"預先設定的答案","examples":[{"en":"Some questionnaires require predefined answers.","zh":"有些問卷要求預先設定的答案。"},{"en":"Predefined answers are answer choices prepared before the respondent sees the question.","zh":"predefined answers 指受訪者看到問題前已準備好的答案選項。"},{"en":"A multiple-choice question gives predefined answers for students to choose from.","zh":"多項選擇題提供預先設定的答案讓學生選擇。"},{"en":"Predefined answers are useful for statistics but may not fit every person’s view.","zh":"預先設定的答案對統計有用，但未必符合每個人的觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to fixed response options.","zh":"這個短語指固定回應選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"postal questionnaire","meaning":"郵寄問卷","examples":[{"en":"A postal questionnaire usually asks for specific answers.","zh":"郵寄問卷通常要求具體答案。"},{"en":"A postal questionnaire is a survey sent and returned by post.","zh":"postal questionnaire 指透過郵寄寄出和回收的調查問卷。"},{"en":"A school may send a postal questionnaire to parents who do not use email.","zh":"學校可能向不用電郵的家長寄出郵寄問卷。"},{"en":"Postal questionnaires can reach many people, but response rates may be low.","zh":"郵寄問卷可以接觸很多人，但回覆率可能低。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a paper survey delivered through the mail.","zh":"這個短語指透過郵件送遞的紙本調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be designed to resemble","meaning":"被設計成像……","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative interviews are designed to resemble casual conversations.","zh":"定性訪談被設計成像閒談。"},{"en":"To be designed to resemble something means to be planned to look or feel like it.","zh":"be designed to resemble something 指被規劃成看起來或感覺像某物。"},{"en":"A learning app may be designed to resemble a game so children feel relaxed.","zh":"學習應用程式可能被設計成像遊戲，讓孩子感到放鬆。"},{"en":"If interviews resemble conversations, participants may speak more naturally.","zh":"如果訪談像對話，參與者可能說得更自然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intentional similarity in design.","zh":"這個短語描述設計上的刻意相似。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"resemble casual conversations","meaning":"像閒談","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative interviews often resemble casual conversations.","zh":"定性訪談通常像閒談。"},{"en":"To resemble casual conversations means to sound relaxed, open, and natural like everyday talk.","zh":"resemble casual conversations 指聽起來像日常對話般放鬆、開放和自然。"},{"en":"A teacher’s informal chat with a student may resemble a casual conversation more than an interview.","zh":"老師與學生的非正式交談，可能比訪談更像閒談。"},{"en":"When interviews resemble casual conversations, participants may share richer stories.","zh":"當訪談像閒談，參與者可能分享更豐富的故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an interview style that feels less formal.","zh":"這個短語描述感覺較不正式的訪談風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"primary forms of data analysis","meaning":"主要數據分析形式","examples":[{"en":"The primary forms of data analysis are verbal descriptions and explanations.","zh":"主要數據分析形式是文字描述和解釋。"},{"en":"Primary forms of data analysis are the main ways researchers examine and explain their data.","zh":"primary forms of data analysis 指研究人員檢視和解釋數據的主要方式。"},{"en":"In qualitative research, the primary forms of analysis may be themes, descriptions, and interpretations.","zh":"在定性研究中，主要分析形式可能是主題、描述和詮釋。"},{"en":"The main analysis method affects how findings are presented to readers.","zh":"主要分析方法會影響研究結果如何呈現給讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the most important analysis methods used.","zh":"這個短語指出所使用的最重要分析方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"verbal descriptions and explanations","meaning":"文字描述和解釋","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative analysis includes verbal descriptions and explanations.","zh":"定性分析包括文字描述和解釋。"},{"en":"Verbal descriptions and explanations are written or spoken accounts that describe what happened and explain its meaning.","zh":"verbal descriptions and explanations 指以書面或口頭方式描述發生了甚麼並解釋其意義。"},{"en":"A researcher may use verbal descriptions and explanations to show how students negotiate group roles.","zh":"研究人員可能使用文字描述和解釋，展示學生如何協商小組角色。"},{"en":"Words can capture context and meaning that numbers alone may not show.","zh":"文字可以捕捉數字 alone 可能不能顯示的情境和意義。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to word-based analysis.","zh":"這個短語指基於文字的分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"involve explicit interpretations of","meaning":"涉及對……作明確詮釋","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative analysis involves explicit interpretations of human behaviour.","zh":"定性分析涉及對人類行為作明確詮釋。"},{"en":"To involve explicit interpretations of something means to include clear explanations of what it means.","zh":"involve explicit interpretations of something 指包括對某事意義的清楚解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher’s report may involve explicit interpretations of why a student avoids speaking in class.","zh":"老師報告可能涉及對學生為何避免在課堂發言作明確詮釋。"},{"en":"Explicit interpretation helps readers understand the meaning behind observed actions.","zh":"明確詮釋幫助讀者理解觀察到的行動背後的意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes analysis that openly explains behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述公開解釋行為的分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"meanings and functions","meaning":"意義和功能","examples":[{"en":"Researchers interpret the meanings and functions of human behaviours.","zh":"研究人員詮釋人類行為的意義和功能。"},{"en":"Meanings and functions are what behaviours signify and what purposes they serve.","zh":"meanings and functions 指行為代表甚麼，以及它們有甚麼用途。"},{"en":"A student’s silence may have different meanings and functions: confusion, politeness, fear, or careful listening.","zh":"學生沉默可能有不同意義和功能：混亂、禮貌、害怕或仔細聆聽。"},{"en":"Understanding meaning and function prevents researchers from judging behaviour too quickly.","zh":"理解意義和功能可以防止研究人員太快判斷行為。"},{"en":"This phrase asks both what an action means and what it does.","zh":"這個短語同時問一個行動代表甚麼，以及它起甚麼作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"human behaviours","meaning":"人類行為","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative researchers interpret human behaviours.","zh":"定性研究人員詮釋人類行為。"},{"en":"Human behaviours are the actions, reactions, habits, and choices people show in social life.","zh":"human behaviours 指人們在社會生活中表現出的行動、反應、習慣和選擇。"},{"en":"A child raising a hand, avoiding eye contact, or helping a classmate are human behaviours.","zh":"孩子舉手、避免眼神接觸或幫助同學，都是人類行為。"},{"en":"Human behaviours often need interpretation because the same action can mean different things.","zh":"人類行為通常需要詮釋，因為同一行動可以有不同意思。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what people do and how those actions may be understood.","zh":"這個短語著重人們做甚麼，以及這些行動可以如何被理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"at most","meaning":"最多；充其量","examples":[{"en":"At most, statistical analysis plays a subordinate role in qualitative research.","zh":"在定性研究中，統計分析最多只扮演次要角色。"},{"en":"At most means no more than this, or only to this limited degree.","zh":"at most 指不超過這個程度，或只到這個有限程度。"},{"en":"The walk to school takes ten minutes at most if there is no traffic.","zh":"如果沒有交通阻塞，步行到學校最多需十分鐘。"},{"en":"This phrase limits the importance, number, or amount of something.","zh":"這個短語限制某事的重要性、數量或程度。"},{"en":"It often suggests that something has only a small role.","zh":"它常暗示某事只具小角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"quantification","meaning":"量化","examples":[{"en":"Quantification plays only a limited role in qualitative research.","zh":"量化在定性研究中只扮演有限角色。"},{"en":"Quantification is the process of turning information into numbers or measurable quantities.","zh":"quantification 指把資料轉化成數字或可量度數量的過程。"},{"en":"A teacher uses quantification when counting how many students submitted homework late.","zh":"老師計算有多少學生遲交功課時，就是在使用量化。"},{"en":"Quantification can make patterns visible, but it may not explain why people behave that way.","zh":"量化可以令模式可見，但未必解釋人們為何那樣行動。"},{"en":"This word refers to making something numerical.","zh":"這個詞指把某事數字化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"statistical analysis","meaning":"統計分析","examples":[{"en":"Statistical analysis plays a subordinate role in qualitative research.","zh":"統計分析在定性研究中扮演次要角色。"},{"en":"Statistical analysis is the use of numbers and calculations to find patterns in data.","zh":"statistical analysis 指使用數字和計算在數據中找出模式。"},{"en":"A school may use statistical analysis to compare exam results across different classes.","zh":"學校可能使用統計分析比較不同班級的考試結果。"},{"en":"Statistical analysis can show what is common, but it may not show personal meaning.","zh":"統計分析可以顯示甚麼常見，但未必顯示個人意義。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to analysing data with statistics.","zh":"這個短語指用統計方法分析數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"play a subordinate role","meaning":"扮演次要角色","examples":[{"en":"Quantification and statistical analysis play a subordinate role.","zh":"量化和統計分析扮演次要角色。"},{"en":"To play a subordinate role means to be less important than other parts of a process.","zh":"play a subordinate role 指在某過程中不如其他部分重要。"},{"en":"In a drama performance, lighting may play a subordinate role to the actors’ dialogue.","zh":"在戲劇表演中，燈光可能相對演員對白扮演次要角色。"},{"en":"In qualitative research, numbers may support the analysis but not lead it.","zh":"在定性研究中，數字可能支援分析，但不主導分析。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a secondary function.","zh":"這個短語描述次要功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the sociology of education","meaning":"教育社會學","examples":[{"en":"The sociology of education was one area where qualitative research developed strongly.","zh":"教育社會學是定性研究大力發展的其中一個範疇。"},{"en":"The sociology of education studies how schools, families, class, culture, and society affect learning.","zh":"sociology of education 研究學校、家庭、階級、文化和社會如何影響學習。"},{"en":"A researcher in the sociology of education may study how social class influences school choices.","zh":"教育社會學研究人員可能研究社會階級如何影響學校選擇。"},{"en":"This field looks beyond individual ability to examine social patterns and inequality.","zh":"這個領域看超越個人能力，檢視社會模式和不平等。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the social study of education.","zh":"這個短語指對教育作社會層面的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"evaluation studies","meaning":"評估研究","examples":[{"en":"Evaluation studies also contributed to the development of qualitative methodologies.","zh":"評估研究也促成定性研究方法的發展。"},{"en":"Evaluation studies are research projects that judge whether a programme, policy, or method works well.","zh":"evaluation studies 指判斷某計劃、政策或方法是否有效的研究項目。"},{"en":"A school may conduct evaluation studies after introducing a new reading scheme.","zh":"學校可能在引入新閱讀計劃後進行評估研究。"},{"en":"Evaluation studies can use interviews and observations to explain why a programme succeeds or fails.","zh":"評估研究可以使用訪談和觀察來解釋計劃為何成功或失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to research that assesses effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語指評估成效的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"initially emerge","meaning":"最初出現","examples":[{"en":"Criticism of quantitative research initially emerged in these areas.","zh":"對定量研究的批評最初在這些範疇出現。"},{"en":"To initially emerge means to first appear or become noticeable.","zh":"initially emerge 指最初出現或變得明顯。"},{"en":"A problem with a school app may initially emerge when students try to submit homework.","zh":"學校應用程式的問題可能在學生嘗試交功課時最初出現。"},{"en":"Early criticism often shows where later debates will develop.","zh":"早期批評通常顯示後來爭論會在哪裡發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first appearance of an idea, problem, or trend.","zh":"這個短語描述想法、問題或趨勢的首次出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in the most intense way","meaning":"以最強烈的方式","examples":[{"en":"The criticism emerged in the most intense way in two research areas.","zh":"這項批評以最強烈的方式在兩個研究範疇中出現。"},{"en":"In the most intense way means with the greatest strength, force, or seriousness.","zh":"in the most intense way 指以最大力度、強度或嚴重程度。"},{"en":"Exam pressure may appear in the most intense way among students preparing for public exams.","zh":"考試壓力可能在準備公開考試的學生中以最強烈的方式出現。"},{"en":"When criticism is intense, it usually signals a major disagreement or problem.","zh":"當批評強烈，通常表示有重大分歧或問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the strongest form of a trend or reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述趨勢或反應的最強形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a series of studies","meaning":"一系列研究","examples":[{"en":"A series of studies in British schools marked the beginning of a trend.","zh":"一系列在英國學校進行的研究標誌着一個趨勢的開始。"},{"en":"A series of studies means several related research projects carried out over time.","zh":"series of studies 指隨時間進行的幾項相關研究。"},{"en":"A university may conduct a series of studies on how homework affects sleep.","zh":"大學可能就功課如何影響睡眠進行一系列研究。"},{"en":"Several studies together can provide stronger evidence than one study alone.","zh":"幾項研究合起來可以比單一研究提供更強證據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to connected research works.","zh":"這個短語指互相關連的研究作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a boys’ grammar school","meaning":"男子文法學校","examples":[{"en":"Lacey studied a boys’ grammar school in Britain.","zh":"Lacey 研究了一所英國男子文法學校。"},{"en":"A boys’ grammar school is a selective secondary school for boys, often with an academic focus.","zh":"boys’ grammar school 指供男生就讀、通常重視學術並具選拔性的中學。"},{"en":"A researcher may study a boys’ grammar school to understand how selection affects student identity.","zh":"研究人員可能研究男子文法學校，以理解選拔如何影響學生身份。"},{"en":"The school type can shape friendships, competition, and classroom culture.","zh":"學校類型可以塑造友誼、競爭和課室文化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific kind of British school.","zh":"這個短語指英國一種特定學校。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a boys’ secondary modern school","meaning":"男子現代中學","examples":[{"en":"The research included a boys’ secondary modern school.","zh":"這項研究包括一所男子現代中學。"},{"en":"A boys’ secondary modern school was a British school type for boys who did not attend grammar schools.","zh":"boys’ secondary modern school 指英國一種供未入讀文法學校的男生就讀的學校類型。"},{"en":"A researcher may compare a boys’ secondary modern school with a grammar school to study social differences.","zh":"研究人員可能把男子現代中學與文法學校比較，以研究社會差異。"},{"en":"Different school types can create different expectations for students.","zh":"不同學校類型可以為學生創造不同期望。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a historically specific British secondary school.","zh":"這個短語指英國歷史上一種特定中學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a girls’ grammar school","meaning":"女子文法學校","examples":[{"en":"The researchers also studied a girls’ grammar school.","zh":"研究人員也研究了一所女子文法學校。"},{"en":"A girls’ grammar school is a selective secondary school for girls, usually with a strong academic focus.","zh":"girls’ grammar school 指供女生就讀、通常重視學術並具選拔性的中學。"},{"en":"Researchers may study a girls’ grammar school to examine friendship, achievement, and gender expectations.","zh":"研究人員可能研究女子文法學校，以檢視友誼、成就和性別期望。"},{"en":"Comparing different schools can show how school culture shapes student behaviour.","zh":"比較不同學校可以顯示學校文化如何塑造學生行為。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an academically selective girls’ school.","zh":"這個短語指具學術選拔性的女子學校。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"mark the beginning of","meaning":"標誌著……的開始","examples":[{"en":"These studies marked the beginning of the trend towards qualitative research.","zh":"這些研究標誌著走向定性研究趨勢的開始。"},{"en":"To mark the beginning of something means to signal the start of a new period, trend, or process.","zh":"mark the beginning of something 指標示一個新時期、趨勢或過程的開始。"},{"en":"A new school policy may mark the beginning of a more student-centred approach.","zh":"新校政可能標誌著更以學生為中心的取向開始。"},{"en":"Important early studies can mark the beginning of wider academic change.","zh":"重要的早期研究可以標誌著更廣泛學術變化的開始。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the starting point of a development.","zh":"這個短語突出某項發展的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the trend towards","meaning":"走向……的趨勢","examples":[{"en":"The studies marked the trend towards qualitative research in education.","zh":"這些研究標誌著教育中走向定性研究的趨勢。"},{"en":"The trend towards something is a general movement or shift in that direction.","zh":"trend towards something 指整體上朝某方向移動或轉變。"},{"en":"Many schools show a trend towards online homework and digital feedback.","zh":"許多學校顯示走向網上功課和數碼回饋的趨勢。"},{"en":"A trend becomes clear when more people or institutions begin to act similarly.","zh":"當更多人或機構開始相似地行動，趨勢就會變清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gradual movement toward a new pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步走向新模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"employ an approach","meaning":"採用一種方法","examples":[{"en":"The researchers employed an ethnographic approach.","zh":"研究人員採用了民族誌研究方法。"},{"en":"To employ an approach means to use a particular method or way of working.","zh":"employ an approach 指使用某種方法或工作方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may employ an approach that starts with examples before explaining grammar rules.","zh":"老師可能採用先用例子再解釋文法規則的方法。"},{"en":"The approach researchers employ shapes what kind of data they collect.","zh":"研究人員採用的方法會塑造他們收集哪種數據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing and using a method.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇並使用某方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"an ethnographic approach","meaning":"民族誌研究方法","examples":[{"en":"The researchers employed an ethnographic approach in schools.","zh":"研究人員在學校採用了民族誌研究方法。"},{"en":"An ethnographic approach studies people’s everyday lives, relationships, and meanings in a natural setting.","zh":"ethnographic approach 指在自然環境中研究人們的日常生活、關係和意義。"},{"en":"A researcher using an ethnographic approach may spend months observing one school community.","zh":"使用民族誌研究方法的研究人員，可能花數月觀察一個學校社群。"},{"en":"This approach can show classroom culture that test scores cannot capture.","zh":"這種方法可以顯示測驗分數不能捕捉的課室文化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a deep, field-based qualitative method.","zh":"這個短語指深入、以實地為本的定性方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"collect some quantitative data","meaning":"收集一些定量數據","examples":[{"en":"The researchers did also collect some quantitative data.","zh":"研究人員也確實收集了一些定量數據。"},{"en":"To collect some quantitative data means to gather some numerical information for analysis.","zh":"collect some quantitative data 指收集一些用於分析的數字資料。"},{"en":"A teacher may collect some quantitative data by counting how many students finish homework each week.","zh":"老師可能透過計算每週有多少學生完成功課來收集一些定量數據。"},{"en":"Quantitative data can support qualitative observations by adding measurable evidence.","zh":"定量數據可以透過加入可量度證據來支持定性觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that research methods can be mixed.","zh":"這個短語顯示研究方法可以混合使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"friendship patterns","meaning":"友誼模式","examples":[{"en":"The researchers collected data on friendship patterns among students.","zh":"研究人員收集關於學生之間友誼模式的數據。"},{"en":"Friendship patterns are regular ways in which friendships form, change, or group people together.","zh":"friendship patterns 指友誼形成、變化或把人分組的常見方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice friendship patterns when the same students always work together.","zh":"當同一批學生總是一起合作，老師可能注意到友誼模式。"},{"en":"Friendship patterns can affect classroom participation, confidence, and peer influence.","zh":"友誼模式可以影響課堂參與、自信和朋輩影響。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to repeated social connections among people.","zh":"這個短語指人與人之間反覆出現的社交連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"among the students","meaning":"在學生之間","examples":[{"en":"The study examined friendship patterns among the students.","zh":"這項研究檢視學生之間的友誼模式。"},{"en":"Among the students means within the group of students.","zh":"among the students 指在學生這個群體之中。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice strong teamwork among the students after several group projects.","zh":"幾次小組專題後，老師可能注意到學生之間有強烈團隊合作。"},{"en":"Studying what happens among students helps researchers understand peer relationships.","zh":"研究學生之間發生的事，幫助研究人員理解朋輩關係。"},{"en":"This phrase places an action or pattern inside the student group.","zh":"這個短語把行動或模式放在學生群體內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"observe lessons","meaning":"觀察課堂","examples":[{"en":"The researchers observed lessons in the schools.","zh":"研究人員在學校觀察課堂。"},{"en":"To observe lessons means to watch classroom teaching and learning carefully.","zh":"observe lessons 指仔細觀看課堂教學和學習。"},{"en":"A trainee teacher may observe lessons before teaching her own class.","zh":"見習老師可能在自己授課前觀察課堂。"},{"en":"Observing lessons can reveal interaction, silence, confusion, and cooperation.","zh":"觀察課堂可以揭示互動、沉默、混亂和合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes classroom observation.","zh":"這個短語描述課室觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"interview both…and…","meaning":"訪問……和……","examples":[{"en":"The researchers interviewed both the teachers and the students.","zh":"研究人員訪問了老師和學生。"},{"en":"Interview both…and… means ask questions to two different groups or people.","zh":"interview both…and… 指向兩個不同群體或人物提問。"},{"en":"A school survey may interview both parents and students before changing homework rules.","zh":"學校在改變功課規則前，可能訪問家長和學生。"},{"en":"Interviewing both sides gives a fuller picture of the situation.","zh":"訪問雙方可以提供更完整的情況。"},{"en":"This structure highlights that two groups are included.","zh":"這個結構突出兩個群體都被包括在內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"examine school records","meaning":"查閱學校紀錄","examples":[{"en":"The researchers examined school records.","zh":"研究人員查閱了學校紀錄。"},{"en":"To examine school records means to look carefully at documents such as attendance, grades, reports, or discipline notes.","zh":"examine school records 指仔細查看出席、成績、報告或紀律記錄等文件。"},{"en":"A researcher may examine school records to track changes in student achievement.","zh":"研究人員可能查閱學校紀錄，以追蹤學生學業表現的變化。"},{"en":"Records can provide background evidence that supports interviews and observations.","zh":"紀錄可以提供背景證據，支援訪談和觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to studying official school documents.","zh":"這個短語指研究正式學校文件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"for a considerable amount of time","meaning":"相當長一段時間","examples":[{"en":"The researchers studied the schools for a considerable amount of time.","zh":"研究人員研究這些學校相當長一段時間。"},{"en":"For a considerable amount of time means for a fairly long period.","zh":"for a considerable amount of time 指持續相當長的期間。"},{"en":"A student who practises speaking for a considerable amount of time usually becomes more fluent.","zh":"花相當長一段時間練習口語的學生，通常會變得更流利。"},{"en":"Long observation helps researchers notice changes that short visits may miss.","zh":"長時間觀察幫助研究人員注意到短暫探訪可能忽略的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the time spent was significant.","zh":"這個短語強調所花時間相當重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"spend many months doing","meaning":"花多個月做……","examples":[{"en":"The researchers spent many months gathering data.","zh":"研究人員花多個月收集數據。"},{"en":"To spend many months doing something means to use a long period of several months on that activity.","zh":"spend many months doing something 指用幾個月的長時間做某活動。"},{"en":"A student may spend many months preparing for a public exam.","zh":"學生可能花多個月準備公開考試。"},{"en":"Long-term work can produce deeper understanding than a quick survey.","zh":"長期工作可以比快速調查產生更深入理解。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights effort over an extended period.","zh":"這個短語突出長時間付出的努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"gather data","meaning":"收集數據","examples":[{"en":"The researchers spent many months gathering data.","zh":"研究人員花多個月收集數據。"},{"en":"To gather data means to collect information for study or analysis.","zh":"gather data 指收集用於研究或分析的資料。"},{"en":"A teacher may gather data by recording students’ reading speed every month.","zh":"老師可能透過每月記錄學生閱讀速度來收集數據。"},{"en":"Good data collection helps researchers support their claims with evidence.","zh":"良好的數據收集幫助研究人員用證據支持其聲稱。"},{"en":"This phrase is a general term for collecting research information.","zh":"這個短語是收集研究資料的一般說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"track changes over time","meaning":"追蹤隨時間出現的變化","examples":[{"en":"The researchers tracked changes over time.","zh":"研究人員追蹤隨時間出現的變化。"},{"en":"To track changes over time means to follow how something develops across days, months, or years.","zh":"track changes over time 指跟進某事在數日、數月或數年中如何發展。"},{"en":"A school may track changes over time in students’ reading scores.","zh":"學校可能追蹤學生閱讀分數隨時間出現的變化。"},{"en":"Tracking change helps researchers see development rather than only one moment.","zh":"追蹤變化幫助研究人員看見發展，而不只是某一刻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-term monitoring.","zh":"這個短語描述長期監察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"look at the following statements","meaning":"查看以下陳述","examples":[{"en":"Students look at the following statements and match them with people.","zh":"學生查看以下陳述，並把它們與人物配對。"},{"en":"To look at the following statements means to read the statements that come next in the question.","zh":"look at the following statements 指閱讀題目接下來列出的陳述。"},{"en":"In an exam, students should look at the following statements before returning to the passage.","zh":"在考試中，學生應先查看以下陳述，再回到文章。"},{"en":"Reading the statements first helps students know what information to search for.","zh":"先閱讀陳述有助學生知道要搜尋甚麼資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"statements or descriptions","meaning":"陳述或描述","examples":[{"en":"The task includes statements or descriptions about the passage.","zh":"任務包括關於文章的陳述或描述。"},{"en":"Statements or descriptions are sentences that give information, opinions, or details to be matched or checked.","zh":"statements or descriptions 指提供資料、意見或細節並需要配對或核對的句子。"},{"en":"A reading task may include statements or descriptions about different researchers.","zh":"閱讀任務可能包括關於不同研究人員的陳述或描述。"},{"en":"Students must read carefully because small wording differences can change the answer.","zh":"學生必須仔細閱讀，因為細微措辭差異可以改變答案。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to written items in a matching or comprehension task.","zh":"這個短語指配對或理解題中的書面項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"list of people","meaning":"人物列表","examples":[{"en":"The question provides a list of people.","zh":"題目提供一個人物列表。"},{"en":"A list of people is a group of names given as answer options.","zh":"list of people 指作為答案選項提供的一組姓名。"},{"en":"In a matching task, a list of people may include researchers, writers, or speakers.","zh":"在配對題中，人物列表可能包括研究人員、作者或講者。"},{"en":"Students use the list to decide who said, believed, or did each thing.","zh":"學生使用列表判斷每件事是誰說、相信或做的。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to named options in a question.","zh":"這個短語指題目中的具名選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"match each statement with","meaning":"將每項陳述與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match each statement with the correct person.","zh":"學生將每項陳述與正確人物配對。"},{"en":"To match each statement with something means to connect every sentence to the option that fits it.","zh":"match each statement with something 指把每句陳述連接到符合它的選項。"},{"en":"Students may match each statement with the paragraph where the idea appears.","zh":"學生可能將每項陳述與出現該想法的段落配對。"},{"en":"Matching requires careful reading because several options may look similar.","zh":"配對需要仔細閱讀，因為幾個選項可能看起來相似。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common reading-test task.","zh":"這個短語描述常見閱讀測驗任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the correct person or people","meaning":"正確人物","examples":[{"en":"Each statement must be matched with the correct person or people.","zh":"每項陳述必須與正確人物配對。"},{"en":"The correct person or people means the name or names that match the information in the passage.","zh":"correct person or people 指與文章資料相符的一個或多個姓名。"},{"en":"A question may require the correct person or people if two researchers share the same view.","zh":"如果兩名研究人員持相同觀點，題目可能要求選出正確人物。"},{"en":"Students should check the text carefully before choosing a name.","zh":"學生在選擇姓名前應仔細核對文章。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the right answer in a people-matching task.","zh":"這個短語指出人物配對題中的正確答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"use any letter more than once","meaning":"可重複使用任何字母","examples":[{"en":"Students may use any letter more than once.","zh":"學生可重複使用任何字母。"},{"en":"Use any letter more than once means the same answer option can be chosen for several questions.","zh":"use any letter more than once 指同一答案選項可以用於幾條題目。"},{"en":"In a matching task, one paragraph letter may be used more than once if it contains several details.","zh":"在配對題中，如果同一段包含幾個細節，一個段落字母可以被重複使用。"},{"en":"Students should not avoid repeating a letter if the passage supports it.","zh":"如果文章支持，學生不應避免重複字母。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction about answer reuse.","zh":"這個短語是關於答案可否重用的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"indicate a child’s perspective","meaning":"顯示孩子的觀點","examples":[{"en":"A wrong answer may indicate a child’s different perspective.","zh":"錯誤答案可能顯示孩子的不同觀點。"},{"en":"To indicate a child’s perspective means to show how the child sees or understands the situation.","zh":"indicate a child’s perspective 指顯示孩子如何看待或理解情況。"},{"en":"A drawing of a noisy classroom may indicate a child’s perspective on school stress.","zh":"一幅嘈吵課室的圖畫可能顯示孩子對學校壓力的觀點。"},{"en":"Children’s answers can reveal their viewpoint, not only their knowledge level.","zh":"兒童的答案可以揭示他們的觀點，而不只是知識水平。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain why an answer may be meaningful even if it is marked wrong.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋為何答案即使被評為錯誤，也可能有意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"different perspective","meaning":"不同角度；不同觀點","examples":[{"en":"The child’s answer may reflect a different perspective.","zh":"孩子的答案可能反映不同角度。"},{"en":"A different perspective is another way of seeing, understanding, or interpreting something.","zh":"different perspective 指另一種看待、理解或詮釋某事的方式。"},{"en":"A parent and a teacher may have a different perspective on the same homework problem.","zh":"家長和老師可能對同一個功課問題有不同觀點。"},{"en":"Different perspectives can make communication richer but also more difficult.","zh":"不同觀點可以令溝通更豐富，但也更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an alternative viewpoint.","zh":"這個短語描述另一種看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"inability to reason","meaning":"推理能力不足","examples":[{"en":"A wrong answer does not always show an inability to reason.","zh":"錯誤答案不一定顯示推理能力不足。"},{"en":"Inability to reason means a lack of ability to think logically and draw sensible conclusions.","zh":"inability to reason 指缺乏有邏輯地思考並得出合理結論的能力。"},{"en":"A child may seem to show inability to reason if the question uses unfamiliar words.","zh":"如果題目使用陌生詞語，孩子可能看似顯示推理能力不足。"},{"en":"Before assuming inability, teachers should check understanding, motivation, and context.","zh":"在假設能力不足前，老師應檢查理解、動機和情境。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to weak logical thinking, but it should be used carefully.","zh":"這個短語指邏輯思考薄弱，但應小心使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"logical reasoning involved in","meaning":"……所涉及的邏輯推理","examples":[{"en":"The logical reasoning involved in the task may be difficult for young children.","zh":"任務所涉及的邏輯推理對年幼兒童來說可能很困難。"},{"en":"Logical reasoning involved in something means the thinking steps required by that activity.","zh":"logical reasoning involved in something 指某活動所需要的思考步驟。"},{"en":"The logical reasoning involved in a timetable question may include comparing times and routes.","zh":"時間表題所涉及的邏輯推理可能包括比較時間和路線。"},{"en":"If the reasoning involved is too advanced, students may need more support.","zh":"如果所涉及的推理太高階，學生可能需要更多支援。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the thinking demands of a task.","zh":"這個短語指出任務的思考要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be beyond","meaning":"超出……範圍","examples":[{"en":"The task may be beyond the children’s stage of cognitive development.","zh":"該任務可能超出兒童認知發展階段的範圍。"},{"en":"To be beyond something means to be too advanced, difficult, or outside its limit.","zh":"be beyond something 指太高階、太困難或超出其限制。"},{"en":"This grammar exercise may be beyond beginners if it uses too many abstract nouns.","zh":"如果文法練習使用太多抽象名詞，可能超出初學者範圍。"},{"en":"If a task is beyond students’ level, wrong answers may not reflect laziness.","zh":"如果任務超出學生水平，錯誤答案未必反映懶惰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something exceeding a person’s current ability or stage.","zh":"這個短語描述某事超出某人目前能力或階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"stage of cognitive development","meaning":"認知發展階段","examples":[{"en":"Children’s answers may depend on their stage of cognitive development.","zh":"兒童的答案可能取決於他們的認知發展階段。"},{"en":"A stage of cognitive development is a level in the growth of thinking and reasoning ability.","zh":"stage of cognitive development 指思考和推理能力成長中的某個水平。"},{"en":"A young child’s stage of cognitive development may affect how she understands quantity or fairness.","zh":"年幼孩子的認知發展階段可能影響她如何理解數量或公平。"},{"en":"Teaching works better when tasks match students’ developmental stage.","zh":"當任務配合學生的發展階段，教學效果會更好。"},{"en":"This phrase links children’s thinking ability to their age and growth.","zh":"這個短語把兒童思考能力與年齡和成長連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"reluctance to follow the rules","meaning":"不願跟從規則","examples":[{"en":"Children’s reluctance to follow the rules may affect the experiment.","zh":"兒童不願跟從規則可能影響實驗。"},{"en":"Reluctance to follow the rules means unwillingness to obey the rules or cooperate with the task.","zh":"reluctance to follow the rules 指不願意遵守規則或配合任務。"},{"en":"A student’s reluctance to follow the rules may come from embarrassment, boredom, or distrust.","zh":"學生不願跟從規則可能源於尷尬、沉悶或不信任。"},{"en":"Reluctance can change test results because participants may not show their true ability.","zh":"不願配合可以改變測驗結果，因為參與者可能沒有顯示真實能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unwillingness, not inability.","zh":"這個短語描述不願意，而不是能力不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"miscommunication","meaning":"溝通失誤","examples":[{"en":"Miscommunication may be another explanation for the results.","zh":"溝通失誤可能是結果的另一個解釋。"},{"en":"Miscommunication happens when people fail to understand one another clearly.","zh":"miscommunication 指人們未能清楚理解彼此時發生的情況。"},{"en":"A student may submit the wrong homework because of miscommunication about the deadline.","zh":"學生可能因為對截止日期的溝通失誤而交錯功課。"},{"en":"Miscommunication can make a correct thinker give an answer that looks wrong.","zh":"溝通失誤可以令一個思考正確的人給出看似錯誤的答案。"},{"en":"This word describes problems caused by unclear or misunderstood communication.","zh":"這個詞描述由不清楚或被誤解的溝通造成的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"another explanation","meaning":"另一個解釋","examples":[{"en":"Critics suggest another explanation for the children’s answers.","zh":"批評者提出兒童答案的另一個解釋。"},{"en":"Another explanation is a different reason that may account for the same result.","zh":"another explanation 指可以解釋同一結果的不同原因。"},{"en":"If a student fails a test, another explanation may be illness rather than lack of study.","zh":"如果學生測驗不合格，另一個解釋可能是生病，而不是沒有溫習。"},{"en":"Considering another explanation prevents people from jumping to one conclusion too quickly.","zh":"考慮另一個解釋可以防止人們太快跳到單一結論。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an alternative cause or interpretation.","zh":"這個短語引入替代成因或詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"evidence of","meaning":"……的證據","examples":[{"en":"The study provides evidence of a qualitative approach to research.","zh":"這項研究提供定性研究取向的證據。"},{"en":"Evidence of something is information that shows or supports the existence of that thing.","zh":"evidence of something 指顯示或支持某事存在的資料。"},{"en":"Detailed classroom notes can provide evidence of how students actually interact.","zh":"詳細課室筆記可以提供學生實際如何互動的證據。"},{"en":"Evidence helps researchers move from opinion to supported argument.","zh":"證據幫助研究人員由意見走向有支持的論點。"},{"en":"This phrase points to proof or support for a claim.","zh":"這個短語指支持某聲稱的證明或資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"systematic observation approach","meaning":"系統性觀察方法","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions a systematic observation approach to research.","zh":"題目提到一種研究中的系統性觀察方法。"},{"en":"A systematic observation approach is a planned method of watching and recording behaviour in organised categories.","zh":"systematic observation approach 指以有計劃方式觀察並按有組織類別記錄行為的方法。"},{"en":"A researcher may use a systematic observation approach to count how often teachers ask open questions.","zh":"研究人員可能使用系統性觀察方法，計算老師有多常提出開放式問題。"},{"en":"This approach produces structured data, but it may miss unexpected meanings.","zh":"這種方法產生結構化數據，但可能漏掉意想不到的意義。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised observation as a research method.","zh":"這個短語指作為研究方法的有組織觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"a flaw in","meaning":"……中的缺陷","examples":[{"en":"There may be a flaw in experiments on children’s language development.","zh":"關於兒童語言發展的實驗中可能有缺陷。"},{"en":"A flaw in something is a weakness, mistake, or problem in its design or reasoning.","zh":"flaw in something 指某物設計或推理中的弱點、錯誤或問題。"},{"en":"A flaw in a survey may be that the questions are too leading.","zh":"問卷中的缺陷可能是問題太具引導性。"},{"en":"If a flaw is serious, the conclusion may become unreliable.","zh":"如果缺陷嚴重，結論可能變得不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a problem inside a method, plan, or argument.","zh":"這個短語指出方法、計劃或論點內部的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"experiments on children’s language development","meaning":"關於兒童語言發展的實驗","examples":[{"en":"Mehan criticised experiments on children’s language development.","zh":"Mehan 批評關於兒童語言發展的實驗。"},{"en":"Experiments on children’s language development are studies testing how children understand, use, or learn language.","zh":"experiments on children’s language development 指測試兒童如何理解、使用或學習語言的研究。"},{"en":"Such experiments may ask children to name pictures, repeat sounds, or choose letters.","zh":"這類實驗可能要求兒童命名圖片、重複聲音或選擇字母。"},{"en":"If the task is culturally confusing, it may not measure language development fairly.","zh":"如果任務在文化上令人混淆，它可能不能公平衡量語言發展。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to research on children’s growing language ability.","zh":"這個短語指關於兒童語言能力成長的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"complete the sentences below","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the sentences below with words from the passage.","zh":"學生用文章中的詞語完成以下句子。"},{"en":"To complete the sentences below means to fill in missing words in the sentences that follow.","zh":"complete the sentences below 指填入接下來句子中的缺失詞語。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete the sentences below by copying suitable words from the text.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過從文本抄寫合適詞語完成以下句子。"},{"en":"Students must check grammar because the answer must fit the sentence.","zh":"學生必須檢查文法，因為答案必須配合句子。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不超過兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Students must choose no more than two words from the passage.","zh":"學生必須從文章中選擇不超過兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer can contain one or two words, but not three.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案可以有一個或兩個詞，但不能有三個。"},{"en":"If the correct answer is “field notes,” it follows the rule because it has two words.","zh":"如果正確答案是 “field notes”，它符合規則，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing extra words can make an answer wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，多寫字也可能令答案錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit in reading tasks.","zh":"這個短語在閱讀任務中給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"identify the word beginning with","meaning":"辨認以……開首的字","examples":[{"en":"The children failed to identify the word beginning with C.","zh":"兒童未能辨認以 C 開首的字。"},{"en":"To identify the word beginning with a letter means to recognise which word starts with that letter.","zh":"identify the word beginning with a letter 指辨認哪個詞以該字母開始。"},{"en":"A child may identify the word beginning with B when shown pictures of a ball, cat, and dog.","zh":"當看到球、貓和狗的圖片，孩子可能辨認以 B 開首的字。"},{"en":"If the child names the picture differently, the expected initial letter may change.","zh":"如果孩子以不同方式命名圖片，預期的開首字母可能會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a phonics or early reading task.","zh":"這個短語描述拼音或早期閱讀任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the flaw could be rectified by","meaning":"可透過……糾正缺陷","examples":[{"en":"Some scholars believed the flaw could be rectified by better experiments.","zh":"有些學者相信該缺陷可透過更好的實驗糾正。"},{"en":"The flaw could be rectified by means the weakness could be corrected through a particular method.","zh":"the flaw could be rectified by 指弱點可以透過某方法被修正。"},{"en":"A confusing worksheet flaw could be rectified by clearer examples and simpler instructions.","zh":"令人混淆的工作紙缺陷可以透過更清楚例子和更簡單指示糾正。"},{"en":"If the problem is technical, better design may repair it.","zh":"如果問題是技術性的，更好設計可能能修補它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a weakness might be fixed.","zh":"這個短語描述缺陷可以如何被修正。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be rectified by","meaning":"可透過……糾正","examples":[{"en":"The flaw could be rectified by more rigorous experimentation.","zh":"該缺陷可透過更嚴謹的實驗糾正。"},{"en":"To be rectified by something means to be corrected or fixed through it.","zh":"be rectified by something 指透過某事被糾正或修正。"},{"en":"A timetable error can be rectified by sending students a revised version.","zh":"時間表錯誤可以透過向學生發送修訂版糾正。"},{"en":"Some research problems can be rectified by clearer questions and better controls.","zh":"有些研究問題可以透過更清楚問題和更好控制糾正。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and means being corrected.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是被修正。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"choose three letters","meaning":"選出三個字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose three letters from the options.","zh":"學生從選項中選出三個字母。"},{"en":"Choose three letters means select three answer options labelled by letters.","zh":"choose three letters 指選出三個以字母標示的答案選項。"},{"en":"In IELTS reading, students may choose three letters from A to F.","zh":"在 IELTS 閱讀中，學生可能從 A 至 F 選出三個字母。"},{"en":"Students should choose only three letters even if more options look possible.","zh":"即使更多選項看似可能，學生也應只選三個字母。"},{"en":"This phrase is a multiple-answer exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是多答案考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"characteristics of qualitative research","meaning":"定性研究的特點","examples":[{"en":"The list includes characteristics of qualitative research.","zh":"列表包括定性研究的特點。"},{"en":"Characteristics of qualitative research are features that commonly describe qualitative methods.","zh":"characteristics of qualitative research 指通常描述定性方法的特徵。"},{"en":"Open-ended questions, field notes, and detailed descriptions are characteristics of qualitative research.","zh":"開放式問題、實地筆記和詳細描述都是定性研究的特點。"},{"en":"Knowing these characteristics helps students distinguish qualitative from quantitative research.","zh":"認識這些特點幫助學生區分定性研究和定量研究。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to typical features of qualitative study.","zh":"這個短語指定性研究的典型特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be mentioned by the writer","meaning":"由作者提及","examples":[{"en":"Some characteristics are mentioned by the writer of the passage.","zh":"有些特點由文章作者提及。"},{"en":"To be mentioned by the writer means to be stated or referred to in the text.","zh":"be mentioned by the writer 指在文本中被作者說明或提到。"},{"en":"An answer is safer if it is mentioned by the writer rather than guessed from background knowledge.","zh":"如果答案由作者提及，而不是由背景知識猜出，會較安全。"},{"en":"Reading questions often ask students to choose only ideas mentioned in the passage.","zh":"閱讀題常要求學生只選文章中提及的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase points to information that appears in the text.","zh":"這個短語指文本中出現的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"in terms of","meaning":"按照；從……方面","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers code behaviour in terms of predefined categories.","zh":"有些研究人員按照預先設定的類別將行為編碼。"},{"en":"In terms of means according to or from the viewpoint of a particular feature.","zh":"in terms of 指按照某特徵或從某角度來看。"},{"en":"A student may compare two schools in terms of location, fees, and teaching style.","zh":"學生可能從地點、學費和教學風格方面比較兩所學校。"},{"en":"This phrase helps specify the basis of comparison or analysis.","zh":"這個短語幫助明確比較或分析的基準。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining how something is judged.","zh":"它在解釋某事如何被判斷時很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"well-organised data","meaning":"組織良好的數據","examples":[{"en":"Well-organised data are usually easier to analyse quantitatively.","zh":"組織良好的數據通常較容易作定量分析。"},{"en":"Well-organised data are information arranged clearly into categories, tables, or usable formats.","zh":"well-organised data 指清楚安排成類別、表格或可用格式的資料。"},{"en":"A teacher has well-organised data if each student’s marks are recorded by date and skill.","zh":"如果每名學生的分數都按日期和技能記錄，老師就有組織良好的數據。"},{"en":"Organised data saves time and reduces mistakes during analysis.","zh":"組織良好的數據在分析時節省時間並減少錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes data that are tidy and ready to use.","zh":"這個短語描述整齊且可使用的數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"analytical categories","meaning":"分析類別","examples":[{"en":"Researchers may organise data into analytical categories.","zh":"研究人員可能把數據整理成分析類別。"},{"en":"Analytical categories are labels used to sort information for study and interpretation.","zh":"analytical categories 指用來分類資料以便研究和詮釋的標籤。"},{"en":"In a classroom study, analytical categories might include “teacher question,” “student response,” and “peer support.”","zh":"在課室研究中，分析類別可能包括「老師提問」、「學生回應」和「朋輩支援」。"},{"en":"Good categories help researchers compare patterns across many examples.","zh":"良好類別幫助研究人員比較許多例子中的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to classification tools used in analysis.","zh":"這個短語指分析中使用的分類工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"detailed data","meaning":"詳細數據","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative researchers often collect detailed data.","zh":"定性研究人員常收集詳細數據。"},{"en":"Detailed data include rich information with context, description, and specific examples.","zh":"detailed data 指帶有情境、描述和具體例子的豐富資料。"},{"en":"A researcher may collect detailed data by recording not only what students say but also when and how they say it.","zh":"研究人員可能不只記錄學生說甚麼，也記錄何時和如何說，從而收集詳細數據。"},{"en":"Detailed data help explain meaning, but they may take longer to analyse.","zh":"詳細數據幫助解釋意義，但可能需要更長時間分析。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to information with depth and context.","zh":"這個短語指有深度和情境的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"questionnaire data","meaning":"問卷數據","examples":[{"en":"Questionnaire data can be useful in quantitative research.","zh":"問卷數據在定量研究中可以有用。"},{"en":"Questionnaire data are answers collected from people through written or online survey questions.","zh":"questionnaire data 指透過書面或網上調查問題向人們收集的答案。"},{"en":"A school may collect questionnaire data from parents about homework pressure.","zh":"學校可能向家長收集關於功課壓力的問卷數據。"},{"en":"Questionnaire data are easy to count when the questions use fixed answer choices.","zh":"當問題使用固定答案選項，問卷數據較容易計算。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to survey-based information.","zh":"這個短語指基於問卷的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"ask for open-ended answers","meaning":"要求開放式答案","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative researchers ask for open-ended answers in interviews.","zh":"定性研究人員在訪談中要求開放式答案。"},{"en":"To ask for open-ended answers means to invite people to answer freely in their own words.","zh":"ask for open-ended answers 指邀請人們用自己的話自由回答。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask for open-ended answers when asking students how they feel about group work.","zh":"老師問學生對小組活動的感受時，可能要求開放式答案。"},{"en":"Open-ended answers can reveal reasons and examples that fixed options would hide.","zh":"開放式答案可以揭示固定選項會隱藏的原因和例子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a flexible questioning style.","zh":"這個短語描述靈活的提問方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"research setting","meaning":"研究場景","examples":[{"en":"Researchers may record the research setting during observation.","zh":"研究人員可能在觀察期間記錄研究場景。"},{"en":"A research setting is the place and situation where a study takes place.","zh":"research setting 指研究發生的地方和情況。"},{"en":"In a classroom study, the research setting includes the room, seating plan, lesson type, and social atmosphere.","zh":"在課室研究中，研究場景包括房間、座位安排、課堂類型和社交氣氛。"},{"en":"The setting matters because behaviour changes in different environments.","zh":"場景很重要，因為行為會在不同環境中改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the context in which research happens.","zh":"這個短語指研究發生的背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"take notes","meaning":"做筆記","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative researchers take notes while observing participants.","zh":"定性研究人員在觀察參與者時做筆記。"},{"en":"To take notes means to write down important information while listening, reading, or watching.","zh":"take notes 指在聆聽、閱讀或觀看時寫下重要資料。"},{"en":"Students take notes during lessons so they can review key points later.","zh":"學生在課堂中做筆記，方便之後複習重點。"},{"en":"Notes help researchers remember details that recordings or numbers may not capture.","zh":"筆記幫助研究人員記住錄音或數字未必能捕捉的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes writing information for later use.","zh":"這個短語描述為日後使用而寫下資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for the main idea question.","zh":"學生為主旨題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option labelled with the right letter.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選出以正確字母標示的答案選項。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice question, students may choose the correct letter after eliminating wrong options.","zh":"在多項選擇題中，學生可能在排除錯誤選項後選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Careful reading is needed because several options may sound partly true.","zh":"需要仔細閱讀，因為幾個選項可能聽起來部分正確。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"the main idea of","meaning":"……的主旨","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for the main idea of the passage.","zh":"題目問文章的主旨。"},{"en":"The main idea of something is the central message or most important point.","zh":"main idea of something 指中心訊息或最重要重點。"},{"en":"Students should find the main idea of a paragraph before choosing a heading.","zh":"學生在選標題前，應先找出段落主旨。"},{"en":"Understanding the main idea helps readers avoid being distracted by small details.","zh":"理解主旨幫助讀者避免被小細節分散注意力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the overall meaning.","zh":"這個短語著重整體意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"be most applicable to","meaning":"最適用於……","examples":[{"en":"Some people claim that quantitative research is most applicable to education.","zh":"有些人聲稱定量研究最適用於教育。"},{"en":"To be most applicable to something means to be most suitable or relevant for it.","zh":"be most applicable to something 指最適合或最相關於某事。"},{"en":"A practical speaking activity may be most applicable to students preparing for interviews.","zh":"實用口語活動可能最適用於準備面試的學生。"},{"en":"A method is not automatically best just because it is applicable to one situation.","zh":"一種方法不會只因適用於某情況就自動是最佳。"},{"en":"This phrase describes suitability for a specific area or purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述對某特定範疇或目的的適合性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"children’s education","meaning":"兒童教育","examples":[{"en":"The passage focuses partly on research into children’s education.","zh":"文章部分集中於關於兒童教育的研究。"},{"en":"Children’s education is the teaching, learning, support, and development of young learners.","zh":"children’s education 指年幼學習者的教學、學習、支援和發展。"},{"en":"Children’s education includes reading, maths, social skills, creativity, and emotional growth.","zh":"兒童教育包括閱讀、數學、社交能力、創意和情緒成長。"},{"en":"Research into children’s education can help schools design fairer and clearer learning tasks.","zh":"關於兒童教育的研究可以幫助學校設計更公平和更清楚的學習任務。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to education for children, not adults.","zh":"這個短語指兒童的教育，而不是成人教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"lack of a deep understanding of","meaning":"對……缺乏深入理解","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to society’s lack of a deep understanding of educational approaches.","zh":"該選項指社會對教育方法缺乏深入理解。"},{"en":"Lack of a deep understanding of something means not knowing it fully or seriously enough.","zh":"lack of a deep understanding of something 指對某事認識不夠完整或不夠深入。"},{"en":"A lack of a deep understanding of exam stress may lead adults to blame students unfairly.","zh":"對考試壓力缺乏深入理解，可能令成年人不公平地責怪學生。"},{"en":"Without deep understanding, people may choose simple solutions for complex problems.","zh":"沒有深入理解，人們可能為複雜問題選擇簡單解決方案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shallow knowledge of an important issue.","zh":"這個短語描述對重要議題的表面認識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"educational approaches","meaning":"教育研究方法；教育取向","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses different educational research approaches.","zh":"文章討論不同教育研究方法。"},{"en":"Educational approaches are ways of teaching, learning, assessing, or researching education.","zh":"educational approaches 指教學、學習、評估或研究教育的方法。"},{"en":"Project learning, direct instruction, and group discussion are educational approaches.","zh":"專題學習、直接教學和小組討論都是教育取向。"},{"en":"Different approaches suit different students, goals, and classroom contexts.","zh":"不同方法適合不同學生、目標和課室情境。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to methods or ways of thinking in education.","zh":"這個短語指教育中的方法或思考方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"criticisms of it","meaning":"對它的批評","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains quantitative research and criticisms of it.","zh":"文章解釋定量研究及對它的批評。"},{"en":"Criticisms of it are objections, doubts, or negative comments about that thing.","zh":"criticisms of it 指對某事的反對意見、疑問或負面評論。"},{"en":"A new school policy may have criticisms of it if parents think it is unfair.","zh":"如果家長認為新校政不公平，它可能受到批評。"},{"en":"Studying criticisms helps readers understand both strengths and weaknesses.","zh":"研究批評幫助讀者理解優點和弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to challenges made against a topic already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指對已提及主題提出的挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"imply that","meaning":"暗示","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not imply that qualitative research is flawless.","zh":"文章並沒有暗示定性研究毫無缺陷。"},{"en":"To imply that means to suggest something indirectly without saying it directly.","zh":"imply that 指間接表示某事，而不是直接說出。"},{"en":"If a teacher says, “This answer needs more evidence,” she may imply that the argument is weak.","zh":"如果老師說「這個答案需要更多證據」，她可能暗示論點薄弱。"},{"en":"Readers must distinguish what a text states from what it implies.","zh":"讀者必須區分文本明說的內容和暗示的內容。"},{"en":"This phrase describes indirect meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述間接意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"flawless compared with","meaning":"與……相比毫無缺陷","examples":[{"en":"Qualitative research is not presented as flawless compared with quantitative research.","zh":"文章並沒有把定性研究呈現為與定量研究相比毫無缺陷。"},{"en":"Flawless compared with something means having no weaknesses when judged against something else.","zh":"flawless compared with something 指與某事相比沒有任何弱點。"},{"en":"One teaching method is rarely flawless compared with another because each has limits.","zh":"一種教學方法很少會與另一種相比毫無缺陷，因為每種方法都有局限。"},{"en":"If a writer says a method is not flawless, readers should expect both strengths and weaknesses.","zh":"如果作者說某方法並非毫無缺陷，讀者應預期它既有優點也有弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against treating one approach as perfect simply because another is criticised.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要因為一種方法受到批評，就把另一種方法視為完美。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 54 - Quantitative Research in Education.pdf","sourcePage":24}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 55":[{"front":"company innovation","meaning":"公司創新","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses company innovation in large and small firms.","zh":"文章討論大公司和小公司的公司創新。"},{"en":"Company innovation means the creation of new ideas, products, services, or business methods within a company.","zh":"公司創新指公司內部創造新意念、產品、服務或商業方法。"},{"en":"A bakery shows company innovation when it starts taking online orders and offering healthier recipes.","zh":"麵包店開始接受網上訂單並提供較健康食譜時，就是展現公司創新。"},{"en":"Company innovation can help a firm survive when customer needs or technology change.","zh":"當顧客需求或科技改變，公司創新可以幫助企業生存。"},{"en":"Without company innovation, even a successful business may become outdated.","zh":"沒有公司創新，即使成功企業也可能變得過時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a scruffy office","meaning":"簡陋凌亂的辦公室","examples":[{"en":"Umagic Systems works from a scruffy office in Midtown Manhattan.","zh":"Umagic Systems 在曼哈頓中城一間簡陋凌亂的辦公室工作。"},{"en":"A scruffy office is an untidy, plain, or slightly shabby workplace.","zh":"a scruffy office 指不整齊、樸素或有點破舊的工作場所。"},{"en":"A start-up may begin in a scruffy office because it spends money on product development instead of decoration.","zh":"初創公司可能在簡陋凌亂的辦公室起步，因為它把錢花在產品開發而不是裝修上。"},{"en":"A scruffy office does not necessarily mean the company lacks talent or ideas.","zh":"簡陋凌亂的辦公室不一定代表公司缺乏人才或意念。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a rough working environment, not a polished corporate headquarters.","zh":"這個短語暗示粗糙的工作環境，而不是光鮮的企業總部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Midtown Manhattan","meaning":"曼哈頓中城","examples":[{"en":"The company is based in Midtown Manhattan.","zh":"該公司位於曼哈頓中城。"},{"en":"Midtown Manhattan is a busy central business area in New York City.","zh":"Midtown Manhattan 是紐約市繁忙的中央商業區。"},{"en":"A small technology company in Midtown Manhattan may be close to investors, media firms, and clients.","zh":"位於曼哈頓中城的小型科技公司，可能接近投資者、媒體公司和客戶。"},{"en":"Being in a famous business district can help a company meet partners more easily.","zh":"位於著名商業區可以幫助公司更容易接觸合作伙伴。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a specific urban business location.","zh":"這個短語指出一個具體城市商業地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"artificial-intelligence programmers","meaning":"人工智能程式員","examples":[{"en":"A team of artificial-intelligence programmers is developing the software.","zh":"一隊人工智能程式員正在開發該軟件。"},{"en":"Artificial-intelligence programmers are people who write computer programs that imitate intelligent human thinking or decision-making.","zh":"artificial-intelligence programmers 指編寫電腦程式來模仿人類智能思考或決策的人。"},{"en":"Artificial-intelligence programmers may build a chatbot that answers customer questions automatically.","zh":"人工智能程式員可能建立自動回答顧客問題的聊天機械人。"},{"en":"Their work can reduce labour costs but may also create concerns about accuracy and privacy.","zh":"他們的工作可以降低人力成本，但也可能引起準確性和私隱問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to software specialists who design AI systems.","zh":"這個短語指設計 AI 系統的軟件專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"simulate the brains of","meaning":"模擬……的大腦；模擬……的思維","examples":[{"en":"The programmers are trying to simulate the brains of several experts.","zh":"程式員正嘗試模擬幾位專家的思維。"},{"en":"To simulate the brains of people means to imitate the way they think, decide, or give advice.","zh":"simulate the brains of people 指模仿他們思考、決策或給予建議的方式。"},{"en":"A medical app may try to simulate the thinking of experienced doctors when suggesting possible symptoms.","zh":"醫療應用程式在提出可能症狀時，可能嘗試模擬有經驗醫生的思維。"},{"en":"Simulation can make expert knowledge available to more users, but it cannot perfectly copy human judgement.","zh":"模擬可以令更多使用者取得專家知識，但不能完美複製人類判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes copying mental patterns through technology.","zh":"這個短語描述透過科技複製思維模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"eminent sexologist","meaning":"傑出的性學家","examples":[{"en":"The software tries to copy the advice of an eminent sexologist.","zh":"該軟件嘗試複製一位傑出性學家的建議。"},{"en":"An eminent sexologist is a highly respected expert who studies human sexuality and sexual health.","zh":"eminent sexologist 指研究人類性和性健康、備受尊重的專家。"},{"en":"A magazine may interview an eminent sexologist about relationship education and public health.","zh":"雜誌可能訪問傑出性學家，討論關係教育和公共健康。"},{"en":"Advice from an eminent expert can attract users because people trust recognised authority.","zh":"來自傑出專家的建議可以吸引用戶，因為人們信任受認可的權威。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a famous specialist in a sensitive field.","zh":"這個短語描述敏感領域中的著名專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"well-known dietitian","meaning":"知名營養師","examples":[{"en":"The system also simulates a well-known dietitian.","zh":"該系統也模擬一位知名營養師。"},{"en":"A well-known dietitian is a recognised nutrition expert who gives advice on food and health.","zh":"well-known dietitian 指受認可、就食物和健康提供建議的營養專家。"},{"en":"A school may invite a well-known dietitian to explain how students can eat before exams.","zh":"學校可能邀請知名營養師解釋學生考試前應如何飲食。"},{"en":"A dietitian’s reputation can make people more willing to follow meal advice.","zh":"營養師的名聲可以令人更願意跟從飲食建議。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a famous professional in nutrition.","zh":"這個短語指營養方面的著名專業人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"celebrity fitness trainer","meaning":"名人健身教練","examples":[{"en":"A celebrity fitness trainer is one of the experts being simulated.","zh":"名人健身教練是正在被模擬的專家之一。"},{"en":"A celebrity fitness trainer is a well-known exercise coach who often trains famous people or appears in the media.","zh":"celebrity fitness trainer 指知名運動教練，通常訓練名人或在媒體上出現。"},{"en":"A celebrity fitness trainer may design short home workouts for busy office workers.","zh":"名人健身教練可能為忙碌上班族設計短時間家居運動。"},{"en":"People may pay more for advice from such a trainer because fame creates trust and curiosity.","zh":"人們可能為這類教練的建議支付更多，因為名氣帶來信任和好奇。"},{"en":"The phrase combines fitness expertise with public popularity.","zh":"這個短語結合健身專業和公眾知名度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"several other experts","meaning":"其他幾位專家","examples":[{"en":"The company is modelling the knowledge of several other experts.","zh":"該公司正在模擬其他幾位專家的知識。"},{"en":"Several other experts means a number of additional specialists besides those already mentioned.","zh":"several other experts 指除已提及人士以外的幾位額外專家。"},{"en":"A school reform team may consult several other experts, such as psychologists, teachers, and parents.","zh":"學校改革團隊可能諮詢其他幾位專家，例如心理學家、老師和家長。"},{"en":"Using several experts can make advice broader because each person brings a different kind of knowledge.","zh":"使用幾位專家可以令建議更廣泛，因為每個人帶來不同知識。"},{"en":"The phrase adds more specialists without naming every one.","zh":"這個短語加入更多專家，但不逐一點名。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"young firm","meaning":"新成立的公司","examples":[{"en":"Umagic Systems is a young firm with an unusual business idea.","zh":"Umagic Systems 是一間有不尋常商業意念的新成立公司。"},{"en":"A young firm is a company that has been created recently and is still developing.","zh":"young firm 指最近創立、仍在發展中的公司。"},{"en":"A young firm may have few employees but a bold plan for a new app.","zh":"新成立的公司可能員工不多，但有開發新應用程式的大膽計劃。"},{"en":"Young firms can move quickly because they are less tied to old systems.","zh":"新公司可以快速行動，因為它們較少受舊系統束縛。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a new company, not the age of its workers.","zh":"這個短語描述新公司，而不是員工年齡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"set up websites","meaning":"建立網站","examples":[{"en":"The company is setting up websites for online consultations.","zh":"該公司正在建立網站，用於網上諮詢。"},{"en":"To set up websites means to create and prepare websites so that people can use them.","zh":"set up websites 指建立並準備網站，讓人們可以使用。"},{"en":"A tutor may set up a website where students can book lessons and download notes.","zh":"導師可能建立網站，讓學生預約課堂和下載筆記。"},{"en":"Setting up websites can help a business reach customers without a physical shop.","zh":"建立網站可以幫助企業在沒有實體店的情況下接觸顧客。"},{"en":"The phrase describes building an online platform for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述為某目的建立網上平台。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"allow clients to consult","meaning":"讓客戶諮詢……","examples":[{"en":"The websites will allow clients to consult virtual experts.","zh":"這些網站將讓客戶諮詢虛擬專家。"},{"en":"To allow clients to consult someone means to make it possible for customers to ask for advice from that person or system.","zh":"allow clients to consult someone 指讓顧客能夠向某人或某系統尋求建議。"},{"en":"A clinic website may allow patients to consult nurses about simple health questions.","zh":"診所網站可能讓病人諮詢護士關於簡單健康問題。"},{"en":"Online consultation can save travel time and make expert advice easier to access.","zh":"網上諮詢可以節省交通時間，並令專家建議更易取得。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a service platform with professional advice.","zh":"這個短語把服務平台與專業建議連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"virtual versions of","meaning":"……的虛擬版本","examples":[{"en":"Clients will consult virtual versions of famous personalities.","zh":"客戶將會諮詢著名人物的虛擬版本。"},{"en":"Virtual versions of people are computer-based representations that imitate those people’s voice, knowledge, or style.","zh":"virtual versions of people 指以電腦為基礎、模仿那些人的聲音、知識或風格的呈現。"},{"en":"A museum may create virtual versions of historical figures to answer visitors’ questions.","zh":"博物館可能創造歷史人物的虛擬版本來回答訪客問題。"},{"en":"Virtual versions can make famous expertise scalable, but they may also raise questions about authenticity.","zh":"虛擬版本可以令名人專業知識擴大使用，但也可能引起真實性問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to digital imitations, not the real people themselves.","zh":"這個短語指數碼模仿物，而不是真人本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"these personalities","meaning":"這些名人；這些人物","examples":[{"en":"The software imitates the advice of these personalities.","zh":"該軟件模仿這些名人的建議。"},{"en":"These personalities means these well-known people with recognisable public identities or expert images.","zh":"these personalities 指這些有可識別公眾身份或專家形象的知名人士。"},{"en":"A fitness app may use these personalities to make exercise advice feel more familiar to users.","zh":"健身應用程式可能使用這些名人，令運動建議對使用者感覺更熟悉。"},{"en":"Famous personalities can attract subscribers because users feel they are receiving advice from someone special.","zh":"名人可以吸引訂戶，因為使用者覺得自己正在得到特別人物的建議。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to the named experts or public figures.","zh":"這個短語指回已命名的專家或公眾人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"subscribers","meaning":"訂戶；付費用戶","examples":[{"en":"Subscribers will enter details about themselves into the system.","zh":"訂戶會把關於自己的資料輸入系統。"},{"en":"Subscribers are people who pay or register to receive a service regularly.","zh":"subscribers 指付費或登記以定期接受服務的人。"},{"en":"Subscribers to an online course may receive weekly lessons and feedback.","zh":"網上課程訂戶可能每週收到課堂和回饋。"},{"en":"A company needs subscribers to keep paying so the service can continue operating.","zh":"公司需要訂戶持續付款，服務才能繼續運作。"},{"en":"The word refers to regular users, often paying users.","zh":"這個詞指定期使用者，通常是付費用戶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"feed in details","meaning":"輸入資料","examples":[{"en":"Subscribers will feed in details about themselves and their goals.","zh":"訂戶會輸入關於自己和目標的資料。"},{"en":"To feed in details means to enter information into a computer system.","zh":"feed in details 指把資料輸入電腦系統。"},{"en":"A student may feed in exam dates to a revision app so it can create a timetable.","zh":"學生可能把考試日期輸入溫習應用程式，讓它製作時間表。"},{"en":"The system can give better advice when users feed in accurate details.","zh":"當使用者輸入準確資料，系統就能提供更好建議。"},{"en":"The phrase describes supplying data to software.","zh":"這個短語描述向軟件提供數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"details about themselves","meaning":"關於自己的資料","examples":[{"en":"Users provide details about themselves before receiving advice.","zh":"使用者在收到建議前提供關於自己的資料。"},{"en":"Details about themselves are personal information such as age, habits, goals, needs, or preferences.","zh":"details about themselves 指個人資料，例如年齡、習慣、目標、需要或偏好。"},{"en":"A fitness app may ask users for details about themselves, including height, weight, and exercise level.","zh":"健身應用程式可能要求使用者提供關於自己的資料，包括身高、體重和運動水平。"},{"en":"Personal details help a system give advice that fits the user better.","zh":"個人資料幫助系統提供更適合使用者的建議。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to information about the user, not general facts.","zh":"這個短語指關於使用者的資料，而不是一般事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"goals","meaning":"目標","examples":[{"en":"The software uses information about the users’ goals.","zh":"該軟件使用關於使用者目標的資料。"},{"en":"Goals are things that people want to achieve.","zh":"goals 指人們想達成的事情。"},{"en":"A student’s goal may be to improve speaking confidence before a job interview.","zh":"學生的目標可能是在求職面試前提升口語信心。"},{"en":"Clear goals help a system or teacher give more suitable advice.","zh":"清楚目標幫助系統或老師提供更合適建議。"},{"en":"Without goals, advice may become too general to be useful.","zh":"沒有目標，建議可能變得太籠統而不實用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"come up with","meaning":"想出；提出","examples":[{"en":"The software will come up with advice for each subscriber.","zh":"該軟件會為每位訂戶提出建議。"},{"en":"To come up with something means to think of or produce an idea, answer, or solution.","zh":"come up with something 指想出或產生意念、答案或解決方案。"},{"en":"A teacher may come up with a new activity when students find grammar boring.","zh":"當學生覺得文法沉悶，老師可能想出新活動。"},{"en":"Good information helps people come up with better solutions.","zh":"良好資訊幫助人們想出更好解決方案。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating an idea, not physically finding an object.","zh":"這個短語描述創造意念，而不是實際找到物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the advice that","meaning":"……會給出的建議","examples":[{"en":"The system produces the advice that the star expert would give.","zh":"該系統產生明星專家會給出的建議。"},{"en":"The advice that someone would give means the recommendation or guidance that person is expected to offer.","zh":"the advice that someone would give 指預期某人會提供的建議或指導。"},{"en":"A study app may try to provide the advice that an experienced tutor would give before an exam.","zh":"學習應用程式可能嘗試提供有經驗導師考試前會給出的建議。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a piece of advice with the person whose judgement it imitates.","zh":"這個短語把一項建議與其模仿的判斷來源連起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing real expert guidance with simulated guidance.","zh":"它適合用於比較真實專家指導與模擬指導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"star expert","meaning":"明星專家","examples":[{"en":"The advice is designed to sound like it comes from a star expert.","zh":"這些建議被設計成聽起來像來自明星專家。"},{"en":"A star expert is a famous specialist whose name attracts attention and trust.","zh":"star expert 指名字能吸引注意和信任的著名專家。"},{"en":"A cooking platform may invite a star expert to design recipes for beginners.","zh":"烹飪平台可能邀請明星專家為初學者設計食譜。"},{"en":"Star experts can help market a service because users recognise their authority.","zh":"明星專家可以幫助推廣服務，因為使用者認得其權威。"},{"en":"The phrase combines professional expertise with celebrity appeal.","zh":"這個短語結合專業知識與名人吸引力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lose money betting on","meaning":"押注……而輸錢","examples":[{"en":"Few people have lost money betting on American consumer behaviour.","zh":"很少人因押注美國消費者行為而輸錢。"},{"en":"To lose money betting on something means to make a financial judgement about it and be wrong.","zh":"lose money betting on something 指對某事作出財務判斷但判斷錯誤。"},{"en":"An investor may lose money betting on a product if customers do not buy it.","zh":"如果顧客不購買某產品，投資者可能因押注該產品而輸錢。"},{"en":"Companies study behaviour carefully because wrong guesses can waste millions.","zh":"公司仔細研究行為，因為錯誤猜測可以浪費數百萬。"},{"en":"The phrase uses gambling language to describe business risk.","zh":"這個短語用賭博語言描述商業風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the neuroses of","meaning":"……的神經質；……的焦慮心理","examples":[{"en":"The business idea depends partly on the neuroses of the American consumer.","zh":"這個商業意念部分取決於美國消費者的焦慮心理。"},{"en":"The neuroses of a group are its worries, anxieties, insecurities, or emotional pressures.","zh":"neuroses of a group 指某群體的擔憂、焦慮、不安全感或情緒壓力。"},{"en":"A beauty company may profit from the neuroses of customers who fear looking old.","zh":"美容公司可能從害怕變老的顧客焦慮心理中獲利。"},{"en":"Businesses can exploit anxiety when they sell products as solutions to personal worries.","zh":"當企業把產品作為個人憂慮的解決方案出售，它們可以利用焦慮。"},{"en":"The phrase is slightly critical because it suggests nervous or insecure behaviour.","zh":"這個短語略帶批評，因為它暗示緊張或缺乏安全感的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"American consumer","meaning":"美國消費者","examples":[{"en":"The American consumer may be willing to pay for virtual expert advice.","zh":"美國消費者可能願意為虛擬專家建議付費。"},{"en":"The American consumer means people in the United States who buy goods and services.","zh":"American consumer 指在美國購買貨品和服務的人。"},{"en":"A company may study the American consumer before launching a new health app.","zh":"公司推出新健康應用程式前，可能研究美國消費者。"},{"en":"Consumer habits can shape which products become successful in a market.","zh":"消費者習慣可以影響哪些產品在市場中成功。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to buyers as a group, not one individual customer.","zh":"這個短語指作為群體的買家，而不是一名個別顧客。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prospects are hard to gauge","meaning":"前景難以估量","examples":[{"en":"Umagic’s prospects are hard to gauge.","zh":"Umagic 的前景難以估量。"},{"en":"If prospects are hard to gauge, it is difficult to judge whether future success is likely.","zh":"prospects are hard to gauge 指難以判斷未來成功的可能性。"},{"en":"A new restaurant’s prospects may be hard to gauge before customers try its food.","zh":"新餐廳在顧客試食前，前景可能難以估量。"},{"en":"Unusual ideas create uncertainty because there may be no clear market history to study.","zh":"不尋常意念會造成不確定性，因為可能沒有清楚市場歷史可供研究。"},{"en":"The phrase means the future is difficult to estimate.","zh":"這個短語意思是未來難以估計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in ten years’ time","meaning":"十年後","examples":[{"en":"In ten years’ time, virtual advice may seem normal.","zh":"十年後，虛擬建議可能看似正常。"},{"en":"In ten years’ time means ten years from now or from the time being discussed.","zh":"in ten years’ time 指從現在或所討論時間起十年後。"},{"en":"In ten years’ time, many students may use AI tutors as naturally as search engines.","zh":"十年後，許多學生可能像使用搜尋器一樣自然地使用 AI 導師。"},{"en":"The phrase helps writers imagine how attitudes may change in the future.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者想像態度日後如何改變。"},{"en":"It sets a clear future time frame.","zh":"它設定清楚的未來時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"consult a computer about","meaning":"就……諮詢電腦","examples":[{"en":"People may one day consult a computer about personal issues.","zh":"人們有一天可能就個人問題諮詢電腦。"},{"en":"To consult a computer about something means to ask a computer system for information or advice on that topic.","zh":"consult a computer about something 指就某主題向電腦系統尋求資訊或建議。"},{"en":"A patient may consult a computer about basic symptoms before calling a clinic.","zh":"病人可能在致電診所前，就基本症狀諮詢電腦。"},{"en":"Computer advice can be fast, but sensitive problems may still need human judgement.","zh":"電腦建議可以很快，但敏感問題可能仍需要人類判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using technology as an advice source.","zh":"這個短語描述把科技用作建議來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"seem natural","meaning":"顯得自然","examples":[{"en":"Consulting a computer about private matters might seem natural in the future.","zh":"將來就私人事情諮詢電腦可能顯得自然。"},{"en":"To seem natural means to feel normal, expected, or not strange.","zh":"seem natural 指感覺正常、理所當然或不奇怪。"},{"en":"Online lessons seemed strange at first, but later they seemed natural to many students.","zh":"網課一開始顯得奇怪，但後來對許多學生來說顯得自然。"},{"en":"Repeated use can make a new technology seem natural over time.","zh":"反覆使用可以令新科技隨時間顯得自然。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how people’s attitudes change through familiarity.","zh":"這個短語描述人們態度如何透過熟悉而改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"seem absurd","meaning":"顯得荒謬","examples":[{"en":"The same idea might also seem absurd to many people.","zh":"同一個想法對許多人來說也可能顯得荒謬。"},{"en":"To seem absurd means to appear ridiculous, unreasonable, or impossible to take seriously.","zh":"seem absurd 指看起來可笑、不合理或難以認真看待。"},{"en":"A plan to replace all teachers with robots may seem absurd to parents.","zh":"用機械人取代所有老師的計劃，對家長來說可能顯得荒謬。"},{"en":"Ideas can seem absurd before society becomes used to new technology.","zh":"在社會習慣新科技之前，一些想法可能顯得荒謬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a reaction of disbelief or ridicule.","zh":"這個短語描述不相信或嘲笑的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"companies like it","meaning":"同類公司","examples":[{"en":"Umagic and companies like it worry large American firms.","zh":"Umagic 和同類公司令美國大企業擔心。"},{"en":"Companies like it means other companies with similar size, style, or business ideas.","zh":"companies like it 指在規模、風格或商業意念上相似的其他公司。"},{"en":"A new online tutor platform and companies like it may challenge traditional tutoring centres.","zh":"新網上補習平台和同類公司可能挑戰傳統補習中心。"},{"en":"When several similar start-ups appear, big firms may feel pressure to respond.","zh":"當幾間相似初創出現，大公司可能感到需要回應的壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase groups one company with similar firms.","zh":"這個短語把一間公司與相似企業歸在一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"begin to spook","meaning":"開始令……不安","examples":[{"en":"Small innovative companies are beginning to spook large American firms.","zh":"小型創新公司開始令美國大企業不安。"},{"en":"To begin to spook someone means to start making them nervous, worried, or afraid.","zh":"begin to spook someone 指開始令某人緊張、擔心或害怕。"},{"en":"A small coffee shop may begin to spook a big chain if customers prefer its service.","zh":"如果顧客較喜歡小咖啡店的服務，它可能開始令大型連鎖店不安。"},{"en":"New competitors spook large firms when they show that old business models may be weak.","zh":"當新競爭者顯示舊商業模式可能脆弱，大公司會感到不安。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and suggests fear caused by uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語較口語，暗示由不確定性引起的恐懼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"large American firms","meaning":"美國大企業","examples":[{"en":"Large American firms are worried about unusual innovative ideas.","zh":"美國大企業擔心不尋常的創新意念。"},{"en":"Large American firms are big companies based in the United States.","zh":"large American firms 指總部或根基在美國的大型公司。"},{"en":"A large American firm may have thousands of workers and offices around the world.","zh":"美國大企業可能有數千名員工和遍布全球的辦公室。"},{"en":"Large firms can have more money, but they may move more slowly than start-ups.","zh":"大企業可能有更多資金，但行動可能比初創公司慢。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to major US companies, not small local businesses.","zh":"這個短語指主要美國公司，而不是小型本地企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"half-barmy ideas","meaning":"有點瘋狂的想法","examples":[{"en":"Some big companies see half-barmy ideas as important sources of innovation.","zh":"有些大公司把有點瘋狂的想法視為重要創新來源。"},{"en":"Half-barmy ideas are ideas that seem partly crazy, strange, or unrealistic.","zh":"half-barmy ideas 指看似有點瘋狂、奇怪或不切實際的想法。"},{"en":"A plan to sell shoes only through a mobile app once might have sounded half-barmy.","zh":"只透過手機應用程式賣鞋的計劃，曾經可能聽起來有點瘋狂。"},{"en":"Strange ideas can become valuable if they meet a real need that others ignore.","zh":"如果奇怪想法滿足了別人忽視的真實需要，它們可以變得有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and slightly humorous.","zh":"這個短語較口語，並帶一點幽默。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"innovative ideas","meaning":"創新意念","examples":[{"en":"Innovative ideas may be the key to future business success.","zh":"創新意念可能是未來商業成功的關鍵。"},{"en":"Innovative ideas are new and useful ideas that change how something is made, sold, taught, or used.","zh":"innovative ideas 指新而有用、能改變某物製作、銷售、教學或使用方式的想法。"},{"en":"A school has an innovative idea when it lets students record speaking practice at home and receive feedback online.","zh":"學校讓學生在家錄口語練習並在網上收到回饋時，就是有創新意念。"},{"en":"Innovative ideas can create new markets or improve old services.","zh":"創新意念可以創造新市場或改善舊服務。"},{"en":"The phrase means more than “new”; the idea must have practical value.","zh":"這個短語不只是「新的」；意念必須有實際價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the key to","meaning":"……的關鍵","examples":[{"en":"Large firms see innovation as the key to their future success.","zh":"大公司把創新視為未來成功的關鍵。"},{"en":"The key to something is the most important factor that helps it happen.","zh":"the key to something 指促成某事的最重要因素。"},{"en":"Regular practice is the key to improving pronunciation.","zh":"定期練習是改善發音的關鍵。"},{"en":"For many companies, understanding customers is the key to designing useful products.","zh":"對許多公司而言，理解顧客是設計有用產品的關鍵。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what is most important for success.","zh":"這個短語指出成功最重要的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"future success","meaning":"未來成功","examples":[{"en":"Innovation may determine a company’s future success.","zh":"創新可能決定公司的未來成功。"},{"en":"Future success is success that may happen later, not success already achieved.","zh":"future success 指日後可能出現的成功，而不是已經取得的成功。"},{"en":"A student’s future success may depend on study habits built long before the exam.","zh":"學生的未來成功可能取決於考試前很久已建立的學習習慣。"},{"en":"Companies invest in new ideas because they want to protect future success.","zh":"公司投資新意念，因為它們希望保障未來成功。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on long-term results.","zh":"這個短語重點是長期結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"become the buzzword of","meaning":"成為……的熱門用語","examples":[{"en":"Innovation has become the buzzword of American management.","zh":"創新已成為美國管理界的熱門用語。"},{"en":"To become the buzzword of a field means to become a fashionable word that many people in that field use repeatedly.","zh":"become the buzzword of a field 指成為該領域中許多人反覆使用的流行詞。"},{"en":"“Well-being” has become a buzzword in many schools and workplaces.","zh":"“Well-being” 已成為許多學校和職場的熱門用語。"},{"en":"A buzzword can show an important trend, but it may also be used without clear meaning.","zh":"熱門用語可以顯示重要趨勢，但也可能被空泛使用。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests popularity in language and discussion.","zh":"這個短語暗示在語言和討論中的流行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"American management","meaning":"美國管理界","examples":[{"en":"Innovation is now central to American management thinking.","zh":"創新現在是美國管理思想的核心。"},{"en":"American management refers to the ideas, methods, and practices used by managers and companies in the United States.","zh":"American management 指美國管理者和公司使用的理念、方法和做法。"},{"en":"American management often influences business schools through case studies and popular management books.","zh":"美國管理界常透過個案研究和流行管理書籍影響商學院。"},{"en":"When American management focuses on innovation, firms may change how they reward employees.","zh":"當美國管理界專注於創新，公司可能改變獎勵員工的方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a business-thinking tradition, not one single company.","zh":"這個短語描述一種商業思維傳統，而不是單一公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be outsourced","meaning":"被外判","examples":[{"en":"Many business functions can now be outsourced.","zh":"許多商業職能現在可以被外判。"},{"en":"To be outsourced means to be given to an outside company instead of being done inside the organisation.","zh":"be outsourced 指工作交由外部公司處理，而不是在機構內部完成。"},{"en":"A school may outsource cleaning services to a professional contractor.","zh":"學校可能把清潔服務外判給專業承辦商。"},{"en":"Outsourcing can reduce costs, but it may also reduce direct control over quality.","zh":"外判可以降低成本，但也可能減少對質素的直接控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving work outside the company.","zh":"這個短語描述把工作移到公司外部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"re-engineered","meaning":"被重新設計；被再造","examples":[{"en":"Many processes have already been re-engineered.","zh":"許多流程已經被重新設計。"},{"en":"Re-engineered means redesigned in a major way to make a process faster, cheaper, or more effective.","zh":"re-engineered 指以重大方式重新設計某流程，使其更快、更便宜或更有效。"},{"en":"A hospital may re-engineer its appointment system so patients wait less time.","zh":"醫院可能重新設計預約系統，讓病人等候時間更短。"},{"en":"Re-engineering can improve efficiency, but competitors may copy the same changes.","zh":"流程再造可以改善效率，但競爭對手可能複製同樣改變。"},{"en":"The word suggests redesigning the whole process, not making tiny adjustments.","zh":"這個詞暗示重新設計整個流程，而不是作微小調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"worryingly","meaning":"令人擔心的是","examples":[{"en":"Worryingly, competitors have made the same improvements.","zh":"令人擔心的是，競爭對手也作出了同樣改善。"},{"en":"Worryingly means in a way that causes concern or anxiety.","zh":"worryingly 指以令人擔憂或焦慮的方式。"},{"en":"Worryingly, several students failed the same basic grammar question.","zh":"令人擔心的是，幾名學生都答錯同一條基本文法題。"},{"en":"The word signals that the following fact is not just neutral but troubling.","zh":"這個詞表示接下來的事實不只是中性，而是令人不安。"},{"en":"It helps the writer show concern without using a long explanation.","zh":"它幫助作者不用長篇解釋也能表達憂慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"by their competitors as well","meaning":"也被競爭對手……","examples":[{"en":"The same changes have been made by their competitors as well.","zh":"同樣改變也被它們的競爭對手作出。"},{"en":"By their competitors as well means the rival companies have also done the same thing.","zh":"by their competitors as well 指競爭公司也做了同樣事情。"},{"en":"A café may lose its advantage if its discount app is copied by competitors as well.","zh":"如果咖啡店的折扣應用程式也被競爭對手複製，它可能失去優勢。"},{"en":"When improvements are made by competitors as well, a company needs a new source of advantage.","zh":"當改善也被競爭對手做到，公司就需要新的優勢來源。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that an improvement is no longer unique.","zh":"這個短語顯示某項改善不再獨特。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the stars of American business","meaning":"美國商界明星","examples":[{"en":"The stars of American business today tend to be innovators.","zh":"今日美國商界明星往往是創新者。"},{"en":"The stars of American business are the most admired, successful, or influential companies or businesspeople in the United States.","zh":"stars of American business 指美國最受推崇、成功或具影響力的公司或商人。"},{"en":"A fast-growing technology firm may become one of the stars of American business if it changes how people shop.","zh":"如果快速成長的科技公司改變人們購物方式，它可能成為美國商界明星之一。"},{"en":"Business stars attract attention because others want to copy their success.","zh":"商界明星吸引注意，因為其他人想模仿其成功。"},{"en":"The phrase uses “stars” to mean leading figures, not entertainers.","zh":"這個短語用 “stars” 表示領軍人物，而不是娛樂明星。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"tend to be","meaning":"往往是","examples":[{"en":"The most successful companies tend to be innovators.","zh":"最成功的公司往往是創新者。"},{"en":"Tend to be means usually are, though not always.","zh":"tend to be 指通常是，雖然不是永遠如此。"},{"en":"Students who read daily tend to be more confident writers.","zh":"每天閱讀的學生往往是較有信心的寫作者。"},{"en":"A company that listens to customers tends to be better at improving products.","zh":"聆聽顧客的公司往往更擅長改善產品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a general pattern, not an absolute rule.","zh":"這個短語描述一般模式，而不是絕對規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"innovators","meaning":"創新者；創新企業","examples":[{"en":"Dell, Amazon and Wal-Mart are presented as innovators.","zh":"Dell、Amazon 和 Wal-Mart 被呈現為創新者。"},{"en":"Innovators are people or companies that create new and useful ways of doing things.","zh":"innovators 指創造新而有用做事方式的人或公司。"},{"en":"A teacher who designs a new way to help shy students speak can be an innovator.","zh":"設計新方法幫助害羞學生發言的老師，可以是創新者。"},{"en":"Innovators often challenge old habits because they see a better method.","zh":"創新者通常挑戰舊習慣，因為他們看見更好方法。"},{"en":"The word describes creators of meaningful change.","zh":"這個詞描述有意義改變的創造者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"produce ideas or products","meaning":"創造意念或產品","examples":[{"en":"Successful firms produce ideas or products that change industries.","zh":"成功公司創造能改變行業的意念或產品。"},{"en":"To produce ideas or products means to create concepts, services, goods, or practical solutions.","zh":"produce ideas or products 指創造概念、服務、貨品或實用解決方案。"},{"en":"A small education company may produce ideas or products such as online quizzes and speaking-practice tools.","zh":"小型教育公司可能創造網上測驗和口語練習工具等意念或產品。"},{"en":"New ideas or products can attract customers and force competitors to improve.","zh":"新意念或產品可以吸引顧客，並迫使競爭對手改善。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both thinking and physical or digital goods.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋思考成果和實體或數碼商品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"change their industries","meaning":"改變其行業","examples":[{"en":"Some innovations have changed their industries.","zh":"有些創新已改變其行業。"},{"en":"To change an industry means to alter how businesses in that field operate, compete, or serve customers.","zh":"change an industry 指改變該領域中企業營運、競爭或服務顧客的方式。"},{"en":"Online booking changed the travel industry by letting customers compare prices instantly.","zh":"網上預訂讓顧客即時比較價格，改變了旅遊業。"},{"en":"When one company changes an industry, competitors may have to copy or adapt.","zh":"當一家公司改變一個行業，競爭對手可能必須模仿或適應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broad business impact, not a small internal change.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛商業影響，而不是小型內部改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a new book by","meaning":"由……撰寫的新書","examples":[{"en":"A new book by two consultants discusses innovation.","zh":"由兩名顧問撰寫的新書討論創新。"},{"en":"A new book by someone means a recently published book written by that person or group.","zh":"a new book by someone 指由某人或某群體撰寫、最近出版的書。"},{"en":"A new book by a language teacher may explain common grammar mistakes.","zh":"由語言老師撰寫的新書可能解釋常見文法錯誤。"},{"en":"New books can spread business ideas by turning research into readable advice.","zh":"新書可以把研究轉化為易讀建議，從而傳播商業想法。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies both the source and the medium of the idea.","zh":"這個短語同時指出想法來源和媒介。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"consultants from","meaning":"來自……的顧問","examples":[{"en":"The book was written by two consultants from Arthur D. Little.","zh":"該書由來自 Arthur D. Little 的兩名顧問撰寫。"},{"en":"Consultants from a company are advisers who work for that organisation and help clients solve problems.","zh":"consultants from a company 指在該機構工作、幫助客戶解決問題的顧問。"},{"en":"Consultants from a marketing firm may advise a restaurant on how to attract younger customers.","zh":"來自市場推廣公司的顧問可能建議餐廳如何吸引年輕顧客。"},{"en":"Consultants often collect data and suggest strategies because they work across many businesses.","zh":"顧問通常收集數據並提出策略，因為他們接觸許多企業。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the professional background of the advisers.","zh":"這個短語指出顧問的專業背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"record that","meaning":"記載；指出","examples":[{"en":"The book records that innovative firms achieved higher returns.","zh":"該書指出創新企業取得較高回報。"},{"en":"To record that means to state, report, or document a fact or finding in writing.","zh":"record that 指以書面陳述、報告或記錄某事實或發現。"},{"en":"A school report may record that attendance improved after breakfast was provided.","zh":"學校報告可能記載提供早餐後出席率改善。"},{"en":"Recording a finding gives readers evidence rather than only opinion.","zh":"記錄一項發現給讀者證據，而不只是意見。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and often used for reports, books, or studies.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於報告、書籍或研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"over the past 15 years","meaning":"在過去十五年","examples":[{"en":"Over the past 15 years, innovative firms have performed strongly.","zh":"在過去十五年，創新企業表現強勁。"},{"en":"Over the past 15 years means during the fifteen-year period leading up to the time being discussed.","zh":"over the past 15 years 指截至所討論時間為止的十五年間。"},{"en":"Over the past 15 years, many schools have added more digital tools.","zh":"在過去十五年，許多學校加入了更多數碼工具。"},{"en":"Looking at a long period helps people see whether success is temporary or consistent.","zh":"觀察較長時期幫助人看出成功是短暫還是持續。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a recent but fairly long time frame.","zh":"這個短語設定近期但相當長的時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"top 20 per cent of firms","meaning":"排名前20%的公司","examples":[{"en":"The top 20 per cent of firms in the poll had high shareholder returns.","zh":"該調查中排名前20%的公司有高股東回報。"},{"en":"The top 20 per cent of firms are the highest-ranking one-fifth of companies in a comparison.","zh":"top 20 per cent of firms 指比較中排名最高的五分之一公司。"},{"en":"In a school competition, the top 20 per cent of students may receive certificates.","zh":"在學校比賽中，排名前20%的學生可能獲得證書。"},{"en":"Comparing the top group with others can show whether strong performance is linked to a factor such as innovation.","zh":"把頂尖群體與其他人比較，可以顯示強表現是否與創新等因素有關。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the best-performing share of a group.","zh":"這個短語指出一個群體中表現最佳的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"annual innovation poll","meaning":"年度創新調查","examples":[{"en":"Fortune magazine runs an annual innovation poll.","zh":"《財富》雜誌進行年度創新調查。"},{"en":"An annual innovation poll is a survey conducted every year to compare how innovative companies are.","zh":"annual innovation poll 指每年進行、比較公司創新程度的調查。"},{"en":"A school may run an annual student satisfaction poll to see which services need improvement.","zh":"學校可能進行年度學生滿意度調查，以了解哪些服務需要改善。"},{"en":"Annual polls help track change because the same question is asked regularly.","zh":"年度調查有助追蹤變化，因為同一問題會定期提出。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a repeated yearly survey about innovation.","zh":"這個短語描述關於創新的每年重複調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Fortune magazine","meaning":"《財富》雜誌","examples":[{"en":"Fortune magazine measured firms’ innovation performance.","zh":"《財富》雜誌衡量公司的創新表現。"},{"en":"Fortune magazine is a business publication that reports on companies, management, and the economy.","zh":"Fortune magazine 是報道公司、管理和經濟的商業刊物。"},{"en":"A business student may read Fortune magazine to learn about famous companies and market trends.","zh":"商科學生可能閱讀《財富》雜誌，以了解著名公司和市場趨勢。"},{"en":"When a recognised magazine runs a poll, the results may influence managers and investors.","zh":"當受認可雜誌進行調查，結果可能影響管理者和投資者。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a source of business reporting.","zh":"這個短語指出商業報道來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"achieve double","meaning":"達到兩倍","examples":[{"en":"The most innovative firms achieved double the shareholder returns of their peers.","zh":"最具創新的公司達到同業股東回報的兩倍。"},{"en":"To achieve double something means to reach twice the amount or level of something.","zh":"achieve double something 指達到某數量或水平的兩倍。"},{"en":"A class may achieve double the pass rate after receiving extra writing practice.","zh":"一班學生接受額外寫作練習後，合格率可能達到兩倍。"},{"en":"Doubling returns suggests a strong advantage compared with competitors.","zh":"回報翻倍暗示與競爭者相比有強大優勢。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses a large numerical improvement.","zh":"這個短語表達巨大的數字改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"shareholder returns","meaning":"股東回報","examples":[{"en":"Innovative firms produced strong shareholder returns.","zh":"創新企業產生強勁股東回報。"},{"en":"Shareholder returns are the financial gains that company owners receive through rising share prices, dividends, or both.","zh":"shareholder returns 指公司擁有人透過股價上升、股息或兩者獲得的財務收益。"},{"en":"If a company’s profits grow, shareholder returns may increase.","zh":"如果公司利潤增長，股東回報可能增加。"},{"en":"Investors care about shareholder returns because they show whether owning the company’s stock was rewarding.","zh":"投資者重視股東回報，因為它顯示持有公司股票是否有回報。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to returns for shareholders, not customers or employees.","zh":"這個短語指股東所得回報，而不是顧客或員工所得。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"their peers","meaning":"同業；同類公司","examples":[{"en":"The top firms outperformed their peers.","zh":"頂尖公司表現優於同業。"},{"en":"Their peers are other companies or people of a similar type, level, or industry.","zh":"their peers 指其他相似類型、水平或行業的公司或人士。"},{"en":"A student may compare her writing progress with her peers in the same class.","zh":"學生可能把自己的寫作進步與同班同學比較。"},{"en":"Outperforming peers shows relative success, not just absolute improvement.","zh":"表現優於同業顯示相對成功，而不只是絕對改善。"},{"en":"The phrase means comparable others, not personal friends only.","zh":"這個短語意思是可比較的其他人或公司，而不只是私人朋友。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"merger boom","meaning":"合併熱潮","examples":[{"en":"Much of the merger boom is linked to the search for new ideas.","zh":"很大部分合併熱潮與尋找新意念有關。"},{"en":"A merger boom is a period when many companies are joining together or buying one another.","zh":"merger boom 指許多公司合併或互相收購的一段時期。"},{"en":"A technology sector may experience a merger boom when large firms buy smaller app companies.","zh":"當大型公司收購較小應用程式公司，科技業可能經歷合併熱潮。"},{"en":"Merger booms can happen when firms believe buying ideas is faster than creating them internally.","zh":"當公司相信購買意念比內部創造更快，合併熱潮可能出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a wave of business combinations.","zh":"這個短語描述企業結合的浪潮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be driven by","meaning":"由……推動","examples":[{"en":"The merger boom is driven by a desperate search for new ideas.","zh":"合併熱潮由對新意念的迫切尋求推動。"},{"en":"To be driven by something means to be caused or strongly motivated by it.","zh":"be driven by something 指由某事造成或強烈激勵。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be driven by a clear goal of entering university.","zh":"學生的進步可能由進入大學的清楚目標推動。"},{"en":"Business decisions are often driven by profit, competition, or customer demand.","zh":"商業決定通常由利潤、競爭或顧客需求推動。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the force behind an action or trend.","zh":"這個短語解釋行動或趨勢背後的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a desperate search for","meaning":"對……的迫切尋求","examples":[{"en":"Companies are engaged in a desperate search for new ideas.","zh":"公司正迫切尋求新意念。"},{"en":"A desperate search for something is an urgent and anxious attempt to find it.","zh":"desperate search for something 指急切而焦慮地嘗試尋找某物。"},{"en":"A hospital may begin a desperate search for nurses during a sudden staff shortage.","zh":"醫院在突然人手短缺期間，可能迫切尋求護士。"},{"en":"Desperation can make companies pay high prices for ideas or talent.","zh":"迫切心態可以令公司為意念或人才支付高價。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests strong pressure and limited time.","zh":"這個短語暗示強大壓力和有限時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the fortune now spent on","meaning":"現時花在……上的巨額金錢","examples":[{"en":"A fortune is now spent on buying others’ intellectual property.","zh":"現時有巨額金錢花在購買他人的知識產權上。"},{"en":"The fortune spent on something means a very large amount of money used for that purpose.","zh":"fortune spent on something 指用於某目的的非常大量金錢。"},{"en":"A company may spend a fortune on advertising before launching a new phone.","zh":"公司推出新手機前，可能在廣告上花費巨額金錢。"},{"en":"Spending a fortune on outside ideas shows that internal innovation may not be enough.","zh":"花巨額金錢購買外部意念，顯示內部創新可能不足。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the huge cost of an activity.","zh":"這個短語強調某活動的巨大成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"licensing","meaning":"授權；特許使用","examples":[{"en":"Companies spend heavily on licensing and buying ideas.","zh":"公司在授權和購買意念方面花費龐大。"},{"en":"Licensing is the legal permission to use someone else’s product, technology, brand, or intellectual property.","zh":"licensing 指合法取得使用他人產品、技術、品牌或知識產權的許可。"},{"en":"A school may pay for licensing so students can use professional design software.","zh":"學校可能支付授權費，讓學生使用專業設計軟件。"},{"en":"Licensing lets firms use ideas without fully owning them.","zh":"授權讓公司使用意念，而不必完全擁有它們。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to paid permission, not free copying.","zh":"這個短語指付費許可，而不是免費複製。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"intellectual property","meaning":"知識產權","examples":[{"en":"Firms are spending more on intellectual property.","zh":"公司在知識產權上的支出增加。"},{"en":"Intellectual property is legally protected creation, such as inventions, designs, brands, software, music, or writing.","zh":"intellectual property 指受法律保護的創作，例如發明、設計、品牌、軟件、音樂或文字作品。"},{"en":"A company’s logo, app code, and patented device can all be intellectual property.","zh":"公司的標誌、應用程式代碼和專利裝置都可以是知識產權。"},{"en":"Protecting intellectual property helps creators earn money from their ideas.","zh":"保護知識產權幫助創作者從意念中賺取收入。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to ownership of ideas and creative work.","zh":"這個短語指對意念和創意作品的擁有權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……所說","examples":[{"en":"According to the Patent and Licence Exchange, trading in intangible assets rose sharply.","zh":"根據專利及授權交易所所說，無形資產交易急劇上升。"},{"en":"According to means based on what a person, report, or organisation says.","zh":"according to 指基於某人、報告或組織所說。"},{"en":"According to the teacher, students should review vocabulary every day.","zh":"根據老師所說，學生應每天重溫詞彙。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to show where information comes from.","zh":"作者使用這個短語顯示資訊來源。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a source, not the writer’s own direct claim.","zh":"這個短語引入來源，而不是作者自己的直接說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Pasadena-based","meaning":"位於帕薩迪納的","examples":[{"en":"The Pasadena-based Patent and Licence Exchange reported the figures.","zh":"位於帕薩迪納的專利及授權交易所報告了這些數字。"},{"en":"Pasadena-based means located in or operating from Pasadena.","zh":"Pasadena-based 指位於帕薩迪納或從帕薩迪納營運。"},{"en":"A London-based education company may teach students online around the world.","zh":"位於倫敦的教育公司可能在網上教授全球學生。"},{"en":"Saying where a company is based helps readers identify its location and background.","zh":"說明公司位於哪裏，幫助讀者識別其地點和背景。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used before the name of an organisation.","zh":"這個短語常用在機構名稱前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Patent and Licence Exchange","meaning":"專利及授權交易所","examples":[{"en":"The Patent and Licence Exchange tracks trading in intangible assets.","zh":"專利及授權交易所追蹤無形資產交易。"},{"en":"The Patent and Licence Exchange is presented as an organisation that monitors or deals with patents, licences, and related transactions.","zh":"Patent and Licence Exchange 在文中指監察或處理專利、授權及相關交易的組織。"},{"en":"A business may use such an exchange to find technology it can legally license.","zh":"企業可能使用這類交易所尋找可合法授權使用的技術。"},{"en":"Tracking these deals helps show how valuable ideas have become in business.","zh":"追蹤這些交易有助顯示意念在商業中變得多有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specialist organisation connected with intellectual property.","zh":"這個短語命名一個與知識產權相關的專門組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"trading in","meaning":"……的交易","examples":[{"en":"Trading in intangible assets increased rapidly.","zh":"無形資產的交易快速增加。"},{"en":"Trading in something means buying and selling that type of item or asset.","zh":"trading in something 指買賣某類物品或資產。"},{"en":"Trading in second-hand textbooks often increases before a new school term.","zh":"二手教科書的交易通常在新學期前增加。"},{"en":"Trading in patents can grow when companies prefer buying technology to developing it themselves.","zh":"當公司偏好購買技術而不是自行開發，專利交易可能增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes commercial exchange in a particular category.","zh":"這個短語描述某一類別中的商業交換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"intangible assets","meaning":"無形資產","examples":[{"en":"Intangible assets include patents, licences and intellectual property.","zh":"無形資產包括專利、授權和知識產權。"},{"en":"Intangible assets are valuable things a company owns that are not physical objects.","zh":"intangible assets 指公司擁有但不是實體物件的有價值事物。"},{"en":"A brand name, software code, and customer database can be intangible assets.","zh":"品牌名稱、軟件代碼和客戶資料庫都可以是無形資產。"},{"en":"Intangible assets matter because ideas and rights can be worth more than buildings or machines.","zh":"無形資產很重要，因為意念和權利可能比建築物或機器更有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes non-physical business value.","zh":"這個短語描述非實體商業價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rose from…to…","meaning":"由……上升至……","examples":[{"en":"Trading in intangible assets rose from $15 billion to $100 billion.","zh":"無形資產交易由150億美元上升至1000億美元。"},{"en":"Rose from A to B means increased from one level to a higher level.","zh":"rose from A to B 指由一個水平增加到更高水平。"},{"en":"A school’s enrolment rose from 300 students to 500 students after it opened new courses.","zh":"學校開辦新課程後，收生人數由300人上升至500人。"},{"en":"A sharp rise can show growing demand or greater market value.","zh":"急劇上升可以顯示需求增加或市場價值提高。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful for describing numerical growth.","zh":"這個短語適合描述數字增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"an increasing proportion of","meaning":"越來越大比例的……","examples":[{"en":"An increasing proportion of the rewards went to small firms and individuals.","zh":"越來越大比例的回報流向小公司和個人。"},{"en":"An increasing proportion of something means a growing share or percentage of it.","zh":"an increasing proportion of something 指某事物中正在增長的份額或百分比。"},{"en":"An increasing proportion of students now use online dictionaries when writing essays.","zh":"越來越大比例的學生現在寫作文時使用網上字典。"},{"en":"When an increasing proportion of rewards goes to small firms, big firms may feel threatened.","zh":"當越來越大比例的回報流向小公司，大公司可能感到受威脅。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a share that is becoming larger over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間變大的份額。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the rewards going to","meaning":"回報流向……","examples":[{"en":"More rewards are going to small firms and individuals.","zh":"更多回報流向小公司和個人。"},{"en":"The rewards going to a group means the benefits, money, or recognition received by that group.","zh":"rewards going to a group 指某群體收到的好處、金錢或認可。"},{"en":"If more awards go to young scientists, universities may invest more in early-career research.","zh":"如果更多獎項流向年輕科學家，大學可能投放更多資源於早期職涯研究。"},{"en":"Rewards going to small firms can encourage more people to start businesses.","zh":"回報流向小公司可以鼓勵更多人創業。"},{"en":"The phrase shows who receives the benefits.","zh":"這個短語顯示誰收到好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"small firms and individuals","meaning":"小公司和個人","examples":[{"en":"Small firms and individuals are gaining more rewards from innovation.","zh":"小公司和個人正從創新中獲得更多回報。"},{"en":"Small firms and individuals means small companies and single inventors, creators, or entrepreneurs.","zh":"small firms and individuals 指小公司，以及個別發明者、創作者或創業者。"},{"en":"A single designer or a small firm may create an app that a big company later buys.","zh":"一名設計師或一間小公司可能創造一個日後被大公司收購的應用程式。"},{"en":"Innovation rewards can shift to small players when technology makes it cheaper to start businesses.","zh":"當科技令創業較便宜，創新回報可以轉向小型參與者。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts small creators with large corporations.","zh":"這個短語把小型創作者與大型公司作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"therein lies","meaning":"問題就在於；關鍵就在於","examples":[{"en":"Therein lies the terror for big companies.","zh":"對大公司來說，問題就在於此。"},{"en":"Therein lies means that the important point or problem is found in what has just been mentioned.","zh":"therein lies 指重要之處或問題就在剛提到的事情之中。"},{"en":"Students often memorise answers without understanding them; therein lies the danger.","zh":"學生常背答案而不理解；危險就在於此。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the deeper reason behind a situation.","zh":"這個短語指出某情況背後更深層原因。"},{"en":"It is formal and dramatic, often used to highlight the core issue.","zh":"它較正式且有戲劇感，常用來突出核心問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the terror for","meaning":"令……恐懼的地方","examples":[{"en":"Innovation outside large companies is the terror for big firms.","zh":"大公司以外的創新正是令大企業恐懼的地方。"},{"en":"The terror for someone is the thing that causes them serious fear or anxiety.","zh":"terror for someone 指令某人感到嚴重恐懼或焦慮的事物。"},{"en":"A sudden rent increase can be the terror for small shop owners.","zh":"租金突然上升可以是令小店店主恐懼的事情。"},{"en":"For big companies, small competitors are frightening when they innovate faster and cheaper.","zh":"對大公司而言，當小型競爭者創新更快更便宜，它們就令人害怕。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly describes what a group fears most.","zh":"這個短語強烈描述某群體最害怕的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"big companies","meaning":"大公司","examples":[{"en":"Big companies are worried that innovation works better outside them.","zh":"大公司擔心創新在它們外部運作得更好。"},{"en":"Big companies are large firms with many employees, resources, customers, and departments.","zh":"big companies 指擁有大量員工、資源、顧客和部門的大型企業。"},{"en":"A big company may have enough money to buy a start-up but may struggle to copy its speed.","zh":"大公司可能有足夠金錢收購初創公司，但未必能模仿其速度。"},{"en":"Size gives big companies power, but it can also slow decision-making.","zh":"規模給予大公司力量，但也可能拖慢決策。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to major established businesses.","zh":"這個短語指主要成熟企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"work best outside","meaning":"在……之外運作得最好","examples":[{"en":"Innovation seems to work best outside large organisations.","zh":"創新似乎在大型組織之外運作得最好。"},{"en":"To work best outside something means to function most effectively beyond that setting or structure.","zh":"work best outside something 指在某環境或結構以外最有效運作。"},{"en":"Some students work best outside noisy classrooms, such as in a quiet library.","zh":"有些學生在嘈雜課室以外的地方學得最好，例如安靜圖書館。"},{"en":"Creative ideas may work best outside large firms because small teams can move quickly.","zh":"創意意念可能在大公司之外運作得最好，因為小團隊行動更快。"},{"en":"The phrase compares where something performs most effectively.","zh":"這個短語比較某事在哪裏表現最有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"established ideas factories","meaning":"已建立的創意工廠","examples":[{"en":"Several established ideas factories have had difficulties recently.","zh":"幾個已建立的創意工廠最近遇到困難。"},{"en":"Established ideas factories are well-known organisations or departments expected to produce many new ideas.","zh":"established ideas factories 指知名、被期望產生大量新意念的組織或部門。"},{"en":"A large research lab may be treated as an established ideas factory inside a company.","zh":"大型研究實驗室可能被視為公司內部已建立的創意工廠。"},{"en":"Even established ideas factories can slow down if rules become too heavy or creativity is controlled too tightly.","zh":"即使已建立的創意工廠，如果規則太多或創意被控制得太緊，也可能放慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formal places designed to generate innovation.","zh":"這個短語描述正式設計來產生創新的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have dry spells","meaning":"經歷創意枯竭期","examples":[{"en":"Some large ideas factories have had dry spells recently.","zh":"一些大型創意工廠最近經歷創意枯竭期。"},{"en":"To have dry spells means to experience periods when few good ideas, results, or successes appear.","zh":"have dry spells 指經歷一段幾乎沒有好意念、成果或成功的時期。"},{"en":"A writer may have a dry spell and struggle to finish even one paragraph.","zh":"作家可能經歷創意枯竭期，連完成一段文字也困難。"},{"en":"Companies worry about dry spells because research spending may continue while useful products do not appear.","zh":"公司擔心創意枯竭期，因為研究開支可能持續，但有用產品沒有出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a temporary lack of creativity or success.","zh":"這個短語描述創意或成功暫時缺乏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"spend ten years developing","meaning":"花十年時間研發","examples":[{"en":"Gillette spent ten years developing its new razor.","zh":"Gillette 花十年時間研發其新剃鬚刀。"},{"en":"To spend ten years developing something means to use a decade designing, testing, and improving it.","zh":"spend ten years developing something 指用十年設計、測試和改善某物。"},{"en":"A medical company may spend ten years developing a new treatment before it is approved.","zh":"醫療公司可能花十年時間研發一種新療法，然後才獲批准。"},{"en":"Long development can produce quality, but it also gives competitors time to copy or respond.","zh":"長期研發可以產生質素，但也給競爭對手時間模仿或回應。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a very long investment of time.","zh":"這個短語強調非常長的時間投資。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reasonable imitation","meaning":"相當像樣的仿製品","examples":[{"en":"A British supermarket produced a reasonable imitation of the razor.","zh":"一間英國超市製造出該剃鬚刀相當像樣的仿製品。"},{"en":"A reasonable imitation is a copy that is fairly similar and good enough to compete.","zh":"reasonable imitation 指相當相似、足以競爭的仿製品。"},{"en":"A small bakery may make a reasonable imitation of a famous cake at a lower price.","zh":"小麵包店可能以較低價格製作名牌蛋糕相當像樣的仿製品。"},{"en":"If competitors can make reasonable imitations quickly, expensive research may lose value.","zh":"如果競爭者能快速製作相當像樣的仿製品，昂貴研究可能失去價值。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a copy that is not perfect but still acceptable.","zh":"這個短語暗示複製品不完美但仍可接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the management of creativity","meaning":"創意管理","examples":[{"en":"Peter Chernin discusses the management of creativity.","zh":"Peter Chernin 討論創意管理。"},{"en":"The management of creativity means organising people, teams, money, and rules so that new ideas can be produced.","zh":"management of creativity 指組織人員、團隊、資金和規則，使新意念能夠產生。"},{"en":"A school manages creativity when it gives students time, materials, and freedom for project work.","zh":"學校給學生時間、材料和自由進行項目學習，就是在管理創意。"},{"en":"Too much control can damage creativity, but no structure at all can waste effort.","zh":"過多控制可以傷害創意，但完全沒有結構也會浪費努力。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how organisations handle creative work.","zh":"這個短語重點是組織如何處理創意工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"size is your enemy","meaning":"規模是你的敵人","examples":[{"en":"Chernin argues that size is your enemy in managing creativity.","zh":"Chernin 認為，在管理創意時，規模是你的敵人。"},{"en":"Size is your enemy means being too large can create problems and reduce effectiveness.","zh":"size is your enemy 指規模太大可能造成問題並降低效能。"},{"en":"A class project may suffer if the group is so large that nobody feels responsible.","zh":"如果小組太大，以致沒有人覺得自己有責任，班級項目可能受影響。"},{"en":"Large organisations may move slowly because decisions pass through too many layers.","zh":"大型組織可能行動緩慢，因為決策要通過太多層級。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that scale can become a disadvantage.","zh":"這個短語警告規模可能變成劣勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"run an empire","meaning":"管理一個龐大業務王國","examples":[{"en":"Peter Chernin runs the Fox television and film empire.","zh":"Peter Chernin 管理 Fox 電視及電影王國。"},{"en":"To run an empire means to manage a very large and powerful business group.","zh":"run an empire 指管理一個非常龐大而有力量的企業集團。"},{"en":"A media executive may run an empire of newspapers, television channels, and streaming platforms.","zh":"媒體高層可能管理由報紙、電視頻道和串流平台組成的業務王國。"},{"en":"Running a huge organisation gives influence but makes personal involvement harder.","zh":"管理龐大組織帶來影響力，但令親身投入更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase uses “empire” to show scale and power.","zh":"這個短語用 “empire” 顯示規模和權力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"television and film empire","meaning":"電視及電影王國","examples":[{"en":"Fox is described as a television and film empire.","zh":"Fox 被形容為一個電視及電影王國。"},{"en":"A television and film empire is a large media business that produces or controls many TV and movie projects.","zh":"television and film empire 指製作或控制許多電視和電影項目的大型媒體企業。"},{"en":"A company with studios, channels, streaming rights, and famous actors may be a television and film empire.","zh":"擁有片廠、頻道、串流版權和著名演員的公司，可以是電視及電影王國。"},{"en":"Such an empire can reach huge audiences but may be difficult to manage creatively.","zh":"這類王國可以接觸龐大觀眾，但創意管理可能困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a powerful media organisation.","zh":"這個短語描述有強大力量的媒體組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as involved as","meaning":"像……一樣投入","examples":[{"en":"A person managing 20 movies cannot be as involved as one managing five.","zh":"管理20部電影的人不可能像管理5部電影的人一樣投入。"},{"en":"As involved as means equally active, present, or personally engaged in something.","zh":"as involved as 指同樣積極、在場或親身參與某事。"},{"en":"A teacher supervising ten groups cannot be as involved as a teacher helping two groups.","zh":"監督十個小組的老師，不可能像幫助兩個小組的老師一樣投入。"},{"en":"When managers handle too many projects, they may not notice small creative problems.","zh":"當管理者處理太多項目，他們可能注意不到細小創意問題。"},{"en":"The phrase compares levels of personal participation.","zh":"這個短語比較親身參與程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"break the studio into","meaning":"把工作室拆分成……","examples":[{"en":"Chernin tried to break the studio into smaller units.","zh":"Chernin 嘗試把工作室拆分成較小單位。"},{"en":"To break an organisation into smaller units means to divide it into smaller teams or sections.","zh":"break an organisation into smaller units 指把組織分成較小團隊或部門。"},{"en":"A school may break a large class into smaller groups for speaking practice.","zh":"學校可能把大班拆分成較小小組進行口語練習。"},{"en":"Smaller units can make communication faster and responsibility clearer.","zh":"較小單位可以令溝通更快、責任更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes restructuring a large group into manageable parts.","zh":"這個短語描述把大群體重組成可管理部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"smaller units","meaning":"較小的單位","examples":[{"en":"Smaller units may help creativity thrive.","zh":"較小的單位可能幫助創意蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"Smaller units are smaller teams, departments, or business sections within a larger organisation.","zh":"smaller units 指大型組織內較小的團隊、部門或業務部分。"},{"en":"A company may create smaller units so each team can focus on one product.","zh":"公司可能設立較小的單位，讓每個團隊專注一種產品。"},{"en":"Smaller units can improve creativity because decisions are faster and members know one another better.","zh":"較小單位可以改善創意，因為決策較快，成員彼此更熟悉。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts compact teams with large complex structures.","zh":"這個短語把精簡團隊與大型複雜結構作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at the risk of","meaning":"冒着……的風險","examples":[{"en":"The studio was divided into smaller units at the risk of higher costs.","zh":"工作室被拆分成較小單位，冒着成本較高的風險。"},{"en":"At the risk of something means accepting the possibility that a negative result may happen.","zh":"at the risk of something 指接受某負面結果可能發生的可能性。"},{"en":"A student may ask a difficult question at the risk of sounding wrong.","zh":"學生可能冒着聽起來錯誤的風險提出困難問題。"},{"en":"Companies sometimes choose speed at the risk of spending more money.","zh":"公司有時選擇速度，冒着花更多錢的風險。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a trade-off between benefit and danger.","zh":"這個短語顯示好處與危險之間的取捨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"incur higher costs","meaning":"招致較高成本","examples":[{"en":"Breaking the studio into smaller units may incur higher costs.","zh":"把工作室拆分成較小單位可能招致較高成本。"},{"en":"To incur higher costs means to have to pay more money because of a decision or action.","zh":"incur higher costs 指因某決定或行動而需要支付更多金錢。"},{"en":"A school may incur higher costs if it runs smaller classes with more teachers.","zh":"如果學校以更多老師開辦小班，可能招致較高成本。"},{"en":"Higher costs may be acceptable if they produce better quality or stronger creativity.","zh":"如果較高成本帶來更好質素或更強創意，它可能是可接受的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an expense created by a choice.","zh":"這個短語描述由選擇造成的開支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ideas thrive","meaning":"意念蓬勃發展","examples":[{"en":"It is easier for ideas to thrive outside big firms.","zh":"意念在大公司之外較容易蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"When ideas thrive, they grow, develop, and become successful.","zh":"ideas thrive 指意念成長、發展並變得成功。"},{"en":"Students’ ideas thrive in a classroom where questions and mistakes are welcomed.","zh":"在歡迎問題和錯誤的課室中，學生的意念會蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"Ideas thrive when people have enough freedom, feedback, and time to test them.","zh":"當人們有足夠自由、回饋和時間測試意念，意念就會蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"The phrase compares ideas to living things that can grow well.","zh":"這個短語把意念比作能夠良好成長的生命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"these days","meaning":"現今；如今","examples":[{"en":"Ideas can develop outside large firms more easily these days.","zh":"現今，意念可以更容易在大公司之外發展。"},{"en":"These days means nowadays or in the present period.","zh":"these days 指如今或現時這段時期。"},{"en":"These days, many students use online notes instead of carrying heavy textbooks.","zh":"如今，許多學生使用網上筆記，而不是攜帶沉重教科書。"},{"en":"The phrase helps compare the present with the past.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較現在與過去。"},{"en":"It often introduces a modern change in habits, technology, or society.","zh":"它常引入習慣、科技或社會上的現代變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"過去","examples":[{"en":"In the past, inventors often took ideas to big companies.","zh":"過去，發明者通常把意念帶到大公司。"},{"en":"In the past means during an earlier time, not now.","zh":"in the past 指在較早的時期，而不是現在。"},{"en":"In the past, students had to search paper encyclopedias for basic facts.","zh":"過去，學生必須翻查紙本百科全書尋找基本資料。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show how conditions have changed over time.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示情況如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"It often introduces an old habit or situation.","zh":"它常引入舊習慣或舊情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"clever scientist","meaning":"聰明的科學家","examples":[{"en":"A clever scientist once needed a big company to commercialise an idea.","zh":"聰明的科學家過去需要大公司把意念商業化。"},{"en":"A clever scientist is an intelligent researcher who can create or understand complex ideas.","zh":"clever scientist 指能創造或理解複雜想法的聰明研究者。"},{"en":"A clever scientist may invent a new battery but still need business help to sell it.","zh":"聰明的科學家可能發明新電池，但仍需要商業協助來出售它。"},{"en":"Scientific talent alone may not be enough if production, funding, and marketing are missing.","zh":"如果缺乏生產、資金和市場推廣，單靠科學才能可能不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes intellectual ability in a research context.","zh":"這個短語描述研究情境中的智力能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"commercialise an idea","meaning":"把意念商業化","examples":[{"en":"A scientist may want to commercialise an idea.","zh":"科學家可能想把意念商業化。"},{"en":"To commercialise an idea means to turn it into a product or service that can be sold.","zh":"commercialise an idea 指把意念變成可出售的產品或服務。"},{"en":"A teacher may commercialise an idea by turning classroom worksheets into a paid learning app.","zh":"老師可能把課堂工作紙變成付費學習應用程式，從而把意念商業化。"},{"en":"Commercialising an idea requires design, money, customers, and a way to deliver the product.","zh":"把意念商業化需要設計、資金、顧客和交付產品的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase connects creativity with business use.","zh":"這個短語把創意與商業用途連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take it first to","meaning":"先把它帶到……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists used to take their ideas first to big companies.","zh":"科學家過去常先把意念帶到大公司。"},{"en":"To take it first to someone means to bring an idea or proposal to that person or organisation before trying other options.","zh":"take it first to someone 指在嘗試其他選項前，先把意念或提案帶給某人或某機構。"},{"en":"A student with a school-club idea may take it first to the class teacher.","zh":"有學校學會意念的學生，可能先把它帶給班主任。"},{"en":"Inventors once took ideas to large firms because they needed money and factories.","zh":"發明者過去把意念帶到大公司，因為他們需要資金和工廠。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the first place someone seeks support.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人首先尋求支持的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cheap venture capital","meaning":"低成本風險投資資金","examples":[{"en":"Cheap venture capital helps entrepreneurs start their own firms.","zh":"低成本風險投資資金幫助創業者開辦自己的公司。"},{"en":"Cheap venture capital is investment money available to start-ups at relatively low cost or easy terms.","zh":"cheap venture capital 指以相對低成本或較寬鬆條件提供給初創公司的投資資金。"},{"en":"A young technology founder may use cheap venture capital to hire programmers before earning profit.","zh":"年輕科技創辦人可能使用低成本風險投資資金，在有利潤前聘請程式員。"},{"en":"When venture capital is cheap, more people can test risky business ideas.","zh":"當風險投資資金成本低，更多人可以測試高風險商業意念。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to accessible investment funding for new companies.","zh":"這個短語指新公司可較易取得的投資資金。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"set up on their own","meaning":"自行創業","examples":[{"en":"Inventors are more likely to set up on their own.","zh":"發明者更有可能自行創業。"},{"en":"To set up on one’s own means to start an independent business instead of working under another company.","zh":"set up on one’s own 指創立獨立企業，而不是在另一家公司底下工作。"},{"en":"A designer may set up on her own after gaining enough clients from freelance work.","zh":"設計師在自由工作中累積足夠客戶後，可能自行創業。"},{"en":"People set up independently when they believe they can develop an idea without a large employer.","zh":"當人們相信自己能在沒有大型僱主下發展意念，就會獨立創業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes starting a business independently.","zh":"這個短語描述獨立開辦生意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"raise $5 million","meaning":"籌集五百萬美元","examples":[{"en":"Umagic has already raised $5 million.","zh":"Umagic 已經籌集五百萬美元。"},{"en":"To raise $5 million means to obtain five million dollars in funding or investment.","zh":"raise $5 million 指取得五百萬美元資金或投資。"},{"en":"A charity may raise $5 million to build a new hospital wing.","zh":"慈善機構可能籌集五百萬美元興建新醫院側翼。"},{"en":"Raising money gives a company resources to hire staff, build products, and market services.","zh":"籌集資金給公司資源聘請員工、建立產品和推廣服務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes collecting financial support, not earning profit from sales.","zh":"這個短語描述收集財政支持，而不是從銷售中賺取利潤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be about to","meaning":"即將","examples":[{"en":"Umagic is about to raise $25 million more.","zh":"Umagic 即將再籌集二千五百萬美元。"},{"en":"Be about to means something is going to happen very soon.","zh":"be about to 指某事很快將會發生。"},{"en":"A class is about to start when students are already sitting down and the teacher opens the lesson.","zh":"當學生已坐下而老師開始課堂，課堂即將開始。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a sense that the next step is imminent.","zh":"這個短語營造下一步即將發生的感覺。"},{"en":"It is used for events that are close, not distant future plans.","zh":"它用於接近發生的事件，而不是遙遠未來計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"capital-intensive businesses","meaning":"資本密集型業務","examples":[{"en":"Pharmaceuticals is a capital-intensive business.","zh":"製藥業是資本密集型業務。"},{"en":"Capital-intensive businesses require large amounts of money for equipment, research, factories, or long development periods.","zh":"capital-intensive businesses 指需要大量資金用於設備、研究、工廠或長期開發的業務。"},{"en":"Building a railway is capital-intensive because trains, tracks, land, and stations cost a lot.","zh":"興建鐵路是資本密集型的，因為列車、路軌、土地和車站都很昂貴。"},{"en":"Capital-intensive industries are harder for small firms because early costs are high.","zh":"資本密集型行業對小公司較困難，因為早期成本高。"},{"en":"The phrase describes businesses that need heavy financial investment.","zh":"這個短語描述需要大量財務投資的業務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pharmaceuticals","meaning":"製藥業","examples":[{"en":"Pharmaceuticals often require expensive clinical trials.","zh":"製藥業通常需要昂貴的臨床試驗。"},{"en":"Pharmaceuticals refers to the drug industry or medicines produced for medical treatment.","zh":"pharmaceuticals 指製藥行業或為醫療治療而生產的藥物。"},{"en":"A pharmaceuticals company may spend years testing a new cancer medicine.","zh":"製藥公司可能花多年測試一種新的癌症藥物。"},{"en":"The industry needs strict safety testing because medicines affect human health directly.","zh":"該行業需要嚴格安全測試，因為藥物直接影響人類健康。"},{"en":"The phrase is connected with drugs, treatment, research, and regulation.","zh":"這個短語與藥物、治療、研究和監管有關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"entrepreneurs","meaning":"創業者","examples":[{"en":"Entrepreneurs can conduct early-stage research before selling to big firms.","zh":"創業者可以在出售給大公司前進行早期研究。"},{"en":"Entrepreneurs are people who start businesses and take risks to develop new ideas.","zh":"entrepreneurs 指創辦企業並承擔風險發展新意念的人。"},{"en":"A student who creates an online tutoring platform after graduation becomes an entrepreneur.","zh":"畢業後建立網上補習平台的學生，就成為創業者。"},{"en":"Entrepreneurs drive innovation because they are willing to test ideas that larger firms may avoid.","zh":"創業者推動創新，因為他們願意測試大公司可能避開的意念。"},{"en":"The word describes business creators, not ordinary employees.","zh":"這個詞描述商業創造者，而不是普通僱員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"conduct early-stage research","meaning":"進行早期研究","examples":[{"en":"Entrepreneurs can conduct early-stage research in pharmaceuticals.","zh":"創業者可以在製藥業進行早期研究。"},{"en":"To conduct early-stage research means to carry out the first rounds of study or testing before full development begins.","zh":"conduct early-stage research 指在全面開發開始前進行第一輪研究或測試。"},{"en":"A food company may conduct early-stage research by asking families to taste a new recipe.","zh":"食品公司可能透過請家庭試食新食譜來進行早期研究。"},{"en":"Early research helps decide whether an idea deserves more money and time.","zh":"早期研究幫助判斷某意念是否值得投入更多金錢和時間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the beginning of the research process.","zh":"這個短語描述研究過程的開端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sell out to","meaning":"出售公司予……","examples":[{"en":"Small firms may sell out to big firms before clinical trials.","zh":"小公司可能在臨床試驗前出售公司予大企業。"},{"en":"To sell out to a company means to sell one’s business or ownership to that company.","zh":"sell out to a company 指把自己的企業或所有權出售給該公司。"},{"en":"A small app developer may sell out to a large technology company after gaining many users.","zh":"小型應用程式開發商在獲得大量用戶後，可能出售公司予大型科技公司。"},{"en":"Selling out can give founders money and resources, but they may lose control of the idea.","zh":"出售公司可以給創辦人金錢和資源，但他們可能失去對意念的控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes transferring ownership to another business.","zh":"這個短語描述把所有權轉移給另一企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"expensive, risky clinical trials","meaning":"昂貴且高風險的臨床試驗","examples":[{"en":"Drug development often involves expensive, risky clinical trials.","zh":"藥物開發通常涉及昂貴且高風險的臨床試驗。"},{"en":"Expensive, risky clinical trials are medical tests on people that cost a lot and may fail or reveal safety problems.","zh":"expensive, risky clinical trials 指在人身上進行、成本高並可能失敗或揭示安全問題的醫學測試。"},{"en":"A new drug may pass laboratory tests but still fail during expensive clinical trials.","zh":"新藥可能通過實驗室測試，但仍在昂貴臨床試驗中失敗。"},{"en":"These trials are necessary because medicines must be proven safe and effective before public use.","zh":"這些試驗是必要的，因為藥物在公眾使用前必須證明安全有效。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why drug innovation is difficult and costly.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何藥物創新困難且昂貴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"clinical trials","meaning":"臨床試驗","examples":[{"en":"Clinical trials are a costly stage in drug development.","zh":"臨床試驗是藥物開發中成本高昂的階段。"},{"en":"Clinical trials are research studies that test medical treatments on people under controlled conditions.","zh":"clinical trials 指在受控條件下在人身上測試醫療方法的研究。"},{"en":"A vaccine usually goes through clinical trials before doctors can recommend it widely.","zh":"疫苗通常在醫生能廣泛建議使用前經過臨床試驗。"},{"en":"Clinical trials protect patients by checking safety, dosage, and effectiveness.","zh":"臨床試驗透過檢查安全性、劑量和成效來保護病人。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to human testing in medicine.","zh":"這個短語指醫學中的人體測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"total revenue","meaning":"總收入","examples":[{"en":"Around a third of drug firms’ total revenue comes from licensed-in technology.","zh":"藥廠總收入約三分之一來自外購授權技術。"},{"en":"Total revenue is all the money a business earns from sales and other income before costs are subtracted.","zh":"total revenue 指企業在扣除成本前從銷售和其他收入中賺到的全部金錢。"},{"en":"A café’s total revenue includes money from drinks, food, and delivery orders.","zh":"咖啡店的總收入包括飲品、食物和外送訂單所得金錢。"},{"en":"If a large share of revenue comes from licensed technology, outside ideas are financially important.","zh":"如果收入中很大部分來自授權技術，外部意念在財務上很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to overall income, not profit.","zh":"這個短語指整體收入，而不是利潤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"licensed-in technology","meaning":"外購授權技術","examples":[{"en":"Drug firms earn revenue from licensed-in technology.","zh":"藥廠從外購授權技術中獲得收入。"},{"en":"Licensed-in technology is technology a company has obtained permission to use from another owner.","zh":"licensed-in technology 指公司從另一擁有人取得許可使用的技術。"},{"en":"A phone maker may use licensed-in camera technology from a specialist supplier.","zh":"手機製造商可能使用來自專門供應商的外購授權相機技術。"},{"en":"Licensing in technology can be faster than inventing everything internally.","zh":"外購授權技術可以比完全內部發明更快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes technology brought into a company through legal permission.","zh":"這個短語描述透過法律許可帶入公司的技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"giants","meaning":"巨企","examples":[{"en":"Some corporate giants have bought many small companies successfully.","zh":"一些企業巨企成功收購了許多小公司。"},{"en":"Giants are very large and powerful companies in an industry.","zh":"giants 指某行業中非常大型且有力量的公司。"},{"en":"A technology giant may buy a small start-up to gain its software and engineers.","zh":"科技巨企可能收購小型初創，以取得其軟件和工程師。"},{"en":"Giants have money and scale, but they may struggle to stay flexible.","zh":"巨企有資金和規模，但可能難以保持靈活。"},{"en":"The word uses size to suggest business power.","zh":"這個詞用規模暗示商業力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"remarkably successful at","meaning":"在……方面非常成功","examples":[{"en":"General Electric and Cisco have been remarkably successful at integrating small companies.","zh":"General Electric 和 Cisco 在整合小公司方面非常成功。"},{"en":"Remarkably successful at something means unusually or noticeably good at doing it.","zh":"remarkably successful at something 指在做某事方面異常或明顯地出色。"},{"en":"A school may be remarkably successful at helping weak readers catch up.","zh":"學校可能在幫助閱讀較弱學生追上進度方面非常成功。"},{"en":"Being remarkably successful at integration means a company can keep value after buying another firm.","zh":"在整合方面非常成功，意思是公司收購另一企業後能保留其價值。"},{"en":"The phrase praises a strong ability in a specific activity.","zh":"這個短語讚揚某項具體活動中的強能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"snap up","meaning":"迅速收購","examples":[{"en":"Some giants snap up promising small companies.","zh":"一些巨企迅速收購有前景的小公司。"},{"en":"To snap up something means to buy or take it quickly before others can get it.","zh":"snap up something 指在其他人得到前快速買下或取得某物。"},{"en":"Parents may snap up seats in a popular summer course as soon as registration opens.","zh":"家長可能在報名一開始就迅速搶購受歡迎暑期課程名額。"},{"en":"Big firms snap up start-ups when they fear competitors may buy them first.","zh":"大公司在擔心競爭對手先買下初創時，會迅速收購它們。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests quick action to secure something valuable.","zh":"這個短語暗示快速行動以取得有價值事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"integrate small companies","meaning":"整合小公司","examples":[{"en":"Large firms try to integrate small companies after buying them.","zh":"大企業收購後嘗試整合小公司。"},{"en":"To integrate small companies means to bring them into a larger company’s systems, teams, and culture.","zh":"integrate small companies 指把小公司納入較大公司的系統、團隊和文化。"},{"en":"After buying a small design studio, a company must integrate its staff, clients, and projects.","zh":"收購小型設計工作室後，公司必須整合其員工、客戶和項目。"},{"en":"Poor integration can cause talented employees to leave and weaken the value of the acquisition.","zh":"整合不佳可以導致有才能員工離開，並削弱收購價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the work after a takeover, not the purchase itself.","zh":"這個短語描述收購後的工作，而不是收購本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"scores of","meaning":"大量；數十個","examples":[{"en":"Some companies have acquired scores of small firms.","zh":"有些公司收購了大量小企業。"},{"en":"Scores of means a large number of people or things, often dozens.","zh":"scores of 指大量人或物，通常是數十個。"},{"en":"Scores of students joined the school fair after teachers promoted it online.","zh":"老師在網上宣傳後，大量學生參加學校嘉年華。"},{"en":"Acquiring scores of companies can create growth but also management complexity.","zh":"收購大量公司可以帶來增長，但也增加管理複雜性。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests many, without giving an exact number.","zh":"這個短語暗示很多，但不給精確數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"worry about","meaning":"擔心","examples":[{"en":"Many large firms worry about the prices they have to pay.","zh":"許多大企業擔心自己必須支付的價格。"},{"en":"To worry about something means to feel concerned or anxious about it.","zh":"worry about something 指對某事感到關注或焦慮。"},{"en":"Students may worry about oral exams if they have not practised speaking.","zh":"如果學生沒有練習口語，可能會擔心口試。"},{"en":"Companies worry about high prices because overpaying can reduce future returns.","zh":"公司擔心高價，因為支付過高價格可以降低未來回報。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a concern or risk.","zh":"這個短語引入一項憂慮或風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the difficulty of","meaning":"……的困難","examples":[{"en":"They also worry about the difficulty of keeping talented people.","zh":"它們也擔心留住人才的困難。"},{"en":"The difficulty of something means the problem or challenge involved in doing it.","zh":"difficulty of something 指做某事所涉及的問題或挑戰。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice the difficulty of keeping students focused after lunch.","zh":"老師可能注意到午飯後讓學生保持專注的困難。"},{"en":"The difficulty of retaining talent increases when employees prefer start-up freedom.","zh":"當員工較喜歡初創自由，留住人才的困難會增加。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces what makes a task hard.","zh":"這個短語引入令任務困難的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hold on to","meaning":"留住","examples":[{"en":"Large firms may struggle to hold on to creative talent.","zh":"大企業可能難以留住創意人才。"},{"en":"To hold on to someone or something means to keep them and not lose them.","zh":"hold on to someone or something 指保留某人或某物，不失去他們。"},{"en":"A school may try to hold on to good teachers by giving them support and respect.","zh":"學校可能透過給予支持和尊重來留住好老師。"},{"en":"Companies offer rewards to hold on to employees who could leave and start their own firms.","zh":"公司提供獎勵來留住可能離職創業的員工。"},{"en":"The phrase describes retaining something valuable.","zh":"這個短語描述保留有價值事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the talent that","meaning":"創造意念的人才","examples":[{"en":"Companies want to keep the talent that created the idea.","zh":"公司想留住創造該意念的人才。"},{"en":"The talent that did something means the skilled people responsible for that achievement.","zh":"talent that did something 指負責該成就的有技能人士。"},{"en":"A film studio wants to keep the talent that made its first movie successful.","zh":"電影片廠想留住令首部電影成功的人才。"},{"en":"If the talent leaves after an acquisition, the buyer may lose the real source of value.","zh":"如果收購後人才離開，買方可能失去真正價值來源。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the people behind the idea, not the idea alone.","zh":"這個短語指出意念背後的人，而不只是意念本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"dream up","meaning":"構思出；想出","examples":[{"en":"Creative employees dream up new ideas.","zh":"有創意的員工構思出新意念。"},{"en":"To dream up something means to imagine or invent a new idea, often something unusual.","zh":"dream up something 指想像或發明新意念，通常是不尋常的想法。"},{"en":"A student may dream up a funny game to help classmates remember vocabulary.","zh":"學生可能構思出有趣遊戲，幫助同學記住詞彙。"},{"en":"Companies need people who can dream up ideas before competitors do.","zh":"公司需要能在競爭對手之前構思出意念的人。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests creative thinking, not ordinary planning.","zh":"這個短語暗示創意思考，而不是普通規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"develop ideas in-house","meaning":"在公司內部開發意念","examples":[{"en":"Many companies want to develop more ideas in-house.","zh":"許多公司想在公司內部開發更多意念。"},{"en":"To develop ideas in-house means to create and improve ideas inside the company rather than buying them from outside.","zh":"develop ideas in-house 指在公司內部創造和改善意念，而不是從外部購買。"},{"en":"A school may develop teaching materials in-house instead of buying worksheets from publishers.","zh":"學校可能自行開發教材，而不是向出版社購買工作紙。"},{"en":"Developing ideas internally can protect knowledge and build staff capability.","zh":"內部開發意念可以保護知識並建立員工能力。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts internal creation with outsourcing or acquisition.","zh":"這個短語把內部創造與外判或收購作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"shift its entire business focus","meaning":"轉移其整個業務焦點","examples":[{"en":"Procter and Gamble is shifting its entire business focus.","zh":"Procter and Gamble 正在轉移其整個業務焦點。"},{"en":"To shift an entire business focus means to change the main direction or priority of the whole company.","zh":"shift an entire business focus 指改變整間公司的主要方向或優先事項。"},{"en":"A tutoring centre may shift its business focus from exam drilling to adult workplace English.","zh":"補習中心可能把業務焦點由考試操練轉向成人職場英語。"},{"en":"A major focus shift can change products, teams, budgets, and rewards.","zh":"重大焦點轉移可以改變產品、團隊、預算和獎勵。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broad strategic change.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛策略改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"from countries to products","meaning":"由國家轉向產品","examples":[{"en":"The company is shifting its focus from countries to products.","zh":"該公司正把焦點由國家轉向產品。"},{"en":"From countries to products means changing the organising focus from geographic markets to product categories.","zh":"from countries to products 指把組織焦點由地理市場改為產品類別。"},{"en":"A business may move from regional teams to product teams so experts can share knowledge globally.","zh":"企業可能由地區團隊轉向產品團隊，讓專家能在全球分享知識。"},{"en":"This shift can help innovations spread across markets rather than stay in one country.","zh":"這種轉變可以幫助創新跨市場傳播，而不是停留在一個國家。"},{"en":"The phrase shows two different ways to organise a company.","zh":"這個短語顯示組織公司的兩種不同方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"get innovations accepted","meaning":"使創新獲得接受","examples":[{"en":"One aim is to get innovations accepted across the company.","zh":"其中一個目標是使創新在全公司範圍內獲得接受。"},{"en":"To get innovations accepted means to make new ideas approved, supported, and used by people in an organisation.","zh":"get innovations accepted 指令新意念獲組織內的人批准、支持和使用。"},{"en":"A school leader may need to get new teaching methods accepted by both teachers and parents.","zh":"學校領導可能需要使新教學方法獲老師和家長接受。"},{"en":"Innovations fail if people resist them or do not understand their value.","zh":"如果人們抗拒創新或不理解其價值，創新就會失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on adoption, not just invention.","zh":"這個短語重點是採用，而不只是發明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"across the company","meaning":"在全公司範圍內","examples":[{"en":"Innovations need to be accepted across the company.","zh":"創新需要在全公司範圍內被接受。"},{"en":"Across the company means throughout the whole organisation, not only in one department or team.","zh":"across the company 指遍及整個組織，而不只是一個部門或團隊。"},{"en":"A new safety rule must be followed across the company if it is to protect all workers.","zh":"如果新安全規則要保護所有工人，就必須在全公司範圍內遵守。"},{"en":"Company-wide acceptance helps an idea spread beyond the team that created it.","zh":"全公司接受有助意念傳播到創造它的團隊以外。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses broad internal coverage.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛的內部覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"elsewhere","meaning":"在其他地方；其他公司","examples":[{"en":"Elsewhere, companies have tried different ways to encourage innovation.","zh":"在其他公司，企業已嘗試不同方法鼓勵創新。"},{"en":"Elsewhere means in other places, situations, or organisations.","zh":"elsewhere 指在其他地方、情況或組織。"},{"en":"One school uses exams to motivate students; elsewhere, another school uses project work.","zh":"一間學校用考試激勵學生；在其他地方，另一間學校使用項目學習。"},{"en":"The word helps writers move from one example to other cases.","zh":"這個詞幫助作者由一個例子轉到其他個案。"},{"en":"It signals that the discussion is widening beyond the current company or place.","zh":"它表示討論正擴展到目前公司或地方以外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the search for innovation","meaning":"對創新的追求","examples":[{"en":"The search for innovation has led to intrapreneurship.","zh":"對創新的追求帶來了內部創業。"},{"en":"The search for innovation is the effort to find new ideas, products, or methods.","zh":"search for innovation 指尋找新意念、產品或方法的努力。"},{"en":"A school’s search for innovation may lead it to test online feedback tools.","zh":"學校對創新的追求可能令它測試網上回饋工具。"},{"en":"When competition increases, companies intensify their search for innovation.","zh":"當競爭增加，公司會加強對創新的追求。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an active attempt to find something new and useful.","zh":"這個短語描述主動尋找新而有用事物的嘗試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lead to a craze for","meaning":"引發對……的熱潮","examples":[{"en":"The search for innovation has led to a craze for intrapreneurship.","zh":"對創新的追求引發對內部創業的熱潮。"},{"en":"To lead to a craze for something means to cause many people or organisations to become very enthusiastic about it.","zh":"lead to a craze for something 指導致許多人或組織對某事非常熱衷。"},{"en":"Success stories about coding jobs may lead to a craze for programming courses.","zh":"關於編程工作的成功故事，可能引發對編程課程的熱潮。"},{"en":"A craze can spread quickly, but not every fashionable idea works well.","zh":"熱潮可以快速傳播，但不是每個流行想法都有效。"},{"en":"The phrase links a cause with sudden strong popularity.","zh":"這個短語把原因與突然強烈流行連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"intrapreneurship","meaning":"內部創業","examples":[{"en":"Intrapreneurship encourages employees to behave like entrepreneurs inside a firm.","zh":"內部創業鼓勵員工在公司內像創業者一樣行動。"},{"en":"Intrapreneurship is the practice of letting employees develop new business ideas within an existing company.","zh":"intrapreneurship 指讓員工在現有公司內發展新商業意念的做法。"},{"en":"A bank may use intrapreneurship by giving staff a small budget to build a new mobile payment service.","zh":"銀行可能透過給員工小額預算建立新流動支付服務來推行內部創業。"},{"en":"Intrapreneurship can keep creative employees from leaving to start their own firms.","zh":"內部創業可以阻止有創意員工離職創辦自己的公司。"},{"en":"The word means entrepreneurship inside a company.","zh":"這個詞意思是在公司內部進行創業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"devolving power","meaning":"下放權力","examples":[{"en":"Devolving power is one way to encourage innovation.","zh":"下放權力是鼓勵創新的其中一種方法。"},{"en":"Devolving power means giving decision-making authority from central leaders to smaller teams or lower levels.","zh":"devolving power 指把決策權由中央領導交給較小團隊或較低層級。"},{"en":"A head teacher devolves power when she lets departments choose their own teaching materials.","zh":"校長讓各科組自行選擇教材時，就是下放權力。"},{"en":"Devolved power can speed up innovation because teams do not need approval for every small decision.","zh":"下放權力可以加快創新，因為團隊不必每個小決定都等批准。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving authority downward or outward.","zh":"這個短語描述把權力向下或向外轉移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"internal ideas factories","meaning":"內部創意工廠","examples":[{"en":"Some companies set up internal ideas factories.","zh":"有些公司設立內部創意工廠。"},{"en":"Internal ideas factories are teams or departments inside a company created to generate new ideas.","zh":"internal ideas factories 指公司內部為產生新意念而設立的團隊或部門。"},{"en":"A retail company may create an internal ideas factory to test new store designs.","zh":"零售公司可能建立內部創意工廠，測試新店舖設計。"},{"en":"Internal idea teams can support innovation, but they may fail if the wider company ignores them.","zh":"內部創意團隊可以支援創新，但如果更廣泛公司忽視它們，就可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formal in-house innovation units.","zh":"這個短語描述正式的公司內部創新單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tracking stock","meaning":"追蹤股票","examples":[{"en":"Some firms offer tracking stock to retain talented staff.","zh":"有些公司提供追蹤股票以挽留有才能員工。"},{"en":"Tracking stock is a type of share linked to the performance of a particular division or project within a company.","zh":"tracking stock 指與公司內某一部門或項目表現掛鈎的一種股票。"},{"en":"A technology firm might offer tracking stock tied to a new AI unit.","zh":"科技公司可能提供與新 AI 部門掛鈎的追蹤股票。"},{"en":"Tracking stock can motivate employees because they benefit if their part of the business succeeds.","zh":"追蹤股票可以激勵員工，因為如果他們負責的業務部分成功，他們會受益。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a financial incentive connected to a specific business area.","zh":"這個短語指與特定業務範疇相關的財務誘因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"talented staff","meaning":"有才能的員工","examples":[{"en":"Companies offer incentives so that talented staff will not leave.","zh":"公司提供誘因，使有才能的員工不會離開。"},{"en":"Talented staff are employees with strong ability, creativity, knowledge, or performance.","zh":"talented staff 指具備強能力、創意、知識或表現的員工。"},{"en":"A school may try to keep talented staff by giving teachers training and promotion paths.","zh":"學校可能透過給老師培訓和晉升路徑來留住有才能員工。"},{"en":"Losing talented staff can damage a company because knowledge and ideas leave with them.","zh":"失去有才能員工可以傷害公司，因為知識和意念也會隨他們離開。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to valuable employees, not simply famous ones.","zh":"這個短語指有價值員工，而不只是有名的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"restructuring","meaning":"重組","examples":[{"en":"Some people think restructuring is not enough to create innovation.","zh":"有些人認為重組不足以創造創新。"},{"en":"Restructuring is the process of changing how an organisation is arranged, managed, or divided.","zh":"restructuring 指改變組織安排、管理或劃分方式的過程。"},{"en":"A company may restructure by merging two departments and creating a new product team.","zh":"公司可能透過合併兩個部門並建立新產品團隊來重組。"},{"en":"Restructuring can improve efficiency, but culture and incentives may also need to change.","zh":"重組可以改善效率，但文化和誘因可能也需要改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organisational change, not just staff movement.","zh":"這個短語指組織改變，而不只是人員調動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"established firms","meaning":"成熟企業；老牌公司","examples":[{"en":"Established firms may find disruptive innovation difficult.","zh":"成熟企業可能覺得顛覆性創新很困難。"},{"en":"Established firms are mature companies that have existed for a long time and already have customers, systems, and routines.","zh":"established firms 指存在已久、已有顧客、系統和慣例的成熟公司。"},{"en":"An established bank may struggle to copy a fast-moving online finance start-up.","zh":"老牌銀行可能難以模仿行動快速的網上金融初創。"},{"en":"Established firms can be strong, but their existing success may make change harder.","zh":"成熟企業可以很強，但既有成功可能令改變更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts older companies with new entrants.","zh":"這個短語把較舊公司與新進入者作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"look after current customers","meaning":"照顧現有客戶","examples":[{"en":"Established firms are good at looking after their current customers.","zh":"成熟企業擅長照顧現有客戶。"},{"en":"To look after current customers means to serve and protect the needs of people who already buy from the company.","zh":"look after current customers 指服務並保護已經向公司購買的人之需要。"},{"en":"A phone company looks after current customers by fixing network problems quickly.","zh":"電訊公司透過快速修復網絡問題來照顧現有客戶。"},{"en":"Focusing too much on current customers can make a firm miss new markets.","zh":"過度專注於現有客戶，可以令公司錯過新市場。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serving existing buyers well.","zh":"這個短語描述良好服務既有買家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"current customers","meaning":"現有客戶","examples":[{"en":"Current customers can influence a firm’s innovation decisions.","zh":"現有客戶可以影響公司的創新決定。"},{"en":"Current customers are people or organisations that already buy from a company.","zh":"current customers 指已經向公司購買的人或組織。"},{"en":"A gym’s current customers may ask for cleaner changing rooms instead of a new app.","zh":"健身室現有客戶可能要求更清潔更衣室，而不是新應用程式。"},{"en":"Companies listen to current customers because they provide steady revenue.","zh":"公司聆聽現有客戶，因為他們提供穩定收入。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to existing customers, not possible future customers.","zh":"這個短語指既有客戶，而不是可能的未來客戶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"hinder innovative behaviour","meaning":"阻礙創新行為","examples":[{"en":"Serving current customers can hinder innovative behaviour.","zh":"服務現有客戶可能阻礙創新行為。"},{"en":"To hinder innovative behaviour means to slow down or block actions that create new ideas or methods.","zh":"hinder innovative behaviour 指拖慢或阻止創造新意念或方法的行動。"},{"en":"Strict school rules may hinder innovative behaviour if teachers cannot try new lesson formats.","zh":"如果老師不能嘗試新課堂形式，嚴格校規可能阻礙創新行為。"},{"en":"A company may avoid risky ideas when current customers only want small improvements.","zh":"當現有客戶只想要小改善，公司可能避開高風險意念。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how something can restrict creativity.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事如何限制創意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"deal with","meaning":"處理；應對","examples":[{"en":"Firms need innovative behaviour to deal with disruptive technologies.","zh":"公司需要創新行為來應對顛覆性技術。"},{"en":"To deal with something means to handle, manage, or respond to it.","zh":"deal with something 指處理、管理或回應某事。"},{"en":"A teacher must deal with noisy students before a lesson can continue.","zh":"老師必須處理吵鬧學生，課堂才能繼續。"},{"en":"Companies need new strategies to deal with technologies that threaten old business models.","zh":"公司需要新策略應對威脅舊商業模式的技術。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical response to a problem or situation.","zh":"這個短語描述對問題或情況的實際回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"disruptive technologies","meaning":"顛覆性技術","examples":[{"en":"Disruptive technologies can threaten established firms.","zh":"顛覆性技術可以威脅成熟企業。"},{"en":"Disruptive technologies are new technologies that change markets and make old products or methods less useful.","zh":"disruptive technologies 指改變市場並令舊產品或方法較不有用的新技術。"},{"en":"Streaming video was disruptive technology for DVD rental shops.","zh":"串流影片對 DVD 租借店來說是顛覆性技術。"},{"en":"Such technologies threaten established firms because customers may move to cheaper or more convenient alternatives.","zh":"這類技術威脅成熟企業，因為顧客可能轉向更便宜或更方便的替代品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes technology that disturbs the existing order.","zh":"這個短語描述擾亂既有秩序的科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"hence","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"Hence, some firms create new businesses that compete with existing ones.","zh":"因此，有些公司創造與現有業務競爭的新業務。"},{"en":"Hence means for this reason or therefore.","zh":"hence 指基於這個原因或因此。"},{"en":"The class had not practised listening; hence, many students found the test difficult.","zh":"該班沒有練習聆聽；因此，許多學生覺得測驗困難。"},{"en":"The word links a cause to a logical result.","zh":"這個詞把原因與邏輯結果連起來。"},{"en":"It is more formal than “so”.","zh":"它比 “so” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the fashion for","meaning":"對……的潮流","examples":[{"en":"There is a fashion for cannibalisation among large firms.","zh":"大公司之間出現業務自我蠶食的潮流。"},{"en":"The fashion for something means a current trend or popular practice.","zh":"fashion for something 指現時趨勢或流行做法。"},{"en":"There is a fashion for open-plan offices, although not every worker likes them.","zh":"現在有開放式辦公室的潮流，雖然不是每位員工都喜歡。"},{"en":"A business fashion can spread quickly when famous companies appear to succeed with it.","zh":"當著名公司似乎靠某做法成功，商業潮流可以快速傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests popularity, not necessarily proven value.","zh":"這個短語暗示流行，但不一定表示已證明有價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"cannibalisation","meaning":"業務自我蠶食","examples":[{"en":"Cannibalisation means creating a new business that competes with an existing one.","zh":"業務自我蠶食指創造與現有業務競爭的新業務。"},{"en":"Cannibalisation happens when a company’s new product takes sales away from its own older product.","zh":"cannibalisation 發生在公司新產品搶走自己舊產品銷售時。"},{"en":"A restaurant chain may face cannibalisation if its new branch opens too close to an old one.","zh":"如果餐飲連鎖的新分店開得太接近舊分店，可能面對業務自我蠶食。"},{"en":"Firms may accept cannibalisation if the new product prevents competitors from taking the market.","zh":"如果新產品能防止競爭對手奪走市場，公司可能接受自我蠶食。"},{"en":"The word describes a company competing with itself.","zh":"這個詞描述公司與自己競爭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"existing ones","meaning":"現有業務","examples":[{"en":"Some new businesses are designed to fight existing ones.","zh":"有些新業務被設計來對抗現有業務。"},{"en":"Existing ones means the businesses, products, or systems that are already there.","zh":"existing ones 指已經存在的業務、產品或系統。"},{"en":"A school may create a new online course that competes with existing ones offered by private tutors.","zh":"學校可能創建新的網上課程，與私人導師提供的現有課程競爭。"},{"en":"New services can threaten existing ones when customers prefer the newer option.","zh":"當顧客較喜歡新選項，新服務可以威脅現有業務。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to things already mentioned or already operating.","zh":"這個短語指回已提及或已運作的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"Bank One, for instance, established an Internet bank.","zh":"例如，Bank One 建立了一間網上銀行。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance 指例如。"},{"en":"Some students learn better visually; for instance, diagrams may help them remember science processes.","zh":"有些學生透過視覺學得更好；例如，圖表可能幫助他們記住科學過程。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a specific example to support a general point.","zh":"這個短語引入具體例子來支持一般觀點。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining abstract ideas with real cases.","zh":"它適合用真實個案解釋抽象想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Internet bank","meaning":"網上銀行","examples":[{"en":"Wingspan is an Internet bank that competes with physical branches.","zh":"Wingspan 是一間與實體分行競爭的網上銀行。"},{"en":"An Internet bank is a bank that provides services mainly online rather than through physical branches.","zh":"Internet bank 指主要透過網上而非實體分行提供服務的銀行。"},{"en":"An Internet bank may let customers open accounts, transfer money, and apply for loans through a website.","zh":"網上銀行可能讓顧客透過網站開戶、轉帳和申請貸款。"},{"en":"Internet banks can reduce branch costs but may worry customers who prefer face-to-face service.","zh":"網上銀行可以減少分行成本，但可能令偏好面對面服務的顧客擔心。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to banking delivered through the internet.","zh":"這個短語指透過互聯網提供的銀行服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"compete with","meaning":"與……競爭","examples":[{"en":"The Internet bank competes with the company’s physical branches.","zh":"網上銀行與公司的實體分行競爭。"},{"en":"To compete with someone or something means to try to attract the same customers, users, marks, or attention.","zh":"compete with someone or something 指嘗試吸引同一批顧客、使用者、分數或注意力。"},{"en":"Small shops compete with supermarkets by offering personal service and local products.","zh":"小店透過提供個人化服務和本地產品與超市競爭。"},{"en":"Competition can force businesses to improve prices, quality, and convenience.","zh":"競爭可以迫使企業改善價格、質素和便利程度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rivalry for the same market or goal.","zh":"這個短語描述對同一市場或目標的競爭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"physical branches","meaning":"實體分行","examples":[{"en":"Traditional banks operate through physical branches.","zh":"傳統銀行透過實體分行營運。"},{"en":"Physical branches are real bank offices that customers can visit in person.","zh":"physical branches 指顧客可以親身到訪的真實銀行辦公地點。"},{"en":"Older customers may prefer physical branches because they can speak to staff face to face.","zh":"年長顧客可能較喜歡實體分行，因為可以面對面與職員交談。"},{"en":"Physical branches cost money to rent and staff, so online banks may be cheaper to run.","zh":"實體分行需要租金和人手成本，所以網上銀行運行可能較便宜。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts real locations with online services.","zh":"這個短語把真實地點與網上服務作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Internet initiative","meaning":"互聯網計劃","examples":[{"en":"General Electric launched an Internet initiative.","zh":"General Electric 推出了一項互聯網計劃。"},{"en":"An Internet initiative is a planned business project using the internet to improve services, sales, or operations.","zh":"Internet initiative 指使用互聯網改善服務、銷售或營運的有計劃商業項目。"},{"en":"A school may launch an Internet initiative to let parents check homework and attendance online.","zh":"學校可能推出互聯網計劃，讓家長網上查看功課和出席情況。"},{"en":"Such initiatives can modernise an organisation if staff and customers actually use them.","zh":"如果員工和顧客真正使用，這類計劃可以令組織現代化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a deliberate online project.","zh":"這個短語描述有意識推行的網上項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"nobody could doubt that","meaning":"沒有人會懷疑……","examples":[{"en":"Nobody could doubt that innovation matters.","zh":"沒有人會懷疑創新很重要。"},{"en":"Nobody could doubt that means the statement is so clear that almost everyone would agree.","zh":"nobody could doubt that 指某陳述非常清楚，幾乎所有人都會同意。"},{"en":"Nobody could doubt that clean water is essential for public health.","zh":"沒有人會懷疑清潔食水對公共健康至關重要。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly emphasises certainty or broad agreement.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調確定性或廣泛共識。"},{"en":"It is useful when introducing a point that the writer treats as obvious.","zh":"當作者把某重點視為明顯時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"innovation matters","meaning":"創新很重要","examples":[{"en":"The passage accepts that innovation matters.","zh":"文章承認創新很重要。"},{"en":"Innovation matters means new ideas and improvements are important and have real effects.","zh":"innovation matters 指新意念和改善很重要，並有實際影響。"},{"en":"In education, innovation matters when old teaching methods no longer help students learn.","zh":"在教育中，當舊教學方法不再幫助學生學習，創新就很重要。"},{"en":"Innovation matters because it can create better services, lower costs, and new opportunities.","zh":"創新很重要，因為它可以創造更好服務、降低成本和帶來新機會。"},{"en":"The phrase is a simple way to stress the importance of change and creativity.","zh":"這個短語是強調改變和創意重要性的簡單說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"quite so pessimistic","meaning":"如此悲觀","examples":[{"en":"The writer asks whether large firms need to be quite so pessimistic.","zh":"作者問大公司是否需要如此悲觀。"},{"en":"Quite so pessimistic means as negative or doubtful as they appear to be.","zh":"quite so pessimistic 指像它們看起來那樣負面或懷疑。"},{"en":"A student should not be quite so pessimistic after one bad test result.","zh":"學生不應在一次測驗成績差後就如此悲觀。"},{"en":"Companies may feel pessimistic when start-ups grow quickly, but the facts may be more balanced.","zh":"當初創快速成長，公司可能感到悲觀，但事實可能更平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase questions whether the negative attitude is too strong.","zh":"這個短語質疑負面態度是否過強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a recent survey of","meaning":"一項關於……的近期調查","examples":[{"en":"A recent survey of top innovations challenged the pessimistic view.","zh":"一項關於頂尖創新的近期調查挑戰了悲觀看法。"},{"en":"A recent survey of something is a newly conducted study that collects information about that topic.","zh":"recent survey of something 指最近進行、收集關於該主題資訊的研究。"},{"en":"A recent survey of students may show that most prefer mixed online and face-to-face lessons.","zh":"一項關於學生的近期調查可能顯示大多數人偏好網上和面授混合課程。"},{"en":"Survey evidence can challenge assumptions by showing a wider pattern.","zh":"調查證據可以透過顯示更廣泛模式來挑戰假設。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces fresh research on a specific subject.","zh":"這個短語引入關於特定主題的新近研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"top 50 innovations","meaning":"五十大創新","examples":[{"en":"The survey examined the top 50 innovations in America.","zh":"該調查研究了美國五十大創新。"},{"en":"Top 50 innovations means the fifty most important, successful, or highly ranked new ideas or products in a list.","zh":"top 50 innovations 指名單中最重要、最成功或排名最高的五十項新意念或產品。"},{"en":"A magazine may list the top 50 innovations in healthcare to show which tools changed patient care.","zh":"雜誌可能列出醫療五十大創新，以顯示哪些工具改變病人護理。"},{"en":"Studying top innovations helps identify where valuable ideas come from.","zh":"研究頂尖創新有助識別有價值意念來自哪裏。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a ranked group of major innovations.","zh":"這個短語指一組排名靠前的重大創新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"as likely to come from…as from…","meaning":"來自……的可能性與來自……一樣高","examples":[{"en":"Ideas are as likely to come from big firms as from small ones.","zh":"意念來自大公司的可能性與來自小公司一樣高。"},{"en":"As likely to come from A as from B means the chance is equal for both sources.","zh":"as likely to come from A as from B 指來自兩個來源的機會相同。"},{"en":"A good classroom idea is as likely to come from a quiet student as from a confident one.","zh":"好課堂意念來自安靜學生的可能性，與來自自信學生一樣高。"},{"en":"This phrase challenges assumptions when people expect one source to be more important.","zh":"當人們預期某一來源更重要時，這個短語會挑戰假設。"},{"en":"It clearly shows equal probability between two origins.","zh":"它清楚顯示兩個來源之間機率相等。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"small ones","meaning":"小公司","examples":[{"en":"Innovative ideas may come from big firms or small ones.","zh":"創新意念可能來自大公司或小公司。"},{"en":"Small ones means small companies or small organisations, depending on the comparison.","zh":"small ones 指小公司或小型組織，視乎比較內容而定。"},{"en":"Large schools may have resources, but small ones may test new teaching methods faster.","zh":"大學校可能有資源，但小學校可能更快測試新教學方法。"},{"en":"Small firms can innovate quickly because fewer people need to approve each decision.","zh":"小公司可以快速創新，因為每個決定需要批准的人較少。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to smaller members of the group being compared.","zh":"這個短語指回被比較群體中較小的成員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"sceptical note","meaning":"懷疑的聲音","examples":[{"en":"Another sceptical note is sounded by Amar Bhidé.","zh":"Amar Bhidé 提出了另一個懷疑的聲音。"},{"en":"A sceptical note is a comment or argument that expresses doubt about an idea.","zh":"sceptical note 指表達對某意念懷疑的評論或論點。"},{"en":"In a meeting, a teacher may sound a sceptical note about buying tablets before training staff.","zh":"在會議中，老師可能對在培訓職員前購買平板電腦提出懷疑聲音。"},{"en":"Sceptical comments can prevent people from accepting fashionable ideas too quickly.","zh":"懷疑評論可以防止人們太快接受流行想法。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a cautious or doubtful viewpoint.","zh":"這個短語引入謹慎或懷疑的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be sounded by","meaning":"由……提出","examples":[{"en":"A sceptical note is sounded by a Harvard Business School professor.","zh":"一個懷疑的聲音由一位哈佛商學院教授提出。"},{"en":"To be sounded by someone means to be expressed or raised by that person.","zh":"be sounded by someone 指由某人表達或提出。"},{"en":"A warning about exam stress was sounded by several school counsellors.","zh":"關於考試壓力的警告由幾位學校輔導員提出。"},{"en":"When a concern is sounded by an expert, people may take it more seriously.","zh":"當憂慮由專家提出，人們可能更認真看待。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and often used with warnings, doubts, or opinions.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常與警告、懷疑或意見一起使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"colleague of","meaning":"……的同事","examples":[{"en":"Amar Bhidé is a colleague of Clayton Christensen.","zh":"Amar Bhidé 是 Clayton Christensen 的同事。"},{"en":"A colleague of someone is a person who works with them in the same organisation or profession.","zh":"colleague of someone 指在同一組織或職業中與某人共事的人。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask a colleague for advice about a difficult class.","zh":"老師可能向同事請教如何處理困難班級。"},{"en":"Mentioning a colleague can show someone’s professional background or intellectual connection.","zh":"提及某人的同事可以顯示其專業背景或思想聯繫。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a work relationship.","zh":"這個短語指出工作關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"entrepreneurship","meaning":"創業精神；創業","examples":[{"en":"Bhidé has written a book on entrepreneurship.","zh":"Bhidé 寫過一本關於創業精神的書。"},{"en":"Entrepreneurship is the activity of starting and developing businesses, especially with new ideas and risk.","zh":"entrepreneurship 指創立和發展企業的活動，尤其涉及新意念和風險。"},{"en":"A student practises entrepreneurship when she creates a small online shop and learns from customers.","zh":"學生建立小型網店並向顧客學習時，就是實踐創業。"},{"en":"Entrepreneurship can create jobs, but it also involves uncertainty and possible failure.","zh":"創業可以創造職位，但也涉及不確定性和可能失敗。"},{"en":"The word refers to the process and spirit of creating businesses.","zh":"這個詞指創造企業的過程和精神。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Rather than reinventing themselves, big companies should focus on certain projects.","zh":"大公司應專注於某些項目，而不是徹底改造自己。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of, and it clearly contrasts two choices.","zh":"rather than 指「而不是」，清楚對比兩個選擇。"},{"en":"Students should fix common grammar errors rather than memorise impressive words only.","zh":"學生應修正常見文法錯誤，而不是只背誦華麗詞語。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show which option is preferred or more sensible.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示哪個選項較可取或較合理。"},{"en":"It separates the suggested action from the rejected one.","zh":"它把建議行動與被否定行動分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reinvent themselves","meaning":"徹底改造自己","examples":[{"en":"Some people think big companies should reinvent themselves.","zh":"有些人認為大公司應該徹底改造自己。"},{"en":"To reinvent themselves means to change their identity, strategy, or way of operating in a major way.","zh":"reinvent themselves 指大幅改變自己的身份、策略或營運方式。"},{"en":"A bookstore may reinvent itself by becoming a café, event space, and online reading platform.","zh":"書店可能透過變成咖啡店、活動空間和網上閱讀平台來徹底改造自己。"},{"en":"Reinvention can help an organisation survive when old customers or markets disappear.","zh":"當舊顧客或市場消失，徹底改造可以幫助組織生存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep transformation, not small improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述深層轉型，而不是小改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"concentrate on","meaning":"專注於","examples":[{"en":"Bhidé believes big companies should concentrate on particular projects.","zh":"Bhidé 認為大公司應專注於特定項目。"},{"en":"To concentrate on something means to focus attention, money, or effort on it.","zh":"concentrate on something 指把注意力、金錢或努力集中在某事上。"},{"en":"A student may concentrate on listening practice if that is her weakest skill.","zh":"如果聆聽是學生最弱的技能，她可能專注於聆聽練習。"},{"en":"Companies concentrate on certain projects when resources are limited and choices must be made.","zh":"當資源有限而必須作選擇，公司會專注於某些項目。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving priority to one area.","zh":"這個短語描述優先處理某一範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"high costs and low uncertainty","meaning":"高成本、低不確定性","examples":[{"en":"Large firms should focus on projects with high costs and low uncertainty.","zh":"大公司應專注於高成本、低不確定性的項目。"},{"en":"High costs and low uncertainty means a project is expensive but its risks and outcomes are relatively clear.","zh":"high costs and low uncertainty 指項目昂貴，但風險和結果相對清楚。"},{"en":"Building a new factory may involve high costs and low uncertainty if demand is already proven.","zh":"如果需求已被證明，興建新工廠可能涉及高成本、低不確定性。"},{"en":"Big companies are suited to such projects because they have money and can manage known risks.","zh":"大公司適合這類項目，因為它們有資金並能管理已知風險。"},{"en":"The phrase combines financial scale with predictable results.","zh":"這個短語結合財務規模和可預測結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"low costs and high uncertainty","meaning":"低成本、高不確定性","examples":[{"en":"Small entrepreneurs can handle projects with low costs and high uncertainty.","zh":"小型創業者可以處理低成本、高不確定性的項目。"},{"en":"Low costs and high uncertainty means a project is cheap to test but its future success is unclear.","zh":"low costs and high uncertainty 指項目測試成本低，但未來成功與否不清楚。"},{"en":"A student can test a low-cost, high-uncertainty idea by selling handmade cards online for one month.","zh":"學生可以透過網上賣手工卡一個月，測試低成本、高不確定性的意念。"},{"en":"Small firms can try uncertain ideas because failure may not destroy the whole business.","zh":"小公司可以嘗試不確定意念，因為失敗未必摧毀整個企業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes experiments that are cheap but risky in outcome.","zh":"這個短語描述便宜但結果有風險的實驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"leave something to","meaning":"把……留給","examples":[{"en":"Bhidé thinks big firms should leave uncertain low-cost projects to entrepreneurs.","zh":"Bhidé 認為大公司應把不確定的低成本項目留給創業者。"},{"en":"To leave something to someone means to let that person or group handle it instead of doing it yourself.","zh":"leave something to someone 指讓某人或某群體處理某事，而不是自己做。"},{"en":"A teacher may leave poster design to artistic students while she checks the content.","zh":"老師可能把海報設計留給有藝術感的學生，而自己檢查內容。"},{"en":"Companies leave some risky experiments to start-ups because start-ups can move faster.","zh":"公司把一些高風險實驗留給初創，因為初創行動更快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes handing responsibility to others.","zh":"這個短語描述把責任交給他人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"as ideas mature","meaning":"隨着意念成熟","examples":[{"en":"As ideas mature, big companies can adopt them.","zh":"隨着意念成熟，大公司可以採用它們。"},{"en":"As ideas mature means as ideas become more developed, tested, and clearer in value.","zh":"as ideas mature 指隨着意念變得更發展成熟、更經過測試，價值更清晰。"},{"en":"A classroom project idea matures when students test it, improve it, and see real results.","zh":"當學生測試、改善並看到真實結果，課堂項目意念就會成熟。"},{"en":"Mature ideas are easier for big firms to judge because risks become more visible.","zh":"成熟意念較容易讓大公司判斷，因為風險變得更可見。"},{"en":"The phrase compares ideas to living things that grow over time.","zh":"這個短語把意念比作會隨時間成長的生命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"risks and rewards","meaning":"風險與回報","examples":[{"en":"The risks and rewards of mature ideas become clearer.","zh":"成熟意念的風險與回報變得更清楚。"},{"en":"Risks and rewards are the possible losses and possible benefits of a decision.","zh":"risks and rewards 指一個決定可能帶來的損失和好處。"},{"en":"Before joining a new job, a person should consider the risks and rewards of leaving the old one.","zh":"加入新工作前，一個人應考慮離開舊工作的風險與回報。"},{"en":"Investors compare risks and rewards before deciding whether to fund a start-up.","zh":"投資者在決定是否資助初創前會比較風險與回報。"},{"en":"The phrase balances danger against potential gain.","zh":"這個短語把危險與潛在收益作平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"become more quantifiable","meaning":"變得更可量化","examples":[{"en":"The risks and rewards become more quantifiable over time.","zh":"風險與回報隨時間變得更可量化。"},{"en":"To become more quantifiable means to become easier to measure with numbers or evidence.","zh":"become more quantifiable 指變得更容易用數字或證據量度。"},{"en":"A student’s progress becomes more quantifiable after several mock test scores are collected.","zh":"收集幾次模擬試分數後，學生進步會變得更可量化。"},{"en":"Investors prefer quantifiable risks because they can compare possible outcomes more clearly.","zh":"投資者偏好可量化風險，因為他們能更清楚比較可能結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving from guesswork toward measurable judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述由猜測走向可量度判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"adopt them","meaning":"採用它們","examples":[{"en":"Big companies can adopt ideas after they mature.","zh":"大公司可以在意念成熟後採用它們。"},{"en":"To adopt ideas means to begin using or supporting those ideas.","zh":"adopt ideas 指開始使用或支持那些意念。"},{"en":"A school may adopt a new reading programme after a pilot class shows strong results.","zh":"學校可能在試驗班顯示強成果後，採用新的閱讀計劃。"},{"en":"Companies adopt mature ideas when evidence makes the risks easier to judge.","zh":"當證據令風險較易判斷，公司會採用成熟意念。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to taking up something developed by others or earlier teams.","zh":"這個短語指採納由他人或早期團隊發展的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"discredit the view that","meaning":"駁斥……的看法","examples":[{"en":"Mr Sanders had to discredit the view that new-product jobs were unimportant.","zh":"Sanders 先生必須駁斥新產品工作不重要的看法。"},{"en":"To discredit the view that something is true means to show that the opinion is wrong or unreliable.","zh":"discredit the view that something is true 指顯示某觀點是錯誤或不可靠的。"},{"en":"A teacher may discredit the view that grammar is useless by showing how it improves writing clarity.","zh":"老師可能透過顯示文法如何提升寫作清晰度，駁斥文法無用的看法。"},{"en":"Discrediting a harmful belief can change how people treat certain work or workers.","zh":"駁斥有害信念可以改變人們如何看待某些工作或工人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes challenging and weakening an opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述挑戰並削弱某種意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"jobs involving","meaning":"涉及……的工作","examples":[{"en":"Some people looked down on jobs involving work on new products.","zh":"有些人看不起涉及新產品工作的職位。"},{"en":"Jobs involving something are jobs that include that activity as part of the work.","zh":"jobs involving something 指包含某活動作為工作一部分的職位。"},{"en":"Jobs involving customer service require patience and clear communication.","zh":"涉及顧客服務的工作需要耐性和清楚溝通。"},{"en":"If jobs involve new products, workers may face uncertainty and frequent changes.","zh":"如果工作涉及新產品，員工可能面對不確定性和頻繁改變。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what kind of work a job includes.","zh":"這個短語指出某工作包含甚麼內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"new products","meaning":"新產品","examples":[{"en":"Work on new products can be central to innovation.","zh":"新產品工作可以是創新的核心。"},{"en":"New products are goods or services that a company has recently created or is preparing to sell.","zh":"new products 指公司最近創造或準備出售的貨品或服務。"},{"en":"A food company may test new products such as low-sugar drinks or ready-made lunches.","zh":"食品公司可能測試低糖飲品或即食午餐等新產品。"},{"en":"New products can attract customers, but they may fail if they do not solve real problems.","zh":"新產品可以吸引顧客，但如果不能解決真實問題，也可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to recent or developing market offerings.","zh":"這個短語指近期或正在開發的市場供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"couldn’t hack it","meaning":"應付不來；做不來","examples":[{"en":"Some people thought new-product jobs were for those who couldn’t hack it in the real business.","zh":"有些人認為新產品工作是給那些在真正核心業務中應付不來的人做的。"},{"en":"Couldn’t hack it means could not handle the pressure, difficulty, or demands of a task.","zh":"couldn’t hack it 指無法應付某任務的壓力、難度或要求。"},{"en":"A student who cannot manage the workload may feel she cannot hack it in a top exam class.","zh":"無法處理工作量的學生，可能覺得自己在頂尖考試班中應付不來。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and can sound harsh or dismissive.","zh":"這個短語較口語，聽起來可以苛刻或輕蔑。"},{"en":"It suggests failure to cope, not lack of basic intelligence.","zh":"它暗示無法承受，而不是缺乏基本智力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the real business","meaning":"真正的核心業務","examples":[{"en":"Some employees saw new-product work as separate from the real business.","zh":"有些員工把新產品工作視為與真正核心業務分開。"},{"en":"The real business means what people consider the main, serious, or core work of a company.","zh":"real business 指人們認為公司主要、嚴肅或核心的工作。"},{"en":"In a school, some may think exam teaching is the real business while clubs are secondary.","zh":"在學校，有些人可能認為考試教學是真正核心業務，而學會是次要。"},{"en":"Calling one area “the real business” can make other important work seem less valuable.","zh":"把某一範疇稱為「真正核心業務」可以令其他重要工作看似較無價值。"},{"en":"The phrase reveals what a group sees as central.","zh":"這個短語揭示某群體視甚麼為中心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"change the culture","meaning":"改變文化","examples":[{"en":"Mr Sanders tried to change the company culture.","zh":"Sanders 先生嘗試改變公司文化。"},{"en":"To change the culture means to alter shared attitudes, habits, values, and expectations inside a group or organisation.","zh":"change the culture 指改變群體或組織內共享的態度、習慣、價值和期望。"},{"en":"A school changes its culture when teachers begin to treat mistakes as learning opportunities.","zh":"當老師開始把錯誤視為學習機會，學校就在改變文化。"},{"en":"Culture change is hard because people may keep old habits even after rules change.","zh":"文化改變很困難，因為即使規則改變，人們也可能保留舊習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deeper change than changing structure or slogans.","zh":"這個短語描述比改變結構或口號更深層的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"preach fuzzy concepts","meaning":"宣揚模糊概念","examples":[{"en":"He did not rely only on preaching fuzzy concepts.","zh":"他沒有只依賴宣揚模糊概念。"},{"en":"To preach fuzzy concepts means to talk repeatedly about vague ideas without giving clear practical actions.","zh":"preach fuzzy concepts 指反覆談論含糊想法，但沒有清楚實際行動。"},{"en":"A manager who only says “be excellent” is preaching fuzzy concepts if no one knows what to do differently.","zh":"如果經理只說「要卓越」但沒有人知道要如何改變，他就是在宣揚模糊概念。"},{"en":"Vague talk may inspire people briefly, but it rarely changes behaviour without incentives and systems.","zh":"含糊說法可能短暫鼓舞人，但沒有誘因和制度，很少能改變行為。"},{"en":"The phrase is critical of unclear management language.","zh":"這個短語批評不清楚的管理語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"fuzzy concepts","meaning":"模糊概念","examples":[{"en":"Innovation culture can be harmed by vague, fuzzy concepts.","zh":"創新文化可能被含糊的模糊概念傷害。"},{"en":"Fuzzy concepts are ideas that sound positive but are unclear, vague, or hard to apply.","zh":"fuzzy concepts 指聽起來正面但不清楚、含糊或難以應用的想法。"},{"en":"“Work smarter” can be a fuzzy concept if the manager gives no examples or tools.","zh":"如果經理沒有給例子或工具，“work smarter” 可以是模糊概念。"},{"en":"Fuzzy concepts confuse workers because they do not show what actions are expected.","zh":"模糊概念令工人困惑，因為它們沒有顯示期望甚麼行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unclear ideas that need practical definition.","zh":"這個短語描述需要實際界定的不清楚想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"hard incentives","meaning":"實質誘因","examples":[{"en":"He introduced hard incentives to encourage innovation.","zh":"他引入實質誘因來鼓勵創新。"},{"en":"Hard incentives are concrete rewards or penalties, such as money, promotion, or clear performance targets.","zh":"hard incentives 指具體獎勵或懲罰，例如金錢、晉升或清晰表現目標。"},{"en":"A school may use hard incentives by giving teachers time and funding for successful new projects.","zh":"學校可能透過為成功新項目提供時間和資金，使用實質誘因。"},{"en":"Hard incentives change behaviour because people can see real consequences.","zh":"實質誘因會改變行為，因為人們能看見真實後果。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts practical rewards with vague encouragement.","zh":"這個短語把實際獎勵與含糊鼓勵作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"increase the rewards for","meaning":"增加給予……的獎勵","examples":[{"en":"The company increased the rewards for successful innovators.","zh":"該公司增加給予成功創新者的獎勵。"},{"en":"To increase the rewards for someone means to give them greater benefits when they perform well.","zh":"increase the rewards for someone 指當某人表現良好時給予更大好處。"},{"en":"A school may increase the rewards for students who read regularly by giving certificates and leadership roles.","zh":"學校可能透過頒發證書和領袖角色，增加給予定期閱讀學生的獎勵。"},{"en":"Higher rewards can encourage people to spend more effort on difficult goals.","zh":"更高獎勵可以鼓勵人們為困難目標付出更多努力。"},{"en":"The phrase connects stronger incentives with desired behaviour.","zh":"這個短語把更強誘因與期望行為連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"come up with successful new ideas","meaning":"想出成功的新意念","examples":[{"en":"Employees were rewarded for coming up with successful new ideas.","zh":"員工因想出成功的新意念而獲獎勵。"},{"en":"To come up with successful new ideas means to create new ideas that actually work or produce good results.","zh":"come up with successful new ideas 指創造實際有效或產生好結果的新意念。"},{"en":"A teacher comes up with a successful new idea when a new activity helps weak students speak more.","zh":"當新活動幫助較弱學生多說話，老師就是想出成功的新意念。"},{"en":"Successful ideas are rewarded because they create value beyond ordinary work.","zh":"成功意念獲獎勵，因為它們創造超越普通工作的價值。"},{"en":"The phrase combines creativity with practical success.","zh":"這個短語結合創意與實際成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"not punish those whose experiments fail","meaning":"不懲罰實驗失敗的人","examples":[{"en":"The company avoided punishing those whose experiments fail.","zh":"該公司避免懲罰實驗失敗的人。"},{"en":"Not punish those whose experiments fail means not penalise people simply because a reasonable trial did not succeed.","zh":"not punish those whose experiments fail 指不因合理嘗試沒有成功而懲罰人。"},{"en":"A science teacher should not punish students whose experiments fail if they followed the method carefully.","zh":"如果學生仔細跟從方法，即使實驗失敗，科學老師也不應懲罰他們。"},{"en":"If people fear punishment for failure, they may stop trying new ideas.","zh":"如果人們害怕因失敗受罰，他們可能停止嘗試新意念。"},{"en":"The phrase supports a culture where sensible risk-taking is allowed.","zh":"這個短語支持容許合理冒險的文化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"experiments fail","meaning":"實驗失敗","examples":[{"en":"Innovation requires tolerance when experiments fail.","zh":"當實驗失敗時，創新需要包容。"},{"en":"Experiments fail when tests or trials do not produce the hoped-for result.","zh":"experiments fail 指測試或嘗試沒有產生希望中的結果。"},{"en":"A cooking experiment fails if the new recipe tastes bad even after careful preparation.","zh":"如果新食譜即使仔細準備後仍味道差，烹飪實驗就失敗。"},{"en":"Failed experiments can still teach useful lessons about what does not work.","zh":"失敗實驗仍可以教人哪些方法行不通。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an unsuccessful trial, not a useless effort.","zh":"這個短語描述不成功的嘗試，而不是沒有價值的努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the genesis of","meaning":"……的起源","examples":[{"en":"The genesis of Depend lay in a previous failure.","zh":"Depend 的起源在於之前一次失敗。"},{"en":"The genesis of something is its origin, beginning, or earliest source.","zh":"genesis of something 指某事物的起源、開始或最早來源。"},{"en":"The genesis of a school club may be one student’s complaint that there were no debate activities.","zh":"一個學校學會的起源，可能是一名學生抱怨沒有辯論活動。"},{"en":"Understanding the genesis of a product can show how failure led to later success.","zh":"理解產品起源可以顯示失敗如何帶來日後成功。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and means where something started.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是某事從哪裏開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"current hits","meaning":"現時熱賣產品","examples":[{"en":"Depend is one of the firm’s current hits.","zh":"Depend 是該公司現時熱賣產品之一。"},{"en":"Current hits are products or services that are popular and successful now.","zh":"current hits 指現在受歡迎且成功的產品或服務。"},{"en":"A bubble tea shop’s current hit may be a mango drink that customers keep ordering.","zh":"珍珠奶茶店現時熱賣產品可能是顧客一直點的芒果飲品。"},{"en":"Current hits can bring profit, but companies still need future products.","zh":"現時熱賣產品可以帶來利潤，但公司仍需要未來產品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes present success in the market.","zh":"這個短語描述市場中的當前成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"dignified","meaning":"有尊嚴的；較體面的","examples":[{"en":"Depend was designed as a more dignified product.","zh":"Depend 被設計成一種較有尊嚴的產品。"},{"en":"Dignified means allowing people to feel respected, decent, and not embarrassed.","zh":"dignified 指讓人感到被尊重、得體而不尷尬。"},{"en":"A hospital gown is more dignified if it covers patients properly and lets them move comfortably.","zh":"如果病人袍能適當遮蓋病人並讓他們舒適活動，就較有尊嚴。"},{"en":"A dignified design matters when a product is connected with sensitive personal needs.","zh":"當產品與敏感個人需要有關，有尊嚴的設計很重要。"},{"en":"The word stresses respect for the user’s self-image.","zh":"這個詞強調尊重使用者的自我形象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"incontinence garment","meaning":"失禁用品","examples":[{"en":"Depend is a more dignified incontinence garment.","zh":"Depend 是一種較有尊嚴的失禁用品。"},{"en":"An incontinence garment is clothing or underwear designed for people who cannot fully control urination or bowel movements.","zh":"incontinence garment 指為無法完全控制小便或排便的人設計的衣物或內褲。"},{"en":"Older patients may use incontinence garments to stay dry during long journeys.","zh":"年長病人在長途旅程中可能使用失禁用品以保持乾爽。"},{"en":"A well-designed garment can protect health while reducing embarrassment.","zh":"設計良好的用品可以保護健康，同時減少尷尬。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a practical product for a sensitive medical condition.","zh":"這個短語指針對敏感醫療情況的實用產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"lie in","meaning":"在於；源於","examples":[{"en":"The idea for the product lay in an earlier unsuccessful product.","zh":"該產品的意念源於較早前一個不成功產品。"},{"en":"To lie in something means to be found in or have its source in that thing.","zh":"lie in something 指存在於某事之中，或源自某事。"},{"en":"The problem may lie in poor instructions, not in students’ ability.","zh":"問題可能在於指示不清，而不是學生能力。"},{"en":"A successful idea can lie in a failed experiment if people learn from it carefully.","zh":"如果人們仔細從失敗實驗中學習，成功意念可以源於其中。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the real location or origin of something.","zh":"這個短語指出某事的真正位置或來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"previous miss","meaning":"之前失敗的產品","examples":[{"en":"A previous miss eventually helped produce a successful product.","zh":"之前失敗的產品最終幫助產生成功產品。"},{"en":"A previous miss is an earlier product, idea, or attempt that failed to succeed.","zh":"previous miss 指較早前未能成功的產品、意念或嘗試。"},{"en":"A restaurant’s previous miss may be a dish that customers did not order again.","zh":"餐廳之前失敗的產品可能是顧客不再點的菜式。"},{"en":"A miss can still be useful if the company understands why it failed.","zh":"如果公司理解它為何失敗，失敗產品仍可以有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an earlier failure, often in product development.","zh":"這個短語描述較早的失敗，常用於產品開發。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"disposable underwear","meaning":"即棄內褲","examples":[{"en":"Kotex Personals was a form of disposable underwear.","zh":"Kotex Personals 是一種即棄內褲。"},{"en":"Disposable underwear is underwear designed to be thrown away after use rather than washed and reused.","zh":"disposable underwear 指設計成使用後丟棄，而不是清洗重用的內褲。"},{"en":"Hospitals may provide disposable underwear to patients after surgery.","zh":"醫院可能在手術後向病人提供即棄內褲。"},{"en":"Disposable products can be convenient but may create more waste.","zh":"即棄產品可以方便，但可能產生更多廢物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes single-use underwear.","zh":"這個短語描述一次性內褲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"menstruating women","meaning":"來月經的女性","examples":[{"en":"The earlier product was designed for menstruating women.","zh":"較早的產品是為來月經的女性設計的。"},{"en":"Menstruating women are women who are having their monthly period.","zh":"menstruating women 指正在經歷每月月經的女性。"},{"en":"Menstruating women may need comfortable, hygienic products for daily activities and work.","zh":"來月經的女性可能需要舒適、衛生的產品來進行日常活動和工作。"},{"en":"Products for menstruating women must consider privacy, comfort, safety, and dignity.","zh":"為來月經女性設計的產品必須考慮私隱、舒適、安全和尊嚴。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a normal biological condition, not an illness.","zh":"這個短語指正常生理情況，而不是疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"creative destruction","meaning":"創造性破壞","examples":[{"en":"The passage asks whether creative destruction can make big firms more creative.","zh":"文章問創造性破壞能否令大公司更有創意。"},{"en":"Creative destruction is the process where new ideas, technologies, or businesses replace old ones.","zh":"creative destruction 指新意念、技術或企業取代舊事物的過程。"},{"en":"Streaming services caused creative destruction in the DVD rental market.","zh":"串流服務在 DVD 租借市場造成創造性破壞。"},{"en":"Creative destruction can hurt old businesses but also create better choices for customers.","zh":"創造性破壞可以傷害舊企業，但也為顧客創造更好選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase describes innovation that destroys and creates at the same time.","zh":"這個短語描述同時破壞和創造的創新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"culture tweaking","meaning":"文化微調","examples":[{"en":"Culture tweaking may not be enough to make large firms innovative.","zh":"文化微調可能不足以令大公司創新。"},{"en":"Culture tweaking means making small adjustments to an organisation’s attitudes, habits, or values.","zh":"culture tweaking 指對組織態度、習慣或價值作小調整。"},{"en":"A school tweaks its culture when it starts praising questions more often in class.","zh":"學校開始更常在課堂中稱讚提問時，就是微調文化。"},{"en":"Small cultural changes may help, but they may not overcome deep fear of failure.","zh":"小型文化改變可能有幫助，但未必能克服對失敗的深層恐懼。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests minor adjustment, not complete transformation.","zh":"這個短語暗示輕微調整，而不是完全轉型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"make big firms more creative","meaning":"令大公司更有創意","examples":[{"en":"The writer questions whether these changes will make big firms more creative.","zh":"作者質疑這些改變會否令大公司更有創意。"},{"en":"To make big firms more creative means to help large companies generate more original and useful ideas.","zh":"make big firms more creative 指幫助大型公司產生更多原創而有用的意念。"},{"en":"Smaller teams and better rewards may make big firms more creative.","zh":"較小團隊和更好獎勵可能令大公司更有創意。"},{"en":"A company becomes more creative when employees are allowed to test ideas without excessive fear.","zh":"當員工被容許測試意念而不過度害怕，公司就會更有創意。"},{"en":"The phrase asks whether management changes truly increase creativity.","zh":"這個短語詢問管理改變是否真正增加創意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"founder of","meaning":"……的創辦人","examples":[{"en":"David Post is the founder of Umagic.","zh":"David Post 是 Umagic 的創辦人。"},{"en":"The founder of a company is the person who started it.","zh":"founder of a company 指創立該公司的人。"},{"en":"The founder of a tutoring centre may design its first courses and hire the first teachers.","zh":"補習中心創辦人可能設計首批課程並聘請首批老師。"},{"en":"Founders often shape a company’s culture because they choose its early direction.","zh":"創辦人通常塑造公司文化，因為他們選擇早期方向。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the person who created an organisation.","zh":"這個短語指出創造某組織的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be sceptical","meaning":"持懷疑態度","examples":[{"en":"David Post is sceptical about intrapreneurship.","zh":"David Post 對內部創業持懷疑態度。"},{"en":"To be sceptical means to doubt whether something is true, useful, or likely to work.","zh":"be sceptical 指懷疑某事是否真實、有用或可能有效。"},{"en":"Parents may be sceptical about a new app until they see students actually improve.","zh":"家長在看到學生真正進步前，可能對新應用程式持懷疑態度。"},{"en":"Scepticism can be healthy when it pushes people to ask for evidence.","zh":"懷疑可以是健康的，當它推動人們要求證據時。"},{"en":"The phrase describes doubt, not complete rejection.","zh":"這個短語描述懷疑，而不是完全拒絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"successful intrapreneurs","meaning":"成功的內部創業者","examples":[{"en":"Post believes successful intrapreneurs usually become entrepreneurs.","zh":"Post 認為成功的內部創業者通常會成為創業者。"},{"en":"Successful intrapreneurs are employees who create valuable new ideas inside a company.","zh":"successful intrapreneurs 指在公司內部創造有價值新意念的員工。"},{"en":"A successful intrapreneur may build a new business unit while still working for a large firm.","zh":"成功的內部創業者可能在仍為大公司工作時建立新業務單位。"},{"en":"Such employees may eventually leave if they want full control and ownership of their ideas.","zh":"如果這類員工想完全控制和擁有自己的意念，他們最終可能離開。"},{"en":"The phrase describes entrepreneurial people working inside organisations.","zh":"這個短語描述在組織內工作的創業型人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"become entrepreneurs","meaning":"成為創業者","examples":[{"en":"Some employees leave large firms and become entrepreneurs.","zh":"有些員工離開大公司並成為創業者。"},{"en":"To become entrepreneurs means to start one’s own business and take responsibility for its risks and rewards.","zh":"become entrepreneurs 指創辦自己的企業，並承擔其風險與回報。"},{"en":"A programmer may become an entrepreneur after building an app that attracts many users.","zh":"程式員在建立吸引大量用戶的應用程式後，可能成為創業者。"},{"en":"Employees become entrepreneurs when they believe they can develop ideas better outside the company.","zh":"當員工相信自己能在公司外更好地發展意念，他們就會成為創業者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the move from employment to business ownership.","zh":"這個短語描述由受僱轉向擁有企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"recall with glee","meaning":"津津樂道地回想","examples":[{"en":"Post recalls with glee how firms reacted to his idea.","zh":"Post 津津樂道地回想公司如何回應他的意念。"},{"en":"To recall with glee means to remember something with amusement, delight, or mischievous pleasure.","zh":"recall with glee 指帶着好笑、愉快或有點淘氣的快感回想某事。"},{"en":"A student may recall with glee how a difficult question finally confused the teacher.","zh":"學生可能津津樂道地回想一道難題最終令老師也困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests the speaker enjoys remembering the reaction or event.","zh":"這個短語暗示說話者享受回想該反應或事件。"},{"en":"It is more emotional than simply saying “remember”.","zh":"它比單純說 “remember” 更有情緒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"total incomprehension","meaning":"完全不理解","examples":[{"en":"He saw looks of total incomprehension when he explained his idea.","zh":"當他解釋自己的意念時，他看到完全不理解的表情。"},{"en":"Total incomprehension means complete failure to understand something.","zh":"total incomprehension 指完全無法理解某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may see total incomprehension on students’ faces after explaining a very abstract grammar rule.","zh":"老師解釋非常抽象的文法規則後，可能在學生臉上看到完全不理解。"},{"en":"New ideas often meet incomprehension when they are too unfamiliar or poorly explained.","zh":"當新意念太陌生或解釋不清，它們通常會遇到不理解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes complete confusion.","zh":"這個短語描述完全困惑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"hawk his idea","meaning":"推銷他的意念","examples":[{"en":"He tried to hawk his virtual experts idea to large firms.","zh":"他嘗試向大公司推銷他的虛擬專家意念。"},{"en":"To hawk an idea means to try hard to sell or promote it, often to many possible buyers.","zh":"hawk an idea 指努力出售或推廣某意念，通常向許多潛在買家。"},{"en":"An inventor may hawk her idea at business fairs until someone agrees to invest.","zh":"發明者可能在商業展覽中推銷自己的意念，直到有人同意投資。"},{"en":"Hawking an idea can be frustrating if people do not understand its value.","zh":"如果人們不理解其價值，推銷意念可以很令人沮喪。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and can suggest repeated, energetic selling.","zh":"這個短語較口語，可以暗示反覆而積極地銷售。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"virtual experts idea","meaning":"虛擬專家意念","examples":[{"en":"IBM did not understand his virtual experts idea.","zh":"IBM 不理解他的虛擬專家意念。"},{"en":"A virtual experts idea is a business concept where computer systems imitate expert advice.","zh":"virtual experts idea 指電腦系統模仿專家建議的商業概念。"},{"en":"A virtual experts idea in education might let students ask a simulated writing examiner for feedback.","zh":"教育中的虛擬專家意念可能讓學生向模擬寫作考官尋求回饋。"},{"en":"Such an idea can reduce access barriers, but users may question whether the advice is truly expert.","zh":"這類意念可以降低取得服務的障礙，但使用者可能質疑建議是否真正專業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a digital service built around simulated expertise.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞模擬專業知識建立的數碼服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"idea labs","meaning":"創意實驗室","examples":[{"en":"He presented the idea to the idea labs of large firms.","zh":"他把意念展示給大公司的創意實驗室。"},{"en":"Idea labs are departments or teams designed to explore, test, and develop new concepts.","zh":"idea labs 指設計用來探索、測試和發展新概念的部門或團隊。"},{"en":"A university may create an idea lab where students design solutions for community problems.","zh":"大學可能建立創意實驗室，讓學生為社區問題設計解決方案。"},{"en":"Idea labs can support innovation, but they may still reject ideas that seem too strange.","zh":"創意實驗室可以支持創新，但仍可能拒絕看似太奇怪的意念。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised spaces for experimenting with new ideas.","zh":"這個短語指有組織地實驗新意念的空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"cheerfully adds","meaning":"愉快地補充說","examples":[{"en":"Post cheerfully adds that the firms could have been right.","zh":"Post 愉快地補充說，這些公司可能是對的。"},{"en":"Cheerfully adds means says something extra in a light, good-humoured, or relaxed way.","zh":"cheerfully adds 指以輕鬆、幽默或放鬆的方式補充說某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may cheerfully add that mistakes are welcome because they help learning.","zh":"老師可能愉快地補充說，錯誤是受歡迎的，因為它們幫助學習。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the speaker is not bitter, even when discussing rejection or doubt.","zh":"這個短語顯示說話者即使討論拒絕或懷疑，也沒有怨恨。"},{"en":"It describes both adding information and the tone of doing so.","zh":"它同時描述補充資訊和說話語氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"they could have been right","meaning":"他們可能是對的","examples":[{"en":"He admits that the sceptical firms could have been right.","zh":"他承認那些持懷疑態度的公司可能是對的。"},{"en":"They could have been right means it is possible that their judgement was correct.","zh":"they could have been right 指他們的判斷有可能是正確的。"},{"en":"If a teacher warned that the test would be hard, students may later admit she could have been right.","zh":"如果老師警告測驗會很難，學生之後可能承認她可能是對的。"},{"en":"The phrase shows humility because the speaker accepts the possibility of being wrong.","zh":"這個短語顯示謙遜，因為說話者接受自己可能錯。"},{"en":"It is used when past doubt may have been justified.","zh":"它用於過去的懷疑可能有道理時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"unlike","meaning":"不像……","examples":[{"en":"Innovation, unlike sex or fitness, cannot be fully guided by a computer.","zh":"創新不像性或健身，不能完全由電腦指導。"},{"en":"Unlike means different from.","zh":"unlike 指不同於。"},{"en":"Unlike a simple spelling mistake, a weak argument may need deeper revision.","zh":"不像簡單串字錯誤，薄弱論點可能需要更深入修改。"},{"en":"The word introduces a contrast between two things.","zh":"這個詞引入兩件事物之間的對比。"},{"en":"It helps show that one example does not follow the same rule as another.","zh":"它幫助顯示一個例子不遵循另一個例子的相同規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"apparently","meaning":"看來；似乎","examples":[{"en":"Apparently, computers may advise people on sex, parenting and fitness.","zh":"看來，電腦可能會就性、育兒和健身向人們提供建議。"},{"en":"Apparently means it seems to be true, based on what has been heard, seen, or reported.","zh":"apparently 指根據所聽、所見或所報道，某事似乎屬實。"},{"en":"Apparently, the new bus route is faster, but students want to test it first.","zh":"看來新巴士路線較快，但學生想先測試。"},{"en":"The word can show mild uncertainty or a slightly humorous distance from a claim.","zh":"這個詞可以顯示輕微不確定，或與某說法保持帶幽默感的距離。"},{"en":"It means “it appears that”, not absolute proof.","zh":"它意思是「似乎」，不是絕對證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"parenting","meaning":"育兒","examples":[{"en":"The passage jokingly compares innovation with parenting and fitness advice.","zh":"文章以玩笑方式把創新與育兒和健身建議作比較。"},{"en":"Parenting is the work of caring for and raising children.","zh":"parenting 指照顧和養育孩子的工作。"},{"en":"New parents may seek parenting advice about sleep, discipline, and school choices.","zh":"新手父母可能尋求關於睡眠、管教和選校的育兒建議。"},{"en":"Parenting advice can be helpful, but every child and family situation is different.","zh":"育兒建議可以有幫助，但每個孩子和家庭情況都不同。"},{"en":"The word refers to the role and practice of being a parent.","zh":"這個詞指作為父母的角色和實踐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"one area where","meaning":"……的一個範疇","examples":[{"en":"Innovation is one area where a computer cannot tell you what to do.","zh":"創新是一個電腦不能告訴你該怎樣做的範疇。"},{"en":"One area where means one particular field or situation in which something is true.","zh":"one area where 指某事屬實的一個特定領域或情況。"},{"en":"Speaking confidence is one area where practice matters more than memorising rules.","zh":"口語信心是一個練習比背規則更重要的範疇。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows a general discussion to a specific case.","zh":"這個短語把一般討論收窄到具體個案。"},{"en":"It helps writers point to a limited but important example.","zh":"它幫助作者指出一個有限但重要的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"cannot tell you what to do","meaning":"不能告訴你該怎樣做","examples":[{"en":"A computer cannot tell you what to do about innovation.","zh":"電腦不能告訴你在創新方面該怎樣做。"},{"en":"Cannot tell you what to do means cannot give a clear, reliable instruction for your situation.","zh":"cannot tell you what to do 指不能為你的情況給出清楚可靠的指示。"},{"en":"A dictionary can explain words, but it cannot always tell you what to do in a difficult conversation.","zh":"字典可以解釋字詞，但不一定能告訴你在困難對話中該怎樣做。"},{"en":"Some problems need human judgement because rules and data are not enough.","zh":"有些問題需要人類判斷，因為規則和數據不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the limits of advice or technology.","zh":"這個短語突出建議或科技的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"which paragraph contains","meaning":"哪一段包含……","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which paragraph contains the required information.","zh":"學生識別哪一段包含所需資料。"},{"en":"Which paragraph contains asks students to find the paragraph where specific information appears.","zh":"which paragraph contains 要求學生找出特定資料出現在哪一段。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may decide which paragraph contains a definition, example, or reason.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能判斷哪一段包含定義、例子或原因。"},{"en":"This task tests scanning because students must locate information quickly and accurately.","zh":"這項任務測試掃讀能力，因為學生必須快速而準確定位資料。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in IELTS-style matching questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 IELTS 式配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the following information","meaning":"以下資料","examples":[{"en":"The task asks students to find the following information in the passage.","zh":"該任務要求學生在文章中找出以下資料。"},{"en":"The following information means the pieces of information listed after the instruction.","zh":"the following information 指指示後列出的資料項目。"},{"en":"Students should read the following information carefully before searching the passage.","zh":"學生在搜尋文章前，應仔細閱讀以下資料。"},{"en":"Understanding the list first helps students know what details to scan for.","zh":"先理解列表，幫助學生知道要掃讀哪些細節。"},{"en":"The phrase is an exam instruction pointing to the items below.","zh":"這個短語是指向下方項目的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"may use any letter more than once","meaning":"可以重複使用任何字母","examples":[{"en":"Students may use any letter more than once in this type of question.","zh":"學生在這類題目中可以重複使用任何字母。"},{"en":"May use any letter more than once means the same paragraph label can be chosen for several answers.","zh":"may use any letter more than once 指同一段落字母可以用於幾個答案。"},{"en":"If paragraph B contains two pieces of information, students may write B twice.","zh":"如果 B 段包含兩項資料，學生可以寫兩次 B。"},{"en":"This instruction prevents students from wrongly using each option only once.","zh":"這項指示防止學生錯誤地每個選項只用一次。"},{"en":"The phrase is important in matching-information questions.","zh":"這個短語在資料配對題中很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"an approach to retaining","meaning":"挽留……的方法","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for an approach to retaining the best employees.","zh":"題目要求找出挽留最優秀員工的方法。"},{"en":"An approach to retaining someone is a method used to keep them from leaving.","zh":"approach to retaining someone 指用來防止某人離開的方法。"},{"en":"Flexible working can be an approach to retaining experienced parents in the workplace.","zh":"彈性工作可以是在職場挽留有經驗家長的方法。"},{"en":"Companies need retention approaches because losing skilled people is expensive.","zh":"公司需要挽留策略，因為失去熟練人才成本很高。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strategy for keeping valuable people.","zh":"這個短語描述保留有價值人士的策略。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"the best employees","meaning":"最優秀的員工","examples":[{"en":"Companies need ways to retain the best employees.","zh":"公司需要方法挽留最優秀的員工。"},{"en":"The best employees are the most capable, valuable, reliable, or creative workers in an organisation.","zh":"best employees 指組織中最有能力、最有價值、最可靠或最有創意的員工。"},{"en":"A school’s best employees may be teachers who help weak students improve and support colleagues.","zh":"學校最優秀的員工可能是幫助弱學生進步並支援同事的老師。"},{"en":"Losing the best employees can weaken performance and morale.","zh":"失去最優秀員工可以削弱表現和士氣。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to top staff, not simply senior staff.","zh":"這個短語指頂尖員工，而不只是高級員工。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"increased spending on","meaning":"在……方面增加開支","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to increased spending on acquiring innovative ideas.","zh":"題目提到在獲取創新意念方面增加開支。"},{"en":"Increased spending on something means more money is being used for that purpose than before.","zh":"increased spending on something 指相比以前有更多金錢用於該目的。"},{"en":"A school may show increased spending on counselling after students report more stress.","zh":"學生表示壓力增加後，學校可能在輔導方面增加開支。"},{"en":"Increased spending can show that a company now treats an area as more important.","zh":"增加開支可以顯示公司現在把某範疇視為更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a rise in financial commitment.","zh":"這個短語描述財務投入上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"acquiring innovative ideas","meaning":"獲取創新意念","examples":[{"en":"Companies may spend money on acquiring innovative ideas.","zh":"公司可能花錢獲取創新意念。"},{"en":"Acquiring innovative ideas means obtaining new and useful ideas from outside or inside the organisation.","zh":"acquiring innovative ideas 指從組織外部或內部取得新而有用的意念。"},{"en":"A publisher may acquire innovative ideas by buying a small education app company.","zh":"出版社可能透過收購小型教育應用程式公司獲取創新意念。"},{"en":"Companies acquire ideas when creating them internally is too slow or uncertain.","zh":"當內部創造意念太慢或太不確定，公司就會獲取意念。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on getting ideas, not only inventing them.","zh":"這個短語重點是取得意念，而不只是發明意念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"adverse effect","meaning":"負面影響","examples":[{"en":"The task asks about an adverse effect of integrating outside firms.","zh":"該任務問整合外部公司的負面影響。"},{"en":"An adverse effect is a harmful or negative result.","zh":"adverse effect 指有害或負面的結果。"},{"en":"A new timetable may have the adverse effect of making students wait longer for buses.","zh":"新時間表可能產生讓學生等巴士更久的負面影響。"},{"en":"Acquiring a small company may have adverse effects if its best people leave.","zh":"如果小公司的最優秀人才離開，收購它可能產生負面影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a downside or unwanted consequence.","zh":"這個短語描述壞處或不想要的後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"integrating outside firms","meaning":"整合外部公司","examples":[{"en":"Integrating outside firms can create management problems.","zh":"整合外部公司可以造成管理問題。"},{"en":"Integrating outside firms means bringing acquired or partner companies into an organisation’s structure, culture, and systems.","zh":"integrating outside firms 指把被收購或合作的公司納入組織結構、文化和系統。"},{"en":"A hospital group may face difficulties integrating outside clinics after buying them.","zh":"醫院集團收購診所後，可能在整合外部診所方面遇到困難。"},{"en":"Integration is hard because different companies may have different habits, software, and values.","zh":"整合很難，因為不同公司可能有不同習慣、軟件和價值觀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes combining external businesses with an existing organisation.","zh":"這個短語描述把外部企業與現有組織結合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"an example of","meaning":"……的例子","examples":[{"en":"The questions ask for an example of a company changing its focus.","zh":"題目要求找出公司改變焦點的例子。"},{"en":"An example of something is one case that shows or illustrates the idea.","zh":"example of something 指顯示或說明某意念的一個個案。"},{"en":"A school switching from paper notices to an app is an example of digital transformation.","zh":"學校由紙本通告轉向應用程式，是數碼轉型的例子。"},{"en":"Examples help learners understand abstract points through concrete cases.","zh":"例子幫助學習者透過具體個案理解抽象重點。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence or illustration.","zh":"這個短語引入證據或說明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"changing its focus","meaning":"改變其焦點","examples":[{"en":"The company is changing its focus from countries to products.","zh":"該公司正把焦點由國家改為產品。"},{"en":"Changing its focus means shifting attention, resources, or strategy from one priority to another.","zh":"changing its focus 指把注意力、資源或策略由一個優先事項轉向另一個。"},{"en":"A school may change its focus from exam results to student well-being after many pupils report stress.","zh":"當許多學生表示有壓力，學校可能把焦點由考試成績改為學生身心健康。"},{"en":"Changing focus can help an organisation respond to new needs or problems.","zh":"改變焦點可以幫助組織回應新需要或問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strategic change in attention.","zh":"這個短語描述注意力上的策略改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"financing an innovative idea independently","meaning":"獨立資助創新意念","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to financing an innovative idea independently.","zh":"題目提到獨立資助創新意念。"},{"en":"Financing an innovative idea independently means paying for a new idea without relying mainly on a large company or outside institution.","zh":"financing an innovative idea independently 指在不主要依靠大公司或外部機構的情況下，為新意念付款。"},{"en":"A designer may finance an innovative idea independently by using savings to build the first sample.","zh":"設計師可能用儲蓄製作第一個樣本，從而獨立資助創新意念。"},{"en":"Independent financing gives creators control, but it also increases personal risk.","zh":"獨立資助給創作者控制權，但也增加個人風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes funding an idea on one’s own.","zh":"這個短語描述自行為意念提供資金。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與文章資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statement agrees with the information in the passage.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與文章資料一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the information means match what the text says.","zh":"agree with the information 指與文本所說相符。"},{"en":"If the passage says small firms can innovate quickly, a statement saying the same thing agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說小公司能快速創新，陳述說同樣內容就與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should choose TRUE only when the text clearly supports the statement.","zh":"只有當文本清楚支持陳述時，學生才應選 TRUE。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in reading-comprehension tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀理解題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文章資料相反","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相反。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章所說相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the text says a company raised money, saying it had no funding contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文本說公司籌得資金，說它沒有資金就與資料相反。"},{"en":"Contradiction requires clear conflict, not just missing information.","zh":"矛盾需要清楚衝突，而不只是缺少資料。"},{"en":"The phrase is important for deciding between FALSE and NOT GIVEN.","zh":"這個短語對判斷 FALSE 和 NOT GIVEN 很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students write “NOT GIVEN” when there is no information on this.","zh":"當文中沒有相關資料時，學生寫 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not give enough evidence to decide.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文章沒有提供足夠證據讓人判斷。"},{"en":"If a passage describes a company’s funding but not its staff salaries, there is no information on salary levels.","zh":"如果文章描述公司資金但沒有提及員工薪金，就沒有薪金水平的相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not use guesses or outside knowledge when the text is silent.","zh":"當文本沒有說明，學生不應使用猜測或外部知識。"},{"en":"The phrase explains when NOT GIVEN is the correct choice.","zh":"這個短語解釋何時 NOT GIVEN 是正確選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"the most successful innovative company","meaning":"最成功的創新公司","examples":[{"en":"The statement describes Umagic as the most successful innovative company in the field.","zh":"該陳述把 Umagic 描述為該領域最成功的創新公司。"},{"en":"The most successful innovative company would be the company that has achieved the greatest results through new ideas.","zh":"most successful innovative company 指透過新意念取得最大成果的公司。"},{"en":"A firm may be innovative without yet being the most successful company in its market.","zh":"公司可以有創新，但未必已是市場中最成功的公司。"},{"en":"Calling a company the most successful requires clear evidence such as profit, users, or market share.","zh":"稱某公司為最成功需要清楚證據，例如利潤、用戶或市場佔有率。"},{"en":"The phrase combines innovation with top performance.","zh":"這個短語結合創新與頂尖表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"in this new field","meaning":"在這個新領域","examples":[{"en":"Umagic works in this new field of virtual expert advice.","zh":"Umagic 在虛擬專家建議這個新領域工作。"},{"en":"In this new field means in this recently developing area of business, study, or technology.","zh":"in this new field 指在這個最近發展中的商業、學術或科技範疇。"},{"en":"A student entering AI ethics is working in a new field where rules are still forming.","zh":"進入 AI 倫理的學生，正在一個規則仍在形成的新領域工作。"},{"en":"New fields are uncertain because customers, laws, and business models may not yet be clear.","zh":"新領域充滿不確定性，因為顧客、法律和商業模式可能仍不清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies an emerging area.","zh":"這個短語指出一個新興範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"share their experience of innovation","meaning":"分享創新經驗","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Amazon and Wal-Mart shared their experience of innovation.","zh":"該陳述問 Amazon 和 Wal-Mart 是否分享創新經驗。"},{"en":"To share one’s experience of innovation means to explain what one has learned from creating and using new ideas.","zh":"share one’s experience of innovation 指解釋自己從創造和使用新意念中學到的東西。"},{"en":"A successful teacher may share her experience of innovation at a professional workshop.","zh":"成功老師可能在專業工作坊分享創新經驗。"},{"en":"Sharing experience helps others avoid mistakes and copy useful methods.","zh":"分享經驗幫助他人避免錯誤並模仿有用方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes passing on practical lessons about innovation.","zh":"這個短語描述傳遞關於創新的實用教訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"originators of new ideas","meaning":"新意念的創造者","examples":[{"en":"Originators of new ideas may now start their own companies.","zh":"新意念的創造者現在可能開辦自己的公司。"},{"en":"Originators of new ideas are the people who first create or propose those ideas.","zh":"originators of new ideas 指最先創造或提出那些意念的人。"},{"en":"A nurse who designs a better patient-checking system is the originator of that new idea.","zh":"設計更好病人檢查系統的護士，就是該新意念的創造者。"},{"en":"When originators can get funding, they may not need to sell their ideas to big firms immediately.","zh":"當創造者能取得資金，他們未必需要立即把意念賣給大公司。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the first creators of ideas.","zh":"這個短語重點是意念的最初創造者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"take them to","meaning":"把它們帶到……","examples":[{"en":"In the past, originators often took their ideas to big companies.","zh":"過去，新意念的創造者常把它們帶到大公司。"},{"en":"To take them to someone means to bring ideas, proposals, or products to that person or organisation for support or approval.","zh":"take them to someone 指把意念、提案或產品帶給某人或某機構，以尋求支持或批准。"},{"en":"A student may take her science project idea to a teacher before entering a competition.","zh":"學生可能在參加比賽前，把科學項目意念帶給老師。"},{"en":"Inventors took ideas to big firms when they needed money, factories, or distribution.","zh":"當發明者需要資金、工廠或分銷，他們會把意念帶到大企業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes seeking help or acceptance from a particular place.","zh":"這個短語描述向特定地方尋求幫助或接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"fail to understand","meaning":"未能理解","examples":[{"en":"IBM appeared to fail to understand Umagic’s proposal.","zh":"IBM 似乎未能理解 Umagic 的提案。"},{"en":"To fail to understand means not to grasp the meaning, value, or purpose of something.","zh":"fail to understand 指沒有掌握某事的意思、價值或目的。"},{"en":"A student may fail to understand a question if it uses unfamiliar wording.","zh":"如果題目使用陌生措辭，學生可能未能理解問題。"},{"en":"Companies may reject good ideas when they fail to understand the market problem being solved.","zh":"當公司未能理解正在解決的市場問題，它們可能拒絕好意念。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a lack of comprehension.","zh":"這個短語描述理解不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"proposal of a new idea","meaning":"新意念的提案","examples":[{"en":"The company’s proposal of a new idea was not understood by some firms.","zh":"該公司新意念的提案不被某些公司理解。"},{"en":"A proposal of a new idea is a formal or informal suggestion for a new product, service, or method.","zh":"proposal of a new idea 指對新產品、服務或方法的正式或非正式建議。"},{"en":"A student council may make a proposal of a new idea for reducing plastic waste at school.","zh":"學生會可能提出減少學校塑膠廢物的新意念提案。"},{"en":"A proposal needs clear examples because unusual ideas can be misunderstood.","zh":"提案需要清楚例子，因為不尋常意念可能被誤解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes presenting a fresh concept for consideration.","zh":"這個短語描述提出新概念供人考慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each multiple-choice question.","zh":"學生為每條選擇題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choose the correct letter means select the answer option labelled with the right letter.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇標有正確字母的答案選項。"},{"en":"If option B matches the passage, students should choose the correct letter B.","zh":"如果 B 選項符合文章，學生應選出正確字母 B。"},{"en":"Careless copying can make a correct choice wrong on the answer sheet.","zh":"粗心抄寫可以令正確選擇在答題紙上變錯。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard multiple-choice instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準選擇題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"author’s opinion on","meaning":"作者對……的看法","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the author’s opinion on innovation.","zh":"題目詢問作者對創新的看法。"},{"en":"The author’s opinion on something is what the writer thinks or believes about that topic.","zh":"author’s opinion on something 指作者對該主題的想法或信念。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students must separate the author’s opinion from facts and examples.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生必須把作者觀點與事實和例子分開。"},{"en":"Tone, contrast words, and conclusions can reveal the author’s opinion.","zh":"語氣、對比詞和結論可以揭示作者觀點。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on viewpoint rather than basic information.","zh":"這個短語重點是觀點，而不是基本資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"increasingly important","meaning":"越來越重要","examples":[{"en":"Innovation is becoming increasingly important in American business.","zh":"創新在美國商業中變得越來越重要。"},{"en":"Increasingly important means becoming more important over time.","zh":"increasingly important 指隨時間變得更重要。"},{"en":"Digital literacy is increasingly important because more services are moving online.","zh":"數碼素養越來越重要，因為更多服務正在轉到網上。"},{"en":"A skill becomes increasingly important when work, society, or technology changes around it.","zh":"當工作、社會或科技圍繞某技能改變，該技能就會變得越來越重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a growing level of importance.","zh":"這個短語描述重要性上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"effects on","meaning":"對……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the effects of innovation on American companies.","zh":"題目詢問創新對美國公司的影響。"},{"en":"Effects on something are the results or impacts that one thing has on it.","zh":"effects on something 指某事對另一事物造成的結果或影響。"},{"en":"Teachers may study the effects of homework on students’ sleep and exam performance.","zh":"老師可能研究功課對學生睡眠和考試表現的影響。"},{"en":"Innovation can have effects on profits, staffing, competition, and company culture.","zh":"創新可以對利潤、人手、競爭和公司文化有影響。"},{"en":"The phrase asks what changes because of something.","zh":"這個短語詢問甚麼因某事而改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"point of view on","meaning":"對……的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for Peter Chernin’s point of view on innovation.","zh":"題目要求找出 Peter Chernin 對創新的觀點。"},{"en":"A point of view on something is a person’s opinion or way of thinking about that topic.","zh":"point of view on something 指某人對該主題的意見或思考方式。"},{"en":"A parent’s point of view on homework may differ from a teacher’s.","zh":"家長對功課的觀點可能與老師不同。"},{"en":"Understanding point of view helps students answer opinion-based reading questions.","zh":"理解觀點幫助學生回答以意見為本的閱讀題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to perspective, not physical sight.","zh":"這個短語指看法，而不是物理視線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"cut costs","meaning":"削減成本","examples":[{"en":"One answer option says companies need to cut costs when risks arise.","zh":"其中一個答案選項說，當風險出現時，公司需要削減成本。"},{"en":"To cut costs means to reduce spending.","zh":"cut costs 指減少開支。"},{"en":"A school may cut costs by using digital notices instead of printing paper letters.","zh":"學校可能透過使用數碼通告而不是打印紙本信件來削減成本。"},{"en":"Companies cut costs when income falls or when a project becomes too expensive.","zh":"當收入下降或項目變得太昂貴，公司會削減成本。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lowering expenses, often under pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述降低開支，通常是在壓力下進行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"risks arise","meaning":"風險出現","examples":[{"en":"Companies may face pressure to cut costs when risks arise.","zh":"當風險出現時，公司可能面對削減成本的壓力。"},{"en":"When risks arise means when possible problems, dangers, or losses appear.","zh":"risks arise 指可能的問題、危險或損失出現。"},{"en":"When health risks arise, a school may cancel outdoor activities.","zh":"當健康風險出現，學校可能取消戶外活動。"},{"en":"Businesses respond quickly when risks arise because delays can increase losses.","zh":"當風險出現，企業會快速回應，因為拖延可以增加損失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the moment potential danger becomes visible.","zh":"這個短語描述潛在危險變得可見的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"at the end of this passage","meaning":"在文章結尾","examples":[{"en":"The final question asks about the author’s opinion at the end of the passage.","zh":"最後一題詢問作者在文章結尾的看法。"},{"en":"At the end of this passage means in the final part or closing section of the text.","zh":"at the end of this passage 指在文本最後部分或結尾段落。"},{"en":"Students should read carefully at the end of the passage because writers often state their final judgement there.","zh":"學生應仔細閱讀文章結尾，因為作者常在那裏表明最終判斷。"},{"en":"A conclusion can change or qualify ideas introduced earlier.","zh":"結論可以改變或限定前文提出的想法。"},{"en":"The phrase points readers to the closing part of the reading text.","zh":"這個短語把讀者指向閱讀文本的最後部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"accidental concept","meaning":"偶然產生的概念","examples":[{"en":"The answer option describes the virtual experts idea as an accidental concept.","zh":"答案選項把虛擬專家意念描述為偶然產生的概念。"},{"en":"An accidental concept is an idea that appears by chance rather than through deliberate planning.","zh":"accidental concept 指偶然出現，而不是透過有意規劃產生的意念。"},{"en":"A teacher may discover an accidental concept when a classroom mistake becomes a useful activity.","zh":"當課堂錯誤變成有用活動，老師可能發現一個偶然產生的概念。"},{"en":"Accidental concepts can still become valuable if someone recognises their usefulness.","zh":"如果有人認出其用途，偶然概念仍可以變得有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests the idea was not intentionally designed at first.","zh":"這個短語暗示意念最初並非刻意設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"easy and straightforward","meaning":"簡單直接","examples":[{"en":"Innovation is not presented as easy and straightforward.","zh":"創新並沒有被呈現為簡單直接。"},{"en":"Easy and straightforward means simple, direct, and not complicated.","zh":"easy and straightforward 指簡單、直接而不複雜。"},{"en":"Filling in a name and date on a form is usually easy and straightforward.","zh":"在表格上填寫姓名和日期通常簡單直接。"},{"en":"Innovation is rarely straightforward because customers, costs, risks, and culture all matter.","zh":"創新很少簡單直接，因為顧客、成本、風險和文化都很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that can be done without much confusion.","zh":"這個短語描述不太令人困惑就能完成的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"set a good example of","meaning":"樹立……的好榜樣","examples":[{"en":"One option asks whether IBM sets a good example of innovation.","zh":"其中一個選項問 IBM 是否樹立了創新的好榜樣。"},{"en":"To set a good example of something means to show a positive model that others can learn from.","zh":"set a good example of something 指展示可供他人學習的正面榜樣。"},{"en":"A teacher sets a good example of lifelong learning when she studies new teaching methods herself.","zh":"當老師自己學習新教學方法，她就是樹立終身學習的好榜樣。"},{"en":"Companies that reward experiments can set a good example of innovation culture.","zh":"獎勵實驗的公司可以樹立創新文化的好榜樣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being a model for others.","zh":"這個短語描述成為他人的榜樣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"attitude towards","meaning":"對……的態度","examples":[{"en":"The final question asks about the author’s attitude towards innovation.","zh":"最後一題詢問作者對創新的態度。"},{"en":"Attitude towards something means the way a person feels or thinks about it.","zh":"attitude towards something 指某人對某事的感受或想法。"},{"en":"A student’s attitude towards mistakes affects whether she learns from feedback.","zh":"學生對錯誤的態度影響她是否從回饋中學習。"},{"en":"In reading tests, words like “worryingly” or “cheerfully” may reveal attitude.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，“worryingly” 或 “cheerfully” 等詞可能揭示態度。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on feeling and judgement, not just facts.","zh":"這個短語重點是感受和判斷，而不只是事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"uncertain","meaning":"不確定的","examples":[{"en":"The writer’s attitude towards innovation is presented as uncertain.","zh":"作者對創新的態度被呈現為不確定的。"},{"en":"Uncertain means not fully sure or not clearly decided.","zh":"uncertain 指不完全肯定或尚未清楚決定。"},{"en":"A student may feel uncertain about an answer if two options both seem possible.","zh":"如果兩個選項都看似可能，學生可能對答案感到不確定。"},{"en":"Uncertainty appears when evidence points in different directions or the future is hard to predict.","zh":"當證據指向不同方向或未來難以預測，不確定性就會出現。"},{"en":"The word describes doubt, hesitation, or lack of complete confidence.","zh":"這個詞描述懷疑、猶豫或缺乏完全信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 55 - Company Innovation.pdf","sourcePage":25}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 56":[{"front":"the Olympic torch","meaning":"奧運火炬","examples":[{"en":"The Olympic torch has become one of the most recognisable symbols of the Games.","zh":"奧運火炬已成為奧運會最容易辨認的象徵之一。"},{"en":"The Olympic torch is the flame-carrying object used in the Olympic relay and ceremonies.","zh":"奧運火炬是在奧運接力和典禮中用來承載火焰的物件。"},{"en":"A student may recognise the Olympic torch even if they do not know every Olympic sport.","zh":"即使學生不認識每項奧運運動，也可能認得奧運火炬。"},{"en":"Because it carries the flame, the torch connects ancient tradition with the modern Games.","zh":"因為火炬承載聖火，它把古代傳統與現代奧運連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to both a physical object and a powerful Olympic symbol.","zh":"這個短語既指實體物件，也指強大的奧運象徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"beginning in 776 BC","meaning":"始於公元前776年","examples":[{"en":"Beginning in 776 BC, the Greeks held the Olympic Games every four years in Olympia.","zh":"始於公元前776年，希臘人每四年在奧林匹亞舉辦奧運會。"},{"en":"Beginning in 776 BC means starting from the year 776 before Christ.","zh":"「beginning in 776 BC」意思是從公元前776年開始。"},{"en":"Beginning in 1997, the school held an annual open day for parents.","zh":"始於1997年，學校每年為家長舉辦開放日。"},{"en":"If an event began in 776 BC, it has extremely ancient historical roots.","zh":"如果一項活動始於公元前776年，它就有極古老的歷史根源。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the starting date of a long tradition.","zh":"這個短語提供一項長久傳統的開始日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hold the Olympic Games","meaning":"舉辦奧運會","examples":[{"en":"The Greeks held the Olympic Games every four years in Olympia.","zh":"希臘人每四年在奧林匹亞舉辦奧運會。"},{"en":"To hold the Olympic Games means to organise and host the Olympic sporting event.","zh":"「hold the Olympic Games」意思是組織並主辦奧運體育盛事。"},{"en":"A city must prepare stadiums, transport, security, and accommodation before it can hold the Games.","zh":"城市在能夠舉辦奧運會前，必須準備場館、交通、保安和住宿。"},{"en":"If a country holds the Olympics, many athletes and visitors travel there.","zh":"如果一個國家舉辦奧運，許多運動員和旅客會前往當地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organising the Games, not simply watching them.","zh":"這個短語描述組織奧運會，而不只是觀看奧運。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"every four years","meaning":"每四年","examples":[{"en":"The Olympic Games were held every four years in Olympia.","zh":"奧運會每四年在奧林匹亞舉行。"},{"en":"Every four years means once in each four-year period.","zh":"「every four years」意思是每四年一次。"},{"en":"Some schools review their long-term curriculum every four years.","zh":"有些學校每四年檢討一次長遠課程。"},{"en":"If an event happens every four years, people may wait a long time for the next one.","zh":"如果一項活動每四年才舉行，人們可能要等很久才等到下一次。"},{"en":"The phrase describes regular timing with a four-year gap.","zh":"這個短語描述相隔四年的固定時間安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Olympia","meaning":"奧林匹亞","examples":[{"en":"The ancient Olympic Games were held in Olympia.","zh":"古代奧運會在奧林匹亞舉行。"},{"en":"Olympia was the ancient Greek site associated with the original Olympic Games.","zh":"奧林匹亞是與最早奧運會有關的古希臘地點。"},{"en":"In a history lesson, students may learn that Olympia was not the same place as Mount Olympus.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生可能會學到奧林匹亞與奧林匹斯山不是同一地方。"},{"en":"Because the Games were held there, Olympia became central to Olympic history.","zh":"因為奧運會在那裡舉行，奧林匹亞成為奧運歷史的核心。"},{"en":"The word names the ancient location, not the modern Olympic organisation.","zh":"這個詞指出古代地點，而不是現代奧運組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"back then","meaning":"當時","examples":[{"en":"Back then, the Olympic torch made a long journey before each opening ceremony.","zh":"當時，奧運火炬在每次開幕典禮前都會經歷一段長途旅程。"},{"en":"Back then means at that time in the past.","zh":"「back then」意思是在過去那個時候。"},{"en":"Back then, students wrote essays by hand rather than typing them on computers.","zh":"當時，學生用手寫作文，而不是在電腦上打字。"},{"en":"If we say “back then”, we are usually comparing the past with the present.","zh":"如果我們說 “back then”，通常是在比較過去和現在。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an earlier period in a simple, conversational way.","zh":"這個短語以簡單口語方式引入較早時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"make a long journey","meaning":"經歷一段長途旅程","examples":[{"en":"The Olympic torch made a long journey before the opening ceremony.","zh":"奧運火炬在開幕典禮前經歷一段長途旅程。"},{"en":"To make a long journey means to travel a great distance or through many stages.","zh":"「make a long journey」意思是行經很遠距離或經過很多階段。"},{"en":"A family may make a long journey by train to visit relatives in another city.","zh":"一家人可能乘火車經歷長途旅程，到另一個城市探親。"},{"en":"If an object makes a long journey, many people may see or carry it along the way.","zh":"如果一件物件經歷長途旅程，沿途可能有許多人看見或傳遞它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes travelling far, not just moving a short distance.","zh":"這個短語描述長距離旅程，而不只是短距離移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"opening ceremony","meaning":"開幕典禮","examples":[{"en":"The torch arrived before the opening ceremony of each Olympic Games.","zh":"火炬在每屆奧運會開幕典禮前抵達。"},{"en":"An opening ceremony is a formal event that marks the beginning of a competition, festival, or public programme.","zh":"「opening ceremony」是標誌比賽、節日或公共活動開始的正式典禮。"},{"en":"A school sports day may begin with an opening ceremony in the playground.","zh":"學校運動會可能在操場以開幕典禮開始。"},{"en":"If a ceremony opens a major event, symbols, speeches, and performances are often included.","zh":"如果典禮為大型活動揭幕，通常會包括象徵物、演講和表演。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the official start, not the whole event.","zh":"這個短語描述正式開始，而不是整個活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"light a flame","meaning":"點燃火焰","examples":[{"en":"The Greek people would light a flame in a cauldron.","zh":"希臘人會在聖火盆中點燃火焰。"},{"en":"To light a flame means to start a fire or make something burn.","zh":"「light a flame」意思是點火或令某物燃燒。"},{"en":"A camper may light a flame carefully before cooking food outdoors.","zh":"露營者可能在戶外煮食前小心點燃火焰。"},{"en":"If a flame is lit for a ceremony, it often carries symbolic meaning.","zh":"如果火焰為典禮而點燃，它通常帶有象徵意義。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the action of starting fire.","zh":"這個短語描述開始燃火的動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cauldron","meaning":"大鍋；聖火盆","examples":[{"en":"The flame was lit in a cauldron on the altar.","zh":"火焰在祭壇上的聖火盆中被點燃。"},{"en":"A cauldron is a large bowl or container used to hold fire, liquid, or ceremonial flames.","zh":"「cauldron」是用來盛載火、液體或儀式火焰的大碗或容器。"},{"en":"In a school play, a cauldron may be used as a prop in a scene about ancient rituals.","zh":"在學校戲劇中，大鍋可能作為古代儀式場景的道具。"},{"en":"If a flame is placed in a cauldron, it can be kept visible and controlled.","zh":"如果火焰放在聖火盆中，它就能保持可見並受到控制。"},{"en":"The word often appears in ceremonial, historical, or mythical contexts.","zh":"這個詞常出現在儀式、歷史或神話語境中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on the altar","meaning":"在祭壇上","examples":[{"en":"The flame was lit in a cauldron on the altar.","zh":"火焰在祭壇上的聖火盆中被點燃。"},{"en":"On the altar means placed on a raised or sacred table used in religious ceremonies.","zh":"「on the altar」意思是放在宗教儀式中使用的高台或神聖桌面上。"},{"en":"Flowers may be placed on the altar during a wedding ceremony.","zh":"婚禮中，鮮花可能被放在祭壇上。"},{"en":"If something is placed on an altar, it is usually part of a ritual or act of respect.","zh":"如果某物被放在祭壇上，它通常是儀式或敬意行為的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a religious or ceremonial location.","zh":"這個短語描述宗教或儀式位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a ritual devoted to","meaning":"獻給……的儀式","examples":[{"en":"Lighting the flame was a ritual devoted to Hera.","zh":"點燃火焰是一項獻給希拉的儀式。"},{"en":"A ritual devoted to someone or something is a formal ceremony performed to honour them.","zh":"「a ritual devoted to」某人或某事，是為了尊崇他們而進行的正式儀式。"},{"en":"A school may hold a ritual devoted to remembering former students who served the community.","zh":"學校可能舉行一項獻給曾服務社區的舊生的紀念儀式。"},{"en":"If a ritual is devoted to a goddess, it shows religious respect and cultural belief.","zh":"如果一項儀式獻給女神，它顯示宗教敬意和文化信念。"},{"en":"The phrase links ceremony with dedication or worship.","zh":"這個短語把儀式與奉獻或崇敬連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Hera","meaning":"希拉","examples":[{"en":"Hera was the Greek goddess of birth and marriage.","zh":"希拉是希臘的生育與婚姻女神。"},{"en":"Hera is a figure in Greek mythology associated with family, marriage, and divine power.","zh":"「Hera」是希臘神話中的人物，與家庭、婚姻和神聖力量有關。"},{"en":"In a mythology lesson, students may compare Hera with other Greek gods and goddesses.","zh":"在神話課中，學生可能把希拉與其他希臘男女神比較。"},{"en":"If a ritual is devoted to Hera, it reflects ancient Greek religious beliefs.","zh":"如果一項儀式獻給希拉，它反映古希臘宗教信仰。"},{"en":"The name refers to a goddess, not a historical queen.","zh":"這個名字指女神，而不是歷史上的王后。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the Greek goddess of","meaning":"希臘……女神","examples":[{"en":"Hera was the Greek goddess of birth and marriage.","zh":"希拉是希臘的生育與婚姻女神。"},{"en":"The Greek goddess of something means a female deity in Greek mythology connected with that area of life.","zh":"「the Greek goddess of」某事，意思是希臘神話中與該生活範疇相關的女神。"},{"en":"Athena was the Greek goddess of wisdom and warfare.","zh":"雅典娜是希臘智慧與戰爭女神。"},{"en":"If a goddess is linked with marriage, people may honour her in wedding-related rituals.","zh":"如果女神與婚姻有關，人們可能在婚禮相關儀式中敬奉她。"},{"en":"The phrase explains a deity’s role or domain.","zh":"這個短語解釋神祇的職能或領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"birth and marriage","meaning":"生育與婚姻","examples":[{"en":"Hera was associated with birth and marriage.","zh":"希拉與生育與婚姻有關。"},{"en":"Birth and marriage are major life events connected with family and social continuity.","zh":"「birth and marriage」是與家庭和社會延續相關的重要人生事件。"},{"en":"Many cultures have rituals for birth and marriage because both events change family life.","zh":"許多文化都有生育與婚姻儀式，因為兩者都會改變家庭生活。"},{"en":"If a goddess is linked with birth and marriage, she may be honoured in family ceremonies.","zh":"如果女神與生育和婚姻有關，她可能在家庭儀式中受到敬奉。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to two important stages in human life.","zh":"這個短語指人生中的兩個重要階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the reintroduction of","meaning":"……的重新引入","examples":[{"en":"The reintroduction of the Olympic flame occurred at the Amsterdam 1928 Games.","zh":"奧運聖火的重新引入發生於1928年阿姆斯特丹奧運會。"},{"en":"The reintroduction of something means bringing it back after it has disappeared or stopped being used.","zh":"「the reintroduction of」某事，意思是在它消失或停止使用後把它重新帶回。"},{"en":"The reintroduction of school reading time helped students rebuild a daily reading habit.","zh":"學校閱讀時間的重新引入幫助學生重建每日閱讀習慣。"},{"en":"If an old tradition is reintroduced, it may connect modern people with the past.","zh":"如果舊傳統被重新引入，它可能把現代人與過去連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes restoring a former practice.","zh":"這個短語描述恢復昔日做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the Olympic flame","meaning":"奧運聖火","examples":[{"en":"The Olympic flame was reintroduced at the Amsterdam 1928 Games.","zh":"奧運聖火在1928年阿姆斯特丹奧運會被重新引入。"},{"en":"The Olympic flame is the symbolic fire associated with the Olympic Games.","zh":"「the Olympic flame」是與奧運會相關的象徵性火焰。"},{"en":"During the Games, the Olympic flame reminds spectators of continuity, ceremony, and tradition.","zh":"奧運期間，奧運聖火提醒觀眾延續、典禮和傳統。"},{"en":"If the flame remains lit, it symbolises the continuing spirit of the Olympics.","zh":"如果聖火保持燃燒，它象徵奧運精神延續。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the ceremonial fire, not just any flame.","zh":"這個短語指儀式火焰，而不只是任何火焰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"occur at","meaning":"發生於……","examples":[{"en":"The reintroduction of the Olympic flame occurred at the Amsterdam 1928 Games.","zh":"奧運聖火的重新引入發生於1928年阿姆斯特丹奧運會。"},{"en":"To occur at an event means to happen during or in connection with that event.","zh":"「occur at」某活動，意思是在該活動期間或與該活動相關地發生。"},{"en":"A prize ceremony may occur at the end of a school sports day.","zh":"頒獎禮可能發生於學校運動會結束時。"},{"en":"If a change occurs at a major event, many people may notice it.","zh":"如果改變發生於大型活動中，許多人可能注意到它。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where or during what event something happened.","zh":"這個短語指出某事發生在哪裡或在哪項活動期間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a cauldron was lit","meaning":"聖火盆被點燃","examples":[{"en":"A cauldron was lit at the Amsterdam 1928 Games.","zh":"1928年阿姆斯特丹奧運會上，聖火盆被點燃。"},{"en":"A cauldron was lit means a ceremonial flame was started in a large container.","zh":"「a cauldron was lit」意思是大型容器中的儀式火焰被點燃。"},{"en":"At a school ceremony, a symbolic lamp may be lit to mark the beginning of the event.","zh":"在學校典禮中，象徵性燈火可能被點燃，以標誌活動開始。"},{"en":"If a cauldron is lit, spectators can see the flame as a central symbol.","zh":"如果聖火盆被點燃，觀眾就能看見作為核心象徵的火焰。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the lighting of a ceremonial fire.","zh":"這個短語描述儀式火焰的點燃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"torch relay","meaning":"火炬接力","examples":[{"en":"There was no torch relay at the Amsterdam 1928 Games.","zh":"1928年阿姆斯特丹奧運會沒有火炬接力。"},{"en":"A torch relay is an event in which many people carry a torch in stages toward a destination.","zh":"「torch relay」是許多人分段傳遞火炬前往目的地的活動。"},{"en":"A school may organise a small relay where students pass a symbolic flag around the campus.","zh":"學校可能舉辦小型接力，讓學生在校園內傳遞象徵性旗幟。"},{"en":"If a torch relay involves many runners, the flame can travel through many communities.","zh":"如果火炬接力涉及許多跑手，聖火就能穿越許多社區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a staged journey, not one person carrying the torch all the way.","zh":"這個短語描述分段旅程，而不是一個人全程拿着火炬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"featured the first","meaning":"首次設有……","examples":[{"en":"The 1936 Berlin Summer Games featured the first Olympic torch relay.","zh":"1936年柏林夏季奧運會首次設有奧運火炬接力。"},{"en":"Featured the first means included the earliest example of something in that event or series.","zh":"「featured the first」意思是在某活動或系列中包括某事物的最早例子。"},{"en":"The school concert featured the first performance by the new choir.","zh":"學校音樂會首次設有新合唱團的表演。"},{"en":"If an event features the first version of a tradition, later events may copy it.","zh":"如果一項活動首次出現某傳統，後來活動可能模仿它。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights an important beginning.","zh":"這個短語突出重要開端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Summer Games","meaning":"夏季奧運會","examples":[{"en":"The Berlin Summer Games featured the first Olympic torch relay.","zh":"柏林夏季奧運會首次設有奧運火炬接力。"},{"en":"The Summer Games are the Summer Olympic Games, held for sports usually associated with summer conditions.","zh":"「Summer Games」是夏季奧運會，舉辦通常與夏季條件相關的運動。"},{"en":"Athletics, swimming, and gymnastics are events people commonly associate with the Summer Games.","zh":"田徑、游泳和體操是人們常與夏季奧運會聯繫起來的項目。"},{"en":"If a tradition begins at the Summer Games, it may later spread to the Winter Olympics.","zh":"如果某傳統始於夏季奧運會，它之後可能傳到冬季奧運會。"},{"en":"The phrase distinguishes the summer Olympics from the winter version.","zh":"這個短語把夏季奧運與冬季版本區分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Winter Olympics","meaning":"冬季奧運會","examples":[{"en":"The torch relay was not introduced at the Winter Olympics until 1952.","zh":"火炬接力直到1952年才被引入冬季奧運會。"},{"en":"The Winter Olympics are Olympic Games for winter sports such as skiing, skating, and ice hockey.","zh":"「Winter Olympics」是冬季運動的奧運會，例如滑雪、溜冰和冰球。"},{"en":"A city with snow and ice facilities is more suitable for the Winter Olympics.","zh":"擁有雪地和冰上設施的城市較適合舉辦冬季奧運會。"},{"en":"If a custom is later introduced at the Winter Olympics, it may have begun in the Summer Games first.","zh":"如果某習俗之後才被引入冬季奧運會，它可能先始於夏季奧運會。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the winter version of the Olympic Games.","zh":"這個短語指奧運會的冬季版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"not introduced until","meaning":"直到……才被引入","examples":[{"en":"The Olympic torch relay was not introduced at the Winter Olympics until 1952.","zh":"奧運火炬接力直到1952年才被引入冬季奧運會。"},{"en":"Not introduced until a time means something did not begin before that time.","zh":"「not introduced until」某時間，意思是在該時間之前某事並未開始。"},{"en":"The new school uniform was not introduced until September.","zh":"新校服直到九月才被引入。"},{"en":"If a tradition is not introduced until later, earlier events did not include it.","zh":"如果某傳統直到較後時間才被引入，較早活動並沒有包括它。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses delayed beginning.","zh":"這個短語強調較遲開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be considered the birthplace of","meaning":"被視為……的發源地","examples":[{"en":"Norway was considered the birthplace of skiing.","zh":"挪威被視為滑雪的發源地。"},{"en":"To be considered the birthplace of something means to be regarded as the place where it began or developed strongly.","zh":"「be considered the birthplace of」某事，意思是被認為是它開始或大力發展的地方。"},{"en":"A city may be considered the birthplace of a music style if many early performers came from there.","zh":"如果許多早期表演者來自某城市，它可能被視為某音樂風格的發源地。"},{"en":"If a country is linked with the origin of a sport, it may be chosen for symbolic reasons.","zh":"如果一個國家與某運動的起源有關，它可能因象徵原因被選中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a place strongly associated with origins.","zh":"這個短語描述與起源強烈相關的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the birthplace of skiing","meaning":"滑雪的發源地","examples":[{"en":"Norway was considered the birthplace of skiing.","zh":"挪威被視為滑雪的發源地。"},{"en":"The birthplace of skiing is the place regarded as the origin of skiing as a sport or practice.","zh":"「the birthplace of skiing」是被視為滑雪這項運動或活動起源的地方。"},{"en":"In a sports-history lesson, Norway may be discussed as the birthplace of skiing.","zh":"在運動歷史課中，挪威可能被討論為滑雪的發源地。"},{"en":"If a flame is lit in a symbolic location, it can connect the Games with sporting history.","zh":"如果聖火在象徵性地點點燃，它可以把奧運與運動歷史連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase names a place of origin for skiing.","zh":"這個短語指出滑雪的起源地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it was not until…that…","meaning":"直到……才……","examples":[{"en":"It was not until the 1964 Winter Olympics that the Olympic flame was reignited at Olympia.","zh":"直到1964年冬季奧運會，奧運聖火才在奧林匹亞重新點燃。"},{"en":"It was not until A that B means B happened only at time A, not before.","zh":"「It was not until A that B」意思是 B 直到 A 時間才發生，之前沒有。"},{"en":"It was not until secondary school that he became confident in speaking English.","zh":"直到中學，他才對英語口語變得有信心。"},{"en":"If we use this structure, we emphasise that something happened later than expected.","zh":"如果使用這個句式，我們會強調某事比預期更遲發生。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to highlight delayed timing.","zh":"這個短語是突出延遲時間的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be reignited at","meaning":"在……重新點燃","examples":[{"en":"The Olympic flame was reignited at Olympia in 1964.","zh":"奧運聖火於1964年在奧林匹亞重新點燃。"},{"en":"To be reignited at a place means to be lit again at that location.","zh":"「be reignited at」某地，意思是在該地再次被點燃。"},{"en":"A ceremonial candle may be reignited at the school hall after being carried from outside.","zh":"儀式蠟燭從外面帶入後，可能在學校禮堂重新點燃。"},{"en":"If a flame is reignited at its ancient site, the action has strong symbolic value.","zh":"如果火焰在其古代地點重新點燃，該行動具有強烈象徵價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lighting something again in a specific place.","zh":"這個短語描述在特定地方再次點燃某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Innsbruck, Austria","meaning":"奧地利因斯布魯克","examples":[{"en":"The 1964 Winter Olympics were held in Innsbruck, Austria.","zh":"1964年冬季奧運會在奧地利因斯布魯克舉行。"},{"en":"Innsbruck, Austria is a city in Austria associated with winter sports and mountain scenery.","zh":"「Innsbruck, Austria」是奧地利一座與冬季運動和山景相關的城市。"},{"en":"A geography student may locate Innsbruck on a map before studying the Winter Olympics.","zh":"地理學生在研究冬季奧運前，可能在地圖上找出因斯布魯克。"},{"en":"If a city has strong winter-sport conditions, it may be suitable for hosting winter events.","zh":"如果城市有良好冬季運動條件，它可能適合主辦冬季項目。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific Olympic host location.","zh":"這個短語指出一個具體奧運主辦地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"an abstract concept","meaning":"抽象概念","examples":[{"en":"The torch begins as an abstract concept created by designers.","zh":"火炬最初是由設計師創作的抽象概念。"},{"en":"An abstract concept is an idea that exists in the mind before it becomes a physical object.","zh":"「an abstract concept」是在成為實體物件前存在於腦中的想法。"},{"en":"A new school logo may begin as an abstract concept before artists draw it.","zh":"新校徽在藝術家畫出來前，可能先是一個抽象概念。"},{"en":"If a design starts as a concept, it must later become practical, safe, and usable.","zh":"如果設計始於概念，它之後必須變得實用、安全和可用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an idea before it has a final form.","zh":"這個短語描述尚未有最終形態的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"created by a designer","meaning":"由設計師創作","examples":[{"en":"The torch begins as an abstract concept created by a designer.","zh":"火炬最初是由設計師創作的抽象概念。"},{"en":"Created by a designer means imagined, planned, or drawn by someone trained in design.","zh":"「created by a designer」意思是由受過設計訓練的人構想、規劃或繪製。"},{"en":"A chair created by a designer should be attractive but also comfortable to sit on.","zh":"由設計師創作的椅子應該美觀，也應坐得舒服。"},{"en":"If an object is created by a designer, its shape usually serves both beauty and function.","zh":"如果一件物件由設計師創作，其形狀通常同時服務美感和功能。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the person responsible for the design idea.","zh":"這個短語指出負責設計想法的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"design teams","meaning":"設計團隊","examples":[{"en":"Several design teams submit their proposals to the Olympic Committee.","zh":"幾個設計團隊向奧林匹克委員會提交提案。"},{"en":"Design teams are groups of people who work together to create the appearance and function of a product.","zh":"「design teams」是共同創作產品外觀和功能的一群人。"},{"en":"A school festival may have design teams for posters, stage decoration, and tickets.","zh":"學校節日可能有負責海報、舞台裝飾和門票的設計團隊。"},{"en":"If several teams compete, the best design can be selected from different ideas.","zh":"如果幾個團隊競爭，就可以從不同想法中選出最佳設計。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to groups responsible for creative planning.","zh":"這個短語指負責創意規劃的團隊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"submit proposals to","meaning":"向……提交提案","examples":[{"en":"Design teams submit their proposals to the Olympic Committee.","zh":"設計團隊向奧林匹克委員會提交提案。"},{"en":"To submit proposals to an organisation means to formally send plans or ideas for consideration.","zh":"「submit proposals to」某機構，意思是正式提交計劃或想法供其考慮。"},{"en":"Students may submit proposals to the principal for a new school club.","zh":"學生可能向校長提交成立新學會的提案。"},{"en":"If a proposal is accepted, the team may get permission to develop the project.","zh":"如果提案被接受，團隊可能獲准發展項目。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formally offering a plan.","zh":"這個短語描述正式提供計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Olympic Committee","meaning":"奧林匹克委員會","examples":[{"en":"Several design teams submit proposals to the Olympic Committee.","zh":"幾個設計團隊向奧林匹克委員會提交提案。"},{"en":"The Olympic Committee is the organisation responsible for overseeing Olympic decisions and standards.","zh":"「the Olympic Committee」是負責監督奧運決策和標準的組織。"},{"en":"A local sports committee may choose rules and venues for a school tournament.","zh":"本地體育委員會可能為學校比賽選擇規則和場地。"},{"en":"If a design is submitted to a committee, it must meet official expectations.","zh":"如果設計提交給委員會，它必須符合官方期望。"},{"en":"The phrase names the body that approves or manages Olympic matters.","zh":"這個短語指出批准或管理奧運事務的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the hope of","meaning":"希望……","examples":[{"en":"Designers submit proposals in the hope of getting the chance to create the torch.","zh":"設計師提交提案，希望有機會創作火炬。"},{"en":"In the hope of doing something means because someone wants that result to happen.","zh":"「in the hope of」做某事，意思是因為某人希望該結果發生。"},{"en":"A student may join a debate club in the hope of becoming more confident.","zh":"學生可能加入辯論隊，希望變得更有信心。"},{"en":"If people work hard in the hope of winning, the desired result motivates their effort.","zh":"如果人們懷着勝出的希望努力，理想結果會推動他們付出。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the purpose behind an action.","zh":"這個短語解釋行動背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get the chance to","meaning":"有機會去……","examples":[{"en":"The winning team gets the chance to create the Olympic torch.","zh":"勝出團隊有機會創作奧運火炬。"},{"en":"To get the chance to do something means to receive an opportunity to do it.","zh":"「get the chance to」做某事，意思是得到做該事的機會。"},{"en":"A student may get the chance to perform on stage after practising for months.","zh":"學生練習數月後，可能有機會上台表演。"},{"en":"If a team wins a competition, it may be trusted with a real project.","zh":"如果團隊贏得比賽，它可能獲信任負責真正項目。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on opportunity.","zh":"這個短語集中於機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the winning group","meaning":"勝出的團隊","examples":[{"en":"The winning group develops a design for the torch.","zh":"勝出的團隊為火炬制定設計。"},{"en":"The winning group is the team chosen as the winner after a competition or selection process.","zh":"「the winning group」是在比賽或選拔過程後被選為勝出的團隊。"},{"en":"In a class project, the winning group may have its poster displayed at the school entrance.","zh":"在班級專題中，勝出團隊的海報可能被展示在學校入口。"},{"en":"If a group wins a design contest, it may receive responsibility for the final product.","zh":"如果團隊贏得設計比賽，它可能獲得最終產品的責任。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the selected successful team.","zh":"這個短語指出被選中的成功團隊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"develop a design for","meaning":"為……制定設計","examples":[{"en":"The winning group develops a design for the Olympic torch.","zh":"勝出的團隊為奧運火炬制定設計。"},{"en":"To develop a design for something means to plan its shape, materials, features, and function.","zh":"「develop a design for」某物，意思是規劃其形狀、材料、特徵和功能。"},{"en":"Students may develop a design for a school garden before asking for funding.","zh":"學生可能先為學校花園制定設計，再申請資金。"},{"en":"If a design must be used outdoors, the team has to consider weather and safety.","zh":"如果設計必須在戶外使用，團隊就要考慮天氣和安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes turning an idea into a workable plan.","zh":"這個短語描述把想法變成可行計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"aesthetic and practical value","meaning":"美學和實用價值","examples":[{"en":"The Olympic torch must have both aesthetic and practical value.","zh":"奧運火炬必須同時具有美學和實用價值。"},{"en":"Aesthetic and practical value means something should look good and work well.","zh":"「aesthetic and practical value」意思是某物應該好看並且好用。"},{"en":"A school bag has aesthetic value if it looks stylish and practical value if it carries books comfortably.","zh":"書包如果外觀時尚就有美學價值，如果能舒適地裝書就有實用價值。"},{"en":"If a torch is beautiful but unsafe, it lacks practical value.","zh":"如果火炬美觀但不安全，它就缺乏實用價值。"},{"en":"The phrase balances appearance with function.","zh":"這個短語平衡外觀與功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"withstand severe weather conditions","meaning":"承受惡劣天氣情況","examples":[{"en":"The torch must withstand severe weather conditions.","zh":"火炬必須承受惡劣天氣情況。"},{"en":"To withstand severe weather conditions means to remain working or undamaged in wind, rain, cold, or heat.","zh":"「withstand severe weather conditions」意思是在風、雨、寒冷或高溫中仍能運作或不受損。"},{"en":"A good umbrella should withstand strong wind without turning inside out.","zh":"好雨傘應能承受強風，而不會反轉。"},{"en":"If the torch fails in bad weather, the relay could be disrupted.","zh":"如果火炬在惡劣天氣中失效，接力可能被打斷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes durability under difficult outdoor conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述在困難戶外環境下的耐用能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"all sorts of","meaning":"各種各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"The torch must withstand all sorts of severe weather conditions.","zh":"火炬必須承受各種各樣的惡劣天氣情況。"},{"en":"All sorts of means many different kinds of something.","zh":"「all sorts of」意思是許多不同種類的某物。"},{"en":"A school fair may include all sorts of games, snacks, and performances.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能包括各種各樣的遊戲、小食和表演。"},{"en":"If a torch travels through many regions, it must handle all sorts of weather.","zh":"如果火炬穿越許多地區，它必須應付各種各樣的天氣。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses variety.","zh":"這個短語強調多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the appearance of","meaning":"……的外觀","examples":[{"en":"The appearance of the modern Olympic torch is attributed to John Hench.","zh":"現代奧運火炬的外觀歸功於 John Hench。"},{"en":"The appearance of something means the way it looks, including shape, colour, and style.","zh":"「the appearance of」某物，意思是它看起來的樣子，包括形狀、顏色和風格。"},{"en":"The appearance of a school poster can affect whether students stop to read it.","zh":"學校海報的外觀可以影響學生是否停下來閱讀。"},{"en":"If the appearance of a product is memorable, people may recognise it quickly.","zh":"如果產品外觀令人難忘，人們可能很快認出它。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on visual design.","zh":"這個短語集中於視覺設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the modern Olympic torch","meaning":"現代奧運火炬","examples":[{"en":"The modern Olympic torch was influenced by John Hench’s design.","zh":"現代奧運火炬受到 John Hench 設計的影響。"},{"en":"The modern Olympic torch is the contemporary version of the torch used in Olympic relays.","zh":"「the modern Olympic torch」是奧運接力中使用的現代版本火炬。"},{"en":"Modern torches are designed to be symbolic, attractive, safe, and weather-resistant.","zh":"現代火炬被設計成具象徵性、美觀、安全並能抵禦天氣。"},{"en":"If design improves over time, the modern torch can be lighter and more reliable.","zh":"如果設計隨時間改善，現代火炬可以更輕、更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the torch used in recent Olympic tradition.","zh":"這個短語指近期奧運傳統中使用的火炬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be attributed to","meaning":"歸功於……","examples":[{"en":"The appearance of the modern Olympic torch is attributed to Disney artist John Hench.","zh":"現代奧運火炬的外觀歸功於迪士尼藝術家 John Hench。"},{"en":"To be attributed to someone means to be credited to that person as the source or cause.","zh":"「be attributed to」某人，意思是把某事的來源或原因歸功於那個人。"},{"en":"A successful school campaign may be attributed to careful planning by the student council.","zh":"成功的學校活動可能歸功於學生會的仔細規劃。"},{"en":"If a design is attributed to an artist, that person is recognised for creating or shaping it.","zh":"如果設計歸功於某藝術家，那個人就因創作或塑造它而受到認可。"},{"en":"The phrase explains who or what is responsible.","zh":"這個短語解釋誰或甚麼負有責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Disney artist","meaning":"迪士尼藝術家","examples":[{"en":"John Hench was a Disney artist who designed an Olympic torch.","zh":"John Hench 是一位設計過奧運火炬的迪士尼藝術家。"},{"en":"A Disney artist is an artist who works for or is associated with Disney’s visual design and creative projects.","zh":"「Disney artist」是為迪士尼工作或與其視覺設計和創意項目有關的藝術家。"},{"en":"A Disney artist may design characters, buildings, posters, or objects for public events.","zh":"迪士尼藝術家可能設計角色、建築、海報或公共活動物件。"},{"en":"If an artist has experience in entertainment design, their work may be visually memorable.","zh":"如果藝術家有娛樂設計經驗，其作品可能視覺上令人難忘。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies John Hench’s creative background.","zh":"這個短語指出 John Hench 的創意背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lay a solid foundation for","meaning":"為……奠定堅實基礎","examples":[{"en":"John Hench’s design laid a solid foundation for future Olympic torches.","zh":"John Hench 的設計為未來奧運火炬奠定堅實基礎。"},{"en":"To lay a solid foundation for something means to create a strong base that later work can build on.","zh":"「lay a solid foundation for」某事，意思是創造一個後續工作可建立其上的強大基礎。"},{"en":"Good phonics teaching can lay a solid foundation for children’s reading.","zh":"良好自然拼讀教學可以為兒童閱讀奠定堅實基礎。"},{"en":"If an early design works well, later designers can improve it rather than start from nothing.","zh":"如果早期設計運作良好，後來設計師可以改進它，而不用從零開始。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating strong support for future development.","zh":"這個短語描述為未來發展建立強大支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"future Olympic torches","meaning":"未來的奧運火炬","examples":[{"en":"His design influenced future Olympic torches.","zh":"他的設計影響了未來的奧運火炬。"},{"en":"Future Olympic torches are torches designed and used in later Olympic Games.","zh":"「future Olympic torches」是後來奧運會設計和使用的火炬。"},{"en":"A successful torch design may influence future Olympic torches in shape, materials, or safety features.","zh":"成功的火炬設計可能在形狀、材料或安全特徵上影響未來奧運火炬。"},{"en":"If one torch sets a strong model, later torches may follow its basic principles.","zh":"如果一支火炬建立了強大範本，後來火炬可能跟隨其基本原則。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to Olympic torches made after an earlier design.","zh":"這個短語指早期設計之後製作的奧運火炬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the Olympic host city","meaning":"奧運主辦城市","examples":[{"en":"The torch makes a long journey to the Olympic host city.","zh":"火炬經歷長途旅程前往奧運主辦城市。"},{"en":"The Olympic host city is the city selected to hold a particular Olympic Games.","zh":"「the Olympic host city」是被選中舉辦某屆奧運會的城市。"},{"en":"Before the Games, the host city prepares venues, transport, hotels, and public ceremonies.","zh":"奧運前，主辦城市會準備場館、交通、酒店和公共典禮。"},{"en":"If the torch reaches the host city, the opening ceremony is usually near.","zh":"如果火炬抵達主辦城市，開幕典禮通常快將開始。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the city responsible for hosting the Games.","zh":"這個短語指出負責主辦奧運會的城市。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"one single torch","meaning":"單一支火炬","examples":[{"en":"The journey to the host city is not completed by one single torch.","zh":"前往主辦城市的旅程不是由單一支火炬完成。"},{"en":"One single torch means only one torch, rather than many separate torches.","zh":"「one single torch」意思是只有一支火炬，而不是許多不同火炬。"},{"en":"A school relay is not usually completed by one single runner; many students take turns.","zh":"學校接力通常不是由單一跑手完成，而是許多學生輪流。"},{"en":"If the Olympic relay is long, many torches may be needed for different runners.","zh":"如果奧運接力很長，可能需要許多火炬給不同跑手使用。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the journey involves more than one object.","zh":"這個短語強調旅程涉及多於一件物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"thousands of them","meaning":"數以千計的火炬","examples":[{"en":"The journey is completed by thousands of torches.","zh":"這段旅程由數以千計的火炬完成。"},{"en":"Thousands of them means a very large number of those objects or people.","zh":"「thousands of them」意思是那些物件或人有非常多，數以千計。"},{"en":"A big charity event may need thousands of wristbands for participants.","zh":"大型慈善活動可能需要數以千計的手帶給參加者。"},{"en":"If every relay runner receives a torch, thousands of them may be produced.","zh":"如果每位接力跑手都得到一支火炬，就可能生產數以千計的火炬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述大量數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be replicated many times","meaning":"被複製很多次","examples":[{"en":"The torch has to be replicated many times.","zh":"火炬必須被複製很多次。"},{"en":"To be replicated many times means to be copied repeatedly in large numbers.","zh":"「be replicated many times」意思是被大量反覆複製。"},{"en":"A school logo may be replicated many times on uniforms, banners, and notebooks.","zh":"學校標誌可能被複製很多次，印在校服、橫額和筆記簿上。"},{"en":"If thousands of runners need torches, the original design must be copied accurately.","zh":"如果數以千計跑手需要火炬，原本設計必須被準確複製。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated production of the same design.","zh":"這個短語描述同一設計的重複生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"approximately","meaning":"大約","examples":[{"en":"Approximately 10,000 to 15,000 torches are produced for the relay.","zh":"大約有10,000至15,000支火炬為接力而生產。"},{"en":"Approximately means about, not exactly.","zh":"「approximately」意思是大約，不是精確。"},{"en":"The journey from home to school takes approximately thirty minutes by bus.","zh":"從家到學校乘巴士大約需三十分鐘。"},{"en":"If a number is approximate, small differences are possible.","zh":"如果數字是大約數，細微差異是可能的。"},{"en":"The word is useful when exact figures are not necessary.","zh":"這個詞在不需要精確數字時很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be produced for","meaning":"為……而生產","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of torches are produced for the runners.","zh":"數以千計的火炬為跑手而生產。"},{"en":"To be produced for someone or something means to be made for that purpose or group.","zh":"「be produced for」某人或某事，意思是為該目的或群體製造。"},{"en":"School badges may be produced for all students taking part in a sports day.","zh":"學校徽章可能為所有參加運動會的學生而生產。"},{"en":"If an event has many participants, special items may be produced for them.","zh":"如果活動有許多參加者，可能為他們製作特別物品。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the purpose of production.","zh":"這個短語解釋生產目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"thousands of runners","meaning":"數以千計的跑手","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of runners take the torches through the Olympic relay.","zh":"數以千計的跑手把火炬帶過奧運接力。"},{"en":"Thousands of runners means a very large number of people who run or carry the torch in the relay.","zh":"「thousands of runners」意思是在接力中跑步或傳遞火炬的人數非常多。"},{"en":"A city marathon may involve thousands of runners from different communities.","zh":"城市馬拉松可能有來自不同社區的數以千計跑手參與。"},{"en":"If thousands of runners join a relay, many neighbourhoods can take part in the celebration.","zh":"如果數以千計跑手加入接力，許多社區都能參與慶祝。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises large public participation.","zh":"這個短語強調大型公眾參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take the torches through","meaning":"把火炬帶過……","examples":[{"en":"The runners take the torches through every section of the relay.","zh":"跑手把火炬帶過接力的每一段。"},{"en":"To take the torches through a place or section means to carry them across it as part of the journey.","zh":"「take the torches through」某地或某段，意思是在旅程中把火炬帶過該處。"},{"en":"Volunteers may take banners through the streets during a community parade.","zh":"義工可能在社區巡遊中把橫額帶過街道。"},{"en":"If each runner carries the torch through one section, the whole route is completed step by step.","zh":"如果每位跑手把火炬帶過一段路線，整條路線就一步步完成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes carrying something along a route.","zh":"這個短語描述沿路線攜帶某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"every section of","meaning":"……的每一段","examples":[{"en":"The torches pass through every section of the Olympic relay.","zh":"火炬經過奧運火炬接力的每一段。"},{"en":"Every section of something means each separate part of a route, process, or document.","zh":"「every section of」某物，意思是一條路線、過程或文件中的每個獨立部分。"},{"en":"A teacher checks every section of an essay before giving final comments.","zh":"老師給最終評語前，會檢查文章的每一部分。"},{"en":"If every section of a relay is covered, the torch reaches the destination.","zh":"如果接力的每一段都完成，火炬就能到達目的地。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses completeness across all parts.","zh":"這個短語強調所有部分都包括在內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the Olympic relay","meaning":"奧運火炬接力","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of runners take part in the Olympic relay.","zh":"數以千計的跑手參與奧運火炬接力。"},{"en":"The Olympic relay is the staged journey in which runners carry the Olympic torch toward the host city.","zh":"「the Olympic relay」是跑手分段把奧運火炬帶向主辦城市的旅程。"},{"en":"A local sports day may have a relay where teams pass a baton from runner to runner.","zh":"本地運動會可能有接力賽，隊伍把接力棒由一位跑手傳給另一位。"},{"en":"If many runners join the Olympic relay, the flame becomes a shared public symbol.","zh":"如果許多跑手加入奧運火炬接力，聖火就成為共同的公共象徵。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the torch-carrying journey before the Games.","zh":"這個短語指奧運會前的火炬傳遞旅程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"choose to buy","meaning":"選擇購買","examples":[{"en":"Each runner can choose to buy his or her torch.","zh":"每位跑手都可以選擇購買自己的火炬。"},{"en":"To choose to buy something means to decide voluntarily to purchase it.","zh":"「choose to buy」某物，意思是自願決定購買它。"},{"en":"A student may choose to buy a school hoodie as a memory of graduation.","zh":"學生可能選擇購買學校衛衣，作為畢業回憶。"},{"en":"If runners buy their torches, the object becomes a personal souvenir.","zh":"如果跑手購買自己的火炬，該物件就成為個人紀念品。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that buying is optional, not compulsory.","zh":"這個短語顯示購買是可選擇的，不是強制的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a treasured souvenir","meaning":"珍貴紀念品","examples":[{"en":"Each runner can buy the torch as a treasured souvenir.","zh":"每位跑手都可以把火炬買下作為珍貴紀念品。"},{"en":"A treasured souvenir is an object kept because it reminds someone of an important experience.","zh":"「a treasured souvenir」是因讓人想起重要經歷而被保存的物件。"},{"en":"A student may keep a medal from sports day as a treasured souvenir.","zh":"學生可能把運動會獎牌保存為珍貴紀念品。"},{"en":"If a runner carries the Olympic torch, keeping it can preserve the memory of that moment.","zh":"如果跑手曾傳遞奧運火炬，保留它可以保存那一刻的回憶。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a keepsake with emotional value.","zh":"這個短語描述具有情感價值的紀念物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"finish one’s part of","meaning":"完成自己負責的部分","examples":[{"en":"A runner may buy the torch after finishing his or her part of the relay.","zh":"跑手完成自己負責的接力部分後，可以購買火炬。"},{"en":"To finish one’s part of something means to complete the section or duty assigned to that person.","zh":"「finish one’s part of」某事，意思是完成分配給該人的部分或責任。"},{"en":"In a group presentation, each student should finish their part before the final rehearsal.","zh":"在小組匯報中，每位學生都應在最後排練前完成自己負責的部分。"},{"en":"If every runner finishes their part, the relay can continue smoothly.","zh":"如果每位跑手都完成自己負責的部分，接力就能順利繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes completing one’s assigned role.","zh":"這個短語描述完成自己的指定角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the modern Olympics","meaning":"現代奧運會","examples":[{"en":"The first torch in the modern Olympics was used at the 1936 Berlin Games.","zh":"現代奧運會中的第一支火炬在1936年柏林奧運會使用。"},{"en":"The modern Olympics are the revived Olympic Games held in the modern era.","zh":"「the modern Olympics」是現代時期復興後的奧運會。"},{"en":"Students studying sports history compare the ancient Games with the modern Olympics.","zh":"學習運動史的學生會比較古代奧運與現代奧運會。"},{"en":"If a tradition appears in the modern Olympics, it may be inspired by ancient practices but adapted for today.","zh":"如果某傳統出現在現代奧運會中，它可能受古代做法啟發，但已為今日改造。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the Olympic Games after their revival.","zh":"這個短語指復興後的奧運會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be made from","meaning":"由……製成","examples":[{"en":"The first modern Olympic torch was made from a slender steel rod.","zh":"第一支現代奧運火炬由細長鋼棒製成。"},{"en":"To be made from something means to be created using that material.","zh":"「be made from」某物，意思是用該材料製造出來。"},{"en":"A notebook may be made from recycled paper.","zh":"筆記簿可以由再造紙製成。"},{"en":"If a torch is made from metal, it can be stronger and more heat-resistant.","zh":"如果火炬由金屬製成，它可以更堅固和更耐熱。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the material used to create something.","zh":"這個短語指出製造某物所用的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a slender steel rod","meaning":"細長鋼棒","examples":[{"en":"The first modern Olympic torch was made from a slender steel rod.","zh":"第一支現代奧運火炬由細長鋼棒製成。"},{"en":"A slender steel rod is a long, thin piece of steel.","zh":"「a slender steel rod」是一條又長又幼的鋼材。"},{"en":"A designer might use a slender steel rod to make a light but strong handle.","zh":"設計師可能用細長鋼棒製作輕巧但堅固的手柄。"},{"en":"If a rod is slender, it can be easier to hold during a relay.","zh":"如果棒身細長，接力期間可能較容易握住。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the torch’s basic shape and material.","zh":"這個短語描述火炬的基本形狀和材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a circular platform","meaning":"圓形平台","examples":[{"en":"The torch had a circular platform at the top.","zh":"火炬頂部有一個圓形平台。"},{"en":"A circular platform is a flat round surface that supports or displays something.","zh":"「a circular platform」是一個用來支撐或展示某物的平坦圓面。"},{"en":"A trophy may stand on a circular platform so it looks balanced.","zh":"獎盃可能放在圓形平台上，看起來更平衡。"},{"en":"If a torch has a platform at the top, it can hold design details or support the flame area.","zh":"如果火炬頂部有平台，它可以承載設計細節或支撐火焰區域。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a round structural part.","zh":"這個短語描述圓形結構部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at the top","meaning":"在頂部","examples":[{"en":"The torch had a circular platform at the top.","zh":"火炬在頂部有一個圓形平台。"},{"en":"At the top means in the highest part of something.","zh":"「at the top」意思是在某物最高的部分。"},{"en":"A school noticeboard may have the date at the top of the page.","zh":"學校通告可能在頁面頂部寫日期。"},{"en":"If the flame is at the top of a torch, people can see it clearly.","zh":"如果火焰在火炬頂部，人們就能清楚看見它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes position.","zh":"這個短語描述位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a circular hole","meaning":"圓孔","examples":[{"en":"The torch had a circular hole in the middle.","zh":"火炬中間有一個圓孔。"},{"en":"A circular hole is a round opening through or into a surface.","zh":"「a circular hole」是穿過或進入某表面的圓形開口。"},{"en":"A sink has a circular hole so water can drain away.","zh":"洗手盆有圓孔，讓水排走。"},{"en":"If a torch has a hole for the flame, gas or fuel can pass through it.","zh":"如果火炬有供火焰使用的孔，氣體或燃料可以通過它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a round opening.","zh":"這個短語描述圓形開口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the middle","meaning":"在中間","examples":[{"en":"A circular hole was placed in the middle of the platform.","zh":"圓孔被放在平台中間。"},{"en":"In the middle means at the centre of something.","zh":"「in the middle」意思是在某物的中央。"},{"en":"A teacher may write the title in the middle of the board.","zh":"老師可能把標題寫在黑板中間。"},{"en":"If a hole is in the middle of a platform, the design may look balanced.","zh":"如果孔位於平台中間，設計可能看起來平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes central position.","zh":"這個短語描述中央位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"emit a flame","meaning":"噴出火焰","examples":[{"en":"The circular hole allowed the torch to emit a flame.","zh":"圓孔讓火炬能噴出火焰。"},{"en":"To emit a flame means to send out or produce fire from an opening or source.","zh":"「emit a flame」意思是從開口或來源釋放或產生火焰。"},{"en":"A gas stove emits a flame when fuel is released and ignited.","zh":"煤氣爐在燃料釋放並點燃時會噴出火焰。"},{"en":"If a torch cannot emit a steady flame, it will not work well in a ceremony.","zh":"如果火炬不能噴出穩定火焰，它在典禮中就不能良好運作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fire coming out from a device.","zh":"這個短語描述火從裝置中冒出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be inscribed on","meaning":"被刻在……上","examples":[{"en":"The runner’s name was inscribed on the platform.","zh":"跑手的名字被刻在平台上。"},{"en":"To be inscribed on something means to be carved, written, or engraved onto its surface.","zh":"「be inscribed on」某物，意思是被雕刻、書寫或刻在其表面上。"},{"en":"A student’s name may be inscribed on a trophy after winning a competition.","zh":"學生比賽勝出後，名字可能被刻在獎盃上。"},{"en":"If a name is inscribed on an object, the object becomes more personal and memorable.","zh":"如果名字被刻在物件上，該物件就變得更個人化和難忘。"},{"en":"The phrase describes permanent writing on a surface.","zh":"這個短語描述表面上的永久文字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as a token of thanks","meaning":"作為謝意的象徵","examples":[{"en":"The runner’s name was inscribed as a token of thanks.","zh":"跑手的名字被刻上，作為謝意的象徵。"},{"en":"As a token of thanks means as a small sign showing gratitude.","zh":"「as a token of thanks」意思是作為表達感謝的小象徵。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students a handwritten card as a token of thanks after a charity event.","zh":"慈善活動後，老師可能送學生手寫卡，作為謝意的象徵。"},{"en":"If volunteers work hard, a small gift can recognise their contribution.","zh":"如果義工努力付出，小禮物可以認可他們的貢獻。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a symbolic expression of appreciation.","zh":"這個短語描述象徵性的感謝表達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in the earlier days","meaning":"在早期","examples":[{"en":"In the earlier days, torches used many different fuels.","zh":"在早期，火炬使用許多不同燃料。"},{"en":"In the earlier days means during an older or earlier period of development.","zh":"「in the earlier days」意思是在較舊或較早的發展階段。"},{"en":"In the earlier days of computers, machines were much larger and slower.","zh":"在電腦早期，機器大得多，也慢得多。"},{"en":"If technology improves, earlier methods may look risky or inefficient later.","zh":"如果科技進步，早期方法後來可能看起來危險或低效。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a past stage.","zh":"這個短語引入過去階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"everything from…to…","meaning":"從……到……各種東西","examples":[{"en":"Early torches used everything from gunpowder to olive oil as fuels.","zh":"早期火炬使用從火藥到橄欖油等各種東西作燃料。"},{"en":"Everything from A to B means many different things across a wide range.","zh":"「everything from A to B」意思是涵蓋很廣範圍的許多不同東西。"},{"en":"The school fair sold everything from handmade cards to hot noodles.","zh":"學校嘉年華售賣從手工卡到熱湯麵等各種東西。"},{"en":"If a list ranges from one extreme to another, it shows great variety.","zh":"如果清單由一個極端到另一個極端，就顯示很大多樣性。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises a broad range of examples.","zh":"這個短語強調例子範圍廣泛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"gunpowder","meaning":"火藥","examples":[{"en":"Some early torches used gunpowder as fuel.","zh":"有些早期火炬使用火藥作燃料。"},{"en":"Gunpowder is an explosive powder that burns quickly and can produce force or flame.","zh":"「gunpowder」是一種會快速燃燒並能產生力量或火焰的爆炸性粉末。"},{"en":"Fireworks traditionally use gunpowder to create sound, light, and movement.","zh":"煙花傳統上使用火藥來產生聲音、光和移動。"},{"en":"If gunpowder is used carelessly, it can be dangerous.","zh":"如果火藥被不小心使用，它可能很危險。"},{"en":"The word refers to a powerful and potentially hazardous material.","zh":"這個詞指一種強力且有潛在危險的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"olive oil","meaning":"橄欖油","examples":[{"en":"Some early torches used olive oil as fuel.","zh":"有些早期火炬使用橄欖油作燃料。"},{"en":"Olive oil is oil pressed from olives and used in cooking, lamps, and some traditional practices.","zh":"「olive oil」是由橄欖壓榨出的油，用於煮食、油燈和某些傳統做法。"},{"en":"A family may use olive oil to cook vegetables or dress a salad.","zh":"家庭可能用橄欖油煮蔬菜或拌沙律。"},{"en":"If oil burns steadily, it can be used as a simple fuel source.","zh":"如果油能穩定燃燒，它就可以作為簡單燃料來源。"},{"en":"The phrase names a natural oil with practical uses.","zh":"這個短語指出一種有實際用途的天然油。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fuel","meaning":"燃料","examples":[{"en":"Different materials were used as fuel for Olympic torches.","zh":"不同材料被用作奧運火炬的燃料。"},{"en":"Fuel is a material that is burned or used to produce energy, heat, or flame.","zh":"「fuel」是被燃燒或用來產生能量、熱力或火焰的材料。"},{"en":"A car needs fuel to move, and a camping stove needs fuel to cook food.","zh":"汽車需要燃料行駛，露營爐需要燃料煮食。"},{"en":"If the wrong fuel is used, a device may be unsafe or fail to work.","zh":"如果使用錯誤燃料，裝置可能不安全或無法運作。"},{"en":"The word describes the material that powers burning or energy production.","zh":"這個詞描述推動燃燒或能量產生的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a combination of","meaning":"……的組合","examples":[{"en":"Some torches used a combination of hexamine and naphthalene.","zh":"有些火炬使用六亞甲基四胺和萘的組合。"},{"en":"A combination of things means two or more things used or joined together.","zh":"「a combination of」幾物，意思是兩種或以上東西被一起使用或結合。"},{"en":"A good study plan uses a combination of reading, practice, feedback, and rest.","zh":"好的溫習計劃使用閱讀、練習、回饋和休息的組合。"},{"en":"If one material alone is not enough, designers may combine several substances.","zh":"如果單一材料不足夠，設計師可能結合幾種物質。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mixing or joining parts.","zh":"這個短語描述混合或結合部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hexamine","meaning":"六亞甲基四胺","examples":[{"en":"Some torches used hexamine as part of their fuel mixture.","zh":"有些火炬使用六亞甲基四胺作為燃料混合物的一部分。"},{"en":"Hexamine is a chemical substance that can be used as a solid fuel in some contexts.","zh":"「hexamine」是一種化學物質，在某些情況下可用作固體燃料。"},{"en":"A science teacher may mention hexamine when discussing how different fuels burn.","zh":"科學老師討論不同燃料如何燃燒時，可能提到六亞甲基四胺。"},{"en":"If a fuel burns strongly but is hard to control, it may create safety concerns.","zh":"如果燃料燃燒強烈但難以控制，它可能造成安全問題。"},{"en":"The word names a specific chemical used in some torch fuels.","zh":"這個詞指出某些火炬燃料中使用的特定化學物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"naphthalene","meaning":"萘","examples":[{"en":"Some torches used naphthalene with a flammable fluid.","zh":"有些火炬把萘與易燃液體一起使用。"},{"en":"Naphthalene is a chemical substance that can burn and has been used in some fuel mixtures.","zh":"「naphthalene」是一種可燃燒的化學物質，曾用於某些燃料混合物。"},{"en":"In chemistry class, students may learn that some substances burn more easily than others.","zh":"在化學課中，學生可能學到有些物質比其他物質更容易燃燒。"},{"en":"If naphthalene is used with other flammable materials, safety must be carefully considered.","zh":"如果萘與其他易燃材料一起使用，必須仔細考慮安全。"},{"en":"The word names a specific chemical mentioned in early torch fuel.","zh":"這個詞指出早期火炬燃料中提及的特定化學物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"flammable fluid","meaning":"易燃液體","examples":[{"en":"Some torches used a flammable fluid with other substances.","zh":"有些火炬把易燃液體與其他物質一起使用。"},{"en":"A flammable fluid is a liquid that can catch fire easily.","zh":"「flammable fluid」是容易着火的液體。"},{"en":"Petrol is a flammable fluid, so it should be stored away from flames.","zh":"汽油是一種易燃液體，所以應遠離火焰存放。"},{"en":"If a flammable fluid leaks, a small spark can become dangerous.","zh":"如果易燃液體洩漏，一點火花也可能變得危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a liquid that must be handled carefully.","zh":"這個短語描述必須小心處理的液體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ideal fuel sources","meaning":"理想燃料來源","examples":[{"en":"These materials were not ideal fuel sources.","zh":"這些材料並不是理想燃料來源。"},{"en":"Ideal fuel sources are fuels that are safe, reliable, efficient, and suitable for the purpose.","zh":"「ideal fuel sources」是安全、可靠、高效並適合用途的燃料。"},{"en":"For a camping stove, an ideal fuel source should be easy to carry and control.","zh":"對露營爐而言，理想燃料來源應容易攜帶和控制。"},{"en":"If a fuel is smoky, unstable, or hazardous, it is not ideal.","zh":"如果燃料多煙、不穩定或危險，它就不理想。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the best kind of fuel for a particular use.","zh":"這個短語描述特定用途中的最佳燃料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be quite hazardous","meaning":"相當危險","examples":[{"en":"Some early fuel sources could be quite hazardous.","zh":"有些早期燃料來源可能相當危險。"},{"en":"To be quite hazardous means to be rather dangerous or likely to cause harm.","zh":"「be quite hazardous」意思是相當危險或可能造成傷害。"},{"en":"Wet floors can be quite hazardous if students run through the corridor.","zh":"如果學生在走廊奔跑，濕滑地板可能相當危險。"},{"en":"If torch fuel burns unpredictably, it may injure the person carrying it.","zh":"如果火炬燃料燃燒得難以預測，可能傷害持火炬的人。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that something carries real risk.","zh":"這個短語警告某事帶有真實風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at times","meaning":"有時","examples":[{"en":"The early fuel sources could be hazardous at times.","zh":"早期燃料來源有時可能危險。"},{"en":"At times means sometimes or on certain occasions.","zh":"「at times」意思是有時或在某些情況下。"},{"en":"A normally quiet classroom can be noisy at times before a holiday.","zh":"平時安靜的課室在假期前有時會很嘈吵。"},{"en":"If a fuel is dangerous at times, it cannot be trusted completely.","zh":"如果燃料有時危險，就不能完全信任它。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something happens occasionally, not always.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事偶爾發生，而不是總是發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the final relay","meaning":"最後一段接力","examples":[{"en":"The torch in the final relay was ignited by magnesium and aluminium.","zh":"最後一段接力中的火炬由鎂和鋁點燃。"},{"en":"The final relay is the last stage of a relay before the destination or ceremony.","zh":"「the final relay」是接力到達目的地或典禮前的最後階段。"},{"en":"In a school race, the final relay may decide which team wins.","zh":"在學校比賽中，最後一段接力可能決定哪一隊勝出。"},{"en":"If a problem happens in the final relay, it is especially visible because the ceremony is near.","zh":"如果最後一段接力出現問題，因典禮將近，會特別顯眼。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the last part of a staged journey.","zh":"這個短語指分段旅程的最後部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be ignited by","meaning":"由……點燃","examples":[{"en":"The torch was ignited by magnesium and aluminium.","zh":"火炬由鎂和鋁點燃。"},{"en":"To be ignited by something means to be set on fire by that material or force.","zh":"「be ignited by」某物，意思是由該材料或力量引發燃燒。"},{"en":"A candle can be ignited by a match or lighter.","zh":"蠟燭可以由火柴或打火機點燃。"},{"en":"If a torch is ignited by unstable materials, the flame may be hard to control.","zh":"如果火炬由不穩定材料點燃，火焰可能難以控制。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what starts the fire.","zh":"這個短語指出甚麼引發火焰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"magnesium","meaning":"鎂","examples":[{"en":"The 1956 torch was ignited by magnesium and aluminium.","zh":"1956年的火炬由鎂和鋁點燃。"},{"en":"Magnesium is a lightweight metal that can burn with a bright flame.","zh":"「magnesium」是一種輕金屬，可以燃燒出明亮火焰。"},{"en":"In a science demonstration, magnesium may be burned carefully to show a bright white light.","zh":"在科學示範中，鎂可能被小心燃燒，以展示明亮白光。"},{"en":"If burning magnesium falls from a torch, it can cause serious burns.","zh":"如果燃燒中的鎂從火炬掉落，可能造成嚴重灼傷。"},{"en":"The word names a metal with strong burning properties.","zh":"這個詞指出一種具有強燃燒特性的金屬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"aluminium","meaning":"鋁","examples":[{"en":"The 1956 torch was ignited by magnesium and aluminium.","zh":"1956年的火炬由鎂和鋁點燃。"},{"en":"Aluminium is a light metal used in objects that need to be strong but not too heavy.","zh":"「aluminium」是一種輕金屬，用於需要堅固但不太重的物件。"},{"en":"Many drink cans, window frames, and bicycle parts are made from aluminium.","zh":"許多飲品罐、窗框和單車零件由鋁製成。"},{"en":"If aluminium is used in torch design, it may help reduce weight.","zh":"如果火炬設計使用鋁，可能有助減輕重量。"},{"en":"The word names a common lightweight metal.","zh":"這個詞指出一種常見輕金屬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"flaming pieces","meaning":"燃燒中的碎片","examples":[{"en":"Some flaming pieces fell off the torch.","zh":"一些燃燒中的碎片從火炬掉落。"},{"en":"Flaming pieces are small burning parts that break away from something.","zh":"「flaming pieces」是從某物分離出來、仍在燃燒的小部分。"},{"en":"If a campfire throws out flaming pieces, people should move back for safety.","zh":"如果營火彈出燃燒中的碎片，人們應後退以保安全。"},{"en":"When burning pieces fall from a torch, the runner can be injured.","zh":"當燃燒碎片從火炬掉落，跑手可能受傷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dangerous fragments that are still on fire.","zh":"這個短語描述仍在着火的危險碎片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fall off","meaning":"掉落","examples":[{"en":"Some flaming pieces fell off and injured the runner.","zh":"一些燃燒中的碎片掉落並弄傷跑手。"},{"en":"To fall off means to drop from something it was attached to or resting on.","zh":"「fall off」意思是從原本附着或放置的地方掉下來。"},{"en":"A button may fall off a shirt if the thread is loose.","zh":"如果線鬆了，鈕扣可能從恤衫掉落。"},{"en":"If burning material falls off a torch, it can create danger immediately.","zh":"如果燃燒材料從火炬掉落，會立即造成危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes accidental separation and downward movement.","zh":"這個短語描述意外分離並向下掉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sear the runner’s arms","meaning":"灼傷跑手的手臂","examples":[{"en":"Some flaming pieces seared the runner’s arms.","zh":"一些燃燒中的碎片灼傷跑手的手臂。"},{"en":"To sear someone’s arms means to burn the skin with very strong heat.","zh":"「sear someone’s arms」意思是用強熱灼傷某人的手臂皮膚。"},{"en":"A cook may sear their hand if they touch a hot pan by accident.","zh":"如果廚師意外觸碰熱鍋，可能灼傷手。"},{"en":"If flaming pieces fall from a torch, they may burn the person carrying it.","zh":"如果燃燒碎片從火炬掉落，它們可能燒傷持火炬的人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes painful injury from heat.","zh":"這個短語描述由熱力造成的疼痛傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"to improve safety","meaning":"為了提高安全性","examples":[{"en":"Liquid fuels were introduced to improve safety.","zh":"液體燃料被引入是為了提高安全性。"},{"en":"To improve safety means to make something less dangerous and more secure.","zh":"「to improve safety」意思是令某事較不危險並更安全。"},{"en":"A school may add railings near stairs to improve safety for younger students.","zh":"學校可能在樓梯旁加裝欄杆，以提高年幼學生的安全性。"},{"en":"If older fuels caused accidents, designers would look for safer alternatives.","zh":"如果舊燃料造成意外，設計師會尋找更安全替代品。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the purpose of a change.","zh":"這個短語解釋改變的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"liquid fuels","meaning":"液體燃料","examples":[{"en":"Liquid fuels made their first appearance at the 1972 Munich Games.","zh":"液體燃料在1972年慕尼黑奧運會首次出現。"},{"en":"Liquid fuels are fuels in liquid form that can be burned to produce energy or flame.","zh":"「liquid fuels」是以液態存在並可燃燒產生能量或火焰的燃料。"},{"en":"Petrol and kerosene are examples of liquid fuels used in different machines.","zh":"汽油和火水是用於不同機器的液體燃料例子。"},{"en":"If liquid fuel is stored safely, it can be easier to control than loose burning materials.","zh":"如果液體燃料安全儲存，它可能比鬆散燃燒材料更容易控制。"},{"en":"The phrase names a category of fuel.","zh":"這個短語指出一類燃料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make one’s first appearance","meaning":"首次出現","examples":[{"en":"Liquid fuels made their first appearance at the 1972 Munich Games.","zh":"液體燃料在1972年慕尼黑奧運會首次出現。"},{"en":"To make one’s first appearance means to be seen or used for the first time.","zh":"「make one’s first appearance」意思是首次被看見或使用。"},{"en":"A new school mascot may make its first appearance at sports day.","zh":"新學校吉祥物可能在運動會首次出現。"},{"en":"If a technology makes its first appearance at a major event, it may influence future designs.","zh":"如果一項科技在大型活動首次出現，它可能影響未來設計。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a debut.","zh":"這個短語標示首次亮相。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the Munich Games","meaning":"慕尼黑奧運會","examples":[{"en":"Liquid fuels were first used at the Munich Games.","zh":"液體燃料首次在慕尼黑奧運會使用。"},{"en":"The Munich Games refers to the Olympic Games held in Munich.","zh":"「the Munich Games」指在慕尼黑舉行的奧運會。"},{"en":"In a history lesson, students may study the Munich Games when learning about Olympic design changes.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生學習奧運設計變化時可能研究慕尼黑奧運會。"},{"en":"If a new fuel was first used there, that Games marked a technological shift.","zh":"如果新燃料首次在那裡使用，該屆奧運就標誌技術轉變。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific Olympic event by its host city.","zh":"這個短語以主辦城市命名一項特定奧運活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"since then","meaning":"自那時起","examples":[{"en":"Since then, torches have used fuels pressurised into liquid form.","zh":"自那時起，火炬使用被加壓成液態的燃料。"},{"en":"Since then means from that time until now or until a later point.","zh":"「since then」意思是從那個時間起直到現在或較後時間。"},{"en":"The school introduced online homework in 2020; since then, fewer students have lost worksheets.","zh":"學校在2020年引入網上功課；自那時起，較少學生遺失工作紙。"},{"en":"If a new method works well, it may continue to be used since then.","zh":"如果新方法效果良好，自那時起可能一直被使用。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a past change with later practice.","zh":"這個短語把過去改變與後來做法連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be pressurised into liquid form","meaning":"被加壓成液態","examples":[{"en":"Modern torch fuels are pressurised into liquid form.","zh":"現代火炬燃料被加壓成液態。"},{"en":"To be pressurised into liquid form means gas or fuel is put under pressure so it becomes or stays liquid.","zh":"「be pressurised into liquid form」意思是氣體或燃料受到壓力，使其變成或保持液態。"},{"en":"Camping gas can be stored under pressure in a small metal canister.","zh":"露營氣體可以在小金屬罐中加壓儲存。"},{"en":"If fuel is stored as liquid, it can fit into a smaller, lighter container.","zh":"如果燃料以液態儲存，它可以放入更小、更輕的容器。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a technical process for storing fuel.","zh":"這個短語描述儲存燃料的技術過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be burnt","meaning":"被燃燒","examples":[{"en":"When the fuels are burnt, they turn into gas.","zh":"當燃料被燃燒時，它們會變成氣體。"},{"en":"To be burnt means to be set on fire or consumed by fire.","zh":"「be burnt」意思是被點燃或被火消耗。"},{"en":"Wood is burnt in a fireplace to produce heat.","zh":"木材在壁爐中被燃燒以產生熱力。"},{"en":"If fuel is burnt efficiently, it can produce a steady flame.","zh":"如果燃料被有效燃燒，它可以產生穩定火焰。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what happens when material catches fire and is used as fuel.","zh":"這個短語描述材料着火並被用作燃料時發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"turn into gas","meaning":"變成氣體","examples":[{"en":"When the fuels are burnt, they turn into gas.","zh":"當燃料被燃燒時，它們會變成氣體。"},{"en":"To turn into gas means to change from liquid or solid form into gaseous form.","zh":"「turn into gas」意思是由液態或固態變成氣態。"},{"en":"Water can turn into gas as steam when it is heated enough.","zh":"水加熱足夠時可以變成水蒸氣。"},{"en":"If torch fuel turns into gas before burning, it can feed a flame steadily.","zh":"如果火炬燃料在燃燒前變成氣體，它可以穩定供應火焰。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change of physical state.","zh":"這個短語描述物理狀態改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"produce a flame","meaning":"產生火焰","examples":[{"en":"The gas burns to produce a flame.","zh":"氣體燃燒以產生火焰。"},{"en":"To produce a flame means to create visible fire.","zh":"「produce a flame」意思是產生可見火焰。"},{"en":"A lighter produces a flame when gas is released and ignited.","zh":"打火機在氣體釋放並被點燃時產生火焰。"},{"en":"If the fuel flow is steady, the flame can remain visible throughout the relay.","zh":"如果燃料流量穩定，火焰就能在整個接力中保持可見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating fire as a result of burning.","zh":"這個短語描述燃燒後產生火。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be stored in","meaning":"儲存在……裏","examples":[{"en":"Liquid fuel can be stored in a light container.","zh":"液體燃料可以儲存在輕便容器裏。"},{"en":"To be stored in something means to be kept inside it for later use.","zh":"「be stored in」某物，意思是被保存在其中以便之後使用。"},{"en":"School sports equipment may be stored in a locked cupboard.","zh":"學校運動器材可能儲存在上鎖櫃裏。"},{"en":"If fuel is stored safely, it is easier to carry and control.","zh":"如果燃料被安全儲存，就更容易攜帶和控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where something is kept.","zh":"這個短語描述某物被保存的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a light container","meaning":"輕便容器","examples":[{"en":"Liquid fuel can be stored in a light container.","zh":"液體燃料可以儲存在輕便容器中。"},{"en":"A light container is a container that does not weigh much and is easy to carry.","zh":"「a light container」是不重、容易攜帶的容器。"},{"en":"A runner needs a light water bottle during a long race.","zh":"跑手在長跑中需要輕便水樽。"},{"en":"If the torch container is light, runners can carry it more comfortably.","zh":"如果火炬容器輕便，跑手就能更舒適地攜帶。"},{"en":"The phrase describes low weight and practical portability.","zh":"這個短語描述重量輕和便於攜帶的實用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be equipped with","meaning":"配備……","examples":[{"en":"The Atlanta torch was equipped with an aluminium base.","zh":"亞特蘭大火炬配備鋁製底座。"},{"en":"To be equipped with something means to have it as a useful part or feature.","zh":"「be equipped with」某物，意思是配有該有用部分或功能。"},{"en":"A classroom equipped with a projector can show videos and slides easily.","zh":"配備投影機的課室可以輕易播放影片和投影片。"},{"en":"If a torch is equipped with a special base, it may hold fuel more safely.","zh":"如果火炬配備特別底座，它可能更安全地容納燃料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes having necessary equipment or features.","zh":"這個短語描述擁有必要設備或功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an aluminium base","meaning":"鋁製底座","examples":[{"en":"The 1996 Atlanta torch had an aluminium base.","zh":"1996年亞特蘭大火炬有鋁製底座。"},{"en":"An aluminium base is the lower supporting part of an object made from aluminium.","zh":"「an aluminium base」是由鋁製成的物件下方支撐部分。"},{"en":"A lamp with an aluminium base may be light but stable.","zh":"有鋁製底座的燈可能輕巧但穩定。"},{"en":"If a torch has an aluminium base, it can support the fuel tank without becoming too heavy.","zh":"如果火炬有鋁製底座，它可以支撐燃料缸而不會太重。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a lightweight metal support.","zh":"這個短語描述輕金屬支撐部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"accommodate a tiny fuel tank","meaning":"容納一個小燃料缸","examples":[{"en":"The aluminium base accommodated a tiny fuel tank.","zh":"鋁製底座容納了一個小燃料缸。"},{"en":"To accommodate a tiny fuel tank means to contain or provide space for a very small fuel container.","zh":"「accommodate a tiny fuel tank」意思是容納或提供空間放置一個很小的燃料容器。"},{"en":"A compact camping stove may accommodate a tiny fuel tank under the burner.","zh":"小型露營爐可能在爐頭下方容納一個小燃料缸。"},{"en":"If the base holds the tank neatly, the torch can stay balanced and portable.","zh":"如果底座整齊容納燃料缸，火炬就能保持平衡和便攜。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fitting a small functional part inside a design.","zh":"這個短語描述把小型功能部件裝入設計中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a tiny fuel tank","meaning":"小燃料缸","examples":[{"en":"The aluminium base held a tiny fuel tank.","zh":"鋁製底座盛載了一個小燃料缸。"},{"en":"A tiny fuel tank is a very small container used to store fuel.","zh":"「a tiny fuel tank」是用來儲存燃料的很小容器。"},{"en":"A model car may have a tiny fuel tank because it does not need much fuel.","zh":"模型車可能有小燃料缸，因為它不需要很多燃料。"},{"en":"If the tank is tiny, the whole torch can be lighter and easier to carry.","zh":"如果燃料缸很小，整支火炬就可以更輕、更容易攜帶。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small fuel container.","zh":"這個短語描述小型燃料容器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rise through","meaning":"經由……上升","examples":[{"en":"The fuel rises through the modified handle.","zh":"燃料經由改良手柄上升。"},{"en":"To rise through something means to move upward inside or along it.","zh":"「rise through」某物，意思是在其內部或沿着它向上移動。"},{"en":"Warm air can rise through a stairwell in a building.","zh":"暖空氣可以經由建築物樓梯井上升。"},{"en":"If fuel rises through the handle, it can reach the burning section at the top.","zh":"如果燃料經由手柄上升，它可以到達頂部燃燒部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes upward movement through a structure.","zh":"這個短語描述穿過結構的向上移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"modified handle","meaning":"經改良的手柄","examples":[{"en":"The fuel rises through the modified handle of the torch.","zh":"燃料經由火炬經改良的手柄上升。"},{"en":"A modified handle is a handle that has been changed or redesigned for a special purpose.","zh":"「modified handle」是為特別目的而被改變或重新設計的手柄。"},{"en":"A bicycle may have a modified handle to make steering easier for a child.","zh":"單車可能有經改良的手柄，令兒童較容易操控方向。"},{"en":"If fuel must pass through the handle, the handle needs a special internal design.","zh":"如果燃料必須穿過手柄，手柄就需要特別內部設計。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a changed part that now has a new function.","zh":"這個短語描述已改變並具有新功能的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be squeezed through","meaning":"被擠壓通過……","examples":[{"en":"The fuel is squeezed through a brass valve.","zh":"燃料被擠壓通過黃銅閥門。"},{"en":"To be squeezed through something means to be forced through a narrow opening or passage.","zh":"「be squeezed through」某物，意思是被迫通過狹窄開口或通道。"},{"en":"Toothpaste is squeezed through the small opening at the end of a tube.","zh":"牙膏被擠壓通過牙膏管末端的小開口。"},{"en":"If fuel is squeezed through tiny openings, its pressure and flow can be controlled.","zh":"如果燃料被擠壓通過小孔，其壓力和流量就可以被控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes forced movement through a small space.","zh":"這個短語描述被迫穿過小空間的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"brass valve","meaning":"黃銅閥門","examples":[{"en":"The fuel passes through a brass valve with many openings.","zh":"燃料通過有許多開口的黃銅閥門。"},{"en":"A brass valve is a metal device made of brass that controls the flow of liquid or gas.","zh":"「brass valve」是由黃銅製成、用來控制液體或氣體流動的金屬裝置。"},{"en":"A plumber may use a brass valve to control water flow in a pipe.","zh":"水喉匠可能用黃銅閥門控制水管中的水流。"},{"en":"If a valve has many tiny openings, it can regulate pressure and fuel movement.","zh":"如果閥門有許多細小開口，它可以調節壓力和燃料流動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a control part in a fuel system.","zh":"這個短語描述燃料系統中的控制部件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"little openings","meaning":"小孔","examples":[{"en":"The brass valve has thousands of little openings.","zh":"黃銅閥門有數千個小孔。"},{"en":"Little openings are very small holes or gaps that allow material to pass through.","zh":"「little openings」是讓物質通過的很小孔洞或縫隙。"},{"en":"A shower head has many little openings so water can come out evenly.","zh":"花灑頭有許多小孔，讓水均勻流出。"},{"en":"If fuel passes through little openings, the flow can become finer and easier to burn.","zh":"如果燃料通過小孔，流動可以變得更細、更容易燃燒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes small passages in a surface or device.","zh":"這個短語描述表面或裝置中的小通道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pass through","meaning":"通過","examples":[{"en":"The fuel passes through the tiny openings.","zh":"燃料通過細小開口。"},{"en":"To pass through something means to move from one side or part of it to another.","zh":"「pass through」某物，意思是從它的一邊或一部分移到另一邊或另一部分。"},{"en":"Air passes through a mask filter before reaching the wearer’s mouth.","zh":"空氣通過口罩濾層後才到達佩戴者口鼻。"},{"en":"If fuel passes through a valve, the device can control how it flows.","zh":"如果燃料通過閥門，裝置就能控制其流動方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement through a space or object.","zh":"這個短語描述穿過空間或物件的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"accumulate pressure","meaning":"積聚壓力","examples":[{"en":"The fuel accumulates pressure as it passes through the openings.","zh":"燃料通過開口時積聚壓力。"},{"en":"To accumulate pressure means to build up force in a gas or liquid system.","zh":"「accumulate pressure」意思是在氣體或液體系統中逐漸建立力量。"},{"en":"Steam can accumulate pressure inside a closed pot if heat continues.","zh":"如果持續加熱，蒸汽可以在密封鍋中積聚壓力。"},{"en":"If pressure builds too much, a system may need a valve for safety.","zh":"如果壓力積聚太多，系統可能需要閥門保安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pressure increasing gradually.","zh":"這個短語描述壓力逐漸增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make its way through","meaning":"穿過；通過","examples":[{"en":"The fuel makes its way through the openings.","zh":"燃料穿過這些開口。"},{"en":"To make its way through something means to move through it gradually, sometimes through a narrow or difficult path.","zh":"「make its way through」某物，意思是逐漸穿過它，有時是穿過狹窄或困難路徑。"},{"en":"Water makes its way through small cracks in old walls after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，水會慢慢穿過舊牆的小裂縫。"},{"en":"If fuel makes its way through tiny openings, its flow changes before it burns.","zh":"如果燃料穿過細小開口，它在燃燒前的流動會改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual movement through a passage.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸穿過通道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pressure decreases","meaning":"壓力下降","examples":[{"en":"The pressure decreases after the fuel passes through the openings.","zh":"燃料通過開口後壓力下降。"},{"en":"Pressure decreases means the force inside a gas or liquid becomes lower.","zh":"「pressure decreases」意思是氣體或液體內部力量降低。"},{"en":"The pressure in a bicycle tyre decreases slowly if there is a tiny leak.","zh":"如果單車胎有很小漏氣，胎內壓力會慢慢下降。"},{"en":"If pressure decreases at the right moment, liquid fuel can change into gas.","zh":"如果壓力在適當時候下降，液體燃料可以變成氣體。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a drop in force.","zh":"這個短語描述力量下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"become gas","meaning":"變成氣體","examples":[{"en":"The liquid becomes gas so it can burn.","zh":"液體變成氣體，因此可以燃燒。"},{"en":"To become gas means to change into a gaseous state.","zh":"「become gas」意思是變成氣態。"},{"en":"Water becomes gas when it boils and turns into steam.","zh":"水沸騰並變成蒸汽時，就是變成氣體。"},{"en":"If liquid fuel becomes gas, it can mix with air and burn more easily.","zh":"如果液體燃料變成氣體，它可以與空氣混合並更容易燃燒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change in physical form.","zh":"這個短語描述物理形態改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be fuelled by","meaning":"以……作燃料","examples":[{"en":"The 1996 torch was fuelled by propylene.","zh":"1996年的火炬以丙烯作燃料。"},{"en":"To be fuelled by something means to use that material as the source of energy or flame.","zh":"「be fuelled by」某物，意思是使用該材料作為能量或火焰來源。"},{"en":"A bus may be fuelled by diesel, electricity, or hydrogen.","zh":"巴士可能以柴油、電力或氫氣作燃料。"},{"en":"If a torch is fuelled by a smoky substance, designers may look for cleaner alternatives.","zh":"如果火炬以多煙物質作燃料，設計師可能尋找更清潔替代品。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what powers the flame.","zh":"這個短語指出甚麼提供火焰動力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"propylene","meaning":"丙烯","examples":[{"en":"The 1996 torch was fuelled by propylene.","zh":"1996年的火炬以丙烯作燃料。"},{"en":"Propylene is a chemical fuel that can burn and produce a visible flame.","zh":"「propylene」是一種可燃燒並產生可見火焰的化學燃料。"},{"en":"In a chemistry lesson, students may compare different gases and how cleanly they burn.","zh":"在化學課中，學生可能比較不同氣體及其燃燒潔淨程度。"},{"en":"If propylene produces too much smoke, it may not be ideal for an environmentally friendly torch.","zh":"如果丙烯產生太多煙，它可能不適合作為環保火炬燃料。"},{"en":"The word names a specific substance used as torch fuel.","zh":"這個詞指出用作火炬燃料的特定物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a type of substance","meaning":"一種物質","examples":[{"en":"Propylene is a type of substance that can produce a bright flame.","zh":"丙烯是一種可以產生明亮火焰的物質。"},{"en":"A type of substance means a particular kind of material with certain properties.","zh":"「a type of substance」意思是一種具有某些特性的材料。"},{"en":"Salt is a type of substance that dissolves easily in water.","zh":"鹽是一種容易溶於水的物質。"},{"en":"If a substance burns brightly, it may be useful in a torch but still need safety testing.","zh":"如果一種物質燃燒明亮，它可能適合用於火炬，但仍需要安全測試。"},{"en":"The phrase classifies a material.","zh":"這個短語為材料分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"produce a bright flame","meaning":"產生明亮火焰","examples":[{"en":"Propylene can produce a bright flame.","zh":"丙烯可以產生明亮火焰。"},{"en":"To produce a bright flame means to create a flame that is strong and easy to see.","zh":"「produce a bright flame」意思是產生強烈而容易看見的火焰。"},{"en":"A good camping lantern should produce a bright flame or light source in the dark.","zh":"好的露營燈應在黑暗中產生明亮火焰或光源。"},{"en":"If a torch flame is bright, spectators can see it clearly from a distance.","zh":"如果火炬火焰明亮，觀眾可以從遠處清楚看見它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a visible and powerful flame.","zh":"這個短語描述可見而強烈的火焰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"carbon-rich","meaning":"含碳量高的","examples":[{"en":"Propylene is carbon-rich and produces plenty of smoke.","zh":"丙烯含碳量高，並產生大量煙霧。"},{"en":"Carbon-rich means containing a large amount of carbon.","zh":"「carbon-rich」意思是含有大量碳。"},{"en":"Coal is carbon-rich, so burning it can release smoke and carbon dioxide.","zh":"煤含碳量高，所以燃燒時可以釋放煙霧和二氧化碳。"},{"en":"If a fuel is carbon-rich, it may burn brightly but create environmental concerns.","zh":"如果燃料含碳量高，它可能燃燒明亮，但造成環境疑慮。"},{"en":"The phrase describes chemical composition linked with burning.","zh":"這個短語描述與燃燒有關的化學成分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"produce plenty of smoke","meaning":"產生大量煙霧","examples":[{"en":"Propylene can produce plenty of smoke.","zh":"丙烯可以產生大量煙霧。"},{"en":"To produce plenty of smoke means to create a large amount of smoke while burning.","zh":"「produce plenty of smoke」意思是燃燒時產生大量煙。"},{"en":"Wet wood can produce plenty of smoke when used in a campfire.","zh":"濕木在營火中燃燒時可以產生大量煙霧。"},{"en":"If a torch produces too much smoke, it may disturb spectators and harm air quality.","zh":"如果火炬產生太多煙，可能滋擾觀眾並損害空氣質素。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a smoky result of burning.","zh":"這個短語描述燃燒造成的多煙結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be detrimental to","meaning":"對……有害","examples":[{"en":"Too much smoke is detrimental to the environment.","zh":"太多煙霧對環境有害。"},{"en":"To be detrimental to something means to harm it or have a negative effect on it.","zh":"「be detrimental to」某事，意思是傷害它或對它有負面影響。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is detrimental to memory, mood, and concentration.","zh":"睡眠不足對記憶、心情和專注力有害。"},{"en":"If a fuel pollutes the air, it is detrimental to public health and the environment.","zh":"如果燃料污染空氣，它對公共健康和環境有害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes harmful impact.","zh":"這個短語描述有害影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the environment","meaning":"環境","examples":[{"en":"The designers wanted a torch that was harmless to the environment.","zh":"設計師想要一支對環境無害的火炬。"},{"en":"The environment means the natural world around us, including air, water, land, plants, and animals.","zh":"「the environment」意思是我們周圍的自然世界，包括空氣、水、土地、植物和動物。"},{"en":"Schools can protect the environment by reducing waste and saving electricity.","zh":"學校可以透過減少廢物和節約電力來保護環境。"},{"en":"If a torch fuel creates less smoke, it may cause less harm to the environment.","zh":"如果火炬燃料產生較少煙霧，對環境的傷害可能較少。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the natural surroundings affected by human actions.","zh":"這個短語指受人類行為影響的自然周遭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"propose a design","meaning":"提出設計","examples":[{"en":"The designers of the Sydney Olympic torch proposed a lighter design.","zh":"悉尼奧運火炬設計師提出了一個更輕巧的設計。"},{"en":"To propose a design means to suggest a plan for how something should look and work.","zh":"「propose a design」意思是建議某物應如何外觀和運作的計劃。"},{"en":"Students may propose a design for a new classroom reading corner.","zh":"學生可能為新的課室閱讀角提出設計。"},{"en":"If designers identify a problem, they may propose a new design to solve it.","zh":"如果設計師發現問題，他們可能提出新設計來解決。"},{"en":"The phrase describes offering a planned creative solution.","zh":"這個短語描述提供有計劃的創意方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a lighter and cheaper design","meaning":"更輕巧和更便宜的設計","examples":[{"en":"The Sydney Olympic torch used a lighter and cheaper design.","zh":"悉尼奧運火炬使用了更輕巧和更便宜的設計。"},{"en":"A lighter and cheaper design weighs less and costs less to make.","zh":"「a lighter and cheaper design」重量較輕，製造成本也較低。"},{"en":"A school may choose a lighter and cheaper stage decoration so students can move it easily.","zh":"學校可能選擇更輕巧和更便宜的舞台裝飾，讓學生容易搬動。"},{"en":"If thousands of torches must be produced, reducing weight and cost matters.","zh":"如果必須生產數以千計火炬，減輕重量和成本就很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical improvement in weight and price.","zh":"這個短語描述重量和價格上的實用改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"harmless to the environment","meaning":"對環境無害","examples":[{"en":"The new design was harmless to the environment.","zh":"新設計對環境無害。"},{"en":"Harmless to the environment means not damaging air, water, land, plants, or animals.","zh":"「harmless to the environment」意思是不損害空氣、水、土地、植物或動物。"},{"en":"A cleaning product is more attractive if it is harmless to the environment.","zh":"如果清潔產品對環境無害，它會更有吸引力。"},{"en":"If a torch fuel creates little smoke, it may be less harmful during public events.","zh":"如果火炬燃料產生很少煙霧，它在公共活動中可能較少造成傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes environmental safety.","zh":"這個短語描述環境安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as fuel","meaning":"作為燃料","examples":[{"en":"The designers chose propane and butane as fuel.","zh":"設計師選擇丙烷和丁烷作為燃料。"},{"en":"As fuel means used as the material that produces heat, energy, or flame.","zh":"「as fuel」意思是用作產生熱力、能量或火焰的材料。"},{"en":"Some households use gas as fuel for cooking.","zh":"有些家庭使用煤氣作為煮食燃料。"},{"en":"If a substance is chosen as fuel, designers must consider safety, cost, and smoke.","zh":"如果某物質被選作燃料，設計師必須考慮安全、成本和煙霧。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the use of a material.","zh":"這個短語指出材料的用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"propane","meaning":"丙烷","examples":[{"en":"Propane is a gas used for cooking and heating.","zh":"丙烷是一種用於煮食和供暖的氣體。"},{"en":"Propane is a fuel gas that can be stored under pressure and burned for heat.","zh":"「propane」是一種燃料氣體，可以加壓儲存並燃燒產生熱力。"},{"en":"A campsite may use propane to run a small stove.","zh":"露營地可能使用丙烷操作小型爐具。"},{"en":"If propane burns cleanly, it can be useful where a strong flame is needed.","zh":"如果丙烷燃燒潔淨，它在需要強火焰的地方可能有用。"},{"en":"The word names a common gas fuel.","zh":"這個詞指出一種常見氣體燃料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cooking and heating","meaning":"煮食和供暖","examples":[{"en":"Propane is used for cooking and heating.","zh":"丙烷用於煮食和供暖。"},{"en":"Cooking and heating means preparing food and making spaces or materials warm.","zh":"「cooking and heating」意思是準備食物，以及令空間或材料變暖。"},{"en":"A small flat may use gas for cooking and heating in winter.","zh":"小型單位冬天可能使用氣體煮食和供暖。"},{"en":"If a fuel is useful for both cooking and heating, it is practical in daily life.","zh":"如果燃料同時適合煮食和供暖，它在日常生活中就很實用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes two common uses of fuel.","zh":"這個短語描述燃料的兩種常見用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"butane","meaning":"丁烷","examples":[{"en":"Butane is a gas obtained from petroleum.","zh":"丁烷是一種從石油取得的氣體。"},{"en":"Butane is a fuel gas often used in lighters, portable stoves, and gas containers.","zh":"「butane」是一種常用於打火機、便攜爐和氣罐的燃料氣體。"},{"en":"A small lighter may contain butane because it can produce a controllable flame.","zh":"小型打火機可能含有丁烷，因為它能產生可控制火焰。"},{"en":"If butane is mixed with another fuel, designers may adjust flame strength and smoke level.","zh":"如果丁烷與另一種燃料混合，設計師可以調整火焰強度和煙霧水平。"},{"en":"The word names a common gas fuel derived from petroleum.","zh":"這個詞指出一種源自石油的常見氣體燃料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be obtained from","meaning":"從……取得","examples":[{"en":"Butane is obtained from petroleum.","zh":"丁烷從石油取得。"},{"en":"To be obtained from something means to be taken, produced, or derived from that source.","zh":"「be obtained from」某物，意思是從該來源取得、生產或衍生出來。"},{"en":"Paper is obtained from wood fibres.","zh":"紙張由木纖維取得。"},{"en":"If a fuel is obtained from petroleum, it comes from oil-based resources.","zh":"如果燃料從石油取得，它就來自油基資源。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of a material.","zh":"這個短語指出材料來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"petroleum","meaning":"石油","examples":[{"en":"Butane is obtained from petroleum.","zh":"丁烷從石油取得。"},{"en":"Petroleum is crude oil or oil-based material from which fuels and chemicals can be produced.","zh":"「petroleum」是原油或油基物質，可用來生產燃料和化學品。"},{"en":"Petrol, diesel, plastics, and some gases are connected with petroleum.","zh":"汽油、柴油、塑膠和某些氣體都與石油有關。"},{"en":"If a product depends on petroleum, its cost may change with oil prices.","zh":"如果產品依賴石油，其成本可能隨油價改變。"},{"en":"The word refers to an important fossil resource.","zh":"這個詞指一種重要化石資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"thus creating","meaning":"從而產生","examples":[{"en":"The designers used propane and butane, thus creating a powerful flame.","zh":"設計師使用丙烷和丁烷，從而產生強烈火焰。"},{"en":"Thus creating means as a result creating or producing something.","zh":"「thus creating」意思是因此創造或產生某物。"},{"en":"The school added more benches, thus creating a more comfortable waiting area.","zh":"學校增加更多長椅，從而創造更舒適的等候區。"},{"en":"If two fuels are combined well, the mixture can create a stronger and cleaner flame.","zh":"如果兩種燃料配合得好，混合物可以產生更強且更潔淨的火焰。"},{"en":"The phrase links an action with its result.","zh":"這個短語把行動與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a powerful flame","meaning":"強烈火焰","examples":[{"en":"The fuel mixture created a powerful flame.","zh":"燃料混合物產生了強烈火焰。"},{"en":"A powerful flame is a strong flame that burns clearly and with force.","zh":"「a powerful flame」是燃燒清楚而有力的強火焰。"},{"en":"A chef may need a powerful flame to heat a wok quickly.","zh":"廚師可能需要強烈火焰快速加熱鑊。"},{"en":"If an Olympic torch has a powerful flame, it remains visible in public ceremonies.","zh":"如果奧運火炬有強烈火焰，它在公共典禮中仍然清晰可見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes flame strength and visibility.","zh":"這個短語描述火焰強度和可見度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"without generating much smoke","meaning":"而不產生大量煙霧","examples":[{"en":"The fuel created a powerful flame without generating much smoke.","zh":"這種燃料產生強烈火焰，而不產生大量煙霧。"},{"en":"Without generating much smoke means without producing a large amount of smoke while burning.","zh":"「without generating much smoke」意思是燃燒時不產生大量煙霧。"},{"en":"A clean camping stove can heat food without generating much smoke.","zh":"潔淨露營爐可以加熱食物，而不產生大量煙霧。"},{"en":"If a torch burns with little smoke, it is better for spectators and the environment.","zh":"如果火炬燃燒時煙霧少，對觀眾和環境都較好。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights cleaner burning.","zh":"這個短語突出較潔淨燃燒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"dual-flame system","meaning":"雙火焰系統","examples":[{"en":"The 1996 and 2000 torches used a dual-flame system.","zh":"1996年和2000年的火炬使用雙火焰系統。"},{"en":"A dual-flame system is a design with two flames that serve different purposes.","zh":"「dual-flame system」是有兩個火焰、各自有不同用途的設計。"},{"en":"A safety lamp may use a small inner flame and a larger visible flame.","zh":"安全燈可能使用小內焰和較大的可見火焰。"},{"en":"If one flame goes out, the second flame can help keep the system working.","zh":"如果一個火焰熄滅，第二個火焰可以幫助系統繼續運作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a two-flame safety and visibility design.","zh":"這個短語描述兼顧安全和可見度的雙火焰設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"enable something to stay lit","meaning":"使……保持燃燒","examples":[{"en":"The dual-flame system enabled the flames to stay lit.","zh":"雙火焰系統使火焰保持燃燒。"},{"en":"To enable something to stay lit means to make it possible for a flame or light to keep burning or shining.","zh":"「enable something to stay lit」意思是使火焰或燈光能繼續燃燒或發亮。"},{"en":"A windproof lantern enables a candle to stay lit outdoors.","zh":"防風燈籠使蠟燭能在戶外保持燃燒。"},{"en":"If a torch must travel through rain and wind, its design must help the flame continue burning.","zh":"如果火炬必須穿越風雨，其設計必須幫助火焰繼續燃燒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes supporting continuous burning.","zh":"這個短語描述支援持續燃燒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stay lit","meaning":"保持燃燒","examples":[{"en":"The flames could stay lit even in severe weather.","zh":"即使在惡劣天氣中，火焰也能保持燃燒。"},{"en":"To stay lit means to continue burning or shining without going out.","zh":"「stay lit」意思是繼續燃燒或發亮而不熄滅。"},{"en":"A good emergency lamp should stay lit during a power cut.","zh":"好的緊急燈應在停電期間保持亮着。"},{"en":"If the torch stays lit in wind, the relay can continue smoothly.","zh":"如果火炬在風中保持燃燒，接力就能順利繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continuous light or flame.","zh":"這個短語描述持續發光或燃燒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"exterior flame","meaning":"外層火焰","examples":[{"en":"The exterior flame burns at a slower rate and at a lower temperature.","zh":"外層火焰以較慢速度和較低溫度燃燒。"},{"en":"The exterior flame is the outer flame that is more visible from the outside.","zh":"「exterior flame」是外面的火焰，從外部較容易看見。"},{"en":"A large exterior flame may help spectators see the torch clearly during a parade.","zh":"大型外層火焰可以幫助觀眾在巡遊中清楚看見火炬。"},{"en":"If the exterior flame is unstable, it may need an inner flame to relight it.","zh":"如果外層火焰不穩定，它可能需要內層火焰重新點燃。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the outer visible flame in a torch system.","zh":"這個短語指火炬系統中的外部可見火焰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"at a slower rate","meaning":"以較慢速度","examples":[{"en":"The exterior flame burns at a slower rate.","zh":"外層火焰以較慢速度燃燒。"},{"en":"At a slower rate means more slowly or with less speed than something else.","zh":"「at a slower rate」意思是比其他事物更慢或速度較低。"},{"en":"A student may read at a slower rate when the article contains difficult vocabulary.","zh":"當文章包含困難詞彙時，學生可能以較慢速度閱讀。"},{"en":"If fuel burns at a slower rate, it may last longer.","zh":"如果燃料以較慢速度燃燒，它可能維持更久。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reduced speed.","zh":"這個短語描述速度降低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"at a lower temperature","meaning":"在較低溫度下","examples":[{"en":"The exterior flame burns at a lower temperature.","zh":"外層火焰在較低溫度下燃燒。"},{"en":"At a lower temperature means with less heat than another condition or object.","zh":"「at a lower temperature」意思是熱度比另一情況或物件低。"},{"en":"Some clothes should be washed at a lower temperature to avoid damage.","zh":"有些衣服應在較低溫度下清洗，以免受損。"},{"en":"If a flame burns at a lower temperature, it may be safer but less intense.","zh":"如果火焰在較低溫度下燃燒，它可能較安全但不那麼強烈。"},{"en":"The phrase compares heat levels.","zh":"這個短語比較熱度水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be perceived easily","meaning":"容易被看見","examples":[{"en":"The exterior flame can be perceived easily because it is large and orange.","zh":"外層火焰因為又大又橙，所以容易被看見。"},{"en":"To be perceived easily means to be seen, noticed, or recognised without difficulty.","zh":"「be perceived easily」意思是容易被看見、注意到或辨認。"},{"en":"A bright exit sign can be perceived easily in a dark cinema.","zh":"明亮的出口標誌在黑暗戲院中容易被看見。"},{"en":"If a torch flame is large and orange, crowds can notice it quickly.","zh":"如果火炬火焰又大又橙，人群可以很快注意到它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes easy visibility or recognition.","zh":"這個短語描述容易看見或辨認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"big orange flame","meaning":"大橙色火焰","examples":[{"en":"The exterior flame appears as a big orange flame.","zh":"外層火焰呈現為大橙色火焰。"},{"en":"A big orange flame is a large, clearly visible flame with an orange colour.","zh":"「big orange flame」是巨大、清晰可見並呈橙色的火焰。"},{"en":"A bonfire at a festival may create a big orange flame that people can see from far away.","zh":"節日營火可能產生從遠處也能看見的大橙色火焰。"},{"en":"If a torch flame is big and orange, it becomes dramatic and easy to photograph.","zh":"如果火炬火焰又大又橙，它就變得壯觀並容易拍攝。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the visible appearance of the flame.","zh":"這個短語描述火焰的可見外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"unstable","meaning":"不穩定的","examples":[{"en":"The exterior flame is visible but unstable.","zh":"外層火焰可見但不穩定。"},{"en":"Unstable means not steady, secure, or reliable.","zh":"「unstable」意思是不穩、不安全或不可靠。"},{"en":"An unstable chair may wobble when someone sits on it.","zh":"不穩定的椅子在人坐下時可能搖晃。"},{"en":"If a flame is unstable, wind may blow it out more easily.","zh":"如果火焰不穩定，風可能更容易把它吹熄。"},{"en":"The word describes something that may change, fail, or fall.","zh":"這個詞描述可能改變、失效或倒下的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"On the other hand, the interior flame burns faster and hotter.","zh":"另一方面，內層火焰燃燒得更快和更熱。"},{"en":"On the other hand introduces a contrasting point or a different side of the comparison.","zh":"「on the other hand」引入對比觀點或比較中的另一面。"},{"en":"Online lessons are convenient; on the other hand, students may miss face-to-face discussion.","zh":"網課很方便；另一方面，學生可能缺少面對面討論。"},{"en":"If one flame is visible but unstable, the other may be smaller but steadier.","zh":"如果一個火焰可見但不穩定，另一個可能較小但更穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase helps compare two different features.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較兩種不同特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"interior flame","meaning":"內層火焰","examples":[{"en":"The interior flame burns faster and hotter.","zh":"內層火焰燃燒得更快和更熱。"},{"en":"The interior flame is the inner flame inside the torch system.","zh":"「interior flame」是火炬系統內部的火焰。"},{"en":"A device may use an interior flame to keep the main flame ready to relight.","zh":"裝置可能使用內層火焰，使主火焰隨時能重新點燃。"},{"en":"If the inner flame is protected from wind, it can remain more stable.","zh":"如果內部火焰受保護免受風吹，它就能保持更穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the flame hidden or placed inside.","zh":"這個短語指隱藏或放置在內部的火焰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"burn faster and hotter","meaning":"燃燒得更快和更熱","examples":[{"en":"The interior flame burns faster and hotter than the exterior flame.","zh":"內層火焰比外層火焰燃燒得更快和更熱。"},{"en":"To burn faster and hotter means to use fuel more quickly and produce more heat.","zh":"「burn faster and hotter」意思是更快消耗燃料並產生更多熱力。"},{"en":"Dry wood burns faster and hotter than wet wood in a campfire.","zh":"在營火中，乾木比濕木燃燒得更快和更熱。"},{"en":"If a flame burns hotter, it may be more stable but also needs careful control.","zh":"如果火焰燃燒得更熱，它可能更穩定，但也需要小心控制。"},{"en":"The phrase compares burning speed and heat.","zh":"這個短語比較燃燒速度和熱度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"generate a small blue flame","meaning":"產生細小藍色火焰","examples":[{"en":"The interior flame generates a small blue flame.","zh":"內層火焰產生細小藍色火焰。"},{"en":"To generate a small blue flame means to produce a small, hot flame that appears blue.","zh":"「generate a small blue flame」意思是產生細小、炙熱並呈藍色的火焰。"},{"en":"A gas stove often generates a small blue flame when the gas burns cleanly.","zh":"煤氣爐在氣體潔淨燃燒時，常產生細小藍色火焰。"},{"en":"If a flame is small but hot, it can serve a practical purpose without being very visible.","zh":"如果火焰細小但很熱，它可以有實用功能，而不一定非常顯眼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the colour, size, and function of a flame.","zh":"這個短語描述火焰的顏色、大小和功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"great stability","meaning":"高穩定性","examples":[{"en":"The interior flame has great stability.","zh":"內層火焰具有高穩定性。"},{"en":"Great stability means strong steadiness and a low chance of failing or going out.","zh":"「great stability」意思是非常穩定，失效或熄滅機會低。"},{"en":"A heavy table has great stability because it does not wobble easily.","zh":"沉重桌子具有高穩定性，因為它不容易搖晃。"},{"en":"If the interior flame is stable, it can help relight the outer flame when needed.","zh":"如果內層火焰穩定，它可以在需要時幫助重新點燃外層火焰。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reliability and steadiness.","zh":"這個短語描述可靠性和穩定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"inner location","meaning":"內部位置","examples":[{"en":"The interior flame is protected because of its inner location.","zh":"內層火焰因其內部位置而受到保護。"},{"en":"Inner location means a position inside something rather than on the outside.","zh":"「inner location」意思是在某物內部而非外部的位置。"},{"en":"A phone battery has an inner location, so it is protected by the outer case.","zh":"手機電池位於內部位置，因此受外殼保護。"},{"en":"If a flame is placed inside the torch, wind is less likely to blow it out.","zh":"如果火焰放在火炬內部，風就較不容易把它吹熄。"},{"en":"The phrase explains protection through position.","zh":"這個短語解釋透過位置得到保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"offer protection from","meaning":"提供免受……影響的保護","examples":[{"en":"The inner location offers protection from the wind.","zh":"內部位置提供免受風影響的保護。"},{"en":"To offer protection from something means to help keep someone or something safe from it.","zh":"「offer protection from」某事，意思是幫助某人或某物免受其傷害。"},{"en":"A raincoat offers protection from heavy rain.","zh":"雨衣提供免受大雨影響的保護。"},{"en":"If the flame is protected from wind, it is more likely to stay lit.","zh":"如果火焰受到保護免受風吹，它更可能保持燃燒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shielding against a danger or difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述抵禦危險或困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"accordingly","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"Accordingly, the interior flame serves as a pilot light.","zh":"因此，內層火焰充當長明小火。"},{"en":"Accordingly means as a result or for that reason.","zh":"「accordingly」意思是因此、基於這個原因。"},{"en":"The classroom was too noisy; accordingly, the teacher moved the group activity outside.","zh":"課室太嘈吵；因此，老師把小組活動移到外面。"},{"en":"If the inner flame is stable, it can therefore be used to relight the outer flame.","zh":"如果內層火焰穩定，它因此可以用來重新點燃外層火焰。"},{"en":"The word links a reason to a logical result.","zh":"這個詞把原因與合乎邏輯的結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"serve as","meaning":"充當；作為","examples":[{"en":"The interior flame serves as a pilot light.","zh":"內層火焰充當長明小火。"},{"en":"To serve as something means to function as it or be used for that purpose.","zh":"「serve as」某物，意思是發揮該功能或被用作該目的。"},{"en":"A school hall can serve as an exam room during test week.","zh":"學校禮堂可以在測驗週充當考場。"},{"en":"If a small flame serves as a pilot light, it helps restart a larger flame.","zh":"如果細小火焰充當長明小火，它可以幫助重新啟動較大火焰。"},{"en":"The phrase explains function.","zh":"這個短語解釋功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"pilot light","meaning":"長明小火；引燃火","examples":[{"en":"The interior flame serves as a pilot light.","zh":"內層火焰充當長明小火。"},{"en":"A pilot light is a small flame kept burning so it can light a larger flame when needed.","zh":"「pilot light」是一個持續燃燒的小火焰，需要時可點燃較大火焰。"},{"en":"Some old gas heaters used a pilot light to restart the main burner.","zh":"有些舊式煤氣暖爐使用長明小火重新啟動主燃燒器。"},{"en":"If the outer flame goes out, the pilot light can help bring it back.","zh":"如果外層火焰熄滅，長明小火可以幫助它重新燃起。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small safety flame.","zh":"這個短語描述細小的安全引燃火。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"relight the external flame","meaning":"重新點燃外層火焰","examples":[{"en":"The pilot light can relight the external flame.","zh":"長明小火可以重新點燃外層火焰。"},{"en":"To relight the external flame means to make the outer flame burn again after it has gone out.","zh":"「relight the external flame」意思是在外層火焰熄滅後令它再次燃燒。"},{"en":"A candle can be relit with a match if wind blows it out.","zh":"如果蠟燭被風吹熄，可以用火柴重新點燃。"},{"en":"If the outer torch flame goes out, an inner flame can restore it quickly.","zh":"如果火炬外層火焰熄滅，內層火焰可以迅速恢復它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lighting something again.","zh":"這個短語描述再次點燃某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"go out","meaning":"熄滅","examples":[{"en":"The external flame can be relit if it goes out.","zh":"如果外層火焰熄滅，它可以被重新點燃。"},{"en":"To go out means for a flame or light to stop burning or shining.","zh":"「go out」意思是火焰或燈光停止燃燒或發亮。"},{"en":"A candle may go out when someone opens a windy window.","zh":"當有人打開有風的窗，蠟燭可能熄滅。"},{"en":"If the torch flame goes out during a relay, the ceremony may be interrupted.","zh":"如果火炬火焰在接力中熄滅，儀式可能被打斷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a flame or light stopping.","zh":"這個短語描述火焰或燈光停止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"as for","meaning":"至於","examples":[{"en":"As for the 2002 torch, its top section was made of glass.","zh":"至於2002年火炬，其頂部部分由玻璃製成。"},{"en":"As for means turning attention to a new topic or item.","zh":"「as for」意思是把注意力轉向新的話題或項目。"},{"en":"The grammar homework is finished; as for the reading task, I still need ten minutes.","zh":"文法功課已完成；至於閱讀任務，我還需要十分鐘。"},{"en":"If a writer compares several torches, “as for” helps move from one torch to another.","zh":"如果作者比較幾支火炬，“as for” 有助由一支轉到另一支。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a new subject in a comparison.","zh":"這個短語在比較中引入新主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"top section","meaning":"頂部部分","examples":[{"en":"The top section of the 2002 torch was made of glass.","zh":"2002年火炬的頂部部分由玻璃製成。"},{"en":"The top section is the upper part of an object.","zh":"「top section」是物件的上方部分。"},{"en":"The top section of a poster usually contains the title and main image.","zh":"海報頂部部分通常包含標題和主要圖片。"},{"en":"If the top section of a torch is transparent, viewers may notice the flame more clearly.","zh":"如果火炬頂部部分透明，觀眾可能更清楚注意到火焰。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the highest part of something.","zh":"這個短語描述某物最高部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be made of glass","meaning":"由玻璃製成","examples":[{"en":"The top section was made of glass.","zh":"頂部部分由玻璃製成。"},{"en":"To be made of glass means to be constructed using glass as the material.","zh":"「be made of glass」意思是使用玻璃作材料製成。"},{"en":"A display case may be made of glass so people can see the objects inside.","zh":"展示櫃可能由玻璃製成，讓人看見裡面的物件。"},{"en":"If a torch section is made of glass, it can reflect light and symbolic meaning.","zh":"如果火炬部分由玻璃製成，它可以反射光線和象徵意義。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies glass as the material.","zh":"這個短語指出玻璃是材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"reflect a theme","meaning":"反映主題","examples":[{"en":"The glass section was designed to reflect the Olympic theme.","zh":"玻璃部分被設計來反映奧運主題。"},{"en":"To reflect a theme means to show or express the main idea of an event, design, or work.","zh":"「reflect a theme」意思是展示或表達活動、設計或作品的主要想法。"},{"en":"A school poster may use green colours to reflect a theme of environmental protection.","zh":"學校海報可能使用綠色來反映環保主題。"},{"en":"If a torch design reflects a theme, its appearance helps communicate the message.","zh":"如果火炬設計反映主題，其外觀就能幫助傳達訊息。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visual expression of an idea.","zh":"這個短語描述以視覺表達想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Light the Fire Within","meaning":"點燃心中的火","examples":[{"en":"The theme of the 2002 Olympics was Light the Fire Within.","zh":"2002年奧運主題是「點燃心中的火」。"},{"en":"Light the Fire Within means awaken inner energy, passion, courage, or determination.","zh":"「Light the Fire Within」意思是喚醒內在能量、熱情、勇氣或決心。"},{"en":"A teacher may tell students to light the fire within before a difficult exam season.","zh":"老師可能在艱難考試季前叫學生點燃心中的火。"},{"en":"If a theme focuses on inner fire, it connects sport with motivation and personal spirit.","zh":"如果主題集中於內在火焰，它就把運動與動機和個人精神連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase is symbolic, not only about a real flame.","zh":"這個短語是象徵性的，不只是關於真實火焰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be of great significance for","meaning":"對……有重大意義","examples":[{"en":"The 2002 torch was of great significance for the design of later torches.","zh":"2002年火炬對後來火炬的設計有重大意義。"},{"en":"To be of great significance for something means to be very important for its development or meaning.","zh":"「be of great significance for」某事，意思是對其發展或意義非常重要。"},{"en":"A student’s first successful speech may be of great significance for their confidence.","zh":"學生第一次成功演講可能對其信心有重大意義。"},{"en":"If one design influences later designs, it has lasting importance.","zh":"如果一個設計影響後來設計，它就有持久重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes major importance.","zh":"這個短語描述重大重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"subsequent torches","meaning":"後來的火炬","examples":[{"en":"The 2002 torch influenced the design of subsequent torches.","zh":"2002年火炬影響了後來火炬的設計。"},{"en":"Subsequent torches are torches that came later in time.","zh":"「subsequent torches」是時間上較後出現的火炬。"},{"en":"A successful school logo may influence subsequent posters and certificates.","zh":"成功的校徽可能影響後來的海報和證書。"},{"en":"If one torch introduces a strong design idea, later torches may borrow from it.","zh":"如果一支火炬引入強有力的設計想法，後來火炬可能借鑑它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to later examples in a sequence.","zh":"這個短語指序列中較後的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete the summary below","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to complete the summary below.","zh":"考生需要完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary below means to fill in missing information in the short passage that follows.","zh":"「complete the summary below」意思是填寫下方短文中缺失的資料。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete the summary below by finding exact words in the text.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過在文本中找原字完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"If candidates understand the main idea, they can choose the missing words more accurately.","zh":"如果考生理解主要意思，就能更準確選出缺失詞語。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"choose no more than three words","meaning":"選擇不多於三個字","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should choose no more than three words from the passage.","zh":"考生應從文章中選擇不多於三個字。"},{"en":"Choose no more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"「choose no more than three words」意思是答案必須包含三個詞或更少。"},{"en":"If the answer is “a light container”, it follows the rule because it has three words.","zh":"如果答案是 “a light container”，它符合規則，因為有三個詞。"},{"en":"If students add extra words, the answer may break the instruction even if the idea is right.","zh":"如果學生加入額外詞語，即使意思正確，答案也可能違反指示。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"from the passage","meaning":"從文章中","examples":[{"en":"The answers must come from the passage.","zh":"答案必須來自文章。"},{"en":"From the passage means the words or information should be taken directly from the reading text.","zh":"「from the passage」意思是詞語或資料應直接取自閱讀文章。"},{"en":"In IELTS Reading, candidates often need to copy exact words from the passage.","zh":"在 IELTS Reading 中，考生常需要從文章中抄寫原字。"},{"en":"If students use their own synonyms, the answer may not match the required wording.","zh":"如果學生使用自己的同義詞，答案可能不符合要求措辭。"},{"en":"The phrase tells students where to find the answer.","zh":"這個短語告訴學生在哪裡找答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"write your answers in","meaning":"將答案寫在……","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write their answers in the boxes on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生將答案寫在答題紙上的方格內。"},{"en":"To write your answers in a place means to put the responses in the correct space.","zh":"「write your answers in」某處，意思是把答案放在正確位置。"},{"en":"Students should write their answers in the numbered boxes, not in the margins.","zh":"學生應將答案寫在有編號的方格內，而不是頁邊。"},{"en":"If answers are written in the wrong place, the marker may not know which question they belong to.","zh":"如果答案寫在錯誤位置，閱卷員可能不知道它們屬於哪一題。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an instruction about answer placement.","zh":"這個短語提供答案位置指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"on your answer sheet","meaning":"在答題紙上","examples":[{"en":"Answers should be written on your answer sheet.","zh":"答案應寫在答題紙上。"},{"en":"On your answer sheet means on the official paper or form where exam answers are recorded.","zh":"「on your answer sheet」意思是在記錄考試答案的正式紙張或表格上。"},{"en":"Candidates should check that the number on the question matches the number on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生應檢查題目編號與答題紙編號相符。"},{"en":"If an answer is written only in the question booklet, it may not be marked.","zh":"如果答案只寫在題簿上，可能不會被評分。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the required place for final answers.","zh":"這個短語指出最終答案所需位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"as requested by","meaning":"按……要求","examples":[{"en":"The Olympic torch is designed as requested by the Olympic Committee.","zh":"奧運火炬按奧林匹克委員會要求設計。"},{"en":"As requested by someone means according to what that person or organisation asked for.","zh":"「as requested by」某人，意思是按照該人或機構的要求。"},{"en":"The report was rewritten as requested by the teacher.","zh":"報告按老師要求被重寫。"},{"en":"If a design is made as requested by a committee, it must follow official requirements.","zh":"如果設計按委員會要求製作，它必須遵從官方要求。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that an action follows instructions.","zh":"這個短語顯示行動跟從指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be carefully designed","meaning":"被仔細設計","examples":[{"en":"The Olympic torch must be carefully designed.","zh":"奧運火炬必須被仔細設計。"},{"en":"To be carefully designed means to be planned with close attention to safety, appearance, materials, and function.","zh":"「be carefully designed」意思是在安全、外觀、材料和功能方面仔細規劃。"},{"en":"A children’s playground must be carefully designed to prevent accidents.","zh":"兒童遊樂場必須被仔細設計，以防意外。"},{"en":"If a torch will be carried by thousands of people, careless design could create risk.","zh":"如果火炬會由數以千計的人傳遞，粗心設計可能造成風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes thoughtful and detailed planning.","zh":"這個短語描述周詳而細緻的規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be capable of withstanding","meaning":"能夠承受……","examples":[{"en":"The torch must be capable of withstanding difficult conditions.","zh":"火炬必須能夠承受困難情況。"},{"en":"To be capable of withstanding something means to be strong enough to resist or survive it.","zh":"「be capable of withstanding」某事，意思是有足夠強度抵受或撐過它。"},{"en":"A school tent must be capable of withstanding rain during an outdoor camp.","zh":"學校帳篷必須能夠承受戶外營中的雨水。"},{"en":"If a torch cannot withstand wind, the flame may go out.","zh":"如果火炬不能承受風力，火焰可能熄滅。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strength against pressure or difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述抵抗壓力或困難的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"all kinds of","meaning":"各種……","examples":[{"en":"The torch must withstand all kinds of severe weather conditions.","zh":"火炬必須承受各種惡劣天氣情況。"},{"en":"All kinds of means many different types of something.","zh":"「all kinds of」意思是許多不同種類的某物。"},{"en":"A community centre may offer all kinds of activities, from yoga to language classes.","zh":"社區中心可能提供各種活動，從瑜伽到語言課都有。"},{"en":"If the relay passes through different climates, the torch must handle all kinds of weather.","zh":"如果接力穿越不同氣候，火炬必須應付各種天氣。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses variety and range.","zh":"這個短語強調多樣和範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"generally","meaning":"一般而言","examples":[{"en":"Generally, the modern Olympic torch has both aesthetic and practical value.","zh":"一般而言，現代奧運火炬同時具有美學和實用價值。"},{"en":"Generally means usually or in most cases.","zh":"「generally」意思是通常或在大多數情況下。"},{"en":"Generally, students write better essays when they plan before writing.","zh":"一般而言，學生寫作前先規劃，文章會寫得更好。"},{"en":"If something is generally true, there may still be exceptions.","zh":"如果某事一般而言正確，仍可能有例外。"},{"en":"The word introduces a broad statement.","zh":"這個詞引入概括說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be copied","meaning":"被複製","examples":[{"en":"The torch must be copied many times for the relay.","zh":"火炬必須為接力被複製很多次。"},{"en":"To be copied means to be reproduced or made again in the same form.","zh":"「be copied」意思是以相同形式被複製或再次製作。"},{"en":"A worksheet may be copied for every student in the class.","zh":"工作紙可能被複印給班上每位學生。"},{"en":"If a torch design is copied thousands of times, the copies must remain safe and accurate.","zh":"如果火炬設計被複製數千次，複製品必須保持安全和準確。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reproduction.","zh":"這個短語描述複製生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be constructed to accommodate","meaning":"被製造以配合……","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of torches are constructed to accommodate thousands of runners.","zh":"數以千計的火炬被製造，以配合數以千計的跑手。"},{"en":"To be constructed to accommodate something means to be built in a way that suits or provides for it.","zh":"「be constructed to accommodate」某事，意思是被建造或製造成能適合或滿足它。"},{"en":"A school hall may be constructed to accommodate large assemblies and exams.","zh":"學校禮堂可能被建造以配合大型集會和考試。"},{"en":"If many runners need torches, enough torches must be made to serve them.","zh":"如果許多跑手需要火炬，就必須製作足夠火炬供他們使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes building something to meet a practical need.","zh":"這個短語描述為滿足實際需要而製造某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"each leg of","meaning":"……的每一段","examples":[{"en":"Runners carry the torch through each leg of the Olympic relay.","zh":"跑手把火炬帶過奧運接力的每一段。"},{"en":"Each leg of a relay means each separate stage or section of the route.","zh":"「each leg of」接力，意思是路線中的每個獨立階段或部分。"},{"en":"In a four-person race, each runner completes one leg of the relay.","zh":"在四人接力賽中，每位跑手完成接力的一段。"},{"en":"If every leg is completed, the torch can move from the start to the host city.","zh":"如果每一段都完成，火炬就能由起點移到主辦城市。"},{"en":"The phrase divides a long journey into smaller parts.","zh":"這個短語把長旅程分成較小部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"have an opportunity to","meaning":"有機會去……","examples":[{"en":"Each runner has an opportunity to purchase the torch.","zh":"每位跑手都有機會購買火炬。"},{"en":"To have an opportunity to do something means to have a chance to do it.","zh":"「have an opportunity to」做某事，意思是有機會做該事。"},{"en":"Students have an opportunity to ask questions after the lecture.","zh":"學生在講座後有機會提問。"},{"en":"If runners are offered the chance to buy the torch, they can keep a memory of the relay.","zh":"如果跑手獲得購買火炬的機會，他們可以保留接力回憶。"},{"en":"The phrase describes having a possible chance.","zh":"這個短語描述擁有可能的機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"purchase the torch","meaning":"購買火炬","examples":[{"en":"Each runner can purchase the torch as a souvenir.","zh":"每位跑手都可以購買火炬作紀念品。"},{"en":"To purchase the torch means to buy the torch formally.","zh":"「purchase the torch」意思是正式買下火炬。"},{"en":"A student may purchase a graduation photo as a memory of school life.","zh":"學生可能購買畢業相，作為學校生活回憶。"},{"en":"If a runner purchases the torch, it becomes a personal object connected with the relay.","zh":"如果跑手購買火炬，它就成為與接力相關的個人物件。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to say “buy the torch”.","zh":"這個短語是 “buy the torch” 的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"at the end of","meaning":"在……結束時","examples":[{"en":"Each runner may buy the torch at the end of his or her leg of the relay.","zh":"每位跑手可在自己那段接力結束時購買火炬。"},{"en":"At the end of something means when that event, period, or section finishes.","zh":"「at the end of」某事，意思是在該事件、時段或部分完成時。"},{"en":"Students submit their essays at the end of the lesson.","zh":"學生在課堂結束時提交文章。"},{"en":"If a runner finishes their section, they may then keep or buy the torch.","zh":"如果跑手完成自己的路段，他之後可能保留或購買火炬。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the finishing point.","zh":"這個短語標示完成點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"look at the following statements","meaning":"查看以下陳述","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should look at the following statements before matching them.","zh":"考生應在配對前查看以下陳述。"},{"en":"To look at the following statements means to read the listed sentences or claims below.","zh":"「look at the following statements」意思是閱讀下方列出的句子或說法。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should look at the following statements before scanning the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先查看以下陳述，再掃讀文章。"},{"en":"If candidates read the statements carefully, they know what information to find.","zh":"如果考生仔細閱讀陳述，就知道要尋找甚麼資料。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an instruction to examine the next items.","zh":"這個短語給出檢視下一批項目的指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the list of","meaning":"……列表","examples":[{"en":"The question provides a list of Olympic torches.","zh":"題目提供奧運火炬列表。"},{"en":"A list of something is a group of items written one after another.","zh":"「a list of」某物，是一組逐項寫出的項目。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students a list of useful phrases before an exam.","zh":"老師可能在考試前給學生一份實用短語列表。"},{"en":"If a question gives a list, candidates must choose from those options.","zh":"如果題目提供列表，考生必須從那些選項中選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a set of choices or items.","zh":"這個短語引入一組選擇或項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"match each statement with","meaning":"將每項陳述與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match each statement with the correct Olympic torch.","zh":"考生將每項陳述與正確的奧運火炬配對。"},{"en":"To match each statement with something means to connect every statement to the right item.","zh":"「match each statement with」某物，意思是把每項陳述連接到正確項目。"},{"en":"Students may match each word with its definition in a vocabulary exercise.","zh":"學生可能在詞彙練習中把每個詞與其定義配對。"},{"en":"If candidates identify the correct evidence, matching becomes easier.","zh":"如果考生找出正確證據，配對就更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a pairing task.","zh":"這個短語描述配對任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the correct Olympic torch","meaning":"正確的奧運火炬","examples":[{"en":"Each statement must be matched with the correct Olympic torch.","zh":"每項陳述必須與正確的奧運火炬配對。"},{"en":"The correct Olympic torch is the torch that matches the information in the statement.","zh":"「the correct Olympic torch」是與陳述資料相符的火炬。"},{"en":"If a statement mentions liquid fuel first appearing, students must find which torch matches that detail.","zh":"如果陳述提到液體燃料首次出現，學生必須找出哪支火炬符合該細節。"},{"en":"Choosing the wrong torch means the evidence has been connected to the wrong example.","zh":"選錯火炬代表證據被連到錯誤例子。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the exact answer in a matching task.","zh":"這個短語指出配對題中的確切答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"first use of","meaning":"首次使用……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the first use of liquid fuel.","zh":"題目問液體燃料的首次使用。"},{"en":"The first use of something means the earliest time it was used.","zh":"「the first use of」某物，意思是它最早被使用的時間。"},{"en":"A museum label may mention the first use of a new machine in local factories.","zh":"博物館標籤可能提到某新機器在本地工廠的首次使用。"},{"en":"If students know when a material was first used, they can follow technological development.","zh":"如果學生知道某材料何時首次使用，就能追蹤技術發展。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the beginning of practical use.","zh":"這個短語指出實際使用的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"not environmentally friendly","meaning":"不環保","examples":[{"en":"One torch was not environmentally friendly because it produced smoke.","zh":"有一支火炬因產生煙霧而不環保。"},{"en":"Not environmentally friendly means harmful or not helpful to the natural environment.","zh":"「not environmentally friendly」意思是對自然環境有害或無益。"},{"en":"A product with too much plastic packaging is not environmentally friendly.","zh":"包裝含太多塑膠的產品並不環保。"},{"en":"If a fuel produces a lot of smoke, it may damage air quality.","zh":"如果燃料產生大量煙霧，可能損害空氣質素。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that has a negative environmental impact.","zh":"這個短語描述對環境有負面影響的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"first to record","meaning":"首次記錄……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which torch was first to record the runner’s name.","zh":"題目問哪支火炬首次記錄跑手姓名。"},{"en":"First to record something means the earliest one to include or write that information.","zh":"「first to record」某事，意思是最早包含或寫下該資料的一個。"},{"en":"A school register may be the first document to record a new student’s name.","zh":"學校名冊可能是首次記錄新生姓名的文件。"},{"en":"If a runner’s name is recorded on a torch, the design recognises individual participation.","zh":"如果跑手姓名被記錄在火炬上，設計就認可個人參與。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the earliest example of recording information.","zh":"這個短語突出記錄資料的最早例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"potentially risky","meaning":"有潛在危險的","examples":[{"en":"Some early torch fuels were potentially risky.","zh":"有些早期火炬燃料有潛在危險。"},{"en":"Potentially risky means possibly dangerous, even if harm does not always happen.","zh":"「potentially risky」意思是可能危險，即使傷害不一定總會發生。"},{"en":"Leaving candles beside curtains is potentially risky because fire can spread quickly.","zh":"把蠟燭放在窗簾旁有潛在危險，因為火可以快速蔓延。"},{"en":"If a fuel source is unpredictable, it may be unsafe for public use.","zh":"如果燃料來源難以預測，它可能不適合公共使用。"},{"en":"The phrase warns about possible danger.","zh":"這個短語警告可能存在危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"burn someone’s arms","meaning":"燒傷某人的手臂","examples":[{"en":"One torch burnt the runner’s arms during the relay.","zh":"有一支火炬在接力期間燒傷跑手的手臂。"},{"en":"To burn someone’s arms means to injure the skin of the arms with heat or fire.","zh":"「burn someone’s arms」意思是用熱力或火傷害某人手臂的皮膚。"},{"en":"A cook may burn their arms if hot oil splashes from a pan.","zh":"如果熱油從鍋中濺出，廚師可能燒傷手臂。"},{"en":"If flaming material falls from a torch, it can burn the person carrying it.","zh":"如果燃燒材料從火炬掉落，它可以燒傷持火炬的人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a physical injury caused by heat.","zh":"這個短語描述由熱力造成的身體傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be specially designed around","meaning":"圍繞……特別設計","examples":[{"en":"The 2002 torch was specially designed around a light theme.","zh":"2002年火炬圍繞光的主題特別設計。"},{"en":"To be specially designed around a theme means to be created with that theme as the central idea.","zh":"「be specially designed around」某主題，意思是以該主題為核心想法創作。"},{"en":"A classroom may be specially designed around a reading theme with bookshelves and quiet corners.","zh":"課室可能圍繞閱讀主題特別設計，設有書架和安靜角落。"},{"en":"If a design is built around a theme, its materials, colours, and shape all support that idea.","zh":"如果設計圍繞主題建立，其材料、顏色和形狀都會支持該想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes theme-centred design.","zh":"這個短語描述以主題為中心的設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"not lit in Greece","meaning":"並非在希臘點燃","examples":[{"en":"One Olympic flame was not lit in Greece.","zh":"有一屆奧運聖火並非在希臘點燃。"},{"en":"Not lit in Greece means the flame was started somewhere other than Greece.","zh":"「not lit in Greece」意思是火焰在希臘以外的地方點燃。"},{"en":"If a ceremonial lamp is not lit in the school hall, it may be lit outside and carried in.","zh":"如果儀式燈不是在學校禮堂點燃，它可能在外面點燃再帶入。"},{"en":"If an Olympic flame is not lit in Greece, the tradition differs from the usual ancient-symbolic practice.","zh":"如果奧運聖火並非在希臘點燃，傳統就與通常的古代象徵做法不同。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a change in the place of lighting.","zh":"這個短語指出點火地點的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"label the diagram below","meaning":"標示下圖","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to label the diagram below.","zh":"考生需要標示下圖。"},{"en":"To label the diagram below means to write the correct names beside parts of the picture underneath the question.","zh":"「label the diagram below」意思是在題目下方圖片的各部分旁寫上正確名稱。"},{"en":"In a science test, students may label the diagram below with words such as valve, tank, and handle.","zh":"在科學測驗中，學生可能用 valve、tank 和 handle 等詞標示下圖。"},{"en":"If candidates understand how the torch works, they can label its parts more accurately.","zh":"如果考生理解火炬如何運作，就能更準確標示其部件。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction in visual reading questions.","zh":"這個短語是圖像閱讀題中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"diagram","meaning":"圖表；示意圖","examples":[{"en":"The diagram shows parts of the Olympic torch.","zh":"圖表顯示奧運火炬的各部分。"},{"en":"A diagram is a simple drawing that explains parts, structure, or a process.","zh":"「diagram」是用來解釋部分、結構或過程的簡單圖畫。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a diagram to show how water moves through a filter.","zh":"老師可能用示意圖展示水如何通過濾水器。"},{"en":"If a process is complicated, a diagram can make it easier to understand.","zh":"如果過程複雜，圖表可以令它更容易理解。"},{"en":"The word refers to an explanatory picture, not a decorative image.","zh":"這個詞指解釋性圖片，而不是裝飾圖片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 56 - The Olympic Torch.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 57":[{"front":"elephant communication","meaning":"大象溝通","examples":[{"en":"The passage explores the complicated science of elephant communication.","zh":"文章探討大象溝通這門複雜科學。"},{"en":"Elephant communication means the different ways elephants send and receive messages.","zh":"大象溝通，指大象傳送和接收信息的不同方式。"},{"en":"Elephants may communicate through sounds, body movement, touch, smell, and ground vibrations.","zh":"大象可能透過聲音、身體動作、觸碰、氣味和地面震動來溝通。"},{"en":"If elephants live far apart, communication helps them find family, danger, and mates.","zh":"如果大象相距很遠，溝通有助牠們尋找家族、危險和配偶。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a complex animal signalling system, not just ordinary noise.","zh":"這個短語指複雜的動物訊號系統，而不只是普通聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"postdoctoral fellow","meaning":"博士後研究員","examples":[{"en":"O’Connell-Rodwell is a postdoctoral fellow at Stanford University.","zh":"O’Connell-Rodwell 是史丹福大學的博士後研究員。"},{"en":"A postdoctoral fellow is a researcher who has finished a doctorate and continues advanced research.","zh":"博士後研究員，是完成博士學位後繼續進行高階研究的研究者。"},{"en":"A postdoctoral fellow may work in a university lab before becoming a professor.","zh":"博士後研究員可能在成為教授前，在大學實驗室工作。"},{"en":"If a postdoctoral fellow studies animals in the field, they collect data after years of specialist training.","zh":"如果博士後研究員在野外研究動物，他們是在多年專業訓練後收集數據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an early-career academic researcher after the PhD stage.","zh":"這個短語指博士階段後的早期學術研究者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"travel to","meaning":"前往","examples":[{"en":"O’Connell-Rodwell travelled to Namibia to study elephants.","zh":"O’Connell-Rodwell 前往納米比亞研究大象。"},{"en":"To travel to a place means to go there, usually over some distance.","zh":"前往某地，指到那裡去，通常跨越一段距離。"},{"en":"A student may travel to another city for a debate competition.","zh":"學生可能前往另一個城市參加辯論比賽。"},{"en":"If researchers travel to a wildlife reserve, they can observe animals in their natural setting.","zh":"如果研究者前往野生動物保護區，就可以在自然環境中觀察動物。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on movement toward a destination.","zh":"這個短語強調朝目的地移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"wildlife reserve","meaning":"野生動物保護區","examples":[{"en":"She travelled to Namibia’s first-ever wildlife reserve.","zh":"她前往納米比亞首個野生動物保護區。"},{"en":"A wildlife reserve is an area where wild animals and their habitats are protected.","zh":"野生動物保護區，是保護野生動物及其棲息地的地區。"},{"en":"Families may visit a wildlife reserve to see animals without harming them.","zh":"家庭可能參觀野生動物保護區，在不傷害動物的情況下觀察牠們。"},{"en":"If a reserve is well managed, endangered animals have a safer place to live.","zh":"如果保護區管理良好，瀕危動物就有更安全的居住地方。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to protected land for wildlife conservation.","zh":"這個短語指用於野生動物保育的受保護土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"explore the realm of","meaning":"探索……的領域","examples":[{"en":"She went to Namibia to explore the realm of elephant communication.","zh":"她前往納米比亞探索大象溝通的領域。"},{"en":"To explore the realm of something means to investigate a field or area of knowledge deeply.","zh":"探索某領域，指深入研究某個知識範圍或範疇。"},{"en":"A student may explore the realm of history by reading diaries, maps, and old letters.","zh":"學生可能透過閱讀日記、地圖和舊信件來探索歷史領域。"},{"en":"If scientists explore a new realm, they may ask questions no one has answered before.","zh":"如果科學家探索新領域，可能提出以前沒有人回答過的問題。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests entering a complex area of study.","zh":"這個短語暗示進入一個複雜研究範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mystical and complicated","meaning":"神秘而複雜的","examples":[{"en":"Elephant communication is described as mystical and complicated.","zh":"大象溝通被描述為神秘而複雜。"},{"en":"Mystical and complicated means mysterious, difficult to understand, and full of hidden details.","zh":"神秘而複雜，指神秘、難以理解，並充滿隱藏細節。"},{"en":"To beginners, advanced grammar may seem mystical and complicated until examples make it clear.","zh":"對初學者來說，高階文法可能看似神秘而複雜，直到例子令它清楚。"},{"en":"If a subject involves invisible signals and animal behaviour, it can feel hard to explain.","zh":"如果一個科目涉及看不見的訊號和動物行為，就可能很難解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests both wonder and difficulty.","zh":"這個短語同時暗示驚奇和困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"along with","meaning":"與……一起","examples":[{"en":"O’Connell-Rodwell, along with her colleagues, joined a scientific revolution.","zh":"O’Connell-Rodwell 與她的同事一起加入了一場科學革命。"},{"en":"Along with means together with or in addition to someone or something.","zh":"與……一起，指和某人或某事一同，或加上某人某事。"},{"en":"A teacher, along with several students, organised a charity sale.","zh":"一位老師與幾名學生一起組織慈善義賣。"},{"en":"If one researcher works along with a team, the project can collect more evidence.","zh":"如果一位研究者與團隊一起工作，項目可以收集更多證據。"},{"en":"The phrase adds another person or group to the action.","zh":"這個短語把另一個人或群體加入行動中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be part of","meaning":"是……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"She is part of a scientific revolution in elephant research.","zh":"她是大象研究科學革命的一部分。"},{"en":"To be part of something means to belong to it or contribute to it.","zh":"是某事的一部分，指屬於它或對它有貢獻。"},{"en":"A student can be part of a school debate team even if they are not the leader.","zh":"即使學生不是領袖，也可以是學校辯論隊的一部分。"},{"en":"If many researchers ask new questions together, each one may be part of a bigger change.","zh":"如果許多研究者一起提出新問題，每個人都可能是更大變化的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase shows membership or involvement.","zh":"這個短語顯示成員身份或參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a scientific revolution","meaning":"科學革命","examples":[{"en":"A scientific revolution changed how researchers understand elephant communication.","zh":"一場科學革命改變了研究者理解大象溝通的方式。"},{"en":"A scientific revolution is a major change in scientific thinking or method.","zh":"科學革命，是科學思維或方法上的重大改變。"},{"en":"The discovery of germs created a scientific revolution in medicine.","zh":"細菌的發現造成了醫學上的科學革命。"},{"en":"If new evidence overturns old ideas, a scientific revolution may begin.","zh":"如果新證據推翻舊想法，科學革命可能開始。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a deep change in expert understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述專家理解上的深層改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"start almost 20 years ago","meaning":"差不多二十年前開始","examples":[{"en":"The scientific revolution started almost 20 years ago.","zh":"這場科學革命差不多二十年前開始。"},{"en":"To start almost 20 years ago means to begin nearly two decades before the time discussed.","zh":"差不多二十年前開始，指在討論時間之前接近二十年開始。"},{"en":"A school tradition that started almost 20 years ago may now feel normal to students.","zh":"一項差不多二十年前開始的學校傳統，現在對學生來說可能很平常。"},{"en":"If a research revolution began long ago, today’s findings may build on years of work.","zh":"如果研究革命很久以前開始，今天的發現可能建立在多年工作之上。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate starting time.","zh":"這個短語給出約略開始時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"make a stunning revelation","meaning":"作出驚人發現","examples":[{"en":"The research made a stunning revelation about elephants.","zh":"這項研究對大象作出驚人發現。"},{"en":"To make a stunning revelation means to reveal something surprising and important.","zh":"作出驚人發現，指揭示令人驚訝而重要的事情。"},{"en":"A hospital study may make a stunning revelation about a simple habit that improves health.","zh":"醫院研究可能對改善健康的簡單習慣作出驚人發現。"},{"en":"If research shows animals communicate in an unexpected way, it can shock experts.","zh":"如果研究顯示動物以意想不到的方式溝通，可能震驚專家。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a discovery that changes understanding.","zh":"這個短語突出改變理解的發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be capable of","meaning":"有能力……","examples":[{"en":"Elephants are capable of communicating over long distances.","zh":"大象有能力遠距離溝通。"},{"en":"To be capable of doing something means to have the ability to do it.","zh":"有能力做某事，指具備做該事的能力。"},{"en":"A beginner may be capable of writing a short paragraph after learning clear sentence patterns.","zh":"初學者學會清楚句式後，可能有能力寫短段落。"},{"en":"If an animal is capable of long-distance communication, researchers must study its signals carefully.","zh":"如果動物有能力遠距離溝通，研究者必須仔細研究其訊號。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ability, not only possibility.","zh":"這個短語描述能力，而不只是可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"communicate with each other","meaning":"互相溝通","examples":[{"en":"Elephants can communicate with each other over long distances.","zh":"大象可以遠距離互相溝通。"},{"en":"To communicate with each other means to exchange information between two or more individuals.","zh":"互相溝通，指兩個或更多個體之間交換資訊。"},{"en":"Students communicate with each other in a group project by sharing ideas and dividing tasks.","zh":"學生在小組項目中透過分享想法和分工互相溝通。"},{"en":"If animals communicate with each other, one animal’s signal can change another’s behaviour.","zh":"如果動物互相溝通，一隻動物的訊號可以改變另一隻的行為。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on two-way or group exchange of messages.","zh":"這個短語強調雙向或群體信息交換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"over long distances","meaning":"遠距離地","examples":[{"en":"Elephants can send signals over long distances.","zh":"大象可以遠距離地發送訊號。"},{"en":"Over long distances means across far spaces rather than nearby areas.","zh":"遠距離地，指跨越很遠空間，而不是附近範圍。"},{"en":"Mobile phones help families communicate over long distances when relatives live abroad.","zh":"當親人住在海外，手機幫助家庭遠距離溝通。"},{"en":"If animals live across a wide area, long-distance signals help them stay connected.","zh":"如果動物分布在廣大地區，遠距離訊號有助牠們保持聯繫。"},{"en":"The phrase describes communication or movement across far space.","zh":"這個短語描述跨越遠距離的溝通或移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"low-frequency sounds","meaning":"低頻聲音","examples":[{"en":"Elephants use low-frequency sounds to communicate.","zh":"大象使用低頻聲音來溝通。"},{"en":"Low-frequency sounds are deep sounds with slow vibrations.","zh":"低頻聲音，是震動較慢的低沉聲音。"},{"en":"A large drum can produce low-frequency sounds that people feel in their chest.","zh":"大鼓可以發出令人胸口感到震動的低頻聲音。"},{"en":"If sounds are low enough, they may travel farther than higher sounds.","zh":"如果聲音足夠低沉，可能比高音傳得更遠。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to deep sound waves, not quiet sounds.","zh":"這個短語指低沉聲波，而不是微弱聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"also known as","meaning":"又稱為","examples":[{"en":"Low-frequency sounds are also known as infrasounds.","zh":"低頻聲音又稱為次聲波。"},{"en":"Also known as means having another name.","zh":"又稱為，指有另一個名稱。"},{"en":"The flu is also known as influenza.","zh":"流感又稱為 influenza。"},{"en":"If a technical term is also known by a simpler name, students can remember it more easily.","zh":"如果專業術語又有較簡單名稱，學生就更容易記住。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an alternative name.","zh":"這個短語引入另一個名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"infrasounds","meaning":"次聲波","examples":[{"en":"Infrasounds are too deep for humans to hear.","zh":"次聲波低沉至人類聽不到。"},{"en":"Infrasounds are sounds with frequencies below the normal range of human hearing.","zh":"次聲波，是頻率低於人類正常聽覺範圍的聲音。"},{"en":"Some large animals and natural events can produce infrasounds that travel far.","zh":"一些大型動物和自然事件可以產生傳得很遠的次聲波。"},{"en":"If humans cannot hear a signal, machines may be needed to detect it.","zh":"如果人類聽不到某個訊號，可能需要機器來偵測。"},{"en":"The word refers to very low-frequency sound.","zh":"這個詞指非常低頻的聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"too deep for humans to hear","meaning":"低沉至人類聽不到","examples":[{"en":"Some elephant sounds are too deep for humans to hear.","zh":"一些大象聲音低沉至人類聽不到。"},{"en":"Too deep for humans to hear means the sound frequency is lower than human hearing can detect.","zh":"低沉至人類聽不到，指聲音頻率低於人類聽覺可偵測範圍。"},{"en":"A machine may record sounds that are too deep for people in the room to hear.","zh":"機器可能錄到房內人們聽不到的低沉聲音。"},{"en":"If a sound is too deep for humans to hear, researchers need special equipment to study it.","zh":"如果聲音低沉至人類聽不到，研究者就需要特殊設備來研究它。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why a sound can exist even when people hear nothing.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何聲音存在但人們聽不見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as might be expected","meaning":"正如可以預期","examples":[{"en":"As might be expected, elephants’ ears may help them detect seismic sound.","zh":"正如可以預期，大象的耳朵可能幫助牠們偵測地面震動聲。"},{"en":"As might be expected means this result is not surprising because it fits what we already know.","zh":"正如可以預期，指這結果不令人意外，因為它符合我們已有認識。"},{"en":"As might be expected, students who practise daily usually improve faster.","zh":"正如可以預期，每天練習的學生通常進步較快。"},{"en":"If an animal has huge ears, it is reasonable to suspect hearing may be important.","zh":"如果動物有巨大耳朵，懷疑聽覺重要是合理的。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an expected or logical point.","zh":"這個短語引入預期中或合乎邏輯的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ability to detect","meaning":"偵測……的能力","examples":[{"en":"African elephants have an ability to detect seismic sound.","zh":"非洲象有偵測地面震動聲的能力。"},{"en":"An ability to detect something is the power to notice or sense it.","zh":"偵測某物的能力，是注意或感應到它的能力。"},{"en":"Smoke alarms have the ability to detect smoke before people see flames.","zh":"煙霧警報器有能力在人們看見火焰前偵測煙霧。"},{"en":"If elephants detect ground vibrations, they may receive messages from far away.","zh":"如果大象偵測到地面震動，牠們可能接收來自遠方的信息。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on sensing something that may not be obvious.","zh":"這個短語強調感應不明顯事物的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"seismic sound","meaning":"地面震動聲；地震波聲音","examples":[{"en":"Seismic sound may be involved in elephant communication.","zh":"地面震動聲可能涉及大象溝通。"},{"en":"Seismic sound is sound or vibration that travels through the ground.","zh":"地面震動聲，是透過地面傳播的聲音或震動。"},{"en":"People may feel seismic vibrations when a heavy train passes nearby.","zh":"當重型火車從附近經過，人們可能感到地面震動。"},{"en":"If elephant signals travel through the ground, their feet and bodies may help detect them.","zh":"如果大象訊號透過地面傳播，牠們的腳和身體可能幫助偵測。"},{"en":"The phrase connects sound with ground movement.","zh":"這個短語把聲音與地面移動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have something to do with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Their ability to detect seismic sound may have something to do with their ears.","zh":"牠們偵測地面震動聲的能力可能與耳朵有關。"},{"en":"To have something to do with something means to be connected with it in some way.","zh":"與某事有關，指以某種方式與它連繫。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may have something to do with staying up late.","zh":"學生疲倦可能與熬夜有關。"},{"en":"If a body feature is unusual, it may be related to a special ability.","zh":"如果身體特徵不尋常，它可能與特殊能力相關。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a possible connection without claiming certainty.","zh":"這個短語暗示可能有連繫，但不表示完全確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hammer bone","meaning":"錘骨","examples":[{"en":"The hammer bone in an elephant’s inner ear is proportionally huge.","zh":"大象內耳中的錘骨按比例來說非常巨大。"},{"en":"The hammer bone is a small bone in the ear that helps transmit sound vibrations.","zh":"錘骨，是耳內幫助傳送聲音震動的小骨頭。"},{"en":"In humans, tiny ear bones help carry sound from the eardrum toward the inner ear.","zh":"在人類身上，細小耳骨幫助把聲音由耳膜傳向內耳。"},{"en":"If an animal’s hammer bone is unusually large, it may affect how vibrations are detected.","zh":"如果動物的錘骨異常巨大，可能影響牠如何偵測震動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a specific hearing-related bone.","zh":"這個短語指與聽覺相關的特定骨頭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"inner ear","meaning":"內耳","examples":[{"en":"The hammer bone is located in an elephant’s inner ear.","zh":"錘骨位於大象的內耳。"},{"en":"The inner ear is the deep part of the ear involved in hearing and balance.","zh":"內耳，是耳朵深處與聽覺和平衡有關的部分。"},{"en":"Ear infections can sometimes affect the inner ear and make people feel dizzy.","zh":"耳部感染有時會影響內耳，令人感到頭暈。"},{"en":"If vibrations reach the inner ear, they may be processed as sound information.","zh":"如果震動到達內耳，就可能被處理成聲音資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase names a body part important for sensing sound.","zh":"這個短語指出對感應聲音重要的身體部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"proportionally huge","meaning":"按比例來說非常巨大","examples":[{"en":"The hammer bone is proportionally huge for a mammal.","zh":"對哺乳動物而言，錘骨按比例來說非常巨大。"},{"en":"Proportionally huge means very large compared with the size of the body or related part.","zh":"按比例來說非常巨大，指與身體或相關部分大小相比非常大。"},{"en":"A child’s schoolbag may look proportionally huge if it is almost as large as their back.","zh":"如果孩子的書包幾乎和背部一樣大，就顯得按比例非常巨大。"},{"en":"If a bone is proportionally huge, scientists may ask what special function it serves.","zh":"如果骨頭按比例非常巨大，科學家可能會問它有甚麼特殊功能。"},{"en":"The phrase compares size by proportion, not absolute size alone.","zh":"這個短語按比例比較大小，而不只是絕對大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"for a mammal","meaning":"對哺乳動物而言","examples":[{"en":"The hammer bone is unusually large for a mammal.","zh":"對哺乳動物而言，錘骨異常巨大。"},{"en":"For a mammal means when compared with animals that give birth to live young and feed them milk.","zh":"對哺乳動物而言，指與會產下幼兒並哺乳的動物相比。"},{"en":"A bat is small for a mammal, while a whale is enormous for a mammal.","zh":"蝙蝠對哺乳動物而言很小，而鯨魚對哺乳動物而言非常巨大。"},{"en":"If a feature is unusual for a mammal, it may reveal a special adaptation.","zh":"如果某特徵對哺乳動物而言不尋常，就可能揭示特殊適應。"},{"en":"The phrase sets the comparison group.","zh":"這個短語設定比較群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rather normal for","meaning":"對……來說相當正常","examples":[{"en":"The bone is rather normal for animals that use vibrational signals.","zh":"對使用震動訊號的動物來說，這塊骨頭相當正常。"},{"en":"Rather normal for something means fairly usual when compared with that group.","zh":"對某群體來說相當正常，指與該群體相比頗為常見。"},{"en":"Long homework may feel heavy for primary students but rather normal for exam candidates.","zh":"長功課對小學生來說可能很重，但對應試考生來說相當正常。"},{"en":"If a large ear bone is normal among vibration-using animals, elephants may belong to that pattern.","zh":"如果大型耳骨在使用震動的動物中正常，大象可能屬於這種模式。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something unusual in one group may be ordinary in another.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事在一群體中不尋常，但在另一群體中可能普通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"vibrational signals","meaning":"震動訊號","examples":[{"en":"Some animals use vibrational signals to communicate.","zh":"一些動物使用震動訊號來溝通。"},{"en":"Vibrational signals are messages sent through movement or shaking in a surface or material.","zh":"震動訊號，是透過表面或材料中的移動或震動傳送的信息。"},{"en":"A phone on silent mode uses vibrational signals to alert its owner.","zh":"手機在靜音模式下使用震動訊號提醒主人。"},{"en":"If insects send vibrations through plant stems, others can detect the message without hearing sound in the air.","zh":"如果昆蟲透過植物莖發送震動，其他昆蟲不用聽到空氣中的聲音也能偵測信息。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to communication through vibration.","zh":"這個短語指透過震動進行溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it may be a sign that","meaning":"這可能是一個跡象，顯示……","examples":[{"en":"The large hammer bone may be a sign that elephants use seismic sounds.","zh":"巨大的錘骨可能是一個跡象，顯示大象使用地面震動聲。"},{"en":"It may be a sign that means it could be evidence suggesting something is true.","zh":"這可能是一個跡象，顯示某事，指它可能是暗示某事為真的證據。"},{"en":"Frequent yawning may be a sign that a student has not slept enough.","zh":"經常打呵欠可能是一個跡象，顯示學生睡眠不足。"},{"en":"If one body feature fits a theory, it may support but not completely prove it.","zh":"如果一個身體特徵符合某理論，它可能支持但不能完全證明該理論。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces cautious evidence.","zh":"這個短語引入謹慎證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"suggest that","meaning":"顯示；表明","examples":[{"en":"The evidence suggests that elephants can use seismic sounds to communicate.","zh":"證據顯示大象可以使用地面震動聲來溝通。"},{"en":"To suggest that means to indicate or make an idea seem likely.","zh":"顯示或表明，指指出或令某想法看似有可能。"},{"en":"A student’s careful notes suggest that they prepared well for the test.","zh":"學生仔細的筆記顯示他為測驗準備充分。"},{"en":"If several pieces of evidence point in the same direction, they suggest a strong possibility.","zh":"如果幾項證據指向同一方向，它們就顯示一種很大的可能性。"},{"en":"The phrase shows inference, not absolute proof.","zh":"這個短語表示推論，而不是絕對證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"use seismic sounds to communicate","meaning":"使用地面震動聲來溝通","examples":[{"en":"Elephants may use seismic sounds to communicate.","zh":"大象可能使用地面震動聲來溝通。"},{"en":"To use seismic sounds to communicate means to send messages through ground-based sound vibrations.","zh":"使用地面震動聲來溝通，指透過地面傳播的聲音震動發送信息。"},{"en":"An animal might use the ground like a telephone line if vibrations travel far enough.","zh":"如果震動傳得足夠遠，動物可能像使用電話線一樣使用地面。"},{"en":"If elephants communicate this way, their feet and trunks may be as important as their ears.","zh":"如果大象這樣溝通，牠們的腳和象鼻可能與耳朵同樣重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes communication through the earth, not only through the air.","zh":"這個短語描述透過土地而不只是空氣進行的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"aspects of elephant anatomy","meaning":"大象解剖結構的各方面","examples":[{"en":"Other aspects of elephant anatomy support this ability.","zh":"大象解剖結構的其他方面支持這種能力。"},{"en":"Aspects of elephant anatomy are different physical features or body structures of elephants.","zh":"大象解剖結構的各方面，是大象不同的身體特徵或身體結構。"},{"en":"An elephant’s ears, feet, skull, and trunk are all aspects of elephant anatomy.","zh":"大象的耳朵、腳、頭骨和象鼻都是大象解剖結構的方面。"},{"en":"If several body parts point to vibration sensing, the theory becomes more plausible.","zh":"如果幾個身體部位都指向震動感應，該理論就更可信。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to parts of the body used as evidence.","zh":"這個短語指作為證據的身體部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"support the existence of","meaning":"支持……的存在","examples":[{"en":"Elephant anatomy supports the existence of seismic communication.","zh":"大象解剖結構支持地面震動通訊的存在。"},{"en":"To support the existence of something means to provide evidence that it is real.","zh":"支持某事的存在，指提供證據顯示它是真的。"},{"en":"Footprints can support the existence of animals in an area even if no one sees them directly.","zh":"即使沒有人直接看見動物，腳印也能支持某地有動物存在。"},{"en":"If body structures match the ability, they help show the ability may truly exist.","zh":"如果身體結構符合該能力，就有助顯示該能力可能真實存在。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence backing a claim.","zh":"這個短語描述支持某主張的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"this ability","meaning":"這種能力","examples":[{"en":"Several physical features support this ability in elephants.","zh":"幾個身體特徵支持大象的這種能力。"},{"en":"This ability refers to the specific power just mentioned, such as detecting seismic vibrations.","zh":"這種能力，指剛才提到的特定能力，例如偵測地面震動。"},{"en":"A student’s ability to summarise improves when they practise identifying main ideas.","zh":"當學生練習識別主旨，其總結能力會改善。"},{"en":"If many body parts support this ability, researchers may investigate it more seriously.","zh":"如果許多身體部位支持這種能力，研究者可能更認真調查它。"},{"en":"The phrase points back to an earlier described skill.","zh":"這個短語回指先前描述的技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"massive bodies","meaning":"龐大的身體","examples":[{"en":"Elephants’ massive bodies help them produce powerful low-frequency sounds.","zh":"大象龐大的身體幫助牠們發出強大的低頻聲音。"},{"en":"Massive bodies are very large and heavy bodies.","zh":"龐大的身體，是非常巨大而沉重的身體。"},{"en":"A whale’s massive body helps it move through deep water with great force.","zh":"鯨魚龐大的身體幫助牠以巨大力量在深水中移動。"},{"en":"If an animal has a massive body, it may produce sounds or vibrations smaller animals cannot make.","zh":"如果動物身體龐大，就可能發出小型動物不能製造的聲音或震動。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights physical size and power.","zh":"這個短語突出身體大小和力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"enable someone to","meaning":"使某人能夠","examples":[{"en":"Their massive bodies enable them to produce very powerful sounds.","zh":"牠們龐大的身體使牠們能夠發出非常強大的聲音。"},{"en":"To enable someone to do something means to make it possible for them to do it.","zh":"使某人能夠做某事，指令某人可以做到該事。"},{"en":"Clear notes enable students to revise faster before exams.","zh":"清楚筆記使學生能夠在考試前更快溫習。"},{"en":"If a body structure enables a behaviour, it helps explain why the behaviour is possible.","zh":"如果身體結構使某行為成為可能，它有助解釋該行為為何能發生。"},{"en":"The phrase links a condition with an ability.","zh":"這個短語把條件與能力連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"produce low-frequency sounds","meaning":"發出低頻聲音","examples":[{"en":"Elephants can produce low-frequency sounds almost as powerful as a jet.","zh":"大象可以發出幾乎與噴射機一樣強大的低頻聲音。"},{"en":"To produce low-frequency sounds means to create deep sounds with slow vibrations.","zh":"發出低頻聲音，指產生震動較慢的低沉聲音。"},{"en":"A large speaker can produce low-frequency sounds that make the floor shake.","zh":"大型喇叭可以發出令地板震動的低頻聲音。"},{"en":"If elephants produce such sounds, the signals may travel far through air or ground.","zh":"如果大象發出這類聲音，訊號可能透過空氣或地面傳得很遠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making deep sound waves.","zh":"這個短語描述製造低沉聲波。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"almost as powerful as","meaning":"幾乎與……一樣強大","examples":[{"en":"Their low-frequency sounds can be almost as powerful as a jet during takeoff.","zh":"牠們的低頻聲音可以幾乎與起飛時的噴射機一樣強大。"},{"en":"Almost as powerful as means nearly equal in strength or force.","zh":"幾乎與某物一樣強大，指力量或強度接近相等。"},{"en":"A small fan is not almost as powerful as an air conditioner in a large room.","zh":"在大房間中，小風扇並不會幾乎與冷氣機一樣強大。"},{"en":"If an animal sound is almost as powerful as a machine, it can travel a great distance.","zh":"如果動物聲音幾乎與機器一樣強大，就可以傳得很遠。"},{"en":"The phrase compares strength while showing it is not exactly equal.","zh":"這個短語比較力量，同時顯示並非完全相等。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a jet during takeoff","meaning":"起飛時的噴射機","examples":[{"en":"An elephant’s low-frequency sound can be compared to a jet during takeoff.","zh":"大象的低頻聲音可以與起飛時的噴射機相比。"},{"en":"A jet during takeoff is an aeroplane producing huge force and noise as it leaves the ground.","zh":"起飛時的噴射機，是飛機離地時產生巨大力量和噪音的狀態。"},{"en":"People near an airport can hear a jet during takeoff from far away.","zh":"在機場附近的人可以從很遠處聽到起飛時的噴射機。"},{"en":"If an elephant sound is compared to that, the sound must be extremely powerful.","zh":"如果大象聲音被拿來與它相比，該聲音必然極其強大。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a vivid comparison for sound strength.","zh":"這個短語為聲音強度提供生動比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"serve as","meaning":"充當；起……作用","examples":[{"en":"Their bodies serve as ideal frames for receiving ground vibrations.","zh":"牠們的身體充當接收地面震動的理想框架。"},{"en":"To serve as something means to function as it or be used for that purpose.","zh":"充當某物，指發揮該功能或被用於該目的。"},{"en":"A school hall can serve as an exam room during test week.","zh":"學校禮堂可以在考試週充當試場。"},{"en":"If a body serves as a receiver, it helps collect signals from the environment.","zh":"如果身體起接收器作用，就幫助收集環境中的訊號。"},{"en":"The phrase describes function or role.","zh":"這個短語描述功能或角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ideal frames for","meaning":"……的理想框架","examples":[{"en":"Elephants’ bodies are ideal frames for receiving vibrations.","zh":"大象身體是接收震動的理想框架。"},{"en":"Ideal frames for something are structures especially suitable for supporting or receiving it.","zh":"某事的理想框架，是特別適合支撐或接收它的結構。"},{"en":"A sturdy desk is an ideal frame for holding heavy computer equipment.","zh":"堅固書桌是放置沉重電腦設備的理想框架。"},{"en":"If an animal’s body is well shaped for receiving vibrations, signals may pass through it effectively.","zh":"如果動物身體形狀適合接收震動，訊號可能有效穿過它。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights physical suitability.","zh":"這個短語突出身體上的適合性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ground vibrations","meaning":"地面震動","examples":[{"en":"Elephants may receive ground vibrations through their bodies.","zh":"大象可能透過身體接收地面震動。"},{"en":"Ground vibrations are movements or shaking that travel through the earth.","zh":"地面震動，是透過土地傳播的移動或震動。"},{"en":"People may feel ground vibrations when a heavy truck passes by.","zh":"當重型貨車經過，人們可能感到地面震動。"},{"en":"If animals can sense ground vibrations, they may detect distant movement or danger.","zh":"如果動物能感應地面震動，就可能偵測遠方移動或危險。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to shaking carried by the ground.","zh":"這個短語指由地面傳送的震動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"transmit something to","meaning":"將某物傳送至","examples":[{"en":"Their bodies may transmit vibrations to the inner ear.","zh":"牠們的身體可能將震動傳送至內耳。"},{"en":"To transmit something to a place means to send or carry it there.","zh":"將某物傳送至某地，指把它發送或帶到那裡。"},{"en":"A phone tower transmits signals to mobile phones.","zh":"電話發射塔將訊號傳送至手機。"},{"en":"If bones transmit vibrations to the ear, ground movement may become sensory information.","zh":"如果骨骼把震動傳到耳朵，地面移動可能變成感官資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes carrying a signal from one point to another.","zh":"這個短語描述把訊號從一點帶到另一點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"toe bones","meaning":"腳趾骨","examples":[{"en":"The elephant’s toe bones are set on a fatty pad.","zh":"大象的腳趾骨位於脂肪墊之上。"},{"en":"Toe bones are the bones inside the toes or toe-like structures of an animal’s foot.","zh":"腳趾骨，是腳趾或動物腳部類似腳趾結構內的骨頭。"},{"en":"A doctor may check toe bones after someone injures their foot.","zh":"有人腳部受傷後，醫生可能檢查腳趾骨。"},{"en":"If toe bones sit on a special pad, the foot may handle pressure and vibration differently.","zh":"如果腳趾骨位於特殊墊上，腳部可能以不同方式處理壓力和震動。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific part of the foot structure.","zh":"這個短語指出腳部結構中的特定部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be set on","meaning":"位於……之上","examples":[{"en":"The elephant’s toe bones are set on a fatty pad.","zh":"大象的腳趾骨位於脂肪墊之上。"},{"en":"To be set on something means to be positioned or placed on top of it.","zh":"位於某物之上，指被放置或定位在它上面。"},{"en":"A bowl may be set on a table before dinner.","zh":"晚餐前，碗可能被放在桌上。"},{"en":"If toe bones are set on a fatty pad, vibrations from the ground may pass through that structure.","zh":"如果腳趾骨位於脂肪墊之上，地面震動可能穿過該結構。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical placement.","zh":"這個短語描述物理位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a fatty pad","meaning":"脂肪墊","examples":[{"en":"A fatty pad may help focus vibrations from the ground.","zh":"脂肪墊可能幫助集中來自地面的震動。"},{"en":"A fatty pad is a soft layer of fat that cushions or supports part of the body.","zh":"脂肪墊，是緩衝或支撐身體某部分的一層柔軟脂肪。"},{"en":"The bottom of a human foot has soft tissue that helps absorb pressure when walking.","zh":"人類腳底有柔軟組織，幫助走路時吸收壓力。"},{"en":"If a fatty pad sits under the bones, it may help transfer pressure or vibration.","zh":"如果脂肪墊位於骨頭下方，可能幫助傳送壓力或震動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a soft supportive body structure.","zh":"這個短語指柔軟的支撐性身體結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"focus vibrations","meaning":"集中震動","examples":[{"en":"The fatty pad might help focus vibrations into the bone.","zh":"脂肪墊可能幫助把震動集中到骨骼中。"},{"en":"To focus vibrations means to direct or concentrate shaking energy toward a particular place.","zh":"集中震動，指把震動能量導向或集中到特定地方。"},{"en":"A microphone cover can help focus sound toward the recording device.","zh":"麥克風罩可以幫助把聲音集中到錄音裝置。"},{"en":"If a body part focuses vibrations, weak signals may become easier to detect.","zh":"如果身體部位集中震動，微弱訊號可能更容易偵測。"},{"en":"The phrase describes concentrating vibration rather than spreading it randomly.","zh":"這個短語描述集中震動，而不是任其隨機擴散。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"from the ground into the bone","meaning":"從地面進入骨骼","examples":[{"en":"Vibrations may pass from the ground into the bone.","zh":"震動可能從地面進入骨骼。"},{"en":"From the ground into the bone means moving from the earth’s surface into the skeleton.","zh":"從地面進入骨骼，指由地球表面移入骨架。"},{"en":"When someone jumps, force travels from the floor into the bones of the legs.","zh":"當某人跳起，力量會由地板進入腿骨。"},{"en":"If vibrations move into bone, the body may carry them toward sensory organs.","zh":"如果震動進入骨骼，身體可能把它們帶向感官器官。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the path of physical energy.","zh":"這個短語描述物理能量的路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"enormous brain","meaning":"巨大的腦部","examples":[{"en":"The elephant has an enormous brain inside its skull.","zh":"大象頭骨內有巨大的腦部。"},{"en":"An enormous brain is a very large brain compared with many other animals.","zh":"巨大的腦部，是與許多其他動物相比非常大的腦。"},{"en":"Humans do not have the largest brain, but brain structure helps explain intelligence.","zh":"人類並沒有最大的腦，但腦部結構有助解釋智力。"},{"en":"If an animal has an enormous brain, it may process complex social information.","zh":"如果動物有巨大腦部，可能處理複雜社交資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights physical size of the brain.","zh":"這個短語突出腦部的物理大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cranial cavity","meaning":"顱腔","examples":[{"en":"The elephant’s brain sits in the cranial cavity.","zh":"大象腦部位於顱腔內。"},{"en":"The cranial cavity is the space inside the skull that holds the brain.","zh":"顱腔，是頭骨內容納腦部的空間。"},{"en":"Doctors study the cranial cavity when checking serious head injuries.","zh":"醫生檢查嚴重頭部受傷時會研究顱腔。"},{"en":"If a brain sits close to hearing structures, scientists may ask how sound is processed.","zh":"如果腦部靠近聽覺結構，科學家可能會問聲音如何被處理。"},{"en":"The phrase names the skull space containing the brain.","zh":"這個短語指出容納腦部的頭骨空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"behind the eyes","meaning":"在眼睛後方","examples":[{"en":"The brain sits in the cranial cavity behind the eyes.","zh":"腦部位於眼睛後方的顱腔內。"},{"en":"Behind the eyes means located at the back of the eye area.","zh":"在眼睛後方，指位於眼部區域後面。"},{"en":"A headache behind the eyes may feel like pressure deep in the head.","zh":"眼睛後方的頭痛可能感覺像頭部深處有壓力。"},{"en":"If a structure is behind the eyes, it is near the front part of the skull.","zh":"如果某結構在眼睛後方，它就在頭骨前部附近。"},{"en":"The phrase describes position in the head.","zh":"這個短語描述頭部位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in line with","meaning":"與……成一直線","examples":[{"en":"The brain sits in line with the auditory canal.","zh":"腦部與耳道成一直線。"},{"en":"In line with means positioned along the same straight direction or level as something.","zh":"與某物成一直線，指位於與它相同的直線方向或水平上。"},{"en":"Students stand in line with the classroom door before entering.","zh":"學生進入課室前站在與課室門成一直線的位置。"},{"en":"If one structure is in line with another, vibrations may travel between them more directly.","zh":"如果一個結構與另一個結構成一直線，震動可能更直接地在兩者之間傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase describes alignment.","zh":"這個短語描述排列對齊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"auditory canal","meaning":"耳道","examples":[{"en":"The elephant’s brain lies in line with the auditory canal.","zh":"大象腦部與耳道成一直線。"},{"en":"The auditory canal is the passage in the ear through which sound travels.","zh":"耳道，是耳朵中讓聲音通過的通道。"},{"en":"Earwax can block the auditory canal and reduce hearing.","zh":"耳垢可能阻塞耳道並降低聽力。"},{"en":"If vibrations reach the auditory canal, they may affect how sound is detected.","zh":"如果震動到達耳道，可能影響聲音如何被偵測。"},{"en":"The phrase names a hearing-related passage in the ear.","zh":"這個短語指出耳內與聽覺有關的通道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the front of the skull","meaning":"頭骨前部","examples":[{"en":"The front of the skull contains many sinus cavities.","zh":"頭骨前部包含許多鼻竇腔。"},{"en":"The front of the skull is the forward part of the bony structure of the head.","zh":"頭骨前部，是頭部骨骼結構的前方部分。"},{"en":"A doctor may examine the front of the skull after a facial injury.","zh":"面部受傷後，醫生可能檢查頭骨前部。"},{"en":"If the front of the skull has many cavities, it may affect resonance and vibration.","zh":"如果頭骨前部有許多空腔，可能影響共鳴和震動。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a specific region of the head.","zh":"這個短語指出頭部的特定區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be riddled with","meaning":"佈滿……","examples":[{"en":"The front of the skull is riddled with sinus cavities.","zh":"頭骨前部佈滿鼻竇腔。"},{"en":"To be riddled with something means to be full of many holes, spaces, or problems.","zh":"佈滿某物，指充滿許多洞、空間或問題。"},{"en":"An old wall may be riddled with cracks after years of rain.","zh":"舊牆經多年雨水侵蝕後，可能佈滿裂縫。"},{"en":"If a bone is riddled with cavities, vibrations may resonate inside it differently.","zh":"如果骨頭佈滿空腔，震動可能在其中以不同方式共鳴。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests many openings or repeated features throughout something.","zh":"這個短語暗示某物內有許多開口或重複特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sinus cavities","meaning":"鼻竇腔","examples":[{"en":"Sinus cavities may help resonate ground vibrations.","zh":"鼻竇腔可能幫助地面震動產生共鳴。"},{"en":"Sinus cavities are air-filled spaces in the skull.","zh":"鼻竇腔，是頭骨內充滿空氣的空間。"},{"en":"People may feel pressure in their sinus cavities when they have a bad cold.","zh":"人們嚴重感冒時，可能感到鼻竇腔有壓力。"},{"en":"If cavities are filled with air, they may affect how sound vibrates inside the head.","zh":"如果空腔充滿空氣，就可能影響聲音如何在頭內震動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to hollow spaces in the skull.","zh":"這個短語指頭骨中的中空空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"function as","meaning":"發揮……的功能","examples":[{"en":"The sinus cavities might function as resonating chambers.","zh":"鼻竇腔可能發揮共鳴腔的功能。"},{"en":"To function as something means to work or act in that role.","zh":"發揮某功能，指以該角色工作或運作。"},{"en":"A kitchen table can function as a study desk in a small flat.","zh":"在小單位中，廚房桌可以發揮書桌功能。"},{"en":"If a body space functions as a chamber, it may change or strengthen vibrations.","zh":"如果身體空間發揮腔室功能，可能改變或增強震動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical role or use.","zh":"這個短語描述實際角色或用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"resonating chambers","meaning":"共鳴腔","examples":[{"en":"Sinus cavities may act as resonating chambers for ground vibrations.","zh":"鼻竇腔可能充當地面震動的共鳴腔。"},{"en":"Resonating chambers are spaces that help sound or vibration echo, deepen, or strengthen.","zh":"共鳴腔，是幫助聲音或震動回響、加深或增強的空間。"},{"en":"The hollow body of a guitar works like a resonating chamber.","zh":"結他中空的琴身就像共鳴腔。"},{"en":"If an animal has resonating chambers, vibrations may become easier to sense or produce.","zh":"如果動物有共鳴腔，震動可能變得更容易感應或產生。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how hollow spaces can affect sound.","zh":"這個短語解釋中空空間如何影響聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"it remains unclear how","meaning":"目前仍不清楚如何……","examples":[{"en":"It remains unclear how elephants detect such vibrations.","zh":"目前仍不清楚大象如何偵測這些震動。"},{"en":"It remains unclear how means researchers still do not know the exact process.","zh":"目前仍不清楚如何，指研究者仍不知道準確過程。"},{"en":"It remains unclear how some students improve quickly while others need much more time.","zh":"目前仍不清楚為何有些學生進步很快，而其他學生需要更多時間。"},{"en":"If a result is observed but the mechanism is unknown, more research is needed.","zh":"如果結果被觀察到但機制未知，就需要更多研究。"},{"en":"The phrase shows uncertainty about method or explanation.","zh":"這個短語顯示對方法或解釋仍不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"detect such vibrations","meaning":"偵測這些震動","examples":[{"en":"Researchers still do not know exactly how elephants detect such vibrations.","zh":"研究者仍不確切知道大象如何偵測這些震動。"},{"en":"To detect such vibrations means to sense those specific shaking signals.","zh":"偵測這些震動，指感應那些特定震動訊號。"},{"en":"A phone can detect vibrations when it is placed on a moving table.","zh":"手機放在移動的桌子上時，可以偵測震動。"},{"en":"If elephants detect vibrations through their feet, sound may not be limited to ears.","zh":"如果大象透過腳偵測震動，聲音就可能不限於耳朵接收。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to sensing physical movement.","zh":"這個短語指感應物理移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pachyderms","meaning":"厚皮動物；大象","examples":[{"en":"These pachyderms may be listening with their trunks and feet.","zh":"這些厚皮動物可能正在用象鼻和腳聽。"},{"en":"Pachyderms is a formal word often used to refer to large thick-skinned animals, especially elephants.","zh":"Pachyderms 是較正式用詞，常指大型厚皮動物，尤其是大象。"},{"en":"A wildlife documentary may call elephants pachyderms when using a scientific tone.","zh":"野生動物紀錄片使用科學語氣時，可能稱大象為 pachyderms。"},{"en":"If these pachyderms use their feet to listen, their whole bodies may be part of communication.","zh":"如果這些厚皮動物用腳聽，牠們整個身體可能都是溝通的一部分。"},{"en":"The word is formal and usually points to elephants in this context.","zh":"這個詞較正式，在此語境通常指大象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"listen with","meaning":"用……聽","examples":[{"en":"Elephants may listen with their trunks and feet instead of their ears.","zh":"大象可能用象鼻和腳聽，而不是用耳朵。"},{"en":"To listen with a body part means to use that part to detect signals or vibrations.","zh":"用某身體部位聽，指用該部位偵測訊號或震動。"},{"en":"A person can feel music with their hands on a speaker even when they cannot hear it clearly.","zh":"即使聽不清楚，人也可以把手放在喇叭上感受音樂。"},{"en":"If elephants listen with their feet, ground vibrations may carry important messages.","zh":"如果大象用腳聽，地面震動可能帶有重要信息。"},{"en":"The phrase expands listening beyond ordinary hearing.","zh":"這個短語把聆聽擴展到普通聽覺以外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"instead of","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Elephants may detect vibrations with their trunks and feet instead of their ears.","zh":"大象可能用象鼻和腳偵測震動，而不是用耳朵。"},{"en":"Instead of means in place of or rather than something else.","zh":"而不是，指代替另一事物或不選另一事物。"},{"en":"A student may take notes on paper instead of using a laptop.","zh":"學生可能用紙做筆記，而不是用手提電腦。"},{"en":"If elephants use feet instead of ears, researchers must rethink what hearing can mean.","zh":"如果大象用腳而不是耳朵，研究者必須重新思考聽覺可以是甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a clear contrast between two methods.","zh":"這個短語在兩種方法之間建立清楚對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"elephant trunk","meaning":"象鼻","examples":[{"en":"The elephant trunk may be the most versatile appendage in nature.","zh":"象鼻可能是自然界中最多功能的附肢。"},{"en":"An elephant trunk is the long flexible nose of an elephant.","zh":"象鼻，是大象長而靈活的鼻子。"},{"en":"An elephant trunk can pick up food, drink water, smell, touch, and signal to others.","zh":"象鼻可以拿起食物、喝水、嗅聞、觸碰和向其他大象發出訊號。"},{"en":"If the trunk detects vibrations, it may be important for communication as well as feeding.","zh":"如果象鼻能偵測震動，它可能不只對進食重要，也對溝通重要。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to one of the elephant’s most useful body parts.","zh":"這個短語指大象最有用的身體部位之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"versatile appendage","meaning":"多功能附肢","examples":[{"en":"The elephant trunk is an extremely versatile appendage.","zh":"象鼻是一個極其多功能的附肢。"},{"en":"A versatile appendage is a body part that can be used for many different purposes.","zh":"多功能附肢，是可用於許多不同目的的身體部位。"},{"en":"A human hand is versatile because it can write, hold, touch, and build things.","zh":"人手很多功能，因為它可以書寫、握持、觸摸和建造東西。"},{"en":"If an appendage is versatile, it may help an animal survive in many situations.","zh":"如果附肢多功能，就可能幫助動物在許多情況下生存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a flexible and multi-purpose body part.","zh":"這個短語描述靈活而多用途的身體部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in nature","meaning":"在自然界中","examples":[{"en":"The elephant trunk may be the most versatile appendage in nature.","zh":"象鼻可能是自然界中最多功能的附肢。"},{"en":"In nature means among living things and natural systems, not human-made objects.","zh":"在自然界中，指在生物和自然系統之中，而不是人造物品。"},{"en":"The spider web is one of the strongest light structures in nature.","zh":"蜘蛛網是自然界中最強韌的輕型結構之一。"},{"en":"If something is remarkable in nature, it stands out among animals, plants, or ecosystems.","zh":"如果某物在自然界中很突出，它就在動物、植物或生態系統中顯得特別。"},{"en":"The phrase places the comparison in the natural world.","zh":"這個短語把比較放在自然世界中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"utilisation encompasses","meaning":"用途包括","examples":[{"en":"The trunk’s utilisation encompasses drinking, bathing, smelling, feeding, and scratching.","zh":"象鼻的用途包括飲水、洗澡、嗅聞、進食和抓癢。"},{"en":"Utilisation encompasses means the use of something includes several functions or activities.","zh":"用途包括，指某物的使用涵蓋幾種功能或活動。"},{"en":"A school library’s utilisation encompasses reading, studying, meetings, and computer work.","zh":"學校圖書館的用途包括閱讀、溫習、會議和電腦工作。"},{"en":"If one body part has many uses, its importance to survival increases.","zh":"如果一個身體部位有很多用途，它對生存的重要性就增加。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and means its uses include.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是其用途包括。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"contain two types of","meaning":"含有兩種……","examples":[{"en":"The trunk and feet contain two types of nerve endings.","zh":"象鼻和腳含有兩種神經末梢。"},{"en":"To contain two types of something means to have two different categories inside.","zh":"含有兩種某物，指內部有兩個不同類別。"},{"en":"A pencil case may contain two types of pens: black pens and coloured pens.","zh":"筆袋可能含有兩種筆：黑筆和彩色筆。"},{"en":"If a body part contains different nerve endings, it may detect different kinds of signals.","zh":"如果身體部位含有不同神經末梢，就可能偵測不同種類訊號。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies two categories within something.","zh":"這個短語指出某物內部的兩個類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"nerve endings","meaning":"神經末梢","examples":[{"en":"The trunk and feet contain nerve endings that are sensitive to pressure.","zh":"象鼻和腳含有對壓力敏感的神經末梢。"},{"en":"Nerve endings are the ends of nerves that detect feelings such as touch, pain, pressure, or vibration.","zh":"神經末梢，是偵測觸覺、疼痛、壓力或震動等感覺的神經末端。"},{"en":"Fingertips have many nerve endings, so people can feel small textures.","zh":"指尖有許多神經末梢，所以人能感覺細小紋理。"},{"en":"If an animal’s feet have sensitive nerve endings, it may detect ground signals.","zh":"如果動物的腳有敏感神經末梢，就可能偵測地面訊號。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to sensory structures in the body.","zh":"這個短語指身體中的感覺結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be sensitive to","meaning":"對……敏感","examples":[{"en":"Some nerve endings are sensitive to pressure.","zh":"一些神經末梢對壓力敏感。"},{"en":"To be sensitive to something means to react easily to it or detect it well.","zh":"對某物敏感，指容易對它作出反應或能很好地偵測它。"},{"en":"Some people are sensitive to bright light and need sunglasses outdoors.","zh":"有些人對強光敏感，在戶外需要太陽眼鏡。"},{"en":"If nerves are sensitive to vibration, even small ground movements may be noticed.","zh":"如果神經對震動敏感，即使細小地面移動也可能被注意到。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong response to a stimulus.","zh":"這個短語描述對刺激有強烈反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pressure","meaning":"壓力","examples":[{"en":"The nerve endings in the trunk and feet are sensitive to pressure.","zh":"象鼻和腳中的神經末梢對壓力敏感。"},{"en":"Pressure is force applied to a surface or part of the body.","zh":"壓力，是施加在表面或身體部位上的力量。"},{"en":"A tight shoe puts pressure on the toes and may cause pain.","zh":"太緊的鞋會對腳趾施加壓力，可能造成疼痛。"},{"en":"If pressure changes under an elephant’s feet, nerves may send signals to the brain.","zh":"如果大象腳下壓力改變，神經可能向腦部傳送訊號。"},{"en":"The word can refer to physical force, not only emotional stress.","zh":"這個詞可以指物理力量，而不只是情緒壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"infrasonic vibrations","meaning":"次聲波震動","examples":[{"en":"One type of nerve ending detects infrasonic vibrations.","zh":"一種神經末梢偵測次聲波震動。"},{"en":"Infrasonic vibrations are very low-frequency vibrations below normal human hearing range.","zh":"次聲波震動，是低於人類正常聽覺範圍的極低頻震動。"},{"en":"Special instruments may detect infrasonic vibrations from distant storms or large animals.","zh":"特殊儀器可能偵測到來自遠方風暴或大型動物的次聲波震動。"},{"en":"If elephants detect infrasonic vibrations, they may sense signals humans cannot hear.","zh":"如果大象偵測次聲波震動，牠們可能感應到人類聽不到的訊號。"},{"en":"The phrase combines low-frequency sound with physical vibration.","zh":"這個短語結合低頻聲音與物理震動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"respond to","meaning":"對……作出反應","examples":[{"en":"The other type of nerve ending responds to higher-frequency vibrations.","zh":"另一種神經末梢對較高頻率的震動作出反應。"},{"en":"To respond to something means to react to it.","zh":"對某事作出反應，指因它而有反應。"},{"en":"Students respond to feedback by correcting mistakes in their next essay.","zh":"學生透過在下一篇作文中改正錯誤來回應回饋。"},{"en":"If nerves respond to higher-frequency vibrations, they send information when those vibrations appear.","zh":"如果神經對較高頻率震動有反應，當那些震動出現時就會傳送資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reaction to a signal or event.","zh":"這個短語描述對訊號或事件的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"higher-frequency vibrations","meaning":"較高頻率的震動","examples":[{"en":"Some nerve endings respond to higher-frequency vibrations.","zh":"一些神經末梢對較高頻率的震動作出反應。"},{"en":"Higher-frequency vibrations are faster vibrations compared with lower-frequency ones.","zh":"較高頻率的震動，是與低頻震動相比更快的震動。"},{"en":"A buzzing phone may create higher-frequency vibrations than a slow, heavy machine.","zh":"嗡嗡作響的手機可能比緩慢沉重的機器產生較高頻率震動。"},{"en":"If different nerves respond to different frequencies, the body can detect more types of signals.","zh":"如果不同神經對不同頻率作反應，身體就能偵測更多種類訊號。"},{"en":"The phrase compares vibration speed.","zh":"這個短語比較震動速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as someone sees it","meaning":"在某人看來","examples":[{"en":"As O’Connell-Rodwell sees it, the research has an unpredictable future.","zh":"在 O’Connell-Rodwell 看來，這項研究有難以預測的未來。"},{"en":"As someone sees it means from that person’s point of view.","zh":"在某人看來，指從該人的角度而言。"},{"en":"As the teacher sees it, regular practice matters more than last-minute study.","zh":"在老師看來，定期練習比臨急抱佛腳更重要。"},{"en":"If a researcher says “as I see it,” they are giving an interpretation rather than a fixed fact.","zh":"如果研究者說「在我看來」，他是在提出解讀，而不是固定事實。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a personal professional view.","zh":"這個短語引入個人專業看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"boundless and unpredictable","meaning":"無邊無際而難以預測的","examples":[{"en":"The future of this research is boundless and unpredictable.","zh":"這項研究的未來無邊無際而難以預測。"},{"en":"Boundless and unpredictable means having no clear limits and being difficult to foresee.","zh":"無邊無際而難以預測，指沒有明確界限，而且難以預見。"},{"en":"A new technology can feel boundless and unpredictable when people do not know how it will be used.","zh":"當人們不知道新科技會如何被使用，它可能感覺無邊無際而難以預測。"},{"en":"If research connects several sciences, it may lead to many unexpected questions.","zh":"如果研究連接幾門科學，就可能引出許多意想不到的問題。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests great possibility and uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語暗示巨大可能性和不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at the interface of","meaning":"位於……的交界","examples":[{"en":"Her work is at the interface of geophysics, neurophysiology, and ecology.","zh":"她的工作位於地球物理學、神經生理學和生態學的交界。"},{"en":"At the interface of fields means located where different areas of study meet and interact.","zh":"位於不同領域的交界，指處於不同研究範圍相遇和互動之處。"},{"en":"Public health is at the interface of medicine, education, and government policy.","zh":"公共健康位於醫學、教育和政府政策的交界。"},{"en":"If research sits at such an interface, it may need knowledge from several disciplines.","zh":"如果研究處於這種交界，就可能需要幾個學科的知識。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights cross-disciplinary work.","zh":"這個短語突出跨學科工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"geophysics","meaning":"地球物理學","examples":[{"en":"Her research is connected to geophysics.","zh":"她的研究與地球物理學有關。"},{"en":"Geophysics is the study of the Earth using physics, including waves, vibrations, and underground structures.","zh":"地球物理學，是用物理學研究地球，包括波、震動和地下結構。"},{"en":"Geophysics can help scientists study earthquakes and ground movement.","zh":"地球物理學可以幫助科學家研究地震和地面移動。"},{"en":"If elephant signals travel through the ground, geophysics becomes relevant to animal communication.","zh":"如果大象訊號透過地面傳播，地球物理學就與動物溝通有關。"},{"en":"The word links Earth processes with physical science.","zh":"這個詞把地球過程與物理科學連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"neurophysiology","meaning":"神經生理學","examples":[{"en":"Her work also involves neurophysiology.","zh":"她的工作也涉及神經生理學。"},{"en":"Neurophysiology is the study of how nerves and the nervous system work.","zh":"神經生理學，是研究神經和神經系統如何運作的學科。"},{"en":"Doctors use neurophysiology to understand how the brain responds to pain or sound.","zh":"醫生使用神經生理學來理解腦部如何回應疼痛或聲音。"},{"en":"If elephant nerves detect vibration, neurophysiology helps explain the sensing process.","zh":"如果大象神經偵測震動，神經生理學有助解釋感應過程。"},{"en":"The word connects body signals with nerve function.","zh":"這個詞把身體訊號與神經功能連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ecology","meaning":"生態學","examples":[{"en":"Elephant communication research is also connected to ecology.","zh":"大象溝通研究也與生態學有關。"},{"en":"Ecology is the study of how living things interact with one another and their environment.","zh":"生態學，是研究生物如何彼此互動以及與環境互動的學科。"},{"en":"Ecology can explain how animals find food, avoid danger, and live in groups.","zh":"生態學可以解釋動物如何尋找食物、避開危險和群居。"},{"en":"If communication affects survival and movement, it becomes part of ecological study.","zh":"如果溝通影響生存和移動，它就成為生態研究的一部分。"},{"en":"The word links animal behaviour with the environment.","zh":"這個詞把動物行為與環境連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"raise questions","meaning":"提出問題","examples":[{"en":"The research raises questions that were never considered before.","zh":"這項研究提出以前從未考慮過的問題。"},{"en":"To raise questions means to create issues that need to be asked, discussed, or investigated.","zh":"提出問題，指造成需要被詢問、討論或調查的議題。"},{"en":"A sudden fall in exam results may raise questions about teaching methods.","zh":"考試成績突然下降，可能對教學方法提出問題。"},{"en":"If new research raises questions, scientists may design new experiments.","zh":"如果新研究提出問題，科學家可能設計新實驗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making people think again.","zh":"這個短語描述令人重新思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"never been considered before","meaning":"以前從未被考慮過","examples":[{"en":"Some questions about elephant communication had never been considered before.","zh":"一些關於大象溝通的問題以前從未被考慮過。"},{"en":"Never been considered before means no one had seriously thought about it earlier.","zh":"以前從未被考慮過，指先前沒有人認真想過。"},{"en":"A school may discover a problem that had never been considered before because no student had reported it.","zh":"學校可能發現以前從未考慮過的問題，因為沒有學生曾報告它。"},{"en":"If a question is new, researchers may need new tools and methods to answer it.","zh":"如果問題是新的，研究者可能需要新工具和方法來回答。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights originality or novelty.","zh":"這個短語突出原創性或新穎性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have long known that","meaning":"早已知道","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have long known that seismic communication is widespread among small animals.","zh":"科學家早已知道地面震動通訊在小型動物中很普遍。"},{"en":"To have long known that means to have understood something for a long time.","zh":"早已知道，指很久以來已理解某事。"},{"en":"Teachers have long known that students learn better with clear examples.","zh":"老師早已知道學生透過清楚例子學得更好。"},{"en":"If scientists have long known a fact, the new discovery may extend it to a new case.","zh":"如果科學家早已知道某事實，新發現可能把它擴展到新個案。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts old knowledge with a new development.","zh":"這個短語把舊知識與新發展作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"seismic communication","meaning":"地面震動通訊","examples":[{"en":"Seismic communication is common among many small animals.","zh":"地面震動通訊在許多小型動物中很常見。"},{"en":"Seismic communication is communication through ground vibrations or vibrations in a surface.","zh":"地面震動通訊，是透過地面震動或表面震動進行的溝通。"},{"en":"Some insects use plant stems for seismic communication.","zh":"一些昆蟲使用植物莖進行地面震動通訊。"},{"en":"If animals cannot see or hear each other clearly, vibrations may carry messages instead.","zh":"如果動物不能清楚看見或聽見彼此，震動可能代替聲音傳遞信息。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to communication through shaking, not spoken language.","zh":"這個短語指透過震動溝通，而不是語言說話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be widespread among","meaning":"在……之中很普遍","examples":[{"en":"Seismic communication is widespread among small animals.","zh":"地面震動通訊在小型動物之中很普遍。"},{"en":"To be widespread among a group means to be common or found in many members of that group.","zh":"在某群體中很普遍，指在該群體許多成員中常見或存在。"},{"en":"Smartphone use is widespread among teenagers in many cities.","zh":"在許多城市中，智能手機使用在青少年之中很普遍。"},{"en":"If a behaviour is widespread among animals, it may serve an important survival function.","zh":"如果某行為在動物中很普遍，它可能有重要生存功能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad occurrence within a group.","zh":"這個短語描述在群體內廣泛出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"small animals","meaning":"小型動物","examples":[{"en":"Many small animals use seismic communication.","zh":"許多小型動物使用地面震動通訊。"},{"en":"Small animals are animals with relatively small bodies compared with larger species.","zh":"小型動物，是與較大型物種相比身體較小的動物。"},{"en":"Frogs, insects, mice, and small birds can all be small animals.","zh":"青蛙、昆蟲、老鼠和小鳥都可以是小型動物。"},{"en":"If small animals use vibrations, the method may work even without loud sound.","zh":"如果小型動物使用震動，這種方法即使沒有大聲音也可能有效。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts smaller species with large animals like elephants.","zh":"這個短語把較小物種與大象等大型動物作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"vertebrate species","meaning":"脊椎動物物種","examples":[{"en":"Some vertebrate species also use seismic communication.","zh":"一些脊椎動物物種也使用地面震動通訊。"},{"en":"Vertebrate species are animal species with backbones.","zh":"脊椎動物物種，是有脊骨的動物物種。"},{"en":"Fish, birds, reptiles, mammals, and frogs are vertebrate species.","zh":"魚、鳥、爬行動物、哺乳動物和青蛙都是脊椎動物物種。"},{"en":"If seismic communication appears in vertebrates, it is not limited to insects.","zh":"如果地面震動通訊出現在脊椎動物中，它就不限於昆蟲。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a biological group defined by the spine.","zh":"這個短語指由脊椎界定的生物群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"white-lipped frogs","meaning":"白唇蛙","examples":[{"en":"White-lipped frogs are one example of animals that use seismic communication.","zh":"白唇蛙是使用地面震動通訊的動物例子之一。"},{"en":"White-lipped frogs are a type of frog known here as a vertebrate using vibration signals.","zh":"白唇蛙是一種青蛙，在此被視為使用震動訊號的脊椎動物。"},{"en":"A biology textbook may list white-lipped frogs when explaining unusual animal communication.","zh":"生物教科書解釋不尋常動物溝通時，可能列出白唇蛙。"},{"en":"If frogs use vibrations, communication can happen through surfaces as well as air.","zh":"如果青蛙使用震動，溝通就可以透過表面以及空氣發生。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a concrete animal example.","zh":"這個短語給出具體動物例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"blind mole rats","meaning":"盲鼴鼠","examples":[{"en":"Blind mole rats are among the animals known to use seismic communication.","zh":"盲鼴鼠是已知使用地面震動通訊的動物之一。"},{"en":"Blind mole rats are underground rodents with poor eyesight that can use vibrations.","zh":"盲鼴鼠是視力弱、生活於地下並能使用震動的囓齒動物。"},{"en":"Animals living underground may depend on vibrations because light and air sounds are limited.","zh":"地下生活的動物可能依賴震動，因為光線和空氣聲音有限。"},{"en":"If blind mole rats communicate through ground signals, their environment shapes their communication.","zh":"如果盲鼴鼠透過地面訊號溝通，其環境就塑造了溝通方式。"},{"en":"The phrase gives another animal example linked to vibration.","zh":"這個短語給出另一個與震動相關的動物例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"kangaroo rats","meaning":"更格盧鼠；袋鼠鼠","examples":[{"en":"Kangaroo rats are examples of vertebrates that use seismic communication.","zh":"袋鼠鼠是使用地面震動通訊的脊椎動物例子。"},{"en":"Kangaroo rats are small rodents known for powerful hind legs and jumping movement.","zh":"袋鼠鼠是以強壯後腿和跳躍動作聞名的小型囓齒動物。"},{"en":"A desert animal like a kangaroo rat may use foot-drumming signals in its environment.","zh":"像袋鼠鼠這樣的沙漠動物，可能在環境中使用踏腳訊號。"},{"en":"If kangaroo rats use ground signals, movement can become communication.","zh":"如果袋鼠鼠使用地面訊號，動作就可以變成溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase names a small vertebrate used as an example.","zh":"這個短語指出用作例子的小型脊椎動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"golden moles","meaning":"金鼴","examples":[{"en":"Golden moles are listed as animals that use seismic communication.","zh":"金鼴被列為使用地面震動通訊的動物。"},{"en":"Golden moles are small burrowing mammals that live mostly underground.","zh":"金鼴是大多生活於地下的小型掘洞哺乳動物。"},{"en":"Underground animals may rely on vibrations to sense movement nearby.","zh":"地下動物可能依靠震動感應附近移動。"},{"en":"If golden moles detect ground signals, seismic communication may help them survive in darkness.","zh":"如果金鼴偵測地面訊號，地面震動通訊可能幫助牠們在黑暗中生存。"},{"en":"The phrase names a small mammal example.","zh":"這個短語指出一個小型哺乳動物例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"nevertheless","meaning":"然而","examples":[{"en":"Nevertheless, O’Connell-Rodwell was the first to make a further argument.","zh":"然而，O’Connell-Rodwell 是首位提出進一步論點的人。"},{"en":"Nevertheless means however or despite what was just said.","zh":"然而，指不過、儘管剛才所說仍然如此。"},{"en":"The homework was difficult; nevertheless, many students finished it on time.","zh":"功課很難；然而，許多學生準時完成。"},{"en":"If seismic communication was known in small animals, nevertheless it was new to argue this for elephants.","zh":"即使地面震動通訊在小型動物中已知，然而把它應用到大象仍是新論點。"},{"en":"The word introduces a contrast or surprising continuation.","zh":"這個詞引入對比或令人意外的延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be the first to argue that","meaning":"是首位提出……的人","examples":[{"en":"O’Connell-Rodwell was the first to argue that a giant land animal could use seismic signals.","zh":"O’Connell-Rodwell 是首位提出大型陸地動物可以使用地面震動訊號的人。"},{"en":"To be the first to argue that means to be the earliest person to propose that idea with reasons.","zh":"是首位提出某事的人，指最早以理由提出該想法的人。"},{"en":"A student may be the first to argue that the class should reduce paper use.","zh":"學生可能是首位提出班級應減少用紙的人。"},{"en":"If no one had applied the idea to large animals before, her argument was original.","zh":"如果以前沒有人把該想法應用於大型動物，她的論點就是原創的。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights priority in making a claim.","zh":"這個短語突出提出主張的先後地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"giant land animal","meaning":"大型陸地動物","examples":[{"en":"Elephants are giant land animals that may send and receive seismic signals.","zh":"大象是可能發送和接收地面震動訊號的大型陸地動物。"},{"en":"A giant land animal is a very large animal that lives mainly on land.","zh":"大型陸地動物，是主要生活在陸地上的非常大型動物。"},{"en":"A giraffe is a giant land animal, while a whale is not because it lives in water.","zh":"長頸鹿是大型陸地動物，而鯨魚不是，因為牠生活在水中。"},{"en":"If a giant land animal uses ground signals, its weight may help produce strong vibrations.","zh":"如果大型陸地動物使用地面訊號，其重量可能幫助產生強烈震動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes size and habitat together.","zh":"這個短語同時描述大小和棲息地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"send and receive","meaning":"發送和接收","examples":[{"en":"A giant land animal could also send and receive seismic signals.","zh":"大型陸地動物也可以發送和接收地面震動訊號。"},{"en":"To send and receive signals means to transmit messages and detect messages from others.","zh":"發送和接收訊號，指傳送信息並偵測來自他人的信息。"},{"en":"Phones send and receive messages when people text one another.","zh":"當人們互相發短訊時，手機會發送和接收信息。"},{"en":"If elephants both send and receive signals, communication can be two-way.","zh":"如果大象既發送又接收訊號，溝通就可以是雙向的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both sides of communication.","zh":"這個短語描述溝通的兩面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"seismic signals","meaning":"地面震動訊號","examples":[{"en":"Elephants may send and receive seismic signals.","zh":"大象可能發送和接收地面震動訊號。"},{"en":"Seismic signals are messages carried by vibrations through the ground.","zh":"地面震動訊號，是由地面震動傳遞的信息。"},{"en":"Sensors can record seismic signals from earthquakes.","zh":"感應器可以記錄來自地震的地面震動訊號。"},{"en":"If animals use seismic signals, the ground becomes part of their communication system.","zh":"如果動物使用地面震動訊號，地面就成為其溝通系統的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to vibration-based messages.","zh":"這個短語指以震動為基礎的信息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"place something on","meaning":"將某物放在……上","examples":[{"en":"She used to place a male planthopper on a stem.","zh":"她以前會將雄性飛蝨放在莖上。"},{"en":"To place something on a surface means to put it there carefully.","zh":"將某物放在某表面上，指小心把它放到那裡。"},{"en":"A teacher may place a model on the desk before explaining an experiment.","zh":"老師可能在講解實驗前把模型放在桌上。"},{"en":"If a researcher places an insect on a stem, they can observe how it reacts to vibrations.","zh":"如果研究者把昆蟲放在莖上，就可以觀察牠如何回應震動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful positioning.","zh":"這個短語描述小心放置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"male planthopper","meaning":"雄性飛蝨","examples":[{"en":"She placed a male planthopper on a stem during the experiment.","zh":"她在實驗中把一隻雄性飛蝨放在莖上。"},{"en":"A male planthopper is a male insect from a group that often lives on plants.","zh":"雄性飛蝨，是屬於常生活在植物上的昆蟲群體中的雄性個體。"},{"en":"A biology student may observe a planthopper moving along a plant stem.","zh":"生物學生可能觀察飛蝨沿植物莖移動。"},{"en":"If a male planthopper responds to a female signal, researchers can study vibration-based communication.","zh":"如果雄性飛蝨回應雌性訊號，研究者就能研究以震動為基礎的溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase names the insect used in the experiment.","zh":"這個短語指出實驗中使用的昆蟲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on a stem","meaning":"在莖上","examples":[{"en":"The male planthopper was placed on a stem.","zh":"雄性飛蝨被放在莖上。"},{"en":"On a stem means on the thin main support of a plant, where leaves or flowers grow.","zh":"在莖上，指在植物細長的主要支撐部分上，葉或花從那裡生長。"},{"en":"A caterpillar may crawl on a stem before reaching a leaf.","zh":"毛蟲可能在到達葉子前沿着莖爬行。"},{"en":"If an insect is on a stem, vibrations can travel through the plant to its legs.","zh":"如果昆蟲在莖上，震動可以透過植物傳到牠的腳。"},{"en":"The phrase describes location on part of a plant.","zh":"這個短語描述在植物某部分上的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"replay the calling sound","meaning":"重播叫聲","examples":[{"en":"She replayed the calling sound of a female planthopper.","zh":"她重播雌性飛蝨的叫聲。"},{"en":"To replay the calling sound means to play a recorded signal again.","zh":"重播叫聲，指再次播放錄下來的訊號。"},{"en":"A teacher may replay a listening track so students can hear the answer more clearly.","zh":"老師可能重播聆聽音軌，讓學生更清楚聽到答案。"},{"en":"If researchers replay an animal call, they can test how another animal responds.","zh":"如果研究者重播動物叫聲，就可以測試另一隻動物如何回應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using recorded sound in an experiment.","zh":"這個短語描述在實驗中使用錄音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"exhibit behaviour","meaning":"表現出行為","examples":[{"en":"The male planthopper exhibited behaviour similar to that of elephants.","zh":"雄性飛蝨表現出與大象相似的行為。"},{"en":"To exhibit behaviour means to show or display a certain action or response.","zh":"表現出行為，指展示某種行動或反應。"},{"en":"A student may exhibit nervous behaviour by tapping a pen before an exam.","zh":"學生考試前敲筆，可能表現出緊張行為。"},{"en":"If two animals exhibit similar behaviour, scientists may compare their communication systems.","zh":"如果兩種動物表現出相似行為，科學家可能比較其溝通系統。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and means show behaviour.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是顯示行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the same kind of behaviour","meaning":"同一類行為","examples":[{"en":"The insect showed the same kind of behaviour that happens in elephants.","zh":"該昆蟲表現出大象也會出現的同一類行為。"},{"en":"The same kind of behaviour means a similar pattern of action or response.","zh":"同一類行為，指相似的行動或反應模式。"},{"en":"Two students may show the same kind of behaviour when both avoid speaking in class because they are shy.","zh":"如果兩名學生都因害羞而避免在課堂發言，就表現出同一類行為。"},{"en":"If insects and elephants react similarly, a shared communication principle may exist.","zh":"如果昆蟲和大象反應相似，可能存在共同溝通原理。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights similarity in action.","zh":"這個短語突出行動上的相似性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"freeze","meaning":"停住不動","examples":[{"en":"The male planthopper would freeze after hearing the sound.","zh":"雄性飛蝨聽到聲音後會停住不動。"},{"en":"To freeze means to stop moving suddenly, often because of fear, attention, or response to a signal.","zh":"停住不動，指突然停止移動，通常因害怕、注意或回應訊號。"},{"en":"A student may freeze when the teacher unexpectedly asks a difficult question.","zh":"當老師突然問難題時，學生可能停住不動。"},{"en":"If an animal freezes after a signal, it may be listening or preparing to react.","zh":"如果動物在訊號後停住不動，可能正在聆聽或準備反應。"},{"en":"The word describes sudden stillness, not only becoming ice.","zh":"這個詞描述突然靜止，而不只是變成冰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"press down on","meaning":"向下壓住","examples":[{"en":"The insect would press down on its legs.","zh":"該昆蟲會向下壓住自己的腿。"},{"en":"To press down on something means to push downward against it.","zh":"向下壓住某物，指向下施力推壓它。"},{"en":"A nurse may press down on a wound to stop bleeding.","zh":"護士可能向下壓住傷口以止血。"},{"en":"If an insect presses down on its legs, it may improve contact with the surface.","zh":"如果昆蟲向下壓住腿部，可能改善與表面的接觸。"},{"en":"The phrase describes applying downward force.","zh":"這個短語描述施加向下力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"move forward","meaning":"向前移動","examples":[{"en":"The insect would move forward a little.","zh":"該昆蟲會向前移動一點。"},{"en":"To move forward means to go ahead or progress in a forward direction.","zh":"向前移動，指朝前方前進或推進。"},{"en":"A student may move forward one seat when the teacher changes the classroom arrangement.","zh":"當老師改變課室座位安排，學生可能向前移動一個座位。"},{"en":"If an animal moves forward after a signal, it may be approaching the source.","zh":"如果動物在訊號後向前移動，可能正在接近訊號來源。"},{"en":"The phrase can mean physical movement or progress.","zh":"這個短語可以指身體移動或進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stay still","meaning":"保持不動","examples":[{"en":"The insect would stay still again.","zh":"該昆蟲會再次保持不動。"},{"en":"To stay still means to remain without moving.","zh":"保持不動，指繼續不移動。"},{"en":"A child must stay still while a doctor checks their ear.","zh":"醫生檢查耳朵時，孩子必須保持不動。"},{"en":"If an animal stays still, it may be listening carefully or avoiding danger.","zh":"如果動物保持不動，可能正在仔細聆聽或避免危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continued lack of movement.","zh":"這個短語描述持續沒有移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"find it fascinating","meaning":"覺得……很吸引","examples":[{"en":"O’Connell-Rodwell found the behaviour fascinating.","zh":"O’Connell-Rodwell 覺得這種行為很吸引。"},{"en":"To find something fascinating means to think it is extremely interesting.","zh":"覺得某事很吸引，指認為它非常有趣。"},{"en":"A student may find space science fascinating after watching a documentary about Mars.","zh":"學生觀看關於火星的紀錄片後，可能覺得太空科學很吸引。"},{"en":"If a behaviour suggests a hidden communication system, researchers may become deeply interested.","zh":"如果某行為暗示隱藏溝通系統，研究者可能深感興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses strong curiosity and interest.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈好奇和興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get someone thinking that","meaning":"令某人開始思考","examples":[{"en":"The observation got her thinking that auditory communication might not be the only method.","zh":"這項觀察令她開始思考聽覺溝通可能不是唯一方法。"},{"en":"To get someone thinking that means to make someone start considering an idea.","zh":"令某人開始思考某事，指使某人開始考慮一個想法。"},{"en":"A low mark may get a student thinking that their study method needs changing.","zh":"低分可能令學生開始思考自己的學習方法需要改變。"},{"en":"If one experiment raises a new possibility, it can lead a researcher toward a new theory.","zh":"如果一個實驗提出新可能性，就可能帶領研究者走向新理論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes triggering a thought process.","zh":"這個短語描述觸發思考過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"auditory communication","meaning":"聽覺溝通","examples":[{"en":"Auditory communication may not be the only thing happening.","zh":"聽覺溝通可能不是唯一正在發生的事情。"},{"en":"Auditory communication is communication through sound that is heard.","zh":"聽覺溝通，是透過可被聽見的聲音進行的溝通。"},{"en":"Talking, singing, and warning calls are forms of auditory communication.","zh":"說話、唱歌和警告叫聲都是聽覺溝通形式。"},{"en":"If animals also use vibrations, auditory communication is only part of the full system.","zh":"如果動物也使用震動，聽覺溝通就只是完整系統的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on hearing-based messages.","zh":"這個短語強調以聽覺為基礎的信息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the only thing going on","meaning":"唯一正在發生的事","examples":[{"en":"Auditory communication is not the only thing going on in animal communication.","zh":"在動物溝通中，聽覺溝通不是唯一正在發生的事。"},{"en":"The only thing going on means the only process or activity happening.","zh":"唯一正在發生的事，指唯一的過程或活動。"},{"en":"In a classroom, speaking is not the only thing going on; students may also be thinking silently.","zh":"在課室中，說話不是唯一正在發生的事；學生也可能正在安靜思考。"},{"en":"If researchers look beyond sound, they may find touch, smell, or vibration signals too.","zh":"如果研究者超越聲音來看，也可能發現觸覺、氣味或震動訊號。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that a situation may include more than it first appears.","zh":"這個短語提醒情況可能比表面更多元。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"confirm that","meaning":"證實","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have confirmed that long-distance communication is essential for elephants.","zh":"科學家已證實遠距離溝通對大象至關重要。"},{"en":"To confirm that means to prove or show more clearly that something is true.","zh":"證實，指證明或更清楚顯示某事為真。"},{"en":"A teacher may confirm that an exam date has changed by sending a written notice.","zh":"老師可能透過發出書面通知證實考試日期已改。"},{"en":"If repeated studies confirm a claim, confidence in the claim increases.","zh":"如果重複研究證實某主張，人們對該主張的信心會增加。"},{"en":"The phrase shows stronger support than a guess.","zh":"這個短語顯示比猜測更強的支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"capacity to communicate","meaning":"溝通能力","examples":[{"en":"An elephant’s capacity to communicate over long distances is essential for survival.","zh":"大象遠距離溝通的能力對生存至關重要。"},{"en":"Capacity to communicate means ability to send and receive information.","zh":"溝通能力，指傳送和接收資訊的能力。"},{"en":"A school team’s capacity to communicate improves when members share updates clearly.","zh":"當成員清楚分享進度，學校團隊的溝通能力會改善。"},{"en":"If elephants need to coordinate across large areas, communication capacity affects survival.","zh":"如果大象需要在廣大地區協調，溝通能力就影響生存。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to communication ability.","zh":"這個短語指溝通方面的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"essential for survival","meaning":"對生存至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Long-distance communication is essential for elephant survival.","zh":"遠距離溝通對大象生存至關重要。"},{"en":"Essential for survival means necessary for staying alive or continuing successfully.","zh":"對生存至關重要，指對維持生命或成功延續是必要的。"},{"en":"Clean water is essential for survival in every community.","zh":"清潔食水對每個社區的生存至關重要。"},{"en":"If elephants cannot warn others about danger or find mates, their survival becomes harder.","zh":"如果大象不能警告其他同伴有危險或尋找配偶，牠們的生存就更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something necessary, not merely useful.","zh":"這個短語描述必要之物，而不只是有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"places like","meaning":"像……這樣的地方","examples":[{"en":"This ability is especially important in places like Etosha.","zh":"這種能力在像 Etosha 這樣的地方尤其重要。"},{"en":"Places like a named location means locations similar to that example.","zh":"像某地這樣的地方，指與該例子相似的地點。"},{"en":"In places like busy train stations, clear signs are very important.","zh":"在像繁忙火車站這樣的地方，清楚標誌非常重要。"},{"en":"If an environment is large and open, long-distance communication becomes more useful.","zh":"如果環境巨大而開闊，遠距離溝通就更有用。"},{"en":"The phrase uses one place as an example of a wider type.","zh":"這個短語用一個地方作更廣泛類型的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"savanna elephants","meaning":"稀樹草原象","examples":[{"en":"More than 2,400 savanna elephants live in the area.","zh":"超過2,400頭稀樹草原象生活在該地區。"},{"en":"Savanna elephants are African elephants that live mainly in open grassland and woodland habitats.","zh":"稀樹草原象，是主要生活在開闊草原和林地棲息地的非洲象。"},{"en":"Savanna elephants may travel long distances to find water and food.","zh":"稀樹草原象可能長距離移動以尋找水和食物。"},{"en":"If many savanna elephants spread across a wide area, long-distance communication becomes important.","zh":"如果許多稀樹草原象分散在廣大地區，遠距離溝通就變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a type of African elephant.","zh":"這個短語指出一種非洲象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"range over","meaning":"在……範圍內活動","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of elephants range over an area larger than New Jersey.","zh":"數千頭大象在比新澤西州更大的地區範圍內活動。"},{"en":"To range over an area means to move around or live across that area.","zh":"在某範圍內活動，指在該地區內移動或生活。"},{"en":"Delivery drivers may range over several districts in one day.","zh":"送貨司機可能一天內在幾個地區範圍內活動。"},{"en":"If animals range over a huge area, finding others can become difficult.","zh":"如果動物在巨大地區活動，尋找其他同伴可能變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement across a wide space.","zh":"這個短語描述在廣大空間中移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"an area larger than","meaning":"比……更大的地區","examples":[{"en":"The elephants range over an area larger than New Jersey.","zh":"大象在比新澤西州更大的地區活動。"},{"en":"An area larger than something means a place whose size is greater than the comparison given.","zh":"比某物更大的地區，指面積大於所給比較對象的地方。"},{"en":"A park larger than a school campus can take hours to walk through.","zh":"比學校校園更大的公園，可能要走幾小時才走完。"},{"en":"If animals spread across an area larger than a state, communication must travel far.","zh":"如果動物分布在比一個州更大的地區，溝通就必須傳得很遠。"},{"en":"The phrase helps readers imagine scale by comparison.","zh":"這個短語透過比較幫助讀者想像規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"find a mate","meaning":"尋找配偶","examples":[{"en":"It can be difficult for an elephant to find a mate in a vast wilderness.","zh":"大象在廣闊荒野中尋找配偶可能很困難。"},{"en":"To find a mate means to locate a suitable partner for reproduction.","zh":"尋找配偶，指找到適合繁殖的伴侶。"},{"en":"Some birds sing loudly in spring to find a mate.","zh":"一些鳥類春天高聲鳴叫來尋找配偶。"},{"en":"If animals are spread far apart, finding a mate becomes more difficult.","zh":"如果動物分散得很遠，尋找配偶就變得更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase is about reproduction and pairing.","zh":"這個短語關於繁殖和配對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"vast wilderness","meaning":"廣闊荒野","examples":[{"en":"It is difficult to find a mate in such a vast wilderness.","zh":"在如此廣闊荒野中尋找配偶很困難。"},{"en":"A vast wilderness is a very large natural area with few people or buildings.","zh":"廣闊荒野，是非常大的自然地區，幾乎沒有居民或建築。"},{"en":"Hikers may get lost in a vast wilderness if they do not carry maps and water.","zh":"如果遠足者沒有帶地圖和水，可能在廣闊荒野中迷路。"},{"en":"If animals live in a vast wilderness, long-distance signals help them locate one another.","zh":"如果動物生活在廣闊荒野中，遠距離訊號有助牠們找到彼此。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests size, wildness, and isolation.","zh":"這個短語暗示巨大、野性和孤立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"reproductive biology","meaning":"繁殖生物學","examples":[{"en":"Elephant reproductive biology complicates the search for a mate.","zh":"大象繁殖生物學令尋找配偶更複雜。"},{"en":"Reproductive biology is the study of how living things reproduce.","zh":"繁殖生物學，是研究生物如何繁殖的學科。"},{"en":"Doctors and scientists study reproductive biology to understand fertility and development.","zh":"醫生和科學家研究繁殖生物學，以理解生育能力和發展。"},{"en":"If an animal can breed only at certain times, finding a mate becomes more urgent.","zh":"如果動物只能在特定時間繁殖，尋找配偶就變得更緊迫。"},{"en":"The phrase connects mating with biological processes.","zh":"這個短語把交配與生物過程連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"complicate the search","meaning":"令尋找過程更複雜","examples":[{"en":"Elephant reproductive biology complicates the search for a mate.","zh":"大象繁殖生物學令尋找配偶的過程更複雜。"},{"en":"To complicate the search means to make the process of finding something more difficult.","zh":"令尋找過程更複雜，指使尋找某物的過程變得更困難。"},{"en":"A missing phone with a dead battery can complicate the search for it.","zh":"如果遺失手機已沒電，就會令尋找它的過程更複雜。"},{"en":"If female elephants are ready to mate only briefly, males must find them at the right time.","zh":"如果雌象只有短時間適合交配，雄象就必須在正確時間找到牠們。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that an extra factor makes searching harder.","zh":"這個短語顯示額外因素令搜尋更困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"breeding herds","meaning":"繁殖象群","examples":[{"en":"Breeding herds use low-frequency sounds to send warnings.","zh":"繁殖象群使用低頻聲音發出警告。"},{"en":"Breeding herds are groups of animals involved in reproduction and raising young.","zh":"繁殖群，是與繁殖和養育幼崽相關的動物群體。"},{"en":"A breeding herd of cattle may include mothers, calves, and mature males.","zh":"一個繁殖牛群可能包括母牛、小牛和成熟公牛。"},{"en":"If a breeding herd has young animals, warning signals become especially important.","zh":"如果繁殖群中有年幼動物，警告訊號就尤其重要。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to animal groups connected with reproduction.","zh":"這個短語指與繁殖相關的動物群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"send alerts regarding","meaning":"發出關於……的警報","examples":[{"en":"Breeding herds send alerts regarding predators.","zh":"繁殖象群發出關於捕食者的警報。"},{"en":"To send alerts regarding something means to warn others about that issue.","zh":"發出關於某事的警報，指就該問題警告他人。"},{"en":"A school may send alerts regarding heavy rain or transport delays.","zh":"學校可能發出關於暴雨或交通延誤的警報。"},{"en":"If elephants send alerts about predators, the herd can prepare before danger reaches them.","zh":"如果大象發出捕食者警報，象群可以在危險到達前準備。"},{"en":"The phrase describes warning communication.","zh":"這個短語描述警告式溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"predators","meaning":"捕食者","examples":[{"en":"Elephants use low-frequency sounds to warn others about predators.","zh":"大象使用低頻聲音警告其他同伴有捕食者。"},{"en":"Predators are animals that hunt and eat other animals.","zh":"捕食者，是捕獵並吃其他動物的動物。"},{"en":"Lions are predators because they hunt animals such as zebras and antelopes.","zh":"獅子是捕食者，因為牠們捕獵斑馬和羚羊等動物。"},{"en":"If predators are nearby, warning calls can help vulnerable animals escape.","zh":"如果捕食者在附近，警告叫聲可以幫助脆弱動物逃走。"},{"en":"The word refers to hunting animals.","zh":"這個詞指捕獵動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"even though","meaning":"即使","examples":[{"en":"Even though adult elephants have few enemies, baby elephants are vulnerable.","zh":"即使成年大象敵人很少，幼象仍容易受傷害。"},{"en":"Even though means despite the fact that.","zh":"即使，指儘管某事實存在。"},{"en":"Even though the homework was difficult, the student finished it before dinner.","zh":"即使功課很難，學生仍在晚飯前完成它。"},{"en":"If adults are safe but babies are vulnerable, the herd still needs warning systems.","zh":"如果成年個體安全但幼崽脆弱，群體仍需要警告系統。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces contrast between two facts.","zh":"這個短語引入兩個事實之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"adult elephants","meaning":"成年大象","examples":[{"en":"Adult elephants have no enemies other than human beings.","zh":"成年大象除人類以外沒有敵人。"},{"en":"Adult elephants are fully grown elephants.","zh":"成年大象，是已完全長大的大象。"},{"en":"Adult elephants can protect younger members of the herd because of their size and strength.","zh":"成年大象因體型和力量，可以保護象群中的較年幼成員。"},{"en":"If adult elephants face few natural predators, human activity becomes a major danger.","zh":"如果成年大象面對很少自然捕食者，人類活動就成為主要危險。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts mature elephants with calves or young elephants.","zh":"這個短語把成熟大象與幼象或年幼大象作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"no enemies other than","meaning":"除……以外沒有敵人","examples":[{"en":"Adult elephants have no enemies other than human beings.","zh":"成年大象除人類以外沒有敵人。"},{"en":"No enemies other than someone means no enemies except that person or group.","zh":"除某人或群體以外沒有敵人，指除了該人或群體之外沒有敵人。"},{"en":"A well-protected island bird may have no enemies other than humans who disturb its habitat.","zh":"受良好保護的島嶼鳥類可能除破壞其棲息地的人類以外沒有敵人。"},{"en":"If elephants have no major enemy except humans, conservation must address human behaviour.","zh":"如果大象除了人類之外沒有主要敵人，保育就必須處理人類行為。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly excludes all except one source of danger.","zh":"這個短語清楚排除除一個危險來源以外的所有來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"human beings","meaning":"人類","examples":[{"en":"Human beings are the only major enemies of adult elephants.","zh":"人類是成年大象唯一主要敵人。"},{"en":"Human beings means people as a species.","zh":"人類，指作為一個物種的人。"},{"en":"Human beings can protect nature, but they can also damage it through hunting and habitat loss.","zh":"人類可以保護自然，但也可以透過狩獵和棲息地喪失破壞自然。"},{"en":"If human beings are the main threat, laws and education can make a difference.","zh":"如果人類是主要威脅，法律和教育可以帶來改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to humans in a general biological or moral sense.","zh":"這個短語以一般生物或道德意義指人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"baby elephants","meaning":"幼象","examples":[{"en":"Baby elephants are vulnerable to attacks by lions and hyenas.","zh":"幼象容易受到獅子和鬣狗攻擊。"},{"en":"Baby elephants are young elephants that have not yet grown strong enough to protect themselves fully.","zh":"幼象，是尚未長得足夠強壯以完全保護自己的年幼大象。"},{"en":"A baby elephant usually stays close to its mother and herd for safety.","zh":"幼象通常為安全而靠近母象和象群。"},{"en":"If predators attack, older elephants may form a circle around the babies.","zh":"如果捕食者攻擊，較年長大象可能在幼象周圍形成圓圈。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to young calves needing protection.","zh":"這個短語指需要保護的年幼小象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be vulnerable","meaning":"容易受傷害","examples":[{"en":"Baby elephants are vulnerable to predators.","zh":"幼象容易受捕食者傷害。"},{"en":"To be vulnerable means to be easily harmed, attacked, or affected.","zh":"容易受傷害，指容易被傷害、攻擊或影響。"},{"en":"Elderly people may be vulnerable during a heatwave if they live alone.","zh":"如果長者獨居，在熱浪中可能容易受傷害。"},{"en":"If young animals are vulnerable, group protection becomes important.","zh":"如果年幼動物容易受傷害，群體保護就變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weakness or exposure to danger.","zh":"這個短語描述弱點或暴露於危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be susceptible to","meaning":"容易受到……影響；易受……攻擊","examples":[{"en":"Baby elephants are susceptible to attacks by lions and hyenas.","zh":"幼象容易受到獅子和鬣狗攻擊。"},{"en":"To be susceptible to something means to be likely to be affected or harmed by it.","zh":"容易受到某事影響，指很可能被它影響或傷害。"},{"en":"Children may be susceptible to colds when they are tired and sleep poorly.","zh":"孩子疲倦和睡眠差時，可能容易感冒。"},{"en":"If baby elephants are susceptible to predators, warning calls help protect them.","zh":"如果幼象容易受到捕食者攻擊，警告叫聲有助保護牠們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being easily affected by a danger or condition.","zh":"這個短語描述容易受危險或狀況影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"attacks by","meaning":"來自……的攻擊","examples":[{"en":"Baby elephants may suffer attacks by lions and hyenas.","zh":"幼象可能遭受來自獅子和鬣狗的攻擊。"},{"en":"Attacks by someone or something means harmful actions carried out by that person, animal, or force.","zh":"來自某人或某物的攻擊，指由該人、動物或力量造成的傷害行動。"},{"en":"A farm may lose chickens after attacks by foxes at night.","zh":"農場晚上可能因來自狐狸的攻擊而失去雞隻。"},{"en":"If attacks by predators increase, animals may change where they feed or rest.","zh":"如果來自捕食者的攻擊增加，動物可能改變進食或休息地點。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of the attack.","zh":"這個短語指出攻擊來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lions and hyenas","meaning":"獅子和鬣狗","examples":[{"en":"Lions and hyenas may attack baby elephants.","zh":"獅子和鬣狗可能攻擊幼象。"},{"en":"Lions and hyenas are African predators that can hunt weaker or younger animals.","zh":"獅子和鬣狗，是能捕獵較弱或年幼動物的非洲捕食者。"},{"en":"Wildlife guides often warn visitors that lions and hyenas are dangerous hunters.","zh":"野生動物導遊常提醒遊客，獅子和鬣狗是危險獵食者。"},{"en":"If lions and hyenas approach a herd, older elephants may protect the young.","zh":"如果獅子和鬣狗接近象群，較年長大象可能保護幼象。"},{"en":"The phrase names two predator species.","zh":"這個短語指出兩種捕食者物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"at the sight of","meaning":"一看見……","examples":[{"en":"At the sight of a predator, older elephants form a protective group.","zh":"一看見捕食者，較年長大象就組成保護群。"},{"en":"At the sight of something means immediately when it is seen.","zh":"一看見某物，指一看到它的時候立即。"},{"en":"At the sight of a teacher entering the room, students may return to their seats.","zh":"一看見老師進入課室，學生可能回到座位。"},{"en":"If elephants see danger, their response may happen before the predator reaches them.","zh":"如果大象看見危險，反應可能在捕食者到達前發生。"},{"en":"The phrase links seeing something with an immediate reaction.","zh":"這個短語把看見某物與即時反應連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"older elephants in the herd","meaning":"象群中的較年長大象","examples":[{"en":"Older elephants in the herd protect the younger ones.","zh":"象群中的較年長大象保護較年幼的個體。"},{"en":"Older elephants in the herd are the more mature members of an elephant group.","zh":"象群中的較年長大象，是象群中較成熟的成員。"},{"en":"In a family, older siblings may protect younger children when crossing a busy road.","zh":"在家庭中，哥哥姐姐過繁忙馬路時可能保護較年幼孩子。"},{"en":"If older elephants lead the response, the herd can protect calves more effectively.","zh":"如果較年長大象帶領反應，象群就能更有效保護幼象。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies age and role within the group.","zh":"這個短語指出群體中的年齡和角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"clump together","meaning":"聚集在一起","examples":[{"en":"Older elephants clump together when they see a predator.","zh":"較年長大象看見捕食者時會聚集在一起。"},{"en":"To clump together means to gather closely in a group.","zh":"聚集在一起，指緊密地聚成一群。"},{"en":"Students may clump together under a shelter during heavy rain.","zh":"暴雨時，學生可能在遮蔽物下聚集在一起。"},{"en":"If elephants clump together, they can form a stronger barrier against danger.","zh":"如果大象聚集在一起，就能形成更強的防線抵禦危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes close grouping.","zh":"這個短語描述緊密成群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"form a protective group","meaning":"組成保護群","examples":[{"en":"Older elephants form a protective group before fleeing.","zh":"較年長大象在逃走前組成保護群。"},{"en":"To form a protective group means to gather in a way that shields weaker members from danger.","zh":"組成保護群，指以保護較弱成員免受危險的方式聚集。"},{"en":"Teachers may form a protective group around young students during a crowded trip.","zh":"在擁擠旅行中，老師可能在年幼學生周圍組成保護群。"},{"en":"If elephants form a group around calves, predators may find it harder to attack.","zh":"如果大象在幼象周圍組成群體，捕食者就更難攻擊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised protection through grouping.","zh":"這個短語描述透過成群進行有組織保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"before fleeing","meaning":"在逃走之前","examples":[{"en":"The elephants form a protective group before fleeing.","zh":"大象在逃走之前組成保護群。"},{"en":"Before fleeing means before running away from danger.","zh":"在逃走之前，指在逃離危險前。"},{"en":"Before fleeing a smoky room, people should warn others if they can do so safely.","zh":"在逃離有煙房間之前，如果安全，人們應先警告其他人。"},{"en":"If elephants protect the young before fleeing, escape becomes safer for the herd.","zh":"如果大象在逃走前保護幼象，象群逃生會更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an action that happens before escape.","zh":"這個短語描述逃離前發生的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"respond to warning calls","meaning":"對警告叫聲作出反應","examples":[{"en":"Elephants can respond to warning calls in the air.","zh":"大象可以對空氣中的警告叫聲作出反應。"},{"en":"To respond to warning calls means to react when danger signals are heard or detected.","zh":"對警告叫聲作出反應，指聽到或偵測到危險訊號時有反應。"},{"en":"Students respond to a fire alarm by leaving the building calmly.","zh":"學生聽到火警鐘時，會冷靜離開大樓作出反應。"},{"en":"If elephants respond quickly to warning calls, they can protect young members sooner.","zh":"如果大象快速回應警告叫聲，就能更早保護年幼成員。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reaction to danger messages.","zh":"這個短語描述對危險信息的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"warning calls","meaning":"警告叫聲","examples":[{"en":"Warning calls can alert elephants to danger.","zh":"警告叫聲可以提醒大象有危險。"},{"en":"Warning calls are sounds made to tell others that danger is near.","zh":"警告叫聲，是用來告訴其他個體危險接近的聲音。"},{"en":"Birds may make warning calls when a cat enters the garden.","zh":"當貓進入花園，鳥類可能發出警告叫聲。"},{"en":"If warning calls travel far, animals can react before seeing the threat.","zh":"如果警告叫聲傳得很遠，動物就能在看見威脅前反應。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to sound signals of danger.","zh":"這個短語指表示危險的聲音訊號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in the air","meaning":"透過空氣傳播","examples":[{"en":"Elephants can respond to warning calls in the air.","zh":"大象可以對透過空氣傳播的警告叫聲作出反應。"},{"en":"In the air means travelling through air as sound waves rather than through the ground.","zh":"透過空氣傳播，指以聲波經空氣傳遞，而不是透過地面。"},{"en":"Music in the air can be heard by people walking near a concert.","zh":"演唱會附近行人可以聽到空氣中傳來的音樂。"},{"en":"If calls are in the air, ears are likely to be involved in detecting them.","zh":"如果叫聲透過空氣傳播，耳朵很可能參與偵測。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts airborne sound with ground vibration.","zh":"這個短語把空氣聲音與地面震動作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be transmitted solely through","meaning":"只透過……傳送","examples":[{"en":"Researchers wanted to know whether signals transmitted solely through the ground could be detected.","zh":"研究者想知道只透過地面傳送的訊號是否能被偵測。"},{"en":"To be transmitted solely through something means to be sent only through that medium.","zh":"只透過某媒介傳送，指只經由該媒介發送。"},{"en":"A message transmitted solely through email will not reach people without internet access.","zh":"只透過電郵傳送的信息，不能到達沒有網絡的人。"},{"en":"If elephant signals travel solely through the ground, airborne sound cannot explain the response.","zh":"如果大象訊號只透過地面傳播，空氣聲音就不能解釋反應。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses one exclusive path of transmission.","zh":"這個短語強調唯一的傳送路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"solely through the ground","meaning":"只透過地面","examples":[{"en":"The team studied signals transmitted solely through the ground.","zh":"團隊研究只透過地面傳送的訊號。"},{"en":"Solely through the ground means only through earth vibrations, not through air or visual signals.","zh":"只透過地面，指只透過土地震動，而不是透過空氣或視覺訊號。"},{"en":"If a message travels solely through a wire, people without that wire cannot receive it.","zh":"如果信息只透過電線傳送，沒有那條電線的人就不能接收。"},{"en":"If elephants detect signals solely through the ground, their feet may play a major role.","zh":"如果大象只透過地面偵測訊號，牠們的腳可能扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises ground-only transmission.","zh":"這個短語強調只經地面傳播。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"look into","meaning":"調查；研究","examples":[{"en":"The research team designed an experiment to look into that matter.","zh":"研究團隊設計實驗來調查那個問題。"},{"en":"To look into something means to investigate or examine it carefully.","zh":"調查某事，指仔細研究或檢查它。"},{"en":"A school may look into a complaint about unfair lunch prices.","zh":"學校可能調查關於午餐價格不公平的投訴。"},{"en":"If scientists look into a question, they usually collect evidence rather than guess.","zh":"如果科學家調查問題，通常會收集證據，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述主動調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"that matter","meaning":"那個問題","examples":[{"en":"The team designed an experiment to investigate that matter.","zh":"團隊設計實驗來調查那個問題。"},{"en":"That matter means the issue or question just mentioned.","zh":"那個問題，指剛才提到的議題或疑問。"},{"en":"If students complain about noise, the principal may call a meeting to discuss that matter.","zh":"如果學生投訴噪音，校長可能召開會議討論那個問題。"},{"en":"If a matter is unclear, an experiment can help provide evidence.","zh":"如果某問題不清楚，實驗可以幫助提供證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to a specific issue.","zh":"這個短語回指特定議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"research team","meaning":"研究團隊","examples":[{"en":"The research team designed an experiment in 2002.","zh":"研究團隊於2002年設計了一個實驗。"},{"en":"A research team is a group of people working together to investigate a question.","zh":"研究團隊，是一起研究某問題的一群人。"},{"en":"A hospital research team may study how sleep affects recovery.","zh":"醫院研究團隊可能研究睡眠如何影響康復。"},{"en":"If a research team combines different skills, the study may become stronger.","zh":"如果研究團隊結合不同技能，研究可能更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a group doing organised research.","zh":"這個短語指進行有組織研究的團體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"design an experiment","meaning":"設計實驗","examples":[{"en":"The research team designed an experiment at Mushara.","zh":"研究團隊在 Mushara 設計了一個實驗。"},{"en":"To design an experiment means to plan a test that can answer a research question.","zh":"設計實驗，指規劃能回答研究問題的測試。"},{"en":"Students may design an experiment to test whether sunlight affects plant growth.","zh":"學生可能設計實驗來測試陽光是否影響植物生長。"},{"en":"If an experiment is well designed, its results are easier to trust.","zh":"如果實驗設計良好，其結果就更容易被信任。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on planning a scientific test.","zh":"這個短語強調規劃科學測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"electronic devices","meaning":"電子裝置","examples":[{"en":"The experiment used electronic devices to transmit signals.","zh":"實驗使用電子裝置來傳送訊號。"},{"en":"Electronic devices are tools or machines that use electricity to work.","zh":"電子裝置，是使用電力運作的工具或機器。"},{"en":"Phones, sensors, speakers, and computers are electronic devices.","zh":"手機、感應器、喇叭和電腦都是電子裝置。"},{"en":"If researchers use electronic devices, they can control signals more precisely.","zh":"如果研究者使用電子裝置，就可以更準確控制訊號。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to electrically powered equipment.","zh":"這個短語指由電力驅動的設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"enable someone to","meaning":"使某人能夠","examples":[{"en":"The devices enabled the researchers to give out signals through the ground.","zh":"這些裝置使研究者能夠透過地面發出訊號。"},{"en":"To enable someone to do something means to make that action possible.","zh":"使某人能夠做某事，指令該行動成為可能。"},{"en":"A bus pass enables students to travel to school more cheaply.","zh":"巴士證使學生能夠較便宜地上學。"},{"en":"If equipment enables researchers to control signals, the experiment becomes more reliable.","zh":"如果設備使研究者能夠控制訊號，實驗就變得更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a tool or condition with a new ability.","zh":"這個短語把工具或條件與新能力連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"give out signals","meaning":"發出訊號","examples":[{"en":"The devices gave out signals through the ground.","zh":"這些裝置透過地面發出訊號。"},{"en":"To give out signals means to send or emit signals.","zh":"發出訊號，指傳送或發射訊號。"},{"en":"A traffic light gives out signals to tell drivers when to stop or go.","zh":"交通燈發出訊號，告訴司機何時停車或前行。"},{"en":"If devices give out ground signals, researchers can test whether animals detect them.","zh":"如果裝置發出地面訊號，研究者就能測試動物是否偵測到它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes producing messages or signs.","zh":"這個短語描述產生信息或標誌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the outcomes of","meaning":"……的結果","examples":[{"en":"The outcomes of the 2002 study revealed an important ability.","zh":"2002年研究的結果揭示了一種重要能力。"},{"en":"The outcomes of something are the results or effects that come from it.","zh":"某事的結果，指由它產生的結果或影響。"},{"en":"The outcomes of a new homework policy may include better marks or more stress.","zh":"新功課政策的結果可能包括成績更好或壓力更大。"},{"en":"If study outcomes show a clear pattern, researchers can draw stronger conclusions.","zh":"如果研究結果顯示清楚模式，研究者就能得出更有力結論。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what happened as a result.","zh":"這個短語指作為結果發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"reveal that","meaning":"揭示；顯示","examples":[{"en":"The study revealed that elephants could sense warning signals through the ground.","zh":"該研究揭示大象可以透過地面感應警告訊號。"},{"en":"To reveal that means to show or make known something that was previously unclear.","zh":"揭示或顯示，指展示或令人知道先前不清楚的事情。"},{"en":"A survey may reveal that students need more time for reading.","zh":"調查可能顯示學生需要更多閱讀時間。"},{"en":"If an experiment reveals a hidden ability, scientists may change their theory.","zh":"如果實驗揭示隱藏能力，科學家可能改變理論。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a finding.","zh":"這個短語引入研究發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"indeed","meaning":"確實","examples":[{"en":"The elephants could indeed sense warning signals through the ground.","zh":"大象確實能透過地面感應警告訊號。"},{"en":"Indeed means really or in fact, often confirming something.","zh":"確實，指真的或事實上，常用來確認某事。"},{"en":"The exam was indeed difficult, as many students had expected.","zh":"正如許多學生預期，考試確實很難。"},{"en":"If elephants indeed sense ground signals, the theory gains support.","zh":"如果大象確實感應地面訊號，該理論就得到支持。"},{"en":"The word strengthens confirmation.","zh":"這個詞加強確認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"sense warning signals","meaning":"感應警告訊號","examples":[{"en":"Elephants could sense warning signals through the ground.","zh":"大象能透過地面感應警告訊號。"},{"en":"To sense warning signals means to detect messages that indicate danger.","zh":"感應警告訊號，指偵測表示危險的信息。"},{"en":"A driver may sense warning signals when a car makes a strange sound.","zh":"當汽車發出奇怪聲音，司機可能感應到警告訊號。"},{"en":"If elephants sense warning signals early, they can gather and protect calves.","zh":"如果大象及早感應警告訊號，就能聚集並保護幼象。"},{"en":"The phrase describes detecting danger-related messages.","zh":"這個短語描述偵測與危險相關的信息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"through the ground","meaning":"透過地面","examples":[{"en":"The warning signals were transmitted through the ground.","zh":"警告訊號透過地面傳送。"},{"en":"Through the ground means by travelling in or across the earth rather than through air.","zh":"透過地面，指在土地中或跨越土地傳播，而不是透過空氣。"},{"en":"People can feel a train’s movement through the ground before it arrives.","zh":"火車到達前，人們可能透過地面感到它的移動。"},{"en":"If signals travel through the ground, animals may detect them with feet or body tissues.","zh":"如果訊號透過地面傳播，動物可能用腳或身體組織偵測它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the medium of transmission.","zh":"這個短語描述傳播媒介。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"set up an experiment","meaning":"設立實驗","examples":[{"en":"An experiment was set up to solve the problem.","zh":"一個實驗被設立來解決問題。"},{"en":"To set up an experiment means to prepare the equipment, conditions, and procedure for a test.","zh":"設立實驗，指為測試準備設備、條件和程序。"},{"en":"Students set up an experiment by placing plants in sunlight and shade.","zh":"學生透過把植物放在陽光和陰影中來設立實驗。"},{"en":"If an experiment is set up carefully, the results are more reliable.","zh":"如果實驗設立得仔細，結果就更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preparing a scientific investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述準備科學調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in the hope of","meaning":"希望能夠","examples":[{"en":"An experiment was set up in the hope of solving the problem.","zh":"實驗被設立，希望能夠解決該問題。"},{"en":"In the hope of means with the aim or wish of achieving something.","zh":"希望能夠，指帶着達成某事的目標或願望。"},{"en":"A student may join a speaking club in the hope of becoming more confident.","zh":"學生可能加入口語學會，希望能夠變得更有信心。"},{"en":"If researchers lack an answer, they may design a test in the hope of finding one.","zh":"如果研究者缺乏答案，可能設計測試，希望能找到答案。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces hopeful purpose.","zh":"這個短語引入帶希望的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"solve the problem","meaning":"解決問題","examples":[{"en":"The experiment was designed to solve the problem.","zh":"該實驗被設計來解決問題。"},{"en":"To solve the problem means to find an answer or remove the difficulty.","zh":"解決問題，指找到答案或消除困難。"},{"en":"A school may hire more buses to solve the problem of long queues.","zh":"學校可能聘用更多巴士來解決長隊問題。"},{"en":"If an experiment answers the research question, it helps solve the scientific problem.","zh":"如果實驗回答了研究問題，就有助解決科學問題。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on finding a workable answer.","zh":"這個短語強調找到可行答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"three different recordings","meaning":"三段不同錄音","examples":[{"en":"The experiment used three different recordings.","zh":"該實驗使用三段不同錄音。"},{"en":"Three different recordings means three separate recorded sounds or audio samples.","zh":"三段不同錄音，指三個分開錄下的聲音或音頻樣本。"},{"en":"A listening test may use three different recordings to compare accents.","zh":"聆聽測驗可能使用三段不同錄音來比較口音。"},{"en":"If researchers compare recordings, they can see whether animals react differently to each sound.","zh":"如果研究者比較錄音，就能看動物是否對每種聲音有不同反應。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the number and variety of sound samples.","zh":"這個短語指出聲音樣本的數量和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the 1994 warning call","meaning":"1994 年的警告叫聲","examples":[{"en":"The experiment used the 1994 warning call from Mushara.","zh":"該實驗使用來自 Mushara 的1994年警告叫聲。"},{"en":"The 1994 warning call means a danger signal recorded in that year.","zh":"1994年的警告叫聲，指在該年錄下的危險訊號。"},{"en":"A researcher may replay an old recording to compare past and present animal responses.","zh":"研究者可能重播舊錄音，以比較過去和現在的動物反應。"},{"en":"If a recorded warning call still causes a reaction, the signal may carry clear meaning.","zh":"如果錄下的警告叫聲仍引起反應，該訊號可能帶有清楚意思。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a specific recorded alarm sound.","zh":"這個短語指出特定錄下的警報聲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"anti-predator call","meaning":"反捕食者叫聲","examples":[{"en":"The researchers played an anti-predator call recorded in Kenya.","zh":"研究者播放在肯尼亞錄下的反捕食者叫聲。"},{"en":"An anti-predator call is a sound used to warn or respond to predators.","zh":"反捕食者叫聲，是用來警告或回應捕食者的聲音。"},{"en":"Birds may make anti-predator calls when they see a cat.","zh":"鳥類看見貓時可能發出反捕食者叫聲。"},{"en":"If elephants react to an anti-predator call, they may understand it as a danger signal.","zh":"如果大象對反捕食者叫聲有反應，牠們可能把它理解為危險訊號。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a call connected with defence against predators.","zh":"這個短語描述與防禦捕食者有關的叫聲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"artificial warbling tone","meaning":"人造顫音","examples":[{"en":"The experiment also used an artificial warbling tone.","zh":"實驗也使用人造顫音。"},{"en":"An artificial warbling tone is a human-made sound that rises and falls or wavers.","zh":"人造顫音，是人為製造、會升降或顫動的聲音。"},{"en":"A phone app can create an artificial tone for a hearing test.","zh":"手機應用程式可以為聽力測試製造人工聲音。"},{"en":"If animals ignore an artificial tone but react to real calls, the difference is meaningful.","zh":"如果動物忽視人造聲音但回應真實叫聲，差異就有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a controlled non-natural sound.","zh":"這個短語描述受控制的非自然聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"to this point","meaning":"到目前為止","examples":[{"en":"The data observed to this point imply that the elephants responded as expected.","zh":"到目前為止觀察到的數據暗示大象按預期反應。"},{"en":"To this point means up to this stage or up to now.","zh":"到目前為止，指直到這個階段或直到現在。"},{"en":"To this point, the class has learned basic nouns, verbs, and sentence patterns.","zh":"到目前為止，班級已學習基本名詞、動詞和句式。"},{"en":"If data to this point support a theory, later evidence may still refine it.","zh":"如果到目前為止的數據支持某理論，後來證據仍可能修正它。"},{"en":"The phrase limits a claim to the evidence collected so far.","zh":"這個短語把主張限制在目前收集到的證據內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"imply that","meaning":"暗示；顯示","examples":[{"en":"The data imply that the elephants were responding as expected.","zh":"數據暗示大象正按預期作出反應。"},{"en":"To imply that means to suggest something indirectly rather than state it as certain.","zh":"暗示某事，指間接顯示它，而不是確定陳述。"},{"en":"A student’s empty notebook may imply that they have not been following the lesson.","zh":"學生筆記簿空白，可能暗示他沒有跟上課堂。"},{"en":"If data imply a pattern, researchers may need more evidence before confirming it.","zh":"如果數據暗示某模式，研究者在證實前可能需要更多證據。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces cautious interpretation.","zh":"這個短語引入謹慎解讀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"respond the way","meaning":"以……方式反應","examples":[{"en":"The elephants responded the way the researcher expected.","zh":"大象以研究者預期的方式反應。"},{"en":"To respond the way someone expected means to react in the predicted manner.","zh":"以某人預期的方式反應，指按預測的方式作出反應。"},{"en":"A student responded the way the teacher expected by checking the evidence before answering.","zh":"學生透過回答前檢查證據，以老師預期的方式反應。"},{"en":"If animals respond the expected way, the hypothesis gains support.","zh":"如果動物以預期方式反應，假說就得到支持。"},{"en":"The phrase connects reaction with prediction.","zh":"這個短語把反應與預測連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"fascinating finding","meaning":"令人着迷的發現","examples":[{"en":"The fascinating finding was that the Kenyan call also caused a response.","zh":"令人着迷的發現是肯尼亞叫聲也引起反應。"},{"en":"A fascinating finding is a discovery that is very interesting and makes people want to know more.","zh":"令人着迷的發現，是非常有趣並令人想知道更多的發現。"},{"en":"A health study may produce a fascinating finding about how music reduces stress.","zh":"健康研究可能得出關於音樂如何減壓的令人着迷發現。"},{"en":"If an unfamiliar call causes a response, researchers may ask whether the signal is widely understood.","zh":"如果陌生叫聲引起反應，研究者可能會問該訊號是否被廣泛理解。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights an especially interesting result.","zh":"這個短語突出特別有趣的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be unfamiliar to","meaning":"對……來說陌生","examples":[{"en":"The anti-predator call from Kenya was unfamiliar to the elephants.","zh":"來自肯尼亞的反捕食者叫聲對大象來說陌生。"},{"en":"To be unfamiliar to someone means not to be known or recognised by them.","zh":"對某人來說陌生，指某人不知道或不認得它。"},{"en":"A new school building may be unfamiliar to students on their first day.","zh":"新校舍對第一天上學的學生來說可能很陌生。"},{"en":"If a signal is unfamiliar but still causes a reaction, it may contain a universal warning pattern.","zh":"如果一個訊號陌生但仍引起反應，它可能包含普遍警告模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lack of previous experience or recognition.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏先前經驗或辨認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"cause someone to","meaning":"令某人……","examples":[{"en":"The unfamiliar call caused the elephants to gather around.","zh":"陌生叫聲令大象聚集起來。"},{"en":"To cause someone to do something means to make them do it or lead them to do it.","zh":"令某人做某事，指使他們做該事或導致他們做該事。"},{"en":"Heavy rain may cause students to stay inside during lunch.","zh":"大雨可能令學生午飯時留在室內。"},{"en":"If a sound causes animals to gather, it likely carries important information.","zh":"如果聲音令動物聚集，它很可能帶有重要信息。"},{"en":"The phrase shows cause and result.","zh":"這個短語顯示原因和結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"gather around","meaning":"聚集起來","examples":[{"en":"The elephants gathered around after hearing the call.","zh":"大象聽到叫聲後聚集起來。"},{"en":"To gather around means to come together near a person, place, or object.","zh":"聚集起來，指靠近某人、地方或物件集合在一起。"},{"en":"Students may gather around a teacher when she shows a science experiment.","zh":"老師展示科學實驗時，學生可能聚集在她周圍。"},{"en":"If elephants gather around after a warning, they may be preparing to defend the group.","zh":"如果大象在警告後聚集，牠們可能正在準備保護群體。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement into a close group.","zh":"這個短語描述移動成緊密群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"tense up","meaning":"繃緊；緊張起來","examples":[{"en":"The elephants tensed up after hearing the warning call.","zh":"大象聽到警告叫聲後繃緊起來。"},{"en":"To tense up means to become physically tight or emotionally alert because of stress or danger.","zh":"繃緊或緊張起來，指因壓力或危險而身體變緊或情緒警覺。"},{"en":"A student may tense up when asked to speak in front of the class.","zh":"學生被要求在全班面前發言時，可能會緊張起來。"},{"en":"If animals tense up after a sound, they may be preparing for possible danger.","zh":"如果動物在聽到聲音後繃緊，可能正在準備面對危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a body becoming tight and ready.","zh":"這個短語描述身體變緊並準備反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"rumble aggressively","meaning":"發出具攻擊性的低吼聲","examples":[{"en":"The elephants rumbled aggressively in response to the call.","zh":"大象回應該叫聲時發出具攻擊性的低吼聲。"},{"en":"To rumble aggressively means to make a deep, low sound in a threatening or forceful way.","zh":"發出具攻擊性的低吼聲，指以具威脅或強烈方式發出低沉聲音。"},{"en":"A dog may growl aggressively when it senses danger near its owner.","zh":"狗感到主人附近有危險時，可能發出具攻擊性的吼聲。"},{"en":"If elephants rumble aggressively, they may be warning others or preparing to defend themselves.","zh":"如果大象發出具攻擊性的低吼聲，可能是在警告其他個體或準備防衛。"},{"en":"The phrase combines low sound with hostile or defensive emotion.","zh":"這個短語結合低沉聲音與敵意或防衛情緒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"flee","meaning":"逃走","examples":[{"en":"The elephants did not always flee after hearing the Kenyan call.","zh":"大象聽到肯尼亞叫聲後並不總是逃走。"},{"en":"To flee means to run away from danger.","zh":"逃走，指逃離危險。"},{"en":"People may flee a building when they hear a serious fire alarm.","zh":"人們聽到嚴重火警鐘時，可能逃離大樓。"},{"en":"If animals do not flee, they may be uncertain, defensive, or gathering information.","zh":"如果動物沒有逃走，可能是不確定、正在防衛或正在收集資訊。"},{"en":"The word describes escape from threat.","zh":"這個詞描述逃離威脅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"clear-cut results","meaning":"明確的結果","examples":[{"en":"The researcher did not expect the results to be that clear-cut.","zh":"研究者沒有預期結果會那麼明確。"},{"en":"Clear-cut results are results that are obvious, definite, and easy to interpret.","zh":"明確的結果，是明顯、確定而容易解讀的結果。"},{"en":"If every student improves after a new lesson plan, the results may look clear-cut.","zh":"如果每個學生在新教案後都有進步，結果可能看起來很明確。"},{"en":"If animals react differently each time, the results are less clear-cut.","zh":"如果動物每次反應不同，結果就較不明確。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence with little ambiguity.","zh":"這個短語描述歧義很少的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"label the diagram","meaning":"標示圖表","examples":[{"en":"Candidates have to label the diagram using words from the passage.","zh":"考生必須使用文章中的字詞標示圖表。"},{"en":"To label the diagram means to write the correct names beside parts of a picture or drawing.","zh":"標示圖表，指在圖片或圖畫的部分旁寫上正確名稱。"},{"en":"In biology, students may label a diagram of the ear, eye, or plant.","zh":"在生物課中，學生可能標示耳朵、眼睛或植物圖。"},{"en":"If the label must come from the passage, spelling and wording matter.","zh":"如果標籤必須來自文章，拼字和措辭就很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction for visual tasks.","zh":"這個短語是視覺題中的常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"choose no more than two words","meaning":"選擇不超過兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Students should choose no more than two words from the passage.","zh":"學生應從文章中選擇不超過兩個字。"},{"en":"Choose no more than two words means the answer must contain one or two words only.","zh":"選擇不超過兩個字，指答案只能包含一個或兩個詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “fatty pad,” students should not add extra words before it.","zh":"如果答案是 “fatty pad”，學生不應在前面加入額外字詞。"},{"en":"If students write three words, the answer may be marked wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"如果學生寫三個詞，即使意思正確，答案也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"write your answers in","meaning":"將答案寫在……內","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write their answers in the boxes on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生將答案寫在答題紙上的方格內。"},{"en":"Write your answers in a place means put the answers in that specific space.","zh":"將答案寫在某處，指把答案填入指定位置。"},{"en":"Students should write their answers in the correct boxes, not beside the questions.","zh":"學生應將答案寫在正確方格內，而不是寫在題目旁。"},{"en":"If answers are written in the wrong place, they may not be marked correctly.","zh":"如果答案寫錯位置，可能不會被正確批改。"},{"en":"The phrase tells candidates where to record final answers.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生在哪裡記錄最終答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the summary with words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill missing words in a short version of the passage.","zh":"完成摘要，指在文章簡短版本中填入缺少的字詞。"},{"en":"Students complete a summary by using grammar clues and passage meaning.","zh":"學生透過文法線索和文章意思完成摘要。"},{"en":"If a summary gap needs a noun, students should not choose a verb.","zh":"如果摘要空格需要名詞，學生就不應選動詞。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不超過三個字","examples":[{"en":"The instruction says to choose no more than three words.","zh":"指示說選擇不超過三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"不超過三個字，指答案必須包含三個詞或以下。"},{"en":"“ground vibrations” is acceptable, but a long phrase with extra words is not.","zh":"“ground vibrations” 可以接受，但加入額外字詞的長短語不可以。"},{"en":"If students exceed the word limit, the answer may be marked wrong.","zh":"如果學生超出字數限制，答案可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict maximum length.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格最大長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"how elephants sense","meaning":"大象如何感應……","examples":[{"en":"The summary asks how elephants sense sound vibrations.","zh":"摘要詢問大象如何感應聲音震動。"},{"en":"How elephants sense something means the way elephants detect or feel it.","zh":"大象如何感應某物，指大象偵測或感覺它的方式。"},{"en":"A biology lesson may ask how humans sense heat, pain, or sound.","zh":"生物課可能問人類如何感應熱、痛或聲音。"},{"en":"If researchers know how elephants sense vibrations, they can understand communication better.","zh":"如果研究者知道大象如何感應震動，就能更好理解溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase asks about the sensing mechanism.","zh":"這個短語詢問感應機制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"sound vibrations","meaning":"聲音震動","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are studying how elephants sense sound vibrations.","zh":"研究者正在研究大象如何感應聲音震動。"},{"en":"Sound vibrations are movements in air, ground, or material caused by sound energy.","zh":"聲音震動，是由聲音能量在空氣、地面或材料中造成的移動。"},{"en":"A loud speaker can create sound vibrations that make a table shake.","zh":"大聲喇叭可以造成令桌子震動的聲音震動。"},{"en":"If sound vibrations travel through the ground, animals may detect them through touch or bone.","zh":"如果聲音震動透過地面傳播，動物可能透過觸覺或骨骼偵測它們。"},{"en":"The phrase links sound with physical movement.","zh":"這個短語把聲音與物理移動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"still unknown","meaning":"仍然未知","examples":[{"en":"How elephants sense the vibrations is still unknown.","zh":"大象如何感應震動仍然未知。"},{"en":"Still unknown means not yet discovered or clearly understood.","zh":"仍然未知，指尚未被發現或清楚理解。"},{"en":"The cause of a student’s sudden illness may be still unknown before medical tests are finished.","zh":"在醫學測試完成前，學生突然生病的原因可能仍然未知。"},{"en":"If a mechanism is still unknown, researchers should avoid overconfident conclusions.","zh":"如果機制仍然未知，研究者應避免過度自信的結論。"},{"en":"The phrase shows continuing uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語顯示持續不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"propose that","meaning":"提出；認為","examples":[{"en":"O’Connell-Rodwell proposes that elephants listen with their trunks and feet.","zh":"O’Connell-Rodwell 提出大象用象鼻和腳聽。"},{"en":"To propose that means to suggest an explanation or idea for others to consider.","zh":"提出某事，指提出解釋或想法讓他人考慮。"},{"en":"A student may propose that the class raise money through a book sale.","zh":"學生可能提出班級透過賣書籌款。"},{"en":"If a scientist proposes a theory, further evidence is needed to test it.","zh":"如果科學家提出理論，就需要進一步證據測試它。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a suggested explanation.","zh":"這個短語引入建議性解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"two kinds of nerve endings","meaning":"兩種神經末梢","examples":[{"en":"Their trunks and feet contain two kinds of nerve endings.","zh":"牠們的象鼻和腳含有兩種神經末梢。"},{"en":"Two kinds of nerve endings means two different types of sensory nerve structures.","zh":"兩種神經末梢，指兩類不同的感覺神經結構。"},{"en":"Human skin has different kinds of nerve endings for pressure, pain, and temperature.","zh":"人類皮膚有不同神經末梢，用於壓力、疼痛和溫度。"},{"en":"If elephant feet have two kinds of nerve endings, they may detect more than one type of vibration.","zh":"如果大象腳部有兩種神經末梢，就可能偵測多於一種震動。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies sensory variety in body parts.","zh":"這個短語指出身體部位中的感覺多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"respond to both","meaning":"對兩者都作出反應","examples":[{"en":"The nerve endings respond to both low and higher frequencies.","zh":"神經末梢對低頻和較高頻率兩者都作出反應。"},{"en":"To respond to both means to react to two different things or categories.","zh":"對兩者都作出反應，指對兩種不同事物或類別都有反應。"},{"en":"Some students respond to both visual examples and spoken explanation.","zh":"有些學生對視覺例子和口頭解釋兩者都有反應。"},{"en":"If nerves respond to both frequency ranges, elephants may sense a wider range of vibrations.","zh":"如果神經對兩個頻率範圍都有反應，大象可能感應更廣範圍的震動。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses reaction to two items, not just one.","zh":"這個短語強調對兩項而不只一項作反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"slightly higher frequencies","meaning":"稍高頻率","examples":[{"en":"Some nerve endings respond to slightly higher frequencies.","zh":"一些神經末梢對稍高頻率作出反應。"},{"en":"Slightly higher frequencies are frequencies a little above another frequency range.","zh":"稍高頻率，是比另一頻率範圍略高的頻率。"},{"en":"A hearing test may compare low tones with slightly higher frequencies.","zh":"聽力測試可能比較低音與稍高頻率。"},{"en":"If nerves detect slightly higher frequencies, they may add detail to the signal.","zh":"如果神經偵測稍高頻率，就可能為訊號加入細節。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small increase in frequency.","zh":"這個短語描述頻率上的小幅提高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"lie at the intersection of","meaning":"位於……的交匯處","examples":[{"en":"O’Connell-Rodwell’s work lies at the intersection of several sciences.","zh":"O’Connell-Rodwell 的工作位於幾門科學的交匯處。"},{"en":"To lie at the intersection of fields means to belong to the area where those fields meet.","zh":"位於不同領域的交匯處，指屬於這些領域相遇的範圍。"},{"en":"Environmental health lies at the intersection of medicine, biology, and public policy.","zh":"環境健康位於醫學、生物學和公共政策的交匯處。"},{"en":"If research lies at an intersection, one discipline alone may not explain it fully.","zh":"如果研究位於交匯處，單一學科可能不能完全解釋它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cross-disciplinary position.","zh":"這個短語描述跨學科位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"indicate that","meaning":"表明；指出","examples":[{"en":"She was the first person to indicate that a large land animal could use seismic signals.","zh":"她是首位指出大型陸地動物可以使用地面震動訊號的人。"},{"en":"To indicate that means to show, suggest, or point out that something may be true.","zh":"表明或指出，指顯示、暗示或指出某事可能為真。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may indicate that the new study method is working.","zh":"學生進步可能表明新學習方法有效。"},{"en":"If evidence indicates a possibility, researchers may investigate it further.","zh":"如果證據表明某可能性，研究者可能進一步調查。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a sign or suggestion.","zh":"這個短語引入跡象或建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a large land animal","meaning":"大型陸地動物","examples":[{"en":"A large land animal can also send and receive seismic signals.","zh":"大型陸地動物也可以發送和接收地面震動訊號。"},{"en":"A large land animal is a big animal that mainly lives on land.","zh":"大型陸地動物，是主要生活在陸地上的大型動物。"},{"en":"Rhinos and giraffes are large land animals.","zh":"犀牛和長頸鹿都是大型陸地動物。"},{"en":"If a large land animal uses ground vibrations, body size may help signal transmission.","zh":"如果大型陸地動物使用地面震動，體型可能幫助訊號傳送。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both size and habitat.","zh":"這個短語同時描述大小和棲息地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"prove the existence of","meaning":"證明……的存在","examples":[{"en":"The behaviour may prove the existence of non-auditory communication.","zh":"這種行為可能證明非聽覺溝通的存在。"},{"en":"To prove the existence of something means to show with evidence that it really exists.","zh":"證明某事的存在，指用證據顯示它真的存在。"},{"en":"Footprints can prove the existence of an animal in a forest.","zh":"腳印可以證明森林中有某種動物存在。"},{"en":"If repeated behaviour matches ground signals, it may help prove a hidden communication method.","zh":"如果重複行為與地面訊號相符，就可能有助證明隱藏溝通方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong evidence for something real.","zh":"這個短語描述證明某事真實存在的有力證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"communication methods other than","meaning":"除……以外的溝通方式","examples":[{"en":"The experiment suggested communication methods other than auditory communication.","zh":"實驗暗示除聽覺溝通以外的溝通方式。"},{"en":"Communication methods other than something are ways of communicating besides that method.","zh":"除某事以外的溝通方式，是除了該方式之外的溝通方法。"},{"en":"People use communication methods other than speech, such as gestures and text messages.","zh":"人們使用說話以外的溝通方式，例如手勢和短訊。"},{"en":"If animals use vibrations, they have communication methods other than sound in the air.","zh":"如果動物使用震動，牠們就有空氣中聲音以外的溝通方式。"},{"en":"The phrase adds alternatives beyond one known method.","zh":"這個短語加入已知方式以外的替代方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"have determined that","meaning":"已確定","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have determined that long-distance communication is essential.","zh":"科學家已確定遠距離溝通至關重要。"},{"en":"To have determined that means to have found or concluded something after study.","zh":"已確定某事，指經研究後發現或得出結論。"},{"en":"Doctors may determine that a patient needs rest after examining test results.","zh":"醫生檢查測試結果後，可能確定病人需要休息。"},{"en":"If scientists have determined a fact, it is based on evidence rather than guesswork.","zh":"如果科學家已確定某事實，它就是基於證據而不是猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a researched conclusion.","zh":"這個短語顯示經研究得出的結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"seeking a mate","meaning":"尋找配偶","examples":[{"en":"Elephants need long-distance communication when they are seeking a mate.","zh":"大象在尋找配偶時需要遠距離溝通。"},{"en":"Seeking a mate means looking for a partner for reproduction.","zh":"尋找配偶，指尋找繁殖伴侶。"},{"en":"Birds may sing loudly when seeking a mate in spring.","zh":"鳥類春天尋找配偶時可能高聲鳴叫。"},{"en":"If animals are spread across a huge area, seeking a mate requires effective signals.","zh":"如果動物分布在巨大地區，尋找配偶需要有效訊號。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the search for a breeding partner.","zh":"這個短語指尋找繁殖伴侶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"warning of predators","meaning":"警告有捕食者","examples":[{"en":"Elephants use long-distance communication when warning of predators.","zh":"大象在警告有捕食者時使用遠距離溝通。"},{"en":"Warning of predators means alerting others that hunting animals are nearby.","zh":"警告有捕食者，指提醒其他個體有獵食動物在附近。"},{"en":"Birds may give warning of predators when a snake approaches a nest.","zh":"當蛇接近鳥巢，鳥類可能警告有捕食者。"},{"en":"If warning signals travel far, vulnerable animals can react earlier.","zh":"如果警告訊號傳得遠，脆弱動物就能更早反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes danger communication about hunters.","zh":"這個短語描述關於獵食者的危險溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"detect warning calls","meaning":"偵測警告叫聲","examples":[{"en":"The 2002 study showed that elephants could detect warning calls through the ground.","zh":"2002年的研究顯示大象能透過地面偵測警告叫聲。"},{"en":"To detect warning calls means to notice signals that warn of danger.","zh":"偵測警告叫聲，指注意到警告危險的訊號。"},{"en":"A security system can detect warning signals from smoke or broken glass.","zh":"保安系統可以偵測來自煙霧或玻璃破碎的警告訊號。"},{"en":"If elephants detect warning calls through the ground, they do not need airborne sound alone.","zh":"如果大象透過地面偵測警告叫聲，就不只依賴空氣聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on sensing danger messages.","zh":"這個短語強調感應危險信息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"考生為每條問題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the option letter that matches the answer.","zh":"選出正確字母，指選擇與答案相符的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice task, students may choose A, B, C, or D.","zh":"在選擇題中，學生可能選 A、B、C 或 D。"},{"en":"If students find the evidence first, they can choose the correct letter more accurately.","zh":"如果學生先找到證據，就能更準確選出正確字母。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"according to the passage","meaning":"根據文章","examples":[{"en":"Students answer the question according to the passage.","zh":"學生根據文章回答問題。"},{"en":"According to the passage means based only on what the text says.","zh":"根據文章，指只基於文本所說內容。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students should answer according to the passage, not their outside knowledge.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應根據文章作答，而不是根據外部知識。"},{"en":"If the passage gives no evidence, students should not guess from common sense.","zh":"如果文章沒有提供證據，學生不應靠常識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase keeps answers tied to the source text.","zh":"這個短語令答案與來源文本連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"long-distance communication","meaning":"遠距離溝通","examples":[{"en":"Long-distance communication is essential for elephant survival.","zh":"遠距離溝通對大象生存至關重要。"},{"en":"Long-distance communication is the sending and receiving of messages across far spaces.","zh":"遠距離溝通，是跨越遠距離傳送和接收信息。"},{"en":"Video calls allow families in different countries to maintain long-distance communication.","zh":"視像通話讓不同國家的家庭維持遠距離溝通。"},{"en":"If animals live far apart, long-distance communication helps them stay connected.","zh":"如果動物相距很遠，遠距離溝通有助牠們保持聯繫。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on communication over wide areas.","zh":"這個短語強調跨越廣大地區的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"for survival","meaning":"為了生存","examples":[{"en":"Elephants need long-distance communication for survival.","zh":"大象為了生存需要遠距離溝通。"},{"en":"For survival means in order to stay alive or continue existing.","zh":"為了生存，指為了維持生命或繼續存在。"},{"en":"People need clean water and food for survival.","zh":"人們為了生存需要清潔食水和食物。"},{"en":"If communication helps elephants avoid danger and find mates, it is important for survival.","zh":"如果溝通幫助大象避開危險和尋找配偶，它就對生存重要。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the life-or-death purpose of something.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事的生死目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"threatening predator","meaning":"構成威脅的捕食者","examples":[{"en":"An elephant may need communication when a threatening predator appears.","zh":"當構成威脅的捕食者出現時，大象可能需要溝通。"},{"en":"A threatening predator is a hunting animal that creates danger.","zh":"構成威脅的捕食者，是造成危險的獵食動物。"},{"en":"A fox near a chicken coop is a threatening predator to the hens.","zh":"雞舍附近的狐狸對母雞來說是構成威脅的捕食者。"},{"en":"If a threatening predator appears, animals may warn others and form a defensive group.","zh":"如果構成威脅的捕食者出現，動物可能警告同伴並組成防衛群。"},{"en":"The phrase combines danger with a hunting animal.","zh":"這個短語結合危險和獵食動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"young elephants","meaning":"年幼大象","examples":[{"en":"Young elephants are more vulnerable to predators than adults.","zh":"年幼大象比成年大象更容易受捕食者傷害。"},{"en":"Young elephants are elephants that have not yet reached full maturity.","zh":"年幼大象，是尚未完全成熟的大象。"},{"en":"Young elephants often stay close to older herd members for protection.","zh":"年幼大象常靠近象群中的較年長成員以獲得保護。"},{"en":"If young elephants are at risk, warning communication becomes especially valuable.","zh":"如果年幼大象有危險，警告溝通就特別有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to calves or not-yet-adult elephants.","zh":"這個短語指幼象或未成年大象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"older members of the herd","meaning":"象群中的較年長成員","examples":[{"en":"Older members of the herd protect the younger elephants.","zh":"象群中的較年長成員保護年幼大象。"},{"en":"Older members of the herd are the mature animals within an animal group.","zh":"象群中的較年長成員，是動物群體中的成熟個體。"},{"en":"In a group trip, older students may guide younger ones through a busy station.","zh":"在團體旅行中，較年長學生可能帶領較年幼學生穿過繁忙車站。"},{"en":"If older members lead protective action, younger members are safer.","zh":"如果較年長成員帶領保護行動，較年幼成員會更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies senior animals in a social group.","zh":"這個短語指出社群中的較年長動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"flee from","meaning":"逃離……","examples":[{"en":"The herd may flee from danger after forming a protective group.","zh":"象群可能在組成保護群後逃離危險。"},{"en":"To flee from something means to run away from it because it is dangerous.","zh":"逃離某事，指因它危險而逃走。"},{"en":"People may flee from a building when a fire spreads quickly.","zh":"當火勢迅速蔓延，人們可能逃離建築物。"},{"en":"If animals flee from predators too late, young members may be harmed.","zh":"如果動物太遲逃離捕食者，年幼成員可能受傷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes escape from a threat.","zh":"這個短語描述逃離威脅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"in estrus","meaning":"處於發情期","examples":[{"en":"A female elephant in estrus may be ready to mate.","zh":"處於發情期的雌象可能已準備交配。"},{"en":"In estrus means in the biological period when a female animal is fertile and ready for mating.","zh":"處於發情期，指雌性動物處於可受孕並準備交配的生物時期。"},{"en":"Farmers may track when an animal is in estrus to manage breeding.","zh":"農民可能追蹤動物何時處於發情期，以管理繁殖。"},{"en":"If a female elephant is in estrus for a limited time, communication helps males locate her.","zh":"如果雌象發情期有限，溝通就幫助雄象找到牠。"},{"en":"The phrase is a biological term related to reproduction.","zh":"這個短語是與繁殖相關的生物學術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"author’s attitude towards","meaning":"作者對……的態度","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the author’s attitude towards the final experiment.","zh":"題目問作者對最後實驗的態度。"},{"en":"The author’s attitude towards something means the writer’s feeling, opinion, or judgement about it.","zh":"作者對某事的態度，指作者對它的感受、意見或判斷。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students may identify whether the author’s attitude is doubtful, supportive, or neutral.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能要判斷作者態度是懷疑、支持還是中立。"},{"en":"If the writer calls a finding fascinating but not clear-cut, the attitude may be interested yet cautious.","zh":"如果作者稱發現令人着迷但不明確，態度可能是感興趣但謹慎。"},{"en":"The phrase asks how the writer views something.","zh":"這個短語詢問作者如何看待某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"using three different recordings","meaning":"使用三段不同錄音","examples":[{"en":"The experiment involved using three different recordings.","zh":"實驗涉及使用三段不同錄音。"},{"en":"Using three different recordings means playing three separate audio samples as part of the test.","zh":"使用三段不同錄音，指播放三個分開的音頻樣本作為測試一部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may test listening skills by using three different recordings of different accents.","zh":"老師可能使用三段不同口音錄音來測試聆聽能力。"},{"en":"If animals react differently to recordings, researchers can compare the meaning of each sound.","zh":"如果動物對錄音有不同反應，研究者可以比較每種聲音的意思。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the method used in an experiment.","zh":"這個短語描述實驗所用方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"outcome","meaning":"結果","examples":[{"en":"The outcome of the experiment was not completely straightforward.","zh":"實驗結果並不完全簡單直接。"},{"en":"An outcome is the result or final effect of an action, event, or experiment.","zh":"結果，是行動、事件或實驗的最終效果。"},{"en":"The outcome of a school meeting may be a new homework policy.","zh":"學校會議的結果可能是一項新功課政策。"},{"en":"If the outcome is mixed, researchers should be careful about strong conclusions.","zh":"如果結果混雜，研究者對強結論應保持謹慎。"},{"en":"The word refers to what happens as a result.","zh":"這個詞指作為結果發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"contrary to","meaning":"與……相反","examples":[{"en":"The outcome was not clearly contrary to the original expectation.","zh":"結果並沒有清楚地與原本預期相反。"},{"en":"Contrary to something means opposite to it or different from what it suggests.","zh":"與某事相反，指與它相對或不同於它所暗示的內容。"},{"en":"Contrary to the weather forecast, the afternoon was sunny.","zh":"與天氣預報相反，下午天氣晴朗。"},{"en":"If results are not contrary to expectations, they may partly support the original idea.","zh":"如果結果不與預期相反，它們可能部分支持原本想法。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces opposition or contrast.","zh":"這個短語引入相反或對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"original expectation","meaning":"原本預期","examples":[{"en":"The data partly matched the researcher’s original expectation.","zh":"數據部分符合研究者的原本預期。"},{"en":"An original expectation is what someone first thought would happen before seeing the results.","zh":"原本預期，是某人在看到結果前最初以為會發生的事情。"},{"en":"A teacher’s original expectation may be that students will find the grammar exercise easy.","zh":"老師的原本預期可能是學生會覺得文法練習容易。"},{"en":"If results partly match the original expectation, the theory may need adjustment, not rejection.","zh":"如果結果部分符合原本預期，理論可能需要調整，而不是被拒絕。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the first prediction.","zh":"這個短語指最初預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"obtain data clearly","meaning":"清楚取得數據","examples":[{"en":"Researchers need clear data before drawing firm conclusions.","zh":"研究者在得出確定結論前需要清楚取得數據。"},{"en":"To obtain data clearly means to collect information in a way that is accurate and easy to interpret.","zh":"清楚取得數據，指以準確且容易解讀的方式收集資料。"},{"en":"A teacher obtains data clearly when every student uses the same survey form.","zh":"當每個學生使用同一份問卷，老師就能較清楚取得數據。"},{"en":"If data are unclear, conclusions may become weak or misleading.","zh":"如果數據不清楚，結論可能變弱或具誤導性。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses reliable collection of evidence.","zh":"這個短語強調可靠地收集證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"somewhat inconclusive","meaning":"有點未能作定論的","examples":[{"en":"The result was somewhat inconclusive because the elephants did not always flee.","zh":"結果有點未能作定論，因為大象並不總是逃走。"},{"en":"Somewhat inconclusive means not fully clear or not strong enough to prove one final answer.","zh":"有點未能作定論，指不完全清楚，或不足以證明一個最終答案。"},{"en":"A class survey with only five responses is somewhat inconclusive.","zh":"只有五個回覆的班級調查有點未能作定論。"},{"en":"If animals react in mixed ways, researchers may need more tests.","zh":"如果動物反應混雜，研究者可能需要更多測試。"},{"en":"The phrase shows partial uncertainty, not total failure.","zh":"這個短語顯示部分不確定，而不是完全失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"inaccurate","meaning":"不準確的","examples":[{"en":"A result may be inaccurate if the data are unclear.","zh":"如果數據不清楚，結果可能不準確。"},{"en":"Inaccurate means not correct or not exact.","zh":"不準確的，指不正確或不精確。"},{"en":"A map is inaccurate if it shows a road that no longer exists.","zh":"如果地圖顯示一條已不存在的道路，它就是不準確的。"},{"en":"If measurements are inaccurate, researchers may draw the wrong conclusion.","zh":"如果量度不準確，研究者可能得出錯誤結論。"},{"en":"The word describes lack of correctness or precision.","zh":"這個詞描述缺乏正確性或精確度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"unfamiliar to the public","meaning":"公眾不熟悉的","examples":[{"en":"The research findings may be unfamiliar to the public.","zh":"這些研究發現可能是公眾不熟悉的。"},{"en":"Unfamiliar to the public means not widely known or understood by ordinary people.","zh":"公眾不熟悉的，指普通人未廣泛知道或理解。"},{"en":"A medical term may be unfamiliar to the public until doctors explain it simply.","zh":"醫學術語可能在醫生簡單解釋前對公眾不熟悉。"},{"en":"If research is unfamiliar to the public, clear examples help people understand why it matters.","zh":"如果研究對公眾陌生，清楚例子有助人們理解它為何重要。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts specialist knowledge with common knowledge.","zh":"這個短語把專業知識與常識作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 57 - Elephant Communication.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 58":[{"front":"texting the television","meaning":"透過短訊與電視節目互動","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the rise of texting the television in Europe.","zh":"文章討論歐洲透過短訊與電視節目互動的興起。"},{"en":"Texting the television means sending text messages to a TV programme to vote, comment, request songs, or join games.","zh":"Texting the television 指向電視節目發送短訊，以投票、評論、點歌或參與遊戲。"},{"en":"A teenager may be texting the television while watching a talent show at home.","zh":"青少年在家觀看才藝節目時，可能透過短訊與電視節目互動。"},{"en":"Texting the television can make viewers feel involved instead of just watching silently.","zh":"透過短訊與電視節目互動可以令觀眾感到參與其中，而不是只是安靜觀看。"},{"en":"This phrase describes television becoming interactive through mobile-phone messages.","zh":"這個片語描述電視透過手提電話短訊變得互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"once upon a time","meaning":"從前；曾幾何時","examples":[{"en":"Once upon a time, TV shows used e-mail addresses to reach young audiences.","zh":"曾幾何時，電視節目使用電郵地址接觸年輕觀眾。"},{"en":"Once upon a time means in the past, often with a slightly story-like or nostalgic feeling.","zh":"Once upon a time 指在過去，常帶有一點故事式或懷舊感覺。"},{"en":"Once upon a time, students had to look up every difficult word in a paper dictionary.","zh":"從前，學生必須在紙本字典中查每個深字。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest that an old habit has now been replaced by something newer.","zh":"這個片語可以暗示舊習慣現在已被更新的事物取代。"},{"en":"In this passage, it contrasts older e-mail contact with newer text-message interaction.","zh":"在這篇文章中，它把較舊的電郵聯絡與較新的短訊互動作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"with any self-respect","meaning":"稍有自尊的；像樣的","examples":[{"en":"A television show with any self-respect wanted to target a young audience.","zh":"稍有自尊的電視節目都想以年輕觀眾為目標。"},{"en":"With any self-respect means if someone or something wants to be seen as proper, serious, or worthy.","zh":"With any self-respect 指如果某人或某事想被視為像樣、認真或值得尊重。"},{"en":"A school with any self-respect should keep its classrooms clean and safe.","zh":"一間像樣的學校應保持課室清潔和安全。"},{"en":"The phrase often sounds slightly humorous or critical because it suggests a basic standard.","zh":"這個片語常帶有少許幽默或批評意味，因為它暗示一個基本標準。"},{"en":"In this context, it means any modern, respectable TV show wanted young viewers.","zh":"在這個語境中，它指任何現代而像樣的電視節目都想吸引年輕觀眾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"target a young audience","meaning":"以年輕觀眾為目標","examples":[{"en":"Television shows used e-mail addresses to target a young audience.","zh":"電視節目使用電郵地址以年輕觀眾為目標。"},{"en":"To target a young audience means to design content or communication for young viewers.","zh":"To target a young audience 指為年輕觀眾設計內容或溝通方式。"},{"en":"A brand may target a young audience by using short videos and social media campaigns.","zh":"品牌可能透過短片和社交媒體宣傳，以年輕觀眾為目標。"},{"en":"If a TV show wants teenagers to watch, it may use music, games, and mobile interaction.","zh":"如果電視節目想吸引青少年觀看，它可能使用音樂、遊戲和手機互動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing a specific age group as the main audience.","zh":"這個片語描述把特定年齡群體選為主要觀眾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"e-mail address","meaning":"電郵地址","examples":[{"en":"TV shows once needed an e-mail address to interact with young viewers.","zh":"電視節目曾經需要電郵地址來與年輕觀眾互動。"},{"en":"An e-mail address is the online address people use to send and receive electronic messages.","zh":"E-mail address 是人們用來發送和接收電子訊息的網上地址。"},{"en":"A student gives an e-mail address to the teacher so homework files can be sent.","zh":"學生把電郵地址給老師，以便接收功課檔案。"},{"en":"If a show lists an e-mail address, viewers can contact the programme after watching.","zh":"如果節目列出電郵地址，觀眾可以觀看後聯絡節目。"},{"en":"In the passage, e-mail addresses represent an older form of audience interaction.","zh":"在文章中，電郵地址代表一種較舊的觀眾互動方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be gradually replaced by","meaning":"逐漸被……取代","examples":[{"en":"E-mail addresses are gradually being replaced by telephone numbers.","zh":"電郵地址正逐漸被電話號碼取代。"},{"en":"To be gradually replaced by something means to be slowly taken over by a newer or different thing.","zh":"To be gradually replaced by something 指慢慢被更新或不同的事物取代。"},{"en":"Paper notices are gradually being replaced by school apps in many schools.","zh":"在許多學校中，紙本通告正逐漸被學校應用程式取代。"},{"en":"If viewers prefer texting, e-mail may slowly become less important for TV interaction.","zh":"如果觀眾較喜歡發短訊，電郵在電視互動中可能慢慢變得較不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a slow change from one method to another.","zh":"這個片語描述由一種方法慢慢轉向另一種方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"so that","meaning":"以便；使得","examples":[{"en":"Shows display telephone numbers so that audiences can text the show.","zh":"節目顯示電話號碼，以便觀眾可以傳短訊給節目。"},{"en":"So that introduces the purpose or intended result of an action.","zh":"So that 用來引出某行動的目的或預期結果。"},{"en":"A teacher writes instructions clearly so that students know exactly what to do.","zh":"老師清楚寫下指示，以便學生確切知道要做甚麼。"},{"en":"If a programme shows a number on screen, viewers can send messages immediately.","zh":"如果節目在螢幕上顯示號碼，觀眾就可以立即發送訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an action with the reason for doing it.","zh":"這個片語把行動與做該行動的原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"text the show","meaning":"傳短訊給節目","examples":[{"en":"Audiences can text the show from their mobile phones.","zh":"觀眾可以用手提電話傳短訊給節目。"},{"en":"To text the show means to send a mobile-phone message to a television programme.","zh":"To text the show 指向電視節目發送手機短訊。"},{"en":"Viewers may text the show to vote for their favourite singer.","zh":"觀眾可能傳短訊給節目，為自己最喜歡的歌手投票。"},{"en":"Texting the show can let producers collect opinions quickly during a live broadcast.","zh":"傳短訊給節目可以讓製作人在直播期間快速收集意見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct audience participation through SMS.","zh":"這個片語描述透過短訊作出的直接觀眾參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mobile phones","meaning":"手提電話","examples":[{"en":"Audiences can interact with television from their mobile phones.","zh":"觀眾可以用手提電話與電視互動。"},{"en":"Mobile phones are portable phones people carry and use for calls, messages, apps, and the internet.","zh":"Mobile phones 是人們隨身攜帶，用作通話、發訊息、使用應用程式和上網的電話。"},{"en":"Students often use mobile phones to check timetables, messages, and homework reminders.","zh":"學生常用手提電話查看時間表、訊息和功課提醒。"},{"en":"Because viewers keep mobile phones nearby, texting a TV show becomes easy.","zh":"因為觀眾把手提電話放在身旁，向電視節目發短訊變得容易。"},{"en":"In this passage, mobile phones are the tool that makes TV interaction simple.","zh":"在這篇文章中，手提電話是令電視互動變得簡單的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"it comes as no surprise that","meaning":"……並不令人意外","examples":[{"en":"It comes as no surprise that texting has surpassed Internet usage.","zh":"短訊已超越互聯網使用量，這並不令人意外。"},{"en":"It comes as no surprise that means something is expected and not shocking.","zh":"It comes as no surprise that 指某事是預期之內，並不令人震驚。"},{"en":"It comes as no surprise that students use phones more than paper diaries for reminders.","zh":"學生使用手機提醒多於紙本手帳，這並不令人意外。"},{"en":"If young people already text constantly, it is unsurprising that TV shows use texting too.","zh":"如果年輕人本來就經常發短訊，電視節目也使用短訊就不令人意外。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a result that seems natural from the situation.","zh":"這個片語引出從情況看來很自然的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據","examples":[{"en":"According to Gartner’s research, texting has recently surpassed Internet usage across Europe.","zh":"根據 Gartner 的研究，短訊最近已在歐洲各地超越互聯網使用量。"},{"en":"According to means based on what a person, report, or organisation says.","zh":"According to 指根據某人、報告或機構所說。"},{"en":"According to the school notice, the exam will begin at nine o’clock.","zh":"根據學校通告，考試將於九時開始。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to show the source of information.","zh":"作者使用這個片語來顯示資訊來源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting research rather than giving personal opinion.","zh":"這個片語適用於報告研究，而不是表達個人意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Gartner’s research","meaning":"Gartner 的研究","examples":[{"en":"Gartner’s research shows that texting is increasingly popular in Europe.","zh":"Gartner 的研究顯示短訊在歐洲越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"Gartner’s research refers to research carried out or reported by the research company Gartner.","zh":"Gartner’s research 指由研究公司 Gartner 進行或發表的研究。"},{"en":"A business may use Gartner’s research to understand how people use new technology.","zh":"企業可能使用 Gartner 的研究來理解人們如何使用新科技。"},{"en":"If research shows texting is rising, TV companies may design more text-based services.","zh":"如果研究顯示短訊使用上升，電視公司可能設計更多短訊服務。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces evidence from a named research source.","zh":"這個片語引出來自具名研究來源的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"surpass Internet usage","meaning":"超越互聯網使用量","examples":[{"en":"Texting has recently surpassed Internet usage across Europe.","zh":"短訊最近已在歐洲各地超越互聯網使用量。"},{"en":"To surpass Internet usage means to become more common or more heavily used than internet use.","zh":"To surpass Internet usage 指變得比互聯網使用更常見或使用量更大。"},{"en":"In one school, messaging apps may surpass e-mail usage among students.","zh":"在某間學校，訊息應用程式使用量可能超越學生的電郵使用量。"},{"en":"If texting surpasses internet use, companies may shift attention to mobile-message services.","zh":"如果短訊超越互聯網使用量，公司可能把注意力轉向手機訊息服務。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two forms of technology use and shows one has become larger.","zh":"這個片語比較兩種科技使用方式，並顯示其中一種已變得更大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"across Europe","meaning":"遍及歐洲","examples":[{"en":"Texting has recently surpassed Internet usage across Europe.","zh":"短訊最近已遍及歐洲超越互聯網使用量。"},{"en":"Across Europe means in many countries or regions throughout Europe.","zh":"Across Europe 指在歐洲許多國家或地區。"},{"en":"A music trend can spread across Europe through television and social media.","zh":"一種音樂潮流可以透過電視和社交媒體遍及歐洲。"},{"en":"If the same behaviour appears across Europe, it is not just a local habit.","zh":"如果同一行為遍及歐洲出現，它就不只是本地習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is geographically widespread.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事在地理上廣泛出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"text messaging","meaning":"短訊；短訊通訊","examples":[{"en":"Text messaging is now used to interact with television.","zh":"短訊現在被用來與電視互動。"},{"en":"Text messaging means sending short written messages through a mobile phone.","zh":"Text messaging 指透過手提電話發送短文字訊息。"},{"en":"Students use text messaging to remind classmates about homework or meeting times.","zh":"學生使用短訊提醒同學功課或集合時間。"},{"en":"Text messaging is quick, so TV shows can collect thousands of responses in a short time.","zh":"短訊很快捷，所以電視節目可以在短時間內收集數以千計回應。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to SMS-style communication, not long e-mails.","zh":"這個片語指短訊式通訊，而不是長電郵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"one of the fastest-growing uses","meaning":"增長最快的用途之一","examples":[{"en":"One of the fastest-growing uses of text messaging is to interact with television.","zh":"短訊增長最快的用途之一是與電視互動。"},{"en":"One of the fastest-growing uses means one purpose that is becoming popular very quickly.","zh":"One of the fastest-growing uses 指正在非常快速變得流行的一種用途。"},{"en":"One of the fastest-growing uses of video calls is online tutoring.","zh":"視像通話增長最快的用途之一是網上補習。"},{"en":"If a use grows quickly, companies may invest more money in it.","zh":"如果某種用途快速增長，公司可能在其中投放更多資金。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a rapidly expanding function of a technology.","zh":"這個片語突出科技中迅速擴展的一項功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"interact with television","meaning":"與電視互動","examples":[{"en":"Many teenagers use text messaging to interact with television.","zh":"許多青少年使用短訊與電視互動。"},{"en":"To interact with television means to respond to or take part in TV content instead of only watching.","zh":"To interact with television 指回應或參與電視內容，而不是只是觀看。"},{"en":"Viewers can interact with television by voting, sending comments, or joining quizzes.","zh":"觀眾可以透過投票、發送評論或參加問答來與電視互動。"},{"en":"Interaction makes television feel more personal because viewers can influence what happens.","zh":"互動令電視感覺更個人化，因為觀眾可以影響發生的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two-way communication between viewers and TV programmes.","zh":"這個片語描述觀眾與電視節目之間的雙向溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"statistics show that","meaning":"統計數字顯示","examples":[{"en":"Gartner’s statistics show that many teenagers have responded to TV programmes by text.","zh":"Gartner 的統計數字顯示許多青少年曾透過短訊回應電視節目。"},{"en":"Statistics show that means numerical data provide evidence for a claim.","zh":"Statistics show that 指數字數據為某主張提供證據。"},{"en":"School statistics may show that attendance improves after later start times.","zh":"學校統計數字可能顯示延遲上課時間後出席率改善。"},{"en":"If statistics show a rise in text voting, broadcasters may treat it as a serious business trend.","zh":"如果統計數字顯示短訊投票上升，廣播機構可能把它視為重要商業趨勢。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces evidence based on numbers.","zh":"這個片語引出基於數字的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"respond to TV programmes","meaning":"回應電視節目","examples":[{"en":"Some teenagers have responded to TV programmes by sending a text message.","zh":"一些青少年曾透過發送短訊回應電視節目。"},{"en":"To respond to TV programmes means to give a reaction, answer, vote, or comment to a show.","zh":"To respond to TV programmes 指對節目作出反應、回答、投票或評論。"},{"en":"A viewer may respond to a news programme by sending an opinion about the topic.","zh":"觀眾可能透過發送對議題的意見來回應新聞節目。"},{"en":"If many viewers respond, producers can see which parts of the programme attract attention.","zh":"如果許多觀眾回應，製作人可以看出節目哪些部分吸引注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes viewers actively reacting to television content.","zh":"這個片語描述觀眾主動回應電視內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"send a text message","meaning":"發送短訊","examples":[{"en":"Viewers can respond to a TV programme by sending a text message.","zh":"觀眾可以透過發送短訊回應電視節目。"},{"en":"To send a text message means to send a short written message from a mobile phone.","zh":"To send a text message 指從手提電話發送短文字訊息。"},{"en":"A parent may send a text message to tell a child that dinner is ready.","zh":"家長可能發送短訊告訴孩子晚餐已準備好。"},{"en":"If a TV number appears on screen, viewers can send a text message immediately.","zh":"如果電視號碼出現在螢幕上，觀眾可以立即發送短訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a quick and simple form of mobile communication.","zh":"這個片語描述一種快捷簡單的手機通訊方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"this phenomenon","meaning":"這種現象","examples":[{"en":"This phenomenon can be largely attributed to the rapid growth of reality TV.","zh":"這種現象很大程度上可歸因於真人騷電視的快速增長。"},{"en":"This phenomenon means the noticeable situation or trend just described.","zh":"This phenomenon 指剛剛描述的顯著情況或趨勢。"},{"en":"If many students suddenly use the same slang, a teacher may ask what caused this phenomenon.","zh":"如果許多學生突然使用同一俚語，老師可能會問這種現象由甚麼造成。"},{"en":"A phenomenon becomes important when it is common enough to affect behaviour or business.","zh":"當一種現象普遍到足以影響行為或商業時，它就變得重要。"},{"en":"In this context, the phenomenon is the rise of texting TV programmes.","zh":"在這個語境中，這種現象是傳短訊給電視節目的興起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be largely attributed to","meaning":"很大程度上歸因於","examples":[{"en":"The popularity of TV-texting can be largely attributed to reality TV shows.","zh":"電視短訊互動的受歡迎程度，很大程度上可歸因於真人騷節目。"},{"en":"To be largely attributed to something means to be mainly explained by that cause.","zh":"To be largely attributed to something 指主要可由某原因解釋。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be largely attributed to regular reading practice.","zh":"學生的進步可能很大程度上歸因於定期閱讀練習。"},{"en":"If reality shows ask viewers to vote, they can help explain why TV-texting grew.","zh":"如果真人騷要求觀眾投票，它們就可以解釋為何電視短訊互動增長。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main cause, while allowing other causes to exist.","zh":"這個片語指出主要原因，同時容許其他原因存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rapid growth","meaning":"快速增長","examples":[{"en":"The rapid growth of reality TV has encouraged TV-texting.","zh":"真人騷電視的快速增長促進了電視短訊互動。"},{"en":"Rapid growth means quick increase in size, number, popularity, or use.","zh":"Rapid growth 指規模、數量、受歡迎程度或使用量快速增加。"},{"en":"A small online shop may experience rapid growth after a popular video recommends it.","zh":"小型網店在熱門影片推薦後，可能經歷快速增長。"},{"en":"When a format grows quickly, related services often grow with it.","zh":"當一種形式快速增長，相關服務通常也會跟着增長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fast expansion over a short period.","zh":"這個片語描述短時間內快速擴展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reality TV shows","meaning":"真人騷節目","examples":[{"en":"Reality TV shows often invite viewers to vote by text message.","zh":"真人騷節目常邀請觀眾透過短訊投票。"},{"en":"Reality TV shows are television programmes based on real people, competitions, or unscripted situations.","zh":"Reality TV shows 是以真實人物、比賽或非劇本情境為基礎的電視節目。"},{"en":"A singing competition where viewers vote for contestants is a kind of reality TV show.","zh":"觀眾為參賽者投票的歌唱比賽就是一種真人騷節目。"},{"en":"Because reality TV depends on audience involvement, texting fits it well.","zh":"因為真人騷依賴觀眾參與，短訊很適合這種節目。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to entertainment programmes that present real-life or competition-based content.","zh":"這個片語指呈現真實生活或比賽內容的娛樂節目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"such as","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"Reality TV shows such as “Big Brother” use text-message voting.","zh":"例如 “Big Brother” 等真人騷節目使用短訊投票。"},{"en":"Such as introduces examples of the thing being discussed.","zh":"Such as 用來引出正在討論事物的例子。"},{"en":"Students need stationery such as pens, notebooks, and folders.","zh":"學生需要筆、筆記簿和文件夾等文具。"},{"en":"When a writer says “such as”, the examples clarify the category.","zh":"當作者說 “such as”，例子會令類別更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers understand a general idea through specific cases.","zh":"這個片語透過具體個案幫助讀者理解一般概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"viewers get to decide","meaning":"觀眾可以決定","examples":[{"en":"In some reality shows, viewers get to decide the result through voting.","zh":"在一些真人騷中，觀眾可以透過投票決定結果。"},{"en":"Viewers get to decide means the audience is allowed to choose or influence the outcome.","zh":"Viewers get to decide 指觀眾被允許選擇或影響結果。"},{"en":"In a school talent show, students may get to decide the winner by voting online.","zh":"在學校才藝表演中，學生可能可以透過網上投票決定勝出者。"},{"en":"If viewers decide the result, they feel more involved in the programme.","zh":"如果觀眾決定結果，他們會感到更投入節目。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights audience power rather than passive watching.","zh":"這個片語突出觀眾權力，而不是被動觀看。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the result through voting","meaning":"透過投票決定結果","examples":[{"en":"Viewers can influence the result through voting.","zh":"觀眾可以透過投票影響結果。"},{"en":"The result through voting means the final outcome is decided by votes.","zh":"The result through voting 指最終結果由票數決定。"},{"en":"A class may choose its monitor through voting instead of letting the teacher decide.","zh":"一個班可以透過投票選班長，而不是由老師決定。"},{"en":"If thousands of viewers vote, the programme result can change quickly.","zh":"如果數以千計觀眾投票，節目結果可以迅速改變。"},{"en":"This phrase links voting with the final decision.","zh":"這個片語把投票與最終決定連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the majority of","meaning":"大部分的","examples":[{"en":"The majority of reality shows are now open to text-message voting.","zh":"大部分真人騷現在都開放予短訊投票。"},{"en":"The majority of means more than half of a group.","zh":"The majority of 指某群體中超過一半。"},{"en":"The majority of students may prefer online reminders to paper notices.","zh":"大部分學生可能較喜歡網上提醒，而不是紙本通告。"},{"en":"If the majority of shows allow texting, text voting has become normal rather than unusual.","zh":"如果大部分節目容許發短訊，短訊投票就已變得正常而不罕見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the larger part of a group.","zh":"這個片語描述某群體中的較大部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be open to","meaning":"開放予……","examples":[{"en":"Most reality shows are now open to text-message voting.","zh":"大多數真人騷現在都開放予短訊投票。"},{"en":"To be open to something means to allow or accept it.","zh":"To be open to something 指容許或接受某事。"},{"en":"A school club may be open to students from all forms.","zh":"學校學會可能開放予所有年級學生。"},{"en":"If a programme is open to text voting, viewers can take part through their phones.","zh":"如果節目開放予短訊投票，觀眾就可以透過手機參與。"},{"en":"This phrase describes access, permission, or willingness to accept participation.","zh":"這個片語描述准入、許可或願意接受參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"text-message voting","meaning":"短訊投票","examples":[{"en":"Text-message voting has become common in reality TV shows.","zh":"短訊投票在真人騷節目中已變得常見。"},{"en":"Text-message voting means voting by sending a mobile-phone text message.","zh":"Text-message voting 指透過發送手機短訊來投票。"},{"en":"Viewers may use text-message voting to choose which contestant stays in a competition.","zh":"觀眾可能使用短訊投票來選擇哪位參賽者留在比賽中。"},{"en":"Because every vote is charged, text-message voting can create revenue for TV companies.","zh":"因為每張票都收費，短訊投票可以為電視公司創造收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple voting system based on SMS.","zh":"這個片語描述以短訊為基礎的簡單投票系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the latest series of","meaning":"最新一輯","examples":[{"en":"The latest series of Norway’s “Big Brother” collected most votes by text.","zh":"挪威 “Big Brother” 最新一輯透過短訊收集了大部分投票。"},{"en":"The latest series of a programme means its most recent season or set of episodes.","zh":"The latest series of a programme 指某節目最近的一季或一組集數。"},{"en":"Fans may discuss the latest series of a drama as soon as new episodes are released.","zh":"新集數推出後，粉絲可能立即討論一套劇的最新一輯。"},{"en":"If the latest series uses texting, it shows the programme has adopted newer interaction methods.","zh":"如果最新一輯使用短訊，它顯示節目已採用更新的互動方式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the newest instalment of a TV show.","zh":"這個片語指電視節目的最新一季。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be collected in this manner","meaning":"以這種方式收集","examples":[{"en":"Most votes were collected in this manner.","zh":"大部分投票都是以這種方式收集。"},{"en":"To be collected in this manner means to be gathered in the way just described.","zh":"To be collected in this manner 指以剛剛描述的方式收集。"},{"en":"Survey answers can be collected in this manner if students submit them through an app.","zh":"如果學生透過應用程式提交問卷答案，答案就可以以這種方式收集。"},{"en":"If votes are collected by text, counting can be faster and more automatic.","zh":"如果投票透過短訊收集，點票可以更快和更自動化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a method already mentioned.","zh":"這個片語回指已提及的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not just about","meaning":"不只是關於","examples":[{"en":"TV-texting is not just about voting.","zh":"電視短訊互動不只是關於投票。"},{"en":"Not just about means not limited to one purpose or idea.","zh":"Not just about 指不限於一個目的或想法。"},{"en":"School is not just about exams; it is also about friendship, confidence, and habits.","zh":"學校不只是關於考試；它也關乎友誼、自信和習慣。"},{"en":"If TV-texting includes games, comments, and requests, it is broader than voting alone.","zh":"如果電視短訊互動包括遊戲、評論和點播，它就比單純投票更廣。"},{"en":"This phrase expands the reader’s understanding of a topic.","zh":"這個片語擴闊讀者對某題目的理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"encourage viewers to","meaning":"鼓勵觀眾去","examples":[{"en":"News shows encourage viewers to comment by text message.","zh":"新聞節目鼓勵觀眾透過短訊發表評論。"},{"en":"To encourage viewers to do something means to invite or motivate the audience to take action.","zh":"To encourage viewers to do something 指邀請或推動觀眾採取行動。"},{"en":"A cooking show may encourage viewers to try a simple recipe at home.","zh":"烹飪節目可能鼓勵觀眾在家嘗試簡單食譜。"},{"en":"If news programmes ask for comments, viewers may feel their opinions matter.","zh":"如果新聞節目徵求評論，觀眾可能覺得自己的意見重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes prompting the audience to participate.","zh":"這個片語描述促使觀眾參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"comment by texting messages","meaning":"透過發短訊發表評論","examples":[{"en":"Viewers can comment by texting messages to news shows.","zh":"觀眾可以透過發短訊給新聞節目來發表評論。"},{"en":"To comment by texting messages means to give an opinion through mobile-phone texts.","zh":"To comment by texting messages 指透過手機短訊給出意見。"},{"en":"A viewer may comment by texting a short reaction after a public debate.","zh":"觀眾可能在公開辯論後透過發短訊作出簡短反應。"},{"en":"When many people comment by text, a programme can display public opinion quickly.","zh":"當許多人透過短訊評論，節目可以快速顯示公眾意見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sending opinions through text messages.","zh":"這個片語描述透過短訊發送意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"enable the audience to","meaning":"使觀眾能夠","examples":[{"en":"Game shows enable the audience to be part of the competition.","zh":"遊戲節目使觀眾能夠成為比賽的一部分。"},{"en":"To enable the audience to do something means to make it possible for viewers to do it.","zh":"To enable the audience to do something 指使觀眾能夠做某事。"},{"en":"A school app can enable parents to check notices immediately.","zh":"學校應用程式可以讓家長立即查看通告。"},{"en":"If texting enables viewers to play along, a programme becomes more interactive.","zh":"如果短訊使觀眾能夠一同參與，節目就變得更互動。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on making an action possible.","zh":"這個片語集中於令某行動成為可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be part of the competition","meaning":"成為比賽的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Game shows allow viewers to be part of the competition.","zh":"遊戲節目讓觀眾成為比賽的一部分。"},{"en":"To be part of the competition means to join or influence the contest rather than only watch it.","zh":"To be part of the competition 指加入或影響比賽，而不是只是觀看。"},{"en":"Students can be part of a competition by answering questions live from their phones.","zh":"學生可以透過手機即時回答問題，成為比賽的一部分。"},{"en":"If viewers can affect scores or results, they feel more involved in the show.","zh":"如果觀眾可以影響分數或結果，他們會更投入節目。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active participation in a contest.","zh":"這個片語描述在比賽中的主動參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"answer requests","meaning":"回應點播要求","examples":[{"en":"Music shows answer requests by taking text messages.","zh":"音樂節目透過接收短訊回應點播要求。"},{"en":"To answer requests means to respond to what people ask for.","zh":"To answer requests 指回應人們所要求的事情。"},{"en":"A teacher may answer requests for extra revision by giving students more practice questions.","zh":"老師可能透過給學生更多練習題，回應額外溫習的要求。"},{"en":"If a music programme answers song requests, viewers feel the show listens to them.","zh":"如果音樂節目回應點歌要求，觀眾會覺得節目有聆聽他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes responding to audience demands or wishes.","zh":"這個片語描述回應觀眾需求或願望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take text messages","meaning":"接收短訊","examples":[{"en":"Music shows take text messages from viewers.","zh":"音樂節目接收觀眾短訊。"},{"en":"To take text messages means to receive and use messages sent by phone.","zh":"To take text messages 指接收並使用由電話發出的訊息。"},{"en":"A radio station may take text messages from listeners during a live discussion.","zh":"電台在直播討論期間可能接收聽眾短訊。"},{"en":"If a show takes messages, producers can choose comments or requests to display.","zh":"如果節目接收短訊，製作人可以選擇評論或點播內容展示。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a programme accepting SMS input from the audience.","zh":"這個片語描述節目接受觀眾的短訊輸入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"broadcasters","meaning":"廣播機構；電視台","examples":[{"en":"Broadcasters set up on-screen chatrooms.","zh":"廣播機構設立螢幕聊天室。"},{"en":"Broadcasters are television or radio companies that send programmes to the public.","zh":"Broadcasters 是向公眾播放節目的電視或電台公司。"},{"en":"Broadcasters may change their schedules when there is breaking news.","zh":"當有突發新聞，廣播機構可能改變節目時間表。"},{"en":"If broadcasters create interactive services, viewers can respond more directly.","zh":"如果廣播機構創造互動服務，觀眾可以更直接回應。"},{"en":"This word refers to organisations that produce or transmit programmes.","zh":"這個詞指製作或傳送節目的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"set up on-screen chatrooms","meaning":"設立螢幕聊天室","examples":[{"en":"Broadcasters set up on-screen chatrooms for viewers.","zh":"廣播機構為觀眾設立螢幕聊天室。"},{"en":"To set up on-screen chatrooms means to create spaces on the TV screen where viewers’ messages appear.","zh":"To set up on-screen chatrooms 指在電視螢幕上建立顯示觀眾訊息的空間。"},{"en":"A music channel may set up an on-screen chatroom during a live concert.","zh":"音樂頻道可能在直播演唱會期間設立螢幕聊天室。"},{"en":"If viewers see their messages on screen, they may feel part of a shared community.","zh":"如果觀眾在螢幕上看見自己的訊息，他們可能感到自己屬於一個共同社群。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using the television screen as a public message space.","zh":"這個片語描述把電視螢幕用作公共訊息空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"tend to","meaning":"往往；傾向於","examples":[{"en":"TV audiences tend to sit on the sofa with their mobile phones nearby.","zh":"電視觀眾往往坐在梳化上，手提電話就在附近。"},{"en":"Tend to means usually or often behave in a particular way.","zh":"Tend to 指通常或常以某種方式行事。"},{"en":"Students tend to remember examples better than abstract definitions.","zh":"學生往往比抽象定義更容易記住例子。"},{"en":"If viewers tend to keep phones nearby, texting a show becomes convenient.","zh":"如果觀眾傾向於把手機放在附近，傳短訊給節目就變得方便。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common habit, not an absolute rule.","zh":"這個片語描述常見習慣，而不是絕對規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"right by their sides","meaning":"就在身旁","examples":[{"en":"Viewers often keep their mobile phones right by their sides.","zh":"觀眾常把手提電話放在自己身旁。"},{"en":"Right by their sides means very close to them and easy to reach.","zh":"Right by their sides 指非常接近他們，而且容易拿到。"},{"en":"A student may keep a water bottle right by their side during revision.","zh":"學生溫習時可能把水樽放在身旁。"},{"en":"If phones are right beside viewers, sending a message takes only a few seconds.","zh":"如果手機就在觀眾旁邊，發送訊息只需幾秒。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses physical closeness and convenience.","zh":"這個片語強調實際距離近和方便。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a natural way to interact","meaning":"自然的互動方式","examples":[{"en":"Texting is a natural way to interact with television.","zh":"發短訊是與電視互動的自然方式。"},{"en":"A natural way to interact means an easy, familiar, and comfortable method of participation.","zh":"Natural way to interact 指一種容易、熟悉而舒服的參與方法。"},{"en":"Asking questions is a natural way to interact with a teacher during a lesson.","zh":"在課堂中提問是與老師互動的自然方式。"},{"en":"Since people already text daily, using texts for TV feels simple.","zh":"既然人們本來每天都發短訊，用短訊參與電視節目就感覺簡單。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a method that fits people’s existing habits.","zh":"這個片語描述符合人們現有習慣的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mobile service providers","meaning":"流動通訊服務供應商","examples":[{"en":"Mobile service providers charge premium rates for certain messages.","zh":"流動通訊服務供應商對某些訊息收取較高收費。"},{"en":"Mobile service providers are companies that provide phone networks, calls, data, and messaging services.","zh":"Mobile service providers 是提供電話網絡、通話、數據和短訊服務的公司。"},{"en":"A mobile service provider may offer students cheaper data plans.","zh":"流動通訊服務供應商可能為學生提供較便宜數據計劃。"},{"en":"If viewers send paid texts, mobile service providers may earn part of the revenue.","zh":"如果觀眾發送付費短訊，流動通訊服務供應商可能賺取部分收入。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to telecom companies, not TV producers.","zh":"這個片語指電訊公司，而不是電視製作人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"charge premium rates","meaning":"收取較高收費","examples":[{"en":"Providers charge premium rates for messages sent to certain numbers.","zh":"服務供應商對發送至某些號碼的訊息收取較高收費。"},{"en":"To charge premium rates means to ask users to pay higher-than-normal prices.","zh":"To charge premium rates 指要求使用者支付高於正常水平的價格。"},{"en":"A hotline may charge premium rates if each call costs more than an ordinary call.","zh":"如果熱線每次通話都比普通通話貴，它可能收取較高收費。"},{"en":"If TV voting texts cost extra, the service can generate large income.","zh":"如果電視投票短訊額外收費，服務就可以產生大量收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes special higher pricing for a service.","zh":"這個片語描述服務的特別較高定價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"certain numbers","meaning":"某些號碼","examples":[{"en":"Messages to certain numbers may cost more.","zh":"發送至某些號碼的訊息可能費用較高。"},{"en":"Certain numbers means specific phone numbers used for particular services.","zh":"Certain numbers 指用於特定服務的指定電話號碼。"},{"en":"A charity may ask people to text certain numbers to donate money.","zh":"慈善機構可能要求人們發短訊到某些號碼來捐款。"},{"en":"If certain numbers have premium charges, viewers should know the cost before texting.","zh":"如果某些號碼有高額收費，觀眾發短訊前應知道費用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to selected numbers, not all phone numbers.","zh":"這個片語指指定號碼，而不是所有電話號碼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bring in a lot of cash","meaning":"帶來大量收入","examples":[{"en":"TV-texting can bring in a lot of cash.","zh":"電視短訊互動可以帶來大量收入。"},{"en":"To bring in a lot of cash means to generate a large amount of money.","zh":"To bring in a lot of cash 指產生大量金錢。"},{"en":"A school fair can bring in a lot of cash if many parents buy food and games.","zh":"如果許多家長購買食物和遊戲券，學校嘉年華可以帶來大量收入。"},{"en":"If every text message costs money, millions of messages can create large profits.","zh":"如果每條短訊都收費，數百萬條短訊可以創造龐大利潤。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and focuses on earning money.","zh":"這個片語較口語，重點在賺錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take something as an example","meaning":"以……為例","examples":[{"en":"Take the latest British series of “Big Brother” as an example.","zh":"以最新一輯英國 “Big Brother” 為例。"},{"en":"To take something as an example means to use it to illustrate a wider point.","zh":"To take something as an example 指用某事來說明更廣泛的重點。"},{"en":"Take a school canteen as an example: small price changes can affect many students.","zh":"以學校飯堂為例：小幅價格變動可以影響許多學生。"},{"en":"Writers use examples to make general claims easier to understand.","zh":"作者使用例子令一般主張更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that a concrete case will support the argument.","zh":"這個片語表示即將用具體例子支持論點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"generate text-message votes","meaning":"產生短訊投票","examples":[{"en":"The latest British series of “Big Brother” generated millions of text-message votes.","zh":"最新一輯英國 “Big Brother” 產生了數百萬張短訊投票。"},{"en":"To generate text-message votes means to produce or attract votes sent by SMS.","zh":"To generate text-message votes 指產生或吸引透過短訊發送的投票。"},{"en":"A popular singing show can generate thousands of text-message votes in one evening.","zh":"一個受歡迎的歌唱節目可以在一晚產生數以千計短訊投票。"},{"en":"More votes can mean more audience engagement and more income for the programme.","zh":"更多投票可以意味着更多觀眾參與和更多節目收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both participation and revenue potential.","zh":"這個片語同時描述參與和收入潛力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in profit","meaning":"利潤達","examples":[{"en":"The show generated £1.35 million in profit.","zh":"該節目利潤達一百三十五萬英鎊。"},{"en":"In profit means earning more money than the costs involved.","zh":"In profit 指賺取的錢多於相關成本。"},{"en":"A school charity stall is in profit if it spends $500 on materials and earns $1,200.","zh":"如果學校慈善攤位花五百元買材料但賺一千二百元，它就是有利潤。"},{"en":"If text-message revenue is higher than operating costs, the programme makes a profit.","zh":"如果短訊收入高於營運成本，節目就有利潤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes financial gain after expenses are considered.","zh":"這個片語描述扣除開支後的財務收益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rival videos","meaning":"互相競爭的影片","examples":[{"en":"MTV’s “Videoclash” asks viewers to vote for one of two rival videos.","zh":"MTV 的 “Videoclash” 要求觀眾為兩段互相競爭的影片之一投票。"},{"en":"Rival videos are videos competing against each other for votes or attention.","zh":"Rival videos 是為票數或注意力互相競爭的影片。"},{"en":"A music class may compare two rival videos and vote for the stronger performance.","zh":"音樂課可能比較兩段互相競爭的影片，並投票選出較強表演。"},{"en":"Rival videos create competition, which encourages viewers to choose a side.","zh":"互相競爭的影片製造競爭，鼓勵觀眾選邊站。"},{"en":"This phrase describes competing video choices in an interactive format.","zh":"這個片語描述互動形式中競爭的影片選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"attract up to","meaning":"吸引多達","examples":[{"en":"The programme attracts up to 40,000 texts per hour.","zh":"該節目每小時吸引多達四萬條短訊。"},{"en":"To attract up to a number means to receive as many as that number, though not always.","zh":"To attract up to a number 指接收多達某數量，但不一定每次都達到。"},{"en":"A popular school event may attract up to 500 visitors in one afternoon.","zh":"受歡迎的學校活動可能在一個下午吸引多達五百名訪客。"},{"en":"If a show attracts up to 40,000 texts per hour, its audience is highly engaged.","zh":"如果節目每小時吸引多達四萬條短訊，其觀眾參與度很高。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a maximum possible figure.","zh":"這個片語給出可能的最高數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"texts per hour","meaning":"每小時短訊數量","examples":[{"en":"The show can receive thousands of texts per hour.","zh":"該節目每小時可以收到數以千計短訊。"},{"en":"Texts per hour means the number of text messages received in one hour.","zh":"Texts per hour 指一小時內收到的短訊數量。"},{"en":"A live charity campaign may receive hundreds of texts per hour from donors.","zh":"直播慈善活動可能每小時收到數百條捐款者短訊。"},{"en":"A high number of texts per hour shows fast audience response.","zh":"每小時短訊數量高顯示觀眾反應快速。"},{"en":"This phrase measures the speed and volume of message traffic.","zh":"這個片語量度訊息流量的速度和數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"according to a consultancy","meaning":"根據一間顧問公司的資料","examples":[{"en":"Each text costs €0.30, according to a consultancy based in Amsterdam.","zh":"根據一間位於阿姆斯特丹的顧問公司的資料，每條短訊收費 €0.30。"},{"en":"According to a consultancy means based on information from a professional advisory company.","zh":"According to a consultancy 指根據專業顧問公司的資料。"},{"en":"According to a consultancy, small shops lose customers when delivery is too slow.","zh":"根據一間顧問公司的資料，送貨太慢時，小店會流失顧客。"},{"en":"Companies may cite a consultancy when they want business data to sound more reliable.","zh":"公司想令商業數據聽起來更可靠時，可能引用顧問公司。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces information from an expert business source.","zh":"這個片語引出來自專業商業來源的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be based in","meaning":"以……為基地","examples":[{"en":"The consultancy is based in Amsterdam.","zh":"該顧問公司以阿姆斯特丹為基地。"},{"en":"To be based in a place means to have the main office or main operations there.","zh":"To be based in a place 指總部或主要營運地點設於某地。"},{"en":"A language school based in Hong Kong may teach students online around the world.","zh":"一間以香港為基地的語言學校可能向全球學生提供網上課程。"},{"en":"If a company is based in Amsterdam, that city is its main operating location.","zh":"如果一間公司以阿姆斯特丹為基地，該城市就是其主要營運地點。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where an organisation mainly works from.","zh":"這個片語指出組織主要在哪裏運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"an eight-round texting match","meaning":"八回合短訊比賽","examples":[{"en":"The quiz show had an eight-round texting match on the side.","zh":"該問答節目附帶一場八回合短訊比賽。"},{"en":"An eight-round texting match is a mobile-message competition with eight stages or rounds.","zh":"Eight-round texting match 是有八個階段或回合的手機短訊比賽。"},{"en":"A school quiz could include an eight-round texting match where students send answers by phone.","zh":"學校問答比賽可以包括一場八回合短訊比賽，讓學生用電話發送答案。"},{"en":"More rounds can keep participants engaged for longer.","zh":"更多回合可以令參加者保持投入更久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a structured SMS-based contest.","zh":"這個片語描述一種有結構的短訊比賽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"on the side","meaning":"附帶地；作為附加活動","examples":[{"en":"The quiz show had a texting match on the side.","zh":"該問答節目附帶一場短訊比賽。"},{"en":"On the side means as an extra activity in addition to the main one.","zh":"On the side 指作為主要活動以外的額外活動。"},{"en":"A teacher may run a vocabulary game on the side while students prepare for a debate.","zh":"老師可能在學生準備辯論時，附帶進行詞彙遊戲。"},{"en":"Extra side activities can make the main event more interesting.","zh":"額外附帶活動可以令主要活動更有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something additional, not the central activity.","zh":"這個片語描述額外事物，而不是核心活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bring in participants","meaning":"吸引參加者","examples":[{"en":"The texting match brought in 110,000 participants in one month.","zh":"該短訊比賽在一個月內吸引了十一萬名參加者。"},{"en":"To bring in participants means to attract people to join an activity.","zh":"To bring in participants 指吸引人參與某活動。"},{"en":"A school competition may bring in participants by offering simple online entry.","zh":"學校比賽可能透過簡單網上報名吸引參加者。"},{"en":"If a game is easy to join by phone, it can attract large numbers quickly.","zh":"如果遊戲容易透過電話參加，它可以快速吸引大量人士。"},{"en":"This phrase describes successful recruitment or audience participation.","zh":"這個片語描述成功招募或觀眾參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cryptic-crossword clue","meaning":"隱晦填字遊戲線索","examples":[{"en":"A cryptic-crossword clue invites viewers to send answers by text.","zh":"隱晦填字遊戲線索邀請觀眾透過短訊發送答案。"},{"en":"A cryptic-crossword clue is a puzzle clue that uses wordplay rather than a direct definition.","zh":"Cryptic-crossword clue 是使用文字遊戲，而不是直接定義的謎題線索。"},{"en":"A newspaper may print a cryptic-crossword clue that makes readers think about hidden meanings.","zh":"報紙可能刊登隱晦填字遊戲線索，令讀者思考隱藏意思。"},{"en":"Because the clue is difficult, viewers may feel challenged and want to participate.","zh":"因為線索困難，觀眾可能感到有挑戰並想參與。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clever puzzle clue used to invite audience responses.","zh":"這個片語描述用來邀請觀眾回應的巧妙謎題線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"invite the audience to","meaning":"邀請觀眾去","examples":[{"en":"The clue invites the audience to send their answers by text.","zh":"該線索邀請觀眾透過短訊發送答案。"},{"en":"To invite the audience to do something means to ask or encourage viewers to participate.","zh":"To invite the audience to do something 指要求或鼓勵觀眾參與。"},{"en":"A presenter may invite the audience to ask questions at the end of a talk.","zh":"主持人可能在演講結束時邀請觀眾提問。"},{"en":"If viewers are invited to send answers, they become active participants.","zh":"如果觀眾被邀請發送答案，他們就成為主動參與者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a direct call for audience action.","zh":"這個片語描述對觀眾行動的直接呼籲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at a cost of","meaning":"費用為","examples":[{"en":"Viewers send their answers by text at a cost of €1.","zh":"觀眾以短訊發送答案，費用為 €1。"},{"en":"At a cost of means with a price of a particular amount.","zh":"At a cost of 指價格為某個金額。"},{"en":"Students can join the workshop at a cost of $50.","zh":"學生可以參加工作坊，費用為五十元。"},{"en":"If each message is sent at a cost of €1, participation can create income quickly.","zh":"如果每條訊息費用為 €1，參與可以快速創造收入。"},{"en":"This phrase states the price someone must pay.","zh":"這個片語說明某人必須支付的價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be entered into the draw","meaning":"被納入抽獎","examples":[{"en":"Viewers can be entered into the draw to win a prize.","zh":"觀眾可以被納入抽獎，以贏取獎品。"},{"en":"To be entered into the draw means to be included in a lottery-style selection for a prize.","zh":"To be entered into the draw 指被加入抽獎式獎品選拔中。"},{"en":"Students who submit a survey may be entered into a draw for book coupons.","zh":"提交問卷的學生可能被納入書券抽獎。"},{"en":"A prize draw can encourage more people to send responses.","zh":"抽獎可以鼓勵更多人發送回應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being included in a chance-based prize selection.","zh":"這個片語描述被包括在隨機獎品選拔中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"win a prize","meaning":"贏取獎品","examples":[{"en":"Viewers can enter the draw to win a €300 prize.","zh":"觀眾可以參加抽獎，贏取 €300 獎品。"},{"en":"To win a prize means to receive a reward after a competition, game, or draw.","zh":"To win a prize 指在比賽、遊戲或抽獎後獲得獎勵。"},{"en":"A student may win a prize for writing the best story in class.","zh":"學生可能因寫出班上最佳故事而贏取獎品。"},{"en":"Prizes can motivate people to participate even when the task is simple.","zh":"獎品可以推動人們參與，即使任務很簡單。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving a reward for luck, skill, or participation.","zh":"這個片語描述因運氣、技巧或參與而獲得獎勵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"participate within one day","meaning":"在一天內參與","examples":[{"en":"Normally, thousands of viewers participate within one day.","zh":"通常，數以千計觀眾會在一天內參與。"},{"en":"To participate within one day means to join during a single day-long period.","zh":"To participate within one day 指在一天時間內加入參與。"},{"en":"Thousands of students may participate within one day if a school survey is sent by phone.","zh":"如果學校問卷透過電話發送，數以千計學生可能在一天內參與。"},{"en":"Easy mobile access can make participation very fast.","zh":"方便的手機渠道可以令參與非常快速。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses how quickly many people join.","zh":"這個片語強調許多人參與得有多快。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at the moment","meaning":"目前","examples":[{"en":"At the moment, TV-related text messaging is an important source of revenue.","zh":"目前，與電視相關的短訊是重要收入來源。"},{"en":"At the moment means right now or at the present time.","zh":"At the moment 指現在或目前。"},{"en":"At the moment, many students use messaging apps more than e-mail.","zh":"目前，許多學生使用訊息應用程式多於電郵。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe a current situation that may change later.","zh":"這個片語可以描述之後可能改變的現時情況。"},{"en":"In this passage, it introduces the present business importance of TV-texting.","zh":"在這篇文章中，它引出電視短訊互動目前的商業重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"TV-related text messaging","meaning":"與電視相關的短訊","examples":[{"en":"TV-related text messaging generates major data revenues.","zh":"與電視相關的短訊產生主要數據收入。"},{"en":"TV-related text messaging means text messages sent in connection with television programmes.","zh":"TV-related text messaging 指與電視節目有關而發送的短訊。"},{"en":"Voting for a contestant by SMS is a form of TV-related text messaging.","zh":"透過短訊為參賽者投票，就是一種與電視相關的短訊。"},{"en":"Because these messages are often charged, they can become a revenue source.","zh":"因為這些訊息通常收費，它們可以成為收入來源。"},{"en":"This phrase links mobile messaging with television business.","zh":"這個片語把手機短訊與電視業務連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"account for","meaning":"佔","examples":[{"en":"TV-related text messaging accounts for a considerable proportion of data revenues.","zh":"與電視相關的短訊佔數據收入相當大的比例。"},{"en":"To account for means to make up or represent a particular share of something.","zh":"To account for 指構成或代表某事物的一定份額。"},{"en":"Homework may account for 30% of a student’s final grade.","zh":"功課可能佔學生最終成績百分之三十。"},{"en":"If text messaging accounts for much revenue, companies will protect and expand it.","zh":"如果短訊佔很多收入，公司會保護並擴展它。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used with percentages, shares, and business figures.","zh":"這個片語常與百分比、份額和商業數字一起使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a considerable proportion of","meaning":"相當大的比例","examples":[{"en":"Text messaging accounts for a considerable proportion of providers’ data revenues.","zh":"短訊佔服務供應商數據收入相當大的比例。"},{"en":"A considerable proportion of something means a large or important part of it.","zh":"A considerable proportion of something 指某事物中一個很大或重要的部分。"},{"en":"A considerable proportion of a family’s budget may go to rent.","zh":"家庭預算中相當大的比例可能用於租金。"},{"en":"If a service creates a considerable proportion of revenue, it becomes strategically important.","zh":"如果某服務創造相當大比例收入，它就變得具有策略重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a share that is too large to ignore.","zh":"這個片語描述大到不能忽視的份額。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"data revenues","meaning":"數據收入","examples":[{"en":"TV-related text messaging contributes to mobile providers’ data revenues.","zh":"與電視相關的短訊為流動通訊服務供應商的數據收入作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Data revenues are income earned from digital services such as messaging, internet access, and mobile data.","zh":"Data revenues 是從短訊、互聯網接入和流動數據等數碼服務賺取的收入。"},{"en":"A phone company’s data revenues may rise when more users watch videos online.","zh":"當更多用戶在網上觀看影片，電話公司的數據收入可能上升。"},{"en":"If texting creates data revenue, mobile providers benefit from TV interaction.","zh":"如果短訊創造數據收入，流動通訊服務供應商就能從電視互動中受益。"},{"en":"This phrase describes money earned from non-voice mobile services.","zh":"這個片語描述從非語音流動服務中賺取的金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"unexpectedly strong results","meaning":"出乎意料地強勁的業績","examples":[{"en":"mmO2 reported unexpectedly strong results in July.","zh":"mmO2 在七月公布出乎意料地強勁的業績。"},{"en":"Unexpectedly strong results are business outcomes that are better than people expected.","zh":"Unexpectedly strong results 是比人們預期更好的商業成果。"},{"en":"A shop may report unexpectedly strong results after a simple online campaign.","zh":"小店在簡單網上宣傳後，可能公布出乎意料地強勁的業績。"},{"en":"If text traffic is very high, a mobile operator’s financial results may improve suddenly.","zh":"如果短訊流量非常高，流動營運商的財務業績可能突然改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes surprising business success.","zh":"這個片語描述令人驚訝的商業成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be attributed to","meaning":"歸因於","examples":[{"en":"The strong results could be attributed to the massive volume of text traffic.","zh":"強勁業績可歸因於大量短訊流量。"},{"en":"To be attributed to something means to be explained as being caused by it.","zh":"To be attributed to something 指被解釋為由某事造成。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be attributed to daily reading and feedback.","zh":"學生進步可能歸因於每天閱讀和回饋。"},{"en":"If profits rise after a popular TV event, the increase may be attributed to message revenue.","zh":"如果熱門電視活動後利潤上升，增長可能歸因於訊息收入。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a cause behind a result.","zh":"這個片語指出結果背後的成因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"massive volume of","meaning":"大量的","examples":[{"en":"“Big Brother” created a massive volume of text traffic.","zh":"“Big Brother” 產生了大量短訊流量。"},{"en":"A massive volume of something means a very large amount of it.","zh":"Massive volume of something 指某事物的數量非常大。"},{"en":"A school may receive a massive volume of applications after winning a public award.","zh":"學校獲得公開獎項後，可能收到大量申請。"},{"en":"If a programme creates a massive volume of texts, networks must process them quickly.","zh":"如果節目產生大量短訊，網絡必須快速處理。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses quantity on a very large scale.","zh":"這個片語強調非常大規模的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"text traffic","meaning":"短訊流量","examples":[{"en":"The programme created heavy text traffic for the operator.","zh":"該節目為營運商創造了大量短訊流量。"},{"en":"Text traffic means the flow or volume of text messages moving through a network.","zh":"Text traffic 指通過網絡流動的短訊流量或數量。"},{"en":"During a live final, text traffic may rise sharply as viewers vote.","zh":"在直播決賽期間，隨着觀眾投票，短訊流量可能急升。"},{"en":"Heavy text traffic can create revenue but also requires reliable technology.","zh":"大量短訊流量可以創造收入，但也需要可靠技術。"},{"en":"This phrase treats messages like traffic moving through a system.","zh":"這個片語把訊息視為通過系統的交通流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"revenue from","meaning":"來自……的收入","examples":[{"en":"Providers usually receive part of the revenue from each text.","zh":"服務供應商通常獲得每條短訊帶來的部分收入。"},{"en":"Revenue from something is money earned because of that activity or source.","zh":"Revenue from something 是因某活動或來源而賺取的金錢。"},{"en":"A school fair may use revenue from ticket sales to buy library books.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能使用來自門票銷售的收入購買圖書館書籍。"},{"en":"If each text creates revenue, all partners may want a share of it.","zh":"如果每條短訊都創造收入，所有合作方都可能想分一杯羹。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where money comes from.","zh":"這個片語指出金錢來自哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the rest is divided among","meaning":"餘額由……分配","examples":[{"en":"The rest is divided among the broadcaster, producer, and technology supplier.","zh":"餘額由廣播機構、製作人和技術供應商分配。"},{"en":"The rest is divided among means the remaining part is shared between several people or groups.","zh":"The rest is divided among 指剩餘部分由幾個人或群體分享。"},{"en":"After rent is paid, the rest of the budget may be divided among food, transport, and savings.","zh":"交租後，預算餘額可能分配給食物、交通和儲蓄。"},{"en":"If revenue is divided among many partners, each partner receives only a share.","zh":"如果收入由許多合作方分配，每一方只收到一份。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a remaining amount is shared.","zh":"這個片語描述剩餘數額如何被分享。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"programme producer","meaning":"節目製作人；節目製作公司","examples":[{"en":"The programme producer receives part of the revenue.","zh":"節目製作人獲得部分收入。"},{"en":"A programme producer is a person or company responsible for creating and managing a TV programme.","zh":"Programme producer 是負責創作和管理電視節目的人或公司。"},{"en":"A producer may choose guests, plan episodes, and control the budget.","zh":"製作人可能選擇嘉賓、規劃集數並控制預算。"},{"en":"If a programme earns money from texting, the producer may receive a share.","zh":"如果節目從短訊賺錢，製作人可能獲得一份收入。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the party that helps make the show.","zh":"這個片語指幫助製作節目的那一方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"message-processing technology","meaning":"訊息處理技術","examples":[{"en":"A company supplies the message-processing technology.","zh":"一間公司供應訊息處理技術。"},{"en":"Message-processing technology is the system that receives, sorts, counts, and manages text messages.","zh":"Message-processing technology 是接收、分類、計算和管理短訊的系統。"},{"en":"A voting show needs message-processing technology to count thousands of votes quickly.","zh":"投票節目需要訊息處理技術來快速計算數以千計投票。"},{"en":"If the technology fails, viewers’ texts may not be recorded correctly.","zh":"如果技術失效，觀眾短訊可能無法被正確記錄。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the technical system behind large-scale texting.","zh":"這個片語描述大規模短訊背後的技術系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"revenues generated from","meaning":"由……產生的收入","examples":[{"en":"Revenues generated from text messages are important to many shows.","zh":"由短訊產生的收入對許多節目很重要。"},{"en":"Revenues generated from something are earnings produced by that source.","zh":"Revenues generated from something 是由某來源產生的收入。"},{"en":"Revenues generated from ticket sales can fund a school concert.","zh":"由門票銷售產生的收入可以資助學校音樂會。"},{"en":"If text messages generate income, programmes may build more activities around them.","zh":"如果短訊產生收入，節目可能圍繞它們建立更多活動。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on money created by a particular activity.","zh":"這個片語集中於某特定活動創造的金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an indispensable part of","meaning":"……不可或缺的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Text-message revenue has become an indispensable part of the business model.","zh":"短訊收入已成為商業模式不可或缺的一部分。"},{"en":"An indispensable part of something is a part that is so important it is almost impossible to remove.","zh":"An indispensable part of something 是重要到幾乎不能移除的一部分。"},{"en":"Clear feedback is an indispensable part of effective learning.","zh":"清晰回饋是有效學習不可或缺的一部分。"},{"en":"If a TV show depends on texting income, that revenue becomes essential to its operation.","zh":"如果電視節目依賴短訊收入，該收入就成為其營運的必要部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something necessary, not merely helpful.","zh":"這個片語描述必要事物，而不只是有幫助的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"business model","meaning":"商業模式","examples":[{"en":"Text-message revenue supports the business model of various shows.","zh":"短訊收入支撐各類節目的商業模式。"},{"en":"A business model is the way a company or programme creates value and earns money.","zh":"Business model 是公司或節目創造價值和賺錢的方式。"},{"en":"A tutoring centre’s business model may depend on monthly fees and trial lessons.","zh":"補習中心的商業模式可能依賴月費和試堂。"},{"en":"If texting becomes profitable, it can change a TV show’s business model.","zh":"如果短訊變得有利可圖，它可以改變電視節目的商業模式。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how an activity is financially organised.","zh":"這個片語解釋某活動在財務上如何組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"there has been grumbling that","meaning":"一直有人抱怨","examples":[{"en":"There has been grumbling that providers take too much of the share.","zh":"一直有人抱怨服務供應商佔去過多份額。"},{"en":"There has been grumbling that means people have been complaining quietly or repeatedly about something.","zh":"There has been grumbling that 指人們一直私下或反覆抱怨某事。"},{"en":"There has been grumbling that the school canteen prices are too high.","zh":"一直有人抱怨學校飯堂價格太高。"},{"en":"If partners feel revenue is unfairly divided, grumbling may grow into open conflict.","zh":"如果合作方覺得收入分配不公平，抱怨可能變成公開衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dissatisfaction, often informal rather than official.","zh":"這個片語描述不滿，通常較非正式而不是官方投訴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take too much of the share","meaning":"佔去過多份額","examples":[{"en":"Some producers think providers take too much of the revenue share.","zh":"一些製作人認為服務供應商佔去過多收入份額。"},{"en":"To take too much of the share means to receive more than others think is fair.","zh":"To take too much of the share 指取得比其他人認為公平的更多份額。"},{"en":"In a group project, one person may complain if another takes too much of the credit.","zh":"在小組專題中，如果某人佔去過多功勞，另一人可能投訴。"},{"en":"If service providers keep too much money, producers may look for ways to bypass them.","zh":"如果服務供應商保留太多金錢，製作人可能尋找方法繞過他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a dispute over fair division.","zh":"這個片語描述關於公平分配的爭議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Netherlands-based production firm","meaning":"總部設於荷蘭的製作公司","examples":[{"en":"Endemol is a Netherlands-based production firm.","zh":"Endemol 是一間總部設於荷蘭的製作公司。"},{"en":"A Netherlands-based production firm is a programme-making company whose main base is in the Netherlands.","zh":"Netherlands-based production firm 是主要基地設於荷蘭的節目製作公司。"},{"en":"A Hong Kong-based design firm may serve clients in several countries.","zh":"一間總部設於香港的設計公司可能服務幾個國家的客戶。"},{"en":"Knowing where a firm is based can help readers understand its business background.","zh":"知道公司基地在哪裏，可以幫助讀者理解其商業背景。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both the company’s location and its industry.","zh":"這個片語同時指出公司的地點和行業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be responsible for","meaning":"負責","examples":[{"en":"Endemol is responsible for many reality TV shows.","zh":"Endemol 負責許多真人騷節目。"},{"en":"To be responsible for something means to have the duty or role of creating, managing, or dealing with it.","zh":"To be responsible for something 指有創造、管理或處理某事的責任或角色。"},{"en":"A class monitor may be responsible for collecting homework.","zh":"班長可能負責收集功課。"},{"en":"If a company is responsible for a show, it may control production decisions.","zh":"如果一間公司負責某節目，它可能控制製作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes duty, control, or authorship.","zh":"這個片語描述責任、控制或創作歸屬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"construct its own database","meaning":"建立自己的資料庫","examples":[{"en":"Endemol has begun constructing its own database for mobile-phone users.","zh":"Endemol 已開始為手提電話用戶建立自己的資料庫。"},{"en":"To construct its own database means to build a private collection of user information.","zh":"To construct its own database 指建立私人用戶資訊集合。"},{"en":"A school may construct its own database of alumni contacts for future events.","zh":"學校可能建立自己的校友聯絡資料庫，以便日後活動使用。"},{"en":"If a company owns its database, it can contact users directly.","zh":"如果公司擁有自己的資料庫，它就可以直接聯絡用戶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes building a data system instead of depending on another company’s records.","zh":"這個片語描述建立數據系統，而不是依賴另一間公司的紀錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"mobile-phone users","meaning":"手提電話用戶","examples":[{"en":"The company is building a database for mobile-phone users.","zh":"該公司正在為手提電話用戶建立資料庫。"},{"en":"Mobile-phone users are people who use mobile phones for calls, texts, apps, or internet access.","zh":"Mobile-phone users 是使用手提電話通話、發短訊、使用應用程式或上網的人。"},{"en":"Mobile-phone users may receive reminders, advertisements, or voting links by message.","zh":"手提電話用戶可能透過訊息收到提醒、廣告或投票連結。"},{"en":"If a TV company knows its mobile-phone users, it can target them more directly.","zh":"如果電視公司認識自己的手提電話用戶，它就可以更直接地以他們為目標。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people as customers or participants through their phones.","zh":"這個片語把人視為透過電話參與的顧客或參與者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"set up a direct billing system","meaning":"設立直接收費系統","examples":[{"en":"Endemol plans to set up a direct billing system with users.","zh":"Endemol 計劃與用戶設立直接收費系統。"},{"en":"To set up a direct billing system means to create a way to charge customers without going through another company.","zh":"To set up a direct billing system 指建立一種不經另一間公司而向顧客收費的方法。"},{"en":"A gym may set up direct billing so members pay monthly from their bank accounts.","zh":"健身中心可能設立直接收費，讓會員每月從銀行戶口付款。"},{"en":"If a TV producer bills users directly, it may keep more of the revenue.","zh":"如果電視製作公司直接向用戶收費，它可能保留更多收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating a direct payment arrangement.","zh":"這個片語描述建立直接付款安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"direct billing system","meaning":"直接收費系統","examples":[{"en":"A direct billing system would let Endemol charge users directly.","zh":"直接收費系統會讓 Endemol 直接向用戶收費。"},{"en":"A direct billing system is a payment system where a company charges customers without an intermediary.","zh":"Direct billing system 是公司不經中介而向顧客收費的付款系統。"},{"en":"A streaming platform uses direct billing when it charges viewers’ cards each month.","zh":"串流平台每月向觀眾信用卡收費時，就是使用直接收費。"},{"en":"Direct billing can reduce dependence on partners who take a share of revenue.","zh":"直接收費可以減少對抽取收入份額的合作方的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a payment route between the company and the user.","zh":"這個片語描述公司與用戶之間的付款渠道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bypass the providers","meaning":"繞過服務供應商","examples":[{"en":"Endemol wants to bypass the mobile service providers.","zh":"Endemol 想繞過流動通訊服務供應商。"},{"en":"To bypass the providers means to avoid using them as intermediaries in the payment or service process.","zh":"To bypass the providers 指在付款或服務過程中避免使用它們作中介。"},{"en":"A shop may bypass a delivery platform by building its own ordering app.","zh":"商店可能透過建立自己的訂購應用程式，繞過外賣平台。"},{"en":"If producers bypass providers, they may keep a larger share of income.","zh":"如果製作人繞過供應商，他們可能保留更大收入份額。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cutting out a middle party.","zh":"這個片語描述移除中間一方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the combination of","meaning":"……的結合","examples":[{"en":"The combination of television and text messaging has proved successful.","zh":"電視和短訊的結合已證明成功。"},{"en":"The combination of two things means the two are used together as one system or idea.","zh":"The combination of two things 指兩件事作為一個系統或想法一起使用。"},{"en":"The combination of online lessons and face-to-face practice can help language learners.","zh":"網上課堂和面對面練習的結合可以幫助語言學習者。"},{"en":"If two tools work well together, their combination may create new opportunities.","zh":"如果兩種工具配合良好，它們的結合可能創造新機會。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the effect of joining two elements.","zh":"這個片語突出兩個元素結合的效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"prove so successful","meaning":"證明非常成功","examples":[{"en":"The combination of television and text messaging has proved so successful.","zh":"電視和短訊的結合已證明非常成功。"},{"en":"To prove so successful means to turn out to be very effective or profitable.","zh":"To prove so successful 指結果顯示非常有效或有利可圖。"},{"en":"A school reading club may prove so successful that more classes join it.","zh":"學校閱讀會可能證明非常成功，以致更多班級加入。"},{"en":"If TV texting produces both engagement and revenue, broadcasters will continue using it.","zh":"如果電視短訊互動同時帶來參與和收入，廣播機構會繼續使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes success shown by results, not just hopes.","zh":"這個片語描述由結果顯示的成功，而不只是希望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"one crucial aspect","meaning":"一個關鍵方面","examples":[{"en":"One crucial aspect is the emergence of short codes.","zh":"一個關鍵方面是短碼的出現。"},{"en":"One crucial aspect means one very important part of a situation.","zh":"One crucial aspect 指情況中一個非常重要的部分。"},{"en":"One crucial aspect of exam preparation is understanding the question, not just memorising answers.","zh":"考試準備的一個關鍵方面是理解題目，而不只是背答案。"},{"en":"If one crucial aspect fails, the whole system may become less effective.","zh":"如果一個關鍵方面失效，整個系統可能變得較不有效。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a key part of an explanation.","zh":"這個片語指出解釋中的關鍵部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the emergence of","meaning":"……的出現","examples":[{"en":"The emergence of short codes changed TV-texting.","zh":"短碼的出現改變了電視短訊互動。"},{"en":"The emergence of something means its appearance or development into importance.","zh":"The emergence of something 指某事物出現或發展成重要事物。"},{"en":"The emergence of online learning changed how many students study at home.","zh":"網上學習的出現改變了許多學生在家學習的方式。"},{"en":"When a new tool emerges, businesses may redesign their services around it.","zh":"當新工具出現，企業可能圍繞它重新設計服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something new becoming visible and influential.","zh":"這個片語描述新事物變得可見並有影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"four-, five- or six-digit numbers","meaning":"四位、五位或六位數字","examples":[{"en":"Short codes are special four-, five- or six-digit numbers.","zh":"短碼是特別的四位、五位或六位數字。"},{"en":"Four-, five- or six-digit numbers are numbers made of four, five, or six digits.","zh":"Four-, five- or six-digit numbers 是由四、五或六個數字組成的號碼。"},{"en":"A TV show may ask viewers to text a five-digit number because it is easy to remember.","zh":"電視節目可能要求觀眾發短訊到五位數字，因為它容易記住。"},{"en":"Short numbers reduce mistakes when viewers type quickly.","zh":"短號碼可以減少觀眾快速輸入時的錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the simple number format used for text services.","zh":"這個片語描述短訊服務使用的簡單號碼格式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"known as","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"Special short numbers are known as short codes.","zh":"特別短號碼被稱為短碼。"},{"en":"Known as means called by a particular name.","zh":"Known as 指被稱作某個名稱。"},{"en":"A student’s final school year is often known as a stressful period.","zh":"學生的最後一年中學常被稱為充滿壓力的時期。"},{"en":"Naming something clearly helps readers understand the technical term.","zh":"清楚命名某事物有助讀者理解技術術語。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what people call a thing.","zh":"這個片語引出人們如何稱呼某事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"short codes","meaning":"短碼","examples":[{"en":"Short codes are easier for viewers to remember.","zh":"短碼對觀眾來說較容易記住。"},{"en":"Short codes are brief phone numbers used for text-message services.","zh":"Short codes 是用於短訊服務的簡短電話號碼。"},{"en":"A charity campaign may use a short code so donors can text quickly.","zh":"慈善活動可能使用短碼，讓捐款者可以快速發短訊。"},{"en":"Because short codes are easy to display on screen, they support TV interaction.","zh":"因為短碼容易在螢幕上顯示，它們支持電視互動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to special short numbers for mobile messaging.","zh":"這個片語指用於手機短訊的特別短號碼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have control over","meaning":"控制；掌管","examples":[{"en":"Every provider has control over its own short codes.","zh":"每個供應商都控制自己的短碼。"},{"en":"To have control over something means to be able to manage, decide, or regulate it.","zh":"To have control over something 指能夠管理、決定或規管某事物。"},{"en":"Teachers have control over classroom rules but not always over students’ home study time.","zh":"老師能控制課堂規則，但未必總能控制學生在家的學習時間。"},{"en":"If each provider controls its own codes, cross-network cooperation becomes harder.","zh":"如果每個供應商控制自己的短碼，跨網絡合作就變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes power to manage or make decisions about something.","zh":"這個片語描述管理或決定某事的權力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not until recently","meaning":"直到最近才","examples":[{"en":"Not until recently did providers realise the value of working together.","zh":"服務供應商直到最近才意識到合作的價值。"},{"en":"Not until recently means only in the recent past, and not before that.","zh":"Not until recently 指只是到近期才發生，而之前沒有。"},{"en":"Not until recently did many schools realise how useful online lessons could be.","zh":"許多學校直到最近才意識到網上課堂可以多有用。"},{"en":"This structure often uses inversion to emphasise delay.","zh":"這個結構常使用倒裝來強調延遲。"},{"en":"In the passage, it shows providers were slow to recognise the benefits of cooperation.","zh":"在文章中，它顯示供應商很遲才認識合作的好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"come to realise that","meaning":"逐漸意識到","examples":[{"en":"Providers have come to realise that cooperation makes sense.","zh":"服務供應商已逐漸意識到合作是合理的。"},{"en":"To come to realise that means to gradually understand something.","zh":"To come to realise that 指逐漸理解某事。"},{"en":"A student may come to realise that small daily practice works better than last-minute revision.","zh":"學生可能逐漸意識到每天小量練習比臨急抱佛腳更有效。"},{"en":"Experience can make companies realise that old methods no longer work.","zh":"經驗可以令公司意識到舊方法不再有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a slow change in understanding.","zh":"這個片語描述理解上的慢慢轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make much more sense","meaning":"更合理；更有道理","examples":[{"en":"It makes much more sense for providers to offer compatible short codes.","zh":"服務供應商提供兼容短碼更合理得多。"},{"en":"To make much more sense means to be clearly more reasonable or practical.","zh":"To make much more sense 指明顯更合理或更實際。"},{"en":"It makes much more sense to revise a little every day than to study all night before an exam.","zh":"每天溫習少量內容比考試前通宵讀書更合理得多。"},{"en":"If one short code works on all networks, viewers are less confused.","zh":"如果一個短碼適用於所有網絡，觀眾就較不混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one option is more logical than another.","zh":"這個片語顯示一個選項比另一個更合邏輯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"work together","meaning":"合作","examples":[{"en":"Providers now work together to offer universal short codes.","zh":"供應商現在合作提供通用短碼。"},{"en":"To work together means to cooperate toward a shared goal.","zh":"To work together 指為共同目標合作。"},{"en":"Students work together when they divide tasks fairly in a group project.","zh":"學生在小組專題中公平分工時，就是合作。"},{"en":"If companies work together, they may create a service that is easier for customers.","zh":"如果公司合作，它們可能創造對顧客更容易使用的服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cooperation rather than separate action.","zh":"這個片語描述合作，而不是各自行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"compatible with","meaning":"與……兼容","examples":[{"en":"Short codes became compatible with all networks.","zh":"短碼變得與所有網絡兼容。"},{"en":"Compatible with means able to work with another system without problems.","zh":"Compatible with 指能夠與另一系統無問題地配合使用。"},{"en":"A charger must be compatible with a phone before it can be used safely.","zh":"充電器必須與手機兼容，才能安全使用。"},{"en":"If a short code is compatible with all networks, any viewer can use it.","zh":"如果短碼與所有網絡兼容，任何觀眾都可以使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes technical fit and smooth operation.","zh":"這個片語描述技術配合和順利運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"all networks","meaning":"所有網絡","examples":[{"en":"Universal short codes are compatible with all networks.","zh":"通用短碼與所有網絡兼容。"},{"en":"All networks means every mobile-phone network involved in the service.","zh":"All networks 指服務涉及的每一個流動電話網絡。"},{"en":"A messaging service that works on all networks is easier for customers to use.","zh":"在所有網絡都可使用的訊息服務，對顧客來說較易使用。"},{"en":"If a code does not work on all networks, some viewers may be excluded.","zh":"如果短碼不是在所有網絡都能使用，一些觀眾可能被排除。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses full coverage across providers.","zh":"這個片語強調跨供應商的全面覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"universal short codes","meaning":"通用短碼","examples":[{"en":"The emergence of universal short codes was a game-changer.","zh":"通用短碼的出現是改變局面的因素。"},{"en":"Universal short codes are short numbers that work across different mobile networks.","zh":"Universal short codes 是可在不同流動網絡使用的短號碼。"},{"en":"A TV vote is easier when one universal short code works for all viewers.","zh":"當一個通用短碼適用於所有觀眾，電視投票就更容易。"},{"en":"Universal short codes reduce confusion and make participation faster.","zh":"通用短碼減少混亂，並令參與更快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shared short numbers used across networks.","zh":"這個片語描述跨網絡使用的共用短號碼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a game-changer","meaning":"改變局面的因素","examples":[{"en":"Universal short codes were a game-changer for TV-texting.","zh":"通用短碼是電視短訊互動的改變局面的因素。"},{"en":"A game-changer is something that changes a situation in a major and practical way.","zh":"Game-changer 是以重大而實際方式改變情況的事物。"},{"en":"Online payment was a game-changer for small shops because customers could buy without visiting.","zh":"網上付款對小店來說是改變局面的因素，因為顧客不用到店也能購買。"},{"en":"If one code works everywhere, TV-texting becomes much easier to use.","zh":"如果一個短碼到處都能使用，電視短訊互動就變得容易得多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a development that changes the rules of a business or activity.","zh":"這個片語描述改變商業或活動規則的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"shown on screen","meaning":"顯示在螢幕上","examples":[{"en":"Short codes are easier to remember when shown on screen.","zh":"短碼顯示在螢幕上時較容易記住。"},{"en":"Shown on screen means displayed visually on a television, computer, or phone screen.","zh":"Shown on screen 指在電視、電腦或手機螢幕上視覺顯示。"},{"en":"Students remember homework better when instructions are shown on screen during class.","zh":"當功課指示在課堂中顯示在螢幕上，學生較容易記住。"},{"en":"If a number is shown on screen, viewers do not need to search for it elsewhere.","zh":"如果號碼顯示在螢幕上，觀眾就不用到其他地方搜尋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information being made visible to viewers.","zh":"這個片語描述資訊被展示給觀眾看見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mobile-marketing company","meaning":"流動市場推廣公司","examples":[{"en":"Flytxt is a mobile-marketing company.","zh":"Flytxt 是一間流動市場推廣公司。"},{"en":"A mobile-marketing company helps businesses reach customers through phones, messages, and mobile services.","zh":"Mobile-marketing company 幫助企業透過電話、訊息和流動服務接觸顧客。"},{"en":"A mobile-marketing company may send discount codes to customers by SMS.","zh":"流動市場推廣公司可能透過短訊向顧客發送折扣碼。"},{"en":"As more viewers use phones, mobile-marketing companies can support interactive TV campaigns.","zh":"隨着更多觀眾使用電話，流動市場推廣公司可以支援互動電視宣傳。"},{"en":"This phrase names a company type focused on marketing through mobile technology.","zh":"這個片語命名專注透過流動科技進行市場推廣的公司類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"operators’ cooperation","meaning":"營運商的合作","examples":[{"en":"Operators’ cooperation is part of a broader trend.","zh":"營運商的合作是更廣泛趨勢的一部分。"},{"en":"Operators’ cooperation means mobile network companies working together rather than separately.","zh":"Operators’ cooperation 指流動網絡公司合作，而不是各自行動。"},{"en":"Operators’ cooperation can make one payment system work across several networks.","zh":"營運商的合作可以令一個付款系統在多個網絡上運作。"},{"en":"If operators cooperate, customers face fewer technical barriers.","zh":"如果營運商合作，顧客會面對較少技術障礙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collaboration between service providers.","zh":"這個片語描述服務供應商之間的協作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"expand the market","meaning":"擴展市場","examples":[{"en":"Operators are cooperating to expand the market.","zh":"營運商正在合作以擴展市場。"},{"en":"To expand the market means to increase the number of customers, uses, or business opportunities.","zh":"To expand the market 指增加顧客、用途或商機的數量。"},{"en":"A language school may expand the market by offering online classes to overseas students.","zh":"語言學校可能透過向海外學生提供網上課程來擴展市場。"},{"en":"If texting becomes easier across networks, more viewers may join and the market grows.","zh":"如果跨網絡發短訊變得更容易，更多觀眾可能加入，市場就會增長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a business area larger.","zh":"這個片語描述令某商業領域變大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"part of a broader trend","meaning":"更廣泛趨勢的一部分","examples":[{"en":"This cooperation is part of a broader trend.","zh":"這種合作是更廣泛趨勢的一部分。"},{"en":"Part of a broader trend means one example of a larger pattern of change.","zh":"Part of a broader trend 指某事是更大變化模式的一個例子。"},{"en":"More students using tablets is part of a broader trend toward digital learning.","zh":"更多學生使用平板電腦，是走向數碼學習這一更廣泛趨勢的一部分。"},{"en":"If many industries start sharing technology, one company’s cooperation may reflect a bigger shift.","zh":"如果許多行業開始共享科技，一間公司的合作可能反映更大轉變。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a single case to a wider development.","zh":"這個片語把單一個案與更廣泛發展連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"faced with a choice between","meaning":"面對在……之間作選擇","examples":[{"en":"Providers were faced with a choice between protecting margins and sharing opportunities.","zh":"供應商面對在保護利潤率和分享機會之間作選擇。"},{"en":"To be faced with a choice between two things means to have to decide which option to follow.","zh":"To be faced with a choice between two things 指必須決定跟隨哪一個選項。"},{"en":"A student may be faced with a choice between joining a club and using the time for revision.","zh":"學生可能面對在加入學會和用時間溫習之間作選擇。"},{"en":"If companies choose profit protection only, they may miss bigger market growth.","zh":"如果公司只選擇保護利潤，它們可能錯失更大市場增長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decision involving two competing options.","zh":"這個片語描述涉及兩個互相競爭選項的決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"protect their margins","meaning":"保護利潤率","examples":[{"en":"Providers once focused on protecting their margins.","zh":"供應商曾專注於保護利潤率。"},{"en":"To protect their margins means to preserve the difference between income and cost, so profits remain high.","zh":"To protect their margins 指維持收入與成本之間的差距，令利潤保持高水平。"},{"en":"A restaurant may protect its margins by controlling food waste and menu prices.","zh":"餐廳可能透過控制食物浪費和餐牌價格來保護利潤率。"},{"en":"If providers keep most revenue for themselves, they protect margins but may discourage partners.","zh":"如果供應商把大部分收入留給自己，它們保護了利潤率，但可能令合作方卻步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes defending profitability.","zh":"這個片語描述維護盈利能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"allow a new medium to emerge","meaning":"讓新媒介出現","examples":[{"en":"Providers can allow a new medium to emerge by sharing revenue.","zh":"供應商可以透過分享收入，讓新媒介出現。"},{"en":"To allow a new medium to emerge means to create conditions for a new communication form to develop.","zh":"To allow a new medium to emerge 指創造條件讓新的溝通形式發展。"},{"en":"Schools allow a new learning medium to emerge when they support online lessons properly.","zh":"當學校妥善支援網上課堂，它們就是讓新的學習媒介出現。"},{"en":"If companies cooperate, text-based interactive television can grow into a new medium.","zh":"如果公司合作，以短訊為基礎的互動電視可以發展成新媒介。"},{"en":"This phrase describes enabling a new form of communication or entertainment.","zh":"這個片語描述促成新的溝通或娛樂形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"choose the former","meaning":"選擇前者","examples":[{"en":"Providers previously chose the former option.","zh":"供應商以往選擇前者。"},{"en":"To choose the former means to select the first of two options just mentioned.","zh":"To choose the former 指選擇剛剛提到的兩個選項中的第一個。"},{"en":"If students can revise or play games, choosing the former means choosing revision.","zh":"如果學生可以溫習或玩遊戲，選擇前者就是選擇溫習。"},{"en":"In the passage, the former option is protecting margins rather than sharing opportunities.","zh":"在文章中，前者是保護利潤率，而不是分享機會。"},{"en":"This phrase depends on a previous contrast between two choices.","zh":"這個片語依賴前文中兩個選項的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"WAP","meaning":"無線應用協定","examples":[{"en":"WAP was a technology for reading cut-down web pages on mobile phones.","zh":"WAP 是一種讓人在手提電話上閱讀簡化版網頁的技術。"},{"en":"WAP was an early mobile internet technology that let phones access simplified web content.","zh":"WAP 是一種早期流動互聯網技術，讓電話接入簡化網頁內容。"},{"en":"Before smartphones, users might use WAP to read basic news or weather pages.","zh":"在智能手機出現前，用戶可能使用 WAP 閱讀基本新聞或天氣頁面。"},{"en":"If a technology is slow, limited, and costly, users may not adopt it widely.","zh":"如果一項技術慢、有限且昂貴，用戶可能不會廣泛採用。"},{"en":"In this passage, WAP is an example of a mobile service that failed to grow as hoped.","zh":"在文章中，WAP 是流動服務未能如預期增長的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cut-down web pages","meaning":"簡化版網頁","examples":[{"en":"WAP allowed mobile-phone users to read cut-down web pages.","zh":"WAP 讓手提電話用戶閱讀簡化版網頁。"},{"en":"Cut-down web pages are simplified web pages with fewer features, images, or details.","zh":"Cut-down web pages 是功能、圖片或細節較少的簡化網頁。"},{"en":"A school website may offer cut-down pages for older phones with slower connections.","zh":"學校網站可能為連線較慢的舊手機提供簡化版網頁。"},{"en":"If pages are cut down too much, users may find the service boring or limited.","zh":"如果網頁被簡化得太多，用戶可能覺得服務沉悶或有限。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reduced versions of normal web pages.","zh":"這個片語描述普通網頁的精簡版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fail because of","meaning":"因……而失敗","examples":[{"en":"WAP failed because of providers’ reluctance to share revenue.","zh":"WAP 因服務供應商不願分享收入而失敗。"},{"en":"To fail because of something means to be unsuccessful due to that reason.","zh":"To fail because of something 指由於某原因而不成功。"},{"en":"A group project may fail because of poor communication among members.","zh":"小組專題可能因組員之間溝通欠佳而失敗。"},{"en":"If companies refuse to share income, content partners may stop supporting the service.","zh":"如果公司拒絕分享收入，內容合作方可能停止支持該服務。"},{"en":"This phrase connects failure with its cause.","zh":"這個片語把失敗與原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reluctance to","meaning":"不願意去","examples":[{"en":"Service providers showed reluctance to share revenue.","zh":"服務供應商表現出不願意分享收入。"},{"en":"Reluctance to do something means unwillingness or hesitation to do it.","zh":"Reluctance to do something 指不願意或猶豫去做某事。"},{"en":"A student may show reluctance to speak if classmates laugh at mistakes.","zh":"如果同學嘲笑錯誤，學生可能表現出不願意發言。"},{"en":"Reluctance to cooperate can slow down a project.","zh":"不願意合作可以拖慢項目。"},{"en":"This phrase describes resistance or unwillingness.","zh":"這個片語描述抗拒或不情願。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"share revenue with","meaning":"與……分享收入","examples":[{"en":"Providers were reluctant to share revenue with content providers.","zh":"供應商不願意與內容供應商分享收入。"},{"en":"To share revenue with someone means to divide income with them.","zh":"To share revenue with someone 指與某人分配收入。"},{"en":"A school club may share revenue with a charity after a fundraising sale.","zh":"學校學會在籌款售賣後，可能與慈善機構分享收入。"},{"en":"If telecom companies share revenue with content creators, more creators may join the platform.","zh":"如果電訊公司與內容創作者分享收入，更多創作者可能加入平台。"},{"en":"This phrase describes splitting money among partners.","zh":"這個片語描述合作方之間分配金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"content providers","meaning":"內容供應商","examples":[{"en":"Content providers wanted a share of mobile-service revenue.","zh":"內容供應商想取得流動服務收入的一部分。"},{"en":"Content providers are people or companies that create material such as shows, games, articles, or music.","zh":"Content providers 是創作節目、遊戲、文章或音樂等材料的人或公司。"},{"en":"A streaming platform depends on content providers to supply videos and programmes.","zh":"串流平台依賴內容供應商提供影片和節目。"},{"en":"If content providers are not paid fairly, they may stop offering good material.","zh":"如果內容供應商沒有得到公平報酬，他們可能停止提供優質內容。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the creators or suppliers of media content.","zh":"這個片語指媒體內容的創作者或供應者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"learn their lesson","meaning":"汲取教訓","examples":[{"en":"Providers have now learnt their lesson.","zh":"供應商現在已經汲取教訓。"},{"en":"To learn their lesson means to understand from a past mistake and change behaviour.","zh":"To learn their lesson 指從過去錯誤中明白問題並改變行為。"},{"en":"A student who failed after last-minute revision may learn their lesson and start earlier next time.","zh":"因臨急抱佛腳而考差的學生，可能汲取教訓，下次更早開始。"},{"en":"If companies lost opportunities before, they may cooperate more wisely later.","zh":"如果公司以前失去機會，它們之後可能更明智地合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improvement after a negative experience.","zh":"這個片語描述在負面經驗後作出改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"alter the way they operate","meaning":"改變運作方式","examples":[{"en":"Providers are altering the way they operate.","zh":"供應商正在改變運作方式。"},{"en":"To alter the way they operate means to change how they run their business or services.","zh":"To alter the way they operate 指改變他們經營業務或服務的方法。"},{"en":"A school may alter the way it operates by moving notices from paper to an app.","zh":"學校可能透過把通告由紙本轉到應用程式來改變運作方式。"},{"en":"If old methods failed, companies may need to change their operating habits.","zh":"如果舊方法失敗，公司可能需要改變營運習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing the practical way an organisation works.","zh":"這個片語描述改變組織實際運作的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"go so far as to","meaning":"甚至做到","examples":[{"en":"Orange has gone so far as to launch a rate card.","zh":"Orange 甚至推出了收費表。"},{"en":"To go so far as to do something means to take a notably strong or unexpected step.","zh":"To go so far as to do something 指採取一個特別強烈或意想不到的步驟。"},{"en":"A teacher may go so far as to call every parent if many students miss homework.","zh":"如果許多學生欠交功課，老師甚至可能逐一致電家長。"},{"en":"If a company publishes prices openly, it may be making a major change toward transparency.","zh":"如果公司公開發布價格，它可能正在向透明度作出重大改變。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the action goes beyond what might normally be expected.","zh":"這個片語強調行動超出一般預期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"launch a rate card","meaning":"推出收費表","examples":[{"en":"Orange launched a rate card for sharing text-message revenue.","zh":"Orange 推出了一份分享短訊收入的收費表。"},{"en":"To launch a rate card means to publish a list explaining prices, fees, or revenue shares.","zh":"To launch a rate card 指發布一份說明價格、費用或收入分成的列表。"},{"en":"A tutoring centre may launch a rate card so parents can compare lesson prices clearly.","zh":"補習中心可能推出收費表，讓家長清楚比較課堂價格。"},{"en":"A clear rate card can reduce arguments because all partners know the charges.","zh":"清楚的收費表可以減少爭議，因為所有合作方都知道收費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formally introducing a pricing document.","zh":"這個片語描述正式推出定價文件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sharing text-message revenue","meaning":"分享短訊收入","examples":[{"en":"The rate card explains the sharing of text-message revenue.","zh":"該收費表解釋短訊收入的分享。"},{"en":"Sharing text-message revenue means dividing money earned from text messages among different parties.","zh":"Sharing text-message revenue 指在不同方之間分配由短訊賺得的金錢。"},{"en":"A TV company, phone operator, and technology supplier may share text-message revenue.","zh":"電視公司、電話營運商和技術供應商可能分享短訊收入。"},{"en":"Fair sharing can encourage more companies to support interactive services.","zh":"公平分享可以鼓勵更多公司支持互動服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how SMS income is split.","zh":"這個片語描述短訊收入如何分配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a new level of transparency","meaning":"新程度的透明度","examples":[{"en":"The rate card created a new level of transparency.","zh":"該收費表創造了新程度的透明度。"},{"en":"A new level of transparency means a higher degree of openness and clarity.","zh":"New level of transparency 指更高程度的公開和清晰。"},{"en":"A school creates a new level of transparency when it clearly explains how grades are calculated.","zh":"學校清楚解釋成績如何計算時，就創造了新程度的透明度。"},{"en":"If pricing becomes transparent, partners can judge whether a deal is fair.","zh":"如果定價變得透明，合作方可以判斷交易是否公平。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information becoming more open and understandable.","zh":"這個片語描述資訊變得更公開和易理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"used to be unimaginable","meaning":"以往難以想像","examples":[{"en":"Such transparency used to be unimaginable.","zh":"這樣的透明度以往難以想像。"},{"en":"Used to be unimaginable means something was once impossible to imagine or expect.","zh":"Used to be unimaginable 指某事曾經難以想像或預期。"},{"en":"Years ago, studying with classmates by video call used to be unimaginable for many families.","zh":"多年前，對許多家庭來說，與同學視像學習以往難以想像。"},{"en":"When industries change, practices that once seemed impossible may become normal.","zh":"當行業改變，曾經看似不可能的做法可能變得正常。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts past expectations with current reality.","zh":"這個片語把過去預期與現實作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"at a recent conference","meaning":"在最近一次會議上","examples":[{"en":"Han Weegink spoke at a recent conference.","zh":"Han Weegink 在最近一次會議上發言。"},{"en":"At a recent conference means during a professional meeting held not long ago.","zh":"At a recent conference 指在不久前舉行的專業會議期間。"},{"en":"A teacher may share new classroom methods at a recent education conference.","zh":"老師可能在最近一次教育會議上分享新課堂方法。"},{"en":"Conferences allow experts to explain trends and exchange ideas.","zh":"會議讓專家解釋趨勢和交流想法。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the setting where a public comment was made.","zh":"這個片語提供某公開評論發表的場合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"text-message infrastructure","meaning":"短訊基建","examples":[{"en":"CMG provides text-message infrastructure to the television industry.","zh":"CMG 向電視業提供短訊基建。"},{"en":"Text-message infrastructure is the technical system that allows large numbers of messages to be sent, received, and processed.","zh":"Text-message infrastructure 是讓大量訊息能夠發送、接收和處理的技術系統。"},{"en":"A voting show needs text-message infrastructure so votes do not disappear or arrive too late.","zh":"投票節目需要短訊基建，讓投票不會消失或太遲到達。"},{"en":"Strong infrastructure makes interactive TV more reliable.","zh":"強大的基建令互動電視更可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the hidden technology supporting SMS services.","zh":"這個片語指支撐短訊服務的隱藏技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"television industry","meaning":"電視業","examples":[{"en":"The television industry is changing in a subtle way.","zh":"電視業正在以細微方式改變。"},{"en":"The television industry includes broadcasters, producers, advertisers, technology firms, and other businesses connected with TV.","zh":"Television industry 包括廣播機構、製作人、廣告商、科技公司和其他與電視有關的企業。"},{"en":"Streaming platforms have pushed the television industry to rethink how people watch shows.","zh":"串流平台推動電視業重新思考人們如何觀看節目。"},{"en":"If texting becomes profitable, the television industry may design more interactive formats.","zh":"如果短訊變得有利可圖，電視業可能設計更多互動形式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the business world around television.","zh":"這個片語指圍繞電視的商業世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"point out that","meaning":"指出","examples":[{"en":"Han Weegink pointed out that the television industry is changing.","zh":"Han Weegink 指出電視業正在改變。"},{"en":"To point out that means to draw attention to a fact or idea.","zh":"To point out that 指把注意力引向某個事實或想法。"},{"en":"A teacher may point out that a small grammar error changes the meaning of a sentence.","zh":"老師可能指出一個小文法錯誤會改變句子意思。"},{"en":"If an expert points out a trend, readers may pay closer attention.","zh":"如果專家指出一種趨勢，讀者可能更仔細留意。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces something someone wants others to notice.","zh":"這個片語引出某人想他人注意的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"subtle yet fundamental","meaning":"細微但根本性的","examples":[{"en":"The television industry is changing in a subtle yet fundamental way.","zh":"電視業正在以細微但根本性的方式改變。"},{"en":"Subtle yet fundamental means not obvious at first, but deeply important.","zh":"Subtle yet fundamental 指起初不明顯，但深層上非常重要。"},{"en":"A school may change in a subtle yet fundamental way when students begin learning more independently.","zh":"當學生開始更自主學習，學校可能以細微但根本性的方式改變。"},{"en":"Texting may seem small, but it changes the relationship between viewers and programmes.","zh":"短訊看似微小，但它改變觀眾與節目的關係。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a quiet change with deep effects.","zh":"這個片語描述帶有深遠影響的安靜變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"instead of","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"More TV shows now involve viewers instead of using only one-way presentation.","zh":"更多電視節目現在加入觀眾，而不是只使用單向呈現。"},{"en":"Instead of introduces the thing that is not chosen or not done.","zh":"Instead of 用來引出沒有被選擇或沒有做的事。"},{"en":"A student may revise with examples instead of memorising rules blindly.","zh":"學生可能用例子溫習，而不是盲目背規則。"},{"en":"If programmes involve viewers instead of only broadcasting to them, TV becomes more interactive.","zh":"如果節目加入觀眾，而不是只向他們播放，電視就變得更互動。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly contrasts two choices.","zh":"這個片語清楚對比兩個選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"one-way presentation","meaning":"單向呈現","examples":[{"en":"Traditional television depended on one-way presentation.","zh":"傳統電視依賴單向呈現。"},{"en":"One-way presentation means information flows from the speaker or broadcaster to the audience without direct response.","zh":"One-way presentation 指資訊由說話者或廣播機構流向觀眾，而沒有直接回應。"},{"en":"A lecture can feel like one-way presentation if students cannot ask questions.","zh":"如果學生不能提問，講課可能感覺像單向呈現。"},{"en":"One-way television limits audience involvement because viewers only receive content.","zh":"單向電視限制觀眾參與，因為觀眾只是接收內容。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts passive watching with interactive participation.","zh":"這個片語把被動觀看與互動參與作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"involve viewers’ reactions","meaning":"加入觀眾反應","examples":[{"en":"More TV shows now involve viewers’ reactions.","zh":"更多電視節目現在加入觀眾反應。"},{"en":"To involve viewers’ reactions means to include audience responses as part of the programme.","zh":"To involve viewers’ reactions 指把觀眾回應納入節目一部分。"},{"en":"A news show may involve viewers’ reactions by showing selected text comments on screen.","zh":"新聞節目可能透過在螢幕上顯示精選短訊評論來加入觀眾反應。"},{"en":"If reactions are included, viewers may feel their opinions affect the programme.","zh":"如果反應被納入，觀眾可能覺得自己的意見影響節目。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making audience response part of the content.","zh":"這個片語描述把觀眾回應變成內容的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"engage audiences","meaning":"吸引觀眾參與","examples":[{"en":"Interactive TV promises to engage audiences more fully.","zh":"互動電視承諾更全面地吸引觀眾參與。"},{"en":"To engage audiences means to hold their attention and involve them actively.","zh":"To engage audiences 指抓住觀眾注意力並令他們主動參與。"},{"en":"A teacher can engage students by asking questions instead of only talking.","zh":"老師可以透過提問而不是只講解來吸引學生參與。"},{"en":"If viewers can vote or comment, they are more likely to stay interested.","zh":"如果觀眾可以投票或評論，他們更可能保持興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making people attentive and involved.","zh":"這個片語描述令人專注並投入參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the promise of","meaning":"……的承諾；……的賣點","examples":[{"en":"Engaging audiences has always been the promise of interactive TV.","zh":"吸引觀眾參與一直是互動電視的賣點。"},{"en":"The promise of something is the benefit or possibility it claims to offer.","zh":"The promise of something 是某事聲稱能提供的好處或可能性。"},{"en":"The promise of online learning is that students can study anywhere.","zh":"網上學習的賣點是學生可以在任何地方學習。"},{"en":"If a technology does not deliver its promise, users may lose interest.","zh":"如果一項科技未能實現其承諾，用戶可能失去興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the attractive potential of an idea or product.","zh":"這個片語描述想法或產品的吸引潛力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"interactive TV","meaning":"互動電視","examples":[{"en":"Interactive TV allows viewers to respond to programmes.","zh":"互動電視讓觀眾回應節目。"},{"en":"Interactive TV is television that lets viewers take part through voting, messages, choices, or other responses.","zh":"Interactive TV 是讓觀眾透過投票、訊息、選擇或其他回應參與的電視。"},{"en":"A quiz show becomes interactive TV when viewers answer questions from home.","zh":"當觀眾在家回答問題，問答節目就變成互動電視。"},{"en":"Interaction can make viewers feel less passive and more connected to the show.","zh":"互動可以令觀眾感覺較不被動，並與節目更有連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes television with two-way participation.","zh":"這個片語描述具有雙向參與的電視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be originally designed to","meaning":"原本設計用來","examples":[{"en":"Interactive TV was originally designed to work with special set-top boxes.","zh":"互動電視原本設計用來與特別機頂盒配合使用。"},{"en":"To be originally designed to do something means it was first created for that purpose.","zh":"To be originally designed to do something 指最初為某目的而創造。"},{"en":"A classroom app may be originally designed to record homework but later used for announcements.","zh":"課堂應用程式可能原本設計用來記錄功課，但後來用作公告。"},{"en":"If a product is used differently from its original design, the market may have changed.","zh":"如果產品用途不同於原本設計，市場可能已經改變。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the first purpose with later use.","zh":"這個片語把最初目的與後來用途作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"work with","meaning":"與……配合使用","examples":[{"en":"Interactive TV was designed to work with set-top boxes.","zh":"互動電視被設計成與機頂盒配合使用。"},{"en":"To work with something means to function properly together with it.","zh":"To work with something 指與某物一起正常運作。"},{"en":"A printer must work with a computer before students can print homework.","zh":"打印機必須與電腦配合使用，學生才能打印功課。"},{"en":"If interactive TV works with phones more easily than boxes, companies may choose phones.","zh":"如果互動電視與電話配合使用比與機頂盒更容易，公司可能選擇電話。"},{"en":"This phrase describes compatibility between tools or systems.","zh":"這個片語描述工具或系統之間的兼容性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"set-top boxes","meaning":"機頂盒","examples":[{"en":"Interactive TV was originally designed around set-top boxes.","zh":"互動電視原本圍繞機頂盒設計。"},{"en":"Set-top boxes are devices connected to a television to provide extra services or channels.","zh":"Set-top boxes 是接駁到電視，以提供額外服務或頻道的裝置。"},{"en":"A household may use a set-top box to receive digital TV channels.","zh":"家庭可能使用機頂盒接收數碼電視頻道。"},{"en":"If set-top boxes are expensive or incompatible, interactive services may grow slowly.","zh":"如果機頂盒昂貴或互不兼容，互動服務可能增長緩慢。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to hardware placed near or connected to a TV.","zh":"這個片語指放在電視附近或連接電視的硬件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be plugged into","meaning":"插入；接駁到","examples":[{"en":"Set-top boxes could be plugged directly into the TV.","zh":"機頂盒可以直接接駁到電視。"},{"en":"To be plugged into something means to be connected to it using a cable or socket.","zh":"To be plugged into something 指使用電線或插座連接到某物。"},{"en":"A laptop may be plugged into a projector before a class presentation.","zh":"課堂匯報前，手提電腦可能接駁到投影機。"},{"en":"If a device must be plugged into the TV, installation may be less convenient than using a phone.","zh":"如果裝置必須接駁到電視，安裝可能不如使用電話方便。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical connection between electronic devices.","zh":"這個片語描述電子裝置之間的實體連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be flawed in many ways","meaning":"在多方面有缺陷","examples":[{"en":"The set-top-box method was flawed in many ways.","zh":"機頂盒方法在多方面有缺陷。"},{"en":"To be flawed in many ways means to have several weaknesses or problems.","zh":"To be flawed in many ways 指有幾個弱點或問題。"},{"en":"A school timetable may be flawed in many ways if students have no lunch break and teachers cannot share rooms.","zh":"如果學生沒有午飯時間，而老師不能共用課室，學校時間表可能在多方面有缺陷。"},{"en":"If a system is costly, slow, and hard to use, users may reject it.","zh":"如果系統昂貴、緩慢且難用，用戶可能拒絕它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a solution with multiple serious defects.","zh":"這個片語描述有多個嚴重缺點的解決方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"develop and test software","meaning":"開發和測試軟件","examples":[{"en":"Developing and testing software for different boxes could be costly.","zh":"為不同機頂盒開發和測試軟件可能成本高昂。"},{"en":"To develop and test software means to create programs and check whether they work correctly.","zh":"To develop and test software 指創造程式並檢查它們是否正確運作。"},{"en":"A school app must be developed and tested before students use it for homework.","zh":"學校應用程式在學生用來交功課前，必須先開發和測試。"},{"en":"If many device types exist, software testing becomes slower and more expensive.","zh":"如果存在許多裝置類型，軟件測試會變得更慢和更昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the technical work needed before a digital service can operate reliably.","zh":"這個片語描述數碼服務可靠運作前所需的技術工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"multiple, incompatible types of","meaning":"多種互不兼容的","examples":[{"en":"Developers had to deal with multiple, incompatible types of set-top box.","zh":"開發人員必須處理多種互不兼容的機頂盒。"},{"en":"Multiple, incompatible types of something means many versions that cannot work together smoothly.","zh":"Multiple, incompatible types of something 指許多不能順利配合運作的版本。"},{"en":"A teacher may struggle if students submit homework in multiple, incompatible file formats.","zh":"如果學生以多種互不兼容的檔案格式交功課，老師可能很吃力。"},{"en":"If devices are incompatible, developers must build separate versions for each one.","zh":"如果裝置互不兼容，開發人員必須為每一種建立獨立版本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes variety that creates technical difficulty.","zh":"這個片語描述造成技術困難的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"not to mention that","meaning":"更不用說","examples":[{"en":"Developing software was costly, not to mention that market penetration was limited.","zh":"開發軟件成本高昂，更不用說市場滲透率有限。"},{"en":"Not to mention that adds another important point, often making the problem stronger.","zh":"Not to mention that 用來加入另一個重要重點，通常令問題更強。"},{"en":"The trip is expensive, not to mention that it takes three hours each way.","zh":"這趟旅程很昂貴，更不用說來回每程要三小時。"},{"en":"This phrase helps add an extra reason after the first one.","zh":"這個片語幫助在第一個原因後加入額外原因。"},{"en":"In the passage, it adds limited market reach to the problem of high development cost.","zh":"在文章中，它把市場覆蓋有限加入高開發成本這個問題中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"market penetration","meaning":"市場滲透率","examples":[{"en":"The market penetration of set-top boxes was lower than that of mobile phones.","zh":"機頂盒的市場滲透率低於手提電話。"},{"en":"Market penetration means how widely a product or service is used in a market.","zh":"Market penetration 指某產品或服務在市場中被使用得多廣泛。"},{"en":"If nearly every student uses a messaging app, its market penetration is high.","zh":"如果幾乎每個學生都使用某訊息應用程式，它的市場滲透率就高。"},{"en":"Low market penetration makes a technology less attractive for large-scale services.","zh":"低市場滲透率令科技對大型服務較不吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase measures how deeply a product has entered a market.","zh":"這個片語量度產品進入市場的深度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"below that of","meaning":"低於……的","examples":[{"en":"The market penetration of set-top boxes was below that of mobile phones.","zh":"機頂盒的市場滲透率低於手提電話的市場滲透率。"},{"en":"Below that of means lower than the level, number, or rate of another thing.","zh":"Below that of 指低於另一事物的水平、數字或比率。"},{"en":"A student’s speaking score may be below that of their writing score.","zh":"學生的口語分數可能低於寫作分數。"},{"en":"If set-top-box use is below phone use, phone-based interaction has a larger audience.","zh":"如果機頂盒使用率低於電話使用率，以電話為基礎的互動就有更大觀眾群。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two figures or levels.","zh":"這個片語比較兩個數字或水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"around 85%","meaning":"約百分之八十五","examples":[{"en":"The market penetration of mobile phones was around 85%.","zh":"手提電話的市場滲透率約為百分之八十五。"},{"en":"Around 85% means approximately 85 per cent, not necessarily exactly.","zh":"Around 85% 指大約百分之八十五，不一定完全準確。"},{"en":"Around 85% of a class may pass if most students prepare well.","zh":"如果大多數學生準備充分，一班約百分之八十五學生可能及格。"},{"en":"If phone ownership is around 85%, a TV-texting service can reach most viewers.","zh":"如果電話擁有率約為百分之八十五，電視短訊服務就能接觸大多數觀眾。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate percentage.","zh":"這個片語給出大約百分比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"what’s more","meaning":"而且","examples":[{"en":"What’s more, it is quicker to develop apps for mobile phones.","zh":"而且，為手提電話開發應用程式更快。"},{"en":"What’s more adds another point that strengthens the previous argument.","zh":"What’s more 用來加入另一個加強前文論點的重點。"},{"en":"The course is affordable; what’s more, students can replay every lesson.","zh":"這個課程價格可負擔；而且，學生可以重播每一堂。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when adding a further advantage or disadvantage.","zh":"這個片語適用於加入進一步優點或缺點。"},{"en":"In the passage, it adds speed of development to the advantages of mobile phones.","zh":"在文章中，它把開發速度加入手提電話的優勢中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"develop and set up apps","meaning":"開發和設立應用程式","examples":[{"en":"It is quicker to develop and set up apps for mobile phones.","zh":"為手提電話開發和設立應用程式更快。"},{"en":"To develop and set up apps means to create mobile applications and prepare them for use.","zh":"To develop and set up apps 指創造流動應用程式並準備讓人使用。"},{"en":"A school may develop and set up an app for homework reminders and notices.","zh":"學校可能開發和設立一個用於功課提醒和通告的應用程式。"},{"en":"If apps are faster to create than set-top-box software, companies may choose mobile solutions.","zh":"如果應用程式比機頂盒軟件更快建立，公司可能選擇流動方案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both building and launching mobile software.","zh":"這個片語同時描述建立和推出流動軟件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"approach the market","meaning":"接觸市場；進入市場","examples":[{"en":"Mobile-phone apps allow companies to approach the market more quickly.","zh":"手提電話應用程式讓公司更快接觸市場。"},{"en":"To approach the market means to reach customers or enter a business area.","zh":"To approach the market 指接觸顧客或進入某商業領域。"},{"en":"A new bakery may approach the market through online orders before opening a shop.","zh":"新麵包店可能在開店前先透過網上訂單接觸市場。"},{"en":"If a company can approach the market quickly, it can test demand sooner.","zh":"如果公司能快速進入市場，它就可以更早測試需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the practical route into customers and business opportunities.","zh":"這個片語描述進入顧客和商機的實際途徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"go through middlemen","meaning":"經過中間人","examples":[{"en":"Companies do not have to go through as many middlemen.","zh":"公司不必經過那麼多中間人。"},{"en":"To go through middlemen means to use intermediaries between the company and the customer.","zh":"To go through middlemen 指在公司和顧客之間使用中介。"},{"en":"A farmer may avoid going through middlemen by selling vegetables directly online.","zh":"農民可能透過網上直接售賣蔬菜，避免經過中間人。"},{"en":"Fewer middlemen can mean lower costs and faster decisions.","zh":"較少中間人可以意味着較低成本和較快決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes depending on extra parties in a transaction.","zh":"這個片語描述在交易中依賴額外一方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"greedy middlemen","meaning":"貪婪的中間人","examples":[{"en":"Mobile apps reduce dependence on greedy middlemen.","zh":"流動應用程式減少對貪婪中間人的依賴。"},{"en":"Greedy middlemen are intermediaries who take too much money or control from a deal.","zh":"Greedy middlemen 是在交易中抽取過多金錢或控制權的中介。"},{"en":"A small shop may dislike greedy middlemen if delivery platforms charge high fees.","zh":"如果外賣平台收取高額費用，小店可能不喜歡貪婪的中間人。"},{"en":"If too many middlemen take a share, creators may earn too little.","zh":"如果太多中間人抽取份額，創作者可能賺得太少。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises intermediaries who seem unfairly profit-focused.","zh":"這個片語批評看似過分逐利的中介。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"providers of set-top box technology","meaning":"機頂盒技術供應商","examples":[{"en":"Providers of set-top box technology are adding texting functionality.","zh":"機頂盒技術供應商正在加入短訊功能。"},{"en":"Providers of set-top box technology are companies that make or supply the devices and systems connected to TVs.","zh":"Providers of set-top box technology 是製造或供應連接電視的裝置和系統的公司。"},{"en":"A technology provider may update its product when customers prefer mobile interaction.","zh":"當顧客較喜歡手機互動，技術供應商可能更新產品。"},{"en":"If texting becomes popular, set-top-box companies must adapt to remain useful.","zh":"如果短訊變得受歡迎，機頂盒公司必須適應，才能保持有用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to firms supplying older interactive-TV hardware.","zh":"這個片語指供應較舊互動電視硬件的公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"texting functionality","meaning":"短訊功能","examples":[{"en":"Set-top box providers are adding texting functionality to their products.","zh":"機頂盒供應商正在為產品加入短訊功能。"},{"en":"Texting functionality means the ability of a device or service to send, receive, or process text messages.","zh":"Texting functionality 指裝置或服務發送、接收或處理短訊的能力。"},{"en":"A school app with texting functionality can send parents quick reminders.","zh":"具有短訊功能的學校應用程式可以向家長發送快速提醒。"},{"en":"Adding texting functionality helps older technology compete with phone-based services.","zh":"加入短訊功能有助較舊科技與電話服務競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a technical feature related to SMS.","zh":"這個片語描述與短訊有關的技術功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the design of their products","meaning":"產品設計","examples":[{"en":"Texting functionality is being added to the design of their products.","zh":"短訊功能正被加入他們的產品設計中。"},{"en":"The design of their products means how their products are planned, built, and made to work.","zh":"The design of their products 指他們的產品如何被規劃、建造和設計運作。"},{"en":"A phone company may change the design of its products after users complain about battery life.","zh":"用戶投訴電池續航力後，電話公司可能改變產品設計。"},{"en":"If texting is added to product design, the device becomes more interactive.","zh":"如果短訊被加入產品設計，裝置就變得更互動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the structure and features built into a product.","zh":"這個片語指產品中建構出的結構和功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the triumph of","meaning":"……的勝利；……的成功","examples":[{"en":"The triumph of TV-related texting shows the power of simple technology.","zh":"與電視相關短訊的成功顯示簡單科技的力量。"},{"en":"The triumph of something means its great success after competition or difficulty.","zh":"The triumph of something 指某事在競爭或困難後取得巨大成功。"},{"en":"The triumph of online booking changed how people buy cinema tickets.","zh":"網上訂票的成功改變了人們購買電影票的方式。"},{"en":"If simple texting beats expensive interactive systems, it shows practicality matters.","zh":"如果簡單短訊勝過昂貴互動系統，就顯示實用性很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear victory or success.","zh":"這個片語描述清楚的勝利或成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"remind everyone in the business of","meaning":"提醒業內所有人","examples":[{"en":"The trend reminds everyone in the business of how quickly technology can change.","zh":"這種趨勢提醒業內所有人科技可以變化得多快。"},{"en":"To remind everyone in the business of something means to make industry people remember or notice it again.","zh":"To remind everyone in the business of something 指令業界人士重新記起或注意某事。"},{"en":"A failed product may remind everyone in the business of the importance of listening to customers.","zh":"失敗產品可能提醒業內所有人聆聽顧客的重要性。"},{"en":"When simple technology succeeds, experts may rethink their assumptions.","zh":"當簡單科技成功，專家可能重新思考自己的假設。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lesson for people working in an industry.","zh":"這個片語描述給某行業從業者的一課。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"fancy technology","meaning":"花巧的技術","examples":[{"en":"A fancy technology can be replaced by a simpler method.","zh":"花巧的技術可以被較簡單的方法取代。"},{"en":"Fancy technology means advanced, complicated, or impressive-looking technology.","zh":"Fancy technology 指先進、複雜或看起來令人印象深刻的技術。"},{"en":"A school does not need fancy technology if a whiteboard and clear explanation work better.","zh":"如果白板和清楚解釋更有效，學校不需要花巧的技術。"},{"en":"Fancy technology can fail when it is expensive, confusing, or hard to access.","zh":"當花巧的技術昂貴、令人混亂或難以接觸，它可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase can be slightly critical when impressive technology is less practical than a simple tool.","zh":"當令人印象深刻的技術不如簡單工具實用時，這個片語可帶少許批評意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be replaced by","meaning":"被……取代","examples":[{"en":"Complex technology can suddenly be replaced by a lower-tech method.","zh":"複雜技術可以突然被較低科技的方法取代。"},{"en":"To be replaced by something means to be removed or made less important because another thing takes its place.","zh":"To be replaced by something 指因另一事物取而代之，而被移除或變得較不重要。"},{"en":"Paper forms may be replaced by online forms in a school office.","zh":"學校辦公室的紙本表格可能被網上表格取代。"},{"en":"If viewers prefer texting, expensive interactive boxes may lose importance.","zh":"如果觀眾較喜歡短訊，昂貴互動機頂盒可能失去重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one thing taking over the role of another.","zh":"這個片語描述一事物接替另一事物的角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"less complicated","meaning":"較不複雜的","examples":[{"en":"A less complicated method may succeed where expensive technology fails.","zh":"較不複雜的方法可能在昂貴科技失敗的地方成功。"},{"en":"Less complicated means simpler and easier to understand or use.","zh":"Less complicated 指更簡單、更容易理解或使用。"},{"en":"A less complicated timetable may help students arrive at classes on time.","zh":"較不複雜的時間表可能幫助學生準時上課。"},{"en":"If a system is easy, more ordinary users may adopt it.","zh":"如果系統容易使用，更多普通用戶可能採用它。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts simplicity with unnecessary complexity.","zh":"這個片語把簡單與不必要的複雜作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"lower-tech method","meaning":"較低科技的方法","examples":[{"en":"Texting is a lower-tech method that works well with television.","zh":"短訊是一種與電視配合良好的較低科技方法。"},{"en":"A lower-tech method uses simpler or less advanced technology than another method.","zh":"Lower-tech method 指使用比另一方法較簡單或較不先進科技的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may use flashcards as a lower-tech method instead of a learning app.","zh":"老師可能使用字卡作為較低科技的方法，而不是學習應用程式。"},{"en":"Lower-tech methods can succeed when they are cheap, familiar, and easy to use.","zh":"當較低科技方法便宜、熟悉且容易使用，它們可以成功。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that simpler technology can sometimes be more effective.","zh":"這個片語顯示較簡單科技有時可以更有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"that being said","meaning":"話雖如此","examples":[{"en":"That being said, the old approach to interactive TV is not necessarily over.","zh":"話雖如此，互動電視的舊方法未必已經結束。"},{"en":"That being said introduces a contrast or qualification after the previous point.","zh":"That being said 用來在前一點之後引出對比或補充限制。"},{"en":"Online lessons are convenient; that being said, face-to-face practice is still valuable.","zh":"網上課堂很方便；話雖如此，面對面練習仍然有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase helps balance an argument instead of making it one-sided.","zh":"這個片語幫助平衡論點，而不是令它單方面。"},{"en":"In the passage, it softens the idea that texting has completely replaced older systems.","zh":"在文章中，它柔化短訊已完全取代舊系統的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"old-fashioned approach","meaning":"舊式方法","examples":[{"en":"The old-fashioned approach to interactive TV may still survive.","zh":"互動電視的舊式方法可能仍然存在。"},{"en":"An old-fashioned approach is an older method that may seem outdated but can still work.","zh":"Old-fashioned approach 是看似過時但仍可能有效的舊方法。"},{"en":"Some teachers use an old-fashioned approach, such as handwriting notes, because it helps memory.","zh":"有些老師使用舊式方法，例如手寫筆記，因為它有助記憶。"},{"en":"A method may look old-fashioned but remain useful for certain users.","zh":"某方法可能看似舊式，但對某些用戶仍有用。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts older methods with newer technology.","zh":"這個片語把舊方法與新科技作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"not necessarily over","meaning":"未必已經結束","examples":[{"en":"The old-fashioned approach is not necessarily over.","zh":"舊式方法未必已經結束。"},{"en":"Not necessarily over means not definitely finished or dead.","zh":"Not necessarily over 指不一定已經完結或消失。"},{"en":"Paper books are not necessarily over just because e-books are popular.","zh":"電子書流行並不代表紙本書未必已經結束。"},{"en":"If some viewers still use set-top systems, older interactive TV may continue.","zh":"如果一些觀眾仍使用機頂盒系統，較舊互動電視可能繼續存在。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against assuming that a trend has ended completely.","zh":"這個片語提醒不要假設某趨勢已完全結束。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"strong demand for","meaning":"對……有強烈需求","examples":[{"en":"There is still strong demand for interactive services.","zh":"對互動服務仍有強烈需求。"},{"en":"Strong demand for something means many people want or need it.","zh":"Strong demand for something 指許多人想要或需要某事物。"},{"en":"There is strong demand for after-school tutoring before public exams.","zh":"公開考試前，對課後補習有強烈需求。"},{"en":"If viewers strongly want interaction, companies will keep developing interactive tools.","zh":"如果觀眾強烈想要互動，公司會繼續開發互動工具。"},{"en":"This phrase describes high customer or audience interest.","zh":"這個片語描述高顧客或觀眾興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"interactive services","meaning":"互動服務","examples":[{"en":"Viewers clearly want more interactive services.","zh":"觀眾顯然想要更多互動服務。"},{"en":"Interactive services are services that let users respond, choose, vote, comment, or participate.","zh":"Interactive services 是讓用戶回應、選擇、投票、評論或參與的服務。"},{"en":"A school website with quizzes and feedback forms provides interactive services.","zh":"具有小測和回饋表格的學校網站提供互動服務。"},{"en":"If viewers want interactive services, simple one-way broadcasting may feel old.","zh":"如果觀眾想要互動服務，單向播放可能感覺陳舊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes services built around user participation.","zh":"這個片語描述圍繞用戶參與建立的服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"stare at the TV screen","meaning":"凝望電視螢幕","examples":[{"en":"Viewers want to do more than simply stare at the TV screen.","zh":"觀眾想做的不只是單純凝望電視螢幕。"},{"en":"To stare at the TV screen means to watch passively without doing anything else.","zh":"To stare at the TV screen 指被動觀看而不做其他事。"},{"en":"A tired student may stare at the screen without really listening to the lesson.","zh":"疲倦學生可能凝望螢幕，卻沒有真正聽課。"},{"en":"If viewers can text and vote, they are no longer just staring at the screen.","zh":"如果觀眾可以發短訊和投票，他們就不再只是凝望螢幕。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests passive watching rather than active involvement.","zh":"這個片語暗示被動觀看，而不是主動參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"after all","meaning":"畢竟","examples":[{"en":"After all, couch potatoes would love some thumb exercises.","zh":"畢竟，長時間坐着看電視的人會喜歡一些拇指運動。"},{"en":"After all introduces a reason that supports or explains the previous idea.","zh":"After all 用來引出支持或解釋前一想法的原因。"},{"en":"Students should bring water to sports day; after all, they will be outside for hours.","zh":"學生運動日應帶水；畢竟，他們會在戶外幾小時。"},{"en":"The phrase often makes the explanation feel natural or obvious.","zh":"這個片語常令解釋感覺自然或明顯。"},{"en":"In this sentence, it adds a humorous reason why viewers may enjoy texting.","zh":"在這句中，它加入一個幽默原因，解釋觀眾為何可能喜歡發短訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"couch potatoes","meaning":"長時間坐着看電視的人","examples":[{"en":"Couch potatoes may enjoy interacting with TV by text.","zh":"長時間坐着看電視的人可能享受透過短訊與電視互動。"},{"en":"Couch potatoes are people who spend a lot of time sitting and watching television.","zh":"Couch potatoes 是花很多時間坐着看電視的人。"},{"en":"A couch potato may watch several episodes on the sofa without moving much.","zh":"長時間坐着看電視的人可能坐在梳化上連看幾集而很少移動。"},{"en":"Texting gives couch potatoes a small way to participate without leaving the sofa.","zh":"短訊給長時間坐着看電視的人一種不用離開梳化也能參與的小方法。"},{"en":"This informal phrase is often humorous and slightly critical.","zh":"這個非正式片語常帶幽默和少許批評意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"thumb exercises","meaning":"拇指運動","examples":[{"en":"Texting gives couch potatoes some thumb exercises.","zh":"發短訊給長時間看電視的人一些拇指運動。"},{"en":"Thumb exercises here humorously means moving the thumbs while typing text messages.","zh":"Thumb exercises 在這裏幽默地指打短訊時移動拇指。"},{"en":"A viewer may joke that voting by text is their only exercise during a long TV night.","zh":"觀眾可能開玩笑說，短訊投票是他漫長電視夜中的唯一運動。"},{"en":"Because texting uses the thumbs, the phrase makes passive viewers sound slightly more active.","zh":"因為發短訊使用拇指，這個片語令被動觀眾聽起來稍微更主動。"},{"en":"This phrase is playful rather than a serious fitness term.","zh":"這個片語是玩笑式表達，而不是嚴肅健身術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct heading for each section.","zh":"考生為每個部分選出正確標題。"},{"en":"To choose the correct heading means to select the title that best summarises a paragraph or section.","zh":"To choose the correct heading 指選出最能概括段落或部分的標題。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should read the whole paragraph before choosing the heading.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先閱讀整段，才選標題。"},{"en":"If a heading is too narrow, it may miss the main idea.","zh":"如果標題太狹窄，它可能錯過主旨。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in IELTS-style reading tasks.","zh":"這個片語是 IELTS 式閱讀題中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The list of headings gives possible titles for the sections.","zh":"標題列表提供各部分可能的標題。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a set of title options that students match with paragraphs.","zh":"List of headings 是一組讓學生與段落配對的標題選項。"},{"en":"Students should eliminate headings that mention details but not the main idea.","zh":"學生應排除只提細節而非主旨的標題。"},{"en":"If there are more headings than sections, some options will not be used.","zh":"如果標題多於段落，一些選項將不會使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the answer bank in a heading-matching task.","zh":"這個片語描述標題配對題中的答案庫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the use of short codes","meaning":"短碼的使用","examples":[{"en":"One heading refers to the use of short codes on the TV screen.","zh":"其中一個標題提到電視螢幕上短碼的使用。"},{"en":"The use of short codes means how special short numbers are applied for texting services.","zh":"The use of short codes 指特別短號碼如何被應用於短訊服務。"},{"en":"A TV charity event may show the use of short codes by asking viewers to text a number to donate.","zh":"電視慈善活動可能要求觀眾發短訊到某號碼捐款，以展示短碼的使用。"},{"en":"Short codes work best when viewers can see and remember them easily.","zh":"當觀眾容易看見和記住短碼時，它們最有效。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the practical role of short numbers.","zh":"這個片語集中於短號碼的實際角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"on the TV screen","meaning":"在電視螢幕上","examples":[{"en":"Short codes are displayed on the TV screen.","zh":"短碼顯示在電視螢幕上。"},{"en":"On the TV screen means visible on the television display.","zh":"On the TV screen 指在電視顯示畫面上可見。"},{"en":"A news alert may appear on the TV screen during an important event.","zh":"重要事件期間，新聞提示可能出現在電視螢幕上。"},{"en":"If a voting number is on the TV screen, viewers can copy it immediately.","zh":"如果投票號碼在電視螢幕上，觀眾可以立即照着輸入。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where the information appears.","zh":"這個片語指出資訊出現的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"an overview of","meaning":"……的概述","examples":[{"en":"One heading gives an overview of a fast-growing business.","zh":"其中一個標題概述一項快速增長的業務。"},{"en":"An overview of something is a general summary of its main points.","zh":"Overview of something 是對某事主要重點的一般總結。"},{"en":"A teacher may give an overview of a chapter before students read the details.","zh":"老師可能在學生閱讀細節前，先概述一章內容。"},{"en":"An overview helps readers understand the big picture before focusing on examples.","zh":"概述幫助讀者在集中細節前理解大方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broad introduction rather than a detailed analysis.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛介紹，而不是詳細分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"fast-growing business","meaning":"快速增長的業務","examples":[{"en":"TV-texting has become a fast-growing business.","zh":"電視短訊互動已成為快速增長的業務。"},{"en":"A fast-growing business is a business that is expanding quickly in customers, revenue, or activity.","zh":"Fast-growing business 是在顧客、收入或活動方面快速擴展的業務。"},{"en":"A small delivery company may become a fast-growing business if many shops use its service.","zh":"如果許多商店使用某小型送貨公司的服務，它可能成為快速增長的業務。"},{"en":"When a business grows fast, competitors and investors quickly notice it.","zh":"當業務快速增長，競爭者和投資者很快會注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes commercial growth at high speed.","zh":"這個片語描述高速商業增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"profitable games","meaning":"有利可圖的遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Text-message games can become profitable games for broadcasters.","zh":"短訊遊戲可以成為廣播機構有利可圖的遊戲。"},{"en":"Profitable games are games that earn more money than they cost to run.","zh":"Profitable games 是賺取的錢多於營運成本的遊戲。"},{"en":"A school fair game becomes profitable if ticket sales are higher than the cost of prizes.","zh":"如果售票收入高於獎品成本，學校嘉年華遊戲就有利可圖。"},{"en":"If every text entry costs money, a simple TV game can produce strong revenue.","zh":"如果每次短訊參加都收費，簡單電視遊戲可以產生強勁收入。"},{"en":"This phrase connects entertainment with financial gain.","zh":"這個片語把娛樂與財務收益連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"take the leading role","meaning":"擔當領導角色","examples":[{"en":"One heading asks why the Netherlands takes the leading role.","zh":"其中一個標題問為何荷蘭擔當領導角色。"},{"en":"To take the leading role means to become the main or most important player in a development.","zh":"To take the leading role 指成為某發展中的主要或最重要參與者。"},{"en":"A school may take the leading role in a recycling campaign if it organises other schools.","zh":"如果一間學校組織其他學校參與回收活動，它可能擔當領導角色。"},{"en":"If a country or company develops the strongest systems first, it may lead the market.","zh":"如果某國或公司最先發展最強系統，它可能引領市場。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being at the front of an activity or trend.","zh":"這個片語描述站在活動或趨勢前方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a new perspective on","meaning":"對……的新看法","examples":[{"en":"The heading suggests a new perspective on sharing business opportunities.","zh":"該標題暗示對分享商機的新看法。"},{"en":"A new perspective on something is a fresh way of understanding or thinking about it.","zh":"New perspective on something 是理解或思考某事的新方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may offer a new perspective on mistakes by treating them as learning clues.","zh":"老師可能透過把錯誤視為學習線索，提供對錯誤的新看法。"},{"en":"If providers see sharing as growth instead of loss, their business strategy changes.","zh":"如果供應商把分享視為增長而非損失，它們的商業策略就會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a changed way of viewing a topic.","zh":"這個片語描述對某題目的觀點改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"business opportunities","meaning":"商機","examples":[{"en":"Providers are sharing business opportunities created by TV-texting.","zh":"供應商正在分享由電視短訊互動創造的商機。"},{"en":"Business opportunities are chances to earn money, enter markets, or build new services.","zh":"Business opportunities 是賺錢、進入市場或建立新服務的機會。"},{"en":"A new railway station can create business opportunities for shops nearby.","zh":"新鐵路站可以為附近商店創造商機。"},{"en":"If TV-texting grows, broadcasters, operators, and technology firms may all benefit.","zh":"如果電視短訊互動增長，廣播機構、營運商和科技公司都可能受益。"},{"en":"This phrase describes openings for commercial success.","zh":"這個片語描述商業成功的機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"revenue gains","meaning":"收入收益","examples":[{"en":"TV-texting creates revenue gains for several parties.","zh":"電視短訊互動為幾方創造收入收益。"},{"en":"Revenue gains are increases in income earned by a business or organisation.","zh":"Revenue gains 是企業或組織賺取收入的增加。"},{"en":"A school bookshop may see revenue gains after offering online ordering.","zh":"學校書店提供網上訂購後，可能看到收入收益。"},{"en":"If each text generates money, all partners may receive revenue gains.","zh":"如果每條短訊都產生金錢，所有合作方都可能獲得收入收益。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on improved income.","zh":"這個片語集中於收入改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"profit sharing","meaning":"利潤分成","examples":[{"en":"Profit sharing is a key issue in TV-texting.","zh":"利潤分成是電視短訊互動中的關鍵問題。"},{"en":"Profit sharing means dividing profits among people or organisations involved in a business.","zh":"Profit sharing 指在參與業務的人或組織之間分配利潤。"},{"en":"A group project business stall may need profit sharing after all costs are paid.","zh":"小組專題售賣攤位在支付所有成本後，可能需要利潤分成。"},{"en":"If profit sharing feels unfair, partners may argue or leave the arrangement.","zh":"如果利潤分成感覺不公平，合作方可能爭論或離開安排。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how financial benefits are split.","zh":"這個片語描述財務收益如何分配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"factors relevant to","meaning":"與……相關的因素","examples":[{"en":"The heading refers to factors relevant to the increase in interactive TV.","zh":"該標題指與互動電視增加相關的因素。"},{"en":"Factors relevant to something are reasons or conditions connected with it.","zh":"Factors relevant to something 是與某事有關的原因或條件。"},{"en":"Sleep, practice, and confidence are factors relevant to speaking-test performance.","zh":"睡眠、練習和自信是與口語考試表現相關的因素。"},{"en":"If several factors support TV-texting, its rapid growth becomes easier to explain.","zh":"如果幾個因素支持電視短訊互動，它的快速增長就更容易解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes causes or conditions that matter to a topic.","zh":"這個片語描述對某題目重要的原因或條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"rapid increase in","meaning":"……的快速增加","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains the rapid increase in interactive TV.","zh":"文章解釋互動電視的快速增加。"},{"en":"A rapid increase in something means a quick rise in its amount, use, or importance.","zh":"Rapid increase in something 指某事物的數量、使用或重要性快速上升。"},{"en":"A rapid increase in online homework may happen after a school introduces tablets.","zh":"學校引入平板電腦後，網上功課可能快速增加。"},{"en":"If interactive TV increases rapidly, companies must adapt quickly.","zh":"如果互動電視快速增加，公司必須迅速適應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fast growth in a particular area.","zh":"這個片語描述某一領域中的快速增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"complex technology","meaning":"複雜技術","examples":[{"en":"Complex technology may be replaced by simpler alternatives.","zh":"複雜技術可能被較簡單的替代方案取代。"},{"en":"Complex technology is technology with many parts, difficult systems, or specialist requirements.","zh":"Complex technology 是包含許多部分、困難系統或專業要求的技術。"},{"en":"A complex learning platform may confuse students if a simple shared document would work.","zh":"如果一份簡單共用文件已經可行，複雜學習平台可能令學生混亂。"},{"en":"If technology is too complex, users may avoid it even when it is powerful.","zh":"如果技術太複雜，即使功能強大，用戶也可能避免使用。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts complicated systems with easier tools.","zh":"這個片語把複雜系統與較容易工具作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"simpler alternatives","meaning":"較簡單的替代方案","examples":[{"en":"Text messaging can be a simpler alternative to set-top boxes.","zh":"短訊可以是機頂盒較簡單的替代方案。"},{"en":"Simpler alternatives are easier options that can replace a more complicated method.","zh":"Simpler alternatives 是可以取代較複雜方法的更容易選項。"},{"en":"A teacher may use paper flashcards as a simpler alternative to an app that often crashes.","zh":"如果應用程式經常故障，老師可能使用紙本字卡作為較簡單的替代方案。"},{"en":"If a simpler alternative is cheaper and easier, it may spread faster.","zh":"如果較簡單的替代方案更便宜和更容易，它可能擴散更快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical substitutes with less complexity.","zh":"這個片語描述複雜度較低的實用替代品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a change of mind among","meaning":"……之中的想法轉變","examples":[{"en":"The heading describes a change of mind among service providers.","zh":"該標題描述服務供應商之中的想法轉變。"},{"en":"A change of mind among a group means that the group has begun to think differently.","zh":"A change of mind among a group 指某群體開始以不同方式思考。"},{"en":"A change of mind among teachers may happen after they see students learn better with examples.","zh":"老師看見學生用例子學得更好後，教師之中可能出現想法轉變。"},{"en":"If providers first protected margins but later shared revenue, their thinking changed.","zh":"如果供應商最初保護利潤率，但後來分享收入，它們的想法就改變了。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift in attitude or opinion within a group.","zh":"這個片語描述群體內態度或意見的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"set-top-box providers","meaning":"機頂盒供應商","examples":[{"en":"Set-top-box providers are now adding texting functionality.","zh":"機頂盒供應商現在正在加入短訊功能。"},{"en":"Set-top-box providers are companies that supply devices connected to TVs for digital or interactive services.","zh":"Set-top-box providers 是供應連接電視、用於數碼或互動服務的裝置的公司。"},{"en":"Set-top-box providers may update their products when viewers prefer phone-based interaction.","zh":"當觀眾較喜歡電話互動，機頂盒供應商可能更新產品。"},{"en":"If their devices lack texting features, they may lose business to simpler mobile systems.","zh":"如果它們的裝置缺乏短訊功能，它們可能把生意輸給較簡單的流動系統。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to firms connected with set-top-box technology.","zh":"這個片語指與機頂盒技術相關的公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"research suggests that","meaning":"研究顯示","examples":[{"en":"Research suggests that young audiences use texting heavily.","zh":"研究顯示年輕觀眾大量使用短訊。"},{"en":"Research suggests that means evidence points to a likely conclusion without necessarily proving it completely.","zh":"Research suggests that 指證據指向可能結論，但未必完全證明。"},{"en":"Research suggests that students remember vocabulary better when examples are concrete.","zh":"研究顯示，當例子具體時，學生記詞彙記得更好。"},{"en":"If research suggests heavy texting among youth, TV companies may target them through SMS.","zh":"如果研究顯示年輕人大量發短訊，電視公司可能透過短訊以他們為目標。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a careful evidence-based claim.","zh":"這個片語引出謹慎而有證據支持的主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"young audiences","meaning":"年輕觀眾","examples":[{"en":"Young audiences often interact with TV through text messages.","zh":"年輕觀眾常透過短訊與電視互動。"},{"en":"Young audiences are viewers who are children, teenagers, or young adults.","zh":"Young audiences 是兒童、青少年或年輕成年人觀眾。"},{"en":"Music shows may target young audiences with social media clips and text voting.","zh":"音樂節目可能透過社交媒體短片和短訊投票以年輕觀眾為目標。"},{"en":"If young audiences already use mobile phones heavily, texting becomes an easy way to reach them.","zh":"如果年輕觀眾本來已大量使用手提電話，短訊就成為接觸他們的簡單方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a youthful viewer group.","zh":"這個片語描述年輕觀眾群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"spend more money on","meaning":"在……上花更多錢","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what young audiences spend more money on.","zh":"題目問年輕觀眾在甚麼上花更多錢。"},{"en":"To spend more money on something means to use a larger amount of money for it than for another thing.","zh":"To spend more money on something 指在某事上使用比另一事更多金錢。"},{"en":"Some students spend more money on snacks than on books.","zh":"有些學生在零食上花的錢多於書本。"},{"en":"If young viewers spend more money on texting, TV shows may see SMS as a business opportunity.","zh":"如果年輕觀眾在短訊上花更多錢，電視節目可能把短訊視為商機。"},{"en":"This phrase compares spending habits.","zh":"這個片語比較消費習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"write e-mails","meaning":"寫電郵","examples":[{"en":"Young audiences are using text messages rather than writing e-mails to shows.","zh":"年輕觀眾正在使用短訊，而不是寫電郵給節目。"},{"en":"To write e-mails means to compose and send electronic messages through e-mail.","zh":"To write e-mails 指撰寫並透過電郵發送電子訊息。"},{"en":"Students may write e-mails to teachers when they need help after class.","zh":"學生課後需要幫助時，可能寫電郵給老師。"},{"en":"If texting is faster than writing e-mails, young viewers may prefer it for TV interaction.","zh":"如果發短訊比寫電郵更快，年輕觀眾可能較喜歡用它與電視互動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a more formal or older digital communication method.","zh":"這個片語描述較正式或較舊的數碼溝通方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"watch TV programmes","meaning":"觀看電視節目","examples":[{"en":"Viewers can interact while they watch TV programmes.","zh":"觀眾可以在觀看電視節目時互動。"},{"en":"To watch TV programmes means to view television shows or broadcasts.","zh":"To watch TV programmes 指觀看電視節目或廣播。"},{"en":"Families may watch TV programmes together after dinner.","zh":"家庭可能在晚飯後一起觀看電視節目。"},{"en":"If viewers can text while watching, the programme becomes more interactive.","zh":"如果觀眾可以邊看邊發短訊，節目就變得更互動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordinary television viewing.","zh":"這個片語描述普通電視觀看。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"talk on mobile phones","meaning":"用手提電話通話","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to talking on mobile phones.","zh":"該選項指用手提電話通話。"},{"en":"To talk on mobile phones means to speak to someone using a mobile phone call.","zh":"To talk on mobile phones 指使用手提電話通話與人說話。"},{"en":"A parent may talk on a mobile phone while waiting outside school.","zh":"家長可能在學校外等候時用手提電話通話。"},{"en":"TV-texting uses written messages, not necessarily talking on mobile phones.","zh":"電視短訊互動使用文字訊息，不一定是用手提電話通話。"},{"en":"This phrase describes voice communication rather than text communication.","zh":"這個片語描述語音通訊，而不是文字通訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"invite the audience to vote","meaning":"邀請觀眾投票","examples":[{"en":"Reality TV shows invite the audience to vote.","zh":"真人騷節目邀請觀眾投票。"},{"en":"To invite the audience to vote means to ask viewers to choose an option or contestant.","zh":"To invite the audience to vote 指要求觀眾選擇某個選項或參賽者。"},{"en":"A school talent show may invite the audience to vote for the best performance.","zh":"學校才藝表演可能邀請觀眾投票選出最佳表演。"},{"en":"If viewers vote, they can influence the result and feel involved.","zh":"如果觀眾投票，他們可以影響結果並感到參與其中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common interactive-TV technique.","zh":"這個片語描述常見互動電視技巧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"get an attractive bonus","meaning":"獲得吸引的獎勵","examples":[{"en":"One option says viewers would get an attractive bonus.","zh":"其中一個選項說觀眾會獲得吸引的獎勵。"},{"en":"To get an attractive bonus means to receive an extra reward that seems appealing.","zh":"To get an attractive bonus 指獲得看起來吸引的額外獎勵。"},{"en":"A shop may offer customers an attractive bonus, such as free delivery, for joining a membership scheme.","zh":"商店可能為加入會員計劃的顧客提供吸引的獎勵，例如免費送貨。"},{"en":"Bonuses can encourage participation, but they are not always the main reason people join.","zh":"獎勵可以鼓勵參與，但它們不一定總是人們參加的主要原因。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an appealing extra benefit.","zh":"這個片語描述吸引人的額外好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"change the result","meaning":"改變結果","examples":[{"en":"Viewers’ participation can change the result of a reality TV show.","zh":"觀眾參與可以改變真人騷節目的結果。"},{"en":"To change the result means to alter the final outcome.","zh":"To change the result 指改變最終結果。"},{"en":"One extra vote can change the result of a class election.","zh":"多一票可以改變班會選舉結果。"},{"en":"If thousands of viewers vote by text, they may decide who wins or leaves.","zh":"如果數以千計觀眾透過短訊投票，他們可能決定誰勝出或離開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes real influence over the final decision.","zh":"這個片語描述對最終決定的實際影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"concentrate on","meaning":"專注於","examples":[{"en":"Interactive TV may stop concentrating mainly on set-top devices.","zh":"互動電視可能不再主要專注於機頂盒裝置。"},{"en":"To concentrate on something means to focus attention, effort, or resources on it.","zh":"To concentrate on something 指把注意力、努力或資源集中於某事。"},{"en":"A student may concentrate on grammar before moving on to essay style.","zh":"學生可能先專注於文法，然後再處理文章風格。"},{"en":"If companies stop concentrating on set-top boxes, they may invest more in mobile interaction.","zh":"如果公司不再專注於機頂盒，它們可能更多投資於流動互動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where attention or effort is placed.","zh":"這個片語描述注意力或努力放在哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"set-top devices","meaning":"機頂盒裝置","examples":[{"en":"Interactive TV once concentrated on set-top devices.","zh":"互動電視曾經專注於機頂盒裝置。"},{"en":"Set-top devices are electronic boxes or equipment connected to a television to add services.","zh":"Set-top devices 是接駁到電視以增加服務的電子盒或設備。"},{"en":"A household may use set-top devices to receive paid channels or interactive menus.","zh":"家庭可能使用機頂盒裝置接收收費頻道或互動選單。"},{"en":"If mobile phones are more common than set-top devices, TV companies may change strategy.","zh":"如果手提電話比機頂盒裝置更普及，電視公司可能改變策略。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to hardware-based television technology.","zh":"這個片語指以硬件為基礎的電視技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"modified set-top box","meaning":"改良版機頂盒","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions a modified set-top box.","zh":"該選項提到改良版機頂盒。"},{"en":"A modified set-top box is a set-top box that has been changed or improved for a new function.","zh":"Modified set-top box 是為新功能而被改動或改進的機頂盒。"},{"en":"A modified classroom computer may include special software for students with visual difficulties.","zh":"改良版課室電腦可能包含供視障學生使用的特殊軟件。"},{"en":"If a set-top box is modified to handle text messages, it may compete with mobile-phone services.","zh":"如果機頂盒被改良以處理短訊，它可能與手提電話服務競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an altered version of a television device.","zh":"這個片語描述電視裝置的改動版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"embedded message platform","meaning":"內置訊息平台","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions building an embedded message platform.","zh":"該選項提到建立內置訊息平台。"},{"en":"An embedded message platform is a messaging system built directly into another device or service.","zh":"Embedded message platform 是直接建入另一裝置或服務中的訊息系統。"},{"en":"A school app may include an embedded message platform so teachers can contact parents inside the app.","zh":"學校應用程式可能包括內置訊息平台，讓老師在應用程式內聯絡家長。"},{"en":"If messaging is embedded, users do not need a separate tool to respond.","zh":"如果訊息功能被內置，用戶不需要另一工具來回應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes messaging technology integrated into a larger system.","zh":"這個片語描述整合到較大系統中的訊息技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"march into","meaning":"進軍","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to marching into the European market.","zh":"該選項提到進軍歐洲市場。"},{"en":"To march into a market means to enter it confidently or aggressively.","zh":"To march into a market 指自信或強勢地進入某市場。"},{"en":"A new tutoring brand may march into the market by opening many branches at once.","zh":"新補習品牌可能透過一次開設多間分校進軍市場。"},{"en":"If a company enters too aggressively, competitors may react quickly.","zh":"如果公司進入市場太強勢，競爭者可能迅速反應。"},{"en":"This phrase gives market entry a strong and active feeling.","zh":"這個片語令市場進入帶有強烈和主動的感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"following descriptions","meaning":"以下描述","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match the following descriptions with companies.","zh":"考生把以下描述與公司配對。"},{"en":"Following descriptions means the descriptions listed after the instruction.","zh":"Following descriptions 指指示後列出的描述。"},{"en":"Students should read the following descriptions before looking for matching names in the passage.","zh":"學生應先閱讀以下描述，再在文章中尋找配對名稱。"},{"en":"If descriptions are paraphrased, students must match meaning rather than exact words.","zh":"如果描述被改寫，學生必須配對意思，而不是完全相同字詞。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces information that candidates need to use.","zh":"這個片語引出考生需要使用的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"match each description with","meaning":"將每項描述與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match each description with the correct company.","zh":"學生將每項描述與正確公司配對。"},{"en":"To match each description with something means to connect every statement to the right answer.","zh":"To match each description with something 指把每個陳述連接到正確答案。"},{"en":"In a reading task, students may match each description with a paragraph, person, or organisation.","zh":"在閱讀任務中，學生可能將每項描述與段落、人物或機構配對。"},{"en":"Accurate matching requires understanding meaning, not just spotting repeated words.","zh":"準確配對需要理解意思，而不只是找重複字詞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common exam task format.","zh":"這個片語描述常見考試題型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"correct company","meaning":"正確公司","examples":[{"en":"Each description should be matched with the correct company.","zh":"每項描述應與正確公司配對。"},{"en":"The correct company is the company that fits the information in the passage.","zh":"Correct company 是符合文章資訊的公司。"},{"en":"Students must check which company provided technology, earned revenue, or built a database.","zh":"學生必須檢查哪間公司提供技術、賺取收入或建立資料庫。"},{"en":"If two companies sound similar, careful reading is needed.","zh":"如果兩間公司聽起來相似，就需要仔細閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the right matching answer in a company-matching task.","zh":"這個片語指公司配對題中的正確配對答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"offer mobile-phone messaging technology","meaning":"提供手提電話短訊技術","examples":[{"en":"Some companies offer mobile-phone messaging technology to TV broadcasters.","zh":"一些公司向電視廣播機構提供手提電話短訊技術。"},{"en":"To offer mobile-phone messaging technology means to provide systems that let organisations send, receive, or process phone messages.","zh":"To offer mobile-phone messaging technology 指提供讓機構發送、接收或處理電話訊息的系統。"},{"en":"A technology firm may offer messaging tools to schools so parents receive notices quickly.","zh":"科技公司可能向學校提供短訊工具，讓家長快速收到通告。"},{"en":"If broadcasters use this technology, they can run votes and comments during programmes.","zh":"如果廣播機構使用這項技術，它們可以在節目期間進行投票和評論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes supplying SMS systems as a service.","zh":"這個片語描述把短訊系統作為服務提供。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"earn a considerable amount of money","meaning":"賺取相當多金錢","examples":[{"en":"A company earned a considerable amount of money through a famous programme.","zh":"一間公司透過一個著名節目賺取相當多金錢。"},{"en":"To earn a considerable amount of money means to make a large and important sum.","zh":"To earn a considerable amount of money 指賺取大而重要的金額。"},{"en":"A school charity concert may earn a considerable amount of money if many families buy tickets.","zh":"如果許多家庭購買門票，學校慈善音樂會可能賺取相當多金錢。"},{"en":"If a programme creates millions of paid texts, a company can earn a lot from it.","zh":"如果節目產生數百萬條付費短訊，公司可以從中賺很多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes significant financial gain.","zh":"這個片語描述顯著財務收益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"through a famous programme","meaning":"透過一個著名節目","examples":[{"en":"The operator earned money through a famous TV programme.","zh":"該營運商透過一個著名電視節目賺錢。"},{"en":"Through a famous programme means by means of or because of a well-known show.","zh":"Through a famous programme 指憑藉或因為一個知名節目。"},{"en":"A singer may become popular through a famous talent programme.","zh":"歌手可能透過一個著名才藝節目變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"If a phone company benefits through a famous programme, the show has commercial value beyond broadcasting.","zh":"如果電話公司透過一個著名節目受益，該節目的商業價值就超越播放本身。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the channel or source of success.","zh":"這個片語指出成功的渠道或來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"express the view that","meaning":"表達……的看法","examples":[{"en":"A company expressed the view that short codes are easy to remember.","zh":"一間公司表達短碼容易記住的看法。"},{"en":"To express the view that means to state an opinion or belief.","zh":"To express the view that 指陳述一個意見或信念。"},{"en":"A teacher may express the view that examples are more useful than long definitions.","zh":"老師可能表達例子比長定義更有用的看法。"},{"en":"If a company expresses a view, it is giving its interpretation of the market.","zh":"如果公司表達看法，它是在給出自己對市場的解讀。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces someone’s opinion rather than a direct fact.","zh":"這個片語引出某人的意見，而不是直接事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"convenient to remember","meaning":"方便記住","examples":[{"en":"Short codes are convenient to remember when displayed on screen.","zh":"短碼顯示在螢幕上時方便記住。"},{"en":"Convenient to remember means easy to keep in mind and use quickly.","zh":"Convenient to remember 指容易記在腦中並快速使用。"},{"en":"A short password is convenient to remember, though it may not always be safe.","zh":"短密碼方便記住，雖然不一定安全。"},{"en":"If a code is convenient to remember, viewers are more likely to send a message.","zh":"如果號碼方便記住，觀眾更可能發送訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes memory-friendly information.","zh":"這個片語描述容易記憶的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"displayed on screen","meaning":"顯示在螢幕上","examples":[{"en":"Short codes are displayed on screen during TV programmes.","zh":"短碼在電視節目期間顯示在螢幕上。"},{"en":"Displayed on screen means shown visually on a television, computer, or phone screen.","zh":"Displayed on screen 指在電視、電腦或手機螢幕上視覺顯示。"},{"en":"During a lesson, key vocabulary may be displayed on screen for students to copy.","zh":"課堂期間，重點詞彙可能顯示在螢幕上，讓學生抄下。"},{"en":"If a number is displayed on screen, viewers can respond without searching elsewhere.","zh":"如果號碼顯示在螢幕上，觀眾不用到其他地方搜尋也能回應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information being visually presented.","zh":"這個片語描述資訊被視覺呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"build its own mobile-user database","meaning":"建立自己的手提電話用戶資料庫","examples":[{"en":"Endemol built its own mobile-user database.","zh":"Endemol 建立了自己的手提電話用戶資料庫。"},{"en":"To build its own mobile-user database means to create a company-controlled list of mobile users and their details.","zh":"To build its own mobile-user database 指建立一份由公司控制的手提電話用戶及其資料清單。"},{"en":"A school may build its own parent-contact database instead of relying on paper forms.","zh":"學校可能建立自己的家長聯絡資料庫，而不是依賴紙本表格。"},{"en":"If a company owns the database, it can contact users directly and reduce dependence on providers.","zh":"如果公司擁有資料庫，它可以直接聯絡用戶，並減少對供應商的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gaining control over user information.","zh":"這個片語描述取得對用戶資料的控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"mobile-user database","meaning":"手提電話用戶資料庫","examples":[{"en":"A mobile-user database allows a company to contact users directly.","zh":"手提電話用戶資料庫讓公司可以直接聯絡用戶。"},{"en":"A mobile-user database is a collection of information about people who use mobile-phone services.","zh":"Mobile-user database 是關於使用手提電話服務人士的資料集合。"},{"en":"A company may use a mobile-user database to send voting reminders or promotions.","zh":"公司可能使用手提電話用戶資料庫發送投票提醒或宣傳。"},{"en":"If the database is accurate, messages reach the right users more effectively.","zh":"如果資料庫準確，訊息會更有效到達正確用戶。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised data about mobile customers or participants.","zh":"這個片語指關於流動電話顧客或參與者的有組織數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"indicate that","meaning":"表示；指出","examples":[{"en":"Gartner indicated that texting is an easy way to interact with TV.","zh":"Gartner 表示短訊是與電視互動的簡單方式。"},{"en":"To indicate that means to show, suggest, or state something.","zh":"To indicate that 指顯示、暗示或指出某事。"},{"en":"A student’s repeated errors may indicate that the grammar point has not been understood.","zh":"學生反覆出錯可能表示文法點尚未被理解。"},{"en":"If research indicates a simple interaction method, companies may adopt it quickly.","zh":"如果研究指出一種簡單互動方法，公司可能快速採用。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces evidence, signs, or a stated conclusion.","zh":"這個片語引出證據、跡象或明示結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"while watching interactive TV","meaning":"觀看互動電視時","examples":[{"en":"People can send messages while watching interactive TV.","zh":"人們可以在觀看互動電視時發送訊息。"},{"en":"While watching interactive TV means during the time when viewers are watching a programme that allows responses.","zh":"While watching interactive TV 指觀眾觀看容許回應的節目期間。"},{"en":"A viewer may vote for a contestant while watching interactive TV at home.","zh":"觀眾可能在家觀看互動電視時為參賽者投票。"},{"en":"If people can respond while watching, the programme feels immediate and engaging.","zh":"如果人們可以邊看邊回應，節目就感覺即時而吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase connects the viewing moment with live participation.","zh":"這個片語把觀看時刻與即時參與連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 58 - Texting the Television.pdf","sourcePage":22}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 59":[{"front":"Preparing for the Threat","meaning":"為威脅作準備","examples":[{"en":"Preparing for the threat of natural disasters requires careful international planning.","zh":"為自然災害的威脅作準備，需要仔細的國際規劃。"},{"en":"Preparing for the threat means getting ready before a danger actually happens.","zh":"Preparing for the threat 指在危險真正發生前做好準備。"},{"en":"A school prepares for the threat of fire by holding drills and checking exits.","zh":"學校透過舉行演習和檢查出口，為火警威脅作準備。"},{"en":"If communities prepare for the threat early, fewer people may be injured when disaster strikes.","zh":"如果社區及早為威脅作準備，災害發生時受傷人數可能較少。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses planning before danger, not reacting only after damage is done.","zh":"這個片語強調在危險前規劃，而不是只在損害發生後反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an unfortunate fact","meaning":"令人遺憾的事實","examples":[{"en":"It is an unfortunate fact that millions of people are affected by natural disasters each year.","zh":"每年有數百萬人受自然災害影響，這是令人遺憾的事實。"},{"en":"An unfortunate fact is a true situation that is sad, serious, or disappointing.","zh":"an unfortunate fact 指一個真實但令人難過、嚴重或失望的情況。"},{"en":"It is an unfortunate fact that some students cannot afford the books they need.","zh":"有些學生負擔不起所需書本，這是令人遺憾的事實。"},{"en":"When an unfortunate fact is recognised, people can start looking for practical solutions.","zh":"當令人遺憾的事實被承認，人們就可以開始尋找實際解決方法。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces bad news in a calm and factual way.","zh":"這個片語以平靜而事實性的方式引出壞消息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"over the past 20 years","meaning":"在過去二十年間","examples":[{"en":"Over the past 20 years, natural disasters have affected millions of people.","zh":"在過去二十年間，自然災害影響了數百萬人。"},{"en":"Over the past 20 years means during the most recent twenty-year period.","zh":"over the past 20 years 指在最近二十年期間。"},{"en":"Over the past 20 years, mobile phones have changed how students learn and communicate.","zh":"在過去二十年間，手機改變了學生學習和溝通的方式。"},{"en":"If a problem has grown over the past 20 years, it is not a short-term issue.","zh":"如果一個問題在過去二十年間增長，它就不是短期問題。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a recent historical time frame.","zh":"這個片語給出近代歷史時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"around 260 million people a year","meaning":"每年約二億六千萬人","examples":[{"en":"Around 260 million people a year have been affected by natural disasters.","zh":"每年約二億六千萬人受到自然災害影響。"},{"en":"Around 260 million people a year means approximately 260 million people every year.","zh":"around 260 million people a year 指每年大約二億六千萬人。"},{"en":"If around 1,000 students a year apply for a course, the school must plan enough places.","zh":"如果每年約1,000名學生申請某課程，學校必須規劃足夠學額。"},{"en":"A number this large shows that disaster impact is a global problem, not a rare event.","zh":"如此龐大的數字顯示災害影響是全球問題，而不是罕見事件。"},{"en":"The word “around” signals that the figure is approximate.","zh":"“around” 這個詞表示該數字是約數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be affected by","meaning":"受……影響","examples":[{"en":"Millions of people are affected by natural disasters every year.","zh":"每年有數百萬人受自然災害影響。"},{"en":"Be affected by means be changed, harmed, or influenced by something.","zh":"be affected by 指被某事改變、傷害或影響。"},{"en":"Students may be affected by noise if construction work happens beside the school.","zh":"如果學校旁邊有建築工程，學生可能受噪音影響。"},{"en":"If families are affected by floods, they may lose homes, jobs, or access to clean water.","zh":"如果家庭受水災影響，可能失去房屋、工作或清潔食水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the people or things that experience an impact.","zh":"這個片語描述經歷影響的人或事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"natural disasters","meaning":"自然災害","examples":[{"en":"Earthquakes, floods and tsunamis are examples of natural disasters.","zh":"地震、水災和海嘯都是自然災害的例子。"},{"en":"Natural disasters are major harmful events caused by natural forces, such as storms, earthquakes, or floods.","zh":"natural disasters 指由自然力量造成的重大有害事件，例如風暴、地震或洪水。"},{"en":"A village may prepare for natural disasters by storing water, food, and emergency tools.","zh":"村莊可以透過儲備水、食物和應急工具，為自然災害作準備。"},{"en":"Natural disasters can destroy homes, interrupt schools, and damage public services.","zh":"自然災害可以摧毀房屋、中斷學校運作並破壞公共服務。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to disasters from nature, not accidents caused only by human error.","zh":"這個片語指來自自然的災害，而不是純粹由人為錯誤造成的事故。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"around the world","meaning":"在世界各地","examples":[{"en":"Natural disasters affect people around the world.","zh":"自然災害影響世界各地的人。"},{"en":"Around the world means in many countries or regions globally.","zh":"around the world 指在全球許多國家或地區。"},{"en":"Students around the world use online lessons when schools close during emergencies.","zh":"當學校在緊急情況下停課，世界各地的學生都會使用網上課堂。"},{"en":"If a problem appears around the world, countries may need to share information and support.","zh":"如果問題在世界各地出現，各國可能需要分享資訊和支援。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a global scope.","zh":"這個片語給出全球範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"regrettably","meaning":"令人遺憾的是","examples":[{"en":"Regrettably, most victims of natural disasters are from developing countries.","zh":"令人遺憾的是，大多數自然災害受害者來自發展中國家。"},{"en":"Regrettably means sadly or unfortunately.","zh":"regrettably 指令人難過地或不幸地。"},{"en":"Regrettably, the school trip was cancelled because of severe weather.","zh":"令人遺憾的是，學校旅行因惡劣天氣而取消。"},{"en":"A writer uses “regrettably” to show that the fact is disappointing but true.","zh":"作者使用 “regrettably” 來表示該事實令人失望但是真實。"},{"en":"The word introduces bad news in a formal tone.","zh":"這個詞以正式語氣引出壞消息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a vast majority of","meaning":"絕大多數","examples":[{"en":"A vast majority of the victims are from developing countries.","zh":"絕大多數受害者來自發展中國家。"},{"en":"A vast majority of means a very large proportion of a group.","zh":"a vast majority of 指某群體中非常大的比例。"},{"en":"A vast majority of students passed the exam after months of practice.","zh":"經過數月練習後，絕大多數學生通過了考試。"},{"en":"If a vast majority of victims are poor, disaster planning must consider inequality.","zh":"如果絕大多數受害者是貧困人士，災害規劃就必須考慮不平等。"},{"en":"The phrase means much more than just “more than half.”","zh":"這個片語遠不只是「超過一半」的意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"victims","meaning":"受害者；災民","examples":[{"en":"Many victims of natural disasters live in poorer countries.","zh":"許多自然災害災民住在較貧窮國家。"},{"en":"Victims are people who are harmed, injured, killed, or made to suffer by an event or action.","zh":"victims 指因事件或行動而受傷、死亡、受害或受苦的人。"},{"en":"Victims of a house fire may need shelter, food, clothes, and emotional support.","zh":"房屋火災的受害者可能需要住所、食物、衣服和情緒支援。"},{"en":"If victims are not helped quickly, their suffering may become worse after the disaster.","zh":"如果災民沒有迅速獲得幫助，災後痛苦可能惡化。"},{"en":"The word focuses on people who suffer harm.","zh":"這個詞集中於遭受傷害的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"developing countries","meaning":"發展中國家","examples":[{"en":"Developing countries are often seriously affected by natural disasters.","zh":"發展中國家常受到自然災害嚴重影響。"},{"en":"Developing countries are countries with lower average income, fewer resources, or less developed infrastructure than richer countries.","zh":"developing countries 指平均收入較低、資源較少或基礎設施較不完善的國家。"},{"en":"A developing country may struggle to rebuild roads and hospitals after a major flood.","zh":"發展中國家在大型水災後，可能難以重建道路和醫院。"},{"en":"If disaster strikes a developing country, limited resources can make recovery slower.","zh":"如果災害打擊發展中國家，有限資源可能令復原較慢。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used when discussing poverty, infrastructure, and global inequality.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論貧窮、基礎設施和全球不平等。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"whether they are…or…","meaning":"不論是……還是……","examples":[{"en":"Whether they are earthquakes, floods or tsunamis, natural disasters affect millions of people.","zh":"不論是地震、水災還是海嘯，自然災害都影響數百萬人。"},{"en":"Whether they are A or B means it does not matter which type they are; the statement remains true.","zh":"whether they are A or B 指不管是哪一類，該陳述仍然成立。"},{"en":"Whether they are essays or speeches, students need clear ideas and good organisation.","zh":"不論是文章還是演講，學生都需要清楚想法和良好組織。"},{"en":"Whether disasters are sudden or slow, communities need preparation.","zh":"不論災害是突然還是緩慢，社區都需要準備。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to include different types under the same point.","zh":"這個片語用來把不同種類納入同一重點之下。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"earthquakes","meaning":"地震","examples":[{"en":"Earthquakes can cause widespread destruction.","zh":"地震可以造成大範圍破壞。"},{"en":"Earthquakes are sudden shaking movements of the ground caused by movement inside the Earth.","zh":"earthquakes 指由地球內部活動造成的地面突然震動。"},{"en":"A school in an earthquake zone may practise hiding under desks and evacuating safely.","zh":"位於地震帶的學校可能練習躲在桌下和安全疏散。"},{"en":"Strong earthquakes can damage buildings, roads, bridges, and water pipes.","zh":"強烈地震可以破壞建築物、道路、橋樑和水管。"},{"en":"The word refers to ground movement, not storms or floods.","zh":"這個詞指地面震動，而不是風暴或洪水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tornadoes","meaning":"龍捲風","examples":[{"en":"Tornadoes are among the natural disasters mentioned in the passage.","zh":"龍捲風是文章提到的自然災害之一。"},{"en":"Tornadoes are violent rotating columns of air that can damage buildings and vehicles.","zh":"tornadoes 指猛烈旋轉的氣柱，可以破壞建築物和車輛。"},{"en":"A family may hide in a basement when a tornado warning is issued.","zh":"當龍捲風警報發出，家庭可能躲進地庫。"},{"en":"Tornadoes can destroy homes within minutes because their winds are extremely powerful.","zh":"龍捲風的風力極強，可以在數分鐘內摧毀房屋。"},{"en":"The word refers to a fast-spinning wind disaster.","zh":"這個詞指快速旋轉的風災。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"floods","meaning":"水災；洪水","examples":[{"en":"Floods can affect large numbers of people.","zh":"水災可以影響大量人口。"},{"en":"Floods happen when water covers land that is usually dry.","zh":"floods 指水覆蓋通常乾燥的土地。"},{"en":"Heavy rain may cause floods that close roads and stop students from going to school.","zh":"大雨可能造成水災，封閉道路並阻止學生上學。"},{"en":"Floods can damage homes, crops, electricity systems, and clean-water supplies.","zh":"水災可以破壞房屋、農作物、電力系統和清潔食水供應。"},{"en":"The word refers to too much water in places where it should not be.","zh":"這個詞指過多水出現在不應有水的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"volcanic eruptions","meaning":"火山爆發","examples":[{"en":"Volcanic eruptions can be extremely destructive.","zh":"火山爆發可以極具破壞性。"},{"en":"Volcanic eruptions happen when lava, ash, gas, or rock is forced out of a volcano.","zh":"volcanic eruptions 指熔岩、火山灰、氣體或岩石從火山噴出。"},{"en":"People living near a volcano may need masks, evacuation plans, and emergency shelters.","zh":"住在火山附近的人可能需要口罩、疏散計劃和緊急庇護所。"},{"en":"A major eruption can cover farms with ash and make air dangerous to breathe.","zh":"大型火山爆發可以用火山灰覆蓋農田，並令空氣不適合呼吸。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to dangerous activity from a volcano.","zh":"這個片語指火山的危險活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tsunamis","meaning":"海嘯","examples":[{"en":"Tsunamis can cause deadly waves across coastal areas.","zh":"海嘯可以在沿海地區造成致命巨浪。"},{"en":"Tsunamis are very large sea waves usually caused by underwater earthquakes or volcanic activity.","zh":"tsunamis 指通常由海底地震或火山活動造成的巨大海浪。"},{"en":"Coastal schools may teach students to move to higher ground after a tsunami warning.","zh":"沿海學校可能教學生在海嘯警報後前往較高地勢。"},{"en":"Tsunamis can travel quickly and hit several countries around the same ocean.","zh":"海嘯可以快速傳播，並襲擊同一海洋周邊幾個國家。"},{"en":"The word refers to ocean waves caused by powerful natural events.","zh":"這個詞指由強大自然事件造成的海浪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"happen more frequently","meaning":"更頻繁發生","examples":[{"en":"Natural disasters have been happening more frequently than before.","zh":"自然災害比以前更頻繁發生。"},{"en":"Happen more frequently means occur more often.","zh":"happen more frequently 指更常發生。"},{"en":"If power cuts happen more frequently, residents may buy backup batteries.","zh":"如果停電更頻繁發生，居民可能購買後備電池。"},{"en":"When disasters happen more frequently, governments must improve warning systems and emergency plans.","zh":"當災害更頻繁發生，政府必須改善預警系統和應急計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an increase in how often something occurs.","zh":"這個片語描述某事發生次數增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"more people than ever before","meaning":"比以往任何時候更多人","examples":[{"en":"Natural disasters are affecting more people than ever before.","zh":"自然災害正影響比以往任何時候更多人。"},{"en":"More people than ever before means a larger number of people than at any earlier time.","zh":"more people than ever before 指人數比過去任何時候都多。"},{"en":"More students than ever before now use online tools for revision.","zh":"現在有比以往任何時候更多學生使用網上工具溫習。"},{"en":"If more people than ever before live in risky coastal areas, disasters may affect larger populations.","zh":"如果比以往任何時候更多人住在高風險沿海地區，災害可能影響更大人口。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises a record-high number.","zh":"這個片語強調創紀錄的高人數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"it follows that","meaning":"因此可見","examples":[{"en":"It follows that the international community should address disaster preparedness.","zh":"因此可見，國際社會應處理災害防備問題。"},{"en":"It follows that means this conclusion logically comes from the previous point.","zh":"it follows that 指這個結論從前一點合理得出。"},{"en":"If many students are confused, it follows that the teacher should explain the topic again.","zh":"如果許多學生感到困惑，因此可見老師應再次解釋該課題。"},{"en":"If disasters are affecting more people, it follows that better preparation is necessary.","zh":"如果災害正影響更多人，因此可見更好準備是必要的。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a logical result.","zh":"這個片語引出邏輯結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"international community","meaning":"國際社會","examples":[{"en":"The international community should work together on disaster preparedness.","zh":"國際社會應共同處理災害防備。"},{"en":"The international community means countries, global organisations, and other actors working on shared world issues.","zh":"international community 指共同處理世界議題的國家、全球組織和其他行動者。"},{"en":"The international community may send aid when a major earthquake destroys a city.","zh":"當大地震摧毀城市，國際社會可能運送援助。"},{"en":"If disasters cross borders, the international community must share warnings and resources.","zh":"如果災害跨越國界，國際社會必須分享警報和資源。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to global cooperation, not one country acting alone.","zh":"這個片語指全球合作，而不是單一國家獨自行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"address the issue of","meaning":"處理……問題","examples":[{"en":"Governments need to address the issue of disaster preparedness.","zh":"政府需要處理災害防備問題。"},{"en":"Address the issue of means deal with a problem seriously and directly.","zh":"address the issue of 指認真而直接地處理某問題。"},{"en":"A school may address the issue of bullying by creating clear reporting channels.","zh":"學校可能透過建立清楚舉報渠道來處理欺凌問題。"},{"en":"If governments address disaster preparedness, they can reduce avoidable deaths and damage.","zh":"如果政府處理災害防備，就能減少可避免的死亡和損害。"},{"en":"The phrase means more than mentioning a problem; it means taking action on it.","zh":"這個片語不只是提到問題，而是對它採取行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"disaster preparedness","meaning":"災害防備","examples":[{"en":"Disaster preparedness can reduce the damage caused by natural disasters.","zh":"災害防備可以減少自然災害造成的損害。"},{"en":"Disaster preparedness means planning, training, and organising resources before a disaster happens.","zh":"disaster preparedness 指在災害發生前作規劃、訓練和資源組織。"},{"en":"A hospital improves disaster preparedness by storing medicine and practising emergency procedures.","zh":"醫院透過儲備藥物和練習緊急程序來改善災害防備。"},{"en":"Good disaster preparedness can save lives because people know where to go and what to do.","zh":"良好災害防備可以拯救生命，因為人們知道該去哪裡和做甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on readiness before a disaster.","zh":"這個片語集中於災害前的準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"establish a process","meaning":"建立程序","examples":[{"en":"The international community should establish a process for dealing with disasters.","zh":"國際社會應建立處理災害的程序。"},{"en":"Establish a process means create a clear set of steps for handling something.","zh":"establish a process 指建立一套清楚步驟來處理某事。"},{"en":"A school may establish a process for reporting lost property.","zh":"學校可能建立程序來舉報失物。"},{"en":"If countries establish a process before disasters, help can arrive faster.","zh":"如果各國在災害前建立程序，援助就能更快到達。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses organised procedure, not random action.","zh":"這個片語強調有組織的程序，而不是隨機行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a process by which","meaning":"一個藉以……的程序","examples":[{"en":"Countries need a process by which natural disasters are dealt with.","zh":"各國需要一個藉以處理自然災害的程序。"},{"en":"A process by which means a method or set of steps through which something happens.","zh":"a process by which 指某事藉以發生的方法或一套步驟。"},{"en":"Schools need a process by which students can ask for help when they feel unsafe.","zh":"學校需要一個程序，讓學生在感到不安全時可以求助。"},{"en":"If there is a clear process by which aid is sent, confusion after disasters is reduced.","zh":"如果有清楚程序藉以運送援助，災後混亂就會減少。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the method used to achieve an outcome.","zh":"這個片語引出達成結果所用的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be dealt with","meaning":"被處理；被應對","examples":[{"en":"Natural disasters should be dealt with through careful preparation.","zh":"自然災害應透過仔細準備被應對。"},{"en":"Be dealt with means be handled, managed, or responded to.","zh":"be dealt with 指被處理、管理或回應。"},{"en":"A complaint should be dealt with quickly before a small problem becomes serious.","zh":"投訴應迅速處理，以免小問題變嚴重。"},{"en":"If disasters are dealt with poorly, recovery may take much longer.","zh":"如果災害處理不善，復原可能需時更久。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how a problem is managed.","zh":"這個片語集中於問題如何被管理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a massive earthquake","meaning":"大地震","examples":[{"en":"A massive earthquake caused a series of deadly tsunamis.","zh":"一場大地震造成一連串致命海嘯。"},{"en":"A massive earthquake is a very powerful earthquake that can cause huge damage.","zh":"massive earthquake 指非常強烈、可以造成巨大破壞的地震。"},{"en":"A city may lose bridges, hospitals, and power lines after a massive earthquake.","zh":"城市在大地震後可能失去橋樑、醫院和電線。"},{"en":"If a massive earthquake occurs under the sea, it may trigger a tsunami.","zh":"如果大地震發生在海底，可能引發海嘯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an earthquake of very large force.","zh":"這個片語描述力量非常大的地震。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be centred off the coast of","meaning":"震央位於……海岸對開","examples":[{"en":"The earthquake was centred off the coast of Sumatra.","zh":"地震震央位於蘇門答臘海岸對開。"},{"en":"Be centred off the coast of means have its central point in the sea near the coast of a place.","zh":"be centred off the coast of 指中心點位於某地海岸附近的海中。"},{"en":"A storm centred off the coast of a city may still bring heavy rain inland.","zh":"位於某城市海岸對開的風暴，仍可能為內陸帶來大雨。"},{"en":"If an earthquake is centred off the coast, coastal communities may face tsunami risk.","zh":"如果地震震央位於海岸對開，沿海社區可能面對海嘯風險。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies an offshore location.","zh":"這個片語指出近海位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Indonesian island of Sumatra","meaning":"印尼蘇門答臘島","examples":[{"en":"The earthquake occurred near the Indonesian island of Sumatra.","zh":"地震發生在印尼蘇門答臘島附近。"},{"en":"The Indonesian island of Sumatra is a large island in Indonesia.","zh":"Indonesian island of Sumatra 指印尼的一個大型島嶼。"},{"en":"A geography lesson may use Sumatra to explain earthquakes near plate boundaries.","zh":"地理課可能用蘇門答臘島來解釋板塊邊界附近的地震。"},{"en":"If a major quake occurs near an island, nearby coastal communities may need urgent warnings.","zh":"如果大型地震在島嶼附近發生，附近沿海社區可能需要緊急警報。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the specific island connected with the disaster.","zh":"這個片語指出與災害相關的特定島嶼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a series of","meaning":"一連串","examples":[{"en":"The earthquake caused a series of deadly tsunamis.","zh":"地震造成一連串致命海嘯。"},{"en":"A series of means several related events or things happening one after another.","zh":"a series of 指幾個相關事件或事物接連發生。"},{"en":"A teacher may give a series of short quizzes before the final exam.","zh":"老師可能在期末考前給一連串小測。"},{"en":"If one disaster triggers a series of problems, rescue work becomes more difficult.","zh":"如果一場災害引發一連串問題，救援工作就變得更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses connected events, not one isolated incident.","zh":"這個片語強調相連事件，而不是單一孤立事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"deadly tsunamis","meaning":"致命海嘯","examples":[{"en":"The massive earthquake caused a series of deadly tsunamis.","zh":"大地震造成一連串致命海嘯。"},{"en":"Deadly tsunamis are tsunami waves that cause many deaths or severe danger.","zh":"deadly tsunamis 指造成許多死亡或嚴重危險的海嘯巨浪。"},{"en":"A coastal town may sound sirens when officials fear deadly tsunamis.","zh":"當官員擔心致命海嘯，沿海城鎮可能響起警報。"},{"en":"Deadly tsunamis can kill people quickly because water moves with great force.","zh":"致命海嘯可以迅速奪命，因為海水以巨大力量移動。"},{"en":"The phrase combines the type of disaster with its fatal effect.","zh":"這個片語把災害種類與其致命效果結合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the Indian Ocean","meaning":"印度洋","examples":[{"en":"The tsunamis spread across the Indian Ocean.","zh":"海嘯擴散至印度洋各地。"},{"en":"The Indian Ocean is a major ocean bordered by Africa, Asia, Australia, and island nations.","zh":"Indian Ocean 指被非洲、亞洲、澳洲和島國圍繞的主要海洋。"},{"en":"Countries around the Indian Ocean may share tsunami-warning information.","zh":"印度洋周邊國家可能共享海嘯預警資訊。"},{"en":"If a disaster spreads across the Indian Ocean, many coastal regions may be affected.","zh":"如果災害擴散至印度洋各地，許多沿海地區可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the ocean region involved.","zh":"這個片語指出涉及的海洋區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"damage from","meaning":"由……造成的損失","examples":[{"en":"The damage from the disaster was estimated at billions of dollars.","zh":"由該災難造成的損失估計達數十億美元。"},{"en":"Damage from something means harm or destruction caused by that event.","zh":"damage from something 指由某事件造成的傷害或破壞。"},{"en":"Damage from a leaking pipe may include wet floors, broken furniture, and mould.","zh":"漏水管造成的損失可能包括地板濕透、家具損壞和霉菌。"},{"en":"If damage from a disaster is severe, rebuilding may take years.","zh":"如果災害造成的損失嚴重，重建可能需要多年。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of the harm.","zh":"這個片語指出傷害來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"extraordinary disaster","meaning":"異常嚴重的災難","examples":[{"en":"The tsunami was an extraordinary disaster.","zh":"該海嘯是一場異常嚴重的災難。"},{"en":"An extraordinary disaster is an unusually severe or remarkable disaster.","zh":"extraordinary disaster 指異常嚴重或非同尋常的災難。"},{"en":"A storm that destroys several cities in one night would be an extraordinary disaster.","zh":"一場在一夜之間摧毀幾個城市的風暴，就是異常嚴重的災難。"},{"en":"If a disaster is extraordinary, normal rescue systems may be overwhelmed.","zh":"如果災難異常嚴重，普通救援系統可能不堪負荷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a disaster far beyond ordinary scale.","zh":"這個片語描述遠超一般規模的災難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be estimated to be","meaning":"估計為","examples":[{"en":"The damage was estimated to be around US$13 billion.","zh":"損失估計為約130億美元。"},{"en":"Be estimated to be means be calculated approximately as a particular amount or level.","zh":"be estimated to be 指被約略計算為某數量或水平。"},{"en":"The cost of repairing the school roof was estimated to be over one million dollars.","zh":"學校屋頂維修費用估計為超過一百萬元。"},{"en":"If exact figures are unavailable, officials may estimate the damage using available data.","zh":"如果沒有準確數字，官員可能使用現有資料估算損失。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an approximate calculation.","zh":"這個片語引出約略計算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the vicinity of","meaning":"大約；接近","examples":[{"en":"The damage was estimated to be in the vicinity of US$13 billion.","zh":"損失估計大約為130億美元。"},{"en":"In the vicinity of means approximately or close to a particular amount or place.","zh":"in the vicinity of 指大約或接近某數量或地方。"},{"en":"The school fair raised in the vicinity of ten thousand dollars.","zh":"學校賣物會籌得大約一萬元。"},{"en":"If losses are in the vicinity of billions, the disaster has a national economic impact.","zh":"如果損失接近數十億，該災難就有全國經濟影響。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to give an approximate figure.","zh":"這個片語是給出約數的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the equivalent of","meaning":"相當於","examples":[{"en":"The damage was the equivalent of a huge amount of national income.","zh":"該損失相當於巨額國民收入。"},{"en":"The equivalent of means equal in value, amount, or effect to something else.","zh":"the equivalent of 指在價值、數量或效果上等同於另一事物。"},{"en":"Missing one week of lessons can be the equivalent of losing several chapters of learning.","zh":"缺課一星期可能相當於失去幾章學習內容。"},{"en":"If disaster damage equals a year of output, recovery becomes extremely difficult.","zh":"如果災害損失相當於一年產出，復原就變得極為困難。"},{"en":"The phrase helps compare one amount with a more familiar measure.","zh":"這個片語幫助把一個數量與較熟悉的量度比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"combined GDP","meaning":"合計本地生產總值","examples":[{"en":"The damage was compared with the combined GDP of developing countries.","zh":"該損失被拿來與發展中國家的合計本地生產總值比較。"},{"en":"Combined GDP means the total economic output of several countries added together.","zh":"combined GDP 指幾個國家的經濟產出加總。"},{"en":"Economists may compare a company’s value with the combined GDP of several small countries.","zh":"經濟學家可能把一間公司的價值與幾個小國的合計本地生產總值比較。"},{"en":"If disaster damage is compared with combined GDP, the writer stresses enormous economic scale.","zh":"如果災害損失與合計本地生產總值比較，作者是在強調巨大經濟規模。"},{"en":"The phrase joins several economies into one total figure.","zh":"這個片語把幾個經濟體合成一個總數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Gross Domestic Product","meaning":"本地生產總值","examples":[{"en":"Gross Domestic Product measures the value of goods and services produced by a country.","zh":"本地生產總值量度一個國家生產的貨品和服務價值。"},{"en":"Gross Domestic Product, or GDP, is the total value of goods and services produced in a country over a period.","zh":"Gross Domestic Product，或 GDP，指一個國家在一段時間內生產的貨品和服務總值。"},{"en":"A country’s GDP may rise when factories, shops, and services produce more value.","zh":"當工廠、商店和服務產生更多價值，一個國家的 GDP 可能上升。"},{"en":"If a disaster destroys a large share of GDP, national recovery becomes harder.","zh":"如果災害摧毀 GDP 的很大部分，國家復原就更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase is a key economic measure of national output.","zh":"這個片語是量度國家產出的重要經濟指標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"an entire year","meaning":"整整一年","examples":[{"en":"The estimated damage equalled the output of an entire year.","zh":"估計損失相當於整整一年的產出。"},{"en":"An entire year means a full year, not just a few months.","zh":"an entire year 指完整一年，而不是幾個月。"},{"en":"A student who misses an entire year of school may need special support to catch up.","zh":"缺課整整一年的學生可能需要特別支援追上進度。"},{"en":"If a disaster wipes out the value of an entire year’s production, its impact is enormous.","zh":"如果災害摧毀整整一年產值，其影響就非常巨大。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the full length or amount of one year.","zh":"這個片語強調完整一年的長度或數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the total value of","meaning":"……的總值","examples":[{"en":"GDP is the total value of goods and services produced by a country.","zh":"GDP 是一個國家生產的貨品和服務總值。"},{"en":"The total value of something is the full combined worth of all its parts.","zh":"the total value of something 指所有部分加起來的完整價值。"},{"en":"The total value of books in a library includes every textbook, novel, and reference book.","zh":"圖書館書籍的總值包括每本教科書、小說和參考書。"},{"en":"If the total value of damage is high, insurance and government support may be needed.","zh":"如果損失總值很高，可能需要保險和政府支援。"},{"en":"The phrase adds all parts together into one amount.","zh":"這個片語把所有部分加總成一個數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"goods and services","meaning":"貨品和服務","examples":[{"en":"GDP measures the value of goods and services produced in a year.","zh":"GDP 量度一年內生產的貨品和服務價值。"},{"en":"Goods and services are physical products and useful activities that people buy or provide.","zh":"goods and services 指人們購買或提供的實體產品和有用活動。"},{"en":"A bakery sells goods, while a tutor provides services.","zh":"麵包店售賣貨品，而補習老師提供服務。"},{"en":"If a disaster stops shops, schools, and transport, both goods and services are affected.","zh":"如果災害令商店、學校和交通停頓，貨品和服務都會受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase covers what an economy produces and offers.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋經濟體生產和提供的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"produced by a country","meaning":"由一個國家生產的","examples":[{"en":"GDP includes goods and services produced by a country.","zh":"GDP 包括由一個國家生產的貨品和服務。"},{"en":"Produced by a country means made, created, or provided within that country’s economy.","zh":"produced by a country 指在該國經濟內製造、創造或提供的。"},{"en":"Cars, food, legal advice, and education can all be produced by a country.","zh":"汽車、食物、法律建議和教育都可以由一個國家生產。"},{"en":"If a disaster damages factories and farms, less may be produced by the country that year.","zh":"如果災害破壞工廠和農場，該國當年生產的東西可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies national economic output.","zh":"這個片語指出國家經濟產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in a matter of seconds","meaning":"在短短幾秒之內","examples":[{"en":"In a matter of seconds, the tsunami waves destroyed years of development.","zh":"在短短幾秒之內，海嘯巨浪摧毀多年發展成果。"},{"en":"In a matter of seconds means within only a few seconds.","zh":"in a matter of seconds 指只在幾秒之內。"},{"en":"A phone can be lost in a matter of seconds if it is left on a busy café table.","zh":"如果手機被留在繁忙咖啡店桌上，可能在短短幾秒之內遺失。"},{"en":"Some disasters strike so quickly that people have almost no time to escape.","zh":"有些災害來得太快，人們幾乎沒有時間逃生。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses extreme speed.","zh":"這個片語強調極快速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"tsunami waves","meaning":"海嘯巨浪","examples":[{"en":"Tsunami waves wiped out years of development.","zh":"海嘯巨浪摧毀多年發展成果。"},{"en":"Tsunami waves are huge sea waves caused by powerful underwater events such as earthquakes.","zh":"tsunami waves 指由地震等強大海底事件造成的巨大海浪。"},{"en":"Coastal residents may move inland when tsunami waves are expected.","zh":"當預計有海嘯巨浪，沿海居民可能向內陸移動。"},{"en":"Tsunami waves can carry cars, boats, trees, and buildings far from the shore.","zh":"海嘯巨浪可以把汽車、船隻、樹木和建築物帶離海岸很遠。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the moving walls of water in a tsunami.","zh":"這個片語指海嘯中移動的巨大水牆。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"wipe out","meaning":"摧毀；徹底消滅","examples":[{"en":"The tsunami waves wiped out years of development.","zh":"海嘯巨浪摧毀多年發展成果。"},{"en":"Wipe out means completely destroy, remove, or eliminate something.","zh":"wipe out 指完全摧毀、清除或消滅某事物。"},{"en":"A computer virus can wipe out a student’s files if there is no backup.","zh":"如果沒有備份，電腦病毒可以徹底清除學生的文件。"},{"en":"If a flood wipes out crops, farmers may lose a whole season of income.","zh":"如果水災摧毀農作物，農民可能失去整季收入。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests total or near-total destruction.","zh":"這個片語暗示完全或近乎完全破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"long years of struggle","meaning":"多年艱苦努力","examples":[{"en":"The waves wiped out long years of struggle for development.","zh":"海浪摧毀了多年為發展而作的艱苦努力。"},{"en":"Long years of struggle means many years of difficult effort toward a goal.","zh":"long years of struggle 指為達成目標而付出的多年困難努力。"},{"en":"A family may spend long years of struggle saving money to buy a small home.","zh":"一個家庭可能多年艱苦努力儲蓄，才買到小房子。"},{"en":"When disaster destroys schools and roads, it can undo years of hard development work.","zh":"當災害摧毀學校和道路，它可以推翻多年艱苦的發展工作。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses effort, time, and difficulty.","zh":"這個片語強調努力、時間和困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"struggle for development","meaning":"為發展而作的努力","examples":[{"en":"The disaster destroyed years of struggle for development.","zh":"災難摧毀了多年為發展而作的努力。"},{"en":"Struggle for development means difficult effort to improve living standards, services, and economic conditions.","zh":"struggle for development 指為改善生活水平、服務和經濟狀況而作的艱難努力。"},{"en":"A village’s struggle for development may include building roads, schools, and clinics.","zh":"村莊為發展而作的努力可能包括建道路、學校和診所。"},{"en":"If disasters repeatedly destroy infrastructure, the struggle for development becomes much harder.","zh":"如果災害反覆摧毀基礎設施，為發展而作的努力就變得困難得多。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long-term effort to improve a society.","zh":"這個片語描述改善社會的長期努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"once again","meaning":"再一次","examples":[{"en":"The world was once again reminded of the power of natural disasters.","zh":"世界再一次被提醒自然災害的力量。"},{"en":"Once again means one more time after something has happened before.","zh":"once again 指某事曾經發生後再次發生。"},{"en":"Once again, the teacher reminded students to read the question carefully.","zh":"老師再一次提醒學生仔細閱讀題目。"},{"en":"If a disaster strikes once again, earlier warnings may seem tragically important.","zh":"如果災害再一次襲來，早前警告可能顯得悲劇性地重要。"},{"en":"The phrase shows repetition of an experience or reminder.","zh":"這個片語顯示經歷或提醒的重複。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be reminded of","meaning":"被提醒；想起","examples":[{"en":"The world was reminded of the destructive power of natural disasters.","zh":"世界被提醒自然災害的破壞力。"},{"en":"Be reminded of means be made to remember or think about something again.","zh":"be reminded of 指被令再次記起或想到某事。"},{"en":"A photo may remind a family of a holiday they took years ago.","zh":"一張照片可能令家庭想起多年前的一次假期。"},{"en":"When a flood destroys homes, people are reminded of why emergency planning matters.","zh":"當水災摧毀房屋，人們就被提醒緊急規劃為何重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes memory or awareness being brought back.","zh":"這個片語描述記憶或意識被重新帶回。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fearsome and destructive power","meaning":"可怕而具破壞性的力量","examples":[{"en":"The tsunami showed the fearsome and destructive power of natural disasters.","zh":"海嘯展示了自然災害可怕而具破壞性的力量。"},{"en":"Fearsome and destructive power means terrifying strength that can cause serious damage.","zh":"fearsome and destructive power 指令人恐懼並能造成嚴重破壞的力量。"},{"en":"A major typhoon can show fearsome and destructive power when it tears roofs from houses.","zh":"當大型颱風掀走房屋屋頂，它可以展示可怕而具破壞性的力量。"},{"en":"If people understand this power, they may take warnings more seriously.","zh":"如果人們理解這種力量，可能會更認真看待警報。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises danger, force, and damage.","zh":"這個片語強調危險、力量和破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the United Nations","meaning":"聯合國","examples":[{"en":"The United Nations has promoted international cooperation on disaster preparedness.","zh":"聯合國一直推動災害防備方面的國際合作。"},{"en":"The United Nations is an international organisation where countries work together on global issues.","zh":"the United Nations 指各國共同處理全球議題的國際組織。"},{"en":"The United Nations may help coordinate aid after wars, disasters, or humanitarian crises.","zh":"聯合國可能在戰爭、災害或人道危機後協調援助。"},{"en":"If a disaster affects many countries, the United Nations can help bring governments together.","zh":"如果災害影響許多國家，聯合國可以幫助各政府合作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a major global institution.","zh":"這個片語指一個主要全球機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"designate something as","meaning":"將……指定為","examples":[{"en":"The United Nations designated the 1990s as a decade for disaster reduction.","zh":"聯合國將1990年代指定為減少災害的十年。"},{"en":"Designate something as means officially name, choose, or assign something for a particular purpose.","zh":"designate something as 指正式命名、選定或分配某物作特定用途。"},{"en":"A school may designate one classroom as an emergency meeting point.","zh":"學校可能將一間課室指定為緊急集合點。"},{"en":"If a period is designated for disaster reduction, governments are encouraged to focus attention on that issue.","zh":"如果某段時期被指定為減災時期，政府就被鼓勵集中關注該議題。"},{"en":"The phrase shows official naming or assignment.","zh":"這個片語顯示官方命名或分配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the International Decade for Natural Disaster Reduction","meaning":"國際減少自然災害十年","examples":[{"en":"The 1990s were designated as the International Decade for Natural Disaster Reduction.","zh":"1990年代被指定為國際減少自然災害十年。"},{"en":"The International Decade for Natural Disaster Reduction was a named period focused on reducing disaster risk and damage.","zh":"International Decade for Natural Disaster Reduction 指一段以降低災害風險和損害為重點的命名時期。"},{"en":"A decade like this can help governments set shared goals and organise international meetings.","zh":"這樣的十年可以幫助政府設定共同目標並組織國際會議。"},{"en":"If disaster reduction receives a special decade, the issue gains global attention.","zh":"如果減災獲得一個特別十年，該議題就得到全球關注。"},{"en":"The phrase names an international initiative.","zh":"這個片語指出一項國際倡議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be active in","meaning":"積極參與","examples":[{"en":"The United Nations has been active in promoting disaster preparedness.","zh":"聯合國一直積極參與推動災害防備。"},{"en":"Be active in means take part energetically or regularly in an activity.","zh":"be active in 指積極或定期參與某活動。"},{"en":"A student can be active in school life by joining clubs and helping events.","zh":"學生可以透過參加學會和協助活動，積極參與校園生活。"},{"en":"If an organisation is active in disaster planning, it does more than watch from the side.","zh":"如果一個組織積極參與災害規劃，它就不只是旁觀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong involvement.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"promote and develop","meaning":"推廣並發展","examples":[{"en":"The UN has helped promote and develop international cooperation.","zh":"聯合國幫助推廣並發展國際合作。"},{"en":"Promote and develop means encourage something and help it grow stronger or more organised.","zh":"promote and develop 指鼓勵某事並幫助它變得更強或更有組織。"},{"en":"A school may promote and develop reading habits through library lessons and book clubs.","zh":"學校可以透過圖書館課和讀書會推廣並發展閱讀習慣。"},{"en":"If leaders promote and develop disaster cooperation, countries may respond more effectively together.","zh":"如果領袖推廣並發展災害合作，各國可能更有效地共同應對。"},{"en":"The phrase combines encouragement with practical growth.","zh":"這個片語結合鼓勵和實際發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"international cooperation","meaning":"國際合作","examples":[{"en":"International cooperation is essential for disaster preparedness.","zh":"國際合作對災害防備至關重要。"},{"en":"International cooperation means countries or organisations working together across borders.","zh":"international cooperation 指國家或組織跨越國界合作。"},{"en":"Countries may use international cooperation to share weather warnings and rescue expertise.","zh":"各國可能透過國際合作分享天氣警報和救援專業知識。"},{"en":"If disasters affect several nations, cooperation can prevent delay and duplication.","zh":"如果災害影響幾個國家，合作可以避免延誤和重複工作。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses joint action beyond one country.","zh":"這個片語強調超越單一國家的共同行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Yokohama Strategy for a Safer World","meaning":"《橫濱更安全世界策略》","examples":[{"en":"The Yokohama Strategy for a Safer World was adopted in 1994.","zh":"《橫濱更安全世界策略》於1994年獲採納。"},{"en":"The Yokohama Strategy for a Safer World was an international plan for reducing disaster risks and improving preparedness.","zh":"Yokohama Strategy for a Safer World 指一項旨在降低災害風險和改善防備的國際計劃。"},{"en":"A strategy document can guide governments by setting goals and recommended actions.","zh":"策略文件可以透過設定目標和建議行動來指引政府。"},{"en":"If countries follow such a strategy, they may build safer communities before disasters happen.","zh":"如果各國跟從這類策略，就可能在災害發生前建立更安全社區。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific disaster-reduction framework.","zh":"這個片語指出一個特定減災框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"guidelines for","meaning":"關於……的指引","examples":[{"en":"The Yokohama Strategy gave guidelines for natural disaster prevention and mitigation.","zh":"《橫濱策略》提供關於自然災害預防和減災的指引。"},{"en":"Guidelines for something are recommended rules or instructions for doing it properly.","zh":"guidelines for something 指做好某事的建議規則或指示。"},{"en":"A school gives guidelines for homework so students know the expected length and format.","zh":"學校給出功課指引，讓學生知道預期長度和格式。"},{"en":"Clear guidelines for disaster response can reduce confusion during emergencies.","zh":"清楚的災害應對指引可以減少緊急情況中的混亂。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical directions, not random advice.","zh":"這個片語指實際方向，而不是隨意建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"natural disaster prevention","meaning":"自然災害預防","examples":[{"en":"Natural disaster prevention should be included in national planning.","zh":"自然災害預防應納入國家規劃。"},{"en":"Natural disaster prevention means actions taken to reduce the chance or impact of disasters before they happen.","zh":"natural disaster prevention 指在災害發生前採取行動，以降低發生機會或影響。"},{"en":"Building flood barriers is one form of natural disaster prevention.","zh":"建造防洪屏障是一種自然災害預防。"},{"en":"Prevention can save money because it avoids some damage before it occurs.","zh":"預防可以節省金錢，因為它在損害發生前避免部分破壞。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on reducing risk in advance.","zh":"這個片語集中於預先降低風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"preparedness and mitigation","meaning":"防備與減災","examples":[{"en":"The guidelines focused on disaster prevention, preparedness and mitigation.","zh":"這些指引集中於災害預防、防備與減災。"},{"en":"Preparedness and mitigation mean getting ready for disasters and reducing their damage.","zh":"preparedness and mitigation 指為災害作好準備並減少其損害。"},{"en":"A town improves preparedness by training volunteers and improves mitigation by strengthening buildings.","zh":"城鎮透過訓練義工改善防備，並透過加固建築改善減災。"},{"en":"If both preparedness and mitigation are weak, even a moderate disaster can become deadly.","zh":"如果防備與減災都薄弱，即使中等程度災害也可能變得致命。"},{"en":"The phrase combines readiness with damage reduction.","zh":"這個片語結合準備和減少損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be adopted in","meaning":"於……獲採納","examples":[{"en":"The Yokohama Strategy was adopted in 1994.","zh":"《橫濱策略》於1994年獲採納。"},{"en":"Be adopted in means be officially accepted or approved in a particular year or place.","zh":"be adopted in 指在某一年或某地被正式接受或批准。"},{"en":"A new school policy may be adopted in September after staff discussion.","zh":"新校政可能在教職員討論後於九月獲採納。"},{"en":"If a strategy is adopted, governments agree to use it as guidance.","zh":"如果策略獲採納，政府就同意以它作為指引。"},{"en":"The phrase marks official acceptance.","zh":"這個片語標示官方接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"among the guidelines","meaning":"在這些指引之中","examples":[{"en":"Among the guidelines, countries were encouraged to use domestic resources.","zh":"在這些指引之中，各國被鼓勵使用國內資源。"},{"en":"Among the guidelines means included as one item within a larger set of recommendations.","zh":"among the guidelines 指作為一大套建議中的其中一項。"},{"en":"Among the school guidelines, students are asked to submit homework on time.","zh":"在學校指引之中，學生被要求準時交功課。"},{"en":"This phrase helps introduce one point from a longer list.","zh":"這個片語幫助從較長列表中引出其中一點。"},{"en":"It signals that the writer is selecting a specific recommendation.","zh":"它表示作者正在選取某項特定建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be encouraged to","meaning":"被鼓勵去","examples":[{"en":"Developing countries were encouraged to organise domestic resources.","zh":"發展中國家被鼓勵去組織國內資源。"},{"en":"Be encouraged to means be advised or supported to do something.","zh":"be encouraged to 指被建議或支持去做某事。"},{"en":"Students are encouraged to ask questions when instructions are unclear.","zh":"當指示不清楚時，學生被鼓勵提問。"},{"en":"If countries are encouraged to prepare early, they may build stronger systems before disasters.","zh":"如果各國被鼓勵及早準備，就可能在災害前建立更強制度。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests guidance and support, not force.","zh":"這個片語暗示引導和支援，而不是強迫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"organise and implement","meaning":"組織並落實","examples":[{"en":"Developing countries were encouraged to organise and implement domestic resources.","zh":"發展中國家被鼓勵組織並落實國內資源。"},{"en":"Organise and implement means arrange resources and put plans into action.","zh":"organise and implement 指安排資源並把計劃付諸行動。"},{"en":"A teacher may organise and implement a revision schedule before exams.","zh":"老師可能在考試前組織並落實溫習時間表。"},{"en":"If disaster resources are organised but not implemented, preparation remains only on paper.","zh":"如果災害資源只被組織但沒有落實，準備就仍只停留在紙上。"},{"en":"The phrase combines planning with real action.","zh":"這個片語結合規劃和真正行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"domestic resources","meaning":"國內資源","examples":[{"en":"Countries should use their domestic resources for disaster reduction.","zh":"各國應使用國內資源進行減災。"},{"en":"Domestic resources are the money, people, skills, materials, and institutions available within a country.","zh":"domestic resources 指一個國家內部可用的金錢、人力、技能、材料和機構。"},{"en":"A city may use domestic resources such as local volunteers and public buildings during an emergency.","zh":"城市在緊急情況中可能使用本地義工和公共建築等國內資源。"},{"en":"If countries rely only on foreign aid, help may arrive too late.","zh":"如果國家只依賴外國援助，幫助可能來得太遲。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses resources already available at home.","zh":"這個片語強調本國已有的資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"disaster reduction activities","meaning":"減災活動","examples":[{"en":"Domestic resources can support disaster reduction activities.","zh":"國內資源可以支援減災活動。"},{"en":"Disaster reduction activities are actions that reduce the risk, damage, or suffering caused by disasters.","zh":"disaster reduction activities 指降低災害風險、損害或痛苦的行動。"},{"en":"Building safer schools and teaching evacuation routes are disaster reduction activities.","zh":"建造更安全的學校和教授疏散路線都是減災活動。"},{"en":"If these activities are done before disasters, they can save lives later.","zh":"如果這些活動在災害前完成，之後就可以拯救生命。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical steps that lower disaster harm.","zh":"這個片語指減少災害傷害的實際步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"donor countries","meaning":"捐助國","examples":[{"en":"Donor countries were encouraged to support disaster preparedness.","zh":"捐助國被鼓勵支援災害防備。"},{"en":"Donor countries are countries that give money, resources, or technical help to other countries.","zh":"donor countries 指向其他國家提供金錢、資源或技術協助的國家。"},{"en":"Donor countries may send medical teams after a major earthquake.","zh":"捐助國可能在大地震後派出醫療隊。"},{"en":"If donor countries support prevention, poorer countries may suffer less damage later.","zh":"如果捐助國支援預防，較貧窮國家日後可能承受較少損害。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to countries that provide aid.","zh":"這個片語指提供援助的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the developed world","meaning":"發達國家；發達世界","examples":[{"en":"Donor countries in the developed world were asked to give more support.","zh":"發達世界的捐助國被要求提供更多支援。"},{"en":"The developed world means richer countries with more advanced economies and infrastructure.","zh":"developed world 指經濟和基礎設施較先進的富裕國家。"},{"en":"The developed world often has stronger hospitals, roads, insurance systems, and emergency services.","zh":"發達世界通常有較強醫院、道路、保險制度和緊急服務。"},{"en":"If the developed world shares resources, poorer countries may improve disaster preparedness.","zh":"如果發達世界分享資源，較貧窮國家可能改善災害防備。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts richer countries with less-developed ones.","zh":"這個片語把較富裕國家與較不發達國家作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"give greater priority to","meaning":"更加優先考慮","examples":[{"en":"Developed countries should give greater priority to disaster prevention.","zh":"發達國家應更加優先考慮災害預防。"},{"en":"Give greater priority to means treat something as more important than before or more important than other things.","zh":"give greater priority to 指比以前或比其他事更重視某事。"},{"en":"A school may give greater priority to mental health after students report high stress.","zh":"當學生反映壓力很大，學校可能更加優先考慮心理健康。"},{"en":"If governments give prevention more priority, they may spend less on emergency recovery later.","zh":"如果政府更優先考慮預防，之後可能較少花費於緊急復原。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a shift in importance.","zh":"這個片語顯示重要性的轉移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"disaster prevention","meaning":"災害預防","examples":[{"en":"Disaster prevention can save lives and reduce damage.","zh":"災害預防可以拯救生命並減少損害。"},{"en":"Disaster prevention means actions taken before a disaster to reduce risk or harm.","zh":"disaster prevention 指在災害前採取行動，以降低風險或傷害。"},{"en":"Planting trees on slopes can be part of disaster prevention if it reduces landslide risk.","zh":"如果在斜坡種樹能降低山泥傾瀉風險，它就可以是災害預防的一部分。"},{"en":"If prevention is ignored, communities may pay a much higher price after disaster strikes.","zh":"如果預防被忽視，社區在災害發生後可能付出更高代價。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on stopping or reducing harm before it happens.","zh":"這個片語集中於在事情發生前阻止或減少傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"assistance programmes","meaning":"援助計劃","examples":[{"en":"Disaster prevention should be included in assistance programmes.","zh":"災害預防應納入援助計劃。"},{"en":"Assistance programmes are organised plans that provide help, funding, training, or resources.","zh":"assistance programmes 指提供幫助、資金、訓練或資源的有組織計劃。"},{"en":"A government may run assistance programmes for families after a flood.","zh":"政府可能在水災後為家庭推行援助計劃。"},{"en":"If assistance programmes include prevention, aid can reduce future risks, not only repair past damage.","zh":"如果援助計劃包括預防，援助就能降低未來風險，而不只是修復過去損害。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to planned support systems.","zh":"這個片語指有計劃的支援制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"assistance budgets","meaning":"援助預算","examples":[{"en":"Donor countries were asked to include disaster preparedness in their budgets.","zh":"捐助國被要求把災害防備納入其援助預算。"},{"en":"Assistance budgets are the funds set aside for aid, support, or development help.","zh":"assistance budgets 指撥作援助、支援或發展幫助的資金。"},{"en":"A charity’s assistance budget may cover food, medicine, transport, and emergency shelter.","zh":"慈善機構的援助預算可能涵蓋食物、藥物、運輸和緊急住所。"},{"en":"If disaster preparedness is included in assistance budgets, countries can invest before emergencies happen.","zh":"如果災害防備納入援助預算，各國就能在緊急情況發生前投資。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to money planned for helping others.","zh":"這個片語指計劃用來幫助他人的金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"financial contributions","meaning":"財政捐助","examples":[{"en":"The guidelines called for increased financial contributions.","zh":"這些指引要求增加財政捐助。"},{"en":"Financial contributions are money given to support a project, organisation, or cause.","zh":"financial contributions 指為支持項目、組織或目標而給予的金錢。"},{"en":"Parents may make financial contributions to a school fundraising event.","zh":"家長可能為學校籌款活動作財政捐助。"},{"en":"If donor countries increase financial contributions, disaster-prevention projects can expand.","zh":"如果捐助國增加財政捐助，災害預防項目就可以擴展。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on monetary support.","zh":"這個片語集中於金錢支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"UN World Conference on Disaster Reduction","meaning":"聯合國世界減災會議","examples":[{"en":"The UN World Conference on Disaster Reduction met in Kobe in 2005.","zh":"聯合國世界減災會議於2005年在神戶舉行。"},{"en":"The UN World Conference on Disaster Reduction was a major international meeting about reducing disaster risks.","zh":"UN World Conference on Disaster Reduction 指一場關於降低災害風險的大型國際會議。"},{"en":"A world conference lets experts, officials, and organisations discuss shared problems.","zh":"世界會議讓專家、官員和組織討論共同問題。"},{"en":"If many countries attend such a conference, they can agree on common goals.","zh":"如果許多國家出席這類會議，它們就可以就共同目標達成一致。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific United Nations disaster conference.","zh":"這個片語指出一場特定聯合國減災會議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Hyogo Prefecture","meaning":"兵庫縣","examples":[{"en":"The conference was held in Kobe, Hyogo Prefecture.","zh":"會議在兵庫縣神戶舉行。"},{"en":"Hyogo Prefecture is a regional administrative area in Japan that includes Kobe.","zh":"Hyogo Prefecture 指日本的一個地區行政單位，包括神戶。"},{"en":"A geography class may use Hyogo Prefecture to locate the city affected by the Great Hanshin earthquake.","zh":"地理課可能用兵庫縣來定位受阪神大地震影響的城市。"},{"en":"Holding the conference in Hyogo connected disaster planning with a place that had experienced a major earthquake.","zh":"在兵庫舉行會議，把災害規劃與曾經歷大地震的地方連接起來。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a Japanese location.","zh":"這個片語指出日本的一個地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"discuss and debate","meaning":"討論和辯論","examples":[{"en":"Delegates met to discuss and debate disaster preparedness.","zh":"代表會面討論和辯論災害防備。"},{"en":"Discuss and debate means exchange ideas and argue different views in order to understand or decide something.","zh":"discuss and debate 指交換想法並爭論不同觀點，以理解或決定某事。"},{"en":"Students discuss and debate whether school uniforms should be compulsory.","zh":"學生討論和辯論校服是否應強制。"},{"en":"If experts discuss and debate disaster plans, weak points may be found before emergencies happen.","zh":"如果專家討論和辯論災害計劃，弱點可能在緊急情況前被發現。"},{"en":"The phrase combines conversation with careful disagreement.","zh":"這個片語結合交談和仔細分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"address issues of","meaning":"處理……議題","examples":[{"en":"The conference considered how to address issues of disaster preparedness.","zh":"會議考慮如何處理災害防備議題。"},{"en":"Address issues of means deal with problems or questions related to a particular topic.","zh":"address issues of 指處理與某主題相關的問題或疑問。"},{"en":"A school meeting may address issues of student stress and homework load.","zh":"學校會議可能處理學生壓力和功課量議題。"},{"en":"If a conference addresses disaster issues, it should lead to practical recommendations.","zh":"如果會議處理災害議題，就應產生實際建議。"},{"en":"The phrase means actively handling a topic’s problems.","zh":"這個片語意思是主動處理某主題的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"disaster mitigation","meaning":"減災","examples":[{"en":"Disaster mitigation was a major topic at the conference.","zh":"減災是會議的主要議題。"},{"en":"Disaster mitigation means reducing the damage, danger, or suffering caused by disasters.","zh":"disaster mitigation 指減少災害造成的損害、危險或痛苦。"},{"en":"Stronger building codes are a form of disaster mitigation in earthquake-prone cities.","zh":"在地震高危城市，更嚴格建築規範是一種減災措施。"},{"en":"If mitigation measures are built early, disasters may still happen but cause less harm.","zh":"如果減災措施及早建立，災害仍可能發生，但造成較少傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on lowering impact rather than stopping nature completely.","zh":"這個片語集中於降低影響，而不是完全阻止自然。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be attended by","meaning":"由……出席","examples":[{"en":"The meeting was attended by over 4,000 delegates.","zh":"該會議由超過4,000名代表出席。"},{"en":"Be attended by means have people present at an event.","zh":"be attended by 指某活動有某些人出席。"},{"en":"The school concert was attended by parents, teachers, and former students.","zh":"學校音樂會由家長、老師和舊生出席。"},{"en":"If a conference is attended by many countries, its decisions may carry more weight.","zh":"如果會議由許多國家出席，其決定可能更有分量。"},{"en":"The phrase tells us who was present.","zh":"這個片語告訴我們誰在場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"delegates representing","meaning":"代表……的代表","examples":[{"en":"The meeting was attended by delegates representing about 168 countries.","zh":"該會議由代表約168個國家的代表出席。"},{"en":"Delegates representing a country or group are people who attend and speak on behalf of that country or group.","zh":"delegates representing a country or group 指代表某國家或群體出席並發言的人。"},{"en":"A student council meeting may include delegates representing different classes.","zh":"學生會會議可能包括代表不同班級的代表。"},{"en":"If delegates represent many countries, the discussion includes more international perspectives.","zh":"如果代表代表許多國家，討論就包括更多國際角度。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies both the people and who they speak for.","zh":"這個片語同時指出人物和他們代表誰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"occur almost ten years to the day after","meaning":"幾乎正好在……十年後舉行","examples":[{"en":"The meeting occurred almost ten years to the day after the Kobe earthquake.","zh":"該會議幾乎正好在神戶地震十年後舉行。"},{"en":"Occur almost ten years to the day after means happen almost exactly ten years after a previous event.","zh":"occur almost ten years to the day after 指幾乎正好在某事件十年後發生。"},{"en":"A memorial service may occur ten years to the day after a school was rebuilt following a fire.","zh":"學校火災後重建十年，紀念儀式可能正好在那天舉行。"},{"en":"Holding a disaster conference on such a date can make memory and planning feel connected.","zh":"在這樣的日期舉行災害會議，可以把記憶和規劃連接起來。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises a nearly exact anniversary.","zh":"這個片語強調幾乎準確的周年。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the Great Hanshin earthquake","meaning":"阪神大地震","examples":[{"en":"The Great Hanshin earthquake caused severe damage in Kobe.","zh":"阪神大地震在神戶造成嚴重破壞。"},{"en":"The Great Hanshin earthquake was a major earthquake that struck the Kobe region of Japan in 1995.","zh":"Great Hanshin earthquake 指1995年襲擊日本神戶地區的大地震。"},{"en":"Students may study the Great Hanshin earthquake to learn how cities recover after disasters.","zh":"學生可能研究阪神大地震，以了解城市災後如何復原。"},{"en":"Because the earthquake caused great loss, it became an important lesson in disaster preparedness.","zh":"因為該地震造成巨大損失，它成為災害防備的重要教訓。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific historical disaster.","zh":"這個片語指出一場特定歷史災害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"provide someone with an opportunity to","meaning":"為某人提供機會去……","examples":[{"en":"The conference provided experts with an opportunity to review the strategy.","zh":"會議為專家提供機會去檢討該策略。"},{"en":"Provide someone with an opportunity to means give someone a chance to do something.","zh":"provide someone with an opportunity to 指給某人機會做某事。"},{"en":"A debate club provides students with an opportunity to practise speaking under pressure.","zh":"辯論學會為學生提供機會在壓力下練習說話。"},{"en":"If a conference provides experts with time to review a strategy, old plans can be improved.","zh":"如果會議給專家時間檢討策略，舊計劃就可以改善。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a useful chance created by an event.","zh":"這個片語突出某活動創造的有用機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"experts and scientists","meaning":"專家和科學家","examples":[{"en":"Experts and scientists from over 150 countries attended the meeting.","zh":"來自超過150個國家的專家和科學家出席會議。"},{"en":"Experts and scientists are people with specialised knowledge, research skills, or professional experience.","zh":"experts and scientists 指具有專門知識、研究技能或專業經驗的人。"},{"en":"A city may ask experts and scientists to assess flood risks before building near a river.","zh":"城市在河邊建築前，可能請專家和科學家評估水災風險。"},{"en":"If experts and scientists share evidence, disaster plans can become more reliable.","zh":"如果專家和科學家分享證據，災害計劃就能更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people who contribute knowledge and analysis.","zh":"這個片語指貢獻知識和分析的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"government officials","meaning":"政府官員","examples":[{"en":"Government officials took part in the disaster reduction conference.","zh":"政府官員參與了減災會議。"},{"en":"Government officials are people who work for the government and help make or carry out public decisions.","zh":"government officials 指在政府工作並協助制定或執行公共決策的人。"},{"en":"Government officials may arrange shelters, road closures, and emergency funding during disasters.","zh":"政府官員可能在災害中安排庇護所、封路和緊急資金。"},{"en":"If officials attend international conferences, they can bring new ideas back to their countries.","zh":"如果官員出席國際會議，就可以把新想法帶回本國。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to public servants with official responsibilities.","zh":"這個片語指有官方責任的公務人員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"non-governmental organisations","meaning":"非政府組織","examples":[{"en":"Non-governmental organisations also attended the conference.","zh":"非政府組織也出席了會議。"},{"en":"Non-governmental organisations are independent groups that work on social, humanitarian, environmental, or development issues outside direct government control.","zh":"non-governmental organisations 指不受政府直接控制、處理社會、人道、環境或發展議題的獨立團體。"},{"en":"A non-governmental organisation may provide food and medical support after a flood.","zh":"非政府組織可能在水災後提供食物和醫療支援。"},{"en":"If NGOs work with governments, disaster aid can reach local communities more effectively.","zh":"如果非政府組織與政府合作，災害援助可以更有效到達本地社區。"},{"en":"The phrase is often shortened to NGOs.","zh":"這個片語常縮寫為 NGOs。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"United Nations representatives","meaning":"聯合國代表","examples":[{"en":"United Nations representatives joined the discussions.","zh":"聯合國代表參與了討論。"},{"en":"United Nations representatives are people who speak or work on behalf of the UN at meetings or events.","zh":"United Nations representatives 指在會議或活動中代表聯合國發言或工作的人。"},{"en":"United Nations representatives may help coordinate international support after a major disaster.","zh":"聯合國代表可能在大型災害後協調國際支援。"},{"en":"If UN representatives join discussions, the issue may gain wider global attention.","zh":"如果聯合國代表參與討論，該議題可能獲得更廣泛全球關注。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies people representing the United Nations.","zh":"這個片語指出代表聯合國的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"review the strategy","meaning":"檢討策略","examples":[{"en":"Participants had an opportunity to review the Yokohama Strategy.","zh":"參加者有機會檢討《橫濱策略》。"},{"en":"Review the strategy means examine a plan carefully to judge whether it still works or needs change.","zh":"review the strategy 指仔細檢視一項計劃，判斷它是否仍有效或需要改變。"},{"en":"A school may review its exam strategy after students perform worse than expected.","zh":"如果學生表現低於預期，學校可能檢討其考試策略。"},{"en":"If disaster risks change, countries must review old strategies instead of assuming they still fit.","zh":"如果災害風險改變，各國必須檢討舊策略，而不是假設它們仍然合適。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful evaluation of a plan.","zh":"這個片語描述對計劃的仔細評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"resulting action plan","meaning":"隨後制定的行動計劃","examples":[{"en":"The resulting action plan covered the years 2005 to 2015.","zh":"隨後制定的行動計劃涵蓋2005年至2015年。"},{"en":"A resulting action plan is the practical plan produced after discussion, review, or decision-making.","zh":"resulting action plan 指討論、檢討或決策後產生的實際計劃。"},{"en":"After a school safety meeting, the resulting action plan may include drills and new emergency signs.","zh":"學校安全會議後，隨後制定的行動計劃可能包括演習和新緊急標誌。"},{"en":"If an action plan results from a conference, it turns debate into concrete steps.","zh":"如果行動計劃由會議產生，它就把辯論轉化為具體步驟。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the plan that comes out of a process.","zh":"這個片語指某過程產生的計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"participant countries and agencies","meaning":"參加國家和機構","examples":[{"en":"Participant countries and agencies were asked to reduce disaster vulnerability.","zh":"參加國家和機構被要求減低災害脆弱性。"},{"en":"Participant countries and agencies are the nations and organisations that take part in a meeting or plan.","zh":"participant countries and agencies 指參與會議或計劃的國家和組織。"},{"en":"In a regional education project, participant schools and agencies may share teaching resources.","zh":"在地區教育項目中，參加學校和機構可能共享教學資源。"},{"en":"If participant countries cooperate, disaster-prevention work can be more consistent.","zh":"如果參加國家合作，災害預防工作可以更一致。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the members involved in an initiative.","zh":"這個片語指出參與某倡議的成員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"over the next 10 years","meaning":"在未來十年間","examples":[{"en":"The plan asked countries to work over the next 10 years.","zh":"該計劃要求各國在未來十年間工作。"},{"en":"Over the next 10 years means during the ten-year period following that moment.","zh":"over the next 10 years 指從當時起接下來十年期間。"},{"en":"A school may plan to improve its library over the next 10 years.","zh":"學校可能計劃在未來十年間改善圖書館。"},{"en":"If disaster risk is reduced over the next 10 years, communities may become safer step by step.","zh":"如果災害風險在未來十年間降低，社區可能逐步變得更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a future time frame for action.","zh":"這個片語給出行動的未來時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reduce vulnerability to","meaning":"減低對……的脆弱性","examples":[{"en":"The action plan aimed to reduce vulnerability to natural disasters.","zh":"該行動計劃旨在減低對自然災害的脆弱性。"},{"en":"Reduce vulnerability to means make people, places, or systems less likely to be harmed by something.","zh":"reduce vulnerability to 指令人民、地方或系統較不容易受某事傷害。"},{"en":"Stronger roofs can reduce vulnerability to typhoons in coastal villages.","zh":"更堅固屋頂可以減低沿海村莊對颱風的脆弱性。"},{"en":"If poor communities receive better housing and warnings, their vulnerability to disasters decreases.","zh":"如果貧困社區獲得較好住屋和警報，其對災害的脆弱性就會下降。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on lowering weakness or exposure to harm.","zh":"這個片語集中於降低弱點或受害風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as a first step","meaning":"作為第一步","examples":[{"en":"As a first step, disaster prevention should be included in development plans.","zh":"作為第一步，災害預防應納入發展計劃。"},{"en":"As a first step means as the first action in a longer process.","zh":"as a first step 指作為較長過程中的第一個行動。"},{"en":"As a first step, a student who is behind should list exactly which chapters are unclear.","zh":"作為第一步，落後的學生應列出到底哪些章節不清楚。"},{"en":"If prevention is the first step, later recovery may become easier and cheaper.","zh":"如果預防是第一步，之後復原可能變得更容易和更便宜。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the beginning of a plan.","zh":"這個片語引出計劃的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"encourage the integration of","meaning":"鼓勵將……融入","examples":[{"en":"The Action Plan encouraged the integration of disaster prevention into planning.","zh":"該行動計劃鼓勵將災害預防融入規劃。"},{"en":"Encourage the integration of means support the act of combining something into a larger system.","zh":"encourage the integration of 指支持把某事結合進較大系統。"},{"en":"A school may encourage the integration of technology into daily lessons.","zh":"學校可能鼓勵將科技融入日常課堂。"},{"en":"If disaster prevention is integrated into development plans, it becomes part of normal decision-making.","zh":"如果災害預防被融入發展計劃，它就成為正常決策的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses bringing separate elements together.","zh":"這個片語強調把分開的元素結合起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"disaster prevention programmes","meaning":"災害預防計劃","examples":[{"en":"Disaster prevention programmes should be part of development planning.","zh":"災害預防計劃應成為發展規劃的一部分。"},{"en":"Disaster prevention programmes are organised projects designed to reduce disaster risks before they happen.","zh":"disaster prevention programmes 指有組織、旨在災害發生前降低風險的項目。"},{"en":"A city may run programmes to strengthen buildings, clear drains, and train rescue volunteers.","zh":"城市可能推行計劃去加固建築、清理渠務和訓練救援義工。"},{"en":"If prevention programmes are funded early, emergency losses may be reduced later.","zh":"如果預防計劃及早獲資助，之後緊急損失可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to structured prevention work.","zh":"這個片語指有結構的預防工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"development and policy-making plans","meaning":"發展及政策制定計劃","examples":[{"en":"Disaster prevention should be included in development and policy-making plans.","zh":"災害預防應納入發展及政策制定計劃。"},{"en":"Development and policy-making plans are official plans for improving a country or community and making public decisions.","zh":"development and policy-making plans 指改善國家或社區以及作公共決策的官方計劃。"},{"en":"A government may include housing, transport, education, and disaster safety in its development plans.","zh":"政府可能在發展計劃中包括住屋、交通、教育和災害安全。"},{"en":"If disaster risk is ignored in policy-making, new buildings may be placed in dangerous areas.","zh":"如果政策制定忽視災害風險，新建築可能被放在危險地區。"},{"en":"The phrase connects long-term growth with government decision-making.","zh":"這個片語把長期增長與政府決策連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"disaster risk reduction","meaning":"災害風險降低","examples":[{"en":"Disaster risk reduction is an essential investment in the future.","zh":"災害風險降低是對未來的必要投資。"},{"en":"Disaster risk reduction means reducing the chance that disasters will cause death, damage, or serious disruption.","zh":"disaster risk reduction 指降低災害造成死亡、損害或嚴重中斷的機會。"},{"en":"Early-warning systems, safe buildings, and public education are forms of disaster risk reduction.","zh":"早期預警系統、安全建築和公眾教育都是災害風險降低的形式。"},{"en":"If risk is reduced before disaster strikes, communities can recover faster.","zh":"如果風險在災害前被降低，社區就能更快復原。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on lowering danger before harm happens.","zh":"這個片語集中於在傷害發生前降低危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an additional expense","meaning":"額外開支","examples":[{"en":"Disaster risk reduction is not merely an additional expense.","zh":"災害風險降低不只是額外開支。"},{"en":"An additional expense is extra money that must be paid on top of existing costs.","zh":"additional expense 指在現有成本之外需要支付的額外金錢。"},{"en":"Buying a printer may seem cheap, but ink becomes an additional expense.","zh":"買打印機可能看似便宜，但墨水會成為額外開支。"},{"en":"Disaster planning should not be seen only as extra cost because it can prevent larger losses.","zh":"災害規劃不應只被視為額外成本，因為它可以防止更大損失。"},{"en":"The phrase often contrasts short-term spending with long-term value.","zh":"這個片語常對比短期花費和長期價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an essential investment","meaning":"必要投資","examples":[{"en":"Disaster risk reduction is an essential investment in our common future.","zh":"災害風險降低是對我們共同未來的必要投資。"},{"en":"An essential investment is spending that is necessary because it brings important future benefits.","zh":"essential investment 指因能帶來重要未來好處而必需的支出。"},{"en":"Teacher training is an essential investment in better education.","zh":"教師培訓是改善教育的必要投資。"},{"en":"If prevention saves lives and money later, it is an investment rather than a waste.","zh":"如果預防日後能拯救生命和金錢，它就是投資而不是浪費。"},{"en":"The phrase describes necessary spending for long-term benefit.","zh":"這個片語描述為長期好處而作的必要支出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"our common future","meaning":"我們共同的未來","examples":[{"en":"Disaster preparedness is an investment in our common future.","zh":"災害防備是對我們共同未來的投資。"},{"en":"Our common future means the future shared by all people, communities, or countries.","zh":"our common future 指所有人、社區或國家共同分享的未來。"},{"en":"Protecting clean air is part of protecting our common future.","zh":"保護清潔空氣是保護我們共同未來的一部分。"},{"en":"If countries ignore disaster risk, everyone’s common future becomes less secure.","zh":"如果各國忽視災害風險，所有人的共同未來都會變得較不安全。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses shared responsibility across borders and generations.","zh":"這個片語強調跨越國界和世代的共同責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the benefits of","meaning":"……的好處","examples":[{"en":"The benefits of disaster preparedness include money saved and lives protected.","zh":"災害防備的好處包括節省金錢和保護生命。"},{"en":"The benefits of something are the good results or advantages it brings.","zh":"the benefits of something 指某事帶來的良好結果或優點。"},{"en":"The benefits of regular revision include better memory and less exam panic.","zh":"定期溫習的好處包括更好記憶和較少考試恐慌。"},{"en":"If people understand the benefits of preparedness, they may support spending on it.","zh":"如果人們理解防備的好處，就可能支持在這方面花費。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces positive results.","zh":"這個片語引出正面結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be calculated not only in","meaning":"不只以……計算","examples":[{"en":"The benefits are calculated not only in money but also in saved lives.","zh":"這些好處不只以金錢計算，也以獲挽救的生命計算。"},{"en":"Be calculated not only in means be measured by more than one type of value.","zh":"be calculated not only in 指不只用一種類型的價值來量度。"},{"en":"The success of a school should be calculated not only in exam marks but also in student wellbeing.","zh":"學校成功不應只以考試分數計算，也應以學生身心健康計算。"},{"en":"Disaster planning should be judged not only by cost but by the lives it protects.","zh":"災害規劃不應只按成本判斷，也應按它保護的生命判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase warns readers not to use one narrow measure only.","zh":"這個片語提醒讀者不要只使用一個狹窄量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"most importantly","meaning":"最重要的是","examples":[{"en":"Most importantly, disaster preparedness can save lives.","zh":"最重要的是，災害防備可以拯救生命。"},{"en":"Most importantly means the most important point is this.","zh":"most importantly 指最重要的一點是這個。"},{"en":"A school trip should be fun, but most importantly, it must be safe.","zh":"學校旅行應該有趣，但最重要的是，它必須安全。"},{"en":"If many benefits are listed, “most importantly” highlights the strongest one.","zh":"如果列出許多好處，“most importantly” 會突出最強的一個。"},{"en":"The phrase signals the writer’s main priority.","zh":"這個片語標示作者的主要優先事項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"saved lives","meaning":"獲挽救的生命","examples":[{"en":"The main benefit of disaster risk reduction is saved lives.","zh":"災害風險降低的主要好處是獲挽救的生命。"},{"en":"Saved lives are lives protected from death through prevention, rescue, or treatment.","zh":"saved lives 指透過預防、救援或治療而免於死亡的生命。"},{"en":"A working fire alarm can lead to saved lives by warning people early.","zh":"有效火警鐘可以透過及早警告人們而帶來獲挽救的生命。"},{"en":"If disaster warnings reach people quickly, saved lives may be the most important result.","zh":"如果災害警報迅速到達人們手中，獲挽救的生命可能是最重要結果。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on human survival rather than money or buildings.","zh":"這個片語集中於人的生存，而不是金錢或建築物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"every corner of the globe","meaning":"全球每一個角落","examples":[{"en":"Disaster preparedness can save lives in every corner of the globe.","zh":"災害防備可以在全球每一個角落拯救生命。"},{"en":"Every corner of the globe means all parts of the world, including distant or remote places.","zh":"every corner of the globe 指世界所有地方，包括遙遠或偏僻地區。"},{"en":"Online news can reach every corner of the globe within minutes.","zh":"網上新聞可以在數分鐘內到達全球每一個角落。"},{"en":"If disaster knowledge reaches every corner of the globe, more communities can prepare.","zh":"如果災害知識到達全球每一個角落，更多社區就能準備。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strong sense of worldwide coverage.","zh":"這個片語給人強烈的全球覆蓋感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"perhaps the most significant work","meaning":"或許最重要的工作","examples":[{"en":"Perhaps the most significant work was the adoption of the Hyogo Declaration.","zh":"或許最重要的工作是採納《兵庫宣言》。"},{"en":"Perhaps the most significant work means possibly the most important achievement or task.","zh":"perhaps the most significant work 指可能是最重要的成就或任務。"},{"en":"In a school reform project, perhaps the most significant work is training teachers well.","zh":"在學校改革項目中，或許最重要的工作是好好培訓老師。"},{"en":"If a declaration guides future action, it may be more important than speeches or meetings.","zh":"如果宣言能指引未來行動，它可能比演講或會議更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a likely key achievement while allowing some caution.","zh":"這個片語突出一項可能的關鍵成就，同時保留謹慎語氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"drafting and adoption","meaning":"起草和採納","examples":[{"en":"The conference led to the drafting and adoption of the Hyogo Declaration.","zh":"會議促成《兵庫宣言》的起草和採納。"},{"en":"Drafting and adoption mean writing a document and then officially accepting it.","zh":"drafting and adoption 指撰寫文件，然後正式接受它。"},{"en":"A student council may spend weeks on the drafting and adoption of new club rules.","zh":"學生會可能花幾星期起草和採納新的學會規則。"},{"en":"If a declaration is drafted but never adopted, it has less official force.","zh":"如果宣言被起草但從未獲採納，它就較少官方效力。"},{"en":"The phrase combines preparation of wording with formal approval.","zh":"這個片語結合文字準備和正式批准。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Hyogo Declaration","meaning":"《兵庫宣言》","examples":[{"en":"The Hyogo Declaration expressed the international community’s determination.","zh":"《兵庫宣言》表達了國際社會的決心。"},{"en":"The Hyogo Declaration was a formal statement connected with international disaster-risk reduction efforts.","zh":"Hyogo Declaration 指與國際災害風險降低工作相關的正式聲明。"},{"en":"A declaration can state shared principles and guide future action.","zh":"宣言可以列明共同原則並指引未來行動。"},{"en":"If countries agree on a declaration, they show public commitment to a goal.","zh":"如果各國同意一項宣言，就公開顯示對某目標的承諾。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific document from the disaster-reduction conference.","zh":"這個片語指出減災會議中的特定文件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"express the united determination of","meaning":"表達……的共同決心","examples":[{"en":"The declaration expressed the united determination of the international community.","zh":"該宣言表達了國際社會的共同決心。"},{"en":"Express the united determination of means clearly show a shared strong decision or commitment by a group.","zh":"express the united determination of 指清楚顯示某群體共同而堅定的決定或承諾。"},{"en":"A school statement may express the united determination of teachers to stop bullying.","zh":"學校聲明可能表達老師們制止欺凌的共同決心。"},{"en":"If many countries express united determination, they are more likely to coordinate action.","zh":"如果許多國家表達共同決心，它們更可能協調行動。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses shared commitment, not separate private opinions.","zh":"這個片語強調共同承諾，而不是各自的私人意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rely not only on…but on…","meaning":"不只依靠……而是依靠……","examples":[{"en":"The declaration relied not only on technology but on people-centred warning systems.","zh":"該宣言不只依靠科技，而是依靠以人為本的預警系統。"},{"en":"Rely not only on A but on B means A is not enough, and B is also necessary or even more important.","zh":"rely not only on A but on B 指 A 並不足夠，B 也必要，甚至更重要。"},{"en":"Good teaching relies not only on textbooks but on clear examples and student practice.","zh":"良好教學不只依靠教科書，而是依靠清楚例子和學生練習。"},{"en":"Disaster safety cannot rely only on machines if people do not understand warnings.","zh":"如果人們不理解警報，災害安全就不能只依靠機器。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a strong contrast between two sources of support.","zh":"這個片語在兩種支持來源之間形成強烈對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"advanced technology","meaning":"先進科技","examples":[{"en":"Disaster preparedness cannot rely only on advanced technology.","zh":"災害防備不能只依靠先進科技。"},{"en":"Advanced technology means modern, highly developed tools, machines, or systems.","zh":"advanced technology 指現代而高度發展的工具、機器或系統。"},{"en":"A hospital may use advanced technology to monitor patients more accurately.","zh":"醫院可能使用先進科技更準確監察病人。"},{"en":"If advanced technology is not supported by training, people may not use it correctly.","zh":"如果先進科技沒有訓練支援，人們可能無法正確使用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to high-level modern equipment or systems.","zh":"這個片語指高層次現代設備或系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"facilities","meaning":"設施","examples":[{"en":"Advanced facilities alone are not enough for disaster preparedness.","zh":"單靠先進設施不足以做好災害防備。"},{"en":"Facilities are buildings, equipment, or services provided for a particular purpose.","zh":"facilities 指為特定目的提供的建築物、設備或服務。"},{"en":"A sports centre needs facilities such as changing rooms, courts, toilets, and first-aid stations.","zh":"體育中心需要更衣室、球場、洗手間和急救站等設施。"},{"en":"If emergency facilities exist but people do not know how to reach them, lives may still be lost.","zh":"如果緊急設施存在但人們不知道如何到達，生命仍可能喪失。"},{"en":"The word refers to practical resources and physical support systems.","zh":"這個詞指實際資源和實體支援系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"people-centred early warning system","meaning":"以人為本的早期預警系統","examples":[{"en":"The declaration called for a people-centred early warning system.","zh":"該宣言呼籲建立以人為本的早期預警系統。"},{"en":"A people-centred early warning system is a warning system designed around people’s needs, behaviour, language, and ability to act.","zh":"people-centred early warning system 指圍繞人們的需要、行為、語言和行動能力設計的預警系統。"},{"en":"A village warning system may use loudspeakers, text messages, and local leaders so everyone understands the danger.","zh":"村莊預警系統可能使用擴音器、短訊和本地領袖，讓每個人都理解危險。"},{"en":"If warnings reach machines but not people, the system fails its main purpose.","zh":"如果警報到達機器但不到達人，系統就失去主要目的。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that warnings must be usable by real communities.","zh":"這個片語強調警報必須能被真實社區使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"effective communication","meaning":"有效溝通","examples":[{"en":"Effective communication is necessary for disaster-resilient communities.","zh":"有效溝通對具抗災能力的社區是必要的。"},{"en":"Effective communication means sharing information clearly, quickly, and in a way people understand.","zh":"effective communication 指清楚、迅速並以人們理解的方式分享資訊。"},{"en":"A teacher uses effective communication when instructions are simple and examples are clear.","zh":"當指示簡單而例子清楚，老師就是在使用有效溝通。"},{"en":"During disasters, effective communication can prevent panic and guide people to safety.","zh":"災害期間，有效溝通可以防止恐慌並引導人們到安全地方。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on information that actually reaches and helps people.","zh":"這個片語集中於真正到達並幫助人的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"education in the building of","meaning":"在建立……方面的教育","examples":[{"en":"Education is important in the building of disaster-resilient countries.","zh":"在建立具抗災能力國家方面，教育十分重要。"},{"en":"Education in the building of something means teaching and learning used to create or strengthen something.","zh":"education in the building of something 指用於創造或強化某事的教與學。"},{"en":"Health education is important in the building of cleaner school habits.","zh":"在建立更清潔校園習慣方面，健康教育十分重要。"},{"en":"If citizens learn what to do before floods or earthquakes, education helps build resilience.","zh":"如果市民學會在水災或地震前該做甚麼，教育就有助建立韌性。"},{"en":"The phrase shows education as part of a larger construction process.","zh":"這個片語顯示教育是較大建設過程的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"disaster-resilient countries and communities","meaning":"具抗災能力的國家和社區","examples":[{"en":"Effective communication helps build disaster-resilient countries and communities.","zh":"有效溝通有助建立具抗災能力的國家和社區。"},{"en":"Disaster-resilient countries and communities can prepare for, withstand, and recover from disasters more effectively.","zh":"disaster-resilient countries and communities 指能更有效準備、承受並從災害中復原的國家和社區。"},{"en":"A disaster-resilient community may have safe shelters, trained volunteers, and clear warning systems.","zh":"具抗災能力的社區可能有安全庇護所、受訓義工和清楚預警系統。"},{"en":"If a country becomes more resilient, disasters may cause less long-term damage.","zh":"如果一個國家變得更具韌性，災害可能造成較少長期損害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes places strong enough to cope with disasters.","zh":"這個片語描述有能力應對災害的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"intergovernmental panels","meaning":"政府間小組","examples":[{"en":"Intergovernmental panels met during the conference.","zh":"政府間小組在會議期間會面。"},{"en":"Intergovernmental panels are groups made up of representatives from different governments who discuss shared issues.","zh":"intergovernmental panels 指由不同政府代表組成、討論共同議題的小組。"},{"en":"An intergovernmental panel may study climate risks that affect several countries.","zh":"政府間小組可能研究影響幾個國家的氣候風險。"},{"en":"If governments meet in panels, they can compare policies and coordinate decisions.","zh":"如果政府在小組中會面，就可以比較政策並協調決定。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to formal discussion groups between governments.","zh":"這個片語指政府之間的正式討論小組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be underway","meaning":"正在進行","examples":[{"en":"The Great Hanshin-Awaji Earthquake Forum was also underway.","zh":"阪神淡路大地震論壇也正在進行。"},{"en":"Be underway means be happening or already started.","zh":"be underway 指正在發生或已經開始。"},{"en":"The school concert was underway when the parents arrived.","zh":"家長到達時，學校音樂會正在進行。"},{"en":"If recovery work is already underway, help has moved from planning to action.","zh":"如果復原工作已經正在進行，幫助就從規劃轉為行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something in progress.","zh":"這個片語描述進行中的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"magnitude-7.3 earthquake","meaning":"7.3 級地震","examples":[{"en":"The magnitude-7.3 earthquake caused widespread destruction.","zh":"7.3級地震造成大範圍破壞。"},{"en":"A magnitude-7.3 earthquake is a strong earthquake measured at 7.3 on the earthquake magnitude scale.","zh":"magnitude-7.3 earthquake 指在地震震級上量度為7.3的強烈地震。"},{"en":"Buildings in earthquake-prone cities must be designed for strong shaking from major quakes.","zh":"位於地震高危城市的建築物，必須能承受大型地震帶來的強烈搖晃。"},{"en":"If a magnitude-7.3 earthquake hits a dense city, damage can be severe.","zh":"如果7.3級地震襲擊人口密集城市，損害可能嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the measured strength of an earthquake.","zh":"這個片語給出地震的量度強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lead to the loss of","meaning":"導致……喪失","examples":[{"en":"The earthquake led to the loss of over 6,400 lives.","zh":"該地震導致超過6,400人喪生。"},{"en":"Lead to the loss of means cause something valuable, especially lives or property, to be lost.","zh":"lead to the loss of 指導致生命、財產等珍貴事物喪失。"},{"en":"A serious fire can lead to the loss of homes and personal belongings.","zh":"嚴重火災可以導致房屋和個人物品喪失。"},{"en":"If weak buildings collapse during earthquakes, they can lead to the loss of many lives.","zh":"如果脆弱建築在地震中倒塌，就可能導致許多生命喪失。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a cause with a tragic result.","zh":"這個片語把原因與悲劇結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"widespread destruction","meaning":"大範圍破壞","examples":[{"en":"The earthquake caused widespread destruction across many households.","zh":"地震在許多住戶中造成大範圍破壞。"},{"en":"Widespread destruction means serious damage spread over a large area or affecting many people.","zh":"widespread destruction 指嚴重破壞分布於大範圍或影響很多人。"},{"en":"A typhoon may cause widespread destruction if it damages roads, power lines, and homes.","zh":"如果颱風破壞道路、電線和房屋，就可能造成大範圍破壞。"},{"en":"When destruction is widespread, recovery needs coordination across many services.","zh":"當破壞範圍廣泛，復原需要多種服務協調。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both scale and severity.","zh":"這個片語同時強調規模和嚴重性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"affect households","meaning":"影響住戶","examples":[{"en":"The earthquake affected some 460,000 households.","zh":"地震影響約460,000個住戶。"},{"en":"Affect households means have an impact on families or homes.","zh":"affect households 指對家庭或住所有影響。"},{"en":"A rent increase can affect households that already spend most income on housing.","zh":"租金上升可以影響本來已把大部分收入用於住屋的家庭。"},{"en":"If a disaster affects many households, relief must include food, shelter, and daily supplies.","zh":"如果災害影響許多住戶，救援就必須包括食物、住所和日用品。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the impact on homes and families.","zh":"這個片語集中於對家庭和住屋的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"public forum","meaning":"公開論壇","examples":[{"en":"The public forum discussed lessons learned from the earthquake.","zh":"公開論壇討論從地震中汲取的教訓。"},{"en":"A public forum is an open meeting where people discuss an issue and share views or experiences.","zh":"public forum 指人們討論議題並分享觀點或經驗的公開會議。"},{"en":"A town may hold a public forum before changing bus routes.","zh":"城鎮可能在更改巴士路線前舉行公開論壇。"},{"en":"If disaster victims speak at a forum, others can learn from real experience.","zh":"如果災民在論壇上發言，其他人可以從真實經驗中學習。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a discussion event open to a wider audience.","zh":"這個片語指向較廣泛觀眾開放的討論活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"offer a variety of sessions","meaning":"提供多場不同環節","examples":[{"en":"The forum offered a variety of sessions on disaster experience.","zh":"該論壇提供多場關於災害經歷的不同環節。"},{"en":"Offer a variety of sessions means provide several different talks, workshops, or activities.","zh":"offer a variety of sessions 指提供幾場不同講座、工作坊或活動。"},{"en":"A school open day may offer a variety of sessions on subjects, clubs, and university planning.","zh":"學校開放日可能提供多場關於科目、學會和大學規劃的環節。"},{"en":"If a forum offers different sessions, attendees can learn from several angles.","zh":"如果論壇提供不同環節，出席者就可以從幾個角度學習。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses multiple organised parts of an event.","zh":"這個片語強調活動中多個有組織的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lessons learned from","meaning":"從……汲取的教訓","examples":[{"en":"The forum discussed lessons learned from the disastrous earthquake.","zh":"論壇討論從該災難性地震中汲取的教訓。"},{"en":"Lessons learned from something are useful understandings gained after an experience, especially a difficult one.","zh":"lessons learned from something 指從某經歷，尤其困難經歷中獲得的有用理解。"},{"en":"A teacher may discuss lessons learned from a failed group project.","zh":"老師可能討論從一次失敗小組專題中汲取的教訓。"},{"en":"If communities use lessons learned from past disasters, they can prepare better next time.","zh":"如果社區使用從過去災害中汲取的教訓，下次就能準備得更好。"},{"en":"The phrase turns painful experience into practical knowledge.","zh":"這個片語把痛苦經驗轉化為實用知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"disastrous earthquake","meaning":"災難性地震","examples":[{"en":"The forum focused on lessons from the disastrous earthquake.","zh":"論壇集中於該災難性地震的教訓。"},{"en":"A disastrous earthquake is an earthquake that causes severe destruction, death, or suffering.","zh":"disastrous earthquake 指造成嚴重破壞、死亡或痛苦的地震。"},{"en":"A disastrous earthquake may leave thousands of families without homes.","zh":"災難性地震可能令數千家庭失去住所。"},{"en":"If buildings are unsafe, even a strong but manageable earthquake can become disastrous.","zh":"如果建築物不安全，即使是強烈但可應對的地震也可能變成災難。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the terrible consequences of the earthquake.","zh":"這個片語強調地震帶來的可怕後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"earthquake expert","meaning":"地震專家","examples":[{"en":"Earthquake expert Professor Tomohiro Kawata spoke at the forum.","zh":"地震專家 Tomohiro Kawata 教授在論壇上發言。"},{"en":"An earthquake expert is a specialist who studies earthquakes, their effects, or ways to reduce their damage.","zh":"earthquake expert 指研究地震、其影響或減少地震損害方法的專家。"},{"en":"A city may ask an earthquake expert to check whether bridges can survive strong shaking.","zh":"城市可能請地震專家檢查橋樑能否承受強烈搖晃。"},{"en":"If experts explain risk clearly, citizens may take safety drills more seriously.","zh":"如果專家清楚解釋風險，市民可能更認真看待安全演習。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a person with specialist knowledge about earthquakes.","zh":"這個片語指出具有地震專門知識的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"over a decade ago","meaning":"十多年前","examples":[{"en":"The disaster happened over a decade ago.","zh":"該災難發生在十多年前。"},{"en":"Over a decade ago means more than ten years before now or before the time being discussed.","zh":"over a decade ago 指距今或距討論時間超過十年。"},{"en":"A school building opened over a decade ago may now need repairs.","zh":"十多年前啟用的校舍現在可能需要維修。"},{"en":"If a disaster happened over a decade ago, memories may fade unless people keep teaching its lessons.","zh":"如果災難發生在十多年前，除非人們持續教授其教訓，記憶可能淡化。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a time distance of more than ten years.","zh":"這個片語給出超過十年的時間距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the memory of","meaning":"對……的記憶","examples":[{"en":"The memory of the devastation can be forgotten.","zh":"對該災難性破壞的記憶可能被遺忘。"},{"en":"The memory of something is people’s remembered experience or awareness of a past event.","zh":"memory of something 指人們對過去事件的記憶經驗或意識。"},{"en":"The memory of a school accident may lead teachers to improve safety rules.","zh":"對學校事故的記憶可能促使老師改善安全規則。"},{"en":"If the memory of a disaster fades, later generations may repeat old mistakes.","zh":"如果對災害的記憶淡化，後代可能重複舊錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on remembrance of the past.","zh":"這個片語集中於對過去的記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"devastation","meaning":"災難性破壞","examples":[{"en":"The forum helped people remember the devastation caused by the earthquake.","zh":"論壇幫助人們記住地震造成的災難性破壞。"},{"en":"Devastation means severe destruction and suffering.","zh":"devastation 指嚴重破壞和痛苦。"},{"en":"A fire that destroys an entire market leaves devastation for shop owners and families.","zh":"摧毀整個市場的火災，會為店主和家庭留下災難性破壞。"},{"en":"When people see devastation with their own eyes, the need for preparation feels real.","zh":"當人們親眼看見災難性破壞，準備的需要就變得真實。"},{"en":"The word describes damage that is large, painful, and shocking.","zh":"這個詞描述巨大、痛苦而令人震驚的損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"make sure that","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"The forum helped make sure that people did not forget the disaster.","zh":"論壇幫助確保人們沒有忘記該災難。"},{"en":"Make sure that means ensure or check that something happens or is true.","zh":"make sure that 指確保或檢查某事發生或屬實。"},{"en":"A teacher may make sure that every student understands the homework before leaving.","zh":"老師可能在離開前確保每位學生明白功課。"},{"en":"If communities make sure that disaster lessons are remembered, future planning improves.","zh":"如果社區確保災害教訓被記住，未來規劃就會改善。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses careful checking or ensuring.","zh":"這個片語強調仔細確認或保證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"back in 1995","meaning":"早在1995年","examples":[{"en":"The earthquake happened back in 1995.","zh":"該地震早在1995年發生。"},{"en":"Back in 1995 means in the year 1995, usually with a sense that it was some time ago.","zh":"back in 1995 指在1995年，通常帶有事情已是以前的感覺。"},{"en":"Back in 1995, many students did not use the internet for homework.","zh":"早在1995年，許多學生不會用互聯網做功課。"},{"en":"If an event happened back in 1995, younger people may know it only through stories or records.","zh":"如果事件早在1995年發生，年輕人可能只透過故事或記錄知道它。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a past date with a slightly conversational tone.","zh":"這個片語以略口語的語氣給出過去日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"personal stories","meaning":"親身經歷","examples":[{"en":"The forum included personal stories from earthquake victims.","zh":"論壇包括地震災民的親身經歷。"},{"en":"Personal stories are real experiences told by individuals in their own words.","zh":"personal stories 指個人用自己的話講述的真實經驗。"},{"en":"A health lesson may use personal stories to show how smoking affects families.","zh":"健康課可能使用親身經歷展示吸煙如何影響家庭。"},{"en":"Personal stories can make statistics feel human and easier to remember.","zh":"親身經歷可以令統計數字變得有人性並更容易記住。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to individual lived experience.","zh":"這個片語指個人的生活經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"earthquake victims","meaning":"地震災民","examples":[{"en":"Earthquake victims shared their experiences at the forum.","zh":"地震災民在論壇分享他們的經歷。"},{"en":"Earthquake victims are people harmed, injured, displaced, or bereaved by an earthquake.","zh":"earthquake victims 指因地震而受傷、流離失所、失去親人或受害的人。"},{"en":"Earthquake victims may need medical care, housing, counselling, and financial help.","zh":"地震災民可能需要醫療照顧、住屋、輔導和財政幫助。"},{"en":"If victims tell their stories, others can learn what rescue and recovery feel like in real life.","zh":"如果災民講述自己的故事，其他人就能了解現實中的救援和復原感受。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on people who suffered because of an earthquake.","zh":"這個片語集中於因地震而受苦的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"attendees","meaning":"出席者","examples":[{"en":"Attendees listened to stories from earthquake victims.","zh":"出席者聆聽地震災民的故事。"},{"en":"Attendees are people who go to or are present at an event.","zh":"attendees 指參加或出席某活動的人。"},{"en":"Attendees at a school seminar may include students, parents, and teachers.","zh":"學校講座的出席者可能包括學生、家長和老師。"},{"en":"If attendees hear real disaster stories, they may take preparedness more seriously.","zh":"如果出席者聽到真實災害故事，可能更認真看待防備。"},{"en":"The word identifies the people present at an event.","zh":"這個詞指出在活動現場的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"house collapsed","meaning":"房屋倒塌","examples":[{"en":"Kumiko Nagota’s house collapsed in the Kobe earthquake.","zh":"Kumiko Nagota 的房屋在神戶地震中倒塌。"},{"en":"House collapsed means the building fell down or broke apart because it lost structural support.","zh":"house collapsed 指建築物因失去結構支撐而倒下或破裂。"},{"en":"A house may collapse after an earthquake if its walls and foundations are weak.","zh":"如果牆身和地基薄弱，房屋可能在地震後倒塌。"},{"en":"If a house collapses, people inside may be trapped and need rescue.","zh":"如果房屋倒塌，裡面的人可能被困並需要救援。"},{"en":"The phrase describes severe structural failure.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重結構失效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be trapped under","meaning":"被困在……下面","examples":[{"en":"She was trapped under her collapsed house.","zh":"她被困在倒塌的房屋下面。"},{"en":"Be trapped under means be stuck beneath something and unable to get out.","zh":"be trapped under 指被困在某物下方，無法逃出。"},{"en":"A worker may be trapped under fallen shelves after a warehouse accident.","zh":"倉庫意外後，工人可能被困在倒下的貨架下面。"},{"en":"If people are trapped under rubble, rescue teams must act quickly and carefully.","zh":"如果人們被困在瓦礫下面，救援隊必須迅速而小心行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a dangerous position beneath heavy material.","zh":"這個片語描述被困在重物下的危險位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"call for help","meaning":"呼救","examples":[{"en":"She tried to call for help after the house collapsed.","zh":"房屋倒塌後，她試圖呼救。"},{"en":"Call for help means shout, phone, or signal because assistance is needed.","zh":"call for help 指因需要協助而大叫、打電話或發出信號。"},{"en":"A child should call for help if they see someone fall into deep water.","zh":"如果孩子看見有人跌入深水，應該呼救。"},{"en":"If a person is trapped, calling for help may help rescuers find them.","zh":"如果一個人被困，呼救可能幫助救援人員找到他。"},{"en":"The phrase describes asking for urgent assistance.","zh":"這個片語描述請求緊急協助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lose one’s voice","meaning":"失聲","examples":[{"en":"After a while, she lost her voice.","zh":"過了一會兒，她失聲了。"},{"en":"Lose one’s voice means become unable to speak loudly or clearly, often after shouting, illness, or strain.","zh":"lose one’s voice 指無法大聲或清楚說話，通常因大叫、疾病或用聲過度。"},{"en":"A teacher may lose her voice after speaking all day without rest.","zh":"老師整天不停說話後可能失聲。"},{"en":"If a trapped person loses their voice, rescuers may find it harder to locate them.","zh":"如果被困者失聲，救援人員可能更難找到他。"},{"en":"The phrase describes temporary loss of speaking ability.","zh":"這個片語描述暫時失去說話能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"wait until help came","meaning":"等到救援到來","examples":[{"en":"She had to wait until help came.","zh":"她必須等到救援到來。"},{"en":"Wait until help came means remain in place until rescuers or assistance arrived.","zh":"wait until help came 指留在原地，直到救援人員或協助到達。"},{"en":"A lost child should stay near a safe landmark and wait until help comes.","zh":"迷路孩子應留在安全地標附近，等到救援到來。"},{"en":"If someone is trapped and cannot move safely, waiting for help may be the only option.","zh":"如果某人被困且不能安全移動，等待救援可能是唯一選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase describes helpless waiting during danger.","zh":"這個片語描述危險中無助地等待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the town mobilised","meaning":"全鎮動員起來","examples":[{"en":"The town mobilised to support recovery and reconstruction.","zh":"全鎮動員起來支援復原和重建。"},{"en":"The town mobilised means the whole community organised people and resources for action.","zh":"the town mobilised 指整個社區組織人力和資源行動起來。"},{"en":"After a storm, a town may mobilise volunteers to clear roads and deliver food.","zh":"風暴後，城鎮可能動員義工清理道路和派送食物。"},{"en":"If a town mobilises quickly, recovery work can begin before outside aid arrives.","zh":"如果城鎮迅速動員，復原工作可以在外部援助到達前開始。"},{"en":"The phrase describes collective community action.","zh":"這個片語描述社區集體行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"facilitate recovery and reconstruction","meaning":"促進復原和重建","examples":[{"en":"The town mobilised to facilitate recovery and reconstruction.","zh":"全鎮動員起來促進復原和重建。"},{"en":"Facilitate recovery and reconstruction means make it easier for people and places to return to normal and rebuild.","zh":"facilitate recovery and reconstruction 指令人民和地方更容易恢復正常並重建。"},{"en":"Clear road access can facilitate recovery by allowing ambulances and supplies to enter.","zh":"清楚道路通道可以讓救護車和物資進入，從而促進復原。"},{"en":"If local officials coordinate volunteers well, reconstruction can proceed faster.","zh":"如果本地官員好好協調義工，重建就能更快進行。"},{"en":"The phrase combines helping recovery with rebuilding damaged places.","zh":"這個片語結合幫助復原和重建受損地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"exhibition hall","meaning":"展覽廳","examples":[{"en":"An exhibition hall displayed objects donated by earthquake victims.","zh":"展覽廳展示由地震災民捐出的物件。"},{"en":"An exhibition hall is a large room or building where objects, pictures, or information are shown to the public.","zh":"exhibition hall 指向公眾展示物件、圖片或資訊的大房間或建築。"},{"en":"A school may use an exhibition hall to display students’ science projects.","zh":"學校可能使用展覽廳展示學生科學專題。"},{"en":"If disaster objects are shown in an exhibition hall, visitors can understand the human impact more clearly.","zh":"如果災物件在展覽廳展出，訪客可以更清楚理解人的影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a place for public display.","zh":"這個片語指公開展示的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"mounds of rubble","meaning":"一堆堆瓦礫","examples":[{"en":"The exhibition showed pictures of mounds of rubble.","zh":"展覽展示了一堆堆瓦礫的圖片。"},{"en":"Mounds of rubble are piles of broken stone, concrete, wood, or building material after destruction.","zh":"mounds of rubble 指破壞後形成的一堆堆碎石、混凝土、木材或建築材料。"},{"en":"After a building collapses, rescue teams may search through mounds of rubble.","zh":"建築物倒塌後，救援隊可能在一堆堆瓦礫中搜索。"},{"en":"Mounds of rubble show how homes and streets can be turned into wreckage.","zh":"一堆堆瓦礫顯示房屋和街道如何變成廢墟。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a clear image of disaster damage.","zh":"這個片語清楚呈現災害破壞的畫面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a display of objects","meaning":"物件展覽","examples":[{"en":"The exhibition included a display of objects donated by victims.","zh":"展覽包括由受害者捐出的物件展覽。"},{"en":"A display of objects is an arranged presentation of things for people to look at and learn from.","zh":"display of objects 指把物件有安排地展示，讓人觀看和學習。"},{"en":"A museum may create a display of objects from old village life.","zh":"博物館可能製作舊村落生活物件展覽。"},{"en":"If objects from a disaster are displayed, they can make history feel personal and real.","zh":"如果災害中的物件被展示，它們可以令歷史感覺個人化和真實。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a visual arrangement of meaningful items.","zh":"這個片語指有意義物件的視覺展示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"donated by","meaning":"由……捐出","examples":[{"en":"The objects were donated by earthquake victims.","zh":"這些物件由地震災民捐出。"},{"en":"Donated by means given freely by a person or group, usually to help or preserve something.","zh":"donated by 指由某人或群體自願給出，通常為幫助或保存某事。"},{"en":"The school library received books donated by former students.","zh":"學校圖書館收到由舊生捐出的書。"},{"en":"If victims donate objects, they help others remember and learn from the disaster.","zh":"如果災民捐出物件，他們就幫助其他人記住並從災害中學習。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who gave something.","zh":"這個片語指出誰給出了某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a broken clock","meaning":"損壞的時鐘","examples":[{"en":"A broken clock was included in the exhibition.","zh":"展覽中包括一個損壞的時鐘。"},{"en":"A broken clock is a damaged timepiece that no longer works properly.","zh":"broken clock 指損壞而不再正常運作的計時器。"},{"en":"A family may keep a broken clock from a disaster because it marks the moment life changed.","zh":"家庭可能保留災害中的損壞時鐘，因為它標記生命改變的一刻。"},{"en":"Ordinary objects can become powerful memories when they survive a disaster.","zh":"當普通物件經歷災害後留下，它們可以成為有力記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase names a damaged object used as evidence or memory.","zh":"這個片語指出作為證據或記憶的受損物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a child’s toy","meaning":"兒童玩具","examples":[{"en":"A child’s toy melted in the fires caused by the earthquake.","zh":"一件兒童玩具在地震造成的火災中熔化。"},{"en":"A child’s toy is an object a child plays with, such as a doll, car, ball, or stuffed animal.","zh":"child’s toy 指孩子用來玩的物件，例如洋娃娃、玩具車、球或毛公仔。"},{"en":"Seeing a child’s toy in a disaster exhibition can make the loss feel personal.","zh":"在災害展覽中看見兒童玩具，可以令損失感覺更個人化。"},{"en":"If a toy is damaged by fire, it reminds viewers that children and families were affected.","zh":"如果玩具被火燒壞，它提醒觀眾兒童和家庭都受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase names a simple personal object with emotional meaning.","zh":"這個片語指出帶有情感意義的簡單個人物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"melt in the fires","meaning":"在火災中熔化","examples":[{"en":"The child’s toy melted in the fires caused by the earthquake.","zh":"兒童玩具在地震造成的火災中熔化。"},{"en":"Melt in the fires means become soft, liquid, or deformed because of intense heat from fire.","zh":"melt in the fires 指因火災高溫而變軟、變成液態或變形。"},{"en":"Plastic containers may melt in a kitchen fire.","zh":"塑膠容器可能在廚房火災中熔化。"},{"en":"If ordinary objects melt in fires, the heat must have been extremely intense.","zh":"如果普通物件在火災中熔化，熱力必然非常強烈。"},{"en":"The phrase shows damage caused by fire and heat.","zh":"這個片語顯示由火和高溫造成的損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"caused by the earthquake","meaning":"由地震引起","examples":[{"en":"The fires were caused by the earthquake.","zh":"火災由地震引起。"},{"en":"Caused by the earthquake means happening as a result of the earthquake.","zh":"caused by the earthquake 指作為地震結果而發生。"},{"en":"Gas leaks caused by an earthquake can lead to fires after the shaking stops.","zh":"由地震引起的煤氣洩漏，可以在震動停止後引發火災。"},{"en":"If damage is caused by the earthquake, rebuilding plans must consider future shaking.","zh":"如果損害由地震引起，重建計劃就必須考慮未來震動。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the earthquake as the cause.","zh":"這個片語指出地震是原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"as well as being","meaning":"除了是……之外","examples":[{"en":"The facility is a place to learn as well as being a memorial.","zh":"該設施除了是紀念設施之外，也是學習的地方。"},{"en":"As well as being means in addition to being something else.","zh":"as well as being 指除了作為另一種東西之外。"},{"en":"A library is a study space as well as being a community meeting place.","zh":"圖書館除了是學習空間之外，也是社區聚會場所。"},{"en":"If a disaster centre is both a memorial and a learning space, it preserves memory and teaches preparation.","zh":"如果災害中心既是紀念設施又是學習空間，它就保存記憶並教授防備。"},{"en":"The phrase adds a second role or identity.","zh":"這個片語加入第二個角色或身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a memorial","meaning":"紀念設施","examples":[{"en":"The facility serves as a memorial to the earthquake.","zh":"該設施作為地震的紀念設施。"},{"en":"A memorial is a place, object, or event that helps people remember someone or something important.","zh":"memorial 指幫助人們記住重要人物或事件的地方、物件或活動。"},{"en":"A school may build a memorial garden for a teacher who passed away.","zh":"學校可能為逝世老師建立紀念花園。"},{"en":"A disaster memorial can honour victims and remind visitors to prepare for future risks.","zh":"災害紀念設施可以紀念受害者，並提醒訪客為未來風險作準備。"},{"en":"The word refers to a public form of remembrance.","zh":"這個詞指公共形式的紀念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a place to learn from","meaning":"從……學習的地方","examples":[{"en":"The forum is a place to learn from earthquake experiences.","zh":"該論壇是從地震經歷中學習的地方。"},{"en":"A place to learn from something is a setting where people gain knowledge from past events or examples.","zh":"place to learn from something 指人們從過去事件或例子中獲得知識的場所。"},{"en":"A museum can be a place to learn from history through objects and stories.","zh":"博物館可以是透過物件和故事從歷史中學習的地方。"},{"en":"If people learn from disaster experiences, future mistakes may be avoided.","zh":"如果人們從災害經歷中學習，未來錯誤可能被避免。"},{"en":"The phrase turns a location into a source of practical learning.","zh":"這個片語把一個地點變成實際學習來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"earthquake experiences","meaning":"地震經歷","examples":[{"en":"The forum helped people learn from earthquake experiences.","zh":"論壇幫助人們從地震經歷中學習。"},{"en":"Earthquake experiences are the real events, feelings, losses, and lessons people go through during and after an earthquake.","zh":"earthquake experiences 指人們在地震期間和之後經歷的真實事件、感受、損失和教訓。"},{"en":"Survivors’ earthquake experiences can teach others what warning signs, rescue, and recovery feel like.","zh":"倖存者的地震經歷可以教其他人警告信號、救援和復原是甚麼感覺。"},{"en":"If experiences are shared, they become lessons for people who did not live through the disaster.","zh":"如果經歷被分享，它們就成為沒有親歷災害的人可學習的教訓。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on lived experience, not only scientific data.","zh":"這個片語集中於親身經歷，而不只是科學數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"incorporate something into","meaning":"將某事物納入……","examples":[{"en":"The forum aimed to incorporate past lessons into future preparations.","zh":"論壇旨在將過去教訓納入未來準備。"},{"en":"Incorporate something into means include it as part of a larger plan, system, or activity.","zh":"incorporate something into 指把某事作為較大計劃、系統或活動的一部分納入其中。"},{"en":"A teacher may incorporate games into grammar lessons to make practice more active.","zh":"老師可能將遊戲納入文法課，令練習更主動。"},{"en":"If past disaster lessons are incorporated into planning, future responses can improve.","zh":"如果過去災害教訓被納入規劃，未來應對就能改善。"},{"en":"The phrase means adding something in a meaningful, practical way.","zh":"這個片語意思是以有意義、實際的方式加入某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"preparations for future disasters","meaning":"為未來災害作出的準備","examples":[{"en":"Lessons from the earthquake were incorporated into preparations for future disasters.","zh":"從地震中汲取的教訓被納入為未來災害作出的準備。"},{"en":"Preparations for future disasters are plans, training, supplies, and systems arranged before later disasters happen.","zh":"preparations for future disasters 指在日後災害發生前安排的計劃、訓練、物資和系統。"},{"en":"A school’s preparations for future disasters may include evacuation maps and emergency contact lists.","zh":"學校為未來災害作出的準備可能包括疏散地圖和緊急聯絡清單。"},{"en":"If preparations are based on past lessons, they are usually more realistic.","zh":"如果準備基於過去教訓，通常會更符合現實。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on readiness for disasters that may happen later.","zh":"這個片語集中於為可能日後發生的災害作好準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"it was agreed that","meaning":"與會者同意","examples":[{"en":"It was agreed that a new disaster-recovery hub would be established.","zh":"與會者同意建立一個新的災後復原樞紐。"},{"en":"It was agreed that means people reached a shared decision or accepted the same point.","zh":"it was agreed that 指人們達成共同決定或接受同一點。"},{"en":"After the meeting, it was agreed that homework deadlines would be changed.","zh":"會議後，大家同意更改功課截止日期。"},{"en":"If participants agree on a new hub, the idea can move toward action.","zh":"如果參加者同意建立新樞紐，該想法就可以走向行動。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a collective decision.","zh":"這個片語引出集體決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a new hub for","meaning":"……的新樞紐","examples":[{"en":"A new hub for disaster recovery support would be established in Kobe.","zh":"一個災後復原支援的新樞紐將在神戶成立。"},{"en":"A new hub for something is a central place or organisation that coordinates a particular activity.","zh":"a new hub for something 指協調某特定活動的中心地點或組織。"},{"en":"A library can become a new hub for after-school study and community events.","zh":"圖書館可以成為課後學習和社區活動的新樞紐。"},{"en":"If a city becomes a hub for recovery support, experts and resources can be coordinated there.","zh":"如果城市成為復原支援樞紐，專家和資源就可以在那裡協調。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a central point for organised activity.","zh":"這個片語描述有組織活動的中心點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"coordination of","meaning":"……的協調","examples":[{"en":"The hub would support the coordination of international recovery activities.","zh":"該樞紐將支援國際復原活動的協調。"},{"en":"Coordination of something means organising different people, groups, or actions so they work together effectively.","zh":"coordination of something 指組織不同人士、群體或行動，使它們有效合作。"},{"en":"A school trip needs coordination of buses, teachers, students, and meal arrangements.","zh":"學校旅行需要協調巴士、老師、學生和膳食安排。"},{"en":"If recovery activities lack coordination, some areas may receive too much aid while others receive none.","zh":"如果復原活動缺乏協調，有些地區可能得到過多援助，而另一些則沒有。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses organised cooperation.","zh":"這個片語強調有組織合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"international disaster recovery support activities","meaning":"國際災後復原支援活動","examples":[{"en":"The new hub would coordinate international disaster recovery support activities.","zh":"新樞紐將協調國際災後復原支援活動。"},{"en":"International disaster recovery support activities are cross-border efforts that help communities rebuild and recover after disasters.","zh":"international disaster recovery support activities 指跨國幫助社區在災後重建和復原的工作。"},{"en":"These activities may include medical aid, rebuilding homes, restoring schools, and training local workers.","zh":"這些活動可能包括醫療援助、重建房屋、恢復學校和培訓本地工人。"},{"en":"If recovery support is international, countries and organisations must coordinate carefully.","zh":"如果復原支援是國際性的，各國和組織必須仔細協調。"},{"en":"The phrase describes global help after disaster damage has occurred.","zh":"這個片語描述災害損害發生後的全球幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be established in","meaning":"在……成立","examples":[{"en":"The new hub would be established in Kobe.","zh":"新樞紐將在神戶成立。"},{"en":"Be established in means be set up, founded, or officially created in a particular place.","zh":"be established in 指在某特定地方設立、創辦或正式建立。"},{"en":"A new community centre may be established in a neighbourhood with few public services.","zh":"新社區中心可能在公共服務不足的社區成立。"},{"en":"If a recovery hub is established in a disaster-hit city, the place becomes a centre for learning and support.","zh":"如果復原樞紐在受災城市成立，該地就成為學習和支援中心。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where something is formally created.","zh":"這個片語指出某事物在哪裡正式建立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"agree with the information given in","meaning":"符合文中資料","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements agree with the information given in the passage.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否符合文章中的資料。"},{"en":"Agree with the information given in means match what is stated in a particular text.","zh":"agree with the information given in 指與某篇文本所陳述的內容相符。"},{"en":"If the passage says the conference was held in Kobe, a statement saying the same thing agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說會議在神戶舉行，意思相同的陳述就符合文中資料。"},{"en":"Students should compare meaning, not only repeated words.","zh":"學生應比較意思，而不只是重複字詞。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in TRUE, FALSE and NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於 TRUE、FALSE 和 NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"If the passage gives no evidence, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文章沒有提供證據，文中就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the text does not state whether the idea is true or false.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文本沒有說明某想法是真還是假。"},{"en":"If a passage discusses disaster planning but not school fees, there is no information on school fees.","zh":"如果文章討論災害規劃但沒有討論學費，文中就沒有學費相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should choose NOT GIVEN when evidence is absent, not when they are unsure from memory.","zh":"當證據缺失時，學生應選 NOT GIVEN，而不是依靠記憶猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase tells readers that the answer cannot be proven from the text.","zh":"這個片語告訴讀者答案不能從文本證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"poorer countries","meaning":"較貧窮國家","examples":[{"en":"Most people affected by natural disasters are from poorer countries.","zh":"大多數受自然災害影響的人來自較貧窮國家。"},{"en":"Poorer countries are countries with fewer financial resources and often weaker infrastructure.","zh":"poorer countries 指財政資源較少，並通常基礎設施較弱的國家。"},{"en":"Poorer countries may struggle to rebuild hospitals and roads after a major disaster.","zh":"較貧窮國家在大型災害後可能難以重建醫院和道路。"},{"en":"If a poor country is hit by repeated floods, development progress can be delayed for years.","zh":"如果貧窮國家反覆受水災打擊，發展進度可能延誤多年。"},{"en":"The phrase compares countries by economic resources.","zh":"這個片語按經濟資源比較國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"present-day natural disasters","meaning":"現今的自然災害","examples":[{"en":"The question compares present-day natural disasters with disasters of the past.","zh":"題目把現今的自然災害與過去的災害作比較。"},{"en":"Present-day natural disasters are natural disasters happening in the modern period.","zh":"present-day natural disasters 指現代時期發生的自然災害。"},{"en":"Present-day natural disasters may affect more people because more communities live in risky areas.","zh":"現今的自然災害可能影響更多人，因為更多社區住在高危地區。"},{"en":"If present-day disasters are reported instantly online, public awareness may grow faster.","zh":"如果現今災害即時在網上被報道，公眾意識可能更快提升。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts modern disasters with earlier historical disasters.","zh":"這個片語把現代災害與較早歷史災害作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"more dangerous than","meaning":"比……更危險","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether present-day disasters are more dangerous than past disasters.","zh":"該陳述問現今災害是否比過去災害更危險。"},{"en":"More dangerous than means having greater risk, harm, or chance of causing injury or death.","zh":"more dangerous than 指具有更大風險、傷害或造成受傷／死亡的機會。"},{"en":"Driving in heavy rain can be more dangerous than driving on a dry road.","zh":"在大雨中駕駛可能比在乾燥道路上駕駛更危險。"},{"en":"A disaster may be more dangerous if it affects crowded cities and weak buildings.","zh":"如果災害影響擁擠城市和脆弱建築，它可能更危險。"},{"en":"The phrase makes a comparison of danger.","zh":"這個片語作危險程度比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"disasters of the past","meaning":"過去的災害","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to disasters of the past.","zh":"題目提到過去的災害。"},{"en":"Disasters of the past are major harmful events that happened in earlier times.","zh":"disasters of the past 指早期發生的重大有害事件。"},{"en":"Students study disasters of the past to understand what mistakes should not be repeated.","zh":"學生研究過去的災害，以理解哪些錯誤不應重複。"},{"en":"If lessons from past disasters are forgotten, modern communities may remain vulnerable.","zh":"如果過去災害的教訓被遺忘，現代社區可能仍然脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase connects history with present preparedness.","zh":"這個片語把歷史與當前防備連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"countries affected by","meaning":"受……影響的國家","examples":[{"en":"Countries affected by the tsunami faced serious damage.","zh":"受海嘯影響的國家面對嚴重損害。"},{"en":"Countries affected by something are countries that experience harm, disruption, or change because of it.","zh":"countries affected by something 指因某事而經歷傷害、中斷或改變的國家。"},{"en":"Countries affected by drought may need food imports and water-saving policies.","zh":"受乾旱影響的國家可能需要進口糧食和節水政策。"},{"en":"If several countries are affected by one disaster, international coordination becomes important.","zh":"如果幾個國家受同一災害影響，國際協調就變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the places harmed by an event.","zh":"這個片語指出受事件傷害的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"take many years to rebuild","meaning":"需要多年重建","examples":[{"en":"Some disaster-hit countries may take many years to rebuild.","zh":"有些受災國家可能需要多年重建。"},{"en":"Take many years to rebuild means need a long period to repair homes, services, infrastructure, and livelihoods.","zh":"take many years to rebuild 指需要很長時間修復房屋、服務、基礎設施和生計。"},{"en":"A school destroyed by fire may take many years to rebuild if funding is limited.","zh":"如果資金有限，被火災摧毀的學校可能需要多年重建。"},{"en":"If roads, hospitals, and businesses are destroyed, recovery cannot happen overnight.","zh":"如果道路、醫院和企業被摧毀，復原不可能一夜完成。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses slow, long-term reconstruction.","zh":"這個片語強調緩慢而長期的重建。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"being prepared","meaning":"有所準備","examples":[{"en":"Being prepared can reduce the effects of a disaster.","zh":"有所準備可以減少災害的影響。"},{"en":"Being prepared means having plans, supplies, knowledge, and training before a problem happens.","zh":"being prepared 指在問題發生前已有計劃、物資、知識和訓練。"},{"en":"A family is prepared for typhoons if it has water, batteries, food, and a safe meeting place.","zh":"如果家庭有水、電池、食物和安全集合點，就算為颱風有所準備。"},{"en":"If people are prepared, they can act faster and panic less during emergencies.","zh":"如果人們有所準備，緊急時就能更快行動並較少恐慌。"},{"en":"The phrase describes readiness before danger arrives.","zh":"這個片語描述危險到來前的準備狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"know what to do","meaning":"知道該怎樣做","examples":[{"en":"People should know what to do in a disaster.","zh":"人們應該知道在災害中該怎樣做。"},{"en":"Know what to do means understand the correct actions to take in a situation.","zh":"know what to do 指明白在某情況中應採取的正確行動。"},{"en":"Students should know what to do if the fire alarm rings during lunch.","zh":"學生應該知道午飯時火警鐘響該怎樣做。"},{"en":"If people know what to do before shaking starts, they may protect themselves more quickly.","zh":"如果人們在震動開始前知道該怎樣做，就可能更快保護自己。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on practical knowledge for action.","zh":"這個片語集中於行動所需的實用知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"global issue","meaning":"全球議題","examples":[{"en":"Disaster preparedness should be treated as a global issue.","zh":"災害防備應被視為全球議題。"},{"en":"A global issue is a problem that affects many countries and requires wider cooperation.","zh":"global issue 指影響許多國家並需要更廣泛合作的問題。"},{"en":"Climate change is a global issue because it affects weather, food, water, and health worldwide.","zh":"氣候變化是全球議題，因為它影響全球天氣、食物、水和健康。"},{"en":"If disaster risk is global, no country should assume it can solve the problem alone.","zh":"如果災害風險是全球性的，任何國家都不應假設可以獨自解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a problem with worldwide importance.","zh":"這個片語描述具有全球重要性的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"according to the passage","meaning":"根據文章","examples":[{"en":"According to the passage, disaster risk reduction saves lives and money.","zh":"根據文章，降低災害風險可以拯救生命和節省金錢。"},{"en":"According to the passage means based on what the text says, not outside knowledge.","zh":"according to the passage 指根據文本所說，而不是外部知識。"},{"en":"According to the passage, students should choose answers supported by the reading text.","zh":"根據文章，學生應選擇有閱讀文本支持的答案。"},{"en":"If a claim is not in the passage, students should not treat it as a reading answer.","zh":"如果某主張不在文章中，學生不應把它當作閱讀答案。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds learners to rely on the source text.","zh":"這個片語提醒學習者依據來源文本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reducing the risk of disasters","meaning":"減低災害風險","examples":[{"en":"Reducing the risk of disasters is an essential investment.","zh":"減低災害風險是一項必要投資。"},{"en":"Reducing the risk of disasters means lowering the chance or severity of harm caused by disasters.","zh":"reducing the risk of disasters 指降低災害造成傷害的機會或嚴重程度。"},{"en":"Stronger drainage can reduce the risk of floods in a neighbourhood.","zh":"更好的排水系統可以減低社區水災風險。"},{"en":"If risks are reduced before disasters happen, recovery costs may be lower.","zh":"如果風險在災害發生前降低，復原成本可能較低。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on prevention and preparation.","zh":"這個片語集中於預防和準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"focus on growth and development","meaning":"專注於增長和發展","examples":[{"en":"Preparedness can help countries focus on growth and development.","zh":"防備可以幫助國家專注於增長和發展。"},{"en":"Focus on growth and development means give attention to improving the economy, services, and living standards.","zh":"focus on growth and development 指關注改善經濟、服務和生活水平。"},{"en":"A school can focus on growth and development when basic safety problems have been solved.","zh":"當基本安全問題解決後，學校可以專注於成長和發展。"},{"en":"If disasters repeatedly destroy infrastructure, countries cannot focus fully on long-term development.","zh":"如果災害反覆摧毀基礎設施，國家就無法完全專注於長期發展。"},{"en":"The phrase connects stability with progress.","zh":"這個片語把穩定與進步連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be drawn together","meaning":"被凝聚起來","examples":[{"en":"Communities may be drawn together in support of each other.","zh":"社區可能在互相支持中被凝聚起來。"},{"en":"Be drawn together means be brought closer through shared experience, purpose, or need.","zh":"be drawn together 指因共同經歷、目的或需要而變得更接近。"},{"en":"A class may be drawn together after working hard on a difficult school project.","zh":"一個班級在共同完成困難專題後可能被凝聚起來。"},{"en":"Disasters can draw communities together when people help neighbours survive and recover.","zh":"當人們幫助鄰居生存和復原，災害可以把社區凝聚起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes people becoming more united.","zh":"這個片語描述人們變得更團結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in support of each other","meaning":"互相支持","examples":[{"en":"Communities can work in support of each other after disasters.","zh":"災後社區可以互相支持地工作。"},{"en":"In support of each other means helping one another emotionally, practically, or financially.","zh":"in support of each other 指在情感、實際或財政上互相幫助。"},{"en":"Students may study in support of each other before a difficult exam.","zh":"學生可能在困難考試前互相支持地溫習。"},{"en":"If neighbours act in support of each other, recovery can begin even before official aid arrives.","zh":"如果鄰居互相支持，正式援助到達前復原已可以開始。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses mutual help.","zh":"這個片語強調相互幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"become more economically stable","meaning":"變得經濟上更穩定","examples":[{"en":"Preparedness may help communities become more economically stable.","zh":"防備可能幫助社區變得經濟上更穩定。"},{"en":"Become more economically stable means become less likely to suffer serious financial disruption.","zh":"become more economically stable 指較不容易遭受嚴重財務中斷。"},{"en":"A family becomes more economically stable when it has savings and steady income.","zh":"當家庭有儲蓄和穩定收入，就會變得經濟上更穩定。"},{"en":"If disaster damage is reduced, businesses and workers can recover faster.","zh":"如果災害損害減少，企業和工人可以更快復原。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stronger financial security.","zh":"這個片語描述更強財務安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"save lives and money","meaning":"拯救生命並節省金錢","examples":[{"en":"Disaster risk reduction can save lives and money.","zh":"災害風險降低可以拯救生命並節省金錢。"},{"en":"Save lives and money means prevent deaths and reduce financial loss at the same time.","zh":"save lives and money 指同時防止死亡並減少財務損失。"},{"en":"Road safety rules can save lives and money by reducing accidents and hospital costs.","zh":"道路安全規則可以透過減少意外和醫療成本來拯救生命並節省金錢。"},{"en":"If flood barriers prevent damage, they may protect families and reduce rebuilding costs.","zh":"如果防洪屏障防止損害，它們可能保護家庭並減少重建成本。"},{"en":"The phrase shows both human and economic benefits.","zh":"這個片語顯示人的好處和經濟好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the most important outcome","meaning":"最重要的成果","examples":[{"en":"The most important outcome of the conference was the Hyogo Declaration.","zh":"會議最重要的成果是《兵庫宣言》。"},{"en":"The most important outcome is the main result or achievement of an event.","zh":"most important outcome 指某活動的主要結果或成就。"},{"en":"The most important outcome of a lesson may be that students can use the grammar correctly.","zh":"一課最重要的成果可能是學生能正確使用文法。"},{"en":"If a conference produces a strong action plan, that may matter more than the speeches.","zh":"如果會議產生有力行動計劃，這可能比演講更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the key result.","zh":"這個片語指出關鍵結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"discussion and debate amongst","meaning":"在……之間的討論和辯論","examples":[{"en":"The conference involved discussion and debate amongst international attendees.","zh":"會議涉及國際出席者之間的討論和辯論。"},{"en":"Discussion and debate amongst means exchange of views and arguments among a group of people.","zh":"discussion and debate amongst 指一群人之間交換觀點和論證。"},{"en":"A class project may involve discussion and debate amongst students before a final decision.","zh":"班級專題在作最終決定前，可能涉及學生之間的討論和辯論。"},{"en":"If international attendees debate openly, stronger solutions may emerge.","zh":"如果國際出席者公開辯論，就可能出現更強解決方案。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active exchange within a group.","zh":"這個片語描述群體內的積極交流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"international community attendees","meaning":"國際社會出席者","examples":[{"en":"International community attendees discussed disaster reduction.","zh":"國際社會出席者討論減災。"},{"en":"International community attendees are people from countries and organisations who attend a global meeting.","zh":"international community attendees 指出席全球會議的各國和組織人士。"},{"en":"At a climate summit, international community attendees may include officials, scientists, and charity workers.","zh":"在氣候峰會上，國際社會出席者可能包括官員、科學家和慈善工作者。"},{"en":"If attendees come from many places, they bring different disaster experiences and solutions.","zh":"如果出席者來自許多地方，他們會帶來不同災害經驗和解決方案。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies participants from the wider global community.","zh":"這個片語指出來自更廣泛全球社會的參與者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"chance for participants to","meaning":"讓參加者有機會去……","examples":[{"en":"The conference gave participants a chance to review the Yokohama Strategy.","zh":"會議讓參加者有機會檢討《橫濱策略》。"},{"en":"Chance for participants to means an opportunity for people taking part to do something.","zh":"chance for participants to 指讓參與者做某事的機會。"},{"en":"A workshop gives participants a chance to practise speaking in small groups.","zh":"工作坊讓參加者有機會在小組中練習說話。"},{"en":"If participants have a chance to review a plan, they can improve it with experience.","zh":"如果參加者有機會檢討計劃，就能用經驗改善它。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights an opportunity created by an event.","zh":"這個片語突出活動創造的機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"writing and acceptance of","meaning":"……的撰寫和接受","examples":[{"en":"The writing and acceptance of the Hyogo Declaration was a major outcome.","zh":"《兵庫宣言》的撰寫和接受是一項主要成果。"},{"en":"Writing and acceptance of a document means creating its wording and then formally agreeing to it.","zh":"writing and acceptance of a document 指撰寫文件內容，然後正式同意它。"},{"en":"A club may spend time on the writing and acceptance of its new rules.","zh":"學會可能花時間撰寫和接受新規則。"},{"en":"If countries accept a declaration, it becomes a shared public commitment.","zh":"如果各國接受宣言，它就成為共同公開承諾。"},{"en":"The phrase combines drafting with approval.","zh":"這個片語結合起草和批准。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"acknowledgement that","meaning":"承認……","examples":[{"en":"The declaration included the acknowledgement that risk reduction matters.","zh":"該宣言包括承認風險降低很重要。"},{"en":"Acknowledgement that means recognition or acceptance that something is true or important.","zh":"acknowledgement that 指承認或接受某事是真實或重要的。"},{"en":"A teacher’s acknowledgement that students are tired can make the class feel understood.","zh":"老師承認學生很累，可以令全班感到被理解。"},{"en":"If leaders acknowledge that risk reduction matters, they are more likely to fund it.","zh":"如果領袖承認風險降低很重要，他們就更可能資助它。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an accepted point.","zh":"這個片語引出被接受的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"investment in the future","meaning":"對未來的投資","examples":[{"en":"Disaster risk reduction is an investment in the future.","zh":"災害風險降低是對未來的投資。"},{"en":"Investment in the future means spending time, effort, or money now to gain long-term benefits later.","zh":"investment in the future 指現在投入時間、努力或金錢，以日後獲得長期好處。"},{"en":"Education is an investment in the future because it improves people’s choices and opportunities.","zh":"教育是對未來的投資，因為它改善人的選擇和機會。"},{"en":"If disaster prevention saves lives later, today’s spending becomes future protection.","zh":"如果災害預防日後拯救生命，今天的支出就成為未來保障。"},{"en":"The phrase frames preparation as long-term value.","zh":"這個片語把準備描述為長期價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be effectively rebuilt","meaning":"有效地重建","examples":[{"en":"Kobe was effectively rebuilt after the earthquake.","zh":"神戶在地震後被有效地重建。"},{"en":"Be effectively rebuilt means be successfully reconstructed so that a place can function again.","zh":"be effectively rebuilt 指被成功重建，使某地能再次運作。"},{"en":"A school can be effectively rebuilt after a fire if classrooms, offices, and safety systems are restored.","zh":"如果課室、辦公室和安全系統被恢復，學校就可以在火災後有效地重建。"},{"en":"If a city is rebuilt effectively, people can return to work, school, and normal life.","zh":"如果城市被有效重建，人們就能回到工作、學校和正常生活。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses successful reconstruction, not just partial repair.","zh":"這個片語強調成功重建，而不只是局部維修。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"due to the support of","meaning":"由於……的支持","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Kobe was rebuilt due to the support of the United Nations.","zh":"題目問神戶是否由於聯合國的支持而重建。"},{"en":"Due to the support of means because of help, backing, or assistance from someone or an organisation.","zh":"due to the support of 指因為來自某人或某組織的幫助、支持或援助。"},{"en":"A student may improve due to the support of patient teachers and family members.","zh":"學生可能由於耐心老師和家人的支持而進步。"},{"en":"If a city recovers due to outside support, that support played an important role.","zh":"如果城市由於外部支持而復原，該支持就發揮了重要作用。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of help behind a result.","zh":"這個片語指出結果背後的幫助來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the stated purpose of","meaning":"明確說明的目的","examples":[{"en":"The stated purpose of the forum was to remember and learn from the disaster.","zh":"論壇明確說明的目的是記住並從該災難中學習。"},{"en":"The stated purpose of something is the goal that is clearly said or written.","zh":"stated purpose of something 指清楚說出或寫明的目標。"},{"en":"The stated purpose of a school trip may be to learn about local history.","zh":"學校旅行明確說明的目的可能是學習本地歷史。"},{"en":"If the stated purpose is learning, activities should help people gain understanding.","zh":"如果明確目的在於學習，活動就應幫助人獲得理解。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the officially expressed aim.","zh":"這個片語指官方表達的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be better prepared for","meaning":"為……作更好準備","examples":[{"en":"The forum helped others be better prepared for future disasters.","zh":"論壇幫助其他人為未來災害作更好準備。"},{"en":"Be better prepared for means have stronger plans, knowledge, or resources for a future situation.","zh":"be better prepared for 指對未來情況有更強計劃、知識或資源。"},{"en":"Students are better prepared for exams when they practise under timed conditions.","zh":"學生在限時條件下練習時，就能為考試作更好準備。"},{"en":"If communities learn from past earthquakes, they can be better prepared for the next one.","zh":"如果社區從過去地震中學習，就能為下一次作更好準備。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improved readiness.","zh":"這個片語描述更佳準備狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"remember and learn from","meaning":"記住並從……學習","examples":[{"en":"The forum encouraged people to remember and learn from what happened.","zh":"論壇鼓勵人們記住並從發生的事情中學習。"},{"en":"Remember and learn from means keep the past in mind and use it to improve future actions.","zh":"remember and learn from 指記住過去，並用它改善未來行動。"},{"en":"A student should remember and learn from mistakes made in a mock exam.","zh":"學生應記住並從模擬考中的錯誤學習。"},{"en":"If communities remember and learn from disasters, they can avoid repeating dangerous habits.","zh":"如果社區記住並從災害中學習，就能避免重複危險習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase combines memory with practical improvement.","zh":"這個片語結合記憶和實際改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"disaster control initiatives","meaning":"災害控制措施","examples":[{"en":"The question asks students to match statements with disaster control initiatives.","zh":"題目要求學生把陳述與災害控制措施配對。"},{"en":"Disaster control initiatives are organised actions or programmes designed to manage or reduce disaster risks.","zh":"disaster control initiatives 指有組織、旨在管理或降低災害風險的行動或計劃。"},{"en":"A city’s disaster control initiatives may include warning systems, evacuation routes, and emergency training.","zh":"城市的災害控制措施可能包括預警系統、疏散路線和緊急訓練。"},{"en":"If initiatives are clear, people know which action belongs to which disaster problem.","zh":"如果措施清楚，人們就知道哪項行動對應哪個災害問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to planned efforts to control disaster impact.","zh":"這個片語指控制災害影響的計劃性努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"people should be the first to","meaning":"人們應首先去……","examples":[{"en":"The initiative suggests that people should be the first to communicate disaster information.","zh":"該措施表示人們應首先傳達災害資料。"},{"en":"People should be the first to means ordinary people should take the earliest or leading action.","zh":"people should be the first to 指普通人應採取最早或帶頭的行動。"},{"en":"Students should be the first to report a broken window if they see it happen.","zh":"如果學生看見窗戶被打破，他們應首先舉報。"},{"en":"If local people communicate warnings first, neighbours may receive information faster.","zh":"如果本地人首先傳達警報，鄰居可能更快收到資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase gives priority to people’s immediate role.","zh":"這個片語把人的即時角色置於優先位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"communicate disaster information","meaning":"傳達災害資料","examples":[{"en":"People should communicate disaster information effectively.","zh":"人們應有效傳達災害資料。"},{"en":"Communicate disaster information means share warnings, instructions, and safety details about a disaster.","zh":"communicate disaster information 指分享關於災害的警報、指示和安全細節。"},{"en":"A village leader may communicate disaster information through loudspeakers and phone messages.","zh":"村長可能透過擴音器和電話短訊傳達災害資料。"},{"en":"If information is communicated clearly, people can evacuate before danger reaches them.","zh":"如果資訊清楚傳達，人們就能在危險到達前疏散。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on sending useful safety information.","zh":"這個片語集中於發送有用安全資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"lead to the creation of","meaning":"導致……的成立","examples":[{"en":"The forum led to the creation of a new disaster-recovery hub.","zh":"論壇導致一個新的災後復原樞紐成立。"},{"en":"Lead to the creation of means cause something new to be made or established.","zh":"lead to the creation of 指導致某新事物被製造或建立。"},{"en":"Student complaints may lead to the creation of a quieter study room.","zh":"學生投訴可能導致一間較安靜自修室的成立。"},{"en":"If a forum leads to a new hub, discussion has produced a practical result.","zh":"如果論壇導致新樞紐成立，討論就產生了實際結果。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an event with a newly created outcome.","zh":"這個片語把事件與新創造的結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a reminder of","meaning":"對……的提醒","examples":[{"en":"The forum served as a reminder of the impact of disasters.","zh":"論壇作為對災害影響的提醒。"},{"en":"A reminder of something is something that makes people remember or think about it again.","zh":"reminder of something 指令人重新記起或想到某事的東西。"},{"en":"A photo on a desk can be a reminder of a family holiday.","zh":"書桌上的照片可以是對家庭假期的提醒。"},{"en":"A disaster exhibition can be a reminder of why safety planning matters.","zh":"災害展覽可以提醒人們安全規劃為何重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that brings memory or awareness back.","zh":"這個片語描述把記憶或意識帶回來的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the impact of disasters","meaning":"災害的影響","examples":[{"en":"The exhibition reminded people of the impact of disasters.","zh":"展覽提醒人們災害的影響。"},{"en":"The impact of disasters means the effects disasters have on people, homes, services, and economies.","zh":"impact of disasters 指災害對人、房屋、服務和經濟造成的影響。"},{"en":"A flooded school shows the impact of disasters on education.","zh":"被水浸的學校顯示災害對教育的影響。"},{"en":"If people see the impact clearly, they may support stronger prevention measures.","zh":"如果人們清楚看見影響，就可能支持更強預防措施。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the consequences of disasters.","zh":"這個片語指災害的後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"in times of disaster","meaning":"在災難時期","examples":[{"en":"Developed countries should help less-developed countries in times of disaster.","zh":"發達國家應在災難時期幫助較不發達國家。"},{"en":"In times of disaster means during periods when disasters are happening or have just happened.","zh":"in times of disaster 指災害正在發生或剛發生後的時期。"},{"en":"In times of disaster, schools may become shelters for families who lost homes.","zh":"在災難時期，學校可能成為失去住所家庭的庇護所。"},{"en":"If neighbours cooperate in times of disaster, emergency services can work more effectively.","zh":"如果鄰居在災難時期合作，緊急服務就能更有效運作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to difficult disaster periods.","zh":"這個片語指困難的災害時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"developed countries","meaning":"發達國家","examples":[{"en":"Developed countries were encouraged to support disaster preparedness.","zh":"發達國家被鼓勵支援災害防備。"},{"en":"Developed countries are richer countries with more advanced economies, infrastructure, and public services.","zh":"developed countries 指經濟、基礎設施和公共服務較先進的富裕國家。"},{"en":"Developed countries may have better rescue equipment and stronger emergency systems.","zh":"發達國家可能有較好救援設備和更強緊急系統。"},{"en":"If developed countries share money and expertise, poorer countries may improve preparedness.","zh":"如果發達國家分享資金和專業知識，較貧窮國家可能改善防備。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used in discussions of global inequality and aid.","zh":"這個片語常用於全球不平等和援助討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"less-developed countries","meaning":"較不發達國家","examples":[{"en":"Less-developed countries may need more support after disasters.","zh":"較不發達國家在災後可能需要更多支援。"},{"en":"Less-developed countries are countries with fewer economic resources and less developed infrastructure.","zh":"less-developed countries 指經濟資源較少且基礎設施較不完善的國家。"},{"en":"A less-developed country may have fewer hospitals, weaker roads, and limited emergency equipment.","zh":"較不發達國家可能有較少醫院、較弱道路和有限緊急設備。"},{"en":"If disasters hit less-developed countries, recovery may require international help.","zh":"如果災害打擊較不發達國家，復原可能需要國際幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase compares development level and resource capacity.","zh":"這個片語比較發展水平和資源能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"do more to help","meaning":"做更多去幫助","examples":[{"en":"Developed countries should do more to help less-developed countries.","zh":"發達國家應做更多去幫助較不發達國家。"},{"en":"Do more to help means take additional action to support someone or solve a problem.","zh":"do more to help 指採取額外行動支援某人或解決問題。"},{"en":"A school can do more to help new students by giving them mentors and clear guides.","zh":"學校可以透過給新生導師和清楚指南，做更多去幫助他們。"},{"en":"If rich countries do more to help, disaster-prevention projects may reach vulnerable communities faster.","zh":"如果富裕國家做更多去幫助，災害預防項目可能更快到達脆弱社區。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests present support is not enough.","zh":"這個片語暗示目前支援不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"national development","meaning":"國家發展","examples":[{"en":"National development should include disaster prevention.","zh":"國家發展應包括災害預防。"},{"en":"National development means the process of improving a country’s economy, services, infrastructure, and living standards.","zh":"national development 指改善一個國家的經濟、服務、基礎設施和生活水平的過程。"},{"en":"Building schools, roads, hospitals, and clean-water systems can be part of national development.","zh":"建設學校、道路、醫院和清潔食水系統都可以是國家發展的一部分。"},{"en":"If development ignores disaster risk, progress can be destroyed by one major event.","zh":"如果發展忽視災害風險，進步可能被一場重大事件摧毀。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to long-term improvement of a country.","zh":"這個片語指一個國家的長期改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be considered at the same time","meaning":"同時被考慮","examples":[{"en":"Disaster prevention and national development should be considered at the same time.","zh":"災害預防和國家發展應同時被考慮。"},{"en":"Be considered at the same time means be thought about together rather than separately.","zh":"be considered at the same time 指一起思考，而不是分開處理。"},{"en":"A school should consider cost and student safety at the same time when planning a trip.","zh":"學校規劃旅行時，應同時考慮成本和學生安全。"},{"en":"If development and disaster prevention are considered together, new projects can be safer from the start.","zh":"如果發展和災害預防一同被考慮，新項目從一開始就可以更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses connected planning.","zh":"這個片語強調連貫規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 59 - PREPARING FOR THE THREAT.pdf","sourcePage":21}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 60":[{"front":"coeducational versus single-sex classrooms","meaning":"男女同校課室與單性別課室的比較","examples":[{"en":"The passage compares coeducational versus single-sex classrooms.","zh":"文章比較男女同校課室與單性別課室。"},{"en":"Coeducational versus single-sex classrooms means a comparison between mixed-gender classes and classes for only boys or only girls.","zh":"coeducational versus single-sex classrooms 指比較男女混合課室與只收男生或只收女生的課室。"},{"en":"Parents may compare coeducational versus single-sex classrooms before choosing a secondary school.","zh":"家長選擇中學前，可能會比較男女同校課室與單性別課室。"},{"en":"This comparison can affect decisions about teaching style, social development, and confidence.","zh":"這種比較可以影響關於教學方式、社交發展和自信的決定。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when two different classroom arrangements are being judged against each other.","zh":"當人們評估兩種不同課室安排時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"across the Western world","meaning":"遍及西方世界","examples":[{"en":"Across the Western world, more parents are reconsidering single-sex education.","zh":"遍及西方世界，越來越多家長正在重新考慮單性別教育。"},{"en":"Across the Western world means in many Western countries or societies.","zh":"across the Western world 指在許多西方國家或社會中。"},{"en":"Across the Western world, schools have debated how to balance academic results with student wellbeing.","zh":"遍及西方世界，學校一直爭論如何平衡學業成績與學生福祉。"},{"en":"When a trend appears across the Western world, it is not limited to one country.","zh":"當一種趨勢遍及西方世界，它就不限於一個國家。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broad pattern found in many Western societies.","zh":"這個短語描述在許多西方社會中出現的廣泛模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an increasing number of","meaning":"越來越多的……","examples":[{"en":"An increasing number of parents are returning to traditional divisions in education.","zh":"越來越多家長正在回歸教育中的傳統分隔模式。"},{"en":"An increasing number of means more and more people or things over time.","zh":"an increasing number of 指人或事物數量隨時間越來越多。"},{"en":"An increasing number of students use online dictionaries when reading difficult articles.","zh":"越來越多學生閱讀困難文章時使用網上字典。"},{"en":"If an increasing number of families move into an area, schools may become crowded.","zh":"如果越來越多家庭搬入一個地區，學校可能變得擠迫。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a number that is rising gradually.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸上升的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"return to traditional divisions","meaning":"回歸傳統分隔模式","examples":[{"en":"Some parents are returning to traditional divisions in their children’s education.","zh":"有些家長正在子女教育中回歸傳統分隔模式。"},{"en":"To return to traditional divisions means to go back to older ways of separating groups.","zh":"return to traditional divisions 指回到較舊的群體分隔方式。"},{"en":"A school may return to traditional divisions if it separates students by ability again.","zh":"如果學校再次按能力分班，就可能回歸傳統分隔模式。"},{"en":"Returning to old divisions can make planning easier, but it may also raise fairness concerns.","zh":"回到舊有分隔方式可以令規劃更容易，但也可能引起公平問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a move back toward older forms of separation.","zh":"這個短語描述重新走向較舊的分隔形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"children’s education","meaning":"子女教育","examples":[{"en":"Parents are making important decisions about their children’s education.","zh":"家長正在就子女教育作出重要決定。"},{"en":"Children’s education means the learning, schooling, and development that children receive.","zh":"children’s education 指孩子接受的學習、學校教育和發展。"},{"en":"Parents may discuss children’s education when choosing schools, tutors, or activities.","zh":"家長選擇學校、補習或活動時，可能會討論子女教育。"},{"en":"Good decisions about children’s education can affect confidence, friendships, and future opportunities.","zh":"關於子女教育的好決定可以影響自信、友誼和未來機會。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the whole process of helping children learn and grow.","zh":"這個短語指幫助孩子學習和成長的整個過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"single-sex classrooms","meaning":"單性別課室","examples":[{"en":"Single-sex classrooms have become more common in many Western countries.","zh":"單性別課室在許多西方國家變得更普遍。"},{"en":"Single-sex classrooms are classes where students are all boys or all girls.","zh":"single-sex classrooms 是全部學生都是男生或全部都是女生的課室。"},{"en":"A school may use single-sex classrooms for certain subjects if it believes students learn more comfortably that way.","zh":"如果學校相信學生這樣學得更自在，可能在某些科目使用單性別課室。"},{"en":"Supporters say single-sex classrooms can reduce social pressure and allow more targeted teaching.","zh":"支持者認為單性別課室可以減少社交壓力，並讓教學更有針對性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes classroom grouping by one gender only.","zh":"這個短語描述只按一種性別分組的課室。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"significantly more common","meaning":"明顯更普遍","examples":[{"en":"Single-sex classrooms have become significantly more common.","zh":"單性別課室已變得明顯更普遍。"},{"en":"Significantly more common means much more frequent or widespread than before.","zh":"significantly more common 指比以前常見或廣泛得多。"},{"en":"Online homework became significantly more common after schools improved their digital systems.","zh":"學校改善數碼系統後，網上功課變得明顯更普遍。"},{"en":"When something becomes significantly more common, people begin to notice it as a clear trend.","zh":"當某事變得明顯更普遍，人們開始注意到它是一個清楚趨勢。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the increase is meaningful, not small.","zh":"這個短語顯示增加幅度有意義，而不是很小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"opt for","meaning":"選擇","examples":[{"en":"Parents must decide whether to opt for single-sex or coeducational schooling.","zh":"家長必須決定是選擇單性別教育還是男女同校教育。"},{"en":"To opt for something means to choose it from several possible options.","zh":"opt for 某事，指從幾個可能選項中選擇它。"},{"en":"A student may opt for history instead of geography if she enjoys reading about the past.","zh":"如果學生喜歡閱讀過去的事情，她可能選擇歷史而不是地理。"},{"en":"People usually opt for the choice that best fits their needs, budget, or values.","zh":"人們通常選擇最符合需要、預算或價值觀的選項。"},{"en":"The phrase is a natural way to describe making a choice.","zh":"這個短語是描述作出選擇的自然說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a mode of teaching","meaning":"一種教學模式","examples":[{"en":"Some parents choose a mode of teaching that improves academic learning.","zh":"有些家長選擇一種能改善學習成效的教學模式。"},{"en":"A mode of teaching is a particular way of teaching students.","zh":"mode of teaching 是教授學生的一種特定方式。"},{"en":"Group discussion is one mode of teaching that helps students practise speaking.","zh":"小組討論是一種幫助學生練習說話的教學模式。"},{"en":"A suitable mode of teaching can make difficult content easier to understand.","zh":"合適的教學模式可以令困難內容更容易理解。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the teaching method or style used in class.","zh":"這個短語指課堂中使用的教學方法或風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"improve academic learning","meaning":"改善學習成效","examples":[{"en":"Single-sex teaching may improve a child’s academic learning.","zh":"單性別教學可能改善孩子的學習成效。"},{"en":"To improve academic learning means to help students understand school subjects better and perform more strongly.","zh":"improve academic learning 指幫助學生更好理解學科並有更強表現。"},{"en":"Clear examples can improve academic learning because students see how ideas work.","zh":"清楚例子可以改善學習成效，因為學生看見概念如何運作。"},{"en":"Smaller classes may improve academic learning by giving teachers more time with each student.","zh":"較小班級可以讓老師有更多時間照顧每名學生，從而改善學習成效。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on progress in school-related knowledge and skills.","zh":"這個短語重點在學校知識和技能方面的進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a coeducational school","meaning":"男女同校學校","examples":[{"en":"Some parents choose a coeducational school for a more rounded education.","zh":"有些家長為了更全面的教育而選擇男女同校學校。"},{"en":"A coeducational school is a school where boys and girls study together.","zh":"coeducational school 是男生和女生一起學習的學校。"},{"en":"A coeducational school may help students learn how to work with classmates of another gender.","zh":"男女同校學校可以幫助學生學會如何與另一性別的同學合作。"},{"en":"Studying together can build social confidence, but it may also create certain social pressures.","zh":"一起學習可以建立社交自信，但也可能造成某些社交壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a mixed-gender school setting.","zh":"這個短語描述男女混合的學校環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a more rounded education","meaning":"更全面的教育","examples":[{"en":"A coeducational school may offer a more rounded education.","zh":"男女同校學校可能提供更全面的教育。"},{"en":"A more rounded education develops not only academic ability but also social skills, confidence, and character.","zh":"more rounded education 不只發展學業能力，也發展社交技巧、自信和品格。"},{"en":"Sports, music, group projects, and mixed friendships can all support a more rounded education.","zh":"運動、音樂、小組項目和混合友誼都可以支持更全面的教育。"},{"en":"Students may benefit when school prepares them for real social situations, not just exams.","zh":"當學校讓學生準備面對真實社交情況，而不只是考試，學生可能受益。"},{"en":"The phrase describes education that is broader and more balanced.","zh":"這個短語描述更廣泛、更平衡的教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"there is no doubt that","meaning":"毫無疑問","examples":[{"en":"There is no doubt that boys and girls may learn in different ways.","zh":"毫無疑問，男生和女生可能以不同方式學習。"},{"en":"There is no doubt that means the writer believes something is clearly true.","zh":"there is no doubt that 指作者認為某事明顯是真實的。"},{"en":"There is no doubt that regular reading helps students build vocabulary.","zh":"毫無疑問，定期閱讀幫助學生建立詞彙量。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to introduce a point the writer treats as certain.","zh":"這個短語用來引出作者視為確定的觀點。"},{"en":"It can make an argument sound confident, so the claim should be well supported.","zh":"它可以令論點聽起來有信心，所以聲稱應有充分支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ways of learning","meaning":"學習方式","examples":[{"en":"Boys and girls may have very different ways of learning.","zh":"男生和女生可能有非常不同的學習方式。"},{"en":"Ways of learning are the methods or styles people use to understand and remember information.","zh":"ways of learning 是人們理解和記住資料所用的方法或風格。"},{"en":"Some students learn through diagrams, while others learn through discussion or practice.","zh":"有些學生透過圖表學習，另一些則透過討論或練習學習。"},{"en":"Different ways of learning can affect how teachers design lessons.","zh":"不同學習方式可以影響老師如何設計課堂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how people take in and use knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述人們如何吸收和使用知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"whereas","meaning":"然而；而","examples":[{"en":"Boys may learn better through movement, whereas girls may learn better through visual means.","zh":"男生可能透過動作學得更好，而女生可能透過視覺方式學得更好。"},{"en":"Whereas is used to show a contrast between two facts or groups.","zh":"whereas 用來顯示兩個事實或群體之間的對比。"},{"en":"Some students prefer quiet study, whereas others learn better by talking through ideas.","zh":"有些學生偏好安靜溫習，而另一些透過討論想法學得更好。"},{"en":"This word helps compare differences without saying one side is always better.","zh":"這個詞幫助比較差異，而不是說一方永遠更好。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful for balanced comparison.","zh":"這個短語適合用於平衡比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"through movement, sound and touch","meaning":"透過動作、聲音和觸覺","examples":[{"en":"Research suggests that boys learn better through movement, sound and touch.","zh":"研究顯示，男生透過動作、聲音和觸覺學得較好。"},{"en":"Through movement, sound and touch means by using physical action, listening, and hands-on contact.","zh":"through movement, sound and touch 指透過身體動作、聆聽和親手接觸。"},{"en":"Young children may learn spelling through movement, sound and touch by clapping syllables and tracing letters.","zh":"幼童可以透過拍打音節和描寫字母，以動作、聲音和觸覺學習串字。"},{"en":"These methods can help active learners stay focused and remember ideas more clearly.","zh":"這些方法可以幫助好動學習者保持專注並更清楚記住概念。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning through body-based and sensory experience.","zh":"這個短語描述透過身體和感官經驗學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"visual and oral means","meaning":"視覺及口語方式","examples":[{"en":"Girls may learn better through visual and oral means.","zh":"女生可能透過視覺及口語方式學得較好。"},{"en":"Visual and oral means are methods involving seeing and speaking or listening.","zh":"visual and oral means 是涉及觀看和說話或聆聽的方法。"},{"en":"Charts, pictures, explanations, and discussion are visual and oral means of learning.","zh":"圖表、圖片、解釋和討論都是視覺及口語學習方式。"},{"en":"Visual and oral methods can help students organise ideas and express them clearly.","zh":"視覺及口語方式可以幫助學生組織想法並清楚表達。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning through sight and spoken language.","zh":"這個短語描述透過視覺和口語學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a clear advantage of","meaning":"……的一個明顯優點","examples":[{"en":"A clear advantage of single-sex education is that teaching can be more targeted.","zh":"單性別教育的一個明顯優點是教學可以更有針對性。"},{"en":"A clear advantage of something is an obvious benefit it provides.","zh":"clear advantage of 某事，是它提供的一個明顯好處。"},{"en":"A clear advantage of online notes is that students can review them at home.","zh":"網上筆記的一個明顯優點是學生可以在家重溫。"},{"en":"When an advantage is clear, people can explain why the choice may be useful.","zh":"當優點明顯，人們可以解釋為何該選擇可能有用。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a strong positive point.","zh":"這個短語引出一個強而正面的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a single-sex educational setting","meaning":"單性別教育環境","examples":[{"en":"Teachers can adapt their methods in a single-sex educational setting.","zh":"老師可以在單性別教育環境中調整教學方法。"},{"en":"A single-sex educational setting is a learning environment where students are all from one gender.","zh":"single-sex educational setting 是學生全部來自同一性別的學習環境。"},{"en":"In a single-sex educational setting, a teacher may design examples around one group’s learning needs.","zh":"在單性別教育環境中，老師可能圍繞某一群體的學習需要設計例子。"},{"en":"Such a setting may reduce certain social pressures but cannot suit every child automatically.","zh":"這種環境可能減少某些社交壓力，但不會自動適合每個孩子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the broader environment, not just the classroom walls.","zh":"這個短語描述更廣泛的環境，而不只是課室牆壁。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tailor teaching styles to","meaning":"因應……調整教學方式","examples":[{"en":"Teachers can tailor teaching styles to the gender being taught.","zh":"老師可以因應所教授的性別調整教學方式。"},{"en":"To tailor teaching styles to a group means to adjust teaching methods to fit that group’s needs.","zh":"tailor teaching styles to 某群體，指調整教學方法以配合該群體需要。"},{"en":"A tutor may tailor teaching styles to shy students by using more pair practice before presentations.","zh":"補習老師可能因應害羞學生調整教學方式，在匯報前加入更多二人練習。"},{"en":"Tailored teaching can improve learning because students receive examples and activities that suit them.","zh":"度身調整的教學可以改善學習，因為學生得到適合自己的例子和活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adapting teaching rather than using one method for everyone.","zh":"這個短語描述調整教學，而不是對所有人使用同一方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the gender being taught","meaning":"所教授的性別","examples":[{"en":"The teacher adapts lessons to the gender being taught.","zh":"老師因應所教授的性別調整課堂。"},{"en":"The gender being taught means the gender group of the students in that class.","zh":"gender being taught 指該班學生所屬的性別群體。"},{"en":"A teacher may think about the gender being taught when choosing examples for a single-sex class.","zh":"老師為單性別班選擇例子時，可能會考慮所教授的性別。"},{"en":"Focusing only on gender can be risky because students within the same gender still differ.","zh":"只集中於性別可能有風險，因為同一性別內的學生仍然不同。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies which student group the lesson is designed for.","zh":"這個短語指出課堂為哪一個學生群體而設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the resurgence of","meaning":"……的重新興起","examples":[{"en":"The resurgence of single-sex education has changed teacher training needs.","zh":"單性別教育的重新興起改變了教師培訓需要。"},{"en":"The resurgence of something means its return or renewed popularity after a period of decline.","zh":"resurgence of 某事，指它在一段衰落後回歸或重新流行。"},{"en":"The resurgence of handwritten notes surprised teachers after years of laptop use.","zh":"在多年使用手提電腦後，手寫筆記的重新興起令老師驚訝。"},{"en":"When an old idea returns, schools may need new rules and training.","zh":"當舊想法回歸，學校可能需要新規則和培訓。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something becoming important again.","zh":"這個短語描述某事再次變得重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"undergo additional training","meaning":"接受額外培訓","examples":[{"en":"Many teachers have had to undergo additional training.","zh":"許多老師不得不接受額外培訓。"},{"en":"To undergo additional training means to receive extra instruction beyond normal training.","zh":"undergo additional training 指接受正常培訓以外的額外指導。"},{"en":"Nurses may undergo additional training before using new medical equipment.","zh":"護士使用新醫療設備前，可能要接受額外培訓。"},{"en":"Additional training helps workers handle situations that ordinary training did not cover.","zh":"額外培訓幫助員工處理普通培訓未涵蓋的情況。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning extra skills for a new need.","zh":"這個短語描述為新需要學習額外技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"techniques appropriate to","meaning":"適合……的技巧","examples":[{"en":"Teachers need techniques appropriate to the single-sex classroom environment.","zh":"老師需要適合單性別課室環境的技巧。"},{"en":"Techniques appropriate to a situation are methods that fit that situation well.","zh":"techniques appropriate to 某情況，是很適合該情況的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher needs techniques appropriate to beginners, such as clear models and simple practice.","zh":"老師需要適合初學者的技巧，例如清楚示範和簡單練習。"},{"en":"Using the wrong technique can make students confused even if the teacher works hard.","zh":"使用錯誤技巧即使老師很努力，也可以令學生困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes methods suited to a particular context.","zh":"這個短語描述適合特定語境的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"potential advantages","meaning":"潛在優點","examples":[{"en":"There are many potential advantages for children in single-sex schools.","zh":"單性別學校對孩子有許多潛在優點。"},{"en":"Potential advantages are possible benefits that may appear under the right conditions.","zh":"potential advantages 是在合適條件下可能出現的好處。"},{"en":"One potential advantage of small classes is that teachers can know students better.","zh":"小班教學的一個潛在優點是老師可以更了解學生。"},{"en":"Potential advantages are not guaranteed; they depend on how a policy is carried out.","zh":"潛在優點不是保證一定發生；它們取決於政策如何執行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes benefits that may happen but still need evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述可能出現但仍需要證據的好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"succeed in","meaning":"在……中取得成功","examples":[{"en":"Some children succeed in single-sex schools.","zh":"有些孩子在單性別學校中取得成功。"},{"en":"To succeed in a place or activity means to do well there.","zh":"succeed in 某地方或活動，指在其中表現良好。"},{"en":"A student may succeed in public speaking after practising with supportive classmates.","zh":"學生在支持自己的同學面前練習後，可能在公開演說中取得成功。"},{"en":"Children succeed when their learning environment matches their needs and confidence level.","zh":"當學習環境配合孩子需要和自信水平，他們就較容易成功。"},{"en":"The phrase describes achieving good results in a particular setting.","zh":"這個短語描述在特定環境中取得好結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the lack of social pressure","meaning":"缺乏社交壓力","examples":[{"en":"Some students benefit from the lack of social pressure.","zh":"有些學生因缺乏社交壓力而受益。"},{"en":"The lack of social pressure means there is less pressure from classmates about how to behave or appear.","zh":"lack of social pressure 指來自同學關於如何行為或外表的壓力較少。"},{"en":"A quiet student may speak more freely when there is a lack of social pressure.","zh":"當缺乏社交壓力，安靜學生可能更自由地說話。"},{"en":"Less social pressure can help students try subjects or activities without fear of judgement.","zh":"較少社交壓力可以幫助學生嘗試科目或活動，而不用害怕被評價。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a more comfortable environment with fewer social expectations.","zh":"這個短語描述社交期望較少、更舒適的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"learn and grow at their own pace","meaning":"按自己的步伐學習和成長","examples":[{"en":"Children may learn and grow at their own pace in single-sex schools.","zh":"孩子可能在單性別學校中按自己的步伐學習和成長。"},{"en":"To learn and grow at one’s own pace means to develop without being forced to match others’ speed.","zh":"learn and grow at one’s own pace 指不用被迫配合他人速度而發展。"},{"en":"A child may learn and grow at her own pace when parents stop comparing her with cousins.","zh":"當家長停止把孩子與表兄弟姊妹比較，她可能按自己的步伐學習和成長。"},{"en":"Students often become more confident when they are allowed enough time to improve.","zh":"當學生被給予足夠時間進步，他們常變得更有信心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes personal development according to individual speed.","zh":"這個短語描述按個人速度進行的個人成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pressure commonly found","meaning":"常見的壓力","examples":[{"en":"Students may avoid the pressure commonly found in coeducational schools.","zh":"學生可能避開男女同校學校中常見的壓力。"},{"en":"Pressure commonly found in a place means stress or expectations often present there.","zh":"pressure commonly found in 某地方，指那裏常出現的壓力或期望。"},{"en":"The pressure commonly found before exams can make students sleep less.","zh":"考試前常見的壓力可以令學生睡少了。"},{"en":"If pressure is common in an environment, many people may treat it as normal even when it is harmful.","zh":"如果壓力在某環境中很常見，許多人可能把它視為正常，即使它有害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a frequent source of stress.","zh":"這個短語描述常見的壓力來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"between the genders","meaning":"不同性別之間","examples":[{"en":"Social pressure can arise between the genders in coeducational schools.","zh":"社交壓力可以在男女同校學校中不同性別之間出現。"},{"en":"Between the genders means between boys and girls, or between male and female groups.","zh":"between the genders 指男生和女生之間，或男性和女性群體之間。"},{"en":"Misunderstandings between the genders may appear when students rarely discuss feelings openly.","zh":"當學生很少公開討論感受，不同性別之間可能出現誤解。"},{"en":"Schools can reduce tension between the genders by teaching respectful communication.","zh":"學校可以透過教授尊重溝通，減少不同性別之間的緊張。"},{"en":"The phrase describes relationships or differences involving gender groups.","zh":"這個短語描述涉及性別群體的關係或差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"research conducted in","meaning":"在……進行的研究","examples":[{"en":"Research conducted in a single-sex school reached a positive conclusion.","zh":"在一所單性別學校進行的研究得出正面結論。"},{"en":"Research conducted in a place means a study carried out there.","zh":"research conducted in 某地方，指在那裏進行的研究。"},{"en":"Research conducted in hospitals can help doctors understand patient care better.","zh":"在醫院進行的研究可以幫助醫生更了解病人護理。"},{"en":"Where research is conducted matters because the setting affects the results.","zh":"研究在哪裏進行很重要，因為環境會影響結果。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the location or context of a study.","zh":"這個短語指出研究的地點或語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"conclude that","meaning":"得出結論認為","examples":[{"en":"The research concluded that students thrived in a close-knit environment.","zh":"研究得出結論認為，學生在關係緊密的環境中茁壯成長。"},{"en":"To conclude that means to decide something after considering evidence.","zh":"conclude that 指在考慮證據後判定某事。"},{"en":"After checking attendance records, the school concluded that later buses caused repeated lateness.","zh":"查核出席紀錄後，學校得出結論認為較遲班次巴士造成反覆遲到。"},{"en":"A strong conclusion should be based on evidence, not only opinion.","zh":"有力結論應基於證據，而不只是意見。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the result of reasoning or research.","zh":"這個短語引出推理或研究的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"thrive in","meaning":"在……中茁壯成長","examples":[{"en":"Students may thrive in a close-knit school environment.","zh":"學生可能在關係緊密的學校環境中茁壯成長。"},{"en":"To thrive in an environment means to grow, learn, or succeed well there.","zh":"thrive in 某環境，指在那裏良好成長、學習或成功。"},{"en":"Some children thrive in small classes because teachers can give them more attention.","zh":"有些孩子在小班中茁壯成長，因為老師可以給他們更多注意。"},{"en":"People thrive when the environment matches their needs and gives them support.","zh":"當環境配合需要並提供支援，人們就會茁壯成長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes doing very well in a particular setting.","zh":"這個短語描述在特定環境中表現非常好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a close-knit environment","meaning":"關係緊密的環境","examples":[{"en":"Students often benefit from a close-knit environment.","zh":"學生常從關係緊密的環境中受益。"},{"en":"A close-knit environment is a place where people know, support, and trust one another.","zh":"close-knit environment 是人們彼此認識、支持和信任的地方。"},{"en":"A small class can become a close-knit environment if students help each other regularly.","zh":"如果學生經常互相幫助，小班可以成為關係緊密的環境。"},{"en":"In a close-knit environment, shy students may feel safer asking questions.","zh":"在關係緊密的環境中，害羞學生可能更安心提問。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a community with strong relationships.","zh":"這個短語描述有強烈人際關係的社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"closer interaction with","meaning":"與……有更密切的互動","examples":[{"en":"Single-sex schools may allow closer interaction with teachers.","zh":"單性別學校可能讓學生與老師有更密切的互動。"},{"en":"Closer interaction with someone means more frequent, direct, or personal communication with that person.","zh":"closer interaction with 某人，指與該人有更頻繁、直接或個人化的溝通。"},{"en":"Smaller tutorial groups allow closer interaction with classmates and the tutor.","zh":"較小的補習小組讓學生與同學和導師有更密切的互動。"},{"en":"Closer interaction can help teachers notice problems before they become serious.","zh":"更密切互動可以幫助老師在問題變嚴重前注意到它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a stronger and more direct relationship.","zh":"這個短語描述更強、更直接的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in surveys of","meaning":"在關於……的調查中","examples":[{"en":"In surveys of over 1,000 single-sex schools, students reported positive experiences.","zh":"在關於一千多所單性別學校的調查中，學生表示有正面經驗。"},{"en":"In surveys of a group means according to questionnaires or studies involving that group.","zh":"in surveys of 某群體，指根據涉及該群體的問卷或研究。"},{"en":"In surveys of office workers, many said flexible hours improved their mood.","zh":"在關於辦公室員工的調查中，許多人表示彈性工時改善了心情。"},{"en":"Survey results can show patterns, but they should be read with care.","zh":"調查結果可以顯示模式，但應小心閱讀。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence collected from many people or organisations.","zh":"這個短語引出從許多人或組織收集的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the absence of the opposite sex","meaning":"沒有異性在場","examples":[{"en":"The absence of the opposite sex was not usually missed.","zh":"沒有異性在場通常沒有令人掛念。"},{"en":"The absence of the opposite sex means boys or girls were not present in that learning environment.","zh":"absence of the opposite sex 指男生或女生不在該學習環境中。"},{"en":"In a girls-only class, the absence of boys may make some students feel less judged.","zh":"在女校班別中，沒有男生在場可能令有些學生較少覺得被評價。"},{"en":"Some students may not miss the opposite sex if the classroom feels focused and supportive.","zh":"如果課室感覺專注和有支援，有些學生未必想念異性在場。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one gender not being present.","zh":"這個短語描述某一性別不在場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be missed","meaning":"被想念；令人掛念","examples":[{"en":"The absence of boys or girls was not missed by many students.","zh":"許多學生並不想念男生或女生不在場。"},{"en":"To be missed means to be noticed and wanted when absent.","zh":"be missed 指某人或某物缺席時被注意到並被想要。"},{"en":"A friendly teacher is missed when she leaves the school.","zh":"一位友善老師離開學校時會令人掛念。"},{"en":"If something is not missed, people do not feel a strong lack of it.","zh":"如果某物沒有令人掛念，人們就不會強烈感到缺少它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes whether absence creates a feeling of loss.","zh":"這個短語描述缺席是否造成失落感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"allow students to","meaning":"讓學生能夠……","examples":[{"en":"Single-sex schools may allow students to focus more seriously on education.","zh":"單性別學校可能讓學生能夠更認真專注於教育。"},{"en":"Allow students to do something means give students the chance or freedom to do it.","zh":"allow students to do something 指給學生機會或自由去做某事。"},{"en":"A quiet reading room can allow students to study without distraction.","zh":"安靜閱讀室可以讓學生能夠不受干擾地學習。"},{"en":"Good classroom rules allow students to learn while still feeling safe.","zh":"良好課室規則讓學生能夠學習，同時仍感到安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making an action possible for students.","zh":"這個短語描述令學生做到某行動成為可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a direct and serious approach to","meaning":"對……採取直接而認真的態度","examples":[{"en":"Students may develop a more direct and serious approach to their education.","zh":"學生可能對自己的教育採取更直接而認真的態度。"},{"en":"A direct and serious approach to something means dealing with it clearly, purposefully, and responsibly.","zh":"direct and serious approach to 某事，指清楚、有目的和負責任地處理它。"},{"en":"A student takes a direct and serious approach to revision when she identifies weak areas and practises them daily.","zh":"當學生找出弱項並每天練習，她就是對溫習採取直接而認真的態度。"},{"en":"This approach can improve results because effort is focused rather than casual.","zh":"這種態度可以改善成績，因為努力是集中而非隨便的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a mature and focused attitude.","zh":"這個短語描述成熟而專注的態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the conventional view","meaning":"傳統看法","examples":[{"en":"The conventional view was that coeducation would reduce gender stereotypes.","zh":"傳統看法是男女同校教育會減少性別定型。"},{"en":"The conventional view is the common or traditional opinion held by many people.","zh":"conventional view 是許多人持有的常見或傳統意見。"},{"en":"The conventional view is that students should revise quietly, but some learn better through discussion.","zh":"傳統看法是學生應安靜溫習，但有些人透過討論學得更好。"},{"en":"Conventional views can be useful, but they may need to be tested against evidence.","zh":"傳統看法可以有用，但可能需要用證據檢驗。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces what people generally used to believe.","zh":"這個短語引出人們一般曾相信的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"coeducation","meaning":"男女同校教育","examples":[{"en":"Coeducation became common in many Western countries.","zh":"男女同校教育在許多西方國家變得普遍。"},{"en":"Coeducation is the education of boys and girls together in the same school or classroom.","zh":"coeducation 是男生和女生在同一學校或課室一起接受教育。"},{"en":"Coeducation can help students practise everyday communication with the opposite gender.","zh":"男女同校教育可以幫助學生練習與異性的日常溝通。"},{"en":"It may also create social pressure if gender stereotypes are strong.","zh":"如果性別定型強烈，它也可能造成社交壓力。"},{"en":"The word describes mixed-gender schooling.","zh":"這個詞描述男女混合的學校教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"break down gender stereotypes","meaning":"打破性別定型","examples":[{"en":"Many people hoped coeducation would break down gender stereotypes.","zh":"許多人希望男女同校教育會打破性別定型。"},{"en":"To break down gender stereotypes means to weaken fixed ideas about what boys or girls should do.","zh":"break down gender stereotypes 指削弱關於男生或女生應做甚麼的固定想法。"},{"en":"A girl joining a robotics club can help break down gender stereotypes about technology.","zh":"女生加入機械人學會可以幫助打破關於科技的性別定型。"},{"en":"Schools break down stereotypes when they encourage all students to try all subjects.","zh":"當學校鼓勵所有學生嘗試所有科目，就是在打破性別定型。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reducing narrow beliefs about gender roles.","zh":"這個短語描述減少對性別角色的狹窄信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"prove to be the case","meaning":"證明情況確是如此","examples":[{"en":"This has not always proved to be the case.","zh":"這並不總是證明情況確是如此。"},{"en":"To prove to be the case means to turn out to be true after evidence or experience is considered.","zh":"prove to be the case 指在考慮證據或經驗後證明是真的。"},{"en":"Teachers hoped the new timetable would reduce stress, but this did not prove to be the case.","zh":"老師希望新時間表會減壓，但這沒有證明情況確是如此。"},{"en":"A belief may sound reasonable but still fail to prove to be the case in real life.","zh":"一個信念可能聽起來合理，但在現實中仍未必證明如此。"},{"en":"The phrase compares expectation with actual result.","zh":"這個短語比較預期與實際結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"advocates of","meaning":"……的支持者","examples":[{"en":"Advocates of single-sex education argue that it can benefit students.","zh":"單性別教育的支持者主張它可以令學生受益。"},{"en":"Advocates of something are people who support and publicly defend it.","zh":"advocates of 某事，是支持並公開維護它的人。"},{"en":"Advocates of school lunches say hungry students cannot concentrate well.","zh":"學校午餐的支持者認為飢餓學生無法好好集中精神。"},{"en":"Advocates often use evidence, examples, and moral arguments to persuade others.","zh":"支持者常使用證據、例子和道德論點說服別人。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies supporters of an idea or policy.","zh":"這個短語指出某想法或政策的支持者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"coeducational settings","meaning":"男女同校環境","examples":[{"en":"Boys in coeducational settings may avoid certain subjects.","zh":"男女同校環境中的男生可能避開某些科目。"},{"en":"Coeducational settings are school or classroom environments where boys and girls learn together.","zh":"coeducational settings 是男生和女生一起學習的學校或課室環境。"},{"en":"In coeducational settings, students may become more used to working with the opposite gender.","zh":"在男女同校環境中，學生可能更習慣與異性合作。"},{"en":"These settings can build social skills, but they may also carry gender expectations.","zh":"這些環境可以建立社交技巧，但也可能帶有性別期望。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mixed-gender learning environments.","zh":"這個短語描述男女混合的學習環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be less likely to","meaning":"較不可能……","examples":[{"en":"Boys may be less likely to study the arts in mixed schools.","zh":"男生在混合學校中可能較不可能修讀藝術科目。"},{"en":"To be less likely to do something means to have a lower chance of doing it.","zh":"be less likely to do something 指做某事的機會較低。"},{"en":"Students are less likely to ask questions if classmates laugh at mistakes.","zh":"如果同學嘲笑錯誤，學生較不可能提問。"},{"en":"A person may be less likely to join an activity when it feels socially risky.","zh":"當活動感覺有社交風險，一個人可能較不可能參加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reduced probability.","zh":"這個短語描述較低可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"study the arts","meaning":"修讀藝術科目","examples":[{"en":"Some boys avoid studying the arts in coeducational settings.","zh":"有些男生在男女同校環境中避免修讀藝術科目。"},{"en":"To study the arts means to learn subjects such as music, drama, visual art, or literature.","zh":"study the arts 指學習音樂、戲劇、視覺藝術或文學等科目。"},{"en":"A student may study the arts because she enjoys painting, acting, or analysing stories.","zh":"學生可能因喜歡繪畫、演戲或分析故事而修讀藝術科目。"},{"en":"Studying the arts can build creativity, expression, and cultural understanding.","zh":"修讀藝術科目可以建立創意、表達能力和文化理解。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to learning artistic and creative subjects.","zh":"這個短語指學習藝術和創意科目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"advanced academic subjects","meaning":"高階學術科目","examples":[{"en":"Some students may avoid advanced academic subjects because of social pressure.","zh":"有些學生可能因社交壓力而避開高階學術科目。"},{"en":"Advanced academic subjects are difficult school subjects studied at a higher level.","zh":"advanced academic subjects 是在較高水平學習的困難學科。"},{"en":"Physics, advanced mathematics, and literature can be advanced academic subjects.","zh":"物理、高階數學和文學都可以是高階學術科目。"},{"en":"Students may avoid advanced subjects if they fear being labelled too serious or unusual.","zh":"如果學生害怕被標籤為太認真或異常，可能會避開高階科目。"},{"en":"The phrase describes challenging courses that require stronger academic ability.","zh":"這個短語描述需要較強學術能力的挑戰性課程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"just to avoid","meaning":"只是為了避免……","examples":[{"en":"Boys may avoid certain subjects just to avoid social categorisation.","zh":"男生可能避開某些科目，只是為了避免社會分類。"},{"en":"Just to avoid means for the sole purpose of escaping something unwanted.","zh":"just to avoid 指唯一目的就是避開某件不想要的事。"},{"en":"A student may sit at the back just to avoid being asked questions.","zh":"學生可能坐在後排，只是為了避免被提問。"},{"en":"People sometimes make choices not because they prefer them, but just to avoid embarrassment.","zh":"人們有時作選擇，不是因為偏好，而只是為了避免尷尬。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that avoidance is the main reason for an action.","zh":"這個短語顯示逃避是行動的主要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"social categorisation","meaning":"社會分類","examples":[{"en":"Students may worry about the social categorisation of certain subjects.","zh":"學生可能擔心某些科目的社會分類。"},{"en":"Social categorisation means putting people or activities into social groups or labels.","zh":"social categorisation 指把人或活動放入社會群體或標籤中。"},{"en":"A boy may avoid dance if social categorisation makes it seem “not for boys”.","zh":"如果社會分類令舞蹈看似「不適合男生」，男生可能會避開它。"},{"en":"Social categorisation can limit choices because students fear how others will judge them.","zh":"社會分類可以限制選擇，因為學生害怕別人如何評價自己。"},{"en":"The phrase describes labelling by society or peer groups.","zh":"這個短語描述由社會或同儕作出的標籤化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the feminine realm","meaning":"女性範疇","examples":[{"en":"Some subjects may be seen as being in the feminine realm.","zh":"有些科目可能被視為屬於女性範疇。"},{"en":"The feminine realm means an area wrongly associated mainly with girls or women.","zh":"feminine realm 指被錯誤地主要聯繫到女生或女性的範疇。"},{"en":"Some people may treat childcare as part of the feminine realm, even though fathers can be excellent carers.","zh":"有些人可能把照顧孩子視為女性範疇，即使父親也可以是出色照顧者。"},{"en":"Labelling a subject as feminine can discourage boys from trying it.","zh":"把一個科目標籤為女性化，可以阻止男生嘗試。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a gendered social label, not a natural rule.","zh":"這個短語描述性別化社會標籤，而不是自然規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tend to avoid","meaning":"往往避免","examples":[{"en":"Girls may tend to avoid science and technology subjects.","zh":"女生可能往往避免科學及科技科目。"},{"en":"To tend to avoid something means to usually keep away from it or choose not to do it.","zh":"tend to avoid 某事，指通常遠離它或選擇不做它。"},{"en":"Shy students may tend to avoid speaking in front of the whole class.","zh":"害羞學生可能往往避免在全班面前說話。"},{"en":"People tend to avoid activities when they expect criticism or failure.","zh":"當人們預期會被批評或失敗，就往往避免某些活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a repeated pattern of avoidance.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆出現的逃避模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"science and technology subjects","meaning":"科學及科技科目","examples":[{"en":"Girls may avoid science and technology subjects in mixed schools.","zh":"女生在混合學校中可能避免科學及科技科目。"},{"en":"Science and technology subjects include areas such as biology, physics, computing, and engineering.","zh":"science and technology subjects 包括生物、物理、電腦和工程等範疇。"},{"en":"Schools can encourage more students to choose science and technology subjects by using real-life projects.","zh":"學校可以透過真實生活項目，鼓勵更多學生選擇科學及科技科目。"},{"en":"If these subjects are treated as only for one gender, many students may lose opportunities.","zh":"如果這些科目被視為只屬於一個性別，許多學生可能失去機會。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to academic subjects connected with scientific and technical knowledge.","zh":"這個短語指與科學和技術知識相關的學科。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"male domain","meaning":"男性領域","examples":[{"en":"Science and technology have traditionally been seen as a male domain.","zh":"科學和科技傳統上被視為男性領域。"},{"en":"A male domain is an area wrongly believed to belong mainly to boys or men.","zh":"male domain 是被錯誤認為主要屬於男生或男性的範疇。"},{"en":"Engineering was once treated as a male domain in many schools and workplaces.","zh":"工程曾在許多學校和工作場所被視為男性領域。"},{"en":"Calling a subject a male domain can make girls feel they do not belong there.","zh":"把一個科目稱為男性領域，可以令女生覺得自己不屬於那裏。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a social stereotype about gender and ability.","zh":"這個短語描述關於性別和能力的社會定型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"flourish once again","meaning":"再次興盛","examples":[{"en":"Single-sex schools are flourishing once again.","zh":"單性別學校正在再次興盛。"},{"en":"To flourish once again means to become successful or popular again after declining.","zh":"flourish once again 指在衰落後再次變得成功或受歡迎。"},{"en":"A small bookstore may flourish once again if the community starts supporting local shops.","zh":"如果社區開始支持本地小店，小書店可能再次興盛。"},{"en":"When an old model flourishes again, people usually ask why it has returned.","zh":"當舊模式再次興盛，人們通常會問它為何回歸。"},{"en":"The phrase describes renewed growth or success.","zh":"這個短語描述重新增長或成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"realise that","meaning":"意識到","examples":[{"en":"Parents may realise that children learn in different ways.","zh":"家長可能意識到孩子以不同方式學習。"},{"en":"To realise that means to become aware of or understand a fact.","zh":"realise that 指察覺或理解一個事實。"},{"en":"A student may realise that copying notes is not the same as understanding them.","zh":"學生可能意識到抄筆記不等於理解筆記。"},{"en":"People often realise a problem only after it affects daily life.","zh":"人們常在問題影響日常生活後才意識到它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a moment of understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述理解某事的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in one’s own individual way","meaning":"以自己獨特的方式","examples":[{"en":"A child may learn best in his or her own individual way.","zh":"孩子可能以自己獨特的方式學得最好。"},{"en":"In one’s own individual way means according to one’s personal style, speed, or needs.","zh":"in one’s own individual way 指按自己的個人風格、速度或需要。"},{"en":"One student may revise through diagrams, while another learns in her own individual way by speaking aloud.","zh":"一名學生可能透過圖表溫習，而另一名則以自己獨特的方式大聲朗讀學習。"},{"en":"Respecting individual ways of learning can reduce unfair comparison.","zh":"尊重個別學習方式可以減少不公平比較。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that people do not all develop in the same manner.","zh":"這個短語強調人並非都以同一方式發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"an important consideration","meaning":"重要考慮因素","examples":[{"en":"A child’s learning style is an important consideration in choosing a school.","zh":"孩子的學習方式是選擇學校時的重要考慮因素。"},{"en":"An important consideration is a factor that should be thought about carefully before a decision.","zh":"important consideration 是作決定前應仔細思考的因素。"},{"en":"Travel time is an important consideration when choosing a workplace.","zh":"選擇工作地點時，通勤時間是一個重要考慮因素。"},{"en":"If people ignore important considerations, they may make a choice that looks good but works badly.","zh":"如果人們忽視重要考慮因素，他們可能作出看似好但實際不好用的選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a factor that matters in decision-making.","zh":"這個短語指出決策中重要的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"attending single-sex secondary schools","meaning":"就讀單性別中學","examples":[{"en":"Students attending single-sex secondary schools showed different performance patterns.","zh":"就讀單性別中學的學生顯示出不同的表現模式。"},{"en":"Attending single-sex secondary schools means studying at secondary schools for only boys or only girls.","zh":"attending single-sex secondary schools 指在只收男生或只收女生的中學讀書。"},{"en":"Students attending single-sex secondary schools may experience a different classroom culture from students in mixed schools.","zh":"就讀單性別中學的學生可能經歷與混合學校學生不同的課室文化。"},{"en":"The school type students attend can affect confidence, friendships, and subject choices.","zh":"學生就讀的學校類型可以影響自信、友誼和選科。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a specific group of students by the schools they go to.","zh":"這個短語按學生就讀的學校指出特定群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a slight tendency for","meaning":"……有輕微傾向","examples":[{"en":"There was a slight tendency for males to outperform females.","zh":"男生表現勝過女生有輕微傾向。"},{"en":"A slight tendency for something means a small pattern or weak trend in that direction.","zh":"slight tendency for 某事，指朝該方向的小模式或弱趨勢。"},{"en":"There may be a slight tendency for students to arrive late on rainy mornings.","zh":"雨天早上學生遲到可能有輕微傾向。"},{"en":"A slight tendency is not a strong rule, so it should not be exaggerated.","zh":"輕微傾向不是強烈規則，所以不應誇大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small but noticeable pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述細小但可注意到的模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"outperform","meaning":"表現勝過","examples":[{"en":"Males in single-sex schools showed a slight tendency to outperform females.","zh":"單性別學校中的男生顯示出表現略勝女生的傾向。"},{"en":"To outperform someone means to do better than them in results or performance.","zh":"outperform 某人，指在成績或表現上做得比對方好。"},{"en":"A student may outperform classmates in writing if she reads widely and practises often.","zh":"如果學生廣泛閱讀並經常練習，她可能在寫作上表現勝過同學。"},{"en":"Better support can help weaker groups outperform expectations.","zh":"更好支援可以幫助較弱群體表現勝過預期。"},{"en":"The word describes stronger performance compared with another person or group.","zh":"這個詞描述與另一人或群體相比有更強表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"In contrast, females tended to outperform males in coeducational schools.","zh":"相比之下，女生在男女同校學校中往往表現勝過男生。"},{"en":"In contrast means by comparison, showing a clear difference from the previous point.","zh":"in contrast 指相比之下，顯示與前一點有清楚差異。"},{"en":"Some students enjoy group work; in contrast, others concentrate better alone.","zh":"有些學生喜歡小組工作；相比之下，另一些獨自學習時更能集中。"},{"en":"The phrase helps readers see a difference between two situations.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者看見兩種情況之間的差異。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing opposite or different patterns.","zh":"它適合比較相反或不同模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a clear tendency for","meaning":"……有明顯傾向","examples":[{"en":"There was a clear tendency for females to outperform males.","zh":"女生表現勝過男生有明顯傾向。"},{"en":"A clear tendency for something means a noticeable and fairly strong pattern in that direction.","zh":"clear tendency for 某事，指朝該方向有明顯而頗強的模式。"},{"en":"There is a clear tendency for students to revise more seriously after receiving low mock scores.","zh":"學生在模擬試低分後更認真溫習有明顯傾向。"},{"en":"A clear tendency is stronger than a slight tendency but still not an absolute rule.","zh":"明顯傾向比輕微傾向更強，但仍不是絕對規則。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an obvious pattern in the data or behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述數據或行為中的明顯模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"it was also noted that","meaning":"亦有人指出","examples":[{"en":"It was also noted that girls were more involved in leadership activities.","zh":"亦有人指出，女生更常參與領導活動。"},{"en":"It was also noted that means another point was observed or mentioned.","zh":"it was also noted that 指另一點被觀察到或被提及。"},{"en":"It was also noted that students who slept earlier made fewer careless mistakes.","zh":"亦有人指出，較早睡的學生犯較少粗心錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an additional finding in a formal way.","zh":"這個短語以正式方式引出額外發現。"},{"en":"It helps add one more observation to an argument.","zh":"它幫助為論點加入另一項觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be more likely to","meaning":"較有可能……","examples":[{"en":"Girls were more likely to be involved in leadership activities.","zh":"女生較有可能參與領導活動。"},{"en":"To be more likely to do something means to have a higher chance of doing it.","zh":"be more likely to do something 指做某事的機會較高。"},{"en":"Students are more likely to ask questions when the teacher responds kindly.","zh":"當老師友善回應，學生較有可能提問。"},{"en":"People are more likely to join an activity if they feel welcome and safe.","zh":"如果人們感到受歡迎和安全，就較有可能參加活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes increased probability.","zh":"這個短語描述較高可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be involved in","meaning":"參與……","examples":[{"en":"Girls were more likely to be involved in extracurricular activities.","zh":"女生較有可能參與課外活動。"},{"en":"To be involved in something means to take part in it or have a role in it.","zh":"be involved in 某事，指參與其中或在其中有角色。"},{"en":"A student may be involved in the school newspaper as a writer or editor.","zh":"學生可能以作者或編輯身份參與校報。"},{"en":"Being involved in activities can build confidence, friendships, and responsibility.","zh":"參與活動可以建立自信、友誼和責任感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes participation.","zh":"這個短語描述參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"leadership activities","meaning":"領導活動","examples":[{"en":"Girls in single-sex schools often joined leadership activities.","zh":"單性別學校中的女生常參加領導活動。"},{"en":"Leadership activities are tasks or groups where students practise organising, guiding, and representing others.","zh":"leadership activities 是讓學生練習組織、引導和代表他人的任務或團體。"},{"en":"Running a class committee meeting is one example of a leadership activity.","zh":"主持班會是領導活動的一個例子。"},{"en":"Leadership activities help students learn responsibility, communication, and decision-making.","zh":"領導活動幫助學生學習責任感、溝通和決策。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to activities that develop leadership skills.","zh":"這個短語指培養領導能力的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"student councils","meaning":"學生會","examples":[{"en":"Student councils are one type of leadership activity.","zh":"學生會是一種領導活動。"},{"en":"Student councils are groups of students elected or chosen to represent classmates and organise school matters.","zh":"student councils 是被選出或挑選出來代表同學並組織學校事務的學生團體。"},{"en":"A student council may collect opinions about lunch, school rules, or activities.","zh":"學生會可能收集關於午餐、校規或活動的意見。"},{"en":"Student councils teach students how to speak for others and solve practical problems.","zh":"學生會教學生如何為他人發聲和解決實際問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a student leadership body within a school.","zh":"這個短語指學校內的學生領導組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"athletic associations","meaning":"體育協會","examples":[{"en":"Athletic associations were mentioned as examples of extracurricular activities.","zh":"體育協會被提及為課外活動的例子。"},{"en":"Athletic associations are groups connected with sports, training, or school athletics.","zh":"athletic associations 是與運動、訓練或學校體育有關的團體。"},{"en":"A school athletic association may organise running, basketball, or swimming events.","zh":"學校體育協會可能組織跑步、籃球或游泳活動。"},{"en":"Joining athletic associations can build teamwork, discipline, and physical confidence.","zh":"加入體育協會可以建立團隊精神、紀律和身體自信。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised sports-related groups.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的體育相關團體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"extracurricular activities","meaning":"課外活動","examples":[{"en":"Girls were more likely to join extracurricular activities in single-sex schools.","zh":"女生在單性別學校中較有可能參加課外活動。"},{"en":"Extracurricular activities are activities outside regular academic lessons.","zh":"extracurricular activities 是常規學術課堂以外的活動。"},{"en":"Debate club, sports teams, music groups, and volunteer work are extracurricular activities.","zh":"辯論學會、運動隊、音樂小組和義工服務都是課外活動。"},{"en":"These activities can help students develop skills that exams do not measure.","zh":"這些活動可以幫助學生發展考試無法量度的技能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes school experiences beyond ordinary classes.","zh":"這個短語描述普通課堂以外的學校經歷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"accordingly","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"Accordingly, some girls reported favouring single-sex schools.","zh":"因此，有些女生表示較喜歡單性別學校。"},{"en":"Accordingly means as a result or for that reason.","zh":"accordingly 指作為結果或基於那個原因。"},{"en":"The classroom was noisy; accordingly, the teacher changed the seating plan.","zh":"課室很嘈吵；因此，老師更改了座位安排。"},{"en":"The word links a result to the information just given.","zh":"這個詞把結果與剛給出的資料連起來。"},{"en":"It is a formal way to show consequence.","zh":"它是顯示後果的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"report favouring","meaning":"表示較喜歡","examples":[{"en":"Girls have reported favouring single-sex schools.","zh":"女生曾表示較喜歡單性別學校。"},{"en":"To report favouring something means to say in a survey or account that one prefers it.","zh":"report favouring 某事，指在調查或記述中表示自己較喜歡它。"},{"en":"Students may report favouring shorter lessons if they find long classes tiring.","zh":"如果學生覺得長課堂疲累，可能表示較喜歡較短課堂。"},{"en":"Reported preferences can help schools understand what students feel comfortable with.","zh":"被報告的偏好可以幫助學校了解學生對甚麼感到自在。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stated preference, not necessarily proven benefit.","zh":"這個短語描述被表達出來的偏好，而不一定是已證明的好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tend to be dominated by","meaning":"往往由……主導","examples":[{"en":"Coeducational environments tend to be dominated by males.","zh":"男女同校環境往往由男性主導。"},{"en":"To tend to be dominated by a group means that group usually has more influence or control.","zh":"tend to be dominated by 某群體，指該群體通常有較多影響力或控制權。"},{"en":"Some classroom discussions may be dominated by confident speakers if teachers do not manage turns.","zh":"如果老師不管理發言次序，課堂討論可能由有自信的發言者主導。"},{"en":"A space dominated by one group can make others speak less or feel less welcome.","zh":"由一個群體主導的空間，可以令其他人較少說話或較不受歡迎。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a repeated imbalance in influence.","zh":"這個短語描述影響力上反覆出現的不平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a situation perpetuated by","meaning":"由……延續的情況","examples":[{"en":"Male domination may be a situation perpetuated by teaching staff.","zh":"男性主導可能是由教職員延續的情況。"},{"en":"A situation perpetuated by someone is a problem that continues because that person or group keeps it going.","zh":"situation perpetuated by 某人，是因該人或群體持續令其存在的問題。"},{"en":"Classroom silence can be perpetuated by teachers if they only praise quick answers.","zh":"如果老師只稱讚快速答案，課室沉默可能由老師延續。"},{"en":"A pattern may continue unintentionally when adults repeat old habits.","zh":"當成人重複舊習慣，某種模式可能無意中持續下去。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how a problem is maintained over time.","zh":"這個短語描述問題如何隨時間被維持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"teaching staff","meaning":"教職員","examples":[{"en":"Teaching staff may unintentionally perpetuate male-dominated classroom patterns.","zh":"教職員可能無意中延續男性主導的課室模式。"},{"en":"Teaching staff are the teachers and education workers who teach or support learning in a school.","zh":"teaching staff 是在學校中教授或支援學習的老師和教育工作者。"},{"en":"Teaching staff meet regularly to discuss students’ progress and classroom problems.","zh":"教職員定期開會討論學生進展和課室問題。"},{"en":"Their expectations can shape how students participate in lessons.","zh":"他們的期望可以塑造學生如何參與課堂。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the professional adults involved in teaching.","zh":"這個短語指參與教學的專業成人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"regardless of","meaning":"不論；儘管","examples":[{"en":"Some people oppose single-sex education regardless of its academic benefits.","zh":"有些人不論單性別教育的學業好處如何，仍反對它。"},{"en":"Regardless of means without being affected by a particular factor.","zh":"regardless of 指不受某特定因素影響。"},{"en":"Students must follow safety rules regardless of how experienced they are.","zh":"學生不論經驗多豐富，都必須遵守安全規則。"},{"en":"People may reject a policy on moral grounds regardless of its practical results.","zh":"人們可能基於道德理由反對某政策，不論其實際結果如何。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one factor does not change the decision.","zh":"這個短語顯示某因素不改變決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"increased levels of academic performance","meaning":"學業表現水平提升","examples":[{"en":"Some schools report increased levels of academic performance.","zh":"有些學校報告學業表現水平提升。"},{"en":"Increased levels of academic performance means students are doing better in schoolwork or exams.","zh":"increased levels of academic performance 指學生在功課或考試中表現更好。"},{"en":"A school may report increased levels of academic performance after introducing reading support.","zh":"學校引入閱讀支援後，可能報告學業表現水平提升。"},{"en":"Better teaching, smaller classes, or stronger motivation can raise academic performance.","zh":"更好教學、較小班級或更強動力可以提高學業表現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improvement in measurable learning results.","zh":"這個短語描述可量度學習結果上的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"academic performance and preference","meaning":"學業表現及偏好","examples":[{"en":"The debate involves both academic performance and student preference.","zh":"這場辯論涉及學業表現及學生偏好。"},{"en":"Academic performance and preference means both students’ results and what they personally like or choose.","zh":"academic performance and preference 指學生的成績表現以及他們個人喜歡或選擇甚麼。"},{"en":"A school policy may improve academic performance but still conflict with student preference.","zh":"學校政策可能改善學業表現，但仍與學生偏好衝突。"},{"en":"Good decisions consider both measurable results and how students feel about the environment.","zh":"好決定會同時考慮可量度結果和學生對環境的感受。"},{"en":"The phrase combines achievement with personal choice.","zh":"這個短語把成就與個人選擇結合起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"people concerned about gender equality","meaning":"關注性別平等的人","examples":[{"en":"People concerned about gender equality may oppose single-sex education.","zh":"關注性別平等的人可能反對單性別教育。"},{"en":"People concerned about gender equality are those who care about fair treatment for all genders.","zh":"people concerned about gender equality 是關心所有性別是否被公平對待的人。"},{"en":"Such people may question school rules if boys and girls are offered different opportunities.","zh":"如果男生和女生獲得不同機會，這類人可能質疑校規。"},{"en":"Concern about equality can lead to criticism of policies that separate students by gender.","zh":"對平等的關注可以引致對按性別分隔學生政策的批評。"},{"en":"The phrase describes people motivated by fairness between genders.","zh":"這個短語描述受性別公平推動的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"oppose something on ethical grounds","meaning":"基於倫理理由反對某事","examples":[{"en":"Some people oppose single-sex education on ethical grounds.","zh":"有些人基於倫理理由反對單性別教育。"},{"en":"To oppose something on ethical grounds means to reject it because it seems morally wrong.","zh":"oppose something on ethical grounds 指因某事看似道德上錯誤而反對它。"},{"en":"Some parents oppose school ranking on ethical grounds because it may shame weaker students.","zh":"有些家長基於倫理理由反對學校排名，因為它可能羞辱較弱學生。"},{"en":"A policy can be effective in results but still be opposed on ethical grounds.","zh":"一項政策可以在結果上有效，但仍基於倫理理由被反對。"},{"en":"The phrase explains moral reasons for disagreement.","zh":"這個短語解釋反對的道德原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"force separation between the sexes on","meaning":"強行把性別分隔加諸於……","examples":[{"en":"Critics argue that single-sex education forces separation between the sexes on students.","zh":"批評者認為單性別教育強行把性別分隔加諸於學生。"},{"en":"To force separation between the sexes on students means to make boys and girls study apart without real choice.","zh":"force separation between the sexes on students 指在沒有真正選擇下令男生和女生分開學習。"},{"en":"Parents may object if a school forces separation between the sexes on children for every activity.","zh":"如果學校在每項活動中都強行把性別分隔加諸於孩子，家長可能反對。"},{"en":"Forced separation can feel unfair when students or families do not want it.","zh":"當學生或家庭不想要它，強制分隔可以令人覺得不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises gender separation as something imposed.","zh":"這個短語批評性別分隔是被強加的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in order for","meaning":"為了讓……能夠","examples":[{"en":"In order for schools to run single-sex classrooms, they must offer another option.","zh":"為了讓學校能夠開辦單性別課室，它們必須提供另一選擇。"},{"en":"In order for something to happen means so that it can happen or be possible.","zh":"in order for 某事 to happen 指為了讓它能發生或成為可能。"},{"en":"In order for students to join the trip, parents must sign the consent form.","zh":"為了讓學生能夠參加旅行，家長必須簽署同意書。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a necessary condition.","zh":"這個短語引出必要條件。"},{"en":"It explains what must be true before something can take place.","zh":"它解釋某事發生前必須符合甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"run single-sex classrooms","meaning":"開辦單性別課室","examples":[{"en":"Schools must follow certain rules to run single-sex classrooms.","zh":"學校必須遵守某些規則才能開辦單性別課室。"},{"en":"To run single-sex classrooms means to organise and operate classes for only one gender.","zh":"run single-sex classrooms 指組織和營運只收一種性別的課堂。"},{"en":"A school may run single-sex classrooms for science if it wants to test a new teaching approach.","zh":"如果學校想測試新教學方法，可能為科學科開辦單性別課室。"},{"en":"Running these classes requires planning, staff training, and clear communication with parents.","zh":"開辦這些課室需要規劃、員工培訓和與家長清楚溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase describes managing this type of class arrangement.","zh":"這個短語描述管理這種課堂安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"offer parents the opportunity to","meaning":"為家長提供……的機會","examples":[{"en":"Schools must offer parents the opportunity to choose coeducational classes.","zh":"學校必須為家長提供選擇男女同校課堂的機會。"},{"en":"To offer parents the opportunity to do something means to give parents a real chance to choose it.","zh":"offer parents the opportunity to do something 指給家長真正機會去選擇某事。"},{"en":"A school may offer parents the opportunity to meet teachers before choosing subjects.","zh":"學校可能為家長提供選科前與老師見面的機會。"},{"en":"Offering a choice can reduce conflict because families feel included in the decision.","zh":"提供選擇可以減少衝突，因為家庭會感到被納入決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving parents an option rather than forcing one path.","zh":"這個短語描述給家長一個選項，而不是強迫一條路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"enrol their children in","meaning":"為子女報讀……","examples":[{"en":"Parents may enrol their children in a traditional coeducational classroom.","zh":"家長可以為子女報讀傳統男女同校課室。"},{"en":"To enrol their children in a school or class means to officially register them there.","zh":"enrol their children in 學校或課堂，指正式為子女在那裏登記。"},{"en":"Parents enrol their children in swimming lessons by filling in a form and paying the fee.","zh":"家長透過填表和付款為子女報讀游泳課。"},{"en":"Enrolment decisions affect a child’s timetable, classmates, and learning environment.","zh":"報讀決定會影響孩子的時間表、同學和學習環境。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formally placing children in an educational programme.","zh":"這個短語描述正式把孩子安排到教育課程中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"with regard to","meaning":"關於；至於","examples":[{"en":"With regard to gender segregation, advocates offer a different argument.","zh":"關於性別隔離，支持者提出另一個論點。"},{"en":"With regard to means concerning or in relation to a particular topic.","zh":"with regard to 指關於或就某特定主題而言。"},{"en":"With regard to homework, the teacher said quality matters more than length.","zh":"關於功課，老師說質素比長度更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase helps organise a discussion by clearly naming the topic.","zh":"這個短語透過清楚指出主題來幫助組織討論。"},{"en":"It is a formal way to say “about”.","zh":"它是 “about” 的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"oppose gender segregation","meaning":"反對學校中的性別隔離","examples":[{"en":"Some people oppose gender segregation in schools.","zh":"有些人反對學校中的性別隔離。"},{"en":"To oppose gender segregation means to disagree with separating people by gender.","zh":"oppose gender segregation 指不同意按性別把人分開。"},{"en":"Parents may oppose gender segregation if they want boys and girls to learn together.","zh":"如果家長希望男生和女生一起學習，可能反對性別隔離。"},{"en":"People may oppose it because they worry separation sends the wrong message about equality.","zh":"人們可能反對它，因為擔心分隔傳遞錯誤的平等訊息。"},{"en":"The phrase describes disagreement with gender-based separation.","zh":"這個短語描述反對基於性別的分隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"advocates of the idea","meaning":"這一想法的支持者","examples":[{"en":"Advocates of the idea believe single-sex classes may reduce stereotypes.","zh":"這一想法的支持者相信單性別課堂可能減少性別定型。"},{"en":"Advocates of the idea are people who support that particular view or proposal.","zh":"advocates of the idea 是支持該特定看法或建議的人。"},{"en":"Advocates of the idea of later school starts say teenagers need more sleep.","zh":"較遲上課這一想法的支持者認為青少年需要更多睡眠。"},{"en":"Advocates usually explain why their idea is fair, useful, or necessary.","zh":"支持者通常解釋為何自己的想法公平、有用或必要。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies supporters of a specific argument.","zh":"這個短語指出某特定論點的支持者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"negate gender stereotypes","meaning":"抵消性別定型","examples":[{"en":"Single-sex classes may actually negate gender stereotypes.","zh":"單性別課堂實際上可能抵消性別定型。"},{"en":"To negate gender stereotypes means to reduce or cancel fixed ideas about what each gender should do.","zh":"negate gender stereotypes 指減少或抵消關於各性別應做甚麼的固定想法。"},{"en":"A girls-only coding class may negate gender stereotypes by showing that technology is not only for boys.","zh":"女生編程班可以透過顯示科技不只是男生的東西來抵消性別定型。"},{"en":"When students try subjects freely, stereotypes become weaker.","zh":"當學生自由嘗試科目，定型觀念會變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes challenging and reducing gender-based assumptions.","zh":"這個短語描述挑戰並減少基於性別的假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as mentioned earlier","meaning":"如前所述","examples":[{"en":"As mentioned earlier, students may avoid subjects linked to gender roles.","zh":"如前所述，學生可能避開與性別角色相關的科目。"},{"en":"As mentioned earlier means as already stated before in the discussion.","zh":"as mentioned earlier 指如討論中之前已說過。"},{"en":"As mentioned earlier, students need exact evidence for reading answers.","zh":"如前所述，學生做閱讀答案時需要準確證據。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to refer back to a previous point without repeating it fully.","zh":"作者使用這個短語回指之前觀點，而不用完整重複。"},{"en":"The phrase helps connect later explanation to earlier information.","zh":"這個短語幫助把後來解釋與之前資料連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a mixed classroom","meaning":"男女混合課室","examples":[{"en":"In a mixed classroom, boys and girls may face different social pressures.","zh":"在男女混合課室中，男生和女生可能面對不同社交壓力。"},{"en":"A mixed classroom is a class where boys and girls learn together.","zh":"mixed classroom 是男生和女生一起學習的班級。"},{"en":"A mixed classroom can help students practise cooperation with different classmates.","zh":"男女混合課室可以幫助學生練習與不同同學合作。"},{"en":"It may also create pressure if students fear being judged by the opposite gender.","zh":"如果學生害怕被異性評價，它也可能造成壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a coeducational class.","zh":"這個短語描述男女同校課堂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tasks related to","meaning":"與……有關的任務","examples":[{"en":"Boys may avoid tasks related to the arts.","zh":"男生可能避開與藝術有關的任務。"},{"en":"Tasks related to something are activities connected with that subject or area.","zh":"tasks related to 某事，是與該主題或範疇有關的活動。"},{"en":"Tasks related to science may include experiments, measurements, and lab reports.","zh":"與科學有關的任務可能包括實驗、測量和實驗報告。"},{"en":"Students may avoid tasks related to public speaking if they fear embarrassment.","zh":"如果學生害怕尷尬，可能避開與公開演說有關的任務。"},{"en":"The phrase shows what area a task belongs to.","zh":"這個短語顯示任務屬於哪個範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"show a lack of interest in","meaning":"對……缺乏興趣","examples":[{"en":"Girls may show a lack of interest in science and technology.","zh":"女生可能對科學和科技缺乏興趣。"},{"en":"To show a lack of interest in something means to appear not very curious or willing to take part.","zh":"show a lack of interest in 某事，指看起來不太好奇或不太願意參與。"},{"en":"A student may show a lack of interest in reading if every book feels too difficult.","zh":"如果每本書都感覺太難，學生可能對閱讀缺乏興趣。"},{"en":"Lack of interest can come from fear, bad past experience, or weak encouragement.","zh":"缺乏興趣可以來自恐懼、不好經驗或鼓勵不足。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visible low motivation toward something.","zh":"這個短語描述對某事可見的低動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"existing bias","meaning":"既有偏見","examples":[{"en":"In single-sex environments, there may be no existing bias about certain subjects.","zh":"在單性別環境中，對某些科目可能沒有既有偏見。"},{"en":"Existing bias means prejudice or unfair preference that is already present.","zh":"existing bias 指已經存在的偏見或不公平偏好。"},{"en":"A club may have an existing bias if members assume only older students can lead.","zh":"如果學會成員假設只有高年級學生能領導，該學會可能有既有偏見。"},{"en":"Existing bias can shape choices before students even try an activity.","zh":"既有偏見可以在學生甚至未嘗試活動前已影響選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase describes prejudice that is already built into a situation.","zh":"這個短語描述已存在於情況中的偏見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"this is for boys","meaning":"這是男孩子的","examples":[{"en":"Single-sex classrooms may reduce the idea that a subject is only for boys.","zh":"單性別課室可能減少某科目只屬於男孩子的想法。"},{"en":"“This is for boys” is a stereotype suggesting that only boys should do a certain activity.","zh":"“this is for boys” 是一種定型，暗示只有男生應做某活動。"},{"en":"A girl may avoid robotics if classmates keep saying, “This is for boys.”","zh":"如果同學一直說「這是男孩子的」，女生可能避開機械人活動。"},{"en":"Such labels can stop students from discovering real interests and abilities.","zh":"這類標籤可以阻止學生發現真正興趣和能力。"},{"en":"The phrase represents a limiting gender assumption.","zh":"這個短語代表限制性的性別假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"that is for girls","meaning":"那是女孩子的","examples":[{"en":"Students may avoid thinking that a subject is only for girls.","zh":"學生可能避免認為某科目只屬於女孩子。"},{"en":"“That is for girls” is a stereotype suggesting that only girls should choose a certain activity.","zh":"“that is for girls” 是一種定型，暗示只有女生應選擇某活動。"},{"en":"A boy may avoid dance if classmates say that is for girls.","zh":"如果同學說那是女孩子的，男生可能避開舞蹈。"},{"en":"These labels can make students choose based on fear rather than interest.","zh":"這些標籤可以令學生基於恐懼而不是興趣作選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase represents a social judgement about gender roles.","zh":"這個短語代表關於性別角色的社會判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, a Cambridge University study supported this point.","zh":"事實上，一項劍橋大學研究支持這一點。"},{"en":"In fact introduces information that confirms, corrects, or strengthens a previous idea.","zh":"in fact 引出確認、修正或加強前一想法的資料。"},{"en":"Many students think reading is slow; in fact, regular reading can save time in exams.","zh":"許多學生認為閱讀很慢；事實上，定期閱讀可以在考試中節省時間。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when they want to add stronger evidence or a surprising truth.","zh":"作者想加入更強證據或令人驚訝的真相時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the next point supports the argument.","zh":"這個短語表示下一點支持該論點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a study released by","meaning":"由……發布的研究","examples":[{"en":"A study released by Cambridge University examined single-sex classrooms.","zh":"一項由劍橋大學發布的研究檢視了單性別課室。"},{"en":"A study released by an institution is research made public by that organisation.","zh":"study released by 某機構，是由該組織公開發布的研究。"},{"en":"A study released by a hospital may change how doctors treat a common illness.","zh":"一項由醫院發布的研究可能改變醫生治療常見疾病的方式。"},{"en":"When a respected institution releases a study, people may take its findings seriously.","zh":"當受尊重機構發布研究，人們可能認真看待其發現。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the organisation that published the research.","zh":"這個短語指出發布研究的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Girls were more interested in science as compared with those in traditional settings.","zh":"與傳統環境中的女生相比，女生對科學更感興趣。"},{"en":"As compared with means when compared with another group or situation.","zh":"as compared with 指與另一群體或情況相比。"},{"en":"Students in small groups may speak more as compared with students in large classes.","zh":"與大班學生相比，小組中的學生可能說話更多。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show a difference between two sets of people or conditions.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示兩組人或條件之間的差異。"},{"en":"It is a formal comparison phrase.","zh":"它是一個正式比較短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"traditional settings","meaning":"傳統環境","examples":[{"en":"The study compared single-sex rooms with traditional settings.","zh":"該研究把單性別課室與傳統環境作比較。"},{"en":"Traditional settings are ordinary or long-established environments that people are used to.","zh":"traditional settings 是人們習慣的普通或長久建立的環境。"},{"en":"A traditional classroom setting usually has one teacher and many students facing the board.","zh":"傳統課室環境通常是一位老師和許多學生面向黑板。"},{"en":"Comparing new methods with traditional settings helps show whether change makes a difference.","zh":"把新方法與傳統環境比較，有助顯示改變是否帶來差異。"},{"en":"The phrase describes familiar, established arrangements.","zh":"這個短語描述熟悉、既有的安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be more interested in","meaning":"對……更感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Girls were more interested in math and science in single-sex rooms.","zh":"女生在單性別課室中對數學和科學更感興趣。"},{"en":"To be more interested in something means to feel greater curiosity or willingness to learn about it.","zh":"be more interested in 某事，指對它有更大好奇心或更願意學習。"},{"en":"Students may be more interested in history when lessons include real people’s stories.","zh":"當課堂包括真實人物故事，學生可能對歷史更感興趣。"},{"en":"Interest can rise when students feel safe, capable, and encouraged.","zh":"當學生感到安全、有能力和受鼓勵，興趣可以上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stronger personal attraction to a subject or activity.","zh":"這個短語描述對某科目或活動有更強個人吸引力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"math and science","meaning":"數學和科學","examples":[{"en":"Girls showed greater interest in math and science.","zh":"女生對數學和科學表現出更大興趣。"},{"en":"Math and science are subjects that involve numbers, logic, experiments, and understanding the natural world.","zh":"math and science 是涉及數字、邏輯、實驗和理解自然世界的科目。"},{"en":"Students use math and science when they measure rainfall or design a simple bridge.","zh":"學生量度雨量或設計簡單橋樑時，會使用數學和科學。"},{"en":"Strong skills in math and science can open paths to medicine, engineering, and technology.","zh":"強大的數學和科學能力可以開啟醫學、工程和科技道路。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to two major academic areas often linked to problem-solving.","zh":"這個短語指兩個常與解難相關的主要學術範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"generally preferred by","meaning":"一般較受……喜歡","examples":[{"en":"Math and science are subjects generally preferred by boys in coeducational settings.","zh":"數學和科學是在男女同校環境中一般較受男生喜歡的科目。"},{"en":"Generally preferred by a group means usually liked or chosen more often by that group.","zh":"generally preferred by 某群體，指通常較常被該群體喜歡或選擇。"},{"en":"Football may be generally preferred by students who enjoy outdoor team sports.","zh":"足球可能一般較受喜歡戶外團隊運動的學生歡迎。"},{"en":"General preference shows a pattern but does not describe every individual.","zh":"一般偏好顯示模式，但不描述每一個個體。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common tendency in choice.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇上的常見傾向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"it is important to remember that","meaning":"重要的是要記住","examples":[{"en":"It is important to remember that coeducation is a modern concept.","zh":"重要的是要記住，男女同校教育是一個現代概念。"},{"en":"It is important to remember that means readers should keep this fact in mind.","zh":"it is important to remember that 指讀者應把這個事實記在心中。"},{"en":"It is important to remember that exam marks are not the only measure of ability.","zh":"重要的是要記住，考試分數不是能力的唯一量度。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to prevent readers from forgetting a key point.","zh":"作者使用這個短語，防止讀者忘記關鍵點。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a fact that shapes how the argument should be understood.","zh":"這個短語引出一個會塑造論點理解方式的事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a modern concept","meaning":"現代概念","examples":[{"en":"Coeducation is a modern concept in mainstream education.","zh":"男女同校教育是主流教育中的現代概念。"},{"en":"A modern concept is an idea that became common relatively recently.","zh":"modern concept 是相對近期才變得普遍的想法。"},{"en":"Online privacy is a modern concept that schools now need to teach.","zh":"網上私隱是學校現在需要教授的現代概念。"},{"en":"Modern concepts may seem normal today but were unfamiliar to earlier generations.","zh":"現代概念今天可能看似正常，但對較早世代而言陌生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an idea associated with recent times.","zh":"這個短語描述與近期時代相關的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"introduced into mainstream education","meaning":"被引入主流教育","examples":[{"en":"Coeducation was introduced into mainstream education less than fifty years ago.","zh":"男女同校教育在不足五十年前被引入主流教育。"},{"en":"Introduced into mainstream education means brought into ordinary, widely accepted schooling.","zh":"introduced into mainstream education 指被帶入普通而廣泛接受的學校教育。"},{"en":"Coding was introduced into mainstream education when schools began teaching it to all students.","zh":"當學校開始向所有學生教授編程，它就被引入主流教育。"},{"en":"When an idea enters mainstream education, teacher training and textbooks may change.","zh":"當一個想法進入主流教育，教師培訓和教科書可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a practice becoming part of normal schooling.","zh":"這個短語描述一種做法成為正常學校教育的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mainstream education","meaning":"主流教育","examples":[{"en":"Coeducation became part of mainstream education relatively recently.","zh":"男女同校教育相對近期才成為主流教育的一部分。"},{"en":"Mainstream education is the ordinary education system used by most schools and students.","zh":"mainstream education 是大多數學校和學生使用的普通教育制度。"},{"en":"A teaching method enters mainstream education when many schools adopt it.","zh":"當許多學校採用某教學方法，它就進入主流教育。"},{"en":"Mainstream education changes slowly because it affects many families and teachers.","zh":"主流教育變化較慢，因為它影響許多家庭和老師。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the regular, widely accepted school system.","zh":"這個短語描述常規且廣泛接受的學校制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"bring substantial changes to","meaning":"為……帶來重大改變","examples":[{"en":"Coeducation has brought substantial changes to many societies.","zh":"男女同校教育為許多社會帶來重大改變。"},{"en":"To bring substantial changes to something means to cause large and meaningful changes in it.","zh":"bring substantial changes to 某事，指為它造成巨大而有意義的改變。"},{"en":"The internet brought substantial changes to how students research and submit work.","zh":"互聯網為學生搜集資料和提交功課的方式帶來重大改變。"},{"en":"Substantial changes can affect habits, expectations, and relationships.","zh":"重大改變可以影響習慣、期望和關係。"},{"en":"The phrase describes change that is important, not minor.","zh":"這個短語描述重要而非輕微的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"societies in which","meaning":"……所在的社會","examples":[{"en":"The method affected the societies in which it was adopted.","zh":"這種方法影響了採用它的社會。"},{"en":"Societies in which something happens means the communities or countries where that thing exists.","zh":"societies in which 某事發生，指該事存在的社群或國家。"},{"en":"The societies in which public exams are highly valued may place strong pressure on students.","zh":"在高度重視公開考試的社會中，學生可能承受強烈壓力。"},{"en":"A policy can have different effects in the societies in which it is used.","zh":"一項政策在不同採用它的社會中可以有不同影響。"},{"en":"The phrase links an idea with the places where it operates.","zh":"這個短語把想法與其運作的地方連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"first introduced in","meaning":"最先在……引入","examples":[{"en":"Coeducation was first introduced in Switzerland.","zh":"男女同校教育最先在瑞士引入。"},{"en":"First introduced in a place means first brought into use there.","zh":"first introduced in 某地，指最先在那裏被帶入使用。"},{"en":"A new library system may be first introduced in one campus before spreading to others.","zh":"新圖書館系統可能最先在一個校園引入，再擴展到其他校園。"},{"en":"Knowing where an idea was first introduced helps trace its development.","zh":"知道一個想法最先在哪裏引入，有助追蹤其發展。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the original place of adoption.","zh":"這個短語指出最初採用地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"spread quickly through","meaning":"迅速傳遍……","examples":[{"en":"The idea spread quickly through most Western countries.","zh":"這一想法迅速傳遍大多數西方國家。"},{"en":"To spread quickly through a place means to move or become common there in a short time.","zh":"spread quickly through 某地，指在短時間內傳播或變得常見。"},{"en":"News of a cancelled exam can spread quickly through a school.","zh":"考試取消的消息可以迅速傳遍一所學校。"},{"en":"Ideas spread quickly when people see them as useful or fashionable.","zh":"當人們視想法為有用或時尚，它們會迅速傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rapid movement or adoption across an area.","zh":"這個短語描述在某範圍內快速流動或採用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not without benefits","meaning":"並非沒有好處","examples":[{"en":"Coeducation is certainly not without benefits.","zh":"男女同校教育當然並非沒有好處。"},{"en":"Not without benefits means it does have some advantages, even if there are also problems.","zh":"not without benefits 指它確實有一些優點，即使也有問題。"},{"en":"Online learning is not without benefits because shy students may ask questions through chat.","zh":"網上學習並非沒有好處，因為害羞學生可以透過聊天欄提問。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a balanced view instead of rejecting something completely.","zh":"這個短語給出平衡看法，而不是完全否定某事。"},{"en":"It is a cautious way to admit positive points.","zh":"它是承認正面之處的謹慎說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be excellent for","meaning":"對……非常有幫助","examples":[{"en":"Parents said that coeducation was excellent for their children’s confidence.","zh":"家長說男女同校教育對孩子的自信非常有幫助。"},{"en":"To be excellent for something means to be very helpful or beneficial for it.","zh":"be excellent for 某事，指對它非常有幫助或有益。"},{"en":"Regular reading is excellent for vocabulary growth.","zh":"定期閱讀對詞彙增長非常有幫助。"},{"en":"A supportive teacher can be excellent for a shy student’s confidence.","zh":"支持學生的老師可以對害羞學生的自信非常有幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong positive effect.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈正面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"confidence","meaning":"自信","examples":[{"en":"Coeducational classrooms may improve children’s confidence.","zh":"男女同校課室可能改善孩子的自信。"},{"en":"Confidence is the feeling that you can do something or handle a situation.","zh":"confidence 是相信自己能做到某事或應付某情況的感覺。"},{"en":"A student builds confidence when she answers one question correctly and receives encouragement.","zh":"當學生答對一題並得到鼓勵，她會建立自信。"},{"en":"Confidence can grow through practice, support, and small successful experiences.","zh":"自信可以透過練習、支援和小成功經驗而增長。"},{"en":"The word describes belief in one’s own ability.","zh":"這個詞描述對自己能力的相信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"overcome shyness","meaning":"克服害羞","examples":[{"en":"Coeducation may help students overcome shyness.","zh":"男女同校教育可能幫助學生克服害羞。"},{"en":"To overcome shyness means to become less afraid of speaking or interacting with others.","zh":"overcome shyness 指變得較不害怕說話或與他人互動。"},{"en":"A student may overcome shyness by first speaking in pairs before presenting to the class.","zh":"學生可以先二人對話，再向全班匯報，逐漸克服害羞。"},{"en":"Supportive classmates can help shy students feel safe enough to practise.","zh":"支持自己的同學可以幫助害羞學生感到安全，敢於練習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradually becoming more socially confident.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸變得更有社交自信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"converse about","meaning":"談論……","examples":[{"en":"Students may learn to converse about everyday topics.","zh":"學生可能學會談論日常話題。"},{"en":"To converse about something means to talk about it in a natural exchange.","zh":"converse about 某事，指以自然交流方式談論它。"},{"en":"Language learners practise speaking by conversing about food, hobbies, and school life.","zh":"語言學習者透過談論食物、興趣和校園生活練習說話。"},{"en":"Being able to converse about ordinary topics helps people build friendships.","zh":"能夠談論普通話題有助人建立友誼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes two-way conversation on a subject.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞某主題的雙向對話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"everyday topics","meaning":"日常話題","examples":[{"en":"Students can discuss everyday topics with the opposite gender.","zh":"學生可以與異性討論日常話題。"},{"en":"Everyday topics are ordinary subjects from daily life, such as school, food, hobbies, or transport.","zh":"everyday topics 是來自日常生活的普通主題，例如學校、食物、興趣或交通。"},{"en":"Beginners often practise English by talking about everyday topics first.","zh":"初學者常先透過談論日常話題練習英語。"},{"en":"Everyday topics help conversation feel natural because everyone has experience with them.","zh":"日常話題令對話感覺自然，因為每個人都有相關經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to simple, common subjects people discuss regularly.","zh":"這個短語指人們經常討論的簡單常見主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a higher percentage of","meaning":"較高比例的……","examples":[{"en":"A higher percentage of girls in the classroom may lower disruption.","zh":"課室中較高比例的女生可能減少課堂干擾。"},{"en":"A higher percentage of a group means a larger proportion of that group in the total number.","zh":"higher percentage of 某群體，指該群體在總數中佔較大比例。"},{"en":"A higher percentage of students passed the exam after the school added revision sessions.","zh":"學校加入溫習課後，較高比例的學生通過考試。"},{"en":"Percentages help compare groups of different sizes fairly.","zh":"百分比幫助公平比較不同大小的群體。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a larger share, not necessarily a larger absolute number.","zh":"這個短語描述較大份額，而不一定是較大的絕對數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lower disruption","meaning":"減少課堂干擾","examples":[{"en":"A higher percentage of girls may lower disruption in class.","zh":"較高比例的女生可能減少課堂干擾。"},{"en":"To lower disruption means to reduce interruptions, noise, or behaviour that stops learning.","zh":"lower disruption 指減少打斷、嘈音或阻礙學習的行為。"},{"en":"Clear classroom rules can lower disruption during group work.","zh":"清晰課室規則可以減少小組活動中的干擾。"},{"en":"Less disruption helps students hear instructions and stay focused.","zh":"較少干擾幫助學生聽到指示並保持專注。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a learning environment calmer and more orderly.","zh":"這個短語描述令學習環境更安靜、更有秩序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"create a better relationship between","meaning":"在……之間建立更好關係","examples":[{"en":"A balanced classroom may create a better relationship between students and teachers.","zh":"平衡的課室可能在學生與老師之間建立更好關係。"},{"en":"To create a better relationship between two groups means to help them trust and work with each other more successfully.","zh":"create a better relationship between 兩個群體，指幫助他們更成功地互相信任和合作。"},{"en":"Regular parent meetings can create a better relationship between families and schools.","zh":"定期家長會可以在家庭與學校之間建立更好關係。"},{"en":"Better relationships reduce misunderstanding and make problems easier to solve.","zh":"更好關係減少誤解，並令問題較容易解決。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improving connection and cooperation between groups.","zh":"這個短語描述改善群體之間的連繫和合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the best type of schooling","meaning":"最合適的教育模式","examples":[{"en":"The best type of schooling depends on the individual child.","zh":"最合適的教育模式取決於個別孩子。"},{"en":"The best type of schooling means the school arrangement that suits a child most effectively.","zh":"best type of schooling 指最有效配合孩子的學校安排。"},{"en":"For one child, the best type of schooling may be a small school with close teacher support.","zh":"對一個孩子而言，最合適的教育模式可能是有密切教師支援的小學校。"},{"en":"For another child, a larger mixed school may provide more activities and friendships.","zh":"對另一個孩子而言，較大的男女混合學校可能提供更多活動和友誼。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that education choices should match personal needs.","zh":"這個短語顯示教育選擇應配合個人需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"depend on","meaning":"取決於","examples":[{"en":"The choice depends on the child and the learning environment.","zh":"選擇取決於孩子和學習環境。"},{"en":"Depend on means be decided or affected by something else.","zh":"depend on 指由另一事物決定或受其影響。"},{"en":"A student’s revision plan depends on how much time she has before the exam.","zh":"學生的溫習計劃取決於考試前還有多少時間。"},{"en":"The best answer often depends on the situation, not a single rule.","zh":"最佳答案常取決於情況，而不是單一規則。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one factor controls or influences another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個因素控制或影響另一個因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the individual child","meaning":"個別孩子","examples":[{"en":"Parents should consider the needs of the individual child.","zh":"家長應考慮個別孩子的需要。"},{"en":"The individual child means one particular child, with his or her own needs and personality.","zh":"individual child 指一個特定孩子，帶有自己的需要和性格。"},{"en":"A quiet child and an energetic child may need different classroom environments.","zh":"安靜孩子和精力充沛孩子可能需要不同課室環境。"},{"en":"Looking at the individual child prevents parents from choosing only by school reputation.","zh":"觀察個別孩子可以避免家長只按學校名聲選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses personal differences among children.","zh":"這個短語強調孩子之間的個人差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the environment in which","meaning":"……所處的環境","examples":[{"en":"The best school depends on the environment in which the child thrives.","zh":"最好的學校取決於孩子能在其中茁壯成長的環境。"},{"en":"The environment in which something happens means the setting or conditions where it takes place.","zh":"environment in which 某事發生，指它發生的場景或條件。"},{"en":"A student may learn best in an environment in which mistakes are treated as part of learning.","zh":"學生可能在一個把錯誤視為學習一部分的環境中學得最好。"},{"en":"The right environment can change how confident and motivated a child feels.","zh":"合適環境可以改變孩子感到多有信心和動力。"},{"en":"The phrase links a result to the conditions surrounding it.","zh":"這個短語把結果與周圍條件連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"thrive","meaning":"茁壯成長","examples":[{"en":"Children learn best in an environment where they can thrive.","zh":"孩子在能讓他們茁壯成長的環境中學得最好。"},{"en":"To thrive means to grow, develop, or succeed strongly.","zh":"thrive 指強健地成長、發展或成功。"},{"en":"A student may thrive when teachers notice her strengths and give useful feedback.","zh":"當老師注意到學生優點並給予有用回饋，她可能茁壯成長。"},{"en":"People thrive in places where they feel safe, challenged, and supported.","zh":"人們在感到安全、有挑戰和有支援的地方茁壯成長。"},{"en":"The word describes healthy and successful development.","zh":"這個詞描述健康而成功的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"parents are recommended to","meaning":"建議家長……","examples":[{"en":"Parents are recommended to seek advice before choosing a school.","zh":"建議家長在選擇學校前尋求意見。"},{"en":"Parents are recommended to do something means they are advised to do it.","zh":"parents are recommended to do something 指有人建議家長做某事。"},{"en":"Parents are recommended to read school reports before applying.","zh":"建議家長在申請前閱讀學校報告。"},{"en":"Recommendations guide decisions, but parents still need to judge their own child’s needs.","zh":"建議能引導決定，但家長仍需判斷自己孩子的需要。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces advice given to parents.","zh":"這個短語引出給家長的建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"seek advice","meaning":"尋求意見","examples":[{"en":"Parents should seek advice before making a school choice.","zh":"家長作出學校選擇前應尋求意見。"},{"en":"To seek advice means to ask someone knowledgeable for guidance.","zh":"seek advice 指向有知識的人尋求指引。"},{"en":"A student may seek advice from a teacher before choosing elective subjects.","zh":"學生選擇選修科目前，可能向老師尋求意見。"},{"en":"Seeking advice can prevent rushed decisions and reveal options people had not considered.","zh":"尋求意見可以避免倉促決定，並揭示人們未考慮過的選項。"},{"en":"The phrase describes asking for help before deciding.","zh":"這個短語描述在決定前尋求幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"do their research","meaning":"做資料搜集","examples":[{"en":"Parents should do their research before making a decision.","zh":"家長作決定前應做資料搜集。"},{"en":"To do their research means to collect information carefully before choosing or judging.","zh":"do their research 指在選擇或判斷前仔細收集資料。"},{"en":"A family should do their research before signing a long mobile phone contract.","zh":"家庭簽長期手機合約前應做資料搜集。"},{"en":"Research helps people avoid choices based only on advertising or rumours.","zh":"資料搜集幫助人避免只基於廣告或謠言作選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful information-gathering before action.","zh":"這個短語描述行動前仔細收集資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"all-important decision","meaning":"至關重要的決定","examples":[{"en":"Choosing a school is an all-important decision.","zh":"選擇學校是一個至關重要的決定。"},{"en":"An all-important decision is a decision that is extremely important and may strongly affect the future.","zh":"all-important decision 是極其重要並可能強烈影響未來的決定。"},{"en":"Choosing a university course can be an all-important decision for a teenager.","zh":"選擇大學課程可以是青少年的至關重要決定。"},{"en":"Important decisions deserve time, evidence, and honest discussion.","zh":"重要決定值得花時間、證據和真誠討論。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that a choice matters greatly.","zh":"這個短語強調某選擇非常重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"考生應為每題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choose the correct letter means select the option marked by the right letter, such as A, B, C, or D.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇以正確字母標示的選項，例如 A、B、C 或 D。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students choose the correct letter after matching the option with evidence.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生把選項與證據配對後選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choosing too quickly can lead to mistakes if two options look similar.","zh":"如果兩個選項看起來相似，太快選擇可能導致錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common multiple-choice instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見選擇題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"write your answers in boxes","meaning":"在方格內寫下答案","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write their answers in boxes on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生在答題紙的方格內寫下答案。"},{"en":"Write your answers in boxes means put each answer in the numbered spaces provided.","zh":"write your answers in boxes 指把每個答案寫在提供的編號空格中。"},{"en":"Students must write answers clearly in boxes so markers can read them.","zh":"學生必須在方格內清楚寫下答案，讓評卷員能閱讀。"},{"en":"Writing the right answer in the wrong box can still cause a lost mark.","zh":"把正確答案寫在錯誤方格內仍可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where exam answers should be placed.","zh":"這個短語描述考試答案應放在哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in single-sex classes","meaning":"在單性別課堂中","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what happens in single-sex classes.","zh":"題目問在單性別課堂中會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"In single-sex classes means inside classes made up only of boys or only of girls.","zh":"in single-sex classes 指在只由男生或只由女生組成的課堂中。"},{"en":"In single-sex classes, students may feel less worried about gender-based judgement.","zh":"在單性別課堂中，學生可能較少擔心基於性別的評價。"},{"en":"Classroom effects may differ depending on the teacher, school culture, and students themselves.","zh":"課室效果可能視乎老師、學校文化和學生本身而不同。"},{"en":"The phrase locates the discussion within one-gender classrooms.","zh":"這個短語把討論定位在單一性別課室內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a wider variety of teaching styles","meaning":"更多樣化的教學方式","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to a wider variety of teaching styles.","zh":"該選項提及更多樣化的教學方式。"},{"en":"A wider variety of teaching styles means more different ways of teaching are used.","zh":"wider variety of teaching styles 指使用更多不同教學方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a wider variety of teaching styles by mixing discussion, diagrams, games, and practice.","zh":"老師可以混合討論、圖表、遊戲和練習，使用更多樣化的教學方式。"},{"en":"More teaching styles can help different learners find a method that works for them.","zh":"更多教學方式可以幫助不同學習者找到適合自己的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broader choice in teaching methods.","zh":"這個短語描述教學方法上更廣泛的選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a coeducational setting","meaning":"男女同校環境","examples":[{"en":"The comparison is made with a coeducational setting.","zh":"這個比較是與男女同校環境作出。"},{"en":"A coeducational setting is an environment where boys and girls learn together.","zh":"coeducational setting 是男生和女生一起學習的環境。"},{"en":"A coeducational setting may help students practise everyday interaction with the opposite gender.","zh":"男女同校環境可以幫助學生練習與異性的日常互動。"},{"en":"It may also create pressure if students worry about how they look or behave.","zh":"如果學生擔心自己的外表或行為，它也可能造成壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a mixed-gender educational environment.","zh":"這個短語描述男女混合的教育環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"due to","meaning":"由於","examples":[{"en":"Some children may thrive due to a more comfortable environment.","zh":"有些孩子可能由於更舒適的環境而茁壯成長。"},{"en":"Due to means because of.","zh":"due to 指因為。"},{"en":"A student may miss class due to illness.","zh":"學生可能由於生病而缺課。"},{"en":"The phrase links a result to its cause.","zh":"這個短語把結果與原因連起來。"},{"en":"It is often used in formal writing to explain why something happened.","zh":"它常用於正式寫作中解釋某事為何發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a more comfortable environment","meaning":"更舒適的環境","examples":[{"en":"Single-sex classes may provide a more comfortable environment.","zh":"單性別課堂可能提供更舒適的環境。"},{"en":"A more comfortable environment is a setting where people feel safer, less judged, and more willing to participate.","zh":"more comfortable environment 是令人感到更安全、較少被評價和更願意參與的環境。"},{"en":"A quiet study room can provide a more comfortable environment for students who need concentration.","zh":"安靜溫習室可以為需要集中精神的學生提供更舒適的環境。"},{"en":"Comfort can improve learning because students spend less energy worrying about others.","zh":"舒適感可以改善學習，因為學生花較少精力擔心別人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an environment that reduces stress.","zh":"這個短語描述減少壓力的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"get a more rounded picture of","meaning":"對……有更全面的了解","examples":[{"en":"Coeducational schools may help students get a more rounded picture of others.","zh":"男女同校學校可能幫助學生對他人有更全面的了解。"},{"en":"To get a more rounded picture of something means to understand it in a broader and more balanced way.","zh":"get a more rounded picture of 某事，指以更廣泛、更平衡的方式理解它。"},{"en":"Students get a more rounded picture of a career when they talk to workers, not just read brochures.","zh":"當學生與從業員交談，而不只是閱讀小冊子，他們會對某職業有更全面的了解。"},{"en":"Meeting different people can reduce narrow assumptions and build fuller understanding.","zh":"接觸不同的人可以減少狹窄假設並建立更完整理解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gaining a less limited view.","zh":"這個短語描述獲得較不局限的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"discourage someone from doing something","meaning":"阻止某人做某事","examples":[{"en":"Social pressure may discourage males from studying certain subjects.","zh":"社交壓力可能阻止男生修讀某些科目。"},{"en":"To discourage someone from doing something means to make them less willing to do it.","zh":"discourage someone from doing something 指令某人較不願意做某事。"},{"en":"Harsh comments can discourage students from speaking English in class.","zh":"刻薄評論可以阻止學生在課堂上說英語。"},{"en":"Fear of being laughed at may discourage children from trying new activities.","zh":"害怕被取笑可能阻止孩子嘗試新活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reducing someone’s motivation or confidence to act.","zh":"這個短語描述降低某人的行動動機或信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"fall in popularity","meaning":"受歡迎程度下降","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that coeducational schools are falling in popularity.","zh":"該選項暗示男女同校學校受歡迎程度下降。"},{"en":"To fall in popularity means to become less liked, chosen, or supported.","zh":"fall in popularity 指變得較少被喜歡、選擇或支持。"},{"en":"A school club may fall in popularity if meetings are boring and badly organised.","zh":"如果會議沉悶且組織差，學會受歡迎程度可能下降。"},{"en":"Falling popularity can lead to fewer applications, members, or customers.","zh":"受歡迎程度下降可以導致申請者、成員或顧客減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a decline in public preference.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾偏好的下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"extracurricular teams and groups","meaning":"課外團隊和小組","examples":[{"en":"Some students are involved in extracurricular teams and groups.","zh":"有些學生參與課外團隊和小組。"},{"en":"Extracurricular teams and groups are clubs, sports teams, committees, or societies outside regular lessons.","zh":"extracurricular teams and groups 是常規課堂以外的學會、運動隊、委員會或社團。"},{"en":"A student may join extracurricular teams and groups to practise leadership and teamwork.","zh":"學生可能加入課外團隊和小組，以練習領導能力和團隊合作。"},{"en":"These groups help students build skills and friendships beyond academic classes.","zh":"這些小組幫助學生在學術課堂以外建立技能和友誼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised school activities outside the normal timetable.","zh":"這個短語描述正常時間表以外的有組織學校活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be offered the option of","meaning":"獲提供……的選擇","examples":[{"en":"Parents must be offered the option of coeducational classes.","zh":"家長必須獲提供男女同校課堂的選擇。"},{"en":"To be offered the option of something means to be given a real choice to select it.","zh":"be offered the option of 某事，指獲給予真正選擇它的機會。"},{"en":"Students may be offered the option of taking either art or music.","zh":"學生可能獲提供修讀美術或音樂的選擇。"},{"en":"Offering an option helps people feel that a decision is not being forced on them.","zh":"提供選擇可以令人覺得決定不是被強加於自己。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being given a choice.","zh":"這個短語描述獲給予選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"push someone to succeed in","meaning":"推動某人在……方面成功","examples":[{"en":"Some parents may push children to succeed in particular tasks.","zh":"有些家長可能推動孩子在特定任務方面成功。"},{"en":"To push someone to succeed in something means to strongly encourage or pressure them to do well.","zh":"push someone to succeed in 某事，指強烈鼓勵或施壓某人做好它。"},{"en":"A coach may push players to succeed in a tournament through extra training.","zh":"教練可能透過額外訓練，推動球員在比賽中成功。"},{"en":"Encouragement can help, but too much pressure may harm confidence.","zh":"鼓勵可以有幫助，但過多壓力可能傷害自信。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe support or pressure, depending on the context.","zh":"這個短語可描述支持或壓力，視乎語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"language tasks","meaning":"語言任務","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions boys succeeding in language tasks.","zh":"該選項提到男生在語言任務中成功。"},{"en":"Language tasks are activities that involve reading, writing, speaking, listening, or vocabulary use.","zh":"language tasks 是涉及閱讀、寫作、說話、聆聽或詞彙使用的活動。"},{"en":"A role-play is a language task because students must use words to communicate.","zh":"角色扮演是語言任務，因為學生必須用字詞溝通。"},{"en":"Good language tasks give learners a clear purpose for using English.","zh":"好語言任務給學習者清楚目的去使用英語。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning activities connected with language skills.","zh":"這個短語描述與語言技能相關的學習活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"confidence issues","meaning":"自信問題","examples":[{"en":"Some parents report that schooling can help with confidence issues.","zh":"有些家長表示學校教育可以幫助處理自信問題。"},{"en":"Confidence issues are problems involving low self-belief or fear of participating.","zh":"confidence issues 是涉及低自信或害怕參與的問題。"},{"en":"A student with confidence issues may know the answer but stay silent in class.","zh":"有自信問題的學生可能知道答案，但在課堂上保持沉默。"},{"en":"Supportive teachers and small successes can help reduce confidence issues over time.","zh":"支持學生的老師和小成功可以隨時間幫助減少自信問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes difficulties with self-confidence.","zh":"這個短語描述與自信有關的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be influential in","meaning":"對……有影響力","examples":[{"en":"Parents may be influential in decisions about school choice.","zh":"家長可能對學校選擇決定有影響力。"},{"en":"To be influential in something means to have power or importance in shaping it.","zh":"be influential in 某事，指在塑造該事上有力量或重要性。"},{"en":"Teachers can be influential in helping students choose suitable subjects.","zh":"老師可以對幫助學生選擇合適科目有影響力。"},{"en":"Influential people affect decisions because others listen to their views.","zh":"有影響力的人會影響決定，因為別人會聽取他們的看法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes having an effect on an outcome.","zh":"這個短語描述對結果有影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete the notes below","meaning":"完成以下筆記","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the notes below using words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成以下筆記。"},{"en":"Complete the notes below means fill in missing words in the notes under the question.","zh":"complete the notes below 指填寫題目下方筆記中的缺字。"},{"en":"Students complete notes by locating the correct part of the reading text.","zh":"學生透過定位閱讀文本中的正確部分來完成筆記。"},{"en":"Checking grammar around each blank can prevent word-form mistakes.","zh":"檢查每個空格周圍的文法可以避免詞形錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction in reading tests.","zh":"這個短語是閱讀測驗中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案應包含不多於兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must have two words or fewer.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案必須是兩個字詞或以下。"},{"en":"“Social pressure” has two words, so it fits this instruction.","zh":"“social pressure” 有兩個字，所以符合這個指示。"},{"en":"Writing three words can lose marks even if the meaning is close.","zh":"即使意思接近，寫三個字也可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit for exam answers.","zh":"這個短語為考試答案給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"intended to reduce","meaning":"旨在減少","examples":[{"en":"Coeducation was intended to reduce gender stereotypes.","zh":"男女同校教育旨在減少性別定型。"},{"en":"Intended to reduce means designed or meant to make something smaller or weaker.","zh":"intended to reduce 指被設計或打算用來令某事變少或變弱。"},{"en":"A school anti-bullying campaign is intended to reduce hurtful behaviour.","zh":"學校反欺凌運動旨在減少傷害性行為。"},{"en":"A policy may be intended to reduce a problem but still fail if poorly designed.","zh":"一項政策可能旨在減少問題，但如果設計差仍可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the purpose behind an action.","zh":"這個短語描述行動背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"traditionally male-dominated","meaning":"傳統上由男性主導的","examples":[{"en":"Some subjects have been traditionally male-dominated.","zh":"有些科目傳統上由男性主導。"},{"en":"Traditionally male-dominated means historically controlled, chosen, or occupied mostly by men.","zh":"traditionally male-dominated 指歷史上主要由男性控制、選擇或佔據。"},{"en":"Engineering has been traditionally male-dominated in many universities.","zh":"工程在許多大學中傳統上由男性主導。"},{"en":"Male-dominated subjects can discourage girls if schools do not actively challenge stereotypes.","zh":"如果學校不主動挑戰定型，男性主導的科目可以令女生卻步。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a long-standing gender imbalance.","zh":"這個短語描述長期存在的性別不平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"converse more easily with","meaning":"更容易與……交談","examples":[{"en":"Coeducation may help students converse more easily with the opposite gender.","zh":"男女同校教育可能幫助學生更容易與異性交談。"},{"en":"To converse more easily with someone means to talk with them more comfortably and naturally.","zh":"converse more easily with 某人，指更舒服、更自然地與對方交談。"},{"en":"Group projects can help shy students converse more easily with new classmates.","zh":"小組項目可以幫助害羞學生更容易與新同學交談。"},{"en":"Regular friendly contact can reduce nervousness in conversation.","zh":"定期友善接觸可以減少對話中的緊張。"},{"en":"The phrase describes smoother and more relaxed communication.","zh":"這個短語描述更順暢、更放鬆的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"do the following statements agree with","meaning":"以下陳述是否與……一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether the statements agree with the passage.","zh":"考生判斷這些陳述是否與文章一致。"},{"en":"Do the following statements agree with asks whether each statement matches the information in the text.","zh":"do the following statements agree with 是問每項陳述是否符合文本資料。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students should check the exact sentence before deciding if a statement agrees.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先檢查準確句子，再判斷陳述是否一致。"},{"en":"A statement may sound reasonable but still fail to agree with the passage.","zh":"陳述可能聽起來合理，但仍不一定與文章一致。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a True, False, or Not Given style task.","zh":"這個短語引出 True、False 或 Not Given 類型題目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與資料一致","examples":[{"en":"A true statement agrees with the information in the passage.","zh":"正確陳述與文章中的資料一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the information means match what the text says.","zh":"agree with the information 指符合文本所說內容。"},{"en":"An answer agrees with the information only if the passage supports it clearly.","zh":"只有文章清楚支持，答案才算與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should not use personal opinion when checking whether a statement agrees.","zh":"學生檢查陳述是否一致時，不應使用個人意見。"},{"en":"The phrase links a statement to textual evidence.","zh":"這個短語把陳述與文本證據連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章中的資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文本內容相反的東西。"},{"en":"If the passage says classes are optional, a statement saying they are compulsory contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說課堂是可選的，而陳述說它們是強制的，該陳述就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction is different from missing information because the text clearly goes against it.","zh":"矛盾不同於資料缺失，因為文本清楚與它相反。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a direct conflict with the passage.","zh":"這個短語描述與文章直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Readers choose this option when there is no information on this point.","zh":"當這一點沒有相關資料時，讀者選擇此選項。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文章沒有說明該陳述是真是假。"},{"en":"If a text mentions school size but not school fees, there is no information on the fees.","zh":"如果文本提到學校規模但沒有提到學費，就是沒有關於學費的資料。"},{"en":"Students should choose this only when the answer cannot be proven from the passage.","zh":"只有當答案不能從文章中證明時，學生才應選這項。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the logic behind a Not Given answer.","zh":"這個短語解釋 Not Given 答案背後的邏輯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"becoming more popular again","meaning":"再次變得更受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Single-sex schools are becoming more popular again.","zh":"單性別學校正再次變得更受歡迎。"},{"en":"Becoming more popular again means gaining support or attention after being less popular before.","zh":"becoming more popular again 指在以前較不受歡迎後重新獲得支持或注意。"},{"en":"Handwritten planners are becoming more popular again among students tired of phone reminders.","zh":"對電話提醒感到疲累的學生中，手寫計劃本正再次變得更受歡迎。"},{"en":"When something becomes popular again, people often compare the old reasons with the new ones.","zh":"當某事再次受歡迎，人們常比較舊原因和新原因。"},{"en":"The phrase describes renewed public interest.","zh":"這個短語描述重新出現的公眾興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"learn as well as","meaning":"學得和……一樣好","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether girls learn as well as boys through speaking.","zh":"該陳述問女生是否透過說話學得和男生一樣好。"},{"en":"To learn as well as someone else means to learn equally successfully.","zh":"learn as well as 某人，指學得同樣成功。"},{"en":"A quiet student may learn as well as a talkative student, but in a different way.","zh":"安靜學生可能學得和健談學生一樣好，只是方式不同。"},{"en":"Comparing whether one group learns as well as another requires careful evidence.","zh":"比較一個群體是否學得和另一群體一樣好，需要仔細證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes equal learning effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語描述相同的學習成效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"through speaking","meaning":"透過說話","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to learning through speaking.","zh":"題目提到透過說話學習。"},{"en":"Through speaking means by using spoken language to practise, explain, or remember ideas.","zh":"through speaking 指透過使用口語來練習、解釋或記住想法。"},{"en":"Students may learn vocabulary through speaking when they use new words in conversation.","zh":"當學生在對話中使用新字詞，他們可能透過說話學習詞彙。"},{"en":"Speaking can strengthen learning because it forces students to organise thoughts quickly.","zh":"說話可以加強學習，因為它迫使學生快速組織想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning by verbal expression.","zh":"這個短語描述透過口頭表達學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be preferred socially","meaning":"在社交方面較受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether coeducational schools are preferred socially.","zh":"該陳述問男女同校學校是否在社交方面較受歡迎。"},{"en":"To be preferred socially means to be favoured because of social benefits or social expectations.","zh":"be preferred socially 指因社交好處或社會期望而較受偏好。"},{"en":"Some parents may prefer mixed schools socially because children meet boys and girls every day.","zh":"有些家長可能在社交方面較喜歡混合學校，因為孩子每天接觸男生和女生。"},{"en":"A school type can be preferred socially even if academic evidence is mixed.","zh":"即使學術證據有混合結果，一種學校類型仍可能在社交方面較受歡迎。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preference based on social life rather than only grades.","zh":"這個短語描述基於社交生活而不只是成績的偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the majority of","meaning":"大多數……","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to the majority of equal opportunity activists.","zh":"該陳述提到大多數平等機會倡議者。"},{"en":"The majority of a group means more than half of that group.","zh":"majority of 某群體，指該群體中超過一半。"},{"en":"The majority of students chose the earlier exam date.","zh":"大多數學生選擇較早的考試日期。"},{"en":"If the majority supports a plan, the school may find it easier to adopt.","zh":"如果大多數人支持某計劃，學校可能較容易採用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the larger part of a group.","zh":"這個短語描述群體中的較大部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"equal opportunity activists","meaning":"平等機會倡議者","examples":[{"en":"Equal opportunity activists may be concerned about gender separation.","zh":"平等機會倡議者可能關注性別分隔。"},{"en":"Equal opportunity activists are people who campaign for fair access and treatment for different groups.","zh":"equal opportunity activists 是為不同群體爭取公平機會和待遇的人。"},{"en":"Equal opportunity activists may challenge hiring rules that favour one gender.","zh":"平等機會倡議者可能挑戰偏袒某一性別的招聘規則。"},{"en":"They often focus on whether everyone has a fair chance to succeed.","zh":"他們常關注每個人是否有公平成功機會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes people who work for fairness and inclusion.","zh":"這個短語描述為公平和共融努力的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"forcing gender separation on","meaning":"強行把性別分隔加諸於……","examples":[{"en":"The statement discusses forcing gender separation on children.","zh":"該陳述討論強行把性別分隔加諸於孩子。"},{"en":"Forcing gender separation on someone means making them separate by gender without real choice.","zh":"forcing gender separation on 某人，指在沒有真正選擇下按性別分開他們。"},{"en":"A school may be criticised for forcing gender separation on students during every subject.","zh":"如果學校每個科目都強行把性別分隔加諸於學生，可能受到批評。"},{"en":"Forced separation can feel unfair when it ignores students’ and parents’ preferences.","zh":"當強制分隔忽視學生和家長偏好，它可以令人覺得不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gender separation as something imposed rather than chosen.","zh":"這個短語把性別分隔描述為被強加，而不是被選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"unethical","meaning":"不合倫理的","examples":[{"en":"Some critics may argue that forced gender separation is unethical.","zh":"有些批評者可能認為強制性別分隔是不合倫理的。"},{"en":"Unethical means morally wrong or unfair according to accepted standards of right behaviour.","zh":"unethical 指根據公認正確行為標準，在道德上錯誤或不公平。"},{"en":"It is unethical for a teacher to share a student’s private information without permission.","zh":"老師未經許可分享學生私人資料是不合倫理的。"},{"en":"A practice may be legal but still unethical if it treats people unfairly.","zh":"一種做法可能合法，但如果待人不公平，仍可能不合倫理。"},{"en":"The word describes behaviour that violates moral principles.","zh":"這個詞描述違反道德原則的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 60 - CO- EDUCATIONAL VERSUS SINGLE SEX CLASSROOMS.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 61":[{"front":"constellations","meaning":"星座","examples":[{"en":"Constellations are groups of stars that appear to form patterns in the sky.","zh":"星座是一組組看起來在天空中形成圖案的星星。"},{"en":"Constellations are named star groupings that people use to recognise parts of the night sky.","zh":"星座是有名稱的星星組合，人們用來辨認夜空的不同部分。"},{"en":"A child may learn constellations by looking for familiar shapes such as a hunter, bear, or horse.","zh":"小孩可能透過尋找獵人、熊或馬等熟悉形狀來學習星座。"},{"en":"Because constellations divide the sky into recognisable areas, they help people talk about star positions.","zh":"因為星座把天空分成可辨認的區域，它們幫助人們談論星星位置。"},{"en":"This word refers to star patterns as seen from Earth, not stars that are necessarily close together in space.","zh":"這個詞指從地球看見的星星圖案，而不是一定在太空中彼此接近的星星。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a group of stars","meaning":"一組星星","examples":[{"en":"A constellation is a group of stars viewed collectively.","zh":"星座是一組被整體觀看的星星。"},{"en":"A group of stars means several stars considered together as one set.","zh":"一組星星，是指幾顆星被一起視為一個組合。"},{"en":"Students may point to a group of stars and ask whether it has a name.","zh":"學生可能指着一組星星，問它是否有名稱。"},{"en":"When stars are seen as a group, people can connect them into a pattern.","zh":"當星星被視為一組，人們就可以把它們連成圖案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes several stars being treated as one visual unit.","zh":"這個短語描述幾顆星被當作一個視覺單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"viewed collectively","meaning":"被整體觀看；合起來看","examples":[{"en":"Stars in a constellation are viewed collectively as a group.","zh":"星座中的星星被整體觀看為一組。"},{"en":"Viewed collectively means seen or considered together rather than separately.","zh":"被整體觀看，是指一起觀看或考慮，而不是分開看。"},{"en":"A class’s exam results may be viewed collectively to understand overall performance.","zh":"全班考試成績可以被整體觀看，以了解整體表現。"},{"en":"When stars are viewed collectively, a pattern may appear even if each star is far apart.","zh":"當星星被合起來看，即使每顆星相距很遠，也可能出現圖案。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show that the group is created by human observation.","zh":"這個短語幫助說明該組合是由人類觀察形成的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"appear to have","meaning":"看起來有……","examples":[{"en":"The stars appear to have physical proximity in the sky.","zh":"這些星星看起來在天空中位置接近。"},{"en":"Appear to have means seem to possess something, even if the reality may be different.","zh":"看起來有某事，是指似乎擁有某特徵，即使現實可能不同。"},{"en":"Two buildings may appear to have the same height from far away.","zh":"從遠處看，兩座建築物可能看起來有相同高度。"},{"en":"Stars may appear close together because of our viewpoint from Earth.","zh":"星星可能因我們從地球觀看的角度而看起來接近。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that what we see may not match the true physical situation.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，所見未必等於真實物理情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"physical proximity","meaning":"位置接近","examples":[{"en":"Stars in a constellation appear to have physical proximity.","zh":"星座中的星星看起來位置接近。"},{"en":"Physical proximity means closeness in actual physical position.","zh":"位置接近，是指在實際物理位置上彼此靠近。"},{"en":"Two students sitting at the same desk have physical proximity in the classroom.","zh":"兩名坐在同一張桌的學生，在課室中位置接近。"},{"en":"In astronomy, apparent closeness does not always mean real physical proximity.","zh":"在天文學中，看起來接近不一定代表真正位置接近。"},{"en":"This phrase describes real nearness, not just visual closeness.","zh":"這個短語描述真實接近，而不只是視覺上接近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the sky","meaning":"在天空中","examples":[{"en":"Constellations appear as patterns in the sky.","zh":"星座在天空中呈現為圖案。"},{"en":"In the sky means in the visible space above the Earth.","zh":"在天空中，是指在地球上方可見的空間中。"},{"en":"Children may see bright stars in the sky on a clear night.","zh":"孩子可能在晴朗夜晚看見天空中的明亮星星。"},{"en":"Clouds, light pollution, and weather can affect what people see in the sky.","zh":"雲、光污染和天氣都會影響人們在天空中看見甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the place where stars, planets, and clouds appear to viewers.","zh":"這個短語描述星星、行星和雲對觀察者而言出現的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"constellation boundaries","meaning":"星座邊界","examples":[{"en":"Constellation boundaries were formalised in 1930.","zh":"星座邊界於 1930 年正式確立。"},{"en":"Constellation boundaries are official lines that divide one constellation from another.","zh":"星座邊界是把一個星座與另一個星座分開的官方界線。"},{"en":"A map has boundaries between districts so people know which area is which.","zh":"地圖有地區邊界，讓人知道哪個範圍是哪一區。"},{"en":"Formal boundaries help astronomers identify exactly which constellation a star belongs to.","zh":"正式邊界幫助天文學家準確辨認某顆星屬於哪個星座。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the official edges of constellation areas.","zh":"這個短語描述星座區域的官方邊緣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"definitions as used today","meaning":"現今使用的定義","examples":[{"en":"The definitions as used today were formalised by the IAU.","zh":"現今使用的定義由國際天文聯會正式確立。"},{"en":"Definitions as used today are the meanings or standards currently accepted.","zh":"現今使用的定義，是目前被接受的意思或標準。"},{"en":"A dictionary may explain the definition of a word as used today, not as it was used centuries ago.","zh":"字典可能解釋一個詞現今使用的定義，而不是幾百年前的用法。"},{"en":"Current definitions help people use the same terms consistently.","zh":"現行定義幫助人們一致地使用相同術語。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts modern usage with older or informal usage.","zh":"這個短語把現代用法與較舊或非正式用法作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Western culture","meaning":"西方文化","examples":[{"en":"Modern constellation definitions are used in Western culture.","zh":"現代星座定義在西方文化中使用。"},{"en":"Western culture refers to traditions, ideas, and systems connected with Europe and societies influenced by it.","zh":"西方文化指與歐洲及受其影響社會有關的傳統、想法和制度。"},{"en":"In Western culture, zodiac signs are often used in magazines and casual conversations.","zh":"在西方文化中，黃道星座常出現在雜誌和日常談話中。"},{"en":"Cultural background can affect how people name and interpret stars.","zh":"文化背景會影響人們如何命名和詮釋星星。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a cultural context, not a scientific rule by itself.","zh":"這個短語描述文化語境，而本身不是科學規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as defined by","meaning":"由……界定","examples":[{"en":"The constellations were defined by the International Astronomical Union.","zh":"這些星座由國際天文聯會界定。"},{"en":"As defined by someone means according to the definition given by that person or organisation.","zh":"由某人界定，是指根據該人或機構給出的定義。"},{"en":"A school rule, as defined by the principal, may apply to all students.","zh":"由校長界定的校規，可能適用於所有學生。"},{"en":"When an official body defines a term, people can use it more consistently.","zh":"當官方機構界定術語，人們可以更一致地使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the authority behind a definition.","zh":"這個短語指出定義背後的權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"International Astronomical Union","meaning":"國際天文聯會","examples":[{"en":"The International Astronomical Union recognises 88 official constellations.","zh":"國際天文聯會承認 88 個官方星座。"},{"en":"The International Astronomical Union is an organisation that sets international standards in astronomy.","zh":"國際天文聯會是一個制定國際天文標準的組織。"},{"en":"Students may read that constellation names are standardised by the International Astronomical Union.","zh":"學生可能讀到星座名稱由國際天文聯會標準化。"},{"en":"Such organisations reduce confusion by agreeing on official names and boundaries.","zh":"這類組織透過同意官方名稱和邊界來減少混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the international authority mentioned in the passage.","zh":"這個短語指篇章中提及的國際權威機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"formalised in","meaning":"於……正式確立","examples":[{"en":"Constellation boundaries were formalised in 1930.","zh":"星座邊界於 1930 年正式確立。"},{"en":"Formalised in a year means officially fixed or established in that year.","zh":"於某年正式確立，是指在該年份被官方固定或建立。"},{"en":"A school’s house system may be formalised in a certain year after being used informally before.","zh":"學校社制可能先非正式使用，然後於某年正式確立。"},{"en":"Once rules are formalised, people have a clearer standard to follow.","zh":"規則一旦正式確立，人們就有更清楚的標準可遵循。"},{"en":"This phrase connects official establishment with a time.","zh":"這個短語把官方確立與時間連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"official constellations","meaning":"官方星座","examples":[{"en":"There are 88 official constellations recognised by the IAU.","zh":"國際天文聯會承認 88 個官方星座。"},{"en":"Official constellations are constellations formally accepted by an astronomical authority.","zh":"官方星座是由天文權威正式接受的星座。"},{"en":"A star pattern may be famous without being one of the official constellations.","zh":"一個星體圖案可以很有名，但未必是官方星座之一。"},{"en":"Official recognition helps astronomers use the same sky map.","zh":"官方承認幫助天文學家使用同一套星空地圖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accepted constellation divisions, not every popular star pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述被接受的星座劃分，而不是每個流行星群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"recognised by","meaning":"獲……承認","examples":[{"en":"There are 88 official constellations recognised by the IAU.","zh":"有 88 個官方星座獲國際天文聯會承認。"},{"en":"Recognised by an organisation means accepted or approved by it.","zh":"獲某機構承認，是指被該機構接受或批准。"},{"en":"A qualification recognised by universities is more useful for students applying abroad.","zh":"獲大學承認的資格，對申請海外升學的學生更有用。"},{"en":"Recognition gives a name or standard official status.","zh":"承認令名稱或標準具有官方地位。"},{"en":"This phrase shows who accepts something as valid.","zh":"這個短語顯示誰接受某事為有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"visible in","meaning":"在……可見","examples":[{"en":"Some constellations are visible in the Northern Hemisphere.","zh":"有些星座在北半球可見。"},{"en":"Visible in a place means able to be seen from that place.","zh":"在某地可見，是指可以從該地方看見。"},{"en":"Fireworks may be visible in several districts if they are high enough.","zh":"如果煙花升得夠高，可能在幾個地區可見。"},{"en":"Which constellations are visible depends on location, season, and sky conditions.","zh":"哪些星座可見取決於位置、季節和天空狀況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where something can be seen.","zh":"這個短語描述某物可從哪裡看見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Northern Hemisphere","meaning":"北半球","examples":[{"en":"The constellations visible in the Northern Hemisphere are based on ancient Greek constellations.","zh":"北半球可見的星座以古希臘星座為基礎。"},{"en":"The Northern Hemisphere is the half of Earth north of the equator.","zh":"北半球是地球赤道以北的一半。"},{"en":"Countries such as Greece, China, and the United States are in the Northern Hemisphere.","zh":"希臘、中國和美國等國家位於北半球。"},{"en":"Observers in the Northern Hemisphere see a different part of the sky from observers far south.","zh":"北半球觀察者看到的天空部分，與遙遠南方的觀察者不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a geographical half of Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述地球的地理半球。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"based on","meaning":"以……為基礎","examples":[{"en":"Northern constellations are based on those established by the ancient Greeks.","zh":"北方星座以古希臘人確立的星座為基礎。"},{"en":"Based on something means built from or influenced by that earlier source.","zh":"以某事為基礎，是指由較早來源建立或受其影響。"},{"en":"A film may be based on a famous novel.","zh":"一部電影可能以著名小說為基礎。"},{"en":"When a system is based on older ideas, it may preserve old names and stories.","zh":"當一個系統以較舊想法為基礎，它可能保留舊名稱和故事。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the foundation of an idea or system.","zh":"這個短語顯示想法或系統的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"established by","meaning":"由……確立","examples":[{"en":"Many northern constellations were established by the ancient Greeks.","zh":"許多北方星座由古希臘人確立。"},{"en":"Established by someone means created, set up, or formally recognised by them.","zh":"由某人確立，是指由他們創造、設立或正式承認。"},{"en":"A school prize may be established by former students to support young writers.","zh":"學校獎項可能由舊生設立，以支持年輕作家。"},{"en":"Once a naming system is established, later users may continue to follow it.","zh":"命名系統一旦確立，後來使用者可能繼續沿用。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who created or fixed something.","zh":"這個短語指出誰創造或固定某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ancient Greeks","meaning":"古希臘人","examples":[{"en":"The ancient Greeks established many constellations in the Northern Hemisphere.","zh":"古希臘人確立了北半球許多星座。"},{"en":"Ancient Greeks were people of ancient Greece, whose culture influenced astronomy, philosophy, and art.","zh":"古希臘人是古代希臘的人，其文化影響天文學、哲學和藝術。"},{"en":"Students may learn about ancient Greeks when studying myths about gods and heroes.","zh":"學生研究神和英雄的神話時，可能會學到古希臘人。"},{"en":"Their star stories influenced later Western constellation names.","zh":"他們的星空故事影響了後來西方星座名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a historical civilisation, not modern Greek people specifically.","zh":"這個短語指歷史文明，而不是特指現代希臘人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"southern hemisphere","meaning":"南半球","examples":[{"en":"The constellations of the southern hemisphere were invisible to the Greeks.","zh":"南半球的星座對希臘人來說不可見。"},{"en":"The southern hemisphere is the half of Earth south of the equator.","zh":"南半球是地球赤道以南的一半。"},{"en":"Australia and much of South America are in the southern hemisphere.","zh":"澳洲和南美洲大部分地區位於南半球。"},{"en":"People in the southern hemisphere see some stars that northern observers cannot see.","zh":"南半球的人會看到一些北方觀察者看不到的星星。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the southern half of Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述地球南方的一半。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"invisible to","meaning":"對……來說不可見","examples":[{"en":"Southern constellations were invisible to the Greeks because of their location.","zh":"南方星座因地理位置而對希臘人不可見。"},{"en":"Invisible to someone means unable to be seen by that person.","zh":"對某人來說不可見，是指該人無法看見。"},{"en":"A small road sign may be invisible to drivers if it is hidden behind a tree.","zh":"如果小路牌被樹遮住，對司機來說可能不可見。"},{"en":"Stars can be invisible to people in one place because Earth blocks their view.","zh":"星星可能因地球阻擋視線，而對某地方的人不可見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that cannot be seen from a certain viewpoint.","zh":"這個短語描述某物從某個視角看不到。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"because of","meaning":"由於；因為","examples":[{"en":"The southern constellations were invisible to the Greeks because of their geographical location.","zh":"南方星座由於希臘人的地理位置而對他們不可見。"},{"en":"Because of means as a result of or due to something.","zh":"由於或因為，是指作為某事的結果。"},{"en":"The match was cancelled because of heavy rain.","zh":"比賽因大雨而取消。"},{"en":"A person’s location can determine which part of the sky they can see.","zh":"一個人的位置可以決定他能看見哪部分天空。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the reason for a situation.","zh":"這個短語引入某情況的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"geographical location","meaning":"地理位置","examples":[{"en":"The Greeks could not see southern constellations because of their geographical location.","zh":"希臘人因地理位置而看不到南方星座。"},{"en":"Geographical location means the place where someone or something is on Earth.","zh":"地理位置，是某人或某物在地球上的位置。"},{"en":"A shop’s geographical location affects how many customers can reach it.","zh":"商店的地理位置影響有多少顧客能到達。"},{"en":"Where people live affects the stars, weather, and natural features they can observe.","zh":"人住在哪裡，會影響他們能觀察到的星星、天氣和自然特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical position on Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述在地球上的實際位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"not defined until","meaning":"直到……才被界定","examples":[{"en":"The constellations of the southern hemisphere were not defined until the early modern era.","zh":"南半球星座直到近代早期才被界定。"},{"en":"Not defined until a time means only given a clear definition at that later time.","zh":"直到某時才被界定，是指到較後時間才被清楚定義。"},{"en":"A school club may not be officially defined until the principal approves its rules.","zh":"學校學會可能直到校長批准規則後才被正式界定。"},{"en":"If something is not defined, people may describe it differently.","zh":"如果某事沒有被界定，人們可能會以不同方式描述它。"},{"en":"This structure emphasises a delayed official definition.","zh":"這個結構強調官方定義較遲出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"early modern era","meaning":"近代早期","examples":[{"en":"Southern constellations were not defined until the early modern era.","zh":"南方星座直到近代早期才被界定。"},{"en":"The early modern era is a historical period after the Middle Ages and before the modern age.","zh":"近代早期是中世紀之後、現代之前的歷史時期。"},{"en":"Students may study voyages of exploration when learning about the early modern era.","zh":"學生學習近代早期時，可能研究探索航海。"},{"en":"New travel and observation helped people define more parts of the southern sky.","zh":"新的旅行和觀察幫助人們界定更多南方天空區域。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a historical period of expanding exploration and knowledge.","zh":"這個短語指探索和知識擴展的歷史時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"arguably","meaning":"可以說","examples":[{"en":"Arguably, the zodiac constellations are the most culturally significant.","zh":"可以說，黃道星座是最具文化重要性的星座。"},{"en":"Arguably means it can be reasonably argued, though not everyone may agree.","zh":"可以說，是指這個說法有合理理據，但不一定人人同意。"},{"en":"Arguably, English is useful because it is used in many international settings.","zh":"可以說，英語很有用，因為它在許多國際場合被使用。"},{"en":"This word softens a claim by showing it is open to debate.","zh":"這個詞透過顯示事情仍可討論，令說法較溫和。"},{"en":"It is useful when making a strong but not absolute judgement.","zh":"它適合提出強但非絕對的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the twelve constellations","meaning":"十二個星座","examples":[{"en":"The twelve constellations are used to represent the signs of the zodiac.","zh":"十二個星座被用來代表黃道十二宮。"},{"en":"The twelve constellations are the star groups linked with the traditional zodiac signs.","zh":"十二個星座，是與傳統黃道星座相連的星群。"},{"en":"A student may know the twelve constellations from horoscopes before learning astronomy.","zh":"學生可能先從星座運程認識十二個星座，然後才學天文學。"},{"en":"These constellations became culturally important because people connected them with birth signs.","zh":"這些星座因人們把它們與出生星座連結而變得具有文化重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the zodiac star groups in the passage.","zh":"這個短語指篇章中的黃道星群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"through which","meaning":"穿過……的","examples":[{"en":"The sun passes through the twelve zodiac constellations.","zh":"太陽穿過十二個黃道星座。"},{"en":"Through which means through the things just mentioned.","zh":"through which 是指穿過剛提到的那些事物。"},{"en":"A road through which buses pass every morning may become crowded.","zh":"每天早上有巴士穿過的道路可能變得擠迫。"},{"en":"In astronomy, this phrase can describe a path crossing a set of sky areas.","zh":"在天文學中，這個短語可以描述一條路徑穿過一組天空區域。"},{"en":"This phrase links a movement with the area it passes across.","zh":"這個短語把移動與其穿過的範圍連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the sun passes","meaning":"太陽經過","examples":[{"en":"The sun passes through twelve constellations linked to the zodiac.","zh":"太陽經過十二個與黃道相關的星座。"},{"en":"The sun passes means the sun appears to move across a particular part of the sky.","zh":"太陽經過，是指太陽看起來移過天空中的某一部分。"},{"en":"From Earth, the sun passes across the sky from morning to evening.","zh":"從地球看，太陽由早到晚經過天空。"},{"en":"The sun’s apparent path helped people connect constellations with calendars and seasons.","zh":"太陽的視覺路徑幫助人們把星座與曆法和季節聯繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes apparent movement as seen from Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述從地球看見的表觀移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"represent","meaning":"代表","examples":[{"en":"The twelve constellations are used to represent the signs of the zodiac.","zh":"十二個星座被用來代表黃道十二宮。"},{"en":"To represent something means to stand for it or be used as its symbol.","zh":"代表某事，是指象徵它或被用作它的標誌。"},{"en":"A school badge may represent the values of the school.","zh":"校徽可能代表學校的價值觀。"},{"en":"Symbols help people connect abstract ideas with visible images.","zh":"象徵幫助人們把抽象想法與可見圖像連接。"},{"en":"This word describes one thing standing in for another.","zh":"這個詞描述一件事物代替另一件事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"signs of the zodiac","meaning":"黃道十二宮","examples":[{"en":"The signs of the zodiac are linked to birth characteristics.","zh":"黃道十二宮與出生性格特徵相關。"},{"en":"Signs of the zodiac are the twelve astrological signs associated with dates of birth.","zh":"黃道十二宮是與出生日期相關的十二個占星星座。"},{"en":"People may ask for someone’s zodiac sign in casual conversation.","zh":"人們可能在日常談話中問某人的星座。"},{"en":"Zodiac signs became popular because they are connected with personality and fate in many cultures.","zh":"黃道星座變得流行，因為它們在許多文化中與性格和命運相連。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to astrological signs, not official astronomy alone.","zh":"這個短語指占星星座，而不只是官方天文學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"define birth characteristics","meaning":"界定出生性格特徵","examples":[{"en":"The zodiac signs are used to define birth characteristics.","zh":"黃道星座被用來界定出生性格特徵。"},{"en":"To define birth characteristics means to describe personality traits believed to be linked to birth signs.","zh":"界定出生性格特徵，是描述被認為與出生星座相關的個性特質。"},{"en":"A magazine may use zodiac signs to describe whether a person is confident or careful.","zh":"雜誌可能用黃道星座描述一個人是否自信或謹慎。"},{"en":"These descriptions can influence how people talk about personality.","zh":"這些描述會影響人們如何談論個性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a cultural or astrological interpretation of birth traits.","zh":"這個短語描述對出生特質的文化或占星詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"culturally significant","meaning":"具文化重要性的","examples":[{"en":"The zodiac constellations are culturally significant and well-known.","zh":"黃道星座具文化重要性且廣為人知。"},{"en":"Culturally significant means important within a society’s beliefs, stories, or traditions.","zh":"具文化重要性，是指在社會信念、故事或傳統中重要。"},{"en":"A festival can be culturally significant because families celebrate it every year.","zh":"節日可能具文化重要性，因為家庭每年都慶祝它。"},{"en":"Zodiac constellations matter culturally because people connect them with identity and personality.","zh":"黃道星座在文化上重要，因為人們把它們與身份和性格連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cultural importance, not only scientific importance.","zh":"這個短語描述文化重要性，而不只是科學重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"well-known","meaning":"廣為人知的","examples":[{"en":"The zodiac constellations are among the most well-known star groupings.","zh":"黃道星座是最廣為人知的星群之一。"},{"en":"Well-known means familiar to many people.","zh":"廣為人知的，是指為很多人熟悉。"},{"en":"A well-known teacher may be recognised by students across the whole school.","zh":"廣為人知的老師可能被全校學生認出。"},{"en":"Something becomes well-known when it appears often in books, media, and conversations.","zh":"某事經常出現在書籍、媒體和談話中，就會變得廣為人知。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wide public familiarity.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛的公眾熟悉度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cultural differences","meaning":"文化差異","examples":[{"en":"Cultural differences affect the interpretation of star constellations.","zh":"文化差異影響對星座的詮釋。"},{"en":"Cultural differences are differences in beliefs, traditions, and ways of understanding the world.","zh":"文化差異是信念、傳統和理解世界方式上的不同。"},{"en":"Cultural differences may affect how families celebrate the same holiday.","zh":"文化差異可能影響家庭如何慶祝同一個節日。"},{"en":"Different cultures may look at the same stars but give them different names and stories.","zh":"不同文化可能看見同一批星星，卻給它們不同名稱和故事。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why people may interpret the same thing differently.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何人們可能以不同方式詮釋同一事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"interpretation and definition","meaning":"詮釋和定義","examples":[{"en":"There are cultural differences in the interpretation and definition of constellations.","zh":"在星座的詮釋和定義方面存在文化差異。"},{"en":"Interpretation and definition mean how something is understood and how it is officially described.","zh":"詮釋和定義，是指某事如何被理解，以及如何被正式描述。"},{"en":"Different schools may vary in the interpretation and definition of good participation.","zh":"不同學校對良好參與的詮釋和定義可能不同。"},{"en":"If people define star groups differently, their sky maps may not match.","zh":"如果人們以不同方式定義星群，他們的星圖可能不一致。"},{"en":"This phrase combines meaning-making with formal description.","zh":"這個短語結合理解意義和正式描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"star constellations","meaning":"星座","examples":[{"en":"Different cultures interpret star constellations in different ways.","zh":"不同文化以不同方式詮釋星座。"},{"en":"Star constellations are patterns or groups of stars recognised by people.","zh":"星座是人們認出的星星圖案或組合。"},{"en":"A museum display may show how different cultures named the same star constellations.","zh":"博物館展覽可能展示不同文化如何命名同一批星座。"},{"en":"Cultural stories can shape how constellations are remembered.","zh":"文化故事可以塑造星座被記住的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to star patterns understood through astronomy and culture.","zh":"這個短語指透過天文和文化理解的星星圖案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mainly relate to","meaning":"主要與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Cultural differences mainly relate to zodiac interpretations.","zh":"文化差異主要與黃道星座詮釋有關。"},{"en":"Mainly relate to means are mostly connected with something.","zh":"主要與某事有關，是指大多與它相連。"},{"en":"A student’s poor sleep may mainly relate to late-night phone use.","zh":"學生睡眠差可能主要與深夜使用手機有關。"},{"en":"When differences mainly relate to one area, that area becomes the focus of discussion.","zh":"當差異主要與某範疇有關，該範疇就成為討論焦點。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the chief connection.","zh":"這個短語指出主要關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"zodiac interpretations","meaning":"對黃道星座的詮釋","examples":[{"en":"Different cultures have different zodiac interpretations.","zh":"不同文化對黃道星座有不同詮釋。"},{"en":"Zodiac interpretations are the meanings or personality ideas people connect with zodiac signs.","zh":"對黃道星座的詮釋，是人們與星座相連的意義或性格想法。"},{"en":"A newspaper horoscope gives one kind of zodiac interpretation for readers.","zh":"報紙星座運程為讀者提供一種黃道星座詮釋。"},{"en":"Interpretations differ because cultures attach different stories and values to the stars.","zh":"詮釋會不同，因為文化把不同故事和價值附加於星星。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to cultural readings of zodiac signs.","zh":"這個短語指對黃道星座的文化解讀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Chinese constellations","meaning":"中國星宿","examples":[{"en":"Chinese constellations differ from those in the Western world.","zh":"中國星宿與西方世界的星座不同。"},{"en":"Chinese constellations are star groupings used in the Chinese astronomical tradition.","zh":"中國星宿是中國天文傳統中使用的星星組合。"},{"en":"Students may learn about Chinese constellations when studying the 28 Xiu.","zh":"學生學習二十八宿時，可能認識中國星宿。"},{"en":"They differ because Chinese astronomy developed its own system and names.","zh":"它們不同，是因為中國天文學發展出自己的制度和名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to constellations in Chinese star-mapping tradition.","zh":"這個短語指中國星圖傳統中的星宿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"differ from","meaning":"與……不同","examples":[{"en":"Chinese constellations differ from those defined in the Western world.","zh":"中國星宿與西方世界所界定的星座不同。"},{"en":"To differ from something means to be different from it.","zh":"與某事不同，是指不一樣。"},{"en":"School rules in one country may differ from those in another.","zh":"一個國家的校規可能與另一個國家的校規不同。"},{"en":"Systems can differ when they develop separately over a long time.","zh":"當系統長時間分開發展，它們可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two things and shows they are not the same.","zh":"這個短語比較兩件事並顯示它們不一樣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the Western world","meaning":"西方世界","examples":[{"en":"Chinese constellations differ from those defined in the Western world.","zh":"中國星宿與西方世界所界定的星座不同。"},{"en":"The Western world refers to Europe and societies strongly influenced by European traditions.","zh":"西方世界指歐洲及深受歐洲傳統影響的社會。"},{"en":"Ideas about zodiac signs are common in parts of the Western world.","zh":"關於黃道星座的想法在西方世界部分地區很常見。"},{"en":"Comparing the Western world with other traditions helps reveal cultural differences.","zh":"把西方世界與其他傳統比較，有助揭示文化差異。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broad cultural and historical region.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛的文化和歷史區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ancient Chinese astronomy","meaning":"中國古代天文學","examples":[{"en":"Ancient Chinese astronomy developed independently.","zh":"中國古代天文學獨立發展。"},{"en":"Ancient Chinese astronomy is the early Chinese system of observing, naming, and interpreting the sky.","zh":"中國古代天文學是中國早期觀察、命名和詮釋天空的系統。"},{"en":"A history class may study ancient Chinese astronomy through calendars and star records.","zh":"歷史課可能透過曆法和星象記錄研究中國古代天文學。"},{"en":"Independent development can produce different names, divisions, and myths.","zh":"獨立發展可以產生不同名稱、劃分和神話。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to China’s historical astronomical tradition.","zh":"這個短語指中國的歷史天文傳統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"developed independently","meaning":"獨立發展","examples":[{"en":"Ancient Chinese astronomy developed independently from Western astronomy.","zh":"中國古代天文學獨立於西方天文學發展。"},{"en":"Developed independently means grew or formed separately, without depending on another system.","zh":"獨立發展，是指分開成長或形成，不依賴另一系統。"},{"en":"Two schools may develop independently and create different teaching methods.","zh":"兩間學校可能獨立發展，創造不同教學方法。"},{"en":"Independent development can explain why two systems do not match exactly.","zh":"獨立發展可以解釋為何兩套系統不完全吻合。"},{"en":"This phrase describes separate growth or formation.","zh":"這個短語描述分開成長或形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"include 28 Xiu","meaning":"包括二十八宿","examples":[{"en":"Chinese constellations include 28 Xiu, or mansions.","zh":"中國星宿包括二十八宿。"},{"en":"Include 28 Xiu means contain a system of twenty-eight traditional Chinese star divisions.","zh":"包括二十八宿，是指包含二十八個中國傳統星空劃分系統。"},{"en":"A textbook on Chinese astronomy may include 28 Xiu in a chapter on star mapping.","zh":"中國天文學教科書可能在星圖章節中包括二十八宿。"},{"en":"This system differs from the Western zodiac because it divides the sky in another way.","zh":"這套系統與西方黃道星座不同，因為它以另一方式劃分天空。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a key part of Chinese constellation tradition.","zh":"這個短語描述中國星宿傳統的重要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mansions","meaning":"宿；星宿","examples":[{"en":"The 28 Xiu are sometimes translated as mansions.","zh":"二十八宿有時被翻譯為 mansions。"},{"en":"Mansions here means traditional star divisions or lunar lodges, not large houses.","zh":"這裡的 mansions 指傳統星空分區或月宿，不是大型豪宅。"},{"en":"A student may misunderstand “mansions” if they think only of expensive homes.","zh":"如果學生只想到昂貴住宅，可能會誤解 mansions。"},{"en":"Context matters because the same English word can have a special astronomical meaning.","zh":"語境很重要，因為同一英文詞可以有特殊天文意思。"},{"en":"This word refers to sections of the sky in this passage.","zh":"這個詞在本文中指天空區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"instead of","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Chinese astronomy includes 28 Xiu instead of the 12 western zodiac counterparts.","zh":"中國天文學包括二十八宿，而不是十二個西方黃道星座對應物。"},{"en":"Instead of means in place of or rather than something else.","zh":"而不是，是指用某事取代另一事。"},{"en":"A student may drink water instead of soda to stay healthier.","zh":"學生可能喝水而不是汽水，以保持較健康。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a clear contrast between two choices or systems.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個選擇或系統之間的清楚對比。"},{"en":"It helps explain that one system uses a different structure from another.","zh":"它幫助解釋一個系統使用不同於另一系統的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"western zodiac counterparts","meaning":"西方黃道星座的對應物","examples":[{"en":"The 28 Xiu are different from the 12 western zodiac counterparts.","zh":"二十八宿與十二個西方黃道星座的對應物不同。"},{"en":"Western zodiac counterparts are the roughly corresponding zodiac signs in Western tradition.","zh":"西方黃道星座的對應物，是西方傳統中大致相應的黃道星座。"},{"en":"A Chinese term may have no exact Western counterpart if the systems developed differently.","zh":"如果系統發展不同，中國術語可能沒有準確西方對應物。"},{"en":"Counterparts help comparison, but they may not be identical.","zh":"對應物有助比較，但未必完全相同。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to similar items in the Western zodiac system.","zh":"這個短語指西方黃道系統中的相似項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Hindu/Vedic astronomy","meaning":"印度／吠陀天文學","examples":[{"en":"In Hindu/Vedic astronomy, constellations are known as rashis.","zh":"在印度／吠陀天文學中，星座被稱為 rashis。"},{"en":"Hindu/Vedic astronomy is an Indian astronomical tradition linked with Hindu and Vedic systems.","zh":"印度／吠陀天文學是與印度教和吠陀系統相關的印度天文傳統。"},{"en":"Students comparing star traditions may study Hindu/Vedic astronomy beside Chinese and Western astronomy.","zh":"比較星空傳統的學生，可能把印度／吠陀天文學與中國和西方天文學一同研究。"},{"en":"Different traditions use different names and divisions for the sky.","zh":"不同傳統使用不同名稱和方式劃分天空。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an Indian system of astronomical and astrological knowledge.","zh":"這個短語指印度的天文和占星知識系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"known as","meaning":"被稱為……","examples":[{"en":"In Hindu astronomy, constellations are known as rashis.","zh":"在印度天文學中，星座被稱為 rashis。"},{"en":"Known as means called by a particular name.","zh":"被稱為，是指以某個特定名稱稱呼。"},{"en":"Hong Kong is sometimes known as an international financial centre.","zh":"香港有時被稱為國際金融中心。"},{"en":"Names can differ across languages and cultures even when they describe similar ideas.","zh":"即使描述相似想法，名稱也會因語言和文化而不同。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what something is called.","zh":"這個短語引入某事物的名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"rashis","meaning":"印度黃道星座","examples":[{"en":"Rashis correspond directly to the twelve Western star signs.","zh":"印度黃道星座直接對應十二個西方星座。"},{"en":"Rashis are zodiac signs in Hindu or Vedic astronomy.","zh":"rashis 是印度或吠陀天文學中的黃道星座。"},{"en":"A student of Indian astrology may learn the twelve rashis before studying Nakshatras.","zh":"研究印度占星的學生可能先學十二個 rashis，再學納克沙特拉。"},{"en":"Rashis allow comparison with Western star signs because the two sets correspond directly.","zh":"rashis 可與西方星座比較，因為兩組直接對應。"},{"en":"This word refers to zodiac divisions in the Hindu/Vedic tradition.","zh":"這個詞指印度／吠陀傳統中的黃道劃分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"corresponding directly to","meaning":"直接對應……","examples":[{"en":"The 12 rashis correspond directly to the twelve Western star signs.","zh":"十二個 rashis 直接對應十二個西方星座。"},{"en":"Corresponding directly to something means matching it clearly and closely.","zh":"直接對應某物，是指與它清楚而緊密地相配。"},{"en":"A textbook answer key corresponds directly to the numbered questions.","zh":"教科書答案表直接對應編號題目。"},{"en":"Direct correspondence makes comparison easier because each item has a clear match.","zh":"直接對應令比較更容易，因為每一項都有清楚配對。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a one-to-one or close relationship.","zh":"這個短語描述一對一或緊密關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Western star signs","meaning":"西方星座","examples":[{"en":"The rashis correspond to the twelve Western star signs.","zh":"rashis 對應十二個西方星座。"},{"en":"Western star signs are the twelve zodiac signs commonly used in Western astrology.","zh":"西方星座是西方占星中常用的十二個黃道星座。"},{"en":"A person may know their Western star sign from their birthday.","zh":"一個人可能根據生日知道自己的西方星座。"},{"en":"Star signs are culturally familiar because they appear in horoscopes and casual talk.","zh":"星座在文化上很熟悉，因為它們出現在星座運程和日常談話中。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to zodiac signs in Western tradition.","zh":"這個短語指西方傳統中的黃道星座。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be acknowledged","meaning":"被承認；被認可","examples":[{"en":"Twelve rashis are acknowledged in Hindu/Vedic astronomy.","zh":"十二個 rashis 在印度／吠陀天文學中被承認。"},{"en":"To be acknowledged means to be recognised or accepted.","zh":"被承認，是指被認可或接受。"},{"en":"A student’s effort may be acknowledged by a teacher even if the final grade is not perfect.","zh":"即使最終成績不完美，老師也可能認可學生的努力。"},{"en":"When a system acknowledges certain categories, those categories become part of its structure.","zh":"當一個系統承認某些類別，那些類別就成為其結構一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official or accepted recognition.","zh":"這個短語描述官方或被接受的承認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"divided again into","meaning":"再被分為……","examples":[{"en":"The twelve rashis are divided again into 27 Nakshatras.","zh":"十二個 rashis 再被分為 27 個納克沙特拉。"},{"en":"Divided again into means separated further into smaller parts.","zh":"再被分為，是指進一步分成更小部分。"},{"en":"A school year may be divided into terms, and each term divided again into weeks.","zh":"一個學年可被分為學期，而每個學期再被分為星期。"},{"en":"Further division helps create a more detailed system.","zh":"進一步劃分有助建立更詳細的系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes breaking a category into smaller units.","zh":"這個短語描述把一個類別分成較小單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Nakshatras","meaning":"納克沙特拉；月宿","examples":[{"en":"Nakshatras are also known as lunar houses.","zh":"納克沙特拉也被稱為月宿。"},{"en":"Nakshatras are lunar divisions used in Hindu/Vedic astronomy.","zh":"納克沙特拉是印度／吠陀天文學中使用的月亮劃分。"},{"en":"A student studying Vedic astrology may learn the Nakshatras after the rashis.","zh":"研究吠陀占星的學生可能在學 rashis 後學納克沙特拉。"},{"en":"They add another layer of detail to the sky-mapping system.","zh":"它們為天空繪圖系統加入另一層細節。"},{"en":"This word refers to moon-related divisions in the Indian tradition.","zh":"這個詞指印度傳統中與月亮相關的劃分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lunar houses","meaning":"月宿","examples":[{"en":"The 27 Nakshatras are lunar houses.","zh":"二十七個納克沙特拉是月宿。"},{"en":"Lunar houses are divisions of the sky connected with the moon’s path.","zh":"月宿是與月亮路徑相關的天空劃分。"},{"en":"A calendar system may use lunar houses to organise observations of the night sky.","zh":"曆法系統可能使用月宿來整理夜空觀察。"},{"en":"They are called lunar because they relate to the moon.","zh":"它們被稱為 lunar，是因為與月亮有關。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moon-related sections of the heavens.","zh":"這個短語描述與月亮相關的天空區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"intricate mythology","meaning":"複雜精細的神話","examples":[{"en":"Many cultures have an intricate mythology behind the stars.","zh":"許多文化在星星背後都有複雜精細的神話。"},{"en":"Intricate mythology means complex and detailed stories about gods, heroes, or supernatural events.","zh":"複雜精細的神話，是關於神、英雄或超自然事件的複雜詳細故事。"},{"en":"A culture may have intricate mythology explaining why certain stars form a hunter’s shape.","zh":"一種文化可能有複雜神話，解釋為何某些星星形成獵人形狀。"},{"en":"Mythology helps people remember star patterns by connecting them with stories.","zh":"神話透過把星群與故事連接，幫助人們記住星星圖案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rich and detailed traditional storytelling.","zh":"這個短語描述豐富而細緻的傳統故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"behind the stars","meaning":"與星星背後相關的","examples":[{"en":"Many cultures have mythology behind the stars and their constellations.","zh":"許多文化都有與星星及其星座背後相關的神話。"},{"en":"Behind the stars means connected with the stories or meanings people attach to stars.","zh":"與星星背後相關，是指與人們附加於星星的故事或意義有關。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain the stories behind the stars before a night-sky activity.","zh":"老師可能在夜空活動前解釋星星背後的故事。"},{"en":"Stories behind stars make astronomy feel cultural as well as scientific.","zh":"星星背後的故事令天文學不只是科學，也具有文化色彩。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the symbolic background of star patterns.","zh":"這個短語指星星圖案的象徵背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Greek mythology","meaning":"希臘神話","examples":[{"en":"Pegasus appears in Greek mythology.","zh":"飛馬珀伽索斯出現在希臘神話中。"},{"en":"Greek mythology is the body of ancient Greek stories about gods, heroes, and monsters.","zh":"希臘神話是古希臘關於神、英雄和怪物的一系列故事。"},{"en":"Students may meet Greek mythology through stories of Zeus, Medusa, and Pegasus.","zh":"學生可能透過宙斯、美杜莎和飛馬的故事接觸希臘神話。"},{"en":"Greek myths influenced the names and meanings of many constellations.","zh":"希臘神話影響了許多星座的名稱和意義。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to ancient Greek traditional stories.","zh":"這個短語指古希臘傳統故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"winged horse","meaning":"有翼飛馬","examples":[{"en":"Pegasus was a winged horse in Greek mythology.","zh":"珀伽索斯是希臘神話中的有翼飛馬。"},{"en":"A winged horse is a horse imagined with wings.","zh":"有翼飛馬，是想像中長有翅膀的馬。"},{"en":"In a children’s story, a winged horse might fly over mountains and rivers.","zh":"在兒童故事中，有翼飛馬可能飛越高山和河流。"},{"en":"The image is memorable because it combines an ordinary animal with a magical feature.","zh":"這個形象令人難忘，因為它把普通動物與神奇特徵結合。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the mythical form of Pegasus.","zh":"這個短語描述珀伽索斯的神話形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"is said to have","meaning":"據說曾經……","examples":[{"en":"Pegasus is said to have sprung from the head of Medusa.","zh":"據說珀伽索斯曾從美杜莎的頭顱中冒出。"},{"en":"Is said to have means people tell or believe that something happened, though it is part of a story or report.","zh":"據說曾經，是指人們傳說或相信某事發生過，雖然它可能屬於故事或報道。"},{"en":"The old castle is said to have a hidden tunnel beneath it.","zh":"據說那座古堡地下曾有一條隧道。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting legends or beliefs rather than proven facts.","zh":"這個短語適合轉述傳說或信念，而不是已證實事實。"},{"en":"It signals that the speaker is passing on a claim or tradition.","zh":"它表示說話者正在轉述一個說法或傳統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sprung from","meaning":"從……冒出；源自……","examples":[{"en":"Pegasus is said to have sprung from the decapitated head of Medusa.","zh":"據說珀伽索斯從美杜莎被斬下的頭顱中冒出。"},{"en":"Sprung from means suddenly came out of or originated from something.","zh":"從某處冒出或源自某事，是指突然出現或起源於某物。"},{"en":"A new idea may spring from a simple classroom question.","zh":"一個新想法可能源自一條簡單課堂問題。"},{"en":"In mythology, strange beings may spring from unusual or dramatic events.","zh":"在神話中，奇異生物可能從不尋常或戲劇性事件中出現。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe both literal emergence and symbolic origin.","zh":"這個短語可以描述實際冒出，也可以描述象徵性起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"decapitated head","meaning":"被斬下的頭顱","examples":[{"en":"Pegasus sprang from the decapitated head of Medusa.","zh":"珀伽索斯從美杜莎被斬下的頭顱中冒出。"},{"en":"A decapitated head is a head separated from the body.","zh":"被斬下的頭顱，是與身體分離的頭。"},{"en":"In old myths, violent images such as a decapitated head often symbolise danger or transformation.","zh":"在古老神話中，被斬下的頭顱等暴力形象常象徵危險或轉變。"},{"en":"This detail makes the story of Pegasus dramatic and memorable.","zh":"這個細節令珀伽索斯的故事戲劇化而令人難忘。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a severed head in a mythological context.","zh":"這個短語在神話語境中描述被斬下的頭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"god-king","meaning":"眾神之王","examples":[{"en":"Zeus was the god-king who used Pegasus to carry thunder and lightning.","zh":"宙斯是眾神之王，使用珀伽索斯把雷電帶到地球。"},{"en":"A god-king is a ruler among gods, or a king-like divine figure.","zh":"眾神之王，是神明中的統治者，或像國王一樣的神聖人物。"},{"en":"In Greek mythology, Zeus is often shown as the powerful ruler of the gods.","zh":"在希臘神話中，宙斯常被描繪為強大的眾神統治者。"},{"en":"Calling Zeus a god-king emphasises both his divine nature and authority.","zh":"稱宙斯為眾神之王，強調他的神性和權威。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a supreme ruler in a mythological system.","zh":"這個短語描述神話系統中的最高統治者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"carry thunder and lightning","meaning":"把雷電帶到……","examples":[{"en":"Pegasus was used to carry thunder and lightning to Earth.","zh":"珀伽索斯被用來把雷電帶到地球。"},{"en":"To carry thunder and lightning means to transport or deliver the powers of storms in a myth.","zh":"把雷電帶到某處，是指在神話中運送或傳遞風暴力量。"},{"en":"A story may describe a magical bird carrying messages from the gods.","zh":"故事可能描寫神鳥把眾神的訊息帶到人間。"},{"en":"This image connects Pegasus with Zeus’s power over the sky.","zh":"這個形象把珀伽索斯與宙斯掌控天空的力量連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mythical task, not ordinary physical transport.","zh":"這個短語描述神話任務，而不是普通實物運輸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"placed among","meaning":"被置於……之中","examples":[{"en":"Pegasus was later placed among the constellations.","zh":"珀伽索斯後來被置於星座之中。"},{"en":"Placed among something means put into or included within a group.","zh":"被置於某物之中，是指被放入或包含在一個群體內。"},{"en":"A student’s drawing may be placed among the best works on the classroom wall.","zh":"學生畫作可能被放在課室牆上的最佳作品之中。"},{"en":"When a mythical figure is placed among the stars, it becomes part of sky storytelling.","zh":"當神話人物被置於星星之中，它就成為天空故事的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inclusion within a larger set.","zh":"這個短語描述被納入較大集合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Western astronomy","meaning":"西方天文學","examples":[{"en":"Modern constellation names in Western astronomy derive from Latin.","zh":"西方天文學中的現代星座名稱源自拉丁文。"},{"en":"Western astronomy is the astronomical tradition developed in Europe and related cultures.","zh":"西方天文學是歐洲及相關文化中發展出的天文傳統。"},{"en":"A student may study Western astronomy when learning names such as Orion and Ursa Major.","zh":"學生學習獵戶座和大熊座等名稱時，可能接觸西方天文學。"},{"en":"Its naming system preserves older European languages and traditions.","zh":"它的命名系統保留了較舊的歐洲語言和傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific astronomical tradition, not all astronomy worldwide.","zh":"這個短語指特定天文傳統，而不是全球所有天文學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"modern constellation names","meaning":"現代星座名稱","examples":[{"en":"All modern constellation names derive from Latin.","zh":"所有現代星座名稱都源自拉丁文。"},{"en":"Modern constellation names are the current official names used for constellations.","zh":"現代星座名稱是目前官方使用的星座名稱。"},{"en":"A star map may use modern constellation names so observers around the world can communicate clearly.","zh":"星圖可能使用現代星座名稱，讓世界各地觀察者能清楚溝通。"},{"en":"Standard names reduce confusion between older, local, and informal names.","zh":"標準名稱減少舊名稱、地方名稱和非正式名稱之間的混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to today’s accepted constellation terminology.","zh":"這個短語指現今被接受的星座術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"derive from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"All modern constellation names derive from Latin.","zh":"所有現代星座名稱都源自拉丁文。"},{"en":"To derive from something means to come from or originate in it.","zh":"源自某物，是指來自或起源於它。"},{"en":"Many English words derive from Latin and French.","zh":"許多英文字源自拉丁文和法文。"},{"en":"Knowing where a word derives from can help students understand its form and meaning.","zh":"知道一個詞源自哪裡，可以幫助學生理解其形式和意思。"},{"en":"This phrase explains origin.","zh":"這個短語解釋來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Latin","meaning":"拉丁文","examples":[{"en":"Modern constellation names in Western astronomy derive from Latin.","zh":"西方天文學中的現代星座名稱源自拉丁文。"},{"en":"Latin is an ancient language once widely used in Europe for learning, law, and religion.","zh":"拉丁文是一種古代語言，曾在歐洲廣泛用於學術、法律和宗教。"},{"en":"Students may see Latin in scientific names for plants and animals.","zh":"學生可能在動植物學名中看到拉丁文。"},{"en":"Latin remains important because many technical terms still come from it.","zh":"拉丁文仍然重要，因為許多專門術語仍源自它。"},{"en":"This word refers to the language behind many Western constellation names.","zh":"這個詞指許多西方星座名稱背後的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stars within the constellations","meaning":"星座內的星星","examples":[{"en":"Some stars within the constellations are named using Latin forms.","zh":"有些星座內的星星使用拉丁形式命名。"},{"en":"Stars within the constellations are individual stars located inside recognised constellation areas.","zh":"星座內的星星，是位於被承認星座區域內的個別星星。"},{"en":"A student may identify a bright star within Orion before learning its formal name.","zh":"學生可能先辨認獵戶座內的一顆亮星，再學其正式名稱。"},{"en":"Naming stars within constellations helps astronomers describe exact locations.","zh":"命名星座內的星星，有助天文學家描述準確位置。"},{"en":"This phrase distinguishes individual stars from the whole constellation.","zh":"這個短語把個別星星與整個星座區分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"genitive form","meaning":"所有格形式","examples":[{"en":"Some stars are named using the genitive form of the Latin word.","zh":"有些星星使用拉丁詞的所有格形式命名。"},{"en":"The genitive form is a grammatical form showing possession or relationship.","zh":"所有格形式是顯示擁有或關係的文法形式。"},{"en":"In English, “the teacher’s book” shows possession, like a genitive idea.","zh":"在英文中，“the teacher’s book” 顯示擁有，類似所有格概念。"},{"en":"Latin genitive forms help show that a star belongs to or is associated with a constellation.","zh":"拉丁文所有格形式幫助顯示某顆星屬於或與某星座相關。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a grammar form used in naming.","zh":"這個短語描述命名中使用的文法形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"following the usual rules of","meaning":"遵循……的一般規則","examples":[{"en":"Star names follow the usual rules of Latin grammar.","zh":"星星名稱遵循拉丁文文法的一般規則。"},{"en":"Following the usual rules of something means obeying the normal patterns of that system.","zh":"遵循某事的一般規則，是指依照該系統的正常模式。"},{"en":"A student forms regular past tense verbs by following the usual rules of English grammar.","zh":"學生透過遵循英文文法的一般規則，形成規則動詞過去式。"},{"en":"Rules help names and sentences remain consistent.","zh":"規則幫助名稱和句子保持一致。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using the standard rules of a system.","zh":"這個短語描述使用系統的標準規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Latin grammar","meaning":"拉丁文文法","examples":[{"en":"The genitive form follows the usual rules of Latin grammar.","zh":"所有格形式遵循拉丁文文法的一般規則。"},{"en":"Latin grammar is the system of word forms and sentence rules in Latin.","zh":"拉丁文文法是拉丁文的詞形和句子規則系統。"},{"en":"Students learning Latin grammar must study endings that show case and number.","zh":"學習拉丁文文法的學生必須研究顯示格和數的詞尾。"},{"en":"Grammar rules affect how scientific and astronomical names are formed.","zh":"文法規則影響科學和天文名稱如何形成。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the structure of the Latin language.","zh":"這個短語指拉丁語言的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"for example","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"For example, the genitive form of Pisces is Piscium.","zh":"例如，Pisces 的所有格形式是 Piscium。"},{"en":"For example introduces a specific case that helps explain a general point.","zh":"例如，用來引入具體例子，以幫助解釋一般重點。"},{"en":"Some fruits are rich in vitamin C; for example, oranges are a common source.","zh":"有些水果富含維他命 C；例如，橙是常見來源。"},{"en":"Examples make abstract rules easier to understand.","zh":"例子令抽象規則更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that a concrete illustration is coming next.","zh":"這個短語表示接下來會有具體說明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in addition","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"In addition, all constellation names have a standard abbreviation.","zh":"此外，所有星座名稱都有標準縮寫。"},{"en":"In addition means also or furthermore.","zh":"此外，是指也、另外。"},{"en":"The school provides textbooks; in addition, students can borrow tablets.","zh":"學校提供教科書；此外，學生可以借用平板電腦。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another point to the previous information.","zh":"這個短語在前面資料之外加入另一點。"},{"en":"It helps writers build a list of related facts.","zh":"它幫助作者建立相關事實清單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"standard three-letter abbreviation","meaning":"標準三字母縮寫","examples":[{"en":"All constellation names have a standard three-letter abbreviation.","zh":"所有星座名稱都有標準三字母縮寫。"},{"en":"A standard three-letter abbreviation is an officially accepted short form made of three letters.","zh":"標準三字母縮寫，是由三個字母組成並被官方接受的簡短形式。"},{"en":"A timetable may use a standard abbreviation such as Mon for Monday.","zh":"時間表可能使用 Mon 這類標準縮寫表示 Monday。"},{"en":"Abbreviations save space and make tables easier to read.","zh":"縮寫節省空間，令表格更容易閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fixed short form used consistently.","zh":"這個短語描述固定且一致使用的簡短形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"assigned by","meaning":"由……指定","examples":[{"en":"The abbreviation is assigned by the IAU.","zh":"該縮寫由國際天文聯會指定。"},{"en":"Assigned by someone means officially given or allocated by that person or organisation.","zh":"由某人指定，是指由該人或機構正式給予或分配。"},{"en":"Student numbers may be assigned by the school office.","zh":"學生編號可能由校務處指定。"},{"en":"Official assignment prevents different people from inventing different labels.","zh":"官方指定可以防止不同人創造不同標籤。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who gives a name, code, or role.","zh":"這個短語指出誰給予名稱、代碼或角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"under which","meaning":"在此制度下","examples":[{"en":"Under this system, Pisces becomes Psc.","zh":"在此制度下，Pisces 變成 Psc。"},{"en":"Under which or under this system means according to that rule or arrangement.","zh":"在此制度下，是指根據該規則或安排。"},{"en":"Under the new school policy, students submit homework online.","zh":"在新校政下，學生網上提交功課。"},{"en":"A system changes how names, rules, or procedures are used.","zh":"制度會改變名稱、規則或程序的使用方式。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what happens within a particular system.","zh":"這個短語引入某特定制度中發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"laypeople","meaning":"外行人；非專業人士","examples":[{"en":"Laypeople may wrongly consider some star patterns to be constellations.","zh":"外行人可能錯誤地把一些星體圖案視為星座。"},{"en":"Laypeople are people who are not specialists in a particular field.","zh":"外行人是某一領域中的非專業人士。"},{"en":"Laypeople may confuse medical terms because they have not studied medicine professionally.","zh":"外行人可能混淆醫學術語，因為他們沒有專業學過醫學。"},{"en":"Non-specialists can make mistakes when technical definitions differ from everyday language.","zh":"當技術定義與日常語言不同，非專業人士可能出錯。"},{"en":"This word contrasts ordinary people with experts.","zh":"這個詞把普通人與專家作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"wrongly consider","meaning":"錯誤地認為","examples":[{"en":"Some laypeople wrongly consider asterisms to be constellations.","zh":"有些外行人錯誤地認為星群是星座。"},{"en":"To wrongly consider something to be something else means to mistake it for another category.","zh":"錯誤地認為某物是另一物，是指把它誤判為另一類別。"},{"en":"A student may wrongly consider a dolphin to be a fish because it lives in water.","zh":"學生可能因海豚住在水中而錯誤地認為它是魚。"},{"en":"Wrong classification happens when everyday appearance differs from technical definition.","zh":"當日常外觀與技術定義不同，錯誤分類就會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mistaken judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述錯誤判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"are actually","meaning":"實際上是……","examples":[{"en":"Some star patterns are actually asterisms.","zh":"有些星體圖案實際上是星群。"},{"en":"Are actually means are in reality, even if people may think otherwise.","zh":"實際上是，是指真實情況是如此，即使人們可能另有想法。"},{"en":"Tomatoes are actually fruits, although many people use them like vegetables.","zh":"番茄實際上是水果，雖然很多人把它當蔬菜使用。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects a common misunderstanding.","zh":"這個短語修正常見誤解。"},{"en":"It introduces the true identity of something.","zh":"它引入某事物的真實身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"asterisms","meaning":"星群；星座內星群","examples":[{"en":"Asterisms are groups of stars that appear to form patterns in the sky.","zh":"星群是一組看起來在天空中形成圖案的星星。"},{"en":"Asterisms are recognisable star patterns that are not official constellations.","zh":"星群是可辨認但不是官方星座的星星圖案。"},{"en":"The Big Dipper is a famous asterism that many children can identify.","zh":"北斗七星是一個著名星群，許多孩子都能辨認。"},{"en":"Asterisms can be easier to remember than full constellations because they form simple shapes.","zh":"星群可能比完整星座更容易記住，因為它們形成簡單形狀。"},{"en":"This word describes informal or smaller star patterns.","zh":"這個詞描述非正式或較小的星星圖案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"appear to form patterns","meaning":"看起來形成圖案","examples":[{"en":"Asterisms appear to form patterns in the sky.","zh":"星群看起來在天空中形成圖案。"},{"en":"Appear to form patterns means seem to create shapes when viewed from Earth.","zh":"看起來形成圖案，是指從地球觀看時似乎組成形狀。"},{"en":"Streetlights on a hill may appear to form patterns when seen from far away.","zh":"遠看山上的街燈時，它們可能看起來形成圖案。"},{"en":"The pattern depends on the viewer’s perspective, not necessarily real connection.","zh":"圖案取決於觀察者視角，不一定代表真實連接。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual arrangement rather than physical joining.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺排列，而不是物理連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"officially defined constellations","meaning":"官方界定的星座","examples":[{"en":"Asterisms are not among the 88 officially defined constellations.","zh":"星群不屬於 88 個官方界定的星座之中。"},{"en":"Officially defined constellations are constellation areas formally accepted by an authority.","zh":"官方界定的星座，是由權威機構正式接受的星座區域。"},{"en":"A popular nickname for a star pattern may not be part of the officially defined list.","zh":"星體圖案的流行暱稱未必屬於官方界定清單。"},{"en":"Official definition gives astronomers a shared technical standard.","zh":"官方定義給天文學家共同技術標準。"},{"en":"This phrase describes constellations recognised by formal rules.","zh":"這個短語描述由正式規則承認的星座。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a famous example of","meaning":"……的一個著名例子","examples":[{"en":"The Big Dipper is a famous example of an asterism.","zh":"北斗七星是星群的一個著名例子。"},{"en":"A famous example of something is a well-known case that shows what that thing is.","zh":"某事的一個著名例子，是能展示該事物的廣為人知個案。"},{"en":"The Eiffel Tower is a famous example of a landmark.","zh":"艾菲爾鐵塔是地標的一個著名例子。"},{"en":"Famous examples help students understand a category more quickly.","zh":"著名例子幫助學生更快理解一個類別。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an easy-to-recognise case.","zh":"這個短語引入容易辨認的個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"mistaken for","meaning":"被誤認為……","examples":[{"en":"The Big Dipper is often mistaken for a constellation.","zh":"北斗七星經常被誤認為星座。"},{"en":"Mistaken for something means wrongly identified as that thing.","zh":"被誤認為某物，是指被錯誤識別為該物。"},{"en":"A plastic plant may be mistaken for a real one from far away.","zh":"遠看時，塑膠植物可能被誤認為真植物。"},{"en":"The Big Dipper is mistaken for a constellation because it is familiar and easy to see.","zh":"北斗七星被誤認為星座，是因為它熟悉又容易看見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes incorrect identification.","zh":"這個短語描述錯誤識別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Big Dipper","meaning":"北斗七星","examples":[{"en":"The Big Dipper is an asterism often mistaken for a constellation.","zh":"北斗七星是一個經常被誤認為星座的星群。"},{"en":"The Big Dipper is a famous star pattern that forms part of Ursa Major.","zh":"北斗七星是一個著名星體圖案，是大熊座的一部分。"},{"en":"A camper may use the Big Dipper to help find direction at night.","zh":"露營者可能使用北斗七星在夜間幫助辨認方向。"},{"en":"It is memorable because its stars look like a ladle or dipper.","zh":"它令人難忘，因為其星星看起來像勺子或斗。"},{"en":"This phrase names a familiar star pattern, not a whole official constellation.","zh":"這個短語命名一個熟悉星體圖案，而不是完整官方星座。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as it is termed","meaning":"正如它在……被稱為","examples":[{"en":"The Big Dipper is the name as it is termed in North America.","zh":"Big Dipper 是它在北美被稱為的名稱。"},{"en":"As it is termed means as it is called in a particular place or context.","zh":"正如它在某地被稱為，是指在特定地方或語境中的稱呼。"},{"en":"The same school subject may be termed differently in different education systems.","zh":"同一學科在不同教育制度中可能有不同稱呼。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights that names can vary by region.","zh":"這個短語突出名稱可因地區而異。"},{"en":"It introduces the local term for something.","zh":"它引入某物的本地名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"North America","meaning":"北美","examples":[{"en":"The Big Dipper is the term used in North America.","zh":"Big Dipper 是北美使用的名稱。"},{"en":"North America is the continent including countries such as the United States and Canada.","zh":"北美是包括美國和加拿大等國家的洲。"},{"en":"A word may be common in North America but less common in Britain.","zh":"一個詞可能在北美常見，但在英國較少使用。"},{"en":"Regional names can differ even when people refer to the same star pattern.","zh":"即使人們指同一星體圖案，地區名稱也可以不同。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the region where a term is used.","zh":"這個短語指出某個稱呼使用的地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the Plough","meaning":"犁星；北斗七星","examples":[{"en":"The Plough is the name used in the UK for the same star pattern.","zh":"The Plough 是英國對同一星體圖案使用的名稱。"},{"en":"The Plough is the British name for the star pattern called the Big Dipper in North America.","zh":"The Plough 是北美稱為 Big Dipper 的星體圖案在英國的名稱。"},{"en":"A British astronomy book may teach children to find the Plough in the night sky.","zh":"英國天文書可能教孩子在夜空中尋找 The Plough。"},{"en":"Different names can refer to the same pattern because cultures imagine different shapes.","zh":"不同名稱可以指同一圖案，因為文化會想像不同形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase names the UK version of the Big Dipper.","zh":"這個短語命名北斗七星的英國說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as it is known in","meaning":"在……被稱為","examples":[{"en":"The pattern is known in the UK as the Plough.","zh":"這個圖案在英國被稱為 The Plough。"},{"en":"As it is known in a place means by the name used in that place.","zh":"在某地被稱為，是指使用該地方的名稱。"},{"en":"A food may be known in one country by a different name from another country.","zh":"一種食物在一個國家可能被稱為與另一國不同的名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase shows regional variation in naming.","zh":"這個短語顯示命名上的地區差異。"},{"en":"It helps connect one object with its local name.","zh":"它幫助把一件事物與本地名稱連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"astronomical terms","meaning":"天文學術語","examples":[{"en":"In astronomical terms, the Big Dipper is part of Ursa Major.","zh":"以天文學術語來說，北斗七星是大熊座的一部分。"},{"en":"Astronomical terms are technical words or ways of speaking used in astronomy.","zh":"天文學術語是天文學中使用的技術詞彙或說法。"},{"en":"In medical terms, a cold and influenza are not exactly the same illness.","zh":"以醫學術語來說，感冒和流感並非完全相同疾病。"},{"en":"Technical terms can correct everyday misunderstandings.","zh":"技術術語可以修正常見日常誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the explanation is from a scientific viewpoint.","zh":"這個短語表示解釋來自科學角度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"star formation","meaning":"星體排列","examples":[{"en":"This famous star formation is part of a larger constellation.","zh":"這個著名星體排列是較大星座的一部分。"},{"en":"A star formation is an arrangement or pattern of stars as seen from Earth.","zh":"星體排列，是從地球看見的星星安排或圖案。"},{"en":"A beginner may recognise a simple star formation before learning its official category.","zh":"初學者可能先認出簡單星體排列，再學其官方類別。"},{"en":"Clear formations help people remember the night sky more easily.","zh":"清楚排列幫助人更容易記住夜空。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visible arrangement of stars.","zh":"這個短語描述可見的星星排列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in fact considered","meaning":"事實上被視為","examples":[{"en":"The Big Dipper is in fact considered only part of Ursa Major.","zh":"北斗七星事實上只被視為大熊座的一部分。"},{"en":"In fact considered means actually regarded as, often correcting a misunderstanding.","zh":"事實上被視為，是指實際上被看作某類，通常用來修正誤解。"},{"en":"A tomato is in fact considered a fruit in botanical terms.","zh":"以植物學術語來說，番茄事實上被視為水果。"},{"en":"This phrase helps clarify the true classification of something.","zh":"這個短語幫助澄清某事的真正分類。"},{"en":"It is useful when everyday belief differs from technical knowledge.","zh":"當日常看法與技術知識不同時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"part of","meaning":"……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"The Big Dipper is part of the larger constellation Ursa Major.","zh":"北斗七星是較大星座大熊座的一部分。"},{"en":"Part of means one section or element within a larger whole.","zh":"某物的一部分，是指較大整體中的一個部分或元素。"},{"en":"A school library is part of the whole school community.","zh":"學校圖書館是整個學校社群的一部分。"},{"en":"Something can be famous by itself while still belonging to a larger system.","zh":"某物可以本身很有名，同時仍屬於較大系統。"},{"en":"This phrase shows inclusion within a bigger whole.","zh":"這個短語顯示被包含在更大整體中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"larger constellation","meaning":"較大的星座","examples":[{"en":"Ursa Major is the larger constellation containing the Big Dipper.","zh":"大熊座是包含北斗七星的較大星座。"},{"en":"A larger constellation is a bigger official star area that can contain smaller patterns.","zh":"較大的星座，是可以包含較小圖案的更大官方星區。"},{"en":"A large district may contain several smaller neighbourhoods.","zh":"大型地區可能包含幾個較小社區。"},{"en":"The Big Dipper is familiar, but it sits within a larger constellation.","zh":"北斗七星很熟悉，但它位於一個較大的星座之內。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the bigger star grouping around a smaller pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞較小圖案的更大星群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"known as Ursa Major","meaning":"被稱為大熊座","examples":[{"en":"The larger constellation is known as Ursa Major.","zh":"較大的星座被稱為大熊座。"},{"en":"Known as Ursa Major means called by the official Latin name Ursa Major.","zh":"被稱為 Ursa Major，是指以官方拉丁名稱 Ursa Major 稱呼。"},{"en":"A student may know the Big Dipper first and later learn that the larger constellation is known as Ursa Major.","zh":"學生可能先認識北斗七星，後來才學到較大星座稱為大熊座。"},{"en":"Learning official names helps connect popular patterns with astronomy terms.","zh":"學習官方名稱有助把流行圖案與天文術語連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the formal name of the larger constellation.","zh":"這個短語給出較大星座的正式名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in order to","meaning":"為了……","examples":[{"en":"In order to identify star positions, astronomers use celestial coordinate systems.","zh":"為了辨認星星位置，天文學家使用天球座標系統。"},{"en":"In order to means for the purpose of doing something.","zh":"為了，是指以做某事為目的。"},{"en":"In order to improve writing, students should read model essays and practise regularly.","zh":"為了改善寫作，學生應閱讀範文並定期練習。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly connects an action with its purpose.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接行動與目的。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining why something is done.","zh":"它適合解釋為何做某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"identify the position of","meaning":"辨認……的位置","examples":[{"en":"Celestial coordinate systems identify the position of stars relative to the Earth.","zh":"天球座標系統辨認星星相對於地球的位置。"},{"en":"To identify the position of something means to locate where it is.","zh":"辨認某物的位置，是指找出它在哪裡。"},{"en":"A map app can identify the position of a shop before you travel there.","zh":"地圖應用程式可以在你前往前辨認商店位置。"},{"en":"Accurate position helps people find, compare, and describe objects.","zh":"準確位置幫助人尋找、比較和描述物件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes locating something clearly.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚定位某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"relative to","meaning":"相對於……","examples":[{"en":"Stars can be located relative to the Earth.","zh":"星星可以相對於地球定位。"},{"en":"Relative to something means compared with or measured in relation to it.","zh":"相對於某物，是指與它比較或以它作關係量度。"},{"en":"A classroom seat may be described relative to the teacher’s desk.","zh":"課室座位可以相對於老師桌子來描述。"},{"en":"Position becomes clearer when there is a reference point.","zh":"有參考點時，位置會更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the point of comparison or measurement.","zh":"這個短語顯示比較或量度的參照點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"celestial coordinate systems","meaning":"天球座標系統","examples":[{"en":"Celestial coordinate systems provide reference points in space.","zh":"天球座標系統在太空中提供參考點。"},{"en":"Celestial coordinate systems are systems for locating objects in the sky.","zh":"天球座標系統是用來定位天空物體的系統。"},{"en":"A map grid helps people locate streets, and celestial coordinates help astronomers locate stars.","zh":"地圖網格幫助人定位街道，而天球座標幫助天文學家定位星星。"},{"en":"Without a coordinate system, describing exact star positions would be difficult.","zh":"沒有座標系統，描述精確星星位置會很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sky-mapping systems.","zh":"這個短語描述天空繪圖系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"provide a detailed reference point","meaning":"提供詳細的參考點","examples":[{"en":"Coordinate systems provide a detailed reference point in space.","zh":"座標系統在太空中提供詳細的參考點。"},{"en":"To provide a detailed reference point means to give an exact basis for locating something.","zh":"提供詳細的參考點，是指給出定位某物的準確基礎。"},{"en":"A classroom seating chart provides a reference point for finding each student.","zh":"課室座位表為尋找每名學生提供參考點。"},{"en":"Detailed reference points reduce confusion when objects are far away or hard to see.","zh":"當物體很遙遠或難以看見，詳細參考點能減少混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving a clear location standard.","zh":"這個短語描述給出清楚定位標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in space","meaning":"在太空中","examples":[{"en":"Celestial coordinate systems provide reference points in space.","zh":"天球座標系統在太空中提供參考點。"},{"en":"In space means in the area beyond Earth’s atmosphere where stars and planets exist.","zh":"在太空中，是指在地球大氣層之外、星星和行星存在的區域。"},{"en":"Satellites travel in space above Earth.","zh":"衛星在地球上方的太空中運行。"},{"en":"Locating objects in space requires reference systems because distances are enormous.","zh":"定位太空中的物體需要參考系統，因為距離極其龐大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical realm beyond Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述地球之外的物理空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"largely similar","meaning":"大致相似","examples":[{"en":"The different celestial systems are largely similar.","zh":"不同天球系統大致相似。"},{"en":"Largely similar means mostly alike, though not exactly the same.","zh":"大致相似，是指大部分相同，但不完全一樣。"},{"en":"Two school timetables may be largely similar, with only lunch time different.","zh":"兩份學校時間表可能大致相似，只是午飯時間不同。"},{"en":"Similar systems are easier to compare because they share basic ideas.","zh":"相似系統較容易比較，因為它們有共同基本想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad similarity with possible small differences.","zh":"這個短語描述大體相似但可能有小差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"differ in","meaning":"在……方面不同","examples":[{"en":"The systems differ in the position of the fundamental plane.","zh":"這些系統在基本平面的位置方面不同。"},{"en":"Differ in something means be different with respect to that feature.","zh":"在某方面不同，是指就該特徵而言不一樣。"},{"en":"Two phones may differ in battery life but have the same screen size.","zh":"兩部手機可能在電池續航方面不同，但螢幕大小相同。"},{"en":"Systems can be similar overall but differ in one important detail.","zh":"系統整體可相似，但在一個重要細節上不同。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the exact area of difference.","zh":"這個短語指出確切差異所在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fundamental plane","meaning":"基本平面","examples":[{"en":"The fundamental plane divides northern and southern hemispheres.","zh":"基本平面劃分南北半球。"},{"en":"A fundamental plane is a basic reference surface used in a coordinate system.","zh":"基本平面是座標系統中使用的基本參考面。"},{"en":"A map grid needs a reference line, just as a coordinate system needs a fundamental plane.","zh":"地圖網格需要參考線，就像座標系統需要基本平面。"},{"en":"Changing the fundamental plane changes how positions are measured.","zh":"改變基本平面會改變位置量度方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main reference surface in a system.","zh":"這個短語描述系統中的主要參考面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the division between","meaning":"……之間的分界","examples":[{"en":"The fundamental plane is the division between northern and southern hemispheres.","zh":"基本平面是南北半球之間的分界。"},{"en":"The division between two things is the boundary or separation that distinguishes them.","zh":"兩者之間的分界，是區分它們的邊界或分隔。"},{"en":"A river may form the division between two districts.","zh":"河流可能形成兩個地區之間的分界。"},{"en":"Clear divisions help people organise space and categories.","zh":"清楚分界幫助人們整理空間和類別。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a separating line or distinction.","zh":"這個短語描述分隔線或區別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"northern and southern hemispheres","meaning":"南北半球","examples":[{"en":"The fundamental plane separates the northern and southern hemispheres.","zh":"基本平面分隔南北半球。"},{"en":"Northern and southern hemispheres are the two halves divided by a reference plane or equator.","zh":"南北半球是由參考平面或赤道劃分的兩半。"},{"en":"Earth’s northern and southern hemispheres have different seasons at the same time.","zh":"地球南北半球在同一時間有不同季節。"},{"en":"In sky mapping, hemispheres help divide what observers can see.","zh":"在天空繪圖中，半球幫助劃分觀察者能看見的範圍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two opposite halves of a sphere or sky system.","zh":"這個短語描述球體或天空系統的兩個相對半部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"most common celestial systems","meaning":"最常見的天球系統","examples":[{"en":"The five most common celestial systems are listed in the passage.","zh":"篇章列出五個最常見的天球系統。"},{"en":"Most common celestial systems are the coordinate systems most often used to locate objects in the sky.","zh":"最常見的天球系統，是最常用來定位天空物體的座標系統。"},{"en":"A beginner may first learn the most common systems before studying rare specialist systems.","zh":"初學者可能先學最常見系統，再研究罕見專門系統。"},{"en":"Common systems are useful because many astronomers understand them.","zh":"常見系統有用，因為許多天文學家都理解它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes widely used sky-coordinate systems.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛使用的天空座標系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Horizontal system","meaning":"地平座標系統","examples":[{"en":"The Horizontal system is one common celestial coordinate system.","zh":"地平座標系統是一種常見天球座標系統。"},{"en":"The Horizontal system locates sky objects using the observer’s horizon as a reference.","zh":"地平座標系統使用觀察者的地平線作參考來定位天空物體。"},{"en":"A stargazing app may use a horizontal-style view to show what is above the local horizon.","zh":"觀星應用程式可能使用地平式視圖顯示本地地平線上方有甚麼。"},{"en":"This system is practical because it relates the sky to where the observer is standing.","zh":"這個系統實用，因為它把天空與觀察者站立位置連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase names one way of locating objects in the sky.","zh":"這個短語命名一種定位天空物體的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Equatorial system","meaning":"赤道座標系統","examples":[{"en":"The Equatorial system is one of the five common celestial systems.","zh":"赤道座標系統是五種常見天球系統之一。"},{"en":"The Equatorial system uses Earth’s equator projected into the sky as a reference.","zh":"赤道座標系統使用投射到天空中的地球赤道作參考。"},{"en":"Astronomers may use the Equatorial system to record star positions consistently.","zh":"天文學家可能使用赤道座標系統一致記錄星星位置。"},{"en":"This system is useful because it is not tied only to one local horizon.","zh":"這個系統有用，因為它不只依附於某一個本地地平線。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major coordinate system in astronomy.","zh":"這個短語命名天文學中的主要座標系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Ecliptical system","meaning":"黃道座標系統","examples":[{"en":"The Ecliptical system is used as a celestial coordinate system.","zh":"黃道座標系統被用作天球座標系統。"},{"en":"The Ecliptical system uses the sun’s apparent path as an important reference.","zh":"黃道座標系統使用太陽的表觀路徑作重要參考。"},{"en":"A lesson about zodiac constellations may mention the Ecliptical system.","zh":"關於黃道星座的課堂可能提到黃道座標系統。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing objects near the sun’s apparent yearly path.","zh":"討論接近太陽一年表觀路徑的物體時，它很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase names a sky-coordinate system linked with the ecliptic.","zh":"這個短語命名與黃道相關的天空座標系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Galactic system","meaning":"銀河座標系統","examples":[{"en":"The Galactic system is one of the common celestial systems.","zh":"銀河座標系統是常見天球系統之一。"},{"en":"The Galactic system uses the Milky Way as a reference for locating objects.","zh":"銀河座標系統使用銀河系作為定位物體的參考。"},{"en":"Astronomers may use the Galactic system when studying stars within our galaxy.","zh":"天文學家研究我們銀河系內的星星時，可能使用銀河座標系統。"},{"en":"A system based on the galaxy helps describe positions on a larger cosmic scale.","zh":"以銀河為基礎的系統有助在更大宇宙尺度上描述位置。"},{"en":"This phrase names a coordinate system connected with the Milky Way.","zh":"這個短語命名與銀河系相關的座標系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Supergalactic system","meaning":"超星系座標系統","examples":[{"en":"The Supergalactic system is another celestial coordinate system.","zh":"超星系座標系統是另一種天球座標系統。"},{"en":"The Supergalactic system is a coordinate system used for very large-scale cosmic structures.","zh":"超星系座標系統是用於極大尺度宇宙結構的座標系統。"},{"en":"Advanced astronomy students may meet the Supergalactic system when studying groups of galaxies.","zh":"高階天文學生研究星系群時，可能接觸超星系座標系統。"},{"en":"Different systems are needed because astronomers study objects at different scales.","zh":"需要不同系統，是因為天文學家研究不同尺度的物體。"},{"en":"This phrase names a coordinate system beyond ordinary star mapping.","zh":"這個短語命名超越普通星星繪圖的座標系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the launch of","meaning":"……的發射","examples":[{"en":"The launch of the Hubble Space Telescope changed astronomy.","zh":"哈勃太空望遠鏡的發射改變了天文學。"},{"en":"The launch of something means the act of sending it into operation, space, or public use.","zh":"某物的發射或推出，是指把它送入運作、太空或公眾使用。"},{"en":"The launch of a new school app may change how parents receive notices.","zh":"新學校應用程式的推出可能改變家長接收通告的方式。"},{"en":"A launch can be important because it begins a new phase of use or discovery.","zh":"發射或推出很重要，因為它開始了使用或發現的新階段。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the starting event of a major project.","zh":"這個短語描述重大項目的起始事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Hubble Space Telescope","meaning":"哈勃太空望遠鏡","examples":[{"en":"The Hubble Space Telescope was launched in April 1990.","zh":"哈勃太空望遠鏡於 1990 年 4 月發射。"},{"en":"The Hubble Space Telescope is a telescope placed in space to observe the universe above Earth’s atmosphere.","zh":"哈勃太空望遠鏡是放置在太空中、位於地球大氣層之上觀測宇宙的望遠鏡。"},{"en":"Students may see Hubble images of galaxies, planets, and gas clouds in science lessons.","zh":"學生可能在科學課中看到哈勃拍攝的星系、行星和氣體雲影像。"},{"en":"Because it is above the atmosphere, it can capture clearer images than many ground-based telescopes.","zh":"因為它位於大氣層之上，所以能比許多地面望遠鏡拍攝更清晰影像。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major space telescope.","zh":"這個短語命名一台重要太空望遠鏡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"changed the way that","meaning":"改變……的方式","examples":[{"en":"The Hubble Space Telescope changed the way that astronomers saw the universe.","zh":"哈勃太空望遠鏡改變了天文學家看待宇宙的方式。"},{"en":"Changed the way that means altered how people understood, viewed, or did something.","zh":"改變某事的方式，是指改變人們理解、觀看或做某事的方法。"},{"en":"Online lessons changed the way that many students studied during school closures.","zh":"停課期間，網上課堂改變了許多學生學習的方式。"},{"en":"New tools can change understanding by revealing details people could not see before.","zh":"新工具可以透過揭示以前看不到的細節來改變理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major shift in thinking or practice.","zh":"這個短語描述思維或做法上的重大轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"astronomers","meaning":"天文學家","examples":[{"en":"Astronomers used Hubble to study the universe.","zh":"天文學家使用哈勃研究宇宙。"},{"en":"Astronomers are scientists who study stars, planets, galaxies, and space.","zh":"天文學家是研究星星、行星、星系和太空的科學家。"},{"en":"Astronomers may observe the night sky through telescopes or analyse digital images.","zh":"天文學家可能透過望遠鏡觀察夜空，或分析數碼影像。"},{"en":"Better instruments help astronomers answer deeper questions about the universe.","zh":"更好的儀器幫助天文學家回答更深入的宇宙問題。"},{"en":"This word refers to scientists who study space.","zh":"這個詞指研究太空的科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the universe","meaning":"宇宙","examples":[{"en":"Hubble changed the way astronomers saw the universe.","zh":"哈勃改變了天文學家看待宇宙的方式。"},{"en":"The universe is all of space, time, matter, and energy.","zh":"宇宙是所有空間、時間、物質和能量。"},{"en":"A child may first imagine the universe as stars, planets, and galaxies.","zh":"小孩可能先把宇宙想像成星星、行星和星系。"},{"en":"Studying the universe helps people understand where Earth fits in the larger cosmos.","zh":"研究宇宙幫助人們理解地球在更大宇宙中的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to everything that exists in space and time.","zh":"這個短語指存在於空間和時間中的一切。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"providing detailed digital images","meaning":"提供詳細的數碼影像","examples":[{"en":"Hubble provided detailed digital images of space objects.","zh":"哈勃提供了太空物體的詳細數碼影像。"},{"en":"Providing detailed digital images means giving clear electronic pictures with many visible details.","zh":"提供詳細的數碼影像，是指給出清晰且有許多可見細節的電子圖片。"},{"en":"A hospital scanner provides detailed digital images of the inside of the body.","zh":"醫院掃描儀提供身體內部的詳細數碼影像。"},{"en":"Detailed images help scientists notice features that ordinary pictures miss.","zh":"詳細影像幫助科學家注意到普通圖片看不到的特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes producing useful visual data.","zh":"這個短語描述產生有用的視覺資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"digital images","meaning":"數碼影像","examples":[{"en":"Hubble captured detailed digital images of constellations and planets.","zh":"哈勃捕捉了星座和行星的詳細數碼影像。"},{"en":"Digital images are pictures stored or produced in electronic form.","zh":"數碼影像是以電子形式儲存或產生的圖片。"},{"en":"A student may submit digital images of homework through an online platform.","zh":"學生可能透過網上平台提交功課的數碼影像。"},{"en":"Digital images can be enlarged, shared, and analysed by computers.","zh":"數碼影像可以被放大、分享和由電腦分析。"},{"en":"This phrase describes electronic pictures rather than printed photographs only.","zh":"這個短語描述電子圖片，而不只是印刷照片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"gas clouds","meaning":"氣體雲","examples":[{"en":"Hubble provided images of planets and gas clouds.","zh":"哈勃提供了行星和氣體雲的影像。"},{"en":"Gas clouds are large collections of gas in space.","zh":"氣體雲是太空中大量氣體的集合。"},{"en":"A science lesson may show a colourful gas cloud where stars are forming.","zh":"科學課可能展示一片正在形成星星的彩色氣體雲。"},{"en":"Observing gas clouds helps astronomers study how stars and galaxies develop.","zh":"觀察氣體雲幫助天文學家研究星星和星系如何發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cloud-like regions of gas in space.","zh":"這個短語描述太空中的雲狀氣體區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"had never been seen before","meaning":"以前從未被看見","examples":[{"en":"Hubble showed objects that had never been seen before.","zh":"哈勃展示了以前從未被看見的物體。"},{"en":"Had never been seen before means no one had observed them previously.","zh":"以前從未被看見，是指之前沒有人觀察到。"},{"en":"A new microscope may reveal cells that students had never seen before.","zh":"新顯微鏡可能展示學生以前從未看見的細胞。"},{"en":"New instruments can expand knowledge by showing previously hidden details.","zh":"新儀器可以透過展示以前隱藏的細節來擴展知識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a first observation.","zh":"這個短語描述首次觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"compared to","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Compared to ground-based telescopes, Hubble is not particularly large.","zh":"與地面望遠鏡相比，哈勃並不特別大。"},{"en":"Compared to means when measured or judged against something else.","zh":"與某物相比，是指以另一物作量度或判斷標準。"},{"en":"Compared to a car, a bicycle is cheaper and easier to park.","zh":"與汽車相比，單車較便宜也較容易泊車。"},{"en":"Comparisons help readers understand size, cost, or importance more clearly.","zh":"比較幫助讀者更清楚理解大小、成本或重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the standard used for comparison.","zh":"這個短語引入比較標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ground-based telescopes","meaning":"地面望遠鏡","examples":[{"en":"Ground-based telescopes observe space from Earth.","zh":"地面望遠鏡從地球觀測太空。"},{"en":"Ground-based telescopes are telescopes located on Earth rather than in space.","zh":"地面望遠鏡是位於地球上而不是太空中的望遠鏡。"},{"en":"A mountain observatory may use ground-based telescopes to study stars.","zh":"山上天文台可能使用地面望遠鏡研究星星。"},{"en":"These telescopes can be powerful, but Earth’s atmosphere may blur their images.","zh":"這些望遠鏡可以很強大，但地球大氣可能令其影像模糊。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts Earth-based instruments with space telescopes.","zh":"這個短語把地球上的儀器與太空望遠鏡作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"not particularly large","meaning":"並不特別大","examples":[{"en":"Hubble is not particularly large compared to ground-based telescopes.","zh":"與地面望遠鏡相比，哈勃並不特別大。"},{"en":"Not particularly large means not especially big.","zh":"並不特別大，是指不是特別巨大。"},{"en":"A laptop may be powerful even if it is not particularly large.","zh":"手提電腦即使並不特別大，也可能很強大。"},{"en":"Size is not the only factor that determines performance.","zh":"體積不是決定表現的唯一因素。"},{"en":"This phrase downplays size while leaving room for other strengths.","zh":"這個短語淡化大小，同時保留其他優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"primary mirror diameter","meaning":"主鏡直徑","examples":[{"en":"Hubble has a primary mirror diameter of 2.4 metres.","zh":"哈勃的主鏡直徑為 2.4 米。"},{"en":"Primary mirror diameter is the width across the main mirror of a telescope.","zh":"主鏡直徑是望遠鏡主要鏡面橫跨的寬度。"},{"en":"A larger mirror diameter can help a telescope collect more light.","zh":"較大的鏡面直徑可以幫助望遠鏡收集更多光。"},{"en":"Mirror size affects what a telescope can see, but other technology also matters.","zh":"鏡面大小影響望遠鏡能看見甚麼，但其他科技也重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important measurement of a telescope.","zh":"這個短語描述望遠鏡的重要量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"medium-sized telescope","meaning":"中型望遠鏡","examples":[{"en":"Hubble would be considered a medium-sized telescope on the ground.","zh":"如果在地面上，哈勃會被視為中型望遠鏡。"},{"en":"A medium-sized telescope is neither very small nor among the largest telescopes.","zh":"中型望遠鏡既不是很小，也不是最大型望遠鏡之一。"},{"en":"A school observatory may own a medium-sized telescope for student activities.","zh":"學校天文台可能擁有中型望遠鏡供學生活動使用。"},{"en":"Hubble’s performance is impressive because it is not extremely large.","zh":"哈勃的表現令人印象深刻，因為它並非極大型。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moderate telescope size.","zh":"這個短語描述中等大小的望遠鏡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"on the ground","meaning":"在地面上","examples":[{"en":"Hubble would be medium-sized if it were on the ground.","zh":"如果哈勃在地面上，它會是中型望遠鏡。"},{"en":"On the ground means located on Earth’s surface rather than in the air or space.","zh":"在地面上，是指位於地球表面，而不是空中或太空中。"},{"en":"A satellite dish on the ground receives signals from space.","zh":"地面上的衛星天線接收來自太空的訊號。"},{"en":"A telescope on the ground must look through Earth’s atmosphere.","zh":"地面上的望遠鏡必須透過地球大氣觀測。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts Earth-based location with space-based location.","zh":"這個短語把地球位置與太空位置作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the combination of","meaning":"……的結合","examples":[{"en":"The combination of Hubble’s features makes up for its size.","zh":"哈勃各項特徵的結合彌補了它的體積。"},{"en":"The combination of things means those things working together as a set.","zh":"某些事物的結合，是指那些事物作為一組共同發揮作用。"},{"en":"A good lesson may come from the combination of clear notes, examples, and practice.","zh":"一堂好課可能來自清楚筆記、例子和練習的結合。"},{"en":"Several strengths together can compensate for one weakness.","zh":"幾項優勢加在一起可以彌補一個弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes different elements acting together.","zh":"這個短語描述不同元素共同作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"precision optics","meaning":"精密光學系統","examples":[{"en":"Hubble’s precision optics help it capture detailed images.","zh":"哈勃的精密光學系統幫助它捕捉詳細影像。"},{"en":"Precision optics are highly accurate lenses and mirrors used to control light.","zh":"精密光學系統是用來控制光線的高度準確鏡片和鏡面。"},{"en":"A camera with precision optics can take sharper photos.","zh":"配備精密光學系統的相機可以拍攝更清晰照片。"},{"en":"Accurate optics matter because small errors can blur images.","zh":"準確光學系統很重要，因為小錯誤也會令影像模糊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes carefully engineered light-handling equipment.","zh":"這個短語描述精心工程設計的控光設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"state-of-the-art instrumentation","meaning":"最先進的儀器設備","examples":[{"en":"Hubble uses state-of-the-art instrumentation.","zh":"哈勃使用最先進的儀器設備。"},{"en":"State-of-the-art instrumentation means the most advanced equipment available at the time.","zh":"最先進的儀器設備，是當時可用的最先進設備。"},{"en":"A modern hospital may use state-of-the-art instrumentation for accurate diagnosis.","zh":"現代醫院可能使用最先進的儀器設備進行準確診斷。"},{"en":"Advanced instruments can improve results even when the main machine is not the largest.","zh":"先進儀器即使在主機不是最大時，也能改善結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cutting-edge technical equipment.","zh":"這個短語描述尖端技術設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unprecedented pointing stability","meaning":"前所未有的指向穩定性","examples":[{"en":"Hubble has unprecedented pointing stability and control.","zh":"哈勃具有前所未有的指向穩定性和控制。"},{"en":"Unprecedented pointing stability means an unusually high ability to stay aimed at a target without shaking.","zh":"前所未有的指向穩定性，是指能異常穩定地對準目標而不晃動。"},{"en":"A photographer needs camera stability to take a clear picture of a distant object.","zh":"攝影師需要相機穩定性，才能拍攝遠處物體的清晰照片。"},{"en":"Better pointing stability helps a telescope collect clearer images over time.","zh":"更好的指向穩定性幫助望遠鏡長時間收集更清晰影像。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an exceptional ability to aim steadily.","zh":"這個短語描述異常穩定瞄準的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"make up for","meaning":"彌補……","examples":[{"en":"Hubble’s technology makes up for its lack of size.","zh":"哈勃的科技彌補了它的體積不足。"},{"en":"To make up for something means to compensate for a weakness or loss.","zh":"彌補某事，是指補償某個弱點或損失。"},{"en":"A student may make up for weak spelling by checking every word carefully.","zh":"學生可能透過仔細檢查每個字來彌補拼字較弱。"},{"en":"Strong technology can compensate when size is not the main advantage.","zh":"當體積不是主要優勢時，強大科技可以作出補償。"},{"en":"This phrase describes balancing a disadvantage with another strength.","zh":"這個短語描述用另一項優勢平衡缺點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lack of size","meaning":"體積不足","examples":[{"en":"Hubble’s precision makes up for its lack of size.","zh":"哈勃的精密度彌補了它的體積不足。"},{"en":"Lack of size means not being large enough or not being as large as others.","zh":"體積不足，是指不夠大或不如其他同類大。"},{"en":"A small shop may make up for its lack of size by offering excellent service.","zh":"小商店可以透過優秀服務彌補其體積不足。"},{"en":"A weakness in size can be offset by quality, accuracy, or location.","zh":"大小上的弱點可以由質素、準確度或位置抵消。"},{"en":"This phrase describes smallness as a possible limitation.","zh":"這個短語描述體積小作為可能限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a range of","meaning":"……的範圍","examples":[{"en":"Hubble has a range of well over 12 billion light-years.","zh":"哈勃有遠超過 120 億光年的觀測範圍。"},{"en":"A range of something means the distance, extent, or variety it can cover.","zh":"某物的範圍，是指它能覆蓋的距離、程度或種類。"},{"en":"A walkie-talkie may have a range of several kilometres.","zh":"對講機可能有幾公里的範圍。"},{"en":"A greater range allows an instrument to reach or observe more distant targets.","zh":"更大範圍讓儀器能到達或觀察更遙遠目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how far or how widely something can operate.","zh":"這個短語描述某物能運作多遠或多廣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"well over","meaning":"遠超過","examples":[{"en":"Hubble has a range of well over 12 billion light-years.","zh":"哈勃的觀測範圍遠超過 120 億光年。"},{"en":"Well over means much more than a stated amount.","zh":"遠超過，是指大大多於所說數量。"},{"en":"The school library has well over ten thousand books.","zh":"學校圖書館藏書遠超過一萬本。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the number is not just slightly above the figure.","zh":"這個短語強調數字不是只略高於該數。"},{"en":"It is useful when stressing a very large amount.","zh":"它適合強調非常大的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"light-years","meaning":"光年","examples":[{"en":"Hubble can observe objects more than 12 billion light-years away.","zh":"哈勃可以觀察超過 120 億光年外的物體。"},{"en":"Light-years are units of distance based on how far light travels in one year.","zh":"光年是距離單位，基於光一年所行走的距離。"},{"en":"A star may be many light-years from Earth, so its light takes years to reach us.","zh":"一顆星可能距離地球許多光年，所以其光需要多年才到達我們。"},{"en":"Astronomers use light-years because space distances are extremely large.","zh":"天文學家使用光年，因為太空距離極其巨大。"},{"en":"This word measures distance, not time in ordinary usage.","zh":"這個詞量度距離，而不是普通用法中的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"location above","meaning":"位於……之上的位置","examples":[{"en":"The telescope’s location above the Earth’s atmosphere has advantages.","zh":"望遠鏡位於地球大氣層之上的位置有優勢。"},{"en":"Location above something means being positioned higher than it.","zh":"位於某物之上的位置，是指處於比它更高的位置。"},{"en":"A security camera’s location above a shop entrance gives it a better view.","zh":"保安攝影機位於商店入口之上的位置，能提供更好視野。"},{"en":"Being above the atmosphere helps Hubble avoid atmospheric distortion.","zh":"位於大氣層之上幫助哈勃避開大氣扭曲。"},{"en":"This phrase connects position with advantage.","zh":"這個短語把位置與優勢連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Earth’s atmosphere","meaning":"地球大氣層","examples":[{"en":"Hubble operates above the Earth’s atmosphere.","zh":"哈勃在地球大氣層之上運作。"},{"en":"Earth’s atmosphere is the layer of gases surrounding our planet.","zh":"地球大氣層是包圍我們星球的氣體層。"},{"en":"Weather happens in Earth’s atmosphere.","zh":"天氣發生在地球大氣層中。"},{"en":"The atmosphere protects life but can interfere with astronomical observation.","zh":"大氣層保護生命，但可能干擾天文觀測。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the gaseous layer around Earth.","zh":"這個短語指地球周圍的氣體層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"significant advantages over","meaning":"相比……有顯著優勢","examples":[{"en":"Hubble has significant advantages over land-based telescopes.","zh":"哈勃相比陸基望遠鏡有顯著優勢。"},{"en":"Significant advantages over something are important benefits compared with it.","zh":"相比某物有顯著優勢，是指與它比較時有重要好處。"},{"en":"Online booking has significant advantages over phone booking because users can see available times instantly.","zh":"網上預約相比電話預約有顯著優勢，因為用戶能即時看到可用時間。"},{"en":"Hubble’s position above the atmosphere gives it clearer observation conditions.","zh":"哈勃位於大氣層之上，令它有更清晰的觀測條件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaningful superiority in certain respects.","zh":"這個短語描述在某些方面有有意義的優越性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"land-based telescopes","meaning":"陸基望遠鏡；地面望遠鏡","examples":[{"en":"Land-based telescopes are affected by the Earth’s atmosphere.","zh":"陸基望遠鏡受地球大氣層影響。"},{"en":"Land-based telescopes are telescopes located on Earth’s surface.","zh":"陸基望遠鏡是位於地球表面的望遠鏡。"},{"en":"A desert observatory may use land-based telescopes because dry air improves visibility.","zh":"沙漠天文台可能使用陸基望遠鏡，因為乾燥空氣改善能見度。"},{"en":"Even strong land-based telescopes must look through the atmosphere.","zh":"即使強大的陸基望遠鏡也必須透過大氣層觀測。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts telescopes on Earth with telescopes in space.","zh":"這個短語把地球上的望遠鏡與太空望遠鏡作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"bends light","meaning":"使光線彎曲","examples":[{"en":"The atmosphere bends light because of diffraction.","zh":"大氣層因衍射而使光線彎曲。"},{"en":"Bends light means changes the direction of light as it travels.","zh":"使光線彎曲，是指改變光線行進方向。"},{"en":"A glass of water can bend light and make a straw look broken.","zh":"一杯水可以使光線彎曲，令飲管看起來像折斷。"},{"en":"When light bends, images may appear less clear.","zh":"當光線彎曲，影像可能顯得較不清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical effect on light.","zh":"這個短語描述對光線的物理影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"due to","meaning":"由於","examples":[{"en":"The atmosphere bends light due to diffraction.","zh":"大氣層由於衍射而使光線彎曲。"},{"en":"Due to means because of.","zh":"due to 意思是「由於」。"},{"en":"The outdoor lesson was cancelled due to bad weather.","zh":"戶外課堂由於天氣惡劣而取消。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the cause of a result.","zh":"這個短語引入結果的原因。"},{"en":"It is often used in formal explanations.","zh":"它常用於正式解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"phenomenon known as","meaning":"被稱為……的現象","examples":[{"en":"Diffraction is a phenomenon known to affect starlight.","zh":"衍射是一種已知會影響星光的現象。"},{"en":"A phenomenon known as something is an observed event or process with that name.","zh":"被稱為某事的現象，是指有該名稱的可觀察事件或過程。"},{"en":"The feeling of panic before speaking may be a phenomenon known as stage fright.","zh":"演講前的恐慌感可能是一種被稱為怯場的現象。"},{"en":"Naming a phenomenon helps people discuss and study it clearly.","zh":"命名現象幫助人們清楚討論和研究它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the name of an observed effect.","zh":"這個短語引入可觀察效應的名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"diffraction","meaning":"衍射","examples":[{"en":"Diffraction causes starlight to appear to twinkle.","zh":"衍射令星光看起來閃爍。"},{"en":"Diffraction is the bending or spreading of light as it passes through or around something.","zh":"衍射是光線穿過或繞過某物時發生的彎曲或擴散。"},{"en":"A science teacher may demonstrate diffraction with light passing through a narrow opening.","zh":"科學老師可能用光穿過窄縫來示範衍射。"},{"en":"Diffraction can make astronomical images less sharp when seen through the atmosphere.","zh":"透過大氣層觀看時，衍射可以令天文影像較不銳利。"},{"en":"This word describes a light-related physical effect.","zh":"這個詞描述與光有關的物理效應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"starlight","meaning":"星光","examples":[{"en":"Diffraction causes starlight to appear to twinkle.","zh":"衍射令星光看起來閃爍。"},{"en":"Starlight is light that comes from stars.","zh":"星光是來自星星的光。"},{"en":"On a clear night, campers may sit quietly and watch starlight above them.","zh":"在晴朗夜晚，露營者可能安靜坐着觀看頭頂星光。"},{"en":"Starlight travels enormous distances before reaching Earth.","zh":"星光在到達地球前行走極其遙遠的距離。"},{"en":"This word refers to light produced by stars.","zh":"這個詞指星星產生的光。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"appear to twinkle","meaning":"看起來閃爍","examples":[{"en":"Starlight appears to twinkle because of diffraction.","zh":"星光因衍射而看起來閃爍。"},{"en":"Appear to twinkle means seem to shine with small changes in brightness.","zh":"看起來閃爍，是指似乎亮度有細微變化地發光。"},{"en":"Distant city lights may appear to twinkle on a hot evening.","zh":"炎熱晚上，遠處城市燈光可能看起來閃爍。"},{"en":"Twinkling happens because light is disturbed before it reaches the observer.","zh":"閃爍發生，是因為光線到達觀察者前受到干擾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how stars seem to flicker in the night sky.","zh":"這個短語描述星星在夜空中似乎忽明忽暗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"leads to","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"Diffraction leads to blurred images through ground-based telescopes.","zh":"衍射導致透過地面望遠鏡看到模糊影像。"},{"en":"Leads to means causes or results in something.","zh":"導致，是指造成或引起某結果。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can lead to poor concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致上課專注力差。"},{"en":"When one process leads to a problem, understanding the cause can help fix it.","zh":"當一個過程導致問題，理解原因可以幫助解決。"},{"en":"This phrase connects cause and result.","zh":"這個短語連接原因和結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"blurred images","meaning":"模糊影像","examples":[{"en":"Ground-based telescopes may produce blurred images.","zh":"地面望遠鏡可能產生模糊影像。"},{"en":"Blurred images are pictures that are unclear or not sharp.","zh":"模糊影像是不清楚或不銳利的圖片。"},{"en":"A moving hand in a photo may create a blurred image.","zh":"照片中移動的手可能造成模糊影像。"},{"en":"In astronomy, blurred images make it harder to see fine details.","zh":"在天文學中，模糊影像令人更難看見細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unclear visual results.","zh":"這個短語描述不清晰的視覺結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"seen through","meaning":"透過……看到","examples":[{"en":"Blurred images are often seen through ground-based telescopes.","zh":"模糊影像經常透過地面望遠鏡看到。"},{"en":"Seen through something means observed by using it as a viewing tool or medium.","zh":"透過某物看到，是指使用它作為觀看工具或媒介來觀察。"},{"en":"Tiny cells can be seen through a microscope.","zh":"微小細胞可以透過顯微鏡看到。"},{"en":"What is seen through an instrument depends on the instrument’s quality and conditions.","zh":"透過儀器看到甚麼，取決於儀器質素和條件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the tool or medium used for viewing.","zh":"這個短語描述用來觀看的工具或媒介。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"observe infrared light","meaning":"觀測紅外線","examples":[{"en":"The Hubble Space Telescope can observe infrared light.","zh":"哈勃太空望遠鏡可以觀測紅外線。"},{"en":"To observe infrared light means to detect and study light beyond the visible red end of the spectrum.","zh":"觀測紅外線，是指偵測和研究可見紅光之外的光。"},{"en":"Special cameras can observe infrared light to detect heat at night.","zh":"特殊相機可以觀測紅外線，以在夜間偵測熱量。"},{"en":"Observing infrared light can reveal objects hidden from ordinary visible-light images.","zh":"觀測紅外線可以揭示普通可見光影像中隱藏的物體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes detecting a type of light humans cannot normally see.","zh":"這個短語描述偵測人類通常看不到的一種光。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"infrared light","meaning":"紅外線","examples":[{"en":"Infrared light would otherwise be blocked by the atmosphere.","zh":"紅外線否則會被大氣層阻擋。"},{"en":"Infrared light is light beyond red light that humans cannot normally see.","zh":"紅外線是紅光之外、人類通常看不到的光。"},{"en":"A thermal camera uses infrared light to show warm and cool areas.","zh":"熱能相機使用紅外線顯示溫暖和寒冷區域。"},{"en":"Some infrared light from space does not reach Earth’s surface because of the atmosphere.","zh":"來自太空的部分紅外線因大氣層而不能到達地球表面。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an invisible form of light useful in astronomy.","zh":"這個短語指一種對天文學有用的不可見光。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"would otherwise be blocked","meaning":"否則會被阻擋","examples":[{"en":"Infrared light would otherwise be blocked by the atmosphere.","zh":"紅外線否則會被大氣層阻擋。"},{"en":"Would otherwise be blocked means would be prevented from passing if the special condition did not exist.","zh":"否則會被阻擋，是指如果沒有特殊條件，它就會被阻止通過。"},{"en":"A message would otherwise be blocked by spam filters if the sender were not approved.","zh":"如果寄件人未獲批准，訊息否則會被垃圾郵件過濾器阻擋。"},{"en":"Being above the atmosphere lets Hubble receive light that ground instruments may miss.","zh":"位於大氣層之上讓哈勃接收到地面儀器可能錯過的光。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what would happen without an advantage or exception.","zh":"這個短語解釋如果沒有優勢或例外會發生甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"blocked by the atmosphere","meaning":"被大氣層阻擋","examples":[{"en":"Some infrared light is blocked by the atmosphere.","zh":"部分紅外線被大氣層阻擋。"},{"en":"Blocked by the atmosphere means prevented from passing through Earth’s gaseous layer.","zh":"被大氣層阻擋，是指被地球氣體層阻止通過。"},{"en":"Some sunlight is filtered or blocked by clouds and air particles.","zh":"部分陽光會被雲和空氣粒子過濾或阻擋。"},{"en":"If light is blocked, telescopes on the ground cannot fully detect it.","zh":"如果光線被阻擋，地面望遠鏡就不能完全偵測到它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes atmospheric interference with incoming light.","zh":"這個短語描述大氣對入射光的干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"despite early setbacks","meaning":"儘管早期遇上挫折","examples":[{"en":"Despite early setbacks, Hubble renewed public interest in space.","zh":"儘管早期遇上挫折，哈勃重新激發了公眾對太空的興趣。"},{"en":"Despite early setbacks means although there were problems at the beginning.","zh":"儘管早期遇上挫折，是指雖然一開始有問題。"},{"en":"Despite early setbacks, a student may still improve greatly by the end of the year.","zh":"儘管早期遇上挫折，學生到學年末仍可能大幅進步。"},{"en":"Early problems do not always prevent long-term success.","zh":"早期問題不一定阻止長期成功。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts initial difficulty with later achievement.","zh":"這個短語把初期困難與後來成就作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"early setbacks","meaning":"早期挫折","examples":[{"en":"Hubble experienced early setbacks after launch.","zh":"哈勃發射後經歷早期挫折。"},{"en":"Early setbacks are problems or failures that happen near the beginning of a project.","zh":"早期挫折是在項目初期發生的問題或失敗。"},{"en":"A new restaurant may face early setbacks if staff training is poor.","zh":"如果員工培訓不足，新餐廳可能面對早期挫折。"},{"en":"Setbacks can delay progress, but they can also be fixed with better planning.","zh":"挫折可以延誤進展，但也可以透過更好規劃修正。"},{"en":"This phrase describes initial difficulties.","zh":"這個短語描述初期困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reflective mirrors","meaning":"反射鏡","examples":[{"en":"One of Hubble’s reflective mirrors had to be replaced.","zh":"哈勃其中一塊反射鏡必須被更換。"},{"en":"Reflective mirrors are mirrors that reflect light for instruments such as telescopes.","zh":"反射鏡是為望遠鏡等儀器反射光線的鏡面。"},{"en":"A telescope uses mirrors to gather and direct light from distant objects.","zh":"望遠鏡使用鏡面收集並引導來自遙遠物體的光。"},{"en":"If a mirror is imperfect, the image may be unclear.","zh":"如果鏡面有缺陷，影像可能不清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes key optical parts of a telescope.","zh":"這個短語描述望遠鏡的重要光學部件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"had to be replaced","meaning":"必須被更換","examples":[{"en":"One reflective mirror had to be replaced after a problem was found.","zh":"發現問題後，一塊反射鏡必須被更換。"},{"en":"Had to be replaced means needed to be removed and changed for another one.","zh":"必須被更換，是指需要被移除並換成另一個。"},{"en":"A cracked classroom window had to be replaced before winter.","zh":"破裂課室窗戶在冬天前必須被更換。"},{"en":"Replacement becomes necessary when a part cannot perform its job properly.","zh":"當某部分不能正常發揮作用，更換就變得必要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unavoidable change of a faulty part.","zh":"這個短語描述有缺陷部件不可避免地被替換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"ground incorrectly","meaning":"被錯誤研磨","examples":[{"en":"The mirror had been ground incorrectly.","zh":"該鏡面被錯誤研磨。"},{"en":"Ground incorrectly means shaped or polished in the wrong way.","zh":"被錯誤研磨，是指以錯誤方式成形或拋光。"},{"en":"A lens ground incorrectly may make a pair of glasses unclear.","zh":"被錯誤研磨的鏡片可能令眼鏡看不清楚。"},{"en":"A tiny manufacturing error can seriously affect a precision instrument.","zh":"微小製造錯誤可以嚴重影響精密儀器。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an error in shaping an optical surface.","zh":"這個短語描述光學表面成形錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"did not produce the images expected","meaning":"未能產生預期影像","examples":[{"en":"The faulty mirror did not produce the images expected.","zh":"有問題的鏡面未能產生預期影像。"},{"en":"Did not produce the images expected means failed to create the quality or type of pictures people had planned for.","zh":"未能產生預期影像，是指沒有製造出人們原本計劃的圖片質素或類型。"},{"en":"A damaged camera lens may not produce the clear photos expected.","zh":"受損相機鏡頭可能未能產生預期的清晰照片。"},{"en":"When results fall short of expectations, engineers must find and fix the cause.","zh":"當結果不符期望，工程師必須找出並修正原因。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disappointing output from a faulty instrument.","zh":"這個短語描述有缺陷儀器帶來令人失望的輸出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reignited interest in","meaning":"重新激發對……的興趣","examples":[{"en":"The telescope reignited interest in space among the public.","zh":"這台望遠鏡重新激發公眾對太空的興趣。"},{"en":"To reignite interest in something means to make people interested in it again.","zh":"重新激發對某事的興趣，是指令 人們再次對它感興趣。"},{"en":"A successful school concert may reignite interest in music lessons.","zh":"成功的學校音樂會可能重新激發學生對音樂課的興趣。"},{"en":"Beautiful images from Hubble made space feel exciting to ordinary people again.","zh":"哈勃拍攝的美麗影像令太空對普通人再次變得令人興奮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bringing back attention and enthusiasm.","zh":"這個短語描述重新帶回注意力和熱情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"amongst the general public","meaning":"在普羅大眾之中","examples":[{"en":"Hubble reignited interest in space amongst the general public.","zh":"哈勃在普羅大眾之中重新激發對太空的興趣。"},{"en":"Amongst the general public means among ordinary people rather than specialists.","zh":"在普羅大眾之中，是指在普通人之中，而不是在專家之中。"},{"en":"A health campaign may raise awareness amongst the general public.","zh":"健康宣傳活動可能在普羅大眾之中提高意識。"},{"en":"Public interest matters when taxpayers help fund scientific projects.","zh":"當納稅人資助科學項目，公眾興趣就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broad non-specialist audience.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛的非專業受眾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"an important outcome","meaning":"重要成果","examples":[{"en":"Public interest was an important outcome of the Hubble project.","zh":"公眾興趣是哈勃項目的一項重要成果。"},{"en":"An important outcome is a significant result of an action or event.","zh":"重要成果是行動或事件帶來的重大結果。"},{"en":"Better student confidence can be an important outcome of a speaking course.","zh":"學生信心提升可以是口語課程的重要成果。"},{"en":"Outcomes matter because they show what a project actually achieved.","zh":"成果很重要，因為它們顯示項目實際達成了甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a meaningful result.","zh":"這個短語描述有意義的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"given that","meaning":"鑑於；考慮到","examples":[{"en":"This was important, given that taxpayers funded the telescope.","zh":"這一點很重要，鑑於納稅人資助了這台望遠鏡。"},{"en":"Given that means considering the fact that.","zh":"鑑於，是指考慮到某個事實。"},{"en":"Given that students have exams next week, the teacher gave them revision time.","zh":"考慮到學生下星期有考試，老師給他們溫習時間。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a fact that explains why something matters.","zh":"這個短語引入一個解釋某事為何重要的事實。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving a reason based on context.","zh":"它適合根據語境給出原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"taxpayers","meaning":"納稅人","examples":[{"en":"Taxpayers funded the telescope’s research and maintenance.","zh":"納稅人資助了望遠鏡的研究和維護。"},{"en":"Taxpayers are people or organisations that pay taxes to the government.","zh":"納稅人是向政府繳稅的個人或機構。"},{"en":"Taxpayers help fund public services such as schools, hospitals, and roads.","zh":"納稅人幫助資助學校、醫院和道路等公共服務。"},{"en":"If taxpayers fund a project, the public may expect visible benefits or results.","zh":"如果納稅人資助項目，公眾可能期望看到明顯好處或成果。"},{"en":"This word refers to those whose taxes support public spending.","zh":"這個詞指以稅款支持公共開支的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"funded","meaning":"資助；提供資金","examples":[{"en":"Taxpayers funded the telescope’s research, deployment and maintenance.","zh":"納稅人資助了望遠鏡的研究、部署和維護。"},{"en":"Funded means paid for or provided money for something.","zh":"資助，是指為某事支付費用或提供金錢。"},{"en":"A scholarship may be funded by former students of a school.","zh":"獎學金可能由學校舊生資助。"},{"en":"Funding makes expensive research possible, but it also creates responsibility to show value.","zh":"資金令昂貴研究成為可能，但也帶來展示價值的責任。"},{"en":"This word describes providing financial support.","zh":"這個詞描述提供財政支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"research, deployment and maintenance","meaning":"研究、部署和維護","examples":[{"en":"Taxpayers funded Hubble’s research, deployment and maintenance.","zh":"納稅人資助了哈勃的研究、部署和維護。"},{"en":"Research, deployment and maintenance mean studying, putting into use, and keeping something working.","zh":"研究、部署和維護，是指研究、投入使用，以及保持某物運作。"},{"en":"A school computer system needs research before purchase, deployment in classrooms, and maintenance afterward.","zh":"學校電腦系統需要購買前研究、在課室部署，以及之後維護。"},{"en":"Large technology projects cost money before, during, and after launch.","zh":"大型科技項目在發射前、期間和之後都需要金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes several stages of a technical project.","zh":"這個短語描述技術項目的幾個階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct heading for each paragraph.","zh":"學生為每段選出正確標題。"},{"en":"To choose the correct heading means to select the title that best summarises a paragraph.","zh":"選出正確標題，是指選擇最能概括段落的題目。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may choose a heading after identifying the paragraph’s main idea.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能先找出段落主旨，再選標題。"},{"en":"Choosing headings tests whether students understand overall meaning, not just keywords.","zh":"選標題測試學生是否理解整體意思，而不只是關鍵字。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The list of headings contains more options than needed.","zh":"標題列表包含多於所需的選項。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a set of possible paragraph titles.","zh":"標題列表是一組可能的段落標題。"},{"en":"Students should read all headings before matching them to paragraphs.","zh":"學生應先閱讀所有標題，再把它們配對至段落。"},{"en":"Extra headings make the task harder because some choices are distractors.","zh":"額外標題令題目更難，因為有些選項是干擾項。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the answer options in a heading-matching task.","zh":"這個短語指標題配對題中的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"write the correct number","meaning":"寫上正確編號","examples":[{"en":"Students write the correct number in the answer boxes.","zh":"學生在答案格寫上正確編號。"},{"en":"To write the correct number means to record the number that matches the chosen answer.","zh":"寫上正確編號，是指記錄與所選答案相配的號碼。"},{"en":"In a matching task, students may write Roman numerals instead of words.","zh":"在配對題中，學生可能寫羅馬數字而不是文字。"},{"en":"Accurate answer transfer matters because a correct idea in the wrong box may lose marks.","zh":"準確填寫答案很重要，因為正確想法放錯格也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how candidates should record their answers.","zh":"這個短語描述考生應如何記錄答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"formal marking of constellations","meaning":"星座的正式劃定","examples":[{"en":"One heading refers to the formal marking of constellations.","zh":"一個標題提到星座的正式劃定。"},{"en":"Formal marking of constellations means officially setting their names, areas, or boundaries.","zh":"星座的正式劃定，是指官方設定其名稱、區域或邊界。"},{"en":"A city may formally mark district boundaries on an official map.","zh":"城市可能在官方地圖上正式劃定地區邊界。"},{"en":"Formal marking reduces confusion by giving everyone the same reference system.","zh":"正式劃定透過給每個人相同參照系統來減少混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official definition or boundary-setting.","zh":"這個短語描述官方定義或邊界設定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"different interpretations of","meaning":"對……的不同詮釋","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses different interpretations of star groupings.","zh":"篇章討論對星群的不同詮釋。"},{"en":"Different interpretations of something are different ways of understanding or explaining it.","zh":"對某事的不同詮釋，是指理解或解釋它的不同方式。"},{"en":"Students may have different interpretations of a poem after reading it.","zh":"學生讀完詩後，可能對它有不同詮釋。"},{"en":"Cultural background can create different interpretations of the same stars.","zh":"文化背景可以為同一批星星創造不同詮釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes varied meanings given to one thing.","zh":"這個短語描述賦予同一事物的不同意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"star groupings","meaning":"星群；星星組合","examples":[{"en":"Different cultures interpret star groupings in different ways.","zh":"不同文化以不同方式詮釋星群。"},{"en":"Star groupings are sets of stars considered together as patterns or categories.","zh":"星群是被一起視為圖案或類別的星星組合。"},{"en":"A beginner may first learn simple star groupings before studying official constellations.","zh":"初學者可能先學簡單星群，再研究官方星座。"},{"en":"Groupings help people organise the crowded night sky.","zh":"星群幫助人們整理繁多的夜空。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stars treated as connected sets.","zh":"這個短語描述被視為相連集合的星星。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"historical and modern reference","meaning":"歷史及現代參照","examples":[{"en":"One heading refers to historical and modern reference systems.","zh":"一個標題提到歷史及現代參照系統。"},{"en":"Historical and modern reference means older and current systems used to locate or describe things.","zh":"歷史及現代參照，是指用來定位或描述事物的舊有和現行系統。"},{"en":"A museum map may show both historical and modern references for street names.","zh":"博物館地圖可能同時顯示街名的歷史和現代參照。"},{"en":"Comparing old and new systems helps explain how knowledge developed.","zh":"比較新舊系統有助解釋知識如何發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reference systems from different periods.","zh":"這個短語描述不同時期的參照系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"common misconceptions","meaning":"常見誤解","examples":[{"en":"The paragraph about asterisms discusses common misconceptions.","zh":"關於星群的段落討論常見誤解。"},{"en":"Common misconceptions are wrong ideas that many people believe.","zh":"常見誤解是許多人相信的錯誤想法。"},{"en":"A common misconception is that all bats are blind.","zh":"一個常見誤解是所有蝙蝠都是盲的。"},{"en":"Misconceptions happen when everyday language differs from technical facts.","zh":"當日常語言與技術事實不同，誤解就會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes widespread misunderstanding.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛存在的誤會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"different methods of locating","meaning":"定位的不同方法","examples":[{"en":"The coordinate systems are different methods of locating stars.","zh":"座標系統是定位星星的不同方法。"},{"en":"Different methods of locating something are different ways to find or identify its position.","zh":"定位某物的不同方法，是尋找或辨認其位置的不同方式。"},{"en":"A phone, a paper map, and street signs are different methods of locating a shop.","zh":"手機、紙本地圖和街道路牌都是定位商店的不同方法。"},{"en":"Astronomers need location methods because stars are spread across a vast sky.","zh":"天文學家需要定位方法，因為星星散佈在廣闊天空中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes alternative ways to find position.","zh":"這個短語描述尋找位置的不同方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"identifying","meaning":"辨認；識別","examples":[{"en":"Coordinate systems help with locating and identifying stars.","zh":"座標系統幫助定位和辨認星星。"},{"en":"Identifying means recognising what something is or naming it correctly.","zh":"辨認，是指認出某物是甚麼或正確命名它。"},{"en":"A teacher may help students identify the main idea of a paragraph.","zh":"老師可能幫助學生辨認段落主旨。"},{"en":"Accurate identification prevents confusion between similar objects.","zh":"準確識別可以避免混淆相似物件。"},{"en":"This word describes recognising and naming something.","zh":"這個詞描述認出並命名某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a better view of","meaning":"對……有更清晰的觀察","examples":[{"en":"Hubble gives astronomers a better view of constellations and space.","zh":"哈勃讓天文學家對星座和太空有更清晰的觀察。"},{"en":"A better view of something means a clearer or more useful way of seeing it.","zh":"對某物有更清晰的觀察，是指以更清楚或更有用的方式看見它。"},{"en":"Sitting near the front gives students a better view of the board.","zh":"坐在前排讓學生更清楚看見黑板。"},{"en":"Better views help people notice details that were previously hidden.","zh":"更清晰觀察幫助人注意到以前隱藏的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improved visual access or understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺接觸或理解上的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"bypassing terrestrial limitations","meaning":"繞過地球上的限制","examples":[{"en":"Hubble bypasses terrestrial limitations by operating above the atmosphere.","zh":"哈勃透過在大氣層之上運作，繞過地球上的限制。"},{"en":"Bypassing terrestrial limitations means avoiding problems caused by conditions on Earth.","zh":"繞過地球上的限制，是指避開由地球環境造成的問題。"},{"en":"Online banking bypasses some limitations of visiting a branch during office hours.","zh":"網上銀行繞過了必須在辦公時間到分行的一些限制。"},{"en":"Hubble avoids atmospheric distortion because it is not located on the ground.","zh":"哈勃因不位於地面而避開大氣扭曲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes avoiding Earth-based restrictions.","zh":"這個短語描述避開地球環境限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"terrestrial limitations","meaning":"地球環境限制","examples":[{"en":"Ground-based telescopes suffer from terrestrial limitations.","zh":"地面望遠鏡受地球環境限制影響。"},{"en":"Terrestrial limitations are restrictions caused by being on Earth.","zh":"地球環境限制，是因位於地球上而產生的限制。"},{"en":"A radio signal may face terrestrial limitations such as mountains and tall buildings.","zh":"無線電訊號可能面對山脈和高樓等地球環境限制。"},{"en":"For telescopes, Earth’s atmosphere is a major terrestrial limitation.","zh":"對望遠鏡而言，地球大氣是主要地球環境限制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes Earth-based barriers.","zh":"這個短語描述地球上的障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"renewed interest in","meaning":"對……重新產生興趣","examples":[{"en":"Hubble created renewed interest in the stars.","zh":"哈勃令大眾對星星重新產生興趣。"},{"en":"Renewed interest in something means fresh attention or excitement about it after a period of less interest.","zh":"對某事重新產生興趣，是指在一段興趣減少後重新有注意或興奮感。"},{"en":"A new film may create renewed interest in a classic novel.","zh":"新電影可能令大眾對經典小說重新產生興趣。"},{"en":"Clear images from Hubble made the public excited about space again.","zh":"哈勃的清晰影像令公眾再次對太空感到興奮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes interest being brought back.","zh":"這個短語描述興趣被重新帶回。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"technological advances","meaning":"科技進步","examples":[{"en":"Hubble represents technological advances in astronomical observation.","zh":"哈勃代表天文觀測中的科技進步。"},{"en":"Technological advances are improvements in tools, machines, or scientific methods.","zh":"科技進步是工具、機器或科學方法上的改善。"},{"en":"Smartphones show technological advances in communication and photography.","zh":"智能手機顯示通訊和攝影方面的科技進步。"},{"en":"Advances can allow people to do things that were previously impossible.","zh":"進步可以讓人做到以前不可能的事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes progress in technology.","zh":"這個短語描述科技上的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"research and development","meaning":"研究與開發","examples":[{"en":"Technological advances support research and development.","zh":"科技進步支持研究與開發。"},{"en":"Research and development means studying problems and creating new or improved solutions.","zh":"研究與開發，是研究問題並創造新的或改良的解決方案。"},{"en":"A company may invest in research and development before launching a new product.","zh":"公司可能在推出新產品前投資研究與開發。"},{"en":"Better technology often comes from years of research and testing.","zh":"更好的科技通常來自多年研究和測試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of discovery and improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述發現和改進的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"ethnic differences","meaning":"種族／民族差異","examples":[{"en":"Some headings mention ethnic differences in celestial mapping.","zh":"有些標題提到天體繪圖中的種族／民族差異。"},{"en":"Ethnic differences are differences connected with cultural or people-group traditions.","zh":"種族／民族差異是與文化或族群傳統相關的差異。"},{"en":"Food customs may show ethnic differences within the same city.","zh":"同一城市中的飲食習俗可能顯示民族差異。"},{"en":"In star mapping, different groups may preserve different names and myths.","zh":"在星空繪圖中，不同群體可能保留不同名稱和神話。"},{"en":"This phrase describes differences linked with cultural identity.","zh":"這個短語描述與文化身份相關的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"celestial mapping","meaning":"天體繪圖；天體分佈圖","examples":[{"en":"Different cultures developed different systems of celestial mapping.","zh":"不同文化發展了不同的天體繪圖系統。"},{"en":"Celestial mapping means creating systems or maps for locating objects in the sky.","zh":"天體繪圖，是建立系統或地圖來定位天空物體。"},{"en":"A planetarium show may introduce children to celestial mapping through star charts.","zh":"天文館節目可能透過星圖向孩子介紹天體繪圖。"},{"en":"Mapping the sky helps people organise stars into meaningful patterns and positions.","zh":"繪製天空幫助人們把星星整理成有意義的圖案和位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes charting the heavens.","zh":"這個短語描述繪製天體分佈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"universal myths","meaning":"普遍存在的神話","examples":[{"en":"Many cultures have myths about constellations.","zh":"許多文化都有關於星座的神話。"},{"en":"Universal myths are stories or mythic themes found across many cultures.","zh":"普遍存在的神話，是在許多文化中都出現的故事或神話主題。"},{"en":"Flood stories may be treated as universal myths because similar versions appear in different societies.","zh":"洪水故事可能被視為普遍存在的神話，因為不同社會中有相似版本。"},{"en":"Star myths feel universal when many cultures connect the sky with gods, heroes, or animals.","zh":"當許多文化都把天空與神、英雄或動物連接，星空神話就顯得普遍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes myths that appear widely across cultures.","zh":"這個短語描述跨文化廣泛出現的神話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"complete the summary below","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary below using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"Complete the summary below means fill in missing words in the short text provided under the question.","zh":"完成以下摘要，是指填上題目下方短文中的缺失字詞。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete the summary after finding key information in the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生在篇章中找到關鍵資料後完成摘要。"},{"en":"This task checks whether students understand main ideas and exact wording.","zh":"這項任務檢查學生是否理解主旨和準確用字。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should use no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案應使用不多於兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer may contain one or two words only.","zh":"不多於兩個字，是指答案只可包含一個或兩個英文詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “gas clouds,” it follows the rule because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “gas clouds”，它符合規則，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing three words may be wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫三個詞也可能錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"initial flaw","meaning":"初期缺陷","examples":[{"en":"Hubble had an initial flaw in one of its mirrors.","zh":"哈勃其中一塊鏡面有初期缺陷。"},{"en":"An initial flaw is a problem or defect present at the beginning.","zh":"初期缺陷是在一開始就存在的問題或瑕疵。"},{"en":"A new app may have an initial flaw that causes it to crash on some phones.","zh":"新應用程式可能有初期缺陷，導致它在某些手機上當機。"},{"en":"Early flaws can damage performance until they are corrected.","zh":"早期缺陷在被修正前可以損害表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a starting defect.","zh":"這個短語描述起始階段的缺陷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"superior to","meaning":"優於……","examples":[{"en":"Hubble is superior to telescopes on land in several ways.","zh":"哈勃在幾方面優於地面上的望遠鏡。"},{"en":"Superior to something means better than it in quality, ability, or performance.","zh":"優於某物，是指在質素、能力或表現上比它好。"},{"en":"A quiet study room may be superior to a noisy café for exam revision.","zh":"安靜自修室可能比嘈雜咖啡店更適合考試溫習。"},{"en":"Hubble is superior in some ways because it avoids atmospheric interference.","zh":"哈勃在某些方面較優越，因為它避開大氣干擾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clear advantage in comparison.","zh":"這個短語描述比較中的明顯優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"telescopes on land","meaning":"地面上的望遠鏡","examples":[{"en":"Telescopes on land are affected by the atmosphere.","zh":"地面上的望遠鏡受大氣層影響。"},{"en":"Telescopes on land are telescopes placed on Earth’s surface.","zh":"地面上的望遠鏡是放置在地球表面的望遠鏡。"},{"en":"A university may build telescopes on land in dry, high-altitude areas.","zh":"大學可能在乾燥高海拔地區建造地面望遠鏡。"},{"en":"They are easier to repair than space telescopes, but atmospheric distortion can affect them.","zh":"它們比太空望遠鏡較容易維修，但大氣扭曲會影響它們。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to Earth-based telescopes.","zh":"這個短語指地球上的望遠鏡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"identify infrared light","meaning":"識別紅外線","examples":[{"en":"Hubble can identify infrared light that would not normally reach Earth.","zh":"哈勃可以識別通常不會到達地球的紅外線。"},{"en":"To identify infrared light means to detect and recognise this invisible form of light.","zh":"識別紅外線，是指偵測並辨認這種不可見光。"},{"en":"A thermal camera can identify infrared light from warm objects.","zh":"熱能相機可以識別來自溫暖物體的紅外線。"},{"en":"Identifying infrared light helps scientists study objects hidden from ordinary sight.","zh":"識別紅外線幫助科學家研究普通視覺中隱藏的物體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes detecting a specific type of light.","zh":"這個短語描述偵測特定種類的光。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"would not normally reach","meaning":"通常不會到達","examples":[{"en":"Infrared light would not normally reach the Earth’s surface.","zh":"紅外線通常不會到達地球表面。"},{"en":"Would not normally reach means usually would not arrive at that place.","zh":"通常不會到達，是指一般不會抵達該地方。"},{"en":"A package would not normally reach a student’s home if the address were incomplete.","zh":"如果地址不完整，包裹通常不會到達學生家中。"},{"en":"The atmosphere can stop some light before it reaches the ground.","zh":"大氣層可以在某些光到達地面前阻止它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something usually being prevented from arriving.","zh":"這個短語描述某物通常被阻止抵達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"Earth’s surface","meaning":"地球表面","examples":[{"en":"Some light does not normally reach the Earth’s surface.","zh":"有些光通常不會到達地球表面。"},{"en":"Earth’s surface is the outer ground and water layer where people live.","zh":"地球表面是人類生活的外層土地和水域。"},{"en":"Rain falls through the atmosphere and reaches Earth’s surface.","zh":"雨水穿過大氣層並到達地球表面。"},{"en":"Light from space may be changed or blocked before reaching the surface.","zh":"來自太空的光在到達表面前可能被改變或阻擋。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the outside physical surface of our planet.","zh":"這個短語指我們星球外部的物理表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"all the more impressive","meaning":"更加令人印象深刻","examples":[{"en":"Hubble’s performance is all the more impressive because it is only medium-sized.","zh":"哈勃的表現更加令人印象深刻，因為它只是中型望遠鏡。"},{"en":"All the more impressive means even more impressive because of the reason given.","zh":"更加令人印象深刻，是指因所給原因而顯得更值得讚賞。"},{"en":"A student’s high score is all the more impressive because they studied while working part-time.","zh":"學生一邊兼職一邊讀書仍取得高分，成績就更加令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"A result can seem stronger when achieved despite a limitation.","zh":"當結果是在限制下取得，它會顯得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises admiration by pointing to a difficulty or contrast.","zh":"這個短語透過指出困難或對比來強調讚賞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"classified as","meaning":"被歸類為……","examples":[{"en":"Hubble is classified as a medium-sized telescope.","zh":"哈勃被歸類為中型望遠鏡。"},{"en":"Classified as means placed into a category.","zh":"被歸類為，是指被放入某一類別。"},{"en":"A book may be classified as fiction or non-fiction in a library.","zh":"一本書在圖書館可能被歸類為小說或非小說。"},{"en":"Classification helps people compare objects of similar type.","zh":"分類幫助人們比較同類物件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal grouping.","zh":"這個短語描述正式分組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"being above the atmosphere","meaning":"位於大氣層之上","examples":[{"en":"Being above the atmosphere gives Hubble important advantages.","zh":"位於大氣層之上給哈勃重要優勢。"},{"en":"Being above the atmosphere means being located higher than Earth’s air layer.","zh":"位於大氣層之上，是指位於比地球空氣層更高的位置。"},{"en":"A camera on a tall building may get a clearer view by being above street obstacles.","zh":"位於高樓上的攝影機可能因高於街道障礙而取得更清晰視野。"},{"en":"Hubble avoids many atmospheric problems because of where it is placed.","zh":"哈勃因其放置位置而避開許多大氣問題。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how location creates benefits.","zh":"這個短語解釋位置如何創造好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"has the advantage of","meaning":"有……的優勢","examples":[{"en":"Hubble has the advantage of avoiding atmospheric distortion.","zh":"哈勃有避免大氣扭曲的優勢。"},{"en":"Has the advantage of something means benefits from that feature or situation.","zh":"有某事的優勢，是指因該特徵或情況而受益。"},{"en":"A school near a train station has the advantage of easy transport.","zh":"靠近火車站的學校有交通方便的優勢。"},{"en":"An advantage can make one option better than another.","zh":"優勢可以令一個選項比另一個更好。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a useful benefit.","zh":"這個短語指出有用的好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"not being affected by","meaning":"不受……影響","examples":[{"en":"Hubble has the advantage of not being affected by diffraction.","zh":"哈勃有不受衍射影響的優勢。"},{"en":"Not being affected by something means not being influenced or damaged by it.","zh":"不受某事影響，是指不被它影響或損害。"},{"en":"Online notes have the advantage of not being affected by messy handwriting.","zh":"網上筆記有不受潦草字跡影響的優勢。"},{"en":"If a telescope is not affected by atmospheric distortion, its images can be clearer.","zh":"如果望遠鏡不受大氣扭曲影響，其影像可以更清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes freedom from a negative influence.","zh":"這個短語描述免受負面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"would otherwise lead to","meaning":"否則會導致……","examples":[{"en":"Diffraction would otherwise lead to blurred images.","zh":"衍射否則會導致模糊影像。"},{"en":"Would otherwise lead to means would cause that result if another condition did not prevent it.","zh":"否則會導致，是指如果沒有另一條件阻止，就會造成該結果。"},{"en":"Regular cleaning prevents dust that would otherwise lead to computer problems.","zh":"定期清潔可以防止灰塵，否則灰塵會導致電腦問題。"},{"en":"Hubble’s position avoids distortion that would otherwise make images unclear.","zh":"哈勃的位置避免了否則會令影像不清的大氣扭曲。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the problem that is prevented.","zh":"這個短語解釋被防止的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 61 - Constellation.pdf","sourcePage":21}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 62":[{"front":"the natural world","meaning":"自然界","examples":[{"en":"The natural world is dominated by regular and recurring cycles.","zh":"自然界由有規律且反覆出現的循環主導。"},{"en":"The natural world means the plants, animals, weather, land, sea, and living systems that exist outside human-made things.","zh":"自然界指植物、動物、天氣、土地、海洋，以及人造事物以外存在的生命系統。"},{"en":"Students study the natural world when they learn about forests, oceans, insects, and weather.","zh":"學生學習森林、海洋、昆蟲和天氣時，就是在研究自然界。"},{"en":"Changes in the natural world can affect food, health, transport, and daily life.","zh":"自然界的變化可以影響食物、健康、交通和日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes nature as a whole, not just one animal or place.","zh":"這個短語描述整體自然，而不只是某一種動物或地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be dominated by","meaning":"由……主導","examples":[{"en":"The natural world is dominated by cycles that are regular and recurring.","zh":"自然界由有規律且反覆出現的循環主導。"},{"en":"To be dominated by something means to be strongly controlled or shaped by it.","zh":"be dominated by something 指被某事強烈控制或塑造。"},{"en":"A student’s week may be dominated by exam revision if a major test is coming.","zh":"如果大考將至，學生的一星期可能由考試溫習主導。"},{"en":"If a city is dominated by traffic, daily travel becomes slow and stressful.","zh":"如果城市由交通問題主導，日常出行會變得緩慢而有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one force or feature has the main influence.","zh":"這個短語顯示某一力量或特徵具有主要影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"regular and recurring","meaning":"有規律且反覆出現的","examples":[{"en":"The moon’s rotation is part of a regular and recurring cycle.","zh":"月球運行是有規律且反覆出現的循環之一。"},{"en":"Regular and recurring means happening again and again in a predictable pattern.","zh":"regular and recurring 指以可預測模式一次又一次發生。"},{"en":"School assemblies may be regular and recurring if they happen every Monday morning.","zh":"如果學校集會每星期一早上舉行，它就是有規律且反覆出現的活動。"},{"en":"Regular and recurring routines help people know what to expect.","zh":"有規律且反覆出現的常規幫助人知道可以預期甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses both order and repetition.","zh":"這個短語同時強調秩序和重複。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the moon’s rotation around Earth","meaning":"月球繞地球運行","examples":[{"en":"The moon’s rotation around Earth is one natural cycle.","zh":"月球繞地球運行是一種自然循環。"},{"en":"The moon’s rotation around Earth refers to the Moon’s regular movement as it travels around our planet.","zh":"the moon’s rotation around Earth 指月球圍繞地球運行的規律移動。"},{"en":"A science class may use diagrams to show the moon’s rotation around Earth.","zh":"科學課可能用圖解展示月球繞地球運行。"},{"en":"This movement affects tides, moon phases, and how people observe the night sky.","zh":"這種運動會影響潮汐、月相和人們觀察夜空的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an astronomical cycle, not a daily human habit.","zh":"這個短語描述天文循環，而不是人類日常習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the changing of the seasons","meaning":"季節變化","examples":[{"en":"The changing of the seasons affects many natural rhythms.","zh":"季節變化影響許多自然節律。"},{"en":"The changing of the seasons means the regular movement from spring to summer, autumn, and winter.","zh":"the changing of the seasons 指春、夏、秋、冬之間的規律轉變。"},{"en":"Farmers plan planting and harvest around the changing of the seasons.","zh":"農民按照季節變化安排播種和收成。"},{"en":"Seasonal change affects daylight, temperature, clothing, food, and animal behaviour.","zh":"季節變化影響日照、溫度、衣着、食物和動物行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a yearly natural cycle.","zh":"這個短語描述一年一度的自然循環。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cycles or rhythms","meaning":"循環或節律","examples":[{"en":"Cycles or rhythms partly control our sleep patterns.","zh":"循環或節律部分控制我們的睡眠模式。"},{"en":"Cycles or rhythms are repeated patterns that happen in nature or in the body.","zh":"cycles or rhythms 指自然界或身體中反覆出現的模式。"},{"en":"A school timetable has a rhythm when lessons, breaks, and lunch happen at set times.","zh":"當上課、小息和午飯在固定時間發生，學校時間表就有一種節律。"},{"en":"Body rhythms affect when people feel hungry, sleepy, energetic, or alert.","zh":"身體節律影響人何時感到肚餓、睏倦、有精神或清醒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated patterns that guide behaviour or change.","zh":"這個短語描述引導行為或變化的反覆模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in part","meaning":"部分地","examples":[{"en":"These rhythms in part control our mood and behaviour.","zh":"這些節律部分地控制我們的情緒與行為。"},{"en":"In part means partly, but not completely.","zh":"in part 指部分地，而不是完全地。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be caused in part by poor sleep and in part by stress.","zh":"學生疲倦可能部分由睡眠不足造成，部分由壓力造成。"},{"en":"If something affects a result in part, other factors may also be involved.","zh":"如果某事部分地影響結果，其他因素也可能牽涉其中。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one explanation is only part of the whole picture.","zh":"這個短語顯示某個解釋只是整體的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"metabolism","meaning":"新陳代謝","examples":[{"en":"Natural rhythms can affect changes in our metabolism.","zh":"自然節律可以影響我們新陳代謝的變化。"},{"en":"Metabolism is the process by which the body turns food into energy and manages physical functions.","zh":"metabolism 指身體把食物轉化為能量並管理生理功能的過程。"},{"en":"Regular meals and sleep can help keep metabolism stable.","zh":"定時進餐和睡眠可以幫助新陳代謝保持穩定。"},{"en":"Poor sleep may affect metabolism and make weight control harder.","zh":"睡眠不足可能影響新陳代謝，令體重控制更困難。"},{"en":"This word refers to the body’s internal energy-use system.","zh":"這個字指身體內部使用能量的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mood and behaviour","meaning":"情緒與行為","examples":[{"en":"Natural cycles can influence our mood and behaviour.","zh":"自然循環可以影響我們的情緒與行為。"},{"en":"Mood and behaviour means how we feel and how we act.","zh":"mood and behaviour 指我們的感受和行動方式。"},{"en":"A tired student may have a low mood and impatient behaviour in class.","zh":"疲倦學生在課堂上可能情緒低落並表現得不耐煩。"},{"en":"Light, sleep, stress, and routines can all affect mood and behaviour.","zh":"光線、睡眠、壓力和作息都可以影響情緒與行為。"},{"en":"This phrase links inner feelings with outward actions.","zh":"這個短語把內在感受與外在行動連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"patterns of sleep","meaning":"睡眠模式","examples":[{"en":"The circadian rhythm affects the patterns of our sleep.","zh":"晝夜節律影響我們的睡眠模式。"},{"en":"Patterns of sleep are the usual times and ways in which a person sleeps and wakes.","zh":"patterns of sleep 指一個人睡覺和醒來的通常時間及方式。"},{"en":"A student’s sleep pattern may change during exams if they study late every night.","zh":"如果學生每晚讀書到很晚，考試期間睡眠模式可能改變。"},{"en":"Irregular sleep patterns can make people tired even if they spend enough hours in bed.","zh":"不規律睡眠模式可以令人疲倦，即使他們在床上的時間足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sleep as a repeated habit.","zh":"這個短語把睡眠描述為反覆習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"circadian rhythm","meaning":"晝夜節律；生理時鐘節律","examples":[{"en":"The circadian rhythm tells the body when to be awake and when to sleep.","zh":"晝夜節律告訴身體何時應清醒、何時應睡覺。"},{"en":"The circadian rhythm is the body’s internal daily clock that follows a roughly 24-hour cycle.","zh":"circadian rhythm 指身體內部約二十四小時循環的每日時鐘。"},{"en":"Bright morning light can help reset the circadian rhythm after a late night.","zh":"早晨明亮光線可以幫助晚睡後重新調整晝夜節律。"},{"en":"When the circadian rhythm is disturbed, people may feel sleepy at the wrong time.","zh":"當晝夜節律被打亂，人可能在錯誤時間感到睏倦。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the body clock that guides sleep, alertness, and energy.","zh":"這個短語指引導睡眠、清醒程度和能量的生理時鐘。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"indicate when to","meaning":"顯示何時應該……","examples":[{"en":"The circadian rhythm indicates when to be awake and when to be asleep.","zh":"晝夜節律顯示何時應清醒、何時應睡覺。"},{"en":"To indicate when to do something means to show the right or expected time to do it.","zh":"indicate when to do something 指顯示做某事的合適或預期時間。"},{"en":"A school timetable indicates when to attend English class and when to take lunch.","zh":"學校時間表顯示何時應上英文課、何時應吃午飯。"},{"en":"Body signals can indicate when to rest, eat, or become active.","zh":"身體訊號可以顯示何時應休息、進食或活動。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a signal with timing.","zh":"這個短語把訊號與時間安排連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"daily rises and falls in","meaning":"……每日的升降變化","examples":[{"en":"The rhythm is controlled by daily rises and falls in light and temperature.","zh":"這種節律由光線和溫度每日的升降變化控制。"},{"en":"Daily rises and falls in something are regular increases and decreases that happen each day.","zh":"daily rises and falls in something 指每天出現的規律增加和減少。"},{"en":"Shops may notice daily rises and falls in customer numbers before and after lunch.","zh":"商店可能注意到午飯前後顧客數量每日的升降變化。"},{"en":"When light and temperature rise and fall each day, the body receives timing signals.","zh":"當光線和溫度每日上升和下降，身體會收到時間訊號。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regular daily ups and downs.","zh":"這個短語描述每日有規律的高低變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"light and temperature","meaning":"光線和溫度","examples":[{"en":"Daily changes in light and temperature control the circadian rhythm.","zh":"光線和溫度的每日變化控制晝夜節律。"},{"en":"Light and temperature are two environmental signals that help the body tell day from night.","zh":"light and temperature 是幫助身體分辨日夜的兩種環境訊號。"},{"en":"A bright, warm morning can make people feel more awake than a dark, cold one.","zh":"明亮溫暖的早晨比黑暗寒冷的早晨更容易令人清醒。"},{"en":"Changes in light and temperature can shift sleepiness, alertness, and energy.","zh":"光線和溫度的變化可以改變睏倦、清醒程度和能量。"},{"en":"This phrase names two key external cues for the body clock.","zh":"這個短語指出生理時鐘的兩個重要外部線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as day turns to night","meaning":"隨着白天轉為黑夜","examples":[{"en":"As day turns to night, the temperature begins to fall.","zh":"隨着白天轉為黑夜，溫度開始下降。"},{"en":"As day turns to night means during the change from daytime to nighttime.","zh":"as day turns to night 指由日間轉入夜間的過程中。"},{"en":"As day turns to night, shops close and street lights begin to come on.","zh":"隨着白天轉為黑夜，商店關門，街燈開始亮起。"},{"en":"This transition brings lower light levels, cooler air, and stronger sleep signals.","zh":"這個轉變帶來較低光線、較冷空氣和更強睡眠訊號。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the evening change from light to darkness.","zh":"這個短語描述黃昏由光轉暗的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"declining light","meaning":"逐漸減弱的光線","examples":[{"en":"Declining light signals to the body that it is time to slow down.","zh":"逐漸減弱的光線向身體發出該放慢下來的訊號。"},{"en":"Declining light means light becoming weaker or darker.","zh":"declining light 指光線變弱或變暗。"},{"en":"Declining light in the evening may make students feel less alert while studying.","zh":"晚上逐漸減弱的光線可能令學生溫習時較不清醒。"},{"en":"When light declines, the body may begin preparing for rest.","zh":"當光線減弱，身體可能開始準備休息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the fading of daylight.","zh":"這個短語描述日光逐漸消退。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lower temperatures","meaning":"較低的溫度","examples":[{"en":"Lower temperatures help signal that sleep time is approaching.","zh":"較低的溫度有助發出睡眠時間將近的訊號。"},{"en":"Lower temperatures are colder conditions compared with earlier or surrounding temperatures.","zh":"lower temperatures 指比之前或周圍更冷的狀況。"},{"en":"Lower temperatures in the evening may make people want warm drinks and blankets.","zh":"晚上較低的溫度可能令人想喝暖飲和蓋被。"},{"en":"Cooler conditions can help the body shift from activity toward rest.","zh":"較冷環境可以幫助身體由活動轉向休息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a drop in warmth.","zh":"這個短語描述溫暖程度下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"signal to the body that","meaning":"向身體發出……的訊號","examples":[{"en":"Declining light signals to the body that it is time to prepare for sleep.","zh":"逐漸減弱的光線向身體發出準備睡眠的訊號。"},{"en":"To signal to the body that something is happening means to give the body a cue or message.","zh":"signal to the body that something is happening 指給身體一個提示或訊息。"},{"en":"Morning sunlight signals to the body that it is time to wake up.","zh":"早晨陽光向身體發出該醒來的訊號。"},{"en":"Regular signals help the body keep a stable rhythm.","zh":"規律訊號幫助身體維持穩定節律。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how the environment sends timing information to the body.","zh":"這個短語解釋環境如何向身體傳送時間資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"slow down","meaning":"放慢下來","examples":[{"en":"The body begins to slow down as night approaches.","zh":"隨着夜晚接近，身體開始放慢下來。"},{"en":"To slow down means to become less active, less fast, or less alert.","zh":"slow down 指變得較不活躍、較慢或較不清醒。"},{"en":"After a long school day, a student may slow down and need a break.","zh":"經過漫長上課日後，學生可能放慢下來並需要休息。"},{"en":"As night comes, the body slows down so sleep becomes easier.","zh":"夜晚來臨時，身體放慢下來，令睡眠更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reduction in activity or speed.","zh":"這個短語描述活動或速度減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"prepare for sleep","meaning":"為睡眠作準備","examples":[{"en":"The body prepares for sleep when light levels fall.","zh":"當光線水平下降，身體會為睡眠作準備。"},{"en":"To prepare for sleep means to begin the physical and mental changes that make sleeping easier.","zh":"prepare for sleep 指開始有助入睡的身體和心理變化。"},{"en":"Turning off screens and dimming lights can help the body prepare for sleep.","zh":"關掉螢幕和調暗燈光可以幫助身體為睡眠作準備。"},{"en":"If the body prepares for sleep too late, falling asleep may become harder.","zh":"如果身體太晚才準備睡眠，入睡可能變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the transition from alertness to rest.","zh":"這個短語描述由清醒轉向休息的過渡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"from sunset onward","meaning":"從日落開始","examples":[{"en":"From sunset onward, people generally become less alert.","zh":"從日落開始，人們一般會變得較不清醒。"},{"en":"From sunset onward means starting at sunset and continuing after that.","zh":"from sunset onward 指由日落開始並在之後持續。"},{"en":"From Monday onward, the school library will close at six o’clock.","zh":"從星期一開始，學校圖書館將於六點關門。"},{"en":"After sunset, lower light can gradually reduce alertness.","zh":"日落後，較低光線可以逐漸降低清醒程度。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a starting point and what follows after it.","zh":"這個短語標示起點以及之後的延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"increasingly less alert","meaning":"越來越不清醒","examples":[{"en":"After sunset, people become increasingly less alert.","zh":"日落後，人們變得越來越不清醒。"},{"en":"Increasingly less alert means becoming less awake or attentive over time.","zh":"increasingly less alert 指隨時間變得較不清醒或不專注。"},{"en":"A student may become increasingly less alert during a very long lecture.","zh":"學生在非常長的講座中可能變得越來越不清醒。"},{"en":"As tiredness grows, reaction, memory, and concentration may become weaker.","zh":"隨着疲倦增加，反應、記憶和專注力可能變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gradual decline in mental sharpness.","zh":"這個短語描述精神敏銳度逐漸下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reaction times","meaning":"反應時間","examples":[{"en":"Reaction times can become noticeably slower in the evening.","zh":"反應時間在晚上可能變得明顯較慢。"},{"en":"Reaction times are the amounts of time people take to respond to something.","zh":"reaction times 指人們對某事作出反應所需的時間。"},{"en":"A driver with slow reaction times may brake too late when a car stops suddenly.","zh":"反應時間慢的司機，在前車突然停下時可能太遲煞車。"},{"en":"Tiredness can lengthen reaction times and increase accident risk.","zh":"疲倦可以延長反應時間並增加意外風險。"},{"en":"This phrase measures how quickly someone responds.","zh":"這個短語量度某人反應有多快。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"noticeably slower","meaning":"明顯較慢","examples":[{"en":"Reaction times can be noticeably slower after sunset.","zh":"日落後，反應時間可能明顯較慢。"},{"en":"Noticeably slower means slow enough that people can clearly see or feel the difference.","zh":"noticeably slower 指慢到人們可以清楚看見或感受到差異。"},{"en":"A phone with too many apps open may become noticeably slower.","zh":"如果手機開了太多應用程式，可能變得明顯較慢。"},{"en":"When people are tired, their thinking and reactions may become noticeably slower.","zh":"當人疲倦時，思考和反應可能變得明顯較慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear drop in speed.","zh":"這個短語描述速度清楚下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a number of factors","meaning":"若干因素","examples":[{"en":"A number of factors can affect our circadian rhythm.","zh":"若干因素可以影響我們的晝夜節律。"},{"en":"A number of factors means several different causes or influences.","zh":"a number of factors 指幾個不同原因或影響。"},{"en":"A number of factors can affect exam results, including sleep, practice, stress, and understanding.","zh":"若干因素可以影響考試成績，包括睡眠、練習、壓力和理解。"},{"en":"When several factors work together, the result may be harder to control.","zh":"當幾個因素共同作用，結果可能更難控制。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces more than one reason.","zh":"這個短語引出不止一個原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"affect our circadian rhythm","meaning":"影響我們的晝夜節律","examples":[{"en":"Night shifts can affect our circadian rhythm.","zh":"夜班可以影響我們的晝夜節律。"},{"en":"To affect our circadian rhythm means to change or disturb the body’s internal daily clock.","zh":"affect our circadian rhythm 指改變或打亂身體內部每日時鐘。"},{"en":"Staying up late with bright screens can affect our circadian rhythm.","zh":"熬夜看明亮螢幕可以影響我們的晝夜節律。"},{"en":"When the rhythm is affected, sleep, alertness, and energy may shift to the wrong times.","zh":"當節律受影響，睡眠、清醒程度和能量可能移到錯誤時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changes to the body clock.","zh":"這個短語描述生理時鐘的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"working night shifts","meaning":"輪夜班","examples":[{"en":"Working night shifts can damage the body’s natural rhythm.","zh":"輪夜班可以損害身體的自然節律。"},{"en":"Working night shifts means working during the night instead of the usual daytime hours.","zh":"working night shifts 指在夜間而不是通常日間時段工作。"},{"en":"Nurses, security guards, and factory workers may work night shifts.","zh":"護士、保安和工廠工人可能輪夜班。"},{"en":"Night work can make people sleep during the day and stay awake when the body expects rest.","zh":"夜間工作可以令人日間睡覺，並在身體預期休息時保持清醒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a work pattern that can disturb the body clock.","zh":"這個短語描述會打亂生理時鐘的工作模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"work against","meaning":"違反；逆着……運作","examples":[{"en":"Night shift workers have to work against the body’s natural rhythm.","zh":"夜班工人必須逆着身體的自然節律工作。"},{"en":"To work against something means to act in opposition to it or make it harder to function normally.","zh":"work against something 指與某事相反地行動，或令其較難正常運作。"},{"en":"Studying with loud music may work against concentration.","zh":"邊聽大聲音樂邊溫習可能不利於專注。"},{"en":"Night work goes against natural sleep signals, so tiredness can increase.","zh":"夜間工作違反自然睡眠訊號，因此疲倦可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase shows conflict between an action and a natural pattern.","zh":"這個短語顯示行動與自然模式之間的衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the body’s natural rhythm","meaning":"身體的自然節律","examples":[{"en":"Night shifts force people to work against the body’s natural rhythm.","zh":"夜班迫使人逆着身體的自然節律工作。"},{"en":"The body’s natural rhythm is the normal internal pattern that guides sleep, energy, hunger, and alertness.","zh":"body’s natural rhythm 指引導睡眠、能量、飢餓和清醒程度的正常內部模式。"},{"en":"A regular bedtime helps protect the body’s natural rhythm.","zh":"規律睡覺時間有助保護身體的自然節律。"},{"en":"If the rhythm is disturbed, people may feel tired at work and awake at night.","zh":"如果節律被打亂，人可能工作時疲倦，晚上卻清醒。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the body’s built-in timing system.","zh":"這個短語指身體內置的時間系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"perhaps the most damaging","meaning":"也許是最具破壞性的","examples":[{"en":"Working night shifts is perhaps the most damaging factor.","zh":"輪夜班也許是最具破壞性的因素。"},{"en":"Perhaps the most damaging means possibly the factor that causes the greatest harm.","zh":"perhaps the most damaging 指可能是造成最大傷害的因素。"},{"en":"For a student’s concentration, lack of sleep is perhaps the most damaging habit.","zh":"對學生專注力而言，睡眠不足也許是最具破壞性的習慣。"},{"en":"A damaging factor creates problems that may affect health, safety, or performance.","zh":"具破壞性的因素會造成可能影響健康、安全或表現的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows uncertainty while highlighting serious harm.","zh":"這個短語在表示不確定的同時突出嚴重傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"despite getting","meaning":"儘管得到","examples":[{"en":"Despite getting enough sleep during the day, night shift workers may still feel tired.","zh":"儘管日間得到足夠睡眠，夜班工人仍可能感到疲倦。"},{"en":"Despite getting something means although someone receives or has it.","zh":"despite getting something 指雖然某人獲得或擁有某物。"},{"en":"Despite getting extra practice, a student may still feel nervous before speaking.","zh":"儘管得到額外練習，學生在演講前仍可能緊張。"},{"en":"Getting daytime sleep may not fully replace sleeping at night.","zh":"日間睡眠未必能完全取代夜間睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast between what someone gets and what still happens.","zh":"這個短語引出得到某物與仍然發生的情況之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"night shift workers","meaning":"夜班工人；輪夜班人士","examples":[{"en":"Night shift workers often feel drowsy during part of the night.","zh":"夜班工人經常在夜間某段時間感到昏昏欲睡。"},{"en":"Night shift workers are people who work during nighttime hours.","zh":"night shift workers 指在夜間時段工作的人。"},{"en":"Hospital nurses and factory staff may be night shift workers.","zh":"醫院護士和工廠員工可能是夜班工人。"},{"en":"Because they work when the body expects sleep, they may face tiredness and accident risks.","zh":"因為他們在身體預期睡覺時工作，可能面對疲倦和意外風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes workers with a nighttime work schedule.","zh":"這個短語描述夜間工作時間表下的工人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tend to feel drowsy","meaning":"往往感到昏昏欲睡","examples":[{"en":"Night shift workers tend to feel drowsy at night.","zh":"夜班工人在夜間往往感到昏昏欲睡。"},{"en":"To tend to feel drowsy means to often feel sleepy or not fully awake.","zh":"tend to feel drowsy 指經常感到睏倦或不完全清醒。"},{"en":"Students tend to feel drowsy in class after staying up too late.","zh":"學生熬夜後，在課堂上往往感到昏昏欲睡。"},{"en":"Drowsiness can slow reaction times and reduce concentration.","zh":"睏倦可以減慢反應時間並降低專注力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common pattern of sleepiness.","zh":"這個短語描述常見的睡意模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at least some of","meaning":"至少一部分的……","examples":[{"en":"They feel drowsy for at least some of the night.","zh":"他們在夜間至少一部分時間感到昏昏欲睡。"},{"en":"At least some of something means part of it, even if not all of it.","zh":"at least some of something 指其中一部分，即使不是全部。"},{"en":"A student may understand at least some of a difficult lecture.","zh":"學生可能至少明白一場困難講座的一部分。"},{"en":"If tiredness appears for at least some of a shift, safety may still be affected.","zh":"如果疲倦在班次至少部分時間出現，安全仍可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids saying the whole amount is involved.","zh":"這個短語避免說整體全部都涉及。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the main factor in","meaning":"……的主要因素","examples":[{"en":"Drowsiness is the main factor in the increase in workplace accidents.","zh":"睏倦是工作場所意外增加的主要因素。"},{"en":"The main factor in something is the most important cause or influence behind it.","zh":"main factor in something 指某事背後最重要的原因或影響。"},{"en":"Lack of practice may be the main factor in weak speaking performance.","zh":"缺乏練習可能是口語表現弱的主要因素。"},{"en":"When one factor is main, it explains more of the problem than other causes.","zh":"當一個因素是主要因素，它比其他原因更能解釋問題。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the leading reason.","zh":"這個短語指出最主要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"workplace accidents","meaning":"工作場所意外","examples":[{"en":"Workplace accidents increase during night shifts.","zh":"工作場所意外在夜班期間增加。"},{"en":"Workplace accidents are injuries or dangerous incidents that happen at work.","zh":"workplace accidents 指在工作中發生的受傷或危險事件。"},{"en":"A slip on a wet factory floor is a workplace accident.","zh":"在濕滑工廠地板上滑倒就是工作場所意外。"},{"en":"Tired workers may make mistakes that increase workplace accident risks.","zh":"疲倦工人可能犯錯，增加工作場所意外風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes safety problems in a work setting.","zh":"這個短語描述工作環境中的安全問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"when compared to","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"There are more accidents during night shifts when compared to day shifts.","zh":"與日班相比，夜班期間意外更多。"},{"en":"When compared to something means when one thing is measured or judged against another.","zh":"when compared to something 指把一件事與另一件事比較來衡量或判斷。"},{"en":"Online lessons may feel flexible when compared to fixed classroom lessons.","zh":"與固定課室課堂相比，網課可能感覺較靈活。"},{"en":"Comparisons help show whether one situation has more risk, benefit, or difficulty.","zh":"比較有助顯示某情況是否有更多風險、好處或困難。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the standard used for comparison.","zh":"這個短語引出比較標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the day shift","meaning":"日班","examples":[{"en":"Night shifts have more workplace accidents than the day shift.","zh":"夜班的工作場所意外比日班更多。"},{"en":"The day shift is the work period that takes place during normal daytime hours.","zh":"day shift 指在正常日間時段進行的工作班次。"},{"en":"A shop assistant on the day shift may work from morning to late afternoon.","zh":"日班店員可能由早上工作到下午較後時間。"},{"en":"Day shifts usually match the body’s natural alert period better than night shifts.","zh":"日班通常比夜班更符合身體自然清醒時段。"},{"en":"This phrase names a daytime work schedule.","zh":"這個短語指出日間工作時間表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have less energy","meaning":"精力較少；較無精神","examples":[{"en":"People may have less energy during winter months.","zh":"人們在冬季月份可能精力較少。"},{"en":"To have less energy means to feel weaker, less active, or less motivated.","zh":"have less energy 指感到較弱、較不活躍或較缺乏動力。"},{"en":"A student who sleeps badly may have less energy for homework after school.","zh":"睡眠差的學生放學後可能較無精神做功課。"},{"en":"Less sunlight and colder weather can make some people feel less energetic.","zh":"較少陽光和較冷天氣可以令一些人感到較無精神。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lower level of physical or mental drive.","zh":"這個短語描述身體或心理動力較低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"winter months","meaning":"冬季月份","examples":[{"en":"There is less sunlight and warmth during the winter months.","zh":"冬季月份期間，陽光和溫暖較少。"},{"en":"Winter months are the months that fall in the winter season.","zh":"winter months 指屬於冬季的月份。"},{"en":"During the winter months, people may wear heavier clothes and use more heating.","zh":"在冬季月份，人們可能穿更厚衣服並使用更多暖氣。"},{"en":"Shorter days in the winter months can affect mood and energy.","zh":"冬季月份日照較短，可以影響情緒和能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a seasonal period.","zh":"這個短語描述一段季節性時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sunlight and warmth","meaning":"陽光和溫暖","examples":[{"en":"Sunlight and warmth can stimulate the brain.","zh":"陽光和溫暖可以刺激大腦。"},{"en":"Sunlight and warmth are light from the sun and the comfortable heat that comes with it.","zh":"sunlight and warmth 指來自太陽的光，以及隨之而來的舒適熱力。"},{"en":"Sitting near a sunny window can give a person sunlight and warmth on a cold morning.","zh":"在寒冷早晨坐近陽光窗戶，可以讓人得到陽光和溫暖。"},{"en":"These signals can make people feel more awake and active.","zh":"這些訊號可以令人感到更清醒和活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two natural cues linked to daytime.","zh":"這個短語描述與日間有關的兩種自然線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stimulate the brain","meaning":"刺激大腦","examples":[{"en":"Sunlight helps stimulate the brain.","zh":"陽光有助刺激大腦。"},{"en":"To stimulate the brain means to make it more active, alert, or responsive.","zh":"stimulate the brain 指令大腦更活躍、更清醒或反應更快。"},{"en":"A challenging puzzle can stimulate the brain and improve concentration.","zh":"具挑戰性的謎題可以刺激大腦並改善專注力。"},{"en":"Morning light can stimulate the brain by signalling that the day has begun.","zh":"早晨光線可以透過發出一天開始的訊號來刺激大腦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making the mind more awake or active.","zh":"這個短語描述令頭腦更清醒或活躍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"international travel","meaning":"國際旅行","examples":[{"en":"International travel can affect the circadian rhythm.","zh":"國際旅行可以影響晝夜節律。"},{"en":"International travel means travelling from one country to another.","zh":"international travel 指從一個國家前往另一個國家。"},{"en":"A business trip from Hong Kong to London is international travel.","zh":"從香港到倫敦出差就是國際旅行。"},{"en":"Crossing time zones can disturb sleep and make the body clock confused.","zh":"跨越時區可以打亂睡眠，令生理時鐘混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes travel across national borders.","zh":"這個短語描述跨越國界的旅行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"notably when","meaning":"尤其當……時","examples":[{"en":"International travel affects the body, notably when travelling for more than four hours.","zh":"國際旅行會影響身體，尤其當飛行超過四小時時。"},{"en":"Notably when means especially when a particular condition is true.","zh":"notably when 指尤其在某特定條件成立時。"},{"en":"Students may feel tired after school, notably when they have had a long exam.","zh":"學生放學後可能疲倦，尤其當他們剛完成長時間考試時。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the situation in which an effect is especially clear.","zh":"這個短語突出某效果特別明顯的情況。"},{"en":"It narrows a general statement to an important case.","zh":"它把一般陳述收窄至重要個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have a significant effect","meaning":"有重大影響","examples":[{"en":"Long-distance travel can have a significant effect on the body clock.","zh":"長途旅行可以對生理時鐘有重大影響。"},{"en":"To have a significant effect means to make an important or noticeable difference.","zh":"have a significant effect 指造成重要或明顯差異。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can have a significant effect on memory and mood.","zh":"睡眠不足可以對記憶和情緒有重大影響。"},{"en":"A significant effect may change how someone feels, works, or performs.","zh":"重大影響可能改變某人的感受、工作或表現。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the impact is not small.","zh":"這個短語強調影響並不微小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in extreme cases","meaning":"在極端情況下","examples":[{"en":"In extreme cases, the rhythm may take a week to reset.","zh":"在極端情況下，節律可能需要一星期重新調整。"},{"en":"In extreme cases means in the most serious or unusual situations.","zh":"in extreme cases 指在最嚴重或最不尋常的情況下。"},{"en":"In extreme cases, a school may close if the weather becomes dangerous.","zh":"在極端情況下，如果天氣變得危險，學校可能關閉。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that the strongest version of a problem can be much worse.","zh":"這個短語提醒人，問題最嚴重的版本可能糟得多。"},{"en":"It is used when describing what can happen at the severe end.","zh":"它用於描述嚴重一端可能發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take up to seven days","meaning":"最多需要七日","examples":[{"en":"It can take up to seven days for the rhythm to reset.","zh":"節律重新調整最多可能需要七日。"},{"en":"To take up to seven days means to require as many as seven days, though it may take less.","zh":"take up to seven days 指最多需要七日，但可能較短。"},{"en":"A delivery may take up to seven days if the address is far away.","zh":"如果地址很遠，送貨最多可能需要七日。"},{"en":"Body rhythms may need several days to adjust after crossing time zones.","zh":"跨越時區後，身體節律可能需要數天調整。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a maximum time limit.","zh":"這個短語給出最長時間限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"reset","meaning":"重新調整","examples":[{"en":"The body’s rhythm may need time to reset after long-distance travel.","zh":"長途旅行後，身體節律可能需要時間重新調整。"},{"en":"To reset means to return to a correct or normal setting.","zh":"reset 指回到正確或正常設定。"},{"en":"A phone may need to reset after a software update.","zh":"手機在軟件更新後可能需要重新啟動或重設。"},{"en":"Morning light and regular sleep can help reset the body clock.","zh":"早晨光線和規律睡眠可以幫助重新調整生理時鐘。"},{"en":"This word describes returning a system to a workable pattern.","zh":"這個字描述讓系統回到可運作模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a phenomenon referred to as","meaning":"一種被稱為……的現象","examples":[{"en":"The effect is a phenomenon referred to as jet lag.","zh":"這種影響是一種被稱為時差反應的現象。"},{"en":"A phenomenon referred to as something is an effect or event given that name.","zh":"a phenomenon referred to as something 指被給予某個名稱的影響或事件。"},{"en":"A sudden fear of missing out is a phenomenon often referred to as FOMO.","zh":"害怕錯過事情的突然焦慮是一種常被稱為 FOMO 的現象。"},{"en":"Naming a phenomenon helps people discuss and recognise it more easily.","zh":"為現象命名有助人們更容易討論和辨認它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the term used for a particular effect.","zh":"這個短語引出某特定影響所使用的術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"jet lag","meaning":"時差反應","examples":[{"en":"Jet lag can occur after long international travel.","zh":"長途國際旅行後可能出現時差反應。"},{"en":"Jet lag is tiredness and body-clock confusion caused by crossing time zones quickly.","zh":"jet lag 指快速跨越時區造成的疲倦和生理時鐘混亂。"},{"en":"A traveller may feel awake at 3 a.m. because of jet lag.","zh":"旅客可能因時差反應而凌晨三點仍很清醒。"},{"en":"Jet lag can disturb sleep, digestion, mood, and concentration.","zh":"時差反應可以打亂睡眠、消化、情緒和專注力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the body’s difficulty adjusting to a new time zone.","zh":"這個短語描述身體難以適應新時區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a similar, although milder, effect","meaning":"類似但較輕微的影響","examples":[{"en":"Daylight saving time can produce a similar, although milder, effect.","zh":"夏令時間可以產生類似但較輕微的影響。"},{"en":"A similar, although milder, effect means a comparable result that is less strong.","zh":"a similar, although milder, effect 指相似但強度較低的結果。"},{"en":"Changing bedtime by one hour may produce a similar, although milder, effect to travelling across time zones.","zh":"改變睡覺時間一小時，可能產生類似跨越時區但較輕微的影響。"},{"en":"Even a small time change can make some people feel tired for a short period.","zh":"即使小小時間改變，也可以令人短暫感到疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two effects while showing one is weaker.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種影響，同時顯示其中一種較弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"daylight saving time","meaning":"夏令時間","examples":[{"en":"Daylight saving time can affect the body clock.","zh":"夏令時間可以影響生理時鐘。"},{"en":"Daylight saving time is a system in which clocks are moved forward or backward to make better use of daylight.","zh":"daylight saving time 指把時鐘撥快或撥慢，以更好利用日光的制度。"},{"en":"Some people feel tired after daylight saving time changes because their sleep schedule shifts.","zh":"有些人在夏令時間轉換後感到疲倦，因為睡眠時間表改變。"},{"en":"Moving the clock can disturb routines even if the change is only one hour.","zh":"即使只改變一小時，撥鐘也可以打亂常規。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a seasonal clock-change system.","zh":"這個短語描述季節性調整時鐘制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"move the clocks forward and backward","meaning":"把時鐘撥快或撥慢","examples":[{"en":"Some countries move the clocks forward and backward depending on the season.","zh":"有些國家視乎季節把時鐘撥快或撥慢。"},{"en":"To move the clocks forward and backward means to officially change the time shown on clocks.","zh":"move the clocks forward and backward 指正式改變時鐘顯示的時間。"},{"en":"In spring, some places move the clocks forward by one hour.","zh":"在春天，有些地方把時鐘撥快一小時。"},{"en":"Clock changes can affect sleep because the body does not adjust instantly.","zh":"撥鐘可以影響睡眠，因為身體不會立即適應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a formal time adjustment, not moving a physical clock across a room.","zh":"這個短語描述正式調整時間，而不是把實體時鐘搬到房間另一邊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"depending on","meaning":"視乎；取決於","examples":[{"en":"The clocks are moved depending on the season.","zh":"時鐘會視乎季節而被調整。"},{"en":"Depending on means decided by or changing according to something.","zh":"depending on 指由某事決定或根據某事改變。"},{"en":"Students may wear jackets or T-shirts depending on the weather.","zh":"學生可能視乎天氣穿外套或 T 恤。"},{"en":"If a decision depends on the season, it changes when the season changes.","zh":"如果決定取決於季節，季節改變時決定也會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the condition that affects a choice.","zh":"這個短語引出影響選擇的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tips for helping","meaning":"幫助……的小貼士","examples":[{"en":"The passage gives tips for helping the body work with its circadian rhythm.","zh":"文章提供幫助身體配合晝夜節律的小貼士。"},{"en":"Tips for helping means practical suggestions that make something easier or better.","zh":"tips for helping 指令某事更容易或更好的實用建議。"},{"en":"A teacher may give tips for helping students remember difficult vocabulary.","zh":"老師可能給出幫助學生記住難詞的小貼士。"},{"en":"Good tips are useful because they turn knowledge into action.","zh":"好的小貼士有用，因為它們把知識轉化為行動。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces advice for solving or improving a situation.","zh":"這個短語引出解決或改善情況的建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"work with","meaning":"配合……運作","examples":[{"en":"You can help your body work with its circadian rhythm.","zh":"你可以幫助身體配合其晝夜節律運作。"},{"en":"To work with something means to cooperate with it rather than fight against it.","zh":"work with something 指配合某事，而不是與它對抗。"},{"en":"A student can work with their energy level by doing difficult homework when they feel most alert.","zh":"學生可以配合自己的精力水平，在最清醒時做困難功課。"},{"en":"Working with the body clock can make sleep and concentration easier.","zh":"配合生理時鐘可以令睡眠和專注更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase shows cooperation with a natural pattern.","zh":"這個短語顯示與自然模式合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"first thing in the morning","meaning":"早上第一時間","examples":[{"en":"First thing in the morning, get as much natural light as possible.","zh":"早上第一時間，盡量接觸最多自然光。"},{"en":"First thing in the morning means immediately after waking up or at the very start of the day.","zh":"first thing in the morning 指剛醒來後或一天開始時立即做。"},{"en":"A student may check the school timetable first thing in the morning.","zh":"學生可能早上第一時間查看學校時間表。"},{"en":"Morning actions can set the tone for the rest of the day.","zh":"早晨行動可以為一天其餘時間定下基調。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses doing something early before other activities.","zh":"這個短語強調在其他活動前很早做某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take a short walk outside","meaning":"到戶外短暫散步","examples":[{"en":"Taking a short walk outside can help reset your rhythm.","zh":"到戶外短暫散步可以幫助重新調整你的節律。"},{"en":"To take a short walk outside means to go outdoors and walk briefly.","zh":"take a short walk outside 指到戶外短時間步行。"},{"en":"A person may take a short walk outside before work to get sunlight and fresh air.","zh":"一個人可能在上班前到戶外短暫散步，以接觸陽光和新鮮空氣。"},{"en":"Outdoor light can help the body recognise that daytime has begun.","zh":"戶外光線可以幫助身體辨認日間已開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple action that supports the body clock.","zh":"這個短語描述支援生理時鐘的簡單行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"open all the curtains","meaning":"拉開所有窗簾","examples":[{"en":"Open all the curtains to let in morning light.","zh":"拉開所有窗簾，讓早晨光線進來。"},{"en":"To open all the curtains means to pull curtains aside so light can enter the room.","zh":"open all the curtains 指把窗簾拉開，讓光線進入房間。"},{"en":"A student may open all the curtains before studying to make the room brighter.","zh":"學生可能在溫習前拉開所有窗簾，令房間更明亮。"},{"en":"Morning light entering the room can help the brain feel more awake.","zh":"早晨光線進入房間可以幫助大腦更清醒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical way to increase natural light indoors.","zh":"這個短語描述在室內增加自然光的實際方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get as much light as possible","meaning":"盡量吸收更多光線","examples":[{"en":"You should get as much light as possible in the morning.","zh":"你應在早上盡量吸收更多光線。"},{"en":"To get as much light as possible means to expose yourself to a high amount of light.","zh":"get as much light as possible 指讓自己接觸大量光線。"},{"en":"Sitting near a window can help office workers get as much light as possible.","zh":"坐近窗邊可以幫助辦公室員工盡量接觸更多光線。"},{"en":"More morning light can strengthen the signal that the day has begun.","zh":"更多早晨光線可以強化一天已開始的訊號。"},{"en":"This phrase describes maximising light exposure.","zh":"這個短語描述最大化光線接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"through the eyes and into the brain","meaning":"經眼睛進入大腦","examples":[{"en":"Light passes through the eyes and into the brain.","zh":"光線經眼睛進入大腦。"},{"en":"Through the eyes and into the brain means light is received by the eyes and then processed as a signal by the brain.","zh":"through the eyes and into the brain 指光線由眼睛接收，然後被大腦處理為訊號。"},{"en":"Bright morning light reaches the brain through the eyes and can affect alertness.","zh":"明亮早晨光線經眼睛到達大腦，並可以影響清醒程度。"},{"en":"Because the brain receives light signals, eye exposure matters for the body clock.","zh":"因為大腦接收光線訊號，眼睛接觸光線對生理時鐘很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the route by which light affects the body.","zh":"這個短語解釋光線影響身體的路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lighting levels","meaning":"照明水平","examples":[{"en":"Lighting levels in homes are usually too low to affect the circadian rhythm strongly.","zh":"家中的照明水平通常太低，不能強烈影響晝夜節律。"},{"en":"Lighting levels mean how bright or dim the light in a place is.","zh":"lighting levels 指某地方的光線有多亮或多暗。"},{"en":"A classroom with low lighting levels may make students feel sleepy.","zh":"照明水平低的課室可能令學生感到睏倦。"},{"en":"Bright lighting can increase alertness, while dim lighting may prepare the body for rest.","zh":"明亮照明可以提升清醒程度，而昏暗照明可能讓身體準備休息。"},{"en":"This phrase measures the amount of light in an environment.","zh":"這個短語量度環境中的光量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"artificial lighting","meaning":"人造照明","examples":[{"en":"Artificial lighting at home is often weaker than sunlight.","zh":"家中的人造照明通常比陽光弱。"},{"en":"Artificial lighting is light produced by lamps, bulbs, screens, or other human-made sources.","zh":"artificial lighting 指由燈、燈泡、螢幕或其他人造來源產生的光。"},{"en":"A desk lamp provides artificial lighting for students studying at night.","zh":"書桌燈為夜間溫習的學生提供人造照明。"},{"en":"Artificial lighting can help people see, but it may not provide the same body-clock signal as sunlight.","zh":"人造照明可以幫助人看見東西，但未必提供與陽光相同的生理時鐘訊號。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts human-made light with natural sunlight.","zh":"這個短語把人造光與自然陽光作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in addition to","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"In addition to light intensity, wavelength is also important.","zh":"除了光線強度之外，波長也很重要。"},{"en":"In addition to means as well as or besides.","zh":"in addition to 指除了某事之外，也包括其他事。"},{"en":"In addition to grammar, students need vocabulary and ideas for good writing.","zh":"除了文法之外，學生要寫得好也需要詞彙和想法。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another important factor to the discussion.","zh":"這個短語把另一個重要因素加入討論。"},{"en":"It shows that more than one thing matters.","zh":"它顯示重要的不止一件事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"light intensity","meaning":"光線強度","examples":[{"en":"Light intensity can affect the circadian rhythm.","zh":"光線強度可以影響晝夜節律。"},{"en":"Light intensity is the strength or brightness of light.","zh":"light intensity 指光的強度或亮度。"},{"en":"A phone screen at full brightness has higher light intensity than a dim bedside lamp.","zh":"全亮度手機螢幕比昏暗床頭燈有更高光線強度。"},{"en":"Strong morning light can send a clearer wake-up signal to the brain.","zh":"強烈早晨光線可以向大腦傳送更清楚的醒來訊號。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how powerful light is.","zh":"這個短語描述光有多強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"wavelength","meaning":"波長","examples":[{"en":"Wavelength, or colour, is another factor in sunlight.","zh":"波長，也就是顏色，是陽光中的另一個因素。"},{"en":"Wavelength is a property of light that is connected with colour.","zh":"wavelength 指光的一種特性，與顏色有關。"},{"en":"Blue light has a different wavelength from red light.","zh":"藍光的波長與紅光不同。"},{"en":"Different wavelengths can affect the brain and body clock in different ways.","zh":"不同波長可以以不同方式影響大腦和生理時鐘。"},{"en":"This word explains why not all light has the same effect.","zh":"這個字解釋為何並非所有光都有相同影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the best source","meaning":"最佳來源","examples":[{"en":"Sunlight is the best source of light for the circadian rhythm.","zh":"陽光是晝夜節律所需光線的最佳來源。"},{"en":"The best source means the most useful or effective place to get something from.","zh":"best source 指獲得某物最有用或最有效的來源。"},{"en":"For clear pronunciation, natural conversation is often the best source of listening practice.","zh":"要練清楚發音，自然對話通常是聆聽練習的最佳來源。"},{"en":"If sunlight is the best source, indoor lamps may be less effective for the body clock.","zh":"如果陽光是最佳來源，室內燈對生理時鐘可能較不有效。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the strongest or most suitable provider.","zh":"這個短語指出最強或最合適的提供者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"plan activities around","meaning":"按照……安排活動","examples":[{"en":"You can plan activities around the highs and lows of your temperature rhythm.","zh":"你可以按照體溫節律的高低起伏安排活動。"},{"en":"To plan activities around something means to arrange activities according to it.","zh":"plan activities around something 指根據某事安排活動。"},{"en":"A student may plan revision around the times when they feel most awake.","zh":"學生可能按照自己最清醒的時間安排溫習。"},{"en":"Planning around energy levels can make difficult tasks easier.","zh":"按照精力水平安排可以令困難工作更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using a pattern to organise your day.","zh":"這個短語描述利用某種模式來組織一天。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"highs and lows","meaning":"高低起伏","examples":[{"en":"Plan your work around the highs and lows of your temperature rhythm.","zh":"按照體溫節律的高低起伏安排工作。"},{"en":"Highs and lows are the points when something is strongest or weakest.","zh":"highs and lows 指某事最強和最弱的時候。"},{"en":"A shop has highs and lows in customer numbers during lunch hours and quiet afternoons.","zh":"商店在午飯時間和安靜下午會有顧客數量的高低起伏。"},{"en":"If you know your energy highs and lows, you can schedule work more wisely.","zh":"如果你知道自己的精力高低起伏，就可以更明智地安排工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes natural rises and drops.","zh":"這個短語描述自然的上升和下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"temperature rhythm","meaning":"體溫節律","examples":[{"en":"Your temperature rhythm affects when you perform best.","zh":"你的體溫節律影響你何時表現最佳。"},{"en":"Temperature rhythm is the daily pattern of rises and falls in body temperature.","zh":"temperature rhythm 指體溫每日上升和下降的模式。"},{"en":"Some people feel more active when their temperature rhythm reaches a higher point.","zh":"有些人在體溫節律達到較高點時感到更活躍。"},{"en":"Body temperature changes can influence strength, alertness, and sleepiness.","zh":"體溫變化可以影響力量、清醒程度和睡意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes body temperature as a daily cycle.","zh":"這個短語把體溫描述為每日循環。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"operate at your physical best","meaning":"身體狀態處於最佳","examples":[{"en":"You may not operate at your physical best early in the morning.","zh":"你在清晨可能未必身體狀態處於最佳。"},{"en":"To operate at your physical best means to perform with your strongest physical energy and coordination.","zh":"operate at your physical best 指以最強體力和協調能力表現。"},{"en":"An athlete may operate at their physical best after warming up properly.","zh":"運動員充分熱身後，可能身體狀態處於最佳。"},{"en":"If the body is still cold and stiff, physical performance may be weaker.","zh":"如果身體仍冷而僵硬，體能表現可能較弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes peak physical condition.","zh":"這個短語描述最佳身體狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"challenging tasks","meaning":"具挑戰性的工作","examples":[{"en":"Late morning is better for challenging tasks.","zh":"上午較後時間更適合做具挑戰性的工作。"},{"en":"Challenging tasks are difficult jobs that require effort, concentration, or skill.","zh":"challenging tasks 指需要努力、專注或技巧的困難工作。"},{"en":"Writing an essay plan can be a challenging task for a tired student.","zh":"對疲倦學生而言，寫作文計劃可以是具挑戰性的工作。"},{"en":"People do challenging tasks better when they are alert and energetic.","zh":"人在清醒和有精神時，較能做好具挑戰性的工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes work that is not easy or automatic.","zh":"這個短語描述不是容易或自動完成的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"feel like nodding off","meaning":"想打瞌睡","examples":[{"en":"After lunch, you may feel like nodding off.","zh":"午飯後，你可能想打瞌睡。"},{"en":"To feel like nodding off means to feel as if you are about to fall asleep briefly.","zh":"feel like nodding off 指感到自己快要短暫睡着。"},{"en":"A student may feel like nodding off during a quiet afternoon lesson.","zh":"學生在安靜的下午課堂中可能想打瞌睡。"},{"en":"Heavy meals and low alertness can make people sleepy after lunch.","zh":"大餐和低清醒度可以令人午飯後睏倦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong feeling of drowsiness.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈睡意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"nod off","meaning":"打瞌睡","examples":[{"en":"Some people nod off after lunch.","zh":"有些人午飯後會打瞌睡。"},{"en":"To nod off means to fall asleep briefly, often without planning to.","zh":"nod off 指短暫睡着，通常不是有意的。"},{"en":"A tired passenger may nod off on the bus and miss their stop.","zh":"疲倦乘客可能在巴士上打瞌睡，並錯過下車站。"},{"en":"People often nod off when they are relaxed, warm, or sleep-deprived.","zh":"人在放鬆、溫暖或睡眠不足時常會打瞌睡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an accidental short sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述意外短暫入睡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"take scheduled breaks","meaning":"按計劃休息","examples":[{"en":"Taking scheduled breaks can help maintain alertness.","zh":"按計劃休息可以幫助維持清醒。"},{"en":"To take scheduled breaks means to rest at planned times instead of waiting until exhaustion.","zh":"take scheduled breaks 指在計劃好的時間休息，而不是等到筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"A student may take scheduled breaks every 45 minutes while revising.","zh":"學生溫習時可能每四十五分鐘按計劃休息。"},{"en":"Planned breaks can reduce tiredness and improve concentration.","zh":"計劃好的休息可以減少疲倦並改善專注力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised rest periods.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的休息時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the best time to exercise","meaning":"最適合做運動的時間","examples":[{"en":"The best time to exercise is in the late afternoon.","zh":"最適合做運動的時間是在下午較後時間。"},{"en":"The best time to exercise means the period when the body is most ready for physical activity.","zh":"best time to exercise 指身體最準備好進行體能活動的時段。"},{"en":"Some people exercise best after school or work because their bodies are fully awake.","zh":"有些人在放學或下班後運動最好，因為身體已完全清醒。"},{"en":"Exercising at the right time may reduce injury risk and improve performance.","zh":"在合適時間運動可能降低受傷風險並改善表現。"},{"en":"This phrase links exercise with body readiness.","zh":"這個短語把運動與身體準備程度連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the late afternoon","meaning":"在下午較後時間","examples":[{"en":"Your body temperature reaches its daily high in the late afternoon.","zh":"你的體溫在下午較後時間達到每日最高點。"},{"en":"In the late afternoon means during the later part of the afternoon, before evening.","zh":"in the late afternoon 指下午較後部分、晚上之前。"},{"en":"Many students feel more awake in the late afternoon than immediately after lunch.","zh":"許多學生在下午較後時間比剛午飯後更清醒。"},{"en":"Body temperature often rises later in the day, supporting physical performance.","zh":"體溫通常在一天較後時間上升，有助身體表現。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific part of the day.","zh":"這個短語指出一天中的特定時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reach its daily high","meaning":"達到每日最高點","examples":[{"en":"The body temperature reaches its daily high in the late afternoon.","zh":"體溫在下午較後時間達到每日最高點。"},{"en":"To reach its daily high means to arrive at the highest point for that day.","zh":"reach its daily high 指達到當天最高水平。"},{"en":"A shop may reach its daily high in sales during lunchtime.","zh":"商店可能在午飯時間達到每日銷售最高點。"},{"en":"When body temperature reaches its high, muscles may feel warmer and more ready.","zh":"當體溫達到高點，肌肉可能感覺更暖、更準備好活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the peak point in a daily cycle.","zh":"這個短語描述每日循環中的高峰點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be warmed up and stretched","meaning":"已熱身並伸展開","examples":[{"en":"Your body is warmed up and stretched after a day at work.","zh":"工作一天後，你的身體已熱身並伸展開。"},{"en":"To be warmed up and stretched means the muscles are less stiff and more ready for movement.","zh":"be warmed up and stretched 指肌肉較不僵硬，並更準備好活動。"},{"en":"After walking around school all day, a student’s body may be more warmed up than early in the morning.","zh":"在學校走動一整天後，學生身體可能比清晨更熱身。"},{"en":"Warmed-up muscles can move more easily and may be less likely to be injured.","zh":"已熱身的肌肉活動更容易，也較不容易受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical readiness for exercise.","zh":"這個短語描述運動前的身體準備狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"avoid driving at times when","meaning":"避免在……的時候駕駛","examples":[{"en":"Avoid driving at times when you would normally sleep.","zh":"避免在你通常會睡覺的時候駕駛。"},{"en":"To avoid driving at times when something is true means not to drive during those risky periods.","zh":"avoid driving at times when something is true 指不要在那些有風險時段駕駛。"},{"en":"A tired worker should avoid driving at times when their body feels least alert.","zh":"疲倦工人應避免在身體最不清醒的時候駕駛。"},{"en":"Driving during normal sleep hours can slow reaction and increase accident risk.","zh":"在正常睡眠時間駕駛可以減慢反應並增加意外風險。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a safety warning based on timing.","zh":"這個短語根據時間提出安全警告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sleepy drivers","meaning":"睏倦的司機","examples":[{"en":"Sleepy drivers should stop for a nap.","zh":"睏倦的司機應停下來小睡。"},{"en":"Sleepy drivers are drivers who feel tired or drowsy while driving.","zh":"sleepy drivers 指駕駛時感到疲倦或昏昏欲睡的司機。"},{"en":"A sleepy driver may drift between lanes or react too slowly to traffic lights.","zh":"睏倦的司機可能偏離行車線，或對交通燈反應太慢。"},{"en":"Sleepiness can be as dangerous as poor attention because it slows reactions.","zh":"睡意可以像注意力不足一樣危險，因為它會減慢反應。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies drivers who should not continue driving without rest.","zh":"這個短語指出不應在沒有休息下繼續駕駛的司機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stop for a nap","meaning":"停下來小睡","examples":[{"en":"A tired driver should stop for a nap.","zh":"疲倦司機應停下來小睡。"},{"en":"To stop for a nap means to pause an activity in order to sleep briefly.","zh":"stop for a nap 指暫停活動以短暫睡眠。"},{"en":"A long-distance driver may stop for a nap at a rest area.","zh":"長途司機可能在休息站停下來小睡。"},{"en":"A short sleep can restore alertness better than simply opening a window.","zh":"短暫睡眠比單純開窗更能恢復清醒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a safety action when someone is too tired to continue.","zh":"這個短語描述太疲倦而不能繼續時的安全行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ineffective substitutes","meaning":"無效的替代方法","examples":[{"en":"Loud music and open windows are ineffective substitutes for sleep.","zh":"大聲音樂和打開窗戶都是睡眠的無效替代方法。"},{"en":"Ineffective substitutes are replacements that do not work well enough.","zh":"ineffective substitutes 指效果不足的替代品或替代方法。"},{"en":"Coffee is an ineffective substitute for proper sleep if a student has stayed awake all night.","zh":"如果學生通宵不睡，咖啡並不能有效替代真正睡眠。"},{"en":"Using weak substitutes can create a false sense of safety.","zh":"使用無效替代方法可能造成虛假的安全感。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that some alternatives cannot replace the real solution.","zh":"這個短語提醒人，有些替代方案不能取代真正解決方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"close the blinds and curtains","meaning":"拉上百葉簾和窗簾","examples":[{"en":"At night, close the blinds and curtains.","zh":"晚上，拉上百葉簾和窗簾。"},{"en":"To close the blinds and curtains means to cover windows so less light enters the room.","zh":"close the blinds and curtains 指遮住窗戶，讓較少光線進入房間。"},{"en":"A night shift worker may close the blinds and curtains before sleeping during the day.","zh":"夜班工人在日間睡覺前可能拉上百葉簾和窗簾。"},{"en":"Blocking outside light can help the brain treat the room as a sleep environment.","zh":"擋住外來光線可以幫助大腦把房間視為睡眠環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical way to make a room darker.","zh":"這個短語描述令房間變暗的實際方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sleep in a dark room","meaning":"在黑暗房間睡覺","examples":[{"en":"You should sleep in a dark room at night.","zh":"你晚上應在黑暗房間睡覺。"},{"en":"To sleep in a dark room means to sleep where there is little or no light.","zh":"sleep in a dark room 指在幾乎沒有光線的房間睡覺。"},{"en":"A person may use blackout curtains to sleep in a dark room.","zh":"一個人可能使用遮光窗簾，在黑暗房間睡覺。"},{"en":"Darkness helps the body receive a stronger signal that it is time to rest.","zh":"黑暗幫助身體接收更強的休息訊號。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sleep-friendly environment.","zh":"這個短語描述有利睡眠的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"keep your brain alert","meaning":"令大腦保持清醒","examples":[{"en":"Bright lights and music can help keep your brain alert.","zh":"明亮燈光和音樂可以幫助令大腦保持清醒。"},{"en":"To keep your brain alert means to help the mind stay awake, focused, and responsive.","zh":"keep your brain alert 指幫助頭腦保持清醒、專注和有反應。"},{"en":"A short walk before class can help keep your brain alert during a lesson.","zh":"上課前短暫散步可以幫助你在課堂中保持清醒。"},{"en":"Alertness helps people react faster and make fewer mistakes.","zh":"清醒度幫助人反應更快並減少錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes maintaining mental wakefulness.","zh":"這個短語描述維持心理清醒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"wear an eye mask","meaning":"戴眼罩","examples":[{"en":"Wear an eye mask to block out light.","zh":"戴眼罩來擋住光線。"},{"en":"To wear an eye mask means to cover the eyes with a soft mask while sleeping or resting.","zh":"wear an eye mask 指睡覺或休息時用柔軟眼罩遮住眼睛。"},{"en":"A traveller may wear an eye mask on a plane to sleep more easily.","zh":"旅客可能在飛機上戴眼罩，讓自己更容易睡着。"},{"en":"Eye masks help reduce light signals that can keep the brain awake.","zh":"眼罩有助減少可能令大腦清醒的光線訊號。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple tool for sleeping in bright environments.","zh":"這個短語描述在明亮環境睡覺的簡單工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"block out the light","meaning":"擋住光線","examples":[{"en":"An eye mask can block out the light when you want to sleep.","zh":"當你想睡覺時，眼罩可以擋住光線。"},{"en":"To block out the light means to stop light from reaching the eyes or room.","zh":"block out the light 指阻止光線到達眼睛或房間。"},{"en":"Thick curtains can block out the light from street lamps at night.","zh":"厚窗簾可以擋住夜間街燈的光線。"},{"en":"Less light can help the body understand that it is time to sleep.","zh":"較少光線可以幫助身體明白現在是睡眠時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preventing light from entering.","zh":"這個短語描述阻止光線進入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"non-nocturnal animals","meaning":"非夜行性動物","examples":[{"en":"Most non-nocturnal animals follow the basic rules of the circadian rhythm.","zh":"大多數非夜行性動物遵循晝夜節律的基本規律。"},{"en":"Non-nocturnal animals are animals that are active mainly during the day rather than at night.","zh":"non-nocturnal animals 指主要在日間而不是夜間活動的動物。"},{"en":"Many birds and farm animals are non-nocturnal animals.","zh":"許多鳥類和農場動物都是非夜行性動物。"},{"en":"These animals usually rest when it is dark and become active when light returns.","zh":"這些動物通常在黑暗時休息，在光線回來時變得活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts daytime animals with night-active animals.","zh":"這個短語把日間活動動物與夜間活動動物作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"follow the basic rules of","meaning":"遵循……的基本規律","examples":[{"en":"Humans follow the basic rules of the circadian rhythm.","zh":"人類遵循晝夜節律的基本規律。"},{"en":"To follow the basic rules of something means to operate according to its main principles.","zh":"follow the basic rules of something 指按照某事的主要原則運作。"},{"en":"A good essay follows the basic rules of clear structure and logical support.","zh":"好文章遵循清晰結構和合理支持的基本規律。"},{"en":"When people follow body-clock rules, they usually sleep better and feel more alert.","zh":"當人們遵循生理時鐘規律，通常睡得更好並更清醒。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that behaviour matches a system’s main pattern.","zh":"這個短語顯示行為符合某系統的主要模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"unique body clocks","meaning":"獨特的生理時鐘","examples":[{"en":"Humans have their own unique body clocks.","zh":"人類有自己獨特的生理時鐘。"},{"en":"Unique body clocks are individual internal timing systems that differ from person to person.","zh":"unique body clocks 指因人而異的個人內部時間系統。"},{"en":"One student may focus best early in the morning, while another works better at night.","zh":"一名學生可能清晨最能專注，另一名學生則晚上表現較好。"},{"en":"Because body clocks differ, the same schedule may not suit everyone equally.","zh":"因為生理時鐘不同，同一時間表未必同樣適合每個人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes personal differences in daily biological timing.","zh":"這個短語描述每日生理時間上的個人差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"daily changes in","meaning":"……的每日變化","examples":[{"en":"Body clocks control daily changes in how we think and feel.","zh":"生理時鐘控制我們思考和感受的每日變化。"},{"en":"Daily changes in something are changes that happen across a normal day.","zh":"daily changes in something 指在正常一天中發生的變化。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice daily changes in students’ energy between morning and afternoon classes.","zh":"老師可能注意到學生在早上和下午課堂之間精力的每日變化。"},{"en":"Daily body-clock changes can affect hunger, focus, mood, and sleepiness.","zh":"生理時鐘的每日變化可以影響飢餓、專注、情緒和睡意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes variations that occur within each day.","zh":"這個短語描述每天內部出現的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"oversee a number of","meaning":"掌管若干……","examples":[{"en":"Body clocks oversee a number of personal characteristics.","zh":"生理時鐘掌管若干個人特徵。"},{"en":"To oversee a number of things means to regulate, manage, or influence several things.","zh":"oversee a number of things 指調節、管理或影響幾項事物。"},{"en":"A class monitor may oversee a number of classroom duties, such as collecting books and checking attendance.","zh":"班長可能掌管若干課室職責，例如收書和點名。"},{"en":"The body clock oversees many functions by sending timing signals through the day.","zh":"生理時鐘透過一天中的時間訊號掌管許多功能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes control or management over several areas.","zh":"這個短語描述對幾個範疇的控制或管理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"personal characteristics","meaning":"個人特徵","examples":[{"en":"Sleep patterns are one of our personal characteristics.","zh":"睡眠模式是我們的個人特徵之一。"},{"en":"Personal characteristics are qualities or patterns that belong to a particular person.","zh":"personal characteristics 指屬於某個人的特質或模式。"},{"en":"Being calm, energetic, shy, or organised can be personal characteristics.","zh":"冷靜、有活力、害羞或有條理都可以是個人特徵。"},{"en":"Some characteristics are shaped by biology, habits, and environment.","zh":"有些特徵由生物因素、習慣和環境塑造。"},{"en":"This phrase describes features that make people different from one another.","zh":"這個短語描述令人與人不同的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sleep patterns","meaning":"睡眠模式","examples":[{"en":"Your body clock affects your sleep patterns.","zh":"你的生理時鐘影響你的睡眠模式。"},{"en":"Sleep patterns are the usual times, length, and quality of a person’s sleep.","zh":"sleep patterns 指一個人睡眠的通常時間、長度和質素。"},{"en":"A teenager’s sleep patterns may shift later during holidays.","zh":"青少年的睡眠模式在假期可能變得較晚。"},{"en":"Stable sleep patterns can improve mood, memory, and concentration.","zh":"穩定睡眠模式可以改善情緒、記憶和專注力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated sleeping habits.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆出現的睡眠習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"dictate whether","meaning":"決定是否","examples":[{"en":"Your body clock dictates whether you are a night owl or an early bird.","zh":"你的生理時鐘決定你是夜貓子還是早起型人。"},{"en":"To dictate whether something happens means to strongly determine which option is true.","zh":"dictate whether something happens 指強烈決定哪個選項成立。"},{"en":"A bus timetable may dictate whether a student can arrive before the bell.","zh":"巴士時間表可能決定學生是否能在鐘響前到達。"},{"en":"A person’s body clock can determine whether mornings or late nights feel easier.","zh":"一個人的生理時鐘可以決定早上或深夜哪個時段較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor decides between alternatives.","zh":"這個短語顯示某因素在不同選項之間作決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"night owl","meaning":"夜貓子；夜型人","examples":[{"en":"A night owl is happy to work late into the night.","zh":"夜貓子樂於工作至深夜。"},{"en":"A night owl is a person who naturally feels more awake and active at night.","zh":"night owl 指天生在夜間較清醒和活躍的人。"},{"en":"A night owl may write essays after midnight when the house is quiet.","zh":"夜貓子可能在午夜後家中安靜時寫文章。"},{"en":"Night owls may struggle with early school or work schedules.","zh":"夜貓子可能難以適應很早開始的學校或工作時間表。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a person whose energy comes later in the day.","zh":"這個短語描述精力在一天較後時間出現的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"work late into the night","meaning":"工作至深夜","examples":[{"en":"Night owls are happy to work late into the night.","zh":"夜貓子樂於工作至深夜。"},{"en":"To work late into the night means to continue working until very late at night.","zh":"work late into the night 指一直工作到晚上很晚。"},{"en":"A student may work late into the night before a project deadline.","zh":"學生可能在專題截止前工作至深夜。"},{"en":"Working too late can disturb sleep and make the next morning harder.","zh":"工作太晚可以打亂睡眠，令翌日早上更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extended work during nighttime.","zh":"這個短語描述夜間延長工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"early bird","meaning":"早起型人","examples":[{"en":"An early bird prefers working in the morning.","zh":"早起型人較喜歡在早上工作。"},{"en":"An early bird is a person who naturally wakes early and feels productive in the morning.","zh":"early bird 指天生早起並在早上感到有效率的人。"},{"en":"An early bird may finish homework before breakfast.","zh":"早起型人可能在早餐前完成功課。"},{"en":"Early birds often prefer schedules that start early and end early.","zh":"早起型人通常較喜歡早開始、早結束的時間表。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a morning-type person.","zh":"這個短語描述晨型人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"prefer the morning","meaning":"較喜歡早上","examples":[{"en":"Early birds prefer the morning.","zh":"早起型人較喜歡早上。"},{"en":"To prefer the morning means to like or work better during the early part of the day.","zh":"prefer the morning 指較喜歡或在一天早段表現較好。"},{"en":"A student may prefer the morning because the house is quiet and the mind is fresh.","zh":"學生可能較喜歡早上，因為家中安靜而頭腦清新。"},{"en":"People who prefer mornings may become tired earlier at night.","zh":"較喜歡早上的人晚上可能較早疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a personal time preference.","zh":"這個短語描述個人時間偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hummingbird","meaning":"早晚皆可工作的人","examples":[{"en":"A hummingbird works well at both ends of the day.","zh":"早晚皆可工作的人在一天的早晚兩段時間都表現良好。"},{"en":"In this context, a hummingbird is a person who can function well both in the morning and in the evening.","zh":"在這個語境中，hummingbird 指早上和晚上都能良好運作的人。"},{"en":"A hummingbird may study before school and still have energy for homework at night.","zh":"早晚皆可工作的人可能上學前溫習，晚上仍有精力做功課。"},{"en":"This type of body clock gives more flexibility in daily planning.","zh":"這類生理時鐘在日常安排上更靈活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone between a night owl and an early bird.","zh":"這個短語描述介乎夜貓子和早起型人之間的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at both ends of the day","meaning":"在一天的早晚兩段時間","examples":[{"en":"A hummingbird can work well at both ends of the day.","zh":"早晚皆可工作的人在一天的早晚兩段時間都能表現良好。"},{"en":"At both ends of the day means during both the early and late parts of the day.","zh":"at both ends of the day 指在一天早段和晚段兩個時段。"},{"en":"A busy parent may exercise at both ends of the day, before work and after dinner.","zh":"忙碌家長可能在一天的早晚兩段時間運動，即上班前和晚飯後。"},{"en":"People who function well at both ends of the day have flexible energy patterns.","zh":"在早晚兩段時間都能良好運作的人，有較靈活的精力模式。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts morning and evening time periods.","zh":"這個短語對比早上和晚上兩個時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"determine not only…but also","meaning":"不但決定……也決定","examples":[{"en":"Your body clock determines not only sleep patterns but also energy levels.","zh":"你的生理時鐘不但決定睡眠模式，也決定精力水平。"},{"en":"Determine not only A but also B means decide or influence two things, not just one.","zh":"determine not only A but also B 指不只決定或影響一件事，也決定或影響另一件事。"},{"en":"A school timetable determines not only lesson times but also when students eat and rest.","zh":"學校時間表不但決定上課時間，也決定學生何時吃飯和休息。"},{"en":"One factor can affect several connected parts of daily life.","zh":"一個因素可以影響日常生活中幾個互相關連的部分。"},{"en":"This phrase expands attention from one result to another.","zh":"這個短語把注意力由一個結果擴展到另一個結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"grumpy","meaning":"脾氣暴躁；易怒","examples":[{"en":"Some people are grumpy before their morning coffee.","zh":"有些人在喝早晨咖啡前脾氣暴躁。"},{"en":"Grumpy means bad-tempered, easily annoyed, or unfriendly because of tiredness or discomfort.","zh":"grumpy 指因疲倦或不舒服而脾氣差、容易煩躁或不友善。"},{"en":"A child may become grumpy if they miss their afternoon nap.","zh":"如果孩子錯過午睡，可能變得易怒。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can make people grumpy because their mood is harder to control.","zh":"睡眠不足可以令人脾氣暴躁，因為情緒較難控制。"},{"en":"This word describes a short-tempered mood.","zh":"這個字描述容易發脾氣的情緒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"throughout the day","meaning":"全日；整天","examples":[{"en":"Your body clock affects when you need to eat throughout the day.","zh":"你的生理時鐘影響你全日何時需要進食。"},{"en":"Throughout the day means during the whole day, from morning to night.","zh":"throughout the day 指由早到晚的整天期間。"},{"en":"A teacher may answer students’ questions throughout the day.","zh":"老師可能整天回答學生問題。"},{"en":"Body-clock signals can change hunger and energy at different times throughout the day.","zh":"生理時鐘訊號可以在一天不同時間改變飢餓和能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something happening across the whole day.","zh":"這個短語描述某事在整天中發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"physical processes","meaning":"身體過程；生理過程","examples":[{"en":"The body clock affects many physical processes.","zh":"生理時鐘影響許多生理過程。"},{"en":"Physical processes are body functions such as digestion, temperature control, and hormone release.","zh":"physical processes 指身體功能，例如消化、體溫控制和荷爾蒙釋放。"},{"en":"Exercise, sleep, and food all influence physical processes.","zh":"運動、睡眠和食物都會影響生理過程。"},{"en":"If the body clock is disrupted, several physical processes may happen at the wrong time.","zh":"如果生理時鐘被打亂，幾個生理過程可能在錯誤時間發生。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to what the body does internally.","zh":"這個短語指身體內部正在做的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"body temperature","meaning":"體溫","examples":[{"en":"The body clock affects body temperature.","zh":"生理時鐘影響體溫。"},{"en":"Body temperature is the level of heat inside the body.","zh":"body temperature 指身體內部的熱度水平。"},{"en":"A thermometer is used to check body temperature when someone may have a fever.","zh":"當某人可能發燒時，會用溫度計檢查體溫。"},{"en":"Body temperature rises and falls during the day, influencing energy and sleepiness.","zh":"體溫在一天中上升和下降，影響能量和睡意。"},{"en":"This phrase names one physical process controlled by the body clock.","zh":"這個短語指出由生理時鐘控制的一個生理過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"blood pressure","meaning":"血壓","examples":[{"en":"The body clock affects blood pressure.","zh":"生理時鐘影響血壓。"},{"en":"Blood pressure is the force of blood pushing against the walls of blood vessels.","zh":"blood pressure 指血液推壓血管壁的力量。"},{"en":"Doctors check blood pressure to understand a person’s heart and circulation health.","zh":"醫生檢查血壓，以了解一個人的心臟和血液循環健康。"},{"en":"Blood pressure can rise and fall at different times of day.","zh":"血壓可以在一天不同時間上升和下降。"},{"en":"This phrase names an important health measurement.","zh":"這個短語指出一項重要健康量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"digestion","meaning":"消化","examples":[{"en":"The body clock affects digestion.","zh":"生理時鐘影響消化。"},{"en":"Digestion is the process of breaking down food so the body can use it.","zh":"digestion 指分解食物，讓身體能使用它的過程。"},{"en":"Eating a heavy meal late at night may disturb digestion and sleep.","zh":"深夜吃大餐可能干擾消化和睡眠。"},{"en":"The body may digest food better when meals match its natural rhythm.","zh":"當進餐時間配合自然節律，身體可能更好地消化食物。"},{"en":"This word describes how the body processes food.","zh":"這個字描述身體如何處理食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hormone levels","meaning":"荷爾蒙水平","examples":[{"en":"The body clock affects hormone levels.","zh":"生理時鐘影響荷爾蒙水平。"},{"en":"Hormone levels are the amounts of chemical messengers in the body.","zh":"hormone levels 指身體內化學訊息物質的數量。"},{"en":"Stress can change hormone levels and affect sleep or appetite.","zh":"壓力可以改變荷爾蒙水平，並影響睡眠或食慾。"},{"en":"Body-clock signals help time the release of hormones during the day and night.","zh":"生理時鐘訊號幫助安排日夜荷爾蒙釋放時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes chemical signals inside the body.","zh":"這個短語描述身體內的化學訊號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"brain activity","meaning":"大腦活動","examples":[{"en":"The body clock affects brain activity such as mood and alertness.","zh":"生理時鐘影響情緒和清醒程度等大腦活動。"},{"en":"Brain activity means the work and signals happening inside the brain.","zh":"brain activity 指大腦內正在進行的工作和訊號。"},{"en":"Brain activity changes when students sleep, study, solve problems, or feel stress.","zh":"學生睡覺、溫習、解難或感受壓力時，大腦活動會改變。"},{"en":"If the body clock is disturbed, brain activity linked to attention may also be affected.","zh":"如果生理時鐘被打亂，與注意力相關的大腦活動也可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental and neurological functioning.","zh":"這個短語描述心理和神經功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"gain a few kilograms","meaning":"增加數公斤體重","examples":[{"en":"Your body clock can cause you to gain a few kilograms in winter.","zh":"你的生理時鐘可以令你在冬季增加數公斤體重。"},{"en":"To gain a few kilograms means to become heavier by several kilograms.","zh":"gain a few kilograms 指體重增加幾公斤。"},{"en":"A person may gain a few kilograms during holidays if they eat more and exercise less.","zh":"如果假期吃得更多而運動較少，一個人可能增加數公斤體重。"},{"en":"Changes in sleep, food timing, and activity can affect body weight.","zh":"睡眠、進食時間和活動量的變化可以影響體重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a moderate increase in weight.","zh":"這個短語描述中等程度的體重增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"autumn and wintertime","meaning":"秋冬時分","examples":[{"en":"Some people gain weight in autumn and wintertime.","zh":"有些人在秋冬時分體重增加。"},{"en":"Autumn and wintertime means the colder seasons of autumn and winter.","zh":"autumn and wintertime 指秋季和冬季這些較冷季節。"},{"en":"In autumn and wintertime, people may stay indoors more and move less.","zh":"在秋冬時分，人們可能更多留在室內並活動較少。"},{"en":"Shorter days and colder weather can change appetite, activity, and sleep.","zh":"日照較短和天氣較冷可以改變食慾、活動量和睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the seasonal period before and during winter.","zh":"這個短語描述冬季之前和冬季期間的季節時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lose weight","meaning":"減重；減肥","examples":[{"en":"The body clock can make it easier to lose weight in spring and summer.","zh":"生理時鐘可以令春夏季減重較容易。"},{"en":"To lose weight means to reduce body weight.","zh":"lose weight 指減少體重。"},{"en":"A person may lose weight by eating balanced meals and exercising regularly.","zh":"一個人可以透過均衡飲食和定期運動減重。"},{"en":"Longer daylight and more activity in warmer months may support weight loss.","zh":"較長日照和暖季中較多活動可能有助減重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decrease in body weight.","zh":"這個短語描述體重下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"spring and summer","meaning":"春夏季","examples":[{"en":"It may be easier to lose weight in spring and summer.","zh":"在春夏季減重可能較容易。"},{"en":"Spring and summer are the warmer seasons after winter and before autumn.","zh":"spring and summer 指冬季之後、秋季之前的較暖季節。"},{"en":"People often spend more time outdoors in spring and summer.","zh":"人們在春夏季通常花更多時間在戶外。"},{"en":"More daylight and warmer weather can encourage walking, sports, and lighter eating.","zh":"更多日照和較暖天氣可以鼓勵步行、運動和較清淡飲食。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the warmer half of the year.","zh":"這個短語描述一年中較暖的一半。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be aware of","meaning":"意識到；知道","examples":[{"en":"Being aware of your body clock can help you maintain healthy rhythms.","zh":"意識到自己的生理時鐘可以幫助你維持健康節律。"},{"en":"To be aware of something means to know about it and notice its effects.","zh":"be aware of something 指知道某事並注意其影響。"},{"en":"A student who is aware of their weak grammar can correct mistakes more carefully.","zh":"意識到自己文法弱的學生，可以更仔細糾正錯誤。"},{"en":"Awareness helps people make better choices because they understand what is happening.","zh":"意識有助人作出更好選擇，因為他們明白正在發生甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes conscious understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述有意識的理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"maintain the best rhythms","meaning":"維持最佳節律","examples":[{"en":"Good routines help us maintain the best rhythms for our body clocks.","zh":"良好常規幫助我們為生理時鐘維持最佳節律。"},{"en":"To maintain the best rhythms means to keep the body’s timing patterns healthy and stable.","zh":"maintain the best rhythms 指保持身體時間模式健康而穩定。"},{"en":"A regular sleep schedule can help students maintain better study and rest rhythms.","zh":"規律睡眠時間表可以幫助學生維持更好的學習和休息節律。"},{"en":"Healthy rhythms support energy, mood, digestion, and concentration.","zh":"健康節律支援能量、情緒、消化和專注力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protecting a good biological pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述保護良好生理模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"body clocks","meaning":"生理時鐘","examples":[{"en":"Our body clocks control many daily physical and mental changes.","zh":"我們的生理時鐘控制許多每日身體和心理變化。"},{"en":"Body clocks are internal timing systems that guide sleep, energy, hunger, and alertness.","zh":"body clocks 指引導睡眠、能量、飢餓和清醒程度的內部時間系統。"},{"en":"Teenagers and adults may have different body clocks, so they feel sleepy at different times.","zh":"青少年和成人可能有不同生理時鐘，因此在不同時間感到睏倦。"},{"en":"When body clocks are disturbed, daily routines can become harder.","zh":"當生理時鐘被打亂，日常常規可能變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the body’s natural timekeeping systems.","zh":"這個短語指身體的自然計時系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tips and tools","meaning":"小貼士和工具","examples":[{"en":"There are tips and tools that can help protect your body clock.","zh":"有些小貼士和工具可以幫助保護你的生理時鐘。"},{"en":"Tips and tools are practical advice and useful objects or methods.","zh":"tips and tools 指實用建議，以及有用物件或方法。"},{"en":"A planner and revision checklist are tips and tools for better study habits.","zh":"計劃表和溫習清單是改善學習習慣的小貼士和工具。"},{"en":"Eye masks, routines, and light exposure can help manage the body clock.","zh":"眼罩、常規和接觸光線可以幫助管理生理時鐘。"},{"en":"This phrase combines guidance with practical aids.","zh":"這個短語結合指引與實用輔助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"keep to the same bedtime routine","meaning":"保持相同的睡前習慣","examples":[{"en":"Keeping to the same bedtime routine is particularly important.","zh":"保持相同的睡前習慣尤其重要。"},{"en":"To keep to the same bedtime routine means to follow similar steps before sleep every night.","zh":"keep to the same bedtime routine 指每晚睡前遵循相似步驟。"},{"en":"A child may brush teeth, read quietly, and turn off the light at the same time each night.","zh":"孩子可能每晚在同一時間刷牙、安靜閱讀和關燈。"},{"en":"A stable routine helps the body recognise when sleep is coming.","zh":"穩定常規幫助身體辨認睡眠即將到來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes consistency before bed.","zh":"這個短語描述睡前一致性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"wake-up schedule","meaning":"起床時間表","examples":[{"en":"A regular wake-up schedule helps maintain the body clock.","zh":"規律起床時間表有助維持生理時鐘。"},{"en":"A wake-up schedule is the planned time or pattern for getting out of bed.","zh":"wake-up schedule 指起床的計劃時間或模式。"},{"en":"A student with a fixed wake-up schedule may get up at seven every morning.","zh":"有固定起床時間表的學生可能每天早上七點起床。"},{"en":"Irregular wake-up times can confuse the body clock.","zh":"不規律起床時間可以令生理時鐘混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the timing of waking.","zh":"這個短語描述醒來的時間安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"days off","meaning":"休息日","examples":[{"en":"You should keep a similar sleep schedule even on your days off.","zh":"即使在休息日，你也應保持相似睡眠時間表。"},{"en":"Days off are days when you do not have to work or attend regular duties.","zh":"days off 指不需要工作或出席日常職責的日子。"},{"en":"A student may sleep late on days off, but this can disturb Monday morning routines.","zh":"學生可能在休息日睡到很晚，但這會打亂星期一早上的常規。"},{"en":"Keeping similar habits on days off helps protect the body clock.","zh":"在休息日保持相似習慣有助保護生理時鐘。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to rest days away from work or school.","zh":"這個短語指不用上班或上學的休息日。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"no more than","meaning":"不多於","examples":[{"en":"There should be no more than a few hours’ difference in bedtime.","zh":"睡覺時間差距應不多於數小時。"},{"en":"No more than means not exceeding a certain amount.","zh":"no more than 指不超過某個數量。"},{"en":"Students should spend no more than ten minutes on one difficult multiple-choice question.","zh":"學生在一條困難選擇題上應花不多於十分鐘。"},{"en":"Setting a limit prevents a difference from becoming too large.","zh":"設定限制可以防止差距變得太大。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a maximum allowed amount.","zh":"這個短語給出最大容許數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a few hours’ difference","meaning":"數小時的差距","examples":[{"en":"There should be only a few hours’ difference in your sleep schedule.","zh":"你的睡眠時間表應只有數小時的差距。"},{"en":"A few hours’ difference means a small gap of several hours between two times.","zh":"a few hours’ difference 指兩個時間之間數小時的小差距。"},{"en":"If you sleep at 11 p.m. on weekdays and 1 a.m. on weekends, there is a two-hour difference.","zh":"如果你平日晚上十一點睡，週末凌晨一點睡，就有兩小時差距。"},{"en":"Keeping the difference small helps the body clock stay stable.","zh":"保持差距小有助生理時鐘穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a limited time gap.","zh":"這個短語描述有限的時間差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"interruptions to your sleep","meaning":"睡眠干擾","examples":[{"en":"Avoiding interruptions to your sleep is very important.","zh":"避免睡眠干擾非常重要。"},{"en":"Interruptions to your sleep are sounds, lights, worries, or events that wake you or disturb rest.","zh":"interruptions to your sleep 指吵聲、光線、憂慮或事件令你醒來或干擾休息。"},{"en":"A barking dog outside may create interruptions to your sleep.","zh":"屋外狗吠可能造成睡眠干擾。"},{"en":"Repeated interruptions can make sleep less refreshing even if you spend many hours in bed.","zh":"反覆干擾可以令睡眠不夠恢復精神，即使你在床上很多小時。"},{"en":"This phrase describes things that break sleep continuity.","zh":"這個短語描述打斷睡眠連續性的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"intermittent, irregular noise","meaning":"間歇且不規律的噪音","examples":[{"en":"Intermittent, irregular noise can disturb sleep.","zh":"間歇且不規律的噪音可以干擾睡眠。"},{"en":"Intermittent, irregular noise means noise that stops and starts unpredictably.","zh":"intermittent, irregular noise 指時停時有、難以預測的噪音。"},{"en":"A dripping tap or occasional car horn can be intermittent, irregular noise at night.","zh":"滴水水龍頭或偶爾響起的車喇叭都可以是夜間間歇且不規律的噪音。"},{"en":"Unpredictable noise can wake the brain because it is harder to ignore.","zh":"難以預測的噪音會喚醒大腦，因為它較難被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uneven noise that breaks rest.","zh":"這個短語描述打斷休息的不均勻噪音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"white noise device","meaning":"白噪音裝置","examples":[{"en":"A white noise device can generate calming sounds.","zh":"白噪音裝置可以產生令人平靜的聲音。"},{"en":"A white noise device is a machine that produces steady background sound to mask other noises.","zh":"white noise device 指產生穩定背景聲以遮蓋其他噪音的機器。"},{"en":"Some people use a white noise device to sleep when neighbours are noisy.","zh":"有些人在鄰居吵鬧時使用白噪音裝置幫助睡眠。"},{"en":"Steady sound can cover sudden noises and make sleep less likely to be interrupted.","zh":"穩定聲音可以蓋過突然噪音，令睡眠較不容易被打斷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a tool for improving sleep conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述改善睡眠環境的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"generate calming sounds","meaning":"產生令人平靜的聲音","examples":[{"en":"A fan or white noise device can generate calming sounds.","zh":"風扇或白噪音裝置可以產生令人平靜的聲音。"},{"en":"To generate calming sounds means to produce soft, steady sounds that help people relax.","zh":"generate calming sounds 指產生柔和穩定、幫助人放鬆的聲音。"},{"en":"A rain-sound app can generate calming sounds for students studying in a noisy home.","zh":"雨聲應用程式可以為在嘈雜家中溫習的學生產生令人平靜的聲音。"},{"en":"Calming sounds can reduce attention to sudden background noise.","zh":"平靜聲音可以減少人對突發背景噪音的注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating sound that supports rest or focus.","zh":"這個短語描述創造支援休息或專注的聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"particularly important for","meaning":"對……尤其重要","examples":[{"en":"Reducing noise is particularly important for night shift workers.","zh":"減少噪音對夜班工人尤其重要。"},{"en":"Particularly important for someone means especially necessary or useful for that group.","zh":"particularly important for someone 指對某群體特別必要或有用。"},{"en":"Clear instructions are particularly important for younger students.","zh":"清楚指示對年幼學生尤其重要。"},{"en":"Daytime sleep can be easily disturbed, so quiet rooms matter greatly for night workers.","zh":"日間睡眠很容易被干擾，因此安靜房間對夜班工人非常重要。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the group that needs something most.","zh":"這個短語突出最需要某事的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"daytime noises","meaning":"日間噪音","examples":[{"en":"Daytime noises are generally louder for night shift workers.","zh":"對夜班工人而言，日間噪音通常更大。"},{"en":"Daytime noises are sounds that happen during the day, such as traffic, construction, or voices.","zh":"daytime noises 指日間發出的聲音，例如交通、工程或人聲。"},{"en":"A night shift worker trying to sleep may be disturbed by daytime noises outside the window.","zh":"試圖睡覺的夜班工人可能被窗外日間噪音干擾。"},{"en":"These noises are harder to avoid because most people are active during the day.","zh":"這些噪音較難避免，因為大多數人在日間活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes daytime sounds that can disturb sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述可以干擾睡眠的日間聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"soft background noise","meaning":"輕柔背景聲","examples":[{"en":"Soft background noise can help people sleep.","zh":"輕柔背景聲可以幫助人入睡。"},{"en":"Soft background noise is gentle sound that stays in the background without being distracting.","zh":"soft background noise 指在背景中持續、不太干擾人的柔和聲音。"},{"en":"A fan can create soft background noise in a bedroom.","zh":"風扇可以在睡房中製造輕柔背景聲。"},{"en":"Steady background sound can make sudden noises less noticeable.","zh":"穩定背景聲可以令突然噪音較不明顯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quiet sound used to support rest.","zh":"這個短語描述用來支援休息的安靜聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"drown out","meaning":"蓋過；掩蓋","examples":[{"en":"Background noise can drown out daytime activity noises.","zh":"背景聲可以蓋過日間活動噪音。"},{"en":"To drown out a sound means to cover it with a louder or steadier sound.","zh":"drown out a sound 指用較大聲或較穩定的聲音蓋過它。"},{"en":"Rain on the roof may drown out traffic noise outside.","zh":"屋頂上的雨聲可能蓋過外面的交通噪音。"},{"en":"If soft sound drowns out sudden noise, sleep may be less interrupted.","zh":"如果柔和聲音蓋過突然噪音，睡眠可能較少被打斷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes masking one sound with another.","zh":"這個短語描述用一種聲音掩蓋另一種聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"daytime activity noises","meaning":"日間活動噪音","examples":[{"en":"Soft sound can drown out daytime activity noises.","zh":"柔和聲音可以蓋過日間活動噪音。"},{"en":"Daytime activity noises are sounds made by people, traffic, work, and daily movement during the day.","zh":"daytime activity noises 指日間由人、交通、工作和日常活動產生的聲音。"},{"en":"Construction, school bells, and neighbours talking can be daytime activity noises.","zh":"工程聲、學校鐘聲和鄰居說話聲都可以是日間活動噪音。"},{"en":"These noises may disturb people who need to sleep after night work.","zh":"這些噪音可能干擾夜班後需要睡覺的人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordinary daytime sounds that become a problem for sleepers.","zh":"這個短語描述對睡眠者變成問題的普通日間聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"small frequent meals","meaning":"少量多餐","examples":[{"en":"Small frequent meals help support metabolism.","zh":"少量多餐有助支援新陳代謝。"},{"en":"Small frequent meals are smaller portions eaten several times across the day.","zh":"small frequent meals 指一天中多次進食較小份量。"},{"en":"A person may eat small frequent meals instead of one very heavy dinner.","zh":"一個人可能少量多餐，而不是只吃一頓很豐富的晚餐。"},{"en":"Regular smaller meals can help keep energy levels more stable.","zh":"規律小餐可以幫助精力水平更穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a meal pattern based on smaller amounts and regular timing.","zh":"這個短語描述以較小份量和規律時間為基礎的進食模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"stoke your metabolism","meaning":"促進新陳代謝","examples":[{"en":"Eating small frequent meals can help stoke your metabolism.","zh":"少量多餐可以幫助促進新陳代謝。"},{"en":"To stoke your metabolism means to keep the body’s energy-burning process active.","zh":"stoke your metabolism 指保持身體燃燒能量的過程活躍。"},{"en":"A balanced breakfast may help stoke your metabolism after sleep.","zh":"均衡早餐可以在睡眠後幫助促進新陳代謝。"},{"en":"Irregular eating may make energy feel less steady during the day.","zh":"不規律進食可能令一日中的能量較不穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase compares metabolism to a fire that needs regular fuel.","zh":"這個短語把新陳代謝比作需要定期燃料的火。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"weight maintenance","meaning":"體重維持","examples":[{"en":"Small regular meals can help with weight maintenance.","zh":"少量定時進餐可以幫助體重維持。"},{"en":"Weight maintenance means keeping body weight stable rather than gaining or losing too much.","zh":"weight maintenance 指保持體重穩定，而不是過度增加或減少。"},{"en":"A person may focus on weight maintenance after reaching a healthy weight.","zh":"一個人達到健康體重後，可能專注於體重維持。"},{"en":"Regular eating habits can reduce overeating and support stable weight.","zh":"規律進食習慣可以減少暴食，並支援體重穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes managing weight over time.","zh":"這個短語描述長期管理體重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"reinforce the day phase","meaning":"強化日間階段","examples":[{"en":"Eating earlier reinforces the day phase of the circadian clock.","zh":"較早進食會強化晝夜節律時鐘的日間階段。"},{"en":"To reinforce the day phase means to strengthen the body’s sense that daytime is the active period.","zh":"reinforce the day phase 指強化身體認為日間是活動時段的感覺。"},{"en":"Eating breakfast in bright light can reinforce the day phase after waking.","zh":"醒來後在明亮光線中吃早餐，可以強化日間階段。"},{"en":"Late-night meals may confuse the body by sending daytime signals at night.","zh":"深夜進食可能在夜間發出日間訊號，令身體混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strengthening the active part of the body clock.","zh":"這個短語描述強化生理時鐘中的活動部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"circadian clock","meaning":"晝夜節律時鐘","examples":[{"en":"Meals can reinforce the day phase of the circadian clock.","zh":"進餐可以強化晝夜節律時鐘的日間階段。"},{"en":"The circadian clock is the body’s internal timing system that follows a daily rhythm.","zh":"circadian clock 指跟隨每日節律的身體內部時間系統。"},{"en":"Light, meals, sleep, and activity all send signals to the circadian clock.","zh":"光線、進餐、睡眠和活動都會向晝夜節律時鐘發出訊號。"},{"en":"If the circadian clock is stable, sleep and energy may become more regular.","zh":"如果晝夜節律時鐘穩定，睡眠和能量可能變得更規律。"},{"en":"This phrase is another way to describe the body clock.","zh":"這個短語是描述生理時鐘的另一種說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"energy-rich foods","meaning":"高能量食物","examples":[{"en":"Eat most of your energy-rich foods earlier in the day.","zh":"把大部分高能量食物安排在一天較早時間進食。"},{"en":"Energy-rich foods are foods that provide a lot of calories or fuel for the body.","zh":"energy-rich foods 指為身體提供大量熱量或燃料的食物。"},{"en":"Rice, bread, pasta, nuts, and oily foods can be energy-rich foods.","zh":"米飯、麵包、意粉、果仁和油脂較高食物都可以是高能量食物。"},{"en":"Eating them earlier may give the body time to use the energy during the day.","zh":"較早進食可以給身體時間在日間使用能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes foods that supply substantial energy.","zh":"這個短語描述提供相當多能量的食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"earlier in the day","meaning":"在一天較早時間","examples":[{"en":"It is better to eat energy-rich foods earlier in the day.","zh":"高能量食物最好在一天較早時間進食。"},{"en":"Earlier in the day means during the morning or early afternoon rather than late at night.","zh":"earlier in the day 指在早上或下午較早時段，而不是深夜。"},{"en":"A student may do difficult revision earlier in the day when they feel fresher.","zh":"學生可能在一天較早時間、精神較好時做困難溫習。"},{"en":"Eating earlier gives the body more time to digest before sleep.","zh":"較早進食給身體更多時間在睡前消化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the first part of the day.","zh":"這個短語指一天的早段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"heavy meal","meaning":"大餐；豐富的一餐","examples":[{"en":"Avoid eating a heavy meal near bedtime.","zh":"避免在接近睡覺時間吃大餐。"},{"en":"A heavy meal is a large, rich, or filling meal that takes more effort to digest.","zh":"heavy meal 指份量大、油膩或很飽肚、需要較多消化工作的餐。"},{"en":"A big fried dinner can be a heavy meal before sleep.","zh":"睡前吃一頓豐富油炸晚餐可以算是大餐。"},{"en":"Heavy meals near bedtime may disturb digestion and make sleep less comfortable.","zh":"接近睡覺時間的大餐可能干擾消化，令睡眠較不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a meal that feels large or burdensome for the body.","zh":"這個短語描述對身體而言份量大或有負擔的一餐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"near bedtime","meaning":"接近睡覺時間","examples":[{"en":"A heavy meal near bedtime can disturb sleep.","zh":"接近睡覺時間吃大餐可以干擾睡眠。"},{"en":"Near bedtime means shortly before the time you usually go to sleep.","zh":"near bedtime 指在你通常睡覺時間之前不久。"},{"en":"Drinking strong coffee near bedtime may keep a person awake.","zh":"接近睡覺時間喝濃咖啡可能令人保持清醒。"},{"en":"Activities near bedtime can affect how quickly the body relaxes.","zh":"睡前活動可以影響身體放鬆得有多快。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the period just before sleep.","zh":"這個短語標示睡眠前的一段時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"all-nighters","meaning":"通宵不睡","examples":[{"en":"Avoid all-nighters before an assessment.","zh":"評估前避免通宵不睡。"},{"en":"All-nighters are nights spent awake without sleeping, usually to work or study.","zh":"all-nighters 指整晚不睡，通常為了工作或溫習。"},{"en":"A student may pull an all-nighter to finish a project, but feel exhausted the next day.","zh":"學生可能通宵不睡完成專題，但第二天筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"All-nighters can reduce memory, concentration, and performance.","zh":"通宵不睡可以降低記憶、專注和表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes staying awake through the entire night.","zh":"這個短語描述整夜保持清醒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"study all night","meaning":"通宵溫習","examples":[{"en":"Studying all night before an assessment may reduce performance.","zh":"評估前通宵溫習可能降低表現。"},{"en":"To study all night means to revise or work through the night without proper sleep.","zh":"study all night 指整夜溫習或工作而沒有足夠睡眠。"},{"en":"A student who studies all night may remember less because the brain has not rested.","zh":"通宵溫習的學生可能記得較少，因為大腦沒有休息。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can cancel out some benefits of extra revision.","zh":"睡眠不足可以抵消部分額外溫習的好處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an extreme study habit before a test.","zh":"這個短語描述考試前的極端學習習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"assessment","meaning":"評估；考核","examples":[{"en":"Students should avoid staying up all night before an assessment.","zh":"學生應避免在評估前通宵不睡。"},{"en":"An assessment is a test, exam, project, or task used to judge learning or performance.","zh":"assessment 指用來判斷學習或表現的測驗、考試、專題或任務。"},{"en":"A speaking exam, essay, or science project can be an assessment.","zh":"口試、作文或科學專題都可以是評估。"},{"en":"Good sleep before an assessment can help memory and concentration.","zh":"評估前睡得好可以幫助記憶和專注。"},{"en":"This word describes something used to evaluate ability or progress.","zh":"這個字描述用來評估能力或進度的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"cut back on sleep","meaning":"減少睡眠","examples":[{"en":"Cutting back on sleep may make you perform less well.","zh":"減少睡眠可能令你表現較差。"},{"en":"To cut back on sleep means to reduce the amount of time spent sleeping.","zh":"cut back on sleep 指減少睡覺時間。"},{"en":"A student may cut back on sleep to finish homework, but feel less focused in class.","zh":"學生可能為完成功課而減少睡眠，但在課堂上較難專注。"},{"en":"Reducing sleep can harm memory, mood, and reaction time.","zh":"減少睡眠可以傷害記憶、情緒和反應時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sleeping less than the body needs.","zh":"這個短語描述睡得少於身體需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"perform less well","meaning":"表現較差","examples":[{"en":"You may perform less well if you sleep too little.","zh":"如果你睡得太少，你可能表現較差。"},{"en":"To perform less well means to do a task with lower quality, accuracy, or success.","zh":"perform less well 指完成任務的質素、準確度或成功程度較低。"},{"en":"A tired student may perform less well in a listening test.","zh":"疲倦學生可能在聆聽測驗中表現較差。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can reduce attention and lead to more mistakes.","zh":"睡眠不足可以降低注意力並導致更多錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weaker performance compared with normal ability.","zh":"這個短語描述比正常能力較弱的表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"reduce changes to","meaning":"減少對……的改動","examples":[{"en":"Reduce changes to your work shift if possible.","zh":"如有可能，減少對工作班次的改動。"},{"en":"To reduce changes to something means to make changes less frequent or less extreme.","zh":"reduce changes to something 指令改動較少發生或較不劇烈。"},{"en":"A student may reduce changes to bedtime by sleeping at similar times each night.","zh":"學生可以透過每晚相似時間睡覺，減少對睡覺時間的改動。"},{"en":"Fewer schedule changes help the body clock stay more stable.","zh":"較少時間表改動有助生理時鐘更穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limiting disruption.","zh":"這個短語描述限制干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"work shift","meaning":"工作班次","examples":[{"en":"Changing your work shift can disturb your body clock.","zh":"改變工作班次可以打亂你的生理時鐘。"},{"en":"A work shift is a scheduled period of work, such as morning, evening, or night duty.","zh":"work shift 指安排好的工作時段，例如早班、晚班或夜班。"},{"en":"A nurse may change from a day shift to a night shift.","zh":"護士可能由日班轉到夜班。"},{"en":"Frequent shift changes can make sleep and meals irregular.","zh":"頻繁轉班可以令睡眠和進餐不規律。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the time block when someone works.","zh":"這個短語描述某人工作的時間段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"avoid alcohol and cigarettes","meaning":"避免酒精和香煙","examples":[{"en":"Avoid alcohol and cigarettes before sleep time.","zh":"睡覺前避免酒精和香煙。"},{"en":"To avoid alcohol and cigarettes means not to drink alcoholic drinks or smoke.","zh":"avoid alcohol and cigarettes 指不飲酒和不吸煙。"},{"en":"A person trying to sleep better may avoid alcohol and cigarettes in the evening.","zh":"想睡得更好的人可能晚上避免酒精和香煙。"},{"en":"These substances can affect sleep quality and make the body less settled.","zh":"這些物質可以影響睡眠質素，令身體較不安定。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a health-related sleep recommendation.","zh":"這個短語給出與健康和睡眠有關的建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"before sleep time","meaning":"睡覺前","examples":[{"en":"Do not drink alcohol or smoke before sleep time.","zh":"睡覺前不要飲酒或吸煙。"},{"en":"Before sleep time means shortly before the period when you plan to sleep.","zh":"before sleep time 指計劃睡覺前不久。"},{"en":"A student should avoid bright screens before sleep time.","zh":"學生睡覺前應避免明亮螢幕。"},{"en":"Habits before sleep time can affect how easily people fall asleep.","zh":"睡覺前的習慣可以影響人有多容易入睡。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the period just before going to bed.","zh":"這個短語指上床睡覺前的一段時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"feel sleepy during the day","meaning":"日間感到睏倦","examples":[{"en":"If you feel sleepy during the day, take a short nap.","zh":"如果你日間感到睏倦，可以小睡一會。"},{"en":"To feel sleepy during the day means to feel tired and ready to sleep during normal waking hours.","zh":"feel sleepy during the day 指在正常清醒時間感到疲倦和想睡。"},{"en":"A student may feel sleepy during the day after staying up late to study.","zh":"學生熬夜溫習後，可能日間感到睏倦。"},{"en":"Daytime sleepiness can reduce concentration and reaction time.","zh":"日間睏倦可以降低專注力和反應時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sleepiness appearing when people are expected to be awake.","zh":"這個短語描述人在應清醒時出現睡意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"take a short nap","meaning":"小睡一會","examples":[{"en":"Taking a short nap can help if you feel sleepy during the day.","zh":"如果你日間感到睏倦，小睡一會可以有幫助。"},{"en":"To take a short nap means to sleep briefly, usually during the day.","zh":"take a short nap 指短暫睡覺，通常在日間。"},{"en":"A student may take a short nap after lunch before continuing revision.","zh":"學生可能午飯後小睡一會，再繼續溫習。"},{"en":"A short nap can restore alertness without disturbing nighttime sleep too much.","zh":"短暫小睡可以恢復清醒，而不會太大程度干擾夜間睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a brief planned rest.","zh":"這個短語描述短暫而有計劃的休息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"set an alarm","meaning":"設定鬧鐘","examples":[{"en":"Set an alarm so that you do not sleep too long.","zh":"設定鬧鐘，這樣你就不會睡太久。"},{"en":"To set an alarm means to arrange a clock or phone to ring at a chosen time.","zh":"set an alarm 指設定時鐘或手機在指定時間響起。"},{"en":"A student may set an alarm before a 20-minute nap.","zh":"學生可能在二十分鐘小睡前設定鬧鐘。"},{"en":"An alarm prevents a short rest from becoming a long sleep.","zh":"鬧鐘防止短暫休息變成長時間睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using a reminder to control time.","zh":"這個短語描述使用提醒來控制時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"no more than about 20 minutes","meaning":"不超過大約二十分鐘","examples":[{"en":"A short nap should last no more than about 20 minutes.","zh":"短暫小睡應不超過大約二十分鐘。"},{"en":"No more than about 20 minutes means roughly 20 minutes at most.","zh":"no more than about 20 minutes 指最多約二十分鐘。"},{"en":"A student taking a power nap may set a timer for no more than about 20 minutes.","zh":"想小睡恢復精神的學生可能設定不超過大約二十分鐘的計時器。"},{"en":"Napping too long may make waking up harder.","zh":"小睡太久可能令醒來更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate maximum time.","zh":"這個短語給出大約最長時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"catnap","meaning":"小睡；打個盹","examples":[{"en":"A catnap is a very short sleep during the day.","zh":"catnap 是日間非常短暫的睡眠。"},{"en":"A catnap means a brief, light sleep, usually used to refresh energy.","zh":"catnap 指短暫而淺的睡眠，通常用來恢復精神。"},{"en":"A tired office worker may take a catnap during lunch break.","zh":"疲倦的辦公室員工可能在午飯時間打個盹。"},{"en":"A short catnap can improve alertness without entering deep sleep.","zh":"短暫小睡可以提升清醒度，而不會進入深層睡眠。"},{"en":"This word describes a quick daytime nap.","zh":"這個字描述快速日間小睡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"enter Stage 3 sleep","meaning":"進入第三階段睡眠","examples":[{"en":"If you nap too long, you may enter Stage 3 sleep.","zh":"如果你小睡太久，可能進入第三階段睡眠。"},{"en":"To enter Stage 3 sleep means to move into a deep stage of sleep.","zh":"enter Stage 3 sleep 指進入深層睡眠階段。"},{"en":"A person who naps for too long may enter Stage 3 sleep and wake up groggy.","zh":"小睡太久的人可能進入第三階段睡眠，醒來時昏沉。"},{"en":"Deep sleep is harder to wake from than light sleep.","zh":"深層睡眠比淺睡更難醒來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving into a deeper sleep stage.","zh":"這個短語描述進入較深睡眠階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"deep sleep","meaning":"深層睡眠","examples":[{"en":"Stage 3 is a period of deep sleep.","zh":"第三階段是一段深層睡眠。"},{"en":"Deep sleep is a heavy sleep stage from which it is harder to wake.","zh":"deep sleep 指較沉、較難醒來的睡眠階段。"},{"en":"A child in deep sleep may not hear quiet conversation nearby.","zh":"進入深層睡眠的孩子可能聽不到旁邊輕聲談話。"},{"en":"Waking from deep sleep can leave people confused or heavy-headed for a while.","zh":"從深層睡眠中醒來，可以令人一段時間內感到迷糊或頭重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong, restorative sleep stage.","zh":"這個短語描述深沉且恢復性的睡眠階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"find it harder to wake up","meaning":"發現較難醒來","examples":[{"en":"After deep sleep, you may find it harder to wake up.","zh":"深層睡眠後，你可能發現較難醒來。"},{"en":"To find it harder to wake up means to experience more difficulty becoming fully awake.","zh":"find it harder to wake up 指變得更難完全清醒。"},{"en":"A student who sleeps after an alarm may find it harder to wake up the second time.","zh":"學生在鬧鐘響後再睡，第二次可能發現更難醒來。"},{"en":"Waking from deep sleep can make people feel slow and confused.","zh":"從深層睡眠醒來可以令人感到遲鈍和迷糊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficulty moving from sleep to alertness.","zh":"這個短語描述由睡眠轉為清醒的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與資料相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the information in the passage.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否與文章資料相符。"},{"en":"To agree with the information means to match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information 指與文章所說內容一致。"},{"en":"If the text says light reaches the brain through the eyes, a statement saying the same thing agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文本說光線經眼睛到達大腦，說同樣內容的陳述就與資料相符。"},{"en":"Students should check the exact wording before choosing TRUE.","zh":"學生選 TRUE 前應檢查準確措辭。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading tasks that test text evidence.","zh":"這個短語常見於測試文本證據的閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the text says naps should be short, a statement recommending very long naps contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文本說小睡應短暫，而陳述建議長時間小睡，就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be clear from the passage, not guessed from outside knowledge.","zh":"矛盾必須從文章清楚看出，而不是靠外部知識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct conflict with the text.","zh":"這個短語描述與文本直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students write NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果沒有相關資料，學生寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not give enough detail to decide.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有提供足夠細節作判斷。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions a person’s age, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文章從未提及某人的年齡，就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when the text is silent.","zh":"當文本沒有說明時，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that evidence is missing.","zh":"這個短語表示證據缺失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"at their slowest","meaning":"處於最慢狀態","examples":[{"en":"The statement claims that our reactions are at their slowest at sunset.","zh":"該陳述聲稱我們的反應在日落時處於最慢狀態。"},{"en":"At their slowest means reaching the lowest speed or longest response time.","zh":"at their slowest 指達到最低速度或最長反應時間。"},{"en":"A computer may be at its slowest when too many programs are open.","zh":"當太多程式開着，電腦可能處於最慢狀態。"},{"en":"Reactions can become slow when people are tired or less alert.","zh":"當人疲倦或較不清醒，反應可能變慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the point of minimum speed.","zh":"這個短語描述速度最低的一點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"tend to get less sleep","meaning":"往往睡得較少","examples":[{"en":"The statement suggests that night shift workers tend to get less sleep.","zh":"該陳述暗示夜班工人往往睡得較少。"},{"en":"To tend to get less sleep means to usually sleep fewer hours than expected or needed.","zh":"tend to get less sleep 指通常睡得比預期或所需時間少。"},{"en":"Students who use phones late at night tend to get less sleep.","zh":"深夜使用手機的學生往往睡得較少。"},{"en":"Less sleep can lead to tiredness, slower reactions, and weaker concentration.","zh":"睡眠較少可以導致疲倦、反應較慢和專注力較弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a usual pattern, not a rule for every person.","zh":"這個短語描述通常模式，而不是每個人都必然如此。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"short journeys by air","meaning":"短途飛行","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to short journeys by air.","zh":"題目提到短途飛行。"},{"en":"Short journeys by air are brief flights, usually over a relatively small distance or time.","zh":"short journeys by air 指時間或距離相對較短的飛行。"},{"en":"A one-hour flight from one city to another is a short journey by air.","zh":"從一個城市到另一個城市的一小時航程就是短途飛行。"},{"en":"Short flights usually cross fewer time zones, so they may affect the body clock less.","zh":"短途飛行通常跨越較少時區，因此對生理時鐘影響可能較小。"},{"en":"This phrase describes brief air travel.","zh":"這個短語描述短時間航空旅行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"have minimal effect on","meaning":"對……影響很小","examples":[{"en":"The statement says short journeys have minimal effect on the body’s rhythm.","zh":"該陳述說短途旅程對身體節律影響很小。"},{"en":"To have minimal effect on something means to affect it very little.","zh":"have minimal effect on something 指對某事影響非常小。"},{"en":"A five-minute delay may have minimal effect on a whole school day.","zh":"五分鐘延誤可能對整個上學日影響很小。"},{"en":"Short travel may not disturb the body clock much if no time zones are crossed.","zh":"如果沒有跨越時區，短途旅行可能不太打亂生理時鐘。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very small impact.","zh":"這個短語描述非常小的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reaches the brain","meaning":"到達大腦","examples":[{"en":"Light reaches the brain through the eyes.","zh":"光線經眼睛到達大腦。"},{"en":"Reaches the brain means arrives as a signal that the brain can process.","zh":"reaches the brain 指以大腦可處理的訊號形式到達。"},{"en":"Sound reaches the brain after the ears receive vibrations and send signals.","zh":"聲音在耳朵接收震動並傳送訊號後到達大腦。"},{"en":"When light reaches the brain, it can affect alertness and body-clock timing.","zh":"當光線到達大腦，它可以影響清醒程度和生理時鐘時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information entering the brain through the senses.","zh":"這個短語描述資訊經感官進入大腦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"equally effective measures","meaning":"同樣有效的措施","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether several measures are equally effective.","zh":"該陳述問幾項措施是否同樣有效。"},{"en":"Equally effective measures are methods that work just as well as one another.","zh":"equally effective measures 指彼此效果一樣好的方法。"},{"en":"For some students, revision cards and practice questions may not be equally effective.","zh":"對有些學生而言，溫習卡和練習題未必同樣有效。"},{"en":"Two methods may seem similar but produce different results.","zh":"兩種方法可能看似相似，但產生不同結果。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the usefulness of different actions.","zh":"這個短語比較不同行動的有效程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"keeping awake","meaning":"保持清醒","examples":[{"en":"The measures are described as ways of keeping awake.","zh":"這些措施被描述為保持清醒的方法。"},{"en":"Keeping awake means staying conscious and alert instead of falling asleep.","zh":"keeping awake 指保持有意識和清醒，而不是睡着。"},{"en":"A tired driver may try keeping awake with music, but sleep is still safer.","zh":"疲倦司機可能嘗試用音樂保持清醒，但睡眠仍更安全。"},{"en":"Some methods only make people feel alert briefly and do not replace rest.","zh":"有些方法只會令人短暫感覺清醒，不能取代休息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes efforts to avoid sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述避免入睡的努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"share the same trends","meaning":"有相同趨勢","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether humans share the same trends in body clocks.","zh":"該陳述問人類在生理時鐘方面是否有相同趨勢。"},{"en":"To share the same trends means to show similar patterns or directions of change.","zh":"share the same trends 指顯示相似模式或變化方向。"},{"en":"Students may share the same trend of feeling sleepy after lunch.","zh":"學生可能有午飯後感到睏倦的相同趨勢。"},{"en":"If people do not share the same trends, their routines may need different adjustments.","zh":"如果人們沒有相同趨勢，他們的作息可能需要不同調整。"},{"en":"This phrase compares patterns across people or groups.","zh":"這個短語比較人或群體之間的模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"with regard to","meaning":"關於；就……而言","examples":[{"en":"The question is about trends with regard to body clocks.","zh":"題目關於生理時鐘方面的趨勢。"},{"en":"With regard to means concerning or about.","zh":"with regard to 指關於或就某方面而言。"},{"en":"With regard to homework, students should check both content and grammar.","zh":"就功課而言，學生應檢查內容和文法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the specific topic being discussed.","zh":"這個短語引出正在討論的特定主題。"},{"en":"It is more formal than simply saying “about.”","zh":"它比簡單說 “about” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"take a short rest","meaning":"短暫休息","examples":[{"en":"The statement says many people take a short rest after lunch.","zh":"該陳述說許多人午飯後短暫休息。"},{"en":"To take a short rest means to pause briefly and relax.","zh":"take a short rest 指短暫停止活動並放鬆。"},{"en":"A student may take a short rest before starting evening revision.","zh":"學生可能在開始晚間溫習前短暫休息。"},{"en":"Short rests can help restore attention without wasting much time.","zh":"短暫休息可以幫助恢復注意力，而不浪費太多時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a brief break from activity.","zh":"這個短語描述短時間暫停活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"just after","meaning":"剛……之後","examples":[{"en":"Some people feel sleepy just after eating lunch.","zh":"有些人剛吃完午飯後感到睏倦。"},{"en":"Just after means immediately or very soon after something happens.","zh":"just after 指某事發生後立即或很快。"},{"en":"A student may feel nervous just after receiving an exam paper.","zh":"學生剛收到試卷後可能感到緊張。"},{"en":"Events that happen just after a meal may be linked to digestion and energy changes.","zh":"剛飯後發生的事情可能與消化和能量變化有關。"},{"en":"This phrase gives close timing after an event.","zh":"這個短語給出某事件後很接近的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"answer the questions below","meaning":"回答以下問題","examples":[{"en":"Students answer the questions below using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞回答以下問題。"},{"en":"To answer the questions below means to respond to the listed questions that follow.","zh":"answer the questions below 指回答下方列出的問題。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should read the instructions before answering the questions below.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生回答以下問題前應先閱讀指示。"},{"en":"Careful answers depend on locating the correct part of the passage.","zh":"仔細作答取決於找到文章中正確部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"using no more than three words","meaning":"使用不多於三個字詞","examples":[{"en":"Students answer using no more than three words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中不多於三個字詞作答。"},{"en":"Using no more than three words means the answer must contain one, two, or three words only.","zh":"using no more than three words 指答案只能包含一個、兩個或三個字詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “late afternoon,” adding extra words may break the limit.","zh":"如果答案是 “late afternoon”，加入額外字詞可能違反限制。"},{"en":"Word limits force students to choose only the necessary words.","zh":"字數限制迫使學生只選必要字詞。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict answer-length rule.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格答案長度規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"除了……之外也","examples":[{"en":"As well as intensity, wavelength is important in sunlight.","zh":"除了強度之外，波長在陽光中也很重要。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to.","zh":"as well as 指除了某事之外，也包括另一事。"},{"en":"A good study plan needs rest as well as practice.","zh":"好的學習計劃除了練習之外也需要休息。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another important item to the same point.","zh":"這個短語把另一個重要項目加入同一觀點。"},{"en":"It shows that two things both matter.","zh":"它顯示兩件事都重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"specific part of the day","meaning":"一天中的特定時段","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for the specific part of the day when the body is warmest.","zh":"題目詢問身體最暖的一天中特定時段。"},{"en":"A specific part of the day means an exact period such as morning, late afternoon, or evening.","zh":"specific part of the day 指確切時段，例如早上、下午較後時間或晚上。"},{"en":"A timetable may ask students to identify the specific part of the day when a class begins.","zh":"時間表可能要求學生辨認課堂開始的一天中特定時段。"},{"en":"Finding the exact time phrase helps answer the question correctly.","zh":"找到確切時間短語有助正確答題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on precise timing within a day.","zh":"這個短語集中於一天中的準確時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"at its warmest","meaning":"處於最暖狀態","examples":[{"en":"The body is at its warmest in the late afternoon.","zh":"身體在下午較後時間處於最暖狀態。"},{"en":"At its warmest means reaching its highest temperature.","zh":"at its warmest 指達到最高溫度。"},{"en":"A room may be at its warmest after sunlight has shone through the window all afternoon.","zh":"當陽光整個下午照進窗戶，房間可能處於最暖狀態。"},{"en":"When the body is warmest, physical movement may feel easier.","zh":"當身體最暖，身體活動可能感覺更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the peak of warmth.","zh":"這個短語描述溫暖程度的高峰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"help them sleep","meaning":"幫助他們入睡","examples":[{"en":"Night shift workers may use an eye mask to help them sleep.","zh":"夜班工人可能使用眼罩幫助他們入睡。"},{"en":"To help them sleep means to make it easier for them to fall asleep or stay asleep.","zh":"help them sleep 指令他們更容易入睡或保持睡眠。"},{"en":"Quiet music may help some children sleep before bedtime.","zh":"安靜音樂可能幫助一些孩子睡覺。"},{"en":"Blocking light can help night workers sleep during the day.","zh":"擋住光線可以幫助夜班工人在日間入睡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes support for better sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述對更好睡眠的支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"work equally well","meaning":"表現同樣好","examples":[{"en":"A hummingbird works equally well in the morning and evening.","zh":"早晚皆可工作的人在早上和晚上表現同樣好。"},{"en":"To work equally well means to perform just as effectively in two situations.","zh":"work equally well 指在兩種情況下表現同樣有效。"},{"en":"A student who studies equally well at home and in the library has flexible habits.","zh":"在家和圖書館都表現同樣好的學生，有靈活學習習慣。"},{"en":"Equal performance gives people more freedom in planning their day.","zh":"表現同樣好給人更多安排一天的自由。"},{"en":"This phrase compares performance across two conditions.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種條件下的表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"after the winter","meaning":"冬天過後","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what the body clock makes easier after the winter.","zh":"題目問生理時鐘在冬天過後令甚麼變得較容易。"},{"en":"After the winter means when winter has ended and warmer seasons begin.","zh":"after the winter 指冬季結束、較暖季節開始之後。"},{"en":"After the winter, people may spend more time outdoors again.","zh":"冬天過後，人們可能再次花更多時間在戶外。"},{"en":"More daylight after winter can affect mood, activity, and weight control.","zh":"冬後更多日照可以影響情緒、活動量和體重控制。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the period following the cold season.","zh":"這個短語指寒冷季節之後的時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"get a good night’s sleep","meaning":"睡個好覺","examples":[{"en":"Avoiding alcohol and cigarettes can help you get a good night’s sleep.","zh":"避免酒精和香煙可以幫助你睡個好覺。"},{"en":"To get a good night’s sleep means to sleep well through the night and wake refreshed.","zh":"get a good night’s sleep 指整晚睡得好，醒來時精神恢復。"},{"en":"A student may get a good night’s sleep by going to bed on time and turning off screens.","zh":"學生可以透過準時上床和關掉螢幕睡個好覺。"},{"en":"Good sleep supports memory, mood, energy, and concentration.","zh":"良好睡眠支援記憶、情緒、能量和專注力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes restful, effective sleep at night.","zh":"這個短語描述夜間有恢復作用的良好睡眠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill missing words in a shortened version of the passage.","zh":"complete the summary 指在文章的簡短版本中填入缺失字詞。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole summary before choosing answers.","zh":"學生選答案前應先讀完整個摘要。"},{"en":"The correct words must fit both the meaning and the grammar of the sentence.","zh":"正確字詞必須同時符合句子的意思和文法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common reading-test task.","zh":"這個短語描述常見閱讀測驗任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"choose no more than two words","meaning":"選擇不多於兩個字詞","examples":[{"en":"Students choose no more than two words from the passage.","zh":"學生從文章中選擇不多於兩個字詞。"},{"en":"Choose no more than two words means select one or two words only.","zh":"choose no more than two words 指只選一個或兩個字詞。"},{"en":"If the correct answer is “white noise,” adding “a white noise” may break the rule.","zh":"如果正確答案是 “white noise”，加入 “a white noise” 可能違反規則。"},{"en":"Word limits require careful copying from the passage.","zh":"字數限制要求學生小心從文章中抄寫。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an exam instruction about answer length.","zh":"這個短語給出關於答案長度的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"follow routines","meaning":"遵循固定作息","examples":[{"en":"You can keep a good rhythm by following routines.","zh":"你可以透過遵循固定作息來保持良好節律。"},{"en":"To follow routines means to do regular activities in a similar order or at similar times.","zh":"follow routines 指以相似次序或相似時間做規律活動。"},{"en":"A student may follow routines by revising, eating, and sleeping at fixed times.","zh":"學生可以透過在固定時間溫習、進食和睡覺來遵循固定作息。"},{"en":"Routines help the body and mind know what to expect.","zh":"固定作息幫助身體和頭腦知道可以預期甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using repeated habits to create stability.","zh":"這個短語描述使用反覆習慣創造穩定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"roughly the same times","meaning":"大約相同時間","examples":[{"en":"Try to sleep and wake at roughly the same times every day.","zh":"嘗試每天在大約相同時間睡覺和起床。"},{"en":"Roughly the same times means almost the same times, with only small differences.","zh":"roughly the same times 指幾乎相同的時間，只有小差異。"},{"en":"A student may study at roughly the same time each evening to build a habit.","zh":"學生可能每天晚上大約相同時間溫習，以建立習慣。"},{"en":"Similar sleep and wake times help keep the body clock steady.","zh":"相似睡覺和起床時間有助生理時鐘穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes approximate consistency, not perfect exactness.","zh":"這個短語描述大致一致，而不是完全精確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"external distractions","meaning":"外來干擾","examples":[{"en":"White noise can help if there are external distractions.","zh":"如果有外來干擾，白噪音可以有幫助。"},{"en":"External distractions are outside things that disturb attention or rest, such as noise or light.","zh":"external distractions 指來自外部、干擾注意力或休息的事物，例如噪音或光線。"},{"en":"A student may close the door to reduce external distractions while studying.","zh":"學生溫習時可能關上門，以減少外來干擾。"},{"en":"Distractions from outside can interrupt sleep even when the room itself is comfortable.","zh":"來自外部的干擾即使房間本身舒適，也可以打斷睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disturbances that come from outside the person or task.","zh":"這個短語描述來自人或任務以外的干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"regular meals","meaning":"定時進餐","examples":[{"en":"Regular meals help keep your metabolism working well.","zh":"定時進餐有助保持新陳代謝良好運作。"},{"en":"Regular meals are meals eaten at consistent times each day.","zh":"regular meals 指每天在一致時間進食。"},{"en":"A student who eats breakfast, lunch, and dinner at similar times has regular meals.","zh":"在相似時間吃早餐、午餐和晚餐的學生，就是定時進餐。"},{"en":"Regular eating can help the body predict when energy is coming.","zh":"規律進食可以幫助身體預測何時會有能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a stable meal schedule.","zh":"這個短語描述穩定進餐時間表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"operating at its best","meaning":"以最佳狀態運作","examples":[{"en":"Small regular meals keep your metabolism operating at its best.","zh":"少量定時進餐令你的新陳代謝以最佳狀態運作。"},{"en":"Operating at its best means working in the most effective or healthy way.","zh":"operating at its best 指以最有效或最健康的方式運作。"},{"en":"A laptop operates at its best when it is charged and not overloaded with apps.","zh":"手提電腦電量充足且沒有太多應用程式負荷時，就以最佳狀態運作。"},{"en":"The body may operate better when sleep, food, and activity are regular.","zh":"當睡眠、飲食和活動規律，身體可能運作得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a system working at its highest quality.","zh":"這個短語描述系統以最高質素運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"limit changes to","meaning":"限制對……的改動","examples":[{"en":"Limit changes to your work shift when possible.","zh":"如有可能，限制對工作班次的改動。"},{"en":"To limit changes to something means to keep the number or size of changes small.","zh":"limit changes to something 指把改動次數或幅度保持較小。"},{"en":"A student may limit changes to bedtime during exam week to stay rested.","zh":"學生可能在考試週限制對睡覺時間的改動，以保持休息。"},{"en":"Fewer changes help routines remain stable and easier to follow.","zh":"較少改動有助常規保持穩定並較容易遵循。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlling disruption.","zh":"這個短語描述控制干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"if necessary","meaning":"如有需要","examples":[{"en":"If necessary, take a short nap during the day.","zh":"如有需要，日間小睡一會。"},{"en":"If necessary means if it is needed or useful in the situation.","zh":"if necessary 指如果在該情況下有需要或有幫助。"},{"en":"If necessary, a student can ask the teacher for extra explanation after class.","zh":"如有需要，學生可以課後請老師額外解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the action is optional and depends on need.","zh":"這個短語顯示行動是可選的，並取決於需要。"},{"en":"It is often used when giving practical advice.","zh":"它常用於給出實用建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 62 - The natural world.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 63":[{"front":"hazard management","meaning":"危害管理","examples":[{"en":"Hazard management is essential in many industrial workplaces.","zh":"危害管理在許多工業工作場所中至關重要。"},{"en":"Hazard management means finding, assessing, controlling, recording, and reviewing things that may cause harm.","zh":"危害管理指找出、評估、控制、記錄和檢討可能造成傷害的事物。"},{"en":"A school science lab needs hazard management because chemicals, glassware, and heat can all injure students.","zh":"學校科學實驗室需要危害管理，因為化學品、玻璃器皿和高溫都可能令學生受傷。"},{"en":"Good hazard management can reduce accidents, protect workers, and prevent expensive damage.","zh":"良好的危害管理可以減少意外、保護工人，並防止昂貴損失。"},{"en":"Without hazard management, a workplace may not notice danger until someone is already hurt.","zh":"沒有危害管理，工作場所可能要到有人受傷後才注意到危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"industrial or manufacturing workplaces","meaning":"工業或製造業工作場所","examples":[{"en":"Hazards must be managed carefully in industrial or manufacturing workplaces.","zh":"在工業或製造業工作場所中，危害必須被小心管理。"},{"en":"Industrial or manufacturing workplaces are places where goods are produced, processed, assembled, or repaired.","zh":"工業或製造業工作場所是生產、加工、組裝或維修貨品的地方。"},{"en":"A factory, warehouse, printing plant, or food-processing site can be an industrial or manufacturing workplace.","zh":"工廠、倉庫、印刷廠或食品加工場都可以是工業或製造業工作場所。"},{"en":"These workplaces often contain machines, chemicals, noise, heat, or heavy materials, so risks must be controlled.","zh":"這些工作場所常有機器、化學品、噪音、高溫或重物，因此必須控制風險。"},{"en":"Safety rules in industrial or manufacturing workplaces are usually stricter than in ordinary offices.","zh":"工業或製造業工作場所的安全規則通常比普通辦公室更嚴格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"managing hazards","meaning":"管理危害","examples":[{"en":"Managing hazards is essential for a successful health and safety system.","zh":"管理危害對成功的健康與安全制度至關重要。"},{"en":"Managing hazards means dealing with dangers before they injure people or damage property.","zh":"managing hazards 指在危險傷害人或損壞財物之前處理它們。"},{"en":"A restaurant manages hazards by keeping wet floors dry and storing knives safely.","zh":"餐廳透過保持濕滑地面乾爽和安全存放刀具來管理危害。"},{"en":"Managing hazards well can stop small risks from becoming serious accidents.","zh":"妥善管理危害可以防止小風險變成嚴重意外。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on active control, not simply noticing that danger exists.","zh":"這個短語著重主動控制，而不只是注意到危險存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be essential for","meaning":"對……至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Managing hazards is essential for workplace safety.","zh":"管理危害對工作場所安全至關重要。"},{"en":"To be essential for something means to be necessary for it to work or succeed.","zh":"be essential for something 指對某事運作或成功來說是必需的。"},{"en":"Clear instructions are essential for students who are doing a difficult experiment.","zh":"清楚指示對正在做困難實驗的學生至關重要。"},{"en":"If something is essential for safety, ignoring it can lead to serious harm.","zh":"如果某事對安全至關重要，忽視它可能導致嚴重傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is not optional but necessary.","zh":"這個短語表示某事不是可有可無，而是必要的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"health and safety system","meaning":"健康與安全制度","examples":[{"en":"A successful health and safety system depends on effective hazard management.","zh":"成功的健康與安全制度取決於有效的危害管理。"},{"en":"A health and safety system is a set of rules, checks, training, and procedures that protect people at work.","zh":"健康與安全制度是一套保護工作中人員的規則、檢查、培訓和程序。"},{"en":"A school’s health and safety system may include fire drills, first-aid plans, and lab rules.","zh":"學校的健康與安全制度可能包括火警演習、急救計劃和實驗室規則。"},{"en":"When the system is weak, workers may not know how to report or control danger.","zh":"當制度薄弱，工人可能不知道如何匯報或控制危險。"},{"en":"A good health and safety system makes safe behaviour normal rather than unusual.","zh":"良好的健康與安全制度會令安全行為變得正常，而不是罕見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an ongoing process","meaning":"持續進行的過程","examples":[{"en":"Hazard management is an ongoing process.","zh":"危害管理是一個持續進行的過程。"},{"en":"An ongoing process is something that continues over time instead of happening only once.","zh":"ongoing process 指隨時間持續進行，而不是只發生一次的事情。"},{"en":"Learning vocabulary is an ongoing process because students need to review and reuse words.","zh":"學習詞彙是一個持續進行的過程，因為學生需要複習並重用詞語。"},{"en":"Hazard management must continue because new machines, staff, and tasks can create new risks.","zh":"危害管理必須持續，因為新機器、新職員和新任務都可能造成新風險。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds learners that some work needs regular checking and improvement.","zh":"這個短語提醒學習者，有些工作需要定期檢查和改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"go through five different stages","meaning":"經歷五個不同階段","examples":[{"en":"The hazard-management process goes through five different stages.","zh":"危害管理過程經歷五個不同階段。"},{"en":"To go through five different stages means to move step by step through five parts of a process.","zh":"go through five different stages 指一步一步經過一個過程中的五個部分。"},{"en":"A writing task may go through five different stages: planning, drafting, checking, editing, and rewriting.","zh":"寫作任務可能經歷五個不同階段：規劃、起草、檢查、修改和重寫。"},{"en":"Breaking a process into stages makes it easier to follow and control.","zh":"把過程分成階段，會令它更容易跟從和控制。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing ordered steps.","zh":"這個短語適合用於描述有順序的步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hazard-management plan","meaning":"危害管理計劃","examples":[{"en":"Each step becomes a stage in the hazard-management plan.","zh":"每一步都成為危害管理計劃中的一個階段。"},{"en":"A hazard-management plan is a written or organised method for dealing with workplace dangers.","zh":"hazard-management plan 指用來處理工作場所危險的書面或有組織方法。"},{"en":"A school workshop may have a hazard-management plan for using drills, saws, and sharp tools.","zh":"學校工作坊可能有危害管理計劃，處理電鑽、鋸和利器的使用。"},{"en":"A clear plan helps staff know what to do before, during, and after a safety problem.","zh":"清晰計劃幫助職員知道在安全問題發生前、期間和之後應做甚麼。"},{"en":"Without a hazard-management plan, safety decisions may become inconsistent or careless.","zh":"沒有危害管理計劃，安全決策可能變得不一致或粗心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"identify potential hazards","meaning":"識別潛在危害","examples":[{"en":"The first step is to identify potential hazards.","zh":"第一步是識別潛在危害。"},{"en":"To identify potential hazards means to find things that could cause harm before they actually do.","zh":"identify potential hazards 指在危害真正造成傷害前，找出可能造成傷害的事物。"},{"en":"Before a school trip, teachers identify potential hazards such as traffic, bad weather, and lost students.","zh":"學校旅行前，老師會識別潛在危害，例如交通、惡劣天氣和學生走失。"},{"en":"Identifying hazards early gives people time to remove or control them.","zh":"及早識別危害讓人有時間移除或控制它們。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on spotting danger before an accident happens.","zh":"這個短語著重在意外發生前發現危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"potential hazards","meaning":"潛在危害","examples":[{"en":"Potential hazards must be identified before risks can be controlled.","zh":"在風險能被控制之前，潛在危害必須被識別。"},{"en":"Potential hazards are things that may cause harm, even if they have not caused an accident yet.","zh":"potential hazards 指可能造成傷害的事物，即使它們尚未造成意外。"},{"en":"Loose wires, wet floors, and unlocked chemicals are potential hazards in a school.","zh":"鬆脫電線、濕滑地板和未鎖好的化學品，都是學校中的潛在危害。"},{"en":"If potential hazards are ignored, small problems can become injuries or damage.","zh":"如果潛在危害被忽視，小問題可能變成傷害或損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to possible danger rather than danger that has already happened.","zh":"這個短語指可能的危險，而不是已發生的危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be defined as","meaning":"被定義為","examples":[{"en":"Hazards are defined as anything that could potentially cause harm.","zh":"危害被定義為任何可能造成傷害的事物。"},{"en":"To be defined as something means to be explained or described with a clear meaning.","zh":"be defined as something 指以清楚意思被解釋或描述為某事。"},{"en":"In a grammar lesson, a noun may be defined as a word that names a person, place, or thing.","zh":"在文法課中，名詞可以被定義為命名人物、地方或事物的詞。"},{"en":"Definitions help people use words consistently and avoid misunderstanding.","zh":"定義幫助人們一致地使用詞語，避免誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic and technical explanations.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術和技術解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"potentially cause harm","meaning":"可能造成傷害","examples":[{"en":"A hazard is anything that could potentially cause harm.","zh":"危害是任何可能造成傷害的事物。"},{"en":"To potentially cause harm means to have the possibility of injuring people or damaging something.","zh":"potentially cause harm 指有可能令人體受傷或令某物受損。"},{"en":"A broken chair could potentially cause harm if a student sits on it and falls.","zh":"如果學生坐上損壞的椅子而跌倒，它可能造成傷害。"},{"en":"Items that seem harmless can still cause harm if they are placed in the wrong place.","zh":"看似無害的物件，如果放錯地方，仍可能造成傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes possible damage before it happens.","zh":"這個短語描述傷害發生前的可能損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not only to…but also to…","meaning":"不但對……也對……","examples":[{"en":"Hazards can cause harm not only to people but also to the organisation.","zh":"危害不但可以對人造成傷害，也可以對機構造成傷害。"},{"en":"Not only to…but also to… is used to show that two different groups or things are affected.","zh":"not only to…but also to… 用來顯示兩個不同群體或事物都受到影響。"},{"en":"Poor communication can cause problems not only to students but also to teachers.","zh":"溝通不善不但可以對學生造成問題，也可以對老師造成問題。"},{"en":"This structure makes the second effect feel additional and important.","zh":"這個結構令第二個影響感覺是額外且重要的。"},{"en":"It helps writers show that a problem has wider consequences.","zh":"它幫助作者顯示問題有更廣泛後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"to illustrate","meaning":"舉例說明","examples":[{"en":"To illustrate, an industrial accident can injure employees and damage equipment.","zh":"舉例說明，工業意外可以令員工受傷並損壞設備。"},{"en":"To illustrate means to give an example that makes an idea clearer.","zh":"to illustrate 指給出例子，使想法更清楚。"},{"en":"To illustrate, a teacher may show a sample answer before students write their own.","zh":"舉例說明，老師可能先展示範文，再讓學生自己寫。"},{"en":"Examples help learners understand abstract ideas by connecting them to real situations.","zh":"例子透過連接真實情況，幫助學習者理解抽象概念。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when moving from explanation to example.","zh":"這個短語適合用於由解釋轉向例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"industrial accident","meaning":"工業意外","examples":[{"en":"An industrial accident can cause injury and lost production.","zh":"工業意外可以造成受傷和生產損失。"},{"en":"An industrial accident is an unexpected harmful event that happens in a factory or similar workplace.","zh":"industrial accident 指在工廠或類似工作場所發生的意外有害事件。"},{"en":"A worker slipping near a machine or being hit by falling materials can be an industrial accident.","zh":"工人在機器旁滑倒，或被墜下材料擊中，都可以是工業意外。"},{"en":"Industrial accidents can stop work, damage equipment, and lead to investigations.","zh":"工業意外可以令工作停止、設備受損，並引發調查。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to accidents connected with industrial work.","zh":"這個短語指與工業工作相關的意外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cause an injury to","meaning":"對……造成傷害","examples":[{"en":"An industrial accident can cause an injury to employees.","zh":"工業意外可以對員工造成傷害。"},{"en":"To cause an injury to someone means to make that person physically hurt.","zh":"cause an injury to someone 指令某人身體受傷。"},{"en":"A wet staircase can cause an injury to a student if it is not marked with a warning sign.","zh":"如果濕滑樓梯沒有警告標示，可能對學生造成傷害。"},{"en":"Preventing injury is easier when hazards are removed before people use the area.","zh":"在人們使用該區域前移除危害，較容易防止受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the harm suffered by a person.","zh":"這個短語著重某人承受的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"result in","meaning":"導致；造成","examples":[{"en":"A workplace accident can result in lost production and wasted resources.","zh":"工作場所意外可以導致生產損失和資源浪費。"},{"en":"To result in something means to cause it to happen.","zh":"result in something 指造成某事發生。"},{"en":"Missing the last bus can result in a long walk home.","zh":"錯過尾班巴士可能導致長時間步行回家。"},{"en":"Small mistakes can result in serious problems if they are repeated or ignored.","zh":"如果小錯誤被重複或忽視，可能導致嚴重問題。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links a cause with its effect.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接原因與結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lost production","meaning":"生產損失","examples":[{"en":"An accident may result in lost production for the company.","zh":"意外可能為公司造成生產損失。"},{"en":"Lost production means work or output that is not completed because something has gone wrong.","zh":"lost production 指因為出現問題而未能完成的工作或產出。"},{"en":"A factory may suffer lost production if a machine breaks down for a whole day.","zh":"如果機器壞了一整天，工廠可能遭受生產損失。"},{"en":"Lost production can reduce income and delay orders.","zh":"生產損失可以減少收入並延誤訂單。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the business cost of stopped or slowed work.","zh":"這個短語描述工作停止或放慢造成的商業成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"broken machinery","meaning":"損壞的機器","examples":[{"en":"Broken machinery can be one consequence of an industrial accident.","zh":"損壞的機器可以是工業意外的一個後果。"},{"en":"Broken machinery refers to machines that are damaged and cannot work properly.","zh":"broken machinery 指受損並不能正常運作的機器。"},{"en":"A printer with broken machinery may jam every sheet of paper.","zh":"有損壞機件的打印機可能每張紙都卡住。"},{"en":"Broken machinery can slow production and create new safety risks.","zh":"損壞的機器可以拖慢生產，並造成新安全風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damaged equipment, not just old equipment.","zh":"這個短語描述受損設備，而不只是舊設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"wasted resources","meaning":"被浪費的資源","examples":[{"en":"Wasted resources can harm the organisation as well as its employees.","zh":"被浪費的資源可以傷害機構，也可以傷害其員工。"},{"en":"Wasted resources are materials, time, money, or energy used without producing useful results.","zh":"wasted resources 指沒有產生有用結果而被用掉的材料、時間、金錢或能源。"},{"en":"Printing the wrong worksheets for a whole class creates wasted resources.","zh":"為全班印錯工作紙會造成被浪費的資源。"},{"en":"Wasted resources can increase costs and reduce efficiency.","zh":"被浪費的資源可以增加成本並降低效率。"},{"en":"This phrase describes loss caused by poor planning, accidents, or mistakes.","zh":"這個短語描述由規劃不善、意外或錯誤造成的損失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"local and national government legislation","meaning":"地方及國家政府法例","examples":[{"en":"Local and national government legislation may regulate hazard identification.","zh":"地方及國家政府法例可能規管危害識別。"},{"en":"Local and national government legislation means laws made by city, regional, or national authorities.","zh":"local and national government legislation 指由城市、地區或國家權威制定的法律。"},{"en":"A restaurant must follow local and national government legislation on food safety.","zh":"餐廳必須遵守關於食物安全的地方及國家政府法例。"},{"en":"Such legislation sets minimum rules so organisations cannot ignore public safety.","zh":"這類法例設定最低規則，使機構不能忽視公共安全。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to legal requirements from different levels of government.","zh":"這個短語指來自不同政府層級的法律要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"strict regulations concerning","meaning":"關於……的嚴格規例","examples":[{"en":"Some industries have strict regulations concerning hazard identification.","zh":"有些行業有關於危害識別的嚴格規例。"},{"en":"Strict regulations concerning something are firm official rules about that issue.","zh":"strict regulations concerning something 指關於某議題的嚴格官方規則。"},{"en":"Schools have strict regulations concerning fire exits because blocked exits can be deadly.","zh":"學校有關於火警出口的嚴格規例，因為被堵塞的出口可以致命。"},{"en":"Strict regulations can force organisations to act safely even when safety costs money.","zh":"嚴格規例可以迫使機構安全行事，即使安全措施需要成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong rules about a specific matter.","zh":"這個短語描述關於某特定事項的強力規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hazard identification","meaning":"危害識別","examples":[{"en":"Hazard identification is required in many dangerous industries.","zh":"許多危險行業都需要危害識別。"},{"en":"Hazard identification means finding and naming possible sources of danger.","zh":"hazard identification 指找出並命名可能的危險來源。"},{"en":"Before a sports day, teachers do hazard identification by checking the track, equipment, and weather.","zh":"運動會前，老師透過檢查跑道、設備和天氣進行危害識別。"},{"en":"Good hazard identification allows risks to be controlled before injuries happen.","zh":"良好的危害識別讓風險在受傷發生前被控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first step in managing workplace danger.","zh":"這個短語描述管理工作場所危險的第一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be perceived to be dangerous","meaning":"被視為危險","examples":[{"en":"Some industries are perceived to be dangerous.","zh":"有些行業被視為危險。"},{"en":"To be perceived to be dangerous means to be seen or judged by people as risky or unsafe.","zh":"be perceived to be dangerous 指被人看作或判斷為有風險或不安全。"},{"en":"Cycling on busy roads may be perceived to be dangerous by parents of young children.","zh":"在繁忙道路踏單車，可能被年幼孩子的父母視為危險。"},{"en":"If a job is perceived as dangerous, workers may expect stronger protection and higher pay.","zh":"如果一份工作被視為危險，工人可能期望更強保護和更高薪酬。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how people view the level of danger.","zh":"這個短語著重人們如何看待危險程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"overlook hazard identification","meaning":"忽視危害識別","examples":[{"en":"Companies that overlook hazard identification can face penalties.","zh":"忽視危害識別的公司可能面對懲罰。"},{"en":"To overlook hazard identification means to ignore or fail to carry out the process of finding dangers.","zh":"overlook hazard identification 指忽略或沒有進行找出危險的過程。"},{"en":"A school may overlook hazard identification if it lets students use broken sports equipment without checking it.","zh":"如果學校不檢查就讓學生使用損壞的運動器材，可能是在忽視危害識別。"},{"en":"Overlooking hazards can lead to accidents that could have been prevented.","zh":"忽視危害可以導致本來可避免的意外。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious failure to notice or manage danger.","zh":"這個短語描述未能注意或管理危險的嚴重失誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"incur severe penalties","meaning":"招致嚴重懲罰","examples":[{"en":"Companies may incur severe penalties if they ignore hazard identification.","zh":"如果公司忽視危害識別，可能招致嚴重懲罰。"},{"en":"To incur severe penalties means to receive serious punishment, usually because rules have been broken.","zh":"incur severe penalties 指受到嚴重懲罰，通常因為違反規則。"},{"en":"A driver may incur severe penalties for speeding near a school.","zh":"司機在學校附近超速可能招致嚴重懲罰。"},{"en":"Severe penalties can include fines, legal action, or loss of permission to operate.","zh":"嚴重懲罰可以包括罰款、法律行動或失去營運許可。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in legal or workplace contexts.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於法律或工作場所語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"having identified","meaning":"在識別……之後","examples":[{"en":"Having identified the potential hazards, the company must assess them.","zh":"在識別潛在危害之後，公司必須評估它們。"},{"en":"Having identified means after finding or recognising something.","zh":"having identified 指在找出或辨認某事之後。"},{"en":"Having identified the weak grammar points, a teacher can design more useful exercises.","zh":"在識別薄弱文法點之後，老師可以設計更有用的練習。"},{"en":"This structure shows that one step is completed before the next step begins.","zh":"這個結構顯示一個步驟完成後，下一步才開始。"},{"en":"It is often used in formal process writing.","zh":"它常用於正式流程寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"assess the hazard","meaning":"評估危害","examples":[{"en":"The next step is to assess the hazard.","zh":"下一步是評估危害。"},{"en":"To assess the hazard means to judge how serious, likely, or damaging the danger may be.","zh":"assess the hazard 指判斷該危險可能有多嚴重、多可能發生或造成多大損害。"},{"en":"A teacher assesses the hazard of a wet playground before deciding whether students can play outside.","zh":"老師會在決定學生能否到戶外玩耍前，評估濕滑操場的危害。"},{"en":"Assessment helps people decide which risks need urgent action.","zh":"評估幫助人們決定哪些風險需要緊急行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes judging danger, not simply naming it.","zh":"這個短語描述判斷危險，而不只是命名它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"that is","meaning":"即是說；換言之","examples":[{"en":"To assess the hazard, that is, to consider how significant it is.","zh":"評估危害，即是說，考慮它有多嚴重。"},{"en":"That is means in other words or more exactly.","zh":"that is 指換言之或更準確地說。"},{"en":"Students need to revise actively, that is, they should test themselves rather than only reread notes.","zh":"學生需要主動溫習，即是說，他們應測試自己，而不是只重讀筆記。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to explain a previous idea more clearly.","zh":"作者使用這個短語，把前面的想法解釋得更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase helps restate a difficult point in simpler words.","zh":"這個短語幫助用較簡單文字重述困難重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"consider how significant","meaning":"考慮……有多嚴重","examples":[{"en":"Risk managers consider how significant each hazard is.","zh":"風險管理人員會考慮每項危害有多嚴重。"},{"en":"To consider how significant something is means to judge how important or serious it is.","zh":"consider how significant something is 指判斷某事有多重要或多嚴重。"},{"en":"A teacher may consider how significant a student’s repeated lateness is before meeting the parents.","zh":"老師在約見家長前，可能會考慮學生反覆遲到有多嚴重。"},{"en":"Considering significance helps people choose a suitable response.","zh":"考慮嚴重程度幫助人們選擇合適回應。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on judging importance, not just noticing something exists.","zh":"這個短語著重判斷重要性，而不只是注意到某事存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"to a degree","meaning":"在某程度上","examples":[{"en":"To a degree, hazard assessment is subjective.","zh":"在某程度上，危害評估是主觀的。"},{"en":"To a degree means partly or to some extent.","zh":"to a degree 指部分地或在某程度上。"},{"en":"To a degree, exam pressure can motivate students, but too much pressure can harm them.","zh":"在某程度上，考試壓力可以推動學生，但壓力太大會傷害他們。"},{"en":"This phrase softens a statement so it does not sound absolute.","zh":"這個短語令陳述不那麼絕對。"},{"en":"It is useful when something is true only in part.","zh":"當某事只部分為真時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"subjective aspect","meaning":"主觀層面","examples":[{"en":"Risk assessment includes a subjective aspect.","zh":"風險評估包括主觀層面。"},{"en":"A subjective aspect is a part that depends on personal judgement rather than only fixed facts.","zh":"subjective aspect 指取決於個人判斷，而不只是固定事實的部分。"},{"en":"Marking a creative story has a subjective aspect because readers may value style differently.","zh":"批改創意故事有主觀層面，因為讀者可能以不同方式重視風格。"},{"en":"Subjective judgement can create inconsistency if there are no clear guidelines.","zh":"如果沒有清楚指引，主觀判斷可能造成不一致。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the human judgement part of a decision.","zh":"這個短語描述決定中的人為判斷部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"risk management","meaning":"風險管理","examples":[{"en":"Risk management involves judging how serious each hazard is.","zh":"風險管理涉及判斷每項危害有多嚴重。"},{"en":"Risk management means identifying possible problems and taking steps to reduce their chance or impact.","zh":"risk management 指識別可能問題，並採取步驟減低其發生機會或影響。"},{"en":"A school uses risk management when it plans emergency exits for a large event.","zh":"學校為大型活動規劃緊急出口時，就是在使用風險管理。"},{"en":"Good risk management prevents avoidable problems and prepares people for unavoidable ones.","zh":"良好的風險管理防止可避免問題，並讓人準備面對不可避免問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on controlling uncertainty and possible harm.","zh":"這個短語著重控制不確定性和可能傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"significant issue","meaning":"重大問題","examples":[{"en":"One person may see a hazard as a significant issue.","zh":"一個人可能把某項危害視為重大問題。"},{"en":"A significant issue is an important problem that deserves attention.","zh":"significant issue 指值得關注的重要問題。"},{"en":"Poor lighting near a staircase is a significant issue because people may fall.","zh":"樓梯附近照明不足是重大問題，因為人們可能跌倒。"},{"en":"If an issue is significant, managers should not dismiss it as a minor complaint.","zh":"如果一個問題重大，管理人員不應把它當作小投訴而忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a matter that could have serious effects.","zh":"這個短語描述可能有嚴重影響的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"acceptable feature of","meaning":"……可接受的特徵","examples":[{"en":"Another person may see the same hazard as an acceptable feature of the workplace.","zh":"另一個人可能把同一危害視為工作場所可接受的特徵。"},{"en":"An acceptable feature of something is a part that people think is normal or tolerable in that setting.","zh":"acceptable feature of something 指人們認為在該環境中正常或可容忍的一部分。"},{"en":"Some noise may be an acceptable feature of a busy café, but not of a library.","zh":"一些噪音可以是繁忙咖啡店可接受的特徵，但不是圖書館可接受的特徵。"},{"en":"What seems acceptable to one person may feel unsafe to another.","zh":"對一個人來說可接受的事情，對另一個人可能感覺不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how judgement can differ by context and person.","zh":"這個短語顯示判斷會因語境和人物而不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"allow for","meaning":"使……成為可能；容許有……","examples":[{"en":"Risk assessment tables allow for a degree of uniformity.","zh":"風險評估表使某程度的一致性成為可能。"},{"en":"To allow for something means to make it possible or to include it in a plan.","zh":"allow for something 指使某事成為可能，或在計劃中包括它。"},{"en":"A school timetable should allow for lunch breaks and travel time between classrooms.","zh":"學校時間表應容許有午膳休息和課室之間的移動時間。"},{"en":"Clear forms allow for more consistent decisions because everyone uses the same categories.","zh":"清楚表格能帶來更一致的決定，因為每個人使用相同分類。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making room for a result, need, or condition.","zh":"這個短語描述為某結果、需要或條件留有空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a degree of uniformity","meaning":"某程度的一致性","examples":[{"en":"The tables create a degree of uniformity in hazard assessment.","zh":"這些表格在危害評估中創造某程度的一致性。"},{"en":"A degree of uniformity means some consistency, though not perfect sameness.","zh":"a degree of uniformity 指某種一致性，但不是完全相同。"},{"en":"A marking scheme gives teachers a degree of uniformity when grading essays.","zh":"評分準則讓老師批改作文時有某程度的一致性。"},{"en":"Uniformity helps reduce unfair differences between people’s judgements.","zh":"一致性幫助減少人們判斷之間的不公平差異。"},{"en":"This phrase describes partial consistency across decisions or actions.","zh":"這個短語描述決定或行動之間的部分一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be rated using","meaning":"使用……評級","examples":[{"en":"Hazards are rated using risk assessment tables.","zh":"危害使用風險評估表評級。"},{"en":"To be rated using something means to be judged or scored with a particular tool or method.","zh":"be rated using something 指使用某工具或方法被判斷或評分。"},{"en":"Students’ presentations may be rated using a checklist for content, fluency, and eye contact.","zh":"學生演講可能使用內容、流暢度和眼神接觸清單評級。"},{"en":"Rating with a shared tool makes comparison easier and fairer.","zh":"使用共同工具評級，令比較更容易且更公平。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a score or judgement is produced.","zh":"這個短語描述分數或判斷如何產生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"risk assessment tables","meaning":"風險評估表","examples":[{"en":"Risk assessment tables help companies compare hazards more consistently.","zh":"風險評估表幫助公司更一致地比較危害。"},{"en":"Risk assessment tables are charts that help people score risks by exposure, likelihood, and possible effects.","zh":"risk assessment tables 指幫助人們根據暴露程度、可能性和可能後果為風險評分的圖表。"},{"en":"A school may use risk assessment tables before approving a camp or sports competition.","zh":"學校可能在批准露營或體育比賽前使用風險評估表。"},{"en":"These tables reduce guesswork by giving people shared categories and numbers.","zh":"這些表格透過提供共同類別和數字，減少猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to tools used to judge and compare danger.","zh":"這個短語指用來判斷和比較危險的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"work by","meaning":"透過……運作","examples":[{"en":"These tables work by assigning point values to three areas.","zh":"這些表格透過為三個範疇分配分值來運作。"},{"en":"To work by doing something means to function through that method.","zh":"work by doing something 指透過某方法運作。"},{"en":"A library booking system works by letting students reserve seats online.","zh":"圖書館預約系統透過讓學生網上預留座位來運作。"},{"en":"Explaining how something works helps users understand the steps behind the result.","zh":"解釋某物如何運作，幫助使用者理解結果背後的步驟。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a system with the method it uses.","zh":"這個短語把系統與其使用的方法連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"assign a point value to","meaning":"給……分配分值","examples":[{"en":"The table assigns a point value to each risk factor.","zh":"表格給每項風險因素分配分值。"},{"en":"To assign a point value to something means to give it a number for scoring or comparison.","zh":"assign a point value to something 指給某事一個數字，以便評分或比較。"},{"en":"A teacher may assign a point value to grammar, vocabulary, and organisation in an essay rubric.","zh":"老師可能在作文評分準則中給文法、詞彙和組織分配分值。"},{"en":"Point values help people compare things that would otherwise be judged only by feeling.","zh":"分值幫助人們比較本來只能靠感覺判斷的事物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes turning judgement into a number.","zh":"這個短語描述把判斷轉化成數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"exposure score","meaning":"暴露分數","examples":[{"en":"The exposure score assesses how often people face the hazard.","zh":"暴露分數評估人們有多經常面對該危害。"},{"en":"An exposure score is a number that shows how often or how long people come into contact with a hazard.","zh":"exposure score 指顯示人們有多頻密或多長時間接觸危害的數字。"},{"en":"A cleaner who uses strong chemicals every day would receive a higher exposure score than someone who uses them once a year.","zh":"每天使用強力化學品的清潔工，暴露分數會比一年使用一次的人高。"},{"en":"Frequent exposure raises risk because there are more chances for something to go wrong.","zh":"頻密暴露會提高風險，因為出錯機會更多。"},{"en":"This phrase measures contact with danger.","zh":"這個短語量度與危險的接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"assess how often","meaning":"評估……有多頻密","examples":[{"en":"The exposure score assesses how often employees are exposed to a hazard.","zh":"暴露分數評估員工有多頻密地暴露於危害。"},{"en":"To assess how often something happens means to judge its frequency.","zh":"assess how often something happens 指判斷某事發生的頻率。"},{"en":"A doctor may assess how often a patient feels pain before choosing treatment.","zh":"醫生在選擇治療前，可能評估病人有多頻密感到疼痛。"},{"en":"Frequency matters because a rare risk and a daily risk should not be treated the same way.","zh":"頻率很重要，因為罕見風險和每日風險不應以同一方式處理。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on measuring how repeated something is.","zh":"這個短語著重量度某事有多反覆。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be exposed to","meaning":"暴露於……；接觸到……","examples":[{"en":"Employees may be exposed to the hazard continuously.","zh":"員工可能持續暴露於該危害。"},{"en":"To be exposed to something means to come into contact with it or be affected by it.","zh":"be exposed to something 指接觸到某事或受其影響。"},{"en":"Students may be exposed to loud noise during construction near the school.","zh":"學校附近施工時，學生可能暴露於巨大噪音。"},{"en":"Long exposure to danger can increase the chance of injury.","zh":"長時間暴露於危險可以增加受傷機會。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for risks, chemicals, noise, disease, or new experiences.","zh":"這個短語常用於風險、化學品、噪音、疾病或新經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"face the risk continuously","meaning":"持續面對風險","examples":[{"en":"If employees face the risk continuously, the exposure score will be high.","zh":"如果員工持續面對風險，暴露分數會很高。"},{"en":"To face the risk continuously means to be in danger all the time or for long periods.","zh":"face the risk continuously 指一直或長時間處於危險之中。"},{"en":"A nurse may face the risk continuously during an outbreak if patients arrive all day.","zh":"疫情爆發期間，如果病人整天到來，護士可能持續面對風險。"},{"en":"Continuous risk requires stronger controls because workers have little time away from danger.","zh":"持續風險需要更強控制，因為工人很少有時間離開危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated or constant exposure to harm.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆或持續暴露於傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"very rare","meaning":"非常罕見","examples":[{"en":"If exposure is very rare, the score will be much lower.","zh":"如果暴露非常罕見，分數會低得多。"},{"en":"Very rare means happening only a few times or almost never.","zh":"very rare 指只發生很少次或幾乎從不發生。"},{"en":"Snow is very rare in many tropical cities.","zh":"在許多熱帶城市，下雪非常罕見。"},{"en":"A very rare hazard may still need planning if its effects would be serious.","zh":"非常罕見的危害如果後果嚴重，仍可能需要規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes low frequency, not zero possibility.","zh":"這個短語描述低頻率，而不是完全不可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"substantially lower","meaning":"大幅較低","examples":[{"en":"Rare exposure receives a substantially lower score.","zh":"罕見暴露會得到大幅較低的分數。"},{"en":"Substantially lower means much lower, not just slightly lower.","zh":"substantially lower 指低很多，而不是只低一點。"},{"en":"A student who revises daily may have substantially lower stress before exams.","zh":"每天溫習的學生在考試前可能有大幅較低的壓力。"},{"en":"Lower exposure can produce a substantially lower risk score because danger is faced less often.","zh":"較低暴露可以產生大幅較低的風險分數，因為面對危險的次數較少。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a clear and meaningful reduction.","zh":"這個短語突出清楚而有意義的下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be multiplied by","meaning":"乘以……","examples":[{"en":"The exposure score is multiplied by the likelihood of injury.","zh":"暴露分數乘以受傷的可能性。"},{"en":"To be multiplied by a number means to be increased according to that number in a calculation.","zh":"be multiplied by a number 指在計算中按照該數字相乘。"},{"en":"In maths, five multiplied by three gives fifteen.","zh":"在數學中，五乘以三等於十五。"},{"en":"In risk assessment, multiplying scores combines different parts of risk into one result.","zh":"在風險評估中，相乘分數把風險的不同部分結合成一個結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when explaining a mathematical calculation.","zh":"這個短語用於解釋數學計算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"likelihood of","meaning":"……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"The calculation includes the likelihood of the hazard causing an injury.","zh":"計算包括該危害造成受傷的可能性。"},{"en":"The likelihood of something means the chance or probability that it will happen.","zh":"likelihood of something 指某事發生的機會或概率。"},{"en":"A doctor may discuss the likelihood of side effects before giving medicine.","zh":"醫生在給藥前可能討論副作用的可能性。"},{"en":"If the likelihood of an accident is high, managers should act quickly.","zh":"如果意外發生的可能性高，管理人員應迅速行動。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on probability.","zh":"這個短語著重概率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ranging from…down to…","meaning":"由……至……不等","examples":[{"en":"The likelihood ranges from “Definite” down to “Unlikely”.","zh":"可能性由「肯定會發生」至「不大可能」不等。"},{"en":"Ranging from…down to… shows a scale from a high level to a lower level.","zh":"ranging from…down to… 顯示由高水平到較低水平的尺度。"},{"en":"Test scores may range from excellent down to fail.","zh":"測驗分數可能由優異至不合格不等。"},{"en":"This structure helps show the full set of possible levels.","zh":"這個結構幫助顯示所有可能等級。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing categories in an assessment table.","zh":"它適合用於描述評估表中的分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"all the time","meaning":"經常；一直","examples":[{"en":"A definite risk happens all the time.","zh":"肯定會發生的風險經常出現。"},{"en":"All the time means very often or continuously.","zh":"all the time 指非常頻繁或持續地。"},{"en":"If a student leaves homework until the last minute all the time, stress will build up.","zh":"如果學生經常把功課留到最後一刻，壓力會累積。"},{"en":"A risk that happens all the time needs urgent control because people face it repeatedly.","zh":"經常出現的風險需要緊急控制，因為人們反覆面對它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something frequent, not occasional.","zh":"這個短語描述頻密發生，而不是偶爾發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be referred to as","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"This part of the calculation is referred to as the chances rating.","zh":"計算的這一部分被稱為機會評級。"},{"en":"To be referred to as something means to be called by that name.","zh":"be referred to as something 指被稱作某名稱。"},{"en":"The final check before an exam is often referred to as revision.","zh":"考試前最後檢查通常被稱為溫習。"},{"en":"Clear names help people discuss complicated processes more easily.","zh":"清楚名稱幫助人們更容易討論複雜過程。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a term used for something.","zh":"這個短語引入某事物所使用的名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"chances rating","meaning":"機會評級；發生機會評分","examples":[{"en":"The chances rating measures the probability of injury.","zh":"機會評級量度受傷的概率。"},{"en":"A chances rating is a score that shows how likely an accident or injury is.","zh":"chances rating 指顯示意外或受傷有多可能發生的分數。"},{"en":"A wet staircase used by hundreds of students may receive a high chances rating.","zh":"每天有數百名學生使用的濕滑樓梯，可能得到高機會評級。"},{"en":"The higher the chances rating, the more likely the hazard is to cause harm.","zh":"機會評級越高，危害造成傷害的可能性越大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the probability part of a risk assessment.","zh":"這個短語描述風險評估中的概率部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the product of","meaning":"……的乘積","examples":[{"en":"The product of the first two scores is then multiplied by the effects score.","zh":"前兩個分數的乘積之後乘以後果分數。"},{"en":"The product of two numbers is the result you get when you multiply them.","zh":"product of two numbers 指兩個數字相乘所得的結果。"},{"en":"In maths homework, the product of six and four is twenty-four.","zh":"在數學功課中，六和四的乘積是二十四。"},{"en":"The product of two scores can then be used in a larger calculation.","zh":"兩個分數的乘積可以再用於更大的計算。"},{"en":"This phrase is a mathematical term for a multiplication result.","zh":"這個短語是指相乘結果的數學術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"effects score","meaning":"後果分數","examples":[{"en":"The effects score considers how serious an accident might be.","zh":"後果分數考慮意外可能有多嚴重。"},{"en":"An effects score is a number that shows the possible severity of an accident’s consequences.","zh":"effects score 指顯示意外後果可能有多嚴重的數字。"},{"en":"A paper cut would have a low effects score, but a chemical explosion would have a high one.","zh":"紙張割傷會有低後果分數，但化學爆炸會有高後果分數。"},{"en":"A high effects score means the result could be very harmful even if the accident is not frequent.","zh":"高後果分數表示即使意外並不頻繁，結果仍可能非常有害。"},{"en":"This phrase measures seriousness rather than frequency.","zh":"這個短語量度嚴重性，而不是頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"how serious something might be","meaning":"……可能有多嚴重","examples":[{"en":"The effects score measures how serious an accident might be.","zh":"後果分數量度意外可能有多嚴重。"},{"en":"How serious something might be means the possible level of harm, damage, or importance.","zh":"how serious something might be 指傷害、損壞或重要性的可能程度。"},{"en":"A doctor checks symptoms to decide how serious an illness might be.","zh":"醫生檢查症狀，以判斷疾病可能有多嚴重。"},{"en":"Judging seriousness helps people decide whether immediate action is needed.","zh":"判斷嚴重程度幫助人們決定是否需要即時行動。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on possible severity.","zh":"這個短語著重可能的嚴重性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"minor first aid","meaning":"輕微急救","examples":[{"en":"A minor injury may require only minor first aid.","zh":"輕傷可能只需要輕微急救。"},{"en":"Minor first aid is simple medical help for small injuries, such as cleaning a cut or applying a plaster.","zh":"minor first aid 指對小傷口提供的簡單醫療幫助，例如清潔傷口或貼膠布。"},{"en":"A student with a small scratch may need minor first aid from the school nurse.","zh":"有小擦傷的學生可能需要校護提供輕微急救。"},{"en":"Minor first aid treats small problems before they become infected or worse.","zh":"輕微急救會在小問題感染或惡化前處理它們。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to basic care, not hospital treatment.","zh":"這個短語指基本護理，而不是醫院治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"right up to","meaning":"一直到；甚至達至","examples":[{"en":"The effects score ranges from minor first aid right up to multiple deaths.","zh":"後果分數由輕微急救一直到多人死亡不等。"},{"en":"Right up to means all the way to the highest, most extreme, or final point mentioned.","zh":"right up to 指一直延伸到所提及的最高、最極端或最後一點。"},{"en":"The course covers basic grammar right up to advanced essay structure.","zh":"課程涵蓋基本文法，一直到高階作文結構。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the full range from small to serious.","zh":"這個短語顯示由輕微到嚴重的完整範圍。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing a scale with very different levels.","zh":"它適合用於描述有非常不同等級的尺度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"multiple deaths","meaning":"多人死亡","examples":[{"en":"The highest effects score is given for multiple deaths.","zh":"多人死亡會被給予最高後果分數。"},{"en":"Multiple deaths means more than one person dies in the same accident or event.","zh":"multiple deaths 指在同一意外或事件中多於一人死亡。"},{"en":"A building fire can lead to multiple deaths if exits are blocked.","zh":"如果出口被堵塞，建築物火災可以導致多人死亡。"},{"en":"Hazards that could cause multiple deaths must be treated as extremely serious.","zh":"可能造成多人死亡的危害必須被視為極度嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the most severe human consequence.","zh":"這個短語描述最嚴重的人命後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be classed as","meaning":"被歸類為","examples":[{"en":"Multiple deaths are classed as a disaster.","zh":"多人死亡被歸類為災難。"},{"en":"To be classed as something means to be placed in a particular category.","zh":"be classed as something 指被放入某個特定類別。"},{"en":"A storm may be classed as severe if wind speeds pass a certain level.","zh":"如果風速超過某水平，風暴可能被歸類為嚴重。"},{"en":"Classifying problems helps organisations decide how urgently to respond.","zh":"將問題分類幫助機構決定回應的迫切程度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official or organised categorisation.","zh":"這個短語描述官方或有組織的分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"disaster","meaning":"災難","examples":[{"en":"Multiple deaths would be rated as a disaster.","zh":"多人死亡會被評為災難。"},{"en":"A disaster is a very serious event that causes great harm, damage, or loss of life.","zh":"disaster 指造成巨大傷害、破壞或人命損失的非常嚴重事件。"},{"en":"A major flood can be a disaster if homes, roads, and hospitals are badly affected.","zh":"如果房屋、道路和醫院受到嚴重影響，大型水災可以是災難。"},{"en":"Disasters require urgent action because normal routines may no longer work.","zh":"災難需要緊急行動，因為正常常規可能已不再有效。"},{"en":"This word describes a severe event, not a small problem.","zh":"這個詞描述嚴重事件，而不是小問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"final risk-assessment result","meaning":"最終風險評估結果","examples":[{"en":"The three scores give the final risk-assessment result.","zh":"三個分數給出最終風險評估結果。"},{"en":"A final risk-assessment result is the overall score or judgement after all risk factors are calculated.","zh":"final risk-assessment result 指所有風險因素計算後的整體分數或判斷。"},{"en":"A school may use the final risk-assessment result to decide whether an activity can go ahead.","zh":"學校可能使用最終風險評估結果來決定活動能否進行。"},{"en":"The final result helps managers compare different hazards and set priorities.","zh":"最終結果幫助管理人員比較不同危害並設定優先次序。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the completed outcome of the assessment.","zh":"這個短語指評估完成後的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in excess of","meaning":"超過","examples":[{"en":"A result in excess of 100 points requires caution.","zh":"結果超過 100 分需要謹慎處理。"},{"en":"In excess of means more than a stated number or amount.","zh":"in excess of 指多於某個指定數字或數量。"},{"en":"A school event with attendance in excess of 500 students needs extra crowd control.","zh":"出席人數超過 500 名學生的學校活動，需要額外人流控制。"},{"en":"When a score is in excess of a safety limit, action should be taken.","zh":"當分數超過安全限制，就應採取行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used with numbers.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常與數字一起使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"require caution","meaning":"需要謹慎處理","examples":[{"en":"A score above 100 requires caution.","zh":"超過 100 的分數需要謹慎處理。"},{"en":"To require caution means to need careful action because there may be danger or risk.","zh":"require caution 指因可能有危險或風險而需要小心行動。"},{"en":"A wet road requires caution because drivers may not stop quickly.","zh":"濕滑道路需要謹慎處理，因為司機可能不能迅速停車。"},{"en":"When caution is required, people should slow down and check conditions carefully.","zh":"當需要謹慎時，人們應放慢並仔細檢查情況。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that careless action could cause harm.","zh":"這個短語警告粗心行動可能造成傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be classed as high priority","meaning":"被列為高度優先","examples":[{"en":"A result of 200 or more is classed as high priority.","zh":"200 分或以上的結果會被列為高度優先。"},{"en":"To be classed as high priority means to be placed in the group that needs attention first.","zh":"be classed as high priority 指被放入需要首先處理的類別。"},{"en":"A leaking gas pipe would be classed as high priority in a school maintenance report.","zh":"漏氣喉管會在學校維修報告中被列為高度優先。"},{"en":"High-priority risks should be controlled before less serious issues.","zh":"高度優先的風險應在較不嚴重問題之前被控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes urgent classification.","zh":"這個短語描述緊急分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"high priority","meaning":"高度優先事項","examples":[{"en":"Serious hazards are treated as high priority.","zh":"嚴重危害會被視為高度優先事項。"},{"en":"High priority means something is important and should be dealt with before other matters.","zh":"high priority 指某事很重要，應在其他事情之前處理。"},{"en":"A student’s breathing difficulty is high priority for the school nurse.","zh":"學生呼吸困難對校護來說是高度優先事項。"},{"en":"High-priority problems receive attention first because delay could make them worse.","zh":"高度優先問題會先得到關注，因為延誤可能令它們惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes urgent importance.","zh":"這個短語描述迫切重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"consistently receive scores of","meaning":"持續獲得……分數","examples":[{"en":"Certain jobs consistently receive scores of over 200.","zh":"某些工作持續獲得超過 200 的分數。"},{"en":"To consistently receive scores of a certain level means to repeatedly get that score or higher in assessments.","zh":"consistently receive scores of a certain level 指在評估中反覆取得該分數或更高分。"},{"en":"A student who consistently receives scores of 90 or above is performing very strongly.","zh":"持續獲得 90 分或以上的學生表現非常強。"},{"en":"Consistent high scores show that the risk is not accidental or occasional.","zh":"持續高分顯示風險不是偶然或偶爾出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated assessment results.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆出現的評估結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fire-fighting","meaning":"消防工作","examples":[{"en":"Fire-fighting often receives a high risk score.","zh":"消防工作經常得到高風險分數。"},{"en":"Fire-fighting is the work of controlling and putting out fires, often in dangerous conditions.","zh":"fire-fighting 指控制和撲滅火災的工作，通常在危險環境中進行。"},{"en":"Fire-fighting requires protective clothing, training, teamwork, and quick judgement.","zh":"消防工作需要防護衣物、培訓、團隊合作和快速判斷。"},{"en":"It receives high risk scores because firefighters may face smoke, heat, falling objects, and explosions.","zh":"它得到高風險分數，因為消防員可能面對濃煙、高溫、墜物和爆炸。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to dangerous emergency work involving fires.","zh":"這個短語指涉及火災的危險緊急工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"additional payments","meaning":"額外津貼","examples":[{"en":"Workers in dangerous jobs may receive additional payments.","zh":"從事危險工作的工人可能收到額外津貼。"},{"en":"Additional payments are extra money paid on top of normal wages or salary.","zh":"additional payments 指在正常工資或薪金以外額外支付的金錢。"},{"en":"A nurse may receive additional payments for working overnight or during public holidays.","zh":"護士可能因通宵工作或公眾假期工作而收到額外津貼。"},{"en":"Employers may offer additional payments to recognise risk, inconvenience, or extra responsibility.","zh":"僱主可能提供額外津貼，以承認風險、不便或額外責任。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to extra pay, not the basic salary.","zh":"這個短語指額外薪酬，而不是基本薪金。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"informally known as","meaning":"俗稱為","examples":[{"en":"These payments are informally known as “danger money”.","zh":"這些津貼俗稱為「危險津貼」。"},{"en":"Informally known as means commonly called by a name in everyday speech rather than in an official way.","zh":"informally known as 指在日常說話中常被稱為某名稱，而不是正式名稱。"},{"en":"The teacher’s quick grammar notes are informally known as “survival sheets” by students.","zh":"老師的快速文法筆記被學生俗稱為「救命紙」。"},{"en":"Informal names are often easier to remember than official terms.","zh":"非正式名稱通常比正式術語更容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a common, unofficial name.","zh":"這個短語引入常見的非官方名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"danger money","meaning":"危險津貼","examples":[{"en":"Danger money may be paid for high-risk work.","zh":"高風險工作可能會支付危險津貼。"},{"en":"Danger money is extra pay given to workers who do dangerous jobs.","zh":"danger money 指給予從事危險工作的工人的額外薪酬。"},{"en":"A worker repairing power lines during a storm may receive danger money.","zh":"在風暴中維修電線的工人可能收到危險津貼。"},{"en":"Danger money recognises that some jobs involve unusual risk of injury or death.","zh":"危險津貼承認某些工作涉及異常受傷或死亡風險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to pay linked directly to dangerous work.","zh":"這個短語指直接與危險工作相關的薪酬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"control hazards","meaning":"控制危害","examples":[{"en":"The third step is to control hazards that have been identified.","zh":"第三步是控制已識別的危害。"},{"en":"To control hazards means to reduce, isolate, or remove dangers so they cannot easily cause harm.","zh":"control hazards 指減少、隔離或移除危險，使它們不容易造成傷害。"},{"en":"A school controls hazards by fixing loose floor tiles and locking cleaning chemicals away.","zh":"學校透過修理鬆脫地磚和鎖好清潔化學品來控制危害。"},{"en":"Controlling hazards is necessary after identifying them because knowing about danger is not enough.","zh":"在識別危害後，控制危害是必要的，因為知道危險存在並不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical action against risk.","zh":"這個短語描述針對風險的實際行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hazard control","meaning":"危害控制","examples":[{"en":"There are three stages to hazard control.","zh":"危害控制有三個階段。"},{"en":"Hazard control is the process of removing, isolating, or reducing hazards.","zh":"hazard control 指移除、隔離或減少危害的過程。"},{"en":"A kitchen uses hazard control when knives are stored safely and hot surfaces are labelled.","zh":"廚房安全存放刀具並標示高溫表面時，就是在使用危害控制。"},{"en":"Hazard control reduces the chance that workers will be injured during normal tasks.","zh":"危害控制減少工人在日常任務中受傷的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the safety actions taken after hazards are found.","zh":"這個短語著重危害被找出後所採取的安全行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"eliminate the hazard","meaning":"消除危害","examples":[{"en":"The first aim is to eliminate the hazard.","zh":"第一個目標是消除危害。"},{"en":"To eliminate the hazard means to remove the danger completely.","zh":"eliminate the hazard 指完全移除危險。"},{"en":"A school can eliminate the hazard of a broken chair by taking it out of use.","zh":"學校可以透過停止使用損壞椅子來消除該危害。"},{"en":"Eliminating a hazard is usually better than only warning people about it.","zh":"消除危害通常比只是警告人們更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the strongest form of hazard control.","zh":"這個短語描述最強的危害控制形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"get rid of","meaning":"擺脫；清除","examples":[{"en":"To eliminate a hazard means to get rid of it altogether.","zh":"消除危害的意思是徹底清除它。"},{"en":"To get rid of something means to remove it or stop having it.","zh":"get rid of something 指移除某物或不再擁有它。"},{"en":"A family may get rid of expired medicine so children cannot take it by mistake.","zh":"家庭可能清除過期藥物，以免孩子誤服。"},{"en":"Getting rid of a hazard prevents people from coming into contact with it.","zh":"清除危害可以防止人們接觸到它。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in everyday English and means removing something unwanted.","zh":"這個短語常見於日常英語，意思是移除不想要的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"altogether","meaning":"完全地；徹底地","examples":[{"en":"The aim is to remove the hazard altogether.","zh":"目標是完全移除危害。"},{"en":"Altogether means completely or entirely.","zh":"altogether 指完全地或徹底地。"},{"en":"A student may stop using social media altogether during exam week.","zh":"學生可能在考試週完全停止使用社交媒體。"},{"en":"Removing a danger altogether is safer than leaving part of it behind.","zh":"徹底移除危險比留下其中一部分更安全。"},{"en":"This word stresses that nothing remains.","zh":"這個詞強調沒有任何東西留下。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be achieved by","meaning":"透過……達成","examples":[{"en":"This can be achieved by removing debris from the workplace.","zh":"這可以透過清除工作場所的碎屑和雜物達成。"},{"en":"To be achieved by doing something means to be successfully done through that action.","zh":"be achieved by doing something 指透過某行動成功做到某事。"},{"en":"Better exam results can be achieved by regular practice and clear feedback.","zh":"更好考試成績可以透過定期練習和清楚回饋達成。"},{"en":"A safety goal is achieved by practical action, not only by writing rules.","zh":"安全目標透過實際行動達成，而不只是透過寫下規則。"},{"en":"This phrase links a result with the method used to reach it.","zh":"這個短語把結果與達成它的方法連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"remove debris","meaning":"清除碎屑；清理雜物","examples":[{"en":"Companies can eliminate hazards by removing debris.","zh":"公司可以透過清除碎屑和雜物來消除危害。"},{"en":"To remove debris means to clear away broken pieces, waste material, or scattered objects.","zh":"remove debris 指清走破碎物、廢料或散落物件。"},{"en":"After a storm, residents remove debris from the road so cars can pass safely.","zh":"風暴後，居民清除道路上的雜物，讓車輛安全通過。"},{"en":"Removing debris prevents trips, falls, blocked exits, and machine damage.","zh":"清除碎屑和雜物可以防止絆倒、跌倒、出口堵塞和機器損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clearing physical mess that may create danger.","zh":"這個短語描述清理可能造成危險的實體雜亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"unnecessary obstacles","meaning":"不必要的障礙物","examples":[{"en":"Unnecessary obstacles should be removed from the workplace.","zh":"不必要的障礙物應從工作場所移除。"},{"en":"Unnecessary obstacles are objects or barriers that block movement without serving a useful purpose.","zh":"unnecessary obstacles 指阻礙移動但沒有實際用途的物件或障礙。"},{"en":"Bags left in a classroom walkway are unnecessary obstacles because students may trip over them.","zh":"放在課室通道上的書包是不必要的障礙物，因為學生可能被絆倒。"},{"en":"Removing unnecessary obstacles makes movement safer and faster.","zh":"移除不必要的障礙物令移動更安全和更快捷。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to things that create avoidable difficulty or danger.","zh":"這個短語指造成可避免困難或危險的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"often, however","meaning":"然而，很多時候","examples":[{"en":"Often, however, eliminating the hazard is not possible.","zh":"然而，很多時候，消除危害是不可能的。"},{"en":"Often, however introduces a contrast that happens frequently.","zh":"often, however 引入一個經常出現的對比。"},{"en":"A teacher may want to give every student personal feedback; often, however, time is limited.","zh":"老師可能想給每名學生個人回饋；然而，很多時候，時間有限。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the ideal solution is not always realistic.","zh":"這個短語顯示理想解決方案不一定現實。"},{"en":"It helps writers move from a general rule to a practical limitation.","zh":"它幫助作者由一般規則轉向實際限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"isolate the hazard","meaning":"隔離危害","examples":[{"en":"If the hazard cannot be removed, the next step is to isolate the hazard.","zh":"如果危害不能被移除，下一步就是隔離危害。"},{"en":"To isolate the hazard means to keep the danger away from people or normal work areas.","zh":"isolate the hazard 指把危險與人或正常工作區域分開。"},{"en":"A school isolates a hazard when it locks broken equipment in a storage room until it is repaired.","zh":"學校把損壞設備鎖在儲物室直到修理好，就是在隔離危害。"},{"en":"Isolation reduces risk by limiting access to the dangerous item or area.","zh":"隔離透過限制接觸危險物件或區域來降低風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes separating danger rather than removing it.","zh":"這個短語描述分隔危險，而不是移除危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"store it out of the way","meaning":"把它存放在不礙事的地方","examples":[{"en":"Hazardous material can be stored out of the way.","zh":"危險材料可以被存放在不礙事的地方。"},{"en":"To store it out of the way means to put it somewhere safe where it will not block or endanger people.","zh":"store it out of the way 指把它放在安全地方，使它不會阻礙或危害人。"},{"en":"A family may store sharp tools out of the way so children cannot reach them.","zh":"家庭可能把鋒利工具存放在不礙事的地方，讓孩子拿不到。"},{"en":"Storing dangerous items out of the way reduces accidental contact.","zh":"把危險物品存放在不礙事的地方，可以減少意外接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes safe placement, not disposal.","zh":"這個短語描述安全放置，而不是棄置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cleaning company","meaning":"清潔公司","examples":[{"en":"A cleaning company cannot completely eliminate hazardous chemicals.","zh":"清潔公司不能完全消除危險化學品。"},{"en":"A cleaning company is a business that provides cleaning services for homes, offices, schools, or public places.","zh":"cleaning company 指為家庭、辦公室、學校或公共場所提供清潔服務的企業。"},{"en":"A cleaning company may clean classrooms after school using detergents and disinfectants.","zh":"清潔公司可能在放學後使用清潔劑和消毒劑清潔課室。"},{"en":"Because cleaners often use chemicals, the company must store and handle them safely.","zh":"由於清潔工常使用化學品，公司必須安全存放和處理它們。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a service business that cleans places for clients.","zh":"這個短語指為客戶清潔地方的服務企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hazardous chemicals","meaning":"危險化學品","examples":[{"en":"Hazardous chemicals must be stored safely.","zh":"危險化學品必須安全存放。"},{"en":"Hazardous chemicals are substances that can harm people, property, or the environment if used or stored wrongly.","zh":"hazardous chemicals 指如果使用或存放不當，可能傷害人、財物或環境的物質。"},{"en":"Bleach, strong acids, and some cleaning fluids can be hazardous chemicals.","zh":"漂白水、強酸和某些清潔液都可以是危險化學品。"},{"en":"Poor storage of hazardous chemicals can lead to burns, poisoning, or dangerous fumes.","zh":"危險化學品存放不當可以導致灼傷、中毒或危險氣體。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to chemicals that need special care.","zh":"這個短語指需要特別小心處理的化學品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"keep something locked away","meaning":"把某物鎖好存放","examples":[{"en":"The company can keep hazardous chemicals locked away until required.","zh":"公司可以把危險化學品鎖好存放，直至需要使用時。"},{"en":"To keep something locked away means to store it behind a lock so only authorised people can access it.","zh":"keep something locked away 指把某物鎖起來存放，使只有獲授權的人能接觸。"},{"en":"Schools keep exam papers locked away before the test begins.","zh":"學校會在測驗開始前把試卷鎖好存放。"},{"en":"Keeping dangerous items locked away prevents careless or unauthorised use.","zh":"把危險物品鎖好存放，可以防止粗心或未獲授權的使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes secure storage.","zh":"這個短語描述安全存放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"until required","meaning":"直至需要使用時","examples":[{"en":"Chemicals should be kept locked away until required.","zh":"化學品應被鎖好存放，直至需要使用時。"},{"en":"Until required means until the time when something is needed for use.","zh":"until required 指直到某物需要被使用的時候。"},{"en":"Sports equipment should remain in storage until required for the lesson.","zh":"運動器材應留在儲物室，直至課堂需要使用時。"},{"en":"Keeping items away until required reduces clutter and accidental misuse.","zh":"把物品存放至需要使用時才取出，可以減少雜亂和意外誤用。"},{"en":"This phrase explains when something should be taken out or used.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物何時應被取出或使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"strictly enforced guidelines","meaning":"嚴格執行的指引","examples":[{"en":"Companies need strictly enforced guidelines for safe storage.","zh":"公司需要關於安全存放的嚴格執行指引。"},{"en":"Strictly enforced guidelines are rules that are not only written down but also actively checked and applied.","zh":"strictly enforced guidelines 指不只是寫下來，而且被主動檢查和應用的規則。"},{"en":"A school needs strictly enforced guidelines for fire drills so students do not treat them as jokes.","zh":"學校需要嚴格執行的火警演習指引，使學生不會把它們當作玩笑。"},{"en":"Guidelines only work when people follow them and managers enforce them.","zh":"指引只有在人們遵守並由管理者執行時才有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rules backed by real action.","zh":"這個短語描述有實際行動支持的規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"regarding","meaning":"關於","examples":[{"en":"The guidelines provide rules regarding safe storage.","zh":"指引提供關於安全存放的規則。"},{"en":"Regarding means about or concerning a particular subject.","zh":"regarding 指關於某個特定主題。"},{"en":"Parents received a notice regarding the new school bus arrangements.","zh":"家長收到一份關於新校車安排的通知。"},{"en":"This word is often used in formal writing to introduce a topic.","zh":"這個詞常用於正式寫作中引入主題。"},{"en":"It helps specify exactly what a rule, message, or discussion is about.","zh":"它幫助明確指出規則、訊息或討論關於甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"safe storage","meaning":"安全存放","examples":[{"en":"Safe storage is necessary for potentially hazardous products.","zh":"潛在危險產品有必要安全存放。"},{"en":"Safe storage means keeping items in a place and manner that prevents harm, damage, or misuse.","zh":"safe storage 指以防止傷害、損壞或誤用的地方和方式存放物品。"},{"en":"A family practises safe storage when medicine is kept away from young children.","zh":"家庭把藥物放在年幼孩子接觸不到的地方，就是實行安全存放。"},{"en":"Safe storage can prevent spills, theft, poisoning, and accidental injury.","zh":"安全存放可以防止洩漏、盜竊、中毒和意外受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to how dangerous or valuable items are kept securely.","zh":"這個短語指危險或貴重物品如何被安全保存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"potentially hazardous products","meaning":"潛在危險產品","examples":[{"en":"Potentially hazardous products must be stored carefully.","zh":"潛在危險產品必須小心存放。"},{"en":"Potentially hazardous products are items that may cause harm if handled, stored, or used incorrectly.","zh":"potentially hazardous products 指如果處理、存放或使用不當，可能造成傷害的物品。"},{"en":"Paint thinner, strong detergent, and pest spray are potentially hazardous products in many homes.","zh":"稀釋劑、強力清潔劑和殺蟲噴霧，是許多家庭中的潛在危險產品。"},{"en":"These products need labels and secure storage because people may not realise the danger.","zh":"這些產品需要標籤和安全存放，因為人們可能沒有意識到危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes products that are not always dangerous but can become dangerous.","zh":"這個短語描述不一定一直危險，但可能變得危險的產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"minimise the risk","meaning":"將風險減至最低","examples":[{"en":"If the hazard cannot be isolated, the company must minimise the risk.","zh":"如果危害不能被隔離，公司必須將風險減至最低。"},{"en":"To minimise the risk means to reduce the chance or seriousness of harm as much as possible.","zh":"minimise the risk 指盡可能減少傷害發生的機會或嚴重性。"},{"en":"Cyclists minimise the risk of injury by wearing helmets and using lights at night.","zh":"單車人士透過戴頭盔和夜間使用車燈，將受傷風險減至最低。"},{"en":"Risk may not disappear completely, but careful action can make it much lower.","zh":"風險可能不會完全消失，但小心行動可以大幅降低它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing danger when it cannot be fully removed.","zh":"這個短語描述在危險不能完全移除時減少危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be achieved through","meaning":"透過……達成","examples":[{"en":"Risk reduction is achieved through staff training and protective equipment.","zh":"風險降低是透過職員培訓和防護裝備達成的。"},{"en":"To be achieved through something means to be successfully reached by using that method or support.","zh":"be achieved through something 指透過某方法或支援成功達到。"},{"en":"Better classroom discipline can be achieved through clear rules and consistent follow-up.","zh":"更好的課室紀律可以透過清楚規則和一致跟進達成。"},{"en":"Safety improvements are achieved through action, not just discussion.","zh":"安全改善是透過行動達成，而不只是討論。"},{"en":"This phrase links a goal with the means used to reach it.","zh":"這個短語把目標與達成它的手段連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"staff training","meaning":"職員培訓","examples":[{"en":"Staff training helps employees handle hazards safely.","zh":"職員培訓幫助員工安全處理危害。"},{"en":"Staff training is instruction given to workers so they can do their jobs correctly and safely.","zh":"staff training 指給予工人的指導，使他們能正確和安全地完成工作。"},{"en":"A new restaurant gives staff training on food hygiene before workers enter the kitchen.","zh":"新餐廳在員工進入廚房前，會提供食物衛生職員培訓。"},{"en":"Training reduces accidents because workers know what to do and what to avoid.","zh":"培訓減少意外，因為工人知道應做甚麼和避免甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to teaching employees the knowledge and skills they need.","zh":"這個短語指教授員工所需知識和技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"safe handling techniques","meaning":"安全處理技巧","examples":[{"en":"Employees must learn safe handling techniques.","zh":"員工必須學習安全處理技巧。"},{"en":"Safe handling techniques are methods for lifting, carrying, using, or storing items without causing harm.","zh":"safe handling techniques 指在搬起、搬運、使用或存放物品時不造成傷害的方法。"},{"en":"Warehouse workers learn safe handling techniques so they do not injure their backs when lifting boxes.","zh":"倉庫工人學習安全處理技巧，避免搬箱時弄傷背部。"},{"en":"These techniques reduce accidents by teaching workers the safest way to perform tasks.","zh":"這些技巧透過教工人以最安全方式執行任務來減少意外。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical skills for dealing with materials or equipment safely.","zh":"這個短語指安全處理材料或設備的實用技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"best practices","meaning":"最佳做法","examples":[{"en":"Best practices help reduce workplace risks.","zh":"最佳做法幫助減少工作場所風險。"},{"en":"Best practices are the safest, most effective, and most accepted ways of doing a task.","zh":"best practices 指執行任務時最安全、最有效且最被接受的方法。"},{"en":"A school shares best practices when experienced teachers show new teachers how to manage a class.","zh":"當有經驗老師向新老師展示如何管理班級，學校就是在分享最佳做法。"},{"en":"Following best practices helps organisations avoid repeating known mistakes.","zh":"遵循最佳做法幫助機構避免重複已知錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to recommended methods based on experience and evidence.","zh":"這個短語指基於經驗和證據的建議方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"provision of","meaning":"……的提供","examples":[{"en":"The provision of protective equipment is part of hazard control.","zh":"提供防護裝備是危害控制的一部分。"},{"en":"Provision of something means supplying or making that thing available.","zh":"provision of something 指供應或提供某物。"},{"en":"The provision of clean drinking water is basic for any school event.","zh":"提供清潔飲用水是任何學校活動的基本要求。"},{"en":"Providing the right equipment allows people to follow safety rules properly.","zh":"提供合適設備讓人們能正確遵守安全規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in reports or policies.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於報告或政策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"personal protective equipment","meaning":"個人防護裝備","examples":[{"en":"Personal protective equipment protects workers from hazards.","zh":"個人防護裝備保護工人免受危害。"},{"en":"Personal protective equipment is clothing or equipment worn to reduce exposure to danger.","zh":"personal protective equipment 指穿戴或使用以減少接觸危險的衣物或設備。"},{"en":"Gloves, helmets, masks, and safety shoes are common forms of personal protective equipment.","zh":"手套、頭盔、口罩和安全鞋都是常見個人防護裝備。"},{"en":"PPE reduces injury by creating a barrier between the worker and the hazard.","zh":"個人防護裝備透過在工人與危害之間建立屏障來減少受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to protection worn by an individual worker.","zh":"這個短語指個別工人穿戴的保護裝備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"PPE","meaning":"個人防護裝備","examples":[{"en":"PPE commonly includes gloves, overalls and protective footwear.","zh":"個人防護裝備通常包括手套、工人工作服和防護鞋。"},{"en":"PPE is the abbreviation for personal protective equipment.","zh":"PPE 是 personal protective equipment 的縮寫。"},{"en":"In a laboratory, PPE may include goggles, gloves, and a lab coat.","zh":"在實驗室中，個人防護裝備可能包括護目鏡、手套和實驗袍。"},{"en":"PPE is important because it protects workers when hazards cannot be fully removed.","zh":"個人防護裝備很重要，因為當危害不能完全移除時，它可以保護工人。"},{"en":"This term is common in health, safety, construction, and medical settings.","zh":"這個術語常見於健康、安全、建築和醫療環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"commonly includes","meaning":"通常包括","examples":[{"en":"PPE commonly includes gloves and steel-reinforced footwear.","zh":"個人防護裝備通常包括手套和鋼頭安全鞋。"},{"en":"Commonly includes means usually contains or often has as part of it.","zh":"commonly includes 指通常包含或經常把某物作為其中一部分。"},{"en":"A school lunch commonly includes rice or noodles, vegetables, and a drink.","zh":"學校午餐通常包括飯或麵、蔬菜和飲品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes typical contents without saying every case is the same.","zh":"這個短語描述典型內容，而不是說每個情況都一樣。"},{"en":"It is useful when listing normal examples.","zh":"它適合用於列出一般例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"gloves","meaning":"手套","examples":[{"en":"Gloves are a common form of personal protective equipment.","zh":"手套是常見的個人防護裝備。"},{"en":"Gloves are coverings worn on the hands to protect them or keep them clean.","zh":"gloves 指戴在手上，用來保護雙手或保持清潔的覆蓋物。"},{"en":"A cleaner wears gloves when using strong detergent.","zh":"清潔工使用強力清潔劑時會戴手套。"},{"en":"Gloves can prevent cuts, burns, infection, and chemical contact.","zh":"手套可以防止割傷、灼傷、感染和接觸化學品。"},{"en":"This word refers to hand protection.","zh":"這個詞指手部保護用品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"overalls","meaning":"工人工作服；連身工作服","examples":[{"en":"Overalls protect workers’ clothing and skin.","zh":"工人工作服保護工人的衣物和皮膚。"},{"en":"Overalls are protective work clothes that cover much of the body.","zh":"overalls 指覆蓋身體大部分位置的防護工作服。"},{"en":"A mechanic may wear overalls to keep oil and dirt off ordinary clothes.","zh":"機械技工可能穿工人工作服，避免油污和塵垢沾上普通衣物。"},{"en":"Overalls reduce contact with dust, chemicals, or sharp materials.","zh":"工人工作服減少與塵埃、化學品或尖銳材料接觸。"},{"en":"This word refers to practical protective clothing used at work.","zh":"這個詞指工作中使用的實用防護衣物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"steel-reinforced footwear","meaning":"鋼頭安全鞋","examples":[{"en":"Steel-reinforced footwear protects workers’ feet.","zh":"鋼頭安全鞋保護工人的雙腳。"},{"en":"Steel-reinforced footwear is safety footwear strengthened with steel to protect toes and feet.","zh":"steel-reinforced footwear 指用鋼材加固、保護腳趾和雙腳的安全鞋。"},{"en":"Warehouse workers wear steel-reinforced footwear in case heavy boxes fall.","zh":"倉庫工人穿鋼頭安全鞋，以防重箱跌下。"},{"en":"This footwear reduces injury when workers handle heavy tools, materials, or machinery.","zh":"當工人處理重型工具、材料或機器時，這種鞋可減少受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to protective shoes for dangerous workplaces.","zh":"這個短語指危險工作場所使用的防護鞋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be connected","meaning":"互相關連","examples":[{"en":"The fourth and fifth steps in the plan are connected.","zh":"計劃中的第四和第五步互相關連。"},{"en":"To be connected means to be related or linked in some way.","zh":"be connected 指以某種方式相關或連接。"},{"en":"Attendance and exam results are often connected because absent students miss practice.","zh":"出席率和考試成績常互相關連，因為缺席學生會錯過練習。"},{"en":"Connected steps affect one another, so they should not be treated separately.","zh":"互相關連的步驟會互相影響，因此不應分開處理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a relationship between ideas, actions, or events.","zh":"這個短語描述想法、行動或事件之間的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"record and review","meaning":"記錄及檢討","examples":[{"en":"The final steps are to record and review the hazard.","zh":"最後步驟是記錄及檢討危害。"},{"en":"To record and review something means to write it down and check it again later.","zh":"record and review something 指把某事記下，並在之後再次檢查。"},{"en":"A teacher may record and review students’ common grammar mistakes after marking essays.","zh":"老師批改作文後，可能記錄及檢討學生常見文法錯誤。"},{"en":"Recording helps people remember what happened, while reviewing helps improve future action.","zh":"記錄幫助人記住發生了甚麼，而檢討幫助改善未來行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes documentation followed by checking.","zh":"這個短語描述先作文件記錄，再進行檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hazard register","meaning":"危害登記冊","examples":[{"en":"The hazard register records identified workplace hazards.","zh":"危害登記冊記錄已識別的工作場所危害。"},{"en":"A hazard register is a formal list or record of hazards found in a workplace.","zh":"hazard register 指工作場所中已發現危害的正式清單或記錄。"},{"en":"A school may keep a hazard register for broken equipment, unsafe areas, and chemical storage problems.","zh":"學校可能保留危害登記冊，記錄損壞設備、不安全區域和化學品存放問題。"},{"en":"A register helps managers track whether reported hazards have been fixed.","zh":"登記冊幫助管理人員追蹤已匯報危害是否已被修正。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the written record used in hazard management.","zh":"這個短語指危害管理中使用的書面記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be continually reviewed","meaning":"持續被檢討","examples":[{"en":"The hazard register is continually reviewed.","zh":"危害登記冊持續被檢討。"},{"en":"To be continually reviewed means to be checked again and again over time.","zh":"be continually reviewed 指隨時間一次又一次被檢查。"},{"en":"A school’s emergency plan should be continually reviewed after drills and real incidents.","zh":"學校的緊急計劃應在演習和真實事件後持續被檢討。"},{"en":"Continual review helps keep information accurate as conditions change.","zh":"持續檢討幫助資料在情況改變時保持準確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated checking, not a one-time inspection.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆檢查，而不是一次性檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ensure best practices are maintained","meaning":"確保維持最佳做法","examples":[{"en":"The register is reviewed to ensure best practices are maintained.","zh":"登記冊會被檢討，以確保維持最佳做法。"},{"en":"To ensure best practices are maintained means to make sure the safest and most effective methods continue to be used.","zh":"ensure best practices are maintained 指確保最安全和最有效的方法繼續被使用。"},{"en":"A head teacher checks lesson plans to ensure best practices are maintained across classes.","zh":"校長檢查教案，以確保各班維持最佳做法。"},{"en":"Regular review prevents good procedures from being forgotten over time.","zh":"定期檢討防止良好程序隨時間被忘記。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on keeping high standards in place.","zh":"這個短語著重保持高標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"severe accident","meaning":"嚴重意外","examples":[{"en":"If a severe accident occurs, investigators check the hazard register.","zh":"如果嚴重意外發生，調查人員會檢查危害登記冊。"},{"en":"A severe accident is a very serious accident that causes major injury, damage, or loss.","zh":"severe accident 指造成重大受傷、損壞或損失的非常嚴重意外。"},{"en":"A bus crash involving several injured passengers would be a severe accident.","zh":"涉及多名乘客受傷的巴士撞車會是嚴重意外。"},{"en":"Severe accidents require investigation because people need to know what went wrong.","zh":"嚴重意外需要調查，因為人們需要知道出了甚麼問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an accident far beyond a minor incident.","zh":"這個短語描述遠超輕微事件的意外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"occur in the workplace","meaning":"在工作場所發生","examples":[{"en":"A severe accident may occur in the workplace.","zh":"嚴重意外可能在工作場所發生。"},{"en":"To occur in the workplace means to happen where people work.","zh":"occur in the workplace 指在人們工作的地方發生。"},{"en":"Arguments, injuries, and equipment failures can occur in the workplace.","zh":"爭執、受傷和設備故障都可能在工作場所發生。"},{"en":"When an accident occurs in the workplace, employers may need to report and investigate it.","zh":"當意外在工作場所發生，僱主可能需要匯報和調查。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event inside a work setting.","zh":"這個短語把事件放在工作環境中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"investigators","meaning":"調查人員","examples":[{"en":"Investigators often consult the hazard register first.","zh":"調查人員通常首先查閱危害登記冊。"},{"en":"Investigators are people who examine facts to find out what happened and why.","zh":"investigators 指檢查事實以找出發生了甚麼以及原因的人。"},{"en":"After a fire, investigators may interview staff and check safety records.","zh":"火災後，調查人員可能訪問職員並檢查安全記錄。"},{"en":"Investigators help prevent future accidents by identifying causes and mistakes.","zh":"調查人員透過找出原因和錯誤，幫助防止未來意外。"},{"en":"This word refers to people who conduct formal inquiries.","zh":"這個詞指進行正式調查的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"consult first","meaning":"首先查閱","examples":[{"en":"Investigators often consult the hazard register first.","zh":"調查人員通常首先查閱危害登記冊。"},{"en":"To consult something first means to check or refer to it before doing anything else.","zh":"consult something first 指在做其他事之前先檢查或參考某物。"},{"en":"Students should consult the question first before reading a long passage in detail.","zh":"學生在仔細閱讀長文前，應首先查閱題目。"},{"en":"Consulting the right record first saves time and prevents guesswork.","zh":"首先查閱正確記錄可以節省時間並避免猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using a source as the first reference point.","zh":"這個短語描述把某資料來源作為第一個參考點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"previously reported","meaning":"之前曾被匯報","examples":[{"en":"Investigators check whether the issue had previously been reported.","zh":"調查人員檢查該問題之前是否曾被匯報。"},{"en":"Previously reported means mentioned, recorded, or brought to attention before the present time.","zh":"previously reported 指在目前之前已被提及、記錄或提出。"},{"en":"A broken window that was previously reported should already be in the maintenance record.","zh":"之前曾被匯報的破窗應已在維修記錄中。"},{"en":"If a hazard was previously reported but not fixed, the organisation may be blamed.","zh":"如果危害之前曾被匯報但沒有修正，機構可能被責備。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show whether people knew about a problem earlier.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示人們早前是否已知道問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"what the company had done about","meaning":"公司曾就……採取甚麼行動","examples":[{"en":"The register shows what the company had done about the hazard.","zh":"登記冊顯示公司曾就該危害採取甚麼行動。"},{"en":"What the company had done about something means the actions the company took to deal with it.","zh":"what the company had done about something 指公司為處理某事所採取的行動。"},{"en":"Parents may ask what the school had done about bullying after repeated complaints.","zh":"在反覆投訴後，家長可能詢問學校曾就欺凌採取甚麼行動。"},{"en":"Records show whether an organisation responded properly or ignored the problem.","zh":"記錄顯示機構是否妥善回應，還是忽視問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on past action taken in response to an issue.","zh":"這個短語著重過去為回應問題而採取的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"it is worth noting that","meaning":"值得注意的是","examples":[{"en":"It is worth noting that workplace accidents have declined significantly.","zh":"值得注意的是，工作場所意外已顯著下降。"},{"en":"It is worth noting that means the following point is important enough to mention.","zh":"it is worth noting that 指接下來的一點重要得值得提及。"},{"en":"It is worth noting that students who sleep well often perform better in exams.","zh":"值得注意的是，睡眠良好的學生考試表現通常更好。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to draw attention to a useful or surprising fact.","zh":"作者使用這個短語，引導讀者注意有用或令人驚訝的事實。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the reader should pay attention.","zh":"這個短語表示讀者應該留意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rigorous application of","meaning":"嚴格應用……","examples":[{"en":"The rigorous application of hazard-management systems has improved safety.","zh":"嚴格應用危害管理系統改善了安全。"},{"en":"Rigorous application of something means using it carefully, strictly, and consistently.","zh":"rigorous application of something 指仔細、嚴格且一致地使用某事。"},{"en":"The rigorous application of marking criteria helps teachers grade essays more fairly.","zh":"嚴格應用評分準則幫助老師更公平地批改作文。"},{"en":"Safety systems work better when they are applied rigorously rather than casually.","zh":"安全系統在被嚴格而不是隨意應用時，效果更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful and disciplined use of a method or rule.","zh":"這個短語描述對方法或規則的仔細而有紀律的使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hazard-management systems","meaning":"危害管理系統","examples":[{"en":"Hazard-management systems have reduced accidents in many industries.","zh":"危害管理系統已減少許多行業的意外。"},{"en":"Hazard-management systems are organised methods for identifying, assessing, controlling, recording, and reviewing workplace hazards.","zh":"hazard-management systems 指用來識別、評估、控制、記錄和檢討工作場所危害的有組織方法。"},{"en":"A factory may use hazard-management systems to track machine safety and chemical storage.","zh":"工廠可能使用危害管理系統來追蹤機器安全和化學品存放。"},{"en":"These systems reduce accidents because risks are handled before they cause harm.","zh":"這些系統減少意外，因為風險在造成傷害前被處理。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to complete safety systems, not one single rule.","zh":"這個短語指完整安全系統，而不是單一規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"workplace accidents","meaning":"工作場所意外","examples":[{"en":"Workplace accidents have declined in many high-risk industries.","zh":"許多高風險行業的工作場所意外已經下降。"},{"en":"Workplace accidents are unexpected harmful events that happen while people are working.","zh":"workplace accidents 指在人們工作時發生的意外有害事件。"},{"en":"Slips, burns, falls, and machine injuries are examples of workplace accidents.","zh":"滑倒、燒傷、跌倒和機器傷害都是工作場所意外的例子。"},{"en":"Fewer workplace accidents mean fewer injuries, less lost time, and lower costs.","zh":"較少工作場所意外意味較少受傷、較少時間損失和較低成本。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to accidents connected with work duties or work environments.","zh":"這個短語指與工作職責或工作環境相關的意外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"decline significantly","meaning":"顯著下降","examples":[{"en":"Workplace accidents have declined significantly in many industries.","zh":"許多行業的工作場所意外已顯著下降。"},{"en":"To decline significantly means to fall by a large and meaningful amount.","zh":"decline significantly 指大幅且有意義地下降。"},{"en":"A student’s stress may decline significantly after she plans revision earlier.","zh":"如果學生更早規劃溫習，她的壓力可能顯著下降。"},{"en":"Accident numbers decline significantly when safety systems are used properly over time.","zh":"當安全系統隨時間被妥善使用，意外數字會顯著下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear decrease, not a tiny change.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚下降，而不是微小變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"high risk","meaning":"高風險","examples":[{"en":"Some industries were previously identified as high risk.","zh":"有些行業之前被識別為高風險。"},{"en":"High risk means having a strong chance of harm, loss, or failure.","zh":"high risk 指有很大機會造成傷害、損失或失敗。"},{"en":"Working on a roof without safety equipment is high risk.","zh":"沒有安全裝備在屋頂工作是高風險。"},{"en":"High-risk activities need stronger planning, training, and supervision.","zh":"高風險活動需要更強規劃、培訓和監督。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a situation where danger is clearly above normal.","zh":"這個短語描述危險明顯高於正常水平的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"answer the questions below","meaning":"回答以下問題","examples":[{"en":"Students answer the questions below using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的詞語回答以下問題。"},{"en":"To answer the questions below means to respond to the questions printed after the passage or instruction.","zh":"answer the questions below 指回答文章或指示後面列出的問題。"},{"en":"In a worksheet, students should read the text first and then answer the questions below.","zh":"在工作紙中，學生應先閱讀文本，然後回答以下問題。"},{"en":"This instruction tells students where the task is and what they must do next.","zh":"這項指示告訴學生任務在哪裡，以及接下來必須做甚麼。"},{"en":"It is a common reading-test phrase.","zh":"這是常見的閱讀測驗短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個詞","examples":[{"en":"The answer must use no more than three words from the passage.","zh":"答案必須使用文章中不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer can contain one, two, or three words, but not four.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案可以有一個、兩個或三個詞，但不能有四個。"},{"en":"If the answer is “safe storage,” it follows the rule because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “safe storage”，它符合規則，因為它有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Students lose marks if they write too many words even when the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，學生寫太多詞也會失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is a word-limit instruction in reading tests.","zh":"這個短語是閱讀測驗中的字數限制指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"write your answers in boxes","meaning":"在方格內填寫答案","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write their answers in boxes on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生在答題紙方格內填寫答案。"},{"en":"To write your answers in boxes means to put each answer in the numbered spaces provided.","zh":"write your answers in boxes 指把每個答案寫在提供的編號空格中。"},{"en":"In an exam, students should write their answers in boxes clearly so markers can read them.","zh":"在考試中，學生應在方格內清楚填寫答案，讓評卷員能讀懂。"},{"en":"Writing in the correct boxes prevents answers from being marked under the wrong question.","zh":"寫在正確方格內可防止答案被當成另一題評改。"},{"en":"This phrase is a practical exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是實用考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"five stages of managing hazards","meaning":"管理危害的五個階段","examples":[{"en":"The five stages of managing hazards form a hazard-management plan.","zh":"管理危害的五個階段組成一項危害管理計劃。"},{"en":"The five stages of managing hazards are the ordered steps used to deal with workplace dangers.","zh":"five stages of managing hazards 指用來處理工作場所危險的有順序步驟。"},{"en":"A safety lesson may teach the five stages of managing hazards before students use workshop tools.","zh":"安全課可能在學生使用工作坊工具前，教授管理危害的五個階段。"},{"en":"Stages help people move from noticing danger to controlling and reviewing it.","zh":"階段幫助人們由注意危險，進展到控制和檢討危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the full process of hazard management.","zh":"這個短語描述危害管理的完整過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"collectively known as","meaning":"統稱為","examples":[{"en":"The five stages are collectively known as a hazard-management plan.","zh":"這五個階段統稱為危害管理計劃。"},{"en":"Collectively known as means that several things together are called by one shared name.","zh":"collectively known as 指幾件事合起來被稱為一個共同名稱。"},{"en":"Reading, writing, listening, and speaking are collectively known as language skills.","zh":"閱讀、寫作、聆聽和口語統稱為語言技能。"},{"en":"A shared name makes related parts easier to discuss as one system.","zh":"共同名稱使相關部分更容易作為一個系統來討論。"},{"en":"This phrase groups several items under one label.","zh":"這個短語把幾個項目歸入一個標籤之下。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"damaged machinery","meaning":"受損機器","examples":[{"en":"Damaged machinery is an example of harm to the organisation.","zh":"受損機器是對機構造成傷害的一個例子。"},{"en":"Damaged machinery means machines that have been broken or weakened and cannot operate normally.","zh":"damaged machinery 指被弄壞或削弱，不能正常運作的機器。"},{"en":"A damaged photocopier can delay printing for the whole school office.","zh":"受損影印機可以延誤整個校務處的打印工作。"},{"en":"Damaged machinery can cost money to repair and may stop production.","zh":"受損機器可能需要花錢維修，並可能令生產停止。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to equipment harmed by accident, misuse, or wear.","zh":"這個短語指因意外、誤用或磨損而受損的設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"examples of hazards to","meaning":"對……造成危害的例子","examples":[{"en":"Broken machinery and wasted resources are examples of hazards to the organisation.","zh":"損壞的機器和被浪費的資源，是對機構造成危害的例子。"},{"en":"Examples of hazards to something are cases that show how danger can harm that thing.","zh":"examples of hazards to something 指顯示危險如何傷害某事物的例子。"},{"en":"Data loss and power failure are examples of hazards to an online learning platform.","zh":"數據遺失和停電是對網上學習平台造成危害的例子。"},{"en":"Examples help people understand that hazards can damage organisations, not only people.","zh":"例子幫助人們理解危害不只會傷害人，也會損害機構。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces concrete cases of possible harm.","zh":"這個短語引入可能傷害的具體例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary with words from the passage.","zh":"學生用文章中的詞語完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill missing words in a short version of the text.","zh":"complete the summary 指在文本的簡短版本中填入缺失詞語。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole paragraph before they complete the summary.","zh":"學生應先閱讀整段，再完成摘要。"},{"en":"Completing a summary tests whether students understand meaning, grammar, and key details.","zh":"完成摘要測試學生是否理解意思、文法和關鍵細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common reading-exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"from Reading Passage 3","meaning":"來自閱讀文章第三篇","examples":[{"en":"The answers must be taken from Reading Passage 3.","zh":"答案必須來自閱讀文章第三篇。"},{"en":"From Reading Passage 3 means the answer must come directly from the third reading text.","zh":"from Reading Passage 3 指答案必須直接來自第三篇閱讀文章。"},{"en":"If the instruction says from Reading Passage 3, students should not use outside knowledge.","zh":"如果指示說來自閱讀文章第三篇，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase limits the source of the answer.","zh":"這個短語限制答案來源。"},{"en":"It reminds candidates to find evidence in the correct passage.","zh":"它提醒考生在正確文章中尋找證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"calculate a risk assessment","meaning":"計算風險評估","examples":[{"en":"Three scores are needed to calculate a risk assessment.","zh":"計算風險評估需要三個分數。"},{"en":"To calculate a risk assessment means to work out a risk score using numbers and set factors.","zh":"calculate a risk assessment 指使用數字和固定因素計算風險分數。"},{"en":"A safety officer may calculate a risk assessment before allowing students into a workshop.","zh":"安全主任可能在允許學生進入工作坊前計算風險評估。"},{"en":"Calculating risk helps people compare hazards more objectively.","zh":"計算風險幫助人們更客觀地比較危害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using a formula to judge danger.","zh":"這個短語描述使用公式判斷危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"mathematically","meaning":"以數學方式","examples":[{"en":"The risk assessment can be calculated mathematically.","zh":"風險評估可以以數學方式計算。"},{"en":"Mathematically means by using numbers, formulas, or calculation.","zh":"mathematically 指使用數字、公式或計算。"},{"en":"A teacher can show mathematically why two fractions are equal.","zh":"老師可以以數學方式顯示為何兩個分數相等。"},{"en":"When something is calculated mathematically, the result is less dependent on personal feeling.","zh":"當某事以數學方式計算，結果較少依賴個人感覺。"},{"en":"This word describes a number-based method.","zh":"這個詞描述基於數字的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"must be considered","meaning":"必須被考慮","examples":[{"en":"Three scores must be considered in the calculation.","zh":"計算中必須考慮三個分數。"},{"en":"Must be considered means must be thought about or included before a decision is made.","zh":"must be considered 指在作決定前必須思考或包括某事。"},{"en":"A student’s effort, accuracy, and organisation must be considered when giving detailed feedback.","zh":"給詳細回饋時，必須考慮學生的努力、準確度和組織。"},{"en":"Important factors must be considered because leaving them out can produce a wrong result.","zh":"重要因素必須被考慮，因為省略它們可能產生錯誤結果。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something cannot be ignored.","zh":"這個短語表示某事不能被忽略。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"amount of time","meaning":"時間長短","examples":[{"en":"The exposure score considers the amount of time spent near the hazard.","zh":"暴露分數考慮在危害附近逗留的時間長短。"},{"en":"Amount of time means how long something lasts or how long someone spends doing something.","zh":"amount of time 指某事持續多久，或某人花多久做某事。"},{"en":"The amount of time students spend reading affects their vocabulary growth.","zh":"學生花在閱讀上的時間長短會影響詞彙增長。"},{"en":"Longer time near danger usually increases exposure and risk.","zh":"在危險附近逗留越久，通常會增加暴露和風險。"},{"en":"This phrase measures duration.","zh":"這個短語量度持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"spend working near","meaning":"花時間在……附近工作","examples":[{"en":"Employees may spend time working near the hazard.","zh":"員工可能花時間在危害附近工作。"},{"en":"To spend time working near something means to do work close to that thing for a period of time.","zh":"spend time working near something 指在某物附近工作一段時間。"},{"en":"A cleaner may spend time working near strong chemicals while cleaning a toilet area.","zh":"清潔工清潔洗手間區域時，可能花時間在強力化學品附近工作。"},{"en":"The longer workers spend near a hazard, the more carefully the risk should be managed.","zh":"工人在危害附近工作越久，風險就越應被小心管理。"},{"en":"This phrase connects work duration with physical closeness to danger.","zh":"這個短語把工作時間與接近危險連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"probability of an accident","meaning":"意外發生的可能性","examples":[{"en":"The chances rating measures the probability of an accident.","zh":"機會評級量度意外發生的可能性。"},{"en":"The probability of an accident is the chance that an accident will happen.","zh":"probability of an accident 指意外會發生的機會。"},{"en":"The probability of an accident rises when students run on a wet floor.","zh":"當學生在濕滑地板上奔跑，意外發生的可能性會上升。"},{"en":"Measuring probability helps managers decide whether a risk is likely or rare.","zh":"量度可能性幫助管理人員判斷風險是可能還是罕見。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how likely an accident is.","zh":"這個短語著重意外有多可能發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"ranging from “Unlikely” to “Definite”","meaning":"由「不大可能」至「肯定會發生」不等","examples":[{"en":"The rating ranges from “Unlikely” to “Definite”.","zh":"評級由「不大可能」至「肯定會發生」不等。"},{"en":"Ranging from “Unlikely” to “Definite” means the scale moves from low probability to certainty.","zh":"ranging from “Unlikely” to “Definite” 指尺度由低可能性到肯定發生。"},{"en":"A weather forecast may range from “unlikely” rain to “definite” storms depending on the data.","zh":"天氣預報可能根據數據，由「不大可能」下雨到「肯定會有」暴風雨不等。"},{"en":"This range helps people place a risk between two clear extremes.","zh":"這個範圍幫助人們把風險放在兩個清楚極端之間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a probability scale.","zh":"這個短語描述概率尺度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be multiplied together","meaning":"相乘","examples":[{"en":"The exposure score and chances rating are multiplied together.","zh":"暴露分數和機會評級會相乘。"},{"en":"To be multiplied together means to be combined by multiplication.","zh":"be multiplied together 指透過乘法結合起來。"},{"en":"In maths class, length and width are multiplied together to find area.","zh":"在數學課中，長度和闊度相乘以找出面積。"},{"en":"Multiplying scores together can show how two risk factors combine.","zh":"把分數相乘可以顯示兩個風險因素如何結合。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a calculation step.","zh":"這個短語描述計算步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"resulting value","meaning":"所得數值","examples":[{"en":"The resulting value is multiplied by the effects score.","zh":"所得數值會乘以後果分數。"},{"en":"The resulting value is the number produced after an earlier calculation.","zh":"resulting value 指早前計算後產生的數字。"},{"en":"If students add all expenses first, the resulting value shows the total cost.","zh":"如果學生先把所有開支相加，所得數值會顯示總成本。"},{"en":"A resulting value can then be used in the next step of a formula.","zh":"所得數值可以再用於公式的下一步。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an intermediate calculation result.","zh":"這個短語指中途計算結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"degree of seriousness","meaning":"嚴重程度","examples":[{"en":"The effects score measures the degree of seriousness of an accident.","zh":"後果分數量度意外的嚴重程度。"},{"en":"Degree of seriousness means how severe or important something is.","zh":"degree of seriousness 指某事有多嚴重或重要。"},{"en":"A doctor checks the degree of seriousness before deciding whether a patient needs hospital care.","zh":"醫生在決定病人是否需要住院前，會檢查嚴重程度。"},{"en":"Higher seriousness usually means faster action and stronger control are needed.","zh":"嚴重程度越高，通常越需要更快行動和更強控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the level of severity.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重性的等級。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"more than one person is killed","meaning":"多於一人死亡","examples":[{"en":"The highest score is given when more than one person is killed.","zh":"當多於一人死亡時，會給予最高分數。"},{"en":"More than one person is killed means at least two people die in the same event.","zh":"more than one person is killed 指同一事件中至少兩人死亡。"},{"en":"A bus accident becomes far more serious if more than one person is killed.","zh":"如果多於一人死亡，巴士意外會變得嚴重得多。"},{"en":"When several lives are lost, the event is treated as a major disaster.","zh":"當多條生命喪失，該事件會被視為重大災難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very severe consequence.","zh":"這個短語描述非常嚴重的後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be considered high priority","meaning":"被視為高度優先","examples":[{"en":"A score of 200 or more is considered high priority.","zh":"200 分或以上的分數被視為高度優先。"},{"en":"To be considered high priority means to be judged as needing urgent attention.","zh":"be considered high priority 指被判斷為需要緊急關注。"},{"en":"A child with a serious allergy is considered high priority during a school lunch incident.","zh":"在學校午餐事件中，有嚴重過敏的孩子會被視為高度優先。"},{"en":"High-priority cases are handled first because delay may increase harm.","zh":"高度優先個案會先被處理，因為延誤可能增加傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a judgement about urgency.","zh":"這個短語描述對迫切性的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"complete the flowchart","meaning":"完成流程圖","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the flowchart using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的詞語完成流程圖。"},{"en":"To complete the flowchart means to fill in missing steps or labels in a process diagram.","zh":"complete the flowchart 指在流程圖中填入缺失步驟或標籤。"},{"en":"Students may complete the flowchart after reading instructions for making a product.","zh":"學生閱讀製作產品的指示後，可能完成流程圖。"},{"en":"Flowcharts test whether students understand sequence and cause-effect relationships.","zh":"流程圖測試學生是否理解順序和因果關係。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction for process texts.","zh":"這個短語是流程文章中常見的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"stages of hazard control","meaning":"危害控制階段","examples":[{"en":"The flowchart shows the stages of hazard control.","zh":"流程圖顯示危害控制階段。"},{"en":"Stages of hazard control are the ordered steps used to reduce or remove danger.","zh":"stages of hazard control 指用來減少或移除危險的有順序步驟。"},{"en":"A safety poster may show the stages of hazard control for handling broken glass.","zh":"安全海報可能顯示處理碎玻璃的危害控制階段。"},{"en":"Following the stages helps workers respond logically rather than panic.","zh":"跟從階段幫助工人有邏輯地回應，而不是恐慌。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the sequence of actions used to control hazards.","zh":"這個短語指用來控制危害的一系列行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"if possible","meaning":"如有可能","examples":[{"en":"The hazard should be eliminated if possible.","zh":"如有可能，危害應被消除。"},{"en":"If possible means if it can be done in the situation.","zh":"if possible 指如果在該情況下能做到。"},{"en":"Students should arrive early if possible so they have time to prepare.","zh":"如有可能，學生應提早到達，好讓自己有時間準備。"},{"en":"In safety work, removing danger is preferred if possible because it gives the strongest protection.","zh":"在安全工作中，如有可能，移除危險是較理想的，因為它提供最強保護。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the ideal action, while accepting that it may not always work.","zh":"這個短語顯示理想行動，同時承認它不一定總是可行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"protective clothing","meaning":"防護衣物","examples":[{"en":"Workers can minimise risk by wearing protective clothing.","zh":"工人可以透過穿防護衣物將風險減至最低。"},{"en":"Protective clothing is clothing worn to protect the body from injury, dirt, chemicals, or heat.","zh":"protective clothing 指用來保護身體免受受傷、污垢、化學品或高溫影響的衣物。"},{"en":"A science student wears protective clothing such as a lab coat and goggles during experiments.","zh":"科學學生在實驗期間會穿實驗袍和護目鏡等防護衣物。"},{"en":"Protective clothing reduces harm when workers must stay near a hazard.","zh":"當工人必須留在危害附近，防護衣物可以減少傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to clothing used for safety, not fashion.","zh":"這個短語指用於安全的衣物，而不是時裝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"follow safety training","meaning":"遵從安全培訓","examples":[{"en":"Employees minimise risk by following safety training.","zh":"員工透過遵從安全培訓將風險減至最低。"},{"en":"To follow safety training means to use the rules and methods learned during safety instruction.","zh":"follow safety training 指使用在安全指導中學到的規則和方法。"},{"en":"A new worker follows safety training when she lifts heavy boxes with the correct posture.","zh":"新工人用正確姿勢搬起重箱時，就是在遵從安全培訓。"},{"en":"Training only reduces risk if employees actually follow it during real work.","zh":"只有當員工在實際工作中真正遵從，培訓才會降低風險。"},{"en":"This phrase connects learning safety rules with applying them.","zh":"這個短語把學習安全規則與應用它們連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"action","meaning":"行動；措施","examples":[{"en":"The flowchart lists the action required at each stage.","zh":"流程圖列出每個階段所需的行動。"},{"en":"Action means what someone must do to deal with a situation or problem.","zh":"action 指某人為處理情況或問題必須做的事。"},{"en":"If a student sees smoke in the corridor, the correct action is to tell a teacher and leave safely.","zh":"如果學生在走廊看到煙，正確行動是告訴老師並安全離開。"},{"en":"Clear action steps help people respond quickly during an emergency.","zh":"清楚的行動步驟幫助人們在緊急情況中迅速回應。"},{"en":"This word focuses on doing something, not only thinking or noticing.","zh":"這個詞著重做事，而不只是思考或注意到。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 63 - HAZARD MANAGEMENT.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 64":[{"front":"low-cost lamps","meaning":"低成本燈具","examples":[{"en":"Low-cost lamps can bring reliable light to rural communities.","zh":"低成本燈具可以為農村社區帶來可靠照明。"},{"en":"Low-cost lamps are lamps that are cheap enough for poor families or communities to buy and use.","zh":"低成本燈具是貧困家庭或社區能夠負擔購買和使用的燈具。"},{"en":"A student in a village can study at night if her family has a low-cost lamp.","zh":"如果家中有低成本燈具，村裏的學生可以在晚上讀書。"},{"en":"Low-cost lamps can reduce spending on fuel because families no longer need to buy as much kerosene.","zh":"低成本燈具可以減少燃料開支，因為家庭不再需要購買那麼多煤油。"},{"en":"A lamp is only truly low-cost if families can afford both the purchase price and the maintenance.","zh":"只有當家庭負擔得起購買價和保養費，燈具才算真正低成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"light rural India","meaning":"照亮印度農村","examples":[{"en":"Low-cost lamps can help light rural India.","zh":"低成本燈具可以幫助照亮印度農村。"},{"en":"To light rural India means to provide reliable lighting for villages and homes in rural parts of India.","zh":"light rural India 指為印度農村地區的村落和家庭提供可靠照明。"},{"en":"A solar project can help light rural India by giving families lamps that work after sunset.","zh":"太陽能項目可以透過給家庭在日落後使用的燈具，幫助照亮印度農村。"},{"en":"Lighting rural India can improve study, safety, and evening work in villages.","zh":"照亮印度農村可以改善村落中的學習、安全和晚間工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improving daily life by bringing light to places without dependable electricity.","zh":"這個短語描述透過把光帶到沒有可靠電力的地方來改善日常生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rural India","meaning":"印度農村","examples":[{"en":"The project aims to bring light to rural India.","zh":"該項目旨在為印度農村帶來光明。"},{"en":"Rural India refers to villages and countryside areas in India, where many people work in farming or local trades.","zh":"rural India 指印度的村落和鄉郊地區，當中許多人從事農業或本地行業。"},{"en":"In rural India, some children still study at night with weak light from fuel lamps.","zh":"在印度農村，有些孩子晚上仍靠燃料燈的微弱光線讀書。"},{"en":"Poor electricity access in rural India can limit education, business, and healthcare.","zh":"印度農村電力不足可以限制教育、商業和醫療。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts village life with urban India.","zh":"這個短語把鄉村生活與印度城市地區作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"until three months ago","meaning":"直到三個月前","examples":[{"en":"Until three months ago, the village had no reliable electric lighting.","zh":"直到三個月前，該村落仍沒有可靠電力照明。"},{"en":"Until three months ago means the situation continued up to that time, but then changed.","zh":"until three months ago 指情況一直持續到那個時間，然後發生改變。"},{"en":"Until three months ago, the class had no online homework system.","zh":"直到三個月前，該班仍沒有網上功課系統。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show a clear before-and-after change.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示清楚的前後轉變。"},{"en":"If life improved after a new system arrived, “until three months ago” marks the old situation.","zh":"如果新系統到來後生活改善，“until three months ago” 標示舊情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"humble village","meaning":"簡陋村落","examples":[{"en":"Life in this humble village changed after solar lamps were installed.","zh":"太陽能燈安裝後，這個簡陋村落的生活改變了。"},{"en":"A humble village is a simple, modest village without many modern facilities.","zh":"humble village 指簡樸、樸素、沒有太多現代設施的村落。"},{"en":"A humble village may have small homes, dirt roads, and few public services.","zh":"簡陋村落可能有細小房屋、泥路和很少公共服務。"},{"en":"Solar lighting can transform a humble village by making evening study and work possible.","zh":"太陽能照明可以令簡陋村落轉變，讓晚間學習和工作成為可能。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests simplicity, not shame.","zh":"這個短語暗示簡樸，而不是羞恥。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"without electricity","meaning":"沒有電力","examples":[{"en":"Many rural villages still live without electricity.","zh":"許多農村村落仍然沒有電力生活。"},{"en":"Without electricity means not having access to electric power for lights, appliances, or machines.","zh":"without electricity 指沒有電力可供照明、電器或機器使用。"},{"en":"A family without electricity may be unable to use a fan, fridge, or computer at home.","zh":"沒有電力的家庭可能無法在家使用風扇、雪櫃或電腦。"},{"en":"Living without electricity can make study harder and limit evening activities.","zh":"沒有電力生活可以令學習更困難，並限制晚間活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a basic infrastructure problem.","zh":"這個短語描述基本基礎設施問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"come to a halt","meaning":"停頓下來","examples":[{"en":"Life in the village would come to a halt after sunset.","zh":"日落後，村裏的生活會停頓下來。"},{"en":"To come to a halt means to stop or slow down completely.","zh":"come to a halt 指停止或完全慢下來。"},{"en":"A school trip may come to a halt if the bus breaks down on the road.","zh":"如果巴士在路上故障，學校旅行可能停頓下來。"},{"en":"Without light, evening work can come to a halt because people cannot see clearly.","zh":"沒有光線，晚間工作可能停頓下來，因為人們看不清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes activity stopping because a necessary condition is missing.","zh":"這個短語描述活動因缺少必要條件而停止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"after sunset","meaning":"日落後","examples":[{"en":"Work and study often became difficult after sunset.","zh":"日落後，工作和學習通常變得困難。"},{"en":"After sunset means after the sun has gone down and the day has become dark.","zh":"after sunset 指太陽落山、天色變暗之後。"},{"en":"Children may need a lamp to finish homework after sunset.","zh":"孩子可能需要燈具在日落後完成功課。"},{"en":"If a village has no electricity, life becomes more limited after sunset.","zh":"如果村落沒有電力，日落後生活會變得更受限制。"},{"en":"The phrase often marks the time when lighting becomes necessary.","zh":"這個短語常標示照明變得必要的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mud-and-clay home","meaning":"泥土和黏土造的房屋","examples":[{"en":"The children used to study inside a mud-and-clay home.","zh":"孩子們過去常在泥土和黏土造的房屋裏讀書。"},{"en":"A mud-and-clay home is a simple house made mainly from earth, mud, and clay.","zh":"mud-and-clay home 指主要由泥土、泥和黏土建成的簡單房屋。"},{"en":"In a rural village, a mud-and-clay home may stay cool but may not have modern wiring.","zh":"在農村村落中，泥土和黏土造的房屋可能保持涼快，但未必有現代電線。"},{"en":"Children in such homes may need safe lamps because smoke from fuel lamps can harm their eyes and lungs.","zh":"住在這類房屋中的孩子可能需要安全燈具，因為燃料燈的煙會傷害眼睛和肺部。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a basic rural dwelling.","zh":"這個短語描述基本農村住所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"used to study","meaning":"過去常常讀書","examples":[{"en":"Ganpat Jadhav’s children used to study by a kerosene lamp.","zh":"Ganpat Jadhav 的孩子過去常常靠煤油燈讀書。"},{"en":"Used to study means they studied in that way regularly in the past, but the situation may have changed now.","zh":"used to study 指他們過去經常以那種方式讀書，但現在情況可能已改變。"},{"en":"A student used to study in the library before online lessons became common.","zh":"網課普及前，學生過去常常在圖書館讀書。"},{"en":"The phrase often helps compare an old habit with a new improvement.","zh":"這個短語常幫助比較舊習慣與新改善。"},{"en":"If children now study under solar light, “used to study” points to the older method.","zh":"如果孩子現在在太陽能燈下讀書，“used to study” 就指向較舊的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dim, smoky glow","meaning":"昏暗帶煙的微光","examples":[{"en":"The children studied in the dim, smoky glow of a kerosene lamp.","zh":"孩子們在煤油燈昏暗帶煙的微光中讀書。"},{"en":"A dim, smoky glow is weak light mixed with smoke, often from a burning fuel lamp.","zh":"dim, smoky glow 指微弱而帶煙的光，通常來自燃料燈。"},{"en":"A room lit by a dim, smoky glow may make reading slow and uncomfortable.","zh":"被昏暗帶煙微光照亮的房間，可能令人閱讀緩慢而不舒服。"},{"en":"This kind of light can strain the eyes and pollute indoor air.","zh":"這種光可以令眼睛吃力，並污染室內空氣。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests poor lighting that is both weak and unhealthy.","zh":"這個短語暗示既微弱又不健康的差劣照明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"kerosene lamp","meaning":"煤油燈","examples":[{"en":"A kerosene lamp was once the family’s main source of light.","zh":"煤油燈曾經是這個家庭的主要光源。"},{"en":"A kerosene lamp is a lamp that burns kerosene fuel to produce light.","zh":"kerosene lamp 指燃燒煤油燃料來發光的燈。"},{"en":"A shop without electricity may use a kerosene lamp during a blackout.","zh":"沒有電力的商店可能在停電時使用煤油燈。"},{"en":"Kerosene lamps can be useful, but they produce smoke and require regular fuel.","zh":"煤油燈可以有用，但會產生煙霧並需要定期補充燃料。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an older fuel-based lighting method.","zh":"這個短語指較舊的燃料照明方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"monthly fuel quota","meaning":"每月燃料配額","examples":[{"en":"The family’s monthly fuel quota ran out too quickly.","zh":"這個家庭的每月燃料配額太快用完。"},{"en":"A monthly fuel quota is a fixed amount of fuel a family is allowed or able to use each month.","zh":"monthly fuel quota 指家庭每月被允許或能夠使用的固定燃料數量。"},{"en":"A household may receive a monthly fuel quota of kerosene for cooking or lighting.","zh":"家庭可能每月收到煤油配額，用於煮食或照明。"},{"en":"If the quota runs out early, families must reduce lighting or find another source.","zh":"如果配額太早用完，家庭必須減少照明或尋找另一來源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a limited monthly supply.","zh":"這個短語描述有限的每月供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"run out","meaning":"用完；耗盡","examples":[{"en":"Their fuel quota ran out in just a fortnight.","zh":"他們的燃料配額短短兩星期內就用完。"},{"en":"To run out means to be used up completely so that none is left.","zh":"run out 指被完全用完，沒有剩下。"},{"en":"A student’s phone battery may run out before she gets home.","zh":"學生的電話電池可能在回家前耗盡。"},{"en":"When kerosene runs out, a family may lose its only evening light.","zh":"當煤油用完，家庭可能失去唯一晚間照明。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a supply reaching zero.","zh":"這個短語描述供應降至零。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in just a fortnight","meaning":"短短兩星期內","examples":[{"en":"The family used up four litres of kerosene in just a fortnight.","zh":"這個家庭短短兩星期內就用完四公升煤油。"},{"en":"In just a fortnight means in only two weeks, often faster than expected.","zh":"in just a fortnight 指只在兩星期內，通常比預期快。"},{"en":"A class may finish a whole project in just a fortnight if everyone works hard.","zh":"如果每個人努力，一班學生可能短短兩星期內完成整個項目。"},{"en":"Using up fuel in just a fortnight shows that the supply is not enough for a month.","zh":"短短兩星期內用完燃料，顯示供應不足以支撐一個月。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses how short the time period is.","zh":"這個短語強調時間很短。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"strain one’s eyes","meaning":"令眼睛吃力","examples":[{"en":"The children had to strain their eyes using the light from a cooking fire.","zh":"孩子們不得不靠煮食爐火的光讀書，令眼睛吃力。"},{"en":"To strain one’s eyes means to force the eyes to work too hard, often because the light is poor.","zh":"strain one’s eyes 指迫使眼睛過度用力，通常因為光線不足。"},{"en":"Students may strain their eyes if they read tiny words on a phone for hours.","zh":"如果學生長時間在電話上閱讀細小文字，可能會令眼睛吃力。"},{"en":"Poor lighting can strain children’s eyes and make study tiring.","zh":"差劣照明可以令孩子眼睛吃力，並使學習疲累。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that seeing clearly requires effort and may cause discomfort.","zh":"這個短語警告看清楚需要用力，並可能造成不適。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cooking fire","meaning":"煮食爐火","examples":[{"en":"They studied by the light from a cooking fire.","zh":"他們靠煮食爐火的光讀書。"},{"en":"A cooking fire is a fire used for preparing food, often in a simple stove or open area.","zh":"cooking fire 指用來準備食物的火，通常在簡單爐灶或開放地方。"},{"en":"In some villages, families gather around a cooking fire in the evening.","zh":"在一些村落，家庭晚上圍在煮食爐火旁。"},{"en":"A cooking fire can give some light, but it is not designed for reading or study.","zh":"煮食爐火可以提供一點光，但並非為閱讀或學習而設計。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to fire for cooking, not proper household lighting.","zh":"這個短語指煮食用火，而不是正式家居照明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"that all changed with","meaning":"這一切因……而改變","examples":[{"en":"That all changed with the installation of solar-powered lamps.","zh":"這一切因太陽能燈的安裝而改變。"},{"en":"That all changed with something means a situation became different because of that event or development.","zh":"that all changed with something 指情況因某事件或發展而變得不同。"},{"en":"The class used to lose papers easily; that all changed with the use of online folders.","zh":"這班學生過去常常弄丟紙張；這一切因使用網上資料夾而改變。"},{"en":"A new light source can change evening routines because people can work after dark.","zh":"新光源可以改變晚間日常，因為人們可以在天黑後工作。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the turning point in a story.","zh":"這個短語引入故事中的轉折點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the installation of","meaning":"……的安裝","examples":[{"en":"The installation of new lamps improved daily life in the village.","zh":"新燈具的安裝改善了村裏的日常生活。"},{"en":"The installation of something means the process of putting equipment in place so it can be used.","zh":"installation of something 指把設備安置好，使其可以使用的過程。"},{"en":"The installation of Wi-Fi in a school can make online learning easier.","zh":"學校安裝 Wi-Fi 可以令網上學習更容易。"},{"en":"Proper installation matters because equipment may not work safely if it is badly fitted.","zh":"正確安裝很重要，因為設備若安裝不良可能無法安全運作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to setting up a device or system.","zh":"這個短語指設置裝置或系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"energy-efficient lamps","meaning":"節能燈","examples":[{"en":"Energy-efficient lamps use much less power than conventional bulbs.","zh":"節能燈比傳統燈泡使用少得多電力。"},{"en":"Energy-efficient lamps are lamps that produce light while using relatively little electricity or fuel.","zh":"energy-efficient lamps 指用較少電力或燃料產生光的燈具。"},{"en":"A family may replace old bulbs with energy-efficient lamps to lower electricity bills.","zh":"家庭可能把舊燈泡換成節能燈，以降低電費。"},{"en":"Energy-efficient lamps reduce waste because more energy becomes light instead of heat.","zh":"節能燈減少浪費，因為更多能源變成光，而不是熱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lamps that save energy while still giving useful light.","zh":"這個短語描述既節省能源又提供有效光線的燈具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"powered entirely by the sun","meaning":"完全由太陽能供電","examples":[{"en":"The lamps are powered entirely by the sun.","zh":"這些燈完全由太陽能供電。"},{"en":"Powered entirely by the sun means using only solar energy, not electricity from the grid or fuel.","zh":"powered entirely by the sun 指只使用太陽能，而不是電網電力或燃料。"},{"en":"A garden light powered entirely by the sun charges during the day and shines at night.","zh":"完全由太陽能供電的花園燈在日間充電，晚上發光。"},{"en":"Solar power can lower running costs because sunlight itself is free.","zh":"太陽能可以降低運行成本，因為陽光本身免費。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the device depends fully on sunlight for energy.","zh":"這個短語顯示裝置完全依賴陽光作能源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be installed by","meaning":"由……安裝","examples":[{"en":"The lights were installed by the Grameen Surya Bijli Foundation.","zh":"這些燈由 Grameen Surya Bijli Foundation 安裝。"},{"en":"To be installed by someone means to be put in place and made ready to use by that person or organisation.","zh":"be installed by someone 指由某人或某機構放置並設置好，以便使用。"},{"en":"The school’s new computers were installed by a local IT company.","zh":"學校的新電腦由本地資訊科技公司安裝。"},{"en":"If lamps are installed by trained workers, they are more likely to work safely.","zh":"如果燈具由受過訓練的人員安裝，它們較可能安全運作。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who set up the equipment.","zh":"這個短語指出誰設置了設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"non-governmental organisation","meaning":"非政府組織","examples":[{"en":"GSBF is an Indian non-governmental organisation.","zh":"GSBF 是一個印度非政府組織。"},{"en":"A non-governmental organisation is a group that works on social, health, environmental, or development issues without being part of the government.","zh":"non-governmental organisation 指處理社會、健康、環境或發展議題，但不屬於政府的組織。"},{"en":"A non-governmental organisation may provide food, education, or medical support to poor communities.","zh":"非政府組織可能向貧困社區提供食物、教育或醫療支援。"},{"en":"NGOs often work where public services are weak or slow to reach people.","zh":"非政府組織通常在公共服務薄弱或難以及時到達的地方工作。"},{"en":"The phrase is often shortened to NGO.","zh":"這個短語常縮寫為 NGO。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be focused on","meaning":"專注於……","examples":[{"en":"The organisation is focused on bringing light to rural India.","zh":"該組織專注於為印度農村帶來光明。"},{"en":"To be focused on something means to give most attention and effort to that goal or activity.","zh":"be focused on something 指把大部分注意力和努力放在某目標或活動上。"},{"en":"A school programme may be focused on improving students’ reading confidence.","zh":"學校計劃可能專注於提升學生閱讀信心。"},{"en":"When an organisation is focused on one clear aim, it can use resources more effectively.","zh":"當組織專注於一個清楚目標，它就能更有效使用資源。"},{"en":"The phrase shows concentration of purpose.","zh":"這個短語顯示目標集中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"bring light to","meaning":"為……帶來光明","examples":[{"en":"GSBF aims to bring light to villages without electricity.","zh":"GSBF 旨在為沒有電力的村落帶來光明。"},{"en":"To bring light to a place means to provide lighting where there was little or none before.","zh":"bring light to a place 指為以前幾乎沒有照明或完全沒有照明的地方提供光。"},{"en":"A community project can bring light to a dark public path by installing solar lamps.","zh":"社區項目可以透過安裝太陽能燈，為黑暗公眾小路帶來光明。"},{"en":"Bringing light to homes can make study, cooking, and evening work safer.","zh":"為家居帶來光明可以令學習、煮食和晚間工作更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase can also suggest bringing hope and improvement.","zh":"這個短語也可以暗示帶來希望和改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"do not yet have electricity","meaning":"尚未有電力供應","examples":[{"en":"Some 100,000 Indian villages do not yet have electricity.","zh":"大約十萬條印度村落尚未有電力供應。"},{"en":"Do not yet have electricity means electricity has not reached those places so far, although it may arrive in the future.","zh":"do not yet have electricity 指到目前為止電力仍未到達那些地方，雖然未來可能會有。"},{"en":"Some mountain homes do not yet have electricity because cables are expensive to install.","zh":"一些山區住宅因安裝電纜昂貴而尚未有電力供應。"},{"en":"Places without electricity often depend on candles, fuel lamps, or solar devices.","zh":"沒有電力的地方通常依賴蠟燭、燃料燈或太陽能裝置。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a lack that may still be solved later.","zh":"這個短語暗示一種日後仍可能被解決的缺乏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"some 100,000","meaning":"大約十萬","examples":[{"en":"Some 100,000 Indian villages still lack electricity.","zh":"大約十萬條印度村落仍缺乏電力。"},{"en":"Some 100,000 means approximately 100,000, not necessarily the exact number.","zh":"some 100,000 指大約十萬，不一定是精確數字。"},{"en":"Some 2,000 students may attend a large university open day.","zh":"大約二千名學生可能參加大型大學開放日。"},{"en":"Writers use “some” before a number when they want to give an estimate.","zh":"作者在數字前使用 “some”，是因為想給出估算。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a large approximate figure.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個大約的大數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"LEDs","meaning":"LED；發光二極管","examples":[{"en":"The GSBF lamps use LEDs instead of conventional bulbs.","zh":"GSBF 燈具使用 LED，而不是傳統燈泡。"},{"en":"LEDs are small electronic lights that use energy efficiently to produce light.","zh":"LED 是細小電子燈，能有效使用能源產生光。"},{"en":"Many desk lamps, traffic lights, and phone screens now use LEDs.","zh":"許多書枱燈、交通燈和電話屏幕現在都使用 LED。"},{"en":"LEDs save power because they produce more light with less wasted heat.","zh":"LED 節省電力，因為它們用較少浪費的熱產生更多光。"},{"en":"The term is short for light-emitting diodes.","zh":"這個詞是 light-emitting diodes 的縮寫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"light-emitting diodes","meaning":"發光二極管","examples":[{"en":"LEDs are light-emitting diodes.","zh":"LED 是發光二極管。"},{"en":"Light-emitting diodes are electronic components that produce light when electricity passes through them.","zh":"light-emitting diodes 指電流通過時會產生光的電子元件。"},{"en":"A small torch may use light-emitting diodes because they are bright and efficient.","zh":"小型電筒可能使用發光二極管，因為它們明亮而有效率。"},{"en":"Light-emitting diodes are useful in villages because they can work with small solar systems.","zh":"發光二極管在村落中有用，因為它們可以配合小型太陽能系統運作。"},{"en":"The phrase is the full technical name for LEDs.","zh":"這個短語是 LED 的完整技術名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"more efficient than","meaning":"比……更有效率","examples":[{"en":"LEDs are more efficient than conventional bulbs.","zh":"LED 比傳統燈泡更有效率。"},{"en":"More efficient than means using less energy, time, or effort to produce the same or better result.","zh":"more efficient than 指使用較少能源、時間或努力來產生相同或更好的結果。"},{"en":"An online form can be more efficient than paper forms because it saves copying time.","zh":"網上表格可以比紙本表格更有效率，因為它節省抄寫時間。"},{"en":"Efficient lamps reduce energy waste and lower running costs.","zh":"高效率燈具減少能源浪費並降低運行成本。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly compares performance between two things.","zh":"這個短語清楚比較兩件事物的效能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"conventional bulb","meaning":"傳統燈泡","examples":[{"en":"An LED is more efficient than a conventional bulb.","zh":"LED 比傳統燈泡更有效率。"},{"en":"A conventional bulb is a traditional light bulb that usually uses more energy than newer lighting technology.","zh":"conventional bulb 指傳統燈泡，通常比新式照明科技使用更多能源。"},{"en":"A classroom may replace each conventional bulb with an LED to save electricity.","zh":"課室可能把每個傳統燈泡換成 LED，以節省電力。"},{"en":"Conventional bulbs often waste energy as heat, so they can cost more to run.","zh":"傳統燈泡通常把能源浪費成熱，所以運行成本可能更高。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to older, standard lighting technology.","zh":"這個短語指較舊、標準的照明科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"installation cost","meaning":"安裝費用","examples":[{"en":"After the installation cost, the lamp can be powered for free.","zh":"支付安裝費用後，該燈可以免費供電。"},{"en":"Installation cost is the money paid to set up equipment so it can be used.","zh":"installation cost 指為設置設備使其能使用而支付的金錢。"},{"en":"A family may pay an installation cost when technicians put solar panels on the roof.","zh":"當技術人員在屋頂安裝太陽能板，家庭可能需要支付安裝費用。"},{"en":"A high installation cost can stop poor households from adopting useful technology.","zh":"高安裝費用可以阻止貧困家庭採用有用科技。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the first setup expense, not daily running cost.","zh":"這個短語指初次設置開支，而不是日常運行成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"solar energy","meaning":"太陽能","examples":[{"en":"Solar energy powers the lamp free of charge.","zh":"太陽能免費為該燈供電。"},{"en":"Solar energy is energy from sunlight that can be converted into electricity or heat.","zh":"solar energy 指來自陽光、可轉化成電力或熱力的能源。"},{"en":"A school may use solar energy to power outdoor lights.","zh":"學校可能使用太陽能為戶外燈供電。"},{"en":"Solar energy can reduce fuel costs because sunlight does not need to be bought.","zh":"太陽能可以減少燃料成本，因為陽光不需要購買。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to energy that comes from the sun.","zh":"這個短語指來自太陽的能源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"free of charge","meaning":"免費","examples":[{"en":"The lamp is powered by solar energy free of charge.","zh":"該燈由太陽能免費供電。"},{"en":"Free of charge means without needing to pay money.","zh":"free of charge 指不需要付款。"},{"en":"A library may offer computer access free of charge to students.","zh":"圖書館可能免費向學生提供電腦使用。"},{"en":"If lighting is free of charge after installation, families can spend less on fuel each month.","zh":"如果安裝後照明免費，家庭每月可以花較少錢買燃料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes zero direct cost to the user.","zh":"這個短語描述對使用者而言沒有直接成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"another example of","meaning":"另一個……例子","examples":[{"en":"LED lighting is another example of useful low-cost technology.","zh":"LED 照明是有用低成本科技的另一個例子。"},{"en":"Another example of something means one more case that shows the same idea.","zh":"another example of something 指另一個能顯示同一想法的個案。"},{"en":"Online banking is another example of technology that saves people travel time.","zh":"網上銀行是科技節省人們交通時間的另一個例子。"},{"en":"Giving another example helps readers see that a point is part of a wider pattern.","zh":"提供另一個例子幫助讀者看見某重點屬於更廣泛模式。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful for adding evidence.","zh":"這個短語適合用來加入證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"low-cost technology","meaning":"低成本科技","examples":[{"en":"Low-cost technology can improve life for poor rural families.","zh":"低成本科技可以改善貧困農村家庭的生活。"},{"en":"Low-cost technology is technology that is cheap enough to be used by people or communities with limited money.","zh":"low-cost technology 指便宜到有限金錢的人或社區也能使用的科技。"},{"en":"A simple water filter can be low-cost technology if it gives clean water without expensive machines.","zh":"如果簡單濾水器不用昂貴機器就能提供清水，它就是低成本科技。"},{"en":"Low-cost technology matters because expensive solutions may never reach the poorest users.","zh":"低成本科技很重要，因為昂貴方案可能永遠到不了最貧困使用者手中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical innovation made affordable.","zh":"這個短語描述變得可負擔的實用創新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"allow someone to","meaning":"讓某人能夠……","examples":[{"en":"This technology could allow poor families to improve their living conditions.","zh":"這項科技可以讓貧困家庭改善生活條件。"},{"en":"To allow someone to do something means to make it possible for them to do it.","zh":"allow someone to do something 指使某人能夠做某事。"},{"en":"A scholarship can allow a student to continue studying instead of leaving school.","zh":"獎學金可以讓學生繼續讀書，而不是離開學校。"},{"en":"Solar lamps allow families to work and study after sunset.","zh":"太陽能燈讓家庭能夠在日落後工作和學習。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on creating opportunity.","zh":"這個短語重點是創造機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the rural poor","meaning":"農村貧困人口","examples":[{"en":"LED lighting could help the rural poor move into the modern age.","zh":"LED 照明可以幫助農村貧困人口進入現代時代。"},{"en":"The rural poor are people living in countryside areas with very limited income and resources.","zh":"rural poor 指住在鄉郊地區、收入和資源非常有限的人。"},{"en":"The rural poor may struggle to pay for electricity, clean water, or transport.","zh":"農村貧困人口可能難以支付電力、清水或交通費。"},{"en":"Low-cost technology can help the rural poor because it reduces everyday expenses.","zh":"低成本科技可以幫助農村貧困人口，因為它減少日常開支。"},{"en":"The phrase describes poverty in rural communities, not poverty in cities.","zh":"這個短語描述農村社區中的貧窮，而不是城市貧窮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"leap into the 21st century","meaning":"躍進21世紀","examples":[{"en":"Low-cost technology could help the rural poor leap into the 21st century.","zh":"低成本科技可以幫助農村貧困人口躍進21世紀。"},{"en":"To leap into the 21st century means to move quickly from old conditions into modern life or technology.","zh":"leap into the 21st century 指快速從舊狀況進入現代生活或科技。"},{"en":"A school without computers can leap into the 21st century by installing internet access and digital classrooms.","zh":"沒有電腦的學校可以透過安裝互聯網和數碼課室躍進21世紀。"},{"en":"Solar lamps help villages leap forward because they provide modern lighting without waiting for a full power grid.","zh":"太陽能燈幫助村落向前躍進，因為它們不用等待完整電網就能提供現代照明。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a fast jump in development.","zh":"這個短語暗示發展上的快速跳躍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"as many as","meaning":"多達","examples":[{"en":"As many as 1.5 billion people use kerosene to light their homes.","zh":"多達15億人使用煤油照亮家居。"},{"en":"As many as is used before a large number to show that the amount is surprisingly high.","zh":"as many as 用於大數字前，顯示數量高得令人驚訝。"},{"en":"As many as fifty students may join a popular school club in one week.","zh":"一個受歡迎的學校學會一星期內可能有多達五十名學生加入。"},{"en":"The phrase draws attention to the scale of a problem or trend.","zh":"這個短語把注意力引向問題或趨勢的規模。"},{"en":"It means “up to this large number”, not a small estimate.","zh":"它意思是「高達這個大數字」，而不是小估算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"nearly 80 million in India alone","meaning":"單在印度就接近八千萬","examples":[{"en":"Nearly 80 million in India alone use kerosene as their main lighting medium.","zh":"單在印度就接近八千萬人使用煤油作為主要照明媒介。"},{"en":"Nearly 80 million in India alone means almost 80 million people in India, not counting other countries.","zh":"nearly 80 million in India alone 指只計印度就接近八千萬人，不包括其他國家。"},{"en":"Nearly 500 students in one school alone may use the same online platform.","zh":"單在一間學校就接近五百名學生可能使用同一個網上平台。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the number is large even within a single place.","zh":"這個短語強調即使只在一個地方，數字已經很大。"},{"en":"“Alone” reminds readers that the global total is even larger.","zh":"“alone” 提醒讀者全球總數更大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"light their houses using","meaning":"使用……照亮家居","examples":[{"en":"Many families light their houses using kerosene.","zh":"許多家庭使用煤油照亮家居。"},{"en":"To light their houses using something means to use that thing as the source of household light.","zh":"light their houses using something 指使用某物作為家居光源。"},{"en":"Some families light their houses using candles during a long power cut.","zh":"在長時間停電期間，有些家庭使用蠟燭照亮家居。"},{"en":"If people light homes using smoky fuel, indoor air quality may become worse.","zh":"如果人們使用帶煙燃料照亮家居，室內空氣質素可能變差。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a lighting method with daily home life.","zh":"這個短語把照明方法與日常家居生活連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"primary lighting medium","meaning":"主要照明媒介","examples":[{"en":"Kerosene is the primary lighting medium for many poor households.","zh":"煤油是許多貧困家庭的主要照明媒介。"},{"en":"A primary lighting medium is the main source or method used to produce light.","zh":"primary lighting medium 指用來產生光的主要來源或方法。"},{"en":"In a home without electricity, candles may become the primary lighting medium.","zh":"在沒有電力的家中，蠟燭可能成為主要照明媒介。"},{"en":"When the primary lighting medium is dirty or expensive, families face health and money problems.","zh":"當主要照明媒介骯髒或昂貴，家庭會面對健康和金錢問題。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main way people get light.","zh":"這個短語指出人們取得光的主要方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dangerous and dirty","meaning":"危險而骯髒","examples":[{"en":"Kerosene is a dangerous and dirty fuel for household lighting.","zh":"煤油是用於家居照明的危險而骯髒燃料。"},{"en":"Dangerous and dirty means unsafe and likely to create pollution, smoke, or mess.","zh":"dangerous and dirty 指不安全，並可能造成污染、煙霧或髒亂。"},{"en":"Burning rubbish at home is dangerous and dirty because it can cause fire and toxic smoke.","zh":"在家燃燒垃圾是危險而骯髒的，因為可能引起火災和有毒煙霧。"},{"en":"A fuel can be dangerous and dirty if it harms health while being used.","zh":"如果燃料在使用時傷害健康，它就是危險而骯髒的。"},{"en":"The phrase gives two reasons why a method should be replaced.","zh":"這個短語給出某方法應被取代的兩個原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"despite being subsidised","meaning":"儘管獲補貼","examples":[{"en":"Kerosene remains costly for rural families despite being subsidised.","zh":"儘管獲補貼，煤油對農村家庭來說仍然昂貴。"},{"en":"Despite being subsidised means although the government or another body pays part of the cost.","zh":"despite being subsidised 指雖然政府或其他機構支付部分成本。"},{"en":"A bus route may still be expensive for poor passengers despite being subsidised.","zh":"儘管獲補貼，某條巴士線對貧困乘客來說仍可能昂貴。"},{"en":"Subsidies can lower prices, but they may not make a product truly affordable.","zh":"補貼可以降低價格，但未必令產品真正可負擔。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a contrast between support and continuing cost.","zh":"這個短語引入支援與持續成本之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"consume nearly","meaning":"消耗近……","examples":[{"en":"Kerosene consumes nearly four per cent of a typical rural household’s budget.","zh":"煤油消耗一般農村家庭預算近百分之四。"},{"en":"To consume nearly a certain amount means to use almost that amount.","zh":"consume nearly a certain amount 指使用接近某數量。"},{"en":"Rent may consume nearly half of a worker’s monthly income in an expensive city.","zh":"在昂貴城市，租金可能消耗工人每月收入近一半。"},{"en":"If fuel consumes a large share of a poor family’s budget, less money remains for food and school.","zh":"如果燃料消耗貧困家庭預算的一大部分，留給食物和上學的錢就更少。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how much of a limited resource is used.","zh":"這個短語顯示有限資源有多少被使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a typical rural household’s budget","meaning":"一般農村家庭預算","examples":[{"en":"Kerosene takes up part of a typical rural household’s budget.","zh":"煤油佔用一般農村家庭預算的一部分。"},{"en":"A typical rural household’s budget is the usual amount of money a village family has and how it is spent.","zh":"typical rural household’s budget 指村落家庭通常擁有的金錢及其開支方式。"},{"en":"A typical rural household’s budget may include food, fuel, school costs, medicine, and transport.","zh":"一般農村家庭預算可能包括食物、燃料、上學費用、藥物和交通。"},{"en":"If lighting takes too much of the budget, families may cut back on other needs.","zh":"如果照明佔用太多預算，家庭可能削減其他需要。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to ordinary family spending in rural areas.","zh":"這個短語指農村地區普通家庭開支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a recent report by","meaning":"……最近一份報告","examples":[{"en":"A recent report by the Intermediate Technology Development Group discusses indoor air pollution.","zh":"Intermediate Technology Development Group 最近一份報告討論室內空氣污染。"},{"en":"A recent report by an organisation is a newly published document written or issued by that group.","zh":"a recent report by an organisation 指由該組織撰寫或發布的新近文件。"},{"en":"A recent report by a hospital may show that more children are suffering from asthma.","zh":"醫院最近一份報告可能顯示更多兒童患上哮喘。"},{"en":"Citing a recent report helps support a claim with evidence.","zh":"引用最近一份報告有助用證據支持說法。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies both the source and the freshness of information.","zh":"這個短語同時指出資訊來源和新近程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"suggest that","meaning":"顯示；指出","examples":[{"en":"The report suggests that indoor air pollution causes many deaths.","zh":"該報告指出室內空氣污染造成許多死亡。"},{"en":"Suggest that means indicate or imply that something is likely to be true.","zh":"suggest that 指顯示或暗示某事很可能屬實。"},{"en":"Falling test scores may suggest that students need more reading support.","zh":"測驗分數下降可能顯示學生需要更多閱讀支援。"},{"en":"Research can suggest a problem even before every detail is fully proved.","zh":"研究可以在每個細節完全證明前指出問題。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used for cautious evidence-based claims.","zh":"這個短語常用於謹慎、以證據為本的說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"indoor air pollution","meaning":"室內空氣污染","examples":[{"en":"Indoor air pollution from kerosene lighting can be deadly.","zh":"來自煤油照明的室內空氣污染可以致命。"},{"en":"Indoor air pollution is dirty or harmful air inside homes, schools, or other buildings.","zh":"indoor air pollution 指家居、學校或其他建築物內骯髒或有害的空氣。"},{"en":"Smoke from cooking fires can create indoor air pollution in small rooms.","zh":"煮食爐火的煙可以在細小房間中造成室內空氣污染。"},{"en":"Indoor air pollution can harm breathing because people breathe the same polluted air for hours.","zh":"室內空氣污染可以傷害呼吸，因為人們長時間吸入同一種受污染空氣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pollution inside buildings, not outdoor smog.","zh":"這個短語描述建築物內的污染，而不是戶外霧霾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"such lighting media","meaning":"這類照明媒介","examples":[{"en":"Such lighting media can create serious health risks.","zh":"這類照明媒介可以造成嚴重健康風險。"},{"en":"Such lighting media means lighting methods of this kind, such as kerosene lamps or smoky fuel lamps.","zh":"such lighting media 指這類照明方法，例如煤油燈或帶煙燃料燈。"},{"en":"Candles and kerosene lamps are such lighting media when families lack electricity.","zh":"當家庭缺乏電力時，蠟燭和煤油燈就是這類照明媒介。"},{"en":"These media can be risky because they burn fuel inside the home.","zh":"這些媒介可能有風險，因為它們在家中燃燒燃料。"},{"en":"The phrase points back to the lighting methods already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指回已提及的照明方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"result in","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"Indoor air pollution results in many deaths worldwide every year.","zh":"室內空氣污染每年在全球導致許多死亡。"},{"en":"To result in something means to cause it to happen.","zh":"result in something 指導致某事發生。"},{"en":"Poor road lighting can result in more accidents at night.","zh":"道路照明不足可以導致夜間更多意外。"},{"en":"If smoky lamps are used every evening, they may result in long-term health problems.","zh":"如果每晚使用帶煙燈具，它們可能導致長期健康問題。"},{"en":"The phrase links a cause with its effect.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"deaths worldwide","meaning":"全球死亡個案","examples":[{"en":"Indoor air pollution causes deaths worldwide every year.","zh":"室內空氣污染每年造成全球死亡個案。"},{"en":"Deaths worldwide means people dying in many countries around the world.","zh":"deaths worldwide 指世界許多國家中有人死亡。"},{"en":"Road accidents cause deaths worldwide, not only in large cities.","zh":"道路意外造成全球死亡個案，而不只是在大城市發生。"},{"en":"When a health problem causes deaths worldwide, it becomes a global concern.","zh":"當健康問題造成全球死亡個案，它就成為全球關注。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the international scale of loss of life.","zh":"這個短語強調生命損失的國際規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"or more specifically","meaning":"更確切地說","examples":[{"en":"LED lamps, or more specifically white LEDs, produce useful light efficiently.","zh":"LED 燈，更確切地說是白光 LED，能有效產生有用光線。"},{"en":"Or more specifically is used to make a statement more exact.","zh":"or more specifically 用來令陳述更準確。"},{"en":"The school needs more support, or more specifically, more trained reading teachers.","zh":"學校需要更多支援，更確切地說，需要更多受過訓練的閱讀老師。"},{"en":"This phrase helps narrow a general idea to a precise detail.","zh":"這個短語幫助把一般想法收窄至精確細節。"},{"en":"It signals that the writer is correcting or refining the wording.","zh":"它表示作者正在修正或細化措辭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"white LEDs","meaning":"白光 LED","examples":[{"en":"White LEDs produce far more useful light than kerosene lamps.","zh":"白光 LED 產生的有效光量遠多於煤油燈。"},{"en":"White LEDs are light-emitting diodes that produce white light suitable for general lighting.","zh":"white LEDs 指產生白光、適合一般照明的發光二極管。"},{"en":"A reading lamp may use white LEDs because they give clear light for studying.","zh":"閱讀燈可能使用白光 LED，因為它們為學習提供清楚光線。"},{"en":"White LEDs can make rural lighting more efficient because they use little power.","zh":"白光 LED 可以令農村照明更有效率，因為它們用電很少。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to LEDs that give white rather than coloured light.","zh":"這個短語指發出白光而非彩色光的 LED。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be believed to","meaning":"被認為","examples":[{"en":"White LEDs are believed to produce much more useful light.","zh":"白光 LED 被認為能產生多得多的有效光量。"},{"en":"Be believed to means people think something is true, often based on evidence or expert opinion.","zh":"be believed to 指人們認為某事屬實，通常基於證據或專家意見。"},{"en":"Regular exercise is believed to improve mood and sleep quality.","zh":"定期運動被認為能改善心情和睡眠質素。"},{"en":"When a technology is believed to be efficient, organisations may test it in real communities.","zh":"當一項科技被認為有效率，機構可能在真實社區中測試它。"},{"en":"The phrase reports a widely held view without stating it as absolute certainty.","zh":"這個短語報告一種廣泛看法，但不把它表述為絕對肯定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"useful light","meaning":"有效光量","examples":[{"en":"LED lamps produce more useful light than kerosene lamps.","zh":"LED 燈產生的有效光量比煤油燈多。"},{"en":"Useful light is light that is bright and steady enough for tasks such as reading, cooking, or working.","zh":"useful light 指足夠明亮和穩定，可用於閱讀、煮食或工作的光。"},{"en":"A weak candle may give light, but not enough useful light for homework.","zh":"微弱蠟燭可能提供光，但不足以提供做功課所需的有效光量。"},{"en":"More useful light improves evening productivity because people can see clearly.","zh":"更多有效光量改善晚間生產力，因為人們能看清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on light that actually helps people do things.","zh":"這個短語重點是實際幫助人做事的光。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"almost 50 times as much","meaning":"幾乎是……的50倍","examples":[{"en":"LEDs produce almost 50 times as much useful light as a conventional bulb.","zh":"LED 產生的有效光量幾乎是傳統燈泡的50倍。"},{"en":"Almost 50 times as much means nearly fifty times the amount.","zh":"almost 50 times as much 指數量接近五十倍。"},{"en":"A new printer may print almost 50 times as much in one hour as an old one.","zh":"新打印機一小時可能打印的數量幾乎是舊打印機的50倍。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a very large difference in quantity or output.","zh":"這個短語強調數量或產出的巨大差異。"},{"en":"It is used when one thing produces far more than another.","zh":"當一件事物產生遠多於另一件事物的東西時，就可使用它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"an entire rural village","meaning":"整條農村","examples":[{"en":"This technology can light an entire rural village.","zh":"這項科技可以照亮整條農村。"},{"en":"An entire rural village means the whole village in the countryside, not just one house or street.","zh":"entire rural village 指整個鄉村村落，而不只是其中一間屋或一條街。"},{"en":"A water project may serve an entire rural village if every household can use the well.","zh":"如果每戶都能使用水井，供水項目就可以服務整條農村。"},{"en":"Lighting an entire village can improve safety and community activities after dark.","zh":"照亮整條村可以改善天黑後的安全和社區活動。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses full coverage of a village community.","zh":"這個短語強調對村落社區的全面覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"with less energy than","meaning":"使用比……更少的能源","examples":[{"en":"The village can be lit with less energy than a single bulb uses.","zh":"該村可以使用比一個燈泡所需更少的能源來照亮。"},{"en":"With less energy than means using a smaller amount of power than another thing uses.","zh":"with less energy than 指使用比另一事物更少的電力或能源。"},{"en":"A tablet may run all day with less energy than a desktop computer uses in a few hours.","zh":"平板電腦可能使用比桌上電腦幾小時用量更少的能源運作一整天。"},{"en":"If a system gives more light with less energy, it is more efficient and cheaper to run.","zh":"如果系統用更少能源提供更多光，它就更有效率且運行較便宜。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly compares energy use.","zh":"這個短語清楚比較能源使用量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a single conventional 100-watt light bulb","meaning":"一個傳統100瓦燈泡","examples":[{"en":"An entire village can be lit with less energy than a single conventional 100-watt light bulb uses.","zh":"整條村可以用比一個傳統100瓦燈泡更少的能源照亮。"},{"en":"A single conventional 100-watt light bulb is one traditional bulb that uses 100 watts of power.","zh":"single conventional 100-watt light bulb 指一個使用100瓦電力的傳統燈泡。"},{"en":"A classroom may once have used several conventional 100-watt bulbs for bright lighting.","zh":"課室過去可能使用幾個傳統100瓦燈泡來提供明亮照明。"},{"en":"If a village can be lit with less power than one such bulb, the technology is extremely efficient.","zh":"如果一條村能用少於這種燈泡的電力照亮，該科技就極有效率。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a concrete comparison for energy use.","zh":"這個短語為能源使用提供具體比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"professor of electrical engineering","meaning":"電機工程教授","examples":[{"en":"Dave Irvine-Halliday is a professor of electrical engineering.","zh":"Dave Irvine-Halliday 是電機工程教授。"},{"en":"A professor of electrical engineering is a university expert who teaches and researches electricity, electronics, and related systems.","zh":"professor of electrical engineering 指教授和研究電力、電子及相關系統的大學專家。"},{"en":"A professor of electrical engineering may design safer batteries or more efficient lights.","zh":"電機工程教授可能設計更安全電池或更高效率燈具。"},{"en":"Such experts can help turn laboratory ideas into practical technology for communities.","zh":"這類專家可以幫助把實驗室想法轉化為社區可用的實用科技。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies an academic specialist in electrical systems.","zh":"這個短語指出電力系統方面的學術專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"founder of","meaning":"……的創辦人","examples":[{"en":"He is the founder of Light Up the World Foundation.","zh":"他是 Light Up the World Foundation 的創辦人。"},{"en":"The founder of an organisation is the person who starts or creates it.","zh":"founder of an organisation 指創立或建立該組織的人。"},{"en":"The founder of a school may decide its mission, values, and first courses.","zh":"學校創辦人可能決定其使命、價值和首批課程。"},{"en":"Founders often shape an organisation because they set its earliest direction.","zh":"創辦人通常會塑造一個組織，因為他們設定最初方向。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who began something.","zh":"這個短語指出誰開始了某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"founded in","meaning":"創立於……","examples":[{"en":"Founded in 1997, LUTW has brought light to many homes.","zh":"LUTW 創立於1997年，已為許多家庭帶來光明。"},{"en":"Founded in a year means started or established in that year.","zh":"founded in a year 指在該年份開始或成立。"},{"en":"A charity founded in 2010 may have grown from one small office to several centres.","zh":"創立於2010年的慈善機構，可能已由一間小辦公室發展到幾個中心。"},{"en":"Knowing when an organisation was founded helps readers understand its history.","zh":"知道一個組織創立於何時，幫助讀者理解其歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the starting date of an organisation or project.","zh":"這個短語給出組織或項目的開始日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"LED technology","meaning":"LED 技術","examples":[{"en":"LUTW has used LED technology in many countries.","zh":"LUTW 已在許多國家使用 LED 技術。"},{"en":"LED technology is the use of light-emitting diodes to produce efficient light.","zh":"LED technology 指使用發光二極管產生高效率光線的技術。"},{"en":"Street signs, reading lamps, and phone screens all use LED technology.","zh":"街道標誌、閱讀燈和電話屏幕都使用 LED 技術。"},{"en":"LED technology can reduce energy use because it creates bright light with little power.","zh":"LED 技術可以減少能源使用，因為它用少量電力產生明亮光線。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the lighting system built around LEDs.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞 LED 建立的照明系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"remote and disadvantaged corners","meaning":"偏遠和貧困地區","examples":[{"en":"LUTW works in remote and disadvantaged corners of many countries.","zh":"LUTW 在許多國家的偏遠和貧困地區工作。"},{"en":"Remote and disadvantaged corners are faraway areas where people have limited services, money, or opportunities.","zh":"remote and disadvantaged corners 指偏遠、服務、金錢或機會有限的地區。"},{"en":"A mobile clinic may visit remote and disadvantaged corners where hospitals are too far away.","zh":"流動診所可能到訪醫院太遠的偏遠和貧困地區。"},{"en":"These places often need low-cost solutions because full infrastructure arrives slowly.","zh":"這些地方通常需要低成本方案，因為完整基礎設施來得很慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes isolated and under-served communities.","zh":"這個短語描述孤立且服務不足的社區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not yet widely known","meaning":"尚未廣為人知","examples":[{"en":"The technology is not yet widely known in India.","zh":"這項科技在印度尚未廣為人知。"},{"en":"Not yet widely known means many people still do not know about it, although awareness may grow later.","zh":"not yet widely known 指許多人仍不知道它，雖然日後認知可能增加。"},{"en":"A new study method may be useful but not yet widely known among parents.","zh":"新學習方法可能有用，但在家長之間尚未廣為人知。"},{"en":"If a technology is not widely known, people may hesitate to trust or buy it.","zh":"如果科技尚未廣為人知，人們可能猶豫是否信任或購買它。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests early-stage public awareness.","zh":"這個短語暗示公眾認知仍處早期階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"face scepticism","meaning":"面對質疑","examples":[{"en":"The technology faces some scepticism in India.","zh":"這項科技在印度面對一些質疑。"},{"en":"To face scepticism means to meet doubt or questioning from people.","zh":"face scepticism 指遇到人們的懷疑或質疑。"},{"en":"A new school policy may face scepticism if parents do not understand its benefits.","zh":"如果家長不理解好處，新校政可能面對質疑。"},{"en":"New technology often faces scepticism when users have never seen it work.","zh":"當使用者從未看過新科技運作，新科技通常會面對質疑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes doubt that must be answered with evidence or experience.","zh":"這個短語描述需要以證據或經驗回應的懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"revolutionise rural lighting","meaning":"改變農村照明","examples":[{"en":"LED systems are revolutionising rural lighting.","zh":"LED 系統正在改變農村照明。"},{"en":"To revolutionise rural lighting means to change village lighting in a major and lasting way.","zh":"revolutionise rural lighting 指以重大而持久的方式改變村落照明。"},{"en":"Solar lamps can revolutionise rural lighting by replacing smoky kerosene lamps.","zh":"太陽能燈可以透過取代帶煙煤油燈來改變農村照明。"},{"en":"A technology revolutionises a service when it makes the old method seem slow, costly, or unsafe.","zh":"當一項科技令舊方法看起來緩慢、昂貴或不安全，它就是徹底改變某服務。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests deep transformation, not a small improvement.","zh":"這個短語暗示深層轉變，而不是小改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"magic solution","meaning":"神奇解決方案","examples":[{"en":"LED lighting is not a magic solution to global energy problems.","zh":"LED 照明不是全球能源問題的神奇解決方案。"},{"en":"A magic solution is an imagined answer that seems to solve everything easily and completely.","zh":"magic solution 指一種看似能輕易而完整解決所有問題的想像答案。"},{"en":"A new app is not a magic solution to poor study habits if students still refuse to practise.","zh":"如果學生仍拒絕練習，新應用程式不是差劣學習習慣的神奇解決方案。"},{"en":"Calling something a magic solution can warn readers not to expect too much from one idea.","zh":"稱某物為神奇解決方案可以提醒讀者不要對單一想法期望過高。"},{"en":"The phrase usually suggests that real problems need more than one fix.","zh":"這個短語通常暗示真正問題需要不止一種修正。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"energy problems","meaning":"能源問題","examples":[{"en":"LED systems cannot solve all the world’s energy problems.","zh":"LED 系統不能解決全球所有能源問題。"},{"en":"Energy problems are difficulties related to producing, supplying, paying for, or using energy safely and fairly.","zh":"energy problems 指與安全公平地生產、供應、支付或使用能源有關的困難。"},{"en":"A city faces energy problems when demand rises faster than power plants can supply electricity.","zh":"當需求上升快過發電廠供電能力，城市就面對能源問題。"},{"en":"Energy problems can affect schools, hospitals, transport, and household life.","zh":"能源問題可以影響學校、醫院、交通和家庭生活。"},{"en":"The phrase covers more than lighting; it includes fuel, electricity, cost, and access.","zh":"這個短語不只涵蓋照明，還包括燃料、電力、成本和取得途徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"head of","meaning":"……的主管","examples":[{"en":"Ashok Jhunjhunwala is head of the electrical engineering department.","zh":"Ashok Jhunjhunwala 是電機工程系主管。"},{"en":"Head of something means the person in charge of a department, team, or organisation.","zh":"head of something 指負責某部門、團隊或組織的人。"},{"en":"The head of a school decides major policies with other senior staff.","zh":"學校校長與其他高級職員決定主要政策。"},{"en":"A department head often manages people, budgets, and research direction.","zh":"部門主管通常管理人員、預算和研究方向。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a leadership position.","zh":"這個短語指出領導職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"electrical engineering department","meaning":"電機工程系","examples":[{"en":"He works in the electrical engineering department at IIT Madras.","zh":"他在 IIT Madras 的電機工程系工作。"},{"en":"An electrical engineering department is a university department that studies electricity, electronics, circuits, and power systems.","zh":"electrical engineering department 指研究電力、電子、電路和電力系統的大學學系。"},{"en":"Students in an electrical engineering department may learn how solar panels and batteries work.","zh":"電機工程系學生可能學習太陽能板和電池如何運作。"},{"en":"Such departments can help develop technology for lighting, communication, and energy supply.","zh":"這類學系可以幫助發展照明、通訊和能源供應科技。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an academic unit focused on electrical systems.","zh":"這個短語指專注於電力系統的學術單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rural population","meaning":"農村人口","examples":[{"en":"Nearly 60 per cent of India’s rural population burns biomass each year.","zh":"印度接近百分之六十的農村人口每年燃燒生物質燃料。"},{"en":"Rural population means the people who live in countryside areas rather than towns or cities.","zh":"rural population 指住在鄉郊地區而非城鎮或城市的人。"},{"en":"A country’s rural population may depend heavily on farming and local markets.","zh":"一個國家的農村人口可能高度依賴農業和本地市場。"},{"en":"If a large rural population lacks clean energy, the health impact can be enormous.","zh":"如果龐大農村人口缺乏清潔能源，健康影響可以很大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes people living outside urban areas.","zh":"這個短語描述住在城市以外的人口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"burn biomass","meaning":"燃燒生物質燃料","examples":[{"en":"Many rural households burn biomass in wood-burning stoves.","zh":"許多農村家庭在燒柴爐灶中燃燒生物質燃料。"},{"en":"To burn biomass means to use plant or animal material, such as wood or crop waste, as fuel.","zh":"burn biomass 指把植物或動物材料，例如木材或農作物廢料，用作燃料燃燒。"},{"en":"A family may burn biomass for cooking when gas or electricity is unavailable.","zh":"當煤氣或電力不可用，家庭可能燃燒生物質燃料煮食。"},{"en":"Burning biomass in primitive stoves can create smoke and waste much of the fuel’s energy.","zh":"在原始爐灶中燃燒生物質燃料會產生煙霧，並浪費大量燃料能源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using organic material as fuel.","zh":"這個短語描述把有機材料用作燃料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"180 million tonnes of biomass","meaning":"1.8億噸生物質燃料","examples":[{"en":"India’s rural population burns 180 million tonnes of biomass each year.","zh":"印度農村人口每年燃燒1.8億噸生物質燃料。"},{"en":"180 million tonnes of biomass means a very large mass of organic fuel such as wood, crop waste, or plant material.","zh":"180 million tonnes of biomass 指大量有機燃料，例如木材、農作物廢料或植物材料。"},{"en":"A country using 180 million tonnes of biomass is relying heavily on traditional fuel sources.","zh":"使用1.8億噸生物質燃料的國家，正高度依賴傳統燃料來源。"},{"en":"Burning such a large amount can create air pollution and pressure on local environments.","zh":"燃燒如此大量燃料可以造成空氣污染，並對本地環境造成壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a concrete measure of fuel use.","zh":"這個短語給出燃料使用的具體量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"primitive wood-burning stoves","meaning":"原始燒柴爐灶","examples":[{"en":"Many people use primitive wood-burning stoves.","zh":"許多人使用原始燒柴爐灶。"},{"en":"Primitive wood-burning stoves are simple old-style stoves that burn wood and often waste energy.","zh":"primitive wood-burning stoves 指燃燒木材、通常浪費能源的簡單舊式爐灶。"},{"en":"A village kitchen may use a primitive wood-burning stove made from clay and stones.","zh":"村落廚房可能使用由黏土和石頭造的原始燒柴爐灶。"},{"en":"Such stoves can fill homes with smoke because they lack efficient design and ventilation.","zh":"這類爐灶可能令家中充滿煙，因為它們缺乏有效設計和通風。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests basic, inefficient cooking technology.","zh":"這個短語暗示基本而低效率的煮食科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"10–15 per cent efficient","meaning":"只有10至15%效率","examples":[{"en":"These stoves are only 10–15 per cent efficient.","zh":"這些爐灶只有10至15%效率。"},{"en":"10–15 per cent efficient means only a small part of the fuel’s energy is usefully converted into heat or work.","zh":"10–15 per cent efficient 指燃料能源中只有小部分有效轉化成熱力或工作。"},{"en":"An old machine that wastes most of its electricity may be only 10–15 per cent efficient.","zh":"浪費大部分電力的舊機器可能只有10至15%效率。"},{"en":"Low efficiency means families need more fuel to get the same result.","zh":"低效率意味家庭需要更多燃料才能得到同樣結果。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that most energy is being wasted.","zh":"這個短語顯示大部分能源正在被浪費。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"against this background","meaning":"在這背景下","examples":[{"en":"Against this background, experts emphasise the need for clean energy.","zh":"在這背景下，專家強調清潔能源的需要。"},{"en":"Against this background means considering the situation that has just been described.","zh":"against this background 指考慮剛剛描述的情況。"},{"en":"Many students are stressed before exams; against this background, schools should teach time management.","zh":"許多學生考試前感到壓力；在這背景下，學校應教授時間管理。"},{"en":"The phrase links a recommendation to the problem that explains it.","zh":"這個短語把建議與解釋該建議的問題連起來。"},{"en":"It means “given these conditions”.","zh":"它意思是「鑑於這些情況」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"emphasise the need for","meaning":"強調……的需要","examples":[{"en":"Jhunjhunwala emphasises the need for a clean energy source.","zh":"Jhunjhunwala 強調清潔能源來源的需要。"},{"en":"To emphasise the need for something means to strongly point out that it is necessary.","zh":"emphasise the need for something 指強烈指出某物是必要的。"},{"en":"A doctor may emphasise the need for clean water during a disease outbreak.","zh":"醫生可能在疾病爆發期間強調清潔食水的需要。"},{"en":"Experts emphasise clean energy because dirty fuels harm health and waste money.","zh":"專家強調清潔能源，因為骯髒燃料傷害健康並浪費金錢。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights an urgent requirement.","zh":"這個短語突出迫切需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"clean energy source","meaning":"清潔能源來源","examples":[{"en":"Rural India needs a clean energy source.","zh":"印度農村需要清潔能源來源。"},{"en":"A clean energy source is an energy supply that creates little pollution when used.","zh":"clean energy source 指使用時產生很少污染的能源供應。"},{"en":"Solar power can be a clean energy source for homes far from the grid.","zh":"太陽能可以成為遠離電網家庭的清潔能源來源。"},{"en":"Clean energy can reduce smoke, illness, and dependence on expensive fuels.","zh":"清潔能源可以減少煙霧、疾病和對昂貴燃料的依賴。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts cleaner energy with dirty fuels such as kerosene or smoky biomass.","zh":"這個短語把較清潔能源與煤油或帶煙生物質等骯髒燃料作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not just for…but for…as well","meaning":"不只是為了……也為了……","examples":[{"en":"Clean energy is needed not just for lighting but for other domestic purposes as well.","zh":"清潔能源不只是為了照明，也為了其他家居用途。"},{"en":"Not just for A but for B as well means something is useful for more than one purpose.","zh":"not just for A but for B as well 指某物不止對一個目的有用。"},{"en":"English is useful not just for exams but for travel and work as well.","zh":"英文不只是為了考試，也為了旅行和工作。"},{"en":"Clean energy matters more when it supports cooking, heating, charging, and lighting.","zh":"當清潔能源支援煮食、取暖、充電和照明，它就更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase expands the reader’s view beyond one use.","zh":"這個短語把讀者視野擴展到一種用途以外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"domestic purposes","meaning":"家居用途","examples":[{"en":"Clean energy is needed for lighting and other domestic purposes.","zh":"清潔能源是照明和其他家居用途所需的。"},{"en":"Domestic purposes are uses connected with home life, such as cooking, heating, cleaning, and lighting.","zh":"domestic purposes 指與家庭生活有關的用途，例如煮食、取暖、清潔和照明。"},{"en":"A family may use electricity for domestic purposes like charging phones and running a fan.","zh":"家庭可能把電力用於充電話和開風扇等家居用途。"},{"en":"Energy for domestic purposes affects health and comfort inside the home.","zh":"家居用途所需能源影響家中的健康和舒適。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to household uses, not industrial uses.","zh":"這個短語指家庭用途，而不是工業用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"launch an ambitious project","meaning":"推出雄心勃勃的計劃","examples":[{"en":"The Indian government launched an ambitious project to electrify rural villages.","zh":"印度政府推出雄心勃勃的計劃，為農村村落供電。"},{"en":"To launch an ambitious project means to start a large and difficult plan with important goals.","zh":"launch an ambitious project 指開始一個目標重要、規模大而困難的計劃。"},{"en":"A city may launch an ambitious project to build affordable housing for thousands of families.","zh":"城市可能推出雄心勃勃的計劃，為數千個家庭興建可負擔住房。"},{"en":"Ambitious projects need money, planning, and long-term commitment.","zh":"雄心勃勃的計劃需要金錢、規劃和長期承諾。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a project that is bold and challenging.","zh":"這個短語暗示大膽而具挑戰性的項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bring electricity to","meaning":"為……帶來電力","examples":[{"en":"The project aims to bring electricity to rural villages.","zh":"該項目旨在為農村村落帶來電力。"},{"en":"To bring electricity to a place means to connect it to a power supply or provide electric power there.","zh":"bring electricity to a place 指把某地方接駁到供電系統，或在那裏提供電力。"},{"en":"A government may bring electricity to a mountain village by building lines and transformers.","zh":"政府可能透過建設電線和變壓器，為山區村落帶來電力。"},{"en":"Bringing electricity to homes can improve lighting, communication, study, and small businesses.","zh":"為家居帶來電力可以改善照明、通訊、學習和小生意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes providing access to electric power.","zh":"這個短語描述提供電力使用途徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the next decade","meaning":"在未來十年","examples":[{"en":"The government wants to bring electricity to many villages in the next decade.","zh":"政府希望在未來十年為許多村落帶來電力。"},{"en":"In the next decade means during the next ten years.","zh":"in the next decade 指在接下來十年期間。"},{"en":"A school may plan to upgrade all classrooms in the next decade.","zh":"學校可能計劃在未來十年升級所有課室。"},{"en":"Long-term projects use this phrase because major infrastructure takes years to complete.","zh":"長期項目會使用這個短語，因為大型基礎設施需要多年完成。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a future ten-year time frame.","zh":"這個短語設定未來十年的時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"remote locations","meaning":"偏遠位置","examples":[{"en":"The remote locations of the villages make the goal difficult.","zh":"村落的偏遠位置令該目標變得困難。"},{"en":"Remote locations are places far from cities, roads, services, or main infrastructure.","zh":"remote locations 指遠離城市、道路、服務或主要基礎設施的地方。"},{"en":"A remote location may be difficult for doctors or teachers to reach regularly.","zh":"偏遠位置可能令醫生或老師難以定期到達。"},{"en":"Remote locations raise costs because materials and workers must travel farther.","zh":"偏遠位置提高成本，因為材料和工人必須走更遠。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why providing services can be hard.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何提供服務可能困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make reaching this goal difficult","meaning":"令達成這目標變得困難","examples":[{"en":"The remote locations make reaching this goal difficult.","zh":"偏遠位置令達成這目標變得困難。"},{"en":"To make reaching this goal difficult means to create obstacles that prevent the aim from being achieved easily.","zh":"make reaching this goal difficult 指製造障礙，使目標不易達成。"},{"en":"A tight deadline can make reaching a project goal difficult for a small team.","zh":"緊迫截止日期可以令小團隊達成項目目標變得困難。"},{"en":"Distance makes rural electrification difficult because equipment must be transported and installed far away.","zh":"距離令農村電氣化困難，因為設備必須運送到遠處並安裝。"},{"en":"The phrase links an obstacle with a goal.","zh":"這個短語把障礙與目標連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"recognise the potential of","meaning":"認識到……的潛力","examples":[{"en":"The government recognises the potential of LED lighting.","zh":"政府認識到 LED 照明的潛力。"},{"en":"To recognise the potential of something means to understand that it could become useful or successful.","zh":"recognise the potential of something 指理解某事物可能變得有用或成功。"},{"en":"A teacher may recognise the potential of a quiet student who writes thoughtful answers.","zh":"老師可能認識到一名安靜學生的潛力，因為她寫出有思想的答案。"},{"en":"Recognising potential does not always mean acting immediately, because cost or risk may still remain.","zh":"認識到潛力不一定表示立即行動，因為成本或風險仍可能存在。"},{"en":"The phrase describes seeing future possibility.","zh":"這個短語描述看見未來可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"powered by solar technology","meaning":"由太陽能技術供電","examples":[{"en":"LED lighting can be powered by solar technology.","zh":"LED 照明可以由太陽能技術供電。"},{"en":"Powered by solar technology means using equipment that converts sunlight into usable energy.","zh":"powered by solar technology 指使用把陽光轉化為可用能源的設備。"},{"en":"A water pump powered by solar technology can work in fields far from the grid.","zh":"由太陽能技術供電的水泵可以在遠離電網的農田運作。"},{"en":"Solar power can make remote systems cheaper to run because they do not need fuel deliveries.","zh":"太陽能可以令偏遠系統運行較便宜，因為不需要運送燃料。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how the device gets its energy.","zh":"這個短語顯示裝置如何取得能源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"express reservations about","meaning":"對……有所保留","examples":[{"en":"The government has expressed reservations about the high costs.","zh":"政府對高昂成本有所保留。"},{"en":"To express reservations about something means to show doubts or concerns about it.","zh":"express reservations about something 指對某事表示懷疑或憂慮。"},{"en":"Parents may express reservations about a school trip if safety arrangements are unclear.","zh":"如果安全安排不清楚，家長可能對學校旅行有所保留。"},{"en":"Governments may support an idea in principle but still worry about its cost.","zh":"政府可能原則上支持一個想法，但仍擔心其成本。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests cautious concern, not complete rejection.","zh":"這個短語暗示謹慎憂慮，而不是完全拒絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"high costs","meaning":"高昂成本","examples":[{"en":"The government is concerned about the high costs of LED lighting.","zh":"政府擔心 LED 照明的高昂成本。"},{"en":"High costs are expenses that are large enough to create financial difficulty or hesitation.","zh":"high costs 指大到足以造成財政困難或令人猶豫的開支。"},{"en":"High costs may stop families from joining a useful course or buying better equipment.","zh":"高昂成本可能阻止家庭報讀有用課程或購買更好設備。"},{"en":"If costs are high, even good technology may fail to reach poor users.","zh":"如果成本高昂，即使好科技也可能無法到達貧困使用者手中。"},{"en":"The phrase points to price as a barrier.","zh":"這個短語指出價格是一種障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"if only","meaning":"要是……就好了","examples":[{"en":"If only LEDs were manufactured locally, the lamps could become cheaper.","zh":"要是 LED 在本地製造就好了，燈具就可以變得更便宜。"},{"en":"If only expresses a strong wish that something were true or could happen.","zh":"if only 表達強烈願望，希望某事屬實或能夠發生。"},{"en":"If only the school had more computers, every student could practise at the same time.","zh":"要是學校有更多電腦就好了，每個學生就可以同時練習。"},{"en":"The phrase often introduces the condition that would solve a problem.","zh":"這個短語通常引入可解決問題的條件。"},{"en":"It shows regret or hope about a situation that is not yet real.","zh":"它顯示對尚未成真的情況的遺憾或希望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"manufactured locally","meaning":"本地製造","examples":[{"en":"LEDs would be cheaper if they were manufactured locally.","zh":"如果 LED 本地製造，它們會較便宜。"},{"en":"Manufactured locally means made in the same country or area where the product will be used.","zh":"manufactured locally 指在產品將被使用的同一國家或地區製造。"},{"en":"School uniforms manufactured locally may be cheaper because transport costs are lower.","zh":"本地製造的校服可能較便宜，因為運輸成本較低。"},{"en":"Local manufacturing can reduce import duties and create jobs.","zh":"本地製造可以減少進口關稅並創造職位。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts local production with importing from abroad.","zh":"這個短語把本地生產與從海外進口作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in bulk","meaning":"大批量地","examples":[{"en":"Costs could fall if LEDs were manufactured locally and in bulk.","zh":"如果 LED 本地和大批量製造，成本可能下降。"},{"en":"In bulk means in large quantities at one time.","zh":"in bulk 指一次大量地。"},{"en":"A school may buy notebooks in bulk to reduce the price per book.","zh":"學校可能大批量購買筆記簿，以降低每本價格。"},{"en":"Manufacturing in bulk can lower costs because machines and materials are used more efficiently.","zh":"大批量製造可以降低成本，因為機器和材料使用得更有效率。"},{"en":"The phrase often explains why large-scale production is cheaper.","zh":"這個短語常解釋為何大規模生產較便宜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lamps installed in","meaning":"安裝在……的燈","examples":[{"en":"The lamps installed in nearly 300 homes cost less than other systems.","zh":"安裝在接近300戶家中的燈，比其他系統便宜。"},{"en":"Lamps installed in a place are lamps that have been set up and made ready for use there.","zh":"lamps installed in a place 指在某地方已設置好並可使用的燈。"},{"en":"Lights installed in a school corridor can make students feel safer after activities.","zh":"安裝在學校走廊的燈可以令學生在活動後感到更安全。"},{"en":"Installed lamps can change daily routines because people can use them immediately.","zh":"已安裝的燈可以改變日常習慣，因為人們可以立即使用它們。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where the lamps have been put in place.","zh":"這個短語指出燈具被安裝的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"nearly half the price of","meaning":"差不多是……價格的一半","examples":[{"en":"The GSBF lamps cost nearly half the price of other solar lighting systems.","zh":"GSBF 燈具的價格差不多是其他太陽能照明系統的一半。"},{"en":"Nearly half the price of something means almost 50 per cent cheaper than that thing.","zh":"nearly half the price of something 指價格幾乎只是某物的50%。"},{"en":"A used textbook may cost nearly half the price of a new one.","zh":"二手教科書的價格可能差不多是新書的一半。"},{"en":"If a product costs nearly half the price, more low-income users may be able to afford it.","zh":"如果產品價格差不多是一半，更多低收入使用者可能能夠負擔。"},{"en":"The phrase makes a clear price comparison.","zh":"這個短語作出清楚價格比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"solar lighting systems","meaning":"太陽能照明系統","examples":[{"en":"Other solar lighting systems are more expensive than the GSBF lamps.","zh":"其他太陽能照明系統比 GSBF 燈具更昂貴。"},{"en":"Solar lighting systems are lighting setups that use sunlight, usually through solar panels and batteries.","zh":"solar lighting systems 指使用陽光的照明裝置，通常透過太陽能板和電池運作。"},{"en":"A village clinic may use solar lighting systems to keep basic lights on at night.","zh":"村落診所可能使用太陽能照明系統，讓夜間基本燈光保持運作。"},{"en":"Such systems are useful in remote areas because they do not need a full power grid.","zh":"這類系統在偏遠地區有用，因為不需要完整電網。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a complete lighting arrangement powered by the sun.","zh":"這個短語指由太陽能供電的完整照明安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"founder of the NGO","meaning":"該非政府組織創辦人","examples":[{"en":"Jasjeet Singh Chaddha is the founder of the NGO.","zh":"Jasjeet Singh Chaddha 是該非政府組織創辦人。"},{"en":"The founder of the NGO is the person who started that non-governmental organisation.","zh":"founder of the NGO 指創立該非政府組織的人。"},{"en":"The founder of an NGO may design its mission and raise its first funds.","zh":"非政府組織創辦人可能設計其使命並籌集第一筆資金。"},{"en":"Founders often continue to influence how an NGO chooses projects and partners.","zh":"創辦人通常會繼續影響非政府組織如何選擇項目和合作伙伴。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the person who created the organisation.","zh":"這個短語指出創立該組織的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"currently imports","meaning":"目前進口","examples":[{"en":"He currently imports his LEDs from China.","zh":"他目前從中國進口 LED。"},{"en":"Currently imports means at present he buys goods from another country and brings them in.","zh":"currently imports 指目前從另一個國家購買貨品並運入本地。"},{"en":"A shop currently imports school bags from Japan but may use local suppliers later.","zh":"一間商店目前從日本進口書包，但日後可能使用本地供應商。"},{"en":"Importing can increase costs if transport fees and duties are high.","zh":"如果運輸費和關稅高，進口會增加成本。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the present source of supply.","zh":"這個短語描述目前的供應來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"set up","meaning":"成立；設立","examples":[{"en":"He wants to set up a manufacturing unit in India.","zh":"他想在印度設立一個製造單位。"},{"en":"To set up something means to establish, start, or arrange it so it can operate.","zh":"set up something 指建立、開始或安排某事，使其能運作。"},{"en":"A teacher may set up a study group for students who need extra practice.","zh":"老師可能為需要額外練習的學生設立學習小組。"},{"en":"Setting up a local factory can reduce imports and create jobs.","zh":"設立本地工廠可以減少進口並創造職位。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating a working system or organisation.","zh":"這個短語描述創造一個可運作系統或組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"manufacturing unit","meaning":"生產單位；製造廠","examples":[{"en":"He wants to create an LED manufacturing unit in India.","zh":"他想在印度建立一個 LED 生產單位。"},{"en":"A manufacturing unit is a factory or production facility that makes a specific product.","zh":"manufacturing unit 指製造特定產品的工廠或生產設施。"},{"en":"A small manufacturing unit may produce school uniforms for local shops.","zh":"小型製造廠可能為本地商店生產校服。"},{"en":"Local manufacturing units can lower costs by reducing transport and import duties.","zh":"本地生產單位可以透過減少運輸和進口關稅來降低成本。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a place where goods are made.","zh":"這個短語指製造貨品的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"solar panel manufacturing unit","meaning":"太陽能板生產單位","examples":[{"en":"He also wants to set up a solar panel manufacturing unit.","zh":"他也想設立一個太陽能板生產單位。"},{"en":"A solar panel manufacturing unit is a facility that produces panels used to turn sunlight into electricity.","zh":"solar panel manufacturing unit 指生產把陽光轉化為電力的太陽能板的設施。"},{"en":"A country may build a solar panel manufacturing unit to reduce dependence on imported energy equipment.","zh":"一個國家可能建立太陽能板生產單位，以減少對進口能源設備的依賴。"},{"en":"Local production of solar panels can make solar lighting systems cheaper.","zh":"本地生產太陽能板可以令太陽能照明系統更便宜。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a factory for making solar panels.","zh":"這個短語指製造太陽能板的工廠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"if manufactured locally","meaning":"如果在本地製造","examples":[{"en":"If manufactured locally, the lamps could become much cheaper.","zh":"如果在本地製造，這些燈具可以變得便宜得多。"},{"en":"If manufactured locally means if the product is made in the country or area where it will be sold or used.","zh":"if manufactured locally 指如果產品在銷售或使用的國家或地區製造。"},{"en":"If manufactured locally, school desks may cost less because transport is cheaper.","zh":"如果在本地製造，學校書桌可能成本較低，因為運輸較便宜。"},{"en":"Local manufacturing can reduce import duties and support local jobs.","zh":"本地製造可以減少進口關稅並支持本地職位。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a condition that could lower cost.","zh":"這個短語引入一個可以降低成本的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"plummet to","meaning":"急跌至","examples":[{"en":"The cost of the LED lamp could plummet to $22.","zh":"LED 燈成本可能急跌至22美元。"},{"en":"To plummet to a price means to fall sharply to that level.","zh":"plummet to a price 指價格急劇下跌至某水平。"},{"en":"Air ticket prices may plummet after the holiday season ends.","zh":"假期季節結束後，機票價格可能急跌。"},{"en":"If import duties are removed, the final price of a product may drop quickly.","zh":"如果進口關稅被取消，產品最終價格可能快速下降。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a sudden and large decrease.","zh":"這個短語暗示突然而大幅的下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"no longer incur","meaning":"不再產生……","examples":[{"en":"The lamps would no longer incur heavy import duties.","zh":"這些燈具將不再產生高額進口關稅。"},{"en":"No longer incur means no longer have to pay, suffer, or be subject to a cost or penalty.","zh":"no longer incur 指不再需要支付、承受或受到某成本或罰則影響。"},{"en":"A school may no longer incur printing costs after moving worksheets online.","zh":"學校把工作紙轉到網上後，可能不再產生打印成本。"},{"en":"If a product is made locally, it may no longer incur import charges.","zh":"如果產品本地製造，它可能不再產生進口費用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a cost that disappears.","zh":"這個短語描述某項成本消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"heavy import duties","meaning":"高額進口關稅","examples":[{"en":"Heavy import duties increase the cost of imported LEDs.","zh":"高額進口關稅增加進口 LED 的成本。"},{"en":"Heavy import duties are high taxes charged on goods brought into a country.","zh":"heavy import duties 指對進入某國的貨品徵收的高額稅項。"},{"en":"A shop may sell imported shoes at a higher price because of heavy import duties.","zh":"商店可能因高額進口關稅而以較高價格出售進口鞋。"},{"en":"Heavy duties can make useful products too expensive for low-income users.","zh":"高額關稅可以令有用產品對低收入使用者來說太昂貴。"},{"en":"The phrase describes taxes that raise import prices significantly.","zh":"這個短語描述顯著提高進口價格的稅項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"close to","meaning":"接近","examples":[{"en":"The project needs close to $5 million.","zh":"該項目需要接近五百萬美元。"},{"en":"Close to a number means almost that number.","zh":"close to a number 指接近某數字。"},{"en":"A school renovation may cost close to one million dollars.","zh":"學校翻新可能花費接近一百萬美元。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when the exact amount is not necessary but the scale matters.","zh":"當精確金額不必要但規模重要時，就會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It suggests the amount is near the stated figure.","zh":"它暗示數量接近所述數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"exempt the lamps from","meaning":"豁免燈具繳付……","examples":[{"en":"Chaddha asked the government to exempt the lamps from import duties.","zh":"Chaddha 要求政府豁免燈具繳付進口關稅。"},{"en":"To exempt something from a duty or rule means to officially free it from that payment or requirement.","zh":"exempt something from a duty or rule 指正式免除某物繳付某款項或遵守某要求。"},{"en":"A government may exempt school books from sales tax to make education cheaper.","zh":"政府可能豁免教科書繳付銷售稅，以令教育較便宜。"},{"en":"Exempting lamps from duties would lower their price for rural families.","zh":"豁免燈具繳付關稅會降低農村家庭購買價格。"},{"en":"The phrase describes official removal of a charge or obligation.","zh":"這個短語描述官方取消某項收費或義務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"such duties","meaning":"這類關稅","examples":[{"en":"The lamps would be cheaper without such duties.","zh":"沒有這類關稅，燈具會較便宜。"},{"en":"Such duties means taxes of the kind already mentioned, especially import duties in this context.","zh":"such duties 指剛提到的那類稅項，在此尤其指進口關稅。"},{"en":"Imported medicine may become cheaper if such duties are reduced.","zh":"如果這類關稅降低，進口藥物可能變得較便宜。"},{"en":"Removing such duties can make essential goods more affordable.","zh":"取消這類關稅可以令必需品更可負擔。"},{"en":"The phrase points back to the taxes just discussed.","zh":"這個短語指回剛剛討論的稅項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"to no avail","meaning":"但沒有結果；徒勞無功","examples":[{"en":"He asked the government for help, but to no avail.","zh":"他向政府求助，但沒有結果。"},{"en":"To no avail means without success or without producing the hoped-for result.","zh":"to no avail 指沒有成功，或沒有產生希望中的結果。"},{"en":"A student searched for her lost notebook all morning, but to no avail.","zh":"學生整個上午尋找遺失的筆記簿，但徒勞無功。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that effort was made but the problem remained.","zh":"這個短語顯示已付出努力，但問題仍然存在。"},{"en":"It often carries a sense of frustration or disappointment.","zh":"它通常帶有挫敗或失望感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"an entrepreneur","meaning":"企業家","examples":[{"en":"Chaddha is an entrepreneur who made his money in plastics.","zh":"Chaddha 是一名靠塑膠業賺錢的企業家。"},{"en":"An entrepreneur is a person who starts or runs a business, often taking financial risks.","zh":"entrepreneur 指創立或經營企業的人，通常承擔財務風險。"},{"en":"A young entrepreneur may open an online shop selling handmade bags.","zh":"年輕企業家可能開設網店出售手工袋。"},{"en":"Entrepreneurs can support new technology by investing their own money and ideas.","zh":"企業家可以透過投入自己的金錢和想法來支持新科技。"},{"en":"The word describes a business creator, not just an employee.","zh":"這個詞描述創造生意的人，而不只是僱員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make one’s money in","meaning":"靠……賺錢","examples":[{"en":"Chaddha made his money in plastics.","zh":"Chaddha 靠塑膠業賺錢。"},{"en":"To make one’s money in an industry means to earn wealth through that field of business.","zh":"make one’s money in an industry 指透過某商業領域賺取財富。"},{"en":"A businesswoman may make her money in property before investing in education.","zh":"女商人可能先靠房地產賺錢，再投資教育。"},{"en":"Money earned in one industry can later fund social or technological projects.","zh":"在一個行業賺來的錢，日後可以資助社會或科技項目。"},{"en":"The phrase explains where someone’s wealth came from.","zh":"這個短語解釋某人的財富來自哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"pour one’s own money into","meaning":"將自己的錢投入……","examples":[{"en":"Chaddha has poured his own money into the project.","zh":"Chaddha 已將自己的錢投入該項目。"},{"en":"To pour one’s own money into something means to invest a large amount of personal money in it.","zh":"pour one’s own money into something 指把大量個人金錢投放到某事上。"},{"en":"A shop owner may pour her own money into renovation before the business earns profit.","zh":"店主可能在生意賺錢前，將自己的錢投入裝修。"},{"en":"Pouring personal money into a project shows commitment but also creates financial risk.","zh":"將個人金錢投入項目顯示承諾，但也造成財務風險。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests serious personal investment.","zh":"這個短語暗示認真的個人投資。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"initial installations","meaning":"首批安裝","examples":[{"en":"The initial installations were provided free of charge.","zh":"首批安裝是免費提供的。"},{"en":"Initial installations are the first equipment setups completed at the beginning of a project.","zh":"initial installations 指項目開始時完成的第一批設備安裝。"},{"en":"A charity may pay for initial installations of water filters in several homes.","zh":"慈善機構可能支付幾戶家庭首批濾水器安裝費。"},{"en":"Free initial installations can help people test a new technology before paying for it.","zh":"免費首批安裝可以幫助人們在付款前測試新科技。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the first round of setting up equipment.","zh":"這個短語指第一輪設備設置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"provide something free of charge","meaning":"免費提供某物","examples":[{"en":"He provided the initial installations free of charge.","zh":"他免費提供首批安裝。"},{"en":"To provide something free of charge means to give or supply it without asking for payment.","zh":"provide something free of charge 指不收費地給予或供應某物。"},{"en":"A clinic may provide basic health checks free of charge during a community event.","zh":"診所可能在社區活動中免費提供基本健康檢查。"},{"en":"Free provision helps poor users try services they could not otherwise afford.","zh":"免費提供服務幫助貧困使用者嘗試他們本來負擔不起的服務。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that no money is paid by the receiver.","zh":"這個短語強調接收者不需付款。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"look to make","meaning":"試圖使……","examples":[{"en":"He looks to make the project self-sustaining.","zh":"他試圖使該項目自給自足地運作。"},{"en":"To look to make something a certain way means to try or plan to make it that way.","zh":"look to make something a certain way 指嘗試或計劃令某物變成那樣。"},{"en":"A school may look to make its reading programme more independent by training student mentors.","zh":"學校可能透過訓練學生導師，試圖使閱讀計劃更獨立。"},{"en":"Project leaders look to make programmes sustainable so they do not depend forever on donations.","zh":"項目負責人試圖令計劃可持續，讓它們不永遠依賴捐款。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an intended goal or plan.","zh":"這個短語描述預定目標或計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"self-sustaining","meaning":"自給自足地運作","examples":[{"en":"Chaddha wants the project to become self-sustaining.","zh":"Chaddha 希望該項目變得能自給自足地運作。"},{"en":"Self-sustaining means able to continue operating without constant outside funding or support.","zh":"self-sustaining 指能夠在沒有持續外部資金或支援下繼續運作。"},{"en":"A school garden becomes self-sustaining if vegetable sales pay for seeds and tools.","zh":"如果學校菜園賣菜收入能支付種子和工具，它就能自給自足地運作。"},{"en":"A self-sustaining project is more likely to survive after the first donations end.","zh":"自給自足的項目在首批捐款結束後較可能生存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a system that can support itself.","zh":"這個短語描述能支持自身的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"urban markets","meaning":"城市市場","examples":[{"en":"Urban markets have shown a keen interest in LED lighting.","zh":"城市市場對 LED 照明表現出濃厚興趣。"},{"en":"Urban markets are customers and businesses in towns and cities.","zh":"urban markets 指城鎮和城市中的顧客及企業。"},{"en":"Urban markets may buy new technology faster because people usually have higher incomes and better access to shops.","zh":"城市市場可能更快購買新科技，因為人們通常收入較高且較易接觸商店。"},{"en":"If urban markets accept a product first, sales there may help lower prices later.","zh":"如果城市市場先接受產品，那裏的銷售日後可能幫助降低價格。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts city demand with rural demand.","zh":"這個短語把城市需求與農村需求作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"show a keen interest in","meaning":"對……表現出濃厚興趣","examples":[{"en":"Urban markets have shown a keen interest in LED lighting.","zh":"城市市場對 LED 照明表現出濃厚興趣。"},{"en":"To show a keen interest in something means to be very interested in it.","zh":"show a keen interest in something 指對某事非常感興趣。"},{"en":"Students may show a keen interest in robotics after watching a robot competition.","zh":"學生觀看機械人比賽後，可能對機械人學表現出濃厚興趣。"},{"en":"Strong interest from buyers can encourage companies to produce more of a product.","zh":"買家的強烈興趣可以鼓勵公司生產更多產品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes clear and active interest.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚而主動的興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"afford the higher price","meaning":"負擔較高價格","examples":[{"en":"Urban consumers can afford the higher price of LED lighting.","zh":"城市消費者能負擔 LED 照明的較高價格。"},{"en":"To afford the higher price means to have enough money to pay more for something.","zh":"afford the higher price 指有足夠金錢為某物支付更高價格。"},{"en":"Some families can afford the higher price of organic food, while others cannot.","zh":"有些家庭能負擔有機食物的較高價格，另一些則不能。"},{"en":"If rural families cannot afford the higher price, the technology may not reach those who need it most.","zh":"如果農村家庭不能負擔較高價格，該科技可能無法到達最需要它的人手中。"},{"en":"The phrase links cost with people’s ability to pay.","zh":"這個短語把成本與人們付款能力連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rural markets","meaning":"農村市場","examples":[{"en":"Rural markets in India cannot yet afford the lamps.","zh":"印度農村市場尚未能負擔這些燈具。"},{"en":"Rural markets are customers and businesses in countryside areas.","zh":"rural markets 指鄉郊地區的顧客和企業。"},{"en":"Rural markets may need cheaper products because incomes are often lower than in cities.","zh":"農村市場可能需要較便宜產品，因為收入通常低於城市。"},{"en":"A company must understand rural markets before selling technology there.","zh":"公司在那裏銷售科技前，必須了解農村市場。"},{"en":"The phrase describes demand and buying power outside urban areas.","zh":"這個短語描述城市以外的需求和購買力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bring down prices","meaning":"降低價格","examples":[{"en":"Rural markets can afford the lamps only when prices are brought down.","zh":"只有當價格降低時，農村市場才能負擔這些燈具。"},{"en":"To bring down prices means to reduce prices.","zh":"bring down prices 指降低價格。"},{"en":"Buying materials in bulk can bring down prices for school uniforms.","zh":"大批量購買材料可以降低校服價格。"},{"en":"Lower prices allow more poor families to buy useful products.","zh":"較低價格讓更多貧困家庭購買有用產品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making something more affordable.","zh":"這個短語描述令某物更可負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have access to microcredit","meaning":"可以獲得小額信貸","examples":[{"en":"Rural families could afford the lamps if they had access to microcredit.","zh":"如果農村家庭可以獲得小額信貸，他們就能負擔這些燈具。"},{"en":"To have access to microcredit means to be able to borrow very small loans designed for low-income people.","zh":"have access to microcredit 指能夠借到為低收入人士設計的小額貸款。"},{"en":"A village shopkeeper may have access to microcredit to buy a new fridge for cold drinks.","zh":"村裏店主可能可以獲得小額信貸，以購買新雪櫃存放凍飲。"},{"en":"Microcredit can help families pay gradually instead of needing the full price at once.","zh":"小額信貸可以幫助家庭逐步付款，而不需一次支付全價。"},{"en":"The phrase connects financial access with practical purchasing power.","zh":"這個短語把金融途徑與實際購買力連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"microcredit","meaning":"小額信貸","examples":[{"en":"Microcredit could help poor families buy LED lamps.","zh":"小額信貸可以幫助貧困家庭購買 LED 燈。"},{"en":"Microcredit is a system of very small loans, often offered to people who cannot use ordinary bank loans.","zh":"microcredit 指非常小額貸款制度，通常提供給無法使用普通銀行貸款的人。"},{"en":"A woman may use microcredit to buy a sewing machine and start a home business.","zh":"一名女性可能使用小額信貸購買縫紉機，開始家庭生意。"},{"en":"Microcredit can spread useful technology by allowing families to pay over time.","zh":"小額信貸可以讓家庭分期付款，從而推廣有用科技。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to small-scale lending for low-income borrowers.","zh":"這個短語指面向低收入借款人的小規模貸款。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"shanty town","meaning":"棚戶區","examples":[{"en":"Tembisa is a shanty town in Johannesburg.","zh":"Tembisa 是約翰內斯堡的一個棚戶區。"},{"en":"A shanty town is a poor urban area where many homes are small, informal, and built from cheap materials.","zh":"shanty town 指貧困城市地區，許多房屋細小、非正式，並由廉價材料建成。"},{"en":"Families in a shanty town may lack safe electricity, clean water, or proper roads.","zh":"棚戶區家庭可能缺乏安全電力、清潔食水或合適道路。"},{"en":"Low-cost lighting can improve safety in shanty towns where power supply is unreliable.","zh":"在供電不可靠的棚戶區，低成本照明可以改善安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a poor settlement, often on the edge of a city.","zh":"這個短語描述貧困聚居地，通常位於城市邊緣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"candles and paraffin","meaning":"蠟燭和石蠟油","examples":[{"en":"Many homes spent money on candles and paraffin every year.","zh":"許多家庭每年花錢購買蠟燭和石蠟油。"},{"en":"Candles and paraffin are traditional lighting fuels used when electricity is unavailable or unreliable.","zh":"candles and paraffin 指在沒有電力或供電不可靠時使用的傳統照明燃料。"},{"en":"A family may buy candles and paraffin during frequent blackouts.","zh":"家庭可能在頻繁停電期間購買蠟燭和石蠟油。"},{"en":"These fuels cost money repeatedly and may create fire or smoke risks.","zh":"這些燃料需要反覆花錢購買，並可能造成火災或煙霧風險。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to older household lighting supplies.","zh":"這個短語指較舊的家居照明用品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as calculations revealed","meaning":"正如計算所顯示","examples":[{"en":"As calculations revealed, families could pay for lighting systems over time.","zh":"正如計算所顯示，家庭可以隨時間支付照明系統費用。"},{"en":"As calculations revealed means the numbers showed or proved this point.","zh":"as calculations revealed 指數字顯示或證明這一點。"},{"en":"As calculations revealed, taking the bus was cheaper than driving every day.","zh":"正如計算所顯示，每天乘巴士比駕車便宜。"},{"en":"Calculations can turn a guess into a clearer financial decision.","zh":"計算可以把猜測變成較清楚的財務決定。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence from numerical working.","zh":"這個短語引入來自數字推算的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"solid-state lighting system","meaning":"固態照明系統","examples":[{"en":"Families could pay for a solid-state lighting system in just over a year.","zh":"家庭可以只需一年多就支付一套固態照明系統。"},{"en":"A solid-state lighting system is a lighting system using electronic components such as LEDs rather than burning fuel or fragile filaments.","zh":"solid-state lighting system 指使用 LED 等電子元件，而不是燃燒燃料或脆弱燈絲的照明系統。"},{"en":"A solar LED lamp can be part of a solid-state lighting system.","zh":"太陽能 LED 燈可以是固態照明系統的一部分。"},{"en":"Solid-state lighting often lasts longer and needs less maintenance than older lighting methods.","zh":"固態照明通常比舊式照明方法使用壽命更長，保養需求更少。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to modern electronic lighting technology.","zh":"這個短語指現代電子照明科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in just over a year","meaning":"只需一年多","examples":[{"en":"The families could pay for the system in just over a year.","zh":"這些家庭可以只需一年多就支付該系統費用。"},{"en":"In just over a year means in a little more than one year.","zh":"in just over a year 指在稍多於一年內。"},{"en":"A student may improve greatly in just over a year if she practises every week.","zh":"如果學生每星期練習，只需一年多就可能大有進步。"},{"en":"If a system pays for itself in just over a year, its long-term savings may be attractive.","zh":"如果一個系統只需一年多就收回成本，其長期節省可能很吸引。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a relatively short repayment period.","zh":"這個短語強調相對短的還款期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"weekly payments","meaning":"每週付款","examples":[{"en":"Weekly payments could match what families normally spent on fuel.","zh":"每週付款可以相當於家庭平時在燃料上的花費。"},{"en":"Weekly payments are small amounts of money paid every week.","zh":"weekly payments 指每星期支付的小額款項。"},{"en":"A family may buy a fridge through weekly payments instead of paying the full price at once.","zh":"家庭可能透過每週付款購買雪櫃，而不是一次支付全價。"},{"en":"Weekly payments make expensive items easier to afford when income is limited.","zh":"當收入有限，每週付款令昂貴物品較容易負擔。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a gradual payment method.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步付款方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"match what someone would normally spend on","meaning":"相當於某人平時在……上的花費","examples":[{"en":"Weekly payments could match what families would normally spend on candles.","zh":"每週付款可以相當於家庭平時在蠟燭上的花費。"},{"en":"To match what someone would normally spend on something means to be equal to their usual spending on it.","zh":"match what someone would normally spend on something 指相等於某人在該物上的通常開支。"},{"en":"A monthly bus pass may match what a worker normally spends on single tickets.","zh":"月票費用可能相當於工人平時在單程車票上的花費。"},{"en":"If loan payments match old fuel costs, families may not feel extra financial pressure.","zh":"如果貸款付款相當於舊燃料成本，家庭可能不會感到額外財務壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase compares a new payment with an existing expense.","zh":"這個短語把新付款與現有開支作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be in the process of","meaning":"正在……的過程中","examples":[{"en":"LUTW is in the process of creating a microcredit facility.","zh":"LUTW 正在建立小額信貸安排的過程中。"},{"en":"To be in the process of doing something means to be currently working on it but not yet finished.","zh":"be in the process of doing something 指目前正在做某事，但尚未完成。"},{"en":"A school is in the process of updating its library system.","zh":"學校正在更新圖書館系統的過程中。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a plan is active and developing.","zh":"這個短語顯示計劃正在進行和發展。"},{"en":"It suggests progress, not completion.","zh":"它暗示進展，而不是完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"microcredit facility","meaning":"小額信貸安排","examples":[{"en":"LUTW is creating a microcredit facility for South Africa.","zh":"LUTW 正在為南非建立小額信貸安排。"},{"en":"A microcredit facility is an arrangement that provides small loans to people who need affordable credit.","zh":"microcredit facility 指向需要可負擔信貸的人提供小額貸款的安排。"},{"en":"A village cooperative may run a microcredit facility for farmers buying seeds.","zh":"村落合作社可能為購買種子的農民營運小額信貸安排。"},{"en":"Such a facility helps poor families buy useful equipment through small repayments.","zh":"這類安排幫助貧困家庭透過小額還款購買有用設備。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a system for providing microloans.","zh":"這個短語指提供小額貸款的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"newly installed","meaning":"新安裝的","examples":[{"en":"The newly installed LED lamps are a source of envy.","zh":"新安裝的 LED 燈令人羨慕。"},{"en":"Newly installed means recently put in place and made ready for use.","zh":"newly installed 指最近安放並設置好可供使用。"},{"en":"Students may enjoy a newly installed air-conditioner in the classroom during summer.","zh":"學生可能在夏天享受課室新安裝的冷氣機。"},{"en":"New equipment can attract attention because people notice the immediate improvement.","zh":"新設備可以吸引注意，因為人們注意到即時改善。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something recently set up.","zh":"這個短語描述最近設置好的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a source of envy","meaning":"令人羨慕的事物","examples":[{"en":"The LED lamps are a source of envy to people connected to the grid.","zh":"LED 燈對接駁到電網的人來說是令人羨慕的事物。"},{"en":"A source of envy is something others wish they had.","zh":"source of envy 指其他人希望自己也擁有的東西。"},{"en":"A student’s quiet study room may be a source of envy for classmates who share crowded homes.","zh":"學生安靜的書房可能令住在擠迫家中的同學羨慕。"},{"en":"Reliable solar lamps can make grid users jealous if their own electricity keeps failing.","zh":"如果電網用戶自己的電力不斷失效，可靠太陽能燈可以令他們羨慕。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one group’s advantage is noticed by others.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個群體的優勢被其他人注意到。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"connected to the grid","meaning":"接駁到電網","examples":[{"en":"Some villagers are already connected to the grid.","zh":"有些村民已經接駁到電網。"},{"en":"Connected to the grid means linked to the public electricity network.","zh":"connected to the grid 指連接到公共電力網絡。"},{"en":"A house connected to the grid can receive electricity from power stations through wires.","zh":"接駁到電網的房屋可以透過電線從發電廠取得電力。"},{"en":"Being connected to the grid does not always mean power is reliable.","zh":"接駁到電網不一定代表供電可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes access to the main electricity system.","zh":"這個短語描述接入主要電力系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"endure power cuts","meaning":"忍受停電","examples":[{"en":"Grid users have to endure power cuts every day.","zh":"電網用戶每天都要忍受停電。"},{"en":"To endure power cuts means to suffer through periods when electricity stops working.","zh":"endure power cuts 指忍受電力停止供應的時段。"},{"en":"Students may endure power cuts during exams if the school has no backup generator.","zh":"如果學校沒有後備發電機，學生可能在考試期間忍受停電。"},{"en":"Frequent power cuts can interrupt study, business, cooking, and communication.","zh":"頻繁停電可以打斷學習、生意、煮食和通訊。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests repeated inconvenience or hardship.","zh":"這個短語暗示反覆的不便或艱難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"up to","meaning":"多達","examples":[{"en":"Power cuts can last up to six or seven hours a day.","zh":"停電每天可以持續多達六或七小時。"},{"en":"Up to means as much as a stated maximum amount.","zh":"up to 指高達所述的最高數量。"},{"en":"A bus journey may take up to two hours during heavy traffic.","zh":"在嚴重塞車時，巴士車程可能多達兩小時。"},{"en":"When power cuts last up to several hours, families need backup lighting.","zh":"當停電持續多達數小時，家庭需要後備照明。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the highest possible amount or duration.","zh":"這個短語給出最高可能數量或時長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"constant energy shortages","meaning":"持續能源短缺","examples":[{"en":"Constant energy shortages are a common problem.","zh":"持續能源短缺是一個常見問題。"},{"en":"Constant energy shortages are repeated or continuing situations where there is not enough electricity or fuel.","zh":"constant energy shortages 指反覆或持續沒有足夠電力或燃料的情況。"},{"en":"A hospital may struggle during constant energy shortages if machines cannot run reliably.","zh":"如果機器不能可靠運作，醫院在持續能源短缺期間可能陷入困難。"},{"en":"Shortages can force people to rely on candles, generators, or fuel lamps.","zh":"短缺可以迫使人依賴蠟燭、發電機或燃料燈。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an ongoing lack of energy supply.","zh":"這個短語描述能源供應持續不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"blackouts","meaning":"停電","examples":[{"en":"Blackouts are common in villages connected to the grid.","zh":"停電在接駁到電網的村落中很常見。"},{"en":"Blackouts are periods when electric power fails and an area becomes dark.","zh":"blackouts 指電力中斷、某地區變黑的時段。"},{"en":"A blackout during dinner may force a family to use candles.","zh":"晚飯期間停電可能迫使家庭使用蠟燭。"},{"en":"Frequent blackouts make electricity unreliable even when homes are connected to the grid.","zh":"頻繁停電令電力不可靠，即使住宅已接駁到電網。"},{"en":"The word refers to power failure, not simply darkness at night.","zh":"這個詞指電力故障，而不只是夜間黑暗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a common problem","meaning":"常見問題","examples":[{"en":"Energy shortages and blackouts are a common problem.","zh":"能源短缺和停電是常見問題。"},{"en":"A common problem is a difficulty that happens often or affects many people.","zh":"common problem 指經常發生或影響許多人的困難。"},{"en":"Slow internet is a common problem during online lessons.","zh":"網課期間網速慢是常見問題。"},{"en":"When a problem is common, communities need practical systems rather than one-time fixes.","zh":"當問題常見，社區需要實用系統，而不是一次性修補。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something frequent and familiar.","zh":"這個短語描述頻繁而熟悉的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"power plants","meaning":"發電廠","examples":[{"en":"Too few power plants contribute to energy shortages.","zh":"發電廠太少會造成能源短缺。"},{"en":"Power plants are facilities that generate electricity for homes, businesses, and public services.","zh":"power plants 指為住宅、企業和公共服務發電的設施。"},{"en":"A city may build a new power plant when electricity demand increases.","zh":"當電力需求增加，城市可能興建新發電廠。"},{"en":"If there are too few power plants, the grid may not supply enough electricity during busy hours.","zh":"如果發電廠太少，電網在繁忙時間可能無法提供足夠電力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to places where electricity is produced.","zh":"這個短語指生產電力的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"transmission and distribution losses","meaning":"輸電和配電損耗","examples":[{"en":"Old technology causes transmission and distribution losses.","zh":"舊技術造成輸電和配電損耗。"},{"en":"Transmission and distribution losses are losses of electricity as power moves through wires and networks to users.","zh":"transmission and distribution losses 指電力透過電線和網絡傳送給使用者時流失的電量。"},{"en":"A weak electricity network may lose power before it reaches distant homes.","zh":"薄弱電力網絡可能在電力到達偏遠住宅前已流失部分電力。"},{"en":"These losses increase shortages because some generated electricity never reaches customers.","zh":"這些損耗增加短缺，因為部分已發電力永遠到不了顧客手中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes energy lost between production and final use.","zh":"這個短語描述由生產到最終使用之間流失的能源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be caused by","meaning":"由……造成","examples":[{"en":"Some losses are caused by old technology and theft.","zh":"有些損耗由舊技術和偷電造成。"},{"en":"To be caused by something means to happen because of that reason.","zh":"be caused by something 指因某原因而發生。"},{"en":"A school delay may be caused by heavy rain and blocked roads.","zh":"學校延誤可能由大雨和道路阻塞造成。"},{"en":"If blackouts are caused by poor infrastructure, better equipment may reduce them.","zh":"如果停電由差劣基礎設施造成，更好設備可能減少停電。"},{"en":"The phrase links an effect to its cause.","zh":"這個短語把結果與原因連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"theft of electricity","meaning":"偷電","examples":[{"en":"Theft of electricity from the grid worsens energy shortages.","zh":"從電網偷電令能源短缺惡化。"},{"en":"Theft of electricity means taking power illegally without paying for it.","zh":"theft of electricity 指非法取得電力而不付款。"},{"en":"Illegal wiring from a public line is one form of electricity theft.","zh":"從公共電線非法接線是偷電的一種形式。"},{"en":"Electricity theft can overload systems and leave paying users with worse supply.","zh":"偷電可以令系統超負荷，並令付費使用者供電更差。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stealing power from the network.","zh":"這個短語描述從網絡偷取電力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"from the grid","meaning":"從電網","examples":[{"en":"Electricity is sometimes stolen from the grid.","zh":"電力有時從電網被偷取。"},{"en":"From the grid means from the public electricity network.","zh":"from the grid 指來自公共電力網絡。"},{"en":"A home can receive power from the grid through cables connected to the national system.","zh":"住宅可以透過連接到國家系統的電纜從電網取得電力。"},{"en":"When electricity is taken illegally from the grid, the system may become less reliable.","zh":"當電力被非法從電網取走，系統可能變得較不可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source as the main power network.","zh":"這個短語指出來源是主要電力網絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"require far less maintenance","meaning":"需要少得多的保養","examples":[{"en":"LED systems require far less maintenance.","zh":"LED 系統需要少得多的保養。"},{"en":"To require far less maintenance means to need much less repair, cleaning, or servicing.","zh":"require far less maintenance 指需要少得多維修、清潔或保養。"},{"en":"A digital noticeboard may require far less maintenance than a wall covered with paper posters.","zh":"數碼告示板可能比貼滿紙張海報的牆需要少得多保養。"},{"en":"Low-maintenance systems save time and money for poor communities.","zh":"低保養系統為貧困社區節省時間和金錢。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a practical advantage after installation.","zh":"這個短語顯示安裝後的實際優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"longer service life","meaning":"更長使用壽命","examples":[{"en":"LED systems have a longer service life than many alternatives.","zh":"LED 系統比許多替代品有更長使用壽命。"},{"en":"Longer service life means something can be used for a longer period before it fails or must be replaced.","zh":"longer service life 指某物在失效或需要更換前可使用更長時間。"},{"en":"A school may choose desks with a longer service life even if they cost more at first.","zh":"學校可能選擇使用壽命較長的書桌，即使一開始較昂貴。"},{"en":"A longer service life lowers long-term cost because replacements are less frequent.","zh":"更長使用壽命降低長期成本，因為更換較不頻繁。"},{"en":"The phrase describes durability over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間的耐用度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no electricity bills","meaning":"沒有電費單","examples":[{"en":"Villagers joke that the lamps create no electricity bills.","zh":"村民開玩笑說這些燈沒有電費單。"},{"en":"No electricity bills means users do not receive regular charges for electric power.","zh":"no electricity bills 指使用者不會收到定期電力收費。"},{"en":"A solar garden light has no electricity bills because it charges from sunlight.","zh":"太陽能花園燈沒有電費單，因為它靠陽光充電。"},{"en":"Avoiding bills helps poor families plan spending more easily.","zh":"避免電費單幫助貧困家庭更容易規劃開支。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the financial advantage of solar-powered lighting.","zh":"這個短語突出太陽能照明的財務優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"have enough power to","meaning":"有足夠電力去……","examples":[{"en":"The lamps have enough power to provide four hours of light a day.","zh":"這些燈有足夠電力每天提供四小時光照。"},{"en":"To have enough power to do something means to have sufficient energy to perform that function.","zh":"have enough power to do something 指有足夠能源執行某功能。"},{"en":"A phone may have enough power to last until the student gets home.","zh":"電話可能有足夠電力支撐到學生回家。"},{"en":"If a lamp has enough power for evening study, children can finish homework after dark.","zh":"如果燈具有足夠電力供晚間學習，孩子可以在天黑後完成功課。"},{"en":"The phrase connects stored energy with what a device can do.","zh":"這個短語把儲存能源與裝置能做的事連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"provide four hours of light a day","meaning":"每天提供四小時光照","examples":[{"en":"The lamps provide four hours of light a day.","zh":"這些燈每天提供四小時光照。"},{"en":"To provide four hours of light a day means to give usable lighting for four hours each day.","zh":"provide four hours of light a day 指每天提供四小時可用照明。"},{"en":"A small solar lamp that provides four hours of light a day can cover evening homework time.","zh":"每天提供四小時光照的小型太陽能燈，可以覆蓋晚間功課時間。"},{"en":"Even limited daily lighting can change routines if it arrives at the right time.","zh":"即使每日照明有限，只要在合適時間提供，也可以改變生活習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a practical measure of lighting usefulness.","zh":"這個短語給出照明實用性的實際量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"nevertheless","meaning":"儘管如此","examples":[{"en":"Nevertheless, four hours of light is useful for villagers.","zh":"儘管如此，四小時光照對村民仍有用。"},{"en":"Nevertheless means despite what has just been said.","zh":"nevertheless 指儘管剛剛所說的情況如此。"},{"en":"The lesson was difficult; nevertheless, the students understood the main idea.","zh":"課堂很難；儘管如此，學生仍理解主要意思。"},{"en":"The lamps do not provide all-night power; nevertheless, they improve evening life.","zh":"這些燈不能提供整夜電力；儘管如此，它們改善晚間生活。"},{"en":"The word introduces a positive or contrasting point after a limitation.","zh":"這個詞在限制之後引入正面或對比重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"finish their work early in the evening","meaning":"在傍晚完成工作","examples":[{"en":"The lamps help people finish their work early in the evening.","zh":"這些燈幫助人們在傍晚完成工作。"},{"en":"To finish work early in the evening means to complete tasks during the first part of the night.","zh":"finish work early in the evening 指在夜晚初段完成任務。"},{"en":"A shopkeeper with reliable light can finish accounts early in the evening.","zh":"有可靠照明的店主可以在傍晚完成帳目。"},{"en":"Evening light helps families complete chores before they become too tired.","zh":"晚間照明幫助家庭在變得太疲倦前完成家務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical time gained after sunset.","zh":"這個短語描述日落後取得的實際時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"more reliable than","meaning":"比……更可靠","examples":[{"en":"The lamps are more reliable than light from India’s electrical grid.","zh":"這些燈比印度電網的照明更可靠。"},{"en":"More reliable than means more dependable and less likely to fail.","zh":"more reliable than 指更可信賴，較不可能失效。"},{"en":"A printed timetable may be more reliable than a website that often crashes.","zh":"紙本時間表可能比經常當機的網站更可靠。"},{"en":"Reliable lighting matters because people can plan study and work around it.","zh":"可靠照明很重要，因為人們可以圍繞它安排學習和工作。"},{"en":"The phrase compares how much users can trust two options.","zh":"這個短語比較使用者對兩個選項的信任程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"electrical grid","meaning":"電網","examples":[{"en":"The lamps are more reliable than India’s electrical grid.","zh":"這些燈比印度電網更可靠。"},{"en":"An electrical grid is a network that carries electricity from power plants to homes and businesses.","zh":"electrical grid 指把電力從發電廠輸送到住宅和企業的網絡。"},{"en":"A city’s electrical grid includes power lines, substations, and distribution systems.","zh":"城市電網包括電線、變電站和配電系統。"},{"en":"If the grid is weak, homes may face frequent power cuts.","zh":"如果電網薄弱，住宅可能面對頻繁停電。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the main electricity supply network.","zh":"這個短語指主要電力供應網絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be trained by","meaning":"由……培訓","examples":[{"en":"Villagers are trained by GSBF officials.","zh":"村民由 GSBF 職員培訓。"},{"en":"To be trained by someone means to be taught skills or instructions by that person or organisation.","zh":"be trained by someone 指由某人或某機構教授技能或指示。"},{"en":"New workers may be trained by senior staff before handling customers alone.","zh":"新員工可能由資深職員培訓，然後才獨自處理顧客。"},{"en":"Training helps users avoid damaging equipment or reducing its life.","zh":"培訓幫助使用者避免損壞設備或縮短其壽命。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who provides the instruction.","zh":"這個短語指出誰提供指導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"make the most of","meaning":"充分利用","examples":[{"en":"Villagers are trained to make the most of the new lamps.","zh":"村民接受培訓，以充分利用新燈具。"},{"en":"To make the most of something means to use it as effectively and fully as possible.","zh":"make the most of something 指盡可能有效而充分地使用某物。"},{"en":"Students make the most of a library by using books, study rooms, and online databases.","zh":"學生透過使用書籍、自修室和網上資料庫，充分利用圖書館。"},{"en":"Training helps villagers make the most of lamps by cleaning and charging them properly.","zh":"培訓幫助村民透過正確清潔和充電來充分利用燈具。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests not wasting an opportunity or resource.","zh":"這個短語暗示不要浪費機會或資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"instruct someone to","meaning":"指示某人去……","examples":[{"en":"A GSBF official instructs the family to clean the lamp regularly.","zh":"一名 GSBF 職員指示該家庭定期清潔燈具。"},{"en":"To instruct someone to do something means to tell or teach them clearly what they should do.","zh":"instruct someone to do something 指清楚告訴或教某人應做甚麼。"},{"en":"A teacher may instruct students to save their work before closing the computer.","zh":"老師可能指示學生關閉電腦前先儲存作品。"},{"en":"Clear instructions prevent mistakes and help equipment last longer.","zh":"清楚指示防止錯誤，並幫助設備使用更久。"},{"en":"The phrase is more formal than simply saying “tell someone to”.","zh":"這個短語比簡單說 “tell someone to” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"clean something regularly","meaning":"定期清潔某物","examples":[{"en":"The family needs to clean the lamp regularly.","zh":"這個家庭需要定期清潔燈具。"},{"en":"To clean something regularly means to remove dirt from it again and again at suitable times.","zh":"clean something regularly 指在合適時間反覆清除某物上的污垢。"},{"en":"Students should clean their water bottles regularly to prevent bad smells.","zh":"學生應定期清潔水樽，以防異味。"},{"en":"Regular cleaning helps lamps stay bright and last longer.","zh":"定期清潔幫助燈具保持明亮並使用更久。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated care, not a one-time action.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆照料，而不是一次性動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"luminosity","meaning":"亮度","examples":[{"en":"The lamp’s luminosity will diminish if dust settles on it.","zh":"如果灰塵積在燈上，燈的亮度會降低。"},{"en":"Luminosity is the brightness or amount of light something gives off.","zh":"luminosity 指某物發出的亮度或光量。"},{"en":"A classroom projector loses luminosity when its lens is dirty.","zh":"課室投影機鏡頭骯髒時，亮度會下降。"},{"en":"If a lamp’s luminosity falls, reading may become harder.","zh":"如果燈具亮度下降，閱讀可能變得更困難。"},{"en":"The word is a formal way to talk about brightness.","zh":"這個詞是談論亮度的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"diminish","meaning":"減少；降低","examples":[{"en":"The lamp’s luminosity and life will diminish without cleaning.","zh":"如果不清潔，燈的亮度和壽命會降低。"},{"en":"To diminish means to become smaller, weaker, or less effective.","zh":"diminish 指變得更小、更弱或較不有效。"},{"en":"A student’s concentration may diminish after several hours without rest.","zh":"學生連續幾小時不休息後，專注力可能降低。"},{"en":"Dust can diminish a lamp’s brightness because it blocks light.","zh":"灰塵可以降低燈的亮度，因為它阻擋光線。"},{"en":"The word describes gradual reduction.","zh":"這個詞描述逐漸減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"let the dust settle on","meaning":"讓灰塵積在……上","examples":[{"en":"The official warned them not to let the dust settle on the lamp.","zh":"該職員警告他們不要讓灰塵積在燈上。"},{"en":"To let the dust settle on something means to allow dust to collect on its surface.","zh":"let the dust settle on something 指讓灰塵聚集在某物表面。"},{"en":"If students let dust settle on a computer fan, the machine may overheat.","zh":"如果學生讓灰塵積在電腦風扇上，機器可能過熱。"},{"en":"Dust settling on lamps can reduce brightness and shorten service life.","zh":"灰塵積在燈上可以降低亮度並縮短使用壽命。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against neglecting simple cleaning.","zh":"這個短語警告不要忽視簡單清潔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"warn someone","meaning":"警告某人","examples":[{"en":"The official warns them to keep the lamp clean.","zh":"該職員警告他們保持燈具清潔。"},{"en":"To warn someone means to tell them about a possible danger or problem before it happens.","zh":"warn someone 指在問題或危險發生前告訴某人。"},{"en":"A teacher may warn students that late homework will lose marks.","zh":"老師可能警告學生遲交功課會扣分。"},{"en":"Warnings help people avoid damage, injury, or unnecessary cost.","zh":"警告幫助人避免損壞、受傷或不必要成本。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving caution in advance.","zh":"這個短語描述預先提醒小心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"for each question","meaning":"對於每題","examples":[{"en":"For each question, only one of the choices is correct.","zh":"對於每題，只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"For each question means separately for every question in the exercise.","zh":"for each question 指對練習中的每一道題目分別而言。"},{"en":"For each question, students should read all options before choosing an answer.","zh":"對於每題，學生應先閱讀所有選項再選答案。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds candidates that the rule applies every time.","zh":"這個短語提醒考生該規則每次都適用。"},{"en":"It is a common instruction in reading tests.","zh":"它是閱讀測驗中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"only one of the choices is correct","meaning":"只有一個選項正確","examples":[{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct in this section.","zh":"在這部分中，只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct means students must select just one answer, not two or more.","zh":"only one of the choices is correct 指學生只能選一個答案，而不是兩個或更多。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice question, two answers may look possible, but only one is correct.","zh":"在選擇題中，兩個答案可能看似可行，但只有一個正確。"},{"en":"This instruction warns students not to choose several options.","zh":"這項指示提醒學生不要選多個選項。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a strict answer rule.","zh":"這個短語設定嚴格答題規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"corresponding letter","meaning":"對應字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the corresponding letter in the appropriate box.","zh":"考生把對應字母寫在適當方格內。"},{"en":"A corresponding letter is the letter that matches the correct answer choice.","zh":"corresponding letter 指與正確答案選項相配的字母。"},{"en":"If option C is correct, the corresponding letter is C.","zh":"如果 C 選項正確，對應字母就是 C。"},{"en":"Students must copy the correct letter carefully or the answer may be marked wrong.","zh":"學生必須小心抄寫正確字母，否則答案可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to answer labels such as A, B, C, or D.","zh":"這個短語指 A、B、C 或 D 等答案標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"appropriate box","meaning":"適當方格","examples":[{"en":"The answer should be written in the appropriate box.","zh":"答案應寫在適當方格內。"},{"en":"The appropriate box is the correct space on the answer sheet for that answer.","zh":"appropriate box 指答題紙上該答案的正確位置。"},{"en":"A student may lose marks if she writes the answer in the wrong box.","zh":"如果學生把答案寫在錯誤方格，可能會失分。"},{"en":"Checking the question number helps candidates use the appropriate box.","zh":"檢查題號幫助考生使用適當方格。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the proper place for writing an answer.","zh":"這個短語指寫答案的正確位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"on your answer sheet","meaning":"在答題紙上","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write their answers on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生把答案寫在答題紙上。"},{"en":"On your answer sheet means in the official paper or digital area where answers must be recorded.","zh":"on your answer sheet 指在必須記錄答案的正式紙張或數碼區域中。"},{"en":"A student should not leave correct answers only on the question paper if the test requires them on the answer sheet.","zh":"如果考試要求答案寫在答題紙上，學生不應只把正確答案留在題目卷上。"},{"en":"Writing in the right place ensures the examiner can mark the response.","zh":"寫在正確位置確保考官能批改答案。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"provide light for","meaning":"為……提供照明","examples":[{"en":"The lamps can provide light for homes without electricity.","zh":"這些燈可以為沒有電力的家居提供照明。"},{"en":"To provide light for a place means to give that place usable illumination.","zh":"provide light for a place 指為某地方提供可用照明。"},{"en":"Street lamps provide light for pedestrians at night.","zh":"街燈在夜間為行人提供照明。"},{"en":"Providing light for homes helps people cook, read, and move safely after dark.","zh":"為家居提供照明幫助人們在天黑後煮食、閱讀和安全走動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the function of a lighting system.","zh":"這個短語描述照明系統的功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"powered by the sun","meaning":"由太陽能供電","examples":[{"en":"The GSBF lamps are powered by the sun.","zh":"GSBF 燈具由太陽能供電。"},{"en":"Powered by the sun means using sunlight as the energy source.","zh":"powered by the sun 指使用陽光作能源來源。"},{"en":"A calculator powered by the sun can work without ordinary batteries in bright light.","zh":"由太陽能供電的計數機在明亮光線下不用普通電池也能運作。"},{"en":"Sun-powered lamps can reduce fuel spending because sunlight is free.","zh":"太陽能燈可以減少燃料開支，因為陽光免費。"},{"en":"The phrase means the device depends on solar energy.","zh":"這個短語意思是裝置依賴太陽能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"more than half of","meaning":"超過一半的……","examples":[{"en":"More than half of India’s rural population uses biomass.","zh":"超過一半的印度農村人口使用生物質燃料。"},{"en":"More than half of a group means over 50 per cent of it.","zh":"more than half of a group 指該群體中超過百分之五十。"},{"en":"More than half of the class may choose online revision if the videos are clear.","zh":"如果影片清楚，超過一半的班級可能選擇網上溫習。"},{"en":"When more than half of a population uses dirty fuel, the health issue is large-scale.","zh":"當超過一半人口使用骯髒燃料，健康問題就是大規模的。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the majority is involved.","zh":"這個短語顯示多數人涉及其中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"cooking fuel","meaning":"煮食燃料","examples":[{"en":"Biomass is used as a cooking fuel in many rural homes.","zh":"生物質燃料在許多農村家庭中被用作煮食燃料。"},{"en":"Cooking fuel is fuel used to produce heat for preparing food.","zh":"cooking fuel 指用來產生熱力準備食物的燃料。"},{"en":"Gas, wood, charcoal, and electricity can all serve as cooking fuel.","zh":"煤氣、木材、木炭和電力都可以作為煮食燃料。"},{"en":"Dirty cooking fuel can create smoke that harms people inside the home.","zh":"骯髒煮食燃料可以產生煙霧，傷害家中人士。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to energy used for cooking, not lighting only.","zh":"這個短語指煮食所用能源，而不只是照明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"too expensive for most people","meaning":"對大多數人來說太昂貴","examples":[{"en":"The lamps are still too expensive for most people in rural areas.","zh":"這些燈對農村地區大多數人來說仍太昂貴。"},{"en":"Too expensive for most people means the price is higher than most people can afford.","zh":"too expensive for most people 指價格高於大多數人能負擔的水平。"},{"en":"A private course may be too expensive for most students if it costs more than a family’s monthly income.","zh":"如果私人課程費用高於家庭月入，它對大多數學生來說可能太昂貴。"},{"en":"When useful products are too expensive, poor communities remain excluded.","zh":"當有用產品太昂貴，貧困社區仍會被排除在外。"},{"en":"The phrase shows price as a barrier to access.","zh":"這個短語顯示價格是取得途徑的障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in rural areas","meaning":"在農村地區","examples":[{"en":"LED lamps can improve life in rural areas.","zh":"LED 燈可以改善農村地區的生活。"},{"en":"In rural areas means in countryside places outside towns and cities.","zh":"in rural areas 指在城鎮和城市以外的鄉郊地方。"},{"en":"In rural areas, schools and clinics may be far apart.","zh":"在農村地區，學校和診所可能相距很遠。"},{"en":"Technology for rural areas must consider distance, income, and limited services.","zh":"為農村地區設計的科技必須考慮距離、收入和有限服務。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts countryside communities with urban ones.","zh":"這個短語把鄉郊社區與城市社區作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"national power grid","meaning":"國家電網","examples":[{"en":"Solar lamps may be more reliable than the national power grid.","zh":"太陽能燈可能比國家電網更可靠。"},{"en":"A national power grid is a countrywide network that supplies electricity to homes and businesses.","zh":"national power grid 指向住宅和企業供電的全國性網絡。"},{"en":"A village connected to the national power grid may still face blackouts if supply is weak.","zh":"接駁到國家電網的村落，如果供應薄弱，仍可能面對停電。"},{"en":"A strong national grid supports schools, hospitals, factories, and households.","zh":"強大的國家電網支援學校、醫院、工廠和家庭。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the main electricity network of a country.","zh":"這個短語指一個國家的主要電力網絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"require skill to use","meaning":"需要技巧使用","examples":[{"en":"Some technologies require skill to use properly.","zh":"有些科技需要技巧才能正確使用。"},{"en":"Require skill to use means users need knowledge or practice before using something safely or effectively.","zh":"require skill to use 指使用者需要知識或練習，才能安全或有效地使用某物。"},{"en":"A sewing machine requires skill to use, unlike a simple pair of scissors.","zh":"縫紉機需要技巧使用，不像簡單剪刀。"},{"en":"Training can reduce mistakes when a device requires skill to use.","zh":"當裝置需要技巧使用，培訓可以減少錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that a product may not be simple for every user.","zh":"這個短語提醒某產品未必對每位使用者都簡單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete the following sentences","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the following sentences using words from the text.","zh":"考生使用文本中的字詞完成以下句子。"},{"en":"Complete the following sentences means fill in the missing parts of the sentences that come next.","zh":"complete the following sentences 指填寫接下來句子中缺漏的部分。"},{"en":"Students complete the following sentences by checking meaning, grammar, and the word limit.","zh":"學生透過檢查意思、文法和字數限制來完成以下句子。"},{"en":"This task tests whether students can locate exact information in a passage.","zh":"這項任務測試學生能否在文章中定位準確資料。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"using no more than three words","meaning":"使用不多於三個字","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should answer using no more than three words.","zh":"考生應使用不多於三個字作答。"},{"en":"Using no more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"using no more than three words 指答案必須包含三個或更少英文詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “monthly fuel quota”, it uses three words and fits the rule.","zh":"如果答案是 “monthly fuel quota”，它有三個詞，符合規則。"},{"en":"Extra words can make a correct idea wrong in a reading test.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，多餘字詞可以令正確意思變成錯誤答案。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語設定嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"from the text","meaning":"從文本中","examples":[{"en":"The answers must be taken from the text.","zh":"答案必須從文本中取得。"},{"en":"From the text means from the reading passage, not from your own ideas or outside knowledge.","zh":"from the text 指來自閱讀篇章，而不是自己的想法或外部知識。"},{"en":"Students should copy the exact phrase from the text if the question requires it.","zh":"如果題目要求，學生應從文本中抄寫準確短語。"},{"en":"Using words not found in the passage may break the instruction.","zh":"使用文章中沒有的字詞可能違反指示。"},{"en":"The phrase tells candidates the source of the answer.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生答案來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"for each gap","meaning":"每個空格","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write no more than three words for each gap.","zh":"考生每個空格寫不多於三個字。"},{"en":"For each gap means for every blank space in the exercise.","zh":"for each gap 指練習中的每一個空白位置。"},{"en":"A summary may have five gaps, and each gap needs its own answer.","zh":"摘要可能有五個空格，而每個空格都需要自己的答案。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds students that the word limit applies separately to every blank.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生字數限制分別適用於每個空格。"},{"en":"It is a common instruction in gap-fill questions.","zh":"它是填空題中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"inexpensive technology","meaning":"廉價科技","examples":[{"en":"Cell phones are another example of inexpensive technology.","zh":"手提電話是廉價科技的另一個例子。"},{"en":"Inexpensive technology is technology that costs relatively little but can still be useful.","zh":"inexpensive technology 指成本相對較低但仍然有用的科技。"},{"en":"A cheap water filter can be inexpensive technology for families without safe drinking water.","zh":"便宜濾水器可以成為沒有安全飲用水家庭的廉價科技。"},{"en":"Inexpensive technology spreads faster because more people can afford it.","zh":"廉價科技傳播較快，因為更多人能負擔。"},{"en":"The phrase is close to “low-cost technology”.","zh":"這個短語接近 “low-cost technology”。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"help poor people in rural areas","meaning":"幫助農村地區貧困人口","examples":[{"en":"Inexpensive technology can help poor people in rural areas.","zh":"廉價科技可以幫助農村地區貧困人口。"},{"en":"To help poor people in rural areas means to improve life for low-income communities in the countryside.","zh":"help poor people in rural areas 指改善鄉郊低收入社區的生活。"},{"en":"A low-cost lamp helps poor rural families when children can study after sunset.","zh":"當孩子能在日落後讀書，低成本燈具就幫助農村貧困家庭。"},{"en":"Helpful technology may reduce costs, improve safety, or create new opportunities.","zh":"有幫助的科技可能減少成本、改善安全或創造新機會。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on practical support for countryside poverty.","zh":"這個短語重點是對鄉郊貧窮的實際支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"produce less useful light than","meaning":"產生的有效光量少於……","examples":[{"en":"Kerosene lamps produce less useful light than LED lamps.","zh":"煤油燈產生的有效光量少於 LED 燈。"},{"en":"Produce less useful light than means give a smaller amount of practical, usable light compared with another source.","zh":"produce less useful light than 指與另一光源相比，提供較少實用可用光線。"},{"en":"A candle produces less useful light than a desk lamp when a student needs to read.","zh":"當學生需要閱讀，蠟燭產生的有效光量少於書枱燈。"},{"en":"Less useful light makes tasks harder because people cannot see details clearly.","zh":"有效光量較少令任務更困難，因為人們看不清細節。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the quality and amount of light produced.","zh":"這個短語比較產生的光的質素和數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"it is unlikely that","meaning":"不大可能","examples":[{"en":"It is unlikely that the government will connect all villages quickly.","zh":"政府不大可能快速把所有村落接駁電力。"},{"en":"It is unlikely that means something probably will not happen.","zh":"it is unlikely that 指某事大概不會發生。"},{"en":"It is unlikely that a student will improve writing without practising full essays.","zh":"學生不練習完整作文而改善寫作是不大可能的。"},{"en":"The phrase is used for cautious prediction when obstacles are clear.","zh":"當障礙清楚時，這個短語用於謹慎預測。"},{"en":"It does not mean impossible; it means not very probable.","zh":"它不等於不可能；它意思是可能性不高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"achieve one’s aim of","meaning":"達成……目標","examples":[{"en":"The government may struggle to achieve its aim of connecting villages to electricity.","zh":"政府可能難以達成把村落接駁電力的目標。"},{"en":"To achieve one’s aim of doing something means to successfully reach that goal.","zh":"achieve one’s aim of doing something 指成功達到該目標。"},{"en":"A student achieves her aim of improving speaking when she can answer interview questions confidently.","zh":"當學生能有信心回答面試問題，她就達成改善口語的目標。"},{"en":"Big aims require planning because many obstacles can delay success.","zh":"大目標需要規劃，因為許多障礙可以延誤成功。"},{"en":"The phrase links a goal with the action needed to reach it.","zh":"這個短語把目標與達成它所需的行動連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"connect villages to electricity","meaning":"將村落接駁電力","examples":[{"en":"The project aims to connect rural villages to electricity.","zh":"該項目旨在將農村村落接駁電力。"},{"en":"To connect villages to electricity means to provide villages with access to electric power, usually through a grid or local system.","zh":"connect villages to electricity 指為村落提供電力使用途徑，通常透過電網或本地系統。"},{"en":"Engineers connect a village to electricity by installing cables, meters, and transformers.","zh":"工程師透過安裝電纜、電錶和變壓器把村落接駁電力。"},{"en":"Connecting villages to electricity can support schools, shops, clinics, and evening study.","zh":"將村落接駁電力可以支援學校、商店、診所和晚間學習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rural electrification in practical terms.","zh":"這個短語以實際方式描述農村電氣化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"if it were not for","meaning":"要不是因為……","examples":[{"en":"The lamps would be cheaper if it were not for import duties.","zh":"要不是因為進口關稅，這些燈具會較便宜。"},{"en":"If it were not for something means if that thing did not exist or did not happen.","zh":"if it were not for something 指如果某事不存在或沒有發生。"},{"en":"The school trip would be easier if it were not for the heavy rain.","zh":"要不是因為大雨，學校旅行會較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the obstacle preventing a better result.","zh":"這個短語指出阻礙更好結果的障礙。"},{"en":"It often introduces a problem that raises cost, slows progress, or blocks success.","zh":"它常引入提高成本、拖慢進度或阻礙成功的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"wipe dust off","meaning":"抹走……上的灰塵","examples":[{"en":"Users need to wipe dust off the LED.","zh":"使用者需要抹走 LED 上的灰塵。"},{"en":"To wipe dust off something means to clean dust from its surface with a cloth or hand.","zh":"wipe dust off something 指用布或手清除某物表面的灰塵。"},{"en":"A student may wipe dust off a laptop screen before joining an online lesson.","zh":"學生可能在參加網課前抹走手提電腦屏幕上的灰塵。"},{"en":"Wiping dust off a lamp helps light pass through clearly.","zh":"抹走燈上的灰塵幫助光線清楚透出。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a simple cleaning action.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單清潔動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"keep it working well","meaning":"讓它保持良好運作","examples":[{"en":"Users clean the lamp to keep it working well.","zh":"使用者清潔燈具，以讓它保持良好運作。"},{"en":"To keep it working well means to maintain it so it continues to function properly.","zh":"keep it working well 指保養某物，使它繼續正常運作。"},{"en":"A student charges her tablet every night to keep it working well for class.","zh":"學生每晚為平板電腦充電，讓它在課堂上保持良好運作。"},{"en":"Regular care prevents small problems from shortening a device’s life.","zh":"定期照料防止小問題縮短裝置壽命。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on maintenance for reliable performance.","zh":"這個短語重點是為可靠表現而保養。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether the statements agree with the information given.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與所給資料一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the information given means match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the text says solar lamps are powered by the sun, the same statement agrees with the information given.","zh":"如果文本說太陽能燈由太陽供電，同樣的陳述就與所給資料一致。"},{"en":"Students must check the exact wording before choosing TRUE.","zh":"學生選 TRUE 前必須檢查準確措辭。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE、FALSE、NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章內容相反的東西。"},{"en":"If the text says the lamps are solar-powered, saying they run on kerosene contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文本說燈具由太陽能供電，說它們靠煤油運作就與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should choose FALSE only when the passage clearly says the opposite.","zh":"只有當文章清楚說出相反內容，學生才應選 FALSE。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a direct conflict with the text.","zh":"這個短語描述與文本直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"The answer is not given when there is no information on this.","zh":"當沒有這方面的資料時，答案就是 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not tell us enough to decide.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有提供足夠資料讓我們判斷。"},{"en":"If a text never mentions the price in another country, there is no information on this comparison.","zh":"如果文本從未提及另一國家的價格，就沒有這方面的比較資料。"},{"en":"Students should not use background knowledge when the passage gives no information.","zh":"當文章沒有提供資料，學生不應使用背景知識作答。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why an answer may be NOT GIVEN.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何答案可能是 NOT GIVEN。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"monthly ration of kerosene","meaning":"每月煤油配給","examples":[{"en":"Ganpat Jadhav’s monthly ration of kerosene was not enough.","zh":"Ganpat Jadhav 的每月煤油配給並不足夠。"},{"en":"A monthly ration of kerosene is a fixed amount of kerosene supplied or allowed each month.","zh":"monthly ration of kerosene 指每月供應或允許使用的固定煤油數量。"},{"en":"A family may receive a monthly ration of kerosene for lamps and cooking.","zh":"家庭可能收到每月煤油配給，用於燈具和煮食。"},{"en":"If the ration is too small, families must reduce lighting or buy extra fuel.","zh":"如果配給太少，家庭必須減少照明或購買額外燃料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a limited monthly fuel allowance.","zh":"這個短語描述有限的每月燃料配額。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be insufficient","meaning":"不足夠","examples":[{"en":"The family’s fuel quota was insufficient for the whole month.","zh":"這個家庭的燃料配額不足以支撐整個月。"},{"en":"To be insufficient means to be not enough for a need or purpose.","zh":"be insufficient 指對某需要或目的而言不夠。"},{"en":"One hour of revision may be insufficient before a major exam.","zh":"大考前只溫習一小時可能不足夠。"},{"en":"Insufficient fuel forces families to choose between lighting, cooking, and saving money.","zh":"燃料不足迫使家庭在照明、煮食和省錢之間作選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shortage compared with what is needed.","zh":"這個短語描述相對於需要而言的短缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"developing countries","meaning":"發展中國家","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to homes in developing countries.","zh":"該陳述提到發展中國家的家庭。"},{"en":"Developing countries are countries with lower average incomes and less developed infrastructure than wealthier industrialised nations.","zh":"developing countries 指平均收入較低、基礎設施比富裕工業化國家較不發達的國家。"},{"en":"In developing countries, some rural schools may lack computers, electricity, or clean water.","zh":"在發展中國家，一些農村學校可能缺乏電腦、電力或清潔食水。"},{"en":"Low-cost technology can be important in developing countries because full infrastructure may be expensive.","zh":"低成本科技在發展中國家可以很重要，因為完整基礎設施可能昂貴。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to national development level, not individual effort.","zh":"這個短語指國家發展水平，而不是個人努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"solve the world’s energy problems","meaning":"解決全球能源問題","examples":[{"en":"LED systems cannot solve the world’s energy problems on their own.","zh":"LED 系統不能單靠自己解決全球能源問題。"},{"en":"To solve the world’s energy problems means to fully fix global issues of energy supply, cost, pollution, and access.","zh":"solve the world’s energy problems 指完全解決全球能源供應、成本、污染和取得途徑的問題。"},{"en":"Solar lamps can help villages, but they cannot by themselves solve every country’s energy crisis.","zh":"太陽能燈可以幫助村落，但它們不能單靠自己解決每個國家的能源危機。"},{"en":"Complex problems require several solutions, including cleaner production, better grids, and fairer access.","zh":"複雜問題需要多種解決方案，包括更清潔生產、更好電網和更公平取得途徑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an extremely large goal.","zh":"這個短語描述極大的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"has so far funded","meaning":"到目前為止資助了……","examples":[{"en":"Chaddha has so far funded the lamp project himself.","zh":"Chaddha 到目前為止親自資助了燈具項目。"},{"en":"Has so far funded means has paid for or supported financially up to this point.","zh":"has so far funded 指到目前為止已支付或財政支持某事。"},{"en":"A teacher has so far funded the reading club herself by buying books with her own money.","zh":"老師到目前為止用自己的錢買書，親自資助了閱讀學會。"},{"en":"If one person has funded a project so far, future expansion may require outside support.","zh":"如果一個人到目前為止資助了項目，日後擴展可能需要外部支援。"},{"en":"The phrase shows financial support up to the present stage.","zh":"這個短語顯示截至目前階段的財政支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"get more people to use","meaning":"令更多人使用……","examples":[{"en":"Microcredit could get more people to use LED lamps.","zh":"小額信貸可以令更多人使用 LED 燈。"},{"en":"To get more people to use something means to make it easier or more attractive for more users to adopt it.","zh":"get more people to use something 指令更多使用者更容易或更願意採用某物。"},{"en":"Free trials can get more students to use a new learning app.","zh":"免費試用可以令更多學生使用新的學習應用程式。"},{"en":"Lower prices and small loans can get more rural families to use solar lighting.","zh":"較低價格和小額貸款可以令更多農村家庭使用太陽能照明。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on increasing adoption.","zh":"這個短語重點是增加採用率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 64 - Low-Cost Lamps Light Rural India.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 65":[{"front":"the rise of the robots","meaning":"機械人的興起","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the rise of the robots and other new technologies.","zh":"文章討論機械人的興起和其他新科技。"},{"en":"The rise of the robots means robots are becoming more common, powerful, and important in daily life.","zh":"the rise of the robots 指機械人在日常生活中變得更常見、更強大和更重要。"},{"en":"The rise of the robots can be seen in homes when robot vacuum cleaners start doing basic chores.","zh":"當機械人吸塵機開始做基本家務，家中就可看見機械人的興起。"},{"en":"As robots become cheaper and smarter, more offices and families may begin to use them.","zh":"隨着機械人變得更便宜和更智能，更多辦公室和家庭可能開始使用它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when technology starts replacing or assisting human work.","zh":"當科技開始取代或協助人類工作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be into technology","meaning":"對科技感興趣","examples":[{"en":"If you are into technology, you are living in wonderful times.","zh":"如果你對科技感興趣，你正生活在美好的時代。"},{"en":"Be into technology means be interested in new devices, machines, software, and inventions.","zh":"be into technology 指對新裝置、機器、軟件和發明感興趣。"},{"en":"A student who is into technology may enjoy testing new apps and building small robots.","zh":"對科技感興趣的學生可能喜歡測試新應用程式和製作小型機械人。"},{"en":"People who are into technology often notice new products before ordinary consumers do.","zh":"對科技感興趣的人常比普通消費者更早注意到新產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing someone’s strong interest in modern inventions.","zh":"描述某人對現代發明有濃厚興趣時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"live in wonderful times","meaning":"生活在美好的時代","examples":[{"en":"People who love technology are living in wonderful times.","zh":"熱愛科技的人正生活在美好的時代。"},{"en":"Live in wonderful times means experience a period full of exciting opportunities or developments.","zh":"live in wonderful times 指經歷一個充滿刺激機會或發展的時期。"},{"en":"Young language learners live in wonderful times because they can practise speaking online with people worldwide.","zh":"年輕語言學習者正生活在美好的時代，因為他們可以在網上與世界各地的人練習說話。"},{"en":"When tools improve quickly, ordinary people can do things that were once difficult or expensive.","zh":"當工具快速改善，普通人也能做到以前困難或昂貴的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing an exciting period of progress.","zh":"描述一個令人興奮的進步時期時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"develop in leaps and bounds","meaning":"突飛猛進地發展","examples":[{"en":"Technology is developing in leaps and bounds.","zh":"科技正突飛猛進地發展。"},{"en":"Develop in leaps and bounds means improve very quickly and noticeably.","zh":"develop in leaps and bounds 指非常快速而明顯地改善。"},{"en":"A student’s English may develop in leaps and bounds after daily speaking practice.","zh":"學生每天練習說英語後，英文可能突飛猛進地進步。"},{"en":"Rapid improvement often happens when better tools, strong effort, and good feedback come together.","zh":"當更好工具、強烈努力和良好回饋結合，快速進步常會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when progress is much faster than normal.","zh":"當進步比平常快得多時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"gadgets","meaning":"小型電子裝置","examples":[{"en":"Many new gadgets are becoming more advanced.","zh":"許多新小型電子裝置正變得更先進。"},{"en":"Gadgets are small electronic devices or tools designed to do useful or interesting tasks.","zh":"gadgets 指設計來完成有用或有趣任務的小型電子裝置或工具。"},{"en":"Smart watches, wireless earphones, and pocket translators are common modern gadgets.","zh":"智能手錶、無線耳機和口袋翻譯機都是常見現代小型電子裝置。"},{"en":"Useful gadgets can save time, entertain people, or make daily tasks easier.","zh":"有用的小型電子裝置可以節省時間、娛樂人，或令日常任務更容易。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing small pieces of consumer technology.","zh":"討論小型消費科技產品時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be set to break through","meaning":"即將取得突破","examples":[{"en":"Several new technologies are set to break through.","zh":"幾項新科技即將取得突破。"},{"en":"Be set to break through means be likely to achieve major progress or public success soon.","zh":"be set to break through 指很可能即將取得重大進展或大眾成功。"},{"en":"A small tutoring app may be set to break through if many students begin recommending it.","zh":"如果許多學生開始推薦，小型補習應用程式可能即將取得突破。"},{"en":"New products break through when the design, price, and public need finally match.","zh":"當設計、價格和公眾需要終於配合，新產品就會取得突破。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a technology is close to becoming successful.","zh":"當一項科技接近成功時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"backyard stargazing","meaning":"後園觀星","examples":[{"en":"Backyard stargazing goes seriously hi-tech with the Celestron SkyScout.","zh":"有了 Celestron SkyScout，後園觀星變得非常高科技。"},{"en":"Backyard stargazing means looking at stars from home or a simple outdoor space near home.","zh":"backyard stargazing 指在家中或家附近簡單戶外空間觀看星星。"},{"en":"A family may enjoy backyard stargazing on a clear night by lying on a blanket and looking up.","zh":"在晴朗晚上，一家人可能躺在毛氈上抬頭看天，享受後園觀星。"},{"en":"With a helpful device, backyard stargazing can become easier for beginners who do not know the sky.","zh":"有了有用裝置，後園觀星可以讓不懂天空的初學者更容易參與。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when astronomy becomes a simple home activity.","zh":"當天文變成簡單家居活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"go seriously hi-tech","meaning":"變得非常高科技","examples":[{"en":"Backyard stargazing goes seriously hi-tech with this device.","zh":"有了這個裝置，後園觀星變得非常高科技。"},{"en":"Go seriously hi-tech means become much more advanced through modern technology.","zh":"go seriously hi-tech 指透過現代科技變得先進很多。"},{"en":"A classroom can go seriously hi-tech when teachers use tablets, smart boards, and online quizzes.","zh":"當老師使用平板電腦、智能白板和網上測驗，課室可以變得非常高科技。"},{"en":"Ordinary activities can feel new when technology adds guidance, speed, or information.","zh":"當科技加入指引、速度或資訊，普通活動可以感覺煥然一新。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a simple activity becomes technologically advanced.","zh":"當簡單活動變得科技先進時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be judged to be","meaning":"被評為","examples":[{"en":"The Celestron SkyScout was judged to be the Best of Innovations.","zh":"Celestron SkyScout 被評為最佳創新獎。"},{"en":"Be judged to be means be officially considered or decided to be something after evaluation.","zh":"be judged to be 指在評估後被正式認為或判定為某事。"},{"en":"A student’s project may be judged to be the best design in a school competition.","zh":"學生的作品可能在學校比賽中被評為最佳設計。"},{"en":"Judges usually compare quality, usefulness, originality, and presentation before making a decision.","zh":"評判通常比較質素、實用性、原創性和展示方式後才作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when awards or evaluations are involved.","zh":"當涉及獎項或評估時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the Best of Innovations","meaning":"最佳創新獎","examples":[{"en":"The SkyScout was judged to be the Best of Innovations at the event.","zh":"SkyScout 在該活動中被評為最佳創新獎。"},{"en":"The Best of Innovations is an award or title given to a product judged highly innovative.","zh":"Best of Innovations 指授予被評為高度創新的產品的獎項或稱號。"},{"en":"A new medical device may win a Best of Innovations award if it solves a serious problem simply.","zh":"如果新醫療裝置能簡單解決嚴重問題，它可能贏得最佳創新獎。"},{"en":"Such awards can draw media attention and make customers trust a product more.","zh":"這類獎項可以吸引媒體注意，並令顧客更信任產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing prize-winning technology.","zh":"討論獲獎科技時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"press preview event","meaning":"傳媒預覽活動","examples":[{"en":"The product was shown at a press preview event in New York.","zh":"該產品在紐約一場傳媒預覽活動中展示。"},{"en":"A press preview event is a special showing for journalists before the public launch.","zh":"press preview event 指在公開推出前，為記者而設的特別展示活動。"},{"en":"A phone company may invite reporters to a press preview event before selling a new model.","zh":"手機公司可能在銷售新型號前邀請記者參加傳媒預覽活動。"},{"en":"Media previews help companies create attention before customers can buy the product.","zh":"傳媒預覽幫助公司在顧客能購買產品前製造關注。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing product launches and publicity.","zh":"討論產品發布和宣傳時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"it is not difficult to see why","meaning":"不難看出原因","examples":[{"en":"It is not difficult to see why the SkyScout impressed the judges.","zh":"不難看出 SkyScout 為何令評判留下深刻印象。"},{"en":"It is not difficult to see why means the reason is clear and easy to understand.","zh":"it is not difficult to see why 指原因清楚且容易理解。"},{"en":"It is not difficult to see why students like the teacher: she explains grammar with simple examples.","zh":"不難看出學生為何喜歡那位老師：她用簡單例子解釋文法。"},{"en":"When a product is useful, clever, and easy to use, people quickly understand its appeal.","zh":"當產品有用、聰明且容易使用，人們很快理解它的吸引力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining an obvious reason.","zh":"解釋明顯原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hand-held viewing device","meaning":"手提式觀測裝置","examples":[{"en":"The SkyScout is a hand-held viewing device for stargazers.","zh":"SkyScout 是供觀星者使用的手提式觀測裝置。"},{"en":"A hand-held viewing device is a small tool held in the hand to look at or identify things.","zh":"hand-held viewing device 指拿在手中用來觀看或識別事物的小工具。"},{"en":"A museum visitor may use a hand-held viewing device to read information about exhibits.","zh":"博物館訪客可能使用手提式觀測裝置讀取展品資訊。"},{"en":"Hand-held devices are useful because people can carry them easily while moving around.","zh":"手提式裝置有用，因為人們可以在四處移動時輕易攜帶。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing portable observation technology.","zh":"描述可攜式觀測科技時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be capable of","meaning":"能夠","examples":[{"en":"The device is capable of finding and identifying celestial objects.","zh":"這個裝置能夠找出並識別天體。"},{"en":"Be capable of means have the ability or power to do something.","zh":"be capable of 指有能力或力量做某事。"},{"en":"A modern phone is capable of translating simple sentences in real time.","zh":"現代手機能夠即時翻譯簡單句子。"},{"en":"A device becomes more useful when it is capable of doing tasks people cannot easily do alone.","zh":"當裝置能夠做人們難以獨自完成的任務，它會變得更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing ability or function.","zh":"描述能力或功能時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"find and identify","meaning":"找出並識別","examples":[{"en":"The SkyScout can find and identify objects in the night sky.","zh":"SkyScout 可以找出並識別夜空中的物體。"},{"en":"Find and identify means locate something and then say what it is.","zh":"find and identify 指找到某物的位置，然後說出它是甚麼。"},{"en":"A plant app can find and identify a flower when you point your camera at it.","zh":"當你把相機對準花朵，植物應用程式可以找出並識別它。"},{"en":"Identification is useful because finding something alone does not explain its name or meaning.","zh":"識別很有用，因為單是找到某物不會解釋其名稱或意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a tool both locates and recognises an object.","zh":"當工具同時定位並辨認物件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"celestial objects","meaning":"天體","examples":[{"en":"The device can identify more than 6,000 celestial objects.","zh":"這個裝置可以識別超過6,000個天體。"},{"en":"Celestial objects are natural objects in space, such as stars, planets, moons, and galaxies.","zh":"celestial objects 指太空中的自然物體，例如恆星、行星、衛星和星系。"},{"en":"Students may learn about celestial objects when studying the solar system.","zh":"學生學習太陽系時，可能會學到天體。"},{"en":"A database helps beginners name celestial objects that they can see but do not recognise.","zh":"資料庫幫助初學者命名他們看見但不認識的天體。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing astronomy.","zh":"討論天文學時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"visible to the naked eye","meaning":"肉眼可見的","examples":[{"en":"The SkyScout identifies celestial objects visible to the naked eye.","zh":"SkyScout 識別肉眼可見的天體。"},{"en":"Visible to the naked eye means able to be seen without a telescope, microscope, or special device.","zh":"visible to the naked eye 指不用望遠鏡、顯微鏡或特殊裝置也能看見。"},{"en":"Some stars are visible to the naked eye on a clear night away from city lights.","zh":"在遠離城市燈光的晴朗晚上，有些星星肉眼可見。"},{"en":"If something is visible to the naked eye, beginners can observe it without expensive equipment.","zh":"如果某物肉眼可見，初學者不用昂貴設備也能觀察它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing what people can see naturally.","zh":"討論人們自然能看見甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"transform something into","meaning":"把某物變成……","examples":[{"en":"The device transforms the night sky into a personal planetarium.","zh":"這個裝置把夜空變成個人天文館。"},{"en":"Transform something into something else means change it into a new form or experience.","zh":"transform something into something else 指把某物改變成新的形式或體驗。"},{"en":"A good teacher can transform a boring grammar point into a useful speaking tool.","zh":"好老師可以把沉悶文法點變成有用的口語工具。"},{"en":"Technology can transform a difficult task into something ordinary people can enjoy.","zh":"科技可以把困難任務變成普通人也能享受的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is changed strongly and meaningfully.","zh":"當某物被強烈而有意義地改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the night sky","meaning":"夜空","examples":[{"en":"The SkyScout helps users understand the night sky.","zh":"SkyScout 幫助使用者理解夜空。"},{"en":"The night sky is the sky seen after dark, especially when stars, planets, or the moon are visible.","zh":"night sky 指天黑後所見的天空，尤其是能看見星星、行星或月亮時。"},{"en":"Children may look at the night sky during a camping trip and ask why some stars are brighter.","zh":"孩子在露營旅行中可能看着夜空，問為甚麼有些星星較亮。"},{"en":"Understanding the night sky can make ordinary evenings feel more connected to science.","zh":"理解夜空可以令普通晚上感覺更與科學相連。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing stars and astronomy.","zh":"討論星星和天文時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"personal planetarium","meaning":"個人天文館","examples":[{"en":"The SkyScout turns the night sky into your own personal planetarium.","zh":"SkyScout 把夜空變成你自己的個人天文館。"},{"en":"A personal planetarium is a private astronomy guide that helps you learn about stars and planets.","zh":"personal planetarium 指私人天文導覽，幫助你認識星星和行星。"},{"en":"A child with a star-finding app may feel they have a personal planetarium in their pocket.","zh":"擁有尋星應用程式的孩子，可能覺得自己口袋裏有個人天文館。"},{"en":"Personal guidance makes complex sky information easier to understand.","zh":"個人化指引令複雜天空資訊更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when technology makes astronomy feel private and interactive.","zh":"當科技令天文感覺私人化和互動化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"GPS technology","meaning":"全球定位系統技術","examples":[{"en":"The SkyScout uses GPS technology to locate stars and planets.","zh":"SkyScout 使用全球定位系統技術定位恆星和行星。"},{"en":"GPS technology uses satellite signals to work out position and location.","zh":"GPS technology 指使用衛星信號判斷位置和方位的技術。"},{"en":"Drivers use GPS technology to find routes through unfamiliar cities.","zh":"司機使用全球定位系統技術，在陌生城市中尋找路線。"},{"en":"Accurate location information helps devices guide people more quickly and confidently.","zh":"準確位置資訊幫助裝置更快速和更有信心地引導人們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing navigation and positioning systems.","zh":"討論導航和定位系統時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"substantial celestial database","meaning":"龐大的天體資料庫","examples":[{"en":"The device uses a substantial celestial database.","zh":"這個裝置使用龐大的天體資料庫。"},{"en":"A substantial celestial database is a large collection of information about stars, planets, and other objects in space.","zh":"substantial celestial database 指關於恆星、行星和其他太空物體的大型資料集合。"},{"en":"A school astronomy app may use a database to explain what students see through a telescope.","zh":"學校天文應用程式可能使用資料庫，解釋學生透過望遠鏡看見的東西。"},{"en":"A large database lets a device identify many objects rather than only a few famous ones.","zh":"大型資料庫讓裝置能識別許多物體，而不只是少數著名物體。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when technology depends on stored astronomical information.","zh":"當科技依賴已儲存天文資訊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"camcorder-sized","meaning":"攝錄機大小的","examples":[{"en":"The SkyScout is a camcorder-sized device.","zh":"SkyScout 是攝錄機大小的裝置。"},{"en":"Camcorder-sized means about the size of a small video camera.","zh":"camcorder-sized 指大小約如小型攝錄機。"},{"en":"A camcorder-sized scanner is small enough to carry but large enough to hold comfortably.","zh":"攝錄機大小的掃描器足夠小，便於攜帶，也足夠大，拿起來舒服。"},{"en":"Size matters because a portable device must be easy to hold and use outdoors.","zh":"大小很重要，因為可攜式裝置必須容易在戶外握持和使用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the physical size of a gadget.","zh":"描述小型電子裝置的實際大小時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"enable stargazers to","meaning":"使觀星者能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The SkyScout enables stargazers to identify objects in the sky.","zh":"SkyScout 使觀星者能夠識別天空中的物體。"},{"en":"Enable stargazers to do something means allow people who watch stars to do that task.","zh":"enable stargazers to do something 指讓觀星者能夠完成某任務。"},{"en":"A clear star map can enable stargazers to find planets without guessing.","zh":"清晰星圖可以使觀星者不用猜測也能找到行星。"},{"en":"Helpful tools make difficult observations easier for beginners.","zh":"有用工具令初學者更容易進行困難觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when technology supports amateur astronomy.","zh":"當科技支援業餘天文時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"point the device at","meaning":"把裝置指向……","examples":[{"en":"Users can point the device at a visible object in the sky.","zh":"使用者可以把裝置指向天空中可見的物體。"},{"en":"Point the device at something means aim the device toward that object.","zh":"point the device at something 指把裝置瞄準某物。"},{"en":"A tourist may point the phone at a building to translate the sign on it.","zh":"遊客可能把手機指向建築物，以翻譯上面的標誌。"},{"en":"Pointing accurately helps the device know what object the user wants information about.","zh":"準確指向幫助裝置知道使用者想取得哪個物件的資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when using cameras, scanners, or viewing tools.","zh":"使用相機、掃描器或觀測工具時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"press a button","meaning":"按一下按鈕","examples":[{"en":"Users press a button to hear information about the object.","zh":"使用者按一下按鈕，便可聽到關於該物體的資訊。"},{"en":"Press a button means push a control on a device to make something happen.","zh":"press a button 指按下裝置上的控制鍵以令某事發生。"},{"en":"A child may press a button on a lift to choose the correct floor.","zh":"孩子可能按一下升降機按鈕來選擇正確樓層。"},{"en":"Simple button controls make technology easier for people who are not experts.","zh":"簡單按鈕控制令非專家也更容易使用科技。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing basic device operation.","zh":"描述基本裝置操作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"listen to a commentary","meaning":"聆聽旁述；聽取講解","examples":[{"en":"Users can listen to a commentary about the star or planet.","zh":"使用者可以聆聽關於該恆星或行星的講解。"},{"en":"Listen to a commentary means hear an explanation or spoken guide about something.","zh":"listen to a commentary 指聽取關於某事物的解釋或語音導覽。"},{"en":"Museum visitors can listen to a commentary while walking through an exhibition.","zh":"博物館訪客可以一邊走過展覽，一邊聆聽旁述。"},{"en":"Audio commentary helps people learn while looking at the object directly.","zh":"語音講解幫助人們在直接觀看物件時學習。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when information is given by spoken explanation.","zh":"當資訊透過口頭解釋提供時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"celestially challenged","meaning":"對天文一竅不通的","examples":[{"en":"The locate feature helps users who are truly celestially challenged.","zh":"定位功能幫助真正對天文一竅不通的使用者。"},{"en":"Celestially challenged humorously means very bad at understanding or finding things in the sky.","zh":"celestially challenged 是幽默說法，指非常不懂理解或尋找天空中的東西。"},{"en":"A beginner who cannot tell Mars from a bright star may be celestially challenged.","zh":"分不清火星和亮星的初學者，可能可說是對天文一竅不通。"},{"en":"Humorous phrases can make a difficult subject feel less embarrassing for learners.","zh":"幽默短語可以令困難科目對學習者來說沒那麼尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when joking kindly about someone’s lack of astronomy knowledge.","zh":"善意開玩笑地描述某人缺乏天文知識時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"do not have a clue","meaning":"完全不知道","examples":[{"en":"Some users do not have a clue where to look in the sky.","zh":"有些使用者完全不知道該看天空哪裏。"},{"en":"Do not have a clue means have no idea or no understanding about something.","zh":"do not have a clue 指對某事毫無概念或完全不明白。"},{"en":"A new student may not have a clue where the school office is on the first day.","zh":"新學生第一天可能完全不知道校務處在哪裏。"},{"en":"When people do not have a clue, clear guidance becomes especially important.","zh":"當人們完全不知道時，清晰指引變得特別重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone is completely uncertain.","zh":"當某人完全不確定時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"which bit of the heavens","meaning":"天空的哪個位置","examples":[{"en":"The device tells users which bit of the heavens to look in.","zh":"這個裝置告訴使用者應該看天空的哪個位置。"},{"en":"Which bit of the heavens means which part of the sky or space someone should look at.","zh":"which bit of the heavens 指某人應該觀看天空或太空的哪一部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may point out which bit of the sky contains the moon during an astronomy lesson.","zh":"在天文課中，老師可能指出天空哪個位置有月亮。"},{"en":"Dividing the sky into smaller areas helps beginners search more easily.","zh":"把天空分成較小區域，幫助初學者更容易尋找。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving informal directions for looking at the sky.","zh":"非正式地給予看天空方向時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"do not despair","meaning":"不要灰心","examples":[{"en":"If you cannot find the star, do not despair.","zh":"如果你找不到那顆星，不要灰心。"},{"en":"Do not despair means do not lose hope or become too discouraged.","zh":"do not despair 指不要失去希望或變得太沮喪。"},{"en":"If you fail your first mock exam, do not despair; use the mistakes to guide revision.","zh":"如果第一次模擬考試不合格，不要灰心；用錯誤來指引溫習。"},{"en":"Encouraging words help people continue when a task feels difficult.","zh":"鼓勵說話幫助人在任務感覺困難時繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comforting someone who is struggling.","zh":"安慰正在掙扎的人時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"locate feature","meaning":"定位功能","examples":[{"en":"The SkyScout’s locate feature guides users to stars and planets.","zh":"SkyScout 的定位功能引導使用者找到恆星和行星。"},{"en":"A locate feature is a function that helps users find where something is.","zh":"locate feature 指幫助使用者找出某物位置的功能。"},{"en":"A phone’s locate feature can help someone find a lost pair of earphones.","zh":"手機的定位功能可以幫助人找到遺失的耳機。"},{"en":"Location tools reduce searching time because they point people in the right direction.","zh":"定位工具透過把人指向正確方向，減少搜尋時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a device helps users find objects.","zh":"當裝置幫助使用者尋找物件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"guide someone to","meaning":"引導某人到……","examples":[{"en":"The SkyScout will guide you to the star or planet.","zh":"SkyScout 會引導你到那顆恆星或行星。"},{"en":"Guide someone to something means show or lead someone toward the correct place or object.","zh":"guide someone to something 指向某人展示或帶領某人前往正確地方或物件。"},{"en":"A school map can guide parents to the correct classroom on open day.","zh":"學校地圖可以在開放日引導家長到正確課室。"},{"en":"Clear guidance prevents people from wasting time searching in the wrong place.","zh":"清晰指引防止人們在錯誤地方浪費時間搜尋。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone needs help finding a target.","zh":"當某人需要幫助尋找目標時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"illuminated arrows","meaning":"發光箭嘴","examples":[{"en":"Illuminated arrows in the viewfinder guide the user.","zh":"取景器中的發光箭嘴引導使用者。"},{"en":"Illuminated arrows are lighted arrow signs that show direction.","zh":"illuminated arrows 指發光的箭嘴標誌，用來顯示方向。"},{"en":"A car park may use illuminated arrows to show drivers where to exit.","zh":"停車場可能使用發光箭嘴指示司機出口位置。"},{"en":"Lighted direction signs are helpful in dark places or when people need quick guidance.","zh":"在黑暗地方或人們需要快速指引時，發光方向標誌很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when visual signals guide movement.","zh":"當視覺訊號引導移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"viewfinder","meaning":"取景器","examples":[{"en":"The user follows the arrows in the viewfinder.","zh":"使用者跟隨取景器中的箭嘴。"},{"en":"A viewfinder is the part of a camera or viewing device that you look through to aim or frame what you see.","zh":"viewfinder 指相機或觀測裝置上供人觀看、瞄準或構圖的部分。"},{"en":"A photographer looks through the viewfinder before taking a picture.","zh":"攝影師拍照前會透過取景器觀看。"},{"en":"A clear viewfinder helps users aim accurately and avoid looking in the wrong direction.","zh":"清晰取景器幫助使用者準確瞄準，避免看錯方向。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing cameras and viewing tools.","zh":"討論相機和觀測工具時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mobile jukebox","meaning":"流動音樂播放器","examples":[{"en":"The Nokia N91 is described as an amazing mobile jukebox.","zh":"Nokia N91 被描述為一部令人驚喜的流動音樂播放器。"},{"en":"A mobile jukebox is a portable device that can store and play many songs.","zh":"mobile jukebox 指可攜帶並能儲存和播放許多歌曲的裝置。"},{"en":"A phone with thousands of songs can become a mobile jukebox for long bus rides.","zh":"一部有數千首歌的手機，可以成為長途巴士旅程中的流動音樂播放器。"},{"en":"Portable music storage changed how people listened to music away from home.","zh":"可攜式音樂儲存改變了人們離家後聽音樂的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a device works mainly as a music player.","zh":"當裝置主要作為音樂播放器時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be due out","meaning":"預定推出","examples":[{"en":"The Nokia N91 is due out early in 2006.","zh":"Nokia N91 預定於2006年初推出。"},{"en":"Be due out means be expected to be released or made available at a certain time.","zh":"be due out 指預計在某時間推出或可供購買。"},{"en":"A new textbook is due out next month, so teachers may wait before buying class copies.","zh":"新課本預定下月推出，所以老師可能等一等才買班本。"},{"en":"Release dates help customers, shops, and reviewers prepare for a product.","zh":"推出日期幫助顧客、商店和評論者為產品作準備。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing expected product launches.","zh":"討論預期產品發布時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"look set to be","meaning":"看來將會","examples":[{"en":"The Nokia N91 looks set to be in a class of its own.","zh":"Nokia N91 看來將會自成一格。"},{"en":"Look set to be means seem very likely to become something.","zh":"look set to be 指看來很可能會成為某種狀態。"},{"en":"A hardworking student looks set to be top of the class if they keep improving.","zh":"如果勤奮學生持續進步，他看來將會成為全班第一。"},{"en":"Early signs can make people expect future success before it fully happens.","zh":"早期跡象可以令人在成功完全發生前預期未來成功。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when predicting a likely result.","zh":"預測可能結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in a class of its own","meaning":"獨一無二；自成一格","examples":[{"en":"The Nokia N91 is in a class of its own as a multimedia phone.","zh":"Nokia N91 作為多媒體手機自成一格。"},{"en":"In a class of its own means much better, more special, or clearly different from others.","zh":"in a class of its own 指比其他事物好得多、更特別或明顯不同。"},{"en":"A teacher who explains difficult ideas with simple examples may be in a class of her own.","zh":"能用簡單例子解釋困難概念的老師，可能是獨一無二的。"},{"en":"A product stands apart when its features are far ahead of competitors.","zh":"當產品功能遠超競爭對手，它就脫穎而出。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is uniquely impressive.","zh":"當某事物獨特而令人印象深刻時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"multimedia mobile phone","meaning":"多媒體手提電話","examples":[{"en":"The N91 is a multimedia mobile phone.","zh":"N91 是一部多媒體手提電話。"},{"en":"A multimedia mobile phone is a phone that handles music, video, web browsing, and other media tasks.","zh":"multimedia mobile phone 指能處理音樂、影片、網頁瀏覽和其他媒體任務的電話。"},{"en":"A student may use a multimedia mobile phone to watch lessons, listen to recordings, and message classmates.","zh":"學生可能用多媒體手機觀看課堂、聆聽錄音和傳訊息給同學。"},{"en":"Phones became more useful when they stopped being only for calls.","zh":"當電話不再只用來通話，它們變得更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a phone combines many media functions.","zh":"當手機結合多種媒體功能時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"surf the web","meaning":"上網瀏覽","examples":[{"en":"The phone can surf the web and download videos.","zh":"這部手機可以上網瀏覽和下載影片。"},{"en":"Surf the web means browse websites and look for information online.","zh":"surf the web 指瀏覽網站並在網上尋找資訊。"},{"en":"A student may surf the web to find examples for a history project.","zh":"學生可能上網瀏覽，為歷史專題尋找例子。"},{"en":"Easy web access lets people check information wherever they are.","zh":"容易上網讓人們無論身在何處都可查資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing casual Internet browsing.","zh":"討論日常網上瀏覽時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"download videos","meaning":"下載影片","examples":[{"en":"The Nokia N91 can download videos.","zh":"Nokia N91 可以下載影片。"},{"en":"Download videos means receive video files from the Internet and save them on a device.","zh":"download videos 指從互聯網接收影片檔案並儲存在裝置上。"},{"en":"Students may download videos before a trip so they can watch lessons without Wi-Fi.","zh":"學生可能在旅行前下載影片，這樣沒有 Wi-Fi 也能觀看課堂。"},{"en":"Downloading media lets people use content later without staying connected online.","zh":"下載媒體讓人們之後不用保持連線也能使用內容。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing digital media storage.","zh":"討論數碼媒體儲存時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"contact details","meaning":"聯絡資料","examples":[{"en":"The phone can store contact details.","zh":"這部手機可以儲存聯絡資料。"},{"en":"Contact details are information such as a person’s phone number, email address, or home address.","zh":"contact details 指某人的電話號碼、電郵地址或住址等資料。"},{"en":"A school office keeps parents’ contact details in case a child becomes ill.","zh":"校務處保存家長聯絡資料，以防孩子生病。"},{"en":"Storing contact details helps people communicate quickly when needed.","zh":"儲存聯絡資料幫助人們在需要時快速溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing personal or business information.","zh":"討論個人或商業資訊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"organise your life","meaning":"安排日常生活","examples":[{"en":"The phone can generally organise your life.","zh":"這部手機大體上可以安排你的日常生活。"},{"en":"Organise your life means help you manage schedules, contacts, reminders, tasks, and daily plans.","zh":"organise your life 指幫助你管理時間表、聯絡人、提醒事項、任務和日常計劃。"},{"en":"A calendar app can organise your life by reminding you about classes, bills, and appointments.","zh":"日曆應用程式可以透過提醒你上課、繳費和約會來安排日常生活。"},{"en":"When people are busy, digital tools reduce forgetting and make routines easier to manage.","zh":"當人們忙碌時，數碼工具減少遺忘，令日常規律更易管理。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when technology helps with daily planning.","zh":"當科技幫助日常規劃時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"robust little phone","meaning":"堅固的小型手機","examples":[{"en":"The N91 is a robust little phone.","zh":"N91 是一部堅固的小型手機。"},{"en":"A robust little phone is a small phone that is strong, reliable, and not easily damaged.","zh":"robust little phone 指一部細小但堅固、可靠且不易損壞的手機。"},{"en":"A robust little phone is useful for students who often drop their bags on the bus.","zh":"對常在巴士上摔下書包的學生來說，堅固的小型手機很有用。"},{"en":"Durable design makes a device more suitable for everyday use.","zh":"耐用設計令裝置更適合日常使用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a small gadget is surprisingly tough.","zh":"當小型電子裝置出乎意料地耐用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"resplendent in","meaning":"以……顯得亮麗","examples":[{"en":"The phone is resplendent in its stainless steel case.","zh":"這部手機以不鏽鋼機身顯得亮麗。"},{"en":"Resplendent in something means looking bright, impressive, or attractive because of what it is wearing or covered with.","zh":"resplendent in something 指因穿着或覆蓋某物而顯得明亮、出眾或吸引。"},{"en":"A new shop may look resplendent in fresh paint and bright lighting.","zh":"新商店可能以新油漆和明亮燈光顯得亮麗。"},{"en":"A stylish outer design can make a product feel more premium.","zh":"時尚外觀設計可以令產品感覺更高級。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a striking appearance.","zh":"描述搶眼外觀時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stainless steel case","meaning":"不鏽鋼機身","examples":[{"en":"The N91 has a stainless steel case.","zh":"N91 有不鏽鋼機身。"},{"en":"A stainless steel case is an outer covering made of strong metal that resists rust.","zh":"stainless steel case 指由抗鏽堅固金屬製成的外殼。"},{"en":"A watch with a stainless steel case may last longer than one made of cheap plastic.","zh":"有不鏽鋼機身的手錶，可能比廉價塑膠製成的手錶更耐用。"},{"en":"Strong casing protects electronic parts and can make a product look more expensive.","zh":"堅固外殼保護電子零件，並可以令產品看起來更昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a device’s outer body.","zh":"描述裝置外殼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be equipped with","meaning":"配備","examples":[{"en":"The N91 is equipped with a hard drive.","zh":"N91 配備硬碟。"},{"en":"Be equipped with means have a particular tool, feature, or piece of equipment included.","zh":"be equipped with 指包括某種工具、功能或設備。"},{"en":"A classroom equipped with projectors and speakers can support more interactive lessons.","zh":"配備投影機和揚聲器的課室，可以支援更互動的課堂。"},{"en":"Extra equipment can make a product more useful for specific tasks.","zh":"額外設備可以令產品對特定任務更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing features built into something.","zh":"描述某物內置功能時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hard drive","meaning":"硬碟","examples":[{"en":"The N91 is the first Nokia phone to have a hard drive.","zh":"N91 是第一部有硬碟的 Nokia 手機。"},{"en":"A hard drive is a storage device used to save digital files such as music, photos, and documents.","zh":"hard drive 指用來儲存音樂、照片和文件等數碼檔案的儲存裝置。"},{"en":"A laptop with a large hard drive can store many videos and school projects.","zh":"有大型硬碟的手提電腦可以儲存許多影片和學校專題。"},{"en":"More storage allows users to keep more media without deleting old files.","zh":"更多儲存空間讓使用者保留更多媒體，而不用刪除舊檔案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing digital storage.","zh":"討論數碼儲存時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"store up to","meaning":"最多可儲存","examples":[{"en":"The hard drive can store up to 3,000 songs.","zh":"這個硬碟最多可儲存3,000首歌。"},{"en":"Store up to means hold a maximum of a particular amount.","zh":"store up to 指最多可容納某一數量。"},{"en":"A water bottle may store up to one litre, so it is enough for a short hike.","zh":"水樽最多可儲存一公升水，所以足夠短途行山。"},{"en":"A higher storage limit lets users carry more files, music, or data.","zh":"較高儲存上限讓使用者攜帶更多檔案、音樂或數據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing maximum capacity.","zh":"描述最大容量時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hi-fi quality headset","meaning":"高保真音質耳機","examples":[{"en":"The N91 has a hi-fi quality headset.","zh":"N91 有高保真音質耳機。"},{"en":"A hi-fi quality headset is a pair of earphones or headphones designed to produce high-quality sound.","zh":"hi-fi quality headset 指設計來產生高質素聲音的耳機。"},{"en":"A student may prefer a hi-fi quality headset when listening to pronunciation recordings.","zh":"學生聽發音錄音時，可能較喜歡高保真音質耳機。"},{"en":"Better sound quality makes music, calls, and language practice clearer.","zh":"更好音質令音樂、通話和語言練習更清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing audio equipment.","zh":"討論音響設備時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"remote control","meaning":"遙控器","examples":[{"en":"The phone comes with a headset and remote control.","zh":"這部手機配有耳機和遙控器。"},{"en":"A remote control is a small device or control unit used to operate something from a distance.","zh":"remote control 指用來從遠處操作某物的小裝置或控制器。"},{"en":"A television remote control lets people change channels without leaving the sofa.","zh":"電視遙控器讓人們不用離開梳化也能轉台。"},{"en":"Remote controls make devices easier to use because users do not need to touch the main machine.","zh":"遙控器令裝置更容易使用，因為使用者不用觸碰主機。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing convenient device control.","zh":"討論便利裝置控制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"support a wide range of","meaning":"支援多種……","examples":[{"en":"The N91 supports a wide range of digital music formats.","zh":"N91 支援多種數碼音樂格式。"},{"en":"Support a wide range of something means work with many different types of it.","zh":"support a wide range of something 指能配合多種不同類型的某物。"},{"en":"A printer that supports a wide range of paper sizes is useful in an office.","zh":"支援多種紙張尺寸的打印機在辦公室很有用。"},{"en":"Wide support reduces compatibility problems for users.","zh":"廣泛支援可以減少使用者的兼容問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a product works with many formats or options.","zh":"當產品能配合多種格式或選項時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"digital music formats","meaning":"數碼音樂格式","examples":[{"en":"The phone supports digital music formats such as MP3 and WMA.","zh":"這部手機支援 MP3 和 WMA 等數碼音樂格式。"},{"en":"Digital music formats are file types used to store music electronically.","zh":"digital music formats 指用來以電子方式儲存音樂的檔案類型。"},{"en":"MP3 is a common digital music format because it works on many devices.","zh":"MP3 是常見數碼音樂格式，因為它可在許多裝置上使用。"},{"en":"Supporting more formats helps users play songs from different sources.","zh":"支援更多格式幫助使用者播放來自不同來源的歌曲。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing music files and media compatibility.","zh":"討論音樂檔案和媒體兼容性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"wireless technology","meaning":"無線技術","examples":[{"en":"The phone uses wireless technology to find and buy music.","zh":"這部手機使用無線技術尋找和購買音樂。"},{"en":"Wireless technology sends data without physical cables.","zh":"wireless technology 指不用實體電線傳送數據的技術。"},{"en":"Wi-Fi and Bluetooth are forms of wireless technology used in homes and schools.","zh":"Wi-Fi 和藍牙是在家庭和學校使用的無線技術形式。"},{"en":"Wireless connections make devices easier to move, share, and use anywhere.","zh":"無線連接令裝置更容易移動、分享和在任何地方使用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing cable-free communication.","zh":"討論無線通訊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"operator’s music store","meaning":"電訊商的音樂商店","examples":[{"en":"Users can buy music from the operator’s music store.","zh":"使用者可以從電訊商的音樂商店購買音樂。"},{"en":"An operator’s music store is a digital shop run by a phone service provider.","zh":"operator’s music store 指由電話服務供應商營運的數碼商店。"},{"en":"A mobile user may download songs from the operator’s music store directly to the phone.","zh":"手機使用者可以從電訊商的音樂商店直接下載歌曲到手機。"},{"en":"Built-in stores make buying content easier because users do not need a separate computer.","zh":"內置商店令購買內容更容易，因為使用者不需要另一部電腦。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing mobile content services.","zh":"討論流動內容服務時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"drag and drop music","meaning":"拖放音樂檔案","examples":[{"en":"Users can drag and drop music from a PC to the N91.","zh":"使用者可以從個人電腦把音樂檔案拖放到 N91。"},{"en":"Drag and drop music means move music files by clicking, holding, and placing them in another location on a screen.","zh":"drag and drop music 指在螢幕上點擊、按住並把音樂檔案放到另一位置。"},{"en":"A student can drag and drop songs into a playlist before a school performance.","zh":"學生可以在學校表演前把歌曲拖放到播放清單中。"},{"en":"Simple file movement makes technology easier for users who dislike complicated menus.","zh":"簡單檔案移動令不喜歡複雜選單的使用者更容易使用科技。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing easy computer file transfer.","zh":"討論簡單電腦檔案傳輸時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"manage and share playlists","meaning":"管理和分享播放清單","examples":[{"en":"Users can manage and share playlists on the phone.","zh":"使用者可以在手機上管理和分享播放清單。"},{"en":"Manage and share playlists means organise song lists and send or show them to other people.","zh":"manage and share playlists 指整理歌曲清單，並把它們傳送或展示給其他人。"},{"en":"A student may manage and share playlists for a class party.","zh":"學生可能為班級派對管理和分享播放清單。"},{"en":"Sharing playlists helps friends enjoy the same music without choosing every song again.","zh":"分享播放清單幫助朋友不用重新選每首歌，也能享受相同音樂。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing digital music organisation.","zh":"討論數碼音樂整理時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get on the blower","meaning":"打電話","examples":[{"en":"If you can find the time, you can get on the blower, too.","zh":"如果你找得到時間，你也可以打電話。"},{"en":"Get on the blower is informal British English meaning make a phone call.","zh":"get on the blower 是非正式英式英語，意思是打電話。"},{"en":"A manager may get on the blower to a supplier when an urgent order is late.","zh":"當緊急訂單遲到，經理可能打電話給供應商。"},{"en":"People use this phrase casually when calling someone is only one of many tasks.","zh":"當打電話只是眾多任務之一，人們會輕鬆地使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in informal speech about using the phone.","zh":"在非正式談話中談及使用電話時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"no ordinary wristwatch","meaning":"不是普通手錶","examples":[{"en":"The Seiko Spectrum is no ordinary wristwatch.","zh":"Seiko Spectrum 不是普通手錶。"},{"en":"No ordinary wristwatch means not a normal watch because it has unusual or advanced features.","zh":"no ordinary wristwatch 指不是普通手錶，因為它有不尋常或先進功能。"},{"en":"A watch that measures heart rate, sleep, and messages is no ordinary wristwatch.","zh":"能量度心率、睡眠和訊息的手錶不是普通手錶。"},{"en":"The phrase prepares readers to expect something special.","zh":"這個短語讓讀者準備期待特別之處。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing a product that is different from normal examples.","zh":"介紹不同於一般例子的產品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at first glance","meaning":"乍看之下","examples":[{"en":"At first glance, the Seiko Spectrum looks like a futuristic bracelet-style watch.","zh":"乍看之下，Seiko Spectrum 像一隻具未來感的手鐲式手錶。"},{"en":"At first glance means when first looking at something, before examining it carefully.","zh":"at first glance 指初次觀看某物時，尚未仔細檢查。"},{"en":"At first glance, the café looked small, but inside it had three floors.","zh":"乍看之下，那間咖啡店很小，但裏面有三層。"},{"en":"First impressions can be incomplete because important details may appear later.","zh":"第一印象可能不完整，因為重要細節可能之後才出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when appearance changes after closer inspection.","zh":"當外觀在仔細觀察後改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"futuristic bracelet-style watch","meaning":"具未來感的手鐲式手錶","examples":[{"en":"The Seiko Spectrum is a futuristic bracelet-style watch.","zh":"Seiko Spectrum 是一隻具未來感的手鐲式手錶。"},{"en":"A futuristic bracelet-style watch is a watch that looks modern, advanced, and shaped like a bracelet.","zh":"futuristic bracelet-style watch 指看起來現代、先進並像手鐲形狀的手錶。"},{"en":"A designer may create a futuristic bracelet-style watch with a curved screen and no buttons.","zh":"設計師可能創造一隻有弧形螢幕且沒有按鈕的具未來感手鐲式手錶。"},{"en":"Unusual design can make a watch feel like fashion and technology at the same time.","zh":"不尋常設計可以令手錶同時感覺像時尚品和科技產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a wearable device looks advanced and stylish.","zh":"當可穿戴裝置看起來先進又有型時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"look closer","meaning":"仔細看","examples":[{"en":"Look closer, and you will notice the unusual display.","zh":"仔細看，你會注意到那個不尋常的顯示屏。"},{"en":"Look closer means examine something more carefully than before.","zh":"look closer 指比之前更仔細地檢查某物。"},{"en":"Look closer at a student’s essay, and you may find the ideas are good even if the grammar is weak.","zh":"仔細看學生的文章，你可能發現即使文法弱，想法仍然好。"},{"en":"Careful observation reveals details that quick judgement misses.","zh":"細心觀察會揭示快速判斷錯過的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when asking readers to notice hidden features.","zh":"要求讀者注意隱藏特徵時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"unlike any you have seen before","meaning":"與你以往見過的都不同","examples":[{"en":"The display is unlike any you have seen before.","zh":"這個顯示屏與你以往見過的都不同。"},{"en":"Unlike any you have seen before means very different from all previous examples you know.","zh":"unlike any you have seen before 指與你知道的所有以往例子非常不同。"},{"en":"A museum exhibition may be unlike any you have seen before if visitors can touch and move every object.","zh":"如果博物館展覽讓訪客觸摸和移動每件物件，它可能與你以往見過的都不同。"},{"en":"This phrase builds excitement by promising something new and unusual.","zh":"這個短語透過承諾新奇和不尋常事物來營造興奮感。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing an innovation that feels fresh.","zh":"描述令人耳目一新的創新時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"The display uses e-paper rather than the usual LCD screen.","zh":"這個顯示屏使用電子紙，而不是一般液晶屏幕。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of, and it clearly contrasts two choices.","zh":"rather than 指而不是，並清楚對比兩個選擇。"},{"en":"A student may revise with short daily practice rather than one stressful night before the exam.","zh":"學生可能用每天短時間練習來溫習，而不是考試前一晚才緊張苦讀。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate the chosen option from the rejected option.","zh":"這個短語幫助區分被選擇的選項和被拒絕的選項。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining why one method is used instead of another.","zh":"解釋為何使用一種方法而不是另一種時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the usual LCD screen","meaning":"一般液晶屏幕","examples":[{"en":"The watch does not use the usual LCD screen.","zh":"這隻手錶沒有使用一般液晶屏幕。"},{"en":"The usual LCD screen means the ordinary liquid-crystal display commonly used in electronic devices.","zh":"usual LCD screen 指電子裝置常用的普通液晶顯示屏。"},{"en":"Many calculators and older phones use the usual LCD screen to show numbers and text.","zh":"許多計數機和較舊手機使用一般液晶屏幕顯示數字和文字。"},{"en":"Choosing a different display can allow new shapes, lower power use, or better contrast.","zh":"選擇不同顯示屏可以帶來新形狀、更低耗電或更好對比度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting a standard screen with a new display.","zh":"對比標準螢幕和新顯示屏時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be made of","meaning":"由……製成","examples":[{"en":"The display is made of e-paper.","zh":"這個顯示屏由電子紙製成。"},{"en":"Be made of means consist of or be produced from a particular material.","zh":"be made of 指由某種特定材料組成或製成。"},{"en":"A school desk may be made of wood, metal, or plastic.","zh":"學校書桌可能由木材、金屬或塑膠製成。"},{"en":"The material something is made of affects its weight, strength, price, and appearance.","zh":"某物由甚麼材料製成，會影響其重量、強度、價格和外觀。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying materials.","zh":"識別材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"e-paper","meaning":"電子紙","examples":[{"en":"The Seiko Spectrum uses e-paper for its display.","zh":"Seiko Spectrum 使用電子紙作為顯示屏。"},{"en":"E-paper is an electronic display material designed to look more like paper than a normal screen.","zh":"e-paper 指設計成比普通螢幕更像紙張的電子顯示材料。"},{"en":"E-readers use e-paper so people can read comfortably for a long time.","zh":"電子閱讀器使用電子紙，讓人們可以長時間舒適閱讀。"},{"en":"E-paper can save power because it does not always need electricity to keep an image visible.","zh":"電子紙可以省電，因為它不一定需要電力來保持影像可見。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing low-power display technology.","zh":"討論低耗電顯示技術時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"electronic paper pioneers","meaning":"電子紙先驅","examples":[{"en":"E Ink Corp is described as one of the electronic paper pioneers.","zh":"E Ink Corp 被描述為電子紙先驅之一。"},{"en":"Electronic paper pioneers are early companies or inventors who helped develop e-paper technology.","zh":"electronic paper pioneers 指早期幫助發展電子紙技術的公司或發明者。"},{"en":"A company can be called a pioneer if it creates a useful technology before most competitors.","zh":"如果公司比大多數競爭者更早創造有用科技，它可以被稱為先驅。"},{"en":"Pioneers shape future markets because later products often build on their work.","zh":"先驅塑造未來市場，因為後來產品常建立在他們的工作之上。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing early leaders in display technology.","zh":"討論顯示技術早期領袖時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"constantly changing mosaic pattern","meaning":"不斷變化的馬賽克圖案","examples":[{"en":"The display shows a constantly changing mosaic pattern.","zh":"顯示屏顯示不斷變化的馬賽克圖案。"},{"en":"A constantly changing mosaic pattern is a design made of many small parts that keeps shifting or updating.","zh":"constantly changing mosaic pattern 指由許多小部分組成並持續轉變或更新的設計。"},{"en":"A digital art wall may show a constantly changing mosaic pattern to attract visitors.","zh":"數碼藝術牆可能顯示不斷變化的馬賽克圖案來吸引訪客。"},{"en":"Moving patterns can make a small display feel lively and futuristic.","zh":"移動圖案可以令小顯示屏感覺生動且有未來感。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a visual design that keeps changing.","zh":"描述持續變化的視覺設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"along with","meaning":"連同；和……一起","examples":[{"en":"The watch shows a mosaic pattern along with the time.","zh":"這隻手錶顯示馬賽克圖案，連同時間。"},{"en":"Along with means together with or in addition to something else.","zh":"along with 指與某事物一起，或除此之外還有。"},{"en":"A school notice may include exam dates along with room numbers and reminders.","zh":"學校通告可能包括考試日期，連同課室編號和提醒事項。"},{"en":"Adding extra information can make a product or message more useful.","zh":"加入額外資訊可以令產品或訊息更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when two things are presented together.","zh":"當兩件事一起呈現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"flexible and thin","meaning":"柔韌而纖薄","examples":[{"en":"E-paper is flexible and thin.","zh":"電子紙柔韌而纖薄。"},{"en":"Flexible and thin means able to bend easily and not thick.","zh":"flexible and thin 指容易彎曲且不厚。"},{"en":"A flexible and thin screen could fit on a curved watch band.","zh":"柔韌而纖薄的螢幕可以裝在彎曲錶帶上。"},{"en":"Thin flexible materials allow designers to create shapes that rigid materials cannot achieve.","zh":"纖薄柔韌材料讓設計師創造硬材料無法做到的形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing modern lightweight materials.","zh":"描述現代輕巧材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"curve round the wrist","meaning":"環繞手腕彎曲","examples":[{"en":"The display can curve round the wrist.","zh":"顯示屏可以環繞手腕彎曲。"},{"en":"Curve round the wrist means bend around the shape of the wrist.","zh":"curve round the wrist 指沿着手腕形狀彎曲。"},{"en":"A fitness band must curve round the wrist comfortably if people wear it all day.","zh":"如果人們整天佩戴，健身手環必須舒適地環繞手腕彎曲。"},{"en":"Curved displays can make wearable devices more natural to wear.","zh":"彎曲顯示屏可以令可穿戴裝置佩戴起來更自然。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing flexible wearable technology.","zh":"描述柔性可穿戴科技時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"watch band","meaning":"錶帶","examples":[{"en":"The display curves round the wrist along with the watch band.","zh":"顯示屏連同錶帶一起環繞手腕彎曲。"},{"en":"A watch band is the strap or bracelet part that holds a watch on the wrist.","zh":"watch band 指把手錶固定在手腕上的錶帶或手鐲部分。"},{"en":"A leather watch band may feel softer, while a metal one may look more formal.","zh":"皮錶帶可能感覺較柔軟，而金屬錶帶可能看起來較正式。"},{"en":"The band affects comfort because it touches the skin all day.","zh":"錶帶影響舒適度，因為它整天接觸皮膚。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing watch design.","zh":"討論手錶設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"conventional liquid-crystal displays","meaning":"傳統液晶顯示屏","examples":[{"en":"Conventional liquid-crystal displays have to be flat.","zh":"傳統液晶顯示屏必須是平面的。"},{"en":"Conventional liquid-crystal displays are traditional LCD screens used in many electronic devices.","zh":"conventional liquid-crystal displays 指許多電子裝置中使用的傳統 LCD 屏幕。"},{"en":"Older calculators, monitors, and phones often used conventional liquid-crystal displays.","zh":"較舊計數機、顯示器和手機常使用傳統液晶顯示屏。"},{"en":"If a display must be flat, designers have fewer choices for curved products.","zh":"如果顯示屏必須是平面的，設計師在彎曲產品上選擇較少。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing old screen technology with newer displays.","zh":"比較舊螢幕科技和新顯示技術時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have to be flat","meaning":"必須是平面的","examples":[{"en":"Conventional liquid-crystal displays have to be flat.","zh":"傳統液晶顯示屏必須是平面的。"},{"en":"Have to be flat means must have a level, non-curved shape.","zh":"have to be flat 指必須有平直、不彎曲的形狀。"},{"en":"A sheet of glass for a normal photo frame usually has to be flat.","zh":"普通相架用的玻璃片通常必須是平面的。"},{"en":"If a material has to be flat, it cannot easily wrap around the body or fit curved surfaces.","zh":"如果材料必須是平面的，它就不容易環繞身體或配合弧形表面。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining a design limitation.","zh":"解釋設計限制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not only…, but…","meaning":"不但……而且……","examples":[{"en":"The e-paper display not only produces better contrast but also uses less power.","zh":"電子紙顯示屏不但產生更好對比度，而且使用較少電力。"},{"en":"Not only…, but… links two advantages or facts, with the second often adding extra force.","zh":"not only…, but… 連接兩個優點或事實，第二個常加強語氣。"},{"en":"A good dictionary not only gives meanings but also shows useful examples.","zh":"好字典不但提供意思，而且展示有用例子。"},{"en":"This structure helps writers present two connected benefits clearly.","zh":"這個結構幫助寫作者清楚呈現兩個相關好處。"},{"en":"It is useful when one thing has more than one important advantage.","zh":"當一件事有多於一個重要優點時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"far better contrast than","meaning":"比……有好得多的對比度","examples":[{"en":"The e-paper display produces far better contrast than an LCD screen.","zh":"電子紙顯示屏比 LCD 螢幕有好得多的對比度。"},{"en":"Far better contrast than means the difference between light and dark is much clearer than in another display.","zh":"far better contrast than 指明暗差異比另一顯示屏清晰很多。"},{"en":"A printed page may have far better contrast than a cheap screen in bright sunlight.","zh":"在強烈陽光下，印刷紙張可能比廉價螢幕有好得多的對比度。"},{"en":"Better contrast makes reading easier because letters stand out more clearly.","zh":"更好對比度令閱讀更容易，因為字母更清楚突出。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing screen readability.","zh":"比較螢幕可讀性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"require no power to","meaning":"不需要電力去……","examples":[{"en":"The display requires no power to retain an image.","zh":"顯示屏不需要電力去保留影像。"},{"en":"Require no power to do something means need no electricity for that action.","zh":"require no power to do something 指做某動作不需要電力。"},{"en":"A printed poster requires no power to show information on a wall.","zh":"印刷海報不需要電力就在牆上顯示資訊。"},{"en":"Devices that need little power can last longer between charges.","zh":"需要很少電力的裝置，兩次充電之間可以使用更久。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing energy-saving technology.","zh":"討論節能科技時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"retain an image","meaning":"保留影像","examples":[{"en":"The e-paper display requires no power to retain an image.","zh":"電子紙顯示屏不需要電力去保留影像。"},{"en":"Retain an image means keep the picture or text visible on a display.","zh":"retain an image 指讓圖像或文字繼續在顯示屏上可見。"},{"en":"An e-reader can retain an image of a page without constantly refreshing like a bright screen.","zh":"電子閱讀器可以保留一頁的影像，而不用像亮屏幕那樣不斷更新。"},{"en":"If a display can retain an image with little power, battery life improves.","zh":"如果顯示屏能以少量電力保留影像，電池續航力就會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how certain screens save energy.","zh":"解釋某些螢幕如何省電時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"batteries last longer","meaning":"電池更耐用","examples":[{"en":"The watch’s batteries last longer because the display uses less power.","zh":"這隻手錶的電池更耐用，因為顯示屏耗電較少。"},{"en":"Batteries last longer means batteries continue working for more time before needing replacement or charging.","zh":"batteries last longer 指電池在需要更換或充電前能運作更長時間。"},{"en":"A wireless mouse’s batteries last longer if it turns off automatically when unused.","zh":"如果無線滑鼠不用時會自動關閉，電池會更耐用。"},{"en":"Lower power use helps portable devices stay useful throughout the day.","zh":"較低耗電量幫助可攜式裝置整天保持有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing energy efficiency.","zh":"討論能源效率時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"release only","meaning":"只推出","examples":[{"en":"Seiko is releasing only 500 of the watches.","zh":"Seiko 只推出500隻這款手錶。"},{"en":"Release only means make only a limited number available for sale or distribution.","zh":"release only 指只提供有限數量作銷售或分發。"},{"en":"A school may release only 100 tickets for a small concert hall.","zh":"學校可能因演奏廳細小而只推出100張門票。"},{"en":"Limited release can make a product feel rare and desirable.","zh":"限量推出可以令產品感覺稀有且令人想要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing scarcity.","zh":"討論稀缺性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"priced at about","meaning":"定價約為","examples":[{"en":"The watches are priced at about £1,250.","zh":"這些手錶定價約為1,250英鎊。"},{"en":"Priced at about means sold for approximately a particular amount.","zh":"priced at about 指以大約某金額出售。"},{"en":"A second-hand laptop may be priced at about £300 if it is still in good condition.","zh":"如果二手手提電腦狀態仍好，它可能定價約為300英鎊。"},{"en":"Approximate pricing helps customers judge whether something is affordable.","zh":"大約價格幫助顧客判斷某物是否可負擔。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving a rough price.","zh":"給出粗略價格時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lose no time","meaning":"不要耽擱","examples":[{"en":"If you want one of the watches, you had better lose no time.","zh":"如果你想要其中一隻手錶，你最好不要耽擱。"},{"en":"Lose no time means act immediately and not delay.","zh":"lose no time 指立即行動，不要延誤。"},{"en":"If scholarship applications close tomorrow, students should lose no time in submitting them.","zh":"如果獎學金申請明天截止，學生應立即提交，不要耽擱。"},{"en":"Urgency matters when supply is limited or the deadline is near.","zh":"當供應有限或截止日期接近，緊急性很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when warning someone to act quickly.","zh":"提醒某人快速行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"high-definition TV","meaning":"高清電視","examples":[{"en":"High-definition TV will hit the UK in 2006.","zh":"高清電視將於2006年在英國推出。"},{"en":"High-definition TV is television with a sharper and clearer picture than older standard TV.","zh":"high-definition TV 指比舊式標準電視影像更銳利、更清晰的電視。"},{"en":"A family may buy high-definition TV to watch sports with clearer detail.","zh":"家庭可能購買高清電視，以更清楚細節觀看體育賽事。"},{"en":"Better image quality can make films, news, and live events feel more realistic.","zh":"更好影像質素可以令電影、新聞和直播活動感覺更真實。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing improved television technology.","zh":"討論改良電視科技時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"already available in","meaning":"已在……推出","examples":[{"en":"HDTV is already available in the United States, Japan, and Australia.","zh":"高清電視已在美國、日本和澳洲推出。"},{"en":"Already available in means people can already buy or use it in those places.","zh":"already available in 指人們已可在那些地方購買或使用。"},{"en":"A new phone may be already available in Korea before it reaches other markets.","zh":"新手機可能在到達其他市場前已在韓國推出。"},{"en":"Availability in one country can create expectation in countries still waiting.","zh":"在一個國家可取得，可以令仍在等待的國家產生期待。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing product release by location.","zh":"按地區比較產品推出時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hit the UK","meaning":"在英國推出","examples":[{"en":"HDTV will hit the UK in 2006.","zh":"高清電視將於2006年在英國推出。"},{"en":"Hit the UK means arrive in the UK market or become available there.","zh":"hit the UK 指進入英國市場或在英國可供購買。"},{"en":"A popular Japanese game may hit the UK months after its first release in Asia.","zh":"熱門日本遊戲可能在亞洲首次推出數月後在英國推出。"},{"en":"When a product hits a market, shops, reviewers, and customers begin responding to it.","zh":"當產品進入市場，商店、評論者和顧客便開始回應它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in informal writing about product launches.","zh":"在非正式文字中討論產品發布時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be filmed in the HD format","meaning":"以高清格式拍攝","examples":[{"en":"A programme filmed in the HD format looks sharper and clearer.","zh":"以高清格式拍攝的節目看起來更銳利和更清晰。"},{"en":"Be filmed in the HD format means be recorded using high-definition video standards.","zh":"be filmed in the HD format 指使用高清影像標準拍攝。"},{"en":"A school concert filmed in the HD format will show faces and stage details more clearly.","zh":"以高清格式拍攝的學校音樂會，會更清楚顯示面孔和舞台細節。"},{"en":"The filming format affects how clear the final image appears on screen.","zh":"拍攝格式影響最終影像在螢幕上看起來多清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why video quality improves.","zh":"解釋影片質素為何改善時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sharper, clearer and more vibrant","meaning":"更銳利、更清晰、更鮮明","examples":[{"en":"HDTV produces a sharper, clearer and more vibrant image.","zh":"高清電視產生更銳利、更清晰、更鮮明的影像。"},{"en":"Sharper, clearer and more vibrant means more detailed, easier to see, and brighter in colour.","zh":"sharper, clearer and more vibrant 指細節更多、更易看見且顏色更鮮明。"},{"en":"A better projector can make classroom pictures sharper, clearer and more vibrant.","zh":"更好的投影機可以令課室圖片更銳利、更清晰、更鮮明。"},{"en":"Improved image quality helps viewers notice details they might otherwise miss.","zh":"改善影像質素幫助觀眾注意到原本可能錯過的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing better visual quality.","zh":"描述更佳視覺質素時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"image","meaning":"影像","examples":[{"en":"HDTV produces a more vibrant image.","zh":"高清電視產生更鮮明的影像。"},{"en":"An image is a picture or visual display shown on a screen, paper, or surface.","zh":"image 指顯示在螢幕、紙張或表面上的圖片或視覺畫面。"},{"en":"A clear image helps students read small labels in a science diagram.","zh":"清晰影像幫助學生閱讀科學圖中的細小標籤。"},{"en":"Better images make information easier to understand and remember.","zh":"更好影像令資訊更容易理解和記住。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing pictures, screens, and visual quality.","zh":"討論圖片、螢幕和視覺質素時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be due partly to","meaning":"部分原因是","examples":[{"en":"The better image is due partly to the way the programme is filmed.","zh":"更好影像部分原因是節目的拍攝方式。"},{"en":"Be due partly to means be caused in part by something, but not only by that thing.","zh":"be due partly to 指部分由某事造成，但不是只由那件事造成。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be due partly to daily practice and partly to better feedback.","zh":"學生進步可能部分原因是每日練習，部分原因是更好回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one result has more than one cause.","zh":"當一個結果有多於一個原因時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It helps writers avoid oversimplifying explanations.","zh":"它幫助寫作者避免把解釋過度簡化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"high-definition TV set","meaning":"高清電視機","examples":[{"en":"The high-definition TV set also helps produce a clearer image.","zh":"高清電視機也有助產生更清晰影像。"},{"en":"A high-definition TV set is a television designed to display high-definition pictures.","zh":"high-definition TV set 指設計來顯示高清影像的電視機。"},{"en":"A family may need a high-definition TV set to enjoy HD sports broadcasts properly.","zh":"家庭可能需要高清電視機，才能好好欣賞高清體育直播。"},{"en":"Even if a programme is filmed well, the screen must support the quality.","zh":"即使節目拍得好，螢幕也必須支援該質素。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the equipment needed for HD viewing.","zh":"討論高清觀看所需設備時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"visible rows of pixels","meaning":"可見像素行","examples":[{"en":"HDTV uses more visible rows of pixels than current sets.","zh":"高清電視比現時電視機使用更多可見像素行。"},{"en":"Visible rows of pixels are horizontal lines of tiny picture units that help form an image on a screen.","zh":"visible rows of pixels 指螢幕上形成影像的一行行微小畫面單位。"},{"en":"A screen with more visible rows of pixels can show finer details in a movie.","zh":"有更多可見像素行的螢幕，可以在電影中顯示更細緻細節。"},{"en":"More pixels usually make the picture look smoother and clearer.","zh":"更多像素通常令畫面看起來更順滑和更清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining screen resolution.","zh":"解釋螢幕解像度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"depending on","meaning":"視乎","examples":[{"en":"The number of visible rows depends on the HDTV format.","zh":"可見像素行的數量視乎高清電視格式。"},{"en":"Depending on means being affected or decided by another factor.","zh":"depending on 指受另一因素影響或由另一因素決定。"},{"en":"A student may take a bus or walk, depending on the weather.","zh":"學生可能搭巴士或步行，視乎天氣。"},{"en":"Choices change when conditions, costs, or requirements change.","zh":"當條件、成本或要求改變，選擇也會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the answer is not the same in every situation.","zh":"當答案在不同情況下不一樣時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"display images","meaning":"顯示影像","examples":[{"en":"HDTV uses rows of pixels to display images.","zh":"高清電視使用多行像素來顯示影像。"},{"en":"Display images means show pictures or visual information on a screen.","zh":"display images 指在螢幕上展示圖片或視覺資訊。"},{"en":"A classroom projector can display images from a teacher’s computer.","zh":"課室投影機可以顯示老師電腦中的影像。"},{"en":"Clear image display helps people understand diagrams, videos, and photographs better.","zh":"清晰影像顯示幫助人們更好理解圖表、影片和照片。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing screens and visual output.","zh":"討論螢幕和視覺輸出時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"HDTV uses more rows of pixels compared with current sets.","zh":"與現時電視機相比，高清電視使用更多行像素。"},{"en":"Compared with means when measured or judged against something else.","zh":"compared with 指與另一事物衡量或判斷時。"},{"en":"Compared with taking a taxi, taking the bus is usually cheaper but slower.","zh":"與乘的士相比，搭巴士通常較便宜但較慢。"},{"en":"Comparisons help readers understand improvement, difference, or scale.","zh":"比較幫助讀者理解改善、差異或規模。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting two things.","zh":"對比兩件事時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"current sets","meaning":"現時的電視機","examples":[{"en":"Current sets use 576 rows of pixels.","zh":"現時的電視機使用576行像素。"},{"en":"Current sets means the television sets commonly available or used at the present time in the passage.","zh":"current sets 指文章所指當時常見或正在使用的電視機。"},{"en":"Current phones may become outdated when new models offer much better batteries.","zh":"當新型號提供好得多的電池，現時手機可能變得過時。"},{"en":"Comparing new devices with current sets shows what has improved.","zh":"把新裝置與現時電視機比較，可以顯示改善之處。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing present technology before a new product arrives.","zh":"討論新產品出現前的現有科技時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be expecting visitors","meaning":"正等候訪客到來","examples":[{"en":"You might use the robot vacuum cleaner when you are expecting visitors.","zh":"當你正等候訪客到來時，你可能會使用機械人吸塵機。"},{"en":"Be expecting visitors means know that guests are going to come to your home or workplace.","zh":"be expecting visitors 指知道客人將會來到你的家或工作場所。"},{"en":"A family may tidy the living room when they are expecting visitors for dinner.","zh":"一家人正等候晚餐客人到來時，可能會整理客廳。"},{"en":"Visitors often make people clean, prepare food, and make a space look welcoming.","zh":"訪客常令人清潔、準備食物，並讓空間看起來歡迎人。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when guests are about to arrive.","zh":"當客人即將到來時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"do not bother to","meaning":"不用費心去……","examples":[{"en":"Do not bother to vacuum before your visitors arrive.","zh":"訪客到來前不用費心先吸塵。"},{"en":"Do not bother to do something means do not spend time or effort doing it because it is unnecessary.","zh":"do not bother to do something 指不用花時間或力氣做某事，因為它沒有必要。"},{"en":"If the shop is already closed, do not bother to walk there tonight.","zh":"如果商店已經關門，今晚不用費心走去那裏。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when an action would waste time or bring little benefit.","zh":"當某行動會浪費時間或幾乎沒有好處，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when telling someone not to make unnecessary effort.","zh":"告訴某人不用作不必要努力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"vacuum first","meaning":"先吸塵","examples":[{"en":"The passage jokes that you should not vacuum first.","zh":"文章開玩笑說你不應先吸塵。"},{"en":"Vacuum first means clean the floor with a vacuum cleaner before doing something else.","zh":"vacuum first 指在做其他事情前先用吸塵機清潔地面。"},{"en":"A family may vacuum first before moving furniture back into the living room.","zh":"家庭可能先吸塵，然後把家具搬回客廳。"},{"en":"Cleaning first can make a room ready, but a robot vacuum changes who does the work.","zh":"先清潔可以令房間準備好，但機械人吸塵機改變了誰做這項工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing cleaning order.","zh":"討論清潔次序時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"entertain someone with","meaning":"用……娛樂某人","examples":[{"en":"You can entertain visitors with the robot vacuum cleaner.","zh":"你可以用機械人吸塵機娛樂訪客。"},{"en":"Entertain someone with something means amuse or interest people by showing or using it.","zh":"entertain someone with something 指透過展示或使用某物令別人感到有趣或被逗樂。"},{"en":"A child may entertain relatives with a magic trick after dinner.","zh":"孩子可能在晚飯後用魔術表演娛樂親戚。"},{"en":"Unusual gadgets can entertain guests because people enjoy watching what they can do.","zh":"不尋常的小型電子裝置可以娛樂客人，因為人們喜歡看它們能做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is used to amuse others.","zh":"當某物被用來逗樂別人時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"robotic vacuum cleaner","meaning":"機械人吸塵機","examples":[{"en":"The Electrolux Trilobite 2.0 is a robotic vacuum cleaner.","zh":"Electrolux Trilobite 2.0 是一部機械人吸塵機。"},{"en":"A robotic vacuum cleaner is a machine that cleans floors automatically without a person pushing it.","zh":"robotic vacuum cleaner 指不用人推動也能自動清潔地面的機器。"},{"en":"A busy parent may use a robotic vacuum cleaner while cooking dinner.","zh":"忙碌家長可能一邊煮晚飯，一邊使用機械人吸塵機。"},{"en":"Automatic cleaning saves time and reduces routine housework.","zh":"自動清潔節省時間，並減少例行家務。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing household robots.","zh":"討論家居機械人時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"navigate its way around","meaning":"自行在……四處移動","examples":[{"en":"The robot navigates its way around your floors using ultrasound.","zh":"這部機械人使用超聲波自行在你的地板四處移動。"},{"en":"Navigate its way around means move through a space while finding a safe route.","zh":"navigate its way around 指在空間中移動，同時找出安全路線。"},{"en":"A delivery robot must navigate its way around tables, chairs, and people in a café.","zh":"送餐機械人必須在咖啡店中自行避開桌子、椅子和人群。"},{"en":"Good navigation prevents machines from getting stuck or hitting objects.","zh":"良好導航防止機器卡住或撞到物件。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a device moves by itself.","zh":"當裝置能自行移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"using ultrasound","meaning":"使用超聲波","examples":[{"en":"The Trilobite moves around using ultrasound.","zh":"Trilobite 使用超聲波四處移動。"},{"en":"Using ultrasound means using high-frequency sound waves to detect objects or measure distance.","zh":"using ultrasound 指使用高頻聲波偵測物件或測量距離。"},{"en":"A hospital scanner may create images using ultrasound.","zh":"醫院掃描器可能使用超聲波產生影像。"},{"en":"Ultrasound can help machines sense nearby surfaces without touching them.","zh":"超聲波可以幫助機器在不接觸物件下感應附近表面。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when sound waves guide technology.","zh":"當聲波引導科技時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"just like a bat","meaning":"就像蝙蝠一樣","examples":[{"en":"The robot uses ultrasound just like a bat.","zh":"這部機械人使用超聲波，就像蝙蝠一樣。"},{"en":"Just like a bat means in a similar way to how bats use sound to sense their surroundings.","zh":"just like a bat 指以類似蝙蝠用聲音感知周圍環境的方式。"},{"en":"A child may say a toy car avoids walls just like a bat if it uses sound sensors.","zh":"如果玩具車使用聲音感應器避開牆壁，孩子可能說它就像蝙蝠一樣。"},{"en":"Comparisons with animals make technology easier to understand.","zh":"以動物作比較令科技更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining a machine through a familiar natural example.","zh":"透過熟悉自然例子解釋機器時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"emit ultrasonic pulses towards","meaning":"向……發出超聲波脈衝","examples":[{"en":"The robot emits ultrasonic pulses towards surfaces.","zh":"機械人向表面發出超聲波脈衝。"},{"en":"Emit ultrasonic pulses towards something means send high-frequency sound signals in that direction.","zh":"emit ultrasonic pulses towards something 指向某方向發出高頻聲音信號。"},{"en":"A parking sensor may emit ultrasonic pulses towards a wall to judge distance.","zh":"泊車感應器可能向牆壁發出超聲波脈衝，以判斷距離。"},{"en":"The returning sound helps the device know where obstacles are.","zh":"反射回來的聲音幫助裝置知道障礙物在哪裏。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining sensor-based navigation.","zh":"解釋以感應器導航時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"create a map of","meaning":"建立……的地圖","examples":[{"en":"The robot creates a map of the room.","zh":"機械人建立房間的地圖。"},{"en":"Create a map of something means build a record of its layout, shape, or important positions.","zh":"create a map of something 指建立某物布局、形狀或重要位置的記錄。"},{"en":"A delivery app creates a map of nearby restaurants and roads.","zh":"外賣應用程式建立附近餐廳和道路的地圖。"},{"en":"Mapping a space helps a machine move more efficiently next time.","zh":"為空間製圖幫助機器下次更有效地移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when technology records where things are.","zh":"當科技記錄物件位置時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"future cleaning assignments","meaning":"日後的清潔任務","examples":[{"en":"The Trilobite remembers the room for future cleaning assignments.","zh":"Trilobite 會記住房間，以便日後的清潔任務。"},{"en":"Future cleaning assignments are cleaning tasks that will be done later.","zh":"future cleaning assignments 指之後要完成的清潔工作。"},{"en":"A cleaner may save a checklist for future cleaning assignments in the same office.","zh":"清潔工可能保存清單，以便同一辦公室日後的清潔任務。"},{"en":"Remembering a room helps a robot clean faster and avoid repeated mistakes.","zh":"記住房間幫助機械人更快清潔並避免重複錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when cleaning work is planned for later.","zh":"當清潔工作安排在日後進行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have no problem doing something","meaning":"做某事沒有問題","examples":[{"en":"The Trilobite has no problem avoiding collisions.","zh":"Trilobite 避免碰撞沒有問題。"},{"en":"Have no problem doing something means can do it easily or without difficulty.","zh":"have no problem doing something 指能輕易或毫無困難地做某事。"},{"en":"A confident student has no problem speaking to visitors in English.","zh":"有自信的學生用英語與訪客交談沒有問題。"},{"en":"When a machine has no problem with a task, users can trust it more.","zh":"當機器完成某任務沒有問題，使用者會更信任它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing easy ability.","zh":"描述輕易做到某事的能力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"avoid collisions with","meaning":"避免與……碰撞","examples":[{"en":"The robot avoids collisions with objects on the floor.","zh":"機械人避免與地上的物件碰撞。"},{"en":"Avoid collisions with something means prevent hitting or crashing into it.","zh":"avoid collisions with something 指防止撞到或碰上某物。"},{"en":"A self-driving car must avoid collisions with pedestrians, bicycles, and other cars.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車必須避免與行人、單車和其他車輛碰撞。"},{"en":"Avoiding collisions protects both the machine and nearby objects.","zh":"避免碰撞可以保護機器和附近物件。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing safe movement.","zh":"討論安全移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"objects placed on the floor","meaning":"放在地上的物件","examples":[{"en":"The Trilobite avoids objects placed on the floor.","zh":"Trilobite 會避開放在地上的物件。"},{"en":"Objects placed on the floor are things left or put on the ground, such as shoes, toys, or bags.","zh":"objects placed on the floor 指留在或放在地上的東西，例如鞋、玩具或袋。"},{"en":"A robot cleaner may slow down when it senses objects placed on the floor near a sofa.","zh":"機械人清潔器感應到梳化附近放在地上的物件時，可能會減速。"},{"en":"Floor obstacles can block movement if a machine cannot detect them.","zh":"如果機器不能偵測地面障礙物，它們可能阻礙移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing household obstacles.","zh":"討論家居障礙物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"magnetic strips","meaning":"磁條","examples":[{"en":"Special magnetic strips are placed in doorways.","zh":"特製磁條被放在門口。"},{"en":"Magnetic strips are narrow pieces of material that use magnetism to guide or control a device.","zh":"magnetic strips 指使用磁力來引導或控制裝置的窄條材料。"},{"en":"A robot vacuum may use magnetic strips to know where it should not go.","zh":"機械人吸塵機可能使用磁條知道哪些地方不應進入。"},{"en":"Boundary strips help machines stay inside safe or intended areas.","zh":"邊界條幫助機器留在安全或指定範圍內。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing simple control systems for robots.","zh":"討論機械人的簡單控制系統時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"doorways","meaning":"門口","examples":[{"en":"Magnetic strips are placed in doorways.","zh":"磁條被放在門口。"},{"en":"Doorways are openings where people enter or leave rooms.","zh":"doorways 指人們進出房間的開口位置。"},{"en":"A parent may put a baby gate in a doorway to stop a toddler from entering the kitchen.","zh":"家長可能在門口放嬰兒閘，阻止幼童進入廚房。"},{"en":"Doorways are useful control points because they connect one space to another.","zh":"門口是有用的控制點，因為它們連接一個空間和另一個空間。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing room boundaries.","zh":"討論房間邊界時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"stairs and other openings","meaning":"樓梯和其他開口位置","examples":[{"en":"Magnetic strips are placed near stairs and other openings.","zh":"磁條被放在樓梯和其他開口位置附近。"},{"en":"Stairs and other openings are places where a robot might fall, leave the room, or enter an unsafe area.","zh":"stairs and other openings 指機械人可能跌落、離開房間或進入不安全區域的地方。"},{"en":"A family may block stairs and other openings when a toddler is learning to walk.","zh":"當幼童學走路時，家庭可能阻擋樓梯和其他開口位置。"},{"en":"Blocking risky openings prevents accidents and keeps movement controlled.","zh":"阻擋危險開口可以防止意外並控制移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing safety boundaries in a room.","zh":"討論房間安全邊界時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"act as a wall","meaning":"起牆壁的作用","examples":[{"en":"The magnetic strips act as a wall.","zh":"磁條起牆壁的作用。"},{"en":"Act as a wall means function like a barrier, even if it is not a real wall.","zh":"act as a wall 指像屏障一樣發揮作用，即使它不是真正的牆。"},{"en":"A line of cones can act as a wall to guide students during sports day.","zh":"一排雪糕筒可以在運動會中起牆壁作用，引導學生。"},{"en":"Invisible or simple barriers help control movement without building permanent structures.","zh":"隱形或簡單屏障幫助控制移動，而不用建造永久結構。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something has the function of a barrier.","zh":"當某物有屏障功能時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"keep something in the room","meaning":"把某物限制在房間內","examples":[{"en":"The magnetic strips keep the Trilobite in the room.","zh":"磁條把 Trilobite 限制在房間內。"},{"en":"Keep something in the room means prevent it from leaving that room.","zh":"keep something in the room 指防止某物離開該房間。"},{"en":"A baby gate can keep a dog in the room while guests are eating.","zh":"客人吃飯時，嬰兒閘可以把狗限制在房間內。"},{"en":"Boundaries are useful when movement outside an area may cause trouble or danger.","zh":"當離開某範圍可能造成麻煩或危險，邊界就很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when controlling where a person, animal, or machine can go.","zh":"控制人、動物或機器能去哪裏時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"programme it to","meaning":"設定它去……","examples":[{"en":"You can programme it to clean while you are away.","zh":"你可以設定它在你外出時清潔。"},{"en":"Programme it to do something means set a machine so it performs a task automatically.","zh":"programme it to do something 指設定機器，使它自動執行某任務。"},{"en":"A coffee machine can be programmed to start brewing before you wake up.","zh":"咖啡機可以被設定在你醒來前開始沖咖啡。"},{"en":"Programming saves effort because the device follows instructions later by itself.","zh":"設定程式可以節省力氣，因為裝置之後會自己按指示運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a machine can be scheduled or controlled in advance.","zh":"當機器可以預先安排或控制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"glide around","meaning":"滑行；四處移動","examples":[{"en":"The robot can glide around while you are at work.","zh":"當你上班時，機械人可以四處滑行。"},{"en":"Glide around means move smoothly and quietly through a space.","zh":"glide around 指在空間中順滑而安靜地移動。"},{"en":"A robot vacuum may glide around the living room while the family watches television.","zh":"家人看電視時，機械人吸塵機可能在客廳四處滑行。"},{"en":"Smooth movement makes a machine feel less disruptive in a home or office.","zh":"順滑移動令機器在家中或辦公室較不打擾人。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing calm, smooth movement.","zh":"描述平穩順滑移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the original Trilobite","meaning":"第一代 Trilobite","examples":[{"en":"Electrolux introduced the original Trilobite in 2001.","zh":"Electrolux 於2001年推出第一代 Trilobite。"},{"en":"The original Trilobite means the first version of the Trilobite robot vacuum cleaner.","zh":"original Trilobite 指 Trilobite 機械人吸塵機的第一個版本。"},{"en":"A company may improve later models after learning from the original product.","zh":"公司可能從第一代產品中學習，然後改良後來型號。"},{"en":"Original versions often show the starting point for later innovation.","zh":"原始版本常顯示後來創新的起點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing first and later models.","zh":"比較第一代和後來型號時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be voted among","meaning":"被選為……之一","examples":[{"en":"The original Trilobite was voted among the 100 most innovative designs.","zh":"第一代 Trilobite 被選為100項最創新設計之一。"},{"en":"Be voted among means be chosen as part of a selected group by voters or judges.","zh":"be voted among 指由投票者或評判選入某個精選群組。"},{"en":"A school project may be voted among the best ten designs in a competition.","zh":"學生作品可能在比賽中被選為十個最佳設計之一。"},{"en":"Being selected can increase reputation and public interest.","zh":"被選中可以提升名聲和公眾興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is chosen for an honour list.","zh":"當某物被選入榮譽名單時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"innovative designs","meaning":"創新設計","examples":[{"en":"The Trilobite was voted among the 100 most innovative designs.","zh":"Trilobite 被選為100項最創新設計之一。"},{"en":"Innovative designs are new and clever ways of making products, spaces, or systems work better.","zh":"innovative designs 指以新穎聰明方式令產品、空間或系統更好運作的設計。"},{"en":"A foldable bicycle is an innovative design because it saves space in small flats.","zh":"摺疊單車是創新設計，因為它在細小單位中節省空間。"},{"en":"Innovative designs solve practical problems in ways people did not expect.","zh":"創新設計以人們意想不到的方式解決實際問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when praising creative product design.","zh":"讚揚創意產品設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"dedicated couch potatoes","meaning":"經常坐着看電視的人","examples":[{"en":"The passage jokes that the judges may have been dedicated couch potatoes.","zh":"文章開玩笑說評判可能是經常坐着看電視的人。"},{"en":"Dedicated couch potatoes are people who spend a lot of time sitting and watching television instead of being active.","zh":"dedicated couch potatoes 指花很多時間坐着看電視而不活動的人。"},{"en":"A dedicated couch potato may love a robot vacuum because it cleans while they stay on the sofa.","zh":"經常坐着看電視的人可能喜歡機械人吸塵機，因為它在人留在梳化時清潔。"},{"en":"The phrase is humorous because it gently criticises laziness.","zh":"這個短語帶幽默感，因為它輕輕批評懶散。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when joking about people who avoid physical effort.","zh":"開玩笑描述避免體力勞動的人時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be biased","meaning":"有偏見；有偏袒","examples":[{"en":"The judges may have been biased in favour of the robot vacuum cleaner.","zh":"評判可能偏袒機械人吸塵機。"},{"en":"Be biased means not judge fairly because of personal preference or prejudice.","zh":"be biased 指因個人偏好或偏見而不能公平判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher should not be biased toward students who speak more confidently.","zh":"老師不應偏袒說話更有自信的學生。"},{"en":"Bias can make a decision unfair even when the result looks official.","zh":"偏見可以令決定不公平，即使結果看起來正式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when questioning fairness.","zh":"質疑公平性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the name comes from","meaning":"名稱來自","examples":[{"en":"The name comes from a hard-shelled sea creature.","zh":"這個名稱來自一種硬殼海洋生物。"},{"en":"The name comes from means the word or title originated from a particular source.","zh":"the name comes from 指詞語或名稱源自某個特定來源。"},{"en":"The name of a street may come from an old village or famous local person.","zh":"街道名稱可能來自古老村莊或著名本地人物。"},{"en":"Knowing where a name comes from can make a product or place more memorable.","zh":"知道名稱來自哪裏，可以令產品或地方更令人記得。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining origins of names.","zh":"解釋名稱起源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hard-shelled sea creature","meaning":"硬殼海洋生物","examples":[{"en":"A trilobite was a hard-shelled sea creature.","zh":"三葉蟲是一種硬殼海洋生物。"},{"en":"A hard-shelled sea creature is an ocean animal with a tough outer covering.","zh":"hard-shelled sea creature 指有堅硬外殼的海洋動物。"},{"en":"Crabs and lobsters are hard-shelled sea creatures because their shells protect their bodies.","zh":"蟹和龍蝦是硬殼海洋生物，因為外殼保護牠們的身體。"},{"en":"A hard shell helps animals survive by reducing injury from predators or rough surfaces.","zh":"硬殼透過減少捕食者或粗糙表面造成的傷害，幫助動物生存。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing sea animals with protective shells.","zh":"描述有保護外殼的海洋動物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the Paleozoic era","meaning":"古生代","examples":[{"en":"The trilobite lived during the Paleozoic era.","zh":"三葉蟲生活在古生代。"},{"en":"The Paleozoic era is an ancient geological period long before humans existed.","zh":"Paleozoic era 指人類出現很久以前的一個古老地質時期。"},{"en":"Students learn about the Paleozoic era when studying fossils and early life on Earth.","zh":"學生學習化石和地球早期生命時，會認識古生代。"},{"en":"Naming the era helps readers place an extinct creature in deep time.","zh":"說明年代幫助讀者把已滅絕生物放在深遠時間中理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing prehistoric life.","zh":"討論史前生命時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"roam the ocean floor","meaning":"在海床上漫遊","examples":[{"en":"The sea creature roamed the ocean floor.","zh":"這種海洋生物在海床上漫遊。"},{"en":"Roam the ocean floor means move around across the bottom of the sea.","zh":"roam the ocean floor 指在海底表面四處移動。"},{"en":"Crabs may roam the ocean floor looking for food and shelter.","zh":"蟹可能在海床上漫遊，尋找食物和藏身處。"},{"en":"Animals roam when they search widely rather than stay in one small place.","zh":"當動物廣泛搜尋而不是留在一小處，牠們就是在漫遊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing movement by sea animals.","zh":"描述海洋動物移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"feed on","meaning":"以……為食","examples":[{"en":"The creature fed on particles and small animals.","zh":"這種生物以微粒和小動物為食。"},{"en":"Feed on means eat a particular kind of food.","zh":"feed on 指吃某一類食物。"},{"en":"Birds may feed on seeds, insects, or fruit depending on the season.","zh":"鳥類可能視乎季節以種子、昆蟲或水果為食。"},{"en":"What an animal feeds on affects where it lives and how it behaves.","zh":"動物以甚麼為食會影響牠居住在哪裏和如何行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing diet in biology.","zh":"在生物學中討論飲食時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"particles","meaning":"微粒","examples":[{"en":"The creature fed on particles and small animals.","zh":"這種生物以微粒和小動物為食。"},{"en":"Particles are very small pieces of matter.","zh":"particles 指非常細小的物質碎片。"},{"en":"Dust particles can be seen in sunlight when they float through a room.","zh":"灰塵微粒在陽光下飄過房間時可以被看見。"},{"en":"Tiny particles can become food for small organisms or pollution in the air.","zh":"細小微粒可以成為小生物的食物，或成為空氣中的污染物。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing small bits of material.","zh":"討論細小物質碎片時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"an extra pair of hands","meaning":"額外幫手","examples":[{"en":"Asimo can provide an extra pair of hands around the office.","zh":"Asimo 可以在辦公室提供額外幫手。"},{"en":"An extra pair of hands means additional help with tasks.","zh":"an extra pair of hands 指在任務上提供額外協助。"},{"en":"A busy restaurant may need an extra pair of hands when many customers arrive at lunchtime.","zh":"當午餐時間大量顧客到來，繁忙餐廳可能需要額外幫手。"},{"en":"Extra help reduces pressure and allows work to be finished faster.","zh":"額外協助減輕壓力，並讓工作更快完成。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone or something helps with practical work.","zh":"當某人或某物幫助實際工作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"look no further","meaning":"不用再找了","examples":[{"en":"If you need help around the office, look no further.","zh":"如果你需要辦公室幫手，不用再找了。"},{"en":"Look no further means you do not need to search anymore because the right option is here.","zh":"look no further 指你不用再搜尋，因為合適選項就在這裏。"},{"en":"If you want a quiet place to study, look no further than the library.","zh":"如果你想找安靜溫習地方，不用再找了，去圖書館就可以。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly recommends a solution as suitable or convenient.","zh":"這個短語強烈推薦某解決方法合適或方便。"},{"en":"It is useful in advertisements and informal recommendations.","zh":"它常用於廣告和非正式推薦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"showcase","meaning":"展示","examples":[{"en":"Honda showcased its second-generation humanoid robot.","zh":"Honda 展示了其第二代人形機械人。"},{"en":"Showcase means publicly display something to show its quality, features, or value.","zh":"showcase 指公開展示某物，以顯示其質素、功能或價值。"},{"en":"A school may showcase students’ artwork during open day.","zh":"學校可能在開放日展示學生藝術作品。"},{"en":"Companies showcase new products to attract attention from customers and journalists.","zh":"公司展示新產品，以吸引顧客和記者注意。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing public demonstrations.","zh":"討論公開示範時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"second-generation humanoid robot","meaning":"第二代人形機械人","examples":[{"en":"Asimo is a second-generation humanoid robot.","zh":"Asimo 是第二代人形機械人。"},{"en":"A second-generation humanoid robot is a newer version of a human-shaped robot improved after the first model.","zh":"second-generation humanoid robot 指在第一個型號後改良的新一代人形機械人。"},{"en":"A second-generation robot may walk more smoothly and understand people better than the first version.","zh":"第二代機械人可能比第一代走得更順暢，並更理解人類。"},{"en":"Later generations usually improve because engineers learn from earlier problems.","zh":"後來世代通常會改善，因為工程師從早期問題中學習。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing improved robot models.","zh":"描述改良機械人型號時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"come a long way since","meaning":"自……以來已有長足進步","examples":[{"en":"Asimo has come a long way since its first incarnation.","zh":"Asimo 自首個版本以來已有長足進步。"},{"en":"Come a long way since means improve greatly from an earlier stage.","zh":"come a long way since 指從早期階段以來大大進步。"},{"en":"A student has come a long way since their first nervous English presentation.","zh":"學生自第一次緊張的英文演講以來，已有長足進步。"},{"en":"Progress becomes clear when we compare the present version with the first attempt.","zh":"當我們把現時版本與第一次嘗試比較，進步就變得清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when praising development over time.","zh":"讚揚隨時間發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"first incarnation","meaning":"首個版本","examples":[{"en":"The robot’s first incarnation appeared five years earlier.","zh":"這部機械人的首個版本在五年前出現。"},{"en":"First incarnation means the first version or form of something.","zh":"first incarnation 指某事物的第一個版本或形式。"},{"en":"The first incarnation of a school website may look simple before later redesigns.","zh":"學校網站的首個版本在後來重新設計前可能看起來很簡單。"},{"en":"Early versions often lack features that later models add.","zh":"早期版本常缺少後來型號加入的功能。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how a product or idea began.","zh":"討論產品或想法如何開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"1.3-metre-tall droid","meaning":"1.3 米高的機械人","examples":[{"en":"Asimo is a 1.3-metre-tall droid.","zh":"Asimo 是一部1.3米高的機械人。"},{"en":"A 1.3-metre-tall droid is a robot about 1.3 metres high, especially one shaped like a person.","zh":"1.3-metre-tall droid 指約1.3米高的機械人，尤其是人形機械人。"},{"en":"A child-sized droid may feel less intimidating than a full-height robot.","zh":"兒童身高大小的機械人可能比成人高度機械人較不令人害怕。"},{"en":"Robot height affects how easily it can move through offices and interact with people.","zh":"機械人高度影響它能否輕易穿梭辦公室並與人互動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the size of a humanoid robot.","zh":"描述人形機械人的大小時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be capable of performing","meaning":"能夠執行","examples":[{"en":"Asimo is capable of performing a variety of office tasks.","zh":"Asimo 能夠執行多種辦公室工作。"},{"en":"Be capable of performing means have the ability to carry out or complete certain actions.","zh":"be capable of performing 指有能力進行或完成某些行動。"},{"en":"A well-trained assistant is capable of performing reception, filing, and scheduling tasks.","zh":"受過良好訓練的助理能夠執行接待、歸檔和排程工作。"},{"en":"The more tasks a robot can perform, the more useful it becomes in a workplace.","zh":"機械人能執行的任務越多，在工作場所就越有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing practical abilities.","zh":"描述實際能力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a variety of office tasks","meaning":"多種辦公室工作","examples":[{"en":"The robot can perform a variety of office tasks.","zh":"這部機械人能執行多種辦公室工作。"},{"en":"A variety of office tasks means several different kinds of work normally done in an office.","zh":"a variety of office tasks 指幾種通常在辦公室完成的不同工作。"},{"en":"Answering visitors, carrying documents, and giving directions are a variety of office tasks.","zh":"接待訪客、搬文件和指路都是多種辦公室工作。"},{"en":"Handling different tasks helps an office run more smoothly.","zh":"處理不同任務幫助辦公室更順暢運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing workplace duties.","zh":"討論工作場所職責時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reception duties","meaning":"接待職務","examples":[{"en":"Asimo can perform reception duties.","zh":"Asimo 能執行接待職務。"},{"en":"Reception duties are tasks related to greeting visitors, giving information, and directing people.","zh":"reception duties 指與迎接訪客、提供資訊和指引人們有關的工作。"},{"en":"A school receptionist performs reception duties when parents arrive for meetings.","zh":"家長到校開會時，學校接待員會執行接待職務。"},{"en":"Good reception duties create the first impression of an office or organisation.","zh":"良好接待職務會創造辦公室或機構的第一印象。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing front-desk work.","zh":"討論前台工作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"serve drinks","meaning":"端送飲品","examples":[{"en":"The robot is capable of serving drinks.","zh":"這部機械人能夠端送飲品。"},{"en":"Serve drinks means bring or provide drinks to people.","zh":"serve drinks 指把飲品送給或提供給人們。"},{"en":"A waiter may serve drinks before taking customers’ food orders.","zh":"侍應可能在為顧客點餐前先端送飲品。"},{"en":"Robots that serve drinks can save staff time during meetings or events.","zh":"能端送飲品的機械人可以在會議或活動中節省員工時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing hospitality tasks.","zh":"討論款待服務任務時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"act as an information guide","meaning":"擔任資料導覽員","examples":[{"en":"Asimo can act as an information guide.","zh":"Asimo 可以擔任資料導覽員。"},{"en":"Act as an information guide means function as someone or something that gives directions and useful facts.","zh":"act as an information guide 指發揮提供方向和有用資料的角色。"},{"en":"A museum tablet can act as an information guide for visitors who do not join a tour.","zh":"博物館平板電腦可以為沒有參加導賞團的訪客擔任資料導覽員。"},{"en":"Information guides help people understand where to go and what they are seeing.","zh":"資料導覽員幫助人們理解要去哪裏，以及正在看甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a person or device explains a place or service.","zh":"當人或裝置解釋地方或服務時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make deliveries","meaning":"送遞物品","examples":[{"en":"Asimo is capable of making deliveries.","zh":"Asimo 能夠送遞物品。"},{"en":"Make deliveries means take items from one place to another for someone.","zh":"make deliveries 指為某人把物品由一個地方帶到另一個地方。"},{"en":"An office assistant may make deliveries by bringing documents to different departments.","zh":"辦公室助理可能把文件帶到不同部門來送遞物品。"},{"en":"Delivery tasks take time, so robots can help reduce simple walking work.","zh":"送遞任務花時間，所以機械人可以幫助減少簡單步行工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing transport of small items.","zh":"討論小型物品運送時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"multiple sensors","meaning":"多個感應器","examples":[{"en":"Asimo uses multiple sensors to recognise its environment.","zh":"Asimo 使用多個感應器來識別其環境。"},{"en":"Multiple sensors are several devices that detect information such as movement, distance, sound, or objects.","zh":"multiple sensors 指幾個偵測移動、距離、聲音或物件等資訊的裝置。"},{"en":"A smart car uses multiple sensors to see lanes, signs, and nearby vehicles.","zh":"智能汽車使用多個感應器看見行車線、標誌和附近車輛。"},{"en":"More sensors can help a robot make safer and more accurate decisions.","zh":"更多感應器可以幫助機械人作出更安全和更準確決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how machines sense the world.","zh":"討論機器如何感知世界時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have the ability to","meaning":"有能力去……","examples":[{"en":"Asimo has the ability to recognise the surrounding environment.","zh":"Asimo 有能力識別周圍環境。"},{"en":"Have the ability to means be able to do something.","zh":"have the ability to 指能夠做某事。"},{"en":"A good translation app has the ability to recognise spoken language quickly.","zh":"好翻譯應用程式有能力快速識別口頭語言。"},{"en":"Abilities become valuable when they solve real problems for users.","zh":"當能力解決使用者的真實問題，它就變得有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing what a person, machine, or system can do.","zh":"描述人、機器或系統能做甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"recognise the surrounding environment","meaning":"識別周圍環境","examples":[{"en":"Asimo can recognise the surrounding environment.","zh":"Asimo 可以識別周圍環境。"},{"en":"Recognise the surrounding environment means detect and understand nearby people, objects, spaces, or obstacles.","zh":"recognise the surrounding environment 指偵測並理解附近的人、物件、空間或障礙物。"},{"en":"A cleaning robot must recognise the surrounding environment before moving under a table.","zh":"清潔機械人在移到桌下前，必須識別周圍環境。"},{"en":"Environmental recognition helps robots avoid danger and respond to people correctly.","zh":"環境識別幫助機械人避開危險，並正確回應人們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when machines understand what is around them.","zh":"當機器理解周圍有甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"interact with people","meaning":"與人互動","examples":[{"en":"The robot can interact with people using integrated circuit tags.","zh":"這部機械人可以使用集成電路標籤與人互動。"},{"en":"Interact with people means communicate with them or respond to their actions.","zh":"interact with people 指與人溝通或回應他們的行動。"},{"en":"A service robot can interact with people by answering questions and giving directions.","zh":"服務機械人可以透過回答問題和指路與人互動。"},{"en":"Good interaction makes technology feel more natural and less frightening.","zh":"良好互動令科技感覺更自然，也較不嚇人。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when machines communicate with humans.","zh":"當機器與人類溝通時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"integrated circuit tags","meaning":"集成電路標籤","examples":[{"en":"Asimo interacts with people using integrated circuit tags.","zh":"Asimo 使用集成電路標籤與人互動。"},{"en":"Integrated circuit tags are small electronic tags containing circuits that can store or send information.","zh":"integrated circuit tags 指含有電路、能儲存或傳送資訊的小型電子標籤。"},{"en":"An office card with an integrated circuit tag may identify a worker at the entrance.","zh":"有集成電路標籤的辦公室證件，可能在入口識別員工。"},{"en":"Electronic tags help machines recognise people, places, or objects automatically.","zh":"電子標籤幫助機器自動識別人、地方或物件。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing identification technology.","zh":"討論識別技術時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"at a fair pace","meaning":"以不錯的速度","examples":[{"en":"Asimo can walk and run at a fair pace.","zh":"Asimo 可以以不錯的速度行走和奔跑。"},{"en":"At a fair pace means at a reasonably good speed, not too slow.","zh":"at a fair pace 指以相當不錯的速度，不算太慢。"},{"en":"A student walking at a fair pace can reach school before the bell rings.","zh":"以不錯速度步行的學生可以在鐘聲響前到校。"},{"en":"A robot that moves at a fair pace can work alongside people more naturally.","zh":"以不錯速度移動的機械人，可以更自然地與人一起工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing moderate but acceptable speed.","zh":"描述中等但可接受速度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"push a cart","meaning":"推手推車","examples":[{"en":"Asimo can push a cart.","zh":"Asimo 可以推手推車。"},{"en":"Push a cart means move a wheeled container or trolley forward by applying force.","zh":"push a cart 指施力推動有輪子的容器或手推車向前移動。"},{"en":"A supermarket worker may push a cart full of goods to restock shelves.","zh":"超市員工可能推着滿載貨品的手推車去補貨。"},{"en":"Robots that push carts can help carry items without tiring human workers.","zh":"能推手推車的機械人可以幫助搬運物品，而不令員工疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing simple physical tasks.","zh":"討論簡單體力任務時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"plan to start using","meaning":"計劃開始使用","examples":[{"en":"Honda plans to start using Asimo’s receptionist functions.","zh":"Honda 計劃開始使用 Asimo 的接待員功能。"},{"en":"Plan to start using means intend to begin using something in the future.","zh":"plan to start using 指打算在將來開始使用某物。"},{"en":"A school may plan to start using online booking for parent meetings next term.","zh":"學校可能計劃下學期開始使用網上預約家長會。"},{"en":"Planning to use a new tool shows that testing may soon become real application.","zh":"計劃使用新工具顯示測試可能很快變成實際應用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when future use is being prepared.","zh":"當未來使用正在準備時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"receptionist functions","meaning":"接待員功能","examples":[{"en":"Honda plans to use Asimo’s receptionist functions in Japan.","zh":"Honda 計劃在日本使用 Asimo 的接待員功能。"},{"en":"Receptionist functions are abilities related to greeting visitors, giving directions, and providing basic information.","zh":"receptionist functions 指與迎接訪客、指路和提供基本資訊有關的能力。"},{"en":"A hotel robot with receptionist functions can tell guests where breakfast is served.","zh":"有接待員功能的酒店機械人可以告訴客人早餐在哪裏供應。"},{"en":"These functions are useful because reception work often involves repeated simple questions.","zh":"這些功能很有用，因為接待工作常涉及重複的簡單問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a machine performs front-desk duties.","zh":"當機器執行前台職責時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"become available for leasing","meaning":"可供租用","examples":[{"en":"It is hoped that Asimo will become available for leasing afterwards.","zh":"人們希望 Asimo 之後會可供租用。"},{"en":"Become available for leasing means become possible for customers to rent for a period rather than buy.","zh":"become available for leasing 指顧客可以租用一段時間，而不是購買。"},{"en":"Expensive office machines may become available for leasing so small companies can use them affordably.","zh":"昂貴辦公室機器可能可供租用，讓小公司能以較可負擔方式使用。"},{"en":"Leasing reduces upfront cost and lets users try technology before owning it.","zh":"租用減少前期成本，並讓使用者在擁有科技前先試用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a product can be rented commercially.","zh":"當產品可作商業租用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"afterwards","meaning":"之後","examples":[{"en":"Asimo may become available for leasing afterwards.","zh":"Asimo 之後可能可供租用。"},{"en":"Afterwards means after that time or event.","zh":"afterwards 指在那個時間或事件之後。"},{"en":"Students may finish the mock test first and discuss mistakes afterwards.","zh":"學生可能先完成模擬測驗，之後再討論錯誤。"},{"en":"This word helps show the order of events clearly.","zh":"這個詞幫助清楚顯示事件次序。"},{"en":"It is useful when one action happens after another.","zh":"當一個行動在另一個行動之後發生時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"at an office near you","meaning":"在你附近的辦公室","examples":[{"en":"Asimo could soon be pushing a cart at an office near you.","zh":"Asimo 可能很快就在你附近的辦公室推手推車。"},{"en":"At an office near you means in a nearby workplace, used playfully to suggest the technology may soon be common.","zh":"at an office near you 指在附近工作場所，帶玩笑語氣，暗示科技可能很快變得常見。"},{"en":"A new delivery robot could soon be serving coffee at a café near you.","zh":"新送餐機械人可能很快就在你附近的咖啡店送咖啡。"},{"en":"This phrase makes future technology feel close to ordinary daily life.","zh":"這個短語令未來科技感覺接近日常生活。"},{"en":"It is useful in informal product writing with a promotional tone.","zh":"它適用於帶宣傳語氣的非正式產品文字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"for each question","meaning":"每條題目","examples":[{"en":"For each question, only one of the choices is correct.","zh":"每條題目只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"For each question means for every individual item in a test or exercise.","zh":"for each question 指對測驗或練習中的每一個題目而言。"},{"en":"For each question, students should read all options before choosing an answer.","zh":"每條題目中，學生應先閱讀所有選項才選答案。"},{"en":"Careful checking prevents mistakes caused by rushing through similar choices.","zh":"仔細檢查可以防止因匆忙處理相似選項而犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"only one of the choices is correct","meaning":"只有一個選項正確","examples":[{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct.","zh":"只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct means students must choose one answer, not several.","zh":"only one of the choices is correct 指學生必須選一個答案，而不是幾個。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice reading question, only one option may match the passage exactly.","zh":"在多項選擇閱讀題中，只有一個選項可能完全符合文章。"},{"en":"This instruction stops students from selecting two answers even if two seem possible.","zh":"這個指示防止學生即使覺得兩個都可能，也選兩個答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when exam answers are strictly single-choice.","zh":"當考試答案嚴格只可單選時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"corresponding letter","meaning":"相應字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the corresponding letter in the box.","zh":"考生在方格內寫下相應字母。"},{"en":"Corresponding letter means the letter that matches the correct answer or option.","zh":"corresponding letter 指與正確答案或選項相配的字母。"},{"en":"If option B is correct, students write the corresponding letter B on the answer sheet.","zh":"如果選項 B 正確，學生就在答題紙上寫下相應字母 B。"},{"en":"Writing the wrong letter loses marks even if the student understood the idea.","zh":"即使學生理解意思，寫錯字母也會失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in multiple-choice and matching questions.","zh":"這個短語適用於多項選擇和配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"appropriate box","meaning":"適當方格","examples":[{"en":"Students write the letter in the appropriate box on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生在答題紙上的適當方格內寫下字母。"},{"en":"Appropriate box means the correct space where an answer should be written.","zh":"appropriate box 指答案應填寫的正確空格。"},{"en":"In an exam, students must put each answer in the appropriate box beside the question number.","zh":"在考試中，學生必須把每個答案寫在題號旁的適當方格。"},{"en":"Writing in the wrong box can make a correct answer look wrong.","zh":"寫在錯誤方格中，可以令正確答案看起來錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in test instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"provide information about","meaning":"提供關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"The Celestron SkyScout can provide information about the stars.","zh":"Celestron SkyScout 可以提供關於星星的資料。"},{"en":"Provide information about something means give facts, explanations, or details about it.","zh":"provide information about something 指提供關於某事物的事實、解釋或細節。"},{"en":"A school website can provide information about fees, timetables, and application dates.","zh":"學校網站可以提供關於費用、時間表和申請日期的資料。"},{"en":"Good information helps users make decisions or understand what they are seeing.","zh":"良好資訊幫助使用者作決定或理解自己正在看甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a person, text, or device explains a topic.","zh":"當人、文本或裝置解釋某主題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"where in the world you are","meaning":"你身處世界哪個位置","examples":[{"en":"GPS technology can tell you where in the world you are.","zh":"全球定位系統技術可以告訴你身處世界哪個位置。"},{"en":"Where in the world you are means your exact or general location on Earth.","zh":"where in the world you are 指你在地球上的準確或大概位置。"},{"en":"A travel app can show where in the world you are when you arrive in an unfamiliar city.","zh":"當你到達陌生城市，旅行應用程式可以顯示你身處世界哪個位置。"},{"en":"Knowing location helps devices provide maps, directions, weather, and local information.","zh":"知道位置幫助裝置提供地圖、方向、天氣和本地資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing global positioning.","zh":"討論全球定位時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"normally visible","meaning":"通常可見的","examples":[{"en":"Some objects in the sky are not normally visible.","zh":"天空中有些物體通常不可見。"},{"en":"Normally visible means usually able to be seen under ordinary conditions.","zh":"normally visible 指在普通情況下通常能看見。"},{"en":"A small road sign may not be normally visible at night without street lights.","zh":"沒有街燈時，小型路牌在晚上可能通常不可見。"},{"en":"Visibility changes with distance, light, weather, and equipment.","zh":"可見性會隨距離、光線、天氣和設備改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing what people can usually see.","zh":"討論人們通常能看見甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be used for surfing the Internet","meaning":"可用作上網瀏覽","examples":[{"en":"The answer option says the watch can be used for surfing the Internet.","zh":"這個答案選項說這隻手錶可用作上網瀏覽。"},{"en":"Be used for surfing the Internet means be used to browse websites online.","zh":"be used for surfing the Internet 指可用來在網上瀏覽網站。"},{"en":"A tablet can be used for surfing the Internet during a train journey.","zh":"平板電腦可以在火車旅程中用作上網瀏覽。"},{"en":"If a device can browse the web, it becomes more useful than a simple single-purpose tool.","zh":"如果裝置能瀏覽網頁，它就比單一用途工具更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing Internet functions.","zh":"描述互聯網功能時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be produced as a limited edition","meaning":"限量生產","examples":[{"en":"The Seiko Spectrum is being produced as a limited edition.","zh":"Seiko Spectrum 正被限量生產。"},{"en":"Be produced as a limited edition means be made in a small fixed number rather than mass-produced.","zh":"be produced as a limited edition 指以固定少量製造，而不是大量生產。"},{"en":"A fashion brand may produce a jacket as a limited edition to make it feel special.","zh":"時裝品牌可能限量生產一件外套，令它感覺特別。"},{"en":"Limited editions can create urgency because customers know supply will run out.","zh":"限量版可以製造緊迫感，因為顧客知道供應會售罄。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing rare products.","zh":"討論稀有產品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ask permission before","meaning":"在……之前徵求許可","examples":[{"en":"The answer option jokes that the robot asks permission before moving rooms.","zh":"這個答案選項開玩笑說機械人在移動房間之前會徵求許可。"},{"en":"Ask permission before doing something means get approval first.","zh":"ask permission before doing something 指先取得批准。"},{"en":"Students should ask permission before leaving the classroom during a lesson.","zh":"學生在課堂中離開課室前應徵求許可。"},{"en":"Asking permission shows respect for rules, safety, or other people’s space.","zh":"徵求許可顯示對規則、安全或他人空間的尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an action needs approval first.","zh":"當行動需要先獲批准時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"move from room to room","meaning":"從一個房間移到另一個房間","examples":[{"en":"A robot vacuum cleaner may move from room to room.","zh":"機械人吸塵機可能從一個房間移到另一個房間。"},{"en":"Move from room to room means go between different rooms in a building.","zh":"move from room to room 指在建築物內不同房間之間移動。"},{"en":"A cleaner may move from room to room while checking whether all windows are closed.","zh":"清潔工可能一邊檢查所有窗戶是否關上，一邊從一個房間移到另一個房間。"},{"en":"Moving between rooms requires a robot to recognise doorways, obstacles, and boundaries.","zh":"在房間之間移動需要機械人識別門口、障礙物和邊界。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing movement inside a home or office.","zh":"描述在家中或辦公室內移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"help it avoid objects","meaning":"幫助它避開物件","examples":[{"en":"The robot uses technology to help it avoid objects.","zh":"機械人使用科技來幫助它避開物件。"},{"en":"Help it avoid objects means assist the robot in not hitting things around it.","zh":"help it avoid objects 指協助機械人不要撞到周圍的東西。"},{"en":"A floor sensor can help a robot avoid shoes left near the doorway.","zh":"地面感應器可以幫助機械人避開留在門口附近的鞋。"},{"en":"Obstacle avoidance protects furniture and keeps the machine working smoothly.","zh":"避障功能保護家具，並保持機器順暢運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining safety features in robots.","zh":"解釋機械人安全功能時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be programmable","meaning":"可編程；可設定程序","examples":[{"en":"The Electrolux Trilobite 2.0 is programmable.","zh":"Electrolux Trilobite 2.0 是可編程的。"},{"en":"Be programmable means can be set or instructed to perform tasks automatically.","zh":"be programmable 指可以被設定或指示自動執行任務。"},{"en":"A programmable oven can start heating dinner before the family gets home.","zh":"可編程焗爐可以在家人回家前開始加熱晚餐。"},{"en":"Programmable devices save time because users do not have to control every action manually.","zh":"可編程裝置節省時間，因為使用者不用手動控制每個動作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a machine can follow preset instructions.","zh":"當機器能跟隨預設指令時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"recognise its surroundings","meaning":"識別周圍環境","examples":[{"en":"Asimo can recognise its surroundings.","zh":"Asimo 可以識別周圍環境。"},{"en":"Recognise its surroundings means sense and understand the area, people, and objects around it.","zh":"recognise its surroundings 指感知並理解周圍的地方、人和物件。"},{"en":"A delivery robot must recognise its surroundings before crossing a busy office lobby.","zh":"送遞機械人在穿過繁忙辦公室大堂前，必須識別周圍環境。"},{"en":"Recognising surroundings helps robots avoid accidents and respond correctly.","zh":"識別周圍環境幫助機械人避免意外並正確回應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when machines understand nearby conditions.","zh":"當機器理解附近情況時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"complete the following sentences","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the following sentences with words from the text.","zh":"考生用文本中的詞語完成以下句子。"},{"en":"Complete the following sentences means fill the gaps so the sentences become finished and correct.","zh":"complete the following sentences 指填補空格，使句子完整且正確。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete the following sentences by copying exact words from the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過從文章抄出準確詞語來完成以下句子。"},{"en":"This task checks whether students understand meaning and follow word limits.","zh":"這個任務檢查學生是否理解意思並遵守字數限制。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in sentence-completion exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於句子填空考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should use no more than three words.","zh":"每個答案應使用不多於三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案必須包含三個詞或更少。"},{"en":"If the answer is “battery power,” it follows the rule because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “battery power”，它符合規則，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Students may lose marks if they write four words, even when the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，學生若寫四個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reading questions have strict word limits.","zh":"當閱讀題有嚴格字數限制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"for each gap","meaning":"每個空格","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose words from the text for each gap.","zh":"考生為每個空格從文本中選擇詞語。"},{"en":"For each gap means for every blank space that needs an answer.","zh":"for each gap 指對每個需要答案的空白位置而言。"},{"en":"Students should check grammar for each gap before writing the final answer.","zh":"學生在寫最後答案前，應為每個空格檢查文法。"},{"en":"Each gap may need a different word form, so copying carelessly can cause mistakes.","zh":"每個空格可能需要不同詞形，所以粗心抄寫會造成錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in gap-fill exercises.","zh":"這個短語適用於填空練習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"help you find a star","meaning":"幫助你找星星","examples":[{"en":"The SkyScout uses GPS and a celestial database to help you find a star.","zh":"SkyScout 使用 GPS 和天體資料庫來幫助你找星星。"},{"en":"Help you find a star means guide you to the correct position of a star in the sky.","zh":"help you find a star 指引導你找到天空中某顆星的正確位置。"},{"en":"A simple astronomy app can help you find a star by showing where to point your phone.","zh":"簡單天文應用程式可以透過顯示手機應指向哪裏，幫助你找星星。"},{"en":"Guidance is useful because many stars look similar to beginners.","zh":"指引很有用，因為對初學者來說，許多星星看起來相似。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when technology assists skywatching.","zh":"當科技協助觀星時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"battery power","meaning":"電池電力","examples":[{"en":"The Seiko Spectrum does not need battery power to retain the image.","zh":"Seiko Spectrum 不需要電池電力來保留影像。"},{"en":"Battery power is the electricity supplied by batteries.","zh":"battery power 指由電池供應的電力。"},{"en":"A torch needs battery power to produce light during a blackout.","zh":"停電時，電筒需要電池電力來發光。"},{"en":"Using less battery power helps portable devices last longer.","zh":"使用較少電池電力幫助可攜式裝置使用更久。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing energy use in small devices.","zh":"討論小型裝置的能源使用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"conventional TV","meaning":"傳統電視","examples":[{"en":"HDTV uses more rows of pixels than conventional TV.","zh":"高清電視比傳統電視使用更多行像素。"},{"en":"Conventional TV means ordinary older television technology before high-definition became common.","zh":"conventional TV 指高清變得普遍前的普通舊式電視技術。"},{"en":"Conventional TV may look less sharp on a large modern screen.","zh":"傳統電視在大型現代螢幕上可能看起來不夠銳利。"},{"en":"New formats can make conventional TV seem outdated by comparison.","zh":"新格式可以令傳統電視相比之下顯得過時。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing old and new television technology.","zh":"比較新舊電視科技時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"could be used to","meaning":"可用作……","examples":[{"en":"The Trilobite 2.0 could be used to entertain guests.","zh":"Trilobite 2.0 可用作娛樂客人。"},{"en":"Could be used to means might serve a particular purpose.","zh":"could be used to 指可能用於某一目的。"},{"en":"A tablet could be used to show photos during a family gathering.","zh":"平板電腦可用作在家庭聚會中展示照片。"},{"en":"Objects can have unexpected uses beyond their main function.","zh":"物件除了主要功能外，可能有意想不到的用途。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when suggesting possible uses.","zh":"提出可能用途時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所提供資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements agree with the information given.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與所提供資料一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the information given means match what the text says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指符合文本所說內容。"},{"en":"In a reading test, a statement agrees with the information given only if the passage clearly supports it.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，只有當文章清楚支持某陳述，它才與所提供資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should compare meaning, not just look for the same words.","zh":"學生應比較意思，而不只是尋找相同字眼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語適用於 TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"if the statement agrees with","meaning":"如果陳述與……一致","examples":[{"en":"Write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information.","zh":"如果陳述與資料一致，寫 TRUE。"},{"en":"If the statement agrees with means if the sentence matches what the text says.","zh":"if the statement agrees with 指如果句子符合文本所說內容。"},{"en":"If the statement agrees with the passage, students should choose TRUE rather than guess another answer.","zh":"如果陳述與文章一致，學生應選 TRUE，而不是猜其他答案。"},{"en":"Agreement must be based on clear evidence from the text.","zh":"一致必須根據文本中的清楚證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining TRUE/FALSE instructions.","zh":"解釋 TRUE/FALSE 指示時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"Write FALSE if the statement contradicts the information.","zh":"如果陳述與資料相矛盾，寫 FALSE。"},{"en":"Contradict the information means say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文本所說相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says a watch uses e-paper, a statement saying it uses only LCD contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說手錶使用電子紙，而陳述說它只使用 LCD，就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"A contradiction needs clear evidence of opposition, not just missing information.","zh":"矛盾需要清楚相反證據，而不只是缺少資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語適用於 TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"Write NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果沒有這方面的資料，寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the text does not say enough to prove or disprove the statement.","zh":"no information on this 指文本沒有足夠資料證明或推翻該陳述。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions the product’s colour, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文章從未提及產品顏色，就沒有這方面的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when the text gives no evidence.","zh":"當文本沒有證據，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when deciding whether an answer is NOT GIVEN.","zh":"判斷答案是否 NOT GIVEN 時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be torn easily","meaning":"容易被撕破","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether e-paper can be torn easily.","zh":"這個陳述問電子紙是否容易被撕破。"},{"en":"Be torn easily means be easily ripped or damaged by pulling.","zh":"be torn easily 指很容易因拉扯而被撕裂或損壞。"},{"en":"Thin wrapping paper can be torn easily if a child pulls it too hard.","zh":"如果孩子太用力拉，薄包裝紙很容易被撕破。"},{"en":"If a material can be torn easily, it may not be suitable for daily wearable products.","zh":"如果材料容易被撕破，它可能不適合日常可穿戴產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing material strength.","zh":"討論材料強度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be filmed differently from","meaning":"與……以不同方式拍攝","examples":[{"en":"HDTV programmes are filmed differently from conventional TV programmes.","zh":"高清電視節目與傳統電視節目以不同方式拍攝。"},{"en":"Be filmed differently from means be recorded using a different method or format.","zh":"be filmed differently from 指使用不同方法或格式拍攝。"},{"en":"A documentary may be filmed differently from a drama because it uses real locations and interviews.","zh":"紀錄片可能與劇情片以不同方式拍攝，因為它使用真實地點和訪問。"},{"en":"Different filming methods can change image quality, mood, and viewer experience.","zh":"不同拍攝方法可以改變影像質素、氣氛和觀眾體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing production techniques.","zh":"比較製作技巧時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"look just like","meaning":"看起來就像……","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether the Trilobite 2.0 looks just like the original design.","zh":"這個陳述問 Trilobite 2.0 是否看起來就像原有設計。"},{"en":"Look just like means have almost exactly the same appearance as something else.","zh":"look just like 指外觀幾乎與另一事物完全相同。"},{"en":"A new school uniform may look just like the old one except for a different badge.","zh":"新校服可能看起來就像舊校服，只是校章不同。"},{"en":"When two products look just like each other, people may not notice internal improvements.","zh":"當兩件產品看起來幾乎一樣，人們可能注意不到內部改良。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing appearance.","zh":"比較外觀時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"original design","meaning":"原有設計","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to the original design of the Trilobite.","zh":"這個陳述提到 Trilobite 的原有設計。"},{"en":"Original design means the first planned or produced form of a product.","zh":"original design 指產品最初被規劃或製作出的形式。"},{"en":"A chair’s original design may be changed after users complain it is uncomfortable.","zh":"如果使用者投訴椅子不舒服，椅子的原有設計可能會被改變。"},{"en":"Later versions often improve on the original design through testing and feedback.","zh":"後來版本常透過測試和回饋改良原有設計。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing first and updated versions.","zh":"比較最初和更新版本時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be available for export","meaning":"可供出口","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Asimo is available for export.","zh":"題目問 Asimo 是否可供出口。"},{"en":"Be available for export means can be sold or sent to other countries.","zh":"be available for export 指可以出售或運送到其他國家。"},{"en":"A local food product may become available for export after it passes safety tests.","zh":"本地食品通過安全測試後，可能可供出口。"},{"en":"Export availability can help a product reach more customers and markets.","zh":"可供出口可以幫助產品接觸更多顧客和市場。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing international sales.","zh":"討論國際銷售時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 65 - Rise of the Robots.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 66":[{"front":"a fun day for","meaning":"對……來說是愉快的一天","examples":[{"en":"Sunday has become a fun day for many modern Brits.","zh":"星期日對許多現代英國人來說已成為愉快的一天。"},{"en":"A fun day for someone is a day when that person can relax, enjoy activities, and feel happy.","zh":"「a fun day for」某人，是指那個人可以放鬆、享受活動並感到快樂的一天。"},{"en":"The school picnic was a fun day for students because they played games and ate together.","zh":"學校野餐對學生來說是愉快的一天，因為他們玩遊戲並一起吃東西。"},{"en":"If shops, parks, and restaurants are open, Sunday can become a fun day for families.","zh":"如果商店、公園和餐廳都開放，星期日可以成為家庭的愉快一天。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on enjoyment, not work or duty.","zh":"這個短語集中於享受，而不是工作或責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"modern Brits","meaning":"現代英國人","examples":[{"en":"The passage compares the Sunday habits of modern Brits with those of people in 1961.","zh":"文章比較現代英國人與1961年人們的星期日習慣。"},{"en":"Modern Brits means British people living in the present or recent period.","zh":"「modern Brits」意思是生活在現代或近代的英國人。"},{"en":"Modern Brits may spend Sunday shopping, eating out, or relaxing with family.","zh":"現代英國人可能在星期日購物、外出用餐或與家人放鬆。"},{"en":"If society changes, modern Brits may use weekends very differently from earlier generations.","zh":"如果社會改變，現代英國人使用週末的方式可能與上一代很不同。"},{"en":"The phrase describes present-day British people, not ancient or historical Britons.","zh":"這個短語描述現今英國人，而不是古代或歷史上的英國人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in a new study","meaning":"在一項新研究中","examples":[{"en":"In a new study, sociologists examined how British Sundays have changed.","zh":"在一項新研究中，社會學家研究英國星期日如何改變。"},{"en":"In a new study means according to recent research or investigation.","zh":"「in a new study」意思是根據近期研究或調查。"},{"en":"In a new study, doctors found that sleep quality affects concentration in teenagers.","zh":"在一項新研究中，醫生發現睡眠質素會影響青少年的專注力。"},{"en":"If new data is collected, researchers can compare old habits with modern behaviour.","zh":"如果收集新數據，研究人員就能把舊習慣與現代行為作比較。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces findings from recent research.","zh":"這個短語引出近期研究的發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sociologists","meaning":"社會學家","examples":[{"en":"Essex University sociologists studied how people spent Sundays.","zh":"埃塞克斯大學的社會學家研究人們如何度過星期日。"},{"en":"Sociologists are researchers who study society, social habits, groups, and human relationships.","zh":"「sociologists」是研究社會、社會習慣、群體和人際關係的學者。"},{"en":"Sociologists may study how teenagers use social media after school.","zh":"社會學家可能研究青少年放學後如何使用社交媒體。"},{"en":"If daily routines change, sociologists can examine what this says about society.","zh":"如果日常規律改變，社會學家可以研究這反映出甚麼社會現象。"},{"en":"The word refers to experts who study social life.","zh":"這個詞指研究社會生活的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dissect the typical British Sunday","meaning":"剖析典型英式星期日","examples":[{"en":"The researchers dissected the typical British Sunday.","zh":"研究人員剖析了典型英式星期日。"},{"en":"To dissect the typical British Sunday means to examine its parts carefully, such as meals, shopping, housework, and leisure.","zh":"「dissect the typical British Sunday」意思是仔細分析其不同部分，例如用餐、購物、家務和休閒。"},{"en":"A teacher may dissect a student’s essay by looking at its introduction, examples, grammar, and conclusion.","zh":"老師可能透過查看引言、例子、文法和結論來剖析學生文章。"},{"en":"If researchers dissect a routine, they can see which parts have changed over time.","zh":"如果研究人員剖析一種日常習慣，他們就能看出哪些部分隨時間改變。"},{"en":"The phrase means analysing something in detail.","zh":"這個短語意思是詳細分析某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get up later","meaning":"較遲起床","examples":[{"en":"Modern Brits get up later on Sundays than people did 40 years ago.","zh":"現代英國人在星期日比40年前的人較遲起床。"},{"en":"To get up later means to leave bed at a later time than usual or than before.","zh":"「get up later」意思是比平時或比以前更遲離開床。"},{"en":"Students often get up later during holidays because they do not need to go to school early.","zh":"學生在假期常較遲起床，因為他們不用早起上學。"},{"en":"If people no longer rush to do chores, they may get up later on Sundays.","zh":"如果人們不再急着做家務，他們可能在星期日較遲起床。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change in morning routine.","zh":"這個短語描述早晨日常習慣的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"do fewer chores","meaning":"做較少家務","examples":[{"en":"People now do fewer chores on Sundays than they used to.","zh":"現在人們在星期日做的家務比以前少。"},{"en":"To do fewer chores means to spend less time doing household tasks such as cleaning, washing, and tidying.","zh":"「do fewer chores」意思是花較少時間做清潔、洗衣和收拾等家務。"},{"en":"A family may do fewer chores on holiday and spend more time sightseeing.","zh":"一家人度假時可能做較少家務，花更多時間觀光。"},{"en":"If housework is spread across the week, people may do fewer chores on Sunday.","zh":"如果家務分散在一星期不同日子，人們星期日可能做較少家務。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a reduction in routine domestic work.","zh":"這個短語顯示日常家務工作減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be far more likely to","meaning":"更有可能……","examples":[{"en":"People are far more likely to go shopping on Sundays now.","zh":"現在人們更有可能在星期日去購物。"},{"en":"To be far more likely to do something means to have a much higher chance of doing it.","zh":"「be far more likely to」做某事，意思是做該事的機會大得多。"},{"en":"Students are far more likely to read if the books match their interests.","zh":"如果書本符合學生興趣，他們更有可能閱讀。"},{"en":"If shops open on Sundays, families are far more likely to go out together.","zh":"如果商店星期日營業，家庭更有可能一起外出。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a strong increase in possibility.","zh":"這個短語強調可能性大幅增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be out shopping","meaning":"外出購物","examples":[{"en":"Modern Brits are more likely to be out shopping on Sundays.","zh":"現代英國人更可能在星期日外出購物。"},{"en":"To be out shopping means to be away from home buying or looking for things in shops.","zh":"「be out shopping」意思是離開家，在商店購買或尋找物品。"},{"en":"Many families are out shopping before Christmas because they need gifts and food.","zh":"聖誕節前，許多家庭會外出購物，因為他們需要禮物和食物。"},{"en":"If shopping centres open all weekend, people may spend more of Sunday outside the home.","zh":"如果商場整個週末營業，人們可能把更多星期日時間花在家外。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shopping as an activity outside the house.","zh":"這個短語描述購物作為外出活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"enjoy ourselves","meaning":"消遣娛樂；玩得開心","examples":[{"en":"People are more likely to be enjoying themselves than doing chores.","zh":"人們更可能在消遣娛樂，而不是做家務。"},{"en":"To enjoy ourselves means to have a good time and feel relaxed or happy.","zh":"「enjoy ourselves」意思是玩得開心並感到放鬆或快樂。"},{"en":"After exams, students enjoy themselves by eating together and watching a film.","zh":"考試後，學生一起吃飯和看電影來放鬆娛樂。"},{"en":"If Sunday becomes less focused on housework, people have more time to enjoy themselves.","zh":"如果星期日較少集中於家務，人們就有更多時間玩得開心。"},{"en":"The phrase is about pleasure and relaxation.","zh":"這個短語關乎愉快和放鬆。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cook Sunday lunch","meaning":"煮星期日午餐","examples":[{"en":"People are less likely to spend Sunday morning cooking Sunday lunch.","zh":"人們較少可能花星期日早上煮星期日午餐。"},{"en":"To cook Sunday lunch means to prepare the main meal traditionally eaten on Sunday.","zh":"「cook Sunday lunch」意思是準備傳統上在星期日吃的主餐。"},{"en":"A family may cook Sunday lunch at home if grandparents are visiting.","zh":"如果祖父母來探訪，一家人可能在家煮星期日午餐。"},{"en":"If people eat out instead, they spend less time cooking Sunday lunch.","zh":"如果人們改為外出用餐，他們就較少時間煮星期日午餐。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a traditional household activity.","zh":"這個短語描述一種傳統家庭活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"academics","meaning":"大學學者","examples":[{"en":"Academics at the university asked people to keep diaries.","zh":"大學學者要求人們寫日記。"},{"en":"Academics are university teachers or researchers who study and write about a subject.","zh":"「academics」是研究某學科並撰寫相關內容的大學教師或研究人員。"},{"en":"Academics may interview families to understand changes in work and home life.","zh":"大學學者可能訪問家庭，以了解工作和家庭生活的變化。"},{"en":"If academics collect careful evidence, they can explain social change more clearly.","zh":"如果大學學者收集仔細證據，他們就能更清楚解釋社會變遷。"},{"en":"The word refers to people working in higher education and research.","zh":"這個詞指在高等教育和研究界工作的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the Institute of Social and Economic Research","meaning":"社會及經濟研究所","examples":[{"en":"The Institute of Social and Economic Research carried out the study.","zh":"社會及經濟研究所進行了這項研究。"},{"en":"The Institute of Social and Economic Research is a research organisation that studies society and the economy.","zh":"「the Institute of Social and Economic Research」是研究社會和經濟的研究機構。"},{"en":"A research institute may collect survey data about families, work, health, and income.","zh":"研究所可能收集有關家庭、工作、健康和收入的調查數據。"},{"en":"If such an institute studies Sundays, it can connect leisure habits with wider social change.","zh":"如果這類研究所研究星期日，它可以把休閒習慣與更廣泛社會變遷連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase names the organisation responsible for the research.","zh":"這個短語指出負責研究的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"keep a detailed diary of","meaning":"詳細記錄……","examples":[{"en":"Participants kept a detailed diary of how they spent Sundays.","zh":"參加者詳細記錄他們如何度過星期日。"},{"en":"To keep a detailed diary of something means to record carefully what happens, often with times and descriptions.","zh":"「keep a detailed diary of」某事，意思是仔細記錄發生的事情，通常包括時間和描述。"},{"en":"A patient may keep a detailed diary of headaches to help a doctor find the cause.","zh":"病人可能詳細記錄頭痛情況，以幫助醫生找出原因。"},{"en":"If people record their day carefully, researchers can compare real habits rather than guesses.","zh":"如果人們仔細記錄一天，研究人員就能比較真實習慣，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful written tracking.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細書面追蹤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"spend Sundays","meaning":"度過星期日","examples":[{"en":"The diaries showed how people spent Sundays in 2001.","zh":"日記顯示人們在2001年如何度過星期日。"},{"en":"To spend Sundays means to use Sunday time in particular activities or routines.","zh":"「spend Sundays」意思是以特定活動或日常安排使用星期日時間。"},{"en":"Some families spend Sundays visiting relatives, eating out, and preparing for Monday.","zh":"有些家庭度過星期日的方式是探親、外出用餐和準備星期一。"},{"en":"If shops and leisure places are open, people may spend Sundays outside the home.","zh":"如果商店和休閒場所開放，人們可能在家外度過星期日。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how Sunday time is used.","zh":"這個短語描述星期日時間如何被使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"compare the results with","meaning":"將結果與……比較","examples":[{"en":"The researchers compared the results with diaries from 1961.","zh":"研究人員將結果與1961年的日記比較。"},{"en":"To compare the results with something means to look at two sets of information and notice similarities or differences.","zh":"「compare the results with」某物，意思是查看兩組資料並注意相似和不同之處。"},{"en":"A teacher may compare this year’s test results with last year’s results.","zh":"老師可能將今年測驗結果與去年結果比較。"},{"en":"If researchers compare old and new diaries, they can see how habits have changed.","zh":"如果研究人員比較新舊日記，他們就能看出習慣如何改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using comparison to understand change.","zh":"這個短語描述透過比較理解變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a treasure trove of information","meaning":"大量珍貴資料","examples":[{"en":"The old diaries were a treasure trove of information.","zh":"這些舊日記是一批大量珍貴資料。"},{"en":"A treasure trove of information is a rich collection of useful and valuable details.","zh":"「a treasure trove of information」是有用而珍貴細節的豐富收藏。"},{"en":"An old family photo album can be a treasure trove of information about past generations.","zh":"一本舊家庭相簿可以是關於上一代的大量珍貴資料。"},{"en":"If researchers find many detailed diaries, they gain rare evidence about daily life.","zh":"如果研究人員找到許多詳細日記，他們就得到關於日常生活的罕有證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes information that is unusually rich and valuable.","zh":"這個短語描述異常豐富且有價值的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be uncovered","meaning":"被發現；被翻出","examples":[{"en":"The diaries were uncovered in the basement of the BBC.","zh":"這些日記在 BBC 的地庫被發現。"},{"en":"To be uncovered means to be found or revealed after being hidden, forgotten, or unknown.","zh":"「be uncovered」意思是在被隱藏、遺忘或不為人知之後被發現或揭露。"},{"en":"Old school records may be uncovered during a library renovation.","zh":"學校圖書館翻新時，舊校務紀錄可能被翻出。"},{"en":"If forgotten documents are uncovered, they may change what researchers know.","zh":"如果被遺忘的文件被發現，它們可能改變研究人員所知道的事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes discovery after something has been hidden.","zh":"這個短語描述隱藏後的發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"egg boxes and a tea chest","meaning":"雞蛋盒和茶葉箱","examples":[{"en":"The diaries were found in two egg boxes and a tea chest.","zh":"這些日記在兩個雞蛋盒和一個茶葉箱中被發現。"},{"en":"Egg boxes and a tea chest are simple containers that can be used to store old papers or objects.","zh":"「egg boxes and a tea chest」是可用來存放舊文件或物件的簡單容器。"},{"en":"A family might keep old letters in shoe boxes, biscuit tins, or a wooden chest.","zh":"家庭可能把舊信件放在鞋盒、餅乾罐或木箱中。"},{"en":"If important records are stored in ordinary boxes, they may be forgotten for years.","zh":"如果重要紀錄被放在普通盒子裡，它們可能被遺忘多年。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a concrete image of where the diaries were found.","zh":"這個短語具體描繪日記被發現的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in the basement of","meaning":"在……的地庫","examples":[{"en":"The diaries were found in the basement of the BBC.","zh":"這些日記在 BBC 的地庫被發現。"},{"en":"In the basement of a building means in the lowest floor, usually below ground level.","zh":"「in the basement of」某建築物，意思是在最低層，通常低於地面。"},{"en":"A school may store old desks in the basement of the main building.","zh":"學校可能把舊書桌存放在主樓的地庫。"},{"en":"If boxes are left in a basement for decades, people may forget what is inside them.","zh":"如果箱子在地庫放了幾十年，人們可能忘記裡面有甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a location below the main floors.","zh":"這個短語描述位於主要樓層下方的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the contrast between","meaning":"……之間的對比","examples":[{"en":"The contrast between the two periods was very clear.","zh":"兩個時期之間的對比非常清楚。"},{"en":"The contrast between two things is the clear difference between them.","zh":"「the contrast between」兩件事，是它們之間清楚的差異。"},{"en":"The contrast between a quiet village and a busy city helps students understand different lifestyles.","zh":"安靜村莊與繁忙城市之間的對比幫助學生理解不同生活方式。"},{"en":"If old diaries and new diaries show different habits, the contrast becomes easy to see.","zh":"如果舊日記和新日記顯示不同習慣，對比就容易看見。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces difference through comparison.","zh":"這個短語透過比較引入差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"could not be more striking","meaning":"再明顯不過","examples":[{"en":"The contrast between the two periods could not be more striking.","zh":"兩個時期之間的對比再明顯不過。"},{"en":"Could not be more striking means extremely clear, obvious, or impressive.","zh":"「could not be more striking」意思是極其清楚、明顯或令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"The difference between a messy first draft and a polished final essay could not be more striking.","zh":"混亂初稿與潤飾後終稿之間的差異再明顯不過。"},{"en":"If habits change completely, the comparison becomes impossible to miss.","zh":"如果習慣完全改變，比較結果就難以忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly emphasises how noticeable something is.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調某事有多明顯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a flurry of activity","meaning":"一陣忙碌；忙個不停","examples":[{"en":"Sunday mornings were once a flurry of activity.","zh":"星期日早上以前是一陣忙碌。"},{"en":"A flurry of activity is a short period full of busy actions and movement.","zh":"「a flurry of activity」是一段充滿忙碌行動和活動的短時間。"},{"en":"Before guests arrive, a home may become a flurry of activity as everyone cleans and cooks.","zh":"客人到達前，家中可能變成一陣忙碌，人人都清潔和煮食。"},{"en":"If chores must be finished before lunch, the morning becomes crowded with tasks.","zh":"如果家務必須在午餐前完成，早上就會被任務塞滿。"},{"en":"The phrase describes energetic busyness.","zh":"這個短語描述充滿活力的忙碌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"catch up on","meaning":"補做；趕做","examples":[{"en":"People used Sunday mornings to catch up on their weekly chores.","zh":"人們以前用星期日早上補做每週家務。"},{"en":"To catch up on something means to do work that has been delayed or left unfinished.","zh":"「catch up on」某事，意思是做被延誤或未完成的工作。"},{"en":"A student may catch up on homework after being sick for two days.","zh":"學生病了兩天後，可能要補做功課。"},{"en":"If people are busy during the week, they may use Sunday to finish delayed tasks.","zh":"如果人們平日很忙，他們可能用星期日完成拖延了的任務。"},{"en":"The phrase means making up for lost time.","zh":"這個短語意思是追回失去的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"weekly chores","meaning":"每週家務","examples":[{"en":"Many families caught up on their weekly chores on Sunday mornings.","zh":"許多家庭在星期日早上補做每週家務。"},{"en":"Weekly chores are household tasks that need to be done every week.","zh":"「weekly chores」是每星期都需要完成的家庭工作。"},{"en":"Washing clothes, cleaning the bathroom, and changing bedsheets can be weekly chores.","zh":"洗衣服、清潔浴室和更換床單都可以是每週家務。"},{"en":"If weekly chores are left until Sunday, the morning can become stressful.","zh":"如果每週家務都留到星期日，早上可能變得有壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to regular housework.","zh":"這個短語指固定家務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cook up a storm","meaning":"大展廚藝；忙着煮很多食物","examples":[{"en":"Many women cooked up a storm in the kitchen on Sundays.","zh":"許多女性星期日在廚房大展廚藝。"},{"en":"To cook up a storm means to cook a lot of food with great energy and skill.","zh":"「cook up a storm」意思是充滿活力和技巧地煮很多食物。"},{"en":"Before Lunar New Year dinner, grandparents may cook up a storm for the whole family.","zh":"農曆新年晚飯前，祖父母可能為全家大展廚藝。"},{"en":"If guests are coming, someone may spend the whole morning cooking up a storm.","zh":"如果有客人來，有人可能花整個早上忙着煮很多食物。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and suggests busy, enthusiastic cooking.","zh":"這個短語較口語，暗示忙碌而熱情地煮食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"allow themselves any leisure","meaning":"讓自己有任何閒暇","examples":[{"en":"Women rarely allowed themselves any leisure until the afternoon.","zh":"女性很少在下午之前讓自己有任何閒暇。"},{"en":"To allow themselves any leisure means to give themselves time to rest or enjoy free activities.","zh":"「allow themselves any leisure」意思是給自己時間休息或享受自由活動。"},{"en":"A parent may not allow herself any leisure until the children’s homework and dinner are finished.","zh":"家長可能要到孩子功課和晚飯完成後，才讓自己有任何閒暇。"},{"en":"If housework fills the morning, personal free time is delayed.","zh":"如果家務填滿早上，個人自由時間就被推遲。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that rest was treated as something to be earned after work.","zh":"這個短語暗示休息被視為工作後才配得到的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"more than a fifth of","meaning":"超過五分之一的……","examples":[{"en":"More than a fifth of adults were sitting at a table by 2 p.m.","zh":"下午二時前，超過五分之一的成人已坐在餐桌旁。"},{"en":"More than a fifth of a group means more than 20 percent of that group.","zh":"「more than a fifth of」一個群體，意思是超過該群體的百分之二十。"},{"en":"More than a fifth of the class forgot to bring their textbooks.","zh":"班上超過五分之一學生忘記帶課本。"},{"en":"If more than a fifth of adults ate at the same time, Sunday lunch was a shared routine.","zh":"如果超過五分之一成人在同一時間用餐，星期日午餐就是共同習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate proportion.","zh":"這個短語給出大約比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"tuck into","meaning":"大口享用；津津有味地吃","examples":[{"en":"Many people were tucking into a roast by 2 p.m.","zh":"下午二時前，許多人已在津津有味地吃烤肉餐。"},{"en":"To tuck into food means to start eating it with enjoyment and appetite.","zh":"「tuck into」食物，意思是帶着享受和食慾開始吃。"},{"en":"After a long hike, students tucked into sandwiches and fruit.","zh":"長途遠足後，學生大口享用三文治和水果。"},{"en":"If a meal smells delicious, people may quickly sit down and tuck into it.","zh":"如果一頓飯聞起來很香，人們可能很快坐下來大口享用。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and suggests eating heartily.","zh":"這個短語較口語，暗示吃得痛快。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a roast with all the trimmings","meaning":"配齊傳統配菜的烤肉餐","examples":[{"en":"Families often ate a roast with all the trimmings on Sundays.","zh":"家庭星期日常吃配齊傳統配菜的烤肉餐。"},{"en":"A roast with all the trimmings is a roast meal served with traditional side dishes and extras.","zh":"「a roast with all the trimmings」是配有傳統配菜和附加食物的烤肉餐。"},{"en":"At Christmas, a family may serve turkey with all the trimmings, such as potatoes and vegetables.","zh":"聖誕節時，家庭可能供應火雞和全部配菜，例如薯仔和蔬菜。"},{"en":"If Sunday lunch was formal, families often prepared a full roast rather than a simple snack.","zh":"如果星期日午餐很正式，家庭常準備完整烤肉餐，而不是簡單小食。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a complete traditional meal.","zh":"這個短語暗示一頓完整的傳統餐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rush to the table","meaning":"趕去餐桌","examples":[{"en":"There was another rush to the table between 5 p.m. and 6 p.m.","zh":"下午五時至六時之間，又有另一波人趕去餐桌。"},{"en":"To rush to the table means to hurry to sit down and eat.","zh":"「rush to the table」意思是趕快坐下吃飯。"},{"en":"Children may rush to the table when they smell their favourite dinner.","zh":"兒童聞到最喜歡的晚餐時，可能趕去餐桌。"},{"en":"If a meal is served at a fixed time, everyone may hurry to gather together.","zh":"如果一餐在固定時間供應，人人可能趕快聚在一起。"},{"en":"The phrase describes quick movement toward a meal.","zh":"這個短語描述快速走向用餐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"high tea","meaning":"傍晚茶餐","examples":[{"en":"Families often returned to the table for high tea.","zh":"家庭常回到餐桌前吃傍晚茶餐。"},{"en":"High tea is a light evening meal or substantial tea-time meal, traditionally eaten in Britain.","zh":"「high tea」是在英國傳統中傍晚吃的輕便晚餐或較豐富茶點餐。"},{"en":"A family might have sandwiches, cakes, and tea for high tea after an afternoon walk.","zh":"一家人下午散步後，可能吃三文治、蛋糕和茶作為傍晚茶餐。"},{"en":"If people ate lunch early, high tea gave them another meal before evening.","zh":"如果人們午餐吃得早，傍晚茶餐就在晚上前提供另一餐。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a British eating tradition.","zh":"這個短語指英國飲食傳統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the arrival of","meaning":"……的出現","examples":[{"en":"The arrival of brunch changed traditional Sunday eating habits.","zh":"早午餐的出現改變了傳統星期日飲食習慣。"},{"en":"The arrival of something means the appearance or introduction of something new.","zh":"「the arrival of」某物，意思是某種新事物的出現或引入。"},{"en":"The arrival of online shopping changed how many families buy groceries.","zh":"網上購物的出現改變了許多家庭購買雜貨的方式。"},{"en":"If a new habit arrives, older routines may disappear or become less common.","zh":"如果新習慣出現，舊日常可能消失或變得較少見。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the beginning of a new influence.","zh":"這個短語突出新影響的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"brunch","meaning":"早午餐","examples":[{"en":"Brunch helped change traditional Sunday mealtimes.","zh":"早午餐幫助改變傳統星期日用餐時間。"},{"en":"Brunch is a meal eaten between breakfast and lunch, often later in the morning.","zh":"「brunch」是在早餐和午餐之間吃的一餐，通常在上午較晚時間。"},{"en":"Friends may meet for brunch at 11 a.m. instead of eating breakfast at home.","zh":"朋友可能在上午十一時一起吃早午餐，而不是在家吃早餐。"},{"en":"If people get up later on Sunday, brunch fits their relaxed schedule.","zh":"如果人們星期日較遲起床，早午餐就適合他們放鬆的時間表。"},{"en":"The word combines breakfast and lunch in both timing and meaning.","zh":"這個詞在時間和意思上結合 breakfast 和 lunch。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"gastropub","meaning":"美食酒吧；美食酒館","examples":[{"en":"Some people now go to a gastropub for Sunday lunch.","zh":"有些人現在去美食酒吧吃星期日午餐。"},{"en":"A gastropub is a pub that serves high-quality or interesting food as well as drinks.","zh":"「gastropub」是除了飲品外，也供應高質素或有特色食物的酒吧。"},{"en":"A family may choose a gastropub when they want a relaxed meal without cooking at home.","zh":"家庭想輕鬆用餐又不想在家煮飯時，可能選擇美食酒吧。"},{"en":"If gastropubs become popular, traditional home-cooked Sunday lunch may become less common.","zh":"如果美食酒吧變得流行，傳統在家煮的星期日午餐可能變少。"},{"en":"The word combines pub culture with restaurant-style food.","zh":"這個詞結合酒吧文化和餐廳式食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"all-you-can-eat Sunday buffet","meaning":"星期日任食自助餐","examples":[{"en":"The all-you-can-eat Sunday buffet has changed Sunday dining habits.","zh":"星期日任食自助餐改變了星期日飲食習慣。"},{"en":"An all-you-can-eat Sunday buffet is a Sunday meal where customers pay once and can eat many dishes.","zh":"「all-you-can-eat Sunday buffet」是在星期日一次付費後可吃多種菜式的一餐。"},{"en":"Families may choose an all-you-can-eat buffet because children and adults can pick different foods.","zh":"家庭可能選擇任食自助餐，因為兒童和成人可以選不同食物。"},{"en":"If buffets become popular, fixed traditional mealtimes may become less important.","zh":"如果自助餐變得流行，固定傳統用餐時間可能變得較不重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a flexible eating-out option.","zh":"這個短語描述靈活的外出用餐選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"local curry house","meaning":"本區咖喱餐廳","examples":[{"en":"Some people eat at the local curry house on Sundays.","zh":"有些人星期日在本區咖喱餐廳用餐。"},{"en":"A local curry house is a nearby restaurant that serves curry and related dishes.","zh":"「local curry house」是附近供應咖喱和相關菜式的餐廳。"},{"en":"A family may go to the local curry house when nobody wants to cook dinner.","zh":"當沒有人想煮晚飯時，一家人可能去本區咖喱餐廳。"},{"en":"If people eat different cuisines on Sunday, traditional British meals become less dominant.","zh":"如果人們星期日吃不同菜系，傳統英式餐就不再那麼主導。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an example of casual local dining.","zh":"這個短語提供日常本地外食例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"traditional mealtimes","meaning":"傳統用餐時間","examples":[{"en":"Traditional mealtimes have largely disappeared.","zh":"傳統用餐時間大致上已消失。"},{"en":"Traditional mealtimes are the fixed times when people used to eat regular meals.","zh":"「traditional mealtimes」是人們過去吃固定餐的固定時間。"},{"en":"A family may still keep traditional mealtimes by eating lunch at noon and dinner at six.","zh":"家庭如果中午吃午餐、六時吃晚餐，就仍保留傳統用餐時間。"},{"en":"If people snack and eat out at different times, traditional mealtimes become weaker.","zh":"如果人們在不同時間吃零食和外食，傳統用餐時間就會變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to old patterns of eating by the clock.","zh":"這個短語指按時吃飯的舊模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"largely disappeared","meaning":"大致上消失","examples":[{"en":"Traditional Sunday mealtimes have largely disappeared.","zh":"傳統星期日用餐時間大致上已消失。"},{"en":"To have largely disappeared means to have mostly gone, though not completely.","zh":"「largely disappeared」意思是大部分已消失，但不是完全沒有。"},{"en":"Handwritten letters have largely disappeared from everyday communication.","zh":"手寫信在日常溝通中大致上已消失。"},{"en":"If people now eat whenever they like, fixed Sunday meals may mostly vanish.","zh":"如果人們現在想甚麼時候吃就甚麼時候吃，固定星期日用餐可能大多消失。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests major decline, not total absence.","zh":"這個短語暗示大幅減少，而非完全不存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"graze throughout the day","meaning":"整天零零碎碎地吃","examples":[{"en":"Today, many people graze throughout the day instead of eating at fixed times.","zh":"今天許多人整天零零碎碎地吃，而不是在固定時間用餐。"},{"en":"To graze throughout the day means to eat small amounts of food again and again rather than having formal meals.","zh":"「graze throughout the day」意思是整天一再吃少量食物，而不是吃正式餐。"},{"en":"A student may graze throughout the day on fruit, biscuits, and sandwiches while studying.","zh":"學生溫習時可能整天吃水果、餅乾和三文治。"},{"en":"If people graze all day, lunch and dinner may no longer feel like fixed events.","zh":"如果人們整天零碎地吃，午餐和晚餐可能不再像固定事件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes casual, repeated snacking.","zh":"這個短語描述隨意而反覆吃小食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"free days a week","meaning":"每週空閒日","examples":[{"en":"Most people only have two free days a week.","zh":"大多數人每週只有兩天空閒日。"},{"en":"Free days a week means days each week when people are not required to work or attend regular duties.","zh":"「free days a week」意思是每星期不用工作或履行固定責任的日子。"},{"en":"A worker with two free days a week may use them for family, rest, and errands.","zh":"每週有兩天空閒日的工人，可能用它們陪家人、休息和辦雜事。"},{"en":"If free days are limited, people try to use them as fully as possible.","zh":"如果空閒日有限，人們會盡量充分利用它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weekly time away from work.","zh":"這個短語描述每週離開工作的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have nothing to do but","meaning":"除了……之外無事可做","examples":[{"en":"People do not want to have nothing to do but watch TV.","zh":"人們不想除了看電視之外無事可做。"},{"en":"To have nothing to do but something means to have no other activity or choice except that thing.","zh":"「have nothing to do but」某事，意思是除了該事之外沒有其他活動或選擇。"},{"en":"If it rains all weekend, children may feel they have nothing to do but stay indoors.","zh":"如果整個週末下雨，兒童可能覺得除了留在室內之外無事可做。"},{"en":"When people want a richer Sunday, they look for shopping, food, travel, or social activities.","zh":"當人們想要更豐富的星期日，他們會尋找購物、食物、出行或社交活動。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests boredom or limited options.","zh":"這個短語暗示沉悶或選擇有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"leapfrog Saturday","meaning":"超越星期六","examples":[{"en":"Sunday has leapfrogged Saturday in the fun stakes.","zh":"星期日在娛樂程度方面已超越星期六。"},{"en":"To leapfrog Saturday means to move ahead of Saturday in importance, popularity, or enjoyment.","zh":"「leapfrog Saturday」意思是在重要性、受歡迎程度或愉快程度上超越星期六。"},{"en":"A small café may leapfrog larger restaurants if customers prefer its food and service.","zh":"如果顧客更喜歡小咖啡店的食物和服務，它可能超越大型餐廳。"},{"en":"If people are tired on Saturday but active on Sunday, Sunday can become the more enjoyable day.","zh":"如果人們星期六疲倦但星期日活躍，星期日就可以成為更愉快的一天。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one thing overtaking another.","zh":"這個短語描述一件事超越另一件事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the fun stakes","meaning":"在娛樂程度方面","examples":[{"en":"Sunday has become more important in the fun stakes.","zh":"星期日在娛樂程度方面已變得更重要。"},{"en":"In the fun stakes means when comparing how enjoyable different things are.","zh":"「in the fun stakes」意思是在比較不同事物有多好玩時。"},{"en":"In the fun stakes, a class picnic may beat a normal lesson easily.","zh":"在娛樂程度方面，班級野餐可能輕易勝過普通課堂。"},{"en":"If Sunday offers shopping, brunch, and outings, it may score higher than Saturday for enjoyment.","zh":"如果星期日有購物、早午餐和外出活動，它在娛樂方面可能比星期六更高分。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and means in terms of fun.","zh":"這個短語較口語，意思是就樂趣而言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"recover from the week","meaning":"從一週的疲累中恢復過來","examples":[{"en":"On Saturdays, many people are still recovering from the week.","zh":"在星期六，許多人仍在從一週疲累中恢復過來。"},{"en":"To recover from the week means to rest after the tiredness and stress of the working week.","zh":"「recover from the week」意思是在一星期工作帶來的疲倦和壓力後休息恢復。"},{"en":"A teacher may recover from the week by sleeping late and avoiding emails on Saturday.","zh":"老師可能透過星期六睡晚一點和避開電郵來恢復一週疲勞。"},{"en":"If people use Saturday to recover, Sunday becomes the day for leisure activities.","zh":"如果人們用星期六恢復精力，星期日就成為休閒活動的一天。"},{"en":"The phrase describes regaining energy after busy weekdays.","zh":"這個短語描述在忙碌平日後重新獲得能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the last bastion of the weekend","meaning":"週末的最後堡壘","examples":[{"en":"Sunday is described as the last bastion of the weekend.","zh":"星期日被描述為週末的最後堡壘。"},{"en":"The last bastion of the weekend means the final remaining part of the weekend that people try to protect and enjoy.","zh":"「the last bastion of the weekend」意思是人們努力保護和享受的週末最後部分。"},{"en":"For a busy worker, Sunday evening may feel like the last bastion of personal time.","zh":"對忙碌工人而言，星期日晚上可能感覺像個人時間的最後堡壘。"},{"en":"If Monday is coming soon, people may try harder to enjoy the last part of the weekend.","zh":"如果星期一快將來臨，人們可能更努力享受週末最後部分。"},{"en":"The phrase presents Sunday as the final defence against the working week.","zh":"這個短語把星期日呈現為抵抗工作週的最後防線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get as much as possible out of","meaning":"盡量充分利用……","examples":[{"en":"People want to get as much as possible out of Sunday.","zh":"人們想盡量充分利用星期日。"},{"en":"To get as much as possible out of something means to use it fully and gain the greatest benefit or enjoyment from it.","zh":"「get as much as possible out of」某事，意思是充分使用它並獲得最大好處或樂趣。"},{"en":"Students try to get as much as possible out of a revision class by asking questions.","zh":"學生透過提問，盡量充分利用溫習課。"},{"en":"If people only have two free days, they may pack Sunday with enjoyable activities.","zh":"如果人們只有兩天空閒日，他們可能把星期日排滿愉快活動。"},{"en":"The phrase means making full use of something.","zh":"這個短語意思是充分利用某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"go back to work","meaning":"回去上班","examples":[{"en":"People want to enjoy Sunday before they have to go back to work.","zh":"人們想在必須回去上班前享受星期日。"},{"en":"To go back to work means to return to one’s job after a break, holiday, or weekend.","zh":"「go back to work」意思是在休息、假期或週末後返回工作崗位。"},{"en":"Many people feel slightly tense on Sunday night because they must go back to work on Monday.","zh":"許多人星期日晚上會有點緊張，因為星期一必須回去上班。"},{"en":"If a weekend feels too short, people may try to make Sunday more enjoyable.","zh":"如果週末感覺太短，人們可能嘗試令星期日更愉快。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the end of free time and the return of duty.","zh":"這個短語標示自由時間結束和責任回歸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"according to researchers","meaning":"根據研究人員所說","examples":[{"en":"According to researchers, shopping has changed British Sundays.","zh":"根據研究人員所說，購物改變了英國星期日。"},{"en":"According to researchers means based on what researchers say or have found.","zh":"「according to researchers」意思是根據研究人員所說或所發現。"},{"en":"According to researchers, regular exercise can improve mood and sleep.","zh":"根據研究人員所說，規律運動可以改善心情和睡眠。"},{"en":"If a claim is based on research, it sounds more evidence-based than personal opinion.","zh":"如果主張基於研究，它聽起來比個人意見更有證據。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces information from experts.","zh":"這個短語引入專家資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"trail around B&Q","meaning":"在 B&Q 到處逛","examples":[{"en":"The ability to trail around B&Q has changed Sunday habits.","zh":"能夠在 B&Q 到處逛改變了星期日習慣。"},{"en":"To trail around B&Q means to walk around the B&Q home-improvement store, often browsing slowly.","zh":"「trail around B&Q」意思是在 B&Q 家居裝修店內慢慢閒逛或瀏覽。"},{"en":"A family may trail around a furniture shop looking for shelves and paint.","zh":"家庭可能在家具店到處逛，尋找架子和油漆。"},{"en":"If large stores open on Sundays, shopping can become a leisure activity rather than a weekday chore.","zh":"如果大型商店星期日開放，購物可以成為休閒活動，而不是平日雜務。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests casual wandering around a shop.","zh":"這個短語暗示在商店中隨意閒逛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make a dramatic difference to","meaning":"對……造成巨大改變","examples":[{"en":"Shopping has made a dramatic difference to people’s Sundays.","zh":"購物對人們的星期日造成巨大改變。"},{"en":"To make a dramatic difference to something means to change it greatly and noticeably.","zh":"「make a dramatic difference to」某事，意思是對它造成巨大而明顯的改變。"},{"en":"A new bus route can make a dramatic difference to students who live far from school.","zh":"新巴士路線可以對住得離學校遠的學生造成巨大改變。"},{"en":"If shops open on Sundays, people’s routines may change from chores to leisure.","zh":"如果商店星期日開放，人們的日常可能由家務轉向休閒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large and obvious impact.","zh":"這個短語描述巨大而明顯的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"spend an average of","meaning":"平均花費……","examples":[{"en":"Adults spent an average of 50 minutes shopping on Sundays in 2001.","zh":"2001年，成年人星期日平均花50分鐘購物。"},{"en":"To spend an average of a certain time means the typical amount of time spent is that number.","zh":"「spend an average of」某段時間，意思是典型花費時間為該數字。"},{"en":"Students may spend an average of two hours on homework each evening.","zh":"學生每晚可能平均花兩小時做功課。"},{"en":"If the average shopping time rises, shopping has become a more important activity.","zh":"如果平均購物時間上升，購物就成為更重要活動。"},{"en":"The phrase reports a typical measured amount.","zh":"這個短語報告典型量度數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"shopping used to be","meaning":"購物以往是……","examples":[{"en":"Shopping used to be a gender-segregated activity.","zh":"購物以往是按性別分隔的活動。"},{"en":"Shopping used to be means shopping was once a certain kind of activity, but may not be so now.","zh":"「shopping used to be」意思是購物過去曾是某種活動，但現在可能不是。"},{"en":"Homework used to be written on paper, but many students now submit it online.","zh":"功課以往寫在紙上，但現在許多學生在網上提交。"},{"en":"If a habit used to be different, comparison can show social change.","zh":"如果一個習慣以往不同，比較就能顯示社會變化。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a past pattern.","zh":"這個短語引入過去模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"gender-segregated activity","meaning":"按性別分隔的活動","examples":[{"en":"Shopping used to be a gender-segregated activity.","zh":"購物以往是按性別分隔的活動。"},{"en":"A gender-segregated activity is an activity done mainly by one gender or separated by gender roles.","zh":"「gender-segregated activity」是主要由某一性別進行，或按性別角色分開的活動。"},{"en":"In the past, cooking was often treated as a gender-segregated activity in many homes.","zh":"在過去，煮食在許多家庭常被視為按性別分隔的活動。"},{"en":"If men and women now shop equally, the activity has become less gender-segregated.","zh":"如果男女現在同樣購物，該活動就較少按性別分隔。"},{"en":"The phrase describes separation based on gender.","zh":"這個短語描述基於性別的分隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take place during the week","meaning":"在平日進行","examples":[{"en":"Shopping usually took place during the week in 1961.","zh":"1961年，購物通常在平日進行。"},{"en":"To take place during the week means to happen on weekdays rather than at the weekend.","zh":"「take place during the week」意思是在平日而非週末發生。"},{"en":"Most school meetings take place during the week because teachers are already on campus.","zh":"大多數學校會議在平日進行，因為老師已在校內。"},{"en":"If shopping happens during the week, Sunday remains free for meals, chores, or rest.","zh":"如果購物在平日進行，星期日就保留給用餐、家務或休息。"},{"en":"The phrase explains when an activity normally happens.","zh":"這個短語解釋活動通常何時發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"while the husband was at work","meaning":"在丈夫上班時","examples":[{"en":"Women often shopped while the husband was at work.","zh":"女性常在丈夫上班時購物。"},{"en":"While the husband was at work means during the time when the husband was away doing his job.","zh":"「while the husband was at work」意思是在丈夫外出工作期間。"},{"en":"A parent may clean the house while the children are at school.","zh":"家長可能在孩子上學時清潔家居。"},{"en":"If shopping was done while men worked, it reflected older gender roles.","zh":"如果購物是在男性上班時完成，這反映較舊的性別角色。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the time and social context of an activity.","zh":"這個短語提供活動的時間和社會背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as much a male activity as a female one","meaning":"男性和女性同樣會做的活動","examples":[{"en":"Shopping is now as much a male activity as a female one.","zh":"購物現在是男性和女性同樣會做的活動。"},{"en":"As much a male activity as a female one means men and women now take part in it to a similar degree.","zh":"「as much a male activity as a female one」意思是男性和女性現在以相近程度參與它。"},{"en":"Cooking is now as much a male activity as a female one in some modern families.","zh":"在一些現代家庭中，煮食現在是男性和女性同樣會做的活動。"},{"en":"If both genders share an activity, older gender divisions become weaker.","zh":"如果兩性共同參與一項活動，舊有性別分工就會變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises equality of participation.","zh":"這個短語強調參與上的平等。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"these days","meaning":"現今；如今","examples":[{"en":"People are more likely to shop or relax on Sunday mornings these days.","zh":"現今，人們更可能在星期日早上購物或放鬆。"},{"en":"These days means nowadays or in the present period.","zh":"「these days」意思是現今、如今。"},{"en":"These days, many students use phones to check homework instructions.","zh":"現今，許多學生用手機查看功課指示。"},{"en":"If people behave differently these days, older routines may no longer apply.","zh":"如果人們現今行為不同，舊日常可能不再適用。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts the present with the past.","zh":"這個短語把現在與過去作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"scrub the floor","meaning":"擦地板","examples":[{"en":"People are less likely to spend Sunday morning scrubbing the floor.","zh":"人們較少可能花星期日早上擦地板。"},{"en":"To scrub the floor means to clean the floor hard with a brush, cloth, or cleaning tool.","zh":"「scrub the floor」意思是用刷子、布或清潔工具用力清潔地板。"},{"en":"After a muddy sports day, cleaners may scrub the floor of the school hall.","zh":"泥濘運動日後，清潔工可能要擦學校禮堂地板。"},{"en":"If people do fewer chores on Sunday, heavy cleaning tasks may move to other days.","zh":"如果人們星期日做較少家務，繁重清潔工作可能移到其他日子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical housework.","zh":"這個短語描述體力家務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put up shelves","meaning":"安裝架子","examples":[{"en":"People are less likely to spend Sunday morning putting up shelves.","zh":"人們較少可能花星期日早上安裝架子。"},{"en":"To put up shelves means to fix shelves onto a wall or build them for use.","zh":"「put up shelves」意思是把架子固定在牆上或組裝出來使用。"},{"en":"A father may put up shelves in a child’s room to hold books and toys.","zh":"父親可能在孩子房間安裝架子，用來放書和玩具。"},{"en":"If DIY work is no longer crowded into Sunday morning, people may have more leisure time.","zh":"如果 DIY 工作不再擠在星期日早上，人們可能有更多休閒時間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a practical home-improvement task.","zh":"這個短語描述實用家居改善工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"stay in bed longer","meaning":"較遲起床；賴床較久","examples":[{"en":"Men now stay in bed longer on Sunday mornings.","zh":"男性現在星期日早上賴床較久。"},{"en":"To stay in bed longer means to remain in bed for more time before getting up.","zh":"「stay in bed longer」意思是起床前在床上待更久。"},{"en":"After a tiring week, a worker may stay in bed longer on Saturday morning.","zh":"經過疲累一週後，工人星期六早上可能較遲起床。"},{"en":"If fewer chores must be done early, people can stay in bed longer.","zh":"如果較少家務必須早早完成，人們就可以賴床較久。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a slower, more relaxed morning.","zh":"這個短語暗示較慢、更放鬆的早晨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as previously","meaning":"像以往那樣","examples":[{"en":"Men no longer get up as previously to work around the house.","zh":"男性不再像以往那樣早起做家居工作。"},{"en":"As previously means in the same way as before.","zh":"「as previously」意思是像以前一樣。"},{"en":"A school may no longer give paper notices as previously because parents now use an app.","zh":"學校可能不再像以往那樣派紙本通告，因為家長現在使用應用程式。"},{"en":"If routines change, people no longer behave exactly as they did in the past.","zh":"如果日常改變，人們就不再完全像過去那樣行事。"},{"en":"The phrase compares present behaviour with earlier behaviour.","zh":"這個短語比較現在行為與以往行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"work around the house","meaning":"做家居工作","examples":[{"en":"Men used to get up early to work around the house.","zh":"男性以前會早起做家居工作。"},{"en":"To work around the house means to do practical tasks at home, such as repairing, cleaning, or tidying.","zh":"「work around the house」意思是在家做維修、清潔或整理等實際工作。"},{"en":"A family may spend Saturday morning working around the house before guests arrive.","zh":"客人到訪前，一家人可能花星期六早上做家居工作。"},{"en":"If household tasks are spread through the day, people no longer need to rush them in the morning.","zh":"如果家務分散於全日，人們就不必早上趕着完成。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to unpaid practical home work.","zh":"這個短語指家中無薪實際工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pursue outside leisure activities","meaning":"參與外出休閒活動","examples":[{"en":"People now get up to shop or pursue outside leisure activities.","zh":"人們現在起床是為了購物或參與外出休閒活動。"},{"en":"To pursue outside leisure activities means to spend free time doing enjoyable things away from home.","zh":"「pursue outside leisure activities」意思是把自由時間用於家外的愉快活動。"},{"en":"Families may pursue outside leisure activities such as hiking, visiting markets, or eating out.","zh":"家庭可能參與遠足、逛市集或外出用餐等外出休閒活動。"},{"en":"If Sundays offer more public entertainment, people leave home more often.","zh":"如果星期日有更多公共娛樂，人們就更常離家。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active leisure beyond the house.","zh":"這個短語描述家外的主動休閒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"unpaid work around the house","meaning":"家中的無薪工作","examples":[{"en":"Men do about the same amount of unpaid work around the house.","zh":"男性做的家中無薪工作量大約和以前一樣。"},{"en":"Unpaid work around the house means household tasks done at home without wages.","zh":"「unpaid work around the house」意思是在家中做而沒有工資的家務。"},{"en":"Cooking, cleaning, repairing, and gardening are unpaid work around the house.","zh":"煮食、清潔、維修和園藝都是家中的無薪工作。"},{"en":"If unpaid work is shared more evenly, family routines may become fairer.","zh":"如果無薪工作更平均地分擔，家庭日常可能更公平。"},{"en":"The phrase describes domestic labour that is not paid employment.","zh":"這個短語描述不是受薪工作的家庭勞動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as they used to","meaning":"像以前那樣","examples":[{"en":"Men do about the same amount of housework as they used to.","zh":"男性做的家務量大約像以前那樣。"},{"en":"As they used to means in the same way or to the same degree as before.","zh":"「as they used to」意思是以與以前相同的方式或程度。"},{"en":"Some grandparents still read printed newspapers as they used to.","zh":"有些祖父母仍像以前那樣閱讀紙本報章。"},{"en":"If a habit has not changed much, people may still do it as they used to.","zh":"如果習慣沒有太大改變，人們可能仍像以前那樣做。"},{"en":"The phrase compares present behaviour with past behaviour.","zh":"這個短語比較現在行為與過去行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be spread throughout","meaning":"分散在……各時段","examples":[{"en":"Men’s unpaid work is spread throughout the whole day.","zh":"男性的無薪家務分散在整天各時段。"},{"en":"To be spread throughout something means to be distributed across all parts of a period or place.","zh":"「be spread throughout」某事，意思是分布於一段時間或地方的各部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may spread revision throughout the week instead of doing it all on Friday.","zh":"老師可能把溫習分散在整個星期，而不是全部放在星期五。"},{"en":"If chores are spread throughout the day, the morning feels less busy.","zh":"如果家務分散在全日，早上就感覺較不忙。"},{"en":"The phrase describes distribution rather than concentration.","zh":"這個短語描述分散，而不是集中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"crammed into the morning","meaning":"擠在早上完成","examples":[{"en":"Housework is no longer crammed into the morning.","zh":"家務不再擠在早上完成。"},{"en":"To be crammed into the morning means to be packed tightly into the morning with little space or time.","zh":"「be crammed into the morning」意思是被密集塞進早上，幾乎沒有空間或時間。"},{"en":"If a school puts three tests before lunch, too much work is crammed into the morning.","zh":"如果學校在午餐前安排三個測驗，就有太多工作擠在早上。"},{"en":"When chores are spread out, Sunday morning becomes less rushed.","zh":"當家務被分散，星期日早上就不再那麼趕。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests too many tasks squeezed into one period.","zh":"這個短語暗示太多任務被擠進同一段時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"do considerably less than","meaning":"做得明顯較少","examples":[{"en":"Women do considerably less housework on Sundays than before.","zh":"女性星期日做的家務比以前明顯較少。"},{"en":"To do considerably less than before means to do much less than in the past.","zh":"「do considerably less than before」意思是比過去做得少很多。"},{"en":"Students may do considerably less handwriting now because they type assignments online.","zh":"學生現在可能明顯較少手寫，因為他們在網上打字提交功課。"},{"en":"If Sunday routines become more relaxed, the amount of housework may fall sharply.","zh":"如果星期日日常變得更放鬆，家務量可能大幅下降。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a clear and noticeable decrease.","zh":"這個短語顯示清楚而明顯的減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pretty much different species","meaning":"幾乎像兩種不同物種","examples":[{"en":"Men and women were pretty much different species in 1961.","zh":"1961年，男性和女性幾乎像兩種不同物種。"},{"en":"Pretty much different species means two groups behaved so differently that they seemed almost completely unlike each other.","zh":"「pretty much different species」意思是兩個群體行為差異大得幾乎完全不像彼此。"},{"en":"In one class, morning students and night students may seem like different species because their routines are so different.","zh":"在一班中，早起學生和夜貓學生可能像不同物種，因為生活規律太不同。"},{"en":"If men spent Sunday outside while women worked at home, their lives looked sharply divided.","zh":"如果男性星期日外出而女性在家工作，他們的生活看起來就明顯分開。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and exaggerated for strong contrast.","zh":"這個短語較口語，並帶誇張語氣，用於強烈對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as far as something is concerned","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"Men and women were very different as far as Sunday habits were concerned.","zh":"就星期日習慣而言，男性和女性非常不同。"},{"en":"As far as something is concerned means when talking about that particular subject.","zh":"「as far as something is concerned」意思是當談及某個特定主題時。"},{"en":"As far as homework is concerned, clear instructions matter more than long explanations.","zh":"就功課而言，清楚指示比冗長解釋更重要。"},{"en":"If we focus only on Sunday habits, the gender difference in 1961 was very clear.","zh":"如果我們只集中於星期日習慣，1961年的性別差異非常清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase limits discussion to one topic.","zh":"這個短語把討論限制在一個主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"far more likely to be out of the house","meaning":"更有可能外出","examples":[{"en":"Men were far more likely to be out of the house before lunch.","zh":"男性午餐前更有可能外出。"},{"en":"To be far more likely to be out of the house means to have a much higher chance of being away from home.","zh":"「far more likely to be out of the house」意思是離家外出的機會高得多。"},{"en":"Teenagers are far more likely to be out of the house during school holidays if friends live nearby.","zh":"如果朋友住在附近，青少年在學校假期更有可能外出。"},{"en":"If men went to pubs or played football, they spent less Sunday morning at home.","zh":"如果男性去酒吧或踢足球，他們星期日早上在家的時間就較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong difference in location and routine.","zh":"這個短語描述位置和日常上的強烈差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at the pub","meaning":"在酒吧","examples":[{"en":"Men were often at the pub before lunch.","zh":"男性午餐前常在酒吧。"},{"en":"At the pub means inside or around a pub, usually drinking, talking, or meeting friends.","zh":"「at the pub」意思是在酒吧內或附近，通常飲酒、聊天或見朋友。"},{"en":"After work, colleagues may meet at the pub for a quick drink.","zh":"下班後，同事可能在酒吧見面喝一杯。"},{"en":"If men spent Sunday morning at the pub, women might have been left with housework at home.","zh":"如果男性星期日早上在酒吧，女性可能被留在家中做家務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a social leisure location.","zh":"這個短語描述一個社交休閒場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"play football","meaning":"踢足球","examples":[{"en":"Men were more likely to be playing football before lunch.","zh":"男性午餐前更可能在踢足球。"},{"en":"To play football means to take part in a football game or match.","zh":"「play football」意思是參與足球遊戲或比賽。"},{"en":"Children often play football in the playground using bags as goalposts.","zh":"兒童常在操場用書包作龍門踢足球。"},{"en":"If men played football on Sunday mornings, their leisure began earlier than many women’s.","zh":"如果男性星期日早上踢足球，他們的休閒時間比許多女性更早開始。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common physical leisure activity.","zh":"這個短語描述常見體能休閒活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"leisure happened only in the afternoon","meaning":"閒暇只在下午才出現","examples":[{"en":"For many women, leisure happened only in the afternoon.","zh":"對許多女性而言，閒暇只在下午才出現。"},{"en":"Leisure happened only in the afternoon means free time was available only after morning duties were finished.","zh":"「leisure happened only in the afternoon」意思是只有在早上責任完成後才有自由時間。"},{"en":"A parent may find that rest happens only at night after children are asleep.","zh":"家長可能發現休息只在孩子睡着後的晚上才出現。"},{"en":"If chores filled the morning, women could not relax until later in the day.","zh":"如果家務填滿早上，女性直到當天較後時間才可以放鬆。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how free time was delayed by responsibilities.","zh":"這個短語顯示自由時間如何被責任推遲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the shapes of men’s and women’s Sundays","meaning":"男女度過星期日的模式","examples":[{"en":"The shapes of men’s and women’s Sundays were much more similar by 2001.","zh":"到2001年，男女度過星期日的模式相似得多。"},{"en":"The shapes of men’s and women’s Sundays means the patterns or structures of how men and women spent Sundays.","zh":"「the shapes of men’s and women’s Sundays」意思是男性和女性如何度過星期日的模式或結構。"},{"en":"A researcher may compare the shape of a student’s day by looking at study, rest, travel, and meals.","zh":"研究人員可能透過查看學習、休息、交通和用餐，來比較學生一天的模式。"},{"en":"If both genders shop, relax, and do chores at similar times, their Sunday patterns become alike.","zh":"如果兩性在相近時間購物、放鬆和做家務，他們的星期日模式就變得相似。"},{"en":"The phrase uses “shape” to mean overall routine.","zh":"這個短語用 “shape” 表示整體日常模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be much more similar","meaning":"相似得多","examples":[{"en":"By 2001, men’s and women’s Sundays were much more similar.","zh":"到2001年，男性和女性的星期日相似得多。"},{"en":"To be much more similar means to have many more shared features than before.","zh":"「be much more similar」意思是比以前有更多共同特徵。"},{"en":"Two schools become much more similar when they use the same timetable and textbooks.","zh":"當兩間學校使用相同時間表和課本，它們就變得相似得多。"},{"en":"If men and women now share shopping and leisure, their routines become less divided.","zh":"如果男女現在共同參與購物和休閒，他們的日常就不再那麼分隔。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a clear reduction in difference.","zh":"這個短語描述差異明顯減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be all about","meaning":"重點在於……","examples":[{"en":"Sunday is all about holding on to the weekend for Jonathan Atchison.","zh":"對 Jonathan Atchison 而言，星期日的重點在於把握週末剩下的時間。"},{"en":"To be all about something means the main purpose or feeling of it is that thing.","zh":"「be all about」某事，意思是某事的主要目的或感覺就是它。"},{"en":"For many students, summer holiday is all about rest, friends, and freedom.","zh":"對許多學生而言，暑假的重點在於休息、朋友和自由。"},{"en":"If Sunday is all about avoiding Monday, people may try to enjoy every remaining hour.","zh":"如果星期日的重點在於避開星期一，人們可能嘗試享受每個剩下的小時。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the central meaning of something.","zh":"這個短語指出某事的核心意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hold on to the weekend","meaning":"把握週末剩下的時間","examples":[{"en":"He sees Sunday as a way of holding on to the weekend.","zh":"他把星期日視為把握週末剩下時間的一種方式。"},{"en":"To hold on to the weekend means to try to keep the relaxed feeling of the weekend for as long as possible.","zh":"「hold on to the weekend」意思是盡量長久保持週末的放鬆感覺。"},{"en":"A worker may hold on to the weekend by having a slow Sunday dinner with friends.","zh":"工人可能透過與朋友慢慢吃星期日晚餐來把握週末剩下的時間。"},{"en":"If Monday feels stressful, people may want Sunday to last longer.","zh":"如果星期一感覺有壓力，人們可能希望星期日更長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes resisting the return of the working week.","zh":"這個短語描述抗拒工作週回歸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stave off Monday","meaning":"暫時避開星期一的來臨","examples":[{"en":"He uses Sunday to stave off Monday.","zh":"他利用星期日暫時避開星期一的來臨。"},{"en":"To stave off Monday means to delay thinking about Monday or the return to work.","zh":"「stave off Monday」意思是延遲想到星期一或回到工作。"},{"en":"A student may watch a film on Sunday night to stave off thoughts of school.","zh":"學生可能在星期日晚上看電影，暫時避開上學的想法。"},{"en":"If people dislike Monday, they may fill Sunday with pleasant activities.","zh":"如果人們不喜歡星期一，他們可能用愉快活動填滿星期日。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests temporarily keeping an unpleasant moment away.","zh":"這個短語暗示暫時把不愉快時刻推開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an ideal Sunday","meaning":"理想的星期日","examples":[{"en":"An ideal Sunday would involve getting up and having a nice lunch.","zh":"理想的星期日會包括起床和吃一頓美好的午餐。"},{"en":"An ideal Sunday is the Sunday someone would most like to have.","zh":"「an ideal Sunday」是某人最想擁有的星期日。"},{"en":"For a busy parent, an ideal Sunday may include sleep, a quiet walk, and no chores.","zh":"對忙碌父母而言，理想的星期日可能包括睡眠、安靜散步和沒有家務。"},{"en":"If people describe an ideal Sunday, they reveal what they value in free time.","zh":"如果人們描述理想的星期日，他們就揭示自己在自由時間中重視甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a perfect or preferred Sunday.","zh":"這個短語描述完美或偏好的星期日。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"involve doing","meaning":"包括做……","examples":[{"en":"An ideal Sunday would involve having a nice lunch.","zh":"理想的星期日會包括吃一頓美好的午餐。"},{"en":"To involve doing something means to include that activity as part of the situation.","zh":"「involve doing」某事，意思是把該活動包括在情況之中。"},{"en":"A good study plan may involve reviewing notes, practising questions, and resting properly.","zh":"好的溫習計劃可能包括重溫筆記、練習題目和好好休息。"},{"en":"If a Sunday involves eating out, people do not need to cook at home.","zh":"如果星期日包括外出用餐，人們就不需要在家煮飯。"},{"en":"The phrase shows what is included in an activity or plan.","zh":"這個短語顯示活動或計劃包含甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"more often","meaning":"更常；多數時候","examples":[{"en":"Sometimes they cook, but more often they go out.","zh":"有時他們會煮飯，但多數時候他們會外出。"},{"en":"More often means on more occasions or more frequently.","zh":"「more often」意思是在更多情況下或更頻繁地。"},{"en":"Students may sometimes study alone, but more often they revise with friends before exams.","zh":"學生有時獨自溫習，但考試前更常與朋友一起溫習。"},{"en":"If people go out more often than they cook, eating habits change.","zh":"如果人們外出用餐比煮飯更常見，飲食習慣就會改變。"},{"en":"The phrase compares frequency.","zh":"這個短語比較頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"go out to get","meaning":"外出吃；外出買","examples":[{"en":"He often goes out to get a roast at a gastropub.","zh":"他常外出去美食酒吧吃烤肉餐。"},{"en":"To go out to get something means to leave home in order to buy, eat, or collect it.","zh":"「go out to get」某物，意思是離家去購買、吃或取回它。"},{"en":"A family may go out to get pizza when nobody wants to cook.","zh":"如果沒有人想煮飯，一家人可能外出買薄餅。"},{"en":"If people can easily go out to get meals, home cooking may become less necessary.","zh":"如果人們能輕易外出吃飯，在家煮飯可能變得較不必要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes leaving home for a specific purchase or meal.","zh":"這個短語描述為了特定購買或用餐而離家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bangers and mash","meaning":"香腸薯蓉","examples":[{"en":"He sometimes has bangers and mash at a gastropub.","zh":"他有時在美食酒吧吃香腸薯蓉。"},{"en":"Bangers and mash is a British dish made of sausages and mashed potatoes.","zh":"「bangers and mash」是一道由香腸和薯蓉組成的英式菜式。"},{"en":"A pub may serve bangers and mash with gravy and peas.","zh":"酒吧可能供應配肉汁和青豆的香腸薯蓉。"},{"en":"If someone wants comfort food, bangers and mash may feel warm and familiar.","zh":"如果某人想吃comfort food，香腸薯蓉可能令人感到溫暖和熟悉。"},{"en":"The phrase names a traditional British meal.","zh":"這個短語指出一道傳統英式餐點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"there is nothing better than","meaning":"沒有比……更好的事","examples":[{"en":"There is nothing better than sitting outside on a nice day.","zh":"在好天氣坐在外面，沒有比這更好的事。"},{"en":"There is nothing better than something means that thing feels extremely enjoyable or satisfying.","zh":"「there is nothing better than」某事，意思是該事感覺極其愉快或滿足。"},{"en":"After a hard exam, there is nothing better than a quiet meal with friends.","zh":"艱難考試後，沒有比與朋友安靜吃飯更好的事。"},{"en":"If the weather is good, sitting outside can make Sunday feel especially relaxing.","zh":"如果天氣好，坐在外面可以令星期日感覺特別放鬆。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly praises an experience.","zh":"這個短語強烈稱讚一種經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"beer garden","meaning":"啤酒花園；酒吧露天座位","examples":[{"en":"He enjoys sitting outside in the beer garden.","zh":"他喜歡坐在啤酒花園的戶外位置。"},{"en":"A beer garden is an outdoor area of a pub where people can sit, drink, and eat.","zh":"「beer garden」是酒吧的戶外區域，人們可以坐下、飲酒和用餐。"},{"en":"Friends may meet in a beer garden on a sunny afternoon.","zh":"朋友可能在陽光明媚的下午於啤酒花園見面。"},{"en":"If a pub has a pleasant beer garden, Sunday lunch can feel more relaxed.","zh":"如果酒吧有舒適的露天座位，星期日午餐會感覺更放鬆。"},{"en":"The phrase names an outdoor social space linked to pubs.","zh":"這個短語指出與酒吧相關的戶外社交空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Sunday papers","meaning":"星期日報章","examples":[{"en":"He likes reading the Sunday papers with a drink.","zh":"他喜歡一邊飲東西，一邊閱讀星期日報章。"},{"en":"Sunday papers are newspapers published for Sunday, often with extra sections and longer features.","zh":"「Sunday papers」是星期日出版的報章，通常有額外版面和較長專題。"},{"en":"Some people read the Sunday papers slowly over breakfast or brunch.","zh":"有些人會在早餐或早午餐時慢慢閱讀星期日報章。"},{"en":"If Sunday is relaxed, people may have time for long articles and reviews.","zh":"如果星期日很放鬆，人們可能有時間閱讀長文章和評論。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a traditional Sunday reading habit.","zh":"這個短語指傳統星期日閱讀習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tabloid","meaning":"小報","examples":[{"en":"He reads one tabloid and one broadsheet.","zh":"他讀一份小報和一份大報。"},{"en":"A tabloid is a newspaper that often uses shorter stories, bold headlines, and popular topics.","zh":"「tabloid」是常使用較短報道、醒目標題和大眾話題的報章。"},{"en":"A commuter may read a tabloid quickly on the bus because the articles are short.","zh":"通勤者可能在巴士上快速閱讀小報，因為文章較短。"},{"en":"If readers want celebrity news or dramatic headlines, they may choose a tabloid.","zh":"如果讀者想看名人新聞或誇張標題，可能選擇小報。"},{"en":"The word contrasts with broadsheet newspapers, which are usually more serious.","zh":"這個詞與通常較嚴肅的大報形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"broadsheet","meaning":"大報；嚴肅報章","examples":[{"en":"He reads one tabloid and one broadsheet.","zh":"他讀一份小報和一份大報。"},{"en":"A broadsheet is a serious newspaper that usually contains longer articles and detailed analysis.","zh":"「broadsheet」是通常包含較長文章和詳細分析的嚴肅報章。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a broadsheet article to discuss politics or economics in class.","zh":"老師可能用大報文章在課堂討論政治或經濟。"},{"en":"If someone wants deeper reporting, they may choose a broadsheet rather than a tabloid.","zh":"如果某人想看更深入報道，可能選擇大報而不是小報。"},{"en":"The word refers to a more serious newspaper style.","zh":"這個詞指較嚴肅的報章風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a chance to","meaning":"做……的機會","examples":[{"en":"Sunday is often a chance to visit other parts of London.","zh":"星期日常是遊覽倫敦其他地區的機會。"},{"en":"A chance to do something is an opportunity to do it.","zh":"「a chance to」做某事，是做該事的機會。"},{"en":"A school trip is a chance to learn outside the classroom.","zh":"學校旅行是走出課室學習的機會。"},{"en":"If people are free on Sunday, they may use it as a chance to explore new places.","zh":"如果人們星期日有空，他們可能把它用作探索新地方的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights opportunity.","zh":"這個短語突出機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"other parts of London","meaning":"倫敦其他地區","examples":[{"en":"Sunday gives him a chance to visit other parts of London.","zh":"星期日給他機會遊覽倫敦其他地區。"},{"en":"Other parts of London means areas of London different from the place where someone usually lives or works.","zh":"「other parts of London」意思是與某人平時居住或工作的地方不同的倫敦地區。"},{"en":"A student living in north London may visit other parts of London to see museums and markets.","zh":"住在北倫敦的學生可能去倫敦其他地區參觀博物館和市集。"},{"en":"If people have free time, they may explore neighbourhoods they do not normally visit.","zh":"如果人們有空，他們可能探索平時不會去的社區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes different districts within the same city.","zh":"這個短語描述同一城市內不同地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as long as","meaning":"只要……","examples":[{"en":"He visits other parts of London as long as they are not too far.","zh":"只要那些地方不太遠，他就會遊覽倫敦其他地區。"},{"en":"As long as means provided that or only if a condition is met.","zh":"「as long as」意思是只要某條件符合。"},{"en":"Students may use phones in class as long as they are doing research.","zh":"只要學生在做資料搜集，他們可以在課堂上使用手機。"},{"en":"If the journey is short enough, he is willing to explore more of the city.","zh":"如果路程夠短，他就願意探索更多城市地區。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a condition.","zh":"這個短語引入條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"go clothes shopping","meaning":"去買衣服","examples":[{"en":"He uses Sundays to go clothes shopping.","zh":"他用星期日去買衣服。"},{"en":"To go clothes shopping means to go out to buy or look for clothes.","zh":"「go clothes shopping」意思是外出購買或尋找衣服。"},{"en":"Friends may go clothes shopping before a graduation dinner.","zh":"朋友可能在畢業晚宴前去買衣服。"},{"en":"If shops are open on Sundays, people can buy clothes during leisure time.","zh":"如果商店星期日營業，人們可以在休閒時間買衣服。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common shopping activity.","zh":"這個短語描述常見購物活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on offer","meaning":"有供應；可選擇的","examples":[{"en":"He enjoys the international foods on offer at Camden Market.","zh":"他喜歡 Camden Market 有供應的國際美食。"},{"en":"On offer means available for people to buy, choose, or use.","zh":"「on offer」意思是可供人購買、選擇或使用。"},{"en":"A school fair may have games, snacks, and handmade gifts on offer.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能有遊戲、小食和手工禮物可選擇。"},{"en":"If many foods are on offer, visitors can try different tastes in one place.","zh":"如果有許多食物供應，遊客可以在同一地方嘗試不同味道。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what is available.","zh":"這個短語描述可供選擇的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hunt for bargains","meaning":"尋找平貨","examples":[{"en":"He enjoys hunting for bargains at Camden Market.","zh":"他喜歡在 Camden Market 尋找平貨。"},{"en":"To hunt for bargains means to look carefully for things sold at a low or good price.","zh":"「hunt for bargains」意思是仔細尋找以低價或好價出售的東西。"},{"en":"Students may hunt for bargains when buying second-hand textbooks.","zh":"學生購買二手教科書時可能尋找平貨。"},{"en":"If prices are high, shoppers may spend more time searching for good deals.","zh":"如果價格高，購物者可能花更多時間尋找優惠。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests active searching for cheap or valuable finds.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動尋找便宜或有價值的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"vintage clothes","meaning":"古着；復古衣服","examples":[{"en":"He likes hunting for bargains and vintage clothes.","zh":"他喜歡尋找平貨和古着。"},{"en":"Vintage clothes are older clothes from a previous period, often valued for style or quality.","zh":"「vintage clothes」是來自較早年代的衣服，常因風格或質素而受重視。"},{"en":"A shopper may buy vintage clothes because they look unique and are not found in modern chain stores.","zh":"購物者可能購買復古衣服，因為它們看起來獨特，現代連鎖店買不到。"},{"en":"If people enjoy old styles, markets selling vintage clothes can become popular.","zh":"如果人們喜歡舊風格，售賣古着的市集可以變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"The phrase describes second-hand or older fashion with character.","zh":"這個短語描述有特色的二手或舊式時裝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"work in communications","meaning":"從事傳訊工作","examples":[{"en":"Jonathan Bentley Atchison works in communications.","zh":"Jonathan Bentley Atchison 從事傳訊工作。"},{"en":"To work in communications means to have a job involving messages, media, public relations, or information sharing.","zh":"「work in communications」意思是從事涉及訊息、媒體、公關或資訊傳遞的工作。"},{"en":"Someone who writes press releases for a company works in communications.","zh":"為公司撰寫新聞稿的人從事傳訊工作。"},{"en":"If a person works in communications, they may spend weekdays writing, planning, and speaking to clients.","zh":"如果某人從事傳訊工作，他平日可能寫作、規劃和與客戶溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broad professional field.","zh":"這個短語描述一個廣泛專業領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make Sunday lunch","meaning":"做星期日午餐","examples":[{"en":"Hazel Hallows is usually at home making Sunday lunch.","zh":"Hazel Hallows 通常在家做星期日午餐。"},{"en":"To make Sunday lunch means to prepare and cook the main meal eaten on Sunday.","zh":"「make Sunday lunch」意思是準備和烹調星期日吃的主餐。"},{"en":"A mother may make Sunday lunch while the children set the table.","zh":"母親可能做星期日午餐，而孩子們擺放餐具。"},{"en":"If the family prefers a home roast, someone must spend time preparing it.","zh":"如果家庭喜歡在家吃烤肉餐，就必須有人花時間準備。"},{"en":"The phrase describes home cooking as part of Sunday routine.","zh":"這個短語描述星期日日常中的家庭煮食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"go out to eat","meaning":"外出用餐","examples":[{"en":"Some of Hazel’s friends go out to eat on Sundays.","zh":"Hazel 的一些朋友星期日外出用餐。"},{"en":"To go out to eat means to leave home and have a meal at a restaurant, café, or pub.","zh":"「go out to eat」意思是離家到餐廳、咖啡店或酒吧吃飯。"},{"en":"A family may go out to eat after a busy week to avoid cooking and washing dishes.","zh":"忙碌一週後，一家人可能外出用餐，以免煮飯和洗碗。"},{"en":"If more restaurants open on Sunday, eating out becomes easier.","zh":"如果更多餐廳星期日營業，外出用餐就更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes restaurant dining instead of home cooking.","zh":"這個短語描述餐廳用餐，而不是在家煮食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"love a roast","meaning":"很喜歡吃烤肉餐","examples":[{"en":"Her husband loves a roast, so they usually eat at home.","zh":"她丈夫很喜歡吃烤肉餐，所以他們通常在家吃。"},{"en":"To love a roast means to really enjoy a roast meal, especially a traditional Sunday roast.","zh":"「love a roast」意思是非常喜歡烤肉餐，尤其傳統星期日烤肉餐。"},{"en":"A grandfather who loves a roast may look forward to potatoes, gravy, and vegetables every Sunday.","zh":"很喜歡烤肉餐的祖父可能每星期日期待薯仔、肉汁和蔬菜。"},{"en":"If someone loves a roast, the family may keep cooking Sunday lunch at home.","zh":"如果某人很喜歡烤肉餐，家庭可能繼續在家做星期日午餐。"},{"en":"The phrase shows strong liking for a traditional meal.","zh":"這個短語顯示對傳統餐點的強烈喜愛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"like every day","meaning":"像平日一樣","examples":[{"en":"Hazel does the washing, like every day.","zh":"Hazel 像平日一樣洗衣服。"},{"en":"Like every day means as usual, in the same way as on other days.","zh":"「like every day」意思是照常，與其他日子一樣。"},{"en":"A student checks messages after breakfast, like every day.","zh":"學生像平日一樣早餐後查看訊息。"},{"en":"If Sunday still includes ordinary chores, it may not feel completely different from weekdays.","zh":"如果星期日仍包括普通家務，它可能不感覺與平日完全不同。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses routine and repetition.","zh":"這個短語強調日常和重複。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take someone to netball","meaning":"帶某人去打籃網球","examples":[{"en":"Hazel takes her daughter to netball.","zh":"Hazel 帶女兒去打籃網球。"},{"en":"To take someone to netball means to bring that person to a netball practice or match.","zh":"「take someone to netball」意思是帶某人去籃網球練習或比賽。"},{"en":"A parent may take a child to football, swimming, or netball on weekends.","zh":"父母可能在週末帶孩子去踢足球、游泳或打籃網球。"},{"en":"If children have sports activities, parents often spend Sunday transporting them.","zh":"如果兒童有運動活動，父母常花星期日接送他們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes parental support for a child’s sport.","zh":"這個短語描述父母對子女運動的支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"watch someone play","meaning":"觀看某人比賽","examples":[{"en":"Hazel watches her daughter play netball.","zh":"Hazel 觀看女兒打籃網球。"},{"en":"To watch someone play means to observe a person taking part in a game or sport.","zh":"「watch someone play」意思是觀看某人參與遊戲或運動。"},{"en":"Parents often watch their children play at school matches.","zh":"父母常在學校比賽中觀看子女比賽。"},{"en":"If parents watch supportively, children may feel encouraged rather than pressured.","zh":"如果父母以支持方式觀看，兒童可能感到受鼓勵而不是受壓。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being a spectator for someone’s activity.","zh":"這個短語描述作為觀眾觀看某人的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"potter around","meaning":"東摸西摸；悠閒地做雜事","examples":[{"en":"Mark potters around at home on Sundays.","zh":"Mark 星期日在家悠閒地做雜事。"},{"en":"To potter around means to do small, light tasks slowly and casually, without rushing.","zh":"「potter around」意思是慢慢地、隨意地做小型輕鬆任務，不趕急。"},{"en":"On a quiet morning, someone may potter around the kitchen making tea and tidying small things.","zh":"在寧靜早上，有人可能在廚房東摸西摸，泡茶和收拾小東西。"},{"en":"If Sunday is relaxed, people may potter around instead of following a strict plan.","zh":"如果星期日很放鬆，人們可能悠閒地做雜事，而不是跟從嚴格計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests gentle, unhurried activity.","zh":"這個短語暗示溫和而不趕急的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tidy the garage","meaning":"收拾車房","examples":[{"en":"Last Sunday, Mark tidied the garage.","zh":"上星期日，Mark 收拾了車房。"},{"en":"To tidy the garage means to organise and clean the space where tools, boxes, or a car may be kept.","zh":"「tidy the garage」意思是整理和清潔存放工具、箱子或汽車的空間。"},{"en":"A family may tidy the garage before moving house.","zh":"一家人搬屋前可能收拾車房。"},{"en":"If old boxes pile up, tidying the garage can take several hours.","zh":"如果舊箱子堆積，收拾車房可能花幾小時。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a practical home chore.","zh":"這個短語描述實際家務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"work six days a week","meaning":"每週工作六天","examples":[{"en":"Mark works six days a week.","zh":"Mark 每週工作六天。"},{"en":"To work six days a week means to have only one day off in a normal week.","zh":"「work six days a week」意思是在正常一星期中只有一天休息。"},{"en":"A shop assistant may work six days a week during a busy sales season.","zh":"銷售旺季期間，店員可能每週工作六天。"},{"en":"If someone works six days a week, Sunday may be especially important for rest.","zh":"如果某人每週工作六天，星期日可能對休息特別重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a heavy weekly work schedule.","zh":"這個短語描述沉重的每週工作時間表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stay at home","meaning":"留在家中","examples":[{"en":"Mark stays at home on Sundays.","zh":"Mark 星期日留在家中。"},{"en":"To stay at home means to remain in one’s house instead of going out.","zh":"「stay at home」意思是留在自己的家，而不是外出。"},{"en":"A family may stay at home during heavy rain and watch films together.","zh":"大雨時，一家人可能留在家中一起看電影。"},{"en":"If someone works all week, staying at home may feel restful.","zh":"如果某人整星期工作，留在家中可能感覺很休息。"},{"en":"The phrase describes choosing home over outside activities.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇家中而非外出活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"every man and his dog","meaning":"人人都；很多人都","examples":[{"en":"Hazel avoids Sunday shopping because every man and his dog is out.","zh":"Hazel 避免星期日購物，因為人人都外出了。"},{"en":"Every man and his dog means a very large number of people, often too many.","zh":"「every man and his dog」意思是非常多人，通常多得有點太多。"},{"en":"During a big sale, every man and his dog seems to be in the shopping centre.","zh":"大減價期間，商場好像人人都在。"},{"en":"If too many people are out shopping, some people avoid the crowds.","zh":"如果外出購物的人太多，有些人會避開人群。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and humorous.","zh":"這個短語較口語，而且帶幽默感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"do it in the week","meaning":"在平日做","examples":[{"en":"Hazel can do her shopping in the week.","zh":"Hazel 可以在平日購物。"},{"en":"To do it in the week means to do an activity on a weekday rather than at the weekend.","zh":"「do it in the week」意思是在平日而非週末做某活動。"},{"en":"A parent may do grocery shopping in the week to avoid weekend crowds.","zh":"家長可能在平日買雜貨，以避開週末人潮。"},{"en":"If someone has time on weekdays, they do not need to shop on Sunday.","zh":"如果某人平日有時間，就不需要星期日購物。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts weekday activity with weekend activity.","zh":"這個短語把平日活動與週末活動作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tend to","meaning":"通常會；傾向於","examples":[{"en":"Hazel tends to watch television and chill out.","zh":"Hazel 通常會看電視和放鬆一下。"},{"en":"To tend to do something means to usually do it or be likely to do it.","zh":"「tend to」做某事，意思是通常會做或很可能做。"},{"en":"Students tend to feel nervous before oral exams.","zh":"學生通常會在口試前感到緊張。"},{"en":"If someone is tired after a long week, they may tend to stay home on Sunday.","zh":"如果某人經過漫長一週後很累，星期日可能傾向留在家中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a usual habit or tendency.","zh":"這個短語描述通常習慣或傾向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"chill out","meaning":"放鬆一下","examples":[{"en":"Hazel tends to watch television and chill out.","zh":"Hazel 通常會看電視和放鬆一下。"},{"en":"To chill out means to relax and stop feeling busy, stressed, or tense.","zh":"「chill out」意思是放鬆，停止感到忙碌、壓力或緊張。"},{"en":"After finishing homework, a student may chill out by listening to music.","zh":"完成功課後，學生可能聽音樂放鬆一下。"},{"en":"If Sunday is used to chill out, it helps people prepare for the new week.","zh":"如果星期日用來放鬆一下，它會幫助人準備新一週。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and means relaxing.","zh":"這個短語較口語，意思是放鬆。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"when summer comes","meaning":"到夏天時","examples":[{"en":"When summer comes, the family goes to barbecues.","zh":"到夏天時，這家人會去燒烤聚會。"},{"en":"When summer comes means when the summer season arrives.","zh":"「when summer comes」意思是當夏季來臨時。"},{"en":"When summer comes, students may spend more time outdoors and less time indoors.","zh":"到夏天時，學生可能花更多時間在戶外，較少留在室內。"},{"en":"If the weather becomes warmer, families may change their weekend activities.","zh":"如果天氣變暖，家庭可能改變週末活動。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a seasonal change.","zh":"這個短語引入季節變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"go to barbecues","meaning":"去燒烤聚會","examples":[{"en":"In summer, they go to barbecues at family or friends’ houses.","zh":"夏天時，他們會去親友家中的燒烤聚會。"},{"en":"To go to barbecues means to attend outdoor meals where food is cooked on a grill.","zh":"「go to barbecues」意思是參加在戶外用烤爐烹調食物的聚餐。"},{"en":"A family may go to barbecues on warm weekends to meet relatives and friends.","zh":"家庭可能在溫暖週末去燒烤聚會，與親戚朋友見面。"},{"en":"If summer weather is pleasant, outdoor eating becomes more popular.","zh":"如果夏天天氣宜人，戶外用餐就更受歡迎。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a social outdoor dining activity.","zh":"這個短語描述社交性戶外餐飲活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"when I was growing up","meaning":"在我成長期間","examples":[{"en":"When Hazel was growing up, her parents divided Sunday tasks.","zh":"Hazel 成長期間，她父母會分配星期日任務。"},{"en":"When I was growing up means during my childhood and teenage years.","zh":"「when I was growing up」意思是在我的童年和青少年時期。"},{"en":"When I was growing up, most homework was written by hand, not typed online.","zh":"在我成長期間，大多數功課是手寫的，不是在網上打字。"},{"en":"If people describe childhood routines, they often compare them with modern life.","zh":"如果人們描述童年日常，他們常把它與現代生活比較。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a personal memory from earlier life.","zh":"這個短語引入早年生活的個人記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"do the gardening","meaning":"做園藝","examples":[{"en":"Her dad would do the gardening on Sundays.","zh":"她爸爸星期日會做園藝。"},{"en":"To do the gardening means to take care of plants, grass, flowers, or soil in a garden.","zh":"「do the gardening」意思是照顧花園中的植物、草地、花或泥土。"},{"en":"A family may do the gardening by cutting grass and watering flowers.","zh":"一家人可能透過剪草和澆花來做園藝。"},{"en":"If gardens need weekly care, Sunday may become a time for outdoor housework.","zh":"如果花園需要每週照顧，星期日可能成為戶外家務時間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical work in a garden.","zh":"這個短語描述花園中的實際工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"paint the fences","meaning":"油圍欄","examples":[{"en":"Her dad would paint the fences on Sundays.","zh":"她爸爸星期日會油圍欄。"},{"en":"To paint the fences means to cover garden or boundary fences with paint.","zh":"「paint the fences」意思是把油漆塗在花園或邊界圍欄上。"},{"en":"A homeowner may paint the fences before winter to protect the wood.","zh":"屋主可能在冬天前油圍欄，以保護木材。"},{"en":"If outdoor repairs are saved for Sunday, the day becomes partly a workday.","zh":"如果戶外維修留到星期日，這一天就部分變成工作日。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a DIY home-maintenance task.","zh":"這個短語描述 DIY 家居保養工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"do housework","meaning":"做家務","examples":[{"en":"Her mum would do housework on Sundays.","zh":"她媽媽星期日會做家務。"},{"en":"To do housework means to do domestic tasks such as cleaning, washing, cooking, or tidying.","zh":"「do housework」意思是做清潔、洗衣、煮食或收拾等家庭工作。"},{"en":"Students may help do housework by washing dishes after dinner.","zh":"學生可以晚飯後洗碗來幫忙做家務。"},{"en":"If one person does most housework, family duties may become unfairly divided.","zh":"如果一個人做大部分家務，家庭責任可能變得分配不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to ordinary work needed to keep a home running.","zh":"這個短語指維持家庭運作所需的普通工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"my late wife","meaning":"我的已故妻子","examples":[{"en":"Bryan Jones talks about his late wife Rose.","zh":"Bryan Jones 談及他的已故妻子 Rose。"},{"en":"My late wife means my wife who has died.","zh":"「my late wife」意思是我已去世的妻子。"},{"en":"A man may keep photographs of his late wife on the living-room shelf.","zh":"一名男子可能把已故妻子的照片放在客廳架上。"},{"en":"If someone mentions a late wife, the topic may involve memory, grief, or past family life.","zh":"如果某人提到已故妻子，話題可能涉及回憶、哀傷或過去家庭生活。"},{"en":"The phrase is respectful and personal.","zh":"這個短語帶尊重和個人情感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"work full-time as","meaning":"全職任職……","examples":[{"en":"Rose worked full-time as a supermarket manager.","zh":"Rose 全職任職超級市場經理。"},{"en":"To work full-time as something means to have that job as one’s main occupation, usually for normal full working hours.","zh":"「work full-time as」某職位，意思是以該工作作為主要職業，通常工作正常全職時數。"},{"en":"A parent may work full-time as a nurse while also caring for children at home.","zh":"家長可能全職任職護士，同時在家照顧孩子。"},{"en":"If someone works full-time, weekends may be important for chores and rest.","zh":"如果某人全職工作，週末可能對家務和休息很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a person’s main paid job.","zh":"這個短語描述某人的主要受薪工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"supermarket manager","meaning":"超級市場經理","examples":[{"en":"Rose worked full-time as a supermarket manager.","zh":"Rose 全職任職超級市場經理。"},{"en":"A supermarket manager is a person responsible for running a supermarket and managing staff, stock, and customers.","zh":"「supermarket manager」是負責營運超級市場並管理員工、貨品和顧客的人。"},{"en":"A supermarket manager may check deliveries, arrange shifts, and handle complaints.","zh":"超級市場經理可能檢查送貨、安排更表和處理投訴。"},{"en":"If the supermarket is busy, the manager may work long hours and feel tired on Sundays.","zh":"如果超級市場很忙，經理可能工作時間長，星期日感到疲倦。"},{"en":"The phrase names a retail management job.","zh":"這個短語指出零售管理職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have just moved to","meaning":"剛搬到……","examples":[{"en":"In 1961, Bryan had just moved to Bristol.","zh":"1961年，Bryan 剛搬到 Bristol。"},{"en":"To have just moved to a place means to have recently started living there.","zh":"「have just moved to」某地，意思是最近才開始住在那裡。"},{"en":"A student who has just moved to a new city may need time to find friends and transport routes.","zh":"剛搬到新城市的學生可能需要時間找朋友和交通路線。"},{"en":"If a couple has just moved, weekends may be filled with unpacking and repairs.","zh":"如果一對夫婦剛搬家，週末可能充滿拆箱和維修。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a recent change of home.","zh":"這個短語描述最近搬遷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"spend Sunday doing","meaning":"花星期日做……","examples":[{"en":"Bryan spent Sunday maintaining the new house.","zh":"Bryan 花星期日維修保養新居。"},{"en":"To spend Sunday doing something means to use Sunday time for that activity.","zh":"「spend Sunday doing」某事，意思是把星期日時間用於該活動。"},{"en":"A student may spend Sunday finishing a project due on Monday.","zh":"學生可能花星期日完成星期一要交的專題。"},{"en":"If a new house needs repairs, Sunday may be used for maintenance instead of leisure.","zh":"如果新屋需要維修，星期日可能用於保養而不是休閒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how someone uses Sunday.","zh":"這個短語描述某人如何使用星期日。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"maintain the new house","meaning":"維修保養新居","examples":[{"en":"Bryan spent Sunday maintaining the new house.","zh":"Bryan 花星期日維修保養新居。"},{"en":"To maintain the new house means to repair, care for, and keep the new home in good condition.","zh":"「maintain the new house」意思是維修、照料並保持新居狀態良好。"},{"en":"New homeowners may maintain the house by painting walls and fixing loose doors.","zh":"新屋主可能透過油牆和修理鬆脫門來保養房子。"},{"en":"If a house is newly bought, many small jobs may need to be done at weekends.","zh":"如果房子剛買下，許多小工作可能要在週末完成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical home upkeep.","zh":"這個短語描述實際家居保養。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"washing and ironing","meaning":"洗衣和熨衫","examples":[{"en":"The washing and ironing had to be done.","zh":"洗衣和熨衫必須完成。"},{"en":"Washing and ironing means cleaning clothes and pressing them flat with an iron.","zh":"「washing and ironing」意思是清洗衣服並用熨斗把它們熨平。"},{"en":"A family may spend Sunday evening doing washing and ironing for the school week.","zh":"家庭可能花星期日晚上洗衣和熨衫，為上學週準備。"},{"en":"If clothes pile up, washing and ironing can take a long time.","zh":"如果衣服堆積，洗衣和熨衫可能花很久。"},{"en":"The phrase describes common household laundry work.","zh":"這個短語描述常見洗衣家務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have to be done","meaning":"必須完成","examples":[{"en":"The washing and ironing had to be done.","zh":"洗衣和熨衫必須完成。"},{"en":"Have to be done means must be completed because it is necessary.","zh":"「have to be done」意思是因為必要而必須完成。"},{"en":"The dishes have to be done before guests arrive.","zh":"客人到達前，碗碟必須洗好。"},{"en":"If chores have to be done, leisure may have to wait.","zh":"如果家務必須完成，休閒可能要等待。"},{"en":"The phrase shows necessity or duty.","zh":"這個短語顯示必要性或責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"work together","meaning":"一起合作","examples":[{"en":"There was a feeling that the couple worked together at home.","zh":"當時有一種感覺，就是這對夫婦在家中一起合作。"},{"en":"To work together means to cooperate and share tasks.","zh":"「work together」意思是合作並分擔任務。"},{"en":"Students work together when they divide a project into research, writing, and design.","zh":"學生把專題分成資料搜集、寫作和設計時，就是一起合作。"},{"en":"If couples work together at home, chores may feel fairer and faster.","zh":"如果夫婦在家中一起合作，家務可能感覺更公平、更快完成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cooperation.","zh":"這個短語描述合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"spend the day with","meaning":"與……共度一天","examples":[{"en":"They sometimes spent the day with Rose’s sister.","zh":"他們有時與 Rose 的妹妹共度一天。"},{"en":"To spend the day with someone means to use most of the day being with that person.","zh":"「spend the day with」某人，意思是用一天大部分時間與那個人在一起。"},{"en":"A child may spend the day with grandparents during school holidays.","zh":"學校假期時，孩子可能與祖父母共度一天。"},{"en":"If people spend Sunday with relatives, the day becomes social rather than only domestic.","zh":"如果人們星期日與親戚共度，這一天就變得社交，而不只是家庭工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shared time with another person.","zh":"這個短語描述與某人共享時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"relatives","meaning":"親戚","examples":[{"en":"They sometimes spent the day with relatives.","zh":"他們有時與親戚共度一天。"},{"en":"Relatives are family members other than one’s immediate household, such as cousins, aunts, uncles, or grandparents.","zh":"「relatives」是直系同住家庭以外的家庭成員，例如表親、姨母、叔伯或祖父母。"},{"en":"Many families visit relatives during festivals or long weekends.","zh":"許多家庭在節日或長週末探望親戚。"},{"en":"If Sunday is used to see relatives, it strengthens family connections.","zh":"如果星期日用來見親戚，它會加強家庭連繫。"},{"en":"The word refers to people connected by family.","zh":"這個詞指有家庭關係的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"for the first time","meaning":"第一次","examples":[{"en":"In 1961, Bryan had a new car for the first time.","zh":"1961年，Bryan 第一次擁有新車。"},{"en":"For the first time means something happens in a person’s experience before it has ever happened to them.","zh":"「for the first time」意思是某事在某人的經驗中首次發生。"},{"en":"A student may give a speech in English for the first time and feel nervous.","zh":"學生第一次用英語演講時，可能感到緊張。"},{"en":"If a family owns a car for the first time, weekend travel becomes easier.","zh":"如果家庭第一次擁有汽車，週末出行就變得更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a new personal experience.","zh":"這個短語標示新的個人經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"spend time in the countryside","meaning":"在郊外消磨時間","examples":[{"en":"They spent time in the countryside or garden centres.","zh":"他們在郊外或園藝中心消磨時間。"},{"en":"To spend time in the countryside means to use time in rural areas away from the city.","zh":"「spend time in the countryside」意思是在遠離城市的鄉郊地區度過時間。"},{"en":"A family may spend time in the countryside walking, picnicking, or visiting farms.","zh":"家庭可能在郊外散步、野餐或參觀農場。"},{"en":"If people have a car, they can travel outside the city more easily on Sundays.","zh":"如果人們有車，星期日就更容易到城市外出遊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes leisure in rural surroundings.","zh":"這個短語描述在鄉郊環境中的休閒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"garden centres","meaning":"園藝中心","examples":[{"en":"Bryan and Rose sometimes visited garden centres.","zh":"Bryan 和 Rose 有時參觀園藝中心。"},{"en":"Garden centres are shops or places that sell plants, gardening tools, soil, and outdoor items.","zh":"「garden centres」是售賣植物、園藝工具、泥土和戶外用品的商店或地方。"},{"en":"A family may visit a garden centre to buy flowers for the balcony.","zh":"家庭可能去園藝中心買花放在露台。"},{"en":"If people enjoy gardening, a garden centre can become a Sunday leisure destination.","zh":"如果人們喜歡園藝，園藝中心可以成為星期日休閒目的地。"},{"en":"The phrase names a place connected with gardening and home life.","zh":"這個短語指出與園藝和家庭生活有關的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"spend a couple of hours doing","meaning":"花兩個小時左右做……","examples":[{"en":"Bryan now spends a couple of hours reading the newspapers.","zh":"Bryan 現在花兩個小時左右閱讀報章。"},{"en":"To spend a couple of hours doing something means to use about two hours for that activity.","zh":"「spend a couple of hours doing」某事，意思是用大約兩小時做該活動。"},{"en":"A student may spend a couple of hours revising vocabulary before a test.","zh":"學生可能在測驗前花兩小時左右溫習詞彙。"},{"en":"If someone has a quiet Sunday, they may spend a few hours reading slowly.","zh":"如果某人有寧靜星期日，可能花幾小時慢慢閱讀。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate amount of time.","zh":"這個短語提供大約時間量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"pensioner","meaning":"退休人士；長者","examples":[{"en":"Bryan Jones is a pensioner living near Bristol.","zh":"Bryan Jones 是住在 Bristol 附近的退休人士。"},{"en":"A pensioner is an older person who has retired and receives a pension.","zh":"「pensioner」是已退休並領取退休金的年長人士。"},{"en":"A pensioner may spend weekday mornings shopping when stores are quieter.","zh":"退休人士可能在商店較安靜的平日上午購物。"},{"en":"If someone is a pensioner, their Sunday routine may differ from that of full-time workers.","zh":"如果某人是退休人士，他的星期日規律可能與全職工作者不同。"},{"en":"The word refers to a retired person, usually an older adult.","zh":"這個詞指退休人士，通常是年長成人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"for each question","meaning":"對於每一道題","examples":[{"en":"For each question, only one of the choices is correct.","zh":"對於每一道題，只有其中一個選項正確。"},{"en":"For each question means separately for every question in the exercise or test.","zh":"「for each question」意思是對練習或測驗中的每一道題分別而言。"},{"en":"For each question, students should read the options before checking the passage.","zh":"對於每一道題，學生應先閱讀選項，再核對文章。"},{"en":"If students treat each question carefully, they avoid carrying one mistake into the next.","zh":"如果學生仔細處理每一道題，就能避免把一個錯誤帶到下一題。"},{"en":"The phrase gives instructions question by question.","zh":"這個短語逐題給出指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"only one of the choices","meaning":"只有其中一個選項","examples":[{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct.","zh":"只有其中一個選項正確。"},{"en":"Only one of the choices means just one option from the list, not two or more.","zh":"「only one of the choices」意思是列表中只有一個選項，而不是兩個或更多。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice test, only one of the choices may match the passage exactly.","zh":"在多項選擇題中，只有其中一個選項可能與文章完全相符。"},{"en":"If students choose two letters when only one is allowed, the answer may be marked wrong.","zh":"如果只容許一個答案時學生選兩個字母，答案可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the answer is singular.","zh":"這個短語強調答案只有一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"corresponding letter","meaning":"對應的字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the corresponding letter in the answer box.","zh":"考生在答案框中寫下對應的字母。"},{"en":"The corresponding letter is the letter that matches the correct option or answer.","zh":"「corresponding letter」是與正確選項或答案相配的字母。"},{"en":"If the correct option is B, students should write the corresponding letter B.","zh":"如果正確選項是 B，學生應寫下對應字母 B。"},{"en":"If students copy the whole sentence instead of the letter, they may not follow the instruction.","zh":"如果學生抄寫整句而不是字母，可能沒有跟從指示。"},{"en":"The phrase links an answer choice to its letter.","zh":"這個短語把答案選項與其字母連結起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"appropriate box","meaning":"適當的方格","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the letter in the appropriate box.","zh":"考生把字母寫在適當的方格中。"},{"en":"The appropriate box is the correct space where an answer should be written.","zh":"「appropriate box」是應寫答案的正確空格。"},{"en":"In an exam, writing the answer in the wrong box may confuse the marker.","zh":"在考試中，把答案寫在錯誤方格可能令閱卷員混淆。"},{"en":"If each answer is placed in the appropriate box, the answer sheet is clear.","zh":"如果每個答案放在適當方格，答題紙就清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the correct place for a response.","zh":"這個短語指作答的正確位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"according to the diaries","meaning":"根據日記記錄","examples":[{"en":"According to the diaries, women rarely had free time on Sunday mornings.","zh":"根據日記記錄，女性星期日早上很少有空閒時間。"},{"en":"According to the diaries means based on what the diary records show.","zh":"「according to the diaries」意思是根據日記記錄所顯示的資料。"},{"en":"According to the diaries, the family spent most Sundays cooking, cleaning, and visiting relatives.","zh":"根據日記記錄，這家人大多數星期日都在煮食、清潔和探親。"},{"en":"If diaries record daily details, they can provide evidence about real behaviour.","zh":"如果日記記錄日常細節，它們可以提供真實行為的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces information from written personal records.","zh":"這個短語引入來自個人書面紀錄的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rarely have free time","meaning":"很少有空閒時間","examples":[{"en":"Women rarely had free time on Sunday mornings in 1961.","zh":"1961年，女性星期日早上很少有空閒時間。"},{"en":"To rarely have free time means to almost never have time for rest or personal activities.","zh":"「rarely have free time」意思是幾乎沒有時間休息或做個人活動。"},{"en":"A student with school, tutoring, and chores may rarely have free time during weekdays.","zh":"有上學、補習和家務的學生，平日可能很少有空閒時間。"},{"en":"If housework takes up the morning, personal leisure becomes difficult.","zh":"如果家務佔據早上，個人休閒就變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a serious lack of leisure.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重缺乏休閒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"want to do more","meaning":"想做更多事情","examples":[{"en":"People want to do more on Sundays now.","zh":"現在人們想在星期日做更多事情。"},{"en":"To want to do more means to wish to have more activities, experiences, or choices.","zh":"「want to do more」意思是希望有更多活動、經驗或選擇。"},{"en":"During holidays, children often want to do more than stay at home.","zh":"假期期間，兒童常想做更多事情，而不只是留在家中。"},{"en":"If people have limited free time, they may try to fill Sunday with enjoyable plans.","zh":"如果人們空閒時間有限，他們可能嘗試用愉快計劃填滿星期日。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a desire for a fuller day.","zh":"這個短語顯示想要更充實一天的願望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"shops are open","meaning":"商店營業","examples":[{"en":"People may do more on Sundays because more shops are open.","zh":"人們星期日可能做更多事情，因為更多商店營業。"},{"en":"Shops are open means shops are trading and customers can enter and buy things.","zh":"「shops are open」意思是商店正在營業，顧客可以進入購物。"},{"en":"If shops are open late, workers can buy groceries after work.","zh":"如果商店營業至較晚，工人下班後可以買雜貨。"},{"en":"When shops open on Sunday, shopping becomes possible during weekend leisure time.","zh":"當商店星期日營業，購物就可以在週末休閒時間進行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes availability of shopping services.","zh":"這個短語描述購物服務可用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be tired on Saturdays","meaning":"星期六感到疲倦","examples":[{"en":"Many people are tired on Saturdays after the working week.","zh":"許多人在一星期工作後，星期六感到疲倦。"},{"en":"To be tired on Saturdays means to feel low in energy on Saturday, often because of weekday work.","zh":"「be tired on Saturdays」意思是在星期六感到能量不足，通常因平日工作所致。"},{"en":"A teacher may be tired on Saturdays after five days of lessons and marking.","zh":"老師經過五天上課和批改後，星期六可能感到疲倦。"},{"en":"If Saturday is used for recovery, Sunday may become the main day for fun.","zh":"如果星期六用來恢復精力，星期日可能成為主要娛樂日。"},{"en":"The phrase links weekend behaviour with weekday exhaustion.","zh":"這個短語把週末行為與平日疲勞連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"shopping habits","meaning":"購物習慣","examples":[{"en":"Shopping habits have changed since 1961.","zh":"自1961年以來，購物習慣已改變。"},{"en":"Shopping habits are the usual ways, times, and reasons people shop.","zh":"「shopping habits」是人們購物的通常方式、時間和原因。"},{"en":"A family’s shopping habits may include buying groceries online every Friday.","zh":"一個家庭的購物習慣可能包括每星期五網上買雜貨。"},{"en":"If shops open on Sundays, shopping habits can shift from weekdays to weekends.","zh":"如果商店星期日營業，購物習慣可以由平日轉向週末。"},{"en":"The phrase describes patterns of buying behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述購買行為模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have changed since","meaning":"自……以來已改變","examples":[{"en":"Shopping habits have changed since 1961.","zh":"自1961年以來，購物習慣已改變。"},{"en":"To have changed since a time means to be different from that time until now.","zh":"「have changed since」某時間，意思是從該時間到現在已變得不同。"},{"en":"School communication has changed since parents started using messaging apps.","zh":"自從家長開始使用通訊應用程式後，學校溝通方式已改變。"},{"en":"If society changes over decades, daily routines also change.","zh":"如果社會在數十年間改變，日常習慣也會改變。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the present with a starting point in the past.","zh":"這個短語把現在與過去某起點比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in that","meaning":"在於；原因是","examples":[{"en":"Shopping habits have changed in that men now shop as much as women.","zh":"購物習慣已改變，在於男性現在購物和女性一樣多。"},{"en":"In that means because or in the specific way that something is true.","zh":"「in that」意思是在於，或某事成立的具體方式是。"},{"en":"Online lessons are different in that students can replay the video.","zh":"網上課堂不同之處在於學生可以重播影片。"},{"en":"If shopping is no longer mainly done by women, the change lies in gender participation.","zh":"如果購物不再主要由女性進行，改變就在於性別參與。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the exact nature of a difference.","zh":"這個短語解釋差異的具體性質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Compared with 1961, women do far less housework on Sundays.","zh":"與1961年相比，女性星期日做的家務少得多。"},{"en":"Compared with means when judged against another time, group, or thing.","zh":"「compared with」意思是與另一時間、群體或事物比較時。"},{"en":"Compared with last year, the class now reads more confidently.","zh":"與去年相比，這班學生現在閱讀更有信心。"},{"en":"If present routines are compared with old routines, social changes become clear.","zh":"如果把現在日常與舊日常比較，社會變化就會變得清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces comparison.","zh":"這個短語引入比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"far less housework","meaning":"少得多的家務","examples":[{"en":"Women do far less housework on Sundays than before.","zh":"女性星期日做的家務比以前少得多。"},{"en":"Far less housework means much fewer domestic tasks or much less time spent on them.","zh":"「far less housework」意思是家務任務少得多，或花在家務上的時間少得多。"},{"en":"A family may do far less housework after hiring a cleaner once a week.","zh":"家庭每星期請一次清潔工後，可能做少得多家務。"},{"en":"If meals are eaten out and chores are spread out, Sunday housework decreases.","zh":"如果外出用餐而家務分散完成，星期日家務就會減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large reduction in domestic work.","zh":"這個短語描述家務大幅減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"complete the following sentences","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the following sentences using words from the text.","zh":"考生使用文章中的詞語完成以下句子。"},{"en":"To complete the following sentences means to fill in the missing parts of the sentences below.","zh":"「complete the following sentences」意思是填入下方句子中缺失的部分。"},{"en":"In a reading test, candidates complete the following sentences by copying exact words from the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，考生透過抄寫文章原字完成以下句子。"},{"en":"If students ignore the grammar of the sentence, the answer may not fit.","zh":"如果學生忽視句子的文法，答案可能不吻合。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個詞","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should use no more than three words for each gap.","zh":"考生每個空格應使用不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"「no more than three words」意思是答案必須包含三個詞或更少。"},{"en":"If the answer is “Sunday papers”, it follows the rule because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “Sunday papers”，它符合規則，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"If candidates write four words, the answer may be wrong even if the meaning is close.","zh":"如果考生寫四個詞，即使意思接近，答案也可能錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"from the text","meaning":"從文章中","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose words from the text.","zh":"考生從文章中選擇詞語。"},{"en":"From the text means the answer must come directly from the passage, not from the student’s own wording.","zh":"「from the text」意思是答案必須直接來自文章，而不是學生自己的措辭。"},{"en":"In IELTS Reading, students often need exact words from the text for completion questions.","zh":"在 IELTS Reading 中，學生常需要從文章中找原字完成填空題。"},{"en":"If candidates use synonyms not found in the passage, the answer may not be accepted.","zh":"如果考生使用文章中沒有的同義詞，答案可能不被接受。"},{"en":"The phrase tells students the source of the answer.","zh":"這個短語告訴學生答案來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"for each gap","meaning":"每個空格","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write no more than three words for each gap.","zh":"考生每個空格寫不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"For each gap means separately for every blank space in the exercise.","zh":"「for each gap」意思是對練習中每一個空白位置分別而言。"},{"en":"For each gap, students should check grammar before writing the answer.","zh":"對於每個空格，學生寫答案前應檢查文法。"},{"en":"If one gap needs a noun and another needs a verb, candidates must answer them separately.","zh":"如果一個空格需要名詞，另一個需要動詞，考生必須分別作答。"},{"en":"The phrase gives instructions blank by blank.","zh":"這個短語逐空格給出指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"thousands of diaries","meaning":"數千本日記","examples":[{"en":"Professor Gershuny discovered thousands of diaries at the BBC.","zh":"Gershuny 教授在 BBC 發現數千本日記。"},{"en":"Thousands of diaries means a very large number of personal daily records.","zh":"「thousands of diaries」意思是非常大量的個人日常記錄。"},{"en":"A historian would be excited to find thousands of diaries from ordinary families.","zh":"歷史學家若發現數千本普通家庭日記，會非常興奮。"},{"en":"If thousands of diaries are available, researchers can study patterns across many lives.","zh":"如果有數千本日記可用，研究人員就能研究許多人生活中的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large collection of written personal evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述大量個人書面證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"not as gender-segregated as","meaning":"不像……那樣按性別分隔","examples":[{"en":"Shopping is not as gender-segregated as it was in 1961.","zh":"購物不像1961年那樣按性別分隔。"},{"en":"Not as gender-segregated as means less divided by gender than before or than another situation.","zh":"「not as gender-segregated as」意思是比以前或比另一情況較少按性別分隔。"},{"en":"Cooking in many families is not as gender-segregated as it was in the past.","zh":"在許多家庭中，煮食不像過去那樣按性別分隔。"},{"en":"If men and women both shop, the activity becomes less tied to one gender.","zh":"如果男女都購物，該活動就較少只與某一性別相連。"},{"en":"The phrase compares how strongly gender roles divide an activity.","zh":"這個短語比較性別角色把活動分隔得有多強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"go for a drink","meaning":"去飲酒；去喝一杯","examples":[{"en":"Men would often go for a drink before lunch.","zh":"男性常在午餐前去喝一杯。"},{"en":"To go for a drink means to go out to have an alcoholic or non-alcoholic drink, usually socially.","zh":"「go for a drink」意思是外出喝酒精或非酒精飲品，通常帶社交性。"},{"en":"Colleagues may go for a drink after work to relax and talk.","zh":"同事可能下班後去喝一杯，放鬆和聊天。"},{"en":"If men went for a drink before lunch, their Sunday mornings included leisure outside the home.","zh":"如果男性午餐前去喝一杯，他們星期日早上就包括家外休閒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a casual social outing.","zh":"這個短語描述隨意社交外出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"before lunch","meaning":"午餐前","examples":[{"en":"Men were often out of the house before lunch.","zh":"男性午餐前常在家外。"},{"en":"Before lunch means during the morning or early part of the day before the midday meal.","zh":"「before lunch」意思是在午飯前的早上或一天較早部分。"},{"en":"A student may finish homework before lunch so the afternoon is free.","zh":"學生可能午餐前完成功課，好讓下午有空。"},{"en":"If men had leisure before lunch while women did chores, the gender gap was clear.","zh":"如果男性午餐前休閒而女性做家務，性別差距就很清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a time marker.","zh":"這個短語提供時間標記。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Some statements agree with the information given in the passage.","zh":"有些陳述與文章所給資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the text says.","zh":"「agree with the information given」意思是與文本所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the passage says shops opened on Sundays, a statement saying Sunday shopping increased may agree with the information.","zh":"如果文章說商店星期日營業，陳述說星期日購物增加可能與資料一致。"},{"en":"If a statement matches the text exactly in meaning, students should choose TRUE or YES.","zh":"如果陳述在意思上與文本完全相符，學生應選 TRUE 或 YES。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in reading-comprehension tasks.","zh":"這個短語用於閱讀理解任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"「contradict the information」意思是說出與文本相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says women did less housework, a statement saying they did more would contradict the information.","zh":"如果文章說女性做較少家務，陳述說她們做更多家務就與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"When a statement contradicts the text, students should not choose TRUE.","zh":"當陳述與文本矛盾時，學生不應選 TRUE。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a direct conflict with the passage.","zh":"這個短語描述與文章直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"Write “NOT GIVEN” if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果沒有這方面的資料，寫 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"「there is no information on this」意思是文章沒有說明該陳述是真或是假。"},{"en":"If a text mentions Sunday shopping but not online shopping, there is no information on online shopping.","zh":"如果文本提到星期日購物，但沒有提到網上購物，就沒有網上購物方面的資料。"},{"en":"When information is missing, students should not guess from common knowledge.","zh":"當資料缺失時，學生不應根據常識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase explains when to choose NOT GIVEN.","zh":"這個短語解釋何時選 NOT GIVEN。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"usually eat out","meaning":"通常外出用餐","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Mr. Atchison usually eats out.","zh":"題目問 Atchison 先生是否通常外出用餐。"},{"en":"To usually eat out means to often have meals in restaurants, cafés, pubs, or other places outside the home.","zh":"「usually eat out」意思是常在餐廳、咖啡店、酒吧或其他家外地方用餐。"},{"en":"A busy worker may usually eat out on Fridays because they are too tired to cook.","zh":"忙碌工人可能星期五通常外出用餐，因為太累不想煮飯。"},{"en":"If someone usually eats out on Sunday, home cooking becomes less central to their routine.","zh":"如果某人星期日通常外出用餐，在家煮飯就不再是其日常核心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a regular habit of dining away from home.","zh":"這個短語描述經常在家外用餐的習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"household chores","meaning":"家務","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Mrs. Hallows’ husband does household chores.","zh":"題目問 Hallows 夫人的丈夫是否做家務。"},{"en":"Household chores are regular tasks needed to keep a home clean and organised.","zh":"「household chores」是保持家居清潔和有條理所需的日常工作。"},{"en":"Washing dishes, taking out rubbish, and vacuuming are household chores.","zh":"洗碗、倒垃圾和吸塵都是家務。"},{"en":"If household chores are shared, one person does not carry all the domestic work.","zh":"如果家務被分擔，就不會由一個人承擔全部家庭工作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to everyday home duties.","zh":"這個短語指日常家庭責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"shops are too busy","meaning":"商店太擠迫","examples":[{"en":"Mrs. Hallows thinks the shops are too busy on Sundays.","zh":"Hallows 夫人認為星期日商店太擠迫。"},{"en":"Shops are too busy means there are too many shoppers, making the place crowded or unpleasant.","zh":"「shops are too busy」意思是購物者太多，令地方擁擠或不愉快。"},{"en":"During a big sale, shops may be too busy for families with young children.","zh":"大減價期間，商店對有年幼孩子的家庭來說可能太擠迫。"},{"en":"If shops are too busy, some people choose to shop on weekdays instead.","zh":"如果商店太擠迫，有些人會改在平日購物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes crowded shopping conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述擠迫的購物環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a widower","meaning":"鰥夫；喪妻男子","examples":[{"en":"A widower is a man whose wife has died.","zh":"鰥夫是妻子已去世的男子。"},{"en":"A widower may live alone after his wife’s death, though some live with family.","zh":"鰥夫在妻子去世後可能獨居，但有些會與家人同住。"},{"en":"A neighbour may invite a widower to Sunday lunch so he does not feel lonely.","zh":"鄰居可能邀請鰥夫吃星期日午餐，讓他不感到孤單。"},{"en":"If a man loses his wife, his daily routines and memories may change deeply.","zh":"如果男子失去妻子，他的日常和回憶可能深受影響。"},{"en":"The word is the male equivalent of widow.","zh":"這個詞是 widow 的男性對應詞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 66 - Sunday Is a Fun Day for Modern Brits.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 67":[{"front":"try to change the world","meaning":"嘗試改變世界","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes teenagers who try to change the world through ethical purchases.","zh":"文章描述青少年透過道德購買嘗試改變世界。"},{"en":"To try to change the world means to take actions that aim to make society fairer, cleaner, or better.","zh":"嘗試改變世界，指採取行動，目標是令社會更公平、更清潔或更好。"},{"en":"Students may try to change the world by reducing plastic waste in their school.","zh":"學生可能透過減少學校塑膠廢物來嘗試改變世界。"},{"en":"If many small actions are repeated by many people, they can create wider change.","zh":"如果許多人重複許多小行動，就可以造成更廣泛改變。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests idealism, effort, and a belief that ordinary people can help.","zh":"這個短語暗示理想主義、努力，以及相信普通人可以幫忙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one purchase at a time","meaning":"透過每一次購買逐步地","examples":[{"en":"Teenagers are trying to change the world one purchase at a time.","zh":"青少年正透過每一次購買逐步地嘗試改變世界。"},{"en":"One purchase at a time means making change gradually through each buying decision.","zh":"透過每一次購買逐步地，指透過每個購買決定逐漸帶來改變。"},{"en":"A family can support local farms one purchase at a time by buying local vegetables each week.","zh":"一個家庭可以每週購買本地蔬菜，透過每一次購買逐步支持本地農場。"},{"en":"If consumers choose ethical products repeatedly, companies may change how they produce goods.","zh":"如果消費者反覆選擇道德產品，公司可能改變生產方式。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that small choices can build a larger effect.","zh":"這個短語顯示小選擇可以累積成更大效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"classes adjourn","meaning":"課堂結束","examples":[{"en":"When classes adjourn, the eighth-graders go to a natural-foods store.","zh":"課堂結束時，八年級學生會去一間天然食品店。"},{"en":"When classes adjourn means when lessons end or stop for the day.","zh":"課堂結束，指一天的課堂完結或停止。"},{"en":"When classes adjourn, students may pack their bags and meet friends outside the classroom.","zh":"課堂結束時，學生可能收拾書包並在課室外見朋友。"},{"en":"If classes adjourn early, students have more time for clubs, homework, or shopping.","zh":"如果課堂提早結束，學生就有更多時間參加學會、做功課或購物。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and means class is dismissed or finished.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是下課或課堂完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"eighth-graders","meaning":"八年級學生","examples":[{"en":"Eighth-graders at Fayerweather Street School often visit the local natural-foods grocer’s.","zh":"Fayerweather Street School 的八年級學生常去本地天然食品店。"},{"en":"Eighth-graders are students in the eighth year of school, usually around thirteen or fourteen years old.","zh":"八年級學生，是學校第八年級的學生，通常大約十三或十四歲。"},{"en":"Eighth-graders may start thinking more independently about fashion, food, and social issues.","zh":"八年級學生可能開始更獨立地思考時裝、食物和社會議題。"},{"en":"If eighth-graders care about ethical buying, younger students may follow their example.","zh":"如果八年級學生關心道德購買，較年幼學生可能仿效他們。"},{"en":"The word identifies a school-year group, not a level of ability.","zh":"這個詞指出學校年級群體，而不是能力水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ignore the mall","meaning":"不理會商場","examples":[{"en":"The students ignore the mall and go to a natural-foods grocer’s instead.","zh":"學生不理會商場，反而去天然食品店。"},{"en":"To ignore the mall means to choose not to go to the shopping centre even though it is available.","zh":"不理會商場，指即使商場可去，也選擇不去。"},{"en":"Teenagers may ignore the mall if they prefer a small café where they can talk quietly.","zh":"如果青少年較喜歡可以安靜聊天的小咖啡店，可能會不理會商場。"},{"en":"If students ignore the mall, it suggests another place feels more meaningful or attractive to them.","zh":"如果學生不理會商場，這暗示另一地方對他們更有意義或吸引力。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a deliberate choice against ordinary teenage shopping.","zh":"這個短語顯示刻意不選普通青少年購物地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"down the street","meaning":"沿街不遠處","examples":[{"en":"The mall is located down the street from the school.","zh":"商場位於學校沿街不遠處。"},{"en":"Down the street means a short distance along the same street or nearby road.","zh":"沿街不遠處，指沿同一條街或附近道路走一小段距離。"},{"en":"A bakery down the street from school may become popular with students after class.","zh":"學校沿街不遠處的麵包店，可能在放學後受學生歡迎。"},{"en":"If a shop is down the street, people can reach it easily on foot.","zh":"如果商店在沿街不遠處，人們可以輕易步行到達。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests the place is nearby and convenient.","zh":"這個短語暗示地點附近且方便。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"go straight to","meaning":"直接前往","examples":[{"en":"The students go straight to the place they consider cooler.","zh":"學生直接前往他們認為更有型的地方。"},{"en":"To go straight to a place means to go there directly without stopping elsewhere.","zh":"直接前往某地，指不在其他地方停留，直接去那裡。"},{"en":"After school, some students go straight to the library to finish homework.","zh":"放學後，有些學生直接前往圖書館完成功課。"},{"en":"If teenagers go straight to one shop, it shows that shop has strong appeal.","zh":"如果青少年直接前往某間店，顯示該店有強大吸引力。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses direct movement and clear preference.","zh":"這個短語強調直接移動和明確偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"local natural-foods grocer’s","meaning":"本地天然食品店","examples":[{"en":"The students gather at the local natural-foods grocer’s after school.","zh":"學生放學後聚集在本地天然食品店。"},{"en":"A local natural-foods grocer’s is a nearby shop that sells healthier or less processed food.","zh":"本地天然食品店，是附近售賣較健康或較少加工食物的商店。"},{"en":"A family may buy organic fruit and whole-grain bread from a local natural-foods grocer’s.","zh":"家庭可能從本地天然食品店購買有機水果和全麥麵包。"},{"en":"If teenagers meet there regularly, the shop becomes both a food store and a social space.","zh":"如果青少年定期在那裡見面，該店就既是食品店，也是社交空間。"},{"en":"The phrase combines location, food values, and small-shop atmosphere.","zh":"這個短語結合地點、飲食價值和小店氣氛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"gather in groups of","meaning":"成群聚集","examples":[{"en":"The students sometimes gather in groups of ten or more.","zh":"學生有時十人或更多人成群聚集。"},{"en":"To gather in groups of a number means to come together in groups of that size.","zh":"以某數量成群聚集，指以那個大小的小組聚在一起。"},{"en":"Students may gather in groups of four to prepare a class presentation.","zh":"學生可能四人一組聚在一起準備課堂匯報。"},{"en":"If teenagers gather in large groups, a shop can become a popular meeting place.","zh":"如果青少年大群聚集，商店可以變成受歡迎的聚會地點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both gathering and group size.","zh":"這個短語同時描述聚集和小組大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be smitten by","meaning":"被……深深吸引","examples":[{"en":"The students are smitten by a marketing atmosphere that links attractiveness to eating well.","zh":"學生被一種把吸引力與健康飲食連繫起來的市場推廣氣氛深深吸引。"},{"en":"To be smitten by something means to be strongly charmed or attracted by it.","zh":"被某物深深吸引，指被它強烈迷住或吸引。"},{"en":"A child may be smitten by a toy shop because of its bright colours and displays.","zh":"孩子可能因玩具店鮮艷顏色和陳列而被它深深吸引。"},{"en":"If teenagers are smitten by a store’s image, they may buy products that match that image.","zh":"如果青少年被商店形象吸引，他們可能購買符合該形象的產品。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests emotional attraction, not just logical interest.","zh":"這個短語暗示情感吸引，而不只是理性興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"marketing atmosphere","meaning":"市場推廣氣氛","examples":[{"en":"The store creates a marketing atmosphere that appeals to teenagers.","zh":"該店營造出吸引青少年的市場推廣氣氛。"},{"en":"A marketing atmosphere is the mood, design, music, message, and image used to attract customers.","zh":"市場推廣氣氛，是用來吸引顧客的情緒、設計、音樂、信息和形象。"},{"en":"A café may use soft lighting and music to create a relaxed marketing atmosphere.","zh":"咖啡店可能用柔和燈光和音樂營造輕鬆市場推廣氣氛。"},{"en":"If the atmosphere feels cool and ethical, young shoppers may want to belong to it.","zh":"如果氣氛感覺有型又道德，年輕購物者可能想成為其中一分子。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to how a place sells an idea, not only a product.","zh":"這個短語指一個地方如何銷售想法，而不只是產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"link attractiveness to","meaning":"將吸引力與……聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"The marketing atmosphere links attractiveness to eating well.","zh":"市場推廣氣氛將吸引力與健康飲食聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To link attractiveness to something means to connect looking good or being appealing with that thing.","zh":"將吸引力與某事聯繫起來，指把好看或有魅力與該事連在一起。"},{"en":"Advertisements often link confidence to wearing certain clothes.","zh":"廣告常把信心與穿某些衣服聯繫起來。"},{"en":"If a shop links attractiveness to healthy food, teenagers may see ethical snacks as stylish.","zh":"如果商店把吸引力與健康食物連繫起來，青少年可能把道德小食視為有型。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a connection created by marketing or social messages.","zh":"這個短語描述由市場推廣或社會信息創造出的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"eating well","meaning":"健康飲食；吃得好","examples":[{"en":"The students associate eating well with looking and feeling good.","zh":"學生把健康飲食與看起來好和感覺好聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Eating well means choosing food that supports health, energy, and well-being.","zh":"健康飲食，指選擇支持健康、能量和身心狀態的食物。"},{"en":"A student eats well when lunch includes vegetables, protein, and enough water.","zh":"當學生午餐包含蔬菜、蛋白質和足夠水分，就是吃得好。"},{"en":"If people eat well regularly, they may feel more energetic and focused.","zh":"如果人們定期健康飲食，可能感到更有精力和專注。"},{"en":"The phrase is about healthy eating, not simply eating expensive food.","zh":"這個短語關於健康飲食，而不只是吃昂貴食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"when it comes time to","meaning":"到了……的時候","examples":[{"en":"When it comes time to buy a snack, the students think about farmers.","zh":"到了買小食的時候，學生會想到農民。"},{"en":"When it comes time to do something means when the moment arrives to do it.","zh":"到了做某事的時候，指做該事的時刻到來。"},{"en":"When it comes time to choose subjects, students should think about interest and ability.","zh":"到了選科的時候，學生應考慮興趣和能力。"},{"en":"If ethical ideas matter, they should influence people when real buying decisions happen.","zh":"如果道德想法重要，它們應在人們真正作購買決定時產生影響。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the moment when a decision must be made.","zh":"這個短語引入必須作決定的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a chocolate treat","meaning":"朱古力小食","examples":[{"en":"Even a chocolate treat can make students think about ethical buying.","zh":"即使一份朱古力小食也可以令學生想到道德購買。"},{"en":"A chocolate treat is a small enjoyable chocolate snack, often bought for pleasure.","zh":"朱古力小食，是小份令人愉快、通常為享受而購買的朱古力零食。"},{"en":"A parent may buy a chocolate treat for a child after a long school day.","zh":"家長可能在孩子漫長上學日後買一份朱古力小食給他。"},{"en":"If a treat is Fair Trade, pleasure can be connected with concern for farmers.","zh":"如果小食是公平貿易產品，享受就可以與關心農民連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that ethical choices can appear in ordinary snacks.","zh":"這個短語顯示道德選擇可以出現在普通零食中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"feel good knowing","meaning":"知道……而感到安心","examples":[{"en":"They feel good knowing that a farmer probably received a fair price.","zh":"他們知道一位農民很可能得到公平價錢，因此感到安心。"},{"en":"To feel good knowing something means to feel pleased or reassured because of that information.","zh":"知道某事而感到安心，指因該資訊而感到高興或放心。"},{"en":"A student may feel good knowing their donation helped buy books for younger children.","zh":"學生知道自己的捐款幫助較年幼孩子買書，可能感到安心。"},{"en":"If consumers believe their money helps workers, they may feel better about buying.","zh":"如果消費者相信自己的金錢幫助工人，購買時可能感覺更好。"},{"en":"The phrase links knowledge with a positive emotional feeling.","zh":"這個短語把知識與正面情感連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"receive a good price","meaning":"獲得合理價錢","examples":[{"en":"A farmer somewhere probably received a good price for the product.","zh":"某地一位農民很可能因該產品獲得合理價錢。"},{"en":"To receive a good price means to be paid a fair or satisfactory amount for something sold.","zh":"獲得合理價錢，指售出某物時得到公平或令人滿意的款項。"},{"en":"A fruit seller receives a good price when customers pay enough to cover work and costs.","zh":"當顧客付足以覆蓋工作和成本的款項，水果小販就獲得合理價錢。"},{"en":"If farmers receive good prices, they can support their families and continue farming.","zh":"如果農民獲得合理價錢，就可以養活家人並繼續務農。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on fair payment to producers.","zh":"這個短語強調給生產者公平報酬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stay alive","meaning":"維持生命","examples":[{"en":"Food is something people need to stay alive.","zh":"食物是人們維持生命所需要的東西。"},{"en":"To stay alive means to continue living.","zh":"維持生命，指繼續生存。"},{"en":"People need water, food, and air to stay alive.","zh":"人們需要水、食物和空氣來維持生命。"},{"en":"If farmers cannot earn enough, the people who grow essential food may suffer.","zh":"如果農民不能賺取足夠收入，種植必需食物的人可能受苦。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds readers that food is not a luxury but a basic need.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者，食物不是奢侈品，而是基本需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pay farmers well","meaning":"給農民合理報酬","examples":[{"en":"Emma believes that paying farmers well is really important.","zh":"Emma 相信給農民合理報酬非常重要。"},{"en":"To pay farmers well means to give farmers fair money for the food or crops they produce.","zh":"給農民合理報酬，指為他們生產的食物或農作物支付公平金錢。"},{"en":"A school can pay farmers well by buying local produce at fair prices.","zh":"學校可以透過以公平價錢購買本地農產品，給農民合理報酬。"},{"en":"If farmers are paid well, they are less likely to be trapped in poverty.","zh":"如果農民獲得合理報酬，就較不容易陷入貧窮。"},{"en":"The phrase connects consumer choices with producers’ living conditions.","zh":"這個短語把消費者選擇與生產者生活條件連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"unprocessed food","meaning":"未經加工的食物","examples":[{"en":"Without unprocessed food, people would rely too much on sweets.","zh":"沒有未經加工的食物，人們就會過度依賴糖果。"},{"en":"Unprocessed food is food that has not been heavily changed in a factory.","zh":"未經加工的食物，是沒有在工廠中被大幅改變的食物。"},{"en":"Fresh fruit, vegetables, eggs, and plain rice are examples of unprocessed or lightly processed food.","zh":"新鮮水果、蔬菜、雞蛋和白飯都是未經加工或輕度加工食物的例子。"},{"en":"If people eat only processed snacks, their diet may lack real nutrients.","zh":"如果人們只吃加工零食，飲食可能缺乏真正營養。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts natural basic food with highly manufactured food.","zh":"這個短語把天然基本食物與高度製造食品作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"live on","meaning":"以……為主要食物","examples":[{"en":"Without real food, people would be living on candy.","zh":"沒有真正食物，人們就會以糖果為主要食物。"},{"en":"To live on a type of food means to eat mainly that food to survive or get through daily life.","zh":"以某類食物為生，指主要吃那種食物來生存或度日。"},{"en":"A busy student should not live on instant noodles during exam week.","zh":"忙碌學生不應在考試週以即食麵為主要食物。"},{"en":"If people live on sweets, their health and energy may become worse.","zh":"如果人們以甜食為主，健康和能量可能變差。"},{"en":"The phrase describes depending on one kind of food too heavily.","zh":"這個短語描述過度依賴一種食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"eating morally","meaning":"有道德地飲食","examples":[{"en":"Eating morally is becoming a priority for teenagers and young adults.","zh":"有道德地飲食正成為青少年和年輕成年人的優先事項。"},{"en":"Eating morally means choosing food in a way that considers fairness, workers, animals, and the environment.","zh":"有道德地飲食，指以考慮公平、工人、動物和環境的方式選擇食物。"},{"en":"A student eats morally when they buy a snack that supports farmers fairly.","zh":"學生購買公平支持農民的小食時，就是有道德地飲食。"},{"en":"If people eat morally, companies may feel pressure to improve how food is produced.","zh":"如果人們有道德地飲食，公司可能感到壓力去改善食物生產方式。"},{"en":"The phrase turns eating into an ethical decision, not just a personal taste.","zh":"這個短語把飲食變成道德決定，而不只是個人口味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"become a priority for","meaning":"成為……的優先事項","examples":[{"en":"Ethical food choices are becoming a priority for young consumers.","zh":"道德食物選擇正成為年輕消費者的優先事項。"},{"en":"To become a priority for someone means to become something they consider important and deal with first.","zh":"成為某人的優先事項，指變成他們認為重要並先處理的事情。"},{"en":"Saving money may become a priority for students who want to study abroad.","zh":"對想出國讀書的學生來說，儲錢可能成為優先事項。"},{"en":"If ethical buying becomes a priority, young people may check labels before buying snacks.","zh":"如果道德購買成為優先事項，年輕人買小食前可能會檢查標籤。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a shift in importance.","zh":"這個短語顯示重要性的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"teenagers as well as adults","meaning":"青少年以及成年人","examples":[{"en":"Eating morally matters to teenagers as well as adults in their early 20s.","zh":"有道德地飲食對青少年以及二十歲出頭的成年人都重要。"},{"en":"Teenagers as well as adults means both teenagers and adults are included.","zh":"青少年以及成年人，指青少年和成年人兩個群體都包括在內。"},{"en":"Online safety concerns teenagers as well as adults because both groups use the internet daily.","zh":"網絡安全關乎青少年以及成年人，因為兩者都每天使用互聯網。"},{"en":"If both age groups care about ethical food, the movement can grow beyond schools.","zh":"如果兩個年齡群體都關心道德食物，運動就可以超越學校而擴大。"},{"en":"The phrase adds another group instead of limiting the idea to one group.","zh":"這個短語加入另一群體，而不是把想法限制於一群人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in their early 20s","meaning":"二十歲出頭","examples":[{"en":"Adults in their early 20s are also interested in ethical consumption.","zh":"二十歲出頭的成年人也對道德消費感興趣。"},{"en":"In their early 20s means aged about twenty to twenty-three.","zh":"二十歲出頭，指大約二十至二十三歲。"},{"en":"People in their early 20s may be university students, new workers, or recent graduates.","zh":"二十歲出頭的人可能是大學生、新入職員工或近期畢業生。"},{"en":"If ethical habits form in the early 20s, they may influence later adult spending.","zh":"如果道德習慣在二十歲出頭形成，可能影響日後成年消費。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate age range.","zh":"這個短語給出約略年齡範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what began as","meaning":"起初是……的事物","examples":[{"en":"What began as a campus campaign has become a wider consumer movement.","zh":"起初是校園運動的事物，已成為更廣泛的消費者運動。"},{"en":"What began as something means something started in one form before changing into something larger or different.","zh":"起初是某物，指某事以一種形式開始，後來變成更大或不同的東西。"},{"en":"What began as a class project may become a school-wide recycling programme.","zh":"起初是班級項目的事情，可能變成全校回收計劃。"},{"en":"If a small campaign spreads, it can grow into a broader movement.","zh":"如果小型運動傳播開去，就可以發展成更廣泛運動。"},{"en":"The phrase shows development from a small beginning.","zh":"這個短語顯示由小開始的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a decade ago","meaning":"十年前","examples":[{"en":"The campaign began about a decade ago on college campuses.","zh":"該運動約十年前在大學校園開始。"},{"en":"A decade ago means about ten years before now or before the time being discussed.","zh":"十年前，指距今或距正在討論的時間約十年之前。"},{"en":"A school building built a decade ago may already need repairs.","zh":"十年前建成的校舍可能已經需要維修。"},{"en":"If a movement began a decade ago, it has had time to spread and mature.","zh":"如果運動十年前開始，它就有時間傳播和成熟。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a ten-year time frame.","zh":"這個短語給出十年時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"college campuses","meaning":"大學校園","examples":[{"en":"Ethical consumer campaigns first gained strength on college campuses.","zh":"道德消費運動最初在大學校園壯大。"},{"en":"College campuses are the grounds and buildings of universities or colleges.","zh":"大學校園，是大學或學院的土地和建築群。"},{"en":"College campuses often have cafeterias, libraries, dormitories, and student clubs.","zh":"大學校園通常有餐廳、圖書館、宿舍和學生組織。"},{"en":"If a movement grows on campuses, student networks can spread it quickly.","zh":"如果運動在校園中成長，學生網絡可以迅速傳播它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to university spaces where young adults study and organise.","zh":"這個短語指年輕成年人學習和組織活動的大學空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"avoid clothing made in","meaning":"避免購買在……製造的衣服","examples":[{"en":"Students campaigned to avoid clothing made in overseas sweatshops.","zh":"學生發起運動，避免購買在海外血汗工場製造的衣服。"},{"en":"To avoid clothing made in a place means to choose not to buy clothes produced there.","zh":"避免購買在某地製造的衣服，指選擇不買在那裡生產的衣服。"},{"en":"A shopper may avoid clothing made in factories known for unsafe conditions.","zh":"購物者可能避免購買在以危險環境聞名的工廠製造的衣服。"},{"en":"If many buyers avoid certain products, companies may investigate their supply chains.","zh":"如果許多買家避免某些產品，公司可能調查其供應鏈。"},{"en":"The phrase connects buying choices with production conditions.","zh":"這個短語把購買選擇與生產條件連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"overseas sweatshops","meaning":"海外血汗工場","examples":[{"en":"Some students avoided clothing made in overseas sweatshops.","zh":"一些學生避免購買在海外血汗工場製造的衣服。"},{"en":"Overseas sweatshops are factories in other countries where workers may be paid poorly and treated unfairly.","zh":"海外血汗工場，是其他國家中工人可能被低薪和不公平對待的工廠。"},{"en":"A brand may be criticised if its shirts are made in overseas sweatshops.","zh":"如果品牌的襯衫由海外血汗工場製造，可能受到批評。"},{"en":"If sweatshop labour is exposed, consumers may demand fairer working conditions.","zh":"如果血汗工場勞工被揭露，消費者可能要求更公平工作條件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unfair factory labour abroad.","zh":"這個短語描述海外不公平工廠勞動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"give birth to","meaning":"催生；產生","examples":[{"en":"The anti-sweatshop campaign gave birth to a similar movement in food and drink.","zh":"反血汗工場運動催生了食品和飲品方面的類似運動。"},{"en":"To give birth to an idea or movement means to produce or lead to it.","zh":"催生某想法或運動，指產生或導致它出現。"},{"en":"A small recycling club can give birth to a larger school environmental campaign.","zh":"小型回收學會可以催生更大型的學校環保運動。"},{"en":"If one ethical campaign succeeds, it may inspire another area of consumer activism.","zh":"如果一個道德運動成功，它可能啟發另一範疇的消費者行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one movement creating another.","zh":"這個短語描述一個運動產生另一個運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a parallel phenomenon","meaning":"類似現象；平行現象","examples":[{"en":"A parallel phenomenon has appeared in the food and beverage industries.","zh":"食品及飲品行業出現了類似現象。"},{"en":"A parallel phenomenon is a similar trend or situation happening in another area.","zh":"類似現象，是在另一範疇出現的相似趨勢或情況。"},{"en":"If students avoid unfair clothing and later avoid unfair coffee, the second trend is a parallel phenomenon.","zh":"如果學生先避免不公平服裝，後來避免不公平咖啡，第二種趨勢就是類似現象。"},{"en":"When similar values move into a new industry, the movement expands.","zh":"當相似價值進入新行業，運動就會擴展。"},{"en":"The phrase compares two related developments.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個相關發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"food and beverage industries","meaning":"食品及飲品行業","examples":[{"en":"Ethical buying has spread to the food and beverage industries.","zh":"道德購買已傳播到食品及飲品行業。"},{"en":"The food and beverage industries are businesses that produce, sell, or serve food and drinks.","zh":"食品及飲品行業，是生產、銷售或供應食物和飲品的企業。"},{"en":"Restaurants, coffee companies, snack brands, and drink makers belong to these industries.","zh":"餐廳、咖啡公司、零食品牌和飲品製造商都屬於這些行業。"},{"en":"If ethical buying reaches food and drinks, daily consumption becomes part of activism.","zh":"如果道德購買進入食物和飲品，日常消費就成為行動主義的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the commercial world of eating and drinking.","zh":"這個短語指飲食商業世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"youthful shoppers","meaning":"年輕購物者","examples":[{"en":"Youthful shoppers are using their money to support ethical goals.","zh":"年輕購物者正在用自己的金錢支持道德目標。"},{"en":"Youthful shoppers are young consumers, usually teenagers or young adults.","zh":"年輕購物者，是年輕消費者，通常指青少年或年輕成年人。"},{"en":"Youthful shoppers may choose Fair Trade chocolate instead of cheaper ordinary snacks.","zh":"年輕購物者可能選擇公平貿易朱古力，而不是較便宜的普通零食。"},{"en":"If youthful shoppers demand ethical products, companies may market more responsibly.","zh":"如果年輕購物者要求道德產品，公司可能更負責任地推廣。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights young people as consumers with influence.","zh":"這個短語突出年輕人作為有影響力的消費者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"leverage their dollars","meaning":"運用自己的金錢影響局面","examples":[{"en":"Youthful shoppers are leveraging their dollars to influence companies.","zh":"年輕購物者正在運用自己的金錢影響公司。"},{"en":"To leverage their dollars means to use their spending power to create influence.","zh":"運用自己的金錢影響局面，指使用消費能力來創造影響力。"},{"en":"Students leverage their dollars when they buy from shops that treat workers fairly.","zh":"當學生向公平對待工人的商店購物，就是運用金錢影響局面。"},{"en":"If enough consumers spend money ethically, businesses may change their practices.","zh":"如果足夠消費者以道德方式花錢，企業可能改變做法。"},{"en":"The phrase shows money being used as a form of pressure.","zh":"這個短語顯示金錢被用作壓力形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in a bid to","meaning":"為了；試圖","examples":[{"en":"Consumers are changing their purchases in a bid to reduce environmental harm.","zh":"消費者正在改變購買選擇，試圖減少環境傷害。"},{"en":"In a bid to means in an attempt to achieve something.","zh":"為了，指嘗試達成某事。"},{"en":"A school may ban plastic bottles in a bid to reduce waste.","zh":"學校可能禁止膠樽，以試圖減少廢物。"},{"en":"If shoppers change brands in a bid to support farmers, their purchases become political.","zh":"如果購物者為了支持農民而轉換品牌，他們的購買就變得具政治和社會意義。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the purpose behind an action.","zh":"這個短語引入行動背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reduce pesticide usage","meaning":"減少殺蟲劑使用","examples":[{"en":"Young shoppers want to reduce pesticide usage through their purchases.","zh":"年輕購物者想透過購買選擇減少殺蟲劑使用。"},{"en":"To reduce pesticide usage means to lower the amount of chemicals used to kill pests on crops.","zh":"減少殺蟲劑使用，指降低農作物上用來殺害害蟲的化學物質用量。"},{"en":"A family may buy organic vegetables to reduce pesticide usage in farming.","zh":"家庭可能購買有機蔬菜，以減少農業中的殺蟲劑使用。"},{"en":"If fewer pesticides are used, soil, water, and farm workers may be safer.","zh":"如果使用較少殺蟲劑，土壤、水源和農場工人可能更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase connects food choices with environmental protection.","zh":"這個短語把食物選擇與環境保護連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"limit deforestation","meaning":"限制森林砍伐","examples":[{"en":"Ethical shoppers try to limit deforestation by choosing responsible products.","zh":"道德購物者透過選擇負責任產品，嘗試限制森林砍伐。"},{"en":"To limit deforestation means to reduce the cutting down of forests.","zh":"限制森林砍伐，指減少砍伐森林。"},{"en":"A shopper may choose recycled paper to help limit deforestation.","zh":"購物者可能選擇再造紙，以幫助限制森林砍伐。"},{"en":"If companies avoid clearing forests for farms, wildlife and local communities are better protected.","zh":"如果公司避免為農場清除森林，野生動物和本地社區會得到更好保護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reducing harm to forests.","zh":"這個短語描述減少對森林的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"make sure that","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Consumers want to make sure that farmers are treated fairly.","zh":"消費者想確保農民受到公平對待。"},{"en":"To make sure that something happens means to check or act so it really happens.","zh":"確保某事發生，指檢查或採取行動，令它真的發生。"},{"en":"Parents make sure that children bring water before a sports day.","zh":"家長會確保孩子在運動日前帶水。"},{"en":"If consumers check labels, they may make sure that producers receive fairer treatment.","zh":"如果消費者檢查標籤，可能確保生產者受到較公平對待。"},{"en":"The phrase shows active care, not passive hope.","zh":"這個短語顯示主動關心，而不是被動希望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be left with a pittance","meaning":"只剩下微薄收入","examples":[{"en":"Young shoppers do not want farmers to be left with a pittance on payday.","zh":"年輕購物者不希望農民在收款時只剩下微薄收入。"},{"en":"To be left with a pittance means to receive only a very small and unfair amount of money.","zh":"只剩下微薄收入，指只得到非常少且不公平的金錢。"},{"en":"A worker may be left with a pittance after high fees are taken from their wages.","zh":"如果高昂費用從工資中扣除，工人可能只剩下微薄收入。"},{"en":"If farmers receive only a pittance, they may not afford food, school, or tools.","zh":"如果農民只得到微薄收入，可能負擔不起食物、學費或工具。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights unfairly low payment.","zh":"這個短語突出不公平的低收入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on payday","meaning":"發薪日；收款時","examples":[{"en":"Farmers should not receive only a pittance on payday.","zh":"農民不應在收款時只得到微薄收入。"},{"en":"On payday means on the day when someone is paid for their work or goods.","zh":"發薪日或收款時，指某人因工作或貨物而收到款項的日子。"},{"en":"Workers may pay rent or buy groceries on payday.","zh":"工人可能在發薪日交租或買日用品。"},{"en":"If someone earns too little on payday, the whole month may become difficult.","zh":"如果某人在收款時賺得太少，整個月可能都很困難。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the moment payment is received.","zh":"這個短語指收到款項的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"once again","meaning":"再一次","examples":[{"en":"Once again, college campuses are setting the pace.","zh":"再一次，大學校園正在引領步伐。"},{"en":"Once again means one more time, especially when something has happened before.","zh":"再一次，指又一次，尤其是某事以前已發生過。"},{"en":"Once again, the school library became crowded before exams.","zh":"再一次，學校圖書館在考試前變得擠迫。"},{"en":"If college students led one movement before and now lead another, the pattern repeats.","zh":"如果大學生以前領導一場運動，現在又領導另一場，模式就重複。"},{"en":"The phrase signals repetition of a familiar role or event.","zh":"這個短語表示熟悉角色或事件再次出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"set the pace","meaning":"帶頭；引領步伐","examples":[{"en":"College campuses are setting the pace for ethical consumption.","zh":"大學校園正在引領道德消費的步伐。"},{"en":"To set the pace means to lead others by moving first or setting a strong example.","zh":"帶頭或引領步伐，指先行動或樹立強有力榜樣來帶領他人。"},{"en":"A top student can set the pace when they start revising early and others follow.","zh":"尖子提早開始溫習而其他人跟隨時，就可以帶頭。"},{"en":"If colleges adopt Fair Trade products first, other schools may copy them later.","zh":"如果大學先採用公平貿易產品，其他學校可能之後仿效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes leadership through example.","zh":"這個短語描述透過榜樣來領導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"persuade administrators to","meaning":"說服行政人員去","examples":[{"en":"Students have persuaded administrators to buy Fair Trade coffee.","zh":"學生已說服行政人員購買公平貿易咖啡。"},{"en":"To persuade administrators to do something means to convince school or organisation leaders to take action.","zh":"說服行政人員去做某事，指令學校或組織領導相信並採取行動。"},{"en":"Students may persuade administrators to add recycling bins by showing waste data.","zh":"學生可能透過展示廢物數據，說服行政人員增設回收箱。"},{"en":"If students present strong reasons, administrators may change purchasing policies.","zh":"如果學生提出有力理由，行政人員可能改變採購政策。"},{"en":"The phrase shows student influence over institutional decisions.","zh":"這個短語顯示學生對機構決定的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cafeteria coffee","meaning":"學校餐廳咖啡","examples":[{"en":"Some students want all cafeteria coffee to carry a Fair Trade label.","zh":"有些學生希望所有學校餐廳咖啡都附有公平貿易標籤。"},{"en":"Cafeteria coffee is coffee sold or served in a school, college, or workplace cafeteria.","zh":"學校餐廳咖啡，是在學校、大學或工作場所餐廳售賣或供應的咖啡。"},{"en":"A teacher may buy cafeteria coffee before morning lessons.","zh":"老師可能在早課前購買學校餐廳咖啡。"},{"en":"If cafeteria coffee becomes Fair Trade, many daily purchases support fairer pay.","zh":"如果餐廳咖啡變成公平貿易產品，許多日常購買就會支持更公平薪酬。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to ordinary coffee bought in an institutional dining place.","zh":"這個短語指在機構餐飲場所購買的普通咖啡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"come with a label","meaning":"附有標籤","examples":[{"en":"The coffee comes with a Fair Trade label.","zh":"這款咖啡附有公平貿易標籤。"},{"en":"To come with a label means to have a label attached or printed on the product.","zh":"附有標籤，指產品上有附上或印上的標籤。"},{"en":"A shirt may come with a label showing washing instructions.","zh":"襯衫可能附有顯示洗滌指示的標籤。"},{"en":"If food comes with an ethical label, shoppers can identify its production standards more easily.","zh":"如果食物附有道德標籤，購物者可以更容易識別其生產標準。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visible information attached to a product.","zh":"這個短語描述產品上附着的可見資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Fair Trade label","meaning":"公平貿易標籤","examples":[{"en":"A Fair Trade label means producers were paid more fairly.","zh":"公平貿易標籤表示生產者獲得較公平報酬。"},{"en":"A Fair Trade label is a mark showing that producers received fairer pay and better trading conditions.","zh":"公平貿易標籤，是顯示生產者獲得較公平報酬和較好貿易條件的標記。"},{"en":"A chocolate bar with a Fair Trade label may support cocoa farmers more fairly.","zh":"附有公平貿易標籤的朱古力條，可能更公平地支持可可農。"},{"en":"If consumers trust the label, they may choose that product over a cheaper one.","zh":"如果消費者信任該標籤，可能選擇該產品而非較便宜產品。"},{"en":"The phrase connects product packaging with ethical standards.","zh":"這個短語把產品包裝與道德標準連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bean pickers","meaning":"咖啡豆採摘工人","examples":[{"en":"Bean pickers in Latin America and Africa were paid above the usual rates.","zh":"拉丁美洲和非洲的咖啡豆採摘工人獲得高於通常水平的工資。"},{"en":"Bean pickers are workers who harvest coffee beans or similar crops by hand.","zh":"咖啡豆採摘工人，是用人手收割咖啡豆或類似農作物的工人。"},{"en":"Bean pickers may work long hours on farms during harvest season.","zh":"咖啡豆採摘工人可能在收成季節於農場長時間工作。"},{"en":"If bean pickers are paid fairly, the final coffee has a more ethical supply chain.","zh":"如果採摘工人得到公平報酬，最終咖啡就有更道德的供應鏈。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the workers behind everyday coffee.","zh":"這個短語強調日常咖啡背後的工人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Latin America","meaning":"拉丁美洲","examples":[{"en":"Fair Trade coffee supports bean pickers in Latin America.","zh":"公平貿易咖啡支持拉丁美洲的咖啡豆採摘工人。"},{"en":"Latin America refers to countries in Central and South America, and sometimes parts of the Caribbean, where Romance languages are spoken.","zh":"拉丁美洲指中美洲和南美洲國家，有時也包括加勒比部分地區，當地使用羅曼語族語言。"},{"en":"Coffee, cocoa, and bananas are produced in many parts of Latin America.","zh":"咖啡、可可和香蕉在拉丁美洲許多地方生產。"},{"en":"If Fair Trade supports farmers there, consumers far away can affect local livelihoods.","zh":"如果公平貿易支持當地農民，遠方消費者就能影響本地生計。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a major region in ethical food production.","zh":"這個短語指出道德食品生產中的重要地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"prevailing rates","meaning":"現行工資水平","examples":[{"en":"Fair Trade workers were paid more than the prevailing rates.","zh":"公平貿易工人的工資高於現行工資水平。"},{"en":"Prevailing rates are the usual pay levels or prices in a place or industry.","zh":"現行工資水平，是某地或某行業中的通常薪酬或價格水平。"},{"en":"A tutor may charge above the prevailing rate if they have special experience.","zh":"如果補習老師有特別經驗，可能收取高於現行水平的費用。"},{"en":"If workers earn above prevailing rates, their income is better than the local norm.","zh":"如果工人收入高於現行工資水平，其收入就比本地常態更好。"},{"en":"The phrase compares payment with the usual standard.","zh":"這個短語把付款與通常標準作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"their peers","meaning":"他們的同輩","examples":[{"en":"Their peers on many other campuses are pushing to follow suit.","zh":"許多其他校園中的同輩正努力推動仿效。"},{"en":"Their peers are people of a similar age, status, or situation.","zh":"他們的同輩，是年齡、身份或處境相似的人。"},{"en":"A student may be influenced by peers who join environmental clubs.","zh":"學生可能受加入環保學會的同輩影響。"},{"en":"If one group of students succeeds, their peers elsewhere may copy the action.","zh":"如果一組學生成功，其他地方的同輩可能複製該行動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to equals or people in the same social group.","zh":"這個短語指同等身份或同一社會群體的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"push to","meaning":"努力推動","examples":[{"en":"Students on other campuses are pushing to follow suit.","zh":"其他校園的學生正努力推動仿效。"},{"en":"To push to do something means to make strong efforts to achieve it.","zh":"努力推動做某事，指為達成它而作出強烈努力。"},{"en":"Parents may push to improve school lunches if children complain about food quality.","zh":"如果孩子投訴食物質素，家長可能努力推動改善學校午餐。"},{"en":"If students push hard enough, administrators may review purchasing rules.","zh":"如果學生推動得足夠強烈，行政人員可能檢討採購規則。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests active pressure and effort.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動施壓和努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"follow suit","meaning":"跟隨做法；仿效","examples":[{"en":"Students at other colleges are pushing to follow suit.","zh":"其他大學的學生正努力推動跟隨做法。"},{"en":"To follow suit means to do the same thing that another person or group has already done.","zh":"跟隨做法，指做另一人或群體已經做過的同一件事。"},{"en":"If one class starts recycling paper, other classes may follow suit.","zh":"如果一班開始回收紙張，其他班可能跟隨做法。"},{"en":"If a successful college adopts Fair Trade coffee, others may copy the policy.","zh":"如果一所成功大學採用公平貿易咖啡，其他大學可能仿效該政策。"},{"en":"The phrase describes imitation after an example is set.","zh":"這個短語描述在有榜樣後進行模仿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據","examples":[{"en":"Many campuses are pushing to follow suit, according to Students United for Fair Trade.","zh":"根據 Students United for Fair Trade，許多校園正推動仿效。"},{"en":"According to means based on information from a person, group, report, or source.","zh":"根據，指基於某人、團體、報告或來源的資料。"},{"en":"According to the school notice, the exam will start at nine.","zh":"根據學校通告，考試會在九點開始。"},{"en":"If a claim is introduced with “according to,” readers know where the information comes from.","zh":"如果主張以「根據」引入，讀者就知道資料從何而來。"},{"en":"The phrase signals source attribution.","zh":"這個短語表示資料來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"coffee is just the beginning","meaning":"咖啡只是開始","examples":[{"en":"Coffee is just the beginning of the ethical food movement.","zh":"咖啡只是道德食品運動的開始。"},{"en":"Coffee is just the beginning means coffee is only the first example, and more products will follow.","zh":"咖啡只是開始，指咖啡只是第一個例子，之後會有更多產品跟隨。"},{"en":"A school’s recycling bins may be just the beginning of a wider environmental plan.","zh":"學校的回收箱可能只是更廣泛環保計劃的開始。"},{"en":"If one ethical product succeeds, companies may expand into chocolate, fruit, and clothing.","zh":"如果一種道德產品成功，公司可能擴展到朱古力、水果和服裝。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a movement is growing beyond its first step.","zh":"這個短語暗示運動正超越第一步而成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"institutional food-service provider","meaning":"機構餐飲服務供應商","examples":[{"en":"Bon Appétit is an institutional food-service provider based in California.","zh":"Bon Appétit 是一家以加州為基地的機構餐飲服務供應商。"},{"en":"An institutional food-service provider is a company that supplies meals to schools, colleges, hospitals, or workplaces.","zh":"機構餐飲服務供應商，是向學校、大學、醫院或工作場所供應膳食的公司。"},{"en":"A university may hire an institutional food-service provider to run its cafeteria.","zh":"大學可能聘請機構餐飲服務供應商營運餐廳。"},{"en":"If such a provider changes its buying policy, many meals can become more ethical.","zh":"如果這類供應商改變採購政策，許多膳食可以變得更道德。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a company serving large organisations, not individual households.","zh":"這個短語指服務大型組織的公司，而不是個別家庭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be based in","meaning":"以……為基地","examples":[{"en":"Bon Appétit is based in California.","zh":"Bon Appétit 以加州為基地。"},{"en":"To be based in a place means to have the main office or main operations there.","zh":"以某地為基地，指主要辦公室或主要營運設在那裡。"},{"en":"A charity based in Hong Kong may still work with communities overseas.","zh":"以香港為基地的慈善機構，仍可能與海外社區合作。"},{"en":"If a company is based in one place, its influence can still reach many schools elsewhere.","zh":"如果公司以某地為基地，其影響仍可到達其他地方許多學校。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a home location for an organisation.","zh":"這個短語指出組織的所在地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rely on","meaning":"依靠；採用","examples":[{"en":"Bon Appétit relies on organic and locally grown produce.","zh":"Bon Appétit 採用有機和本地種植的農產品。"},{"en":"To rely on something means to depend on it for support or normal operation.","zh":"依靠某物，指依賴它來支援或正常運作。"},{"en":"Students rely on clear notes when preparing for exams.","zh":"學生準備考試時依靠清楚筆記。"},{"en":"If a food company relies on local produce, nearby farmers may benefit.","zh":"如果餐飲公司依靠本地農產品，附近農民可能受益。"},{"en":"The phrase shows dependence on a source or method.","zh":"這個短語顯示對來源或方法的依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"organic produce","meaning":"有機農產品","examples":[{"en":"The company uses organic produce in its food services.","zh":"該公司在餐飲服務中使用有機農產品。"},{"en":"Organic produce is fruit, vegetables, or other farm food grown without many synthetic chemicals.","zh":"有機農產品，是沒有使用許多合成化學物質種植的水果、蔬菜或其他農場食物。"},{"en":"A school cafeteria may serve organic produce to reduce pesticide exposure.","zh":"學校餐廳可能供應有機農產品，以減少接觸殺蟲劑。"},{"en":"If demand for organic produce rises, farmers may change how they grow crops.","zh":"如果有機農產品需求上升，農民可能改變種植方式。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to farm products grown under organic standards.","zh":"這個短語指按有機標準種植的農場產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"locally grown produce","meaning":"本地種植的農產品","examples":[{"en":"Bon Appétit relies on locally grown produce.","zh":"Bon Appétit 採用本地種植的農產品。"},{"en":"Locally grown produce is food grown near the place where it is sold or eaten.","zh":"本地種植的農產品，是在銷售或食用地點附近種植的食物。"},{"en":"A restaurant may buy locally grown produce from farms outside the city.","zh":"餐廳可能向城市外的農場購買本地種植的農產品。"},{"en":"If food is grown locally, transport may be shorter and farmers nearby may earn more.","zh":"如果食物在本地種植，運輸可能較短，附近農民可能賺得更多。"},{"en":"The phrase connects food with place and community.","zh":"這個短語把食物與地方和社區連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in each year since","meaning":"自……以來每年","examples":[{"en":"In each year since 2001, many colleges have contacted the company.","zh":"自2001年以來每年，許多大學都聯絡該公司。"},{"en":"In each year since a time means every year from that time until now or the period discussed.","zh":"自某時間以來每年，指由那時間到現在或討論期間的每一年。"},{"en":"In each year since joining the school, the student has entered the writing competition.","zh":"自加入學校以來每年，該學生都參加寫作比賽。"},{"en":"If colleges contacted the company every year, interest was continuous rather than temporary.","zh":"如果大學每年都聯絡該公司，興趣就是持續的，而不是暫時的。"},{"en":"The phrase shows repeated yearly action.","zh":"這個短語顯示每年重複的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bid on contracts","meaning":"競投合約","examples":[{"en":"More than 25 colleges have asked the company to bid on their contracts.","zh":"超過25所大學要求該公司競投其合約。"},{"en":"To bid on contracts means to offer a price or proposal in order to win work.","zh":"競投合約，指提出價格或方案，以爭取獲得工作。"},{"en":"A cleaning company may bid on a school contract by offering services and costs.","zh":"清潔公司可能透過提供服務和費用來競投學校合約。"},{"en":"If many colleges invite bids, they are seriously considering changing providers.","zh":"如果許多大學邀請競投，表示它們認真考慮更換供應商。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to competing for formal business agreements.","zh":"這個短語指競爭正式商業協議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"food-service contracts","meaning":"餐飲服務合約","examples":[{"en":"Colleges invited Bon Appétit to bid on food-service contracts.","zh":"大學邀請 Bon Appétit 競投餐飲服務合約。"},{"en":"Food-service contracts are formal agreements to provide meals or cafeteria services.","zh":"餐飲服務合約，是提供膳食或餐廳服務的正式協議。"},{"en":"A hospital may sign food-service contracts with companies that can feed patients and staff.","zh":"醫院可能與能為病人和員工供餐的公司簽訂餐飲服務合約。"},{"en":"If a contract requires ethical food, the provider must buy ingredients more carefully.","zh":"如果合約要求道德食物，供應商就必須更仔細採購食材。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to business agreements for serving food.","zh":"這個短語指供應食物的商業協議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"intentionally limit growth","meaning":"有意限制增長","examples":[{"en":"Bon Appétit intentionally limits its growth.","zh":"Bon Appétit 有意限制其增長。"},{"en":"To intentionally limit growth means to deliberately avoid expanding too quickly or too much.","zh":"有意限制增長，指故意避免擴張得太快或太大。"},{"en":"A small tutoring centre may intentionally limit growth to maintain teaching quality.","zh":"小型補習中心可能有意限制增長，以維持教學質素。"},{"en":"If a company grows too fast, it may lose control over standards.","zh":"如果公司增長太快，可能失去對標準的控制。"},{"en":"The phrase shows planned restraint, not failure.","zh":"這個短語顯示有計劃的克制，而不是失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"collegiate client list","meaning":"大學客戶名單","examples":[{"en":"The company’s collegiate client list has grown in recent years.","zh":"該公司的大學客戶名單近年有所增長。"},{"en":"A collegiate client list is the list of college or university customers served by a company.","zh":"大學客戶名單，是公司所服務的大學或學院客戶列表。"},{"en":"A food provider’s collegiate client list may include small colleges and large universities.","zh":"餐飲供應商的大學客戶名單可能包括小型學院和大型大學。"},{"en":"If the list grows, more campuses are choosing that company’s services.","zh":"如果名單增長，表示更多校園選擇該公司的服務。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on higher-education customers.","zh":"這個短語強調高等教育客戶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in that period","meaning":"在那段期間","examples":[{"en":"The client list grew from 58 to 71 in that period.","zh":"客戶名單在那段期間由58增至71。"},{"en":"In that period means during the time already mentioned.","zh":"在那段期間，指在剛才提到的時間內。"},{"en":"A school’s club membership may rise from 20 to 45 in that period.","zh":"學校學會會員人數可能在那段期間由20增至45。"},{"en":"If numbers increase in that period, the trend is measurable.","zh":"如果數字在那段期間增加，趨勢就是可量度的。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to a specific time span.","zh":"這個短語回指特定時間跨度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"become concerned with","meaning":"開始關心","examples":[{"en":"Students have become concerned with where their food comes from.","zh":"學生開始關心食物從哪裡來。"},{"en":"To become concerned with something means to start caring about it or paying attention to it.","zh":"開始關心某事，指開始在意或注意它。"},{"en":"Parents may become concerned with screen time when children sleep badly.","zh":"當孩子睡得差，家長可能開始關心螢幕時間。"},{"en":"If students learn about farming conditions, they may care more about food sources.","zh":"如果學生了解農業條件，就可能更關心食物來源。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a new area of worry or interest.","zh":"這個短語顯示新的憂慮或興趣範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"where their food was coming from","meaning":"食物來源","examples":[{"en":"Students are concerned with where their food is coming from.","zh":"學生關心自己的食物來源。"},{"en":"Where their food is coming from means the origin, farm, factory, or supply chain behind the food.","zh":"食物來源，指食物背後的原產地、農場、工廠或供應鏈。"},{"en":"A family may ask where their vegetables are coming from before buying them.","zh":"家庭購買蔬菜前，可能詢問它們來自哪裡。"},{"en":"If food comes from unfair farms, consumers may choose another product.","zh":"如果食物來自不公平農場，消費者可能選擇另一產品。"},{"en":"The phrase asks about the source and conditions behind food.","zh":"這個短語詢問食物背後的來源和條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prior to that","meaning":"在那之前","examples":[{"en":"Prior to that, students were more excited about sugared cereal.","zh":"在那之前，學生對加糖穀物早餐更感興奮。"},{"en":"Prior to that means before the time or change just mentioned.","zh":"在那之前，指在剛提到的時間或變化之前。"},{"en":"Prior to the new rule, students could eat lunch anywhere on campus.","zh":"在新規則之前，學生可以在校園任何地方吃午飯。"},{"en":"If students cared only about sweet food before, their new ethical concern marks a change.","zh":"如果學生以前只關心甜食，新的道德關注就標誌着改變。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts an earlier situation with a later one.","zh":"這個短語把較早情況與較後情況作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be excited to be getting","meaning":"因能得到……而興奮","examples":[{"en":"Students were excited to be getting sugared cereal.","zh":"學生因能得到加糖穀物早餐而興奮。"},{"en":"To be excited to be getting something means to feel happy because you will receive or have it.","zh":"因能得到某物而興奮，指因將會收到或擁有它而感到高興。"},{"en":"Children may be excited to be getting new books before the school year starts.","zh":"孩子在新學年開始前，可能因能得到新書而興奮。"},{"en":"If students are excited about sweet cereal, taste may matter more than ethics at that time.","zh":"如果學生對甜穀物感到興奮，當時味道可能比道德更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase shows anticipation and pleasure.","zh":"這個短語顯示期待和愉快。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sugared cereal","meaning":"加糖穀物早餐","examples":[{"en":"Students used to be excited about sugared cereal.","zh":"學生以前對加糖穀物早餐感到興奮。"},{"en":"Sugared cereal is breakfast cereal with added sugar, often sweet and popular with children.","zh":"加糖穀物早餐，是加入糖的早餐穀物，通常味甜並受孩子歡迎。"},{"en":"A child may choose sugared cereal because it tastes like dessert.","zh":"孩子可能選擇加糖穀物早餐，因為它吃起來像甜品。"},{"en":"If students move from sugared cereal to ethical food concerns, their priorities have changed.","zh":"如果學生由加糖穀物早餐轉向道德食物關注，他們的優先事項已改變。"},{"en":"The phrase represents ordinary sweet processed breakfast food.","zh":"這個短語代表普通甜味加工早餐食品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reach a younger set","meaning":"接觸較年輕的一群人","examples":[{"en":"Equal Exchange tried to reach a younger set that often does not drink coffee.","zh":"Equal Exchange 嘗試接觸較年輕、通常不喝咖啡的一群人。"},{"en":"To reach a younger set means to attract or communicate with a younger group of people.","zh":"接觸較年輕的一群人，指吸引或與較年輕群體溝通。"},{"en":"A museum may use games to reach a younger set of visitors.","zh":"博物館可能使用遊戲來接觸較年輕的訪客群。"},{"en":"If young people do not drink coffee, a Fair Trade company may offer chocolate instead.","zh":"如果年輕人不喝咖啡，公平貿易公司可能改為提供朱古力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adapting a message to younger consumers.","zh":"這個短語描述把信息調整給較年輕消費者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Fair Trade importer","meaning":"公平貿易進口商","examples":[{"en":"Equal Exchange is a Fair Trade importer.","zh":"Equal Exchange 是一家公平貿易進口商。"},{"en":"A Fair Trade importer buys products from producers under fairer trading conditions and brings them into a market.","zh":"公平貿易進口商，是以較公平貿易條件向生產者購買產品並把它們帶入市場的公司。"},{"en":"A Fair Trade importer may buy coffee or cocoa from farmers overseas.","zh":"公平貿易進口商可能向海外農民購買咖啡或可可。"},{"en":"If importers pay producers fairly, the supply chain becomes more ethical.","zh":"如果進口商公平支付生產者，供應鏈就變得更道德。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a business role in ethical international trade.","zh":"這個短語指道德國際貿易中的商業角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"roll out","meaning":"推出","examples":[{"en":"Equal Exchange rolled out a line of cocoa and chocolate bars.","zh":"Equal Exchange 推出一系列可可和朱古力條。"},{"en":"To roll out a product means to launch or introduce it to the market.","zh":"推出產品，指把產品發布或引入市場。"},{"en":"A school may roll out a new online homework system after testing it with one class.","zh":"學校可能先用一班測試後，推出新的網上功課系統。"},{"en":"If a company rolls out chocolate products, it is trying to reach new buyers.","zh":"如果公司推出朱古力產品，就是嘗試接觸新買家。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a planned public launch.","zh":"這個短語描述有計劃的公開發布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a line of cocoa","meaning":"一系列可可產品","examples":[{"en":"The company rolled out a line of cocoa in 2003.","zh":"該公司於2003年推出一系列可可產品。"},{"en":"A line of cocoa means a range or series of cocoa products sold by a company.","zh":"一系列可可產品，指公司售賣的一組或一系列可可產品。"},{"en":"A shop may introduce a line of teas with different flavours.","zh":"商店可能推出一系列不同口味的茶。"},{"en":"If a line of cocoa sells well, the company may add chocolate bars later.","zh":"如果一系列可可產品賣得好，公司可能後來加入朱古力條。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a product range, not one single item.","zh":"這個短語指產品系列，而不是單一物品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"chocolate bars","meaning":"朱古力條","examples":[{"en":"Equal Exchange introduced chocolate bars in 2004.","zh":"Equal Exchange 於2004年推出朱古力條。"},{"en":"Chocolate bars are solid pieces of chocolate sold as snacks.","zh":"朱古力條，是作為零食出售的固體朱古力。"},{"en":"Students may sell chocolate bars during a school fundraiser.","zh":"學生可能在學校籌款活動中售賣朱古力條。"},{"en":"If chocolate bars are Fair Trade, a simple snack can support cocoa farmers.","zh":"如果朱古力條是公平貿易產品，簡單小食也可以支持可可農。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a common packaged chocolate product.","zh":"這個短語指常見包裝朱古力產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"profits in both sectors","meaning":"兩個範疇的利潤","examples":[{"en":"Profits in both sectors have justified the project.","zh":"兩個範疇的利潤證明該項目值得推行。"},{"en":"Profits in both sectors means money earned in two different business areas.","zh":"兩個範疇的利潤，指在兩個不同商業範圍中賺得的金錢。"},{"en":"A company may see profits in both online sales and physical shops.","zh":"公司可能在網上銷售和實體店兩個範疇都有利潤。"},{"en":"If cocoa and chocolate both make money, the project appears commercially worthwhile.","zh":"如果可可和朱古力都賺錢，該項目看起來在商業上值得做。"},{"en":"The phrase compares financial success across two areas.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個範圍的財務成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"justify the project","meaning":"證明該項目值得推行","examples":[{"en":"The profits have justified the cocoa and chocolate project.","zh":"這些利潤證明可可和朱古力項目值得推行。"},{"en":"To justify the project means to show that the project was worth doing.","zh":"證明該項目值得推行，指顯示該項目值得做。"},{"en":"Strong exam improvement can justify a school’s new tutoring programme.","zh":"顯著考試進步可以證明學校新補習計劃值得推行。"},{"en":"If a project creates both profit and social value, people are more likely to support it.","zh":"如果項目同時創造利潤和社會價值，人們更可能支持它。"},{"en":"The phrase connects results with the reason for continuing an action.","zh":"這個短語把結果與繼續行動的理由連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"what is more","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"What is more, schools have contacted the firm for its products.","zh":"此外，學校已聯絡該公司購買其產品。"},{"en":"What is more introduces an additional point that strengthens what was just said.","zh":"此外，引入一個加強剛才內容的額外重點。"},{"en":"The programme is affordable; what is more, students enjoy using it.","zh":"該計劃價格合理；此外，學生喜歡使用它。"},{"en":"If profits are strong and schools are interested, the project looks even more successful.","zh":"如果利潤強勁而學校有興趣，項目看起來更加成功。"},{"en":"The phrase adds another supporting detail.","zh":"這個短語加入另一個支持細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dozens of schools","meaning":"數十間學校","examples":[{"en":"Dozens of schools have contacted Equal Exchange.","zh":"數十間學校已聯絡 Equal Exchange。"},{"en":"Dozens of schools means many schools, usually several tens of them.","zh":"數十間學校，指許多學校，通常是幾十間。"},{"en":"Dozens of schools may join a recycling campaign if the idea is easy to copy.","zh":"如果回收運動容易仿效，數十間學校可能加入。"},{"en":"If many schools contact a company, demand is broader than one campus.","zh":"如果許多學校聯絡一間公司，需求就不只限於一個校園。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a large but approximate number.","zh":"這個短語顯示大但約略的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"contact the firm","meaning":"聯絡該公司","examples":[{"en":"Schools contacted the firm to use its products.","zh":"學校聯絡該公司，以使用其產品。"},{"en":"To contact the firm means to communicate with the company by phone, email, letter, or another method.","zh":"聯絡該公司，指透過電話、電郵、信件或其他方法與公司溝通。"},{"en":"A school may contact a firm to ask about lunch delivery prices.","zh":"學校可能聯絡公司詢問午餐送遞價格。"},{"en":"If many schools contact the firm, the company may see a new market.","zh":"如果許多學校聯絡該公司，公司可能看見新市場。"},{"en":"The phrase describes starting communication with a business.","zh":"這個短語描述開始與企業溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"use its products in fundraisers","meaning":"在籌款活動中使用其產品","examples":[{"en":"Schools use the company’s products in fundraisers.","zh":"學校在籌款活動中使用該公司的產品。"},{"en":"To use its products in fundraisers means to sell or include the company’s goods in events that raise money.","zh":"在籌款活動中使用其產品，指在籌款活動中售賣或加入該公司的貨品。"},{"en":"A class may sell Fair Trade chocolate in a fundraiser for a school trip.","zh":"班級可能在為學校旅行籌款時售賣公平貿易朱古力。"},{"en":"If ethical products are used in fundraisers, students can raise money while teaching values.","zh":"如果道德產品被用於籌款，學生可以一邊籌錢，一邊傳遞價值。"},{"en":"The phrase connects selling goods with social or school fundraising.","zh":"這個短語把售賣貨品與社會或學校籌款連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"classroom teaching tools","meaning":"課堂教學工具","examples":[{"en":"The products can also be used as classroom teaching tools.","zh":"這些產品也可以用作課堂教學工具。"},{"en":"Classroom teaching tools are materials or objects used to help students learn.","zh":"課堂教學工具，是用來幫助學生學習的材料或物件。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a food label as a classroom teaching tool to explain supply chains.","zh":"老師可能用食物標籤作課堂教學工具，解釋供應鏈。"},{"en":"If Fair Trade chocolate is used in class, students can discuss farmers, prices, and ethics.","zh":"如果公平貿易朱古力被用於課堂，學生可以討論農民、價格和道德。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that products can teach ideas beyond their ordinary use.","zh":"這個短語顯示產品可以教授超出普通用途的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"agitate in the family","meaning":"在家庭中積極推動","examples":[{"en":"Kids often agitate in the family for eco-friendly practices.","zh":"孩子常在家庭中積極推動環保做法。"},{"en":"To agitate in the family means to actively push relatives to change their behaviour or support a cause.","zh":"在家庭中積極推動，指主動促使親人改變行為或支持某個主張。"},{"en":"A child may agitate in the family until everyone starts separating rubbish for recycling.","zh":"孩子可能在家庭中積極推動，直到人人開始分類垃圾回收。"},{"en":"If children keep reminding parents about the environment, household habits may change.","zh":"如果孩子不斷提醒父母注意環境，家庭習慣可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests energetic pressure inside the home.","zh":"這個短語暗示家庭內的積極施壓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"eco-friendly practices","meaning":"環保做法","examples":[{"en":"Children often encourage recycling and other eco-friendly practices.","zh":"孩子常鼓勵回收和其他環保做法。"},{"en":"Eco-friendly practices are actions that reduce harm to the environment.","zh":"環保做法，是減少對環境傷害的行動。"},{"en":"Using reusable bottles and turning off lights are simple eco-friendly practices.","zh":"使用可重用水樽和關燈都是簡單環保做法。"},{"en":"If families adopt eco-friendly practices, they can reduce waste and energy use.","zh":"如果家庭採用環保做法，就能減少廢物和能源使用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to daily habits that protect the environment.","zh":"這個短語指保護環境的日常習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a ripe audience","meaning":"成熟而合適的受眾","examples":[{"en":"Young people are a ripe audience for Fair Trade products.","zh":"年輕人是公平貿易產品成熟而合適的受眾。"},{"en":"A ripe audience is a group that is ready, suitable, and likely to respond well to an idea or product.","zh":"成熟而合適的受眾，是已準備好、適合並很可能對某想法或產品反應良好的群體。"},{"en":"Teenagers who care about climate change are a ripe audience for reusable products.","zh":"關心氣候變化的青少年，是可重用產品的合適受眾。"},{"en":"If a group already cares about ethics, Fair Trade marketing may work well with them.","zh":"如果某群體已經關心道德，公平貿易市場推廣可能對他們有效。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests the timing and audience are suitable.","zh":"這個短語暗示時間和受眾都合適。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"concerns of","meaning":"……的關注","examples":[{"en":"The concerns of young food shoppers reflect a broader idealism.","zh":"年輕食品購物者的關注反映更廣泛的理想主義。"},{"en":"The concerns of a group are the worries, interests, or issues that matter to them.","zh":"某群體的關注，是他們在意的憂慮、興趣或議題。"},{"en":"The concerns of parents may include safety, homework, and school fees.","zh":"家長的關注可能包括安全、功課和學費。"},{"en":"If young shoppers worry about farmers and forests, their choices become more ethical.","zh":"如果年輕購物者關心農民和森林，他們的選擇就變得更道德。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what a group cares about.","zh":"這個短語指出某群體關心甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in some ways","meaning":"在某些方面","examples":[{"en":"Their concerns seem in some ways to reflect earlier idealism.","zh":"他們的關注在某些方面似乎反映早期理想主義。"},{"en":"In some ways means partly or from certain points of view.","zh":"在某些方面，指部分地或從某些角度來看。"},{"en":"Online learning is, in some ways, more flexible than classroom learning.","zh":"網上學習在某些方面比課室學習更靈活。"},{"en":"If today’s students care about fairness like older activists did, the movements are partly similar.","zh":"如果今天學生像早期行動者一樣關心公平，這些運動就部分相似。"},{"en":"The phrase shows limited comparison, not complete sameness.","zh":"這個短語顯示有限比較，而不是完全相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reflect the idealism","meaning":"反映理想主義","examples":[{"en":"Young shoppers’ concerns reflect the idealism of previous generations.","zh":"年輕購物者的關注反映前幾代人的理想主義。"},{"en":"To reflect the idealism means to show hopes for a fairer or better world.","zh":"反映理想主義，指顯示對更公平或更好世界的希望。"},{"en":"A student campaign for cleaner air can reflect the idealism of young activists.","zh":"學生爭取更清潔空氣的運動，可以反映年輕行動者的理想主義。"},{"en":"If people buy ethically because they want justice, their shopping reflects ideals.","zh":"如果人們因想要公義而道德購物，他們的購物就反映理想。"},{"en":"The phrase links behaviour with hopeful values.","zh":"這個短語把行為與充滿希望的價值連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"previous generations","meaning":"前幾代人","examples":[{"en":"Previous generations joined boycotts in solidarity with farm workers.","zh":"前幾代人曾參與杯葛行動，以聲援農場工人。"},{"en":"Previous generations are people who lived or were young before the current generation.","zh":"前幾代人，是在現代一代之前生活或年輕的人。"},{"en":"Previous generations may have fought for rights that young people now take for granted.","zh":"前幾代人可能曾爭取今天年輕人視為理所當然的權利。"},{"en":"If today’s youth repeat older patterns of activism, they are linked to previous generations.","zh":"如果今天年輕人重複較早的行動主義模式，他們就與前幾代人連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase connects present behaviour with the past.","zh":"這個短語把當前行為與過去連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"join boycotts","meaning":"參與杯葛行動","examples":[{"en":"Earlier activists joined boycotts to support farm workers.","zh":"早期行動者參與杯葛行動，以支持農場工人。"},{"en":"To join boycotts means to take part in organised refusals to buy or use certain products or services.","zh":"參與杯葛行動，指參加有組織地拒絕購買或使用某些產品或服務。"},{"en":"Consumers may join boycotts against companies that mistreat workers.","zh":"消費者可能參與杯葛行動，反對虐待工人的公司。"},{"en":"If enough people join a boycott, a company may lose money and change policy.","zh":"如果足夠多人參與杯葛，公司可能損失金錢並改變政策。"},{"en":"The phrase describes protest through refusal to buy.","zh":"這個短語描述透過拒絕購買來抗議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in solidarity with","meaning":"聲援；支持","examples":[{"en":"Previous generations joined boycotts in solidarity with farm workers.","zh":"前幾代人參與杯葛行動，以聲援農場工人。"},{"en":"In solidarity with someone means acting to support them because you share or respect their struggle.","zh":"聲援某人，指因認同或尊重其困境而採取行動支持他們。"},{"en":"Students may wear a ribbon in solidarity with classmates affected by a disaster.","zh":"學生可能佩戴絲帶，聲援受災難影響的同學。"},{"en":"If consumers refuse unfair products, they show support for workers they may never meet.","zh":"如果消費者拒絕不公平產品，就是支持他們可能從未見過的工人。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses unity and support.","zh":"這個短語表達團結和支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"farm workers","meaning":"農場工人","examples":[{"en":"Boycotts were organised in solidarity with farm workers.","zh":"杯葛行動是為聲援農場工人而組織的。"},{"en":"Farm workers are people who work on farms, planting, picking, packing, or caring for crops and animals.","zh":"農場工人，是在農場工作，負責種植、採摘、包裝或照顧作物和動物的人。"},{"en":"Farm workers may pick fruit early in the morning before the weather becomes too hot.","zh":"農場工人可能清晨採摘水果，以避開太熱天氣。"},{"en":"If farm workers are paid badly, cheap food may hide unfair labour conditions.","zh":"如果農場工人工資很低，廉價食物可能隱藏不公平勞動條件。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the labour behind agricultural products.","zh":"這個短語指農產品背後的勞動者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be distinct in that","meaning":"其獨特之處在於","examples":[{"en":"Today’s efforts are distinct in that young consumers do not want to make sacrifices.","zh":"今天努力的獨特之處在於年輕消費者不想作出犧牲。"},{"en":"To be distinct in that means to be different because of a particular feature.","zh":"其獨特之處在於，指因某個特徵而不同。"},{"en":"This school is distinct in that students help design some lessons.","zh":"這所學校的獨特之處在於學生幫助設計部分課堂。"},{"en":"If a movement offers good products without sacrifice, it differs from older forms of activism.","zh":"如果一場運動提供好產品而不要求犧牲，它就不同於較舊形式的行動主義。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the specific reason something is different.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事不同的具體原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make sacrifices","meaning":"作出犧牲","examples":[{"en":"Youthful consumers say they do not want to make sacrifices.","zh":"年輕消費者說他們不想作出犧牲。"},{"en":"To make sacrifices means to give up comfort, money, time, or pleasure for a larger purpose.","zh":"作出犧牲，指為更大目的放棄舒適、金錢、時間或享受。"},{"en":"A student may make sacrifices by studying on weekends to prepare for an exam.","zh":"學生可能為準備考試而週末溫習，作出犧牲。"},{"en":"If ethical products are stylish and affordable, consumers feel they do not need to sacrifice quality.","zh":"如果道德產品有型又負擔得起，消費者會覺得不需要犧牲質素。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests giving something up.","zh":"這個短語暗示放棄某些東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"high-quality goods","meaning":"高質素商品","examples":[{"en":"Young consumers want high-quality goods that are ethically produced.","zh":"年輕消費者想要以道德方式生產的高質素商品。"},{"en":"High-quality goods are products that are well made, useful, attractive, or long-lasting.","zh":"高質素商品，是製作良好、有用、吸引或耐用的產品。"},{"en":"A backpack with strong zips and comfortable straps is a high-quality good.","zh":"拉鏈堅固、肩帶舒適的背包就是高質素商品。"},{"en":"If ethical goods are also high-quality, consumers have fewer reasons to reject them.","zh":"如果道德商品同時高質素，消費者就較少理由拒絕它們。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on product standard, not only moral value.","zh":"這個短語強調產品標準，而不只是道德價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"competitively priced goods","meaning":"價格具競爭力的商品","examples":[{"en":"They want competitively priced goods that do not exploit workers.","zh":"他們想要價格具競爭力且不剝削工人的商品。"},{"en":"Competitively priced goods are products sold at prices similar to or better than other products in the market.","zh":"價格具競爭力的商品，是以與市場其他產品相近或更好的價格出售的產品。"},{"en":"A café offers competitively priced drinks if students can afford them compared with nearby shops.","zh":"如果學生與附近商店相比負擔得起，咖啡店飲品就是價格具競爭力。"},{"en":"If ethical products are too expensive, fewer young consumers may buy them.","zh":"如果道德產品太昂貴，較少年輕消費者可能購買。"},{"en":"The phrase combines affordability with market comparison.","zh":"這個短語結合可負擔性與市場比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"require exploitation of","meaning":"需要剝削……","examples":[{"en":"They want goods that do not require exploitation of workers or the environment.","zh":"他們想要不需要剝削工人或環境的商品。"},{"en":"To require exploitation of someone or something means to depend on using them unfairly.","zh":"需要剝削某人或某物，指依賴不公平使用他們來完成。"},{"en":"A cheap shirt may require exploitation of workers if they are paid extremely low wages.","zh":"如果一件便宜襯衫的工人工資極低，就可能需要剝削工人。"},{"en":"If a product can be made fairly, buyers do not have to benefit from hidden harm.","zh":"如果產品可以公平製造，買家就不必從隱藏傷害中得益。"},{"en":"The phrase questions the human and environmental cost of goods.","zh":"這個短語質疑商品的人力和環境代價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"exploitation of workers","meaning":"剝削工人","examples":[{"en":"Ethical consumers object to the exploitation of workers.","zh":"道德消費者反對剝削工人。"},{"en":"Exploitation of workers means treating workers unfairly for profit, such as paying too little or making them work in unsafe conditions.","zh":"剝削工人，指為了利潤不公平對待工人，例如支付過低工資或令他們在不安全環境工作。"},{"en":"Long hours, low pay, and no breaks can be signs of exploitation of workers.","zh":"長工時、低工資和沒有休息可以是剝削工人的跡象。"},{"en":"If consumers reject exploitative goods, companies may improve labour conditions.","zh":"如果消費者拒絕剝削性商品，公司可能改善勞工條件。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights unfair treatment behind production.","zh":"這個短語突出產品生產背後的不公平待遇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"exploitation of the environment","meaning":"對環境的剝削","examples":[{"en":"They also object to the exploitation of the environment.","zh":"他們也反對對環境的剝削。"},{"en":"Exploitation of the environment means using natural resources in a harmful or careless way for profit.","zh":"對環境的剝削，指為了利潤以有害或粗心方式使用自然資源。"},{"en":"Cutting down forests for cheap products can be exploitation of the environment.","zh":"為廉價產品砍伐森林，可以是對環境的剝削。"},{"en":"If companies exploit land, water, or forests, future communities may suffer.","zh":"如果公司剝削土地、水源或森林，未來社區可能受苦。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unfair treatment of nature, not only people.","zh":"這個短語描述對自然的不公平對待，而不只是人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"gladly reward companies","meaning":"樂意回饋公司","examples":[{"en":"Young consumers will gladly reward companies that deliver ethical goods.","zh":"年輕消費者會樂意回饋能提供道德商品的公司。"},{"en":"To gladly reward companies means to willingly support them, usually by buying their products.","zh":"樂意回饋公司，指願意支持它們，通常是購買其產品。"},{"en":"Customers may reward a local shop by returning often when it treats staff well.","zh":"當本地商店善待員工，顧客可能透過經常光顧來回饋它。"},{"en":"If companies offer ethical and attractive products, young shoppers may buy from them again.","zh":"如果公司提供有道德又吸引的產品，年輕購物者可能再次購買。"},{"en":"The phrase shows positive consumer support.","zh":"這個短語顯示正面消費者支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deliver","meaning":"兌現承諾；做到","examples":[{"en":"They will reward companies that deliver on their promises.","zh":"他們會回饋能兌現承諾的公司。"},{"en":"To deliver means to do what was promised or expected.","zh":"兌現承諾，指做到承諾或預期的事情。"},{"en":"A tutor delivers when students receive clear feedback and improve.","zh":"如果補習老師提供清楚回饋並令學生進步，就是做到承諾。"},{"en":"If a brand promises fair trade but does not pay farmers fairly, it has failed to deliver.","zh":"如果品牌承諾公平貿易卻沒有公平支付農民，就是未能兌現。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on real performance, not just marketing words.","zh":"這個短語強調真實表現，而不只是市場宣傳語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"share this sentiment","meaning":"有同樣看法","examples":[{"en":"Summer Rayne Oakes shares this sentiment with many of her peers.","zh":"Summer Rayne Oakes 與許多同輩有同樣看法。"},{"en":"To share this sentiment means to have the same feeling, opinion, or attitude.","zh":"有同樣看法，指擁有相同感受、意見或態度。"},{"en":"Many students share the sentiment that school food should be healthier.","zh":"許多學生都有同樣看法，認為學校食物應更健康。"},{"en":"If many peers share the same view, it may become a generational attitude.","zh":"如果許多同輩有相同看法，它可能成為一代人的態度。"},{"en":"The phrase connects one person’s opinion with a wider group.","zh":"這個短語把一個人的意見與更廣泛群體連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hear it repeatedly from","meaning":"反覆從……聽到","examples":[{"en":"Oakes hears this sentiment repeatedly from her peers.","zh":"Oakes 反覆從同輩聽到這種看法。"},{"en":"To hear something repeatedly from people means to hear the same idea many times from them.","zh":"反覆從某些人聽到某事，指多次從他們那裡聽到同一想法。"},{"en":"A teacher may hear repeatedly from students that homework instructions are unclear.","zh":"老師可能反覆從學生聽到功課指示不清楚。"},{"en":"If an opinion is heard repeatedly, it may show a common concern.","zh":"如果某意見反覆被聽到，就可能顯示共同關注。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a pattern, not one isolated comment.","zh":"這個短語暗示一種模式，而不是孤立評論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"peers","meaning":"同輩","examples":[{"en":"Oakes hears similar opinions from her peers.","zh":"Oakes 從同輩聽到相似意見。"},{"en":"Peers are people of similar age, status, or social position.","zh":"同輩，是年齡、身份或社會位置相近的人。"},{"en":"Teenagers often listen closely to their peers when choosing clothes or music.","zh":"青少年在選衣服或音樂時，常很重視同輩意見。"},{"en":"If peers support ethical buying, one young person may feel encouraged to join.","zh":"如果同輩支持道德購買，某位年輕人可能受鼓勵加入。"},{"en":"The word refers to equals within a group.","zh":"這個詞指群體中的同等身份者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"recent college graduate","meaning":"近期大學畢業生","examples":[{"en":"Summer Rayne Oakes is a recent college graduate and fashion model.","zh":"Summer Rayne Oakes 是近期大學畢業生兼時裝模特兒。"},{"en":"A recent college graduate is someone who finished college or university not long ago.","zh":"近期大學畢業生，是不久前完成大學或學院課程的人。"},{"en":"A recent college graduate may be looking for a first full-time job.","zh":"近期大學畢業生可能正在尋找第一份全職工作。"},{"en":"If a recent graduate promotes ethical fashion, younger students may see activism as modern and stylish.","zh":"如果近期畢業生推廣道德時裝，較年輕學生可能把行動主義視為現代又有型。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a person just after higher education.","zh":"這個短語指出剛完成高等教育的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fashion model","meaning":"時裝模特兒","examples":[{"en":"Oakes works as a fashion model and promotes Fair Trade clothing.","zh":"Oakes 擔任時裝模特兒，並推廣公平貿易服裝。"},{"en":"A fashion model is a person who wears or presents clothes for designers, shops, or advertisements.","zh":"時裝模特兒，是為設計師、商店或廣告穿着或展示服裝的人。"},{"en":"A fashion model may appear in magazines, runway shows, or online campaigns.","zh":"時裝模特兒可能出現在雜誌、天橋表演或網上宣傳中。"},{"en":"If a model promotes Fair Trade clothing, ethical products may look more stylish to young consumers.","zh":"如果模特兒推廣公平貿易服裝，道德產品可能在年輕消費者眼中更有型。"},{"en":"The phrase connects the clothing industry with public image.","zh":"這個短語把服裝行業與公眾形象連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"promote stylish Fair Trade clothing","meaning":"推廣有型的公平貿易服裝","examples":[{"en":"Oakes promotes stylish Fair Trade clothing.","zh":"Oakes 推廣有型的公平貿易服裝。"},{"en":"To promote stylish Fair Trade clothing means to encourage people to buy clothes that are both attractive and ethically made.","zh":"推廣有型的公平貿易服裝，指鼓勵人購買既吸引又以道德方式製造的衣服。"},{"en":"A model may promote stylish Fair Trade clothing through photoshoots and public talks.","zh":"模特兒可能透過拍攝和公開演講推廣有型的公平貿易服裝。"},{"en":"If ethical clothing looks good, consumers may not feel they are making a sacrifice.","zh":"如果道德服裝看起來好，消費者就不會覺得自己在犧牲。"},{"en":"The phrase combines fashion appeal with social responsibility.","zh":"這個短語結合時尚吸引力與社會責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stand on its own","meaning":"本身有吸引力；靠自身質素站得住腳","examples":[{"en":"Oakes will not buy something unless it can stand on its own.","zh":"Oakes 不會購買任何不能靠自身質素站得住腳的東西。"},{"en":"If a product can stand on its own, it is good enough by itself without needing sympathy or excuses.","zh":"如果產品靠自身質素站得住腳，指它本身已足夠好，不需要同情或藉口。"},{"en":"A school project should stand on its own because of strong research, not just a pretty cover.","zh":"學校項目應憑扎實研究站得住腳，而不只是封面漂亮。"},{"en":"If Fair Trade clothing is unattractive or poor quality, ethics alone may not be enough.","zh":"如果公平貿易服裝不吸引或質素差，單靠道德可能不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase means the product must succeed by its own quality.","zh":"這個短語指產品必須憑自身質素成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"socially responsible","meaning":"具社會責任","examples":[{"en":"She will not buy poor-quality goods just because they are socially responsible.","zh":"她不會只因商品具社會責任，就購買質素差的商品。"},{"en":"Socially responsible means acting in a way that considers society, workers, communities, and the environment.","zh":"具社會責任，指行事時考慮社會、工人、社區和環境。"},{"en":"A socially responsible company may pay fair wages and reduce waste.","zh":"具社會責任的公司可能支付公平工資並減少廢物。"},{"en":"If a product is socially responsible but badly made, some consumers may still reject it.","zh":"如果產品具社會責任但製作差，一些消費者仍可能拒絕。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ethical behaviour beyond profit.","zh":"這個短語描述超越利潤的道德行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"come to terms with","meaning":"接受；面對","examples":[{"en":"Her generation has come to terms with being consumers.","zh":"她那一代已接受自己是消費者這個現實。"},{"en":"To come to terms with something means to accept and understand a reality, especially one that may be uncomfortable.","zh":"接受或面對某事，指接受並理解某個現實，尤其是可能令人不舒服的現實。"},{"en":"A student may come to terms with needing extra help after failing a test.","zh":"學生測驗不合格後，可能接受自己需要額外幫助。"},{"en":"If young people accept that they buy things, they can ask how to buy more responsibly.","zh":"如果年輕人接受自己會購物，就可以問如何更負責任地購買。"},{"en":"The phrase describes realistic acceptance.","zh":"這個短語描述現實地接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the fact that","meaning":"……這個事實","examples":[{"en":"Her generation accepts the fact that everyone buys things.","zh":"她那一代接受人人都會購買東西這個事實。"},{"en":"The fact that introduces something presented as true or real.","zh":"……這個事實，用來引入被呈現為真實或現實的事情。"},{"en":"Teachers must consider the fact that students learn at different speeds.","zh":"老師必須考慮學生學習速度不同這個事實。"},{"en":"If everyone buys things, consumption can become a place for ethical choices.","zh":"如果人人都會購物，消費就可以成為道德選擇的場所。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a reality that cannot be ignored.","zh":"這個短語突出不可忽視的現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"what are the consequences","meaning":"後果是甚麼","examples":[{"en":"She asks what the consequences are when she buys food.","zh":"她問自己購買食物時後果是甚麼。"},{"en":"What are the consequences asks what results or effects will follow from an action.","zh":"後果是甚麼，是問某行動之後會有甚麼結果或影響。"},{"en":"A student should ask what the consequences are before skipping homework.","zh":"學生逃避功課前，應問後果是甚麼。"},{"en":"If buying cheap food harms farmers, the consequences of shopping are ethical as well as personal.","zh":"如果購買廉價食物傷害農民，購物的後果就既是道德的，也是個人的。"},{"en":"The phrase encourages people to think beyond the immediate action.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵人思考即時行動以外的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ameliorate the world’s big problems","meaning":"改善世界上的重大問題","examples":[{"en":"Many young people want to ameliorate the world’s big problems.","zh":"許多年輕人想改善世界上的重大問題。"},{"en":"To ameliorate the world’s big problems means to improve serious global issues, even if they cannot be solved completely at once.","zh":"改善世界上的重大問題，指令嚴重全球議題變得較好，即使不能一次完全解決。"},{"en":"Students may try to ameliorate hunger by volunteering at a food bank.","zh":"學生可能透過在食物銀行做義工來改善飢餓問題。"},{"en":"If young people feel powerless, small ethical actions may give them a way to help.","zh":"如果年輕人感到無力，小型道德行動可能給他們幫忙的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase means make major problems better, not magically remove them.","zh":"這個短語指令重大問題改善，而不是神奇地消除它們。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"feel ineffective","meaning":"感到無能為力","examples":[{"en":"Young people may feel ineffective because of their age.","zh":"年輕人可能因年紀而感到無能為力。"},{"en":"To feel ineffective means to feel unable to make a real difference or achieve results.","zh":"感到無能為力，指覺得自己無法帶來真正改變或達成效果。"},{"en":"A student may feel ineffective when adults ignore every suggestion they make.","zh":"當成年人忽視學生每個建議，學生可能感到無能為力。"},{"en":"If teenagers feel too young to vote or lead, buying ethically may feel like one available action.","zh":"如果青少年覺得自己太年輕，不能投票或領導，道德購買可能感覺像一種可行行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a feeling of limited power.","zh":"這個短語描述權力有限的感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"because of their age","meaning":"因為年紀","examples":[{"en":"Some teenagers feel powerless because of their age.","zh":"一些青少年因為年紀而感到無力。"},{"en":"Because of their age means due to how young or old they are.","zh":"因為年紀，指由於他們年輕或年長的程度。"},{"en":"A child may not be allowed to sign a contract because of their age.","zh":"孩子可能因為年紀而不被允許簽合約。"},{"en":"If teenagers cannot vote yet, they may look for other ways to influence society.","zh":"如果青少年還不能投票，可能尋找其他影響社會的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase gives age as the reason for a limitation.","zh":"這個短語把年齡作為限制的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"figure out","meaning":"弄清楚；理解","examples":[{"en":"Marketers are figuring out how teenagers respond to ethical products.","zh":"市場推廣人員正在弄清楚青少年如何回應道德產品。"},{"en":"To figure out something means to understand or solve it after thinking or studying.","zh":"弄清楚某事，指經思考或研究後理解或解決它。"},{"en":"A student may figure out a grammar rule after seeing several examples.","zh":"學生可能在看過幾個例子後弄清楚文法規則。"},{"en":"If marketers figure out what makes teenagers feel powerful, they can design stronger campaigns.","zh":"如果市場推廣人員弄清楚甚麼令青少年感到有力量，就能設計更有力宣傳。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests active problem-solving or understanding.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動解決問題或理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"resent this feeling of powerlessness","meaning":"厭惡這種無力感","examples":[{"en":"Teenagers resent this feeling of powerlessness.","zh":"青少年厭惡這種無力感。"},{"en":"To resent this feeling of powerlessness means to dislike or feel angry about being unable to influence things.","zh":"厭惡這種無力感，指不喜歡或因無法影響事情而感到憤怒。"},{"en":"Students may resent feeling powerless when school rules change without consultation.","zh":"當校規未經諮詢就改變，學生可能厭惡無力感。"},{"en":"If teenagers resent powerlessness, they may welcome products that make them feel involved.","zh":"如果青少年厭惡無力感，他們可能歡迎令自己感到參與其中的產品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes emotional resistance to having little control.","zh":"這個短語描述對缺乏控制的情緒抗拒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"push products","meaning":"推廣產品","examples":[{"en":"Marketers are pushing products that make young buyers feel powerful.","zh":"市場推廣人員正在推廣令年輕買家感到有力量的產品。"},{"en":"To push products means to promote or sell products actively and strongly.","zh":"推廣產品，指積極而強力地宣傳或銷售產品。"},{"en":"Shops may push products near exam season by advertising stationery and study snacks.","zh":"商店可能在考試季前推廣文具和學習小食。"},{"en":"If a product promises social impact, marketers may push it to idealistic teenagers.","zh":"如果產品承諾有社會影響，市場人員可能向理想主義青少年推廣它。"},{"en":"The phrase can suggest strong marketing pressure.","zh":"這個短語可以暗示強烈市場推廣壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make a difference","meaning":"帶來改變","examples":[{"en":"Young buyers want to feel as though they are making a difference.","zh":"年輕買家想感覺自己正在帶來改變。"},{"en":"To make a difference means to have a positive effect or help change a situation.","zh":"帶來改變，指產生正面影響或幫助改變情況。"},{"en":"A student can make a difference by helping a classmate understand homework.","zh":"學生可以透過幫同學理解功課來帶來改變。"},{"en":"If buying a product funds clean water, the consumer may feel their money matters.","zh":"如果購買產品能資助淨水，消費者可能覺得自己的金錢有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses meaningful impact.","zh":"這個短語表達有意義的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"contribute five cents from","meaning":"從……捐出五仙","examples":[{"en":"Ethos Water contributes five cents from every bottle sold.","zh":"Ethos Water 從每售出一瓶中捐出五仙。"},{"en":"To contribute five cents from each item means to donate that amount of money from each sale.","zh":"從每件商品捐出五仙，指每次銷售都捐出該金額。"},{"en":"A school shop may contribute one dollar from every notebook sold to a library fund.","zh":"學校商店可能從每本筆記簿售價中捐出一元給圖書館基金。"},{"en":"If many bottles are sold, small donations can add up to a larger amount.","zh":"如果售出很多瓶，小額捐款可以累積成較大金額。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a donation linked to each purchase.","zh":"這個短語顯示與每次購買連繫的捐款。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"every bottle sold","meaning":"每售出一瓶","examples":[{"en":"The company donates money from every bottle sold.","zh":"該公司從每售出一瓶中捐款。"},{"en":"Every bottle sold means each bottle that customers buy.","zh":"每售出一瓶，指顧客購買的每一瓶。"},{"en":"A charity drink may give ten cents from every bottle sold to a children’s hospital.","zh":"慈善飲品可能從每售出一瓶中捐出十仙給兒童醫院。"},{"en":"If sales increase, the total donation from every bottle sold also increases.","zh":"如果銷量增加，來自每售出一瓶的總捐款也會增加。"},{"en":"The phrase links each sale with a repeated action.","zh":"這個短語把每次銷售與重複行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"water-purification centres","meaning":"淨水中心","examples":[{"en":"Ethos Water supports water-purification centres in developing countries.","zh":"Ethos Water 支持發展中國家的淨水中心。"},{"en":"Water-purification centres are places that clean unsafe water so people can drink it safely.","zh":"淨水中心，是清潔不安全食水，使人能安全飲用的地方。"},{"en":"A village may need a water-purification centre if wells contain dirty water.","zh":"如果水井含有污水，村莊可能需要淨水中心。"},{"en":"If clean water becomes available, children may suffer fewer illnesses.","zh":"如果清潔食水變得可得，孩子可能較少生病。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to facilities that make water safe.","zh":"這個短語指令水變安全的設施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"developing countries","meaning":"發展中國家","examples":[{"en":"Water-purification centres are built in developing countries.","zh":"淨水中心建於發展中國家。"},{"en":"Developing countries are countries with lower average income and less developed infrastructure than wealthy industrialised nations.","zh":"發展中國家，是平均收入較低、基礎建設較富裕工業國家不成熟的國家。"},{"en":"Some developing countries need more investment in schools, roads, hospitals, and clean water.","zh":"一些發展中國家需要更多投資於學校、道路、醫院和清潔食水。"},{"en":"If clean-water projects reach developing countries, public health may improve.","zh":"如果淨水項目到達發展中國家，公共健康可能改善。"},{"en":"The phrase describes countries still building economic and social systems.","zh":"這個短語描述仍在建立經濟和社會系統的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"an easy way to","meaning":"……的簡單方法","examples":[{"en":"Buying bottled water is an easy way for young people to contribute.","zh":"購買樽裝水是年輕人作出貢獻的簡單方法。"},{"en":"An easy way to do something is a simple method that does not require much effort.","zh":"做某事的簡單方法，是不需要太多努力的簡單途徑。"},{"en":"Bringing a reusable bag is an easy way to reduce plastic waste.","zh":"帶可重用袋是減少塑膠廢物的簡單方法。"},{"en":"If activism feels too difficult, easy actions may help beginners get started.","zh":"如果行動主義感覺太困難，簡單行動可能幫助初學者開始。"},{"en":"The phrase presents a simple route into action.","zh":"這個短語呈現進入行動的簡單路線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"bottled water","meaning":"樽裝水","examples":[{"en":"Young people can contribute by buying bottled water.","zh":"年輕人可以透過購買樽裝水作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Bottled water is drinking water sold in plastic or glass bottles.","zh":"樽裝水，是用塑膠樽或玻璃樽出售的飲用水。"},{"en":"Students may buy bottled water after sports practice if they forget their own bottle.","zh":"如果學生忘記帶自己的水樽，運動練習後可能購買樽裝水。"},{"en":"If bottled water funds clean-water projects, the purchase is linked to charity.","zh":"如果樽裝水資助淨水項目，購買就與慈善連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a common everyday drink product.","zh":"這個短語指常見日常飲品產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"support global issues","meaning":"支持全球議題","examples":[{"en":"Some companies give young people ways to support global issues.","zh":"一些公司給年輕人支持全球議題的方法。"},{"en":"To support global issues means to help address problems affecting people across the world.","zh":"支持全球議題，指幫助處理影響世界各地人們的問題。"},{"en":"Students may support global issues by raising money for disaster relief or clean water.","zh":"學生可能透過為救災或淨水籌款來支持全球議題。"},{"en":"If a product funds overseas projects, buying it can feel connected to global action.","zh":"如果產品資助海外項目，購買它就可能感覺與全球行動有關。"},{"en":"The phrase links local choices with worldwide concerns.","zh":"這個短語把本地選擇與世界關注連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"get involved","meaning":"參與其中","examples":[{"en":"Buying ethical products is one way for young people to get involved.","zh":"購買道德產品是年輕人參與其中的一種方法。"},{"en":"To get involved means to take part in an activity, cause, or movement.","zh":"參與其中，指參加某活動、主張或運動。"},{"en":"A student may get involved in school recycling by joining the green team.","zh":"學生可以透過加入環保小組，參與學校回收工作。"},{"en":"If teenagers cannot vote, consumer choices may offer another way to participate.","zh":"如果青少年不能投票，消費選擇可能提供另一種參與方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving from interest to action.","zh":"這個短語描述由興趣轉為行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"appreciate that","meaning":"感激；欣賞","examples":[{"en":"Young consumers appreciate ways to support global issues.","zh":"年輕消費者欣賞支持全球議題的方法。"},{"en":"To appreciate something means to value it or feel grateful for it.","zh":"欣賞某事，指重視它或對它感到感激。"},{"en":"Students appreciate clear feedback because it tells them how to improve.","zh":"學生欣賞清楚回饋，因為它告訴他們如何改善。"},{"en":"If ethical products give young people a role, they may value that opportunity.","zh":"如果道德產品給年輕人一個角色，他們可能珍惜那個機會。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses positive recognition.","zh":"這個短語表達正面認同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"consumer activism","meaning":"消費者行動主義","examples":[{"en":"Convenience is also driving consumer activism.","zh":"方便性也正在推動消費者行動主義。"},{"en":"Consumer activism is social or political action carried out through buying, refusing to buy, or pressuring companies.","zh":"消費者行動主義，是透過購買、拒絕購買或向公司施壓而進行的社會或政治行動。"},{"en":"A boycott of an unfair brand is a form of consumer activism.","zh":"杯葛不公平品牌是一種消費者行動主義。"},{"en":"If shopping becomes a way to express values, ordinary consumers gain influence.","zh":"如果購物變成表達價值的方法，普通消費者就獲得影響力。"},{"en":"The phrase turns consumption into social action.","zh":"這個短語把消費變成社會行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"national coordinator","meaning":"全國統籌員","examples":[{"en":"Joe Curnow is the national coordinator of United Students for Fair Trade.","zh":"Joe Curnow 是 United Students for Fair Trade 的全國統籌員。"},{"en":"A national coordinator is a person who organises activities across a whole country.","zh":"全國統籌員，是在全國範圍組織活動的人。"},{"en":"A national coordinator may connect school clubs in different cities.","zh":"全國統籌員可能連接不同城市的學校學會。"},{"en":"If a movement grows nationwide, coordination helps local groups share plans.","zh":"如果運動在全國成長，統籌有助本地小組分享計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a leadership role at national level.","zh":"這個短語指出全國層面的領導角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"first get involved","meaning":"首次參與","examples":[{"en":"Joe Curnow first got involved while spending time in cafés.","zh":"Joe Curnow 首次參與，是在咖啡店消磨時間期間。"},{"en":"To first get involved means to begin taking part in a cause, group, or activity for the first time.","zh":"首次參與，指第一次開始參加某主張、團體或活動。"},{"en":"A student may first get involved in volunteering through a school service day.","zh":"學生可能透過學校服務日首次參與義工活動。"},{"en":"If the first experience feels meaningful, a person may stay active for years.","zh":"如果第一次經驗感覺有意義，一個人可能多年保持活躍。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the starting point of participation.","zh":"這個短語標示參與的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as a high schooler","meaning":"作為高中生","examples":[{"en":"She first got involved as a high schooler.","zh":"她作為高中生時首次參與。"},{"en":"As a high schooler means when she was a student at high school.","zh":"作為高中生，指當她是高中學生時。"},{"en":"As a high schooler, a teenager may join clubs, part-time work, or community projects.","zh":"作為高中生，青少年可能加入學會、兼職或社區項目。"},{"en":"If activism begins in high school, it can shape later university choices.","zh":"如果行動主義在高中開始，它可能塑造日後大學選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the life stage when something happened.","zh":"這個短語給出事情發生的人生階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"hang out in cafés","meaning":"在咖啡店消磨時間","examples":[{"en":"She spent time hanging out in cafés.","zh":"她花時間在咖啡店消磨時間。"},{"en":"To hang out in cafés means to spend relaxed social time in coffee shops.","zh":"在咖啡店消磨時間，指在咖啡店輕鬆地社交或逗留。"},{"en":"Students may hang out in cafés after school to talk, study, or use Wi-Fi.","zh":"學生放學後可能在咖啡店消磨時間，聊天、溫習或使用 Wi-Fi。"},{"en":"If teenagers spend time in cafés, coffee labels and shop values may influence them.","zh":"如果青少年在咖啡店消磨時間，咖啡標籤和店舖價值可能影響他們。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and describes casual social time.","zh":"這個短語較口語，描述輕鬆社交時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"eco-friendly label","meaning":"環保標籤","examples":[{"en":"Buying coffee with an eco-friendly label expressed her beliefs.","zh":"購買有環保標籤的咖啡表達了她的信念。"},{"en":"An eco-friendly label is a mark showing that a product is less harmful to the environment.","zh":"環保標籤，是顯示產品對環境傷害較少的標記。"},{"en":"A notebook with an eco-friendly label may be made from recycled paper.","zh":"有環保標籤的筆記簿可能由再造紙製成。"},{"en":"If a product carries such a label, shoppers may feel it matches their environmental values.","zh":"如果產品帶有這類標籤，購物者可能覺得它符合自己的環保價值。"},{"en":"The phrase connects product information with environmental responsibility.","zh":"這個短語把產品資訊與環境責任連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"express what someone believes in","meaning":"表達某人的信念","examples":[{"en":"Buying ethical coffee helped her express what she believed in.","zh":"購買道德咖啡幫助她表達自己的信念。"},{"en":"To express what someone believes in means to show their values through words or actions.","zh":"表達某人的信念，指透過言語或行動展示其價值觀。"},{"en":"A student may express what they believe in by joining a charity walk.","zh":"學生可能透過參加慈善步行來表達自己的信念。"},{"en":"If a purchase reflects someone’s values, shopping becomes a form of self-expression.","zh":"如果購買反映某人的價值觀，購物就成為自我表達的一種形式。"},{"en":"The phrase links belief with visible behaviour.","zh":"這個短語把信念與可見行為連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"for young teens","meaning":"對年輕青少年來說","examples":[{"en":"For young teens, consumption is often their first step into activism.","zh":"對年輕青少年來說，消費常是他們進入行動主義的第一步。"},{"en":"For young teens means from the perspective or situation of younger teenagers.","zh":"對年輕青少年來說，指從較年輕青少年的角度或處境而言。"},{"en":"For young teens, school clubs may be the safest way to try leadership.","zh":"對年輕青少年來說，學校學會可能是嘗試領導的最安全方法。"},{"en":"If young teens have limited political power, shopping choices may feel more accessible.","zh":"如果年輕青少年政治權力有限，購物選擇可能感覺更容易接觸。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on a particular age group.","zh":"這個短語聚焦特定年齡群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"consumption","meaning":"消費","examples":[{"en":"Consumption can be a first form of activism for teenagers.","zh":"消費可以是青少年第一種行動主義形式。"},{"en":"Consumption means buying and using goods or services.","zh":"消費，指購買和使用商品或服務。"},{"en":"A family’s weekly shopping is a form of consumption.","zh":"家庭每週購物是一種消費。"},{"en":"If consumption choices support fair companies, spending becomes socially meaningful.","zh":"如果消費選擇支持公平公司，花錢就變得有社會意義。"},{"en":"The word refers to what people buy and use.","zh":"這個詞指人們購買和使用的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"first foray into","meaning":"初次嘗試；首次涉足","examples":[{"en":"For young teens, consumption is their first foray into activism.","zh":"對年輕青少年來說，消費是他們首次涉足行動主義。"},{"en":"A first foray into something is a first attempt or first experience in a new area.","zh":"初次涉足某事，是在新範疇中的第一次嘗試或第一次經驗。"},{"en":"A student’s first foray into public speaking may be a short class presentation.","zh":"學生首次涉足公開演說，可能是一個短課堂匯報。"},{"en":"If ethical buying is a first foray into activism, it may lead to deeper involvement later.","zh":"如果道德購買是首次涉足行動主義，它日後可能帶來更深入參與。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an initial step into unfamiliar activity.","zh":"這個短語描述進入陌生活動的第一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"activism","meaning":"行動主義；社會行動","examples":[{"en":"Ethical consumption can introduce teenagers to activism.","zh":"道德消費可以把青少年引入行動主義。"},{"en":"Activism is action taken to support social, political, environmental, or moral change.","zh":"行動主義，是為支持社會、政治、環境或道德改變而採取的行動。"},{"en":"Students practise activism when they organise a petition for safer streets.","zh":"當學生為更安全街道組織請願，就是在實踐行動主義。"},{"en":"If activism begins with shopping, it may later grow into volunteering or campaigning.","zh":"如果行動主義由購物開始，日後可能發展成義工服務或倡議運動。"},{"en":"The word refers to active effort to change society.","zh":"這個詞指主動努力改變社會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"team up with","meaning":"與……合作","examples":[{"en":"Emma Lewis teamed up with classmates to sell Fair Trade products.","zh":"Emma Lewis 與同學合作售賣公平貿易產品。"},{"en":"To team up with people means to work together with them toward a shared goal.","zh":"與某人合作，指與他們一起為共同目標工作。"},{"en":"Students may team up with friends to prepare a debate.","zh":"學生可能與朋友合作準備辯論。"},{"en":"If classmates team up, they can organise a bigger fundraiser than one student alone.","zh":"如果同學合作，他們可以組織比單一學生更大的籌款活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cooperation.","zh":"這個短語描述合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"classmates","meaning":"同學","examples":[{"en":"Emma teamed up with classmates to organise a fundraiser.","zh":"Emma 與同學合作組織籌款活動。"},{"en":"Classmates are students who study in the same class or school group.","zh":"同學，是在同一班或學校小組中學習的學生。"},{"en":"Classmates may share notes, discuss homework, or work on projects together.","zh":"同學可能分享筆記、討論功課或一起做項目。"},{"en":"If classmates support one another, a small idea can become a group activity.","zh":"如果同學互相支持，小想法可以變成小組活動。"},{"en":"The word refers to fellow students.","zh":"這個詞指一起學習的學生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sell Fair Trade chocolate","meaning":"售賣公平貿易朱古力","examples":[{"en":"The students sold Fair Trade chocolate at a school fundraiser.","zh":"學生在學校籌款活動中售賣公平貿易朱古力。"},{"en":"To sell Fair Trade chocolate means to offer ethically certified chocolate for people to buy.","zh":"售賣公平貿易朱古力，指提供經道德認證的朱古力讓人購買。"},{"en":"A class may sell Fair Trade chocolate to raise money and teach buyers about farmers.","zh":"班級可能售賣公平貿易朱古力，以籌款並教買家認識農民。"},{"en":"If students sell ethical products, fundraising can also become education.","zh":"如果學生售賣道德產品，籌款也可以成為教育。"},{"en":"The phrase combines commerce, charity, and social values.","zh":"這個短語結合商業、慈善和社會價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"school fundraiser","meaning":"學校籌款活動","examples":[{"en":"The students sold Fair Trade products at a school fundraiser.","zh":"學生在學校籌款活動中售賣公平貿易產品。"},{"en":"A school fundraiser is an event where students, parents, or staff raise money for a school cause.","zh":"學校籌款活動，是學生、家長或員工為學校目的籌集金錢的活動。"},{"en":"A school fundraiser may include selling cakes, books, or handmade crafts.","zh":"學校籌款活動可能包括售賣蛋糕、書籍或手工藝品。"},{"en":"If a fundraiser uses ethical products, it can support both the school and producers.","zh":"如果籌款活動使用道德產品，就可以同時支持學校和生產者。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to money-raising activity in a school community.","zh":"這個短語指學校社群中的籌款活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"when the tally reached","meaning":"當總數達到……時","examples":[{"en":"When the tally reached $8,000, the students realised their message mattered.","zh":"當總數達到8,000美元時，學生意識到自己的信息很重要。"},{"en":"When the tally reached an amount means when the total counted amount became that number.","zh":"當總數達到某金額，指計算所得總數變成該數字時。"},{"en":"When the tally reached 100 signatures, the students sent the petition to the principal.","zh":"當簽名總數達到100個時，學生把請願書交給校長。"},{"en":"If a fundraising tally grows high, students may see that others support their cause.","zh":"如果籌款總數增長很高，學生可能看見其他人支持其主張。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the moment a total becomes meaningful.","zh":"這個短語標示總數變得有意義的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"strike a chord","meaning":"引起共鳴","examples":[{"en":"The students realised they were striking a chord with others.","zh":"學生意識到自己正在引起他人共鳴。"},{"en":"To strike a chord means to connect emotionally with people or make them feel something familiar.","zh":"引起共鳴，指與人們在情感上連接，或令他們感到熟悉。"},{"en":"A speech about exam stress may strike a chord with tired students.","zh":"關於考試壓力的演講，可能引起疲倦學生的共鳴。"},{"en":"If ethical chocolate sells well, the message may match what people already care about.","zh":"如果公平貿易朱古力賣得好，該信息可能符合人們已經關心的事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating emotional resonance.","zh":"這個短語描述創造情感共鳴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"hasten to point out","meaning":"急於指出","examples":[{"en":"Some adults hasten to point out the limitations of ethical consumption.","zh":"一些成年人急於指出道德消費的局限。"},{"en":"To hasten to point out something means to quickly mention it, often because one thinks others are being too optimistic.","zh":"急於指出某事，指很快提及它，通常因為認為他人過分樂觀。"},{"en":"A teacher may hasten to point out that a good idea still needs evidence.","zh":"老師可能急於指出好想法仍需要證據。"},{"en":"If young people praise ethical shopping, adults may quickly warn that it is not enough.","zh":"如果年輕人讚揚道德購物，成年人可能迅速提醒這還不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests quick correction or caution.","zh":"這個短語暗示快速糾正或提醒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"limitations of","meaning":"……的局限","examples":[{"en":"Some adults point out the limitations of ethical consumption.","zh":"一些成年人指出道德消費的局限。"},{"en":"The limitations of something are the things it cannot do or the weaknesses it has.","zh":"某事的局限，是它不能做到的事情或它具有的弱點。"},{"en":"The limitations of online learning include poor internet access and less face-to-face support.","zh":"網上學習的局限包括網絡不佳和較少面對面支援。"},{"en":"If ethical consumption cannot solve every problem, other forms of action are still needed.","zh":"如果道德消費不能解決每個問題，仍需要其他形式行動。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show the boundary of an idea or method.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示想法或方法的界限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"ethical consumption","meaning":"道德消費","examples":[{"en":"Ethical consumption may not be enough by itself.","zh":"道德消費本身可能不足夠。"},{"en":"Ethical consumption means buying goods in a way that considers fairness, workers, animals, and the environment.","zh":"道德消費，指以考慮公平、工人、動物和環境的方式購買商品。"},{"en":"Choosing Fair Trade coffee is one form of ethical consumption.","zh":"選擇公平貿易咖啡是一種道德消費。"},{"en":"If ethical consumption changes demand, companies may improve production practices.","zh":"如果道德消費改變需求，公司可能改善生產做法。"},{"en":"The phrase turns shopping into a moral choice.","zh":"這個短語把購物變成道德選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a tool for","meaning":"……的工具","examples":[{"en":"Ethical consumption can be a tool for doing good deeds.","zh":"道德消費可以是做好事的工具。"},{"en":"A tool for something is a method or instrument that helps achieve that purpose.","zh":"某事的工具，是幫助達成該目的的方法或器具。"},{"en":"A notebook can be a tool for organising revision.","zh":"筆記簿可以是整理溫習的工具。"},{"en":"If buying Fair Trade products helps farmers, shopping becomes one tool for change.","zh":"如果購買公平貿易產品幫助農民，購物就成為改變的一種工具。"},{"en":"The phrase means useful method, not necessarily a physical tool.","zh":"這個短語指有用方法，不一定是實體工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"doing good deeds","meaning":"做好事","examples":[{"en":"Some adults question whether buying products is enough for doing good deeds.","zh":"一些成年人質疑購買產品是否足以算是做好事。"},{"en":"Doing good deeds means taking actions that help others or support a good cause.","zh":"做好事，指採取幫助他人或支持好事情的行動。"},{"en":"Visiting an elderly neighbour or donating food can be examples of doing good deeds.","zh":"探訪年長鄰居或捐贈食物，都可以是做好事的例子。"},{"en":"If good deeds always bring a reward to the giver, their moral value may be questioned.","zh":"如果做好事總是為施予者帶來回報，其道德價值可能被質疑。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on helpful actions.","zh":"這個短語強調有幫助的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"personal growth","meaning":"個人成長","examples":[{"en":"Helping others can support children’s personal growth.","zh":"幫助他人可以支持孩子的個人成長。"},{"en":"Personal growth means development in character, confidence, responsibility, or understanding.","zh":"個人成長，指性格、信心、責任感或理解力上的發展。"},{"en":"A student’s personal growth may show when they learn to apologise sincerely.","zh":"當學生學會真誠道歉，就可能顯示個人成長。"},{"en":"If children help without reward, they may become more caring and mature.","zh":"如果孩子沒有回報也幫助別人，可能變得更有愛心和成熟。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to inner development, not physical growth.","zh":"這個短語指內在發展，而不是身體成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"encourage Fair Trade purchases","meaning":"鼓勵購買公平貿易產品","examples":[{"en":"Gary Lindsay encourages Fair Trade purchases.","zh":"Gary Lindsay 鼓勵購買公平貿易產品。"},{"en":"To encourage Fair Trade purchases means to support or promote buying Fair Trade products.","zh":"鼓勵購買公平貿易產品，指支持或推廣購買公平貿易商品。"},{"en":"A teacher may encourage Fair Trade purchases during a lesson on global inequality.","zh":"老師可能在全球不平等課堂中鼓勵購買公平貿易產品。"},{"en":"If people are encouraged to buy Fair Trade, producers may receive fairer pay.","zh":"如果人們被鼓勵購買公平貿易產品，生產者可能得到較公平報酬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes promoting ethical buying.","zh":"這個短語描述推廣道德購買。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"organise projects","meaning":"組織項目","examples":[{"en":"Lindsay also organises projects that help children serve others.","zh":"Lindsay 也組織幫助孩子服務他人的項目。"},{"en":"To organise projects means to plan and arrange activities with a clear purpose.","zh":"組織項目，指規劃和安排有明確目的的活動。"},{"en":"A teacher may organise projects where students collect books for a community centre.","zh":"老師可能組織項目，讓學生為社區中心收集書籍。"},{"en":"If projects are organised well, children can learn responsibility through action.","zh":"如果項目組織得好，孩子可以透過行動學習責任感。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on planning practical activities.","zh":"這個短語強調規劃實際活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"collect toys for","meaning":"為……收集玩具","examples":[{"en":"Children collect toys for foster children.","zh":"孩子為寄養兒童收集玩具。"},{"en":"To collect toys for someone means to gather toys to give to that group.","zh":"為某人收集玩具，指聚集玩具並送給該群體。"},{"en":"A class may collect toys for children in hospital before Christmas.","zh":"班級可能在聖誕節前為住院兒童收集玩具。"},{"en":"If children collect toys for others, they learn to think beyond their own needs.","zh":"如果孩子為他人收集玩具，就學會思考自己的需要以外的事情。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a simple donation activity.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單捐贈活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"foster children","meaning":"寄養兒童","examples":[{"en":"The children collect toys for foster children.","zh":"孩子為寄養兒童收集玩具。"},{"en":"Foster children are children who live with foster families because they cannot live safely with their birth families at that time.","zh":"寄養兒童，是因當時不能安全地與親生家庭同住，而與寄養家庭生活的孩子。"},{"en":"A community group may prepare gifts for foster children during holidays.","zh":"社區團體可能在假期為寄養兒童準備禮物。"},{"en":"If foster children receive support, they may feel more included and cared for.","zh":"如果寄養兒童得到支持，可能感到更被接納和照顧。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to children in temporary care arrangements.","zh":"這個短語指處於臨時照顧安排中的兒童。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"save coins for","meaning":"為……儲硬幣","examples":[{"en":"Children save coins for a playground-construction project.","zh":"孩子為遊樂場建設項目儲硬幣。"},{"en":"To save coins for something means to collect small amounts of money over time for a purpose.","zh":"為某事儲硬幣，指為某目的隨時間收集小額金錢。"},{"en":"Students may save coins for a class charity box.","zh":"學生可能為班級慈善箱儲硬幣。"},{"en":"If many children save small amounts, the total can support a larger project.","zh":"如果許多孩子儲起小額金錢，總數可以支持更大型項目。"},{"en":"The phrase shows small giving through repeated saving.","zh":"這個短語顯示透過反覆儲蓄作小額捐助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"playground-construction project","meaning":"遊樂場建設項目","examples":[{"en":"The children save coins for a playground-construction project in Tanzania.","zh":"孩子為坦桑尼亞的遊樂場建設項目儲硬幣。"},{"en":"A playground-construction project is an organised effort to build a play area for children.","zh":"遊樂場建設項目，是為孩子建造遊樂空間的有組織努力。"},{"en":"A school may raise money for a playground-construction project in a poorer community.","zh":"學校可能為較貧困社區的遊樂場建設項目籌款。"},{"en":"If a playground is built, children gain a safer place to play and meet friends.","zh":"如果遊樂場建成，孩子就得到更安全的地方玩耍和見朋友。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a practical development project for children.","zh":"這個短語指為兒童而設的實際發展項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"learn to enjoy helping others","meaning":"學會享受幫助別人","examples":[{"en":"Children should learn to enjoy helping others.","zh":"孩子應學會享受幫助別人。"},{"en":"To learn to enjoy helping others means to develop pleasure and satisfaction from serving people in need.","zh":"學會享受幫助別人，指從服務有需要的人中培養快樂和滿足感。"},{"en":"A child may learn to enjoy helping others by reading to younger students each week.","zh":"孩子可能透過每週為較年幼學生朗讀，學會享受幫助別人。"},{"en":"If helping feels meaningful, children may continue serving even without rewards.","zh":"如果幫助感覺有意義，孩子即使沒有回報也可能繼續服務。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on building generous habits.","zh":"這個短語強調建立慷慨習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"get anything tangible in return","meaning":"得到任何實質回報","examples":[{"en":"Children should help even when they do not get anything tangible in return.","zh":"孩子即使得不到任何實質回報，也應幫助他人。"},{"en":"To get anything tangible in return means to receive a real physical reward or clear material benefit.","zh":"得到任何實質回報，指收到真實可見的獎勵或明確物質好處。"},{"en":"A student who volunteers without snacks, money, or gifts gets nothing tangible in return.","zh":"如果學生做義工而沒有小食、金錢或禮物，就是沒有得到實質回報。"},{"en":"If children help without material rewards, they may learn that kindness itself matters.","zh":"如果孩子在沒有物質獎勵下幫人，可能學會善意本身很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts real objects with inner satisfaction.","zh":"這個短語把實物與內在滿足作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in return","meaning":"作為回報","examples":[{"en":"They should help others without expecting something in return.","zh":"他們應幫助別人，而不期待某些東西作為回報。"},{"en":"In return means as repayment, reward, or exchange for something done.","zh":"作為回報，指為某行動而得到的償還、獎勵或交換。"},{"en":"A friend may help you move house and expect only a thank-you in return.","zh":"朋友可能幫你搬屋，而只期待一句謝謝作為回報。"},{"en":"If people always expect something in return, generosity becomes closer to a trade.","zh":"如果人們總期待某些東西作為回報，慷慨就更接近交易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what comes back after an action.","zh":"這個短語描述行動之後回來的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"when we are benefiting","meaning":"當我們正在得益時","examples":[{"en":"Lindsay asks how much we are really giving when we are benefiting.","zh":"Lindsay 問，當我們正在得益時，我們真正付出了多少。"},{"en":"When we are benefiting means while we are also gaining something for ourselves.","zh":"當我們正在得益時，指我們自己也正在得到某些好處時。"},{"en":"If students volunteer mainly for certificates, they are benefiting from the service.","zh":"如果學生主要為證書做義工，他們就是從服務中得益。"},{"en":"If the giver gains status, products, or rewards, the act may be less purely generous.","zh":"如果施予者獲得地位、產品或獎勵，該行為可能沒有那麼純粹慷慨。"},{"en":"The phrase questions whether help is selfless when the helper gains too.","zh":"這個短語質疑當幫助者也得益時，幫助是否無私。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"how much are we really giving","meaning":"我們真正付出了多少","examples":[{"en":"He questions how much people are really giving when they also benefit.","zh":"他質疑當人們也得益時，真正付出了多少。"},{"en":"How much are we really giving asks whether our help is truly generous or partly self-serving.","zh":"我們真正付出了多少，是問我們的幫助是否真正慷慨，還是部分為自己。"},{"en":"A student may ask this if a charity event mainly gives volunteers prizes and attention.","zh":"如果慈善活動主要給義工獎品和關注，學生可能問這個問題。"},{"en":"If a good deed benefits the giver too much, its generosity may be questioned.","zh":"如果好事令施予者得益太多，其慷慨程度可能被質疑。"},{"en":"The phrase encourages honest reflection about motive.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵誠實反思動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"expect that","meaning":"期望","examples":[{"en":"Lindsay criticises the expectation that people should get something from every good deed.","zh":"Lindsay 批評人們期望每件好事都應得到某些東西。"},{"en":"To expect that something will happen means to believe it should or probably will happen.","zh":"期望某事會發生，指相信它應該或很可能會發生。"},{"en":"Students may expect that hard work will lead to better marks.","zh":"學生可能期望努力會帶來更好成績。"},{"en":"If people expect rewards for every kind action, giving becomes less generous.","zh":"如果人們期望每個善行都有回報，付出就變得較不慷慨。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a belief about what should happen.","zh":"這個短語引入對應該發生事情的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"get something out of","meaning":"從……中得到好處","examples":[{"en":"Some people expect to get something out of everything they do.","zh":"有些人期望從自己做的每件事中得到好處。"},{"en":"To get something out of an action means to gain a benefit from it.","zh":"從某行動中得到好處，指從中取得利益。"},{"en":"A student may get confidence out of joining a speech competition.","zh":"學生可能從參加演講比賽中得到信心。"},{"en":"If people only help when they get something out of it, their motive may look selfish.","zh":"如果人們只有在能得到好處時才幫忙，其動機可能顯得自私。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on personal gain.","zh":"這個短語強調個人得益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a selfish attitude","meaning":"自私的態度","examples":[{"en":"Lindsay thinks that expecting a reward for every good deed is a selfish attitude.","zh":"Lindsay 認為期望每件好事都有回報是一種自私的態度。"},{"en":"A selfish attitude is a way of thinking that focuses mainly on personal benefit.","zh":"自私的態度，是主要關注個人利益的思考方式。"},{"en":"A student shows a selfish attitude if they only help classmates to gain praise.","zh":"如果學生只為得到稱讚才幫同學，就是表現出自私的態度。"},{"en":"If good deeds become only a way to receive rewards, generosity is weakened.","zh":"如果做好事只變成獲取回報的方法，慷慨就被削弱。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises motives centred on the self.","zh":"這個短語批評以自我為中心的動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"for each question","meaning":"對於每條問題","examples":[{"en":"For each question, only one of the choices is correct.","zh":"對於每條問題，只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"For each question means for every individual question in the task.","zh":"對於每條問題，指任務中的每一道獨立題目。"},{"en":"For each question, students should read all options before choosing.","zh":"對於每條問題，學生都應先閱讀所有選項再選擇。"},{"en":"If only one answer is correct for each question, guessing too quickly can be risky.","zh":"如果每條問題只有一個答案正確，太快猜答案可能有風險。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"only one of the choices is correct","meaning":"只有一個選項正確","examples":[{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct for each question.","zh":"每條問題只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct means students must select a single right option.","zh":"只有一個選項正確，指學生必須選出單一正確選項。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice exercise, two similar answers may appear, but only one is correct.","zh":"在選擇題練習中，兩個答案可能相似，但只有一個正確。"},{"en":"If students choose more than one option, the answer may be marked wrong.","zh":"如果學生選多於一個選項，答案可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase warns students not to select several answers.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生不要選多個答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"corresponding letter","meaning":"對應字母","examples":[{"en":"Students write the corresponding letter in the answer box.","zh":"學生在答案框中寫上對應字母。"},{"en":"A corresponding letter is the letter that matches the correct option or answer.","zh":"對應字母，是與正確選項或答案相配的字母。"},{"en":"If the correct option is B, students write the corresponding letter B.","zh":"如果正確選項是 B，學生就寫上對應字母 B。"},{"en":"If a student knows the answer but writes the wrong letter, the response may still be marked wrong.","zh":"如果學生知道答案但寫錯字母，回應仍可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an answer choice with its letter.","zh":"這個短語把答案選項與其字母連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"appropriate box","meaning":"適當方格","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the answer in the appropriate box on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生把答案寫在答題紙上的適當方格中。"},{"en":"The appropriate box is the correct space where an answer should be written.","zh":"適當方格，是應填寫答案的正確空間。"},{"en":"On a form, a phone number should be written in the appropriate box.","zh":"在表格上，電話號碼應寫在適當方格中。"},{"en":"If an answer is written in the wrong box, it may not be counted correctly.","zh":"如果答案寫在錯誤方格中，可能不能被正確計算。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the correct answer space.","zh":"這個短語指正確答案位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"answer sheet","meaning":"答題紙","examples":[{"en":"Students write their answers on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生把答案寫在答題紙上。"},{"en":"An answer sheet is the paper or digital form where exam answers are recorded.","zh":"答題紙，是記錄考試答案的紙張或電子表格。"},{"en":"Students should check the answer sheet before time ends.","zh":"學生應在時間結束前檢查答題紙。"},{"en":"If answers are written only on the question paper, they may not be marked.","zh":"如果答案只寫在試題紙上，可能不會被批改。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the official place for final answers.","zh":"這個短語指最終答案的正式位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"through what people purchase","meaning":"透過人們購買的東西","examples":[{"en":"The question asks how people try to change the world through what they purchase.","zh":"題目問人們如何透過購買的東西嘗試改變世界。"},{"en":"Through what people purchase means by using buying choices as a method.","zh":"透過人們購買的東西，指把購買選擇用作方法。"},{"en":"A family can support local shops through what they purchase each week.","zh":"家庭可以透過每週購買的東西支持本地商店。"},{"en":"If people choose ethical products, their purchases can send a message to companies.","zh":"如果人們選擇道德產品，其購買可以向公司傳遞信息。"},{"en":"The phrase links consumer behaviour with social influence.","zh":"這個短語把消費行為與社會影響連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"begin with","meaning":"以……開始","examples":[{"en":"The movement began with campaigns against sweatshop clothing.","zh":"該運動以反對血汗工場服裝的運動開始。"},{"en":"To begin with something means to start from that point or action.","zh":"以某事開始，指從該點或行動開始。"},{"en":"A school environmental campaign may begin with collecting plastic bottles.","zh":"學校環保運動可能以收集膠樽開始。"},{"en":"If a movement begins with one issue, it may later expand to related areas.","zh":"如果運動以一個議題開始，後來可能擴展至相關範疇。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the starting point.","zh":"這個短語指出起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"use its services","meaning":"使用其服務","examples":[{"en":"Many colleges used Bon Appétit’s food services.","zh":"許多大學使用 Bon Appétit 的餐飲服務。"},{"en":"To use its services means to hire or rely on the help a company provides.","zh":"使用其服務，指聘用或依靠某公司提供的幫助。"},{"en":"A school may use a bus company’s services for student trips.","zh":"學校可能在學生旅行中使用巴士公司的服務。"},{"en":"If many colleges use one provider’s services, that provider gains influence.","zh":"如果許多大學使用同一供應商的服務，該供應商就獲得影響力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to receiving practical service from an organisation.","zh":"這個短語指接受某組織的實際服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"provide money for","meaning":"為……提供資金","examples":[{"en":"Buying Ethos Water helps provide money for clean-water projects.","zh":"購買 Ethos Water 有助為淨水項目提供資金。"},{"en":"To provide money for something means to supply funds to support it.","zh":"為某事提供資金，指供應金錢來支持它。"},{"en":"A charity concert can provide money for hospital equipment.","zh":"慈善音樂會可以為醫院設備提供資金。"},{"en":"If each purchase provides money for a project, consumers help fund it indirectly.","zh":"如果每次購買都為某項目提供資金，消費者就間接資助它。"},{"en":"The phrase links financial support with a purpose.","zh":"這個短語把財務支援與目的連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"clean water projects","meaning":"淨水項目","examples":[{"en":"Ethos Water supports clean water projects in developing countries.","zh":"Ethos Water 支持發展中國家的淨水項目。"},{"en":"Clean water projects are organised efforts to provide safe drinking water to communities.","zh":"淨水項目，是為社區提供安全飲用水的有組織努力。"},{"en":"A clean water project may build wells, pipes, or purification centres.","zh":"淨水項目可能建造水井、水管或淨水中心。"},{"en":"If clean water projects succeed, fewer people may become sick from unsafe water.","zh":"如果淨水項目成功，較少人可能因不安全食水而生病。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical work improving access to safe water.","zh":"這個短語指改善安全食水供應的實際工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"first got involved with","meaning":"首次參與","examples":[{"en":"Joe Curnow first got involved with consumer activism through coffee.","zh":"Joe Curnow 透過咖啡首次參與消費者行動主義。"},{"en":"To first get involved with something means to begin participating in it for the first time.","zh":"首次參與某事，指第一次開始參加它。"},{"en":"A student may first get involved with volunteering through a school charity day.","zh":"學生可能透過學校慈善日首次參與義工服務。"},{"en":"If coffee introduced her to activism, an everyday product became a starting point.","zh":"如果咖啡把她引入行動主義，日常產品就成為起點。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a person’s first connection with an activity or movement.","zh":"這個短語標示某人與活動或運動的第一次連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the following sentences","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the following sentences using words from the text.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成以下句子。"},{"en":"To complete the following sentences means to fill in missing words in the sentences below.","zh":"完成以下句子，指填寫下面句子中缺少的字詞。"},{"en":"Students complete sentences by checking grammar and meaning around each gap.","zh":"學生透過檢查每個空格前後的文法和意思來完成句子。"},{"en":"If answers must come from the text, students should copy the exact word required.","zh":"如果答案必須來自文章，學生應抄寫所需的準確字詞。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard completion-task instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準填充題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than one word","meaning":"不超過一個字","examples":[{"en":"Students must use no more than one word for each gap.","zh":"學生每個空格必須使用不超過一個字。"},{"en":"No more than one word means the answer must be a single word only.","zh":"不超過一個字，指答案必須只有一個詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “growth,” students should not write “the growth.”","zh":"如果答案是 “growth”，學生不應寫 “the growth”。"},{"en":"If students write two words, the answer may be wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"如果學生寫兩個詞，即使意思正確，答案也可能錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"from the text","meaning":"來自文章","examples":[{"en":"The answer must come from the text.","zh":"答案必須來自文章。"},{"en":"From the text means taken directly from the passage, not invented or guessed from outside knowledge.","zh":"來自文章，指直接取自篇章，而不是自行創作或用外部知識猜測。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should copy the answer from the text when instructed.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，當指示要求時，學生應從文章抄寫答案。"},{"en":"If a word is not in the passage, it may not be accepted even if it is a synonym.","zh":"如果某詞不在文章中，即使是同義詞也可能不被接受。"},{"en":"The phrase keeps answers grounded in the source.","zh":"這個短語令答案以來源為根據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"for each gap","meaning":"每個空格","examples":[{"en":"Students choose one word for each gap.","zh":"學生為每個空格選擇一個字。"},{"en":"For each gap means for every blank space in the exercise.","zh":"每個空格，指練習中每一個空白位置。"},{"en":"Students should read the words before and after each gap before answering.","zh":"學生作答前應閱讀每個空格前後的字詞。"},{"en":"If one gap needs a noun and another needs a verb, the answer form must change.","zh":"如果一個空格需要名詞，另一個需要動詞，答案形式必須改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to every missing-word position.","zh":"這個短語指每個缺詞位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"The students go to the grocer’s rather than the mall.","zh":"學生去食品店，而不是商場。"},{"en":"Rather than shows that one choice is made instead of another.","zh":"而不是，顯示選擇一件事而非另一件事。"},{"en":"A student may revise in the library rather than at home if home is noisy.","zh":"如果家中嘈吵，學生可能在圖書館溫習，而不是在家。"},{"en":"If teenagers choose an ethical food store rather than a mall, their values affect where they go.","zh":"如果青少年選擇道德食品店而不是商場，其價值觀就影響他們去哪裡。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a clear contrast between two options.","zh":"這個短語在兩個選項之間建立清楚對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"limit its growth","meaning":"限制其增長","examples":[{"en":"Bon Appétit limits its growth intentionally.","zh":"Bon Appétit 有意限制其增長。"},{"en":"To limit its growth means to control how much or how quickly a company expands.","zh":"限制其增長，指控制公司擴張多少或多快。"},{"en":"A tutoring centre may limit its growth so teachers can still know every student well.","zh":"補習中心可能限制其增長，讓老師仍能了解每個學生。"},{"en":"If growth is limited, quality may be easier to protect.","zh":"如果增長被限制，質素可能較容易保護。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests careful control rather than unlimited expansion.","zh":"這個短語暗示仔細控制，而不是無限制擴張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"previously","meaning":"以前","examples":[{"en":"Previously, young generations were willing to make sacrifices.","zh":"以前，年輕世代願意作出犧牲。"},{"en":"Previously means before the time being discussed.","zh":"以前，指在正在討論的時間之前。"},{"en":"Previously, students submitted homework on paper; now they use an online platform.","zh":"以前，學生交紙本功課；現在他們使用網上平台。"},{"en":"If previous generations accepted sacrifice, today’s demand for quality marks a change.","zh":"如果前幾代人接受犧牲，今天對質素的要求就標示改變。"},{"en":"The word contrasts past and present.","zh":"這個詞對比過去與現在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"feel frustrated and powerless","meaning":"感到沮喪和無力","examples":[{"en":"Young people can feel frustrated and powerless because of their age.","zh":"年輕人可能因年紀而感到沮喪和無力。"},{"en":"To feel frustrated and powerless means to feel upset because you cannot change a situation.","zh":"感到沮喪和無力，指因不能改變情況而感到不快。"},{"en":"Students may feel frustrated and powerless when adults make all decisions without listening.","zh":"當成年人不聆聽就作出所有決定，學生可能感到沮喪和無力。"},{"en":"If teenagers feel powerless politically, consumer activism may feel like one available tool.","zh":"如果青少年在政治上感到無力，消費者行動主義可能感覺像一種可用工具。"},{"en":"The phrase combines anger, disappointment, and lack of control.","zh":"這個短語結合憤怒、失望和缺乏控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"make use of","meaning":"利用；使用","examples":[{"en":"Gary Lindsay encourages people to buy products that make use of Fair Trade.","zh":"Gary Lindsay 鼓勵人購買使用公平貿易的產品。"},{"en":"To make use of something means to use it for a practical purpose.","zh":"使用某物，指把它用於實際目的。"},{"en":"A teacher may make use of news articles to teach reading skills.","zh":"老師可能使用新聞文章來教授閱讀技巧。"},{"en":"If a product makes use of Fair Trade, it uses ethical trade principles in its supply chain.","zh":"如果產品使用公平貿易，它就在供應鏈中採用道德貿易原則。"},{"en":"The phrase means use something actively, not merely mention it.","zh":"這個短語指主動使用某物，而不只是提及它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the information given.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否與所給資料相符。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"與所給資料相符，指符合文章所說內容。"},{"en":"If the text says students sold chocolate, a statement saying they sold chocolate agrees with it.","zh":"如果文本說學生售賣朱古力，陳述說他們售賣朱古力就是相符。"},{"en":"If a statement adds unsupported details, it may not agree with the information.","zh":"如果陳述加入未被支持的細節，就可能不符合資料。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個短語用於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"FALSE 陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text states.","zh":"與資料相矛盾，指說出與文本所述相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says coffee was Fair Trade, saying it was not Fair Trade contradicts it.","zh":"如果文章說咖啡是公平貿易，說它不是公平貿易就是相矛盾。"},{"en":"When a statement contradicts the text, the correct answer is usually FALSE.","zh":"當陳述與文本矛盾，正確答案通常是 FALSE。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct conflict with the source.","zh":"這個短語描述與來源直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students choose “NOT GIVEN” if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果沒有相關資料，學生選擇 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not say enough to judge the statement.","zh":"沒有相關資料，指文章沒有說足夠內容來判斷陳述。"},{"en":"If the text mentions coffee labels but not coffee price, price may be NOT GIVEN.","zh":"如果文本提到咖啡標籤但沒有提到咖啡價格，價格可能是 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when the passage gives no information.","zh":"當文章沒有提供資料時，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"The phrase signals insufficient evidence.","zh":"這個短語表示證據不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"more expensive than usual coffee","meaning":"比普通咖啡更貴","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Fair Trade coffee is more expensive than usual coffee.","zh":"該陳述問公平貿易咖啡是否比普通咖啡更貴。"},{"en":"More expensive than usual coffee means costing more than ordinary coffee.","zh":"比普通咖啡更貴，指價錢高於一般咖啡。"},{"en":"A café drink may be more expensive than usual coffee if it uses special beans.","zh":"如果咖啡店飲品使用特別咖啡豆，可能比普通咖啡更貴。"},{"en":"If the passage does not mention price, students cannot assume Fair Trade coffee costs more.","zh":"如果文章沒有提及價格，學生不能假設公平貿易咖啡較貴。"},{"en":"The phrase compares price between two kinds of coffee.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種咖啡的價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"used to sell","meaning":"以前售賣","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Bon Appétit used to sell sugared cereal.","zh":"該陳述問 Bon Appétit 是否以前售賣加糖穀物早餐。"},{"en":"Used to sell means sold in the past but may not sell now.","zh":"以前售賣，指過去曾售賣，但現在可能不再售賣。"},{"en":"A school tuck shop used to sell sweets before the healthy eating policy.","zh":"學校小食部在健康飲食政策前以前售賣糖果。"},{"en":"If a passage only says students liked sugared cereal, it may not prove who sold it.","zh":"如果文章只說學生喜歡加糖穀物早餐，未必證明誰售賣它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a past regular practice.","zh":"這個短語指過去的定期做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"understand the importance of","meaning":"明白……的重要性","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether kids understand the importance of protecting the environment.","zh":"該陳述問孩子是否明白保護環境的重要性。"},{"en":"To understand the importance of something means to know why it matters.","zh":"明白某事的重要性，指知道它為何重要。"},{"en":"Students understand the importance of sleep when they notice how tiredness affects learning.","zh":"當學生注意到疲倦如何影響學習，就會明白睡眠的重要性。"},{"en":"If children push recycling at home, they may understand why environmental action matters.","zh":"如果孩子在家推動回收，他們可能明白環境行動為何重要。"},{"en":"The phrase links knowledge with value.","zh":"這個短語把知識與價值連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"protecting the environment","meaning":"保護環境","examples":[{"en":"Children often support recycling and protecting the environment.","zh":"孩子常支持回收和保護環境。"},{"en":"Protecting the environment means taking action to reduce harm to air, water, land, animals, and natural resources.","zh":"保護環境，指採取行動減少對空氣、水、土地、動物和自然資源的傷害。"},{"en":"Using less plastic and saving electricity are ways of protecting the environment.","zh":"少用塑膠和節省電力都是保護環境的方法。"},{"en":"If families protect the environment at home, children learn responsibility through daily habits.","zh":"如果家庭在家中保護環境，孩子就透過日常習慣學習責任。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to caring for nature through action.","zh":"這個短語指透過行動照顧自然。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"as long as","meaning":"只要","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Oakes would wear unattractive clothes as long as they promote Fair Trade.","zh":"該陳述問 Oakes 是否只要衣服推廣公平貿易，就會穿不吸引的衣服。"},{"en":"As long as means provided that or on the condition that.","zh":"只要，指在某條件成立的情況下。"},{"en":"A student may join a club as long as meetings do not clash with lessons.","zh":"學生只要會議不與課堂衝突，就可能加入學會。"},{"en":"If someone buys ugly clothing just because it is ethical, quality is being sacrificed.","zh":"如果某人只因衣服道德就購買醜陋衣服，質素就是被犧牲。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a condition.","zh":"這個短語引入條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"promote Fair Trade","meaning":"推廣公平貿易","examples":[{"en":"Some clothing brands promote Fair Trade principles.","zh":"一些服裝品牌推廣公平貿易原則。"},{"en":"To promote Fair Trade means to support or advertise trading practices that pay producers fairly.","zh":"推廣公平貿易，指支持或宣傳公平支付生產者的貿易做法。"},{"en":"A school poster can promote Fair Trade by explaining how farmers benefit.","zh":"學校海報可以透過解釋農民如何受益來推廣公平貿易。"},{"en":"If brands promote Fair Trade honestly, they should also provide products of good quality.","zh":"如果品牌誠實推廣公平貿易，也應提供質素良好的產品。"},{"en":"The phrase connects publicity with ethical trade.","zh":"這個短語把宣傳與道德貿易連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"do more than just","meaning":"做的不只是……","examples":[{"en":"Gary Lindsay thinks people should do more than just consume ethically.","zh":"Gary Lindsay 認為人們應做的不只是有道德地消費。"},{"en":"To do more than just do something means to go beyond one action and add deeper or broader effort.","zh":"做的不只是某事，指超越一個行動，加入更深入或更廣泛的努力。"},{"en":"Students should do more than just memorise vocabulary; they should use it in sentences.","zh":"學生做的不應只是背詞彙；他們應在句子中使用它。"},{"en":"If people only buy ethical goods but never help directly, their contribution may be limited.","zh":"如果人們只購買道德商品但從不直接幫助，貢獻可能有限。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests one action is useful but not enough.","zh":"這個短語暗示某行動有用但不足夠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"consume ethically","meaning":"有道德地消費","examples":[{"en":"People can consume ethically, but they should also learn to give without reward.","zh":"人們可以有道德地消費，但也應學會不求回報地付出。"},{"en":"To consume ethically means to buy and use products in a way that considers fairness and harm.","zh":"有道德地消費，指以考慮公平和傷害的方式購買和使用產品。"},{"en":"A person consumes ethically when they choose goods made without exploiting workers.","zh":"當一個人選擇不剝削工人而製成的商品，就是有道德地消費。"},{"en":"If people consume ethically, companies may improve supply chains, but personal service may still matter.","zh":"如果人們有道德地消費，公司可能改善供應鏈，但個人服務仍可能重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moral decision-making in buying and using goods.","zh":"這個短語描述購買和使用商品中的道德決策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 67 - Teens Try to Change the World, One Purchase at a Time.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 68":[{"front":"Care in the Community","meaning":"社區照顧","examples":[{"en":"Care in the community allows some mentally ill patients to live outside institutions.","zh":"社區照顧容許一些精神病患者在院舍以外生活。"},{"en":"Care in the community is a system in which people receive mental-health support while living in ordinary neighbourhoods.","zh":"Care in the community 是讓人們住在普通社區中同時接受精神健康支援的制度。"},{"en":"A patient may receive care in the community through home visits, medication support, and counselling.","zh":"病人可以透過家訪、藥物支援和輔導接受社區照顧。"},{"en":"If care in the community is well organised, patients can live more independently.","zh":"如果社區照顧安排妥善，病人可以生活得更獨立。"},{"en":"Without enough professional support, care in the community may leave vulnerable patients isolated.","zh":"如果沒有足夠專業支援，社區照顧可能令脆弱病人被孤立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"become synonymous with","meaning":"成為……的代名詞","examples":[{"en":"“Bedlam” has become synonymous with chaos and disorder.","zh":"“Bedlam” 已成為混亂和失序的代名詞。"},{"en":"To become synonymous with something means to become strongly associated with that idea.","zh":"To become synonymous with something 指變得與某個概念強烈相關。"},{"en":"A restaurant may become synonymous with poor service if customers repeatedly complain.","zh":"如果顧客反覆投訴，餐廳可能成為劣質服務的代名詞。"},{"en":"If a school is always disorganised, its name may become synonymous with confusion.","zh":"如果一間學校總是組織混亂，它的名字可能成為混亂的代名詞。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when one name almost automatically makes people think of another idea.","zh":"這個片語用於某個名稱幾乎會自動令人想到另一個概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"chaos and disorder","meaning":"混亂和失序","examples":[{"en":"The word “Bedlam” is associated with chaos and disorder.","zh":"“Bedlam” 這個詞與混亂和失序有關。"},{"en":"Chaos and disorder means a situation with confusion, noise, and little control.","zh":"Chaos and disorder 指充滿混亂、噪音且缺乏控制的情況。"},{"en":"A classroom may fall into chaos and disorder if no rules are followed.","zh":"如果沒有人遵守規則，課室可能陷入混亂和失序。"},{"en":"After a sudden power cut, a busy station may experience chaos and disorder.","zh":"突然停電後，繁忙車站可能出現混亂和失序。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a situation where normal organisation breaks down.","zh":"這個片語描述正常秩序崩潰的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the term itself","meaning":"這個詞本身","examples":[{"en":"The term itself derives from the name of a former London institution.","zh":"這個詞本身源自一間前倫敦機構的名稱。"},{"en":"The term itself means the word or phrase being discussed, not just the idea behind it.","zh":"The term itself 指正在討論的字詞或片語本身，而不只是背後概念。"},{"en":"The term itself may sound modern, but its history can be very old.","zh":"這個詞本身可能聽起來現代，但其歷史可以很古老。"},{"en":"If students understand the term itself, they can use it more accurately in writing.","zh":"如果學生理解這個詞本身，就能在寫作中更準確使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase helps focus attention on the actual word or expression.","zh":"這個片語幫助把注意力集中在實際字詞或表達上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"derive from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"The term derives from a shortened name for a London institution.","zh":"這個詞源自一間倫敦機構的簡稱。"},{"en":"To derive from something means to come from it or have it as an origin.","zh":"To derive from something 指來自某事或以某事為起源。"},{"en":"Many English words derive from Latin, French, or Greek.","zh":"許多英文字源自拉丁文、法文或希臘文。"},{"en":"If a school tradition derives from an old ceremony, knowing its origin can make it more meaningful.","zh":"如果學校傳統源自古老儀式，知道其起源可以令它更有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase explains where a word, custom, or idea comes from.","zh":"這個片語解釋字詞、習俗或想法來自哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"shortened name for","meaning":"……的簡稱","examples":[{"en":"“Bedlam” derives from the shortened name for St. Mary of Bethlehem.","zh":"“Bedlam” 源自 St. Mary of Bethlehem 的簡稱。"},{"en":"A shortened name for something is a shorter version of its full name.","zh":"A shortened name for something 是某完整名稱的較短版本。"},{"en":"“Lab” is a shortened name for laboratory.","zh":"“Lab” 是 laboratory 的簡稱。"},{"en":"Shortened names are useful because long official names can be difficult to say repeatedly.","zh":"簡稱很有用，因為冗長正式名稱難以反覆說出。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a full name becomes reduced in everyday speech.","zh":"這個片語用於完整名稱在日常說話中被縮短。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"former 16th-century London institution","meaning":"前十六世紀倫敦機構","examples":[{"en":"St. Mary of Bethlehem was a former 16th-century London institution.","zh":"St. Mary of Bethlehem 是一間前十六世紀倫敦機構。"},{"en":"A former 16th-century London institution is an organisation that existed in London in the 1500s but no longer functions in the same way.","zh":"Former 16th-century London institution 指一個在十六世紀倫敦存在、但現已不再以同樣方式運作的組織。"},{"en":"A museum guide may describe an old hospital as a former London institution.","zh":"博物館導賞員可能把一間舊醫院描述為前倫敦機構。"},{"en":"If an institution has a long history, its name may survive even after its role changes.","zh":"如果一個機構歷史悠久，即使其角色改變，名稱仍可能保留下來。"},{"en":"This phrase places an old organisation in both time and place.","zh":"這個片語同時交代舊機構的時間和地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the mentally ill","meaning":"精神病患者","examples":[{"en":"The institution was built for the mentally ill.","zh":"這間機構是為精神病患者而建的。"},{"en":"The mentally ill are people who suffer from mental-health conditions.","zh":"The mentally ill 指患有精神健康疾病的人。"},{"en":"Hospitals and community teams should treat the mentally ill with dignity and patience.","zh":"醫院和社區團隊應以尊嚴和耐性對待精神病患者。"},{"en":"If the mentally ill are isolated without support, their condition may worsen.","zh":"如果精神病患者在沒有支援下被孤立，其狀況可能惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a group of people, so it should be used respectfully.","zh":"這個片語指一群人，因此應尊重地使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"known as","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"The institution was known as St. Mary of Bethlehem.","zh":"這間機構被稱為 St. Mary of Bethlehem。"},{"en":"Known as means called by a particular name.","zh":"Known as 指被某個特定名稱稱呼。"},{"en":"Hong Kong is known as a busy international city.","zh":"香港被稱為繁忙的國際城市。"},{"en":"If a teacher is known as strict but fair, students may respect her rules.","zh":"如果老師被稱為嚴格但公平，學生可能尊重她的規則。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the name or reputation attached to someone or something.","zh":"這個片語引出某人或某事的名稱或名聲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"so notorious that","meaning":"臭名昭著到……","examples":[{"en":"The institution was so notorious that its name became a byword for mayhem.","zh":"這間機構臭名昭著到其名稱成為大混亂的代名詞。"},{"en":"So notorious that means so famous for bad reasons that a clear result follows.","zh":"So notorious that 指因壞事而極有名，以致帶來明顯結果。"},{"en":"The restaurant was so notorious that people avoided it even after it changed owners.","zh":"這間餐廳臭名昭著到即使換了老闆，人們仍避開它。"},{"en":"If a hospital is so notorious that patients fear going there, serious reform is needed.","zh":"如果一間醫院臭名昭著到病人害怕前往，就需要嚴重改革。"},{"en":"This phrase links a very bad reputation with its consequence.","zh":"這個片語把極差名聲與其後果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"become a byword for","meaning":"成為……的代名詞","examples":[{"en":"The name became a byword for mayhem.","zh":"這個名稱成為大混亂的代名詞。"},{"en":"To become a byword for something means to become a well-known symbol of it.","zh":"To become a byword for something 指成為某事的著名象徵。"},{"en":"A badly managed project can become a byword for waste and confusion.","zh":"管理差劣的項目可以成為浪費和混亂的代名詞。"},{"en":"If a school becomes a byword for discipline, parents may trust its routines.","zh":"如果一間學校成為紀律的代名詞，家長可能信任其常規。"},{"en":"This phrase can be used for either a good or bad reputation.","zh":"這個片語可用於好名聲或壞名聲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mayhem","meaning":"大混亂；騷亂","examples":[{"en":"The institution’s name became associated with mayhem.","zh":"這間機構的名稱與大混亂聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Mayhem means violent confusion, disorder, or noisy chaos.","zh":"Mayhem 指帶有激烈混亂、失序或嘈雜混亂的情況。"},{"en":"There was mayhem at the bus stop when three buses arrived late at once.","zh":"當三架巴士同時遲到到站，巴士站一片大混亂。"},{"en":"If emergency instructions are unclear, a fire drill can turn into mayhem.","zh":"如果緊急指示不清晰，火警演習可能變成大混亂。"},{"en":"This word describes confusion that feels intense and uncontrolled.","zh":"這個詞描述強烈且失控的混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"patient treatment","meaning":"病人待遇；病人治療","examples":[{"en":"Patient treatment at the institution was extremely poor.","zh":"這間機構的病人待遇極差。"},{"en":"Patient treatment means the way patients are cared for, medically and personally.","zh":"Patient treatment 指病人在醫療和個人層面上如何被照顧。"},{"en":"Good patient treatment includes clear explanations, clean rooms, and respectful communication.","zh":"良好病人待遇包括清晰解釋、清潔房間和尊重溝通。"},{"en":"If patient treatment is poor, people may avoid seeking help.","zh":"如果病人待遇差，人們可能避免求助。"},{"en":"This phrase concerns both medical care and human dignity.","zh":"這個片語涉及醫療照顧和人的尊嚴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"amount to little more than","meaning":"只不過是……","examples":[{"en":"Patient treatment amounted to little more than legitimised abuse.","zh":"病人待遇只不過是合法化虐待。"},{"en":"To amount to little more than something means to be almost only that bad or limited thing.","zh":"To amount to little more than something 指幾乎只是某種差劣或有限的東西。"},{"en":"A lesson with no explanation may amount to little more than copying notes.","zh":"沒有解釋的課堂可能只不過是抄筆記。"},{"en":"If a support scheme gives no real help, it amounts to little more than a name on paper.","zh":"如果支援計劃沒有真正幫助，它只不過是紙上的名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises something by saying it is far less valuable than it claims.","zh":"這個片語透過指出某事遠低於其聲稱價值來作批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"legitimised abuse","meaning":"合法化虐待","examples":[{"en":"The treatment of patients amounted to legitimised abuse.","zh":"對病人的待遇只不過是合法化虐待。"},{"en":"Legitimised abuse means mistreatment that is allowed, accepted, or protected by an official system.","zh":"Legitimised abuse 指被正式制度容許、接受或保護的虐待。"},{"en":"If workers are punished unfairly under company rules, that may feel like legitimised abuse.","zh":"如果工人在公司規則下被不公平懲罰，那可能像合法化虐待。"},{"en":"When a system excuses cruelty, victims may have no easy way to complain.","zh":"當制度為殘酷行為開脫，受害者可能沒有簡單途徑投訴。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when abuse is treated as normal or lawful.","zh":"這個片語用於虐待被視為正常或合法的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"inmates","meaning":"院友；被收容者","examples":[{"en":"Inmates were beaten and forced to live in unsanitary conditions.","zh":"院友被毆打，並被迫住在不衛生環境中。"},{"en":"Inmates are people kept inside an institution, prison, or similar place.","zh":"Inmates 指被留在院舍、監獄或類似地方的人。"},{"en":"Inmates in a care institution should still be treated as human beings with rights.","zh":"照顧院舍中的院友仍應被視為有權利的人。"},{"en":"If inmates are locked away without proper care, abuse becomes easier to hide.","zh":"如果院友在沒有適當照顧下被鎖起來，虐待就更容易被隱藏。"},{"en":"This word often suggests people who have limited freedom.","zh":"這個詞通常暗示人們自由受限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be forced to","meaning":"被迫去……","examples":[{"en":"Inmates were forced to live in unsanitary conditions.","zh":"院友被迫住在不衛生環境中。"},{"en":"To be forced to do something means to have no real choice but to do it.","zh":"To be forced to do something 指沒有真正選擇，只能做某事。"},{"en":"Students may be forced to study online if a school building becomes unsafe.","zh":"如果校舍變得不安全，學生可能被迫上網課。"},{"en":"If patients are forced to obey rules without explanation, they may feel powerless.","zh":"如果病人被迫在沒有解釋下服從規則，他們可能感到無力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows pressure, lack of choice, or compulsion.","zh":"這個片語顯示壓力、缺乏選擇或強迫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"unsanitary conditions","meaning":"不衛生的環境","examples":[{"en":"Many patients lived in unsanitary conditions.","zh":"許多病人住在不衛生的環境中。"},{"en":"Unsanitary conditions are dirty or unhealthy conditions that can spread disease.","zh":"Unsanitary conditions 是骯髒或不健康、可能傳播疾病的環境。"},{"en":"A restaurant kitchen with insects and spoiled food has unsanitary conditions.","zh":"有昆蟲和變壞食物的餐廳廚房是不衛生的環境。"},{"en":"If patients live in unsanitary conditions, infections may spread quickly.","zh":"如果病人住在不衛生環境中，感染可能迅速擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes surroundings that are unsafe for health.","zh":"這個片語描述對健康不安全的周遭環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be placed on display","meaning":"被展示出來","examples":[{"en":"Some patients were placed on display to a curious public.","zh":"一些病人被展示給好奇的公眾觀看。"},{"en":"To be placed on display means to be shown publicly, often for others to look at.","zh":"To be placed on display 指被公開展示，通常讓別人觀看。"},{"en":"Artworks are placed on display in museums so visitors can view them.","zh":"藝術品在博物館被展示出來，讓訪客觀賞。"},{"en":"If vulnerable people are placed on display, they may be treated as objects rather than people.","zh":"如果脆弱人士被展示出來，他們可能被當作物件而不是人。"},{"en":"This phrase can be neutral for objects but cruel when used about people.","zh":"這個片語用於物件時可以中性，但用於人時可能很殘酷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a curious public","meaning":"好奇的公眾","examples":[{"en":"Patients were displayed to a curious public as a sideshow.","zh":"病人被當作旁枝節目展示給好奇的公眾。"},{"en":"A curious public means members of the public who are eager to look, know, or be entertained.","zh":"Curious public 指急於觀看、了解或尋求娛樂的公眾。"},{"en":"A celebrity scandal may attract a curious public even when privacy is being harmed.","zh":"名人醜聞可能吸引好奇的公眾，即使私隱正被傷害。"},{"en":"If a hospital displays patients to a curious public, it violates their dignity.","zh":"如果醫院把病人展示給好奇的公眾，就是侵犯他們的尊嚴。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest interest, but also intrusive or insensitive attention.","zh":"這個片語可以表示興趣，也可暗示侵犯性或冷漠的關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as a sideshow","meaning":"作為助興表演；作為旁枝節目","examples":[{"en":"Some patients were treated as a sideshow for visitors.","zh":"一些病人被當作訪客的助興表演。"},{"en":"As a sideshow means as a minor entertainment or spectacle rather than as the main serious matter.","zh":"As a sideshow 指被當作次要娛樂或奇觀，而不是嚴肅主題。"},{"en":"A serious debate should not be treated as a sideshow for online attention.","zh":"嚴肅辯論不應被當作博取網上注意的旁枝節目。"},{"en":"If patients are treated as a sideshow, their suffering is turned into entertainment.","zh":"如果病人被當作助興表演，他們的痛苦就被變成娛樂。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises situations where people ignore the real human issue.","zh":"這個片語批評人們忽視真正人道問題的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"there is little indication to suggest","meaning":"幾乎沒有跡象顯示","examples":[{"en":"There is little indication to suggest that other institutions were much better.","zh":"幾乎沒有跡象顯示其他機構好得多。"},{"en":"There is little indication to suggest means there is little evidence showing that something is true.","zh":"There is little indication to suggest 指幾乎沒有證據顯示某事為真。"},{"en":"There is little indication to suggest that the new rule has improved student behaviour.","zh":"幾乎沒有跡象顯示新規則改善了學生行為。"},{"en":"If no records show improvement, it is hard to claim the system worked well.","zh":"如果沒有紀錄顯示改善，就很難聲稱制度運作良好。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when evidence is weak or missing.","zh":"這個片語用於證據薄弱或缺失的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be founded at around the same time","meaning":"大約同一時期成立","examples":[{"en":"Other institutions founded at around the same time were probably not much better.","zh":"大約同一時期成立的其他機構可能也沒有好得多。"},{"en":"To be founded at around the same time means to be established during roughly the same period.","zh":"To be founded at around the same time 指在大致相同時期成立。"},{"en":"Two schools founded at around the same time may share similar traditions.","zh":"兩間大約同一時期成立的學校可能有相似傳統。"},{"en":"If institutions are founded in the same historical period, they may reflect similar attitudes.","zh":"如果機構在同一歷史時期成立，它們可能反映相似態度。"},{"en":"This phrase compares when organisations began.","zh":"這個片語比較組織成立的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"much better","meaning":"好得多","examples":[{"en":"There is little indication that other institutions were much better.","zh":"幾乎沒有跡象顯示其他機構好得多。"},{"en":"Much better means clearly or significantly better, not just slightly improved.","zh":"Much better 指明顯或大幅較好，而不只是稍微改善。"},{"en":"A student’s essay becomes much better when examples are specific and organised.","zh":"當例子具體且有組織，學生作文會好得多。"},{"en":"If care homes become much better, residents may feel safer and more respected.","zh":"如果護理院舍好得多，住客可能感到更安全和更受尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a real improvement in quality.","zh":"這個片語突出質素上的真正改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"until the mid-twentieth century","meaning":"直到二十世紀中期","examples":[{"en":"Until the mid-twentieth century, mental institutions were often places of isolation.","zh":"直到二十世紀中期，精神病院通常是隔離的地方。"},{"en":"Until the mid-twentieth century means up to about the middle of the 1900s.","zh":"Until the mid-twentieth century 指一直到約二十世紀中段。"},{"en":"Until the mid-twentieth century, many homes did not have modern appliances.","zh":"直到二十世紀中期，許多家庭仍沒有現代電器。"},{"en":"If a practice continued until the mid-twentieth century, it lasted much longer than many students expect.","zh":"如果某做法持續到二十世紀中期，它比許多學生想像中更長久。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a historical time limit.","zh":"這個片語給出歷史時間界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"institutions for the mentally ill","meaning":"精神病院；精神病患者收容機構","examples":[{"en":"Institutions for the mentally ill were once viewed as places of isolation.","zh":"精神病患者收容機構曾被視為隔離之地。"},{"en":"Institutions for the mentally ill are hospitals or facilities created to house and treat people with mental illness.","zh":"Institutions for the mentally ill 是為收容和治療精神病患者而設的醫院或設施。"},{"en":"Some old institutions for the mentally ill separated patients from ordinary community life.","zh":"一些舊精神病院把病人與普通社區生活分隔開。"},{"en":"If such institutions focus only on control, patients may lose independence.","zh":"如果這類機構只着重控制，病人可能失去獨立性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal places of mental-health care or confinement.","zh":"這個片語指正式的精神健康照顧或收容場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be regarded more as…than as…","meaning":"與其說是……不如說是……","examples":[{"en":"These institutions were regarded more as places of punishment than as places of healing.","zh":"這些機構與其說是治療之地，不如說是懲罰之地。"},{"en":"To be regarded more as A than as B means people see something mainly as A, not B.","zh":"To be regarded more as A than as B 指人們主要把某事看成 A，而不是 B。"},{"en":"Some exams are regarded more as pressure tests than as learning tools.","zh":"有些考試與其說是學習工具，不如說是壓力測試。"},{"en":"If a hospital is regarded more as a prison than as a clinic, patients will fear it.","zh":"如果醫院與其說是診所，不如說是監獄，病人會害怕它。"},{"en":"This structure shows contrast between how something is seen and how it should perhaps be seen.","zh":"這個結構顯示某物如何被看待與它或許應如何被看待之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"places of isolation and punishment","meaning":"隔離和懲罰的地方","examples":[{"en":"Many institutions were places of isolation and punishment.","zh":"許多機構是隔離和懲罰的地方。"},{"en":"Places of isolation and punishment are places where people are separated from society and treated harshly.","zh":"Places of isolation and punishment 是人們被隔離於社會之外並受到嚴厲對待的地方。"},{"en":"A badly run facility may become a place of isolation and punishment instead of support.","zh":"管理差劣的設施可能變成隔離和懲罰的地方，而不是支援場所。"},{"en":"If patients are hidden away and controlled, recovery becomes harder.","zh":"如果病人被藏起來並受控制，康復會更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests harsh confinement rather than care.","zh":"這個片語暗示嚴酷禁閉，而不是照顧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"places of healing and solace","meaning":"治療和慰藉的地方","examples":[{"en":"Institutions should have been places of healing and solace.","zh":"這些機構本應是治療和慰藉的地方。"},{"en":"Places of healing and solace are places where people recover and find comfort.","zh":"Places of healing and solace 是人們恢復健康並得到安慰的地方。"},{"en":"A good clinic should be a place of healing and solace for worried patients.","zh":"好診所應成為憂心病人的治療和慰藉之地。"},{"en":"If staff listen kindly, even a hospital can feel less frightening.","zh":"如果職員友善聆聽，即使醫院也可以不那麼可怕。"},{"en":"This phrase describes care that treats both illness and emotional pain.","zh":"這個片語描述同時照顧疾病和情緒痛苦的護理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"popular literature","meaning":"通俗文學","examples":[{"en":"Popular literature of the Victorian era reflected true-life events.","zh":"維多利亞時代的通俗文學反映真實事件。"},{"en":"Popular literature means books and stories read by many ordinary people.","zh":"Popular literature 指許多普通人閱讀的書籍和故事。"},{"en":"Crime novels are a form of popular literature because many readers enjoy them.","zh":"犯罪小說是一種通俗文學，因為許多讀者喜歡。"},{"en":"If popular literature reflects social fears, it can show what people worried about at the time.","zh":"如果通俗文學反映社會恐懼，它可以顯示當時人們擔心甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to widely read writing, not only high academic literature.","zh":"這個片語指被廣泛閱讀的文字，不只是高深學術文學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Victorian era","meaning":"維多利亞時代","examples":[{"en":"The Victorian era produced many stories about madhouses.","zh":"維多利亞時代產生了許多關於瘋人院的故事。"},{"en":"The Victorian era was the period of Queen Victoria’s reign in Britain.","zh":"Victorian era 是英國維多利亞女王統治的時期。"},{"en":"A history lesson on the Victorian era may discuss factories, poverty, empire, and social reform.","zh":"關於維多利亞時代的歷史課可能討論工廠、貧窮、帝國和社會改革。"},{"en":"If a novel was written in the Victorian era, it may reflect the values and fears of that time.","zh":"如果小說寫於維多利亞時代，它可能反映當時的價值觀和恐懼。"},{"en":"This phrase places events in nineteenth-century British history.","zh":"這個片語把事件放在十九世紀英國歷史中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reflect true-life events","meaning":"反映真實事件","examples":[{"en":"Some Victorian literature reflected true-life events.","zh":"一些維多利亞時代文學反映真實事件。"},{"en":"To reflect true-life events means to show or be influenced by things that really happened.","zh":"To reflect true-life events 指呈現或受到真實發生事情影響。"},{"en":"A film about school bullying may reflect true-life events from students’ experiences.","zh":"關於校園欺凌的電影可能反映學生經歷中的真實事件。"},{"en":"If fiction reflects real events, readers may understand society more deeply.","zh":"如果小說反映真實事件，讀者可能更深入理解社會。"},{"en":"This phrase links stories with reality.","zh":"這個片語把故事與現實連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be sent to the madhouse","meaning":"被送進瘋人院","examples":[{"en":"Unwanted relatives were sometimes sent to the madhouse.","zh":"不受歡迎的親人有時被送進瘋人院。"},{"en":"To be sent to the madhouse means to be placed in an old mental institution.","zh":"To be sent to the madhouse 指被送入舊式精神病院。"},{"en":"In old stories, a difficult family member might be sent to the madhouse unfairly.","zh":"在舊故事中，難相處的家庭成員可能被不公平地送進瘋人院。"},{"en":"If institutions were misused, people could be removed from family life without proper medical reason.","zh":"如果機構被濫用，人們可能在沒有適當醫療理由下被移離家庭生活。"},{"en":"This phrase reflects old and often cruel attitudes toward mental illness.","zh":"這個片語反映過去對精神病的古老且常常殘酷的態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as a legal means of","meaning":"作為……的合法手段","examples":[{"en":"The madhouse was sometimes used as a legal means of removing unwanted people.","zh":"瘋人院有時被用作移除不受歡迎人士的合法手段。"},{"en":"As a legal means of something means as a method allowed or protected by law.","zh":"As a legal means of something 指作為法律容許或保護的方法。"},{"en":"A contract can serve as a legal means of protecting both employer and worker.","zh":"合約可以作為保護僱主和工人的合法手段。"},{"en":"If a legal method is used unfairly, it can still cause serious harm.","zh":"如果合法方法被不公平使用，它仍可造成嚴重傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how law can be used to achieve a purpose.","zh":"這個片語解釋法律如何被用來達到某目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"permanently disposing of","meaning":"永久除掉……","examples":[{"en":"Some people used institutions for permanently disposing of an unwanted heir or spouse.","zh":"有些人用機構來永久除掉不受歡迎的繼承人或配偶。"},{"en":"Permanently disposing of someone means removing them in a lasting and often cruel way.","zh":"Permanently disposing of someone 指以長久且通常殘酷的方式移除某人。"},{"en":"A family in an old novel may try to dispose of an inconvenient relative by sending him away.","zh":"舊小說中的家庭可能試圖把麻煩親人送走來除掉他。"},{"en":"If a person is locked away permanently, they lose control over their own life.","zh":"如果一個人被永久關起來，他就失去對自己人生的控制。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds cold because it treats a person like a problem to be removed.","zh":"這個片語聽起來冷酷，因為它把人當成要移除的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"an unwanted heir or spouse","meaning":"不受歡迎的繼承人或配偶","examples":[{"en":"An unwanted heir or spouse could be sent away permanently.","zh":"不受歡迎的繼承人或配偶可能被永久送走。"},{"en":"An unwanted heir or spouse is a family member whom others see as inconvenient or undesirable.","zh":"An unwanted heir or spouse 是被其他人視為麻煩或不受歡迎的家庭成員。"},{"en":"In old inheritance disputes, an unwanted heir might be treated as a threat.","zh":"在舊式繼承糾紛中，不受歡迎的繼承人可能被視為威脅。"},{"en":"If legal systems are abused, vulnerable relatives can be removed for others’ benefit.","zh":"如果法律制度被濫用，脆弱親人可能為了他人利益而被移除。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how family power could be used selfishly.","zh":"這個片語顯示家庭權力如何可能被自私使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"carry out invasive brain surgery","meaning":"進行入侵性腦部手術","examples":[{"en":"Some institutions carried out invasive brain surgery on violent patients.","zh":"一些機構在有暴力傾向的病人身上進行入侵性腦部手術。"},{"en":"To carry out invasive brain surgery means to perform an operation that enters or alters the brain.","zh":"To carry out invasive brain surgery 指進行進入或改變腦部的手術。"},{"en":"Doctors should carry out serious surgery only when there is strong medical justification.","zh":"醫生只有在有充分醫療理由時才應進行嚴重手術。"},{"en":"If surgery is done without consent, it becomes a serious violation of patient rights.","zh":"如果手術未經同意進行，就是嚴重侵犯病人權利。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major medical procedure, not a simple treatment.","zh":"這個片語描述重大醫療程序，而不是簡單治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"invasive brain surgery","meaning":"入侵性腦部手術","examples":[{"en":"A lobotomy was an invasive brain surgery.","zh":"腦葉切除術是一種入侵性腦部手術。"},{"en":"Invasive brain surgery is an operation that physically enters or changes brain tissue.","zh":"Invasive brain surgery 是實際進入或改變腦組織的手術。"},{"en":"In modern medicine, invasive brain surgery requires careful testing, consent, and specialist skill.","zh":"在現代醫學中，入侵性腦部手術需要仔細檢查、同意和專科技術。"},{"en":"If invasive brain surgery damages healthy tissue, the effects can be permanent.","zh":"如果入侵性腦部手術損害健康組織，影響可以是永久性的。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a high-risk medical operation.","zh":"這個片語暗示高風險醫療手術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"known as a lobotomy","meaning":"稱為腦葉切除術","examples":[{"en":"Institutions carried out invasive brain surgery known as a lobotomy.","zh":"機構進行稱為腦葉切除術的入侵性腦部手術。"},{"en":"Known as a lobotomy means called by the medical name “lobotomy.”","zh":"Known as a lobotomy 指被稱為 “lobotomy” 這個醫學名稱。"},{"en":"A lobotomy was once used to alter patients’ behaviour by cutting parts of the brain.","zh":"腦葉切除術曾被用來透過切割腦部部分來改變病人行為。"},{"en":"If a treatment known as a lobotomy left patients damaged, later criticism was unavoidable.","zh":"如果稱為腦葉切除術的治療令病人受損，後來的批評就無可避免。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the specific name of a controversial operation.","zh":"這個片語引出一項具爭議手術的特定名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"violent patients","meaning":"有暴力傾向的病人","examples":[{"en":"Lobotomies were sometimes performed on violent patients.","zh":"腦葉切除術有時在有暴力傾向的病人身上進行。"},{"en":"Violent patients are patients whose behaviour may seriously harm themselves or others.","zh":"Violent patients 是其行為可能嚴重傷害自己或他人的病人。"},{"en":"A hospital must protect staff and other patients when caring for violent patients.","zh":"醫院照顧有暴力傾向的病人時，必須保護職員和其他病人。"},{"en":"If violent patients are treated only with force, their deeper needs may be ignored.","zh":"如果只用武力處理有暴力傾向的病人，其更深層需要可能被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes risk behaviour, not a person’s full identity.","zh":"這個片語描述風險行為，而不是一個人的完整身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"without their consent","meaning":"未經他們同意","examples":[{"en":"Some patients underwent surgery without their consent.","zh":"一些病人在未經他們同意下接受手術。"},{"en":"Without their consent means without their clear permission or agreement.","zh":"Without their consent 指沒有得到他們清楚許可或同意。"},{"en":"A doctor should not share a patient’s private information without their consent.","zh":"醫生不應在未經病人同意下分享其私人資料。"},{"en":"If someone is treated without consent, their rights and autonomy are violated.","zh":"如果某人在未經同意下接受治療，其權利和自主會被侵犯。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in medical, legal, and personal situations.","zh":"這個片語在醫療、法律和個人情況中都重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the aim was to","meaning":"目的在於","examples":[{"en":"The aim was to calm the patient.","zh":"目的在於令病人平靜。"},{"en":"The aim was to means the purpose was to do something.","zh":"The aim was to 指目的在於做某事。"},{"en":"The aim was to reduce waiting time by adding more staff.","zh":"目的在於透過增加人手來減少等候時間。"},{"en":"If the aim is good but the method is harmful, the policy still deserves criticism.","zh":"如果目的良好但方法有害，政策仍值得批評。"},{"en":"This phrase explains intention or purpose.","zh":"這個片語解釋意圖或目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"calm the patient","meaning":"令病人平靜","examples":[{"en":"The procedure was intended to calm the patient.","zh":"這項程序旨在令病人平靜。"},{"en":"To calm the patient means to reduce the patient’s fear, agitation, or distress.","zh":"To calm the patient 指減少病人的恐懼、激動或痛苦。"},{"en":"A nurse may calm the patient by speaking slowly and explaining each step.","zh":"護士可能透過慢慢說話和解釋每一步來令病人平靜。"},{"en":"If a patient feels safe, they may become calmer without force.","zh":"如果病人感到安全，他們可能不用武力也能變得較平靜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing distress, ideally through humane care.","zh":"這個片語描述減少痛苦，理想上透過人道照顧做到。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the procedure","meaning":"這項程序；這項手術","examples":[{"en":"The procedure could leave the patient seriously damaged.","zh":"這項程序可能令病人嚴重受損。"},{"en":"The procedure means the medical operation or formal method being discussed.","zh":"The procedure 指正在討論的醫療手術或正式方法。"},{"en":"Before a procedure, doctors should explain the risks clearly.","zh":"在程序前，醫生應清楚解釋風險。"},{"en":"If the procedure is unsafe, the patient may suffer lasting harm.","zh":"如果這項程序不安全，病人可能遭受持久傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific action carried out step by step.","zh":"這個片語指按步驟執行的特定行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"leave someone little more than","meaning":"令某人變得幾乎只是……","examples":[{"en":"The procedure could leave the patient little more than a zombie.","zh":"這項程序可能令病人變得幾乎只是行屍走肉。"},{"en":"To leave someone little more than something means to reduce them almost to that state.","zh":"To leave someone little more than something 指令某人幾乎變成某種狀態。"},{"en":"Exhausting work can leave a person little more than a machine if they never rest.","zh":"如果一個人從不休息，耗人的工作可以令他幾乎變成機器。"},{"en":"If a treatment destroys someone’s personality, it may leave them unable to live normally.","zh":"如果治療摧毀某人的人格，它可能令其無法正常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly criticises damage to a person’s humanity or ability.","zh":"這個片語強烈批評對人的人性或能力造成的損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a zombie","meaning":"行屍走肉般的人","examples":[{"en":"The patient could be left little more than a zombie.","zh":"病人可能被弄得幾乎只是行屍走肉。"},{"en":"A zombie here means a person who seems alive but has lost energy, awareness, or personality.","zh":"A zombie 在這裏指看似活着但失去精力、意識或人格的人。"},{"en":"After working all night, a student may feel like a zombie in class.","zh":"通宵工作後，學生上課時可能感覺像行屍走肉。"},{"en":"If medication is too strong, a patient may become passive and unresponsive.","zh":"如果藥物太強，病人可能變得被動且沒有反應。"},{"en":"This word is used metaphorically here, not literally as a monster.","zh":"這個詞在這裏是比喻用法，不是真的怪物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"devastating effects","meaning":"災難性的影響","examples":[{"en":"The procedure’s devastating effects were later widely discussed.","zh":"這項程序的災難性影響後來被廣泛討論。"},{"en":"Devastating effects are extremely damaging results that cause serious harm.","zh":"Devastating effects 是造成嚴重傷害的極具破壞性結果。"},{"en":"A serious fire can have devastating effects on a family’s home and savings.","zh":"嚴重火災可以對家庭住所和儲蓄造成災難性影響。"},{"en":"If a treatment damages memory, speech, and personality, its effects are devastating.","zh":"如果治療損害記憶、說話和人格，其影響就是災難性的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harm that is deep and difficult to recover from.","zh":"這個片語描述深遠且難以恢復的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be well documented in","meaning":"在……中有充分記錄","examples":[{"en":"The devastating effects are well documented in the film.","zh":"這些災難性影響在電影中有充分記錄。"},{"en":"To be well documented in something means to be clearly recorded or shown there.","zh":"To be well documented in something 指在某處被清楚記錄或展示。"},{"en":"The school’s improvement is well documented in inspection reports.","zh":"學校的改善在視學報告中有充分記錄。"},{"en":"If abuse is well documented, it becomes harder for officials to deny it.","zh":"如果虐待有充分記錄，官員就更難否認。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that evidence is detailed and available.","zh":"這個片語顯示證據詳細且可查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"One Flew Over the Cuckoo’s Nest","meaning":"《飛越瘋人院》","examples":[{"en":"One Flew Over the Cuckoo’s Nest shows the devastating effects of such treatment.","zh":"《飛越瘋人院》展示這類治療的災難性影響。"},{"en":"One Flew Over the Cuckoo’s Nest is a famous film often linked with criticism of psychiatric institutions.","zh":"One Flew Over the Cuckoo’s Nest 是一部常與批評精神病院制度相關的著名電影。"},{"en":"A film class may discuss One Flew Over the Cuckoo’s Nest when studying power and patient rights.","zh":"電影課研究權力和病人權利時，可能討論《飛越瘋人院》。"},{"en":"If a story makes viewers feel the cruelty of a system, it can influence public debate.","zh":"如果故事令觀眾感受到制度的殘酷，它可以影響公共討論。"},{"en":"This title is used as a cultural reference to harsh institutional treatment.","zh":"這個片名被用作對嚴酷院舍待遇的文化參照。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"little wonder then that","meaning":"難怪","examples":[{"en":"Little wonder then that such treatment led to calls for change.","zh":"難怪這類待遇引發改革呼聲。"},{"en":"Little wonder then that means it is not surprising that something happened.","zh":"Little wonder then that 指某事發生並不令人驚訝。"},{"en":"Little wonder then that parents complained after the school ignored safety warnings.","zh":"學校忽視安全警告後，難怪家長投訴。"},{"en":"If patients were abused for years, it is natural that reformers demanded change.","zh":"如果病人多年受虐，改革者要求改變是自然的。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a predictable reaction to a serious situation.","zh":"這個片語引出對嚴重情況的可預期反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"appalling catalogue of treatment","meaning":"一連串駭人的待遇","examples":[{"en":"The appalling catalogue of treatment shocked social activists.","zh":"一連串駭人的待遇震驚社會運動人士。"},{"en":"An appalling catalogue of treatment means a long list of shocking and cruel ways people were treated.","zh":"Appalling catalogue of treatment 指一長串令人震驚且殘酷的對待方式。"},{"en":"A report may reveal an appalling catalogue of treatment in a badly run care home.","zh":"報告可能揭露管理差劣護理院中的一連串駭人待遇。"},{"en":"If abuses happen repeatedly, they become a pattern rather than isolated mistakes.","zh":"如果虐待反覆發生，它們就成為模式，而不是個別錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses both the number and seriousness of wrong actions.","zh":"這個片語強調錯誤行為的數量和嚴重性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lead to a call for change","meaning":"引發改革呼聲","examples":[{"en":"The treatment of the mentally ill led to a call for change.","zh":"對精神病患者的待遇引發改革呼聲。"},{"en":"To lead to a call for change means to cause people to demand reform.","zh":"To lead to a call for change 指導致人們要求改革。"},{"en":"Repeated traffic accidents may lead to a call for change in road design.","zh":"反覆交通意外可能引發對道路設計改革的呼聲。"},{"en":"If a hospital scandal becomes public, families may call for better patient protection.","zh":"如果醫院醜聞曝光，家屬可能要求更好病人保障。"},{"en":"This phrase links a problem with public pressure for reform.","zh":"這個片語把問題與公眾改革壓力連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"social activists","meaning":"社會運動人士","examples":[{"en":"Social activists called for changes in mental-health treatment.","zh":"社會運動人士呼籲改變精神健康治療。"},{"en":"Social activists are people who campaign for changes in society.","zh":"Social activists 是為社會改變而推動運動的人。"},{"en":"Social activists may organise petitions, protests, or public education campaigns.","zh":"社會運動人士可能組織請願、示威或公眾教育活動。"},{"en":"If a law harms vulnerable people, social activists may pressure the government to amend it.","zh":"如果法律傷害弱勢人士，社會運動人士可能向政府施壓要求修訂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people who try to change unfair systems.","zh":"這個片語描述試圖改變不公平制度的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"psychologists alike","meaning":"心理學家也一樣","examples":[{"en":"Social activists and psychologists alike called for reform.","zh":"社會運動人士和心理學家也一樣呼籲改革。"},{"en":"Psychologists alike means psychologists also shared the same view or action.","zh":"Psychologists alike 指心理學家也持有同樣看法或採取同樣行動。"},{"en":"Parents and teachers alike worried about students’ sleep.","zh":"家長和老師也一樣擔心學生睡眠。"},{"en":"If doctors and nurses alike criticise a policy, the problem is probably serious.","zh":"如果醫生和護士也一樣批評某政策，問題可能很嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that more than one group agrees or acts in the same way.","zh":"這個片語顯示不止一個群體有相同看法或行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"improvements began","meaning":"改善開始","examples":[{"en":"Improvements began in institutions from the mid-1950s onwards.","zh":"從二十世紀五十年代中期開始，院舍內的改善開始出現。"},{"en":"Improvements began means things started to get better.","zh":"Improvements began 指事情開始變好。"},{"en":"Improvements began after the school listened to students’ complaints.","zh":"學校聆聽學生投訴後，改善開始了。"},{"en":"If extra staff are hired, improvements may begin in patient care.","zh":"如果聘請額外人手，病人照顧方面可能開始改善。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the starting point of positive change.","zh":"這個片語標示正面改變的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"from the mid-1950s onwards","meaning":"從二十世紀五十年代中期開始","examples":[{"en":"From the mid-1950s onwards, mental-health care began to improve.","zh":"從二十世紀五十年代中期開始，精神健康照顧開始改善。"},{"en":"From the mid-1950s onwards means starting around the middle of the 1950s and continuing after that.","zh":"From the mid-1950s onwards 指由1950年代中期左右開始，並在此後延續。"},{"en":"From the mid-1950s onwards, many countries expanded public healthcare.","zh":"從二十世紀五十年代中期開始，許多國家擴展公共醫療。"},{"en":"If a reform started from the mid-1950s onwards, it belongs to the post-war period.","zh":"如果改革從二十世紀五十年代中期開始，它屬於戰後時期。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a historical starting point and continuation.","zh":"這個片語給出歷史起點和延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"along with the introduction of","meaning":"伴隨……的引入","examples":[{"en":"Institutional improvements came along with the introduction of community care.","zh":"院舍改善伴隨社區照顧的引入而來。"},{"en":"Along with the introduction of something means happening together with the start of a new system or idea.","zh":"Along with the introduction of something 指與新制度或新想法的開始同時發生。"},{"en":"School results improved along with the introduction of smaller classes.","zh":"學校成績伴隨小班教學的引入而改善。"},{"en":"If support services grow along with a new policy, the policy is more likely to work.","zh":"如果支援服務伴隨新政策一起增長，政策較可能奏效。"},{"en":"This phrase connects one change with another new development.","zh":"這個片語把一項改變與另一新發展連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"less severely ill patients","meaning":"病情較輕的病人","examples":[{"en":"Care in the community was introduced for less severely ill patients.","zh":"社區照顧是為病情較輕的病人而引入的。"},{"en":"Less severely ill patients are patients whose condition is serious but not at the most dangerous level.","zh":"Less severely ill patients 指病情嚴重但未達最危險程度的病人。"},{"en":"A less severely ill patient may live at home if regular support is available.","zh":"如果有定期支援，病情較輕的病人可能住在家中。"},{"en":"If patients are less severely ill, community care may offer a better balance of freedom and safety.","zh":"如果病人病情較輕，社區照顧可能在自由和安全之間提供較好平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase compares different levels of illness.","zh":"這個片語比較不同病情程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"community care","meaning":"社區照顧","examples":[{"en":"Community care was seen as a more humane approach.","zh":"社區照顧被視為較人道的方法。"},{"en":"Community care is support given to people while they live in ordinary homes or neighbourhoods.","zh":"Community care 是在人們住在普通住所或社區時提供的支援。"},{"en":"Community care may include home visits, social workers, nurses, and day centres.","zh":"社區照顧可以包括家訪、社工、護士和日間中心。"},{"en":"If community care is properly funded, patients can avoid unnecessary institutional life.","zh":"如果社區照顧有適當資金，病人可以避免不必要的院舍生活。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on care outside large hospitals or institutions.","zh":"這個片語集中於大型醫院或院舍以外的照顧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be seen as","meaning":"被視為","examples":[{"en":"Community care was seen as a more humane way to help patients.","zh":"社區照顧被視為幫助病人的較人道方式。"},{"en":"To be seen as something means to be regarded or understood in that way.","zh":"To be seen as something 指被看作或理解為某事。"},{"en":"Homework can be seen as useful practice when it clearly connects to lessons.","zh":"如果功課清楚連接課堂，它可以被視為有用練習。"},{"en":"If a policy is seen as unfair, people may resist it.","zh":"如果政策被視為不公平，人們可能抗拒它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public opinion or interpretation.","zh":"這個片語描述公眾看法或詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a more humane and purposeful approach","meaning":"更人道且更有目的的方法","examples":[{"en":"Community care was seen as a more humane and purposeful approach.","zh":"社區照顧被視為更人道且更有目的的方法。"},{"en":"A more humane and purposeful approach is a kinder method with a clear aim.","zh":"More humane and purposeful approach 是較仁慈且有清晰目的的方法。"},{"en":"A school may use a more humane approach by supporting weak students instead of simply punishing them.","zh":"學校可以透過支援弱學生而非只是懲罰他們，採用較人道的方法。"},{"en":"If care has a clear purpose, patients are more likely to receive the right help.","zh":"如果照顧有清晰目的，病人更可能得到適當幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts thoughtful support with harsh control.","zh":"這個片語把有思想的支援與嚴厲控制作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dealing with","meaning":"處理；應對","examples":[{"en":"Community care offered a different way of dealing with the mentally ill.","zh":"社區照顧提供了另一種處理精神病患者的方法。"},{"en":"Dealing with something means handling, managing, or responding to it.","zh":"Dealing with something 指處理、管理或回應某事。"},{"en":"Teachers need calm methods for dealing with conflict between students.","zh":"老師需要冷靜方法來處理學生之間的衝突。"},{"en":"If a problem is dealt with early, it may not become serious.","zh":"如果問題及早處理，它可能不會變嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical response to a person, issue, or situation.","zh":"這個片語描述對人、問題或情況的實際回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"whereas","meaning":"然而；相比之下","examples":[{"en":"Whereas institutionalised patients lived in confinement, community patients had more freedom.","zh":"被收容於院舍的病人在禁閉中生活，相比之下，社區病人有更多自由。"},{"en":"Whereas introduces a contrast between two facts or groups.","zh":"Whereas 引出兩個事實或群體之間的對比。"},{"en":"Some students prefer quiet study, whereas others learn better in discussion.","zh":"有些學生喜歡安靜溫習，然而另一些人在討論中學得更好。"},{"en":"Whereas institutions may provide control, community care may provide independence.","zh":"院舍可能提供控制，相比之下，社區照顧可能提供獨立。"},{"en":"This word helps compare two different situations clearly.","zh":"這個詞幫助清楚比較兩種不同情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"institutionalised patients","meaning":"被收容於院舍的病人","examples":[{"en":"Institutionalised patients lived under strict rules.","zh":"被收容於院舍的病人生活在嚴格規則之下。"},{"en":"Institutionalised patients are patients who live inside hospitals or care institutions for long periods.","zh":"Institutionalised patients 指長期住在醫院或照顧院舍內的病人。"},{"en":"Institutionalised patients may lose confidence in making everyday decisions.","zh":"被收容於院舍的病人可能失去作日常決定的信心。"},{"en":"If people spend years in institutions, returning to ordinary life can be difficult.","zh":"如果人們在院舍中度過多年，回到普通生活可能困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes patients shaped by long-term institutional living.","zh":"這個片語描述受長期院舍生活影響的病人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"live out their existence","meaning":"在……中度過一生","examples":[{"en":"Some patients lived out their existence in confinement.","zh":"一些病人在禁閉中度過一生。"},{"en":"To live out one’s existence means to spend one’s life in a particular condition, often sadly or passively.","zh":"To live out one’s existence 指在某種狀態中度過人生，通常帶有悲傷或被動感。"},{"en":"No one should live out their existence in a room without friendship or purpose.","zh":"沒有人應在沒有友誼或目的的房間中度過一生。"},{"en":"If patients are isolated for years, life becomes survival rather than growth.","zh":"如果病人多年被孤立，人生就變成生存而不是成長。"},{"en":"This phrase often sounds bleak because it suggests a limited life.","zh":"這個片語通常聽起來沉重，因為它暗示受限制的人生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in confinement","meaning":"在禁閉中；被隔離","examples":[{"en":"Institutionalised patients often lived in confinement.","zh":"被收容於院舍的病人常在禁閉中生活。"},{"en":"In confinement means kept in a restricted place with limited freedom.","zh":"In confinement 指被留在受限制的地方，只有有限自由。"},{"en":"A person in confinement may not be able to leave, choose visitors, or follow normal routines.","zh":"被禁閉的人可能不能離開、選擇訪客或跟隨正常日常生活。"},{"en":"If patients live in confinement for too long, social confidence may decline.","zh":"如果病人在禁閉中生活太久，社交信心可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical restriction and social separation.","zh":"這個片語描述身體限制和社會分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be forced to obey","meaning":"被迫服從","examples":[{"en":"Patients were forced to obey institutional regulations.","zh":"病人被迫服從院舍規則。"},{"en":"To be forced to obey means to have no choice but to follow rules or orders.","zh":"To be forced to obey 指沒有選擇，只能遵守規則或命令。"},{"en":"Children may feel powerless if they are forced to obey rules they do not understand.","zh":"如果孩子被迫服從自己不理解的規則，他們可能感到無力。"},{"en":"If patients are forced to obey without discussion, trust in staff may weaken.","zh":"如果病人在沒有討論下被迫服從，對職員的信任可能減弱。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights control rather than voluntary cooperation.","zh":"這個片語突出控制，而不是自願合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"institutional regulations","meaning":"院舍規則","examples":[{"en":"Patients had to obey institutional regulations.","zh":"病人必須服從院舍規則。"},{"en":"Institutional regulations are official rules used inside an organisation or facility.","zh":"Institutional regulations 是機構或設施內使用的正式規則。"},{"en":"Hospital regulations may cover visiting hours, medicine storage, and hygiene.","zh":"醫院規則可能涵蓋探病時間、藥物儲存和衛生。"},{"en":"If institutional regulations are too harsh, they can reduce dignity and independence.","zh":"如果院舍規則太嚴苛，它們可以降低尊嚴和獨立性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to rules that govern life inside an institution.","zh":"這個片語指管理院舍內生活的規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a relatively independent life","meaning":"相對獨立的生活","examples":[{"en":"Patients in the community could live a relatively independent life.","zh":"社區中的病人可以過相對獨立的生活。"},{"en":"A relatively independent life is a life with some freedom and self-control, though support may still be needed.","zh":"Relatively independent life 是有一定自由和自我控制、但可能仍需支援的生活。"},{"en":"An elderly person may live a relatively independent life with home-care visits.","zh":"長者如果有家居照顧探訪，可能過相對獨立的生活。"},{"en":"If patients can shop, cook, and manage appointments, they gain confidence.","zh":"如果病人能購物、煮食和管理預約，他們會建立信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes partial independence, not complete absence of help.","zh":"這個片語描述部分獨立，而不是完全沒有幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be meant to","meaning":"旨在；理應","examples":[{"en":"The patient was not meant to be left entirely alone.","zh":"病人理應不是被完全獨自留下。"},{"en":"To be meant to do something means to be intended or supposed to do it.","zh":"To be meant to do something 指旨在或理應做某事。"},{"en":"Homework is meant to help students practise, not to punish them.","zh":"功課旨在幫助學生練習，而不是懲罰他們。"},{"en":"If community care is meant to support patients, services must be easy to reach.","zh":"如果社區照顧旨在支援病人，服務就必須容易取得。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the intended purpose of an action or system.","zh":"這個片語解釋行動或制度的原本目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be left entirely to their own devices","meaning":"完全任由自己處理","examples":[{"en":"Patients were not meant to be left entirely to their own devices.","zh":"病人理應不會被完全任由自己處理。"},{"en":"To be left entirely to one’s own devices means to be left without help, guidance, or supervision.","zh":"To be left entirely to one’s own devices 指在沒有幫助、指導或監督下被留下。"},{"en":"A new employee should not be left entirely to their own devices on the first day.","zh":"新員工第一天不應被完全任由自己處理。"},{"en":"If vulnerable patients are left alone, they may miss medication or avoid help.","zh":"如果脆弱病人被獨自留下，他們可能忘記服藥或避免求助。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests neglect rather than healthy independence.","zh":"這個片語暗示忽視，而不是健康獨立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a variety of services","meaning":"各種服務","examples":[{"en":"A variety of services could theoretically be accessed.","zh":"理論上可以取得各種服務。"},{"en":"A variety of services means several different kinds of support or help.","zh":"A variety of services 指幾種不同形式的支援或幫助。"},{"en":"A community centre may offer a variety of services, such as counselling, classes, and job advice.","zh":"社區中心可能提供各種服務，例如輔導、課程和求職建議。"},{"en":"If patients can access a variety of services, their needs can be met more fully.","zh":"如果病人能取得各種服務，其需要可以更全面被滿足。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that support is not limited to one form.","zh":"這個片語顯示支援不限於單一形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"theoretically","meaning":"理論上","examples":[{"en":"Patients could theoretically access several support services.","zh":"病人理論上可以取得幾種支援服務。"},{"en":"Theoretically means in theory, though it may not always happen in real life.","zh":"Theoretically 指在理論上，雖然現實中不一定發生。"},{"en":"A student can theoretically finish homework in one hour, but distractions may make it longer.","zh":"學生理論上可以一小時完成功課，但分心可能令時間更長。"},{"en":"If services exist only theoretically, patients may still fail to receive help.","zh":"如果服務只是在理論上存在，病人仍可能得不到幫助。"},{"en":"This word often contrasts official possibility with practical reality.","zh":"這個詞常把官方可能性與實際現實作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be accessed","meaning":"可被使用；可被取得","examples":[{"en":"Support services could be accessed by patients in the community.","zh":"社區中的病人可以取得支援服務。"},{"en":"To be accessed means to be reached, used, or obtained.","zh":"To be accessed 指能夠到達、使用或取得。"},{"en":"Online lessons can be accessed from home if students have internet.","zh":"如果學生有互聯網，他們可以在家使用網上課堂。"},{"en":"If mental-health services cannot be accessed easily, patients may delay seeking help.","zh":"如果精神健康服務不易取得，病人可能延遲求助。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether people can actually use a service.","zh":"這個片語集中於人們是否真的能使用服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in its early stages","meaning":"在初期階段","examples":[{"en":"In its early stages, community care relied heavily on families.","zh":"在初期階段，社區照顧非常依賴家庭。"},{"en":"In its early stages means during the first period of development.","zh":"In its early stages 指在最初發展時期。"},{"en":"In its early stages, a new business may depend on friends and family for support.","zh":"在初期階段，新企業可能依靠朋友和家人支援。"},{"en":"If a policy lacks resources in its early stages, problems may appear quickly.","zh":"如果政策在初期階段缺乏資源，問題可能很快出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning phase of a system or project.","zh":"這個片語描述制度或項目的開始階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"consist primarily of","meaning":"主要由……組成","examples":[{"en":"Early community care consisted primarily of help from relatives.","zh":"早期社區照顧主要由親屬幫助組成。"},{"en":"To consist primarily of something means to be made mainly of that thing.","zh":"To consist primarily of something 指主要由某事物組成。"},{"en":"A beginner English course may consist primarily of speaking practice and basic grammar.","zh":"初學者英語課程可能主要由口語練習和基礎文法組成。"},{"en":"If support consists mainly of family help, professional care may be limited.","zh":"如果支援主要由家庭幫助組成，專業照顧可能有限。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main part of something.","zh":"這個片語指出某事物的主要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"extended family network","meaning":"大家庭支援網絡","examples":[{"en":"The extended family network provided much of the early support.","zh":"大家庭支援網絡提供了大部分早期支援。"},{"en":"An extended family network includes relatives beyond parents and children, such as grandparents, aunts, uncles, and cousins.","zh":"Extended family network 包括父母和子女以外的親屬，例如祖父母、姨姨叔叔和表兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"A patient may rely on an extended family network for meals, visits, and transport.","zh":"病人可能依賴大家庭支援網絡提供膳食、探訪和交通。"},{"en":"If the extended family network is weak, community care may need more professional services.","zh":"如果大家庭支援網絡薄弱，社區照顧可能需要更多專業服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes family support spread across many relatives.","zh":"這個片語描述由許多親屬分擔的家庭支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in more recent years","meaning":"近年來","examples":[{"en":"In more recent years, community care has become more professional.","zh":"近年來，社區照顧變得更專業。"},{"en":"In more recent years means during the later or current period, compared with the past.","zh":"In more recent years 指與過去相比，在較後或目前時期。"},{"en":"In more recent years, schools have used more digital learning tools.","zh":"近年來，學校使用了更多數碼學習工具。"},{"en":"If services have improved in more recent years, old criticisms may need updating.","zh":"如果服務近年來有所改善，舊批評可能需要更新。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the present or recent past with earlier times.","zh":"這個片語把現在或近期與較早時期比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"extend to the provision of","meaning":"擴展至提供……","examples":[{"en":"Community care has extended to the provision of specialist teams.","zh":"社區照顧已擴展至提供專門團隊。"},{"en":"To extend to the provision of something means to grow until it includes offering that thing.","zh":"To extend to the provision of something 指發展至包括提供某事物。"},{"en":"A school support scheme may extend to the provision of counselling and lunch assistance.","zh":"學校支援計劃可能擴展至提供輔導和午餐援助。"},{"en":"If community care extends to specialist teams, patients can receive more targeted help.","zh":"如果社區照顧擴展至專門團隊，病人可以得到更針對性的幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a service becoming broader and more complete.","zh":"這個片語描述服務變得更廣和更完整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"specialist community mental health teams","meaning":"專門社區精神健康團隊","examples":[{"en":"Specialist community mental health teams provide support in the UK.","zh":"專門社區精神健康團隊在英國提供支援。"},{"en":"Specialist community mental health teams are professional groups that support people with mental illness outside hospitals.","zh":"Specialist community mental health teams 是在醫院以外支援精神病患者的專業團隊。"},{"en":"Such teams may include nurses, social workers, psychologists, and psychiatrists.","zh":"這類團隊可能包括護士、社工、心理學家和精神科醫生。"},{"en":"If these teams visit patients regularly, crises may be noticed earlier.","zh":"如果這些團隊定期探訪病人，危機可能更早被察覺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes professional mental-health support based in the community.","zh":"這個片語描述設於社區中的專業精神健康支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"CMHTs","meaning":"社區精神健康團隊","examples":[{"en":"CMHTs cover a wide range of mental-health services.","zh":"CMHTs 涵蓋多種精神健康服務。"},{"en":"CMHTs stands for community mental health teams.","zh":"CMHTs 是 community mental health teams 的縮寫。"},{"en":"CMHTs may help patients manage medication, housing problems, and recovery plans.","zh":"CMHTs 可能幫助病人管理藥物、住屋問題和康復計劃。"},{"en":"If CMHTs are understaffed, patients may wait too long for help.","zh":"如果 CMHTs 人手不足，病人可能等太久才得到幫助。"},{"en":"This abbreviation refers to organised professional teams in community mental healthcare.","zh":"這個縮寫指社區精神醫療中的有組織專業團隊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cover a wide range of services","meaning":"涵蓋多種服務","examples":[{"en":"Community mental health teams cover a wide range of services.","zh":"社區精神健康團隊涵蓋多種服務。"},{"en":"To cover a wide range of services means to include many different types of support.","zh":"To cover a wide range of services 指包括許多不同類型的支援。"},{"en":"A community centre may cover a wide range of services, from childcare to job advice.","zh":"社區中心可能涵蓋多種服務，從託兒到求職建議都有。"},{"en":"If a team covers many services, patients do not need to visit many separate offices.","zh":"如果一個團隊涵蓋多種服務，病人就不需要到許多不同辦公室。"},{"en":"This phrase shows broad service coverage.","zh":"這個片語顯示服務範圍廣泛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rehabilitation","meaning":"復康","examples":[{"en":"Rehabilitation is one of the services offered by community mental health teams.","zh":"復康是社區精神健康團隊提供的服務之一。"},{"en":"Rehabilitation means support that helps people recover skills, health, or independence after illness or injury.","zh":"Rehabilitation 指幫助人們在疾病或受傷後恢復技能、健康或獨立能力的支援。"},{"en":"After an accident, a patient may need rehabilitation to walk confidently again.","zh":"意外後，病人可能需要復康才能再次有信心走路。"},{"en":"In mental healthcare, rehabilitation can help patients rebuild daily routines and social confidence.","zh":"在精神健康照顧中，復康可以幫助病人重建日常規律和社交信心。"},{"en":"This word focuses on recovery and return to ordinary life.","zh":"這個詞集中於恢復和重返普通生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"home treatment and assessment","meaning":"家居治療和評估","examples":[{"en":"Community teams may provide home treatment and assessment.","zh":"社區團隊可能提供家居治療和評估。"},{"en":"Home treatment and assessment means care and evaluation given to patients in their own homes.","zh":"Home treatment and assessment 指在病人家中提供的照顧和評估。"},{"en":"A nurse may visit a patient at home to assess mood, medication use, and safety.","zh":"護士可能到病人家中評估情緒、用藥和安全。"},{"en":"If home assessment detects a crisis early, hospital admission may be avoided.","zh":"如果家居評估及早發現危機，可能避免入院。"},{"en":"This phrase describes professional support delivered outside a clinic.","zh":"這個片語描述在診所以外提供的專業支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in addition","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"In addition, psychiatric nurses can administer medication.","zh":"此外，精神科護士可以施用藥物。"},{"en":"In addition means also or besides what has already been mentioned.","zh":"In addition 指另外，或除了剛提到的事情之外。"},{"en":"The school offers homework help; in addition, it provides counselling.","zh":"學校提供功課支援；此外，它也提供輔導。"},{"en":"If one service is not enough, additional support may make care more complete.","zh":"如果單一服務不足，額外支援可能令照顧更完整。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another point to an explanation.","zh":"這個片語為解釋加入另一點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"psychiatric nurses","meaning":"精神科護士","examples":[{"en":"Psychiatric nurses help patients take their medication safely.","zh":"精神科護士幫助病人安全服藥。"},{"en":"Psychiatric nurses are nurses trained to care for people with mental-health conditions.","zh":"Psychiatric nurses 是受訓照顧精神健康病人的護士。"},{"en":"A psychiatric nurse may visit a patient at home to check symptoms and medication.","zh":"精神科護士可能到病人家中檢查症狀和用藥情況。"},{"en":"If psychiatric nurses are available, patients may receive help before problems become severe.","zh":"如果有精神科護士，病人可能在問題變嚴重前得到幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to nursing specialists in mental healthcare.","zh":"這個片語指精神醫療中的護理專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be on hand to","meaning":"隨時可提供協助去……","examples":[{"en":"Psychiatric nurses are on hand to administer medication.","zh":"精神科護士隨時可提供協助施用藥物。"},{"en":"To be on hand to do something means to be available and ready to help.","zh":"To be on hand to do something 指在場或可隨時提供幫助。"},{"en":"Teachers were on hand to guide students during the open day.","zh":"開放日期間，老師隨時可協助指導學生。"},{"en":"If nurses are on hand, patients can receive urgent advice more quickly.","zh":"如果護士隨時可提供協助，病人可以更快得到緊急建議。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests practical help is nearby and ready.","zh":"這個片語暗示實際幫助就在附近並已準備好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"administer prescription medication","meaning":"施用處方藥物","examples":[{"en":"Psychiatric nurses administer prescription medication to patients.","zh":"精神科護士為病人施用處方藥物。"},{"en":"To administer prescription medication means to give or manage medicine ordered by a doctor.","zh":"To administer prescription medication 指給予或管理由醫生開出的藥物。"},{"en":"A nurse may administer prescription medication at the correct time each day.","zh":"護士可能每天在正確時間施用處方藥物。"},{"en":"If medication is administered wrongly, the patient’s health may be put at risk.","zh":"如果藥物施用錯誤，病人健康可能受威脅。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled medical support with prescribed drugs.","zh":"這個片語描述使用處方藥的受控醫療支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"give injections","meaning":"打針；注射","examples":[{"en":"Some psychiatric nurses give injections to patients.","zh":"一些精神科護士為病人打針。"},{"en":"To give injections means to put medicine into the body using a needle.","zh":"To give injections 指用針把藥物注入身體。"},{"en":"A nurse may give injections when tablets are not suitable.","zh":"當藥片不合適時，護士可能會打針。"},{"en":"If patients miss injections, their symptoms may become harder to control.","zh":"如果病人錯過注射，症狀可能更難控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common medical method of delivering medicine.","zh":"這個片語描述給予藥物的常見醫療方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be provided with","meaning":"獲提供","examples":[{"en":"The patient is provided with the help they need.","zh":"病人獲提供他們所需的幫助。"},{"en":"To be provided with something means to be given or supplied with it.","zh":"To be provided with something 指獲給予或供應某物。"},{"en":"Students should be provided with clear instructions before an exam.","zh":"學生考試前應獲提供清晰指示。"},{"en":"If patients are provided with regular support, they are less likely to be abandoned.","zh":"如果病人獲提供定期支援，他們較不可能被遺棄。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on receiving necessary resources or help.","zh":"這個片語集中於獲得必要資源或幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the help they need","meaning":"他們所需的幫助","examples":[{"en":"Patients should receive the help they need to live safely.","zh":"病人應得到他們所需的幫助，以安全生活。"},{"en":"The help they need means the specific support required for a person’s situation.","zh":"The help they need 指符合某人情況的特定支援。"},{"en":"A child with reading difficulties needs help that matches the exact problem.","zh":"有閱讀困難的孩子需要配合具體問題的幫助。"},{"en":"If patients do not receive the help they need, small problems may become crises.","zh":"如果病人得不到他們所需的幫助，小問題可能變成危機。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses suitable support, not just any support.","zh":"這個片語強調合適支援，而不只是任何支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"survive in the everyday world","meaning":"在日常世界中生活下去","examples":[{"en":"Community care helps patients survive in the everyday world.","zh":"社區照顧幫助病人在日常世界中生活下去。"},{"en":"To survive in the everyday world means to manage ordinary daily life outside an institution.","zh":"To survive in the everyday world 指在院舍以外應付普通日常生活。"},{"en":"A young adult leaving home must learn how to survive in the everyday world by budgeting and cooking.","zh":"離家的年輕成年人必須透過理財和煮食學會在日常世界生活。"},{"en":"If patients can manage shopping, transport, and appointments, they can live more safely outside hospital.","zh":"如果病人能處理購物、交通和預約，他們可以在醫院外生活得更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical daily living.","zh":"這個片語集中於實際日常生活能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"maintain a degree of autonomy","meaning":"保持某程度的自主","examples":[{"en":"Patients can maintain a degree of autonomy in the community.","zh":"病人在社區中可以保持某程度的自主。"},{"en":"To maintain a degree of autonomy means to keep some control over one’s own decisions and life.","zh":"To maintain a degree of autonomy 指保持對自己決定和生活的一定控制。"},{"en":"Elderly people may maintain a degree of autonomy if they receive help with heavy tasks only.","zh":"如果長者只在重活上得到協助，他們可能保持某程度的自主。"},{"en":"If patients choose their routines, they may feel more respected and motivated.","zh":"如果病人能選擇自己的日常安排，他們可能感到更受尊重和更有動力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes partial independence with support.","zh":"這個片語描述有支援下的部分獨立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"when a policy is put into practice","meaning":"當政策付諸實行時","examples":[{"en":"Problems often appear when a policy is put into practice.","zh":"當政策付諸實行時，問題往往出現。"},{"en":"When a policy is put into practice means when an idea or rule is actually carried out.","zh":"When a policy is put into practice 指一個想法或規則被實際執行時。"},{"en":"A school rule may sound simple until it is put into practice with hundreds of students.","zh":"學校規則聽起來可能簡單，直到它要在數百名學生身上實行。"},{"en":"If a policy lacks staff or money, implementation may reveal its weaknesses.","zh":"如果政策缺乏人手或資金，執行時可能揭示其弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts theory with real-world application.","zh":"這個片語把理論與現實應用作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"put something into practice","meaning":"將……付諸實行","examples":[{"en":"Care in the community can be difficult to put into practice.","zh":"社區照顧可能很難付諸實行。"},{"en":"To put something into practice means to carry out an idea, plan, or policy in real life.","zh":"To put something into practice 指在現實中執行想法、計劃或政策。"},{"en":"Students put grammar into practice when they use it in speaking and writing.","zh":"學生在說話和寫作中使用文法時，就是把文法付諸實行。"},{"en":"If a plan is put into practice without resources, it may fail.","zh":"如果計劃在沒有資源下付諸實行，它可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving from theory to action.","zh":"這個片語描述由理論走向行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"failings become apparent","meaning":"缺點變得明顯","examples":[{"en":"The failings of a policy may become apparent after implementation.","zh":"政策實施後，其缺點可能變得明顯。"},{"en":"Failings become apparent means weaknesses become clear or visible.","zh":"Failings become apparent 指弱點變得清楚或可見。"},{"en":"A timetable’s failings become apparent when students keep arriving late.","zh":"當學生不斷遲到，時間表的缺點就變得明顯。"},{"en":"If community services are hard to reach, the policy’s weaknesses soon become clear.","zh":"如果社區服務難以取得，政策弱點很快會變得清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hidden problems becoming obvious.","zh":"這個片語描述隱藏問題變得明顯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"this is true of","meaning":"……也是如此","examples":[{"en":"This is true of the policy of care in the community.","zh":"社區照顧政策也是如此。"},{"en":"This is true of something means the same point applies to that thing.","zh":"This is true of something 指同一點也適用於某事。"},{"en":"Good planning matters in schools, and this is true of hospitals too.","zh":"良好規劃對學校重要，醫院也是如此。"},{"en":"If a policy looks good on paper but fails in practice, this may be true of many public services.","zh":"如果一項政策紙上看來很好但實行失敗，許多公共服務可能也是如此。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a general idea to a specific example.","zh":"這個片語把一般想法連接到具體例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"backup services","meaning":"後備支援服務","examples":[{"en":"Backup services may exist but not be used by the patient.","zh":"後備支援服務可能存在，但病人沒有使用。"},{"en":"Backup services are extra support services available when normal help is not enough.","zh":"Backup services 是當一般幫助不足時可使用的額外支援服務。"},{"en":"A school may provide backup services for students who need counselling after class.","zh":"學校可能為課後需要輔導的學生提供後備支援服務。"},{"en":"If backup services are difficult to contact, they may not help during a crisis.","zh":"如果後備支援服務難以聯絡，它們在危機中可能幫不上忙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes safety-net support.","zh":"這個片語描述安全網式支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"call upon","meaning":"求助於；使用","examples":[{"en":"A patient may not call upon support services when needed.","zh":"病人有需要時可能沒有求助於支援服務。"},{"en":"To call upon a service means to ask for or use it.","zh":"To call upon a service 指請求或使用該服務。"},{"en":"A family may call upon social workers when caring becomes too difficult.","zh":"當照顧變得太困難，家庭可能求助於社工。"},{"en":"If patients cannot recognise danger, they may fail to call upon help in time.","zh":"如果病人不能識別危險，他們可能未能及時求助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes actively seeking support.","zh":"這個片語描述主動尋求支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"due to reluctance or inability","meaning":"由於不願意或無能力","examples":[{"en":"A patient may avoid help due to reluctance or inability.","zh":"病人可能由於不願意或無能力而避免求助。"},{"en":"Due to reluctance or inability means because someone is unwilling or unable to do something.","zh":"Due to reluctance or inability 指因某人不願意或無能力做某事。"},{"en":"A student may avoid asking questions due to reluctance or inability to explain the problem.","zh":"學生可能由於不願意或無能力解釋問題而避免提問。"},{"en":"If patients feel ashamed or confused, they may not seek help even when services exist.","zh":"如果病人感到羞恥或混亂，即使有服務也可能不求助。"},{"en":"This phrase explains non-action through either unwillingness or lack of capacity.","zh":"這個片語以不願意或能力不足解釋沒有行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"assess their own condition","meaning":"評估自己的狀況","examples":[{"en":"Some patients cannot assess their own condition accurately.","zh":"一些病人不能準確評估自己的狀況。"},{"en":"To assess their own condition means to judge how well or unwell they are.","zh":"To assess their own condition 指判斷自己健康或病情如何。"},{"en":"A patient may need a nurse because it is hard to assess symptoms alone.","zh":"病人可能需要護士，因為獨自評估症狀很困難。"},{"en":"If people cannot assess their own condition, they may not seek help at the right time.","zh":"如果人們不能評估自己的狀況，他們可能無法在適當時間求助。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when discussing self-awareness and health risk.","zh":"這個片語在討論自我覺察和健康風險時很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, a patient may be alone during a critical phase.","zh":"因此，病人可能在病情關鍵階段獨自一人。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what has just been described.","zh":"As a result 指因為剛剛描述的事情。"},{"en":"The clinic closed early; as a result, patients had to return the next day.","zh":"診所提早關門；因此，病人不得不翌日再來。"},{"en":"If support is not used, the patient may face crisis alone as a result.","zh":"如果支援沒有被使用，病人可能因此獨自面對危機。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a consequence.","zh":"這個片語引出後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a critical phase of","meaning":"……的關鍵階段","examples":[{"en":"A patient may be alone during a critical phase of their illness.","zh":"病人可能在病情的關鍵階段獨自一人。"},{"en":"A critical phase of something is a very important or dangerous stage in its development.","zh":"A critical phase of something 是某事發展中非常重要或危險的階段。"},{"en":"Exam week is a critical phase of a student’s preparation.","zh":"考試週是學生備考的關鍵階段。"},{"en":"If support fails during a critical phase, the final outcome may be much worse.","zh":"如果支援在關鍵階段失效，最終結果可能差得多。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a period when action matters especially much.","zh":"這個片語突出行動尤其重要的一段時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lead someone to self-harm","meaning":"導致某人自殘","examples":[{"en":"Isolation may lead a patient to self-harm.","zh":"孤立可能導致病人自殘。"},{"en":"To lead someone to self-harm means to contribute to a situation in which someone hurts themselves.","zh":"To lead someone to self-harm 指促成某人傷害自己的情況。"},{"en":"A school should act quickly if loneliness or bullying may lead a student to self-harm.","zh":"如果孤獨或欺凌可能導致學生自殘，學校應迅速行動。"},{"en":"If a patient is in crisis, immediate support can reduce the danger.","zh":"如果病人處於危機中，即時支援可以減少危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious mental-health risk that requires urgent care.","zh":"這個片語描述需要緊急照顧的嚴重精神健康風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"self-harm","meaning":"自殘","examples":[{"en":"Patients may be at risk of self-harm during a crisis.","zh":"病人在危機期間可能有自殘風險。"},{"en":"Self-harm means deliberately hurting oneself, often because of severe emotional distress.","zh":"Self-harm 指故意傷害自己，通常因嚴重情緒痛苦而發生。"},{"en":"A person at risk of self-harm should receive immediate support from trusted adults or professionals.","zh":"有自殘風險的人應立即從可信成人或專業人士得到支援。"},{"en":"If warning signs are ignored, the risk may increase.","zh":"如果警號被忽視，風險可能增加。"},{"en":"This word describes a serious safety concern, not attention-seeking behaviour.","zh":"這個詞描述嚴重安全問題，而不是博取注意的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pose a threat to","meaning":"對……構成威脅","examples":[{"en":"A patient in crisis may pose a threat to others.","zh":"處於危機中的病人可能對他人構成威脅。"},{"en":"To pose a threat to someone means to create a possible danger to them.","zh":"To pose a threat to someone 指對某人造成可能危險。"},{"en":"A broken staircase can pose a threat to students and visitors.","zh":"破爛樓梯可以對學生和訪客構成威脅。"},{"en":"If a person is untreated during a severe crisis, safety planning may be necessary.","zh":"如果人在嚴重危機中未接受治療，可能需要安全規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes potential danger, not guaranteed harm.","zh":"這個片語描述潛在危險，而不是必然傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"members of their community","meaning":"社區成員","examples":[{"en":"The patient may pose a threat to members of their community.","zh":"病人可能對其社區成員構成威脅。"},{"en":"Members of their community are the people who live, work, or interact around them.","zh":"Members of their community 是在其周圍生活、工作或互動的人。"},{"en":"Neighbours, shopkeepers, teachers, and social workers can all be members of a person’s community.","zh":"鄰居、店主、老師和社工都可以是一個人社區中的成員。"},{"en":"If community care fails, both the patient and nearby people may be affected.","zh":"如果社區照顧失效，病人和附近的人都可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the wider social circle around an individual.","zh":"這個片語描述個人周圍較廣泛的社會圈子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an extreme scenario","meaning":"極端情況","examples":[{"en":"Self-harm or violence is an extreme scenario.","zh":"自殘或暴力是極端情況。"},{"en":"An extreme scenario is a very serious situation that may happen but is not the normal case.","zh":"An extreme scenario 是可能發生但並非常態的非常嚴重情況。"},{"en":"A school evacuation is an extreme scenario, but staff still prepare for it.","zh":"學校疏散是極端情況，但職員仍會作準備。"},{"en":"If planners consider extreme scenarios, they can reduce serious risks.","zh":"如果規劃者考慮極端情況，就能減少嚴重風險。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate rare severe cases from everyday situations.","zh":"這個片語幫助區分罕見嚴重個案和日常情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the issue of social alienation","meaning":"社會疏離的問題","examples":[{"en":"The issue of social alienation also needs to be considered.","zh":"社會疏離的問題也需要被考慮。"},{"en":"The issue of social alienation is the problem of people feeling separated from society.","zh":"The issue of social alienation 是人們感到與社會分離的問題。"},{"en":"A teenager may face social alienation if classmates always exclude him.","zh":"如果同學總是排斥一名青少年，他可能面對社會疏離。"},{"en":"If patients leave institutions but cannot build relationships, loneliness may continue.","zh":"如果病人離開院舍卻無法建立關係，孤獨可能持續。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on social separation, not only medical symptoms.","zh":"這個片語集中於社會分離，而不只是醫療症狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"social alienation","meaning":"社會疏離","examples":[{"en":"Social alienation can worsen mental-health problems.","zh":"社會疏離可以惡化精神健康問題。"},{"en":"Social alienation means feeling cut off from other people or from normal community life.","zh":"Social alienation 指感到與他人或正常社區生活隔絕。"},{"en":"A newcomer may experience social alienation if no one talks to them at school.","zh":"如果在學校沒有人跟新同學說話，他可能經歷社會疏離。"},{"en":"If people feel alienated, they may avoid help and become more isolated.","zh":"如果人們感到疏離，他們可能避免求助並變得更孤立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional and social distance from others.","zh":"這個片語描述與他人的情感和社會距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"need to be considered","meaning":"需要被考慮","examples":[{"en":"The risk of social exclusion needs to be considered.","zh":"社會排斥的風險需要被考慮。"},{"en":"Need to be considered means should be thought about seriously before a decision is made.","zh":"Need to be considered 指在作決定前應認真思考。"},{"en":"Students’ travel time needs to be considered when planning after-school lessons.","zh":"規劃課後課程時，需要考慮學生交通時間。"},{"en":"If social risks are not considered, a policy may fail even with good intentions.","zh":"如果社會風險沒有被考慮，即使政策原意良好也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights an important factor that should not be ignored.","zh":"這個片語突出不應被忽視的重要因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"integration into the community","meaning":"融入社區","examples":[{"en":"Integration into the community may not be enough for recovery.","zh":"融入社區可能不足以幫助康復。"},{"en":"Integration into the community means becoming part of ordinary social life in a neighbourhood.","zh":"Integration into the community 指成為社區普通社交生活的一部分。"},{"en":"A patient may need help joining classes, meeting neighbours, and finding work to achieve integration.","zh":"病人可能需要協助參加課程、認識鄰居和找工作，才能真正融入社區。"},{"en":"If integration fails, a person may live near others but still feel alone.","zh":"如果融入失敗，一個人可能住在他人附近卻仍感到孤單。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaningful social inclusion, not just physical presence.","zh":"這個片語描述有意義的社會包容，而不只是身處社區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be sufficient to","meaning":"足以……","examples":[{"en":"Community integration may not be sufficient to help a patient find work.","zh":"融入社區可能不足以幫助病人找到工作。"},{"en":"To be sufficient to do something means to be enough to achieve a result.","zh":"To be sufficient to do something 指足夠達成某結果。"},{"en":"Reading notes once is not sufficient to prepare for a difficult exam.","zh":"只讀一次筆記不足以準備困難考試。"},{"en":"If support is not sufficient, patients may still struggle after leaving hospital.","zh":"如果支援不足，病人離院後仍可能掙扎。"},{"en":"This phrase judges whether something is enough.","zh":"這個片語判斷某事是否足夠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"find work","meaning":"找到工作","examples":[{"en":"Some patients struggle to find work after leaving institutions.","zh":"一些病人離開院舍後難以找到工作。"},{"en":"To find work means to get a job or paid employment.","zh":"To find work 指取得工作或受薪職位。"},{"en":"A graduate may need time to find work after finishing university.","zh":"大學畢業生畢業後可能需要時間找工作。"},{"en":"If former patients cannot find work, poverty and isolation may follow.","zh":"如果前病人找不到工作，貧窮和孤立可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important step toward independence.","zh":"這個片語描述邁向獨立的重要一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"leading to poverty and isolation","meaning":"導致貧窮和孤立","examples":[{"en":"Unemployment may lead to poverty and isolation.","zh":"失業可能導致貧窮和孤立。"},{"en":"Leading to poverty and isolation means causing people to become poor and socially separated.","zh":"Leading to poverty and isolation 指導致人們變窮並與社會分離。"},{"en":"Losing a job without support can lead to poverty and isolation for a family.","zh":"失去工作而沒有支援，可以導致一個家庭陷入貧窮和孤立。"},{"en":"If patients cannot work or build friendships, daily life may become harder.","zh":"如果病人不能工作或建立友誼，日常生活可能變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase connects social and economic problems.","zh":"這個片語連接社會和經濟問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"social exclusion","meaning":"社會排斥","examples":[{"en":"Social exclusion can cause a relapse.","zh":"社會排斥可以導致復發。"},{"en":"Social exclusion means being shut out from normal social, work, or community life.","zh":"Social exclusion 指被排除在正常社交、工作或社區生活之外。"},{"en":"A person may feel social exclusion if no one invites them to group activities.","zh":"如果沒有人邀請某人參加小組活動，他可能感到社會排斥。"},{"en":"If patients experience social exclusion, their mental health may deteriorate.","zh":"如果病人經歷社會排斥，其精神健康可能惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being pushed to the margins of society.","zh":"這個片語描述被推到社會邊緣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cause a relapse","meaning":"導致復發","examples":[{"en":"Social exclusion could cause a relapse in vulnerable patients.","zh":"社會排斥可能導致脆弱病人復發。"},{"en":"To cause a relapse means to make an illness or problem return after improvement.","zh":"To cause a relapse 指令疾病或問題在改善後再次出現。"},{"en":"Severe stress can cause a relapse in someone recovering from depression.","zh":"嚴重壓力可以導致正在從抑鬱康復的人復發。"},{"en":"If support stops too early, symptoms may return.","zh":"如果支援太早停止，症狀可能再次出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when recovery is interrupted.","zh":"這個片語常用於康復被中斷的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be left to battle","meaning":"被留下獨自對抗","examples":[{"en":"The individual may be left to battle mental-health problems alone.","zh":"個人可能被留下獨自對抗精神健康問題。"},{"en":"To be left to battle something means to be forced to deal with a difficult problem without enough help.","zh":"To be left to battle something 指被迫在缺乏足夠幫助下應對困難問題。"},{"en":"A student should not be left to battle anxiety without adult support.","zh":"學生不應在沒有成人支援下被留下獨自對抗焦慮。"},{"en":"If patients battle illness alone, the risk of crisis may increase.","zh":"如果病人獨自對抗疾病，危機風險可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests struggle and neglect.","zh":"這個片語暗示掙扎和被忽視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mental-health problems","meaning":"精神健康問題","examples":[{"en":"Social exclusion can worsen mental-health problems.","zh":"社會排斥可以惡化精神健康問題。"},{"en":"Mental-health problems are difficulties affecting mood, thinking, behaviour, or emotional well-being.","zh":"Mental-health problems 是影響情緒、思維、行為或心理福祉的困難。"},{"en":"Stress, anxiety, and depression are common mental-health problems.","zh":"壓力、焦慮和抑鬱是常見精神健康問題。"},{"en":"If mental-health problems are ignored, school, work, and relationships may suffer.","zh":"如果精神健康問題被忽視，學業、工作和關係都可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase covers a wide range of psychological difficulties.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋多種心理困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the solution is to ensure that","meaning":"解決方法是確保","examples":[{"en":"The solution is to ensure that patients remain connected to professional helpers.","zh":"解決方法是確保病人仍與專業支援人員保持聯繫。"},{"en":"The solution is to ensure that means the answer is to make certain something happens.","zh":"The solution is to ensure that 指答案是要確保某事發生。"},{"en":"The solution is to ensure that every student understands the instructions before the test begins.","zh":"解決方法是確保每名學生在測驗開始前理解指示。"},{"en":"If patients remain connected to professionals, warning signs can be noticed earlier.","zh":"如果病人保持與專業人士聯繫，警號可以更早被注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a practical answer to a problem.","zh":"這個片語引出問題的實際解決方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be in touch with","meaning":"與……保持聯絡","examples":[{"en":"Patients should stay in touch with professional helpers.","zh":"病人應與專業支援人員保持聯絡。"},{"en":"To be in touch with someone means to keep communication with them.","zh":"To be in touch with someone 指與某人保持溝通。"},{"en":"A teacher may stay in touch with parents if a student is struggling.","zh":"如果學生有困難，老師可能與家長保持聯絡。"},{"en":"If patients are in touch with helpers, they can ask for support before a crisis.","zh":"如果病人與支援人員保持聯絡，他們可以在危機前求助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continuing contact.","zh":"這個片語描述持續聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"professional helpers","meaning":"專業支援人員","examples":[{"en":"Professional helpers can support patients in the community.","zh":"專業支援人員可以支援社區中的病人。"},{"en":"Professional helpers are trained workers such as nurses, counsellors, social workers, or therapists.","zh":"Professional helpers 是受訓工作者，例如護士、輔導員、社工或治療師。"},{"en":"A professional helper may teach a patient how to manage medication and appointments.","zh":"專業支援人員可能教病人如何管理藥物和預約。"},{"en":"If professional helpers visit regularly, patients are less likely to be left alone.","zh":"如果專業支援人員定期探訪，病人較不可能被獨自留下。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trained support, not informal family help only.","zh":"這個片語描述受訓支援，而不只是非正式家庭幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be left alone to fend for themselves","meaning":"被留下自生自滅","examples":[{"en":"Patients should not be left alone to fend for themselves.","zh":"病人不應被留下自生自滅。"},{"en":"To be left alone to fend for oneself means to be forced to manage without help or protection.","zh":"To be left alone to fend for oneself 指被迫在沒有幫助或保護下自行應付。"},{"en":"New students should not be left alone to fend for themselves on the first day of school.","zh":"新生第一天上學不應被留下自生自滅。"},{"en":"If vulnerable patients must manage everything alone, they may miss essential care.","zh":"如果脆弱病人必須獨自處理所有事情，他們可能錯過必要照顧。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly suggests neglect and lack of support.","zh":"這個片語強烈暗示忽視和缺乏支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"it should always be remembered that","meaning":"應該永遠記住","examples":[{"en":"It should always be remembered that community care requires continuing support.","zh":"應該永遠記住，社區照顧需要持續支援。"},{"en":"It should always be remembered that means this important point should not be forgotten.","zh":"It should always be remembered that 指這個重要重點不應被忘記。"},{"en":"It should always be remembered that students learn at different speeds.","zh":"應該永遠記住，學生學習速度不同。"},{"en":"If policymakers forget this point, they may design unrealistic services.","zh":"如果政策制定者忘記這一點，他們可能設計出不切實際的服務。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a key warning or principle.","zh":"這個片語突出關鍵警告或原則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take the patient out of the institution","meaning":"將病人帶離院舍","examples":[{"en":"You can take the patient out of the institution, but support may still be needed.","zh":"你可以將病人帶離院舍，但支援可能仍然需要。"},{"en":"To take the patient out of the institution means to move the patient from institutional care into ordinary community life.","zh":"To take the patient out of the institution 指把病人從院舍照顧轉到普通社區生活。"},{"en":"A hospital may discharge a patient, but daily living support may still be necessary.","zh":"醫院可能讓病人出院，但日常生活支援可能仍然必要。"},{"en":"If patients leave institutions without preparation, they may struggle outside.","zh":"如果病人未經準備便離開院舍，他們可能在外面生活困難。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that physical release is only one part of recovery.","zh":"這個片語顯示身體上離開只是康復的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take the institution out of the patient","meaning":"令病人擺脫院舍化影響","examples":[{"en":"You cannot always take the institution out of the patient.","zh":"你不一定能令病人擺脫院舍化影響。"},{"en":"To take the institution out of the patient means to remove the habits, fears, and dependence created by long institutional life.","zh":"To take the institution out of the patient 指去除長期院舍生活造成的習慣、恐懼和依賴。"},{"en":"A person may leave hospital but still wait for others to make every decision.","zh":"一個人可能已離開醫院，但仍等待別人替他作每個決定。"},{"en":"If years of institutional living shape behaviour, independence takes time to rebuild.","zh":"如果多年院舍生活塑造了行為，重建獨立需要時間。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that psychological change is harder than physical relocation.","zh":"這個片語暗示心理改變比身體搬離更困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"opinions are divided","meaning":"意見分歧","examples":[{"en":"Opinions about care in the community are divided.","zh":"人們對社區照顧意見分歧。"},{"en":"Opinions are divided means people disagree and hold different views.","zh":"Opinions are divided 指人們不同意並持有不同看法。"},{"en":"Opinions are divided on whether homework should be reduced.","zh":"人們對是否應減少功課意見分歧。"},{"en":"If a policy has both benefits and risks, opinions are likely to be divided.","zh":"如果政策既有好處又有風險，意見很可能分歧。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public or professional disagreement.","zh":"這個片語描述公眾或專業界分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"members of the public","meaning":"公眾人士","examples":[{"en":"Members of the public have different views on community care.","zh":"公眾人士對社區照顧有不同看法。"},{"en":"Members of the public are ordinary people, not officials or specialists.","zh":"Members of the public 是普通人，而不是官員或專家。"},{"en":"Members of the public may worry about safety if they do not understand a policy.","zh":"如果公眾人士不了解政策，他們可能擔心安全。"},{"en":"If public information is poor, fear and misunderstanding may spread.","zh":"如果公眾資訊不足，恐懼和誤解可能擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to society at large.","zh":"這個片語指整體社會中的普通人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"mental-healthcare profession","meaning":"精神醫療專業","examples":[{"en":"Opinions are divided within the mental-healthcare profession itself.","zh":"精神醫療專業內部本身也意見分歧。"},{"en":"The mental-healthcare profession means the field of trained workers who treat and support mental health.","zh":"Mental-healthcare profession 指治療和支援精神健康的受訓工作者領域。"},{"en":"Psychologists, psychiatrists, nurses, and therapists belong to the mental-healthcare profession.","zh":"心理學家、精神科醫生、護士和治療師都屬於精神醫療專業。"},{"en":"If professionals disagree, the issue is probably complex.","zh":"如果專業人士也不同意，問題可能很複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the professional world of mental-health support.","zh":"這個片語指精神健康支援的專業世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"practising clinical psychologist","meaning":"執業臨床心理學家","examples":[{"en":"Dr. Mayalla is a practising clinical psychologist.","zh":"Mayalla 醫生是一名執業臨床心理學家。"},{"en":"A practising clinical psychologist is a trained psychologist who currently works with patients.","zh":"Practising clinical psychologist 是目前與病人工作的受訓心理學家。"},{"en":"A practising clinical psychologist may assess anxiety, depression, trauma, or family stress.","zh":"執業臨床心理學家可能評估焦慮、抑鬱、創傷或家庭壓力。"},{"en":"If such a psychologist comments on community care, the view is shaped by real clinical experience.","zh":"如果這類心理學家評論社區照顧，其觀點會受真實臨床經驗影響。"},{"en":"This phrase distinguishes active professional practice from purely academic study.","zh":"這個片語把正在執業的專業工作與純學術研究區分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be inclined to believe that","meaning":"傾向相信","examples":[{"en":"Dr. Mayalla is inclined to believe that community care is not suitable for everyone.","zh":"Mayalla 醫生傾向相信社區照顧並非適合所有人。"},{"en":"To be inclined to believe that means to tend to think something is true.","zh":"To be inclined to believe that 指傾向認為某事是真。"},{"en":"After seeing the evidence, a teacher may be inclined to believe that smaller classes help.","zh":"看過證據後，老師可能傾向相信小班教學有幫助。"},{"en":"If a professional has seen many difficult cases, they may be cautious in their judgement.","zh":"如果專業人士見過許多困難個案，他們的判斷可能較謹慎。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a careful tendency, not absolute certainty.","zh":"這個片語表達謹慎傾向，而不是絕對肯定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"certain patients","meaning":"某些病人","examples":[{"en":"Certain patients may benefit from care in the community.","zh":"某些病人可能從社區照顧中受益。"},{"en":"Certain patients means some particular patients, not all patients.","zh":"Certain patients 指某些特定病人，而不是所有病人。"},{"en":"Certain patients need regular home visits, while others need hospital care.","zh":"某些病人需要定期家訪，而另一些需要住院照顧。"},{"en":"If a scheme suits only certain patients, assessment must be careful.","zh":"如果計劃只適合某些病人，評估就必須謹慎。"},{"en":"This phrase limits a statement to a specific group.","zh":"這個片語把說法限制在特定群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"benefit from","meaning":"從……受益","examples":[{"en":"Some patients benefit from care in the community.","zh":"一些病人從社區照顧中受益。"},{"en":"To benefit from something means to gain help, advantage, or improvement from it.","zh":"To benefit from something 指從某事得到幫助、好處或改善。"},{"en":"Students benefit from clear examples when learning new vocabulary.","zh":"學生在學習新詞彙時從清晰例子中受益。"},{"en":"If patients benefit from independence, community care can support recovery.","zh":"如果病人從獨立中受益，社區照顧可以支持康復。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something has a positive effect.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事有正面效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the scheme isn’t for everyone","meaning":"這項計劃並非適合所有人","examples":[{"en":"Dr. Mayalla believes the scheme isn’t for everyone.","zh":"Mayalla 醫生認為這項計劃並非適合所有人。"},{"en":"The scheme isn’t for everyone means the plan is suitable for some people but not all.","zh":"The scheme isn’t for everyone 指計劃適合某些人，但不適合全部人。"},{"en":"Online learning is useful, but the scheme isn’t for everyone because some students need face-to-face support.","zh":"網上學習有用，但這項安排並非適合所有人，因為有些學生需要面授支援。"},{"en":"If a patient needs intensive care, community living may not be safe enough.","zh":"如果病人需要密集照顧，社區生活可能不夠安全。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against treating one solution as universal.","zh":"這個片語提醒人們不要把一個解決方法當作普遍適用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"those suffering moderate cases of","meaning":"患有中度……的人","examples":[{"en":"Those suffering moderate cases of mental illness may gain more from community care.","zh":"患有中度精神病的人可能從社區照顧中獲益更多。"},{"en":"Those suffering moderate cases of something are people whose condition is neither mild nor extremely severe.","zh":"Those suffering moderate cases of something 指病情既非輕微也非極嚴重的人。"},{"en":"Patients suffering moderate anxiety may need counselling but not hospital admission.","zh":"患有中度焦慮的病人可能需要輔導，但不需住院。"},{"en":"If illness is moderate, community support may be enough when it is consistent.","zh":"如果病情屬中度，持續社區支援可能已足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a middle level of severity.","zh":"這個片語指出中等嚴重程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"mental illness","meaning":"精神病；精神疾病","examples":[{"en":"People with mental illness may need different levels of support.","zh":"患有精神病的人可能需要不同程度的支援。"},{"en":"Mental illness refers to conditions that affect mood, thinking, behaviour, or daily functioning.","zh":"Mental illness 指影響情緒、思維、行為或日常功能的疾病。"},{"en":"Depression, schizophrenia, and anxiety disorders are examples of mental illness.","zh":"抑鬱症、精神分裂症和焦慮症都是精神疾病的例子。"},{"en":"If mental illness is treated early, recovery and stability may be easier.","zh":"如果精神病及早治療，康復和穩定可能較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase should be used carefully and respectfully.","zh":"這個片語應謹慎並尊重地使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stand to gain more from","meaning":"有望從……獲益更多","examples":[{"en":"Moderately ill patients stand to gain more from community care.","zh":"病情中度的病人有望從社區照顧中獲益更多。"},{"en":"To stand to gain more from something means to be likely to benefit more from it.","zh":"To stand to gain more from something 指很可能從某事獲得更多好處。"},{"en":"Students who practise speaking daily stand to gain more from an English course.","zh":"每天練習口語的學生有望從英語課中獲益更多。"},{"en":"If patients are already stable, they may gain more from community life than from confinement.","zh":"如果病人已經穩定，他們可能從社區生活中比從禁閉中獲益更多。"},{"en":"This phrase predicts who is most likely to benefit.","zh":"這個片語預測誰最可能受益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"more pronounced mental illness","meaning":"較嚴重的精神病","examples":[{"en":"Patients with more pronounced mental illness may need more intensive support.","zh":"患有較嚴重精神病的病人可能需要更密集支援。"},{"en":"More pronounced mental illness means mental illness that is clearer, stronger, or more severe.","zh":"More pronounced mental illness 指更明顯、更強或更嚴重的精神病。"},{"en":"A patient with more pronounced symptoms may need hospital care rather than occasional visits.","zh":"症狀較明顯的病人可能需要住院照顧，而不是偶爾探訪。"},{"en":"If the illness is more pronounced, ordinary community support may not be enough.","zh":"如果病情較嚴重，普通社區支援可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase compares severity of illness.","zh":"這個片語比較疾病嚴重程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"one-size-fits-all policy","meaning":"一刀切政策","examples":[{"en":"Community care should not be treated as a one-size-fits-all policy.","zh":"社區照顧不應被視為一刀切政策。"},{"en":"A one-size-fits-all policy is a single policy applied to everyone without considering different needs.","zh":"One-size-fits-all policy 是不考慮不同需要而套用於所有人的單一政策。"},{"en":"A school rule may fail if it treats all learners as exactly the same.","zh":"如果學校規則把所有學習者視為完全一樣，它可能失敗。"},{"en":"If patients have different illnesses and risks, one policy cannot suit all of them.","zh":"如果病人有不同疾病和風險，一項政策不可能適合所有人。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises oversimplified solutions.","zh":"這個片語批評過度簡化的解決方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"far better infrastructure","meaning":"好得多的基礎支援架構","examples":[{"en":"There is now a far better infrastructure of helpers and social workers.","zh":"現在已有好得多的支援人員和社工基礎架構。"},{"en":"Far better infrastructure means a much stronger support system, organisation, or network.","zh":"Far better infrastructure 指強得多的支援系統、組織或網絡。"},{"en":"A city has far better infrastructure when transport, hospitals, and internet services work reliably.","zh":"當交通、醫院和網絡服務可靠運作，城市就有好得多的基建。"},{"en":"If mental-health infrastructure improves, community care becomes safer.","zh":"如果精神健康基礎支援改善，社區照顧會更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes major improvement in the systems behind a service.","zh":"這個片語描述服務背後系統的重大改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"helpers and social workers","meaning":"支援人員和社工","examples":[{"en":"Helpers and social workers support community-care schemes.","zh":"支援人員和社工支援社區照顧計劃。"},{"en":"Helpers and social workers are people who provide practical, emotional, or social support.","zh":"Helpers and social workers 是提供實際、情緒或社會支援的人。"},{"en":"Social workers may help patients find housing, benefits, and counselling.","zh":"社工可能幫助病人尋找住屋、福利和輔導。"},{"en":"If helpers and social workers are available, families do not carry the whole burden alone.","zh":"如果有支援人員和社工，家庭就不用獨自承擔全部負擔。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people who support vulnerable individuals in daily life.","zh":"這個片語指在日常生活中支援脆弱人士的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in place","meaning":"已經存在；已安排好","examples":[{"en":"There is now a better support system in place.","zh":"現在已有較好的支援系統安排好。"},{"en":"In place means already arranged, available, or operating.","zh":"In place 指已經安排、可用或正在運作。"},{"en":"A school should have emergency procedures in place before a storm arrives.","zh":"學校應在風暴到來前已有緊急程序安排好。"},{"en":"If support systems are in place, patients can receive help more quickly.","zh":"如果支援系統已經存在，病人可以更快得到幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that preparation or structure already exists.","zh":"這個片語顯示準備或架構已存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"than previously","meaning":"比以前","examples":[{"en":"The infrastructure is stronger now than previously.","zh":"現在的基礎支援架構比以前更強。"},{"en":"Than previously means compared with before.","zh":"Than previously 指與以前相比。"},{"en":"The new timetable gives students more rest than previously.","zh":"新時間表比以前給學生更多休息時間。"},{"en":"If services are better than previously, patients may have a greater chance of recovery.","zh":"如果服務比以前更好，病人可能有更大康復機會。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the present with an earlier situation.","zh":"這個片語把現在與較早情況作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stand a greater chance of success","meaning":"有更大成功機會","examples":[{"en":"The scheme stands a greater chance of success than in the past.","zh":"這項計劃比過去有更大成功機會。"},{"en":"To stand a greater chance of success means to be more likely to succeed.","zh":"To stand a greater chance of success 指更有可能成功。"},{"en":"A student stands a greater chance of success if they practise regularly and ask for feedback.","zh":"如果學生定期練習並尋求回饋，就有更大成功機會。"},{"en":"If community care has better staff and services, it is more likely to work.","zh":"如果社區照顧有更好人手和服務，它就更可能奏效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improved likelihood of a positive result.","zh":"這個片語描述取得正面結果的機會提高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take a different view","meaning":"持不同看法","examples":[{"en":"Anita Brown takes a different view of community care.","zh":"Anita Brown 對社區照顧持不同看法。"},{"en":"To take a different view means to have another opinion.","zh":"To take a different view 指持有另一種意見。"},{"en":"Parents may take a different view of online learning from teachers.","zh":"家長對網上學習的看法可能與老師不同。"},{"en":"If people have different experiences, they may reach different conclusions.","zh":"如果人們有不同經驗，他們可能得出不同結論。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces disagreement or an alternative perspective.","zh":"這個片語引出分歧或另一角度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be protective towards","meaning":"對……有保護意識","examples":[{"en":"Anita Brown is protective towards her children.","zh":"Anita Brown 對她的孩子有保護意識。"},{"en":"To be protective towards someone means to want to keep them safe from harm.","zh":"To be protective towards someone 指想保護某人免受傷害。"},{"en":"Parents are often protective towards young children near busy roads.","zh":"家長通常在繁忙道路附近對年幼孩子很有保護意識。"},{"en":"If someone feels protective towards family members, they may oppose policies they see as risky.","zh":"如果某人對家人有保護意識，他們可能反對自己視為有風險的政策。"},{"en":"This phrase describes care mixed with caution.","zh":"這個片語描述帶有謹慎的關懷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"would not support any scheme that","meaning":"不會支持任何……的計劃","examples":[{"en":"She would not support any scheme that might put her children in danger.","zh":"她不會支持任何可能令她孩子陷入危險的計劃。"},{"en":"Would not support any scheme that means would reject any plan if it has that feature or risk.","zh":"Would not support any scheme that 指如果任何計劃有某特點或風險，就會拒絕支持。"},{"en":"Parents may not support any scheme that reduces student safety.","zh":"家長可能不支持任何降低學生安全的計劃。"},{"en":"If a policy seems to put children at risk, some families will oppose it strongly.","zh":"如果政策似乎令孩子有風險，一些家庭會強烈反對。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a firm condition for rejection.","zh":"這個片語表達拒絕的堅定條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"put someone in danger","meaning":"令某人陷入危險","examples":[{"en":"She worries that the scheme might put her children in danger.","zh":"她擔心這項計劃可能令她的孩子陷入危險。"},{"en":"To put someone in danger means to expose them to possible harm.","zh":"To put someone in danger 指令某人面對可能傷害。"},{"en":"Leaving medicine within a child’s reach can put the child in danger.","zh":"把藥物放在孩子可觸及的地方，可以令孩子陷入危險。"},{"en":"If safety checks fail, the public may be put in danger.","zh":"如果安全檢查失效，公眾可能陷入危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating risk for another person.","zh":"這個片語描述為他人造成風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"I guess","meaning":"我估計；我想","examples":[{"en":"I guess there must be assessment methods in place.","zh":"我估計一定已有評估方法。"},{"en":"I guess means I think, but I am not completely certain.","zh":"I guess 指我想或我估計，但不是完全肯定。"},{"en":"I guess the bus is late because the traffic is heavy.","zh":"我想巴士遲到是因為交通繁忙。"},{"en":"If someone says “I guess,” they are often expressing a cautious opinion.","zh":"如果有人說 “I guess”，他們通常是在表達謹慎看法。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds informal and less certain than “I believe.”","zh":"這個片語較口語化，肯定程度低於 “I believe”。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"assessment methods","meaning":"評估方法","examples":[{"en":"Assessment methods should identify dangerous individuals.","zh":"評估方法應識別危險人物。"},{"en":"Assessment methods are ways of judging a person’s condition, risk, or needs.","zh":"Assessment methods 是判斷某人狀況、風險或需要的方法。"},{"en":"Schools use assessment methods such as tests, projects, and interviews.","zh":"學校使用測驗、專題和面談等評估方法。"},{"en":"If assessment methods are weak, unsuitable patients may be placed in the wrong care setting.","zh":"如果評估方法薄弱，不合適的病人可能被安排到錯誤照顧環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the tools used to make careful decisions.","zh":"這個片語描述用來作謹慎決定的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"ensure that","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Assessment methods should ensure that dangerous individuals are not released.","zh":"評估方法應確保危險人物不會被放出。"},{"en":"To ensure that means to make certain that something happens or does not happen.","zh":"To ensure that 指確保某事發生或不發生。"},{"en":"Teachers check attendance to ensure that every student is safe.","zh":"老師檢查出席，以確保每名學生安全。"},{"en":"If services ensure that patients receive follow-up care, risks may be reduced.","zh":"如果服務確保病人得到跟進照顧，風險可能降低。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on making an outcome certain.","zh":"這個片語集中於令結果確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"dangerous individuals","meaning":"危險人物","examples":[{"en":"The speaker worries that dangerous individuals may enter the community.","zh":"說話者擔心危險人物可能進入社區。"},{"en":"Dangerous individuals are people who may seriously harm others if not properly supervised or treated.","zh":"Dangerous individuals 是如果沒有適當監督或治療，可能嚴重傷害他人的人。"},{"en":"A court may require dangerous individuals to receive close monitoring.","zh":"法庭可能要求危險人物接受密切監察。"},{"en":"If assessment is careful, genuinely dangerous individuals can be identified before release.","zh":"如果評估謹慎，真正危險的人可以在釋放前被識別。"},{"en":"This phrase should be used cautiously because it can easily create stigma.","zh":"這個片語應謹慎使用，因為它容易造成污名。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be let loose amongst the public","meaning":"被放到公眾之中","examples":[{"en":"Dangerous individuals should not be let loose amongst the public.","zh":"危險人物不應被放到公眾之中。"},{"en":"To be let loose amongst the public means to be released into society without enough control or supervision.","zh":"To be let loose amongst the public 指在沒有足夠控制或監督下被釋放到社會。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds fearful because it suggests danger spreading into ordinary public life.","zh":"這個片語聽起來帶有恐懼，因為它暗示危險進入普通公共生活。"},{"en":"If someone is genuinely unsafe, release without support may endanger both them and others.","zh":"如果某人確實不安全，沒有支援地釋放可能危及他本人和他人。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses public anxiety about safety.","zh":"這個片語表達公眾對安全的焦慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"not for it at all","meaning":"完全不支持","examples":[{"en":"Anita Brown is not for the scheme at all.","zh":"Anita Brown 完全不支持這項計劃。"},{"en":"Not for it at all means completely against an idea or plan.","zh":"Not for it at all 指完全反對某想法或計劃。"},{"en":"Some parents are not for it at all when a school proposes longer class hours.","zh":"當學校建議延長上課時間，一些家長完全不支持。"},{"en":"If someone fears a policy will harm their family, they may reject it totally.","zh":"如果某人擔心政策傷害其家庭，他可能完全拒絕它。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and shows strong opposition.","zh":"這個片語較口語化，顯示強烈反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"feel secure","meaning":"感到安全","examples":[{"en":"She wants to feel secure where she lives.","zh":"她想在自己居住的地方感到安全。"},{"en":"To feel secure means to feel safe, protected, and free from serious worry.","zh":"To feel secure 指感到安全、受保護且沒有重大憂慮。"},{"en":"Children feel secure when adults respond calmly and consistently.","zh":"當成人冷靜且一致地回應，孩子會感到安全。"},{"en":"If residents do not feel secure, they may oppose community-care housing nearby.","zh":"如果居民感到不安全，他們可能反對附近設社區照顧住所。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional safety as well as physical safety.","zh":"這個片語描述情緒安全以及身體安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"where I live","meaning":"我居住的地方","examples":[{"en":"She wants to feel secure where she lives.","zh":"她想在自己居住的地方感到安全。"},{"en":"Where I live means the place or neighbourhood in which I live.","zh":"Where I live 指我生活的地方或社區。"},{"en":"Where I live, buses are frequent but flats are expensive.","zh":"在我居住的地方，巴士很頻密，但樓價很高。"},{"en":"If people worry about safety where they live, local policy becomes personal.","zh":"如果人們擔心自己居住地方的安全，本地政策就變得很切身。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a general issue to someone’s own home area.","zh":"這個片語把一般議題連接到某人的居住地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"more to the point","meaning":"更重要的是","examples":[{"en":"More to the point, she wants her children to be safe.","zh":"更重要的是，她希望她的孩子安全。"},{"en":"More to the point means more importantly or more directly relevant.","zh":"More to the point 指更重要或更直接相關。"},{"en":"The flat is small; more to the point, it is too far from school.","zh":"這個單位很小；更重要的是，它離學校太遠。"},{"en":"If a policy is expensive, that matters; more to the point, it must also be safe.","zh":"如果政策昂貴，那固然重要；更重要的是，它也必須安全。"},{"en":"This phrase shifts attention to the most important issue.","zh":"這個片語把注意力轉向最重要的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be under threat","meaning":"受到威脅","examples":[{"en":"She does not want her children to be under any threat.","zh":"她不希望她的孩子受到任何威脅。"},{"en":"To be under threat means to face possible danger or harm.","zh":"To be under threat 指面對可能危險或傷害。"},{"en":"A school may be under threat of closure if student numbers fall sharply.","zh":"如果學生人數大幅下降，學校可能面臨關閉威脅。"},{"en":"If residents feel under threat, they may demand stronger safety measures.","zh":"如果居民感到受到威脅，他們可能要求更強安全措施。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a state of danger or pressure.","zh":"這個片語描述危險或壓力狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"former mental health nurse","meaning":"前精神科護士","examples":[{"en":"Bob Ratchett is a former mental health nurse.","zh":"Bob Ratchett 是一名前精神科護士。"},{"en":"A former mental health nurse is someone who used to work as a nurse in mental-health care.","zh":"Former mental health nurse 是曾在精神健康照顧中任職護士的人。"},{"en":"A former mental health nurse may understand both hospital routines and patient needs.","zh":"前精神科護士可能了解醫院常規和病人需要。"},{"en":"If someone worked in the field before, their opinion may be shaped by practical experience.","zh":"如果某人過去曾在該領域工作，其意見可能受實際經驗影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a person’s past professional role.","zh":"這個片語描述一個人過去的專業角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"take a more positive view of","meaning":"對……持較正面的看法","examples":[{"en":"Bob Ratchett takes a more positive view of community-care projects.","zh":"Bob Ratchett 對社區照顧計劃持較正面的看法。"},{"en":"To take a more positive view of something means to judge it more favourably.","zh":"To take a more positive view of something 指對某事作較有利的判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher may take a more positive view of homework if students use it to improve.","zh":"如果學生用功課來改善，老師可能對功課持較正面看法。"},{"en":"If someone has seen patients succeed, they may view community care more positively.","zh":"如果某人見過病人成功，他可能對社區照顧看法較正面。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a favourable attitude compared with another view.","zh":"這個片語引出比另一觀點更有利的態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"community-care projects","meaning":"社區照顧計劃","examples":[{"en":"Community-care projects can help suitable patients live independently.","zh":"社區照顧計劃可以幫助合適病人獨立生活。"},{"en":"Community-care projects are organised schemes that support patients outside institutions.","zh":"Community-care projects 是在院舍以外支援病人的有組織計劃。"},{"en":"A community-care project may provide home visits, group activities, and medication checks.","zh":"社區照顧計劃可能提供家訪、小組活動和藥物檢查。"},{"en":"If community-care projects are well funded, families and patients receive stronger support.","zh":"如果社區照顧計劃有充足資金，家庭和病人會得到更強支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical programmes for care in ordinary communities.","zh":"這個片語描述在普通社區中提供照顧的實際計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"having worked in the field","meaning":"曾在該領域工作","examples":[{"en":"Having worked in the field, Bob Ratchett has seen patients benefit.","zh":"曾在該領域工作，Bob Ratchett 見過病人受益。"},{"en":"Having worked in the field means because someone has direct professional experience in that area.","zh":"Having worked in the field 指因某人在該範疇有直接專業經驗。"},{"en":"Having worked in education, a teacher understands why students fear exams.","zh":"曾在教育界工作，老師理解學生為何害怕考試。"},{"en":"If someone has worked in mental health, their opinion may be grounded in real cases.","zh":"如果某人曾在精神健康領域工作，其意見可能建基於真實個案。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a person’s view may be informed by experience.","zh":"這個片語解釋某人的看法為何受經驗支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in the field","meaning":"在該領域","examples":[{"en":"He worked in the field of mental health.","zh":"他曾在精神健康領域工作。"},{"en":"In the field means in a particular area of work or study.","zh":"In the field 指在某特定工作或研究範疇中。"},{"en":"A researcher in the field of education studies how students learn.","zh":"教育領域的研究員研究學生如何學習。"},{"en":"If someone has years in the field, they may understand practical difficulties better.","zh":"如果某人在該領域有多年經驗，他可能更了解實際困難。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a professional or academic area.","zh":"這個片語指出專業或學術範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"benefit from living","meaning":"從……生活中受益","examples":[{"en":"Patients can benefit from living an independent life.","zh":"病人可以從獨立生活中受益。"},{"en":"To benefit from living in a certain way means to improve because of that living arrangement.","zh":"To benefit from living in a certain way 指因某種生活安排而改善。"},{"en":"Children may benefit from living near school because they sleep longer and travel less.","zh":"孩子可能從住在學校附近受益，因為他們睡得更久、通勤更少。"},{"en":"If patients benefit from living outside institutions, their confidence may grow.","zh":"如果病人從院舍外生活中受益，他們的信心可能增長。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a lifestyle with its positive effects.","zh":"這個片語把生活方式與其正面效果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"away from an institution","meaning":"離開院舍","examples":[{"en":"Some patients do better away from an institution.","zh":"一些病人離開院舍後表現更好。"},{"en":"Away from an institution means outside a hospital, care home, or formal facility.","zh":"Away from an institution 指在醫院、護理院或正式設施以外。"},{"en":"A patient may feel more relaxed away from an institution and closer to family.","zh":"病人離開院舍並接近家人時，可能感到較放鬆。"},{"en":"If life away from an institution includes support, independence can become safer.","zh":"如果離開院舍後的生活包括支援，獨立可以變得更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts community life with institutional living.","zh":"這個片語把社區生活與院舍生活作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"well on their way to recovery","meaning":"康復進展良好","examples":[{"en":"Only patients well on their way to recovery should join such schemes.","zh":"只有康復進展良好的病人應加入這類計劃。"},{"en":"Well on their way to recovery means already making clear progress toward becoming well again.","zh":"Well on their way to recovery 指已明顯朝康復方向進展。"},{"en":"A student is well on their way to recovery when they return to school gradually after illness.","zh":"學生生病後逐步回校時，就是康復進展良好。"},{"en":"If patients are not yet stable, community care may be too risky.","zh":"如果病人尚未穩定，社區照顧可能風險太高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong progress, not complete recovery.","zh":"這個片語描述良好進展，而不是完全康復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"suitable for consideration","meaning":"適合被考慮","examples":[{"en":"Recovering patients may be suitable for consideration as participants.","zh":"正在康復的病人可能適合被考慮成為參加者。"},{"en":"Suitable for consideration means appropriate enough to be seriously thought about.","zh":"Suitable for consideration 指合適到值得被認真考慮。"},{"en":"A student with strong interest may be suitable for consideration for a leadership role.","zh":"有強烈興趣的學生可能適合被考慮擔任領袖角色。"},{"en":"If a patient is stable and supported, they may be considered for community care.","zh":"如果病人穩定且有支援，他可能被考慮接受社區照顧。"},{"en":"This phrase does not guarantee acceptance; it means the option is worth reviewing.","zh":"這個片語不保證被接受；它指某選項值得審視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"participants in such a scheme","meaning":"這類計劃的參加者","examples":[{"en":"Only suitable patients should become participants in such a scheme.","zh":"只有合適病人應成為這類計劃的參加者。"},{"en":"Participants in such a scheme are people who take part in that organised programme.","zh":"Participants in such a scheme 是參與該組織計劃的人。"},{"en":"Participants in a training scheme may receive lessons, support, and regular assessment.","zh":"培訓計劃的參加者可能接受課堂、支援和定期評估。"},{"en":"If participants are chosen carefully, the scheme is more likely to succeed.","zh":"如果參加者被謹慎選擇，計劃較可能成功。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the people included in a programme.","zh":"這個片語指出被納入計劃的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"condemn someone to","meaning":"判定某人要承受……","examples":[{"en":"It may be unfair to condemn a patient to life in an institution.","zh":"判定病人要一生留在院舍可能是不公平的。"},{"en":"To condemn someone to something means to force them into a bad or limiting situation.","zh":"To condemn someone to something 指迫使某人進入糟糕或受限制的情況。"},{"en":"A child should not be condemned to poor education because of family income.","zh":"孩子不應因家庭收入而被迫承受劣質教育。"},{"en":"If a patient could live safely in the community, permanent confinement may be unfair.","zh":"如果病人能安全地在社區生活，永久禁閉可能不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests harsh judgement or unfair punishment.","zh":"這個片語通常暗示嚴苛判斷或不公平懲罰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a lifetime in an institution","meaning":"一生在院舍中","examples":[{"en":"Some patients should not be forced into a lifetime in an institution.","zh":"一些病人不應被迫一生留在院舍中。"},{"en":"A lifetime in an institution means spending one’s whole life in a hospital or care facility.","zh":"A lifetime in an institution 指一生在醫院或照顧設施中度過。"},{"en":"A person may lose ordinary skills after a lifetime in an institution.","zh":"一個人一生在院舍中生活後，可能失去普通生活技能。"},{"en":"If community care is possible, a lifetime in an institution may be unnecessarily restrictive.","zh":"如果社區照顧可行，一生在院舍中可能是不必要的限制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-term confinement and loss of ordinary life.","zh":"這個片語描述長期禁閉和失去普通生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a fairly fulfilled and independent life","meaning":"相當充實而獨立的生活","examples":[{"en":"Some patients can live a fairly fulfilled and independent life outside institutions.","zh":"一些病人可以在院舍以外過相當充實而獨立的生活。"},{"en":"A fairly fulfilled and independent life is a life with meaning, routine, relationships, and some self-control.","zh":"Fairly fulfilled and independent life 是有意義、規律、關係和一定自主的生活。"},{"en":"A patient may feel fulfilled by working part-time, seeing friends, and managing daily tasks.","zh":"病人可能透過兼職工作、見朋友和處理日常任務而感到充實。"},{"en":"If support is reliable, independence can become realistic rather than dangerous.","zh":"如果支援可靠，獨立就可以變得實際，而不是危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a positive life that is not necessarily perfect.","zh":"這個片語描述正面但不一定完美的生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"outside the institution","meaning":"在院舍以外","examples":[{"en":"Some patients can live successfully outside the institution.","zh":"一些病人可以在院舍以外成功生活。"},{"en":"Outside the institution means not living within the hospital or care facility.","zh":"Outside the institution 指不是住在醫院或照顧設施之內。"},{"en":"A patient may live outside the institution but still attend regular appointments.","zh":"病人可能住在院舍以外，但仍定期覆診。"},{"en":"If life outside the institution is supported, it may improve confidence.","zh":"如果院舍以外的生活有支援，它可能提升信心。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts community living with institutional care.","zh":"這個片語把社區生活與院舍照顧作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"which of the following statements is accurate","meaning":"以下哪項陳述準確","examples":[{"en":"Students must decide which of the following statements is accurate.","zh":"學生必須判斷以下哪項陳述準確。"},{"en":"Which of the following statements is accurate means students must choose the true or correct option.","zh":"Which of the following statements is accurate 指學生必須選出真確或正確選項。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should compare each option with the passage before choosing.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先把每個選項與文章比較，再作選擇。"},{"en":"If one word in an option changes the meaning, the statement may become inaccurate.","zh":"如果選項中一個字改變意思，陳述可能變得不準確。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common multiple-choice instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見選擇題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"illegal surgical procedures","meaning":"非法外科手術","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions illegal surgical procedures on mentally ill patients.","zh":"題目提及在精神病患者身上進行非法外科手術。"},{"en":"Illegal surgical procedures are operations performed against the law.","zh":"Illegal surgical procedures 是違反法律進行的手術。"},{"en":"A clinic carrying out operations without proper approval may perform illegal surgical procedures.","zh":"沒有適當批准便進行手術的診所，可能正在進行非法外科手術。"},{"en":"If surgery is illegal, patients may be harmed without protection or accountability.","zh":"如果手術非法，病人可能在缺乏保障和問責下受害。"},{"en":"This phrase combines medical action with legal wrongdoing.","zh":"這個片語結合醫療行動和法律錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be carried out on","meaning":"在……身上進行","examples":[{"en":"Some surgical procedures were carried out on mentally ill patients.","zh":"一些外科程序在精神病患者身上進行。"},{"en":"To be carried out on someone means to be performed on that person.","zh":"To be carried out on someone 指在某人身上執行某事。"},{"en":"A medical test may be carried out on a patient before treatment begins.","zh":"治療開始前，醫療測試可能在病人身上進行。"},{"en":"If a procedure is carried out without consent, ethical problems arise.","zh":"如果程序未經同意進行，就會出現倫理問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for tests, operations, or experiments.","zh":"這個片語常用於測試、手術或實驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"see an increase in","meaning":"見證……增加","examples":[{"en":"The Victorian era did not necessarily see an increase in mental illness.","zh":"維多利亞時代不一定見證精神病增加。"},{"en":"To see an increase in something means to experience or record a rise in it.","zh":"To see an increase in something 指經歷或錄得某事上升。"},{"en":"A school may see an increase in absences during flu season.","zh":"學校可能在流感季節見證缺席人數增加。"},{"en":"If a city sees an increase in homelessness, public services may face pressure.","zh":"如果城市見證無家者增加，公共服務可能面對壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rise observed in a period or place.","zh":"這個片語描述某時期或地方觀察到的上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"amongst married couples","meaning":"在已婚夫婦之中","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to mental illness amongst married couples.","zh":"題目提及已婚夫婦之中的精神病。"},{"en":"Amongst married couples means among husbands and wives or people in marriages.","zh":"Amongst married couples 指在丈夫和妻子或婚姻關係人士之中。"},{"en":"Financial stress can create tension amongst married couples.","zh":"經濟壓力可以在已婚夫婦之中造成緊張。"},{"en":"If mental-health support is unavailable, difficulties may affect both partners.","zh":"如果沒有精神健康支援，困難可能影響雙方。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific group of people in marriage relationships.","zh":"這個片語指出婚姻關係中的特定群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"mental institutions","meaning":"精神病院；精神病機構","examples":[{"en":"Mental institutions were once associated with isolation and punishment.","zh":"精神病院曾與隔離和懲罰有關。"},{"en":"Mental institutions are facilities where people with mental illness are housed or treated.","zh":"Mental institutions 是收容或治療精神病患者的設施。"},{"en":"Old mental institutions often separated patients from family and community life.","zh":"舊精神病院常把病人與家庭和社區生活分隔開。"},{"en":"If mental institutions focus only on control, they may harm patients’ dignity.","zh":"如果精神病院只注重控制，它們可能傷害病人尊嚴。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal places for psychiatric care or confinement.","zh":"這個片語指精神科照顧或收容的正式場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"better-equipped for","meaning":"更有設備去應付","examples":[{"en":"Old mental institutions were not necessarily better-equipped for patient care.","zh":"舊精神病機構不一定更有設備去照顧病人。"},{"en":"Better-equipped for something means having better tools, staff, knowledge, or facilities to handle it.","zh":"Better-equipped for something 指擁有更好的工具、人手、知識或設施去處理某事。"},{"en":"A school with trained counsellors is better-equipped for student mental-health problems.","zh":"有受訓輔導員的學校更有能力應付學生精神健康問題。"},{"en":"If a hospital is better-equipped for emergencies, patients can be treated faster.","zh":"如果醫院更有設備應付緊急情況，病人可更快接受治療。"},{"en":"This phrase describes readiness and resources.","zh":"這個片語描述準備程度和資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"benefitted when","meaning":"在……時得益","examples":[{"en":"Some people may have benefitted when a relative was sent away.","zh":"有些人在親人被送走時可能得益。"},{"en":"Benefitted when means gained an advantage at the time something happened.","zh":"Benefitted when 指在某事發生時獲得好處。"},{"en":"A business may have benefitted when a competitor closed down.","zh":"當競爭對手結業時，一間企業可能得益。"},{"en":"If an unwanted heir was removed, another relative might gain property or power.","zh":"如果不受歡迎的繼承人被移除，另一名親屬可能獲得財產或權力。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest an unfair advantage from someone else’s misfortune.","zh":"這個片語可以暗示從他人不幸中取得不公平利益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be sent to a mental asylum","meaning":"被送進精神病院","examples":[{"en":"An unwanted relative could be sent to a mental asylum.","zh":"不受歡迎的親人可能被送進精神病院。"},{"en":"To be sent to a mental asylum means to be placed in an old-style institution for mental illness.","zh":"To be sent to a mental asylum 指被送進舊式精神病收容機構。"},{"en":"In the past, some people feared being sent to a mental asylum unfairly.","zh":"過去，有些人害怕被不公平地送進精神病院。"},{"en":"If asylum admission was abused, families could remove inconvenient relatives.","zh":"如果收容制度被濫用，家庭可以移除麻煩親人。"},{"en":"This phrase reflects historical institutional treatment.","zh":"這個片語反映歷史上的院舍治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"what the writer means by","meaning":"作者所指的是","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what the writer means by “legitimised abuse.”","zh":"題目問作者所指的 “legitimised abuse” 是甚麼意思。"},{"en":"What the writer means by asks students to explain the intended meaning of a phrase.","zh":"What the writer means by 要求學生解釋某片語的原意。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students should use context to decide what the writer means by a difficult expression.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應用語境判斷作者所指的困難表達。"},{"en":"If a phrase is metaphorical, the answer should explain the idea, not translate word by word.","zh":"如果片語是比喻，答案應解釋概念，而不是逐字翻譯。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in meaning-in-context questions.","zh":"這個片語用於語境詞義題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"proper guidelines for","meaning":"關於……的正式指引","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to proper guidelines for punishment.","zh":"選項提及關於懲罰的正式指引。"},{"en":"Proper guidelines for something are clear and appropriate rules for doing it.","zh":"Proper guidelines for something 是處理某事的清晰且合適規則。"},{"en":"Schools need proper guidelines for handling bullying complaints.","zh":"學校需要關於處理欺凌投訴的正式指引。"},{"en":"If staff lack proper guidelines, decisions may become unfair or inconsistent.","zh":"如果職員缺乏正式指引，決定可能變得不公平或不一致。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official instructions that should guide action.","zh":"這個片語描述應指導行動的正式指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"punishment of","meaning":"對……的懲罰","examples":[{"en":"The punishment of mentally ill patients was common in old institutions.","zh":"在舊院舍中，對精神病患者的懲罰很常見。"},{"en":"Punishment of someone means making them suffer a penalty for behaviour seen as wrong.","zh":"Punishment of someone 指因被視為錯誤的行為而令某人承受懲罰。"},{"en":"The punishment of students should never involve humiliation or physical harm.","zh":"對學生的懲罰絕不應涉及羞辱或身體傷害。"},{"en":"If illness is treated as bad behaviour, punishment may replace proper care.","zh":"如果疾病被當成壞行為，懲罰可能取代適當照顧。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on who receives the penalty.","zh":"這個片語集中於誰承受懲罰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"maltreatment of","meaning":"對……的虐待","examples":[{"en":"The maltreatment of mentally ill patients was often tolerated.","zh":"對精神病患者的虐待往往被容忍。"},{"en":"Maltreatment of someone means cruel, unfair, or harmful treatment of that person.","zh":"Maltreatment of someone 指對某人的殘酷、不公平或有害對待。"},{"en":"The maltreatment of workers may include unsafe housing and unpaid wages.","zh":"對工人的虐待可能包括不安全住宿和欠薪。"},{"en":"If maltreatment is ignored, victims may lose trust in the system.","zh":"如果虐待被忽視，受害者可能失去對制度的信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious mistreatment, not minor inconvenience.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重不當對待，而不是小不便。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be tolerated","meaning":"被容忍","examples":[{"en":"Abuse was tolerated because it was not treated as illegal.","zh":"虐待被容忍，因為它沒有被視為非法。"},{"en":"To be tolerated means to be allowed to continue, even if it is wrong or unpleasant.","zh":"To be tolerated 指即使某事錯誤或令人不快，仍被容許繼續。"},{"en":"Bullying should not be tolerated in any school.","zh":"任何學校都不應容忍欺凌。"},{"en":"If poor treatment is tolerated for years, it can become part of the system.","zh":"如果惡劣待遇多年被容忍，它可以成為制度的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase shows acceptance or failure to stop something.","zh":"這個片語顯示接受或未能阻止某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be legally entitled to","meaning":"在法律上有權去……","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether certain people were legally entitled to punish patients.","zh":"選項問某些人在法律上是否有權懲罰病人。"},{"en":"To be legally entitled to do something means to have the right to do it under the law.","zh":"To be legally entitled to do something 指在法律下有權做某事。"},{"en":"Tenants may be legally entitled to safe living conditions.","zh":"租客在法律上可能有權享有安全居住環境。"},{"en":"If staff are not legally entitled to use force, doing so may be abuse.","zh":"如果職員在法律上無權使用武力，這樣做可能是虐待。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a right recognised by law.","zh":"這個片語指法律承認的權利。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"physical abuse","meaning":"身體虐待","examples":[{"en":"Physical abuse of patients occurred in some institutions.","zh":"一些機構中曾發生對病人的身體虐待。"},{"en":"Physical abuse means hurting someone’s body through violence, force, or harmful treatment.","zh":"Physical abuse 指透過暴力、武力或有害對待傷害某人的身體。"},{"en":"Physical abuse can include hitting, restraining, or injuring a vulnerable person.","zh":"身體虐待可以包括毆打、束縛或傷害脆弱人士。"},{"en":"If physical abuse happens in a care setting, protection systems have failed.","zh":"如果身體虐待在照顧環境中發生，保障制度已經失效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bodily harm, not just emotional cruelty.","zh":"這個片語描述身體傷害，而不只是情緒殘酷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a legal requirement","meaning":"法律要求","examples":[{"en":"Physical abuse was not a legal requirement of mental institutions.","zh":"身體虐待並不是精神病機構的法律要求。"},{"en":"A legal requirement is something the law says must be done.","zh":"A legal requirement 是法律規定必須做的事情。"},{"en":"Wearing seat belts is a legal requirement in many places.","zh":"在許多地方，佩戴安全帶是法律要求。"},{"en":"If something is not a legal requirement, people cannot claim the law forced them to do it.","zh":"如果某事不是法律要求，人們不能聲稱法律迫使他們這樣做。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an obligation created by law.","zh":"這個片語描述由法律產生的義務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"bring about changes","meaning":"帶來改變","examples":[{"en":"Public criticism helped bring about changes in patient treatment.","zh":"公眾批評有助帶來病人待遇的改變。"},{"en":"To bring about changes means to cause changes to happen.","zh":"To bring about changes 指造成改變發生。"},{"en":"Student feedback can bring about changes in how a course is taught.","zh":"學生回饋可以帶來課程教法的改變。"},{"en":"If activists expose abuse, public pressure may bring about reform.","zh":"如果運動人士揭露虐待，公眾壓力可能帶來改革。"},{"en":"This phrase connects action with resulting change.","zh":"這個片語把行動與隨之而來的改變連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"treatment of mentally ill patients","meaning":"對精神病患者的治療","examples":[{"en":"The treatment of mentally ill patients gradually changed.","zh":"對精神病患者的治療逐漸改變。"},{"en":"Treatment of mentally ill patients means the way people with mental illness are cared for, managed, or medically treated.","zh":"Treatment of mentally ill patients 指精神病患者被照顧、管理或醫療治療的方式。"},{"en":"Good treatment of mentally ill patients includes respect, therapy, medication, and social support.","zh":"良好精神病患者治療包括尊重、治療、藥物和社會支援。"},{"en":"If treatment improves, patients may regain dignity and independence.","zh":"如果治療改善，病人可能重新獲得尊嚴和獨立。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both medical care and everyday human treatment.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋醫療照顧和日常人道對待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"radio documentary","meaning":"電台紀錄片","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions a radio documentary about patient maltreatment.","zh":"選項提及一部關於病人受虐待的電台紀錄片。"},{"en":"A radio documentary is a factual audio programme that investigates or explains a topic.","zh":"Radio documentary 是調查或解釋某主題的真實音頻節目。"},{"en":"A radio documentary may interview patients, doctors, and families.","zh":"電台紀錄片可能訪問病人、醫生和家屬。"},{"en":"If a documentary exposes abuse, it can influence public opinion.","zh":"如果紀錄片揭露虐待，它可以影響公眾看法。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to non-fiction reporting in audio form.","zh":"這個片語指音頻形式的非虛構報道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"expose patient maltreatment","meaning":"揭露病人受虐待","examples":[{"en":"A documentary can expose patient maltreatment.","zh":"紀錄片可以揭露病人受虐待。"},{"en":"To expose patient maltreatment means to reveal cruel or unfair treatment of patients.","zh":"To expose patient maltreatment 指揭露對病人的殘酷或不公平待遇。"},{"en":"A journalist may expose patient maltreatment by interviewing witnesses and checking records.","zh":"記者可能透過訪問證人和查核紀錄揭露病人受虐待。"},{"en":"If maltreatment is exposed, authorities may be forced to investigate.","zh":"如果虐待被揭露，當局可能被迫調查。"},{"en":"This phrase connects public revelation with wrongdoing in care.","zh":"這個片語把公開揭露與照顧中的錯誤行為連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"rebel against","meaning":"反抗；反對","examples":[{"en":"People rebelled against the abuse of mentally ill patients.","zh":"人們反對虐待精神病患者。"},{"en":"To rebel against something means to resist or oppose it strongly.","zh":"To rebel against something 指強烈抵抗或反對某事。"},{"en":"Students may rebel against unfair rules if they feel ignored.","zh":"如果學生感到被忽視，他們可能反抗不公平規則。"},{"en":"If people rebel against abuse, they may demand new laws and better oversight.","zh":"如果人們反對虐待，他們可能要求新法律和更好監管。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active opposition to authority or injustice.","zh":"這個片語描述對權威或不公的主動反抗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"consistent abuse","meaning":"持續虐待","examples":[{"en":"Consistent abuse of patients led to calls for reform.","zh":"對病人的持續虐待引發改革呼聲。"},{"en":"Consistent abuse means repeated or continuing mistreatment.","zh":"Consistent abuse 指反覆或持續的不當對待。"},{"en":"Consistent abuse in a workplace may include regular insults, threats, or unsafe demands.","zh":"工作場所中的持續虐待可能包括經常侮辱、威脅或不安全要求。"},{"en":"If abuse is consistent, it becomes a pattern rather than a single incident.","zh":"如果虐待是持續的，它就成為模式，而不是單一事件。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses repeated harm over time.","zh":"這個片語強調隨時間反覆發生的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be proved to be ineffective","meaning":"被證明無效","examples":[{"en":"Some previous treatments were later proved to be ineffective.","zh":"一些以往治療後來被證明無效。"},{"en":"To be proved to be ineffective means evidence later shows that something does not work.","zh":"To be proved to be ineffective 指證據後來顯示某事不起作用。"},{"en":"A study may prove a popular study method to be ineffective.","zh":"研究可能證明某種流行溫習方法無效。"},{"en":"If a treatment is ineffective, patients may suffer without receiving real benefit.","zh":"如果治療無效，病人可能受苦而沒有真正得益。"},{"en":"This phrase describes failure shown by evidence.","zh":"這個片語描述由證據顯示的失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be revealed","meaning":"被揭露","examples":[{"en":"Maltreatment of patients could eventually be revealed.","zh":"對病人的虐待最終可能被揭露。"},{"en":"To be revealed means to become known after being hidden or unknown.","zh":"To be revealed 指隱藏或未知的事情變得被知道。"},{"en":"Exam results are revealed after marking is finished.","zh":"考試成績在改卷完成後被公布。"},{"en":"If abuse is revealed publicly, institutions may face pressure to change.","zh":"如果虐待被公開揭露，機構可能面對改革壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information becoming visible.","zh":"這個片語描述資訊變得可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a feature of","meaning":"……的一個特點","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about a feature of early community-care schemes.","zh":"題目問早期社區照顧計劃的一個特點。"},{"en":"A feature of something is an important characteristic or part of it.","zh":"A feature of something 是某事物的重要特徵或部分。"},{"en":"A useful feature of online lessons is that students can review recordings.","zh":"網上課堂的一個有用特點是學生可以重看錄影。"},{"en":"If family support was a feature of early care, relatives carried much responsibility.","zh":"如果家庭支援是早期照顧的特點，親屬就承擔很多責任。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what belongs to or characterises something.","zh":"這個片語指出某事物擁有或表現出的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"early care in the community schemes","meaning":"早期社區照顧計劃","examples":[{"en":"Early care in the community schemes relied heavily on families.","zh":"早期社區照顧計劃非常依賴家庭。"},{"en":"Early care in the community schemes were the first versions of programmes supporting patients outside institutions.","zh":"Early care in the community schemes 是支援病人在院舍外生活的最初版本計劃。"},{"en":"These early schemes often depended more on relatives than trained professionals.","zh":"這些早期計劃往往較依賴親屬，而不是受訓專業人士。"},{"en":"If early schemes lacked services, families had to fill the gaps.","zh":"如果早期計劃缺乏服務，家庭就要填補缺口。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the beginning stage of community-based mental-health support.","zh":"這個片語指社區為本精神健康支援的初期階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"patient support","meaning":"病人支援","examples":[{"en":"Patient support was initially provided mainly by relatives.","zh":"病人支援最初主要由親屬提供。"},{"en":"Patient support means the practical, medical, and emotional help given to patients.","zh":"Patient support 指給予病人的實際、醫療和情緒幫助。"},{"en":"Patient support may include transport to appointments, medication reminders, and counselling.","zh":"病人支援可以包括覆診交通、服藥提醒和輔導。"},{"en":"If patient support is weak, recovery can become harder.","zh":"如果病人支援薄弱，康復可能變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes help centred on the patient’s needs.","zh":"這個片語描述以病人需要為中心的幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the responsibility of relatives","meaning":"親屬的責任","examples":[{"en":"Early patient support was more the responsibility of relatives than professionals.","zh":"早期病人支援較多是親屬的責任，而不是專業人士的責任。"},{"en":"The responsibility of relatives means duties carried by family members.","zh":"The responsibility of relatives 指由家庭成員承擔的職責。"},{"en":"Caring for an elderly parent may become the responsibility of relatives when public services are limited.","zh":"當公共服務有限時，照顧年老父母可能成為親屬的責任。"},{"en":"If relatives carry too much responsibility, they may become exhausted.","zh":"如果親屬承擔太多責任，他們可能筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"This phrase shows who is expected to provide help.","zh":"這個片語顯示誰被期望提供幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"advanced professional help","meaning":"先進的專業協助","examples":[{"en":"Advanced professional help was not the main feature of early schemes.","zh":"先進的專業協助不是早期計劃的主要特點。"},{"en":"Advanced professional help means specialised support from trained experts.","zh":"Advanced professional help 指來自受訓專家的專門支援。"},{"en":"A child with serious speech difficulties may need advanced professional help from a therapist.","zh":"有嚴重語言困難的孩子可能需要治療師提供先進專業協助。"},{"en":"If early community care lacked advanced help, families had fewer expert resources.","zh":"如果早期社區照顧缺乏先進協助，家庭就有較少專家資源。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts expert support with informal assistance.","zh":"這個片語把專家支援與非正式幫助作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be available to","meaning":"可供……使用","examples":[{"en":"More professional services are now available to patients.","zh":"現在有更多專業服務可供病人使用。"},{"en":"To be available to someone means they can use or receive it.","zh":"To be available to someone 指某人可以使用或取得。"},{"en":"Free tutoring may be available to students from low-income families.","zh":"低收入家庭學生可能可使用免費補習。"},{"en":"If services are available to patients, help becomes easier to obtain.","zh":"如果服務可供病人使用，幫助就更容易取得。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on access.","zh":"這個片語集中於可取得性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"enjoy full independence","meaning":"享有完全獨立","examples":[{"en":"Patients were not intended to enjoy full independence without support.","zh":"病人原本並不是要在沒有支援下享有完全獨立。"},{"en":"To enjoy full independence means to live with complete freedom and self-management.","zh":"To enjoy full independence 指以完全自由和自我管理的方式生活。"},{"en":"A teenager may want full independence, but still need guidance with money and safety.","zh":"青少年可能想享有完全獨立，但仍需要金錢和安全方面的指導。"},{"en":"If patients are given full independence too early, risks may increase.","zh":"如果病人太早獲得完全獨立，風險可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete autonomy, not supported independence.","zh":"這個片語描述完全自主，而不是有支援的獨立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"what is true of","meaning":"關於……甚麼是正確的","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what is true of community care today.","zh":"題目問關於現今社區照顧甚麼是正確的。"},{"en":"What is true of something asks which statement correctly describes it.","zh":"What is true of something 詢問哪項陳述正確描述某事。"},{"en":"A reading question may ask what is true of the first experiment.","zh":"閱讀題可能問關於第一個實驗甚麼是正確的。"},{"en":"Students should choose the answer supported by the text, not by common sense alone.","zh":"學生應選擇文章支持的答案，而不只靠常識。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to test accurate understanding.","zh":"這個片語用來測試準確理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"permit greater patient autonomy","meaning":"容許病人有更大自主權","examples":[{"en":"Modern community care can permit greater patient autonomy.","zh":"現代社區照顧可以容許病人有更大自主權。"},{"en":"To permit greater patient autonomy means to allow patients more control over their own lives and choices.","zh":"To permit greater patient autonomy 指容許病人對自己的生活和選擇有更多控制。"},{"en":"A hospital may permit greater patient autonomy by letting patients discuss treatment plans.","zh":"醫院可以透過讓病人討論治療計劃，容許病人有更大自主權。"},{"en":"If patients have more autonomy, they may feel respected and responsible.","zh":"如果病人有更多自主權，他們可能感到受尊重和有責任感。"},{"en":"This phrase connects freedom with patient-centred care.","zh":"這個片語把自由與以病人為中心的照顧連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"professional services","meaning":"專業服務","examples":[{"en":"More professional services are available to patients today.","zh":"現今有更多專業服務可供病人使用。"},{"en":"Professional services are support services provided by trained specialists.","zh":"Professional services 是由受訓專家提供的支援服務。"},{"en":"Counselling, nursing visits, and psychiatric assessment are professional services.","zh":"輔導、護士探訪和精神科評估都是專業服務。"},{"en":"If professional services are accessible, community care becomes more reliable.","zh":"如果專業服務容易取得，社區照顧會變得更可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts trained help with informal support.","zh":"這個片語把受訓幫助與非正式支援作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"family support networks","meaning":"家庭支援網絡","examples":[{"en":"Family support networks remain important for some patients.","zh":"家庭支援網絡對一些病人仍然重要。"},{"en":"Family support networks are relatives who help someone emotionally, practically, or financially.","zh":"Family support networks 是在情緒、實際或財政上幫助某人的親屬。"},{"en":"A patient’s family support network may help with meals, transport, and daily reminders.","zh":"病人的家庭支援網絡可能幫忙膳食、交通和日常提醒。"},{"en":"If family support is strong, community care may work more smoothly.","zh":"如果家庭支援強，社區照顧可能運作得更順利。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised or informal help from family members.","zh":"這個片語描述來自家庭成員的有組織或非正式幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"become unnecessary","meaning":"變得不再需要","examples":[{"en":"Family support has not necessarily become unnecessary.","zh":"家庭支援不一定已變得不再需要。"},{"en":"To become unnecessary means to no longer be needed.","zh":"To become unnecessary 指不再被需要。"},{"en":"Textbooks do not become unnecessary just because students use tablets.","zh":"學生使用平板電腦，不代表課本變得不再需要。"},{"en":"If professional services improve, family help may still remain valuable.","zh":"即使專業服務改善，家庭幫助仍可能有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a need disappearing, often after conditions change.","zh":"這個片語描述需要消失，通常因情況改變而發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"become part of","meaning":"成為……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Not all patients can become part of community-care schemes.","zh":"並非所有病人都能成為社區照顧計劃的一部分。"},{"en":"To become part of something means to be included in it.","zh":"To become part of something 指被納入某事物之中。"},{"en":"A student may become part of a sports team after regular training.","zh":"學生經過定期訓練後，可能成為運動隊的一部分。"},{"en":"If a patient is unstable, they may not be suitable to join a community-care scheme.","zh":"如果病人不穩定，他可能不適合加入社區照顧計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inclusion in a group, system, or plan.","zh":"這個片語描述被納入群體、制度或計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the writer’s attitude towards","meaning":"作者對……的態度","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the writer’s attitude towards community care.","zh":"題目問作者對社區照顧的態度。"},{"en":"The writer’s attitude towards something means the writer’s opinion, tone, or position about it.","zh":"The writer’s attitude towards something 指作者對某事的意見、語氣或立場。"},{"en":"In reading tests, words like “however” and “unfortunately” can reveal the writer’s attitude.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，像 “however” 和 “unfortunately” 這類詞可以透露作者態度。"},{"en":"If the writer mentions both benefits and risks, the attitude may be balanced.","zh":"如果作者同時提及好處和風險，其態度可能是平衡的。"},{"en":"This phrase asks students to infer viewpoint, not just locate facts.","zh":"這個片語要求學生推斷觀點，而不只是定位事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"prove to be a failure","meaning":"證明是失敗","examples":[{"en":"The scheme has not necessarily proved to be a failure.","zh":"這項計劃不一定已證明是失敗。"},{"en":"To prove to be a failure means to turn out unsuccessful after being tried.","zh":"To prove to be a failure 指嘗試後結果顯示不成功。"},{"en":"A study plan may prove to be a failure if students cannot follow it.","zh":"如果學生無法跟從，溫習計劃可能證明是失敗。"},{"en":"If a policy has mixed results, it should not be called a complete failure too quickly.","zh":"如果政策結果好壞參半，不應太快稱為完全失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes failure shown by results.","zh":"這個片語描述由結果顯示的失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"work under certain circumstances","meaning":"在某些情況下奏效","examples":[{"en":"Community care may work under certain circumstances.","zh":"社區照顧可能在某些情況下奏效。"},{"en":"To work under certain circumstances means to succeed only when particular conditions are present.","zh":"To work under certain circumstances 指只有在特定條件存在時才成功。"},{"en":"Online lessons work under certain circumstances, such as when students have quiet rooms and stable internet.","zh":"網上課堂在某些情況下奏效，例如學生有安靜房間和穩定網絡。"},{"en":"If patients are stable and support is strong, community care may work well.","zh":"如果病人穩定且支援強，社區照顧可能運作良好。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that success depends on conditions.","zh":"這個片語提醒成功取決於條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be disadvantaged","meaning":"處於不利位置","examples":[{"en":"Mentally ill patients may be disadvantaged without proper support.","zh":"沒有適當支援時，精神病患者可能處於不利位置。"},{"en":"To be disadvantaged means to be placed in a weaker or less favourable position.","zh":"To be disadvantaged 指處於較弱或較不有利的位置。"},{"en":"Students without internet access may be disadvantaged in online learning.","zh":"沒有互聯網的學生在網上學習中可能處於不利位置。"},{"en":"If patients lack housing, work, or professional help, they may be disadvantaged in community life.","zh":"如果病人缺乏住屋、工作或專業幫助，他們在社區生活中可能處於不利位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unfair or difficult conditions.","zh":"這個片語描述不公平或困難條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"patient neglect","meaning":"對病人的忽視","examples":[{"en":"Patient neglect by professional helpers would damage the scheme.","zh":"專業支援人員對病人的忽視會破壞這項計劃。"},{"en":"Patient neglect means failing to give patients the care, attention, or protection they need.","zh":"Patient neglect 指未能給予病人所需照顧、關注或保護。"},{"en":"Patient neglect may include missed medication, ignored complaints, or unsafe living conditions.","zh":"對病人的忽視可能包括漏服藥、投訴被忽視或不安全生活環境。"},{"en":"If neglect happens in community care, patients may relapse or become isolated.","zh":"如果社區照顧中出現忽視，病人可能復發或變得孤立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harm caused by failure to care.","zh":"這個片語描述因未能照顧而造成的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"look at the following statements","meaning":"查看以下陳述","examples":[{"en":"Students look at the following statements and match them with speakers.","zh":"學生查看以下陳述，並把它們與說話者配對。"},{"en":"Look at the following statements means read the listed sentences carefully.","zh":"Look at the following statements 指仔細閱讀列出的句子。"},{"en":"In an exam, students should look at the following statements before scanning the passage.","zh":"在考試中，學生掃讀文章前應查看以下陳述。"},{"en":"If students ignore key words in the statements, they may match them wrongly.","zh":"如果學生忽略陳述中的關鍵字，他們可能錯誤配對。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a set of information for a task.","zh":"這個片語引出題目中的一組資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the list of people","meaning":"人物列表","examples":[{"en":"The task provides a list of people.","zh":"題目提供一個人物列表。"},{"en":"The list of people is the set of names or speakers students must choose from.","zh":"The list of people 是學生必須從中選擇的一組姓名或說話者。"},{"en":"Students should check the list of people before reading the statements.","zh":"學生閱讀陳述前應查看人物列表。"},{"en":"If a person appears more than once, students may use the same name for several answers.","zh":"如果某人物可出現多次，學生可能在幾題中使用同一姓名。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the answer options in a matching task.","zh":"這個片語描述配對題中的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"match each statement to","meaning":"將每項陳述配對至……","examples":[{"en":"Students match each statement to the correct person.","zh":"學生將每項陳述配對至正確人物。"},{"en":"To match each statement to someone means to connect each idea with the person who said or believed it.","zh":"To match each statement to someone 指把每個想法連接到說出或相信該想法的人。"},{"en":"In a reading task, students must match each statement to the paragraph that supports it.","zh":"在閱讀題中，學生必須將每項陳述配對至支持它的段落。"},{"en":"If two people express similar opinions, careful comparison is needed.","zh":"如果兩個人表達相似意見，就需要仔細比較。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in matching questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"acknowledge certain inadequacies in","meaning":"承認……中的某些不足","examples":[{"en":"Dr. Mayalla acknowledges certain inadequacies in community care.","zh":"Mayalla 醫生承認社區照顧中的某些不足。"},{"en":"To acknowledge certain inadequacies in something means to admit that it has some weaknesses.","zh":"To acknowledge certain inadequacies in something 指承認某事有一些弱點。"},{"en":"A headteacher may acknowledge certain inadequacies in the school’s support system.","zh":"校長可能承認學校支援系統中的某些不足。"},{"en":"If professionals admit weaknesses, they can improve the scheme more honestly.","zh":"如果專業人士承認弱點，他們可以更誠實地改善計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase shows balanced criticism rather than complete rejection.","zh":"這個片語顯示平衡批評，而不是完全否定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the concept of","meaning":"……的概念","examples":[{"en":"The concept of care in the community is debated.","zh":"社區照顧的概念受到爭議。"},{"en":"The concept of something means the general idea behind it.","zh":"The concept of something 指某事背後的一般想法。"},{"en":"Students may understand the concept of fairness before they learn legal terms.","zh":"學生可能在學法律術語前已理解公平的概念。"},{"en":"If people disagree about the concept, they may design policies differently.","zh":"如果人們對概念有分歧，他們可能設計不同政策。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an idea, not just a specific example.","zh":"這個片語指一個想法，而不只是具體例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"recognise that","meaning":"承認；意識到","examples":[{"en":"He recognises that attempts have been made to improve the scheme.","zh":"他承認已作出嘗試去改善這項計劃。"},{"en":"To recognise that means to understand or admit that something is true.","zh":"To recognise that 指理解或承認某事為真。"},{"en":"A teacher may recognise that a student is trying hard even if marks remain low.","zh":"即使分數仍低，老師可能意識到學生正在努力。"},{"en":"If critics recognise improvements, their argument becomes more balanced.","zh":"如果批評者承認已有改善，他們的論點會更平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase shows awareness or acceptance of a fact.","zh":"這個片語顯示對事實的意識或接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"attempts have been made to","meaning":"已作出嘗試去……","examples":[{"en":"Attempts have been made to improve community-care schemes.","zh":"已作出嘗試去改善社區照顧計劃。"},{"en":"Attempts have been made to means people have tried to do something.","zh":"Attempts have been made to 指人們已嘗試做某事。"},{"en":"Attempts have been made to reduce bullying through workshops and clearer rules.","zh":"已作出嘗試透過工作坊和更清晰規則來減少欺凌。"},{"en":"If attempts have been made but problems remain, stronger action may be needed.","zh":"如果已作出嘗試但問題仍存在，可能需要更強行動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows effort, but not necessarily success.","zh":"這個片語顯示努力，但不一定表示成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"improve on existing schemes","meaning":"改善現有計劃","examples":[{"en":"Modern services try to improve on existing schemes.","zh":"現代服務嘗試改善現有計劃。"},{"en":"To improve on existing schemes means to make current programmes better.","zh":"To improve on existing schemes 指令目前計劃變得更好。"},{"en":"A school may improve on an existing homework policy by adding feedback sessions.","zh":"學校可能透過加入回饋課節來改善現有功課政策。"},{"en":"If old schemes fail some patients, new services should fix those weaknesses.","zh":"如果舊計劃未能幫助某些病人，新服務應修補那些弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes building on what already exists.","zh":"這個片語描述在已有基礎上改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"whilst emphasising","meaning":"在強調……的同時","examples":[{"en":"Whilst emphasising patient benefits, Bob criticises traditional care.","zh":"Bob 在強調對病人的好處時，也批評傳統照顧。"},{"en":"Whilst emphasising means while strongly pointing out or highlighting something.","zh":"Whilst emphasising 指在強烈指出或突出某事的同時。"},{"en":"Whilst emphasising safety, a school may still encourage independence.","zh":"學校在強調安全的同時，仍可能鼓勵獨立。"},{"en":"If someone praises one part while criticising another, their view is more nuanced.","zh":"如果某人讚揚一部分同時批評另一部分，其觀點更有層次。"},{"en":"This phrase shows two ideas happening together.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩個想法同時存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"benefits to the patient","meaning":"對病人的好處","examples":[{"en":"The benefits to the patient include greater independence.","zh":"對病人的好處包括更大獨立性。"},{"en":"Benefits to the patient are the positive effects a patient receives from treatment or support.","zh":"Benefits to the patient 是病人從治療或支援中得到的正面效果。"},{"en":"Benefits to the patient may include better mood, safer routines, and stronger relationships.","zh":"對病人的好處可能包括情緒改善、更安全日常規律和更強人際關係。"},{"en":"If a scheme has clear patient benefits, it is easier to justify.","zh":"如果計劃對病人有明顯好處，就較容易合理化。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how the patient is helped.","zh":"這個片語集中於病人如何得到幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be critical of","meaning":"批評……","examples":[{"en":"Bob is critical of traditional care methods.","zh":"Bob 批評傳統照顧方法。"},{"en":"To be critical of something means to judge it negatively or point out its weaknesses.","zh":"To be critical of something 指對某事作負面判斷或指出其弱點。"},{"en":"A student can be critical of an argument without being rude.","zh":"學生可以批評某論點而不粗魯。"},{"en":"If professionals are critical of old methods, reform may become more likely.","zh":"如果專業人士批評舊方法，改革可能更有機會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reasoned criticism.","zh":"這個片語描述有理據的批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"traditional care methods","meaning":"傳統照顧方法","examples":[{"en":"Traditional care methods often relied on institutions.","zh":"傳統照顧方法通常依賴院舍。"},{"en":"Traditional care methods are older ways of treating or supporting patients.","zh":"Traditional care methods 是較舊的治療或支援病人方式。"},{"en":"A traditional care method may keep patients in hospitals for long periods.","zh":"傳統照顧方法可能讓病人長期留在醫院。"},{"en":"If traditional methods focus on control, patients may lose independence.","zh":"如果傳統方法集中於控制，病人可能失去獨立。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts older care with newer community-based approaches.","zh":"這個片語把舊式照顧與較新的社區為本方法作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be moderated by","meaning":"受到……調和；變得較溫和","examples":[{"en":"A person’s views may be moderated by professional experience.","zh":"一個人的看法可能受到專業經驗調和。"},{"en":"To be moderated by something means to be softened, balanced, or influenced by it.","zh":"To be moderated by something 指被某事軟化、平衡或影響。"},{"en":"A parent’s worries may be moderated by clear information from doctors.","zh":"家長的擔心可能因醫生清晰資訊而變得較溫和。"},{"en":"If fear is moderated by experience, opinions may become less extreme.","zh":"如果恐懼受到經驗調和，意見可能變得沒那麼極端。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor makes a view more measured.","zh":"這個片語顯示某因素令看法更有分寸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"professional contact with","meaning":"與……的專業接觸","examples":[{"en":"Professional contact with mentally ill patients can shape opinions.","zh":"與精神病患者的專業接觸可以塑造意見。"},{"en":"Professional contact with someone means work-related interaction with them.","zh":"Professional contact with someone 指與某人的工作相關互動。"},{"en":"A teacher’s professional contact with struggling students may change how she views discipline.","zh":"老師與有困難學生的專業接觸可能改變她對紀律的看法。"},{"en":"If people have professional contact with patients, they may understand their needs better.","zh":"如果人們與病人有專業接觸，他們可能更理解其需要。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights experience gained through work.","zh":"這個片語突出透過工作獲得的經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"place the welfare of others above","meaning":"將其他人的福祉置於……之上","examples":[{"en":"Anita places the welfare of others above that of the mentally ill.","zh":"Anita 將其他人的福祉置於精神病患者的福祉之上。"},{"en":"To place the welfare of others above someone else’s means to treat one group’s safety or well-being as more important.","zh":"To place the welfare of others above someone else’s 指把某群體的安全或福祉看得比另一群體更重要。"},{"en":"A school may place younger children’s welfare above convenience when planning playground rules.","zh":"學校規劃操場規則時，可能把年幼孩子的福祉置於方便之上。"},{"en":"If public safety is prioritised too strongly, patient rights may be overlooked.","zh":"如果公共安全被過度優先考慮，病人權利可能被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ranking one group’s welfare over another’s.","zh":"這個片語描述把一群人的福祉排在另一群人之上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"welfare of others","meaning":"其他人的福祉","examples":[{"en":"She is concerned about the welfare of others in the community.","zh":"她關心社區中其他人的福祉。"},{"en":"Welfare of others means the safety, health, and well-being of other people.","zh":"Welfare of others 指其他人的安全、健康和福祉。"},{"en":"A driver should consider the welfare of others before speeding near a school.","zh":"司機在學校附近超速前，應考慮其他人的福祉。"},{"en":"If community policy ignores the welfare of others, public trust may fall.","zh":"如果社區政策忽視其他人的福祉，公眾信任可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on responsibility toward people beyond oneself.","zh":"這個片語集中於對自己以外人士的責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"acknowledge that","meaning":"承認","examples":[{"en":"A speaker may acknowledge that public mistrust is understandable.","zh":"說話者可能承認公眾不信任是可以理解的。"},{"en":"To acknowledge that means to admit or recognise that something is true or reasonable.","zh":"To acknowledge that 指承認或意識到某事真實或合理。"},{"en":"A teacher may acknowledge that an exam was difficult before giving feedback.","zh":"老師在給回饋前可能承認考試很困難。"},{"en":"If officials acknowledge public fear, discussion may become calmer.","zh":"如果官員承認公眾恐懼，討論可能變得較冷靜。"},{"en":"This phrase shows recognition rather than denial.","zh":"這個片語顯示承認，而不是否認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"mistrust of","meaning":"對……的不信任","examples":[{"en":"Some people express mistrust of community-care schemes.","zh":"有些人表達對社區照顧計劃的不信任。"},{"en":"Mistrust of something means lack of trust or confidence in it.","zh":"Mistrust of something 指對某事缺乏信任或信心。"},{"en":"People may have mistrust of a company after repeated scandals.","zh":"公司反覆出現醜聞後，人們可能對它不信任。"},{"en":"If public information is unclear, mistrust of a policy may grow.","zh":"如果公眾資訊不清楚，對政策的不信任可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes suspicion or lack of confidence.","zh":"這個片語描述懷疑或缺乏信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"may be unfounded","meaning":"可能沒有根據","examples":[{"en":"Some fears about community care may be unfounded.","zh":"一些對社區照顧的恐懼可能沒有根據。"},{"en":"May be unfounded means may not be supported by evidence or facts.","zh":"May be unfounded 指可能沒有證據或事實支持。"},{"en":"A rumour about a school closure may be unfounded if no official notice exists.","zh":"如果沒有官方通告，關於學校停辦的傳聞可能沒有根據。"},{"en":"If fears are unfounded, clear information can help reduce anxiety.","zh":"如果恐懼沒有根據，清晰資訊可以幫助減少焦慮。"},{"en":"This phrase questions whether a worry has a real basis.","zh":"這個片語質疑憂慮是否有真實基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"agree with the information given in","meaning":"符合文中資料","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the information given in the text.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否符合文中資料。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given in the text means to match what the passage says.","zh":"To agree with the information given in the text 指與文章所說相符。"},{"en":"In TRUE questions, students must check whether the statement agrees with the exact meaning.","zh":"在 TRUE 題中，學生必須檢查陳述是否符合確切意思。"},{"en":"If the statement says more than the text supports, it may not agree with the information.","zh":"如果陳述說得比文章支持的更多，它可能不符合資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading-comprehension instructions.","zh":"這個片語常見於閱讀理解指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the information in the text.","zh":"陳述可能與文中資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"To contradict the information 指說出與文章相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says “most patients improved,” an option saying “no patients improved” contradicts it.","zh":"如果文章說「大多數病人改善」，選項說「沒有病人改善」就是矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should look for direct conflict between the statement and the passage.","zh":"學生應尋找陳述與文章之間的直接衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase is important for FALSE questions.","zh":"這個片語對 FALSE 題很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"If the text gives no evidence, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文章沒有提供證據，文中就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not say enough to decide.","zh":"There is no information on this 指文章沒有說足夠內容來判斷。"},{"en":"If a question asks about a patient’s age but the text never mentions it, the answer is not given.","zh":"如果題目問病人年齡，但文章從未提及，答案就是 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when there is no information in the passage.","zh":"當文章沒有資料時，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to NOT GIVEN answers.","zh":"這個片語是 NOT GIVEN 答案的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"better understanding of","meaning":"對……有更好理解","examples":[{"en":"There may be a better understanding of mental illness today.","zh":"今天人們可能對精神病有更好理解。"},{"en":"A better understanding of something means clearer, deeper, or more accurate knowledge of it.","zh":"A better understanding of something 指對某事有更清晰、更深入或更準確的認識。"},{"en":"Teachers gain a better understanding of students when they listen to their difficulties.","zh":"當老師聆聽學生困難時，就會對學生有更好理解。"},{"en":"If society has a better understanding of mental illness, stigma may decrease.","zh":"如果社會對精神病有更好理解，污名可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improvement in knowledge or awareness.","zh":"這個片語描述知識或意識上的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"dynamics of mental illness","meaning":"精神病的運作機制","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to the dynamics of mental illness.","zh":"陳述提及精神病的運作機制。"},{"en":"Dynamics of mental illness means how mental illness develops, changes, and affects behaviour over time.","zh":"Dynamics of mental illness 指精神病如何發展、變化並隨時間影響行為。"},{"en":"Doctors study the dynamics of anxiety to understand triggers and recovery patterns.","zh":"醫生研究焦慮的運作機制，以理解觸發因素和康復模式。"},{"en":"If professionals understand these dynamics, they can design better support plans.","zh":"如果專業人士理解這些機制，他們可以設計更好支援計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how a condition works, not just its name.","zh":"這個片語集中於疾病如何運作，而不只是其名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"adequate psychological support","meaning":"足夠的心理支援","examples":[{"en":"Community-care schemes may need adequate psychological support.","zh":"社區照顧計劃可能需要足夠的心理支援。"},{"en":"Adequate psychological support means enough emotional and mental-health help for a person’s needs.","zh":"Adequate psychological support 指足以配合某人需要的情緒和精神健康幫助。"},{"en":"A student facing grief may need adequate psychological support from counsellors and teachers.","zh":"面對喪親的學生可能需要輔導員和老師提供足夠心理支援。"},{"en":"If patients lack adequate support, independence can become unsafe.","zh":"如果病人缺乏足夠支援，獨立可能變得不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that support must be sufficient, not merely present.","zh":"這個片語強調支援必須足夠，而不只是存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"less successful than in the past","meaning":"比過去較不成功","examples":[{"en":"Dr. Mayalla does not say the scheme is less successful than in the past.","zh":"Mayalla 醫生沒有說這項計劃比過去較不成功。"},{"en":"Less successful than in the past means achieving poorer results now than before.","zh":"Less successful than in the past 指現在取得的結果比以前差。"},{"en":"A study method may be less successful than in the past if the exam format changes.","zh":"如果考試形式改變，某溫習方法可能比過去較不成功。"},{"en":"If services improve, a scheme may be more successful rather than less successful.","zh":"如果服務改善，計劃可能更成功，而不是較不成功。"},{"en":"This phrase compares current success with earlier success.","zh":"這個片語比較現時成功程度與以往成功程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"the goal of","meaning":"……的目標","examples":[{"en":"The goal of community care is to help suitable patients live more independently.","zh":"社區照顧的目標是幫助合適病人生活得更獨立。"},{"en":"The goal of something is its main purpose or intended result.","zh":"The goal of something 是某事的主要目的或預期結果。"},{"en":"The goal of a reading lesson is not only to answer questions but to understand meaning.","zh":"閱讀課的目標不只是答題，而是理解意思。"},{"en":"If the goal is independence, support should teach patients daily skills.","zh":"如果目標是獨立，支援就應教病人日常技能。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what a plan is trying to achieve.","zh":"這個片語指出計劃試圖達成甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"make patients less dependent on","meaning":"令病人較少依賴……","examples":[{"en":"Community care aims to make patients less dependent on institutions.","zh":"社區照顧旨在令病人較少依賴院舍。"},{"en":"To make patients less dependent on something means to help them rely on it less.","zh":"To make patients less dependent on something 指幫助病人較少依賴某事物。"},{"en":"Teaching budgeting skills can make young adults less dependent on parents.","zh":"教授理財技能可以令年輕成年人較少依賴父母。"},{"en":"If patients learn daily routines, they may become less dependent on hospital staff.","zh":"如果病人學會日常規律，他們可能較少依賴醫院職員。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing reliance while still allowing support.","zh":"這個片語描述減少依賴，同時仍容許支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"the system","meaning":"制度；系統","examples":[{"en":"The system should support patients without making them completely dependent.","zh":"制度應支援病人，而不令他們完全依賴。"},{"en":"The system means the organised set of services, rules, people, and institutions involved.","zh":"The system 指由服務、規則、人員和機構組成的有組織整體。"},{"en":"A school system includes teachers, timetables, rules, exams, and support services.","zh":"學校制度包括老師、時間表、規則、考試和支援服務。"},{"en":"If the system is badly designed, even good workers may struggle to help patients.","zh":"如果制度設計差，即使好員工也可能難以幫助病人。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the whole organised structure, not one person only.","zh":"這個片語指整個有組織架構，而不只是某個人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 68 - Care in the Community.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 69":[{"front":"speech dysfluency","meaning":"言語不流暢","examples":[{"en":"A speech dysfluency is a break, irregularity or sound-filled pause in speech.","zh":"言語不流暢是說話中的中斷、不規律之處或有聲停頓。"},{"en":"Speech dysfluency means speech that is interrupted, repeated, paused, or not smoothly completed.","zh":"言語不流暢指說話被打斷、重複、停頓或未能順暢完成。"},{"en":"A nervous student may show speech dysfluency by saying “um” several times before answering.","zh":"緊張的學生回答前多次說 “um”，可能顯示言語不流暢。"},{"en":"Speech dysfluency can happen when the speaker is tired, anxious, or still planning the next idea.","zh":"當說話者疲倦、焦慮或仍在構思下一個想法時，可能出現言語不流暢。"},{"en":"Speech dysfluency is common in natural conversation, even among fluent speakers.","zh":"言語不流暢在自然對話中很常見，即使流利說話者也會出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"popular fillers","meaning":"常見填充語","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses speech dysfluency and popular fillers.","zh":"文章討論言語不流暢和常見填充語。"},{"en":"Popular fillers are common sounds or words people use to fill pauses in speech.","zh":"常見填充語是人們用來填補說話停頓的常見聲音或字詞。"},{"en":"In English, “um”, “uh” and “well” are popular fillers in everyday conversation.","zh":"在英語中，“um”、“uh”和“well”是日常對話中的常見填充語。"},{"en":"Popular fillers give speakers a little time to think before continuing.","zh":"常見填充語給說話者一點時間思考，然後繼續說下去。"},{"en":"Popular fillers are common, but too many of them can make a speech sound less confident.","zh":"常見填充語很普遍，但太多會令演講聽起來較不自信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"breaks and irregularities","meaning":"中斷和不規律之處","examples":[{"en":"Speech dysfluencies include breaks and irregularities in spoken language.","zh":"言語不流暢包括口語中的中斷和不規律之處。"},{"en":"Breaks and irregularities are interruptions or uneven parts in speech.","zh":"中斷和不規律之處是說話中的停頓、打斷或不平均部分。"},{"en":"A speaker may have breaks and irregularities when they stop mid-sentence and restart.","zh":"說話者說到一半停下再重新開始時，可能出現中斷和不規律之處。"},{"en":"Breaks and irregularities often appear when people are choosing words carefully.","zh":"當人們仔細選詞時，中斷和不規律之處常會出現。"},{"en":"These breaks and irregularities make spoken language different from polished written language.","zh":"這些中斷和不規律之處令口語不同於修飾好的書面語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sound-filled pauses","meaning":"有聲停頓","examples":[{"en":"Fillers are often sound-filled pauses that speakers use while talking.","zh":"填充語通常是說話者說話時使用的有聲停頓。"},{"en":"Sound-filled pauses are pauses filled with sounds such as “um”, “uh” or “hmm”.","zh":"有聲停頓是由 “um”、“uh” 或 “hmm” 等聲音填補的停頓。"},{"en":"A presenter may use sound-filled pauses while trying to remember the next point.","zh":"主持人嘗試記起下一個重點時，可能使用有聲停頓。"},{"en":"Sound-filled pauses can show that the speaker has not finished speaking yet.","zh":"有聲停頓可以顯示說話者尚未說完。"},{"en":"In conversation, sound-filled pauses are often more natural than complete silence.","zh":"在對話中，有聲停頓通常比完全沉默更自然。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"when we are speaking","meaning":"當我們說話時","examples":[{"en":"People often use fillers when they are speaking.","zh":"人們當說話時常使用填充語。"},{"en":"When we are speaking means during the act of talking aloud.","zh":"When we are speaking 指正在開口說話的時候。"},{"en":"When we are speaking in front of a class, we may pause more than usual.","zh":"當我們在班上說話時，可能比平時停頓更多。"},{"en":"We may use fillers when we are speaking because our brain is still planning the next words.","zh":"當我們說話時可能使用填充語，因為大腦仍在構思接下來的字詞。"},{"en":"Written sentences can be edited, but mistakes appear more easily when we are speaking.","zh":"書面句子可以修改，但當我們說話時，錯誤更容易出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"commonly known as","meaning":"通常稱為","examples":[{"en":"Speech dysfluencies are commonly known as fillers.","zh":"言語不流暢通常稱為填充語。"},{"en":"Commonly known as means usually called by a particular name.","zh":"Commonly known as 指通常被稱作某個名稱。"},{"en":"The MTR is commonly known as the main railway system in Hong Kong.","zh":"港鐵通常稱為香港主要鐵路系統。"},{"en":"If a technical term is difficult, writers may introduce what it is commonly known as.","zh":"如果技術術語困難，作者可能介紹它通常稱為甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect a formal term with a familiar name.","zh":"這個片語幫助把正式術語與熟悉名稱連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fillers","meaning":"填充語","examples":[{"en":"Fillers include sounds such as “uh”, “um” and “hmm”.","zh":"填充語包括 “uh”、“um” 和 “hmm” 等聲音。"},{"en":"Fillers are sounds, words or phrases used to fill gaps while speaking.","zh":"填充語是說話時用來填補空隙的聲音、字詞或片語。"},{"en":"A student may say “well” as a filler before giving an opinion.","zh":"學生發表意見前可能說 “well” 作為填充語。"},{"en":"Fillers can help speakers keep their turn while they think.","zh":"填充語可以幫助說話者在思考時保留發言權。"},{"en":"Fillers are normal in conversation, but formal speeches usually use fewer of them.","zh":"填充語在對話中很正常，但正式演講通常較少使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"words and sentences that are not finished","meaning":"未完成的字詞和句子","examples":[{"en":"Fillers can include words and sentences that are not finished.","zh":"填充語可以包括未完成的字詞和句子。"},{"en":"Words and sentences that are not finished are speech parts that stop before completion.","zh":"未完成的字詞和句子是未完成就停止的說話部分。"},{"en":"A speaker may say, “I think we should—well, maybe not,” leaving the first sentence unfinished.","zh":"說話者可能說：“I think we should—well, maybe not”，令第一句未完成。"},{"en":"People often leave words or sentences unfinished when they change their mind while speaking.","zh":"人們說話時改變想法，常會留下未完成的字詞或句子。"},{"en":"Unfinished speech can reveal real-time thinking more clearly than written language.","zh":"未完成的說話比書面語更能顯示即時思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"repeated phrases","meaning":"重複的片語","examples":[{"en":"Repeated phrases are one type of speech dysfluency.","zh":"重複的片語是一種言語不流暢。"},{"en":"Repeated phrases are phrases said more than once in a short stretch of speech.","zh":"重複的片語是在短時間說話中被說出多於一次的片語。"},{"en":"A nervous speaker may say “I think, I think” before finishing the sentence.","zh":"緊張的說話者可能在完成句子前說 “I think, I think”。"},{"en":"Repeated phrases can happen when the speaker is searching for the next idea.","zh":"當說話者正在尋找下一個想法時，可能出現重複的片語。"},{"en":"In casual speech, repeated phrases are common and do not always mean the speaker is weak.","zh":"在隨意說話中，重複的片語很常見，並不一定代表說話者能力弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"repeated syllables","meaning":"重複的音節","examples":[{"en":"Some dysfluencies involve repeated syllables.","zh":"一些言語不流暢涉及重複的音節。"},{"en":"Repeated syllables are parts of words that are spoken again before the word is completed.","zh":"重複的音節是字詞完成前被再次說出的部分。"},{"en":"A child may say “ba-ba-baby” when struggling to say the word smoothly.","zh":"孩子難以順暢說出某字時，可能說 “ba-ba-baby”。"},{"en":"Repeated syllables can appear when someone is nervous, excited or stuttering.","zh":"當某人緊張、興奮或口吃時，可能出現重複的音節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repetition inside a word, not repetition of a whole sentence.","zh":"這個片語描述字詞內部的重複，而不是整句重複。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"instances of","meaning":"……的例子；……的情況","examples":[{"en":"The passage mentions instances of speakers correcting their own mistakes.","zh":"文章提到說話者糾正自己錯誤的情況。"},{"en":"Instances of something are examples or cases of it happening.","zh":"Instances of something 是某事發生的例子或情況。"},{"en":"A teacher may record instances of late homework to see whether the problem is repeated.","zh":"老師可能記錄遲交功課的例子，以查看問題是否反覆出現。"},{"en":"If there are many instances of self-correction, the speaker may be thinking carefully.","zh":"如果有很多自我修正的情況，說話者可能正在仔細思考。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing examples found in data or observation.","zh":"這個片語適用於討論數據或觀察中發現的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"correct their own mistakes","meaning":"糾正自己的錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Speakers sometimes correct their own mistakes as they speak.","zh":"說話者有時在說話時糾正自己的錯誤。"},{"en":"To correct their own mistakes means to notice and fix errors by themselves.","zh":"To correct their own mistakes 指自己注意到錯誤並加以修正。"},{"en":"A student may say “yesterday—sorry, last week” to correct their own mistake.","zh":"學生可能說 “yesterday—sorry, last week” 來糾正自己的錯誤。"},{"en":"Speakers correct their own mistakes because spoken language happens in real time.","zh":"說話者糾正自己的錯誤，因為口語是即時發生的。"},{"en":"Self-correction can make speech sound natural rather than perfectly scripted.","zh":"自我修正可以令說話聽起來自然，而不是完全像稿件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as they speak","meaning":"在說話時","examples":[{"en":"Speakers may correct their own mistakes as they speak.","zh":"說話者可能在說話時糾正自己的錯誤。"},{"en":"As they speak means while they are talking, not after the conversation ends.","zh":"As they speak 指在他們說話期間，而不是對話結束後。"},{"en":"A presenter may change a word as they speak if they realise it is unclear.","zh":"如果主持人發現某字不清楚，可能在說話時改用另一個字。"},{"en":"Because speaking is immediate, people often edit ideas as they speak.","zh":"因為說話是即時的，人們常在說話時修改想法。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the action happens during speech itself.","zh":"這個片語顯示行動在說話本身期間發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"words such as","meaning":"例如……等字詞","examples":[{"en":"Fillers include words such as “huh”, “uh”, “um” and “well”.","zh":"填充語包括 “huh”、“uh”、“um” 和 “well” 等字詞。"},{"en":"Words such as introduces examples of the kind of words being discussed.","zh":"Words such as 用來引出正在討論的一類字詞的例子。"},{"en":"Students often confuse words such as “affect” and “effect”.","zh":"學生常混淆 “affect” 和 “effect” 等字詞。"},{"en":"If a writer gives words such as these, readers can understand the category more easily.","zh":"如果作者給出這類字詞，讀者可以更容易理解該類別。"},{"en":"This phrase is used before examples, not before a complete explanation.","zh":"這個片語用於例子之前，而不是完整解釋之前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"“huh”, “uh”, “erm”, “um”, “hmm” and “err”","meaning":"「吓」、「呃」、「嗯」等填充音","examples":[{"en":"Sounds such as “huh”, “uh”, “erm”, “um”, “hmm” and “err” are common fillers.","zh":"“huh”、“uh”、“erm”、“um”、“hmm” 和 “err” 等聲音是常見填充語。"},{"en":"“Huh”, “uh”, “erm”, “um”, “hmm” and “err” are sounds speakers use when pausing or thinking.","zh":"“huh”、“uh”、“erm”、“um”、“hmm” 和 “err” 是說話者停頓或思考時使用的聲音。"},{"en":"A student may say “erm” before answering a difficult question in class.","zh":"學生在課堂上回答困難問題前，可能會說 “erm”。"},{"en":"These sounds can give the speaker time to organise the next part of a sentence.","zh":"這些聲音可以給說話者時間組織句子的下一部分。"},{"en":"They are common in speech, but they are usually removed from formal writing.","zh":"它們在口語中很常見，但通常會從正式寫作中刪除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"“like”, “you know” and “well”","meaning":"“like”、“you know”和“well”等填充語","examples":[{"en":"Words and phrases such as “like”, “you know” and “well” can work as fillers.","zh":"“like”、“you know” 和 “well” 等字詞和片語可以用作填充語。"},{"en":"“Like”, “you know” and “well” can be used to soften speech or buy thinking time.","zh":"“like”、“you know” 和 “well” 可用來柔化說話或爭取思考時間。"},{"en":"A teenager may say “like” while explaining a story to friends.","zh":"青少年向朋友解釋故事時，可能會說 “like”。"},{"en":"“Well” can signal that the speaker is about to answer carefully.","zh":"“Well” 可以表示說話者即將謹慎回答。"},{"en":"These expressions may be meaningful in some contexts but filler-like in others.","zh":"這些表達在某些語境中有意思，但在另一些語境中像填充語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"parts of speech","meaning":"話語成分","examples":[{"en":"Fillers are described as parts of speech that are not generally recognised as meaningful.","zh":"填充語被描述為通常不被視為有意義的話語成分。"},{"en":"Parts of speech are units or elements that appear in spoken or written language.","zh":"Parts of speech 是出現在口語或書面語中的單位或元素。"},{"en":"In grammar lessons, nouns, verbs and adjectives are common parts of speech.","zh":"在文法課中，名詞、動詞和形容詞是常見詞類。"},{"en":"Fillers are unusual because they appear in speech but may not carry clear dictionary meaning.","zh":"填充語較特別，因為它們出現在口語中，但未必有清楚字典意思。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer broadly to the components that make up language.","zh":"這個片語可廣泛指構成語言的成分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not generally recognised as meaningful","meaning":"通常不被視為有意義","examples":[{"en":"Fillers are not generally recognised as meaningful.","zh":"填充語通常不被視為有意義。"},{"en":"Not generally recognised as meaningful means most people do not treat something as carrying clear meaning.","zh":"Not generally recognised as meaningful 指大多數人不把某事物視為帶有清楚意思。"},{"en":"A pause like “uh” may not be meaningful like a noun or verb.","zh":"像 “uh” 這樣的停頓，未必像名詞或動詞那樣有意義。"},{"en":"Even if a filler lacks clear meaning, it may still help manage conversation.","zh":"即使填充語缺乏清楚意思，它仍可能幫助管理對話。"},{"en":"This phrase separates dictionary meaning from conversational function.","zh":"這個片語區分字典意思與對話功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"speech problems","meaning":"說話問題","examples":[{"en":"Fillers may include speech problems such as stuttering.","zh":"填充語可能包括口吃等說話問題。"},{"en":"Speech problems are difficulties that affect how clearly or smoothly someone speaks.","zh":"Speech problems 是影響某人說話清晰度或流暢度的困難。"},{"en":"A child with speech problems may need support from a speech therapist.","zh":"有說話問題的孩子可能需要言語治療師支援。"},{"en":"Speech problems can make presentations stressful because speaking takes more effort.","zh":"說話問題可以令匯報變得有壓力，因為說話需要更多努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficulties in producing spoken language.","zh":"這個片語描述產出口語時的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stuttering","meaning":"口吃","examples":[{"en":"Stuttering can involve repeating the first consonant of some words.","zh":"口吃可能涉及重複某些字詞的首個輔音。"},{"en":"Stuttering is a speech difficulty in which sounds, syllables or words may be repeated or blocked.","zh":"口吃是一種說話困難，聲音、音節或字詞可能被重複或卡住。"},{"en":"A person who stutters may need extra time to finish a sentence.","zh":"口吃的人可能需要更多時間完成句子。"},{"en":"Stress or pressure can sometimes make stuttering more noticeable.","zh":"壓力有時會令口吃更明顯。"},{"en":"Stuttering should be treated with patience, not mockery.","zh":"面對口吃應有耐性，而不是嘲笑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the first consonant","meaning":"首個輔音","examples":[{"en":"Stuttering may involve repeating the first consonant of a word.","zh":"口吃可能涉及重複一個字的首個輔音。"},{"en":"The first consonant is the first non-vowel sound at the beginning of a word.","zh":"The first consonant 是字詞開首第一個非元音聲音。"},{"en":"In the word “book”, the first consonant is “b”.","zh":"在 “book” 這個字中，首個輔音是 “b”。"},{"en":"If someone repeats the first consonant, “book” may sound like “b-b-book”.","zh":"如果某人重複首個輔音，“book” 可能聽起來像 “b-b-book”。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining pronunciation and speech difficulties.","zh":"這個片語適用於解釋發音和說話困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be normally avoided","meaning":"通常會被避免","examples":[{"en":"Fillers are normally avoided on television and in films.","zh":"填充語在電視和電影中通常會被避免。"},{"en":"To be normally avoided means people usually try not to use or include something.","zh":"To be normally avoided 指人們通常嘗試不使用或不包括某事物。"},{"en":"Very long pauses are normally avoided in formal presentations.","zh":"在正式匯報中，通常會避免很長停頓。"},{"en":"Fillers are avoided in edited media because they can make dialogue sound messy.","zh":"在經剪輯媒體中會避免填充語，因為它們可令對白聽起來雜亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that is common in real life but usually removed in polished contexts.","zh":"這個片語描述某事在現實生活中常見，但在修飾語境中通常被移除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on television and in films","meaning":"在電視和電影中","examples":[{"en":"Fillers are usually avoided on television and in films.","zh":"填充語通常在電視和電影中被避免。"},{"en":"On television and in films means in broadcast programmes and movies.","zh":"On television and in films 指在電視節目和電影中。"},{"en":"Speech on television and in films is often edited to sound clearer than real conversation.","zh":"電視和電影中的說話通常會被剪輯得比真實對話更清楚。"},{"en":"Fillers may be removed because audiences expect smooth and concise dialogue.","zh":"填充語可能被移除，因為觀眾期待流暢而簡潔的對白。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies media contexts rather than everyday conversation.","zh":"這個片語指出媒體語境，而不是日常對話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"occur quite regularly","meaning":"相當經常出現","examples":[{"en":"Fillers occur quite regularly in everyday conversation.","zh":"填充語在日常對話中相當經常出現。"},{"en":"To occur quite regularly means to happen fairly often.","zh":"To occur quite regularly 指相當頻密地發生。"},{"en":"Small pronunciation mistakes occur quite regularly when students speak a new language.","zh":"學生說新語言時，小發音錯誤相當經常出現。"},{"en":"Fillers occur regularly because speakers need time to think while talking.","zh":"填充語經常出現，因為說話者需要邊說邊思考。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something is normal and repeated, not rare.","zh":"這個片語表示某事正常且反覆出現，而不是罕見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"everyday conversation","meaning":"日常對話","examples":[{"en":"Fillers are common in everyday conversation.","zh":"填充語在日常對話中很常見。"},{"en":"Everyday conversation is ordinary informal speech between people in daily life.","zh":"Everyday conversation 是人們日常生活中的普通非正式說話。"},{"en":"Chatting with classmates before school is everyday conversation.","zh":"上課前與同學聊天就是日常對話。"},{"en":"In everyday conversation, people often pause, repeat themselves and change direction.","zh":"在日常對話中，人們常會停頓、重複自己並改變方向。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts casual speech with formal speeches or written language.","zh":"這個片語把隨意說話與正式演講或書面語作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make up more than","meaning":"佔超過……","examples":[{"en":"Fillers can sometimes make up more than 20% of spoken words.","zh":"填充語有時可以佔說話字詞超過百分之二十。"},{"en":"To make up more than a percentage means to form over that share of a whole.","zh":"To make up more than a percentage 指構成整體中超過某個比例。"},{"en":"Homework may make up more than half of a student’s evening routine.","zh":"功課可能佔學生晚上日程超過一半。"},{"en":"If fillers make up too much of a speech, the main message may become harder to follow.","zh":"如果填充語佔演講太大比例，主要訊息可能更難跟上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes proportion or percentage within a larger amount.","zh":"這個片語描述較大整體中的比例或百分比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"“words” in speech","meaning":"說話中的「字詞」","examples":[{"en":"Fillers can make up a large percentage of “words” in speech.","zh":"填充語可以佔說話中的「字詞」很大百分比。"},{"en":"“Words” in speech can include ordinary words as well as fillers counted in spoken language.","zh":"“Words” in speech 可以包括普通字詞，以及在口語中被計算的填充語。"},{"en":"A transcript may count “um” and “uh” as “words” in speech.","zh":"逐字稿可能把 “um” 和 “uh” 計作說話中的「字詞」。"},{"en":"Counting these “words” shows how different spoken language is from edited writing.","zh":"計算這些「字詞」顯示口語與經修飾寫作有多不同。"},{"en":"The quotation marks suggest that fillers are counted like words, even if they are not meaningful words.","zh":"引號表示填充語雖不一定有意義，但仍被像字詞一樣計算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"provide a pause for thought","meaning":"提供思考停頓","examples":[{"en":"Fillers can provide a pause for thought.","zh":"填充語可以提供思考停頓。"},{"en":"To provide a pause for thought means to give the speaker a short moment to think.","zh":"To provide a pause for thought 指給說話者短暫時間思考。"},{"en":"A student may say “well” to provide a pause for thought before answering a difficult question.","zh":"學生回答困難問題前可能說 “well”，以提供思考停頓。"},{"en":"This pause can help the speaker choose clearer words.","zh":"這種停頓可以幫助說話者選擇更清楚的字詞。"},{"en":"Fillers are not always useless; they can help speakers organise ideas.","zh":"填充語不一定無用；它們可以幫助說話者組織想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"research in linguistics","meaning":"語言學研究","examples":[{"en":"Research in linguistics has shown that fillers vary across cultures.","zh":"語言學研究顯示填充語因文化而異。"},{"en":"Research in linguistics is academic study of language and how people use it.","zh":"Research in linguistics 是對語言以及人們如何使用語言的學術研究。"},{"en":"Research in linguistics may examine accents, grammar, conversation and word choice.","zh":"語言學研究可能考察口音、文法、對話和用字選擇。"},{"en":"Such research helps explain why speakers in different cultures pause in different ways.","zh":"這類研究幫助解釋為何不同文化中的說話者以不同方式停頓。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to systematic study of language, not casual opinion.","zh":"這個片語指對語言的系統研究，而不是隨意意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"show that","meaning":"顯示","examples":[{"en":"Research has shown that fillers change across cultures.","zh":"研究顯示填充語因文化而變化。"},{"en":"To show that means to provide evidence or make something clear.","zh":"To show that 指提供證據或令某事清楚。"},{"en":"Test results may show that students need more practice with grammar.","zh":"測驗結果可能顯示學生需要更多文法練習。"},{"en":"If several studies show the same pattern, the conclusion becomes stronger.","zh":"如果幾項研究顯示同一模式，結論會更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what evidence suggests.","zh":"這個片語引出證據所表明的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"change across cultures","meaning":"因文化而異","examples":[{"en":"Fillers change across cultures.","zh":"填充語因文化而異。"},{"en":"To change across cultures means to differ from one culture or society to another.","zh":"To change across cultures 指從一種文化或社會到另一種有所不同。"},{"en":"Greetings change across cultures; some people bow, while others shake hands.","zh":"問候方式因文化而異；有些人鞠躬，有些人握手。"},{"en":"Fillers change across cultures because different languages use different habits of pausing.","zh":"填充語因文化而異，因為不同語言使用不同停頓習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights cultural variation in behaviour or language.","zh":"這個片語突出行為或語言上的文化差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"different English-speaking nations","meaning":"不同英語國家","examples":[{"en":"Different English-speaking nations use different fillers.","zh":"不同英語國家使用不同填充語。"},{"en":"Different English-speaking nations are countries where English is widely spoken but local habits may differ.","zh":"Different English-speaking nations 是英語被廣泛使用但本地習慣可能不同的國家。"},{"en":"Speakers from Britain, America and Australia may use different informal expressions.","zh":"英國、美國和澳洲的說話者可能使用不同非正式表達。"},{"en":"If English is used in many countries, its spoken habits can vary widely.","zh":"如果英語在許多國家使用，其口語習慣可以差異很大。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds learners that English is not identical everywhere.","zh":"這個片語提醒學習者，英語並非各地完全一樣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"use different fillers","meaning":"使用不同填充語","examples":[{"en":"Different English-speaking nations use different fillers.","zh":"不同英語國家使用不同填充語。"},{"en":"To use different fillers means to rely on different pause words or sounds while speaking.","zh":"To use different fillers 指說話時依賴不同停頓字詞或聲音。"},{"en":"One speaker may say “um”, while another often says “er”.","zh":"一位說話者可能說 “um”，另一位則常說 “er”。"},{"en":"Different fillers can reflect local accent, age, culture or speech habit.","zh":"不同填充語可以反映本地口音、年齡、文化或說話習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes variation in how people fill pauses.","zh":"這個片語描述人們如何填補停頓的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"for example","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"For example, Americans and British speakers use different fillers.","zh":"例如，美國人和英國說話者使用不同填充語。"},{"en":"For example introduces a specific case that helps explain a general idea.","zh":"For example 用來引出幫助解釋一般想法的具體例子。"},{"en":"Many students struggle with articles; for example, they may omit “the” before a specific noun.","zh":"許多學生在冠詞上有困難；例如，他們可能在特定名詞前省略 “the”。"},{"en":"Examples make an explanation easier to understand because readers can see the idea in action.","zh":"例子令解釋更易理解，因為讀者可以看見想法如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when moving from a rule to a concrete case.","zh":"這個片語適用於由規則轉向具體情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pauses such as","meaning":"例如……等停頓語","examples":[{"en":"Americans use pauses such as “um” or “em”.","zh":"美國人使用 “um” 或 “em” 等停頓語。"},{"en":"Pauses such as introduces examples of the pause sounds being discussed.","zh":"Pauses such as 用來引出正在討論的停頓聲音例子。"},{"en":"A speaker may use pauses such as “uh” while searching for the right word.","zh":"說話者尋找合適字詞時，可能使用 “uh” 等停頓語。"},{"en":"These pauses can signal that the speaker is not finished yet.","zh":"這些停頓可以表示說話者尚未說完。"},{"en":"This phrase helps list examples of hesitation sounds.","zh":"這個片語幫助列出猶豫聲音的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"whereas","meaning":"然而；而","examples":[{"en":"Americans often use “um”, whereas British speakers may say “uh” or “eh”.","zh":"美國人常使用 “um”，而英國說話者可能說 “uh” 或 “eh”。"},{"en":"Whereas is used to contrast two different facts or situations.","zh":"Whereas 用來對比兩個不同事實或情況。"},{"en":"Some students prefer writing essays, whereas others prefer speaking tasks.","zh":"有些學生較喜歡寫作文，而另一些較喜歡口語任務。"},{"en":"This word helps compare two groups without saying one is better than the other.","zh":"這個詞幫助比較兩個群體，而不表示其中一方較好。"},{"en":"Whereas is useful when the difference between two things is the main point.","zh":"當兩件事的差異是重點時，whereas 很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Spanish speakers","meaning":"西班牙語使用者","examples":[{"en":"Spanish speakers often say “ehhh” as a filler.","zh":"西班牙語使用者常說 “ehhh” 作為填充語。"},{"en":"Spanish speakers are people who speak Spanish as a first or additional language.","zh":"Spanish speakers 是以西班牙語作為母語或額外語言的人。"},{"en":"Spanish speakers may use different pause sounds from English speakers.","zh":"西班牙語使用者可能使用不同於英語使用者的停頓聲音。"},{"en":"When learners listen to Spanish speakers, they may notice fillers that do not appear in textbooks.","zh":"當學習者聆聽西班牙語使用者，他們可能注意到教科書中沒有的填充語。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to language users, not only people from Spain.","zh":"這個片語指語言使用者，而不只是西班牙人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Latin America","meaning":"拉丁美洲","examples":[{"en":"In Latin America, “este” is sometimes used as a filler.","zh":"在拉丁美洲，“este” 有時被用作填充語。"},{"en":"Latin America refers to countries in the Americas where Spanish, Portuguese or related languages are widely used.","zh":"Latin America 指美洲中廣泛使用西班牙語、葡萄牙語或相關語言的國家。"},{"en":"A student may study Latin America to learn about languages, music and history.","zh":"學生可能研究拉丁美洲，以學習語言、音樂和歷史。"},{"en":"Fillers in Latin America may differ from those in Spain or the United States.","zh":"拉丁美洲的填充語可能不同於西班牙或美國的填充語。"},{"en":"This phrase names a broad cultural and geographical region.","zh":"這個片語命名一個廣泛的文化及地理地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"normally meaning","meaning":"通常意思是","examples":[{"en":"“Este” is used as a filler, although it normally means “this”.","zh":"“Este” 被用作填充語，雖然它通常意思是「這個」。"},{"en":"Normally meaning introduces the usual meaning of a word in ordinary use.","zh":"Normally meaning 用來引出某字在普通用法中的通常意思。"},{"en":"“Well” normally means healthy, but it can also be used as a filler.","zh":"“Well” 通常意思是健康，但也可以用作填充語。"},{"en":"A word may have one normal meaning and another conversational function.","zh":"一個字可以有一個正常意思，也可以有另一個對話功能。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate dictionary meaning from special spoken use.","zh":"這個片語幫助區分字典意思和特殊口語用法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"recent linguistic research","meaning":"近期語言學研究","examples":[{"en":"Recent linguistic research has linked fillers with mental and emotional states.","zh":"近期語言學研究把填充語與心理和情緒狀態連繫起來。"},{"en":"Recent linguistic research is newer academic study of how language works and changes.","zh":"Recent linguistic research 是較新的關於語言如何運作和變化的學術研究。"},{"en":"Recent linguistic research may use recordings, surveys and computer analysis.","zh":"近期語言學研究可能使用錄音、調查和電腦分析。"},{"en":"New research can challenge older beliefs about why people use fillers.","zh":"新研究可以挑戰關於人們為何使用填充語的舊觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to up-to-date study in the field of language.","zh":"這個片語指語言學領域中的最新研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"suggest that","meaning":"表明；指出","examples":[{"en":"Research has suggested that the use of “uh” and “um” is connected to the speaker’s state.","zh":"研究指出 “uh” 和 “um” 的使用與說話者狀態有關。"},{"en":"Suggest that means to indicate something may be true, often without proving it completely.","zh":"Suggest that 指顯示某事可能是真實的，但通常未完全證明。"},{"en":"A student’s repeated yawning may suggest that they did not sleep enough.","zh":"學生反覆打呵欠可能表明他睡眠不足。"},{"en":"If research suggests a pattern, more evidence may still be needed.","zh":"如果研究指出某模式，可能仍需要更多證據。"},{"en":"This phrase presents a careful conclusion rather than an absolute fact.","zh":"這個片語提出謹慎結論，而不是絕對事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the use of","meaning":"……的使用","examples":[{"en":"The use of “uh” and “um” differs between speakers.","zh":"“uh” 和 “um” 的使用在說話者之間有所不同。"},{"en":"The use of something means how, when or how often people use it.","zh":"The use of something 指人們如何、何時或多常使用某事物。"},{"en":"The use of phones in class may depend on the teacher’s rules.","zh":"課堂上手機的使用可能取決於老師規則。"},{"en":"Studying the use of fillers can show differences in age, gender and culture.","zh":"研究填充語的使用可以顯示年齡、性別和文化差異。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on actual behaviour, not just the word itself.","zh":"這個片語集中於實際行為，而不只是字詞本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be connected to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The use of fillers may be connected to the speaker’s mental state.","zh":"填充語的使用可能與說話者的心理狀態有關。"},{"en":"To be connected to something means to have a relationship or link with it.","zh":"To be connected to something 指與某事有關係或聯繫。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be connected to staying up late.","zh":"學生疲倦可能與熬夜有關。"},{"en":"If filler choice is connected to emotion, speech can reveal more than words alone.","zh":"如果填充語選擇與情緒有關，說話能揭示比字面更多的資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a relationship, not always direct cause.","zh":"這個片語顯示關係，但不一定是直接原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mental and emotional state","meaning":"心理和情緒狀態","examples":[{"en":"Fillers may reflect the speaker’s mental and emotional state.","zh":"填充語可能反映說話者的心理和情緒狀態。"},{"en":"Mental and emotional state means a person’s thoughts, feelings and inner condition at a moment.","zh":"Mental and emotional state 指某一刻人的想法、感受和內在狀況。"},{"en":"Before an exam, a student’s mental and emotional state may include worry and pressure.","zh":"考試前，學生的心理和情緒狀態可能包括擔心和壓力。"},{"en":"If someone pauses often, they may be nervous, careful or unsure.","zh":"如果某人經常停頓，他可能緊張、謹慎或不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase connects speech behaviour with what is happening inside the speaker.","zh":"這個片語把說話行為與說話者內在情況連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pausing to say","meaning":"停頓並說出……","examples":[{"en":"The brain may be planning what to say next while pausing to say “uh” or “um”.","zh":"大腦可能在停頓並說出 “uh” 或 “um” 時構思接下來要說甚麼。"},{"en":"Pausing to say a filler means stopping briefly and using a sound while thinking.","zh":"Pausing to say a filler 指短暫停下並在思考時使用一個聲音。"},{"en":"A student may pause to say “um” before giving the final answer.","zh":"學生可能在給出最終答案前停頓並說 “um”。"},{"en":"This pause gives the speaker time to organise grammar and ideas.","zh":"這個停頓給說話者時間組織文法和想法。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a filler can be part of thinking, not just noise.","zh":"這個片語顯示填充語可以是思考的一部分，而不只是噪音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"plan what to say next","meaning":"構思接下來要說甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The brain may plan what to say next during a pause.","zh":"大腦可能在停頓期間構思接下來要說甚麼。"},{"en":"To plan what to say next means to prepare the next words or idea before speaking.","zh":"To plan what to say next 指在說出來之前準備下一些字詞或想法。"},{"en":"In an interview, a candidate may pause briefly to plan what to say next.","zh":"在面試中，應徵者可能短暫停頓來構思接下來要說甚麼。"},{"en":"Planning the next idea can make an answer clearer and less rushed.","zh":"構思下一個想法可以令答案更清楚和不太倉促。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why pauses naturally appear in speech.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何停頓自然出現在口語中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"According to Mark Liberman, “um” usually comes before a longer pause.","zh":"根據 Mark Liberman，“um” 通常出現在較長停頓之前。"},{"en":"According to means based on what a person, study or source says.","zh":"According to 指根據某人、研究或來源所說。"},{"en":"According to the teacher, the speaking test will start after lunch.","zh":"根據老師所說，口語測驗會在午飯後開始。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to show where information comes from.","zh":"作者使用這個片語來顯示資訊來源。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a source rather than the writer’s own unsupported opinion.","zh":"這個片語引出來源，而不是作者自己沒有支持的意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"generally comes before","meaning":"通常出現在……之前","examples":[{"en":"“Um” generally comes before a longer or more important pause than “uh”.","zh":"“Um” 通常出現在比 “uh” 更長或更重要的停頓之前。"},{"en":"Generally comes before means usually appears earlier than something else.","zh":"Generally comes before 指通常比另一事物更早出現。"},{"en":"In a lesson, the explanation generally comes before the exercise.","zh":"在課堂中，解釋通常出現在練習之前。"},{"en":"If “um” usually comes before longer pauses, it may signal more planning time.","zh":"如果 “um” 通常出現在較長停頓之前，它可能表示需要更多構思時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common order, not an absolute rule.","zh":"這個片語描述常見次序，而不是絕對規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a longer or more important pause","meaning":"較長或較重要的停頓","examples":[{"en":"Liberman once thought that “um” came before a longer or more important pause.","zh":"Liberman 曾經認為 “um” 出現在較長或較重要的停頓之前。"},{"en":"A longer or more important pause is a pause that lasts more time or signals a bigger planning moment.","zh":"A longer or more important pause 是持續時間較長，或表示較大構思時刻的停頓。"},{"en":"A speaker may take a longer pause before answering a personal question.","zh":"說話者回答私人問題前，可能作出較長停頓。"},{"en":"Important pauses can show that the speaker is choosing words carefully.","zh":"重要停頓可以顯示說話者正在仔細選詞。"},{"en":"This phrase links pause length with the difficulty or importance of the next idea.","zh":"這個片語把停頓長短與下一個想法的難度或重要性連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at least","meaning":"至少","examples":[{"en":"At least, that is what Liberman used to think.","zh":"至少，那是 Liberman 過去所想的。"},{"en":"At least can mean “anyway”, “in any case” or “to a minimum degree”.","zh":"At least 可以表示「無論如何」、「至少」或「最低程度上」。"},{"en":"The answer was not perfect, but at least it was clear.","zh":"答案並不完美，但至少很清楚。"},{"en":"A writer may use “at least” to soften or limit a statement.","zh":"作者可能使用 “at least” 來柔化或限制說法。"},{"en":"In this context, it suggests the view was true only as far as he once believed.","zh":"在這個語境中，它暗示這個看法只是他曾經相信的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"used to think","meaning":"過去認為","examples":[{"en":"Liberman used to think that “um” came before a longer pause than “uh”.","zh":"Liberman 過去認為 “um” 出現在比 “uh” 更長的停頓之前。"},{"en":"Used to think means someone believed something in the past but may not believe it now.","zh":"Used to think 指某人過去相信某事，但現在可能不再相信。"},{"en":"I used to think grammar was only about rules, but now I see it as meaning and choice.","zh":"我過去認為文法只是規則，但現在我把它看作意思和選擇。"},{"en":"Research can change what experts used to think.","zh":"研究可以改變專家過去認為的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a past belief that has been revised.","zh":"這個片語突出已被修正的過去信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"discover that","meaning":"發現","examples":[{"en":"Liberman discovered that older Americans use “uh” more than “um”.","zh":"Liberman 發現年長美國人使用 “uh” 多於 “um”。"},{"en":"To discover that means to find out something through observation, study or experience.","zh":"To discover that 指透過觀察、研究或經驗找出某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may discover that students learn better with examples than with long definitions.","zh":"老師可能發現學生透過例子學習比長定義更有效。"},{"en":"If researchers discover a pattern, they may design a larger study to test it.","zh":"如果研究人員發現一種模式，他們可能設計更大型研究來測試它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a finding that was not known before.","zh":"這個片語引出以前未知的發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as Americans get older","meaning":"隨着美國人年紀增長","examples":[{"en":"As Americans get older, they use “uh” more than “um”.","zh":"隨着美國人年紀增長，他們使用 “uh” 多於 “um”。"},{"en":"As Americans get older means while or when American speakers increase in age.","zh":"As Americans get older 指當美國說話者年齡增加時。"},{"en":"As people get older, their speech habits may become more stable.","zh":"隨着人們年紀增長，他們的說話習慣可能更穩定。"},{"en":"If filler use changes with age, researchers can compare younger and older speakers.","zh":"如果填充語使用隨年齡改變，研究人員可以比較年輕和年長說話者。"},{"en":"This phrase connects age with a change in language behaviour.","zh":"這個片語把年齡與語言行為變化連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"use “uh” more than “um”","meaning":"使用“uh”多於“um”","examples":[{"en":"Older Americans use “uh” more than “um”.","zh":"年長美國人使用 “uh” 多於 “um”。"},{"en":"To use “uh” more than “um” means to choose “uh” more frequently as a filler.","zh":"To use “uh” more than “um” 指較頻繁選用 “uh” 作為填充語。"},{"en":"In a recording, one speaker may use “uh” many times but hardly say “um”.","zh":"在錄音中，一位說話者可能多次使用 “uh”，但幾乎不說 “um”。"},{"en":"This pattern may reveal differences in age, habit or identity.","zh":"這種模式可能揭示年齡、習慣或身份差異。"},{"en":"The phrase compares how often two fillers are used.","zh":"這個片語比較兩個填充語被使用的頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"no matter their age","meaning":"不論年齡","examples":[{"en":"Men use “uh” more than women no matter their age.","zh":"男性不論年齡都比女性更多使用 “uh”。"},{"en":"No matter their age means regardless of whether they are young or old.","zh":"No matter their age 指無論他們年輕或年老。"},{"en":"Students need clear feedback no matter their age or level.","zh":"學生不論年齡或程度都需要清晰回饋。"},{"en":"If a pattern appears no matter the speaker’s age, gender may be part of the explanation.","zh":"如果某模式不論說話者年齡都出現，性別可能是解釋的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that age does not change the point being made.","zh":"這個片語顯示年齡不會改變所提出的重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the opposite is true of","meaning":"對……而言情況相反","examples":[{"en":"The opposite is true of “um”.","zh":"對 “um” 而言情況相反。"},{"en":"The opposite is true of something means the reverse pattern applies to that thing.","zh":"The opposite is true of something 指相反模式適用於某事物。"},{"en":"Some students enjoy writing but dislike speaking; the opposite is true of others.","zh":"有些學生喜歡寫作但不喜歡說話；另一些學生則情況相反。"},{"en":"If men use one filler more, the opposite may be true of women and another filler.","zh":"如果男性更多使用某填充語，女性和另一填充語可能情況相反。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare two contrasting patterns.","zh":"這個片語幫助比較兩種相反模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"more often than","meaning":"比……更經常","examples":[{"en":"Young people say “um” more often than older people.","zh":"年輕人說 “um” 比年長人士更經常。"},{"en":"More often than means with greater frequency than another person or group.","zh":"More often than 指比另一個人或群體更頻繁。"},{"en":"Some students check messages more often than they check school emails.","zh":"有些學生查看訊息比查看學校電郵更經常。"},{"en":"If one group uses a filler more often than another, researchers may look for social reasons.","zh":"如果一個群體使用填充語比另一群體更頻繁，研究人員可能尋找社會原因。"},{"en":"This phrase compares frequency between two sides.","zh":"這個片語比較兩方之間的頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at every age","meaning":"在每個年齡層","examples":[{"en":"Women say “um” more often than men at every age.","zh":"女性在每個年齡層都比男性更常說 “um”。"},{"en":"At every age means in all age groups.","zh":"At every age 指在所有年齡組別中。"},{"en":"People need enough sleep at every age, from children to older adults.","zh":"人們在每個年齡層都需要足夠睡眠，從兒童到長者都是。"},{"en":"If a pattern appears at every age, it is not limited to young speakers only.","zh":"如果某模式在每個年齡層都出現，它就不限於年輕說話者。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the statement applies across the whole age range.","zh":"這個片語顯示說法適用於整個年齡範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"an unexpected result","meaning":"意料之外的結果","examples":[{"en":"This was an unexpected result for researchers.","zh":"對研究人員來說，這是意料之外的結果。"},{"en":"An unexpected result is a finding that researchers did not predict.","zh":"Unexpected result 是研究人員沒有預測到的發現。"},{"en":"A teacher may get an unexpected result when quiet students perform best in a speaking task.","zh":"當安靜學生在口語任務中表現最好時，老師可能得到意料之外的結果。"},{"en":"Unexpected results can make researchers question their original assumptions.","zh":"意料之外的結果可以令研究人員質疑原本假設。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a surprising outcome.","zh":"這個片語描述令人驚訝的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be closely related to","meaning":"與……密切相關","examples":[{"en":"Scientists used to think fillers were closely related to pause length.","zh":"科學家過去認為填充語與停頓長短密切相關。"},{"en":"To be closely related to something means to have a strong connection with it.","zh":"To be closely related to something 指與某事有強烈聯繫。"},{"en":"A student’s exam performance may be closely related to sleep and regular practice.","zh":"學生考試表現可能與睡眠和定期練習密切相關。"},{"en":"If fillers were closely related to pause length, longer pauses would predict certain fillers.","zh":"如果填充語與停頓長短密切相關，較長停頓就會預示某些填充語。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong link between two things.","zh":"這個片語描述兩件事之間的強烈聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the length of a speaker’s pauses","meaning":"說話者停頓的長短","examples":[{"en":"Scientists once linked fillers to the length of a speaker’s pauses.","zh":"科學家曾把填充語與說話者停頓的長短連繫起來。"},{"en":"The length of a speaker’s pauses means how long the speaker stops while talking.","zh":"The length of a speaker’s pauses 指說話者說話時停下多久。"},{"en":"In a speaking test, long pauses may show that a student is searching for words.","zh":"在口語測驗中，長停頓可能顯示學生正在尋找字詞。"},{"en":"If pause length changes, listeners may feel the speaker is more hesitant or more thoughtful.","zh":"如果停頓長短改變，聽者可能覺得說話者更猶豫或更深思。"},{"en":"This phrase measures timing inside spoken language.","zh":"這個片語量度口語中的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"speaker’s identity","meaning":"說話者身份","examples":[{"en":"The choice of filler may be related to the speaker’s identity.","zh":"填充語的選擇可能與說話者身份有關。"},{"en":"Speaker’s identity means personal or social features such as age, gender, background or community.","zh":"Speaker’s identity 指年齡、性別、背景或社群等個人或社會特徵。"},{"en":"A speaker’s identity may influence accent, vocabulary and informal expressions.","zh":"說話者身份可能影響口音、詞彙和非正式表達。"},{"en":"If filler choice changes by age and gender, identity may help explain the pattern.","zh":"如果填充語選擇隨年齡和性別改變，身份可能有助解釋該模式。"},{"en":"This phrase links language use with who the speaker is.","zh":"這個片語把語言使用與說話者是誰連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"mention one’s finding to","meaning":"向……提及自己的發現","examples":[{"en":"Liberman mentioned his finding to fellow linguists in the Netherlands.","zh":"Liberman 向荷蘭的語言學界同僚提及自己的發現。"},{"en":"To mention one’s finding to someone means to tell them about a research result or observation.","zh":"To mention one’s finding to someone 指向某人說出自己的研究結果或觀察。"},{"en":"A teacher may mention her finding to colleagues after noticing a common grammar mistake.","zh":"老師注意到常見文法錯誤後，可能向同事提及自己的發現。"},{"en":"Sharing a finding can encourage other people to test whether the same pattern appears elsewhere.","zh":"分享發現可以鼓勵其他人測試同一模式是否在其他地方出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes informal or formal sharing of a discovery.","zh":"這個片語描述正式或非正式分享發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fellow linguists","meaning":"語言學界同僚","examples":[{"en":"Liberman discussed his finding with fellow linguists.","zh":"Liberman 與語言學界同僚討論他的發現。"},{"en":"Fellow linguists are other people who also study language professionally.","zh":"Fellow linguists 是同樣專業研究語言的人。"},{"en":"A linguist may ask fellow linguists whether the same speech pattern appears in another language.","zh":"語言學家可能問語言學界同僚，同一說話模式是否出現在另一語言中。"},{"en":"Working with fellow linguists can help researchers compare data from different countries.","zh":"與語言學界同僚合作可以幫助研究人員比較不同國家的數據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to colleagues in the same academic field.","zh":"這個片語指同一學術領域中的同事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"encourage someone to","meaning":"鼓勵某人去……","examples":[{"en":"This encouraged the group to look for a pattern outside American English.","zh":"這鼓勵該團隊在美式英語以外尋找模式。"},{"en":"To encourage someone to do something means to make them feel motivated or interested in doing it.","zh":"To encourage someone to do something 指令某人有動力或興趣去做某事。"},{"en":"A good teacher can encourage shy students to speak by praising small efforts.","zh":"好老師可以透過讚賞小努力，鼓勵害羞學生發言。"},{"en":"A surprising finding can encourage researchers to ask new questions.","zh":"令人驚訝的發現可以鼓勵研究人員提出新問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving someone a reason or confidence to act.","zh":"這個片語描述給予某人行動理由或信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"look for a pattern","meaning":"尋找模式","examples":[{"en":"The linguists looked for a pattern outside American English.","zh":"語言學家在美式英語以外尋找模式。"},{"en":"To look for a pattern means to search for a repeated or meaningful arrangement in data.","zh":"To look for a pattern 指在數據中尋找重複或有意義的安排。"},{"en":"A teacher may look for a pattern in students’ mistakes before designing a review lesson.","zh":"老師設計溫習課前，可能在學生錯誤中尋找模式。"},{"en":"If a pattern appears in several languages, it may suggest a wider change.","zh":"如果某模式出現在幾種語言中，它可能顯示更廣泛變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes searching for regularity, not just collecting examples.","zh":"這個片語描述尋找規律，而不只是收集例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"outside American English","meaning":"在美式英語以外","examples":[{"en":"The researchers looked for similar patterns outside American English.","zh":"研究人員在美式英語以外尋找類似模式。"},{"en":"Outside American English means in varieties or languages other than American English.","zh":"Outside American English 指在美式英語以外的變體或語言中。"},{"en":"A pronunciation rule may work in American English but not outside American English.","zh":"某發音規則可能適用於美式英語，但不適用於美式英語以外的語境。"},{"en":"If a filler pattern appears outside American English, it may not be only an American habit.","zh":"如果填充語模式在美式英語以外出現，它可能不只是美國習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase helps widen the comparison beyond one variety of English.","zh":"這個片語幫助把比較擴展至單一英語變體以外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"British and Scottish English","meaning":"英格蘭及蘇格蘭英語","examples":[{"en":"The researchers studied British and Scottish English.","zh":"研究人員研究英格蘭及蘇格蘭英語。"},{"en":"British and Scottish English are varieties of English used in Britain and Scotland.","zh":"British and Scottish English 是在英國和蘇格蘭使用的英語變體。"},{"en":"Learners may hear differences between British and Scottish English in pronunciation and vocabulary.","zh":"學習者可能在發音和詞彙上聽到英格蘭及蘇格蘭英語的差異。"},{"en":"Comparing these varieties can show whether a speech pattern is shared across regions.","zh":"比較這些變體可以顯示某說話模式是否跨地區共享。"},{"en":"This phrase names English varieties used for linguistic comparison.","zh":"這個片語命名用於語言比較的英語變體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in those languages as well","meaning":"在那些語言中也一樣","examples":[{"en":"Women and younger people used “um” more than “uh” in those languages as well.","zh":"女性和年輕人在那些語言中也一樣使用 “um” 多於 “uh”。"},{"en":"In those languages as well means the same pattern also appears in the languages just mentioned.","zh":"In those languages as well 指同一模式也出現在剛提到的那些語言中。"},{"en":"If a grammar pattern appears in French and Spanish as well, it may be more widespread than expected.","zh":"如果某文法模式在法語和西班牙語中也一樣出現，它可能比預期更廣泛。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show that a finding is not limited to one language.","zh":"這個片語幫助顯示某發現不限於一種語言。"},{"en":"It adds another piece of evidence to a broader comparison.","zh":"它為更廣泛比較加入另一項證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"their conclusion is that","meaning":"他們的結論是","examples":[{"en":"Their conclusion is that a language change is in progress.","zh":"他們的結論是，一場語言變化正在進行中。"},{"en":"Their conclusion is that introduces the final idea reached after considering evidence.","zh":"Their conclusion is that 用來引出考慮證據後得出的最終想法。"},{"en":"After checking attendance records, the teacher’s conclusion is that the problem happens mainly on Mondays.","zh":"檢查出席紀錄後，老師的結論是問題主要發生在星期一。"},{"en":"A conclusion should be supported by patterns, not just one example.","zh":"結論應由模式支持，而不只是單一例子。"},{"en":"This phrase presents what researchers think the evidence means.","zh":"這個片語呈現研究人員認為證據意味着甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"simply a case of","meaning":"只不過是……的情況","examples":[{"en":"The pattern is simply a case of language change in progress.","zh":"這個模式只不過是語言變化正在進行中的情況。"},{"en":"Simply a case of means it is just an example of a particular situation.","zh":"Simply a case of 指它只是某種特定情況的一個例子。"},{"en":"A student’s silence may be simply a case of nervousness, not laziness.","zh":"學生沉默可能只不過是緊張的情況，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"If “um” is spreading, it may simply be a case of normal language change.","zh":"如果 “um” 正在擴散，它可能只不過是正常語言變化的情況。"},{"en":"This phrase simplifies the explanation by placing it in a known category.","zh":"這個片語透過把事情放入已知類別來簡化解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"language change in progress","meaning":"正在進行中的語言變化","examples":[{"en":"The use of “um” may show language change in progress.","zh":"“um” 的使用可能顯示正在進行中的語言變化。"},{"en":"Language change in progress means a language is currently changing while people are using it.","zh":"Language change in progress 指語言在人們使用時正在改變。"},{"en":"New slang in schools can show language change in progress.","zh":"學校中的新俚語可以顯示正在進行中的語言變化。"},{"en":"If young speakers use a form more often, that form may spread over time.","zh":"如果年輕說話者更常使用某形式，該形式可能隨時間擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes change happening now, not only in the past.","zh":"這個片語描述正在發生的變化，而不只是過去的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lead the change","meaning":"引領變化","examples":[{"en":"Women and younger people are leading the change.","zh":"女性和年輕人正在引領變化。"},{"en":"To lead the change means to be the group that starts or spreads a change first.","zh":"To lead the change 指成為首先開始或擴散變化的群體。"},{"en":"Students may lead the change when a school begins using less plastic.","zh":"當學校開始減少使用塑膠時，學生可能引領變化。"},{"en":"If young speakers adopt a new word first, they may lead language change.","zh":"如果年輕說話者首先採用新詞，他們可能引領語言變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes who is at the front of a shift.","zh":"這個片語描述誰站在轉變的前端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"there is nothing strange about","meaning":"……並不奇怪","examples":[{"en":"There is nothing strange about women and young people leading language change.","zh":"女性和年輕人引領語言變化並不奇怪。"},{"en":"There is nothing strange about something means it is normal or not surprising.","zh":"There is nothing strange about something 指某事正常或不令人驚訝。"},{"en":"There is nothing strange about students feeling nervous before their first speech.","zh":"學生在第一次演講前感到緊張並不奇怪。"},{"en":"If young people create new expressions, that is a normal part of language life.","zh":"如果年輕人創造新表達，那是語言生活的正常部分。"},{"en":"This phrase reduces the sense that something is unusual.","zh":"這個片語降低某事的不尋常感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pioneers of language change","meaning":"語言變化的先驅","examples":[{"en":"Women and young people are often pioneers of language change.","zh":"女性和年輕人常是語言變化的先驅。"},{"en":"Pioneers of language change are groups that first use or spread new language forms.","zh":"Pioneers of language change 是首先使用或擴散新語言形式的群體。"},{"en":"Teenagers can be pioneers of language change when new slang spreads through schools.","zh":"當新俚語在學校中傳播，青少年可以成為語言變化的先驅。"},{"en":"When pioneers use a form often, others may gradually copy it.","zh":"當先驅者經常使用某形式，其他人可能逐漸模仿。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first movers in language development.","zh":"這個片語描述語言發展中的先行者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"what is strange, however, is that","meaning":"然而奇怪的是","examples":[{"en":"What is strange, however, is that “um” is replacing “uh” across several languages.","zh":"然而奇怪的是，“um” 正在多種語言中取代 “uh”。"},{"en":"What is strange, however, is that introduces a surprising contrast after something normal has been mentioned.","zh":"What is strange, however, is that 用來在提到正常事情後引出令人驚訝的對比。"},{"en":"Students often copy slang from friends; what is strange, however, is that the same slang appeared in several schools at once.","zh":"學生常從朋友那裏模仿俚語；然而奇怪的是，同一俚語同時出現在幾間學校。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers shift from expected information to an unexpected point.","zh":"這個片語幫助作者從預期資訊轉向意外重點。"},{"en":"It highlights the part of the situation that still needs explanation.","zh":"它突出情況中仍需要解釋的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"replace “uh”","meaning":"取代“uh”","examples":[{"en":"“Um” appears to be replacing “uh” in several languages.","zh":"“Um” 似乎正在幾種語言中取代 “uh”。"},{"en":"To replace “uh” means to take the place of “uh” as the more common filler.","zh":"To replace “uh” 指取代 “uh” 成為更常見填充語。"},{"en":"In a school, a new slang word may replace an older one among younger students.","zh":"在學校裏，新俚語可能在年輕學生中取代舊俚語。"},{"en":"If “um” spreads while “uh” declines, one filler is replacing another.","zh":"如果 “um” 擴散而 “uh” 減少，就是一個填充語正在取代另一個。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift from one language form to another.","zh":"這個片語描述由一種語言形式轉向另一種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"across at least two continents","meaning":"橫跨至少兩個洲","examples":[{"en":"The change is happening across at least two continents.","zh":"這項變化正在橫跨至少兩個洲發生。"},{"en":"Across at least two continents means in regions located on two or more continents.","zh":"Across at least two continents 指在位於兩個或以上大洲的地區中。"},{"en":"A music trend across at least two continents is no longer just a local fashion.","zh":"橫跨至少兩個洲的音樂潮流，已不再只是本地時尚。"},{"en":"If a language change crosses continents, researchers may look for international influence.","zh":"如果語言變化跨越大洲，研究人員可能尋找國際影響。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the pattern is geographically widespread.","zh":"這個片語強調該模式在地理上很廣泛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Germanic languages","meaning":"日耳曼語族語言","examples":[{"en":"The researchers studied several Germanic languages.","zh":"研究人員研究了幾種日耳曼語族語言。"},{"en":"Germanic languages are a language family that includes English, German, Dutch and related languages.","zh":"Germanic languages 是包括英語、德語、荷蘭語及相關語言的語族。"},{"en":"A linguistics class may compare Germanic languages to find shared word patterns.","zh":"語言學課可能比較日耳曼語族語言，以尋找共同詞語模式。"},{"en":"If the same filler change appears in several Germanic languages, the pattern becomes more interesting.","zh":"如果同一填充語變化出現在幾種日耳曼語族語言中，模式就更有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase names a family of historically related languages.","zh":"這個片語命名一組歷史上相關的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a mystery","meaning":"謎團","examples":[{"en":"The spread of “um” across languages remains a mystery.","zh":"“um” 跨語言擴散仍是一個謎團。"},{"en":"A mystery is something that is not yet fully understood or explained.","zh":"Mystery 是尚未被完全理解或解釋的事情。"},{"en":"It may be a mystery why one class suddenly improves while another does not.","zh":"為何一班突然進步而另一班沒有，可能是一個謎團。"},{"en":"A mystery encourages researchers to collect more evidence and test explanations.","zh":"謎團會鼓勵研究人員收集更多證據並測試解釋。"},{"en":"This word shows that the answer is still uncertain.","zh":"這個詞顯示答案仍不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sociolinguist","meaning":"社會語言學家","examples":[{"en":"Josef Fruehwald is a sociolinguist at the University of Edinburgh.","zh":"Josef Fruehwald 是愛丁堡大學的社會語言學家。"},{"en":"A sociolinguist studies how language is connected to society, identity and groups.","zh":"Sociolinguist 研究語言如何與社會、身份和群體相連。"},{"en":"A sociolinguist may study how teenagers, adults and older people use different words.","zh":"社會語言學家可能研究青少年、成年人和長者如何使用不同字詞。"},{"en":"Sociolinguists ask why speech changes across age, gender, class or region.","zh":"社會語言學家探問為何說話隨年齡、性別、階級或地區而變化。"},{"en":"This word describes a language researcher who focuses on social patterns.","zh":"這個詞描述專注社會模式的語言研究者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"may have an answer","meaning":"可能有答案","examples":[{"en":"Josef Fruehwald may have an answer to the mystery.","zh":"Josef Fruehwald 可能對這個謎團有答案。"},{"en":"May have an answer means someone possibly has a useful explanation, but it is not certain.","zh":"May have an answer 指某人可能有有用解釋，但仍未確定。"},{"en":"A doctor may have an answer after seeing the test results.","zh":"醫生看過測試結果後，可能有答案。"},{"en":"If one explanation fits the evidence, it may help solve the puzzle.","zh":"如果一個解釋符合證據，它可能有助解開謎題。"},{"en":"This phrase presents a possible solution carefully.","zh":"這個片語謹慎提出可能解決方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in his view","meaning":"在他看來","examples":[{"en":"In his view, “um” and “uh” are pretty much equivalent.","zh":"在他看來，“um” 和 “uh” 差不多等同。"},{"en":"In his view means according to his opinion or interpretation.","zh":"In his view 指根據他的意見或解讀。"},{"en":"In her view, students learn better when examples come before rules.","zh":"在她看來，當例子先於規則出現，學生學得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the statement belongs to one person’s perspective.","zh":"這個片語顯示該說法屬於某人的觀點。"},{"en":"It is useful when different experts may disagree.","zh":"當不同專家可能不同意時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pretty much equivalent","meaning":"差不多等同","examples":[{"en":"Fruehwald thinks “um” and “uh” are pretty much equivalent.","zh":"Fruehwald 認為 “um” 和 “uh” 差不多等同。"},{"en":"Pretty much equivalent means almost the same in meaning, use or function.","zh":"Pretty much equivalent 指在意思、用途或功能上幾乎相同。"},{"en":"Two bus routes may be pretty much equivalent if both reach school in about the same time.","zh":"如果兩條巴士路線都差不多時間到校，它們可能差不多等同。"},{"en":"If “um” and “uh” serve the same function, choosing one may not change the message much.","zh":"如果 “um” 和 “uh” 發揮相同功能，選其中一個可能不太改變訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests strong similarity, though not perfect sameness.","zh":"這個片語表示高度相似，但不是完全一樣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the fact that","meaning":"……這一事實","examples":[{"en":"The fact that young people prefer “um” may not be significant.","zh":"年輕人較喜歡使用 “um” 這一事實可能並不重要。"},{"en":"The fact that introduces a situation or truth being discussed.","zh":"The fact that 用來引出正在討論的情況或事實。"},{"en":"The fact that a student is quiet does not mean they are not thinking.","zh":"學生安靜這一事實不代表他沒有思考。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to focus attention on one specific point.","zh":"作者使用這個片語，把注意力集中在某一具體重點。"},{"en":"This phrase turns a whole idea into something that can be discussed.","zh":"這個片語把整個想法變成可以討論的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"prefer “um”","meaning":"較喜歡使用“um”","examples":[{"en":"Young people and women appear to prefer “um”.","zh":"年輕人和女性似乎較喜歡使用 “um”。"},{"en":"To prefer “um” means to use “um” more often or choose it more naturally than another filler.","zh":"To prefer “um” 指更常使用或更自然地選擇 “um” 而非另一填充語。"},{"en":"A speaker may prefer “um” without consciously deciding to use it.","zh":"說話者可能在沒有有意識決定的情況下較喜歡使用 “um”。"},{"en":"If a group prefers one filler, that preference may spread through conversation.","zh":"如果某群體偏好一個填充語，該偏好可能透過對話擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a habit of choosing one speech form over another.","zh":"這個片語描述選擇一種說話形式多於另一種的習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not significant","meaning":"並不重要；並無重大意義","examples":[{"en":"Fruehwald argues that the preference for “um” is not significant.","zh":"Fruehwald 認為對 “um” 的偏好並不重要。"},{"en":"Not significant means not important enough to change the explanation or conclusion.","zh":"Not significant 指重要性不足以改變解釋或結論。"},{"en":"A one-mark difference may be not significant if the test was very easy.","zh":"如果測驗很容易，一分差距可能並無重大意義。"},{"en":"If two fillers mean almost the same thing, choosing one may not be socially important.","zh":"如果兩個填充語意思幾乎一樣，選其中一個可能沒有重要社會意義。"},{"en":"This phrase downplays the importance of a finding.","zh":"這個片語降低某發現的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"when there are two options","meaning":"當有兩個選項時","examples":[{"en":"This often happens in language when there are two options.","zh":"當語言中有兩個選項時，這種情況常會發生。"},{"en":"When there are two options means when people can choose between two possible forms.","zh":"When there are two options 指人們可以在兩種可能形式之間選擇。"},{"en":"In English, learners sometimes choose between “begin” and “start” when there are two options.","zh":"在英語中，當有兩個選項時，學習者有時會在 “begin” 和 “start” 之間選擇。"},{"en":"If one option becomes more popular, the other may slowly disappear.","zh":"如果其中一個選項變得更受歡迎，另一個可能慢慢消失。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a situation where choice leads to change.","zh":"這個片語引出選擇導致變化的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"start using one more often","meaning":"開始更常使用其中一個","examples":[{"en":"People may start using one option more often than the other.","zh":"人們可能開始更常使用其中一個選項。"},{"en":"To start using one more often means to gradually choose one form with greater frequency.","zh":"To start using one more often 指逐漸更頻繁選擇其中一種形式。"},{"en":"Students may start using “because” more often after learning how to explain reasons.","zh":"學生學會如何解釋原因後，可能開始更常使用 “because”。"},{"en":"If many speakers start using one form more often, language change may follow.","zh":"如果許多說話者開始更常使用一種形式，語言變化可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the early stage of a shift in usage.","zh":"這個片語描述用法轉變的早期階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"no longer an option","meaning":"不再是一個選項","examples":[{"en":"One form may disappear until it is no longer an option.","zh":"一種形式可能消失，直到它不再是一個選項。"},{"en":"No longer an option means it is not available or normally used anymore.","zh":"No longer an option 指不再可用或不再正常使用。"},{"en":"Paying by cash may be no longer an option in some online shops.","zh":"在一些網店中，用現金付款可能不再是一個選項。"},{"en":"If a language form disappears, future speakers may not choose it at all.","zh":"如果某語言形式消失，未來說話者可能完全不會選用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something being removed from real choice.","zh":"這個片語描述某事從真正選擇中被移除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"it’s just one of those things","meaning":"這種事就是這樣","examples":[{"en":"Fruehwald suggests that the shift is just one of those things.","zh":"Fruehwald 暗示這種轉變就是這樣。"},{"en":"It’s just one of those things means something happens naturally and may not need a deep explanation.","zh":"It’s just one of those things 指某事自然發生，可能不需要深層解釋。"},{"en":"If one slang word becomes popular for no clear reason, it may be just one of those things.","zh":"如果某俚語無明顯原因地變得流行，它可能就是這種事。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a change feels normal, random or hard to explain.","zh":"這個片語用於變化感覺正常、隨機或難以解釋時。"},{"en":"It often downplays mystery by treating the situation as ordinary.","zh":"它常透過把情況視為普通來淡化謎團。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as to how","meaning":"至於如何","examples":[{"en":"As to how the trend spread, Fruehwald offers a simple explanation.","zh":"至於這種趨勢如何擴散，Fruehwald 提出了一個簡單解釋。"},{"en":"As to how means concerning the question of how something happened.","zh":"As to how 指關於某事如何發生這個問題。"},{"en":"As to how students improved so quickly, the teacher pointed to daily practice.","zh":"至於學生如何進步得這麼快，老師指出是因為每天練習。"},{"en":"This phrase shifts attention to the method or process behind an event.","zh":"這個片語把注意力轉向事件背後的方法或過程。"},{"en":"It is useful when separating what happened from how it happened.","zh":"當要區分發生了甚麼和如何發生時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"such a trend","meaning":"這樣的趨勢","examples":[{"en":"Such a trend may have spread from one language to another.","zh":"這樣的趨勢可能從一種語言傳到另一種語言。"},{"en":"Such a trend means a trend of the kind just described.","zh":"Such a trend 指剛剛描述的那種趨勢。"},{"en":"If many students begin using the same phrase online, such a trend may soon enter classroom speech.","zh":"如果許多學生開始在網上使用同一句話，這樣的趨勢可能很快進入課堂口語。"},{"en":"A trend can spread when people hear it often and begin copying it.","zh":"當人們經常聽到某趨勢並開始模仿，它就可以擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a previously mentioned pattern of change.","zh":"這個片語回指之前提到的變化模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"go from one language to another","meaning":"從一種語言傳到另一種語言","examples":[{"en":"The trend may have gone from one language to another through English.","zh":"這種趨勢可能透過英語從一種語言傳到另一種語言。"},{"en":"To go from one language to another means to spread or move between languages.","zh":"To go from one language to another 指在語言之間擴散或移動。"},{"en":"A word like “coffee” has gone from one language to another over history.","zh":"“coffee” 這類字在歷史上曾從一種語言傳到另一種語言。"},{"en":"If a filler spreads through media, it may move into other languages without formal teaching.","zh":"如果填充語透過媒體擴散，它可能在沒有正式教學下進入其他語言。"},{"en":"This phrase describes linguistic borrowing or influence across languages.","zh":"這個片語描述跨語言借用或影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a simple explanation","meaning":"簡單的解釋","examples":[{"en":"Fruehwald offers a simple explanation for the spread of “um”.","zh":"Fruehwald 為 “um” 的擴散提出一個簡單的解釋。"},{"en":"A simple explanation is an easy-to-understand reason for something.","zh":"Simple explanation 是容易理解的原因。"},{"en":"A simple explanation for a student’s tiredness may be that they slept late.","zh":"學生疲倦的一個簡單解釋可能是他睡得晚。"},{"en":"Simple explanations are useful, but researchers still need evidence to support them.","zh":"簡單解釋很有用，但研究人員仍需要證據支持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an explanation that is not complicated.","zh":"這個片語描述不複雜的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"influence other languages","meaning":"影響其他語言","examples":[{"en":"English may be influencing the other languages.","zh":"英語可能正在影響其他語言。"},{"en":"To influence other languages means to affect how those languages are spoken or written.","zh":"To influence other languages 指影響那些語言的說話或書寫方式。"},{"en":"English can influence other languages when people borrow words from films, music or the internet.","zh":"當人們從電影、音樂或互聯網借用字詞時，英語可以影響其他語言。"},{"en":"If one language has global media power, its expressions may spread widely.","zh":"如果一種語言有全球媒體力量，其表達可能廣泛擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes language contact and outside influence.","zh":"這個片語描述語言接觸和外來影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"borrow words and expressions from","meaning":"從……借用字詞和表達","examples":[{"en":"Many languages borrow words and expressions from English.","zh":"許多語言從英語借用字詞和表達。"},{"en":"To borrow words and expressions from a language means to adopt them into another language.","zh":"To borrow words and expressions from a language 指把它們吸收到另一種語言中。"},{"en":"Cantonese speakers may borrow words from English when talking about technology or business.","zh":"粵語使用者談論科技或商業時，可能從英語借用字詞。"},{"en":"Borrowed expressions spread when people hear them often in media and daily life.","zh":"當人們經常在媒體和日常生活中聽到借用表達，它們就會擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one way languages influence each other.","zh":"這個片語描述語言互相影響的一種方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"why not","meaning":"為何不……","examples":[{"en":"If languages borrow words from English, why not borrow fillers too?","zh":"如果語言會從英語借用字詞，為何不也借用填充語？"},{"en":"Why not is used to suggest that something is reasonable or possible.","zh":"Why not 用來表示某事合理或可能。"},{"en":"If students can learn vocabulary through songs, why not learn pronunciation that way too?","zh":"如果學生可以透過歌曲學詞彙，為何不也用這種方式學發音？"},{"en":"This phrase often challenges people to consider an option they may have ignored.","zh":"這個片語常挑戰人們考慮自己可能忽略的選項。"},{"en":"It makes a suggestion sound simple and logical.","zh":"它令建議聽起來簡單而合乎邏輯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"borrow fillers","meaning":"借用填充語","examples":[{"en":"Languages may borrow fillers from English.","zh":"語言可能從英語借用填充語。"},{"en":"To borrow fillers means to adopt pause words or sounds from another language.","zh":"To borrow fillers 指從另一種語言採用停頓字詞或聲音。"},{"en":"A bilingual speaker may borrow a filler from English while speaking another language.","zh":"雙語說話者說另一語言時，可能從英語借用填充語。"},{"en":"Fillers can spread through films, social media and everyday contact.","zh":"填充語可以透過電影、社交媒體和日常接觸擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase treats fillers as language items that can move between languages.","zh":"這個片語把填充語視為可以在語言之間移動的語言項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"know for a fact whether","meaning":"確切知道是否……","examples":[{"en":"Researchers do not know for a fact whether English is spreading “um”.","zh":"研究人員並不確切知道是否英語正在傳播 “um”。"},{"en":"To know for a fact whether something is true means to know it with clear proof.","zh":"To know for a fact whether something is true 指有清楚證據地知道某事是否真實。"},{"en":"A teacher may suspect cheating, but cannot know for a fact without evidence.","zh":"老師可能懷疑作弊，但沒有證據就不能確切知道。"},{"en":"If researchers lack direct data, they should not claim certainty.","zh":"如果研究人員缺乏直接數據，就不應聲稱確定。"},{"en":"This phrase separates confirmed knowledge from likely explanation.","zh":"這個片語把已確認知識與合理解釋分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"what is actually happening","meaning":"實際上正在發生的事","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are unsure what is actually happening with “um”.","zh":"研究人員不確定 “um” 實際上正在發生甚麼事。"},{"en":"What is actually happening means the real process or situation behind the visible pattern.","zh":"What is actually happening 指可見模式背後的真正過程或情況。"},{"en":"A teacher may see poor marks but still ask what is actually happening in students’ study habits.","zh":"老師可能看見低分，但仍會問學生學習習慣中實際發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"If a trend is visible but its cause is unclear, researchers must investigate further.","zh":"如果趨勢可見但原因不清楚，研究人員必須進一步調查。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for the real explanation, not just surface observation.","zh":"這個片語詢問真正解釋，而不只是表面觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a likely story","meaning":"合理的說法","examples":[{"en":"The idea that English is spreading “um” is a likely story.","zh":"英語正在傳播 “um” 這個想法是一個合理的說法。"},{"en":"A likely story is an explanation that seems reasonable, though it may not be proven.","zh":"Likely story 是看似合理但未必已被證明的解釋。"},{"en":"If many students learned a phrase from the same video, that is a likely story for its sudden popularity.","zh":"如果許多學生從同一影片學到某片語，這就是它突然流行的合理說法。"},{"en":"A likely story can guide research, but it still needs evidence.","zh":"合理說法可以引導研究，但仍需要證據。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a plausible explanation.","zh":"這個片語表示可信的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether each statement agrees with the information in the text.","zh":"考生判斷每項陳述是否與文中資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information means to match what the text says.","zh":"To agree with the information 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the passage says fillers are common, a statement saying they occur often agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說填充語很常見，陳述說它們經常出現就是與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should check the exact meaning before deciding an answer.","zh":"學生作答前應檢查確切意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"given in the text","meaning":"文中提供的","examples":[{"en":"The statements must be checked against the information given in the text.","zh":"這些陳述必須根據文中提供的資料檢查。"},{"en":"Given in the text means provided or stated in the passage.","zh":"Given in the text 指文章中提供或說明的內容。"},{"en":"Students should not answer from general knowledge if the answer must come from information given in the text.","zh":"如果答案必須來自文中提供的資料，學生不應憑常識作答。"},{"en":"If the text gives no detail about a claim, the answer may be NOT GIVEN.","zh":"如果文章沒有提供某主張的細節，答案可能是 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds candidates to rely on the passage.","zh":"這個片語提醒考生依賴文章。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"contradicts the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the text.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文中資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"To contradict the information 指說出與文章內容相反的意思。"},{"en":"If the passage says fillers are common, a statement saying they are rare contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說填充語很常見，陳述說它們罕見就是與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should look for direct opposition, not just different wording.","zh":"學生應尋找直接相反，而不只是不同措辭。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when an answer should be FALSE.","zh":"這個片語用於答案應為 FALSE 的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"“Not Given” means there is no information on this in the text.","zh":"“Not Given” 指文中沒有這方面的相關資料。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"There is no information on this 指文章沒有說明該陳述是真是假。"},{"en":"If a passage discusses fillers but not the speaker’s education level, that detail may be NOT GIVEN.","zh":"如果文章討論填充語但沒有討論說話者教育程度，該細節可能是 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from outside knowledge when the text is silent.","zh":"當文章沒有提及時，學生不應用外部知識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the logic behind NOT GIVEN answers.","zh":"這個片語解釋 NOT GIVEN 答案背後的邏輯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be usually expressed as","meaning":"通常以……表達","examples":[{"en":"Fillers are usually expressed as pauses or short sounds.","zh":"填充語通常以停頓或短聲音表達。"},{"en":"To be usually expressed as something means to commonly appear in that form.","zh":"To be usually expressed as something 指通常以某種形式出現。"},{"en":"Nervousness may be expressed as silence, fast speech or repeated fillers.","zh":"緊張可能以沉默、快速說話或重複填充語表達。"},{"en":"If hesitation is expressed as “um”, listeners know the speaker is still thinking.","zh":"如果猶豫以 “um” 表達，聽者知道說話者仍在思考。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an idea with the form it takes.","zh":"這個片語把某想法與它採取的形式連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have no linguistic meaning","meaning":"沒有語言學意義","examples":[{"en":"Some fillers may have no clear linguistic meaning.","zh":"一些填充語可能沒有清楚語言學意義。"},{"en":"To have no linguistic meaning means not to carry ordinary word meaning in the language system.","zh":"To have no linguistic meaning 指在語言系統中不帶普通字詞意思。"},{"en":"“Uh” may help a speaker pause, but it does not name an object or action.","zh":"“Uh” 可以幫助說話者停頓，但它不命名物件或動作。"},{"en":"Even without linguistic meaning, a filler can still have a conversational function.","zh":"即使沒有語言學意義，填充語仍可以有對話功能。"},{"en":"This phrase separates meaning in grammar from usefulness in speech.","zh":"這個片語把文法中的意思與口語中的用途分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have a purpose","meaning":"有用途","examples":[{"en":"Fillers may have a purpose even if they are not meaningful words.","zh":"填充語即使不是有意義字詞，也可能有用途。"},{"en":"To have a purpose means to serve a function or be useful for something.","zh":"To have a purpose 指發揮功能或對某事有用。"},{"en":"A pause may have a purpose if it gives the speaker time to think.","zh":"如果停頓給說話者時間思考，它可能有用途。"},{"en":"Fillers can help manage conversation by showing the speaker wants to continue.","zh":"填充語可以透過顯示說話者想繼續來幫助管理對話。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds learners that something can be useful even if it looks unnecessary.","zh":"這個片語提醒學習者，某事即使看似不必要，也可以有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"vary across cultures","meaning":"因文化而異","examples":[{"en":"Fillers vary across cultures.","zh":"填充語因文化而異。"},{"en":"To vary across cultures means to be different in different societies or language communities.","zh":"To vary across cultures 指在不同社會或語言社群中有所不同。"},{"en":"Table manners vary across cultures, so travellers should observe before judging.","zh":"餐桌禮儀因文化而異，所以旅客應先觀察再判斷。"},{"en":"If fillers vary across cultures, learners need exposure to real speech, not only textbooks.","zh":"如果填充語因文化而異，學習者需要接觸真實口語，而不只是教科書。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights cultural difference in language behaviour.","zh":"這個片語突出語言行為中的文化差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be uncommon in everyday language","meaning":"在日常語言中並不常見","examples":[{"en":"The statement claims that fillers are uncommon in everyday language.","zh":"該陳述聲稱填充語在日常語言中並不常見。"},{"en":"To be uncommon in everyday language means to appear rarely in normal daily speech.","zh":"To be uncommon in everyday language 指在正常日常說話中很少出現。"},{"en":"Very formal phrases may be uncommon in everyday language because people prefer simpler words.","zh":"非常正式的片語可能在日常語言中並不常見，因為人們較喜歡簡單字詞。"},{"en":"If fillers are actually frequent in conversation, calling them uncommon would contradict the text.","zh":"如果填充語實際上在對話中很頻繁，說它們不常見就會與文章相矛盾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that ordinary speakers do not use often.","zh":"這個片語描述普通說話者不常使用的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"more often than older speakers","meaning":"比年長說話者更常","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether younger speakers use a filler more often than older speakers.","zh":"題目問年輕說話者是否比年長說話者更常使用某填充語。"},{"en":"More often than older speakers means with greater frequency than people from older age groups.","zh":"More often than older speakers 指比年長年齡組別的人更頻繁。"},{"en":"Younger speakers may use new slang more often than older speakers.","zh":"年輕說話者可能比年長說話者更常使用新俚語。"},{"en":"If young people use a form more often, they may be leading a language change.","zh":"如果年輕人更常使用某形式，他們可能正在引領語言變化。"},{"en":"This phrase compares speech frequency by age group.","zh":"這個片語按年齡組別比較說話頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"過去","examples":[{"en":"In the past, linguists had a different view of fillers.","zh":"過去，語言學家對填充語有不同看法。"},{"en":"In the past means before the present time.","zh":"In the past 指在現在之前。"},{"en":"In the past, students used dictionaries more often than translation apps.","zh":"過去，學生比現在更常使用字典，而不是翻譯應用程式。"},{"en":"Research can change ideas that people held in the past.","zh":"研究可以改變人們過去持有的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts earlier beliefs with current understanding.","zh":"這個片語把早前信念與現有理解作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be related to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Fillers may be related to the amount of time a speaker hesitates.","zh":"填充語可能與說話者猶豫的時間長短有關。"},{"en":"To be related to something means to have a connection with it.","zh":"To be related to something 指與某事有聯繫。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be related to sleeping too late.","zh":"學生疲倦可能與睡得太晚有關。"},{"en":"If filler choice is related to hesitation time, longer pauses may predict different fillers.","zh":"如果填充語選擇與猶豫時間有關，較長停頓可能預示不同填充語。"},{"en":"This phrase shows connection, but not always direct cause.","zh":"這個片語顯示聯繫，但不一定是直接原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the amount of time","meaning":"時間長短","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to the amount of time a speaker hesitates.","zh":"該陳述指說話者猶豫的時間長短。"},{"en":"The amount of time means how long something lasts.","zh":"The amount of time 指某事持續多久。"},{"en":"The amount of time students spend reading can affect their vocabulary.","zh":"學生花在閱讀上的時間長短可以影響詞彙量。"},{"en":"If a speaker hesitates for a long time, listeners may notice the pause more clearly.","zh":"如果說話者猶豫很久，聽者可能更清楚注意到停頓。"},{"en":"This phrase measures duration.","zh":"這個片語量度持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hesitate","meaning":"猶豫；停頓","examples":[{"en":"A speaker may hesitate before choosing the next word.","zh":"說話者可能在選擇下一個字前猶豫。"},{"en":"To hesitate means to pause because you are unsure, nervous or still thinking.","zh":"To hesitate 指因不確定、緊張或仍在思考而停頓。"},{"en":"A student may hesitate before answering a difficult question.","zh":"學生回答困難問題前可能會猶豫。"},{"en":"Hesitation can create pauses, fillers and unfinished sentences.","zh":"猶豫可以造成停頓、填充語和未完成句子。"},{"en":"This word describes a short delay before action or speech.","zh":"這個詞描述行動或說話前的短暫延遲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"during a coffee break","meaning":"在咖啡小休期間","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions researchers chatting during a coffee break.","zh":"題目提到研究人員在咖啡小休期間聊天。"},{"en":"During a coffee break means in a short rest period when people stop work and drink coffee or relax.","zh":"During a coffee break 指人們停止工作、喝咖啡或放鬆的短暫休息時間。"},{"en":"Teachers may discuss student progress during a coffee break.","zh":"老師可能在咖啡小休期間討論學生進度。"},{"en":"Informal conversations during breaks can sometimes lead to useful research ideas.","zh":"小休期間的非正式對話有時可以帶來有用研究想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a relaxed moment between work sessions.","zh":"這個片語描述工作時段之間的輕鬆時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"chat with","meaning":"與……聊天","examples":[{"en":"Liberman may have chatted with other researchers about his finding.","zh":"Liberman 可能與其他研究人員聊天，談及他的發現。"},{"en":"To chat with someone means to talk informally with them.","zh":"To chat with someone 指與某人非正式地交談。"},{"en":"Students often chat with friends before class starts.","zh":"學生常在上課前與朋友聊天。"},{"en":"A casual chat with a colleague can help develop a new idea.","zh":"與同事的一次隨意聊天可以幫助發展新想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relaxed conversation, not a formal presentation.","zh":"這個片語描述輕鬆對話，而不是正式匯報。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a small group of researchers","meaning":"一小群研究人員","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to a small group of researchers.","zh":"該陳述指一小群研究人員。"},{"en":"A small group of researchers means a limited number of people studying a question together.","zh":"A small group of researchers 指一小群一起研究某問題的人。"},{"en":"A small group of researchers may compare recordings from different countries.","zh":"一小群研究人員可能比較來自不同國家的錄音。"},{"en":"Small groups can move quickly, but their findings may need larger studies later.","zh":"小團隊可以迅速行動，但其發現之後可能需要更大型研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the size and role of a research team.","zh":"這個片語描述研究團隊的大小和角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"age and gender differences","meaning":"年齡和性別差異","examples":[{"en":"Researchers discuss age and gender differences in the use of fillers.","zh":"研究人員討論填充語使用中的年齡和性別差異。"},{"en":"Age and gender differences are patterns that vary according to how old people are and whether they are male or female.","zh":"Age and gender differences 是按人們年齡和性別而變化的模式。"},{"en":"A school may find age and gender differences in reading preferences.","zh":"學校可能在閱讀偏好中發現年齡和性別差異。"},{"en":"If filler use changes by age and gender, speech habits may reflect social identity.","zh":"如果填充語使用隨年齡和性別改變，說話習慣可能反映社會身份。"},{"en":"This phrase describes comparison across age groups and genders.","zh":"這個片語描述跨年齡組別和性別的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be related to","meaning":"與……相關","examples":[{"en":"Age and gender differences may be related to “um” and “uh”.","zh":"年齡和性別差異可能與 “um” 和 “uh” 相關。"},{"en":"To be related to something means to have some connection with it.","zh":"To be related to something 指與某事有某種聯繫。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may be related to how much speaking practice they receive.","zh":"學生自信可能與他得到多少口語練習相關。"},{"en":"If age and gender are related to filler choice, researchers can compare groups more carefully.","zh":"如果年齡和性別與填充語選擇相關，研究人員可以更仔細比較群體。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a link that may need further explanation.","zh":"這個片語顯示可能需要進一步解釋的聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"考生為每條問題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option that best fits the question.","zh":"To choose the correct letter 指選擇最符合題目的答案選項。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice task, students may choose A, B, C or D.","zh":"在多項選擇題中，學生可能選 A、B、C 或 D。"},{"en":"Candidates should read all options before choosing the correct letter.","zh":"考生應閱讀所有選項後才選出正確字母。"},{"en":"This phrase is a standard instruction in exam questions.","zh":"這個片語是考試題中的標準指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"give the speaker time to think","meaning":"給說話者時間思考","examples":[{"en":"Fillers can give the speaker time to think.","zh":"填充語可以給說話者時間思考。"},{"en":"To give the speaker time to think means to create a short moment for planning the next words.","zh":"To give the speaker time to think 指創造短暫時刻來計劃接下來的字詞。"},{"en":"Saying “well” before an answer can give the speaker time to think.","zh":"回答前說 “well” 可以給說話者時間思考。"},{"en":"This extra moment may help the speaker avoid saying something unclear.","zh":"這額外一刻可能幫助說話者避免說出不清楚的內容。"},{"en":"This phrase explains one practical function of fillers.","zh":"這個片語解釋填充語的一個實際功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"phrases that are restated","meaning":"被重新說出的片語","examples":[{"en":"Fillers can include phrases that are restated.","zh":"填充語可以包括被重新說出的片語。"},{"en":"Phrases that are restated are phrases repeated or said again in a slightly different way.","zh":"Phrases that are restated 是被重複或以稍微不同方式再說一次的片語。"},{"en":"A speaker may say, “I mean, I mean we should wait,” restating the phrase while thinking.","zh":"說話者可能說：“I mean, I mean we should wait”，在思考時重新說出片語。"},{"en":"Restated phrases can happen when the speaker repairs or clarifies the message.","zh":"當說話者修正或澄清訊息時，可能出現重新說出的片語。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repetition used during real-time speech.","zh":"這個片語描述即時口語中的重複。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"used across cultures","meaning":"跨文化使用","examples":[{"en":"Fillers are used across cultures.","zh":"填充語被跨文化使用。"},{"en":"Used across cultures means found or practised in many different cultural groups.","zh":"Used across cultures 指在許多不同文化群體中被發現或實踐。"},{"en":"Greetings are used across cultures, but their forms differ.","zh":"問候語跨文化使用，但形式各有不同。"},{"en":"If fillers are used across cultures, hesitation in speech is not limited to one language.","zh":"如果填充語跨文化使用，說話中的猶豫就不限於一種語言。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights widespread use with cultural variation.","zh":"這個片語突出廣泛使用以及文化差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"popular with the media","meaning":"受傳媒歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Fillers are not usually popular with the media.","zh":"填充語通常不受傳媒歡迎。"},{"en":"Popular with the media means liked, accepted or commonly used in television, film or news production.","zh":"Popular with the media 指被電視、電影或新聞製作喜歡、接受或常用。"},{"en":"Short, clear statements are often popular with the media because they are easy to edit.","zh":"短而清晰的說法常受傳媒歡迎，因為容易剪輯。"},{"en":"Fillers may be removed because edited media prefers smooth speech.","zh":"填充語可能被移除，因為經剪輯媒體偏好流暢說話。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what media producers tend to accept or avoid.","zh":"這個片語描述媒體製作人傾向接受或避免甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"it had originally seemed to","meaning":"原本在……看來","examples":[{"en":"It had originally seemed to Liberman that “um” came before a longer pause.","zh":"原本在 Liberman 看來，“um” 出現在較長停頓之前。"},{"en":"It had originally seemed to someone means that person first believed or thought something appeared true.","zh":"It had originally seemed to someone 指某人最初相信或覺得某事似乎真實。"},{"en":"It had originally seemed to the teacher that the test was easy, but many students struggled.","zh":"原本在老師看來，測驗很容易，但許多學生覺得吃力。"},{"en":"Later evidence can change what originally seemed true.","zh":"後來的證據可以改變原本看似真實的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an earlier impression that may be revised.","zh":"這個片語引出可能被修正的早期印象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be followed by","meaning":"後面接着……","examples":[{"en":"“Uh” may be followed by a shorter pause than “um”.","zh":"“Uh” 後面接着的停頓可能比 “um” 短。"},{"en":"To be followed by something means to have that thing come after it.","zh":"To be followed by something 指某事之後接着另一事。"},{"en":"In a timetable, English may be followed by Maths.","zh":"在時間表中，英文課後面可能接着數學課。"},{"en":"If a filler is followed by a long pause, it may signal deeper planning.","zh":"如果填充語後面接着長停頓，它可能表示較深層構思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sequence or order.","zh":"這個片語描述先後次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a less significant pause","meaning":"較不重要的停頓","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to a less significant pause.","zh":"該選項指較不重要的停頓。"},{"en":"A less significant pause is a pause that seems shorter, lighter or less important in speech planning.","zh":"Less significant pause 是在說話構思中較短、較輕或較不重要的停頓。"},{"en":"A speaker may take a less significant pause before adding a small example.","zh":"說話者在加入小例子前，可能作出較不重要的停頓。"},{"en":"If the pause is less significant, listeners may barely notice it.","zh":"如果停頓較不重要，聽者可能幾乎沒有注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase compares pause importance, not just pause length.","zh":"這個片語比較停頓的重要性，而不只是停頓長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a shorter pause","meaning":"較短的停頓","examples":[{"en":"Liberman once thought “uh” was followed by a shorter pause than “um”.","zh":"Liberman 曾認為 “uh” 後接的停頓比 “um” 較短。"},{"en":"A shorter pause is a pause that lasts less time.","zh":"Shorter pause 是持續時間較少的停頓。"},{"en":"A confident speaker may use shorter pauses when answering familiar questions.","zh":"自信的說話者回答熟悉問題時，可能使用較短停頓。"},{"en":"Shorter pauses can make speech sound faster and more fluent.","zh":"較短停頓可以令說話聽起來更快和更流暢。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the duration of two pauses.","zh":"這個片語比較兩個停頓的持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a longer pause","meaning":"較長的停頓","examples":[{"en":"“Um” was thought to come before a longer pause.","zh":"“Um” 被認為出現在較長停頓之前。"},{"en":"A longer pause is a pause that lasts more time than another pause.","zh":"Longer pause 是比另一停頓持續更久的停頓。"},{"en":"A student may take a longer pause before answering a difficult question.","zh":"學生回答困難問題前，可能作出較長停頓。"},{"en":"Longer pauses can show hesitation, planning or careful thinking.","zh":"較長停頓可以顯示猶豫、構思或謹慎思考。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a pause with greater duration.","zh":"這個片語描述持續時間較長的停頓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"contrary to what","meaning":"與……相反","examples":[{"en":"Contrary to what linguists used to think, speaker identity may matter.","zh":"與語言學家過去所想相反，說話者身份可能重要。"},{"en":"Contrary to what means opposite to an earlier belief, claim or expectation.","zh":"Contrary to what 指與早前信念、主張或預期相反。"},{"en":"Contrary to what many students think, good writing often uses simple sentences clearly.","zh":"與許多學生所想相反，好的寫作常清楚使用簡單句子。"},{"en":"If new evidence contradicts old views, researchers must change their explanation.","zh":"如果新證據與舊觀點相矛盾，研究人員必須改變解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces contrast with a previous idea.","zh":"這個片語引出與先前想法的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the choice of filler","meaning":"填充語的選擇","examples":[{"en":"The choice of filler may depend on the speaker.","zh":"填充語的選擇可能取決於說話者。"},{"en":"The choice of filler means which filler a speaker uses, such as “uh” or “um”.","zh":"Choice of filler 指說話者使用哪個填充語，例如 “uh” 或 “um”。"},{"en":"One speaker’s choice of filler may sound natural in their community but unusual elsewhere.","zh":"一位說話者的填充語選擇在其社群中可能自然，但在其他地方不尋常。"},{"en":"If age and gender affect filler choice, speech can reveal social patterns.","zh":"如果年齡和性別影響填充語選擇，說話可以揭示社會模式。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on selecting one filler rather than another.","zh":"這個片語集中於選擇一個填充語而不是另一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"depend on","meaning":"取決於","examples":[{"en":"The choice of filler may depend on the characteristics of the speaker.","zh":"填充語的選擇可能取決於說話者的特徵。"},{"en":"Depend on means be influenced or decided by something.","zh":"Depend on 指受某事影響或由某事決定。"},{"en":"A student’s answer may depend on how carefully they read the question.","zh":"學生答案可能取決於他多仔細閱讀題目。"},{"en":"If filler choice depends on age, young and old speakers may show different patterns.","zh":"如果填充語選擇取決於年齡，年輕和年長說話者可能顯示不同模式。"},{"en":"This phrase links a result to the factor that shapes it.","zh":"這個片語把結果與塑造它的因素連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"characteristics of the speaker","meaning":"說話者的特徵","examples":[{"en":"Age and gender are characteristics of the speaker.","zh":"年齡和性別是說話者的特徵。"},{"en":"Characteristics of the speaker are features such as age, gender, accent, background and community.","zh":"Characteristics of the speaker 是年齡、性別、口音、背景和社群等特徵。"},{"en":"A listener may notice characteristics of the speaker from pronunciation and word choice.","zh":"聽者可能從發音和用字中注意到說話者的特徵。"},{"en":"If filler use changes with speaker characteristics, language reflects social identity.","zh":"如果填充語使用隨說話者特徵改變，語言就反映社會身份。"},{"en":"This phrase describes personal or social features of the person speaking.","zh":"這個片語描述說話人的個人或社會特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have nothing to do with","meaning":"與……無關","examples":[{"en":"The option claims that filler choice has nothing to do with sex.","zh":"該選項聲稱填充語選擇與性別無關。"},{"en":"To have nothing to do with something means to have no connection with it.","zh":"To have nothing to do with something 指與某事沒有關係。"},{"en":"A student’s accent has nothing to do with how intelligent they are.","zh":"學生的口音與他的智力無關。"},{"en":"If research shows gender differences, saying filler choice has nothing to do with sex would be wrong.","zh":"如果研究顯示性別差異，說填充語選擇與性別無關就是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly denies a relationship.","zh":"這個片語強烈否定關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"only matter to","meaning":"只對……重要","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that filler choice only matters to older people.","zh":"該選項暗示填充語選擇只對年長人士重要。"},{"en":"Only matter to a group means be important only for that group and not others.","zh":"Only matter to a group 指只對某群體重要，而不對其他人重要。"},{"en":"Exam rules do not only matter to weak students; they matter to everyone.","zh":"考試規則不只對弱學生重要；它們對每個人都重要。"},{"en":"If filler choice varies across all ages, it does not only matter to older people.","zh":"如果填充語選擇在所有年齡層都有差異，它就不只對年長人士重要。"},{"en":"This phrase limits importance to one group.","zh":"這個片語把重要性限制於某一群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"it is still a puzzle why","meaning":"為何……仍是謎團","examples":[{"en":"It is still a puzzle why this language change is so widespread.","zh":"為何這項語言變化如此廣泛，仍是謎團。"},{"en":"It is still a puzzle why means the reason remains difficult to explain.","zh":"It is still a puzzle why 指原因仍難以解釋。"},{"en":"It is still a puzzle why some students understand grammar in class but forget it in writing.","zh":"為何有些學生在課堂上理解文法，但寫作時忘記，仍是謎團。"},{"en":"If a trend spreads across countries without a clear cause, it remains puzzling.","zh":"如果一種趨勢無明顯原因地跨國擴散，它仍令人困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an unanswered question.","zh":"這個片語引出尚未解答的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a specific language change","meaning":"一項具體語言變化","examples":[{"en":"The use of “um” may represent a specific language change.","zh":"“um” 的使用可能代表一項具體語言變化。"},{"en":"A specific language change is one particular shift in how people speak or write.","zh":"Specific language change 是人們說話或書寫方式中的某一項特定轉變。"},{"en":"The rise of a new slang word can be a specific language change in a school community.","zh":"新俚語興起可以是一個學校社群中的具體語言變化。"},{"en":"If one filler replaces another, that is a focused change in usage.","zh":"如果一個填充語取代另一個，那就是用法上的明確轉變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to one identifiable change, not language change in general.","zh":"這個片語指一項可識別的變化，而不是泛指語言變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"so widespread","meaning":"如此廣泛","examples":[{"en":"The spread of “um” is so widespread that researchers find it puzzling.","zh":"“um” 的擴散如此廣泛，以致研究人員覺得困惑。"},{"en":"So widespread means appearing in many places, groups or situations.","zh":"So widespread 指出現在許多地方、群體或情況中。"},{"en":"Smartphone use is so widespread that schools need clear rules for it.","zh":"智能手機使用如此廣泛，以致學校需要清晰規則。"},{"en":"If a speech habit is so widespread, it may be shaped by media, contact or social change.","zh":"如果某說話習慣如此廣泛，它可能受媒體、接觸或社會變化影響。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises how broadly something has spread.","zh":"這個片語強調某事擴散得多廣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be comparable","meaning":"可作比較；相近","examples":[{"en":"Fruehwald thinks “um” and “uh” are comparable.","zh":"Fruehwald 認為 “um” 和 “uh” 可作比較。"},{"en":"To be comparable means to be similar enough to be compared fairly.","zh":"To be comparable 指相似到可以公平比較。"},{"en":"Two exam results are comparable only if the tests have similar difficulty.","zh":"只有在測驗難度相近時，兩個考試結果才可作比較。"},{"en":"If two fillers have similar functions, researchers can compare their use.","zh":"如果兩個填充語功能相似，研究人員可以比較它們的使用。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests meaningful similarity between two things.","zh":"這個片語暗示兩件事之間有有意義的相似性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be preferred by","meaning":"較受……偏好","examples":[{"en":"“Um” is preferred by women and young people.","zh":"“Um” 較受女性和年輕人偏好。"},{"en":"To be preferred by a group means that group chooses it more often or likes it more.","zh":"To be preferred by a group 指該群體更常選擇或更喜歡它。"},{"en":"Online homework may be preferred by students who travel long distances.","zh":"網上功課可能較受通勤距離長的學生偏好。"},{"en":"If “um” is preferred by young speakers, it may spread through younger networks.","zh":"如果 “um” 較受年輕說話者偏好，它可能透過年輕人網絡擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preference from the perspective of a group.","zh":"這個片語從群體角度描述偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"normal changes","meaning":"正常變化","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to normal changes in language.","zh":"題目提及語言中的正常變化。"},{"en":"Normal changes are ordinary developments that happen naturally over time.","zh":"Normal changes 是隨時間自然發生的普通發展。"},{"en":"New words entering everyday speech are normal changes in a living language.","zh":"新詞進入日常說話是活語言中的正常變化。"},{"en":"If younger speakers adopt new forms, language may change without anyone planning it.","zh":"如果年輕說話者採用新形式，語言可能在沒有人計劃下改變。"},{"en":"This phrase makes change sound natural rather than alarming.","zh":"這個片語令變化聽起來自然，而不是令人驚慌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"go through","meaning":"經歷","examples":[{"en":"All languages go through changes over time.","zh":"所有語言都會隨時間經歷變化。"},{"en":"To go through something means to experience a process or period.","zh":"To go through something 指經歷一個過程或時期。"},{"en":"Students go through many stages before they become confident speakers.","zh":"學生成為自信說話者前，會經歷許多階段。"},{"en":"Languages go through change because each generation uses them slightly differently.","zh":"語言會經歷變化，因為每一代人使用它們的方式略有不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes experiencing a process from beginning to end or over time.","zh":"這個片語描述從開始到結束或隨時間經歷某過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"as time goes by","meaning":"隨着時間過去","examples":[{"en":"Languages change as time goes by.","zh":"語言隨着時間過去而改變。"},{"en":"As time goes by means as time passes.","zh":"As time goes by 指隨着時間流逝。"},{"en":"As time goes by, students often become more comfortable speaking in English.","zh":"隨着時間過去，學生通常會更自在地用英語說話。"},{"en":"Habits can change gradually as time goes by, even without conscious effort.","zh":"習慣可以隨着時間過去逐漸改變，即使沒有刻意努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow development over time.","zh":"這個片語描述隨時間慢慢發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"play a more important role than","meaning":"比……發揮更重要作用","examples":[{"en":"Women may play a more important role than men in language change.","zh":"女性在語言變化中可能比男性發揮更重要作用。"},{"en":"To play a more important role than another group means to have greater influence in a process.","zh":"To play a more important role than another group 指在某過程中有更大影響力。"},{"en":"Parents may play a more important role than tutors in building a child’s daily reading habit.","zh":"在建立孩子日常閱讀習慣方面，家長可能比補習老師發揮更重要作用。"},{"en":"If one group spreads a new form faster, it may shape the direction of change.","zh":"如果一個群體更快擴散新形式，它可能塑造變化方向。"},{"en":"This phrase compares influence between two groups.","zh":"這個片語比較兩個群體之間的影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the fact that","meaning":"……這一事實","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the fact that “um” is used more than “uh”.","zh":"題目問到 “um” 比 “uh” 更常被使用這一事實。"},{"en":"The fact that introduces a specific point that is being treated as true or important.","zh":"The fact that 用來引出被視為真實或重要的具體重點。"},{"en":"The fact that students ask many questions can show curiosity, not weakness.","zh":"學生問很多問題這一事實可以顯示好奇心，而不是弱點。"},{"en":"In reading questions, this phrase often points to the exact idea being tested.","zh":"在閱讀題中，這個片語常指向正在考核的確切想法。"},{"en":"This phrase turns a whole clause into a topic for discussion.","zh":"這個片語把整個子句變成討論題目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be used more than","meaning":"比……更常被使用","examples":[{"en":"“Um” is used more than “uh” by women and younger people.","zh":"“Um” 被女性和年輕人比 “uh” 更常使用。"},{"en":"To be used more than something means to appear or be chosen more frequently than it.","zh":"To be used more than something 指比另一事物更頻繁出現或被選用。"},{"en":"In text messages, short forms may be used more than full formal phrases.","zh":"在短訊中，簡寫可能比完整正式片語更常被使用。"},{"en":"If one filler is used more than another, it may be becoming more common.","zh":"如果一個填充語比另一個更常被使用，它可能正變得更常見。"},{"en":"This phrase compares frequency of use.","zh":"這個片語比較使用頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"have different meanings","meaning":"有不同意思","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether “um” and “uh” have different meanings.","zh":"該選項問 “um” 和 “uh” 是否有不同意思。"},{"en":"To have different meanings means to express different ideas or functions.","zh":"To have different meanings 指表達不同想法或功能。"},{"en":"“Borrow” and “lend” have different meanings, so students must choose carefully.","zh":"“Borrow” 和 “lend” 有不同意思，所以學生必須小心選擇。"},{"en":"If two fillers have the same function, their difference may be social rather than semantic.","zh":"如果兩個填充語功能相同，它們的差異可能是社會性的，而不是語義上的。"},{"en":"This phrase compares meaning between two forms.","zh":"這個片語比較兩種形式之間的意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"just a coincidence","meaning":"只是巧合","examples":[{"en":"Fruehwald treats the preference for “um” as just a coincidence.","zh":"Fruehwald 把對 “um” 的偏好視為只是巧合。"},{"en":"Just a coincidence means something happened by chance, without a meaningful cause.","zh":"Just a coincidence 指某事偶然發生，沒有有意義的原因。"},{"en":"If two students wear the same colour by accident, it may be just a coincidence.","zh":"如果兩名學生碰巧穿同一顏色，那可能只是巧合。"},{"en":"Researchers must decide whether a pattern is meaningful or just a coincidence.","zh":"研究人員必須判斷某模式有意義，還是只是巧合。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that an event may not need a deeper explanation.","zh":"這個片語暗示某事件可能不需要更深層解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 69 - SPEECH DYSFLUENCY AND POPULAR FILLERS.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 70":[{"front":"the beginnings of","meaning":"……的起源","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains the beginnings of art therapy.","zh":"文章解釋藝術治療的起源。"},{"en":"The beginnings of something are its early stages or origins.","zh":"the beginnings of something 指某事物的早期階段或起源。"},{"en":"A history lesson may explain the beginnings of a city, a school, or a social movement.","zh":"歷史課可能解釋一個城市、一所學校或一場社會運動的起源。"},{"en":"Understanding the beginnings of a profession helps us see why it developed.","zh":"理解一門專業的起源，有助我們看見它為何發展。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when tracing how something first started.","zh":"這個片語適用於追溯某事物如何開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"art therapy","meaning":"藝術治療","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy became a profession in the mid-20th century.","zh":"藝術治療在20世紀中期成為一門專業。"},{"en":"Art therapy is a form of therapy that uses art-making to support emotional, mental, or physical wellbeing.","zh":"art therapy 指使用藝術創作來支援情緒、精神或身體健康的治療形式。"},{"en":"A child who finds it hard to speak about fear may express feelings through art therapy.","zh":"難以說出恐懼的孩子，可能透過藝術治療表達感受。"},{"en":"Art therapy can help patients explore stress, trauma, or illness in a safer way.","zh":"藝術治療可以幫助病人以較安全的方式探索壓力、創傷或疾病。"},{"en":"It is therapy through creative expression, not simply an ordinary art lesson.","zh":"它是透過創意表達進行的治療，而不只是普通藝術課。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a relative newcomer to","meaning":"在……中相對較新的事物","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy is a relative newcomer to the therapeutic field.","zh":"藝術治療在治療領域中是相對較新的事物。"},{"en":"A relative newcomer to a field is something that has joined or developed more recently than others.","zh":"a relative newcomer to a field 指比同領域其他事物較近期加入或發展的東西。"},{"en":"Online counselling is a relative newcomer to many traditional healthcare systems.","zh":"網上輔導在許多傳統醫療系統中是相對較新的事物。"},{"en":"Because art therapy developed later than older therapies, its professional rules took time to form.","zh":"因為藝術治療比一些較古老療法發展得晚，其專業規則需要時間形成。"},{"en":"The phrase compares one thing with older, more established things in the same area.","zh":"這個片語把某事物與同領域中較早確立的事物比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"therapeutic field","meaning":"治療領域","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy is a relative newcomer to the therapeutic field.","zh":"藝術治療在治療領域中是相對較新的事物。"},{"en":"The therapeutic field includes professions and practices that help people recover, cope, or improve wellbeing.","zh":"therapeutic field 包括幫助人康復、應對困難或改善健康的專業和做法。"},{"en":"Counselling, physiotherapy, speech therapy, and art therapy all belong to the therapeutic field.","zh":"輔導、物理治療、言語治療和藝術治療都屬於治療領域。"},{"en":"As new needs appear, the therapeutic field may develop new methods of support.","zh":"隨着新需要出現，治療領域可能發展出新的支援方法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the broad area of treatment and healing.","zh":"這個片語指治療與康復的廣泛範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as a profession","meaning":"作為一門專業","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy as a profession began in the mid-20th century.","zh":"藝術治療作為一門專業始於20世紀中期。"},{"en":"As a profession means as a recognised job or specialised career with training and standards.","zh":"as a profession 指作為一份受承認、具專門訓練和標準的職業。"},{"en":"Teaching as a profession requires more than knowing the subject; it also requires training.","zh":"教學作為一門專業，不只是懂得科目，還需要訓練。"},{"en":"When art therapy became a profession, practitioners needed clearer roles and qualifications.","zh":"當藝術治療成為一門專業，從業者需要更清楚的角色和資格。"},{"en":"The phrase separates casual practice from formal professional work.","zh":"這個片語把非正式實踐與正式專業工作區分開來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the mid-20th century","meaning":"在20世紀中期","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy as a profession began in the mid-20th century.","zh":"藝術治療作為一門專業始於20世紀中期。"},{"en":"In the mid-20th century means around the middle decades of the 1900s.","zh":"in the mid-20th century 指大約20世紀中間的幾十年。"},{"en":"Many modern social services expanded in the mid-20th century after major wars and reforms.","zh":"許多現代社會服務在重大戰爭和改革後於20世紀中期擴展。"},{"en":"If a profession began in the mid-20th century, it is relatively modern compared with medicine or law.","zh":"如果一門專業始於20世紀中期，相比醫學或法律，它就相對現代。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a historical time period, not an exact year.","zh":"這個片語給出歷史時期，而不是準確年份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"arise independently","meaning":"獨立出現；獨立興起","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy arose independently in different countries.","zh":"藝術治療在不同國家獨立興起。"},{"en":"Arise independently means develop separately without being directly copied from one single source.","zh":"arise independently 指分開發展，而不是直接從單一來源複製而來。"},{"en":"Similar school rules may arise independently in different countries because students face similar problems.","zh":"相似校規可能在不同國家獨立出現，因為學生面對相似問題。"},{"en":"If a practice arises independently in several places, it may be responding to a shared need.","zh":"如果某做法在多地獨立興起，它可能是在回應共同需要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses separate origins.","zh":"這個片語強調分開的起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"English-speaking countries","meaning":"英語國家","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy developed in English-speaking countries and European countries.","zh":"藝術治療在英語國家和歐洲國家發展。"},{"en":"English-speaking countries are countries where English is widely used in public life, education, or professional work.","zh":"English-speaking countries 指英語在公共生活、教育或專業工作中廣泛使用的國家。"},{"en":"Students may study in English-speaking countries to improve language and gain overseas experience.","zh":"學生可能到英語國家讀書，以改善語言和獲得海外經驗。"},{"en":"If a profession develops in English-speaking countries, its early literature may be written in English.","zh":"如果一門專業在英語國家發展，其早期文獻可能以英文寫成。"},{"en":"The phrase groups countries by language use.","zh":"這個片語按語言使用來歸類國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"European countries","meaning":"歐洲國家","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy arose independently in European countries.","zh":"藝術治療在歐洲國家獨立興起。"},{"en":"European countries are countries located in Europe, such as France, Germany, Italy, and Britain.","zh":"European countries 指位於歐洲的國家，例如法國、德國、意大利和英國。"},{"en":"A student comparing healthcare systems may study several European countries.","zh":"比較醫療制度的學生可能研究幾個歐洲國家。"},{"en":"When a movement develops in European countries, it may reflect different languages and medical traditions.","zh":"當一場運動在歐洲國家發展，它可能反映不同語言和醫療傳統。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a geographical group of countries.","zh":"這個片語指出一組地理上的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"early practitioners of","meaning":"……的早期從業者","examples":[{"en":"Many early practitioners of art therapy acknowledged outside influences.","zh":"許多藝術治療的早期從業者承認外來影響。"},{"en":"Early practitioners of a field are the first people who worked in or developed that field.","zh":"early practitioners of a field 指最早在某領域工作或發展該領域的人。"},{"en":"Early practitioners of online teaching had to invent methods before clear guidelines existed.","zh":"網上教學的早期從業者在清楚指引出現前，需要自行創造方法。"},{"en":"Because early practitioners shape a profession, their ideas can influence later training.","zh":"因為早期從業者塑造一門專業，他們的想法可以影響後來訓練。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the first generation of people doing a particular practice.","zh":"這個片語指從事某種實踐的第一代人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"acknowledge the influence of","meaning":"承認……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Early practitioners acknowledged the influence of several disciplines.","zh":"早期從業者承認幾個學科的影響。"},{"en":"Acknowledge the influence of means openly recognise that something has shaped one’s ideas or work.","zh":"acknowledge the influence of 指公開承認某事物塑造了自己的思想或工作。"},{"en":"A writer may acknowledge the influence of a teacher who encouraged them to read widely.","zh":"作家可能承認一位鼓勵他廣泛閱讀的老師對自己的影響。"},{"en":"If therapists acknowledge outside influences, they show where their methods came from.","zh":"如果治療師承認外來影響，就能顯示其方法來源。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when discussing intellectual or professional development.","zh":"這個片語適用於討論思想或專業發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a variety of disciplines","meaning":"多種學科","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy was shaped by a variety of disciplines.","zh":"藝術治療受到多種學科塑造。"},{"en":"A variety of disciplines means several different fields of study or professional knowledge.","zh":"a variety of disciplines 指幾個不同研究領域或專業知識範疇。"},{"en":"Public health draws on a variety of disciplines, including medicine, education, and statistics.","zh":"公共衞生借用多種學科，包括醫學、教育和統計學。"},{"en":"When a field uses ideas from many disciplines, it can develop richer methods.","zh":"當一個領域使用多種學科的想法，它可以發展出更豐富的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses mixed academic or professional influences.","zh":"這個片語強調混合的學術或專業影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ranging from…through to…","meaning":"由……一直到……","examples":[{"en":"The influences ranged from psychoanalysis through to aesthetics and education.","zh":"這些影響由精神分析一直到美學和教育。"},{"en":"Ranging from A through to B means covering a wide range from one type to another.","zh":"ranging from A through to B 指涵蓋由一種類型到另一種類型的廣泛範圍。"},{"en":"A school fair may include activities ranging from sports through to music and food stalls.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能包括由體育一直到音樂和食物攤位的活動。"},{"en":"If influences range across many fields, the final practice may become broad and flexible.","zh":"如果影響跨越許多領域，最終做法可能變得廣泛而靈活。"},{"en":"The phrase shows variety across a spectrum.","zh":"這個片語顯示一個範圍內的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"psychoanalysis","meaning":"精神分析","examples":[{"en":"Psychoanalysis influenced some early art therapists.","zh":"精神分析影響了一些早期藝術治療師。"},{"en":"Psychoanalysis is a psychological approach that explores unconscious feelings, memories, and conflicts.","zh":"psychoanalysis 指探索潛意識感受、記憶和衝突的心理學取向。"},{"en":"A therapist using psychoanalysis may ask how childhood experiences affect present behaviour.","zh":"使用精神分析的治療師可能詢問童年經歷如何影響現在行為。"},{"en":"In art therapy, drawings may be examined for hidden feelings or inner conflicts.","zh":"在藝術治療中，繪畫可能被檢視以了解隱藏感受或內在衝突。"},{"en":"The word is often linked with Freud and depth psychology.","zh":"這個詞常與佛洛伊德和深層心理學有關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"aesthetics","meaning":"美學","examples":[{"en":"Aesthetics was one of the disciplines that influenced art therapy.","zh":"美學是影響藝術治療的其中一個學科。"},{"en":"Aesthetics is the study of beauty, artistic experience, and how people respond to art.","zh":"aesthetics 指研究美、藝術經驗以及人們如何回應藝術的學問。"},{"en":"A design student studies aesthetics when learning why colours or shapes feel pleasing.","zh":"設計學生學習顏色或形狀為何令人愉悅時，就是在研究美學。"},{"en":"If therapy uses art, ideas about aesthetics may affect how images are understood.","zh":"如果治療使用藝術，美學觀念可能影響人們如何理解影像。"},{"en":"The word connects art with beauty, perception, and judgement.","zh":"這個詞把藝術與美、感知和判斷連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"early childhood education","meaning":"幼兒教育","examples":[{"en":"Early childhood education also influenced early art therapy practice.","zh":"幼兒教育也影響了早期藝術治療實踐。"},{"en":"Early childhood education is the teaching and care of young children before and during the first years of school.","zh":"early childhood education 指兒童入學前和入學初期的教育與照顧。"},{"en":"Kindergarten teachers use early childhood education methods when helping children learn through play and drawing.","zh":"幼稚園老師透過遊戲和繪畫幫助孩子學習時，就是使用幼兒教育方法。"},{"en":"Because young children often express feelings through pictures, this field influenced therapeutic art practice.","zh":"因為年幼兒童常透過圖畫表達感受，這個領域影響了藝術治療實踐。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to education for very young children.","zh":"這個片語指非常年幼兒童的教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the roots of","meaning":"……的根源","examples":[{"en":"The roots of art as therapy go back to the late 18th century.","zh":"作為治療的藝術，其根源可追溯至18世紀末。"},{"en":"The roots of something are its deeper origins or earliest sources.","zh":"the roots of something 指某事物較深層的起源或最早來源。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain the roots of a festival before students celebrate it.","zh":"老師可能在學生慶祝節日前解釋該節日的根源。"},{"en":"Knowing the roots of a practice helps us understand its present form.","zh":"了解一種做法的根源，有助我們理解其現代形式。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests something began earlier than it may first appear.","zh":"這個片語暗示某事物開始得比表面看來更早。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"art as therapy","meaning":"作為治療的藝術","examples":[{"en":"The roots of art as therapy go back much further than the 20th century.","zh":"作為治療的藝術，其根源遠早於20世紀。"},{"en":"Art as therapy means using art-making itself to support healing or emotional relief.","zh":"art as therapy 指使用藝術創作本身來支持療癒或情緒紓緩。"},{"en":"A patient may use art as therapy when painting helps them cope with fear.","zh":"當繪畫幫助病人應對恐懼時，病人可能把藝術作為治療。"},{"en":"If making art calms the mind and allows expression, it can become therapeutic.","zh":"如果創作藝術能安定心神並容許表達，它就可以變得有治療作用。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on art’s healing function.","zh":"這個片語集中於藝術的療癒功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"go back as far as","meaning":"可追溯至","examples":[{"en":"The roots of art as therapy go back as far as the late 18th century.","zh":"作為治療的藝術，其根源可追溯至18世紀末。"},{"en":"Go back as far as means have origins that reach a particular early time.","zh":"go back as far as 指起源早至某個特定時期。"},{"en":"Some local traditions go back as far as the Qing dynasty.","zh":"有些本地傳統可追溯至清朝。"},{"en":"If an idea goes back centuries, it has a much longer history than expected.","zh":"如果一個想法可追溯數百年，它的歷史就比預期更長。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to trace something back in time.","zh":"這個片語用來把某事物追溯到過去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the late 18th century","meaning":"18世紀末","examples":[{"en":"Arts were used in treatment as early as the late 18th century.","zh":"早在18世紀末，藝術已被用於治療。"},{"en":"The late 18th century means the final decades of the 1700s.","zh":"the late 18th century 指18世紀最後幾十年。"},{"en":"A museum may display objects from the late 18th century to show daily life at that time.","zh":"博物館可能展示18世紀末的物件，以呈現當時日常生活。"},{"en":"If a practice existed in the late 18th century, it has a long historical background.","zh":"如果某做法在18世紀末已存在，它就有悠久歷史背景。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a historical period rather than an exact year.","zh":"這個片語給出歷史時期，而不是準確年份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"moral treatment","meaning":"道德療法","examples":[{"en":"Arts were used in the moral treatment of psychiatric patients.","zh":"藝術被用於精神病患者的道德療法中。"},{"en":"Moral treatment was an older approach to mental healthcare that emphasised humane care, routine, and meaningful activity.","zh":"moral treatment 是較早期的精神健康照護方法，強調人道照顧、規律和有意義活動。"},{"en":"A hospital using moral treatment might encourage patients to garden, read, or make art.","zh":"使用道德療法的醫院可能鼓勵病人園藝、閱讀或創作藝術。"},{"en":"This approach helped move care away from punishment and toward dignity.","zh":"這種方法幫助治療由懲罰轉向尊嚴。"},{"en":"The phrase belongs to the history of psychiatric treatment.","zh":"這個片語屬於精神病治療史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"psychiatric patients","meaning":"精神病患者","examples":[{"en":"Arts were used in the treatment of psychiatric patients.","zh":"藝術被用於精神病患者的治療。"},{"en":"Psychiatric patients are people receiving treatment for mental-health conditions.","zh":"psychiatric patients 指正在接受精神健康疾病治療的人。"},{"en":"Psychiatric patients may need medication, counselling, structured activities, or hospital care.","zh":"精神病患者可能需要藥物、輔導、有結構活動或住院照顧。"},{"en":"If treatment respects patients’ dignity, recovery and trust may improve.","zh":"如果治療尊重病人尊嚴，康復和信任可能改善。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to patients in mental-health care.","zh":"這個片語指精神健康照護中的病人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it wasn’t until…that…","meaning":"直到……才……","examples":[{"en":"It wasn’t until 1942 that Adrian Hill coined the term “art therapy”.","zh":"直到1942年，Adrian Hill 才創造 “art therapy” 一詞。"},{"en":"It wasn’t until A that B means B happened only at time A, later than one might expect.","zh":"It wasn’t until A that B 指 B 直到 A 這個時間才發生，比人們可能預期更遲。"},{"en":"It wasn’t until university that she realised she enjoyed public speaking.","zh":"直到大學，她才意識到自己喜歡公開演說。"},{"en":"This structure emphasises delay or a late turning point.","zh":"這個結構強調延遲或較晚出現的轉捩點。"},{"en":"It is often used when the timing of an event is important.","zh":"當事件發生時間很重要時，這個句式常被使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"British artist","meaning":"英國藝術家","examples":[{"en":"Adrian Hill was the British artist who coined the term “art therapy”.","zh":"Adrian Hill 是創造 “art therapy” 一詞的英國藝術家。"},{"en":"A British artist is an artist from Britain or strongly associated with Britain.","zh":"British artist 指來自英國或與英國密切相關的藝術家。"},{"en":"A British artist may work in painting, sculpture, illustration, design, or performance.","zh":"英國藝術家可能從事繪畫、雕塑、插畫、設計或表演。"},{"en":"When a British artist coined the term, the wording became linked with British medical and artistic history.","zh":"當一位英國藝術家創造該詞，這個用語就與英國醫療和藝術史連結起來。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the person by nationality and profession.","zh":"這個片語以國籍和職業識別人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"coin the term","meaning":"創造／首創……一詞","examples":[{"en":"Adrian Hill coined the term “art therapy” in 1942.","zh":"Adrian Hill 在1942年創造 “art therapy” 一詞。"},{"en":"Coin the term means create or first use a new word or phrase.","zh":"coin the term 指創造或首次使用一個新詞或片語。"},{"en":"A scientist may coin a term when discovering a new process that needs a name.","zh":"科學家發現需要命名的新過程時，可能創造一個術語。"},{"en":"Once a useful term is coined, other professionals can discuss the idea more clearly.","zh":"一旦有用術語被創造，其他專業人士就能更清楚討論該想法。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used in the history of concepts.","zh":"這個片語常用於概念史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"recover from","meaning":"從……康復","examples":[{"en":"Adrian Hill was recovering from tuberculosis in a sanatorium.","zh":"Adrian Hill 當時正在療養院從肺結核康復。"},{"en":"Recover from means gradually become healthy again after illness, injury, or difficulty.","zh":"recover from 指在疾病、受傷或困難後逐漸恢復健康。"},{"en":"A student recovering from flu may return to school slowly and rest more.","zh":"從流感康復的學生可能慢慢返校並多休息。"},{"en":"During recovery, people may need quiet activities that support both body and mind.","zh":"在康復期間，人們可能需要支援身心的安靜活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the process after a problem, not the illness itself.","zh":"這個片語描述問題之後的恢復過程，而不是疾病本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"tuberculosis","meaning":"肺結核","examples":[{"en":"Adrian Hill discovered art’s therapeutic benefits while recovering from tuberculosis.","zh":"Adrian Hill 在從肺結核康復期間發現藝術的治療益處。"},{"en":"Tuberculosis is a serious infectious disease that mainly affects the lungs.","zh":"tuberculosis 指主要影響肺部的嚴重傳染病。"},{"en":"A patient with tuberculosis may need medical treatment and a long period of rest.","zh":"肺結核患者可能需要醫療治療和長時間休息。"},{"en":"Serious illness can make people search for activities that calm the mind.","zh":"嚴重疾病可以令人尋找安定心神的活動。"},{"en":"The word names the disease connected with Hill’s recovery experience.","zh":"這個詞指出與 Hill 康復經歷相關的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sanatorium","meaning":"療養院","examples":[{"en":"Hill was recovering from tuberculosis in a sanatorium.","zh":"Hill 當時正在療養院從肺結核康復。"},{"en":"A sanatorium is a medical place where patients, especially those with long illnesses, rest and recover.","zh":"sanatorium 指讓病人，尤其是長期病患者，休息和康復的醫療場所。"},{"en":"Before modern antibiotics, tuberculosis patients often stayed in sanatoriums for fresh air and rest.","zh":"在現代抗生素出現前，肺結核患者常住在療養院中呼吸新鮮空氣和休息。"},{"en":"A sanatorium provided the quiet setting in which Hill explored drawing and painting.","zh":"療養院提供了安靜環境，讓 Hill 探索素描和繪畫。"},{"en":"The word refers to a recovery institution, not an ordinary hotel.","zh":"這個詞指康復機構，而不是普通酒店。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"therapeutic benefits","meaning":"治療益處","examples":[{"en":"Hill discovered the therapeutic benefits of drawing and painting.","zh":"Hill 發現素描和繪畫的治療益處。"},{"en":"Therapeutic benefits are positive effects that help healing, coping, or wellbeing.","zh":"therapeutic benefits 指有助療癒、應對困難或改善健康的正面效果。"},{"en":"Walking slowly after injury can have therapeutic benefits if it rebuilds strength safely.","zh":"受傷後慢慢步行，如果能安全重建力量，就可能有治療益處。"},{"en":"If drawing reduces anxiety and helps expression, it has therapeutic benefits.","zh":"如果繪畫能減少焦慮並幫助表達，它就有治療益處。"},{"en":"The phrase describes helpful effects in a treatment context.","zh":"這個片語描述治療語境中的有益效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be derived from","meaning":"源自；來自","examples":[{"en":"Therapeutic benefits could be derived from drawing and painting.","zh":"治療益處可以源自素描和繪畫。"},{"en":"Be derived from means come from or be obtained from a source.","zh":"be derived from 指來自某來源或由某來源獲得。"},{"en":"Many medicines are derived from plants or natural chemicals.","zh":"許多藥物來自植物或天然化學物。"},{"en":"If calmness is derived from painting, the activity itself becomes helpful.","zh":"如果平靜感來自繪畫，該活動本身就變得有幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of a result.","zh":"這個片語指出結果的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"during his recovery","meaning":"在康復期間","examples":[{"en":"Hill discovered the value of art during his recovery.","zh":"Hill 在康復期間發現藝術的價值。"},{"en":"During his recovery means while he was getting better after illness or injury.","zh":"during his recovery 指在他從疾病或受傷中逐漸好轉的期間。"},{"en":"During his recovery from surgery, a patient may read, draw, or practise gentle movement.","zh":"病人手術康復期間，可能閱讀、繪畫或練習輕柔活動。"},{"en":"Recovery periods can give people time to notice what helps their mind and body.","zh":"康復期可以給人時間注意甚麼有助身心。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the time context for an experience.","zh":"這個片語給出某經歷的時間背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"become therapeutic","meaning":"變得有治療作用","examples":[{"en":"Hill claimed that art could become therapeutic.","zh":"Hill 聲稱藝術可以變得有治療作用。"},{"en":"Become therapeutic means begin to have a healing or supportive effect.","zh":"become therapeutic 指開始具有療癒或支援效果。"},{"en":"Writing a diary can become therapeutic when it helps a student organise painful feelings.","zh":"當寫日記幫助學生整理痛苦感受，它可以變得有治療作用。"},{"en":"An ordinary activity may become therapeutic if it brings calm, expression, or confidence.","zh":"如果普通活動帶來平靜、表達或信心，它可能變得有治療作用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something gaining a healing function.","zh":"這個片語描述某事物獲得療癒功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be capable of","meaning":"能夠","examples":[{"en":"Art was capable of completely engrossing the mind.","zh":"藝術能夠令思想完全投入其中。"},{"en":"Be capable of means have the ability or power to do something.","zh":"be capable of 指有能力或力量做某事。"},{"en":"A clear timetable is capable of helping students manage stress before exams.","zh":"清楚時間表能夠幫助學生在考試前管理壓力。"},{"en":"If art is capable of holding attention, it can distract patients from pain or worry.","zh":"如果藝術能夠吸引注意力，它就可以讓病人暫時離開疼痛或擔憂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ability or potential.","zh":"這個片語描述能力或潛力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"completely engross the mind","meaning":"令思想完全投入其中","examples":[{"en":"Art can completely engross the mind during the creative process.","zh":"藝術可以在創作過程中令思想完全投入其中。"},{"en":"Completely engross the mind means fully absorb someone’s attention and thoughts.","zh":"completely engross the mind 指完全吸引某人的注意力和思想。"},{"en":"A difficult puzzle can completely engross the mind until a student forgets the time.","zh":"困難謎題可以令學生完全投入其中，直到忘記時間。"},{"en":"If an activity fully engages the mind, anxious thoughts may become quieter for a while.","zh":"如果活動充分吸引心神，焦慮想法可能暫時安靜下來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep mental absorption.","zh":"這個片語描述深度精神投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"release creative energy","meaning":"釋放創造力","examples":[{"en":"Art can release the creative energy of the patient.","zh":"藝術可以釋放病人的創造力。"},{"en":"Release creative energy means allow imagination and expression to come out freely.","zh":"release creative energy 指讓想像力和表達自由流露。"},{"en":"A music workshop may release creative energy in students who are usually quiet.","zh":"音樂工作坊可能釋放平時安靜學生的創造力。"},{"en":"If patients release creative energy, they may express feelings they cannot easily explain in words.","zh":"如果病人釋放創造力，他們可能表達難以用文字說明的感受。"},{"en":"The phrase connects creativity with emotional expression.","zh":"這個片語把創造力與情緒表達連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"creative energy","meaning":"創造力；創作能量","examples":[{"en":"Hill believed that art released the patient’s creative energy.","zh":"Hill 相信藝術釋放病人的創造力。"},{"en":"Creative energy is the inner drive or ability to imagine, make, and express ideas.","zh":"creative energy 指想像、創作和表達想法的內在動力或能力。"},{"en":"A child’s creative energy may appear in drawing, storytelling, building blocks, or music.","zh":"孩子的創作能量可能出現在繪畫、說故事、積木或音樂中。"},{"en":"If creative energy has no outlet, a person may feel restless or blocked.","zh":"如果創作能量沒有出口，一個人可能感到不安或受阻。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the power behind creative expression.","zh":"這個片語描述創意表達背後的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"inhibited patient","meaning":"受壓抑的病人","examples":[{"en":"Art could help the frequently inhibited patient express themselves.","zh":"藝術可以幫助經常受壓抑的病人表達自己。"},{"en":"An inhibited patient is a patient who feels blocked, shy, or unable to express feelings freely.","zh":"inhibited patient 指感到受阻、害羞或無法自由表達感受的病人。"},{"en":"A quiet teenager in counselling may be an inhibited patient who needs non-verbal ways to communicate.","zh":"輔導中安靜的青少年可能是受壓抑的病人，需要非語言方式溝通。"},{"en":"If a patient is inhibited, drawing may feel safer than direct conversation.","zh":"如果病人受壓抑，繪畫可能比直接交談感覺更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes emotional restraint or blocked expression.","zh":"這個片語描述情緒克制或表達受阻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in turn","meaning":"反過來；繼而","examples":[{"en":"This effect could in turn help the patient.","zh":"這種效果反過來可以幫助病人。"},{"en":"In turn means as a result of the previous thing, or as the next step in a chain.","zh":"in turn 指作為前一件事的結果，或作為連鎖中的下一步。"},{"en":"Better sleep can improve concentration, which in turn can improve school performance.","zh":"更好睡眠可以改善專注力，繼而改善學業表現。"},{"en":"If art reduces anxiety, it may in turn help patients speak more openly.","zh":"如果藝術減少焦慮，它可能繼而幫助病人更坦誠說話。"},{"en":"The phrase connects one result to another result.","zh":"這個片語把一個結果連接到另一個結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"build up","meaning":"建立；增強","examples":[{"en":"Art could help patients build up a strong defence against misfortune.","zh":"藝術可以幫助病人建立對抗不幸的強大防禦。"},{"en":"Build up means gradually develop, increase, or strengthen something.","zh":"build up 指逐漸發展、增加或增強某事物。"},{"en":"Students build up confidence by practising speaking in small, safe steps.","zh":"學生透過小步而安全地練習說話來建立信心。"},{"en":"If therapy helps patients build up emotional strength, they may cope better with difficulty.","zh":"如果治療幫助病人增強情緒力量，他們可能更能應對困難。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests gradual strengthening over time.","zh":"這個片語暗示隨時間逐漸加強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a strong defence against","meaning":"對抗……的強大防禦","examples":[{"en":"Art could build up a strong defence against the patient’s misfortunes.","zh":"藝術可以建立對抗病人不幸的強大防禦。"},{"en":"A strong defence against something is a powerful way to protect oneself from harm or difficulty.","zh":"strong defence against something 指保護自己免受傷害或困難影響的有力方法。"},{"en":"Good savings can be a strong defence against sudden job loss.","zh":"良好儲蓄可以是對抗突然失業的強大防禦。"},{"en":"If patients develop confidence and self-expression, they may have a stronger defence against despair.","zh":"如果病人發展信心和自我表達，就可能有更強力量對抗絕望。"},{"en":"The phrase describes protection, not physical fighting only.","zh":"這個片語描述保護，不只是身體上的戰鬥。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"misfortunes","meaning":"不幸；逆境","examples":[{"en":"Hill believed that art could help patients cope with their misfortunes.","zh":"Hill 相信藝術可以幫助病人應對其不幸。"},{"en":"Misfortunes are unlucky, painful, or difficult events in life.","zh":"misfortunes 指生活中不幸、痛苦或困難的事件。"},{"en":"Losing a job, falling ill, or experiencing family conflict can be misfortunes.","zh":"失業、生病或經歷家庭衝突都可以是不幸。"},{"en":"If people have ways to express pain, misfortunes may become easier to bear.","zh":"如果人們有方式表達痛苦，逆境可能變得較易承受。"},{"en":"The word refers to hardships rather than small inconveniences.","zh":"這個詞指艱難經歷，而不是小不便。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be founded","meaning":"成立","examples":[{"en":"The British Association of Art Therapists was founded in 1964.","zh":"英國藝術治療師協會於1964年成立。"},{"en":"Be founded means be established or formally created.","zh":"be founded 指被建立或正式創立。"},{"en":"A student club may be founded when several students and a teacher agree on its purpose.","zh":"當幾名學生和一位老師同意學會目的，學生學會可能成立。"},{"en":"When an association is founded, a profession gains clearer organisation and identity.","zh":"當協會成立，一門專業就獲得更清楚的組織和身份。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used for institutions, organisations, and movements.","zh":"這個片語常用於機構、組織和運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"British Association of Art Therapists","meaning":"英國藝術治療師協會","examples":[{"en":"The British Association of Art Therapists was founded in 1964.","zh":"英國藝術治療師協會於1964年成立。"},{"en":"The British Association of Art Therapists is a professional body connected with art therapy in Britain.","zh":"British Association of Art Therapists 指與英國藝術治療相關的專業團體。"},{"en":"A professional association may support training, standards, and public understanding of a field.","zh":"專業協會可能支援訓練、標準和公眾對某領域的理解。"},{"en":"Such an association can help art therapists share knowledge and build credibility.","zh":"這類協會可以幫助藝術治療師分享知識並建立可信度。"},{"en":"The phrase names an organisation in the history of art therapy.","zh":"這個片語指出藝術治療史中的一個組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"proponents of","meaning":"……的支持者","examples":[{"en":"Proponents of art therapy fell into two categories.","zh":"藝術治療的支持者分為兩類。"},{"en":"Proponents of something are people who support or argue in favour of it.","zh":"proponents of something 指支持或主張某事的人。"},{"en":"Proponents of online learning say it can help students in remote areas.","zh":"網上學習的支持者認為它可以幫助偏遠地區學生。"},{"en":"If proponents disagree about methods, a field may develop several approaches.","zh":"如果支持者對方法有分歧，一個領域可能發展出幾種取向。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to supporters, not opponents.","zh":"這個片語指支持者，而不是反對者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fall into one of two categories","meaning":"分為兩類之一","examples":[{"en":"Proponents of art therapy fell into one of two categories.","zh":"藝術治療的支持者分為兩類之一。"},{"en":"Fall into one of two categories means belong to one of two main groups.","zh":"fall into one of two categories 指屬於兩個主要類別中的其中一類。"},{"en":"Exam questions often fall into one of two categories: factual questions or opinion questions.","zh":"考試題目常分為兩類之一：事實題或觀點題。"},{"en":"Dividing ideas into categories helps students understand differences more clearly.","zh":"把想法分類可以幫助學生更清楚理解差異。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to classify people, ideas, or methods.","zh":"這個片語用於分類人、想法或方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"therapeutic effect","meaning":"治療效果","examples":[{"en":"Some practitioners believed in the therapeutic effect of art.","zh":"有些從業者相信藝術的治療效果。"},{"en":"A therapeutic effect is a healing or helpful result produced by an activity, medicine, or treatment.","zh":"therapeutic effect 指活動、藥物或治療所產生的療癒或有益結果。"},{"en":"Gentle exercise can have a therapeutic effect on stress and sleep.","zh":"輕柔運動可以對壓力和睡眠有治療效果。"},{"en":"If making art reduces fear or improves expression, the art has a therapeutic effect.","zh":"如果創作藝術減少恐懼或改善表達，藝術就有治療效果。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the useful result of treatment.","zh":"這個片語集中於治療的有用結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lie in","meaning":"在於","examples":[{"en":"Some therapists believed that art’s value lay in its psychoanalytic use.","zh":"有些治療師認為藝術的價值在於其精神分析用途。"},{"en":"Lie in means be found in or depend on something as the main source of value.","zh":"lie in 指存在於某事中，或以某事作為主要價值來源。"},{"en":"The strength of a good example lies in how clearly it teaches meaning.","zh":"好例句的力量在於它多清楚地教出意思。"},{"en":"If art’s value lies in analysis, the therapist focuses on what the image reveals.","zh":"如果藝術價值在於分析，治療師就集中於影像揭示了甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where the importance of something is located.","zh":"這個片語指出某事的重要性所在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"effectiveness as","meaning":"作為……的成效","examples":[{"en":"Art could be valued for its effectiveness as a psychoanalytic tool.","zh":"藝術可以因其作為精神分析工具的成效而受到重視。"},{"en":"Effectiveness as means how useful or successful something is in a particular role.","zh":"effectiveness as 指某事在特定角色中有多有用或成功。"},{"en":"A checklist may be judged by its effectiveness as a study tool.","zh":"清單可以按其作為學習工具的成效來評價。"},{"en":"If drawings reveal hidden feelings, art may be effective as a therapeutic method.","zh":"如果圖畫揭示隱藏感受，藝術作為治療方法可能有效。"},{"en":"The phrase measures performance in a specific function.","zh":"這個片語量度某事在特定功能中的表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"psychoanalytic tool","meaning":"精神分析工具","examples":[{"en":"Some practitioners used art as a psychoanalytic tool.","zh":"有些從業者把藝術用作精神分析工具。"},{"en":"A psychoanalytic tool is something used to explore unconscious feelings, memories, or conflicts.","zh":"psychoanalytic tool 指用來探索潛意識感受、記憶或衝突的東西。"},{"en":"A therapist may use dreams as a psychoanalytic tool during counselling.","zh":"治療師可能在輔導中把夢用作精神分析工具。"},{"en":"In art therapy, a drawing may act as a tool for discussing hidden emotions.","zh":"在藝術治療中，一幅畫可能成為討論隱藏情緒的工具。"},{"en":"The phrase describes art as a way to support psychological analysis.","zh":"這個片語描述藝術作為支援心理分析的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"assess a patient through","meaning":"透過……評估病人","examples":[{"en":"Therapists could assess a patient through their drawings.","zh":"治療師可以透過病人的圖畫評估病人。"},{"en":"Assess a patient through something means evaluate a patient by using that material or activity as evidence.","zh":"assess a patient through something 指利用某材料或活動作證據來評估病人。"},{"en":"A doctor may assess a patient through blood tests, questions, and physical examination.","zh":"醫生可能透過驗血、提問和身體檢查評估病人。"},{"en":"If a patient cannot speak easily, drawings may give clues about feelings or fears.","zh":"如果病人不容易說話，圖畫可能提供關於感受或恐懼的線索。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using one method to understand a patient.","zh":"這個片語描述使用某方法理解病人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hold the belief that","meaning":"持有……信念","examples":[{"en":"Some practitioners held the belief that art-making was an end in itself.","zh":"有些從業者持有藝術創作本身就是目的的信念。"},{"en":"Hold the belief that means believe or maintain a particular view.","zh":"hold the belief that 指相信或持有某一特定觀點。"},{"en":"Some teachers hold the belief that mistakes are necessary for learning.","zh":"有些老師相信錯誤是學習所必需的。"},{"en":"If therapists hold different beliefs, they may use different treatment methods.","zh":"如果治療師持有不同信念，他們可能使用不同治療方法。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a person’s viewpoint.","zh":"這個片語引出某人的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"art-making","meaning":"藝術創作","examples":[{"en":"Some therapists believed that art-making itself could be therapeutic.","zh":"有些治療師相信藝術創作本身可以有治療作用。"},{"en":"Art-making means the act or process of creating visual art.","zh":"art-making 指創造視覺藝術的行為或過程。"},{"en":"A student may use art-making to relax after a stressful school day.","zh":"學生可能用藝術創作在壓力大的上學日後放鬆。"},{"en":"If the process matters more than the final picture, art-making itself becomes meaningful.","zh":"如果過程比最終圖畫更重要，藝術創作本身就變得有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on creating art, not only viewing it.","zh":"這個片語集中於創作藝術，而不只是觀看藝術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"an end in itself","meaning":"本身就是目的","examples":[{"en":"For some therapists, art-making was an end in itself.","zh":"對有些治療師而言，藝術創作本身就是目的。"},{"en":"An end in itself means something is valuable for its own sake, not just as a tool for another purpose.","zh":"an end in itself 指某事本身有價值，而不只是達成其他目的的工具。"},{"en":"Reading for pleasure can be an end in itself, not only exam preparation.","zh":"為樂趣而閱讀本身可以是目的，而不只是考試準備。"},{"en":"If art-making is an end in itself, the patient does not need to produce a perfect artwork.","zh":"如果藝術創作本身就是目的，病人不需要創作完美作品。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses intrinsic value.","zh":"這個片語強調內在價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"creative process","meaning":"創作過程","examples":[{"en":"The creative process can act therapeutically on the patient.","zh":"創作過程可以對病人產生治療作用。"},{"en":"The creative process is the series of steps and experiences involved in making something new.","zh":"creative process 指創造新事物所涉及的一連串步驟和經驗。"},{"en":"Writing, sketching, revising, and choosing colours can all be part of the creative process.","zh":"寫作、素描、修改和選擇顏色都可以是創作過程的一部分。"},{"en":"If the creative process helps people organise feelings, it can support therapy.","zh":"如果創作過程幫助人整理感受，它就能支持治療。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the making, not only the finished product.","zh":"這個片語集中於製作過程，而不只是完成品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"act therapeutically on","meaning":"對……產生治療作用","examples":[{"en":"The creative process may act therapeutically on the patient.","zh":"創作過程可能對病人產生治療作用。"},{"en":"Act therapeutically on means have a healing or helpful effect on someone.","zh":"act therapeutically on 指對某人產生療癒或有益效果。"},{"en":"Regular breathing exercises can act therapeutically on people who feel anxious.","zh":"規律呼吸練習可以對感到焦慮的人產生治療作用。"},{"en":"If painting calms a patient and helps expression, it acts therapeutically on them.","zh":"如果繪畫使病人平靜並幫助表達，它就對病人產生治療作用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a positive treatment-like effect.","zh":"這個片語描述類似治療的正面效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not incompatible","meaning":"並非不能並存","examples":[{"en":"The two approaches were not incompatible.","zh":"這兩種取向並非不能並存。"},{"en":"Not incompatible means two things can exist or work together without contradiction.","zh":"not incompatible 指兩件事可以同時存在或合作，而不互相矛盾。"},{"en":"Strict exam training and creative teaching are not incompatible if lessons are well designed.","zh":"如果課堂設計得好，嚴格考試訓練和創意教學並非不能並存。"},{"en":"If two approaches overlap, therapists do not have to choose only one.","zh":"如果兩種取向有重疊，治療師不必只選其中一種。"},{"en":"The phrase means “can go together,” not “exactly the same.”","zh":"這個片語意思是「可以並存」，而不是「完全相同」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a degree of overlap","meaning":"某程度上的重疊","examples":[{"en":"There was a degree of overlap between the two practices.","zh":"這兩種實踐之間有某程度上的重疊。"},{"en":"A degree of overlap means some shared features or common ground.","zh":"a degree of overlap 指有一些共同特徵或共同基礎。"},{"en":"There is a degree of overlap between grammar lessons and writing lessons.","zh":"文法課和寫作課之間有某程度上的重疊。"},{"en":"If two therapies both use self-expression, they may overlap in practice.","zh":"如果兩種治療都使用自我表達，它們在實踐上可能有重疊。"},{"en":"The phrase shows partial similarity, not complete identity.","zh":"這個片語表示部分相似，而不是完全相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"occur between","meaning":"在……之間出現","examples":[{"en":"A degree of overlap occurred between the two practices.","zh":"這兩種實踐之間出現了某程度上的重疊。"},{"en":"Occur between means happen or exist in the space or relationship linking two things.","zh":"occur between 指在兩件事物之間的空間或關係中發生或存在。"},{"en":"Misunderstandings may occur between teachers and students when instructions are unclear.","zh":"當指示不清楚，老師和學生之間可能出現誤解。"},{"en":"If overlap occurs between two methods, they may share goals or techniques.","zh":"如果兩種方法之間出現重疊，它們可能共享目標或技巧。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something happening in a relationship between two sides.","zh":"這個片語描述某事在兩方關係中出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"produce work","meaning":"創作作品","examples":[{"en":"A patient could produce work that revealed self-expression.","zh":"病人可以創作揭示自我表達的作品。"},{"en":"Produce work means create a piece of writing, art, music, or other output.","zh":"produce work 指創作文章、藝術、音樂或其他成果。"},{"en":"Students produce work when they write essays, make posters, or complete projects.","zh":"學生寫文章、製作海報或完成專題時，就是創作作品。"},{"en":"In art therapy, the work produced may show feelings the patient cannot say directly.","zh":"在藝術治療中，創作出來的作品可能顯示病人無法直接說出的感受。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on making a creative or practical product.","zh":"這個片語集中於製作創意或實用成果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be analysed for","meaning":"就……被分析","examples":[{"en":"A patient’s artwork could be analysed for content.","zh":"病人的藝術作品可以就內容被分析。"},{"en":"Be analysed for means be examined in order to find or understand a particular feature.","zh":"be analysed for 指為了尋找或理解某特定特徵而被檢視。"},{"en":"A student’s essay may be analysed for grammar mistakes and argument structure.","zh":"學生文章可以就文法錯誤和論證結構被分析。"},{"en":"If artwork is analysed for symbols, the therapist looks for possible meanings.","zh":"如果藝術作品就象徵被分析，治療師會尋找可能意思。"},{"en":"The phrase shows what the analysis is looking for.","zh":"這個片語顯示分析要尋找甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"content","meaning":"內容","examples":[{"en":"The therapist could analyse the content of a patient’s artwork.","zh":"治療師可以分析病人藝術作品的內容。"},{"en":"Content means the ideas, images, subjects, or meaning inside a piece of work.","zh":"content 指作品中的想法、影像、主題或意思。"},{"en":"A teacher may praise an essay’s content even if the grammar needs improvement.","zh":"即使文法需要改善，老師也可能稱讚文章內容。"},{"en":"In therapy, artwork content may include memories, fears, hopes, or relationships.","zh":"在治療中，藝術作品內容可能包括記憶、恐懼、希望或關係。"},{"en":"The word refers to what is expressed, not only how it looks.","zh":"這個詞指表達了甚麼，而不只是外觀如何。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"forms of self-expression","meaning":"自我表達形式","examples":[{"en":"The patient’s work could reveal forms of self-expression.","zh":"病人的作品可以揭示自我表達形式。"},{"en":"Forms of self-expression are ways people show thoughts, feelings, identity, or experience.","zh":"forms of self-expression 指人們展示思想、感受、身份或經歷的方法。"},{"en":"Music, clothing, writing, and drawing can all be forms of self-expression.","zh":"音樂、服裝、寫作和繪畫都可以是自我表達形式。"},{"en":"If a person cannot speak openly, another form of self-expression may feel safer.","zh":"如果一個人無法坦誠說話，另一種自我表達形式可能感覺更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes different ways of showing the inner self.","zh":"這個片語描述展示內在自我的不同方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"creative outlet","meaning":"創意出口；創作抒發途徑","examples":[{"en":"Art can provide a creative outlet for patients.","zh":"藝術可以為病人提供創意出口。"},{"en":"A creative outlet is an activity that lets people express feelings, ideas, or energy creatively.","zh":"creative outlet 指讓人以創意方式表達感受、想法或能量的活動。"},{"en":"A student may use music as a creative outlet after a stressful day.","zh":"學生可能在壓力大的一天後把音樂用作創作抒發途徑。"},{"en":"If patients have a creative outlet, they may release feelings instead of keeping them inside.","zh":"如果病人有創意出口，他們可能釋放感受，而不是把感受壓在心裡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a safe channel for expression.","zh":"這個片語描述安全的表達渠道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"同時","examples":[{"en":"The artwork could be analysed and provide a creative outlet at the same time.","zh":"藝術作品可以被分析，同時提供創意出口。"},{"en":"At the same time means simultaneously or during the same period.","zh":"at the same time 指同時或在同一段時間內。"},{"en":"A teacher can correct grammar and encourage confidence at the same time.","zh":"老師可以同時糾正文法和鼓勵信心。"},{"en":"In art therapy, one activity may support expression and provide material for discussion at the same time.","zh":"在藝術治療中，一項活動可以同時支持表達並提供討論材料。"},{"en":"The phrase shows two things happening together.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩件事一起發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in all its forms","meaning":"以各種形式","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy in all its forms has proved effective.","zh":"藝術治療以各種形式都已被證明有效。"},{"en":"In all its forms means in every type or version of something.","zh":"in all its forms 指以某事物的每一種類型或版本。"},{"en":"Learning, in all its forms, can happen through reading, practice, conversation, and mistakes.","zh":"學習以各種形式發生，可以透過閱讀、練習、交談和錯誤。"},{"en":"If art therapy works in many forms, it may support many different needs.","zh":"如果藝術治療以多種形式有效，它可能支援許多不同需要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses broad coverage of different types.","zh":"這個片語強調涵蓋不同類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prove effective in","meaning":"被證明在……方面有效","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy has proved effective in the treatment of many difficulties.","zh":"藝術治療已被證明在治療許多困難方面有效。"},{"en":"Prove effective in means be shown to work well in a particular situation.","zh":"prove effective in 指被顯示在某特定情況中效果良好。"},{"en":"Short daily revision can prove effective in improving vocabulary memory.","zh":"每日短時間溫習可以被證明在改善詞彙記憶方面有效。"},{"en":"If therapy proves effective in helping patients cope, it gains professional value.","zh":"如果治療被證明能有效幫助病人應對困難，它就獲得專業價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes demonstrated usefulness.","zh":"這個片語描述已被證明的有用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"treatment of individuals","meaning":"對個人的治療","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy can be used in the treatment of individuals with different needs.","zh":"藝術治療可以用於對有不同需要的個人的治療。"},{"en":"Treatment of individuals means helping particular people through medical, psychological, or supportive care.","zh":"treatment of individuals 指透過醫療、心理或支援性照護幫助特定人士。"},{"en":"A hospital plans the treatment of individuals according to symptoms, age, and personal needs.","zh":"醫院根據症狀、年齡和個人需要規劃對個人的治療。"},{"en":"Art therapy may be adapted because each person’s difficulties are different.","zh":"藝術治療可能需要調整，因為每個人的困難不同。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on care for particular people, not only groups.","zh":"這個片語集中於對特定個人的照護，而不只是群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"suffer from","meaning":"患有；遭受","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy can help individuals suffering from a wide range of difficulties.","zh":"藝術治療可以幫助遭受廣泛困難的個人。"},{"en":"Suffer from means experience an illness, problem, pain, or difficulty.","zh":"suffer from 指經歷疾病、問題、痛苦或困難。"},{"en":"A student may suffer from anxiety before public speaking.","zh":"學生可能在公開演說前患有焦慮。"},{"en":"If people suffer from emotional problems, they may need support beyond ordinary advice.","zh":"如果人們遭受情緒問題，他們可能需要普通建議以外的支援。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being affected by something negative.","zh":"這個片語描述受到負面事物影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a wide range of","meaning":"廣泛的……","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy can support people with a wide range of difficulties.","zh":"藝術治療可以支援有廣泛困難的人。"},{"en":"A wide range of means many different types of something.","zh":"a wide range of 指許多不同種類的某物。"},{"en":"A library offers a wide range of books for children, teenagers, and adults.","zh":"圖書館為兒童、青少年和成人提供廣泛書籍。"},{"en":"If therapy helps a wide range of clients, it can be used flexibly.","zh":"如果治療能幫助廣泛求助者，它就能被靈活使用。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses variety and breadth.","zh":"這個片語強調多樣性和廣度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"difficulties or disabilities","meaning":"困難或殘疾","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy can help people with various difficulties or disabilities.","zh":"藝術治療可以幫助有各種困難或殘疾的人。"},{"en":"Difficulties or disabilities are problems, limitations, or conditions that affect daily life or functioning.","zh":"difficulties or disabilities 指影響日常生活或功能的問題、限制或狀況。"},{"en":"A school may support students with learning difficulties or physical disabilities.","zh":"學校可能支援有學習困難或身體殘疾的學生。"},{"en":"If support is adapted, people with different difficulties can participate more fully.","zh":"如果支援經過調整，有不同困難的人就能更充分參與。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both general problems and recognised disabilities.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋一般問題和被承認的殘疾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"emotional problems","meaning":"情緒問題","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy can help individuals with emotional problems.","zh":"藝術治療可以幫助有情緒問題的人。"},{"en":"Emotional problems are difficulties involving feelings such as sadness, fear, anger, or anxiety.","zh":"emotional problems 指涉及悲傷、恐懼、憤怒或焦慮等感受的困難。"},{"en":"A student with emotional problems may cry often, withdraw from friends, or lose motivation.","zh":"有情緒問題的學生可能常哭、疏遠朋友或失去動力。"},{"en":"If feelings are hard to explain, art may help people show them indirectly.","zh":"如果感受難以解釋，藝術可能幫助人間接展示它們。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to problems of mood and feeling.","zh":"這個片語指心情和感受上的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"behavioural problems","meaning":"行為問題","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy may be used with people who have behavioural problems.","zh":"藝術治療可能用於有行為問題的人。"},{"en":"Behavioural problems are repeated actions that cause difficulty for the person or others.","zh":"behavioural problems 指反覆出現並為本人或他人造成困難的行為。"},{"en":"A child with behavioural problems may hit classmates, refuse instructions, or leave the classroom suddenly.","zh":"有行為問題的孩子可能打同學、拒絕指示或突然離開課室。"},{"en":"If therapy helps the child express anger safely, behaviour may improve.","zh":"如果治療幫助孩子安全表達憤怒，行為可能改善。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on outward actions.","zh":"這個片語集中於外在行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"mental-health problems","meaning":"精神健康問題","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy can support people with mental-health problems.","zh":"藝術治療可以支援有精神健康問題的人。"},{"en":"Mental-health problems are difficulties affecting thoughts, emotions, mood, or psychological wellbeing.","zh":"mental-health problems 指影響思想、情緒、心情或心理健康的困難。"},{"en":"Anxiety, depression, and trauma-related stress are examples of mental-health problems.","zh":"焦慮、抑鬱和創傷相關壓力都是精神健康問題的例子。"},{"en":"If people receive support early, mental-health problems may become easier to manage.","zh":"如果人們及早獲得支援，精神健康問題可能較易管理。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to psychological health issues.","zh":"這個片語指心理健康相關問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"learning disabilities","meaning":"學習障礙","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy can help individuals with learning disabilities.","zh":"藝術治療可以幫助有學習障礙的人。"},{"en":"Learning disabilities are conditions that make learning certain skills more difficult.","zh":"learning disabilities 指令學習某些技能更困難的狀況。"},{"en":"A student with learning disabilities may need extra time, visual support, or different instructions.","zh":"有學習障礙的學生可能需要額外時間、視覺支援或不同指示。"},{"en":"Art therapy can offer another way to communicate when words are difficult.","zh":"當語言困難時，藝術治療可以提供另一種溝通方式。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to learning-related difficulties, not lack of effort.","zh":"這個片語指與學習有關的困難，而不是不努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"physical disabilities","meaning":"身體殘疾","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy may benefit people with physical disabilities.","zh":"藝術治療可能令有身體殘疾的人受益。"},{"en":"Physical disabilities are conditions that affect movement, strength, coordination, or bodily function.","zh":"physical disabilities 指影響移動、力量、協調或身體功能的狀況。"},{"en":"A person with physical disabilities may use a wheelchair, support worker, or adapted tools.","zh":"有身體殘疾的人可能使用輪椅、支援人員或改良工具。"},{"en":"If art materials are adjusted, people with limited movement can still create artwork.","zh":"如果藝術材料經過調整，行動受限的人仍能創作藝術作品。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to disabilities affecting the body.","zh":"這個片語指影響身體的殘疾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"neurological conditions","meaning":"神經系統疾病","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy can be used with patients who have neurological conditions.","zh":"藝術治療可以用於有神經系統疾病的病人。"},{"en":"Neurological conditions are disorders affecting the brain, nerves, or nervous system.","zh":"neurological conditions 指影響大腦、神經或神經系統的疾病。"},{"en":"Stroke, epilepsy, and Parkinson’s disease are examples of neurological conditions.","zh":"中風、癲癇和柏金遜症都是神經系統疾病的例子。"},{"en":"If the nervous system is affected, art therapy may support communication, memory, or confidence.","zh":"如果神經系統受影響，藝術治療可能支援溝通、記憶或信心。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to medical conditions involving the nervous system.","zh":"這個片語指涉及神經系統的醫療狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"physical illness","meaning":"身體疾病","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy can also support people with physical illness.","zh":"藝術治療也可以支援有身體疾病的人。"},{"en":"Physical illness is sickness affecting the body rather than only the mind.","zh":"physical illness 指影響身體而不只是心理的疾病。"},{"en":"A patient with a long physical illness may feel fear, boredom, or loss of control.","zh":"長期身體疾病患者可能感到恐懼、沉悶或失去控制感。"},{"en":"Art therapy can help patients cope emotionally while medical treatment addresses the illness.","zh":"醫療治療處理疾病時，藝術治療可以幫助病人在情緒上應對。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to bodily disease or sickness.","zh":"這個片語指身體上的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on a group or individual basis","meaning":"以小組或個人形式","examples":[{"en":"Therapy can be provided on a group or individual basis.","zh":"治療可以以小組或個人形式提供。"},{"en":"On a group or individual basis means either with several people together or with one person alone.","zh":"on a group or individual basis 指與幾個人一起進行，或單獨與一個人進行。"},{"en":"A school may offer counselling on a group or individual basis depending on students’ needs.","zh":"學校可能根據學生需要，以小組或個人形式提供輔導。"},{"en":"Group sessions can build shared support, while individual sessions allow private attention.","zh":"小組課節可以建立共同支援，而個人課節容許私人關注。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how a service is organised.","zh":"這個片語描述服務如何組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據","examples":[{"en":"Therapy is provided according to the clients’ needs.","zh":"治療根據求助者的需要提供。"},{"en":"According to means based on or depending on a rule, source, or situation.","zh":"according to 指基於或取決於某規則、來源或情況。"},{"en":"Teachers may change homework according to students’ ability and exam dates.","zh":"老師可能根據學生能力和考試日期調整功課。"},{"en":"If therapy is planned according to needs, each client receives more suitable support.","zh":"如果治療根據需要規劃，每位求助者就能得到更合適支援。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the basis for a decision.","zh":"這個片語顯示決定的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"clients’ needs","meaning":"客戶／求助者的需要","examples":[{"en":"The form of therapy depends on the clients’ needs.","zh":"治療形式取決於求助者的需要。"},{"en":"Clients’ needs are the particular problems, goals, abilities, and circumstances of people receiving a service.","zh":"clients’ needs 指接受服務的人所具備的特定問題、目標、能力和情況。"},{"en":"A tutor plans lessons according to clients’ needs, such as grammar, speaking, or exam writing.","zh":"補習老師會根據客戶需要安排課堂，例如文法、口語或考試寫作。"},{"en":"If clients’ needs are different, one fixed approach may not work for everyone.","zh":"如果求助者需要不同，一種固定方法未必適合所有人。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses personalised support.","zh":"這個片語強調個人化支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"adopt an approach","meaning":"採用某種方法","examples":[{"en":"The therapist may adopt a psychoanalytic or creative approach.","zh":"治療師可能採用精神分析或創作取向。"},{"en":"Adopt an approach means choose and use a particular method or way of working.","zh":"adopt an approach 指選擇並使用某種方法或工作方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may adopt a visual approach for students who learn better through diagrams.","zh":"對較善於透過圖像學習的學生，老師可能採用視覺方法。"},{"en":"If a therapist adopts the wrong approach, the client may not feel understood.","zh":"如果治療師採用錯誤方法，求助者可能感到不被理解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes selecting a method.","zh":"這個片語描述選擇方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"psychoanalytic approach","meaning":"精神分析取向","examples":[{"en":"Some therapists adopt a psychoanalytic approach.","zh":"有些治療師採用精神分析取向。"},{"en":"A psychoanalytic approach focuses on hidden feelings, unconscious thoughts, and past experiences.","zh":"psychoanalytic approach 集中於隱藏感受、潛意識思想和過去經歷。"},{"en":"A counsellor using a psychoanalytic approach may ask about dreams or childhood memories.","zh":"使用精神分析取向的輔導員可能詢問夢或童年記憶。"},{"en":"In art therapy, this approach may analyse images for symbolic meaning.","zh":"在藝術治療中，這種取向可能分析影像的象徵意義。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a therapy style influenced by psychoanalysis.","zh":"這個片語描述受精神分析影響的治療風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"creative approach","meaning":"創作取向","examples":[{"en":"Other therapists adopt a creative approach.","zh":"其他治療師採用創作取向。"},{"en":"A creative approach focuses on making, expressing, exploring, and experiencing art itself.","zh":"creative approach 集中於創作、表達、探索和經驗藝術本身。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a creative approach by asking students to design posters instead of only taking notes.","zh":"老師可能要求學生設計海報，而不只是抄筆記，以使用創作取向。"},{"en":"In therapy, a creative approach may value the process more than interpretation.","zh":"在治療中，創作取向可能更重視過程而不是解讀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a method centred on creativity.","zh":"這個片語描述以創意為中心的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"multifaceted","meaning":"多方面的","examples":[{"en":"The effect of art therapy is multifaceted.","zh":"藝術治療的效果是多方面的。"},{"en":"Multifaceted means having many different parts, sides, or effects.","zh":"multifaceted 指具有許多不同部分、方面或效果。"},{"en":"A student’s stress is often multifaceted, involving sleep, family, exams, and friendships.","zh":"學生壓力通常是多方面的，涉及睡眠、家庭、考試和友誼。"},{"en":"If therapy is multifaceted, it may affect emotions, thinking, behaviour, and confidence.","zh":"如果治療是多方面的，它可能影響情緒、思考、行為和信心。"},{"en":"The word describes something with several dimensions.","zh":"這個詞描述具有幾個層面的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"partake in","meaning":"參與","examples":[{"en":"Partaking in art therapy can raise a patient’s self-awareness.","zh":"參與藝術治療可以提高病人的自我覺察。"},{"en":"Partake in means take part in or participate in an activity.","zh":"partake in 指參加或參與某活動。"},{"en":"Students partake in group discussions when they speak, listen, and respond.","zh":"當學生發言、聆聽和回應時，就是參與小組討論。"},{"en":"If patients partake in therapy regularly, they may build trust over time.","zh":"如果病人定期參與治療，他們可能隨時間建立信任。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to say “participate in.”","zh":"這個片語是 “participate in” 的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"raise self-awareness","meaning":"提高自我覺察","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy can raise a patient’s self-awareness.","zh":"藝術治療可以提高病人的自我覺察。"},{"en":"Raise self-awareness means help someone understand their own feelings, thoughts, habits, and reactions better.","zh":"raise self-awareness 指幫助某人更了解自己的感受、思想、習慣和反應。"},{"en":"Keeping a diary can raise self-awareness because students notice patterns in mood and behaviour.","zh":"寫日記可以提高自我覺察，因為學生會注意到心情和行為模式。"},{"en":"If patients understand themselves better, they may manage stress more effectively.","zh":"如果病人更了解自己，就可能更有效管理壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improving understanding of oneself.","zh":"這個片語描述改善對自我的理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"enable someone to","meaning":"使某人能夠","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy can enable patients to deal with stress.","zh":"藝術治療可以使病人能夠應付壓力。"},{"en":"Enable someone to means make it possible for someone to do something.","zh":"enable someone to 指使某人有可能或有能力做某事。"},{"en":"Clear subtitles can enable language learners to understand a film more easily.","zh":"清楚字幕可以使語言學習者更容易理解電影。"},{"en":"If therapy gives patients tools for expression, it enables them to manage difficult feelings.","zh":"如果治療給病人表達工具，就能使他們管理困難感受。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving ability or opportunity.","zh":"這個片語描述給予能力或機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"deal with stress","meaning":"應付壓力","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy can help patients deal with stress.","zh":"藝術治療可以幫助病人應付壓力。"},{"en":"Deal with stress means manage pressure, worry, or emotional strain.","zh":"deal with stress 指管理壓力、擔憂或情緒負擔。"},{"en":"Students deal with stress by planning revision, sleeping enough, and asking for help.","zh":"學生透過規劃溫習、足夠睡眠和求助來應付壓力。"},{"en":"If stress is not dealt with, it may affect sleep, mood, and concentration.","zh":"如果壓力沒有被處理，它可能影響睡眠、心情和專注力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes coping with pressure.","zh":"這個片語描述應對壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"traumatic experiences","meaning":"創傷經歷","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy can help patients process traumatic experiences.","zh":"藝術治療可以幫助病人處理創傷經歷。"},{"en":"Traumatic experiences are deeply distressing events that may leave lasting emotional effects.","zh":"traumatic experiences 指非常痛苦、可能留下長期情緒影響的事件。"},{"en":"A serious accident, violence, or sudden loss can become a traumatic experience.","zh":"嚴重意外、暴力或突然失去親人都可以成為創傷經歷。"},{"en":"If people cannot talk about trauma directly, art may help them approach it slowly.","zh":"如果人們無法直接談論創傷，藝術可能幫助他們慢慢接近它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to experiences that wound the mind emotionally.","zh":"這個片語指在情緒上傷害心靈的經歷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in addition","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"In addition, art therapy can enhance cognitive abilities.","zh":"此外，藝術治療可以提升認知能力。"},{"en":"In addition means also or as another point.","zh":"in addition 指此外、另外。"},{"en":"The school offers English lessons; in addition, it provides speaking workshops.","zh":"學校提供英文課；此外，它也提供口語工作坊。"},{"en":"This phrase helps add one more idea without replacing the previous one.","zh":"這個片語幫助加入另一個想法，而不是取代前一個想法。"},{"en":"It is useful in essays when adding another benefit, reason, or example.","zh":"在文章中加入另一個好處、理由或例子時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"art therapy sessions","meaning":"藝術治療課節","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy sessions can improve a patient’s self-awareness.","zh":"藝術治療課節可以改善病人的自我覺察。"},{"en":"Art therapy sessions are planned meetings where a therapist uses art-making to support a client.","zh":"art therapy sessions 指治療師使用藝術創作支援求助者的有計劃會面。"},{"en":"A session may involve drawing, discussing feelings, and reflecting on the artwork.","zh":"一節課可能涉及繪畫、討論感受和反思作品。"},{"en":"Regular sessions can help clients build trust and explore difficult emotions gradually.","zh":"定期課節可以幫助求助者建立信任並逐步探索困難情緒。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the actual meetings in therapy.","zh":"這個片語指治療中的實際會面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"enhance cognitive abilities","meaning":"提升認知能力","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy sessions can enhance a patient’s cognitive abilities.","zh":"藝術治療課節可以提升病人的認知能力。"},{"en":"Enhance cognitive abilities means improve thinking skills such as attention, memory, planning, and problem-solving.","zh":"enhance cognitive abilities 指改善注意力、記憶、規劃和解難等思考能力。"},{"en":"Puzzle games may enhance cognitive abilities in older adults by training attention and memory.","zh":"益智遊戲可能透過訓練注意力和記憶來提升長者認知能力。"},{"en":"If art tasks require planning and choices, they may support thinking skills.","zh":"如果藝術任務需要規劃和選擇，它們可能支援思考能力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improving mental processing.","zh":"這個片語描述改善心理處理能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cognitive abilities","meaning":"認知能力","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy may help improve cognitive abilities.","zh":"藝術治療可能有助改善認知能力。"},{"en":"Cognitive abilities are mental skills used for thinking, learning, remembering, and solving problems.","zh":"cognitive abilities 指用於思考、學習、記憶和解決問題的心理技能。"},{"en":"Students use cognitive abilities when they compare ideas, follow instructions, and organise essays.","zh":"學生比較想法、跟從指示和組織文章時，都會使用認知能力。"},{"en":"Illness or injury can affect cognitive abilities, making daily tasks harder.","zh":"疾病或受傷可以影響認知能力，令日常任務更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to thinking-related skills.","zh":"這個片語指與思考相關的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"life-affirming pleasures","meaning":"肯定生命的樂趣","examples":[{"en":"Patients may enjoy the life-affirming pleasures of making art.","zh":"病人可能享受創作藝術所帶來的肯定生命的樂趣。"},{"en":"Life-affirming pleasures are joys that make people feel that life is meaningful, valuable, or worth continuing.","zh":"life-affirming pleasures 指令人感到生命有意義、有價值或值得延續的喜悅。"},{"en":"Gardening, music, cooking, or caring for a pet can give people life-affirming pleasures.","zh":"園藝、音樂、烹飪或照顧寵物都可以給人肯定生命的樂趣。"},{"en":"If illness makes life feel narrow, art can restore small moments of joy and purpose.","zh":"如果疾病令生活感到狹窄，藝術可以恢復小小的喜悅和目的感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes positive experiences that support hope.","zh":"這個片語描述支援希望的正面經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"making art","meaning":"創作藝術","examples":[{"en":"Making art can be enjoyable and therapeutic.","zh":"創作藝術可以令人享受並具有治療作用。"},{"en":"Making art means creating visual works such as drawings, paintings, sculptures, or digital images.","zh":"making art 指創作素描、繪畫、雕塑或數碼影像等視覺作品。"},{"en":"A student may enjoy making art after school because it allows quiet concentration.","zh":"學生可能喜歡放學後創作藝術，因為它讓人安靜專注。"},{"en":"If making art helps someone express feelings safely, it can support wellbeing.","zh":"如果創作藝術幫助某人安全表達感受，它就能支援身心健康。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the act of creation.","zh":"這個片語集中於創作行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"art therapy session","meaning":"藝術治療課節","examples":[{"en":"An art therapy session is different from an art class.","zh":"藝術治療課節不同於藝術班。"},{"en":"An art therapy session is a therapeutic meeting where art is used to explore feelings, experiences, or needs.","zh":"art therapy session 指使用藝術探索感受、經歷或需要的治療性會面。"},{"en":"In an art therapy session, a client may draw freely and discuss what the image means to them.","zh":"在藝術治療課節中，求助者可能自由繪畫並討論影像對自己的意義。"},{"en":"The goal is emotional support and understanding, not producing the best artwork.","zh":"目標是情緒支援和理解，而不是創作最佳藝術作品。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to one meeting within art therapy.","zh":"這個片語指藝術治療中的一次會面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be fundamentally different from","meaning":"與……根本不同","examples":[{"en":"An art therapy session is fundamentally different from an art class.","zh":"藝術治療課節與藝術班根本不同。"},{"en":"Be fundamentally different from means be different in basic purpose, nature, or structure.","zh":"be fundamentally different from 指在基本目的、性質或結構上不同。"},{"en":"A job interview is fundamentally different from a casual chat with friends.","zh":"求職面試與朋友閒聊根本不同。"},{"en":"Art therapy focuses on feelings and healing, while an art class often focuses on technique.","zh":"藝術治療集中於感受和療癒，而藝術班通常集中於技巧。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a deep difference, not a small detail.","zh":"這個片語強調深層差異，而不是小細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"art class","meaning":"藝術班","examples":[{"en":"An art therapy session is not the same as an art class.","zh":"藝術治療課節不同於藝術班。"},{"en":"An art class is a lesson where students learn artistic skills, techniques, or styles.","zh":"art class 指學生學習藝術技能、技巧或風格的課堂。"},{"en":"In an art class, students may practise shading, colour mixing, or drawing from objects.","zh":"在藝術班中，學生可能練習明暗、調色或寫生。"},{"en":"Art classes often judge improvement by technique, while art therapy focuses more on expression.","zh":"藝術班通常按技巧判斷進步，而藝術治療更集中於表達。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to education in art, not therapy.","zh":"這個片語指藝術教育，而不是治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be encouraged to","meaning":"被鼓勵去","examples":[{"en":"The individual is encouraged to focus on internal feelings.","zh":"個人被鼓勵去集中於內在感受。"},{"en":"Be encouraged to means be gently supported or advised to do something.","zh":"be encouraged to 指被溫和地支持或建議去做某事。"},{"en":"Students are encouraged to ask questions when they do not understand a lesson.","zh":"當學生不理解課堂時，他們被鼓勵提問。"},{"en":"If patients are encouraged to express feelings, they may feel safer and less judged.","zh":"如果病人被鼓勵表達感受，他們可能感到更安全且較少被評判。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests support, not force.","zh":"這個片語暗示支援，而不是強迫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"focus more on","meaning":"更集中於","examples":[{"en":"Patients are encouraged to focus more on internal feelings.","zh":"病人被鼓勵更集中於內在感受。"},{"en":"Focus more on means give greater attention to one thing than to another.","zh":"focus more on 指比起另一事物，更加注意某事。"},{"en":"A student preparing for speaking should focus more on fluency than perfect grammar at first.","zh":"準備口語的學生起初應更集中於流暢度，而不是完美文法。"},{"en":"In art therapy, clients focus more on what they feel than on whether the drawing is beautiful.","zh":"在藝術治療中，求助者更集中於自己的感受，而不是畫得是否美。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a shift in attention.","zh":"這個片語顯示注意力的轉移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"internal feelings","meaning":"內在感受","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy focuses on the patient’s internal feelings.","zh":"藝術治療集中於病人的內在感受。"},{"en":"Internal feelings are emotions, worries, memories, or inner experiences that may not be visible outside.","zh":"internal feelings 指情緒、擔憂、記憶或內在經驗，這些未必在外表可見。"},{"en":"A student may smile in class while hiding difficult internal feelings.","zh":"學生可能在課堂上微笑，卻隱藏困難的內在感受。"},{"en":"If therapy gives attention to internal feelings, the client may feel more understood.","zh":"如果治療關注內在感受，求助者可能感到更被理解。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what a person feels inside.","zh":"這個片語指一個人內心感受到的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"express them","meaning":"表達它們","examples":[{"en":"Patients are encouraged to express their feelings through art.","zh":"病人被鼓勵透過藝術表達自己的感受。"},{"en":"Express them means show or communicate those feelings, ideas, or thoughts.","zh":"express them 指展示或傳達那些感受、想法或思想。"},{"en":"A child may express worries by drawing a dark room or a lonely figure.","zh":"孩子可能透過畫一間黑暗房間或孤單人物來表達擔憂。"},{"en":"If people express feelings safely, they may feel less overwhelmed by them.","zh":"如果人們安全地表達感受，他們可能較不會被感受壓倒。"},{"en":"The phrase points back to something already mentioned, such as feelings.","zh":"這個片語指回前面已提到的東西，例如感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy focuses on internal feelings rather than external objects.","zh":"藝術治療集中於內在感受，而不是外在物件。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of, or in contrast to something else.","zh":"rather than 指而不是，或與另一事物形成對比。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to explain their thinking rather than memorise model answers.","zh":"老師可能要求學生解釋思考，而不是背誦範文答案。"},{"en":"In therapy, the goal is expression rather than technical perfection.","zh":"在治療中，目標是表達，而不是技巧完美。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly contrasts two choices or focuses.","zh":"這個片語清楚對比兩個選擇或焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"portray external objects","meaning":"描繪外在物件","examples":[{"en":"Traditional art classes may ask students to portray external objects.","zh":"傳統藝術班可能要求學生描繪外在物件。"},{"en":"Portray external objects means draw, paint, or represent things seen outside the self.","zh":"portray external objects 指素描、繪畫或呈現自我以外看見的事物。"},{"en":"Students may portray external objects such as fruit, chairs, buildings, or people.","zh":"學生可能描繪水果、椅子、建築物或人物等外在物件。"},{"en":"If the task is to portray objects accurately, technique becomes important.","zh":"如果任務是準確描繪物件，技巧就變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts outward observation with inner expression.","zh":"這個片語把外在觀察與內在表達作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"traditional art classes","meaning":"傳統藝術班","examples":[{"en":"Traditional art classes may ask participants to draw from imagination.","zh":"傳統藝術班可能要求參加者憑想像繪畫。"},{"en":"Traditional art classes are ordinary lessons that teach drawing, painting, design, or technique.","zh":"traditional art classes 指教授素描、繪畫、設計或技巧的普通課堂。"},{"en":"A traditional art class may teach students how to shade a still-life drawing.","zh":"傳統藝術班可能教學生如何為靜物素描加上明暗。"},{"en":"Unlike therapy, traditional art classes often focus on skill, style, and final appearance.","zh":"與治療不同，傳統藝術班通常集中於技能、風格和最終外觀。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to art education in a usual classroom setting.","zh":"這個片語指一般課室環境中的藝術教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"draw from their imagination","meaning":"憑想像繪畫","examples":[{"en":"Participants may be asked to draw from their imagination.","zh":"參加者可能被要求憑想像繪畫。"},{"en":"Draw from their imagination means create images from thoughts or ideas rather than copying what they see.","zh":"draw from their imagination 指從思想或想法創造影像，而不是臨摹眼前所見。"},{"en":"A child may draw from imagination when inventing a dragon, a dream house, or a future city.","zh":"孩子創作龍、夢想中的房子或未來城市時，可能憑想像繪畫。"},{"en":"If clients draw from imagination, hidden feelings or wishes may appear in the image.","zh":"如果求助者憑想像繪畫，隱藏感受或願望可能出現在影像中。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts imaginative creation with direct observation.","zh":"這個片語把想像創作與直接觀察作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"inner world","meaning":"內心世界","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy gives importance to the patient’s inner world.","zh":"藝術治療重視病人的內心世界。"},{"en":"A person’s inner world includes feelings, memories, fears, thoughts, hopes, and private meanings.","zh":"inner world 指一個人的感受、記憶、恐懼、思想、希望和私人意義。"},{"en":"A quiet student may have a rich inner world that teachers cannot see immediately.","zh":"安靜的學生可能有豐富內心世界，而老師未必立刻看見。"},{"en":"If therapy respects the inner world, clients may feel safer sharing difficult experiences.","zh":"如果治療尊重內心世界，求助者可能更安全地分享困難經歷。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a person’s private emotional and mental life.","zh":"這個片語指一個人的私人情緒和心理生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"images, feelings, thoughts and ideas","meaning":"影像、感受、思想及意念","examples":[{"en":"The patient’s images, feelings, thoughts and ideas are central to art therapy.","zh":"病人的影像、感受、思想及意念是藝術治療的核心。"},{"en":"Images, feelings, thoughts and ideas are the inner materials that a patient may express through art.","zh":"images, feelings, thoughts and ideas 指病人可能透過藝術表達的內在材料。"},{"en":"A drawing may show images from memory, feelings of fear, thoughts about family, or ideas about hope.","zh":"一幅畫可能顯示記憶中的影像、恐懼感受、關於家庭的思想或關於希望的意念。"},{"en":"When these inner materials are expressed, the therapist can understand the client more deeply.","zh":"當這些內在材料被表達，治療師可以更深入理解求助者。"},{"en":"The phrase lists what art therapy pays close attention to.","zh":"這個片語列出藝術治療密切關注的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"of primary importance","meaning":"最重要的","examples":[{"en":"The patient’s inner world is of primary importance in art therapy.","zh":"病人的內心世界在藝術治療中是最重要的。"},{"en":"Of primary importance means more important than other things in a particular situation.","zh":"of primary importance 指在某情況中比其他事物更重要。"},{"en":"In a fire drill, safety is of primary importance, not speed or appearance.","zh":"在火警演習中，安全最重要，而不是速度或外觀。"},{"en":"In art therapy, the client’s feelings matter more than artistic skill.","zh":"在藝術治療中，求助者的感受比藝術技巧更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main priority.","zh":"這個片語指出主要優先事項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"any type of visual art","meaning":"任何類型的視覺藝術","examples":[{"en":"Any type of visual art can be used in art therapy.","zh":"任何類型的視覺藝術都可以用於藝術治療。"},{"en":"Any type of visual art means any art form that is mainly seen, such as drawing, painting, sculpture, or digital images.","zh":"any type of visual art 指任何主要透過視覺觀看的藝術形式，例如素描、繪畫、雕塑或數碼影像。"},{"en":"A therapist may use clay, collage, photography, or paint depending on the client’s needs.","zh":"治療師可能根據求助者需要使用黏土、拼貼、攝影或顏料。"},{"en":"If one medium feels uncomfortable, another visual art form may work better.","zh":"如果某媒材令人不舒服，另一種視覺藝術形式可能更合適。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses flexibility in artistic materials and methods.","zh":"這個片語強調藝術材料和方法上的靈活性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"medium","meaning":"媒介；藝術媒材","examples":[{"en":"Any visual art medium can be employed in therapy.","zh":"任何視覺藝術媒介都可以用於治療。"},{"en":"A medium is the material or method used to create art, such as paint, clay, pencil, or photography.","zh":"medium 指創作藝術所使用的材料或方法，例如顏料、黏土、鉛筆或攝影。"},{"en":"A student may choose pencil as a medium because it feels easy to control.","zh":"學生可能選擇鉛筆作媒材，因為它感覺容易控制。"},{"en":"If a client has limited hand movement, the therapist may choose a more suitable medium.","zh":"如果求助者手部活動受限，治療師可能選擇更合適的媒材。"},{"en":"The word refers to the means used to make artwork.","zh":"這個詞指製作藝術作品所用的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be employed in","meaning":"被用於","examples":[{"en":"Painting and sculpture can be employed in the therapeutic process.","zh":"繪畫和雕塑可以被用於治療過程。"},{"en":"Be employed in means be used as part of a particular activity or process.","zh":"be employed in 指被用作某特定活動或過程的一部分。"},{"en":"Role-play can be employed in language lessons to practise real conversations.","zh":"角色扮演可以被用於語言課，以練習真實對話。"},{"en":"If different art forms are employed in therapy, clients have more ways to express themselves.","zh":"如果不同藝術形式被用於治療，求助者就有更多方式表達自己。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to say “be used in.”","zh":"這個片語是 “be used in” 的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"therapeutic process","meaning":"治療過程","examples":[{"en":"Different art forms can be used in the therapeutic process.","zh":"不同藝術形式可以用於治療過程。"},{"en":"The therapeutic process is the gradual course of treatment, support, reflection, and change.","zh":"therapeutic process 指治療、支援、反思和改變的逐步過程。"},{"en":"In counselling, the therapeutic process may include trust-building, discussion, practice, and review.","zh":"在輔導中，治療過程可能包括建立信任、討論、練習和檢討。"},{"en":"In art therapy, creative activities become part of the patient’s healing process.","zh":"在藝術治療中，創意活動成為病人療癒過程的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to therapy as an ongoing journey.","zh":"這個片語指治療作為一段持續旅程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"painting, drawing and sculpture","meaning":"繪畫、素描及雕塑","examples":[{"en":"Painting, drawing and sculpture can all be used in art therapy.","zh":"繪畫、素描及雕塑都可以用於藝術治療。"},{"en":"Painting, drawing and sculpture are visual art forms using colour, lines, shapes, and three-dimensional materials.","zh":"painting, drawing and sculpture 是使用顏色、線條、形狀和立體材料的視覺藝術形式。"},{"en":"A patient may choose drawing for quick expression, painting for colour, or sculpture for touch.","zh":"病人可能選擇素描作快速表達，選擇繪畫使用顏色，或選擇雕塑接觸材料。"},{"en":"Different art forms give clients different ways to explore feelings.","zh":"不同藝術形式給求助者不同方式探索感受。"},{"en":"The phrase lists common materials and methods in visual art.","zh":"這個片語列出視覺藝術中常見的材料和方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"photography and digital art","meaning":"攝影及數碼藝術","examples":[{"en":"Photography and digital art can be employed in the therapeutic process.","zh":"攝影及數碼藝術可以被用於治療過程。"},{"en":"Photography and digital art are visual forms that use cameras, computers, tablets, or digital tools.","zh":"photography and digital art 指使用相機、電腦、平板或數碼工具的視覺形式。"},{"en":"A teenager may use photography to show places that feel safe or stressful.","zh":"青少年可能使用攝影展示令自己感到安全或有壓力的地方。"},{"en":"Digital art can help clients who prefer screens or have difficulty using traditional materials.","zh":"數碼藝術可以幫助偏好螢幕或難以使用傳統材料的求助者。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that modern media can also be used in therapy.","zh":"這個片語顯示現代媒體也可以用於治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be led by","meaning":"由……帶領","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy sessions are usually led by qualified professionals.","zh":"藝術治療課節通常由合資格專業人士帶領。"},{"en":"Be led by means be guided, directed, or managed by someone.","zh":"be led by 指由某人引導、指揮或管理。"},{"en":"A school workshop may be led by a trained counsellor.","zh":"學校工作坊可能由受訓輔導員帶領。"},{"en":"If a therapy session is led by a qualified professional, clients are more likely to receive safe support.","zh":"如果治療課節由合資格專業人士帶領，求助者更可能獲得安全支援。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who guides the activity.","zh":"這個片語指出由誰引導活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"qualified professionals","meaning":"合資格專業人士","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy sessions are usually led by qualified professionals.","zh":"藝術治療課節通常由合資格專業人士帶領。"},{"en":"Qualified professionals are people who have the training, education, and approval needed to do specialist work.","zh":"qualified professionals 指具有從事專門工作所需訓練、教育和認可的人。"},{"en":"A hospital should hire qualified professionals to handle counselling, medicine, and rehabilitation.","zh":"醫院應聘請合資格專業人士處理輔導、醫療和康復。"},{"en":"If therapy is led by unqualified people, clients may be put at risk.","zh":"如果治療由不合資格人士帶領，求助者可能面對風險。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses proper training and competence.","zh":"這個片語強調適當訓練和能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"primary role","meaning":"主要角色","examples":[{"en":"The therapist’s primary role is to guide the patient’s artistic expression.","zh":"治療師的主要角色是引導病人的藝術表達。"},{"en":"Primary role means the main duty or most important function someone has.","zh":"primary role 指某人最主要的職責或最重要功能。"},{"en":"A teacher’s primary role is to help students learn, not simply to give marks.","zh":"老師的主要角色是幫助學生學習，而不只是給分。"},{"en":"If the therapist’s primary role is guidance, they support rather than control the client’s expression.","zh":"如果治療師的主要角色是引導，他們就是支援而不是控制求助者表達。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the central responsibility.","zh":"這個片語指出核心責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"attend to","meaning":"留意；照顧","examples":[{"en":"The therapist attends to the patient’s artistic expression.","zh":"治療師留意病人的藝術表達。"},{"en":"Attend to means pay careful attention to or take care of something.","zh":"attend to 指仔細留意或照顧某事。"},{"en":"A good teacher attends to students’ questions instead of rushing through the lesson.","zh":"好老師會留意學生問題，而不是匆忙完成課堂。"},{"en":"If a therapist attends carefully to the artwork, the client may feel respected.","zh":"如果治療師細心留意作品，求助者可能感到被尊重。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests active, caring attention.","zh":"這個片語暗示主動而關懷的注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"guide and encourage","meaning":"引導並鼓勵","examples":[{"en":"The therapist guides and encourages the patient’s artistic expression.","zh":"治療師引導並鼓勵病人的藝術表達。"},{"en":"Guide and encourage means gently direct someone while giving confidence and support.","zh":"guide and encourage 指溫和地指引某人，同時給予信心和支援。"},{"en":"A coach guides and encourages beginners by showing technique and praising effort.","zh":"教練透過示範技巧和稱讚努力來引導並鼓勵初學者。"},{"en":"If patients feel guided and encouraged, they may take more creative risks.","zh":"如果病人感到被引導和鼓勵，他們可能更願意作創意嘗試。"},{"en":"The phrase combines direction with emotional support.","zh":"這個片語結合方向和情緒支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"artistic expression","meaning":"藝術表達","examples":[{"en":"The therapist encourages the patient’s artistic expression.","zh":"治療師鼓勵病人的藝術表達。"},{"en":"Artistic expression is the use of art to show feelings, ideas, identity, or experience.","zh":"artistic expression 指使用藝術展示感受、想法、身份或經歷。"},{"en":"A student may use artistic expression to show anger without shouting.","zh":"學生可能使用藝術表達來展示憤怒，而不用大叫。"},{"en":"If people cannot express themselves in words, artistic expression may offer another path.","zh":"如果人們無法用文字表達自己，藝術表達可能提供另一條路。"},{"en":"The phrase describes communication through art.","zh":"這個片語描述透過藝術溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in keeping with","meaning":"與……一致","examples":[{"en":"The therapist’s role is in keeping with the Greek meaning of “therapeia”.","zh":"治療師的角色與 “therapeia” 這個希臘字的意思一致。"},{"en":"In keeping with means consistent with or matching something.","zh":"in keeping with 指與某事一致或相配。"},{"en":"A school’s strict phone policy may be in keeping with its focus on concentration.","zh":"學校嚴格的手機政策可能與其重視專注的方針一致。"},{"en":"If a therapist listens attentively, the practice is in keeping with the idea of care.","zh":"如果治療師細心聆聽，該實踐就與照顧的概念一致。"},{"en":"The phrase shows agreement between an action and a principle.","zh":"這個片語顯示行動與原則相符。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"original sense of","meaning":"……的原本意思","examples":[{"en":"The original sense of the Greek word means “being attentive to”.","zh":"這個希臘字的原本意思是「細心留意」。"},{"en":"The original sense of a word is its earlier or first meaning.","zh":"original sense of a word 指一個詞較早或最初的意思。"},{"en":"A language teacher may explain the original sense of a word before showing modern usage.","zh":"語言老師可能先解釋一個詞的原本意思，再展示現代用法。"},{"en":"If a word’s original sense is remembered, its modern meaning may become clearer.","zh":"如果記住詞語的原本意思，其現代意思可能變得更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to early meaning.","zh":"這個片語指早期意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Greek word","meaning":"希臘字","examples":[{"en":"The Greek word “therapeia” means being attentive to.","zh":"希臘字 “therapeia” 的意思是細心留意。"},{"en":"A Greek word is a word from the Greek language, often used in the history of English terms.","zh":"Greek word 指來自希臘語的詞，常用於英文術語史。"},{"en":"Many medical terms come from Greek words because ancient Greek influenced science and medicine.","zh":"許多醫學術語來自希臘字，因為古希臘影響了科學和醫學。"},{"en":"Knowing a Greek word’s meaning can help students understand modern professional vocabulary.","zh":"了解希臘字的意思可以幫助學生理解現代專業詞彙。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the language origin of a term.","zh":"這個片語指出術語的語言來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"being attentive to","meaning":"對……細心留意","examples":[{"en":"The word “therapeia” carries the meaning of being attentive to someone.","zh":"“therapeia” 這個詞帶有對某人細心留意的意思。"},{"en":"Being attentive to means paying careful, caring attention to a person or need.","zh":"being attentive to 指以關懷方式仔細留意某人或某需要。"},{"en":"A teacher is attentive to students when noticing who is confused or upset.","zh":"老師注意到誰困惑或不安時，就是對學生細心留意。"},{"en":"In therapy, being attentive to the client helps build trust and safety.","zh":"在治療中，對求助者細心留意有助建立信任和安全感。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests careful presence, not passive watching.","zh":"這個片語暗示細心陪伴，而不是被動觀看。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"regulation of","meaning":"對……的規管","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the regulation of art therapy.","zh":"文章討論對藝術治療的規管。"},{"en":"Regulation of something means official control through rules, standards, or laws.","zh":"regulation of something 指透過規則、標準或法律作官方控制。"},{"en":"Regulation of private tutoring may protect students from unqualified teachers.","zh":"對私人補習的規管可能保護學生免受不合資格老師影響。"},{"en":"If a profession lacks regulation, the quality of services may vary widely.","zh":"如果一門專業缺乏規管，服務質素可能差異很大。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to how an activity is officially controlled.","zh":"這個片語指某活動如何受到官方控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"requirements for","meaning":"對……的要求","examples":[{"en":"Requirements for becoming an art therapist vary by country.","zh":"成為藝術治療師的要求因國家而異。"},{"en":"Requirements for something are the conditions or qualifications needed to do it.","zh":"requirements for something 指做某事所需的條件或資格。"},{"en":"Requirements for university entry may include exam results, interviews, and language scores.","zh":"大學入學要求可能包括考試成績、面試和語言分數。"},{"en":"If requirements are strict, fewer untrained people can enter the profession.","zh":"如果要求嚴格，較少未受訓人士能進入該專業。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what must be completed or satisfied.","zh":"這個片語指出必須完成或符合的事項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"those wishing to become","meaning":"希望成為……的人","examples":[{"en":"Those wishing to become an art therapist must meet different requirements.","zh":"希望成為藝術治療師的人必須符合不同要求。"},{"en":"Those wishing to become means people who want to enter a role or profession.","zh":"those wishing to become 指希望進入某角色或專業的人。"},{"en":"Those wishing to become teachers should understand both the subject and classroom management.","zh":"希望成為老師的人應了解科目和課室管理。"},{"en":"If someone wishes to enter a regulated profession, they must check training rules early.","zh":"如果某人希望進入受規管專業，就必須及早查看訓練規則。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people with a career goal.","zh":"這個片語指有職業目標的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"art therapist","meaning":"藝術治療師","examples":[{"en":"An art therapist must usually receive specialist training.","zh":"藝術治療師通常必須接受專門訓練。"},{"en":"An art therapist is a professional who uses art-making to support clients’ emotional, mental, or physical wellbeing.","zh":"art therapist 指使用藝術創作支援求助者情緒、精神或身體健康的專業人士。"},{"en":"An art therapist may work in hospitals, schools, rehabilitation centres, or community services.","zh":"藝術治療師可能在醫院、學校、康復中心或社區服務中工作。"},{"en":"Because clients may be vulnerable, an art therapist needs training and ethical awareness.","zh":"因為求助者可能較脆弱，藝術治療師需要訓練和倫理意識。"},{"en":"The phrase names the professional who provides art therapy.","zh":"這個片語指出提供藝術治療的專業人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"vary from country to country","meaning":"因國家而異","examples":[{"en":"Requirements vary from country to country.","zh":"要求因國家而異。"},{"en":"Vary from country to country means be different in different nations.","zh":"vary from country to country 指在不同國家有所不同。"},{"en":"Driving rules vary from country to country, so travellers should check local laws.","zh":"駕駛規則因國家而異，所以旅客應查閱本地法律。"},{"en":"If professional requirements vary, international qualifications may not be accepted everywhere.","zh":"如果專業要求不同，國際資格未必在每個地方都獲接受。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses differences between national systems.","zh":"這個片語強調國家制度之間的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"entry to the profession","meaning":"進入該專業","examples":[{"en":"Entry to the profession is highly regulated in the USA.","zh":"在美國，進入該專業受到嚴格規管。"},{"en":"Entry to the profession means the process of becoming officially allowed to work in that profession.","zh":"entry to the profession 指正式獲准在某專業中工作的過程。"},{"en":"Entry to the medical profession requires years of training and examinations.","zh":"進入醫學專業需要多年訓練和考試。"},{"en":"If entry is regulated, the public can better trust practitioners’ qualifications.","zh":"如果進入專業受到規管，公眾就更能信任從業者資格。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to joining a professional field.","zh":"這個片語指加入某專業領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"highly regulated","meaning":"受到嚴格規管","examples":[{"en":"Entry to art therapy is highly regulated in the USA.","zh":"在美國，進入藝術治療專業受到嚴格規管。"},{"en":"Highly regulated means controlled by many strict rules, standards, or official requirements.","zh":"highly regulated 指受到許多嚴格規則、標準或官方要求控制。"},{"en":"Aviation is highly regulated because mistakes can endanger many lives.","zh":"航空業受到嚴格規管，因為錯誤可以危及許多人生命。"},{"en":"If art therapy is highly regulated, practitioners must meet training and practice standards.","zh":"如果藝術治療受到嚴格規管，從業者必須符合訓練和實踐標準。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests strong official control.","zh":"這個片語暗示強力官方控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"master’s degree","meaning":"碩士學位","examples":[{"en":"A master’s degree in art therapy is essential in the USA.","zh":"在美國，藝術治療碩士學位是必不可少的。"},{"en":"A master’s degree is a postgraduate academic qualification usually completed after a bachelor’s degree.","zh":"master’s degree 指通常在學士學位後完成的研究生學術資格。"},{"en":"A counsellor may need a master’s degree before practising professionally.","zh":"輔導員可能需要碩士學位才能專業執業。"},{"en":"If a field requires a master’s degree, entry becomes more demanding and specialised.","zh":"如果某領域要求碩士學位，進入門檻就變得更高和更專門。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an advanced university qualification.","zh":"這個片語指高等大學資格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be essential","meaning":"必不可少","examples":[{"en":"A master’s degree is essential for entering the profession in the USA.","zh":"在美國，碩士學位對進入該專業必不可少。"},{"en":"Be essential means be absolutely necessary or very important.","zh":"be essential 指絕對必要或非常重要。"},{"en":"Clear instructions are essential when students complete exam exercises.","zh":"當學生完成考試練習時，清楚指示是必不可少的。"},{"en":"If training is essential, people cannot enter the profession without it.","zh":"如果訓練是必不可少的，人們沒有它就不能進入該專業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that cannot be left out.","zh":"這個片語描述不能缺少的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"enter the profession","meaning":"進入該專業","examples":[{"en":"Those entering the profession must show artistic proficiency.","zh":"進入該專業的人必須展示藝術能力。"},{"en":"Enter the profession means begin working officially in a particular professional field.","zh":"enter the profession 指正式開始在某專業領域工作。"},{"en":"New teachers enter the profession after training, assessment, and school placement.","zh":"新老師完成訓練、評估和學校實習後進入該專業。"},{"en":"If people enter the profession without enough preparation, clients may not receive safe support.","zh":"如果人們在準備不足下進入該專業，求助者可能得不到安全支援。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the start of professional practice.","zh":"這個片語描述專業實踐的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take courses in","meaning":"修讀……課程","examples":[{"en":"Candidates must take courses in several studio art disciplines.","zh":"申請人必須修讀幾個工作室藝術學科的課程。"},{"en":"Take courses in means study particular subjects or areas through organised classes.","zh":"take courses in 指透過有組織課堂學習特定科目或領域。"},{"en":"A student may take courses in psychology before applying for counselling training.","zh":"學生申請輔導訓練前，可能修讀心理學課程。"},{"en":"If candidates take studio art courses, they can develop practical artistic skills.","zh":"如果申請人修讀工作室藝術課程，就能發展實際藝術技能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formal study of a subject.","zh":"這個片語描述正式學習某科目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"studio art disciplines","meaning":"工作室藝術學科","examples":[{"en":"Candidates must study a variety of studio art disciplines.","zh":"申請人必須學習多種工作室藝術學科。"},{"en":"Studio art disciplines are practical art areas such as drawing, painting, sculpture, ceramics, or printmaking.","zh":"studio art disciplines 指素描、繪畫、雕塑、陶藝或版畫等實踐藝術範疇。"},{"en":"An art student may explore several studio art disciplines before choosing a specialism.","zh":"藝術學生可能先探索幾個工作室藝術學科，再選擇專修方向。"},{"en":"Art therapists need studio experience so they can understand materials and creative processes.","zh":"藝術治療師需要工作室經驗，才能理解材料和創作過程。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to hands-on art subjects.","zh":"這個片語指動手實踐的藝術科目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"demonstrate artistic proficiency","meaning":"展示藝術能力","examples":[{"en":"Candidates must demonstrate artistic proficiency.","zh":"申請人必須展示藝術能力。"},{"en":"Demonstrate artistic proficiency means show that one has sufficient skill and understanding in making art.","zh":"demonstrate artistic proficiency 指顯示自己在藝術創作上有足夠技能和理解。"},{"en":"A portfolio can help students demonstrate artistic proficiency when applying to art school.","zh":"作品集可以幫助學生申請藝術學校時展示藝術能力。"},{"en":"If therapists understand art materials well, they can guide clients more safely and flexibly.","zh":"如果治療師充分理解藝術材料，就能更安全和靈活地引導求助者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes proving practical artistic ability.","zh":"這個片語描述證明實際藝術能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"artistic proficiency","meaning":"藝術能力","examples":[{"en":"Studio art courses help candidates demonstrate artistic proficiency.","zh":"工作室藝術課程幫助申請人展示藝術能力。"},{"en":"Artistic proficiency is the ability to use artistic materials and techniques competently.","zh":"artistic proficiency 指有能力熟練使用藝術材料和技巧。"},{"en":"A student shows artistic proficiency by controlling line, colour, composition, and materials.","zh":"學生透過控制線條、顏色、構圖和材料展示藝術能力。"},{"en":"In art therapy training, artistic proficiency helps practitioners understand the creative process from experience.","zh":"在藝術治療訓練中，藝術能力幫助從業者從經驗理解創作過程。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to skill in making art.","zh":"這個片語指創作藝術的技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"on completion of","meaning":"在完成……後","examples":[{"en":"On completion of the master’s degree, candidates need supervised client contact.","zh":"在完成碩士學位後，申請人需要受監督的客戶接觸。"},{"en":"On completion of means after finishing something.","zh":"on completion of 指在完成某事後。"},{"en":"On completion of the course, students receive a certificate.","zh":"完成課程後，學生會收到證書。"},{"en":"If candidates need more practice after the degree, training continues beyond classroom study.","zh":"如果申請人在學位後仍需要更多實踐，訓練就超越課堂學習。"},{"en":"The phrase marks what happens after a requirement is finished.","zh":"這個片語標示完成某要求後發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"candidates","meaning":"申請人；候選人","examples":[{"en":"Candidates must complete postgraduate direct client contact.","zh":"申請人必須完成研究生階段的直接客戶接觸。"},{"en":"Candidates are people applying for a position, qualification, exam, or professional status.","zh":"candidates 指申請職位、資格、考試或專業身份的人。"},{"en":"Job candidates prepare CVs and interviews before meeting employers.","zh":"求職者在見僱主前會準備履歷和面試。"},{"en":"If candidates do not meet the requirements, they may not enter the profession.","zh":"如果申請人不符合要求，就可能不能進入該專業。"},{"en":"The word refers to applicants being considered or assessed.","zh":"這個詞指正在被考慮或評估的申請者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"at least","meaning":"至少","examples":[{"en":"Candidates must complete at least 1,000 hours of client contact.","zh":"申請人必須完成至少1,000小時的客戶接觸。"},{"en":"At least means no less than a particular amount or number.","zh":"at least 指不少於某個數量或數字。"},{"en":"Students should sleep at least seven hours before an important exam.","zh":"學生在重要考試前應至少睡七小時。"},{"en":"If a rule says at least 1,000 hours, 900 hours is not enough.","zh":"如果規則說至少1,000小時，900小時就不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a minimum requirement.","zh":"這個片語設定最低要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"postgraduate direct client contact","meaning":"研究生階段的直接客戶接觸","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need postgraduate direct client contact after the master’s degree.","zh":"申請人在碩士學位後需要研究生階段的直接客戶接觸。"},{"en":"Postgraduate direct client contact means supervised practical work with clients after graduate-level study.","zh":"postgraduate direct client contact 指研究生程度學習後，在監督下與客戶進行的實踐工作。"},{"en":"A trainee counsellor may need direct client contact before becoming fully qualified.","zh":"實習輔導員在完全合資格前可能需要直接客戶接觸。"},{"en":"Practical contact helps trainees apply theory to real people’s needs.","zh":"實踐接觸幫助受訓者把理論應用到真人需要上。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to hands-on professional experience after advanced study.","zh":"這個片語指高階學習後的實際專業經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be approved by","meaning":"獲……批准","examples":[{"en":"The client contact must be approved by the American Art Therapy Association.","zh":"客戶接觸必須獲美國藝術治療協會批准。"},{"en":"Be approved by means be officially accepted or authorised by a person or organisation.","zh":"be approved by 指由某人或組織正式接受或授權。"},{"en":"A school trip must be approved by the principal before students can go.","zh":"學校旅行必須獲校長批准，學生才可以去。"},{"en":"If training hours are approved by a professional body, they count toward qualification.","zh":"如果訓練時數獲專業團體批准，就可計入資格要求。"},{"en":"The phrase shows official permission or recognition.","zh":"這個片語顯示官方許可或認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"American Art Therapy Association","meaning":"美國藝術治療協會","examples":[{"en":"The American Art Therapy Association approves the required client contact.","zh":"美國藝術治療協會批准所需的客戶接觸。"},{"en":"The American Art Therapy Association is a professional organisation connected with art therapy in the United States.","zh":"American Art Therapy Association 指與美國藝術治療相關的專業組織。"},{"en":"A professional association can set standards, support training, and guide ethical practice.","zh":"專業協會可以設定標準、支援訓練並引導倫理實踐。"},{"en":"If an association approves training, it helps protect professional quality.","zh":"如果協會批准訓練，就有助保護專業質素。"},{"en":"The phrase names a key organisation in art therapy regulation.","zh":"這個片語指出藝術治療規管中的關鍵組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"whilst","meaning":"雖然","examples":[{"en":"Whilst entry is regulated in the USA, this is not true everywhere.","zh":"雖然在美國進入該專業受到規管，但同樣情況並非適用於所有地方。"},{"en":"Whilst means although or while, often used in more formal British English.","zh":"whilst 指雖然或當……時，常見於較正式英式英語。"},{"en":"Whilst online learning is convenient, some students still need face-to-face support.","zh":"雖然網上學習方便，有些學生仍需要面對面支援。"},{"en":"This word introduces a contrast between two situations.","zh":"這個詞引出兩種情況之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is similar to “although” when showing contrast.","zh":"當表示對比時，它與 “although” 相似。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"strictly regulated","meaning":"受到嚴格規管","examples":[{"en":"Entry to the profession is strictly regulated in the USA.","zh":"在美國，進入該專業受到嚴格規管。"},{"en":"Strictly regulated means controlled by clear and firm rules.","zh":"strictly regulated 指受到清楚而嚴格的規則控制。"},{"en":"Medicines are strictly regulated because unsafe products can harm patients.","zh":"藥物受到嚴格規管，因為不安全產品可以傷害病人。"},{"en":"If entry to therapy is strictly regulated, clients are more likely to receive qualified care.","zh":"如果進入治療專業受到嚴格規管，求助者更可能獲得合資格照顧。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong rule-based control.","zh":"這個片語描述強力規則控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the same does not hold true for","meaning":"同樣情況並不適用於……","examples":[{"en":"The same does not hold true for many other countries.","zh":"同樣情況並不適用於許多其他國家。"},{"en":"The same does not hold true for means the situation is not the same in another case.","zh":"the same does not hold true for 指在另一情況中並非相同。"},{"en":"Some schools require uniforms, but the same does not hold true for all international schools.","zh":"有些學校要求穿校服，但同樣情況並不適用於所有國際學校。"},{"en":"If one country regulates a profession strictly, other countries may not follow the same model.","zh":"如果一個國家嚴格規管某專業，其他國家未必跟從同一模式。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts one situation with another.","zh":"這個片語對比一種情況與另一種情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"developing field","meaning":"發展中的領域","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy is still considered a developing field.","zh":"藝術治療仍被視為發展中的領域。"},{"en":"A developing field is an area of knowledge or practice that is still growing and becoming more established.","zh":"developing field 指仍在成長並逐步確立的知識或實踐範疇。"},{"en":"Artificial intelligence in education is a developing field with changing rules and methods.","zh":"教育中的人工智能是一個發展中的領域，其規則和方法仍在改變。"},{"en":"If a field is developing, training standards may differ between places.","zh":"如果一個領域仍在發展，不同地方的訓練標準可能不同。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests growth, change, and incomplete establishment.","zh":"這個片語暗示成長、變化和未完全確立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"as such","meaning":"因此；基於這一點","examples":[{"en":"As such, art therapy remains unregulated in many countries.","zh":"因此，藝術治療在許多國家仍未受規管。"},{"en":"As such means because of this or in that role or condition.","zh":"as such 指因此、基於這一點，或以該身份／狀態而言。"},{"en":"The programme is still experimental; as such, it may change next year.","zh":"該計劃仍屬實驗性；因此，明年可能改變。"},{"en":"If art therapy is a developing field, it may not yet have full regulation everywhere.","zh":"如果藝術治療是發展中的領域，它可能尚未在各地受到完整規管。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a previous point to its consequence.","zh":"這個片語把前一點與其結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"truly established as","meaning":"真正確立為……","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy is not yet truly established as a therapy in some countries.","zh":"在一些國家，藝術治療尚未真正確立為一種治療。"},{"en":"Truly established as means fully recognised and accepted in a particular role.","zh":"truly established as 指在某特定角色中被完全承認和接受。"},{"en":"Online teaching became truly established as a normal option after schools used it widely.","zh":"當學校廣泛使用網上教學後，它才真正確立為正常選項。"},{"en":"If a practice is not truly established, people may question its standards or status.","zh":"如果某做法尚未真正確立，人們可能質疑其標準或地位。"},{"en":"The phrase describes full acceptance, not just early use.","zh":"這個片語描述完整接受，而不只是早期使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"practice and application","meaning":"實踐及應用","examples":[{"en":"The practice and application of art therapy remain unregulated in many places.","zh":"藝術治療的實踐及應用在許多地方仍未受規管。"},{"en":"Practice and application mean how something is actually used in real situations.","zh":"practice and application 指某事在現實情況中實際如何被使用。"},{"en":"A theory may sound good, but its practice and application in schools can be difficult.","zh":"一個理論可能聽起來很好，但在學校中的實踐及應用可能困難。"},{"en":"If practice is unregulated, different therapists may use very different methods.","zh":"如果實踐未受規管，不同治療師可能使用非常不同的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase moves from idea to real-world use.","zh":"這個片語由想法轉向現實使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"remain unregulated","meaning":"仍未受規管","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy will remain unregulated in many countries for some time.","zh":"藝術治療在許多國家未來一段時間內仍會未受規管。"},{"en":"Remain unregulated means continue without official rules, standards, or legal control.","zh":"remain unregulated 指繼續沒有官方規則、標準或法律控制。"},{"en":"A new online service may remain unregulated until the government creates clear laws.","zh":"新網上服務可能一直未受規管，直到政府制定清楚法律。"},{"en":"If therapy remains unregulated, clients may find it harder to judge practitioner quality.","zh":"如果治療仍未受規管，求助者可能更難判斷從業者質素。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a continuing lack of formal control.","zh":"這個片語描述正式控制的持續缺乏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"for some time yet","meaning":"在未來一段時間內仍然","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy may remain unregulated for some time yet.","zh":"藝術治療在未來一段時間內仍可能未受規管。"},{"en":"For some time yet means for a further period into the future.","zh":"for some time yet 指在未來一段時間內仍然如此。"},{"en":"The school building may remain under repair for some time yet.","zh":"校舍在未來一段時間內仍可能維修中。"},{"en":"If a field is still developing, regulation may take some time yet to appear.","zh":"如果一個領域仍在發展，規管可能仍需要一段時間才會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests the situation will continue.","zh":"這個片語暗示情況會繼續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements agree with the information in the text.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與文中資料一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the information means match what the text says.","zh":"agree with the information 指與文本所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the text says art therapy began as a profession in the mid-20th century, a similar statement agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文本說藝術治療作為專業始於20世紀中期，意思相同的陳述就與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should check meaning carefully, not only repeated words.","zh":"學生應仔細檢查意思，而不只是重複字詞。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in TRUE, FALSE and NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於 TRUE、FALSE 和 NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"information given in the text","meaning":"文中給出的資料","examples":[{"en":"The statements must be checked against the information given in the text.","zh":"陳述必須與文中給出的資料核對。"},{"en":"Information given in the text means facts or details actually stated in the passage.","zh":"information given in the text 指文章實際陳述的事實或細節。"},{"en":"In reading exams, students should use information given in the text rather than outside knowledge.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生應使用文中給出的資料，而不是外部知識。"},{"en":"If the text does not mention a point, students should not invent an answer.","zh":"如果文本沒有提到某點，學生不應自行編造答案。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds learners to rely on the passage.","zh":"這個片語提醒學習者依據文章。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相反","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章中的資料相反。"},{"en":"Contradict the information means say the opposite of what the text states.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文本陳述相反的意思。"},{"en":"If the passage says two approaches can overlap, a statement saying they never overlap contradicts it.","zh":"如果文章說兩種取向可以重疊，而陳述說它們從不重疊，就是與資料相反。"},{"en":"Students should choose FALSE only when the conflict is clear.","zh":"學生只有在衝突清楚時才應選 FALSE。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct disagreement with the text.","zh":"這個片語描述與文本直接不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students write “NOT GIVEN” when there is no information on this.","zh":"當文中沒有相關資料時，學生寫 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the text does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文本沒有說明陳述是真還是假。"},{"en":"If the passage discusses training but not salaries, there is no information on salaries.","zh":"如果文章討論訓練但沒有討論薪金，文中就沒有薪金相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when the passage gives no evidence.","zh":"當文章沒有證據時，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase explains when NOT GIVEN is the correct answer.","zh":"這個片語解釋何時 NOT GIVEN 是正確答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be strongly influenced by","meaning":"深受……影響","examples":[{"en":"The statement claims that Hill was strongly influenced by psychoanalytic theories.","zh":"該陳述聲稱 Hill 深受精神分析理論影響。"},{"en":"Be strongly influenced by means be shaped in an important way by someone or something.","zh":"be strongly influenced by 指被某人或某事以重要方式塑造。"},{"en":"A student may be strongly influenced by a teacher who encourages daily reading.","zh":"學生可能深受鼓勵每日閱讀的老師影響。"},{"en":"If a therapist is strongly influenced by one theory, their practice may follow that theory closely.","zh":"如果治療師深受某理論影響，其實踐可能緊密跟隨該理論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes powerful influence, not a small suggestion.","zh":"這個片語描述強大影響，而不是小小建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"psychoanalytic theories","meaning":"精神分析理論","examples":[{"en":"Psychoanalytic theories influenced some approaches to art therapy.","zh":"精神分析理論影響了一些藝術治療取向。"},{"en":"Psychoanalytic theories are ideas about unconscious feelings, hidden conflicts, and the influence of past experience.","zh":"psychoanalytic theories 指關於潛意識感受、隱藏衝突和過去經歷影響的觀念。"},{"en":"A counsellor may use psychoanalytic theories to explore why a fear keeps returning.","zh":"輔導員可能使用精神分析理論探索某種恐懼為何反覆出現。"},{"en":"In art therapy, these theories may lead therapists to analyse symbols in artwork.","zh":"在藝術治療中，這些理論可能使治療師分析作品中的象徵。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to theory, not one single technique.","zh":"這個片語指理論，而不是單一技巧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"formulate ideas on","meaning":"形成關於……的想法","examples":[{"en":"Adrian Hill formulated his ideas on art therapy during his recovery.","zh":"Adrian Hill 在康復期間形成關於藝術治療的想法。"},{"en":"Formulate ideas on means develop and organise thoughts about a subject.","zh":"formulate ideas on 指發展並組織關於某主題的想法。"},{"en":"Students formulate ideas on an essay topic by brainstorming examples and reasons.","zh":"學生透過腦震盪例子和理由，形成關於作文題目的想法。"},{"en":"If Hill formed his ideas during recovery, illness helped shape his view of art.","zh":"如果 Hill 在康復期間形成想法，疾病就幫助塑造他對藝術的看法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating a clear set of thoughts.","zh":"這個片語描述建立一套清楚想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"focus on treating","meaning":"專注於治療","examples":[{"en":"Modern art therapy focuses on treating mental and physical health problems.","zh":"現代藝術治療專注於治療精神和身體健康問題。"},{"en":"Focus on treating means give main attention to helping or managing a condition.","zh":"focus on treating 指主要關注幫助或管理某狀況。"},{"en":"A clinic may focus on treating children with speech difficulties.","zh":"診所可能專注於治療有言語困難的兒童。"},{"en":"If therapy focuses on treating health problems, it must be guided by professional care.","zh":"如果治療專注於處理健康問題，就必須由專業照護引導。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main purpose of a treatment.","zh":"這個片語指出治療的主要目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"mental or physical health problems","meaning":"精神或身體健康問題","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy can support people with mental or physical health problems.","zh":"藝術治療可以支援有精神或身體健康問題的人。"},{"en":"Mental or physical health problems are difficulties affecting the mind, emotions, or body.","zh":"mental or physical health problems 指影響思想、情緒或身體的困難。"},{"en":"Anxiety is a mental health problem, while chronic pain is a physical health problem.","zh":"焦慮是精神健康問題，而慢性疼痛是身體健康問題。"},{"en":"If illness affects both body and mood, supportive therapy may help the whole person.","zh":"如果疾病同時影響身體和心情，支援性治療可能幫助整個人。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both psychological and bodily conditions.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋心理和身體狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"deal with moral issues","meaning":"處理道德問題","examples":[{"en":"The statement contrasts treating illness with dealing with moral issues.","zh":"該陳述把治療疾病與處理道德問題作對比。"},{"en":"Deal with moral issues means address questions of right, wrong, values, or ethical behaviour.","zh":"deal with moral issues 指處理關於對錯、價值或倫理行為的問題。"},{"en":"A school may deal with moral issues when discussing cheating or bullying.","zh":"學校討論作弊或欺凌時，可能是在處理道德問題。"},{"en":"If therapy treats illness rather than moral issues, it focuses on health, not judging character.","zh":"如果治療處理疾病而不是道德問題，它就集中於健康，而不是評判品格。"},{"en":"The phrase describes handling ethical questions.","zh":"這個片語描述處理倫理問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be broadly considered to be","meaning":"可大致被視為","examples":[{"en":"Approaches to art therapy can be broadly considered to be creative or psychoanalytic.","zh":"藝術治療取向可大致被視為創作取向或精神分析取向。"},{"en":"Be broadly considered to be means be generally understood or classified as something.","zh":"be broadly considered to be 指一般被理解或分類為某事。"},{"en":"School subjects can be broadly considered to be practical, academic, or artistic.","zh":"學校科目可大致被視為實用、學術或藝術類。"},{"en":"If approaches are broadly considered in two types, details may still overlap.","zh":"如果取向大致分成兩類，細節仍可能重疊。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a general classification, not a strict rule.","zh":"這個片語給出一般分類，而不是嚴格規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"creative or psychoanalytic","meaning":"創作取向或精神分析取向","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy approaches may be creative or psychoanalytic.","zh":"藝術治療取向可能是創作取向或精神分析取向。"},{"en":"Creative or psychoanalytic means focused either on the art-making process or on psychological analysis.","zh":"creative or psychoanalytic 指集中於藝術創作過程，或集中於心理分析。"},{"en":"A therapist may use a creative approach one day and a psychoanalytic discussion another day.","zh":"治療師可能某天使用創作取向，另一天使用精神分析討論。"},{"en":"If both approaches help the client, they may be combined in practice.","zh":"如果兩種取向都幫到求助者，它們可以在實踐中結合。"},{"en":"The phrase names two major ways of understanding art therapy.","zh":"這個片語指出理解藝術治療的兩種主要方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"practitioners tend to","meaning":"從業者往往會","examples":[{"en":"The statement says that practitioners tend to avoid combining the two approaches.","zh":"該陳述說從業者往往會避免結合兩種取向。"},{"en":"Practitioners tend to means people working in a field usually or commonly do something.","zh":"practitioners tend to 指某領域工作者通常或常常做某事。"},{"en":"Teachers tend to give more examples when students look confused.","zh":"當學生看起來困惑時，老師往往會給更多例子。"},{"en":"If practitioners tend to follow one method, a field may develop clear schools of practice.","zh":"如果從業者往往跟隨一種方法，某領域可能發展出清楚的實踐流派。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a general habit, not an absolute rule.","zh":"這個片語描述一般習慣，而不是絕對規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"avoid combining","meaning":"避免結合","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not say that therapists avoid combining the two practices.","zh":"文章沒有說治療師避免結合兩種實踐。"},{"en":"Avoid combining means deliberately not mix two things together.","zh":"avoid combining 指刻意不把兩件事混合在一起。"},{"en":"A student may avoid combining too many difficult structures in one sentence.","zh":"學生可能避免在一句中結合太多困難句式。"},{"en":"If two therapy approaches are not incompatible, practitioners may not need to avoid combining them.","zh":"如果兩種治療取向並非不能並存，從業者未必需要避免結合它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes choosing not to mix methods or elements.","zh":"這個片語描述選擇不混合方法或元素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"schools of practice","meaning":"實踐流派","examples":[{"en":"The two schools of practice can overlap.","zh":"這兩個實踐流派可以重疊。"},{"en":"Schools of practice are recognised approaches or traditions within a profession.","zh":"schools of practice 指某專業內受承認的取向或傳統。"},{"en":"In teaching, one school of practice may stress exams, while another stresses creativity.","zh":"在教學中，一個實踐流派可能強調考試，另一個強調創意。"},{"en":"If schools of practice overlap, real professionals may use ideas from both.","zh":"如果實踐流派有重疊，真正專業人士可能同時使用兩者的想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes different professional approaches.","zh":"這個片語描述不同專業取向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"respond best to","meaning":"對……反應最好","examples":[{"en":"The statement discusses which clients respond best to art therapy.","zh":"該陳述討論哪些求助者對藝術治療反應最好。"},{"en":"Respond best to means benefit most from or react most positively to something.","zh":"respond best to 指從某事中受益最多或作出最正面反應。"},{"en":"Some students respond best to visual examples, while others need spoken explanation.","zh":"有些學生對視覺例子反應最好，另一些則需要口頭解釋。"},{"en":"If clients respond best to art therapy, they may become calmer and more expressive.","zh":"如果求助者對藝術治療反應最好，他們可能變得更平靜和更能表達。"},{"en":"The phrase compares what works most effectively for someone.","zh":"這個片語比較甚麼對某人最有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"previous background in art","meaning":"以往的藝術背景","examples":[{"en":"A previous background in art is not described as necessary.","zh":"文中沒有描述以往的藝術背景是必要的。"},{"en":"A previous background in art means earlier experience, study, or training in art.","zh":"previous background in art 指早前在藝術方面的經驗、學習或訓練。"},{"en":"A student without a previous background in art can still enjoy drawing freely.","zh":"沒有以往藝術背景的學生仍可以享受自由繪畫。"},{"en":"If therapy focuses on expression, artistic training may not be required for clients.","zh":"如果治療集中於表達，求助者未必需要藝術訓練。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to earlier art experience.","zh":"這個片語指早前的藝術經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be more concerned with","meaning":"更關注","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy is more concerned with expression than with artistic skill.","zh":"藝術治療更關注表達，而不是藝術技巧。"},{"en":"Be more concerned with means care more about one thing than another.","zh":"be more concerned with 指比起另一事物，更關心某事。"},{"en":"A good doctor is more concerned with patient safety than with finishing quickly.","zh":"好醫生更關注病人安全，而不是快速完成。"},{"en":"If therapy is more concerned with expression, imperfect drawings can still be meaningful.","zh":"如果治療更關注表達，不完美的圖畫仍可以有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase shows priority.","zh":"這個片語顯示優先次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"expression through art","meaning":"透過藝術表達","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy emphasises expression through art.","zh":"藝術治療強調透過藝術表達。"},{"en":"Expression through art means communicating feelings, thoughts, or experiences by making images or objects.","zh":"expression through art 指透過創作影像或物件來傳達感受、思想或經歷。"},{"en":"A child may show sadness through art by drawing a lonely figure.","zh":"孩子可能透過畫孤單人物來透過藝術表達悲傷。"},{"en":"If words feel too difficult, expression through art can offer another route.","zh":"如果語言感覺太困難，透過藝術表達可以提供另一條路。"},{"en":"The phrase describes art as a communication method.","zh":"這個片語描述藝術作為溝通方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"artwork created","meaning":"創作出來的藝術作品","examples":[{"en":"The therapy focuses more on expression than on the artwork created.","zh":"治療更集中於表達，而不是創作出來的藝術作品。"},{"en":"Artwork created means the final picture, sculpture, or visual piece produced by a person.","zh":"artwork created 指某人創作出的最終圖畫、雕塑或視覺作品。"},{"en":"In art class, the artwork created may be graded for technique and appearance.","zh":"在藝術班中，創作出來的藝術作品可能按技巧和外觀評分。"},{"en":"In therapy, the artwork created matters because of what it expresses, not because it is perfect.","zh":"在治療中，創作出來的藝術作品重要，是因為它表達了甚麼，而不是因為它完美。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the finished creative product.","zh":"這個片語指完成的創意產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"insufficiently qualified","meaning":"資歷不足","examples":[{"en":"The statement suggests that many art therapists are insufficiently qualified.","zh":"該陳述暗示許多藝術治療師資歷不足。"},{"en":"Insufficiently qualified means not having enough training, education, or approval for a role.","zh":"insufficiently qualified 指沒有足夠訓練、教育或認可去擔任某角色。"},{"en":"A person is insufficiently qualified to drive a bus if they have no proper licence.","zh":"如果一個人沒有適當牌照，就沒有足夠資格駕駛巴士。"},{"en":"If therapists are insufficiently qualified, clients may not receive safe or effective support.","zh":"如果治療師資歷不足，求助者可能得不到安全或有效支援。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a lack of required competence or credentials.","zh":"這個片語描述缺乏所需能力或證書。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be aware of","meaning":"知道；意識到","examples":[{"en":"Therapists should be aware of the regulations in their country.","zh":"治療師應知道其國家的規例。"},{"en":"Be aware of means know about or notice something important.","zh":"be aware of 指知道或注意到重要事情。"},{"en":"Students should be aware of exam time limits before they start writing.","zh":"學生開始寫作前，應知道考試時間限制。"},{"en":"If therapists are aware of local regulations, they can practise more responsibly.","zh":"如果治療師知道本地規例，就能更負責任地執業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes knowledge and attention.","zh":"這個片語描述知識和注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"regulations regarding","meaning":"關於……的規例","examples":[{"en":"Some countries have regulations regarding the practice of art therapy.","zh":"有些國家有關於藝術治療實踐的規例。"},{"en":"Regulations regarding something are official rules about that activity or issue.","zh":"regulations regarding something 指關於某活動或議題的官方規則。"},{"en":"Schools must follow regulations regarding student safety and data privacy.","zh":"學校必須遵守關於學生安全和資料私隱的規例。"},{"en":"If regulations regarding therapy are clear, clients can better understand their protections.","zh":"如果關於治療的規例清楚，求助者就能更明白自己的保障。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the topic controlled by rules.","zh":"這個片語引出受規則控制的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"practice of art therapy","meaning":"藝術治療的實踐","examples":[{"en":"The practice of art therapy is unregulated in many countries.","zh":"藝術治療的實踐在許多國家未受規管。"},{"en":"The practice of art therapy means the actual professional use of art therapy with clients.","zh":"practice of art therapy 指與求助者進行藝術治療的實際專業使用。"},{"en":"The practice of art therapy may include assessment, creative work, discussion, and reflection.","zh":"藝術治療的實踐可能包括評估、創作、討論和反思。"},{"en":"If the practice is unregulated, training and methods may differ widely.","zh":"如果實踐未受規管，訓練和方法可能差異很大。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to how art therapy is carried out in real life.","zh":"這個片語指藝術治療在現實生活中如何進行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"limited interaction between","meaning":"……之間有限的互動","examples":[{"en":"The statement says that sessions involve limited interaction between therapist and client.","zh":"該陳述說課節涉及治療師與求助者之間有限的互動。"},{"en":"Limited interaction between means only a small amount of communication or contact between two sides.","zh":"limited interaction between 指兩方之間只有少量溝通或接觸。"},{"en":"Online lessons may have limited interaction between teacher and students if cameras and microphones are off.","zh":"如果鏡頭和麥克風關閉，網課中老師和學生之間可能互動有限。"},{"en":"If therapy had limited interaction, it would be harder to guide and encourage the client.","zh":"如果治療互動有限，就較難引導和鼓勵求助者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes restricted communication.","zh":"這個片語描述受限制的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"therapist and client","meaning":"治療師與求助者","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy involves interaction between the therapist and client.","zh":"藝術治療涉及治療師與求助者之間的互動。"},{"en":"Therapist and client means the professional providing therapy and the person receiving support.","zh":"therapist and client 指提供治療的專業人士和接受支援的人。"},{"en":"Trust between therapist and client is important in counselling and art therapy.","zh":"在輔導和藝術治療中，治療師與求助者之間的信任很重要。"},{"en":"If the client feels judged, communication with the therapist may become difficult.","zh":"如果求助者感到被評判，與治療師的溝通可能變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the two main people in a therapy relationship.","zh":"這個片語指出治療關係中的兩個主要人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete the sentences below","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the sentences below using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成以下句子。"},{"en":"Complete the sentences below means fill in the missing parts of the sentences that follow.","zh":"complete the sentences below 指填上接下來句子中缺失的部分。"},{"en":"In reading exams, students complete the sentences below by copying suitable words from the text.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生透過從文章抄寫合適字詞來完成以下句子。"},{"en":"If the grammar of the sentence does not fit, the answer may be wrong.","zh":"如果句子文法不合，答案可能錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個詞","examples":[{"en":"The answer should use no more than three words from the passage.","zh":"答案應使用文章中不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案必須包含三個詞或更少。"},{"en":"“Creative process” is acceptable under a three-word limit.","zh":"“Creative process” 符合三詞限制。"},{"en":"If students write four words, they may lose the mark even if the idea is correct.","zh":"如果學生寫四個詞，即使意思正確，也可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個片語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"early pioneers of","meaning":"……的早期先驅","examples":[{"en":"The early pioneers of art therapy admitted that they were influenced by other disciplines.","zh":"藝術治療的早期先驅承認他們受到其他學科影響。"},{"en":"Early pioneers of a field are the first people who develop, promote, or practise it.","zh":"early pioneers of a field 指最早發展、推動或實踐某領域的人。"},{"en":"Early pioneers of aviation took risks before flying became safe and common.","zh":"航空業早期先驅在飛行變得安全和普遍前承擔風險。"},{"en":"Because pioneers work before rules are fully formed, they often shape later standards.","zh":"因為先驅在規則尚未完全形成前工作，他們常塑造後來標準。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the first important developers of a field.","zh":"這個片語指某領域最早的重要發展者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"admit that","meaning":"承認","examples":[{"en":"The early pioneers admitted that their beliefs had been shaped by many influences.","zh":"早期先驅承認他們的信念受到許多影響塑造。"},{"en":"Admit that means accept or say openly that something is true.","zh":"admit that 指接受或公開說出某事是真實的。"},{"en":"A student may admit that they did not understand the homework instructions.","zh":"學生可能承認自己不明白功課指示。"},{"en":"If practitioners admit outside influence, they show honesty about how their ideas developed.","zh":"如果從業者承認外來影響，他們就誠實展示自己的想法如何發展。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an open acknowledgement.","zh":"這個片語引出公開承認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be shaped by","meaning":"受……塑造","examples":[{"en":"Their beliefs had been shaped by a variety of influences.","zh":"他們的信念受到多種影響塑造。"},{"en":"Be shaped by means be formed or influenced by something over time.","zh":"be shaped by 指隨時間由某事形成或影響。"},{"en":"A child’s confidence can be shaped by family support and school experiences.","zh":"孩子的信心可以受家庭支援和學校經歷塑造。"},{"en":"If a profession is shaped by several disciplines, its methods may become mixed and flexible.","zh":"如果一門專業受幾個學科塑造，其方法可能變得混合而靈活。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how something develops under influence.","zh":"這個片語描述某事如何在影響下發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a variety of influences","meaning":"多種影響","examples":[{"en":"Early art therapists were shaped by a variety of influences.","zh":"早期藝術治療師受到多種影響塑造。"},{"en":"A variety of influences means many different things that affect how ideas or behaviour develop.","zh":"a variety of influences 指許多不同事物影響想法或行為如何發展。"},{"en":"A student’s career choice may reflect a variety of influences, including family, teachers, and interests.","zh":"學生的職業選擇可能反映多種影響，包括家庭、老師和興趣。"},{"en":"When many influences shape a field, its history becomes more complex.","zh":"當許多影響塑造一個領域，其歷史就變得更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses several sources of influence.","zh":"這個片語強調幾個影響來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"realise the benefits of","meaning":"意識到……的好處","examples":[{"en":"Adrian Hill realised the benefits of art as therapy.","zh":"Adrian Hill 意識到藝術作為治療的好處。"},{"en":"Realise the benefits of means become aware of the good effects or advantages of something.","zh":"realise the benefits of 指意識到某事的良好效果或優點。"},{"en":"Students may realise the benefits of planning after one well-organised essay scores higher.","zh":"當一篇組織良好的文章取得較高分，學生可能意識到規劃的好處。"},{"en":"If patients feel calmer after drawing, they may realise the benefits of creative activity.","zh":"如果病人繪畫後感到更平靜，他們可能意識到創意活動的好處。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recognising value through experience.","zh":"這個片語描述透過經驗認識價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"support art therapy","meaning":"支持藝術治療","examples":[{"en":"Those supporting art therapy advised different approaches.","zh":"支持藝術治療的人建議不同取向。"},{"en":"Support art therapy means believe in, promote, or recommend the use of art therapy.","zh":"support art therapy 指相信、推動或推薦使用藝術治療。"},{"en":"A hospital may support art therapy by hiring trained therapists for long-term patients.","zh":"醫院可能透過聘請受訓治療師照顧長期病人來支持藝術治療。"},{"en":"If professionals support art therapy, they may help it gain public trust.","zh":"如果專業人士支持藝術治療，他們可能幫助它獲得公眾信任。"},{"en":"The phrase describes approval and practical backing.","zh":"這個片語描述認同和實際支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"alternatively","meaning":"或者；作為另一選擇","examples":[{"en":"Some supported a psychoanalytic approach, while others alternatively emphasised creativity.","zh":"有些人支持精神分析取向，而另一些人則轉而強調創造力。"},{"en":"Alternatively means as another option or different possibility.","zh":"alternatively 指作為另一個選項或不同可能性。"},{"en":"Students can revise with flashcards; alternatively, they can practise by teaching a friend.","zh":"學生可以用字卡溫習；或者，他們可以透過教朋友來練習。"},{"en":"If one approach does not fit a client, the therapist may try another method alternatively.","zh":"如果一種取向不適合求助者，治療師可能改用另一方法。"},{"en":"The word introduces a different choice.","zh":"這個詞引出不同選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"place more emphasis on","meaning":"更加重視","examples":[{"en":"Some therapists placed more emphasis on the creative process itself.","zh":"有些治療師更加重視創作過程本身。"},{"en":"Place more emphasis on means give greater importance or attention to something.","zh":"place more emphasis on 指給予某事更大重要性或更多注意。"},{"en":"A teacher may place more emphasis on clear ideas than on difficult vocabulary.","zh":"老師可能更加重視清楚想法，而不是艱深詞彙。"},{"en":"If therapists emphasise the process, clients do not need to worry about perfect results.","zh":"如果治療師重視過程，求助者就不用擔心完美成果。"},{"en":"The phrase shows what is treated as more important.","zh":"這個片語顯示甚麼被視為更重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the creative process itself","meaning":"創作過程本身","examples":[{"en":"One approach placed more emphasis on the creative process itself.","zh":"一種取向更加重視創作過程本身。"},{"en":"The creative process itself means the act of making art, apart from analysis or final appearance.","zh":"creative process itself 指藝術創作的行為本身，而不包括分析或最終外觀。"},{"en":"In a writing workshop, the creative process itself may include planning, drafting, and revising.","zh":"在寫作工作坊中，創作過程本身可能包括規劃、起草和修改。"},{"en":"If the process itself is therapeutic, the final product does not have to be impressive.","zh":"如果過程本身有治療作用，最終作品不一定要令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the value of making, not just results.","zh":"這個片語強調創作的價值，而不只是結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"theories behind","meaning":"……背後的理論","examples":[{"en":"The theories behind art therapy may differ.","zh":"藝術治療背後的理論可能不同。"},{"en":"Theories behind something are the ideas or explanations that support a practice.","zh":"theories behind something 指支撐某種實踐的想法或解釋。"},{"en":"The theories behind a teaching method explain why it should help students learn.","zh":"教學方法背後的理論解釋它為何應能幫助學生學習。"},{"en":"If theories differ, practitioners may explain the same activity in different ways.","zh":"如果理論不同，從業者可能以不同方式解釋同一活動。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the thinking underneath a method.","zh":"這個片語指向方法背後的思想。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"differ in practice","meaning":"在實踐上有所不同","examples":[{"en":"The theories may differ, but the practices can overlap.","zh":"理論可能不同，但實踐可以重疊。"},{"en":"Differ in practice means be different when actually used, not only in theory.","zh":"differ in practice 指在實際使用時有所不同，而不只是理論上不同。"},{"en":"Two schools may share the same policy but differ in practice because teachers apply it differently.","zh":"兩所學校可能有相同政策，但因老師應用方式不同而在實踐上有所不同。"},{"en":"If art therapists differ in practice, clients may experience different session styles.","zh":"如果藝術治療師在實踐上有所不同，求助者可能經歷不同課節風格。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts real-world use with abstract ideas.","zh":"這個片語把現實使用與抽象想法作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"evolved into","meaning":"演變成","examples":[{"en":"The summary explains how art therapy evolved into its modern form.","zh":"摘要解釋藝術治療如何演變成其現代形式。"},{"en":"Evolved into means gradually developed and changed into something else.","zh":"evolved into 指逐漸發展並變成另一事物。"},{"en":"A small study group may evolve into a formal student society.","zh":"小型學習小組可能演變成正式學生學會。"},{"en":"Art therapy evolved as ideas from medicine, art, and psychology came together.","zh":"當醫學、藝術和心理學的想法結合，藝術治療逐漸演變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual development over time.","zh":"這個片語描述隨時間逐步發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"modern form","meaning":"現代形式","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy evolved into its modern form during the 20th century.","zh":"藝術治療在20世紀演變成其現代形式。"},{"en":"Modern form means the version or structure something has today or in recent times.","zh":"modern form 指某事物今天或近代具有的版本或結構。"},{"en":"The modern form of schooling includes classrooms, timetables, exams, and trained teachers.","zh":"現代學校形式包括課室、時間表、考試和受訓老師。"},{"en":"If we study a field’s modern form, we can see how older ideas changed.","zh":"如果我們研究某領域的現代形式，就能看見舊想法如何改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the current developed version.","zh":"這個片語指目前發展成熟的版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"modern-day art therapy","meaning":"現代藝術治療","examples":[{"en":"Modern-day art therapy has its beginnings in the 1940s.","zh":"現代藝術治療起源於1940年代。"},{"en":"Modern-day art therapy means art therapy as it is understood and practised in recent times.","zh":"modern-day art therapy 指近代所理解和實踐的藝術治療。"},{"en":"Modern-day art therapy may take place in hospitals, schools, clinics, and community centres.","zh":"現代藝術治療可能在醫院、學校、診所和社區中心進行。"},{"en":"Although its roots are older, its professional identity developed much more recently.","zh":"雖然其根源更早，但其專業身份較近期才發展。"},{"en":"The phrase distinguishes current practice from historical origins.","zh":"這個片語把當前實踐與歷史起源區分開來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"have its beginnings in","meaning":"起源於","examples":[{"en":"Modern art therapy has its beginnings in the 1940s.","zh":"現代藝術治療起源於1940年代。"},{"en":"Have its beginnings in means start or originate in a particular time, place, or situation.","zh":"have its beginnings in 指起始或源於某個時間、地方或情況。"},{"en":"A school tradition may have its beginnings in a student event many years ago.","zh":"學校傳統可能起源於多年前的一次學生活動。"},{"en":"If a profession has its beginnings in wartime or illness, those experiences may shape its values.","zh":"如果一門專業起源於戰爭或疾病，這些經歷可能塑造其價值。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where or when something started.","zh":"這個片語指出某事物在何處或何時開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"effective in helping","meaning":"對幫助……有效","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy was effective in helping patients express themselves.","zh":"藝術治療對幫助病人表達自己有效。"},{"en":"Effective in helping means successful at supporting someone to do something.","zh":"effective in helping 指成功支援某人做某事。"},{"en":"Visual examples are effective in helping students understand abstract grammar.","zh":"視覺例子對幫助學生理解抽象文法有效。"},{"en":"If therapy is effective in helping expression, clients may communicate more safely.","zh":"如果治療對幫助表達有效，求助者可能更安全地溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a method that works for a specific purpose.","zh":"這個片語描述某方法對特定目的有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"create strong resistance to","meaning":"建立對……的強大抵抗力","examples":[{"en":"Art could help patients create strong resistance to psychological stress.","zh":"藝術可以幫助病人建立對心理壓力的強大抵抗力。"},{"en":"Create strong resistance to means build the ability to withstand or cope with something harmful.","zh":"create strong resistance to 指建立承受或應對有害事物的能力。"},{"en":"Regular exercise can create resistance to tiredness and poor mood.","zh":"規律運動可以建立對疲倦和低落情緒的抵抗力。"},{"en":"If patients build emotional strength, they may resist stress more effectively.","zh":"如果病人建立情緒力量，就可能更有效抵抗壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes developing protection against difficulty.","zh":"這個片語描述發展對困難的保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"psychological and social stresses","meaning":"心理及社會壓力","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy may help patients deal with psychological and social stresses.","zh":"藝術治療可能幫助病人應對心理及社會壓力。"},{"en":"Psychological and social stresses are pressures from inner mental strain and outside relationships or society.","zh":"psychological and social stresses 指來自內在心理負擔和外在人際或社會環境的壓力。"},{"en":"Exam anxiety is psychological stress, while bullying or family conflict can be social stress.","zh":"考試焦慮是心理壓力，而欺凌或家庭衝突可以是社會壓力。"},{"en":"If both kinds of stress affect a patient, therapy may need to address feelings and relationships.","zh":"如果兩種壓力都影響病人，治療可能需要處理感受和關係。"},{"en":"The phrase combines internal and external pressures.","zh":"這個片語結合內在和外在壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"particularly benefit from","meaning":"從……中特別受益","examples":[{"en":"Inhibited patients may particularly benefit from an artistic outlet.","zh":"受壓抑的病人可能從藝術抒發途徑中特別受益。"},{"en":"Particularly benefit from means gain especially strong help or advantage from something.","zh":"particularly benefit from 指從某事中獲得特別強的幫助或好處。"},{"en":"Shy students may particularly benefit from small-group speaking practice.","zh":"害羞學生可能從小組口語練習中特別受益。"},{"en":"If patients struggle to speak, they may benefit especially from non-verbal expression.","zh":"如果病人難以說話，他們可能特別受益於非語言表達。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights who gains more than others.","zh":"這個片語突出誰比其他人獲益更多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"artistic outlet","meaning":"藝術抒發途徑","examples":[{"en":"Art therapy gives inhibited patients an artistic outlet.","zh":"藝術治療給受壓抑的病人一個藝術抒發途徑。"},{"en":"An artistic outlet is a way to express feelings or ideas through art.","zh":"artistic outlet 指透過藝術表達感受或想法的方法。"},{"en":"A teenager may use drawing as an artistic outlet when words feel too direct.","zh":"當語言感覺太直接，青少年可能把繪畫用作藝術抒發途徑。"},{"en":"If people have an artistic outlet, difficult emotions may become easier to handle.","zh":"如果人們有藝術抒發途徑，困難情緒可能變得較易處理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes art as a safe channel for expression.","zh":"這個片語描述藝術作為安全表達渠道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"emphasise a creative approach","meaning":"強調創作取向","examples":[{"en":"One type of practice emphasises a creative approach.","zh":"一種實踐強調創作取向。"},{"en":"Emphasise a creative approach means give special importance to creativity and the process of making art.","zh":"emphasise a creative approach 指特別重視創意和藝術創作過程。"},{"en":"A teacher may emphasise a creative approach by letting students design their own projects.","zh":"老師可能讓學生設計自己的專題，以強調創作取向。"},{"en":"If therapy emphasises creativity, clients may focus less on analysis and more on expression.","zh":"如果治療強調創意，求助者可能較少集中於分析，而更多集中於表達。"},{"en":"The phrase describes placing creativity at the centre of practice.","zh":"這個片語描述把創意置於實踐中心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"overlap between","meaning":"……之間的重疊","examples":[{"en":"Today there is often an overlap between the two practices.","zh":"今天，這兩種實踐之間常有重疊。"},{"en":"Overlap between means shared features or common ground linking two things.","zh":"overlap between 指連接兩件事的共同特徵或共同基礎。"},{"en":"There is overlap between reading and writing because both require vocabulary and meaning.","zh":"閱讀和寫作之間有重疊，因為兩者都需要詞彙和意思。"},{"en":"If two therapy practices overlap, a therapist may use elements from both.","zh":"如果兩種治療實踐有重疊，治療師可能同時使用兩者的元素。"},{"en":"The phrase describes partial similarity between two areas.","zh":"這個片語描述兩個範疇之間的部分相似。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 70 - The Beginnings of Art Therapy.pdf","sourcePage":21}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 71":[{"front":"Jack the Ripper","meaning":"開膛手傑克","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses murder enquiries relating to Jack the Ripper.","zh":"文章討論與開膛手傑克有關的謀殺案調查。"},{"en":"Jack the Ripper is the name given to an unidentified serial killer in Victorian London.","zh":"開膛手傑克是給予維多利亞時代倫敦一名身份不明連環殺手的名稱。"},{"en":"Students may hear about Jack the Ripper when studying crime, policing, or Victorian society.","zh":"學生學習罪案、警務或維多利亞時代社會時，可能會聽到開膛手傑克。"},{"en":"The name became famous because the murders were brutal and the killer was never caught.","zh":"這個名字變得著名，是因為謀殺案殘暴，而且兇手從未被捕。"},{"en":"Jack the Ripper is often discussed as a case where public fear, media attention, and police failure met.","zh":"開膛手傑克常被討論為一宗公眾恐懼、媒體關注和警方失敗交織的案件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a bungled investigation","meaning":"處理失當的調查","examples":[{"en":"The title asks whether the Ripper case was a bungled investigation.","zh":"標題問開膛手傑克案件是否是一宗處理失當的調查。"},{"en":"A bungled investigation is an enquiry handled badly through mistakes, confusion, or poor judgement.","zh":"bungled investigation 指因錯誤、混亂或判斷差劣而處理不好的調查。"},{"en":"A school cheating case may become a bungled investigation if teachers lose the evidence.","zh":"如果老師遺失證據，學校作弊案件可能變成處理失當的調查。"},{"en":"Poor communication and weak procedures can turn a serious enquiry into a bungled investigation.","zh":"溝通差和程序薄弱可以把嚴肅調查變成處理失當的調查。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that the failure came not only from difficulty, but also from mishandling.","zh":"這個短語暗示失敗不只是因為困難，也因為處理不善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"murder enquiries","meaning":"謀殺案調查","examples":[{"en":"Few murder enquiries have stirred the public imagination as much as the Ripper case.","zh":"很少謀殺案調查像開膛手傑克案件那樣激發大眾想像。"},{"en":"Murder enquiries are official investigations into killings.","zh":"murder enquiries 是對殺人案件的正式調查。"},{"en":"Police begin murder enquiries when a death appears to be caused deliberately by another person.","zh":"當死亡看似由他人蓄意造成，警方會展開謀殺案調查。"},{"en":"Murder enquiries usually involve witnesses, evidence, timelines, and possible suspects.","zh":"謀殺案調查通常涉及證人、證據、時間線和可能疑犯。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and often appears in crime reports or legal writing.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常見於罪案報道或法律寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"stir the public imagination","meaning":"激發大眾想像","examples":[{"en":"The Ripper murders stirred the public imagination to a remarkable extent.","zh":"開膛手傑克謀殺案在驚人程度上激發了大眾想像。"},{"en":"To stir the public imagination means to make many people curious, fearful, excited, or fascinated.","zh":"stir the public imagination 指令很多人好奇、恐懼、興奮或著迷。"},{"en":"A mysterious discovery can stir the public imagination if no one can explain it clearly.","zh":"如果沒有人能清楚解釋一項神秘發現，它可以激發大眾想像。"},{"en":"Media stories stir the public imagination when they leave people asking what really happened.","zh":"當媒體故事令人不斷追問真相，它就會激發大眾想像。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong public emotional and imaginative response.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈的公眾情緒和想像反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"to such an extent","meaning":"到如此程度","examples":[{"en":"The murder enquiries stirred public interest to such an extent that the case became famous.","zh":"這些謀殺案調查激發公眾興趣到如此程度，以致案件變得著名。"},{"en":"To such an extent means to such a high degree that a clear result follows.","zh":"to such an extent 指程度高到產生明顯結果。"},{"en":"The traffic was delayed to such an extent that many students missed the first lesson.","zh":"交通延誤到如此程度，以致許多學生錯過第一堂課。"},{"en":"A story can spread to such an extent that even people outside the city hear about it.","zh":"一個故事可以傳播到如此程度，連城市以外的人也聽過。"},{"en":"The phrase links a high level of something with its consequence.","zh":"這個短語把某事的高程度與其後果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"relating to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The passage focuses on enquiries relating to Jack the Ripper.","zh":"文章集中於與開膛手傑克有關的調查。"},{"en":"Relating to means connected with or about a particular subject.","zh":"relating to 指與某特定主題有連繫或關於該主題。"},{"en":"Students should keep all documents relating to their application in one folder.","zh":"學生應把所有與申請有關的文件放在同一文件夾。"},{"en":"Questions relating to safety should be answered before the school trip begins.","zh":"與安全有關的問題應在學校旅行開始前回答。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when linking information to a topic.","zh":"這個短語適合用來把資料連到某主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"reports of","meaning":"關於……的報道","examples":[{"en":"Reports of the murders shocked Victorian society.","zh":"關於這些謀殺案的報道震驚了維多利亞時代社會。"},{"en":"Reports of something are news stories or accounts about that event.","zh":"reports of 某事，是關於該事件的新聞或記述。"},{"en":"Reports of food poisoning made parents worried about the school canteen.","zh":"關於食物中毒的報道令家長擔心學校飯堂。"},{"en":"When reports of a problem spread, public pressure can increase quickly.","zh":"當關於問題的報道擴散，公眾壓力可以迅速增加。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces what people heard or read about an event.","zh":"這個短語引出人們聽到或讀到的事件資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be worthy of","meaning":"配得上；足以稱為","examples":[{"en":"The murders were described as crimes worthy of a depraved savage.","zh":"這些謀殺案被形容為足以稱為墮落殘暴者所犯的罪行。"},{"en":"To be worthy of something means to deserve that description, treatment, or response.","zh":"be worthy of 某事，指值得該描述、待遇或回應。"},{"en":"A student who helps classmates every day is worthy of praise.","zh":"每天幫助同學的學生值得稱讚。"},{"en":"A serious mistake may be worthy of investigation if it puts people at risk.","zh":"如果嚴重錯誤令人陷入風險，它可能值得調查。"},{"en":"The phrase judges whether something deserves a particular label or reaction.","zh":"這個短語判斷某事是否配得上某標籤或反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a depraved savage","meaning":"墮落殘暴的人","examples":[{"en":"The reports described the killer as a depraved savage.","zh":"報道把兇手描述為墮落殘暴的人。"},{"en":"A depraved savage is a highly negative description of someone seen as morally corrupt and violently cruel.","zh":"depraved savage 是非常負面的描述，指被視為道德敗壞且極度殘忍的人。"},{"en":"Newspapers may use words like depraved savage to make a criminal seem terrifying.","zh":"報章可能使用墮落殘暴的人這類字眼，令罪犯看起來可怕。"},{"en":"Such language can increase fear because it presents the offender as inhuman.","zh":"這種語言會增加恐懼，因為它把犯案者描寫得不像人。"},{"en":"The phrase is strong, judgemental, and usually used in descriptions of extreme brutality.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈、帶判斷性，通常用於描述極端殘暴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"simultaneously appal and enthral","meaning":"同時令人震驚和著迷","examples":[{"en":"The murders simultaneously appalled and enthralled Victorian society.","zh":"這些謀殺案同時令維多利亞時代社會震驚和著迷。"},{"en":"To simultaneously appal and enthral means to shock people deeply while also making them unable to look away.","zh":"simultaneously appal and enthral 指深深震驚人，同時又令他們移不開視線。"},{"en":"A frightening news story can simultaneously appal and enthral readers if it is terrible but mysterious.","zh":"如果恐怖新聞既可怕又神秘，它可以同時令讀者震驚和著迷。"},{"en":"This mixed reaction happens when fear and curiosity appear together.","zh":"當恐懼和好奇同時出現，這種混合反應就會發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being horrified and fascinated at the same time.","zh":"這個短語描述同時感到驚駭和著迷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Victorian society","meaning":"維多利亞時代社會","examples":[{"en":"Victorian society was shocked by the brutality of the murders.","zh":"維多利亞時代社會被謀殺案的殘暴震驚。"},{"en":"Victorian society refers to British society during the reign of Queen Victoria.","zh":"Victorian society 指維多利亞女王統治時期的英國社會。"},{"en":"Students study Victorian society to understand class, poverty, work, and moral attitudes in 19th-century Britain.","zh":"學生研究維多利亞時代社會，以理解十九世紀英國的階級、貧窮、工作和道德態度。"},{"en":"Public scandals in Victorian society often caused strong moral debate.","zh":"維多利亞時代社會中的公眾醜聞常引起強烈道德爭論。"},{"en":"The phrase places people, events, and values in a specific historical period.","zh":"這個短語把人物、事件和價值觀放在特定歷史時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"come to a close","meaning":"接近尾聲","examples":[{"en":"The murders occurred as the 19th century came to a close.","zh":"這些謀殺案發生在十九世紀接近尾聲之時。"},{"en":"To come to a close means to approach an end.","zh":"come to a close 指接近結束。"},{"en":"As the school year comes to a close, students begin preparing for final exams.","zh":"當學年接近尾聲，學生開始準備期末考試。"},{"en":"When a period comes to a close, people often look back and judge what has changed.","zh":"當一個時期接近尾聲，人們常回顧並判斷有何改變。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to say something is ending.","zh":"這個短語是表示某事結束的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the unleashing of","meaning":"……的釋放；……的爆發","examples":[{"en":"The unleashing of a serial killer onto London caught police unprepared.","zh":"一名連環殺手在倫敦爆發般出現，令警方措手不及。"},{"en":"The unleashing of something means the sudden release or appearance of something dangerous or powerful.","zh":"unleashing of 某事，指危險或強大事物突然被釋放或出現。"},{"en":"The unleashing of a computer virus can disrupt offices, schools, and hospitals.","zh":"電腦病毒的爆發可以擾亂辦公室、學校和醫院。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that a force has been let loose and is hard to control.","zh":"這個短語暗示某股力量被放出，而且難以控制。"},{"en":"It is often used for threats, violence, anger, or sudden destructive energy.","zh":"它常用於威脅、暴力、怒氣或突發破壞性能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"serial killer","meaning":"連環殺手","examples":[{"en":"The Ripper was an early example of a serial killer in London.","zh":"開膛手傑克是倫敦早期連環殺手例子。"},{"en":"A serial killer is someone who murders several people in separate events.","zh":"serial killer 是在不同事件中殺害多人的人。"},{"en":"Police treat a case differently if they believe one serial killer is responsible for repeated attacks.","zh":"如果警方相信同一連環殺手負責多次襲擊，他們會以不同方式處理案件。"},{"en":"Serial killer cases often create fear because people worry the crimes may continue.","zh":"連環殺手案件常造成恐懼，因為人們擔心罪案會持續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a repeated pattern of murder by the same offender.","zh":"這個短語描述同一犯案者重複殺人的模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"catch someone unprepared","meaning":"令某人措手不及","examples":[{"en":"The brutality of the killings caught the police unprepared.","zh":"這些殺人案的殘暴令警方措手不及。"},{"en":"To catch someone unprepared means to surprise them before they are ready to respond.","zh":"catch someone unprepared 指在某人未準備好回應前令他驚訝。"},{"en":"A sudden fire drill can catch a new teacher unprepared on her first day.","zh":"突然的消防演習可能令第一天上班的新老師措手不及。"},{"en":"If a crisis catches a team unprepared, mistakes become more likely.","zh":"如果危機令團隊措手不及，錯誤會更可能出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being taken by surprise without enough planning or tools.","zh":"這個短語描述因缺乏計劃或工具而被突如其來的事情震住。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"unprecedented brutality","meaning":"前所未有的殘暴","examples":[{"en":"The killings were marked by unprecedented brutality.","zh":"這些殺人案以前所未有的殘暴為特徵。"},{"en":"Unprecedented brutality means cruelty more extreme than anything previously seen or expected.","zh":"unprecedented brutality 指比以往所見或預期更極端的殘忍。"},{"en":"A report may describe an attack as unprecedented brutality if even experienced officers are shocked.","zh":"如果連有經驗的警員也震驚，報告可能把襲擊形容為前所未有的殘暴。"},{"en":"Such brutality can increase public fear and pressure on police.","zh":"這種殘暴可以增加公眾恐懼和警方壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the violence was unusually and historically severe.","zh":"這個短語強調暴力異常且在歷史上嚴重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"earn someone a nickname","meaning":"使某人獲得綽號","examples":[{"en":"The brutality of the crimes earned the perpetrator the nickname Jack the Ripper.","zh":"這些罪行的殘暴使犯案者獲得「開膛手傑克」這個綽號。"},{"en":"To earn someone a nickname means to cause people to give that person a particular name.","zh":"earn someone a nickname 指令人們給某人一個特定名稱。"},{"en":"A student who always fixes computers may earn the nickname “Tech Doctor”.","zh":"總是修理電腦的學生可能獲得「科技醫生」這個綽號。"},{"en":"Nicknames often come from repeated behaviour, appearance, or reputation.","zh":"綽號常來自重複行為、外表或名聲。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how actions lead to a public label.","zh":"這個短語顯示行動如何導致公開標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"perpetrator","meaning":"犯案者；兇手","examples":[{"en":"The perpetrator was never captured by the police.","zh":"犯案者從未被警方拘捕。"},{"en":"A perpetrator is the person who commits a crime or harmful act.","zh":"perpetrator 是犯下罪行或有害行為的人。"},{"en":"In a school vandalism case, the perpetrator is the student who damaged the property.","zh":"在學校破壞公物案件中，犯案者就是損壞財物的學生。"},{"en":"Identifying the perpetrator is important before anyone is punished.","zh":"在任何人受懲罰前，找出犯案者很重要。"},{"en":"The word is formal and often used in crime or legal contexts.","zh":"這個詞較正式，常用於罪案或法律語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"given the heightened public interest","meaning":"鑑於公眾興趣高漲","examples":[{"en":"Given the heightened public interest, the failure to catch the Ripper was striking.","zh":"鑑於公眾興趣高漲，未能捉到開膛手傑克令人震驚。"},{"en":"Given the heightened public interest means considering how much extra attention the public was paying.","zh":"given the heightened public interest 指考慮到公眾額外關注的程度。"},{"en":"Given the heightened public interest in a school scandal, the principal had to explain the facts clearly.","zh":"鑑於公眾對學校醜聞興趣高漲，校長必須清楚解釋事實。"},{"en":"When public interest is high, failure by authorities becomes more noticeable.","zh":"當公眾興趣高漲，當局失敗會變得更顯眼。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a reason why something seems especially surprising.","zh":"這個短語引出某事特別令人驚訝的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"heightened public interest","meaning":"高漲的公眾興趣","examples":[{"en":"The case attracted heightened public interest.","zh":"這宗案件吸引了高漲的公眾興趣。"},{"en":"Heightened public interest means unusually strong attention from ordinary people.","zh":"heightened public interest 指普通人異常強烈的關注。"},{"en":"A missing-child case may attract heightened public interest because many parents feel concerned.","zh":"失蹤兒童案件可能吸引高漲的公眾興趣，因為許多家長感到擔心。"},{"en":"Heightened public interest can push newspapers to publish more stories.","zh":"高漲的公眾興趣可以推動報章刊登更多報道。"},{"en":"The phrase describes public attention that has risen above normal levels.","zh":"這個短語描述高於平常水平的公眾關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"police force","meaning":"警隊","examples":[{"en":"The police force had become increasingly competent by the late 19th century.","zh":"到十九世紀後期，警隊已變得越來越有能力。"},{"en":"A police force is an organised body of officers responsible for enforcing the law.","zh":"police force 是負責執法的有組織警務人員團體。"},{"en":"A city’s police force may patrol streets, investigate crimes, and protect public safety.","zh":"城市警隊可能巡邏街道、調查罪案和保護公共安全。"},{"en":"A stronger police force can solve more cases when it has training, records, and public trust.","zh":"當警隊有訓練、紀錄和公眾信任，它能偵破更多案件。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the institution of policing, not one individual officer.","zh":"這個短語指警務制度，而不是個別警員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"increasingly competent","meaning":"越來越有能力的","examples":[{"en":"The Metropolitan Police had become increasingly competent since its formation.","zh":"大都會警察自成立以來變得越來越有能力。"},{"en":"Increasingly competent means becoming more skilled, capable, and effective over time.","zh":"increasingly competent 指隨時間變得更熟練、更有能力和更有效。"},{"en":"A new teacher becomes increasingly competent after planning lessons and receiving feedback.","zh":"新老師在備課和接受回饋後會變得越來越有能力。"},{"en":"Training and experience can make a team increasingly competent.","zh":"訓練和經驗可以令團隊越來越有能力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual improvement in ability.","zh":"這個短語描述能力上的逐漸改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the formation of","meaning":"……的成立","examples":[{"en":"The formation of the Metropolitan Police took place in 1829.","zh":"大都會警察於1829年成立。"},{"en":"The formation of an organisation means its creation or establishment.","zh":"formation of 一個組織，指它的創立或成立。"},{"en":"The formation of a student council can give students a stronger voice.","zh":"學生會的成立可以令學生有更強聲音。"},{"en":"After the formation of a new department, work may become better organised.","zh":"新部門成立後，工作可能變得更有組織。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the beginning of a group, system, or institution.","zh":"這個短語指群體、系統或機構的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"evade capture","meaning":"逃避拘捕","examples":[{"en":"The Ripper managed to evade capture despite intense public interest.","zh":"開膛手傑克儘管受到強烈公眾關注，仍成功逃避拘捕。"},{"en":"To evade capture means to avoid being caught by the police or authorities.","zh":"evade capture 指避免被警方或當局捉到。"},{"en":"A thief may evade capture by changing clothes and leaving the area quickly.","zh":"竊賊可能透過換衣服並迅速離開該區來逃避拘捕。"},{"en":"Weak evidence and poor communication can help a suspect evade capture.","zh":"證據薄弱和溝通不良可以幫助疑犯逃避拘捕。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on escaping arrest or detention.","zh":"這個短語重點在逃避被捕或拘留。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be charged with","meaning":"被控以……罪名","examples":[{"en":"No one was charged with the five murders attributed to the Ripper.","zh":"沒有人被控以歸因於開膛手傑克的五宗謀殺罪名。"},{"en":"To be charged with a crime means to be formally accused of committing it.","zh":"be charged with 某罪，指被正式指控犯下該罪。"},{"en":"A driver may be charged with dangerous driving after causing a serious accident.","zh":"司機造成嚴重意外後，可能被控以危險駕駛罪。"},{"en":"Being charged does not automatically mean a person is guilty.","zh":"被控罪並不自動代表一個人有罪。"},{"en":"The phrase belongs to formal legal and police language.","zh":"這個短語屬於正式法律和警務語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be attributed to","meaning":"被歸因於……","examples":[{"en":"Five murders were attributed to Jack the Ripper.","zh":"五宗謀殺案被歸因於開膛手傑克。"},{"en":"To be attributed to someone means to be believed to be caused or done by that person.","zh":"be attributed to 某人，指被認為由該人造成或做出。"},{"en":"A sudden improvement in results may be attributed to better teaching and daily practice.","zh":"成績突然改善可能被歸因於更好教學和每日練習。"},{"en":"Attribution can be uncertain if evidence is incomplete.","zh":"如果證據不完整，歸因可能不確定。"},{"en":"The phrase links an event or result to a suspected cause.","zh":"這個短語把事件或結果連到被懷疑的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"conspiracy theorists","meaning":"陰謀論者","examples":[{"en":"Conspiracy theorists claim that the police uncovered the Ripper’s identity.","zh":"陰謀論者聲稱警方揭露了開膛手傑克的身份。"},{"en":"Conspiracy theorists are people who believe secret groups are hiding the truth behind events.","zh":"conspiracy theorists 是相信秘密群體在事件背後隱藏真相的人。"},{"en":"Conspiracy theorists may say a public mistake was planned rather than accidental.","zh":"陰謀論者可能說一個公開錯誤是有計劃的，而不是意外。"},{"en":"Their theories often grow when official information is limited or unclear.","zh":"當官方資料有限或不清楚，這類理論常會增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes people who explain events through hidden plots.","zh":"這個短語描述透過隱藏陰謀解釋事件的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"would have us believe that","meaning":"想令我們相信","examples":[{"en":"Conspiracy theorists would have us believe that the truth was covered up.","zh":"陰謀論者想令我們相信真相被掩蓋了。"},{"en":"Would have us believe that means tries to make us accept a claim, often with doubt implied.","zh":"would have us believe that 指試圖令我們接受某聲稱，常帶有懷疑意味。"},{"en":"The advertisement would have us believe that one drink can solve all health problems.","zh":"廣告想令我們相信一款飲品可以解決所有健康問題。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when they question someone else’s version of events.","zh":"作者質疑別人的事件版本時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests the claim may be misleading or exaggerated.","zh":"這個短語暗示該聲稱可能誤導或誇張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"contrary to public belief","meaning":"與大眾看法相反","examples":[{"en":"Contrary to public belief, some people claimed that the police knew the killer’s identity.","zh":"與大眾看法相反，有些人聲稱警方知道兇手身份。"},{"en":"Contrary to public belief means different from what most people think.","zh":"contrary to public belief 指與大多數人所想不同。"},{"en":"Contrary to public belief, quiet students may have very strong opinions.","zh":"與大眾看法相反，安靜學生可能有非常強烈的意見。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a surprising contrast with common assumptions.","zh":"這個短語引出與常見假設相反的驚人對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when correcting a popular but possibly wrong idea.","zh":"它適合用來修正流行但可能錯誤的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"uncover someone’s identity","meaning":"揭露某人的身份","examples":[{"en":"Some theorists believe that the police uncovered the Ripper’s identity.","zh":"有些理論家相信警方揭露了開膛手傑克的身份。"},{"en":"To uncover someone’s identity means to discover who that person really is.","zh":"uncover someone’s identity 指發現某人真正是誰。"},{"en":"A school may uncover a cyberbully’s identity by checking computer login records.","zh":"學校可能透過檢查電腦登入紀錄揭露網絡欺凌者的身份。"},{"en":"Investigators uncover identity by connecting evidence, witnesses, and records.","zh":"調查員透過連接證據、證人和紀錄來揭露身份。"},{"en":"The phrase describes revealing a hidden or unknown person’s name.","zh":"這個短語描述揭開隱藏或未知人物的名字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prove so unpalatable that","meaning":"令人難以接受到……","examples":[{"en":"The truth supposedly proved so unpalatable that it had to be hidden.","zh":"據說真相令人難以接受到必須被隱藏。"},{"en":"To prove so unpalatable that something happens means to turn out so unacceptable that people react strongly.","zh":"prove so unpalatable that 指結果令人如此難以接受，以致人們作出強烈反應。"},{"en":"The audit results proved so unpalatable that the company tried to delay publication.","zh":"審計結果令人難以接受到公司試圖延遲發布。"},{"en":"Bad news can prove unpalatable when it damages powerful people’s reputation.","zh":"當壞消息損害有權勢者名聲，它可能令人難以接受。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a truth that is too unpleasant for others to accept easily.","zh":"這個短語描述太令人不快而難以接受的真相。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be hushed up","meaning":"被掩蓋","examples":[{"en":"Some people believed that the truth about the Ripper was hushed up.","zh":"有些人相信開膛手傑克的真相被掩蓋。"},{"en":"To be hushed up means to be deliberately kept secret to avoid embarrassment or trouble.","zh":"be hushed up 指為避免尷尬或麻煩而被蓄意保密。"},{"en":"A school accident should not be hushed up if students’ safety is involved.","zh":"如果涉及學生安全，學校意外不應被掩蓋。"},{"en":"When a scandal is hushed up, public trust usually falls if the truth later appears.","zh":"當醜聞被掩蓋，若真相後來出現，公眾信任通常會下降。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests concealment by people with power.","zh":"這個短語暗示由有權力的人隱瞞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"far-fetched as it may seem","meaning":"雖然聽起來牽強","examples":[{"en":"Far-fetched as it may seem, some people thought Prince Albert Victor was the Ripper.","zh":"雖然聽起來牽強，有些人認為阿爾伯特・維克托王子是開膛手傑克。"},{"en":"Far-fetched as it may seem means although the idea sounds unlikely or exaggerated.","zh":"far-fetched as it may seem 指雖然想法聽起來不大可能或誇張。"},{"en":"Far-fetched as it may seem, a tiny app can become a global business.","zh":"雖然聽起來牽強，一個小小應用程式也可以成為全球企業。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an unlikely claim before explaining why some people considered it.","zh":"這個短語在解釋為何有人考慮某說法前，引出一個不大可能的聲稱。"},{"en":"It tells readers the writer knows the idea sounds hard to believe.","zh":"它告訴讀者作者知道該想法聽起來難以相信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be thought by some to be","meaning":"被一些人認為是……","examples":[{"en":"Prince Albert Victor was thought by some to be Jack the Ripper.","zh":"阿爾伯特・維克托王子被一些人認為是開膛手傑克。"},{"en":"To be thought by some to be something means some people believed this, though not everyone agreed.","zh":"be thought by some to be 某事，指有些人相信如此，但並非所有人同意。"},{"en":"A difficult teacher may be thought by some to be unfair, while others see him as strict but helpful.","zh":"一位嚴厲老師可能被一些人認為不公平，而另一些人則認為他嚴格但有幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase is careful because it reports a belief without confirming it as fact.","zh":"這個短語很謹慎，因為它報道一種信念，而非確認為事實。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing disputed claims.","zh":"它適合討論有爭議的聲稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"frequent places of ill repute","meaning":"經常出入聲名狼藉的地方","examples":[{"en":"Prince Albert Victor did frequent places of ill repute.","zh":"阿爾伯特・維克托王子確曾經常出入聲名狼藉的地方。"},{"en":"To frequent places of ill repute means to often visit places with a bad moral or social reputation.","zh":"frequent places of ill repute 指經常到訪道德或社會名聲差的地方。"},{"en":"A school may worry if students frequent places of ill repute after class.","zh":"如果學生放學後經常出入聲名狼藉的地方，學校可能會擔心。"},{"en":"Regular visits to such places can damage a person’s reputation.","zh":"經常到訪這些地方可以損害一個人的名聲。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and suggests repeated visits to disreputable locations.","zh":"這個短語較正式，暗示反覆到訪名聲差的地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"places of ill repute","meaning":"聲名狼藉的地方","examples":[{"en":"The prince was said to have visited places of ill repute.","zh":"據說王子曾到訪聲名狼藉的地方。"},{"en":"Places of ill repute are locations known for immoral, illegal, or socially disapproved activity.","zh":"places of ill repute 是因不道德、非法或不被社會認可的活動而聞名的地點。"},{"en":"Parents may warn teenagers to avoid places of ill repute late at night.","zh":"家長可能提醒青少年深夜避開聲名狼藉的地方。"},{"en":"Being seen in such places can create gossip even without proof of wrongdoing.","zh":"即使沒有犯錯證據，被人看見在這類地方出現也可能引起流言。"},{"en":"The phrase describes locations with a bad public reputation.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾名聲差的地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tangible evidence","meaning":"實質證據","examples":[{"en":"There is no tangible evidence to support the theory.","zh":"沒有實質證據支持這個理論。"},{"en":"Tangible evidence is real, concrete proof that can be examined or clearly shown.","zh":"tangible evidence 是可以檢視或清楚展示的真實、具體證據。"},{"en":"A teacher needs tangible evidence, such as copied answers, before accusing a student of cheating.","zh":"老師在指控學生作弊前，需要抄襲答案等實質證據。"},{"en":"Without tangible evidence, a theory may remain only a rumour.","zh":"沒有實質證據，理論可能只停留在謠言層面。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts solid proof with guesswork or suspicion.","zh":"這個短語把堅實證明與猜測或懷疑作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"support a theory","meaning":"支持某個理論","examples":[{"en":"No tangible evidence supports the sensationalist theory.","zh":"沒有實質證據支持這個嘩眾取寵的理論。"},{"en":"To support a theory means to provide evidence that makes it more believable.","zh":"support a theory 指提供證據令某理論更可信。"},{"en":"Test results may support a theory that students learn better with shorter lessons.","zh":"測驗結果可能支持學生在較短課堂中學得更好的理論。"},{"en":"A theory becomes stronger when several independent facts support it.","zh":"當幾項獨立事實支持一個理論，它就變得更強。"},{"en":"The phrase links evidence with an explanation.","zh":"這個短語把證據與解釋連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sensationalist theory","meaning":"嘩眾取寵的理論","examples":[{"en":"The idea that a royal figure was the Ripper is a sensationalist theory.","zh":"認為一名皇室人物是開膛手傑克的想法，是嘩眾取寵的理論。"},{"en":"A sensationalist theory is an explanation designed to shock or attract attention more than to prove truth.","zh":"sensationalist theory 是旨在震驚或吸引注意，而不是證明真相的解釋。"},{"en":"A newspaper may print a sensationalist theory to sell more copies.","zh":"報章可能刊登嘩眾取寵的理論來賣出更多份。"},{"en":"Such theories often use dramatic claims but lack strong evidence.","zh":"這類理論常使用戲劇性聲稱，但缺乏有力證據。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises an idea as attention-seeking and unreliable.","zh":"這個短語批評某想法追求注意且不可靠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"successfully evade the police","meaning":"成功逃避警方","examples":[{"en":"The Ripper may have successfully evaded the police for ordinary reasons.","zh":"開膛手傑克可能因普通原因成功逃避警方。"},{"en":"To successfully evade the police means to avoid being caught by police officers.","zh":"successfully evade the police 指避免被警員捉到。"},{"en":"A shoplifter may successfully evade the police if the security camera is broken.","zh":"如果保安攝影機壞掉，店舖小偷可能成功逃避警方。"},{"en":"Poor records, darkness, and confusion can help a suspect evade the police.","zh":"紀錄不清、黑暗和混亂可以幫助疑犯逃避警方。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on escaping law enforcement.","zh":"這個短語重點在逃避執法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"prosaic reasons","meaning":"平凡而實際的原因","examples":[{"en":"The Ripper may have escaped for far more prosaic reasons.","zh":"開膛手傑克可能因平凡而實際得多的原因逃脫。"},{"en":"Prosaic reasons are ordinary, practical, and not dramatic reasons.","zh":"prosaic reasons 是普通、實際而不戲劇化的原因。"},{"en":"A student may miss class for a prosaic reason, such as a delayed bus.","zh":"學生可能因巴士延誤等平凡原因缺課。"},{"en":"Prosaic reasons can be more believable than exciting conspiracy theories.","zh":"平凡而實際的原因可以比刺激的陰謀論更可信。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts simple explanations with dramatic ones.","zh":"這個短語把簡單解釋與戲劇性解釋作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"back in 1888","meaning":"早在1888年","examples":[{"en":"Back in 1888, the Ripper began his reign of terror in Whitechapel.","zh":"早在1888年，開膛手傑克就在白教堂區展開恐怖時期。"},{"en":"Back in 1888 means in the year 1888, viewed from a later time.","zh":"back in 1888 指從後來時間回看1888年。"},{"en":"Back in 2005, many students still submitted homework on paper rather than online.","zh":"早在2005年，許多學生仍以紙本而非網上方式交功課。"},{"en":"The phrase helps readers move back to an earlier historical moment.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者回到較早的歷史時刻。"},{"en":"It often introduces background information from the past.","zh":"它常引出過去的背景資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"begin one’s reign of terror","meaning":"展開恐怖統治","examples":[{"en":"The Ripper began his reign of terror in the streets of Whitechapel.","zh":"開膛手傑克在白教堂區街頭展開恐怖統治。"},{"en":"To begin one’s reign of terror means to start a period in which one person creates widespread fear.","zh":"begin one’s reign of terror 指開始一段由某人造成廣泛恐懼的時期。"},{"en":"A bully may begin a reign of terror in a classroom if no adult stops repeated threats.","zh":"如果沒有成人制止反覆威脅，欺凌者可能在課室展開恐怖統治。"},{"en":"Such a period continues when victims feel unsafe and authorities fail to control the person.","zh":"當受害者感到不安全而當局未能控制該人，這段時期會持續。"},{"en":"The phrase is dramatic and used for repeated fear-causing behaviour.","zh":"這個短語語氣戲劇化，用於反覆造成恐懼的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"reign of terror","meaning":"恐怖統治；恐怖時期","examples":[{"en":"The murders created a reign of terror in Whitechapel.","zh":"這些謀殺案在白教堂區造成恐怖時期。"},{"en":"A reign of terror is a period when people live in fear because of repeated threats or violence.","zh":"reign of terror 是人們因反覆威脅或暴力而活在恐懼中的時期。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood may feel under a reign of terror if robberies happen every night.","zh":"如果每晚都有搶劫案，社區可能感到處於恐怖時期。"},{"en":"A reign of terror damages daily life because people stop feeling safe.","zh":"恐怖時期會破壞日常生活，因為人們不再感到安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fear spreading across a community.","zh":"這個短語描述恐懼在社區中擴散。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the streets of Whitechapel","meaning":"白教堂區的街頭","examples":[{"en":"The Ripper attacks took place in the streets of Whitechapel.","zh":"開膛手傑克的襲擊發生在白教堂區的街頭。"},{"en":"The streets of Whitechapel refers to the public roads and alleys of the Whitechapel district in London.","zh":"streets of Whitechapel 指倫敦白教堂區的公共道路和小巷。"},{"en":"A history lesson may mention the streets of Whitechapel when discussing poverty and crime in Victorian London.","zh":"歷史課討論維多利亞時代倫敦的貧窮和罪案時，可能提及白教堂區的街頭。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the case a specific urban setting.","zh":"這個短語給案件一個具體城市場景。"},{"en":"It helps readers imagine the local environment where the events occurred.","zh":"它幫助讀者想像事件發生的本地環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"forensic science","meaning":"法證科學","examples":[{"en":"Forensic science was barely in its infancy in 1888.","zh":"法證科學在1888年尚處於萌芽階段。"},{"en":"Forensic science uses scientific methods to examine evidence for criminal investigations.","zh":"forensic science 使用科學方法檢驗刑事調查中的證據。"},{"en":"Police may use forensic science to study fingerprints, blood, fibres, or digital records.","zh":"警方可能使用法證科學研究指紋、血液、纖維或數碼紀錄。"},{"en":"Strong forensic science can connect a suspect to a crime scene more reliably.","zh":"強大的法證科學可以更可靠地把疑犯與犯罪現場連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to science used in law and criminal evidence.","zh":"這個短語指用於法律和刑事證據的科學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"barely in its infancy","meaning":"尚處於萌芽階段","examples":[{"en":"Forensic science was barely in its infancy during the Ripper investigation.","zh":"在開膛手傑克調查期間，法證科學尚處於萌芽階段。"},{"en":"Barely in its infancy means only just beginning and still very undeveloped.","zh":"barely in its infancy 指才剛開始，仍非常未成熟。"},{"en":"Online education was barely in its infancy when most families had no reliable internet.","zh":"當大多數家庭沒有可靠互聯網時，網上教育尚處於萌芽階段。"},{"en":"A field in its infancy lacks tools, rules, and experienced specialists.","zh":"處於萌芽階段的領域缺乏工具、規則和有經驗專家。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a very early stage of development.","zh":"這個短語描述非常早期的發展階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"rudimentary awareness of","meaning":"對……只有初步認識","examples":[{"en":"Investigators had only a rudimentary awareness of crime-scene preservation.","zh":"調查員對犯罪現場保存只有初步認識。"},{"en":"Rudimentary awareness of something means only a basic and incomplete understanding of it.","zh":"rudimentary awareness of 某事，指只有基本而不完整的理解。"},{"en":"A beginner may have a rudimentary awareness of grammar but still make many sentence errors.","zh":"初學者可能對文法只有初步認識，因此仍犯許多句子錯誤。"},{"en":"Rudimentary awareness is not enough when a task requires careful professional skill.","zh":"當任務需要仔細專業技能，初步認識並不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes early, simple knowledge rather than deep expertise.","zh":"這個短語描述早期、簡單知識，而非深入專業能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"keep a murder scene intact","meaning":"保持謀殺案現場完整","examples":[{"en":"Police had some awareness of the need to keep a murder scene intact.","zh":"警方對保持謀殺案現場完整的需要有一些認識。"},{"en":"To keep a murder scene intact means to leave it unchanged so evidence is not lost or damaged.","zh":"keep a murder scene intact 指保持現場不變，以免證據遺失或受損。"},{"en":"Police may stop people entering a room to keep a murder scene intact.","zh":"警方可能阻止人進入房間，以保持謀殺案現場完整。"},{"en":"If a scene is disturbed, footprints, fingerprints, or objects may lose their value as evidence.","zh":"如果現場被擾亂，腳印、指紋或物件可能失去證據價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes protecting the original condition of a crime scene.","zh":"這個短語描述保護犯罪現場的原始狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"preserve vital clues","meaning":"保存重要線索","examples":[{"en":"A murder scene must be kept intact to preserve vital clues.","zh":"謀殺案現場必須保持完整，以保存重要線索。"},{"en":"To preserve vital clues means to protect important evidence so it can be studied later.","zh":"preserve vital clues 指保護重要證據，使其之後可被研究。"},{"en":"A teacher preserves vital clues about cheating by keeping the original test papers.","zh":"老師透過保留原本試卷來保存作弊的重要線索。"},{"en":"If clues are not preserved, investigators may never know what happened.","zh":"如果線索沒有保存，調查員可能永遠不知道發生甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes safeguarding important evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述保護重要證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"vital clues","meaning":"重要線索","examples":[{"en":"The police may have lost vital clues during the investigation.","zh":"警方可能在調查中失去重要線索。"},{"en":"Vital clues are important pieces of evidence that can help solve a problem or case.","zh":"vital clues 是可以幫助解決問題或案件的重要證據。"},{"en":"A broken lock may be a vital clue in a burglary investigation.","zh":"在入屋爆竊調查中，壞掉的鎖可能是重要線索。"},{"en":"Losing vital clues can prevent police from identifying the person responsible.","zh":"失去重要線索可以令警方無法識別責任人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence that matters greatly.","zh":"這個短語描述非常重要的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the means to","meaning":"……的方法；……的手段","examples":[{"en":"The means to analyse evidence through DNA testing did not yet exist.","zh":"透過 DNA 檢測分析證據的方法當時尚未存在。"},{"en":"The means to do something are the tools, methods, or resources needed to do it.","zh":"means to do something 是做某事所需的工具、方法或資源。"},{"en":"A student without internet may not have the means to attend an online lesson.","zh":"沒有互聯網的學生可能沒有方法參加網上課。"},{"en":"Without the means to test evidence, investigators must rely on weaker methods.","zh":"沒有檢測證據的方法，調查員就必須依賴較弱的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on practical ability, not just desire.","zh":"這個短語重點在實際能力，而不只是願望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"thoroughly analyse","meaning":"徹底分析","examples":[{"en":"Modern science can thoroughly analyse evidence from a crime scene.","zh":"現代科學可以徹底分析犯罪現場的證據。"},{"en":"To thoroughly analyse something means to examine it carefully, completely, and in detail.","zh":"thoroughly analyse 某事，指仔細、完整而詳細地檢查它。"},{"en":"A doctor may thoroughly analyse test results before choosing treatment.","zh":"醫生可能在選擇治療前徹底分析檢查結果。"},{"en":"Thorough analysis can reveal details that a quick look misses.","zh":"徹底分析可以揭示快速一看所錯過的細節。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep and careful examination.","zh":"這個短語描述深入而仔細的檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"DNA testing","meaning":"DNA 檢測","examples":[{"en":"DNA testing was still unavailable during the Ripper investigation.","zh":"在開膛手傑克調查期間，DNA 檢測仍未可用。"},{"en":"DNA testing is a scientific method that compares genetic material to identify people or relationships.","zh":"DNA testing 是比較遺傳物質以識別人物或親屬關係的科學方法。"},{"en":"Police may use DNA testing to connect a suspect with evidence left at a scene.","zh":"警方可能使用 DNA 檢測，把疑犯與現場留下的證據連起來。"},{"en":"Hospitals can use DNA testing to diagnose some inherited diseases.","zh":"醫院可以使用 DNA 檢測診斷某些遺傳病。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to modern genetic analysis.","zh":"這個短語指現代遺傳分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be light-years away","meaning":"遙不可及","examples":[{"en":"DNA testing was still light-years away in 1888.","zh":"在1888年，DNA 檢測仍然遙不可及。"},{"en":"To be light-years away means to be far in the future or far beyond current ability.","zh":"be light-years away 指在遙遠未來，或遠超當前能力。"},{"en":"For many small schools, virtual reality classrooms are still light-years away.","zh":"對許多小學校而言，虛擬實境課室仍然遙不可及。"},{"en":"The phrase does not literally measure distance here; it stresses extreme remoteness.","zh":"這個短語在此不是字面量度距離，而是強調極度遙遠。"},{"en":"It shows that a method was not realistically available at the time.","zh":"它顯示某方法在當時並不實際可用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the publication of","meaning":"……的出版","examples":[{"en":"The publication of Hans Gross’s handbook helped establish forensic science.","zh":"Hans Gross 手冊的出版幫助確立法證科學。"},{"en":"The publication of a book or article means its release for people to read.","zh":"publication of 書或文章，指它被發行供人閱讀。"},{"en":"The publication of new exam guidelines can change how teachers prepare students.","zh":"新考試指引的出版可以改變老師如何準備學生。"},{"en":"Publication matters because ideas become available to a wider audience.","zh":"出版很重要，因為想法會變得可供更廣泛讀者接觸。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the moment written knowledge enters public or professional use.","zh":"這個短語標示書面知識進入公眾或專業使用的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lay the foundation for","meaning":"為……奠定基礎","examples":[{"en":"Hans Gross’s handbook laid the foundation for forensic science.","zh":"Hans Gross 的手冊為法證科學奠定基礎。"},{"en":"To lay the foundation for something means to create the basic ideas or conditions needed for it to develop.","zh":"lay the foundation for 某事，指創造其發展所需的基本想法或條件。"},{"en":"Good phonics teaching can lay the foundation for confident reading.","zh":"良好自然拼讀教學可以為自信閱讀奠定基礎。"},{"en":"Early rules and methods can lay the foundation for a new profession.","zh":"早期規則和方法可以為新專業奠定基礎。"},{"en":"The phrase describes building the starting base for later progress.","zh":"這個短語描述為後來進步建立起點基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"too late to help","meaning":"太遲而無法幫助","examples":[{"en":"The handbook appeared too late to help the Ripper investigation.","zh":"這本手冊出現得太遲，無法幫助開膛手傑克調查。"},{"en":"Too late to help means arriving after the moment when it could have made a useful difference.","zh":"too late to help 指在本可發揮作用的時刻之後才出現。"},{"en":"Extra revision notes are too late to help if they arrive after the exam.","zh":"如果額外溫習筆記在考試後才到，就太遲而無法幫助。"},{"en":"A solution can be good but still too late to help a particular case.","zh":"解決方法可以很好，但對某特定案件仍然來得太遲而無法幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase describes missed timing rather than uselessness.","zh":"這個短語描述錯過時機，而不是本身無用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lack knowledge of","meaning":"缺乏對……的認識","examples":[{"en":"The investigators lacked knowledge of modern forensic techniques.","zh":"調查員缺乏對現代法證技術的認識。"},{"en":"To lack knowledge of something means not to know enough about it.","zh":"lack knowledge of 某事，指對它了解不足。"},{"en":"A student may lack knowledge of essay structure even if her vocabulary is strong.","zh":"學生即使詞彙強，也可能缺乏對文章結構的認識。"},{"en":"Lacking knowledge of a method can cause people to miss useful solutions.","zh":"缺乏對某方法的認識，可以令人錯過有用解決方案。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a gap in understanding.","zh":"這個短語指出理解上的缺口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"modern forensic techniques","meaning":"現代法證技術","examples":[{"en":"The Ripper investigators did not have modern forensic techniques.","zh":"開膛手傑克案調查員沒有現代法證技術。"},{"en":"Modern forensic techniques are current scientific methods used to examine crime evidence.","zh":"modern forensic techniques 是用來檢驗犯罪證據的現代科學方法。"},{"en":"Fingerprint databases, DNA testing, and digital analysis are modern forensic techniques.","zh":"指紋資料庫、DNA 檢測和數碼分析都是現代法證技術。"},{"en":"These techniques can make investigations more accurate and less dependent on guesswork.","zh":"這些技術可以令調查更準確，較少依賴猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to advanced scientific tools in criminal investigation.","zh":"這個短語指刑事調查中的先進科學工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"miss out on","meaning":"錯過","examples":[{"en":"The Ripper investigation just missed out on developments in fingerprint identification.","zh":"開膛手傑克調查剛好錯過了指紋識別方面的發展。"},{"en":"To miss out on something means to fail to benefit from an opportunity or development.","zh":"miss out on 某事，指未能從機會或發展中受益。"},{"en":"A student may miss out on a scholarship if she submits the form late.","zh":"如果學生遲交表格，可能錯過獎學金。"},{"en":"Missing out on new technology can leave people using weaker old methods.","zh":"錯過新科技可能令人繼續使用較弱的舊方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes losing a chance to use or enjoy something.","zh":"這個短語描述失去使用或享受某物的機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"developments in","meaning":"……方面的發展","examples":[{"en":"The police missed developments in fingerprint identification.","zh":"警方錯過了指紋識別方面的發展。"},{"en":"Developments in a field are new improvements, discoveries, or changes in that area.","zh":"developments in 某領域，是該範疇中的新改進、發現或變化。"},{"en":"Teachers follow developments in education technology to improve lessons.","zh":"老師關注教育科技方面的發展，以改善課堂。"},{"en":"New developments can change what professionals are able to do.","zh":"新發展可以改變專業人士能做到甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase points to progress within a specific subject.","zh":"這個短語指出某特定主題內的進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fingerprint identification","meaning":"指紋識別","examples":[{"en":"Fingerprint identification might have helped police identify the Ripper.","zh":"指紋識別本可能幫助警方識別開膛手傑克。"},{"en":"Fingerprint identification is the use of fingerprints to recognise or confirm a person’s identity.","zh":"fingerprint identification 是使用指紋辨認或確認人物身份。"},{"en":"Police use fingerprint identification when prints are left on glass, doors, or tools.","zh":"當指紋留在玻璃、門或工具上，警方會使用指紋識別。"},{"en":"Because fingerprints are highly individual, they can provide powerful evidence.","zh":"因為指紋高度個人化，它們可以提供有力證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes identifying people through finger marks.","zh":"這個短語描述透過手指印記識別人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lead police to","meaning":"引領警方找到……","examples":[{"en":"Fingerprint evidence might have led police to the Ripper’s identity.","zh":"指紋證據本可能引領警方找到開膛手傑克的身份。"},{"en":"To lead police to something means to guide investigators toward a discovery or suspect.","zh":"lead police to 某物，指引導調查員找到發現或疑犯。"},{"en":"A witness statement may lead police to a stolen bicycle hidden nearby.","zh":"證人供詞可能引領警方找到藏在附近的失竊單車。"},{"en":"Strong evidence can lead police to the right person faster.","zh":"有力證據可以更快引領警方找到正確人物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence pointing investigators in a useful direction.","zh":"這個短語描述證據把調查員指向有用方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the identity of","meaning":"……的身份","examples":[{"en":"The police failed to discover the identity of the Ripper.","zh":"警方未能發現開膛手傑克的身份。"},{"en":"The identity of someone means who that person really is.","zh":"identity of 某人，指該人真正是誰。"},{"en":"A school may try to discover the identity of a student who posted anonymous insults.","zh":"學校可能嘗試找出匿名發布侮辱內容的學生身份。"},{"en":"Finding identity often requires evidence such as records, witnesses, or personal details.","zh":"找出身份常需要紀錄、證人或個人資料等證據。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on naming or recognising a person.","zh":"這個短語重點在命名或辨認某人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"nearly a decade prior to","meaning":"早於……接近十年","examples":[{"en":"Dr Henry Faulds published his letter nearly a decade prior to the first Ripper murder.","zh":"Henry Faulds 醫生早於第一宗開膛手傑克謀殺案接近十年發表了他的信。"},{"en":"Nearly a decade prior to means almost ten years before something.","zh":"nearly a decade prior to 指早於某事接近十年。"},{"en":"The school building was planned nearly a decade prior to its opening.","zh":"學校建築早於開幕接近十年已被規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare the timing of two events.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較兩件事的時間。"},{"en":"It suggests that an idea existed before the later event, but perhaps was not yet widely used.","zh":"它暗示某想法早於後來事件存在，但可能尚未廣泛使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"scientific journal","meaning":"科學期刊","examples":[{"en":"Dr Henry Faulds published a letter in the scientific journal Nature.","zh":"Henry Faulds 醫生在科學期刊《Nature》發表了一封信。"},{"en":"A scientific journal is a publication where researchers share studies, evidence, and professional arguments.","zh":"scientific journal 是研究人員分享研究、證據和專業論點的刊物。"},{"en":"University students read scientific journals to find reliable research for essays.","zh":"大學生閱讀科學期刊，為論文尋找可靠研究。"},{"en":"Publishing in a journal allows other experts to examine and discuss new ideas.","zh":"在期刊發表可以讓其他專家檢視和討論新想法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a formal source of scientific knowledge.","zh":"這個短語指正式科學知識來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"outline for the first time","meaning":"首次概述","examples":[{"en":"Faulds outlined for the first time the use of fingerprints for identification.","zh":"Faulds 首次概述使用指紋作識別用途。"},{"en":"To outline something for the first time means to present the basic idea publicly before others have done so.","zh":"outline for the first time 指在其他人之前公開呈現某想法的基本內容。"},{"en":"A teacher may outline for the first time a new marking scheme before an exam.","zh":"老師可能在考試前首次概述新的評分方案。"},{"en":"An outline gives the main points, not every detail.","zh":"概述提供主要重點，而不是每個細節。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the first clear presentation of an idea.","zh":"這個短語標示某想法首次被清楚呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the possibility of","meaning":"……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"He described the possibility of using fingerprints for identification.","zh":"他描述了使用指紋作識別用途的可能性。"},{"en":"The possibility of something means the chance that it can happen or be done.","zh":"possibility of 某事，指它發生或被做到的機會。"},{"en":"A school may discuss the possibility of starting lessons later in the morning.","zh":"學校可能討論早上較遲開始上課的可能性。"},{"en":"Considering a possibility allows people to plan before it becomes certain.","zh":"考慮一種可能性，讓人們在它變成確定前作規劃。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an option or potential future action.","zh":"這個短語引出一個選項或潛在未來行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"for identification purposes","meaning":"作識別用途","examples":[{"en":"Fingerprints could be used for identification purposes.","zh":"指紋可以作識別用途。"},{"en":"For identification purposes means in order to recognise or confirm who someone is.","zh":"for identification purposes 指為了辨認或確認某人身份。"},{"en":"Students may show ID cards for identification purposes before entering an exam hall.","zh":"學生進入試場前可能要出示學生證作識別用途。"},{"en":"Information used for identification purposes should be handled carefully.","zh":"作識別用途的資料應小心處理。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the purpose of recognising identity.","zh":"這個短語解釋確認身份的用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"put theory into practice","meaning":"將理論付諸實踐","examples":[{"en":"Sir Francis Galton sought to put fingerprint theory into practice.","zh":"Francis Galton 爵士試圖將指紋理論付諸實踐。"},{"en":"To put theory into practice means to turn an idea into real action or use.","zh":"put theory into practice 指把想法轉化為實際行動或使用。"},{"en":"A student puts grammar theory into practice when she uses the rule correctly in an essay.","zh":"當學生在文章中正確使用文法規則，她就是將文法理論付諸實踐。"},{"en":"Ideas become useful only when people can apply them in real situations.","zh":"想法只有在人們能應用於真實情況時才變得有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving from thinking to doing.","zh":"這個短語描述從思考走向行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"new-found method","meaning":"新發現的方法","examples":[{"en":"The new-found method of dactyloscopy helped identify criminals.","zh":"新發現的指紋鑑定法幫助識別罪犯。"},{"en":"A new-found method is a recently discovered way of doing something.","zh":"new-found method 是最近發現的做事方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a new-found method to help weak students remember vocabulary.","zh":"老師可能使用新發現的方法，幫助較弱學生記住詞彙。"},{"en":"New-found methods can change a field when they solve old problems better.","zh":"當新發現的方法更好地解決舊問題，它們可以改變一個領域。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights recent discovery and practical use.","zh":"這個短語突出近期發現和實際用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dactyloscopy","meaning":"指紋鑑定法","examples":[{"en":"Dactyloscopy was later known as fingerprinting.","zh":"dactyloscopy 後來被稱為指紋鑑定。"},{"en":"Dactyloscopy is the scientific identification of people through fingerprints.","zh":"dactyloscopy 是透過指紋科學識別人物的方法。"},{"en":"Police used dactyloscopy to compare marks left at crime scenes with suspects’ fingers.","zh":"警方使用指紋鑑定法，把犯罪現場留下的印記與疑犯手指作比較。"},{"en":"The method became important because fingerprints can be highly distinctive.","zh":"這種方法變得重要，因為指紋可以高度獨特。"},{"en":"The word is technical and is now more commonly expressed as fingerprinting.","zh":"這個詞較技術性，現在更常說成 fingerprinting。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"later known as","meaning":"後來被稱為","examples":[{"en":"Dactyloscopy was later known as fingerprinting.","zh":"dactyloscopy 後來被稱為 fingerprinting。"},{"en":"Later known as means given another name at a later time.","zh":"later known as 指後來被給予另一個名稱。"},{"en":"A small study group was later known as the school debate team.","zh":"一個小型學習小組後來被稱為學校辯論隊。"},{"en":"Names may change when an idea becomes more common or easier to understand.","zh":"當想法變得更普及或更易理解，名稱可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an earlier term with a later name.","zh":"這個短語把早期術語與後來名稱連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fingerprinting","meaning":"指紋鑑定","examples":[{"en":"Fingerprinting became an important tool for identifying criminals.","zh":"指紋鑑定成為識別罪犯的重要工具。"},{"en":"Fingerprinting is the recording and comparing of fingerprints for identification.","zh":"fingerprinting 是記錄和比較指紋作身份識別。"},{"en":"Police may use fingerprinting when a thief touches a window or door handle.","zh":"當竊賊觸碰窗戶或門柄，警方可能使用指紋鑑定。"},{"en":"Fingerprinting helps because each person’s fingerprints are usually unique.","zh":"指紋鑑定有幫助，因為每個人的指紋通常獨一無二。"},{"en":"The word refers to a practical method of identity checking.","zh":"這個詞指身份查核的實用方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"employ the technique to","meaning":"運用該技術去……","examples":[{"en":"Galton employed the technique to identify criminals successfully.","zh":"Galton 運用該技術成功識別罪犯。"},{"en":"To employ the technique to do something means to use that method for a specific purpose.","zh":"employ the technique to do something 指為特定目的使用該方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may employ the technique of mind maps to help students plan essays.","zh":"老師可能運用心智圖技術去幫助學生規劃文章。"},{"en":"A technique becomes useful when people know when and how to apply it.","zh":"當人們知道何時和如何應用技術，它就變得有用。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to say “use the method to”.","zh":"這個短語是 “use the method to” 的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"successfully identify criminals","meaning":"成功識別罪犯","examples":[{"en":"Fingerprinting helped police successfully identify criminals.","zh":"指紋鑑定幫助警方成功識別罪犯。"},{"en":"To successfully identify criminals means to correctly discover who committed crimes.","zh":"successfully identify criminals 指正確找出犯案者是誰。"},{"en":"Security footage can help shops successfully identify criminals who steal goods.","zh":"保安錄像可以幫助店舖成功識別偷貨罪犯。"},{"en":"Correct identification prevents innocent people from being blamed.","zh":"正確識別可以防止無辜者被責怪。"},{"en":"The phrase describes accurate recognition of offenders.","zh":"這個短語描述對犯案者的準確認出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"arrive just too late for","meaning":"對……而言來得太遲","examples":[{"en":"New fingerprinting technology arrived just too late for the Ripper investigators.","zh":"新指紋鑑定技術對開膛手傑克案調查員而言來得太遲。"},{"en":"To arrive just too late for someone means to become available shortly after it could have helped them.","zh":"arrive just too late for 某人，指在本可幫到他們之後不久才出現。"},{"en":"The medicine arrived just too late for the patient who needed it urgently.","zh":"藥物對急需它的病人而言來得太遲。"},{"en":"A tool can be valuable but still arrive too late for a particular problem.","zh":"工具可以有價值，但對某特定問題而言仍來得太遲。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises unfortunate timing.","zh":"這個短語強調不幸的時機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"could not be blamed for","meaning":"不能因……而被責怪","examples":[{"en":"The investigators could not be blamed for lacking future forensic knowledge.","zh":"調查員不能因缺乏未來法證知識而被責怪。"},{"en":"Could not be blamed for something means it would be unfair to hold someone responsible for it.","zh":"could not be blamed for 某事，指要某人為此負責並不公平。"},{"en":"A student could not be blamed for missing class if the school bus broke down.","zh":"如果校巴壞了，學生不能因缺課而被責怪。"},{"en":"People cannot be blamed for not using technology that did not yet exist.","zh":"人們不能因沒有使用當時尚不存在的科技而被責怪。"},{"en":"The phrase separates understandable limitation from real fault.","zh":"這個短語把可理解的限制與真正過錯分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lack of forensic knowledge","meaning":"缺乏法證知識","examples":[{"en":"The police had a serious lack of forensic knowledge.","zh":"警方嚴重缺乏法證知識。"},{"en":"Lack of forensic knowledge means not having enough understanding of scientific crime investigation.","zh":"lack of forensic knowledge 指對科學刑事調查了解不足。"},{"en":"A lack of forensic knowledge can cause officers to destroy evidence accidentally.","zh":"缺乏法證知識可以令警員意外破壞證據。"},{"en":"Training reduces this lack by teaching police how to collect and protect clues.","zh":"培訓透過教警方如何收集和保護線索來減少這種缺乏。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an important gap in investigative skill.","zh":"這個短語描述調查技能中的重要缺口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"failure to apply","meaning":"未能應用……","examples":[{"en":"Their failure to apply known methods suggested incompetence.","zh":"他們未能應用已知方法，顯示出無能。"},{"en":"Failure to apply something means not using a method, rule, or idea when it should be used.","zh":"failure to apply 某事，指在應使用方法、規則或想法時沒有使用。"},{"en":"A student’s failure to apply grammar rules can weaken an otherwise good essay.","zh":"學生未能應用文法規則，可以削弱一篇本來不錯的文章。"},{"en":"If workers know safety rules but ignore them, the failure to apply them can cause accidents.","zh":"如果工人知道安全規則卻忽視它們，未能應用規則可以造成意外。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises not using available knowledge.","zh":"這個短語批評沒有使用可用知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"investigative methods","meaning":"調查方法","examples":[{"en":"Known investigative methods were not always used properly.","zh":"已知調查方法並不總是被妥善使用。"},{"en":"Investigative methods are procedures used to discover facts in an enquiry.","zh":"investigative methods 是在調查中用來發現事實的程序。"},{"en":"Interviewing witnesses, collecting evidence, and checking records are investigative methods.","zh":"訪問證人、收集證據和查核紀錄都是調查方法。"},{"en":"Good methods make an investigation fairer and more reliable.","zh":"好方法令調查更公平、更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the practical tools of enquiry.","zh":"這個短語指調查的實用工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"crime scene","meaning":"犯罪現場","examples":[{"en":"Crime-scene procedures were poorly handled in the Ripper case.","zh":"開膛手傑克案件中的犯罪現場程序處理得很差。"},{"en":"A crime scene is the place where a crime happened or where evidence may be found.","zh":"crime scene 是罪案發生或可能找到證據的地方。"},{"en":"Police may close a street to protect a crime scene after a serious attack.","zh":"嚴重襲擊後，警方可能封鎖街道以保護犯罪現場。"},{"en":"If a crime scene is not protected, evidence can be lost or contaminated.","zh":"如果犯罪現場沒有被保護，證據可能遺失或被污染。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a location central to an investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述調查中的核心地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"smack of incompetence","meaning":"顯得無能；帶有無能意味","examples":[{"en":"The failure to use known methods smacked of incompetence.","zh":"未能使用已知方法顯得無能。"},{"en":"To smack of incompetence means to strongly suggest lack of ability or poor professional judgement.","zh":"smack of incompetence 指強烈顯示缺乏能力或專業判斷差。"},{"en":"Losing every student’s exam paper would smack of incompetence.","zh":"遺失每名學生的試卷會顯得無能。"},{"en":"Repeated mistakes can make an organisation’s work smack of incompetence.","zh":"反覆錯誤可以令一個組織的工作帶有無能意味。"},{"en":"The phrase is critical and implies that the failure looked avoidable.","zh":"這個短語帶批評意味，暗示失敗看似本可避免。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"standard practice","meaning":"標準做法","examples":[{"en":"Photographing a crime scene was not standard practice at the time.","zh":"拍攝犯罪現場在當時並不是標準做法。"},{"en":"Standard practice is the normal accepted way of doing something in a profession.","zh":"standard practice 是某專業中正常被接受的做事方式。"},{"en":"Taking attendance before a school trip is standard practice.","zh":"學校旅行前點名是標準做法。"},{"en":"Standard practice helps people work consistently and avoid careless mistakes.","zh":"標準做法幫助人們一致工作並避免粗心錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what is usually done as a rule.","zh":"這個短語描述通常按規矩會做的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"known procedure","meaning":"已知程序","examples":[{"en":"Crime-scene photography was a known procedure even then.","zh":"犯罪現場攝影即使在當時也是已知程序。"},{"en":"A known procedure is a method that people already understand or recognise.","zh":"known procedure 是人們已經理解或認識的方法。"},{"en":"Fire drills are a known procedure for preparing students to leave safely.","zh":"消防演習是讓學生準備安全離開的已知程序。"},{"en":"If a known procedure is ignored, the mistake is harder to excuse.","zh":"如果已知程序被忽視，錯誤就更難辯解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a method already available at the time.","zh":"這個短語描述當時已可使用的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lead the investigation","meaning":"領導調查","examples":[{"en":"The officers leading the investigation made questionable decisions.","zh":"負責領導調查的警員作出了可疑的決定。"},{"en":"To lead the investigation means to direct and manage the enquiry.","zh":"lead the investigation 指指揮和管理調查。"},{"en":"A senior teacher may lead the investigation into missing exam papers.","zh":"高級老師可能領導遺失試卷的調查。"},{"en":"The person leading the investigation decides what evidence to collect and whom to interview.","zh":"領導調查的人決定收集甚麼證據和訪問誰。"},{"en":"The phrase describes taking responsibility for guiding an enquiry.","zh":"這個短語描述負責引導調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"see fit to","meaning":"認為適合去……","examples":[{"en":"The officers saw fit to photograph only one victim at the crime scene.","zh":"警員認為適合只在犯罪現場拍攝一名受害者。"},{"en":"To see fit to do something means to decide that it is appropriate or worth doing.","zh":"see fit to do something 指決定某事合適或值得做。"},{"en":"A principal may see fit to cancel outdoor lessons during a typhoon warning.","zh":"校長可能認為在颱風警告期間取消戶外課是合適的。"},{"en":"The phrase can sound critical if the decision seems strange or inadequate.","zh":"如果決定看起來奇怪或不足，這個短語可以帶批評意味。"},{"en":"It describes someone’s judgement about what should be done.","zh":"它描述某人對應做甚麼的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"even more bizarrely","meaning":"更奇怪的是","examples":[{"en":"Even more bizarrely, the photographs focused mainly on the victim’s eyes.","zh":"更奇怪的是，照片主要集中於受害者的眼睛。"},{"en":"Even more bizarrely means even more strangely or unexpectedly than what was already mentioned.","zh":"even more bizarrely 指比已提及的事情更奇怪或更出乎意料。"},{"en":"The student forgot his homework; even more bizarrely, he brought an empty folder instead.","zh":"那名學生忘記帶功課；更奇怪的是，他帶了一個空文件夾。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a detail that makes a situation seem stranger.","zh":"這個短語引出令情況看起來更奇怪的細節。"},{"en":"It signals that the writer finds the action very unusual.","zh":"它表示作者覺得該行動非常不尋常。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"focus mainly on","meaning":"主要集中於……","examples":[{"en":"The photographs focused mainly on the victim’s eyes.","zh":"照片主要集中於受害者的眼睛。"},{"en":"To focus mainly on something means to give most attention to that thing.","zh":"focus mainly on 某事，指把大部分注意力放在該事上。"},{"en":"A teacher may focus mainly on grammar if students keep making sentence errors.","zh":"如果學生不斷犯句子錯誤，老師可能主要集中於文法。"},{"en":"Focusing mainly on one detail can cause people to miss other important evidence.","zh":"主要集中於一個細節，可以令人錯過其他重要證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where attention is concentrated.","zh":"這個短語描述注意力集中在哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"to the neglect of all else","meaning":"而忽略其他一切","examples":[{"en":"The photographs focused on the eyes to the neglect of all else.","zh":"這些照片集中於眼睛，而忽略其他一切。"},{"en":"To the neglect of all else means while ignoring everything else that also matters.","zh":"to the neglect of all else 指忽略其他同樣重要的事情。"},{"en":"A student who studies vocabulary to the neglect of all else may still write weak essays.","zh":"只顧溫習詞彙而忽略其他一切的學生，文章可能仍然薄弱。"},{"en":"Over-focusing on one area can damage overall performance.","zh":"過度集中於一個範疇可以損害整體表現。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises an unbalanced focus.","zh":"這個短語批評不平衡的專注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"forlorn hope","meaning":"渺茫的希望","examples":[{"en":"The idea that the killer’s image remained on the retina was a forlorn hope.","zh":"認為兇手影像留在視網膜上的想法，是一個渺茫的希望。"},{"en":"A forlorn hope is a hope that is almost certain to fail.","zh":"forlorn hope 是幾乎必定失敗的希望。"},{"en":"Waiting for a closed shop to reopen at midnight may be a forlorn hope.","zh":"午夜等待已關門的店重開，可能是渺茫的希望。"},{"en":"People may cling to a forlorn hope when they have no better solution.","zh":"當人們沒有更好解決方法，可能會抓住渺茫希望。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a desperate and unrealistic expectation.","zh":"這個短語描述絕望且不現實的期待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the imprint of","meaning":"……的印記","examples":[{"en":"Investigators hoped to find the imprint of the Ripper on the victim’s retina.","zh":"調查員希望在受害者視網膜上找到開膛手傑克的印記。"},{"en":"The imprint of something is a mark, image, or lasting trace left by it.","zh":"imprint of 某物，是它留下的痕跡、影像或持久印象。"},{"en":"A wet shoe can leave the imprint of its sole on a clean floor.","zh":"濕鞋可以在乾淨地板上留下鞋底印記。"},{"en":"A strong childhood memory can leave an imprint on a person’s later choices.","zh":"強烈童年記憶可以在一個人後來選擇上留下印記。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe a physical mark or a lasting influence.","zh":"這個短語可描述實體痕跡或持久影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be recorded on","meaning":"被記錄在……上","examples":[{"en":"They believed the killer’s image might have been recorded on the victim’s retina.","zh":"他們相信兇手影像可能被記錄在受害者視網膜上。"},{"en":"To be recorded on something means to be captured, stored, or marked there.","zh":"be recorded on 某物，指被捕捉、儲存或標記在那裏。"},{"en":"A school meeting may be recorded on video for absent parents.","zh":"學校會議可能被記錄在影片上，供缺席家長觀看。"},{"en":"Information recorded on paper or a device can be reviewed later.","zh":"記錄在紙上或裝置上的資料可以之後查看。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where evidence or information is preserved.","zh":"這個短語描述證據或資料保存的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"retina","meaning":"視網膜","examples":[{"en":"The police focused on the victim’s retina in the photographs.","zh":"警方在照片中集中於受害者的視網膜。"},{"en":"The retina is the light-sensitive layer at the back of the eye.","zh":"retina 是眼睛後方感光的一層組織。"},{"en":"Doctors examine the retina to check eye health and some medical conditions.","zh":"醫生檢查視網膜，以了解眼睛健康和某些醫療狀況。"},{"en":"Damage to the retina can affect vision because it helps receive images.","zh":"視網膜受損可以影響視力，因為它幫助接收影像。"},{"en":"The word refers to an important part of the eye.","zh":"這個詞指眼睛的重要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at the time of someone’s death","meaning":"在某人死亡的一刻","examples":[{"en":"They thought the image might have been recorded at the time of the victim’s death.","zh":"他們認為影像可能在受害者死亡的一刻被記錄下來。"},{"en":"At the time of someone’s death means at the moment when that person died.","zh":"at the time of someone’s death 指某人死亡的那一刻。"},{"en":"A doctor records a patient’s condition at the time of death for legal and medical reasons.","zh":"醫生基於法律和醫療原因，記錄病人在死亡一刻的情況。"},{"en":"Details from that moment can matter in an investigation.","zh":"那一刻的細節在調查中可能很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase fixes an event to the exact moment of death.","zh":"這個短語把事件固定在死亡的準確時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"draw conclusions from","meaning":"從……得出結論","examples":[{"en":"No conclusions were drawn from the unusual photographic undertaking.","zh":"沒有人從這次不尋常的攝影行動中得出結論。"},{"en":"To draw conclusions from something means to decide what it shows after examining it.","zh":"draw conclusions from 某事，指檢視後判斷它顯示甚麼。"},{"en":"A teacher should not draw conclusions from one test if a student was ill that day.","zh":"如果學生當日生病，老師不應從一次測驗得出結論。"},{"en":"Good conclusions need enough evidence and careful reasoning.","zh":"好結論需要足夠證據和仔細推理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a judgement based on information.","zh":"這個短語描述基於資料作出判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"undertaking","meaning":"行動；工作","examples":[{"en":"No useful conclusions came from the photographic undertaking.","zh":"這次攝影行動沒有得出有用結論。"},{"en":"An undertaking is a task, project, or piece of work that someone takes on.","zh":"undertaking 是某人承擔的任務、項目或工作。"},{"en":"Organising a school concert is a large undertaking because it needs planning, rehearsal, and equipment.","zh":"組織學校音樂會是一項大型工作，因為它需要規劃、排練和設備。"},{"en":"A difficult undertaking can fail if its purpose is unclear.","zh":"如果目的不清楚，困難工作可能失敗。"},{"en":"The word is formal and often refers to work requiring effort.","zh":"這個詞較正式，常指需要努力的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"serious criticism","meaning":"嚴重批評","examples":[{"en":"A serious criticism was levelled against the investigating police.","zh":"針對負責調查的警方有人提出嚴重批評。"},{"en":"Serious criticism is strong disapproval of someone’s actions, often because the mistake matters.","zh":"serious criticism 是對某人行動的強烈不滿，通常因錯誤很重要。"},{"en":"A hospital may face serious criticism if it loses patient records.","zh":"如果醫院遺失病人紀錄，可能面對嚴重批評。"},{"en":"Serious criticism can force an organisation to review its procedures.","zh":"嚴重批評可以迫使組織檢討程序。"},{"en":"The phrase describes blame that is important and not casual.","zh":"這個短語描述重要而非隨便的責難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be levelled against","meaning":"針對……提出","examples":[{"en":"Criticism has been levelled against the police for tampering with evidence.","zh":"有人針對警方干預證據提出批評。"},{"en":"To be levelled against someone means to be directed at them as an accusation or criticism.","zh":"be levelled against 某人，指指控或批評被指向他們。"},{"en":"Complaints were levelled against the bus company after repeated delays.","zh":"巴士公司反覆延誤後，投訴被針對該公司提出。"},{"en":"When criticism is levelled against an organisation, it must usually respond publicly.","zh":"當批評針對一個組織，它通常必須公開回應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where blame is aimed.","zh":"這個短語描述責難指向哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"investigating police","meaning":"負責調查的警方","examples":[{"en":"The investigating police were accused of mishandling evidence.","zh":"負責調查的警方被指處理證據不當。"},{"en":"Investigating police are the officers responsible for examining a case.","zh":"investigating police 是負責查驗案件的警員。"},{"en":"The investigating police may interview witnesses, collect records, and visit the scene.","zh":"負責調查的警方可能訪問證人、收集紀錄和到訪現場。"},{"en":"If investigating police mishandle evidence, the whole case may weaken.","zh":"如果負責調查的警方處理證據不當，整宗案件可能變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the police team working on the enquiry.","zh":"這個短語指出正在處理調查的警方團隊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"deliberate tampering with evidence","meaning":"蓄意干預證據","examples":[{"en":"The police were criticised for deliberate tampering with evidence.","zh":"警方因蓄意干預證據而受到批評。"},{"en":"Deliberate tampering with evidence means intentionally changing, removing, or damaging evidence.","zh":"deliberate tampering with evidence 指有意改變、移除或損壞證據。"},{"en":"A student hiding a classmate’s answer sheet is deliberate tampering with evidence.","zh":"學生藏起同學的答題紙，就是蓄意干預證據。"},{"en":"Tampering with evidence can prevent the truth from being discovered.","zh":"干預證據可以阻止真相被發現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a serious act because it interferes with justice.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重行為，因為它妨礙公義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"semi-illiterate message","meaning":"半文盲式留言","examples":[{"en":"A semi-illiterate message was found near one of the victims.","zh":"一則半文盲式留言在其中一名受害者附近被發現。"},{"en":"A semi-illiterate message is writing that shows poor spelling, grammar, or basic literacy.","zh":"semi-illiterate message 是顯示拼寫、文法或基本讀寫能力差的文字。"},{"en":"A note full of broken words and unclear grammar may look semi-illiterate.","zh":"一張充滿破碎字詞和不清楚文法的字條可能看起來像半文盲式留言。"},{"en":"Such a message can still be important evidence even if it is badly written.","zh":"即使寫得差，這類留言仍可以是重要證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the quality of the writing, not necessarily the writer’s full intelligence.","zh":"這個短語描述文字質素，而不一定代表作者的整體智力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be scrawled above","meaning":"被潦草地寫在……上方","examples":[{"en":"A message was scrawled above one of the Ripper’s victims.","zh":"一則留言被潦草地寫在開膛手傑克其中一名受害者上方。"},{"en":"To be scrawled above something means to be written carelessly or roughly in a place higher than it.","zh":"be scrawled above 某物，指被粗心或粗略地寫在比它高的位置。"},{"en":"A warning may be scrawled above a broken lift in a housing block.","zh":"一則警告可能被潦草地寫在屋苑壞升降機上方。"},{"en":"Scrawled writing can be hard to read but still carry meaning.","zh":"潦草文字可能難以閱讀，但仍有意思。"},{"en":"The phrase describes messy writing positioned above something.","zh":"這個短語描述位於某物上方的潦草書寫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"properly analysed","meaning":"得到妥善分析","examples":[{"en":"The message was removed before it could be properly analysed.","zh":"這則留言在能得到妥善分析前被移除。"},{"en":"Properly analysed means examined carefully, correctly, and with suitable methods.","zh":"properly analysed 指被仔細、正確並以合適方法檢查。"},{"en":"A student’s writing should be properly analysed before the teacher gives advice.","zh":"老師給建議前，學生文章應得到妥善分析。"},{"en":"Evidence that is not properly analysed may lead to wrong conclusions.","zh":"沒有得到妥善分析的證據，可能導致錯誤結論。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses careful and professional examination.","zh":"這個短語強調仔細而專業的檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"investigating officer","meaning":"負責調查的警員","examples":[{"en":"The investigating officer ordered that the message be removed.","zh":"負責調查的警員下令移除該留言。"},{"en":"An investigating officer is a police officer responsible for examining a case or part of a case.","zh":"investigating officer 是負責查驗案件或案件部分的警員。"},{"en":"The investigating officer may decide which witnesses to interview first.","zh":"負責調查的警員可能決定先訪問哪些證人。"},{"en":"A poor decision by the investigating officer can affect the whole enquiry.","zh":"負責調查的警員作出差劣決定，可以影響整個調查。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the officer taking investigative responsibility.","zh":"這個短語指出承擔調查責任的警員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"order that something be removed","meaning":"下令移除某物","examples":[{"en":"The officer ordered that the written message be removed.","zh":"該警員下令移除那則書面留言。"},{"en":"To order that something be removed means to formally tell others to take it away.","zh":"order that something be removed 指正式命令他人把某物拿走。"},{"en":"A principal may order that a dangerous broken chair be removed from a classroom.","zh":"校長可能下令移除課室中危險的破椅子。"},{"en":"Removing something can protect people, but it can also destroy evidence if done too soon.","zh":"移除某物可以保護人，但如果太早進行，也可能破壞證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an official instruction to take something away.","zh":"這個短語描述要求拿走某物的正式指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"implicate the Jews","meaning":"將猶太人牽涉其中","examples":[{"en":"The message was thought to implicate the Jews.","zh":"該留言被認為將猶太人牽涉其中。"},{"en":"To implicate the Jews means to suggest, rightly or wrongly, that Jewish people were connected with wrongdoing.","zh":"implicate the Jews 指不論對錯地暗示猶太人與不當行為有關。"},{"en":"A careless accusation can unfairly implicate a whole group instead of one responsible person.","zh":"粗心指控可以不公平地牽涉整個群體，而不是一名責任人。"},{"en":"Such wording can create prejudice and social tension if it is not handled carefully.","zh":"如果處理不慎，這種字眼可以造成偏見和社會緊張。"},{"en":"The phrase must be treated critically because it involves blaming a group.","zh":"這個短語必須批判地處理，因為它涉及責怪一個群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"racial repercussions","meaning":"種族後果；種族衝突風險","examples":[{"en":"The police feared racial repercussions if the message remained.","zh":"警方擔心如果留言保留，會有種族後果。"},{"en":"Racial repercussions are harmful social consequences connected with race or ethnic identity.","zh":"racial repercussions 是與種族或族裔身份有關的有害社會後果。"},{"en":"A false rumour about one ethnic group can create racial repercussions in a neighbourhood.","zh":"關於某族群的虛假謠言可以在社區造成種族衝突風險。"},{"en":"Officials may act carefully when words could lead to discrimination or violence.","zh":"當文字可能導致歧視或暴力，官員可能會小心行事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the wider racial harm that may follow an event.","zh":"這個短語描述事件之後可能出現的更廣泛種族傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be feared","meaning":"令人擔憂；被擔心","examples":[{"en":"Racial repercussions were feared by the investigating officer.","zh":"種族後果令負責調查的警員擔憂。"},{"en":"To be feared means to be considered a possible danger or bad result.","zh":"be feared 指被視為可能的危險或壞結果。"},{"en":"Delays are feared when heavy rain begins before school dismissal.","zh":"當大雨在放學前開始，人們會擔心延誤。"},{"en":"A risk may be feared even before it actually happens.","zh":"風險即使尚未真正發生，也可能令人擔心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes concern about a possible negative outcome.","zh":"這個短語描述對可能負面結果的憂慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"well-intentioned","meaning":"出於善意的","examples":[{"en":"The motive was well-intentioned, but the action may have damaged the investigation.","zh":"動機是出於善意的，但行動可能損害了調查。"},{"en":"Well-intentioned means meant to help or do good, even if the result is poor.","zh":"well-intentioned 指本意是幫助或做好事，即使結果不好。"},{"en":"A well-intentioned friend may give advice that accidentally hurts someone’s feelings.","zh":"出於善意的朋友可能給出意外傷害別人感受的建議。"},{"en":"Good intentions do not always lead to good outcomes.","zh":"好意不一定帶來好結果。"},{"en":"The phrase separates motive from result.","zh":"這個短語把動機與結果分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"destroy vital clues","meaning":"破壞重要線索","examples":[{"en":"The removal of the message may have destroyed vital clues.","zh":"移除該留言可能破壞了重要線索。"},{"en":"To destroy vital clues means to damage or remove important evidence.","zh":"destroy vital clues 指損壞或移除重要證據。"},{"en":"Cleaning a broken window too soon can destroy vital clues after a burglary.","zh":"入屋爆竊後太早清潔破窗，可以破壞重要線索。"},{"en":"Once vital clues are destroyed, investigators may never recover them.","zh":"一旦重要線索被破壞，調查員可能永遠無法恢復它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes losing evidence that could help solve a case.","zh":"這個短語描述失去本可幫助破案的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a final problem","meaning":"最後一個問題","examples":[{"en":"A final problem was the lack of co-operation between different groups.","zh":"最後一個問題是不同群體之間缺乏合作。"},{"en":"A final problem is the last major issue mentioned in an explanation.","zh":"final problem 是解釋中提到的最後一個主要問題。"},{"en":"A final problem in a school project may be that no one checked the sources.","zh":"學校項目的最後一個問題，可能是沒有人檢查資料來源。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to introduce the last part of a list of difficulties.","zh":"作者使用這個短語來引出困難清單的最後一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that one more important obstacle remains.","zh":"這個短語表示仍有一個重要障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lack of co-operation","meaning":"缺乏合作","examples":[{"en":"The investigation suffered from a lack of co-operation.","zh":"這項調查因缺乏合作而受損。"},{"en":"Lack of co-operation means people or groups did not work together effectively.","zh":"lack of co-operation 指人或群體未能有效合作。"},{"en":"A group project may fail because of a lack of co-operation between members.","zh":"小組項目可能因成員之間缺乏合作而失敗。"},{"en":"When there is no co-operation, information is not shared and work is repeated.","zh":"當缺乏合作，資料不會共享，工作會重複。"},{"en":"The phrase describes teamwork failure.","zh":"這個短語描述團隊合作失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not just between…but also between","meaning":"不只是……也在……之間","examples":[{"en":"The problem existed not just between the Press and police but also between police forces.","zh":"問題不只是存在於傳媒與警方之間，也存在於不同警隊之間。"},{"en":"Not just between A but also between B means the issue happened in more than one relationship.","zh":"not just between A but also between B 指問題發生在多於一種關係中。"},{"en":"Miscommunication occurred not just between teachers and students but also between departments.","zh":"溝通失誤不只是發生在老師和學生之間，也發生在部門之間。"},{"en":"The phrase widens the problem from one pair of groups to another.","zh":"這個短語把問題由一對群體擴展到另一對群體。"},{"en":"It shows that the difficulty was broader than it first appeared.","zh":"它顯示困難比最初看來更廣泛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the Press","meaning":"傳媒；報界","examples":[{"en":"The police distrusted the Press during the Ripper investigation.","zh":"在開膛手傑克調查期間，警方不信任傳媒。"},{"en":"The Press means newspapers and journalists as a group.","zh":"the Press 指作為一個群體的報章和記者。"},{"en":"A school may speak to the Press after a major public event.","zh":"學校在重大公開事件後可能向傳媒發言。"},{"en":"The Press can spread information quickly, but it can also increase pressure on officials.","zh":"傳媒可以快速傳播資料，但也可以增加官員壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the news media, especially printed newspapers in historical contexts.","zh":"這個短語指新聞媒體，尤其在歷史語境中指報章。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"law enforcement agencies","meaning":"執法機構","examples":[{"en":"Law enforcement agencies failed to exchange information effectively.","zh":"執法機構未能有效交換資料。"},{"en":"Law enforcement agencies are organisations that enforce laws, such as police forces.","zh":"law enforcement agencies 是執行法律的組織，例如警隊。"},{"en":"Different law enforcement agencies may work together during cross-border crime cases.","zh":"不同執法機構可能在跨境罪案中合作。"},{"en":"If these agencies do not share information, suspects may escape.","zh":"如果這些機構不共享資料，疑犯可能逃脫。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to official bodies responsible for policing and public order.","zh":"這個短語指負責警務和公共秩序的官方機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"with regard to","meaning":"關於……","examples":[{"en":"With regard to the Press, the police released only limited information.","zh":"關於傳媒，警方只發布有限資料。"},{"en":"With regard to means concerning or in relation to a particular topic.","zh":"with regard to 指關於或就某特定主題而言。"},{"en":"With regard to homework, the teacher said quality matters more than length.","zh":"關於功課，老師說質素比長度更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase helps organise discussion by topic.","zh":"這個短語幫助按主題組織討論。"},{"en":"It is a formal way to introduce what you are talking about.","zh":"它是引出談論內容的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the former problem","meaning":"前者的問題","examples":[{"en":"The former problem involved distrust between the police and the Press.","zh":"前者的問題涉及警方與傳媒之間的不信任。"},{"en":"The former problem means the first of two problems just mentioned.","zh":"former problem 指剛提到的兩個問題中的第一個。"},{"en":"If a teacher mentions lateness and homework, the former problem refers to lateness.","zh":"如果老師提到遲到和功課，前者的問題就是遲到。"},{"en":"The phrase helps readers track two items in order.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者按順序追蹤兩項內容。"},{"en":"It is useful in formal comparison or explanation.","zh":"它適合用於正式比較或解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"police distrust of","meaning":"警方對……的不信任","examples":[{"en":"Police distrust of the Press limited the release of information.","zh":"警方對傳媒的不信任限制了資料發布。"},{"en":"Police distrust of someone means the police did not trust that person or group.","zh":"police distrust of 某人，指警方不信任該人或群體。"},{"en":"Police distrust of a witness may grow if the witness keeps changing the story.","zh":"如果證人不斷改變說法，警方對證人的不信任可能增加。"},{"en":"Distrust can reduce communication and make cooperation harder.","zh":"不信任可以減少溝通並令合作更難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lack of confidence from the police toward another party.","zh":"這個短語描述警方對另一方缺乏信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"Distrust of the Press led to limited information being released.","zh":"對傳媒的不信任導致只有有限資料被發布。"},{"en":"To lead to something means to cause it or make it happen.","zh":"lead to 某事，指造成它或令它發生。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can lead to weaker concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致課堂專注力下降。"},{"en":"Small communication mistakes can lead to serious misunderstanding.","zh":"小小溝通錯誤可以導致嚴重誤解。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a cause with a result.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"limited information","meaning":"有限資料","examples":[{"en":"Limited information was released to the newspapers.","zh":"有限資料被發放給報章。"},{"en":"Limited information means only a small amount of detail is available or shared.","zh":"limited information 指只有少量細節可用或被分享。"},{"en":"A student cannot write a strong report with limited information from one short note.","zh":"學生不能只靠一張短筆記中的有限資料寫出有力報告。"},{"en":"Limited information can protect an investigation but also prevent useful public help.","zh":"有限資料可以保護調查，但也可能阻止有用的公眾協助。"},{"en":"The phrase describes restricted or incomplete information.","zh":"這個短語描述受限制或不完整的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be released to","meaning":"被發放給……","examples":[{"en":"Only limited information was released to the newspapers.","zh":"只有有限資料被發放給報章。"},{"en":"To be released to someone means to be officially given or made available to them.","zh":"be released to 某人，指被正式提供或開放給他們。"},{"en":"Exam results may be released to students after teachers finish checking them.","zh":"老師完成核對後，考試成績可能被發放給學生。"},{"en":"Information released too early can create confusion if it is incomplete.","zh":"如果資料不完整，太早發布可能造成混亂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes controlled sharing of information.","zh":"這個短語描述受控制的資訊分享。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"due to a fear that","meaning":"由於擔心……","examples":[{"en":"Information was withheld due to a fear that it could alert a suspect.","zh":"資料被扣起，是由於擔心它會驚動疑犯。"},{"en":"Due to a fear that means because people were worried that something bad might happen.","zh":"due to a fear that 指因為人們擔心某壞事可能發生。"},{"en":"A school trip was cancelled due to a fear that the storm would worsen.","zh":"學校旅行因擔心風暴惡化而被取消。"},{"en":"Fear can lead people to hold back information or delay action.","zh":"恐懼可以令人保留資料或延遲行動。"},{"en":"The phrase explains a decision by pointing to a specific worry.","zh":"這個短語透過指出具體憂慮來解釋決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be made public","meaning":"被公開","examples":[{"en":"The police feared that information made public could alert a suspect.","zh":"警方擔心被公開的資料可能驚動疑犯。"},{"en":"To be made public means to be shared openly with ordinary people.","zh":"be made public 指被公開分享給普通人。"},{"en":"School inspection results may be made public on the government website.","zh":"學校視學結果可能在政府網站被公開。"},{"en":"Once information is made public, it can spread quickly and cannot easily be controlled.","zh":"資料一旦被公開，可以迅速擴散，且不易控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving information from private to public knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述資料由私人或內部轉為公眾知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"alert a suspect","meaning":"驚動疑犯","examples":[{"en":"Public information might alert a suspect.","zh":"公開資料可能會驚動疑犯。"},{"en":"To alert a suspect means to warn a possible offender that police are investigating or getting close.","zh":"alert a suspect 指警告可能犯案者警方正在調查或接近真相。"},{"en":"If police reveal too much, they may alert a suspect who then destroys evidence.","zh":"如果警方透露太多，他們可能驚動疑犯，令對方破壞證據。"},{"en":"Investigators sometimes keep details secret to avoid alerting suspects.","zh":"調查員有時保密細節，以避免驚動疑犯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes accidentally warning someone under suspicion.","zh":"這個短語描述意外警示受懷疑的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"generate false leads","meaning":"產生錯誤線索","examples":[{"en":"The police feared that publicity could generate false leads.","zh":"警方擔心公開報道會產生錯誤線索。"},{"en":"To generate false leads means to create incorrect clues or reports that waste investigators’ time.","zh":"generate false leads 指產生錯誤線索或報告，浪費調查員時間。"},{"en":"A rumour on social media can generate false leads during a missing-person search.","zh":"社交媒體謠言可以在尋人期間產生錯誤線索。"},{"en":"False leads slow an investigation because officers follow paths that go nowhere.","zh":"錯誤線索會拖慢調查，因為警員追查沒有結果的方向。"},{"en":"The phrase describes misleading information being produced.","zh":"這個短語描述誤導性資料被產生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"false leads","meaning":"錯誤線索","examples":[{"en":"False leads could waste valuable investigative time.","zh":"錯誤線索可能浪費寶貴調查時間。"},{"en":"False leads are clues or reports that seem useful but turn out to be wrong.","zh":"false leads 是看似有用但結果錯誤的線索或報告。"},{"en":"A witness who mistakes one red car for another may create a false lead.","zh":"把一輛紅車誤認為另一輛的證人，可能造成錯誤線索。"},{"en":"Investigators must check false leads carefully before rejecting them.","zh":"調查員在排除錯誤線索前，仍必須仔細查核。"},{"en":"The phrase describes misleading paths in an investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述調查中的誤導方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"waste time","meaning":"浪費時間","examples":[{"en":"False leads wasted time during the investigation.","zh":"錯誤線索在調查期間浪費了時間。"},{"en":"To waste time means to use time on something unhelpful or unnecessary.","zh":"waste time 指把時間用在沒有幫助或不必要的事情上。"},{"en":"A student may waste time copying notes beautifully but never reviewing them.","zh":"學生可能花時間把筆記抄得漂亮，卻從不溫習，這就是浪費時間。"},{"en":"In an investigation, wasted time can allow a suspect to escape.","zh":"在調查中，浪費時間可以讓疑犯逃走。"},{"en":"The phrase describes time being used without useful result.","zh":"這個短語描述時間被用掉但沒有有用結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be circulated publicly","meaning":"被公開傳播","examples":[{"en":"If information had been circulated publicly, witnesses might have come forward.","zh":"如果資料被公開傳播，證人可能會出面。"},{"en":"To be circulated publicly means to be spread openly among the public.","zh":"be circulated publicly 指在公眾之間公開傳播。"},{"en":"A missing-pet notice may be circulated publicly through posters and social media.","zh":"失蹤寵物通告可能透過海報和社交媒體被公開傳播。"},{"en":"Public circulation can reach people who may hold useful information.","zh":"公開傳播可以接觸到可能掌握有用資料的人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes open distribution of information.","zh":"這個短語描述資訊的公開分發。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"important information might have been uncovered","meaning":"重要資料本可能被揭露","examples":[{"en":"Important information might have been uncovered if more details had been released.","zh":"如果更多細節被發布，重要資料本可能被揭露。"},{"en":"Important information might have been uncovered means useful facts could have been discovered.","zh":"important information might have been uncovered 指有用事實本可能被發現。"},{"en":"If the school had asked students earlier, important information about bullying might have been uncovered.","zh":"如果學校早點詢問學生，關於欺凌的重要資料本可能被揭露。"},{"en":"Releasing the right details can help witnesses remember what they saw.","zh":"發布正確細節可以幫助證人記起所見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a lost possibility of discovering key facts.","zh":"這個短語描述發現關鍵事實的機會已失去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lead to the arrest of","meaning":"導致……被拘捕","examples":[{"en":"New information might have led to the arrest of the Ripper.","zh":"新資料本可能導致開膛手傑克被拘捕。"},{"en":"To lead to the arrest of someone means to result in that person being caught and taken by police.","zh":"lead to the arrest of 某人，指導致該人被警方捉拿。"},{"en":"A clear CCTV image can lead to the arrest of a shoplifter.","zh":"清晰閉路電視影像可以導致店舖小偷被拘捕。"},{"en":"Evidence must be strong enough before it leads to an arrest.","zh":"證據必須足夠有力，才會導致拘捕。"},{"en":"The phrase connects information or evidence with police action.","zh":"這個短語把資料或證據與警方行動連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as regards","meaning":"至於","examples":[{"en":"As regards the police forces, rivalry hindered the investigation.","zh":"至於各警隊，競爭妨礙了調查。"},{"en":"As regards means concerning or when speaking about a particular topic.","zh":"as regards 指關於或談到某特定主題時。"},{"en":"As regards homework, the teacher said late work would lose marks.","zh":"至於功課，老師說遲交會扣分。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and helps move to a new part of the discussion.","zh":"這個短語較正式，幫助轉到討論的新部分。"},{"en":"It signals exactly which issue the writer is now addressing.","zh":"它清楚標示作者現在處理哪個議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"infighting and rivalry","meaning":"內鬥和競爭","examples":[{"en":"Infighting and rivalry between police forces delayed the exchange of information.","zh":"警隊之間的內鬥和競爭延誤了資料交流。"},{"en":"Infighting and rivalry mean internal conflict and competition within or between related groups.","zh":"infighting and rivalry 指相關群體內部或彼此之間的衝突和競爭。"},{"en":"A school committee may fail if infighting and rivalry stop members from sharing ideas.","zh":"如果內鬥和競爭阻止成員分享想法，學校委員會可能失敗。"},{"en":"Rivalry can waste energy that should be used to solve the main problem.","zh":"競爭可以浪費本應用來解決主要問題的精力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes damaging competition among people who should cooperate.","zh":"這個短語描述本應合作的人之間有害的競爭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"serve to","meaning":"起到……作用","examples":[{"en":"The rivalry served to delay the exchange of information.","zh":"競爭起到了延誤資料交流的作用。"},{"en":"To serve to do something means to have the effect of doing it.","zh":"serve to do something 指具有做某事的效果。"},{"en":"Clear classroom rules serve to reduce arguments between students.","zh":"清晰課室規則可以起到減少學生爭執的作用。"},{"en":"A small delay can serve to make a problem larger if timing is important.","zh":"如果時機重要，小小延誤可以起到令問題擴大的作用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the function or effect of something.","zh":"這個短語描述某事的功能或效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"delay the exchange of information","meaning":"延誤資料交流","examples":[{"en":"Rivalry between police forces delayed the exchange of information.","zh":"警隊之間的競爭延誤資料交流。"},{"en":"To delay the exchange of information means to slow down the sharing of facts between people or groups.","zh":"delay the exchange of information 指拖慢人或群體之間分享事實。"},{"en":"Poor email habits can delay the exchange of information between teachers and parents.","zh":"差劣電郵習慣可以延誤老師和家長之間的資料交流。"},{"en":"Delayed information sharing can cause repeated work and missed opportunities.","zh":"資料分享延誤可以造成重複工作和錯失機會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow communication between parties.","zh":"這個短語描述各方之間溝通緩慢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"further hinder proceedings","meaning":"進一步妨礙調查進程","examples":[{"en":"The lack of co-operation further hindered proceedings.","zh":"缺乏合作進一步妨礙了調查進程。"},{"en":"To further hinder proceedings means to make an existing process even harder or slower.","zh":"further hinder proceedings 指令已有進程更加困難或緩慢。"},{"en":"A missing laptop can further hinder proceedings during an online exam.","zh":"在網上考試期間，一部遺失的手提電腦可以進一步妨礙進程。"},{"en":"When a process is already difficult, extra obstacles can delay it more.","zh":"當過程本已困難，額外障礙會令它更加延誤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes additional obstruction to ongoing work.","zh":"這個短語描述對正在進行工作的額外阻礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"complete the diagram below","meaning":"完成下方圖表","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to complete the diagram below using words from the passage.","zh":"考生需要使用文章中的字詞完成下方圖表。"},{"en":"Complete the diagram below means fill in the missing labels or blanks in the diagram under the instructions.","zh":"complete the diagram below 指按指示填寫下方圖表中缺失的標籤或空格。"},{"en":"In a science worksheet, students may complete the diagram below by naming parts of a plant.","zh":"在科學工作紙中，學生可能透過寫出植物部位名稱完成下方圖表。"},{"en":"Reading the labels around the blanks helps students choose the correct words.","zh":"閱讀空格周圍的標籤有助學生選出正確字詞。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction for diagram-completion tasks.","zh":"這個短語是圖表填充題常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個字","examples":[{"en":"Answers should contain no more than three words from the passage.","zh":"答案應包含不多於三個來自文章的字詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must have three words or fewer.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案必須是三個字詞或以下。"},{"en":"If the answer is “crime scene photography”, it has three words and fits the limit.","zh":"如果答案是 “crime scene photography”，它有三個字，符合限制。"},{"en":"Writing four words can lose marks even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫四個字也可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase is a strict word-limit instruction in reading tests.","zh":"這個短語是閱讀測驗中的嚴格字數限制指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"from the passage","meaning":"從文章中","examples":[{"en":"The answers must be taken from the passage.","zh":"答案必須從文章中提取。"},{"en":"From the passage means the words or information must come directly from the reading text.","zh":"from the passage 指字詞或資料必須直接來自閱讀文本。"},{"en":"Students should not use their own general knowledge if the answer must come from the passage.","zh":"如果答案必須從文章中來，學生不應使用自己的常識。"},{"en":"Copying the exact phrase from the text can help avoid changing the meaning.","zh":"從文本抄出準確短語可以避免改變意思。"},{"en":"The phrase tells candidates where evidence and wording should come from.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生證據和字眼應來自哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"write answers in boxes","meaning":"在方格內寫上答案","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write their answers in boxes on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生在答題紙的方格內寫上答案。"},{"en":"Write answers in boxes means put each answer in the numbered space provided.","zh":"write answers in boxes 指把每個答案寫在指定編號空格內。"},{"en":"In public exams, students must write answers in boxes clearly so markers can read them.","zh":"在公開考試中，學生必須在方格內清楚寫上答案，以便評卷員閱讀。"},{"en":"Putting an answer in the wrong box can cause marks to be lost.","zh":"把答案寫錯方格可能導致失分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the required place for writing exam answers.","zh":"這個短語描述考試答案應寫的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be left unexamined","meaning":"未被檢驗","examples":[{"en":"Evidence may be left unexamined when no suitable technology is available.","zh":"當沒有合適科技可用，證據可能未被檢驗。"},{"en":"To be left unexamined means not to be checked, studied, or analysed.","zh":"be left unexamined 指沒有被檢查、研究或分析。"},{"en":"A teacher may leave a suspicious answer unexamined if there is no time to compare scripts.","zh":"如果沒有時間比較試卷，老師可能讓可疑答案未被檢驗。"},{"en":"Unexamined evidence can hide useful facts.","zh":"未被檢驗的證據可能隱藏有用事實。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence that remains unused or unchecked.","zh":"這個短語描述仍未被使用或查核的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be available to analyse","meaning":"可用於分析……","examples":[{"en":"Modern technology was not available to analyse the evidence.","zh":"現代科技當時不可用於分析證據。"},{"en":"To be available to analyse something means to exist and be usable for examining it.","zh":"be available to analyse 某物，指存在並可用來檢查它。"},{"en":"A microscope may not be available to analyse a sample in a small school laboratory.","zh":"在小型學校實驗室中，顯微鏡可能不可用於分析樣本。"},{"en":"If the right tool is unavailable, even good evidence may remain unclear.","zh":"如果正確工具不可用，即使好證據也可能仍不清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase connects technology or methods with their practical use.","zh":"這個短語把科技或方法與其實際用途連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"fingerprints are not used","meaning":"指紋未被使用","examples":[{"en":"Fingerprints were not used in the Ripper investigation.","zh":"指紋未在開膛手傑克調查中被使用。"},{"en":"Fingerprints are not used means investigators do not apply fingerprint evidence in a case.","zh":"fingerprints are not used 指調查員沒有在案件中使用指紋證據。"},{"en":"Fingerprints are not used if a surface is too wet, dirty, or touched by many people.","zh":"如果表面太濕、太髒或被許多人觸碰，指紋可能不被使用。"},{"en":"When fingerprints are not used, police may lose one possible way to identify a suspect.","zh":"當指紋未被使用，警方可能失去一種識別疑犯的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the absence of a common evidence method.","zh":"這個短語描述一種常見證據方法缺席。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"one of the Ripper’s victims","meaning":"開膛手傑克的其中一名受害者","examples":[{"en":"Only one of the Ripper’s victims was photographed at the crime scene.","zh":"只有開膛手傑克的其中一名受害者在犯罪現場被拍攝。"},{"en":"One of the Ripper’s victims means one person among those killed in the Ripper case.","zh":"one of the Ripper’s victims 指開膛手傑克案件中被殺害者之一。"},{"en":"In a history question, students may need to identify one of the Ripper’s victims from the passage.","zh":"在歷史題中，學生可能需要從文章中辨認開膛手傑克的其中一名受害者。"},{"en":"Mentioning one victim can show how unevenly evidence was recorded.","zh":"提及一名受害者可以顯示證據記錄如何不平均。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a single individual within a group of victims.","zh":"這個短語指受害者群體中的一個個體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"at the crime scene","meaning":"在犯罪現場","examples":[{"en":"One victim was photographed at the crime scene.","zh":"一名受害者在犯罪現場被拍攝。"},{"en":"At the crime scene means at the place where the crime happened or evidence was found.","zh":"at the crime scene 指在罪案發生或發現證據的地方。"},{"en":"Police collect objects at the crime scene before allowing cleaners to enter.","zh":"警方在允許清潔工進入前，會在犯罪現場收集物件。"},{"en":"Evidence found at the crime scene can connect events, suspects, and victims.","zh":"在犯罪現場找到的證據可以連接事件、疑犯和受害者。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the exact investigative location.","zh":"這個短語給出準確的調查地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"images taken","meaning":"所拍攝的影像","examples":[{"en":"The images taken focused mainly on the victim’s eyes.","zh":"所拍攝的影像主要集中於受害者的眼睛。"},{"en":"Images taken are photographs or visual records that have been captured.","zh":"images taken 是已被拍攝的照片或視覺紀錄。"},{"en":"The images taken during a school event may be used in the newsletter.","zh":"學校活動中所拍攝的影像可能用於通訊。"},{"en":"Images taken at the wrong angle may miss important details.","zh":"從錯誤角度拍攝的影像可能錯過重要細節。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the photographs already produced.","zh":"這個短語指已經產生的照片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"capture the victim’s eyes","meaning":"拍攝受害者的眼睛","examples":[{"en":"The photographs were mainly intended to capture the victim’s eyes.","zh":"這些照片主要旨在拍攝受害者的眼睛。"},{"en":"To capture the victim’s eyes means to photograph or visually record the eyes of the victim.","zh":"capture the victim’s eyes 指拍照或視覺記錄受害者的眼睛。"},{"en":"A photographer may capture a speaker’s eyes to show emotion during a speech.","zh":"攝影師可能拍攝演講者的眼睛，以顯示演講時的情緒。"},{"en":"In this case, focusing on the eyes meant other evidence may have been ignored.","zh":"在這宗案件中，集中拍攝眼睛意味其他證據可能被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the intended subject of the photographs.","zh":"這個短語描述照片原本想拍攝的主體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"vital written evidence","meaning":"重要書面證據","examples":[{"en":"Vital written evidence was removed before analysis.","zh":"重要書面證據在分析前被移除。"},{"en":"Vital written evidence is important written material that may help explain a case.","zh":"vital written evidence 是可能幫助解釋案件的重要文字材料。"},{"en":"A threatening note can be vital written evidence in a school bullying investigation.","zh":"威脅字條可以是學校欺凌調查中的重要書面證據。"},{"en":"If written evidence is removed too early, handwriting, wording, and location may be lost.","zh":"如果書面證據太早被移除，筆跡、措辭和位置可能會失去。"},{"en":"The phrase describes important evidence in written form.","zh":"這個短語描述以文字形式出現的重要證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"on the orders of","meaning":"按照……的命令","examples":[{"en":"The evidence was removed on the orders of a police investigator.","zh":"證據按照一名警方調查員的命令被移除。"},{"en":"On the orders of someone means because that person officially instructed it.","zh":"on the orders of 某人，指因為該人正式下令。"},{"en":"The playground was closed on the orders of the principal after a safety inspection.","zh":"安全檢查後，操場按照校長命令被關閉。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who gave the instruction.","zh":"這個短語指出誰給出指示。"},{"en":"It is often used when an action follows authority.","zh":"它常用於行動跟隨權威命令時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"police investigator","meaning":"警方調查員","examples":[{"en":"A police investigator ordered the removal of the message.","zh":"一名警方調查員下令移除該留言。"},{"en":"A police investigator is an officer who examines evidence and facts in a case.","zh":"police investigator 是查驗案件中證據和事實的警員。"},{"en":"A police investigator may interview witnesses and compare statements.","zh":"警方調查員可能訪問證人並比較供詞。"},{"en":"The quality of an investigator’s decisions can affect whether a case is solved.","zh":"調查員決定的質素可以影響案件能否偵破。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a police officer doing investigative work.","zh":"這個短語指從事調查工作的警員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"rival law enforcement agencies","meaning":"互相競爭的執法機構","examples":[{"en":"Rival law enforcement agencies failed to exchange information.","zh":"互相競爭的執法機構未能交換資料。"},{"en":"Rival law enforcement agencies are policing bodies that compete instead of cooperating fully.","zh":"rival law enforcement agencies 是互相競爭而非充分合作的警務機構。"},{"en":"Two departments may act like rival agencies if each wants credit for solving a case.","zh":"如果兩個部門都想爭取破案功勞，它們可能像互相競爭的機構。"},{"en":"Rivalry between agencies can slow communication and weaken investigations.","zh":"機構之間競爭可以拖慢溝通並削弱調查。"},{"en":"The phrase describes official bodies whose competition damages cooperation.","zh":"這個短語描述因競爭而損害合作的官方機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"fail to exchange information","meaning":"未能交換資料","examples":[{"en":"The rival agencies failed to exchange information efficiently.","zh":"互相競爭的機構未能有效交換資料。"},{"en":"To fail to exchange information means not to share facts or records properly.","zh":"fail to exchange information 指未能妥善分享事實或紀錄。"},{"en":"Teachers may fail to exchange information if a student’s learning needs are not passed to the next class teacher.","zh":"如果學生的學習需要沒有交給下一位班主任，老師可能未能交換資料。"},{"en":"Poor information exchange can create repeated mistakes and missed clues.","zh":"資料交流差可以造成重複錯誤和錯失線索。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a communication failure between groups.","zh":"這個短語描述群體之間的溝通失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"complete the notes below","meaning":"完成以下筆記","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to complete the notes below with words from the passage.","zh":"考生需要使用文章中的字詞完成以下筆記。"},{"en":"Complete the notes below means fill in missing words in the notes under the question.","zh":"complete the notes below 指填寫題目下方筆記中的缺字。"},{"en":"In a reading exercise, students complete the notes below by locating exact words in the text.","zh":"在閱讀練習中，學生透過在文本中定位準確字詞來完成以下筆記。"},{"en":"Good note completion requires checking grammar before and after each blank.","zh":"做好筆記填充需要檢查每個空格前後的文法。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction in IELTS-style reading tasks.","zh":"這個短語是 IELTS 式閱讀題常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"what is so startling about","meaning":"令人如此震驚的是","examples":[{"en":"What is so startling about the case is that the killer escaped capture.","zh":"這宗案件令人如此震驚的是兇手逃避了拘捕。"},{"en":"What is so startling about something means the part that is especially surprising or shocking.","zh":"what is so startling about 某事，指其中尤其令人驚訝或震驚的部分。"},{"en":"What is so startling about the exam result is that the weakest class improved the most.","zh":"考試結果令人如此震驚的是最弱班級進步最大。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the most unexpected feature of a situation.","zh":"這個短語突出情況中最出乎意料的特徵。"},{"en":"It prepares readers for the writer’s main surprise.","zh":"它為讀者準備好理解作者的主要驚訝點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"manage to","meaning":"成功做到","examples":[{"en":"The murderer managed to evade capture against the odds.","zh":"兇手在困難重重下成功逃避拘捕。"},{"en":"To manage to do something means to succeed in doing it, often despite difficulty.","zh":"manage to do something 指成功做到某事，通常是在困難之下。"},{"en":"A student managed to pass the exam after months of extra practice.","zh":"學生經過數月額外練習後，成功通過考試。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests effort, difficulty, or surprise.","zh":"這個短語常暗示努力、困難或驚訝。"},{"en":"It describes success in achieving an action.","zh":"它描述成功達成一項行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"against the odds","meaning":"在困難重重下","examples":[{"en":"The Ripper escaped capture against the odds.","zh":"開膛手傑克在困難重重下逃避拘捕。"},{"en":"Against the odds means despite a situation in which success seems unlikely.","zh":"against the odds 指儘管成功看似不大可能。"},{"en":"A small school team won the final against the odds after losing two key players.","zh":"一支小校隊失去兩名主力後仍在困難重重下贏得決賽。"},{"en":"People use the phrase when the result is surprising because many factors were against it.","zh":"當結果因多項不利因素而令人驚訝，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It describes success under difficult conditions.","zh":"它描述困難條件下的成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"on closer investigation","meaning":"經更仔細調查後","examples":[{"en":"On closer investigation, the reasons for failure become clearer.","zh":"經更仔細調查後，失敗原因變得更清楚。"},{"en":"On closer investigation means after examining something more carefully.","zh":"on closer investigation 指在更仔細檢查某事之後。"},{"en":"On closer investigation, the teacher found that the copied answers came from an old worksheet.","zh":"經更仔細調查後，老師發現抄襲答案來自舊工作紙。"},{"en":"Careful investigation can reveal causes that are not obvious at first.","zh":"仔細調查可以揭示起初不明顯的原因。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a deeper look at a situation.","zh":"這個短語引出對情況的更深入檢視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"become more apparent","meaning":"變得更明顯","examples":[{"en":"The reasons for the failure become more apparent later.","zh":"失敗原因後來變得更明顯。"},{"en":"To become more apparent means to become clearer or easier to see.","zh":"become more apparent 指變得更清楚或更容易看見。"},{"en":"A student’s progress may become more apparent after comparing essays from two months apart.","zh":"比較相隔兩個月的文章後，學生進步可能變得更明顯。"},{"en":"Evidence makes a hidden problem become more apparent.","zh":"證據會令隱藏問題變得更明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something gradually becoming obvious.","zh":"這個短語描述某事逐漸變得明顯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be disturbed","meaning":"被擾亂","examples":[{"en":"A murder scene was often disturbed before evidence could be preserved.","zh":"謀殺案現場常在證據能被保存前被擾亂。"},{"en":"To be disturbed means to be moved, changed, or interfered with.","zh":"be disturbed 指被移動、改變或干擾。"},{"en":"A desk should not be disturbed if teachers are checking who used it last.","zh":"如果老師正在查誰最後使用書桌，書桌不應被擾亂。"},{"en":"If a crime scene is disturbed, evidence may no longer show what originally happened.","zh":"如果犯罪現場被擾亂，證據可能不再顯示原本發生的事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes disruption of an original condition.","zh":"這個短語描述原始狀態被打亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"scientific investigative methods","meaning":"科學調查方法","examples":[{"en":"Scientific investigative methods were introduced too late for the Ripper case.","zh":"科學調查方法對開膛手傑克案件而言引入得太遲。"},{"en":"Scientific investigative methods are evidence-based techniques used to examine cases more accurately.","zh":"scientific investigative methods 是用證據為基礎、更準確檢查案件的技術。"},{"en":"Laboratory testing and fingerprint comparison are scientific investigative methods.","zh":"實驗室測試和指紋比較都是科學調查方法。"},{"en":"Such methods reduce guesswork by relying on measurable evidence.","zh":"這類方法透過依靠可量度證據來減少猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase describes scientific tools used in investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述調查中使用的科學工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be introduced","meaning":"被引入","examples":[{"en":"More scientific methods were introduced after the publication of Hans Gross’s book.","zh":"更多科學方法在 Hans Gross 的書出版後被引入。"},{"en":"To be introduced means to be brought into use for the first time.","zh":"be introduced 指首次被帶入使用。"},{"en":"A new homework system may be introduced at the start of the school year.","zh":"新功課系統可能在學年開始時被引入。"},{"en":"When a method is introduced, people need time to learn how to use it.","zh":"當方法被引入，人們需要時間學會如何使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a new practice entering a system.","zh":"這個短語描述新做法進入一個系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"greatly aid the police in","meaning":"大大協助警方……","examples":[{"en":"Fingerprinting greatly aided the police in identifying criminals.","zh":"指紋鑑定大大協助警方識別罪犯。"},{"en":"To greatly aid the police in something means to help police a lot with that task.","zh":"greatly aid the police in 某事，指在該任務上大大幫助警方。"},{"en":"Clear CCTV footage can greatly aid the police in finding a missing child.","zh":"清晰閉路電視片段可以大大協助警方尋找失蹤兒童。"},{"en":"Good evidence aids police by narrowing the search and reducing uncertainty.","zh":"好證據透過收窄搜索範圍和減少不確定性來協助警方。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong practical assistance to police work.","zh":"這個短語描述對警務工作的強大實際幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"identifying criminals","meaning":"識別罪犯","examples":[{"en":"Dactyloscopy helped the police in identifying criminals.","zh":"指紋鑑定法幫助警方識別罪犯。"},{"en":"Identifying criminals means discovering which people committed crimes.","zh":"identifying criminals 指找出哪些人犯下罪行。"},{"en":"Shop cameras can help in identifying criminals who steal from shelves.","zh":"店舖攝影機可以幫助識別從貨架偷東西的罪犯。"},{"en":"Accurate identification helps protect innocent people from false accusation.","zh":"準確識別有助保護無辜者免受錯誤指控。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the process of finding offenders.","zh":"這個短語描述找出犯案者的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"curiously","meaning":"奇怪的是","examples":[{"en":"Curiously, known investigative methods were not always employed.","zh":"奇怪的是，已知調查方法並不總是被採用。"},{"en":"Curiously means strangely or in a way that invites question.","zh":"curiously 指奇怪地，或以令人疑問的方式。"},{"en":"Curiously, the student who never revised scored the highest mark.","zh":"奇怪的是，從不溫習的學生取得最高分。"},{"en":"Writers use this word when a fact seems surprising or difficult to explain.","zh":"當事實令人驚訝或難以解釋，作者會使用這個詞。"},{"en":"It signals that the next detail deserves attention.","zh":"它表示下一個細節值得注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be known to police","meaning":"為警方所知","examples":[{"en":"Some investigative methods were known to police at the time.","zh":"有些調查方法在當時已為警方所知。"},{"en":"To be known to police means police were already aware of it.","zh":"be known to police 指警方已經知道它。"},{"en":"A suspect may be known to police if he has been involved in earlier cases.","zh":"如果疑犯曾涉及早前案件，他可能已為警方所知。"},{"en":"If a method is known to police but not used, the failure may seem less excusable.","zh":"如果方法為警方所知卻沒有使用，失敗可能較難辯解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes police awareness of a person, method, or fact.","zh":"這個短語描述警方對人物、方法或事實的認識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be employed","meaning":"被採用","examples":[{"en":"Crime-scene photography was known but rarely employed.","zh":"犯罪現場攝影已為人所知，但很少被採用。"},{"en":"To be employed means to be used for a particular purpose.","zh":"be employed 指為特定目的被使用。"},{"en":"Group discussion may be employed to help students practise speaking.","zh":"小組討論可能被採用來幫助學生練習說話。"},{"en":"A method can be known but still not employed in real situations.","zh":"一種方法可以為人所知，但在真實情況中仍未被採用。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to say “used”.","zh":"這個短語是 “used” 的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"crime-scene photography","meaning":"犯罪現場攝影","examples":[{"en":"Crime-scene photography was not properly used in the Ripper investigation.","zh":"犯罪現場攝影在開膛手傑克調查中沒有被妥善使用。"},{"en":"Crime-scene photography is the photographing of a crime location to preserve visual evidence.","zh":"crime-scene photography 是拍攝犯罪地點，以保存視覺證據。"},{"en":"Police use crime-scene photography before objects are moved or cleaned.","zh":"警方在物件被移動或清潔前使用犯罪現場攝影。"},{"en":"Good photographs help investigators review details after the scene changes.","zh":"好照片幫助調查員在現場改變後回看細節。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visual recording of evidence at the scene.","zh":"這個短語描述在現場對證據作視覺記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"which two statements are supported by","meaning":"哪兩項陳述得到……支持","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose which two statements are supported by the passage.","zh":"考生選擇哪兩項陳述得到文章支持。"},{"en":"Which two statements are supported by means students must find two options backed by evidence.","zh":"which two statements are supported by 指學生必須找出兩個有證據支持的選項。"},{"en":"In a reading test, a statement is supported only if the text clearly says or proves it.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，只有文本清楚說明或證明，陳述才算得到支持。"},{"en":"Students should not choose an answer just because it sounds reasonable.","zh":"學生不應只因答案聽起來合理就選它。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for evidence-based selection.","zh":"這個短語要求基於證據作選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be supported by the passage","meaning":"得到文章支持","examples":[{"en":"A correct statement must be supported by the passage.","zh":"正確陳述必須得到文章支持。"},{"en":"To be supported by the passage means the reading text provides evidence for the statement.","zh":"be supported by the passage 指閱讀文本為該陳述提供證據。"},{"en":"An answer is not supported by the passage if it relies only on common knowledge.","zh":"如果答案只依賴常識，就不是得到文章支持。"},{"en":"Students should underline the lines that support their answer.","zh":"學生應劃出支持答案的行句。"},{"en":"The phrase links exam answers to textual proof.","zh":"這個短語把考試答案與文本證據連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"limited forensic knowledge","meaning":"有限的法證知識","examples":[{"en":"Limited forensic knowledge affected the Ripper investigation.","zh":"有限的法證知識影響了開膛手傑克調查。"},{"en":"Limited forensic knowledge means only a small or incomplete understanding of scientific evidence methods.","zh":"limited forensic knowledge 指對科學證據方法只有少量或不完整的理解。"},{"en":"Limited forensic knowledge may cause police to collect fingerprints wrongly.","zh":"有限的法證知識可能令警方錯誤收集指紋。"},{"en":"When knowledge is limited, investigators may depend too much on guesses and witnesses.","zh":"當知識有限，調查員可能過度依賴猜測和證人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shortage of scientific investigative understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述科學調查理解不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"affect the outcome of","meaning":"影響……的結果","examples":[{"en":"A lack of forensic knowledge may have affected the outcome of the case.","zh":"缺乏法證知識可能影響了案件結果。"},{"en":"To affect the outcome of something means to change or influence the final result.","zh":"affect the outcome of 某事，指改變或影響最終結果。"},{"en":"One careless mistake can affect the outcome of an exam if it appears in every answer.","zh":"如果一個粗心錯誤出現在每個答案中，它可以影響考試結果。"},{"en":"Evidence quality can affect the outcome of a trial.","zh":"證據質素可以影響審訊結果。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a factor with the final result.","zh":"這個短語把某因素與最終結果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"convince someone of a need for","meaning":"使某人相信有……的需要","examples":[{"en":"The murders may have convinced people of a need for better methods.","zh":"這些謀殺案可能使人們相信有更好方法的需要。"},{"en":"To convince someone of a need for something means to make them believe that thing is necessary.","zh":"convince someone of a need for 某事，指令某人相信該事物是必要的。"},{"en":"Repeated accidents can convince a school of a need for better safety rules.","zh":"反覆意外可以使學校相信有更好安全規則的需要。"},{"en":"Public failure often convinces organisations that old methods are not enough.","zh":"公開失敗常使組織相信舊方法不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes persuasion created by evidence or experience.","zh":"這個短語描述由證據或經驗造成的說服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"sophisticated investigative methods","meaning":"先進調查方法","examples":[{"en":"Modern police work relies on sophisticated investigative methods.","zh":"現代警務依賴先進調查方法。"},{"en":"Sophisticated investigative methods are advanced, complex, and careful ways of examining cases.","zh":"sophisticated investigative methods 是先進、複雜且仔細的案件檢查方法。"},{"en":"Digital tracking and DNA analysis are sophisticated investigative methods.","zh":"數碼追蹤和 DNA 分析都是先進調查方法。"},{"en":"Such methods can reveal connections that ordinary observation misses.","zh":"這類方法可以揭示普通觀察錯過的聯繫。"},{"en":"The phrase describes advanced tools and procedures for investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述用於調查的先進工具和程序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"disagreement existed amongst","meaning":"在……之間存在分歧","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether disagreement existed amongst the police.","zh":"該陳述問警方之間是否存在分歧。"},{"en":"Disagreement existed amongst a group means members of that group did not share the same view.","zh":"disagreement existed amongst 某群體，指該群體成員意見不一致。"},{"en":"Disagreement existed amongst teachers about whether homework should be reduced.","zh":"老師之間對是否應減少功課存在分歧。"},{"en":"Internal disagreement can slow decisions if no one has clear authority.","zh":"如果沒有清晰權威，內部分歧可以拖慢決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes division inside a group.","zh":"這個短語描述群體內部分裂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"information should be released to","meaning":"資料應發放給……","examples":[{"en":"The police had concerns about what information should be released to the Press.","zh":"警方擔心哪些資料應發放給傳媒。"},{"en":"Information should be released to someone means certain details ought to be officially shared with them.","zh":"information should be released to 某人，指某些細節應正式分享給他們。"},{"en":"A school must decide what information should be released to parents after an accident.","zh":"學校在意外後必須決定哪些資料應發放給家長。"},{"en":"Sharing too little can reduce trust, but sharing too much can create risk.","zh":"分享太少會降低信任，但分享太多可以造成風險。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on judging what information should be given.","zh":"這個短語重點在判斷應給出甚麼資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be united in","meaning":"在……方面一致","examples":[{"en":"The statement suggests that the police were united in their dislike of the Press.","zh":"該陳述暗示警方在厭惡傳媒方面一致。"},{"en":"To be united in something means to share the same feeling, aim, or opinion.","zh":"be united in 某事，指共享同一感受、目標或意見。"},{"en":"Students may be united in wanting cleaner classrooms.","zh":"學生可能在希望課室更乾淨方面一致。"},{"en":"A group united in one view can act more quickly, but may ignore other perspectives.","zh":"在某觀點上一致的群體可以更快行動，但也可能忽視其他角度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes agreement within a group.","zh":"這個短語描述群體內部一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"dislike of the Press","meaning":"對傳媒的厭惡","examples":[{"en":"The police showed distrust of the Press during the investigation.","zh":"警方在調查期間表現出對傳媒的不信任。"},{"en":"Dislike of the Press means negative feeling toward newspapers and journalists.","zh":"dislike of the Press 指對報章和記者的負面感受。"},{"en":"A politician’s dislike of the Press may grow after repeated critical articles.","zh":"政客在反覆受到批評文章攻擊後，對傳媒的厭惡可能增加。"},{"en":"Dislike can reduce cooperation even when sharing information would help.","zh":"即使分享資料有幫助，厭惡也可以減少合作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a hostile attitude toward news media.","zh":"這個短語描述對新聞媒體的敵意態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"make good use of","meaning":"充分利用","examples":[{"en":"The police did not always make good use of available techniques.","zh":"警方並不總是充分利用可用技術。"},{"en":"To make good use of something means to use it effectively and sensibly.","zh":"make good use of 某物，指有效而明智地使用它。"},{"en":"Students make good use of feedback when they revise their essays carefully.","zh":"學生仔細修改文章時，就是充分利用回饋。"},{"en":"Having a tool is not enough if people fail to make good use of it.","zh":"擁有工具並不足夠，如果人們未能充分利用它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes effective practical use.","zh":"這個短語描述有效的實際使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"available techniques","meaning":"可用技術","examples":[{"en":"Available techniques were not consistently used by the investigators.","zh":"調查員沒有一貫使用可用技術。"},{"en":"Available techniques are methods that already exist and can be used.","zh":"available techniques 是已存在並可使用的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher should use available techniques, such as examples and diagrams, to explain difficult grammar.","zh":"老師應使用例子和圖表等可用技術，解釋困難文法。"},{"en":"If available techniques are ignored, performance may remain weak.","zh":"如果可用技術被忽視，表現可能仍然薄弱。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to usable methods already within reach.","zh":"這個短語指已可取得並可使用的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"at the time","meaning":"當時","examples":[{"en":"Some investigative procedures were already known at the time.","zh":"有些調查程序在當時已為人所知。"},{"en":"At the time means during the period being discussed.","zh":"at the time 指在正在討論的那個時期。"},{"en":"At the time, the school had no computers in ordinary classrooms.","zh":"當時，學校普通課室沒有電腦。"},{"en":"The phrase helps readers judge people’s actions by what was available then.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者根據當時可用條件判斷人的行動。"},{"en":"It points to the historical moment of the event.","zh":"它指出事件發生的歷史時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 71 - Jack the Ripper - A Bungled Investigation?.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 72":[{"front":"driverless cars","meaning":"無人駕駛汽車","examples":[{"en":"Driverless cars may be set to become a reality.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車可能即將成為現實。"},{"en":"Driverless cars are vehicles that can travel without a human driver controlling them.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車是可以在沒有真人司機控制下行駛的車輛。"},{"en":"A city may test driverless cars on quiet roads before allowing them in busy traffic.","zh":"城市可能先在寧靜道路上測試無人駕駛汽車，然後才讓它們進入繁忙交通。"},{"en":"If driverless cars become common, taxi companies may need fewer human drivers.","zh":"如果無人駕駛汽車變得普遍，的士公司可能需要較少人類司機。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to cars controlled by technology rather than by a person behind the wheel.","zh":"這個短語指由科技控制，而不是由坐在駕駛席上的人控制的汽車。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be set to become a reality","meaning":"即將成為現實","examples":[{"en":"Driverless cars may be set to become a reality.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車可能即將成為現實。"},{"en":"To be set to become a reality means to be likely to happen or exist soon.","zh":"即將成為現實，是指某事很可能很快發生或真正存在。"},{"en":"Online medical consultations are set to become a reality in more clinics.","zh":"網上醫療諮詢即將在更多診所成為現實。"},{"en":"When money, technology and public interest are ready, an idea may become real.","zh":"當資金、科技和公眾興趣都準備好，一個想法就可能成為現實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that is moving from plan or imagination into real life.","zh":"這個短語描述某事正由計劃或想像走向現實生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"if someone is to be believed","meaning":"如果某人的說法可信","examples":[{"en":"Driverless cars may arrive soon if Uber executives are to be believed.","zh":"如果 Uber 高層的說法可信，無人駕駛汽車可能很快到來。"},{"en":"If someone is to be believed means if that person’s claim is true or trustworthy.","zh":"如果某人的說法可信，是指如果那人的聲稱是真實或可靠的。"},{"en":"If the weather forecast is to be believed, the school picnic will be cancelled tomorrow.","zh":"如果天氣預報可信，學校旅行明天將會取消。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a little caution because the speaker is reporting someone else’s view.","zh":"這個短語暗示一點謹慎，因為說話者是在轉述別人的看法。"},{"en":"It is useful when the information depends on whether a source is reliable.","zh":"當資訊取決於來源是否可靠時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"executives behind","meaning":"……背後的高層","examples":[{"en":"The executives behind Uber believe driverless cars may soon become real.","zh":"Uber 背後的高層相信無人駕駛汽車可能很快成為現實。"},{"en":"The executives behind a company are the senior people who lead or influence it.","zh":"一間公司背後的高層，是領導或影響該公司的高級人員。"},{"en":"The executives behind a new shopping app may decide how it expands into other cities.","zh":"新購物應用程式背後的高層，可能決定它如何擴展到其他城市。"},{"en":"When executives support a project, the company may invest money and staff in it.","zh":"當高層支持某項目，公司可能會投放金錢和人手。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the decision-makers behind an organisation.","zh":"這個短語指組織背後的決策者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"taxi app","meaning":"叫車應用程式","examples":[{"en":"Uber is widely known as a taxi app.","zh":"Uber 廣為人知是一個叫車應用程式。"},{"en":"A taxi app is a mobile application that helps people book rides by car.","zh":"叫車應用程式是幫助人們透過手機預約乘車服務的應用程式。"},{"en":"A student may use a taxi app to get home safely after a late lesson.","zh":"學生可能在夜間課堂後使用叫車應用程式安全回家。"},{"en":"Taxi apps can make travel easier because users can see prices, routes and driver details.","zh":"叫車應用程式可以令出行更方便，因為用戶可看到價格、路線和司機資料。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an app for arranging paid car journeys.","zh":"這個短語指安排付費汽車旅程的應用程式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"take one’s biggest steps yet towards","meaning":"朝……邁出至今最大的一步","examples":[{"en":"Uber is taking its biggest steps yet towards a driver-free world.","zh":"Uber 正朝無司機的世界邁出至今最大的一步。"},{"en":"To take one’s biggest steps yet towards something means to make the most important progress so far towards it.","zh":"朝某事邁出至今最大的一步，是指向該目標取得到目前為止最重要的進展。"},{"en":"A school takes its biggest step yet towards digital learning when it gives every student a tablet.","zh":"學校給每名學生一部平板電腦，就是朝數碼學習邁出至今最大的一步。"},{"en":"Major investment can show that an idea is moving closer to reality.","zh":"重大投資可以顯示某想法正更接近現實。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises progress that is larger than previous efforts.","zh":"這個短語強調比之前努力更大的進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"driver-free world","meaning":"無司機的世界","examples":[{"en":"Uber is taking major steps towards a driver-free world.","zh":"Uber 正朝無司機的世界邁出重大步伐。"},{"en":"A driver-free world is a future in which many vehicles operate without human drivers.","zh":"無司機的世界，是許多車輛在沒有真人司機下運作的未來。"},{"en":"In a driver-free world, a commuter might read or rest while the car drives itself.","zh":"在無司機的世界中，通勤者可以在汽車自動行駛時閱讀或休息。"},{"en":"Such a world could reduce driving stress, but it could also threaten driving jobs.","zh":"這樣的世界可以減少駕駛壓力，但也可能威脅司機工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a future transport system with little or no human driving.","zh":"這個短語描述一個很少或沒有真人駕駛的未來交通系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"launch a centre","meaning":"成立中心","examples":[{"en":"Uber is launching the Uber Advanced Technologies Centre in Pittsburgh.","zh":"Uber 正在匹茲堡成立 Uber 先進科技中心。"},{"en":"To launch a centre means to officially start or open an organisation for a special purpose.","zh":"成立中心，是指正式開始或開設一個有特定目的的機構。"},{"en":"A university may launch a centre for language learning to support international students.","zh":"大學可能成立語言學習中心，以支援國際學生。"},{"en":"Launching a centre often shows long-term commitment to research or development.","zh":"成立中心通常顯示對研究或發展的長期承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formally starting a new institution.","zh":"這個短語描述正式開設新機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Uber Advanced Technologies Centre","meaning":"Uber 先進科技中心","examples":[{"en":"The Uber Advanced Technologies Centre focuses on driverless technology.","zh":"Uber 先進科技中心專注於無人駕駛技術。"},{"en":"The Uber Advanced Technologies Centre is a research centre created to develop advanced transport technology.","zh":"Uber 先進科技中心是一個為發展先進交通科技而成立的研究中心。"},{"en":"Engineers at such a centre may test sensors, maps and safety systems.","zh":"這類中心的工程師可能測試感測器、地圖和安全系統。"},{"en":"A specialised technology centre can help a company move faster into a new field.","zh":"專門科技中心可以幫助公司更快進入新領域。"},{"en":"This phrase names Uber’s research centre for advanced vehicle technology.","zh":"這個短語命名 Uber 的先進車輛科技研究中心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the ultimate goal of","meaning":"……的最終目標","examples":[{"en":"The ultimate goal of the institution is to conduct research and development.","zh":"該機構的最終目標是進行研究與開發。"},{"en":"The ultimate goal of something is its final or most important aim.","zh":"某事的最終目標，是它最後或最重要的目的。"},{"en":"The ultimate goal of a school reading programme may be to help students enjoy books independently.","zh":"學校閱讀計劃的最終目標可能是幫助學生自主享受閱讀。"},{"en":"Knowing the ultimate goal helps people understand why money and effort are being spent.","zh":"知道最終目標有助人們理解為何要投放金錢和努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main purpose behind an action or organisation.","zh":"這個短語描述行動或機構背後的主要目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"institution","meaning":"機構","examples":[{"en":"The institution carries out research into mapping and vehicle safety.","zh":"該機構進行地圖繪製和車輛安全方面的研究。"},{"en":"An institution is an organisation created for a specific purpose, such as education, research or public service.","zh":"機構是為教育、研究或公共服務等特定目的而建立的組織。"},{"en":"A hospital is an institution that provides medical care to the community.","zh":"醫院是為社區提供醫療服務的機構。"},{"en":"Institutions can gather experts, money and equipment to solve complex problems.","zh":"機構可以集合專家、資金和設備來解決複雜問題。"},{"en":"This word refers to an organised body, not just a building.","zh":"這個詞指有組織的團體，而不只是建築物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"research and development","meaning":"研究與開發","examples":[{"en":"The centre conducts research and development in several areas.","zh":"該中心在幾個範疇進行研究與開發。"},{"en":"Research and development means studying ideas and turning them into useful products or systems.","zh":"研究與開發，是研究想法並把它們變成有用產品或系統。"},{"en":"A phone company may spend heavily on research and development before releasing a new model.","zh":"手機公司可能在推出新型號前大量投資研究與開發。"},{"en":"Without research and development, new technology may remain only an idea.","zh":"沒有研究與開發，新科技可能只停留在想法階段。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the process of investigating and creating improvements.","zh":"這個短語指調查和創造改進的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"primarily in the areas of","meaning":"主要在……範疇","examples":[{"en":"The research is primarily in the areas of mapping and vehicle safety.","zh":"研究主要在地圖繪製和車輛安全範疇。"},{"en":"Primarily in the areas of something means mainly focused on those fields.","zh":"主要在某些範疇，是指主要集中於那些領域。"},{"en":"A school improvement plan may focus primarily in the areas of reading and student wellbeing.","zh":"學校改善計劃可能主要集中於閱讀和學生福祉範疇。"},{"en":"Stating the main areas helps readers see what the project values most.","zh":"說明主要範疇有助讀者看出項目最重視甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the chief fields of work or study.","zh":"這個短語引入工作或研究的主要領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"mapping","meaning":"地圖繪製；測繪","examples":[{"en":"Mapping is one area of research for driverless cars.","zh":"地圖繪製是無人駕駛汽車的一個研究範疇。"},{"en":"Mapping means creating detailed maps that show roads, lanes, signs and surroundings.","zh":"地圖繪製，是建立顯示道路、行車線、標誌和周圍環境的詳細地圖。"},{"en":"A delivery company may use mapping to plan faster routes for its drivers.","zh":"送貨公司可能使用地圖繪製來為司機規劃更快路線。"},{"en":"Driverless cars need accurate mapping because they must know where they are and what is nearby.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車需要準確地圖繪製，因為它們必須知道自己在哪裡以及附近有甚麼。"},{"en":"This word refers to making or using maps, not simply reading a paper map.","zh":"這個詞指製作或使用地圖，而不只是閱讀紙本地圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"vehicle safety","meaning":"車輛安全","examples":[{"en":"Vehicle safety is a major focus of Uber’s research centre.","zh":"車輛安全是 Uber 研究中心的主要焦點。"},{"en":"Vehicle safety means designing and operating vehicles so they reduce accidents and injuries.","zh":"車輛安全是設計和操作車輛，使其減少意外和傷害。"},{"en":"Seat belts, airbags and brake systems are all part of vehicle safety.","zh":"安全帶、安全氣囊和煞車系統都是車輛安全的一部分。"},{"en":"Driverless-car companies must improve vehicle safety before the public will trust them.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車公司必須改善車輛安全，公眾才會信任它們。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to protecting passengers, pedestrians and other road users.","zh":"這個短語指保護乘客、行人和其他道路使用者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"autonomy technology","meaning":"自主駕駛技術","examples":[{"en":"Autonomy technology is essential for fully driverless cars.","zh":"自主駕駛技術對完全無人駕駛汽車必不可少。"},{"en":"Autonomy technology is technology that allows a machine or vehicle to operate by itself.","zh":"自主駕駛技術是讓機器或車輛自行運作的科技。"},{"en":"A robot vacuum uses simple autonomy technology to move around a room without constant control.","zh":"機械人吸塵機使用簡單自主技術，在不用持續控制下在房間內移動。"},{"en":"Better autonomy technology can reduce the need for human decisions during driving.","zh":"更好的自主駕駛技術可以減少駕駛時對人類決策的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the systems that make self-control possible.","zh":"這個短語指令自行控制成為可能的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"to date","meaning":"至今","examples":[{"en":"To date, Uber has provided a chauffeur-driven taxi service.","zh":"至今，Uber 一直提供由司機駕駛的的士服務。"},{"en":"To date means up to the present time.","zh":"至今，是指直到現在為止。"},{"en":"To date, the school has collected enough donations to buy twenty computers.","zh":"至今，學校已籌得足夠捐款購買二十部電腦。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the situation may change in the future.","zh":"這個短語暗示情況將來可能改變。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing what has happened so far with what may happen next.","zh":"它適合把目前已發生的事與之後可能發生的事作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"provide a chauffeur-driven taxi service","meaning":"提供由司機駕駛的的士服務","examples":[{"en":"Uber has provided a chauffeur-driven taxi service for American clients.","zh":"Uber 為美國客戶提供由司機駕駛的的士服務。"},{"en":"To provide a chauffeur-driven taxi service means to offer car rides with a human driver.","zh":"提供由司機駕駛的的士服務，是指提供有真人司機接載的汽車旅程。"},{"en":"A hotel may provide a chauffeur-driven taxi service for guests arriving from the airport.","zh":"酒店可能為從機場抵達的住客提供由司機駕駛的的士服務。"},{"en":"This service costs money partly because a driver must be paid.","zh":"這種服務需要收費，部分原因是必須支付司機薪酬。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts human-driven transport with driverless transport.","zh":"這個短語把真人駕駛交通與無人駕駛交通作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"chauffeur-driven","meaning":"由司機駕駛的","examples":[{"en":"Uber began with chauffeur-driven taxi services.","zh":"Uber 最初提供由司機駕駛的的士服務。"},{"en":"Chauffeur-driven means driven by a paid professional driver.","zh":"由司機駕駛的，是指由受薪專業司機駕駛。"},{"en":"A business visitor may book a chauffeur-driven car for an important meeting.","zh":"商務訪客可能為重要會議預約由司機駕駛的汽車。"},{"en":"If a service is chauffeur-driven, labour cost becomes part of the fare.","zh":"如果服務由司機駕駛，人工成本就成為車費的一部分。"},{"en":"This word describes transport operated by a human driver for passengers.","zh":"這個詞描述由真人司機為乘客操作的交通工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"American clients","meaning":"美國客戶","examples":[{"en":"Uber has provided services for American clients.","zh":"Uber 一直為美國客戶提供服務。"},{"en":"American clients are customers or users in the United States.","zh":"美國客戶是在美國的顧客或用戶。"},{"en":"A tutoring company may design English courses for American clients who need business writing.","zh":"補習公司可能為需要商務寫作的美國客戶設計英語課程。"},{"en":"Serving American clients may require understanding local laws, prices and expectations.","zh":"服務美國客戶可能需要了解當地法律、價格和期望。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to customers from or based in America.","zh":"這個短語指來自美國或位於美國的客戶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"venture into the realms of","meaning":"涉足……領域","examples":[{"en":"Uber is venturing into the realms of driverless cars.","zh":"Uber 正涉足無人駕駛汽車領域。"},{"en":"To venture into the realms of something means to enter a new and possibly risky field.","zh":"涉足某領域，是指進入一個新的、可能有風險的範疇。"},{"en":"A small bakery may venture into the realm of online delivery for the first time.","zh":"小型麵包店可能首次涉足網上送貨領域。"},{"en":"Entering a new field can create growth, but it can also bring uncertainty and cost.","zh":"進入新領域可以帶來增長，但也會帶來不確定性和成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving into unfamiliar territory.","zh":"這個短語描述進入陌生領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a new direction","meaning":"新方向","examples":[{"en":"Driverless cars represent a new direction for Uber.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車代表 Uber 的新方向。"},{"en":"A new direction is a different path, plan or focus from before.","zh":"新方向是與過去不同的道路、計劃或焦點。"},{"en":"A school may take a new direction by focusing more on project-based learning.","zh":"學校可能透過更重視專題式學習來採取新方向。"},{"en":"A new direction can require new skills, investment and public support.","zh":"新方向可能需要新技能、投資和公眾支持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major shift in strategy.","zh":"這個短語描述策略上的重大轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"require massive investment","meaning":"需要巨額投資","examples":[{"en":"This new direction will require massive investment.","zh":"這個新方向將需要巨額投資。"},{"en":"To require massive investment means to need a very large amount of money, time or resources.","zh":"需要巨額投資，是指需要非常大量金錢、時間或資源。"},{"en":"Building a new hospital requires massive investment in land, equipment and staff.","zh":"興建新醫院需要在土地、設備和人手上作巨額投資。"},{"en":"If a technology requires massive investment, companies must believe the future reward is worth the risk.","zh":"如果一項科技需要巨額投資，公司必須相信未來回報值得冒險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a project that is expensive and resource-heavy.","zh":"這個短語描述昂貴且資源需求大的項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a huge leap of faith","meaning":"大膽一試；憑信心作出的重大嘗試","examples":[{"en":"Investing in driverless cars is a huge leap of faith for Uber.","zh":"投資無人駕駛汽車對 Uber 而言是一次大膽嘗試。"},{"en":"A huge leap of faith is a major decision made with confidence despite uncertainty.","zh":"大膽一試，是在不確定下仍憑信心作出的重大決定。"},{"en":"Leaving a stable job to start a small business can be a huge leap of faith.","zh":"離開穩定工作去創辦小生意，可以是一次大膽嘗試。"},{"en":"This kind of decision is risky because success is not guaranteed.","zh":"這種決定有風險，因為成功沒有保證。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a bold move based partly on belief rather than proof.","zh":"這個短語描述部分基於信念而非證明的大膽行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on someone’s part","meaning":"對某人而言；由某人作出","examples":[{"en":"The investment is a huge leap of faith on Uber’s part.","zh":"這項投資是 Uber 作出的一次大膽嘗試。"},{"en":"On someone’s part means done by that person or organisation.","zh":"on someone’s part 是指由該人或機構作出。"},{"en":"Offering extra homework help was a kind gesture on the teacher’s part.","zh":"提供額外功課幫助，是老師作出的善意舉動。"},{"en":"When a company takes a risk on its part, it accepts responsibility for that choice.","zh":"當公司作出風險選擇，它就接受該選擇的責任。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who is taking the action or responsibility.","zh":"這個短語指出誰作出行動或承擔責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have yet to catch up with","meaning":"尚未追上……","examples":[{"en":"Technology has yet to catch up with the idea of a fully autonomous vehicle.","zh":"科技尚未追上完全自動駕駛車輛的概念。"},{"en":"To have yet to catch up with something means still not to be advanced enough for it.","zh":"尚未追上某事，是指仍未發展到足夠做到它的程度。"},{"en":"School rules may have yet to catch up with students’ use of artificial intelligence tools.","zh":"校規可能尚未追上學生使用人工智能工具的情況。"},{"en":"When technology has not caught up, an idea may be possible in theory but not ready in practice.","zh":"當科技尚未追上，想法可能理論上可行，但實際上未準備好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gap between ambition and current ability.","zh":"這個短語描述抱負與現有能力之間的差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the idea of","meaning":"……的概念","examples":[{"en":"Technology has not fully caught up with the idea of a driverless vehicle.","zh":"科技尚未完全追上無人駕駛車輛的概念。"},{"en":"The idea of something means the concept or possibility of it.","zh":"某事的概念，是指它的想法或可能性。"},{"en":"The idea of studying abroad may excite students before they know the full cost.","zh":"留學的概念可能在學生知道全部費用前已令他們興奮。"},{"en":"An idea can sound attractive before the practical details are solved.","zh":"一個概念在實際細節解決前，可能聽起來很吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a concept rather than the finished reality.","zh":"這個短語指概念，而不是已完成的現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fully autonomous vehicle","meaning":"完全自動駕駛車輛","examples":[{"en":"A fully autonomous vehicle can operate without a human driver.","zh":"完全自動駕駛車輛可以在沒有真人司機下運作。"},{"en":"A fully autonomous vehicle is a vehicle that can drive itself in all necessary situations.","zh":"完全自動駕駛車輛，是能在所有必要情況下自行駕駛的車輛。"},{"en":"A delivery company may hope to use fully autonomous vehicles to move goods at night.","zh":"送貨公司可能希望使用完全自動駕駛車輛在夜間運送貨物。"},{"en":"Full autonomy requires sensors, maps, decision-making software and strong safety systems.","zh":"完全自主駕駛需要感測器、地圖、決策軟件和強大安全系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the highest level of self-driving vehicle.","zh":"這個短語描述最高級別的自動駕駛車輛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on the plus side","meaning":"正面來看","examples":[{"en":"On the plus side, some self-driving features already exist.","zh":"正面來看，一些自動駕駛功能已經存在。"},{"en":"On the plus side introduces a positive point after mentioning a difficulty or risk.","zh":"正面來看，是在提及困難或風險後，引入正面重點。"},{"en":"The flat is small; on the plus side, it is close to school.","zh":"這個單位很小；正面來看，它很接近學校。"},{"en":"This phrase helps balance criticism with something encouraging.","zh":"這個短語幫助用令人鼓舞的內容平衡批評。"},{"en":"It signals that the next point is an advantage.","zh":"它表示下一點是一項優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be equipped with","meaning":"配備","examples":[{"en":"Some cars are already equipped with self-driving technology.","zh":"有些汽車已配備自動駕駛技術。"},{"en":"To be equipped with something means to have it installed or provided for use.","zh":"配備某物，是指安裝或提供該物以供使用。"},{"en":"A classroom equipped with projectors and speakers can support video lessons.","zh":"配備投影機和揚聲器的課室可以支援影片課堂。"},{"en":"Cars equipped with sensors can detect lanes, obstacles and nearby vehicles.","zh":"配備感測器的汽車可以偵測行車線、障礙物和附近車輛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes having useful tools or technology built in.","zh":"這個短語描述內置有用工具或科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"self-driving technology","meaning":"自動駕駛技術","examples":[{"en":"Cars equipped with self-driving technology can already park themselves.","zh":"配備自動駕駛技術的汽車已經能自行泊車。"},{"en":"Self-driving technology allows a car to perform some or all driving tasks automatically.","zh":"自動駕駛技術讓汽車自動執行部分或全部駕駛任務。"},{"en":"A modern car may use self-driving technology to keep a safe distance on the highway.","zh":"現代汽車可能使用自動駕駛技術在公路上保持安全距離。"},{"en":"If this technology improves, cars may need less human control.","zh":"如果這項技術改進，汽車可能需要較少人類控制。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to systems that help vehicles drive themselves.","zh":"這個短語指幫助車輛自行駕駛的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"stay in their lane","meaning":"保持在行車線內","examples":[{"en":"Some driverless systems can help cars stay in their lane.","zh":"一些無人駕駛系統可以幫助汽車保持在行車線內。"},{"en":"To stay in their lane means to remain within the marked road lane.","zh":"保持在行車線內，是指留在道路標示的行車線中。"},{"en":"A tired driver may drift, but lane-assist technology can help the car stay in its lane.","zh":"疲倦司機可能偏離路線，但車道輔助技術可以幫助汽車保持在行車線內。"},{"en":"Staying in the correct lane reduces the risk of hitting nearby vehicles.","zh":"保持在正確行車線內可以減少撞到附近車輛的風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled position on the road.","zh":"這個短語描述道路上的受控位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"maintain a steady cruising speed","meaning":"保持穩定巡航速度","examples":[{"en":"Some cars can maintain a steady cruising speed.","zh":"有些汽車能保持穩定巡航速度。"},{"en":"To maintain a steady cruising speed means to keep moving at a regular speed for a period of travel.","zh":"保持穩定巡航速度，是指在一段行程中保持規律速度行駛。"},{"en":"Cruise control helps a driver maintain a steady speed on a long motorway journey.","zh":"巡航控制幫助司機在長途高速公路旅程中保持穩定速度。"},{"en":"A steady speed can save fuel and reduce sudden braking.","zh":"穩定速度可以節省燃油並減少突然煞車。"},{"en":"This phrase describes smooth, consistent movement rather than stop-start driving.","zh":"這個短語描述平穩一致的移動，而不是走走停停的駕駛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in a patchwork fashion","meaning":"以拼湊方式","examples":[{"en":"These capabilities could build towards automation in a patchwork fashion.","zh":"這些能力可以以拼湊方式逐步發展至自動化。"},{"en":"In a patchwork fashion means by adding separate pieces gradually rather than creating one complete system at once.","zh":"以拼湊方式，是指逐步加入不同部分，而不是一次建立完整系統。"},{"en":"A school may improve technology in a patchwork fashion by upgrading one classroom at a time.","zh":"學校可能以拼湊方式改善科技設備，一次升級一間課室。"},{"en":"Patchwork development can be practical, but the final system may feel uneven at first.","zh":"拼湊式發展可以實際可行，但最終系統初期可能不夠一致。"},{"en":"This phrase describes progress made through separate, gradual additions.","zh":"這個短語描述透過分開而逐步加入來取得進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"these capabilities","meaning":"這些能力","examples":[{"en":"These capabilities may eventually lead to almost full automation.","zh":"這些能力可能最終導致近乎完全自動化。"},{"en":"These capabilities are the abilities or functions that have just been mentioned.","zh":"這些能力，是剛才提到的能力或功能。"},{"en":"A phone’s camera, GPS and payment tools are capabilities that make it useful in daily life.","zh":"手機的相機、GPS 和付款工具都是令它在日常生活中有用的能力。"},{"en":"When several capabilities combine, they can create a much more powerful system.","zh":"當幾種能力結合起來，就能創造更強大的系統。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to specific abilities already discussed.","zh":"這個短語回指已討論的具體能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"build towards","meaning":"逐步發展至……","examples":[{"en":"Current vehicle features could build towards almost full automation.","zh":"現有車輛功能可以逐步發展至近乎完全自動化。"},{"en":"To build towards something means to gradually develop in the direction of a final goal.","zh":"逐步發展至某事，是指朝着最終目標慢慢發展。"},{"en":"Daily vocabulary practice can build towards stronger writing skills.","zh":"每日詞彙練習可以逐步發展成更強寫作能力。"},{"en":"Small improvements can become important when they all move toward the same goal.","zh":"當小改善都朝同一目標前進時，它們可以變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes step-by-step progress.","zh":"這個短語描述一步一步的進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"almost full automation","meaning":"近乎完全自動化","examples":[{"en":"Several driving features could eventually build towards almost full automation.","zh":"幾種駕駛功能最終可以逐步發展至近乎完全自動化。"},{"en":"Almost full automation means a system can do nearly all tasks by itself, with little human help.","zh":"近乎完全自動化，是指系統幾乎能自行完成所有任務，只需很少人類協助。"},{"en":"A factory with almost full automation may need workers mainly to monitor machines.","zh":"近乎完全自動化的工廠可能主要需要工人監察機器。"},{"en":"In cars, almost full automation could reduce driving work but still require human oversight.","zh":"在汽車中，近乎完全自動化可以減少駕駛工作，但仍可能需要人類監督。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a stage close to complete automation.","zh":"這個短語描述接近完全自動化的階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"readily embrace the idea of","meaning":"欣然接受……的想法","examples":[{"en":"Uber believes car owners will readily embrace the idea of driverless taxis.","zh":"Uber 相信車主會欣然接受無人駕駛的士的想法。"},{"en":"To readily embrace the idea of something means to accept it willingly and quickly.","zh":"欣然接受某想法，是指願意而快速地接受它。"},{"en":"Students may readily embrace the idea of shorter homework if it still helps them learn.","zh":"如果較短功課仍能幫助學習，學生可能欣然接受這個想法。"},{"en":"People accept new technology more easily when it saves money or reduces stress.","zh":"當新科技能省錢或減壓，人們較容易接受它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes warm and willing acceptance.","zh":"這個短語描述熱切而願意的接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"driverless taxis","meaning":"無人駕駛的士","examples":[{"en":"Uber believes that many people will use driverless taxis.","zh":"Uber 相信許多人會使用無人駕駛的士。"},{"en":"Driverless taxis are taxi services operated by self-driving cars instead of human drivers.","zh":"無人駕駛的士是由自動駕駛汽車而非真人司機營運的的士服務。"},{"en":"A passenger might call a driverless taxi through an app after leaving a concert.","zh":"乘客可能在離開音樂會後，透過應用程式叫一輛無人駕駛的士。"},{"en":"Driverless taxis could lower fares if companies no longer pay drivers.","zh":"如果公司不再支付司機薪酬，無人駕駛的士可以降低車費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taxis controlled by automated systems.","zh":"這個短語描述由自動系統控制的的士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in someone’s eyes","meaning":"在某人看來","examples":[{"en":"In Uber’s eyes, car owners only stand to gain from this technology.","zh":"在 Uber 看來，車主只會從這項技術中受益。"},{"en":"In someone’s eyes means from that person’s or organisation’s point of view.","zh":"在某人看來，是指從該人或機構的角度而言。"},{"en":"In a parent’s eyes, a strict bedtime may be necessary for a child’s health.","zh":"在父母看來，嚴格睡覺時間可能對孩子健康有必要。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that the view may be subjective.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者該看法可能是主觀的。"},{"en":"It is useful when reporting one side’s opinion.","zh":"它適合轉述某一方的意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"stand to gain from","meaning":"有望從……中受益","examples":[{"en":"Current car owners stand to gain from driverless taxi technology.","zh":"現有車主有望從無人駕駛的士技術中受益。"},{"en":"To stand to gain from something means to be likely to benefit from it.","zh":"有望從某事中受益，是指很可能因它得到好處。"},{"en":"Students stand to gain from smaller classes because teachers can give more attention.","zh":"學生有望從小班教學中受益，因為老師能給予更多關注。"},{"en":"If driverless taxis reduce travel costs, passengers may benefit directly.","zh":"如果無人駕駛的士降低出行成本，乘客可能直接受益。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a likely advantage from a change.","zh":"這個短語描述變化帶來的可能好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the introduction of","meaning":"……的引入","examples":[{"en":"Car owners may benefit from the introduction of driverless technology.","zh":"車主可能因無人駕駛技術的引入而受益。"},{"en":"The introduction of something means the first use or arrival of it in a place or system.","zh":"某事的引入，是指它在某地方或系統中首次使用或出現。"},{"en":"The introduction of online booking made clinic appointments easier.","zh":"網上預約的引入令診所預約更方便。"},{"en":"A new technology’s introduction can change prices, jobs and daily habits.","zh":"新技術的引入可以改變價格、工作和日常習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bringing something new into use.","zh":"這個短語描述把新事物帶入使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"such technology","meaning":"這類技術","examples":[{"en":"Such technology could reduce the cost of taxi journeys.","zh":"這類技術可以降低的士旅程成本。"},{"en":"Such technology means technology of the kind just mentioned.","zh":"這類技術，是指剛才提到的那種科技。"},{"en":"Schools may use tablets and learning apps; such technology can make lessons more interactive.","zh":"學校可能使用平板電腦和學習應用程式；這類技術可以令課堂更互動。"},{"en":"When such technology becomes cheaper, more people may start using it.","zh":"當這類技術變得較便宜，更多人可能開始使用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a type of technology already discussed.","zh":"這個短語回指已討論的一種科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hire a driverless cab","meaning":"乘搭無人駕駛的士","examples":[{"en":"Hiring a driverless cab could be cheaper than hiring a normal taxi.","zh":"乘搭無人駕駛的士可能比乘搭普通的士便宜。"},{"en":"To hire a driverless cab means to pay for a ride in a taxi without a human driver.","zh":"乘搭無人駕駛的士，是指付費乘坐沒有真人司機的的士。"},{"en":"A traveller might hire a driverless cab from the airport to a hotel.","zh":"旅客可能從機場乘搭無人駕駛的士到酒店。"},{"en":"The fare may fall if no driver’s wage is included in the cost.","zh":"如果車費不包括司機薪酬，收費可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using an automated taxi service.","zh":"這個短語描述使用自動化的士服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cab fee","meaning":"的士車費","examples":[{"en":"The client would not need to pay for the driver in the cab fee.","zh":"客戶不需要在的士車費中支付司機成本。"},{"en":"A cab fee is the amount a passenger pays for a taxi journey.","zh":"的士車費是乘客為的士旅程支付的金額。"},{"en":"A late-night cab fee may be higher because demand is greater.","zh":"深夜的士車費可能較高，因為需求較大。"},{"en":"If the cab fee does not include a driver’s wage, the ride may become cheaper.","zh":"如果的士車費不包括司機薪酬，車程可能變得較便宜。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the price charged for a taxi ride.","zh":"這個短語指的士旅程所收取的價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cost incurred by","meaning":"由……產生的費用","examples":[{"en":"The only cost incurred by clients is for fuel and wear and tear.","zh":"由客戶產生的唯一費用是燃料和損耗。"},{"en":"Cost incurred by someone means the expense that person has to pay or is responsible for.","zh":"由某人產生的費用，是該人必須支付或負責的開支。"},{"en":"The cost incurred by a student on a field trip may include transport and lunch.","zh":"學生參加考察所產生的費用可能包括交通和午餐。"},{"en":"If fewer costs are incurred by passengers, the service becomes more attractive.","zh":"如果乘客需要承擔的費用較少，服務就變得更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who bears a particular expense.","zh":"這個短語指出誰承擔某項開支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"plus wear and tear","meaning":"加上損耗","examples":[{"en":"Clients may only pay for fuel, plus wear and tear.","zh":"客戶可能只支付燃料，加上損耗。"},{"en":"Plus wear and tear means with an additional cost for the gradual damage caused by use.","zh":"加上損耗，是指再加上因使用而造成逐漸損壞的成本。"},{"en":"A car rental fee may include fuel plus wear and tear on the vehicle.","zh":"租車費可能包括燃料，加上車輛損耗。"},{"en":"Even if no driver is paid, every journey still slightly damages the car.","zh":"即使不用支付司機，每次旅程仍會令汽車有輕微損耗。"},{"en":"This phrase adds the cost of normal use and ageing.","zh":"這個短語加上正常使用和老化的成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"wear and tear","meaning":"損耗","examples":[{"en":"Wear and tear is part of the cost of using a vehicle.","zh":"損耗是使用車輛成本的一部分。"},{"en":"Wear and tear means gradual damage caused by normal use over time.","zh":"損耗是長期正常使用造成的逐漸損壞。"},{"en":"School desks show wear and tear after many years of students using them.","zh":"學校桌子經過多年學生使用後會顯示損耗。"},{"en":"A car needs repairs because tyres, brakes and seats suffer wear and tear.","zh":"汽車需要維修，因為輪胎、煞車和座椅都會承受損耗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordinary damage, not sudden accidents.","zh":"這個短語描述普通損壞，而不是突然意外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an attractive proposition","meaning":"吸引人的提議；有吸引力的方案","examples":[{"en":"A cheaper driverless taxi is an attractive proposition.","zh":"較便宜的無人駕駛的士是一個有吸引力的方案。"},{"en":"An attractive proposition is an idea or offer that seems appealing and worthwhile.","zh":"有吸引力的方案，是看起來吸引且值得考慮的想法或提議。"},{"en":"A four-day school week may be an attractive proposition for tired students.","zh":"四天上課週對疲倦學生來說可能是吸引人的提議。"},{"en":"A proposal becomes attractive when it saves money, time or effort.","zh":"當方案能省錢、省時間或省力，它就變得有吸引力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an option that people may want to accept.","zh":"這個短語描述人們可能想接受的選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stand to benefit","meaning":"有望受益","examples":[{"en":"Uber stands to benefit from driverless taxis.","zh":"Uber 有望從無人駕駛的士中受益。"},{"en":"To stand to benefit means to be likely to gain an advantage.","zh":"有望受益，是指很可能得到好處。"},{"en":"A shop stands to benefit if a new train station brings more customers nearby.","zh":"如果新火車站帶來更多附近顧客，商店有望受益。"},{"en":"Uber may benefit if driverless taxis reduce labour costs.","zh":"如果無人駕駛的士降低人工成本，Uber 可能受益。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a likely future gain.","zh":"這個短語描述未來可能得到的好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be removed from the company’s payroll","meaning":"從公司的薪酬名冊中移除","examples":[{"en":"Taxi drivers could be removed from the company’s payroll.","zh":"的士司機可能被從公司的薪酬名冊中移除。"},{"en":"To be removed from the company’s payroll means no longer to be paid as employees or workers by the company.","zh":"從公司的薪酬名冊中移除，是指不再由公司作為員工或工人支付薪酬。"},{"en":"If a restaurant closes one branch, some staff may be removed from the payroll.","zh":"如果餐廳關閉一間分店，有些員工可能被從薪酬名冊中移除。"},{"en":"Automation can reduce costs by reducing the number of paid workers.","zh":"自動化可以透過減少受薪員工數目來降低成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes workers losing paid positions in a company.","zh":"這個短語描述工人失去公司中的受薪職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"company payroll","meaning":"公司薪酬名冊","examples":[{"en":"Driverless taxis would reduce the number of workers on the company payroll.","zh":"無人駕駛的士會減少公司薪酬名冊上的工人數目。"},{"en":"A company payroll is the list of workers a company pays wages or salaries to.","zh":"公司薪酬名冊是公司支付工資或薪金的員工名單。"},{"en":"A school’s payroll may include teachers, clerks, cleaners and security guards.","zh":"學校薪酬名冊可能包括老師、文員、清潔工和保安員。"},{"en":"If fewer people are on the payroll, the company spends less on wages.","zh":"如果薪酬名冊上的人較少，公司在工資上的支出就較少。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to paid staff from the company’s point of view.","zh":"這個短語從公司角度指受薪員工。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a win-win situation","meaning":"雙贏局面","examples":[{"en":"For car users and Uber, driverless taxis may be a win-win situation.","zh":"對汽車用戶和 Uber 來說，無人駕駛的士可能是雙贏局面。"},{"en":"A win-win situation is one in which both sides benefit.","zh":"雙贏局面，是雙方都受益的情況。"},{"en":"If students get more reading time and teachers see better results, it is a win-win situation.","zh":"如果學生得到更多閱讀時間，而老師看到更好成效，這就是雙贏局面。"},{"en":"Driverless taxis may help passengers save money and help Uber reduce labour costs.","zh":"無人駕駛的士可能幫助乘客省錢，也幫助 Uber 降低人工成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an outcome where more than one party gains.","zh":"這個短語描述多於一方得益的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not everyone will benefit from","meaning":"並非所有人都會從……受益","examples":[{"en":"Not everyone will benefit from driverless technology.","zh":"並非所有人都會從無人駕駛技術中受益。"},{"en":"Not everyone will benefit from something means some people may gain, but others may lose or be unaffected.","zh":"並非所有人都會從某事受益，是指有些人可能得益，但其他人可能受損或沒有影響。"},{"en":"Not everyone benefits from online lessons; some students need face-to-face support.","zh":"並非所有人都從網上課堂受益；有些學生需要面對面支援。"},{"en":"New technology can help customers while harming workers whose jobs are replaced.","zh":"新科技可以幫助顧客，同時傷害工作被取代的工人。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that benefits are unevenly shared.","zh":"這個短語提醒人好處並非平均分配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"an obvious example","meaning":"明顯例子","examples":[{"en":"The car industry is an obvious example of a group that may lose out.","zh":"汽車行業是一個可能受損群體的明顯例子。"},{"en":"An obvious example is a clear case that is easy to see or understand.","zh":"明顯例子是容易看見或理解的清楚個案。"},{"en":"If rising rents hurt small shops, a family-run café is an obvious example.","zh":"如果租金上升傷害小商店，家庭經營咖啡店就是明顯例子。"},{"en":"Writers use obvious examples to make an argument easier to follow.","zh":"作者使用明顯例子，令論點較容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a case that clearly illustrates a point.","zh":"這個短語引入清楚說明某點的個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not surprisingly","meaning":"不足為奇","examples":[{"en":"Not surprisingly, the car industry is worried about self-driving cars.","zh":"汽車行業對自動駕駛汽車感到擔心，這不足為奇。"},{"en":"Not surprisingly means the situation is expected and easy to understand.","zh":"不足為奇，是指情況可預期且容易理解。"},{"en":"Not surprisingly, students were tired after three exams in one day.","zh":"一天考三科後，學生感到疲倦不足為奇。"},{"en":"If a new technology threatens jobs, concern from affected workers is expected.","zh":"如果新科技威脅工作，受影響工人感到擔心是可預期的。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a reaction that should not shock the reader.","zh":"這個短語引入不應令讀者驚訝的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"view something with alarm","meaning":"對某事感到憂慮","examples":[{"en":"The car industry views self-driving cars with alarm.","zh":"汽車行業對自動駕駛汽車感到憂慮。"},{"en":"To view something with alarm means to look at it with serious worry or fear.","zh":"對某事感到憂慮，是指以嚴重擔心或恐懼看待它。"},{"en":"Parents may view a dangerous road near school with alarm.","zh":"父母可能對學校附近危險道路感到憂慮。"},{"en":"Industries may feel alarm when new technology threatens their business model.","zh":"當新科技威脅商業模式，行業可能感到憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong concern, not mild interest.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈擔心，而不是輕微興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the concept of","meaning":"……的概念","examples":[{"en":"The industry is worried about the concept of self-driving cars.","zh":"業界擔心自動駕駛汽車的概念。"},{"en":"The concept of something means the general idea behind it.","zh":"某事的概念，是它背後的一般想法。"},{"en":"The concept of working from home sounded strange to some companies at first.","zh":"在家工作這個概念最初對某些公司而言很陌生。"},{"en":"A concept can cause concern even before the final product is common.","zh":"即使最終產品尚未普及，概念本身也可能引起憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the idea itself rather than one specific example.","zh":"這個短語指想法本身，而不是某一個具體例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a sense of growing alarm","meaning":"日益加深的憂慮感","examples":[{"en":"The car industry views driverless technology with a sense of growing alarm.","zh":"汽車行業以日益加深的憂慮感看待無人駕駛技術。"},{"en":"A sense of growing alarm is a feeling of worry that becomes stronger over time.","zh":"日益加深的憂慮感，是隨時間變得更強的擔心。"},{"en":"Residents may feel a sense of growing alarm if traffic accidents increase near their homes.","zh":"如果家附近交通意外增加，居民可能感到日益加深的憂慮。"},{"en":"As a threat becomes clearer, worry may grow from mild concern to serious fear.","zh":"隨着威脅變得更清楚，擔心可能由輕微關注變成嚴重恐懼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing anxiety about a situation.","zh":"這個短語描述對某情況日益增加的焦慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"could well prove","meaning":"很可能證明是……","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving cars could well prove damaging to private car ownership.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車很可能證明會損害私家車擁有權。"},{"en":"Could well prove means may very possibly turn out to be true or have that effect.","zh":"很可能證明是，是指很有可能最後顯示為真或產生那種效果。"},{"en":"A new study method could well prove useful if students practise it regularly.","zh":"如果學生定期練習，新的學習方法很可能證明有用。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a strong possibility, but not complete certainty.","zh":"這個短語表示強烈可能性，但不是完全肯定。"},{"en":"It is useful when predicting an outcome carefully.","zh":"它適合謹慎預測結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the death knell for","meaning":"……的喪鐘；……終結的信號","examples":[{"en":"Driverless taxis could be the death knell for private car ownership.","zh":"無人駕駛的士可能成為私家車擁有權的喪鐘。"},{"en":"The death knell for something means a sign that it may soon end or disappear.","zh":"某事的喪鐘，是指它可能很快結束或消失的信號。"},{"en":"Online news was seen by some people as the death knell for printed newspapers.","zh":"網上新聞曾被一些人視為印刷報紙的喪鐘。"},{"en":"If driverless taxis become cheap and convenient, fewer people may need private cars.","zh":"如果無人駕駛的士便宜又方便，較少人可能需要私家車。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a development that may signal the end of something.","zh":"這個短語描述可能預示某事終結的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"private car ownership","meaning":"私家車擁有權","examples":[{"en":"Driverless taxis may reduce private car ownership.","zh":"無人駕駛的士可能減少私家車擁有權。"},{"en":"Private car ownership means individuals or households owning their own cars.","zh":"私家車擁有權，是個人或家庭擁有自己的汽車。"},{"en":"In areas with excellent public transport, private car ownership may be less common.","zh":"在公共交通優良的地區，私家車擁有權可能較不普遍。"},{"en":"If taxis become cheap and reliable, some families may decide not to buy a car.","zh":"如果的士變得便宜又可靠，有些家庭可能決定不買車。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to personal ownership of cars rather than shared transport.","zh":"這個短語指個人擁有汽車，而不是共享交通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, the car industry is delaying the introduction of automated vehicles.","zh":"因此，汽車行業正在推遲自動化車輛的引入。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what has just been mentioned.","zh":"因此，是指因為剛才提到的事情。"},{"en":"The road was flooded; as a result, buses arrived late.","zh":"道路水浸；因此，巴士遲到。"},{"en":"If companies fear losing sales, they may slow down new technology.","zh":"如果公司害怕失去銷售，它們可能放慢新科技推出。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with its consequence.","zh":"這個短語連接原因和後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"drag one’s feet over","meaning":"拖延；遲遲不行動","examples":[{"en":"The car industry is dragging its feet over fully automated vehicles.","zh":"汽車行業在全自動車輛問題上拖延。"},{"en":"To drag one’s feet over something means to delay action or move very slowly on purpose.","zh":"拖延某事，是指故意延遲行動或進展很慢。"},{"en":"A student may drag his feet over revision because he dislikes the subject.","zh":"學生可能因不喜歡某科而拖延溫習。"},{"en":"Companies may delay a change if they fear it will damage their profits.","zh":"如果公司害怕改變會損害利潤，可能會推遲改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reluctant or deliberate delay.","zh":"這個短語描述不情願或故意拖延。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the manufacture and introduction of","meaning":"……的製造和引入","examples":[{"en":"The industry is delaying the manufacture and introduction of automated vehicles.","zh":"業界正在推遲自動化車輛的製造和引入。"},{"en":"The manufacture and introduction of something means making it and bringing it into use or onto the market.","zh":"某物的製造和引入，是指生產它並把它投入使用或投放市場。"},{"en":"The manufacture and introduction of a new vaccine requires testing, approval and distribution.","zh":"新疫苗的製造和引入需要測試、批准和分發。"},{"en":"Delays can happen when companies worry about cost, safety or public reaction.","zh":"當公司擔心成本、安全或公眾反應，延誤可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both production and first use.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋生產和首次使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fully automated vehicles","meaning":"全自動車輛","examples":[{"en":"Fully automated vehicles may threaten private car ownership.","zh":"全自動車輛可能威脅私家車擁有權。"},{"en":"Fully automated vehicles are vehicles that can operate without direct human driving.","zh":"全自動車輛是可以在沒有真人直接駕駛下運作的車輛。"},{"en":"A delivery company may use fully automated vehicles to move packages at night.","zh":"送貨公司可能使用全自動車輛在夜間運送包裹。"},{"en":"If such vehicles become safe and cheap, they may change how people travel.","zh":"如果這類車輛變得安全又便宜，它們可能改變人們出行方式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to vehicles controlled mainly or entirely by automation.","zh":"這個短語指主要或完全由自動化控制的車輛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"onto the market","meaning":"投放市場","examples":[{"en":"Car manufacturers are slow to put fully automated vehicles onto the market.","zh":"汽車製造商遲遲未把全自動車輛投放市場。"},{"en":"To put something onto the market means to make it available for customers to buy or use.","zh":"把某物投放市場，是指讓顧客可以購買或使用它。"},{"en":"A company may test a new phone for months before putting it onto the market.","zh":"公司可能測試新手機數月後才把它投放市場。"},{"en":"Products may be delayed if safety, cost or public trust is uncertain.","zh":"如果安全、成本或公眾信任仍不確定，產品可能被推遲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving a product from development to public sale or use.","zh":"這個短語描述產品由開發階段走向公開銷售或使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"for commercial reasons","meaning":"出於商業原因","examples":[{"en":"The industry is delaying the technology for commercial reasons.","zh":"業界出於商業原因推遲這項技術。"},{"en":"For commercial reasons means because of business interests, profit or market concerns.","zh":"出於商業原因，是指因商業利益、利潤或市場顧慮。"},{"en":"A shop may open later on weekdays for commercial reasons if most customers come in the evening.","zh":"如果大多數顧客晚上才來，商店可能出於商業原因在平日較遲開門。"},{"en":"Companies may delay useful technology if it threatens existing sales.","zh":"如果有用科技威脅現有銷售，公司可能推遲推出。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a decision based on business rather than public benefit alone.","zh":"這個短語解釋基於商業，而不只是公共利益的決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"apart from","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"Apart from the commercial aspect, there is also the issue of safety.","zh":"除了商業層面之外，還有安全問題。"},{"en":"Apart from something means besides or in addition to it.","zh":"除了某事之外，是指除此以外或另外還有。"},{"en":"Apart from homework, students also need time for rest and exercise.","zh":"除了功課之外，學生也需要時間休息和運動。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another factor to the discussion.","zh":"這個短語為討論加入另一因素。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing that one issue is not the only concern.","zh":"當要顯示某議題不是唯一顧慮時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the commercial aspect","meaning":"商業層面","examples":[{"en":"The commercial aspect is not the only concern about driverless cars.","zh":"商業層面並不是無人駕駛汽車的唯一顧慮。"},{"en":"The commercial aspect means the business, profit or market side of an issue.","zh":"商業層面，是某議題的生意、利潤或市場方面。"},{"en":"A school trip has an educational aspect, but the commercial aspect includes transport and ticket costs.","zh":"學校旅行有教育層面，但商業層面包括交通和門票成本。"},{"en":"Focusing only on the commercial aspect may ignore safety, fairness or social impact.","zh":"只關注商業層面可能忽略安全、公平或社會影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the business side of a topic.","zh":"這個短語描述主題的商業方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the issue of safety","meaning":"安全問題","examples":[{"en":"The issue of safety remains important for driverless cars.","zh":"安全問題對無人駕駛汽車仍然重要。"},{"en":"The issue of safety means the question of whether something is safe enough.","zh":"安全問題，是某事是否足夠安全的問題。"},{"en":"Before a new playground opens, the issue of safety must be checked carefully.","zh":"新遊樂場開放前，必須仔細檢查安全問題。"},{"en":"If people worry about safety, they may reject a new technology even if it is convenient.","zh":"如果人們擔心安全，即使新科技很方便，他們也可能拒絕它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces safety as a serious concern.","zh":"這個短語把安全引入為嚴肅顧慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"respond to most eventualities","meaning":"應對大多數可能情況","examples":[{"en":"A fully automated car could respond to most eventualities during a trip.","zh":"全自動汽車可以在旅程中應對大多數可能情況。"},{"en":"To respond to most eventualities means to deal with most possible situations that may happen.","zh":"應對大多數可能情況，是指處理大部分可能發生的情況。"},{"en":"A good teacher prepares extra activities to respond to most eventualities in class.","zh":"好老師會準備額外活動，以應對課堂中的大多數可能情況。"},{"en":"Driverless cars must handle sudden stops, roadworks and unusual driver behaviour.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車必須處理突然停車、道路工程和不尋常司機行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being ready for many possible events.","zh":"這個短語描述為許多可能事件做好準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the course of","meaning":"在……過程中","examples":[{"en":"A driverless car may face unexpected events in the course of a trip.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車可能在旅程過程中遇到意外事件。"},{"en":"In the course of something means during the process or period of it.","zh":"在某事過程中，是指在該事的進行過程或期間。"},{"en":"In the course of a school day, students may attend lessons, eat lunch and join activities.","zh":"在一個上學日過程中，學生可能上課、吃午餐和參加活動。"},{"en":"Problems can appear while an activity is already happening.","zh":"問題可以在活動已經進行時出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes events occurring during a process.","zh":"這個短語描述在過程中發生的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be capable of responding to","meaning":"能夠應對……","examples":[{"en":"A driverless car must be capable of responding to unforeseen events.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車必須能夠應對無法預見的事件。"},{"en":"To be capable of responding to something means to have the ability to react properly to it.","zh":"能夠應對某事，是指有能力對它作出適當反應。"},{"en":"A receptionist must be capable of responding to angry customers calmly.","zh":"接待員必須能夠冷靜應對憤怒顧客。"},{"en":"If a system cannot respond to unexpected problems, it may be unsafe.","zh":"如果系統不能應對意外問題，它可能不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical ability to react.","zh":"這個短語描述實際反應能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"unforeseen events","meaning":"無法預見的事件","examples":[{"en":"Driverless cars may struggle with unforeseen events.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車可能難以應對無法預見的事件。"},{"en":"Unforeseen events are events that were not expected or planned for.","zh":"無法預見的事件，是沒有被預期或計劃到的事件。"},{"en":"A sudden illness before an exam is an unforeseen event for a student.","zh":"考試前突然生病，對學生而言是無法預見的事件。"},{"en":"Unforeseen events create difficulty because people or machines may not have a prepared response.","zh":"無法預見的事件會造成困難，因為人或機器可能沒有預備好的反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unexpected situations.","zh":"這個短語描述意外情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"changes in route","meaning":"路線改變","examples":[{"en":"A driverless car must respond to changes in route.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車必須應對路線改變。"},{"en":"Changes in route are alterations to the planned road or path of travel.","zh":"路線改變，是原定道路或行程路徑的變動。"},{"en":"A bus may face changes in route when a road is closed for repairs.","zh":"當道路因維修關閉，巴士可能面對路線改變。"},{"en":"If a vehicle cannot handle route changes, it may get stuck or choose an unsafe path.","zh":"如果車輛不能處理路線改變，可能會被困或選擇不安全路線。"},{"en":"This phrase describes travel plans being adjusted.","zh":"這個短語描述出行計劃被調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"unexpected diversions","meaning":"突然改道","examples":[{"en":"Unexpected diversions may create problems for driverless cars.","zh":"突然改道可能為無人駕駛汽車造成問題。"},{"en":"Unexpected diversions are sudden changes that force traffic away from the normal route.","zh":"突然改道，是迫使交通離開正常路線的突然變動。"},{"en":"Police may set up an unexpected diversion after a road accident.","zh":"交通意外後，警方可能設置突然改道安排。"},{"en":"Diversions are difficult for automated cars because the road layout may not match stored maps.","zh":"改道對自動化汽車困難，因為道路布局可能與已儲存地圖不符。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unplanned route changes.","zh":"這個短語描述未計劃的路線改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"legislative authorities","meaning":"立法機關；立法當局","examples":[{"en":"Legislative authorities share concerns about the safety of driverless cars.","zh":"立法當局同樣擔心無人駕駛汽車的安全。"},{"en":"Legislative authorities are official bodies or people responsible for making laws.","zh":"立法機關或立法當局，是負責制定法律的官方機構或人士。"},{"en":"Legislative authorities may debate whether electric scooters should be allowed on roads.","zh":"立法當局可能辯論是否應允許電動滑板車在道路上行駛。"},{"en":"If lawmakers are worried about safety, they may delay legal approval.","zh":"如果立法者擔心安全，他們可能推遲法律批准。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to those with power to create or change laws.","zh":"這個短語指有權制定或修改法律的人或機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"share these safety concerns","meaning":"有同樣的安全憂慮","examples":[{"en":"Legislative authorities share these safety concerns.","zh":"立法當局有同樣的安全憂慮。"},{"en":"To share these safety concerns means to have the same worries about safety as others.","zh":"有同樣的安全憂慮，是指與其他人一樣擔心安全問題。"},{"en":"Parents and teachers may share safety concerns about students crossing a busy road.","zh":"父母和老師可能對學生橫過繁忙道路有同樣的安全憂慮。"},{"en":"When many groups share concerns, a project may face stronger restrictions.","zh":"當多個群體有同樣憂慮，項目可能面對更強限制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes common worry about risk.","zh":"這個短語描述對風險的共同擔心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"no matter how much","meaning":"無論有多少……","examples":[{"en":"No matter how much automation a car has, the law still requires a driver.","zh":"無論汽車有多少自動化，法律仍要求有司機。"},{"en":"No matter how much means regardless of the amount or degree.","zh":"無論有多少，是指不管數量或程度如何。"},{"en":"No matter how much a student revises, they still need to read the question carefully.","zh":"無論學生溫習多少，他們仍需要仔細閱讀題目。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one condition remains true even if another factor increases.","zh":"這個短語顯示即使另一因素增加，某條件仍成立。"},{"en":"It is useful for emphasising limits or rules.","zh":"它適合強調限制或規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"automation","meaning":"自動化","examples":[{"en":"Automation does not remove the legal need for a driver.","zh":"自動化不會取消法律上對司機的需要。"},{"en":"Automation means using machines or technology to do tasks with little human control.","zh":"自動化是使用機器或科技在很少人類控制下完成任務。"},{"en":"A supermarket self-checkout is a form of automation.","zh":"超級市場自助付款是一種自動化。"},{"en":"Automation can reduce labour costs, but it may also affect jobs and regulations.","zh":"自動化可以降低人工成本，但也可能影響工作和規例。"},{"en":"This word describes work being done automatically by systems.","zh":"這個詞描述工作由系統自動完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a full licence","meaning":"正式駕駛執照","examples":[{"en":"The law requires a driver with a full licence.","zh":"法律要求司機持有正式駕駛執照。"},{"en":"A full licence is an official driving licence that allows a person to drive legally without learner restrictions.","zh":"正式駕駛執照是官方駕駛執照，容許人在沒有學牌限制下合法駕駛。"},{"en":"A learner driver may need supervision, but a person with a full licence can drive alone.","zh":"學車司機可能需要監督，但持有正式駕駛執照的人可以獨自駕駛。"},{"en":"Requiring a full licence ensures that a trained person is legally responsible for the vehicle.","zh":"要求正式駕駛執照，可確保有受訓人士依法負責車輛。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to complete legal permission to drive.","zh":"這個短語指完整合法駕駛許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"behind the wheel","meaning":"坐在駕駛席上","examples":[{"en":"The law still requires a licensed driver behind the wheel.","zh":"法律仍要求有持牌司機坐在駕駛席上。"},{"en":"Behind the wheel means sitting in the driver’s seat and controlling or ready to control a vehicle.","zh":"坐在駕駛席上，是指坐在司機位置並控制或準備控制車輛。"},{"en":"A person should not use a phone while behind the wheel.","zh":"人在駕駛席上時不應使用手機。"},{"en":"If the law requires someone behind the wheel, the car is not treated as fully driverless.","zh":"如果法律要求有人坐在駕駛席上，汽車就不被視為完全無人駕駛。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the driver’s position in a vehicle.","zh":"這個短語指車輛中的司機位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"public roads","meaning":"公共道路","examples":[{"en":"Fully automated cars cannot travel legally on public roads without a driver.","zh":"全自動汽車沒有司機便不能合法在公共道路上行駛。"},{"en":"Public roads are roads open for ordinary people and vehicles to use.","zh":"公共道路是開放給一般人和車輛使用的道路。"},{"en":"A company may test a vehicle on private land before using it on public roads.","zh":"公司可能先在私人土地測試車輛，然後才在公共道路上使用。"},{"en":"Rules for public roads are stricter because many different road users are involved.","zh":"公共道路規則較嚴格，因為涉及許多不同道路使用者。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to shared roads governed by traffic laws.","zh":"這個短語指受交通法例管制的共用道路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"robot drivers","meaning":"機械人司機","examples":[{"en":"Robot drivers may generally be safer than human drivers.","zh":"機械人司機一般可能比人類司機更安全。"},{"en":"Robot drivers are automated systems that control vehicles instead of human beings.","zh":"機械人司機是代替人類控制車輛的自動化系統。"},{"en":"A robot driver does not get tired, angry or distracted by a phone.","zh":"機械人司機不會疲倦、憤怒或被手機分心。"},{"en":"However, robot drivers must still be tested for unusual road situations.","zh":"然而，機械人司機仍必須接受不尋常道路情況測試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes machine-based driving control.","zh":"這個短語描述以機器為基礎的駕駛控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on the whole","meaning":"整體而言","examples":[{"en":"On the whole, robot drivers are generally safer than human drivers.","zh":"整體而言，機械人司機一般比人類司機更安全。"},{"en":"On the whole means generally, when considering everything together.","zh":"整體而言，是指把所有事情一起考慮時，大致上如此。"},{"en":"On the whole, the school trip was successful, although the bus was late.","zh":"整體而言，學校旅行很成功，雖然巴士遲到。"},{"en":"This phrase allows for exceptions while giving an overall judgement.","zh":"這個短語容許例外，同時給出整體判斷。"},{"en":"It is useful when summarising a broad pattern.","zh":"它適合總結廣泛模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"human counterparts","meaning":"對應的人類司機","examples":[{"en":"Robot drivers may be safer than their human counterparts.","zh":"機械人司機可能比對應的人類司機更安全。"},{"en":"Human counterparts are people who perform the same role as a machine, group or person being compared.","zh":"對應的人類，是指與被比較的機器、群體或人物執行相同角色的人。"},{"en":"Online tutors may be compared with their human counterparts in face-to-face classrooms.","zh":"網上導師可能與面對面課室中的對應真人導師比較。"},{"en":"Comparing robot drivers with human counterparts helps discuss safety and reliability.","zh":"比較機械人司機與對應人類司機，有助討論安全和可靠性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the human equivalent of something.","zh":"這個短語指某事物的人類對應者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"does not guarantee that","meaning":"並不保證","examples":[{"en":"Greater safety does not guarantee that driverless cars will become legal.","zh":"更高安全性並不保證無人駕駛汽車會變成合法。"},{"en":"Does not guarantee that means does not make a result certain.","zh":"並不保證，是指不會令某結果必然發生。"},{"en":"Studying hard does not guarantee that a student will get full marks.","zh":"努力溫習並不保證學生會取得滿分。"},{"en":"Even if a technology is safer, laws and public trust may still delay it.","zh":"即使某科技較安全，法律和公眾信任仍可能延遲它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one positive factor is not enough to ensure an outcome.","zh":"這個短語顯示單一正面因素不足以確保結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"become legal","meaning":"變成合法","examples":[{"en":"Driverless cars may not quickly become legal.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車未必很快變成合法。"},{"en":"To become legal means to be allowed by law.","zh":"變成合法，是指被法律允許。"},{"en":"A new type of electric scooter may become legal only after road-safety rules are written.","zh":"新型電動滑板車可能要等道路安全規則制定後才變成合法。"},{"en":"Technology can exist before it becomes legal for public use.","zh":"科技可以先存在，然後才變成可供公眾使用的合法事物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change in legal permission.","zh":"這個短語描述法律許可上的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as someone put it","meaning":"正如某人所說","examples":[{"en":"As a consortium of researchers put it, fewer deaths might still mean many lawsuits.","zh":"正如一個研究人員聯盟所說，死亡人數較少仍可能意味着很多訴訟。"},{"en":"As someone put it means as someone expressed or described the idea.","zh":"正如某人所說，是指按照某人表達或描述該想法的方式。"},{"en":"As my teacher put it, grammar is a tool, not a punishment.","zh":"正如我的老師所說，文法是工具，不是懲罰。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces another person’s wording or summary.","zh":"這個短語引入另一人的用語或總結。"},{"en":"It is useful when quoting or paraphrasing a clear comment.","zh":"它適合引用或轉述清楚評論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"consortium of researchers","meaning":"研究人員聯盟","examples":[{"en":"A consortium of researchers commented on the legal risks of driverless cars.","zh":"一個研究人員聯盟評論了無人駕駛汽車的法律風險。"},{"en":"A consortium of researchers is a group of researchers working together on a shared issue.","zh":"研究人員聯盟是一群研究人員為共同議題而合作的組織。"},{"en":"A consortium of universities may study climate change across several countries.","zh":"大學聯盟可能跨幾個國家研究氣候變化。"},{"en":"Researchers may form a consortium when one institution alone cannot cover the whole problem.","zh":"當單一機構無法涵蓋整個問題時，研究人員可能組成聯盟。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a cooperative research group.","zh":"這個短語描述合作研究群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cut something in half","meaning":"將某事減半","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving cars could cut traffic fatalities in half.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車可以將交通死亡人數減半。"},{"en":"To cut something in half means to reduce it by 50%.","zh":"將某事減半，是指把它減少百分之五十。"},{"en":"A shop may cut delivery time in half by opening a warehouse nearby.","zh":"商店可以透過在附近開設倉庫，將送貨時間減半。"},{"en":"If road deaths are cut in half, many lives would be saved.","zh":"如果道路死亡人數減半，許多生命將被挽救。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large reduction to half the original amount.","zh":"這個短語描述大幅減少至原來一半。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"roughly","meaning":"大約","examples":[{"en":"There are roughly 40,000 annual traffic fatalities in the United States.","zh":"美國每年大約有四萬宗交通死亡。"},{"en":"Roughly means approximately, not exactly.","zh":"大約，是指近似，而不是完全準確。"},{"en":"It takes roughly twenty minutes to walk from my home to school.","zh":"從我家步行到學校大約需要二十分鐘。"},{"en":"Writers use “roughly” when an exact number is not necessary or not certain.","zh":"當準確數字不必要或不確定時，作者會使用 roughly。"},{"en":"This word signals an approximate figure.","zh":"這個詞表示近似數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"annual traffic fatalities","meaning":"每年交通死亡人數","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving cars might reduce annual traffic fatalities.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車可能減少每年交通死亡人數。"},{"en":"Annual traffic fatalities are the number of people killed in road accidents each year.","zh":"每年交通死亡人數，是每年在道路意外中死亡的人數。"},{"en":"A government may study annual traffic fatalities to decide where to improve road safety.","zh":"政府可能研究每年交通死亡人數，以決定在哪裡改善道路安全。"},{"en":"Reducing these deaths is a major reason for developing safer vehicle technology.","zh":"減少這些死亡是發展更安全車輛技術的主要原因。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to yearly road-death figures.","zh":"這個短語指每年的道路死亡數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"car makers","meaning":"汽車製造商","examples":[{"en":"Car makers may face lawsuits after driverless-car accidents.","zh":"汽車製造商可能在無人駕駛汽車意外後面對訴訟。"},{"en":"Car makers are companies that design and manufacture cars.","zh":"汽車製造商是設計和製造汽車的公司。"},{"en":"Car makers test new models before selling them to the public.","zh":"汽車製造商在向公眾出售新車型前會進行測試。"},{"en":"If an automated car crashes, people may blame the company that made it.","zh":"如果自動化汽車發生意外，人們可能責怪製造它的公司。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to automobile manufacturers.","zh":"這個短語指汽車生產商。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"thank-you notes","meaning":"感謝信","examples":[{"en":"Car makers might receive lawsuits rather than thank-you notes.","zh":"汽車製造商可能收到訴訟，而不是感謝信。"},{"en":"Thank-you notes are written messages expressing gratitude.","zh":"感謝信是表達感激的書面訊息。"},{"en":"A patient may send thank-you notes to nurses after receiving good care.","zh":"病人接受良好照顧後，可能向護士寄感謝信。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts gratitude with blame: companies may be sued even if deaths decrease.","zh":"這個短語把感激與責備作對比：即使死亡減少，公司也可能被起訴。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to messages of appreciation.","zh":"這個短語指表達欣賞的訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lawsuits","meaning":"訴訟","examples":[{"en":"Car makers could face lawsuits after accidents involving self-driving cars.","zh":"汽車製造商可能在涉及自動駕駛汽車的意外後面對訴訟。"},{"en":"Lawsuits are legal cases brought to court by people or organisations.","zh":"訴訟是由個人或機構帶到法庭的法律案件。"},{"en":"A customer may file a lawsuit if a company sells a dangerous product.","zh":"如果公司出售危險產品，顧客可能提出訴訟。"},{"en":"Fear of lawsuits can make companies cautious about releasing new technology.","zh":"對訴訟的恐懼可以令公司謹慎推出新科技。"},{"en":"This word refers to formal legal action.","zh":"這個詞指正式法律行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"undertake a hiring campaign","meaning":"展開招聘行動","examples":[{"en":"Uber is undertaking an aggressive hiring campaign for taxi drivers.","zh":"Uber 正在為的士司機展開積極招聘行動。"},{"en":"To undertake a hiring campaign means to actively start a planned effort to recruit workers.","zh":"展開招聘行動，是指主動開始有計劃地招募工人。"},{"en":"A hospital may undertake a hiring campaign when it lacks enough nurses.","zh":"醫院缺乏足夠護士時，可能展開招聘行動。"},{"en":"Hiring campaigns show that an organisation still needs human workers for current demand.","zh":"招聘行動顯示機構目前仍需要人類工人來滿足需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised recruitment.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的招聘。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"aggressive hiring campaign","meaning":"積極的招聘行動","examples":[{"en":"Uber is undertaking an aggressive hiring campaign for taxi drivers.","zh":"Uber 正在為的士司機展開積極的招聘行動。"},{"en":"An aggressive hiring campaign is a strong and active effort to recruit many workers quickly.","zh":"積極的招聘行動，是強而主動地快速招募大量工人的努力。"},{"en":"A new restaurant chain may launch an aggressive hiring campaign before opening ten branches.","zh":"新餐廳連鎖店在開設十間分店前，可能展開積極招聘行動。"},{"en":"Such a campaign suggests the company has high demand or urgent staffing needs.","zh":"這種行動暗示公司需求高或人手需要迫切。"},{"en":"This phrase describes energetic, large-scale recruitment.","zh":"這個短語描述有力而大規模的招聘。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"meet the demand for","meaning":"滿足對……的需求","examples":[{"en":"Uber is hiring drivers to meet the demand for its taxi app.","zh":"Uber 正在聘請司機，以滿足對其叫車應用程式的需求。"},{"en":"To meet the demand for something means to provide enough supply for what people want or need.","zh":"滿足對某物的需求，是指提供足夠供應，以應付人們想要或需要的東西。"},{"en":"A bakery may hire more staff to meet the demand for mooncakes before Mid-Autumn Festival.","zh":"麵包店可能在中秋節前聘請更多員工，以滿足對月餅的需求。"},{"en":"If demand grows faster than supply, customers may wait longer.","zh":"如果需求增長快於供應，顧客可能等更久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes satisfying customer or public need.","zh":"這個短語描述滿足顧客或公眾需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"less than confident that","meaning":"對……並非十分有信心","examples":[{"en":"Uber seems less than confident that driverless taxis will soon become a reality.","zh":"Uber 似乎對無人駕駛的士很快成為現實並非十分有信心。"},{"en":"Less than confident that means not fully sure or not very confident about something.","zh":"對某事並非十分有信心，是指不完全肯定或不是很有信心。"},{"en":"A student may be less than confident that they passed after finding the exam difficult.","zh":"學生覺得考試困難後，可能對自己是否合格並非十分有信心。"},{"en":"If a company still hires many drivers, it may not fully trust that automation is ready.","zh":"如果公司仍聘請大量司機，它可能並不完全相信自動化已準備好。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests doubt or hesitation.","zh":"這個短語暗示懷疑或猶豫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"whether…or…","meaning":"無論是……還是……","examples":[{"en":"Whether Uber is pursuing a doomed venture or introducing a popular technology depends on your viewpoint.","zh":"Uber 無論是在推行注定失敗的項目，還是在引入受歡迎科技，都取決於你的觀點。"},{"en":"Whether A or B presents two possible alternatives without choosing between them.","zh":"whether A or B 提出兩個可能選項，而不直接選其中一個。"},{"en":"Whether a student studies online or in person depends on their needs and schedule.","zh":"學生無論是網上學習還是面授學習，都取決於他們的需要和時間表。"},{"en":"This structure is useful when different people may see the same situation differently.","zh":"當不同人可能以不同方式看待同一情況時，這個結構很有用。"},{"en":"It introduces a balanced comparison between two possibilities.","zh":"它引入兩種可能性之間的平衡比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pursue a doomed venture","meaning":"推行注定失敗的項目","examples":[{"en":"Uber may be pursuing a doomed venture.","zh":"Uber 可能正在推行注定失敗的項目。"},{"en":"To pursue a doomed venture means to continue a project that is likely to fail.","zh":"推行注定失敗的項目，是指繼續進行很可能失敗的計劃。"},{"en":"A shop may pursue a doomed venture if it opens in an area with no customers.","zh":"如果商店開在沒有顧客的地區，它可能是在推行注定失敗的項目。"},{"en":"People may call a project doomed when costs are high and success seems unlikely.","zh":"當成本高而成功看似不可能，人們可能稱項目注定失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a risky effort expected to end badly.","zh":"這個短語描述預期結局不好的冒險努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be about to","meaning":"即將","examples":[{"en":"Uber may be about to introduce a major new technology.","zh":"Uber 可能即將引入一項重大新科技。"},{"en":"To be about to do something means to be going to do it very soon.","zh":"即將做某事，是指很快就會做該事。"},{"en":"The teacher is about to start the test, so students should put away their notes.","zh":"老師即將開始測驗，所以學生應收起筆記。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the action is close, not distant in the future.","zh":"這個短語暗示行動很接近，而不是遙遠未來。"},{"en":"It is useful when something is expected to happen almost immediately.","zh":"當某事預期幾乎立即發生時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"universally welcomed","meaning":"受到普遍歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The technology may or may not be universally welcomed.","zh":"這項技術可能會，也可能不會受到普遍歡迎。"},{"en":"Universally welcomed means accepted or supported by everyone or almost everyone.","zh":"受到普遍歡迎，是指被所有人或幾乎所有人接受或支持。"},{"en":"Free school meals might be widely welcomed, but not every policy is universally welcomed.","zh":"免費學校午餐可能廣受歡迎，但不是每項政策都受到普遍歡迎。"},{"en":"New technology may please users while worrying workers or regulators.","zh":"新科技可能令用戶高興，同時令工人或監管者擔心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad public acceptance.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛公眾接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"depend entirely on","meaning":"完全取決於……","examples":[{"en":"The judgement depends entirely on your viewpoint.","zh":"判斷完全取決於你的觀點。"},{"en":"To depend entirely on something means to be completely decided by it.","zh":"完全取決於某事，是指完全由它決定。"},{"en":"Whether online classes are convenient may depend entirely on a student’s home environment.","zh":"網上課堂是否方便，可能完全取決於學生的家居環境。"},{"en":"If judgement depends on viewpoint, different people can reach different conclusions.","zh":"如果判斷取決於觀點，不同人可以得出不同結論。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor fully controls the answer.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個因素完全控制答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"viewpoint","meaning":"觀點；看法","examples":[{"en":"People have different viewpoints on driverless cars.","zh":"人們對無人駕駛汽車有不同觀點。"},{"en":"A viewpoint is a person’s opinion or way of looking at an issue.","zh":"觀點是某人對議題的意見或看法。"},{"en":"A parent and a teenager may have different viewpoints on phone use at night.","zh":"父母和青少年對晚上使用手機可能有不同觀點。"},{"en":"Viewpoints can differ because people have different jobs, risks and values.","zh":"觀點會不同，因為人們有不同工作、風險和價值觀。"},{"en":"This word describes perspective or opinion.","zh":"這個詞描述角度或意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"attitude towards","meaning":"對……的態度","examples":[{"en":"John Reynolds is angry at Uber’s attitude towards automated technology.","zh":"John Reynolds 對 Uber 對自動化技術的態度感到憤怒。"},{"en":"Attitude towards something means the way someone thinks or feels about it.","zh":"對某事的態度，是某人對它的想法或感受。"},{"en":"A student’s attitude towards homework affects how carefully they complete it.","zh":"學生對功課的態度會影響他們完成得有多仔細。"},{"en":"A negative attitude can lead to criticism, resistance or anger.","zh":"負面態度可以導致批評、抗拒或憤怒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone’s position or feeling about an issue.","zh":"這個短語描述某人對議題的立場或感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fully automated technology","meaning":"全自動技術","examples":[{"en":"John Reynolds criticises Uber’s support for fully automated technology.","zh":"John Reynolds 批評 Uber 支持全自動技術。"},{"en":"Fully automated technology is technology that can perform tasks with little or no human control.","zh":"全自動技術是可以在很少或沒有人工控制下執行任務的科技。"},{"en":"A fully automated checkout can scan products and take payment without a cashier.","zh":"全自動收銀機可以在沒有收銀員下掃描商品和收款。"},{"en":"Fully automated technology may increase efficiency but reduce some jobs.","zh":"全自動技術可能提高效率，但減少某些工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes technology that works almost entirely by itself.","zh":"這個短語描述幾乎完全自行運作的科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"completely disregard","meaning":"完全漠視","examples":[{"en":"John believes Uber is completely disregarding individual livelihoods.","zh":"John 認為 Uber 正完全漠視個人生計。"},{"en":"To completely disregard something means to ignore it totally and not consider its importance.","zh":"完全漠視某事，是指完全忽視它，不考慮其重要性。"},{"en":"A manager completely disregards staff wellbeing if workers are forced to skip every break.","zh":"如果經理強迫員工每次休息都取消，就是完全漠視員工福祉。"},{"en":"If a company disregards livelihoods, affected workers may feel angry and betrayed.","zh":"如果公司漠視生計，受影響工人可能感到憤怒和被背叛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes total lack of concern.","zh":"這個短語描述完全缺乏關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"individual livelihoods","meaning":"個人生計","examples":[{"en":"Driverless taxis may threaten individual livelihoods.","zh":"無人駕駛的士可能威脅個人生計。"},{"en":"Individual livelihoods are the ways individual people earn money to support themselves and their families.","zh":"個人生計是個人賺錢養活自己和家人的方式。"},{"en":"A market closure may threaten the livelihoods of small stall owners.","zh":"市集關閉可能威脅小攤檔檔主的生計。"},{"en":"When technology replaces workers, individual livelihoods can be damaged even if customers benefit.","zh":"當科技取代工人，即使顧客受益，個人生計也可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to real people’s income and survival.","zh":"這個短語指真人的收入和生活維持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"such as mine","meaning":"例如我的","examples":[{"en":"John worries about individual livelihoods such as mine.","zh":"John 擔心例如我這樣的個人生計。"},{"en":"Such as mine means like my own example or situation.","zh":"例如我的，是指像我自己的例子或情況。"},{"en":"A small shopkeeper may say that rising rent harms businesses such as mine.","zh":"小店主可能說，租金上升傷害例如我這樣的生意。"},{"en":"This phrase personalises a general issue by connecting it to the speaker.","zh":"這個短語把一般議題與說話者連接，使它變得個人化。"},{"en":"It means the speaker belongs to the group being discussed.","zh":"它表示說話者屬於正在討論的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as well as those of","meaning":"以及……的","examples":[{"en":"John worries about taxi drivers as well as those of car manufacturers.","zh":"John 擔心的士司機，以及汽車製造商的生計。"},{"en":"As well as those of means and also the ones belonging to another group.","zh":"以及某群體的，是指也包括屬於另一群體的那些。"},{"en":"A policy may affect students’ schedules as well as those of teachers.","zh":"一項政策可能影響學生的時間表，以及老師的時間表。"},{"en":"This phrase helps include two groups without repeating the same noun.","zh":"這個短語幫助包含兩個群體，而不用重複同一名詞。"},{"en":"It shows that the concern extends beyond the first group mentioned.","zh":"它顯示顧慮不只限於第一個提及的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"big car manufacturers","meaning":"大型汽車製造商","examples":[{"en":"Driverless cars may affect big car manufacturers.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車可能影響大型汽車製造商。"},{"en":"Big car manufacturers are large companies that produce cars on a major scale.","zh":"大型汽車製造商是大規模生產汽車的大公司。"},{"en":"Big car manufacturers may invest millions in factories, workers and new models.","zh":"大型汽車製造商可能在工廠、工人和新車型上投資數百萬。"},{"en":"If private car ownership falls, large manufacturers may sell fewer vehicles.","zh":"如果私家車擁有率下降，大型製造商可能賣出較少車輛。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to major companies in the car industry.","zh":"這個短語指汽車行業中的大型公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in the pursuit of money","meaning":"為了追求金錢","examples":[{"en":"John says Uber is acting in the pursuit of money.","zh":"John 說 Uber 是為了追求金錢而行動。"},{"en":"In the pursuit of money means trying to gain profit or financial reward.","zh":"為了追求金錢，是指試圖獲得利潤或財務回報。"},{"en":"A company may cut customer service in the pursuit of money.","zh":"公司可能為了追求金錢而削減客戶服務。"},{"en":"If profit is pursued without safeguards, workers or customers may be harmed.","zh":"如果在沒有保障下追求利潤，工人或顧客可能受害。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound critical because it suggests money is being valued too much.","zh":"這個短語可能帶批評意味，因為它暗示金錢被過度重視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"admittedly","meaning":"誠然","examples":[{"en":"Admittedly, things change and workers must adapt.","zh":"誠然，事情會改變，工人必須適應。"},{"en":"Admittedly means used to accept that something is true before making another point.","zh":"誠然，是用來承認某事為真，然後再提出另一點。"},{"en":"Admittedly, online lessons are convenient, but some students still need face-to-face help.","zh":"誠然，網上課堂很方便，但有些學生仍需要面對面幫助。"},{"en":"This word helps make an argument sound fair and balanced.","zh":"這個詞令論點聽起來公平而平衡。"},{"en":"It introduces a concession before a contrast or qualification.","zh":"它在對比或修正前引入讓步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"roll with the times","meaning":"與時並進","examples":[{"en":"John accepts that people have to roll with the times.","zh":"John 接受人們必須與時並進。"},{"en":"To roll with the times means to adapt to changes in society, technology or habits.","zh":"與時並進，是指適應社會、科技或習慣的變化。"},{"en":"A teacher rolls with the times by learning how to use online homework platforms.","zh":"老師學會使用網上功課平台，就是與時並進。"},{"en":"People who refuse to adapt may find it harder to keep their jobs or businesses.","zh":"拒絕適應的人可能較難保住工作或生意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical acceptance of change.","zh":"這個短語描述對改變的實際接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"safeguards in place","meaning":"已設立的保障措施","examples":[{"en":"There should be safeguards in place to protect affected workers.","zh":"應有已設立的保障措施來保護受影響工人。"},{"en":"Safeguards in place are protective rules, systems or measures already arranged.","zh":"已設立的保障措施，是已安排好的保護規則、系統或措施。"},{"en":"A school trip needs safeguards in place, such as teacher supervision and emergency contacts.","zh":"學校旅行需要已設立的保障措施，例如老師監督和緊急聯絡。"},{"en":"Safeguards reduce harm when a new policy or technology creates risk.","zh":"當新政策或科技帶來風險時，保障措施可以減少傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protection prepared before problems happen.","zh":"這個短語描述問題發生前已準備的保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"protect those potentially affected by","meaning":"保護可能受……影響的人","examples":[{"en":"New policies should protect those potentially affected by new technologies.","zh":"新政策應保護可能受新技術影響的人。"},{"en":"To protect those potentially affected by something means to safeguard people who may be harmed by it.","zh":"保護可能受某事影響的人，是指保障可能因它受害的人。"},{"en":"A school should protect students potentially affected by a timetable change.","zh":"學校應保護可能受時間表改變影響的學生。"},{"en":"If new technology removes jobs, retraining and financial support may protect workers.","zh":"如果新科技取代工作，再培訓和財政支援可以保護工人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes caring for people at risk from a change.","zh":"這個短語描述照顧因變化而面臨風險的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the introduction of new technologies","meaning":"新技術的引入","examples":[{"en":"The introduction of new technologies can affect workers.","zh":"新技術的引入可以影響工人。"},{"en":"The introduction of new technologies means bringing new tools or systems into use.","zh":"新技術的引入，是把新工具或系統帶入使用。"},{"en":"The introduction of online payment changed how many small shops handle money.","zh":"網上付款的引入改變了許多小商店處理金錢的方式。"},{"en":"New technologies can improve efficiency while also changing the skills workers need.","zh":"新技術可以提高效率，同時改變工人所需技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes new technology entering daily or business life.","zh":"這個短語描述新科技進入日常或商業生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"I guess I’m biased","meaning":"我想我是有偏見的","examples":[{"en":"John says, “I guess I’m biased, being a taxi driver myself.”","zh":"John 說：「我想我是有偏見的，因為我自己也是的士司機。」"},{"en":"I guess I’m biased means I think my opinion may be influenced by my own situation.","zh":"我想我是有偏見的，是指我認為自己的意見可能受到自身情況影響。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “I guess I’m biased,” when praising the school where they work.","zh":"老師讚揚自己任教的學校時，可能說：「我想我是有偏見的。」"},{"en":"Admitting bias can make a speaker sound more honest and self-aware.","zh":"承認偏見可以令說話者聽起來更誠實和有自知之明。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the speaker may not be completely neutral.","zh":"這個短語顯示說話者可能並非完全中立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"being a taxi driver myself","meaning":"因為我自己也是的士司機","examples":[{"en":"Being a taxi driver myself, I find the issue difficult to judge objectively.","zh":"因為我自己也是的士司機，我覺得很難客觀判斷這個問題。"},{"en":"Being a taxi driver myself means because I personally work as a taxi driver.","zh":"因為我自己也是的士司機，是指因為我本人從事的士司機工作。"},{"en":"Being a parent myself, I understand why parents worry about school safety.","zh":"因為我自己也是父母，我理解父母為何擔心學校安全。"},{"en":"Personal experience can make an issue feel more important and emotional.","zh":"個人經驗可以令議題感覺更重要和更情緒化。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why the speaker’s view may be personally affected.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何說話者的看法可能受個人身份影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"see it objectively","meaning":"客觀地看待它","examples":[{"en":"John finds it difficult to see the issue objectively.","zh":"John 覺得很難客觀地看待這個問題。"},{"en":"To see it objectively means to judge it fairly without being controlled by personal feelings.","zh":"客觀地看待某事，是指公平判斷它，而不被個人感受控制。"},{"en":"A student may find it hard to see a teacher’s criticism objectively if they feel embarrassed.","zh":"如果學生感到尷尬，可能很難客觀地看待老師的批評。"},{"en":"Personal interest can make objective judgement more difficult.","zh":"個人利益可以令客觀判斷更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fair and neutral evaluation.","zh":"這個短語描述公平而中立的評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"resident of","meaning":"……的居民","examples":[{"en":"Susie Greenacre is a resident of Pittsburgh.","zh":"Susie Greenacre 是匹茲堡的居民。"},{"en":"A resident of a place is someone who lives there.","zh":"某地的居民，是住在那裡的人。"},{"en":"A resident of a housing estate may attend meetings about building repairs.","zh":"屋苑居民可能參加關於大廈維修的會議。"},{"en":"Residents often care about local transport because it affects their daily lives.","zh":"居民通常關心本地交通，因為它影響日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where a person lives.","zh":"這個短語指出某人居住在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have no such reservations about","meaning":"對……沒有這些顧慮","examples":[{"en":"Susie has no such reservations about driverless cars.","zh":"Susie 對無人駕駛汽車沒有這些顧慮。"},{"en":"To have no such reservations about something means not to share the doubts or concerns mentioned earlier.","zh":"對某事沒有這些顧慮，是指不具有前面提到的懷疑或擔心。"},{"en":"Some parents worry about online classes, but others have no such reservations.","zh":"有些父母擔心網上課堂，但其他父母沒有這些顧慮。"},{"en":"If someone has no reservations, they are more likely to support the idea quickly.","zh":"如果某人沒有顧慮，他們更可能很快支持該想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes absence of hesitation or concern.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有猶豫或擔心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reservations about","meaning":"對……的保留；顧慮","examples":[{"en":"Some people have reservations about driverless cars.","zh":"有些人對無人駕駛汽車有顧慮。"},{"en":"Reservations about something are doubts or concerns that prevent full support.","zh":"對某事的顧慮，是阻止完全支持的懷疑或擔心。"},{"en":"A parent may have reservations about a school trip if safety plans are unclear.","zh":"如果安全計劃不清楚，父母可能對學校旅行有顧慮。"},{"en":"People may support an idea generally but still have reservations about cost or risk.","zh":"人們可能大致支持某想法，但仍對成本或風險有保留。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cautious doubt.","zh":"這個短語描述謹慎懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"I’m all for it","meaning":"我完全支持","examples":[{"en":"Susie says she is all for driverless cars.","zh":"Susie 說她完全支持無人駕駛汽車。"},{"en":"I’m all for it means I completely support the idea.","zh":"我完全支持，是指我完全贊成這個想法。"},{"en":"If the school wants to reduce unnecessary homework, many students may say, “I’m all for it.”","zh":"如果學校想減少不必要功課，許多學生可能說：「我完全支持。」"},{"en":"This phrase sounds enthusiastic and informal.","zh":"這個短語聽起來熱情而非正式。"},{"en":"It shows strong approval rather than mild agreement.","zh":"它顯示強烈支持，而不是輕微同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have someone’s backing","meaning":"得到某人的支持","examples":[{"en":"Driverless cars have Susie’s backing.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車得到 Susie 的支持。"},{"en":"To have someone’s backing means to have that person’s support.","zh":"得到某人的支持，是指有該人的贊成或支持。"},{"en":"A student council proposal may have the principal’s backing if it helps the whole school.","zh":"如果學生會提案有助全校，它可能得到校長支持。"},{"en":"Support from local residents can make a transport project easier to accept.","zh":"得到本地居民支持，可以令交通項目較容易被接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes approval or support from someone.","zh":"這個短語描述得到某人的認可或支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"any day","meaning":"隨時；無論何時都","examples":[{"en":"Susie would support driverless cars any day.","zh":"Susie 任何時候都會支持無人駕駛汽車。"},{"en":"Any day means without hesitation, whenever the choice is offered.","zh":"any day 是指毫不猶豫，只要有選擇就會如此。"},{"en":"I would choose a quiet library over a noisy café any day.","zh":"我隨時都會選安靜圖書館，而不是嘈雜咖啡店。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong preference and confidence.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈偏好和信心。"},{"en":"It is informal and often used to emphasise enthusiastic agreement.","zh":"它較非正式，常用來強調熱切同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rush-hour traffic","meaning":"繁忙時間交通","examples":[{"en":"Susie hates the stress of rush-hour traffic.","zh":"Susie 討厭繁忙時間交通帶來的壓力。"},{"en":"Rush-hour traffic is heavy traffic during the busiest travel times of the day.","zh":"繁忙時間交通，是一天中出行最繁忙時段的擠塞交通。"},{"en":"Office workers often face rush-hour traffic when travelling home after work.","zh":"辦公室員工下班回家時通常面對繁忙時間交通。"},{"en":"Heavy traffic can make commuting slow, stressful and tiring.","zh":"擠塞交通可以令通勤變得緩慢、有壓力和疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to traffic congestion during peak hours.","zh":"這個短語指高峰時段的交通擠塞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"hop in","meaning":"跳上；坐進","examples":[{"en":"Susie would like to hop in a driverless car.","zh":"Susie 想坐進一輛無人駕駛汽車。"},{"en":"To hop in means to get into a vehicle quickly or casually.","zh":"hop in 是指快速或隨意地坐進交通工具。"},{"en":"A parent may tell a child to hop in the car before it starts raining.","zh":"下雨前，父母可能叫孩子快點上車。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests convenience because the person can enter and go easily.","zh":"這個短語暗示方便，因為人可以輕鬆上車出發。"},{"en":"It is informal and common in everyday speech.","zh":"它較非正式，常見於日常口語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take someone anywhere","meaning":"載某人到任何地方","examples":[{"en":"A driverless car could take Susie anywhere she wanted.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車可以載 Susie 到任何她想去的地方。"},{"en":"To take someone anywhere means to transport that person to any place they choose.","zh":"載某人到任何地方，是指把那人送到他們選擇的任何地點。"},{"en":"A reliable taxi service can take an elderly person anywhere they need to go.","zh":"可靠的士服務可以載長者到任何他們需要去的地方。"},{"en":"Flexible transport gives people more freedom and reduces the need to drive themselves.","zh":"靈活交通給人更多自由，並減少自己駕駛的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes convenient personal transport.","zh":"這個短語描述方便的個人交通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"never want to drive again","meaning":"再也不想駕駛","examples":[{"en":"Susie says she would never want to drive again.","zh":"Susie 說她再也不想駕駛。"},{"en":"To never want to drive again means to strongly prefer not to drive at any future time.","zh":"再也不想駕駛，是指強烈不希望將來再開車。"},{"en":"After a stressful accident, a person may feel they never want to drive again.","zh":"經歷壓力大的意外後，一個人可能覺得再也不想駕駛。"},{"en":"If driverless cars are comfortable and reliable, some people may happily give up driving.","zh":"如果無人駕駛汽車舒適可靠，有些人可能樂意放棄駕駛。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a strong rejection of driving.","zh":"這個短語顯示對駕駛的強烈拒絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be inclined to agree with","meaning":"傾向同意……","examples":[{"en":"Jason Steiner is inclined to agree with Susie.","zh":"Jason Steiner 傾向同意 Susie。"},{"en":"To be inclined to agree with someone means to tend to support their view, though perhaps not completely.","zh":"傾向同意某人，是指較傾向支持其看法，但可能不是完全同意。"},{"en":"A student may be inclined to agree with a classmate after hearing a strong argument.","zh":"學生聽到同學有力論點後，可能傾向同意對方。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests cautious agreement rather than total certainty.","zh":"這個短語暗示謹慎同意，而不是完全肯定。"},{"en":"It describes leaning towards another person’s opinion.","zh":"它描述偏向另一人的意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"not averse to","meaning":"不反對；並不討厭","examples":[{"en":"Jason is not averse to driving.","zh":"Jason 並不討厭駕駛。"},{"en":"Not averse to something means not against it or not unwilling to do it.","zh":"不反對某事，是指不抗拒或不不願意做它。"},{"en":"I am not averse to working on Saturday if the project is urgent.","zh":"如果項目緊急，我不反對星期六工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is softer than saying someone likes something very much.","zh":"這個短語比說某人非常喜歡某事更溫和。"},{"en":"It means the person can accept the activity.","zh":"它表示這個人可以接受該活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"swap something for something","meaning":"用……換取……","examples":[{"en":"Jason would swap the daily commute for a driverless journey.","zh":"Jason 會用每日通勤換取無人駕駛旅程。"},{"en":"To swap something for something means to exchange one thing for another.","zh":"用某物換取某物，是指以一件事交換另一件事。"},{"en":"A student may swap a sugary drink for water to become healthier.","zh":"學生可能用含糖飲品換取清水，以變得更健康。"},{"en":"People may swap an old habit for a better one if the new option reduces stress.","zh":"如果新選擇能減少壓力，人們可能用舊習慣換取更好習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes replacing one choice with another.","zh":"這個短語描述以一個選擇取代另一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"stressful daily commute","meaning":"壓力大的日常通勤","examples":[{"en":"Jason dislikes the stressful daily commute by car.","zh":"Jason 不喜歡壓力大的汽車日常通勤。"},{"en":"A stressful daily commute is a repeated journey to and from work or school that causes pressure.","zh":"壓力大的日常通勤，是每天往返工作或學校並造成壓力的旅程。"},{"en":"Crowded trains and traffic jams can make a daily commute stressful.","zh":"擠迫火車和交通擠塞可以令日常通勤變得有壓力。"},{"en":"A stressful commute can leave people tired before work even begins.","zh":"壓力大的通勤可以令人在工作開始前已感到疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regular travel that creates stress.","zh":"這個短語描述帶來壓力的定期出行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"driverless journey","meaning":"無人駕駛旅程","examples":[{"en":"Jason would prefer a driverless journey to a stressful commute.","zh":"Jason 會較喜歡無人駕駛旅程，而不是壓力大的通勤。"},{"en":"A driverless journey is a trip made in a vehicle that drives itself.","zh":"無人駕駛旅程，是乘坐自行駕駛車輛完成的旅程。"},{"en":"A worker might use a driverless journey to answer emails instead of focusing on traffic.","zh":"工人可能利用無人駕駛旅程回覆電郵，而不用專注交通。"},{"en":"If the vehicle handles the driving, the passenger may feel less pressure.","zh":"如果車輛處理駕駛，乘客可能感到較少壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes travel without human driving.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有真人駕駛的出行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"if I had the chance","meaning":"如果我有機會","examples":[{"en":"Jason would use a driverless car if he had the chance.","zh":"如果 Jason 有機會，他會使用無人駕駛汽車。"},{"en":"If I had the chance means if I were given the opportunity.","zh":"如果我有機會，是指如果我得到機會。"},{"en":"If I had the chance, I would study abroad for one semester.","zh":"如果我有機會，我會到海外讀一個學期。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a wish or possible action that depends on opportunity.","zh":"這個短語描述取決於機會的願望或可能行動。"},{"en":"It is often used when the speaker cannot do something yet.","zh":"當說話者尚未能做某事時，它常被使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take the pressure off","meaning":"減輕……的壓力","examples":[{"en":"A driverless car would take the pressure off driving.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車會減輕駕駛的壓力。"},{"en":"To take the pressure off something means to reduce stress, responsibility or difficulty.","zh":"減輕某事的壓力，是指降低壓力、責任或困難。"},{"en":"A clear checklist can take the pressure off students before a presentation.","zh":"清楚清單可以減輕學生匯報前的壓力。"},{"en":"If the car controls the journey, the passenger no longer has to watch every road condition.","zh":"如果汽車控制旅程，乘客就不再需要注意每個路面情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a task less stressful.","zh":"這個短語描述令任務較不緊張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be slightly wary of","meaning":"對……有點警惕","examples":[{"en":"Jason is slightly wary of depending on a robot-driven car.","zh":"Jason 對依賴由機械人駕駛的汽車有點警惕。"},{"en":"To be slightly wary of something means to be a little cautious or suspicious about it.","zh":"對某事有點警惕，是指對它有一點謹慎或懷疑。"},{"en":"A parent may be slightly wary of a new app that asks children for personal information.","zh":"如果新應用程式要求孩子提供個人資料，父母可能有點警惕。"},{"en":"Worry about safety can make people cautious even when they like an idea.","zh":"對安全的擔心會令人即使喜歡某想法也保持謹慎。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mild concern, not complete rejection.","zh":"這個短語描述輕微顧慮，而不是完全拒絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be completely dependent on","meaning":"完全依賴……","examples":[{"en":"Jason is wary of being completely dependent on a robot-driven car.","zh":"Jason 對完全依賴由機械人駕駛的汽車感到警惕。"},{"en":"To be completely dependent on something means to rely on it fully, with no backup or control.","zh":"完全依賴某物，是指完全倚靠它，沒有後備或控制權。"},{"en":"Students should not be completely dependent on translation apps when learning English.","zh":"學生學英語時不應完全依賴翻譯應用程式。"},{"en":"Complete dependence can feel risky if the system fails.","zh":"如果系統失效，完全依賴可能感覺有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes total reliance.","zh":"這個短語描述完全倚靠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"robot-driven car","meaning":"由機械人駕駛的汽車","examples":[{"en":"Jason worries about being dependent on a robot-driven car.","zh":"Jason 擔心依賴由機械人駕駛的汽車。"},{"en":"A robot-driven car is a car controlled by an automated driving system rather than a human.","zh":"由機械人駕駛的汽車，是由自動駕駛系統而非真人控制的汽車。"},{"en":"A commuter might relax in a robot-driven car while it handles traffic.","zh":"通勤者可能在由機械人駕駛的汽車中放鬆，讓汽車處理交通。"},{"en":"People may worry about robot-driven cars because they cannot easily predict every road event.","zh":"人們可能擔心機械人駕駛汽車，因為它們不容易預測每個道路事件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a car driven by machine intelligence.","zh":"這個短語描述由機器智能駕駛的汽車。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"react to","meaning":"對……作出反應","examples":[{"en":"A driverless car must react to unexpected obstacles.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車必須對意外障礙物作出反應。"},{"en":"To react to something means to respond when it happens.","zh":"對某事作出反應，是指在它發生時作出回應。"},{"en":"A teacher must react quickly if a student suddenly feels unwell.","zh":"如果學生突然不適，老師必須快速作出反應。"},{"en":"Good reaction is important because road conditions can change in seconds.","zh":"良好反應很重要，因為道路情況可以在幾秒內改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes responding to a situation or event.","zh":"這個短語描述對情況或事件作出回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"unexpected obstacles","meaning":"意外障礙物","examples":[{"en":"Jason worries about unexpected obstacles in the road.","zh":"Jason 擔心道路上的意外障礙物。"},{"en":"Unexpected obstacles are objects or problems that suddenly appear and block progress.","zh":"意外障礙物，是突然出現並阻礙前進的物件或問題。"},{"en":"A fallen tree can become an unexpected obstacle on a country road.","zh":"倒下的樹可以成為鄉郊道路上的意外障礙物。"},{"en":"Obstacles are dangerous because vehicles must notice and avoid them quickly.","zh":"障礙物很危險，因為車輛必須快速發現並避開它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sudden barriers that were not planned for.","zh":"這個短語描述未被預計的突然障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in the road","meaning":"在路上","examples":[{"en":"A robot-driven car may have to react to obstacles in the road.","zh":"由機械人駕駛的汽車可能必須對路上的障礙物作出反應。"},{"en":"In the road means on the part of the street or route where vehicles travel.","zh":"在路上，是指在車輛行駛的街道或路線部分。"},{"en":"Drivers must slow down if there is a large box in the road.","zh":"如果路上有大箱子，司機必須減速。"},{"en":"Objects in the road can force vehicles to brake, change lanes or stop.","zh":"路上的物件可以迫使車輛煞車、轉線或停下。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something blocking or occupying the driving path.","zh":"這個短語描述阻擋或佔用行車路徑的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"for each question","meaning":"每條題目","examples":[{"en":"For each question, only one of the choices is correct.","zh":"每條題目只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"For each question means for every individual question in a set.","zh":"每條題目，是指一組題目中的每一個個別問題。"},{"en":"For each question in the quiz, students must choose one answer.","zh":"小測中每條題目，學生都必須選一個答案。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds candidates to treat every item separately.","zh":"這個短語提醒考生要分別處理每一題。"},{"en":"It is common in exam instructions.","zh":"它常見於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"only one of the choices is correct","meaning":"只有一個選項正確","examples":[{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct.","zh":"只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct means exactly one option is the right answer.","zh":"只有一個選項正確，是指剛好只有一個選項是正確答案。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice grammar question, only one of the four options may fit the sentence.","zh":"在多項選擇文法題中，四個選項可能只有一個適合句子。"},{"en":"If students choose two answers, they may lose marks even if one is right.","zh":"如果學生選兩個答案，即使其中一個正確，也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase tells candidates to select one answer only.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生只選一個答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"corresponding letter","meaning":"相應字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the corresponding letter in the appropriate box.","zh":"考生在適當方格寫上相應字母。"},{"en":"A corresponding letter is the letter that matches the correct answer or item.","zh":"相應字母是與正確答案或項目相配的字母。"},{"en":"If answer A matches statement 1, students write the corresponding letter A.","zh":"如果答案 A 配對陳述 1，學生就寫上相應字母 A。"},{"en":"This phrase helps students transfer answers accurately to the answer sheet.","zh":"這個短語幫助學生準確把答案填到答題紙。"},{"en":"It refers to the letter linked with a specific choice.","zh":"它指與特定選項相關的字母。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"appropriate box","meaning":"適當方格","examples":[{"en":"Students write the letter in the appropriate box on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生把字母寫在答題紙上的適當方格。"},{"en":"The appropriate box is the correct space where an answer should be written.","zh":"適當方格，是應該寫答案的正確空格。"},{"en":"In an exam, writing the answer in the wrong box may cause confusion.","zh":"在考試中，把答案寫在錯誤方格可能造成混亂。"},{"en":"Using the appropriate box helps markers know which answer belongs to which question.","zh":"使用適當方格幫助閱卷者知道哪個答案屬於哪題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the correct answer space.","zh":"這個短語指正確答案空格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Which of the following statements is accurate?","meaning":"以下哪項陳述是準確的？","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which of the following statements is accurate.","zh":"題目問以下哪項陳述是準確的。"},{"en":"Which of the following statements is accurate? asks students to choose the statement that is true or correct.","zh":"以下哪項陳述是準確的，是要求學生選出真實或正確的陳述。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students must check the passage before deciding which statement is accurate.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生必須先查閱篇章，再決定哪項陳述準確。"},{"en":"A statement may sound reasonable but still be wrong if the text does not support it.","zh":"陳述可能聽起來合理，但如果文本不支持，仍然是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a multiple-choice accuracy question.","zh":"這個短語引入多項選擇準確性題目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"conform to safety regulations","meaning":"符合安全規例","examples":[{"en":"Driverless cars must conform to safety regulations.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車必須符合安全規例。"},{"en":"To conform to safety regulations means to follow official rules designed to prevent harm.","zh":"符合安全規例，是指遵守為防止傷害而設的官方規則。"},{"en":"A school bus must conform to safety regulations before carrying students.","zh":"校車在接載學生前必須符合安全規例。"},{"en":"If a product does not meet safety rules, it may not be allowed on the market.","zh":"如果產品不符合安全規則，它可能不被允許投放市場。"},{"en":"This phrase describes obeying safety laws or standards.","zh":"這個短語描述遵守安全法律或標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"an obvious market for","meaning":"……的明顯市場","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe there is an obvious market for automated cars.","zh":"有些人相信自動化汽車有明顯市場。"},{"en":"An obvious market for something means a clear group of customers who would probably want it.","zh":"某物的明顯市場，是指一群清楚可能想要它的顧客。"},{"en":"There is an obvious market for cheap lunch boxes near a school.","zh":"學校附近有廉價飯盒的明顯市場。"},{"en":"If many people dislike driving, driverless cars may have strong demand.","zh":"如果許多人不喜歡駕駛，無人駕駛汽車可能有強大需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clear customer demand.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚的顧客需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"human drivers","meaning":"人類司機","examples":[{"en":"Human drivers may face competition from driverless cars.","zh":"人類司機可能面對來自無人駕駛汽車的競爭。"},{"en":"Human drivers are real people who drive vehicles.","zh":"人類司機是真正駕駛車輛的人。"},{"en":"A human driver can make eye contact with pedestrians and react using judgement.","zh":"人類司機可以與行人眼神接觸，並使用判斷力作反應。"},{"en":"Driverless technology may replace some tasks currently done by human drivers.","zh":"無人駕駛技術可能取代目前由人類司機完成的一些任務。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts people with automated driving systems.","zh":"這個短語把人與自動駕駛系統作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be no competition for","meaning":"不是……的對手","examples":[{"en":"Some people claim that human drivers are no competition for driverless cars.","zh":"有些人聲稱人類司機不是無人駕駛汽車的對手。"},{"en":"To be no competition for someone or something means to be much weaker or less effective than them.","zh":"不是某人或某物的對手，是指比對方弱很多或效率差很多。"},{"en":"A small local team may be no competition for a professional football club.","zh":"小型本地球隊可能不是職業足球會的對手。"},{"en":"If robot drivers make fewer mistakes, human drivers may seem less competitive.","zh":"如果機械人司機犯錯較少，人類司機可能顯得競爭力較弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being clearly outmatched.","zh":"這個短語描述明顯不敵對方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"potentially","meaning":"潛在地；可能","examples":[{"en":"Potentially, automated taxis could be cheaper than normal taxis.","zh":"自動化的士可能比普通的士便宜。"},{"en":"Potentially means possibly, if conditions are right.","zh":"潛在地，是指在條件合適時有可能。"},{"en":"A quiet student could potentially become a strong speaker with enough practice.","zh":"安靜學生在足夠練習下，可能成為強大的演講者。"},{"en":"This word shows possibility without claiming certainty.","zh":"這個詞顯示可能性，而不是聲稱肯定。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing future benefits or risks.","zh":"它適合討論未來好處或風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"cost-effective","meaning":"具成本效益的","examples":[{"en":"Fully automated taxis may be more cost-effective than normal taxis.","zh":"全自動的士可能比普通的士更具成本效益。"},{"en":"Cost-effective means giving good value for the money spent.","zh":"具成本效益的，是指花費的金錢能帶來良好價值。"},{"en":"A school may choose cost-effective software that helps many students at a low price.","zh":"學校可能選擇具成本效益的軟件，以低價格幫助許多學生。"},{"en":"Removing driver wages could make automated taxis cheaper to operate.","zh":"取消司機薪酬可以令自動化的士營運成本較低。"},{"en":"This phrase describes financial efficiency.","zh":"這個短語描述財務效率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"normal taxis","meaning":"普通的士","examples":[{"en":"Driverless taxis could be cheaper than normal taxis.","zh":"無人駕駛的士可能比普通的士便宜。"},{"en":"Normal taxis are ordinary taxis driven by human drivers.","zh":"普通的士是由真人司機駕駛的傳統的士。"},{"en":"A passenger may choose a normal taxi if they prefer speaking to a human driver.","zh":"如果乘客較喜歡與真人司機交流，可能選擇普通的士。"},{"en":"Normal taxis include driver wages in their operating costs.","zh":"普通的士的營運成本包括司機薪酬。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts traditional taxi services with automated ones.","zh":"這個短語把傳統的士服務與自動化服務作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"invest in a technology","meaning":"投資於一項技術","examples":[{"en":"Uber is investing in a technology that may prove controversial.","zh":"Uber 正投資於一項可能證明具爭議性的技術。"},{"en":"To invest in a technology means to spend money or resources to develop or use it.","zh":"投資於一項技術，是指花金錢或資源去開發或使用它。"},{"en":"A school may invest in a technology that helps students practise pronunciation.","zh":"學校可能投資於一項幫助學生練習發音的技術。"},{"en":"Investment is risky if the technology is expensive and public reaction is uncertain.","zh":"如果技術昂貴且公眾反應不確定，投資就有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes putting resources into a technical idea or system.","zh":"這個短語描述把資源投放到技術想法或系統中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"prove controversial","meaning":"證明具爭議性","examples":[{"en":"Driverless-car technology may prove controversial.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車技術可能證明具爭議性。"},{"en":"To prove controversial means to turn out to cause disagreement or public debate.","zh":"證明具爭議性，是指結果引起分歧或公眾討論。"},{"en":"A new school rule on phone use may prove controversial among students and parents.","zh":"關於手機使用的新校規可能在學生和家長之間證明具爭議性。"},{"en":"Driverless cars may be controversial because they affect safety, jobs and laws.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車可能有爭議，因為它們影響安全、工作和法律。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that may create opposing opinions.","zh":"這個短語描述可能引起相反意見的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"tried and tested","meaning":"經過試驗並證實可靠","examples":[{"en":"Some technologies are safer because they have been tried and tested.","zh":"有些技術較安全，因為它們已經過試驗並證實可靠。"},{"en":"Tried and tested means already used and proven reliable through experience.","zh":"經過試驗並證實可靠，是指已被使用並透過經驗證明可靠。"},{"en":"A teacher may prefer a tried and tested revision method before an important exam.","zh":"老師可能在重要考試前較喜歡經過試驗並證實可靠的溫習方法。"},{"en":"New technology may be riskier because it has not yet been tested widely.","zh":"新技術可能風險較高，因為尚未被廣泛測試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something with a proven record.","zh":"這個短語描述有可靠紀錄的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be unlikely to prove cost-effective","meaning":"不大可能證明具成本效益","examples":[{"en":"A technology may be unlikely to prove cost-effective.","zh":"一項技術可能不大可能證明具成本效益。"},{"en":"To be unlikely to prove cost-effective means probably not to give enough value for the money spent.","zh":"不大可能證明具成本效益，是指很可能不能為花費帶來足夠價值。"},{"en":"A school may reject a very expensive app if it is unlikely to prove cost-effective.","zh":"如果一個應用程式非常昂貴且不大可能具成本效益，學校可能拒絕使用。"},{"en":"If development costs are too high, savings may not cover the investment.","zh":"如果開發成本太高，節省下來的金額可能無法抵消投資。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doubtful financial value.","zh":"這個短語描述可疑的財務價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"What is not true about","meaning":"關於……哪項不正確","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what is not true about driverless cars.","zh":"題目問關於無人駕駛汽車哪項不正確。"},{"en":"What is not true about something asks students to find the incorrect statement.","zh":"關於某事哪項不正確，是要求學生找出錯誤陳述。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students must check which option is not true about the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生必須查清哪個選項不符合文章。"},{"en":"This question type is tricky because most options may be correct.","zh":"這類題目較棘手，因為大多數選項可能是正確的。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for the false answer, not the true one.","zh":"這個短語要求找出錯誤答案，而不是正確答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in many countries","meaning":"在許多國家","examples":[{"en":"Driverless cars have not become common in many countries.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車在許多國家尚未變得普遍。"},{"en":"In many countries means across a large number of nations.","zh":"在許多國家，是指橫跨大量國家。"},{"en":"Online payment is common in many countries, but cash is still used in some places.","zh":"網上付款在許多國家很普遍，但有些地方仍使用現金。"},{"en":"A technology may spread unevenly because laws and public trust differ by country.","zh":"科技可能擴散不均，因為各國法律和公眾信任不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad international coverage, not every country.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛國際範圍，而不是每一個國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"improve road safety","meaning":"改善道路安全","examples":[{"en":"Driverless cars may improve road safety.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車可能改善道路安全。"},{"en":"To improve road safety means to reduce accidents, injuries and deaths on roads.","zh":"改善道路安全，是指減少道路上的意外、受傷和死亡。"},{"en":"Better street lighting can improve road safety near schools.","zh":"更好的街燈可以改善學校附近的道路安全。"},{"en":"If automated cars make fewer mistakes, they may reduce crashes.","zh":"如果自動化汽車犯錯較少，它們可能減少撞車。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making roads safer for drivers, passengers and pedestrians.","zh":"這個短語描述令道路對司機、乘客和行人更安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reduce the cost of travelling","meaning":"降低出行成本","examples":[{"en":"Driverless taxis may reduce the cost of travelling.","zh":"無人駕駛的士可能降低出行成本。"},{"en":"To reduce the cost of travelling means to make journeys cheaper.","zh":"降低出行成本，是指令旅程更便宜。"},{"en":"A student discount on buses can reduce the cost of travelling to school.","zh":"巴士學生優惠可以降低上學出行成本。"},{"en":"Removing driver wages may lower the price of taxi journeys.","zh":"取消司機薪酬可能降低的士旅程價格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making transport more affordable.","zh":"這個短語描述令交通更可負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"endanger jobs","meaning":"危及工作職位","examples":[{"en":"Driverless technology may endanger jobs.","zh":"無人駕駛技術可能危及工作職位。"},{"en":"To endanger jobs means to put people’s employment at risk.","zh":"危及工作職位，是指使人們的就業面臨風險。"},{"en":"A factory robot may endanger jobs if it replaces many workers on the production line.","zh":"如果工廠機械人取代生產線上許多工人，它可能危及工作職位。"},{"en":"Workers may oppose technology when they fear it will remove their income.","zh":"當工人擔心科技會奪去收入，他們可能反對它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a threat to employment.","zh":"這個短語描述對就業的威脅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"current legislation","meaning":"現行法例","examples":[{"en":"Current legislation does not fully support driverless cars.","zh":"現行法例並不完全支持無人駕駛汽車。"},{"en":"Current legislation means the laws that are in force at the present time.","zh":"現行法例是目前有效的法律。"},{"en":"Current legislation may not mention new technology if the laws were written years ago.","zh":"如果法律多年前制定，現行法例可能沒有提及新科技。"},{"en":"When technology changes quickly, laws may need to be updated.","zh":"當科技快速改變，法律可能需要更新。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to existing legal rules.","zh":"這個短語指現有法律規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be in favour of","meaning":"支持；有利於","examples":[{"en":"Some laws are not yet in favour of fully automated cars.","zh":"有些法律尚未支持全自動汽車。"},{"en":"To be in favour of something means to support it or help it happen.","zh":"支持或有利於某事，是指贊成它或幫助它發生。"},{"en":"A school policy may be in favour of healthy eating if it bans sugary drinks.","zh":"如果校政禁止含糖飲品，可能是有利於健康飲食。"},{"en":"If laws are not in favour of a technology, companies may struggle to use it publicly.","zh":"如果法律不支持某科技，公司可能難以公開使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes support or advantage.","zh":"這個短語描述支持或有利條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"favour fully automated cars","meaning":"有利於全自動汽車","examples":[{"en":"Current legislation does not favour fully automated cars.","zh":"現行法例並不有利於全自動汽車。"},{"en":"To favour fully automated cars means to support or make it easier for those cars to be used legally.","zh":"有利於全自動汽車，是指支持或令這些汽車更容易合法使用。"},{"en":"A city may favour electric buses by giving them special funding.","zh":"城市可能透過提供特別資助來支持電動巴士。"},{"en":"If laws do not favour automated cars, road testing may be limited.","zh":"如果法律不利於自動化汽車，道路測試可能受限制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes legal or official support for a technology.","zh":"這個短語描述對某技術的法律或官方支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"keep up with technology","meaning":"跟上科技發展","examples":[{"en":"Laws may struggle to keep up with technology.","zh":"法律可能難以跟上科技發展。"},{"en":"To keep up with technology means to develop or change fast enough to match technological progress.","zh":"跟上科技發展，是指發展或改變得夠快，以配合科技進步。"},{"en":"Teachers may need training to keep up with technology in online learning.","zh":"老師可能需要培訓，以跟上網上學習科技發展。"},{"en":"If laws cannot keep up, new inventions may create legal confusion.","zh":"如果法律不能跟上，新發明可能造成法律混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes matching the speed of technological change.","zh":"這個短語描述配合科技變化速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"accommodate driverless cars","meaning":"容納；配合無人駕駛汽車","examples":[{"en":"Current law does not fully accommodate driverless cars.","zh":"現行法律並未完全配合無人駕駛汽車。"},{"en":"To accommodate driverless cars means to allow for them and make rules suitable for them.","zh":"配合無人駕駛汽車，是指容許它們並制定適合它們的規則。"},{"en":"A school timetable may accommodate students who need extra language support.","zh":"學校時間表可能配合需要額外語言支援的學生。"},{"en":"If the law cannot accommodate new vehicles, they may not be allowed on public roads.","zh":"如果法律不能配合新車輛，它們可能不被允許在公共道路上行駛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adjusting a system to fit a new need.","zh":"這個短語描述調整系統以符合新需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"general view held by","meaning":"……持有的普遍看法","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the general view held by car manufacturers.","zh":"題目問汽車製造商持有的普遍看法。"},{"en":"The general view held by a group is the broad opinion that many members of that group share.","zh":"某群體持有的普遍看法，是該群體許多成員共有的大致意見。"},{"en":"The general view held by teachers may be that smaller classes help learning.","zh":"老師持有的普遍看法可能是小班教學有助學習。"},{"en":"A general view may not represent every individual, but it describes the common position.","zh":"普遍看法未必代表每個個人，但描述共同立場。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about the overall opinion of a group.","zh":"這個短語問某群體的整體意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"non-automated cars","meaning":"非自動駕駛汽車","examples":[{"en":"Driverless cars are compared with non-automated cars.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車與非自動駕駛汽車作比較。"},{"en":"Non-automated cars are cars that require human drivers to control them.","zh":"非自動駕駛汽車是需要真人司機控制的汽車。"},{"en":"Most older family cars are non-automated cars with no self-driving functions.","zh":"大多數較舊家庭汽車是沒有自動駕駛功能的非自動汽車。"},{"en":"Comparing automated and non-automated cars helps discuss safety, cost and convenience.","zh":"比較自動和非自動汽車，有助討論安全、成本和方便程度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes traditional cars without automation.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有自動化的傳統汽車。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"too expensive to manufacture","meaning":"製造成本太高","examples":[{"en":"Some people may think fully automated cars are too expensive to manufacture.","zh":"有些人可能認為全自動汽車製造成本太高。"},{"en":"Too expensive to manufacture means production costs are so high that making the product may not be practical.","zh":"製造成本太高，是指生產成本高到製造該產品可能不實際。"},{"en":"A school may reject a science kit if it is too expensive to manufacture and buy.","zh":"如果科學工具套裝製造和購買成本太高，學校可能拒絕採用。"},{"en":"High manufacturing costs can delay a product’s arrival on the market.","zh":"高製造成本可以延遲產品投放市場。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cost as a barrier to production.","zh":"這個短語描述成本成為生產障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"threaten someone’s livelihood","meaning":"威脅某人的生計","examples":[{"en":"The introduction of driverless cars may threaten drivers’ livelihoods.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車的引入可能威脅司機的生計。"},{"en":"To threaten someone’s livelihood means to put their ability to earn a living at risk.","zh":"威脅某人的生計，是指使其謀生能力面臨風險。"},{"en":"A sudden rent increase may threaten a small shop owner’s livelihood.","zh":"租金突然上升可能威脅小店主的生計。"},{"en":"Workers may resist change if it threatens the income their families depend on.","zh":"如果改變威脅家庭依賴的收入，工人可能抗拒它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes danger to a person’s work and income.","zh":"這個短語描述對某人工作和收入的危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"too underdeveloped to","meaning":"發展得太不成熟而不能……","examples":[{"en":"Some people think the technology is too underdeveloped to use widely.","zh":"有些人認為這項技術發展得太不成熟，不能廣泛使用。"},{"en":"Too underdeveloped to do something means not advanced or mature enough to do it safely or effectively.","zh":"發展得太不成熟而不能做某事，是指尚未先進或成熟到能安全有效地做到。"},{"en":"A new app may be too underdeveloped to use in an important exam system.","zh":"新應用程式可能發展得太不成熟，不能用於重要考試系統。"},{"en":"If technology is underdeveloped, errors and safety problems may remain.","zh":"如果技術不成熟，錯誤和安全問題可能仍然存在。"},{"en":"This phrase describes immaturity as a barrier to use.","zh":"這個短語描述不成熟成為使用障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the writer’s opinion of","meaning":"作者對……的看法","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the writer’s opinion of driverless cars.","zh":"題目問作者對無人駕駛汽車的看法。"},{"en":"The writer’s opinion of something is the attitude or judgement the writer shows about it.","zh":"作者對某事的看法，是作者對它表現出的態度或判斷。"},{"en":"In a reading passage, students must separate the writer’s opinion from facts and examples.","zh":"在閱讀篇章中，學生必須把作者看法與事實和例子分開。"},{"en":"The writer may present different views before giving or withholding a final judgement.","zh":"作者可能先呈現不同觀點，然後才給出或保留最終判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase asks what the author thinks.","zh":"這個短語問作者怎樣想。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be uninterested in","meaning":"對……不感興趣","examples":[{"en":"The writer is not simply uninterested in driverless technology.","zh":"作者並不只是對無人駕駛技術不感興趣。"},{"en":"To be uninterested in something means not to care about it or not find it worth attention.","zh":"對某事不感興趣，是指不關心它或不覺得它值得注意。"},{"en":"A student may be uninterested in football but excited by music.","zh":"學生可能對足球不感興趣，但對音樂感到興奮。"},{"en":"If a writer discusses many sides of a topic, they are probably not uninterested in it.","zh":"如果作者討論一個主題的多個方面，他們大概不是對它不感興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lack of interest.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be sceptical about","meaning":"對……持懷疑態度","examples":[{"en":"Some readers may be sceptical about driverless technology.","zh":"有些讀者可能對無人駕駛技術持懷疑態度。"},{"en":"To be sceptical about something means to doubt it or question whether it will work.","zh":"對某事持懷疑態度，是指懷疑它或質疑它是否會成功。"},{"en":"Parents may be sceptical about a new study app until they see real improvement.","zh":"父母在看到真正改善前，可能對新學習應用程式持懷疑態度。"},{"en":"People may become sceptical when promises sound too ambitious.","zh":"當承諾聽起來過於雄心勃勃，人們可能變得懷疑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doubt rather than complete rejection.","zh":"這個短語描述懷疑，而不是完全拒絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reserve judgement as to whether","meaning":"對……暫不作判斷","examples":[{"en":"The writer reserves judgement as to whether driverless cars will succeed.","zh":"作者對無人駕駛汽車是否會成功暫不作判斷。"},{"en":"To reserve judgement as to whether something will happen means to avoid giving a final opinion yet.","zh":"對某事是否會發生暫不作判斷，是指暫時避免給出最終意見。"},{"en":"A teacher may reserve judgement as to whether a new textbook works until students have used it for a term.","zh":"老師可能等學生使用新教科書一個學期後，才判斷它是否有效。"},{"en":"Reserving judgement is sensible when evidence is incomplete or mixed.","zh":"當證據不完整或混雜時，暫不作判斷是合理的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes waiting before deciding.","zh":"這個短語描述先等待再決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"become a reality","meaning":"成為現實","examples":[{"en":"The writer discusses whether driverless cars will become a reality.","zh":"作者討論無人駕駛汽車是否會成為現實。"},{"en":"To become a reality means to change from an idea or plan into something real.","zh":"成為現實，是指由想法或計劃變成真正存在的東西。"},{"en":"A student’s dream of studying overseas may become a reality after winning a scholarship.","zh":"學生獲得獎學金後，海外升學夢想可能成為現實。"},{"en":"Many technical, legal and financial problems must be solved before an idea becomes real.","zh":"在想法成為現實前，許多技術、法律和財務問題必須解決。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an idea turning into actual existence.","zh":"這個短語描述想法變成實際存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be critical of","meaning":"批評……","examples":[{"en":"Some people are critical of Uber’s plans.","zh":"有些人批評 Uber 的計劃。"},{"en":"To be critical of something means to express disapproval or point out problems.","zh":"批評某事，是指表達不滿或指出問題。"},{"en":"Parents may be critical of a school policy if it gives students too much homework.","zh":"如果校政給學生太多功課，父母可能批評它。"},{"en":"People may criticise technology when they believe it harms workers or safety.","zh":"當人們認為科技傷害工人或安全時，可能批評科技。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a negative or questioning attitude.","zh":"這個短語描述負面或質疑態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"plans to introduce","meaning":"引入……的計劃","examples":[{"en":"Uber has plans to introduce fully automated cars.","zh":"Uber 有引入全自動汽車的計劃。"},{"en":"Plans to introduce something are intentions to bring something new into use.","zh":"引入某物的計劃，是把新事物帶入使用的意圖。"},{"en":"A school may have plans to introduce a new reading programme next term.","zh":"學校可能有計劃在下學期引入新閱讀計劃。"},{"en":"Introducing a major change usually requires preparation, testing and public explanation.","zh":"引入重大改變通常需要準備、測試和向公眾解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intended future introduction.","zh":"這個短語描述預定的未來引入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"look at the following statements","meaning":"查看以下陳述","examples":[{"en":"Candidates look at the following statements and match them to people.","zh":"考生查看以下陳述，並把它們配對至人物。"},{"en":"To look at the following statements means to read and consider the statements listed below.","zh":"查看以下陳述，是指閱讀並考慮下面列出的陳述。"},{"en":"In a reading task, students look at the following statements before choosing matching names.","zh":"在閱讀題中，學生先查看以下陳述，再選擇配對人物。"},{"en":"Careful reading prevents students from matching a statement to the wrong person.","zh":"仔細閱讀可以避免學生把陳述配對到錯誤人物。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the list of people","meaning":"人物列表","examples":[{"en":"The question provides a list of people.","zh":"題目提供人物列表。"},{"en":"The list of people is the set of names or individuals candidates can choose from.","zh":"人物列表是考生可以選擇的一組姓名或人物。"},{"en":"A matching exercise may give a list of people such as doctors, teachers and drivers.","zh":"配對練習可能提供人物列表，例如醫生、老師和司機。"},{"en":"Students must connect each statement to the correct name from the list.","zh":"學生必須把每項陳述連接到列表中的正確姓名。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the available answer options involving people.","zh":"這個短語指涉及人物的可選答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"match each statement to","meaning":"將每項陳述配對至……","examples":[{"en":"Students match each statement to the correct person.","zh":"學生將每項陳述配對至正確人物。"},{"en":"To match each statement to something means to connect every statement with the right answer.","zh":"將每項陳述配對至某物，是指把每項陳述連接到正確答案。"},{"en":"In a history task, students may match each statement to the correct leader.","zh":"在歷史題中，學生可能把每項陳述配對至正確領袖。"},{"en":"Matching requires understanding both the statement and the person’s view.","zh":"配對需要理解陳述和該人物的看法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pairing information accurately.","zh":"這個短語描述準確配對資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the correct person","meaning":"正確人物","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct person for each statement.","zh":"考生為每項陳述選擇正確人物。"},{"en":"The correct person is the individual whose view or information matches the statement.","zh":"正確人物，是其觀點或資料與陳述相符的人。"},{"en":"If Susie supports driverless cars, a supportive statement should be matched to her.","zh":"如果 Susie 支持無人駕駛汽車，支持性陳述應配對給她。"},{"en":"Choosing the correct person requires checking details, not just guessing from keywords.","zh":"選擇正確人物需要檢查細節，而不只是憑關鍵字猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the right person in a matching task.","zh":"這個短語指出配對題中的正確人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"more than once","meaning":"多於一次","examples":[{"en":"Students may use any letter more than once.","zh":"學生可以使用任何字母多於一次。"},{"en":"More than once means two times or more.","zh":"多於一次，是指兩次或以上。"},{"en":"In a matching exercise, the same person’s letter may be used more than once.","zh":"在配對練習中，同一人物的字母可能被使用多於一次。"},{"en":"This instruction prevents students from wrongly assuming each answer can be used only once.","zh":"這項指示避免學生錯誤假設每個答案只能使用一次。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated use.","zh":"這個短語描述重複使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be willing to give up control of","meaning":"願意放棄對……的控制","examples":[{"en":"Some people are willing to give up control of their vehicle.","zh":"有些人願意放棄對自己車輛的控制。"},{"en":"To be willing to give up control of something means to accept no longer being in charge of it.","zh":"願意放棄對某物的控制，是指接受不再親自掌管它。"},{"en":"A manager may be willing to give up control of a project if a specialist can do it better.","zh":"如果專家能做得更好，經理可能願意放棄對項目的控制。"},{"en":"People must trust driverless technology before they give up control of a car.","zh":"人們必須信任無人駕駛技術，才會放棄對汽車的控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accepting loss of direct control.","zh":"這個短語描述接受失去直接控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"appreciate the benefits of","meaning":"欣賞……的好處","examples":[{"en":"Supporters appreciate the benefits of fully automated cars.","zh":"支持者欣賞全自動汽車的好處。"},{"en":"To appreciate the benefits of something means to understand and value its advantages.","zh":"欣賞某事的好處，是指理解並重視其優點。"},{"en":"Students may appreciate the benefits of planning after it helps them finish an essay on time.","zh":"當計劃幫助學生準時完成文章，他們可能欣賞計劃的好處。"},{"en":"People who hate traffic may appreciate how driverless cars reduce driving stress.","zh":"討厭交通的人可能欣賞無人駕駛汽車如何減少駕駛壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognising positive value.","zh":"這個短語描述認出正面價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"have no regrets about","meaning":"對……不會後悔","examples":[{"en":"Susie would have no regrets about giving up driving.","zh":"Susie 對放棄駕駛不會後悔。"},{"en":"To have no regrets about something means not to feel sorry or unhappy about choosing it.","zh":"對某事不後悔，是指不因選擇它而感到抱歉或不快。"},{"en":"A student may have no regrets about joining a club if it helps them make friends.","zh":"如果參加學會幫助學生交朋友，他們可能不會後悔加入。"},{"en":"If a driverless car makes travel easier, some people may not miss driving at all.","zh":"如果無人駕駛汽車令出行更容易，有些人可能完全不會懷念駕駛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being satisfied with a decision.","zh":"這個短語描述對決定感到滿意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"give up driving entirely","meaning":"完全放棄駕駛","examples":[{"en":"Some people would give up driving entirely.","zh":"有些人會完全放棄駕駛。"},{"en":"To give up driving entirely means to stop driving completely.","zh":"完全放棄駕駛，是指徹底停止駕駛。"},{"en":"An older person may give up driving entirely if public transport becomes easy and reliable.","zh":"如果公共交通變得方便可靠，年長人士可能完全放棄駕駛。"},{"en":"People may stop driving if another option is safer, cheaper or less stressful.","zh":"如果另一選擇更安全、更便宜或壓力較少，人們可能停止駕駛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a complete end to driving.","zh":"這個短語描述駕駛的完全終止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"in favour of being driven by","meaning":"轉而選擇由……接載","examples":[{"en":"Susie supports giving up driving in favour of being driven by a robot car.","zh":"Susie 支持放棄駕駛，轉而選擇由機械人汽車接載。"},{"en":"In favour of being driven by something means choosing that option instead of driving oneself.","zh":"轉而選擇由某物接載，是指選擇該方式，而不是自己駕駛。"},{"en":"A tired commuter may stop cycling in favour of being driven by a shuttle bus.","zh":"疲倦通勤者可能停止踩單車，轉而選擇由接駁巴士接載。"},{"en":"People may choose an easier transport option when it reduces stress and effort.","zh":"當交通選擇能減少壓力和努力，人們可能選擇較容易的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase shows preference for one option over another.","zh":"這個短語顯示對一個選項而非另一個選項的偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be aware that","meaning":"意識到","examples":[{"en":"Jason is aware that driverless cars may have limits.","zh":"Jason 意識到無人駕駛汽車可能有限制。"},{"en":"To be aware that something is true means to know or realise it.","zh":"意識到某事，是指知道或明白它。"},{"en":"A student should be aware that copied homework can lead to punishment.","zh":"學生應意識到抄功課可能導致懲罰。"},{"en":"Awareness of limits makes a person more cautious about using new technology.","zh":"意識到限制會令人對使用新科技更謹慎。"},{"en":"This phrase describes knowledge or realisation.","zh":"這個短語描述知道或察覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"provide an adequate substitute for","meaning":"為……提供足夠的替代","examples":[{"en":"Driverless cars may not provide an adequate substitute for a human driver.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車可能無法為人類司機提供足夠替代。"},{"en":"To provide an adequate substitute for something means to replace it well enough for the purpose.","zh":"為某物提供足夠替代，是指為該目的足夠好地取代它。"},{"en":"An online lesson may not provide an adequate substitute for laboratory practice in science.","zh":"在科學科中，網上課堂可能無法充分替代實驗室實習。"},{"en":"If a substitute cannot handle unusual situations, people may still prefer the original option.","zh":"如果替代品不能處理不尋常情況，人們可能仍偏好原本選項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes whether a replacement is good enough.","zh":"這個短語描述替代是否足夠好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"adequate substitute","meaning":"足夠的替代品","examples":[{"en":"A robot driver may not be an adequate substitute for a human driver.","zh":"機械人司機可能不是人類司機的足夠替代品。"},{"en":"An adequate substitute is a replacement that is good enough to do the same job.","zh":"足夠的替代品，是足以完成同一工作的替代物。"},{"en":"A video call may be an adequate substitute for a short meeting, but not for hands-on training.","zh":"視像通話可能足以替代短會議，但不足以替代實作訓練。"},{"en":"A substitute must handle the important parts of the original role.","zh":"替代品必須處理原本角色的重要部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a replacement that may or may not be sufficient.","zh":"這個短語描述可能足夠或不足夠的替代物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"affected adversely by","meaning":"受到……的不利影響","examples":[{"en":"Some workers may be affected adversely by new technology.","zh":"有些工人可能受到新科技的不利影響。"},{"en":"To be affected adversely by something means to be harmed or negatively influenced by it.","zh":"受到某事的不利影響，是指被它傷害或負面影響。"},{"en":"Small shops may be affected adversely by a new shopping mall nearby.","zh":"附近新商場可能對小商店造成不利影響。"},{"en":"Workers can be harmed if technology reduces demand for their skills.","zh":"如果科技減少對工人技能的需求，工人可能受害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a negative impact.","zh":"這個短語描述負面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be protected from","meaning":"受到保護以免受……影響","examples":[{"en":"Those affected by new technology should be protected from its effects.","zh":"受新科技影響的人應受到保護，以免受其影響。"},{"en":"To be protected from something means to be kept safe from harm or risk.","zh":"受到保護以免受某事影響，是指避免受到傷害或風險。"},{"en":"Children should be protected from dangerous traffic near schools.","zh":"兒童應受到保護，免受學校附近危險交通影響。"},{"en":"Workers may need retraining or financial support to protect them from job loss.","zh":"工人可能需要再培訓或財政支援，以保護他們免受失業影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing harm from a danger.","zh":"這個短語描述減少危險帶來的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"under favourable conditions","meaning":"在有利條件下","examples":[{"en":"Jason enjoys driving under favourable conditions.","zh":"Jason 在有利條件下享受駕駛。"},{"en":"Under favourable conditions means when the situation is good or helpful.","zh":"在有利條件下，是指情況良好或有幫助時。"},{"en":"Students learn better under favourable conditions, such as quiet rooms and clear instructions.","zh":"學生在安靜房間和清楚指示等有利條件下學得更好。"},{"en":"Driving may be pleasant when roads are clear, weather is good and there is no pressure.","zh":"當道路暢通、天氣良好且沒有壓力時，駕駛可能令人愉快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a situation that makes success or comfort easier.","zh":"這個短語描述令成功或舒適更容易的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所提供資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether statements agree with the information given in the text.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與文本所提供資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the text says.","zh":"與所提供資料一致，是指符合文本所說的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says Uber is hiring drivers, a statement saying Uber is hiring drivers agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說 Uber 正聘請司機，而陳述也說 Uber 正聘請司機，它就與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students must use the text, not their own opinions, to answer this question type.","zh":"學生必須使用文本，而不是自己的意見，回答這類題目。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the information in the text.","zh":"陳述可能與文本資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"與資料相矛盾，是指說出與文本所說相反的內容。"},{"en":"If a passage says a service is expensive, a statement saying it is cheap may contradict the information.","zh":"如果篇章說一項服務昂貴，而陳述說它便宜，就可能與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be based on clear evidence from the passage.","zh":"矛盾必須基於篇章中的清楚證據。"},{"en":"This phrase usually points to a FALSE answer.","zh":"這個短語通常指向 FALSE 答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"Students write NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果沒有這方面的資料，學生寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the text does not say whether the point is true or false.","zh":"沒有這方面的資料，是指文本沒有說明該點是真是假。"},{"en":"If a passage mentions a driver but not his age, there is no information on his age.","zh":"如果篇章提到一名司機但沒有提及其年齡，就沒有關於年齡的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from general knowledge when the passage gives no evidence.","zh":"當篇章沒有證據，學生不應根據常識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase corresponds to a NOT GIVEN answer.","zh":"這個短語對應 NOT GIVEN 答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"overcome legal and safety obstacles","meaning":"克服法律和安全障礙","examples":[{"en":"Driverless technology must overcome legal and safety obstacles.","zh":"無人駕駛技術必須克服法律和安全障礙。"},{"en":"To overcome legal and safety obstacles means to solve problems involving law and public protection.","zh":"克服法律和安全障礙，是指解決涉及法律和公眾保護的問題。"},{"en":"A new medicine must overcome legal and safety obstacles before doctors can prescribe it.","zh":"新藥在醫生可處方前，必須克服法律和安全障礙。"},{"en":"If these obstacles remain, the technology may not be widely used.","zh":"如果這些障礙仍存在，技術可能無法廣泛使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes removing major barriers to acceptance.","zh":"這個短語描述移除通往接受的主要障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"legal and safety obstacles","meaning":"法律和安全障礙","examples":[{"en":"Driverless cars face legal and safety obstacles.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車面對法律和安全障礙。"},{"en":"Legal and safety obstacles are barriers involving laws, rules, accidents or public protection.","zh":"法律和安全障礙，是涉及法律、規則、意外或公眾保護的阻礙。"},{"en":"A new school bus system may face legal and safety obstacles before approval.","zh":"新校巴系統在獲批准前可能面對法律和安全障礙。"},{"en":"These obstacles can slow down a useful technology even when the idea is popular.","zh":"即使想法受歡迎，這些障礙也可以拖慢有用科技。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rule-based and risk-based problems.","zh":"這個短語描述基於規則和風險的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"become completely viable","meaning":"變得完全可行","examples":[{"en":"Driverless technology must overcome obstacles to become completely viable.","zh":"無人駕駛技術必須克服障礙，才會變得完全可行。"},{"en":"To become completely viable means to become fully practical, workable and likely to succeed.","zh":"變得完全可行，是指變得完全實際、可運作並可能成功。"},{"en":"A small business idea becomes viable when it can earn enough money to survive.","zh":"當小生意構想能賺取足夠金錢維持下去，它就變得可行。"},{"en":"Technology is not completely viable until it works safely, legally and affordably.","zh":"科技必須安全、合法且價格可負擔，才算完全可行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming fully workable in real life.","zh":"這個短語描述在現實生活中變得完全可運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"show complete confidence in","meaning":"對……表現出完全信心","examples":[{"en":"Uber has not shown complete confidence in driverless taxis.","zh":"Uber 並未對無人駕駛的士表現出完全信心。"},{"en":"To show complete confidence in something means to act as if one fully believes it will succeed.","zh":"對某事表現出完全信心，是指行動上顯示完全相信它會成功。"},{"en":"A teacher shows complete confidence in a student by giving them responsibility for a class activity.","zh":"老師讓學生負責班級活動，就是對學生表現出完全信心。"},{"en":"If a company still prepares backup plans, it may not have complete confidence in one solution.","zh":"如果公司仍準備後備計劃，它可能並未對單一方案有完全信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes full trust shown through action.","zh":"這個短語描述透過行動顯示完全信任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"investment in","meaning":"對……的投資","examples":[{"en":"Uber’s investment in driverless cars may involve risk.","zh":"Uber 對無人駕駛汽車的投資可能涉及風險。"},{"en":"Investment in something means money, time or resources put into it to gain future benefit.","zh":"對某事的投資，是把金錢、時間或資源投入其中，以獲得未來好處。"},{"en":"A family’s investment in education may include tuition fees, books and time.","zh":"家庭對教育的投資可能包括學費、書本和時間。"},{"en":"Investment can bring reward, but it can also fail if the project does not succeed.","zh":"投資可以帶來回報，但如果項目不成功，也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes resources committed to a future goal.","zh":"這個短語描述投入未來目標的資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"safety issues","meaning":"安全問題","examples":[{"en":"Safety issues remain a concern for driverless technology.","zh":"安全問題仍是無人駕駛技術的顧慮。"},{"en":"Safety issues are problems or questions about whether something may cause harm.","zh":"安全問題是關於某事是否可能造成傷害的問題或疑問。"},{"en":"A school laboratory has safety issues if chemicals are not stored properly.","zh":"如果化學品沒有妥善儲存，學校實驗室就有安全問題。"},{"en":"If safety issues are unresolved, people may hesitate to use a new product.","zh":"如果安全問題未解決，人們可能猶豫是否使用新產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes risks that must be addressed.","zh":"這個短語描述必須處理的風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be likely to be resolved","meaning":"可能會被解決","examples":[{"en":"The safety issues may not be likely to be resolved quickly.","zh":"這些安全問題可能不會很快被解決。"},{"en":"To be likely to be resolved means to be expected to be solved.","zh":"可能會被解決，是指預期問題會得到處理。"},{"en":"A simple timetable problem is likely to be resolved after one meeting.","zh":"簡單時間表問題可能在一次會議後被解決。"},{"en":"Complex safety issues may take years of testing and legal discussion.","zh":"複雜安全問題可能需要多年測試和法律討論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the probability that a problem will be solved.","zh":"這個短語描述問題被解決的可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"fairly quickly","meaning":"相當迅速地","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether safety issues will be resolved fairly quickly.","zh":"題目問安全問題是否會相當迅速地被解決。"},{"en":"Fairly quickly means rather soon or in a reasonably short time.","zh":"相當迅速地，是指頗快或在合理短時間內。"},{"en":"A small computer problem may be fixed fairly quickly by the IT teacher.","zh":"小型電腦問題可能由資訊科技老師相當迅速地修好。"},{"en":"Major legal and safety problems usually cannot be solved fairly quickly.","zh":"重大法律和安全問題通常不能相當迅速地解決。"},{"en":"This phrase describes speed that is quite fast, but not instant.","zh":"這個短語描述頗快但不是立即的速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 72 - Driverless cars.pdf","sourcePage":22}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 73":[{"front":"all you need to know about","meaning":"關於……你需要知道的一切","examples":[{"en":"The passage gives readers all they need to know about snow.","zh":"文章給讀者關於雪所需要知道的一切。"},{"en":"All you need to know about something means the main information needed to understand it clearly.","zh":"all you need to know about something 指理解某事所需的主要資料。"},{"en":"A guide called “All you need to know about exam registration” should explain dates, fees, documents, and rules.","zh":"名為「關於考試報名你需要知道的一切」的指南，應解釋日期、費用、文件和規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a text gives a complete beginner-friendly overview.","zh":"當文本提供完整而適合初學者的概覽時，可以使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It does not mean every tiny detail; it means the important points readers need.","zh":"它不是指每一個微小細節，而是讀者需要的重要重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"types of snowfall","meaning":"降雪類型","examples":[{"en":"The first section explains different types of snowfall.","zh":"第一部分解釋不同降雪類型。"},{"en":"Types of snowfall are different ways snow can form or fall under different weather conditions.","zh":"types of snowfall 指雪在不同天氣條件下形成或降下的不同方式。"},{"en":"A weather lesson may compare lake-effect snow, mountain snow, and snow from weather fronts.","zh":"天氣課可能比較湖泊效應雪、山區降雪和鋒面降雪。"},{"en":"Knowing the types of snowfall helps forecasters explain why some places get heavier snow than others.","zh":"了解降雪類型有助天氣預報員解釋為何某些地方下雪較多。"},{"en":"This phrase groups snowfall by cause, pattern, or environment.","zh":"這個短語按成因、模式或環境把降雪分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be typically the product of","meaning":"通常是……的產物","examples":[{"en":"Snow is typically the product of certain weather conditions.","zh":"雪通常是某些天氣狀況的產物。"},{"en":"To be typically the product of something means to usually result from it.","zh":"be typically the product of something 指通常由某事造成。"},{"en":"Traffic jams are typically the product of too many cars and too little road space.","zh":"交通擠塞通常是車輛太多和道路空間太少的產物。"},{"en":"If a result is typically the product of certain causes, those causes usually appear before it.","zh":"如果某結果通常是某些原因的產物，那些原因通常會先出現。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the normal cause behind a situation.","zh":"這個短語解釋某情況背後的一般原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"weather conditions","meaning":"天氣狀況","examples":[{"en":"Snow depends on particular weather conditions in the atmosphere.","zh":"雪取決於大氣中特定的天氣狀況。"},{"en":"Weather conditions are the state of the air, including temperature, wind, humidity, and precipitation.","zh":"weather conditions 指空氣狀態，包括溫度、風、濕度和降水。"},{"en":"A school sports day may be cancelled if weather conditions become unsafe.","zh":"如果天氣狀況變得不安全，學校運動會可能取消。"},{"en":"Weather conditions affect whether rain, snow, fog, or storms develop.","zh":"天氣狀況會影響雨、雪、霧或風暴是否形成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the atmospheric situation at a certain time and place.","zh":"這個短語描述某時某地的大氣情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"extratropical cyclone","meaning":"溫帶氣旋","examples":[{"en":"Snow can form when an extratropical cyclone has developed.","zh":"當溫帶氣旋形成後，雪可以形成。"},{"en":"An extratropical cyclone is a large weather system outside the tropics that can bring wind, rain, or snow.","zh":"extratropical cyclone 指熱帶以外的大型天氣系統，可帶來風、雨或雪。"},{"en":"A winter storm warning may mention an extratropical cyclone moving across the ocean.","zh":"冬季風暴警告可能提到一個溫帶氣旋正移過海洋。"},{"en":"Such systems can become dangerous when they bring strong winds and heavy precipitation.","zh":"當這類系統帶來強風和強降水，就可能變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is a technical weather term for a major mid-latitude storm system.","zh":"這個短語是指中緯度大型風暴系統的技術性天氣術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"has formed","meaning":"已形成","examples":[{"en":"An extratropical cyclone has formed under certain weather conditions.","zh":"溫帶氣旋在某些天氣條件下已形成。"},{"en":"Has formed means has developed or come into existence.","zh":"has formed 指已發展出來或已出現。"},{"en":"A queue has formed outside the clinic when many patients arrive before opening time.","zh":"當許多病人在開門前到達，診所外已形成隊伍。"},{"en":"Once a weather system has formed, forecasters can track where it may move next.","zh":"一旦天氣系統已形成，預報員就可以追蹤它下一步可能移向哪裡。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a process of development is now complete enough to notice.","zh":"這個短語顯示某個發展過程已完成到可以被注意的程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"bring hazardous weather","meaning":"帶來危險天氣","examples":[{"en":"Extratropical cyclones can bring hazardous weather.","zh":"溫帶氣旋可以帶來危險天氣。"},{"en":"To bring hazardous weather means to cause dangerous weather conditions.","zh":"bring hazardous weather 指造成危險的天氣狀況。"},{"en":"A typhoon can bring hazardous weather such as flooding, falling trees, and rough seas.","zh":"颱風可以帶來水浸、塌樹和大浪等危險天氣。"},{"en":"Hazardous weather may close schools, delay transport, and endanger people outdoors.","zh":"危險天氣可能令學校停課、交通延誤，並危及戶外人士。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a weather system with danger.","zh":"這個短語把天氣系統與危險連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"extremely hazardous weather","meaning":"極度危險的天氣","examples":[{"en":"Extratropical cyclones bring extremely hazardous weather.","zh":"溫帶氣旋帶來極度危險的天氣。"},{"en":"Extremely hazardous weather means weather that is very dangerous and may cause serious harm.","zh":"extremely hazardous weather 指非常危險、可能造成嚴重傷害的天氣。"},{"en":"Heavy snow, freezing roads, and violent winds can create extremely hazardous weather for drivers.","zh":"大雪、結冰道路和猛烈強風可以為司機造成極度危險的天氣。"},{"en":"When weather becomes extremely hazardous, people may be told to stay indoors.","zh":"當天氣變得極度危險，人們可能被要求留在室內。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a high level of weather danger.","zh":"這個短語強調高度天氣危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"high winds","meaning":"強風","examples":[{"en":"High winds may accompany an extratropical cyclone.","zh":"強風可能伴隨溫帶氣旋出現。"},{"en":"High winds are strong winds that can make travel and outdoor activity unsafe.","zh":"high winds 指可能令交通和戶外活動不安全的強烈風力。"},{"en":"High winds may blow umbrellas inside out and knock branches onto roads.","zh":"強風可能把雨傘吹反，並把樹枝吹到道路上。"},{"en":"If high winds arrive with rain or snow, visibility and safety can worsen quickly.","zh":"如果強風伴隨雨或雪出現，能見度和安全情況可能迅速惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wind strong enough to create problems.","zh":"這個短語描述強到足以造成問題的風。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"heavy rain or snow","meaning":"大雨或大雪","examples":[{"en":"Extratropical cyclones may bring heavy rain or snow.","zh":"溫帶氣旋可能帶來大雨或大雪。"},{"en":"Heavy rain or snow means a large amount of rain or snow falling within a period of time.","zh":"heavy rain or snow 指一段時間內有大量雨或雪降下。"},{"en":"Heavy rain or snow can delay buses, close roads, and make people late for work.","zh":"大雨或大雪可以令巴士延誤、道路封閉，並令人上班遲到。"},{"en":"When heavy precipitation lasts for hours, flooding or deep snow may develop.","zh":"當強降水持續數小時，水浸或深雪可能形成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intense precipitation.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈降水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be referred to as","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"Extratropical cyclones are often referred to as windstorms in Europe.","zh":"溫帶氣旋在歐洲常被稱為風暴。"},{"en":"To be referred to as something means to be called by that name.","zh":"be referred to as something 指被稱作某個名稱。"},{"en":"A school principal may be referred to as the headteacher in British English.","zh":"在英式英語中，學校校長可能被稱為 headteacher。"},{"en":"Different places may refer to the same thing by different names.","zh":"不同地方可能用不同名稱稱呼同一事物。"},{"en":"This phrase explains naming or terminology.","zh":"這個短語解釋命名或術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"windstorms","meaning":"風暴","examples":[{"en":"Extratropical cyclones are often called windstorms in Europe.","zh":"溫帶氣旋在歐洲常被稱為風暴。"},{"en":"Windstorms are storms in which strong winds are the main danger.","zh":"windstorms 指以強風為主要危險的風暴。"},{"en":"A windstorm may damage roofs, trees, signs, and power lines.","zh":"風暴可能損壞屋頂、樹木、路牌和電線。"},{"en":"If a windstorm arrives during heavy rain, transport can become especially dangerous.","zh":"如果風暴在大雨期間到來，交通可能變得特別危險。"},{"en":"This word describes a storm mainly known for powerful wind.","zh":"這個字描述主要以強風為特徵的風暴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"band of precipitation","meaning":"降水帶","examples":[{"en":"A band of precipitation is often associated with a warm front.","zh":"降水帶常與暖鋒有關。"},{"en":"A band of precipitation is a long area where rain, snow, or other precipitation is falling.","zh":"band of precipitation 指一條長形區域，當中有雨、雪或其他降水。"},{"en":"Weather radar may show a band of precipitation moving across a city.","zh":"天氣雷達可能顯示一條降水帶正移過城市。"},{"en":"If the band is wide and slow-moving, rain or snow may last for hours.","zh":"如果降水帶廣闊且移動緩慢，雨或雪可能持續數小時。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a stretched area of falling moisture.","zh":"這個短語描述一片拉長的降水區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be associated with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The band of precipitation is associated with the warm front.","zh":"這條降水帶與暖鋒有關。"},{"en":"To be associated with something means to be connected with it.","zh":"be associated with something 指與某事有連繫。"},{"en":"Exam stress is often associated with poor sleep and last-minute revision.","zh":"考試壓力常與睡眠不足和臨急溫習有關。"},{"en":"When two things are associated, one often appears with or because of the other.","zh":"當兩件事有關，其中一件常會與另一件一起出現或因另一件而出現。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a connection, not always a direct cause.","zh":"這個短語表示連繫，不一定是直接原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"warm front","meaning":"暖鋒","examples":[{"en":"A warm front can be linked to extensive precipitation.","zh":"暖鋒可以與廣泛降水有關。"},{"en":"A warm front is the boundary where warmer air moves into an area of cooler air.","zh":"warm front 指較暖空氣移入較冷空氣區域時形成的邊界。"},{"en":"A weather map may show a warm front approaching before steady rain begins.","zh":"天氣圖可能在持續下雨前顯示暖鋒接近。"},{"en":"Warm fronts often bring broad areas of cloud and precipitation.","zh":"暖鋒常帶來大範圍雲層和降水。"},{"en":"This phrase names a weather boundary involving warmer air.","zh":"這個短語指出涉及較暖空氣的天氣邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"very extensive","meaning":"非常廣闊","examples":[{"en":"The band of precipitation can be very extensive.","zh":"降水帶可以非常廣闊。"},{"en":"Very extensive means covering a very large area.","zh":"very extensive 指覆蓋非常大的範圍。"},{"en":"A school library with very extensive reading materials has books for many subjects and levels.","zh":"有非常廣泛閱讀材料的學校圖書館，會有不同科目和程度的書。"},{"en":"If snowfall is very extensive, several towns may be affected at the same time.","zh":"如果降雪範圍非常廣闊，幾個城鎮可能同時受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses large coverage or range.","zh":"這個短語強調覆蓋範圍或涵蓋程度很大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cold front","meaning":"冷鋒","examples":[{"en":"Snow can result when a warm front and a cold front collide.","zh":"當暖鋒和冷鋒相遇時，可能形成雪。"},{"en":"A cold front is the boundary where colder air pushes into warmer air.","zh":"cold front 指較冷空氣推入較暖空氣時形成的邊界。"},{"en":"A cold front may arrive with strong wind, falling temperatures, and heavy showers.","zh":"冷鋒到來時可能伴隨強風、降溫和大驟雨。"},{"en":"When cold air meets warm moist air, precipitation may become more intense.","zh":"當冷空氣遇上溫暖潮濕空氣，降水可能變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase names a weather boundary involving advancing cold air.","zh":"這個短語指出涉及推進中冷空氣的天氣邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"collide","meaning":"碰撞；相遇","examples":[{"en":"Snow may form when warm and cold fronts collide.","zh":"當暖鋒和冷鋒相遇時，雪可能形成。"},{"en":"To collide means to crash into or meet with force.","zh":"collide 指碰撞或有力地相遇。"},{"en":"Two cyclists may collide if both turn into the same narrow path too quickly.","zh":"如果兩名單車手太快轉入同一條窄路，他們可能碰撞。"},{"en":"When air masses collide, the meeting can create clouds, rain, or snow.","zh":"當氣團相遇，這種相遇可以產生雲、雨或雪。"},{"en":"This word describes a strong meeting between moving things.","zh":"這個字描述移動事物之間的強烈相遇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"snow can result","meaning":"可能形成雪","examples":[{"en":"When the two fronts collide, snow can result.","zh":"當兩個鋒面相遇時，可能形成雪。"},{"en":"Snow can result means snow may happen as a consequence.","zh":"snow can result 指雪可能作為結果出現。"},{"en":"If cold air meets moist air over a city, snow can result overnight.","zh":"如果冷空氣在城市上空遇到潮濕空氣，夜間可能形成雪。"},{"en":"Weather outcomes depend on temperature, moisture, and air movement.","zh":"天氣結果取決於溫度、水分和空氣流動。"},{"en":"This phrase links a weather cause with the possible formation of snow.","zh":"這個短語把天氣原因與雪的可能形成連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"poleward side","meaning":"向極一側","examples":[{"en":"Snow can occur on the poleward side of the precipitation band.","zh":"雪可以在降水帶的向極一側出現。"},{"en":"The poleward side is the side facing or lying closer to the nearest pole.","zh":"poleward side 指面向或較接近最近極地的一側。"},{"en":"In the Northern Hemisphere, the poleward side usually means the northern side.","zh":"在北半球，向極一側通常指北側。"},{"en":"Colder air is often found on the poleward side, so snow is more likely there.","zh":"較冷空氣常位於向極一側，因此那裡較可能下雪。"},{"en":"This phrase gives direction in relation to the poles.","zh":"這個短語以地球兩極作方向參照。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"precipitation band","meaning":"降水帶","examples":[{"en":"Snow may form on one side of the precipitation band.","zh":"雪可能在降水帶的一側形成。"},{"en":"A precipitation band is a long zone where rain, snow, or sleet is falling.","zh":"precipitation band 指雨、雪或雨夾雪降下的長形區域。"},{"en":"On a weather app, a precipitation band may appear as a long strip of coloured radar echoes.","zh":"在天氣應用程式上，降水帶可能顯示為一長條彩色雷達回波。"},{"en":"If temperatures differ across the band, one side may receive rain and the other snow.","zh":"如果降水帶兩側溫度不同，一側可能下雨，另一側可能下雪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the area where precipitation is concentrated.","zh":"這個短語描述降水集中的區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"that is","meaning":"即是；也就是說","examples":[{"en":"That is, snow forms on the northern side in the Northern Hemisphere.","zh":"也就是說，在北半球，雪在北側形成。"},{"en":"That is means in other words or to explain more clearly.","zh":"that is 指換句話說或更清楚地解釋。"},{"en":"The library closes at noon; that is, students must borrow books before lunchtime.","zh":"圖書館中午關門；也就是說，學生必須在午飯前借書。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when they want to clarify a previous point.","zh":"作者想澄清前一句時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a clearer explanation of what was just said.","zh":"這個短語引出對剛才內容更清楚的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Northern Hemisphere","meaning":"北半球","examples":[{"en":"Snow forms on the northern side in the Northern Hemisphere.","zh":"在北半球，雪在北側形成。"},{"en":"The Northern Hemisphere is the half of Earth north of the equator.","zh":"Northern Hemisphere 指赤道以北的地球一半。"},{"en":"Hong Kong, Britain, Canada, and Japan are in the Northern Hemisphere.","zh":"香港、英國、加拿大和日本都位於北半球。"},{"en":"In the Northern Hemisphere, the poleward direction is generally north.","zh":"在北半球，向極方向通常是北方。"},{"en":"This phrase names one half of the planet by position.","zh":"這個短語按位置命名地球的一半。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Southern Hemisphere","meaning":"南半球","examples":[{"en":"Snow forms on the southern side in the Southern Hemisphere.","zh":"在南半球，雪在南側形成。"},{"en":"The Southern Hemisphere is the half of Earth south of the equator.","zh":"Southern Hemisphere 指赤道以南的地球一半。"},{"en":"Australia, New Zealand, and Argentina are partly or wholly in the Southern Hemisphere.","zh":"澳洲、新西蘭和阿根廷部分或全部位於南半球。"},{"en":"In the Southern Hemisphere, the poleward direction is generally south.","zh":"在南半球，向極方向通常是南方。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain why directions change between hemispheres.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋為何不同半球方向會改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lake-effect snow","meaning":"湖泊效應雪","examples":[{"en":"Lake-effect snow is another common type of snowfall.","zh":"湖泊效應雪是另一種常見降雪類型。"},{"en":"Lake-effect snow is snow produced when cold air moves over warmer water and picks up moisture.","zh":"lake-effect snow 指冷空氣移過較暖水面並吸收水分後形成的雪。"},{"en":"A town beside a large lake may receive lake-effect snow while nearby inland areas stay dry.","zh":"大湖旁的城鎮可能出現湖泊效應雪，而附近內陸地區仍然乾燥。"},{"en":"The warmer water feeds moisture into the cold air, producing heavy snow clouds.","zh":"較暖水面把水分供給冷空氣，形成大雪雲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes snow caused by the interaction between water and cold air.","zh":"這個短語描述由水體與冷空氣互動造成的雪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"common snowfall","meaning":"常見降雪","examples":[{"en":"Lake-effect snow is a common form of snowfall.","zh":"湖泊效應雪是一種常見降雪。"},{"en":"Common snowfall means snowfall that happens fairly often in suitable places or seasons.","zh":"common snowfall 指在合適地方或季節相當經常出現的降雪。"},{"en":"In some mountain towns, common snowfall is part of normal winter life.","zh":"在某些山區城鎮，常見降雪是正常冬季生活的一部分。"},{"en":"If snowfall is common, people usually prepare snow tyres, salt, and winter clothing.","zh":"如果降雪常見，人們通常會準備雪胎、鹽和冬季衣物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes snow that is not rare.","zh":"這個短語描述並不罕見的雪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the name suggests that","meaning":"名稱顯示；名稱暗示","examples":[{"en":"The name suggests that this precipitation is associated only with lakes.","zh":"這個名稱暗示這種降水只與湖泊有關。"},{"en":"The name suggests that means the name makes people think something is true.","zh":"the name suggests that 指名稱令人覺得某事是真的。"},{"en":"The name “fast food” suggests that the meal can be prepared quickly.","zh":"“fast food” 這個名稱暗示餐點可以快速準備。"},{"en":"A name can suggest an idea even when the full reality is more complicated.","zh":"名稱可以暗示某個想法，即使完整現實更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what a name seems to imply.","zh":"這個短語引出名稱似乎暗示的意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"this type of precipitation","meaning":"這種降水","examples":[{"en":"This type of precipitation can be generated by narrow bodies of water.","zh":"這種降水可以由狹長水體產生。"},{"en":"This type of precipitation means this particular form of falling moisture, such as snow or rain.","zh":"this type of precipitation 指這一種特定形式的降水，例如雪或雨。"},{"en":"A weather report may explain that this type of precipitation is common near warm lakes in winter.","zh":"天氣報告可能解釋這種降水在冬天較暖湖泊附近很常見。"},{"en":"Different types of precipitation form under different temperature and moisture conditions.","zh":"不同降水類型會在不同溫度和水分條件下形成。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to the specific precipitation being discussed.","zh":"這個短語指回正在討論的特定降水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be associated only with","meaning":"只與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Lake-effect snow is not associated only with lakes.","zh":"湖泊效應雪並不只與湖泊有關。"},{"en":"To be associated only with something means to be linked exclusively with that thing and nothing else.","zh":"be associated only with something 指只與某事有關，而不與其他事有關。"},{"en":"Good leadership is not associated only with managers; students can show it too.","zh":"良好領導力並不只與經理有關；學生也可以展現它。"},{"en":"If something is not associated only with one cause, other causes or settings may also produce it.","zh":"如果某事並不只與一個原因有關，其他原因或環境也可能產生它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for correcting an overly narrow assumption.","zh":"這個短語適合用來修正過於狹窄的假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"narrow body of water","meaning":"狹長水體","examples":[{"en":"Any narrow body of water may generate lake-effect snow.","zh":"任何狹長水體都可能產生湖泊效應雪。"},{"en":"A narrow body of water is a long, thin area of water such as a lake, strait, or channel.","zh":"narrow body of water 指長而窄的水域，例如湖、海峽或水道。"},{"en":"A town beside a narrow body of water may experience special local weather.","zh":"位於狹長水體旁的城鎮可能經歷特殊本地天氣。"},{"en":"If cold air crosses warmer water, the water can add moisture to the air.","zh":"如果冷空氣越過較暖水面，水體可以為空氣增加水分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a water area by its shape.","zh":"這個短語按形狀描述水域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"generate it","meaning":"產生它","examples":[{"en":"A narrow body of water may generate lake-effect snow.","zh":"狹長水體可能產生湖泊效應雪。"},{"en":"To generate it means to produce it or cause it to form.","zh":"generate it 指產生它或令它形成。"},{"en":"A busy road can generate noise that disturbs nearby homes.","zh":"繁忙道路可以產生噪音，打擾附近住宅。"},{"en":"Warm water can generate snow clouds when cold air passes over it.","zh":"當冷空氣經過較暖水面，暖水可以產生雪雲。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something acts as the source of a result.","zh":"這個短語顯示某物是某結果的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"water temperature","meaning":"水溫","examples":[{"en":"Lake-effect snow occurs when the water temperature is much higher than the air temperature.","zh":"當水溫遠高於氣溫時，湖泊效應雪會出現。"},{"en":"Water temperature is how warm or cold a body of water is.","zh":"water temperature 指水體有多暖或多冷。"},{"en":"Swimmers check water temperature before entering the sea in winter.","zh":"游泳者冬天入海前會檢查水溫。"},{"en":"A warmer water temperature can add heat and moisture to cold air above it.","zh":"較暖水溫可以為上方冷空氣增加熱力和水分。"},{"en":"This phrase measures the warmth of water, not the air.","zh":"這個短語量度水的溫度，而不是空氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"considerably higher than","meaning":"明顯高於","examples":[{"en":"The water temperature is considerably higher than the air temperature.","zh":"水溫明顯高於氣溫。"},{"en":"Considerably higher than means much higher than, not just slightly higher than.","zh":"considerably higher than 指高很多，而不是只高一點。"},{"en":"A restaurant’s dinner prices may be considerably higher than its lunch prices.","zh":"餐廳晚餐價格可能明顯高於午餐價格。"},{"en":"A large temperature difference can create strong upward movement in the air.","zh":"大溫差可以在空氣中產生強烈上升運動。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a clear and important difference.","zh":"這個短語強調清楚而重要的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"air temperature","meaning":"氣溫","examples":[{"en":"The air temperature above the water may be much lower than the water temperature.","zh":"水面上方的氣溫可能遠低於水溫。"},{"en":"Air temperature is how warm or cold the air is.","zh":"air temperature 指空氣有多暖或多冷。"},{"en":"A weather app shows air temperature so people know what to wear.","zh":"天氣應用程式顯示氣溫，讓人知道穿甚麼。"},{"en":"When air temperature falls below freezing, rain may turn into snow.","zh":"當氣溫降至冰點以下，雨可能變成雪。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the temperature of the atmosphere around us.","zh":"這個短語指我們周圍大氣的溫度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cold front progressing over","meaning":"冷鋒正在移過……","examples":[{"en":"Lake-effect snow can occur when a cold front is progressing over a water mass.","zh":"當冷鋒正在移過水體時，湖泊效應雪可能出現。"},{"en":"A cold front progressing over something means a boundary of cold air is moving across it.","zh":"cold front progressing over something 指冷空氣邊界正移過某物。"},{"en":"A cold front progressing over a lake can make temperatures drop quickly nearby.","zh":"冷鋒正在移過湖泊時，附近氣溫可能迅速下降。"},{"en":"As the cold front moves over warmer water, it can lift moist air and form snow clouds.","zh":"當冷鋒移過較暖水面，它可以抬升潮濕空氣並形成雪雲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cold air advancing across a surface.","zh":"這個短語描述冷空氣向前越過某表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"large water mass","meaning":"大型水體","examples":[{"en":"A cold front may progress over a large water mass.","zh":"冷鋒可能移過大型水體。"},{"en":"A large water mass is a big body of water such as a lake, sea, or wide bay.","zh":"large water mass 指大型水域，例如湖泊、海洋或寬闊海灣。"},{"en":"A city beside a large water mass may have different weather from inland areas.","zh":"位於大型水體旁的城市，天氣可能與內陸地區不同。"},{"en":"Large water masses can store heat and moisture that affect nearby air.","zh":"大型水體可以儲存熱力和水分，影響附近空氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sizeable area of water.","zh":"這個短語描述相當大的水域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"warm, moist air","meaning":"溫暖潮濕的空氣","examples":[{"en":"Warm, moist air is drawn upward during lake-effect snowfall.","zh":"湖泊效應降雪期間，溫暖潮濕的空氣被向上帶動。"},{"en":"Warm, moist air is air that is both relatively warm and full of water vapour.","zh":"warm, moist air 指相對溫暖且含有大量水汽的空氣。"},{"en":"A bathroom after a hot shower is filled with warm, moist air.","zh":"洗熱水澡後的浴室充滿溫暖潮濕的空氣。"},{"en":"When warm, moist air rises and cools, clouds and precipitation may form.","zh":"當溫暖潮濕的空氣上升並冷卻，雲和降水可能形成。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the air that supplies heat and moisture for snow clouds.","zh":"這個短語指出為雪雲提供熱力和水分的空氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be drawn upward","meaning":"被向上帶動","examples":[{"en":"Warm, moist air is drawn upward at a relatively fast rate.","zh":"溫暖潮濕的空氣以相對較快的速度被向上帶動。"},{"en":"To be drawn upward means to be pulled or lifted higher.","zh":"be drawn upward 指被拉動或抬升到較高位置。"},{"en":"Smoke from a fire is drawn upward because hot air rises.","zh":"火災產生的煙會被向上帶動，因為熱空氣上升。"},{"en":"When moist air is drawn upward, it can cool and condense into clouds.","zh":"當潮濕空氣被向上帶動，它可以冷卻並凝結成雲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes upward movement caused by heat or air flow.","zh":"這個短語描述由熱力或氣流造成的向上移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at a relatively fast rate","meaning":"以相對較快的速度","examples":[{"en":"The air rises at a relatively fast rate.","zh":"空氣以相對較快的速度上升。"},{"en":"At a relatively fast rate means fairly quickly compared with another speed or situation.","zh":"at a relatively fast rate 指相對於另一速度或情況而言相當快速。"},{"en":"A student learning vocabulary every day may improve at a relatively fast rate.","zh":"每天學詞彙的學生可能以相對較快的速度進步。"},{"en":"Fast-rising air can form tall clouds more quickly.","zh":"快速上升的空氣可以更快形成高大的雲。"},{"en":"This phrase compares speed rather than giving an exact number.","zh":"這個短語比較速度，而不是給出精確數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"condense to form","meaning":"凝結形成","examples":[{"en":"Warm, moist air condenses to form clouds.","zh":"溫暖潮濕的空氣凝結形成雲。"},{"en":"To condense to form something means water vapour cools and changes into droplets or ice that create it.","zh":"condense to form something 指水汽冷卻並變成水滴或冰，從而形成某物。"},{"en":"Steam may condense to form water drops on a cold kitchen window.","zh":"蒸汽可能在冰冷廚房窗戶上凝結形成水滴。"},{"en":"When moist air condenses, clouds, fog, rain, or snow may develop.","zh":"當潮濕空氣凝結，雲、霧、雨或雪可能形成。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how invisible moisture becomes visible.","zh":"這個短語解釋看不見的水分如何變得可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"vertically oriented clouds","meaning":"垂直取向的雲；垂直發展的雲","examples":[{"en":"The rising air condenses to form vertically oriented clouds.","zh":"上升空氣凝結形成垂直發展的雲。"},{"en":"Vertically oriented clouds are clouds that grow upward more than sideways.","zh":"vertically oriented clouds 指向上生長多於橫向擴展的雲。"},{"en":"Tall storm clouds are vertically oriented when they build high into the sky.","zh":"當高大風暴雲向天空高處發展時，就是垂直取向的雲。"},{"en":"Strong rising air can create vertical clouds that produce heavy rain or snow.","zh":"強烈上升氣流可以形成會帶來大雨或大雪的垂直雲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clouds with strong upward development.","zh":"這個短語描述具有強烈向上發展的雲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"temperature difference","meaning":"溫差","examples":[{"en":"A significant temperature difference can lead to heavy snowfall.","zh":"顯著溫差可以導致大雪。"},{"en":"Temperature difference means the gap between two temperatures.","zh":"temperature difference 指兩個溫度之間的差距。"},{"en":"A large temperature difference between indoors and outdoors can make windows misty.","zh":"室內和室外的巨大溫差可以令窗戶起霧。"},{"en":"In lake-effect snow, the difference between warm water and cold air drives cloud formation.","zh":"在湖泊效應雪中，暖水和冷空氣之間的溫差推動雲形成。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how far apart two temperatures are.","zh":"這個短語集中於兩個溫度相差多遠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the body of water","meaning":"水體","examples":[{"en":"The body of water may be much warmer than the air above it.","zh":"該水體可能比上方空氣暖得多。"},{"en":"The body of water means the lake, sea, river, or other area of water being discussed.","zh":"body of water 指正在討論的湖、海、河或其他水域。"},{"en":"A small town may be built beside a body of water for fishing and transport.","zh":"小鎮可能建於水體旁，以便捕魚和交通。"},{"en":"A warm body of water can supply moisture to passing air.","zh":"較暖水體可以為經過的空氣提供水分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific water area.","zh":"這個短語指特定水域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the air above","meaning":"上方的空氣","examples":[{"en":"The air above the water can be much colder.","zh":"水面上方的空氣可能冷得多。"},{"en":"The air above means the layer of air directly over a place or object.","zh":"the air above 指某地方或物件正上方的一層空氣。"},{"en":"The air above a hot road may shimmer in summer.","zh":"夏天時，熱路面上方的空氣可能看似閃動。"},{"en":"If the air above water is much colder than the water, rising moisture can form clouds.","zh":"如果水面上方的空氣比水冷得多，上升水分可以形成雲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the air located over something.","zh":"這個短語描述位於某物上方的空氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"significant","meaning":"顯著的","examples":[{"en":"A significant temperature difference may produce heavy snowfall.","zh":"顯著溫差可能產生大雪。"},{"en":"Significant means important, large enough to matter, or clearly noticeable.","zh":"significant 指重要、足以產生影響或清楚可見。"},{"en":"A significant drop in marks may show that a student needs help.","zh":"成績顯著下降可能顯示學生需要幫助。"},{"en":"Significant weather changes can affect transport, safety, and school schedules.","zh":"顯著天氣變化可以影響交通、安全和學校時間表。"},{"en":"This word stresses that something is not minor.","zh":"這個字強調某事並非微小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"result in","meaning":"導致；造成","examples":[{"en":"A large temperature difference can result in heavy snowfall.","zh":"大溫差可以導致大雪。"},{"en":"To result in something means to cause it to happen.","zh":"result in something 指造成某事發生。"},{"en":"Poor planning can result in late homework and unnecessary stress.","zh":"規劃不足可以導致功課遲交和不必要壓力。"},{"en":"In weather, small changes in temperature can result in rain instead of snow.","zh":"在天氣中，溫度小變化可以導致下雨而不是下雪。"},{"en":"This phrase shows cause and effect.","zh":"這個短語顯示因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"heavy and prolonged snowfall","meaning":"大而持續的降雪","examples":[{"en":"The temperature difference can result in heavy and prolonged snowfall.","zh":"溫差可以導致大而持續的降雪。"},{"en":"Heavy and prolonged snowfall means a lot of snow falling for a long time.","zh":"heavy and prolonged snowfall 指大量雪長時間降下。"},{"en":"Heavy and prolonged snowfall may close mountain roads for several days.","zh":"大而持續的降雪可能令山路封閉數天。"},{"en":"Long-lasting snow can build up, making travel and clearing work difficult.","zh":"持續降雪會累積，使交通和清理工作變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes snowfall that is both intense and extended.","zh":"這個短語描述既強烈又持久的降雪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mountainous areas","meaning":"山區","examples":[{"en":"Mountainous areas are also prone to heavy snowfall.","zh":"山區也容易出現大雪。"},{"en":"Mountainous areas are places with many mountains or high slopes.","zh":"mountainous areas 指有許多山或高斜坡的地方。"},{"en":"Mountainous areas often have colder temperatures than nearby lowlands.","zh":"山區氣溫通常比附近低地更低。"},{"en":"When moist air rises over mountains, snow may fall heavily on the slopes.","zh":"當潮濕空氣越過山脈上升，山坡上可能下大雪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes high, uneven regions where weather can change quickly.","zh":"這個短語描述高而不平坦、天氣可快速變化的地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be prone to","meaning":"容易出現","examples":[{"en":"Mountainous areas are prone to experiencing heavy snowfall.","zh":"山區容易出現大雪。"},{"en":"To be prone to something means to be likely to experience it.","zh":"be prone to something 指較可能經歷某事。"},{"en":"A student who sleeps late is prone to feeling tired in morning lessons.","zh":"晚睡的學生容易在早上課堂感到疲倦。"},{"en":"Places prone to heavy snow need stronger roofs and safer roads.","zh":"容易出現大雪的地方需要更堅固的屋頂和更安全的道路。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a tendency or higher risk.","zh":"這個短語描述傾向或較高風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"accumulations","meaning":"積雪","examples":[{"en":"Snow accumulations typically occur on the windward side of a mountain.","zh":"積雪通常出現在山的迎風面。"},{"en":"Accumulations are amounts of something that build up over time.","zh":"accumulations 指某物隨時間累積起來的數量。"},{"en":"Dust accumulations on a shelf show that it has not been cleaned for weeks.","zh":"架上的塵埃積聚顯示它已數星期沒有清潔。"},{"en":"Snow accumulations can block roads and increase avalanche risk.","zh":"積雪可以堵塞道路並增加雪崩風險。"},{"en":"This word describes material that has gathered or piled up.","zh":"這個字描述聚集或堆積起來的物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"typically occur","meaning":"通常發生","examples":[{"en":"Accumulations typically occur on the windward side of the mountain.","zh":"積雪通常發生在山的迎風面。"},{"en":"Typically occur means usually happen in a particular place or situation.","zh":"typically occur 指通常在某地方或情況下發生。"},{"en":"Traffic jams typically occur near schools during morning drop-off time.","zh":"交通擠塞通常發生在早上送學生上學時的學校附近。"},{"en":"If something typically occurs in one place, people can prepare for it there.","zh":"如果某事通常發生在一個地方，人們可以在那裡作準備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a usual pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述常見模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"windward side","meaning":"迎風面","examples":[{"en":"Snow often accumulates on the windward side of a mountain.","zh":"雪常在山的迎風面累積。"},{"en":"The windward side is the side facing the incoming wind.","zh":"windward side 指面向來風的一側。"},{"en":"The windward side of a hill may be wetter because moist air rises there.","zh":"山丘的迎風面可能較潮濕，因為潮濕空氣在那裡上升。"},{"en":"When air rises on the windward side, it cools and may produce rain or snow.","zh":"當空氣在迎風面上升，它會冷卻並可能產生雨或雪。"},{"en":"This phrase gives direction based on where the wind comes from.","zh":"這個短語根據風從哪裡來給出方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be squeezed out of","meaning":"從……被擠出","examples":[{"en":"Precipitation is squeezed out of warm moist air.","zh":"降水從溫暖潮濕的空氣中被擠出。"},{"en":"To be squeezed out of something means to be forced out of it by pressure or cooling.","zh":"be squeezed out of something 指因壓力或冷卻而被迫從某物中出來。"},{"en":"Water is squeezed out of a wet towel when someone twists it tightly.","zh":"扭緊濕毛巾時，水會被擠出。"},{"en":"When moist air rises and cools, water can be squeezed out as rain or snow.","zh":"當潮濕空氣上升並冷卻，水分可以以雨或雪的形式被擠出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moisture being forced out of air.","zh":"這個短語描述水分被迫從空氣中釋出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"warm moist air","meaning":"溫暖潮濕的空氣","examples":[{"en":"Heavy snowfall can occur when warm moist air rises over mountains.","zh":"當溫暖潮濕的空氣越過山脈上升時，可能出現大雪。"},{"en":"Warm moist air is air that contains heat and plenty of water vapour.","zh":"warm moist air 指含有熱力和大量水汽的空氣。"},{"en":"Warm moist air from a bathroom can fog up a mirror.","zh":"浴室中的溫暖潮濕空氣可以令鏡子起霧。"},{"en":"When warm moist air is lifted into colder areas, clouds and precipitation may form.","zh":"當溫暖潮濕的空氣被抬升至較冷地區，雲和降水可能形成。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies air that can supply moisture for rain or snow.","zh":"這個短語指出能為雨或雪提供水分的空氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be forced to ascend","meaning":"被迫上升","examples":[{"en":"The air is forced to ascend the mountain slopes.","zh":"空氣被迫沿山坡上升。"},{"en":"To be forced to ascend means to be pushed upward.","zh":"be forced to ascend 指被推動向上移動。"},{"en":"Smoke may be forced to ascend quickly if hot air rises through a narrow chimney.","zh":"如果熱空氣穿過狹窄煙囪上升，煙可能被迫快速上升。"},{"en":"When wind pushes moist air up a mountain, the air cools and moisture condenses.","zh":"當風把潮濕空氣推上山，空氣會冷卻，水分會凝結。"},{"en":"This phrase describes upward movement caused by terrain or pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述由地形或壓力造成的向上移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ascend the slopes","meaning":"沿山坡上升","examples":[{"en":"Warm air ascends the slopes and cools at higher altitudes.","zh":"暖空氣沿山坡上升，並在較高海拔冷卻。"},{"en":"To ascend the slopes means to move upward along the sides of a mountain or hill.","zh":"ascend the slopes 指沿着山或丘陵的側面向上移動。"},{"en":"Hikers ascend the slopes slowly because steep paths are tiring.","zh":"行山者沿山坡上升時會慢慢走，因為陡路很吃力。"},{"en":"Air that ascends slopes cools, so moisture inside it may turn into precipitation.","zh":"沿山坡上升的空氣會冷卻，因此其中水分可能變成降水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes upward movement along sloping ground.","zh":"這個短語描述沿斜坡地面向上移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the moisture condenses","meaning":"水分凝結","examples":[{"en":"The moisture condenses when it meets colder air.","zh":"水分遇到較冷空氣時凝結。"},{"en":"The moisture condenses means water vapour changes into tiny droplets or ice.","zh":"the moisture condenses 指水汽變成微小水滴或冰。"},{"en":"Moisture condenses on a cold glass when warm room air touches it.","zh":"當溫暖室內空氣接觸冰冷玻璃，水分會在玻璃上凝結。"},{"en":"Condensed moisture can form clouds, fog, rain, or snow.","zh":"凝結的水分可以形成雲、霧、雨或雪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes water vapour becoming visible or solid.","zh":"這個短語描述水汽變得可見或變成固體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"upon contact with","meaning":"一接觸到……便","examples":[{"en":"The moisture condenses upon contact with colder air.","zh":"水分一接觸到較冷空氣便凝結。"},{"en":"Upon contact with something means immediately when it touches or meets it.","zh":"upon contact with something 指一碰到或遇到某物便立即發生。"},{"en":"Some cleaning chemicals react upon contact with water.","zh":"有些清潔化學品一接觸到水便會反應。"},{"en":"Warm moist air may condense upon contact with a cold surface.","zh":"溫暖潮濕的空氣一接觸到冷表面便可能凝結。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one event happens as soon as two things meet.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩件事一相遇，另一件事便發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"colder air","meaning":"較冷空氣","examples":[{"en":"Moisture condenses when it reaches colder air.","zh":"水分到達較冷空氣時會凝結。"},{"en":"Colder air is air with a lower temperature than the air around it or before it.","zh":"colder air 指比周圍或之前空氣溫度更低的空氣。"},{"en":"Colder air near an open freezer can make your hands feel numb.","zh":"開着的冰格附近較冷空氣可以令你的手感到麻木。"},{"en":"When warm moist air meets colder air, cloud droplets or ice crystals may form.","zh":"當溫暖潮濕空氣遇上較冷空氣，雲滴或冰晶可能形成。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the lower-temperature air that changes moisture.","zh":"這個短語指出會改變水分狀態的較低溫空氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"higher altitudes","meaning":"較高海拔","examples":[{"en":"Colder air is found at higher altitudes.","zh":"較冷空氣可在較高海拔找到。"},{"en":"Higher altitudes are places farther above sea level.","zh":"higher altitudes 指離海平面更高的地方。"},{"en":"Mountain villages at higher altitudes often feel colder than towns near the coast.","zh":"位於較高海拔的山村通常比海邊城鎮更冷。"},{"en":"As air rises to higher altitudes, it usually cools and may form clouds.","zh":"當空氣上升到較高海拔，它通常會冷卻並可能形成雲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes height above sea level.","zh":"這個短語描述高於海平面的高度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sufficiently cold","meaning":"足夠寒冷","examples":[{"en":"Heavy snowfall can occur if ground conditions are sufficiently cold.","zh":"如果地面條件足夠寒冷，可能出現大雪。"},{"en":"Sufficiently cold means cold enough for a particular result to happen.","zh":"sufficiently cold 指冷到足以讓某結果發生。"},{"en":"Water will freeze outside if the night is sufficiently cold.","zh":"如果夜晚足夠寒冷，戶外的水會結冰。"},{"en":"If the ground is not sufficiently cold, falling snow may melt quickly.","zh":"如果地面不夠寒冷，落下的雪可能很快融化。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that enough coldness is required.","zh":"這個短語顯示需要足夠低溫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ground conditions","meaning":"地面條件","examples":[{"en":"Ground conditions must be sufficiently cold for heavy snowfall.","zh":"地面條件必須足夠寒冷，才會出現大雪。"},{"en":"Ground conditions are the state of the surface, including temperature, wetness, and firmness.","zh":"ground conditions 指地表狀態，包括溫度、濕度和硬度。"},{"en":"A football match may be cancelled if ground conditions are icy or muddy.","zh":"如果地面條件結冰或泥濘，足球比賽可能取消。"},{"en":"Cold ground conditions help snow remain instead of melting on contact.","zh":"寒冷地面條件有助雪停留，而不是一接觸地面就融化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical state of the land surface.","zh":"這個短語描述地表的物理狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"how snow is formed","meaning":"雪是如何形成的","examples":[{"en":"The next section explains how snow is formed.","zh":"下一部分解釋雪是如何形成的。"},{"en":"How snow is formed means the process by which snow develops from moisture in clouds.","zh":"how snow is formed 指雪如何由雲中的水分發展而成的過程。"},{"en":"A science teacher may use diagrams to show how snow is formed in cold clouds.","zh":"科學老師可能用圖解展示雪如何在寒冷雲中形成。"},{"en":"Understanding how snow is formed helps students connect temperature, moisture, and ice crystals.","zh":"理解雪是如何形成的，有助學生連繫溫度、水分和冰晶。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an explanation of a natural process.","zh":"這個短語引入對自然過程的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"snow crystals","meaning":"雪晶","examples":[{"en":"Snow crystals form from supercooled cloud droplets.","zh":"雪晶由過冷雲滴形成。"},{"en":"Snow crystals are tiny ice structures that can grow into snowflakes.","zh":"snow crystals 指可以長成雪花的微小冰結構。"},{"en":"Under a microscope, snow crystals may show delicate branches or simple plates.","zh":"在顯微鏡下，雪晶可能顯示精細分枝或簡單板狀。"},{"en":"Snow crystals grow when water vapour freezes onto existing ice.","zh":"當水汽凍結到已有冰上，雪晶會生長。"},{"en":"This phrase names the small ice forms that make up snow.","zh":"這個短語指出構成雪的小型冰形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"form from","meaning":"由……形成","examples":[{"en":"Snow crystals form from tiny droplets in clouds.","zh":"雪晶由雲中的微小水滴形成。"},{"en":"To form from something means to develop out of that material or starting point.","zh":"form from something 指由某材料或起點發展而成。"},{"en":"Ice cubes form from water when the tray is placed in a freezer.","zh":"當冰格放入冰箱，冰粒由水形成。"},{"en":"Snow forms from cloud moisture when temperatures and particles allow freezing.","zh":"當溫度和粒子容許結冰，雪由雲中水分形成。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what something develops out of.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物由甚麼發展而來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tiny cloud droplets","meaning":"微小雲滴","examples":[{"en":"Snow crystals begin as tiny cloud droplets.","zh":"雪晶最初是微小雲滴。"},{"en":"Tiny cloud droplets are very small drops of water floating inside clouds.","zh":"tiny cloud droplets 指漂浮在雲中的非常細小水滴。"},{"en":"Fog is made of tiny droplets close to the ground, while cloud droplets float higher in the air.","zh":"霧由接近地面的微小水滴組成，而雲滴漂浮在較高空氣中。"},{"en":"If tiny cloud droplets freeze, they can become the starting point of ice crystals.","zh":"如果微小雲滴結冰，它們可以成為冰晶的起點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the small water drops inside clouds.","zh":"這個短語描述雲內的小水滴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"supercooled cloud droplets","meaning":"過冷雲滴","examples":[{"en":"Snow crystals form from tiny, supercooled cloud droplets.","zh":"雪晶由微小的過冷雲滴形成。"},{"en":"Supercooled cloud droplets are liquid water droplets that remain unfrozen even below freezing temperature.","zh":"supercooled cloud droplets 指溫度低於冰點但仍未結冰的液態水滴。"},{"en":"Supercooled droplets can freeze quickly when they touch an ice nucleus.","zh":"過冷水滴一碰到冰核，就可能迅速結冰。"},{"en":"Their unusual state helps snow crystals begin forming inside cold clouds.","zh":"這種特殊狀態有助雪晶在冷雲內開始形成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes water droplets colder than freezing but still liquid.","zh":"這個短語描述低於冰點但仍是液態的水滴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"extremely low temperatures","meaning":"極低溫","examples":[{"en":"Snow crystals form at extremely low temperatures in the atmosphere.","zh":"雪晶在大氣中的極低溫下形成。"},{"en":"Extremely low temperatures are temperatures far below ordinary cold conditions.","zh":"extremely low temperatures 指遠低於普通寒冷狀態的溫度。"},{"en":"Food freezes quickly in extremely low temperatures inside an industrial freezer.","zh":"食物在工業冰箱的極低溫下會迅速結冰。"},{"en":"Very low temperatures can make water freeze without needing much outside help.","zh":"極低溫可以令水不太需要外來幫助便結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses intense cold.","zh":"這個短語強調極端寒冷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in the atmosphere","meaning":"在大氣中","examples":[{"en":"Snow crystals form in the atmosphere.","zh":"雪晶在大氣中形成。"},{"en":"In the atmosphere means in the layer of gases surrounding Earth.","zh":"in the atmosphere 指在圍繞地球的氣體層中。"},{"en":"Clouds, winds, rain, and snow all develop in the atmosphere.","zh":"雲、風、雨和雪都在大氣中發展。"},{"en":"Changes in the atmosphere affect weather at the ground.","zh":"大氣中的變化會影響地面的天氣。"},{"en":"This phrase places a process in the air above Earth.","zh":"這個短語把某過程放在地球上方的空氣中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lower than","meaning":"低於","examples":[{"en":"Temperatures lower than minus 35 degrees Celsius are required.","zh":"需要低於攝氏零下35度的溫度。"},{"en":"Lower than means below a particular level, number, or standard.","zh":"lower than 指低於某個水平、數字或標準。"},{"en":"A score lower than 50 may mean the student has failed the test.","zh":"分數低於50可能表示學生測驗不合格。"},{"en":"If the temperature is lower than freezing, water may turn into ice.","zh":"如果溫度低於冰點，水可能變成冰。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one amount with a reference point.","zh":"這個短語把某數量與參照點比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"minus 35 degrees Celsius","meaning":"攝氏零下 35 度","examples":[{"en":"Supercooled moisture can freeze by itself below minus 35 degrees Celsius.","zh":"過冷水分在攝氏零下35度以下可以自行結冰。"},{"en":"Minus 35 degrees Celsius means 35 degrees below zero on the Celsius scale.","zh":"minus 35 degrees Celsius 指攝氏溫標中低於零度35度。"},{"en":"A place at minus 35 degrees Celsius is dangerously cold for exposed skin.","zh":"攝氏零下35度的地方對外露皮膚而言非常危險。"},{"en":"Such low temperatures can allow moisture to freeze without a particle to start the process.","zh":"如此低溫可以讓水分在沒有粒子啟動過程下結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a precise temperature below freezing.","zh":"這個短語給出低於冰點的精確溫度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be required for","meaning":"……是必需的","examples":[{"en":"Very low temperatures are required for the moisture to freeze by itself.","zh":"水分要自行結冰，極低溫是必需的。"},{"en":"To be required for something means to be necessary for it to happen.","zh":"be required for something 指某事發生所必需。"},{"en":"A password is required for students to enter the online learning system.","zh":"學生登入網上學習系統需要密碼。"},{"en":"If a condition is required, the process may not happen without it.","zh":"如果某條件是必需的，沒有它過程可能不會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a necessary condition.","zh":"這個短語指出必要條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"supercooled moisture","meaning":"過冷水分","examples":[{"en":"Supercooled moisture needs very low temperatures to freeze by itself.","zh":"過冷水分需要極低溫才能自行結冰。"},{"en":"Supercooled moisture is water that remains liquid even though it is below freezing temperature.","zh":"supercooled moisture 指溫度低於冰點但仍保持液態的水。"},{"en":"Supercooled moisture in clouds can suddenly freeze when it meets dust or ice.","zh":"雲中的過冷水分遇到塵埃或冰時，可能突然結冰。"},{"en":"This moisture is important because it can grow into ice crystals.","zh":"這些水分很重要，因為它可以長成冰晶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unusually cold liquid water in the air.","zh":"這個短語描述空氣中異常寒冷的液態水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"freeze by itself","meaning":"自行結冰","examples":[{"en":"Supercooled moisture can freeze by itself at extremely low temperatures.","zh":"過冷水分在極低溫下可以自行結冰。"},{"en":"To freeze by itself means to turn into ice without needing a particle or outside trigger.","zh":"freeze by itself 指不需要粒子或外來觸發便變成冰。"},{"en":"Water in a bottle may freeze by itself if it is left outside on a very cold night.","zh":"如果水樽在非常寒冷的夜晚被放在室外，水可能自行結冰。"},{"en":"In clouds, moisture may need extremely low temperatures to freeze without help.","zh":"在雲中，水分可能需要極低溫才可在沒有幫助下結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes freezing that happens naturally without a starting particle.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有起始粒子也自然發生的結冰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"warmer clouds","meaning":"較暖的雲","examples":[{"en":"In warmer clouds, a particle is needed for freezing to start.","zh":"在較暖的雲中，需要粒子讓結冰開始。"},{"en":"Warmer clouds are clouds that are not cold enough for water to freeze easily by itself.","zh":"warmer clouds 指未冷到足以讓水容易自行結冰的雲。"},{"en":"Warmer clouds may still contain supercooled droplets below freezing temperature.","zh":"較暖的雲仍可能含有低於冰點的過冷水滴。"},{"en":"If a cloud is warmer, dust or another particle may be needed to begin ice formation.","zh":"如果雲較暖，可能需要塵埃或其他粒子開始形成冰。"},{"en":"This phrase compares clouds by temperature.","zh":"這個短語按溫度比較雲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"aerosol particle","meaning":"氣溶膠粒子","examples":[{"en":"An aerosol particle may help freezing begin in a warmer cloud.","zh":"氣溶膠粒子可能幫助較暖雲中的結冰開始。"},{"en":"An aerosol particle is a tiny solid or liquid particle floating in the air.","zh":"aerosol particle 指漂浮在空氣中的微小固體或液體粒子。"},{"en":"Dust, sea salt, and smoke can contain aerosol particles.","zh":"塵埃、海鹽和煙霧都可以含有氣溶膠粒子。"},{"en":"Aerosol particles can give water droplets a surface on which to freeze.","zh":"氣溶膠粒子可以為水滴提供一個可結冰的表面。"},{"en":"This phrase names a tiny airborne particle that can affect clouds.","zh":"這個短語指出能影響雲的微小空氣粒子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"desert dust","meaning":"沙漠塵埃","examples":[{"en":"Desert dust can act as a particle that helps freezing begin.","zh":"沙漠塵埃可以作為幫助結冰開始的粒子。"},{"en":"Desert dust is fine dust blown from dry desert regions into the air.","zh":"desert dust 指從乾旱沙漠地區被風吹入空氣中的細塵。"},{"en":"Winds can carry desert dust across seas and into distant countries.","zh":"風可以把沙漠塵埃帶過海洋，送到遙遠國家。"},{"en":"In clouds, desert dust may help ice crystals start forming.","zh":"在雲中，沙漠塵埃可能幫助冰晶開始形成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes natural dust that can influence weather processes.","zh":"這個短語描述能影響天氣過程的自然塵埃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ice nucleus","meaning":"冰核","examples":[{"en":"An ice nucleus is needed for freezing to start in warmer clouds.","zh":"在較暖的雲中，需要冰核讓結冰開始。"},{"en":"An ice nucleus is a tiny particle that helps water freeze into ice.","zh":"ice nucleus 指幫助水結冰成冰的微小粒子。"},{"en":"Dust can act as an ice nucleus when cloud droplets attach to it and freeze.","zh":"當雲滴附着在塵埃上並結冰，塵埃可以作為冰核。"},{"en":"Without an ice nucleus, warmer cloud droplets may remain liquid for longer.","zh":"沒有冰核，較暖雲滴可能保持液態更久。"},{"en":"This phrase names the starting point for ice formation.","zh":"這個短語指出冰形成的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"for the freezing to start","meaning":"讓結冰開始","examples":[{"en":"A particle is needed for the freezing to start.","zh":"需要一個粒子讓結冰開始。"},{"en":"For the freezing to start means so that the process of becoming ice can begin.","zh":"for the freezing to start 指讓變成冰的過程可以開始。"},{"en":"In some science experiments, a seed crystal is needed for crystallisation to start.","zh":"在某些科學實驗中，需要晶種讓結晶開始。"},{"en":"Once freezing starts, more water may attach to the ice and grow.","zh":"一旦結冰開始，更多水分可能附着在冰上並生長。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the beginning of the freezing process.","zh":"這個短語集中於結冰過程的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a droplet of water","meaning":"一滴水","examples":[{"en":"A droplet of water starts to grow after it has frozen.","zh":"一滴水結冰後開始生長。"},{"en":"A droplet of water is a very small drop of water.","zh":"a droplet of water 指非常小的一滴水。"},{"en":"A droplet of water may form on a cold drink glass in summer.","zh":"夏天時，一滴水可能在冰冷飲品杯外形成。"},{"en":"In a cloud, a frozen droplet can become the centre of a growing ice crystal.","zh":"在雲中，結冰的水滴可以成為冰晶生長的中心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a tiny amount of water.","zh":"這個短語描述極少量的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"has frozen","meaning":"已結冰","examples":[{"en":"Once a droplet has frozen, it grows in the cloud.","zh":"一旦水滴已結冰，它便在雲中生長。"},{"en":"Has frozen means has changed from liquid water into ice.","zh":"has frozen 指已由液態水變成冰。"},{"en":"A puddle has frozen when its surface becomes hard and slippery.","zh":"當水窪表面變硬和濕滑，它就已結冰。"},{"en":"After a droplet has frozen, more moisture can collect on it.","zh":"水滴結冰後，更多水分可以聚集在其上。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the completed change from liquid to solid ice.","zh":"這個短語標示由液體變成固體冰的完成變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"supersaturated environment","meaning":"過飽和環境","examples":[{"en":"The frozen droplet grows in the supersaturated environment of the cloud.","zh":"結冰水滴在雲的過飽和環境中生長。"},{"en":"A supersaturated environment contains more water vapour than the air would normally hold at that temperature.","zh":"supersaturated environment 指空氣中含有比該溫度下通常可容納更多的水汽。"},{"en":"A sugary drink becomes supersaturated if more sugar is dissolved than usual.","zh":"如果含糖飲品溶入比平常更多的糖，它就會變成過飽和。"},{"en":"In clouds, supersaturation helps ice crystals grow because extra vapour attaches to them.","zh":"在雲中，過飽和有助冰晶生長，因為額外水汽會附着其上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an environment overloaded with vapour.","zh":"這個短語描述充滿過量水汽的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"eventually","meaning":"最終","examples":[{"en":"Eventually, the cloud can no longer hold the growing ice crystal.","zh":"最終，雲不再能承托正在生長的冰晶。"},{"en":"Eventually means after some time or at the end of a process.","zh":"eventually 指經過一段時間後或在過程結尾。"},{"en":"If a student practises every day, they will eventually speak more confidently.","zh":"如果學生每天練習，最終會說得更有信心。"},{"en":"In weather processes, small changes can eventually produce visible results.","zh":"在天氣過程中，小變化最終可以產生可見結果。"},{"en":"This word shows that something happens later, not immediately.","zh":"這個字顯示某事稍後發生，而不是立即發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ice crystal","meaning":"冰晶","examples":[{"en":"An ice crystal may fall to the ground as snow.","zh":"冰晶可能以雪的形式落到地面。"},{"en":"An ice crystal is a small solid structure made of frozen water.","zh":"ice crystal 指由結冰水構成的小型固體結構。"},{"en":"Frost on a window is made of tiny ice crystals.","zh":"窗戶上的霜由微小冰晶組成。"},{"en":"When ice crystals grow heavy enough, they can fall from clouds.","zh":"當冰晶長到足夠重，它們可以從雲中落下。"},{"en":"This phrase names a basic building block of snow.","zh":"這個短語指出雪的基本構成單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"no longer hold","meaning":"不再能承托","examples":[{"en":"The cloud can no longer hold the ice crystal.","zh":"雲不再能承托冰晶。"},{"en":"To no longer hold something means to be unable to support or contain it anymore.","zh":"no longer hold something 指不再能支撐或容納某物。"},{"en":"A full bag can no longer hold more books without tearing.","zh":"裝滿的袋子不再能承載更多書本，否則可能撕裂。"},{"en":"When an ice crystal becomes too heavy, the cloud can no longer keep it suspended.","zh":"當冰晶變得太重，雲不再能讓它懸浮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the point when support or capacity ends.","zh":"這個短語描述支撐或容量結束的一刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at this point","meaning":"在這一刻；到了這時","examples":[{"en":"At this point, the ice crystal will fall to the ground.","zh":"到了這時，冰晶會落到地面。"},{"en":"At this point means at this stage in a process or situation.","zh":"at this point 指在某過程或情況的這個階段。"},{"en":"A cake is ready when the knife comes out clean; at this point, you can remove it from the oven.","zh":"當刀插入蛋糕後取出仍乾淨，這時就可以把蛋糕從焗爐取出。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show the order of steps in an explanation.","zh":"這個短語有助顯示解釋中的步驟次序。"},{"en":"It introduces what happens next after a condition has been reached.","zh":"它引出某條件達成後接下來發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fall to the ground","meaning":"落到地面","examples":[{"en":"The ice crystal falls to the ground as snow.","zh":"冰晶以雪的形式落到地面。"},{"en":"To fall to the ground means to move downward until reaching the Earth’s surface.","zh":"fall to the ground 指向下移動直到到達地球表面。"},{"en":"Leaves fall to the ground when trees lose them in autumn.","zh":"秋天樹木落葉時，葉子會落到地面。"},{"en":"Snow reaches us only if ice crystals fall without melting on the way down.","zh":"只有冰晶下落途中沒有融化，雪才會到達我們身邊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes downward movement to the surface.","zh":"這個短語描述向下移動至表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"melted by warmer air","meaning":"被較暖空氣融化","examples":[{"en":"The ice crystal may be melted by warmer air at lower altitudes.","zh":"冰晶可能在較低海拔被較暖空氣融化。"},{"en":"Melted by warmer air means changed from ice into water because it passes through air above freezing temperature.","zh":"melted by warmer air 指因穿過高於冰點的空氣而由冰變成水。"},{"en":"Snowflakes can be melted by warmer air before they reach the ground.","zh":"雪花到達地面前可能被較暖空氣融化。"},{"en":"If the lower air is warm enough, falling snow may turn into rain.","zh":"如果低層空氣足夠溫暖，落下的雪可能變成雨。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why snow sometimes disappears before landing.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何雪有時在落地前消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lower altitudes","meaning":"較低海拔","examples":[{"en":"Warmer air may occur at lower altitudes.","zh":"較暖空氣可能出現在較低海拔。"},{"en":"Lower altitudes are places closer to sea level.","zh":"lower altitudes 指較接近海平面的地方。"},{"en":"A mountain top may be snowy while lower altitudes receive rain.","zh":"山頂可能下雪，而較低海拔地區下雨。"},{"en":"Because air is often warmer lower down, snow may melt before reaching the ground.","zh":"由於低層空氣通常較暖，雪可能在到達地面前融化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes height closer to the surface.","zh":"這個短語描述較接近地表的高度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"do so as snow","meaning":"以雪的形式落下","examples":[{"en":"If the crystal is not melted, it will fall as snow.","zh":"如果冰晶沒有融化，它會以雪的形式落下。"},{"en":"To do so as snow means to fall or arrive in the form of snow.","zh":"do so as snow 指以雪的形式降下或到達。"},{"en":"Moisture may fall as rain in warm air but do so as snow in colder air.","zh":"水分在暖空氣中可能以下雨形式降下，但在冷空氣中以雪的形式落下。"},{"en":"The same cloud may produce different precipitation depending on the temperature below it.","zh":"同一朵雲可能因下方溫度不同而產生不同降水形式。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the form in which the falling ice reaches the ground.","zh":"這個短語顯示落下的冰以甚麼形式到達地面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"land on the ground","meaning":"落在地面","examples":[{"en":"Ice crystals that land on the ground are actually transparent.","zh":"落在地面的冰晶其實是透明的。"},{"en":"To land on the ground means to reach and settle on the Earth’s surface.","zh":"land on the ground 指到達並停留在地球表面。"},{"en":"A dropped leaf may land on the ground near the tree.","zh":"落下的葉子可能落在樹旁地面。"},{"en":"Snowflakes that land on the ground can build up into visible snow cover.","zh":"落在地面的雪花可以累積成可見雪層。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the final arrival of falling objects.","zh":"這個短語描述下落物體的最終到達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"actually transparent","meaning":"實際上是透明的","examples":[{"en":"The ice crystals are actually transparent.","zh":"冰晶實際上是透明的。"},{"en":"Actually transparent means truly clear or see-through, even if they appear different.","zh":"actually transparent 指實際上清澈或透光，即使外觀看起來不同。"},{"en":"Clear glass is actually transparent because light passes through it.","zh":"透明玻璃實際上是透明的，因為光線可以穿過。"},{"en":"Snow may look white even though individual ice crystals are transparent.","zh":"雪看起來可能是白色，即使單個冰晶是透明的。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects what people may assume from appearance.","zh":"這個短語修正人們可能從外觀作出的假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hollow imperfections","meaning":"空心瑕疵","examples":[{"en":"Hollow imperfections inside the crystals scatter light.","zh":"晶體內的空心瑕疵會散射光線。"},{"en":"Hollow imperfections are tiny empty spaces or flaws inside a material.","zh":"hollow imperfections 指材料內部微小的空洞或缺陷。"},{"en":"Bubbles inside ice cubes are hollow imperfections that make the ice look cloudy.","zh":"冰塊中的氣泡是空心瑕疵，會令冰看起來混濁。"},{"en":"These imperfections affect how light moves through or reflects from the crystal.","zh":"這些瑕疵會影響光線穿過或反射晶體的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes small internal flaws that change appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述改變外觀的微小內部缺陷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"light is scattered","meaning":"光線被散射","examples":[{"en":"Light is scattered by imperfections in the ice crystals.","zh":"光線被冰晶中的瑕疵散射。"},{"en":"Light is scattered means light is sent in many different directions.","zh":"light is scattered 指光線被送往許多不同方向。"},{"en":"Fog looks white because tiny water droplets scatter light.","zh":"霧看起來是白色，因為微小水滴散射光線。"},{"en":"When light is scattered many times, transparent objects may appear white or cloudy.","zh":"當光線被多次散射，透明物體可能顯得白色或混濁。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why appearance can differ from actual colour.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何外觀可以不同於真實顏色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"appear white in colour","meaning":"顯得白色","examples":[{"en":"Snow often appears white in colour.","zh":"雪通常顯得白色。"},{"en":"To appear white in colour means to look white to the eye.","zh":"appear white in colour 指對眼睛看起來是白色。"},{"en":"A wall may appear white in colour under bright light even if it is slightly grey.","zh":"牆壁在強光下可能顯得白色，即使它略帶灰色。"},{"en":"Snow appears white because light is reflected and scattered many times.","zh":"雪顯得白色，因為光線被多次反射和散射。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual appearance, not necessarily actual material colour.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺外觀，而不一定是材料本身顏色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"owing to","meaning":"由於","examples":[{"en":"Snow appears white owing to diffuse reflection.","zh":"雪由於漫反射而顯得白色。"},{"en":"Owing to means because of.","zh":"owing to 指由於。"},{"en":"The school trip was delayed owing to heavy traffic.","zh":"學校旅行因交通嚴重擠塞而延誤。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the reason for a result in a formal way.","zh":"這個短語以正式方式引出結果的原因。"},{"en":"It is similar to “due to” but often sounds slightly more formal.","zh":"它與 “due to” 相似，但通常稍為正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"diffuse reflection","meaning":"漫反射","examples":[{"en":"Snow appears white because of diffuse reflection.","zh":"雪因漫反射而顯得白色。"},{"en":"Diffuse reflection is reflection in many directions rather than one clear direction.","zh":"diffuse reflection 指光線向多個方向反射，而不是朝單一清晰方向反射。"},{"en":"A rough wall shows diffuse reflection because light spreads instead of forming a mirror image.","zh":"粗糙牆面會產生漫反射，因為光線散開而不形成鏡像。"},{"en":"Diffuse reflection from many ice surfaces makes snow look bright and white.","zh":"許多冰面造成的漫反射令雪看起來明亮而白。"},{"en":"This phrase explains scattered reflection of light.","zh":"這個短語解釋光線分散反射。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the whole spectrum of light","meaning":"整個光譜","examples":[{"en":"Snow reflects the whole spectrum of light.","zh":"雪反射整個光譜。"},{"en":"The whole spectrum of light means all the colours or wavelengths that make up visible light.","zh":"whole spectrum of light 指構成可見光的所有顏色或波長。"},{"en":"A rainbow separates the whole spectrum of light into different colours.","zh":"彩虹把整個光譜分成不同顏色。"},{"en":"When all visible colours are reflected together, the result may look white.","zh":"當所有可見顏色一起被反射，結果可能看起來是白色。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the full range of visible light.","zh":"這個短語指可見光的完整範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the shape of a snowflake","meaning":"雪花的形狀","examples":[{"en":"The shape of a snowflake depends on atmospheric conditions.","zh":"雪花的形狀取決於大氣條件。"},{"en":"The shape of a snowflake is the form or pattern the snow crystal takes as it grows.","zh":"shape of a snowflake 指雪晶生長時形成的形態或模式。"},{"en":"A snowflake may look like a flat plate, needle, prism, or complex star.","zh":"雪花可能看起來像平板、針狀、棱柱或複雜星形。"},{"en":"Temperature and humidity influence how the crystal grows, so they affect its shape.","zh":"溫度和濕度影響晶體如何生長，因此也影響其形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the visible form of a snowflake.","zh":"這個短語集中於雪花的可見形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be determined by","meaning":"由……決定","examples":[{"en":"The shape of a snowflake is determined by temperature and humidity.","zh":"雪花的形狀由溫度和濕度決定。"},{"en":"To be determined by something means to be decided or controlled by it.","zh":"be determined by something 指由某事決定或控制。"},{"en":"A student’s travel time is determined by distance, traffic, and transport choice.","zh":"學生通勤時間由距離、交通和交通工具選擇決定。"},{"en":"If snowflake shape is determined by weather conditions, changes in the air change the crystal.","zh":"如果雪花形狀由天氣條件決定，空氣變化就會改變晶體。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the factors that decide a result.","zh":"這個短語指出決定結果的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"atmospheric conditions","meaning":"大氣條件","examples":[{"en":"Atmospheric conditions affect the shape of a snowflake.","zh":"大氣條件影響雪花的形狀。"},{"en":"Atmospheric conditions are conditions in the air, such as temperature, moisture, and pressure.","zh":"atmospheric conditions 指空氣中的狀況，例如溫度、水分和氣壓。"},{"en":"Pilots check atmospheric conditions before flying through stormy regions.","zh":"飛行員飛越風暴區前會檢查大氣條件。"},{"en":"Changing atmospheric conditions can alter clouds, precipitation, and visibility.","zh":"不斷變化的大氣條件可以改變雲、降水和能見度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the state of the atmosphere at a time and place.","zh":"這個短語描述某時某地的大氣狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"present at the time of","meaning":"在……時存在的","examples":[{"en":"The conditions present at the time of formation determine the shape.","zh":"形成時存在的條件決定其形狀。"},{"en":"Present at the time of something means existing when that event happens.","zh":"present at the time of something 指某事件發生時存在。"},{"en":"The teacher present at the time of the accident can explain what happened.","zh":"意外發生時在場的老師可以解釋發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"Conditions present at the time of freezing affect how the ice crystal grows.","zh":"結冰時存在的條件會影響冰晶如何生長。"},{"en":"This phrase links an outcome to the conditions existing during an event.","zh":"這個短語把結果與事件期間存在的條件連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"formation","meaning":"形成","examples":[{"en":"The temperature at the time of formation affects the snowflake.","zh":"形成時的溫度會影響雪花。"},{"en":"Formation means the process by which something is created or develops.","zh":"formation 指某物被創造或發展出來的過程。"},{"en":"The formation of a study group begins when students decide to meet regularly.","zh":"學習小組的形成始於學生決定定期見面。"},{"en":"In weather, formation often depends on temperature, moisture, and movement.","zh":"在天氣中，形成通常取決於溫度、水分和運動。"},{"en":"This word focuses on how something comes into being.","zh":"這個字集中於某物如何出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"specifically","meaning":"具體而言","examples":[{"en":"The shape is determined specifically by temperature and humidity.","zh":"具體而言，形狀由溫度和濕度決定。"},{"en":"Specifically means in a more exact or detailed way.","zh":"specifically 指以更精確或更詳細方式來說。"},{"en":"The teacher asked students to revise grammar, specifically verb tenses and articles.","zh":"老師要求學生溫習文法，具體而言是動詞時態和冠詞。"},{"en":"This word narrows a general point to precise details.","zh":"這個字把一般觀點收窄至精確細節。"},{"en":"It helps readers know exactly which factors matter.","zh":"它幫助讀者知道確切哪些因素重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"humidity","meaning":"濕度","examples":[{"en":"Humidity helps determine the shape of a snowflake.","zh":"濕度有助決定雪花的形狀。"},{"en":"Humidity is the amount of water vapour in the air.","zh":"humidity 指空氣中的水汽含量。"},{"en":"High humidity can make a hot day feel sticky and uncomfortable.","zh":"高濕度可以令炎熱日子感覺黏膩而不舒服。"},{"en":"In clouds, humidity affects how ice crystals grow and branch.","zh":"在雲中，濕度會影響冰晶如何生長和分枝。"},{"en":"This word describes moisture in the air.","zh":"這個字描述空氣中的水分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"thin flat crystals","meaning":"薄而扁平的晶體","examples":[{"en":"Thin flat crystals grow between 0°C and −3°C.","zh":"薄而扁平的晶體在攝氏0度至零下3度之間形成。"},{"en":"Thin flat crystals are ice crystals that are narrow and plate-like rather than tall.","zh":"thin flat crystals 指狹薄而呈板狀、不是高柱狀的冰晶。"},{"en":"A thin flat biscuit breaks more easily than a thick cube of sugar.","zh":"薄而扁平的餅乾比厚方糖更容易碎。"},{"en":"Certain temperatures encourage snow crystals to spread sideways into flat shapes.","zh":"某些溫度會促使雪晶向橫向擴展成扁平形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the form of a snow crystal.","zh":"這個短語描述雪晶的形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"planar crystals","meaning":"平面晶體","examples":[{"en":"Planar crystals form at temperatures between 0°C and −3°C.","zh":"平面晶體在攝氏0度至零下3度之間形成。"},{"en":"Planar crystals are flat crystals that grow mainly in a plane.","zh":"planar crystals 指主要在一個平面上生長的扁平晶體。"},{"en":"A flat paper cut-out is planar because it spreads across a surface rather than upward.","zh":"扁平剪紙是平面的，因為它沿表面展開，而不是向上發展。"},{"en":"In snow, planar crystals form when atmospheric conditions favour sideways growth.","zh":"在雪中，當大氣條件有利於橫向生長，平面晶體就會形成。"},{"en":"This phrase is a technical way to describe flat crystal shapes.","zh":"這個短語是描述扁平晶體形狀的技術說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"grow","meaning":"生長；形成","examples":[{"en":"Thin flat crystals grow under particular atmospheric conditions.","zh":"薄而扁平的晶體在特定大氣條件下形成。"},{"en":"To grow means to develop, increase in size, or form over time.","zh":"grow 指隨時間發展、變大或形成。"},{"en":"A plant grows when it receives water, light, and suitable soil.","zh":"植物得到水、光和合適泥土時會生長。"},{"en":"Snow crystals grow when water vapour attaches to them in the cloud.","zh":"當水汽在雲中附着到雪晶上，雪晶就會生長。"},{"en":"This word describes gradual development.","zh":"這個字描述逐漸發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"form needles or prisms","meaning":"形成針狀或棱柱狀","examples":[{"en":"At lower temperatures, the crystals form needles or prisms.","zh":"在較低溫度下，晶體形成針狀或棱柱狀。"},{"en":"To form needles or prisms means to grow into long thin shapes or column-like shapes.","zh":"form needles or prisms 指長成細長針狀或柱狀形態。"},{"en":"Ice in a freezer may sometimes form sharp needle-like patterns.","zh":"冰箱中的冰有時可能形成尖銳的針狀圖案。"},{"en":"Temperature changes can cause snow crystals to grow into very different forms.","zh":"溫度變化可以令雪晶長成非常不同的形態。"},{"en":"This phrase describes specific crystal shapes produced by cold conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述低溫條件產生的特定晶體形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"prisms","meaning":"棱柱","examples":[{"en":"Some snow crystals form prisms with pencil-like shapes.","zh":"有些雪晶形成像鉛筆般形狀的棱柱。"},{"en":"Prisms are solid shapes with flat sides and a repeated cross-section.","zh":"prisms 指具有平面側面和重複截面的立體形狀。"},{"en":"A triangular glass prism can split light into rainbow colours.","zh":"三角玻璃棱柱可以把光分成彩虹顏色。"},{"en":"In snow, prism-like crystals are more column-shaped than flat.","zh":"在雪中，棱柱狀晶體比扁平晶體更像柱狀。"},{"en":"This word describes a geometric crystal form.","zh":"這個字描述一種幾何晶體形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pencil-like shapes","meaning":"像鉛筆般的形狀","examples":[{"en":"The crystals may form needles or prisms with pencil-like shapes.","zh":"晶體可能形成針狀或有像鉛筆般形狀的棱柱。"},{"en":"Pencil-like shapes are long, narrow shapes similar to a pencil.","zh":"pencil-like shapes 指類似鉛筆的細長形狀。"},{"en":"Some icicles have pencil-like shapes when they are thin and straight.","zh":"有些冰柱又細又直時，具有像鉛筆般的形狀。"},{"en":"Snow crystals take pencil-like shapes under certain cold atmospheric conditions.","zh":"雪晶在某些寒冷大氣條件下會呈像鉛筆般的形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase helps learners picture the long narrow form.","zh":"這個短語幫助學習者想像細長形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"revert to","meaning":"回復為","examples":[{"en":"The crystal shape then reverts to plate-like forms.","zh":"晶體形狀然後回復為板狀形態。"},{"en":"To revert to something means to return to an earlier or previous form or state.","zh":"revert to something 指回到較早或之前的形式或狀態。"},{"en":"A student may revert to old habits if they stop following a study plan.","zh":"如果學生停止跟隨學習計劃，可能回復舊習慣。"},{"en":"In snow crystals, shape can revert to flat forms when temperature conditions change.","zh":"在雪晶中，當溫度條件改變，形狀可以回復為扁平形態。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a return to a former pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述回到先前模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"plate-like forms","meaning":"板狀形態","examples":[{"en":"The crystals revert to plate-like forms at certain temperatures.","zh":"晶體在某些溫度下回復為板狀形態。"},{"en":"Plate-like forms are flat, broad shapes similar to small plates.","zh":"plate-like forms 指類似小碟的扁平而寬闊形狀。"},{"en":"Thin ice on a pond may break into plate-like pieces.","zh":"池塘上的薄冰可能裂成板狀碎片。"},{"en":"Snow crystals can grow into plate-like forms when conditions favour flat growth.","zh":"當條件有利於扁平生長，雪晶可以長成板狀形態。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a flat crystal shape.","zh":"這個短語描述扁平晶體形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"below which","meaning":"低於這溫度時","examples":[{"en":"The temperature reaches −22°C, below which column-like structures form again.","zh":"溫度達到攝氏零下22度，低於這溫度時柱狀結構再次形成。"},{"en":"Below which means at temperatures or levels lower than that point.","zh":"below which 指在低於該點的溫度或水平下。"},{"en":"The medicine must be stored below 8°C, below which it remains safe for longer.","zh":"藥物必須存放於攝氏8度以下，低於這溫度時可保持更久安全。"},{"en":"In science writing, this phrase links a threshold with what happens under it.","zh":"在科學寫作中，這個短語把臨界值與其以下會發生的事連起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is used after a stated limit.","zh":"這個短語用於已說明的限制之後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"column-like structures","meaning":"柱狀結構","examples":[{"en":"Column-like structures begin to form again below −22°C.","zh":"柱狀結構在攝氏零下22度以下再次開始形成。"},{"en":"Column-like structures are shapes that look like small columns or pillars.","zh":"column-like structures 指看起來像小柱或支柱的形狀。"},{"en":"A row of tall building supports may have column-like structures.","zh":"一排高大的建築支撐物可能具有柱狀結構。"},{"en":"In snow crystals, very low temperatures can encourage vertical, column-like growth.","zh":"在雪晶中，極低溫可以促進垂直、柱狀生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes upright or pillar-shaped forms.","zh":"這個短語描述直立或柱形形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"begin to form again","meaning":"再次開始形成","examples":[{"en":"Needles and prisms begin to form again at very low temperatures.","zh":"針狀和棱柱狀在極低溫下再次開始形成。"},{"en":"Begin to form again means start developing once more after stopping or changing.","zh":"begin to form again 指在停止或改變後再次開始發展。"},{"en":"Queues begin to form again when a popular shop reopens after lunch.","zh":"受歡迎商店午飯後重開時，隊伍可能再次開始形成。"},{"en":"Crystal shapes can begin to form again when temperature returns to the right range.","zh":"當溫度回到合適範圍，晶體形狀可以再次開始形成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the return of a formation process.","zh":"這個短語描述形成過程的回歸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"complex growth patterns","meaning":"複雜生長形態","examples":[{"en":"More complex growth patterns also form at very low temperatures.","zh":"更複雜的生長形態也在極低溫下形成。"},{"en":"Complex growth patterns are detailed ways in which something develops or branches.","zh":"complex growth patterns 指某物發展或分枝的精細方式。"},{"en":"A tree may show complex growth patterns after years of wind and pruning.","zh":"樹木經多年風吹和修剪後，可能顯示複雜生長形態。"},{"en":"Snow crystals can develop complex patterns when temperature and humidity interact in delicate ways.","zh":"當溫度和濕度以精細方式互相作用，雪晶可以形成複雜圖案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth that is not simple or uniform.","zh":"這個短語描述並不簡單或一致的生長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"snowfall in the British Isles","meaning":"不列顛群島的降雪","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses snowfall in the British Isles.","zh":"文章討論不列顛群島的降雪。"},{"en":"Snowfall in the British Isles means snow that falls in Britain, Ireland, and nearby islands.","zh":"snowfall in the British Isles 指在英國、愛爾蘭及附近島嶼降下的雪。"},{"en":"A geography lesson may compare snowfall in the British Isles with snowfall in Canada.","zh":"地理課可能比較不列顛群島的降雪與加拿大的降雪。"},{"en":"The region’s surrounding ocean and currents affect how much snow it receives.","zh":"該地區周圍海洋和洋流會影響其降雪量。"},{"en":"This phrase places the topic of snow in a specific region.","zh":"這個短語把雪的主題放在特定地區中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"occur frequently","meaning":"經常發生","examples":[{"en":"Snowfall occurs frequently in the United Kingdom.","zh":"降雪在英國經常發生。"},{"en":"To occur frequently means to happen often.","zh":"occur frequently 指經常發生。"},{"en":"Traffic delays occur frequently near schools at pickup time.","zh":"放學接送時間，學校附近經常發生交通延誤。"},{"en":"If snow occurs frequently, people may be familiar with winter warnings.","zh":"如果降雪經常發生，人們可能熟悉冬季警告。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how often something happens.","zh":"這個短語描述某事發生的頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the quantities are typically small","meaning":"數量通常很少","examples":[{"en":"Snowfall occurs often, but the quantities are typically small.","zh":"降雪經常發生，但數量通常很少。"},{"en":"The quantities are typically small means the amounts are usually not large.","zh":"the quantities are typically small 指數量通常不大。"},{"en":"A student may read every day, but the quantities are typically small if they only read one page.","zh":"學生可能每天閱讀，但如果只讀一頁，數量通常很少。"},{"en":"Frequent snow does not always mean deep snow if the amounts are small.","zh":"經常下雪不一定代表深雪，如果每次降雪量很少。"},{"en":"This phrase separates frequency from amount.","zh":"這個短語把發生頻率與數量分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"seldom persists","meaning":"很少持續","examples":[{"en":"Snow in the United Kingdom seldom persists for very long.","zh":"英國的雪很少持續很久。"},{"en":"Seldom persists means rarely continues or remains for a long time.","zh":"seldom persists 指很少長時間持續或保留。"},{"en":"Morning fog seldom persists after strong sunlight appears.","zh":"早晨霧氣在強烈陽光出現後很少持續。"},{"en":"If snow seldom persists, roads may clear naturally without deep accumulation.","zh":"如果雪很少持續，道路可能自然融雪而不會深積。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that usually does not last.","zh":"這個短語描述某事通常不會維持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"for very long","meaning":"很長時間","examples":[{"en":"Snow seldom remains for very long.","zh":"雪很少停留很長時間。"},{"en":"For very long means for a long period of time.","zh":"for very long 指很長一段時間。"},{"en":"Ice cream will not stay solid for very long in hot weather.","zh":"雪糕在炎熱天氣中不會保持固體很長時間。"},{"en":"Snow that does not remain for very long may still disrupt travel briefly.","zh":"不會停留很久的雪仍可能短暫干擾交通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes duration.","zh":"這個短語描述持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in recent years","meaning":"近年來","examples":[{"en":"In recent years, British winters have tended to be milder and wetter.","zh":"近年來，英國冬季傾向較溫和和較潮濕。"},{"en":"In recent years means during the last several years.","zh":"in recent years 指過去數年間。"},{"en":"In recent years, many schools have used more online learning tools.","zh":"近年來，許多學校使用更多網上學習工具。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts modern patterns with older ones.","zh":"這個短語把現代模式與舊有模式作對比。"},{"en":"It helps show that a trend is fairly new.","zh":"它有助顯示某趨勢相當新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a trend towards","meaning":"趨向……的趨勢","examples":[{"en":"There has been a trend towards milder, wetter winters.","zh":"出現了趨向較溫和、較潮濕冬季的趨勢。"},{"en":"A trend towards something is a gradual movement or change in that direction.","zh":"trend towards something 指逐漸朝某方向移動或改變。"},{"en":"There is a trend towards cashless payment in many shops.","zh":"許多商店出現趨向無現金支付的趨勢。"},{"en":"A trend towards warmer winters may reduce snow reliability.","zh":"趨向較暖冬季的趨勢可能降低降雪穩定性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a developing pattern of change.","zh":"這個短語描述正在發展的變化模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"milder, wetter winters","meaning":"較溫和、較潮濕的冬季","examples":[{"en":"A trend towards milder, wetter winters has been developing.","zh":"趨向較溫和、較潮濕冬季的趨勢正在形成。"},{"en":"Milder, wetter winters are winters that are less cold and have more rain or moisture.","zh":"milder, wetter winters 指較不寒冷且有更多雨水或水分的冬季。"},{"en":"Milder, wetter winters may mean fewer snow days but more muddy fields.","zh":"較溫和、較潮濕的冬季可能意味着較少下雪日，但更多泥濘田地。"},{"en":"Such winters can affect farming, transport, tourism, and heating demand.","zh":"這類冬季可以影響農業、交通、旅遊和供暖需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes winters that are warmer and more humid than expected.","zh":"這個短語描述比預期更暖、更潮濕的冬季。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be developing","meaning":"正在形成；正在發展","examples":[{"en":"A trend towards milder winters has been developing.","zh":"趨向較溫和冬季的趨勢正在形成。"},{"en":"To be developing means to be forming, growing, or becoming clearer over time.","zh":"be developing 指正在形成、增長或隨時間變得更清楚。"},{"en":"A friendship may be developing when two students start talking every day.","zh":"當兩名學生開始每天聊天，友誼可能正在發展。"},{"en":"A developing trend becomes easier to see after several examples appear.","zh":"當幾個例子出現後，正在形成的趨勢會更容易看見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes change that is still in progress.","zh":"這個短語描述仍在進行中的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"buck the trend","meaning":"逆轉趨勢；與趨勢相反","examples":[{"en":"Three winters seem to have bucked the trend towards milder weather.","zh":"三個冬季似乎與趨向較溫和天氣的趨勢相反。"},{"en":"To buck the trend means to go against the general pattern.","zh":"buck the trend 指與一般模式相反。"},{"en":"If most shops lose sales but one small bakery grows, that bakery bucks the trend.","zh":"如果大多數商店銷售下跌，但一間小麵包店增長，該麵包店就是逆勢而行。"},{"en":"Cold winters can buck a warming trend if they are unusually severe.","zh":"如果寒冬異常嚴重，就可以與變暖趨勢相反。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights an exception to a broader pattern.","zh":"這個短語突出較大模式中的例外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"represent","meaning":"代表","examples":[{"en":"Those winters represent the longest period of consecutive cold winters for more than 50 years.","zh":"那些冬季代表五十多年來最長的連續寒冬時期。"},{"en":"To represent something means to stand for it or be an example of it.","zh":"represent something 指代表某事或作為其例子。"},{"en":"A high exam score may represent months of steady practice.","zh":"高考試分數可能代表數月穩定練習。"},{"en":"Several cold winters together may represent a possible change in climate pattern.","zh":"幾個寒冬連續出現可能代表氣候模式的可能變化。"},{"en":"This word connects an example with a larger meaning.","zh":"這個字把例子與更大意義連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"longest period of","meaning":"最長時期的……","examples":[{"en":"The recent winters represent the longest period of cold winters for decades.","zh":"近期冬季代表數十年來最長時期的寒冬。"},{"en":"The longest period of something means the greatest length of time during which it continued.","zh":"longest period of something 指某事持續時間最長的一段。"},{"en":"A school may record its longest period of perfect attendance in ten years.","zh":"學校可能錄得十年來最長時期的全勤紀錄。"},{"en":"Long periods of cold weather can have stronger effects than one short cold spell.","zh":"長時間寒冷天氣比一次短暫寒潮影響更大。"},{"en":"This phrase measures duration by comparing it with earlier periods.","zh":"這個短語透過與過去時期比較來量度持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"consecutive cold winters","meaning":"連續寒冬","examples":[{"en":"The winters formed a period of consecutive cold winters.","zh":"這些冬季形成一段連續寒冬時期。"},{"en":"Consecutive cold winters are cold winters that happen one after another without interruption.","zh":"consecutive cold winters 指一個接一個、沒有中斷出現的寒冷冬季。"},{"en":"Three consecutive exam failures mean a student failed three exams in a row.","zh":"三次連續考試不合格，表示學生連續三次考試失敗。"},{"en":"Consecutive cold winters may make people question whether a wider climate pattern is changing.","zh":"連續寒冬可能令人質疑更廣泛的氣候模式是否正在改變。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses repeated winters in sequence.","zh":"這個短語強調按次序反覆出現的冬季。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"for more than 50 years","meaning":"五十多年來","examples":[{"en":"The cold winters were the longest such period for more than 50 years.","zh":"這些寒冬是五十多年來最長的同類時期。"},{"en":"For more than 50 years means for a period longer than half a century.","zh":"for more than 50 years 指超過半個世紀的時間。"},{"en":"A school building that has stood for more than 50 years may need careful repair.","zh":"已存在五十多年的校舍可能需要仔細維修。"},{"en":"When a weather pattern is unusual for more than 50 years, people notice it.","zh":"當某天氣模式在五十多年來都罕見，人們會注意到它。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a long historical comparison.","zh":"這個短語給出長期歷史比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"for its latitude","meaning":"以其緯度而言","examples":[{"en":"For its latitude, the British Isles should experience more cold weather.","zh":"以其緯度而言，不列顛群島應經歷更多寒冷天氣。"},{"en":"For its latitude means considering how far north or south a place is.","zh":"for its latitude 指考慮某地位於多北或多南的位置。"},{"en":"For its latitude, a city may be warmer than expected because of ocean currents.","zh":"以其緯度而言，某城市可能因洋流而比預期更暖。"},{"en":"Latitude affects sunlight and temperature, but other factors can change the result.","zh":"緯度影響陽光和溫度，但其他因素可以改變結果。"},{"en":"This phrase compares expected climate with geographical position.","zh":"這個短語把預期氣候與地理位置作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"prolonged cold weather","meaning":"持續寒冷天氣","examples":[{"en":"The British Isles should see more prolonged cold weather in winter.","zh":"不列顛群島冬季應有更多持續寒冷天氣。"},{"en":"Prolonged cold weather is cold weather that lasts for a long time.","zh":"prolonged cold weather 指持續很久的寒冷天氣。"},{"en":"Prolonged cold weather can increase heating bills and make roads icy for days.","zh":"持續寒冷天氣可以增加暖氣費，並令道路結冰數天。"},{"en":"When cold lasts longer, snow and ice have more time to accumulate.","zh":"當寒冷持續更久，雪和冰有更多時間累積。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses duration, not just low temperature.","zh":"這個短語強調持續時間，而不只是低溫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"regular snowfall","meaning":"規律降雪","examples":[{"en":"For its latitude, the British Isles should receive regular snowfall.","zh":"以其緯度而言，不列顛群島應有規律降雪。"},{"en":"Regular snowfall means snow that happens repeatedly or predictably.","zh":"regular snowfall 指反覆或可預測地出現的降雪。"},{"en":"A ski town with regular snowfall can plan winter tourism more confidently.","zh":"有規律降雪的滑雪城鎮可以更有信心規劃冬季旅遊。"},{"en":"If snowfall is regular, communities may build routines for clearing roads.","zh":"如果降雪規律，社區可能建立清理道路的常規。"},{"en":"This phrase describes snow that is expected rather than rare.","zh":"這個短語描述預期中的雪，而不是罕見降雪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the Gulf Stream","meaning":"墨西哥灣暖流","examples":[{"en":"The Gulf Stream keeps the British climate warmer.","zh":"墨西哥灣暖流令英國氣候較暖。"},{"en":"The Gulf Stream is a warm Atlantic current that influences nearby climates.","zh":"Gulf Stream 指影響附近氣候的溫暖大西洋洋流。"},{"en":"Geography students learn about the Gulf Stream when studying why Britain is mild for its latitude.","zh":"地理學生研究英國以其緯度而言為何溫和時，會學到墨西哥灣暖流。"},{"en":"Warm ocean currents can move heat from one region to another.","zh":"溫暖洋流可以把熱力從一個地區移到另一個地區。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major current affecting the British Isles.","zh":"這個短語指出影響不列顛群島的重要洋流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Atlantic Ocean current","meaning":"大西洋洋流","examples":[{"en":"The Gulf Stream is a mild Atlantic Ocean current.","zh":"墨西哥灣暖流是一股溫和的大西洋洋流。"},{"en":"An Atlantic Ocean current is a large movement of seawater in the Atlantic Ocean.","zh":"Atlantic Ocean current 指大西洋中的大型海水流動。"},{"en":"Ocean currents can carry warm or cold water across long distances.","zh":"洋流可以把暖水或冷水帶到遠距離。"},{"en":"A warm Atlantic current can make nearby coastal climates milder.","zh":"溫暖的大西洋洋流可以令附近沿海氣候較溫和。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving seawater in the Atlantic.","zh":"這個短語描述大西洋中移動的海水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"keep the climate warmer","meaning":"令氣候較暖","examples":[{"en":"The Gulf Stream keeps Britain’s climate several degrees warmer.","zh":"墨西哥灣暖流令英國氣候暖幾度。"},{"en":"To keep the climate warmer means to maintain higher average temperatures.","zh":"keep the climate warmer 指維持較高平均溫度。"},{"en":"A nearby sea can keep a coastal town warmer in winter than an inland town.","zh":"附近海洋可以令沿海城鎮冬天比內陸城鎮較暖。"},{"en":"Warm currents reduce severe cold by bringing heat into the region.","zh":"暖流透過把熱力帶入地區，減少嚴寒。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how one factor prevents a place from becoming as cold as expected.","zh":"這個短語解釋某因素如何防止某地變得如預期般寒冷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"several degrees warmer","meaning":"暖幾度","examples":[{"en":"The Gulf Stream makes the climate several degrees warmer.","zh":"墨西哥灣暖流令氣候暖幾度。"},{"en":"Several degrees warmer means a few degrees higher in temperature.","zh":"several degrees warmer 指溫度高出幾度。"},{"en":"A classroom near sunny windows may be several degrees warmer than one in the shade.","zh":"靠近陽光窗戶的課室可能比陰暗課室暖幾度。"},{"en":"A difference of several degrees can decide whether precipitation falls as rain or snow.","zh":"幾度差異可以決定降水是雨還是雪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a meaningful temperature increase.","zh":"這個短語描述有意義的溫度上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"regions of similar latitude","meaning":"緯度相若的地區","examples":[{"en":"Britain is warmer than regions of similar latitude elsewhere.","zh":"英國比其他緯度相若的地區更暖。"},{"en":"Regions of similar latitude are places at about the same distance north or south of the equator.","zh":"regions of similar latitude 指距離赤道南北位置大約相同的地方。"},{"en":"Two cities at similar latitude may still have different climates because of oceans or mountains.","zh":"兩個緯度相若的城市仍可能因海洋或山脈而有不同氣候。"},{"en":"Comparing similar latitudes helps show the influence of other climate factors.","zh":"比較緯度相若地區有助顯示其他氣候因素的影響。"},{"en":"This phrase groups places by geographical position.","zh":"這個短語按地理位置把地方分組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"other parts of the world","meaning":"世界其他地區","examples":[{"en":"Other parts of the world at similar latitude may be colder.","zh":"世界其他緯度相若的地區可能更冷。"},{"en":"Other parts of the world means different regions outside the place being discussed.","zh":"other parts of the world 指正在討論地點以外的不同地區。"},{"en":"Food that is cheap locally may be expensive in other parts of the world.","zh":"本地便宜的食物，在世界其他地區可能很昂貴。"},{"en":"Comparing one region with other parts of the world helps reveal what makes it unusual.","zh":"把一個地區與世界其他地區比較，有助揭示它有何不尋常。"},{"en":"This phrase broadens the comparison beyond one place.","zh":"這個短語把比較擴展到單一地點以外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as a consequence","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a consequence, Britain’s winters are typically not very severe.","zh":"因此，英國冬季通常不太嚴寒。"},{"en":"As a consequence means as a result.","zh":"as a consequence 指因此或作為結果。"},{"en":"The train was delayed; as a consequence, many students arrived late.","zh":"火車延誤；因此，許多學生遲到。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause in the previous sentence with its result.","zh":"這個短語把前一句中的原因與其結果連起來。"},{"en":"It is a formal way to show cause and effect.","zh":"它是表示因果關係的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"despite","meaning":"儘管","examples":[{"en":"Despite occasional prolonged cold, Britain’s winters are usually not severe.","zh":"儘管偶爾出現持續寒冷，英國冬季通常並不嚴寒。"},{"en":"Despite means although something happens or is true.","zh":"despite 指雖然某事發生或屬實。"},{"en":"Despite the rain, the students finished the outdoor activity.","zh":"儘管下雨，學生仍完成戶外活動。"},{"en":"This word introduces a contrast between an obstacle and the main point.","zh":"這個字引出障礙與主要觀點之間的對比。"},{"en":"It shows that one fact does not cancel the other.","zh":"它顯示一個事實不會抵消另一個事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"occasional incident of","meaning":"偶爾出現","examples":[{"en":"Britain sometimes experiences an occasional incident of prolonged cold.","zh":"英國有時偶爾出現持續寒冷。"},{"en":"An occasional incident of something is an event that happens sometimes but not regularly.","zh":"occasional incident of something 指偶爾發生但不規律的事件。"},{"en":"A school may have an occasional incident of bullying even if the general atmosphere is safe.","zh":"即使整體氣氛安全，學校也可能偶爾出現欺凌事件。"},{"en":"Occasional incidents do not always prove a long-term pattern.","zh":"偶發事件不一定證明長期模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that happens now and then.","zh":"這個短語描述時不時出現的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"not very severe","meaning":"不太嚴寒","examples":[{"en":"Britain’s winters are typically not very severe.","zh":"英國冬季通常不太嚴寒。"},{"en":"Not very severe means not extremely harsh, serious, or difficult.","zh":"not very severe 指不是極端惡劣、嚴重或困難。"},{"en":"A cold is not very severe if the student can still attend class and rest at home.","zh":"如果學生仍能上課並在家休息，感冒就不太嚴重。"},{"en":"Winters that are not very severe may still include short icy periods.","zh":"不太嚴寒的冬季仍可能包括短暫結冰時段。"},{"en":"This phrase softens the idea of difficulty or harshness.","zh":"這個短語減弱困難或嚴酷的程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"little, if any","meaning":"即使有也很少","examples":[{"en":"Some parts of the isles see little, if any, snow.","zh":"群島某些地區即使有雪，也很少。"},{"en":"Little, if any means very little, and possibly none at all.","zh":"little, if any 指非常少，甚至可能完全沒有。"},{"en":"A student who never revises may show little, if any, improvement.","zh":"從不溫習的學生即使有進步，也可能很少。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when the amount is extremely small or uncertain.","zh":"當數量極少或不確定時，可以使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It means the writer doubts there is much of something.","zh":"它表示作者懷疑某物數量並不多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"from year to year","meaning":"年復一年","examples":[{"en":"Some parts see little snow from year to year.","zh":"某些地區年復一年都很少下雪。"},{"en":"From year to year means across different years or each year over time.","zh":"from year to year 指跨不同年份或多年來每一年。"},{"en":"A student’s timetable may change from year to year as subjects change.","zh":"隨着科目改變，學生時間表可能年復一年都有變化。"},{"en":"Weather can vary from year to year even in the same place.","zh":"即使在同一地方，天氣也可能年復一年不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes comparison over repeated years.","zh":"這個短語描述多年之間的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"snow-prone","meaning":"容易下雪的","examples":[{"en":"The Pennines and the Scottish Highlands are among the most snow-prone areas.","zh":"奔寧山脈和蘇格蘭高地屬於最容易下雪的地區。"},{"en":"Snow-prone means likely to receive snow often or in large amounts.","zh":"snow-prone 指經常或大量下雪的可能性較高。"},{"en":"A snow-prone mountain road may need regular clearing in winter.","zh":"容易下雪的山路冬天可能需要定期清理。"},{"en":"Places that are snow-prone need better winter preparation than mild lowland areas.","zh":"容易下雪的地方比溫和低地需要更好冬季準備。"},{"en":"This word describes a higher likelihood of snow.","zh":"這個字描述較高降雪可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the Pennines","meaning":"奔寧山脈","examples":[{"en":"The Pennines are one of the most snow-prone areas in the British Isles.","zh":"奔寧山脈是不列顛群島最容易下雪的地區之一。"},{"en":"The Pennines are a range of hills and mountains in northern England.","zh":"Pennines 指英格蘭北部的一系列丘陵和山地。"},{"en":"A geography class may study the Pennines when learning about upland weather.","zh":"地理課學習高地天氣時，可能研究奔寧山脈。"},{"en":"Higher land in the Pennines can receive more snow than nearby lowland towns.","zh":"奔寧山脈的較高地區可以比附近低地城鎮收到更多雪。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific upland region in Britain.","zh":"這個短語指出英國一個特定高地地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the Scottish Highlands","meaning":"蘇格蘭高地","examples":[{"en":"The Scottish Highlands are among the snowiest areas in the British Isles.","zh":"蘇格蘭高地是不列顛群島降雪最多的地區之一。"},{"en":"The Scottish Highlands are a mountainous region in northern Scotland.","zh":"Scottish Highlands 指蘇格蘭北部的山區。"},{"en":"Tourists visit the Scottish Highlands for mountains, scenery, and winter sports.","zh":"遊客到蘇格蘭高地欣賞山景、風景和冬季運動。"},{"en":"High altitude makes parts of the Highlands more likely to receive snow.","zh":"高海拔令高地部分地區較可能下雪。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major upland region in Scotland.","zh":"這個短語指出蘇格蘭一個主要高地地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the Welsh Hills","meaning":"威爾斯丘陵","examples":[{"en":"The Welsh Hills are more snow-prone than many lowland areas.","zh":"威爾斯丘陵比許多低地地區更容易下雪。"},{"en":"The Welsh Hills are hill regions in Wales where elevation can affect weather.","zh":"Welsh Hills 指威爾斯的丘陵地區，海拔會影響天氣。"},{"en":"Walkers in the Welsh Hills may need winter gear when snow is forecast.","zh":"當預報有雪，威爾斯丘陵的行山者可能需要冬季裝備。"},{"en":"Hills often receive colder air and more snow than surrounding lowlands.","zh":"丘陵通常比周圍低地接收更冷空氣和更多雪。"},{"en":"This phrase names upland areas in Wales.","zh":"這個短語指出威爾斯的高地地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the mountains of Northern Ireland","meaning":"北愛爾蘭山區","examples":[{"en":"The mountains of Northern Ireland can experience more snow.","zh":"北愛爾蘭山區可能經歷更多降雪。"},{"en":"The mountains of Northern Ireland are upland areas in Northern Ireland where snow may fall more often.","zh":"mountains of Northern Ireland 指北愛爾蘭的高地地區，那裡可能較常下雪。"},{"en":"A winter weather report may warn drivers about icy roads in the mountains of Northern Ireland.","zh":"冬季天氣報告可能提醒司機注意北愛爾蘭山區的結冰道路。"},{"en":"Elevation can make these mountains colder than nearby coastal towns.","zh":"海拔可以令這些山區比附近沿海城鎮更冷。"},{"en":"This phrase names a regional mountain area.","zh":"這個短語指出一個區域性山區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"boast","meaning":"擁有；以……自豪","examples":[{"en":"The Scottish Highlands boast the isles’ highest peaks.","zh":"蘇格蘭高地擁有群島最高山峰。"},{"en":"To boast something means to have it as a notable or impressive feature.","zh":"boast something 指擁有某個值得注意或令人印象深刻的特色。"},{"en":"The school boasts a large library and a strong music programme.","zh":"學校擁有大型圖書館和優秀音樂課程。"},{"en":"A region may boast mountains, beaches, or famous historic sites.","zh":"一個地區可能擁有山脈、海灘或著名歷史景點。"},{"en":"This word often sounds positive and proud.","zh":"這個字通常帶有正面和自豪語氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"highest peaks","meaning":"最高山峰","examples":[{"en":"The Scottish Highlands contain the isles’ highest peaks.","zh":"蘇格蘭高地包含群島最高山峰。"},{"en":"Highest peaks are the tallest mountain tops in a region.","zh":"highest peaks 指某地區中最高的山頂。"},{"en":"Climbers often train carefully before attempting the highest peaks.","zh":"登山者嘗試攀登最高山峰前通常會仔細訓練。"},{"en":"Highest peaks are colder and more exposed, so they often receive more snow.","zh":"最高山峰更冷且更暴露，因此通常接收更多雪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the tallest points of mountains.","zh":"這個短語描述山脈的最高點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"winter ski resorts","meaning":"冬季滑雪度假村","examples":[{"en":"The Scottish Highlands have the isles’ only winter ski resorts.","zh":"蘇格蘭高地擁有群島唯一的冬季滑雪度假村。"},{"en":"Winter ski resorts are holiday areas where people ski during snowy winter months.","zh":"winter ski resorts 指人們在冬季有雪時滑雪的度假地。"},{"en":"A winter ski resort needs snow, lifts, slopes, staff, and visitors.","zh":"冬季滑雪度假村需要雪、吊車、滑雪坡、員工和遊客。"},{"en":"If snowfall becomes unreliable, ski resorts may lose income and visitors.","zh":"如果降雪變得不穩定，滑雪度假村可能失去收入和遊客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes tourism businesses based on winter snow sports.","zh":"這個短語描述以冬季雪上運動為基礎的旅遊業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"unreliable snowfall","meaning":"不穩定降雪","examples":[{"en":"Unreliable snowfall has threatened the Scottish ski resorts.","zh":"不穩定降雪威脅了蘇格蘭滑雪度假村。"},{"en":"Unreliable snowfall means snow that does not fall regularly or predictably enough.","zh":"unreliable snowfall 指降雪不夠規律或不夠可預測。"},{"en":"A ski school suffers when unreliable snowfall makes lessons difficult to schedule.","zh":"當不穩定降雪令課堂難以安排，滑雪學校會受影響。"},{"en":"If snowfall is unreliable, businesses cannot plan a stable winter season.","zh":"如果降雪不穩定，企業無法規劃穩定冬季旺季。"},{"en":"This phrase describes snow that cannot be depended on.","zh":"這個短語描述不能依賴的雪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"threaten to close","meaning":"威脅要令……關閉","examples":[{"en":"Unreliable snowfall has threatened to close the resorts.","zh":"不穩定降雪威脅要令度假村關閉。"},{"en":"To threaten to close means to create a serious risk that a place or business will shut down.","zh":"threaten to close 指造成某地方或企業關閉的嚴重風險。"},{"en":"Falling student numbers may threaten to close a small rural school.","zh":"學生人數下降可能威脅要令小型鄉村學校關閉。"},{"en":"If a business loses its main source of income, closure becomes more likely.","zh":"如果企業失去主要收入來源，關閉就更可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes danger to continued operation.","zh":"這個短語描述持續營運受到威脅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"three consecutive bumper seasons","meaning":"連續三個豐收旺季","examples":[{"en":"The resorts have had three consecutive bumper seasons.","zh":"這些度假村已經歷連續三個豐收旺季。"},{"en":"Three consecutive bumper seasons means three very successful seasons in a row.","zh":"three consecutive bumper seasons 指連續三個非常成功的季節。"},{"en":"A restaurant has three consecutive bumper months if sales are excellent for three months straight.","zh":"如果餐廳連續三個月銷售出色，就有連續三個豐收月份。"},{"en":"Good snowfall can create bumper ski seasons by attracting more visitors.","zh":"良好降雪可以透過吸引更多遊客創造滑雪旺季。"},{"en":"This phrase combines repeated success with no interruption.","zh":"這個短語結合連續成功和不中斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"less pressure on","meaning":"對……的壓力較少","examples":[{"en":"There is now less pressure on the Scottish ski industry.","zh":"現在對蘇格蘭滑雪業的壓力較少。"},{"en":"Less pressure on something means less stress, difficulty, or threat affecting it.","zh":"less pressure on something 指影響某事的壓力、困難或威脅較少。"},{"en":"More teachers can put less pressure on a crowded school timetable.","zh":"更多老師可以減少擁擠學校時間表的壓力。"},{"en":"Good winter seasons reduce pressure on ski businesses by improving income.","zh":"良好冬季旺季透過改善收入，減少滑雪企業壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reduced burden.","zh":"這個短語描述負擔減輕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"ski industry","meaning":"滑雪業","examples":[{"en":"The Scottish ski industry was once under serious pressure.","zh":"蘇格蘭滑雪業曾承受嚴重壓力。"},{"en":"The ski industry includes businesses and workers connected with skiing tourism.","zh":"ski industry 指與滑雪旅遊相關的企業和工作者。"},{"en":"Ski schools, lift operators, hotels, and equipment shops are part of the ski industry.","zh":"滑雪學校、吊車營運商、酒店和器材店都是滑雪業的一部分。"},{"en":"The ski industry depends heavily on weather, snow reliability, and visitor numbers.","zh":"滑雪業高度依賴天氣、降雪穩定性和遊客數量。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the economic activity around skiing.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞滑雪的經濟活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"not so long ago","meaning":"不久之前","examples":[{"en":"Not so long ago, the Scottish ski industry was in danger.","zh":"不久之前，蘇格蘭滑雪業仍處於危險中。"},{"en":"Not so long ago means fairly recently, not in the distant past.","zh":"not so long ago 指相當近期，而不是遙遠過去。"},{"en":"Not so long ago, many students used paper dictionaries instead of phone apps.","zh":"不久之前，許多學生使用紙本字典，而不是手機應用程式。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that a situation changed within a relatively short time.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者，情況在相對短時間內已改變。"},{"en":"It often introduces a contrast with the present.","zh":"它常引出與現在的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be threatened with","meaning":"面臨……威脅","examples":[{"en":"The ski industry was threatened with going out of existence.","zh":"滑雪業曾面臨消失的威脅。"},{"en":"To be threatened with something means to face the danger of it happening.","zh":"be threatened with something 指面臨某事發生的危險。"},{"en":"A small shop may be threatened with closure if rent rises too much.","zh":"如果租金大幅上升，小店可能面臨結業威脅。"},{"en":"Industries are threatened when income falls and operating costs remain high.","zh":"當收入下降而營運成本仍高，行業會受到威脅。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious possible negative outcome.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重的可能負面結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"go out of existence","meaning":"消失；不復存在","examples":[{"en":"The ski industry was once threatened with going out of existence.","zh":"滑雪業曾面臨消失的威脅。"},{"en":"To go out of existence means to disappear completely or stop existing.","zh":"go out of existence 指完全消失或停止存在。"},{"en":"A traditional craft may go out of existence if no young people learn it.","zh":"如果沒有年輕人學習，傳統工藝可能消失。"},{"en":"Businesses can go out of existence when customers, workers, or resources disappear.","zh":"當顧客、工人或資源消失，企業可能不復存在。"},{"en":"This phrase describes total disappearance.","zh":"這個短語描述完全消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"long-term weather forecasts","meaning":"長期天氣預測","examples":[{"en":"Long-term weather forecasts for the British Isles are hard to get right.","zh":"不列顛群島的長期天氣預測很難準確。"},{"en":"Long-term weather forecasts are predictions about weather far ahead in time.","zh":"long-term weather forecasts 指對較遠未來天氣的預測。"},{"en":"A farmer may look at long-term weather forecasts before planning crops.","zh":"農民可能在規劃農作物前查看長期天氣預測。"},{"en":"Forecasts become harder when they look weeks or months into the future.","zh":"當預測延伸到數星期或數月後，就會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weather predictions over an extended period.","zh":"這個短語描述較長時期的天氣預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"notoriously hard to","meaning":"出名地難以……","examples":[{"en":"Long-term forecasts are notoriously hard to get right.","zh":"長期預測出名地難以準確。"},{"en":"Notoriously hard to do something means widely known to be difficult.","zh":"notoriously hard to do something 指眾所周知很難做到。"},{"en":"Parking near a busy hospital is notoriously hard to find.","zh":"在繁忙醫院附近找泊車位出名地困難。"},{"en":"Long-range weather prediction is difficult because many atmospheric factors can change.","zh":"長期天氣預測困難，因為許多大氣因素會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the difficulty is well known.","zh":"這個短語強調困難是廣為人知的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"get right","meaning":"準確預測","examples":[{"en":"Weather forecasts are difficult to get right over the long term.","zh":"長期而言，天氣預測很難準確。"},{"en":"To get something right means to make it accurate or correct.","zh":"get something right 指令某事準確或正確。"},{"en":"A student needs practice to get the spelling of difficult words right.","zh":"學生需要練習才能把難字串法寫對。"},{"en":"Weather forecasts are harder to get right when they cover a long future period.","zh":"當天氣預測涵蓋較遠未來時，就更難準確。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on accuracy.","zh":"這個短語集中於準確性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"so far","meaning":"到目前為止","examples":[{"en":"So far, forecasters are predicting another cold winter.","zh":"到目前為止，天氣預報員預測又一個寒冬。"},{"en":"So far means up to this point in time.","zh":"so far 指截至目前這一刻。"},{"en":"So far, the class has finished three chapters of the book.","zh":"到目前為止，全班已完成該書三章。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the situation may still change later.","zh":"這個短語暗示情況之後仍可能改變。"},{"en":"It is useful when reporting current progress or evidence.","zh":"它適合用來報告目前進展或證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"official start","meaning":"正式開始","examples":[{"en":"December marks the official start of the meteorological winter.","zh":"十二月標誌氣象冬季正式開始。"},{"en":"Official start means the formally recognised beginning of something.","zh":"official start 指某事被正式承認的開始。"},{"en":"The official start of the school year may be listed on the school calendar.","zh":"學年正式開始日期可能列在學校日曆上。"},{"en":"An official start gives everyone the same reference date.","zh":"正式開始日期給所有人同一參照日期。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the accepted beginning point.","zh":"這個短語指出被接受的開始點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"meteorological winter","meaning":"氣象冬季","examples":[{"en":"The meteorological winter officially starts in December.","zh":"氣象冬季正式在十二月開始。"},{"en":"Meteorological winter is the winter period defined by weather experts, usually using calendar months.","zh":"meteorological winter 指由天氣專家按月份界定的冬季時段。"},{"en":"Meteorological winter helps forecasters compare winter weather from year to year.","zh":"氣象冬季幫助預報員逐年比較冬季天氣。"},{"en":"It may differ from the astronomical winter based on solstice dates.","zh":"它可能不同於按冬至日期界定的天文冬季。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a weather-based definition of winter.","zh":"這個短語指基於天氣統計的冬季定義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"forecasters","meaning":"天氣預報員","examples":[{"en":"Forecasters are predicting another winter of low temperatures.","zh":"天氣預報員預測又一個低溫冬季。"},{"en":"Forecasters are people who predict future weather or trends.","zh":"forecasters 指預測未來天氣或趨勢的人。"},{"en":"Weather forecasters warn the public before storms, heatwaves, or heavy snow.","zh":"天氣預報員會在風暴、熱浪或大雪前提醒公眾。"},{"en":"Good forecasters use data, models, and experience to judge what may happen.","zh":"優秀預報員使用資料、模型和經驗判斷可能發生的事。"},{"en":"This word refers to people who make predictions.","zh":"這個字指作出預測的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"predict","meaning":"預測","examples":[{"en":"Forecasters predict another winter of record-breaking low temperatures.","zh":"天氣預報員預測又一個破紀錄低溫的冬季。"},{"en":"To predict means to say what is likely to happen in the future.","zh":"predict 指說出未來可能發生甚麼。"},{"en":"A teacher may predict that a hardworking student will improve by the next exam.","zh":"老師可能預測勤力學生到下一次考試會進步。"},{"en":"Predictions are stronger when they are based on evidence, not guesswork.","zh":"基於證據而非猜測的預測會更有力。"},{"en":"This word describes making a future judgement.","zh":"這個字描述對未來作出判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"record-breaking low temperatures","meaning":"破紀錄低溫","examples":[{"en":"Forecasters are predicting record-breaking low temperatures.","zh":"天氣預報員預測破紀錄低溫。"},{"en":"Record-breaking low temperatures are temperatures lower than any previously recorded level.","zh":"record-breaking low temperatures 指比以往所有紀錄都低的溫度。"},{"en":"A city may open emergency shelters during record-breaking low temperatures.","zh":"城市在破紀錄低溫期間可能開放緊急庇護中心。"},{"en":"Such temperatures can strain heating systems, roads, and public health services.","zh":"這類低溫可以令供暖系統、道路和公共健康服務受壓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extreme cold that sets a new record.","zh":"這個短語描述創下新紀錄的極端寒冷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"point to","meaning":"指出；以……作為依據","examples":[{"en":"Forecasters point to several indicators of a cold winter.","zh":"天氣預報員指出幾個寒冬指標。"},{"en":"To point to something means to use it as evidence or a sign.","zh":"point to something 指把某事作為證據或跡象。"},{"en":"A doctor may point to test results as evidence of infection.","zh":"醫生可能以化驗結果作為感染證據。"},{"en":"Weather indicators can point to a possible pattern before winter begins.","zh":"天氣指標可以在冬季開始前指向可能模式。"},{"en":"This phrase links evidence with a conclusion.","zh":"這個短語把證據與結論連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"sunspot activity","meaning":"太陽黑子活動","examples":[{"en":"Sunspot activity may be a key indicator of winter weather.","zh":"太陽黑子活動可能是冬季天氣的關鍵指標。"},{"en":"Sunspot activity means changes in dark spots and magnetic activity on the Sun’s surface.","zh":"sunspot activity 指太陽表面黑點和磁場活動的變化。"},{"en":"Scientists may study sunspot activity when examining possible links between the Sun and climate.","zh":"科學家研究太陽與氣候的可能關係時，可能研究太陽黑子活動。"},{"en":"If sunspot activity changes, some forecasters may look for effects on weather patterns.","zh":"如果太陽黑子活動改變，有些預報員可能尋找對天氣模式的影響。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to solar activity that may be used as an indicator.","zh":"這個短語指可被用作指標的太陽活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"geothermal activity","meaning":"地熱活動","examples":[{"en":"Forecasters point to geothermal activity as one possible indicator.","zh":"天氣預報員指出地熱活動是其中一個可能指標。"},{"en":"Geothermal activity is heat-related activity from inside the Earth.","zh":"geothermal activity 指來自地球內部的熱相關活動。"},{"en":"Hot springs and volcanic areas are linked with geothermal activity.","zh":"溫泉和火山地區與地熱活動有關。"},{"en":"Some people may consider geothermal activity when discussing wider Earth systems.","zh":"討論更廣泛地球系統時，有些人可能考慮地熱活動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to heat processes from within the planet.","zh":"這個短語指地球內部的熱過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the strength of","meaning":"……的強度","examples":[{"en":"Changes in the strength of the Gulf Stream may affect winter weather.","zh":"墨西哥灣暖流強度的變化可能影響冬季天氣。"},{"en":"The strength of something means how powerful, intense, or forceful it is.","zh":"strength of something 指某事物有多強、有多強烈或有多有力。"},{"en":"The strength of a Wi-Fi signal affects how smoothly a video call works.","zh":"Wi-Fi 訊號強度會影響視像通話是否順暢。"},{"en":"If the strength of an ocean current changes, nearby climates may also change.","zh":"如果洋流強度改變，附近氣候也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase measures power or intensity.","zh":"這個短語量度力量或強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"key indicators","meaning":"關鍵指標","examples":[{"en":"Sunspot activity and Gulf Stream changes are key indicators.","zh":"太陽黑子活動和墨西哥灣暖流變化是關鍵指標。"},{"en":"Key indicators are important signs used to judge what is happening or may happen.","zh":"key indicators 指用來判斷正在發生或可能發生甚麼的重要跡象。"},{"en":"Attendance and homework completion are key indicators of a student’s study habits.","zh":"出席率和功課完成情況是學生學習習慣的關鍵指標。"},{"en":"In weather forecasting, key indicators help forecasters build predictions.","zh":"在天氣預測中，關鍵指標幫助預報員建立預測。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies important clues.","zh":"這個短語指出重要線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in prospect","meaning":"即將可能出現","examples":[{"en":"A cold winter is in prospect.","zh":"寒冬即將可能出現。"},{"en":"In prospect means likely or expected to happen in the future.","zh":"in prospect 指未來可能或預期會發生。"},{"en":"If exams are in prospect, students should begin revising early.","zh":"如果考試即將出現，學生應及早開始溫習。"},{"en":"Something in prospect is not yet certain, but it appears possible.","zh":"in prospect 的事情尚未確定，但看來可能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a future possibility.","zh":"這個短語描述未來可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"were their predictions to be realised","meaning":"如果他們的預測成真","examples":[{"en":"Were their predictions to be realised, the climate might be changing.","zh":"如果他們的預測成真，氣候可能正在改變。"},{"en":"Were their predictions to be realised means if their predictions came true.","zh":"were their predictions to be realised 指如果他們的預測成真。"},{"en":"Were the school’s plans to be realised, students would have a new library next year.","zh":"如果學校的計劃成真，學生明年就會有新圖書館。"},{"en":"This formal structure introduces a possible future condition.","zh":"這個正式結構引出未來可能條件。"},{"en":"It is a more formal version of “if their predictions are realised.”","zh":"它是 “if their predictions are realised” 的較正式版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"point to","meaning":"顯示；指向","examples":[{"en":"Another cold winter would point to a subtle climatic change.","zh":"又一個寒冬會顯示微妙的氣候變化。"},{"en":"To point to something means to suggest or indicate it as a possible conclusion.","zh":"point to something 指暗示或顯示某事是可能結論。"},{"en":"Repeated absences may point to a problem at home rather than laziness.","zh":"反覆缺席可能指向家庭問題，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"Several cold winters together could point to a wider climate pattern.","zh":"幾個寒冬連續出現可能指向更廣泛的氣候模式。"},{"en":"This phrase means evidence seems to lead toward an explanation.","zh":"這個短語表示證據似乎通向某個解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"undergo a change","meaning":"正在經歷變化","examples":[{"en":"The British Isles may be undergoing a climatic change.","zh":"不列顛群島可能正在經歷氣候變化。"},{"en":"To undergo a change means to experience a process of becoming different.","zh":"undergo a change 指經歷變得不同的過程。"},{"en":"A school may undergo a change when it introduces a new curriculum.","zh":"當學校引入新課程，它可能正在經歷變化。"},{"en":"Climate systems may undergo change slowly, so patterns become clear only over time.","zh":"氣候系統可能緩慢經歷變化，因此模式要經過時間才清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being affected by a process of change.","zh":"這個短語描述受到變化過程影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"subtle climatic change","meaning":"微妙的氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"The British Isles may be undergoing a subtle climatic change.","zh":"不列顛群島可能正在經歷微妙的氣候變化。"},{"en":"A subtle climatic change is a small or gradual change in climate that may not be obvious at first.","zh":"subtle climatic change 指氣候中細微或逐漸的變化，起初未必明顯。"},{"en":"A few slightly colder winters may suggest a subtle climatic change if the pattern continues.","zh":"如果模式持續，幾個略冷冬季可能暗示微妙的氣候變化。"},{"en":"Subtle changes are easy to miss because they do not look dramatic immediately.","zh":"微妙變化容易被忽略，因為它們不會立即顯得劇烈。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a quiet but possibly important climate shift.","zh":"這個短語描述安靜但可能重要的氣候轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a return to","meaning":"回到……","examples":[{"en":"The trend may suggest a return to more severe winters.","zh":"這個趨勢可能暗示回到更嚴寒的冬季。"},{"en":"A return to something means going back to an earlier condition or pattern.","zh":"return to something 指回到較早的情況或模式。"},{"en":"A school may see a return to face-to-face lessons after months of online learning.","zh":"經過數月網課後，學校可能回到面授課堂。"},{"en":"If cold winters return, people may need to prepare as they did in the past.","zh":"如果寒冬回歸，人們可能需要像過去一樣準備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement back to a previous state.","zh":"這個短語描述回到先前狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"severe winters","meaning":"嚴寒冬季","examples":[{"en":"The British Isles may experience more severe winters in general.","zh":"不列顛群島一般可能經歷更多嚴寒冬季。"},{"en":"Severe winters are winters with harsh cold, heavy snow, ice, or difficult conditions.","zh":"severe winters 指有嚴寒、大雪、結冰或困難狀況的冬季。"},{"en":"Severe winters can increase heating costs and make travel dangerous.","zh":"嚴寒冬季可以增加供暖費並令交通危險。"},{"en":"If severe winters become more common, public services must prepare better.","zh":"如果嚴寒冬季變得更常見，公共服務必須更好準備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes winters that are unusually hard to live through.","zh":"這個短語描述異常難以度過的冬季。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"in general","meaning":"一般而言","examples":[{"en":"The change may mean more severe winters in general.","zh":"這種變化可能意味着一般而言冬季更嚴寒。"},{"en":"In general means usually, broadly, or overall.","zh":"in general 指通常、廣泛而言或整體而言。"},{"en":"In general, students learn better when examples are clear and concrete.","zh":"一般而言，當例子清楚而具體，學生學得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a broad pattern rather than every single case.","zh":"這個短語引出廣泛模式，而不是每一個個案。"},{"en":"It allows for exceptions while stating the main tendency.","zh":"它在說明主要傾向時容許例外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether statements agree with the information given.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與所給資料相符。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文章所說內容一致。"},{"en":"If the text says snow is rare in one region, a matching statement agrees with the information given.","zh":"如果文本說某地降雪罕見，吻合的陳述就與所給資料相符。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students should check the passage, not answer from memory.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應核對文章，而不是憑記憶作答。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"views of the writer","meaning":"作者的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The task asks whether each statement agrees with the views of the writer.","zh":"題目要求判斷每項陳述是否與作者的觀點一致。"},{"en":"Views of the writer are the opinions or attitudes expressed by the author.","zh":"views of the writer 指作者表達的意見或態度。"},{"en":"A question about the writer’s views asks what the author thinks, not just what happened.","zh":"關於作者觀點的題目問作者怎樣想，而不只是發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"Students must separate factual information from the writer’s opinion.","zh":"學生必須分清事實資料與作者意見。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on author attitude.","zh":"這個短語集中於作者態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A “NO” answer means the statement contradicts the views of the writer.","zh":"“NO” 答案表示該陳述與作者觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what that person thinks.","zh":"contradict the views of someone 指說出與某人想法相反的內容。"},{"en":"If a writer supports public transport, a statement praising only private cars may contradict the writer’s views.","zh":"如果作者支持公共交通，只讚揚私家車的陳述可能與作者觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"In exam tasks, contradiction must be clear from the text.","zh":"在考試題中，矛盾必須從文本清楚看出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct disagreement with an author’s opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述與作者意見直接相反。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Students choose “NOT GIVEN” if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"如果無法判斷作者怎樣想，學生選擇 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"impossible to say 指資料不足，不能作出判斷。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions the writer’s opinion on schools, it is impossible to say whether they support a policy.","zh":"如果文章從未提及作者對學校的看法，就無法判斷他是否支持某政策。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when the text gives no evidence.","zh":"當文本沒有證據時，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the answer cannot be determined from the passage.","zh":"這個短語表示答案無法從文章中確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"more likely to occur","meaning":"更有可能發生","examples":[{"en":"Snow is more likely to occur on the poleward side of the weather system.","zh":"雪更有可能在天氣系統的向極一側發生。"},{"en":"More likely to occur means having a higher chance of happening.","zh":"more likely to occur 指發生機會較高。"},{"en":"Traffic jams are more likely to occur near schools during morning rush hour.","zh":"早上繁忙時間，學校附近更有可能發生交通擠塞。"},{"en":"Snow is more likely when air is cold enough and moisture is available.","zh":"當空氣足夠寒冷且有水分，雪更有可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase compares probability.","zh":"這個短語比較可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"weather system","meaning":"天氣系統","examples":[{"en":"A warm front and a cold front can form part of a weather system.","zh":"暖鋒和冷鋒可以構成天氣系統的一部分。"},{"en":"A weather system is an organised pattern of air movement, pressure, temperature, and precipitation.","zh":"weather system 指由氣流、氣壓、溫度和降水組成的有組織模式。"},{"en":"A storm is a weather system that can bring rain, wind, thunder, or snow.","zh":"風暴是一種可以帶來雨、風、雷或雪的天氣系統。"},{"en":"Weather systems move and change, so their effects can spread across regions.","zh":"天氣系統會移動和改變，因此其影響可以擴散到不同地區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a connected set of atmospheric conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述一組相互連繫的大氣條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"aptly named","meaning":"名稱恰當的","examples":[{"en":"Lake-effect snow may not be aptly named if it is not limited to lakes.","zh":"如果湖泊效應雪不限於湖泊，它的名稱可能不算恰當。"},{"en":"Aptly named means given a suitable or accurate name.","zh":"aptly named 指名稱合適或準確。"},{"en":"A quiet reading room is aptly named if people really use it for silent study.","zh":"如果安靜閱讀室真的供人安靜自修，它就是名稱恰當。"},{"en":"If a name misleads people, it may not be aptly named.","zh":"如果名稱誤導人，它可能不算恰當。"},{"en":"This phrase judges whether a name fits the thing it describes.","zh":"這個短語判斷名稱是否符合所描述事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"weather phenomenon","meaning":"天氣現象","examples":[{"en":"Lake-effect snow is a weather phenomenon linked to bodies of water.","zh":"湖泊效應雪是一種與水體有關的天氣現象。"},{"en":"A weather phenomenon is an observable event or pattern in the atmosphere.","zh":"weather phenomenon 指大氣中可觀察的事件或模式。"},{"en":"Fog, hail, lightning, and snowstorms are weather phenomena.","zh":"霧、冰雹、閃電和暴雪都是天氣現象。"},{"en":"Studying a weather phenomenon helps scientists explain when and why it happens.","zh":"研究天氣現象有助科學家解釋它何時及為何發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a noticeable weather event or process.","zh":"這個短語描述可注意到的天氣事件或過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"exposed to high winds","meaning":"暴露於強風之中","examples":[{"en":"The windward side of a mountain is exposed to high winds.","zh":"山的迎風面暴露於強風之中。"},{"en":"Exposed to high winds means open to strong winds without much protection.","zh":"exposed to high winds 指缺乏保護而受到強風影響。"},{"en":"A balcony on the top floor may be exposed to high winds during a storm.","zh":"頂樓露台在風暴期間可能暴露於強風之中。"},{"en":"Exposed places can be colder and more dangerous because wind removes heat and affects balance.","zh":"暴露地點可能更冷、更危險，因為風會帶走熱力並影響平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes vulnerability to strong wind.","zh":"這個短語描述容易受強風影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"in the absence of","meaning":"在缺乏……的情況下","examples":[{"en":"In the absence of dust, freezing may require much lower temperatures.","zh":"在缺乏塵埃的情況下，結冰可能需要低得多的溫度。"},{"en":"In the absence of something means when that thing is not present.","zh":"in the absence of something 指當某物不存在時。"},{"en":"In the absence of clear rules, students may not know what is allowed.","zh":"在缺乏清楚規則的情況下，學生可能不知道甚麼被允許。"},{"en":"Without dust particles, water droplets may need colder conditions to freeze.","zh":"沒有塵埃粒子時，水滴可能需要更冷條件才結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what happens when something is missing.","zh":"這個短語引出缺少某物時會發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"start the freezing process","meaning":"啟動結冰過程","examples":[{"en":"Dust can help start the freezing process in warmer clouds.","zh":"塵埃可以幫助啟動較暖雲中的結冰過程。"},{"en":"To start the freezing process means to begin the change from liquid water into ice.","zh":"start the freezing process 指開始由液態水變成冰的變化。"},{"en":"A seed crystal can start the freezing process in a supercooled liquid.","zh":"晶種可以在過冷液體中啟動結冰過程。"},{"en":"Once freezing begins, ice can grow as more water attaches to it.","zh":"一旦結冰開始，更多水分附着其上，冰就會生長。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the first step of becoming ice.","zh":"這個短語集中於變成冰的第一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"mean temperature","meaning":"平均溫度","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to a cloud whose mean temperature is relatively high.","zh":"該陳述指一朵平均溫度相對較高的雲。"},{"en":"Mean temperature is the average temperature measured across a place, period, or object.","zh":"mean temperature 指某地、某段時間或某物的平均溫度。"},{"en":"The mean temperature of a week is found by averaging the daily temperatures.","zh":"一星期的平均溫度可由每日溫度平均計算得出。"},{"en":"A cloud with a higher mean temperature may need particles for freezing to begin.","zh":"平均溫度較高的雲可能需要粒子讓結冰開始。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to average temperature, not the hottest or coldest point.","zh":"這個短語指平均溫度，而不是最高或最低點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"real colour of snow","meaning":"雪的真實顏色","examples":[{"en":"The real colour of snow is not necessarily the colour it appears to be.","zh":"雪的真實顏色未必就是它看起來的顏色。"},{"en":"The real colour of snow refers to the actual colour of the ice crystals, not their visual appearance from scattered light.","zh":"real colour of snow 指冰晶的實際顏色，而不是光線散射造成的視覺外觀。"},{"en":"A glass window may look bright white from reflected sunlight, even though its real material is transparent.","zh":"玻璃窗可能因反射陽光而看起來明亮白色，即使其材料實際上透明。"},{"en":"Snow looks white because of light reflection, not because each crystal is truly white.","zh":"雪看起來是白色，是因為光線反射，而不是每粒晶體真的白色。"},{"en":"This phrase separates actual material colour from what the human eye sees.","zh":"這個短語把材料真實顏色與人眼所見分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"to the human eye","meaning":"對人眼而言","examples":[{"en":"Snow appears white to the human eye.","zh":"對人眼而言，雪顯得白色。"},{"en":"To the human eye means as seen by people without special instruments.","zh":"to the human eye 指人在沒有特殊儀器下所看見的樣子。"},{"en":"To the human eye, a distant star may look like a tiny point of light.","zh":"對人眼而言，遙遠星星可能像一個小光點。"},{"en":"Some things appear different under a microscope than they do to the human eye.","zh":"有些東西在顯微鏡下看起來與人眼所見不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordinary visual perception.","zh":"這個短語描述普通視覺感知。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"shaped like a prism","meaning":"呈棱柱狀","examples":[{"en":"Snowflakes shaped like a prism form under certain conditions.","zh":"呈棱柱狀的雪花在某些條件下形成。"},{"en":"Shaped like a prism means having a long geometric form with flat sides.","zh":"shaped like a prism 指具有平面側面的細長幾何形態。"},{"en":"A glass ornament shaped like a prism can bend light into colours.","zh":"呈棱柱狀的玻璃飾物可以把光折射成顏色。"},{"en":"In snow, prism-shaped crystals form when temperature conditions favour column growth.","zh":"在雪中，當溫度條件有利於柱狀生長，棱柱狀晶體便形成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific geometric appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述特定幾何外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"milder weather","meaning":"較溫和天氣","examples":[{"en":"Prism-shaped flakes can form in relatively milder weather than complex patterns.","zh":"與複雜形態相比，棱柱狀雪花可以在相對較溫和天氣中形成。"},{"en":"Milder weather is weather that is less cold, harsh, or severe.","zh":"milder weather 指較不寒冷、嚴酷或惡劣的天氣。"},{"en":"People may wear lighter coats during milder weather in winter.","zh":"冬季較溫和天氣期間，人們可能穿較薄外套。"},{"en":"Slightly warmer conditions can change the shape of snow crystals.","zh":"稍暖條件可以改變雪晶形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weather that is gentler than extreme cold.","zh":"這個短語描述比極端寒冷更溫和的天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"intricate growth patterns","meaning":"複雜細緻的生長形態","examples":[{"en":"More intricate growth patterns form at very low temperatures.","zh":"更複雜細緻的生長形態在極低溫下形成。"},{"en":"Intricate growth patterns are very detailed and complex forms of development.","zh":"intricate growth patterns 指非常細緻而複雜的發展形態。"},{"en":"A snowflake with many branches has an intricate pattern.","zh":"有許多分枝的雪花具有複雜細緻的圖案。"},{"en":"Intricate patterns may form when moisture and temperature interact in precise ways.","zh":"當水分和溫度以精確方式互相作用，複雜圖案可能形成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fine, complicated structure.","zh":"這個短語描述精細而複雜的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"more voluminous than","meaning":"比……體積更大","examples":[{"en":"The statement compares whether thin flat crystals are more voluminous than column-like crystals.","zh":"該陳述比較薄而扁平晶體是否比柱狀晶體體積更大。"},{"en":"More voluminous than means larger in volume or taking up more space than something else.","zh":"more voluminous than 指體積更大或佔用更多空間。"},{"en":"A thick winter coat is more voluminous than a light jacket.","zh":"厚冬衣比薄外套體積更大。"},{"en":"Different crystal shapes may take up different amounts of space even if they contain similar material.","zh":"不同晶體形狀即使含有相似材料，也可能佔用不同空間。"},{"en":"This phrase compares physical size by volume.","zh":"這個短語按體積比較實體大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"complete the sentences below","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the sentences below using words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成以下句子。"},{"en":"To complete the sentences below means to fill in the missing words in the sentences that follow.","zh":"complete the sentences below 指填寫下方句子的缺失字詞。"},{"en":"Students should read the grammar before and after each gap before choosing an answer.","zh":"學生選答案前應閱讀空格前後的文法。"},{"en":"Sentence completion tests both meaning and exact word form.","zh":"句子填空同時測試意思和準確詞形。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不超過三個字","examples":[{"en":"Students should choose no more than three words from the passage.","zh":"學生應從文章中選擇不超過三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain one, two, or three words only.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案只能包含一個、兩個或三個字。"},{"en":"“higher altitudes” fits this rule, but adding extra words may make the answer wrong.","zh":"“higher altitudes” 符合這條規則，但加入多餘字詞可能令答案錯。"},{"en":"Word limits require students to copy only the necessary words.","zh":"字數限制要求學生只抄寫必要字詞。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict answer-length rule.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格答案長度規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"uncommon feature of","meaning":"……並不罕見的特徵","examples":[{"en":"Snowfall is not an uncommon feature of a United Kingdom winter.","zh":"降雪並不是英國冬季中罕見的特徵。"},{"en":"An uncommon feature of something is something unusual within it.","zh":"uncommon feature of something 指某事中的不尋常特徵。"},{"en":"Heavy traffic is not an uncommon feature of Monday mornings in a busy city.","zh":"嚴重交通擠塞並不是繁忙城市星期一早上的罕見特徵。"},{"en":"Saying snow is not uncommon means it happens often enough to be expected.","zh":"說雪並不罕見，意思是它發生得足夠常見，可被預期。"},{"en":"This phrase describes whether something is usual in a particular situation.","zh":"這個短語描述某事在特定情況中是否常見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"significant accumulations","meaning":"大量積雪","examples":[{"en":"It is rare for significant accumulations of snow to remain.","zh":"大量積雪停留是罕見的。"},{"en":"Significant accumulations are large enough amounts that matter or cause effects.","zh":"significant accumulations 指大到有影響或值得注意的累積量。"},{"en":"Significant accumulations of rubbish can attract insects and create bad smells.","zh":"大量垃圾積聚可以吸引昆蟲並產生臭味。"},{"en":"Significant snow accumulations can block paths and slow transport.","zh":"大量積雪可以堵塞小路並拖慢交通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes build-up large enough to be noticed.","zh":"這個短語描述足以被注意的累積。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"remain on the ground","meaning":"留在地面上","examples":[{"en":"Snow rarely remains on the ground for a long time in the United Kingdom.","zh":"在英國，雪很少長時間留在地面上。"},{"en":"To remain on the ground means to stay on the surface without melting or being removed.","zh":"remain on the ground 指停留在表面而沒有融化或被移走。"},{"en":"Fallen leaves may remain on the ground until workers sweep them away.","zh":"落葉可能留在地面上，直到工人掃走它們。"},{"en":"Snow remains longer when the ground is cold and temperatures stay below freezing.","zh":"當地面寒冷且氣溫維持在冰點以下，雪會停留更久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes snow staying after it has fallen.","zh":"這個短語描述雪落下後仍停留。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"for any great length of time","meaning":"長時間","examples":[{"en":"Snow rarely remains for any great length of time.","zh":"雪很少長時間停留。"},{"en":"For any great length of time means for a long period.","zh":"for any great length of time 指很長一段時間。"},{"en":"A phone battery will not last for any great length of time if many apps are running.","zh":"如果許多應用程式正在運行，手機電池不會維持很長時間。"},{"en":"Snow that does not last long may still cause short-term travel problems.","zh":"不會持續很久的雪仍可能造成短期交通問題。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises long duration, usually in a negative sentence.","zh":"這個短語強調長時間，通常用於否定句中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"fail to follow","meaning":"未有跟隨","examples":[{"en":"Three consecutive winters have failed to follow the warming trend.","zh":"三個連續冬季未有跟隨變暖趨勢。"},{"en":"To fail to follow a trend means not to match the expected pattern.","zh":"fail to follow a trend 指沒有符合預期模式。"},{"en":"If most students improve but one class does not, that class fails to follow the trend.","zh":"如果大多數學生進步但某班沒有，該班就是未有跟隨趨勢。"},{"en":"A few winters can fail to follow a mild trend by becoming unusually cold.","zh":"幾個冬季可以因異常寒冷而未有跟隨溫和趨勢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an exception to an expected pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述預期模式中的例外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"towards milder weather","meaning":"朝向較溫和天氣","examples":[{"en":"The trend was towards milder, wetter weather.","zh":"趨勢是朝向較溫和、較潮濕的天氣。"},{"en":"Towards milder weather means moving in the direction of less cold conditions.","zh":"towards milder weather 指朝較不寒冷的情況發展。"},{"en":"A city may see a shift towards milder weather as spring approaches.","zh":"隨着春天接近，城市可能出現朝向較溫和天氣的轉變。"},{"en":"If a climate trend moves towards milder weather, severe cold may become less common.","zh":"如果氣候趨勢朝向較溫和天氣，嚴寒可能變得較少見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the direction of climate or weather change.","zh":"這個短語描述氣候或天氣變化的方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"on account of","meaning":"由於","examples":[{"en":"The British Isles are warmer on account of the Gulf Stream.","zh":"不列顛群島由於墨西哥灣暖流而較暖。"},{"en":"On account of means because of.","zh":"on account of 指由於。"},{"en":"The match was delayed on account of heavy rain.","zh":"比賽由於大雨而延遲。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the reason for a situation.","zh":"這個短語引出某情況的原因。"},{"en":"It is more formal than simply saying “because of.”","zh":"它比簡單說 “because of” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"the influence of","meaning":"……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The British climate is affected by the influence of the Gulf Stream.","zh":"英國氣候受到墨西哥灣暖流的影響。"},{"en":"The influence of something is the effect it has on another thing.","zh":"influence of something 指某事對另一事物造成的影響。"},{"en":"The influence of a good teacher can last long after students leave school.","zh":"好老師的影響可以在學生離校後仍持續很久。"},{"en":"Ocean currents influence climate by moving heat around the planet.","zh":"洋流透過在地球各處移動熱力來影響氣候。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the power one thing has to affect another.","zh":"這個短語描述某事影響另一事的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"should next winter be","meaning":"如果下一個冬季是……","examples":[{"en":"Should next winter be unusually cold, it may indicate climatic change.","zh":"如果下一個冬季異常寒冷，這可能顯示氣候變化。"},{"en":"Should next winter be means if next winter is, in a formal conditional structure.","zh":"should next winter be 指「如果下一個冬季是……」，屬正式條件句。"},{"en":"Should the exam be postponed, students will receive a new timetable.","zh":"如果考試延期，學生將收到新時間表。"},{"en":"This structure is formal and often used in written explanations.","zh":"這個結構較正式，常用於書面解釋。"},{"en":"It introduces a possible future condition.","zh":"它引出未來可能條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"unusually cold","meaning":"異常寒冷","examples":[{"en":"Another unusually cold winter may suggest a climatic shift.","zh":"又一個異常寒冷的冬季可能暗示氣候轉變。"},{"en":"Unusually cold means colder than normal or expected.","zh":"unusually cold 指比正常或預期更冷。"},{"en":"An unusually cold classroom may make students keep their coats on.","zh":"異常寒冷的課室可能令學生一直穿着外套。"},{"en":"If several winters are unusually cold, people may look for a larger pattern.","zh":"如果幾個冬季都異常寒冷，人們可能尋找更大的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cold that stands out from normal conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述明顯不同於正常情況的寒冷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be indicative of","meaning":"顯示；表明","examples":[{"en":"A cold winter may be indicative of climatic change.","zh":"寒冬可能顯示氣候變化。"},{"en":"To be indicative of something means to be a sign that it may be happening.","zh":"be indicative of something 指作為某事可能正在發生的跡象。"},{"en":"Repeated lateness may be indicative of transport problems or poor sleep.","zh":"反覆遲到可能表明交通問題或睡眠不足。"},{"en":"One sign alone may not prove the cause, but it can point toward it.","zh":"單一跡象未必證明原因，但可以指向原因。"},{"en":"This phrase connects evidence with a possible explanation.","zh":"這個短語把證據與可能解釋連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be under way","meaning":"正在進行","examples":[{"en":"A subtle climatic change may be under way.","zh":"微妙的氣候變化可能正在進行。"},{"en":"To be under way means to be happening or in progress.","zh":"be under way 指正在發生或進行中。"},{"en":"Construction of the new library is under way if workers have already started building.","zh":"如果工人已開始建造，新圖書館工程就是正在進行。"},{"en":"A change under way may not be complete yet, but signs are visible.","zh":"正在進行的變化未必已完成，但跡象可見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a process already happening.","zh":"這個短語描述已經發生中的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the summary with words from the list.","zh":"考生用列表中的詞語完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill gaps in a shortened version of the passage.","zh":"complete the summary 指在文章縮短版本中填補空格。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole summary before choosing words from the list.","zh":"學生從詞語列表選字前，應先讀完整個摘要。"},{"en":"A good answer must fit both meaning and grammar.","zh":"好答案必須同時符合意思和文法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common reading-test task.","zh":"這個短語描述常見閱讀測驗任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"list of words","meaning":"詞語列表","examples":[{"en":"The task provides a list of words for the summary.","zh":"題目提供一個摘要用的詞語列表。"},{"en":"A list of words is a set of possible words students can choose from.","zh":"list of words 指學生可從中選擇的一組可能詞語。"},{"en":"In a vocabulary quiz, a list of words may help students fill blanks correctly.","zh":"在詞彙測驗中，詞語列表可能幫助學生正確填空。"},{"en":"Extra words in the list may distract students from the correct answer.","zh":"列表中的額外詞語可能干擾學生選出正確答案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the answer choices for a completion task.","zh":"這個短語描述填空題的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"an uncommon sight","meaning":"並不罕見的景象","examples":[{"en":"Snowfall is not an uncommon sight in Britain during winter.","zh":"冬季在英國，降雪並不是罕見景象。"},{"en":"An uncommon sight is something people do not often see.","zh":"uncommon sight 指人們不常看見的景象。"},{"en":"A bicycle on a motorway is an uncommon sight because it is not normally allowed there.","zh":"高速公路上出現單車是罕見景象，因為通常不容許單車在那裡行駛。"},{"en":"Saying snow is not an uncommon sight means people do see it from time to time.","zh":"說雪並不是罕見景象，意思是人們時不時會看見它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how often something is seen.","zh":"這個短語描述某事被看見的頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"rarely persist","meaning":"很少持續","examples":[{"en":"Snowy weather rarely persists for very long in Britain.","zh":"英國的下雪天氣很少持續很久。"},{"en":"Rarely persist means usually does not continue for a long time.","zh":"rarely persist 指通常不會長時間持續。"},{"en":"A short headache rarely persists if the student rests and drinks water.","zh":"如果學生休息並喝水，短暫頭痛通常很少持續。"},{"en":"Snow that rarely persists may melt before large accumulations build up.","zh":"很少持續的雪可能在大量積雪形成前融化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that usually ends quickly.","zh":"這個短語描述通常很快結束的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"up until a few years ago","meaning":"直到幾年前","examples":[{"en":"Up until a few years ago, British winters seemed to be getting milder.","zh":"直到幾年前，英國冬季似乎正變得更溫和。"},{"en":"Up until a few years ago means until a recent point in the past.","zh":"up until a few years ago 指直到過去較近期的某個時間點。"},{"en":"Up until a few years ago, many students submitted homework on paper.","zh":"直到幾年前，許多學生仍以紙本提交功課。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a past pattern that may have changed recently.","zh":"這個短語引出最近可能已改變的過去模式。"},{"en":"It helps contrast earlier expectations with current evidence.","zh":"它有助把早前預期與現有證據作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"perception has changed","meaning":"看法已經改變","examples":[{"en":"This perception has changed fairly dramatically.","zh":"這種看法已經相當顯著地改變。"},{"en":"Perception has changed means people now see or understand something differently.","zh":"perception has changed 指人們現在以不同方式看待或理解某事。"},{"en":"Public perception of online learning has changed as more students use it successfully.","zh":"隨着更多學生成功使用網上學習，公眾對它的看法已經改變。"},{"en":"New evidence can change perception quickly.","zh":"新證據可以迅速改變看法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift in how people think.","zh":"這個短語描述人們想法的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"fairly dramatically","meaning":"相當顯著地","examples":[{"en":"The perception has changed fairly dramatically over recent winters.","zh":"這種看法在近幾個冬季已相當顯著地改變。"},{"en":"Fairly dramatically means quite noticeably or strongly.","zh":"fairly dramatically 指相當明顯或強烈地。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may improve fairly dramatically after regular speaking practice.","zh":"經過定期口語練習，學生信心可能相當顯著地提升。"},{"en":"Several unusual winters can change public opinion fairly dramatically.","zh":"幾個不尋常冬季可以相當顯著地改變公眾意見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change that is clearly noticeable.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚可見的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"over the last three winters","meaning":"在過去三個冬季","examples":[{"en":"The perception changed over the last three winters.","zh":"這種看法在過去三個冬季改變了。"},{"en":"Over the last three winters means during the most recent three winter seasons.","zh":"over the last three winters 指在最近三個冬季期間。"},{"en":"Over the last three school terms, the student’s writing became more accurate.","zh":"在過去三個學期，該學生寫作變得更準確。"},{"en":"A pattern seen over three winters may feel stronger than one unusual season.","zh":"三個冬季中出現的模式，比單一不尋常季節感覺更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a recent time frame.","zh":"這個短語給出近期時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"more than half a century","meaning":"半個多世紀以來","examples":[{"en":"The cold period was the longest for more than half a century.","zh":"這段寒冷時期是半個多世紀以來最長的。"},{"en":"More than half a century means more than fifty years.","zh":"more than half a century 指超過五十年。"},{"en":"A theatre that has served the community for more than half a century has a long history.","zh":"服務社區半個多世紀的劇院有悠久歷史。"},{"en":"A weather event unusual for more than half a century feels historically significant.","zh":"半個多世紀以來罕見的天氣事件，感覺具有歷史意義。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a long period of comparison.","zh":"這個短語強調長期比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"it is now feared that","meaning":"現在人們擔心","examples":[{"en":"It is now feared that the climate of the British Isles is changing.","zh":"現在人們擔心不列顛群島的氣候正在改變。"},{"en":"It is now feared that means people are now worried that something may be true.","zh":"it is now feared that 指人們現在擔心某事可能是真的。"},{"en":"It is now feared that the old bridge may be unsafe after years of damage.","zh":"現在人們擔心舊橋多年受損後可能不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a serious concern, not a confirmed fact.","zh":"這個短語引出嚴重憂慮，而不是已確認事實。"},{"en":"It shows anxiety based on recent evidence.","zh":"它顯示基於近期證據的焦慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"equally severe","meaning":"同樣嚴寒","examples":[{"en":"If the next few winters are equally severe, the climate may be changing.","zh":"如果接下來幾個冬季同樣嚴寒，氣候可能正在改變。"},{"en":"Equally severe means just as harsh or serious as something else.","zh":"equally severe 指與另一事物一樣嚴酷或嚴重。"},{"en":"Two exams are equally severe if both are long, difficult, and strictly marked.","zh":"如果兩場考試都很長、很難且評分嚴格，它們就是同樣嚴苛。"},{"en":"If several winters are equally severe, people may see a repeated pattern.","zh":"如果幾個冬季同樣嚴寒，人們可能看見重複模式。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the same high level of severity.","zh":"這個短語比較同樣高程度的嚴重性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"signal a permanent move to","meaning":"顯示永久轉向","examples":[{"en":"Severe winters could signal a permanent move to colder weather.","zh":"嚴寒冬季可能顯示永久轉向較冷天氣。"},{"en":"To signal a permanent move to something means to show a lasting shift toward it.","zh":"signal a permanent move to something 指顯示朝某方向出現持久轉變。"},{"en":"A company closing all physical shops may signal a permanent move to online sales.","zh":"公司關閉所有實體店，可能顯示永久轉向網上銷售。"},{"en":"Repeated cold winters may signal a longer-lasting shift rather than a short exception.","zh":"反覆出現寒冬可能顯示較長期轉變，而不是短暫例外。"},{"en":"This phrase links a sign with a possible lasting change.","zh":"這個短語把跡象與可能持久改變連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"winter weather in general","meaning":"整體冬季天氣","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses possible changes in winter weather in general.","zh":"文章討論整體冬季天氣可能出現的變化。"},{"en":"Winter weather in general means the overall pattern of winter conditions, not one single storm.","zh":"winter weather in general 指冬季狀況的整體模式，而不是單一風暴。"},{"en":"Winter weather in general includes temperature, snow, rain, wind, and ice.","zh":"整體冬季天氣包括溫度、雪、雨、風和冰。"},{"en":"One cold week may not change winter weather in general, but repeated seasons might.","zh":"一個寒冷星期未必改變整體冬季天氣，但反覆出現的季節可能會。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on broad winter patterns.","zh":"這個短語集中於廣泛冬季模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"scientists blame","meaning":"科學家將……歸因於","examples":[{"en":"Scientists blame several factors for the predicted cold winter.","zh":"科學家將預測中的寒冬歸因於幾個因素。"},{"en":"Scientists blame something when they identify it as a cause or explanation.","zh":"scientists blame something 指科學家把某事辨認為原因或解釋。"},{"en":"Doctors may blame poor sleep for a student’s constant tiredness.","zh":"醫生可能把學生持續疲倦歸因於睡眠不足。"},{"en":"Blaming several factors suggests the result has more than one possible cause.","zh":"將結果歸因於幾個因素，暗示它有多於一個可能原因。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces causes identified by experts.","zh":"這個短語引出專家指出的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"以及","examples":[{"en":"Scientists mention sunspot activity as well as the Gulf Stream.","zh":"科學家提到太陽黑子活動以及墨西哥灣暖流。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to.","zh":"as well as 指以及、除此之外。"},{"en":"A good after-school programme supports homework as well as social skills.","zh":"好的課後計劃支援功課以及社交技能。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another item to the discussion.","zh":"這個短語把另一項加入討論。"},{"en":"It shows that more than one factor is involved.","zh":"它顯示涉及不止一個因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"until now","meaning":"直到現在","examples":[{"en":"Until now, the Gulf Stream has kept Britain relatively mild.","zh":"直到現在，墨西哥灣暖流一直令英國相對溫和。"},{"en":"Until now means up to the present moment.","zh":"until now 指截至現在這一刻。"},{"en":"Until now, the student has always revised alone.","zh":"直到現在，該學生一直獨自溫習。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the previous situation may be changing.","zh":"這個短語暗示之前的情況可能正在改變。"},{"en":"It contrasts past and present expectations.","zh":"它對比過去和現在的預期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"throughout the rest of the world","meaning":"在世界其他地方","examples":[{"en":"Similar latitudes throughout the rest of the world may be colder.","zh":"在世界其他地方，緯度相若地區可能更冷。"},{"en":"Throughout the rest of the world means in other places around the world outside the place being discussed.","zh":"throughout the rest of the world 指正在討論地點以外的世界其他地方。"},{"en":"A fashion popular locally may be unknown throughout the rest of the world.","zh":"本地流行的時尚，在世界其他地方可能不為人知。"},{"en":"This phrase broadens comparison beyond one region.","zh":"這個短語把比較擴展到單一地區以外。"},{"en":"It helps show whether a place is unusual internationally.","zh":"它有助顯示某地方在國際比較中是否不尋常。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"uninterrupted period","meaning":"連續不斷的時期","examples":[{"en":"The winters may represent an uninterrupted period of cold weather.","zh":"這些冬季可能代表一段連續不斷的寒冷天氣時期。"},{"en":"An uninterrupted period is a stretch of time with no break in the pattern.","zh":"uninterrupted period 指某模式沒有中斷的一段時間。"},{"en":"A student who studies for three uninterrupted hours works without stopping.","zh":"連續不斷學習三小時的學生，是沒有停下來地學習。"},{"en":"Several cold winters in a row create an uninterrupted period of cold conditions.","zh":"幾個寒冬接連出現，形成連續不斷的寒冷時期。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses continuity.","zh":"這個短語強調連續性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"waning influence","meaning":"減弱中的影響","examples":[{"en":"A waning influence of the Gulf Stream could make winters colder.","zh":"墨西哥灣暖流減弱中的影響可能令冬季更冷。"},{"en":"Waning influence means weakening effect or decreasing power.","zh":"waning influence 指影響力減弱或力量下降。"},{"en":"A teacher’s waning influence may appear when students stop following classroom routines.","zh":"當學生不再遵守課室常規，老師的影響力可能正在減弱。"},{"en":"If a warm current’s influence wanes, the climate it warms may become colder.","zh":"如果暖流影響減弱，它所暖化的氣候可能變冷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes influence becoming weaker over time.","zh":"這個短語描述影響力隨時間變弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"extreme winter weather","meaning":"極端冬季天氣","examples":[{"en":"A climatic change could bring more extreme winter weather.","zh":"氣候變化可能帶來更多極端冬季天氣。"},{"en":"Extreme winter weather means unusually severe winter conditions, such as intense cold, heavy snow, or dangerous ice.","zh":"extreme winter weather 指異常嚴重的冬季狀況，例如嚴寒、大雪或危險結冰。"},{"en":"Extreme winter weather may close schools and make roads unsafe.","zh":"極端冬季天氣可能令學校停課並令道路不安全。"},{"en":"If extreme winter weather becomes more common, communities need stronger preparation.","zh":"如果極端冬季天氣變得更常見，社區需要更強準備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes winter weather beyond normal difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述超出正常困難程度的冬季天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 73 - ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW ABOUT SNOW.pdf","sourcePage":24}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 74":[{"front":"Map Wars","meaning":"地圖之爭","examples":[{"en":"Map Wars explores how different world maps express different assumptions.","zh":"《地圖之爭》探討不同世界地圖如何表達不同假設。"},{"en":"Map Wars refers to debates about which world map is fair, useful, accurate, or misleading.","zh":"Map Wars 指關於哪種世界地圖公平、有用、準確或具誤導性的爭論。"},{"en":"Students may discuss Map Wars when they compare how Europe and Africa look on different maps.","zh":"學生比較歐洲和非洲在不同地圖上的樣子時，可能討論地圖之爭。"},{"en":"Map Wars happen because every flat map has to distort the round earth in some way.","zh":"地圖之爭之所以出現，是因為每張平面地圖都必須以某種方式扭曲圓形地球。"},{"en":"This title suggests that maps are not neutral pictures; they can reflect choices and values.","zh":"這個標題暗示地圖不是中立圖片；它們可以反映選擇和價值觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"express a point of view","meaning":"表達一種觀點","examples":[{"en":"A map of the world expresses a point of view.","zh":"一張世界地圖表達一種觀點。"},{"en":"To express a point of view means to show a particular way of seeing or judging something.","zh":"express a point of view 指展示某種看待或判斷事物的方式。"},{"en":"A newspaper headline can express a point of view even before the article begins.","zh":"報紙標題甚至在文章開始前，已經可以表達一種觀點。"},{"en":"Maps express a point of view when they make some places look central, large, or important.","zh":"當地圖令某些地方看起來居中、龐大或重要，它們就是在表達一種觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds students that information can be shaped by perspective.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生，資訊可以被視角塑造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a correct model of","meaning":"……的正確模型","examples":[{"en":"A correct model of the earth is a sphere or an ellipsoid.","zh":"地球的正確模型是球體或橢球體。"},{"en":"A correct model of something is a representation that matches its real shape or structure closely.","zh":"a correct model of something 指與某物真實形狀或結構非常相符的呈現。"},{"en":"A correct model of a heart helps medical students understand how blood flows.","zh":"心臟的正確模型幫助醫科學生理解血液如何流動。"},{"en":"If a model is inaccurate, people may misunderstand the object it represents.","zh":"如果模型不準確，人們可能誤解它所代表的物件。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when comparing a representation with reality.","zh":"這個短語用於比較呈現方式與現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a sphere","meaning":"球體","examples":[{"en":"A correct model of the earth is a sphere.","zh":"地球的正確模型是球體。"},{"en":"A sphere is a round three-dimensional shape like a ball.","zh":"sphere 指像球一樣的圓形立體形狀。"},{"en":"A football is roughly a sphere, while a book is not.","zh":"足球大致是球體，而書本不是。"},{"en":"A globe looks like a sphere because it represents the round earth.","zh":"地球儀看起來像球體，因為它代表圓形的地球。"},{"en":"This word is useful when describing objects that are round in every direction.","zh":"這個詞用於描述各個方向都呈圓形的物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an ellipsoid","meaning":"橢球體","examples":[{"en":"An ellipsoid is a more precise model of the earth.","zh":"橢球體是地球更精確的模型。"},{"en":"An ellipsoid is a three-dimensional shape like a slightly stretched or flattened sphere.","zh":"ellipsoid 指像略為拉長或壓扁的球體那樣的立體形狀。"},{"en":"A rugby ball is closer to an ellipsoid than a perfect sphere.","zh":"欖球比完美球體更接近橢球體。"},{"en":"Scientists use an ellipsoid when a simple sphere is not accurate enough.","zh":"當簡單球體不夠準確，科學家會使用橢球體。"},{"en":"This word suggests a round shape that is not perfectly round.","zh":"這個詞暗示一種圓形但並非完美圓的形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"to be precise","meaning":"準確來說","examples":[{"en":"The earth is an ellipsoid, to be precise.","zh":"準確來說，地球是橢球體。"},{"en":"To be precise means to give a more exact or careful statement.","zh":"to be precise 指給出更準確或更仔細的說法。"},{"en":"The lesson starts at 8:30, or 8:28 to be precise, because students must arrive early.","zh":"課堂 8:30 開始，準確來說是 8:28，因為學生必須提早到達。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when a general statement needs a more accurate version.","zh":"當一般說法需要更準確版本時，作者會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the speaker is correcting or sharpening the details.","zh":"這個短語表示說話者正在更正或精確化細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"photographs of the earth from space","meaning":"從太空拍攝的地球照片","examples":[{"en":"Photographs of the earth from space show that the planet is round.","zh":"從太空拍攝的地球照片顯示這個星球是圓的。"},{"en":"Photographs of the earth from space are images taken from outside the planet that show its overall shape.","zh":"photographs of the earth from space 指在地球外拍攝、顯示地球整體形狀的影像。"},{"en":"A science teacher may show photographs of the earth from space to explain why flat maps are limited.","zh":"科學老師可能展示從太空拍攝的地球照片，以解釋平面地圖為何有限。"},{"en":"Such photographs make the earth’s roundness easier to accept because students can see it directly.","zh":"這些照片讓地球是圓的這一點更容易被接受，因為學生可以直接看見。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to visual evidence from space.","zh":"這個短語指來自太空的視覺證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"provide reassurance on","meaning":"就……提供保證","examples":[{"en":"Photographs of the earth from space provide reassurance on that point.","zh":"從太空拍攝的地球照片就這一點提供保證。"},{"en":"To provide reassurance on something means to make people feel more certain or less worried about it.","zh":"provide reassurance on something 指令人在某方面更肯定或較不擔心。"},{"en":"A doctor’s clear explanation can provide reassurance on a patient’s test result.","zh":"醫生清楚解釋檢查結果，可以就病人的情況提供保證。"},{"en":"Evidence provides reassurance when it confirms what people were unsure about.","zh":"當證據確認人們不確定的事情，它就提供保證。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving confidence about a particular issue.","zh":"這個短語描述就某特定問題給予信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"comforting reassurance","meaning":"令人安心的保證","examples":[{"en":"Space photographs provide comforting reassurance that the earth is round.","zh":"太空照片提供令人安心的保證，顯示地球是圓的。"},{"en":"Comforting reassurance is evidence or explanation that makes people feel calmer and more certain.","zh":"comforting reassurance 指令人更平靜、更肯定的證據或解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher’s feedback can give comforting reassurance before an important exam.","zh":"重要考試前，老師的回饋可以給學生令人安心的保證。"},{"en":"Reassurance is comforting when it removes fear or doubt.","zh":"當保證消除恐懼或疑慮，它就是令人安心的。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests emotional relief as well as factual confidence.","zh":"這個短語暗示情感上的紓緩以及事實上的信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on that point","meaning":"在這一點上","examples":[{"en":"Photographs from space provide reassurance on that point.","zh":"太空照片在這一點上提供保證。"},{"en":"On that point means about that particular issue or detail.","zh":"on that point 指關於某個特定問題或細節。"},{"en":"The school rules are clear on that point: phones must be switched off during exams.","zh":"校規在這一點上很清楚：考試期間手機必須關掉。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase to focus attention on one specific matter.","zh":"說話者使用這個短語，把注意力集中在某一具體事項上。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate one detail from the wider discussion.","zh":"這個短語幫助把一個細節從更大討論中分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"relative positions of","meaning":"……的相對位置","examples":[{"en":"A globe shows the relative positions of the continents and oceans.","zh":"地球儀顯示大洲和海洋的相對位置。"},{"en":"Relative positions of things are where they are in relation to one another.","zh":"relative positions of things 指事物彼此之間的位置關係。"},{"en":"A classroom seating plan shows the relative positions of students, doors, and the teacher’s desk.","zh":"課室座位表顯示學生、門口和老師桌子的相對位置。"},{"en":"If relative positions are wrong, people may misunderstand distance or direction.","zh":"如果相對位置錯誤，人們可能誤解距離或方向。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing locations rather than describing one place alone.","zh":"這個短語用於比較位置，而不是單獨描述一個地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"continents and oceans","meaning":"大洲和海洋","examples":[{"en":"A globe shows the relative positions of the continents and oceans.","zh":"地球儀顯示大洲和海洋的相對位置。"},{"en":"Continents and oceans are the large land masses and bodies of water that make up the earth’s surface.","zh":"continents and oceans 指構成地球表面的大片陸地和水域。"},{"en":"Children often learn the names of continents and oceans in geography lessons.","zh":"孩子常在地理課學習大洲和海洋的名稱。"},{"en":"Understanding continents and oceans helps students see how countries connect across the world.","zh":"理解大洲和海洋幫助學生看見世界各國如何相互連接。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the largest physical divisions of the planet.","zh":"這個短語指地球最大的自然分區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"go out and buy yourself","meaning":"出去給自己買","examples":[{"en":"You should go out and buy yourself a globe to understand world geography.","zh":"你應該出去給自己買一個地球儀，以理解世界地理。"},{"en":"To go out and buy yourself something means to leave and purchase something for your own use.","zh":"go out and buy yourself something 指外出購買某物供自己使用。"},{"en":"If you keep losing notes, you should go out and buy yourself a proper notebook.","zh":"如果你經常遺失筆記，你應該出去給自己買一本合適的筆記簿。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds direct and practical, as if the speaker is giving friendly advice.","zh":"這個短語聽起來直接而實際，好像說話者在給友善建議。"},{"en":"It often suggests that the item will solve a simple problem.","zh":"它常暗示該物品可以解決一個簡單問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a globe","meaning":"地球儀","examples":[{"en":"A globe gives a three-dimensional representation of the earth.","zh":"地球儀提供地球的三維呈現。"},{"en":"A globe is a round model of the earth that shows land and sea on a sphere.","zh":"globe 指顯示陸地和海洋的圓形地球模型。"},{"en":"A student may use a globe to see why routes over the poles can be shorter than they look on a flat map.","zh":"學生可能用地球儀看出，經兩極的路線為何比平面地圖上看起來更短。"},{"en":"A globe avoids some distortions because it keeps the earth’s round shape.","zh":"地球儀避免部分扭曲，因為它保留地球的圓形。"},{"en":"This word refers to the physical round model, not a flat map.","zh":"這個詞指實體圓形模型，而不是平面地圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"spin it around","meaning":"把它轉動","examples":[{"en":"You can spin a globe around to see the continents and oceans.","zh":"你可以把地球儀轉動，以看見大洲和海洋。"},{"en":"To spin it around means to turn an object quickly or smoothly so different sides can be seen.","zh":"spin it around 指快速或順暢地轉動物件，使不同面向可被看見。"},{"en":"A child may spin a chair around while playing in the classroom.","zh":"孩子可能在課室玩耍時把椅子轉動。"},{"en":"Spinning a globe around helps learners view the world from different angles.","zh":"轉動地球儀幫助學習者從不同角度觀看世界。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rotating something by hand.","zh":"這個短語描述用手旋轉某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be pinned to a wall","meaning":"被釘在牆上","examples":[{"en":"A globe cannot be pinned to a wall.","zh":"地球儀不能被釘在牆上。"},{"en":"To be pinned to a wall means to be attached flat against a wall with pins or similar tools.","zh":"be pinned to a wall 指用圖釘或類似工具把某物平貼在牆上。"},{"en":"A teacher may pin a timetable to the classroom wall so everyone can see it.","zh":"老師可能把時間表釘在課室牆上，讓所有人都看見。"},{"en":"Round objects cannot easily be pinned to a wall because they are not flat.","zh":"圓形物件不容易被釘在牆上，因為它們不是平面的。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a globe is less convenient than a paper map.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何地球儀不如紙本地圖方便。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"printed in a book","meaning":"印在書上","examples":[{"en":"A globe cannot be printed in a book.","zh":"地球儀不能印在書上。"},{"en":"Printed in a book means reproduced on a flat page as text or an image.","zh":"printed in a book 指作為文字或圖像複製在平面書頁上。"},{"en":"A school map can be printed in a book so students can study it at home.","zh":"學校地圖可以印在書上，讓學生在家學習。"},{"en":"Three-dimensional objects must be simplified before they can be printed on paper.","zh":"三維物件必須先被簡化，才可以印在紙上。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts flat printed images with physical objects.","zh":"這個短語把平面印刷圖像與實體物件作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a two-dimensional representation","meaning":"二維呈現","examples":[{"en":"A map is a two-dimensional representation of the earth.","zh":"地圖是地球的二維呈現。"},{"en":"A two-dimensional representation shows something on a flat surface with height and width but no depth.","zh":"two-dimensional representation 指在平面上以高度和闊度呈現某物，但沒有深度。"},{"en":"A floor plan is a two-dimensional representation of a classroom.","zh":"平面圖是課室的二維呈現。"},{"en":"Two-dimensional representations are convenient, but they often leave out depth or shape.","zh":"二維呈現很方便，但常省略深度或形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a flat version of something more complex.","zh":"這個短語描述較複雜事物的平面版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"this is where the problems start","meaning":"問題就是從這裏開始","examples":[{"en":"This is where the problems start with map-making.","zh":"地圖製作的問題就是從這裏開始。"},{"en":"This is where the problems start means this is the point at which difficulties begin.","zh":"this is where the problems start 指困難正是在這一點開始。"},{"en":"A student may understand vocabulary, but writing full sentences is where the problems start.","zh":"學生可能理解詞彙，但寫完整句子時，問題就是從這裏開始。"},{"en":"Problems start when a simple idea must be applied to a complicated situation.","zh":"當簡單想法必須應用到複雜情況，問題就會開始。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the first major difficulty in an explanation.","zh":"這個短語引入解釋中的第一個主要困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"project information onto","meaning":"將資料投射到……上","examples":[{"en":"You cannot project three-dimensional information onto a flat plane without distortion.","zh":"你不可能把三維資料投射到平面上而沒有扭曲。"},{"en":"To project information onto a surface means to transfer or represent it on that surface.","zh":"project information onto a surface 指把資料轉移或呈現在某表面上。"},{"en":"A teacher may project a diagram onto the board so the whole class can see it.","zh":"老師可能把圖表投射到白板上，讓全班看見。"},{"en":"When round-earth information is projected onto a flat map, some distortion must happen.","zh":"當圓形地球資料投射到平面地圖上，某種扭曲必然發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving information from one form or surface to another.","zh":"這個短語描述把資料從一種形式或表面移到另一種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"three-dimensional information","meaning":"三維資料","examples":[{"en":"Maps try to represent three-dimensional information on a flat surface.","zh":"地圖試圖在平面上呈現三維資料。"},{"en":"Three-dimensional information describes height, width, and depth in real space.","zh":"three-dimensional information 描述真實空間中的高度、闊度和深度。"},{"en":"A model of a building contains three-dimensional information that a simple photo may not show.","zh":"建築模型包含一張簡單照片未必能顯示的三維資料。"},{"en":"When three-dimensional information is flattened, some details become simplified or distorted.","zh":"當三維資料被壓成平面，一些細節會被簡化或扭曲。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to information about real shape and depth.","zh":"這個短語指關於真實形狀和深度的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a flat plane","meaning":"平面","examples":[{"en":"A map projects the earth onto a flat plane.","zh":"地圖把地球投射到平面上。"},{"en":"A flat plane is a completely flat surface.","zh":"flat plane 指完全平坦的表面。"},{"en":"A sheet of paper is a flat plane, while a ball is not.","zh":"一張紙是平面，而球不是。"},{"en":"Putting a round earth onto a flat plane forces mapmakers to change some shapes or sizes.","zh":"把圓形地球放到平面上，迫使地圖製作者改變一些形狀或大小。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when explaining geometry and map projection.","zh":"這個短語常用於解釋幾何和地圖投影。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make certain assumptions","meaning":"作出某些假設","examples":[{"en":"Cartographers must make certain assumptions when drawing world maps.","zh":"地圖繪製者畫世界地圖時，必須作出某些假設。"},{"en":"To make certain assumptions means to accept some starting ideas before making a decision or design.","zh":"make certain assumptions 指在作決定或設計前，先接受某些起始想法。"},{"en":"A teacher may make certain assumptions about students’ grammar before planning a lesson.","zh":"老師在備課前，可能對學生文法程度作出某些假設。"},{"en":"Assumptions matter because they shape what is included, ignored, or emphasised.","zh":"假設很重要，因為它們塑造甚麼被包括、忽略或強調。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that choices are being made behind the final result.","zh":"這個短語顯示最終結果背後有選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"arguments between cartographers","meaning":"地圖繪製者之間的爭論","examples":[{"en":"Arguments between cartographers concern the assumptions behind maps.","zh":"地圖繪製者之間的爭論關乎地圖背後的假設。"},{"en":"Arguments between cartographers are disagreements among mapmakers about how maps should represent the world.","zh":"arguments between cartographers 指地圖製作者之間關於地圖應如何呈現世界的分歧。"},{"en":"Two designers may have arguments about whether a school map should show distance or simplicity more clearly.","zh":"兩名設計者可能爭論學校地圖應更清楚顯示距離還是簡潔性。"},{"en":"These arguments arise because no flat map can show everything perfectly.","zh":"這些爭論出現，是因為沒有平面地圖可以完美顯示一切。"},{"en":"This phrase describes professional disagreement about mapping choices.","zh":"這個短語描述關於製圖選擇的專業分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"concern what","meaning":"關乎……","examples":[{"en":"The arguments mostly concern what assumptions should be made.","zh":"這些爭論主要關乎應作出甚麼假設。"},{"en":"To concern what something is means to be about that issue or question.","zh":"concern what something is 指關於該問題或疑問。"},{"en":"The meeting will concern what rules students should follow during exams.","zh":"會議將關乎學生考試期間應遵守甚麼規則。"},{"en":"A discussion concerns a topic when that topic is the main focus.","zh":"當某課題是主要焦點，討論就關乎該課題。"},{"en":"This phrase helps identify the subject of a debate or problem.","zh":"這個短語幫助指出辯論或問題的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what those assumptions should be","meaning":"這些假設應該是甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Cartographers disagree about what those assumptions should be.","zh":"地圖繪製者不同意這些假設應該是甚麼。"},{"en":"What those assumptions should be means which starting beliefs or priorities should guide the work.","zh":"what those assumptions should be 指哪些起始信念或優先事項應該引導工作。"},{"en":"Teachers may disagree about what their assumptions should be when planning a beginner class.","zh":"老師規劃初級班時，可能不同意假設應該是甚麼。"},{"en":"Different assumptions lead to different methods, examples, and results.","zh":"不同假設會導致不同方法、例子和結果。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on choosing the principles behind a decision.","zh":"這個短語著重選擇決定背後的原則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the simplest representation","meaning":"最簡單的呈現方式","examples":[{"en":"The simplest representation is a cylindrical projection.","zh":"最簡單的呈現方式是圓柱投影。"},{"en":"The simplest representation is the easiest way to show or model something.","zh":"simplest representation 指展示或模擬某事物的最容易方式。"},{"en":"A stick figure may be the simplest representation of a person in a quick drawing.","zh":"在快速繪圖中，火柴人可能是人的最簡單呈現方式。"},{"en":"Simple representations are useful, but they often leave out important detail.","zh":"簡單呈現方式有用，但常省略重要細節。"},{"en":"This phrase compares ways of showing information.","zh":"這個短語比較呈現資料的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cylindrical projection","meaning":"圓柱投影","examples":[{"en":"A cylindrical projection is made by wrapping paper around a globe.","zh":"圓柱投影是透過把紙包圍地球儀而製成的。"},{"en":"A cylindrical projection is a map method that imagines the globe projected onto a cylinder.","zh":"cylindrical projection 指一種想像把地球投射到圓柱上的製圖方法。"},{"en":"Students can understand cylindrical projection by wrapping paper around a ball and then flattening it.","zh":"學生可以透過把紙包着球再攤平，來理解圓柱投影。"},{"en":"This method preserves some directions but stretches areas near the poles.","zh":"這種方法保留部分方向，但會拉長兩極附近地區。"},{"en":"This phrase names one common method of turning the round earth into a flat map.","zh":"這個短語命名把圓形地球變成平面地圖的一種常見方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what you get by","meaning":"透過……所得出的東西","examples":[{"en":"A cylindrical projection is what you get by wrapping paper around a globe.","zh":"圓柱投影就是透過把紙包圍地球儀所得出的東西。"},{"en":"What you get by doing something means the result produced by that action.","zh":"what you get by doing something 指透過某行動產生的結果。"},{"en":"A summary is what you get by cutting a long article down to its main ideas.","zh":"摘要就是透過把長文章刪減成主要想法所得出的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a result through a simple process.","zh":"這個短語透過簡單過程解釋結果。"},{"en":"It helps learners connect an action with its outcome.","zh":"它幫助學習者把行動與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"wrap a sheet of paper around","meaning":"將一張紙包圍着……","examples":[{"en":"You can imagine wrapping a sheet of paper around a globe.","zh":"你可以想像將一張紙包圍着地球儀。"},{"en":"To wrap a sheet of paper around something means to cover it by bending paper around its surface.","zh":"wrap a sheet of paper around something 指把紙彎曲並覆蓋在某物表面。"},{"en":"A child may wrap a sheet of paper around a bottle to make a simple label.","zh":"孩子可能把一張紙包圍着瓶子，做成簡單標籤。"},{"en":"Wrapping flat paper around a round object shows why flattening it later creates problems.","zh":"把平面紙張包圍圓形物件，顯示之後攤平它為何會產生問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes covering an object with paper.","zh":"這個短語描述用紙包裹物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"transfer information across","meaning":"把資料轉移過去","examples":[{"en":"The information is transferred across from the globe to the paper.","zh":"資料從地球儀被轉移到紙上。"},{"en":"To transfer information across means to move details from one place, form, or system to another.","zh":"transfer information across 指把細節從一個地方、形式或系統移到另一個。"},{"en":"A teacher may transfer information across from a textbook to a worksheet.","zh":"老師可能把資料從教科書轉移到工作紙上。"},{"en":"Information can change when it is transferred across into a new format.","zh":"當資料被轉移到新格式，它可能會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving content from one medium to another.","zh":"這個短語描述把內容從一種媒介移到另一種媒介。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"indicate true north and south","meaning":"顯示真正的南北方向","examples":[{"en":"A cylindrical projection indicates true north and south.","zh":"圓柱投影顯示真正的南北方向。"},{"en":"To indicate true north and south means to show the real direction toward the poles.","zh":"indicate true north and south 指顯示通往兩極的真實方向。"},{"en":"A compass can indicate true north and south when it is used correctly.","zh":"羅盤在正確使用時可以顯示真正的南北方向。"},{"en":"Correct directions help travellers avoid going the wrong way.","zh":"正確方向幫助旅客避免走錯路。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accurate direction marking on a map.","zh":"這個短語描述地圖上準確標示方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"directly north of","meaning":"正正在……以北","examples":[{"en":"Newfoundland is directly north of Venezuela.","zh":"紐芬蘭正正在委內瑞拉以北。"},{"en":"Directly north of a place means located straight above it on a north-south line.","zh":"directly north of a place 指位於某地正北方，在同一南北線上。"},{"en":"In a classroom map, the library may be directly north of the playground.","zh":"在校園地圖中，圖書館可能正正在操場以北。"},{"en":"If one place is directly north of another, you would travel south to return to the lower place.","zh":"如果一地正正在另一地以北，你要返回較南的位置就會向南行。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a precise direction relationship.","zh":"這個短語給出精確方向關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"appear that way","meaning":"以那種方式顯示","examples":[{"en":"Newfoundland appears that way on the map.","zh":"紐芬蘭在地圖上以那種方式顯示。"},{"en":"To appear that way means to look like that from a particular viewpoint or representation.","zh":"appear that way 指從某個視角或呈現方式看起來是那樣。"},{"en":"The classroom appears larger in the photo because the camera is close to the door.","zh":"因為相機靠近門口，課室在照片中看起來更大。"},{"en":"Maps can make places appear a certain way even when reality is more complicated.","zh":"地圖可以令地方以某種方式顯示，即使現實更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how something seems, not necessarily what it fully is.","zh":"這個短語描述某事看起來如何，而不一定是其完整真相。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"likewise","meaning":"同樣地","examples":[{"en":"East and west are likewise indicated correctly.","zh":"東西方向同樣地被正確顯示。"},{"en":"Likewise means in the same way or similarly.","zh":"likewise 指以同樣方式或相似地。"},{"en":"The first student submitted the homework on time; the second did likewise.","zh":"第一名學生準時交功課；第二名學生同樣地做了。"},{"en":"Writers use likewise to show that a second point follows the same pattern as the first.","zh":"作者使用 likewise 來顯示第二點跟第一點遵循同一模式。"},{"en":"This word connects two similar ideas or actions.","zh":"這個詞連接兩個相似想法或行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be indicated correctly","meaning":"被正確顯示","examples":[{"en":"East and west are indicated correctly on the map.","zh":"東西方向在地圖上被正確顯示。"},{"en":"To be indicated correctly means to be shown accurately.","zh":"be indicated correctly 指被準確顯示。"},{"en":"Emergency exits must be indicated correctly on a school floor plan.","zh":"學校平面圖上必須正確顯示緊急出口。"},{"en":"If directions are not indicated correctly, people may take the wrong route.","zh":"如果方向沒有被正確顯示，人們可能走錯路。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accurate marking or display.","zh":"這個短語描述準確標示或展示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fidelity of axis","meaning":"軸向保真度","examples":[{"en":"A map with fidelity of axis shows true north, south, east and west.","zh":"有軸向保真度的地圖顯示真正的東南西北。"},{"en":"Fidelity of axis means a map keeps the main directional axes accurate.","zh":"fidelity of axis 指地圖保持主要方向軸準確。"},{"en":"A subway map may sacrifice distance but keep enough directional accuracy to guide passengers.","zh":"地鐵圖可能犧牲距離，但保持足夠方向準確度來引導乘客。"},{"en":"Fidelity of axis helps users judge basic directions more easily.","zh":"軸向保真度幫助使用者更容易判斷基本方向。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to preserving north-south and east-west alignment.","zh":"這個短語指保留南北和東西方向排列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"longest-lived","meaning":"存在時間最長的","examples":[{"en":"The Mercator projection is one of the longest-lived cylindrical projections.","zh":"麥卡托投影是存在時間最長的圓柱投影之一。"},{"en":"Longest-lived means having lasted for a very long time compared with similar things.","zh":"longest-lived 指與同類事物相比持續了很長時間。"},{"en":"A family restaurant may be one of the longest-lived businesses in the neighbourhood.","zh":"一間家庭餐廳可能是社區中存在時間最長的商店之一。"},{"en":"Something longest-lived survives because people keep finding it useful or familiar.","zh":"存在時間很長的事物得以延續，是因為人們仍覺得它有用或熟悉。"},{"en":"This word describes durability over time.","zh":"這個詞描述隨時間延續的耐久性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be based on the needs of","meaning":"基於……的需要","examples":[{"en":"The projection was based on the needs of sixteenth-century navigators.","zh":"這種投影基於十六世紀航海家的需要。"},{"en":"To be based on the needs of a group means to be designed according to what that group requires.","zh":"be based on the needs of a group 指根據該群體所需而設計。"},{"en":"A school timetable should be based on the needs of students, teachers, and families.","zh":"學校時間表應基於學生、老師和家庭的需要。"},{"en":"Designs based on one group’s needs may not work equally well for everyone else.","zh":"基於某一群體需要而設計的東西，未必同樣適合所有其他人。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose behind a design.","zh":"這個短語解釋設計背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sixteenth-century navigators","meaning":"十六世紀航海家","examples":[{"en":"Sixteenth-century navigators needed maps for sea travel.","zh":"十六世紀航海家需要海上旅行用的地圖。"},{"en":"Sixteenth-century navigators were sailors or explorers in the 1500s who used maps and instruments to travel by sea.","zh":"sixteenth-century navigators 指 1500 年代使用地圖和儀器航海的水手或探險家。"},{"en":"Sixteenth-century navigators needed reliable compass directions because they crossed unfamiliar oceans.","zh":"十六世紀航海家需要可靠羅盤方向，因為他們橫越陌生海洋。"},{"en":"Their needs shaped maps that were useful for navigation but distorted land size.","zh":"他們的需要塑造了有利導航但扭曲陸地大小的地圖。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to early modern sea travellers.","zh":"這個短語指近代早期的海上旅行者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Flemish mathematician","meaning":"佛蘭芒數學家","examples":[{"en":"Gerhard Kremer was a Flemish mathematician.","zh":"Gerhard Kremer 是一名佛蘭芒數學家。"},{"en":"A Flemish mathematician is a mathematics expert from Flanders, a historical region in Europe.","zh":"Flemish mathematician 指來自歐洲歷史地區佛蘭德斯的數學專家。"},{"en":"A Flemish mathematician might use geometry to solve problems in mapping and navigation.","zh":"佛蘭芒數學家可能用幾何學解決製圖和航海問題。"},{"en":"Mathematical knowledge helped early mapmakers design projections for practical use.","zh":"數學知識幫助早期地圖製作者設計實用投影。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both a person’s regional background and academic field.","zh":"這個短語同時指出人物的地域背景和學術領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"produce one’s view of the world","meaning":"製作某人的世界觀","examples":[{"en":"Gerhard Kremer produced his view of the world in 1569.","zh":"Gerhard Kremer 在 1569 年製作了他的世界觀。"},{"en":"To produce one’s view of the world means to create a representation shaped by one’s choices and understanding.","zh":"produce one’s view of the world 指創造一種受自身選擇和理解塑造的世界呈現。"},{"en":"An artist may produce her view of the city by painting busy streets rather than quiet homes.","zh":"藝術家可能透過畫繁忙街道而不是安靜住宅，製作她對城市的看法。"},{"en":"A mapmaker’s view of the world affects what is central, large, or useful.","zh":"地圖製作者的世界觀會影響甚麼是中心、巨大或有用。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that a map is a constructed interpretation.","zh":"這個短語暗示地圖是一種被建構出來的詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"translate to","meaning":"翻譯為","examples":[{"en":"Kremer translates to merchant in English.","zh":"Kremer 在英文中翻譯為 merchant。"},{"en":"To translate to a word means to have that meaning in another language.","zh":"translate to a word 指在另一種語言中有該意思。"},{"en":"The French word “maison” translates to “house” in English.","zh":"法文 “maison” 在英文中翻譯為 “house”。"},{"en":"Translation helps readers understand names, terms, and cultural references.","zh":"翻譯幫助讀者理解名字、術語和文化參照。"},{"en":"This phrase connects words across languages.","zh":"這個短語把不同語言的詞語連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"survive to this day","meaning":"流傳至今","examples":[{"en":"The Mercator projection survives to this day in many books and maps.","zh":"麥卡托投影在許多書本和地圖中流傳至今。"},{"en":"To survive to this day means to continue existing until the present time.","zh":"survive to this day 指一直存在直到現在。"},{"en":"Some old street names survive to this day even though the neighbourhood has changed.","zh":"有些舊街名即使社區已改變，仍流傳至今。"},{"en":"A design survives when people keep using it despite newer alternatives.","zh":"當人們在有更新選擇下仍繼續使用某設計，它就得以流傳。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long continuation from the past to now.","zh":"這個短語強調從過去延續到現在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Mercator projection","meaning":"麥卡托投影","examples":[{"en":"The Mercator projection was useful for early navigators.","zh":"麥卡托投影對早期航海家很有用。"},{"en":"The Mercator projection is a world map projection that preserves direction but greatly enlarges areas near the poles.","zh":"Mercator projection 指一種保留方向但大幅放大兩極附近地區的世界地圖投影。"},{"en":"Students may recognise the Mercator projection because it appears in many classrooms and atlases.","zh":"學生可能認得麥卡托投影，因為它出現在許多課室和地圖集。"},{"en":"It helped sailors plot routes, but it made Greenland and Europe look unusually large.","zh":"它幫助水手規劃航線，但令格陵蘭和歐洲看起來異常巨大。"},{"en":"This phrase names a famous map projection with both practical strengths and serious distortions.","zh":"這個短語命名一種著名地圖投影，既有實用優點，也有嚴重扭曲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"intermediate compass directions","meaning":"中間羅盤方向","examples":[{"en":"The Mercator projection shows intermediate compass directions fairly accurately.","zh":"麥卡托投影相當準確地顯示中間羅盤方向。"},{"en":"Intermediate compass directions are directions between the main points, such as north-east and south-west.","zh":"intermediate compass directions 指主要方向之間的方向，例如東北和西南。"},{"en":"A hiker may use intermediate compass directions to walk north-west toward a mountain path.","zh":"遠足者可能使用中間羅盤方向，向西北走到山徑。"},{"en":"Showing these directions accurately helps travellers choose a route.","zh":"準確顯示這些方向幫助旅客選擇路線。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to directions between north, south, east, and west.","zh":"這個短語指東南西北之間的方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"north-west","meaning":"西北","examples":[{"en":"North-west is an intermediate compass direction.","zh":"西北是一個中間羅盤方向。"},{"en":"North-west means the direction halfway between north and west.","zh":"north-west 指介乎北方和西方之間的方向。"},{"en":"If the library is north-west of the classroom, students must walk partly north and partly west to reach it.","zh":"如果圖書館在課室西北方，學生要向北和向西之間的方向走。"},{"en":"Knowing north-west helps people describe routes more precisely than saying “over there.”","zh":"知道西北方有助人比說「那邊」更精確地描述路線。"},{"en":"This word names one of the four diagonal compass directions.","zh":"這個詞命名四個斜向羅盤方向之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"more or less accurately","meaning":"大致準確地","examples":[{"en":"The map shows compass directions more or less accurately.","zh":"這張地圖大致準確地顯示羅盤方向。"},{"en":"More or less accurately means mostly correctly, though not perfectly.","zh":"more or less accurately 指大部分正確，但並不完美。"},{"en":"A student may remember a story more or less accurately but forget a few names.","zh":"學生可能大致準確地記得故事，但忘記幾個名字。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is close enough for practical use but not exact.","zh":"當某事接近得足以實際使用，但並不精確時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It gives a cautious judgement of accuracy.","zh":"它給出對準確度的謹慎判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"conclude from","meaning":"從……推斷","examples":[{"en":"You can conclude from the map that Brazil is south-west of Liberia.","zh":"你可以從地圖推斷巴西位於利比里亞西南方。"},{"en":"To conclude from something means to reach an idea or judgement based on evidence.","zh":"conclude from something 指根據證據得出想法或判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher may conclude from repeated errors that students need more grammar practice.","zh":"老師可能從反覆錯誤推斷學生需要更多文法練習。"},{"en":"Conclusions are stronger when the evidence clearly supports them.","zh":"當證據清楚支持結論，推斷會更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase links evidence with a final judgement.","zh":"這個短語把證據與最終判斷連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"plot a course","meaning":"規劃航線","examples":[{"en":"A navigator could plot a course using the Mercator projection.","zh":"航海家可以使用麥卡托投影規劃航線。"},{"en":"To plot a course means to plan the route that a ship, plane, or traveller will follow.","zh":"plot a course 指規劃船隻、飛機或旅客將跟隨的路線。"},{"en":"A sailor plots a course before leaving harbour to avoid dangerous waters.","zh":"水手離港前會規劃航線，以避開危險水域。"},{"en":"Accurate directions help people plot a course safely.","zh":"準確方向幫助人安全規劃航線。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planning a route carefully.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細規劃路線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in that direction","meaning":"朝那個方向","examples":[{"en":"If you travel in that direction, you will eventually arrive.","zh":"如果你朝那個方向行進，最終會到達。"},{"en":"In that direction means toward the place or compass point already mentioned.","zh":"in that direction 指朝向已提及的地點或羅盤方向。"},{"en":"If the station is east of the school, students should walk in that direction after the lesson.","zh":"如果車站在學校東面，學生下課後應朝那個方向走。"},{"en":"Following the right direction matters because a small error can grow over distance.","zh":"跟隨正確方向很重要，因為小錯誤會隨距離變大。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a direction already identified.","zh":"這個短語指回已被指出的方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"eventually arrive at","meaning":"最終到達","examples":[{"en":"If you plot the course correctly, you will eventually arrive at your destination.","zh":"如果你正確規劃航線，你最終會到達目的地。"},{"en":"To eventually arrive at a place means to reach it after some time or effort.","zh":"eventually arrive at a place 指經過一段時間或努力後到達某地。"},{"en":"A student who follows the signs will eventually arrive at the exam hall.","zh":"按照指示牌走的學生最終會到達考試禮堂。"},{"en":"Careful planning increases the chance that travellers arrive where they intended.","zh":"仔細規劃會增加旅客到達原定地點的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching a final place after a journey.","zh":"這個短語描述旅程後到達最終地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"arrive at your destination","meaning":"到達目的地","examples":[{"en":"Navigators used the map to arrive at their destination.","zh":"航海家使用地圖到達目的地。"},{"en":"To arrive at your destination means to reach the place you planned to go.","zh":"arrive at your destination 指到達你計劃前往的地方。"},{"en":"If the bus route is correct, passengers will arrive at their destination without changing buses.","zh":"如果巴士路線正確，乘客不用轉車也會到達目的地。"},{"en":"Good maps help people arrive at their destination safely and efficiently.","zh":"好地圖幫助人安全而有效率地到達目的地。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the successful end of a journey.","zh":"這個短語著重旅程的成功終點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"no wonder","meaning":"難怪","examples":[{"en":"No wonder the Mercator projection was appreciated by early explorers.","zh":"難怪麥卡托投影受到早期探險家欣賞。"},{"en":"No wonder means it is not surprising because there is a clear reason.","zh":"no wonder 指因為有清楚原因，所以並不令人驚訝。"},{"en":"No wonder the student improved; she practised writing every day for three months.","zh":"難怪學生進步；她連續三個月每天練習寫作。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when the previous explanation makes the result expected.","zh":"當早前解釋令結果變得可預期，作者會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase connects cause with understandable reaction.","zh":"這個短語把原因與可理解反應連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be appreciated by","meaning":"受到……欣賞","examples":[{"en":"The Mercator projection was appreciated by early explorers.","zh":"麥卡托投影受到早期探險家欣賞。"},{"en":"To be appreciated by someone means to be valued or recognised as useful by them.","zh":"be appreciated by someone 指被某人重視或認為有用。"},{"en":"A clear revision checklist is appreciated by students before an exam.","zh":"考試前，清晰的溫習清單會受到學生欣賞。"},{"en":"Something is appreciated when it solves a real problem for its users.","zh":"當某物解決使用者的真實問題，它就會受到欣賞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving positive recognition.","zh":"這個短語描述得到正面認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"early explorers","meaning":"早期探險家","examples":[{"en":"Early explorers valued maps that showed compass directions accurately.","zh":"早期探險家重視能準確顯示羅盤方向的地圖。"},{"en":"Early explorers were travellers who went into unfamiliar regions before they were well known to others.","zh":"early explorers 指在某些地區尚未廣為人知前前往陌生地區的旅客。"},{"en":"Early explorers needed maps, supplies, and courage to cross unknown seas.","zh":"早期探險家需要地圖、補給和勇氣去橫越未知海洋。"},{"en":"Their journeys helped expand geographical knowledge but often involved danger and conflict.","zh":"他們的旅程幫助擴展地理知識，但常涉及危險和衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people who explored before modern transport and mapping.","zh":"這個短語指在現代交通和製圖出現前探索的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be said to have","meaning":"被稱為具有","examples":[{"en":"A map is said to have fidelity of angle if it preserves directions.","zh":"如果地圖保留方向，它被稱為具有角度保真度。"},{"en":"Be said to have means people describe something as possessing a particular quality.","zh":"be said to have 指人們描述某物擁有某種特質。"},{"en":"A student is said to have strong listening skills if she understands fast speech easily.","zh":"如果學生能輕易理解快速說話，她會被稱為具有強聆聽能力。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in formal explanations and definitions.","zh":"這個短語常用於正式解釋和定義。"},{"en":"It allows the writer to introduce a technical description.","zh":"它讓作者引入技術性描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fidelity of angle","meaning":"角度保真度","examples":[{"en":"The Mercator projection has fidelity of angle.","zh":"麥卡托投影具有角度保真度。"},{"en":"Fidelity of angle means a map preserves compass directions or angular relationships accurately.","zh":"fidelity of angle 指地圖準確保留羅盤方向或角度關係。"},{"en":"Sailors valued fidelity of angle because it helped them follow a steady course.","zh":"水手重視角度保真度，因為它幫助他們沿穩定航線前進。"},{"en":"Keeping angle accurate can require sacrificing correct size or shape.","zh":"保持角度準確可能需要犧牲正確大小或形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to one kind of accuracy in map projection.","zh":"這個短語指地圖投影中的一種準確性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be achieved at a cost","meaning":"以付出代價換來","examples":[{"en":"Fidelity of angle is only achieved at a cost.","zh":"角度保真度只能以付出代價換來。"},{"en":"To be achieved at a cost means to be gained only by giving up something else.","zh":"be achieved at a cost 指只有透過放棄其他東西才能取得某成果。"},{"en":"A student may achieve perfect neatness at the cost of writing too slowly.","zh":"學生可能以寫得太慢為代價，換來字體非常整齊。"},{"en":"In map-making, one kind of accuracy may be achieved at the cost of another kind.","zh":"在地圖製作中，一種準確性可能以犧牲另一種準確性換來。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a trade-off.","zh":"這個短語突出取捨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make it work","meaning":"令它可行","examples":[{"en":"To make the projection work, the lines of latitude must be moved apart.","zh":"為了令這種投影可行，緯線必須被拉開。"},{"en":"To make it work means to make a plan, system, or design function properly.","zh":"make it work 指令計劃、系統或設計正常運作。"},{"en":"To make a group project work, each student needs a clear role.","zh":"為了令小組項目可行，每名學生都需要清楚角色。"},{"en":"Sometimes making one part work creates problems in another part.","zh":"有時令一部分可行，會在另一部分造成問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical functioning.","zh":"這個短語著重實際運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the further away you get from","meaning":"你離……越遠","examples":[{"en":"The further away you get from the equator, the more distorted the map becomes.","zh":"你離赤道越遠，地圖就變得越扭曲。"},{"en":"The further away you get from something means as the distance from it increases.","zh":"the further away you get from something 指隨着離某物的距離增加。"},{"en":"The further away you get from school, the longer the bus journey becomes.","zh":"你離學校越遠，巴士車程就越長。"},{"en":"This structure often shows one change increasing together with another.","zh":"這個結構常顯示一種變化隨另一種變化一起增加。"},{"en":"It helps explain a relationship between distance and result.","zh":"它幫助解釋距離與結果之間的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the equator","meaning":"赤道","examples":[{"en":"The equator appears lower than expected on the traditional Mercator map.","zh":"赤道在傳統麥卡托地圖上看起來比預期更低。"},{"en":"The equator is the imaginary line around the middle of the earth, halfway between the poles.","zh":"equator 指環繞地球中部、位於兩極正中間的想像線。"},{"en":"Countries near the equator often have warm climates because they receive strong sunlight.","zh":"赤道附近的國家通常氣候溫暖，因為它們接收強烈陽光。"},{"en":"On a world map, the position of the equator affects how we judge north and south.","zh":"在世界地圖上，赤道的位置影響我們如何判斷南北。"},{"en":"This word names a central reference line in geography.","zh":"這個詞命名地理中的中央參照線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"horizontal lines of latitude","meaning":"橫向緯線","examples":[{"en":"The horizontal lines of latitude must be moved further apart.","zh":"橫向緯線必須被移得更開。"},{"en":"Horizontal lines of latitude are east-west lines on a map that show distance north or south of the equator.","zh":"horizontal lines of latitude 指地圖上東西向、顯示距赤道南北距離的線。"},{"en":"Students can use horizontal lines of latitude to compare whether two cities are at similar north-south positions.","zh":"學生可以用橫向緯線比較兩個城市是否位於相似南北位置。"},{"en":"Moving these lines changes how large some regions appear.","zh":"移動這些線會改變某些地區看起來的大小。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to one part of the map grid.","zh":"這個短語指地圖網格的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lines of latitude","meaning":"緯線","examples":[{"en":"Lines of latitude show positions north and south of the equator.","zh":"緯線顯示赤道以北和以南的位置。"},{"en":"Lines of latitude are imaginary horizontal lines used to measure location on the earth.","zh":"lines of latitude 指用來量度地球位置的想像橫線。"},{"en":"A city at 50 degrees north lies on a line of latitude north of the equator.","zh":"位於北緯 50 度的城市，位於赤道以北的一條緯線上。"},{"en":"Latitude helps people compare climate, sunlight, and position.","zh":"緯度幫助人比較氣候、陽光和位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to reading world maps.","zh":"這個短語是閱讀世界地圖的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"further apart","meaning":"相隔更遠","examples":[{"en":"The lines of latitude are placed further apart near the poles.","zh":"緯線在兩極附近被放得相隔更遠。"},{"en":"Further apart means with more distance between things.","zh":"further apart 指事物之間距離更大。"},{"en":"Desks are placed further apart during exams to prevent cheating.","zh":"考試期間，書桌會被放得相隔更遠，以防作弊。"},{"en":"When lines are placed further apart, spaces on the map can look larger.","zh":"當線條被放得相隔更遠，地圖上的空間會看起來更大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increased separation.","zh":"這個短語描述分隔增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as these distances increase","meaning":"隨着這些距離增加","examples":[{"en":"As these distances increase, the apparent sizes of countries increase too.","zh":"隨着這些距離增加，國家看起來的大小也增加。"},{"en":"As these distances increase means while the spaces between things become larger.","zh":"as these distances increase 指當事物之間的空間變得更大時。"},{"en":"As the distance between bus stops increases, passengers may need to walk farther.","zh":"隨着巴士站之間距離增加，乘客可能需要走更遠。"},{"en":"In map projection, increasing line spacing can make land areas appear larger.","zh":"在地圖投影中，線距增加可以令陸地面積看起來更大。"},{"en":"This phrase links a gradual change with its result.","zh":"這個短語把漸進變化與其結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sizes of countries","meaning":"國家的大小","examples":[{"en":"The sizes of countries are distorted on the Mercator projection.","zh":"國家的大小在麥卡托投影上被扭曲。"},{"en":"Sizes of countries means how large countries are in land area.","zh":"sizes of countries 指國家在土地面積上有多大。"},{"en":"Students may compare the sizes of countries by looking at their actual square kilometres.","zh":"學生可以透過查看實際平方公里，比較國家的大小。"},{"en":"A map can mislead people if the sizes of countries appear larger or smaller than reality.","zh":"如果國家的大小看起來比現實更大或更小，地圖可以誤導人。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on area, not population or power.","zh":"這個短語著重面積，而不是人口或權力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"underneath them","meaning":"在其下方","examples":[{"en":"The countries underneath the lines appear larger.","zh":"在這些線下方的國家看起來更大。"},{"en":"Underneath them means below those things in position or on a diagram.","zh":"underneath them 指在那些事物的位置或圖表下方。"},{"en":"In a chart, the notes underneath the table explain where the data came from.","zh":"在圖表中，表格下方的註解解釋數據來自哪裡。"},{"en":"On a map, objects underneath certain lines may be affected by how the grid is drawn.","zh":"在地圖上，位於某些線下方的物件可能受網格畫法影響。"},{"en":"This phrase points to something located below another thing.","zh":"這個短語指出位於另一事物下方的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"by the time","meaning":"到……的時候","examples":[{"en":"By the time you get to the poles, the distortion is extreme.","zh":"到你到達兩極的時候，扭曲已經極端。"},{"en":"By the time means when a particular point or stage is reached.","zh":"by the time 指當某個時刻或階段到達時。"},{"en":"By the time students reach Form 6, they should know how to plan essays quickly.","zh":"到學生升上中六的時候，他們應知道如何快速規劃作文。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows that a situation has changed greatly by a later stage.","zh":"這個短語常顯示情況到後期已發生很大變化。"},{"en":"It connects progress through time or space with a result.","zh":"它把時間或空間上的推進與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the North and South Poles","meaning":"南北兩極","examples":[{"en":"The North and South Poles cannot be represented properly on the map.","zh":"南北兩極不能在地圖上被妥善呈現。"},{"en":"The North and South Poles are the two ends of the earth’s axis, in the Arctic and Antarctic regions.","zh":"North and South Poles 指地球軸線的兩端，分別位於北極和南極地區。"},{"en":"Students learn about the North and South Poles when studying climate and polar ice.","zh":"學生學習氣候和極地冰時，會學到南北兩極。"},{"en":"Map projections often distort the poles because they are hard to place on a flat surface.","zh":"地圖投影常扭曲兩極，因為它們難以放到平面上。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the earth’s two polar points.","zh":"這個短語指地球的兩個極點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"infinitely far apart","meaning":"無限遠地分開","examples":[{"en":"The lines would be drawn infinitely far apart near the poles.","zh":"這些線在兩極附近會被畫成無限遠地分開。"},{"en":"Infinitely far apart means separated by an unlimited or impossible distance in theory.","zh":"infinitely far apart 指在理論上相隔無限或不可能的距離。"},{"en":"In mathematics, two lines may be treated as infinitely far apart in a model.","zh":"在數學模型中，兩條線可能被視為無限遠地分開。"},{"en":"If map lines become infinitely far apart, the map can no longer show the area normally.","zh":"如果地圖線條變成無限遠地分開，地圖就不能正常顯示該區域。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an extreme theoretical separation.","zh":"這個短語描述極端的理論分隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Arctic and Antarctic regions","meaning":"北極和南極地區","examples":[{"en":"The Arctic and Antarctic regions can scarcely be represented.","zh":"北極和南極地區幾乎無法被呈現。"},{"en":"Arctic and Antarctic regions are the polar areas around the North Pole and South Pole.","zh":"Arctic and Antarctic regions 指北極和南極周圍的極地區域。"},{"en":"Scientists study Arctic and Antarctic regions to understand ice, climate, and sea levels.","zh":"科學家研究北極和南極地區，以理解冰、氣候和海平面。"},{"en":"These regions are difficult to show accurately on some flat maps.","zh":"在某些平面地圖上，這些地區難以準確顯示。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the earth’s far northern and far southern polar areas.","zh":"這個短語指地球最北和最南的極地地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"can scarcely be represented","meaning":"幾乎無法被呈現","examples":[{"en":"The polar regions can scarcely be represented on the Mercator projection.","zh":"極地地區在麥卡托投影上幾乎無法被呈現。"},{"en":"Can scarcely be represented means can hardly be shown properly.","zh":"can scarcely be represented 指幾乎不能被妥善顯示。"},{"en":"A complex family history can scarcely be represented in one simple chart.","zh":"複雜家族歷史幾乎無法用一張簡單圖表呈現。"},{"en":"Some information is lost when a difficult reality is squeezed into a limited format.","zh":"當困難現實被擠進有限格式，一些資料就會流失。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that representation is almost impossible or very poor.","zh":"這個短語顯示呈現幾乎不可能或非常差。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"infinitely large","meaning":"無限大","examples":[{"en":"The polar regions would become infinitely large on the projection.","zh":"極地地區在投影上會變得無限大。"},{"en":"Infinitely large means having no limit in size in a mathematical or theoretical sense.","zh":"infinitely large 指在數學或理論意義上大小沒有界限。"},{"en":"A number line can continue in both directions and seem infinitely large.","zh":"數線可以向兩邊延伸，似乎無限大。"},{"en":"If a map makes an area infinitely large, the projection has broken down at that point.","zh":"如果地圖令某區域變得無限大，投影在該點已經失效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an extreme result that cannot work in ordinary reality.","zh":"這個短語描述在普通現實中不可行的極端結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"more importantly","meaning":"更重要的是","examples":[{"en":"More importantly, the relative sizes of intermediate areas are distorted.","zh":"更重要的是，中間地區的相對大小被扭曲。"},{"en":"More importantly means the next point matters more than the previous one.","zh":"more importantly 指下一點比前一點更重要。"},{"en":"The room is small; more importantly, it has no emergency exit.","zh":"這個房間很小；更重要的是，它沒有緊急出口。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to guide readers toward the most serious issue.","zh":"作者使用這個短語，引導讀者注意最嚴重問題。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a stronger reason or more important problem.","zh":"這個短語表示更強理由或更重要問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"relative sizes of","meaning":"……的相對大小","examples":[{"en":"The relative sizes of countries are distorted.","zh":"國家的相對大小被扭曲。"},{"en":"Relative sizes of things are their sizes when compared with one another.","zh":"relative sizes of things 指事物互相比較時的大小。"},{"en":"A chart can show the relative sizes of different school budgets.","zh":"圖表可以顯示不同學校預算的相對大小。"},{"en":"If relative sizes are wrong, readers may misunderstand which item is larger or smaller.","zh":"如果相對大小錯誤，讀者可能誤解哪個項目較大或較小。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on comparison, not absolute measurement alone.","zh":"這個短語著重比較，而不只是絕對量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"intermediate areas","meaning":"中間地區","examples":[{"en":"Intermediate areas are also distorted by the projection.","zh":"中間地區也受到這種投影扭曲。"},{"en":"Intermediate areas are regions between the equator and the poles.","zh":"intermediate areas 指赤道與兩極之間的地區。"},{"en":"Countries in intermediate areas may not look as extremely distorted as polar regions, but they can still be misleading.","zh":"位於中間地區的國家，可能不像極地那樣極端扭曲，但仍可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"Distortion in intermediate areas affects how viewers compare continents.","zh":"中間地區的扭曲影響觀眾如何比較大洲。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to middle-latitude regions on a world map.","zh":"這個短語指世界地圖上的中緯度地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be completely distorted","meaning":"被完全扭曲","examples":[{"en":"The relative sizes of some countries are completely distorted.","zh":"有些國家的相對大小被完全扭曲。"},{"en":"To be completely distorted means to be changed so much that the original form or proportion is no longer clear.","zh":"be completely distorted 指被改變得非常厲害，以致原本形態或比例不再清楚。"},{"en":"A photo can be completely distorted if it is stretched too wide on a screen.","zh":"如果照片在螢幕上被拉得太闊，就可能被完全扭曲。"},{"en":"Complete distortion can lead viewers to form false impressions.","zh":"完全扭曲可以令觀眾形成錯誤印象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severe inaccuracy in appearance or proportion.","zh":"這個短語描述外觀或比例上的嚴重不準確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"whereas in fact","meaning":"然而事實上","examples":[{"en":"South America seems smaller than Europe, whereas in fact it is larger.","zh":"南美洲看起來比歐洲小，然而事實上它更大。"},{"en":"Whereas in fact means but the truth is actually different from what was just stated or implied.","zh":"whereas in fact 指但真相其實與剛才所說或暗示的不同。"},{"en":"The shop looks expensive, whereas in fact its lunch sets are cheaper than nearby cafés.","zh":"這間店看起來很貴，然而事實上它的午餐套餐比附近咖啡店便宜。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts appearance with reality.","zh":"這個短語把表象與現實作對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when correcting a misleading impression.","zh":"它在更正誤導印象時很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"twice the size","meaning":"兩倍大","examples":[{"en":"South America is in fact twice the size of Europe.","zh":"南美洲事實上是歐洲的兩倍大。"},{"en":"Twice the size means two times as large.","zh":"twice the size 指大小是兩倍。"},{"en":"The new classroom is twice the size of the old one, so it can hold more students.","zh":"新課室是舊課室的兩倍大，因此可以容納更多學生。"},{"en":"Saying something is twice the size helps readers understand scale quickly.","zh":"說某物是兩倍大，幫助讀者快速理解規模。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two areas, objects, or quantities.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個面積、物件或數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"changes in scale","meaning":"比例上的變化","examples":[{"en":"Changes in scale distort the size and shape of countries.","zh":"比例上的變化扭曲國家的大小和形狀。"},{"en":"Changes in scale are changes in the relationship between real size and represented size.","zh":"changes in scale 指真實大小與呈現大小之間關係的變化。"},{"en":"A model car uses changes in scale so it can fit on a desk.","zh":"模型車使用比例上的變化，才能放在桌上。"},{"en":"If scale changes unevenly, some parts may look larger or smaller than they should.","zh":"如果比例變化不均，有些部分可能看起來比應有更大或更小。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how representation can alter perceived size.","zh":"這個短語解釋呈現方式如何改變感知大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"distort both the size and shape of","meaning":"同時扭曲……的大小和形狀","examples":[{"en":"These changes distort both the size and shape of countries.","zh":"這些變化同時扭曲國家的大小和形狀。"},{"en":"To distort both the size and shape of something means to make it look wrong in area and outline.","zh":"distort both the size and shape of something 指令某物在面積和輪廓上看起來都錯誤。"},{"en":"A badly resized photo can distort both the size and shape of a person’s face.","zh":"調整不當的照片可以同時扭曲人的臉部大小和形狀。"},{"en":"When both size and shape are distorted, viewers may misunderstand the object completely.","zh":"當大小和形狀都被扭曲，觀眾可能完全誤解該物件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two kinds of visual inaccuracy at the same time.","zh":"這個短語同時描述兩種視覺不準確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"given such defects","meaning":"鑑於這些缺點","examples":[{"en":"Given such defects, the survival of the Mercator projection is surprising.","zh":"鑑於這些缺點，麥卡托投影能流傳至今令人驚訝。"},{"en":"Given such defects means considering these problems or weaknesses.","zh":"given such defects 指考慮到這些問題或弱點。"},{"en":"Given such defects, the school should not continue using the broken registration system.","zh":"鑑於這些缺點，學校不應繼續使用故障的登記系統。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a judgement based on known disadvantages.","zh":"這個短語根據已知缺點引入判斷。"},{"en":"It helps explain why a later fact seems unexpected.","zh":"它幫助解釋為何後來的事實顯得出乎意料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"such defects","meaning":"這些缺點","examples":[{"en":"The Mercator projection has such defects but remains widely used.","zh":"麥卡托投影有這些缺點，但仍被廣泛使用。"},{"en":"Such defects means problems of the kind already mentioned.","zh":"such defects 指前面已提到的那類問題。"},{"en":"A phone with such defects should be repaired before students use it for online lessons.","zh":"有這些缺點的手機應在學生用於網課前維修。"},{"en":"Serious defects may not stop people using something if it is familiar or convenient.","zh":"如果某物熟悉或方便，嚴重缺點未必阻止人們使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to previously discussed weaknesses.","zh":"這個短語指回前文討論過的弱點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"survive so long","meaning":"存在這麼久","examples":[{"en":"It is surprising that the Mercator projection has survived so long.","zh":"麥卡托投影存在這麼久令人驚訝。"},{"en":"To survive so long means to continue existing or being used for an unusually long time.","zh":"survive so long 指持續存在或被使用異常長的時間。"},{"en":"It is surprising that an old shop has survived so long despite rising rent.","zh":"儘管租金上升，老店存在這麼久令人驚訝。"},{"en":"Something survives for a long time when people continue to trust, need, or recognise it.","zh":"當人們繼續信任、需要或認得某物，它就能長久存在。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses unexpected durability.","zh":"這個短語強調出乎意料的持久性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dozens of","meaning":"數十個","examples":[{"en":"Dozens of more satisfactory projections have appeared since Mercator.","zh":"自麥卡托之後，數十個較令人滿意的投影已經出現。"},{"en":"Dozens of means many, usually several groups of twelve or a large number.","zh":"dozens of 指許多，通常是幾組十二個或大量。"},{"en":"Dozens of students stayed after class to ask questions before the exam.","zh":"考試前，數十名學生課後留下來提問。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests there are far more examples than just one or two.","zh":"這個短語暗示例子遠不止一兩個。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing a large but not exact number.","zh":"它適合描述很大但不精確的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"more satisfactory projections","meaning":"較令人滿意的投影","examples":[{"en":"More satisfactory projections have appeared since Mercator.","zh":"自麥卡托之後，較令人滿意的投影已經出現。"},{"en":"More satisfactory projections are map methods that solve some problems better than earlier ones.","zh":"more satisfactory projections 指比早期方法更好解決某些問題的地圖方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may choose a more satisfactory diagram if the old one confuses students.","zh":"如果舊圖令學生混淆，老師可能選擇較令人滿意的圖表。"},{"en":"A projection becomes more satisfactory when it fits the user’s purpose more closely.","zh":"當投影更貼合使用者目的，它就變得較令人滿意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improved alternatives, not perfect solutions.","zh":"這個短語描述改善了的替代方案，而不是完美解決方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"one of the best known","meaning":"最著名的……之一","examples":[{"en":"The Aitoff projection is one of the best known alternatives.","zh":"艾托夫投影是最著名的替代方案之一。"},{"en":"One of the best known means among the most widely recognised examples.","zh":"one of the best known 指屬於最廣為人知的例子之一。"},{"en":"The local museum is one of the best known buildings in the town.","zh":"本地博物館是鎮上最著名的建築之一。"},{"en":"Something becomes well known when it is used, discussed, or taught often.","zh":"當某物經常被使用、討論或教授，它就會變得著名。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights familiarity rather than proving superiority.","zh":"這個短語突出熟悉程度，而不是證明優越性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Aitoff projection","meaning":"艾托夫投影","examples":[{"en":"The Aitoff projection attempted to represent country sizes and shapes more correctly.","zh":"艾托夫投影嘗試更正確地呈現國家的大小和形狀。"},{"en":"The Aitoff projection is a world map projection designed to reduce some distortions in size and shape.","zh":"Aitoff projection 指一種旨在減少大小和形狀扭曲的世界地圖投影。"},{"en":"A geography teacher may show the Aitoff projection beside the Mercator projection for comparison.","zh":"地理老師可能把艾托夫投影與麥卡托投影並列展示作比較。"},{"en":"It improves some aspects of representation but sacrifices straight grid lines.","zh":"它改善某些呈現方面，但犧牲直線網格。"},{"en":"This phrase names an alternative map projection.","zh":"這個短語命名一種替代地圖投影。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"attempt to","meaning":"嘗試去","examples":[{"en":"The Aitoff projection attempted to reduce distortion.","zh":"艾托夫投影嘗試去減少扭曲。"},{"en":"To attempt to do something means to try to do it.","zh":"attempt to do something 指嘗試做某事。"},{"en":"A student may attempt to improve pronunciation by recording herself every day.","zh":"學生可能嘗試每天錄音來改善發音。"},{"en":"An attempt may improve a problem without solving it completely.","zh":"嘗試可以改善問題，但未必完全解決它。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on effort toward a goal.","zh":"這個短語著重朝目標付出的努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"represent country sizes and shapes","meaning":"呈現國家的大小和形狀","examples":[{"en":"The Aitoff projection represents country sizes and shapes more correctly.","zh":"艾托夫投影更正確地呈現國家的大小和形狀。"},{"en":"To represent country sizes and shapes means to show how large countries are and what their outlines look like.","zh":"represent country sizes and shapes 指顯示國家有多大，以及其輪廓看起來如何。"},{"en":"A geography textbook should represent country sizes and shapes carefully so students are not misled.","zh":"地理教科書應仔細呈現國家的大小和形狀，以免誤導學生。"},{"en":"Better representation helps viewers compare continents more fairly.","zh":"更好的呈現幫助觀眾更公平地比較大洲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes showing both area and outline on a map.","zh":"這個短語描述在地圖上同時顯示面積和輪廓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"require a compromise","meaning":"需要作出妥協","examples":[{"en":"Representing country shapes more accurately required a compromise.","zh":"更準確地呈現國家形狀需要作出妥協。"},{"en":"To require a compromise means to need one thing to be partly sacrificed so another thing can improve.","zh":"require a compromise 指需要部分犧牲一件事，以改善另一件事。"},{"en":"A school timetable may require a compromise between longer lessons and enough lunch time.","zh":"學校時間表可能需要在較長課節和足夠午膳時間之間作出妥協。"},{"en":"In map-making, improving shape may reduce directional accuracy.","zh":"在地圖製作中，改善形狀可能會降低方向準確度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a necessary trade-off.","zh":"這個短語描述必要取捨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lines of latitude and longitude","meaning":"經緯線","examples":[{"en":"The lines of latitude and longitude had to be bent.","zh":"經緯線必須被彎曲。"},{"en":"Lines of latitude and longitude are the horizontal and vertical grid lines used to locate places on the earth.","zh":"lines of latitude and longitude 指用來定位地球上地方的橫向和縱向網格線。"},{"en":"Students use lines of latitude and longitude to find cities on a world map.","zh":"學生使用經緯線在世界地圖上尋找城市。"},{"en":"If these lines are bent, directions may become harder to judge.","zh":"如果這些線被彎曲，方向可能更難判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the coordinate grid of maps.","zh":"這個短語指地圖上的座標網格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be bent","meaning":"被彎曲","examples":[{"en":"The lines of latitude and longitude had to be bent.","zh":"經緯線必須被彎曲。"},{"en":"To be bent means to be curved or forced away from a straight shape.","zh":"be bent 指被彎成曲線或被迫離開直線形狀。"},{"en":"A metal ruler may be bent if someone presses it too hard.","zh":"如果有人太用力按壓金屬尺，它可能被彎曲。"},{"en":"Bent lines on a map can make direction less immediately clear.","zh":"地圖上的彎曲線條可以令方向不那麼一目了然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change from straight to curved.","zh":"這個短語描述由直變彎的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"had thus been lost","meaning":"因而失去","examples":[{"en":"Fidelity of axis had thus been lost.","zh":"軸向保真度因而失去。"},{"en":"Had thus been lost means had been lost as a result of what happened before.","zh":"had thus been lost 指由於前面發生的事而失去。"},{"en":"The file was moved without a backup, and the original version had thus been lost.","zh":"檔案在沒有備份下被移動，原版本因而失去。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a consequence caused by an earlier change.","zh":"這個短語解釋早前變化造成的後果。"},{"en":"It is often used in formal writing to show cause and result.","zh":"它常用於正式寫作中顯示因果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"judge north, south, east and west","meaning":"判斷東南西北","examples":[{"en":"You could no longer judge north, south, east and west so easily.","zh":"你再也不能那麼容易判斷東南西北。"},{"en":"To judge north, south, east and west means to work out the basic directions.","zh":"judge north, south, east and west 指判斷基本方向。"},{"en":"A visitor may find it hard to judge north, south, east and west in a large shopping mall.","zh":"遊客在大型商場中可能很難判斷東南西北。"},{"en":"Clear map lines help people judge direction quickly.","zh":"清楚的地圖線條幫助人快速判斷方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognising compass directions.","zh":"這個短語描述辨認羅盤方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"most of us","meaning":"我們大多數人","examples":[{"en":"Most of us did not notice that the projections were different.","zh":"我們大多數人沒有注意到這些投影不同。"},{"en":"Most of us means the majority of people, including the speaker and readers.","zh":"most of us 指包括說話者和讀者在內的大多數人。"},{"en":"Most of us use maps without thinking about how they were made.","zh":"我們大多數人使用地圖時，沒有思考它們如何製作。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a shared feeling that a mistake or habit is common.","zh":"這個短語創造一種共同感覺，表示錯誤或習慣很普遍。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing ordinary public understanding.","zh":"它適合用於討論一般公眾理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"assume that","meaning":"假設；以為","examples":[{"en":"Many people assumed that all maps were factual statements.","zh":"許多人以為所有地圖都是事實陳述。"},{"en":"To assume that means to believe something is true without checking it carefully.","zh":"assume that 指未仔細核查就相信某事是真的。"},{"en":"A student may assume that a long answer is correct simply because it looks detailed.","zh":"學生可能只因答案看起來詳細，就以為長答案是正確的。"},{"en":"Assumptions can cause mistakes when they are not tested.","zh":"當假設沒有被檢驗，就可能造成錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accepting an idea too easily.","zh":"這個短語描述太容易接受某想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"factual statements","meaning":"事實陳述","examples":[{"en":"Maps are not simply factual statements.","zh":"地圖並不只是事實陳述。"},{"en":"Factual statements are statements that present information as objective facts.","zh":"factual statements 指把資料呈現為客觀事實的陳述。"},{"en":"“The school opens at 8 a.m.” is a factual statement if it is true.","zh":"如果屬實，「學校上午八時開門」就是事實陳述。"},{"en":"A factual statement can still be incomplete if it leaves out important context.","zh":"事實陳述如果省略重要背景，仍可能不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts fact-based claims with opinions or interpretations.","zh":"這個短語把基於事實的聲稱與意見或詮釋作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be irritated by","meaning":"對……感到惱怒","examples":[{"en":"Dr Arno Peters was irritated by the maps he saw widely published.","zh":"Arno Peters 博士對他看到被廣泛出版的地圖感到惱怒。"},{"en":"To be irritated by something means to feel annoyed because of it.","zh":"be irritated by something 指因某事感到煩躁或惱怒。"},{"en":"A student may be irritated by unclear instructions on a worksheet.","zh":"學生可能對工作紙上不清楚的指示感到惱怒。"},{"en":"People become irritated when a problem keeps appearing and others ignore it.","zh":"當問題不斷出現而其他人忽視它，人們會感到惱怒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mild but clear annoyance.","zh":"這個短語描述輕微但清楚的不滿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"widely published","meaning":"廣泛出版","examples":[{"en":"The maps were widely published in books and atlases.","zh":"這些地圖在書本和地圖集中被廣泛出版。"},{"en":"Widely published means printed or released in many places or by many publishers.","zh":"widely published 指在許多地方或由許多出版者印刷或發布。"},{"en":"A poem may become widely published after it wins a national competition.","zh":"一首詩在贏得全國比賽後，可能被廣泛出版。"},{"en":"When an image is widely published, many people may accept it as normal.","zh":"當一幅圖像被廣泛出版，許多人可能把它視為正常。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad distribution of written or visual material.","zh":"這個短語描述文字或視覺材料的廣泛發行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in particular","meaning":"尤其","examples":[{"en":"He was irritated in particular by the survival of the Mercator projection.","zh":"他尤其對麥卡托投影流傳至今感到惱怒。"},{"en":"In particular means especially or more than the other things mentioned.","zh":"in particular 指尤其，或比其他提及事物更突出。"},{"en":"The teacher praised the class, and in particular the students who helped weaker classmates.","zh":"老師稱讚全班，尤其是那些幫助能力較弱同學的學生。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows attention from a general point to a specific example.","zh":"這個短語把注意力由一般重點收窄到具體例子。"},{"en":"It is useful when one item deserves special focus.","zh":"當某項目值得特別關注時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Eurocentric view","meaning":"歐洲中心主義的世界觀","examples":[{"en":"Peters argued that the Mercator projection gave a Eurocentric view of the world.","zh":"Peters 認為麥卡托投影呈現歐洲中心主義的世界觀。"},{"en":"A Eurocentric view sees or presents the world mainly from a European perspective.","zh":"Eurocentric view 指主要從歐洲角度看待或呈現世界。"},{"en":"A history book may show a Eurocentric view if it treats European events as more important than others.","zh":"如果歷史書把歐洲事件視為比其他地區更重要，它可能呈現歐洲中心主義的世界觀。"},{"en":"A Eurocentric view can make non-European places seem less central or less significant.","zh":"歐洲中心主義的世界觀可以令非歐洲地方看起來較不中心或較不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes perspective shaped around Europe.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞歐洲形成的視角。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"shrink developing countries","meaning":"縮小發展中國家","examples":[{"en":"The Mercator projection shrank the developing countries.","zh":"麥卡托投影縮小了發展中國家。"},{"en":"To shrink developing countries means to make them appear smaller than they really are.","zh":"shrink developing countries 指令發展中國家看起來比真實大小更小。"},{"en":"A badly scaled chart may shrink poorer districts and make their needs look less serious.","zh":"比例不當的圖表可能縮小較貧窮地區，令其需要看起來較不嚴重。"},{"en":"Shrinking countries on a map can affect how viewers judge their importance.","zh":"在地圖上縮小國家，可以影響觀眾如何判斷其重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual reduction that may carry political meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述可能帶有政治意義的視覺縮小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"developing countries","meaning":"發展中國家","examples":[{"en":"Many developing countries lie near the equator.","zh":"許多發展中國家位於赤道附近。"},{"en":"Developing countries are countries with lower average income or less industrial development than richer countries.","zh":"developing countries 指平均收入較低或工業發展較少的國家。"},{"en":"Developing countries may need investment in schools, hospitals, roads, and clean water.","zh":"發展中國家可能需要學校、醫院、道路和清潔食水方面的投資。"},{"en":"How maps show developing countries can affect how people imagine their size and importance.","zh":"地圖如何顯示發展中國家，可以影響人們想像其大小和重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to countries still building economic and social capacity.","zh":"這個短語指仍在建立經濟和社會能力的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"around the equator","meaning":"在赤道附近","examples":[{"en":"Many developing countries are around the equator.","zh":"許多發展中國家在赤道附近。"},{"en":"Around the equator means near the imaginary line across the middle of the earth.","zh":"around the equator 指靠近橫跨地球中部的想像線。"},{"en":"Countries around the equator often experience warm weather throughout the year.","zh":"赤道附近的國家通常全年天氣溫暖。"},{"en":"On some maps, places around the equator may appear smaller than their true area.","zh":"在某些地圖上，赤道附近的地方可能看起來比真實面積更小。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location near the earth’s central latitude line.","zh":"這個短語描述靠近地球中央緯線的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"expand the richer countries","meaning":"放大較富裕國家","examples":[{"en":"The projection expanded the richer countries.","zh":"這種投影放大了較富裕國家。"},{"en":"To expand the richer countries means to make wealthy countries appear larger on the map.","zh":"expand the richer countries 指令富裕國家在地圖上看起來更大。"},{"en":"A distorted chart may expand rich districts and make them look more dominant.","zh":"扭曲的圖表可能放大富裕地區，令它們看起來更具支配性。"},{"en":"Enlarging richer countries can make viewers feel they are more important than they are by area.","zh":"放大較富裕國家，可以令觀眾感到它們在面積上比實際更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual enlargement linked to inequality in representation.","zh":"這個短語描述與呈現不平等相關的視覺放大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lie farther north","meaning":"位於較北方","examples":[{"en":"Many richer countries lie farther north.","zh":"許多較富裕國家位於較北方。"},{"en":"To lie farther north means to be located at a more northern position.","zh":"lie farther north 指位於更偏北的位置。"},{"en":"A city that lies farther north may have colder winters than a city near the equator.","zh":"位於較北方的城市，冬天可能比赤道附近城市更冷。"},{"en":"On the Mercator projection, places that lie farther north can look larger than they are.","zh":"在麥卡托投影上，位於較北方的地方可能看起來比實際更大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes geographical position.","zh":"這個短語描述地理位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"two thirds of the way down","meaning":"在往下三分之二的位置","examples":[{"en":"The equator is shown two thirds of the way down the traditional Mercator map.","zh":"赤道在傳統麥卡托地圖上顯示在往下三分之二的位置。"},{"en":"Two thirds of the way down means at a point about two-thirds from the top toward the bottom.","zh":"two thirds of the way down 指從頂部往下約三分之二的位置。"},{"en":"On the noticeboard, the exam timetable is two thirds of the way down the page.","zh":"在告示板上，考試時間表位於頁面往下三分之二的位置。"},{"en":"If the equator is placed low, the northern half of the world appears visually dominant.","zh":"如果赤道被放得很低，世界北半部就會在視覺上顯得佔優。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a position on a page or image.","zh":"這個短語描述頁面或圖像上的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"traditional Mercator map","meaning":"傳統麥卡托地圖","examples":[{"en":"The traditional Mercator map places the equator unusually low.","zh":"傳統麥卡托地圖把赤道放在異常低的位置。"},{"en":"The traditional Mercator map is the familiar world map based on Mercator’s projection.","zh":"traditional Mercator map 指基於麥卡托投影的常見世界地圖。"},{"en":"Many classrooms once used a traditional Mercator map because it looked familiar and orderly.","zh":"許多課室曾使用傳統麥卡托地圖，因為它看起來熟悉而整齊。"},{"en":"Its familiar appearance can hide serious distortions of country size.","zh":"它熟悉的外觀可以隱藏國家大小的嚴重扭曲。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the common version of the Mercator world map.","zh":"這個短語指常見版本的麥卡托世界地圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"insist that","meaning":"堅稱","examples":[{"en":"Dr Peters insisted that his map used an equal-area projection.","zh":"Peters 博士堅稱他的地圖使用等積投影。"},{"en":"To insist that means to state something firmly, especially when others may disagree.","zh":"insist that 指堅定地陳述某事，尤其在其他人可能不同意時。"},{"en":"A student may insist that her answer is correct because the passage clearly supports it.","zh":"學生可能堅稱自己的答案正確，因為文章清楚支持它。"},{"en":"People insist on a point when they believe it is important and should not be ignored.","zh":"當人們相信某點很重要、不應被忽視，就會堅持該點。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong certainty or determination.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈肯定或決心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"first appear","meaning":"首次出現","examples":[{"en":"The Peters map first appeared in 1985.","zh":"彼得斯地圖於 1985 年首次出現。"},{"en":"To first appear means to be seen, published, or introduced for the first time.","zh":"first appear 指首次被看見、出版或引入。"},{"en":"A new school rule may first appear in the handbook before teachers explain it in class.","zh":"新校規可能先在手冊中首次出現，然後老師再在課堂解釋。"},{"en":"When an idea first appears, people may not yet understand its importance.","zh":"當一個想法首次出現，人們未必理解其重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the beginning of public visibility.","zh":"這個短語標記開始公開出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"equal-area projection","meaning":"等積投影","examples":[{"en":"An equal-area projection shows countries according to their true relative area.","zh":"等積投影按照國家的真實相對面積顯示國家。"},{"en":"An equal-area projection is a map method that preserves the correct relative sizes of land areas.","zh":"equal-area projection 指保留陸地面積正確相對大小的製圖方法。"},{"en":"A geography teacher may use an equal-area projection to compare Africa and Europe fairly.","zh":"地理老師可能使用等積投影來公平比較非洲和歐洲。"},{"en":"Equal area can be gained only by sacrificing some accuracy in shape or direction.","zh":"等積只能透過犧牲某些形狀或方向準確度來取得。"},{"en":"This phrase names a projection that prioritises area over other map features.","zh":"這個短語命名一種優先考慮面積的投影。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"no country is given prominence over another","meaning":"沒有國家比另一國更突出","examples":[{"en":"In an equal-area projection, no country is given prominence over another.","zh":"在等積投影中，沒有國家比另一國更突出。"},{"en":"No country is given prominence over another means no country is made to look more important through larger area.","zh":"no country is given prominence over another 指沒有國家透過較大面積被塑造成更重要。"},{"en":"A fair class display gives no student prominence over another unless there is a clear reason.","zh":"公平的班級展示不會讓某學生比另一學生更突出，除非有清楚理由。"},{"en":"Equal treatment in design can reduce hidden bias.","zh":"設計上的平等處理可以減少隱藏偏見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual fairness between countries.","zh":"這個短語描述國家之間的視覺公平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"plus","meaning":"加上；以及","examples":[{"en":"Peters wanted equal area plus fidelity of axis.","zh":"Peters 想要等積加上軸向保真度。"},{"en":"Plus means together with or in addition to something else.","zh":"plus 指連同或另外加上某事。"},{"en":"The course includes grammar practice plus weekly writing feedback.","zh":"課程包括文法練習，以及每週寫作回饋。"},{"en":"Adding one feature plus another can improve usefulness, but it may create trade-offs.","zh":"加上一個特徵再加上另一個，可以提高實用性，但可能造成取捨。"},{"en":"This word joins two desired qualities or items.","zh":"這個詞連接兩種想要的品質或項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"avoid the disorientating effect of","meaning":"避免……令人迷失方向的影響","examples":[{"en":"Peters wanted to avoid the disorientating effect of bent lines.","zh":"Peters 想避免彎曲線條令人迷失方向的影響。"},{"en":"To avoid the disorientating effect of something means to prevent it from making people confused about direction or position.","zh":"avoid the disorientating effect of something 指防止某事令人對方向或位置感到混亂。"},{"en":"A shopping mall uses clear signs to avoid the disorientating effect of many similar corridors.","zh":"商場使用清楚標示，以避免許多相似走廊令人迷失方向的影響。"},{"en":"Straight map lines can help users avoid feeling lost.","zh":"直線地圖線條可以幫助使用者避免迷路感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preventing confusion caused by a design feature.","zh":"這個短語描述防止設計特徵造成混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"disorientating effect","meaning":"令人迷失方向的效果","examples":[{"en":"Bent lines of latitude and longitude can have a disorientating effect.","zh":"彎曲的經緯線可以產生令人迷失方向的效果。"},{"en":"A disorientating effect is a confusing effect that makes people feel unsure about direction or position.","zh":"disorientating effect 指令人混亂、對方向或位置不確定的效果。"},{"en":"Poor signs in a hospital can have a disorientating effect on visitors.","zh":"醫院標示差，可以對訪客產生令人迷失方向的效果。"},{"en":"When a map has a disorientating effect, users may struggle to judge where places are.","zh":"當地圖有令人迷失方向的效果，使用者可能難以判斷地方在哪裡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes confusion caused by layout or representation.","zh":"這個短語描述由布局或呈現造成的混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"country shape","meaning":"國家形狀","examples":[{"en":"Country shape is another problem in map projections.","zh":"國家形狀是地圖投影中的另一個問題。"},{"en":"Country shape means the outline or form of a country on a map.","zh":"country shape 指國家在地圖上的輪廓或形態。"},{"en":"Students may recognise Italy by its country shape because it looks like a boot.","zh":"學生可能透過國家形狀認出意大利，因為它像一隻靴。"},{"en":"Projections can change country shape when the round earth is flattened.","zh":"當圓形地球被壓成平面，投影可以改變國家形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on outline, not area alone.","zh":"這個短語著重輪廓，而不只是面積。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take a photo of","meaning":"拍攝……的照片","examples":[{"en":"If you took a photo of a globe, some countries would look more accurate than others.","zh":"如果你拍攝地球儀的照片，有些國家會比其他國家看起來更準確。"},{"en":"To take a photo of something means to use a camera to capture its image.","zh":"take a photo of something 指用相機捕捉某物的影像。"},{"en":"A student may take a photo of the homework board before leaving school.","zh":"學生可能離校前拍攝功課板的照片。"},{"en":"A photo shows one viewpoint, so some parts may look clearer than others.","zh":"照片顯示一個視角，因此某些部分可能比其他部分更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating a visual record with a camera.","zh":"這個短語描述用相機製作視覺紀錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in its normal position","meaning":"在正常位置","examples":[{"en":"A globe in its normal position shows equatorial countries fairly well.","zh":"地球儀在正常位置時，會相當好地顯示赤道國家。"},{"en":"In its normal position means placed in the usual or standard way.","zh":"in its normal position 指以通常或標準方式擺放。"},{"en":"A projector works best when it is in its normal position facing the screen directly.","zh":"投影機在正常位置、正對螢幕時效果最好。"},{"en":"The position of an object affects what viewers can see clearly.","zh":"物件的位置會影響觀眾能清楚看見甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the usual arrangement of something.","zh":"這個短語指某物的通常擺放方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"come out of it pretty well","meaning":"顯示得相當不錯","examples":[{"en":"Countries around the equator would come out of it pretty well.","zh":"赤道附近的國家會顯示得相當不錯。"},{"en":"To come out of it pretty well means to be shown or affected fairly successfully in that situation.","zh":"come out of it pretty well 指在某情況中被顯示或受影響得相當成功。"},{"en":"A student may come out of a difficult interview pretty well if she answers calmly.","zh":"如果學生冷靜回答，她可能在困難面試中表現得相當不錯。"},{"en":"In a photo of a globe, countries near the centre may come out better than those near the edges.","zh":"在地球儀照片中，靠近中心的國家可能比邊緣國家顯示得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reasonably good result after a process.","zh":"這個短語描述經過某過程後得到相當好的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"relatively large","meaning":"相對較大","examples":[{"en":"Equatorial countries would be shown relatively large.","zh":"赤道國家會被顯示得相對較大。"},{"en":"Relatively large means large compared with something else in the same situation.","zh":"relatively large 指與同一情況中的其他事物相比較大。"},{"en":"A small flat may feel relatively large if it has good storage and open space.","zh":"如果小單位有良好收納和開放空間，可能感覺相對較大。"},{"en":"Relative size depends on what is being compared.","zh":"相對大小取決於正在比較的事物。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a comparison rather than an absolute measurement.","zh":"這個短語給出比較，而不是絕對量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"close to their correct shape","meaning":"接近其正確形狀","examples":[{"en":"Some countries would appear close to their correct shape.","zh":"有些國家會看起來接近其正確形狀。"},{"en":"Close to their correct shape means looking almost like their true outline.","zh":"close to their correct shape 指看起來幾乎像其真實輪廓。"},{"en":"A drawing of a classroom may be close to its correct shape even if the furniture is not exact.","zh":"課室圖畫即使家具不精確，仍可能接近其正確形狀。"},{"en":"When shapes are close to correct, viewers can recognise places more easily.","zh":"當形狀接近正確，觀眾較容易認出地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes approximate visual accuracy.","zh":"這個短語描述大約的視覺準確性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"further north or south","meaning":"更北或更南","examples":[{"en":"Further north or south, there are considerable distortions.","zh":"在更北或更南的地方，會有相當大的扭曲。"},{"en":"Further north or south means at locations farther away from the equator toward either pole.","zh":"further north or south 指在離赤道更遠、朝任一極方向的位置。"},{"en":"Cities further north or south may have stronger seasonal changes than places near the equator.","zh":"更北或更南的城市可能比赤道附近地方有更強季節變化。"},{"en":"On some maps, places further north or south are more distorted.","zh":"在某些地圖上，更北或更南的地方會被扭曲得更多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position away from the earth’s middle.","zh":"這個短語描述遠離地球中部的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"considerable distortions","meaning":"相當大的扭曲","examples":[{"en":"Countries far from the equator suffer considerable distortions.","zh":"遠離赤道的國家受到相當大的扭曲。"},{"en":"Considerable distortions are large and noticeable changes from the true shape, size, or position.","zh":"considerable distortions 指與真實形狀、大小或位置相比，有大型且明顯的改變。"},{"en":"A face in a stretched photo may suffer considerable distortions.","zh":"被拉長的照片中的臉可能受到相當大的扭曲。"},{"en":"Considerable distortions can make viewers misjudge what they are seeing.","zh":"相當大的扭曲可以令觀眾誤判所見內容。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious but not necessarily total inaccuracy.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重但不一定完全的失準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tail away alarmingly","meaning":"以令人吃驚的方式逐漸變形","examples":[{"en":"Australia tails away alarmingly in some projections.","zh":"澳洲在某些投影中以令人吃驚的方式逐漸變形。"},{"en":"To tail away alarmingly means to narrow or stretch away in a way that looks worrying or strange.","zh":"tail away alarmingly 指以令人擔心或奇怪的方式逐漸變窄或拉長。"},{"en":"A badly printed logo may tail away alarmingly at one edge if the image is stretched.","zh":"如果圖像被拉伸，印刷差的標誌可能在一邊以令人吃驚的方式變形。"},{"en":"When a country tails away on a map, its shape no longer looks natural.","zh":"當一個國家在地圖上逐漸變形，其形狀就不再自然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a disturbing visual distortion.","zh":"這個短語描述令人不安的視覺扭曲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"least distortion","meaning":"最少扭曲","examples":[{"en":"Peters decided that the least distortion should occur at 45 degrees latitude.","zh":"Peters 決定最少扭曲應出現在 45 度緯線。"},{"en":"Least distortion means the smallest amount of change from the true shape or size.","zh":"least distortion 指與真實形狀或大小相比改變最少。"},{"en":"A photographer may stand in the centre of a room to get the least distortion in a wide-angle photo.","zh":"攝影師可能站在房間中央，以在廣角照片中取得最少扭曲。"},{"en":"Mapmakers choose where least distortion should occur based on what they value most.","zh":"地圖製作者根據自己最重視甚麼，選擇最少扭曲應出現在哪裡。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the most accurate part of an imperfect representation.","zh":"這個短語指不完美呈現中最準確的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"occur at","meaning":"發生於","examples":[{"en":"The least distortion occurs at the 45-degree lines of latitude.","zh":"最少扭曲發生於 45 度緯線。"},{"en":"To occur at a place means to happen or be found there.","zh":"occur at a place 指在某地發生或出現。"},{"en":"Traffic jams often occur at the school gate before lessons begin.","zh":"上課前，交通擠塞常發生於校門口。"},{"en":"In a map projection, distortion can occur at different locations with different intensity.","zh":"在地圖投影中，扭曲可以在不同位置以不同強度發生。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an event or feature with a location.","zh":"這個短語把事件或特徵與位置連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"45-degree lines of latitude","meaning":"45 度緯線","examples":[{"en":"Peters placed the least distortion at the 45-degree lines of latitude.","zh":"Peters 把最少扭曲放在 45 度緯線。"},{"en":"The 45-degree lines of latitude are the lines halfway between the equator and the poles in each hemisphere.","zh":"45-degree lines of latitude 指每個半球中赤道與兩極之間大約一半位置的緯線。"},{"en":"Cities near 45 degrees latitude often lie in temperate regions.","zh":"45 度緯線附近的城市通常位於溫帶地區。"},{"en":"Choosing these lines affects which countries appear most accurately.","zh":"選擇這些緯線會影響哪些國家顯示得最準確。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to specific latitude lines on the world map.","zh":"這個短語指世界地圖上的特定緯線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"much more populated areas","meaning":"人口密度高得多的地區","examples":[{"en":"The 45-degree lines pass through much more populated areas.","zh":"45 度緯線穿過人口密度高得多的地區。"},{"en":"Much more populated areas are places where many more people live compared with other regions.","zh":"much more populated areas 指與其他地區相比有更多人居住的地方。"},{"en":"A bus route through much more populated areas will usually have more passengers.","zh":"經過人口密度高得多地區的巴士路線，通常會有更多乘客。"},{"en":"If map accuracy is placed in populated areas, more viewers may see familiar regions clearly.","zh":"如果地圖準確度放在人口密集地區，更多觀眾可能清楚看見熟悉地區。"},{"en":"This phrase compares population concentration.","zh":"這個短語比較人口集中程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"controversial Peters map","meaning":"具爭議的彼得斯地圖","examples":[{"en":"The controversial Peters map changed the shape of Africa and South America.","zh":"具爭議的彼得斯地圖改變了非洲和南美洲的形狀。"},{"en":"The controversial Peters map is Peters’s world map, which caused debate because it challenged familiar map views.","zh":"controversial Peters map 指 Peters 的世界地圖，因挑戰熟悉地圖觀而引發爭論。"},{"en":"A teacher may use the controversial Peters map to make students question what maps show.","zh":"老師可能使用具爭議的彼得斯地圖，讓學生質疑地圖顯示了甚麼。"},{"en":"It became controversial because it made familiar continents look strange while claiming greater fairness in area.","zh":"它之所以具爭議，是因為它令熟悉的大洲看起來陌生，同時聲稱在面積上更公平。"},{"en":"This phrase names a map that provoked public discussion.","zh":"這個短語命名一張引發公共討論的地圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"radically change","meaning":"徹底改變","examples":[{"en":"The Peters map radically changes the shape of some continents.","zh":"彼得斯地圖徹底改變某些大洲的形狀。"},{"en":"To radically change something means to change it in a very deep or dramatic way.","zh":"radically change something 指以非常深刻或戲劇性的方式改變某事。"},{"en":"Online learning radically changed how some students attended lessons.","zh":"網上學習徹底改變了一些學生上課的方式。"},{"en":"Radical changes can make familiar things look strange at first.","zh":"徹底改變可以令熟悉事物起初看起來陌生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes major transformation, not small adjustment.","zh":"這個短語描述重大轉變，而不是小調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Africa and South America","meaning":"非洲和南美洲","examples":[{"en":"Africa and South America look different on the Peters projection.","zh":"非洲和南美洲在彼得斯投影上看起來不同。"},{"en":"Africa and South America are two large continents often discussed in debates about map distortion.","zh":"Africa and South America 是兩個大型大洲，常在地圖扭曲爭論中被討論。"},{"en":"Students may compare Africa and South America with Europe to see how map projections affect size.","zh":"學生可能把非洲和南美洲與歐洲比較，以看見地圖投影如何影響大小。"},{"en":"On some maps, Africa and South America appear smaller or differently shaped than expected.","zh":"在某些地圖上，非洲和南美洲看起來比預期更小或形狀不同。"},{"en":"This phrase names two continents central to the discussion of fair representation.","zh":"這個短語命名公平呈現討論中的兩個核心大洲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"distort to some extent","meaning":"在某程度上扭曲","examples":[{"en":"All projections distort the world to some extent.","zh":"所有投影都在某程度上扭曲世界。"},{"en":"To distort to some extent means to change something partly, though not completely.","zh":"distort to some extent 指部分改變某事，但不是完全改變。"},{"en":"A timetable summary may distort reality to some extent because it leaves out delays and breaks.","zh":"時間表摘要可能在某程度上扭曲現實，因為它省略延誤和休息時間。"},{"en":"Any simplified representation distorts reality to some extent.","zh":"任何簡化呈現都會在某程度上扭曲現實。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a balanced statement about limited inaccuracy.","zh":"這個短語對有限的不準確作出平衡說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"to some extent","meaning":"在某程度上","examples":[{"en":"All global maps distort reality to some extent.","zh":"所有全球地圖都在某程度上扭曲現實。"},{"en":"To some extent means partly or in a limited way.","zh":"to some extent 指部分地或在有限程度上。"},{"en":"Homework helps students to some extent, but feedback is also important.","zh":"功課在某程度上幫助學生，但回饋也很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase softens a statement so it is not too absolute.","zh":"這個短語令陳述不那麼絕對。"},{"en":"It is useful when something is true, but not completely true.","zh":"當某事為真但並非完全為真時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"exceptionally long and thin","meaning":"異常修長","examples":[{"en":"Africa appears exceptionally long and thin on the Peters map.","zh":"非洲在彼得斯地圖上顯得異常修長。"},{"en":"Exceptionally long and thin means unusually stretched in length and narrow in width.","zh":"exceptionally long and thin 指長度被異常拉長而闊度狹窄。"},{"en":"A photo can make a person look exceptionally long and thin if the camera angle is wrong.","zh":"如果相機角度錯誤，照片可以令人看起來異常修長。"},{"en":"Such distortion may make viewers feel that a familiar shape is strange.","zh":"這種扭曲可能令觀眾覺得熟悉形狀很奇怪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an extreme visual stretching effect.","zh":"這個短語描述極端視覺拉伸效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the oddity of","meaning":"……的怪異之處","examples":[{"en":"The oddity of the Peters projection helped make it successful.","zh":"彼得斯投影的怪異之處幫助它成功。"},{"en":"The oddity of something is the strange or unusual quality it has.","zh":"oddity of something 指某物具有的奇怪或不尋常特質。"},{"en":"The oddity of a new building may make people stop and look at it.","zh":"新建築的怪異之處可能令人停下來觀看。"},{"en":"Something unusual can attract attention even when people disagree with it.","zh":"不尋常的東西即使令人不同意，也可以吸引注意。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on strangeness as a noticeable feature.","zh":"這個短語著重怪異作為顯眼特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be partly responsible for","meaning":"是……的部分原因","examples":[{"en":"The oddity of the Peters projection was partly responsible for its success.","zh":"彼得斯投影的怪異之處是其成功的部分原因。"},{"en":"To be partly responsible for something means to be one of the causes of it.","zh":"be partly responsible for something 指是某事的其中一個原因。"},{"en":"Poor sleep may be partly responsible for a student’s weak concentration.","zh":"睡眠不足可能是學生專注力弱的部分原因。"},{"en":"A result often has several causes, and one factor may be only partly responsible.","zh":"一個結果常有幾個原因，而某因素可能只是部分原因。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a cautious explanation of cause.","zh":"這個短語給出謹慎的因果解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"widespread discussion","meaning":"廣泛討論","examples":[{"en":"The Peters map created widespread discussion about map distortion.","zh":"彼得斯地圖引發關於地圖扭曲的廣泛討論。"},{"en":"Widespread discussion means many people in different places are talking about an issue.","zh":"widespread discussion 指不同地方的許多人都在討論某議題。"},{"en":"A new school policy may create widespread discussion among parents and teachers.","zh":"新校政可能在家長和老師之間引發廣泛討論。"},{"en":"Widespread discussion can make a hidden problem become publicly recognised.","zh":"廣泛討論可以令隱藏問題得到公眾承認。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad public debate.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛公共辯論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"misrepresentation of","meaning":"對……的錯誤呈現","examples":[{"en":"The map raised awareness of the misrepresentation of country sizes.","zh":"這張地圖提高了人們對國家大小錯誤呈現的意識。"},{"en":"Misrepresentation of something means showing or describing it in a false or misleading way.","zh":"misrepresentation of something 指以虛假或誤導方式顯示或描述某事。"},{"en":"An advertisement may involve misrepresentation of a product if it hides important weaknesses.","zh":"如果廣告隱藏產品重要弱點，就可能涉及對產品的錯誤呈現。"},{"en":"Misrepresentation can shape people’s beliefs before they realise the information is unfair.","zh":"錯誤呈現可以在人們意識到資訊不公平前塑造其信念。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inaccurate or biased presentation.","zh":"這個短語描述不準確或偏頗的呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"country sizes","meaning":"國家大小","examples":[{"en":"The misrepresentation of country sizes became a major issue.","zh":"國家大小的錯誤呈現成為重大議題。"},{"en":"Country sizes are the land areas of countries compared with one another.","zh":"country sizes 指各國土地面積彼此比較的大小。"},{"en":"Students may be surprised when they compare country sizes using actual data rather than a familiar map.","zh":"當學生用實際數據而不是熟悉地圖比較國家大小時，可能會感到驚訝。"},{"en":"Misreading country sizes can affect how people imagine power, importance, and distance.","zh":"誤讀國家大小可以影響人們如何想像權力、重要性和距離。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to national land area.","zh":"這個短語指國土面積。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"previous maps","meaning":"以往的地圖","examples":[{"en":"Previous maps often misrepresented the sizes of countries.","zh":"以往的地圖常錯誤呈現國家的大小。"},{"en":"Previous maps are maps made or used before the current one being discussed.","zh":"previous maps 指在目前討論的地圖之前製作或使用的地圖。"},{"en":"A teacher may compare previous maps with modern ones to show how ideas changed.","zh":"老師可能比較以往的地圖與現代地圖，以顯示想法如何改變。"},{"en":"Older maps may carry assumptions that later viewers need to question.","zh":"舊地圖可能帶有後來觀眾需要質疑的假設。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to maps from an earlier period.","zh":"這個短語指較早時期的地圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"raise issues","meaning":"提出議題","examples":[{"en":"The Peters map raises issues about fairness and perspective.","zh":"彼得斯地圖提出關於公平和視角的議題。"},{"en":"To raise issues means to bring problems or questions into discussion.","zh":"raise issues 指把問題或疑問帶入討論。"},{"en":"A student survey may raise issues about homework pressure and sleep.","zh":"學生調查可能提出關於功課壓力和睡眠的議題。"},{"en":"Raising issues helps people notice problems they may have ignored.","zh":"提出議題幫助人們注意到可能忽視的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes starting important discussion.","zh":"這個短語描述開始重要討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"relatively simple","meaning":"相對簡單","examples":[{"en":"The issues raised by the Peters map are relatively simple.","zh":"彼得斯地圖提出的議題相對簡單。"},{"en":"Relatively simple means not very difficult compared with other related matters.","zh":"relatively simple 指與其他相關事項相比不算很困難。"},{"en":"Learning the alphabet is relatively simple compared with writing a full essay.","zh":"與寫完整作文相比，學習字母相對簡單。"},{"en":"A problem can be relatively simple in theory but still controversial in public debate.","zh":"問題在理論上可以相對簡單，但在公共辯論中仍具爭議。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a careful comparison of difficulty.","zh":"這個短語對難度作出謹慎比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"resembling","meaning":"類似","examples":[{"en":"An equal-area map with fidelity of axis will resemble the Peters projection.","zh":"具有軸向保真度的等積地圖會類似彼得斯投影。"},{"en":"Resembling means looking like or being similar to something.","zh":"resembling 指看起來像或與某事相似。"},{"en":"A new school logo may resemble the old one if it keeps the same colours and shape.","zh":"如果新校徽保留相同顏色和形狀，它可能類似舊校徽。"},{"en":"Things resemble each other when they share important visual or structural features.","zh":"當事物共享重要視覺或結構特徵，它們就會相似。"},{"en":"This word describes similarity, not exact sameness.","zh":"這個詞描述相似，而不是完全一樣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"more significant","meaning":"更重要","examples":[{"en":"If you think shape is more significant, you will choose a different projection.","zh":"如果你認為形狀更重要，你會選擇另一種投影。"},{"en":"More significant means more important or meaningful in a particular decision.","zh":"more significant 指在某個決定中更重要或更有意義。"},{"en":"For a young student, clear feedback may be more significant than a high mark.","zh":"對年幼學生來說，清楚回饋可能比高分更重要。"},{"en":"What seems more significant depends on the purpose of the task.","zh":"甚麼看似更重要，取決於任務目的。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare priorities.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較優先事項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"something else","meaning":"另一種東西","examples":[{"en":"If shape matters more, you will get something else.","zh":"如果形狀更重要，你會得到另一種東西。"},{"en":"Something else means another result, option, or kind of thing.","zh":"something else 指另一個結果、選項或種類的東西。"},{"en":"If the café is full, we can eat somewhere else.","zh":"如果咖啡店坐滿了，我們可以去另一個地方吃。"},{"en":"Choosing a different priority often gives you something else, not the same outcome.","zh":"選擇不同優先事項，通常會得到另一種結果，而不是同一結果。"},{"en":"This phrase points to an alternative.","zh":"這個短語指向替代選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the real value of","meaning":"……的真正價值","examples":[{"en":"The real value of the Peters projection is that it changed how people think about maps.","zh":"彼得斯投影的真正價值在於它改變了人們如何思考地圖。"},{"en":"The real value of something is its most important benefit or meaning.","zh":"the real value of something 指某事最重要的好處或意義。"},{"en":"The real value of a school trip may be helping students understand people outside the classroom.","zh":"學校旅行的真正價值可能是幫助學生理解課室外的人。"},{"en":"Sometimes the real value of an idea is not practical use but the questions it raises.","zh":"有時一個想法的真正價值不是實際用途，而是它提出的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase points to deeper importance.","zh":"這個短語指向更深層的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make the world think about","meaning":"令全世界思考","examples":[{"en":"The Peters projection made the world think about map bias.","zh":"彼得斯投影令全世界思考地圖偏見。"},{"en":"To make the world think about something means to bring an issue to wide public attention.","zh":"make the world think about something 指把某議題帶到廣泛公眾注意之中。"},{"en":"A powerful documentary can make the world think about food waste.","zh":"有力的紀錄片可以令全世界思考食物浪費。"},{"en":"Public attention can change when one example makes a hidden problem visible.","zh":"當一個例子令隱藏問題變得可見，公眾注意力可以改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes causing broad reflection or debate.","zh":"這個短語描述引發廣泛反思或辯論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"take something seriously","meaning":"認真看待某事","examples":[{"en":"People had never taken the bias of maps seriously before.","zh":"人們以前從未認真看待地圖的偏見。"},{"en":"To take something seriously means to treat it as important and worth careful thought.","zh":"take something seriously 指把某事視為重要並值得仔細思考。"},{"en":"Students should take sleep seriously because it affects memory and mood.","zh":"學生應認真看待睡眠，因為它影響記憶和心情。"},{"en":"A problem may grow worse if people do not take it seriously early enough.","zh":"如果人們不及早認真看待問題，問題可能變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving proper attention to an issue.","zh":"這個短語描述對某議題給予適當注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"represent a point of view","meaning":"代表一種觀點","examples":[{"en":"Maps of the world represent a point of view.","zh":"世界地圖代表一種觀點。"},{"en":"To represent a point of view means to show a particular perspective through words, images, or design.","zh":"represent a point of view 指透過文字、圖像或設計展示某特定視角。"},{"en":"A school poster can represent a point of view by showing only the benefits of a new rule.","zh":"學校海報如果只展示新規則的好處，就可以代表一種觀點。"},{"en":"Representing one viewpoint may make other viewpoints less visible.","zh":"代表一種觀點可能令其他觀點較不明顯。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds learners that presentation is not always neutral.","zh":"這個短語提醒學習者，呈現方式不一定中立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"press articles","meaning":"報章文章","examples":[{"en":"Maps can express a viewpoint just as press articles do.","zh":"地圖可以像報章文章一樣表達觀點。"},{"en":"Press articles are written pieces published in newspapers, magazines, or news websites.","zh":"press articles 指刊登在報紙、雜誌或新聞網站上的文章。"},{"en":"Students may compare press articles to see how different writers present the same event.","zh":"學生可能比較報章文章，以看出不同作者如何呈現同一事件。"},{"en":"Press articles can inform readers, but word choice can also reveal a viewpoint.","zh":"報章文章可以向讀者提供資訊，但用詞也可以透露觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to written journalism.","zh":"這個短語指新聞寫作文章。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"TV programmes","meaning":"電視節目","examples":[{"en":"Maps can express a viewpoint just as TV programmes do.","zh":"地圖可以像電視節目一樣表達觀點。"},{"en":"TV programmes are shows broadcast on television or through similar media platforms.","zh":"TV programmes 指在電視或類似媒體平台播放的節目。"},{"en":"A TV programme about travel may show only luxury hotels and ignore local poverty.","zh":"關於旅遊的電視節目可能只展示豪華酒店，而忽視本地貧窮。"},{"en":"Programmes can shape public opinion through what they include and leave out.","zh":"節目可以透過包括和省略的內容塑造公眾意見。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to televised content.","zh":"這個短語指電視播放內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"it isn’t recommended that","meaning":"不建議","examples":[{"en":"It isn’t recommended that you navigate using a single global projection.","zh":"不建議你使用單一全球投影來導航。"},{"en":"It isn’t recommended that means people should not normally do something because it may be unwise or unsafe.","zh":"it isn’t recommended that 指人們通常不應做某事，因為它可能不明智或不安全。"},{"en":"It isn’t recommended that students revise only on the night before an exam.","zh":"不建議學生只在考試前一晚溫習。"},{"en":"Advice is often written this way when the writer wants to sound formal and careful.","zh":"當作者想語氣正式而謹慎時，常用這種方式表達建議。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a warning or cautious recommendation.","zh":"這個短語引入警告或謹慎建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"navigate a 747 round the world","meaning":"駕駛 747 環遊世界","examples":[{"en":"You should not navigate a 747 round the world with the Peters projection.","zh":"你不應用彼得斯投影來駕駛 747 環遊世界。"},{"en":"To navigate a 747 round the world means to guide a large aircraft around the globe.","zh":"navigate a 747 round the world 指引導大型飛機環繞地球飛行。"},{"en":"Pilots need specialised navigation systems to fly long international routes safely.","zh":"飛機師需要專門導航系統，才能安全飛行長途國際航線。"},{"en":"A map designed for fairness in area may not be suitable for aircraft navigation.","zh":"為面積公平而設計的地圖，未必適合飛機導航。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a vivid example of using the wrong map for the wrong purpose.","zh":"這個短語生動地說明把錯誤地圖用於錯誤目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"single global projection","meaning":"單一全球投影","examples":[{"en":"No single global projection is perfect for navigation.","zh":"沒有單一全球投影完全適合導航。"},{"en":"A single global projection is one map method used to represent the whole world on a flat surface.","zh":"single global projection 指用一種地圖方法在平面上呈現整個世界。"},{"en":"A classroom may use one single global projection for convenience, but students should know its limits.","zh":"課室可能為方便而使用單一全球投影，但學生應知道其限制。"},{"en":"No single projection can preserve area, shape, distance, and direction perfectly at once.","zh":"沒有單一投影可以同時完美保留面積、形狀、距離和方向。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to one flat-map system for the entire earth.","zh":"這個短語指用於整個地球的一種平面地圖系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lead you astray","meaning":"令你誤入歧途","examples":[{"en":"Any single global projection could lead you astray.","zh":"任何單一全球投影都可能令你誤入歧途。"},{"en":"To lead you astray means to guide you in the wrong direction or make you believe something wrong.","zh":"lead you astray 指引導你走錯方向或令你相信錯誤事情。"},{"en":"A misleading sign at a station can lead passengers astray.","zh":"車站中具誤導性的標示可以令乘客誤入歧途。"},{"en":"A map can lead you astray if you use it for a purpose it was not designed for.","zh":"如果你把地圖用於非原本設計目的，它可以令你誤入歧途。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being misled or sent the wrong way.","zh":"這個短語描述被誤導或被帶往錯誤方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words from the box.","zh":"學生使用方框中的詞語完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill missing parts of a short version of the passage.","zh":"complete the summary 指填補文章簡短版本中的缺失部分。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete the summary by choosing words that match grammar and meaning.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過選擇符合文法和意思的詞語完成摘要。"},{"en":"Completing a summary checks whether students understand the main ideas and details.","zh":"完成摘要檢查學生是否理解主旨和細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"choose your answers from","meaning":"從……選擇答案","examples":[{"en":"Students choose their answers from the box below the summary.","zh":"學生從摘要下方的方框中選擇答案。"},{"en":"To choose your answers from a place means to select only from the options provided there.","zh":"choose your answers from a place 指只從該處提供的選項中選擇。"},{"en":"Students must choose their answers from the word list, not invent their own words.","zh":"學生必須從詞語列表中選擇答案，而不是自行創造詞語。"},{"en":"This instruction limits the possible answers and helps students focus.","zh":"這項指示限制可能答案，幫助學生集中。"},{"en":"This phrase tells candidates where the answer options are.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生答案選項在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"more words than you will need","meaning":"詞語比所需更多","examples":[{"en":"There are more words than you will need to fill the gaps.","zh":"詞語比你填補空格所需的更多。"},{"en":"More words than you will need means the list contains extra options that will not be used.","zh":"more words than you will need 指列表包含不會被使用的額外選項。"},{"en":"In a vocabulary exercise, there may be more words than you will need so guessing becomes harder.","zh":"在詞彙練習中，詞語可能比所需更多，令猜答案更困難。"},{"en":"Extra words test whether students understand meaning, not just word order.","zh":"額外詞語測試學生是否理解意思，而不只是詞序。"},{"en":"This phrase warns students that not every option is correct.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生不是每個選項都正確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"fill the gaps","meaning":"填補空格","examples":[{"en":"Students use suitable words to fill the gaps.","zh":"學生使用合適詞語填補空格。"},{"en":"To fill the gaps means to put missing words or information into empty spaces.","zh":"fill the gaps 指把缺失詞語或資料放入空白位置。"},{"en":"A student fills the gaps in a sentence by choosing the correct verb form.","zh":"學生透過選擇正確動詞形式來填補句子空格。"},{"en":"Gap-filling tasks test grammar, meaning, and attention to detail.","zh":"填空任務測試文法、意思和細節注意力。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in language exercises.","zh":"這個短語常見於語言練習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"for four centuries","meaning":"四個世紀以來","examples":[{"en":"For four centuries, mapmakers have tried to improve world maps.","zh":"四個世紀以來，地圖製作者一直嘗試改善世界地圖。"},{"en":"For four centuries means during a period of four hundred years.","zh":"for four centuries 指在四百年的期間內。"},{"en":"For four centuries, some families have passed down the same farming methods.","zh":"四個世紀以來，有些家族一直傳承相同耕作方法。"},{"en":"A problem lasting for four centuries is clearly difficult to solve completely.","zh":"持續四個世紀的問題，顯然很難完全解決。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a long historical time span.","zh":"這個短語給出很長的歷史時間跨度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"convert information onto","meaning":"將資料轉換到……上","examples":[{"en":"Mapmakers convert three-dimensional information onto a two-dimensional plane.","zh":"地圖製作者將三維資料轉換到二維平面上。"},{"en":"To convert information onto a surface means to change it into a form that can be shown there.","zh":"convert information onto a surface 指把資料改成可在該表面顯示的形式。"},{"en":"A teacher may convert survey results onto a chart so students can understand them quickly.","zh":"老師可能把調查結果轉換到圖表上，讓學生快速理解。"},{"en":"When information is converted, some details may be simplified.","zh":"當資料被轉換，一些細節可能被簡化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing information from one format to another.","zh":"這個短語描述把資料從一種格式改成另一種格式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"as accurately as possible","meaning":"盡可能準確地","examples":[{"en":"Mapmakers try to represent the world as accurately as possible.","zh":"地圖製作者嘗試盡可能準確地呈現世界。"},{"en":"As accurately as possible means with the highest level of accuracy that the situation allows.","zh":"as accurately as possible 指在情況允許下以最高準確度。"},{"en":"Students should copy the quotation as accurately as possible in a reading answer.","zh":"學生在閱讀答案中應盡可能準確地抄寫引文。"},{"en":"When perfection is impossible, people still try to be as accurate as possible.","zh":"當完美不可能時，人們仍會嘗試盡可能準確。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses careful effort toward accuracy.","zh":"這個短語強調為準確而作出的仔細努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"two-dimensional plane","meaning":"二維平面","examples":[{"en":"A map is drawn on a two-dimensional plane.","zh":"地圖繪製在二維平面上。"},{"en":"A two-dimensional plane is a flat surface with length and width but no depth.","zh":"two-dimensional plane 指有長度和闊度但沒有深度的平面。"},{"en":"A worksheet, screen, or whiteboard can act as a two-dimensional plane.","zh":"工作紙、螢幕或白板都可以作為二維平面。"},{"en":"Representing a round object on a two-dimensional plane creates distortion.","zh":"在二維平面上呈現圓形物件會產生扭曲。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the flat surface used for drawings or maps.","zh":"這個短語指用於圖畫或地圖的平面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"each method of projection","meaning":"每種投影方法","examples":[{"en":"Each method of projection involves a compromise.","zh":"每種投影方法都涉及妥協。"},{"en":"Each method of projection means every way of turning the globe into a flat map.","zh":"each method of projection 指每一種把地球儀變成平面地圖的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may show each method of projection so students can compare its strengths and weaknesses.","zh":"老師可能展示每種投影方法，讓學生比較其優缺點。"},{"en":"Different projection methods preserve different features and sacrifice others.","zh":"不同投影方法保留不同特徵，也犧牲其他特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the various systems used in map-making.","zh":"這個短語指製圖中使用的各種系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"involve a compromise","meaning":"涉及妥協","examples":[{"en":"Every map projection involves a compromise.","zh":"每種地圖投影都涉及妥協。"},{"en":"To involve a compromise means to require a trade-off between two or more desirable things.","zh":"involve a compromise 指需要在兩個或多個理想事物之間作出取捨。"},{"en":"Choosing a school may involve a compromise between distance, fees, and teaching quality.","zh":"選學校可能涉及距離、學費和教學質素之間的妥協。"},{"en":"Map projections involve compromise because no flat map can preserve everything perfectly.","zh":"地圖投影涉及妥協，因為沒有平面地圖可以完美保留一切。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a situation where one benefit is gained by giving up another.","zh":"這個短語描述透過放棄一項好處來取得另一項好處的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"misrepresent the relative size of","meaning":"錯誤呈現……的相對大小","examples":[{"en":"The Mercator projection misrepresents the relative size of countries.","zh":"麥卡托投影錯誤呈現國家的相對大小。"},{"en":"To misrepresent the relative size of something means to show its size incorrectly compared with other things.","zh":"misrepresent the relative size of something 指把某物與其他事物相比的大小顯示錯誤。"},{"en":"A pie chart can misrepresent the relative size of expenses if the sections are drawn wrongly.","zh":"如果扇形區域畫錯，圓形圖可以錯誤呈現開支的相對大小。"},{"en":"Misrepresenting relative size can make small things look important and large things look minor.","zh":"錯誤呈現相對大小可以令小事看似重要，大事看似次要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes misleading comparison of size.","zh":"這個短語描述具誤導性的大小比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"avoid this distortion","meaning":"避免這種扭曲","examples":[{"en":"Other cartographers bent the grid lines to avoid this distortion.","zh":"其他地圖繪製者彎曲網格線以避免這種扭曲。"},{"en":"To avoid this distortion means to prevent this particular kind of inaccurate shape or size change.","zh":"avoid this distortion 指防止這種特定的不準確形狀或大小改變。"},{"en":"A designer may avoid distortion by keeping a photo’s original proportions.","zh":"設計師可能透過保持照片原有比例來避免扭曲。"},{"en":"Avoiding one distortion may create another problem elsewhere.","zh":"避免一種扭曲可能在其他地方造成另一個問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trying to remove a specific visual error.","zh":"這個短語描述嘗試移除某個具體視覺錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"round the lines of","meaning":"將……的線條彎曲","examples":[{"en":"Some cartographers rounded the lines of latitude and longitude.","zh":"有些地圖繪製者將經緯線彎曲。"},{"en":"To round the lines of something means to make straight lines curved or circular.","zh":"round the lines of something 指把直線變成彎曲或圓弧形。"},{"en":"A designer may round the lines of a logo to make it look softer.","zh":"設計師可能將標誌的線條彎曲，使它看起來較柔和。"},{"en":"Rounding map lines can reduce some distortions but make direction harder to judge.","zh":"彎曲地圖線條可以減少某些扭曲，但令方向較難判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing straight lines into curved ones.","zh":"這個短語描述把直線變成曲線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"present a first-world perspective","meaning":"呈現第一世界視角","examples":[{"en":"Peters felt that such maps presented a first-world perspective.","zh":"Peters 覺得這類地圖呈現第一世界視角。"},{"en":"To present a first-world perspective means to show the world mainly from the viewpoint of richer industrialised countries.","zh":"present a first-world perspective 指主要從較富裕工業化國家的視角呈現世界。"},{"en":"A news report may present a first-world perspective if it ignores how poorer countries experience the same problem.","zh":"如果新聞報道忽視較貧窮國家如何經歷同一問題，就可能呈現第一世界視角。"},{"en":"Such a perspective can make wealthy countries seem more central or important.","zh":"這種視角可以令富裕國家看起來更中心或更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bias toward rich countries’ viewpoints.","zh":"這個短語描述偏向富裕國家觀點的偏見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"enable someone to","meaning":"使某人能夠","examples":[{"en":"An equal-area map enables viewers to compare country sizes.","zh":"等積地圖使觀眾能夠比較國家大小。"},{"en":"To enable someone to do something means to make it possible for them to do it.","zh":"enable someone to do something 指使某人可以做某事。"},{"en":"Clear subtitles enable students to understand a foreign documentary.","zh":"清楚字幕使學生能夠理解外國紀錄片。"},{"en":"Good tools enable people to complete tasks more accurately.","zh":"好工具使人們能夠更準確完成任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving someone the ability or opportunity to act.","zh":"這個短語描述給予某人能力或機會去行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"compare the size of","meaning":"比較……的大小","examples":[{"en":"The Peters projection enables us to compare the size of one country with another.","zh":"彼得斯投影使我們能夠比較一個國家與另一個國家的大小。"},{"en":"To compare the size of two things means to judge which is larger, smaller, or similar in area or amount.","zh":"compare the size of two things 指判斷兩者在面積或數量上哪個較大、較小或相似。"},{"en":"Students compare the size of two classrooms before deciding where to hold the meeting.","zh":"學生在決定在哪裡開會前，會比較兩間課室的大小。"},{"en":"Accurate comparison helps people avoid false impressions.","zh":"準確比較幫助人避免錯誤印象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes judging size through comparison.","zh":"這個短語描述透過比較判斷大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"match the map projections with","meaning":"將地圖投影與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match the map projections with the listed characteristics.","zh":"學生將地圖投影與列出的特徵配對。"},{"en":"To match the map projections with characteristics means to connect each projection to the description that fits it.","zh":"match the map projections with characteristics 指把每種投影連接到符合它的描述。"},{"en":"In a reading exercise, students may match vocabulary items with their meanings.","zh":"在閱讀練習中，學生可能把詞彙項目與其意思配對。"},{"en":"Matching tasks test whether students can recognise details accurately.","zh":"配對題測試學生是否能準確辨認細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pairing items with correct descriptions.","zh":"這個短語描述把項目與正確描述配對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"projection types","meaning":"投影類型","examples":[{"en":"The task asks students to identify different projection types.","zh":"任務要求學生辨認不同投影類型。"},{"en":"Projection types are different methods for representing the round earth on a flat map.","zh":"projection types 指在平面地圖上呈現圓形地球的不同方法。"},{"en":"Students may compare projection types by looking at area, shape, and direction.","zh":"學生可能透過觀察面積、形狀和方向來比較投影類型。"},{"en":"Each projection type solves some problems and creates others.","zh":"每種投影類型都解決一些問題，也造成另一些問題。"},{"en":"This phrase categorises different map-making methods.","zh":"這個短語把不同製圖方法分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"characteristics listed below","meaning":"以下列出的特徵","examples":[{"en":"Students match projections with the characteristics listed below.","zh":"學生將投影與以下列出的特徵配對。"},{"en":"Characteristics listed below are the features or descriptions provided under the question.","zh":"characteristics listed below 指題目下方提供的特徵或描述。"},{"en":"In a worksheet, students may match animals with the characteristics listed below each picture.","zh":"在工作紙中，學生可能把動物與每幅圖下方列出的特徵配對。"},{"en":"Reading all listed characteristics first helps avoid careless matching.","zh":"先閱讀所有列出的特徵，有助避免粗心配對。"},{"en":"This phrase directs attention to the options provided later.","zh":"這個短語把注意力指向後面提供的選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"designed for the needs of","meaning":"為……的需要而設計","examples":[{"en":"The Mercator projection was designed for the needs of early navigators.","zh":"麥卡托投影是為早期航海家的需要而設計。"},{"en":"Designed for the needs of a group means made to serve what that group requires.","zh":"designed for the needs of a group 指被製作來服務該群體的需要。"},{"en":"A school app should be designed for the needs of students, parents, and teachers.","zh":"學校應用程式應為學生、家長和老師的需要而設計。"},{"en":"A design made for one group may not suit another group equally well.","zh":"為某群體設計的東西，未必同樣適合另一群體。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the intended users of a design.","zh":"這個短語解釋設計的目標使用者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"make Europe seem larger than it is","meaning":"令歐洲看起來比實際更大","examples":[{"en":"Some projections make Europe seem larger than it is.","zh":"有些投影令歐洲看起來比實際更大。"},{"en":"To make Europe seem larger than it is means to show Europe as bigger than its true area.","zh":"make Europe seem larger than it is 指把歐洲顯示得比其真實面積更大。"},{"en":"A misleading chart can make a small expense seem larger than it is.","zh":"具誤導性的圖表可以令小開支看起來比實際更大。"},{"en":"Making one region look larger can change how viewers judge importance.","zh":"令一個地區看起來更大，可以改變觀眾如何判斷其重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distortion that affects perception of size.","zh":"這個短語描述影響大小感知的扭曲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"maximum distortions","meaning":"最大扭曲","examples":[{"en":"The maximum distortions occur near the poles.","zh":"最大扭曲出現在兩極附近。"},{"en":"Maximum distortions are the largest or most extreme changes from the true shape or size.","zh":"maximum distortions 指與真實形狀或大小相比最大或最極端的改變。"},{"en":"In a stretched photo, maximum distortions may appear at the edges.","zh":"在被拉伸的照片中，最大扭曲可能出現在邊緣。"},{"en":"Knowing where maximum distortions occur helps users read a map more carefully.","zh":"知道最大扭曲出現在哪裡，有助使用者更小心閱讀地圖。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where inaccuracy is greatest.","zh":"這個短語指出不準確程度最大的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"at the poles","meaning":"在兩極","examples":[{"en":"Some projections show maximum distortion at the poles.","zh":"有些投影在兩極顯示最大扭曲。"},{"en":"At the poles means at the North Pole and South Pole.","zh":"at the poles 指在北極和南極。"},{"en":"Temperatures at the poles are often much colder than near the equator.","zh":"兩極的氣溫通常比赤道附近低得多。"},{"en":"Map distortion at the poles occurs because flat maps struggle with the earth’s curved ends.","zh":"兩極的地圖扭曲出現，是因為平面地圖難以處理地球彎曲的兩端。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the polar locations of the earth.","zh":"這個短語指出地球的極地位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"maintain greatest accuracy","meaning":"保持最大準確度","examples":[{"en":"The Peters projection maintains greatest accuracy at 45 degrees latitude.","zh":"彼得斯投影在 45 度緯線保持最大準確度。"},{"en":"To maintain greatest accuracy means to keep the highest level of correctness in a particular area or feature.","zh":"maintain greatest accuracy 指在某特定區域或特徵中保持最高正確度。"},{"en":"A camera may maintain greatest accuracy near the centre of the image.","zh":"相機可能在圖像中心附近保持最大準確度。"},{"en":"Mapmakers decide where a projection should maintain greatest accuracy based on their priorities.","zh":"地圖製作者根據自己的優先事項，決定投影應在哪裡保持最大準確度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preserving the best accuracy in a chosen place.","zh":"這個短語描述在所選位置保留最佳準確性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"most distort the position of","meaning":"最大程度扭曲……的位置","examples":[{"en":"One projection most distorts the position of the equator.","zh":"一種投影最大程度扭曲赤道的位置。"},{"en":"To most distort the position of something means to change its location more than other options do.","zh":"most distort the position of something 指比其他選項更大程度改變某物位置。"},{"en":"A badly printed floor plan may most distort the position of the emergency exit.","zh":"印刷差的平面圖可能最大程度扭曲緊急出口的位置。"},{"en":"Distorting position can mislead users even if shape or size looks familiar.","zh":"即使形狀或大小看起來熟悉，位置扭曲仍可以誤導使用者。"},{"en":"This phrase compares which option causes the greatest location error.","zh":"這個短語比較哪個選項造成最大位置錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the position of the equator","meaning":"赤道的位置","examples":[{"en":"The position of the equator can be distorted on a map.","zh":"赤道的位置可以在地圖上被扭曲。"},{"en":"The position of the equator means where the equator appears on a map or model.","zh":"the position of the equator 指赤道在地圖或模型上出現的位置。"},{"en":"Students may draw a line across the middle of a globe to understand the position of the equator.","zh":"學生可能在地球儀中間畫一條線，以理解赤道的位置。"},{"en":"If the equator is shown too low, the northern hemisphere may look more dominant.","zh":"如果赤道被顯示得太低，北半球可能看起來更具支配性。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the placement of the earth’s central latitude line.","zh":"這個短語著重地球中央緯線的放置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"more accurately represent","meaning":"更準確地呈現","examples":[{"en":"The Aitoff projection more accurately represents country shapes and sizes.","zh":"艾托夫投影更準確地呈現國家形狀和大小。"},{"en":"To more accurately represent something means to show it in a way that is closer to reality.","zh":"more accurately represent something 指以更接近現實的方式顯示某事。"},{"en":"A well-labelled chart can more accurately represent students’ reading progress.","zh":"標示清楚的圖表可以更準確地呈現學生閱讀進度。"},{"en":"More accurate representation reduces misunderstanding.","zh":"更準確的呈現可以減少誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improvement in how information is shown.","zh":"這個短語描述資訊顯示方式的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"country shapes and sizes","meaning":"國家形狀和大小","examples":[{"en":"Some projections represent country shapes and sizes better than others.","zh":"有些投影比其他投影更好地呈現國家形狀和大小。"},{"en":"Country shapes and sizes are the outlines and land areas of countries on a map.","zh":"country shapes and sizes 指地圖上國家的輪廓和土地面積。"},{"en":"Students compare country shapes and sizes to see why some maps look unfamiliar.","zh":"學生比較國家形狀和大小，以了解為何有些地圖看起來陌生。"},{"en":"A projection may show size well but shape poorly, or the other way round.","zh":"一種投影可能很好地顯示大小，但差劣地顯示形狀，或相反。"},{"en":"This phrase combines two major concerns in map-making.","zh":"這個短語結合製圖中的兩個主要關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"choose one drawing to match","meaning":"選一幅圖來配對","examples":[{"en":"Students choose one drawing to match each projection type.","zh":"學生為每種投影類型選一幅圖來配對。"},{"en":"To choose one drawing to match something means to select the picture that corresponds to it.","zh":"choose one drawing to match something 指選出與某物相對應的圖片。"},{"en":"In a science worksheet, students may choose one drawing to match each animal label.","zh":"在科學工作紙中，學生可能為每個動物標籤選一幅圖來配對。"},{"en":"This task checks whether students can recognise visual features, not just words.","zh":"這項任務檢查學生是否能辨認視覺特徵，而不只是文字。"},{"en":"This phrase describes selecting the correct visual option.","zh":"這個短語描述選出正確視覺選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"more drawings than names","meaning":"圖像比名稱多","examples":[{"en":"There are more drawings than names in the question.","zh":"題目中的圖像比名稱多。"},{"en":"More drawings than names means the task provides extra pictures that will not all be used.","zh":"more drawings than names 指任務提供額外圖片，不會全部用上。"},{"en":"A matching exercise may have more pictures than words to make guessing harder.","zh":"配對練習可能有比詞語更多的圖片，以令猜測更困難。"},{"en":"Extra drawings force students to compare details carefully.","zh":"額外圖像迫使學生仔細比較細節。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that some visual options are distractors.","zh":"這個短語提醒有些視覺選項是干擾項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"you will not use all of them","meaning":"你不會全部用上","examples":[{"en":"Students will not use all of the drawings.","zh":"學生不會全部用上這些圖像。"},{"en":"You will not use all of them means some options are extra and should be left unused.","zh":"you will not use all of them 指有些選項是額外的，應留空不用。"},{"en":"In a word-box exercise, students will not use all of the words.","zh":"在詞語方框練習中，學生不會全部用上所有詞語。"},{"en":"This instruction prevents students from forcing every option into an answer.","zh":"這項指示防止學生硬把每個選項塞進答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in exam tasks with distractors.","zh":"這個短語常見於有干擾項的考試題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the main point made by","meaning":"作者提出的主要觀點","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for the main point made by the writer.","zh":"題目問作者提出的主要觀點。"},{"en":"The main point made by someone is the central idea they want readers to understand.","zh":"main point made by someone 指某人希望讀者理解的中心思想。"},{"en":"In an essay, students should identify the main point made by each paragraph before summarising it.","zh":"在作文中，學生應先找出每段提出的主要觀點，再作摘要。"},{"en":"Finding the main point prevents students from being distracted by minor examples.","zh":"找出主要觀點可防止學生被次要例子分散注意。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the writer’s central message.","zh":"這個短語著重作者的中心訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"objective","meaning":"客觀的","examples":[{"en":"The passage suggests that maps are not completely objective.","zh":"文章暗示地圖並非完全客觀。"},{"en":"Objective means based on facts rather than personal feelings, opinions, or bias.","zh":"objective 指基於事實，而不是個人感受、意見或偏見。"},{"en":"A fair exam mark should be as objective as possible.","zh":"公平的考試分數應盡可能客觀。"},{"en":"Something may look objective but still be shaped by hidden choices.","zh":"某事可能看起來客觀，但仍受隱藏選擇塑造。"},{"en":"This word contrasts neutral fact with personal viewpoint.","zh":"這個詞把中立事實與個人觀點作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"not objective","meaning":"並非客觀","examples":[{"en":"The writer wants readers to understand that maps are not objective.","zh":"作者希望讀者理解地圖並非客觀。"},{"en":"Not objective means influenced by choices, opinions, or assumptions rather than being purely neutral.","zh":"not objective 指受到選擇、意見或假設影響，而不是純粹中立。"},{"en":"A school report is not objective if it praises one class while ignoring the same problems in another.","zh":"如果學校報告讚揚一班，卻忽視另一班相同問題，它就並非客觀。"},{"en":"Maps are not objective when projection choices change how viewers judge the world.","zh":"當投影選擇改變觀眾如何判斷世界，地圖就並非客觀。"},{"en":"This phrase challenges the idea that a source simply shows facts.","zh":"這個短語挑戰資料來源只是展示事實的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the importance of latitude and longitude","meaning":"經緯度的重要性","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the importance of latitude and longitude in map-making.","zh":"文章討論經緯度在地圖製作中的重要性。"},{"en":"The importance of latitude and longitude is their role in locating places and shaping map grids.","zh":"importance of latitude and longitude 指它們在定位地方和塑造地圖網格中的作用。"},{"en":"Students learn the importance of latitude and longitude when finding cities on a world map.","zh":"學生在世界地圖上尋找城市時，會學到經緯度的重要性。"},{"en":"Without latitude and longitude, global location would be much harder to describe accurately.","zh":"沒有經緯度，全球位置會更難準確描述。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why map grid lines matter.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何地圖網格線重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"understand map-making","meaning":"了解地圖製作","examples":[{"en":"Readers need to understand map-making as a process involving choices.","zh":"讀者需要了解地圖製作是一個涉及選擇的過程。"},{"en":"To understand map-making means to know how maps are designed, simplified, and shaped by decisions.","zh":"understand map-making 指知道地圖如何被設計、簡化並受決定塑造。"},{"en":"Students understand map-making better when they compare a globe with several flat maps.","zh":"當學生比較地球儀與幾張平面地圖，他們會更了解地圖製作。"},{"en":"Understanding map-making helps people question what maps include, distort, or emphasise.","zh":"了解地圖製作幫助人質疑地圖包括、扭曲或強調甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning the process behind maps.","zh":"這個短語描述學習地圖背後的製作過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"understand maps","meaning":"了解地圖","examples":[{"en":"Readers should understand that maps express viewpoints.","zh":"讀者應了解地圖會表達觀點。"},{"en":"To understand maps means to read them critically, not just look at their colours and labels.","zh":"understand maps 指批判地閱讀地圖，而不只是看顏色和標籤。"},{"en":"Students understand maps better when they ask what has been distorted and why.","zh":"當學生問甚麼被扭曲以及為何被扭曲，他們就更了解地圖。"},{"en":"Understanding maps helps travellers, learners, and citizens avoid being misled.","zh":"了解地圖幫助旅客、學習者和公民避免被誤導。"},{"en":"This phrase means knowing how maps communicate information and perspective.","zh":"這個短語指知道地圖如何傳達資訊和視角。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"latitude and longitude","meaning":"緯度和經度","examples":[{"en":"Latitude and longitude are central to the way maps represent the world.","zh":"緯度和經度是地圖呈現世界方式的核心。"},{"en":"Latitude and longitude are the horizontal and vertical coordinate lines used to locate places on earth.","zh":"latitude and longitude 指用來定位地球上地方的橫向和縱向座標線。"},{"en":"A pilot uses latitude and longitude to identify exact positions during a flight.","zh":"飛機師在飛行期間使用緯度和經度識別精確位置。"},{"en":"These coordinates make global location more precise than ordinary place names alone.","zh":"這些座標令全球定位比單靠普通地名更精確。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the basic coordinate system of geography.","zh":"這個短語指地理中的基本座標系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"perspective","meaning":"角度；視角","examples":[{"en":"A map can present a particular perspective on the world.","zh":"地圖可以呈現對世界的某種特定視角。"},{"en":"Perspective is a way of seeing, interpreting, or presenting something.","zh":"perspective 指看待、詮釋或呈現某事的方式。"},{"en":"A student’s perspective on homework may differ from a teacher’s perspective.","zh":"學生對功課的視角可能不同於老師的視角。"},{"en":"Different perspectives can highlight different problems and hide others.","zh":"不同視角可以突出不同問題，也可以隱藏其他問題。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing viewpoint and interpretation.","zh":"這個詞在討論觀點和詮釋時很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"axis","meaning":"軸線；軸向","examples":[{"en":"Fidelity of axis helps a map show north, south, east and west correctly.","zh":"軸向保真度幫助地圖正確顯示東南西北。"},{"en":"An axis is an imaginary line used to organise direction, position, or rotation.","zh":"axis 指用來組織方向、位置或旋轉的想像線。"},{"en":"The earth turns around its axis, which runs between the North and South Poles.","zh":"地球圍繞其軸線轉動，而這條軸線連接南北兩極。"},{"en":"On a map, axes help viewers understand direction and alignment.","zh":"在地圖上，軸線幫助觀眾理解方向和排列。"},{"en":"This word is used in geography, mathematics, and science.","zh":"這個詞用於地理、數學和科學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"angle","meaning":"角度","examples":[{"en":"Fidelity of angle helps navigators follow compass directions.","zh":"角度保真度幫助航海家跟隨羅盤方向。"},{"en":"An angle is the space or turn between two lines or directions.","zh":"angle 指兩條線或兩個方向之間的空間或轉向。"},{"en":"Students measure an angle with a protractor in a geometry lesson.","zh":"學生在幾何課用量角器量度角度。"},{"en":"Preserving angle can help with navigation even if size becomes distorted.","zh":"保留角度可以幫助導航，即使大小變得扭曲。"},{"en":"This word is important in geometry and map projection.","zh":"這個詞在幾何和地圖投影中很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"direction","meaning":"方向","examples":[{"en":"The Mercator projection is useful because it preserves direction.","zh":"麥卡托投影有用，因為它保留方向。"},{"en":"Direction means the way in which something points or moves, such as north or south-west.","zh":"direction 指某物指向或移動的方式，例如北方或西南方。"},{"en":"A bus driver needs clear direction to reach the correct stop.","zh":"巴士司機需要清楚方向才能到達正確車站。"},{"en":"Preserving direction is important when a map is used for travel.","zh":"當地圖用於旅行時，保留方向很重要。"},{"en":"This word describes orientation or route.","zh":"這個詞描述方位或路線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"projection","meaning":"投影","examples":[{"en":"Every projection makes some form of compromise.","zh":"每種投影都會作出某種妥協。"},{"en":"A projection is a method of showing the round earth on a flat map.","zh":"projection 指在平面地圖上顯示圓形地球的方法。"},{"en":"Students compare different projections to see how each one changes the world’s appearance.","zh":"學生比較不同投影，以看出每種如何改變世界外觀。"},{"en":"A projection may preserve area, direction, or shape, but not all perfectly at once.","zh":"投影可能保留面積、方向或形狀，但不能同時完美保留所有。"},{"en":"This word names the map-making method behind a flat world map.","zh":"這個詞命名平面世界地圖背後的製圖方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"distances","meaning":"距離","examples":[{"en":"Distances between lines of latitude increase near the poles.","zh":"緯線之間的距離在兩極附近增加。"},{"en":"Distances are the amounts of space between places or objects.","zh":"distances 指地方或物件之間的空間量。"},{"en":"A map scale helps students estimate distances between cities.","zh":"地圖比例尺幫助學生估計城市之間的距離。"},{"en":"If distances are shown unevenly, a map may make some regions appear larger.","zh":"如果距離顯示得不均，地圖可能令某些地區看起來更大。"},{"en":"This word is central to understanding space and measurement.","zh":"這個詞是理解空間和量度的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"estimate","meaning":"估計","examples":[{"en":"A map may help users estimate the relative positions of countries.","zh":"地圖可能幫助使用者估計國家的相對位置。"},{"en":"To estimate means to make a reasonable guess based on available information.","zh":"estimate 指根據已有資料作合理猜測。"},{"en":"A student may estimate the answer before using a calculator to check it.","zh":"學生可能先估計答案，再用計算機檢查。"},{"en":"Maps help people estimate distance and direction, but not always perfectly.","zh":"地圖幫助人估計距離和方向，但不一定完美。"},{"en":"This word describes careful guessing rather than exact calculation.","zh":"這個詞描述仔細猜測，而不是精確計算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"model","meaning":"模型","examples":[{"en":"A globe is a more accurate model of the earth than a flat map.","zh":"地球儀是比平面地圖更準確的地球模型。"},{"en":"A model is a simplified representation used to understand a real object, system, or idea.","zh":"model 指用來理解真實物件、系統或想法的簡化呈現。"},{"en":"A science class may use a model of the solar system to show how planets move.","zh":"科學課可能使用太陽系模型來顯示行星如何運行。"},{"en":"Models help learning, but they may leave out details.","zh":"模型有助學習，但可能省略細節。"},{"en":"This word refers to a representation, not the real thing itself.","zh":"這個詞指呈現物，而不是真實事物本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"accurately","meaning":"準確地","examples":[{"en":"Mapmakers try to represent the earth accurately on a flat plane.","zh":"地圖製作者嘗試在平面上準確地呈現地球。"},{"en":"Accurately means correctly and closely matching the truth.","zh":"accurately 指正確並接近真相。"},{"en":"Students should copy numbers accurately when completing a table.","zh":"學生完成表格時，應準確地抄寫數字。"},{"en":"If information is not recorded accurately, later answers may be wrong.","zh":"如果資料沒有被準確記錄，之後答案可能錯誤。"},{"en":"This word describes correctness in detail.","zh":"這個詞描述細節上的正確性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"judge","meaning":"判斷","examples":[{"en":"Some projections make it harder to judge compass directions.","zh":"有些投影令判斷羅盤方向更困難。"},{"en":"To judge means to decide or estimate something after looking at evidence or details.","zh":"judge 指在查看證據或細節後作決定或估計。"},{"en":"A teacher may judge whether students understand by reading their examples.","zh":"老師可能透過閱讀學生例句，判斷他們是否理解。"},{"en":"Maps help users judge direction, distance, and relative size.","zh":"地圖幫助使用者判斷方向、距離和相對大小。"},{"en":"This word describes forming a conclusion.","zh":"這個詞描述形成結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"change","meaning":"改變","examples":[{"en":"Different projections change the apparent size and shape of countries.","zh":"不同投影會改變國家看起來的大小和形狀。"},{"en":"To change something means to make it different from before.","zh":"change something 指使某事物變得不同於以前。"},{"en":"A new bus route can change how students travel to school.","zh":"新巴士路線可以改變學生上學方式。"},{"en":"In maps, small design choices can change how viewers understand the world.","zh":"在地圖中，小小設計選擇可以改變觀眾如何理解世界。"},{"en":"This word describes alteration in form, meaning, or result.","zh":"這個詞描述形式、意思或結果上的改動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 74 - Map wars.pdf","sourcePage":21}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 75":[{"front":"team-based learning","meaning":"團隊為本學習","examples":[{"en":"Team-based learning prepares students for collaborative work.","zh":"團隊為本學習讓學生準備好面對協作工作。"},{"en":"Team-based learning is an approach in which students learn by working together in organised groups.","zh":"團隊為本學習是一種讓學生透過有組織小組合作來學習的方法。"},{"en":"In a science class, team-based learning may ask students to solve a lab problem together.","zh":"在科學課中，團隊為本學習可能要求學生一起解決實驗室問題。"},{"en":"Team-based learning can build communication skills because students must explain ideas and listen to others.","zh":"團隊為本學習可以培養溝通技巧，因為學生必須解釋想法並聆聽他人。"},{"en":"It is different from silent individual study because the group becomes part of the learning process.","zh":"它不同於安靜的個人學習，因為小組本身成為學習過程的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"globalisation of information technology","meaning":"資訊科技全球化","examples":[{"en":"The globalisation of information technology has changed the modern workplace.","zh":"資訊科技全球化改變了現代職場。"},{"en":"The globalisation of information technology means IT tools and digital systems are now used across countries and industries.","zh":"資訊科技全球化指資訊科技工具和數碼系統如今在不同國家和行業中使用。"},{"en":"A small company can serve overseas clients because of the globalisation of information technology.","zh":"小公司可以服務海外客戶，是因為資訊科技全球化。"},{"en":"This globalisation creates new jobs, but it also makes workers need stronger digital skills.","zh":"這種全球化創造新工作，但也令工人需要更強數碼技能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how technology has become international, not limited to one country.","zh":"這個短語描述科技變得國際化，而不是局限於單一國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"worldwide access to","meaning":"全球都可接觸到……","examples":[{"en":"Worldwide access to the Internet has affected all areas of learning.","zh":"全球都可接觸到互聯網，影響了各個學習領域。"},{"en":"Worldwide access to something means people in many parts of the world can use or reach it.","zh":"worldwide access to something 指世界許多地方的人都可以使用或接觸到某物。"},{"en":"Worldwide access to online lessons allows students in remote towns to study with overseas teachers.","zh":"全球都可接觸到網上課程，讓偏遠城鎮學生能向海外老師學習。"},{"en":"When people have worldwide access to information, learning becomes faster and less limited by place.","zh":"當人們全球都可接觸到資訊，學習會變得更快，也較少受地點限制。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses broad global availability.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛的全球可用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"all areas of learning","meaning":"各個學習領域","examples":[{"en":"People from all areas of learning now use information technology.","zh":"來自各個學習領域的人現在都使用資訊科技。"},{"en":"All areas of learning means every subject, field, or type of study.","zh":"all areas of learning 指每個學科、領域或學習類型。"},{"en":"Students use tablets in all areas of learning, from languages to science and art.","zh":"學生在各個學習領域都使用平板電腦，由語文到科學和藝術都是如此。"},{"en":"When technology spreads across all areas of learning, teachers must rethink how lessons are delivered.","zh":"當科技擴展到各個學習領域，老師必須重新思考課堂如何傳遞。"},{"en":"The phrase means learning as a whole, not just one school subject.","zh":"這個短語指整體學習，而不是單一學科。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"find themselves doing something","meaning":"發現自己正在做某事","examples":[{"en":"Many people find themselves using information technology in the workplace.","zh":"許多人發現自己正在職場上使用資訊科技。"},{"en":"To find yourself doing something means to realise that you are doing it, often because circumstances have changed.","zh":"find yourself doing something 指你意識到自己正在做某事，通常因為環境已經改變。"},{"en":"A shy student may find herself speaking English more often after joining a group project.","zh":"害羞學生加入小組項目後，可能發現自己更常說英語。"},{"en":"When workplaces become digital, employees may find themselves learning new software quickly.","zh":"當職場變得數碼化，員工可能發現自己正在快速學習新軟件。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests an unexpected or gradual change in behaviour.","zh":"這個短語常暗示行為上出乎意料或逐漸出現的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"some form of","meaning":"某種形式的……","examples":[{"en":"Workers often use some form of information technology.","zh":"工人通常使用某種形式的資訊科技。"},{"en":"Some form of something means one type or version of it, even if it is simple or different from others.","zh":"some form of something 指某物的一種類型或版本，即使它很簡單或與其他形式不同。"},{"en":"Most students use some form of online learning, such as videos, quizzes, or shared notes.","zh":"大多數學生使用某種形式的網上學習，例如影片、測驗或共享筆記。"},{"en":"When a tool becomes common, people may use some form of it without thinking much about it.","zh":"當工具變得普遍，人們可能不太思考就使用某種形式的它。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when the exact type is not important.","zh":"當具體類型不重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"information technology","meaning":"資訊科技","examples":[{"en":"Information technology is now common in many workplaces.","zh":"資訊科技現在在許多職場都很常見。"},{"en":"Information technology means the use of computers, software, networks, and digital systems to store and share information.","zh":"information technology 指使用電腦、軟件、網絡和數碼系統來儲存和分享資訊。"},{"en":"A school uses information technology when teachers upload homework to an online platform.","zh":"當老師把功課上載到網上平台，學校就是在使用資訊科技。"},{"en":"Information technology improves speed, but it also requires workers to learn new skills.","zh":"資訊科技提高速度，但也要求工人學習新技能。"},{"en":"The phrase is often shortened to IT.","zh":"這個短語常縮寫為 IT。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the workplace","meaning":"在職場上","examples":[{"en":"Many graduates need information technology skills in the workplace.","zh":"許多畢業生在職場上需要資訊科技技能。"},{"en":"In the workplace means in a job, office, company, or working environment.","zh":"in the workplace 指在工作、辦公室、公司或工作環境中。"},{"en":"In the workplace, employees often need to write emails clearly and attend meetings on time.","zh":"在職場上，員工通常需要清楚寫電郵並準時參加會議。"},{"en":"Skills learned at school become valuable when students use them in the workplace.","zh":"學校中學到的技能，當學生在職場上使用時就變得有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts work situations with school, home, or personal life.","zh":"這個短語把工作情境與學校、家庭或個人生活作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the corporate world","meaning":"企業界","examples":[{"en":"The corporate world has seen a boom in the use of IT tools.","zh":"企業界見證資訊科技工具使用急速增長。"},{"en":"The corporate world means the business environment of companies and large organisations.","zh":"the corporate world 指公司和大型機構的商業環境。"},{"en":"A graduate entering the corporate world may need to work in teams, use software, and meet deadlines.","zh":"投身企業界的畢業生可能需要團隊合作、使用軟件和趕上截止日期。"},{"en":"Changes in the corporate world affect what skills universities try to teach.","zh":"企業界的變化會影響大學試圖教授哪些技能。"},{"en":"The phrase usually refers to professional business life.","zh":"這個短語通常指專業商業生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"see a boom in","meaning":"見證……急速增長","examples":[{"en":"The corporate world has seen a boom in IT use.","zh":"企業界見證資訊科技使用急速增長。"},{"en":"To see a boom in something means to experience a rapid and strong increase in it.","zh":"see a boom in something 指經歷某事快速而強勁增加。"},{"en":"A school may see a boom in online applications after it launches a new website.","zh":"學校推出新網站後，可能見證網上申請急速增長。"},{"en":"A boom in technology use creates demand for workers who can manage digital tools.","zh":"科技使用急速增長會創造對能管理數碼工具的工人的需求。"},{"en":"The phrase describes noticeable growth over a period of time.","zh":"這個短語描述一段時間內明顯增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"IT tools","meaning":"資訊科技工具","examples":[{"en":"Many companies rely on IT tools to improve productivity.","zh":"許多公司依賴資訊科技工具提高生產力。"},{"en":"IT tools are digital systems, software, or devices used to complete work more efficiently.","zh":"IT tools 指用來更有效完成工作的數碼系統、軟件或裝置。"},{"en":"A teacher uses IT tools when she marks quizzes online and shares notes through a cloud folder.","zh":"老師網上批改測驗並透過雲端資料夾分享筆記時，就是使用資訊科技工具。"},{"en":"Good IT tools can reduce repeated work and help teams communicate faster.","zh":"良好資訊科技工具可以減少重複工作，並幫助團隊更快溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical technology used for tasks.","zh":"這個短語指用於任務的實用科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"conversely","meaning":"相反","examples":[{"en":"IT use has grown rapidly; conversely, skilled workers are in short supply.","zh":"資訊科技使用快速增長；相反，熟練工人供應不足。"},{"en":"Conversely introduces an opposite or contrasting point.","zh":"conversely 用來引入相反或對比的重點。"},{"en":"Some students enjoy group work; conversely, others prefer quiet individual study.","zh":"有些學生喜歡小組工作；相反，另一些學生偏好安靜的個人學習。"},{"en":"This word helps writers show that two trends move in different directions.","zh":"這個詞幫助作者顯示兩個趨勢方向不同。"},{"en":"It is more formal than simply saying “on the other hand”.","zh":"它比簡單說 “on the other hand” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a shortage of","meaning":"缺乏……","examples":[{"en":"There is a shortage of people with strong IT skills.","zh":"缺乏具備強資訊科技技能的人。"},{"en":"A shortage of something means there is not enough of it to meet demand.","zh":"a shortage of something 指某物不足以滿足需求。"},{"en":"A hospital may face a shortage of nurses during a flu outbreak.","zh":"醫院在流感爆發期間可能面對護士短缺。"},{"en":"A shortage of skilled workers can delay projects and raise salaries.","zh":"熟練工人短缺可以延誤項目並推高薪金。"},{"en":"The phrase describes insufficient supply.","zh":"這個短語描述供應不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"enter the workplace","meaning":"投身職場","examples":[{"en":"Graduates need the skills to enter the workplace confidently.","zh":"畢業生需要技能，才能有信心地投身職場。"},{"en":"To enter the workplace means to begin working in a job or professional environment.","zh":"enter the workplace 指開始在工作或專業環境中工作。"},{"en":"Students who learn interview skills may enter the workplace with more confidence.","zh":"學會面試技巧的學生可能更有信心投身職場。"},{"en":"Universities prepare students to enter the workplace by teaching both knowledge and practical skills.","zh":"大學透過教授知識和實用技能，讓學生準備投身職場。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the transition from study to employment.","zh":"這個短語描述由學習轉向就業的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be productive with","meaning":"在……情況下具生產力","examples":[{"en":"Employers want graduates who can be productive with minimal training.","zh":"僱主希望畢業生能在最少培訓下具生產力。"},{"en":"To be productive with something means to work effectively under that condition or using that support.","zh":"be productive with something 指在某條件下或使用某種支援時有效工作。"},{"en":"A new employee is productive with clear instructions and a simple checklist.","zh":"新員工在有清楚指示和簡單清單的情況下可以具生產力。"},{"en":"If graduates can be productive with little training, companies save time and money.","zh":"如果畢業生能在少量培訓下具生產力，公司就節省時間和金錢。"},{"en":"The phrase links work effectiveness with the amount of help or resources needed.","zh":"這個短語把工作效率與所需幫助或資源量連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"minimal on-the-job training","meaning":"最少量的在職培訓","examples":[{"en":"Companies prefer workers who need minimal on-the-job training.","zh":"公司偏好需要最少量在職培訓的員工。"},{"en":"Minimal on-the-job training means very little training after a person has started working.","zh":"minimal on-the-job training 指一個人開始工作後只需要很少培訓。"},{"en":"A receptionist with strong computer skills may need minimal on-the-job training.","zh":"具備強電腦技能的接待員可能只需要最少量在職培訓。"},{"en":"Employers value this because staff can contribute sooner and require less supervision.","zh":"僱主重視這點，因為員工能更早作出貢獻並需要較少監督。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses readiness for work.","zh":"這個短語強調工作準備度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a recent issue of","meaning":"最近一期……","examples":[{"en":"A recent issue of the New York Times reported on IT recruitment.","zh":"最近一期《紐約時報》報道了資訊科技招聘情況。"},{"en":"A recent issue of a newspaper or magazine means one of its latest published editions.","zh":"a recent issue of a newspaper or magazine 指該報紙或雜誌最新出版的其中一期。"},{"en":"A recent issue of a school newsletter may announce new exam arrangements.","zh":"最近一期學校通訊可能公布新考試安排。"},{"en":"Referring to a recent issue suggests the information is timely.","zh":"提到最近一期，暗示資訊具有時效性。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where and when the reported information appeared.","zh":"這個短語指出所報道資訊出現的來源和時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"look for","meaning":"尋找","examples":[{"en":"Many companies are looking for smart students with IT potential.","zh":"許多公司正在尋找具資訊科技潛力的聰明學生。"},{"en":"To look for someone or something means to search for them because you need or want them.","zh":"look for someone or something 指因需要或想要而尋找某人或某物。"},{"en":"A school may look for volunteers to help younger students read.","zh":"學校可能尋找義工幫助低年級學生閱讀。"},{"en":"Companies look for capable graduates when they expect future growth.","zh":"當公司預期未來增長，它們會尋找有能力的畢業生。"},{"en":"The phrase shows active searching.","zh":"這個短語顯示主動搜尋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"smart students","meaning":"聰明的學生","examples":[{"en":"Companies are looking for smart students with a budding interest in IT.","zh":"公司正在尋找對資訊科技有剛萌芽興趣的聰明學生。"},{"en":"Smart students are students who learn quickly, think clearly, and solve problems well.","zh":"smart students 指學得快、思考清晰並善於解決問題的學生。"},{"en":"A smart student may not know everything yet, but she can learn new software fast.","zh":"聰明學生未必已知道所有事情，但她可以快速學會新軟件。"},{"en":"Employers value smart students because they can grow into skilled workers.","zh":"僱主重視聰明學生，因為他們可以成長為熟練工人。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to ability and learning potential, not only exam marks.","zh":"這個短語指能力和學習潛力，而不只是考試分數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a budding interest in","meaning":"對……剛萌芽的興趣","examples":[{"en":"Some students have a budding interest in information technology.","zh":"有些學生對資訊科技有剛萌芽的興趣。"},{"en":"A budding interest in something is a new interest that is just beginning to grow.","zh":"a budding interest in something 指剛開始增長的新興趣。"},{"en":"A child may show a budding interest in music after learning one simple song.","zh":"孩子學會一首簡單歌曲後，可能對音樂有剛萌芽的興趣。"},{"en":"Employers may train students with a budding interest because they can develop into specialists.","zh":"僱主可能培訓有剛萌芽興趣的學生，因為他們可以發展成專家。"},{"en":"The phrase describes early curiosity, not full expertise.","zh":"這個短語描述早期好奇心，而不是完整專業能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"encourage students to","meaning":"鼓勵學生去……","examples":[{"en":"Companies try to encourage students to attend interviews.","zh":"公司嘗試鼓勵學生參加面試。"},{"en":"To encourage students to do something means to make them feel willing or confident enough to do it.","zh":"encourage students to do something 指令學生願意或有信心去做某事。"},{"en":"Teachers encourage students to speak English by praising effort, not only perfect answers.","zh":"老師透過稱讚努力，而不只是完美答案，鼓勵學生說英語。"},{"en":"Good benefits can encourage students to consider a company seriously.","zh":"良好福利可以鼓勵學生認真考慮一家公司。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests support, motivation, or persuasion.","zh":"這個短語暗示支持、激勵或說服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"attend interviews","meaning":"參加面試","examples":[{"en":"Companies encourage potential recruits to attend interviews.","zh":"公司鼓勵潛在招聘對象參加面試。"},{"en":"To attend interviews means to go to formal meetings where employers ask questions before hiring.","zh":"attend interviews 指前往正式會面，僱主在聘用前提出問題。"},{"en":"A graduate may attend interviews with three companies before choosing a job.","zh":"畢業生可能在選擇工作前參加三家公司面試。"},{"en":"Attending interviews helps applicants learn what employers expect.","zh":"參加面試幫助申請人了解僱主期望。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to participating in job-selection meetings.","zh":"這個短語指參與工作遴選會面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"salary packages","meaning":"薪酬待遇","examples":[{"en":"Some companies offer good salary packages to attract applicants.","zh":"有些公司提供良好薪酬待遇以吸引申請人。"},{"en":"Salary packages are the total pay and benefits offered for a job.","zh":"salary packages 指一份工作提供的總薪金和福利。"},{"en":"A salary package may include monthly pay, bonuses, medical insurance, and paid leave.","zh":"薪酬待遇可能包括月薪、花紅、醫療保險和有薪假期。"},{"en":"Attractive salary packages can help companies compete for talented graduates.","zh":"吸引人的薪酬待遇可以幫助公司競爭有才華的畢業生。"},{"en":"The phrase means more than basic salary alone.","zh":"這個短語意思不只是基本薪金。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"challenging work environments","meaning":"具挑戰性的工作環境","examples":[{"en":"Students may be attracted by challenging work environments.","zh":"學生可能被具挑戰性的工作環境吸引。"},{"en":"Challenging work environments are workplaces where tasks are difficult but can help people grow.","zh":"challenging work environments 指任務困難但能幫助人成長的工作場所。"},{"en":"A hospital emergency department is a challenging work environment because staff must think quickly.","zh":"醫院急症室是具挑戰性的工作環境，因為員工必須快速思考。"},{"en":"Challenging environments can develop skills, but they may also create stress.","zh":"具挑戰性的環境可以發展技能，但也可能造成壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests work that is demanding and stimulating.","zh":"這個短語暗示要求高且令人受刺激的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"IT consulting company","meaning":"資訊科技顧問公司","examples":[{"en":"An IT consulting company may offer high salaries to recruits.","zh":"資訊科技顧問公司可能向招聘對象提供高薪。"},{"en":"An IT consulting company advises other organisations on computer systems, software, and digital strategy.","zh":"IT consulting company 指就電腦系統、軟件和數碼策略向其他機構提供建議的公司。"},{"en":"A school may hire an IT consulting company to improve its online learning platform.","zh":"學校可能聘請資訊科技顧問公司改善網上學習平台。"},{"en":"Such companies need skilled workers because clients expect practical technology solutions.","zh":"這類公司需要熟練工人，因為客戶期望實用科技解決方案。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a business that provides technology advice and services.","zh":"這個短語指提供科技建議和服務的企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"annual bonuses","meaning":"年度花紅","examples":[{"en":"The company offers high salaries and annual bonuses.","zh":"該公司提供高薪和年度花紅。"},{"en":"Annual bonuses are extra payments given once a year, usually based on performance or company profit.","zh":"annual bonuses 指通常根據表現或公司利潤每年一次發放的額外款項。"},{"en":"A sales worker may receive an annual bonus if the team exceeds its target.","zh":"如果團隊超過目標，銷售員可能收到年度花紅。"},{"en":"Annual bonuses can attract applicants because they increase total income beyond monthly salary.","zh":"年度花紅可以吸引申請人，因為它提高月薪以外的總收入。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to yearly extra pay.","zh":"這個短語指每年額外薪酬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"immediate stock options","meaning":"即時股票期權","examples":[{"en":"Potential recruits may receive immediate stock options.","zh":"潛在招聘對象可能獲得即時股票期權。"},{"en":"Immediate stock options are rights given at once to buy company shares later at a set price.","zh":"immediate stock options 指立即給予日後以指定價格購買公司股份的權利。"},{"en":"A technology start-up may offer immediate stock options when it cannot pay very high salaries.","zh":"科技初創公司在無法支付很高薪金時，可能提供即時股票期權。"},{"en":"Stock options can become valuable if the company grows and its share price rises.","zh":"如果公司成長且股價上升，股票期權可以變得有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a financial benefit linked to company ownership.","zh":"這個短語描述與公司所有權相關的金錢福利。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"potential recruits","meaning":"潛在招聘對象","examples":[{"en":"The company offers attractive benefits to potential recruits.","zh":"該公司向潛在招聘對象提供吸引人的福利。"},{"en":"Potential recruits are people who may be hired by an organisation in the future.","zh":"potential recruits 指未來可能被某機構聘用的人。"},{"en":"A school may invite potential recruits to observe lessons before applying for teaching posts.","zh":"學校可能邀請潛在招聘對象觀課，再申請教席。"},{"en":"Companies compete for potential recruits when skilled workers are in short supply.","zh":"當熟練工人短缺，公司會競爭潛在招聘對象。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to possible future employees.","zh":"這個短語指可能的未來僱員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"bring in","meaning":"邀請；引入","examples":[{"en":"The company brings in prospective applicants for a two-day visit.","zh":"該公司邀請有意申請者進行兩日訪問。"},{"en":"To bring in people means to invite or arrange for them to come into a place or organisation.","zh":"bring in people 指邀請或安排某人進入某地方或機構。"},{"en":"A school may bring in guest speakers to talk about career planning.","zh":"學校可能邀請嘉賓講者來談職涯規劃。"},{"en":"Companies bring in applicants so they can observe skills, teamwork, and attitude directly.","zh":"公司邀請申請人到場，以便直接觀察技能、團隊合作和態度。"},{"en":"The phrase often means introducing people from outside into a setting.","zh":"這個短語常指把外部人員引入某環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prospective applicants","meaning":"有意申請者","examples":[{"en":"Prospective applicants visit the company before being hired.","zh":"有意申請者在被聘用前到訪公司。"},{"en":"Prospective applicants are people who are likely to apply for a job, course, or opportunity.","zh":"prospective applicants 指可能申請工作、課程或機會的人。"},{"en":"A university open day gives prospective applicants a chance to see the campus.","zh":"大學開放日讓有意申請者有機會參觀校園。"},{"en":"Employers may impress prospective applicants by showing real projects and friendly teams.","zh":"僱主可能透過展示真實項目和友善團隊，令有意申請者留下好印象。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to possible future applicants.","zh":"這個短語指可能的未來申請人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at a time","meaning":"每次","examples":[{"en":"The company invites 25 to 40 applicants at a time.","zh":"公司每次邀請25至40名申請人。"},{"en":"At a time means during one occasion or in one group.","zh":"at a time 指在一次場合或一組之中。"},{"en":"A teacher may meet five students at a time for speaking practice.","zh":"老師可能每次與五名學生進行口語練習。"},{"en":"Limiting the number at a time helps organisers manage activities more smoothly.","zh":"限制每次人數幫助組織者更順利管理活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how many people or things are handled in one round.","zh":"這個短語描述一輪中處理多少人或事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a two-day visit","meaning":"兩日訪問","examples":[{"en":"Applicants take part in a two-day visit to the company.","zh":"申請人參加對公司的兩日訪問。"},{"en":"A two-day visit is a visit that lasts for two days.","zh":"a two-day visit 指持續兩天的訪問。"},{"en":"A university may arrange a two-day visit for students to experience campus life.","zh":"大學可能安排兩日訪問，讓學生體驗校園生活。"},{"en":"A longer visit lets applicants see interviews, team tasks, and social events more fully.","zh":"較長訪問讓申請人更完整地看見面試、團隊任務和社交活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both the duration and purpose of a visit.","zh":"這個短語同時描述訪問的時間長度和目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"team exercises","meaning":"團隊練習","examples":[{"en":"The visit includes interviews, team exercises and social events.","zh":"該訪問包括面試、團隊練習和社交活動。"},{"en":"Team exercises are activities designed to make people work together to solve a task or show teamwork skills.","zh":"team exercises 指設計來讓人合作完成任務或展示團隊合作技巧的活動。"},{"en":"A teacher may use team exercises to help students plan a group presentation.","zh":"老師可能使用團隊練習幫助學生規劃小組匯報。"},{"en":"Team exercises reveal how people communicate, share ideas, and handle disagreement.","zh":"團隊練習揭示人們如何溝通、分享想法和處理分歧。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to structured group activities, not ordinary chatting.","zh":"這個短語指有結構的小組活動，而不是普通聊天。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"social events","meaning":"社交活動","examples":[{"en":"Applicants attend interviews, team exercises and social events.","zh":"申請人參加面試、團隊練習和社交活動。"},{"en":"Social events are gatherings where people meet, talk, and build relationships in a less formal setting.","zh":"social events 指人們在較非正式環境中見面、交談和建立關係的聚會。"},{"en":"A school may hold social events so new students can make friends before classes start.","zh":"學校可能舉辦社交活動，讓新生在開課前結識朋友。"},{"en":"Social events help employers observe how applicants interact outside formal interviews.","zh":"社交活動幫助僱主觀察申請人在正式面試以外如何互動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised occasions for social interaction.","zh":"這個短語指為社交互動而組織的場合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the idea behind","meaning":"……背後的理念","examples":[{"en":"The idea behind the team exercises is to show how employees work together.","zh":"團隊練習背後的理念是展示員工如何一起工作。"},{"en":"The idea behind something means the reason, purpose, or thinking that explains it.","zh":"the idea behind something 指解釋某事的原因、目的或想法。"},{"en":"The idea behind homework is to help students practise skills after class.","zh":"功課背後的理念是幫助學生在課後練習技能。"},{"en":"Understanding the idea behind an activity helps people take it more seriously.","zh":"理解活動背後的理念，幫助人更認真看待它。"},{"en":"The phrase asks why something was designed or used.","zh":"這個短語詢問某事為何被設計或使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get to see that","meaning":"得以看到","examples":[{"en":"Applicants get to see that they will work with other smart people.","zh":"申請人得以看到自己將會與其他聰明人合作。"},{"en":"To get to see that means to have the chance to realise or observe something directly.","zh":"get to see that 指有機會直接意識到或觀察到某事。"},{"en":"Students who visit a workplace get to see that engineers often solve problems in teams.","zh":"參觀職場的學生得以看到工程師通常以團隊方式解決問題。"},{"en":"Direct experience can help people get to see realities that brochures cannot show.","zh":"直接經驗可以幫助人看見宣傳冊不能展示的現實。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests learning through observation.","zh":"這個短語暗示透過觀察學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"work with other smart people","meaning":"與其他聰明人合作","examples":[{"en":"Applicants see that they will work with other smart people.","zh":"申請人看到自己將會與其他聰明人合作。"},{"en":"To work with other smart people means to collaborate with capable, thoughtful, and quick-learning colleagues.","zh":"work with other smart people 指與有能力、思考清晰和學得快的同事協作。"},{"en":"A student may improve faster when she works with other smart people in a debate team.","zh":"學生在辯論隊中與其他聰明人合作時，可能進步更快。"},{"en":"Working with smart colleagues can raise standards because everyone brings ideas and asks good questions.","zh":"與聰明同事合作可以提高標準，因為每個人都帶來想法並提出好問題。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights teamwork with capable peers.","zh":"這個短語突出與有能力同伴合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"The work involves teamwork rather than sitting alone writing code.","zh":"工作涉及團隊合作，而不是獨自坐着寫程式。"},{"en":"Rather than shows a contrast: one thing is true or preferred, not the other.","zh":"rather than 顯示對比：某事是真實或較可取，而不是另一件事。"},{"en":"A good lesson asks students to use examples rather than memorise rules silently.","zh":"好課堂要求學生使用例子，而不是安靜地背規則。"},{"en":"Employers want graduates who can solve problems with others rather than work in isolation all the time.","zh":"僱主希望畢業生能與他人解決問題，而不是一直孤立工作。"},{"en":"The phrase helps separate the real situation from a mistaken idea.","zh":"這個短語幫助把真實情況與錯誤想法分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sitting alone writing code","meaning":"獨自坐着寫程式","examples":[{"en":"The company wants applicants to see that the job is not just sitting alone writing code.","zh":"公司希望申請人看到這份工作不只是獨自坐着寫程式。"},{"en":"Sitting alone writing code means working by yourself at a computer to create software, without much teamwork.","zh":"sitting alone writing code 指自己一個人在電腦前創作軟件，沒有太多團隊合作。"},{"en":"Some programmers enjoy sitting alone writing code, but many projects also require meetings and testing with others.","zh":"有些程式員喜歡獨自寫程式，但許多項目也需要與他人開會和測試。"},{"en":"If a job is only imagined as solitary coding, applicants may underestimate the importance of communication.","zh":"如果一份工作只被想像成孤獨寫程式，申請人可能低估溝通的重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase represents a narrow stereotype of IT work.","zh":"這個短語代表對資訊科技工作的狹窄刻板印象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the past 10 years","meaning":"在過去十年","examples":[{"en":"In the past 10 years, employers have recognised the value of collaboration.","zh":"在過去十年，僱主已認識到協作的價值。"},{"en":"In the past 10 years means during the ten-year period leading up to now or to the time being discussed.","zh":"in the past 10 years 指截至現在或所討論時間為止的十年間。"},{"en":"In the past 10 years, many schools have added more online learning tools.","zh":"在過去十年，許多學校加入了更多網上學習工具。"},{"en":"Changes over ten years can show a clear shift in workplace expectations.","zh":"十年間的變化可以顯示職場期望的明顯轉變。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a recent time frame.","zh":"這個短語設定近期時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"marked benefits","meaning":"明顯好處","examples":[{"en":"Employers have seen marked benefits from collaborative projects.","zh":"僱主已從協作項目中看見明顯好處。"},{"en":"Marked benefits are clear and noticeable advantages.","zh":"marked benefits 指清楚而明顯的優勢。"},{"en":"A school may see marked benefits when students receive regular feedback on writing.","zh":"當學生定期收到寫作回饋，學校可能看見明顯好處。"},{"en":"If teamwork improves speed and creativity, companies can see marked benefits from collaboration.","zh":"如果團隊合作提高速度和創意，公司可以從協作中看見明顯好處。"},{"en":"The phrase means the benefits are not small or hidden.","zh":"這個短語意思是好處並不微小或隱藏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"collaborative projects","meaning":"協作項目","examples":[{"en":"Collaborative projects can improve product development.","zh":"協作項目可以改善產品開發。"},{"en":"Collaborative projects are tasks or projects completed by people working together.","zh":"collaborative projects 指由多人合作完成的任務或項目。"},{"en":"A class magazine is a collaborative project because writers, editors, and designers share the work.","zh":"班級雜誌是一個協作項目，因為作者、編輯和設計者分擔工作。"},{"en":"Collaborative projects can produce better ideas because different people notice different problems.","zh":"協作項目可以產生更好想法，因為不同人注意到不同問題。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses shared effort toward a common result.","zh":"這個短語強調為共同成果而付出的共同努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"product development","meaning":"產品開發","examples":[{"en":"Teamwork has brought benefits in product development.","zh":"團隊合作在產品開發方面帶來好處。"},{"en":"Product development is the process of designing, testing, and improving a product before it reaches customers.","zh":"product development 指產品到達顧客前，設計、測試和改善它的過程。"},{"en":"A company developing a new app needs product development to decide features, design, and user experience.","zh":"開發新應用程式的公司需要產品開發，以決定功能、設計和用戶體驗。"},{"en":"Good teamwork can improve product development because designers, engineers, and users give different feedback.","zh":"良好團隊合作可以改善產品開發，因為設計師、工程師和用戶提供不同回饋。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to turning an idea into a usable product.","zh":"這個短語指把想法變成可用產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"apart from","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"Apart from the work environment, research also supports team-based instruction.","zh":"除了工作環境之外，研究也支持團隊為本教學。"},{"en":"Apart from means besides or in addition to something already mentioned.","zh":"apart from 指除了已提及的某事之外。"},{"en":"Apart from exam scores, teachers should also consider students’ confidence and effort.","zh":"除了考試分數之外，老師也應考慮學生的信心和努力。"},{"en":"The phrase adds another reason or area to the discussion.","zh":"這個短語為討論加入另一個理由或範疇。"},{"en":"It helps writers move beyond one point to a second related point.","zh":"它幫助作者由一個重點轉到第二個相關重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a similar body of research","meaning":"一系列相似研究","examples":[{"en":"A similar body of research supports small team-based instruction.","zh":"一系列相似研究支持小組為本教學。"},{"en":"A body of research means a collection of studies on the same topic.","zh":"body of research 指關於同一主題的一組研究。"},{"en":"A body of research on sleep shows that students learn better when they rest enough.","zh":"關於睡眠的一系列研究顯示，學生休息足夠時學得更好。"},{"en":"When many studies point in the same direction, the argument becomes stronger.","zh":"當許多研究指向同一方向，論點會變得更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests evidence from several studies, not one opinion.","zh":"這個短語暗示來自多項研究的證據，而不是一個意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"indicate that","meaning":"顯示；表明","examples":[{"en":"Research indicates that team-based instruction can produce desirable results.","zh":"研究顯示團隊為本教學可以產生理想成果。"},{"en":"Indicate that means show or suggest that something is true.","zh":"indicate that 指顯示或暗示某事屬實。"},{"en":"Low attendance may indicate that students find the course too difficult or badly timed.","zh":"低出席率可能表明學生覺得課程太難或時間安排不好。"},{"en":"Research findings indicate patterns that teachers and employers can use for decisions.","zh":"研究結果顯示可供老師和僱主決策使用的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and often used with evidence.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常與證據一起使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"small team-based instruction","meaning":"小組為本教學","examples":[{"en":"Small team-based instruction can lead to educational benefits.","zh":"小組為本教學可以帶來教育好處。"},{"en":"Small team-based instruction is teaching that organises students into small groups to learn and solve tasks together.","zh":"small team-based instruction 指把學生組織成小組，一起學習和解決任務的教學方式。"},{"en":"In a language class, small team-based instruction may ask four students to plan a short dialogue.","zh":"在語文課中，小組為本教學可能要求四名學生策劃一段短對話。"},{"en":"Small teams can help quieter students speak more because the group feels safer than the whole class.","zh":"小組可以幫助較安靜的學生多說話，因為小組比全班更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes teaching through small-group cooperation.","zh":"這個短語描述透過小組合作進行的教學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"帶來；導致","examples":[{"en":"Team-based instruction can lead to desirable educational results.","zh":"團隊為本教學可以帶來理想教育成果。"},{"en":"To lead to something means to cause it or help produce it.","zh":"lead to something 指造成某事或促成某事。"},{"en":"Regular reading can lead to better vocabulary and faster comprehension.","zh":"定期閱讀可以帶來更好詞彙和更快理解。"},{"en":"Team learning can lead to stronger communication because students must discuss ideas.","zh":"團隊學習可以帶來更強溝通能力，因為學生必須討論想法。"},{"en":"The phrase shows cause and result.","zh":"這個短語顯示原因和結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"desirable educational results","meaning":"理想的教育成果","examples":[{"en":"Team-based instruction can produce desirable educational results.","zh":"團隊為本教學可以產生理想的教育成果。"},{"en":"Desirable educational results are learning outcomes that teachers, schools, or students want to achieve.","zh":"desirable educational results 指老師、學校或學生希望達成的學習成果。"},{"en":"Better confidence, deeper understanding, and stronger teamwork are desirable educational results.","zh":"更好信心、更深入理解和更強團隊合作都是理想的教育成果。"},{"en":"Clear goals and well-designed group tasks can help produce these results.","zh":"清楚目標和設計良好的小組任務可以幫助產生這些成果。"},{"en":"The phrase means positive learning outcomes.","zh":"這個短語意思是正面的學習成果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in order to","meaning":"為了","examples":[{"en":"Universities use team-based models in order to prepare IT graduates.","zh":"大學使用團隊為本模式，是為了培養資訊科技畢業生。"},{"en":"In order to means for the purpose of doing something.","zh":"in order to 指為了做某事。"},{"en":"Students revise past papers in order to understand exam patterns.","zh":"學生操練歷屆試題，是為了理解考試模式。"},{"en":"Schools introduce teamwork in order to help students practise workplace communication.","zh":"學校引入團隊合作，是為了幫助學生練習職場溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly shows purpose.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"prepare someone to","meaning":"使某人準備好……","examples":[{"en":"Colleges prepare IT graduates to meet workplace requirements.","zh":"大專院校使資訊科技畢業生準備好符合職場要求。"},{"en":"To prepare someone to do something means to give them the skills, knowledge, or confidence needed for it.","zh":"prepare someone to do something 指給予某人所需技能、知識或信心去做某事。"},{"en":"Mock interviews prepare students to answer questions calmly in real job interviews.","zh":"模擬面試讓學生準備好在真實求職面試中冷靜回答問題。"},{"en":"Team projects prepare graduates to communicate, share tasks, and solve problems at work.","zh":"團隊項目讓畢業生準備好在工作中溝通、分工和解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on readiness for a future task.","zh":"這個短語重點是為未來任務做好準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"IT graduates","meaning":"資訊科技畢業生","examples":[{"en":"IT graduates need teamwork skills for the modern workplace.","zh":"資訊科技畢業生需要現代職場所需的團隊合作技能。"},{"en":"IT graduates are people who have completed university or college programmes in information technology.","zh":"IT graduates 指完成資訊科技大學或大專課程的人。"},{"en":"An IT graduate may work as a software developer, data analyst, or technical consultant.","zh":"資訊科技畢業生可能擔任軟件開發員、數據分析師或技術顧問。"},{"en":"IT graduates need more than coding skills because many projects require teamwork and communication.","zh":"資訊科技畢業生需要的不只是編程技能，因為許多項目需要團隊合作和溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to graduates trained in digital and computer-related fields.","zh":"這個短語指接受數碼和電腦相關領域訓練的畢業生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"meet workplace requirements","meaning":"符合職場要求","examples":[{"en":"Graduates must meet workplace requirements after leaving university.","zh":"畢業生離開大學後必須符合職場要求。"},{"en":"To meet workplace requirements means to have the skills, behaviour, and standards employers expect.","zh":"meet workplace requirements 指具備僱主期望的技能、行為和標準。"},{"en":"A new nurse must meet workplace requirements by following safety rules and communicating clearly.","zh":"新護士必須透過遵守安全規則和清楚溝通來符合職場要求。"},{"en":"Universities design courses to help graduates meet requirements such as teamwork and problem-solving.","zh":"大學設計課程，以幫助畢業生符合團隊合作和解難等要求。"},{"en":"The phrase describes matching what jobs demand.","zh":"這個短語描述符合工作的需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"colleges and universities","meaning":"大專院校","examples":[{"en":"Colleges and universities are including team-based educational models.","zh":"大專院校正在加入團隊為本教育模式。"},{"en":"Colleges and universities are higher education institutions that teach students after secondary school.","zh":"colleges and universities 指在中學後教育學生的高等教育機構。"},{"en":"Colleges and universities may offer degrees, diplomas, professional training, and research opportunities.","zh":"大專院校可能提供學位、文憑、專業培訓和研究機會。"},{"en":"When employers demand teamwork, colleges and universities may change course design.","zh":"當僱主要求團隊合作，大專院校可能改變課程設計。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to post-secondary education institutions.","zh":"這個短語指專上教育機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"beginning to include","meaning":"開始加入","examples":[{"en":"Universities are beginning to include team-based models.","zh":"大學開始加入團隊為本模式。"},{"en":"Beginning to include means starting to add something that was not fully present before.","zh":"beginning to include 指開始加入以前未完全存在的東西。"},{"en":"Schools are beginning to include financial education in life-planning lessons.","zh":"學校開始在生涯規劃課中加入理財教育。"},{"en":"A new teaching idea may spread slowly as more institutions begin to include it.","zh":"隨着更多機構開始加入新教學理念，它可能慢慢擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests an early stage of change.","zh":"這個短語暗示變化的早期階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"team-based educational models","meaning":"團隊為本教育模式","examples":[{"en":"Team-based educational models prepare students for collaborative work.","zh":"團隊為本教育模式讓學生準備好面對協作工作。"},{"en":"Team-based educational models are teaching systems built around group work, shared responsibility, and team assessment.","zh":"team-based educational models 指圍繞小組工作、共同責任和團隊評估建立的教學系統。"},{"en":"A business course may use team-based educational models by asking students to run a simulated company together.","zh":"商業課程可能使用團隊為本教育模式，要求學生一起經營模擬公司。"},{"en":"These models help students practise the teamwork expected in many jobs.","zh":"這些模式幫助學生練習許多工作中需要的團隊合作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to structured education built around teams.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞團隊建立的結構化教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"one of the leaders in","meaning":"……的領導者之一","examples":[{"en":"AIU is one of the leaders in promoting team-based education.","zh":"AIU 是推動團隊為本教育的領導者之一。"},{"en":"One of the leaders in a field means one of the organisations or people most active or influential in that area.","zh":"one of the leaders in a field 指在某領域中最活躍或最有影響力的機構或人物之一。"},{"en":"A school may be one of the leaders in online learning if others copy its system.","zh":"如果其他學校模仿某校系統，該校可能是網上學習的領導者之一。"},{"en":"Leaders in education often influence how other institutions design courses.","zh":"教育界的領導者通常會影響其他機構如何設計課程。"},{"en":"The phrase shows importance within a particular field.","zh":"這個短語顯示在特定領域中的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"promoting team-based education","meaning":"推動團隊為本教育","examples":[{"en":"AIU plays a role in promoting team-based education.","zh":"AIU 在推動團隊為本教育方面扮演角色。"},{"en":"Promoting team-based education means actively supporting, spreading, or encouraging learning through teams.","zh":"promoting team-based education 指積極支持、傳播或鼓勵透過團隊進行學習。"},{"en":"A university promotes team-based education when it trains teachers to design group projects.","zh":"當大學訓練老師設計小組項目時，就是在推動團隊為本教育。"},{"en":"Promotion can make teamwork more common in courses that used to rely on lectures.","zh":"推動可以令團隊合作在過去依賴講課的課程中更常見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active support for a teaching approach.","zh":"這個短語描述對某種教學方法的積極支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"campuses worldwide","meaning":"全球校園","examples":[{"en":"AIU has campuses worldwide.","zh":"AIU 有全球校園。"},{"en":"Campuses worldwide means school or university sites located in different countries or regions around the world.","zh":"campuses worldwide 指位於世界不同國家或地區的學校或大學校區。"},{"en":"A university with campuses worldwide can let students study in different cities.","zh":"擁有全球校園的大學可以讓學生在不同城市學習。"},{"en":"Worldwide campuses may create more international classrooms and cultural exchange.","zh":"全球校園可能創造更多國際課堂和文化交流。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses global presence.","zh":"這個短語強調全球存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"offer programmes in","meaning":"提供……課程","examples":[{"en":"AIU offers programmes in information technology.","zh":"AIU 提供資訊科技課程。"},{"en":"To offer programmes in a subject means to provide courses or study paths in that field.","zh":"offer programmes in a subject 指提供某領域的課程或學習路徑。"},{"en":"A college may offer programmes in nursing, business, and design.","zh":"大專院校可能提供護理、商業和設計課程。"},{"en":"When universities offer IT programmes, they help prepare students for digital careers.","zh":"當大學提供資訊科技課程，它們幫助學生準備數碼職業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes educational provision.","zh":"這個短語描述教育上的提供。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a major portion of","meaning":"主要部分","examples":[{"en":"A major portion of the curriculum is based on team projects.","zh":"課程內容的主要部分以團隊項目為基礎。"},{"en":"A major portion of something means a large and important part of it.","zh":"a major portion of something 指某事物大而重要的一部分。"},{"en":"A major portion of a language course may focus on speaking practice.","zh":"語言課程的主要部分可能集中於口語練習。"},{"en":"If a major portion of a course uses teamwork, students cannot succeed by working alone only.","zh":"如果課程主要部分使用團隊合作，學生不能只靠單獨工作取得成功。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a large share of the whole.","zh":"這個短語突出整體中的大部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the curriculum","meaning":"課程內容","examples":[{"en":"The curriculum includes a large number of team projects.","zh":"課程內容包括大量團隊項目。"},{"en":"The curriculum is the planned content, subjects, skills, and activities taught in a course or school.","zh":"curriculum 指課程或學校中有計劃教授的內容、科目、技能和活動。"},{"en":"A school curriculum may include reading, writing, science, physical education, and project work.","zh":"學校課程內容可能包括閱讀、寫作、科學、體育和項目學習。"},{"en":"When the curriculum includes teamwork, students practise social and academic skills together.","zh":"當課程內容包括團隊合作，學生就一起練習社交和學術技能。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what is formally taught.","zh":"這個短語指正式教授的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"以……為基礎","examples":[{"en":"The curriculum is based on team projects.","zh":"課程內容以團隊項目為基礎。"},{"en":"To be based on something means to be built or organised around it.","zh":"be based on something 指圍繞某事物建立或組織。"},{"en":"A writing course may be based on weekly essays and detailed feedback.","zh":"寫作課程可能以每週作文和詳細回饋為基礎。"},{"en":"If a course is based on projects, students learn by doing rather than only listening.","zh":"如果課程以項目為基礎，學生就是透過做事學習，而不只是聆聽。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the foundation or main structure of something.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事物的基礎或主要結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"team projects","meaning":"團隊項目","examples":[{"en":"Students gain experience through team projects.","zh":"學生透過團隊項目獲得經驗。"},{"en":"Team projects are assignments or tasks completed by a group of students working together.","zh":"team projects 指由一組學生合作完成的作業或任務。"},{"en":"Students may create a website as a team project in an IT course.","zh":"學生可能在資訊科技課程中把建立網站作為團隊項目。"},{"en":"Team projects teach planning, communication, and responsibility because members depend on one another.","zh":"團隊項目教授規劃、溝通和責任感，因為成員彼此依賴。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised group assignments.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的小組作業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a large body of","meaning":"大量……","examples":[{"en":"AIU has a large body of international students.","zh":"AIU 有大量國際學生。"},{"en":"A large body of people means a large group or population.","zh":"a large body of people 指一大群人或大量人口。"},{"en":"A school with a large body of part-time students may offer evening classes.","zh":"有大量兼讀學生的學校可能提供夜間課程。"},{"en":"A large student body can create more varied opinions and learning experiences.","zh":"大量學生群體可以創造更多元觀點和學習經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a sizeable group.","zh":"這個短語描述相當大的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"international students","meaning":"國際學生","examples":[{"en":"International students can benefit from team-based classrooms.","zh":"國際學生可以從團隊為本課堂中得益。"},{"en":"International students are students who study in a country or institution outside their home country.","zh":"international students 指在自己國家以外的國家或院校學習的學生。"},{"en":"An international student may need time to adjust to a new language and classroom style.","zh":"國際學生可能需要時間適應新語言和課堂方式。"},{"en":"Team learning can help international students build friendships and understand local expectations.","zh":"團隊學習可以幫助國際學生建立友誼並理解本地期望。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to students from other countries.","zh":"這個短語指來自其他國家的學生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"educational backgrounds","meaning":"教育背景","examples":[{"en":"The students come from different educational backgrounds.","zh":"學生來自不同教育背景。"},{"en":"Educational backgrounds are the types of schools, courses, training, and learning experiences people had before.","zh":"educational backgrounds 指人們以往曾就讀的學校、課程、培訓和學習經驗。"},{"en":"In one university class, some students may have strong maths backgrounds while others studied business.","zh":"在一個大學課堂中，有些學生可能有強數學背景，另一些則讀過商業。"},{"en":"Different educational backgrounds can enrich a team because members bring different knowledge.","zh":"不同教育背景可以豐富團隊，因為成員帶來不同知識。"},{"en":"The phrase describes past learning experience.","zh":"這個短語描述過往學習經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a sense of","meaning":"……的感覺","examples":[{"en":"Team-based learning gives students a sense of support.","zh":"團隊為本學習給學生一種支持感。"},{"en":"A sense of something means a feeling or awareness of it.","zh":"a sense of something 指對某事的一種感覺或意識。"},{"en":"A friendly class can give new students a sense of belonging.","zh":"友善班級可以給新生歸屬感。"},{"en":"When students work in teams, they may feel a sense of support because others share the task.","zh":"當學生以團隊合作，他們可能感到支持感，因為其他人分擔任務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an emotional or social feeling.","zh":"這個短語描述情緒或社交感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"social and technical support","meaning":"社交及技術支援","examples":[{"en":"Students receive social and technical support within the group.","zh":"學生在小組內得到社交及技術支援。"},{"en":"Social and technical support means help with relationships, communication, and practical or digital tasks.","zh":"social and technical support 指在人際關係、溝通，以及實務或數碼任務上的幫助。"},{"en":"A classmate gives social support by encouraging a nervous student and technical support by helping fix a file.","zh":"同學鼓勵緊張學生是社交支援，幫忙修復文件則是技術支援。"},{"en":"Teamwork provides support because students can share both emotional pressure and practical problems.","zh":"團隊合作提供支援，因為學生可以分擔情緒壓力和實際問題。"},{"en":"The phrase combines human help with skill-based help.","zh":"這個短語結合人際幫助和技能型幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"within the group","meaning":"在小組內","examples":[{"en":"Students support one another within the group.","zh":"學生在小組內互相支持。"},{"en":"Within the group means inside the team or among its members.","zh":"within the group 指在團隊內部或成員之間。"},{"en":"Within the group, one student may lead discussion while another checks grammar.","zh":"在小組內，一名學生可能帶領討論，另一名檢查文法。"},{"en":"Good support within the group helps members solve problems before asking the teacher.","zh":"小組內的良好支援幫助成員在詢問老師前先解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on what happens among team members.","zh":"這個短語重點是團隊成員之間發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"first-hand experience of","meaning":"……的第一手經驗","examples":[{"en":"Students gain first-hand experience of working with others.","zh":"學生獲得與他人合作的第一手經驗。"},{"en":"First-hand experience of something means direct personal experience, not just reading or hearing about it.","zh":"first-hand experience of something 指直接親身經驗，而不只是閱讀或聽聞。"},{"en":"A student gains first-hand experience of customer service by working in a shop.","zh":"學生在商店工作時，獲得顧客服務的第一手經驗。"},{"en":"First-hand experience teaches lessons that lectures alone may not show clearly.","zh":"第一手經驗教授一些單靠講課未必清楚顯示的教訓。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses direct involvement.","zh":"這個短語強調直接參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"potential successes","meaning":"潛在成功","examples":[{"en":"Teamwork gives students experience of potential successes.","zh":"團隊合作讓學生經歷潛在成功。"},{"en":"Potential successes are positive results that may happen if people work well.","zh":"potential successes 指如果人們合作良好可能出現的正面結果。"},{"en":"A team project has potential successes such as a strong presentation and shared confidence.","zh":"團隊項目的潛在成功包括出色匯報和共同信心。"},{"en":"Seeing potential successes can motivate students to cooperate more seriously.","zh":"看見潛在成功可以激勵學生更認真合作。"},{"en":"The phrase points to possible good outcomes, not guaranteed results.","zh":"這個短語指可能的好結果，而不是保證結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"inherent problems","meaning":"固有問題","examples":[{"en":"Students also experience inherent problems in teamwork.","zh":"學生也會經歷團隊合作中的固有問題。"},{"en":"Inherent problems are difficulties that naturally exist inside a situation or system.","zh":"inherent problems 指自然存在於某情況或系統內的困難。"},{"en":"Group projects have inherent problems because members may have different schedules and standards.","zh":"小組項目有固有問題，因為成員可能有不同時間表和標準。"},{"en":"Recognising inherent problems helps teams plan rules before conflict grows.","zh":"認識固有問題幫助團隊在衝突擴大前制定規則。"},{"en":"The phrase describes built-in difficulties, not unusual accidents only.","zh":"這個短語描述內在困難，而不只是異常事故。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be encountered when","meaning":"在……時遇到","examples":[{"en":"Problems are often encountered when students work with others.","zh":"問題通常在學生與他人合作時遇到。"},{"en":"To be encountered when something happens means to be met or experienced during that situation.","zh":"be encountered when something happens 指在某情況中遇到或經歷某事。"},{"en":"Technical problems may be encountered when students submit homework online.","zh":"學生網上提交功課時可能遇到技術問題。"},{"en":"Conflicts are encountered when team members have different opinions or effort levels.","zh":"當團隊成員有不同意見或努力程度時，就會遇到衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase describes problems appearing during a particular activity.","zh":"這個短語描述問題在某活動期間出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"work with others","meaning":"與他人合作","examples":[{"en":"Students learn how to work with others effectively.","zh":"學生學習如何有效地與他人合作。"},{"en":"To work with others means to cooperate, communicate, and share tasks with other people.","zh":"work with others 指與其他人合作、溝通和分擔任務。"},{"en":"A student works with others when she plans a presentation with classmates.","zh":"學生與同學策劃匯報時，就是與他人合作。"},{"en":"Working with others can improve ideas because people notice different details.","zh":"與他人合作可以改善想法，因為人們注意到不同細節。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights cooperation rather than individual effort alone.","zh":"這個短語突出合作，而不只是個人努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"team-oriented instruction","meaning":"團隊導向教學","examples":[{"en":"Team-oriented instruction is becoming more important in IT education.","zh":"團隊導向教學在資訊科技教育中變得更重要。"},{"en":"Team-oriented instruction is teaching designed around teamwork and group problem-solving.","zh":"team-oriented instruction 指圍繞團隊合作和小組解難而設計的教學。"},{"en":"A teacher uses team-oriented instruction when students learn coding by building an app together.","zh":"當學生透過一起製作應用程式來學編程，老師就是使用團隊導向教學。"},{"en":"This approach prepares students for workplaces where projects are completed by teams.","zh":"這種方法讓學生準備好面對項目由團隊完成的職場。"},{"en":"The phrase describes instruction that points students toward collaboration.","zh":"這個短語描述把學生導向協作的教學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the common mode of delivery","meaning":"常見授課模式","examples":[{"en":"Team-oriented instruction has not been the common mode of delivery in traditional colleges.","zh":"團隊導向教學在傳統大學中一直不是常見授課模式。"},{"en":"The common mode of delivery is the usual way a course or lesson is taught.","zh":"common mode of delivery 指課程或課堂通常被教授的方式。"},{"en":"In many schools, lectures and worksheets are the common mode of delivery.","zh":"在許多學校，講課和工作紙是常見授課模式。"},{"en":"If teamwork is not the common mode of delivery, students may have little practice collaborating.","zh":"如果團隊合作不是常見授課模式，學生可能很少練習協作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the normal teaching format.","zh":"這個短語描述正常教學形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"traditional college settings","meaning":"傳統大學環境","examples":[{"en":"Teamwork was not always common in traditional college settings.","zh":"團隊合作在傳統大學環境中並不總是常見。"},{"en":"Traditional college settings are conventional university or college environments, often based on lectures and individual assignments.","zh":"traditional college settings 指傳統大學或大專環境，通常以講課和個人作業為基礎。"},{"en":"In traditional college settings, students may listen to lectures in large classrooms.","zh":"在傳統大學環境中，學生可能在大型課室聽講課。"},{"en":"These settings can provide knowledge but may not always train workplace teamwork.","zh":"這些環境可以提供知識，但未必總能訓練職場團隊合作。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts older education formats with newer collaborative models.","zh":"這個短語把較舊教育形式與較新的協作模式作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"choose to go into","meaning":"選擇投身……","examples":[{"en":"Many graduates choose to go into an IT work environment.","zh":"許多畢業生選擇投身資訊科技工作環境。"},{"en":"To choose to go into a field means to decide to enter that career or area of work.","zh":"choose to go into a field 指決定進入某職業或工作領域。"},{"en":"A student may choose to go into teaching because she enjoys helping children.","zh":"學生可能因喜歡幫助孩子而選擇投身教學。"},{"en":"Career choice affects what skills students need to develop before graduation.","zh":"職業選擇影響學生畢業前需要發展哪些技能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deciding on a professional path.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇專業道路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an IT work environment","meaning":"資訊科技工作環境","examples":[{"en":"Graduates often encounter teamwork in an IT work environment.","zh":"畢業生通常在資訊科技工作環境中遇到團隊合作。"},{"en":"An IT work environment is a workplace where people design, manage, support, or use digital systems and technology.","zh":"IT work environment 指人們設計、管理、支援或使用數碼系統和科技的工作場所。"},{"en":"A software company, data team, or technical support office can be an IT work environment.","zh":"軟件公司、數據團隊或技術支援辦公室都可以是資訊科技工作環境。"},{"en":"Such environments often require teamwork because complex systems need different skills.","zh":"這類環境通常需要團隊合作，因為複雜系統需要不同技能。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the professional setting of information technology work.","zh":"這個短語指資訊科技工作的專業環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"encounter some form of teamwork","meaning":"遇到某種形式的團隊合作","examples":[{"en":"Most IT graduates will encounter some form of teamwork at work.","zh":"大多數資訊科技畢業生在工作中會遇到某種形式的團隊合作。"},{"en":"To encounter some form of teamwork means to experience at least one type of group collaboration.","zh":"encounter some form of teamwork 指經歷至少一種小組協作。"},{"en":"A new employee may encounter teamwork when asked to join a project meeting.","zh":"新員工被要求參加項目會議時，可能會遇到團隊合作。"},{"en":"Because IT projects are complex, graduates often need to share tasks with designers, managers, and users.","zh":"因為資訊科技項目複雜，畢業生通常需要與設計師、經理和用戶分擔任務。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests teamwork is difficult to avoid in modern work.","zh":"這個短語暗示現代工作中難以避開團隊合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"benefit from","meaning":"從……中得益","examples":[{"en":"Students benefit from collaborative learning.","zh":"學生從協作學習中得益。"},{"en":"To benefit from something means to gain help, advantage, or improvement from it.","zh":"benefit from something 指從某事中獲得幫助、優勢或改善。"},{"en":"Students benefit from feedback when teachers explain exactly how to improve.","zh":"當老師清楚解釋如何改善，學生就從回饋中得益。"},{"en":"Learners benefit from teamwork because peers can explain ideas in different ways.","zh":"學習者從團隊合作中得益，因為同伴可以用不同方式解釋想法。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a positive result gained from something.","zh":"這個短語顯示從某事獲得正面結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"collaborative learning","meaning":"協作學習","examples":[{"en":"Collaborative learning helps students work with different people.","zh":"協作學習幫助學生與不同的人合作。"},{"en":"Collaborative learning is learning through cooperation, discussion, and shared tasks.","zh":"collaborative learning 指透過合作、討論和共同任務進行學習。"},{"en":"In collaborative learning, students may solve a case study together instead of listening silently.","zh":"在協作學習中，學生可能一起解決個案研究，而不是安靜聽課。"},{"en":"Collaborative learning builds communication because students must explain and defend ideas.","zh":"協作學習培養溝通能力，因為學生必須解釋和捍衛想法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to learning with others, not just beside others.","zh":"這個短語指與他人一起學習，而不只是坐在他人旁邊學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be taught the tools needed to","meaning":"獲教授做……所需的工具","examples":[{"en":"Students are taught the tools needed to achieve common goals.","zh":"學生獲教授達成共同目標所需的工具。"},{"en":"To be taught the tools needed to do something means to learn the skills or methods required for that task.","zh":"be taught the tools needed to do something 指學習完成某任務所需的技能或方法。"},{"en":"Students are taught the tools needed to write essays when they learn planning, paragraphing, and evidence use.","zh":"學生學習構思、分段和使用證據時，就是獲教授寫作文所需的工具。"},{"en":"Teaching tools for teamwork helps students cooperate more effectively.","zh":"教授團隊合作工具幫助學生更有效合作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical preparation.","zh":"這個短語指實用準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"work with different people","meaning":"與不同的人合作","examples":[{"en":"Students need to work with different people in the workplace.","zh":"學生在職場上需要與不同的人合作。"},{"en":"To work with different people means to cooperate with people who have different skills, cultures, personalities, or opinions.","zh":"work with different people 指與擁有不同技能、文化、性格或意見的人合作。"},{"en":"A nurse must work with different people, including doctors, patients, and families.","zh":"護士必須與不同的人合作，包括醫生、病人和家屬。"},{"en":"Working with different people can create conflict, but it also brings wider ideas.","zh":"與不同的人合作可能產生衝突，但也帶來更廣泛想法。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses adaptability in cooperation.","zh":"這個短語強調合作中的適應能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"achieve common goals","meaning":"達成共同目標","examples":[{"en":"Team members work together to achieve common goals.","zh":"團隊成員一起合作以達成共同目標。"},{"en":"To achieve common goals means to reach shared aims that everyone in the group is working toward.","zh":"achieve common goals 指達到小組中每個人共同努力的目標。"},{"en":"A class can achieve common goals when students help organise a successful charity fair.","zh":"當學生協助組織成功慈善義賣會，班級就能達成共同目標。"},{"en":"Clear goals help teams divide tasks and measure progress.","zh":"清楚目標幫助團隊分配任務和衡量進度。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on shared success rather than individual victory.","zh":"這個短語重點是共同成功，而不是個人勝利。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"common goals or objectives","meaning":"共同目標","examples":[{"en":"Teamwork helps people achieve common goals or objectives.","zh":"團隊合作幫助人們達成共同目標。"},{"en":"Common goals or objectives are aims shared by members of a group.","zh":"common goals or objectives 指小組成員共同擁有的目標。"},{"en":"A sports team has common goals or objectives, such as improving fitness and winning matches.","zh":"運動隊有共同目標，例如改善體能和贏得比賽。"},{"en":"When common goals are clear, team members are less likely to work in different directions.","zh":"當共同目標清楚，團隊成員較不可能向不同方向工作。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights shared purpose.","zh":"這個短語突出共同目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in-class time","meaning":"課堂時間","examples":[{"en":"Students spend much of their in-class time working in teams.","zh":"學生把大部分課堂時間用於團隊工作。"},{"en":"In-class time is the time students spend during scheduled lessons or class meetings.","zh":"in-class time 指學生在已安排課堂或課堂會面中的時間。"},{"en":"A teacher may use in-class time for discussion and leave reading for homework.","zh":"老師可能把課堂時間用於討論，並把閱讀留作功課。"},{"en":"How in-class time is used affects whether students practise listening, speaking, or problem-solving.","zh":"課堂時間如何使用，會影響學生是否練習聆聽、說話或解難。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to lesson time, not private study time.","zh":"這個短語指上課時間，而不是私人自修時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"permanent and heterogeneous teams","meaning":"固定且異質的小組","examples":[{"en":"Students work in permanent and heterogeneous teams.","zh":"學生在固定且異質的小組中工作。"},{"en":"Permanent and heterogeneous teams are fixed groups made up of members with different backgrounds or abilities.","zh":"permanent and heterogeneous teams 指固定小組，由不同背景或能力的成員組成。"},{"en":"A class may form permanent and heterogeneous teams so stronger and weaker students learn together.","zh":"班級可能組成固定且異質的小組，讓較強和較弱學生一起學習。"},{"en":"These teams allow trust to grow while exposing students to different perspectives.","zh":"這些小組讓信任得以建立，同時讓學生接觸不同角度。"},{"en":"The phrase combines stability with diversity.","zh":"這個短語結合穩定性和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be made up of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"Most teams are made up of students with different backgrounds.","zh":"大多數團隊由不同背景的學生組成。"},{"en":"To be made up of something means to consist of those parts or members.","zh":"be made up of something 指由那些部分或成員構成。"},{"en":"A school committee may be made up of teachers, parents, and students.","zh":"學校委員會可能由老師、家長和學生組成。"},{"en":"A diverse team is made up of people who bring different skills and experiences.","zh":"多元團隊由帶來不同技能和經驗的人組成。"},{"en":"The phrase explains composition.","zh":"這個短語解釋組成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"socio-cultural backgrounds","meaning":"社會文化背景","examples":[{"en":"Teams include students from different socio-cultural backgrounds.","zh":"團隊包括來自不同社會文化背景的學生。"},{"en":"Socio-cultural backgrounds are the social and cultural experiences that shape how people think, speak, and behave.","zh":"socio-cultural backgrounds 指塑造人們思考、說話和行為的社會及文化經驗。"},{"en":"Students from different socio-cultural backgrounds may have different ideas about leadership and politeness.","zh":"來自不同社會文化背景的學生，可能對領導和禮貌有不同想法。"},{"en":"Working across backgrounds can teach students to explain assumptions more clearly.","zh":"跨背景合作可以教學生更清楚解釋自己的假設。"},{"en":"The phrase combines social background and cultural background.","zh":"這個短語結合社會背景和文化背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"varying skill levels","meaning":"不同技能水平","examples":[{"en":"Team members often have varying skill levels.","zh":"團隊成員通常有不同技能水平。"},{"en":"Varying skill levels means different degrees of ability among people in a group.","zh":"varying skill levels 指小組中人們能力程度不同。"},{"en":"In a coding class, some students may be beginners while others have advanced skills.","zh":"在編程課中，有些學生可能是初學者，另一些則有高階技能。"},{"en":"Varying skill levels can create challenges, but they also allow peer teaching.","zh":"不同技能水平可能帶來挑戰，但也容許同儕教學。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mixed ability.","zh":"這個短語描述混合能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"concentrate on","meaning":"集中於；側重於","examples":[{"en":"Team activities concentrate on using concepts.","zh":"團隊活動集中於運用概念。"},{"en":"To concentrate on something means to focus attention and effort on it.","zh":"concentrate on something 指把注意力和努力集中在某事上。"},{"en":"A writing lesson may concentrate on paragraph structure before moving to vocabulary.","zh":"寫作課可能先集中於段落結構，然後才轉到詞彙。"},{"en":"When students concentrate on application, they learn how knowledge works in real tasks.","zh":"當學生集中於應用，他們會學到知識如何在真實任務中運作。"},{"en":"The phrase means to give priority to one area.","zh":"這個短語意思是優先處理某一範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"using rather than just learning concepts","meaning":"運用概念，而不只是學習概念","examples":[{"en":"Team activities focus on using rather than just learning concepts.","zh":"團隊活動集中於運用概念，而不只是學習概念。"},{"en":"Using rather than just learning concepts means applying ideas to tasks, not only memorising them.","zh":"using rather than just learning concepts 指把想法應用到任務中，而不只是記住它們。"},{"en":"A maths class uses concepts when students design a budget instead of only copying formulas.","zh":"數學課讓學生設計預算，而不只是抄公式，就是在運用概念。"},{"en":"Application helps students see why ideas matter and how they solve problems.","zh":"應用幫助學生看見想法為何重要，以及它們如何解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts practical use with passive study.","zh":"這個短語把實際使用與被動學習作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"student grades","meaning":"學生成績","examples":[{"en":"Student grades are based partly on team performance.","zh":"學生成績部分建基於團隊表現。"},{"en":"Student grades are marks or scores that show how well students have performed.","zh":"student grades 指顯示學生表現如何的分數或等級。"},{"en":"A student’s grade may include exam marks, project work, and participation.","zh":"學生成績可能包括考試分數、項目作業和課堂參與。"},{"en":"When grades include teamwork, students must care about both personal effort and group results.","zh":"當成績包括團隊合作，學生必須同時重視個人努力和小組成果。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to formal academic assessment.","zh":"這個短語指正式學術評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a combination of","meaning":"……的結合","examples":[{"en":"Student grades are a combination of team performance and peer evaluation.","zh":"學生成績是團隊表現和同儕評估的結合。"},{"en":"A combination of two things means those things are used together.","zh":"combination of two things 指兩件事被一起使用。"},{"en":"A good language course may use a combination of grammar practice and real conversation.","zh":"好語言課程可能使用文法練習和真實對話的結合。"},{"en":"Combining team performance and peer evaluation can balance group results with individual contribution.","zh":"結合團隊表現和同儕評估，可以平衡小組成果與個人貢獻。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights multiple parts working together.","zh":"這個短語突出多個部分共同作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"overall team performance","meaning":"團隊整體表現","examples":[{"en":"Grades include overall team performance.","zh":"成績包括團隊整體表現。"},{"en":"Overall team performance is how well the whole team completes its work, communicates, and reaches its goal.","zh":"overall team performance 指整個團隊完成工作、溝通和達成目標的表現。"},{"en":"A teacher may judge overall team performance by the quality of the final presentation and cooperation.","zh":"老師可能透過最終匯報質素和合作情況判斷團隊整體表現。"},{"en":"If one member works hard but the team fails to coordinate, overall performance may still suffer.","zh":"如果一名成員很努力但團隊未能協調，整體表現仍可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase looks at the group as a whole.","zh":"這個短語從整體看待小組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"peer evaluation","meaning":"同儕評估","examples":[{"en":"Peer evaluation is used to assess individual team members.","zh":"同儕評估用來評估個別團隊成員。"},{"en":"Peer evaluation is assessment made by classmates or team members rather than only by the teacher.","zh":"peer evaluation 指由同學或團隊成員，而不只是老師作出的評估。"},{"en":"In a group project, students may use peer evaluation to rate each member’s contribution.","zh":"在小組項目中，學生可能使用同儕評估來評分每名成員的貢獻。"},{"en":"Peer evaluation can discourage free-riding because team members know their effort will be judged.","zh":"同儕評估可以阻止搭便車，因為團隊成員知道自己的努力會被評價。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to students assessing one another.","zh":"這個短語指學生互相評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"individual team members","meaning":"個別團隊成員","examples":[{"en":"Peer evaluation assesses individual team members.","zh":"同儕評估評估個別團隊成員。"},{"en":"Individual team members are the separate people who make up a team.","zh":"individual team members 指組成團隊的每一個人。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask individual team members to explain their own part of a project.","zh":"老師可能要求個別團隊成員解釋自己負責的項目部分。"},{"en":"Assessing individual members helps prevent one hardworking student from carrying the whole group alone.","zh":"評估個別成員有助防止一名努力學生獨自承擔整個小組工作。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on each person inside the team.","zh":"這個短語重點是團隊中的每個人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in a team-based environment","meaning":"在團隊為本環境中","examples":[{"en":"In a team-based environment, the teacher acts as a facilitator.","zh":"在團隊為本環境中，老師擔任促進者。"},{"en":"In a team-based environment means in a setting where learning or work is organised around teams.","zh":"in a team-based environment 指在學習或工作圍繞團隊而組織的環境中。"},{"en":"In a team-based environment, students may sit in groups instead of rows.","zh":"在團隊為本環境中，學生可能分組而坐，而不是排排坐。"},{"en":"Such an environment changes the teacher’s role because students must discuss and solve problems together.","zh":"這種環境改變老師角色，因為學生必須一起討論和解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a setting built around collaboration.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞協作建立的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take on the role of","meaning":"擔任……角色","examples":[{"en":"The teacher takes on the role of a facilitator.","zh":"老師擔任促進者的角色。"},{"en":"To take on the role of someone means to begin performing that function or responsibility.","zh":"take on the role of someone 指開始履行某功能或責任。"},{"en":"In a group project, one student may take on the role of organiser.","zh":"在小組項目中，一名學生可能擔任組織者角色。"},{"en":"When teachers take on a guiding role, students become more active in learning.","zh":"當老師擔任引導角色，學生在學習中會變得更主動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes accepting a particular responsibility.","zh":"這個短語描述接受某特定責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a facilitator","meaning":"促進者","examples":[{"en":"The teacher becomes a facilitator rather than only a lecturer.","zh":"老師成為促進者，而不只是講師。"},{"en":"A facilitator is someone who helps a group work, discuss, and learn more effectively.","zh":"facilitator 指幫助小組更有效工作、討論和學習的人。"},{"en":"In a workshop, a facilitator may ask guiding questions instead of giving all the answers.","zh":"在工作坊中，促進者可能提出引導問題，而不是給出所有答案。"},{"en":"A good facilitator keeps discussion focused and helps quiet members speak.","zh":"好促進者讓討論保持焦點，並幫助安靜成員發言。"},{"en":"The word describes a guide who supports learning rather than simply delivering information.","zh":"這個詞描述支援學習的引導者，而不只是傳遞資訊的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"manager of learning","meaning":"學習管理者","examples":[{"en":"The teacher acts as a manager of learning.","zh":"老師擔任學習管理者。"},{"en":"A manager of learning organises, guides, and monitors how students learn.","zh":"manager of learning 指組織、引導和監察學生如何學習的人。"},{"en":"A teacher becomes a manager of learning when she designs tasks, checks progress, and supports groups.","zh":"當老師設計任務、檢查進度並支援小組，她就成為學習管理者。"},{"en":"This role helps students take responsibility while still receiving structure.","zh":"這個角色幫助學生承擔責任，同時仍得到結構。"},{"en":"The phrase describes teaching as guided learning management.","zh":"這個短語把教學描述為受引導的學習管理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"instead of","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"The teacher guides learning instead of just providing information.","zh":"老師引導學習，而不是只提供資訊。"},{"en":"Instead of shows that one action replaces another action.","zh":"instead of 顯示一個行動取代另一個行動。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to solve a problem instead of giving the answer immediately.","zh":"老師可能要求學生解決問題，而不是立即給答案。"},{"en":"Team learning uses discussion instead of relying only on lectures.","zh":"團隊學習使用討論，而不是只依賴講課。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly shows contrast between two choices.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示兩個選擇之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"passive students","meaning":"被動學生","examples":[{"en":"The teacher does not simply provide information to passive students.","zh":"老師不只是向被動學生提供資訊。"},{"en":"Passive students are learners who mainly receive information without actively asking, discussing, or applying it.","zh":"passive students 指主要接收資訊，而不主動提問、討論或應用資訊的學習者。"},{"en":"Students become passive if lessons only require them to copy notes quietly.","zh":"如果課堂只要求學生安靜抄筆記，學生會變得被動。"},{"en":"Team tasks can reduce passivity because students must speak and contribute.","zh":"團隊任務可以減少被動，因為學生必須發言和貢獻。"},{"en":"The phrase describes students who are not actively involved in learning.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有主動參與學習的學生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"guide the team in","meaning":"指導團隊去……","examples":[{"en":"The teacher guides the team in identifying its goals.","zh":"老師指導團隊確立目標。"},{"en":"To guide the team in doing something means to help the group complete a task without doing it for them.","zh":"guide the team in doing something 指幫助小組完成任務，但不是替他們完成。"},{"en":"A coach guides the team in planning training but expects players to practise themselves.","zh":"教練指導團隊規劃訓練，但期望球員自己練習。"},{"en":"Guidance helps teams avoid confusion while still giving students responsibility.","zh":"指導幫助團隊避免混亂，同時仍讓學生承擔責任。"},{"en":"The phrase describes supportive direction.","zh":"這個短語描述支援性的方向引導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"identify goals","meaning":"確立目標","examples":[{"en":"Students learn to identify goals as a team.","zh":"學生學習以團隊方式確立目標。"},{"en":"To identify goals means to decide clearly what the group wants to achieve.","zh":"identify goals 指清楚決定小組想達成甚麼。"},{"en":"A study group identifies goals when it agrees to finish two practice papers by Friday.","zh":"學習小組同意星期五前完成兩份練習卷，就是確立目標。"},{"en":"Clear goals help teams divide work and check progress.","zh":"清楚目標幫助團隊分工和檢查進度。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on making aims clear.","zh":"這個短語重點是令目標清晰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"establish standards of","meaning":"制定……標準","examples":[{"en":"The facilitator helps establish standards of team performance.","zh":"促進者幫助制定團隊表現標準。"},{"en":"To establish standards of something means to set clear expectations for quality or behaviour.","zh":"establish standards of something 指為質素或行為設定清楚期望。"},{"en":"A teacher may establish standards of essay writing by showing examples of strong paragraphs.","zh":"老師可能透過展示強段落例子，制定作文標準。"},{"en":"Clear standards help team members know what good work looks like.","zh":"清楚標準幫助團隊成員知道好作品應是甚麼樣子。"},{"en":"The phrase means creating rules or expectations for judgement.","zh":"這個短語意思是建立評判用的規則或期望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"team performance","meaning":"團隊表現","examples":[{"en":"Teams need clear standards of team performance.","zh":"團隊需要清楚的團隊表現標準。"},{"en":"Team performance is how well a group works together and completes its task.","zh":"team performance 指小組合作和完成任務的表現。"},{"en":"A team’s performance may be judged by planning, communication, final quality, and time management.","zh":"團隊表現可能根據規劃、溝通、最終質素和時間管理來評估。"},{"en":"Poor communication can reduce team performance even when members are individually strong.","zh":"即使成員個別能力強，差劣溝通也可以降低團隊表現。"},{"en":"The phrase looks at the group’s effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語看的是小組效能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"problem-solving skills","meaning":"解難能力","examples":[{"en":"Team exercises help students improve problem-solving skills.","zh":"團隊練習幫助學生改善解難能力。"},{"en":"Problem-solving skills are the abilities needed to understand a problem, find options, and choose a workable solution.","zh":"problem-solving skills 指理解問題、找出選項並選擇可行解決方案所需的能力。"},{"en":"A student uses problem-solving skills when a group presentation file suddenly fails to open.","zh":"當小組匯報文件突然無法打開，學生就需要使用解難能力。"},{"en":"Teamwork improves these skills because students hear different possible solutions.","zh":"團隊合作改善這些技能，因為學生聽到不同可能解決方案。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical thinking under difficulty.","zh":"這個短語指困難中的實際思考能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"apply theory to","meaning":"將理論應用於……","examples":[{"en":"Students apply theory to simulated real-world situations.","zh":"學生將理論應用於模擬真實情境。"},{"en":"To apply theory to a situation means to use ideas or principles to deal with a practical case.","zh":"apply theory to a situation 指使用想法或原則處理實際個案。"},{"en":"Business students apply theory to a shop problem when they use pricing ideas to set discounts.","zh":"商科學生使用定價概念設定折扣來處理商店問題時，就是將理論應用於該問題。"},{"en":"Applying theory helps students see whether classroom knowledge works in practice.","zh":"應用理論幫助學生看見課堂知識在實踐中是否有效。"},{"en":"The phrase connects abstract learning with real tasks.","zh":"這個短語把抽象學習與真實任務連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"simulated real-world situations","meaning":"模擬真實情境","examples":[{"en":"Team exercises use simulated real-world situations.","zh":"團隊練習使用模擬真實情境。"},{"en":"Simulated real-world situations are practice scenarios that imitate problems people may face outside the classroom.","zh":"simulated real-world situations 指模仿人們在課堂外可能面對問題的練習情境。"},{"en":"A nursing class may use a simulated real-world situation where a patient suddenly feels dizzy.","zh":"護理課可能使用病人突然感到暈眩的模擬真實情境。"},{"en":"Simulations let students make decisions safely before facing real consequences.","zh":"模擬讓學生在面對真實後果前安全地作決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes realistic practice without full real-world risk.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有完整真實世界風險的現實練習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"adopt new roles","meaning":"承擔新角色","examples":[{"en":"Working as a team allows students to adopt new roles.","zh":"以團隊方式工作讓學生承擔新角色。"},{"en":"To adopt new roles means to take on different responsibilities or positions from usual.","zh":"adopt new roles 指承擔與平時不同的責任或位置。"},{"en":"A quiet student may adopt the role of timekeeper during a group project.","zh":"安靜學生可能在小組項目中承擔計時員角色。"},{"en":"Trying new roles helps students discover strengths they may not have noticed.","zh":"嘗試新角色幫助學生發現自己未必注意到的強項。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing one’s function in a group.","zh":"這個短語描述在小組中改變自己的功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"empower someone to","meaning":"賦權予某人去……","examples":[{"en":"Teamwork empowers students to control their own learning.","zh":"團隊合作賦權予學生去掌控自己的學習。"},{"en":"To empower someone to do something means to give them the confidence, authority, or ability to do it.","zh":"empower someone to do something 指給予某人信心、權力或能力去做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher empowers students to revise independently by teaching them how to plan study time.","zh":"老師透過教學生如何規劃溫習時間，賦權予學生獨立溫習。"},{"en":"When students are empowered, they become less dependent on the teacher for every answer.","zh":"當學生被賦權，他們就不再每個答案都依賴老師。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on giving people real ability and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語重點是給人真正能力和責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"control their own learning","meaning":"掌控自己的學習","examples":[{"en":"Students are empowered to control their own learning.","zh":"學生被賦權去掌控自己的學習。"},{"en":"To control their own learning means to take responsibility for planning, monitoring, and improving how they learn.","zh":"control their own learning 指負責規劃、監察和改善自己的學習方式。"},{"en":"A student controls her own learning when she checks mistakes and chooses extra practice herself.","zh":"當學生自己檢查錯誤並選擇額外練習，她就是掌控自己的學習。"},{"en":"Team-based tasks encourage this because students must prepare and contribute without waiting passively.","zh":"團隊任務鼓勵這一點，因為學生必須準備和貢獻，而不是被動等待。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active learner responsibility.","zh":"這個短語描述主動的學習者責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"use each other as resources","meaning":"把彼此當作資源","examples":[{"en":"Students are taught to use each other as resources.","zh":"學生獲教導把彼此當作資源。"},{"en":"To use each other as resources means to learn from classmates’ knowledge, questions, and support.","zh":"use each other as resources 指從同學的知識、問題和支援中學習。"},{"en":"In a writing group, students use each other as resources by giving feedback on introductions.","zh":"在寫作小組中，學生透過就引言給予回饋，把彼此當作資源。"},{"en":"This habit helps students solve problems before relying only on the teacher.","zh":"這種習慣幫助學生在只依賴老師前先解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase treats classmates as useful sources of learning.","zh":"這個短語把同學視為有用的學習來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"accept the responsibility of","meaning":"承擔……的責任","examples":[{"en":"Students accept the responsibility of managing tasks.","zh":"學生承擔管理任務的責任。"},{"en":"To accept the responsibility of doing something means to agree that you must take care of that duty.","zh":"accept the responsibility of doing something 指同意自己必須照顧某項責任。"},{"en":"A group leader accepts the responsibility of reminding members about deadlines.","zh":"小組組長承擔提醒成員截止日期的責任。"},{"en":"Accepting responsibility helps teams work smoothly because duties are clear.","zh":"承擔責任幫助團隊順利運作，因為職責清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses duty and ownership.","zh":"這個短語強調責任和承擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"managing tasks","meaning":"管理任務","examples":[{"en":"Team members share responsibility for managing tasks.","zh":"團隊成員分擔管理任務的責任。"},{"en":"Managing tasks means organising work, setting priorities, checking progress, and finishing duties on time.","zh":"managing tasks 指組織工作、設定優次、檢查進度並準時完成職責。"},{"en":"Students manage tasks when they divide research, slides, and speaking parts before a presentation.","zh":"學生在匯報前分配資料搜集、簡報和發言部分，就是管理任務。"},{"en":"Good task management prevents last-minute panic and unfair workload.","zh":"良好任務管理防止最後一刻慌亂和工作量不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical organisation of work.","zh":"這個短語指工作的實際組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"assigned material","meaning":"指定材料","examples":[{"en":"Team members must study assigned material individually.","zh":"團隊成員必須個別學習指定材料。"},{"en":"Assigned material is reading, video, or other content that a teacher has given students to study.","zh":"assigned material 指老師要求學生學習的閱讀、影片或其他內容。"},{"en":"Before a history discussion, students may read assigned material about a war.","zh":"在歷史討論前，學生可能閱讀關於一場戰爭的指定材料。"},{"en":"Studying assigned material before class helps team discussion become deeper and faster.","zh":"課前學習指定材料幫助團隊討論變得更深入和更快。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to required learning content.","zh":"這個短語指必須學習的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"individually","meaning":"個別地","examples":[{"en":"Students must prepare individually before team activities.","zh":"學生必須在團隊活動前個別準備。"},{"en":"Individually means separately, by each person alone.","zh":"individually 指每個人分開、獨自地。"},{"en":"Students may first answer questions individually before comparing ideas in groups.","zh":"學生可能先個別回答問題，再在小組中比較想法。"},{"en":"Individual preparation makes team discussion fairer because everyone brings something to the group.","zh":"個人準備令團隊討論更公平，因為每個人都帶東西進小組。"},{"en":"The word contrasts personal work with group work.","zh":"這個詞把個人工作與小組工作作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ensure preparation for","meaning":"確保為……做好準備","examples":[{"en":"Students study assigned material to ensure preparation for classes.","zh":"學生學習指定材料，以確保為課堂做好準備。"},{"en":"To ensure preparation for something means to make sure people are ready for it.","zh":"ensure preparation for something 指確保人們為某事做好準備。"},{"en":"A teacher may give a reading task to ensure preparation for tomorrow’s debate.","zh":"老師可能給閱讀任務，以確保學生為明天辯論做好準備。"},{"en":"Preparation improves team work because members can discuss ideas instead of learning basics for the first time.","zh":"準備改善團隊工作，因為成員可以討論想法，而不是第一次學基本內容。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses readiness before an activity.","zh":"這個短語強調活動前的準備度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"individual assessment tests","meaning":"個人評估測驗","examples":[{"en":"Individual assessment tests check whether students have prepared.","zh":"個人評估測驗檢查學生是否已準備。"},{"en":"Individual assessment tests are tests completed by each student alone to measure personal understanding.","zh":"individual assessment tests 指每名學生獨自完成、用來量度個人理解的測驗。"},{"en":"A teacher may give an individual assessment test before group discussion begins.","zh":"老師可能在小組討論開始前給個人評估測驗。"},{"en":"These tests encourage preparation because each student must show their own knowledge.","zh":"這些測驗鼓勵準備，因為每名學生都必須展示自己的知識。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to personal testing, not group marks.","zh":"這個短語指個人測驗，而不是小組分數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"determine whether","meaning":"判斷是否","examples":[{"en":"Tests determine whether students understand the concepts.","zh":"測驗判斷學生是否理解概念。"},{"en":"To determine whether means to find out if something is true or not.","zh":"determine whether 指找出某事是否屬實。"},{"en":"A doctor may run tests to determine whether a patient has an infection.","zh":"醫生可能進行測試，以判斷病人是否受感染。"},{"en":"Teachers use quizzes to determine whether students are ready for harder tasks.","zh":"老師使用小測來判斷學生是否準備好做更難任務。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a yes-or-no judgement based on evidence.","zh":"這個短語引入基於證據的是非判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"understand the concepts","meaning":"理解概念","examples":[{"en":"Students must understand the concepts of the module.","zh":"學生必須理解該單元的概念。"},{"en":"To understand the concepts means to know the main ideas clearly enough to explain or use them.","zh":"understand the concepts 指清楚掌握主要想法，足以解釋或使用它們。"},{"en":"A student understands grammar concepts when she can use them in her own sentences.","zh":"當學生能在自己的句子中使用文法概念，她就是理解概念。"},{"en":"Understanding concepts is important because memorised words alone may not solve new problems.","zh":"理解概念很重要，因為單靠背誦字詞未必能解決新問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to deeper grasp of ideas.","zh":"這個短語指對想法的更深入掌握。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the module","meaning":"單元","examples":[{"en":"The tests check whether students understand the module.","zh":"測驗檢查學生是否理解該單元。"},{"en":"A module is one unit or section of a course, usually focused on a particular topic.","zh":"module 指課程中的一個單位或部分，通常集中於特定主題。"},{"en":"An IT course may have a module on databases and another on web design.","zh":"資訊科技課程可能有一個關於資料庫的單元，另一個關於網頁設計。"},{"en":"Completing one module helps students build knowledge step by step.","zh":"完成一個單元幫助學生逐步建立知識。"},{"en":"The word refers to a structured part of a course.","zh":"這個詞指課程中有結構的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"apply something to given problems","meaning":"將某物應用於指定問題","examples":[{"en":"Students must apply the concepts to given problems.","zh":"學生必須將概念應用於指定問題。"},{"en":"To apply something to given problems means to use what you have learned to solve specific tasks provided by the teacher or test.","zh":"apply something to given problems 指使用所學內容解決老師或測驗提供的具體任務。"},{"en":"A maths student applies formulas to given problems when solving exam questions.","zh":"數學學生解答考試題時，就是將公式應用於指定問題。"},{"en":"Application shows whether students can use knowledge, not only repeat definitions.","zh":"應用顯示學生是否能使用知識，而不只是重複定義。"},{"en":"The phrase connects learned ideas with specific problem-solving.","zh":"這個短語把已學想法與具體解難連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"team assessment tests","meaning":"團隊評估測驗","examples":[{"en":"Team assessment tests require students to discuss a problem.","zh":"團隊評估測驗要求學生討論一個問題。"},{"en":"Team assessment tests are tests completed by a group, where members must agree on answers or solutions.","zh":"team assessment tests 指由小組完成、成員必須就答案或解決方案達成一致的測驗。"},{"en":"In a business class, a team assessment test may ask students to choose the best marketing plan together.","zh":"在商業課中，團隊評估測驗可能要求學生一起選擇最佳市場推廣計劃。"},{"en":"These tests build discussion skills because students must explain and defend their thinking.","zh":"這些測驗培養討論技巧，因為學生必須解釋和捍衛自己的想法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to group-based assessment.","zh":"這個短語指以小組為本的評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"present a problem for discussion","meaning":"提出問題供討論","examples":[{"en":"Team tests present a problem for discussion.","zh":"團隊測驗提出問題供討論。"},{"en":"To present a problem for discussion means to give a group an issue to talk about and solve.","zh":"present a problem for discussion 指給小組一個議題，讓他們討論和解決。"},{"en":"A teacher may present a problem for discussion by asking how to reduce food waste at school.","zh":"老師可能透過詢問如何減少學校食物浪費，提出問題供討論。"},{"en":"Discussion problems help students practise reasoning, listening, and compromise.","zh":"討論問題幫助學生練習推理、聆聽和妥協。"},{"en":"The phrase describes introducing a task that needs group thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述引入需要小組思考的任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"require consensus","meaning":"要求達成共識","examples":[{"en":"Team assessment tests require consensus.","zh":"團隊評估測驗要求達成共識。"},{"en":"To require consensus means to need group members to reach a shared agreement.","zh":"require consensus 指需要小組成員達成共同協議。"},{"en":"A class committee may require consensus before choosing the theme of a school fair.","zh":"班會在選擇校園嘉年華主題前，可能要求達成共識。"},{"en":"Requiring consensus forces members to explain, listen, and compromise.","zh":"要求達成共識迫使成員解釋、聆聽和妥協。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses agreement among people, not individual answers only.","zh":"這個短語強調人與人之間的同意，而不只是個人答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"critical communication skills","meaning":"重要溝通技巧","examples":[{"en":"Consensus helps students learn critical communication skills.","zh":"共識幫助學生學習重要溝通技巧。"},{"en":"Critical communication skills are essential abilities for explaining ideas, listening, questioning, and resolving disagreement.","zh":"critical communication skills 指解釋想法、聆聽、提問和解決分歧所必需的能力。"},{"en":"A nurse needs critical communication skills to explain medicine clearly to patients.","zh":"護士需要重要溝通技巧，以向病人清楚解釋藥物。"},{"en":"Team tests build these skills because members must reach agreement under pressure.","zh":"團隊測驗培養這些技巧，因為成員必須在壓力下達成一致。"},{"en":"The phrase means communication skills that are very important, not negative criticism.","zh":"這個短語意思是非常重要的溝通技巧，而不是負面批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"enable someone to","meaning":"使某人能夠……","examples":[{"en":"Team tests enable students to deal with conflicts.","zh":"團隊測驗使學生能夠處理衝突。"},{"en":"To enable someone to do something means to make it possible for them to do it.","zh":"enable someone to do something 指使某人有可能做某事。"},{"en":"Online dictionaries enable students to check pronunciation after class.","zh":"網上字典使學生能夠在課後檢查發音。"},{"en":"Team activities enable students to practise difficult conversations before entering the workplace.","zh":"團隊活動使學生能夠在投身職場前練習困難對話。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something gives people ability or opportunity.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事給人能力或機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"deal with conflicts","meaning":"處理衝突","examples":[{"en":"Students learn to deal with conflicts between team members.","zh":"學生學習處理團隊成員之間的衝突。"},{"en":"To deal with conflicts means to handle disagreements or tensions in a practical and respectful way.","zh":"deal with conflicts 指以實際而尊重的方式處理分歧或緊張。"},{"en":"A group deals with conflict when it discusses unfair workload instead of blaming one person loudly.","zh":"小組討論工作量不公平，而不是大聲責怪一個人，就是處理衝突。"},{"en":"Handling conflict early prevents small disagreements from damaging the whole project.","zh":"及早處理衝突防止小分歧破壞整個項目。"},{"en":"The phrase describes managing disagreement, not pretending it does not exist.","zh":"這個短語描述管理分歧，而不是假裝分歧不存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"escalate to crises","meaning":"升級成危機","examples":[{"en":"Conflicts should be handled before they escalate to crises.","zh":"衝突應在升級成危機前被處理。"},{"en":"To escalate to crises means to become much more serious and turn into major problems.","zh":"escalate to crises 指變得嚴重得多，並轉化為重大問題。"},{"en":"A small misunderstanding in a group can escalate to a crisis if nobody communicates.","zh":"如果沒有人溝通，小組中的小誤會可以升級成危機。"},{"en":"Early discussion can stop tension from escalating into anger or project failure.","zh":"及早討論可以阻止緊張升級成憤怒或項目失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that unmanaged problems can grow quickly.","zh":"這個短語警告未被管理的問題可以快速變大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"written or verbal","meaning":"書面或口頭","examples":[{"en":"Team presentations may be written or verbal.","zh":"團隊匯報可以是書面或口頭。"},{"en":"Written or verbal means in writing or spoken aloud.","zh":"written or verbal 指以書寫形式或口頭說出。"},{"en":"A report is written, while an oral presentation is verbal.","zh":"報告是書面，而口頭匯報是口頭。"},{"en":"Students need both written and verbal communication because workplaces use emails, reports, meetings, and speeches.","zh":"學生需要書面和口頭溝通，因為職場使用電郵、報告、會議和演講。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts two forms of communication.","zh":"這個短語對比兩種溝通形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"build cohesion","meaning":"建立凝聚力","examples":[{"en":"Team presentations help students build cohesion.","zh":"團隊匯報幫助學生建立凝聚力。"},{"en":"To build cohesion means to create unity, trust, and connection within a group.","zh":"build cohesion 指在小組內建立團結、信任和連繫。"},{"en":"A sports team builds cohesion by training together and supporting weaker players.","zh":"運動隊透過一起訓練和支持較弱球員來建立凝聚力。"},{"en":"Shared presentations build cohesion because members must agree on one message.","zh":"共同匯報建立凝聚力，因為成員必須就同一訊息達成一致。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a group work more like one unit.","zh":"這個短語描述令小組更像一個整體地運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"share the responsibility for","meaning":"分擔……的責任","examples":[{"en":"Team members share the responsibility for presenting their viewpoint.","zh":"團隊成員分擔呈現自己觀點的責任。"},{"en":"To share the responsibility for something means several people are jointly accountable for it.","zh":"share the responsibility for something 指幾個人共同對某事負責。"},{"en":"In a group project, students share responsibility for research, slides, and speaking.","zh":"在小組項目中，學生分擔資料搜集、簡報和發言的責任。"},{"en":"Shared responsibility prevents one person from carrying the whole task alone.","zh":"分擔責任防止一個人獨自承擔整個任務。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses joint duty.","zh":"這個短語強調共同責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"persuade the audience to","meaning":"說服觀眾去……","examples":[{"en":"Students try to persuade the audience to accept their viewpoint.","zh":"學生嘗試說服觀眾接受他們的觀點。"},{"en":"To persuade the audience to do something means to convince listeners or viewers through reasons, evidence, and delivery.","zh":"persuade the audience to do something 指透過理由、證據和表達方式說服聽眾或觀眾。"},{"en":"A student may persuade the audience to support recycling by showing waste statistics and clear solutions.","zh":"學生可能透過展示浪費統計和清楚解決方案，說服觀眾支持回收。"},{"en":"Persuasion improves when the speaker understands what the audience cares about.","zh":"當講者理解觀眾關心甚麼，說服力會提高。"},{"en":"The phrase describes influencing an audience’s judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述影響觀眾判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"accept their viewpoint","meaning":"接受他們的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The team persuades the audience to accept its viewpoint.","zh":"團隊說服觀眾接受其觀點。"},{"en":"To accept a viewpoint means to agree with or be convinced by a particular opinion.","zh":"accept a viewpoint 指同意或被某一意見說服。"},{"en":"A class may accept a group’s viewpoint after hearing strong evidence in a debate.","zh":"班級在辯論中聽到有力證據後，可能接受某小組的觀點。"},{"en":"Clear examples help people accept a viewpoint because they can see how it works.","zh":"清楚例子幫助人接受觀點，因為他們能看見它如何成立。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to agreement with an opinion.","zh":"這個短語指同意某意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"feedback on","meaning":"關於……的回饋","examples":[{"en":"The facilitator gives feedback on how the team is functioning.","zh":"促進者就團隊如何運作給予回饋。"},{"en":"Feedback on something means comments or advice about how well it is working and how it can improve.","zh":"feedback on something 指關於某事運作得如何及如何改善的評論或建議。"},{"en":"A teacher gives feedback on an essay by pointing out unclear topic sentences.","zh":"老師透過指出不清楚的主題句，給予作文回饋。"},{"en":"Feedback helps teams adjust before problems become serious.","zh":"回饋幫助團隊在問題變嚴重前調整。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to useful comments about performance.","zh":"這個短語指關於表現的有用意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"how the team is functioning","meaning":"團隊如何運作","examples":[{"en":"Feedback shows how the team is functioning.","zh":"回饋顯示團隊如何運作。"},{"en":"How the team is functioning means how well the team is working together, organising tasks, and solving problems.","zh":"how the team is functioning 指團隊合作、組織任務和解決問題的情況如何。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask how the team is functioning if two members do all the work.","zh":"如果兩名成員完成所有工作，老師可能詢問團隊如何運作。"},{"en":"Understanding team functioning helps improve communication and fairness.","zh":"理解團隊運作有助改善溝通和公平。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the working health of the team.","zh":"這個短語重點是團隊的工作健康狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in terms of","meaning":"就……而言；在……方面","examples":[{"en":"The team is assessed in terms of task management and team dynamics.","zh":"團隊就任務管理和團隊動態而言受到評估。"},{"en":"In terms of means with regard to or from the viewpoint of a particular aspect.","zh":"in terms of 指就某一方面或從某一角度而言。"},{"en":"A school may judge a course in terms of student progress, cost, and satisfaction.","zh":"學校可能就學生進步、成本和滿意度評估課程。"},{"en":"Looking at a team in terms of communication helps identify different problems from looking only at grades.","zh":"從溝通方面看團隊，會識別出與只看分數不同的問題。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows evaluation to specific areas.","zh":"這個短語把評估收窄到特定範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"task management","meaning":"任務管理","examples":[{"en":"The facilitator gives feedback on task management.","zh":"促進者就任務管理給予回饋。"},{"en":"Task management is the organisation of work, deadlines, responsibilities, and progress.","zh":"task management 指對工作、截止日期、責任和進度的組織。"},{"en":"A project group practises task management when it creates a schedule and assigns roles.","zh":"項目小組制定時間表並分配角色時，就是練習任務管理。"},{"en":"Poor task management can cause missed deadlines even when students understand the topic.","zh":"即使學生理解主題，差劣任務管理也可以導致錯過截止日期。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to managing the practical side of work.","zh":"這個短語指管理工作的實際一面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"team dynamics","meaning":"團隊動態","examples":[{"en":"Team dynamics affect how well students work together.","zh":"團隊動態影響學生合作得有多好。"},{"en":"Team dynamics are the relationships, roles, communication patterns, and tensions inside a group.","zh":"team dynamics 指小組內部的關係、角色、溝通模式和緊張情況。"},{"en":"Team dynamics improve when quiet members feel safe enough to speak.","zh":"當安靜成員感到安全而能發言，團隊動態會改善。"},{"en":"Poor team dynamics can make a strong group perform badly because members do not trust one another.","zh":"差劣團隊動態可以令強小組表現差，因為成員互不信任。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how people interact within a team.","zh":"這個短語描述人們在團隊內如何互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"overall work","meaning":"整體工作表現","examples":[{"en":"The facilitator comments on the team’s overall work.","zh":"促進者評論團隊的整體工作表現。"},{"en":"Overall work means the team’s complete performance or output, not one small part only.","zh":"overall work 指團隊完整表現或成果，而不只是其中一小部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may praise a group’s overall work while still correcting weak slides.","zh":"老師可能稱讚小組整體工作表現，同時仍修正較弱簡報頁。"},{"en":"Looking at overall work helps evaluators judge quality, effort, organisation, and final result together.","zh":"查看整體工作表現，幫助評估者一併判斷質素、努力、組織和最終結果。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the whole body of work.","zh":"這個短語指整體工作成果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"application-oriented","meaning":"以應用為導向的","examples":[{"en":"Application-oriented exercises help students use concepts practically.","zh":"以應用為導向的練習幫助學生實際使用概念。"},{"en":"Application-oriented means focused on using knowledge in practical tasks.","zh":"application-oriented 指集中於在實際任務中使用知識。"},{"en":"An application-oriented grammar lesson asks students to write real emails, not only label tenses.","zh":"以應用為導向的文法課要求學生寫真實電郵，而不只是標示時態。"},{"en":"Application-oriented learning helps students transfer classroom ideas to workplace problems.","zh":"以應用為導向的學習幫助學生把課堂想法轉移到職場問題。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts practical use with theory alone.","zh":"這個短語把實際使用與單純理論作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"practical application of concepts","meaning":"概念的實際應用","examples":[{"en":"Students experience the practical application of concepts.","zh":"學生經歷概念的實際應用。"},{"en":"Practical application of concepts means using ideas in real or realistic tasks.","zh":"practical application of concepts 指在真實或現實化任務中使用想法。"},{"en":"A business student sees the practical application of concepts when she uses supply and demand to explain prices.","zh":"商科學生用供求解釋價格時，就是看見概念的實際應用。"},{"en":"Practical application makes learning memorable because students see why the concept matters.","zh":"實際應用令學習更難忘，因為學生看見概念為何重要。"},{"en":"The phrase connects understanding with use.","zh":"這個短語把理解與使用連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"learn from other students’ perspectives","meaning":"從其他學生的角度學習","examples":[{"en":"Team members learn from other students’ perspectives.","zh":"團隊成員從其他學生的角度學習。"},{"en":"To learn from other students’ perspectives means to understand ideas through classmates’ different viewpoints and experiences.","zh":"learn from other students’ perspectives 指透過同學不同觀點和經驗理解想法。"},{"en":"In a group discussion, a quiet student may learn from another student’s way of explaining a problem.","zh":"在小組討論中，安靜學生可能從另一名學生解釋問題的方式中學習。"},{"en":"Different perspectives can reveal weaknesses in an idea and make solutions stronger.","zh":"不同角度可以揭示想法中的弱點，並令解決方案更強。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses learning through viewpoint diversity.","zh":"這個短語強調透過觀點多樣性學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"especially beneficial in","meaning":"對……尤其有益","examples":[{"en":"Team-based classrooms are especially beneficial in colleges with international students.","zh":"團隊為本課堂對有國際學生的大專院校尤其有益。"},{"en":"Especially beneficial in means particularly helpful in a certain situation or place.","zh":"especially beneficial in 指在某情況或地方中特別有幫助。"},{"en":"Peer support is especially beneficial in classes where students have very different language levels.","zh":"在學生語言水平差異很大的班級中，同儕支援尤其有益。"},{"en":"Team learning can be especially beneficial when students need social connection as well as academic help.","zh":"當學生既需要社交連繫，也需要學術幫助時，團隊學習尤其有益。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a situation where the advantage is strongest.","zh":"這個短語突出優勢最強的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"listen and communicate with others","meaning":"聆聽並與他人溝通","examples":[{"en":"Team learning encourages students to listen and communicate with others.","zh":"團隊學習鼓勵學生聆聽並與他人溝通。"},{"en":"To listen and communicate with others means to hear others carefully and express your own ideas clearly.","zh":"listen and communicate with others 指仔細聆聽他人，並清楚表達自己的想法。"},{"en":"Students listen and communicate with others when they ask questions before disagreeing.","zh":"學生在不同意前先提問，就是聆聽並與他人溝通。"},{"en":"Good listening reduces conflict because people feel respected and understood.","zh":"良好聆聽減少衝突，因為人們感到被尊重和理解。"},{"en":"The phrase combines receiving ideas with expressing ideas.","zh":"這個短語結合接收想法和表達想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"share problems","meaning":"分享問題","examples":[{"en":"Students learn to share problems in a team.","zh":"學生學會在團隊中分享問題。"},{"en":"To share problems means to tell others about difficulties so the group can help solve them.","zh":"share problems 指告訴他人困難，好讓小組幫忙解決。"},{"en":"A student shares a problem when she tells teammates that she cannot understand the data.","zh":"學生告訴隊友自己不理解數據時，就是分享問題。"},{"en":"Sharing problems early prevents hidden confusion from delaying the whole project.","zh":"及早分享問題防止隱藏困惑延誤整個項目。"},{"en":"The phrase means opening up difficulties, not complaining without action.","zh":"這個短語意思是提出困難，而不是沒有行動地抱怨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"resolve personal conflicts","meaning":"解決個人衝突","examples":[{"en":"Team learning helps students resolve personal conflicts.","zh":"團隊學習幫助學生解決個人衝突。"},{"en":"To resolve personal conflicts means to settle disagreements or tensions between individuals.","zh":"resolve personal conflicts 指解決個人之間的分歧或緊張。"},{"en":"Two classmates resolve a personal conflict when they agree on a fairer division of work.","zh":"兩名同學同意更公平地分工時，就是解決個人衝突。"},{"en":"Resolving conflict builds trust because members learn they can discuss problems safely.","zh":"解決衝突建立信任，因為成員學會可以安全地討論問題。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on repairing relationships and moving forward.","zh":"這個短語重點是修復關係並繼續前進。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"manage time and resources","meaning":"管理時間和資源","examples":[{"en":"Students learn to manage time and resources.","zh":"學生學會管理時間和資源。"},{"en":"To manage time and resources means to plan how to use available hours, materials, money, and people effectively.","zh":"manage time and resources 指規劃如何有效使用可用時間、材料、金錢和人手。"},{"en":"A project team manages time and resources when it sets deadlines and decides who brings which materials.","zh":"項目團隊設定截止日期並決定誰帶哪些材料時，就是管理時間和資源。"},{"en":"Poor management can lead to rushed work and wasted effort.","zh":"管理不善可以導致匆忙完成工作和浪費努力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical planning for successful completion.","zh":"這個短語描述成功完成任務所需的實際規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a new social situation","meaning":"新的社交處境","examples":[{"en":"Team learning supports students in a new social situation.","zh":"團隊學習在新的社交處境中支援學生。"},{"en":"A new social situation is an unfamiliar setting where people must interact with others.","zh":"new social situation 指人們必須與他人互動的陌生環境。"},{"en":"A first-year student faces a new social situation when joining a class with people from many countries.","zh":"一年級學生加入一個有許多國家學生的班級時，面對新的社交處境。"},{"en":"Teamwork can make new social situations easier because students have clear tasks to discuss.","zh":"團隊合作可以令新的社交處境較容易，因為學生有清楚任務可討論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unfamiliar human interaction.","zh":"這個短語描述陌生的人際互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"social interaction","meaning":"社交互動","examples":[{"en":"Social interaction plays an important role during teamwork.","zh":"社交互動在團隊合作期間扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"Social interaction is communication and contact between people.","zh":"social interaction 指人與人之間的溝通和接觸。"},{"en":"Students have social interaction when they discuss ideas, ask questions, and help classmates.","zh":"學生討論想法、提問和幫助同學時，就是進行社交互動。"},{"en":"Good social interaction can build trust and reduce loneliness in a new class.","zh":"良好社交互動可以建立信任並減少新班級中的孤獨感。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people relating to one another.","zh":"這個短語指人們彼此建立關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"play an important role","meaning":"扮演重要角色","examples":[{"en":"Social interaction plays an important role in team learning.","zh":"社交互動在團隊學習中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"To play an important role means to be a key part of making something happen or work well.","zh":"play an important role 指在促成某事或令某事運作良好方面是關鍵部分。"},{"en":"Sleep plays an important role in memory and concentration.","zh":"睡眠在記憶和專注力方面扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"Communication plays an important role in teamwork because it keeps members aligned.","zh":"溝通在團隊合作中扮演重要角色，因為它讓成員保持一致。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a major function or influence.","zh":"這個短語突出主要功能或影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"added advantage","meaning":"額外優勢","examples":[{"en":"Team learning has an added advantage for some students.","zh":"團隊學習對某些學生有額外優勢。"},{"en":"An added advantage is an extra benefit in addition to the main benefit.","zh":"added advantage 指主要好處以外的額外好處。"},{"en":"Online lessons save travel time, and an added advantage is that recordings can be replayed.","zh":"網課節省交通時間，而額外優勢是錄影可以重看。"},{"en":"Team learning teaches content, but an added advantage is that students make friends.","zh":"團隊學習教授內容，但額外優勢是學生能結交朋友。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an extra positive point.","zh":"這個短語引入額外正面重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be comfortable in","meaning":"適應……；在……感到自在","examples":[{"en":"Some students are not comfortable in traditional classroom settings.","zh":"有些學生在傳統課堂環境中感到不自在。"},{"en":"To be comfortable in a place or situation means to feel relaxed, safe, and able to participate.","zh":"be comfortable in a place or situation 指在某地方或情況中感到放鬆、安全並能參與。"},{"en":"A shy student may feel comfortable in a small group but nervous in front of the whole class.","zh":"害羞學生可能在小組中感到自在，但在全班面前緊張。"},{"en":"Students who feel comfortable are more likely to speak and ask questions.","zh":"感到自在的學生較可能發言和提問。"},{"en":"The phrase describes emotional ease in a setting.","zh":"這個短語描述在某環境中的情緒舒適感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"traditional classroom settings","meaning":"傳統課堂環境","examples":[{"en":"Some students feel uncomfortable in traditional classroom settings.","zh":"有些學生在傳統課堂環境中感到不自在。"},{"en":"Traditional classroom settings are familiar lesson environments where teachers lead and students often listen individually.","zh":"traditional classroom settings 指熟悉的課堂環境，由老師主導，而學生通常個別聆聽。"},{"en":"In traditional classroom settings, students may sit in rows and answer questions one by one.","zh":"在傳統課堂環境中，學生可能排排坐並逐一回答問題。"},{"en":"Some learners feel anxious in these settings because attention falls on one student at a time.","zh":"有些學習者在這些環境中感到焦慮，因為注意力一次集中在一名學生身上。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts conventional lessons with team-based classrooms.","zh":"這個短語把傳統課堂與團隊為本課堂作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"students from different cultures","meaning":"來自不同文化的學生","examples":[{"en":"Teamwork helps students from different cultures understand one another.","zh":"團隊合作幫助來自不同文化的學生互相理解。"},{"en":"Students from different cultures are learners shaped by different languages, customs, values, and social habits.","zh":"students from different cultures 指受不同語言、習俗、價值觀和社會習慣塑造的學習者。"},{"en":"In an international class, students from different cultures may have different ideas about group leadership.","zh":"在國際課堂中，來自不同文化的學生可能對小組領導有不同想法。"},{"en":"Working together helps them explain differences instead of misunderstanding them.","zh":"一起合作幫助他們解釋差異，而不是誤解差異。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights cultural diversity among learners.","zh":"這個短語突出學習者之間的文化多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"understand their differences","meaning":"理解彼此的差異","examples":[{"en":"Students learn to understand their differences.","zh":"學生學習理解彼此的差異。"},{"en":"To understand their differences means to recognise and respect how people’s backgrounds, habits, or opinions are not the same.","zh":"understand their differences 指認識並尊重人們背景、習慣或意見上的不同。"},{"en":"Classmates understand their differences when they discuss why some people prefer direct feedback and others prefer softer comments.","zh":"同學討論為何有些人偏好直接回饋，而另一些人偏好較柔和評論時，就是理解彼此差異。"},{"en":"Understanding differences can reduce conflict and make cooperation smoother.","zh":"理解差異可以減少衝突並令合作更順暢。"},{"en":"The phrase means learning from diversity rather than ignoring it.","zh":"這個短語意思是從多樣性中學習，而不是忽視它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"use them productively","meaning":"有效運用它們","examples":[{"en":"Students can use their differences productively.","zh":"學生可以有效運用彼此的差異。"},{"en":"To use differences productively means to turn different skills, views, or backgrounds into useful teamwork.","zh":"use differences productively 指把不同技能、觀點或背景轉化為有用的團隊合作。"},{"en":"A group uses differences productively when one member writes well and another designs clear slides.","zh":"當一名成員擅長寫作，另一名擅長設計清晰簡報，小組就是有效運用差異。"},{"en":"Differences become productive when teams divide tasks according to strengths.","zh":"當團隊按強項分工，差異就會變得有生產力。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that diversity can be a resource.","zh":"這個短語顯示多樣性可以成為資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"express themselves freely","meaning":"自由表達自己","examples":[{"en":"Students can express themselves freely in a team context.","zh":"學生可以在團隊情境中自由表達自己。"},{"en":"To express themselves freely means to share thoughts or feelings without fear or strong restriction.","zh":"express themselves freely 指沒有恐懼或強烈限制地分享想法或感受。"},{"en":"Students may express themselves freely in a small group if classmates listen respectfully.","zh":"如果同學尊重地聆聽，學生可能在小組中自由表達自己。"},{"en":"Free expression helps teams discover problems and ideas that would otherwise stay hidden.","zh":"自由表達幫助團隊發現本來會被隱藏的問題和想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes open and confident communication.","zh":"這個短語描述開放而有信心的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in a team context","meaning":"在團隊情境中","examples":[{"en":"Students may feel safer speaking in a team context.","zh":"學生在團隊情境中發言可能感到較安全。"},{"en":"In a team context means in a situation where people are working or learning as a group.","zh":"in a team context 指在人們以小組方式工作或學習的情況中。"},{"en":"In a team context, a shy student may share ideas with three classmates before speaking to the whole class.","zh":"在團隊情境中，害羞學生可能先與三名同學分享想法，再向全班發言。"},{"en":"A team context can reduce pressure because responsibility is shared.","zh":"團隊情境可以減少壓力，因為責任被分擔。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a group-based setting.","zh":"這個短語描述以小組為基礎的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"feel singled out","meaning":"感到被單獨點名","examples":[{"en":"Students may feel singled out when answering questions alone.","zh":"學生獨自回答問題時可能感到被單獨點名。"},{"en":"To feel singled out means to feel that attention is unfairly or uncomfortably focused on you alone.","zh":"feel singled out 指感到注意力不公平或令人不舒服地只集中在自己身上。"},{"en":"A student may feel singled out if the teacher asks only her to explain a mistake in front of the class.","zh":"如果老師只要求某學生在全班面前解釋錯誤，她可能感到被單獨點名。"},{"en":"Feeling singled out can make shy students avoid participation.","zh":"感到被單獨點名可以令害羞學生避免參與。"},{"en":"The phrase describes uncomfortable individual attention.","zh":"這個短語描述令人不舒服的個別注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"answer questions in a traditional classroom","meaning":"在傳統課堂回答問題","examples":[{"en":"Some students feel singled out when answering questions in a traditional classroom.","zh":"有些學生在傳統課堂回答問題時感到被單獨點名。"},{"en":"To answer questions in a traditional classroom means to respond individually when a teacher asks questions during a conventional lesson.","zh":"answer questions in a traditional classroom 指在傳統課堂中老師提問時個別作答。"},{"en":"A student may feel nervous answering questions in a traditional classroom if everyone is watching.","zh":"如果全班都在看，學生在傳統課堂回答問題時可能感到緊張。"},{"en":"Team-based learning can reduce this pressure by letting students discuss answers first.","zh":"團隊為本學習可以讓學生先討論答案，從而減少這種壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common teacher-led classroom activity.","zh":"這個短語描述常見的教師主導課堂活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be designed to","meaning":"旨在","examples":[{"en":"This learning model was designed to prepare students for the workplace.","zh":"這種學習模式旨在讓學生準備面對職場。"},{"en":"To be designed to do something means to be planned for that purpose.","zh":"be designed to do something 指為某目的而設計。"},{"en":"A speaking exercise may be designed to help students answer interview questions confidently.","zh":"口語練習可能旨在幫助學生有信心回答面試問題。"},{"en":"If a course is designed to build teamwork, its tasks must require real cooperation.","zh":"如果課程旨在培養團隊合作，其任務必須要求真正合作。"},{"en":"The phrase explains intended purpose.","zh":"這個短語解釋預定目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"better prepare students for","meaning":"讓學生更好地準備面對……","examples":[{"en":"Team-based learning better prepares students for today’s workplace.","zh":"團隊為本學習讓學生更好地準備面對現今職場。"},{"en":"To better prepare students for something means to make them more ready for it than before or than another method would.","zh":"better prepare students for something 指令學生比以前或比另一種方法更準備好面對某事。"},{"en":"Mock interviews better prepare students for job applications by letting them practise under pressure.","zh":"模擬面試透過讓學生在壓力下練習，讓學生更好地準備求職。"},{"en":"Team-based learning prepares students because modern workplaces often require cooperation and communication.","zh":"團隊為本學習讓學生做好準備，因為現代職場通常要求合作和溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase compares readiness and improvement.","zh":"這個短語比較準備程度和改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"today’s global workplace","meaning":"現今全球化職場","examples":[{"en":"Students need teamwork skills for today’s global workplace.","zh":"學生需要現今全球化職場所需的團隊合作技能。"},{"en":"Today’s global workplace is the modern working world where people often collaborate across countries, cultures, and digital platforms.","zh":"today’s global workplace 指現代工作世界，人們通常跨國家、文化和數碼平台協作。"},{"en":"A designer in Hong Kong may work with programmers in India and clients in Canada in today’s global workplace.","zh":"在現今全球化職場中，香港設計師可能與印度程式員和加拿大客戶合作。"},{"en":"This workplace demands communication skills because teams may never meet face to face.","zh":"這種職場要求溝通技巧，因為團隊可能從未面對面見過。"},{"en":"The phrase describes modern work as international and connected.","zh":"這個短語描述現代工作具有國際性和互聯性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be encouraged to","meaning":"被鼓勵去……","examples":[{"en":"Students are encouraged to explore ideas together.","zh":"學生被鼓勵一起探索想法。"},{"en":"To be encouraged to do something means to be supported or motivated to do it.","zh":"be encouraged to do something 指得到支持或激勵去做某事。"},{"en":"Children are encouraged to ask questions when teachers welcome mistakes as part of learning.","zh":"當老師歡迎錯誤作為學習一部分，孩子會被鼓勵提問。"},{"en":"Encouragement can make students more willing to speak and try unfamiliar tasks.","zh":"鼓勵可以令學生更願意發言和嘗試陌生任務。"},{"en":"The phrase shows positive support, not force.","zh":"這個短語顯示正面支持，而不是強迫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"explore ideas together","meaning":"一起探索想法","examples":[{"en":"Team-based learning encourages students to explore ideas together.","zh":"團隊為本學習鼓勵學生一起探索想法。"},{"en":"To explore ideas together means to discuss, test, and develop thoughts as a group.","zh":"explore ideas together 指以小組方式討論、測試和發展想法。"},{"en":"Students explore ideas together when they compare possible solutions before choosing one.","zh":"學生在選擇一個方案前比較可能解決方案，就是一起探索想法。"},{"en":"Exploring ideas together can produce stronger answers because members challenge and improve one another’s thinking.","zh":"一起探索想法可以產生更強答案，因為成員挑戰並改善彼此思考。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on shared thinking.","zh":"這個短語重點是共同思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"build communication skills","meaning":"培養溝通技巧","examples":[{"en":"Students build communication skills through teamwork.","zh":"學生透過團隊合作培養溝通技巧。"},{"en":"To build communication skills means to develop the ability to listen, speak, explain, ask, and respond effectively.","zh":"build communication skills 指發展有效聆聽、說話、解釋、提問和回應的能力。"},{"en":"Group discussions build communication skills when students practise disagreeing politely.","zh":"當學生練習有禮地不同意，小組討論就能培養溝通技巧。"},{"en":"Communication skills improve when students receive feedback on both clarity and tone.","zh":"當學生收到關於清晰度和語氣的回饋，溝通技巧會改善。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual improvement in interpersonal expression.","zh":"這個短語描述人際表達能力的逐步提升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"achieve superior results","meaning":"取得更優秀成果","examples":[{"en":"Students may achieve superior results through collaboration.","zh":"學生可能透過協作取得更優秀成果。"},{"en":"To achieve superior results means to produce better outcomes than usual or better than other methods.","zh":"achieve superior results 指產生比平常或比其他方法更好的成果。"},{"en":"A team may achieve superior results when members combine research, design, and speaking skills.","zh":"當團隊成員結合資料搜集、設計和演說技巧，小組可能取得更優秀成果。"},{"en":"Collaboration can improve results because different people catch different mistakes.","zh":"協作可以改善成果，因為不同人能發現不同錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests high-quality outcomes.","zh":"這個短語暗示高質素成果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"it is likely that","meaning":"很可能","examples":[{"en":"It is likely that employers will increasingly seek these skills.","zh":"僱主很可能會越來越積極尋找這些技能。"},{"en":"It is likely that means there is a strong chance something will happen.","zh":"it is likely that 指某事有很大機會發生。"},{"en":"It is likely that students will need digital skills in most future jobs.","zh":"學生在大多數未來工作中很可能需要數碼技能。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when making a careful prediction, not a guarantee.","zh":"作者作出謹慎預測而非保證時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a probable future result.","zh":"這個短語引入可能的未來結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"increasingly seek out","meaning":"越來越積極尋找","examples":[{"en":"Employers will increasingly seek out students with teamwork skills.","zh":"僱主會越來越積極尋找具團隊合作技能的學生。"},{"en":"To increasingly seek out someone or something means to look for them more and more actively.","zh":"increasingly seek out someone or something 指越來越主動地尋找某人或某物。"},{"en":"Schools increasingly seek out teachers who can use both classroom and online tools.","zh":"學校越來越積極尋找能同時使用課堂和網上工具的老師。"},{"en":"Employers seek out teamwork skills because projects now depend on cooperation.","zh":"僱主尋找團隊合作技能，因為項目如今依賴協作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growing active demand.","zh":"這個短語描述日益增長的主動需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"as we move into the future","meaning":"隨着我們邁向未來","examples":[{"en":"These skills will become more important as we move into the future.","zh":"隨着我們邁向未來，這些技能會變得更重要。"},{"en":"As we move into the future means as time passes and society develops.","zh":"as we move into the future 指隨着時間過去和社會發展。"},{"en":"As we move into the future, students may need to work with people they never meet in person.","zh":"隨着我們邁向未來，學生可能需要與從未親身見面的人合作。"},{"en":"Future workplaces may make teamwork and digital communication even more important.","zh":"未來職場可能令團隊合作和數碼溝通更加重要。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a forward-looking idea.","zh":"這個短語引入面向未來的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete the summary below","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the summary below using words from the box.","zh":"考生使用方框中的字詞完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"Complete the summary below means fill in missing words in the short passage that follows.","zh":"complete the summary below 指填寫接下來短文中的缺漏字詞。"},{"en":"Students should complete the summary below after finding the matching information in the reading passage.","zh":"學生應在閱讀篇章中找到相應資料後，完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"This task tests whether students understand main ideas and exact wording.","zh":"這項任務測試學生是否理解主要意思和準確措辭。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"choose your answers from","meaning":"從……中選擇答案","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose their answers from the list of words.","zh":"考生從字詞列表中選擇答案。"},{"en":"Choose your answers from something means select the correct answers only from the given options.","zh":"choose your answers from something 指只從所提供選項中選擇正確答案。"},{"en":"In a vocabulary exercise, students choose their answers from a word box.","zh":"在詞彙練習中，學生從詞彙框中選擇答案。"},{"en":"This instruction prevents students from using their own words.","zh":"這項指示防止學生使用自己的字詞。"},{"en":"The phrase tells candidates where the answers must come from.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生答案必須來自哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"more words than you will need","meaning":"字詞數量多於所需","examples":[{"en":"The box contains more words than candidates will need.","zh":"方框中的字詞數量多於考生所需。"},{"en":"More words than you will need means there are extra options that should not all be used.","zh":"more words than you will need 指有額外選項，不應全部使用。"},{"en":"A grammar exercise may give ten words for six blanks, so students must choose carefully.","zh":"文法練習可能為六個空格提供十個字，所以學生必須小心選擇。"},{"en":"Extra words make the task harder because students must reject unsuitable choices.","zh":"額外字詞令任務更難，因為學生必須排除不合適選項。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that not every option is correct.","zh":"這個短語提醒不是每個選項都正確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"fill the gaps","meaning":"填補空格","examples":[{"en":"Candidates use suitable words to fill the gaps.","zh":"考生使用合適字詞填補空格。"},{"en":"To fill the gaps means to put missing words or information into blank spaces.","zh":"fill the gaps 指把缺少的字詞或資料填入空白位置。"},{"en":"Students fill the gaps in a summary by using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章字詞填補摘要中的空格。"},{"en":"Correct gap-filling requires grammar fit and accurate meaning.","zh":"正確填空需要文法配合和意思準確。"},{"en":"The phrase describes completing blanks in an exercise.","zh":"這個短語描述完成練習中的空白。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"leading career choices","meaning":"主要職業選擇","examples":[{"en":"IT is one of the leading career choices made by graduates.","zh":"資訊科技是畢業生作出的主要職業選擇之一。"},{"en":"Leading career choices are popular and important job paths chosen by many people.","zh":"leading career choices 指許多人選擇的受歡迎而重要的職業道路。"},{"en":"Healthcare may become a leading career choice when society needs more nurses and carers.","zh":"當社會需要更多護士和護理員，醫療可能成為主要職業選擇。"},{"en":"A leading career choice often reflects demand in the economy.","zh":"主要職業選擇通常反映經濟中的需求。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careers that attract many applicants.","zh":"這個短語描述吸引許多申請人的職業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the industry’s demand for","meaning":"業界對……的需求","examples":[{"en":"The industry’s demand for skilled workers exceeds supply.","zh":"業界對熟練工人的需求超過供應。"},{"en":"The industry’s demand for something means how much that sector needs it.","zh":"industry’s demand for something 指某行業需要某物的程度。"},{"en":"The restaurant industry’s demand for part-time staff rises during holidays.","zh":"餐飲業界對兼職員工的需求在假期期間上升。"},{"en":"When demand exceeds supply, companies may offer better pay to attract workers.","zh":"當需求超過供應，公司可能提供更好薪酬吸引工人。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an industry with its needs.","zh":"這個短語把某行業與其需要連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"qualified applicants","meaning":"合資格申請者","examples":[{"en":"Companies need qualified applicants for IT roles.","zh":"公司需要適合資訊科技職位的合資格申請者。"},{"en":"Qualified applicants are people who have the skills, training, or experience needed for a position.","zh":"qualified applicants 指具備某職位所需技能、培訓或經驗的人。"},{"en":"A school needs qualified applicants when hiring teachers for senior exam classes.","zh":"學校聘請高年級考試班老師時，需要合資格申請者。"},{"en":"If there are too few qualified applicants, employers may struggle to fill vacancies.","zh":"如果合資格申請者太少，僱主可能難以填補空缺。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to applicants who meet the requirements.","zh":"這個短語指符合要求的申請人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"exceed the supply of","meaning":"超過……的供應","examples":[{"en":"Demand may exceed the supply of skilled IT personnel.","zh":"需求可能超過具技能資訊科技人員的供應。"},{"en":"To exceed the supply of something means to be greater than the amount available.","zh":"exceed the supply of something 指大於可用數量。"},{"en":"Demand for masks may exceed supply during a sudden health crisis.","zh":"在突發健康危機期間，口罩需求可能超過供應。"},{"en":"When demand exceeds supply, prices or salaries may rise.","zh":"當需求超過供應，價格或薪金可能上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shortage caused by demand being higher than availability.","zh":"這個短語描述需求高於可用量所造成的短缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"skilled IT personnel","meaning":"具技能的資訊科技人員","examples":[{"en":"There is a shortage of skilled IT personnel.","zh":"缺乏具技能的資訊科技人員。"},{"en":"Skilled IT personnel are workers with strong knowledge and practical ability in information technology.","zh":"skilled IT personnel 指在資訊科技方面有強知識和實際能力的工人。"},{"en":"Skilled IT personnel can include programmers, network engineers, and data specialists.","zh":"具技能的資訊科技人員可以包括程式員、網絡工程師和數據專家。"},{"en":"Companies need skilled IT personnel to build, maintain, and protect digital systems.","zh":"公司需要具技能的資訊科技人員建立、維持和保護數碼系統。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to trained technology workers.","zh":"這個短語指受過訓練的科技工作者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"despite the current widespread use of","meaning":"儘管目前……被廣泛使用","examples":[{"en":"Despite the current widespread use of technology, employers face recruitment difficulties.","zh":"儘管目前科技被廣泛使用，僱主仍在招聘方面遇到困難。"},{"en":"Despite the current widespread use of something means although it is now used by many people.","zh":"despite the current widespread use of something 指雖然某物現在被許多人使用。"},{"en":"Despite the current widespread use of online dictionaries, students still need to learn how to choose words carefully.","zh":"儘管目前網上字典被廣泛使用，學生仍需要學習如何小心選詞。"},{"en":"Widespread use does not automatically mean there are enough skilled users.","zh":"廣泛使用不會自動代表有足夠熟練使用者。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a contrast between popularity and a remaining problem.","zh":"這個短語引入普及程度與仍然存在問題之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"computer technology","meaning":"電腦科技","examples":[{"en":"Computer technology is used in all areas of life.","zh":"電腦科技被用於生活各方面。"},{"en":"Computer technology means computers, software, networks, and digital tools used to process information.","zh":"computer technology 指用來處理資訊的電腦、軟件、網絡和數碼工具。"},{"en":"Students use computer technology when they write essays, search online, or submit homework digitally.","zh":"學生寫作文、網上搜尋或以數碼方式交功課時，就是使用電腦科技。"},{"en":"Computer technology changes daily life by speeding up communication and access to information.","zh":"電腦科技透過加快溝通和資訊取得來改變日常生活。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to technology built around computers.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞電腦建立的科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"in all areas of life","meaning":"在生活各方面","examples":[{"en":"Technology is now common in all areas of life.","zh":"科技現在在生活各方面都很常見。"},{"en":"In all areas of life means in work, school, home, travel, health, communication, and daily decisions.","zh":"in all areas of life 指在工作、學校、家庭、旅遊、健康、溝通和日常決定中。"},{"en":"Smartphones affect all areas of life, from paying bills to contacting family.","zh":"智能手機影響生活各方面，由繳費到聯絡家人都是如此。"},{"en":"When technology enters all areas of life, digital skills become basic life skills.","zh":"當科技進入生活各方面，數碼技能就變成基本生活技能。"},{"en":"The phrase means almost every part of daily living.","zh":"這個短語意思是幾乎日常生活的每一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"face difficulties recruiting","meaning":"在招聘……方面遇到困難","examples":[{"en":"Employers face difficulties recruiting skilled workers.","zh":"僱主在招聘熟練工人方面遇到困難。"},{"en":"To face difficulties recruiting means to have problems finding and hiring suitable people.","zh":"face difficulties recruiting 指在尋找和聘用合適人選方面有問題。"},{"en":"A school may face difficulties recruiting science teachers if few graduates choose teaching.","zh":"如果很少畢業生選擇教學，學校可能在招聘科學老師方面遇到困難。"},{"en":"Recruitment difficulties can delay projects and increase pressure on existing staff.","zh":"招聘困難可以延誤項目並增加現有員工壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes problems in hiring.","zh":"這個短語描述聘請人手方面的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"equip someone to","meaning":"裝備某人去……","examples":[{"en":"Education should equip graduates to work productively.","zh":"教育應裝備畢業生有效率地工作。"},{"en":"To equip someone to do something means to give them the skills, knowledge, or tools needed for it.","zh":"equip someone to do something 指給予某人所需技能、知識或工具去做某事。"},{"en":"A first-aid course equips students to respond calmly in an emergency.","zh":"急救課程裝備學生在緊急情況中冷靜應對。"},{"en":"Team-based education equips graduates to communicate and solve problems with colleagues.","zh":"團隊為本教育裝備畢業生與同事溝通和解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on practical preparation.","zh":"這個短語重點是實際準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"commence working productively","meaning":"開始有效率地工作","examples":[{"en":"Graduates are expected to commence working productively.","zh":"畢業生被期望開始有效率地工作。"},{"en":"To commence working productively means to begin doing useful and effective work.","zh":"commence working productively 指開始進行有用而有效的工作。"},{"en":"A new assistant can commence working productively if training materials are clear.","zh":"如果培訓材料清楚，新助理就能開始有效率地工作。"},{"en":"Employers prefer graduates who can contribute soon after starting the job.","zh":"僱主偏好能在入職後很快作出貢獻的畢業生。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and means to start working effectively.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是開始有效工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"without further training","meaning":"毋須進一步培訓","examples":[{"en":"Employers prefer graduates who can work without further training.","zh":"僱主偏好毋須進一步培訓就能工作的畢業生。"},{"en":"Without further training means without needing additional instruction after being hired or placed in a role.","zh":"without further training 指在被聘用或被安排到某角色後，不需要額外指導。"},{"en":"A receptionist who already knows the booking system can start work without further training.","zh":"已熟悉預約系統的接待員可以毋須進一步培訓就開始工作。"},{"en":"Working without further training saves employers time and money.","zh":"毋須進一步培訓就能工作，為僱主節省時間和金錢。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses job readiness.","zh":"這個短語強調工作準備度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"business organisations","meaning":"商業機構","examples":[{"en":"Several business organisations offer inducements to potential employees.","zh":"幾個商業機構向潛在僱員提供誘因。"},{"en":"Business organisations are companies, firms, or groups that operate for commercial purposes.","zh":"business organisations 指以商業目的運作的公司、企業或團體。"},{"en":"A business organisation may hire graduates for marketing, finance, or IT roles.","zh":"商業機構可能聘請畢業生擔任市場推廣、財務或資訊科技職位。"},{"en":"These organisations compete for talent when skilled workers are scarce.","zh":"當熟練工人稀缺，這些機構會競爭人才。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised commercial employers.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的商業僱主。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"income and other financial inducements","meaning":"收入及其他金錢誘因","examples":[{"en":"Companies offer income and other financial inducements.","zh":"公司提供收入及其他金錢誘因。"},{"en":"Income and other financial inducements are pay and money-related benefits used to attract people.","zh":"income and other financial inducements 指用來吸引人的薪酬和與金錢相關的福利。"},{"en":"A company may offer salary, bonuses, stock options, and housing support as financial inducements.","zh":"公司可能提供薪金、花紅、股票期權和住房支援作為金錢誘因。"},{"en":"Strong inducements can persuade applicants to attend interviews or accept job offers.","zh":"強金錢誘因可以說服申請人參加面試或接受工作邀請。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to money-based attractions.","zh":"這個短語指以金錢為基礎的吸引因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"potential employees","meaning":"潛在僱員","examples":[{"en":"Business organisations try to attract potential employees.","zh":"商業機構嘗試吸引潛在僱員。"},{"en":"Potential employees are people who may become workers in an organisation.","zh":"potential employees 指可能成為某機構員工的人。"},{"en":"A company may invite potential employees to an open day before recruitment begins.","zh":"公司可能在招聘開始前邀請潛在僱員參加開放日。"},{"en":"Employers offer benefits to potential employees because they want strong applicants to choose them.","zh":"僱主向潛在僱員提供福利，因為他們希望強申請者選擇自己。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to possible future staff.","zh":"這個短語指可能的未來員工。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"selection procedures","meaning":"遴選程序","examples":[{"en":"Group activities are included in selection procedures.","zh":"小組活動被包括在遴選程序中。"},{"en":"Selection procedures are the steps used to choose people for a job, course, or opportunity.","zh":"selection procedures 指用來選出工作、課程或機會人選的步驟。"},{"en":"A school’s selection procedures may include interviews, written tests, and group tasks.","zh":"學校的遴選程序可能包括面試、筆試和小組任務。"},{"en":"Group activities help employers see communication and teamwork before hiring.","zh":"小組活動幫助僱主在聘用前看見溝通和團隊合作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to formal choosing processes.","zh":"這個短語指正式選拔流程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"invite up to forty candidates","meaning":"邀請多達四十名候選人","examples":[{"en":"Companies may invite up to forty candidates for a visit.","zh":"公司可能邀請多達四十名候選人參觀。"},{"en":"To invite up to forty candidates means to ask as many as forty applicants to attend.","zh":"invite up to forty candidates 指邀請最多四十名申請人出席。"},{"en":"A university may invite up to forty candidates to a scholarship interview day.","zh":"大學可能邀請多達四十名候選人參加獎學金面試日。"},{"en":"Inviting a large group allows organisers to compare applicants in similar tasks.","zh":"邀請大群人讓組織者在相似任務中比較申請人。"},{"en":"The phrase sets the maximum number invited.","zh":"這個短語設定被邀請人數上限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"demonstrate the reality of","meaning":"展示……的實際情況","examples":[{"en":"The visit demonstrates the reality of the working environment.","zh":"該訪問展示工作環境的實際情況。"},{"en":"To demonstrate the reality of something means to show what it is actually like.","zh":"demonstrate the reality of something 指展示某事實際上是怎樣的。"},{"en":"A hospital visit can demonstrate the reality of nursing better than a brochure.","zh":"醫院參觀比宣傳冊更能展示護理工作的實際情況。"},{"en":"Real experience helps applicants understand whether the job matches their expectations.","zh":"真實經驗幫助申請人理解工作是否符合自己期望。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts real conditions with assumptions.","zh":"這個短語把真實情況與假設作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the working environment","meaning":"工作環境","examples":[{"en":"Applicants can see the real working environment.","zh":"申請人可以看見真實工作環境。"},{"en":"The working environment is the physical, social, and professional setting in which people do their jobs.","zh":"working environment 指人們工作時的實體、社交和專業環境。"},{"en":"A quiet office, friendly team, and clear management all form part of the working environment.","zh":"安靜辦公室、友善團隊和清晰管理都是工作環境的一部分。"},{"en":"A good working environment can help employees feel supported and productive.","zh":"良好工作環境可以幫助員工感到受支持並具生產力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the conditions surrounding work.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞工作的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"challenging co-operative projects","meaning":"具挑戰性的合作項目","examples":[{"en":"The job may involve challenging co-operative projects.","zh":"該工作可能涉及具挑戰性的合作項目。"},{"en":"Challenging co-operative projects are difficult tasks that require people to work together.","zh":"challenging co-operative projects 指需要人們合作完成的困難任務。"},{"en":"Designing a new app in one month can be a challenging co-operative project for an IT team.","zh":"在一個月內設計新應用程式，可以是資訊科技團隊的具挑戰性合作項目。"},{"en":"Such projects build skill because members must solve problems under pressure together.","zh":"這類項目培養技能，因為成員必須一起在壓力下解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase combines difficulty with collaboration.","zh":"這個短語結合困難和協作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"individualised tasks","meaning":"個人化任務","examples":[{"en":"The work is more likely to involve teamwork than individualised tasks.","zh":"該工作較可能涉及團隊合作，而不是個人化任務。"},{"en":"Individualised tasks are tasks designed to be completed by one person separately.","zh":"individualised tasks 指設計成由一個人分開完成的任務。"},{"en":"Writing a personal reflection is an individualised task, while building a website together is a team task.","zh":"寫個人反思是個人化任務，而一起建立網站是團隊任務。"},{"en":"Too many individualised tasks may leave students unprepared for collaborative workplaces.","zh":"太多個人化任務可能令學生未能準備好面對協作職場。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts single-person work with teamwork.","zh":"這個短語把個人工作與團隊合作作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"reflect the views of","meaning":"反映……的觀點","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether the statements reflect the views of the writer.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否反映作者的觀點。"},{"en":"To reflect the views of someone means to match or show that person’s opinions.","zh":"reflect the views of someone 指符合或顯示某人的意見。"},{"en":"A summary reflects the writer’s views when it accurately reports the argument without adding personal opinion.","zh":"摘要若準確報告論點而不加入個人意見，就是反映作者觀點。"},{"en":"Reading questions about views require attention to tone and claims, not only facts.","zh":"關於觀點的閱讀題需要注意語氣和主張，而不只是事實。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on whether an idea matches the author’s opinion.","zh":"這個短語重點是某想法是否符合作者意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A “No” answer means the statement contradicts the writer’s views.","zh":"“No” 答案表示陳述與作者觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what that person believes or claims.","zh":"contradict the views of someone 指說出與某人相信或主張相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the writer supports teamwork, a statement saying teamwork is useless may contradict the writer’s views.","zh":"如果作者支持團隊合作，陳述說團隊合作沒有用可能與作者觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students need clear evidence before deciding that a statement contradicts the author.","zh":"學生在判斷陳述與作者相矛盾前，需要清楚證據。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in Yes/No/Not Given questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 Yes/No/Not Given 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"“Not Given” means it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"“Not Given” 表示無法判斷作者怎樣想。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資訊作出判斷。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions students’ age, it is impossible to say whether they are teenagers or adults.","zh":"如果文章從未提到學生年齡，就無法判斷他們是青少年還是成年人。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when the text gives no clear evidence.","zh":"當文本沒有清楚證據，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that the answer cannot be determined from the passage.","zh":"這個短語提醒答案不能從文章中判定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"includes team-based learning in","meaning":"在……中加入團隊為本學習","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether AIU includes team-based learning in all courses.","zh":"該陳述問 AIU 是否在所有課程中加入團隊為本學習。"},{"en":"Includes team-based learning in means puts team-based learning into a course, programme, or curriculum.","zh":"includes team-based learning in 指把團隊為本學習放入課程、項目或課程內容中。"},{"en":"A school includes team-based learning in science when students complete lab tasks in groups.","zh":"學校讓學生以小組完成實驗任務時，就是在科學課中加入團隊為本學習。"},{"en":"Including teamwork in courses gives students repeated practice in collaboration.","zh":"在課程中加入團隊合作，讓學生反覆練習協作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adding team learning to an educational setting.","zh":"這個短語描述把團隊學習加入教育環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"on all its campuses","meaning":"在其所有校園","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to courses on all its campuses.","zh":"該陳述提到其所有校園的課程。"},{"en":"On all its campuses means at every campus the institution operates.","zh":"on all its campuses 指在該機構營運的每一個校園。"},{"en":"A university may offer the same library system on all its campuses.","zh":"大學可能在其所有校園提供相同圖書館系統。"},{"en":"If a policy applies on all campuses, students in different locations receive similar treatment.","zh":"如果政策適用於所有校園，不同地點的學生會得到相似對待。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses complete coverage across locations.","zh":"這個短語強調跨地點的全面涵蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the composition of teams","meaning":"團隊組成","examples":[{"en":"The composition of teams may affect team performance.","zh":"團隊組成可能影響團隊表現。"},{"en":"The composition of teams means who is included in each team and what mix of backgrounds or skills they have.","zh":"composition of teams 指每個團隊包括哪些人，以及他們的背景或技能組合如何。"},{"en":"A team with writers, designers, and speakers has a different composition from a team of only strong writers.","zh":"有作者、設計者和講者的團隊，與只有強寫作者的團隊有不同組成。"},{"en":"Good team composition can improve cooperation because members bring complementary strengths.","zh":"良好團隊組成可以改善合作，因為成員帶來互補強項。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how a team is made up.","zh":"這個短語重點是團隊如何構成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be changed regularly","meaning":"定期更改","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether teams are changed regularly.","zh":"該陳述問團隊是否定期更改。"},{"en":"To be changed regularly means to be replaced or rearranged often and at planned intervals.","zh":"be changed regularly 指經常並按計劃間隔被替換或重新安排。"},{"en":"Seating plans may be changed regularly so students work with different classmates.","zh":"座位表可能定期更改，讓學生與不同同學合作。"},{"en":"Regular changes can increase variety, but they may also prevent long-term trust from forming.","zh":"定期更改可以增加多樣性，但也可能阻礙長期信任形成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated adjustment over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間反覆調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"theoretical problems","meaning":"理論問題","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to theoretical problems in team activities.","zh":"該陳述提到團隊活動中的理論問題。"},{"en":"Theoretical problems are problems about ideas, principles, or concepts rather than direct practical action.","zh":"theoretical problems 指關於想法、原則或概念的問題，而不是直接實際行動。"},{"en":"A philosophy class may discuss theoretical problems about justice and freedom.","zh":"哲學課可能討論關於公義和自由的理論問題。"},{"en":"Team-based IT activities often focus on applying concepts, not only discussing theoretical problems.","zh":"團隊為本資訊科技活動通常集中於應用概念，而不只是討論理論問題。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts abstract issues with practical tasks.","zh":"這個短語把抽象議題與實際任務作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"team activity","meaning":"團隊活動","examples":[{"en":"Application-based tasks are an important team activity.","zh":"應用為本任務是重要的團隊活動。"},{"en":"A team activity is a task completed by a group of people working together.","zh":"team activity 指由一組人合作完成的任務。"},{"en":"Preparing a group presentation is a common team activity in school.","zh":"準備小組匯報是學校中常見的團隊活動。"},{"en":"Team activities teach students to divide work, discuss ideas, and manage time.","zh":"團隊活動教學生分工、討論想法和管理時間。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to structured group work.","zh":"這個短語指有結構的小組工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"participate in assessment","meaning":"參與評估","examples":[{"en":"Team members participate in assessment of one another.","zh":"團隊成員參與彼此的評估。"},{"en":"To participate in assessment means to take part in judging or evaluating performance.","zh":"participate in assessment 指參與判斷或評價表現。"},{"en":"Students participate in assessment when they give marks and comments on classmates’ group work.","zh":"學生為同學小組工作給分和評論時，就是參與評估。"},{"en":"Participation in assessment can make students more aware of fair contribution.","zh":"參與評估可以令學生更意識到公平貢獻。"},{"en":"The phrase describes involvement in evaluation.","zh":"這個短語描述參與評價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"other team members","meaning":"其他團隊成員","examples":[{"en":"Students assess the work of other team members.","zh":"學生評估其他團隊成員的工作。"},{"en":"Other team members are the remaining people in the same group, apart from oneself.","zh":"other team members 指同一小組中除自己以外的其他人。"},{"en":"A student may ask other team members whether the presentation slides are clear.","zh":"學生可能詢問其他團隊成員簡報是否清楚。"},{"en":"Team success depends on how well members support and assess one another.","zh":"團隊成功取決於成員支援和評估彼此的程度。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to classmates or colleagues in the same team.","zh":"這個短語指同一團隊中的同學或同事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"prefer traditional classroom learning to","meaning":"較喜歡……而不是……","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether international students prefer traditional classroom learning to team-based learning.","zh":"該陳述問國際學生是否較喜歡傳統課堂學習而不是團隊為本學習。"},{"en":"To prefer A to B means to like or choose A more than B.","zh":"prefer A to B 指比起 B 更喜歡或選擇 A。"},{"en":"Some students prefer written feedback to verbal feedback because they can read it again.","zh":"有些學生較喜歡書面回饋而不是口頭回饋，因為可以重看。"},{"en":"Preference may depend on culture, confidence, language level, and previous schooling.","zh":"偏好可能取決於文化、信心、語言水平和以往 schooling。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly compares two choices.","zh":"這個短語清楚比較兩個選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"choose one phrase from","meaning":"從……中選擇一個短語","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose one phrase from the list of phrases.","zh":"考生從短語列表中選擇一個短語。"},{"en":"Choose one phrase from something means select a single phrase from the options provided.","zh":"choose one phrase from something 指從提供的選項中選擇一個短語。"},{"en":"In a sentence-completion task, students choose one phrase from a box to finish each sentence.","zh":"在句子完成題中，學生從方框中選擇一個短語完成每句。"},{"en":"This instruction means candidates should not invent their own wording.","zh":"這項指示表示考生不應自行創造措辭。"},{"en":"The phrase tells students the source and number of answers.","zh":"這個短語告訴學生答案的來源和數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"complete each sentence","meaning":"完成每個句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete each sentence with a suitable phrase.","zh":"考生使用合適短語完成每個句子。"},{"en":"Complete each sentence means fill in every unfinished sentence so that it becomes grammatically and logically complete.","zh":"complete each sentence 指填補每個未完成句子，使其在文法和邏輯上完整。"},{"en":"Students complete each sentence by checking both meaning and grammar.","zh":"學生透過檢查意思和文法來完成每個句子。"},{"en":"A phrase may be wrong if it fits the meaning but breaks the grammar.","zh":"如果短語意思合適但破壞文法，它仍可能是錯的。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction in sentence-completion tasks.","zh":"這個短語是句子完成題中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"not use all of them","meaning":"不會全部用上","examples":[{"en":"There are more phrases than questions, so candidates will not use all of them.","zh":"短語比題目多，所以考生不會全部用上。"},{"en":"Not use all of them means some options are extra and should be left unused.","zh":"not use all of them 指有些選項是額外的，應留下不用。"},{"en":"A matching exercise may give eight endings for five sentences, so students will not use all of them.","zh":"配對練習可能為五個句子提供八個句尾，所以學生不會全部用上。"},{"en":"Extra choices make students compare meaning more carefully.","zh":"額外選項令學生更仔細比較意思。"},{"en":"The phrase warns candidates not to force every option into an answer.","zh":"這個短語提醒考生不要硬把每個選項都放進答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"compete with other teams","meaning":"與其他團隊競爭","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions competing with other teams.","zh":"該選項提到與其他團隊競爭。"},{"en":"To compete with other teams means to try to perform better than other groups.","zh":"compete with other teams 指試圖比其他小組表現更好。"},{"en":"A debate team competes with other teams by presenting stronger arguments.","zh":"辯論隊透過提出更強論點與其他團隊競爭。"},{"en":"Competition can motivate students, but it may also reduce cooperation if poorly managed.","zh":"競爭可以激勵學生，但若管理不善，也可能減少合作。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on rivalry between groups.","zh":"這個短語重點是小組之間的競爭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"as judged by","meaning":"由……評定","examples":[{"en":"The teams may be judged by the facilitator.","zh":"團隊可能由促進者評定。"},{"en":"As judged by someone means according to that person’s evaluation.","zh":"as judged by someone 指根據某人的評估。"},{"en":"A presentation may be successful as judged by the teacher and audience feedback.","zh":"一次匯報是否成功，可能由老師和觀眾回饋評定。"},{"en":"Who judges the work affects what criteria are used.","zh":"由誰評定作品，會影響使用哪些標準。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the evaluator.","zh":"這個短語指出評估者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"individual tests and exams","meaning":"個人測驗及考試","examples":[{"en":"Students may be assessed by individual tests and exams.","zh":"學生可能透過個人測驗及考試接受評估。"},{"en":"Individual tests and exams are assessments completed by each student alone.","zh":"individual tests and exams 指每名學生獨自完成的評估。"},{"en":"A student takes an individual exam when she answers questions without help from classmates.","zh":"學生在沒有同學幫助下回答問題，就是參加個人考試。"},{"en":"Individual assessment checks personal understanding even in a team-based course.","zh":"即使在團隊為本課程中，個人評估也檢查個人理解。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts personal testing with group assessment.","zh":"這個短語把個人測試與小組評估作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"the strongest point of view","meaning":"最強烈的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to the strongest point of view in the group.","zh":"該選項指小組中最強烈的觀點。"},{"en":"The strongest point of view is the most convincing or forcefully supported opinion.","zh":"strongest point of view 指最有說服力或最有力支持的意見。"},{"en":"In a debate group, the strongest point of view may be the one with the clearest evidence.","zh":"在辯論小組中，最強觀點可能是有最清楚證據的觀點。"},{"en":"A team should not simply accept the loudest view; it should test which view is strongest.","zh":"團隊不應只接受最大聲的觀點；它應測試哪個觀點最有力。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on argument strength, not volume.","zh":"這個短語重點是論點強度，而不是音量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"by their peers","meaning":"由同儕評估","examples":[{"en":"Students may be assessed by their peers.","zh":"學生可能由同儕評估。"},{"en":"By their peers means by people of the same group, level, or status, such as classmates.","zh":"by their peers 指由同一群體、層級或身份的人評估，例如同學。"},{"en":"A student’s group contribution may be rated by peers who worked with her.","zh":"學生的小組貢獻可能由曾與她合作的同儕評分。"},{"en":"Peer assessment can reveal effort that the teacher may not see.","zh":"同儕評估可以揭示老師未必看見的努力。"},{"en":"The phrase means evaluation by equals, not by superiors only.","zh":"這個短語指由平輩評估，而不只是由上級評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"as a team","meaning":"以團隊形式","examples":[{"en":"Students may also be assessed as a team.","zh":"學生也可能以團隊形式接受評估。"},{"en":"As a team means together as one group rather than separately as individuals.","zh":"as a team 指作為一個小組一起，而不是作為個人分開。"},{"en":"Students present as a team when each member contributes to one shared presentation.","zh":"當每名成員為一個共同匯報作出貢獻，學生就是以團隊形式匯報。"},{"en":"Assessment as a team encourages members to support one another and coordinate work.","zh":"以團隊形式評估鼓勵成員互相支持和協調工作。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses group identity and shared performance.","zh":"這個短語強調小組身份和共同表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"the development of communication skills","meaning":"溝通技巧的發展","examples":[{"en":"Consensus assists in the development of communication skills.","zh":"共識有助於溝通技巧的發展。"},{"en":"The development of communication skills is the process of improving how people listen, speak, explain, and respond.","zh":"development of communication skills 指人們在聆聽、說話、解釋和回應方面逐漸改善的過程。"},{"en":"Group discussion supports the development of communication skills because students practise real interaction.","zh":"小組討論支持溝通技巧的發展，因為學生練習真實互動。"},{"en":"Communication skills develop when learners receive feedback and try again.","zh":"當學習者收到回饋並再次嘗試，溝通技巧就會發展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual improvement in communication ability.","zh":"這個短語描述溝通能力的逐步改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"put theory into practice","meaning":"將理論付諸實踐","examples":[{"en":"Team activities help students put theory into practice.","zh":"團隊活動幫助學生將理論付諸實踐。"},{"en":"To put theory into practice means to use learned ideas in real or realistic situations.","zh":"put theory into practice 指在真實或現實化情境中使用已學想法。"},{"en":"A business student puts theory into practice by using marketing concepts to design an advertisement.","zh":"商科學生使用市場推廣概念設計廣告時，就是將理論付諸實踐。"},{"en":"Practising theory helps students understand its limits and usefulness.","zh":"實踐理論幫助學生理解其限制和用途。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts doing with merely knowing.","zh":"這個短語把實踐與單純知道作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"assist international and non-traditional students","meaning":"協助國際及非傳統學生","examples":[{"en":"Team-based classrooms may assist international and non-traditional students.","zh":"團隊為本課堂可能協助國際及非傳統學生。"},{"en":"To assist international and non-traditional students means to help students from overseas or from less typical educational paths.","zh":"assist international and non-traditional students 指幫助來自海外或較非典型教育路徑的學生。"},{"en":"A mature student returning to study after work may benefit from group support.","zh":"工作後重返學習的成年學生可能從小組支援中得益。"},{"en":"Team-based classrooms assist these students by creating social connection and shared learning.","zh":"團隊為本課堂透過創造社交連繫和共同學習來協助這些學生。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on support for students who may need extra adjustment.","zh":"這個短語重點是支援可能需要額外適應的學生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"get to know new friends and colleagues","meaning":"認識新朋友和同伴","examples":[{"en":"Teamwork can help students get to know new friends and colleagues.","zh":"團隊合作可以幫助學生認識新朋友和同伴。"},{"en":"To get to know new friends and colleagues means to become familiar with people you may study or work with.","zh":"get to know new friends and colleagues 指逐漸熟悉你可能一起學習或工作的人。"},{"en":"A new student gets to know classmates by completing a group task with them.","zh":"新生透過與同學完成小組任務來認識他們。"},{"en":"Knowing friends and colleagues makes teamwork easier because trust grows.","zh":"認識朋友和同伴令團隊合作更容易，因為信任會增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes building relationships through shared activity.","zh":"這個短語描述透過共同活動建立關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"students’ work is assessed","meaning":"學生的作業受到評估","examples":[{"en":"Students’ work is assessed individually, by peers and as a team.","zh":"學生的作業以個人、同儕和團隊形式受到評估。"},{"en":"Students’ work is assessed means their assignments, tests, or performance are evaluated.","zh":"students’ work is assessed 指他們的作業、測驗或表現受到評價。"},{"en":"A teacher assesses students’ work by checking accuracy, effort, and improvement.","zh":"老師透過檢查準確度、努力和進步來評估學生作業。"},{"en":"When work is assessed in several ways, it can capture both personal and group contribution.","zh":"當作業以幾種方式評估，就能同時捕捉個人和小組貢獻。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to formal judgement of learning.","zh":"這個短語指對學習的正式判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"make a joint presentation","meaning":"作聯合匯報","examples":[{"en":"The teams make a joint presentation to share their viewpoint.","zh":"團隊作聯合匯報以分享其觀點。"},{"en":"To make a joint presentation means to give one presentation together as a group.","zh":"make a joint presentation 指以小組形式一起作一個匯報。"},{"en":"Students make a joint presentation when each member explains one section of the same topic.","zh":"當每名成員解釋同一主題的一個部分，學生就是作聯合匯報。"},{"en":"Joint presentations require planning because the speakers must sound connected, not separate.","zh":"聯合匯報需要規劃，因為講者聽起來必須相互連接，而不是各自分開。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shared public speaking.","zh":"這個短語描述共同公開發言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"the need to achieve consensus","meaning":"達成共識的需要","examples":[{"en":"The need to achieve consensus helps students communicate effectively.","zh":"達成共識的需要幫助學生有效溝通。"},{"en":"The need to achieve consensus means the requirement for group members to reach agreement.","zh":"need to achieve consensus 指小組成員必須達成一致的要求。"},{"en":"A committee feels the need to achieve consensus before announcing a new school policy.","zh":"委員會在公布新校政前會感到達成共識的需要。"},{"en":"This need encourages listening because members cannot finish until they agree.","zh":"這種需要鼓勵聆聽，因為成員在達成一致前不能完成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how shared decision-making creates communication pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述共同決策如何創造溝通壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 75 - TEAM-BASED LEARNING.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 76":[{"front":"the hemp revival","meaning":"工業大麻復興","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes the hemp revival as a return of interest in an old industrial crop.","zh":"文章把工業大麻復興描述為人們重新關注一種古老工業作物。"},{"en":"The hemp revival means hemp is becoming important again after a long period of decline.","zh":"hemp revival 指工業大麻在長期衰落後再次變得重要。"},{"en":"A town may experience a hemp revival if farmers start growing hemp for textiles and building materials again.","zh":"如果農民重新種植工業大麻，用於紡織品和建築材料，城鎮可能經歷工業大麻復興。"},{"en":"Rising interest in renewable resources can help cause the hemp revival.","zh":"人們對可再生資源的興趣增加，可以促成工業大麻復興。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an old crop returns because people discover new uses for it.","zh":"當一種古老作物因新用途被重新發現而回歸時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hemp plant","meaning":"工業大麻植物","examples":[{"en":"The hemp plant is one of the world’s oldest industrial resources.","zh":"工業大麻植物是世界上最古老的工業資源之一。"},{"en":"A hemp plant is a type of cannabis grown mainly for fibre, seeds, and industrial uses.","zh":"hemp plant 指主要為纖維、種子和工業用途而種植的一種大麻植物。"},{"en":"Farmers may grow the hemp plant to make rope, cloth, paper, or building panels.","zh":"農民可能種植工業大麻植物來製造繩索、布料、紙張或建築板材。"},{"en":"Because many parts of the plant can be used, hemp can support several industries.","zh":"由於植物許多部分都可使用，工業大麻可以支援多個產業。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about hemp as a crop, not as a drug.","zh":"當談論工業大麻作為農作物，而不是毒品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one of the world’s oldest","meaning":"世界上最古老的……之一","examples":[{"en":"Hemp is one of the world’s oldest industrial resources.","zh":"工業大麻是世界上最古老的工業資源之一。"},{"en":"One of the world’s oldest means among the earliest known examples in human history.","zh":"one of the world’s oldest 指屬於人類歷史中已知最早的例子之一。"},{"en":"Rice is one of the world’s oldest food crops because people have grown it for thousands of years.","zh":"稻米是世界上最古老的糧食作物之一，因為人類已種植它數千年。"},{"en":"Calling something one of the world’s oldest shows it has a long historical importance.","zh":"稱某物為世界上最古老之一，表示它有悠久歷史重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing that something has existed for a very long time.","zh":"強調某物已存在很長時間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"industrial resources","meaning":"工業資源","examples":[{"en":"Hemp has long been used as an industrial resource.","zh":"工業大麻長久以來被用作工業資源。"},{"en":"Industrial resources are materials used to make products, support production, or supply industry.","zh":"industrial resources 指用來製造產品、支援生產或供應工業的材料。"},{"en":"Wood, cotton, oil, and metal are industrial resources because factories can turn them into useful goods.","zh":"木材、棉花、石油和金屬都是工業資源，因為工廠可以把它們製成有用商品。"},{"en":"When an industrial resource becomes cheaper or cleaner, businesses may start using it more.","zh":"當一種工業資源變得更便宜或更環保，企業可能開始更多使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing materials that support manufacturing.","zh":"討論支援製造業的材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"is back","meaning":"重新受到重視；回歸","examples":[{"en":"The hemp plant is back as an important industrial material.","zh":"工業大麻植物作為重要工業材料重新受到重視。"},{"en":"Is back means has returned after being absent, unpopular, or less important for a time.","zh":"is back 指某事物在一段時間缺席、不流行或不重要後回歸。"},{"en":"Vinyl records are back because some music fans enjoy their sound and physical feel.","zh":"黑膠唱片重新流行，因為有些音樂愛好者喜歡其聲音和實體質感。"},{"en":"Something may come back when people rediscover its value or need it for new reasons.","zh":"當人們重新發現某物價值，或因新原因需要它，它可能回歸。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an old trend, product, or idea becomes popular again.","zh":"當舊潮流、產品或想法再次受歡迎時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rediscovery of","meaning":"對……的重新發現","examples":[{"en":"The rediscovery of hemp has made it important again.","zh":"對工業大麻的重新發現令它再次重要。"},{"en":"The rediscovery of something means people begin to notice its value again after forgetting or ignoring it.","zh":"rediscovery of something 指人們在忘記或忽視某物後，重新注意到它的價值。"},{"en":"The rediscovery of local crafts can help young people respect traditional skills.","zh":"對本地手工藝的重新發現，可以幫助年輕人尊重傳統技藝。"},{"en":"Rediscovery often happens when old knowledge solves a modern problem.","zh":"當舊知識解決現代問題，重新發現常會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something old becomes useful again.","zh":"當舊事物再次變得有用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"renewable resource","meaning":"可再生資源","examples":[{"en":"Hemp is a renewable resource with many industrial uses.","zh":"工業大麻是一種有多種工業用途的可再生資源。"},{"en":"A renewable resource is a natural material that can be replaced or grown again in a reasonable time.","zh":"renewable resource 指可以在合理時間內再生或重新種植的天然材料。"},{"en":"Bamboo is a renewable resource because it grows quickly and can be harvested repeatedly.","zh":"竹是一種可再生資源，因為它生長快速並可反覆收割。"},{"en":"Renewable resources can reduce pressure on materials that take much longer to replace.","zh":"可再生資源可以減少對需要更長時間補充的材料的壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing cleaner or more sustainable materials.","zh":"討論更潔淨或更可持續的材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fibre of choice","meaning":"首選纖維","examples":[{"en":"Hemp is becoming the fibre of choice for future textiles.","zh":"工業大麻正成為未來紡織品的首選纖維。"},{"en":"Fibre of choice means the preferred fibre for a particular use.","zh":"fibre of choice 指某用途中的優先或首選纖維。"},{"en":"Cotton is often the fibre of choice for T-shirts because it is soft and familiar.","zh":"棉花常是 T 恤的首選纖維，因為它柔軟且大家熟悉。"},{"en":"A fibre becomes the fibre of choice when it performs well and meets market needs.","zh":"當一種纖維表現良好並符合市場需要，它就會成為首選纖維。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one material is preferred over others.","zh":"當一種材料比其他材料更受偏好時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"future textiles","meaning":"未來紡織品","examples":[{"en":"Hemp may become important in future textiles.","zh":"工業大麻可能在未來紡織品中變得重要。"},{"en":"Future textiles are fabrics and cloth products that may be widely used in the coming years.","zh":"future textiles 指未來數年可能被廣泛使用的布料和紡織產品。"},{"en":"Future textiles may need to be stronger, lighter, cheaper, and more environmentally friendly.","zh":"未來紡織品可能需要更堅韌、更輕、更便宜和更環保。"},{"en":"New consumer demands can push companies to search for better fibres for future textiles.","zh":"新的消費者需求可以推動公司為未來紡織品尋找更好纖維。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing materials for tomorrow’s clothing and fabrics.","zh":"討論未來衣物和布料材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"personal care products","meaning":"個人護理產品","examples":[{"en":"Hemp can be used in personal care products.","zh":"工業大麻可以用於個人護理產品。"},{"en":"Personal care products are items people use on the body for cleaning, skin care, hair care, or hygiene.","zh":"personal care products 指人們用在身體上作清潔、護膚、護髮或衛生用途的物品。"},{"en":"Shampoo, soap, lotion, toothpaste, and face cream are personal care products.","zh":"洗頭水、肥皂、潤膚露、牙膏和面霜都是個人護理產品。"},{"en":"Natural ingredients can make personal care products more attractive to health-conscious consumers.","zh":"天然成分可以令個人護理產品更吸引注重健康的消費者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing everyday body-care goods.","zh":"討論日常身體護理用品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"building materials","meaning":"建築材料","examples":[{"en":"Hemp is used in building materials, paper and fuel.","zh":"工業大麻用於建築材料、紙張和燃料。"},{"en":"Building materials are substances used to construct houses, schools, offices, and other structures.","zh":"building materials 指用來建造房屋、學校、辦公室和其他結構的物質。"},{"en":"Wood, concrete, glass, steel, and bricks are common building materials.","zh":"木材、混凝土、玻璃、鋼和磚都是常見建築材料。"},{"en":"Stronger or lighter building materials can reduce costs and improve safety.","zh":"更堅固或更輕的建築材料可以降低成本並改善安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing construction and housing.","zh":"討論建築和房屋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"grown for","meaning":"為……而種植","examples":[{"en":"Hemp has been grown for paper, textiles, food and medicine.","zh":"工業大麻一直為紙張、紡織品、食物和醫藥而種植。"},{"en":"Grown for something means cultivated in order to produce or supply that thing.","zh":"grown for something 指為了生產或供應某物而栽培。"},{"en":"Some flowers are grown for perfume, while others are grown for decoration.","zh":"有些花為香水而種植，另一些則為裝飾而種植。"},{"en":"Farmers choose what crops are grown for according to market demand and climate.","zh":"農民會根據市場需求和氣候決定作物為甚麼而種植。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the purpose of growing a plant.","zh":"解釋種植植物的目的時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"throughout human history","meaning":"貫穿人類歷史","examples":[{"en":"Hemp has been used throughout human history.","zh":"工業大麻貫穿人類歷史一直被使用。"},{"en":"Throughout human history means across many periods from ancient times to the present.","zh":"throughout human history 指從古代到現在跨越許多時期。"},{"en":"People have used fire for cooking, warmth, and protection throughout human history.","zh":"貫穿人類歷史，人們使用火來烹飪、取暖和保護自己。"},{"en":"If something appears throughout human history, it has been useful to many societies.","zh":"如果某事物貫穿人類歷史出現，它對許多社會都很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing very long-term human use.","zh":"強調人類長期使用某物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"earliest known","meaning":"已知最早的","examples":[{"en":"The earliest known woven fabric was made of hemp.","zh":"已知最早的編織布料由工業大麻製成。"},{"en":"Earliest known means the oldest example that people have discovered or recorded so far.","zh":"earliest known 指到目前為止人們已發現或記錄的最古老例子。"},{"en":"The earliest known writing systems help historians understand ancient trade and government.","zh":"已知最早的書寫系統幫助歷史學家了解古代貿易和政府。"},{"en":"New discoveries can change what experts call the earliest known example.","zh":"新發現可以改變專家所稱的已知最早例子。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing ancient evidence.","zh":"討論古代證據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"woven fabric","meaning":"編織布料","examples":[{"en":"The earliest known woven fabric was made of hemp.","zh":"已知最早的編織布料由工業大麻製成。"},{"en":"Woven fabric is cloth made by crossing threads over and under one another.","zh":"woven fabric 指透過把線一上一下交叉織成的布料。"},{"en":"Shirts, curtains, bags, and tablecloths can all be made from woven fabric.","zh":"恤衫、窗簾、袋和桌布都可以由編織布料製成。"},{"en":"Strong fibres help woven fabric last longer under daily use.","zh":"堅韌纖維有助編織布料在日常使用中更耐用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing cloth and textile production.","zh":"討論布料和紡織品生產時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"made of hemp","meaning":"由工業大麻製成","examples":[{"en":"The earliest known woven fabric was made of hemp.","zh":"已知最早的編織布料由工業大麻製成。"},{"en":"Made of hemp means produced using hemp fibre, seeds, or other parts of the hemp plant.","zh":"made of hemp 指使用工業大麻纖維、種子或植物其他部分製成。"},{"en":"A bag made of hemp may be strong enough for daily shopping.","zh":"由工業大麻製成的袋可能足夠堅韌，適合日常購物。"},{"en":"Products made of hemp can reduce dependence on less renewable materials.","zh":"由工業大麻製成的產品可以減少對較不可再生材料的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying the material used to make something.","zh":"說明某物使用甚麼材料製成時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"dates back to","meaning":"追溯至……","examples":[{"en":"The earliest known hemp fabric dates back to the eighth millennium BC.","zh":"已知最早的工業大麻布料可追溯至公元前第八個千禧年。"},{"en":"Dates back to means began or existed at a particular time in the past.","zh":"dates back to 指開始於或存在於過去某一時間。"},{"en":"This village temple dates back to the seventeenth century.","zh":"這座村廟可追溯至十七世紀。"},{"en":"When something dates back far in history, it may have cultural or archaeological value.","zh":"當某物可追溯至很久以前，它可能有文化或考古價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how old something is.","zh":"解釋某物有多古老時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the eighth millennium","meaning":"第八個千禧年","examples":[{"en":"The earliest hemp fabric dates back to the eighth millennium BC.","zh":"最早的工業大麻布料可追溯至公元前第八個千禧年。"},{"en":"The eighth millennium means a period of one thousand years, usually referring here to about 8000 to 7001 BC.","zh":"eighth millennium 指一千年的時段，這裏通常指約公元前8000年至公元前7001年。"},{"en":"Archaeologists use terms like the eighth millennium when discussing very ancient evidence.","zh":"考古學家討論非常古老的證據時，會使用第八個千禧年這類說法。"},{"en":"Such dating shows that a material or practice existed extremely early in human history.","zh":"這種年代標示顯示某材料或做法在人類歷史中極早已存在。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reading about ancient periods.","zh":"閱讀古代時期相關內容時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the majority of","meaning":"大部分……","examples":[{"en":"The majority of sails, clothes and rope were once made from hemp.","zh":"大部分船帆、衣物和繩索曾經由工業大麻製成。"},{"en":"The majority of something means most of it, or more than half.","zh":"the majority of something 指某物的大部分，或超過一半。"},{"en":"The majority of students in the class chose the simpler writing topic.","zh":"班中大部分學生選擇較簡單的寫作題目。"},{"en":"When the majority of a product once came from one material, that material was clearly important.","zh":"當某產品大部分曾來自一種材料，那種材料明顯很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing what is most common.","zh":"描述最常見情況時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sails","meaning":"船帆","examples":[{"en":"Many sails were historically made from hemp.","zh":"歷史上許多船帆由工業大麻製成。"},{"en":"Sails are large pieces of strong cloth used to catch wind and move a boat or ship.","zh":"sails 指用來捕捉風力並推動船隻的大塊堅韌布料。"},{"en":"A sailing club must repair its sails if the cloth tears in strong wind.","zh":"如果布料在強風中撕裂，帆船會必須修補船帆。"},{"en":"Strong fibres are important because sails face wind, water, and constant pulling.","zh":"堅韌纖維很重要，因為船帆要承受風、水和持續拉力。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing ships and traditional materials.","zh":"討論船隻和傳統材料時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tents","meaning":"帳篷","examples":[{"en":"Hemp was used to make tents and rugs.","zh":"工業大麻曾被用來製作帳篷和地氈。"},{"en":"Tents are portable shelters made from fabric and poles, often used for camping or outdoor work.","zh":"tents 指由布料和支架製成的可移動遮蔽物，常用於露營或戶外工作。"},{"en":"Students may sleep in tents during a school camp.","zh":"學生可能在學校營中睡在帳篷裏。"},{"en":"Tent fabric must be strong enough to resist wind, rain, and repeated packing.","zh":"帳篷布料必須足夠堅韌，以抵擋風雨和反覆收納。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing outdoor equipment.","zh":"討論戶外裝備時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rugs","meaning":"地氈；小地毯","examples":[{"en":"Rugs were among the many products made from hemp.","zh":"地氈是許多由工業大麻製成的產品之一。"},{"en":"Rugs are small or medium-sized floor coverings made from thick fabric or woven material.","zh":"rugs 指由厚布或編織材料製成的小型或中型地面覆蓋物。"},{"en":"A family may place rugs in the living room to make the floor warmer and more comfortable.","zh":"家庭可能在客廳放地氈，令地面更溫暖和舒適。"},{"en":"Durable fibres help rugs survive foot traffic and regular cleaning.","zh":"耐用纖維幫助地氈承受人流和定期清潔。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing household textiles.","zh":"討論家居紡織品時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rope","meaning":"繩索","examples":[{"en":"Hemp was commonly used to make rope.","zh":"工業大麻常被用來製作繩索。"},{"en":"Rope is a thick strong cord made by twisting fibres together.","zh":"rope 指把纖維扭在一起製成的粗而堅韌的繩。"},{"en":"Workers may use rope to tie boxes, pull equipment, or secure a tent.","zh":"工人可能用繩索綁箱、拉設備或固定帳篷。"},{"en":"Rope needs strong fibres because it often carries weight or pressure.","zh":"繩索需要堅韌纖維，因為它常承受重量或壓力。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing practical materials for tying and lifting.","zh":"討論捆綁和吊運用實用材料時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"twine","meaning":"細繩；麻線","examples":[{"en":"Hemp was used to produce rope and twine.","zh":"工業大麻曾被用來生產繩索和細繩。"},{"en":"Twine is a thin strong string made by twisting fibres together.","zh":"twine 指把纖維扭在一起製成的幼而堅韌的線。"},{"en":"A gardener may use twine to tie young plants to wooden sticks.","zh":"園丁可能用細繩把幼苗綁在木棍上。"},{"en":"Twine is useful because it is light, flexible, and easy to cut.","zh":"細繩有用，因為它輕、靈活且容易剪開。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing simple tying materials.","zh":"討論簡單捆綁材料時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"art canvas","meaning":"畫布","examples":[{"en":"Art canvas was once commonly made from hemp.","zh":"畫布曾經常由工業大麻製成。"},{"en":"Art canvas is a strong cloth surface used by painters.","zh":"art canvas 指畫家使用的堅韌布面。"},{"en":"An art student may stretch art canvas over a wooden frame before painting.","zh":"美術學生可能在繪畫前把畫布拉緊在木框上。"},{"en":"A strong canvas helps paint stay supported for many years.","zh":"堅韌畫布有助油畫在多年後仍得到支撐。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing painting materials.","zh":"討論繪畫材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"paints and varnishes","meaning":"油漆和清漆","examples":[{"en":"Hemp was used in paints and varnishes.","zh":"工業大麻曾用於油漆和清漆。"},{"en":"Paints and varnishes are liquids used to colour, protect, or finish surfaces.","zh":"paints and varnishes 指用來為表面上色、保護或完成表面處理的液體。"},{"en":"A carpenter may apply paints and varnishes to protect a wooden table.","zh":"木匠可能塗上油漆和清漆來保護木桌。"},{"en":"Oils from plants can be useful in paints and varnishes because they help form a smooth coating.","zh":"植物油可以用於油漆和清漆，因為它們有助形成平滑塗層。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing surface treatment materials.","zh":"討論表面處理材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lighting oil","meaning":"照明油","examples":[{"en":"Lighting oil was once made from hemp.","zh":"照明油曾經由工業大麻製成。"},{"en":"Lighting oil is oil burned in lamps to produce light.","zh":"lighting oil 指在油燈中燃燒以產生光的油。"},{"en":"Before electric lights, families used lighting oil to brighten homes at night.","zh":"在電燈出現以前，家庭使用照明油在夜晚照亮家中。"},{"en":"Reliable lighting oil was important when people had no modern electricity.","zh":"當人們沒有現代電力，可靠的照明油很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing older forms of household energy.","zh":"討論較舊的家用能源形式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hemp seeds","meaning":"大麻籽；火麻仁","examples":[{"en":"Hemp seeds were regularly used as food.","zh":"大麻籽經常被用作食物。"},{"en":"Hemp seeds are the small edible seeds of the hemp plant.","zh":"hemp seeds 指工業大麻植物可食用的小種子。"},{"en":"People may add hemp seeds to porridge, bread, or salad for extra nutrition.","zh":"人們可能把大麻籽加入粥、麵包或沙律，以增加營養。"},{"en":"Seeds rich in protein can help make a simple meal more nourishing.","zh":"富含蛋白質的種子可以令簡單餐食更有營養。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing hemp as food.","zh":"討論工業大麻作為食物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a source of food and protein","meaning":"食物和蛋白質來源","examples":[{"en":"Hemp seeds were used as a source of food and protein.","zh":"大麻籽曾被用作食物和蛋白質來源。"},{"en":"A source of food and protein is something people can eat that also supplies body-building nutrients.","zh":"source of food and protein 指可以食用並提供身體建構所需營養的東西。"},{"en":"Beans are a source of food and protein for many families who eat little meat.","zh":"對許多少吃肉的家庭來說，豆類是食物和蛋白質來源。"},{"en":"Protein sources are important because the body needs them to grow and repair tissue.","zh":"蛋白質來源很重要，因為身體需要它們來生長和修復組織。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing nutritious foods.","zh":"討論有營養食物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"for centuries","meaning":"數百年來","examples":[{"en":"Hemp seeds were used as food for centuries.","zh":"大麻籽數百年來被用作食物。"},{"en":"For centuries means for hundreds of years.","zh":"for centuries 指持續數百年。"},{"en":"People have used herbal remedies for centuries in many communities.","zh":"許多社區數百年來一直使用草藥療法。"},{"en":"If something has lasted for centuries, it has usually served a practical or cultural purpose.","zh":"如果某事物持續數百年，它通常具有實際或文化用途。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing long historical use.","zh":"描述長期歷史使用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"drastic decline","meaning":"急劇衰落","examples":[{"en":"Hemp experienced a drastic decline in use and importance.","zh":"工業大麻在用途和重要性上經歷急劇衰落。"},{"en":"A drastic decline is a very large and sudden fall.","zh":"drastic decline 指非常大且突然的下降。"},{"en":"A shop may suffer a drastic decline in customers after a new shopping mall opens nearby.","zh":"新商場在附近開幕後，小店顧客可能急劇減少。"},{"en":"A drastic decline can force businesses or industries to close, change, or seek support.","zh":"急劇衰落可以迫使企業或產業關閉、改變或尋求支援。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something falls sharply, not slowly.","zh":"當某事物急速而非緩慢下跌時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"decline in use and importance","meaning":"用途和重要性的下降","examples":[{"en":"The decline in use and importance of hemp happened within fifty years.","zh":"工業大麻用途和重要性的下降在五十年內發生。"},{"en":"A decline in use and importance means something is used less and matters less than before.","zh":"decline in use and importance 指某物被使用得更少，也比以前較不重要。"},{"en":"The decline in use and importance of paper maps happened after smartphones became common.","zh":"智能手機普及後，紙本地圖的用途和重要性下降。"},{"en":"New technology, laws, or public opinion can cause a material to lose importance.","zh":"新科技、法律或公眾意見可以令某種材料失去重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something becomes less common and less valued.","zh":"當某物變得較不常見且較不受重視時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"within a matter of","meaning":"在短短……之內","examples":[{"en":"Hemp declined within a matter of fifty years.","zh":"工業大麻在短短五十年內衰落。"},{"en":"Within a matter of means in only that amount of time, often suggesting the change was fast.","zh":"within a matter of 指只在某段時間內，常暗示變化很快。"},{"en":"A small video can become popular within a matter of hours.","zh":"一段短片可以在短短幾小時內走紅。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the time needed was surprisingly short.","zh":"這個短語強調所需時間短得令人驚訝。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing rapid change.","zh":"描述快速變化時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"widely considered to have been","meaning":"被廣泛認為曾經……","examples":[{"en":"The decline is widely considered to have been caused by powerful industries.","zh":"這種衰落被廣泛認為是由強大產業造成的。"},{"en":"Widely considered to have been means many people believe something happened in that way.","zh":"widely considered to have been 指許多人相信某事曾以那種方式發生。"},{"en":"The old factory is widely considered to have been important to the town’s growth.","zh":"那間舊工廠被廣泛認為曾對城鎮發展很重要。"},{"en":"A view becomes widely considered when many experts, writers, or citizens accept it.","zh":"當許多專家、作者或市民接受某看法，它就會被廣泛認為如此。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting a common belief.","zh":"報道常見信念時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"brought about by","meaning":"由……造成","examples":[{"en":"The decline of hemp was brought about by industrial interests.","zh":"工業大麻的衰落由工業利益造成。"},{"en":"Brought about by means caused by or produced by something.","zh":"brought about by 指由某事造成或產生。"},{"en":"A change in school rules may be brought about by repeated complaints from parents.","zh":"學校規則改變可能由家長反覆投訴造成。"},{"en":"Major changes are often brought about by several pressures working together.","zh":"重大變化常由幾種壓力共同造成。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining causes.","zh":"解釋原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"timber industry","meaning":"木材工業","examples":[{"en":"The timber industry was threatened by the growth of hemp.","zh":"木材工業受到工業大麻增長的威脅。"},{"en":"The timber industry is the business of cutting, processing, and selling wood.","zh":"timber industry 指砍伐、加工和銷售木材的行業。"},{"en":"The timber industry supplies wood for furniture, housing, paper, and packaging.","zh":"木材工業為家具、房屋、紙張和包裝供應木材。"},{"en":"A new plant-based material can threaten the timber industry if it replaces wood products.","zh":"如果新的植物材料取代木製品，它可以威脅木材工業。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing wood-related business.","zh":"討論與木材相關的商業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"petrochemical industry","meaning":"石化工業","examples":[{"en":"The petrochemical industry also had interests threatened by hemp.","zh":"石化工業的利益也受到工業大麻威脅。"},{"en":"The petrochemical industry produces chemicals and materials from oil and natural gas.","zh":"petrochemical industry 指由石油和天然氣生產化學品和材料的行業。"},{"en":"Plastics, synthetic fibres, and some industrial chemicals come from the petrochemical industry.","zh":"塑膠、合成纖維和一些工業化學品來自石化工業。"},{"en":"Plant-based alternatives can challenge petrochemical companies if customers want cleaner materials.","zh":"如果顧客想要更潔淨材料，植物性替代品可以挑戰石化公司。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing oil-based chemical production.","zh":"討論以石油為基礎的化學品生產時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"by the mid-1930s","meaning":"到二十世紀三十年代中期","examples":[{"en":"By the mid-1930s, changes in technology were affecting hemp.","zh":"到二十世紀三十年代中期，科技變化開始影響工業大麻。"},{"en":"By the mid-1930s means by around the middle years of the 1930s.","zh":"by the mid-1930s 指到1930年代中期左右。"},{"en":"By the mid-2000s, many students had started using mobile phones daily.","zh":"到二十世紀二千年代中期，許多學生已開始每日使用手機。"},{"en":"This phrase places a development in a specific historical period.","zh":"這個短語把某發展放在特定歷史時期中。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining when a trend had already begun.","zh":"解釋某趨勢何時已經開始時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"changes in technology","meaning":"科技變化","examples":[{"en":"Changes in technology began to affect the hemp industry.","zh":"科技變化開始影響工業大麻產業。"},{"en":"Changes in technology are new tools, machines, or methods that alter how work is done.","zh":"changes in technology 指新工具、機器或方法改變工作方式。"},{"en":"Online payment is one of the changes in technology that has changed shopping habits.","zh":"網上付款是改變購物習慣的科技變化之一。"},{"en":"New technology can make an old product cheaper, faster, or more competitive.","zh":"新科技可以令舊產品更便宜、更快捷或更具競爭力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when inventions change industries.","zh":"當發明改變產業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"impact on","meaning":"對……產生影響","examples":[{"en":"New technology began to impact on the hemp industry.","zh":"新科技開始對工業大麻產業產生影響。"},{"en":"Impact on something means affect it in a noticeable way.","zh":"impact on something 指以明顯方式影響某事物。"},{"en":"A new bus route can impact on local shops by bringing more customers.","zh":"新巴士路線可以透過帶來更多顧客，對本地商店產生影響。"},{"en":"If a change impacts an industry, businesses may need to adjust quickly.","zh":"如果變化影響一個行業，企業可能需要快速調整。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing effects.","zh":"描述影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"hemp industry","meaning":"工業大麻產業","examples":[{"en":"Technology and prohibition affected the hemp industry.","zh":"科技和禁令影響了工業大麻產業。"},{"en":"The hemp industry includes farming, processing, manufacturing, and selling hemp products.","zh":"hemp industry 包括工業大麻種植、加工、製造和產品銷售。"},{"en":"A growing hemp industry may create jobs in agriculture, textiles, construction, and food production.","zh":"發展中的工業大麻產業可以在農業、紡織、建築和食品生產方面創造工作。"},{"en":"Laws and public opinion can strongly affect whether the hemp industry grows or declines.","zh":"法律和公眾意見可以強烈影響工業大麻產業增長或衰落。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing hemp as a business sector.","zh":"討論工業大麻作為商業界別時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mechanical stripping equipment","meaning":"機械剝皮設備","examples":[{"en":"Mechanical stripping equipment became available and affordable.","zh":"機械剝皮設備變得可取得且價格可負擔。"},{"en":"Mechanical stripping equipment is machinery used to remove useful fibres or outer layers from plant stems.","zh":"mechanical stripping equipment 指用來從植物莖上移除有用纖維或外層的機器。"},{"en":"A factory may use mechanical stripping equipment to process crops faster than workers can by hand.","zh":"工廠可能使用機械剝皮設備，比人手更快地加工農作物。"},{"en":"When such equipment becomes affordable, farmers can process more material at lower cost.","zh":"當這類設備變得可負擔，農民可以以較低成本加工更多材料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing machines that improve crop processing.","zh":"討論改善作物加工的機器時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"conserve hemp’s high-cellulose pulp","meaning":"保存工業大麻的高纖維素紙漿","examples":[{"en":"Machines could conserve hemp’s high-cellulose pulp.","zh":"機器可以保存工業大麻的高纖維素紙漿。"},{"en":"To conserve hemp’s high-cellulose pulp means preserve the useful cellulose-rich part during processing.","zh":"conserve hemp’s high-cellulose pulp 指在加工過程中保留富含纖維素的有用部分。"},{"en":"A paper factory wants to conserve useful pulp so less material is wasted.","zh":"造紙廠想保存有用紙漿，以減少材料浪費。"},{"en":"Better processing can increase value because more of the crop becomes usable.","zh":"更好的加工可以增加價值，因為作物有更多部分變得可用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when machinery protects a valuable plant material.","zh":"當機器保護有價值植物材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"high-cellulose pulp","meaning":"高纖維素紙漿","examples":[{"en":"Hemp’s high-cellulose pulp was useful for paper production.","zh":"工業大麻的高纖維素紙漿對造紙有用。"},{"en":"High-cellulose pulp is plant material rich in cellulose, the substance needed to make strong paper and fibre products.","zh":"high-cellulose pulp 指富含纖維素的植物材料，而纖維素是製作堅韌紙張和纖維產品所需的物質。"},{"en":"A paper mill may prefer high-cellulose pulp because it can produce stronger sheets.","zh":"造紙廠可能偏好高纖維素紙漿，因為它可以生產更堅韌的紙張。"},{"en":"Materials with more cellulose can be more valuable for paper and board manufacturing.","zh":"纖維素較多的材料在紙張和板材製造中可以更有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing plant material for paper-making.","zh":"討論造紙用植物材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"became available and affordable","meaning":"變得可取得且價格可負擔","examples":[{"en":"New machines became available and affordable.","zh":"新機器變得可取得且價格可負擔。"},{"en":"Became available and affordable means people could obtain something and pay for it reasonably.","zh":"became available and affordable 指人們能取得某物，而且能以合理價格支付。"},{"en":"Online lessons became available and affordable when more teachers started using video platforms.","zh":"當更多老師開始使用視像平台，網上課程變得可取得且價格可負擔。"},{"en":"When technology becomes cheaper and easier to get, more people can use it.","zh":"當科技變得更便宜且更容易取得，更多人可以使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when access and price both improve.","zh":"當取得途徑和價格同時改善時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"holding companies","meaning":"控股公司","examples":[{"en":"Timber and paper holding companies stood to lose money.","zh":"木材和紙業控股公司可能損失金錢。"},{"en":"Holding companies are companies that own or control shares in other companies.","zh":"holding companies 指擁有或控制其他公司股份的公司。"},{"en":"A holding company may own several hotels, restaurants, and property firms.","zh":"控股公司可能擁有幾間酒店、餐廳和地產公司。"},{"en":"If a new material threatens one business, the holding company behind it may also lose money.","zh":"如果新材料威脅其中一門生意，其背後控股公司也可能損失金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing corporate ownership.","zh":"討論公司所有權時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stood to lose","meaning":"可能損失……","examples":[{"en":"Paper companies stood to lose billions of dollars.","zh":"紙業公司可能損失數十億美元。"},{"en":"Stood to lose means were likely to lose something if a situation developed in a certain way.","zh":"stood to lose 指如果情況以某方式發展，就很可能損失某物。"},{"en":"A shop stood to lose customers if a cheaper supermarket opened next door.","zh":"如果較便宜超市在隔壁開張，小店可能損失顧客。"},{"en":"People may oppose change when they stand to lose money, power, or market share.","zh":"當人們可能損失金錢、權力或市場份額，他們可能反對改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone has something at risk.","zh":"當某人有東西處於風險中時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"billions of dollars","meaning":"數十億美元","examples":[{"en":"Companies stood to lose billions of dollars if hemp expanded.","zh":"如果工業大麻擴張，公司可能損失數十億美元。"},{"en":"Billions of dollars means a very large amount of money measured in thousands of millions.","zh":"billions of dollars 指以十億計算的極大量金錢。"},{"en":"Governments may spend billions of dollars on transport, hospitals, or disaster recovery.","zh":"政府可能在交通、醫院或災後重建上花費數十億美元。"},{"en":"When billions of dollars are involved, businesses and politicians may act very strongly.","zh":"當涉及數十億美元，企業和政客可能採取非常強烈行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing extremely large financial stakes.","zh":"討論極大財務利益時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"grown on a large scale","meaning":"大規模種植","examples":[{"en":"Paper companies feared hemp would be grown on a large scale.","zh":"紙業公司擔心工業大麻會被大規模種植。"},{"en":"Grown on a large scale means cultivated in very large quantities over wide areas.","zh":"grown on a large scale 指在廣闊地區以大量方式種植。"},{"en":"Rice is grown on a large scale in regions where it is a main food.","zh":"在稻米是主要食物的地區，稻米被大規模種植。"},{"en":"When a crop is grown on a large scale, it can affect prices, jobs, and competing industries.","zh":"當作物被大規模種植，它可以影響價格、工作和競爭產業。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when farming becomes widespread and commercial.","zh":"當農業變得廣泛且商業化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a resurgence of","meaning":"……的復興","examples":[{"en":"A resurgence of the hemp industry threatened petrochemical companies.","zh":"工業大麻產業的復興威脅到石化公司。"},{"en":"A resurgence of something means a strong return or renewed growth after decline.","zh":"resurgence of something 指某事在衰落後強勢回歸或重新增長。"},{"en":"A resurgence of local markets may happen when people want fresher food and community shopping.","zh":"當人們想要更新鮮食物和社區購物，本地市場可能復興。"},{"en":"Resurgence often follows renewed public interest, lower costs, or better technology.","zh":"復興常伴隨重新出現的公眾興趣、較低成本或更好科技。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something becomes powerful again.","zh":"當某事物重新變得有力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"threatened","meaning":"威脅到","examples":[{"en":"Hemp threatened companies that had patented pulp-processing chemicals.","zh":"工業大麻威脅到已為紙漿處理化學品申請專利的公司。"},{"en":"Threatened means put someone or something at risk of harm, loss, or decline.","zh":"threatened 指令某人或某事面臨傷害、損失或衰落風險。"},{"en":"A new shopping centre may threaten small shops by drawing customers away.","zh":"新商場可能透過吸走顧客威脅小店。"},{"en":"When an industry feels threatened, it may lobby, advertise, or change strategy.","zh":"當一個產業感到受威脅，它可能游說、宣傳或改變策略。"},{"en":"This word is useful when competition creates danger for existing interests.","zh":"當競爭為既有利益帶來危險時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"emerging petrochemical companies","meaning":"新興石化公司","examples":[{"en":"Emerging petrochemical companies were threatened by hemp’s return.","zh":"新興石化公司受到工業大麻回歸的威脅。"},{"en":"Emerging petrochemical companies are newly growing businesses that make chemicals from oil or gas.","zh":"emerging petrochemical companies 指正在新近成長、以石油或天然氣製造化學品的企業。"},{"en":"Emerging companies may fear older natural materials if those materials compete with their new products.","zh":"如果較舊天然材料與新產品競爭，新興公司可能會擔心。"},{"en":"New industries can still feel vulnerable when another technology challenges their future market.","zh":"當另一種技術挑戰未來市場，新產業仍可能感到脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing young industrial businesses.","zh":"討論年輕工業企業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"patented the chemicals","meaning":"為化學品申請專利","examples":[{"en":"Petrochemical companies had patented the chemicals for pulp processing.","zh":"石化公司已為紙漿處理用化學品申請專利。"},{"en":"Patented the chemicals means legally registered the right to control the use or sale of those chemicals.","zh":"patented the chemicals 指依法登記控制那些化學品使用或銷售的權利。"},{"en":"A company may patent a new cleaning chemical so competitors cannot copy it freely.","zh":"公司可能為新的清潔化學品申請專利，令競爭者不能自由複製。"},{"en":"Patents can protect profits because they limit who can use an invention.","zh":"專利可以保護利潤，因為它限制誰能使用一項發明。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing business protection of inventions.","zh":"討論企業保護發明時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pulp processing","meaning":"紙漿處理","examples":[{"en":"The chemicals were used for pulp processing.","zh":"這些化學品用於紙漿處理。"},{"en":"Pulp processing is the treatment of plant or wood pulp so it can be made into paper or board.","zh":"pulp processing 指處理植物或木材紙漿，使其可製成紙張或板材。"},{"en":"A paper mill uses pulp processing to turn raw plant material into smooth sheets.","zh":"造紙廠使用紙漿處理，把原植物材料變成平滑紙張。"},{"en":"Better pulp processing can improve paper quality and reduce waste.","zh":"更好的紙漿處理可以改善紙張質素並減少浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how paper materials are prepared.","zh":"討論紙張材料如何準備時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"newspaper articles","meaning":"報章文章","examples":[{"en":"Newspaper articles began to link hemp with violent crime.","zh":"報章文章開始把工業大麻與暴力罪行聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Newspaper articles are written reports or opinion pieces published in newspapers.","zh":"newspaper articles 指刊登在報章上的新聞報道或評論文章。"},{"en":"Newspaper articles can influence public opinion about health, crime, business, or politics.","zh":"報章文章可以影響公眾對健康、罪案、商業或政治的看法。"},{"en":"Repeated articles can make readers associate a subject with fear or danger.","zh":"反覆出現的文章可以令讀者把某主題與恐懼或危險聯繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when media writing shapes public attitudes.","zh":"當媒體文字塑造公眾態度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"began to appear","meaning":"開始出現","examples":[{"en":"Newspaper articles began to appear against hemp.","zh":"反對工業大麻的報章文章開始出現。"},{"en":"Began to appear means started to be seen, published, or noticed.","zh":"began to appear 指開始被看見、被刊登或被注意到。"},{"en":"Complaints began to appear online after the new bus timetable caused delays.","zh":"新巴士時間表造成延誤後，投訴開始在網上出現。"},{"en":"When many similar messages begin to appear, they can create a public impression.","zh":"當許多相似訊息開始出現，它們可以創造公眾印象。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something starts becoming visible.","zh":"當某事開始變得可見時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"linking hemp with","meaning":"將工業大麻與……聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"Newspaper articles began linking hemp with violent crime.","zh":"報章文章開始將工業大麻與暴力罪行聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Linking hemp with something means connecting hemp to that thing in people’s minds.","zh":"linking hemp with something 指在人們心中把工業大麻與某事物連接。"},{"en":"A campaign may link exercise with better mood so people feel motivated to move more.","zh":"宣傳活動可能把運動與更好心情聯繫起來，令人更有動力多活動。"},{"en":"Repeated links in media can shape public opinion, even when the connection is unfair.","zh":"媒體反覆建立聯繫可以塑造公眾意見，即使那種連結不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one idea is associated with another.","zh":"當一個想法與另一個想法被關聯時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"violent crime","meaning":"暴力罪行","examples":[{"en":"Some articles linked hemp with violent crime.","zh":"有些文章把工業大麻與暴力罪行聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Violent crime is crime that involves physical force, injury, or the threat of injury.","zh":"violent crime 指涉及身體武力、傷害或傷害威脅的罪行。"},{"en":"Robbery with weapons and serious assault are examples of violent crime.","zh":"持械搶劫和嚴重襲擊都是暴力罪行例子。"},{"en":"Linking a product to violent crime can make the public fear it.","zh":"把產品與暴力罪行聯繫起來，可以令公眾害怕它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing serious criminal behaviour.","zh":"討論嚴重犯罪行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the term used","meaning":"所使用的詞語","examples":[{"en":"The term used was “marijuana” instead of hemp.","zh":"所使用的詞語是 “marijuana”，而不是 hemp。"},{"en":"The term used means the word or expression chosen to describe something.","zh":"term used 指被選來描述某事物的字詞或表達。"},{"en":"In a school notice, the term used should be clear so parents understand the message.","zh":"在學校通告中，所使用的詞語應清楚，讓家長理解訊息。"},{"en":"The term used can change how people feel about the same object or idea.","zh":"所使用的詞語可以改變人們對同一物件或想法的感受。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when word choice affects meaning.","zh":"當用詞影響意思時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"distance it from","meaning":"使它與……區分開","examples":[{"en":"The term “marijuana” was used to distance the plant from industrial hemp.","zh":"“marijuana” 這個詞被用來使該植物與工業大麻區分開。"},{"en":"Distance it from something means make people see it as separate or different from that thing.","zh":"distance it from something 指令人把它看作與某事物分開或不同。"},{"en":"A company may distance a new healthy snack from ordinary sweets by changing its packaging.","zh":"公司可能透過改變包裝，使新的健康小食與普通糖果區分開。"},{"en":"Word choice can distance one idea from another, even when they are closely related.","zh":"用詞可以把一個想法與另一個想法區分開，即使兩者關係密切。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when language creates separation.","zh":"當語言製造分隔時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"industrial purposes","meaning":"工業用途","examples":[{"en":"Hemp was used for industrial purposes.","zh":"工業大麻被用於工業用途。"},{"en":"Industrial purposes are practical uses connected with manufacturing, construction, energy, or large-scale production.","zh":"industrial purposes 指與製造、建築、能源或大規模生產有關的實際用途。"},{"en":"A plant grown for industrial purposes may be used to make paper, fuel, or building panels.","zh":"為工業用途而種植的植物可能用來製造紙張、燃料或建築板材。"},{"en":"A crop used for industrial purposes can support factories as well as farms.","zh":"用於工業用途的作物可以同時支援工廠和農場。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a material is used for production rather than leisure.","zh":"當材料用於生產而不是休閒時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"few people realised that","meaning":"很少人意識到……","examples":[{"en":"Few people realised that marijuana and hemp came from the same plant species.","zh":"很少人意識到 marijuana 和 hemp 來自同一植物物種。"},{"en":"Few people realised that means not many people understood or noticed the fact.","zh":"few people realised that 指沒有很多人理解或注意到某事實。"},{"en":"Few people realised that the old warehouse was once the town’s main cinema.","zh":"很少人意識到那座舊貨倉曾是城鎮的主要戲院。"},{"en":"If few people realise a fact, public opinion may be based on misunderstanding.","zh":"如果很少人意識到某事實，公眾意見可能建立在誤解之上。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an important truth was not widely known.","zh":"當重要真相不為人廣泛知道時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"came from the same plant species","meaning":"來自同一植物物種","examples":[{"en":"Marijuana and hemp came from the same plant species.","zh":"marijuana 和 hemp 來自同一植物物種。"},{"en":"Came from the same plant species means originated from plants belonging to the same biological group.","zh":"came from the same plant species 指源自屬於同一生物分類群的植物。"},{"en":"Different apple varieties can come from the same plant species but taste very different.","zh":"不同蘋果品種可以來自同一植物物種，但味道非常不同。"},{"en":"Plants from the same species can still be bred for very different uses.","zh":"來自同一物種的植物仍可被培育作非常不同用途。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining biological relationship without saying two things are identical.","zh":"解釋生物關係但不表示兩者完全相同時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"virtually nobody suspected that","meaning":"幾乎沒有人懷疑……","examples":[{"en":"Virtually nobody suspected that the prohibition would destroy the hemp industry.","zh":"幾乎沒有人懷疑該禁令會摧毀工業大麻產業。"},{"en":"Virtually nobody suspected that means almost no one thought or expected that something was true.","zh":"virtually nobody suspected that 指幾乎沒有人認為或預期某事是真。"},{"en":"Virtually nobody suspected that the quiet student would win the debate competition.","zh":"幾乎沒有人想到那位安靜學生會贏得辯論比賽。"},{"en":"When nobody expects a result, the result can later seem shocking or ironic.","zh":"當沒有人預期某結果，結果後來可能顯得震驚或諷刺。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing something almost no one foresaw.","zh":"描述幾乎沒有人預見的事情時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Marijuana Prohibition","meaning":"大麻禁令","examples":[{"en":"The Marijuana Prohibition damaged the hemp industry.","zh":"大麻禁令損害了工業大麻產業。"},{"en":"Marijuana Prohibition means laws or policies that banned marijuana and affected related cannabis plants.","zh":"Marijuana Prohibition 指禁止大麻並影響相關大麻植物的法律或政策。"},{"en":"A prohibition can reshape an industry by making certain crops, products, or activities illegal.","zh":"禁令可以透過令某些作物、產品或活動變成非法而重塑產業。"},{"en":"When a law bans one product, similar or related products may also be harmed.","zh":"當法律禁止一種產品，相似或相關產品也可能受害。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the historical banning of marijuana.","zh":"討論大麻被禁的歷史時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"destroy the hemp industry","meaning":"摧毀工業大麻產業","examples":[{"en":"The Marijuana Prohibition helped destroy the hemp industry.","zh":"大麻禁令幫助摧毀工業大麻產業。"},{"en":"Destroy the hemp industry means damage it so severely that it can no longer operate normally.","zh":"destroy the hemp industry 指嚴重損害該產業，使其不能正常運作。"},{"en":"A sudden ban on a crop can destroy an industry if farmers and factories lose their legal market.","zh":"如果農民和工廠失去合法市場，突然禁止某作物可以摧毀一個產業。"},{"en":"Industries can be destroyed by laws, competition, public fear, or loss of investment.","zh":"產業可以被法律、競爭、公眾恐懼或投資流失摧毀。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an economic sector is almost wiped out.","zh":"當一個經濟界別幾乎被消滅時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"supporting the theory that","meaning":"支持……這個理論","examples":[{"en":"Two articles supported the theory that marijuana was banned to destroy hemp.","zh":"兩篇文章支持大麻被禁止是為了摧毀工業大麻這個理論。"},{"en":"Supporting the theory that means giving evidence or arguments that make an explanation seem possible.","zh":"supporting the theory that 指提供證據或論點，使某解釋看似可能。"},{"en":"Falling test scores may support the theory that students need more reading practice.","zh":"測驗分數下降可能支持學生需要更多閱讀練習這個理論。"},{"en":"A theory becomes stronger when several pieces of evidence point in the same direction.","zh":"當幾項證據指向同一方向，理論會變得更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence backs an explanation.","zh":"當證據支持某解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"was banned to","meaning":"被禁止以便……","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe marijuana was banned to destroy the hemp industry.","zh":"有些人認為大麻被禁止，以便摧毀工業大麻產業。"},{"en":"Was banned to do something means was made illegal for the purpose of achieving that result.","zh":"was banned to do something 指某事被列為非法，目的是達到某結果。"},{"en":"A dangerous toy may be banned to protect young children from injury.","zh":"危險玩具可能被禁止，以便保護幼童免受傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase links a ban with its intended purpose or suspected purpose.","zh":"這個短語把禁令與其目的或被懷疑目的連接起來。"},{"en":"This structure is useful when explaining why something was prohibited.","zh":"解釋某事為何被禁止時，這個結構很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"written just before","meaning":"就在……之前撰寫","examples":[{"en":"Two articles were written just before the Marijuana Prohibition.","zh":"兩篇文章就在大麻禁令之前撰寫。"},{"en":"Written just before means produced shortly before a particular event.","zh":"written just before 指在某事件之前不久寫成。"},{"en":"A warning letter written just before the accident may become important evidence.","zh":"就在意外之前撰寫的警告信，可能成為重要證據。"},{"en":"Timing can matter because a document may show what people expected before a major change.","zh":"時間點可以很重要，因為文件可能顯示人們在重大變化前預期甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when linking a text to an event that followed soon after.","zh":"把文本與隨後很快發生的事件連接時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"claiming that","meaning":"聲稱","examples":[{"en":"The articles claimed that hemp was becoming a super crop.","zh":"這些文章聲稱工業大麻正成為超級農作物。"},{"en":"Claiming that means saying something is true, especially when others may question it.","zh":"claiming that 指說某事是真，尤其是當其他人可能質疑它。"},{"en":"A shop may advertise a drink by claiming that it improves energy.","zh":"商店可能透過聲稱一款飲品能提升精力來宣傳它。"},{"en":"Claims need evidence because readers may not accept them automatically.","zh":"聲稱需要證據，因為讀者不一定自動接受。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting what someone says or argues.","zh":"報道某人說法或論點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"on the verge of becoming","meaning":"即將成為……","examples":[{"en":"Hemp was on the verge of becoming a super crop.","zh":"工業大麻即將成為超級農作物。"},{"en":"On the verge of becoming means very close to changing into or achieving something.","zh":"on the verge of becoming 指非常接近變成或達到某狀態。"},{"en":"A small business may be on the verge of becoming successful after its product goes viral.","zh":"小企業在產品走紅後，可能即將變得成功。"},{"en":"Being on the verge suggests the change has not fully happened yet, but is near.","zh":"on the verge 暗示變化尚未完全發生，但已很接近。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is about to reach a new stage.","zh":"當某事即將到達新階段時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"super crop","meaning":"超級農作物","examples":[{"en":"Hemp was described as a potential super crop.","zh":"工業大麻被描述為潛在超級農作物。"},{"en":"A super crop is a crop considered unusually useful, profitable, productive, or versatile.","zh":"super crop 指被認為特別有用、有利可圖、高產或用途廣泛的農作物。"},{"en":"A crop that provides food, fibre, oil, and building material could be called a super crop.","zh":"如果一種作物能提供食物、纖維、油和建築材料，它可以被稱為超級農作物。"},{"en":"Farmers may support a super crop if it brings high income with fewer environmental costs.","zh":"如果超級農作物帶來高收入且環境成本較低，農民可能支持它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a plant has many valuable uses.","zh":"當植物有許多有價值用途時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"well-respected magazines","meaning":"備受尊重的雜誌","examples":[{"en":"The articles appeared in well-respected magazines.","zh":"這些文章刊登在備受尊重的雜誌上。"},{"en":"Well-respected magazines are publications that many people consider reliable, serious, or influential.","zh":"well-respected magazines 指許多人認為可靠、嚴肅或有影響力的刊物。"},{"en":"A scientist may publish an article in a well-respected magazine to reach educated readers.","zh":"科學家可能在備受尊重的雜誌發表文章，以接觸受教育讀者。"},{"en":"Information can seem more persuasive when it appears in respected publications.","zh":"當資訊出現在受尊重刊物上，它可能更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing source credibility.","zh":"討論來源可信度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"praised the usefulness and potential of","meaning":"讚揚……的用途和潛力","examples":[{"en":"The magazines praised the usefulness and potential of hemp.","zh":"這些雜誌讚揚工業大麻的用途和潛力。"},{"en":"Praised the usefulness and potential of something means spoke positively about what it can do now and what it may do in the future.","zh":"praised the usefulness and potential of something 指正面談論某物現在能做甚麼和未來可能做到甚麼。"},{"en":"Teachers may praise the usefulness and potential of online dictionaries for language learners.","zh":"老師可能讚揚網上字典對語言學習者的用途和潛力。"},{"en":"Positive praise can increase public interest, investment, and acceptance.","zh":"正面讚揚可以增加公眾興趣、投資和接受度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is valued for present and future benefits.","zh":"當某物因現時和未來好處而被重視時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"usefulness and potential","meaning":"用途和潛力","examples":[{"en":"The articles praised hemp’s usefulness and potential.","zh":"這些文章讚揚工業大麻的用途和潛力。"},{"en":"Usefulness and potential means how helpful something is now and how valuable it may become later.","zh":"usefulness and potential 指某物現在有多有用，以及將來可能變得多有價值。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice a student’s usefulness and potential in helping classmates learn.","zh":"老師可能注意到學生在幫助同學學習方面的用途和潛力。"},{"en":"Something with both usefulness and potential can attract support and investment.","zh":"同時有用途和潛力的事物可以吸引支持和投資。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when present value and future value are both important.","zh":"當現時價值和未來價值同樣重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"produce more than","meaning":"生產超過……","examples":[{"en":"Hemp can be used to produce more than 25,000 products.","zh":"工業大麻可用來生產超過25,000種產品。"},{"en":"Produce more than means make a number greater than the amount stated.","zh":"produce more than 指製造出比所述數量更多的東西。"},{"en":"A busy bakery may produce more than 500 loaves of bread in one morning.","zh":"繁忙麵包店可能在一個早上生產超過500條麵包。"},{"en":"High production ability can make a material or business more valuable.","zh":"高生產能力可以令材料或企業更有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing a large output.","zh":"強調大量產出時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prove profitable and desirable","meaning":"證明有利可圖且理想","examples":[{"en":"Hemp would prove profitable and desirable for farmers and the public.","zh":"工業大麻會證明對農民和公眾都有利可圖且理想。"},{"en":"Prove profitable and desirable means turn out to make money and be wanted by people.","zh":"prove profitable and desirable 指最終顯示能賺錢，而且受人需要。"},{"en":"A new school canteen plan may prove profitable and desirable if students buy healthier meals happily.","zh":"如果學生樂意購買較健康餐膳，新的學校飯堂計劃可能證明有利可圖且理想。"},{"en":"A crop becomes attractive when it benefits both producers and consumers.","zh":"當作物同時有利於生產者和消費者，它就會變得吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something becomes both commercially and socially appealing.","zh":"當某物在商業和社會上都吸引時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"profitable","meaning":"有利可圖的","examples":[{"en":"Hemp was described as a profitable crop.","zh":"工業大麻被描述為有利可圖的作物。"},{"en":"Profitable means able to make more money than it costs.","zh":"profitable 指能賺到比成本更多的錢。"},{"en":"A café is profitable if its sales are higher than rent, wages, and ingredient costs.","zh":"如果咖啡店銷售額高於租金、工資和材料成本，它就是有利可圖的。"},{"en":"Farmers prefer profitable crops because they support income and future investment.","zh":"農民偏好有利可圖的作物，因為它們支撐收入和未來投資。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing business success.","zh":"討論商業成功時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"desirable crop","meaning":"理想的農作物","examples":[{"en":"Hemp was described as a desirable crop for farmers.","zh":"工業大麻被描述為對農民來說理想的農作物。"},{"en":"A desirable crop is a crop that farmers want to grow because it has useful qualities.","zh":"desirable crop 指農民因其有用特質而想種植的作物。"},{"en":"A crop may be desirable if it sells well, needs little water, and resists pests.","zh":"如果一種作物銷情好、需水少且抗蟲，它可能是理想作物。"},{"en":"Desirable crops can improve farm income and reduce risk.","zh":"理想農作物可以改善農場收入並降低風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why farmers favour one crop over another.","zh":"解釋農民為何偏好某作物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"billion-dollar crop","meaning":"十億美元農作物","examples":[{"en":"Hemp was the first crop described as a billion-dollar crop.","zh":"工業大麻是第一種被描述為十億美元農作物的作物。"},{"en":"A billion-dollar crop is a crop expected to create extremely large economic value.","zh":"billion-dollar crop 指被預期能創造極大經濟價值的作物。"},{"en":"Coffee is a billion-dollar crop in countries where it supports exports, farms, and jobs.","zh":"在咖啡支撐出口、農場和工作的國家，咖啡是十億美元農作物。"},{"en":"Calling a crop billion-dollar suggests major profit and industrial potential.","zh":"稱一種作物為十億美元農作物，暗示它有重大利潤和工業潛力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a crop is seen as economically powerful.","zh":"當作物被視為經濟上強大時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"took effect","meaning":"生效","examples":[{"en":"The Marijuana Prohibition took effect less than one year later.","zh":"大麻禁令不到一年後生效。"},{"en":"Took effect means started to operate officially or began to have real influence.","zh":"took effect 指正式開始運作或開始產生實際影響。"},{"en":"The new school rule took effect on Monday, so students had to arrive earlier.","zh":"新校規在星期一生效，所以學生必須更早到校。"},{"en":"Once a law takes effect, people and businesses must follow it.","zh":"法律一旦生效，人和企業就必須遵守。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing when a rule or policy begins.","zh":"描述規則或政策何時開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"to what extent","meaning":"在多大程度上","examples":[{"en":"To what extent a conspiracy was involved is still debated.","zh":"陰謀在多大程度上涉及其中仍在爭論。"},{"en":"To what extent means how much or how far something is true.","zh":"to what extent 指某事在多大程度上為真。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask to what extent homework improves exam results.","zh":"老師可能問功課在多大程度上改善考試成績。"},{"en":"This phrase invites a balanced answer, not a simple yes or no.","zh":"這個短語要求平衡答案，而不是簡單的是或否。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing degree, scale, or strength of influence.","zh":"討論程度、規模或影響力強弱時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"conspiracy","meaning":"陰謀","examples":[{"en":"Whether a conspiracy was involved is still being debated.","zh":"是否有陰謀涉及其中仍在被爭論。"},{"en":"A conspiracy is a secret plan by a group to do something harmful or dishonest.","zh":"conspiracy 指一群人秘密計劃做有害或不誠實事情。"},{"en":"If several managers secretly agree to hide safety problems, that may be a conspiracy.","zh":"如果幾名經理秘密同意隱瞞安全問題，那可能是陰謀。"},{"en":"Claims of conspiracy need strong evidence because they accuse people of deliberate wrongdoing.","zh":"陰謀指控需要有力證據，因為它指控人蓄意作惡。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing hidden plans and suspicion.","zh":"討論隱藏計劃和懷疑時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"was involved","meaning":"涉及其中","examples":[{"en":"It is still debated whether a conspiracy was involved.","zh":"是否有陰謀涉及其中仍在爭論。"},{"en":"Was involved means took part in or had a role in something.","zh":"was involved 指參與某事或在其中有作用。"},{"en":"Police may ask whether a second car was involved in an accident.","zh":"警方可能詢問是否有第二輛車涉及意外。"},{"en":"If someone was involved, they may have influenced what happened.","zh":"如果某人涉及其中，他可能影響了事情發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying participation or responsibility.","zh":"識別參與或責任時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"still being debated","meaning":"仍在被爭論","examples":[{"en":"The role of conspiracy is still being debated.","zh":"陰謀的角色仍在被爭論。"},{"en":"Still being debated means people have not yet reached agreement about it.","zh":"still being debated 指人們尚未就某事達成共識。"},{"en":"The best way to reduce homework stress is still being debated by parents and teachers.","zh":"減少功課壓力的最佳方法仍在家長和老師之間被爭論。"},{"en":"Topics remain debated when evidence is incomplete or people interpret it differently.","zh":"當證據不完整或人們詮釋不同，議題會仍在被爭論。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an issue remains unsettled.","zh":"當議題仍未有定論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"used extensively","meaning":"被廣泛使用","examples":[{"en":"For thousands of years, hemp was used extensively.","zh":"數千年來，工業大麻被廣泛使用。"},{"en":"Used extensively means used widely, often, and in many places or ways.","zh":"used extensively 指被廣泛、頻繁並以多種方式或在多地使用。"},{"en":"Smartphones are used extensively by students for communication, research, and entertainment.","zh":"智能手機被學生廣泛用於溝通、研究和娛樂。"},{"en":"A material used extensively usually has practical value and many applications.","zh":"被廣泛使用的材料通常有實用價值和許多用途。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is common and widely applied.","zh":"當某物常見且應用廣泛時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"over a short period","meaning":"在短時間內","examples":[{"en":"Over a short period, hemp became illegal in many places.","zh":"在短時間內，工業大麻在許多地方變成非法。"},{"en":"Over a short period means within a brief length of time.","zh":"over a short period 指在短暫時間內。"},{"en":"A small café can become popular over a short period if many customers share photos online.","zh":"如果許多顧客在網上分享照片，小咖啡店可以在短時間內走紅。"},{"en":"Rapid change can surprise people because there is little time to adjust.","zh":"快速變化可以令人驚訝，因為人們很少時間適應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something happens quickly.","zh":"當某事快速發生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"became illegal","meaning":"變成非法","examples":[{"en":"Hemp became illegal in many parts of the world.","zh":"工業大麻在世界多個地區變成非法。"},{"en":"Became illegal means was no longer allowed by law.","zh":"became illegal 指不再被法律容許。"},{"en":"A product may become illegal if it is found to be dangerous to children.","zh":"如果某產品被發現對兒童危險，它可能變成非法。"},{"en":"When something becomes illegal, producers and users may face punishment.","zh":"當某事變成非法，生產者和使用者可能面對懲罰。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when law changes what people may do.","zh":"當法律改變人們可做的事時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in many parts of the world","meaning":"在世界多個地區","examples":[{"en":"Hemp became illegal in many parts of the world.","zh":"工業大麻在世界多個地區變成非法。"},{"en":"In many parts of the world means in many different countries or regions.","zh":"in many parts of the world 指在許多不同國家或地區。"},{"en":"Rice is eaten daily in many parts of the world.","zh":"稻米在世界多個地區被每日食用。"},{"en":"If a rule spreads to many regions, its effects can become global.","zh":"如果規則擴散至許多地區，其影響可以變成全球性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something happens widely across countries.","zh":"當某事在多國廣泛發生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the focus is on","meaning":"重點在於……","examples":[{"en":"Today, the focus is on developing hemp as an industrial resource.","zh":"今天，重點在於把工業大麻發展為工業資源。"},{"en":"The focus is on something means the main attention is given to that thing.","zh":"the focus is on something 指主要注意力放在某事上。"},{"en":"In beginner English lessons, the focus is on clear pronunciation and useful daily sentences.","zh":"在初級英文課中，重點在於清晰發音和實用日常句子。"},{"en":"When priorities change, the focus may move from one goal to another.","zh":"當優先次序改變，重點可能由一個目標轉向另一個目標。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying the main concern.","zh":"識別主要關注點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"development of","meaning":"……的發展","examples":[{"en":"The focus is on the development of hemp as an industrial resource.","zh":"重點在於工業大麻作為工業資源的發展。"},{"en":"Development of something means the process of improving, expanding, or bringing it into use.","zh":"development of something 指改善、擴展或把某事物投入使用的過程。"},{"en":"The development of public transport can make a city easier to live in.","zh":"公共交通的發展可以令城市更宜居。"},{"en":"Development often needs research, investment, planning, and public support.","zh":"發展常需要研究、投資、規劃和公眾支持。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is being built or improved over time.","zh":"當某事物正隨時間被建立或改善時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"industrial resource","meaning":"工業資源","examples":[{"en":"Hemp is being developed as an industrial resource.","zh":"工業大麻正被發展成工業資源。"},{"en":"An industrial resource is a material that can be used in manufacturing or large-scale production.","zh":"industrial resource 指可用於製造業或大規模生產的材料。"},{"en":"Recycled plastic can become an industrial resource if factories use it to make new products.","zh":"如果工廠用回收塑膠製造新產品，它可以成為工業資源。"},{"en":"A good industrial resource must be useful, affordable, and available in enough quantity.","zh":"良好的工業資源必須有用、可負擔且供應量足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a material supports industry.","zh":"當材料支援工業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"initially","meaning":"起初；首先","examples":[{"en":"Initially, a distinction needs to be made between two types of hemp.","zh":"首先，需要區分兩種工業大麻。"},{"en":"Initially means at the beginning or first stage.","zh":"initially 指在開始或第一階段。"},{"en":"Initially, new students may feel nervous before they know their classmates.","zh":"起初，新學生在認識同學前可能感到緊張。"},{"en":"What happens initially can shape how people understand the rest of the topic.","zh":"起初發生的事情可以塑造人們如何理解後續內容。"},{"en":"This word is useful when introducing the first step in an explanation.","zh":"引入解釋的第一步時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a distinction needs to be made","meaning":"需要作出區分","examples":[{"en":"A distinction needs to be made between hemp and marijuana.","zh":"工業大麻和大麻之間需要作出區分。"},{"en":"A distinction needs to be made means two things must be clearly separated or compared.","zh":"a distinction needs to be made 指必須清楚分開或比較兩件事。"},{"en":"A distinction needs to be made between careless mistakes and serious misunderstanding in student writing.","zh":"在學生寫作中，粗心錯誤和嚴重誤解之間需要作出區分。"},{"en":"Clear distinctions prevent confusion and unfair judgement.","zh":"清楚區分可以避免混淆和不公平判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when two similar things should not be mixed up.","zh":"當兩件相似事物不應混為一談時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"evolved into","meaning":"演化成……","examples":[{"en":"Cannabis has evolved into two basic species.","zh":"大麻屬植物已演化成兩個基本物種。"},{"en":"Evolved into means gradually changed or developed into a different form.","zh":"evolved into 指逐漸改變或發展成另一種形式。"},{"en":"A small family shop may evolve into a large online business over many years.","zh":"小型家庭店舖可能多年後演化成大型網上企業。"},{"en":"Evolution or gradual development can create different types from a common origin.","zh":"演化或逐步發展可以從共同來源產生不同類型。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something changes over time into a new form.","zh":"當某事隨時間變成新形式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"two basic species","meaning":"兩個基本物種","examples":[{"en":"Cannabis has evolved into two basic species.","zh":"大麻屬植物已演化成兩個基本物種。"},{"en":"Two basic species means two main biological types.","zh":"two basic species 指兩種主要生物類型。"},{"en":"A science lesson may explain two basic species before discussing smaller varieties.","zh":"科學課可能先解釋兩個基本物種，再討論較小品種。"},{"en":"Starting with basic species helps students organise more detailed information later.","zh":"從基本物種開始，有助學生之後整理更詳細資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when simplifying biological classification.","zh":"簡化生物分類時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"plants grown for fibre and seed","meaning":"為纖維和種子而種植的植物","examples":[{"en":"Plants grown for fibre and seed are called hemp.","zh":"為纖維和種子而種植的植物被稱為工業大麻。"},{"en":"Plants grown for fibre and seed are crops cultivated to produce usable fibres and edible or useful seeds.","zh":"plants grown for fibre and seed 指為生產可用纖維和可食用或有用種子而栽培的作物。"},{"en":"Farmers may choose plants grown for fibre and seed if both the stem and seed can be sold.","zh":"如果莖和種子都可出售，農民可能選擇為纖維和種子而種植的植物。"},{"en":"Multiple usable parts can make a crop more profitable.","zh":"多個可用部分可以令作物更有利可圖。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why a plant is cultivated.","zh":"解釋植物為何被種植時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"universally called","meaning":"普遍被稱為……","examples":[{"en":"Plants grown for fibre and seed are universally called hemp.","zh":"為纖維和種子而種植的植物普遍被稱為工業大麻。"},{"en":"Universally called means known by the same name everywhere or by almost everyone.","zh":"universally called 指在各地或幾乎所有人之間以同一名稱被認識。"},{"en":"A doctor is universally called a medical professional because the term is widely understood.","zh":"醫生普遍被稱為醫療專業人士，因為這個說法被廣泛理解。"},{"en":"A universal name reduces confusion across countries, industries, and classrooms.","zh":"通用名稱可以減少國家、行業和課堂之間的混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a term is widely accepted.","zh":"當術語被廣泛接受時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"drug content","meaning":"毒品成分；藥物成分","examples":[{"en":"Cannabis grown for its drug content is called marijuana.","zh":"為其毒品成分而種植的大麻屬植物被稱為 marijuana。"},{"en":"Drug content means the amount of psychoactive or medicinal substance in a plant or product.","zh":"drug content 指植物或產品中精神活性或藥用物質的含量。"},{"en":"Medicines are carefully controlled because drug content affects strength and safety.","zh":"藥物受到仔細管制，因為藥物成分影響強度和安全。"},{"en":"If drug content is high, laws and health risks may be different.","zh":"如果毒品成分高，法律和健康風險可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing chemical strength in a controlled context.","zh":"在受管制語境中討論化學強度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"commonly called","meaning":"通常被稱為……","examples":[{"en":"Drug-type cannabis is commonly called marijuana.","zh":"毒品型大麻通常被稱為 marijuana。"},{"en":"Commonly called means usually known by that name.","zh":"commonly called 指通常以某名稱被認識。"},{"en":"A mobile phone is commonly called a phone in everyday speech.","zh":"mobile phone 在日常說話中通常被稱為 phone。"},{"en":"Common names can be easier to remember than scientific or technical names.","zh":"常用名稱通常比科學或技術名稱更容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving a familiar name for something.","zh":"為某事物提供熟悉名稱時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"drug cannabis","meaning":"毒品大麻","examples":[{"en":"Marijuana is also called drug cannabis.","zh":"marijuana 也被稱為毒品大麻。"},{"en":"Drug cannabis means cannabis grown or used for its intoxicating drug effects rather than industrial fibre or seeds.","zh":"drug cannabis 指為其令人產生迷幻或興奮效果而種植或使用的大麻，而不是為工業纖維或種子。"},{"en":"Laws often treat drug cannabis differently from industrial hemp.","zh":"法律常把毒品大麻與工業大麻不同處理。"},{"en":"Confusing drug cannabis with hemp can create public misunderstanding.","zh":"把毒品大麻與工業大麻混淆可以造成公眾誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when separating intoxicating cannabis from industrial hemp.","zh":"區分具迷幻作用大麻和工業大麻時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"drug-type cannabis","meaning":"毒品型大麻","examples":[{"en":"Drug-type cannabis varies widely in THC content.","zh":"毒品型大麻在四氫大麻酚含量方面差異很大。"},{"en":"Drug-type cannabis is cannabis grown for psychoactive drug content rather than industrial fibre.","zh":"drug-type cannabis 指為精神活性毒品成分而不是工業纖維而種植的大麻。"},{"en":"Regulators may test drug-type cannabis to measure its chemical strength.","zh":"監管者可能測試毒品型大麻，以量度其化學強度。"},{"en":"Different chemical levels can affect legal classification and health concerns.","zh":"不同化學水平可以影響法律分類和健康憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing cannabis types in a technical way.","zh":"以技術方式討論大麻類型時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"varies widely in","meaning":"在……方面差異很大","examples":[{"en":"Drug-type cannabis varies widely in THC content.","zh":"毒品型大麻在四氫大麻酚含量方面差異很大。"},{"en":"Varies widely in something means differs greatly in that particular feature.","zh":"varies widely in something 指在某一特徵上差別很大。"},{"en":"Restaurants vary widely in price, service, and food quality.","zh":"餐廳在價格、服務和食物質素方面差異很大。"},{"en":"When products vary widely, consumers need clear information before choosing.","zh":"當產品差異很大，消費者選擇前需要清楚資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when differences are large.","zh":"當差別很大時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"THC content","meaning":"四氫大麻酚含量","examples":[{"en":"Modern marijuana varieties can contain high THC content.","zh":"現代 marijuana 品種可以含有高四氫大麻酚含量。"},{"en":"THC content means the amount of tetrahydrocannabinol, the main psychoactive chemical, in cannabis.","zh":"THC content 指大麻中四氫大麻酚這種主要精神活性化學物質的含量。"},{"en":"A laboratory may measure THC content to classify a cannabis sample legally.","zh":"實驗室可能量度四氫大麻酚含量，以依法分類大麻樣本。"},{"en":"Higher THC content can change how a product is regulated and assessed for risk.","zh":"較高四氫大麻酚含量可以改變產品的監管方式和風險評估。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing cannabis chemistry in a factual way.","zh":"以事實方式討論大麻化學時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"unselected strains","meaning":"未經篩選的品種","examples":[{"en":"Unselected strains may contain only 1–2% THC.","zh":"未經篩選的品種可能只含有1至2%的 THC。"},{"en":"Unselected strains are plant varieties that have not been specially bred or chosen for a particular trait.","zh":"unselected strains 指沒有為某一特徵特別培育或挑選的植物品種。"},{"en":"A farmer may get uneven results from unselected strains because the plants vary naturally.","zh":"農民使用未經篩選的品種可能得到不一致結果，因為植物自然差異很大。"},{"en":"Selective breeding can increase or reduce certain qualities in later generations.","zh":"選擇性育種可以增加或減少後代中的某些特質。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing plant breeding and natural variation.","zh":"討論植物育種和自然差異時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"modern varieties","meaning":"現代品種","examples":[{"en":"The best modern varieties can contain around 10% THC.","zh":"最好的現代品種可含有約10% THC。"},{"en":"Modern varieties are newer plant types developed or selected in recent times.","zh":"modern varieties 指近代發展或挑選出來的新植物類型。"},{"en":"Modern varieties of tomatoes may be bred to resist disease and travel well.","zh":"現代番茄品種可能被培育成抗病且適合運輸。"},{"en":"New varieties can change farming results because they have different traits from older plants.","zh":"新品種可以改變農業結果，因為它們與較舊植物有不同特質。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing newer plant types with older ones.","zh":"比較較新和較舊植物類型時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cited in","meaning":"引自……","examples":[{"en":"The passage includes information cited in Watson, 1994.","zh":"文章包括引自 Watson, 1994 的資料。"},{"en":"Cited in means the information is quoted, referenced, or taken from a named source.","zh":"cited in 指資料被引用、參考或取自某個指定來源。"},{"en":"A student may write that a statistic was cited in a government report.","zh":"學生可能寫某項統計數字引自政府報告。"},{"en":"Citations help readers see where information came from and judge reliability.","zh":"引用幫助讀者看見資料來源，並判斷可靠性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving source attribution.","zh":"註明來源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"contains virtually none of","meaning":"幾乎不含……","examples":[{"en":"Hemp contains virtually none of the active ingredients of drug-type cannabis.","zh":"工業大麻幾乎不含毒品型大麻的活性成分。"},{"en":"Contains virtually none of something means has almost no amount of it.","zh":"contains virtually none of something 指幾乎沒有某物。"},{"en":"Decaffeinated coffee contains virtually none of the caffeine found in regular coffee.","zh":"低咖啡因咖啡幾乎不含普通咖啡中的咖啡因。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate two products that may look related but work very differently.","zh":"這個短語幫助區分兩種看似相關但作用非常不同的產品。"},{"en":"It is useful when stressing that a substance is almost absent.","zh":"強調某種物質幾乎不存在時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"active ingredients","meaning":"活性成分","examples":[{"en":"Hemp contains almost none of the active ingredients found in drug cannabis.","zh":"工業大麻幾乎不含毒品大麻中的活性成分。"},{"en":"Active ingredients are the substances in a product that produce its main effect.","zh":"active ingredients 指產品中產生主要作用的物質。"},{"en":"The active ingredients in medicine are listed so doctors know what affects the body.","zh":"藥物中的活性成分會被列出，讓醫生知道甚麼會影響身體。"},{"en":"If two products have different active ingredients, they may have very different effects.","zh":"如果兩種產品有不同活性成分，它們的作用可能非常不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing chemicals that make a product work.","zh":"討論令產品發揮作用的化學物質時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not feasible to","meaning":"不可行","examples":[{"en":"It is not feasible to get high on hemp.","zh":"吸食工業大麻後產生快感是不可行的。"},{"en":"Not feasible to do something means not practical, realistic, or possible in normal conditions.","zh":"not feasible to do something 指在正常情況下不實際、不現實或不可能。"},{"en":"It is not feasible to finish a full research project in one evening.","zh":"一個晚上完成整個研究項目是不可行的。"},{"en":"When something is not feasible, people should choose a more realistic plan.","zh":"當某事不可行，人們應選擇更現實的計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining that an idea cannot work practically.","zh":"解釋某想法實際上不能行得通時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get high","meaning":"吸食後產生快感；感到興奮","examples":[{"en":"It is not feasible to get high on hemp.","zh":"吸食工業大麻後產生快感是不可行的。"},{"en":"Get high means experience an intoxicating effect from a psychoactive drug.","zh":"get high 指因精神活性毒品而產生迷幻或興奮效果。"},{"en":"A health lesson may explain that different substances have different risks and effects.","zh":"健康課可能解釋不同物質有不同風險和作用。"},{"en":"Hemp is described as different because it lacks the active ingredients needed for that effect.","zh":"工業大麻被描述為不同，因為它缺乏產生該效果所需的活性成分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing drug effects in a factual health or legal context.","zh":"在事實性的健康或法律語境中討論毒品作用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"produces very low-quality fibre","meaning":"產生質素很低的纖維","examples":[{"en":"Most marijuana produces very low-quality fibre.","zh":"大多數 marijuana 產生質素很低的纖維。"},{"en":"Produces very low-quality fibre means gives fibre that is weak, poor, or unsuitable for good industrial use.","zh":"produces very low-quality fibre 指產生脆弱、差劣或不適合良好工業用途的纖維。"},{"en":"A plant with short, brittle stems may produce very low-quality fibre for rope-making.","zh":"莖短而易碎的植物，可能為製繩產生質素很低的纖維。"},{"en":"Poor fibre quality reduces a crop’s value for textiles and industrial products.","zh":"纖維質素差會降低作物在紡織和工業產品中的價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing plants by material quality.","zh":"按材料質素比較植物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"should never be confused with","meaning":"絕不應與……混淆","examples":[{"en":"Hemp should never be confused with marijuana.","zh":"工業大麻絕不應與 marijuana 混淆。"},{"en":"Should never be confused with means must not be mistaken for something else.","zh":"should never be confused with 指絕不能被誤認為另一事物。"},{"en":"A food allergy should never be confused with simply disliking a food.","zh":"食物敏感絕不應與單純不喜歡某種食物混淆。"},{"en":"Confusing two different things can lead to wrong decisions and unfair judgement.","zh":"混淆兩件不同事物可以導致錯誤決定和不公平判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when two similar terms need strong separation.","zh":"當兩個相似術語需要強烈區分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not interchangeable","meaning":"不可互換","examples":[{"en":"Hemp and marijuana are not interchangeable.","zh":"工業大麻和 marijuana 不可互換。"},{"en":"Not interchangeable means two things cannot be used or treated as if they are the same.","zh":"not interchangeable 指兩件事不能被當作相同事物使用或處理。"},{"en":"A student card and an identity card are not interchangeable in every situation.","zh":"學生證和身份證在所有情況下並不可互換。"},{"en":"When terms are not interchangeable, using the wrong one can change the meaning completely.","zh":"當術語不可互換，使用錯誤一個可以完全改變意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when similar things have different functions or meanings.","zh":"當相似事物有不同功能或意思時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"it is evident that","meaning":"很明顯","examples":[{"en":"It is evident that hemp is an extraordinary fibre.","zh":"很明顯，工業大麻是一種非凡纖維。"},{"en":"It is evident that means it is clear or easy to see that something is true.","zh":"it is evident that 指某事很清楚或容易看出是真。"},{"en":"It is evident that the student practised because their pronunciation improved greatly.","zh":"很明顯那學生練習過，因為他的發音大大改善。"},{"en":"Evidence makes a claim easier to accept.","zh":"證據令一個說法更容易被接受。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing a conclusion based on clear facts.","zh":"根據清楚事實引入結論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"extraordinary fibre","meaning":"非凡的纖維","examples":[{"en":"Hemp is an extraordinary fibre.","zh":"工業大麻是一種非凡的纖維。"},{"en":"An extraordinary fibre is a fibre with unusually strong, useful, or valuable qualities.","zh":"extraordinary fibre 指具有異常堅韌、有用或有價值特質的纖維。"},{"en":"A fibre that is strong, soft, durable, and resistant to mildew may be called extraordinary.","zh":"一種堅韌、柔軟、耐用且防霉的纖維，可以被稱為非凡纖維。"},{"en":"Extraordinary fibres can change industries because they perform better than common materials.","zh":"非凡纖維可以改變產業，因為它們比普通材料表現更好。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when praising a material’s unusual qualities.","zh":"讚揚材料不尋常特質時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"stems and seeds","meaning":"莖和種子","examples":[{"en":"Both hemp stems and seeds can be utilised.","zh":"工業大麻的莖和種子都可以被利用。"},{"en":"Stems and seeds are the stalk parts and seed parts of a plant.","zh":"stems and seeds 指植物的莖部和種子部分。"},{"en":"In some crops, stems and seeds can both be sold for different purposes.","zh":"在某些作物中，莖和種子都可以因不同用途而出售。"},{"en":"A crop becomes more valuable when more than one part can be used.","zh":"當作物有多於一個部分可使用，它會變得更有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing useful plant parts.","zh":"討論有用植物部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"can be utilised","meaning":"可以被利用","examples":[{"en":"Both stems and seeds can be utilised.","zh":"莖和種子都可以被利用。"},{"en":"Can be utilised means can be used for a practical purpose.","zh":"can be utilised 指可以為實際目的而使用。"},{"en":"Old school computers can be utilised for basic typing practice.","zh":"舊學校電腦可以被用於基本打字練習。"},{"en":"When waste materials can be utilised, fewer resources are thrown away.","zh":"當廢料可以被利用，較少資源會被丟棄。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing that something has practical value.","zh":"顯示某事物有實際價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"most significantly","meaning":"最重要的是","examples":[{"en":"Most significantly, hemp can be grown without pesticides.","zh":"最重要的是，工業大麻無需殺蟲劑也能種植。"},{"en":"Most significantly means most importantly or most worth noticing.","zh":"most significantly 指最重要或最值得注意。"},{"en":"The school improved its classrooms, but most significantly, it trained teachers better.","zh":"學校改善了課室，但最重要的是，它更好地培訓了老師。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the point that matters most in the argument.","zh":"這個短語突出論點中最重要的一點。"},{"en":"It is useful when one fact is more important than the others.","zh":"當一項事實比其他事實更重要時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"grown without pesticides and herbicides","meaning":"無需殺蟲劑和除草劑也能種植","examples":[{"en":"Hemp can be grown without pesticides and herbicides.","zh":"工業大麻無需殺蟲劑和除草劑也能種植。"},{"en":"Grown without pesticides and herbicides means cultivated without chemicals used to kill insects or weeds.","zh":"grown without pesticides and herbicides 指不用殺蟲或除草化學品也能栽培。"},{"en":"Some vegetables are grown without pesticides and herbicides to appeal to organic-food customers.","zh":"有些蔬菜無需殺蟲劑和除草劑也能種植，以吸引有機食品顧客。"},{"en":"Crops grown with fewer chemicals may reduce pollution and farming costs.","zh":"使用較少化學品種植的作物，可以減少污染和農業成本。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing cleaner agriculture.","zh":"討論更潔淨農業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pesticides","meaning":"殺蟲劑","examples":[{"en":"Hemp can be grown without pesticides.","zh":"工業大麻無需殺蟲劑也能種植。"},{"en":"Pesticides are chemicals used to kill insects or other pests that damage crops.","zh":"pesticides 指用來殺死破壞作物的昆蟲或其他害蟲的化學品。"},{"en":"Farmers may use pesticides when caterpillars begin eating vegetable leaves.","zh":"當毛蟲開始吃蔬菜葉，農民可能使用殺蟲劑。"},{"en":"Too many pesticides can harm soil, water, wildlife, or human health.","zh":"太多殺蟲劑可以傷害土壤、水、野生動物或人類健康。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing farming chemicals.","zh":"討論農業化學品時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"herbicides","meaning":"除草劑","examples":[{"en":"Hemp can be grown without herbicides.","zh":"工業大麻無需除草劑也能種植。"},{"en":"Herbicides are chemicals used to kill unwanted plants or weeds.","zh":"herbicides 指用來殺死不需要植物或雜草的化學品。"},{"en":"A farmer may use herbicides to stop weeds competing with young crops.","zh":"農民可能使用除草劑，阻止雜草與幼小作物競爭。"},{"en":"If a crop naturally suppresses weeds, farmers may need fewer herbicides.","zh":"如果作物能自然抑制雜草，農民可能需要較少除草劑。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing weed control in farming.","zh":"討論農業中的雜草控制時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"has the ability to","meaning":"有能力去……","examples":[{"en":"The plant has the ability to suppress weeds.","zh":"這種植物有能力抑制雜草。"},{"en":"Has the ability to means can do something or has the power to do it.","zh":"has the ability to 指能夠做某事或有力量做某事。"},{"en":"A good app has the ability to remind students to revise every day.","zh":"好應用程式有能力提醒學生每天溫習。"},{"en":"When a crop has the ability to solve a farming problem, it becomes more valuable.","zh":"當作物有能力解決農業問題，它會變得更有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing capability.","zh":"描述能力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"suppress weeds","meaning":"抑制雜草","examples":[{"en":"Hemp has the ability to suppress weeds.","zh":"工業大麻有能力抑制雜草。"},{"en":"Suppress weeds means stop unwanted plants from growing strongly.","zh":"suppress weeds 指阻止不需要的植物強勢生長。"},{"en":"Thick grass can suppress weeds by blocking sunlight from reaching the soil.","zh":"茂密草地可以透過阻擋陽光到達土壤來抑制雜草。"},{"en":"A crop that suppresses weeds may reduce the need for chemical herbicides.","zh":"能抑制雜草的作物可能減少對化學除草劑的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when plants naturally control competition.","zh":"當植物自然控制競爭時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"soil-borne diseases","meaning":"土傳病害","examples":[{"en":"Hemp can suppress weeds and soil-borne diseases.","zh":"工業大麻可以抑制雜草和土傳病害。"},{"en":"Soil-borne diseases are plant diseases that live in or spread through the soil.","zh":"soil-borne diseases 指存在於土壤中或透過土壤傳播的植物病害。"},{"en":"A farmer may rotate crops to reduce soil-borne diseases in vegetable fields.","zh":"農民可能輪作，以減少菜田中的土傳病害。"},{"en":"If soil diseases are controlled, crops can grow more strongly and safely.","zh":"如果土壤病害受到控制，作物可以更強壯和安全地生長。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing crop health and soil management.","zh":"討論作物健康和土壤管理時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"established overseas hemp industries","meaning":"已建立的海外工業大麻產業","examples":[{"en":"Established overseas hemp industries show strong demand for hemp products.","zh":"已建立的海外工業大麻產業顯示對工業大麻產品有強勁需求。"},{"en":"Established overseas hemp industries are developed hemp businesses already operating in other countries.","zh":"established overseas hemp industries 指已在其他國家運作成熟的工業大麻企業和產業。"},{"en":"A local government may study established overseas hemp industries before changing farming policy.","zh":"本地政府在改變農業政策前，可能研究已建立的海外工業大麻產業。"},{"en":"Existing overseas examples can show whether a crop has a real market.","zh":"既有海外例子可以顯示某作物是否有真實市場。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when foreign industries provide evidence of demand.","zh":"當外國產業提供需求證據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"strong demand for","meaning":"對……有強勁需求","examples":[{"en":"There is strong demand for hemp products.","zh":"對工業大麻產品有強勁需求。"},{"en":"Strong demand for something means many people or businesses want to buy or use it.","zh":"strong demand for something 指許多人或企業想購買或使用某物。"},{"en":"There is strong demand for private tutors before major public exams.","zh":"重大公開考試前，對私人補習老師有強勁需求。"},{"en":"Strong demand can raise prices, increase production, and attract investment.","zh":"強勁需求可以提高價格、增加生產並吸引投資。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a product or service is wanted by many people.","zh":"當產品或服務受到許多人需要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hemp products","meaning":"工業大麻產品","examples":[{"en":"Strong demand exists for hemp products.","zh":"工業大麻產品存在強勁需求。"},{"en":"Hemp products are goods made from hemp fibre, seeds, oil, or other parts of the plant.","zh":"hemp products 指由工業大麻纖維、種子、油或植物其他部分製成的商品。"},{"en":"Hemp products may include bags, clothing, paper, food, shampoo, and building materials.","zh":"工業大麻產品可以包括袋、衣服、紙張、食品、洗頭水和建築材料。"},{"en":"The variety of hemp products makes the crop useful in several markets.","zh":"工業大麻產品種類多，使這種作物在幾個市場都有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing what hemp can be turned into.","zh":"討論工業大麻可以製成甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"highly profitable","meaning":"利潤很高","examples":[{"en":"Hemp can be highly profitable.","zh":"工業大麻可以利潤很高。"},{"en":"Highly profitable means able to make a large amount of profit.","zh":"highly profitable 指能賺取大量利潤。"},{"en":"A small bakery may become highly profitable if its rent is low and cakes sell quickly.","zh":"如果租金低且蛋糕賣得快，小麵包店可以變得利潤很高。"},{"en":"A crop can be highly profitable when it has high demand and low growing costs.","zh":"當作物需求高且種植成本低，它可以利潤很高。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something can earn a lot of money.","zh":"當某事能賺很多錢時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on an annual basis","meaning":"按年計算","examples":[{"en":"On an annual basis, one acre of hemp produces as much fibre as several acres of cotton.","zh":"按年計算，一英畝工業大麻產生的纖維與數英畝棉花一樣多。"},{"en":"On an annual basis means measured or calculated over one year.","zh":"on an annual basis 指按一年時間量度或計算。"},{"en":"A school may review student progress on an annual basis.","zh":"學校可能按年檢討學生進度。"},{"en":"Annual comparisons help people see long-term productivity rather than one short result.","zh":"年度比較幫助人看見長期生產力，而不是一次短期結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing yearly output or performance.","zh":"比較年度產量或表現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"one acre of","meaning":"一英畝的……","examples":[{"en":"One acre of hemp can produce as much fibre as 2 to 3 acres of cotton.","zh":"一英畝工業大麻可以產生相當於2至3英畝棉花的纖維。"},{"en":"One acre of something means an area of land measuring one acre used for that crop or purpose.","zh":"one acre of something 指一英畝土地用於某作物或目的。"},{"en":"One acre of vegetables can feed many families if it is farmed carefully.","zh":"如果細心耕種，一英畝蔬菜可以養活許多家庭。"},{"en":"Land productivity matters because farmers have limited space.","zh":"土地生產力很重要，因為農民空間有限。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing crop output by land area.","zh":"按土地面積比較作物產量時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as much fibre as","meaning":"與……一樣多的纖維","examples":[{"en":"One acre of hemp produces as much fibre as 2 to 3 acres of cotton.","zh":"一英畝工業大麻產生的纖維與2至3英畝棉花一樣多。"},{"en":"As much fibre as means the same quantity of fibre as another source produces.","zh":"as much fibre as 指纖維數量與另一來源產生的相同。"},{"en":"A small field of one crop may produce as much fibre as a larger field of another crop.","zh":"一種作物的小田地可能產生與另一種作物較大田地一樣多的纖維。"},{"en":"Higher fibre output from less land can make a crop more efficient.","zh":"用較少土地產生更多纖維，可以令作物更有效率。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing production amounts.","zh":"比較產量時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"stronger and softer than","meaning":"比……更堅韌和柔軟","examples":[{"en":"Hemp fibre is stronger and softer than cotton.","zh":"工業大麻纖維比棉花更堅韌和柔軟。"},{"en":"Stronger and softer than means having more strength and a gentler texture compared with something else.","zh":"stronger and softer than 指相比某物有更高強度和更柔和質感。"},{"en":"A blanket may be stronger and softer than an old one if it uses better fibre.","zh":"如果毛氈使用更好纖維，它可能比舊毛氈更堅韌和柔軟。"},{"en":"Materials with both strength and softness are valuable for clothing and household goods.","zh":"同時堅韌和柔軟的材料，對衣物和家居用品有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing physical qualities.","zh":"比較物理特質時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lasts twice as long","meaning":"耐用時間長一倍","examples":[{"en":"Hemp fibre lasts twice as long as cotton.","zh":"工業大麻纖維耐用時間比棉花長一倍。"},{"en":"Lasts twice as long means remains usable for two times the length of time.","zh":"lasts twice as long 指可用時間是另一物的兩倍。"},{"en":"A good school bag may last twice as long as a cheap one if the stitching is stronger.","zh":"如果縫線更堅固，好書包可能比便宜書包耐用時間長一倍。"},{"en":"Products that last longer can save money and reduce waste.","zh":"更耐用的產品可以省錢並減少浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing durability.","zh":"比較耐用程度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"will not mildew","meaning":"不會發霉","examples":[{"en":"Hemp fibre will not mildew.","zh":"工業大麻纖維不會發霉。"},{"en":"Will not mildew means will not easily develop mould in damp conditions.","zh":"will not mildew 指在潮濕環境中不容易長霉。"},{"en":"A bathroom curtain that will not mildew is easier to keep clean.","zh":"不會發霉的浴室簾較容易保持清潔。"},{"en":"Mildew resistance is valuable in humid places because fabric can otherwise smell and weaken.","zh":"在潮濕地方，防霉能力很有價值，因為布料否則可能有味道並變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing material resistance to dampness.","zh":"討論材料抗潮能力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"warm climates","meaning":"溫暖氣候","examples":[{"en":"Cotton grows only in warm climates.","zh":"棉花只在溫暖氣候中生長。"},{"en":"Warm climates are regions where temperatures are generally high enough for heat-loving plants.","zh":"warm climates 指溫度通常足夠高，適合喜熱植物生長的地區。"},{"en":"Mangoes grow well in warm climates but may fail in cold winters.","zh":"芒果在溫暖氣候中生長良好，但可能在寒冬中失敗。"},{"en":"Climate limits where certain crops can be grown successfully.","zh":"氣候限制某些作物能在哪裏成功種植。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing farming conditions.","zh":"討論農業條件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"requires more water","meaning":"需要更多水","examples":[{"en":"Cotton requires more water than hemp.","zh":"棉花比工業大麻需要更多水。"},{"en":"Requires more water means needs a larger amount of water to grow or operate.","zh":"requires more water 指生長或運作需要較大量的水。"},{"en":"A garden with many flowers may require more water than one planted with drought-resistant shrubs.","zh":"有很多花的花園可能比種植耐旱灌木的花園需要更多水。"},{"en":"Crops that require more water can be harder to grow in dry regions.","zh":"需要更多水的作物在乾旱地區較難種植。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing resource needs.","zh":"比較資源需求時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"more fertiliser","meaning":"更多肥料","examples":[{"en":"Cotton requires more fertiliser than hemp.","zh":"棉花比工業大麻需要更多肥料。"},{"en":"More fertiliser means a larger amount of substances added to soil to help plants grow.","zh":"more fertiliser 指更多加入土壤以幫助植物生長的物質。"},{"en":"Vegetables grown in poor soil may need more fertiliser to produce a good harvest.","zh":"在貧瘠土壤中種植的蔬菜，可能需要更多肥料才能有好收成。"},{"en":"Crops needing more fertiliser can cost more and increase environmental pressure.","zh":"需要更多肥料的作物可能成本更高，並增加環境壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing agricultural inputs.","zh":"比較農業投入時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"large quantities of","meaning":"大量的……","examples":[{"en":"Cotton requires large quantities of pesticides and herbicides.","zh":"棉花需要大量殺蟲劑和除草劑。"},{"en":"Large quantities of something means a lot of it.","zh":"large quantities of something 指大量某物。"},{"en":"A school event may require large quantities of water if hundreds of students attend.","zh":"如果數百名學生參加，學校活動可能需要大量清水。"},{"en":"Using large quantities of chemicals can increase costs and environmental risks.","zh":"使用大量化學品可以增加成本和環境風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing a high amount.","zh":"強調數量多時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"produce fibreboard","meaning":"生產纖維板","examples":[{"en":"Hemp can be used to produce fibreboard.","zh":"工業大麻可用來生產纖維板。"},{"en":"Produce fibreboard means make a board material from compressed fibres.","zh":"produce fibreboard 指由壓縮纖維製造板材。"},{"en":"A factory may produce fibreboard from plant waste instead of cutting more trees.","zh":"工廠可能由植物廢料生產纖維板，而不是砍伐更多樹木。"},{"en":"Fibreboard production can create useful building materials from renewable crops.","zh":"纖維板生產可以由可再生作物創造有用建築材料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing manufactured boards.","zh":"討論人造板材時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"fibreboard","meaning":"纖維板","examples":[{"en":"Hemp fibreboard is stronger and lighter than wood.","zh":"工業大麻纖維板比木材更堅固和輕。"},{"en":"Fibreboard is a board made by pressing fibres together with binders or heat.","zh":"fibreboard 指把纖維用黏合劑或熱力壓合而成的板材。"},{"en":"Furniture makers may use fibreboard for shelves, cupboards, or wall panels.","zh":"家具製造商可能用纖維板製作層架、櫃或牆板。"},{"en":"Strong and light fibreboard can reduce transport costs and make construction easier.","zh":"堅固而輕的纖維板可以降低運輸成本，並令建築更容易。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing engineered building materials.","zh":"討論工程建築材料時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stronger and lighter than","meaning":"比……更堅固和輕","examples":[{"en":"Hemp fibreboard is stronger and lighter than wood.","zh":"工業大麻纖維板比木材更堅固和輕。"},{"en":"Stronger and lighter than means more able to resist force while weighing less.","zh":"stronger and lighter than 指更能承受力量，同時重量較低。"},{"en":"A new suitcase may be stronger and lighter than an old one if it uses better materials.","zh":"如果新行李箱使用更好材料，它可能比舊行李箱更堅固和輕。"},{"en":"Materials that are both strong and light are useful for transport and construction.","zh":"同時堅固和輕的材料對運輸和建築有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing performance and weight.","zh":"比較性能和重量時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"fire-retardant","meaning":"阻燃的","examples":[{"en":"Hemp fibreboard is fire-retardant.","zh":"工業大麻纖維板是阻燃的。"},{"en":"Fire-retardant means able to slow the spread of fire or resist burning.","zh":"fire-retardant 指能減慢火勢蔓延或抗燃燒。"},{"en":"Curtains in a school hall may need to be fire-retardant for safety reasons.","zh":"學校禮堂的窗簾可能因安全原因需要阻燃。"},{"en":"Fire-retardant materials can give people more time to escape during an emergency.","zh":"阻燃材料可以在緊急情況中給人更多逃生時間。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing building safety.","zh":"討論建築安全時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"unlike","meaning":"與……不同","examples":[{"en":"Unlike paper from wood pulp, hemp paper contains no dioxin.","zh":"與木漿製成的紙不同，工業大麻紙不含二噁英。"},{"en":"Unlike means different from or in contrast to something else.","zh":"unlike 指與某事物不同或形成對比。"},{"en":"Unlike buses, trains are not usually delayed by road traffic.","zh":"與巴士不同，火車通常不會因道路交通而延誤。"},{"en":"This word clearly introduces a contrast between two things.","zh":"這個詞清楚引入兩件事之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when one item has a feature that another does not have.","zh":"當一件事有另一件事沒有的特徵時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"wood pulp","meaning":"木漿","examples":[{"en":"Paper from wood pulp may contain toxic residue.","zh":"由木漿製成的紙可能含有有毒殘留物。"},{"en":"Wood pulp is soft processed wood material used to make paper.","zh":"wood pulp 指經加工變軟、用來造紙的木材材料。"},{"en":"A paper factory turns logs or wood chips into wood pulp before making sheets.","zh":"造紙廠在製成紙張前，會把原木或木片變成木漿。"},{"en":"The chemicals used in processing wood pulp can affect paper quality and pollution.","zh":"木漿處理中使用的化學品可以影響紙張質素和污染。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing paper production.","zh":"討論造紙生產時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"contains no dioxin","meaning":"不含二噁英","examples":[{"en":"Hemp paper contains no dioxin.","zh":"工業大麻紙不含二噁英。"},{"en":"Contains no dioxin means has none of a toxic chemical called dioxin.","zh":"contains no dioxin 指完全沒有一種叫二噁英的有毒化學物質。"},{"en":"A cleaner manufacturing process may produce paper that contains no harmful residue.","zh":"較潔淨的製造過程可能生產不含有害殘留物的紙。"},{"en":"Avoiding toxic chemicals can make products safer for people and the environment.","zh":"避免有毒化學品可以令產品對人和環境更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing chemical safety in materials.","zh":"討論材料中的化學安全時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"toxic residue","meaning":"有毒殘留物","examples":[{"en":"Hemp paper contains no dioxin or other toxic residue.","zh":"工業大麻紙不含二噁英或其他有毒殘留物。"},{"en":"Toxic residue is harmful leftover material from manufacturing, chemicals, or pollution.","zh":"toxic residue 指製造、化學品或污染留下的有害物質。"},{"en":"A factory must clean equipment carefully to avoid toxic residue in food packaging.","zh":"工廠必須仔細清潔設備，以避免食品包裝中有有毒殘留物。"},{"en":"Toxic residue can harm people, animals, soil, or water if it is not controlled.","zh":"如果不受控制，有毒殘留物可以傷害人、動物、土壤或水。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing pollution and product safety.","zh":"討論污染和產品安全時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a single acre of","meaning":"單單一英畝的……","examples":[{"en":"A single acre of hemp can produce as much paper as four acres of trees.","zh":"單單一英畝工業大麻可生產與四英畝樹木一樣多的紙。"},{"en":"A single acre of something means just one acre of land used for that crop or material.","zh":"a single acre of something 指僅一英畝土地用於某作物或材料。"},{"en":"A single acre of vegetables can be valuable if it produces several harvests a year.","zh":"如果一年可有幾次收成，單單一英畝蔬菜也可以很有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses how much output can come from a limited area.","zh":"這個短語強調有限土地可產生多少產出。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing land efficiency.","zh":"比較土地效率時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the same amount of paper as","meaning":"與……相同數量的紙","examples":[{"en":"Hemp can produce the same amount of paper as several acres of trees.","zh":"工業大麻可以生產與幾英畝樹木相同數量的紙。"},{"en":"The same amount of paper as means an equal quantity of paper compared with another source.","zh":"same amount of paper as 指與另一來源相比有相同紙張數量。"},{"en":"One printer cartridge may print the same amount of paper as two cheaper cartridges.","zh":"一個打印機墨盒可能打印出與兩個較便宜墨盒相同數量的紙。"},{"en":"Equal output from fewer resources can make a method more efficient.","zh":"用較少資源得到相同產出，可以令方法更有效率。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing production efficiency.","zh":"比較生產效率時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take 20 years to harvest","meaning":"需要二十年才可收割","examples":[{"en":"Trees take 20 years to harvest.","zh":"樹木需要二十年才可收割。"},{"en":"Take 20 years to harvest means require twenty years of growth before being ready to cut or collect.","zh":"take 20 years to harvest 指需要二十年生長才準備好被砍伐或收取。"},{"en":"Some fruit trees take several years to harvest, so farmers must plan far ahead.","zh":"有些果樹需要幾年才可收成，所以農民必須長遠規劃。"},{"en":"Long growing times make replacement slower and resource planning more difficult.","zh":"生長時間長會令補充較慢，資源規劃也更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing crop growth periods.","zh":"比較作物生長期時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a single season","meaning":"一個生長季節","examples":[{"en":"Hemp takes only a single season to harvest.","zh":"工業大麻只需一個生長季節便可收割。"},{"en":"A single season means one growing period, such as one spring-to-summer crop cycle.","zh":"single season 指一個生長時段，例如由春至夏的一個作物周期。"},{"en":"Lettuce can often be grown in a single season, so farmers can harvest it quickly.","zh":"生菜常可在一個生長季節內種成，因此農民能快速收成。"},{"en":"A crop that grows in one season can produce income faster than trees.","zh":"一季內長成的作物可以比樹木更快產生收入。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing short growing cycles.","zh":"討論短生長周期時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"harvested two or even three times a year","meaning":"一年可收割兩次甚至三次","examples":[{"en":"In warm climates, hemp can be harvested two or even three times a year.","zh":"在溫暖氣候中，工業大麻一年可收割兩次甚至三次。"},{"en":"Harvested two or even three times a year means collected from the field more than once annually.","zh":"harvested two or even three times a year 指每年可從田地收取多於一次。"},{"en":"Some fast-growing vegetables can be harvested several times a year in warm regions.","zh":"在溫暖地區，有些快速生長的蔬菜一年可收割多次。"},{"en":"Multiple harvests increase output from the same land.","zh":"多次收割增加同一土地的產出。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing high agricultural productivity.","zh":"討論高農業生產力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"from tissue paper to cardboard","meaning":"從紙巾到紙板","examples":[{"en":"From tissue paper to cardboard, many paper products can be made from hemp.","zh":"從紙巾到紙板，許多紙製品都可以由工業大麻製成。"},{"en":"From tissue paper to cardboard means covering a wide range from very thin paper to thick board.","zh":"from tissue paper to cardboard 指範圍由很薄的紙到厚紙板。"},{"en":"A stationery shop sells products from notebooks to envelopes, showing a wide product range.","zh":"文具店售賣從筆記簿到信封的產品，顯示產品範圍很廣。"},{"en":"This structure shows variety by naming two opposite or distant examples.","zh":"這個結構透過列出兩個相反或相距較遠的例子來顯示多樣性。"},{"en":"It is useful when a material can be used for many product types.","zh":"當一種材料可用於許多產品類型時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"paper products","meaning":"紙製品","examples":[{"en":"All types of paper products can be produced from hemp.","zh":"各類紙製品都可以由工業大麻生產。"},{"en":"Paper products are items made from paper or paper-like material.","zh":"paper products 指由紙或類似紙的材料製成的物品。"},{"en":"Notebooks, envelopes, boxes, tissues, and greeting cards are paper products.","zh":"筆記簿、信封、盒、紙巾和賀卡都是紙製品。"},{"en":"If a crop can supply many paper products, it may reduce demand for wood pulp.","zh":"如果一種作物能供應許多紙製品，它可能減少對木漿的需求。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing goods made from paper.","zh":"討論由紙製成的商品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"produced from hemp","meaning":"由工業大麻製成","examples":[{"en":"All types of paper products can be produced from hemp.","zh":"各類紙製品都可以由工業大麻製成。"},{"en":"Produced from hemp means made using hemp as the raw material.","zh":"produced from hemp 指使用工業大麻作為原材料製成。"},{"en":"A notebook produced from hemp may use less tree-based paper.","zh":"由工業大麻製成的筆記簿可能使用較少樹木紙。"},{"en":"Products produced from renewable crops can appeal to environmentally aware customers.","zh":"由可再生作物製成的產品可以吸引有環保意識的顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying the source material.","zh":"識別來源材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"superior to","meaning":"優於……","examples":[{"en":"The quality of hemp paper is superior to tree-based paper.","zh":"工業大麻紙的質素優於以樹木製成的紙。"},{"en":"Superior to means better than something else in quality, performance, or value.","zh":"superior to 指在質素、表現或價值上比另一物更好。"},{"en":"A waterproof school bag may be superior to a cloth bag during rainy season.","zh":"在雨季，防水書包可能優於布袋。"},{"en":"If one material lasts longer and performs better, it may be superior to another.","zh":"如果一種材料更耐用且表現更好，它可能優於另一種材料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when making a quality comparison.","zh":"作質素比較時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"tree-based paper","meaning":"以樹木製成的紙","examples":[{"en":"Hemp paper is more durable than tree-based paper.","zh":"工業大麻紙比以樹木製成的紙更耐用。"},{"en":"Tree-based paper is paper made from wood or tree pulp.","zh":"tree-based paper 指由木材或木漿製成的紙。"},{"en":"Most office paper is tree-based paper because wood pulp is widely used.","zh":"大多數辦公室用紙是以樹木製成的紙，因為木漿被廣泛使用。"},{"en":"If alternatives become cheaper, companies may use less tree-based paper.","zh":"如果替代品變得更便宜，公司可能使用較少樹木紙。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing paper sources.","zh":"比較紙張來源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"last hundreds of years","meaning":"可保存數百年","examples":[{"en":"Hemp paper can last hundreds of years without degrading.","zh":"工業大麻紙可保存數百年而不會劣化。"},{"en":"Last hundreds of years means remain usable or readable for several centuries.","zh":"last hundreds of years 指可使用或閱讀數個世紀。"},{"en":"Museum documents must be stored carefully if they are meant to last hundreds of years.","zh":"如果博物館文件要保存數百年，就必須仔細儲存。"},{"en":"Long-lasting materials help preserve records, art, and cultural memory.","zh":"耐久材料有助保存紀錄、藝術和文化記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing durability over centuries.","zh":"討論跨世紀耐用性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"without degrading","meaning":"不會劣化","examples":[{"en":"Hemp paper can last hundreds of years without degrading.","zh":"工業大麻紙可保存數百年而不會劣化。"},{"en":"Without degrading means without breaking down, weakening, or losing quality.","zh":"without degrading 指沒有分解、變弱或失去質素。"},{"en":"A good photo album should protect pictures without degrading over time.","zh":"好相簿應保護照片，而且隨時間不會劣化。"},{"en":"Materials that resist degradation are useful for archives and important documents.","zh":"抗劣化材料對檔案和重要文件有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something keeps its quality for a long time.","zh":"當某物長時間保持質素時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"recycled many more times","meaning":"可多次回收","examples":[{"en":"Hemp paper can be recycled many more times than tree-based paper.","zh":"工業大麻紙比樹木紙可多次回收更多次。"},{"en":"Recycled many more times means processed and reused repeatedly more often than another material.","zh":"recycled many more times 指比另一材料更能反覆被加工和重新使用。"},{"en":"A strong glass bottle can be recycled many more times than a weak plastic container.","zh":"堅固玻璃瓶可以比脆弱塑膠容器回收更多次。"},{"en":"Materials that can be recycled more often reduce waste and save resources.","zh":"可更常回收的材料能減少廢物並節省資源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing reusability.","zh":"比較可重用性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"industrialised nations","meaning":"工業化國家","examples":[{"en":"Industrialised nations are waking up to the potential of hemp.","zh":"工業化國家正開始意識到工業大麻的潛力。"},{"en":"Industrialised nations are countries with advanced manufacturing, technology, and large modern economies.","zh":"industrialised nations 指擁有先進製造業、科技和大型現代經濟的國家。"},{"en":"Industrialised nations often invest in new materials for cars, buildings, and consumer goods.","zh":"工業化國家常為汽車、建築和消費品投資新材料。"},{"en":"When industrialised nations adopt a resource, global demand may rise quickly.","zh":"當工業化國家採用某資源，全球需求可能迅速上升。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing developed economies.","zh":"討論已發展經濟體時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"around the world","meaning":"世界各地","examples":[{"en":"Industrialised nations around the world are reconsidering hemp.","zh":"世界各地的工業化國家正在重新考慮工業大麻。"},{"en":"Around the world means in many countries or regions globally.","zh":"around the world 指在全球許多國家或地區。"},{"en":"Students around the world use online videos to learn difficult subjects.","zh":"世界各地的學生使用網上影片學習困難科目。"},{"en":"When an idea spreads around the world, it can influence markets and laws internationally.","zh":"當想法在世界各地傳播，它可以影響國際市場和法律。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing global reach.","zh":"描述全球範圍時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"wake up to","meaning":"開始意識到……","examples":[{"en":"Many countries are waking up to the enormous potential of hemp.","zh":"許多國家正開始意識到工業大麻的巨大潛力。"},{"en":"Wake up to something means finally realise or recognise something important.","zh":"wake up to something 指終於意識到或認識到重要事情。"},{"en":"Schools are waking up to the importance of mental health after students report stress.","zh":"學生表示有壓力後，學校開始意識到心理健康的重要性。"},{"en":"People often wake up to a problem or opportunity only after evidence becomes clear.","zh":"人們常在證據變得清楚後，才開始意識到問題或機會。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when awareness arrives after delay.","zh":"當認知延遲後才出現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"enormous potential","meaning":"巨大潛力","examples":[{"en":"Hemp has enormous potential as an industrial crop.","zh":"工業大麻作為工業作物有巨大潛力。"},{"en":"Enormous potential means very great possible value, ability, or future success.","zh":"enormous potential 指非常大的可能價值、能力或未來成功。"},{"en":"A hardworking student with strong curiosity may have enormous potential.","zh":"勤奮且好奇心強的學生可能有巨大潛力。"},{"en":"Potential becomes real only when people provide support, practice, and investment.","zh":"潛力只有在人們提供支援、練習和投資時才會成真。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when future value is very large.","zh":"當未來價值很大時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"laws against hemp cultivation","meaning":"禁止種植工業大麻的法律","examples":[{"en":"Some countries never had laws against hemp cultivation.","zh":"有些國家從未有禁止種植工業大麻的法律。"},{"en":"Laws against hemp cultivation are rules that prohibit or restrict growing hemp.","zh":"laws against hemp cultivation 指禁止或限制種植工業大麻的規則。"},{"en":"Farmers cannot legally grow a crop if there are strict laws against its cultivation.","zh":"如果有嚴格禁止種植某作物的法律，農民就不能合法種植它。"},{"en":"Removing such laws can allow a farming industry to develop again.","zh":"取消這類法律可以讓農業產業重新發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing legal barriers to crop production.","zh":"討論作物生產的法律障礙時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"hemp cultivation","meaning":"工業大麻種植","examples":[{"en":"China and India have not always had laws against hemp cultivation.","zh":"中國和印度並非一直有禁止工業大麻種植的法律。"},{"en":"Hemp cultivation means the farming or growing of hemp plants.","zh":"hemp cultivation 指工業大麻植物的農業種植。"},{"en":"Hemp cultivation requires suitable land, seeds, water, harvesting equipment, and legal permission.","zh":"工業大麻種植需要合適土地、種子、水、收割設備和法律許可。"},{"en":"If hemp cultivation expands, factories may receive more raw material for processing.","zh":"如果工業大麻種植擴大，工廠可能獲得更多原材料加工。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing hemp farming.","zh":"討論工業大麻農業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"legalising industrial hemp","meaning":"將工業大麻合法化","examples":[{"en":"Some countries are legalising industrial hemp.","zh":"有些國家正在將工業大麻合法化。"},{"en":"Legalising industrial hemp means making it lawful to grow, process, or sell hemp for industrial uses.","zh":"legalising industrial hemp 指使為工業用途種植、加工或銷售工業大麻成為合法。"},{"en":"A country may legalise industrial hemp so farmers can produce fibre and seeds legally.","zh":"國家可能將工業大麻合法化，讓農民合法生產纖維和種子。"},{"en":"Legalisation can create new business opportunities but usually requires clear regulation.","zh":"合法化可以創造新商機，但通常需要清晰規管。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing changes in hemp law.","zh":"討論工業大麻法律變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"after many years of","meaning":"在多年……之後","examples":[{"en":"Some countries are legalising hemp after many years of restriction.","zh":"有些國家在多年限制之後正將工業大麻合法化。"},{"en":"After many years of something means following a long period of that condition.","zh":"after many years of something 指經過長期某種情況之後。"},{"en":"After many years of saving, a family may finally buy a small flat.","zh":"在多年儲蓄之後，一個家庭可能終於買到小單位。"},{"en":"Long periods of restriction can make later change feel especially important.","zh":"長期限制可以令之後的改變顯得特別重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when change follows a long history.","zh":"當改變接在長久歷史之後，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lumping it together with","meaning":"將它與……混為一談","examples":[{"en":"Some countries lumped hemp together with marijuana.","zh":"有些國家把工業大麻與 marijuana 混為一談。"},{"en":"Lumping it together with something means treating two different things as if they are the same.","zh":"lumping it together with something 指把兩件不同事物當作相同處理。"},{"en":"A teacher should not lump careless spelling mistakes together with serious grammar problems.","zh":"老師不應把粗心串字錯誤與嚴重文法問題混為一談。"},{"en":"Lumping different things together can lead to unfair rules and poor understanding.","zh":"把不同事物混為一談可以導致不公平規則和差劣理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when criticising careless grouping.","zh":"批評粗心分類時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"emerging from","meaning":"從……出現","examples":[{"en":"New products are emerging from the international hemp industry.","zh":"新產品正從國際工業大麻產業中出現。"},{"en":"Emerging from means coming out of or developing from a source or situation.","zh":"emerging from 指從某來源或情況中出現或發展出來。"},{"en":"New teaching methods are emerging from online classrooms.","zh":"新教學方法正從網上課室中出現。"},{"en":"When new products emerge from an industry, it shows the industry is developing.","zh":"當新產品從某產業中出現，顯示該產業正在發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something new appears from a larger system.","zh":"當新事物由較大系統中出現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"international hemp industry","meaning":"國際工業大麻產業","examples":[{"en":"New fabrics are emerging from the international hemp industry.","zh":"新布料正從國際工業大麻產業中出現。"},{"en":"The international hemp industry is the global network of businesses that grow, process, and sell hemp products.","zh":"international hemp industry 指全球種植、加工和銷售工業大麻產品的企業網絡。"},{"en":"The international hemp industry includes farmers, textile makers, paper companies, and exporters.","zh":"國際工業大麻產業包括農民、紡織製造商、紙業公司和出口商。"},{"en":"A global industry can spread technology, standards, and product ideas across countries.","zh":"全球產業可以把技術、標準和產品想法傳播到各國。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when hemp business is discussed worldwide.","zh":"當工業大麻生意在全球層面討論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"finding strong demand","meaning":"找到強勁需求","examples":[{"en":"Hemp products are finding strong demand globally.","zh":"工業大麻產品在全球找到強勁需求。"},{"en":"Finding strong demand means discovering that many customers want to buy or use something.","zh":"finding strong demand 指發現許多顧客想購買或使用某物。"},{"en":"A new tutoring app may find strong demand if students need cheaper practice.","zh":"如果學生需要較便宜練習，新補習應用程式可能找到強勁需求。"},{"en":"Strong demand can encourage businesses to produce more and enter new markets.","zh":"強勁需求可以鼓勵企業生產更多並進入新市場。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a product becomes wanted by many people.","zh":"當產品變得被許多人需要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"eco-aware global community","meaning":"有環保意識的全球社群","examples":[{"en":"Hemp products appeal to an eco-aware global community.","zh":"工業大麻產品吸引有環保意識的全球社群。"},{"en":"An eco-aware global community is a worldwide group of people who care about environmental issues.","zh":"eco-aware global community 指全球關注環境議題的一群人。"},{"en":"Eco-aware consumers may choose reusable bottles, low-waste packaging, and renewable materials.","zh":"有環保意識的消費者可能選擇可重用水樽、低廢包裝和可再生材料。"},{"en":"Environmental awareness can create demand for cleaner products.","zh":"環保意識可以創造對更潔淨產品的需求。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when global consumers care about sustainability.","zh":"當全球消費者關注可持續性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agricultural crop","meaning":"農作物","examples":[{"en":"Hemp is an agricultural crop for the twenty-first century.","zh":"工業大麻是二十一世紀的農作物。"},{"en":"An agricultural crop is a plant grown by farmers for food, fibre, fuel, medicine, or other uses.","zh":"agricultural crop 指農民為食物、纖維、燃料、醫藥或其他用途而種植的植物。"},{"en":"Wheat, rice, cotton, and hemp are agricultural crops.","zh":"小麥、稻米、棉花和工業大麻都是農作物。"},{"en":"A crop becomes important when it meets economic, environmental, and social needs.","zh":"當作物符合經濟、環境和社會需要，它就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing plants grown in farming.","zh":"討論農業種植植物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the twenty-first century","meaning":"二十一世紀","examples":[{"en":"Hemp is described as a crop for the twenty-first century.","zh":"工業大麻被描述為二十一世紀的作物。"},{"en":"The twenty-first century is the period from 2001 to 2100.","zh":"twenty-first century 指2001年至2100年這段時期。"},{"en":"Schools in the twenty-first century need to teach digital skills as well as reading and writing.","zh":"二十一世紀的學校需要教授數碼技能以及讀寫能力。"},{"en":"Calling something suited to the twenty-first century suggests it fits modern needs.","zh":"稱某物適合二十一世紀，暗示它符合現代需要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when linking an idea to the modern age.","zh":"把想法與現代時代連接時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reorder the following letters","meaning":"重新排列以下字母","examples":[{"en":"Students reorder the following letters to show the sequence of events.","zh":"學生重新排列以下字母，以顯示事件次序。"},{"en":"Reorder the following letters means put the given lettered options into the correct order.","zh":"reorder the following letters 指把所給字母選項放入正確次序。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may reorder letters A to D according to what happened first.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能根據事件先後重新排列 A 至 D。"},{"en":"This task checks whether students understand time order, not just individual facts.","zh":"這個任務檢查學生是否理解時間順序，而不只是個別事實。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in sequencing questions.","zh":"這個短語適用於排序題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"sequence of events","meaning":"事件次序","examples":[{"en":"The question asks students to show the sequence of events.","zh":"題目要求學生顯示事件次序。"},{"en":"A sequence of events is the order in which things happened.","zh":"sequence of events 指事情發生的先後次序。"},{"en":"Students can understand a story better if they identify the sequence of events clearly.","zh":"如果學生清楚辨認事件次序，他們能更好理解故事。"},{"en":"Getting the sequence wrong can change the cause-and-effect meaning of a passage.","zh":"把次序弄錯可以改變文章中的因果意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when arranging historical or story information.","zh":"安排歷史或故事資料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"according to the passage","meaning":"根據文章","examples":[{"en":"The sequence should be arranged according to the passage.","zh":"次序應根據文章排列。"},{"en":"According to the passage means based only on the information in the reading text.","zh":"according to the passage 指只根據閱讀文本中的資料。"},{"en":"Students should answer according to the passage, not according to outside knowledge.","zh":"學生應根據文章作答，而不是根據外部知識。"},{"en":"This instruction prevents guessing from memory or personal opinion.","zh":"這個指示防止學生憑記憶或個人意見猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading-comprehension tasks.","zh":"這個短語適用於閱讀理解任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"widespread cultivation","meaning":"廣泛種植","examples":[{"en":"Widespread cultivation of hemp occurred before its decline.","zh":"工業大麻的廣泛種植發生在其衰落之前。"},{"en":"Widespread cultivation means growing a crop in many places or over large areas.","zh":"widespread cultivation 指在許多地方或大片地區種植某作物。"},{"en":"Widespread cultivation of rice supports food supply in many Asian regions.","zh":"稻米的廣泛種植支撐許多亞洲地區的糧食供應。"},{"en":"When cultivation is widespread, many farmers and businesses may depend on the crop.","zh":"當種植廣泛，許多農民和企業可能依賴該作物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when farming is common and extensive.","zh":"當農業種植普遍而廣泛時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"timber and petrochemical industries","meaning":"木材及石化工業","examples":[{"en":"The timber and petrochemical industries were threatened by hemp.","zh":"木材及石化工業受到工業大麻威脅。"},{"en":"Timber and petrochemical industries are the wood-related and oil-chemical business sectors.","zh":"timber and petrochemical industries 指與木材相關和石油化學相關的商業界別。"},{"en":"New renewable materials can compete with timber and petrochemical industries in paper, fuel, and fibres.","zh":"新可再生材料可以在紙張、燃料和纖維方面與木材及石化工業競爭。"},{"en":"Existing industries may resist a new crop if it threatens their products and profits.","zh":"如果新作物威脅產品和利潤，既有產業可能抵抗它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing competing industrial sectors.","zh":"討論互相競爭的工業界別時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"articles praise","meaning":"文章讚揚……","examples":[{"en":"Some articles praised hemp as a billion-dollar crop.","zh":"有些文章讚揚工業大麻是十億美元農作物。"},{"en":"Articles praise something when written pieces describe it positively or admire its value.","zh":"articles praise something 指書面文章正面描述或欣賞某物的價值。"},{"en":"Newspaper articles may praise a new library if it helps students and elderly residents.","zh":"如果新圖書館幫助學生和長者，報章文章可能讚揚它。"},{"en":"Praise in the media can make the public see a product or idea more favourably.","zh":"媒體中的讚揚可以令公眾更正面看待產品或想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when texts express approval.","zh":"當文本表達認可時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"potential billion-dollar crop","meaning":"潛在十億美元農作物","examples":[{"en":"Hemp was praised as a potential billion-dollar crop.","zh":"工業大麻被讚揚為潛在十億美元農作物。"},{"en":"A potential billion-dollar crop is a crop that may create enormous economic value in the future.","zh":"potential billion-dollar crop 指未來可能創造巨大經濟價值的作物。"},{"en":"A new drought-resistant grain may be called a potential billion-dollar crop if many countries want it.","zh":"如果許多國家想要一種新耐旱穀物，它可能被稱為潛在十億美元農作物。"},{"en":"Potential value attracts farmers, investors, and industries before full success is proven.","zh":"潛在價值會在完全成功被證明前吸引農民、投資者和產業。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a crop’s future market looks very large.","zh":"當作物未來市場看似很大時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"link hemp to violent crime","meaning":"將工業大麻與暴力罪行聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"Newspaper articles linked hemp to violent crime.","zh":"報章文章將工業大麻與暴力罪行聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Link hemp to violent crime means connect hemp in public opinion with serious physical crime.","zh":"link hemp to violent crime 指在公眾意見中把工業大麻與嚴重身體罪行連接。"},{"en":"A misleading report can link a harmless product to danger without enough evidence.","zh":"誤導性報道可以在證據不足下，把無害產品與危險聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Linking a crop to crime can create fear and support for strict laws.","zh":"把作物與罪行聯繫起來，可以製造恐懼並支持嚴厲法律。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when media creates a negative association.","zh":"當媒體創造負面聯想時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"development of stripping machines","meaning":"剝皮機器的發展","examples":[{"en":"The development of stripping machines changed the hemp industry.","zh":"剝皮機器的發展改變了工業大麻產業。"},{"en":"The development of stripping machines means the creation and improvement of machines that remove fibres from plant stems.","zh":"development of stripping machines 指創造和改良從植物莖上移除纖維的機器。"},{"en":"The development of washing machines changed household work by saving time.","zh":"洗衣機的發展透過節省時間改變了家務。"},{"en":"New machines can make a slow manual process faster and cheaper.","zh":"新機器可以令緩慢人手過程變得更快和更便宜。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when machinery changes an industry.","zh":"當機器改變一個產業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the following","meaning":"完成以下內容","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the following using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的詞語完成以下內容。"},{"en":"Complete the following means fill in the unfinished sentences, notes, table, or diagram below.","zh":"complete the following 指填寫下方未完成的句子、筆記、表格或圖表。"},{"en":"In a reading exercise, students complete the following by copying the correct words from the text.","zh":"在閱讀練習中，學生透過從文本抄出正確詞語來完成以下內容。"},{"en":"This task checks both understanding and careful word choice.","zh":"這個任務同時檢查理解和仔細選詞。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個字","examples":[{"en":"Students should use no more than three words from the passage.","zh":"學生應使用文章中不多於三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案必須包含三個字或更少。"},{"en":"If the answer is “high-cellulose pulp,” it follows the rule because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “high-cellulose pulp”，它符合規則，因為它有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing four words can lose marks even when the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫四個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reading questions have strict word limits.","zh":"當閱讀題有嚴格字數限制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"strong and durable","meaning":"堅韌耐用","examples":[{"en":"Hemp fibre is strong and durable.","zh":"工業大麻纖維堅韌耐用。"},{"en":"Strong and durable means able to resist force and last for a long time.","zh":"strong and durable 指能抵抗力量並長時間使用。"},{"en":"A strong and durable school bag can carry heavy books for several years.","zh":"堅韌耐用的書包可以承載重書多年。"},{"en":"Durable materials reduce waste because they do not need to be replaced often.","zh":"耐用材料可以減少浪費，因為它們不需要經常更換。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing material quality.","zh":"描述材料質素時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"classify the following as","meaning":"將以下項目分類為……","examples":[{"en":"Students classify the following items as characteristics of different materials.","zh":"學生將以下項目分類為不同材料的特徵。"},{"en":"Classify the following as means sort the given items into the correct categories.","zh":"classify the following as 指把所給項目歸入正確類別。"},{"en":"In science class, students may classify the following objects as solids, liquids, or gases.","zh":"在科學課中，學生可能將以下物件分類為固體、液體或氣體。"},{"en":"Classification helps learners organise details instead of memorising them separately.","zh":"分類幫助學習者整理細節，而不是分開死記。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in table-completion and matching tasks.","zh":"這個短語適用於表格填空和配對任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"characteristic of","meaning":"……的特徵","examples":[{"en":"Mildew resistance is a characteristic of hemp.","zh":"防霉是工業大麻的一項特徵。"},{"en":"A characteristic of something is a feature or quality that belongs to it.","zh":"characteristic of something 指屬於某物的特點或品質。"},{"en":"A calm voice may be a characteristic of a good customer-service worker.","zh":"平靜聲線可能是良好客服員的特徵。"},{"en":"Knowing characteristics helps people compare materials, people, or places clearly.","zh":"了解特徵有助人清楚比較材料、人物或地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying features.","zh":"識別特點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"mildew-resistant","meaning":"防霉的","examples":[{"en":"Hemp fibre is mildew-resistant.","zh":"工業大麻纖維是防霉的。"},{"en":"Mildew-resistant means able to resist mould growth in damp conditions.","zh":"mildew-resistant 指能在潮濕環境中抵抗霉菌生長。"},{"en":"A mildew-resistant shower curtain is useful in a humid bathroom.","zh":"防霉浴簾在潮濕浴室中很有用。"},{"en":"Materials that resist mildew stay cleaner and last longer in wet environments.","zh":"抗霉材料在潮濕環境中保持更清潔並更耐用。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing fabric performance.","zh":"討論布料表現時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"by-product of processing","meaning":"加工過程的副產品","examples":[{"en":"Dioxin can be a by-product of paper processing.","zh":"二噁英可以是紙張加工過程的副產品。"},{"en":"A by-product of processing is something produced unintentionally during manufacturing or treatment.","zh":"by-product of processing 指在製造或處理過程中非有意產生的東西。"},{"en":"Sawdust can be a by-product of cutting wood in a furniture factory.","zh":"鋸木屑可以是家具廠切割木材過程的副產品。"},{"en":"Some by-products are useful, but others may be harmful waste.","zh":"有些副產品有用，但其他可能是有害廢物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing what manufacturing creates besides the main product.","zh":"討論製造業除了主要產品外還產生甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"can be harvested more than once a year","meaning":"一年可收割多於一次","examples":[{"en":"Hemp can be harvested more than once a year in warm climates.","zh":"工業大麻在溫暖氣候中一年可收割多於一次。"},{"en":"Can be harvested more than once a year means farmers can collect the crop multiple times annually.","zh":"can be harvested more than once a year 指農民每年可以收取該作物多次。"},{"en":"Some herbs can be harvested more than once a year if they regrow quickly.","zh":"如果香草快速再生，有些香草一年可收割多於一次。"},{"en":"Multiple harvests can increase income from the same piece of land.","zh":"多次收割可以增加同一塊土地的收入。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing crop productivity.","zh":"比較作物生產力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"large amounts of fertiliser","meaning":"大量肥料","examples":[{"en":"Cotton needs large amounts of fertiliser.","zh":"棉花需要大量肥料。"},{"en":"Large amounts of fertiliser means a lot of soil nutrients must be added for the crop to grow well.","zh":"large amounts of fertiliser 指必須加入很多土壤養分，作物才能生長良好。"},{"en":"A flower farm may need large amounts of fertiliser if the soil is poor.","zh":"如果土壤貧瘠，花場可能需要大量肥料。"},{"en":"High fertiliser use can raise farming costs and affect rivers if chemicals wash away.","zh":"高肥料使用量可以提高農業成本，並在化學物被沖走時影響河流。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing input-heavy farming.","zh":"討論投入密集型農業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"fire-retardant properties","meaning":"阻燃特性","examples":[{"en":"Hemp fibreboard has fire-retardant properties.","zh":"工業大麻纖維板具有阻燃特性。"},{"en":"Fire-retardant properties are qualities that slow burning or reduce fire spread.","zh":"fire-retardant properties 指能減慢燃燒或減少火勢蔓延的特質。"},{"en":"Public buildings often need materials with fire-retardant properties for safety.","zh":"公共建築常因安全需要使用具有阻燃特性的材料。"},{"en":"Materials with these properties can reduce danger during an emergency.","zh":"具有這些特性的材料可以在緊急情況中降低危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing safety features of materials.","zh":"討論材料安全特徵時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"requires warm temperatures","meaning":"需要溫暖氣溫","examples":[{"en":"Cotton requires warm temperatures to grow well.","zh":"棉花需要溫暖氣溫才能生長良好。"},{"en":"Requires warm temperatures means needs consistently warm weather in order to grow successfully.","zh":"requires warm temperatures 指需要持續溫暖天氣才能成功生長。"},{"en":"Tomatoes require warm temperatures, so they may fail during frost.","zh":"番茄需要溫暖氣溫，所以在霜凍時可能失敗。"},{"en":"Temperature requirements limit where certain crops can be planted.","zh":"溫度需求限制某些作物可以在哪裏種植。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing climate needs in farming.","zh":"討論農業中的氣候需要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"main purpose of","meaning":"……的主要目的","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the main purpose of the article.","zh":"題目問文章的主要目的。"},{"en":"The main purpose of something is the most important reason it was written, said, or done.","zh":"main purpose of something 指某事被撰寫、說出或完成的最重要原因。"},{"en":"The main purpose of a school notice may be to inform parents about a timetable change.","zh":"學校通告的主要目的可能是通知家長時間表變更。"},{"en":"Identifying the main purpose helps readers understand the writer’s overall direction.","zh":"辨認主要目的有助讀者理解作者整體方向。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading questions about author intention.","zh":"這個短語適用於關於作者意圖的閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"criticise government policy","meaning":"批評政府政策","examples":[{"en":"One option says the article criticises government policy on hemp.","zh":"一個選項說文章批評政府對工業大麻的政策。"},{"en":"Criticise government policy means point out problems in official rules, decisions, or laws.","zh":"criticise government policy 指指出官方規則、決定或法律中的問題。"},{"en":"Citizens may criticise government policy if public transport becomes too expensive.","zh":"如果公共交通變得太昂貴，市民可能批評政府政策。"},{"en":"Criticism can pressure officials to explain, change, or defend a policy.","zh":"批評可以迫使官員解釋、改變或捍衛政策。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing disagreement with official action.","zh":"討論對官方行動的不滿時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"economic benefits","meaning":"經濟效益","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the economic benefits of hemp.","zh":"文章討論工業大麻的經濟效益。"},{"en":"Economic benefits are advantages related to money, jobs, production, trade, or business growth.","zh":"economic benefits 指與金錢、工作、生產、貿易或商業增長有關的好處。"},{"en":"A new railway may bring economic benefits by helping workers and customers reach shops more easily.","zh":"新鐵路可以透過幫助工人和顧客更容易到達商店而帶來經濟效益。"},{"en":"If a crop creates jobs and profit, it has economic benefits for a community.","zh":"如果一種作物創造工作和利潤，它對社區有經濟效益。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing financial and business advantages.","zh":"討論財務和商業好處時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"compare hemp and marijuana","meaning":"比較工業大麻和大麻","examples":[{"en":"The passage compares hemp and marijuana in one section.","zh":"文章在其中一部分比較工業大麻和 marijuana。"},{"en":"Compare hemp and marijuana means explain similarities and differences between the two cannabis-related plants or plant types.","zh":"compare hemp and marijuana 指解釋這兩種與大麻相關植物或植物類型的相似和差異。"},{"en":"A science teacher may compare two plants to show why similar appearance does not mean identical use.","zh":"科學老師可能比較兩種植物，以顯示外表相似不代表用途相同。"},{"en":"Comparison helps reduce confusion when two terms are often mixed together.","zh":"當兩個術語常被混淆，比較有助減少混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a text separates industrial hemp from drug cannabis.","zh":"當文本區分工業大麻和毒品大麻時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"promote research into","meaning":"推廣對……的研究","examples":[{"en":"One option says the article promotes research into new uses of hemp.","zh":"一個選項說文章推廣對工業大麻新用途的研究。"},{"en":"Promote research into something means encourage study or investigation of that topic.","zh":"promote research into something 指鼓勵對某主題進行研究或調查。"},{"en":"A hospital may promote research into better treatment for childhood asthma.","zh":"醫院可能推廣對兒童哮喘更好治療方法的研究。"},{"en":"Research is promoted when people believe a topic has practical value or unanswered questions.","zh":"當人們相信某主題有實際價值或未解問題，研究就會被推廣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when encouraging further study.","zh":"鼓勵進一步研究時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"new uses of hemp","meaning":"工業大麻的新用途","examples":[{"en":"The article discusses new and renewed uses of hemp.","zh":"文章討論工業大麻新的和重新出現的用途。"},{"en":"New uses of hemp are fresh ways of using hemp in products, industries, or daily life.","zh":"new uses of hemp 指在產品、產業或日常生活中使用工業大麻的新方式。"},{"en":"New uses of hemp may include eco-friendly packaging, building panels, or personal care products.","zh":"工業大麻的新用途可能包括環保包裝、建築板材或個人護理產品。"},{"en":"Discovering new uses can turn an old crop into a modern industrial resource.","zh":"發現新用途可以把古老作物變成現代工業資源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when hemp is applied in updated ways.","zh":"當工業大麻以更新方式被應用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 76 - The hemp revival.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 77":[{"front":"kids and sport","meaning":"兒童與運動","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the relationship between kids and sport.","zh":"文章討論兒童與運動之間的關係。"},{"en":"Kids and sport refers to how children play, train, compete, and develop through physical activity.","zh":"「kids and sport」指兒童如何透過體能活動遊玩、訓練、比賽和發展。"},{"en":"In many families, kids and sport becomes a weekly topic because parents must arrange lessons and transport.","zh":"在許多家庭中，兒童與運動成為每星期的話題，因為父母要安排課堂和接送。"},{"en":"If sport becomes too controlled by adults, children may lose some joy and freedom.","zh":"如果運動變得太受成人控制，兒童可能失去部分樂趣和自由。"},{"en":"The phrase is about children’s experience of sport, not only professional training.","zh":"這個短語關乎兒童的運動經驗，而不只是專業訓練。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Italian psychologists","meaning":"意大利心理學家","examples":[{"en":"Two Italian psychologists describe children’s traditional sporting activities.","zh":"兩位意大利心理學家描述兒童的傳統運動活動。"},{"en":"Italian psychologists are psychologists from Italy who study behaviour, emotions, and development.","zh":"「Italian psychologists」是來自意大利、研究行為、情緒和發展的心理學家。"},{"en":"Italian psychologists might observe how children behave during play in schools or parks.","zh":"意大利心理學家可能觀察兒童在學校或公園玩耍時的行為。"},{"en":"If psychologists study children’s sport, they may focus on confidence, motivation, and social development.","zh":"如果心理學家研究兒童運動，他們可能集中於信心、動機和社交發展。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the experts and their national background.","zh":"這個短語指出專家的身份和國籍背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"traditional spontaneous practice of sport","meaning":"傳統自發性的運動方式","examples":[{"en":"Marte and Notarnicola describe the traditional spontaneous practice of sport by children.","zh":"Marte 和 Notarnicola 描述兒童傳統自發性的運動方式。"},{"en":"Traditional spontaneous practice of sport means children naturally playing physical games without strict adult organisation.","zh":"「traditional spontaneous practice of sport」指兒童在沒有嚴格成人安排下，自然地玩體能遊戲。"},{"en":"Children running, climbing, and inventing games in a park are showing spontaneous sport.","zh":"兒童在公園跑步、爬高和自創遊戲，就是展現自發性運動。"},{"en":"When children choose the rules themselves, they learn freedom and responsibility.","zh":"當兒童自己選擇規則，他們會學習自由和責任。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts free play with adult-led sports lessons.","zh":"這個短語把自由玩耍與成人主導的運動課作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"spontaneous practice","meaning":"自發性的活動方式","examples":[{"en":"Children once enjoyed the spontaneous practice of sport outdoors.","zh":"兒童昔日享受在戶外進行自發性的運動方式。"},{"en":"Spontaneous practice means doing an activity naturally and freely, without much planning.","zh":"「spontaneous practice」意思是自然、自由地進行活動，而沒有太多安排。"},{"en":"Children may start a football game spontaneously when they find an empty playground.","zh":"兒童看到空操場時，可能自發地開始一場足球遊戲。"},{"en":"If play is spontaneous, children decide when to start, stop, and change the rules.","zh":"如果遊戲是自發的，兒童會決定何時開始、停止和改變規則。"},{"en":"The phrase shows freedom rather than formal instruction.","zh":"這個短語顯示自由，而不是正式教學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"climbing trees","meaning":"爬樹","examples":[{"en":"Climbing trees was part of children’s spontaneous sporting activity.","zh":"爬樹是兒童自發性運動活動的一部分。"},{"en":"Climbing trees means using hands and feet to move up branches or trunks.","zh":"「climbing trees」意思是用手腳沿着樹枝或樹幹向上移動。"},{"en":"In a village, children may climb trees for fun, challenge, and adventure.","zh":"在村莊中，兒童可能為了樂趣、挑戰和冒險而爬樹。"},{"en":"Climbing trees can build balance and courage, but it can also involve risk.","zh":"爬樹可以建立平衡感和勇氣，但也可能有風險。"},{"en":"The phrase represents natural outdoor play rather than organised sport.","zh":"這個短語代表自然戶外玩耍，而不是有組織運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"riding a bicycle along quiet roads","meaning":"沿着寧靜道路踏單車","examples":[{"en":"Riding a bicycle along quiet roads was a form of free sporting activity.","zh":"沿着寧靜道路踏單車是一種自由運動活動。"},{"en":"Riding a bicycle along quiet roads means cycling in calm places with little traffic.","zh":"「riding a bicycle along quiet roads」意思是在交通較少的平靜地方踏單車。"},{"en":"Children may enjoy riding a bicycle along quiet roads near their village after school.","zh":"放學後，兒童可能喜歡在村莊附近沿着寧靜道路踏單車。"},{"en":"If roads are quiet, children can explore safely and feel independent.","zh":"如果道路寧靜，兒童可以安全探索並感到獨立。"},{"en":"The phrase describes free movement, outdoor play, and personal discovery.","zh":"這個短語描述自由移動、戶外玩耍和個人探索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"racing their friends across the fields","meaning":"與朋友在田野上賽跑","examples":[{"en":"Children enjoyed racing their friends across the fields.","zh":"兒童喜歡與朋友在田野上賽跑。"},{"en":"Racing their friends across the fields means running quickly against friends over open land.","zh":"「racing their friends across the fields」意思是在開闊土地上與朋友快速奔跑比賽。"},{"en":"At a picnic, children may race their friends across a grassy field for fun.","zh":"野餐時，兒童可能為了好玩而與朋友在草地上賽跑。"},{"en":"Such races help children test speed, effort, and friendship without formal competition.","zh":"這類賽跑幫助兒童在沒有正式比賽下測試速度、努力和友誼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes energetic, informal outdoor play.","zh":"這個短語描述充滿活力的非正式戶外玩耍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an activity of freedom","meaning":"一種自由活動","examples":[{"en":"The psychologists describe children’s sport as an activity of freedom.","zh":"心理學家把兒童運動描述為一種自由活動。"},{"en":"An activity of freedom is an activity where children choose, explore, and act independently.","zh":"「an activity of freedom」是讓兒童選擇、探索和獨立行動的活動。"},{"en":"Building a game with no teacher instructions can be an activity of freedom for children.","zh":"沒有老師指示下自創遊戲，可以是兒童的一種自由活動。"},{"en":"If children control the activity, they learn decision-making as well as movement.","zh":"如果兒童掌控活動，他們除了學會活動身體，也學會作決定。"},{"en":"The phrase shows sport as self-directed play, not adult control.","zh":"這個短語把運動呈現為自主玩耍，而不是成人控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"discovery and learning","meaning":"探索與學習","examples":[{"en":"Free sport is a special activity of discovery and learning.","zh":"自由運動是一種特別的探索與學習活動。"},{"en":"Discovery and learning means finding out new things and gaining skills or understanding.","zh":"「discovery and learning」意思是發現新事物並獲得技能或理解。"},{"en":"A child discovers balance and learns courage while trying to ride a bicycle.","zh":"兒童嘗試踏單車時，會探索平衡並學習勇氣。"},{"en":"If children explore games freely, they learn rules, limits, and teamwork naturally.","zh":"如果兒童自由探索遊戲，他們會自然學到規則、界限和團隊合作。"},{"en":"The phrase connects sport with personal growth.","zh":"這個短語把運動與個人成長連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the case of","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"In the case of free sporting activity, the child’s time belongs to the activity.","zh":"就自由運動活動而言，兒童的時間屬於該活動本身。"},{"en":"In the case of means when we are talking about a particular example or situation.","zh":"「in the case of」意思是當我們談及某個特定例子或情況時。"},{"en":"In the case of young children, short breaks may help them concentrate better.","zh":"就年幼兒童而言，短暫小休可能幫助他們更好集中。"},{"en":"If the situation changes, the explanation may also change.","zh":"如果情況改變，解釋也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase helps focus on one specific case.","zh":"這個短語幫助集中於一個特定個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"free sporting activity","meaning":"自由運動活動","examples":[{"en":"Free sporting activity gives children space to discover sport for themselves.","zh":"自由運動活動給兒童空間自行探索運動。"},{"en":"Free sporting activity is physical play chosen and organised mainly by children themselves.","zh":"「free sporting activity」是主要由兒童自己選擇和組織的體能玩耍。"},{"en":"Children playing basketball in a park without a coach are enjoying free sporting activity.","zh":"兒童在公園沒有教練下打籃球，就是享受自由運動活動。"},{"en":"If free sport disappears, children may depend too much on adult direction.","zh":"如果自由運動消失，兒童可能過度依賴成人指示。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses choice, movement, and self-discovery.","zh":"這個短語強調選擇、活動和自我探索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be given up entirely to","meaning":"完全投入於……","examples":[{"en":"The child’s time is given up entirely to the activity.","zh":"兒童的時間完全投入於該活動。"},{"en":"To be given up entirely to something means to be fully devoted to it.","zh":"「be given up entirely to」某事，意思是完全奉獻或投入於它。"},{"en":"During a music rehearsal, the afternoon may be given up entirely to practice.","zh":"在音樂排練中，整個下午可能完全投入於練習。"},{"en":"If children are fully absorbed in a game, they forget the clock and keep playing.","zh":"如果兒童完全沉浸在遊戲中，他們會忘記時間並繼續玩。"},{"en":"The phrase describes complete involvement.","zh":"這個短語描述完全投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"endless games of football","meaning":"沒完沒了的足球遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Children may spend hours playing endless games of football.","zh":"兒童可能花數小時玩沒完沒了的足球遊戲。"},{"en":"Endless games of football are football games that seem to continue for a very long time.","zh":"「endless games of football」是看似持續很長時間的足球遊戲。"},{"en":"In a housing estate playground, children may play endless games of football after school.","zh":"在屋邨遊樂場，兒童放學後可能玩沒完沒了的足球遊戲。"},{"en":"Long informal games allow children to practise skills without feeling tested.","zh":"長時間非正式遊戲讓兒童練習技巧，而不覺得被測試。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests free, energetic play that children do not want to stop.","zh":"這個短語暗示兒童不想停止的自由而有活力的遊戲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be followed by","meaning":"隨後是……","examples":[{"en":"Games of football may be followed by bicycle races or a swim in the river.","zh":"足球遊戲之後可能隨後是單車賽或在河中游泳。"},{"en":"To be followed by something means to have that thing happen next.","zh":"「be followed by」某事，意思是之後發生該事。"},{"en":"A school assembly may be followed by a short class discussion.","zh":"學校早會之後可能隨後是一段短課堂討論。"},{"en":"If one game is followed by another, children keep exploring different movements.","zh":"如果一個遊戲之後接着另一個遊戲，兒童會繼續探索不同動作。"},{"en":"The phrase shows sequence.","zh":"這個短語顯示先後次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a swim in the river","meaning":"在河中游泳","examples":[{"en":"The children might finish the day with a swim in the river.","zh":"兒童可能以在河中游泳結束一天。"},{"en":"A swim in the river means swimming in a natural river rather than a pool.","zh":"「a swim in the river」意思是在天然河流中游泳，而不是在泳池中。"},{"en":"On a hot day, village children may enjoy a swim in the river after cycling.","zh":"在炎熱日子，村中兒童踏單車後可能享受在河中游泳。"},{"en":"Natural places can make sport feel adventurous, but safety matters.","zh":"天然地方可以令運動感覺有冒險性，但安全很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase represents informal outdoor activity close to nature.","zh":"這個短語代表親近自然的非正式戶外活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"children’s discovery of sport","meaning":"兒童對運動的探索","examples":[{"en":"Children’s discovery of sport has become very different today.","zh":"今天兒童對運動的探索已變得很不同。"},{"en":"Children’s discovery of sport means the way children first explore and understand physical activity.","zh":"「children’s discovery of sport」意思是兒童最初探索和理解體能活動的方式。"},{"en":"A child may discover sport by playing tag with friends before joining any club.","zh":"兒童可能在加入任何球會前，透過與朋友玩捉人遊戲探索運動。"},{"en":"If adults organise every step, children’s discovery becomes less independent.","zh":"如果成人安排每一步，兒童的探索會較不獨立。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how children meet sport for themselves.","zh":"這個短語集中於兒童如何親自接觸運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"become very different","meaning":"變得很不同","examples":[{"en":"Children’s experience of sport has become very different.","zh":"兒童的運動經驗已變得很不同。"},{"en":"To become very different means to change greatly from what it was before.","zh":"「become very different」意思是與以前相比發生很大改變。"},{"en":"Homework has become very different since students started using online platforms.","zh":"自從學生開始使用網上平台，功課已變得很不同。"},{"en":"If cities become crowded, children’s outdoor play may change sharply.","zh":"如果城市變得擠迫，兒童戶外玩耍可能大幅改變。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a major change over time.","zh":"這個短語強調隨時間出現重大變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"take their children to","meaning":"帶子女去……","examples":[{"en":"Parents often take their children to sports grounds or sports halls.","zh":"父母常帶子女去運動場或體育館。"},{"en":"To take their children to a place means to bring or drive them there.","zh":"「take their children to」某地，意思是帶或駕車送子女到該處。"},{"en":"Parents may take their children to music lessons every Saturday morning.","zh":"父母可能每星期六早上帶子女去音樂課。"},{"en":"If children must be taken everywhere, sport becomes dependent on adult schedules.","zh":"如果兒童去任何地方都要被接送，運動就變得依賴成人時間表。"},{"en":"The phrase shows adult involvement in children’s activities.","zh":"這個短語顯示成人參與兒童活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"swimming pool","meaning":"游泳池","examples":[{"en":"Parents may take young children to the swimming pool.","zh":"父母可能帶年幼子女去游泳池。"},{"en":"A swimming pool is a built place filled with water for swimming lessons, exercise, or play.","zh":"「swimming pool」是建造出來、注滿水供游泳課、運動或玩耍的地方。"},{"en":"Children may learn basic water safety at a swimming pool before swimming in the sea.","zh":"兒童在海中游泳前，可能先在游泳池學習基本水上安全。"},{"en":"If sport happens only in formal facilities, children may see it as scheduled training.","zh":"如果運動只在正式設施中發生，兒童可能把它視為排定的訓練。"},{"en":"The phrase names a common organised sports location.","zh":"這個短語指出常見的有組織運動場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sports grounds","meaning":"運動場","examples":[{"en":"Children are often taken to sports grounds by their parents.","zh":"兒童常由父母帶到運動場。"},{"en":"Sports grounds are outdoor places designed for games such as football, athletics, or rugby.","zh":"「sports grounds」是為足球、田徑或欖球等運動而設的戶外場所。"},{"en":"A school sports ground may be used for matches, training, and sports days.","zh":"學校運動場可能用於比賽、訓練和運動會。"},{"en":"If sports grounds are far away, children need adults to bring them there.","zh":"如果運動場很遠，兒童需要成人帶他們去。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to formal outdoor sports spaces.","zh":"這個短語指正式戶外運動空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sports halls","meaning":"體育館","examples":[{"en":"Some children first experience sport in sports halls.","zh":"有些兒童第一次接觸運動是在體育館。"},{"en":"Sports halls are indoor spaces designed for games, training, and physical education.","zh":"「sports halls」是為遊戲、訓練和體育課而設的室內空間。"},{"en":"A school sports hall may be used for badminton, basketball, or indoor fitness.","zh":"學校體育館可能用於羽毛球、籃球或室內健身。"},{"en":"If rain is heavy, children may move their games into a sports hall.","zh":"如果大雨，兒童可能把遊戲移到體育館內。"},{"en":"The phrase names a formal indoor place for sport.","zh":"這個短語指出正式室內運動場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"first experience of sport","meaning":"初次接觸運動的經驗","examples":[{"en":"Children’s first experience of sport often takes place as an organised activity.","zh":"兒童初次接觸運動的經驗常以有組織活動形式發生。"},{"en":"First experience of sport means the first time a child meets or tries physical activity.","zh":"「first experience of sport」意思是兒童第一次接觸或嘗試體能活動。"},{"en":"A child’s first experience of sport may be a swimming lesson arranged by parents.","zh":"兒童初次接觸運動的經驗可能是父母安排的游泳課。"},{"en":"If the first experience feels strict or frightening, the child may not enjoy sport later.","zh":"如果第一次經驗感覺嚴格或可怕，孩子日後可能不享受運動。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how children begin their relationship with sport.","zh":"這個短語集中於兒童如何開始與運動建立關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"take place as","meaning":"以……形式發生","examples":[{"en":"Their first experience of sport takes place as an organised activity.","zh":"他們初次接觸運動的經驗以有組織活動形式發生。"},{"en":"To take place as something means to happen in that form or way.","zh":"「take place as」某事，意思是以該形式或方式發生。"},{"en":"A school meeting may take place as an online video call.","zh":"學校會議可能以網上視像通話形式進行。"},{"en":"If sport takes place as a class, children may follow adult rules from the beginning.","zh":"如果運動以課堂形式發生，兒童一開始就可能遵從成人規則。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the form in which an event happens.","zh":"這個短語解釋事件發生的形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"organised activity","meaning":"有組織的活動","examples":[{"en":"Children may see sport as an organised activity.","zh":"兒童可能把運動視為有組織的活動。"},{"en":"An organised activity is planned and controlled by adults, teachers, clubs, or institutions.","zh":"「organised activity」是由成人、老師、球會或機構規劃和控制的活動。"},{"en":"A football lesson with a coach and timetable is an organised activity.","zh":"有教練和時間表的足球課就是有組織的活動。"},{"en":"If every game is organised, children may have less chance to invent their own rules.","zh":"如果每個遊戲都有組織，兒童自創規則的機會可能較少。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts planned sport with free play.","zh":"這個短語把計劃好的運動與自由玩耍作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the organisation of their free time","meaning":"對自由時間的安排","examples":[{"en":"Children may see sport as the organisation of their free time.","zh":"兒童可能把運動視為對自由時間的安排。"},{"en":"The organisation of their free time means adults planning how children use their leisure hours.","zh":"「the organisation of their free time」意思是成人規劃兒童如何使用休閒時間。"},{"en":"A child whose evenings are full of lessons has their free time organised by others.","zh":"如果孩子晚上排滿課堂，他的自由時間就是由別人安排。"},{"en":"If free time is over-organised, children may not learn to choose activities themselves.","zh":"如果自由時間被過度安排，兒童可能學不到自己選擇活動。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that leisure can become controlled rather than free.","zh":"這個短語暗示休閒可以變得受控制，而不是自由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"organise sport for children","meaning":"為兒童安排運動","examples":[{"en":"Adults often organise sport for children.","zh":"成人常為兒童安排運動。"},{"en":"To organise sport for children means to plan games, lessons, teams, schedules, and competitions for them.","zh":"「organise sport for children」意思是為兒童規劃遊戲、課堂、隊伍、時間表和比賽。"},{"en":"A community centre may organise sport for children during the summer holiday.","zh":"社區中心可能在暑假為兒童安排運動。"},{"en":"If adults organise everything, children may not practise self-management.","zh":"如果成人安排一切，兒童可能無法練習自我管理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adult planning of children’s physical activity.","zh":"這個短語描述成人規劃兒童體能活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"decide for them","meaning":"替他們作決定","examples":[{"en":"Parents often decide for children instead of letting them choose.","zh":"父母常替兒童作決定，而不是讓他們選擇。"},{"en":"To decide for someone means to make a choice on that person’s behalf.","zh":"「decide for someone」意思是代替某人作選擇。"},{"en":"A parent may decide for a child which after-school class to attend.","zh":"父母可能替孩子決定參加哪個課後班。"},{"en":"If adults always decide for children, children may lose confidence in their own choices.","zh":"如果成人總是替兒童作決定，兒童可能失去對自己選擇的信心。"},{"en":"The phrase shows control replacing autonomy.","zh":"這個短語顯示控制取代自主。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"create an imbalance","meaning":"造成失衡","examples":[{"en":"Organising sport for children can create an imbalance.","zh":"為兒童安排運動可能造成失衡。"},{"en":"To create an imbalance means to make a situation uneven or unfairly weighted in one direction.","zh":"「create an imbalance」意思是令情況變得不平均或過度偏向一方。"},{"en":"Too much homework can create an imbalance between study and rest.","zh":"太多功課可以造成學習與休息之間的失衡。"},{"en":"If adult control becomes too strong, children’s freedom becomes too weak.","zh":"如果成人控制太強，兒童自由就會太弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a loss of healthy balance.","zh":"這個短語描述健康平衡的喪失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prevent someone from managing","meaning":"阻止某人管理","examples":[{"en":"Adult control can prevent children from managing their own play time.","zh":"成人控制可能阻止兒童管理自己的遊戲時間。"},{"en":"To prevent someone from managing something means to stop them from controlling or organising it themselves.","zh":"「prevent someone from managing」某事，意思是阻止某人自己控制或安排它。"},{"en":"If parents plan every hour, they prevent children from managing their own weekend.","zh":"如果父母安排每一小時，他們就是阻止孩子管理自己的週末。"},{"en":"When children cannot manage time, they may depend more on adults.","zh":"當兒童不能管理時間，他們可能更依賴成人。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how control can block independence.","zh":"這個短語顯示控制如何阻礙獨立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"manage their own play time","meaning":"管理自己的遊戲時間","examples":[{"en":"Children should learn to manage their own play time.","zh":"兒童應學習管理自己的遊戲時間。"},{"en":"To manage their own play time means to decide when, how, and with whom they play.","zh":"「manage their own play time」意思是自己決定何時、如何以及與誰玩。"},{"en":"Children manage their own play time when they choose a game and agree rules with friends.","zh":"當兒童自己選擇遊戲並與朋友商定規則，他們就是管理自己的遊戲時間。"},{"en":"If children practise this, they learn responsibility and negotiation.","zh":"如果兒童練習這樣做，他們會學到責任和協商。"},{"en":"The phrase describes independence in leisure.","zh":"這個短語描述休閒中的獨立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"deny someone the opportunity for","meaning":"剝奪某人……的機會","examples":[{"en":"Over-organisation may deny children the opportunity for autonomy.","zh":"過度安排可能剝奪兒童自主的機會。"},{"en":"To deny someone the opportunity for something means to stop them from having that chance.","zh":"「deny someone the opportunity for」某事，意思是阻止某人擁有該機會。"},{"en":"Doing a student’s project for them may deny them the opportunity to learn.","zh":"替學生完成專題可能剝奪他們學習的機會。"},{"en":"If adults control every game, children lose chances to make decisions.","zh":"如果成人控制每個遊戲，兒童會失去作決定的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes taking away a valuable chance.","zh":"這個短語描述拿走有價值機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"autonomy and independence","meaning":"自主與獨立","examples":[{"en":"Children need opportunities for autonomy and independence.","zh":"兒童需要自主與獨立的機會。"},{"en":"Autonomy and independence mean the ability to make choices and act without constant control.","zh":"「autonomy and independence」意思是能夠在沒有持續控制下作選擇和行動。"},{"en":"A teenager gains autonomy when they plan their own study timetable.","zh":"青少年自己規劃溫習時間表時，就獲得自主。"},{"en":"If children practise independence in play, they may handle problems more confidently.","zh":"如果兒童在玩耍中練習獨立，他們可能更有信心處理問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the freedom to manage oneself.","zh":"這個短語描述自我管理的自由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"possible in the past","meaning":"過去可能做到的","examples":[{"en":"Such independence was more possible in the past.","zh":"這種獨立在過去較可能做到。"},{"en":"Possible in the past means something could happen more easily in earlier times.","zh":"「possible in the past」意思是某事在以前較容易發生。"},{"en":"Walking to school alone was more possible in the past in some quiet villages.","zh":"在某些寧靜村莊，獨自步行上學在過去較可能做到。"},{"en":"If cities become busier, freedoms once possible may become harder to provide.","zh":"如果城市變得更繁忙，昔日可能做到的自由可能更難提供。"},{"en":"The phrase compares past conditions with the present.","zh":"這個短語比較過去與現在的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a possible reason for","meaning":"……的一個可能原因","examples":[{"en":"A possible reason for the imbalance is modern urban society.","zh":"這種失衡的一個可能原因是現代城市社會。"},{"en":"A possible reason for something is one explanation that may account for it.","zh":"「a possible reason for」某事，是可能解釋它的一個原因。"},{"en":"A possible reason for tired students is late-night phone use.","zh":"學生疲倦的一個可能原因是深夜使用手機。"},{"en":"If several causes exist, writers may introduce one carefully as a possible reason.","zh":"如果存在幾個原因，作者可能謹慎地引出其中一個可能原因。"},{"en":"The phrase presents an explanation without claiming absolute certainty.","zh":"這個短語提出解釋，但不表示絕對確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the imbalance in","meaning":"……方面的失衡","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the imbalance in children’s practice of sport.","zh":"文章討論兒童運動方式方面的失衡。"},{"en":"The imbalance in something means the uneven or unhealthy distribution within it.","zh":"「the imbalance in」某事，意思是其中不平均或不健康的分配。"},{"en":"An imbalance in study and sleep can make students exhausted.","zh":"學習和睡眠方面的失衡可以令學生筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"If children get too much training and too little free play, an imbalance appears.","zh":"如果兒童有太多訓練而太少自由玩耍，失衡就會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a problem of proportion.","zh":"這個短語指出比例上的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the practice of sport","meaning":"參與運動；運動方式","examples":[{"en":"The practice of sport by children has changed.","zh":"兒童參與運動的方式已經改變。"},{"en":"The practice of sport means the way people take part in sport or physical activity.","zh":"「the practice of sport」意思是人們參與運動或體能活動的方式。"},{"en":"In some schools, the practice of sport includes lessons, clubs, and informal games.","zh":"在一些學校中，運動方式包括課堂、學會和非正式遊戲。"},{"en":"If sport becomes too formal, children’s practice of sport may feel less free.","zh":"如果運動變得太正式，兒童參與運動可能感覺較不自由。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to participation and habits, not only training drills.","zh":"這個短語指參與和習慣，而不只是訓練動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be linked to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The first imbalance is linked to urban society.","zh":"第一種失衡與城市社會有關。"},{"en":"To be linked to something means to be connected with it.","zh":"「be linked to」某事，意思是與它有連繫。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is often linked to too much screen time at night.","zh":"睡眠差常與晚上過度使用屏幕有關。"},{"en":"If children lack open spaces, the problem may be linked to city design.","zh":"如果兒童缺乏開放空間，問題可能與城市設計有關。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a relationship between two things.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩件事之間的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"urban society","meaning":"城市社會","examples":[{"en":"Urban society has changed children’s relationship with sport.","zh":"城市社會改變了兒童與運動的關係。"},{"en":"Urban society means life in towns and cities, with dense buildings, roads, and organised services.","zh":"「urban society」意思是城鎮和城市中的生活，包括密集建築、道路和有組織服務。"},{"en":"In urban society, children may have less open space for spontaneous games.","zh":"在城市社會中，兒童可能較少開放空間進行自發遊戲。"},{"en":"If traffic and buildings fill the city, outdoor play becomes harder.","zh":"如果交通和建築填滿城市，戶外玩耍就變得更難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes city-based social life.","zh":"這個短語描述以城市為基礎的社會生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"need not regret the past","meaning":"不必懷念過去","examples":[{"en":"We need not regret the past, but we should recreate children’s freedom.","zh":"我們不必懷念過去，但應重建兒童的自由。"},{"en":"Need not regret the past means we do not have to feel sad that old times are gone.","zh":"「need not regret the past」意思是我們不必因昔日已逝而感到傷感。"},{"en":"A school need not regret old teaching methods if it can preserve their best parts in new ways.","zh":"如果學校能用新方式保留舊教學方法的優點，就不必懷念過去。"},{"en":"If society changes, the aim is not nostalgia but wise reconstruction.","zh":"如果社會改變，目標不是懷舊，而是明智地重建。"},{"en":"The phrase rejects simple longing for the past.","zh":"這個短語拒絕單純懷念過去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a question of knowing how to","meaning":"關鍵在於知道如何……","examples":[{"en":"It is a question of knowing how to recreate this freedom.","zh":"關鍵在於知道如何重建這種自由。"},{"en":"A question of knowing how to do something means the main issue is finding the right method.","zh":"「a question of knowing how to」做某事，意思是主要問題在於找到正確方法。"},{"en":"Helping shy students speak is a question of knowing how to create a safe classroom.","zh":"幫助害羞學生說話，關鍵在於知道如何建立安全課室。"},{"en":"If adults value children’s freedom, they must learn how to provide it safely.","zh":"如果成人重視兒童自由，就必須學會如何安全地提供它。"},{"en":"The phrase shifts attention from whether to do something to how to do it.","zh":"這個短語把焦點由是否做某事轉向如何做。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"recreate this freedom","meaning":"重建這種自由","examples":[{"en":"Adults need to recreate this freedom for children.","zh":"成人需要為兒童重建這種自由。"},{"en":"To recreate this freedom means to bring back similar chances for free choice and independent play.","zh":"「recreate this freedom」意思是重新帶回類似的自由選擇和獨立玩耍機會。"},{"en":"A school may recreate this freedom by leaving part of recess unstructured.","zh":"學校可以透過把部分小息時間保持非正式，重建這種自由。"},{"en":"If parks and safe streets are available, children can choose games more freely.","zh":"如果有公園和安全街道，兒童可以更自由地選擇遊戲。"},{"en":"The phrase means rebuilding freedom in a modern setting.","zh":"這個短語意思是在現代環境中重建自由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in our towns and in the country","meaning":"在城鎮和鄉郊","examples":[{"en":"Freedom should be recreated in our towns and in the country.","zh":"自由應在城鎮和鄉郊被重建。"},{"en":"In our towns and in the country means in both urban and rural places.","zh":"「in our towns and in the country」意思是在城市和鄉郊兩種地方。"},{"en":"Children need safe play spaces in our towns and in the country, not only in wealthy areas.","zh":"兒童在城鎮和鄉郊都需要安全遊戲空間，而不只是富裕地區。"},{"en":"If both city and rural children need freedom, solutions must fit different places.","zh":"如果城市和鄉郊兒童都需要自由，解決方法就必須適合不同地方。"},{"en":"The phrase includes many types of community.","zh":"這個短語包括多種社區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"increasingly based on","meaning":"越來越建基於……","examples":[{"en":"Children’s sport is increasingly based on organised leisure activities.","zh":"兒童運動越來越建基於有組織的康樂活動。"},{"en":"Increasingly based on means relying more and more on something over time.","zh":"「increasingly based on」意思是隨時間越來越依賴某事。"},{"en":"Learning is increasingly based on digital platforms in many schools.","zh":"在許多學校，學習越來越建基於數碼平台。"},{"en":"If children’s sport is based on organised activities, free play may become rarer.","zh":"如果兒童運動建基於有組織活動，自由玩耍可能變得較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a growing dependence.","zh":"這個短語描述不斷增加的依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"organised leisure activities","meaning":"有組織的康樂活動","examples":[{"en":"Sport is increasingly based on organised leisure activities.","zh":"運動越來越建基於有組織的康樂活動。"},{"en":"Organised leisure activities are planned free-time activities run by adults, clubs, or institutions.","zh":"「organised leisure activities」是由成人、球會或機構安排的休閒活動。"},{"en":"Swimming lessons, football clubs, and dance classes are organised leisure activities.","zh":"游泳課、足球會和舞蹈班都是有組織的康樂活動。"},{"en":"If leisure is always organised, children may have less time for spontaneous play.","zh":"如果休閒總是被安排，兒童可能較少時間自發玩耍。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts planned recreation with self-directed free time.","zh":"這個短語把計劃好的康樂與自主自由時間作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"doing one sport","meaning":"只做一項運動","examples":[{"en":"Doing one sport is now the rule in clubs.","zh":"在球會中，只做一項運動現在已成為常規。"},{"en":"Doing one sport means focusing on a single sport instead of trying several.","zh":"「doing one sport」意思是集中於一項運動，而不是嘗試幾項。"},{"en":"A child who only trains in tennis all year is doing one sport.","zh":"一個全年只訓練網球的孩子，就是只做一項運動。"},{"en":"If children specialise too early, they may miss broader movement experiences.","zh":"如果兒童太早專項化，他們可能錯過更廣泛的動作經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests narrow training rather than varied play.","zh":"這個短語暗示狹窄訓練，而不是多元玩耍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be now the rule","meaning":"現在已成為常規","examples":[{"en":"Doing one sport is now the rule in clubs.","zh":"只做一項運動現在已成為球會常規。"},{"en":"To be now the rule means to have become the normal or expected practice today.","zh":"「be now the rule」意思是如今已成為正常或被預期的做法。"},{"en":"Online homework is now the rule in many schools.","zh":"網上功課在許多學校現在已成為常規。"},{"en":"If specialisation is now the rule, children may have fewer chances to try other sports.","zh":"如果專項化現在已成為常規，兒童嘗試其他運動的機會可能較少。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something has become common.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事已變得常見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"on the outskirts of cities","meaning":"在城市邊緣","examples":[{"en":"Sports grounds are often on the outskirts of cities.","zh":"運動場常位於城市邊緣。"},{"en":"On the outskirts of cities means near the outer edge of urban areas.","zh":"「on the outskirts of cities」意思是在城市地區外圍邊緣附近。"},{"en":"Large sports centres may be built on the outskirts of cities because land is cheaper there.","zh":"大型體育中心可能建於城市邊緣，因為那裡土地較便宜。"},{"en":"If facilities are far from homes, children depend on adults for transport.","zh":"如果設施離家很遠，兒童就依賴成人接送。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a location away from the city centre.","zh":"這個短語描述遠離市中心的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"overcrowded","meaning":"過度擠迫","examples":[{"en":"Sports grounds are often overcrowded.","zh":"運動場常過度擠迫。"},{"en":"Overcrowded means containing too many people for the available space.","zh":"「overcrowded」意思是某地方人數太多，超出可用空間。"},{"en":"A classroom becomes overcrowded when too many students are placed in it.","zh":"如果太多學生被安排在同一課室，課室就會過度擠迫。"},{"en":"If a sports ground is overcrowded, children may have little room to play freely.","zh":"如果運動場過度擠迫，兒童可能沒有足夠空間自由玩耍。"},{"en":"The word describes a place that is too full.","zh":"這個詞描述一個太滿的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"invariably enclosed","meaning":"總是被圍封","examples":[{"en":"Sports grounds are overcrowded and invariably enclosed.","zh":"運動場過度擠迫，而且總是被圍封。"},{"en":"Invariably enclosed means almost always surrounded or closed off by fences or walls.","zh":"「invariably enclosed」意思是幾乎總是被圍欄或牆包圍或封閉。"},{"en":"Some private playgrounds are invariably enclosed, so children cannot enter freely.","zh":"有些私人遊樂場總是被圍封，所以兒童不能自由進入。"},{"en":"If sports spaces are enclosed, spontaneous access becomes more difficult.","zh":"如果運動空間被圍封，自發使用就變得更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a lack of open, flexible space.","zh":"這個短語暗示缺乏開放而靈活的空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"recreational areas","meaning":"康樂區；休憩活動區","examples":[{"en":"There are very few recreational areas for spontaneous play.","zh":"可供自發玩耍的康樂區寥寥可數。"},{"en":"Recreational areas are places where people can relax, play, exercise, or spend free time.","zh":"「recreational areas」是人們可以放鬆、玩耍、運動或使用自由時間的地方。"},{"en":"A public park is a recreational area where children can run and invent games.","zh":"公園是兒童可以奔跑和自創遊戲的康樂區。"},{"en":"If recreational areas disappear, children may spend more time indoors.","zh":"如果康樂區消失，兒童可能花更多時間留在室內。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to spaces for leisure, not only formal sport.","zh":"這個短語指休閒空間，而不只是正式運動場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hard-packed surfaces","meaning":"硬實地面","examples":[{"en":"Parks and hard-packed surfaces are very few and far between.","zh":"公園和硬實地面都十分少見。"},{"en":"Hard-packed surfaces are firm, compacted areas of ground suitable for running or games.","zh":"「hard-packed surfaces」是堅實、被壓實並適合跑步或遊戲的地面。"},{"en":"A school playground with hard-packed surfaces can support ball games during recess.","zh":"有硬實地面的學校操場可以支援小息時的球類遊戲。"},{"en":"If there are few such surfaces, children have fewer places for informal sport.","zh":"如果這類地面很少，兒童可進行非正式運動的地方就較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes usable outdoor ground for play.","zh":"這個短語描述可用於玩耍的戶外地面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"very few and far between","meaning":"寥寥可數；十分少見","examples":[{"en":"Open recreational areas are very few and far between.","zh":"開放康樂區寥寥可數。"},{"en":"Very few and far between means rare and not easy to find.","zh":"「very few and far between」意思是很稀少、不容易找到。"},{"en":"Quiet study spaces are very few and far between during exam season.","zh":"考試季期間，安靜自修空間十分少見。"},{"en":"If safe play areas are rare, children’s spontaneous sport becomes harder.","zh":"如果安全遊戲區很稀少，兒童自發運動就更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses scarcity.","zh":"這個短語強調稀缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a varied and spontaneous relationship to sport","meaning":"與運動之間多元而自發的關係","examples":[{"en":"Children need a varied and spontaneous relationship to sport.","zh":"兒童需要與運動之間多元而自發的關係。"},{"en":"A varied and spontaneous relationship to sport means children try different activities freely and naturally.","zh":"「a varied and spontaneous relationship to sport」意思是兒童自由而自然地嘗試不同活動。"},{"en":"A child who runs, swims, cycles, and invents games has a varied sporting life.","zh":"會跑步、游泳、踏單車和自創遊戲的孩子，擁有多元運動生活。"},{"en":"If children experience many sports freely, they may develop broader skills.","zh":"如果兒童自由體驗多種運動，他們可能發展更廣泛技能。"},{"en":"The phrase values diversity and freedom in children’s sport.","zh":"這個短語重視兒童運動中的多樣性和自由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"under such conditions","meaning":"在這種情況下","examples":[{"en":"It is difficult to create sporting freedom under such conditions.","zh":"在這種情況下，要創造運動自由很困難。"},{"en":"Under such conditions means in circumstances like the ones just described.","zh":"「under such conditions」意思是在剛描述的那些情況下。"},{"en":"Under such conditions, a noisy classroom makes concentration difficult.","zh":"在這種情況下，嘈吵課室會令人難以集中。"},{"en":"If spaces are crowded and enclosed, children cannot easily play freely.","zh":"如果空間擠迫又被圍封，兒童就不容易自由玩耍。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a problem with its surrounding situation.","zh":"這個短語把問題與其周圍情況連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"interesting answers have been suggested","meaning":"有人提出了一些有意思的答案","examples":[{"en":"Some interesting answers have been suggested.","zh":"有人提出了一些有意思的答案。"},{"en":"Interesting answers have been suggested means people have proposed useful or thought-provoking solutions.","zh":"「interesting answers have been suggested」意思是人們提出了有用或發人深省的解決方法。"},{"en":"Teachers have suggested interesting answers to the problem of students avoiding reading.","zh":"老師對學生逃避閱讀的問題提出了一些有意思的答案。"},{"en":"If a problem is serious, new answers may involve changes in space, rules, and attitude.","zh":"如果問題嚴重，新答案可能涉及空間、規則和態度的改變。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces possible solutions.","zh":"這個短語引出可能解決方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take into account","meaning":"考慮到","examples":[{"en":"These answers take into account the need to recreate freedom.","zh":"這些答案考慮到重建自由的需要。"},{"en":"To take something into account means to consider it before making a decision.","zh":"「take something into account」意思是在作決定前考慮某因素。"},{"en":"A teacher should take students’ levels into account when designing homework.","zh":"老師設計功課時應考慮到學生程度。"},{"en":"If planners ignore children’s need for freedom, new sports facilities may fail.","zh":"如果規劃者忽視兒童對自由的需要，新運動設施可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase means to include an important factor in thinking.","zh":"這個短語意思是把重要因素納入思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"experience such freedom","meaning":"經歷這種自由","examples":[{"en":"Children who experience such freedom may become more capable later.","zh":"經歷這種自由的兒童日後可能變得能力較強。"},{"en":"To experience such freedom means to personally have the chance to choose and play independently.","zh":"「experience such freedom」意思是親身有機會選擇並獨立玩耍。"},{"en":"Children experience such freedom when they create games without adults giving rules.","zh":"當兒童在沒有成人給規則下自創遊戲，他們就是經歷這種自由。"},{"en":"If children experience freedom early, they may learn creativity and responsibility.","zh":"如果兒童早期經歷自由，他們可能學會創造力和責任。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to living through freedom, not only hearing about it.","zh":"這個短語指親身經歷自由，而不只是聽說它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be considered by someone to be","meaning":"被某人認為是……","examples":[{"en":"These children were considered by trainers to be more capable.","zh":"這些兒童被教練認為能力較強。"},{"en":"To be considered by someone to be something means that person judges or regards them in that way.","zh":"「be considered by someone to be」某物，意思是某人如此判斷或看待他們。"},{"en":"A student may be considered by teachers to be ready for a harder class.","zh":"學生可能被老師認為已準備好上較難課程。"},{"en":"If trainers see children solving problems in play, they may judge them as more capable.","zh":"如果教練看見兒童在遊戲中解決問題，可能判斷他們能力較強。"},{"en":"The phrase reports someone’s opinion or assessment.","zh":"這個短語報告某人的意見或評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sports trainers","meaning":"運動教練","examples":[{"en":"Sports trainers considered these children more capable.","zh":"運動教練認為這些兒童能力較強。"},{"en":"Sports trainers are people who coach athletes and help them develop skills and fitness.","zh":"「sports trainers」是教導運動員並幫助他們發展技巧和體能的人。"},{"en":"Sports trainers may teach warm-ups, techniques, teamwork, and safe practice.","zh":"運動教練可能教授熱身、技巧、團隊合作和安全練習。"},{"en":"If trainers understand child development, they can avoid pushing children too hard.","zh":"如果教練理解兒童發展，就能避免過度催谷兒童。"},{"en":"The phrase names adults who guide sporting performance.","zh":"這個短語指出指導運動表現的成人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"more capable","meaning":"能力較強","examples":[{"en":"Children with early sporting freedom were considered more capable.","zh":"早期有運動自由的兒童被認為能力較強。"},{"en":"More capable means better able to do something successfully or independently.","zh":"「more capable」意思是更能成功或獨立地做某事。"},{"en":"A student becomes more capable when they learn to plan homework without reminders.","zh":"當學生學會不用提醒也能規劃功課，他就變得能力較強。"},{"en":"If children solve problems during free play, they may become more capable in organised sport.","zh":"如果兒童在自由玩耍中解決問題，他們在有組織運動中可能能力較強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stronger ability or readiness.","zh":"這個短語描述更強能力或準備程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"join organised sport","meaning":"參加有組織的運動","examples":[{"en":"Some children join organised sport at ages 12 to 13.","zh":"有些兒童在十二至十三歲時參加有組織的運動。"},{"en":"To join organised sport means to enter a structured team, club, class, or competition.","zh":"「join organised sport」意思是加入有結構的隊伍、球會、課程或比賽。"},{"en":"A child may join organised sport after years of playing casually with friends.","zh":"兒童可能在多年與朋友隨意玩耍後參加有組織的運動。"},{"en":"If children join too early, they may feel pressure before they are ready.","zh":"如果兒童太早加入，可能在準備好之前已感到壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase marks movement from free play into formal sport.","zh":"這個短語標示由自由玩耍轉入正式運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at ages 12 to 13","meaning":"在十二至十三歲時","examples":[{"en":"They joined organised sport at ages 12 to 13.","zh":"他們在十二至十三歲時參加有組織的運動。"},{"en":"At ages 12 to 13 means when children are twelve or thirteen years old.","zh":"「at ages 12 to 13」意思是在兒童十二或十三歲時。"},{"en":"Some students become more ready for formal competition at ages 12 to 13.","zh":"有些學生在十二至十三歲時更準備好參加正式比賽。"},{"en":"If children have played freely before this age, they may enter clubs with confidence.","zh":"如果兒童在這年齡前曾自由玩耍，他們可能更有信心加入球會。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a specific age range.","zh":"這個短語提供特定年齡範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"formal training","meaning":"正式訓練","examples":[{"en":"No formal training can replace children’s first free experiences.","zh":"沒有正式訓練能取代兒童最初的自由經驗。"},{"en":"Formal training is structured instruction led by coaches, teachers, or organisations.","zh":"「formal training」是由教練、老師或機構帶領的有結構指導。"},{"en":"A tennis lesson with drills and correction is formal training.","zh":"有練習動作和糾正的網球課就是正式訓練。"},{"en":"If formal training begins too early, children may miss natural play and exploration.","zh":"如果正式訓練太早開始，兒童可能錯過自然玩耍和探索。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts organised instruction with free experience.","zh":"這個短語把有組織指導與自由經驗作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"no matter how early","meaning":"無論多早","examples":[{"en":"No formal training, no matter how early it begins, can replace free play.","zh":"沒有正式訓練，無論多早開始，都不能取代自由玩耍。"},{"en":"No matter how early means even if something starts very early.","zh":"「no matter how early」意思是即使某事很早開始。"},{"en":"No matter how early a child learns grammar, they still need practice using it.","zh":"無論孩子多早學文法，他們仍需要練習使用它。"},{"en":"If training starts before children are ready, early timing alone will not guarantee success.","zh":"如果訓練在兒童準備好之前開始，單靠早開始也不能保證成功。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that timing does not change the main point.","zh":"這個短語顯示時間早晚不改變主要觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take place","meaning":"發生；進行","examples":[{"en":"The training took place early in life.","zh":"訓練在人生早期進行。"},{"en":"To take place means to happen or occur.","zh":"「take place」意思是發生或進行。"},{"en":"The school sports day usually takes place in March.","zh":"學校運動會通常在三月舉行。"},{"en":"If training takes place too early, children may feel pressured before they are mature.","zh":"如果訓練太早進行，兒童可能在成熟前感到壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase simply states when or where something happens.","zh":"這個短語簡單說明某事何時或何地發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"replace these first experiences","meaning":"取代這些初期經驗","examples":[{"en":"Formal training cannot replace these first experiences.","zh":"正式訓練不能取代這些初期經驗。"},{"en":"To replace these first experiences means to take the place of children’s early free sporting memories.","zh":"「replace these first experiences」意思是代替兒童早期自由運動記憶的位置。"},{"en":"A worksheet cannot replace a child’s first experience of planting seeds in real soil.","zh":"工作紙不能取代孩子首次在真泥土中種種子的經驗。"},{"en":"If early play teaches discovery, formal drills cannot fully provide the same learning.","zh":"如果早期玩耍教會探索，正式操練不能完全提供同樣學習。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that some early experiences are unique.","zh":"這個短語強調某些早期經驗是獨特的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"measures that could reverse","meaning":"可扭轉……的措施","examples":[{"en":"The passage suggests measures that could reverse this imbalance.","zh":"文章提出可扭轉這種失衡的措施。"},{"en":"Measures that could reverse something are actions that may reduce or undo a problem.","zh":"「measures that could reverse」某事，是可能減少或消除問題的行動。"},{"en":"Extra reading time could reverse a decline in students’ vocabulary.","zh":"額外閱讀時間可以扭轉學生詞彙量下降。"},{"en":"If children lack free play, new play spaces may reverse part of the imbalance.","zh":"如果兒童缺乏自由玩耍，新遊戲空間可能扭轉部分失衡。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces practical solutions.","zh":"這個短語引入實際解決方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reverse this imbalance","meaning":"扭轉這種失衡","examples":[{"en":"More open facilities could help reverse this imbalance.","zh":"更多開放設施可以幫助扭轉這種失衡。"},{"en":"To reverse this imbalance means to restore a healthier balance between opposing factors.","zh":"「reverse this imbalance」意思是恢復相反因素之間較健康的平衡。"},{"en":"A school may reverse an imbalance between study and rest by reducing unnecessary homework.","zh":"學校可以透過減少不必要功課，扭轉學習與休息的失衡。"},{"en":"If children regain free play, adult organisation becomes less dominant.","zh":"如果兒童重新獲得自由玩耍，成人安排就不再那麼主導。"},{"en":"The phrase describes correcting an unhealthy situation.","zh":"這個短語描述糾正不健康情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"increase the number of","meaning":"增加……的數量","examples":[{"en":"One measure is to increase the number of suitable sports facilities.","zh":"其中一項措施是增加合適運動設施的數量。"},{"en":"To increase the number of something means to make more of it available.","zh":"「increase the number of」某物，意思是令更多該物可供使用。"},{"en":"A school may increase the number of reading corners to encourage quiet study.","zh":"學校可能增加閱讀角數量，以鼓勵安靜閱讀。"},{"en":"If communities increase play spaces, more children can take part freely.","zh":"如果社區增加遊戲空間，更多兒童可以自由參與。"},{"en":"The phrase describes raising quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述提高數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sports facilities","meaning":"運動設施","examples":[{"en":"Children need sports facilities that encourage self-organisation.","zh":"兒童需要鼓勵自行組織的運動設施。"},{"en":"Sports facilities are places and equipment used for playing or training in sport.","zh":"「sports facilities」是用來進行或訓練運動的地方和設備。"},{"en":"A school’s sports facilities may include a gym, playground, running track, and courts.","zh":"學校的運動設施可能包括健身室、操場、跑道和球場。"},{"en":"If facilities are open and flexible, children can use them more independently.","zh":"如果設施開放而靈活，兒童就能更獨立地使用它們。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the physical support needed for sport.","zh":"這個短語指運動所需的實體支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"encourage self-organisation","meaning":"鼓勵自行組織","examples":[{"en":"Some facilities encourage self-organisation by children.","zh":"有些設施鼓勵兒童自行組織。"},{"en":"To encourage self-organisation means to help people plan and manage activities by themselves.","zh":"「encourage self-organisation」意思是幫助人們自己規劃和管理活動。"},{"en":"A playground with open space can encourage children to organise their own games.","zh":"有開放空間的遊樂場可以鼓勵兒童自行組織遊戲。"},{"en":"If children organise play themselves, they practise leadership and cooperation.","zh":"如果兒童自己組織玩耍，他們會練習領導和合作。"},{"en":"The phrase values independence rather than adult direction.","zh":"這個短語重視獨立，而不是成人指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"set up","meaning":"設立","examples":[{"en":"Communities should set up unstructured playing areas.","zh":"社區應設立非正式遊戲場地。"},{"en":"To set up something means to establish, create, or arrange it.","zh":"「set up」某物，意思是建立、創立或安排它。"},{"en":"A school may set up a reading club for students who enjoy novels.","zh":"學校可能為喜歡小說的學生設立閱讀會。"},{"en":"If a community sets up open play areas, children get more chances to play freely.","zh":"如果社區設立開放遊戲區，兒童就有更多機會自由玩耍。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating something for use.","zh":"這個短語描述創造可使用的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"unstructured playing areas","meaning":"非正式遊戲場地","examples":[{"en":"Children need unstructured playing areas with little equipment.","zh":"兒童需要幾乎沒有設備的非正式遊戲場地。"},{"en":"Unstructured playing areas are open spaces without strict rules, schedules, or fixed activities.","zh":"「unstructured playing areas」是沒有嚴格規則、時間表或固定活動的開放空間。"},{"en":"An empty playground after school can become an unstructured playing area.","zh":"放學後的空操場可以成為非正式遊戲場地。"},{"en":"If children use such spaces, they can invent games and manage rules themselves.","zh":"如果兒童使用這類空間，他們可以自創遊戲並自行管理規則。"},{"en":"The phrase describes flexible spaces for free play.","zh":"這個短語描述供自由玩耍的靈活空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"with little in the way of equipment","meaning":"幾乎沒有甚麼設備","examples":[{"en":"The areas should have little in the way of equipment.","zh":"這些場地應幾乎沒有甚麼設備。"},{"en":"With little in the way of equipment means with very few tools, machines, or fixed structures.","zh":"「with little in the way of equipment」意思是幾乎沒有工具、機器或固定結構。"},{"en":"Children can play tag in a field with little in the way of equipment.","zh":"兒童可以在幾乎沒有設備的田地玩捉人遊戲。"},{"en":"If play needs little equipment, it becomes cheaper and easier to organise.","zh":"如果遊戲需要很少設備，它就更便宜、更容易安排。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses simplicity.","zh":"這個短語強調簡單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"street sport","meaning":"街頭運動","examples":[{"en":"Areas where street sport can be practised need to be established.","zh":"需要設立可進行街頭運動的地方。"},{"en":"Street sport is informal sport played in public spaces such as streets, courts, or open areas.","zh":"「street sport」是在街道、球場或開放地方進行的非正式運動。"},{"en":"Children playing basketball beside a housing estate are taking part in street sport.","zh":"兒童在屋邨旁打籃球，就是參與街頭運動。"},{"en":"If street sport is supported, children without club membership can still play.","zh":"如果街頭運動得到支持，沒有球會會籍的兒童仍可玩運動。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests accessible, everyday sport outside formal clubs.","zh":"這個短語暗示正式球會以外、容易接觸的日常運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be practised","meaning":"被進行；被練習","examples":[{"en":"Street sport can be practised in open areas.","zh":"街頭運動可以在開放地方進行。"},{"en":"To be practised means to be done repeatedly or regularly as an activity.","zh":"「be practised」意思是某活動被反覆或定期進行。"},{"en":"Speaking skills can be practised with classmates before an oral exam.","zh":"口語技巧可以在口試前與同學練習。"},{"en":"If sport can be practised near home, children may play more often.","zh":"如果運動可以在家附近進行，兒童可能更常玩。"},{"en":"The phrase describes doing an activity, not only learning theory.","zh":"這個短語描述進行活動，而不只是學習理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"need to be established","meaning":"需要被設立","examples":[{"en":"Areas for street sport need to be established.","zh":"街頭運動場地需要被設立。"},{"en":"Need to be established means should be created, built, or officially provided.","zh":"「need to be established」意思是應該被創造、興建或正式提供。"},{"en":"Clear school rules need to be established before a new club begins.","zh":"新學會開始前，需要設立清楚校規。"},{"en":"If play spaces are not established, children may have nowhere safe to gather.","zh":"如果遊戲空間沒有被設立，兒童可能沒有安全地方聚集。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses a need for creation or formal provision.","zh":"這個短語表達創建或正式提供的需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"offer multidisciplinary sports training","meaning":"提供多項運動訓練","examples":[{"en":"Some sports clubs offer multidisciplinary sports training.","zh":"有些體育會提供多項運動訓練。"},{"en":"To offer multidisciplinary sports training means to provide training in several different sports or movement skills.","zh":"「offer multidisciplinary sports training」意思是提供幾種不同運動或動作技能的訓練。"},{"en":"A children’s club may offer running, swimming, ball games, and gymnastics in one programme.","zh":"兒童球會可能在一個課程中提供跑步、游泳、球類和體操。"},{"en":"If training is multidisciplinary, children develop broader skills and avoid early narrow specialisation.","zh":"如果訓練是多項運動式，兒童會發展更廣泛技能，並避免過早狹窄專項化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes varied training across more than one sport.","zh":"這個短語描述跨越多於一項運動的多元訓練。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be supported","meaning":"應得到支持","examples":[{"en":"Sports clubs offering varied training should be supported.","zh":"提供多元訓練的體育會應得到支持。"},{"en":"To be supported means to receive help, resources, approval, or encouragement.","zh":"「be supported」意思是得到幫助、資源、認可或鼓勵。"},{"en":"A school reading programme should be supported by teachers, parents, and the library.","zh":"學校閱讀計劃應得到老師、家長和圖書館支持。"},{"en":"If varied sports clubs are supported, more children can try different activities.","zh":"如果多元體育會得到支持，更多兒童可以嘗試不同活動。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that help is needed for something valuable to continue.","zh":"這個短語顯示有價值的事物需要幫助才能延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pre-school activities","meaning":"學前活動","examples":[{"en":"Children should be offered pre-school activities involving different sports.","zh":"兒童應獲提供涉及不同運動的學前活動。"},{"en":"Pre-school activities are activities designed for children before they enter primary school.","zh":"「pre-school activities」是為進入小學前的兒童設計的活動。"},{"en":"A pre-school activity may use simple games to develop balance and coordination.","zh":"學前活動可能使用簡單遊戲來發展平衡和協調。"},{"en":"If young children try different activities early, they may enjoy movement more naturally.","zh":"如果年幼兒童早期嘗試不同活動，他們可能更自然地享受動作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to learning and play before formal schooling.","zh":"這個短語指正式上學前的學習和玩耍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"discover different sports","meaning":"探索不同運動","examples":[{"en":"Young children should discover different sports.","zh":"年幼兒童應探索不同運動。"},{"en":"To discover different sports means to try and learn about several kinds of physical activity.","zh":"「discover different sports」意思是嘗試並了解幾種體能活動。"},{"en":"A child may discover different sports through school games, family outings, and community events.","zh":"兒童可能透過學校遊戲、家庭外出和社區活動探索不同運動。"},{"en":"If children try many sports, they can find what they enjoy and what suits their bodies.","zh":"如果兒童嘗試多種運動，他們可以找到自己喜歡和適合身體的活動。"},{"en":"The phrase values exploration before specialisation.","zh":"這個短語重視在專項化前先探索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a special kind of discovery and learning","meaning":"一種特別的探索與學習","examples":[{"en":"Sport remains a special kind of discovery and learning for children.","zh":"運動對兒童而言仍是一種特別的探索與學習。"},{"en":"A special kind of discovery and learning means a unique way to explore oneself, others, and the world.","zh":"「a special kind of discovery and learning」意思是探索自己、他人和世界的獨特方式。"},{"en":"Through playground games, children learn courage, rules, teamwork, and limits.","zh":"透過操場遊戲，兒童學會勇氣、規則、團隊合作和界限。"},{"en":"If sport is too controlled, this special learning may become weaker.","zh":"如果運動太受控制，這種特別學習可能變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase shows sport as education through experience.","zh":"這個短語把運動呈現為透過經驗進行的教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"no matter how much","meaning":"無論有多……","examples":[{"en":"Sport remains valuable no matter how much adults control it.","zh":"無論成人有多控制運動，它仍然有價值。"},{"en":"No matter how much means regardless of the amount or degree.","zh":"「no matter how much」意思是不論數量或程度有多少。"},{"en":"No matter how much a student practises, rest is still necessary.","zh":"無論學生練習有多少，休息仍然必要。"},{"en":"If adults control sport too much, children may still search for freedom inside it.","zh":"如果成人過度控制運動，兒童可能仍會在其中尋找自由。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the main idea remains true despite degree.","zh":"這個短語顯示主要想法不受程度影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"limit and control","meaning":"限制和控制","examples":[{"en":"Adults may limit and control early sports training.","zh":"成人可能限制和控制早期運動訓練。"},{"en":"To limit and control something means to restrict it and decide how it happens.","zh":"「limit and control」某事，意思是限制它並決定它如何發生。"},{"en":"Schools may limit and control phone use during lessons.","zh":"學校可能在課堂期間限制和控制電話使用。"},{"en":"If adults limit and control all play, children have fewer chances to choose freely.","zh":"如果成人限制和控制所有玩耍，兒童自由選擇的機會就較少。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests strong adult management.","zh":"這個短語暗示強烈的成人管理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"early intensive training","meaning":"早期密集訓練","examples":[{"en":"The passage criticises excessive early intensive training.","zh":"文章批評過度早期密集訓練。"},{"en":"Early intensive training is serious, focused training that begins when children are very young.","zh":"「early intensive training」是兒童年紀很小時開始的認真集中訓練。"},{"en":"A five-year-old training every day for one sport is receiving early intensive training.","zh":"一名五歲孩子每天訓練一項運動，就是接受早期密集訓練。"},{"en":"If training is too intense too early, children may lose enjoyment or suffer pressure.","zh":"如果訓練太早而太密集，兒童可能失去樂趣或承受壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes early specialisation with heavy demands.","zh":"這個短語描述要求沉重的早期專項化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a second example of imbalance","meaning":"第二個失衡例子","examples":[{"en":"Early intensive training is a second example of imbalance.","zh":"早期密集訓練是第二個失衡例子。"},{"en":"A second example of imbalance means another case showing an unhealthy lack of balance.","zh":"「a second example of imbalance」意思是另一個顯示不健康失衡的個案。"},{"en":"Too much testing is a second example of imbalance in school life after too much homework.","zh":"在太多功課之後，太多測驗是學校生活中第二個失衡例子。"},{"en":"If one imbalance comes from space, another may come from training pressure.","zh":"如果一種失衡來自空間，另一種可能來自訓練壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase adds another case to support the argument.","zh":"這個短語加入另一個個案來支持論點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the youngest possible age","meaning":"盡可能年幼的年紀","examples":[{"en":"Early intensive training begins at the youngest possible age.","zh":"早期密集訓練在盡可能年幼的年紀開始。"},{"en":"The youngest possible age means the earliest age at which something can be started.","zh":"「the youngest possible age」意思是某事可以開始的最早年齡。"},{"en":"Some parents enrol children in music lessons at the youngest possible age.","zh":"有些父母在孩子盡可能年幼時報讀音樂課。"},{"en":"If training begins too early, children may not be emotionally ready.","zh":"如果訓練太早開始，兒童可能在情緒上未準備好。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses very early starting.","zh":"這個短語強調非常早開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"before the age of six","meaning":"六歲前","examples":[{"en":"Some children begin intensive training before the age of six.","zh":"有些兒童在六歲前開始密集訓練。"},{"en":"Before the age of six means before a child turns six years old.","zh":"「before the age of six」意思是在孩子滿六歲之前。"},{"en":"Some children learn swimming before the age of six for safety and confidence.","zh":"有些孩子為安全和信心在六歲前學游泳。"},{"en":"If intensive training starts before six, play may become serious very early.","zh":"如果密集訓練在六歲前開始，玩耍可能很早就變得嚴肅。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a clear early-childhood time marker.","zh":"這個短語提供清楚的幼兒時期時間標記。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"one specific sport","meaning":"一項特定運動","examples":[{"en":"Young children often train in one specific sport.","zh":"年幼兒童常訓練一項特定運動。"},{"en":"One specific sport means one clearly chosen sport, rather than several different activities.","zh":"「one specific sport」意思是一項明確選定的運動，而不是幾種不同活動。"},{"en":"A child who only practises gymnastics is focusing on one specific sport.","zh":"只練體操的孩子就是集中於一項特定運動。"},{"en":"If training is limited to one sport, other movement skills may be neglected.","zh":"如果訓練只限於一項運動，其他動作技能可能被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase describes narrow specialisation.","zh":"這個短語描述狹窄專項化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"within an organised framework","meaning":"在有組織的框架內","examples":[{"en":"The sport usually takes place within an organised framework.","zh":"該運動通常在有組織的框架內進行。"},{"en":"Within an organised framework means inside a planned system with rules, schedules, and adult control.","zh":"「within an organised framework」意思是在有規則、時間表和成人控制的計劃系統內。"},{"en":"A school debate club works within an organised framework of meetings and competitions.","zh":"學校辯論會在會議和比賽的有組織框架內運作。"},{"en":"If children train within a framework, they may have less freedom to change the activity.","zh":"如果兒童在框架內訓練，他們改變活動的自由可能較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes structure and control.","zh":"這個短語描述結構和控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"adult-style competitions","meaning":"成人式比賽","examples":[{"en":"Adult-style competitions may be introduced too early.","zh":"成人式比賽可能被過早引入。"},{"en":"Adult-style competitions are contests for children that copy the pressure, rules, and seriousness of adult sport.","zh":"「adult-style competitions」是兒童比賽中模仿成人運動壓力、規則和嚴肅程度的競賽。"},{"en":"A children’s league with rankings, trophies, and harsh selection can become adult-style.","zh":"有排名、獎盃和嚴格選拔的兒童聯賽，可能變成成人式比賽。"},{"en":"If children face adult-style competition too soon, they may feel fear instead of joy.","zh":"如果兒童太早面對成人式比賽，他們可能感到恐懼而不是樂趣。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises making children’s sport too serious.","zh":"這個短語批評把兒童運動弄得太嚴肅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be introduced at an early age","meaning":"在年幼時被引入","examples":[{"en":"Competitions are sometimes introduced at an early age.","zh":"比賽有時在年幼時被引入。"},{"en":"To be introduced at an early age means to be brought into a child’s life when they are still young.","zh":"「be introduced at an early age」意思是在孩子仍年幼時把某事帶入其生活。"},{"en":"Foreign languages may be introduced at an early age through songs and games.","zh":"外語可以透過歌曲和遊戲在年幼時被引入。"},{"en":"If serious competition is introduced too early, children may feel unnecessary pressure.","zh":"如果嚴肅比賽太早被引入，兒童可能感到不必要壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes early exposure to an activity or system.","zh":"這個短語描述早期接觸某活動或制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"balanced development","meaning":"均衡發展","examples":[{"en":"Sport should encourage the balanced development of children.","zh":"運動應鼓勵兒童均衡發展。"},{"en":"Balanced development means healthy growth in body, mind, emotions, and social ability.","zh":"「balanced development」意思是身體、心智、情緒和社交能力的健康成長。"},{"en":"A good school supports balanced development through study, play, rest, and friendship.","zh":"好學校透過學習、玩耍、休息和友誼支持均衡發展。"},{"en":"If children only train to win, other parts of development may be neglected.","zh":"如果兒童只為勝利訓練，其他發展部分可能被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses whole-child growth.","zh":"這個短語強調全人發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"through sport","meaning":"透過運動","examples":[{"en":"Children can develop through sport.","zh":"兒童可以透過運動發展。"},{"en":"Through sport means by using sport as the way or medium for growth or learning.","zh":"「through sport」意思是以運動作為成長或學習的途徑。"},{"en":"Children learn teamwork through sport when they pass the ball and support teammates.","zh":"當兒童傳球和支持隊友時，他們透過運動學習團隊合作。"},{"en":"If sport is enjoyable, it can teach discipline without feeling like punishment.","zh":"如果運動令人享受，它可以教授紀律，而不感覺像懲罰。"},{"en":"The phrase shows sport as a route to development.","zh":"這個短語顯示運動是發展的途徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"no longer respected","meaning":"不再受到尊重","examples":[{"en":"The conditions for balanced development are no longer respected.","zh":"均衡發展的條件不再受到尊重。"},{"en":"No longer respected means once valued or followed, but not valued or followed now.","zh":"「no longer respected」意思是曾被重視或遵守，但現在不再被重視或遵守。"},{"en":"In some workplaces, lunch breaks are no longer respected when meetings fill every hour.","zh":"在一些工作場所，當會議填滿每小時，午膳時間就不再受到尊重。"},{"en":"If children’s need for rest is no longer respected, training may harm them.","zh":"如果兒童對休息的需要不再受到尊重，訓練可能傷害他們。"},{"en":"The phrase signals a loss of proper regard.","zh":"這個短語表示適當重視的喪失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"far more widely available","meaning":"普及得多","examples":[{"en":"Early intensive training is far more widely available today.","zh":"早期密集訓練今天普及得多。"},{"en":"Far more widely available means much easier for many people to access than before.","zh":"「far more widely available」意思是比以前容易得多讓許多人接觸到。"},{"en":"Online lessons are far more widely available now than ten years ago.","zh":"網上課程現在比十年前普及得多。"},{"en":"If intensive training becomes easier to access, more children may enter it early.","zh":"如果密集訓練更容易取得，更多兒童可能早期加入。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a big increase in availability.","zh":"這個短語描述可取得程度大幅增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sports organisations","meaning":"體育組織","examples":[{"en":"Many sports organisations support early intensive training.","zh":"許多體育組織支持早期密集訓練。"},{"en":"Sports organisations are clubs, associations, federations, or groups that manage sporting activities.","zh":"「sports organisations」是管理運動活動的球會、協會、聯會或團體。"},{"en":"A football association is a sports organisation that sets rules and runs competitions.","zh":"足球總會是制定規則和舉辦比賽的體育組織。"},{"en":"If sports organisations value early success too much, children may face pressure.","zh":"如果體育組織太重視早期成功，兒童可能面對壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase names institutions that shape how sport is practised.","zh":"這個短語指出塑造運動方式的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be forced to use","meaning":"被迫使用","examples":[{"en":"Some organisations claim they are forced to use intensive training.","zh":"有些組織聲稱它們被迫使用密集訓練。"},{"en":"To be forced to use something means to feel there is no real choice but to use it.","zh":"「be forced to use」某物，意思是覺得除了使用它之外沒有真正選擇。"},{"en":"A school may be forced to use online lessons when a building is closed.","zh":"當校舍關閉時，學校可能被迫使用網課。"},{"en":"If competition demands early ability, clubs may feel pushed into intensive training.","zh":"如果比賽要求早期能力，球會可能感到被推向密集訓練。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests pressure rather than free choice.","zh":"這個短語暗示壓力，而不是自由選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"this type of training","meaning":"這類訓練","examples":[{"en":"Sports organisations defend this type of training.","zh":"體育組織為這類訓練辯護。"},{"en":"This type of training means the particular training method just mentioned.","zh":"「this type of training」意思是剛提及的特定訓練方法。"},{"en":"Daily drills for very young athletes are one example of this type of training.","zh":"年幼運動員每日操練，是這類訓練的一個例子。"},{"en":"If this type of training is too intense, children may become tired or discouraged.","zh":"如果這類訓練太密集，兒童可能變得疲倦或灰心。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to a specific training approach.","zh":"這個短語指回一種特定訓練方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"what is called","meaning":"所謂的","examples":[{"en":"The idea is linked to what is called the golden age.","zh":"這個想法與所謂的黃金期有關。"},{"en":"What is called introduces a term or name used for something.","zh":"「what is called」用來引出某事的術語或名稱。"},{"en":"Children often experience what is called separation anxiety on the first day of school.","zh":"兒童在開學第一天常經歷所謂的分離焦慮。"},{"en":"If a special term is introduced, readers know how experts label the idea.","zh":"如果引入特殊術語，讀者就知道專家如何命名該想法。"},{"en":"The phrase helps explain terminology.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the golden age","meaning":"黃金期","examples":[{"en":"Some coaches refer to the golden age for acquiring physical skills.","zh":"有些教練提到掌握身體技能的黃金期。"},{"en":"The golden age means the period believed to be best for learning a particular ability.","zh":"「the golden age」意思是被認為最適合學習某種能力的時期。"},{"en":"Some parents think early childhood is the golden age for language learning.","zh":"有些父母認為幼兒期是語言學習的黃金期。"},{"en":"If coaches believe a golden age will be missed, they may push early training.","zh":"如果教練相信黃金期會被錯過，他們可能推動早期訓練。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an ideal learning window.","zh":"這個短語描述理想學習時機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"acquire physical skills","meaning":"掌握身體技能","examples":[{"en":"The golden age is seen as a key time to acquire physical skills.","zh":"黃金期被視為掌握身體技能的關鍵時間。"},{"en":"To acquire physical skills means to learn body movements such as balance, speed, strength, and coordination.","zh":"「acquire physical skills」意思是學會平衡、速度、力量和協調等身體動作。"},{"en":"Children acquire physical skills when they climb, jump, swim, and throw balls.","zh":"兒童爬高、跳躍、游泳和投球時，就是掌握身體技能。"},{"en":"If children practise varied movement, they may build a stronger physical base.","zh":"如果兒童練習多樣動作，他們可能建立更強身體基礎。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning how to use the body effectively.","zh":"這個短語描述學習有效使用身體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be considered unthinkable","meaning":"被認為不可想像","examples":[{"en":"It is considered unthinkable for young athletes to miss this period.","zh":"年輕運動員錯過這段時期被認為不可想像。"},{"en":"To be considered unthinkable means to be regarded as impossible to accept or imagine.","zh":"「be considered unthinkable」意思是被視為無法接受或想像。"},{"en":"For some parents, leaving a child unsupervised online is considered unthinkable.","zh":"對某些父母而言，讓孩子無監管地上網被認為不可想像。"},{"en":"If missing a training window is seen as unthinkable, pressure on children increases.","zh":"如果錯過訓練時機被視為不可想像，兒童壓力就會增加。"},{"en":"The phrase shows very strong belief or fear.","zh":"這個短語顯示非常強烈的信念或恐懼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"young skater or gymnast","meaning":"年輕溜冰運動員或體操運動員","examples":[{"en":"A young skater or gymnast may be pushed into early training.","zh":"年輕溜冰運動員或體操運動員可能被推入早期訓練。"},{"en":"A young skater or gymnast is a child athlete training in skating or gymnastics.","zh":"「young skater or gymnast」是在溜冰或體操方面訓練的兒童運動員。"},{"en":"A young gymnast may practise flexibility and balance several times a week.","zh":"年輕體操運動員可能每星期幾次練習柔軟度和平衡。"},{"en":"If a sport rewards early technical skill, children may start training very young.","zh":"如果一項運動重視早期技術能力，兒童可能很年幼就開始訓練。"},{"en":"The phrase gives examples of sports often linked with early specialisation.","zh":"這個短語提供常與早期專項化相關的運動例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"miss this period","meaning":"錯過這段時期","examples":[{"en":"Coaches worry that young athletes may miss this period.","zh":"教練擔心年輕運動員可能錯過這段時期。"},{"en":"To miss this period means to fail to use an important time for learning or development.","zh":"「miss this period」意思是未能利用一段重要學習或發展時間。"},{"en":"A student may miss the best revision period if they start studying only the night before.","zh":"如果學生只在前一晚開始溫習，可能錯過最佳溫習期。"},{"en":"If athletes miss a key learning stage, coaches fear they may progress more slowly.","zh":"如果運動員錯過關鍵學習階段，教練擔心他們進步較慢。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses anxiety about losing a valuable opportunity.","zh":"這個短語表達失去寶貴機會的焦慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fall so far behind","meaning":"落後太多","examples":[{"en":"Children may fall so far behind the best athletes.","zh":"兒童可能落後最頂尖運動員太多。"},{"en":"To fall so far behind means to become much less advanced than others.","zh":"「fall so far behind」意思是變得比其他人落後很多。"},{"en":"A student who misses many lessons may fall far behind classmates.","zh":"缺席很多課的學生可能落後同學很多。"},{"en":"If training starts late in a highly competitive sport, catching up may feel difficult.","zh":"如果在高度競爭的運動中訓練開始得晚，追上可能感到困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large gap in progress.","zh":"這個短語描述進度上的巨大差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the best","meaning":"最頂尖的人","examples":[{"en":"Young athletes are compared with the best in their sport.","zh":"年輕運動員被拿來與其運動中最頂尖的人比較。"},{"en":"The best means the highest-performing people in a group or field.","zh":"「the best」意思是一個群體或領域中表現最高的人。"},{"en":"A young pianist may compare herself with the best players in a competition.","zh":"年輕鋼琴手可能把自己與比賽中最頂尖的人比較。"},{"en":"If children are measured only against the best, they may feel inadequate.","zh":"如果兒童只被用最頂尖的人來衡量，他們可能感到不足。"},{"en":"The phrase points to top-level performers.","zh":"這個短語指最高水平的表現者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hope to catch up","meaning":"有望追上","examples":[{"en":"They may never hope to catch up.","zh":"他們可能永遠沒有望追上。"},{"en":"To hope to catch up means to believe it may still be possible to reach others’ level.","zh":"「hope to catch up」意思是相信仍可能達到他人的水平。"},{"en":"A student who missed lessons may hope to catch up by studying during the holiday.","zh":"缺課的學生可能希望透過假期溫習追上。"},{"en":"If the gap becomes too large, catching up feels unrealistic.","zh":"如果差距變得太大，追上就感覺不現實。"},{"en":"The phrase describes trying to close a difference in progress.","zh":"這個短語描述嘗試縮小進度差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be faced with","meaning":"面對","examples":[{"en":"Trainers are faced with a demand for early ability.","zh":"教練面對對早期能力的要求。"},{"en":"To be faced with something means to have to deal with a situation or problem.","zh":"「be faced with」某事，意思是必須處理某情況或問題。"},{"en":"A teacher may be faced with a class where students have very different levels.","zh":"老師可能面對一班程度差異很大的學生。"},{"en":"If coaches face pressure for early results, they may push children too hard.","zh":"如果教練面對早期成績壓力，他們可能過度催谷兒童。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being confronted by a challenge.","zh":"這個短語描述面臨挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"demand for early ability","meaning":"對早期能力的要求","examples":[{"en":"The demand for early ability has encouraged intensive training.","zh":"對早期能力的要求鼓勵了密集訓練。"},{"en":"Demand for early ability means pressure for children to show skill at a very young age.","zh":"「demand for early ability」意思是要求兒童很年幼時已展示技能的壓力。"},{"en":"In music or sport, parents may create demand for early ability by comparing children too soon.","zh":"在音樂或運動中，父母太早比較孩子可能造成對早期能力的要求。"},{"en":"If early ability is demanded, children may train before they are emotionally ready.","zh":"如果早期能力被要求，兒童可能在情緒準備好前就接受訓練。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pressure to perform early.","zh":"這個短語描述對早早表現的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"put a safety net in place","meaning":"設立安全網","examples":[{"en":"A safety net should be put in place for young athletes.","zh":"應為年輕運動員設立安全網。"},{"en":"To put a safety net in place means to create protection in case something goes wrong.","zh":"「put a safety net in place」意思是建立保護措施，以防事情出問題。"},{"en":"Schools put a safety net in place when they offer counselling before exams.","zh":"學校在考試前提供輔導，就是設立安全網。"},{"en":"If intensive training continues, safeguards must protect children’s health and motivation.","zh":"如果密集訓練繼續，保障措施必須保護兒童健康和動機。"},{"en":"The phrase describes building protective support.","zh":"這個短語描述建立保護性支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"maximise the benefits","meaning":"將好處最大化","examples":[{"en":"A safety net can maximise the benefits of intensive training.","zh":"安全網可以將密集訓練的好處最大化。"},{"en":"To maximise the benefits means to make the positive effects as great as possible.","zh":"「maximise the benefits」意思是令正面效果盡可能大。"},{"en":"Students maximise the benefits of revision by sleeping well and reviewing mistakes.","zh":"學生透過睡得好和檢視錯誤，將溫習好處最大化。"},{"en":"If training is carefully managed, children may improve without being harmed.","zh":"如果訓練被仔細管理，兒童可能進步而不受傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on increasing good outcomes.","zh":"這個短語集中於增加好結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"minimise the disadvantages","meaning":"將壞處減至最低","examples":[{"en":"Good safeguards can minimise the disadvantages of intensive training.","zh":"良好保障可以將密集訓練的壞處減至最低。"},{"en":"To minimise the disadvantages means to reduce the negative effects as much as possible.","zh":"「minimise the disadvantages」意思是盡量減少負面效果。"},{"en":"A school can minimise the disadvantages of homework by keeping tasks short and useful.","zh":"學校可以透過保持功課簡短而有用，將功課壞處減至最低。"},{"en":"If children rest enough, the harms of hard training may be reduced.","zh":"如果兒童有足夠休息，艱苦訓練的傷害可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on limiting bad outcomes.","zh":"這個短語集中於限制壞結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"give up sport","meaning":"放棄運動","examples":[{"en":"Many young children give up sport.","zh":"許多年幼兒童放棄運動。"},{"en":"To give up sport means to stop taking part in sport.","zh":"「give up sport」意思是停止參與運動。"},{"en":"A child may give up sport if every match ends with criticism.","zh":"如果每場比賽都以批評結束，孩子可能放棄運動。"},{"en":"If sport stops being enjoyable, children may choose other activities instead.","zh":"如果運動不再令人享受，兒童可能改選其他活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes quitting physical activity.","zh":"這個短語描述退出體能活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the most common reason for","meaning":"……最常見的原因","examples":[{"en":"The most common reason for leaving a sport is to change to another sport.","zh":"放棄某項運動最常見的原因是轉玩另一項運動。"},{"en":"The most common reason for something is the reason that appears most often.","zh":"「the most common reason for」某事，是出現得最頻密的原因。"},{"en":"The most common reason for lateness may be unreliable transport.","zh":"遲到最常見的原因可能是交通不可靠。"},{"en":"If many children leave one sport to try another, leaving is not always negative.","zh":"如果許多兒童離開一項運動去嘗試另一項，離開不一定負面。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the most frequent cause.","zh":"這個短語指出最常見原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"leave a sport","meaning":"放棄某項運動","examples":[{"en":"Children may leave a sport because of negative experiences.","zh":"兒童可能因負面經驗而放棄某項運動。"},{"en":"To leave a sport means to stop participating in that particular sport.","zh":"「leave a sport」意思是停止參與某一特定運動。"},{"en":"A child may leave football and start swimming instead.","zh":"兒童可能放棄足球，改為開始游泳。"},{"en":"If children feel criticised or excluded, they may leave the sport completely.","zh":"如果兒童感到被批評或排斥，他們可能完全放棄該運動。"},{"en":"The phrase can mean changing activity or quitting because of pressure.","zh":"這個短語可以指轉換活動，也可以指因壓力而退出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"change to another sport","meaning":"轉玩另一項運動","examples":[{"en":"Leaving one sport to change to another sport is not necessarily bad.","zh":"放棄一項運動去轉玩另一項運動本身不一定不好。"},{"en":"To change to another sport means to stop one sport and begin a different one.","zh":"「change to another sport」意思是停止一項運動並開始另一項。"},{"en":"A child may change from tennis to basketball after discovering they enjoy team games.","zh":"兒童發現自己喜歡團隊遊戲後，可能由網球轉玩籃球。"},{"en":"If children change sports, they may find an activity that fits them better.","zh":"如果兒童轉換運動，他們可能找到更適合自己的活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes switching rather than giving up activity altogether.","zh":"這個短語描述轉換，而不是完全放棄活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in itself","meaning":"本身","examples":[{"en":"Changing to another sport is in itself no bad thing.","zh":"轉玩另一項運動本身不是壞事。"},{"en":"In itself means considered alone, without other related factors.","zh":"「in itself」意思是單獨看待，不連同其他相關因素。"},{"en":"Making a mistake is not in itself a failure if the student learns from it.","zh":"如果學生從錯誤中學習，犯錯本身不是失敗。"},{"en":"If a child changes sport happily, the change alone is not a problem.","zh":"如果孩子愉快地轉換運動，單是轉變本身並不是問題。"},{"en":"The phrase separates one fact from its wider context.","zh":"這個短語把一個事實與較廣語境分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"no bad thing","meaning":"不是壞事","examples":[{"en":"Changing sport is in itself no bad thing.","zh":"轉換運動本身不是壞事。"},{"en":"No bad thing means not harmful and possibly even useful.","zh":"「no bad thing」意思是沒有害處，甚至可能有用。"},{"en":"Taking a short break from studying is no bad thing if it helps students return focused.","zh":"如果短暫休息能幫助學生重新集中，暫停溫習不是壞事。"},{"en":"If changing sport keeps a child active and happy, it should not be treated as failure.","zh":"如果轉換運動令孩子保持活躍和快樂，就不應被視為失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase gently rejects a negative judgment.","zh":"這個短語溫和地否定負面判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"receive too much criticism","meaning":"受到太多批評","examples":[{"en":"Children may feel that they have received too much criticism.","zh":"兒童可能覺得自己受到太多批評。"},{"en":"To receive too much criticism means to be corrected or judged negatively too often.","zh":"「receive too much criticism」意思是太經常被糾正或被負面評價。"},{"en":"A student may lose confidence if every essay receives too much criticism and no praise.","zh":"如果每篇作文都受到太多批評而沒有讚賞，學生可能失去信心。"},{"en":"If children are criticised constantly, they may stop enjoying sport.","zh":"如果兒童不斷被批評，他們可能停止享受運動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes excessive negative feedback.","zh":"這個短語描述過度負面回饋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"negative assessments","meaning":"負面評估","examples":[{"en":"Children may leave sport because of negative assessments.","zh":"兒童可能因負面評估而放棄運動。"},{"en":"Negative assessments are unfavourable judgments about someone’s ability or performance.","zh":"「negative assessments」是對某人能力或表現的不利評價。"},{"en":"A child who is always told they are slow receives negative assessments.","zh":"總被說很慢的孩子，就是收到負面評估。"},{"en":"If feedback only points out failure, children may feel they are not good enough.","zh":"如果回饋只指出失敗，兒童可能覺得自己不夠好。"},{"en":"The phrase describes discouraging evaluation.","zh":"這個短語描述令人灰心的評價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"assess their own level of competence","meaning":"評估自己的能力水平","examples":[{"en":"Young children cannot assess their own level of competence.","zh":"年幼兒童不能評估自己的能力水平。"},{"en":"To assess one’s own level of competence means to judge how skilled or capable one is.","zh":"「assess one’s own level of competence」意思是判斷自己有多熟練或有能力。"},{"en":"A beginner may not assess their own English level accurately without a teacher’s help.","zh":"初學者沒有老師幫助時，可能不能準確評估自己的英語水平。"},{"en":"If children cannot judge their ability, adult comments affect them strongly.","zh":"如果兒童不能判斷自己能力，成人評論就會強烈影響他們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes self-evaluation of ability.","zh":"這個短語描述對能力的自我評價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"level of competence","meaning":"能力水平","examples":[{"en":"Children may misunderstand their own level of competence.","zh":"兒童可能誤解自己的能力水平。"},{"en":"Level of competence means how skilled or capable someone is at a task.","zh":"「level of competence」意思是某人在任務中有多熟練或有能力。"},{"en":"A teacher checks a student’s level of competence before choosing reading materials.","zh":"老師選擇閱讀材料前會檢查學生的能力水平。"},{"en":"If children think effort equals ability, they may misjudge their actual level.","zh":"如果兒童認為努力等於能力，他們可能誤判實際水平。"},{"en":"The phrase describes degree of ability.","zh":"這個短語描述能力程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make an effort","meaning":"付出努力","examples":[{"en":"Young children believe that making an effort shows competence.","zh":"年幼兒童相信付出努力顯示能力。"},{"en":"To make an effort means to try hard to do something.","zh":"「make an effort」意思是努力嘗試做某事。"},{"en":"A student makes an effort when they rewrite an essay after feedback.","zh":"學生在收到回饋後重寫文章，就是付出努力。"},{"en":"If children try hard but still lose, they need encouragement rather than shame.","zh":"如果兒童努力但仍然落敗，他們需要鼓勵而不是羞辱。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on trying, not only winning.","zh":"這個短語集中於嘗試，而不只是勝利。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a sign of competence","meaning":"能力的標誌","examples":[{"en":"Children see effort as a sign of competence.","zh":"兒童把努力視為能力的標誌。"},{"en":"A sign of competence is something that shows a person has ability or skill.","zh":"「a sign of competence」是顯示某人有能力或技能的事物。"},{"en":"Asking thoughtful questions can be a sign of competence in a classroom.","zh":"在課室中提出有思想的問題，可以是能力的標誌。"},{"en":"If young children link effort with ability, criticism of results may hurt them deeply.","zh":"如果年幼兒童把努力與能力連繫起來，對結果的批評可能深深傷害他們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence of ability.","zh":"這個短語描述能力的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be particularly sensitive to","meaning":"對……特別敏感","examples":[{"en":"Young children are particularly sensitive to criticism.","zh":"年幼兒童對批評特別敏感。"},{"en":"To be particularly sensitive to something means to react strongly to it.","zh":"「be particularly sensitive to」某事，意思是對它反應強烈。"},{"en":"A tired student may be particularly sensitive to jokes about their mistakes.","zh":"疲倦學生可能對別人取笑其錯誤特別敏感。"},{"en":"If children are sensitive to criticism, coaches must choose words carefully.","zh":"如果兒童對批評敏感，教練必須小心選字。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong emotional reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈情緒反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"criticism from adults or peers","meaning":"來自成人或同輩的批評","examples":[{"en":"Children may be hurt by criticism from adults or peers.","zh":"兒童可能被來自成人或同輩的批評傷害。"},{"en":"Criticism from adults or peers means negative comments from grown-ups or children of the same age group.","zh":"「criticism from adults or peers」是來自成人或同齡孩子的負面評論。"},{"en":"A child may feel embarrassed if classmates and teachers both criticise their performance.","zh":"如果同學和老師都批評其表現，孩子可能感到尷尬。"},{"en":"If criticism comes from people children trust, it can affect confidence strongly.","zh":"如果批評來自兒童信任的人，會強烈影響信心。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where negative judgment comes from.","zh":"這個短語指出負面評價來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"pay particular attention to","meaning":"特別注意","examples":[{"en":"Trainers must pay particular attention to children’s sensitivity.","zh":"教練必須特別注意兒童的敏感度。"},{"en":"To pay particular attention to something means to notice it carefully because it is important.","zh":"「pay particular attention to」某事，意思是因它重要而仔細留意。"},{"en":"Teachers should pay particular attention to quiet students who rarely ask for help.","zh":"老師應特別注意很少求助的安靜學生。"},{"en":"If coaches understand children’s feelings, they can avoid unnecessary harm.","zh":"如果教練理解兒童感受，就能避免不必要傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase shows focused care.","zh":"這個短語顯示集中而細心的關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"avoid excessive criticism","meaning":"避免過度批評","examples":[{"en":"Trainers should avoid excessive criticism.","zh":"教練應避免過度批評。"},{"en":"To avoid excessive criticism means to stop giving too much negative feedback.","zh":"「avoid excessive criticism」意思是避免給予太多負面回饋。"},{"en":"A teacher can avoid excessive criticism by pointing out one strength before one correction.","zh":"老師可以先指出一個優點，再給一個修正，以避免過度批評。"},{"en":"If children hear only faults, they may lose motivation.","zh":"如果兒童只聽到缺點，他們可能失去動機。"},{"en":"The phrase encourages balanced feedback.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵平衡回饋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"discriminate against","meaning":"歧視；差別對待","examples":[{"en":"Trainers should avoid strategies that discriminate against children.","zh":"教練應避免歧視兒童的策略。"},{"en":"To discriminate against someone means to treat them unfairly because of a feature, status, or group.","zh":"「discriminate against」某人，意思是因某特徵、身份或群體而不公平對待他。"},{"en":"A club discriminates against weaker players if it never gives them a chance to join games.","zh":"如果球會從不給較弱球員參與比賽機會，就是差別對待他們。"},{"en":"If children feel unfairly excluded, they may leave sport.","zh":"如果兒童感到被不公平排斥，他們可能離開運動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unfair treatment.","zh":"這個短語描述不公平對待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"team sports","meaning":"團隊運動","examples":[{"en":"In team sports, naming reserves can make children feel excluded.","zh":"在團隊運動中，點名後備球員可能令兒童感到被排除。"},{"en":"Team sports are sports where players work together in groups against another group.","zh":"「team sports」是球員以小組合作對抗另一組的運動。"},{"en":"Football, basketball, and volleyball are common team sports.","zh":"足球、籃球和排球都是常見團隊運動。"},{"en":"If team roles are handled badly, some children may feel less valued.","zh":"如果團隊角色處理不好，有些兒童可能感到自己較不被重視。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to sports based on cooperation and shared performance.","zh":"這個短語指以合作和共同表現為基礎的運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"first-choice players","meaning":"正選球員","examples":[{"en":"Trainers should be careful when naming first-choice players.","zh":"教練點名正選球員時應小心。"},{"en":"First-choice players are the players selected before others to start or represent the team.","zh":"「first-choice players」是優先被選出開始比賽或代表隊伍的球員。"},{"en":"In a school match, first-choice players may play first while others wait.","zh":"在學校比賽中，正選球員可能先上場，而其他人等待。"},{"en":"If coaches always choose the same children, others may feel ignored.","zh":"如果教練總是選同一批孩子，其他人可能感到被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preferred or starting players.","zh":"這個短語描述被優先選擇或先發的球員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reserves","meaning":"後備球員","examples":[{"en":"Some children may feel discouraged if they are always reserves.","zh":"如果總是後備球員，有些兒童可能感到灰心。"},{"en":"Reserves are players who are not chosen to start but may play later if needed.","zh":"「reserves」是沒有被選為首發，但需要時可能之後上場的球員。"},{"en":"A reserve on a school football team may sit on the bench during the first half.","zh":"學校足球隊的後備球員可能在上半場坐在後備席。"},{"en":"If a child is always a reserve, they may feel less important to the team.","zh":"如果孩子總是後備球員，他可能感到對隊伍較不重要。"},{"en":"The phrase names backup players.","zh":"這個短語指出替補球員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"it should be remembered that","meaning":"應記住","examples":[{"en":"It should be remembered that primary school children mainly want fun.","zh":"應記住，小學生主要想要樂趣。"},{"en":"It should be remembered that means people should not forget an important point.","zh":"「it should be remembered that」意思是人們不應忘記一個重要重點。"},{"en":"It should be remembered that students need rest, not only homework.","zh":"應記住，學生需要休息，而不只是功課。"},{"en":"If adults forget children’s motives, sports programmes may become too serious.","zh":"如果成人忘記兒童的動機，運動計劃可能變得太嚴肅。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a reminder.","zh":"這個短語引入提醒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"primary school children","meaning":"小學生","examples":[{"en":"Primary school children’s main desire is to have fun and socialise.","zh":"小學生的主要願望是玩得開心和社交。"},{"en":"Primary school children are children who attend the early years of formal schooling.","zh":"「primary school children」是接受早期正式學校教育的兒童。"},{"en":"Primary school children often learn well through games, movement, and simple teamwork.","zh":"小學生通常透過遊戲、活動和簡單團隊合作學得好。"},{"en":"If coaches treat them like adults, they may feel stressed or confused.","zh":"如果教練把他們當成人看待，他們可能感到壓力或困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to young school-age children.","zh":"這個短語指年幼學齡兒童。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"main desire","meaning":"主要願望","examples":[{"en":"Their main desire is to enjoy sport.","zh":"他們的主要願望是享受運動。"},{"en":"Main desire means the strongest wish or most important thing someone wants.","zh":"「main desire」意思是某人最強烈的願望或最想要的事。"},{"en":"A tired student’s main desire after exams may be to sleep.","zh":"疲倦學生考試後的主要願望可能是睡覺。"},{"en":"If children’s main desire is fun, programmes should not focus only on winning.","zh":"如果兒童的主要願望是樂趣，計劃就不應只集中於勝利。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the central motivation.","zh":"這個短語指出核心動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have fun and socialise","meaning":"玩得開心和社交","examples":[{"en":"Young children want to have fun and socialise through sport.","zh":"年幼兒童想透過運動玩得開心和社交。"},{"en":"To have fun and socialise means to enjoy oneself and spend time interacting with others.","zh":"「have fun and socialise」意思是享受自己並花時間與他人互動。"},{"en":"Children have fun and socialise when they play ball games with classmates at recess.","zh":"小息時與同學玩球類遊戲，兒童就是玩得開心和社交。"},{"en":"If sport gives children friendship and enjoyment, they are more likely to continue.","zh":"如果運動給兒童友誼和樂趣，他們更可能繼續參與。"},{"en":"The phrase shows sport as play and connection.","zh":"這個短語顯示運動是玩耍和連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"become a good competitor","meaning":"成為出色的競爭者","examples":[{"en":"The desire to become a good competitor develops later.","zh":"成為出色競爭者的願望較後才發展。"},{"en":"To become a good competitor means to learn to compete seriously, fairly, and effectively.","zh":"「become a good competitor」意思是學會認真、公平而有效地競爭。"},{"en":"A child may become a good competitor after first learning to enjoy practice and teamwork.","zh":"兒童可能先學會享受練習和團隊合作，之後才成為出色競爭者。"},{"en":"If competition is introduced too early, children may fear losing instead of learning.","zh":"如果競爭太早引入，兒童可能害怕失敗而不是學習。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to mature competitive ability.","zh":"這個短語指成熟的競爭能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"develop later","meaning":"較後才發展","examples":[{"en":"The desire to compete seriously will develop later.","zh":"認真競爭的願望會較後才發展。"},{"en":"To develop later means to appear or grow at a later stage.","zh":"「develop later」意思是在較後階段出現或成長。"},{"en":"A child’s interest in reading long novels may develop later than basic reading skills.","zh":"兒童對長篇小說的興趣可能比基本閱讀能力較後才發展。"},{"en":"If adults wait, competitive motivation may arise naturally when children are ready.","zh":"如果成人等待，競爭動機可能在兒童準備好時自然出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes delayed growth or emergence.","zh":"這個短語描述延後的成長或出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"knowledge of child development","meaning":"兒童發展知識","examples":[{"en":"Knowledge of child development is essential for sports trainers.","zh":"兒童發展知識對運動教練至關重要。"},{"en":"Knowledge of child development means understanding how children grow physically, mentally, socially, and emotionally.","zh":"「knowledge of child development」意思是理解兒童在身體、心智、社交和情緒方面如何成長。"},{"en":"Teachers use knowledge of child development to choose suitable tasks for different ages.","zh":"老師利用兒童發展知識為不同年齡選擇合適任務。"},{"en":"If coaches lack this knowledge, they may expect too much too soon.","zh":"如果教練缺乏這知識，可能太早期望太多。"},{"en":"The phrase describes understanding children’s growth needs.","zh":"這個短語描述對兒童成長需要的理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be indispensable for","meaning":"對……不可或缺","examples":[{"en":"Knowledge of child development is indispensable for those working with children.","zh":"兒童發展知識對與兒童工作的人不可或缺。"},{"en":"To be indispensable for something means to be absolutely necessary for it.","zh":"「be indispensable for」某事，意思是對它絕對必要。"},{"en":"Clear instructions are indispensable for students doing a difficult experiment.","zh":"清楚指示對進行困難實驗的學生不可或缺。"},{"en":"If coaches work with young children, understanding development is not optional.","zh":"如果教練與年幼兒童工作，理解發展並非可有可無。"},{"en":"The phrase means something is essential.","zh":"這個短語意思是某事必不可少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"take care of children","meaning":"照顧兒童","examples":[{"en":"Trainers and doctors take care of children at this age.","zh":"教練和醫生在這年齡照顧兒童。"},{"en":"To take care of children means to protect, guide, support, and meet their needs.","zh":"「take care of children」意思是保護、引導、支援並滿足兒童需要。"},{"en":"Teachers take care of children by keeping classrooms safe and respectful.","zh":"老師透過保持課室安全和互相尊重來照顧兒童。"},{"en":"If adults take care of young athletes properly, sport becomes safer and happier.","zh":"如果成人妥善照顧年輕運動員，運動就變得更安全、更快樂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes responsibility for children’s wellbeing.","zh":"這個短語描述對兒童福祉的責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"it is up to","meaning":"取決於；有賴於","examples":[{"en":"It is up to trainers and psychologists to limit excessive training.","zh":"限制過度訓練有賴於教練和心理學家。"},{"en":"It is up to someone means that person has the responsibility to decide or act.","zh":"「it is up to」某人，意思是該人有責任作決定或行動。"},{"en":"It is up to teachers to create a safe environment for discussion.","zh":"創造安全討論環境有賴於老師。"},{"en":"If children cannot protect themselves from pressure, adults must take responsibility.","zh":"如果兒童不能保護自己免受壓力，成人就必須承擔責任。"},{"en":"The phrase assigns responsibility.","zh":"這個短語分配責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sports doctors","meaning":"運動醫生","examples":[{"en":"Sports doctors should help protect young athletes.","zh":"運動醫生應幫助保護年輕運動員。"},{"en":"Sports doctors are medical specialists who deal with injuries, health, and performance in sport.","zh":"「sports doctors」是處理運動中的傷患、健康和表現的醫學專家。"},{"en":"A sports doctor may check whether a young runner’s knee pain needs rest.","zh":"運動醫生可能檢查年輕跑手的膝痛是否需要休息。"},{"en":"If doctors monitor young athletes, serious injury may be prevented.","zh":"如果醫生監測年輕運動員，嚴重受傷可能被預防。"},{"en":"The phrase names medical professionals in sport.","zh":"這個短語指出運動中的醫療專業人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"implement the measures","meaning":"實施措施","examples":[{"en":"Professionals must implement the measures necessary to protect children.","zh":"專業人士必須實施保護兒童所需的措施。"},{"en":"To implement the measures means to put planned actions into practice.","zh":"「implement the measures」意思是把計劃好的行動付諸實行。"},{"en":"A school may implement safety measures after a playground accident.","zh":"學校可能在遊樂場意外後實施安全措施。"},{"en":"If rules are written but not implemented, children remain unprotected.","zh":"如果規則只是寫下而沒有實施，兒童仍然得不到保護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes turning plans into action.","zh":"這個短語描述把計劃變成行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"limit excessive early practice","meaning":"限制過度早期運動訓練","examples":[{"en":"Adults should limit excessive early practice of sport by children.","zh":"成人應限制兒童過度早期運動訓練。"},{"en":"To limit excessive early practice means to reduce training that is too heavy and begins too young.","zh":"「limit excessive early practice」意思是減少過重且開始得太早的訓練。"},{"en":"A coach may limit early practice by giving children more rest days and more varied games.","zh":"教練可以透過給兒童更多休息日和更多元遊戲來限制早期訓練。"},{"en":"If practice is limited sensibly, children can improve without burning out.","zh":"如果練習被合理限制，兒童可以進步而不被耗盡。"},{"en":"The phrase aims to protect children from overtraining.","zh":"這個短語旨在保護兒童免受過度訓練。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"parental attitudes","meaning":"父母態度","examples":[{"en":"Parental attitudes are a third source of imbalance.","zh":"父母態度是第三個失衡來源。"},{"en":"Parental attitudes are parents’ beliefs, expectations, and behaviours toward their children.","zh":"「parental attitudes」是父母對子女的信念、期望和行為。"},{"en":"A parent’s attitude to grades can affect whether a child enjoys learning.","zh":"父母對成績的態度可以影響孩子是否享受學習。"},{"en":"If parents focus only on winning, children may feel sport is pressure rather than play.","zh":"如果父母只集中於勝利，兒童可能覺得運動是壓力而不是玩耍。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how parents’ mindset shapes children’s experience.","zh":"這個短語顯示父母心態如何塑造兒童經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a source of imbalance","meaning":"失衡的來源","examples":[{"en":"Parental pressure is a source of imbalance in children’s sport.","zh":"父母壓力是兒童運動中失衡的來源。"},{"en":"A source of imbalance is a cause that creates an unhealthy lack of balance.","zh":"「a source of imbalance」是造成不健康失衡的原因。"},{"en":"Too many after-school classes can be a source of imbalance in family life.","zh":"太多課後班可以是家庭生活失衡的來源。"},{"en":"If parents push too hard, enjoyment and pressure become uneven.","zh":"如果父母催谷太狠，樂趣和壓力就變得不平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where the problem comes from.","zh":"這個短語指出問題來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"threaten children and sport","meaning":"威脅兒童與運動","examples":[{"en":"Parental attitudes can threaten children and sport.","zh":"父母態度可以威脅兒童與運動。"},{"en":"To threaten children and sport means to put children’s wellbeing and their positive relationship with sport at risk.","zh":"「threaten children and sport」意思是令兒童福祉和他們與運動的正面關係陷入風險。"},{"en":"Excessive pressure can threaten children’s love of music in the same way it can threaten sport.","zh":"過度壓力可以威脅兒童對音樂的熱愛，就像威脅運動一樣。"},{"en":"If children associate sport with fear, their long-term participation may decline.","zh":"如果兒童把運動與恐懼聯繫起來，他們的長期參與可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that adult behaviour can harm children’s sporting experience.","zh":"這個短語警告成人行為可以傷害兒童運動經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"emphasise that","meaning":"強調","examples":[{"en":"Rainer Martens emphasises that adults can destroy children’s joy of sport.","zh":"Rainer Martens 強調成人可以破壞兒童在運動中的樂趣。"},{"en":"To emphasise that means to strongly state or highlight an important point.","zh":"「emphasise that」意思是強烈指出或突出一個重要重點。"},{"en":"A teacher may emphasise that mistakes are part of learning.","zh":"老師可能強調錯誤是學習的一部分。"},{"en":"If an expert emphasises a risk, readers should pay close attention.","zh":"如果專家強調某風險，讀者應特別留意。"},{"en":"The phrase signals importance.","zh":"這個短語表示重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"children’s joy of sports","meaning":"兒童在運動中的樂趣","examples":[{"en":"Children’s joy of sports can be damaged by adult pressure.","zh":"兒童在運動中的樂趣可能被成人壓力損害。"},{"en":"Children’s joy of sports means the happiness and excitement children feel when playing sport.","zh":"「children’s joy of sports」意思是兒童玩運動時感到的快樂和興奮。"},{"en":"A child’s joy of sport is clear when they run back to the game smiling after falling.","zh":"孩子跌倒後笑着跑回遊戲中，兒童在運動中的樂趣就很清楚。"},{"en":"If winning becomes the only aim, this joy may disappear.","zh":"如果勝利成為唯一目標，這種樂趣可能消失。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on enjoyment rather than results.","zh":"這個短語集中於享受，而不是結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be destroyed by","meaning":"被……破壞","examples":[{"en":"Children’s enjoyment may be destroyed by adults.","zh":"兒童的享受可能被成人破壞。"},{"en":"To be destroyed by something means to be seriously damaged or ruined because of it.","zh":"「be destroyed by」某事，意思是因它而被嚴重損害或毀掉。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence can be destroyed by constant public humiliation.","zh":"學生信心可以被持續公開羞辱破壞。"},{"en":"If adults shout at children after every mistake, enjoyment may be destroyed.","zh":"如果成人在每次錯誤後都向兒童大叫，樂趣可能被破壞。"},{"en":"The phrase describes severe harm caused by something.","zh":"這個短語描述由某事造成的嚴重傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"want glory through victory","meaning":"透過勝利獲得榮耀","examples":[{"en":"Some adults want glory through victory.","zh":"有些成人想透過勝利獲得榮耀。"},{"en":"To want glory through victory means to seek pride, praise, or status by winning.","zh":"「want glory through victory」意思是透過勝利尋求自豪、讚賞或地位。"},{"en":"A parent may want glory through a child’s competition results.","zh":"父母可能想透過孩子的比賽成績獲得榮耀。"},{"en":"If adults chase glory through victory, children may feel used rather than supported.","zh":"如果成人追求透過勝利得榮耀，兒童可能感到被利用而非被支持。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises making children’s sport serve adult pride.","zh":"這個短語批評把兒童運動變成服務成人自尊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"several studies have shown that","meaning":"多項研究顯示","examples":[{"en":"Several studies have shown that parental pressure makes children leave sport.","zh":"多項研究顯示，父母壓力令兒童離開運動。"},{"en":"Several studies have shown that means more than one research project has found the same thing.","zh":"「several studies have shown that」意思是不止一項研究發現同一件事。"},{"en":"Several studies have shown that sleep affects memory and attention.","zh":"多項研究顯示睡眠影響記憶和注意力。"},{"en":"If several studies point in the same direction, the claim becomes more convincing.","zh":"如果多項研究指向同一方向，主張就變得更有說服力。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces research-based support.","zh":"這個短語引入研究支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"parental pressure","meaning":"父母壓力","examples":[{"en":"Parental pressure is high on the list of reasons why children leave sport.","zh":"父母壓力是兒童離開運動的主要原因之一。"},{"en":"Parental pressure means stress children feel because parents expect too much from them.","zh":"「parental pressure」意思是兒童因父母期望太高而感到的壓力。"},{"en":"A child may feel parental pressure when every match is followed by criticism at home.","zh":"如果每場比賽後回家都被批評，孩子可能感到父母壓力。"},{"en":"If pressure is too strong, sport may feel like duty rather than play.","zh":"如果壓力太大，運動可能感覺像責任而不是玩耍。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pressure coming from parents’ expectations.","zh":"這個短語描述來自父母期望的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be high on the list of reasons","meaning":"是主要原因之一","examples":[{"en":"Parental pressure is high on the list of reasons for leaving sport.","zh":"父母壓力是放棄運動的主要原因之一。"},{"en":"To be high on the list of reasons means to be one of the main explanations.","zh":"「be high on the list of reasons」意思是某事是主要解釋之一。"},{"en":"Stress is high on the list of reasons why students sleep badly.","zh":"壓力是學生睡得差的主要原因之一。"},{"en":"If parental pressure is a main reason, reducing it may help children stay in sport.","zh":"如果父母壓力是主要原因，減少它可能幫助兒童繼續運動。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a cause is important and frequent.","zh":"這個短語顯示原因重要且常見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the presence of mothers and fathers","meaning":"父母在場","examples":[{"en":"The presence of mothers and fathers can affect children’s view of sport.","zh":"父母在場可以影響兒童對運動的看法。"},{"en":"The presence of mothers and fathers means parents being there and watching or taking part.","zh":"「the presence of mothers and fathers」意思是父母在場觀看或參與。"},{"en":"At a school match, the presence of parents can encourage children or make them nervous.","zh":"在學校比賽中，父母在場可以鼓勵兒童，也可能令他們緊張。"},{"en":"If parents watch with pressure, children may feel judged rather than supported.","zh":"如果父母帶着壓力觀看，兒童可能感到被評價而不是被支持。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the impact of parents being physically present.","zh":"這個短語描述父母親身在場的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"consider sport as their own","meaning":"把運動視為自己的事","examples":[{"en":"Children should be able to consider sport as their own.","zh":"兒童應能夠把運動視為自己的事。"},{"en":"To consider sport as their own means to feel that sport belongs to them and their experience.","zh":"「consider sport as their own」意思是感到運動屬於自己和自己的經驗。"},{"en":"Children consider sport their own when they choose games, rules, and teammates.","zh":"當兒童自己選擇遊戲、規則和隊友，他們就是把運動視為自己的事。"},{"en":"If adults dominate sport, children may feel it belongs to coaches and parents instead.","zh":"如果成人主導運動，兒童可能覺得運動屬於教練和父母。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses ownership and personal meaning.","zh":"這個短語強調擁有感和個人意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"master technical difficulties","meaning":"掌握技術難題","examples":[{"en":"Sport helps children master technical difficulties.","zh":"運動幫助兒童掌握技術難題。"},{"en":"To master technical difficulties means to learn how to handle difficult skills or movements.","zh":"「master technical difficulties」意思是學會處理困難技巧或動作。"},{"en":"A young swimmer masters technical difficulties when they learn correct breathing and kicking.","zh":"年輕游泳者學會正確呼吸和踢水時，就是掌握技術難題。"},{"en":"If children practise patiently, difficult techniques become easier.","zh":"如果兒童耐心練習，困難技巧會變得較容易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes overcoming skill-based challenges.","zh":"這個短語描述克服技能上的挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"manage interpersonal relations","meaning":"處理人際關係","examples":[{"en":"Children learn to manage interpersonal relations through sport.","zh":"兒童透過運動學會處理人際關係。"},{"en":"To manage interpersonal relations means to handle relationships with other people.","zh":"「manage interpersonal relations」意思是處理與其他人的關係。"},{"en":"In a team game, children manage interpersonal relations by sharing, listening, and solving arguments.","zh":"在團隊遊戲中，兒童透過分享、聆聽和解決爭執來處理人際關係。"},{"en":"If children learn cooperation in sport, they may use it in school and family life.","zh":"如果兒童在運動中學會合作，他們可能在學校和家庭生活中使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes social relationship skills.","zh":"這個短語描述社交關係技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"experience success and failure","meaning":"經歷成功與失敗","examples":[{"en":"Children need to experience success and failure.","zh":"兒童需要經歷成功與失敗。"},{"en":"To experience success and failure means to go through both winning and losing or doing well and doing badly.","zh":"「experience success and failure」意思是經歷勝利和落敗，或做得好和做得不好。"},{"en":"A student experiences success and failure when some tests go well and others do not.","zh":"當學生有些測驗考得好、有些不理想，他就是經歷成功與失敗。"},{"en":"If children learn from both, they become more resilient.","zh":"如果兒童從兩者中學習，他們會變得更有韌性。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that both positive and negative outcomes teach lessons.","zh":"這個短語顯示正面和負面結果都能教人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"solely to blame","meaning":"完全要負責","examples":[{"en":"Martens says adults are solely to blame for this problem.","zh":"Martens 說成人對這個問題完全要負責。"},{"en":"Solely to blame means completely responsible for something bad.","zh":"「solely to blame」意思是對壞事完全負有責任。"},{"en":"If a teacher gives unclear instructions, students are not solely to blame for mistakes.","zh":"如果老師指示不清，學生不應為錯誤完全負責。"},{"en":"If adults create too much pressure, children should not be blamed for losing joy.","zh":"如果成人製造太多壓力，兒童不應因失去樂趣而受責備。"},{"en":"The phrase places full responsibility on one side.","zh":"這個短語把全部責任放在一方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"become synonymous with","meaning":"變得等同於……","examples":[{"en":"Joy and sadness may become synonymous with victory and defeat.","zh":"快樂和悲傷可能變得等同於勝利和失敗。"},{"en":"To become synonymous with something means to become closely associated with it or almost mean the same thing.","zh":"「become synonymous with」某事，意思是與它緊密相關或幾乎意思相同。"},{"en":"For some students, exams become synonymous with stress.","zh":"對有些學生而言，考試變得等同於壓力。"},{"en":"If sport becomes synonymous with winning, children may fear losing too much.","zh":"如果運動變得等同於勝利，兒童可能太害怕失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase shows one idea being tightly linked to another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個概念與另一個概念緊密連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in a child’s mind","meaning":"在兒童心目中","examples":[{"en":"Victory and defeat may shape sport in a child’s mind.","zh":"勝利與失敗可能在兒童心目中塑造運動。"},{"en":"In a child’s mind means in the way a child thinks, feels, or understands something.","zh":"「in a child’s mind」意思是在兒童思考、感受或理解某事的方式中。"},{"en":"In a child’s mind, a teacher’s small criticism may feel very serious.","zh":"在兒童心目中，老師的小批評可能感覺很嚴重。"},{"en":"If sport means only winning in a child’s mind, enjoyment becomes fragile.","zh":"如果運動在兒童心目中只等於勝利，樂趣就變得脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on a child’s inner understanding.","zh":"這個短語集中於兒童內在理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"victory and defeat","meaning":"勝利與失敗","examples":[{"en":"Adults may make sport seem only about victory and defeat.","zh":"成人可能令運動看似只關乎勝利與失敗。"},{"en":"Victory and defeat mean winning and losing.","zh":"「victory and defeat」意思是勝出和落敗。"},{"en":"A child should learn that a match includes teamwork and effort, not only victory and defeat.","zh":"兒童應學會一場比賽包括團隊合作和努力，而不只是勝利與失敗。"},{"en":"If adults focus only on results, children may stop enjoying practice.","zh":"如果成人只集中於結果，兒童可能停止享受練習。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts two outcomes of competition.","zh":"這個短語對比比賽的兩種結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make the decisions","meaning":"作決定","examples":[{"en":"If children make the decisions, they are more likely to enjoy sport.","zh":"如果兒童作決定，他們更可能享受運動。"},{"en":"To make the decisions means to choose what happens or what action to take.","zh":"「make the decisions」意思是選擇發生甚麼或採取甚麼行動。"},{"en":"Children make the decisions when they choose teams and rules in a playground game.","zh":"當兒童在操場遊戲中選隊伍和規則，他們就是作決定。"},{"en":"If children make decisions, they feel more ownership and responsibility.","zh":"如果兒童作決定，他們會更有擁有感和責任感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active control.","zh":"這個短語描述主動控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"ensure that","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Allowing children to decide ensures that they enjoy sport.","zh":"讓兒童作決定確保他們享受運動。"},{"en":"To ensure that means to make certain that something happens.","zh":"「ensure that」意思是確保某事發生。"},{"en":"A teacher checks instructions to ensure that students understand the task.","zh":"老師檢查指示，以確保學生明白任務。"},{"en":"If adults protect children’s choice, they help ensure enjoyment remains central.","zh":"如果成人保護兒童選擇權，他們有助確保樂趣仍然是核心。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses making an outcome more certain.","zh":"這個短語表達令結果更確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"enjoy sport as children","meaning":"以兒童身份享受運動","examples":[{"en":"Children should enjoy sport as children.","zh":"兒童應以兒童身份享受運動。"},{"en":"To enjoy sport as children means to experience sport in a way suitable for childhood, with play, fun, and discovery.","zh":"「enjoy sport as children」意思是以適合童年的方式體驗運動，包括玩耍、樂趣和探索。"},{"en":"Children enjoy sport as children when they laugh, experiment, and play with friends.","zh":"當兒童笑着、嘗試和與朋友玩耍，他們就是以兒童身份享受運動。"},{"en":"If adults make sport too serious, children may be pushed into adult expectations.","zh":"如果成人把運動變得太嚴肅，兒童可能被推進成人期望。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds adults not to treat children like miniature professionals.","zh":"這個短語提醒成人不要把兒童當成小型專業運動員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be relaxed about","meaning":"對……感到輕鬆","examples":[{"en":"Children should be relaxed about their development.","zh":"兒童應對自己的發展感到輕鬆。"},{"en":"To be relaxed about something means not to feel too worried, pressured, or tense about it.","zh":"「be relaxed about」某事，意思是對它不感到太擔心、壓迫或緊張。"},{"en":"Parents should be relaxed about small mistakes when children are learning a new sport.","zh":"孩子學新運動時，父母應對小錯誤感到放鬆。"},{"en":"If children feel relaxed, they may try new skills more bravely.","zh":"如果兒童感到輕鬆，他們可能更勇敢嘗試新技能。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests calm acceptance rather than pressure.","zh":"這個短語暗示冷靜接納，而不是壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"development as human beings","meaning":"作為人的發展","examples":[{"en":"Sport supports children’s development as human beings.","zh":"運動支持兒童作為人的發展。"},{"en":"Development as human beings means growth in character, emotions, relationships, and self-understanding.","zh":"「development as human beings」意思是性格、情緒、關係和自我理解方面的成長。"},{"en":"A school should support students’ development as human beings, not only their exam scores.","zh":"學校應支持學生作為人的發展，而不只是考試分數。"},{"en":"If sport teaches courage and cooperation, it helps children grow beyond physical skill.","zh":"如果運動教授勇氣和合作，它就幫助兒童在身體技能以外成長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes whole-person development.","zh":"這個短語描述全人發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"need only observe","meaning":"只需觀察","examples":[{"en":"We need only observe playground games to understand children’s instincts.","zh":"我們只需觀察操場遊戲，就能理解兒童的本能。"},{"en":"Need only observe means simply observing is enough to see or understand something.","zh":"「need only observe」意思是單靠觀察已足以看見或理解某事。"},{"en":"A teacher need only observe group work to see who listens and who dominates.","zh":"老師只需觀察小組合作，就能看出誰聆聽、誰主導。"},{"en":"If children naturally run and chase, observation shows their need for physical activity.","zh":"如果兒童自然地奔跑和追逐，觀察就顯示他們對體能活動的需要。"},{"en":"The phrase says evidence is visible without complicated testing.","zh":"這個短語表示證據不用複雜測試也可看見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"school playground","meaning":"學校操場","examples":[{"en":"Children organise games in a school playground.","zh":"兒童在學校操場組織遊戲。"},{"en":"A school playground is an outdoor or indoor area where children play during breaks.","zh":"「school playground」是兒童在小息期間玩耍的戶外或室內區域。"},{"en":"During recess, a school playground may become a place for football, chasing games, and conversation.","zh":"小息時，學校操場可能成為足球、追逐遊戲和聊天的地方。"},{"en":"If the playground is too small, children have fewer chances to move freely.","zh":"如果操場太小，兒童自由活動的機會就較少。"},{"en":"The phrase names a familiar place for children’s spontaneous play.","zh":"這個短語指出兒童自發玩耍的熟悉地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"improvised playing field","meaning":"臨時遊戲場地","examples":[{"en":"Children can create games on an improvised playing field.","zh":"兒童可以在臨時遊戲場地上創造遊戲。"},{"en":"An improvised playing field is a temporary play space created from whatever area is available.","zh":"「improvised playing field」是由任何可用空間臨時創造出來的遊戲場地。"},{"en":"Children may turn an empty car park into an improvised playing field after school.","zh":"放學後，兒童可能把空停車場變成臨時遊戲場地。"},{"en":"If formal spaces are lacking, children often adapt ordinary spaces for games.","zh":"如果缺乏正式空間，兒童常把普通空間改作遊戲用途。"},{"en":"The phrase shows creativity in using space.","zh":"這個短語顯示使用空間的創意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"genetic traces","meaning":"遺傳痕跡","examples":[{"en":"Children show genetic traces of the hunter instinct.","zh":"兒童顯示獵人本能的遺傳痕跡。"},{"en":"Genetic traces are inherited signs or remains of older human tendencies.","zh":"「genetic traces」是較古老人類傾向遺傳下來的跡象或殘留。"},{"en":"A child’s urge to run, chase, and explore may be seen as genetic traces of survival behaviour.","zh":"兒童想奔跑、追逐和探索的衝動，可能被視為生存行為的遺傳痕跡。"},{"en":"If certain behaviours are rooted in human history, they may appear naturally in play.","zh":"如果某些行為植根於人類歷史，它們可能自然出現在遊戲中。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests deep biological roots.","zh":"這個短語暗示深層生物根源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"hunter instinct","meaning":"獵人本能","examples":[{"en":"The hunter instinct naturally leads children to physical activity.","zh":"獵人本能自然引導兒童進行體能活動。"},{"en":"Hunter instinct means an inherited drive to chase, move, explore, and respond physically.","zh":"「hunter instinct」意思是追逐、移動、探索和作出身體反應的遺傳驅動力。"},{"en":"Children playing chasing games may be expressing a simple form of hunter instinct.","zh":"兒童玩追逐遊戲時，可能是在表達簡單形式的獵人本能。"},{"en":"If this instinct is channelled through sport, children can use energy safely.","zh":"如果這種本能透過運動被引導，兒童可以安全地使用能量。"},{"en":"The phrase links play with older human survival behaviour.","zh":"這個短語把遊戲與古老人類生存行為連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"naturally lead someone to","meaning":"自然引導某人去……","examples":[{"en":"The hunter instinct naturally leads children to physical activity.","zh":"獵人本能自然引導兒童去體能活動。"},{"en":"To naturally lead someone to something means to make them move toward it without force.","zh":"「naturally lead someone to」某事，意思是在沒有強迫下使某人走向它。"},{"en":"Curiosity naturally leads children to ask questions in class.","zh":"好奇心自然引導兒童在課堂上提問。"},{"en":"If movement feels natural, children do not need much persuasion to be active.","zh":"如果活動身體感覺自然，兒童不需要太多說服也會活躍。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an automatic or instinctive direction.","zh":"這個短語描述自動或本能的方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"physical activity","meaning":"體能活動","examples":[{"en":"Sport leads children to physical activity.","zh":"運動引導兒童進行體能活動。"},{"en":"Physical activity means movement of the body that uses energy, such as running, jumping, or swimming.","zh":"「physical activity」意思是使用能量的身體活動，例如跑步、跳躍或游泳。"},{"en":"Walking to school is a simple form of physical activity.","zh":"步行上學是一種簡單體能活動。"},{"en":"If children get enough physical activity, they may build strength, coordination, and confidence.","zh":"如果兒童有足夠體能活動，他們可能建立力量、協調和信心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active body movement.","zh":"這個短語描述活躍身體移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"identify something as","meaning":"把……視為","examples":[{"en":"Children identify sport as a means of release.","zh":"兒童把運動視為一種釋放情緒的方法。"},{"en":"To identify something as something means to recognise or define it in that way.","zh":"「identify something as」某物，意思是以該方式辨認或定義它。"},{"en":"A teacher may identify tiredness as the reason for a student’s poor focus.","zh":"老師可能把疲倦視為學生專注力差的原因。"},{"en":"If children see sport as release, they use it to express energy and emotion.","zh":"如果兒童把運動視為釋放，他們會用它表達能量和情緒。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how someone understands something.","zh":"這個短語解釋某人如何理解某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a means of release","meaning":"釋放情緒的方法","examples":[{"en":"Sport is a means of release for children.","zh":"運動是兒童釋放情緒的方法。"},{"en":"A means of release is a way to let out energy, stress, or emotion.","zh":"「a means of release」是釋放能量、壓力或情緒的方法。"},{"en":"Drawing can be a means of release for a child who finds speaking difficult.","zh":"對不善表達的孩子而言，繪畫可以是釋放情緒的方法。"},{"en":"If children run and play, they may release tension built up during school.","zh":"如果兒童奔跑和玩耍，他們可以釋放在學校累積的緊張。"},{"en":"The phrase shows sport as emotional relief.","zh":"這個短語把運動呈現為情緒舒緩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a form of self-expression","meaning":"自我表達的形式","examples":[{"en":"Sport is also a form of self-expression.","zh":"運動也是自我表達的形式。"},{"en":"A form of self-expression is a way for people to show feelings, identity, or personality.","zh":"「a form of self-expression」是人們展現感受、身份或個性的方式。"},{"en":"Dance can be a form of self-expression for children who love music.","zh":"對喜歡音樂的兒童而言，舞蹈可以是自我表達的形式。"},{"en":"If children choose how to move and play, sport becomes personal and meaningful.","zh":"如果兒童選擇如何活動和玩耍，運動就變得個人化且有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase shows sport as more than exercise.","zh":"這個短語顯示運動不只是鍛煉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"act as a route to","meaning":"作為通往……的途徑","examples":[{"en":"Sport acts as a route to self-discovery.","zh":"運動作為通往自我探索的途徑。"},{"en":"To act as a route to something means to provide a path or way toward it.","zh":"「act as a route to」某事，意思是提供通往它的道路或方式。"},{"en":"Reading biographies can act as a route to understanding different careers.","zh":"閱讀傳記可以作為理解不同職業的途徑。"},{"en":"If sport lets children test courage and limits, it becomes a path to knowing themselves.","zh":"如果運動讓兒童測試勇氣和極限，它就成為認識自己的途徑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a means of reaching a deeper result.","zh":"這個短語描述達到更深結果的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"self-discovery","meaning":"自我探索","examples":[{"en":"Sport gives children a route to self-discovery.","zh":"運動給兒童一條通往自我探索的途徑。"},{"en":"Self-discovery means learning more about one’s own abilities, feelings, limits, and identity.","zh":"「self-discovery」意思是更加了解自己的能力、感受、極限和身份。"},{"en":"A student may experience self-discovery when they lead a group for the first time.","zh":"學生第一次帶領小組時，可能經歷自我探索。"},{"en":"If children try difficult movements, they learn what they fear and what they can overcome.","zh":"如果兒童嘗試困難動作，他們會了解自己害怕甚麼，以及能克服甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning about oneself.","zh":"這個短語描述認識自己。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"know their limits","meaning":"了解自己的極限","examples":[{"en":"Sport gives children the opportunity to know their limits.","zh":"運動給兒童了解自己極限的機會。"},{"en":"To know their limits means to understand what they can and cannot do safely or effectively.","zh":"「know their limits」意思是理解自己能安全或有效做到甚麼，以及不能做到甚麼。"},{"en":"A runner knows their limits when they learn when to slow down and rest.","zh":"跑手知道何時要放慢和休息，就是了解自己的極限。"},{"en":"If children know their limits, they can challenge themselves without unnecessary danger.","zh":"如果兒童了解自己的極限，他們可以挑戰自己而避免不必要危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes realistic self-awareness.","zh":"這個短語描述現實的自我認知。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"acquire tools","meaning":"掌握工具","examples":[{"en":"Children acquire tools that help them surpass their limits.","zh":"兒童掌握幫助他們超越極限的工具。"},{"en":"To acquire tools means to gain skills, methods, or resources that help solve problems.","zh":"「acquire tools」意思是獲得幫助解決問題的技能、方法或資源。"},{"en":"Students acquire tools for writing when they learn planning, examples, and proofreading.","zh":"學生學會規劃、例子和校對時，就是掌握寫作工具。"},{"en":"If children learn breathing, balance, and teamwork, they gain tools for sport and life.","zh":"如果兒童學會呼吸、平衡和團隊合作，他們就獲得運動和生活工具。"},{"en":"The phrase often means learning practical abilities, not only getting physical objects.","zh":"這個短語常指學習實用能力，而不只是取得實體物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"surpass their limits","meaning":"超越自己的極限","examples":[{"en":"Sport can help children surpass their limits.","zh":"運動可以幫助兒童超越自己的極限。"},{"en":"To surpass their limits means to go beyond what they thought they could do.","zh":"「surpass their limits」意思是超過他們以為自己能做到的程度。"},{"en":"A shy student may surpass their limits by speaking in front of the class.","zh":"害羞學生在全班面前說話時，可能超越自己的極限。"},{"en":"If children practise safely, they may achieve more than they expected.","zh":"如果兒童安全地練習，他們可能做到比預期更多。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growth beyond previous ability.","zh":"這個短語描述超越以往能力的成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a source of learning, progress and pleasure","meaning":"學習、進步和樂趣的來源","examples":[{"en":"Playing sport is a source of learning, progress and pleasure.","zh":"玩運動是學習、進步和樂趣的來源。"},{"en":"A source of learning, progress and pleasure is something that teaches, improves, and brings enjoyment.","zh":"「a source of learning, progress and pleasure」是能教人、令人進步並帶來享受的事物。"},{"en":"Reading can be a source of learning, progress and pleasure when students choose books they like.","zh":"當學生選擇自己喜歡的書，閱讀可以是學習、進步和樂趣的來源。"},{"en":"If sport offers all three, children are more likely to keep playing.","zh":"如果運動提供三者，兒童更可能繼續玩。"},{"en":"The phrase presents sport as educational, developmental, and enjoyable.","zh":"這個短語把運動呈現為教育性、發展性和令人愉快的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"enrich life","meaning":"豐富生活","examples":[{"en":"Sport is an additional way of enriching life.","zh":"運動是豐富生活的另一種方式。"},{"en":"To enrich life means to make life fuller, more meaningful, or more enjoyable.","zh":"「enrich life」意思是令生活更充實、更有意義或更愉快。"},{"en":"Music, friendship, travel, and reading can enrich life beyond work and study.","zh":"音樂、友誼、旅遊和閱讀可以在工作和學習以外豐富生活。"},{"en":"If sport gives children confidence and friendship, it enriches their lives.","zh":"如果運動給兒童信心和友誼，它就豐富他們的生活。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adding value to everyday living.","zh":"這個短語描述為日常生活增加價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的詞語完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill in missing information in a shortened version of the text.","zh":"「complete the summary」意思是在文本的簡短版本中填入缺失資料。"},{"en":"In a reading exam, students complete a summary by finding exact words in the passage.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生透過在文章中找出原字完成摘要。"},{"en":"If students understand the main ideas, they can choose missing words more accurately.","zh":"如果學生理解主要意思，就能更準確選出缺失詞語。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"using no more than two words","meaning":"使用不多於兩個字詞","examples":[{"en":"Students must answer using no more than two words from the passage.","zh":"學生必須使用文章中不多於兩個字詞作答。"},{"en":"Using no more than two words means the answer must contain one or two words only.","zh":"「using no more than two words」意思是答案只能包含一個或兩個詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “parental pressure”, it follows the rule because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “parental pressure”，它符合規則，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"If students write three words, the answer may be marked wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"如果學生寫三個詞，即使意思正確，答案也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"define A as B","meaning":"把A定義為B","examples":[{"en":"Marte and Notarnicola define children’s sporting games as activities of freedom.","zh":"Marte 和 Notarnicola 把兒童運動遊戲定義為自由活動。"},{"en":"To define A as B means to explain that A should be understood as B.","zh":"「define A as B」意思是解釋 A 應被理解為 B。"},{"en":"A teacher may define plagiarism as using someone else’s work without credit.","zh":"老師可能把抄襲定義為使用他人作品而不註明來源。"},{"en":"If writers define sport as freedom, readers understand their main viewpoint.","zh":"如果作者把運動定義為自由，讀者就明白其主要觀點。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a clear meaning or interpretation.","zh":"這個短語引入清楚意思或詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"spontaneous sporting games","meaning":"自發性的運動遊戲","examples":[{"en":"The summary refers to the spontaneous sporting games of children.","zh":"摘要提到兒童自發性的運動遊戲。"},{"en":"Spontaneous sporting games are physical games children create or play naturally without strict adult planning.","zh":"「spontaneous sporting games」是兒童在沒有嚴格成人安排下自然創造或玩的體能遊戲。"},{"en":"A group of children inventing a running game in the playground are playing spontaneous sporting games.","zh":"一群孩子在操場自創跑步遊戲，就是在玩自發性的運動遊戲。"},{"en":"If such games are allowed, children learn rules and cooperation by doing.","zh":"如果這類遊戲被允許，兒童會透過實踐學習規則和合作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes free, child-led physical play.","zh":"這個短語描述自由、由兒童主導的體能玩耍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"lose their autonomy","meaning":"失去自主權","examples":[{"en":"Children lose their autonomy when adults decide everything for them.","zh":"當成人替兒童決定一切，他們就失去自主權。"},{"en":"To lose their autonomy means to lose the ability or freedom to make their own choices.","zh":"「lose their autonomy」意思是失去自己作選擇的能力或自由。"},{"en":"Students lose autonomy if a teacher chooses every book, topic, and method for them.","zh":"如果老師為學生選定每本書、每個題目和每種方法，學生就失去自主。"},{"en":"If children lose autonomy in sport, they may feel the activity no longer belongs to them.","zh":"如果兒童在運動中失去自主，他們可能覺得活動不再屬於自己。"},{"en":"The phrase describes loss of independence.","zh":"這個短語描述失去獨立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a first imbalance occurs because","meaning":"第一種失衡出現，是因為……","examples":[{"en":"A first imbalance occurs because sports spaces are often inaccessible.","zh":"第一種失衡出現，是因為運動空間往往難以使用。"},{"en":"A first imbalance occurs because introduces the first cause of an uneven situation.","zh":"「a first imbalance occurs because」用來引出不平衡情況的第一個原因。"},{"en":"A first imbalance occurs because some students have quiet study rooms while others do not.","zh":"第一種失衡出現，是因為有些學生有安靜自修室，而另一些沒有。"},{"en":"If facilities are far away or enclosed, children cannot access sport freely.","zh":"如果設施遙遠或被圍封，兒童就不能自由接觸運動。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the first reason for a problem.","zh":"這個短語解釋問題的第一個原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"out of the city","meaning":"在城市之外","examples":[{"en":"Sports grounds are often out of the city.","zh":"運動場常在城市之外。"},{"en":"Out of the city means outside the main urban area or away from the centre.","zh":"「out of the city」意思是在主要市區之外或遠離市中心。"},{"en":"A family may travel out of the city to find cheaper sports facilities.","zh":"家庭可能到城市之外尋找較便宜的運動設施。"},{"en":"If play spaces are out of the city, children need transport to reach them.","zh":"如果遊戲空間在城市之外，兒童需要交通工具才能到達。"},{"en":"The phrase describes distance from everyday urban life.","zh":"這個短語描述與日常城市生活的距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"limited number of","meaning":"有限數量的……","examples":[{"en":"There are a limited number of open recreational areas.","zh":"開放康樂區數量有限。"},{"en":"A limited number of something means only a small amount is available.","zh":"「limited number of」某物，意思是可用數量很少。"},{"en":"A school may have a limited number of computers for students to borrow.","zh":"學校可能有有限數量的電腦供學生借用。"},{"en":"If play areas are limited, many children must share too little space.","zh":"如果遊戲區有限，許多兒童就要共用太少空間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shortage.","zh":"這個短語描述短缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"open recreational areas","meaning":"開放康樂區","examples":[{"en":"Children need open recreational areas for spontaneous play.","zh":"兒童需要開放康樂區進行自發玩耍。"},{"en":"Open recreational areas are accessible spaces where people can relax, play, or exercise freely.","zh":"「open recreational areas」是人們可自由放鬆、玩耍或運動的可進入空間。"},{"en":"A public park with open grass is an open recreational area for families.","zh":"有開放草地的公園是家庭使用的開放康樂區。"},{"en":"If open areas are available, children can play without booking a club or lesson.","zh":"如果有開放區域，兒童不用預約球會或課堂也能玩。"},{"en":"The phrase describes free public space for leisure.","zh":"這個短語描述供休閒使用的自由公共空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"play spontaneously","meaning":"自發地玩耍","examples":[{"en":"Children should have places where they can play spontaneously.","zh":"兒童應有可以自發地玩耍的地方。"},{"en":"To play spontaneously means to start and shape games naturally without fixed adult plans.","zh":"「play spontaneously」意思是沒有固定成人計劃下自然開始並塑造遊戲。"},{"en":"Children play spontaneously when they turn a few stones into goalposts.","zh":"當兒童把幾塊石頭變成龍門，他們就是自發地玩耍。"},{"en":"If play is spontaneous, children practise imagination and decision-making.","zh":"如果玩耍是自發的，兒童會練習想像力和決策。"},{"en":"The phrase describes natural, child-led play.","zh":"這個短語描述自然、兒童主導的玩耍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"participate in","meaning":"參與","examples":[{"en":"Young children may participate in only one specific activity.","zh":"年幼兒童可能只參與一項特定活動。"},{"en":"To participate in something means to take part in it.","zh":"「participate in」某事，意思是參加它。"},{"en":"Students participate in sports day by running, cheering, or helping teachers.","zh":"學生可以透過跑步、打氣或幫老師來參與運動會。"},{"en":"If children participate in only one activity, their experience may become narrow.","zh":"如果兒童只參與一項活動，其經驗可能變得狹窄。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active involvement.","zh":"這個短語描述主動參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"specific activity","meaning":"特定活動","examples":[{"en":"Early training often focuses on one specific activity.","zh":"早期訓練常集中於一項特定活動。"},{"en":"A specific activity is one clearly defined task, game, or sport.","zh":"「specific activity」是一項清楚界定的任務、遊戲或運動。"},{"en":"A child may practise one specific activity, such as skating jumps, every week.","zh":"兒童可能每星期練習一項特定活動，例如溜冰跳躍。"},{"en":"If training is too specific, children may not develop wider movement skills.","zh":"如果訓練太特定，兒童可能無法發展更廣泛動作技能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a narrow, clearly chosen activity.","zh":"這個短語描述狹窄而清楚選定的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"attitudes of their parents","meaning":"父母的態度","examples":[{"en":"The attitudes of their parents can affect whether children continue sport.","zh":"父母的態度可以影響兒童是否繼續參與運動。"},{"en":"Attitudes of their parents means the way parents think, feel, and behave toward something.","zh":"「attitudes of their parents」意思是父母對某事的想法、感受和行為方式。"},{"en":"A child may enjoy music more if the attitudes of their parents are calm and supportive.","zh":"如果父母態度冷靜而支持，孩子可能更享受音樂。"},{"en":"If parents see sport only as competition, children may feel heavy pressure.","zh":"如果父母只把運動視為競爭，兒童可能感到沉重壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that parents’ mindset matters.","zh":"這個短語顯示父母心態很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"exert pressure on","meaning":"對……施加壓力","examples":[{"en":"Parents may exert pressure on children to win.","zh":"父母可能對兒童施加勝利壓力。"},{"en":"To exert pressure on someone means to push them strongly to do or achieve something.","zh":"「exert pressure on」某人，意思是強烈推動他們做某事或達成某事。"},{"en":"Parents exert pressure on students when they demand perfect marks every time.","zh":"父母每次都要求滿分時，就是對學生施加壓力。"},{"en":"If children feel pressured to win, sport may become stressful.","zh":"如果兒童感到被迫勝利，運動可能變得有壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes applying emotional or social force.","zh":"這個短語描述施加情緒或社會力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Parents may push children to win rather than to enjoy sport.","zh":"父母可能推動兒童去勝利，而不是享受運動。"},{"en":"Rather than shows contrast: not one thing, but another thing instead.","zh":"「rather than」顯示對比：不是一件事，而是另一件事。"},{"en":"A teacher may encourage students to understand mistakes rather than fear them.","zh":"老師可能鼓勵學生理解錯誤，而不是害怕錯誤。"},{"en":"If the aim is enjoyment rather than victory, children may feel freer.","zh":"如果目標是享受而不是勝利，兒童可能感到更自由。"},{"en":"The phrase helps separate the wrong focus from the better focus.","zh":"這個短語幫助分開錯誤焦點和更好焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生為每題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choose the correct letter means select the letter that matches the right answer option.","zh":"「choose the correct letter」意思是選出與正確答案選項相符的字母。"},{"en":"If option C matches the passage, students should write C on the answer sheet.","zh":"如果 C 選項符合文章，學生應在答題紙上寫 C。"},{"en":"If students choose without checking the text, they may select a distractor.","zh":"如果學生不核對文本就選擇，可能選到干擾選項。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard multiple-choice instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準多項選擇指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"children’s expression of freedom","meaning":"兒童對自由的表現","examples":[{"en":"The question asks why children’s expression of freedom is important.","zh":"題目問兒童對自由的表現為何重要。"},{"en":"Children’s expression of freedom means the way children show independence through choices and play.","zh":"「children’s expression of freedom」意思是兒童透過選擇和玩耍展示獨立的方式。"},{"en":"A child expresses freedom when they invent rules for a game with friends.","zh":"當孩子與朋友自創遊戲規則，他就是表現自由。"},{"en":"If children can express freedom, they feel sport belongs to them.","zh":"如果兒童能表現自由，他們會覺得運動屬於自己。"},{"en":"The phrase connects freedom with visible action.","zh":"這個短語把自由與可見行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"put someone in charge of","meaning":"讓某人掌管","examples":[{"en":"Freedom puts children in charge of what they do.","zh":"自由讓兒童掌管自己做甚麼。"},{"en":"To put someone in charge of something means to give them control or responsibility for it.","zh":"「put someone in charge of」某事，意思是給某人控制權或責任。"},{"en":"A teacher may put students in charge of organising a class game.","zh":"老師可能讓學生掌管組織班內遊戲。"},{"en":"If children are in charge of play, they practise planning and leadership.","zh":"如果兒童掌管玩耍，他們會練習規劃和領導。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving authority.","zh":"這個短語描述給予權力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"what they do and when they do it","meaning":"他們做甚麼以及何時做","examples":[{"en":"Children should control what they do and when they do it.","zh":"兒童應控制他們做甚麼以及何時做。"},{"en":"What they do and when they do it means both the activity chosen and the timing of it.","zh":"「what they do and when they do it」意思是所選活動和其時間安排。"},{"en":"During free play, children decide what they do and when they do it without a timetable.","zh":"在自由玩耍中，兒童不用時間表也能決定做甚麼以及何時做。"},{"en":"If adults decide both activity and timing, children’s autonomy becomes limited.","zh":"如果成人同時決定活動和時間，兒童自主就變得有限。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses control over content and time.","zh":"這個短語強調對內容和時間的控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"relieve someone from","meaning":"免除某人……","examples":[{"en":"One option says this freedom relieves parents from transporting children.","zh":"其中一個選項說這種自由免除父母接送子女的責任。"},{"en":"To relieve someone from something means to free them from a duty, burden, or responsibility.","zh":"「relieve someone from」某事，意思是使某人免於某責任、負擔或職責。"},{"en":"A school bus can relieve parents from driving children to school every morning.","zh":"校巴可以免除父母每天早上接送子女上學。"},{"en":"If children can play near home, parents may have less transport pressure.","zh":"如果兒童可以在家附近玩耍，父母可能有較少接送壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes removing a burden.","zh":"這個短語描述移除負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"transport their children","meaning":"接送子女","examples":[{"en":"Parents often transport their children to sports activities.","zh":"父母常接送子女去運動活動。"},{"en":"To transport their children means to take them from one place to another, usually by car or public transport.","zh":"「transport their children」意思是把子女由一個地方帶到另一個地方，通常用車或公共交通。"},{"en":"Parents may transport their children to football practice after work.","zh":"父母可能下班後接送子女去足球練習。"},{"en":"If sports grounds are far away, transport becomes part of children’s sport.","zh":"如果運動場很遠，交通接送就成為兒童運動的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the practical travel burden on parents.","zh":"這個短語描述父母實際交通負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"develop this freedom","meaning":"發展這種自由","examples":[{"en":"The question asks how adults can help children develop this freedom.","zh":"題目問成人如何幫助兒童發展這種自由。"},{"en":"To develop this freedom means to build and strengthen children’s ability to choose and organise play.","zh":"「develop this freedom」意思是建立並加強兒童選擇和組織遊戲的能力。"},{"en":"Schools develop this freedom by giving children open spaces and time to invent games.","zh":"學校透過給兒童開放空間和時間自創遊戲來發展這種自由。"},{"en":"If freedom is supported safely, children learn independence without being abandoned.","zh":"如果自由被安全地支持，兒童會學會獨立，而不是被放任。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growing autonomy through practice.","zh":"這個短語描述透過練習成長的自主。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a range of different sports","meaning":"一系列不同運動","examples":[{"en":"Children benefit from a range of different sports.","zh":"兒童受惠於一系列不同運動。"},{"en":"A range of different sports means several varied sports rather than only one.","zh":"「a range of different sports」意思是幾種不同運動，而不是只有一種。"},{"en":"A child may try swimming, football, cycling, and gymnastics in one year.","zh":"兒童可能一年內嘗試游泳、足球、踏單車和體操。"},{"en":"If children try a range of sports, they develop more balanced physical skills.","zh":"如果兒童嘗試一系列運動，他們會發展更均衡的身體技能。"},{"en":"The phrase encourages variety.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"sporting tuition","meaning":"運動教學","examples":[{"en":"One option refers to sporting tuition for pre-school children.","zh":"其中一個選項提到學前兒童的運動教學。"},{"en":"Sporting tuition means instruction or coaching in sport.","zh":"「sporting tuition」意思是運動方面的指導或教練教學。"},{"en":"A child may receive sporting tuition in swimming, tennis, or gymnastics.","zh":"兒童可能接受游泳、網球或體操的運動教學。"},{"en":"If sporting tuition is playful and varied, it may support rather than limit development.","zh":"如果運動教學生動而多元，它可能支持而不是限制發展。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to taught sport, not free play.","zh":"這個短語指被教授的運動，而不是自由玩耍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"continue with sport","meaning":"繼續參與運動","examples":[{"en":"Adults should encourage young children to continue with sport.","zh":"成人應鼓勵年幼兒童繼續參與運動。"},{"en":"To continue with sport means to keep participating in physical activities over time.","zh":"「continue with sport」意思是長期保持參與體能活動。"},{"en":"A child may continue with sport if practices feel friendly and enjoyable.","zh":"如果練習感覺友善而有趣，兒童可能繼續參與運動。"},{"en":"If children face too much pressure, they may stop instead of continuing.","zh":"如果兒童面對太多壓力，他們可能停止而不是繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long-term participation.","zh":"這個短語描述長期參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"accurate feedback","meaning":"準確回饋","examples":[{"en":"Children may need encouragement more than accurate feedback.","zh":"兒童可能更需要鼓勵，而不是準確回饋。"},{"en":"Accurate feedback is correct and specific information about performance.","zh":"「accurate feedback」是關於表現的正確而具體資料。"},{"en":"A coach gives accurate feedback when they say exactly how a child’s kick can improve.","zh":"當教練清楚指出孩子踢球可如何改善，就是給出準確回饋。"},{"en":"If feedback is accurate but too harsh, young children may still feel hurt.","zh":"如果回饋準確但太嚴厲，年幼兒童仍可能受傷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes useful correction, but tone matters.","zh":"這個短語描述有用修正，但語氣很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"mix socially with their peers","meaning":"與同輩社交","examples":[{"en":"Children should have opportunities to mix socially with their peers.","zh":"兒童應有機會與同輩社交。"},{"en":"To mix socially with their peers means to spend time interacting with children of a similar age.","zh":"「mix socially with their peers」意思是花時間與相近年齡的兒童互動。"},{"en":"Children mix socially with peers when they chat and play together during recess.","zh":"兒童在小息時一起聊天和玩耍，就是與同輩社交。"},{"en":"If sport allows social mixing, children build friendships as well as skills.","zh":"如果運動容許社交混合，兒童除了技能，也會建立友誼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes social contact with other children.","zh":"這個短語描述與其他兒童的社交接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the author believes that","meaning":"作者認為","examples":[{"en":"The final question asks what the author believes about children’s sport.","zh":"最後一題問作者認為兒童運動是怎樣的。"},{"en":"The author believes that introduces the writer’s opinion or viewpoint.","zh":"「the author believes that」引出作者的意見或觀點。"},{"en":"The author believes that homework should help learning, not simply fill time.","zh":"作者認為功課應幫助學習，而不是單純填滿時間。"},{"en":"If a reading question asks this, students should look for the writer’s attitude.","zh":"如果閱讀題這樣問，學生應尋找作者態度。"},{"en":"The phrase signals opinion rather than a simple fact.","zh":"這個短語表示意見，而不是簡單事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"an important part of children’s development","meaning":"兒童發展的重要部分","examples":[{"en":"Playing sport is an important part of children’s development.","zh":"玩運動是兒童發展的重要部分。"},{"en":"An important part of children’s development is something that helps children grow physically, socially, emotionally, or mentally.","zh":"「an important part of children’s development」是幫助兒童在身體、社交、情緒或心智方面成長的事物。"},{"en":"Friendship is an important part of children’s development because it teaches sharing and trust.","zh":"友誼是兒童發展的重要部分，因為它教分享和信任。"},{"en":"If sport builds confidence and cooperation, it supports children’s growth beyond fitness.","zh":"如果運動建立信心和合作，它就支持兒童在體能以外的成長。"},{"en":"The phrase shows sport as part of whole-child development.","zh":"這個短語顯示運動是全人發展的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"psychologically and physiologically damaged","meaning":"在心理和生理上受損","examples":[{"en":"One option suggests that children can be psychologically and physiologically damaged by sport.","zh":"其中一個選項暗示兒童可能因運動而在心理和生理上受損。"},{"en":"Psychologically and physiologically damaged means harmed in both mind and body.","zh":"「psychologically and physiologically damaged」意思是在心理和身體兩方面受到傷害。"},{"en":"A child may be psychologically damaged by constant fear and physiologically damaged by overtraining.","zh":"兒童可能因持續恐懼而心理受損，因過度訓練而生理受損。"},{"en":"If sport is too intense and critical, it can affect confidence, mood, and physical health.","zh":"如果運動太密集又充滿批評，它可以影響信心、情緒和身體健康。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious harm on two levels.","zh":"這個短語描述兩個層面的嚴重傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 77 - Kids and Sport.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 78":[{"front":"on the same planet","meaning":"生活在同一個世界；看法是否完全脫節","examples":[{"en":"The title asks whether the two reporters are on the same planet.","zh":"標題問這兩名記者是否生活在同一個世界。"},{"en":"If two people are not on the same planet, their views are so different that they seem to live in completely different realities.","zh":"如果兩個人好像不在同一個世界，他們的看法差異大得像活在完全不同的現實中。"},{"en":"After reading two opposite reviews of the same film, a student may ask whether the reviewers are on the same planet.","zh":"讀完兩篇對同一部電影完全相反的影評後，學生可能會問這些影評人是否生活在同一個世界。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when people interpret the same facts in totally different ways.","zh":"這個短語常用於人們對同一事實有完全不同解讀時。"},{"en":"It suggests not just disagreement, but a deep gap in worldview.","zh":"它暗示的不只是不同意，而是世界觀上的深層差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an essay by","meaning":"由……撰寫的文章","examples":[{"en":"This passage is an essay by Dr David Suzuki.","zh":"這篇文章是由 David Suzuki 博士撰寫的文章。"},{"en":"An essay by someone is a written piece created by that person.","zh":"由某人撰寫的文章，是指由那個人創作的文字作品。"},{"en":"A class may read an essay by a scientist to understand climate change.","zh":"班級可能閱讀由科學家撰寫的文章，以理解氣候變化。"},{"en":"Naming the writer helps readers judge the viewpoint and background behind the argument.","zh":"說明作者有助讀者判斷論點背後的觀點和背景。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the author of a written text.","zh":"這個短語指出文章作者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"scientist, educator and environmentalist","meaning":"科學家、教育家及環保人士","examples":[{"en":"Dr David Suzuki is described as a scientist, educator and environmentalist.","zh":"David Suzuki 博士被描述為科學家、教育家及環保人士。"},{"en":"A scientist, educator and environmentalist is someone who studies science, teaches others and works to protect the environment.","zh":"科學家、教育家及環保人士，是指研究科學、教育他人並致力保護環境的人。"},{"en":"A public speaker may be introduced as a scientist, educator and environmentalist before giving a talk on pollution.","zh":"一位講者在發表污染講座前，可能被介紹為科學家、教育家及環保人士。"},{"en":"These roles suggest that the person speaks with scientific knowledge and public concern.","zh":"這些身份暗示此人既有科學知識，也有公共關懷。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a person’s professional identity and values.","zh":"這個短語交代一個人的專業身份和價值取向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a number of","meaning":"一些；若干","examples":[{"en":"A number of books and programmes have challenged warnings about the environment.","zh":"一些書籍和節目質疑有關環境的警告。"},{"en":"A number of means several, but usually not a very exact number.","zh":"a number of 是指一些或若干，但通常不是非常精確的數目。"},{"en":"A number of students stayed after class to ask questions.","zh":"一些學生課後留下來問問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the exact total is not important.","zh":"當準確總數不重要時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It suggests more than one, but not necessarily many.","zh":"它表示多於一個，但不一定很多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dispute the reality of","meaning":"質疑……的真實性","examples":[{"en":"Some articles dispute the reality of global warming.","zh":"有些文章質疑全球暖化的真實性。"},{"en":"To dispute the reality of something means to question whether it truly exists or is happening.","zh":"質疑某事的真實性，是指懷疑它是否真的存在或正在發生。"},{"en":"Some people may dispute the reality of exam stress until they see students become exhausted.","zh":"有些人可能質疑考試壓力的真實性，直到看見學生變得筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong doubt, not just mild uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語表示強烈懷疑，而不只是輕微不確定。"},{"en":"It is often used when people challenge accepted evidence or warnings.","zh":"它常用於人們挑戰已被接受的證據或警告時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"claimed hazards of","meaning":"所聲稱的……危害","examples":[{"en":"Some writers dispute the claimed hazards of global warming.","zh":"有些作者質疑全球暖化所聲稱的危害。"},{"en":"Claimed hazards of something are dangers that someone says exist, though others may question them.","zh":"所聲稱的某事危害，是指有人說存在、但其他人可能質疑的危險。"},{"en":"A company may deny the claimed hazards of a chemical used in its products.","zh":"公司可能否認其產品所用化學品所聲稱的危害。"},{"en":"The word “claimed” suggests that the danger is being reported, but not accepted by everyone.","zh":"claimed 一詞暗示該危險被提出，但並非人人接受。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing disputed risks.","zh":"這個短語適合討論具爭議的風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"global warming","meaning":"全球暖化","examples":[{"en":"Global warming is one of the environmental hazards discussed in the passage.","zh":"全球暖化是篇章中討論的環境危害之一。"},{"en":"Global warming means the long-term rise in Earth’s average temperature.","zh":"全球暖化是指地球平均氣溫長期上升。"},{"en":"Students may learn about global warming by studying hotter summers and melting ice.","zh":"學生可以透過研究更炎熱的夏天和冰層融化來學習全球暖化。"},{"en":"Global warming can affect weather, sea levels and ecosystems.","zh":"全球暖化可以影響天氣、海平面和生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a major environmental issue connected with climate change.","zh":"這個短語指與氣候變化相關的重大環境議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"overpopulation","meaning":"人口過剩","examples":[{"en":"Overpopulation is presented as one of the dangers facing the planet.","zh":"人口過剩被呈現為地球面對的危險之一。"},{"en":"Overpopulation happens when there are more people than an area can support sustainably.","zh":"人口過剩是指某地人口多於該地可持續支撐的程度。"},{"en":"A city may suffer from overpopulation if housing, schools and hospitals cannot keep up.","zh":"如果房屋、學校和醫院跟不上需求，城市可能出現人口過剩。"},{"en":"Overpopulation can increase pressure on food, water, jobs and land.","zh":"人口過剩可以增加食物、水、工作和土地的壓力。"},{"en":"This word describes population growth beyond available resources.","zh":"這個詞描述人口增長超出可用資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"deforestation","meaning":"森林砍伐","examples":[{"en":"Deforestation is one of the environmental problems mentioned by Suzuki.","zh":"森林砍伐是 Suzuki 提到的環境問題之一。"},{"en":"Deforestation means the cutting down or clearing of forests.","zh":"森林砍伐是指砍掉或清除森林。"},{"en":"A country may experience deforestation when forests are cleared for farms or roads.","zh":"當森林被清除作農田或道路時，一個國家可能出現森林砍伐。"},{"en":"Deforestation can destroy habitats, reduce biodiversity and worsen climate problems.","zh":"森林砍伐可以破壞棲息地、減少生物多樣性並惡化氣候問題。"},{"en":"This word describes large-scale forest loss.","zh":"這個詞描述大規模森林流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ozone depletion","meaning":"臭氧層耗損","examples":[{"en":"Ozone depletion has been discussed in many environmental programmes.","zh":"臭氧層耗損曾在許多環境節目中被討論。"},{"en":"Ozone depletion means the thinning or reduction of the ozone layer.","zh":"臭氧層耗損是指臭氧層變薄或減少。"},{"en":"Science students may study ozone depletion when learning how sunlight affects life on Earth.","zh":"科學學生學習陽光如何影響地球生命時，可能研究臭氧層耗損。"},{"en":"If ozone depletion worsens, more harmful ultraviolet radiation can reach the surface.","zh":"如果臭氧層耗損惡化，更多有害紫外線可以到達地表。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damage to the protective ozone layer.","zh":"這個短語描述保護性臭氧層受損。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"newspaper commentaries","meaning":"報章評論","examples":[{"en":"Two newspaper commentaries show very different views on the planet’s future.","zh":"兩篇報章評論顯示對地球未來非常不同的看法。"},{"en":"Newspaper commentaries are opinion articles in newspapers that discuss current issues.","zh":"報章評論是報紙中討論時事的意見文章。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to compare two newspaper commentaries on housing policy.","zh":"老師可能要求學生比較兩篇關於房屋政策的報章評論。"},{"en":"Commentaries often reveal the writer’s values, not just facts.","zh":"評論通常揭示作者的價值觀，而不只是事實。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to newspaper-based opinion writing.","zh":"這個短語指報章中的意見寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"profound differences of opinion","meaning":"深刻的意見分歧","examples":[{"en":"The two articles show profound differences of opinion on environmental issues.","zh":"這兩篇文章顯示在環境議題上有深刻的意見分歧。"},{"en":"Profound differences of opinion are deep and serious disagreements.","zh":"深刻的意見分歧是深入而嚴重的不同看法。"},{"en":"Two parents may have profound differences of opinion about whether their child should study overseas.","zh":"兩位家長可能對孩子是否應該海外升學有深刻的意見分歧。"},{"en":"Such differences can lead to debate because people start from very different assumptions.","zh":"這類分歧可以引發辯論，因為人們從非常不同的假設出發。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disagreement that is not small or superficial.","zh":"這個短語描述並非細小或表面的不同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"critical issues affecting the planet","meaning":"影響地球的重大議題","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses critical issues affecting the planet.","zh":"篇章討論影響地球的重大議題。"},{"en":"Critical issues affecting the planet are urgent global problems that influence Earth and human life.","zh":"影響地球的重大議題，是影響地球和人類生活的迫切全球問題。"},{"en":"Climate change, water shortages and pollution are critical issues affecting the planet.","zh":"氣候變化、水資源短缺和污染都是影響地球的重大議題。"},{"en":"If these issues are ignored, they can damage future living conditions.","zh":"如果這些議題被忽視，它們可能損害未來生活條件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes major worldwide environmental concerns.","zh":"這個短語描述重大的全球環境關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"generate both fear and denial","meaning":"引起恐懼和否認","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan’s article has generated both fear and denial.","zh":"Kaplan 的文章引起恐懼和否認。"},{"en":"To generate both fear and denial means to make some people worried while making others reject the warning.","zh":"引起恐懼和否認，是指令一些人擔心，同時令另一些人拒絕接受警告。"},{"en":"A report about a new disease may generate both fear and denial in the public.","zh":"一份關於新疾病的報告可能在公眾中引起恐懼和否認。"},{"en":"Strong warnings can divide readers because some feel alarmed and others feel defensive.","zh":"強烈警告可以令讀者分裂，因為有人感到恐慌，有人感到防衛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mixed reactions to troubling information.","zh":"這個短語描述人們對令人不安資訊的混合反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be entitled","meaning":"題為","examples":[{"en":"The first commentary is entitled The Coming Anarchy.","zh":"第一篇評論題為《即將來臨的無政府狀態》。"},{"en":"To be entitled something means to have that title or name.","zh":"題為某名稱，是指作品有該標題或名字。"},{"en":"A student may write an essay entitled “The Future of Hong Kong Transport.”","zh":"學生可能寫一篇題為《香港交通的未來》的文章。"},{"en":"A title can guide readers toward the main theme of a text.","zh":"標題可以引導讀者理解文本主題。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the name of a written work.","zh":"這個短語引入文字作品的名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"The Coming Anarchy","meaning":"《即將來臨的無政府狀態》","examples":[{"en":"The Coming Anarchy paints a dark picture of humanity’s future.","zh":"《即將來臨的無政府狀態》描繪人類未來的黑暗圖像。"},{"en":"The Coming Anarchy is the title of Kaplan’s commentary about disorder and collapse.","zh":"《即將來臨的無政府狀態》是 Kaplan 關於混亂和崩潰的評論標題。"},{"en":"A title like The Coming Anarchy prepares readers for a frightening argument.","zh":"像《即將來臨的無政府狀態》這樣的標題，讓讀者預期一個可怕論點。"},{"en":"The word “anarchy” suggests loss of government control and social order.","zh":"“anarchy” 一詞暗示政府控制和社會秩序喪失。"},{"en":"This title signals a pessimistic view of the future.","zh":"這個標題顯示對未來的悲觀看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"paint a horrifying picture of","meaning":"描繪……的可怕景象","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan’s report paints a horrifying picture of the future.","zh":"Kaplan 的報告描繪未來的可怕景象。"},{"en":"To paint a horrifying picture of something means to describe it in a frightening and vivid way.","zh":"描繪某事的可怕景象，是指以令人害怕而生動的方式描述它。"},{"en":"A newspaper article may paint a horrifying picture of life after a major flood.","zh":"報章文章可能描繪大洪水後生活的可怕景象。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the description is powerful enough to make readers feel alarmed.","zh":"這個短語暗示描述有力量令讀者感到警惕。"},{"en":"It is often used for dark predictions or severe warnings.","zh":"它常用於黑暗預測或嚴厲警告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the future for humanity","meaning":"人類的未來","examples":[{"en":"The report discusses the future for humanity.","zh":"這份報告討論人類的未來。"},{"en":"The future for humanity means what may happen to human beings as a whole.","zh":"人類的未來，是指整體人類可能會發生的事。"},{"en":"Climate scientists often discuss the future for humanity when talking about rising temperatures.","zh":"氣候科學家談到氣溫上升時，通常會討論人類的未來。"},{"en":"Decisions made today can shape the future for humanity.","zh":"今天作出的決定可以塑造人類的未來。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the long-term fate of people worldwide.","zh":"這個短語指全球人類的長遠命運。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"terrible consequences","meaning":"可怕後果","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan warns of the terrible consequences of environmental collapse.","zh":"Kaplan 警告環境崩潰的可怕後果。"},{"en":"Terrible consequences are very serious and harmful results.","zh":"可怕後果是非常嚴重而有害的結果。"},{"en":"Ignoring fire safety rules can have terrible consequences in a crowded building.","zh":"在擁擠建築物中忽視消防安全規則可能有可怕後果。"},{"en":"Environmental damage can create terrible consequences if it affects food, water and health.","zh":"如果環境破壞影響食物、水和健康，就可能造成可怕後果。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses how serious the results may be.","zh":"這個短語強調結果可能很嚴重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the conjunction between","meaning":"……之間的結合","examples":[{"en":"He focuses on the conjunction between population growth and environmental degradation.","zh":"他聚焦於人口增長與環境退化之間的結合。"},{"en":"The conjunction between two things is the way they come together and affect each other.","zh":"兩件事之間的結合，是指它們如何走在一起並互相影響。"},{"en":"A doctor may study the conjunction between poor sleep and exam stress.","zh":"醫生可能研究睡眠不足與考試壓力之間的結合。"},{"en":"When two problems combine, their impact can become stronger.","zh":"當兩個問題結合，它們的影響可能變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the interaction between two forces.","zh":"這個短語突出兩股力量之間的互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"exploding human population","meaning":"急劇膨脹的人口","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan links the crisis to an exploding human population.","zh":"Kaplan 把危機與急劇膨脹的人口聯繫起來。"},{"en":"An exploding human population is a population increasing extremely quickly.","zh":"急劇膨脹的人口，是指以極快速度增加的人口。"},{"en":"A city with an exploding population may struggle to provide enough housing.","zh":"人口急劇膨脹的城市可能難以提供足夠住房。"},{"en":"Rapid population growth can put pressure on land, water and public services.","zh":"快速人口增長可以對土地、水和公共服務造成壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dramatic population increase.","zh":"這個短語描述劇烈的人口增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"environmental degradation","meaning":"環境退化","examples":[{"en":"Environmental degradation may destabilise societies.","zh":"環境退化可能破壞社會穩定。"},{"en":"Environmental degradation means the worsening or damage of natural conditions.","zh":"環境退化是指自然環境變差或受損。"},{"en":"A river full of industrial waste is an example of environmental degradation.","zh":"充滿工業廢物的河流是環境退化的例子。"},{"en":"Degraded environments can reduce food supply, health and economic stability.","zh":"退化的環境可以減少食物供應、健康和經濟穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the decline of environmental quality.","zh":"這個短語描述環境質素下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"already visible in","meaning":"已在……中可見","examples":[{"en":"The consequences are already visible in Africa and Southeast Asia.","zh":"這些後果已在非洲和東南亞可見。"},{"en":"Already visible in a place means the effects can already be seen there.","zh":"已在某地可見，是指影響已經能在那裏看見。"},{"en":"The effects of heavy tourism are already visible in crowded village streets.","zh":"大量旅遊的影響已在擁擠的村莊街道中可見。"},{"en":"Visible signs make a warning harder to dismiss.","zh":"可見跡象令警告更難被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that a problem is not only future, but present.","zh":"這個短語暗示問題不只是未來的，也是現在的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"parts of Southeast Asia","meaning":"東南亞部分地區","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan discusses problems in Africa and parts of Southeast Asia.","zh":"Kaplan 討論非洲和東南亞部分地區的問題。"},{"en":"Parts of Southeast Asia means some areas within the Southeast Asian region.","zh":"東南亞部分地區，是指東南亞區域內的一些地方。"},{"en":"Flooding may affect parts of Southeast Asia during the rainy season.","zh":"雨季期間，水災可能影響東南亞部分地區。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids claiming that every country in the region is affected.","zh":"這個短語避免聲稱該區每個國家都受影響。"},{"en":"It describes a limited but significant geographical area.","zh":"它描述有限但重要的地理範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be destabilised by","meaning":"被……破壞穩定","examples":[{"en":"Society can be destabilised by disease and environmental pressure.","zh":"社會可能被疾病和環境壓力破壞穩定。"},{"en":"To be destabilised by something means to become less secure or less orderly because of it.","zh":"被某事破壞穩定，是指因它而變得較不安全或較無秩序。"},{"en":"A school can be destabilised by sudden staff shortages before exams.","zh":"學校可能在考試前被突然的教師短缺破壞穩定。"},{"en":"When basic systems fail, communities can become unstable.","zh":"當基本系統失效，社區可能變得不穩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a force that weakens stability.","zh":"這個短語描述削弱穩定的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the AIDS epidemic","meaning":"愛滋病疫症","examples":[{"en":"The AIDS epidemic is mentioned as one factor destabilising society.","zh":"愛滋病疫症被提及為破壞社會穩定的因素之一。"},{"en":"The AIDS epidemic means the widespread spread of AIDS within populations.","zh":"愛滋病疫症是指愛滋病在人群中廣泛傳播。"},{"en":"Public health classes may study the AIDS epidemic to understand disease prevention.","zh":"公共衛生課可能研究愛滋病疫症，以理解疾病預防。"},{"en":"An epidemic can affect families, healthcare systems and economic life.","zh":"疫症可以影響家庭、醫療系統和經濟生活。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a serious public health crisis.","zh":"這個短語指嚴重公共衛生危機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"government control evaporates","meaning":"政府控制消失","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan describes a future in which government control evaporates.","zh":"Kaplan 描述一個政府控制消失的未來。"},{"en":"If government control evaporates, official authority disappears or becomes ineffective.","zh":"如果政府控制消失，官方權威就不見了或變得無效。"},{"en":"During a severe crisis, government control may evaporate if police, courts and services stop functioning.","zh":"在嚴重危機中，如果警察、法院和服務停止運作，政府控制可能消失。"},{"en":"The verb “evaporates” suggests control disappears quickly and completely.","zh":"evaporates 這個動詞暗示控制迅速而完全地消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the collapse of state authority.","zh":"這個短語描述國家權威崩潰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"national borders crumble","meaning":"國界瓦解","examples":[{"en":"National borders may crumble under environmental pressure.","zh":"國界可能在環境壓力下瓦解。"},{"en":"If national borders crumble, countries lose the ability to control or protect their borders.","zh":"如果國界瓦解，國家就失去控制或保護邊界的能力。"},{"en":"Large refugee movements can make borders seem to crumble if governments cannot manage them.","zh":"如果政府無法管理，大規模難民流動可能令國界看似瓦解。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests political order breaking down.","zh":"這個短語暗示政治秩序崩潰。"},{"en":"It describes a severe loss of national control.","zh":"它描述嚴重的國家控制喪失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"beneath the pressure of","meaning":"在……壓力下","examples":[{"en":"National borders crumble beneath the pressure of environmental refugees.","zh":"國界在環境難民的壓力下瓦解。"},{"en":"Beneath the pressure of something means under the force or burden created by it.","zh":"在某事壓力下，是指處於它造成的力量或負擔之下。"},{"en":"A hospital may struggle beneath the pressure of too many emergency patients.","zh":"醫院可能在太多急症病人的壓力下難以應付。"},{"en":"When pressure becomes too strong, systems may fail.","zh":"當壓力變得太強，系統可能失效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a burden powerful enough to weaken something.","zh":"這個短語描述足以削弱某事的負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"environmental refugees","meaning":"環境難民","examples":[{"en":"Environmental refugees may put pressure on national borders.","zh":"環境難民可能對國界造成壓力。"},{"en":"Environmental refugees are people forced to leave their homes because environmental conditions become unsafe or unlivable.","zh":"環境難民是因環境變得不安全或不宜居而被迫離開家園的人。"},{"en":"Families may become environmental refugees after drought destroys their farms.","zh":"乾旱摧毀農田後，家庭可能成為環境難民。"},{"en":"Large movements of environmental refugees can create social and political pressure.","zh":"大量環境難民流動可以造成社會和政治壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes displaced people caused by environmental crisis.","zh":"這個短語描述由環境危機造成的流離失所者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"local populations","meaning":"本地人口","examples":[{"en":"Local populations may react defensively to fleeing groups.","zh":"本地人口可能對逃難群體作出防衛性反應。"},{"en":"Local populations are the people who already live in a particular area.","zh":"本地人口是指已經住在某一地區的人。"},{"en":"Local populations may worry if sudden migration increases pressure on jobs and housing.","zh":"如果突然移民增加就業和住房壓力，本地人口可能感到憂慮。"},{"en":"Tension can rise when local populations feel resources are limited.","zh":"當本地人口覺得資源有限，緊張可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to existing residents of a place.","zh":"這個短語指某地原有居民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"revert to tribalism","meaning":"回復部落主義","examples":[{"en":"Some populations may revert to tribalism in times of crisis.","zh":"有些人口在危機時可能回復部落主義。"},{"en":"To revert to tribalism means to return to loyalty based mainly on tribe, ethnic group or small group identity.","zh":"回復部落主義，是指重新以部落、族群或小群體身份作主要忠誠基礎。"},{"en":"In a school conflict, students may revert to group loyalty instead of judging fairly.","zh":"在學校衝突中，學生可能回到小圈子忠誠，而不是公平判斷。"},{"en":"Crisis can make people trust only their own group.","zh":"危機可以令人只信任自己的群體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a return to narrow group identity.","zh":"這個短語描述回到狹窄群體身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"settle old scores","meaning":"清算舊怨","examples":[{"en":"Groups may use disorder as a chance to settle old scores.","zh":"群體可能利用混亂作為清算舊怨的機會。"},{"en":"To settle old scores means to take revenge for past conflicts or wrongs.","zh":"清算舊怨，是指為過去的衝突或錯事報復。"},{"en":"Two classmates should not use a group project to settle old scores from an earlier argument.","zh":"兩名同學不應利用小組專題清算早前爭執的舊怨。"},{"en":"When law and order weaken, old grudges may become dangerous.","zh":"當法律和秩序削弱，舊怨可能變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes revenge based on past resentment.","zh":"這個短語描述基於過去怨恨的報復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"defend against","meaning":"抵禦……","examples":[{"en":"Local populations may defend against fleeing masses.","zh":"本地人口可能抵禦逃難群眾。"},{"en":"To defend against something means to protect oneself from a threat or pressure.","zh":"抵禦某事，是指保護自己免受威脅或壓力影響。"},{"en":"A school may defend against cyberattacks by improving its password system.","zh":"學校可能透過改善密碼系統來抵禦網絡攻擊。"},{"en":"People defend against danger when they believe their safety or resources are at risk.","zh":"當人們相信安全或資源有風險，就會抵禦危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protective action against something.","zh":"這個短語描述針對某事的保護行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fleeing masses","meaning":"逃難群眾","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes fleeing masses moving across borders.","zh":"篇章描述逃難群眾跨越國界。"},{"en":"Fleeing masses are large groups of people escaping danger or hardship.","zh":"逃難群眾是逃離危險或困苦的大批人群。"},{"en":"After a severe flood, fleeing masses may leave low-lying villages.","zh":"嚴重水災後，逃難群眾可能離開低窪村莊。"},{"en":"Large movements of people can overwhelm transport, housing and public services.","zh":"大規模人口流動可以壓垮交通、住房和公共服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes many people escaping at the same time.","zh":"這個短語描述許多人同時逃離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"bands of stateless nomads","meaning":"一群群無國籍遊牧者","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan imagines bands of stateless nomads on the move.","zh":"Kaplan 想像一群群無國籍遊牧者在遷移中。"},{"en":"Bands of stateless nomads are groups of people without a country who move from place to place.","zh":"一群群無國籍遊牧者，是指沒有國家並四處移動的人群。"},{"en":"In a fictional disaster story, bands of stateless nomads may travel in search of water.","zh":"在災難小說中，一群群無國籍遊牧者可能為尋找水源而旅行。"},{"en":"Statelessness makes people vulnerable because no government clearly protects them.","zh":"無國籍令人脆弱，因為沒有政府明確保護他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes displaced groups with no stable national home.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有穩定國家歸屬的流離群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on the move","meaning":"在遷移中","examples":[{"en":"Stateless nomads are constantly on the move.","zh":"無國籍遊牧者不斷在遷移中。"},{"en":"To be on the move means to be travelling or changing location rather than staying still.","zh":"在遷移中，是指正在旅行或轉換地點，而不是停留原地。"},{"en":"A family may be on the move all day when relocating to a new flat.","zh":"一個家庭搬到新單位時，可能整天都在遷移中。"},{"en":"People on the move may lack stable housing, schooling and healthcare.","zh":"在遷移中的人可能缺乏穩定住房、教育和醫療。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continuous movement.","zh":"這個短語描述持續移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a global pattern of","meaning":"……的全球模式","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan sees a global pattern of social disintegration.","zh":"Kaplan 看見社會瓦解的全球模式。"},{"en":"A global pattern of something means a repeated trend appearing across the world.","zh":"某事的全球模式，是指在世界各地反覆出現的趨勢。"},{"en":"Researchers may notice a global pattern of rising city temperatures.","zh":"研究人員可能注意到城市氣溫上升的全球模式。"},{"en":"A global pattern suggests the problem is not isolated or local.","zh":"全球模式暗示問題不是孤立或局部的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a worldwide trend.","zh":"這個短語描述全球趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"disintegration of","meaning":"……的瓦解","examples":[{"en":"He predicts the disintegration of social and political infrastructure.","zh":"他預測社會及政治基礎架構的瓦解。"},{"en":"Disintegration of something means its breakdown into disorder or weakness.","zh":"某事的瓦解，是指它崩壞成混亂或變得薄弱。"},{"en":"A club may face the disintegration of teamwork if members stop communicating.","zh":"如果成員停止溝通，社團可能面對團隊合作的瓦解。"},{"en":"When systems disintegrate, they can no longer function properly.","zh":"當系統瓦解，它們就不能正常運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious collapse or breaking apart.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重崩潰或分裂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"social, political and economic infrastructure","meaning":"社會、政治及經濟基礎架構","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan warns that social, political and economic infrastructure could collapse.","zh":"Kaplan 警告社會、政治及經濟基礎架構可能崩潰。"},{"en":"Social, political and economic infrastructure means the systems that support society, government and the economy.","zh":"社會、政治及經濟基礎架構，是支持社會、政府和經濟的系統。"},{"en":"Schools, courts, banks and transport networks are parts of a country’s infrastructure.","zh":"學校、法院、銀行和交通網絡都是國家基礎架構的一部分。"},{"en":"If these systems fail, ordinary life becomes difficult and unsafe.","zh":"如果這些系統失效，日常生活會變得困難而不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the basic structures that keep society functioning.","zh":"這個短語描述維持社會運作的基本結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"under the impact of","meaning":"在……影響下","examples":[{"en":"Infrastructure may collapse under the impact of ecological degradation.","zh":"基礎架構可能在生態退化的影響下崩潰。"},{"en":"Under the impact of something means affected by its force or consequences.","zh":"在某事影響下，是指受到其力量或後果影響。"},{"en":"A small business may close under the impact of rising rent.","zh":"小企業可能在租金上升的影響下倒閉。"},{"en":"Strong impacts can weaken systems that once seemed stable.","zh":"強大影響可以削弱曾經看似穩定的系統。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the pressure causing damage or change.","zh":"這個短語顯示造成損害或改變的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ecological degradation","meaning":"生態退化","examples":[{"en":"Ecological degradation can create pressure on societies.","zh":"生態退化可以對社會造成壓力。"},{"en":"Ecological degradation means damage to ecosystems and natural relationships.","zh":"生態退化是指生態系統和自然關係受損。"},{"en":"A polluted wetland is an example of ecological degradation.","zh":"受污染的濕地是生態退化的例子。"},{"en":"When ecosystems degrade, food chains, water quality and habitats can suffer.","zh":"當生態系統退化，食物鏈、水質和棲息地都可能受害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the decline of ecological health.","zh":"這個短語描述生態健康下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"population pressure","meaning":"人口壓力","examples":[{"en":"Population pressure is one factor in Kaplan’s scenario.","zh":"人口壓力是 Kaplan 情景中的一個因素。"},{"en":"Population pressure is stress created when many people need limited resources.","zh":"人口壓力是當大量人口需要有限資源時造成的壓力。"},{"en":"A town may face population pressure if many new residents arrive but housing is limited.","zh":"如果大量新居民到來但住房有限，城鎮可能面對人口壓力。"},{"en":"Population pressure can affect jobs, food, water and public services.","zh":"人口壓力可以影響工作、食物、水和公共服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strain caused by population size or growth.","zh":"這個短語描述由人口數量或增長造成的負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ecosystems collapse","meaning":"生態系統崩潰","examples":[{"en":"As ecosystems collapse, social disorder may spread.","zh":"隨着生態系統崩潰，社會混亂可能蔓延。"},{"en":"Ecosystems collapse when natural systems can no longer support the plants, animals and processes inside them.","zh":"生態系統崩潰，是指自然系統再不能支撐其中的植物、動物和過程。"},{"en":"A coral reef ecosystem may collapse if warming and pollution kill too many species.","zh":"如果暖化和污染殺死太多物種，珊瑚礁生態系統可能崩潰。"},{"en":"Ecosystem collapse can reduce food, clean water and natural protection.","zh":"生態系統崩潰可以減少食物、清潔水和自然保護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severe failure of natural systems.","zh":"這個短語描述自然系統嚴重失效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"this scenario could sweep the planet","meaning":"這種情況可能席捲全球","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan believes this scenario could sweep the planet.","zh":"Kaplan 認為這種情況可能席捲全球。"},{"en":"If a scenario could sweep the planet, it could spread across the world quickly or widely.","zh":"如果一種情況可能席捲全球，它可能快速或廣泛傳遍世界。"},{"en":"A new economic crisis could sweep the planet if many countries depend on the same markets.","zh":"如果許多國家依賴相同市場，新的經濟危機可能席捲全球。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the problem may not stay local.","zh":"這個短語暗示問題可能不會停留在本地。"},{"en":"It describes a frightening possibility of global spread.","zh":"它描述全球蔓延的可怕可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"industrialised countries","meaning":"工業化國家","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan believes the crisis could eventually reach industrialised countries.","zh":"Kaplan 認為危機最終可能到達工業化國家。"},{"en":"Industrialised countries are countries with developed industries, infrastructure and modern economies.","zh":"工業化國家是擁有成熟工業、基礎架構和現代經濟的國家。"},{"en":"Japan, Germany and Canada are examples of industrialised countries.","zh":"日本、德國和加拿大是工業化國家的例子。"},{"en":"Problems that begin elsewhere may still affect industrialised countries through trade, migration and climate.","zh":"始於其他地方的問題仍可能透過貿易、移民和氣候影響工業化國家。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to economically developed nations.","zh":"這個短語指經濟發達國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a frightening scenario","meaning":"可怕的情景","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan presents a frightening scenario of global disorder.","zh":"Kaplan 提出一個全球混亂的可怕情景。"},{"en":"A frightening scenario is a possible future situation that causes fear.","zh":"可怕的情景，是令人害怕的可能未來情況。"},{"en":"A doctor may describe a frightening scenario if a patient ignores serious symptoms.","zh":"如果病人忽視嚴重症狀，醫生可能描述一個可怕情景。"},{"en":"Scenarios help readers imagine consequences before they happen.","zh":"情景幫助讀者在事情發生前想像後果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an alarming possible outcome.","zh":"這個短語描述令人警覺的可能結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be built on","meaning":"建基於……","examples":[{"en":"The scenario is built on an attempt to predict ecological consequences.","zh":"這個情景建基於預測生態後果的嘗試。"},{"en":"To be built on something means to be based on it.","zh":"建基於某事，是指以它為基礎。"},{"en":"A good essay is built on clear evidence and logical explanation.","zh":"好作文建基於清晰證據和邏輯解釋。"},{"en":"If the foundation is weak, the argument built on it may also be weak.","zh":"如果基礎薄弱，建基於其上的論點也可能薄弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the basis of an idea.","zh":"這個短語描述想法的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a serious attempt to","meaning":"認真嘗試去……","examples":[{"en":"The article is a serious attempt to project the aftermath of ecological destruction.","zh":"這篇文章是認真嘗試預測生態破壞後果的作品。"},{"en":"A serious attempt to do something is a careful and genuine effort to do it.","zh":"認真嘗試做某事，是指仔細而真誠地努力做它。"},{"en":"A student may make a serious attempt to improve writing by revising every essay.","zh":"學生可能透過修改每篇作文，認真嘗試改善寫作。"},{"en":"Serious attempts require effort, evidence and attention to detail.","zh":"認真嘗試需要努力、證據和對細節的重視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an effort that should be taken seriously.","zh":"這個短語描述值得認真看待的努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"project the aftermath of","meaning":"預測……的後果","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan tries to project the aftermath of ecological destruction.","zh":"Kaplan 嘗試預測生態破壞的後果。"},{"en":"To project the aftermath of something means to predict what may happen after it.","zh":"預測某事的後果，是指估計它之後可能發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Economists may project the aftermath of a sudden rise in food prices.","zh":"經濟學家可能預測食物價格突然上升的後果。"},{"en":"Projection helps people prepare for consequences before they arrive.","zh":"預測有助人們在後果到來前作準備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes forecasting later effects.","zh":"這個短語描述預測後續影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ecological destruction","meaning":"生態破壞","examples":[{"en":"The passage warns of the aftermath of ecological destruction.","zh":"篇章警告生態破壞的後果。"},{"en":"Ecological destruction means severe damage to ecosystems and natural life-support systems.","zh":"生態破壞是指對生態系統和自然生命維持系統造成嚴重損害。"},{"en":"Cutting down a rainforest for short-term profit can cause ecological destruction.","zh":"為短期利益砍伐雨林可以造成生態破壞。"},{"en":"Such destruction can affect animals, plants, water and human communities.","zh":"這種破壞可以影響動物、植物、水源和人類社群。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious damage to nature.","zh":"這個短語描述對自然的嚴重損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"core recognition","meaning":"核心認知","examples":[{"en":"The argument comes from a core recognition that the planet is finite.","zh":"這個論點來自一項核心認知：地球資源有限。"},{"en":"A core recognition is a basic understanding at the centre of an argument.","zh":"核心認知是一個論點中心的基本理解。"},{"en":"A health campaign may begin with the core recognition that prevention is cheaper than treatment.","zh":"健康宣傳可能始於一項核心認知：預防比治療便宜。"},{"en":"Once this central truth is accepted, other conclusions become easier to understand.","zh":"一旦接受這個核心事實，其他結論就較容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fundamental insight.","zh":"這個短語描述根本洞見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the planet is finite","meaning":"地球資源有限","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan’s argument recognises that the planet is finite.","zh":"Kaplan 的論點承認地球資源有限。"},{"en":"The planet is finite means Earth has limited space, resources and ecological capacity.","zh":"地球資源有限，是指地球的空間、資源和生態承載力有限。"},{"en":"A family budget is finite, so members cannot spend endlessly.","zh":"家庭預算有限，所以成員不能無止境花錢。"},{"en":"If Earth is finite, endless growth in consumption creates pressure.","zh":"如果地球資源有限，消費無限增長就會造成壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses natural limits.","zh":"這個短語強調自然限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"consumption","meaning":"消耗；消費","examples":[{"en":"Consumption has social, political and economic consequences.","zh":"消耗會帶來社會、政治及經濟後果。"},{"en":"Consumption means the use of goods, resources or energy.","zh":"消耗或消費是指使用貨品、資源或能源。"},{"en":"Buying new clothes every week is a form of high consumption.","zh":"每星期購買新衣服是一種高消費。"},{"en":"High consumption can increase waste, pollution and resource pressure.","zh":"高消費可以增加浪費、污染和資源壓力。"},{"en":"This word describes what people or societies use up.","zh":"這個詞描述人或社會使用掉的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"vast ramifications","meaning":"深遠影響","examples":[{"en":"Consumption has vast ramifications for society and politics.","zh":"消費對社會和政治有深遠影響。"},{"en":"Vast ramifications are very wide and important consequences.","zh":"深遠影響是非常廣泛而重要的後果。"},{"en":"Closing a major hospital can have vast ramifications for patients, staff and nearby clinics.","zh":"關閉大型醫院可能對病人、員工和附近診所有深遠影響。"},{"en":"A decision with vast ramifications affects many areas, not just one.","zh":"有深遠影響的決定會影響許多範疇，而不只是單一方面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes far-reaching effects.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛而長遠的效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"social, political and economic ramifications","meaning":"社會、政治及經濟影響","examples":[{"en":"Environmental damage has social, political and economic ramifications.","zh":"環境破壞有社會、政治及經濟影響。"},{"en":"Social, political and economic ramifications are consequences affecting society, government and the economy.","zh":"社會、政治及經濟影響，是影響社會、政府和經濟的後果。"},{"en":"A housing crisis can have social, political and economic ramifications.","zh":"房屋危機可以有社會、政治及經濟影響。"},{"en":"Environmental problems can change how people live, vote and earn a living.","zh":"環境問題可以改變人們如何生活、投票和謀生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad effects across major areas of life.","zh":"這個短語描述跨越主要生活範疇的廣泛影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"generate discussion and controversy","meaning":"引發討論和爭議","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan’s article has generated discussion and controversy.","zh":"Kaplan 的文章引發討論和爭議。"},{"en":"To generate discussion and controversy means to make people talk, debate and disagree.","zh":"引發討論和爭議，是指令人談論、辯論和不同意。"},{"en":"A new exam policy may generate discussion and controversy among parents.","zh":"新考試政策可能在家長之間引發討論和爭議。"},{"en":"Controversial ideas often attract attention because people feel strongly about them.","zh":"具爭議的想法通常吸引注意，因為人們對它們感受強烈。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public debate caused by an issue.","zh":"這個短語描述由某議題造成的公共辯論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pronounce someone’s vision dead wrong","meaning":"宣稱某人的看法完全錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Marcus Gee pronounces Kaplan’s vision dead wrong.","zh":"Marcus Gee 宣稱 Kaplan 的看法完全錯誤。"},{"en":"To pronounce someone’s vision dead wrong means to state strongly that their view of the future is completely mistaken.","zh":"宣稱某人的看法完全錯誤，是指強烈表示對方對未來的看法完全錯了。"},{"en":"A critic may pronounce a school reform plan dead wrong if they believe it ignores students’ needs.","zh":"如果批評者認為學校改革計劃忽視學生需要，可能宣稱該計劃完全錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is forceful and leaves little room for compromise.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈，幾乎沒有妥協空間。"},{"en":"It describes a strong rejection of someone’s prediction or worldview.","zh":"它描述對某人預測或世界觀的強烈否定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dead wrong","meaning":"完全錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Gee believes Kaplan is dead wrong.","zh":"Gee 認為 Kaplan 完全錯誤。"},{"en":"Dead wrong means completely wrong.","zh":"dead wrong 是指完全錯誤。"},{"en":"If a student says 7 times 8 is 54, the answer is dead wrong.","zh":"如果學生說 7 乘 8 等於 54，答案就是完全錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase is stronger than simply saying “incorrect.”","zh":"這個短語比單純說「不正確」更強烈。"},{"en":"It is often used when the speaker is very confident.","zh":"它常用於說話者非常有信心時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a major article headlined","meaning":"一篇標題為……的重要文章","examples":[{"en":"Gee wrote a major article headlined Apocalypse Deferred.","zh":"Gee 寫了一篇標題為《末日延後》的重要文章。"},{"en":"A major article headlined something is an important article with that title.","zh":"一篇標題為某名稱的重要文章，是指有該標題的重要文章。"},{"en":"A newspaper may publish a major article headlined “Schools Under Pressure.”","zh":"報紙可能刊登一篇標題為《學校承受壓力》的重要文章。"},{"en":"The headline frames how readers first understand the article.","zh":"標題塑造讀者最初如何理解文章。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces both importance and title.","zh":"這個短語同時引入重要性和標題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Apocalypse Deferred","meaning":"《末日延後》","examples":[{"en":"Apocalypse Deferred challenges Kaplan’s warnings about global crisis.","zh":"《末日延後》挑戰 Kaplan 對全球危機的警告。"},{"en":"Apocalypse Deferred is the title of Gee’s article arguing that disaster has been delayed or exaggerated.","zh":"《末日延後》是 Gee 的文章標題，主張災難已被延後或被誇大。"},{"en":"A title like Apocalypse Deferred suggests that the end of the world has not arrived.","zh":"像《末日延後》這樣的標題暗示世界末日尚未到來。"},{"en":"The phrase signals a more optimistic or sceptical view of environmental warnings.","zh":"這個短語顯示對環境警告較樂觀或懷疑的看法。"},{"en":"This title contrasts with darker predictions of collapse.","zh":"這個標題與較黑暗的崩潰預測形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"attack the doomsayers","meaning":"攻擊末日論者","examples":[{"en":"Gee attacks the doomsayers who predict environmental catastrophe.","zh":"Gee 攻擊預測環境災難的末日論者。"},{"en":"To attack the doomsayers means to criticise people who predict disaster.","zh":"攻擊末日論者，是指批評那些預測災難的人。"},{"en":"A writer may attack the doomsayers who say new technology will destroy all jobs.","zh":"作者可能攻擊那些說新科技會摧毀所有工作的末日論者。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests strong criticism of pessimistic voices.","zh":"這個短語暗示對悲觀聲音的強烈批評。"},{"en":"It is used when someone rejects disaster-focused arguments.","zh":"它用於某人拒絕災難式論點時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"counter with","meaning":"以……反駁","examples":[{"en":"Gee counters Kaplan’s argument with statistics.","zh":"Gee 以統計數據反駁 Kaplan 的論點。"},{"en":"To counter with something means to respond to an argument by using another point or evidence.","zh":"以某事反駁，是指用另一個觀點或證據回應某論點。"},{"en":"A student may counter a classmate’s opinion with examples from the text.","zh":"學生可能以文本例子反駁同學的意見。"},{"en":"Strong counterarguments directly challenge the original claim.","zh":"強反駁會直接挑戰原本主張。"},{"en":"This phrase describes answering one argument with another.","zh":"這個短語描述用另一論點回應原論點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"statistics favoured by","meaning":"……所偏好的統計數據","examples":[{"en":"Gee uses statistics favoured by believers in economic growth.","zh":"Gee 使用經濟增長信奉者所偏好的統計數據。"},{"en":"Statistics favoured by a group are data that the group likes to use because they support its view.","zh":"某群體所偏好的統計數據，是他們喜歡使用、因為支持其觀點的數據。"},{"en":"A school may use statistics favoured by supporters of smaller classes.","zh":"學校可能使用支持小班教學者所偏好的統計數據。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that data can be selected to support a particular argument.","zh":"這個短語暗示數據可以被選來支持特定論點。"},{"en":"It reminds readers to ask why certain numbers are chosen.","zh":"它提醒讀者詢問為何選用某些數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"believers in","meaning":"相信……的人","examples":[{"en":"Some writers are believers in the limitless benefits of economic growth.","zh":"有些作者是相信經濟增長有無限好處的人。"},{"en":"Believers in something are people who strongly trust or support it.","zh":"相信某事的人，是強烈信任或支持它的人。"},{"en":"Some teachers are believers in daily reading as the best way to improve English.","zh":"有些老師是相信每日閱讀是改善英文最佳方法的人。"},{"en":"Belief can shape which evidence people notice and value.","zh":"信念可以塑造人們注意和重視哪些證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong supporters of an idea.","zh":"這個短語描述某想法的強烈支持者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"limitless benefits and potential","meaning":"無限的好處和潛力","examples":[{"en":"Gee believes in the limitless benefits and potential of economic growth.","zh":"Gee 相信經濟增長有無限的好處和潛力。"},{"en":"Limitless benefits and potential means unlimited advantages and future possibilities.","zh":"無限的好處和潛力，是指沒有上限的優勢和未來可能性。"},{"en":"Some people believe technology has limitless benefits and potential in education.","zh":"有些人相信科技在教育中有無限的好處和潛力。"},{"en":"Suzuki would question this view because natural resources have limits.","zh":"Suzuki 會質疑這種看法，因為自然資源有限。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very strong optimism about something.","zh":"這個短語描述對某事極強的樂觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"economic growth","meaning":"經濟增長","examples":[{"en":"Economic growth is central to Gee’s optimistic argument.","zh":"經濟增長是 Gee 樂觀論點的核心。"},{"en":"Economic growth means an increase in the production, income or wealth of an economy.","zh":"經濟增長是指一個經濟體的生產、收入或財富增加。"},{"en":"A city may experience economic growth when new businesses create jobs.","zh":"當新企業創造工作，城市可能經歷經濟增長。"},{"en":"Economic growth can raise incomes, but it may also increase resource use.","zh":"經濟增長可以提高收入，但也可能增加資源使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes expansion in economic activity.","zh":"這個短語描述經濟活動擴張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cite improvements in","meaning":"引用……方面的改善","examples":[{"en":"Gee cites improvements in health, education and food availability.","zh":"Gee 引用健康、教育和食物供應方面的改善。"},{"en":"To cite improvements in something means to mention better results as evidence.","zh":"引用某方面的改善，是指提及較好結果作為證據。"},{"en":"A principal may cite improvements in attendance to show a new policy is working.","zh":"校長可能引用出席率方面的改善，來顯示新政策有效。"},{"en":"Citing improvements helps support an optimistic argument.","zh":"引用改善有助支持樂觀論點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using positive changes as evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述使用正面變化作證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"spectacular improvements","meaning":"顯著改善","examples":[{"en":"Gee points to spectacular improvements in human well-being.","zh":"Gee 指出人類福祉有顯著改善。"},{"en":"Spectacular improvements are very impressive and noticeable changes for the better.","zh":"顯著改善是非常令人印象深刻而明顯的好轉。"},{"en":"A school may show spectacular improvements if exam pass rates double in one year.","zh":"如果學校考試合格率一年內翻倍，就可能顯示顯著改善。"},{"en":"Such improvements can make people feel hopeful about the future.","zh":"這類改善可以令人對未來感到有希望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dramatic positive change.","zh":"這個短語描述劇烈的正面變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"human health","meaning":"人類健康","examples":[{"en":"Human health has improved in many parts of the world.","zh":"世界許多地區的人類健康已有改善。"},{"en":"Human health means the physical and sometimes mental well-being of people.","zh":"人類健康是指人的身體，有時也包括心理福祉。"},{"en":"Vaccines, clean water and hospitals can improve human health.","zh":"疫苗、清潔食水和醫院可以改善人類健康。"},{"en":"Poor environments can damage human health through disease and pollution.","zh":"惡劣環境可以透過疾病和污染損害人類健康。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the health condition of people.","zh":"這個短語指人的健康狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"levels of education and literacy","meaning":"教育和識字水平","examples":[{"en":"Gee mentions higher levels of education and literacy.","zh":"Gee 提到較高的教育和識字水平。"},{"en":"Levels of education and literacy refer to how much schooling people receive and how well they can read and write.","zh":"教育和識字水平，是指人們接受多少教育，以及閱讀和寫作能力有多好。"},{"en":"A country may improve levels of education and literacy by building more schools.","zh":"一個國家可以透過興建更多學校來改善教育和識字水平。"},{"en":"Higher literacy helps people access jobs, information and public services.","zh":"較高識字率幫助人們取得工作、資訊和公共服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes educational development in a population.","zh":"這個短語描述人口中的教育發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"availability of food","meaning":"食物供應","examples":[{"en":"The availability of food has improved in Gee’s view.","zh":"在 Gee 看來，食物供應已有改善。"},{"en":"Availability of food means how easily people can obtain enough food.","zh":"食物供應是指人們取得足夠食物有多容易。"},{"en":"Food availability improves when farms, transport and markets work well.","zh":"當農場、運輸和市場運作良好，食物供應就會改善。"},{"en":"If food availability falls, malnutrition and unrest may increase.","zh":"如果食物供應下降，營養不良和社會不安可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to access to food supply.","zh":"這個短語指取得食物供應的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"length of life","meaning":"壽命","examples":[{"en":"Gee argues that the length of life has increased.","zh":"Gee 認為壽命已經延長。"},{"en":"Length of life means how long people usually live.","zh":"壽命是指人們通常能活多久。"},{"en":"Better medicine can increase the average length of life.","zh":"更好的醫療可以增加平均壽命。"},{"en":"Longer life may reflect better health, nutrition and living conditions.","zh":"更長壽命可能反映更好健康、營養和生活條件。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to lifespan or longevity.","zh":"這個短語指生命長度或長壽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the developing world","meaning":"發展中國家","examples":[{"en":"Gee says progress has occurred even in the developing world.","zh":"Gee 說即使在發展中國家也出現了進步。"},{"en":"The developing world refers to poorer or less industrialised countries that are still building their economies.","zh":"發展中國家是指較貧窮或工業化程度較低、仍在建設經濟的國家。"},{"en":"Education programmes in the developing world may focus on literacy and basic healthcare.","zh":"發展中國家的教育計劃可能聚焦識字和基本醫療。"},{"en":"Progress in the developing world can improve millions of lives.","zh":"發展中國家的進步可以改善數百萬人的生活。"},{"en":"This phrase refers broadly to less economically developed regions.","zh":"這個短語廣泛指經濟發展程度較低的地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fivefold increase","meaning":"五倍增長","examples":[{"en":"Gee links the fivefold increase in the world economy to human progress.","zh":"Gee 把世界經濟的五倍增長與人類進步聯繫起來。"},{"en":"A fivefold increase means something becomes five times as large as before.","zh":"五倍增長是指某物變成原來的五倍。"},{"en":"If a club grows from 10 members to 50, it has a fivefold increase in membership.","zh":"如果社團由 10 名成員增至 50 名，會員數就有五倍增長。"},{"en":"Large increases can be used as evidence of growth or success.","zh":"大幅增長可以被用作增長或成功的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very large rise.","zh":"這個短語描述非常大的上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the world economy","meaning":"世界經濟","examples":[{"en":"The world economy has expanded greatly since 1950.","zh":"自 1950 年以來，世界經濟大幅擴張。"},{"en":"The world economy means the combined economic activity of all countries.","zh":"世界經濟是指所有國家的經濟活動總和。"},{"en":"Trade, jobs, production and investment are all part of the world economy.","zh":"貿易、就業、生產和投資都是世界經濟的一部分。"},{"en":"When the world economy grows, some people may become richer, but resource use may also rise.","zh":"當世界經濟增長，有些人可能變得更富裕，但資源使用也可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the global economic system.","zh":"這個短語指全球經濟系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the cause of this good news","meaning":"這些好消息的成因","examples":[{"en":"Gee sees economic growth as the cause of this good news.","zh":"Gee 視經濟增長為這些好消息的成因。"},{"en":"The cause of this good news means the reason behind the positive developments.","zh":"這些好消息的成因，是指正面發展背後的原因。"},{"en":"A principal may say better teaching is the cause of this good news about exam results.","zh":"校長可能說更好的教學是考試成績好消息的成因。"},{"en":"Identifying the cause helps explain why improvement happened.","zh":"找出成因有助解釋為何出現改善。"},{"en":"This phrase links positive outcomes to their supposed reason.","zh":"這個短語把正面結果與其所謂原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"concede that","meaning":"承認","examples":[{"en":"Gee does concede that immense problems remain.","zh":"Gee 確實承認仍存在重大問題。"},{"en":"To concede that something is true means to admit it, often despite arguing another point.","zh":"承認某事為真，是指承認它，通常是在主張另一觀點時。"},{"en":"A student may concede that their essay has grammar errors, while still defending the main argument.","zh":"學生可能承認自己的作文有文法錯誤，但仍為主要論點辯護。"},{"en":"Conceding a point can make an argument seem more balanced.","zh":"承認某一點可以令論點看起來更平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase means to acknowledge something reluctantly or fairly.","zh":"這個短語表示勉強或公平地承認某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"immense problems remain","meaning":"仍存在重大問題","examples":[{"en":"Gee concedes that immense problems remain.","zh":"Gee 承認仍存在重大問題。"},{"en":"Immense problems remain means very serious problems still exist.","zh":"仍存在重大問題，是指非常嚴重的問題仍然存在。"},{"en":"Even after a school improves its exam results, immense problems may remain in student stress.","zh":"即使學校改善考試成績，學生壓力方面仍可能存在重大問題。"},{"en":"Admitting that problems remain prevents optimism from becoming unrealistic.","zh":"承認問題仍然存在，可以避免樂觀變得不現實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large unresolved difficulties.","zh":"這個短語描述尚未解決的大困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ethnic nationalism","meaning":"種族民族主義","examples":[{"en":"Ethnic nationalism is listed as one of the continuing problems.","zh":"種族民族主義被列為持續存在的問題之一。"},{"en":"Ethnic nationalism is strong loyalty to one ethnic group, sometimes at the expense of others.","zh":"種族民族主義是對某一族群的強烈忠誠，有時以犧牲其他群體為代價。"},{"en":"A society may become divided if ethnic nationalism encourages suspicion between groups.","zh":"如果種族民族主義鼓勵群體之間互相猜疑，社會可能分裂。"},{"en":"Ethnic nationalism can create conflict when identity becomes more important than shared citizenship.","zh":"當身份認同變得比共同公民身份更重要，種族民族主義可能造成衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes politics based on ethnic identity.","zh":"這個短語描述以族群身份為本的政治。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tropical deforestation","meaning":"熱帶森林砍伐","examples":[{"en":"Tropical deforestation remains a serious environmental problem.","zh":"熱帶森林砍伐仍是一個嚴重環境問題。"},{"en":"Tropical deforestation means the clearing of forests in tropical regions.","zh":"熱帶森林砍伐是指清除熱帶地區的森林。"},{"en":"Tropical deforestation may happen when rainforest is cleared for cattle farms or crops.","zh":"當雨林被清除作牧牛場或農作物用地時，可能出現熱帶森林砍伐。"},{"en":"It can damage biodiversity and release stored carbon.","zh":"它可以損害生物多樣性並釋放儲存的碳。"},{"en":"This phrase describes forest loss in warm tropical areas.","zh":"這個短語描述溫暖熱帶地區的森林流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"malnutrition","meaning":"營養不良","examples":[{"en":"Malnutrition is one of the problems Gee acknowledges.","zh":"營養不良是 Gee 承認的問題之一。"},{"en":"Malnutrition happens when people do not get enough nutrients or the right balance of food.","zh":"營養不良是指人們得不到足夠營養或正確食物平衡。"},{"en":"Children may suffer malnutrition if their meals lack protein and vitamins.","zh":"如果膳食缺乏蛋白質和維他命，兒童可能營養不良。"},{"en":"Malnutrition can weaken health, growth and learning.","zh":"營養不良可以削弱健康、成長和學習。"},{"en":"This word describes poor nutrition, not simply hunger.","zh":"這個詞描述營養狀況差，而不只是飢餓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cropland losses","meaning":"耕地流失","examples":[{"en":"Cropland losses are mentioned as a continuing problem.","zh":"耕地流失被提及為持續存在的問題。"},{"en":"Cropland losses mean the loss of land suitable for growing crops.","zh":"耕地流失是指適合種植農作物的土地喪失。"},{"en":"A farming region may face cropland losses because of erosion, drought or construction.","zh":"農業地區可能因侵蝕、乾旱或建設而面對耕地流失。"},{"en":"Losing cropland can reduce food production and rural income.","zh":"失去耕地可以減少糧食生產和農村收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the disappearance or damage of farmland.","zh":"這個短語描述農田消失或受損。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"exaggerate the crises","meaning":"誇大危機","examples":[{"en":"Gee claims that Kaplan has exaggerated many of the crises.","zh":"Gee 聲稱 Kaplan 誇大了許多危機。"},{"en":"To exaggerate the crises means to describe the problems as worse than they really are.","zh":"誇大危機，是指把問題描述得比實際更嚴重。"},{"en":"A student may exaggerate a small homework problem and call it a disaster.","zh":"學生可能誇大一個小功課問題，稱它為災難。"},{"en":"Accusations of exaggeration often appear when people disagree about risk.","zh":"當人們對風險有分歧，指責對方誇大通常會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes overstating danger or seriousness.","zh":"這個短語描述過度強調危險或嚴重性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"miss the broad pattern of progress","meaning":"忽略整體進步趨勢","examples":[{"en":"Gee thinks Kaplan has missed the broad pattern of progress.","zh":"Gee 認為 Kaplan 忽略了整體進步趨勢。"},{"en":"To miss the broad pattern of progress means to fail to notice the general trend of improvement.","zh":"忽略整體進步趨勢，是指未能注意到普遍改善的方向。"},{"en":"A teacher may miss the broad pattern of progress if they focus only on one bad quiz.","zh":"如果老師只聚焦一次差小測，可能忽略學生的整體進步趨勢。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts individual problems with the overall direction.","zh":"這個短語把個別問題與整體方向作對比。"},{"en":"It suggests someone is looking too narrowly.","zh":"它暗示某人看得太狹窄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"broad pattern of progress","meaning":"整體進步趨勢","examples":[{"en":"Gee believes there is a broad pattern of progress.","zh":"Gee 相信存在整體進步趨勢。"},{"en":"A broad pattern of progress is a general trend showing improvement across many areas.","zh":"整體進步趨勢，是指在許多範疇顯示改善的一般趨勢。"},{"en":"Better attendance, higher scores and fewer complaints may show a broad pattern of progress in a school.","zh":"更好出席率、更高分數和更少投訴，可能顯示學校的整體進步趨勢。"},{"en":"A broad pattern matters because it is larger than a single example.","zh":"整體趨勢很重要，因為它大於單一例子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wide and repeated improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛而反覆的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"focus on statistics of","meaning":"聚焦於……的統計數據","examples":[{"en":"Gee focuses on statistics of child mortality and longevity.","zh":"Gee 聚焦於兒童死亡率和壽命的統計數據。"},{"en":"To focus on statistics of something means to use numerical data about that issue as the main evidence.","zh":"聚焦於某事的統計數據，是指以該議題的數字資料作為主要證據。"},{"en":"A health report may focus on statistics of smoking and hospital visits.","zh":"健康報告可能聚焦於吸煙和求診的統計數據。"},{"en":"Statistics can support an argument, but they may not show every human experience.","zh":"統計數據可以支持論點，但未必顯示每一種人類經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence based on numbers.","zh":"這個短語描述以數字為本的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"decline in child mortality","meaning":"兒童死亡率下降","examples":[{"en":"Gee points to the decline in child mortality.","zh":"Gee 指出兒童死亡率下降。"},{"en":"Decline in child mortality means fewer children are dying before reaching adulthood.","zh":"兒童死亡率下降，是指較少兒童在成年前死亡。"},{"en":"Vaccination and clean water can lead to a decline in child mortality.","zh":"疫苗接種和清潔食水可以導致兒童死亡率下降。"},{"en":"A falling child mortality rate is often seen as evidence of better public health.","zh":"兒童死亡率下降通常被視為公共衛生改善的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improvement in child survival.","zh":"這個短語描述兒童存活率改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rise in longevity","meaning":"壽命延長","examples":[{"en":"Gee mentions the rise in longevity worldwide.","zh":"Gee 提到全球壽命延長。"},{"en":"Rise in longevity means people are living longer on average.","zh":"壽命延長，是指人們平均活得更久。"},{"en":"Better hospitals and safer childbirth can contribute to a rise in longevity.","zh":"更好的醫院和更安全的分娩可以促成壽命延長。"},{"en":"Longer lifespans may reflect improvements in medicine, food and sanitation.","zh":"更長壽命可能反映醫療、食物和衛生改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increase in average length of life.","zh":"這個短語描述平均生命長度增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"food production","meaning":"糧食生產","examples":[{"en":"Food production has increased in many regions.","zh":"許多地區的糧食生產已經增加。"},{"en":"Food production means the growing, raising or making of food.","zh":"糧食生產是指種植、飼養或製造食物。"},{"en":"Rice farming, fishing and bread-making are all parts of food production.","zh":"種稻、捕魚和製麵包都是糧食生產的一部分。"},{"en":"Higher food production can reduce hunger if food is distributed fairly.","zh":"如果食物分配公平，更高糧食生產可以減少飢餓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the creation of food supplies.","zh":"這個短語描述食物供應的創造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"adult literacy","meaning":"成人識字率","examples":[{"en":"Adult literacy has improved according to Gee’s statistics.","zh":"根據 Gee 的統計數據，成人識字率已有改善。"},{"en":"Adult literacy means the ability of adults to read and write.","zh":"成人識字率是指成年人閱讀和寫作的能力。"},{"en":"Evening classes can improve adult literacy in a community.","zh":"夜校課程可以改善社區的成人識字率。"},{"en":"Higher adult literacy helps people understand contracts, medicine labels and public notices.","zh":"較高成人識字率幫助人們理解合約、藥物標籤和公共通告。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reading and writing ability among adults.","zh":"這個短語描述成年人中的讀寫能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reach the conclusion that","meaning":"得出……的結論","examples":[{"en":"Gee reaches the conclusion that things have never been better.","zh":"Gee 得出情況從未如此好的結論。"},{"en":"To reach the conclusion that something is true means to decide it after considering evidence.","zh":"得出某事為真的結論，是指考慮證據後作出判斷。"},{"en":"After checking the data, a teacher may reach the conclusion that students need more writing practice.","zh":"檢查數據後，老師可能得出學生需要更多寫作練習的結論。"},{"en":"A conclusion should follow from evidence, not just feeling.","zh":"結論應來自證據，而不只是感覺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arriving at a judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述得出判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"things have never been better","meaning":"情況從未如此好","examples":[{"en":"Gee argues that things have never been better.","zh":"Gee 認為情況從未如此好。"},{"en":"Things have never been better means conditions are better now than at any previous time.","zh":"情況從未如此好，是指現時條件比過去任何時候都好。"},{"en":"A coach may say things have never been better after the team wins five matches in a row.","zh":"球隊連勝五場後，教練可能說情況從未如此好。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses strong optimism about present conditions.","zh":"這個短語表達對現況的強烈樂觀。"},{"en":"It can sound exaggerated if serious problems remain.","zh":"如果仍存在嚴重問題，它可能聽起來誇張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"economic indicators","meaning":"經濟指標","examples":[{"en":"Gee’s optimism rests on economic indicators.","zh":"Gee 的樂觀建基於經濟指標。"},{"en":"Economic indicators are numbers that show how an economy is performing.","zh":"經濟指標是顯示經濟表現的數字。"},{"en":"Employment rates, exports and income levels are economic indicators.","zh":"就業率、出口和收入水平都是經濟指標。"},{"en":"Economic indicators can show growth, but they may not show environmental damage.","zh":"經濟指標可以顯示增長，但未必顯示環境破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to data used to judge economic health.","zh":"這個短語指用來判斷經濟健康的數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"gross world product","meaning":"世界生產總值","examples":[{"en":"Gross world product is used as evidence of economic progress.","zh":"世界生產總值被用作經濟進步的證據。"},{"en":"Gross world product means the total value of goods and services produced worldwide.","zh":"世界生產總值是指全球生產的貨品和服務總價值。"},{"en":"Economists may use gross world product to compare global growth over time.","zh":"經濟學家可能使用世界生產總值比較不同時期的全球增長。"},{"en":"A rising gross world product can show more production, but not necessarily fair distribution.","zh":"世界生產總值上升可以顯示生產增加，但不一定表示分配公平。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the global equivalent of total economic output.","zh":"這個短語指全球總經濟產出的概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"total exports","meaning":"出口總額","examples":[{"en":"Total exports are used as an indicator of progress.","zh":"出口總額被用作進步的指標。"},{"en":"Total exports mean the full value or amount of goods and services sold to other countries.","zh":"出口總額是指銷售到其他國家的貨品和服務總價值或總量。"},{"en":"A country’s total exports may rise when its factories sell more products overseas.","zh":"當一個國家的工廠向海外銷售更多產品，出口總額可能上升。"},{"en":"Higher exports can show economic activity, but not all citizens may benefit equally.","zh":"較高出口可以顯示經濟活動，但不是所有公民都同樣受益。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to overall outward trade.","zh":"這個短語指整體對外貿易。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"remarkable sustained and dramatic progress","meaning":"顯著、持續而劇烈的進步","examples":[{"en":"Gee describes economic progress as remarkable, sustained and dramatic.","zh":"Gee 把經濟進步描述為顯著、持續而劇烈。"},{"en":"Remarkable, sustained and dramatic progress means progress that is impressive, continuous and large.","zh":"顯著、持續而劇烈的進步，是指令人印象深刻、連續而巨大的進步。"},{"en":"A student who improves from failing to top marks over two years shows remarkable, sustained and dramatic progress.","zh":"一名學生兩年間由不合格進步至最高分，就是顯著、持續而劇烈的進步。"},{"en":"This phrase is very positive and strongly emphasises improvement.","zh":"這個短語非常正面，強烈強調改善。"},{"en":"It describes progress that is not small, short-lived or ordinary.","zh":"它描述不小、不短暫也不普通的進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"steadily better","meaning":"持續改善","examples":[{"en":"Gee believes life is getting steadily better.","zh":"Gee 相信生活正在持續改善。"},{"en":"Steadily better means improving gradually and continuously.","zh":"持續改善，是指逐漸而不斷變好。"},{"en":"A student’s writing may get steadily better after weekly feedback.","zh":"學生每星期收到回饋後，寫作可能持續改善。"},{"en":"Steady improvement is less dramatic than a sudden jump, but it can be reliable.","zh":"穩定改善不如突然跳升那麼戲劇化，但可以很可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continuous positive change.","zh":"這個短語描述持續正面變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in almost every category","meaning":"在幾乎每個類別中","examples":[{"en":"Gee claims that life is improving in almost every category.","zh":"Gee 聲稱生活在幾乎每個類別中都在改善。"},{"en":"In almost every category means in nearly all areas being measured.","zh":"在幾乎每個類別中，是指在幾乎所有被量度的範疇中。"},{"en":"A school may improve in almost every category, including attendance, grades and behaviour.","zh":"學校可能在出席率、成績和行為等幾乎每個類別中都有改善。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests very broad improvement, though not necessarily universal improvement.","zh":"這個短語暗示非常廣泛的改善，但不一定是全面無例外的改善。"},{"en":"It allows for a few exceptions.","zh":"它容許少數例外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rest heavily on","meaning":"很大程度上依賴……","examples":[{"en":"Gee’s conclusions rest heavily on economic indicators.","zh":"Gee 的結論很大程度上依賴經濟指標。"},{"en":"To rest heavily on something means to depend strongly on it.","zh":"很大程度上依賴某事，是指強烈依靠它。"},{"en":"A student’s argument may rest heavily on one survey result.","zh":"學生的論點可能很大程度上依賴一項問卷結果。"},{"en":"If the supporting evidence is limited, the conclusion may become weaker.","zh":"如果支持證據有限，結論可能變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong dependence on a particular basis.","zh":"這個短語描述對某基礎的強烈依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"annual rise","meaning":"每年增長","examples":[{"en":"Gee points out the annual rise in the global economy.","zh":"Gee 指出全球經濟每年增長。"},{"en":"Annual rise means an increase that happens each year.","zh":"每年增長，是指每一年都出現增加。"},{"en":"A school may report an annual rise in library borrowing.","zh":"學校可能報告圖書借閱量每年增長。"},{"en":"Repeated annual rises can create a long-term upward trend.","zh":"反覆每年增長可以形成長期上升趨勢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes year-by-year growth.","zh":"這個短語描述逐年增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the global economy","meaning":"全球經濟","examples":[{"en":"The global economy has grown steadily in Gee’s account.","zh":"在 Gee 的說法中，全球經濟穩步增長。"},{"en":"The global economy means the connected economic activities of countries around the world.","zh":"全球經濟是指世界各國互相連接的經濟活動。"},{"en":"A factory closure in one country can affect the global economy if it supplies important parts.","zh":"如果某國工廠供應重要零件，它倒閉可能影響全球經濟。"},{"en":"Growth in the global economy can increase trade, jobs and resource use.","zh":"全球經濟增長可以增加貿易、就業和資源使用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the worldwide economic system.","zh":"這個短語指全球經濟系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"more than doubling of","meaning":"超過一倍的增長","examples":[{"en":"Gee notes the more than doubling of gross output per person.","zh":"Gee 指出人均總產出超過一倍的增長。"},{"en":"More than doubling of something means it has increased to over twice its original amount.","zh":"某事超過一倍的增長，是指它增加至超過原來的兩倍。"},{"en":"A school may celebrate the more than doubling of student participation in debate club.","zh":"學校可能慶祝辯論學會學生參與人數超過一倍的增長。"},{"en":"Such growth is large enough to be used as strong evidence of increase.","zh":"這種增長幅度很大，足以用作增長的有力證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increase greater than 100 per cent.","zh":"這個短語描述超過百分之一百的增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"gross output per person","meaning":"人均總產出","examples":[{"en":"Gross output per person has more than doubled over thirty years.","zh":"人均總產出在三十年間增加超過一倍。"},{"en":"Gross output per person means total economic output divided by the number of people.","zh":"人均總產出是指總經濟產出除以人口數。"},{"en":"Economists may use gross output per person to estimate average economic productivity.","zh":"經濟學家可能使用人均總產出估計平均經濟生產力。"},{"en":"A higher figure can suggest economic growth, but it may hide inequality.","zh":"較高數字可以暗示經濟增長，但可能掩蓋不平等。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to average output for each person.","zh":"這個短語指每人的平均產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"over the past thirty years","meaning":"在過去三十年","examples":[{"en":"Gee discusses economic growth over the past thirty years.","zh":"Gee 討論過去三十年的經濟增長。"},{"en":"Over the past thirty years means during the thirty-year period before the time being discussed.","zh":"在過去三十年，是指正在討論的時間之前三十年間。"},{"en":"Over the past thirty years, many classrooms have moved from chalkboards to digital screens.","zh":"在過去三十年，許多課室由黑板轉向電子屏幕。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a long-term time frame for comparison.","zh":"這個短語為比較提供長期時間框架。"},{"en":"It helps readers see change across decades.","zh":"它幫助讀者看見跨數十年的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"world trade","meaning":"世界貿易","examples":[{"en":"World trade has grown strongly.","zh":"世界貿易強勁增長。"},{"en":"World trade means the buying and selling of goods and services between countries.","zh":"世界貿易是指國家之間買賣貨品和服務。"},{"en":"A phone assembled in one country may depend on world trade for parts from many places.","zh":"在一個國家組裝的手機可能依賴世界貿易取得各地零件。"},{"en":"Growing world trade can increase economic links between countries.","zh":"世界貿易增長可以增加國家之間的經濟聯繫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes international commercial exchange.","zh":"這個短語描述國際商業交換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"grow annually","meaning":"每年增長","examples":[{"en":"World trade has grown annually by 6 per cent.","zh":"世界貿易每年增長百分之六。"},{"en":"To grow annually means to increase each year.","zh":"每年增長，是指每一年增加。"},{"en":"A company’s online sales may grow annually if more customers use its website.","zh":"如果更多顧客使用網站，公司的網上銷售可能每年增長。"},{"en":"Annual growth over many years can create a large total increase.","zh":"多年每年增長可以造成很大的總增幅。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated yearly growth.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆逐年增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"tariffs","meaning":"關稅","examples":[{"en":"Tariffs have fallen sharply since 1947.","zh":"自 1947 年以來，關稅大幅下降。"},{"en":"Tariffs are taxes placed on goods imported from other countries.","zh":"關稅是對從其他國家進口的貨品徵收的稅。"},{"en":"A government may reduce tariffs to make imported food cheaper.","zh":"政府可能降低關稅，令進口食品更便宜。"},{"en":"High tariffs can raise product prices and reduce trade.","zh":"高關稅可以提高產品價格並減少貿易。"},{"en":"This word refers to import taxes.","zh":"這個詞指進口稅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fall from…to…","meaning":"從……下降至……","examples":[{"en":"Tariffs have fallen from about 40 per cent to 5 per cent.","zh":"關稅已從約百分之四十下降至百分之五。"},{"en":"Fall from A to B means decrease from the first level to the second level.","zh":"從 A 下降至 B，是指由第一個水平減少到第二個水平。"},{"en":"A student’s screen time may fall from five hours to two hours after a new study plan.","zh":"新溫習計劃後，學生的螢幕時間可能從五小時下降至兩小時。"},{"en":"This structure clearly shows the starting point and final point of a decrease.","zh":"這個結構清楚顯示下降的起點和終點。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing numerical change.","zh":"它適合描述數字變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a product’s price","meaning":"產品價格","examples":[{"en":"Tariffs used to make up a large share of a product’s price.","zh":"關稅以往佔產品價格的一大部分。"},{"en":"A product’s price is the amount of money customers must pay for that item.","zh":"產品價格是顧客購買該物品必須支付的金額。"},{"en":"Transport costs can increase a product’s price in a supermarket.","zh":"運輸成本可以提高超級市場中的產品價格。"},{"en":"Taxes, labour and materials can all affect a product’s price.","zh":"稅項、勞工和材料都可以影響產品價格。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the selling cost of an item.","zh":"這個短語指物品的售價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"skip lightly over","meaning":"輕輕帶過","examples":[{"en":"Gee skips lightly over some serious social problems.","zh":"Gee 輕輕帶過一些嚴重社會問題。"},{"en":"To skip lightly over something means to mention it briefly without giving it enough attention.","zh":"輕輕帶過某事，是指簡短提及但沒有給予足夠重視。"},{"en":"A student may skip lightly over the weakest evidence in their presentation.","zh":"學生可能在匯報中輕輕帶過最薄弱的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests unfair or careless treatment of an important issue.","zh":"這個短語通常暗示對重要議題的處理不公平或草率。"},{"en":"It means the writer does not examine the problem deeply.","zh":"它表示作者沒有深入檢視問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Third World debt","meaning":"第三世界債務","examples":[{"en":"Third World debt is one issue Gee does not emphasise.","zh":"第三世界債務是 Gee 沒有強調的一個議題。"},{"en":"Third World debt means money owed by poorer developing countries to richer countries or institutions.","zh":"第三世界債務是指較貧窮發展中國家欠富裕國家或機構的金錢。"},{"en":"A country with heavy debt may have less money for schools and hospitals.","zh":"債務沉重的國家可能較少資金用於學校和醫院。"},{"en":"Debt can limit development even when global trade grows.","zh":"即使全球貿易增長，債務仍可能限制發展。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to debt burdens in poorer nations.","zh":"這個短語指較貧窮國家的債務負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the daily toll of","meaning":"每日造成的死亡人數","examples":[{"en":"Suzuki mentions the daily toll of child deaths.","zh":"Suzuki 提到每日兒童死亡人數。"},{"en":"The daily toll of something means the number of people harmed or killed each day by it.","zh":"某事每日造成的死亡人數，是指每天因它受害或死亡的人數。"},{"en":"A newspaper may report the daily toll of a heatwave during summer.","zh":"報紙可能在夏季報道熱浪每日造成的死亡人數。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a problem feel urgent because it happens every day.","zh":"這個短語令人覺得問題迫切，因為它每天都發生。"},{"en":"It describes repeated human cost.","zh":"它描述反覆出現的人命代價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"child deaths","meaning":"兒童死亡","examples":[{"en":"The daily toll of child deaths is a serious concern.","zh":"每日兒童死亡人數是一項嚴重關注。"},{"en":"Child deaths are deaths of children, often discussed in health or poverty contexts.","zh":"兒童死亡是指兒童死亡，通常在健康或貧窮語境中討論。"},{"en":"Clean water can reduce child deaths from disease.","zh":"清潔食水可以減少因疾病造成的兒童死亡。"},{"en":"High child deaths show that basic healthcare and nutrition may be failing.","zh":"高兒童死亡數字顯示基本醫療和營養可能失效。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to children dying before adulthood.","zh":"這個短語指兒童在成年前死亡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"easily preventable disease","meaning":"容易預防的疾病","examples":[{"en":"Many children die from easily preventable disease.","zh":"許多兒童死於容易預防的疾病。"},{"en":"An easily preventable disease is an illness that can be avoided with simple, known measures.","zh":"容易預防的疾病，是可以透過簡單而已知措施避免的疾病。"},{"en":"Vaccination can stop many easily preventable diseases.","zh":"疫苗接種可以阻止許多容易預防的疾病。"},{"en":"Deaths from preventable disease often show inequality or poor public health systems.","zh":"因可預防疾病而死亡，通常顯示不平等或公共衛生系統不足。"},{"en":"This phrase describes illness that should not normally cause death.","zh":"這個短語描述正常情況下不應致命的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fail to mention","meaning":"未有提及","examples":[{"en":"Gee fails to mention the widening gap between rich and poor countries.","zh":"Gee 未有提及貧富國家之間不斷擴大的差距。"},{"en":"To fail to mention something means not to include an important point.","zh":"未有提及某事，是指沒有包括一個重要重點。"},{"en":"A student may fail to mention the strongest counterargument in an essay.","zh":"學生可能在作文中未有提及最強的反方論點。"},{"en":"Leaving out important facts can make an argument seem one-sided.","zh":"遺漏重要事實可以令論點看起來片面。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises omission.","zh":"這個短語批評遺漏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"during this period","meaning":"在這段期間","examples":[{"en":"The gap between rich and poor countries increased during this period.","zh":"在這段期間，貧富國家之間的差距擴大。"},{"en":"During this period means within the time being discussed.","zh":"在這段期間，是指在正在討論的時間範圍內。"},{"en":"During this period, the school changed its timetable and exam policy.","zh":"在這段期間，學校更改了時間表和考試政策。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect an event to a specific time frame.","zh":"這個短語幫助把事件連接到特定時間框架。"},{"en":"It is useful for explaining historical change.","zh":"它適合解釋歷史變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the gulf between rich and poor countries","meaning":"貧富國家之間的鴻溝","examples":[{"en":"The gulf between rich and poor countries has increased.","zh":"貧富國家之間的鴻溝已經擴大。"},{"en":"The gulf between rich and poor countries means the large gap in wealth and living conditions between them.","zh":"貧富國家之間的鴻溝，是指它們在財富和生活條件上的巨大差距。"},{"en":"A global charity may focus on reducing the gulf between rich and poor countries.","zh":"全球慈善機構可能專注於縮小貧富國家之間的鴻溝。"},{"en":"If the gulf widens, global progress may not be shared fairly.","zh":"如果鴻溝擴大，全球進步可能未能公平共享。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep international inequality.","zh":"這個短語描述深層國際不平等。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"acknowledge the threats of","meaning":"承認……的威脅","examples":[{"en":"Gee acknowledges the threats of pollution and resource loss.","zh":"Gee 承認污染和資源流失的威脅。"},{"en":"To acknowledge the threats of something means to admit that those dangers exist.","zh":"承認某事的威脅，是指承認那些危險存在。"},{"en":"A school may acknowledge the threats of cyberbullying before creating safety rules.","zh":"學校可能先承認網絡欺凌的威脅，再制定安全規則。"},{"en":"Acknowledging a threat does not always mean believing it will cause disaster.","zh":"承認威脅不一定代表相信它會造成災難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognising danger.","zh":"這個短語描述認可危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"loss of topsoil","meaning":"表土流失","examples":[{"en":"Loss of topsoil threatens long-term food production.","zh":"表土流失威脅長期糧食生產。"},{"en":"Loss of topsoil means the removal or erosion of the fertile upper layer of soil.","zh":"表土流失是指肥沃的土壤上層被移走或侵蝕。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can cause loss of topsoil on unprotected farmland.","zh":"大雨可以造成未受保護農田的表土流失。"},{"en":"Without topsoil, crops may grow poorly and farms may become less productive.","zh":"沒有表土，作物可能生長不良，農場生產力可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious agricultural problem.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重農業問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"pollution of the air","meaning":"空氣污染","examples":[{"en":"Pollution of the air is one of the environmental threats mentioned.","zh":"空氣污染是被提及的環境威脅之一。"},{"en":"Pollution of the air means harmful substances entering the air people breathe.","zh":"空氣污染是指有害物質進入人們呼吸的空氣。"},{"en":"Traffic fumes can cause pollution of the air near busy roads.","zh":"交通廢氣可以在繁忙道路附近造成空氣污染。"},{"en":"Air pollution can lead to asthma, heart problems and poor visibility.","zh":"空氣污染可以導致哮喘、心臟問題和能見度下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes contamination of the atmosphere.","zh":"這個短語描述大氣受污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"contamination of water","meaning":"水源污染","examples":[{"en":"Contamination of water can damage human health and ecosystems.","zh":"水源污染可以損害人類健康和生態系統。"},{"en":"Contamination of water means water becomes polluted by harmful substances.","zh":"水源污染是指水被有害物質污染。"},{"en":"A factory leak can cause contamination of water in a nearby river.","zh":"工廠洩漏可以造成附近河流水源污染。"},{"en":"Contaminated water can spread disease and harm fish.","zh":"受污染的水可以傳播疾病並傷害魚類。"},{"en":"This phrase describes water pollution.","zh":"這個短語描述水污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"little evidence","meaning":"證據不足","examples":[{"en":"Gee concludes that there is little evidence of serious danger.","zh":"Gee 得出結論，認為嚴重危險的證據不足。"},{"en":"Little evidence means not much proof or support.","zh":"證據不足是指沒有太多證明或支持。"},{"en":"A teacher may find little evidence that a student copied if the answers are different.","zh":"如果答案不同，老師可能發現學生抄襲的證據不足。"},{"en":"Saying there is little evidence weakens the claim being discussed.","zh":"說證據不足會削弱正在討論的主張。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lack of strong proof.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏有力證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"serious enough to","meaning":"嚴重到足以……","examples":[{"en":"Gee doubts that environmental threats are serious enough to halt progress.","zh":"Gee 懷疑環境威脅是否嚴重到足以阻止進步。"},{"en":"Serious enough to do something means severe enough to cause that result.","zh":"嚴重到足以造成某結果，是指嚴重程度足以引起該結果。"},{"en":"A fever may be serious enough to keep a student home from school.","zh":"發燒可能嚴重到足以令學生留在家中不上學。"},{"en":"The phrase links the level of danger with a possible consequence.","zh":"這個短語把危險程度與可能後果連接起來。"},{"en":"It asks whether a problem reaches the required level of seriousness.","zh":"它詢問問題是否達到所需嚴重程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"halt human progress","meaning":"阻止人類進步","examples":[{"en":"Gee does not believe environmental problems will halt human progress.","zh":"Gee 不相信環境問題會阻止人類進步。"},{"en":"To halt human progress means to stop people from improving their lives, knowledge or society.","zh":"阻止人類進步，是指阻止人類改善生活、知識或社會。"},{"en":"A war can halt human progress by destroying schools, hospitals and research.","zh":"戰爭可以透過摧毀學校、醫院和研究來阻止人類進步。"},{"en":"If progress is halted, earlier gains may stop growing.","zh":"如果進步被阻止，早前成果可能停止增長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stopping advancement.","zh":"這個短語描述停止進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reverse human progress","meaning":"逆轉人類進步","examples":[{"en":"Gee doubts that environmental threats can reverse human progress.","zh":"Gee 懷疑環境威脅能否逆轉人類進步。"},{"en":"To reverse human progress means to undo improvements and make conditions worse again.","zh":"逆轉人類進步，是指取消改善並令情況再次變差。"},{"en":"A serious epidemic can reverse progress in public health.","zh":"嚴重疫症可以逆轉公共衛生方面的進步。"},{"en":"Reversing progress is worse than slowing progress because earlier gains are lost.","zh":"逆轉進步比放慢進步更嚴重，因為早前成果會失去。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving backward after improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述改善後倒退。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"challenge the notion of","meaning":"質疑……的觀念","examples":[{"en":"Gee challenges the notion of a population crisis.","zh":"Gee 質疑人口危機的觀念。"},{"en":"To challenge the notion of something means to question whether that idea is true.","zh":"質疑某觀念，是指懷疑該想法是否正確。"},{"en":"A student may challenge the notion that good English only means difficult vocabulary.","zh":"學生可能質疑好英文只等於困難詞彙的觀念。"},{"en":"Challenging a notion asks readers to rethink an accepted belief.","zh":"質疑觀念要求讀者重新思考已接受的信念。"},{"en":"This phrase describes questioning an idea.","zh":"這個短語描述懷疑一個想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a population crisis","meaning":"人口危機","examples":[{"en":"Gee rejects the idea of a population crisis.","zh":"Gee 拒絕人口危機的想法。"},{"en":"A population crisis is a serious problem caused by population size, growth or movement.","zh":"人口危機是由人口數量、增長或流動造成的嚴重問題。"},{"en":"A small island may face a population crisis if there is not enough water for residents.","zh":"如果沒有足夠食水供居民使用，小島可能面對人口危機。"},{"en":"Population crises can affect housing, food, jobs and political stability.","zh":"人口危機可以影響住房、食物、工作和政治穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severe pressure linked to population.","zh":"這個短語描述與人口相關的嚴重壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"never before have so many people","meaning":"從未有如此多人……","examples":[{"en":"Gee argues that never before have so many people been so well off.","zh":"Gee 認為從未有如此多人生活如此富足。"},{"en":"Never before have so many people means this number of people has not experienced the situation at any earlier time.","zh":"從未有如此多人，是指在過去任何時候都沒有這麼多人經歷該情況。"},{"en":"Never before have so many students used online lessons at the same time.","zh":"從未有如此多學生同時使用網上課堂。"},{"en":"This inverted structure gives the sentence a formal and dramatic tone.","zh":"這個倒裝結構令句子較正式和戲劇化。"},{"en":"It emphasises that the present situation is historically unusual.","zh":"它強調現況在歷史上不尋常。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be well off","meaning":"生活富裕；境況良好","examples":[{"en":"Gee claims that many people are better off than before.","zh":"Gee 聲稱許多人比以前境況更好。"},{"en":"To be well off means to have enough money or live in comfortable conditions.","zh":"生活富裕或境況良好，是指有足夠金錢或生活條件舒適。"},{"en":"A family may be well off if they can afford good housing, healthcare and education.","zh":"如果家庭負擔得起良好住房、醫療和教育，可能算是生活富裕。"},{"en":"Being well off does not necessarily mean being extremely rich.","zh":"生活富裕不一定代表極其富有。"},{"en":"This phrase describes economic comfort.","zh":"這個短語描述經濟上舒適。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"furthermore","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"Furthermore, Gee sees population growth as a source of new talent.","zh":"此外，Gee 把人口增長視為新人才的來源。"},{"en":"Furthermore means in addition, and it introduces another supporting point.","zh":"furthermore 是指此外，用來引入另一個支持重點。"},{"en":"The school library is quiet; furthermore, it has many useful reference books.","zh":"學校圖書館很安靜；此外，它有許多有用參考書。"},{"en":"This word helps build an argument by adding more evidence.","zh":"這個詞透過加入更多證據幫助建立論點。"},{"en":"It is more formal than “also.”","zh":"它比 also 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a limit to population","meaning":"人口上限","examples":[{"en":"Gee suggests there will never be a limit to population.","zh":"Gee 暗示人口永遠不會有上限。"},{"en":"A limit to population means a maximum number of people that can be supported.","zh":"人口上限是指能夠被支撐的最高人口數。"},{"en":"A classroom has a limit to student numbers because space and teachers are limited.","zh":"課室有學生人數上限，因為空間和教師有限。"},{"en":"If resources are finite, many environmentalists argue that population must have limits.","zh":"如果資源有限，許多環保人士認為人口必須有上限。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a boundary on how large a population can become.","zh":"這個短語描述人口可增長至多大的界限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"more people mean more Einsteins","meaning":"人口越多，天才也越多","examples":[{"en":"Gee suggests that more people mean more Einsteins.","zh":"Gee 暗示人口越多，天才也越多。"},{"en":"More people mean more Einsteins means a larger population may produce more geniuses or talented innovators.","zh":"人口越多，天才也越多，是指人口更大可能產生更多天才或創新人才。"},{"en":"A larger school may discover more talented musicians simply because it has more students.","zh":"較大的學校可能發現更多有才華的音樂人，只因學生人數更多。"},{"en":"This phrase treats population growth as a possible source of human talent.","zh":"這個短語把人口增長視為人類人才的可能來源。"},{"en":"It is an optimistic argument about numbers and creativity.","zh":"它是關於數量和創造力的樂觀論點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"someone’s outlook rests on","meaning":"某人的看法建基於……","examples":[{"en":"Gee’s outlook rests on a small group of scientists.","zh":"Gee 的看法建基於一小群科學家。"},{"en":"Someone’s outlook rests on something means their view depends on that support or belief.","zh":"某人的看法建基於某事，是指其觀點依賴該支持或信念。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may rest on the encouragement of one good teacher.","zh":"學生的信心可能建基於一位好老師的鼓勵。"},{"en":"If the foundation is narrow, the outlook may be open to criticism.","zh":"如果基礎狹窄，該看法可能受到批評。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what supports a person’s view.","zh":"這個短語描述支撐某人觀點的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a tiny minority of","meaning":"極少數的……","examples":[{"en":"Gee’s optimism rests on a tiny minority of scientists.","zh":"Gee 的樂觀建基於極少數科學家。"},{"en":"A tiny minority of people means a very small part of a group.","zh":"極少數人，是指一個群體中非常小的一部分。"},{"en":"Only a tiny minority of students may choose the hardest elective.","zh":"只有極少數學生可能選擇最難的選修科。"},{"en":"Referring to a tiny minority can suggest that the view is not widely accepted.","zh":"提到極少數可以暗示該觀點並不廣泛被接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very small subgroup.","zh":"這個短語描述非常小的子群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have faith in","meaning":"對……有信心","examples":[{"en":"These scientists have faith in science and technology.","zh":"這些科學家對科學與技術有信心。"},{"en":"To have faith in something means to trust it strongly.","zh":"對某事有信心，是指強烈信任它。"},{"en":"Some parents have faith in daily reading as a way to improve language skills.","zh":"有些家長對每日閱讀作為改善語言能力的方法有信心。"},{"en":"Faith can encourage confidence, but it may also overlook limits.","zh":"信心可以帶來自信，但也可能忽略限制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong trust or belief.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈信任或信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the boundless potential of","meaning":"……的無限潛力","examples":[{"en":"They believe in the boundless potential of technology.","zh":"他們相信技術的無限潛力。"},{"en":"The boundless potential of something means its unlimited possible power or usefulness.","zh":"某事的無限潛力，是指其可能力量或用途沒有上限。"},{"en":"Some teachers believe in the boundless potential of online learning.","zh":"有些老師相信網上學習的無限潛力。"},{"en":"Suzuki would question whether any human tool truly has no limits.","zh":"Suzuki 會質疑是否有任何人類工具真正沒有界限。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extreme optimism about what something can do.","zh":"這個短語描述對某事能力的極度樂觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"science and technology","meaning":"科學與技術","examples":[{"en":"Gee trusts the power of science and technology.","zh":"Gee 信任科學與技術的力量。"},{"en":"Science and technology mean scientific knowledge and the tools or methods developed from it.","zh":"科學與技術是指科學知識，以及由此發展出的工具或方法。"},{"en":"Medicine, satellites and clean-energy systems all depend on science and technology.","zh":"醫藥、衛星和清潔能源系統都依賴科學與技術。"},{"en":"Science and technology can solve many problems, but they may also create new ones.","zh":"科學與技術可以解決許多問題，但也可能創造新問題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to knowledge and practical invention together.","zh":"這個短語同時指知識和實際發明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"overcome the physical constraints of","meaning":"克服……的物理限制","examples":[{"en":"Technology may not overcome the physical constraints of air, water and soil.","zh":"技術未必能克服空氣、水和土壤的物理限制。"},{"en":"To overcome the physical constraints of something means to defeat or get beyond its natural limits.","zh":"克服某事的物理限制，是指戰勝或超越其自然界限。"},{"en":"A small classroom cannot easily overcome the physical constraints of limited space.","zh":"小課室不容易克服空間有限的物理限制。"},{"en":"Some limits remain even when technology improves.","zh":"即使科技改善，有些限制仍然存在。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trying to move beyond material limits.","zh":"這個短語描述嘗試超越物質限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"physical constraints","meaning":"物理限制","examples":[{"en":"The planet has physical constraints that technology cannot simply remove.","zh":"地球有技術不能簡單移除的物理限制。"},{"en":"Physical constraints are natural or material limits.","zh":"物理限制是自然或物質上的界限。"},{"en":"A bus has physical constraints because it can carry only a certain number of passengers.","zh":"巴士有物理限制，因為它只能載一定數量乘客。"},{"en":"Ignoring physical constraints can lead to unsafe or unrealistic plans.","zh":"忽視物理限制可能導致不安全或不現實的計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limits created by the real world.","zh":"這個短語描述由現實世界造成的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a much larger population","meaning":"大得多的人口","examples":[{"en":"Gee believes the planet can sustain a much larger population.","zh":"Gee 相信地球可以維持大得多的人口。"},{"en":"A much larger population means many more people than at present or than before.","zh":"大得多的人口，是指比現在或以前多很多的人。"},{"en":"A school would need more classrooms to serve a much larger student population.","zh":"學校若要服務大得多的學生人口，就需要更多課室。"},{"en":"Supporting a larger population requires more food, water, housing and energy.","zh":"支撐更大人口需要更多食物、水、住房和能源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major increase in population size.","zh":"這個短語描述人口規模大幅增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be sustained","meaning":"得以維持","examples":[{"en":"A much larger population may not be sustained indefinitely.","zh":"大得多的人口未必能無限期地得以維持。"},{"en":"To be sustained means to be supported or maintained over time.","zh":"得以維持，是指長時間得到支撐或保持。"},{"en":"A student’s concentration cannot be sustained all night without rest.","zh":"學生如果沒有休息，注意力不能整晚維持。"},{"en":"If resources run out, growth cannot be sustained.","zh":"如果資源耗盡，增長就不能維持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping something going.","zh":"這個短語描述讓某事持續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"final proof","meaning":"最後證據","examples":[{"en":"Gee’s final proof is the rise in living standards.","zh":"Gee 的最後證據是生活水平上升。"},{"en":"Final proof means the last piece of evidence used to support an argument.","zh":"最後證據是用來支持論點的最後一項證據。"},{"en":"A student may use a quote from the text as final proof in an essay.","zh":"學生可能在作文中使用文本引文作為最後證據。"},{"en":"The final proof often gives the argument its closing force.","zh":"最後證據通常為論點帶來收結力量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the last supporting evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述最後的支持證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"general rise in","meaning":"普遍上升","examples":[{"en":"Gee points to the general rise in living standards.","zh":"Gee 指出生活水平普遍上升。"},{"en":"A general rise in something means an overall increase across many cases.","zh":"某事普遍上升，是指在許多情況中整體增加。"},{"en":"A school may see a general rise in reading scores after a new programme.","zh":"學校在推行新計劃後，可能看見閱讀分數普遍上升。"},{"en":"A general rise does not mean every individual improved.","zh":"普遍上升不代表每一個人都有改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad upward movement.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛向上變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"living standards","meaning":"生活水平","examples":[{"en":"Living standards have risen in many countries.","zh":"許多國家的生活水平已經上升。"},{"en":"Living standards mean the quality of people’s everyday life, including income, health, housing and services.","zh":"生活水平是指人們日常生活質素，包括收入、健康、住房和服務。"},{"en":"Clean water and safe housing can raise living standards in a village.","zh":"清潔食水和安全住房可以提高村莊的生活水平。"},{"en":"Economic growth may improve living standards, but not automatically for everyone.","zh":"經濟增長可能改善生活水平，但不會自動令所有人受益。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how well people live.","zh":"這個短語描述人們生活得有多好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"along with","meaning":"伴隨著","examples":[{"en":"Living standards have risen along with population growth.","zh":"生活水平伴隨着人口增長而上升。"},{"en":"Along with means together with or at the same time as something else.","zh":"along with 是指與某事一起或同時發生。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may grow along with better exam results.","zh":"學生信心可能伴隨更好考試成績而增長。"},{"en":"This phrase shows two things happening together, but not necessarily one causing the other.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩件事一起發生，但不一定是一事造成另一事。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing parallel changes.","zh":"它適合描述並行變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"population growth","meaning":"人口增長","examples":[{"en":"Population growth is central to the debate.","zh":"人口增長是這場辯論的核心。"},{"en":"Population growth means an increase in the number of people in a place or in the world.","zh":"人口增長是指某地或全球人口數量增加。"},{"en":"A town may experience population growth after new jobs are created.","zh":"城鎮在新工作機會出現後可能經歷人口增長。"},{"en":"Population growth can support markets, but it can also increase pressure on resources.","zh":"人口增長可以支持市場，但也可以增加資源壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the rise in population size.","zh":"這個短語描述人口規模上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the relationship between","meaning":"……之間的關係","examples":[{"en":"The relationship between population and living standards is complex.","zh":"人口與生活水平之間的關係很複雜。"},{"en":"The relationship between two things means how they are connected or influence each other.","zh":"兩件事之間的關係，是指它們如何相連或互相影響。"},{"en":"A teacher may study the relationship between homework time and test results.","zh":"老師可能研究功課時間與測驗結果之間的關係。"},{"en":"A relationship can be strong, weak, direct or indirect.","zh":"關係可以強、弱、直接或間接。"},{"en":"This phrase describes connection between two factors.","zh":"這個短語描述兩個因素之間的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a correlation, not proof of","meaning":"只是相關性，而非……的證明","examples":[{"en":"The relationship is a correlation, not proof of causal connection.","zh":"這種關係只是相關性，而非因果關係的證明。"},{"en":"A correlation, not proof of something means two things happen together, but one has not been shown to cause the other.","zh":"只是相關性，而非某事的證明，是指兩件事一起發生，但未證明一事造成另一事。"},{"en":"Ice cream sales and swimming accidents may both rise in summer, but that is correlation, not proof of cause.","zh":"雪糕銷售和游泳意外可能都在夏天增加，但那只是相關性，而非因果證明。"},{"en":"This phrase warns readers not to confuse connection with causation.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者不要把關聯與因果混淆。"},{"en":"It is useful in data interpretation.","zh":"它適合用於數據解讀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"causal connection","meaning":"因果關係","examples":[{"en":"Suzuki says the statistics do not prove a causal connection.","zh":"Suzuki 說這些統計數據不能證明因果關係。"},{"en":"A causal connection means one thing directly causes another.","zh":"因果關係是指一件事直接造成另一件事。"},{"en":"If lack of sleep makes a student perform worse, there may be a causal connection.","zh":"如果睡眠不足令學生表現更差，兩者可能有因果關係。"},{"en":"Proving causation requires more than showing two things happen together.","zh":"證明因果需要的不只是顯示兩件事同時發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a cause-and-effect link.","zh":"這個短語描述原因與結果的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ignore basic reality","meaning":"忽視基本現實","examples":[{"en":"Suzuki argues that Gee is ignoring basic reality.","zh":"Suzuki 認為 Gee 正在忽視基本現實。"},{"en":"To ignore basic reality means to overlook clear facts or limits.","zh":"忽視基本現實，是指忽略明顯事實或限制。"},{"en":"A student who plans to finish ten essays in one hour is ignoring basic reality.","zh":"計劃一小時完成十篇作文的學生，就是在忽視基本現實。"},{"en":"Ignoring reality can make an argument sound optimistic but unrealistic.","zh":"忽視現實可以令論點聽起來樂觀但不切實際。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises a view as detached from facts.","zh":"這個短語批評某觀點脫離事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"economic as well as scientific reality","meaning":"經濟及科學現實","examples":[{"en":"Gee is ignoring economic as well as scientific reality.","zh":"Gee 忽視經濟及科學現實。"},{"en":"Economic as well as scientific reality means both financial facts and natural scientific facts.","zh":"經濟及科學現實，是指財務事實和自然科學事實兩者。"},{"en":"A city planning project must consider economic as well as scientific reality, including cost and flood risk.","zh":"城市規劃項目必須考慮經濟及科學現實，包括成本和水災風險。"},{"en":"Ignoring either side can lead to poor decisions.","zh":"忽視任何一方都可能導致差劣決策。"},{"en":"This phrase joins two kinds of real-world limits.","zh":"這個短語連接兩種現實世界限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"inherit a bank account","meaning":"繼承一個銀行戶口","examples":[{"en":"Suzuki uses the example of inheriting a bank account.","zh":"Suzuki 使用繼承一個銀行戶口的例子。"},{"en":"To inherit a bank account means to receive it from someone after they die or pass it on.","zh":"繼承一個銀行戶口，是指在某人去世或傳給你後接收它。"},{"en":"A child may inherit a bank account from a grandparent.","zh":"孩子可能從祖父母繼承一個銀行戶口。"},{"en":"Suzuki uses this example to explain the difference between using interest and using capital.","zh":"Suzuki 使用這個例子來解釋使用利息和使用本金的分別。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a financial metaphor for natural resources.","zh":"這個短語引入關於自然資源的財務比喻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"earn interest annually","meaning":"每年賺取利息","examples":[{"en":"The bank account earns interest annually.","zh":"這個銀行戶口每年賺取利息。"},{"en":"To earn interest annually means to receive extra money from savings each year.","zh":"每年賺取利息，是指每年從儲蓄中得到額外金錢。"},{"en":"A savings account may earn interest annually if money is left in the bank.","zh":"如果錢留在銀行，儲蓄戶口可能每年賺取利息。"},{"en":"Interest can be used without spending the original savings.","zh":"利息可以被使用，而不用花掉原本儲蓄。"},{"en":"This phrase supports Suzuki’s metaphor of living off renewable income.","zh":"這個短語支持 Suzuki 關於靠可再生收入生活的比喻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"withdraw money","meaning":"提款","examples":[{"en":"A person can withdraw money from the account each year.","zh":"一個人每年可以從戶口提款。"},{"en":"To withdraw money means to take money out of a bank account.","zh":"提款是指從銀行戶口取出金錢。"},{"en":"A student may withdraw money from an ATM before buying lunch.","zh":"學生可能在買午餐前從自動櫃員機提款。"},{"en":"If withdrawals are too large, the account balance will fall.","zh":"如果提款額太大，戶口結餘會下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking funds out.","zh":"這個短語描述取出資金。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"suppose we start to","meaning":"假設我們開始……","examples":[{"en":"Suppose we start to increase our withdrawals each year.","zh":"假設我們開始每年增加提款額。"},{"en":"Suppose we start to means imagine that we begin to do something.","zh":"假設我們開始，是指想像我們開始做某事。"},{"en":"Suppose we start to spend more than we earn each month; our savings will fall.","zh":"假設我們開始每月花多於收入，儲蓄就會下降。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a hypothetical example.","zh":"這個短語引入假設例子。"},{"en":"It helps readers test an idea through imagination.","zh":"它幫助讀者透過想像測試一個想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"increase our withdrawals","meaning":"增加提款額","examples":[{"en":"Increasing withdrawals will eventually drain the account.","zh":"增加提款額最終會耗盡戶口。"},{"en":"To increase our withdrawals means to take out more money than before.","zh":"增加提款額，是指取出比以前更多的金錢。"},{"en":"A family that increases its withdrawals from savings every month may soon have no savings left.","zh":"每月增加從儲蓄提款的家庭，很快可能沒有儲蓄剩下。"},{"en":"Larger withdrawals reduce the balance more quickly.","zh":"更大的提款會更快降低結餘。"},{"en":"This phrase represents using resources faster than they are replaced.","zh":"這個短語代表使用資源的速度快於補充速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"yield cash","meaning":"產生現金","examples":[{"en":"For many years, the account would still yield cash.","zh":"多年來，該戶口仍會產生現金。"},{"en":"To yield cash means to produce or provide money.","zh":"產生現金，是指產出或提供金錢。"},{"en":"A small shop may yield cash every day if customers keep buying.","zh":"如果顧客持續購買，小店每天都可能產生現金。"},{"en":"A source can still yield cash for a while even if it is being slowly depleted.","zh":"即使來源正慢慢被耗盡，它仍可能一段時間內產生現金。"},{"en":"This phrase describes producing financial return.","zh":"這個短語描述產生金錢回報。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"it would be foolish to conclude that","meaning":"認為……是愚蠢的","examples":[{"en":"It would be foolish to conclude that we could withdraw money forever.","zh":"認為我們可以永遠提款是愚蠢的。"},{"en":"It would be foolish to conclude that means it would be unwise to believe that result.","zh":"認為某事是愚蠢的，是指相信該結論並不明智。"},{"en":"It would be foolish to conclude that one good test means no more revision is needed.","zh":"認為一次好測驗代表不用再溫習，是愚蠢的。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against a careless conclusion.","zh":"這個短語警告不要草率下結論。"},{"en":"It shows that short-term evidence may not prove long-term safety.","zh":"它顯示短期證據未必能證明長期安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"keep drawing more from","meaning":"不斷從……提取更多","examples":[{"en":"We cannot keep drawing more from the account indefinitely.","zh":"我們不能無限期地不斷從戶口提取更多。"},{"en":"To keep drawing more from something means to continue taking increasing amounts from it.","zh":"不斷從某物提取更多，是指持續從中取出越來越多。"},{"en":"A student cannot keep drawing more time from sleep without becoming tired.","zh":"學生不能不斷從睡眠中提取更多時間而不變得疲倦。"},{"en":"Taking more and more from a limited source eventually causes depletion.","zh":"從有限來源取得越來越多，最終會造成耗盡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unsustainable extraction.","zh":"這個短語描述不可持續的提取。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"indefinitely","meaning":"無限期地","examples":[{"en":"The planet’s resources cannot be used indefinitely.","zh":"地球資源不能被無限期地使用。"},{"en":"Indefinitely means without a fixed end or limit in time.","zh":"無限期地，是指沒有固定結束時間或時間限制。"},{"en":"A student cannot delay homework indefinitely because the deadline will arrive.","zh":"學生不能無限期地拖延功課，因為截止日期會到來。"},{"en":"If something cannot continue indefinitely, it must eventually stop or change.","zh":"如果某事不能無限期持續，它最終必須停止或改變。"},{"en":"This word describes endless continuation.","zh":"這個詞描述無止境的延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"ocean fisheries","meaning":"海洋漁業","examples":[{"en":"Ocean fisheries show that humans are using up natural capital.","zh":"海洋漁業顯示人類正在耗用自然資本。"},{"en":"Ocean fisheries are areas or industries where fish are caught from the sea.","zh":"海洋漁業是從海洋捕魚的地區或行業。"},{"en":"A coastal town may depend on ocean fisheries for jobs and food.","zh":"沿海城鎮可能依賴海洋漁業提供工作和食物。"},{"en":"Overfishing can damage ocean fisheries and reduce future catches.","zh":"過度捕魚可以損害海洋漁業並減少未來捕獲量。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to fish resources and fishing activity in the oceans.","zh":"這個短語指海洋中的魚類資源和捕魚活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"use up","meaning":"耗盡；用光","examples":[{"en":"Humans are using up the ecological capital of the planet.","zh":"人類正在耗盡地球的生態資本。"},{"en":"To use up something means to consume all or most of it.","zh":"耗盡某物，是指消耗掉全部或大部分。"},{"en":"A student may use up all their phone battery before getting home.","zh":"學生可能在回家前用光手機電量。"},{"en":"If people use up resources faster than they are renewed, shortages follow.","zh":"如果人們使用資源的速度快於其再生速度，就會出現短缺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes depletion through use.","zh":"這個短語描述透過使用造成耗盡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"ecological capital","meaning":"生態資本","examples":[{"en":"We are using up the ecological capital of the planet.","zh":"我們正在耗用地球的生態資本。"},{"en":"Ecological capital means the natural resources and systems that support life and economies.","zh":"生態資本是指支持生命和經濟的自然資源和系統。"},{"en":"Forests, fisheries, soil and clean water are forms of ecological capital.","zh":"森林、漁業、土壤和清潔水都是生態資本。"},{"en":"If ecological capital is spent like savings, future generations lose support.","zh":"如果生態資本像儲蓄一樣被花掉，未來世代就會失去支撐。"},{"en":"This phrase describes nature as a life-supporting asset.","zh":"這個短語把自然描述為支撐生命的資產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"biodiversity","meaning":"生物多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Biodiversity is part of the planet’s ecological capital.","zh":"生物多樣性是地球生態資本的一部分。"},{"en":"Biodiversity means the variety of living things in an ecosystem or on Earth.","zh":"生物多樣性是指生態系統或地球上生命形式的多樣程度。"},{"en":"A healthy forest has biodiversity because it contains many plants, insects, birds and animals.","zh":"健康森林有生物多樣性，因為它包含許多植物、昆蟲、鳥類和動物。"},{"en":"Losing biodiversity can make ecosystems weaker and less stable.","zh":"失去生物多樣性可以令生態系統較弱且較不穩定。"},{"en":"This word refers to the richness of life forms.","zh":"這個詞指生命形式的豐富程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"live off the interest","meaning":"靠利息生活","examples":[{"en":"Suzuki argues that we should live off the interest rather than consume the capital.","zh":"Suzuki 認為我們應靠利息生活，而不是消耗本金。"},{"en":"To live off the interest means to use only the renewable income, not the original savings.","zh":"靠利息生活，是指只使用可再生收入，而不是原本儲蓄。"},{"en":"A family with savings may live off the interest if the interest pays their monthly bills.","zh":"如果利息足夠支付每月賬單，有儲蓄的家庭可能靠利息生活。"},{"en":"In Suzuki’s metaphor, nature’s renewable output is the interest, and natural capital is the savings.","zh":"在 Suzuki 的比喻中，自然的可再生產出是利息，自然資本是儲蓄。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sustainable use instead of depletion.","zh":"這個短語描述可持續使用，而不是耗盡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"dangerous deception","meaning":"危險的錯覺","examples":[{"en":"It is a dangerous deception to think economies can keep growing forever.","zh":"認為經濟可以永遠增長是一種危險的錯覺。"},{"en":"A dangerous deception is a false belief that can lead to harmful decisions.","zh":"危險的錯覺，是可以導致有害決定的錯誤信念。"},{"en":"Believing that sleep is unnecessary before exams is a dangerous deception.","zh":"相信考試前不需要睡眠是一種危險的錯覺。"},{"en":"Such deception is dangerous because it hides real limits or risks.","zh":"這種錯覺危險，因為它掩蓋真正限制或風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a misleading idea with serious consequences.","zh":"這個短語描述具嚴重後果的誤導想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"human-created artifice","meaning":"人類創造的人為結構","examples":[{"en":"Economies are described as a human-created artifice.","zh":"經濟被描述為人類創造的人為結構。"},{"en":"A human-created artifice is a system or structure invented by people, not nature.","zh":"人類創造的人為結構，是由人發明而不是自然產生的系統或結構。"},{"en":"A timetable is a human-created artifice that organises school life.","zh":"時間表是人類創造的人為結構，用來組織學校生活。"},{"en":"Because economies are human-made, they depend on natural systems rather than replacing them.","zh":"因為經濟是人造的，它們依賴自然系統，而不能取代自然系統。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts artificial systems with natural reality.","zh":"這個短語把人造系統與自然現實作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"keep the indicators rising","meaning":"令指標持續上升","examples":[{"en":"Gee believes economies can keep the indicators rising.","zh":"Gee 相信經濟可以令指標持續上升。"},{"en":"To keep the indicators rising means to make the measured numbers continue increasing.","zh":"令指標持續上升，是指令被量度的數字繼續增加。"},{"en":"A school may try to keep attendance indicators rising by supporting absent students.","zh":"學校可能透過支援缺席學生，令出席率指標持續上升。"},{"en":"Rising indicators can look positive even if deeper problems are hidden.","zh":"指標上升可能看似正面，即使深層問題被隱藏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes maintaining upward statistical trends.","zh":"這個短語描述維持向上的統計趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"life support systems","meaning":"生命維持系統","examples":[{"en":"The planet’s life support systems are continuing to decline.","zh":"地球的生命維持系統正繼續衰退。"},{"en":"Life support systems are natural systems that make life possible, such as air, water, soil and ecosystems.","zh":"生命維持系統是令生命得以存在的自然系統，例如空氣、水、土壤和生態系統。"},{"en":"Forests and oceans are life support systems because they help regulate air and climate.","zh":"森林和海洋是生命維持系統，因為它們幫助調節空氣和氣候。"},{"en":"If these systems decline, human economies and health are also at risk.","zh":"如果這些系統衰退，人類經濟和健康也有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes nature’s basic support for life.","zh":"這個短語描述自然對生命的基本支撐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"continue to decline","meaning":"繼續衰退","examples":[{"en":"Natural life support systems continue to decline.","zh":"自然生命維持系統繼續衰退。"},{"en":"To continue to decline means to keep getting worse or weaker.","zh":"繼續衰退，是指持續變差或變弱。"},{"en":"A student’s health may continue to decline if they sleep only four hours every night.","zh":"如果學生每晚只睡四小時，健康可能繼續衰退。"},{"en":"Continued decline is worrying because the problem is not stopping.","zh":"持續衰退令人憂慮，因為問題沒有停止。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing deterioration.","zh":"這個短語描述正在持續惡化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"value system","meaning":"價值體系","examples":[{"en":"Suzuki criticises the value system that dominates the media.","zh":"Suzuki 批評主導媒體的價值體系。"},{"en":"A value system is a set of beliefs about what is important or worth pursuing.","zh":"價值體系是一套關於甚麼重要或值得追求的信念。"},{"en":"A school’s value system may emphasise effort, respect and honesty.","zh":"學校的價值體系可能強調努力、尊重和誠實。"},{"en":"A value system shapes what people praise, buy and ignore.","zh":"價值體系塑造人們讚賞、購買和忽視甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beliefs guiding judgement and behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述指導判斷和行為的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"dominate the popular media","meaning":"主導大眾傳媒","examples":[{"en":"A particular value system dominates the popular media.","zh":"某種價值體系主導大眾傳媒。"},{"en":"To dominate the popular media means to have strong influence over newspapers, television, websites and other mass outlets.","zh":"主導大眾傳媒，是指對報章、電視、網站和其他大眾渠道有強大影響力。"},{"en":"Celebrity culture may dominate the popular media during award season.","zh":"在頒獎季，名人文化可能主導大眾傳媒。"},{"en":"When one idea dominates media, other viewpoints may receive less attention.","zh":"當一種想法主導媒體，其他觀點可能較少受到注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong control over public communication.","zh":"這個短語描述對公共傳播的強大控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"promote the delusion that","meaning":"宣揚……的錯覺","examples":[{"en":"The media promotes the delusion that resources can expand forever.","zh":"媒體宣揚資源可以永遠擴張的錯覺。"},{"en":"To promote the delusion that something is true means to spread a false belief.","zh":"宣揚某事為真的錯覺，是指傳播錯誤信念。"},{"en":"Advertising may promote the delusion that buying more things will always make people happy.","zh":"廣告可能宣揚買更多東西一定令人快樂的錯覺。"},{"en":"A delusion is dangerous when it makes people ignore limits.","zh":"當錯覺令人忽視限制，它就很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes spreading a misleading belief.","zh":"這個短語描述傳播誤導性信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"resources and the economy","meaning":"資源與經濟","examples":[{"en":"Many people believe resources and the economy can keep expanding.","zh":"許多人相信資源與經濟可以持續擴張。"},{"en":"Resources and the economy refer to natural supplies and the human system of production and trade.","zh":"資源與經濟是指自然供應，以及人類的生產和貿易系統。"},{"en":"A country may grow its economy while using more water, fuel and land resources.","zh":"一個國家可能在使用更多水、燃料和土地資源的同時發展經濟。"},{"en":"Suzuki argues that the economy depends on resources, not the other way round.","zh":"Suzuki 認為經濟依賴資源，而不是相反。"},{"en":"This phrase links natural limits with economic activity.","zh":"這個短語把自然限制與經濟活動連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"expand indefinitely","meaning":"無限擴張","examples":[{"en":"Resources and the economy cannot continue to expand indefinitely.","zh":"資源與經濟不能繼續無限擴張。"},{"en":"To expand indefinitely means to keep growing without any end or limit.","zh":"無限擴張，是指沒有終點或限制地持續增長。"},{"en":"A school cannot expand indefinitely if the campus has limited space.","zh":"如果校園空間有限，學校不能無限擴張。"},{"en":"Unlimited expansion is unrealistic when space and resources are finite.","zh":"當空間和資源有限，無限擴張並不現實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes endless growth.","zh":"這個短語描述無止境增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"blind the public to","meaning":"令公眾看不見……","examples":[{"en":"This value system blinds the public to environmental warnings.","zh":"這種價值體系令公眾看不見環境警告。"},{"en":"To blind the public to something means to stop ordinary people from seeing or understanding it clearly.","zh":"令公眾看不見某事，是指阻止普通人清楚看見或理解它。"},{"en":"Constant advertising can blind consumers to the environmental cost of fast fashion.","zh":"持續廣告可以令消費者看不見快速時裝的環境成本。"},{"en":"If people are blinded to risks, they may ignore urgent action.","zh":"如果人們看不見風險，就可能忽視緊急行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hiding awareness or understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述隱藏意識或理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the urgency and credibility of","meaning":"……的迫切性和可信性","examples":[{"en":"The public may ignore the urgency and credibility of environmental warnings.","zh":"公眾可能忽視環境警告的迫切性和可信性。"},{"en":"Urgency and credibility mean how immediate and believable something is.","zh":"迫切性和可信性，是指某事有多即時重要和可信。"},{"en":"A fire alarm has urgency and credibility when smoke is already visible.","zh":"當煙霧已經可見，火警就有迫切性和可信性。"},{"en":"If people doubt credibility, they may delay action even when the issue is urgent.","zh":"如果人們懷疑可信性，即使事情迫切，他們也可能拖延行動。"},{"en":"This phrase joins seriousness of timing with trustworthiness.","zh":"這個短語結合時間上的嚴重性與可信程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"environmental warnings","meaning":"環境警告","examples":[{"en":"Environmental warnings should be taken seriously.","zh":"環境警告應該被認真看待。"},{"en":"Environmental warnings are messages that alert people to dangers facing nature and human life.","zh":"環境警告是提醒人們自然和人類生活面對危險的訊息。"},{"en":"A warning about water pollution is an environmental warning.","zh":"關於水污染的警告就是環境警告。"},{"en":"Ignoring environmental warnings can delay action until damage becomes harder to fix.","zh":"忽視環境警告可能拖延行動，直到損害更難修復。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to alerts about environmental danger.","zh":"這個短語指關於環境危險的警示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"an environmental crisis confronts us","meaning":"我們正面對環境危機","examples":[{"en":"Suzuki argues that an environmental crisis confronts us.","zh":"Suzuki 認為我們正面對環境危機。"},{"en":"If an environmental crisis confronts us, we are facing a serious environmental problem directly.","zh":"如果我們正面對環境危機，就表示我們正直接面對嚴重環境問題。"},{"en":"A city may say a waste crisis confronts it when landfills are nearly full.","zh":"當堆填區接近爆滿，城市可能說它正面對廢物危機。"},{"en":"The verb “confronts” makes the crisis feel immediate and unavoidable.","zh":"confronts 這個動詞令危機感覺即時而無法逃避。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious problem now facing people.","zh":"這個短語描述人們現在面對的嚴重問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"use the information in","meaning":"使用……中的資料","examples":[{"en":"Students use the information in the passage to match opinions with people.","zh":"學生使用篇章中的資料把觀點與人物配對。"},{"en":"To use the information in a text means to base answers on what the text says.","zh":"使用文本中的資料，是指根據文本所說內容作答。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should use the information in the passage, not outside knowledge.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應使用篇章中的資料，而不是外部知識。"},{"en":"This instruction keeps answers evidence-based.","zh":"這項指示令答案以證據為本。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds students where their support must come from.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生支持答案的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"match the people with the opinions","meaning":"將人物與觀點配對","examples":[{"en":"The task asks students to match the people with the opinions listed below.","zh":"題目要求學生將人物與下方列出的觀點配對。"},{"en":"To match the people with the opinions means to connect each view to the person who holds it.","zh":"將人物與觀點配對，是指把每個看法連接到持有該看法的人。"},{"en":"Students may match “technology can solve the problem” with the writer who believes in innovation.","zh":"學生可能把「技術可以解決問題」配對到相信創新的作者。"},{"en":"This task tests understanding of viewpoints, not only vocabulary.","zh":"這項任務測試對觀點的理解，而不只是詞彙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an opinion-matching exercise.","zh":"這個短語描述觀點配對練習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"listed below","meaning":"列於下方","examples":[{"en":"The opinions are listed below the question.","zh":"觀點列於題目下方。"},{"en":"Listed below means written in a list underneath the instruction or question.","zh":"列於下方，是指以清單形式寫在指示或題目之下。"},{"en":"Students should choose from the options listed below the table.","zh":"學生應從表格下方列出的選項中選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase tells readers where to look for answer choices.","zh":"這個短語告訴讀者到哪裏找答案選項。"},{"en":"It is common in exam instructions.","zh":"它常見於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"more than one correct answer","meaning":"多於一個正確答案","examples":[{"en":"There may be more than one correct answer.","zh":"可能有多於一個正確答案。"},{"en":"More than one correct answer means two or more answers may be accepted.","zh":"多於一個正確答案，是指兩個或以上答案可能被接受。"},{"en":"In a matching task, more than one correct answer may apply to the same opinion.","zh":"在配對題中，同一觀點可能有多於一個正確答案。"},{"en":"Students should not stop after finding only one possible answer if the instruction allows more.","zh":"如果指示容許多於一個答案，學生找到一個可能答案後不應立即停止。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that answers may not be one-to-one.","zh":"這個短語提醒答案未必是一對一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"environmental challenges","meaning":"環境挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Some writers believe environmental challenges will be solved by technology.","zh":"有些作者相信環境挑戰會由技術解決。"},{"en":"Environmental challenges are difficult problems involving nature, resources or pollution.","zh":"環境挑戰是涉及自然、資源或污染的困難問題。"},{"en":"Plastic waste and water shortages are environmental challenges for many cities.","zh":"塑膠廢物和水資源短缺是許多城市的環境挑戰。"},{"en":"Challenges become more serious when they threaten health or future resources.","zh":"當挑戰威脅健康或未來資源，它們會變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes problems connected with the environment.","zh":"這個短語描述與環境相關的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be met by","meaning":"由……應對；以……解決","examples":[{"en":"Environmental challenges may be met by technological advances.","zh":"環境挑戰可能由技術進步應對。"},{"en":"To be met by something means to be dealt with or answered by it.","zh":"由某事應對，是指由它處理或回應問題。"},{"en":"A school’s need for extra lessons may be met by online classes.","zh":"學校對額外課堂的需要可能由網上課程解決。"},{"en":"If a challenge is met successfully, the problem becomes easier to manage.","zh":"如果挑戰被成功應對，問題就較容易管理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a solution responding to a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述解決方法回應問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"technological advances","meaning":"技術進步","examples":[{"en":"Gee places great trust in technological advances.","zh":"Gee 對技術進步抱有很大信任。"},{"en":"Technological advances are improvements in tools, machines, systems or scientific applications.","zh":"技術進步是工具、機器、系統或科學應用方面的改善。"},{"en":"Solar panels and better batteries are technological advances in energy.","zh":"太陽能板和更好的電池是能源方面的技術進步。"},{"en":"Advances can solve problems, but they may not remove every natural limit.","zh":"技術進步可以解決問題，但未必能移除每一個自然限制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes progress in technology.","zh":"這個短語描述科技上的進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"patterns of consumption","meaning":"消費模式","examples":[{"en":"Our patterns of consumption are using up natural resources.","zh":"我們的消費模式正在耗盡自然資源。"},{"en":"Patterns of consumption are the regular ways people buy, use and waste goods or resources.","zh":"消費模式是人們購買、使用和浪費貨品或資源的規律方式。"},{"en":"A family’s pattern of consumption may include frequent takeaway meals and online shopping.","zh":"家庭的消費模式可能包括經常外賣和網購。"},{"en":"Unsustainable consumption patterns can increase pollution and resource depletion.","zh":"不可持續的消費模式可以增加污染和資源耗竭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated habits of using resources.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆使用資源的習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"crises beginning in","meaning":"始於……的危機","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan believes crises beginning in poorer regions may spread.","zh":"Kaplan 相信始於較貧困地區的危機可能蔓延。"},{"en":"Crises beginning in a place are serious problems that start there.","zh":"始於某地的危機，是指從那裏開始的嚴重問題。"},{"en":"A food shortage beginning in one province may affect nearby cities.","zh":"始於某省的食物短缺可能影響附近城市。"},{"en":"Local crises can spread when systems are connected.","zh":"當系統互相連接，本地危機可以蔓延。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the starting location of a crisis.","zh":"這個短語指出危機開始的地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the Third World","meaning":"第三世界","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses problems in the Third World.","zh":"篇章討論第三世界的問題。"},{"en":"The Third World is an older term for poorer developing countries.","zh":"第三世界是指較貧窮發展中國家的舊稱。"},{"en":"Writers today often prefer terms such as developing countries or low-income countries.","zh":"現今作者通常較喜歡使用發展中國家或低收入國家等說法。"},{"en":"In older texts, the Third World often refers to places facing poverty and development challenges.","zh":"在較舊文本中，第三世界通常指面對貧窮和發展挑戰的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes less economically developed regions in older terminology.","zh":"這個短語用較舊術語描述經濟發展程度較低的地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"spread to","meaning":"蔓延至……","examples":[{"en":"Environmental crises may spread to developed countries.","zh":"環境危機可能蔓延至發達國家。"},{"en":"To spread to a place means to move or extend there.","zh":"蔓延至某地，是指移動或擴展到那裏。"},{"en":"A flu outbreak may spread to nearby schools if students continue attending class while sick.","zh":"如果學生生病仍上課，流感爆發可能蔓延至附近學校。"},{"en":"Problems spread when people, trade or natural systems connect places.","zh":"當人、貿易或自然系統連接不同地方，問題就會蔓延。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement from one area to another.","zh":"這個短語描述由一地移向另一地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"developed countries","meaning":"發達國家","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan believes crises may eventually reach developed countries.","zh":"Kaplan 相信危機最終可能到達發達國家。"},{"en":"Developed countries are wealthy, industrialised countries with advanced infrastructure.","zh":"發達國家是富裕、工業化並具先進基礎架構的國家。"},{"en":"Developed countries may still face environmental risks despite strong economies.","zh":"即使經濟強大，發達國家仍可能面對環境風險。"},{"en":"Global problems can reach developed countries through migration, markets and climate systems.","zh":"全球問題可以透過移民、市場和氣候系統到達發達國家。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to economically advanced nations.","zh":"這個短語指經濟先進國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"scientific progress","meaning":"科學進步","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe scientific progress can solve environmental problems.","zh":"有些人相信科學進步可以解決環境問題。"},{"en":"Scientific progress means improvement in scientific knowledge and methods.","zh":"科學進步是指科學知識和方法的改善。"},{"en":"New vaccines are an example of scientific progress in medicine.","zh":"新疫苗是醫學科學進步的例子。"},{"en":"Scientific progress can create solutions, but it may still depend on political and social action.","zh":"科學進步可以創造解決方法，但仍可能依賴政治和社會行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes advancement in science.","zh":"這個短語描述科學上的進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"enable something to","meaning":"使……能夠","examples":[{"en":"Scientific progress may enable the planet to sustain more people.","zh":"科學進步可能使地球能夠維持更多人口。"},{"en":"To enable something to happen means to make it possible.","zh":"使某事能夠發生，是指令它成為可能。"},{"en":"Online lessons enable students to study from home.","zh":"網上課堂使學生能夠在家學習。"},{"en":"A tool enables a result when the result could not easily happen without it.","zh":"當沒有某工具就難以出現某結果時，該工具使該結果成為可能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making something possible.","zh":"這個短語描述令某事可行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"sustain increased population","meaning":"維持增加的人口","examples":[{"en":"Technology may help the planet sustain increased population.","zh":"技術可能幫助地球維持增加的人口。"},{"en":"To sustain increased population means to support a larger number of people over time.","zh":"維持增加的人口，是指長時間支撐更多人口。"},{"en":"A town needs more schools and clinics to sustain an increased population.","zh":"城鎮需要更多學校和診所來維持增加的人口。"},{"en":"Sustaining more people requires food, water, housing and waste systems.","zh":"支撐更多人口需要食物、水、住房和廢物系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes supporting population growth.","zh":"這個短語描述支撐人口增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"social and political infrastructure","meaning":"社會及政治基礎架構","examples":[{"en":"Social and political infrastructure could collapse under pressure.","zh":"社會及政治基礎架構可能在壓力下崩潰。"},{"en":"Social and political infrastructure means the institutions and systems that keep society and government working.","zh":"社會及政治基礎架構是維持社會和政府運作的機構和系統。"},{"en":"Schools, courts, public offices and welfare systems are part of social and political infrastructure.","zh":"學校、法院、公共辦公室和福利系統都是社會及政治基礎架構的一部分。"},{"en":"If this infrastructure collapses, people may lose order, services and protection.","zh":"如果這種基礎架構崩潰，人們可能失去秩序、服務和保護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes basic systems of society and government.","zh":"這個短語描述社會和政府的基本系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"collapse","meaning":"崩潰","examples":[{"en":"Ecosystems and social systems may collapse if pressure continues.","zh":"如果壓力持續，生態系統和社會系統可能崩潰。"},{"en":"To collapse means to fail suddenly or break down completely.","zh":"崩潰是指突然失效或完全瓦解。"},{"en":"A school timetable may collapse if half the teachers are absent.","zh":"如果一半老師缺席，學校時間表可能崩潰。"},{"en":"Collapse happens when a system can no longer carry the pressure placed on it.","zh":"當系統再不能承受施加於它的壓力，就會崩潰。"},{"en":"This word describes serious failure.","zh":"這個詞描述嚴重失效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"at critical risk","meaning":"處於嚴重風險中","examples":[{"en":"Suzuki believes Earth’s life support systems are at critical risk.","zh":"Suzuki 相信地球的生命維持系統處於嚴重風險中。"},{"en":"At critical risk means in serious and urgent danger.","zh":"處於嚴重風險中，是指面對嚴重而迫切的危險。"},{"en":"A patient may be at critical risk if their breathing becomes unstable.","zh":"如果病人呼吸變得不穩定，可能處於嚴重風險中。"},{"en":"When something is at critical risk, delay can make the damage worse.","zh":"當某事處於嚴重風險中，拖延可能令損害惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes danger at a very serious level.","zh":"這個短語描述非常嚴重程度的危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"threat to progress","meaning":"對進步的威脅","examples":[{"en":"Gee claims environmental problems are not a threat to progress.","zh":"Gee 聲稱環境問題不是對進步的威脅。"},{"en":"A threat to progress is something that may stop or reverse improvement.","zh":"對進步的威脅，是可能阻止或逆轉改善的事物。"},{"en":"Poor internet access can be a threat to progress in online learning.","zh":"網絡連接差可以是網上學習進步的威脅。"},{"en":"Whether something is a threat depends on how serious and widespread its effects are.","zh":"某事是否構成威脅，取決於其影響有多嚴重和廣泛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a danger to continued improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述對持續改善的危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"choose one phrase from","meaning":"從……中選出一個短語","examples":[{"en":"Students choose one phrase from the list to complete each sentence.","zh":"學生從清單中選出一個短語完成每句。"},{"en":"To choose one phrase from a list means to select one option provided.","zh":"從清單中選出一個短語，是指選擇所提供的一個選項。"},{"en":"In a grammar exercise, students may choose one phrase from a box of answers.","zh":"在文法練習中，學生可能從答案框中選出一個短語。"},{"en":"This instruction limits students to the given choices.","zh":"這項指示限制學生只能使用給定選項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes selecting from provided options.","zh":"這個短語描述從提供的選項中選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"complete each sentence","meaning":"完成每個句子","examples":[{"en":"The phrases are used to complete each sentence.","zh":"這些短語用來完成每個句子。"},{"en":"To complete each sentence means to fill in the missing part so the sentence makes sense.","zh":"完成每個句子，是指填上缺失部分，使句子有意思。"},{"en":"Students complete each sentence by choosing the correct verb form.","zh":"學生透過選擇正確動詞形式來完成每個句子。"},{"en":"A completed sentence must be grammatically correct and meaningful.","zh":"完成後的句子必須文法正確且有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"more phrases than questions","meaning":"短語數目多於題目數目","examples":[{"en":"There are more phrases than questions.","zh":"短語數目多於題目數目。"},{"en":"More phrases than questions means some answer options will not be needed.","zh":"短語數目多於題目數目，是指有些答案選項不會用上。"},{"en":"In a matching task, there may be ten phrases but only six questions.","zh":"在配對題中，可能有十個短語但只有六條題目。"},{"en":"This prevents students from solving the task by simple elimination only.","zh":"這防止學生只靠簡單排除法完成任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extra options in an exercise.","zh":"這個短語描述練習中有額外選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"will not use all of them","meaning":"不會全部使用","examples":[{"en":"Students will not use all of the phrases.","zh":"學生不會全部使用這些短語。"},{"en":"Will not use all of them means some choices must be left unused.","zh":"不會全部使用，是指有些選項必須留空不用。"},{"en":"In a vocabulary box, students may not use all of the listed words.","zh":"在詞彙框中，學生可能不會使用所有列出的詞。"},{"en":"This instruction tells students to choose carefully rather than force every option in.","zh":"這項指示告訴學生要仔細選擇，而不是強行用完每個選項。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that extra answers are included.","zh":"這個短語提醒題目包括額外答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"lead to a drop in","meaning":"導致……下降","examples":[{"en":"Economic problems can lead to a drop in living standards.","zh":"經濟問題可以導致生活水平下降。"},{"en":"To lead to a drop in something means to cause it to decrease.","zh":"導致某事下降，是指造成它減少。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can lead to a drop in concentration during class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致課堂專注力下降。"},{"en":"Drops often happen when pressure, cost or damage increases.","zh":"當壓力、成本或損害增加時，下降通常會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a cause producing a decline.","zh":"這個短語描述一個原因造成下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"standard of living","meaning":"生活水平","examples":[{"en":"The standard of living has risen in many countries.","zh":"許多國家的生活水平已經上升。"},{"en":"Standard of living means the level of comfort, health and material well-being people enjoy.","zh":"生活水平是指人們享有的舒適、健康和物質福祉程度。"},{"en":"Access to clean water and safe homes can raise a community’s standard of living.","zh":"獲得清潔食水和安全住房可以提高社區生活水平。"},{"en":"A higher income does not always mean every part of the standard of living improves.","zh":"較高收入不一定表示生活水平的每一部分都有改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quality of everyday life.","zh":"這個短語描述日常生活質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"cause and effect","meaning":"因果關係","examples":[{"en":"A correlation is not the same as cause and effect.","zh":"相關性不等同於因果關係。"},{"en":"Cause and effect means one thing makes another thing happen.","zh":"因果關係是指一件事令另一件事發生。"},{"en":"If studying more leads to higher marks, that may show cause and effect.","zh":"如果多溫習導致更高分數，那可能顯示因果關係。"},{"en":"Two things can happen together without having a cause-and-effect relationship.","zh":"兩件事可以同時發生，但沒有因果關係。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a direct link between reason and result.","zh":"這個短語描述原因與結果之間的直接連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"pose a threat to","meaning":"對……構成威脅","examples":[{"en":"Environmental problems may pose a threat to human progress.","zh":"環境問題可能對人類進步構成威脅。"},{"en":"To pose a threat to something means to create a danger for it.","zh":"對某事構成威脅，是指為它造成危險。"},{"en":"Poor road design can pose a threat to cyclists.","zh":"差劣道路設計可以對騎單車者構成威脅。"},{"en":"A threat may not cause damage immediately, but it creates risk.","zh":"威脅未必立即造成損害，但會製造風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that endangers another thing.","zh":"這個短語描述某事危害另一事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be accompanied by","meaning":"伴隨著……","examples":[{"en":"The growth of world trade has been accompanied by a fall in tariffs.","zh":"世界貿易增長伴隨着關稅下降。"},{"en":"To be accompanied by something means to happen together with it.","zh":"伴隨着某事，是指與它一起發生。"},{"en":"A rise in online learning may be accompanied by a fall in printed homework.","zh":"網上學習增加可能伴隨着紙本功課減少。"},{"en":"This phrase shows two changes occurring together, not necessarily causation.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩種變化同時出現，但不一定是因果。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing parallel trends.","zh":"它適合描述並行趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"a fall in tariffs","meaning":"關稅下降","examples":[{"en":"World trade has been accompanied by a fall in tariffs.","zh":"世界貿易伴隨着關稅下降。"},{"en":"A fall in tariffs means a reduction in taxes on imported goods.","zh":"關稅下降是指進口貨品稅項減少。"},{"en":"A fall in tariffs can make imported school computers cheaper.","zh":"關稅下降可以令進口學校電腦更便宜。"},{"en":"Lower tariffs may increase trade because products cost less.","zh":"較低關稅可能增加貿易，因為產品成本下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reduced import taxes.","zh":"這個短語描述進口稅減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"natural resources","meaning":"天然資源","examples":[{"en":"Natural resources cannot expand indefinitely.","zh":"天然資源不能無限擴張。"},{"en":"Natural resources are materials and systems from nature, such as water, forests, soil and minerals.","zh":"天然資源是來自自然的材料和系統，例如水、森林、土壤和礦物。"},{"en":"A village depends on natural resources if it relies on rivers, farmland and nearby forests.","zh":"如果村莊依賴河流、農田和附近森林，它就是依賴天然資源。"},{"en":"If natural resources are used faster than they recover, shortages can occur.","zh":"如果天然資源被使用的速度快於恢復速度，就可能出現短缺。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to useful things provided by nature.","zh":"這個短語指自然提供的有用事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"which of the following","meaning":"以下哪一項","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which of the following is not stated by Kaplan.","zh":"題目問以下哪一項不是 Kaplan 所陳述的。"},{"en":"Which of the following means students must choose from the listed options.","zh":"以下哪一項，是指學生必須從列出的選項中選擇。"},{"en":"In a reading test, “which of the following” usually signals a multiple-choice question.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，which of the following 通常表示多項選擇題。"},{"en":"Students should check each option against the passage carefully.","zh":"學生應仔細把每個選項與篇章核對。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a choice-based question.","zh":"這個短語引入選擇題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be stated by","meaning":"由……陳述","examples":[{"en":"The factor is not stated by Kaplan as a key cause.","zh":"該因素沒有被 Kaplan 陳述為主要原因。"},{"en":"To be stated by someone means to be said or written by that person.","zh":"由某人陳述，是指由那人說出或寫出。"},{"en":"If an answer is not stated by the writer, students should not treat it as directly supported.","zh":"如果答案不是由作者陳述，學生不應把它當作有直接支持。"},{"en":"Reading questions often test whether information is actually stated in the text.","zh":"閱讀題常測試資料是否真的在文本中被陳述。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the source of a claim.","zh":"這個短語指出主張的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"key contributing factor","meaning":"主要促成因素","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about a key contributing factor to global instability.","zh":"題目問潛在全球不穩的主要促成因素。"},{"en":"A key contributing factor is an important cause that helps produce a result.","zh":"主要促成因素，是幫助造成某結果的重要原因。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can be a key contributing factor to poor exam performance.","zh":"睡眠不足可以是考試表現差的主要促成因素。"},{"en":"Contributing factors may work together rather than act alone.","zh":"促成因素可能共同發揮作用，而不是單獨作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important cause among several causes.","zh":"這個短語描述多個原因中的重要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"potential global destabilisation","meaning":"潛在全球不穩","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses potential global destabilisation.","zh":"篇章討論潛在全球不穩。"},{"en":"Potential global destabilisation means the possible weakening of order and stability across the world.","zh":"潛在全球不穩，是指世界各地秩序和穩定可能被削弱。"},{"en":"A major food crisis could create potential global destabilisation if many countries are affected.","zh":"如果許多國家受影響，重大糧食危機可能造成潛在全球不穩。"},{"en":"The word “potential” shows the danger is possible, not guaranteed.","zh":"potential 一詞顯示危險是可能的，而非必然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible worldwide breakdown of stability.","zh":"這個短語描述世界穩定可能崩壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"political corruption","meaning":"政治腐敗","examples":[{"en":"Political corruption is listed as one possible factor in the option.","zh":"政治腐敗在選項中被列為可能因素之一。"},{"en":"Political corruption means dishonest or illegal behaviour by people in government or politics.","zh":"政治腐敗是指政府或政治人物的不誠實或非法行為。"},{"en":"A mayor taking public money for personal use is an example of political corruption.","zh":"市長把公款用作私人用途，就是政治腐敗的例子。"},{"en":"Corruption can weaken public trust and damage social stability.","zh":"腐敗可以削弱公眾信任並損害社會穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes abuse of political power.","zh":"這個短語描述濫用政治權力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"collapse of ecosystems","meaning":"生態系統崩潰","examples":[{"en":"The collapse of ecosystems is central to Kaplan’s warning.","zh":"生態系統崩潰是 Kaplan 警告的核心。"},{"en":"Collapse of ecosystems means natural systems break down and can no longer function properly.","zh":"生態系統崩潰，是指自然系統瓦解，無法再正常運作。"},{"en":"A lake ecosystem may collapse if pollution kills the fish and plants.","zh":"如果污染殺死魚類和植物，湖泊生態系統可能崩潰。"},{"en":"Ecosystem collapse can reduce food, clean water and natural protection.","zh":"生態系統崩潰可以減少食物、清潔水和自然保護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the failure of natural systems.","zh":"這個短語描述自然系統失效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"population explosion","meaning":"人口爆炸","examples":[{"en":"Kaplan warns about a population explosion.","zh":"Kaplan 警告人口爆炸。"},{"en":"A population explosion is a sudden or very rapid increase in population.","zh":"人口爆炸是人口突然或非常快速增加。"},{"en":"A city may face a population explosion if many workers arrive in a short time.","zh":"如果大量工人在短時間內到來，城市可能面對人口爆炸。"},{"en":"Population explosions can overload housing, transport and public services.","zh":"人口爆炸可以令住房、交通和公共服務超負荷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extremely fast population growth.","zh":"這個短語描述極快速人口增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"main source of","meaning":"……的主要來源","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the main source of Gee’s optimism.","zh":"題目問 Gee 樂觀態度的主要來源。"},{"en":"Main source of something means the most important origin or reason for it.","zh":"某事的主要來源，是指它最重要的起源或原因。"},{"en":"Practice is the main source of a student’s improvement in speaking.","zh":"練習是學生口語進步的主要來源。"},{"en":"Identifying the main source helps explain why someone holds a view.","zh":"辨認主要來源有助解釋某人為何持有某觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the central cause or basis.","zh":"這個短語描述核心原因或基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"optimism","meaning":"樂觀態度","examples":[{"en":"Gee’s optimism comes mainly from economic indicators.","zh":"Gee 的樂觀態度主要來自經濟指標。"},{"en":"Optimism means the belief that things will improve or turn out well.","zh":"樂觀態度是相信事情會改善或有好結果。"},{"en":"A student may feel optimism after receiving better mock exam results.","zh":"學生收到較好模擬試成績後可能感到樂觀。"},{"en":"Optimism can motivate action, but it may be risky if it ignores problems.","zh":"樂觀可以推動行動，但如果忽視問題，也可能有風險。"},{"en":"This word describes a hopeful attitude.","zh":"這個詞描述抱有希望的態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"decreasing Third World debt","meaning":"第三世界債務下降","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions decreasing Third World debt.","zh":"選項提到第三世界債務下降。"},{"en":"Decreasing Third World debt means debt owed by poorer developing countries is becoming smaller.","zh":"第三世界債務下降，是指較貧窮發展中國家所欠債務變少。"},{"en":"A debt-relief programme may lead to decreasing Third World debt.","zh":"債務減免計劃可能導致第三世界債務下降。"},{"en":"Lower debt can give governments more money for schools, hospitals and infrastructure.","zh":"較低債務可以讓政府有更多資金用於學校、醫院和基礎架構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reduction in poorer countries’ debt burden.","zh":"這個短語描述較貧窮國家債務負擔減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"rise in the standard of living worldwide","meaning":"全球生活水平上升","examples":[{"en":"Gee points to the rise in the standard of living worldwide.","zh":"Gee 指出全球生活水平上升。"},{"en":"Rise in the standard of living worldwide means people in many countries are living better than before.","zh":"全球生活水平上升，是指許多國家的人生活得比以前更好。"},{"en":"Better housing, healthcare and food supply can show a rise in standard of living worldwide.","zh":"更好住房、醫療和食物供應可以顯示全球生活水平上升。"},{"en":"A worldwide rise may still hide inequality between rich and poor groups.","zh":"全球上升仍可能掩蓋貧富群體之間的不平等。"},{"en":"This phrase describes global improvement in everyday living conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述日常生活條件的全球改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"infer about","meaning":"推斷關於……","examples":[{"en":"Students must infer about the author’s views.","zh":"學生必須推斷關於作者觀點的內容。"},{"en":"To infer about something means to work it out from clues rather than direct statements.","zh":"推斷關於某事，是指根據線索而非直接陳述推想出來。"},{"en":"If a writer praises Kaplan and criticises Gee, students may infer about the writer’s position.","zh":"如果作者讚賞 Kaplan 並批評 Gee，學生可能推斷作者立場。"},{"en":"Inference requires careful reading of tone, evidence and emphasis.","zh":"推斷需要仔細閱讀語氣、證據和重點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes drawing conclusions from clues.","zh":"這個短語描述從線索得出結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"views are closer to","meaning":"觀點較接近……","examples":[{"en":"Suzuki’s views are closer to Kaplan’s than to Gee’s.","zh":"Suzuki 的觀點較接近 Kaplan，而不是 Gee。"},{"en":"If someone’s views are closer to another person’s, they agree more with that person than with others.","zh":"如果某人的觀點較接近另一人，就是與那人比與其他人更一致。"},{"en":"A student’s views on homework may be closer to the teacher’s than to classmates’.","zh":"學生對功課的看法可能較接近老師，而不是同學。"},{"en":"Comparing views helps readers understand where a writer stands.","zh":"比較觀點幫助讀者理解作者立場。"},{"en":"This phrase describes similarity in opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述意見相似。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"main purpose","meaning":"主要目的","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the main purpose of the passage.","zh":"題目問篇章的主要目的。"},{"en":"Main purpose means the most important reason a text was written.","zh":"主要目的，是指文本被撰寫的最重要原因。"},{"en":"The main purpose of a warning notice is to prevent danger.","zh":"警告通告的主要目的是防止危險。"},{"en":"Understanding purpose helps students choose the best summary or title.","zh":"理解目的有助學生選出最佳摘要或標題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the central aim of a text.","zh":"這個短語指文本的核心目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"alert someone to","meaning":"提醒某人注意……","examples":[{"en":"The author wants to alert readers to an environmental crisis.","zh":"作者想提醒讀者注意一場環境危機。"},{"en":"To alert someone to something means to warn them or make them aware of it.","zh":"提醒某人注意某事，是指警告他們或令他們意識到它。"},{"en":"A teacher may alert students to common grammar mistakes before an exam.","zh":"老師可能在考試前提醒學生注意常見文法錯誤。"},{"en":"Alerts are useful when people may not notice a danger by themselves.","zh":"當人們可能自己沒有注意到危險，提醒就很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes drawing attention to a risk or problem.","zh":"這個短語描述把注意力引向風險或問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"create uncertainty about","meaning":"對……造成不確定感","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not simply create uncertainty about the future.","zh":"篇章並不只是對未來造成不確定感。"},{"en":"To create uncertainty about something means to make people unsure about it.","zh":"對某事造成不確定感，是指令人對它不肯定。"},{"en":"Conflicting exam dates can create uncertainty about a school schedule.","zh":"互相矛盾的考試日期可以對學校時間表造成不確定感。"},{"en":"Uncertainty may make people hesitate before making decisions.","zh":"不確定感可能令人作決定前猶豫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes causing doubt or lack of clarity.","zh":"這個短語描述造成疑慮或不清晰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"challenge current economic theory","meaning":"挑戰當前經濟理論","examples":[{"en":"Suzuki challenges current economic assumptions about endless growth.","zh":"Suzuki 挑戰關於無止境增長的當前經濟假設。"},{"en":"To challenge current economic theory means to question accepted ideas about how economies work.","zh":"挑戰當前經濟理論，是指質疑關於經濟如何運作的既有想法。"},{"en":"A student may challenge current economic theory by asking whether growth can continue with limited resources.","zh":"學生可能透過詢問資源有限下增長能否持續，來挑戰當前經濟理論。"},{"en":"Challenging theory forces people to examine hidden assumptions.","zh":"挑戰理論迫使人們檢視隱藏假設。"},{"en":"This phrase describes questioning mainstream economic thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述質疑主流經濟思想。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 78 - Are these two reporters on the same planet?.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 79":[{"front":"mystery of the mummies","meaning":"木乃伊之謎","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the mystery of the mummies and the evidence found in them.","zh":"文章討論木乃伊之謎，以及在它們身上發現的證據。"},{"en":"The mystery of the mummies means an unexplained question about ancient preserved bodies.","zh":"木乃伊之謎，指關於古代保存遺體的未解問題。"},{"en":"A museum may face a mystery of the mummies if tests reveal substances no one expected.","zh":"如果測試顯示出沒有人預料到的物質，博物館可能面對木乃伊之謎。"},{"en":"If new evidence does not fit accepted history, the mystery becomes harder to solve.","zh":"如果新證據不符合既有歷史，這個謎就更難解開。"},{"en":"The phrase connects ancient remains with puzzling scientific evidence.","zh":"這個短語把古代遺骸與令人困惑的科學證據連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"make a discovery","meaning":"有所發現","examples":[{"en":"A German scientist made a discovery that challenged established knowledge.","zh":"一位德國科學家有所發現，挑戰了既有知識。"},{"en":"To make a discovery means to find something new, important, or unexpected.","zh":"有所發現，指找到新的、重要的或意料之外的東西。"},{"en":"A student may make a discovery when a science experiment gives an unusual result.","zh":"當科學實驗出現異常結果，學生可能有所發現。"},{"en":"If a discovery challenges old ideas, researchers must check the evidence carefully.","zh":"如果一項發現挑戰舊想法，研究者必須仔細檢查證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes finding something that was not known before.","zh":"這個短語描述找到以前未知的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"upend entire fields of study","meaning":"顛覆整個學術領域","examples":[{"en":"The discovery could upend entire fields of study.","zh":"這項發現可能顛覆整個學術領域。"},{"en":"To upend entire fields of study means to completely challenge or overturn established academic areas.","zh":"顛覆整個學術領域，指完全挑戰或推翻既有學術範疇。"},{"en":"A new medical finding can upend a field if it proves a standard treatment wrong.","zh":"如果新的醫學發現證明標準治療是錯的，就可以顛覆一個領域。"},{"en":"If one small test changes archaeology, botany, and history, its impact is enormous.","zh":"如果一項小測試改變考古學、植物學和歷史，其影響就非常巨大。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a discovery powerful enough to change expert thinking.","zh":"這個短語暗示某發現有力量改變專家思維。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fields of study","meaning":"學術領域","examples":[{"en":"The discovery affected several fields of study, including archaeology and botany.","zh":"這項發現影響了幾個學術領域，包括考古學和植物學。"},{"en":"Fields of study are academic subjects or areas of research.","zh":"學術領域，是學術科目或研究範圍。"},{"en":"History, biology, law, and economics are different fields of study.","zh":"歷史、生物、法律和經濟都是不同學術領域。"},{"en":"If evidence affects more than one field, scholars from different subjects may need to work together.","zh":"如果證據影響多於一個領域，不同學科的學者可能需要合作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised areas of knowledge.","zh":"這個短語指有系統的知識範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"from history and archaeology to chemistry and botany","meaning":"由歷史學和考古學到化學和植物學","examples":[{"en":"The discovery had implications from history and archaeology to chemistry and botany.","zh":"這項發現的含意由歷史學和考古學延伸到化學和植物學。"},{"en":"From A to B means covering a wide range of areas between those examples.","zh":"由 A 到 B，指涵蓋這些例子之間的廣泛範圍。"},{"en":"A school project may involve subjects from geography and economics to biology and art.","zh":"一個學校項目可能涉及由地理和經濟到生物和藝術的科目。"},{"en":"If one discovery affects both ancient trade and plant origins, it crosses many disciplines.","zh":"如果一項發現同時影響古代貿易和植物起源，它就跨越許多學科。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the broad reach of an issue.","zh":"這個短語強調某議題影響範圍廣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"archaeology","meaning":"考古學","examples":[{"en":"Archaeology was one of the fields affected by the discovery.","zh":"考古學是受這項發現影響的領域之一。"},{"en":"Archaeology is the study of past human life through objects, buildings, bones, and remains.","zh":"考古學是透過物件、建築、骨骼和遺骸研究過去人類生活的學科。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may study old graves to understand how ancient people lived.","zh":"考古學家可能研究古墓，以了解古人如何生活。"},{"en":"If a mummy contains unexpected substances, archaeology may need to reconsider ancient contact and trade.","zh":"如果木乃伊含有意外物質，考古學可能需要重新思考古代接觸和貿易。"},{"en":"The word focuses on material evidence from the past.","zh":"這個詞強調來自過去的物質證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"chemistry and botany","meaning":"化學及植物學","examples":[{"en":"The discovery was relevant to both chemistry and botany.","zh":"這項發現同時與化學及植物學有關。"},{"en":"Chemistry studies substances and reactions, while botany studies plants.","zh":"化學研究物質和反應，而植物學研究植物。"},{"en":"A medicine made from a plant can interest both chemistry and botany.","zh":"由植物製成的藥物可以同時引起化學和植物學興趣。"},{"en":"If tests find plant-based chemicals in a mummy, both fields become important.","zh":"如果測試在木乃伊中發現植物性化學物質，兩個領域都變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase links chemical analysis with plant knowledge.","zh":"這個短語把化學分析與植物知識連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"forensic specialist","meaning":"法證專家","examples":[{"en":"Dr Svetlana Balabanova was a forensic specialist.","zh":"Svetlana Balabanova 博士是一位法證專家。"},{"en":"A forensic specialist uses scientific methods to investigate evidence, often for legal or medical questions.","zh":"法證專家使用科學方法調查證據，常用於法律或醫學問題。"},{"en":"A forensic specialist may test hair, blood, or tissue to find hidden substances.","zh":"法證專家可能測試頭髮、血液或組織，以尋找隱藏物質。"},{"en":"If a forensic specialist finds unexpected chemicals, the result must be checked very carefully.","zh":"如果法證專家發現意外化學物質，結果必須被非常仔細地檢查。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an expert in evidence-based scientific investigation.","zh":"這個短語指以證據為基礎進行科學調查的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"perform tissue tests on","meaning":"對……進行組織測試","examples":[{"en":"The scientist was performing tissue tests on an Egyptian mummy.","zh":"這位科學家正在對一具埃及木乃伊進行組織測試。"},{"en":"To perform tissue tests on something means to examine body tissue scientifically.","zh":"對某物進行組織測試，指以科學方式檢查身體組織。"},{"en":"Doctors may perform tissue tests on a small sample to check for disease.","zh":"醫生可能對小樣本進行組織測試，以檢查疾病。"},{"en":"If tissue tests reveal unexpected substances, researchers may need to repeat them.","zh":"如果組織測試顯示意外物質，研究者可能需要重複測試。"},{"en":"The phrase describes laboratory testing of biological material.","zh":"這個短語描述對生物材料進行實驗室測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tissue tests","meaning":"組織測試；組織化驗","examples":[{"en":"The tissue tests revealed unexpected substances in the mummy.","zh":"組織測試顯示木乃伊中有意外物質。"},{"en":"Tissue tests are laboratory examinations of body tissue.","zh":"組織測試是對身體組織進行的實驗室檢查。"},{"en":"A hospital may use tissue tests to identify infection or abnormal cells.","zh":"醫院可能使用組織測試來識別感染或異常細胞。"},{"en":"If tissue tests are reliable, their results can provide strong evidence.","zh":"如果組織測試可靠，其結果可以提供有力證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to scientific analysis of body material.","zh":"這個短語指對身體材料進行科學分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Egyptian mummy","meaning":"埃及木乃伊","examples":[{"en":"The tests were carried out on an Egyptian mummy.","zh":"測試是在一具埃及木乃伊上進行的。"},{"en":"An Egyptian mummy is a preserved dead body from ancient Egypt.","zh":"埃及木乃伊，是來自古埃及、經保存處理的死者遺體。"},{"en":"Museums often display Egyptian mummies to teach visitors about burial customs.","zh":"博物館常展出埃及木乃伊，以教訪客了解喪葬習俗。"},{"en":"If an Egyptian mummy contains unexpected chemicals, it may raise historical questions.","zh":"如果埃及木乃伊含有意外化學物質，可能引發歷史問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an ancient preserved body from Egypt.","zh":"這個短語指來自埃及的古代保存遺體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"museum collection","meaning":"博物館藏品","examples":[{"en":"The mummy was part of a German museum collection.","zh":"該木乃伊是德國一個博物館藏品的一部分。"},{"en":"A museum collection is a group of objects kept, studied, or displayed by a museum.","zh":"博物館藏品，是由博物館保存、研究或展示的一組物件。"},{"en":"A museum collection may include paintings, tools, bones, and ancient documents.","zh":"博物館藏品可能包括畫作、工具、骨骼和古代文件。"},{"en":"If an object belongs to a museum collection, researchers may be allowed to study it.","zh":"如果某物屬於博物館藏品，研究者可能獲准研究它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to items held by a museum.","zh":"這個短語指博物館持有的物品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"mummified remains","meaning":"木乃伊遺骸","examples":[{"en":"The mummified remains belonged to a woman named Henut-Taui.","zh":"這些木乃伊遺骸屬於一名叫 Henut-Taui 的女子。"},{"en":"Mummified remains are preserved body parts or bodies that have not decayed normally.","zh":"木乃伊遺骸，是沒有正常腐爛、被保存下來的身體部分或遺體。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may study mummified remains to learn about diet, disease, and burial practices.","zh":"考古學家可能研究木乃伊遺骸，以了解飲食、疾病和喪葬做法。"},{"en":"If remains are well preserved, they can contain evidence from thousands of years ago.","zh":"如果遺骸保存良好，就可以包含數千年前的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to preserved human or animal bodies.","zh":"這個短語指被保存下來的人類或動物遺體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a woman named","meaning":"一名叫作……的女子","examples":[{"en":"The mummy was a woman named Henut-Taui.","zh":"這具木乃伊是一名叫作 Henut-Taui 的女子。"},{"en":"A woman named X means a woman whose name was X.","zh":"一名叫作 X 的女子，指名字是 X 的女性。"},{"en":"A witness named Maria may give evidence in court.","zh":"一名叫 Maria 的證人可能在法庭作證。"},{"en":"If a mummy is linked to a named person, historians can study her identity more closely.","zh":"如果木乃伊與一個有名有姓的人連繫起來，歷史學家可以更仔細研究其身份。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a person by name.","zh":"這個短語用名字介紹人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"over 3,000 years ago","meaning":"三千多年前","examples":[{"en":"Henut-Taui had died over 3,000 years ago.","zh":"Henut-Taui 已於三千多年前去世。"},{"en":"Over 3,000 years ago means more than three thousand years before the present time.","zh":"三千多年前，指距今超過三千年以前。"},{"en":"Some ancient buildings were constructed over 3,000 years ago.","zh":"一些古代建築建於三千多年前。"},{"en":"If a body is that old, any modern substance found in it seems surprising.","zh":"如果一具遺體有如此久歷史，在其中發現現代物質就令人驚訝。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a very ancient time frame.","zh":"這個短語給出非常古老的時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"amazingly","meaning":"令人驚訝的是","examples":[{"en":"Amazingly, the tests revealed cocaine and nicotine in her body.","zh":"令人驚訝的是，測試顯示她體內有可卡因和尼古丁。"},{"en":"Amazingly means surprisingly or in a way that is hard to believe.","zh":"令人驚訝的是，指事情令人意外或難以相信。"},{"en":"Amazingly, the lost wallet was found in the same classroom a week later.","zh":"令人驚訝的是，遺失的銀包一星期後在同一課室被找到。"},{"en":"If a result contradicts accepted knowledge, writers may use this word to show surprise.","zh":"如果結果與既有知識矛盾，作者可能用這個詞表示驚訝。"},{"en":"The word signals that the information is unexpected.","zh":"這個詞表示資料出乎意料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tests revealed that","meaning":"測試顯示","examples":[{"en":"The tests revealed that the mummy contained unusual substances.","zh":"測試顯示該木乃伊含有不尋常物質。"},{"en":"Tests revealed that means scientific examinations showed or uncovered a fact.","zh":"測試顯示，指科學檢查展示或揭示某事實。"},{"en":"Blood tests revealed that the patient lacked iron.","zh":"血液測試顯示病人缺鐵。"},{"en":"If tests reveal something unexpected, researchers must decide whether the result is real.","zh":"如果測試顯示意外結果，研究者必須判斷結果是否真實。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence found through testing.","zh":"這個短語引入透過測試找到的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"contain large quantities of","meaning":"含有大量……","examples":[{"en":"The body contained large quantities of cocaine and nicotine.","zh":"該遺體含有大量可卡因和尼古丁。"},{"en":"To contain large quantities of something means to have a lot of it inside.","zh":"含有大量某物，指內部有很多該物質。"},{"en":"A sugary drink may contain large quantities of sugar.","zh":"含糖飲品可能含有大量糖。"},{"en":"If an ancient body contains large quantities of an unexpected substance, contamination or trade must be considered.","zh":"如果古代遺體含有大量意外物質，就必須考慮污染或貿易。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses amount, not just presence.","zh":"這個短語強調數量，而不只是存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cocaine and nicotine","meaning":"可卡因和尼古丁","examples":[{"en":"The tests found cocaine and nicotine in the mummy.","zh":"測試在木乃伊中發現可卡因和尼古丁。"},{"en":"Cocaine and nicotine are chemical substances associated with coca and tobacco plants.","zh":"可卡因和尼古丁是與古柯和煙草植物相關的化學物質。"},{"en":"A forensic test may detect cocaine and nicotine in hair or tissue samples.","zh":"法證測試可能在頭髮或組織樣本中偵測到可卡因和尼古丁。"},{"en":"If these substances appear in an ancient mummy, their origin becomes a major question.","zh":"如果這些物質出現在古代木乃伊中，其來源就成為重大問題。"},{"en":"The phrase names the unexpected substances in the evidence.","zh":"這個短語指出證據中的意外物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"testing methods","meaning":"測試方法","examples":[{"en":"Dr Balabanova had regularly used the same testing methods.","zh":"Balabanova 博士經常使用相同的測試方法。"},{"en":"Testing methods are the procedures or techniques used to examine samples.","zh":"測試方法，是用來檢查樣本的程序或技術。"},{"en":"A school science experiment needs clear testing methods so results can be trusted.","zh":"學校科學實驗需要清楚測試方法，結果才可信。"},{"en":"If the same method works in legal cases, its mummy results are harder to dismiss.","zh":"如果同一方法在法律案件中有效，其木乃伊測試結果就較難被否定。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to how tests are carried out.","zh":"這個短語指測試如何進行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"convict people of drug use","meaning":"判定某人吸毒","examples":[{"en":"The same methods had been used to convict people of drug use.","zh":"相同方法曾被用來判定某人吸毒。"},{"en":"To convict people of drug use means to legally judge them guilty of using drugs.","zh":"判定某人吸毒，指在法律上裁定他們使用毒品有罪。"},{"en":"Courts may convict someone if reliable tests prove illegal drug use.","zh":"如果可靠測試證明有人使用非法毒品，法庭可能定罪。"},{"en":"If a method is strong enough for court, critics must explain why it fails here.","zh":"如果某方法強到足以用於法庭，批評者就必須解釋為何它在此失效。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the testing method had serious legal authority.","zh":"這個短語顯示該測試方法具有嚴肅法律權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"drug use","meaning":"吸毒；使用毒品","examples":[{"en":"The tests had been used as evidence of drug use.","zh":"這些測試曾被用作吸毒證據。"},{"en":"Drug use means taking illegal or controlled substances.","zh":"吸毒，指使用非法或受管制物質。"},{"en":"A workplace may test for drug use when safety is a serious concern.","zh":"當安全是嚴重關注時，工作場所可能測試是否有人吸毒。"},{"en":"If tests show drug use, the result may affect legal or employment decisions.","zh":"如果測試顯示吸毒，結果可能影響法律或僱傭決定。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to substance use, not ordinary medicine in this context.","zh":"這個短語在此指使用毒品，而不是普通藥物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not expect to find","meaning":"沒有預料會發現","examples":[{"en":"She had not expected to find cocaine in an ancient Egyptian mummy.","zh":"她沒有預料會在古埃及木乃伊中發現可卡因。"},{"en":"To not expect to find something means to be surprised because it was not predicted.","zh":"沒有預料會發現某物，指因沒有預測到它而感到驚訝。"},{"en":"A teacher may not expect to find a perfect essay from a beginner.","zh":"老師可能沒有預料會從初學者那裡看到完美作文。"},{"en":"If evidence appears where it should not exist, researchers must investigate further.","zh":"如果證據出現在理應不存在的地方，研究者就必須進一步調查。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights surprise caused by an unlikely discovery.","zh":"這個短語突出由不太可能的發現帶來的驚訝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ancient Egyptian mummy","meaning":"古埃及木乃伊","examples":[{"en":"Nicotine and cocaine were not expected in an ancient Egyptian mummy.","zh":"人們沒有預料尼古丁和可卡因會出現在古埃及木乃伊中。"},{"en":"An ancient Egyptian mummy is a preserved body from Egypt thousands of years ago.","zh":"古埃及木乃伊，是數千年前埃及保存下來的遺體。"},{"en":"An ancient Egyptian mummy can teach historians about health, religion, and burial customs.","zh":"古埃及木乃伊可以教歷史學家了解健康、宗教和喪葬習俗。"},{"en":"If modern-looking chemicals are found in such a mummy, the dating and source must be checked.","zh":"如果這類木乃伊中發現看似現代的化學物質，就必須檢查年代和來源。"},{"en":"The phrase combines great age, Egyptian origin, and preservation.","zh":"這個短語結合悠久年代、埃及來源和遺體保存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it is generally accepted that","meaning":"一般認為","examples":[{"en":"It is generally accepted that these plants were native to the Americas.","zh":"一般認為這些植物原產於美洲。"},{"en":"It is generally accepted that means most experts or people believe something is true.","zh":"一般認為，指大多數專家或人們相信某事是真的。"},{"en":"It is generally accepted that regular practice improves language learning.","zh":"一般認為定期練習會改善語言學習。"},{"en":"If new evidence challenges what is generally accepted, controversy may follow.","zh":"如果新證據挑戰一般認為的事情，爭議可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a widely held belief.","zh":"這個短語引入廣泛持有的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"native to the Americas","meaning":"原產於美洲","examples":[{"en":"Coca and tobacco are native to the Americas.","zh":"古柯和煙草原產於美洲。"},{"en":"Native to the Americas means originally found or growing naturally in North, Central, or South America.","zh":"原產於美洲，指原本在北美洲、中美洲或南美洲自然存在或生長。"},{"en":"Potatoes and tomatoes are also plants native to the Americas.","zh":"馬鈴薯和番茄也是原產於美洲的植物。"},{"en":"If a plant is native to one region, finding it elsewhere in ancient times raises questions.","zh":"如果植物原產於一個地區，古代時在其他地方發現它就會引發問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes original geographical origin.","zh":"這個短語描述原本的地理起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"other continents","meaning":"其他大洲","examples":[{"en":"These plants were not thought to exist on other continents.","zh":"人們認為這些植物並不存在於其他大洲。"},{"en":"Other continents means continents apart from the one already mentioned.","zh":"其他大洲，指除了已提及的大洲之外的洲。"},{"en":"If a plant is native to Asia, Africa and Europe are other continents in that comparison.","zh":"如果一種植物原產於亞洲，在該比較中非洲和歐洲就是其他大洲。"},{"en":"If a plant was absent from other continents, ancient trade becomes one possible explanation for its movement.","zh":"如果某植物在其他大洲不存在，古代貿易就成為其移動的一種可能解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase helps compare geographical regions.","zh":"這個短語有助比較地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prior to","meaning":"在……之前","examples":[{"en":"The plants were not believed to exist elsewhere prior to European exploration.","zh":"人們不相信這些植物在歐洲探索之前存在於其他地方。"},{"en":"Prior to means before a particular time or event.","zh":"在某事之前，指在特定時間或事件之前。"},{"en":"Students should read the instructions prior to answering exam questions.","zh":"學生應在回答考試題目前閱讀指示。"},{"en":"If a substance appears before it was thought to arrive, history may need revision.","zh":"如果某物在原本以為它到達之前已出現，歷史可能需要修正。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an earlier time boundary.","zh":"這個短語給出較早的時間界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"European exploration","meaning":"歐洲人的探索","examples":[{"en":"The plants were thought to have spread after European exploration.","zh":"人們認為這些植物是在歐洲人的探索之後傳播開來。"},{"en":"European exploration refers to journeys by Europeans to other regions, especially from the late fifteenth century onward.","zh":"歐洲人的探索，指歐洲人前往其他地區的旅程，尤其是十五世紀末以後。"},{"en":"History lessons often discuss European exploration of the Americas, Africa, and Asia.","zh":"歷史課常討論歐洲人對美洲、非洲和亞洲的探索。"},{"en":"If a plant reached Egypt before European exploration, accepted timelines become difficult.","zh":"如果植物在歐洲探索前已到達埃及，既有時間線就變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a major period of global contact.","zh":"這個短語標示全球接觸的一個重要時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"repeat the tests","meaning":"重複測試","examples":[{"en":"Dr Balabanova repeated the tests to check the results.","zh":"Balabanova 博士重複測試以檢查結果。"},{"en":"To repeat the tests means to perform the same tests again to confirm accuracy.","zh":"重複測試，指再次進行相同測試以確認準確性。"},{"en":"A science student repeats an experiment if the first result looks unusual.","zh":"如果第一次結果看起來不尋常，科學學生會重複實驗。"},{"en":"If repeated tests give the same answer, the result becomes harder to dismiss.","zh":"如果重複測試給出相同答案，結果就更難被否定。"},{"en":"The phrase shows careful checking.","zh":"這個短語顯示仔細核查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"send out fresh samples to","meaning":"把新樣本送往……","examples":[{"en":"She sent out fresh samples to three other labs.","zh":"她把新樣本送往另外三間實驗室。"},{"en":"To send out fresh samples to labs means to give new material to other laboratories for independent testing.","zh":"把新樣本送往實驗室，指把新的材料交給其他實驗室作獨立測試。"},{"en":"A hospital may send out fresh samples to another clinic for confirmation.","zh":"醫院可能把新樣本送往另一間診所作確認。"},{"en":"If other labs test new samples, the original result can be checked more fairly.","zh":"如果其他實驗室測試新樣本，原本結果就能被更公平地檢查。"},{"en":"The phrase describes independent verification through new samples.","zh":"這個短語描述透過新樣本進行獨立驗證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fresh samples","meaning":"新樣本","examples":[{"en":"Fresh samples were sent to other laboratories for testing.","zh":"新樣本被送往其他實驗室進行測試。"},{"en":"Fresh samples are newly taken pieces of material used for testing.","zh":"新樣本，是新取得、用於測試的材料。"},{"en":"A doctor may take fresh samples if an earlier test result seems doubtful.","zh":"如果早前測試結果令人懷疑，醫生可能取得新樣本。"},{"en":"If fresh samples give the same result, contamination becomes less likely.","zh":"如果新樣本給出相同結果，污染的可能性就較低。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the material is newly collected, not reused.","zh":"這個短語強調材料是新收集，而不是重用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"labs","meaning":"實驗室","examples":[{"en":"The samples were tested in three other labs.","zh":"這些樣本在另外三間實驗室接受測試。"},{"en":"Labs are laboratories where scientific tests and experiments are carried out.","zh":"實驗室，是進行科學測試和實驗的地方。"},{"en":"Students may use school labs to test water quality or study plants.","zh":"學生可能使用學校實驗室測試水質或研究植物。"},{"en":"If several labs reach the same result, confidence in the finding increases.","zh":"如果幾間實驗室得到相同結果，對發現的信心會增加。"},{"en":"The word is an informal short form of laboratories.","zh":"這個詞是 laboratories 的非正式縮寫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"come back positive","meaning":"結果呈陽性","examples":[{"en":"The results came back positive.","zh":"結果呈陽性。"},{"en":"To come back positive means a test result shows the substance or condition being tested for is present.","zh":"結果呈陽性，指測試顯示所檢測的物質或狀況存在。"},{"en":"A medical test may come back positive for an infection.","zh":"醫學測試可能對某種感染呈陽性。"},{"en":"If several samples come back positive, the finding cannot easily be ignored.","zh":"如果幾個樣本都呈陽性，這項發現就不容易被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a test confirming presence.","zh":"這個短語描述測試確認某物存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"publish a paper","meaning":"發表論文","examples":[{"en":"She published a paper with two other scientists.","zh":"她與另外兩位科學家發表了一篇論文。"},{"en":"To publish a paper means to make a research article available to other scholars or the public.","zh":"發表論文，指把研究文章提供給其他學者或公眾閱讀。"},{"en":"A university researcher may publish a paper after years of laboratory work.","zh":"大學研究者可能經過多年實驗室工作後發表論文。"},{"en":"If a paper challenges accepted ideas, other experts may examine it closely.","zh":"如果論文挑戰既有想法，其他專家可能仔細檢查它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formally sharing research results.","zh":"這個短語描述正式分享研究結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be shocked by","meaning":"對……感到震驚","examples":[{"en":"Balabanova was shocked by the results of her tests.","zh":"Balabanova 對其測試結果感到震驚。"},{"en":"To be shocked by something means to be very surprised or upset by it.","zh":"對某事感到震驚，指因它而非常驚訝或不安。"},{"en":"A teacher may be shocked by how many students misunderstand a simple instruction.","zh":"老師可能對許多學生誤解簡單指示感到震驚。"},{"en":"If evidence contradicts everything expected, a scientist may feel shocked first.","zh":"如果證據與所有預期相反，科學家最初可能感到震驚。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses a strong emotional reaction.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈情緒反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be even more shocked at","meaning":"對……更加震驚","examples":[{"en":"She was even more shocked at the hostile response to her paper.","zh":"她對論文受到敵意回應更加震驚。"},{"en":"To be even more shocked at something means to feel greater surprise than before because of it.","zh":"對某事更加震驚，指因此感到比之前更大的驚訝。"},{"en":"A student may be shocked by a low mark but even more shocked at unfair comments.","zh":"學生可能對低分感到震驚，但對不公平評語更加震驚。"},{"en":"If a researcher expects debate but receives insults, the reaction may be more disturbing than the result.","zh":"如果研究者預期辯論卻收到侮辱，反應可能比結果更令人不安。"},{"en":"The phrase compares two levels of shock.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種震驚程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"hostile response","meaning":"敵意回應","examples":[{"en":"Her publication received a hostile response.","zh":"她的論文發表收到敵意回應。"},{"en":"A hostile response is an angry, unfriendly, or aggressive reaction.","zh":"敵意回應，是憤怒、不友善或具攻擊性的反應。"},{"en":"A new school rule may receive a hostile response if students feel ignored.","zh":"如果學生覺得被忽視，新校規可能收到敵意回應。"},{"en":"If scholars attack a researcher personally, discussion becomes less scientific.","zh":"如果學者人身攻擊研究者，討論就變得較不科學。"},{"en":"The phrase describes opposition with strong negativity.","zh":"這個短語描述帶強烈負面情緒的反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"publication","meaning":"論文發表；出版物","examples":[{"en":"The publication caused a strong reaction.","zh":"這次論文發表引起強烈反應。"},{"en":"A publication is a written work that has been formally released, such as a paper, book, or article.","zh":"出版物是正式發表的書面作品，例如論文、書籍或文章。"},{"en":"A school magazine is a publication created for students and parents.","zh":"校刊是為學生和家長製作的出版物。"},{"en":"If a publication presents controversial evidence, readers may respond strongly.","zh":"如果出版物提出具爭議的證據，讀者可能強烈回應。"},{"en":"The word can refer to both the act of publishing and the published work.","zh":"這個詞可以指發表行為，也可以指已出版作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"insulting letters","meaning":"侮辱性的信件","examples":[{"en":"She received many insulting letters after publishing her results.","zh":"她發表結果後收到許多侮辱性的信件。"},{"en":"Insulting letters are letters that attack, offend, or show disrespect toward someone.","zh":"侮辱性的信件，是攻擊、冒犯或不尊重某人的信件。"},{"en":"A public official may receive insulting letters after making an unpopular decision.","zh":"公職人員作出不受歡迎的決定後，可能收到侮辱性信件。"},{"en":"If criticism becomes insulting, it stops helping people understand the evidence.","zh":"如果批評變成侮辱，就不再幫助人理解證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes personal attacks in written form.","zh":"這個短語描述書面形式的人身攻擊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"accuse someone of fraud","meaning":"指控某人造假","examples":[{"en":"Some critics accused her of fraud.","zh":"一些批評者指控她造假。"},{"en":"To accuse someone of fraud means to claim that they have deliberately deceived others.","zh":"指控某人造假，指聲稱他們故意欺騙他人。"},{"en":"A company may be accused of fraud if it lies about its accounts.","zh":"如果公司在帳目上說謊，可能被指控造假。"},{"en":"If a scientist is accused of fraud, their honesty and methods are being attacked.","zh":"如果科學家被指控造假，其誠信和方法正受到攻擊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a serious charge of deliberate dishonesty.","zh":"這個短語描述故意不誠實的嚴重指控。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fraud","meaning":"詐騙；造假","examples":[{"en":"The hostile letters accused the scientist of fraud.","zh":"敵意信件指控該科學家造假。"},{"en":"Fraud is deliberate deception, usually to gain advantage or avoid responsibility.","zh":"詐騙或造假，是故意欺騙，通常為取得利益或逃避責任。"},{"en":"Using fake receipts to claim money is a form of fraud.","zh":"使用假收據報銷是一種詐騙。"},{"en":"If fraud occurs in research, the results cannot be trusted.","zh":"如果研究中出現造假，結果就不能被信任。"},{"en":"The word refers to intentional dishonesty, not an honest mistake.","zh":"這個詞指有意不誠實，而不是誠實錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"come immediately to mind","meaning":"立即浮現在腦海中","examples":[{"en":"Two explanations came immediately to mind.","zh":"兩種解釋立即浮現在腦海中。"},{"en":"If something comes immediately to mind, you think of it quickly and naturally.","zh":"如果某事立即浮現在腦海中，你會很快而自然地想到它。"},{"en":"When a student is late, traffic may come immediately to mind as a possible reason.","zh":"當學生遲到時，交通問題可能立即浮現在腦海中作為可能原因。"},{"en":"If evidence seems impossible, simple explanations are considered first.","zh":"如果證據看似不可能，人們會先考慮簡單解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the first ideas that occur to someone.","zh":"這個短語描述某人最先想到的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"false result","meaning":"錯誤結果","examples":[{"en":"One possible explanation was that the tests had produced a false result.","zh":"一種可能解釋是測試產生了錯誤結果。"},{"en":"A false result is a test result that is wrong or misleading.","zh":"錯誤結果，是錯誤或具誤導性的測試結果。"},{"en":"A thermometer may give a false result if it is broken.","zh":"如果溫度計壞了，可能給出錯誤結果。"},{"en":"If a false result occurs, researchers may repeat the test with new samples.","zh":"如果出現錯誤結果，研究者可能用新樣本重複測試。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an error in testing.","zh":"這個短語描述測試中的錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mummies tested","meaning":"被測試的木乃伊","examples":[{"en":"The mummies tested might not have been truly ancient.","zh":"被測試的木乃伊可能並非真正古老。"},{"en":"The mummies tested means the particular mummies that were examined in the study.","zh":"被測試的木乃伊，指研究中實際被檢查的那些木乃伊。"},{"en":"In a science project, the plants tested are the plants actually used in the experiment.","zh":"在科學項目中，被測試的植物就是實驗中實際使用的植物。"},{"en":"If the mummies tested were not genuine, the results would not prove ancient drug presence.","zh":"如果被測試的木乃伊不是真品，結果就不能證明古代存在毒品。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the objects included in the test.","zh":"這個短語指出測試中包含的物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"truly ancient Egyptian","meaning":"真正屬於古埃及的","examples":[{"en":"The second explanation was that the bodies were not truly ancient Egyptian.","zh":"第二種解釋是這些遺體並非真正屬於古埃及。"},{"en":"Truly ancient Egyptian means genuinely from ancient Egypt, not later or fake.","zh":"真正屬於古埃及，指確實來自古埃及，而不是較後年代或偽造。"},{"en":"A museum object must be tested before experts call it truly ancient Egyptian.","zh":"博物館物件必須經測試，專家才可稱它真正屬於古埃及。"},{"en":"If a mummy is not truly ancient, unexpected substances become easier to explain.","zh":"如果木乃伊並非真正古老，意外物質就更容易解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase questions authenticity and age.","zh":"這個短語質疑真確性和年代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"relatively modern bodies","meaning":"年代相對較近的遺體","examples":[{"en":"Perhaps the mummies were relatively modern bodies.","zh":"也許這些木乃伊是年代相對較近的遺體。"},{"en":"Relatively modern bodies are bodies from a more recent period compared with ancient remains.","zh":"年代相對較近的遺體，是與古代遺骸相比來自較近時期的遺體。"},{"en":"A hundred-year-old body is relatively modern compared with a three-thousand-year-old mummy.","zh":"與三千年木乃伊相比，一具百年遺體屬於年代相對較近。"},{"en":"If bodies are relatively modern, they may have been exposed to modern substances.","zh":"如果遺體年代較近，它們可能接觸過現代物質。"},{"en":"The phrase compares age rather than saying something is new.","zh":"這個短語是在比較年代，而不是說某物全新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"contain traces of","meaning":"含有微量……；有……痕跡","examples":[{"en":"The bodies may have contained traces of cocaine.","zh":"這些遺體可能含有微量可卡因。"},{"en":"To contain traces of something means to have a very small amount of it.","zh":"含有某物痕跡，指有非常少量該物質。"},{"en":"A cup may contain traces of milk even after it is rinsed quickly.","zh":"杯子即使快速沖洗後，仍可能有牛奶痕跡。"},{"en":"If traces of a substance are found, scientists must ask where they came from.","zh":"如果發現某物質的痕跡，科學家必須問它們從何而來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a tiny but detectable presence.","zh":"這個短語描述微小但可檢測到的存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"traces of cocaine","meaning":"微量可卡因","examples":[{"en":"The scientists considered whether the bodies contained traces of cocaine.","zh":"科學家考慮這些遺體是否含有微量可卡因。"},{"en":"Traces of cocaine are very small detectable amounts of cocaine.","zh":"微量可卡因，是可被檢測到的極少量可卡因。"},{"en":"Forensic labs may look for traces of substances in hair or cloth.","zh":"法證實驗室可能在頭髮或布料中尋找物質痕跡。"},{"en":"If traces of cocaine appear in ancient tissue, the source must be explained.","zh":"如果古代組織出現微量可卡因，就必須解釋其來源。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on small chemical evidence.","zh":"這個短語強調微小化學證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"examine tissue from","meaning":"檢查來自……的組織","examples":[{"en":"Dr Balabanova examined tissue from naturally preserved bodies.","zh":"Balabanova 博士檢查來自自然保存遺體的組織。"},{"en":"To examine tissue from something means to study body material taken from that source.","zh":"檢查來自某物的組織，指研究從該來源取得的身體材料。"},{"en":"A doctor may examine tissue from a patient to identify abnormal cells.","zh":"醫生可能檢查來自病人的組織，以識別異常細胞。"},{"en":"If tissue from different bodies gives similar results, the finding becomes more interesting.","zh":"如果來自不同遺體的組織給出相似結果，發現就更有趣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes studying biological material from a particular source.","zh":"這個短語描述研究來自特定來源的生物材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"naturally preserved bodies","meaning":"自然保存的遺體","examples":[{"en":"The tissue came from naturally preserved bodies in Sudan.","zh":"組織來自蘇丹自然保存的遺體。"},{"en":"Naturally preserved bodies are bodies kept from decay by natural conditions, not deliberate mummification.","zh":"自然保存的遺體，是由自然條件而非刻意木乃伊化保存、未腐爛的遺體。"},{"en":"Cold, dry, or salty environments can create naturally preserved bodies.","zh":"寒冷、乾燥或含鹽環境可以形成自然保存的遺體。"},{"en":"If bodies are naturally preserved, they may still hold old chemical evidence.","zh":"如果遺體自然保存，它們仍可能保留舊化學證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preservation caused by environment.","zh":"這個短語描述由環境造成的保存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"over a thousand years old","meaning":"有超過一千年歷史","examples":[{"en":"The preserved bodies were over a thousand years old.","zh":"這些保存遺體有超過一千年歷史。"},{"en":"Over a thousand years old means more than one thousand years in age.","zh":"有超過一千年歷史，指年齡多於一千年。"},{"en":"A temple over a thousand years old may need careful preservation.","zh":"一座有超過一千年歷史的寺廟可能需要細心保存。"},{"en":"If remains are over a thousand years old, modern contamination must be ruled out carefully.","zh":"如果遺骸有超過一千年歷史，就必須仔細排除現代污染。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an ancient but not exact age.","zh":"這個短語給出古老但不精確的年代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"excavated cemetery","meaning":"經發掘的墓地","examples":[{"en":"The bodies were discovered in an excavated cemetery.","zh":"這些遺體是在經發掘的墓地中被發現的。"},{"en":"An excavated cemetery is a burial ground that has been dug up and studied by archaeologists.","zh":"經發掘的墓地，是已被考古學家挖掘和研究的 burial ground。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may uncover pottery, bones, and grave goods in an excavated cemetery.","zh":"考古學家可能在經發掘的墓地中發現陶器、骨骼和陪葬品。"},{"en":"If bodies come from an excavated cemetery, their archaeological context can be studied.","zh":"如果遺體來自經發掘的墓地，其考古背景就可被研究。"},{"en":"The phrase links burial remains with formal excavation.","zh":"這個短語把墓葬遺骸與正式發掘連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the Sudan","meaning":"蘇丹","examples":[{"en":"The preserved bodies were discovered in the Sudan.","zh":"這些保存遺體在蘇丹被發現。"},{"en":"The Sudan refers to Sudan, a country in northeastern Africa.","zh":"蘇丹指位於非洲東北部的國家 Sudan。"},{"en":"Archaeologists study sites in the Sudan because the region has a long ancient history.","zh":"考古學家研究蘇丹遺址，因為該地區有悠久古代歷史。"},{"en":"If similar substances are found in Sudanese remains, the mummy evidence is not isolated.","zh":"如果在蘇丹遺骸中發現相似物質，木乃伊證據就不是孤立個案。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the geographical location of the bodies.","zh":"這個短語指出遺體的地理位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"test positive for","meaning":"對……測試呈陽性","examples":[{"en":"About a third of the bodies tested positive for nicotine or cocaine.","zh":"約三分之一的遺體對尼古丁或可卡因測試呈陽性。"},{"en":"To test positive for something means a test shows that the substance is present.","zh":"對某物測試呈陽性，指測試顯示該物質存在。"},{"en":"A patient may test positive for a virus after a laboratory test.","zh":"病人經實驗室測試後，可能對某病毒呈陽性。"},{"en":"If many ancient bodies test positive, researchers must explain the repeated pattern.","zh":"如果許多古代遺體測試呈陽性，研究者必須解釋這種重複模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes confirmation through testing.","zh":"這個短語描述透過測試確認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"something had happened even earlier","meaning":"更早之前曾發生某事","examples":[{"en":"Something had happened even earlier that should have prompted discussion.","zh":"更早之前曾發生某事，本應引發討論。"},{"en":"Something had happened even earlier means a relevant event occurred before the later event being discussed.","zh":"更早之前曾發生某事，指相關事件在正在討論的較後事件之前已發生。"},{"en":"A school conflict may seem new, but something may have happened earlier to create tension.","zh":"學校衝突可能看似新問題，但更早之前可能已有事情造成緊張。"},{"en":"If an earlier discovery was ignored, later evidence may force the question to return.","zh":"如果較早發現被忽視，後來證據可能迫使問題再次浮現。"},{"en":"The phrase points back to a previous important event.","zh":"這個短語回指先前的重要事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"initiate serious discussion","meaning":"引發嚴肅討論","examples":[{"en":"The earlier discovery should have initiated serious discussion.","zh":"較早的發現本應引發嚴肅討論。"},{"en":"To initiate serious discussion means to start careful and important debate about an issue.","zh":"引發嚴肅討論，指開始對某議題作仔細而重要的辯論。"},{"en":"A sudden drop in exam results should initiate serious discussion among teachers.","zh":"考試成績突然下降，應在老師之間引發嚴肅討論。"},{"en":"If evidence challenges accepted ideas, experts should discuss it rather than ignore it.","zh":"如果證據挑戰既有想法，專家應討論它，而不是忽視它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes beginning meaningful debate.","zh":"這個短語描述開始有意義的辯論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"mummified remains of Ramses II","meaning":"拉美西斯二世的木乃伊遺骸","examples":[{"en":"The mummified remains of Ramses II arrived in Paris for repair work.","zh":"拉美西斯二世的木乃伊遺骸抵達巴黎接受修復工作。"},{"en":"The mummified remains of Ramses II means the preserved body of the ancient Egyptian pharaoh Ramses II.","zh":"拉美西斯二世的木乃伊遺骸，指古埃及法老拉美西斯二世被保存下來的身體。"},{"en":"A famous ruler’s remains may be studied with extra care because of their historical importance.","zh":"著名統治者的遺骸因其歷史重要性，可能被格外仔細研究。"},{"en":"If such important remains contain tobacco, the discovery becomes difficult to dismiss.","zh":"如果如此重要的遺骸含有煙草，該發現就難以被否定。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a historically significant mummy.","zh":"這個短語指出一具具有重大歷史意義的木乃伊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"arrive in Paris for repair work","meaning":"抵達巴黎接受修復","examples":[{"en":"The mummy arrived in Paris for repair work.","zh":"這具木乃伊抵達巴黎接受修復工作。"},{"en":"To arrive in Paris for repair work means to be brought to Paris so experts can restore or fix damage.","zh":"抵達巴黎接受修復，指被帶到巴黎，讓專家修復或修補損害。"},{"en":"A painting may arrive in a museum workshop for repair work after being damaged.","zh":"畫作受損後，可能抵達博物館工作室接受修復。"},{"en":"If a mummy is moved for repair, experts may notice details that were missed before.","zh":"如果木乃伊被移送修復，專家可能注意到以前錯過的細節。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why the object was taken to Paris.","zh":"這個短語解釋物件為何被帶到巴黎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"repair work","meaning":"修復工作","examples":[{"en":"The remains were taken to Paris for repair work.","zh":"這些遺骸被帶到巴黎接受修復工作。"},{"en":"Repair work means work done to fix damage or restore something to better condition.","zh":"修復工作，指修補損害或使某物恢復較好狀態的工作。"},{"en":"A school roof may need repair work after a storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，學校屋頂可能需要修復工作。"},{"en":"If ancient remains are fragile, repair work must be done carefully.","zh":"如果古代遺骸脆弱，修復工作必須仔細進行。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to fixing or restoring damaged material.","zh":"這個短語指修補或修復受損材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sections of bandages","meaning":"繃帶切片；繃帶部分","examples":[{"en":"The researcher looked at sections of bandages from the mummy.","zh":"研究者查看來自木乃伊的繃帶切片。"},{"en":"Sections of bandages are pieces or parts cut or taken from wrapping cloth.","zh":"繃帶切片，是從包裹布料中切下或取出的部分。"},{"en":"A doctor may examine sections of bandages to check whether a wound is bleeding.","zh":"醫生可能檢查繃帶部分，以查看傷口是否流血。"},{"en":"If a plant fragment is trapped in bandage fibres, those sections become evidence.","zh":"如果植物碎片被困在繃帶纖維中，這些切片就成為證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to small parts of the mummy’s wrapping.","zh":"這個短語指木乃伊包裹物的小部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"within the fibres","meaning":"在纖維之中","examples":[{"en":"A plant fragment was found within the fibres.","zh":"一塊植物碎片在纖維之中被發現。"},{"en":"Within the fibres means inside or among the tiny threads of a material.","zh":"在纖維之中，指在材料的細小線狀結構內或之間。"},{"en":"Dust may be trapped within the fibres of an old carpet.","zh":"灰塵可能被困在舊地毯的纖維之中。"},{"en":"If something is found within fibres, it may have been caught there during wrapping.","zh":"如果某物在纖維中被發現，它可能是在包裹過程中被夾住。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a location inside thread-like material.","zh":"這個短語描述位於線狀材料內的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"plant fragment","meaning":"植物碎片","examples":[{"en":"The scientist found a plant fragment inside the bandage fibres.","zh":"科學家在繃帶纖維內發現一塊植物碎片。"},{"en":"A plant fragment is a small broken piece of plant material.","zh":"植物碎片，是植物材料破裂後的小部分。"},{"en":"A leaf fragment stuck to a shoe may show where someone has walked.","zh":"黏在鞋上的葉片碎片可能顯示某人走過哪裡。"},{"en":"If a plant fragment is identified as tobacco, it can become important evidence.","zh":"如果植物碎片被識別為煙草，它就能成為重要證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a tiny piece of a plant.","zh":"這個短語指植物的一小片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"under a microscope","meaning":"在顯微鏡下","examples":[{"en":"She checked the plant fragment under a microscope.","zh":"她在顯微鏡下檢查植物碎片。"},{"en":"Under a microscope means using a microscope to see very small details.","zh":"在顯微鏡下，指使用顯微鏡觀察非常細小的細節。"},{"en":"Students may look at onion cells under a microscope in biology class.","zh":"學生可能在生物課中於顯微鏡下觀察洋蔥細胞。"},{"en":"If a fragment is tiny, a microscope can reveal features invisible to the eye.","zh":"如果碎片很小，顯微鏡可以揭示肉眼看不見的特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase describes close scientific observation.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細的科學觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be amazed to discover","meaning":"驚訝地發現","examples":[{"en":"She was amazed to discover that the plant was tobacco.","zh":"她驚訝地發現該植物是煙草。"},{"en":"To be amazed to discover something means to be extremely surprised when finding it.","zh":"驚訝地發現某事，指在找到它時感到極其驚訝。"},{"en":"A teacher may be amazed to discover that a quiet student writes powerful poems.","zh":"老師可能驚訝地發現一位安靜學生寫出有力詩作。"},{"en":"If a New World plant appears in an ancient Egyptian context, surprise is natural.","zh":"如果新世界植物出現在古埃及語境中，感到驚訝是自然的。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a discovery that is hard to believe.","zh":"這個短語突出難以相信的發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tobacco","meaning":"煙草","examples":[{"en":"Tobacco was found in the mummified body of Ramses II.","zh":"煙草在拉美西斯二世的木乃伊遺體中被發現。"},{"en":"Tobacco is a plant whose leaves contain nicotine.","zh":"煙草是一種葉片含有尼古丁的植物。"},{"en":"Historians connect tobacco strongly with the Americas before modern global trade.","zh":"歷史學家把煙草與現代全球貿易前的美洲密切連繫起來。"},{"en":"If tobacco is found in an ancient Egyptian mummy, accepted trade history becomes difficult.","zh":"如果煙草在古埃及木乃伊中被發現，既有貿易史就變得困難。"},{"en":"The word names the plant behind the surprising evidence.","zh":"這個詞指出驚人證據背後的植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fearing that","meaning":"因擔心……","examples":[{"en":"Fearing that she had made a mistake, she repeated her tests.","zh":"因擔心自己犯錯，她多次重複測試。"},{"en":"Fearing that means because someone was worried that something might be true.","zh":"因擔心，指因為某人憂慮某事可能是真的。"},{"en":"Fearing that the answer was wrong, a student checked the passage again.","zh":"因擔心答案錯了，學生再次檢查文章。"},{"en":"If a result seems impossible, researchers may fear that an error has occurred.","zh":"如果結果看似不可能，研究者可能擔心出現錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the worry behind an action.","zh":"這個短語引入某行動背後的憂慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"make a mistake","meaning":"犯錯","examples":[{"en":"The scientist feared that she had made a mistake.","zh":"這位科學家擔心自己犯錯。"},{"en":"To make a mistake means to do something incorrectly or reach a wrong result.","zh":"犯錯，指做某事不正確或得到錯誤結果。"},{"en":"A student may make a mistake by copying the wrong number from a chart.","zh":"學生可能因從圖表抄錯數字而犯錯。"},{"en":"If scientists fear a mistake, they repeat procedures to check accuracy.","zh":"如果科學家擔心犯錯，他們會重複程序以檢查準確性。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to error, not deliberate dishonesty.","zh":"這個短語指錯誤，而不是故意不誠實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"repeat the tests several times","meaning":"多次重複測試","examples":[{"en":"She repeated the tests several times.","zh":"她多次重複測試。"},{"en":"To repeat the tests several times means to run the same tests more than once for confirmation.","zh":"多次重複測試，指為確認而不止一次進行相同測試。"},{"en":"A laboratory may repeat a blood test several times if the result is unusual.","zh":"如果血液測試結果不尋常，實驗室可能多次重複測試。"},{"en":"If each repeat gives the same result, confidence in the finding increases.","zh":"如果每次重複都給出相同結果，對發現的信心就增加。"},{"en":"The phrase shows careful scientific checking.","zh":"這個短語顯示仔細科學核查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"with the same result each time","meaning":"每次結果都相同","examples":[{"en":"The tests produced the same result each time.","zh":"測試每次都產生相同結果。"},{"en":"With the same result each time means every repeated test gave an identical answer.","zh":"每次結果都相同，指每次重複測試都給出一樣答案。"},{"en":"If students solve a maths problem three ways with the same result each time, the answer seems reliable.","zh":"如果學生用三種方法解數學題，每次結果都相同，答案就看似可靠。"},{"en":"Repeated identical results make accidental error less likely.","zh":"重複出現相同結果會令偶然錯誤的可能性降低。"},{"en":"The phrase strengthens confidence in a finding.","zh":"這個短語加強對發現的信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"New World plant","meaning":"新世界植物","examples":[{"en":"Tobacco was a New World plant found on an Old World mummy.","zh":"煙草是一種在舊世界木乃伊上發現的新世界植物。"},{"en":"A New World plant is a plant associated with the Americas before modern global exchange.","zh":"新世界植物，是與現代全球交流前的美洲相關的植物。"},{"en":"Potatoes and tobacco are often described as New World plants.","zh":"馬鈴薯和煙草常被描述為新世界植物。"},{"en":"If a New World plant appears in ancient Egypt, scholars must explain how it arrived there.","zh":"如果新世界植物出現在古埃及，學者必須解釋它如何到達那裡。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts American plant origins with Old World locations.","zh":"這個短語把美洲植物起源與舊世界地點作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Old World mummy","meaning":"舊世界木乃伊","examples":[{"en":"A New World plant was found on an Old World mummy.","zh":"一種新世界植物在舊世界木乃伊上被發現。"},{"en":"An Old World mummy is a mummy from Europe, Africa, or Asia, rather than the Americas.","zh":"舊世界木乃伊，是來自歐洲、非洲或亞洲，而非美洲的木乃伊。"},{"en":"An Egyptian mummy is an Old World mummy because Egypt is in Africa.","zh":"埃及木乃伊是舊世界木乃伊，因為埃及位於非洲。"},{"en":"If an Old World mummy contains a New World plant, the evidence creates a puzzle.","zh":"如果舊世界木乃伊含有新世界植物，證據就造成謎團。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts ancient Afro-Eurasia with the Americas.","zh":"這個短語把古代亞非歐與美洲作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cause a sensation","meaning":"引起轟動","examples":[{"en":"The results caused a sensation in Europe.","zh":"這些結果在歐洲引起轟動。"},{"en":"To cause a sensation means to create great public excitement, shock, or discussion.","zh":"引起轟動，指造成巨大公眾興奮、震驚或討論。"},{"en":"A school’s unexpected victory may cause a sensation in the local community.","zh":"學校意外勝出比賽，可能在本地社區引起轟動。"},{"en":"If scientific results challenge history, newspapers and scholars may react strongly.","zh":"如果科學結果挑戰歷史，報章和學者可能強烈反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a reaction much bigger than ordinary interest.","zh":"這個短語描述遠超普通興趣的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"by chance","meaning":"偶然地","examples":[{"en":"Some wondered whether tobacco had been dropped by chance.","zh":"有些人懷疑煙草是否偶然掉落。"},{"en":"By chance means accidentally, not deliberately or by design.","zh":"偶然地，指意外地，而不是故意或有計劃地。"},{"en":"A student may find an old photo by chance while cleaning a drawer.","zh":"學生清理抽屜時，可能偶然找到舊照片。"},{"en":"If tobacco fell by chance from a modern pipe, the mummy evidence would be contamination.","zh":"如果煙草是從現代煙斗偶然掉下，木乃伊證據就是污染。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests accident rather than intention.","zh":"這個短語暗示意外，而不是意圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"from the pipe of","meaning":"從……的煙斗","examples":[{"en":"The tobacco might have fallen from the pipe of an archaeologist.","zh":"煙草可能是從某位考古學家的煙斗掉下來。"},{"en":"From the pipe of someone means coming out of that person’s smoking pipe.","zh":"從某人的煙斗，指從該人的吸煙煙斗中出來。"},{"en":"Ash may fall from the pipe of an old man sitting outside a shop.","zh":"坐在店外的老人煙斗中可能掉出煙灰。"},{"en":"If tobacco came from a modern pipe, it would not prove ancient contact.","zh":"如果煙草來自現代煙斗，就不能證明古代接觸。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a possible source of contamination.","zh":"這個短語指出可能的污染來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"forgotten archaeologist","meaning":"被遺忘的考古學家","examples":[{"en":"The contamination theory blamed a forgotten archaeologist.","zh":"污染理論把責任歸咎於一位被遺忘的考古學家。"},{"en":"A forgotten archaeologist is an archaeologist from the past whose actions are no longer clearly remembered.","zh":"被遺忘的考古學家，是過去的考古學家，其行動已不再被清楚記得。"},{"en":"An old excavation note may mention a forgotten archaeologist who handled the artefacts decades ago.","zh":"舊發掘筆記可能提及幾十年前處理文物的一位被遺忘考古學家。"},{"en":"If such a person smoked near a mummy, tobacco could have contaminated it.","zh":"如果這人曾在木乃伊附近吸煙，煙草可能污染它。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests an unknown earlier source of error.","zh":"這個短語暗示早前未知的錯誤來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"respond to this charge of","meaning":"回應這項……指控","examples":[{"en":"Dr Lescot responded to this charge of contamination.","zh":"Lescot 博士回應這項污染指控。"},{"en":"To respond to this charge of something means to answer an accusation about it.","zh":"回應這項某事指控，指回答關於該事的指控。"},{"en":"A student accused of copying may respond to the charge by showing their notes.","zh":"被指抄襲的學生可能透過展示筆記回應指控。"},{"en":"If contamination is alleged, the researcher must show why the evidence is still reliable.","zh":"如果有人指稱污染，研究者必須展示證據為何仍可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes replying to a serious criticism.","zh":"這個短語描述回應嚴重批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"charge of contamination","meaning":"污染指控","examples":[{"en":"The researcher had to respond to the charge of contamination.","zh":"研究者必須回應污染指控。"},{"en":"A charge of contamination is an accusation that a sample was polluted by outside material.","zh":"污染指控，是指控樣本被外來材料污染。"},{"en":"A lab may face a charge of contamination if fingerprints appear on a clean sample.","zh":"如果乾淨樣本上出現指紋，實驗室可能面對污染指控。"},{"en":"If the charge is correct, the test result may no longer be reliable.","zh":"如果指控正確，測試結果可能不再可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a criticism about spoiled evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述關於證據受污染的批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"extract new samples from","meaning":"從……抽取新樣本","examples":[{"en":"She carefully extracted new samples from the abdomen.","zh":"她小心地從腹部抽取新樣本。"},{"en":"To extract new samples from something means to remove fresh material from it for testing.","zh":"從某處抽取新樣本，指從其中取出新材料作測試。"},{"en":"A doctor may extract a sample from a patient’s skin to examine it.","zh":"醫生可能從病人皮膚抽取樣本來檢查。"},{"en":"If samples are taken from inside the body, surface contamination becomes less likely.","zh":"如果樣本取自身體內部，表面污染的可能性就較低。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful removal of material for analysis.","zh":"這個短語描述為分析而小心取出材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"abdomen","meaning":"腹部","examples":[{"en":"The new samples were taken from the abdomen.","zh":"新樣本取自腹部。"},{"en":"The abdomen is the part of the body between the chest and the hips.","zh":"腹部是身體中位於胸部與臀部之間的部分。"},{"en":"A doctor may press the abdomen gently to check for pain.","zh":"醫生可能輕按腹部以檢查疼痛。"},{"en":"If a sample comes from the abdomen of a mummy, it is less likely to be a loose surface fragment.","zh":"如果樣本來自木乃伊腹部，就較不可能是鬆散表面碎片。"},{"en":"The word identifies a body region.","zh":"這個詞指出身體部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the entire process","meaning":"整個過程","examples":[{"en":"The entire process was recorded on film.","zh":"整個過程被拍攝記錄下來。"},{"en":"The entire process means every step from beginning to end.","zh":"整個過程，指由開始到結束的每一步。"},{"en":"A science teacher may film the entire process of an experiment for fairness.","zh":"科學老師可能為公平起見拍下實驗的整個過程。"},{"en":"If every step is recorded, critics have less room to claim hidden contamination.","zh":"如果每一步都被記錄，批評者就較難聲稱有隱藏污染。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses completeness.","zh":"這個短語強調完整性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"recorded on film","meaning":"被拍攝記錄下來","examples":[{"en":"The process was recorded on film to prevent accusations of contamination.","zh":"該過程被拍攝記錄下來，以防污染指控。"},{"en":"Recorded on film means captured as moving images by a camera.","zh":"被拍攝記錄下來，指由攝影機捕捉成活動影像。"},{"en":"A school performance may be recorded on film so parents can watch it later.","zh":"學校表演可能被拍攝記錄下來，讓家長之後觀看。"},{"en":"If sample collection is filmed, others can see whether the method was careful.","zh":"如果樣本收集過程被拍下，其他人就能看到方法是否仔細。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visual documentation.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"could not be droppings","meaning":"不可能是掉落物","examples":[{"en":"The samples could not be droppings from another source.","zh":"這些樣本不可能是來自其他來源的掉落物。"},{"en":"Could not be droppings means could not be loose bits that accidentally fell from somewhere else.","zh":"不可能是掉落物，指不可能是從其他地方意外掉下的鬆散碎屑。"},{"en":"Dust found inside a sealed box could not easily be droppings from the ceiling.","zh":"在密封盒內發現的灰塵，不容易解釋為天花板掉落物。"},{"en":"If a sample comes from inside the abdomen, accidental surface falling becomes unlikely.","zh":"如果樣本來自腹部內部，表面意外掉落就不太可能。"},{"en":"The phrase helps reject a contamination explanation.","zh":"這個短語有助排除污染解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be shown to be","meaning":"被證實為","examples":[{"en":"The samples were shown to be tobacco.","zh":"這些樣本被證實為煙草。"},{"en":"To be shown to be something means evidence proved or demonstrated that it was that thing.","zh":"被證實為某物，指證據證明或展示它就是該物。"},{"en":"A stain may be shown to be ink after chemical testing.","zh":"化學測試後，污漬可能被證實為墨水。"},{"en":"If a plant fragment is shown to be tobacco, the identification becomes evidence.","zh":"如果植物碎片被證實為煙草，該識別就成為證據。"},{"en":"The phrase indicates proof through examination.","zh":"這個短語表示透過檢查得到證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tobacco fragments","meaning":"煙草碎片","examples":[{"en":"Tobacco fragments were found in the body of Ramses II.","zh":"煙草碎片在拉美西斯二世的遺體中被發現。"},{"en":"Tobacco fragments are small pieces of tobacco plant material.","zh":"煙草碎片，是煙草植物材料的小片。"},{"en":"Tiny tobacco fragments can be trapped in cloth, dust, or body cavities.","zh":"微小煙草碎片可以被困在布料、塵埃或身體空腔中。"},{"en":"If tobacco fragments are found inside a mummy, accidental surface contamination becomes less convincing.","zh":"如果煙草碎片在木乃伊內部被發現，表面意外污染就較不具說服力。"},{"en":"The phrase names small pieces of the tobacco evidence.","zh":"這個短語指出煙草證據的小碎片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have a profound influence upon","meaning":"對……產生深遠影響","examples":[{"en":"The discovery should have had a profound influence upon historical understanding.","zh":"這項發現本應對歷史理解產生深遠影響。"},{"en":"To have a profound influence upon something means to affect it deeply and importantly.","zh":"對某事產生深遠影響，指對它有深刻而重要的影響。"},{"en":"A new vaccine can have a profound influence upon public health.","zh":"新疫苗可以對公共健康產生深遠影響。"},{"en":"If a discovery changes how scholars understand ancient contact, its influence is profound.","zh":"如果一項發現改變學者對古代接觸的理解，其影響就是深遠的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep impact, not a small effect.","zh":"這個短語描述深刻影響，而不是小效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"our whole understanding of","meaning":"我們對……的整體理解","examples":[{"en":"The evidence could change our whole understanding of ancient trade.","zh":"這項證據可能改變我們對古代貿易的整體理解。"},{"en":"Our whole understanding of something means everything we believe or know about it.","zh":"我們對某事的整體理解，指我們關於它所相信或知道的一切。"},{"en":"A new document can change our whole understanding of why a war began.","zh":"一份新文件可以改變我們對戰爭為何爆發的整體理解。"},{"en":"If ancient Egypt traded across oceans, many historical assumptions would need revision.","zh":"如果古埃及曾跨洋貿易，許多歷史假設就需要修正。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a complete change in knowledge.","zh":"這個短語強調知識上的全面改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the relationship between A and B","meaning":"A與B之間的關係","examples":[{"en":"The discovery affected ideas about the relationship between ancient Egypt and America.","zh":"這項發現影響了關於古埃及與美洲之間關係的想法。"},{"en":"The relationship between A and B means the connection or interaction between two things.","zh":"A 與 B 之間的關係，指兩者之間的連繫或互動。"},{"en":"A teacher may discuss the relationship between sleep and exam performance.","zh":"老師可能討論睡眠與考試表現之間的關係。"},{"en":"If evidence links Egypt and America, the relationship between them becomes historically important.","zh":"如果證據把埃及和美洲連起來，它們之間的關係就具有歷史重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase asks how two things are connected.","zh":"這個短語詢問兩件事如何連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Ancient Egypt and America","meaning":"古埃及與美洲","examples":[{"en":"The evidence raised questions about contact between Ancient Egypt and America.","zh":"這項證據提出關於古埃及與美洲之間接觸的問題。"},{"en":"Ancient Egypt and America refers to ancient Egyptian civilisation and the American continents.","zh":"古埃及與美洲，指古埃及文明和美洲大陸。"},{"en":"Historians normally treat Ancient Egypt and America as separate ancient worlds.","zh":"歷史學家通常把古埃及和美洲視為分開的古代世界。"},{"en":"If evidence suggests contact between them, accepted history becomes more complicated.","zh":"如果證據暗示兩者有接觸，既有歷史就變得更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase sets up a surprising geographical comparison.","zh":"這個短語建立一個令人意外的地理比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"piece of evidence","meaning":"一項證據","examples":[{"en":"This piece of evidence was simply ignored.","zh":"這一項證據被直接忽略。"},{"en":"A piece of evidence is one item or fact used to support an argument or investigation.","zh":"一項證據，是用來支持論點或調查的一個物件或事實。"},{"en":"A fingerprint can be a piece of evidence in a police case.","zh":"指紋可以是警方案件中的一項證據。"},{"en":"If one piece of evidence does not fit a theory, scholars should still examine it.","zh":"如果一項證據不符合某理論，學者仍應檢查它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a single supporting fact or object.","zh":"這個短語指單一支持性事實或物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be simply ignored","meaning":"被直接忽略","examples":[{"en":"The evidence was simply ignored because it raised difficult questions.","zh":"這項證據因引發困難問題而被直接忽略。"},{"en":"To be simply ignored means to be dismissed without proper attention or discussion.","zh":"被直接忽略，指沒有得到適當注意或討論就被排除。"},{"en":"A student’s warning may be simply ignored until the same problem happens again.","zh":"學生的警告可能被直接忽略，直到同一問題再次發生。"},{"en":"If evidence is inconvenient, people may avoid it instead of explaining it.","zh":"如果證據令人不便，人們可能避開它而不是解釋它。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises careless rejection.","zh":"這個短語批評草率否定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"raise too many questions","meaning":"引發太多問題","examples":[{"en":"The discovery raised too many questions for accepted theories.","zh":"這項發現對既有理論引發太多問題。"},{"en":"To raise too many questions means to create many difficult doubts or problems.","zh":"引發太多問題，指造成許多困難疑問或問題。"},{"en":"A school policy raises too many questions if nobody knows who is responsible for enforcing it.","zh":"如果沒有人知道誰負責執行，學校政策就會引發太多問題。"},{"en":"If evidence creates more problems than a theory can handle, experts may resist it.","zh":"如果證據造成的問題超出理論可處理範圍，專家可能抗拒它。"},{"en":"The phrase shows why an idea becomes uncomfortable.","zh":"這個短語顯示某想法為何令人不安。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"too far outside","meaning":"太超出……範圍","examples":[{"en":"The evidence was too far outside accepted scientific views.","zh":"這項證據太超出既有科學觀點範圍。"},{"en":"Too far outside something means too different from it to be easily accepted.","zh":"太超出某範圍，指與它相差太遠，以致難以輕易接受。"},{"en":"A theory may be too far outside the textbook explanation for beginners to accept quickly.","zh":"某理論可能太超出教科書解釋，使初學者難以迅速接受。"},{"en":"If evidence falls far beyond normal assumptions, it may be rejected before full discussion.","zh":"如果證據遠超正常假設，可能在充分討論前就被拒絕。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extreme distance from accepted thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述與既有思維的巨大距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"commonly accepted scientific views","meaning":"普遍接受的科學觀點","examples":[{"en":"The finding was outside commonly accepted scientific views.","zh":"這項發現超出了普遍接受的科學觀點。"},{"en":"Commonly accepted scientific views are ideas most scientists in a field generally support.","zh":"普遍接受的科學觀點，是某領域大多數科學家一般支持的想法。"},{"en":"It is commonly accepted that careful evidence should guide medical decisions.","zh":"人們普遍接受醫療決定應由仔細證據引導。"},{"en":"If a result conflicts with accepted views, scientists may demand stronger proof.","zh":"如果結果與既有觀點衝突，科學家可能要求更強證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to mainstream expert opinion.","zh":"這個短語指主流專家意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the question has returned","meaning":"問題再次浮現","examples":[{"en":"The question has returned because of new mummy evidence.","zh":"由於新的木乃伊證據，問題再次浮現。"},{"en":"The question has returned means an old issue has become important again.","zh":"問題再次浮現，指舊議題再次變得重要。"},{"en":"A school uniform debate may return when students complain again years later.","zh":"當學生多年後再次投訴，校服辯論可能再次浮現。"},{"en":"If new evidence appears, a question once ignored may need fresh attention.","zh":"如果新證據出現，曾被忽略的問題可能需要重新關注。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an old debate becoming active again.","zh":"這個短語描述舊爭議再次活躍起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ancient Egyptian trade","meaning":"古埃及貿易","examples":[{"en":"The passage asks whether ancient Egyptian trade crossed the Atlantic.","zh":"文章詢問古埃及貿易是否橫跨大西洋。"},{"en":"Ancient Egyptian trade means the exchange of goods by ancient Egyptians with other regions.","zh":"古埃及貿易，指古埃及人與其他地區交換貨品。"},{"en":"Ancient Egyptian trade may have involved gold, incense, grain, and luxury goods.","zh":"古埃及貿易可能涉及黃金、香料、穀物和奢侈品。"},{"en":"If trade reached farther than expected, historians must rethink ancient travel routes.","zh":"如果貿易比預期到達更遠地方，歷史學家必須重新思考古代航線。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on Egypt’s commercial contacts in ancient times.","zh":"這個短語強調埃及在古代的商業接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stretch all the way across","meaning":"一直延伸橫跨……","examples":[{"en":"Ancient Egyptian trade may have stretched all the way across the Atlantic Ocean.","zh":"古埃及貿易可能一直延伸橫跨大西洋。"},{"en":"To stretch all the way across something means to extend completely from one side to another.","zh":"一直延伸橫跨某物，指從一邊完全延伸到另一邊。"},{"en":"A bridge may stretch all the way across a wide river.","zh":"一座橋可能一直橫跨寬闊河流。"},{"en":"If a trade network stretched across an ocean, it would show long-distance contact.","zh":"如果貿易網絡橫跨海洋，就顯示長距離接觸。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises a very long span.","zh":"這個短語強調非常長的跨度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Atlantic Ocean","meaning":"大西洋","examples":[{"en":"The possible trade route would have crossed the Atlantic Ocean.","zh":"這條可能貿易路線會橫跨大西洋。"},{"en":"The Atlantic Ocean is the ocean between the Americas and Europe or Africa.","zh":"大西洋是位於美洲與歐洲或非洲之間的海洋。"},{"en":"Ships crossing the Atlantic Ocean travel between two major sides of the world.","zh":"橫渡大西洋的船隻在世界兩大側之間航行。"},{"en":"If ancient people crossed the Atlantic, it would challenge common historical timelines.","zh":"如果古人曾橫渡大西洋，就會挑戰常見歷史時間線。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the ocean central to the trade question.","zh":"這個短語指出貿易問題中的核心海洋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"an idea so unbelievable","meaning":"一個極難相信的想法","examples":[{"en":"This was an idea so unbelievable that other explanations had to be eliminated first.","zh":"這是一個極難相信的想法，以致必須先排除其他解釋。"},{"en":"An idea so unbelievable is a claim that seems extremely hard to accept.","zh":"一個極難相信的想法，是看起來非常難接受的主張。"},{"en":"A student saying the dog ate their whole project may offer an idea so unbelievable that the teacher asks for proof.","zh":"如果學生說狗吃掉整份項目，這可能是極難相信的想法，老師會要求證明。"},{"en":"If an idea seems impossible, researchers must rule out simpler explanations first.","zh":"如果想法看似不可能，研究者必須先排除較簡單解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase shows why strong evidence is required.","zh":"這個短語顯示為何需要有力證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be considered after","meaning":"在……之後才被考慮","examples":[{"en":"The idea could only be considered after other possibilities were eliminated.","zh":"這個想法只能在其他可能性被排除之後才被考慮。"},{"en":"To be considered after something means to be examined only once earlier steps or explanations are dealt with.","zh":"在某事之後才被考慮，指只有先前步驟或解釋被處理後才被檢視。"},{"en":"A doctor may consider rare diseases after common causes are ruled out.","zh":"醫生可能在常見原因被排除後才考慮罕見疾病。"},{"en":"If ordinary explanations fail, a surprising theory becomes more reasonable to discuss.","zh":"如果普通解釋失敗，令人驚訝的理論就較值得討論。"},{"en":"The phrase shows an order of reasoning.","zh":"這個短語顯示推理次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"other possibilities","meaning":"其他可能性","examples":[{"en":"Other possibilities had to be eliminated before transoceanic trade was considered.","zh":"在考慮跨洋貿易之前，必須排除其他可能性。"},{"en":"Other possibilities are alternative explanations that might also account for the evidence.","zh":"其他可能性，是也可能解釋證據的替代解釋。"},{"en":"If a student is absent, illness, transport problems, and family issues are other possibilities.","zh":"如果學生缺席，疾病、交通問題和家庭事情都是其他可能性。"},{"en":"If other possibilities are not checked, the final conclusion may be too quick.","zh":"如果其他可能性沒有被檢查，最終結論可能太倉促。"},{"en":"The phrase keeps reasoning open before deciding.","zh":"這個短語讓推理在決定前保持開放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be eliminated","meaning":"被排除","examples":[{"en":"All other explanations had to be eliminated first.","zh":"所有其他解釋都必須先被排除。"},{"en":"To be eliminated means to be removed from consideration because it is no longer possible or likely.","zh":"被排除，指因不再可能或不太可能而不再被考慮。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice question, wrong options should be eliminated before choosing.","zh":"在選擇題中，錯誤選項應先被排除。"},{"en":"If contamination is eliminated, the ancient-trade theory becomes harder to avoid.","zh":"如果污染被排除，古代貿易理論就更難避開。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ruling something out.","zh":"這個短語描述排除某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"obtain imports from","meaning":"從……取得進口品","examples":[{"en":"The Egyptians may have obtained imports from a distant continent.","zh":"埃及人可能從遙遠大洲取得進口品。"},{"en":"To obtain imports from a place means to get goods brought from that place.","zh":"從某地取得進口品，指得到從該地帶來的貨物。"},{"en":"A city may obtain imports from another country when local supply is limited.","zh":"當本地供應有限，城市可能從另一國取得進口品。"},{"en":"If Egypt obtained plants from far away, trade networks must have been wider than expected.","zh":"如果埃及從遠方取得植物，貿易網絡就必然比預期更廣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes receiving goods from outside.","zh":"這個短語描述從外部取得貨物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a continent thousands of miles away","meaning":"數千英里外的大洲","examples":[{"en":"The imports may have come from a continent thousands of miles away.","zh":"這些進口品可能來自數千英里外的大洲。"},{"en":"A continent thousands of miles away is an extremely distant landmass.","zh":"數千英里外的大洲，是極其遙遠的大陸。"},{"en":"A fruit imported from South America to Asia comes from a continent thousands of miles away.","zh":"從南美洲進口到亞洲的水果，來自數千英里外的大洲。"},{"en":"If goods crossed such a distance in ancient times, travel and trade were highly advanced.","zh":"如果貨物在古代跨越如此距離，旅行和貿易就非常先進。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises geographical distance.","zh":"這個短語強調地理距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"supposedly","meaning":"據稱；按說","examples":[{"en":"America was supposedly not discovered until thousands of years later.","zh":"按說，美洲直到數千年後才被發現。"},{"en":"Supposedly means according to what people generally say or believe, though it may be questioned.","zh":"據稱，指根據人們一般所說或所信，但可能被質疑。"},{"en":"The restaurant is supposedly the best in town, but not everyone agrees.","zh":"據稱那間餐廳是城中最好，但並非人人同意。"},{"en":"If something supposedly happened later, earlier evidence creates a problem.","zh":"如果某事按說較後才發生，較早證據就造成問題。"},{"en":"The word can signal distance from a common claim.","zh":"這個詞可以表示與常見說法保持距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"thousands of years later","meaning":"數千年後","examples":[{"en":"The continent was supposedly discovered thousands of years later.","zh":"據稱該大洲在數千年後才被發現。"},{"en":"Thousands of years later means many thousands of years after the earlier event.","zh":"數千年後，指在較早事件之後許多千年。"},{"en":"A tool invented in ancient times may be improved thousands of years later.","zh":"古代發明的工具可能在數千年後被改良。"},{"en":"If a plant appears before its supposed discovery by thousands of years, the timeline is challenged.","zh":"如果植物比其據稱被發現的時間早數千年出現，時間線就被挑戰。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a very large time gap.","zh":"這個短語顯示非常大的時間差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"coca","meaning":"古柯","examples":[{"en":"Coca is a plant from South America.","zh":"古柯是一種來自南美洲的植物。"},{"en":"Coca is a plant whose leaves contain chemical substances including cocaine.","zh":"古柯是一種葉片含有包括可卡因在內的化學物質的植物。"},{"en":"Botanists may study coca to understand where the plant grows naturally.","zh":"植物學家可能研究古柯，以了解該植物自然生長地。"},{"en":"If coca-related substances are found in Egypt, their route there becomes a puzzle.","zh":"如果與古柯相關的物質在埃及被發現，其到達路線就成為謎團。"},{"en":"The word names a plant central to the mummy mystery.","zh":"這個詞指出木乃伊之謎中的核心植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"find its way to","meaning":"到達；流入","examples":[{"en":"Coca may have found its way to Egypt 3,000 years ago.","zh":"古柯可能在三千年前已到達埃及。"},{"en":"To find its way to a place means to reach that place, often through an unclear route.","zh":"到達某地，指抵達該地，通常路線並不清楚。"},{"en":"A rumour can find its way to the whole school within one day.","zh":"謠言可以在一天內傳遍整間學校。"},{"en":"If a plant finds its way across oceans, trade or travel may explain the movement.","zh":"如果植物跨越海洋到達某地，貿易或旅行可能解釋其移動。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests arrival without fully explaining the route.","zh":"這個短語暗示到達，但不完全解釋路線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"explained by contamination","meaning":"以污染解釋","examples":[{"en":"The cocaine could not easily be explained by contamination.","zh":"這些可卡因不容易以污染解釋。"},{"en":"Explained by contamination means accounted for as the result of outside pollution of a sample.","zh":"以污染解釋，指把結果說成是樣本受到外來污染所造成。"},{"en":"A lab result may be explained by contamination if a dirty tool touched the sample.","zh":"如果髒工具接觸樣本，實驗結果可能以污染解釋。"},{"en":"If careful sampling still finds the substance, contamination becomes less convincing.","zh":"如果仔細採樣後仍發現該物質，污染解釋就較不具說服力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one possible explanation for unexpected evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述對意外證據的一種可能解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fake mummies","meaning":"假木乃伊","examples":[{"en":"Fake mummies were considered as one possible explanation.","zh":"假木乃伊被視為一種可能解釋。"},{"en":"Fake mummies are bodies or objects falsely presented as genuine ancient mummies.","zh":"假木乃伊，是被錯誤呈現為真正古代木乃伊的遺體或物件。"},{"en":"A museum may test an object to check whether it is a fake mummy or an authentic one.","zh":"博物館可能測試物件，以檢查它是假木乃伊還是真品。"},{"en":"If the mummies were fake, modern substances inside them would not be surprising.","zh":"如果木乃伊是假的，內含現代物質就不令人驚訝。"},{"en":"The phrase questions authenticity.","zh":"這個短語質疑真確性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Egyptian plants containing it","meaning":"含有該物質的埃及植物","examples":[{"en":"One possibility was that Egyptian plants contained the same substance.","zh":"一種可能性是埃及植物含有相同物質。"},{"en":"Egyptian plants containing it means plants from Egypt that naturally have that substance inside them.","zh":"含有該物質的埃及植物，指埃及本地植物自然帶有那種物質。"},{"en":"Scientists may ask whether local plants contain a chemical before assuming it was imported.","zh":"科學家可能先問本地植物是否含有某化學物質，再假設它是進口的。"},{"en":"If Egyptian plants contained the substance, transoceanic trade would not be needed to explain it.","zh":"如果埃及植物含有該物質，就不需要跨洋貿易來解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase offers a local botanical explanation.","zh":"這個短語提供本地植物學解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"there appeared to be","meaning":"似乎有","examples":[{"en":"There appeared to be another interesting possibility.","zh":"似乎有另一個有趣可能性。"},{"en":"There appeared to be means it seemed that something existed or was possible.","zh":"似乎有，指看來某事存在或可能。"},{"en":"There appeared to be a mistake in the timetable when two classes used the same room.","zh":"當兩班使用同一課室時，時間表似乎有錯誤。"},{"en":"If the simple explanations fail, another possibility may seem worth considering.","zh":"如果簡單解釋失敗，另一可能性可能看似值得考慮。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses cautious observation.","zh":"這個短語表達謹慎觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"trade route","meaning":"貿易路線","examples":[{"en":"A trade route may have linked Egypt to the Americas.","zh":"一條貿易路線可能把埃及與美洲連繫起來。"},{"en":"A trade route is a path used to move goods between places.","zh":"貿易路線，是用來在不同地方之間運送貨物的路線。"},{"en":"Ancient caravans followed trade routes to carry spices, silk, and metals.","zh":"古代商隊沿貿易路線運送香料、絲綢和金屬。"},{"en":"If a trade route existed across the ocean, plants could travel between continents.","zh":"如果跨洋貿易路線存在，植物就可以在大洲之間移動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a regular path of exchange.","zh":"這個短語指固定的交換路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"with links all the way to","meaning":"一直連接到……","examples":[{"en":"The route may have had links all the way to the Americas.","zh":"該路線可能一直連接到美洲。"},{"en":"With links all the way to a place means connected through a long chain reaching that place.","zh":"一直連接到某地，指透過長鏈條連到該地。"},{"en":"A supply network may have links all the way to farms in another country.","zh":"供應網絡可能一直連接到另一國的農場。"},{"en":"If Egypt had links all the way to America, goods could travel through many stages.","zh":"如果埃及一直連接到美洲，貨物就可以經多個階段流動。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a long-distance connection.","zh":"這個短語強調長距離連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make great efforts to","meaning":"努力去","examples":[{"en":"The Egyptians did make great efforts to obtain valuable plants.","zh":"埃及人確實努力取得珍貴植物。"},{"en":"To make great efforts to do something means to try very hard to achieve it.","zh":"努力去做某事，指非常努力嘗試達成它。"},{"en":"Students may make great efforts to improve speaking before an interview.","zh":"學生可能在面試前努力改善口語。"},{"en":"If a society strongly values a product, it may travel far to obtain it.","zh":"如果一個社會非常重視某產品，可能遠行取得它。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises determination and hard work.","zh":"這個短語強調決心和努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"obtain incense","meaning":"取得香料","examples":[{"en":"The Egyptians tried to obtain incense for religious ceremonies.","zh":"埃及人嘗試取得用於宗教儀式的香料。"},{"en":"To obtain incense means to get aromatic plant material used for scent or ritual.","zh":"取得香料，指獲得用於香氣或儀式的芳香植物材料。"},{"en":"A temple may obtain incense for worship and ceremonial use.","zh":"寺廟可能取得香料，用於敬拜和儀式。"},{"en":"If incense was important religiously, traders might travel far to bring it back.","zh":"如果香料在宗教上重要，商人可能遠行把它帶回來。"},{"en":"The phrase connects trade with ritual needs.","zh":"這個短語把貿易與儀式需要連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"valuable plants","meaning":"珍貴植物","examples":[{"en":"The Egyptians obtained valuable plants for medicine and religion.","zh":"埃及人取得用於醫藥和宗教的珍貴植物。"},{"en":"Valuable plants are plants considered useful, rare, expensive, or culturally important.","zh":"珍貴植物，是被視為有用、稀有、昂貴或具文化重要性的植物。"},{"en":"Herbs used for healing may become valuable plants in a community.","zh":"用於治療的草藥可能成為社區中的珍貴植物。"},{"en":"If a plant has medical or religious value, people may trade over long distances for it.","zh":"如果植物有醫療或宗教價值，人們可能遠距離貿易取得它。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why plants could matter economically.","zh":"這個短語解釋植物為何有經濟意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"religious ceremonies","meaning":"宗教儀式","examples":[{"en":"Incense was used in religious ceremonies.","zh":"香料被用於宗教儀式。"},{"en":"Religious ceremonies are formal acts of worship or ritual connected with religion.","zh":"宗教儀式，是與宗教相關的正式敬拜或禮儀行動。"},{"en":"Weddings, funerals, and temple rituals can be religious ceremonies.","zh":"婚禮、葬禮和寺廟儀式都可以是宗教儀式。"},{"en":"If incense is needed for ceremonies, demand for it may support trade.","zh":"如果儀式需要香料，對香料的需求可能支持貿易。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised sacred practices.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的神聖做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"herbal medicines","meaning":"草藥","examples":[{"en":"Valuable plants were used in herbal medicines.","zh":"珍貴植物被用於草藥。"},{"en":"Herbal medicines are treatments made from plants or plant extracts.","zh":"草藥，是由植物或植物提取物製成的治療用品。"},{"en":"Some families use herbal medicines for mild coughs or stomach discomfort.","zh":"一些家庭會用草藥處理輕微咳嗽或胃部不適。"},{"en":"If a plant is believed to heal illness, it can become valuable in trade.","zh":"如果人們相信某植物能治病，它就可能在貿易中變得珍貴。"},{"en":"The phrase connects plants with traditional treatment.","zh":"這個短語把植物與傳統治療連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the majority of","meaning":"大多數……","examples":[{"en":"The majority of archaeologists reject the idea of ancient transoceanic trade.","zh":"大多數考古學家拒絕古代跨洋貿易這個想法。"},{"en":"The majority of means more than half of a group.","zh":"大多數，指某群體中超過一半。"},{"en":"The majority of students may prefer online notes to printed handouts.","zh":"大多數學生可能較喜歡網上筆記，而不是紙本講義。"},{"en":"If the majority of experts reject a theory, strong evidence is needed to change minds.","zh":"如果大多數專家拒絕某理論，就需要強證據來改變想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the larger part of a group.","zh":"這個短語描述群體中的較大部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"archaeologists","meaning":"考古學家","examples":[{"en":"Many archaeologists are sceptical about ancient trade with America.","zh":"許多考古學家對古代與美洲貿易持懷疑態度。"},{"en":"Archaeologists are scholars who study the past through material remains.","zh":"考古學家是透過物質遺存研究過去的學者。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may dig carefully to find pottery, tools, and bones.","zh":"考古學家可能仔細挖掘，以尋找陶器、工具和骨骼。"},{"en":"If archaeologists find no artefacts, they may doubt a trade theory.","zh":"如果考古學家找不到文物，可能懷疑貿易理論。"},{"en":"The word refers to experts in physical evidence from history.","zh":"這個詞指研究歷史實物證據的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hardly worth talking about","meaning":"幾乎不值得討論","examples":[{"en":"To many archaeologists, the idea is hardly worth talking about.","zh":"對許多考古學家而言，這個想法幾乎不值得討論。"},{"en":"Hardly worth talking about means almost not worth discussing because it seems too unlikely or unimportant.","zh":"幾乎不值得討論，指因太不可能或不重要而幾乎不值得談。"},{"en":"A rumour without evidence may be hardly worth talking about in a serious meeting.","zh":"沒有證據的謠言，在嚴肅會議中可能幾乎不值得討論。"},{"en":"If experts think an idea lacks support, they may dismiss it quickly.","zh":"如果專家認為某想法缺乏支持，可能很快否定它。"},{"en":"The phrase shows strong scepticism.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Egyptologist","meaning":"埃及學家","examples":[{"en":"Professor John Baines is an Egyptologist from Oxford University.","zh":"John Baines 教授是牛津大學的埃及學家。"},{"en":"An Egyptologist is a specialist who studies ancient Egypt.","zh":"埃及學家，是專門研究古埃及的專家。"},{"en":"An Egyptologist may study hieroglyphs, temples, mummies, and royal history.","zh":"埃及學家可能研究象形文字、神廟、木乃伊和王室歷史。"},{"en":"If an Egyptologist doubts a trade theory, their objection carries subject expertise.","zh":"如果埃及學家懷疑貿易理論，其反對意見帶有學科專業性。"},{"en":"The word names a scholar of ancient Egyptian civilisation.","zh":"這個詞指出研究古埃及文明的學者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not at all likely","meaning":"完全不大可能","examples":[{"en":"He does not think such a trade network is at all likely.","zh":"他認為這種貿易網絡完全不大可能。"},{"en":"Not at all likely means extremely unlikely or almost impossible.","zh":"完全不大可能，指極不可能或幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"It is not at all likely that a student will score full marks without reading the question.","zh":"學生不讀題就取得滿分，完全不大可能。"},{"en":"If no supporting artefacts exist, an ancient trade network may seem very unlikely.","zh":"如果沒有支持文物，古代貿易網絡可能看似非常不可能。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses strong doubt.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ancient trade network","meaning":"古代貿易網絡","examples":[{"en":"The idea involves an ancient trade network that included America.","zh":"這個想法涉及一個包括美洲在內的古代貿易網絡。"},{"en":"An ancient trade network is a connected system of routes and traders from the distant past.","zh":"古代貿易網絡，是遠古時代由路線和商人連接而成的系統。"},{"en":"Ancient trade networks carried silk, spices, metals, and luxury goods between regions.","zh":"古代貿易網絡在地區之間運送絲綢、香料、金屬和奢侈品。"},{"en":"If America was part of such a network, historians must rethink early global contact.","zh":"如果美洲是這種網絡的一部分，歷史學家必須重新思考早期全球接觸。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised exchange in ancient times.","zh":"這個短語指古代有組織的交換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"essential problem with","meaning":"……的根本問題","examples":[{"en":"The essential problem with the theory is the lack of artefacts.","zh":"這個理論的根本問題是缺乏文物。"},{"en":"The essential problem with something is its most basic and serious weakness.","zh":"某事的根本問題，是其最基本和最嚴重的弱點。"},{"en":"The essential problem with a study plan may be that it leaves no time for practice.","zh":"學習計劃的根本問題可能是沒有留時間練習。"},{"en":"If a theory lacks physical evidence, that weakness may be difficult to overcome.","zh":"如果理論缺乏實物證據，這個弱點可能難以克服。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the core objection.","zh":"這個短語引入核心反對理由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"any such idea","meaning":"任何這類想法","examples":[{"en":"Any such idea must explain the absence of artefacts.","zh":"任何這類想法都必須解釋文物缺失。"},{"en":"Any such idea means any idea of that kind just mentioned.","zh":"任何這類想法，指剛提到那一類想法中的任何一個。"},{"en":"Any such plan to change school rules must explain how students will be protected.","zh":"任何這類更改校規的計劃，都必須解釋學生如何受保護。"},{"en":"If a theory proposes ancient contact, it must explain why supporting objects are missing.","zh":"如果理論提出古代接觸，就必須解釋為何缺少支持物件。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to a whole type of proposal.","zh":"這個短語回指整類提議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"artefacts","meaning":"文物","examples":[{"en":"No artefacts have been found to support the theory.","zh":"沒有發現文物支持該理論。"},{"en":"Artefacts are objects made, used, or changed by humans and studied as historical evidence.","zh":"文物，是由人製造、使用或改造，並作為歷史證據研究的物件。"},{"en":"Pottery, tools, jewellery, and written tablets can be artefacts.","zh":"陶器、工具、珠寶和書寫泥板都可以是文物。"},{"en":"If a trade route existed, archaeologists may expect artefacts from both regions.","zh":"如果貿易路線存在，考古學家可能預期兩地都有相關文物。"},{"en":"The word refers to physical human-made evidence.","zh":"這個詞指人造實物證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"either in Europe or in America","meaning":"在歐洲或美洲任何一方","examples":[{"en":"No supporting artefacts have been found either in Europe or in America.","zh":"在歐洲或美洲任何一方都沒有發現支持文物。"},{"en":"Either in Europe or in America means in one of those two regions, or both when used in a negative sentence.","zh":"在歐洲或美洲任何一方，指在這兩個地區之一；在否定句中可表示兩邊都沒有。"},{"en":"If a missing book is not either in the classroom or in the library, students must search elsewhere.","zh":"如果遺失書本不在課室，也不在圖書館，學生就必須到別處找。"},{"en":"If no artefacts appear on either side, the trade theory becomes weaker.","zh":"如果兩邊都沒有文物出現，貿易理論就變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses absence across two regions.","zh":"這個短語強調兩個地區都缺乏證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"other experts aren’t so sure","meaning":"其他專家並不那麼肯定","examples":[{"en":"Other experts are not so sure that the idea should be rejected.","zh":"其他專家並不那麼肯定這個想法應被拒絕。"},{"en":"Other experts aren’t so sure means some specialists have doubts about dismissing the idea.","zh":"其他專家並不那麼肯定，指一些專家對否定該想法仍有疑問。"},{"en":"One doctor may reject a diagnosis, but other experts may not be so sure.","zh":"一位醫生可能否定某診斷，但其他專家可能並不那麼肯定。"},{"en":"If evidence is unusual but repeated, some scholars may keep the possibility open.","zh":"如果證據異常但重複出現，一些學者可能保持可能性開放。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces disagreement among experts.","zh":"這個短語引入專家之間的分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"historian","meaning":"歷史學家","examples":[{"en":"Professor Martin Bernal was a historian from Cornell University.","zh":"Martin Bernal 教授是康奈爾大學的歷史學家。"},{"en":"A historian is a scholar who studies and interprets the past.","zh":"歷史學家，是研究和解釋過去的學者。"},{"en":"A historian may use documents, artefacts, maps, and earlier research.","zh":"歷史學家可能使用文件、文物、地圖和早前研究。"},{"en":"If a historian sees trade evidence differently from archaeologists, debate may grow.","zh":"如果歷史學家對貿易證據的看法與考古學家不同，辯論可能增加。"},{"en":"The word refers to an expert in history.","zh":"這個詞指歷史專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"more and more evidence of","meaning":"越來越多……的證據","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are getting more and more evidence of early world trade.","zh":"研究者正獲得越來越多早期世界貿易的證據。"},{"en":"More and more evidence of something means an increasing amount of proof or support for it.","zh":"越來越多某事的證據，指支持它的證明或資料不斷增加。"},{"en":"Teachers may see more and more evidence of improvement as students write every week.","zh":"當學生每週寫作，老師可能看到越來越多進步證據。"},{"en":"If evidence keeps growing, a once-unlikely idea may deserve more attention.","zh":"如果證據持續增加，曾經不太可能的想法可能值得更多注意。"},{"en":"The phrase shows accumulating support.","zh":"這個短語顯示支持逐漸累積。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"world trade","meaning":"世界貿易","examples":[{"en":"There is evidence of world trade at an earlier stage.","zh":"有證據顯示世界貿易在更早階段已存在。"},{"en":"World trade means the exchange of goods across distant regions of the world.","zh":"世界貿易，指世界不同遙遠地區之間的貨物交換。"},{"en":"Silk, spices, metals, and luxury goods moved through world trade networks.","zh":"絲綢、香料、金屬和奢侈品透過世界貿易網絡流動。"},{"en":"If world trade began earlier than expected, ancient societies were more connected than assumed.","zh":"如果世界貿易比預期更早開始，古代社會就比假設中更相互連接。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to long-distance international exchange.","zh":"這個短語指長距離國際交換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"at an earlier stage","meaning":"在更早階段","examples":[{"en":"Evidence suggests that world trade existed at an earlier stage.","zh":"證據顯示世界貿易在更早階段已存在。"},{"en":"At an earlier stage means at a previous or more ancient point in development.","zh":"在更早階段，指在較早或較古老的發展點上。"},{"en":"Students should ask questions at an earlier stage, before mistakes become habits.","zh":"學生應在更早階段發問，避免錯誤變成習慣。"},{"en":"If trade existed earlier, historical timelines must shift backward.","zh":"如果貿易更早已存在，歷史時間線就必須向前推。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an earlier point in time or development.","zh":"這個短語指時間或發展上的較早點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Chinese silk","meaning":"中國絲綢","examples":[{"en":"Chinese silk had definitely arrived in Egypt by 1000 BC.","zh":"到公元前1000年時，中國絲綢肯定已到達埃及。"},{"en":"Chinese silk is fine cloth made from silk fibres and associated with China.","zh":"中國絲綢，是由絲纖維製成並與中國相關的精細布料。"},{"en":"Ancient elites valued Chinese silk because it was smooth, light, and difficult to produce.","zh":"古代精英重視中國絲綢，因為它柔滑、輕盈且難以生產。"},{"en":"If Chinese silk reached Egypt, long-distance trade was already possible.","zh":"如果中國絲綢到達埃及，長距離貿易已經可能存在。"},{"en":"The phrase provides an example of early international exchange.","zh":"這個短語提供早期國際交流的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"definitely arriving in","meaning":"肯定已到達……","examples":[{"en":"Chinese silk was definitely arriving in Egypt by 1000 BC.","zh":"到公元前1000年時，中國絲綢肯定已到達埃及。"},{"en":"Definitely arriving in a place means certainly reaching that place.","zh":"肯定已到達某地，指確實抵達該地方。"},{"en":"Exam papers are definitely arriving in schools before the test date.","zh":"試卷肯定會在測驗日期前送到學校。"},{"en":"If silk was certainly reaching Egypt, ancient trade networks were active.","zh":"如果絲綢確實到達埃及，古代貿易網絡就是活躍的。"},{"en":"The phrase removes doubt about arrival.","zh":"這個短語消除對抵達的疑問。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"by 1000 BC","meaning":"到公元前1000年時","examples":[{"en":"Chinese silk had reached Egypt by 1000 BC.","zh":"到公元前1000年時，中國絲綢已到達埃及。"},{"en":"By 1000 BC means no later than the year 1000 before Christ.","zh":"到公元前1000年時，指不遲於公元前1000年。"},{"en":"By Monday, students should have finished the first draft.","zh":"到星期一時，學生應已完成初稿。"},{"en":"If goods arrived by 1000 BC, the trade must have existed at or before that time.","zh":"如果貨物到公元前1000年時已到達，貿易必然在該時或之前已存在。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a latest possible time.","zh":"這個短語給出最遲可能時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in his opinion","meaning":"在他看來","examples":[{"en":"In his opinion, modern people underestimate ancient trade.","zh":"在他看來，現代人低估了古代貿易。"},{"en":"In his opinion means according to what he personally thinks or believes.","zh":"在他看來，指根據他個人的想法或信念。"},{"en":"In her opinion, students learn grammar better through examples than memorisation.","zh":"在她看來，學生透過例子學文法比死記更好。"},{"en":"If a writer uses this phrase, the statement is presented as a viewpoint, not a proven fact.","zh":"如果作者使用這個短語，該陳述就是觀點，而非已證事實。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a personal judgement.","zh":"這個短語指出個人判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"arrogance on the part of","meaning":"……方面的傲慢","examples":[{"en":"He sees arrogance on the part of modern people.","zh":"他認為現代人方面存在傲慢。"},{"en":"Arrogance on the part of a group means proud or superior behaviour shown by that group.","zh":"某群體方面的傲慢，指該群體表現出的驕傲或優越態度。"},{"en":"A manager shows arrogance on the part of leadership if they ignore all staff concerns.","zh":"如果管理層忽視所有員工憂慮，就是領導層方面的傲慢。"},{"en":"If modern people assume ancient societies were incapable, that may be arrogant.","zh":"如果現代人假設古代社會沒有能力，那可能是傲慢。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises an attitude of superiority.","zh":"這個短語批評優越態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"modern people","meaning":"現代人","examples":[{"en":"Modern people may underestimate what ancient societies could do.","zh":"現代人可能低估古代社會能做到甚麼。"},{"en":"Modern people are people living in recent or present times.","zh":"現代人，是生活在近代或當代的人。"},{"en":"Modern people often rely on phones and may forget older navigation skills.","zh":"現代人常依賴手機，可能忘記較古老的導航技巧。"},{"en":"If modern people judge the past only by today’s technology, they may misjudge ancient ability.","zh":"如果現代人只用今天科技判斷過去，可能誤判古人的能力。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts present-day people with people from earlier times.","zh":"這個短語把當代人與較早時代的人作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"transoceanic trading network","meaning":"跨洋貿易網絡","examples":[{"en":"A transoceanic trading network may have existed in ancient times.","zh":"跨洋貿易網絡可能在古代已存在。"},{"en":"A transoceanic trading network is a system of trade routes crossing oceans.","zh":"跨洋貿易網絡，是橫跨海洋的貿易路線系統。"},{"en":"A modern shipping network carrying goods between Asia and America is transoceanic.","zh":"現代把貨物從亞洲運到美洲的航運網絡就是跨洋的。"},{"en":"If such a network existed anciently, goods could move between continents by sea.","zh":"如果這種網絡在古代存在，貨物就能經海路在大洲間流動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ocean-crossing trade connections.","zh":"這個短語描述橫越海洋的貿易連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be set up","meaning":"被建立","examples":[{"en":"Such a trading network may have been set up long ago.","zh":"這樣的貿易網絡可能很久以前已被建立。"},{"en":"To be set up means to be created, arranged, or established.","zh":"被建立，指被創造、安排或設立。"},{"en":"A study group can be set up before exams to share practice questions.","zh":"考試前可以建立學習小組來分享練習題。"},{"en":"If a trade network was set up, people must have organised routes, goods, and contacts.","zh":"如果貿易網絡被建立，人們必然組織了路線、貨物和聯絡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes establishing a system.","zh":"這個短語描述建立系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in recent times","meaning":"在近代","examples":[{"en":"It is arrogant to assume that such networks existed only in recent times.","zh":"假設這類網絡只在近代存在是傲慢的。"},{"en":"In recent times means in the modern or relatively near past.","zh":"在近代，指在現代或相對較近的過去。"},{"en":"In recent times, many students have used online platforms for learning.","zh":"在近代，許多學生使用網上平台學習。"},{"en":"If people think global trade is only recent, they may underestimate ancient societies.","zh":"如果人們認為全球貿易只是近代才有，可能低估古代社會。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts the modern period with ancient history.","zh":"這個短語把現代時期與古代歷史作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"discoveries in mummies","meaning":"木乃伊中的發現","examples":[{"en":"The discoveries in mummies challenged accepted views.","zh":"木乃伊中的發現挑戰了既有觀點。"},{"en":"Discoveries in mummies are findings made by studying preserved ancient bodies.","zh":"木乃伊中的發現，是透過研究保存古代遺體得到的發現。"},{"en":"Scientists may make discoveries in mummies about disease, diet, or burial customs.","zh":"科學家可能在木乃伊中發現關於疾病、飲食或喪葬習俗的資料。"},{"en":"If mummy discoveries contradict plant history, several subjects may be affected.","zh":"如果木乃伊發現與植物史矛盾，幾個學科可能受到影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to evidence found inside or on preserved bodies.","zh":"這個短語指在保存遺體內部或表面找到的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"challenge conventional beliefs","meaning":"挑戰傳統觀念","examples":[{"en":"The findings have challenged conventional beliefs.","zh":"這些發現挑戰了傳統觀念。"},{"en":"To challenge conventional beliefs means to question ideas that most people have long accepted.","zh":"挑戰傳統觀念，指質疑大多數人長期接受的想法。"},{"en":"A new teaching method can challenge conventional beliefs about how children learn.","zh":"新教學方法可以挑戰關於孩子如何學習的傳統觀念。"},{"en":"If evidence does not fit standard history, traditional assumptions may be questioned.","zh":"如果證據不符合標準歷史，傳統假設可能被質疑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pressure on accepted thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述對既有思維造成壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"no longer possible to exclude","meaning":"不再可能排除……","examples":[{"en":"It is no longer possible to exclude the hypothesis completely.","zh":"現在不再可能完全排除這個假說。"},{"en":"No longer possible to exclude means it cannot now be completely ruled out.","zh":"不再可能排除，指現在不能完全把它排除在外。"},{"en":"If several witnesses give the same description, it is no longer possible to exclude that suspect.","zh":"如果幾名證人給出相同描述，就不再可能排除那名嫌疑人。"},{"en":"If evidence keeps appearing, scholars may have to keep a theory open.","zh":"如果證據持續出現，學者可能必須保留某理論的可能性。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that doubt remains but rejection is no longer easy.","zh":"這個短語顯示仍有疑問，但已不容易否定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"hypothesis of","meaning":"……的假說","examples":[{"en":"The hypothesis of transoceanic trade remains possible.","zh":"跨洋貿易的假說仍然可能成立。"},{"en":"A hypothesis of something is a possible explanation that can be tested or examined.","zh":"某事的假說，是可以被測試或檢查的可能解釋。"},{"en":"A science student may form a hypothesis of why one plant grew faster than another.","zh":"科學學生可能形成一個假說，解釋為何一株植物比另一株長得快。"},{"en":"If evidence supports a hypothesis, researchers investigate it further.","zh":"如果證據支持某假說，研究者會進一步調查。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a proposed explanation.","zh":"這個短語引入一個提出的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"transoceanic trade","meaning":"跨洋貿易","examples":[{"en":"The passage considers the possibility of transoceanic trade in ancient times.","zh":"文章考慮古代跨洋貿易的可能性。"},{"en":"Transoceanic trade is trade that crosses oceans.","zh":"跨洋貿易，是橫跨海洋的貿易。"},{"en":"Modern container shipping between continents is a form of transoceanic trade.","zh":"現代大洲間貨櫃航運是一種跨洋貿易。"},{"en":"If transoceanic trade existed anciently, goods and plants could travel far earlier than expected.","zh":"如果跨洋貿易在古代存在，貨物和植物可能比預期更早遠距離移動。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on ocean-crossing exchange.","zh":"這個短語強調跨越海洋的交換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"ancient times","meaning":"古代","examples":[{"en":"The trade may have taken place in ancient times.","zh":"這種貿易可能發生於古代。"},{"en":"Ancient times means a very old historical period, usually thousands of years ago.","zh":"古代，指非常久遠的歷史時期，通常是數千年前。"},{"en":"In ancient times, people used tools, boats, and trade routes very different from today’s.","zh":"在古代，人們使用與今天非常不同的工具、船隻和貿易路線。"},{"en":"If an event happened in ancient times, physical evidence may be rare or fragile.","zh":"如果事件發生在古代，實物證據可能稀少或脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase places an event far in the past.","zh":"這個短語把事件放在遙遠過去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the tale of","meaning":"……的故事","examples":[{"en":"The tale of Henut-Taui shows how evidence can be resisted.","zh":"Henut-Taui 的故事顯示證據如何可能遭到抗拒。"},{"en":"The tale of someone means the story or case involving that person.","zh":"某人的故事，指涉及該人的故事或個案。"},{"en":"The tale of a failed business can teach future owners what to avoid.","zh":"一間失敗企業的故事可以教未來老闆避免甚麼。"},{"en":"If one person’s case reveals a larger problem, the tale becomes more than biography.","zh":"如果一個人的個案揭示更大問題，該故事就不只是 biography。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a story with a lesson or meaning.","zh":"這個短語引入帶有教訓或意義的故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"show that","meaning":"顯示","examples":[{"en":"The stories show that accepted facts can be questioned.","zh":"這些故事顯示，被接受的事實可以受到質疑。"},{"en":"To show that means to demonstrate or make clear that something is true.","zh":"顯示，指證明或清楚表明某事為真。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement can show that regular practice works.","zh":"學生的進步可以顯示定期練習有效。"},{"en":"If several cases point to the same problem, they show that the issue deserves attention.","zh":"如果幾個個案指向同一問題，它們顯示該議題值得關注。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces what evidence proves or suggests.","zh":"這個短語引入證據證明或暗示的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"facts can be rejected","meaning":"事實可能被否定","examples":[{"en":"Facts can be rejected if they do not fit existing beliefs.","zh":"如果事實不符合既有信念，就可能被否定。"},{"en":"Facts can be rejected means true evidence may be dismissed or denied.","zh":"事實可能被否定，指真實證據可能被排斥或否認。"},{"en":"A class may reject test feedback if students do not want to admit weak preparation.","zh":"如果學生不想承認準備不足，班級可能否定測驗回饋。"},{"en":"If evidence threatens people’s beliefs, they may attack the evidence instead of changing their view.","zh":"如果證據威脅人們的信念，他們可能攻擊證據，而不是改變觀點。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that humans do not always accept facts fairly.","zh":"這個短語提醒人類不一定公平接受事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"fit with our beliefs","meaning":"符合我們的信念","examples":[{"en":"Some evidence is rejected when it does not fit with our beliefs.","zh":"當某些證據不符合我們的信念時，它會被拒絕。"},{"en":"To fit with our beliefs means to match what we already think is true.","zh":"符合我們的信念，指與我們已經認為是真的事情相配。"},{"en":"A student may ignore advice if it does not fit with their belief that talent is fixed.","zh":"如果建議不符合學生「才能固定」的信念，學生可能忽視它。"},{"en":"If evidence fails to fit existing beliefs, people may feel uncomfortable.","zh":"如果證據不符合既有信念，人們可能感到不舒服。"},{"en":"The phrase describes agreement with a belief system.","zh":"這個短語描述與信念體系一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be believed to be proven","meaning":"被認為已獲證實","examples":[{"en":"What is believed to be proven may actually be uncertain.","zh":"被認為已獲證實的事情，其實可能並不確定。"},{"en":"To be believed to be proven means people think something has already been fully demonstrated.","zh":"被認為已獲證實，指人們以為某事已被完全證明。"},{"en":"A study method may be believed to be proven until new research questions it.","zh":"某學習方法可能被認為已獲證實，直到新研究質疑它。"},{"en":"If accepted proof is weaker than expected, scholars should stay open to revision.","zh":"如果既有證明比預期薄弱，學者應保持開放接受修正。"},{"en":"The phrase separates belief in proof from actual certainty.","zh":"這個短語把對證明的相信與真正確定性分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"actually be uncertain","meaning":"其實並不確定","examples":[{"en":"Established beliefs may actually be uncertain.","zh":"既有信念其實可能並不確定。"},{"en":"To actually be uncertain means to be less definite or secure than people assume.","zh":"其實並不確定，指比人們假設的更不明確或不穩固。"},{"en":"A student may seem confident but actually be uncertain about the answer.","zh":"學生可能看起來有信心，但其實並不確定答案。"},{"en":"If a belief rests on limited evidence, it may not be as proven as people think.","zh":"如果信念建立在有限證據上，它可能不像人們以為般已被證實。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts appearance of certainty with real doubt.","zh":"這個短語對比表面確定與真正疑問。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"it is understandable, then, why","meaning":"因此不難理解為何……","examples":[{"en":"It is understandable, then, why routine tests could change whole fields of knowledge.","zh":"因此不難理解，為何例行測試可以改變整個知識領域。"},{"en":"It is understandable, then, why means the reason now makes sense after what was explained.","zh":"因此不難理解為何，指在解釋之後，原因變得合理。"},{"en":"If a student slept only two hours, it is understandable, then, why they lost concentration.","zh":"如果學生只睡了兩小時，因此不難理解為何他失去專注力。"},{"en":"If routine tests challenge accepted history, their importance becomes easier to understand.","zh":"如果例行測試挑戰既有歷史，其重要性就更容易理解。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a logical explanation after evidence.","zh":"這個短語在證據之後引入合理解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"routine tests","meaning":"例行測試","examples":[{"en":"A few routine tests produced surprising results.","zh":"幾項例行測試產生了驚人結果。"},{"en":"Routine tests are ordinary, regular tests that are not expected to produce dramatic findings.","zh":"例行測試，是普通、定期且不預期產生戲劇性發現的測試。"},{"en":"A doctor may order routine tests during a yearly health check.","zh":"醫生可能在年度健康檢查中安排例行測試。"},{"en":"If routine tests reveal something unexpected, a major discovery can begin quietly.","zh":"如果例行測試顯示意外結果，重大發現可以悄悄開始。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts ordinary procedure with surprising results.","zh":"這個短語把普通程序與驚人結果作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"fields of knowledge","meaning":"知識領域","examples":[{"en":"The findings could upend entire fields of knowledge.","zh":"這些發現可能顛覆整個知識領域。"},{"en":"Fields of knowledge are broad areas of human understanding, such as history, science, or medicine.","zh":"知識領域，是人類理解的廣泛範圍，例如歷史、科學或醫學。"},{"en":"Climate research belongs to a field of knowledge that affects public policy.","zh":"氣候研究屬於影響公共政策的知識領域。"},{"en":"If one discovery changes several fields of knowledge, many textbooks may need revision.","zh":"如果一項發現改變幾個知識領域，許多教科書可能需要修訂。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised areas of what people know.","zh":"這個短語指人類知識的有組織範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"take for granted","meaning":"視為理所當然","examples":[{"en":"The discoveries challenged things we had taken for granted.","zh":"這些發現挑戰了我們視為理所當然的事情。"},{"en":"To take something for granted means to accept it as true or normal without questioning it.","zh":"視某事為理所當然，指不加質疑地接受它為真或正常。"},{"en":"Students may take clean classrooms for granted until cleaners stop working.","zh":"學生可能把乾淨課室視為理所當然，直到清潔工停止工作。"},{"en":"If evidence challenges something taken for granted, people may feel uncomfortable.","zh":"如果證據挑戰被視為理所當然的事情，人們可能感到不舒服。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against assuming too easily.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要太容易假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生為每條問題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the option letter that matches the answer.","zh":"選出正確字母，指選擇與答案相符的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice question, students may choose A, B, C, or D.","zh":"在選擇題中，學生可能選 A、B、C 或 D。"},{"en":"If students read the evidence carefully, they can choose the correct letter more confidently.","zh":"如果學生仔細閱讀證據，就能更有信心選出正確字母。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"what most surprised","meaning":"最令……驚訝的是甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what most surprised Dr Balabanova about her discovery.","zh":"題目問 Dr Balabanova 對其發現最驚訝的是甚麼。"},{"en":"What most surprised someone means the thing that caused the greatest shock or surprise.","zh":"最令某人驚訝的是甚麼，指造成最大震驚或意外的事情。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask what most surprised students about a documentary.","zh":"老師可能問學生紀錄片中最令他們驚訝的是甚麼。"},{"en":"If several events were surprising, students must identify the strongest one from the text.","zh":"如果幾件事都令人驚訝，學生必須從文本中識別最強的一件。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for the main source of surprise.","zh":"這個短語詢問驚訝的主要來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the presence of","meaning":"……的存在","examples":[{"en":"The presence of drugs in the mummies was unexpected.","zh":"木乃伊中毒品的存在出乎意料。"},{"en":"The presence of something means the fact that it exists or is found there.","zh":"某物的存在，指它存在或在那裡被發現這一事實。"},{"en":"The presence of smoke in a corridor may signal a fire.","zh":"走廊中煙霧的存在可能表示有火警。"},{"en":"If the presence of a substance is unexpected, researchers must explain how it got there.","zh":"如果某物質的存在出乎意料，研究者必須解釋它如何到那裡。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on existence in a place.","zh":"這個短語強調某物在某地存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"drugs in the mummies","meaning":"木乃伊中的毒品","examples":[{"en":"The discovery involved drugs in the mummies.","zh":"這項發現涉及木乃伊中的毒品。"},{"en":"Drugs in the mummies means drug-related substances detected in preserved ancient bodies.","zh":"木乃伊中的毒品，指在古代保存遺體中檢測到與毒品相關的物質。"},{"en":"If a hospital found medicine in old tissue, it would study what the substance was and why it was there.","zh":"如果醫院在舊組織中發現藥物，就會研究物質是甚麼以及為何存在。"},{"en":"If drugs are found in ancient remains, historians must ask whether they were used, traded, or introduced later.","zh":"如果古代遺骸中發現毒品，歷史學家必須問它們是被使用、交易，還是後來進入。"},{"en":"The phrase names the central surprising evidence.","zh":"這個短語指出核心驚人證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"originate in","meaning":"起源於","examples":[{"en":"The plants originated in the western hemisphere.","zh":"這些植物起源於西半球。"},{"en":"To originate in a place means to begin or come from that place originally.","zh":"起源於某地，指最初從該地開始或來自該地。"},{"en":"Tea drinking originated in China before spreading widely.","zh":"飲茶起源於中國，然後廣泛傳播。"},{"en":"If a plant originates in one region, finding it elsewhere may require a historical explanation.","zh":"如果植物起源於一個地區，在其他地方發現它可能需要歷史解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies original source.","zh":"這個短語指出原始來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"western hemisphere","meaning":"西半球","examples":[{"en":"Coca and tobacco originated in the western hemisphere.","zh":"古柯和煙草起源於西半球。"},{"en":"The western hemisphere generally means the half of the Earth containing the Americas.","zh":"西半球一般指包含美洲的地球半球。"},{"en":"Many crops from the western hemisphere later spread around the world.","zh":"許多來自西半球的農作物後來傳遍世界。"},{"en":"If substances from the western hemisphere appear in ancient Egypt, the timeline becomes puzzling.","zh":"如果來自西半球的物質出現在古埃及，時間線就變得令人困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a broad geographical origin.","zh":"這個短語給出廣泛地理來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"positive results","meaning":"陽性結果","examples":[{"en":"The positive results of tests on other mummies supported the finding.","zh":"對其他木乃伊測試所得的陽性結果支持了這項發現。"},{"en":"Positive results are test results showing that the tested substance or condition is present.","zh":"陽性結果，是顯示所測物質或狀況存在的測試結果。"},{"en":"Positive results from several labs are stronger than one isolated result.","zh":"幾間實驗室所得的陽性結果，比單一孤立結果更有力。"},{"en":"If other mummies also test positive, the discovery seems less accidental.","zh":"如果其他木乃伊也測試呈陽性，這項發現就較不像偶然。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to confirming test outcomes.","zh":"這個短語指確認性的測試結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"hostile reaction","meaning":"敵對反應","examples":[{"en":"The hostile reaction of the scientific community shocked the researcher.","zh":"科學界的敵對反應令研究者震驚。"},{"en":"A hostile reaction is an aggressive, unfriendly, or angry response.","zh":"敵對反應，是具攻擊性、不友善或憤怒的回應。"},{"en":"A student may face a hostile reaction if classmates dislike their unpopular opinion.","zh":"如果同學不喜歡某學生不受歡迎的意見，他可能面對敵對反應。"},{"en":"If criticism becomes hostile, careful discussion may break down.","zh":"如果批評變得敵對，仔細討論可能瓦解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong negative response.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈負面回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"scientific community","meaning":"科學界","examples":[{"en":"The scientific community reacted strongly to the publication.","zh":"科學界對這篇論文發表反應強烈。"},{"en":"The scientific community means scientists and researchers working within related fields.","zh":"科學界，指在相關領域工作的科學家和研究者。"},{"en":"The scientific community may debate new evidence before accepting it.","zh":"科學界可能在接受新證據前進行辯論。"},{"en":"If a finding threatens accepted theories, the scientific community may respond cautiously or harshly.","zh":"如果某發現威脅既有理論，科學界可能謹慎或嚴厲回應。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the wider group of scientists.","zh":"這個短語指更廣泛的科學家群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"which of the following","meaning":"以下哪一項","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which of the following explanations was ruled out.","zh":"題目問以下哪一項解釋已被排除。"},{"en":"Which of the following means students must choose from the listed options.","zh":"以下哪一項，指學生必須從列出的選項中選擇。"},{"en":"A test may ask which of the following statements is supported by the passage.","zh":"測驗可能問以下哪一項陳述得到文章支持。"},{"en":"If a question uses this phrase, students should compare every option with the text.","zh":"如果題目使用這個短語，學生應把每個選項與文本比較。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common multiple-choice instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見選擇題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be ruled out by","meaning":"被……排除","examples":[{"en":"One explanation was ruled out by Dr Lescot’s investigation.","zh":"一種解釋被 Lescot 博士的調查排除。"},{"en":"To be ruled out by something means to be rejected because evidence shows it is unlikely or impossible.","zh":"被某事排除，指因證據顯示不太可能或不可能而被拒絕。"},{"en":"A doctor may rule out flu after a negative test.","zh":"醫生可能在測試陰性後排除流感。"},{"en":"If filmed sampling disproves contamination, that explanation is ruled out.","zh":"如果拍攝的採樣過程反駁污染說，該解釋就被排除。"},{"en":"The phrase describes elimination through evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述透過證據排除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"investigation","meaning":"調查","examples":[{"en":"Dr Lescot’s investigation tested the contamination theory.","zh":"Lescot 博士的調查測試了污染理論。"},{"en":"An investigation is a careful search for facts about a question or problem.","zh":"調查，是對某問題或事件仔細尋找事實的過程。"},{"en":"A school may conduct an investigation after exam papers go missing.","zh":"試卷遺失後，學校可能進行調查。"},{"en":"If an investigation is well recorded, its conclusion becomes more credible.","zh":"如果調查被妥善記錄，其結論就更可信。"},{"en":"The word refers to organised fact-finding.","zh":"這個詞指有組織地查明事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be dropped onto","meaning":"掉到……上","examples":[{"en":"The tobacco might have been dropped onto the mummy by chance.","zh":"煙草可能偶然掉到木乃伊上。"},{"en":"To be dropped onto something means to fall or be accidentally placed on its surface.","zh":"掉到某物上，指落下或意外落在其表面。"},{"en":"Crumbs may be dropped onto a desk during lunch.","zh":"午餐時，食物碎屑可能掉到桌上。"},{"en":"If tobacco was dropped onto the mummy recently, it would not be ancient evidence.","zh":"如果煙草是近期掉到木乃伊上的，它就不是古代證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes accidental surface contact.","zh":"這個短語描述意外表面接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"grow in ancient Egypt","meaning":"在古埃及生長","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether tobacco grew in ancient Egypt.","zh":"題目問煙草是否在古埃及生長。"},{"en":"To grow in ancient Egypt means to live or be cultivated there during ancient Egyptian times.","zh":"在古埃及生長，指在古埃及時期於當地生存或被種植。"},{"en":"Wheat and flax grew in ancient Egypt because farmers cultivated them along the Nile.","zh":"小麥和亞麻在古埃及生長，因為農民在尼羅河沿岸種植它們。"},{"en":"If tobacco did not grow there, its presence requires another explanation.","zh":"如果煙草沒有在當地生長，其存在就需要另一解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase asks about ancient plant distribution.","zh":"這個短語詢問古代植物分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"produce false test results","meaning":"產生錯誤測試結果","examples":[{"en":"Chemicals may sometimes produce false test results.","zh":"化學物質有時可能產生錯誤測試結果。"},{"en":"To produce false test results means to cause tests to show an incorrect answer.","zh":"產生錯誤測試結果，指令測試顯示不正確答案。"},{"en":"Dirty equipment can produce false test results in a school experiment.","zh":"骯髒器材可以在學校實驗中產生錯誤測試結果。"},{"en":"If false results are possible, repeating tests becomes important.","zh":"如果可能出現錯誤結果，重複測試就變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how errors may arise in testing.","zh":"這個短語描述測試錯誤如何產生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be fake","meaning":"是假的","examples":[{"en":"Some critics wondered whether the mummies were fake.","zh":"一些批評者懷疑木乃伊是否是假的。"},{"en":"To be fake means to be not genuine or falsely presented as real.","zh":"是假的，指不是真品或被虛假呈現為真。"},{"en":"A fake signature looks real but was not written by the correct person.","zh":"假簽名看似真實，但不是由正確的人書寫。"},{"en":"If the mummies were fake, the unusual chemical results would be less surprising.","zh":"如果木乃伊是假的，不尋常化學結果就較不令人驚訝。"},{"en":"The phrase questions authenticity.","zh":"這個短語質疑真確性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contamination was suspected","meaning":"懷疑受到污染","examples":[{"en":"The discovery was questioned because contamination was suspected.","zh":"這項發現受到質疑，因為有人懷疑樣本受到污染。"},{"en":"Contamination was suspected means people thought the sample may have been polluted by outside material.","zh":"懷疑受到污染，指人們認為樣本可能被外來材料污染。"},{"en":"A water test may be repeated if contamination is suspected in the bottle.","zh":"如果懷疑瓶子受污染，水質測試可能需要重做。"},{"en":"If contamination is suspected, researchers must show how samples were protected.","zh":"如果懷疑受到污染，研究者必須展示樣本如何被保護。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why evidence is doubted.","zh":"這個短語解釋證據為何受到懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"raise difficult questions","meaning":"提出難以回答的問題","examples":[{"en":"The evidence raised difficult questions for accepted historical views.","zh":"這項證據對既有歷史觀點提出難以回答的問題。"},{"en":"To raise difficult questions means to create issues that are hard to answer or explain.","zh":"提出難以回答的問題，指造成很難回答或解釋的問題。"},{"en":"A sudden fall in school results may raise difficult questions about teaching methods.","zh":"學生成績突然下跌可能對教學方法提出難以回答的問題。"},{"en":"If evidence does not fit the standard story, historians must face uncomfortable problems.","zh":"如果證據不符合標準故事，歷史學家必須面對令人不舒服的問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence that makes simple explanations harder.","zh":"這個短語描述令簡單解釋變困難的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the researcher was a woman","meaning":"研究員是女性","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that the researcher was ignored because she was a woman.","zh":"該選項暗示研究員因是女性而被忽視。"},{"en":"The researcher was a woman states the sex or gender of the person who carried out the research.","zh":"研究員是女性，陳述進行研究的人之性別。"},{"en":"A reading question may mention this detail to test whether the passage supports it.","zh":"閱讀題可能提及這細節，以測試文章是否支持它。"},{"en":"If the text gives no evidence of sexism, students should not assume this explanation.","zh":"如果文本沒有性別歧視證據，學生不應自行假設這解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a possible but source-dependent reason.","zh":"這個短語指出一個可能但取決於文本的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"match one of the researchers to","meaning":"將其中一位研究人員配對至……","examples":[{"en":"Students match one of the researchers to each statement.","zh":"學生將其中一位研究人員配對至每項陳述。"},{"en":"To match one of the researchers to a statement means to choose which researcher is connected with that idea or action.","zh":"將其中一位研究人員配對至某陳述，指選出哪位研究者與該想法或行動相關。"},{"en":"In a history task, students may match each scientist to their discovery.","zh":"在歷史任務中，學生可能把每位科學家與其發現配對。"},{"en":"If several researchers are mentioned, students must track who said or did what.","zh":"如果文章提到幾位研究者，學生必須追蹤誰說了或做了甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a matching question.","zh":"這個短語描述配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"there may be more than one correct answer","meaning":"可能有多於一個正確答案","examples":[{"en":"There may be more than one correct answer in this type of task.","zh":"這類題目可能有多於一個正確答案。"},{"en":"There may be more than one correct answer means two or more options could be right.","zh":"可能有多於一個正確答案，指兩個或以上選項可能正確。"},{"en":"In a matching exercise, one researcher may fit two statements.","zh":"在配對練習中，一位研究者可能符合兩項陳述。"},{"en":"If students assume only one answer is possible, they may miss a correct option.","zh":"如果學生假設只可能有一個答案，可能錯過正確選項。"},{"en":"The phrase warns students to read instructions carefully.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生仔細閱讀指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"first to find","meaning":"首位發現……的人","examples":[{"en":"The question asks who was first to find a substance from the Americas in a mummy.","zh":"題目問誰是首位在木乃伊中發現來自美洲物質的人。"},{"en":"First to find means the earliest person to discover something.","zh":"首位發現的人，指最早發現某物的人。"},{"en":"A student may be first to find a mistake in a worksheet.","zh":"學生可能是首位發現工作紙錯誤的人。"},{"en":"If one researcher found tobacco before another found cocaine, sequence matters.","zh":"如果一位研究者先發現煙草，另一位後來發現可卡因，先後次序就很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase asks about order of discovery.","zh":"這個短語詢問發現次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a substance from the Americas","meaning":"來自美洲的物質","examples":[{"en":"Tobacco and cocaine are substances associated with the Americas.","zh":"煙草和可卡因是與美洲相關的物質。"},{"en":"A substance from the Americas means a material or chemical originally linked to the American continents.","zh":"來自美洲的物質，指原本與美洲大陸相關的材料或化學物質。"},{"en":"A plant chemical from South America would be a substance from the Americas.","zh":"來自南美洲的植物化學物質，就是來自美洲的物質。"},{"en":"If such a substance appears in an Egyptian mummy, it challenges normal expectations.","zh":"如果這種物質出現在埃及木乃伊中，就挑戰正常預期。"},{"en":"The phrase connects chemical evidence with geographical origin.","zh":"這個短語把化學證據與地理來源連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"argue against","meaning":"反駁；反對","examples":[{"en":"One researcher argues against the idea of transoceanic trade.","zh":"一位研究者反對跨洋貿易這個想法。"},{"en":"To argue against something means to give reasons why it is wrong or unlikely.","zh":"反對某事，指提出理由說明它錯誤或不太可能。"},{"en":"A student may argue against school uniforms by discussing cost and comfort.","zh":"學生可能透過討論成本和舒適度來反對校服。"},{"en":"If a scholar argues against a theory, they should provide evidence and reasoning.","zh":"如果學者反對某理論，應提供證據和推理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes opposition through argument.","zh":"這個短語描述透過論證提出反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"lack of evidence","meaning":"缺乏證據","examples":[{"en":"The argument against transoceanic trade is based on a lack of evidence.","zh":"反對跨洋貿易的論點基於缺乏證據。"},{"en":"Lack of evidence means there is not enough proof to support a claim.","zh":"缺乏證據，指沒有足夠證明支持某主張。"},{"en":"A teacher may reject an essay argument because of a lack of evidence.","zh":"老師可能因缺乏證據而否定作文論點。"},{"en":"If no artefacts support a trade route, the theory becomes weak.","zh":"如果沒有文物支持貿易路線，該理論就變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies missing support.","zh":"這個短語指出缺少支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"defend against attacks on","meaning":"為……辯護以回應攻擊","examples":[{"en":"The scientist had to defend against attacks on her research methodology.","zh":"這位科學家必須為自己的研究方法辯護，以回應攻擊。"},{"en":"To defend against attacks on something means to answer criticism and protect it from being dismissed.","zh":"為某事辯護以回應攻擊，指回答批評並保護它不被否定。"},{"en":"A student may defend against attacks on their presentation by explaining their sources.","zh":"學生可能透過解釋資料來源，為自己的匯報辯護。"},{"en":"If critics attack the method, the researcher must show that the method was reliable.","zh":"如果批評者攻擊方法，研究者必須展示方法可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes responding to criticism.","zh":"這個短語描述回應批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"attacks on research methodology","meaning":"對研究方法的攻擊","examples":[{"en":"The publication led to attacks on research methodology.","zh":"論文發表引來對研究方法的攻擊。"},{"en":"Attacks on research methodology are criticisms of how a study was designed, tested, or analysed.","zh":"對研究方法的攻擊，是批評研究如何設計、測試或分析。"},{"en":"A survey may face attacks on methodology if it includes too few participants.","zh":"如果調查參與者太少，其方法可能受到攻擊。"},{"en":"If methodology is weak, conclusions become less trustworthy.","zh":"如果研究方法薄弱，結論就較不可信。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on criticism of research methods, not only results.","zh":"這個短語強調對研究方法的批評，而不只是結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"research methodology","meaning":"研究方法","examples":[{"en":"The critics questioned the researcher’s methodology.","zh":"批評者質疑研究者的研究方法。"},{"en":"Research methodology means the methods and procedures used to conduct a study.","zh":"研究方法，指進行研究所用的方法和程序。"},{"en":"A clear methodology explains how samples were chosen and how data was analysed.","zh":"清楚研究方法會解釋樣本如何選取、數據如何分析。"},{"en":"If methodology is strong, surprising findings are harder to dismiss.","zh":"如果研究方法有力，驚人發現就較難被否定。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the design and process of research.","zh":"這個短語指研究的設計和過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"extensive Egyptian trade","meaning":"廣泛的埃及貿易","examples":[{"en":"One scholar gives evidence of extensive Egyptian trade in ancient times.","zh":"一位學者提供古代廣泛埃及貿易的證據。"},{"en":"Extensive Egyptian trade means wide-ranging exchange of goods by ancient Egypt.","zh":"廣泛的埃及貿易，指古埃及廣泛交換貨物。"},{"en":"Trade in incense, silk, and luxury goods may suggest extensive contact with distant regions.","zh":"香料、絲綢和奢侈品貿易可能暗示與遙遠地區有廣泛接觸。"},{"en":"If trade was extensive, unusual imports become more plausible.","zh":"如果貿易廣泛，不尋常進口品就更合理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad commercial activity connected with Egypt.","zh":"這個短語描述與埃及相關的廣泛商業活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"publication of research results","meaning":"研究結果的發表","examples":[{"en":"The publication of research results was controversial.","zh":"研究結果的發表具爭議性。"},{"en":"Publication of research results means formally sharing findings through a paper, article, or report.","zh":"研究結果的發表，指透過論文、文章或報告正式分享發現。"},{"en":"A university may announce the publication of research results after peer review.","zh":"大學可能在同行評審後宣布研究結果的發表。"},{"en":"If results challenge accepted beliefs, publication may trigger debate.","zh":"如果結果挑戰既有信念，發表可能引發辯論。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on making findings public.","zh":"這個短語強調把發現公開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"controversial","meaning":"具爭議性","examples":[{"en":"The results were controversial because they challenged accepted history.","zh":"這些結果具爭議性，因為它們挑戰了既有歷史。"},{"en":"Controversial means causing disagreement, debate, or strong opposing opinions.","zh":"具爭議性，指引起分歧、辯論或強烈相反意見。"},{"en":"A school rule banning phones may be controversial among students and parents.","zh":"禁止手機的校規可能在學生和家長之間具爭議性。"},{"en":"If evidence threatens accepted history, reactions may become divided and emotional.","zh":"如果證據威脅既有歷史，反應可能變得分裂和情緒化。"},{"en":"The word describes something people strongly disagree about.","zh":"這個詞描述人們強烈不同意的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reflect the opinions of the writer","meaning":"反映作者觀點","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements reflect the opinions of the writer.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否反映作者觀點。"},{"en":"To reflect the opinions of the writer means to match what the writer thinks or argues.","zh":"反映作者觀點，指符合作者所想或所論證的內容。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students must separate the writer’s view from other people’s views.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生必須區分作者觀點和其他人觀點。"},{"en":"If a statement matches only a critic’s view, it may not reflect the writer’s opinion.","zh":"如果陳述只符合某批評者觀點，就未必反映作者意見。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in YES/NO/NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語用於 YES/NO/NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"agree with the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點一致","examples":[{"en":"A “yes” answer agrees with the views of the writer.","zh":"“yes” 答案與作者的觀點一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the views of someone means to match that person’s opinions or claims.","zh":"與某人的觀點一致，指符合該人的意見或主張。"},{"en":"A student’s answer agrees with the writer’s view if it says what the writer believes.","zh":"如果學生答案說出作者相信的內容，就與作者觀點一致。"},{"en":"If evidence shows the writer supports a claim, the answer should be yes.","zh":"如果證據顯示作者支持某主張，答案應是 yes。"},{"en":"The phrase tests opinion, not only factual information.","zh":"這個短語測試觀點，而不只是事實資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相反","examples":[{"en":"A “no” answer contradicts the views of the writer.","zh":"“no” 答案與作者的觀點相反。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what that person thinks.","zh":"與某人的觀點相反，指說出與該人想法相反的內容。"},{"en":"If a writer supports school libraries, saying the writer wants to close them contradicts their view.","zh":"如果作者支持學校圖書館，說作者想關閉它們就是與其觀點相反。"},{"en":"If a statement conflicts with the writer’s argument, students should choose no.","zh":"如果陳述與作者論點衝突，學生應選 no。"},{"en":"The phrase describes opposition to an expressed opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述與已表達意見相反。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Students choose “not given” when it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"當無法判斷作者想法時，學生選 “not given”。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means the text does not give enough evidence to decide.","zh":"無法判斷，指文本沒有提供足夠證據作決定。"},{"en":"If a passage mentions a scientist’s work but not their childhood, details about childhood may be impossible to say.","zh":"如果文章提及科學家的工作但沒有提及童年，關於童年的細節可能無法判斷。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from outside knowledge when the passage is silent.","zh":"當文章沒有說明時，學生不應用外部知識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that evidence is insufficient.","zh":"這個短語表示證據不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"proof that","meaning":"……的證據","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether there is proof that tobacco was grown in ancient Egypt.","zh":"該陳述問是否有證據顯示煙草曾在古埃及種植。"},{"en":"Proof that something happened means evidence strong enough to show it is true.","zh":"某事的證據，指足以顯示它為真的有力資料。"},{"en":"A receipt can be proof that a customer paid for an item.","zh":"收據可以是顧客已付款的證據。"},{"en":"If there is no proof that tobacco grew in Egypt, that explanation remains uncertain.","zh":"如果沒有證據顯示煙草在埃及生長，該解釋仍不確定。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for strong supporting evidence.","zh":"這個短語詢問有力支持證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"trade routes across the Atlantic Ocean","meaning":"橫跨大西洋的貿易路線","examples":[{"en":"The passage considers whether trade routes across the Atlantic Ocean existed.","zh":"文章考慮橫跨大西洋的貿易路線是否存在。"},{"en":"Trade routes across the Atlantic Ocean are paths of exchange crossing the ocean between the Americas and Europe or Africa.","zh":"橫跨大西洋的貿易路線，是穿越美洲與歐洲或非洲之間海洋的交換路徑。"},{"en":"Modern ships follow trade routes across the Atlantic Ocean to carry food, machines, and raw materials.","zh":"現代船隻沿橫跨大西洋的貿易路線運送食物、機器和原材料。"},{"en":"If ancient routes crossed the Atlantic, goods could have moved between Egypt and America.","zh":"如果古代路線橫跨大西洋，貨物就可能在埃及與美洲之間流動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long-distance ocean trade paths.","zh":"這個短語描述長距離海洋貿易路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"exist thousands of years ago","meaning":"數千年前已存在","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether such routes existed thousands of years ago.","zh":"題目問這些路線是否在數千年前已存在。"},{"en":"To exist thousands of years ago means to have been present in the very distant past.","zh":"數千年前已存在，指在非常遙遠的過去已經存在。"},{"en":"Some farming systems existed thousands of years ago and still influence food today.","zh":"一些農業制度數千年前已存在，並仍影響今天食物。"},{"en":"If trade routes existed that long ago, ancient people were more mobile than assumed.","zh":"如果貿易路線在那麼久以前已存在，古人的流動能力就比假設中更強。"},{"en":"The phrase places existence deep in history.","zh":"這個短語把存在時間放在深遠歷史中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"ship builders","meaning":"造船者","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to whether ancient Egyptians were great ship builders.","zh":"該陳述提到古埃及人是否是偉大的造船者。"},{"en":"Ship builders are people who design and construct boats or ships.","zh":"造船者，是設計和建造船隻的人。"},{"en":"A coastal town may have ship builders who repair fishing boats.","zh":"沿海城鎮可能有修理漁船的造船者。"},{"en":"If ancient Egyptians were skilled ship builders, long sea journeys become more plausible.","zh":"如果古埃及人是熟練造船者，長途海上旅程就更可信。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies people with boat-making ability.","zh":"這個短語指出具備造船能力的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"generally reject","meaning":"普遍拒絕接受","examples":[{"en":"The scientific community generally rejects the idea of ancient contact with America.","zh":"科學界普遍拒絕接受古代與美洲接觸的想法。"},{"en":"To generally reject something means most people in a group do not accept it.","zh":"普遍拒絕接受某事，指某群體中大多數人不接受它。"},{"en":"Teachers may generally reject answers that are not supported by the text.","zh":"老師通常會拒絕接受沒有文本支持的答案。"},{"en":"If experts generally reject a theory, it remains outside the mainstream.","zh":"如果專家普遍拒絕某理論，它就仍在主流之外。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad but not necessarily total rejection.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛但未必完全一致的否定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"contact between A and B","meaning":"A與B之間的接觸","examples":[{"en":"The idea concerns contact between ancient Egypt and the Americas.","zh":"這個想法關於古埃及與美洲之間的接觸。"},{"en":"Contact between A and B means interaction, communication, or exchange between two people, places, or groups.","zh":"A 與 B 之間的接觸，指兩個人、地方或群體之間的互動、溝通或交換。"},{"en":"Contact between schools can lead to exchange visits and shared projects.","zh":"學校之間的接觸可以帶來交流探訪和共同項目。"},{"en":"If there was contact between Egypt and America, plants and goods might have moved.","zh":"如果埃及與美洲之間有接觸，植物和貨物可能曾移動。"},{"en":"The phrase asks whether two sides interacted.","zh":"這個短語詢問兩方是否互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"unusual test results","meaning":"異常測試結果","examples":[{"en":"The unusual test results were difficult to explain.","zh":"異常測試結果很難解釋。"},{"en":"Unusual test results are results that are unexpected or different from normal findings.","zh":"異常測試結果，是出乎意料或與正常發現不同的結果。"},{"en":"A doctor may repeat unusual test results before giving a diagnosis.","zh":"醫生可能在診斷前重複異常測試結果。"},{"en":"If unusual results appear in several samples, they may reveal a real pattern.","zh":"如果異常結果出現在幾個樣本中，它們可能揭示真實模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes results that require further investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述需要進一步調查的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"come from","meaning":"來自","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether the results could have come from another plant.","zh":"題目問結果是否可能來自另一種植物。"},{"en":"To come from something means to have that thing as the source or origin.","zh":"來自某物，指以該物為來源或起源。"},{"en":"A strange smell may come from food left in a bag.","zh":"奇怪氣味可能來自留在袋中的食物。"},{"en":"If a chemical comes from a local plant, distant trade may not be needed to explain it.","zh":"如果化學物質來自本地植物，就不需要遠距離貿易來解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase asks about source.","zh":"這個短語詢問來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"native to North Africa","meaning":"原產於北非","examples":[{"en":"The plant in the option is described as native to North Africa.","zh":"選項中的植物被描述為原產於北非。"},{"en":"Native to North Africa means originally growing naturally in that region.","zh":"原產於北非，指原本在該地區自然生長。"},{"en":"A desert plant native to North Africa may survive heat and drought well.","zh":"原產於北非的沙漠植物可能很能抵受高溫和乾旱。"},{"en":"If a similar chemical comes from a plant native to North Africa, the mummy evidence may have a local explanation.","zh":"如果相似化學物質來自原產於北非的植物，木乃伊證據可能有本地解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase gives regional plant origin.","zh":"這個短語給出植物的地區來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"main idea of the passage","meaning":"文章主旨","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for the main idea of the passage.","zh":"題目要求找出文章主旨。"},{"en":"The main idea of the passage is the central message or overall point of the text.","zh":"文章主旨，是文本的核心信息或整體重點。"},{"en":"Students should find the main idea before answering detailed questions.","zh":"學生應先找出文章主旨，再回答細節題。"},{"en":"If many paragraphs discuss evidence challenging beliefs, the main idea should include that theme.","zh":"如果許多段落討論挑戰信念的證據，主旨就應包括該主題。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for the whole passage, not one small detail.","zh":"這個短語問整篇文章，而不是一個小細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"experimental research","meaning":"實驗研究","examples":[{"en":"Experimental research can produce results that challenge beliefs.","zh":"實驗研究可以產生挑戰信念的結果。"},{"en":"Experimental research is research that uses tests or experiments to investigate a question.","zh":"實驗研究，是使用測試或實驗來調查問題的研究。"},{"en":"A science class does experimental research when students test how light affects plant growth.","zh":"當學生測試光線如何影響植物生長，科學課就在進行實驗研究。"},{"en":"If experiments produce unexpected results, accepted ideas may need checking.","zh":"如果實驗產生意外結果，既有想法可能需要檢查。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to knowledge gained through controlled testing.","zh":"這個短語指透過受控測試獲得的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"give false results","meaning":"得出錯誤結果","examples":[{"en":"One option suggests that experimental research often gives false results.","zh":"一個選項暗示實驗研究常得出錯誤結果。"},{"en":"To give false results means to produce answers that are incorrect or misleading.","zh":"得出錯誤結果，指產生不正確或具誤導性的答案。"},{"en":"A broken scale can give false results when measuring weight.","zh":"壞掉的磅在量度重量時可能得出錯誤結果。"},{"en":"If research often gave false results, scientists would need repeated testing and verification.","zh":"如果研究常得出錯誤結果，科學家就需要重複測試和驗證。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unreliable outcomes.","zh":"這個短語描述不可靠結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"long-held beliefs","meaning":"長久以來持有的信念","examples":[{"en":"Long-held beliefs can be challenged by new information.","zh":"長久以來持有的信念可以被新資料挑戰。"},{"en":"Long-held beliefs are ideas people have believed for a long time.","zh":"長久以來持有的信念，是人們相信了很久的想法。"},{"en":"A family may have long-held beliefs about education that younger members question.","zh":"家庭可能對教育有長久以來持有的信念，而年輕成員會質疑它們。"},{"en":"If new evidence appears, old beliefs may no longer feel secure.","zh":"如果新證據出現，舊信念可能不再穩固。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on beliefs with a long history.","zh":"這個短語強調有悠久歷史的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be challenged by new information","meaning":"被新資料挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Established ideas can be challenged by new information.","zh":"既有想法可以被新資料挑戰。"},{"en":"To be challenged by new information means to be questioned because fresh evidence does not fit them.","zh":"被新資料挑戰，指因新證據不符合它們而受到質疑。"},{"en":"A student’s answer may be challenged by a sentence they missed in the passage.","zh":"學生答案可能被文章中他漏看的句子挑戰。"},{"en":"If new information contradicts an old theory, scholars must reconsider it.","zh":"如果新資料與舊理論矛盾，學者必須重新考慮它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pressure created by fresh evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述新證據造成的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"conservative by nature","meaning":"本質上保守","examples":[{"en":"One option describes the scientific community as conservative by nature.","zh":"一個選項把科學界描述為本質上保守。"},{"en":"Conservative by nature means naturally cautious and slow to accept major change.","zh":"本質上保守，指天然謹慎，並較慢接受重大改變。"},{"en":"A school may be conservative by nature if it keeps old rules for many years.","zh":"如果學校多年保留舊規則，它可能本質上保守。"},{"en":"If a community is conservative by nature, it may demand very strong proof before accepting new theories.","zh":"如果一個群體本質上保守，在接受新理論前可能要求非常有力證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a cautious basic tendency.","zh":"這個短語描述謹慎的基本傾向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"belief system","meaning":"信念體系","examples":[{"en":"Ideas that do not fit a belief system may be rejected.","zh":"不符合信念體系的想法可能被拒絕。"},{"en":"A belief system is a connected set of ideas people use to understand the world.","zh":"信念體系，是人們用來理解世界的一套相互連接的想法。"},{"en":"A school’s belief system may include ideas about discipline, effort, and success.","zh":"學校的信念體系可能包括關於紀律、努力和成功的想法。"},{"en":"If evidence threatens a belief system, people may defend the system before examining the evidence.","zh":"如果證據威脅信念體系，人們可能先捍衛體系，而不是檢查證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a whole structure of beliefs, not one opinion.","zh":"這個短語指整套信念結構，而不是單一意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 79 - Mystery of the mummies.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 80":[{"front":"Long-Term Forecast: Hot and Dry","meaning":"長期預測：炎熱乾旱","examples":[{"en":"The long-term forecast suggests that many regions may become hotter and drier.","zh":"長期預測顯示許多地區可能變得更炎熱和乾旱。"},{"en":"A long-term forecast is a prediction about conditions far into the future.","zh":"Long-term forecast 是關於遙遠未來情況的預測。"},{"en":"A school may use a long-term forecast to decide whether classrooms need better cooling systems.","zh":"學校可能使用長期預測來決定課室是否需要更好的降溫系統。"},{"en":"If a long-term forecast predicts hotter weather, cities may need to plan for water shortages.","zh":"如果長期預測預計天氣更熱，城市可能需要為缺水作規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when the prediction covers years or decades, not just tomorrow’s weather.","zh":"這個片語用於預測涵蓋多年或數十年，而不只是明天天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"melting land ice","meaning":"陸地冰融化","examples":[{"en":"Melting land ice in the Arctic is expected to raise sea levels.","zh":"北極地區陸地冰融化預計會令海平面上升。"},{"en":"Melting land ice is ice on land turning into water because temperatures are rising.","zh":"Melting land ice 是陸地上的冰因氣溫上升而變成水。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain melting land ice by showing how an ice cube on a tray turns into water.","zh":"老師可能透過展示托盤上的冰粒如何變成水來解釋陸地冰融化。"},{"en":"When land ice melts and flows into the ocean, sea levels can rise.","zh":"當陸地冰融化並流入海洋，海平面可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to ice on land, not sea ice already floating in the ocean.","zh":"這個片語指陸地上的冰，而不是已漂浮在海上的海冰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the Arctic","meaning":"北極地區","examples":[{"en":"Melting land ice in the Arctic will affect global sea levels.","zh":"北極地區陸地冰融化將影響全球海平面。"},{"en":"The Arctic is the cold region around the North Pole.","zh":"The Arctic 是北極周圍的寒冷地區。"},{"en":"Students may study the Arctic when learning about polar bears, ice, and climate change.","zh":"學生學習北極熊、冰和氣候變化時，可能研究北極地區。"},{"en":"If the Arctic warms quickly, ice melt can affect places far away from the poles.","zh":"如果北極地區快速變暖，冰融化可以影響離兩極很遠的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase names a polar region important in climate discussions.","zh":"這個片語命名氣候討論中重要的極地地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be set to","meaning":"將會；預計會","examples":[{"en":"Melting land ice is set to cause a global rise in sea levels.","zh":"陸地冰融化預計會導致全球海平面上升。"},{"en":"To be set to do something means to be expected or likely to do it.","zh":"To be set to do something 指預計或很可能會做某事。"},{"en":"The school is set to open a new library next year.","zh":"學校預計明年會開設新圖書館。"},{"en":"If rainfall is set to fall, farmers may need to store more water.","zh":"如果降雨預計會減少，農民可能需要儲存更多水。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for future developments that seem likely.","zh":"這個片語常用於看似很可能發生的未來發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cause a global rise in","meaning":"導致全球……上升","examples":[{"en":"Melting land ice may cause a global rise in sea levels.","zh":"陸地冰融化可能導致全球海平面上升。"},{"en":"To cause a global rise in something means to make that thing increase around the world.","zh":"To cause a global rise in something 指令某事物在全球範圍內增加。"},{"en":"A worldwide shortage of wheat may cause a global rise in bread prices.","zh":"全球小麥短缺可能導致全球麵包價格上升。"},{"en":"If many glaciers melt at the same time, they can push sea levels higher globally.","zh":"如果許多冰川同時融化，它們可以推高全球海平面。"},{"en":"This phrase links one cause with a worldwide increase.","zh":"這個片語把某一原因與全球性上升連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sea levels","meaning":"海平面","examples":[{"en":"Sea levels will rise as glaciers and land ice melt.","zh":"隨着冰川和陸地冰融化，海平面將會上升。"},{"en":"Sea levels are the average height of the ocean surface.","zh":"Sea levels 是海洋表面的平均高度。"},{"en":"Coastal cities watch sea levels because higher seas can flood roads and homes.","zh":"沿海城市關注海平面，因為較高海水可以淹浸道路和房屋。"},{"en":"If sea levels rise, low-lying islands may lose land.","zh":"如果海平面上升，低窪島嶼可能失去土地。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to discussions of climate change and coastal risk.","zh":"這個片語是氣候變化和沿海風險討論的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"leading to","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"Rising sea levels may lead to disastrous effects for people and wildlife.","zh":"海平面上升可能導致對人類和野生動物的災難性影響。"},{"en":"Leading to means causing something to happen as a result.","zh":"Leading to 指造成某事作為結果發生。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can lead to weak concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致上課專注力弱。"},{"en":"If roads are flooded, this may lead to school closures and transport delays.","zh":"如果道路被水淹浸，這可能導致停課和交通延誤。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with its consequence.","zh":"這個片語把原因與後果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"disastrous effects","meaning":"災難性的影響","examples":[{"en":"Climate change can have disastrous effects on people and wildlife.","zh":"氣候變化可以對人類和野生動物造成災難性的影響。"},{"en":"Disastrous effects are very serious and harmful results.","zh":"Disastrous effects 是非常嚴重和有害的結果。"},{"en":"A long power cut can have disastrous effects on hospitals that need machines to keep patients alive.","zh":"長時間停電可以對需要機器維持病人生命的醫院造成災難性影響。"},{"en":"If flooding destroys homes and farms, the effects can be disastrous.","zh":"如果水浸摧毀家園和農場，影響可能是災難性的。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when the damage is large, painful, and difficult to recover from.","zh":"這個片語用於形容損害巨大、痛苦且難以復原。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"people and wildlife","meaning":"人類和野生動物","examples":[{"en":"Global warming threatens both people and wildlife.","zh":"全球變暖威脅人類和野生動物。"},{"en":"People and wildlife means human communities together with wild animals and plants.","zh":"People and wildlife 指人類社區以及野生動植物。"},{"en":"A polluted river can harm people and wildlife by damaging drinking water and habitats.","zh":"受污染河流可以透過破壞食水和棲息地來傷害人類和野生動物。"},{"en":"If a forest dries out, local families and animals may both lose important resources.","zh":"如果森林乾枯，本地家庭和動物都可能失去重要資源。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that environmental problems affect humans and nature together.","zh":"這個片語提醒讀者，環境問題同時影響人類和自然。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"species worldwide","meaning":"全球物種","examples":[{"en":"Many species worldwide are threatened with extinction.","zh":"全球許多物種面臨絕種威脅。"},{"en":"Species worldwide means different kinds of animals and plants across the world.","zh":"Species worldwide 指世界各地不同種類的動物和植物。"},{"en":"Students may learn about species worldwide when studying rainforests, oceans, and deserts.","zh":"學生學習雨林、海洋和沙漠時，可能認識全球物種。"},{"en":"If habitats shrink, species worldwide may struggle to survive.","zh":"如果棲息地縮小，全球物種可能難以生存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes biodiversity on a global scale.","zh":"這個片語描述全球尺度上的生物多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be threatened with extinction","meaning":"面臨絕種威脅","examples":[{"en":"Many animals are threatened with extinction because of climate change.","zh":"許多動物因氣候變化而面臨絕種威脅。"},{"en":"To be threatened with extinction means to face the risk of disappearing forever as a species.","zh":"To be threatened with extinction 指某物種面臨永遠消失的風險。"},{"en":"A rare frog may be threatened with extinction if its wetland home dries up.","zh":"如果濕地家園乾涸，稀有青蛙可能面臨絕種威脅。"},{"en":"When food sources and habitats vanish, animals can move closer to extinction.","zh":"當食物來源和棲息地消失，動物可能更接近絕種。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very serious survival risk for a species.","zh":"這個片語描述物種非常嚴重的生存風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"low-lying islands","meaning":"低窪島嶼","examples":[{"en":"Low-lying islands may disappear as sea levels rise.","zh":"隨着海平面上升，低窪島嶼可能消失。"},{"en":"Low-lying islands are islands that sit only a little above sea level.","zh":"Low-lying islands 是只比海平面高少許的島嶼。"},{"en":"A small island village may flood easily if storms push seawater inland.","zh":"如果風暴把海水推入內陸，小島村莊可能容易水浸。"},{"en":"If sea levels keep rising, low-lying islands may lose beaches, homes, and farmland.","zh":"如果海平面持續上升，低窪島嶼可能失去海灘、房屋和農地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes places especially vulnerable to flooding.","zh":"這個片語描述特別容易受水浸威脅的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"land masses","meaning":"陸塊","examples":[{"en":"Some low-lying land masses may disappear entirely.","zh":"一些低窪陸塊可能完全消失。"},{"en":"Land masses are large areas of land, such as islands, continents, or coastal regions.","zh":"Land masses 是大片土地，例如島嶼、大陸或沿海地區。"},{"en":"A map shows land masses in different colours from oceans.","zh":"地圖會用不同於海洋的顏色顯示陸塊。"},{"en":"If sea levels rise, small low land masses may be partly or fully covered by water.","zh":"如果海平面上升，小型低窪陸塊可能部分或完全被水覆蓋。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to physical areas of land.","zh":"這個片語指實體土地區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"disappear entirely","meaning":"完全消失","examples":[{"en":"Some islands may disappear entirely because of sea-level rise.","zh":"一些島嶼可能因海平面上升而完全消失。"},{"en":"To disappear entirely means to vanish completely, with nothing left visible.","zh":"To disappear entirely 指完全消失，看不見任何剩餘部分。"},{"en":"A chalk drawing on the playground may disappear entirely after heavy rain.","zh":"操場上的粉筆畫可能在大雨後完全消失。"},{"en":"If a coastal village is swallowed by the sea, it may disappear entirely from the map.","zh":"如果沿海村莊被海水吞沒，它可能從地圖上完全消失。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses complete loss, not just damage.","zh":"這個片語強調完全喪失，而不只是受損。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the havoc wreaked by","meaning":"由……造成的嚴重破壞","examples":[{"en":"The havoc wreaked by greenhouse gases is not limited to flooding.","zh":"由溫室氣體造成的嚴重破壞不限於水浸。"},{"en":"The havoc wreaked by something means the serious damage caused by it.","zh":"The havoc wreaked by something 指由某事造成的嚴重破壞。"},{"en":"The havoc wreaked by a typhoon can include broken windows, flooded shops, and cancelled classes.","zh":"由颱風造成的嚴重破壞可以包括窗戶破裂、商店水浸和停課。"},{"en":"If greenhouse gases change rainfall and temperature, the damage can appear in many forms.","zh":"如果溫室氣體改變降雨和氣溫，損害可以以多種形式出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for widespread destruction or disruption.","zh":"這個片語用於廣泛破壞或干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"greenhouse gases","meaning":"溫室氣體","examples":[{"en":"Greenhouse gases contribute to global warming.","zh":"溫室氣體促成全球變暖。"},{"en":"Greenhouse gases are gases in the atmosphere that trap heat.","zh":"Greenhouse gases 是大氣中會困住熱量的氣體。"},{"en":"Carbon dioxide from cars and power stations is a common example of a greenhouse gas.","zh":"汽車和發電站排放的二氧化碳是常見溫室氣體例子。"},{"en":"If greenhouse gas levels rise, more heat may stay near Earth’s surface.","zh":"如果溫室氣體水平上升，更多熱量可能停留在地球表面附近。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to climate-change discussions.","zh":"這個片語是氣候變化討論的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be confined to","meaning":"限於……","examples":[{"en":"The effects of greenhouse gases will not be confined to excess water.","zh":"溫室氣體的影響不會限於過量水分。"},{"en":"To be confined to something means to be limited to that thing only.","zh":"To be confined to something 指只限於某事。"},{"en":"A school problem may not be confined to one class if students across many levels are affected.","zh":"如果多個級別的學生受影響，學校問題可能不限於一個班。"},{"en":"If climate damage is not confined to flooding, drought and disease may also become concerns.","zh":"如果氣候損害不限於水浸，乾旱和疾病也可能成為憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show that a problem is broader than one area.","zh":"這個片語幫助顯示問題比單一範疇更廣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"excess water","meaning":"過量水分","examples":[{"en":"Flooding is a problem of excess water.","zh":"水浸是一種過量水分問題。"},{"en":"Excess water means more water than a place can safely hold or absorb.","zh":"Excess water 指某地方無法安全容納或吸收的過多水分。"},{"en":"A playground may close if excess water covers the ground after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，如果過量水分覆蓋地面，操場可能關閉。"},{"en":"If drains cannot remove excess water, streets may flood quickly.","zh":"如果排水渠無法排走過量水分，街道可能很快水浸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes too much water causing trouble.","zh":"這個片語描述水太多而造成問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the absence of water","meaning":"缺水","examples":[{"en":"The absence of water can also become a serious environmental problem.","zh":"缺水也可以成為嚴重環境問題。"},{"en":"The absence of water means a lack of water where it is needed.","zh":"The absence of water 指在需要水的地方缺乏水。"},{"en":"The absence of water in a school garden can make plants dry out and die.","zh":"學校花園缺水可以令植物乾枯死亡。"},{"en":"If a region lacks water for years, soil and vegetation may degrade.","zh":"如果一個地區多年缺水，土壤和植被可能退化。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights drought and dryness rather than flooding.","zh":"這個片語突出乾旱和缺水，而不是水浸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in other words","meaning":"換言之","examples":[{"en":"The absence of water can cause desertification, in other words.","zh":"換言之，缺水可以造成荒漠化。"},{"en":"In other words introduces the same idea in a clearer or simpler way.","zh":"In other words 用來以更清楚或更簡單方式表達同一想法。"},{"en":"The shop made a loss; in other words, it spent more money than it earned.","zh":"這間店錄得虧損；換言之，它花的錢多於賺的錢。"},{"en":"If a scientific idea is difficult, writers use this phrase to restate it simply.","zh":"如果科學概念困難，作者會用這個片語簡單重述。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain or rephrase a point.","zh":"這個片語幫助解釋或改述重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"desertification","meaning":"荒漠化","examples":[{"en":"Desertification can turn formerly productive land into dry, degraded land.","zh":"荒漠化可以把以往具生產力的土地變成乾燥退化土地。"},{"en":"Desertification is the process in which dry land becomes less fertile and more desert-like.","zh":"Desertification 是乾旱土地變得較不肥沃並更像沙漠的過程。"},{"en":"A farming village may face desertification if soil is overused and rainfall keeps falling.","zh":"如果土壤被過度使用且降雨持續減少，農村可能面對荒漠化。"},{"en":"When vegetation disappears, wind can remove soil and worsen desertification.","zh":"當植被消失，風可以吹走土壤並加劇荒漠化。"},{"en":"This word describes land becoming too dry and damaged to support normal life.","zh":"這個詞描述土地變得太乾和受損，無法支持正常生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a decrease in","meaning":"……的減少","examples":[{"en":"A decrease in rainfall can increase the risk of desertification.","zh":"降雨量減少可以增加荒漠化風險。"},{"en":"A decrease in something means a reduction in its amount, level, or number.","zh":"A decrease in something 指某物的數量、水平或數目減少。"},{"en":"A decrease in sleep can make students tired and less focused.","zh":"睡眠減少可以令學生疲倦和較難專注。"},{"en":"If rainfall decreases, crops may receive less water and soil may dry out.","zh":"如果降雨減少，作物可能得到較少水分，土壤也可能變乾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something becoming smaller or lower.","zh":"這個片語描述某事變少或變低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the total amount of rainfall","meaning":"總降雨量","examples":[{"en":"The total amount of rainfall may fall in dry regions.","zh":"乾旱地區的總降雨量可能下降。"},{"en":"The total amount of rainfall is the full quantity of rain received over a period.","zh":"The total amount of rainfall 是某段時間內收到的全部雨量。"},{"en":"Farmers may record the total amount of rainfall each month to plan irrigation.","zh":"農民可能每月記錄總降雨量，以規劃灌溉。"},{"en":"If the total amount of rainfall falls, rivers and reservoirs may shrink.","zh":"如果總降雨量下降，河流和水塘可能縮小。"},{"en":"This phrase measures overall rain, not just one storm.","zh":"這個片語量度整體雨量，而不只是一次暴雨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"arid and semi-arid areas","meaning":"乾旱及半乾旱地區","examples":[{"en":"Arid and semi-arid areas are especially vulnerable to desertification.","zh":"乾旱及半乾旱地區特別容易受到荒漠化影響。"},{"en":"Arid and semi-arid areas are places with very little or limited rainfall.","zh":"Arid and semi-arid areas 是降雨極少或有限的地方。"},{"en":"A farm in a semi-arid area may need careful irrigation to grow crops.","zh":"半乾旱地區的農場可能需要仔細灌溉才能種植作物。"},{"en":"If rainfall drops further in these areas, soil can degrade quickly.","zh":"如果這些地區降雨進一步減少，土壤可以迅速退化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dry regions where water is already scarce.","zh":"這個片語描述水分本來已經稀缺的乾燥地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"increase the total area of","meaning":"增加……的總面積","examples":[{"en":"Lower rainfall could increase the total area of drylands worldwide.","zh":"降雨減少可能增加全球乾旱地的總面積。"},{"en":"To increase the total area of something means to make the overall land covered by it larger.","zh":"To increase the total area of something 指令某物覆蓋的整體土地面積變大。"},{"en":"Building new parks can increase the total area of green space in a city.","zh":"興建新公園可以增加城市綠化空間的總面積。"},{"en":"If dry conditions spread, the total area of drylands may expand.","zh":"如果乾燥環境擴散，乾旱地總面積可能擴大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth in physical coverage.","zh":"這個片語描述實體覆蓋範圍增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"drylands worldwide","meaning":"全球乾旱地","examples":[{"en":"Drylands worldwide may expand as rainfall decreases.","zh":"隨着降雨減少，全球乾旱地可能擴大。"},{"en":"Drylands worldwide are dry regions around the world where water is limited.","zh":"Drylands worldwide 是世界各地水分有限的乾燥地區。"},{"en":"Drylands worldwide include places where farming depends heavily on short rainy seasons.","zh":"全球乾旱地包括農業高度依賴短暫雨季的地方。"},{"en":"If drylands expand, more communities may struggle with farming and water supply.","zh":"如果乾旱地擴大，更多社區可能在農業和供水方面遇到困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dry ecosystems on a global scale.","zh":"這個片語描述全球尺度上的乾燥生態系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"potentially at risk from","meaning":"可能面臨……風險","examples":[{"en":"More land may be potentially at risk from desertification.","zh":"更多土地可能面臨荒漠化風險。"},{"en":"To be potentially at risk from something means it may be harmed by that thing in the future.","zh":"To be potentially at risk from something 指未來可能受到某事傷害。"},{"en":"A low-lying school is potentially at risk from flooding during heavy storms.","zh":"低窪學校在強風暴期間可能面臨水浸風險。"},{"en":"If soil is already dry and weak, it may be at risk from further degradation.","zh":"如果土壤已經乾燥和脆弱，它可能面臨進一步退化風險。"},{"en":"This phrase shows possible danger, not guaranteed damage.","zh":"這個片語顯示可能危險，而不是必然受損。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"officially recognised as","meaning":"被正式認定為","examples":[{"en":"Desertification is officially recognised as land degradation in dry areas.","zh":"荒漠化被正式認定為乾旱地區的土地退化。"},{"en":"To be officially recognised as something means to be formally accepted or defined that way.","zh":"To be officially recognised as something 指被正式接受或定義為某事物。"},{"en":"A building may be officially recognised as a heritage site after government review.","zh":"一座建築經政府審查後，可能被正式認定為文物古蹟。"},{"en":"If a problem is officially recognised, governments may be more likely to create policies for it.","zh":"如果問題被正式認定，政府更可能為它制定政策。"},{"en":"This phrase shows formal acceptance, not just casual opinion.","zh":"這個片語顯示正式接受，而不只是隨意看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"land degradation","meaning":"土地退化","examples":[{"en":"Land degradation reduces the productivity of soil and vegetation.","zh":"土地退化會降低土壤和植被的生產力。"},{"en":"Land degradation is the worsening of land quality so that it supports fewer crops, plants, or animals.","zh":"Land degradation 是土地質素惡化，以致支持較少作物、植物或動物。"},{"en":"A farm may suffer land degradation if the same field is overused for many years.","zh":"如果同一片田地多年被過度使用，農場可能出現土地退化。"},{"en":"When soil becomes weak, dry, or salty, farming becomes harder.","zh":"當土壤變弱、變乾或變鹹，農業會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes land becoming less useful and less healthy.","zh":"這個片語描述土地變得較無用和較不健康。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"dry sub-humid areas","meaning":"乾燥亞濕潤地區","examples":[{"en":"Desertification can occur in dry sub-humid areas.","zh":"荒漠化可以發生在乾燥亞濕潤地區。"},{"en":"Dry sub-humid areas are places that are not deserts but still have limited moisture.","zh":"Dry sub-humid areas 是並非沙漠但水分仍有限的地方。"},{"en":"Farmers in dry sub-humid areas may depend on seasonal rain for crops.","zh":"乾燥亞濕潤地區的農民可能依賴季節性雨水種植作物。"},{"en":"If these areas lose rainfall or vegetation, they may move toward desertification.","zh":"如果這些地區失去降雨或植被，它們可能走向荒漠化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regions between humid land and drier land.","zh":"這個片語描述介乎濕潤土地和較乾土地之間的地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"resulting from","meaning":"由……造成","examples":[{"en":"Desertification results from climatic variations and human activities.","zh":"荒漠化由氣候變異和人類活動造成。"},{"en":"Resulting from means caused by or coming from something.","zh":"Resulting from 指由某事造成或源自某事。"},{"en":"A delay resulting from traffic may make a student late for school.","zh":"由交通造成的延誤可能令學生上學遲到。"},{"en":"If land damage results from poor farming, changing farming methods may help.","zh":"如果土地損害由欠佳農業造成，改變農業方法可能有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase links an effect to its cause.","zh":"這個片語把結果與原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"various factors","meaning":"各種因素","examples":[{"en":"Desertification results from various factors.","zh":"荒漠化由各種因素造成。"},{"en":"Various factors are several different causes or influences.","zh":"Various factors 是幾個不同原因或影響。"},{"en":"A student’s exam result may depend on various factors, such as sleep, practice, and stress.","zh":"學生考試成績可能取決於各種因素，例如睡眠、練習和壓力。"},{"en":"If a problem has various factors, one simple solution may not be enough.","zh":"如果一個問題有各種因素，單一簡單解決方法可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a situation has more than one cause.","zh":"這個片語顯示某情況有不止一個原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"climatic variations","meaning":"氣候變化；氣候變異","examples":[{"en":"Climatic variations can contribute to land degradation.","zh":"氣候變異可以促成土地退化。"},{"en":"Climatic variations are changes in climate patterns, such as rainfall, temperature, or drought frequency.","zh":"Climatic variations 是氣候模式的變化，例如降雨、氣溫或乾旱頻率。"},{"en":"Farmers notice climatic variations when rainy seasons arrive later than usual.","zh":"當雨季比平常遲來，農民會注意到氣候變異。"},{"en":"If climate patterns vary too much, crops and water systems become harder to manage.","zh":"如果氣候模式變化太大，作物和水系統會更難管理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes natural or long-term changes in climate conditions.","zh":"這個片語描述自然或長期氣候狀況變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"human activities","meaning":"人類活動","examples":[{"en":"Human activities can accelerate desertification.","zh":"人類活動可以加速荒漠化。"},{"en":"Human activities are things people do, such as farming, building, cutting trees, or using water.","zh":"Human activities 是人們所做的事情，例如耕作、建設、砍樹或用水。"},{"en":"Overusing a field is a human activity that can weaken soil.","zh":"過度使用田地是一種可以削弱土壤的人類活動。"},{"en":"If human activities remove vegetation, wind and heat can damage the land more easily.","zh":"如果人類活動移除植被，風和熱更容易破壞土地。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that environmental damage is not caused by nature alone.","zh":"這個片語提醒我們，環境破壞不只是由自然造成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"formerly productive land","meaning":"以往具生產力的土地","examples":[{"en":"Formerly productive land can become degraded through desertification.","zh":"以往具生產力的土地可以因荒漠化而退化。"},{"en":"Formerly productive land is land that used to grow crops or support life well.","zh":"Formerly productive land 是過去能良好種植作物或支持生命的土地。"},{"en":"A farm that once produced vegetables may become formerly productive land after years of misuse.","zh":"一個曾經出產蔬菜的農場，在多年濫用後可能變成以往具生產力的土地。"},{"en":"If soil loses nutrients and water, productive land can stop producing food.","zh":"如果土壤失去養分和水分，具生產力的土地可能停止生產食物。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the land’s useful past with its damaged present.","zh":"這個片語對比土地有用的過去和受損的現在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a complex process","meaning":"複雜過程","examples":[{"en":"Desertification is a complex process involving many causes.","zh":"荒漠化是一個涉及多個成因的複雜過程。"},{"en":"A complex process is a process with many connected steps, causes, or effects.","zh":"Complex process 是包含許多相連步驟、原因或影響的過程。"},{"en":"Learning to write well is a complex process because grammar, ideas, and organisation all matter.","zh":"學會寫作是一個複雜過程，因為文法、想法和組織都重要。"},{"en":"If a process is complex, simple answers may miss important details.","zh":"如果過程複雜，簡單答案可能忽略重要細節。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something cannot be explained by one cause only.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事不能只用一個原因解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"multiple causes","meaning":"多重成因","examples":[{"en":"The process of desertification involves multiple causes.","zh":"荒漠化過程涉及多重成因。"},{"en":"Multiple causes are several different reasons that work together to create a result.","zh":"Multiple causes 是幾個不同原因共同造成結果。"},{"en":"A student’s poor attendance may have multiple causes, including illness, transport, and family problems.","zh":"學生出席率差可能有多重成因，包括疾病、交通和家庭問題。"},{"en":"If a problem has multiple causes, solving only one may not fix it.","zh":"如果問題有多重成因，只解決一個可能不能修復它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining complicated problems.","zh":"這個片語適用於解釋複雜問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"proceed at varying rates","meaning":"以不同速度進行","examples":[{"en":"Desertification proceeds at varying rates in different climates.","zh":"荒漠化在不同氣候中以不同速度進行。"},{"en":"To proceed at varying rates means to happen at different speeds in different situations.","zh":"To proceed at varying rates 指在不同情況下以不同速度發生。"},{"en":"Students learn vocabulary at varying rates because some practise more often than others.","zh":"學生以不同速度學習詞彙，因為有些人練習得更頻密。"},{"en":"If land is dry and poorly managed, degradation may proceed faster.","zh":"如果土地乾燥且管理欠佳，退化可能進行得更快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an uneven speed of development.","zh":"這個片語描述發展速度不平均。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in different climates","meaning":"在不同氣候中","examples":[{"en":"The process occurs at different rates in different climates.","zh":"這個過程在不同氣候中以不同速度發生。"},{"en":"In different climates means under different patterns of temperature, rainfall, and weather.","zh":"In different climates 指在不同氣溫、降雨和天氣模式下。"},{"en":"The same plant may grow differently in different climates.","zh":"同一種植物在不同氣候中可能有不同生長情況。"},{"en":"If a place is hotter and drier, land damage may develop faster than in a wetter region.","zh":"如果某地更熱更乾，土地損害可能比濕潤地區發展更快。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how conditions change across regions.","zh":"這個片語比較不同地區條件如何改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"intensify a climatic trend","meaning":"加劇氣候趨勢","examples":[{"en":"Desertification may intensify a general climatic trend.","zh":"荒漠化可能加劇一般氣候趨勢。"},{"en":"To intensify a climatic trend means to make an existing climate pattern stronger.","zh":"To intensify a climatic trend 指令已有氣候模式變得更強。"},{"en":"More concrete in a city can intensify a warming trend by trapping heat.","zh":"城市中更多混凝土可以透過困住熱量而加劇變暖趨勢。"},{"en":"If land loses vegetation, dryness may become even stronger.","zh":"如果土地失去植被，乾燥情況可能變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a climate pattern more severe.","zh":"這個片語描述令氣候模式更嚴重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"initiate a change in","meaning":"引發……的轉變","examples":[{"en":"Desertification may initiate a change in local climate.","zh":"荒漠化可能引發本地氣候的轉變。"},{"en":"To initiate a change in something means to start a change in it.","zh":"To initiate a change in something 指開始令某事出現改變。"},{"en":"A new timetable may initiate a change in students’ morning routines.","zh":"新時間表可能引發學生早上日常安排的轉變。"},{"en":"If vegetation disappears, it may start changing rainfall and temperature near the ground.","zh":"如果植被消失，它可能開始改變地面附近的降雨和氣溫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of a change.","zh":"這個片語描述轉變的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"local climate","meaning":"本地氣候","examples":[{"en":"Desertification can alter the local climate.","zh":"荒漠化可以改變本地氣候。"},{"en":"Local climate is the usual weather pattern of a particular area.","zh":"Local climate 是某特定地區的通常天氣模式。"},{"en":"A coastal town may have a local climate that is cooler than inland areas.","zh":"沿海小鎮的本地氣候可能比內陸地區較涼。"},{"en":"If forests are removed, the local climate may become hotter and drier.","zh":"如果森林被移除，本地氣候可能變得更熱和更乾。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to climate at a specific place, not the whole planet.","zh":"這個片語指特定地方的氣候，而不是整個地球。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lead towards greater aridity","meaning":"導向更乾旱","examples":[{"en":"Both processes lead towards greater aridity.","zh":"兩個過程都導向更乾旱。"},{"en":"To lead towards greater aridity means to move conditions toward being drier.","zh":"To lead towards greater aridity 指令環境朝更乾燥方向發展。"},{"en":"Cutting trees and using too much groundwater can lead towards greater aridity in a farming area.","zh":"砍樹和過度使用地下水可以令農業地區導向更乾旱。"},{"en":"If the land becomes drier, plants grow less easily and soil damage may increase.","zh":"如果土地變得更乾，植物較難生長，土壤損害可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a movement toward more dryness.","zh":"這個片語描述朝更乾燥方向轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"aridity","meaning":"乾旱程度","examples":[{"en":"Greater aridity makes land more vulnerable to degradation.","zh":"更高乾旱程度令土地更容易退化。"},{"en":"Aridity is the condition of being very dry because there is little water or rainfall.","zh":"Aridity 是因水或降雨很少而非常乾燥的狀況。"},{"en":"Farmers can see aridity when soil cracks and plants need constant watering.","zh":"當土壤裂開而植物需要不斷澆水時，農民可以看見乾旱程度。"},{"en":"If aridity increases, farming becomes harder and water demand rises.","zh":"如果乾旱程度增加，農業會更困難，用水需求也會上升。"},{"en":"This word describes the dryness of a place.","zh":"這個詞描述一個地方的乾燥程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be associated with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"More arid conditions are associated with desertification.","zh":"更乾旱的狀況與荒漠化有關。"},{"en":"To be associated with something means to be connected with it in some way.","zh":"To be associated with something 指以某種方式與某事有關。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is often associated with weaker concentration at school.","zh":"睡眠不足常與學校專注力較弱有關。"},{"en":"If dry conditions are associated with land damage, scientists will study the link carefully.","zh":"如果乾燥狀況與土地損害有關，科學家會仔細研究這種關係。"},{"en":"This phrase shows connection, but not always direct cause.","zh":"這個片語顯示關聯，但不一定是直接原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"accelerate the depletion of","meaning":"加速……的耗損","examples":[{"en":"Desertification can accelerate the depletion of vegetation and soils.","zh":"荒漠化可以加速植被和土壤的耗損。"},{"en":"To accelerate the depletion of something means to make it disappear or weaken more quickly.","zh":"To accelerate the depletion of something 指令某物更快消失或變弱。"},{"en":"Overuse of a school printer can accelerate the depletion of paper supplies.","zh":"過度使用學校打印機可以加速紙張供應耗盡。"},{"en":"If plants disappear faster, soil may become exposed and damaged more easily.","zh":"如果植物更快消失，土壤可能暴露並更容易受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes speeding up loss or exhaustion.","zh":"這個片語描述加快流失或耗盡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"vegetation and soils","meaning":"植被和土壤","examples":[{"en":"The depletion of vegetation and soils worsens desertification.","zh":"植被和土壤的耗損會惡化荒漠化。"},{"en":"Vegetation and soils means plant cover and the ground material in which plants grow.","zh":"Vegetation and soils 指植物覆蓋和植物生長其中的地面物質。"},{"en":"A school garden needs healthy vegetation and soils to grow flowers and vegetables.","zh":"學校花園需要健康的植被和土壤來種花和蔬菜。"},{"en":"If vegetation disappears, soil can be blown away by wind.","zh":"如果植被消失，土壤可以被風吹走。"},{"en":"This phrase names two basic parts of a healthy land ecosystem.","zh":"這個片語命名健康土地生態系統的兩個基本部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"occur all over the world","meaning":"發生於世界各地","examples":[{"en":"Land degradation occurs all over the world.","zh":"土地退化發生於世界各地。"},{"en":"To occur all over the world means to happen in many countries and regions globally.","zh":"To occur all over the world 指在全球許多國家和地區發生。"},{"en":"Plastic waste problems occur all over the world, from cities to beaches.","zh":"塑膠垃圾問題發生於世界各地，從城市到海灘都有。"},{"en":"If a problem occurs worldwide, international cooperation may be needed.","zh":"如果問題全球發生，可能需要國際合作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an issue is global, not local.","zh":"這個片語顯示議題是全球性，而不是本地性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be referred to as","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"Land degradation is referred to as desertification when it occurs in drylands.","zh":"土地退化發生在乾旱地時被稱為荒漠化。"},{"en":"To be referred to as something means to be called by that name.","zh":"To be referred to as something 指被稱作某名稱。"},{"en":"A school’s main hall may be referred to as the assembly hall.","zh":"學校禮堂可能被稱為集會堂。"},{"en":"If land degradation happens in dry areas, experts may refer to it as desertification.","zh":"如果土地退化發生在乾旱地區，專家可能稱之為荒漠化。"},{"en":"This phrase explains naming or terminology.","zh":"這個片語解釋命名或術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take place in drylands","meaning":"發生在乾旱地","examples":[{"en":"The process is called desertification when it takes place in drylands.","zh":"這個過程發生在乾旱地時，被稱為荒漠化。"},{"en":"To take place in drylands means to happen in dry regions with limited water.","zh":"To take place in drylands 指在水分有限的乾燥地區發生。"},{"en":"A farming study may take place in drylands to test water-saving crops.","zh":"農業研究可能在乾旱地進行，以測試節水作物。"},{"en":"If land degradation takes place in drylands, recovery may be slow and difficult.","zh":"如果土地退化發生在乾旱地，恢復可能緩慢而困難。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where the process happens.","zh":"這個片語指出過程發生的地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be prone to","meaning":"容易出現……","examples":[{"en":"Drylands are prone to more permanent damage.","zh":"乾旱地容易出現更永久性的破壞。"},{"en":"To be prone to something means to be likely to suffer from it.","zh":"To be prone to something 指很可能遭受某事。"},{"en":"A student who sleeps too little is prone to making careless mistakes.","zh":"睡眠太少的學生容易出現粗心錯誤。"},{"en":"If land is already dry, it is more prone to damage from wind and heat.","zh":"如果土地本來已乾燥，它更容易受風和熱破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong tendency or vulnerability.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈傾向或脆弱性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"permanent damage","meaning":"永久性破壞","examples":[{"en":"Drylands are especially prone to permanent damage.","zh":"乾旱地特別容易出現永久性破壞。"},{"en":"Permanent damage is harm that cannot easily be repaired or reversed.","zh":"Permanent damage 是不容易修復或逆轉的傷害。"},{"en":"A phone may suffer permanent damage if it is dropped into water and not repaired quickly.","zh":"如果手機掉進水裏且未及時維修，可能出現永久性損壞。"},{"en":"If soil is lost completely, farming may not recover for many years.","zh":"如果土壤完全流失，農業可能多年都無法恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damage that lasts for a very long time.","zh":"這個片語描述持續很久的破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"degraded land","meaning":"退化土地","examples":[{"en":"Degraded land may spread and merge into desert-like conditions.","zh":"退化土地可能擴散並融合成類似沙漠的狀況。"},{"en":"Degraded land is land whose soil, vegetation, or productivity has been damaged.","zh":"Degraded land 是土壤、植被或生產力受損的土地。"},{"en":"A field can become degraded land if crops are grown on it every year without rest.","zh":"如果一塊田每年都種植而沒有休耕，它可能變成退化土地。"},{"en":"If degraded land spreads, nearby farms may also become less productive.","zh":"如果退化土地擴散，附近農場也可能變得較無生產力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes land that has lost quality and usefulness.","zh":"這個片語描述失去質素和用途的土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"spread and merge together","meaning":"擴散並融合","examples":[{"en":"Areas of degraded land can spread and merge together.","zh":"退化土地區域可以擴散並融合。"},{"en":"To spread and merge together means to expand and join into a larger connected area.","zh":"To spread and merge together 指擴大並連接成更大的相連區域。"},{"en":"Small puddles on a playground may spread and merge together after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，操場上的小水氹可能擴散並融合。"},{"en":"If patches of damaged land join, the affected area becomes harder to restore.","zh":"如果受損土地斑塊連在一起，受影響區域會更難恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes separate areas becoming one larger area.","zh":"這個片語描述分散地區變成更大區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"desert-like conditions","meaning":"類似沙漠的狀況","examples":[{"en":"Degraded drylands may form desert-like conditions.","zh":"退化乾旱地可能形成類似沙漠的狀況。"},{"en":"Desert-like conditions are dry, barren conditions similar to a desert.","zh":"Desert-like conditions 是乾燥、貧瘠並類似沙漠的狀況。"},{"en":"A neglected garden may develop desert-like conditions if the soil dries and no plants survive.","zh":"如果土壤乾透且沒有植物存活，被忽視的花園可能出現類似沙漠的狀況。"},{"en":"If land becomes desert-like, farming and grazing become extremely difficult.","zh":"如果土地變得像沙漠，耕作和放牧會極其困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes land that resembles a desert even if it is not officially one.","zh":"這個片語描述土地像沙漠，即使它不一定正式是沙漠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"brought about by","meaning":"由……引起","examples":[{"en":"Global warming is brought about by increasing greenhouse gas levels.","zh":"全球變暖由溫室氣體水平增加引起。"},{"en":"To be brought about by something means to be caused by it.","zh":"To be brought about by something 指由某事造成。"},{"en":"A change in school rules may be brought about by repeated safety problems.","zh":"學校規則改變可能由反覆安全問題引起。"},{"en":"If rising emissions bring about warming, reducing emissions becomes important.","zh":"如果排放上升引起變暖，減少排放就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase links a result to its cause.","zh":"這個片語把結果與原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"greenhouse gas levels","meaning":"溫室氣體水平","examples":[{"en":"Increasing greenhouse gas levels are expected to change weather patterns.","zh":"溫室氣體水平增加預計會改變天氣模式。"},{"en":"Greenhouse gas levels are the amounts of heat-trapping gases in the atmosphere.","zh":"Greenhouse gas levels 是大氣中困住熱量氣體的數量。"},{"en":"Scientists measure greenhouse gas levels to understand how quickly climate risks are growing.","zh":"科學家量度溫室氣體水平，以了解氣候風險增長得有多快。"},{"en":"If these levels keep rising, global temperatures may continue to increase.","zh":"如果這些水平持續上升，全球氣溫可能繼續增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the concentration of climate-warming gases.","zh":"這個片語描述令氣候變暖氣體的濃度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the atmosphere","meaning":"在大氣中","examples":[{"en":"Greenhouse gas levels in the atmosphere are increasing.","zh":"大氣中的溫室氣體水平正在上升。"},{"en":"In the atmosphere means in the layer of air surrounding Earth.","zh":"In the atmosphere 指在包圍地球的空氣層中。"},{"en":"Smoke in the atmosphere can make the sky look grey and reduce visibility.","zh":"大氣中的煙可以令天空變灰並降低能見度。"},{"en":"If more heat-trapping gases remain in the atmosphere, temperatures may rise.","zh":"如果更多困住熱量的氣體停留在大氣中，氣溫可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase shows where gases, dust, or particles are located.","zh":"這個片語顯示氣體、塵埃或粒子所在位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be expected to","meaning":"預計會","examples":[{"en":"Global warming is expected to increase extreme weather events.","zh":"全球變暖預計會增加極端天氣事件。"},{"en":"To be expected to do something means people think it is likely to happen.","zh":"To be expected to do something 指人們認為某事很可能發生。"},{"en":"The new bus route is expected to reduce travel time for students.","zh":"新巴士路線預計會減少學生通勤時間。"},{"en":"If temperatures are expected to rise, governments may prepare heat-warning systems.","zh":"如果氣溫預計會上升，政府可能準備高溫警告系統。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a likely future result.","zh":"這個片語表達可能的未來結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"variability of weather conditions","meaning":"天氣狀況的變化幅度","examples":[{"en":"Climate change may increase the variability of weather conditions.","zh":"氣候變化可能增加天氣狀況的變化幅度。"},{"en":"Variability of weather conditions means weather becomes more changeable or less predictable.","zh":"Variability of weather conditions 指天氣變得更易變或更難預測。"},{"en":"A school picnic becomes harder to plan if weather conditions vary greatly from day to day.","zh":"如果天氣每天變化很大，學校野餐會更難安排。"},{"en":"If rainfall and temperature become more variable, farmers cannot rely on old patterns.","zh":"如果降雨和氣溫變得更不穩定，農民不能依賴舊模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unstable weather behaviour.","zh":"這個片語描述不穩定的天氣行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"extreme events","meaning":"極端事件","examples":[{"en":"Global warming is expected to increase extreme events.","zh":"全球變暖預計會增加極端事件。"},{"en":"Extreme events are unusually severe events, such as heatwaves, floods, droughts, or storms.","zh":"Extreme events 是異常嚴重的事件，例如熱浪、水災、乾旱或風暴。"},{"en":"A city may open emergency shelters during extreme events.","zh":"城市可能在極端事件期間開放緊急庇護中心。"},{"en":"If extreme events become more common, insurance and public services may face pressure.","zh":"如果極端事件變得更常見，保險和公共服務可能面對壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes events outside normal conditions.","zh":"這個片語描述超出正常情況的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"face increasingly low and erratic rainfall","meaning":"面對越來越少且不穩定的降雨","examples":[{"en":"Many dryland areas face increasingly low and erratic rainfall.","zh":"許多乾旱地區面對越來越少且不穩定的降雨。"},{"en":"To face increasingly low and erratic rainfall means to deal with less rain and more unpredictable rain over time.","zh":"To face increasingly low and erratic rainfall 指隨時間面對更少且更難預測的降雨。"},{"en":"Farmers may face this problem when rain comes late, suddenly, or not at all.","zh":"當雨來得遲、突然來，或完全不來，農民可能面對這個問題。"},{"en":"If rainfall becomes both lower and less reliable, crops may fail more often.","zh":"如果降雨既減少又較不可靠，農作物可能更常歉收。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a worsening water problem in dry regions.","zh":"這個片語描述乾燥地區日益惡化的水分問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"erratic rainfall","meaning":"不穩定降雨","examples":[{"en":"Erratic rainfall makes farming more difficult in drylands.","zh":"不穩定降雨令乾旱地區的農業更困難。"},{"en":"Erratic rainfall is rain that comes irregularly and unpredictably.","zh":"Erratic rainfall 是不規則且難以預測的降雨。"},{"en":"A farmer may struggle if rain falls heavily one week and disappears for months.","zh":"如果雨一星期下得很大，之後幾個月消失，農民可能很吃力。"},{"en":"If rainfall is erratic, crops may be planted at the wrong time.","zh":"如果降雨不穩定，作物可能在錯誤時間種植。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rain that farmers cannot rely on.","zh":"這個片語描述農民不能依賴的雨水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"coupled with","meaning":"加上；伴隨着","examples":[{"en":"Low rainfall is coupled with wind erosion of soil.","zh":"低降雨量加上風蝕土壤。"},{"en":"Coupled with means together with another factor, often making a problem worse.","zh":"Coupled with 指連同另一因素，通常令問題更嚴重。"},{"en":"Long working hours, coupled with poor sleep, can damage health.","zh":"長工時加上睡眠不足，可以損害健康。"},{"en":"If low rainfall is coupled with soil erosion, land degradation becomes more serious.","zh":"如果低降雨量加上土壤侵蝕，土地退化會更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase links two conditions that act together.","zh":"這個片語把兩個共同作用的條件連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"wind erosion of soil","meaning":"風蝕土壤","examples":[{"en":"Wind erosion of soil damages dryland environments.","zh":"風蝕土壤會破壞乾旱地環境。"},{"en":"Wind erosion of soil happens when wind blows away the top layer of soil.","zh":"Wind erosion of soil 是風把土壤表層吹走。"},{"en":"A dry field without plants is more likely to suffer wind erosion.","zh":"沒有植物的乾燥田地更容易遭受風蝕。"},{"en":"If topsoil is removed by wind, crops have fewer nutrients to grow.","zh":"如果表土被風吹走，作物生長所需養分會減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes soil being lost through wind.","zh":"這個片語描述土壤因風而流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"drying up of water resources","meaning":"水資源枯竭","examples":[{"en":"Rising temperatures may cause the drying up of water resources.","zh":"氣溫上升可能造成水資源枯竭。"},{"en":"Drying up of water resources means rivers, wells, lakes, or reservoirs losing water.","zh":"Drying up of water resources 指河流、水井、湖泊或水塘失去水分。"},{"en":"A village may face the drying up of water resources after several years of drought.","zh":"幾年乾旱後，村莊可能面對水資源枯竭。"},{"en":"If water resources dry up, families, farms, and hospitals may all suffer.","zh":"如果水資源枯竭，家庭、農場和醫院都可能受苦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes water supplies becoming unavailable.","zh":"這個片語描述水供應變得不可用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"regional temperatures rise","meaning":"地區氣溫上升","examples":[{"en":"Water resources may dry up as regional temperatures rise.","zh":"隨着地區氣溫上升，水資源可能枯竭。"},{"en":"Regional temperatures rise means a particular area becomes hotter over time.","zh":"Regional temperatures rise 指某特定地區隨時間變得更熱。"},{"en":"If regional temperatures rise, schools may need more shade and drinking water stations.","zh":"如果地區氣溫上升，學校可能需要更多遮蔭和飲水站。"},{"en":"Higher regional temperatures can increase evaporation from lakes and soil.","zh":"較高地區氣溫可以增加湖泊和土壤中的蒸發。"},{"en":"This phrase describes warming in a specific region, not necessarily everywhere equally.","zh":"這個片語描述特定地區變暖，而不一定各地同等升溫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"deforestation","meaning":"砍伐森林","examples":[{"en":"Deforestation can reduce rainfall and increase desertification.","zh":"砍伐森林可以減少降雨並增加荒漠化。"},{"en":"Deforestation is the cutting down or removal of forests.","zh":"Deforestation 是砍倒或移除森林。"},{"en":"A hillside may suffer after deforestation because tree roots no longer hold the soil.","zh":"砍伐森林後，山坡可能受損，因為樹根不再固定土壤。"},{"en":"If forests disappear, local rainfall and soil protection may weaken.","zh":"如果森林消失，本地降雨和土壤保護可能減弱。"},{"en":"This word describes forest loss caused by human activity or land use.","zh":"這個詞描述由人類活動或土地使用造成的森林流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reduce rainfall","meaning":"減少降雨","examples":[{"en":"Deforestation can reduce rainfall in certain areas.","zh":"砍伐森林可以減少某些地區的降雨。"},{"en":"To reduce rainfall means to make the amount of rain lower.","zh":"To reduce rainfall 指令雨量降低。"},{"en":"A long-term change in wind patterns may reduce rainfall over farming land.","zh":"風向模式的長期改變可能減少農地上的降雨。"},{"en":"If rainfall is reduced, reservoirs may refill more slowly.","zh":"如果降雨減少，水塘補水可能更慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decrease in rain supply.","zh":"這個片語描述雨水供應減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"increase the threat of","meaning":"增加……的威脅","examples":[{"en":"Deforestation can increase the threat of desertification.","zh":"砍伐森林可以增加荒漠化的威脅。"},{"en":"To increase the threat of something means to make that danger more likely or more serious.","zh":"To increase the threat of something 指令某危險更可能發生或更嚴重。"},{"en":"Poor hygiene can increase the threat of illness in a crowded classroom.","zh":"衛生欠佳可以增加擁擠課室中的疾病威脅。"},{"en":"If trees are removed, land may be more exposed to heat, wind, and erosion.","zh":"如果樹木被移除，土地可能更暴露於高溫、風和侵蝕。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a danger becoming stronger.","zh":"這個片語描述危險變得更強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"despite sophisticated technology","meaning":"儘管有先進技術","examples":[{"en":"Despite sophisticated technology, prediction remains difficult.","zh":"儘管有先進技術，預測仍然困難。"},{"en":"Despite sophisticated technology means even though advanced tools and methods exist.","zh":"Despite sophisticated technology 指即使存在先進工具和方法。"},{"en":"Despite sophisticated apps, students still need discipline to study regularly.","zh":"儘管有先進應用程式，學生仍需要自律才能定期學習。"},{"en":"If a natural system is complex, even advanced technology may not predict it perfectly.","zh":"如果自然系統複雜，即使先進科技也未必能完美預測。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts modern tools with continuing difficulty.","zh":"這個片語把現代工具與持續困難作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"identify with an acceptable degree of reliability","meaning":"以可接受的可靠程度識別","examples":[{"en":"Scientists cannot yet identify future desertification areas with an acceptable degree of reliability.","zh":"科學家尚未能以可接受的可靠程度識別未來荒漠化地區。"},{"en":"To identify something with an acceptable degree of reliability means to find it accurately enough to be trusted.","zh":"To identify something with an acceptable degree of reliability 指準確到足以被信任地找出某事物。"},{"en":"A school should not label students as at risk unless it can identify the problem reliably.","zh":"除非學校能可靠地識別問題，否則不應把學生標籤為有風險。"},{"en":"If data are weak, predictions may not be reliable enough for policy decisions.","zh":"如果數據薄弱，預測可能不夠可靠，無法支援政策決定。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that identification must be trustworthy, not just possible.","zh":"這個片語強調識別必須可信，而不只是可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"acceptable degree of reliability","meaning":"可接受的可靠程度","examples":[{"en":"Predictions must reach an acceptable degree of reliability.","zh":"預測必須達到可接受的可靠程度。"},{"en":"An acceptable degree of reliability is a level of trustworthiness high enough to be useful.","zh":"Acceptable degree of reliability 是高到足以有用的可信程度。"},{"en":"A teacher needs an acceptable degree of reliability before using test results to change a course.","zh":"老師在用測驗結果改變課程前，需要可接受的可靠程度。"},{"en":"If reliability is too low, decisions based on the prediction may be risky.","zh":"如果可靠程度太低，根據預測作出的決定可能有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a standard of confidence in information.","zh":"這個片語描述對資訊信心的標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"those parts of the Earth","meaning":"地球上那些地區","examples":[{"en":"Scientists cannot reliably identify those parts of the Earth where desertification will occur.","zh":"科學家不能可靠地識別地球上那些會發生荒漠化的地區。"},{"en":"Those parts of the Earth means particular regions or areas on the planet.","zh":"Those parts of the Earth 指地球上的特定地區或區域。"},{"en":"Some parts of the Earth are wet and forested, while others are dry and fragile.","zh":"地球上有些地區潮濕多林，有些則乾燥脆弱。"},{"en":"If scientists can identify risky areas, governments can prepare earlier.","zh":"如果科學家能識別高風險地區，政府可以更早準備。"},{"en":"This phrase points to specific places rather than the whole world equally.","zh":"這個片語指特定地方，而不是整個世界同等受影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"existing drylands","meaning":"現有乾旱地","examples":[{"en":"Existing drylands cover over 40 per cent of the world’s land area.","zh":"現有乾旱地覆蓋世界陸地面積超過百分之四十。"},{"en":"Existing drylands are dry regions that already exist now.","zh":"Existing drylands 是現在已經存在的乾燥地區。"},{"en":"A map of existing drylands can help students see where water is naturally limited.","zh":"現有乾旱地地圖可以幫助學生看見水分自然有限的地方。"},{"en":"If existing drylands become hotter, they may face higher risk of degradation.","zh":"如果現有乾旱地變得更熱，它們可能面對更高退化風險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to current dry areas, not future ones only.","zh":"這個片語指目前乾燥地區，而不只是未來地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cover over 40 per cent of","meaning":"覆蓋超過百分之四十的……","examples":[{"en":"Drylands cover over 40 per cent of the world’s total land area.","zh":"乾旱地覆蓋世界總土地面積超過百分之四十。"},{"en":"To cover over 40 per cent of something means to occupy more than two-fifths of it.","zh":"To cover over 40 per cent of something 指佔據某物超過五分之二。"},{"en":"If parks cover over 40 per cent of a district, residents have many green spaces.","zh":"如果公園覆蓋一個地區超過百分之四十，居民就有許多綠化空間。"},{"en":"When drylands cover such a large area, desertification becomes a global concern.","zh":"當乾旱地覆蓋如此大面積，荒漠化就成為全球關注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the size or spread of something by percentage.","zh":"這個片語用百分比描述某事物的大小或分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"total land area","meaning":"總土地面積","examples":[{"en":"Drylands cover a large share of the world’s total land area.","zh":"乾旱地覆蓋世界總土地面積很大部分。"},{"en":"Total land area is the full amount of land in a place, excluding water.","zh":"Total land area 是某地方全部土地面積，不包括水域。"},{"en":"City planners may measure total land area before deciding where to build parks.","zh":"城市規劃者可能先量度總土地面積，再決定在哪裏建公園。"},{"en":"If dry regions form a large share of total land area, land management becomes very important.","zh":"如果乾燥地區佔總土地面積很大部分，土地管理就變得非常重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the complete physical area of land.","zh":"這個片語描述完整的實體土地面積。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"most significantly","meaning":"最顯著地","examples":[{"en":"Drylands are found most significantly in Africa and Asia.","zh":"乾旱地最顯著地分布於非洲和亞洲。"},{"en":"Most significantly means most importantly or most noticeably.","zh":"Most significantly 指最重要地或最明顯地。"},{"en":"A school’s results improved most significantly in writing after extra practice.","zh":"額外練習後，學校成績在寫作方面改善最顯著。"},{"en":"If a problem appears most significantly in one region, resources may need to focus there.","zh":"如果問題在某一地區最顯著地出現，資源可能需要集中在那裏。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the most important place, change, or result.","zh":"這個片語突出最重要的地方、改變或結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at risk from climate change","meaning":"面臨氣候變化風險","examples":[{"en":"Existing drylands are most at risk from climate change.","zh":"現有乾旱地最面臨氣候變化風險。"},{"en":"To be at risk from climate change means to be likely to suffer harm because the climate is changing.","zh":"To be at risk from climate change 指可能因氣候變化而受害。"},{"en":"A coastal school may be at risk from climate change if storms and floods become stronger.","zh":"如果風暴和水浸變得更強，沿海學校可能面臨氣候變化風險。"},{"en":"If a place already lacks water, climate change can make its situation worse.","zh":"如果某地本來已缺水，氣候變化可以令情況更差。"},{"en":"This phrase describes vulnerability to climate-related harm.","zh":"這個片語描述容易受到氣候相關傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"experience low rainfall","meaning":"經歷低降雨量","examples":[{"en":"These areas already experience low rainfall.","zh":"這些地區已經經歷低降雨量。"},{"en":"To experience low rainfall means to receive little rain over time.","zh":"To experience low rainfall 指長期收到很少雨水。"},{"en":"A village that experiences low rainfall may depend on wells and stored water.","zh":"經歷低降雨量的村莊可能依賴水井和儲水。"},{"en":"If low rainfall continues, crops may need irrigation or may fail.","zh":"如果低降雨量持續，作物可能需要灌溉，否則可能歉收。"},{"en":"This phrase describes places where rain is naturally limited.","zh":"這個片語描述雨水自然有限的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the form of","meaning":"以……形式","examples":[{"en":"Rainfall often comes in the form of short, intense storms.","zh":"降雨通常以短暫而強烈的暴雨形式出現。"},{"en":"In the form of means appearing as a particular type or shape of something.","zh":"In the form of 指以某種特定類型或形式出現。"},{"en":"Homework may come in the form of a short quiz rather than a long essay.","zh":"功課可以以小測形式出現，而不是長作文。"},{"en":"If rain comes only as sudden storms, much water may run away instead of soaking into soil.","zh":"如果降雨只以突發暴雨形式出現，許多水可能流走，而不是滲入土壤。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the particular way something appears.","zh":"這個片語解釋某事出現的特定方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"high-intensity storms","meaning":"高強度暴雨","examples":[{"en":"Dryland rainfall often occurs as short, erratic, high-intensity storms.","zh":"乾旱地降雨通常以短暫、不穩定、高強度暴雨形式出現。"},{"en":"High-intensity storms are storms with very heavy rain, strong wind, or severe conditions.","zh":"High-intensity storms 是帶有極大雨量、強風或嚴重情況的風暴。"},{"en":"A high-intensity storm can flood streets within minutes.","zh":"高強度暴雨可以在幾分鐘內淹浸街道。"},{"en":"If rain falls too intensely, soil may wash away before plants can benefit from the water.","zh":"如果雨下得太猛烈，土壤可能在植物受益前被沖走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes storms that are short but powerful.","zh":"這個片語描述短暫但強力的風暴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"suffer from land degradation","meaning":"受土地退化之苦","examples":[{"en":"Many drylands suffer from land degradation.","zh":"許多乾旱地受土地退化之苦。"},{"en":"To suffer from land degradation means to be damaged by declining soil and vegetation quality.","zh":"To suffer from land degradation 指因土壤和植被質素下降而受損。"},{"en":"A farm may suffer from land degradation after years of overgrazing.","zh":"多年過度放牧後，農場可能受土地退化之苦。"},{"en":"If land suffers degradation, it may produce less food and support fewer animals.","zh":"如果土地退化，它可能生產較少食物並支持較少動物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harm to the usefulness of land.","zh":"這個片語描述土地用途受損。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"due to","meaning":"由於","examples":[{"en":"Land degradation can occur due to over-cultivation and poor irrigation.","zh":"土地退化可能由於過度耕作和欠佳灌溉而發生。"},{"en":"Due to means because of.","zh":"Due to 指因為。"},{"en":"The lesson was cancelled due to heavy rain.","zh":"課堂由於大雨而取消。"},{"en":"If soil becomes salty due to poor irrigation, crops may grow badly.","zh":"如果土壤由於欠佳灌溉而變鹹，作物可能生長不良。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the reason for a result.","zh":"這個片語引出結果的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"over-cultivation","meaning":"過度耕作","examples":[{"en":"Over-cultivation can damage soil in dryland areas.","zh":"過度耕作可以破壞乾旱地區的土壤。"},{"en":"Over-cultivation means farming land too much without allowing soil to recover.","zh":"Over-cultivation 指過度耕種土地而不讓土壤恢復。"},{"en":"A farmer may cause over-cultivation by planting crops on the same field every season.","zh":"農民如果每季都在同一片田種植，可能造成過度耕作。"},{"en":"If soil is overused, it may lose nutrients and hold less water.","zh":"如果土壤被過度使用，它可能失去養分並儲水能力下降。"},{"en":"This word describes excessive farming that weakens land.","zh":"這個詞描述削弱土地的過量耕作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"overgrazing","meaning":"過度放牧","examples":[{"en":"Overgrazing contributes to land degradation.","zh":"過度放牧促成土地退化。"},{"en":"Overgrazing happens when too many animals feed on the same land for too long.","zh":"Overgrazing 是太多動物長時間在同一片土地上吃草。"},{"en":"A hillside may become bare if goats graze there every day without rest.","zh":"如果山羊每天在同一山坡放牧而土地沒有休息，山坡可能變得光禿。"},{"en":"If plants are eaten faster than they regrow, soil becomes exposed.","zh":"如果植物被吃掉的速度快過重新生長，土壤就會暴露。"},{"en":"This word describes excessive animal grazing that damages vegetation and soil.","zh":"這個詞描述破壞植被和土壤的過量放牧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"poor irrigation practices","meaning":"欠佳灌溉做法","examples":[{"en":"Poor irrigation practices can worsen land degradation.","zh":"欠佳灌溉做法可以惡化土地退化。"},{"en":"Poor irrigation practices are bad ways of watering farmland that waste water or damage soil.","zh":"Poor irrigation practices 是浪費水或破壞土壤的欠佳農田澆水方法。"},{"en":"A farm may use poor irrigation if water is poured unevenly and some fields become waterlogged.","zh":"如果水分分配不平均，部分田地積水，農場可能正在使用欠佳灌溉。"},{"en":"If irrigation leaves too much salt in the soil, crops may grow poorly.","zh":"如果灌溉令土壤留下太多鹽分，作物可能生長不良。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harmful water-management methods in farming.","zh":"這個片語描述農業中有害的水管理方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"it is a misconception that","meaning":"認為……是一種誤解","examples":[{"en":"It is a misconception that droughts directly cause desertification.","zh":"認為乾旱直接造成荒漠化是一種誤解。"},{"en":"It is a misconception that means many people believe something, but it is wrong or too simple.","zh":"It is a misconception that 指許多人相信某事，但那是錯誤或過於簡單。"},{"en":"It is a misconception that good students never make mistakes.","zh":"認為好學生從不犯錯是一種誤解。"},{"en":"If people misunderstand the cause of a problem, they may choose the wrong solution.","zh":"如果人們誤解問題成因，他們可能選擇錯誤解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects a common but false belief.","zh":"這個片語糾正常見但錯誤的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"droughts","meaning":"乾旱；旱災","examples":[{"en":"Droughts are common in arid and semi-arid lands.","zh":"乾旱在乾旱和半乾旱土地中很常見。"},{"en":"Droughts are long periods with little or no rainfall.","zh":"Droughts 是長時間降雨很少或沒有降雨的時期。"},{"en":"During droughts, families may be asked to save water at home.","zh":"旱災期間，家庭可能被要求在家節約用水。"},{"en":"If droughts last too long, crops, animals, and water supplies may suffer.","zh":"如果乾旱持續太久，農作物、動物和供水都可能受苦。"},{"en":"This word describes serious dry periods, not just a sunny week.","zh":"這個詞描述嚴重乾燥時期，而不只是晴朗一星期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"well-managed lands","meaning":"管理良好的土地","examples":[{"en":"Well-managed lands can recover from drought.","zh":"管理良好的土地可以從乾旱中恢復。"},{"en":"Well-managed lands are lands cared for with good farming, grazing, and water practices.","zh":"Well-managed lands 是以良好耕作、放牧和用水做法照顧的土地。"},{"en":"A well-managed school garden uses compost, careful watering, and rest periods for soil.","zh":"管理良好的學校花園會使用堆肥、仔細澆水，並讓土壤休息。"},{"en":"If land is managed well, it can survive dry periods more easily.","zh":"如果土地管理良好，它可以較容易渡過乾燥時期。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts healthy management with land abuse.","zh":"這個片語把健康管理與土地濫用作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"recover from drought","meaning":"從乾旱中恢復","examples":[{"en":"Well-managed lands can recover from drought when the rains return.","zh":"當雨水重臨時，管理良好的土地可以從乾旱中恢復。"},{"en":"To recover from drought means to regain health or productivity after a dry period.","zh":"To recover from drought 指在乾旱時期後恢復健康或生產力。"},{"en":"A garden may recover from drought if it is watered slowly and damaged plants are removed.","zh":"如果慢慢澆水並移除受損植物，花園可能從乾旱中恢復。"},{"en":"If soil and roots remain healthy, land can recover once rain comes back.","zh":"如果土壤和根部仍健康，雨水回來後土地可以恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improvement after water shortage.","zh":"這個片語描述缺水後的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"when the rains return","meaning":"當雨水重臨時","examples":[{"en":"Land can recover when the rains return.","zh":"當雨水重臨時，土地可以恢復。"},{"en":"When the rains return means when rainfall starts again after a dry period.","zh":"When the rains return 指乾旱時期後降雨重新開始。"},{"en":"Farmers may plant seeds when the rains return after months of drought.","zh":"幾個月乾旱後，當雨水重臨時，農民可能播種。"},{"en":"If rain returns in time, damaged plants may grow again.","zh":"如果雨水及時回來，受損植物可能重新生長。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the return of water after dryness.","zh":"這個片語標示乾燥後水分回歸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"continued land abuse","meaning":"持續濫用土地","examples":[{"en":"Continued land abuse during drought increases land degradation.","zh":"乾旱期間持續濫用土地會加劇土地退化。"},{"en":"Continued land abuse means ongoing harmful use of land, such as overgrazing or over-cultivation.","zh":"Continued land abuse 指持續有害地使用土地，例如過度放牧或過度耕作。"},{"en":"A farm shows land abuse if animals keep grazing when grass has already disappeared.","zh":"如果草已消失而動物仍繼續放牧，農場就是在濫用土地。"},{"en":"If harmful practices continue during drought, the land has less chance to recover.","zh":"如果有害做法在乾旱期間持續，土地恢復機會會較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated damage caused by poor land use.","zh":"這個片語描述由欠佳土地使用造成的重複損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"increase land degradation","meaning":"加劇土地退化","examples":[{"en":"Poor land use can increase land degradation.","zh":"欠佳土地使用可以加劇土地退化。"},{"en":"To increase land degradation means to make land quality decline faster or more seriously.","zh":"To increase land degradation 指令土地質素更快或更嚴重下降。"},{"en":"Dumping waste on farmland can increase land degradation by poisoning soil.","zh":"在農地傾倒廢物可以透過毒害土壤加劇土地退化。"},{"en":"If farmers remove too many plants, erosion may increase land degradation.","zh":"如果農民移除太多植物，侵蝕可能加劇土地退化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes actions that make damaged land worse.","zh":"這個片語描述令受損土地更差的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"occur in linear patterns","meaning":"以線性模式發生","examples":[{"en":"Desertification does not occur in linear patterns.","zh":"荒漠化並不以線性模式發生。"},{"en":"To occur in linear patterns means to happen in a straight, regular, and predictable way.","zh":"To occur in linear patterns 指以直線、規律且可預測的方式發生。"},{"en":"Student progress rarely occurs in a linear pattern; some weeks improve faster than others.","zh":"學生進步很少以線性模式發生；有些星期進步較快。"},{"en":"If desertification is not linear, damaged patches may appear in unexpected places.","zh":"如果荒漠化不是線性的，受損斑塊可能出現在意想不到的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts regular progress with irregular development.","zh":"這個片語把規律進展與不規則發展作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"easily definable patterns","meaning":"容易界定的模式","examples":[{"en":"Desertification does not follow easily definable patterns.","zh":"荒漠化不遵循容易界定的模式。"},{"en":"Easily definable patterns are patterns that are simple to see, describe, or predict.","zh":"Easily definable patterns 是容易看見、描述或預測的模式。"},{"en":"A teacher likes easily definable patterns in mistakes because they show what students need to practise.","zh":"老師喜歡錯誤中有容易界定的模式，因為它們顯示學生需要練習甚麼。"},{"en":"If a problem lacks clear patterns, it becomes harder to monitor and solve.","zh":"如果問題缺乏清晰模式，就更難監察和解決。"},{"en":"This phrase describes patterns that can be clearly identified.","zh":"這個片語描述可以清楚識別的模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"advance erratically","meaning":"不規則地推進","examples":[{"en":"Deserts advance erratically along their borders.","zh":"沙漠沿着邊緣不規則地推進。"},{"en":"To advance erratically means to move forward irregularly and unpredictably.","zh":"To advance erratically 指以不規則且難以預測的方式向前移動。"},{"en":"A queue may advance erratically if one counter keeps opening and closing.","zh":"如果一個櫃枱不斷開關，隊伍可能不規則地前進。"},{"en":"If deserts advance erratically, some areas may degrade quickly while nearby areas remain stable.","zh":"如果沙漠不規則地推進，有些地區可能迅速退化，而附近地區仍穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uneven and unpredictable movement.","zh":"這個片語描述不平均且難以預測的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"form patches","meaning":"形成斑塊","examples":[{"en":"Desertification can form patches on desert borders.","zh":"荒漠化可以在沙漠邊緣形成斑塊。"},{"en":"To form patches means to appear as separate small areas rather than one continuous area.","zh":"To form patches 指以分散小區域出現，而不是一整片連續區域。"},{"en":"Rain may form patches of mud on a school playground.","zh":"雨水可能在學校操場形成一片片泥濘。"},{"en":"If land degradation forms patches, damage may be scattered and harder to notice.","zh":"如果土地退化形成斑塊，損害可能分散且較難察覺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes small separated areas appearing.","zh":"這個片語描述分散小區域出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"on their borders","meaning":"在其邊緣","examples":[{"en":"Deserts can form patches on their borders.","zh":"沙漠可以在其邊緣形成斑塊。"},{"en":"On their borders means along the edges of those areas.","zh":"On their borders 指沿着那些區域的邊緣。"},{"en":"Small shops often appear on the borders of busy shopping districts.","zh":"小店常出現在繁忙購物區的邊緣。"},{"en":"If desert damage begins on its borders, nearby villages may be the first affected.","zh":"如果沙漠損害從其邊緣開始，附近村莊可能最先受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies activity at the edge, not the centre.","zh":"這個片語指出活動在邊緣，而不是中心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"far from natural deserts","meaning":"遠離天然沙漠","examples":[{"en":"Areas far from natural deserts can still degrade quickly.","zh":"遠離天然沙漠的地區仍可以迅速退化。"},{"en":"Far from natural deserts means not close to existing desert regions.","zh":"Far from natural deserts 指不接近現有沙漠地區。"},{"en":"A farm far from a natural desert may still become dry if water is mismanaged.","zh":"遠離天然沙漠的農場，如果用水管理不善，仍可能變乾。"},{"en":"If poor land management continues, distance from a desert does not guarantee safety.","zh":"如果欠佳土地管理持續，遠離沙漠並不能保證安全。"},{"en":"This phrase challenges the idea that only desert borders are at risk.","zh":"這個片語挑戰只有沙漠邊緣有風險的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"degrade quickly to","meaning":"迅速退化成","examples":[{"en":"Poorly managed land can degrade quickly to barren soil.","zh":"管理欠佳的土地可以迅速退化成貧瘠土壤。"},{"en":"To degrade quickly to something means to become damaged and change into a worse state rapidly.","zh":"To degrade quickly to something 指快速受損並變成較差狀態。"},{"en":"A playground can degrade quickly to a muddy field if drainage is poor.","zh":"如果排水差，操場可以迅速退化成泥地。"},{"en":"If plants are removed and soil dries out, useful farmland can become barren quickly.","zh":"如果植物被移除而土壤乾枯，有用農地可以迅速變得貧瘠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rapid decline into a damaged condition.","zh":"這個片語描述快速下降至受損狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"barren soil","meaning":"貧瘠土壤","examples":[{"en":"Poor land management can turn land into barren soil.","zh":"欠佳土地管理可以把土地變成貧瘠土壤。"},{"en":"Barren soil is soil that is too poor, dry, or damaged to support healthy plant growth.","zh":"Barren soil 是太貧乏、太乾或受損，以致不能支持植物健康生長的土壤。"},{"en":"A garden with barren soil may need compost before flowers can grow.","zh":"有貧瘠土壤的花園可能需要堆肥才能種花。"},{"en":"If topsoil is lost, fertile land may become barren soil.","zh":"如果表土流失，肥沃土地可能變成貧瘠土壤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes soil that has lost its productive power.","zh":"這個片語描述失去生產力的土壤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"poor land management","meaning":"欠佳土地管理","examples":[{"en":"Poor land management can cause rapid land degradation.","zh":"欠佳土地管理可以造成快速土地退化。"},{"en":"Poor land management means using land carelessly or unsustainably.","zh":"Poor land management 指粗心或不可持續地使用土地。"},{"en":"Letting too many animals graze on a small field is poor land management.","zh":"讓太多動物在小田地上放牧，是欠佳土地管理。"},{"en":"If land is managed badly, soil, water, and vegetation may all decline.","zh":"如果土地管理差，土壤、水分和植被都可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harmful decisions about how land is used.","zh":"這個片語描述關於土地使用的有害決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the presence of","meaning":"……的存在","examples":[{"en":"The presence of a nearby desert does not directly cause desertification.","zh":"附近沙漠的存在並不直接造成荒漠化。"},{"en":"The presence of something means that it exists or is there.","zh":"The presence of something 指某物存在或在場。"},{"en":"The presence of a teacher in the room can make students behave more carefully.","zh":"老師在房間裏的存在可以令學生行為更謹慎。"},{"en":"If a desert is nearby, that fact alone does not prove it caused land degradation.","zh":"如果附近有沙漠，單是這個事實並不能證明它造成土地退化。"},{"en":"This phrase points to existence, not necessarily cause.","zh":"這個片語指出存在，而不一定是原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"nearby desert","meaning":"附近的沙漠","examples":[{"en":"A nearby desert has no direct relationship to desertification.","zh":"附近的沙漠與荒漠化沒有直接關係。"},{"en":"A nearby desert is a desert located close to a particular area.","zh":"Nearby desert 是位於某特定地區附近的沙漠。"},{"en":"A village near a desert may still remain healthy if water and land are managed well.","zh":"接近沙漠的村莊，如果水和土地管理良好，仍可能保持健康。"},{"en":"If land far from deserts can degrade, a nearby desert is not the only risk factor.","zh":"如果遠離沙漠的土地也會退化，附近的沙漠就不是唯一風險因素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location, not automatic danger.","zh":"這個片語描述位置，而不是自動危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"no direct relationship to","meaning":"與……沒有直接關係","examples":[{"en":"A nearby desert has no direct relationship to desertification.","zh":"附近沙漠與荒漠化沒有直接關係。"},{"en":"No direct relationship to something means there is no clear immediate connection with it.","zh":"No direct relationship to something 指與某事沒有清楚的直接聯繫。"},{"en":"A student’s neat handwriting may have no direct relationship to their understanding of history.","zh":"學生字體整齊可能與他對歷史的理解沒有直接關係。"},{"en":"If two things appear together, that does not always mean one directly causes the other.","zh":"如果兩件事同時出現，並不總代表其中一件直接造成另一件。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for separating correlation from cause.","zh":"這個片語有助區分相關和因果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"undergo desertification","meaning":"經歷荒漠化","examples":[{"en":"An area undergoing desertification may not be noticed immediately.","zh":"一個正在經歷荒漠化的地區可能不會立即被注意到。"},{"en":"To undergo desertification means to experience the process of becoming dry, degraded, and desert-like.","zh":"To undergo desertification 指經歷變得乾燥、退化和類似沙漠的過程。"},{"en":"A farming area may undergo desertification after years of drought and poor land use.","zh":"農業地區在多年乾旱和欠佳土地使用後，可能經歷荒漠化。"},{"en":"If an area undergoes desertification slowly, people may notice only after crops begin failing.","zh":"如果一個地區慢慢經歷荒漠化，人們可能到作物開始歉收才注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place going through environmental decline.","zh":"這個片語描述地方正在經歷環境衰退。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be brought to public attention","meaning":"引起公眾關注","examples":[{"en":"Desertification is often brought to public attention too late.","zh":"荒漠化往往太遲才引起公眾關注。"},{"en":"To be brought to public attention means to become known or noticed by ordinary people.","zh":"To be brought to public attention 指被普通人知道或注意到。"},{"en":"A school safety problem may be brought to public attention after parents complain online.","zh":"學校安全問題可能在家長網上投訴後引起公眾關注。"},{"en":"If environmental damage is noticed too late, recovery may be much harder.","zh":"如果環境損害太遲被注意到，恢復可能困難得多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an issue becoming publicly visible.","zh":"這個片語描述問題變得被公眾看見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"well underway","meaning":"已經進行了一段時間","examples":[{"en":"The process may be well underway before people notice it.","zh":"在人們注意到之前，這個過程可能已經進行了一段時間。"},{"en":"Well underway means already started and developed to a significant degree.","zh":"Well underway 指已經開始並發展到明顯程度。"},{"en":"By the time parents arrive, the school concert may already be well underway.","zh":"到家長到達時，學校音樂會可能已經進行了一段時間。"},{"en":"If land degradation is well underway, early warning signs have already been missed.","zh":"如果土地退化已進行一段時間，早期警號已經被錯過。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a process is not just beginning.","zh":"這個片語顯示過程不是剛開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"little or no data","meaning":"幾乎沒有數據","examples":[{"en":"Little or no data may be available for some affected areas.","zh":"一些受影響地區可能幾乎沒有可用數據。"},{"en":"Little or no data means there is very little information or none at all.","zh":"Little or no data 指資料非常少或完全沒有。"},{"en":"A teacher cannot judge progress fairly if there is little or no data about homework and tests.","zh":"如果幾乎沒有關於功課和測驗的數據，老師不能公平判斷進步。"},{"en":"If scientists lack data, they may not know how fast land has changed.","zh":"如果科學家缺乏數據，他們可能不知道土地變化有多快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious shortage of evidence.","zh":"這個片語描述證據嚴重不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be available to indicate","meaning":"可用以顯示","examples":[{"en":"Data may not be available to indicate the previous state of the ecosystem.","zh":"數據可能不可用以顯示生態系統之前的狀態。"},{"en":"To be available to indicate something means to exist and be usable for showing it.","zh":"To be available to indicate something 指資料存在且可用來顯示某事。"},{"en":"Attendance records may be available to indicate whether students are arriving later than before.","zh":"出席紀錄可能可用以顯示學生是否比以前更遲到。"},{"en":"If old environmental data are missing, scientists cannot compare past and present conditions.","zh":"如果舊環境數據缺失，科學家不能比較過去和現在情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence that can show a condition or change.","zh":"這個片語描述可顯示狀況或變化的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"previous state of","meaning":"……之前的狀態","examples":[{"en":"Scientists may not know the previous state of the ecosystem.","zh":"科學家可能不知道生態系統之前的狀態。"},{"en":"The previous state of something is its condition before a change happened.","zh":"The previous state of something 是某事改變前的狀況。"},{"en":"A mechanic may ask about the previous state of a car before it broke down.","zh":"修車技工可能詢問汽車故障前的狀態。"},{"en":"If we do not know the previous state of land, it is hard to measure degradation.","zh":"如果我們不知道土地之前的狀態，就難以量度退化。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare before and after conditions.","zh":"這個片語幫助比較前後情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ecosystem","meaning":"生態系統","examples":[{"en":"The previous state of the ecosystem may be unknown.","zh":"生態系統之前的狀態可能未知。"},{"en":"An ecosystem is a community of living things and their physical environment.","zh":"Ecosystem 是生物群落及其物理環境。"},{"en":"A pond ecosystem includes fish, plants, insects, water, sunlight, and soil.","zh":"池塘生態系統包括魚、植物、昆蟲、水、陽光和土壤。"},{"en":"If one part of an ecosystem is damaged, other parts may also suffer.","zh":"如果生態系統的一部分受損，其他部分也可能受害。"},{"en":"This word describes nature as an interconnected system.","zh":"這個詞把自然描述為互相連繫的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rate of degradation","meaning":"退化速度","examples":[{"en":"Data may not show the rate of degradation.","zh":"數據可能無法顯示退化速度。"},{"en":"The rate of degradation is how quickly land or an environment is becoming worse.","zh":"Rate of degradation 是土地或環境變差的速度。"},{"en":"A teacher may track the rate of improvement by comparing test scores each month.","zh":"老師可能透過比較每月測驗分數來追蹤進步速度。"},{"en":"If degradation happens quickly, action must be taken sooner.","zh":"如果退化快速發生，就必須更早採取行動。"},{"en":"This phrase measures the speed of decline.","zh":"這個片語量度衰退速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"scientists still question whether","meaning":"科學家仍然質疑是否","examples":[{"en":"Scientists still question whether desertification is permanent.","zh":"科學家仍然質疑荒漠化是否永久。"},{"en":"Scientists still question whether means experts continue to ask and debate if something is true.","zh":"Scientists still question whether 指專家仍繼續詢問和討論某事是否真實。"},{"en":"Doctors may still question whether a new treatment works better than existing ones.","zh":"醫生可能仍質疑新療法是否比現有療法更有效。"},{"en":"If evidence is mixed, scientists may avoid giving a final answer.","zh":"如果證據不一致，科學家可能避免給出最終答案。"},{"en":"This phrase shows ongoing uncertainty in research.","zh":"這個片語顯示研究中的持續不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a process of global change","meaning":"全球變化過程","examples":[{"en":"Desertification may be viewed as a process of global change.","zh":"荒漠化可被視為全球變化過程。"},{"en":"A process of global change is a worldwide shift that develops over time.","zh":"Process of global change 是隨時間發展的全球性轉變。"},{"en":"Urbanisation can be viewed as a process of global change because cities are growing in many countries.","zh":"城市化可被視為全球變化過程，因為許多國家的城市都在增長。"},{"en":"If desertification affects many regions, it becomes part of wider environmental change.","zh":"如果荒漠化影響許多地區，它就成為更廣泛環境變化的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large-scale transformation.","zh":"這個片語描述大規模轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be halted or reversed","meaning":"被停止或逆轉","examples":[{"en":"Scientists ask how desertification can be halted or reversed.","zh":"科學家詢問荒漠化如何能被停止或逆轉。"},{"en":"To be halted or reversed means to be stopped or made to move back toward a better state.","zh":"To be halted or reversed 指被停止，或被帶回較好狀態。"},{"en":"A student’s falling marks can be halted or reversed with regular practice and feedback.","zh":"學生成績下跌可以透過定期練習和回饋被停止或逆轉。"},{"en":"If land degradation is caught early, better management may slow it or restore the land.","zh":"如果土地退化及早被發現，較好管理可能減慢它或恢復土地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stopping decline or undoing damage.","zh":"這個片語描述停止衰退或逆轉損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not be limited to","meaning":"不限於","examples":[{"en":"Desertification will not be limited to the drylands of Africa and Asia.","zh":"荒漠化將不限於非洲和亞洲的乾旱地。"},{"en":"To not be limited to something means to extend beyond that place, group, or situation.","zh":"To not be limited to something 指超出某地方、群體或情況。"},{"en":"Exam stress is not limited to weak students; high achievers can feel it too.","zh":"考試壓力不限於成績弱的學生；高成就學生也可能感受到。"},{"en":"If climate damage is not limited to one region, more countries must prepare.","zh":"如果氣候損害不限於一個地區，更多國家就必須準備。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the problem is wider than expected.","zh":"這個片語顯示問題比預期更廣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據","examples":[{"en":"According to Greenpeace, the Mediterranean will also suffer.","zh":"根據 Greenpeace，地中海地區也會受苦。"},{"en":"According to means based on what a person, organisation, or source says.","zh":"According to 指根據某人、組織或來源所說。"},{"en":"According to the school notice, the exam will start at nine o’clock.","zh":"根據學校通告，考試將於九時開始。"},{"en":"If a claim begins with according to, the reader knows where the information comes from.","zh":"如果主張以 according to 開始，讀者知道資訊來自哪裏。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a source.","zh":"這個片語引出來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"environmental organisation","meaning":"環保組織","examples":[{"en":"Greenpeace is an environmental organisation.","zh":"Greenpeace 是一個環保組織。"},{"en":"An environmental organisation is a group that works to protect nature and reduce environmental harm.","zh":"Environmental organisation 是致力保護自然和減少環境損害的團體。"},{"en":"An environmental organisation may organise beach clean-ups or climate campaigns.","zh":"環保組織可能組織清潔海灘或氣候運動。"},{"en":"If pollution increases, such organisations may pressure governments to act.","zh":"如果污染增加，這類組織可能向政府施壓要求行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a group focused on environmental protection.","zh":"這個片語描述專注環境保護的團體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"suffer substantially","meaning":"受到重大影響","examples":[{"en":"The Mediterranean may suffer substantially from climate change.","zh":"地中海地區可能受到氣候變化重大影響。"},{"en":"To suffer substantially means to experience serious or large harm.","zh":"To suffer substantially 指經歷嚴重或大幅傷害。"},{"en":"A small shop may suffer substantially if a road closure stops customers from visiting.","zh":"如果封路令顧客不能到訪，小店可能受到重大影響。"},{"en":"If droughts become frequent, farms and towns may suffer greatly.","zh":"如果乾旱變得頻繁，農場和城鎮可能嚴重受苦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damage that is important, not minor.","zh":"這個片語描述重要而非輕微的損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"current trends in","meaning":"……的現時趨勢","examples":[{"en":"Current trends in greenhouse gas emissions may continue.","zh":"溫室氣體排放的現時趨勢可能持續。"},{"en":"Current trends in something are the present patterns or directions of change.","zh":"Current trends in something 是某事目前的模式或變化方向。"},{"en":"Current trends in student reading show that many prefer short online texts.","zh":"學生閱讀的現時趨勢顯示，許多人較喜歡短篇網上文本。"},{"en":"If current trends continue, future conditions may become more serious.","zh":"如果現時趨勢持續，未來情況可能變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what is happening now and where it seems to be heading.","zh":"這個片語描述現在正在發生甚麼，以及它似乎朝哪個方向發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"emissions of greenhouse gases","meaning":"溫室氣體排放","examples":[{"en":"Emissions of greenhouse gases are driving climate change.","zh":"溫室氣體排放正在推動氣候變化。"},{"en":"Emissions of greenhouse gases are releases of heat-trapping gases into the atmosphere.","zh":"Emissions of greenhouse gases 是把困住熱量的氣體釋放到大氣中。"},{"en":"Cars, factories, and power stations can produce emissions of greenhouse gases.","zh":"汽車、工廠和發電站可以產生溫室氣體排放。"},{"en":"If emissions keep increasing, warming is likely to continue.","zh":"如果排放持續增加，變暖很可能繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the release of gases that contribute to global warming.","zh":"這個片語描述促成全球變暖的氣體釋放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"global temperatures","meaning":"全球氣溫","examples":[{"en":"Global temperatures are expected to rise rapidly.","zh":"全球氣溫預計會快速上升。"},{"en":"Global temperatures are average temperatures measured across the world.","zh":"Global temperatures 是在全球範圍量度的平均氣溫。"},{"en":"Scientists compare global temperatures over many years to identify warming trends.","zh":"科學家比較多年全球氣溫，以識別變暖趨勢。"},{"en":"If global temperatures rise, heatwaves and drought risks may increase.","zh":"如果全球氣溫上升，熱浪和乾旱風險可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes temperature patterns at the worldwide level.","zh":"這個片語描述全球層面的氣溫模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rise faster over","meaning":"在……期間上升得更快","examples":[{"en":"Temperatures are expected to rise faster over the next century.","zh":"氣溫預計會在下一個世紀期間上升得更快。"},{"en":"To rise faster over a period means to increase more quickly during that time.","zh":"To rise faster over a period 指在某段時間內更快速增加。"},{"en":"Rent may rise faster over the summer if many families are looking for flats.","zh":"如果許多家庭正在找單位，租金可能在夏季期間上升得更快。"},{"en":"If temperatures rise faster, communities have less time to adapt.","zh":"如果氣溫上升得更快，社區就有較少時間適應。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the speed of increase across a future period.","zh":"這個片語比較未來某段時間內上升速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"over the next century","meaning":"在下一個世紀","examples":[{"en":"Climate change may accelerate over the next century.","zh":"氣候變化可能在下一個世紀加快。"},{"en":"Over the next century means during the coming one hundred years.","zh":"Over the next century 指在未來一百年間。"},{"en":"Cities may change greatly over the next century because of technology and climate risks.","zh":"城市可能因科技和氣候風險在下一個世紀大幅改變。"},{"en":"If planning covers the next century, governments must think beyond short-term elections.","zh":"如果規劃涵蓋下一個世紀，政府必須思考短期選舉以外的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very long future period.","zh":"這個片語描述非常長的未來時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"during the last 10,000 years","meaning":"在過去一萬年間","examples":[{"en":"The projected warming may be faster than at any time during the last 10,000 years.","zh":"預測中的變暖速度可能快過過去一萬年間任何時候。"},{"en":"During the last 10,000 years means within the most recent ten thousand years.","zh":"During the last 10,000 years 指在最近一萬年內。"},{"en":"Scientists study climate during the last 10,000 years to understand human civilisation’s environment.","zh":"科學家研究過去一萬年間的氣候，以理解人類文明的環境。"},{"en":"If warming is faster than anything in that period, the change is historically unusual.","zh":"如果變暖速度快過該時期任何情況，這種變化在歷史上就不尋常。"},{"en":"This phrase places climate change in a long historical timescale.","zh":"這個片語把氣候變化放入長期歷史時間尺度中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"significant uncertainties surround","meaning":"……存在重大不確定性","examples":[{"en":"Significant uncertainties surround predictions of regional climate change.","zh":"對區域氣候變化的預測存在重大不確定性。"},{"en":"Significant uncertainties surround something means there are many important unknowns about it.","zh":"Significant uncertainties surround something 指某事存在許多重要未知因素。"},{"en":"Significant uncertainties surround a new policy if no one knows how people will respond.","zh":"如果沒有人知道人們會如何反應，新政策就存在重大不確定性。"},{"en":"If uncertainties remain, predictions should be used carefully.","zh":"如果不確定性仍存在，預測應謹慎使用。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a topic cannot be predicted with complete confidence.","zh":"這個片語警告某題目不能以完全信心預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"predictions of","meaning":"對……的預測","examples":[{"en":"Predictions of regional climate changes remain uncertain.","zh":"對區域氣候變化的預測仍不確定。"},{"en":"Predictions of something are statements about what may happen in the future.","zh":"Predictions of something 是關於未來可能發生甚麼的說法。"},{"en":"Teachers may make predictions of exam performance based on mock results.","zh":"老師可能根據模擬試結果，作出對考試表現的預測。"},{"en":"If predictions are uncertain, people should prepare for several possible outcomes.","zh":"如果預測不確定，人們應為幾種可能結果作準備。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces future expectations about a topic.","zh":"這個片語引出關於某題目的未來預期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"regional climate changes","meaning":"區域氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"Regional climate changes are difficult to predict precisely.","zh":"區域氣候變化難以精確預測。"},{"en":"Regional climate changes are climate shifts affecting particular areas rather than the whole world equally.","zh":"Regional climate changes 是影響特定地區，而不是全世界同等受影響的氣候轉變。"},{"en":"A coastal region and an inland region may experience different climate changes.","zh":"沿海地區和內陸地區可能經歷不同的氣候變化。"},{"en":"If regional changes are severe, local farming and water planning may need to change.","zh":"如果區域變化嚴重，本地農業和水資源規劃可能需要改變。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on climate change at a local or regional scale.","zh":"這個片語集中於本地或區域尺度的氣候變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the Mediterranean region","meaning":"地中海地區","examples":[{"en":"The Mediterranean region may warm significantly.","zh":"地中海地區可能顯著變暖。"},{"en":"The Mediterranean region is the area around the Mediterranean Sea.","zh":"Mediterranean region 是地中海周圍的地區。"},{"en":"Many tourists visit the Mediterranean region for beaches, old cities, and warm weather.","zh":"許多旅客到地中海地區欣賞海灘、古城和溫暖天氣。"},{"en":"If the Mediterranean becomes hotter and drier, farming and tourism may both be affected.","zh":"如果地中海變得更熱和更乾，農業和旅遊業都可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase names a region likely to face climate pressure.","zh":"這個片語命名一個可能面對氣候壓力的地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"warm significantly","meaning":"顯著變暖","examples":[{"en":"The Mediterranean region is likely to warm significantly.","zh":"地中海地區很可能顯著變暖。"},{"en":"To warm significantly means to become noticeably and importantly hotter.","zh":"To warm significantly 指明顯且重要地變得更熱。"},{"en":"A classroom can warm significantly if air-conditioning fails on a summer afternoon.","zh":"如果夏日下午冷氣故障，課室可以顯著變暖。"},{"en":"If a region warms significantly, drought and heat-health risks may increase.","zh":"如果一個地區顯著變暖，乾旱和高溫健康風險可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes warming that is large enough to matter.","zh":"這個片語描述大到足以重要的變暖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"increase the frequency and severity of","meaning":"增加……的頻率和嚴重程度","examples":[{"en":"Warming may increase the frequency and severity of droughts.","zh":"變暖可能增加乾旱的頻率和嚴重程度。"},{"en":"To increase the frequency and severity of something means to make it happen more often and become more serious.","zh":"To increase the frequency and severity of something 指令某事更常發生且變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"Poor road design can increase the frequency and severity of traffic accidents.","zh":"欠佳道路設計可以增加交通意外的頻率和嚴重程度。"},{"en":"If droughts become both more common and stronger, farming becomes much harder.","zh":"如果乾旱既更常見又更強，農業會困難得多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a problem becoming more frequent and more damaging.","zh":"這個片語描述問題變得更頻密且更具破壞性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"across the region","meaning":"整個地區","examples":[{"en":"Droughts may become more severe across the region.","zh":"乾旱可能在整個地區變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"Across the region means throughout the whole area being discussed.","zh":"Across the region 指遍及正在討論的整個區域。"},{"en":"Schools across the region may close if a strong storm approaches.","zh":"如果強風暴接近，整個地區的學校可能停課。"},{"en":"If drought spreads across a region, water competition may increase between towns and farms.","zh":"如果乾旱蔓延整個地區，城鎮和農場之間的水資源競爭可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that many parts of an area are affected.","zh":"這個片語顯示某區域的許多部分受影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as the world warms","meaning":"隨着全球變暖","examples":[{"en":"As the world warms, sea levels will rise.","zh":"隨着全球變暖，海平面將上升。"},{"en":"As the world warms means while global temperatures are increasing.","zh":"As the world warms 指當全球氣溫正在上升時。"},{"en":"As the city warms, more families may install fans or air-conditioners.","zh":"隨着城市變暖，更多家庭可能安裝風扇或冷氣機。"},{"en":"If the world warms, ice melts and oceans expand, pushing sea levels higher.","zh":"如果全球變暖，冰會融化，海洋會膨脹，推高海平面。"},{"en":"This phrase links warming with changes happening at the same time.","zh":"這個片語把變暖與同時發生的變化連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"oceans expand","meaning":"海洋膨脹","examples":[{"en":"Sea levels rise partly because oceans expand.","zh":"海平面上升部分原因是海洋膨脹。"},{"en":"Oceans expand means seawater takes up more space as it becomes warmer.","zh":"Oceans expand 指海水變暖時佔據更多空間。"},{"en":"A science teacher may show expansion by heating water in a glass tube.","zh":"科學老師可能透過加熱玻璃管中的水來展示膨脹。"},{"en":"If oceans expand, coastlines may face higher water levels even without ice melt.","zh":"如果海洋膨脹，即使沒有冰融化，海岸線也可能面對更高水位。"},{"en":"This phrase explains one reason sea levels rise.","zh":"這個片語解釋海平面上升的一個原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"glaciers melt","meaning":"冰川融化","examples":[{"en":"Sea levels rise as glaciers melt.","zh":"隨着冰川融化，海平面上升。"},{"en":"Glaciers melt means large bodies of land ice turn into water.","zh":"Glaciers melt 指大型陸地冰體變成水。"},{"en":"A documentary may show glaciers melting at the edge of a mountain valley.","zh":"紀錄片可能展示山谷邊緣的冰川正在融化。"},{"en":"If melted glacier water reaches the ocean, it can contribute to sea-level rise.","zh":"如果融化冰川水到達海洋，它可以促成海平面上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ice loss caused by warming.","zh":"這個片語描述由變暖造成的冰流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Mediterranean basin","meaning":"地中海盆地","examples":[{"en":"Sea levels may rise around much of the Mediterranean basin.","zh":"地中海盆地大部分地區周圍的海平面可能上升。"},{"en":"The Mediterranean basin is the land and sea area around the Mediterranean Sea.","zh":"Mediterranean basin 是地中海周圍的陸地和海域。"},{"en":"A geography class may study the Mediterranean basin to understand climate, trade, and farming.","zh":"地理課可能研究地中海盆地，以理解氣候、貿易和農業。"},{"en":"If sea levels rise in this basin, coastal cities and wetlands may face danger.","zh":"如果該盆地海平面上升，沿海城市和濕地可能面對危險。"},{"en":"This phrase names the wider area surrounding the Mediterranean Sea.","zh":"這個片語命名地中海周邊更廣泛區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rise by close to","meaning":"上升接近……","examples":[{"en":"Sea levels could rise by close to one metre by 2100.","zh":"到2100年，海平面可能上升接近一米。"},{"en":"To rise by close to an amount means to increase by almost that amount.","zh":"To rise by close to an amount 指增加接近某個數量。"},{"en":"School fees may rise by close to ten per cent if costs keep increasing.","zh":"如果成本持續增加，學費可能上升接近百分之十。"},{"en":"If sea levels rise by nearly one metre, low coastal areas may flood more often.","zh":"如果海平面上升接近一米，低窪沿海地區可能更常水浸。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate amount of increase.","zh":"這個片語給出大約增幅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"by 2100","meaning":"到2100年","examples":[{"en":"Sea levels may rise significantly by 2100.","zh":"到2100年，海平面可能顯著上升。"},{"en":"By 2100 means before or at the year 2100.","zh":"By 2100 指在2100年之前或到2100年時。"},{"en":"A city may aim to become carbon neutral by 2050.","zh":"一座城市可能目標到2050年達至碳中和。"},{"en":"If sea levels rise by 2100, today’s planning decisions will affect future generations.","zh":"如果海平面到2100年上升，今天的規劃決定會影響未來世代。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a future deadline or time point.","zh":"這個片語設定未來期限或時間點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, some coastal areas may be lost.","zh":"因此，一些沿海地區可能喪失。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what has just been mentioned.","zh":"As a result 指因為剛剛提到的事情。"},{"en":"The lift broke down; as a result, students had to use the stairs.","zh":"升降機故障；因此，學生必須使用樓梯。"},{"en":"If sea levels rise, coastal land may flood or erode as a result.","zh":"如果海平面上升，沿海土地可能因此水浸或受侵蝕。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a consequence.","zh":"這個片語引出後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"low-lying coastal areas","meaning":"低窪沿海地區","examples":[{"en":"Low-lying coastal areas may be lost through flooding.","zh":"低窪沿海地區可能因水浸而喪失。"},{"en":"Low-lying coastal areas are seaside places that sit close to sea level.","zh":"Low-lying coastal areas 是接近海平面的海邊地方。"},{"en":"A low-lying coastal town may flood during storms and high tides.","zh":"低窪沿海城鎮可能在風暴和漲潮期間水浸。"},{"en":"If sea levels rise, these areas may need sea walls or evacuation plans.","zh":"如果海平面上升，這些地區可能需要海堤或疏散計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes coastal places with high flood risk.","zh":"這個片語描述水浸風險高的沿海地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be lost through","meaning":"因……而喪失","examples":[{"en":"Coastal areas may be lost through flooding or erosion.","zh":"沿海地區可能因水浸或侵蝕而喪失。"},{"en":"To be lost through something means to disappear or be destroyed because of that process.","zh":"To be lost through something 指因某過程而消失或被破壞。"},{"en":"A family’s savings may be lost through careless spending.","zh":"家庭儲蓄可能因粗心花費而喪失。"},{"en":"If coastlines are lost through erosion, land slowly disappears into the sea.","zh":"如果海岸線因侵蝕而喪失，土地會慢慢消失到海裏。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the process that causes loss.","zh":"這個片語解釋造成損失的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"flooding or erosion","meaning":"水浸或侵蝕","examples":[{"en":"Flooding or erosion may destroy coastal areas.","zh":"水浸或侵蝕可能摧毀沿海地區。"},{"en":"Flooding or erosion means damage caused by too much water or by land being worn away.","zh":"Flooding or erosion 指由過量水分或土地被磨蝕帶來的損害。"},{"en":"A beach may lose sand through erosion after repeated storms.","zh":"沙灘可能在反覆風暴後因侵蝕而失去沙。"},{"en":"If flooding and erosion happen together, coastal homes may become unsafe.","zh":"如果水浸和侵蝕同時發生，沿海房屋可能變得不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase names two common ways coastlines can be damaged.","zh":"這個片語命名海岸線受損的兩種常見方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"coastal aquifers","meaning":"沿海含水層","examples":[{"en":"Coastal aquifers may become more salty as sea levels rise.","zh":"隨着海平面上升，沿海含水層可能變得更鹹。"},{"en":"Coastal aquifers are underground water stores near the coast.","zh":"Coastal aquifers 是靠近海岸的地下儲水層。"},{"en":"A town may depend on coastal aquifers for drinking water.","zh":"城鎮可能依賴沿海含水層作飲用水。"},{"en":"If seawater enters an aquifer, the freshwater can become too salty to use.","zh":"如果海水進入含水層，淡水可能變得太鹹而不能使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes underground water resources vulnerable to sea-level rise.","zh":"這個片語描述容易受海平面上升影響的地下水資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"become more salty","meaning":"變得更鹹","examples":[{"en":"Rivers and coastal aquifers may become more salty.","zh":"河流和沿海含水層可能變得更鹹。"},{"en":"To become more salty means to contain a higher amount of salt.","zh":"To become more salty 指含有更多鹽分。"},{"en":"Soup becomes more salty if too much seasoning is added.","zh":"如果加入太多調味料，湯會變得更鹹。"},{"en":"If seawater mixes with freshwater, rivers or wells may become more salty.","zh":"如果海水與淡水混合，河流或水井可能變得更鹹。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing salt content.","zh":"這個片語描述鹽分含量增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"worst affected areas","meaning":"受影響最嚴重的地區","examples":[{"en":"The Nile Delta and Venice may be among the worst affected areas.","zh":"尼羅河三角洲和威尼斯可能屬於受影響最嚴重的地區。"},{"en":"Worst affected areas are places that suffer the most serious damage.","zh":"Worst affected areas 是遭受最嚴重損害的地方。"},{"en":"After a flood, the worst affected areas may need emergency food and medical help first.","zh":"水災後，受影響最嚴重的地區可能最先需要緊急糧食和醫療協助。"},{"en":"If low land sinks while sea levels rise, it may become one of the worst affected areas.","zh":"如果低窪土地下沉而海平面上升，它可能成為受影響最嚴重地區之一。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where harm is greatest.","zh":"這個片語指出傷害最大的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Nile Delta","meaning":"尼羅河三角洲","examples":[{"en":"The Nile Delta is one of the worst affected areas mentioned.","zh":"尼羅河三角洲是文中提到受影響最嚴重的地區之一。"},{"en":"The Nile Delta is the low-lying area where the Nile River spreads out before reaching the sea.","zh":"Nile Delta 是尼羅河入海前分散流動的低窪地區。"},{"en":"A geography class may study the Nile Delta because many people farm and live there.","zh":"地理課可能研究尼羅河三角洲，因為許多人在那裏耕作和生活。"},{"en":"If sea levels rise, low delta land can be flooded or become salty.","zh":"如果海平面上升，低窪三角洲土地可能被淹浸或變鹹。"},{"en":"This phrase names a vulnerable coastal river region.","zh":"這個片語命名一個脆弱的沿海河流地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"local subsidence","meaning":"本地下沉","examples":[{"en":"Local subsidence can make sea-level rise more severe.","zh":"本地下沉可以令海平面上升更嚴重。"},{"en":"Local subsidence is the sinking of land in a particular area.","zh":"Local subsidence 是某特定地區土地下沉。"},{"en":"A city may suffer local subsidence if too much groundwater is pumped out.","zh":"如果抽取太多地下水，城市可能出現本地下沉。"},{"en":"If land sinks while the sea rises, flooding becomes more serious.","zh":"如果土地下沉而海面上升，水浸會更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes downward movement of land.","zh":"這個片語描述土地向下移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"one-and-a-half times as much as elsewhere","meaning":"是其他地方的一倍半","examples":[{"en":"Sea levels could rise one-and-a-half times as much as elsewhere.","zh":"海平面可能上升至其他地方的一倍半。"},{"en":"One-and-a-half times as much as elsewhere means 50 per cent more than in other places.","zh":"One-and-a-half times as much as elsewhere 指比其他地方多百分之五十。"},{"en":"A taxi ride may cost one-and-a-half times as much as usual during a holiday surcharge.","zh":"在假日附加費期間，的士車程可能花費平常的一倍半。"},{"en":"If sea-level rise is higher than elsewhere, local damage may be much worse.","zh":"如果海平面上升幅度高於其他地方，當地損害可能嚴重得多。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one amount with another area’s amount.","zh":"這個片語把一個數量與另一地區的數量作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the consequences of","meaning":"……的後果","examples":[{"en":"The consequences of climate change are far-reaching.","zh":"氣候變化的後果影響深遠。"},{"en":"The consequences of something are the results or effects that follow from it.","zh":"The consequences of something 是某事之後出現的結果或影響。"},{"en":"The consequences of missing school for weeks can include weaker grades and lost confidence.","zh":"缺課數星期的後果可以包括成績變弱和失去信心。"},{"en":"If climate change affects food, water, and health, its consequences are wide.","zh":"如果氣候變化影響食物、水和健康，其後果就很廣泛。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what happens because of an event or process.","zh":"這個片語引出因某事件或過程而發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"far-reaching","meaning":"影響深遠的","examples":[{"en":"The consequences of desertification are far-reaching.","zh":"荒漠化的後果影響深遠。"},{"en":"Far-reaching means affecting many people, places, or areas of life.","zh":"Far-reaching 指影響許多人、地方或生活範疇。"},{"en":"A new railway line can have far-reaching effects on housing, jobs, and shopping.","zh":"新鐵路線可以對住屋、工作和購物產生深遠影響。"},{"en":"If land degradation affects food, migration, and health, its impact is far-reaching.","zh":"如果土地退化影響食物、遷移和健康，其影響就是深遠的。"},{"en":"This word describes influence that extends widely.","zh":"這個詞描述廣泛延伸的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a gloomy picture","meaning":"悲觀的景象","examples":[{"en":"Greenpeace presents a gloomy picture of the future.","zh":"Greenpeace 呈現一幅未來的悲觀景象。"},{"en":"A gloomy picture is a negative or worrying description of what may happen.","zh":"Gloomy picture 是對可能發生事情的負面或令人擔憂描述。"},{"en":"A report may paint a gloomy picture if it predicts falling jobs and rising costs.","zh":"如果報告預測職位下降和成本上升，它可能描繪悲觀景象。"},{"en":"If climate risks are serious, an organisation may present a gloomy picture to urge action.","zh":"如果氣候風險嚴重，組織可能呈現悲觀景象以促使行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a pessimistic outlook.","zh":"這個片語描述悲觀前景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"livestock production","meaning":"畜牧生產","examples":[{"en":"Livestock production would suffer as rangeland deteriorates.","zh":"隨着牧場退化，畜牧生產會受損。"},{"en":"Livestock production is the raising of animals for meat, milk, wool, or other farm products.","zh":"Livestock production 是飼養動物以生產肉、奶、羊毛或其他農產品。"},{"en":"A farm with cattle and sheep depends on livestock production for income.","zh":"有牛和羊的農場依靠畜牧生產取得收入。"},{"en":"If grazing land becomes poor, animals may have less food and production may fall.","zh":"如果放牧地變差，動物可能食物較少，產量可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes animal-based farming output.","zh":"這個片語描述以動物為基礎的農業產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"suffer due to","meaning":"因……而受損","examples":[{"en":"Livestock production may suffer due to poorer rangeland.","zh":"畜牧生產可能因牧場質素較差而受損。"},{"en":"To suffer due to something means to be harmed because of it.","zh":"To suffer due to something 指因某事而受害。"},{"en":"Students may suffer due to poor classroom lighting if they read for long periods.","zh":"如果學生長時間閱讀，可能因課室照明差而受影響。"},{"en":"If animals have less grass to eat, livestock production may decline.","zh":"如果動物可吃的草較少，畜牧生產可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase connects harm with its cause.","zh":"這個片語把傷害與原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"deterioration in the quality of","meaning":"……質素惡化","examples":[{"en":"Drought may cause a deterioration in the quality of rangeland.","zh":"乾旱可能造成牧場質素惡化。"},{"en":"Deterioration in the quality of something means it becomes worse or less useful.","zh":"Deterioration in the quality of something 指某物變差或較無用。"},{"en":"A deterioration in the quality of school lunches may lead to student complaints.","zh":"學校午餐質素惡化可能引起學生投訴。"},{"en":"If rangeland quality falls, animals may become weaker or produce less.","zh":"如果牧場質素下降，動物可能變弱或產量減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decline in standard or condition.","zh":"這個片語描述標準或狀況下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"rangeland","meaning":"牧場；放牧地","examples":[{"en":"Livestock production depends on the quality of rangeland.","zh":"畜牧生產取決於牧場質素。"},{"en":"Rangeland is open land where animals graze on natural vegetation.","zh":"Rangeland 是動物在天然植被上放牧的開闊土地。"},{"en":"A cattle farmer needs healthy rangeland so animals have enough grass.","zh":"養牛農民需要健康牧場，讓動物有足夠草吃。"},{"en":"If rangeland deteriorates, farmers may need to buy extra feed.","zh":"如果牧場退化，農民可能需要購買額外飼料。"},{"en":"This word refers to land used for grazing animals.","zh":"這個詞指用於動物放牧的土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"yields of grains","meaning":"穀物產量","examples":[{"en":"Yields of grains may decrease because of drought.","zh":"穀物產量可能因乾旱而下降。"},{"en":"Yields of grains are the amounts of grain crops harvested.","zh":"Yields of grains 是收割到的穀物作物數量。"},{"en":"A farmer checks grain yields to know whether the season was successful.","zh":"農民檢查穀物產量，以知道該季是否成功。"},{"en":"If yields fall, food prices may rise and farmers may earn less.","zh":"如果產量下降，食物價格可能上升，農民收入可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase measures how much grain is produced.","zh":"這個片語量度穀物生產多少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"other crops","meaning":"其他農作物","examples":[{"en":"Other crops may also be affected by drought.","zh":"其他農作物也可能受乾旱影響。"},{"en":"Other crops means additional plants grown for food, fibre, or sale.","zh":"Other crops 指另外種植作為食物、纖維或出售的植物。"},{"en":"Besides rice, a farm may grow other crops such as beans, vegetables, or fruit.","zh":"除了稻米，農場可能種植豆類、蔬菜或水果等其他作物。"},{"en":"If drought affects several crops, farmers have fewer ways to recover income.","zh":"如果乾旱影響幾種作物，農民恢復收入的方法就較少。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to crops beyond the main one being discussed.","zh":"這個片語指正在討論的主要作物以外的作物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"decrease substantially","meaning":"大幅下降","examples":[{"en":"Crop yields could decrease substantially across the Mediterranean.","zh":"整個地中海地區的農作物產量可能大幅下降。"},{"en":"To decrease substantially means to fall by a large or meaningful amount.","zh":"To decrease substantially 指大幅或有意義地下降。"},{"en":"A student’s screen time may decrease substantially if parents set clear rules.","zh":"如果家長設立清晰規則，學生的螢幕時間可能大幅下降。"},{"en":"If harvests decrease substantially, food supply and farm income can suffer.","zh":"如果收成大幅下降，糧食供應和農民收入都可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious reduction, not a tiny drop.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重減少，而不是小幅下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"increased frequency of drought","meaning":"乾旱頻率增加","examples":[{"en":"Crop yields may fall because of the increased frequency of drought.","zh":"農作物產量可能因乾旱頻率增加而下降。"},{"en":"Increased frequency of drought means droughts happen more often than before.","zh":"Increased frequency of drought 指乾旱比以前更常發生。"},{"en":"If a town faces drought every summer instead of once every few years, the frequency has increased.","zh":"如果城鎮每年夏天都面對乾旱，而不是每幾年一次，頻率就增加了。"},{"en":"More frequent droughts give soil and water supplies less time to recover.","zh":"更頻繁乾旱令土壤和供水有較少時間恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes drought becoming a more regular problem.","zh":"這個片語描述乾旱變成更經常的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"crop production","meaning":"農作物生產","examples":[{"en":"Crop production would be threatened by water shortages.","zh":"農作物生產會受到缺水威脅。"},{"en":"Crop production is the growing and harvesting of plants for food, fibre, or sale.","zh":"Crop production 是種植和收割植物作食物、纖維或出售。"},{"en":"A farming family depends on crop production to earn money and feed itself.","zh":"農民家庭依靠農作物生產賺錢和供養自己。"},{"en":"If water becomes scarce, crop production may decline sharply.","zh":"如果水變得稀缺，農作物生產可能大幅下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes plant-based agricultural output.","zh":"這個片語描述以植物為基礎的農業產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be further threatened by","meaning":"進一步受到……威脅","examples":[{"en":"Crop production would be further threatened by competition for water.","zh":"農作物生產會因水資源競爭而進一步受到威脅。"},{"en":"To be further threatened by something means to face an additional danger from it.","zh":"To be further threatened by something 指因某事面對額外危險。"},{"en":"A small shop may be further threatened by rising rent after already losing customers.","zh":"小店在已失去顧客後，可能因租金上升而進一步受到威脅。"},{"en":"If drought is already harming crops, water competition makes the risk worse.","zh":"如果乾旱已在傷害作物，水資源競爭會令風險更差。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another layer of danger.","zh":"這個片語加入另一層危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"increased competition for water","meaning":"對水資源的競爭加劇","examples":[{"en":"Increased competition for water may damage agriculture.","zh":"對水資源的競爭加劇可能損害農業。"},{"en":"Increased competition for water means more people or sectors are fighting for limited water supplies.","zh":"Increased competition for water 指更多人或行業爭奪有限水供應。"},{"en":"Farmers, factories, and households may compete for water during a drought.","zh":"乾旱期間，農民、工廠和家庭可能爭奪水資源。"},{"en":"If water competition increases, weaker communities may receive less.","zh":"如果水資源競爭加劇，較弱勢社區可能獲得較少水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pressure caused by limited water demand.","zh":"這個片語描述由有限水需求造成的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"greater prevalence of","meaning":"……更普遍","examples":[{"en":"A greater prevalence of pests and diseases could threaten crops.","zh":"害蟲和疾病更普遍可能威脅作物。"},{"en":"Greater prevalence of something means it becomes more common in a population or area.","zh":"Greater prevalence of something 指某事在人群或地區中變得更常見。"},{"en":"A greater prevalence of flu in winter may make schools remind students to wash hands.","zh":"冬季流感更普遍時，學校可能提醒學生洗手。"},{"en":"If pests become more common, farmers may lose more crops.","zh":"如果害蟲變得更普遍，農民可能失去更多作物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a problem appearing more often.","zh":"這個片語描述問題更常出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"pests and diseases","meaning":"害蟲和疾病","examples":[{"en":"Pests and diseases can reduce crop production.","zh":"害蟲和疾病可以減少農作物生產。"},{"en":"Pests and diseases are insects, animals, or illnesses that harm plants, animals, or people.","zh":"Pests and diseases 是傷害植物、動物或人的昆蟲、動物或疾病。"},{"en":"A vegetable farm may lose leaves and fruit because of pests and diseases.","zh":"蔬菜農場可能因害蟲和疾病失去葉和果實。"},{"en":"If warmer weather helps pests survive, crop damage may increase.","zh":"如果較暖天氣幫助害蟲存活，作物損害可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase names living threats to agriculture and health.","zh":"這個片語命名對農業和健康的生物威脅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"land loss through","meaning":"因……造成的土地流失","examples":[{"en":"Crop production may be threatened by land loss through desertification.","zh":"農作物生產可能受到因荒漠化造成的土地流失威脅。"},{"en":"Land loss through something means land disappearing or becoming unusable because of that process.","zh":"Land loss through something 指土地因某過程而消失或變得不可使用。"},{"en":"A coastal village may suffer land loss through erosion after repeated storms.","zh":"沿海村莊可能在反覆風暴後遭受因侵蝕造成的土地流失。"},{"en":"If farmland is lost through desertification, food production may fall.","zh":"如果農地因荒漠化而流失，食物生產可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the process by which land is lost.","zh":"這個片語解釋土地因哪個過程而流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"sea-level rise","meaning":"海平面上升","examples":[{"en":"Sea-level rise can cause flooding and land loss.","zh":"海平面上升可以造成水浸和土地流失。"},{"en":"Sea-level rise is the increase in the average height of the ocean surface.","zh":"Sea-level rise 是海洋表面平均高度上升。"},{"en":"A coastal city may build higher sea walls because of sea-level rise.","zh":"沿海城市可能因海平面上升而興建更高海堤。"},{"en":"If seas rise, low roads, homes, and farms may flood more often.","zh":"如果海面上升，低窪道路、房屋和農場可能更常水浸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major climate risk for coastal areas.","zh":"這個片語描述沿海地區的主要氣候風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the combination of","meaning":"……的結合","examples":[{"en":"The combination of heat and pollution may harm health.","zh":"高溫和污染的結合可能損害健康。"},{"en":"The combination of two things means they act together as one situation.","zh":"The combination of two things 指兩件事共同作用成一種情況。"},{"en":"The combination of stress and little sleep can make students feel exhausted.","zh":"壓力和睡眠不足的結合可以令學生感到筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"If heat and pollution occur together, the health risk may become worse than either alone.","zh":"如果高溫和污染同時出現，健康風險可能比任何一者單獨出現更差。"},{"en":"This phrase shows two factors working together.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩個因素共同作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"heat and pollution","meaning":"高溫和污染","examples":[{"en":"Heat and pollution can increase respiratory illness.","zh":"高溫和污染可以增加呼吸系統疾病。"},{"en":"Heat and pollution means high temperatures together with dirty or harmful air.","zh":"Heat and pollution 指高溫加上污濁或有害空氣。"},{"en":"On a hot polluted day, children with asthma may need to stay indoors.","zh":"在又熱又污染的日子，患哮喘的兒童可能需要留在室內。"},{"en":"If heat traps polluted air in a city, breathing problems may become more common.","zh":"如果高溫把污染空氣困在城市裏，呼吸問題可能變得更常見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two environmental pressures on health.","zh":"這個片語描述對健康的兩種環境壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"lead to an upsurge in","meaning":"導致……激增","examples":[{"en":"Heat and pollution could lead to an upsurge in respiratory illness.","zh":"高溫和污染可能導致呼吸系統疾病激增。"},{"en":"To lead to an upsurge in something means to cause a sudden or large increase in it.","zh":"To lead to an upsurge in something 指造成某事突然或大幅增加。"},{"en":"A flu outbreak can lead to an upsurge in absences from school.","zh":"流感爆發可以導致學校缺席人數激增。"},{"en":"If air quality worsens during heatwaves, breathing problems may rise quickly.","zh":"如果熱浪期間空氣質素惡化，呼吸問題可能迅速上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sharp increase caused by a condition.","zh":"這個片語描述由某條件造成的急劇增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"respiratory illness","meaning":"呼吸系統疾病","examples":[{"en":"Respiratory illness may increase among urban populations.","zh":"呼吸系統疾病可能在城市人口中增加。"},{"en":"Respiratory illness is illness affecting breathing, the lungs, or the airways.","zh":"Respiratory illness 是影響呼吸、肺部或呼吸道的疾病。"},{"en":"A child with respiratory illness may cough, wheeze, or feel short of breath.","zh":"患有呼吸系統疾病的孩子可能咳嗽、喘鳴或感到氣促。"},{"en":"If air pollution worsens, more people may need treatment for breathing problems.","zh":"如果空氣污染惡化，更多人可能需要治療呼吸問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes health problems linked to breathing.","zh":"這個片語描述與呼吸有關的健康問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"urban populations","meaning":"城市人口","examples":[{"en":"Urban populations may suffer from heat and pollution.","zh":"城市人口可能受高溫和污染影響。"},{"en":"Urban populations are people living in cities or towns.","zh":"Urban populations 是生活在城市或城鎮的人口。"},{"en":"Urban populations often depend on public transport, apartments, and city services.","zh":"城市人口通常依賴公共交通、公寓和城市服務。"},{"en":"If cities become hotter, urban populations may face stronger heat stress.","zh":"如果城市變得更熱，城市人口可能面對更強高溫壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people living in built-up areas.","zh":"這個片語指生活在建成區的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"extreme weather events","meaning":"極端天氣事件","examples":[{"en":"Extreme weather events could increase death and injury rates.","zh":"極端天氣事件可能增加死亡和受傷率。"},{"en":"Extreme weather events are unusually severe weather situations such as storms, floods, heatwaves, and droughts.","zh":"Extreme weather events 是異常嚴重的天氣情況，例如風暴、水災、熱浪和乾旱。"},{"en":"Schools may close during extreme weather events to protect students.","zh":"學校可能在極端天氣事件期間停課，以保護學生。"},{"en":"If extreme weather becomes more common, emergency services may face heavier pressure.","zh":"如果極端天氣變得更常見，緊急服務可能面對更大壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dangerous weather beyond normal conditions.","zh":"這個片語描述超出正常情況的危險天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"death and injury rates","meaning":"死亡和受傷率","examples":[{"en":"Extreme weather events could increase death and injury rates.","zh":"極端天氣事件可能增加死亡和受傷率。"},{"en":"Death and injury rates are the numbers or proportions of people who die or get hurt.","zh":"Death and injury rates 是死亡或受傷人數或比例。"},{"en":"A city tracks road death and injury rates to decide where crossings are needed.","zh":"城市追蹤道路死亡和受傷率，以決定哪裏需要行人過路處。"},{"en":"If storms become stronger, more people may be harmed unless protection improves.","zh":"如果風暴變得更強，除非保護改善，否則更多人可能受害。"},{"en":"This phrase measures the human cost of danger.","zh":"這個片語量度危險的人命代價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"water shortages","meaning":"缺水","examples":[{"en":"Water shortages could increase the risk of disease.","zh":"缺水可能增加疾病風險。"},{"en":"Water shortages happen when there is not enough clean or usable water.","zh":"Water shortages 是沒有足夠清潔或可用水。"},{"en":"A school may face water shortages if pipes burst and drinking fountains stop working.","zh":"如果水管爆裂且飲水機停止運作，學校可能面對缺水。"},{"en":"If people lack clean water, hygiene becomes harder and illness may spread.","zh":"如果人們缺乏清潔水，衛生會更難維持，疾病可能擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lack of water that can affect daily life and health.","zh":"這個片語描述會影響日常生活和健康的水不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"damaged infrastructure","meaning":"受損基建","examples":[{"en":"Damaged infrastructure can increase public-health risks.","zh":"受損基建可以增加公共健康風險。"},{"en":"Damaged infrastructure means broken systems such as roads, pipes, bridges, hospitals, or power lines.","zh":"Damaged infrastructure 指受破壞的系統，例如道路、水管、橋樑、醫院或電線。"},{"en":"After a flood, damaged infrastructure may stop ambulances from reaching patients.","zh":"水災後，受損基建可能阻止救護車到達病人。"},{"en":"If water pipes break, clean water may mix with dirty water.","zh":"如果水管破裂，清潔水可能與污水混合。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harm to basic systems society depends on.","zh":"這個片語描述社會依賴的基本系統受損。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"increase the risk of","meaning":"增加……的風險","examples":[{"en":"Water shortages can increase the risk of cholera and dysentery.","zh":"缺水可以增加霍亂和痢疾的風險。"},{"en":"To increase the risk of something means to make it more likely to happen.","zh":"To increase the risk of something 指令某事更可能發生。"},{"en":"Not wearing a helmet can increase the risk of injury when cycling.","zh":"踩單車不戴頭盔可以增加受傷風險。"},{"en":"If clean water is scarce, waterborne diseases may become more likely.","zh":"如果清潔食水稀缺，水傳播疾病可能更容易發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a higher chance of harm.","zh":"這個片語描述傷害機會較高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"cholera and dysentery","meaning":"霍亂和痢疾","examples":[{"en":"Water shortages may increase the risk of cholera and dysentery.","zh":"缺水可能增加霍亂和痢疾的風險。"},{"en":"Cholera and dysentery are serious diseases often linked to unsafe water and poor sanitation.","zh":"Cholera and dysentery 是常與不安全食水和惡劣衛生有關的嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"After a flood, health workers may warn people about cholera and dysentery.","zh":"水災後，醫護人員可能提醒人們注意霍亂和痢疾。"},{"en":"If clean water and toilets are unavailable, these diseases can spread quickly.","zh":"如果清潔水和廁所不可用，這些疾病可以迅速傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase names two dangerous water-related illnesses.","zh":"這個片語命名兩種危險的水相關疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"increase the incidence of","meaning":"增加……的發病率","examples":[{"en":"Higher temperatures may increase the incidence of infectious diseases.","zh":"較高氣溫可能增加傳染病的發病率。"},{"en":"To increase the incidence of something means to make cases of it more common.","zh":"To increase the incidence of something 指令某事的個案更常見。"},{"en":"Poor hand hygiene can increase the incidence of stomach illness in schools.","zh":"手部衛生欠佳可以增加學校腸胃病發病率。"},{"en":"If mosquitoes survive in warmer areas, disease cases may rise.","zh":"如果蚊子能在較暖地區存活，疾病個案可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increase in how often a problem occurs.","zh":"這個片語描述問題發生頻率增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"infectious diseases","meaning":"傳染病","examples":[{"en":"Infectious diseases may become more common as temperatures rise.","zh":"隨着氣溫上升，傳染病可能變得更常見。"},{"en":"Infectious diseases are illnesses that can spread from one person, animal, or environment to another.","zh":"Infectious diseases 是可以由一個人、動物或環境傳播到另一方的疾病。"},{"en":"Schools try to reduce infectious diseases by encouraging handwashing and sick leave.","zh":"學校透過鼓勵洗手和病假來減少傳染病。"},{"en":"If climate change helps disease carriers spread, infectious diseases may reach new areas.","zh":"如果氣候變化幫助疾病媒介擴散，傳染病可能到達新地區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes diseases that can be transmitted.","zh":"這個片語描述可以傳播的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"malaria and dengue fever","meaning":"瘧疾和登革熱","examples":[{"en":"Malaria and dengue fever may increase with higher temperatures.","zh":"瘧疾和登革熱可能隨着氣溫上升而增加。"},{"en":"Malaria and dengue fever are mosquito-borne diseases that can cause serious illness.","zh":"Malaria and dengue fever 是由蚊子傳播、可造成嚴重疾病的病。"},{"en":"Communities may remove standing water to reduce mosquitoes that spread dengue fever.","zh":"社區可能清除積水，以減少傳播登革熱的蚊子。"},{"en":"If warmer weather helps mosquitoes survive, these diseases may become more common.","zh":"如果較暖天氣幫助蚊子存活，這些疾病可能變得更常見。"},{"en":"This phrase names two infectious diseases linked to mosquitoes.","zh":"這個片語命名兩種與蚊子相關的傳染病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"serious social disruption","meaning":"嚴重社會混亂","examples":[{"en":"Climate change could cause serious social disruption.","zh":"氣候變化可能造成嚴重社會混亂。"},{"en":"Serious social disruption means major disturbance to normal community life.","zh":"Serious social disruption 指正常社區生活受到重大干擾。"},{"en":"A long transport strike can cause serious social disruption by stopping people from reaching work or school.","zh":"長期交通罷工可以令市民無法上班或上學，造成嚴重社會混亂。"},{"en":"If climate change forces migration and conflict over water, society may become unstable.","zh":"如果氣候變化迫使人遷移並造成水資源衝突，社會可能變得不穩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severe disturbance beyond environmental damage alone.","zh":"這個片語描述超出單純環境損害的嚴重干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be forced from their homelands","meaning":"被迫離開家園","examples":[{"en":"Millions may be forced from their homelands.","zh":"數百萬人可能被迫離開家園。"},{"en":"To be forced from one’s homeland means to have to leave one’s home country or region unwillingly.","zh":"To be forced from one’s homeland 指被迫離開自己的家鄉、國家或地區。"},{"en":"Families may be forced from their homes if floods destroy their villages.","zh":"如果水災摧毀村莊，家庭可能被迫離開家園。"},{"en":"If harvests fail for many years, people may migrate to survive.","zh":"如果收成多年失敗，人們可能為求生存而遷移。"},{"en":"This phrase describes displacement caused by danger or hardship.","zh":"這個片語描述由危險或困苦造成的流離失所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"poor harvests","meaning":"收成欠佳","examples":[{"en":"Poor harvests may force people to leave their homes.","zh":"收成欠佳可能迫使人們離開家園。"},{"en":"Poor harvests are harvests that produce much less food than expected.","zh":"Poor harvests 是產出的食物遠少於預期的收成。"},{"en":"A farmer may face poor harvests if drought dries the fields before crops mature.","zh":"如果乾旱在作物成熟前令田地乾枯，農民可能面對收成欠佳。"},{"en":"If poor harvests continue, families may lose income and food security.","zh":"如果收成欠佳持續，家庭可能失去收入和糧食安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disappointing or insufficient crop production.","zh":"這個片語描述令人失望或不足的作物產量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"international disputes over","meaning":"關於……的國際爭端","examples":[{"en":"International disputes over shared water resources could increase.","zh":"關於共享水資源的國際爭端可能增加。"},{"en":"International disputes over something are disagreements between countries about it.","zh":"International disputes over something 是國家之間就某事產生的分歧。"},{"en":"Countries may have international disputes over rivers that cross borders.","zh":"國家之間可能因跨境河流出現國際爭端。"},{"en":"If water becomes scarce, governments may argue over who has the right to use it.","zh":"如果水變得稀缺，政府可能爭論誰有權使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes conflict between nations over a shared issue.","zh":"這個片語描述國家之間圍繞共同議題的衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"shared water resources","meaning":"共享水資源","examples":[{"en":"Shared water resources could become a source of conflict.","zh":"共享水資源可能成為衝突來源。"},{"en":"Shared water resources are rivers, lakes, or groundwater supplies used by more than one group or country.","zh":"Shared water resources 是由不止一個群體或國家使用的河流、湖泊或地下水供應。"},{"en":"Two towns may share the same reservoir during a dry season.","zh":"兩個城鎮可能在旱季共用同一個水塘。"},{"en":"If shared water becomes scarce, cooperation may become harder.","zh":"如果共享水資源變得稀缺，合作可能變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes water that different users depend on together.","zh":"這個片語描述不同使用者共同依賴的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"turn into conflict","meaning":"演變成衝突","examples":[{"en":"Disputes over water could turn into conflict.","zh":"關於水資源的爭端可能演變成衝突。"},{"en":"To turn into conflict means to develop from disagreement into serious confrontation or fighting.","zh":"To turn into conflict 指由分歧發展成嚴重對抗或戰鬥。"},{"en":"A small argument between classmates can turn into conflict if no one listens.","zh":"如果沒有人聆聽，同學之間的小爭論可以演變成衝突。"},{"en":"If countries cannot agree on water use, tension may become more dangerous.","zh":"如果國家不能就用水達成協議，緊張局勢可能變得更危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a problem becoming more serious.","zh":"這個片語描述問題變得更嚴重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"future climate change","meaning":"未來氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"Future climate change could undermine sustainable development.","zh":"未來氣候變化可能削弱可持續發展。"},{"en":"Future climate change means climate shifts expected to happen in the years ahead.","zh":"Future climate change 指預計在未來年月發生的氣候轉變。"},{"en":"A city may plan for future climate change by improving drainage and heat shelters.","zh":"城市可能透過改善排水和高溫庇護設施來規劃未來氣候變化。"},{"en":"If future climate change is ignored, today’s buildings may not be safe enough later.","zh":"如果忽視未來氣候變化，今天的建築之後可能不夠安全。"},{"en":"This phrase looks ahead to climate risks that have not fully happened yet.","zh":"這個片語展望尚未完全發生的氣候風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"critically undermine","meaning":"嚴重削弱","examples":[{"en":"Climate change could critically undermine development efforts.","zh":"氣候變化可能嚴重削弱發展努力。"},{"en":"To critically undermine something means to seriously weaken or damage it.","zh":"To critically undermine something 指嚴重削弱或破壞某事。"},{"en":"Constant staff shortages can critically undermine a hospital’s ability to provide care.","zh":"持續人手短缺可以嚴重削弱醫院提供護理的能力。"},{"en":"If floods destroy roads and farms, development gains may be lost.","zh":"如果水災摧毀道路和農場，發展成果可能喪失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damage that threatens the success of something important.","zh":"這個片語描述威脅重要事情成功的損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"efforts towards","meaning":"為……所作的努力","examples":[{"en":"Climate change may undermine efforts towards sustainable development.","zh":"氣候變化可能削弱為可持續發展所作的努力。"},{"en":"Efforts towards something are actions taken to achieve that goal.","zh":"Efforts towards something 是為達成某目標而採取的行動。"},{"en":"A student’s efforts towards better writing include reading examples and rewriting essays.","zh":"學生為改善寫作所作的努力包括閱讀例子和重寫作文。"},{"en":"If climate disasters keep damaging infrastructure, development efforts may slow down.","zh":"如果氣候災害不斷破壞基建，發展努力可能減慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes work directed at a target.","zh":"這個片語描述朝某目標而作的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"sustainable development","meaning":"可持續發展","examples":[{"en":"Sustainable development may be threatened by climate change.","zh":"可持續發展可能受到氣候變化威脅。"},{"en":"Sustainable development is development that meets present needs without damaging future generations’ ability to meet theirs.","zh":"Sustainable development 是滿足當前需要，同時不損害未來世代滿足自身需要能力的發展。"},{"en":"A city supports sustainable development when it builds housing near reliable public transport.","zh":"城市把房屋建在可靠公共交通附近時，就是支持可持續發展。"},{"en":"If growth destroys water, land, and health, it is not truly sustainable.","zh":"如果增長破壞水、土地和健康，它就不是真正可持續。"},{"en":"This phrase combines economic progress with long-term environmental and social care.","zh":"這個片語把經濟進步與長期環境和社會照顧結合起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"its impacts on","meaning":"其對……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Climate change affects the environment and social well-being.","zh":"氣候變化影響環境和社會福祉。"},{"en":"Its impacts on something means the effects it has on that thing.","zh":"Its impacts on something 指它對某事造成的影響。"},{"en":"A school may study a new timetable and its impacts on sleep, homework, and family life.","zh":"學校可能研究新時間表及其對睡眠、功課和家庭生活的影響。"},{"en":"If climate change affects health and income, its impacts are both environmental and social.","zh":"如果氣候變化影響健康和收入，其影響就是環境和社會兩方面的。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the results felt by a specific area or group.","zh":"這個片語集中於某範疇或群體感受到的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"social and economic well-being","meaning":"社會和經濟福祉","examples":[{"en":"Climate change may damage social and economic well-being.","zh":"氣候變化可能損害社會和經濟福祉。"},{"en":"Social and economic well-being means people’s quality of life, community stability, jobs, and income.","zh":"Social and economic well-being 指人們的生活質素、社區穩定、工作和收入。"},{"en":"A town’s well-being improves when families have safe homes, stable work, and good public services.","zh":"當家庭有安全住所、穩定工作和良好公共服務，城鎮福祉會改善。"},{"en":"If climate disasters destroy livelihoods, both social life and economic security suffer.","zh":"如果氣候災害摧毀生計，社會生活和經濟安全都會受損。"},{"en":"This phrase connects community health with financial stability.","zh":"這個片語把社區健康與財政穩定連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"in many respects","meaning":"在許多方面","examples":[{"en":"In many respects, climate change worsens existing problems.","zh":"在許多方面，氣候變化會惡化現有問題。"},{"en":"In many respects means in many ways or from many points of view.","zh":"In many respects 指在許多方式或從許多角度來看。"},{"en":"In many respects, online learning is convenient, but it can also feel lonely.","zh":"在許多方面，網上學習很方便，但也可能令人感到孤單。"},{"en":"If climate change affects water, food, health, and migration, it matters in many respects.","zh":"如果氣候變化影響水、食物、健康和遷移，它就在許多方面重要。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces several different aspects of a situation.","zh":"這個片語引出某情況的幾個不同方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"exacerbate existing problems","meaning":"加劇現有問題","examples":[{"en":"Climate change often exacerbates existing problems.","zh":"氣候變化往往加劇現有問題。"},{"en":"To exacerbate existing problems means to make problems that already exist worse.","zh":"To exacerbate existing problems 指令已存在的問題變得更差。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can exacerbate existing stress before exams.","zh":"睡眠不足可以在考試前加劇現有壓力。"},{"en":"If a region already lacks water, higher temperatures can make that shortage worse.","zh":"如果一個地區本來已缺水，較高氣溫可以令短缺更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes worsening old problems rather than creating entirely new ones.","zh":"這個片語描述惡化舊問題，而不是創造全新問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"instead of creating new ones","meaning":"而不是製造新的問題","examples":[{"en":"Climate change often worsens old problems instead of creating new ones.","zh":"氣候變化往往惡化舊問題，而不是製造新的問題。"},{"en":"Instead of creating new ones means rather than producing completely new problems.","zh":"Instead of creating new ones 指而不是產生完全新的問題。"},{"en":"A bad timetable may worsen tiredness instead of creating a new learning problem.","zh":"糟糕時間表可能惡化疲倦，而不是製造新的學習問題。"},{"en":"If a city already floods easily, climate change may deepen that problem rather than start a new one.","zh":"如果城市本來已容易水浸，氣候變化可能加深該問題，而不是開始新問題。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts worsening existing issues with making new issues.","zh":"這個片語把惡化現有問題與製造新問題作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the sheer magnitude of","meaning":"……的巨大規模","examples":[{"en":"The sheer magnitude of the problem means it cannot be ignored.","zh":"這個問題的巨大規模意味着它不能被忽視。"},{"en":"The sheer magnitude of something means its very large size or seriousness.","zh":"The sheer magnitude of something 指某事非常大的規模或嚴重程度。"},{"en":"The sheer magnitude of exam pressure can surprise parents who only see final marks.","zh":"考試壓力的巨大規模可能令只看見最終分數的家長驚訝。"},{"en":"If a problem affects food, water, health, and migration, its magnitude is enormous.","zh":"如果問題影響食物、水、健康和遷移，其規模就非常巨大。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises scale very strongly.","zh":"這個片語非常強烈地強調規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"potential problem","meaning":"潛在問題","examples":[{"en":"The potential problem is too large to ignore.","zh":"這個潛在問題太大，不能忽視。"},{"en":"A potential problem is a problem that may happen in the future.","zh":"Potential problem 是未來可能發生的問題。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice a potential problem if many students submit homework late.","zh":"如果許多學生遲交功課，老師可能注意到一個潛在問題。"},{"en":"If a potential problem is serious enough, action should begin before it fully appears.","zh":"如果潛在問題足夠嚴重，就應在它完全出現前開始行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a risk that has not fully become reality yet.","zh":"這個片語描述尚未完全成真的風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"cannot be ignored","meaning":"不能被忽視","examples":[{"en":"The threat of climate change cannot be ignored.","zh":"氣候變化的威脅不能被忽視。"},{"en":"Cannot be ignored means must be noticed, considered, or dealt with.","zh":"Cannot be ignored 指必須被注意、考慮或處理。"},{"en":"A student’s repeated absence cannot be ignored by the school.","zh":"學生反覆缺席不能被學校忽視。"},{"en":"If a warning sign is serious, ignoring it may make the final damage worse.","zh":"如果警號嚴重，忽視它可能令最終損害更差。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that action or attention is necessary.","zh":"這個片語強調有必要行動或關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"there is some scope for","meaning":"仍有……空間","examples":[{"en":"There is some scope for adaptation.","zh":"仍有一些適應空間。"},{"en":"There is some scope for something means there is some room or possibility for it.","zh":"There is some scope for something 指仍有一些空間或可能性去做某事。"},{"en":"There is some scope for improving a lesson if students give clear feedback.","zh":"如果學生給出清晰回饋，課堂仍有改善空間。"},{"en":"If a problem cannot be avoided completely, there may still be scope for reducing harm.","zh":"如果問題不能完全避免，仍可能有減少傷害的空間。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests limited but real possibility.","zh":"這個片語暗示可能性有限但真實存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"adaptation","meaning":"適應；調適","examples":[{"en":"Adaptation can reduce some effects of climate change.","zh":"適應可以減少氣候變化的一些影響。"},{"en":"Adaptation means changing behaviour, systems, or infrastructure to cope with new conditions.","zh":"Adaptation 指改變行為、系統或基建，以應對新情況。"},{"en":"A school adapts to hotter weather by adding fans, shade, and more water breaks.","zh":"學校透過增加風扇、遮蔭和飲水休息來適應更熱天氣。"},{"en":"If climate risks increase, adaptation can reduce harm even before emissions fall.","zh":"如果氣候風險增加，即使排放尚未下降，適應也可以減少傷害。"},{"en":"This word describes practical adjustment to change.","zh":"這個詞描述對變化作出的實際調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"irrespective of climate change","meaning":"不論是否有氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"Many measures would be beneficial irrespective of climate change.","zh":"不論是否有氣候變化，許多措施都會有益。"},{"en":"Irrespective of climate change means whether or not climate change happens.","zh":"Irrespective of climate change 指無論氣候變化是否發生。"},{"en":"Saving water is useful irrespective of climate change because it reduces waste and bills.","zh":"不論是否有氣候變化，節約用水都有用，因為它減少浪費和帳單。"},{"en":"If a policy improves health anyway, it is valuable even without climate concerns.","zh":"如果政策本來就改善健康，即使沒有氣候憂慮，它仍有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is useful under different conditions.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事在不同條件下都有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"radical changes","meaning":"根本性改變","examples":[{"en":"Radical changes in policies and practices may be needed.","zh":"政策和做法可能需要根本性改變。"},{"en":"Radical changes are major and deep changes, not small adjustments.","zh":"Radical changes 是重大而深層的改變，不是小調整。"},{"en":"A failing school may need radical changes in teaching methods and support systems.","zh":"表現不佳的學校可能需要在教學方法和支援制度上作根本性改變。"},{"en":"If current habits cause serious damage, small improvements may not be enough.","zh":"如果現有習慣造成嚴重損害，小改善可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fundamental change.","zh":"這個片語描述根本改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"policies and practices","meaning":"政策和做法","examples":[{"en":"Policies and practices must change to address climate risks.","zh":"政策和做法必須改變，以應對氣候風險。"},{"en":"Policies and practices are official rules and the actual ways people do things.","zh":"Policies and practices 是正式規則以及人們實際做事的方法。"},{"en":"A school’s policies and practices include attendance rules and how teachers follow them.","zh":"學校的政策和做法包括出席規則，以及老師如何執行它們。"},{"en":"If policy says water should be saved but practice wastes water, the system will fail.","zh":"如果政策說要節水，但實際做法浪費水，系統就會失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase combines formal decisions with everyday actions.","zh":"這個片語結合正式決定和日常行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"it is vital that","meaning":"至關重要的是","examples":[{"en":"It is vital that developed countries help developing countries adapt.","zh":"至關重要的是，發達國家幫助發展中國家適應。"},{"en":"It is vital that means it is extremely important that something happens.","zh":"It is vital that 指某事發生極其重要。"},{"en":"It is vital that students read the instructions before answering exam questions.","zh":"至關重要的是，學生在回答考試題目前先閱讀指示。"},{"en":"If support is vital, delay can make the problem much worse.","zh":"如果支援至關重要，延誤可以令問題嚴重得多。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises necessity.","zh":"這個片語強烈強調必要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"developed countries","meaning":"發達國家","examples":[{"en":"Developed countries should assist adaptation in poorer countries.","zh":"發達國家應協助較貧窮國家適應。"},{"en":"Developed countries are wealthy countries with advanced industries, infrastructure, and public services.","zh":"Developed countries 是擁有先進產業、基建和公共服務的富裕國家。"},{"en":"Developed countries often have more resources to build flood defences and heat-warning systems.","zh":"發達國家通常有更多資源興建防洪設施和高溫警報系統。"},{"en":"If poorer countries face climate risks, developed countries may be expected to provide support.","zh":"如果較貧窮國家面對氣候風險，發達國家可能被期望提供支援。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts richer industrialised nations with developing countries.","zh":"這個片語把較富裕工業化國家與發展中國家作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"meet their obligations to","meaning":"履行責任去……","examples":[{"en":"Developed countries should meet their obligations to assist adaptation.","zh":"發達國家應履行責任去協助適應。"},{"en":"To meet their obligations to do something means to fulfil their duties or responsibilities.","zh":"To meet their obligations to do something 指履行其職責或責任。"},{"en":"Parents meet their obligations to children by providing care, safety, and education.","zh":"家長透過提供照顧、安全和教育來履行對孩子的責任。"},{"en":"If countries promised climate finance, they must provide support rather than only make speeches.","zh":"如果國家承諾氣候資金，就必須提供支援，而不只是發表演說。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses responsibility that should be honoured.","zh":"這個片語強調應被履行的責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"assist adaptation in","meaning":"協助……適應","examples":[{"en":"Developed countries should assist adaptation in developing countries.","zh":"發達國家應協助發展中國家適應。"},{"en":"To assist adaptation in a place means to help that place adjust to new conditions.","zh":"To assist adaptation in a place 指幫助某地適應新情況。"},{"en":"A school can assist adaptation in new students by giving them mentors and clear routines.","zh":"學校可以透過給新學生導師和清晰常規，協助他們適應。"},{"en":"If poorer countries lack money and technology, outside help can support climate adaptation.","zh":"如果較貧窮國家缺乏金錢和科技，外部幫助可以支持氣候適應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes helping others adjust successfully.","zh":"這個片語描述幫助他人成功調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"developing countries","meaning":"發展中國家","examples":[{"en":"Developing countries may need help adapting to climate change.","zh":"發展中國家可能需要協助來適應氣候變化。"},{"en":"Developing countries are countries whose economies and public systems are still growing or less wealthy.","zh":"Developing countries 是經濟和公共系統仍在發展或較不富裕的國家。"},{"en":"Developing countries may have fewer resources to protect farms, hospitals, and coastal towns.","zh":"發展中國家可能有較少資源保護農場、醫院和沿海城鎮。"},{"en":"If climate risks rise, these countries may need finance, technology, and training.","zh":"如果氣候風險上升，這些國家可能需要資金、科技和培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes countries with greater development needs.","zh":"這個片語描述有較大发展需要的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"access to know-how","meaning":"取得專業知識","examples":[{"en":"Developing countries need access to know-how and financial assistance.","zh":"發展中國家需要取得專業知識和財政援助。"},{"en":"Access to know-how means the ability to obtain practical knowledge, skills, and expertise.","zh":"Access to know-how 指能夠取得實用知識、技能和專業能力。"},{"en":"A new teacher needs access to know-how about lesson planning and classroom management.","zh":"新老師需要取得關於備課和課堂管理的專業知識。"},{"en":"If communities gain technical knowledge, they can adapt more effectively.","zh":"如果社區取得技術知識，它們可以更有效適應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being able to use expert practical knowledge.","zh":"這個片語描述能夠使用專家實用知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"financial assistance","meaning":"財政援助","examples":[{"en":"Financial assistance can help countries adapt to climate change.","zh":"財政援助可以幫助國家適應氣候變化。"},{"en":"Financial assistance is money or funding given to help someone deal with a need or problem.","zh":"Financial assistance 是為幫助某人處理需要或問題而提供的金錢或資金。"},{"en":"A student may receive financial assistance to pay school fees.","zh":"學生可能獲得財政援助來支付學費。"},{"en":"If a country lacks funds, financial assistance can support new water systems or flood defences.","zh":"如果國家缺乏資金，財政援助可以支持新供水系統或防洪設施。"},{"en":"This phrase describes money-based help.","zh":"這個片語描述金錢形式的幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"ultimately","meaning":"最終","examples":[{"en":"Ultimately, emissions must be cut to stabilise the climate.","zh":"最終，必須削減排放以穩定氣候。"},{"en":"Ultimately means in the end or after everything important is considered.","zh":"Ultimately 指最終，或在考慮所有重要事情之後。"},{"en":"A student may try many methods, but ultimately regular practice matters most.","zh":"學生可能嘗試許多方法，但最終定期練習最重要。"},{"en":"If adaptation helps only partly, emissions must eventually fall to reduce the main risk.","zh":"如果適應只能部分幫助，排放最終必須下降以減少主要風險。"},{"en":"This word introduces the final or most important conclusion.","zh":"這個詞引出最後或最重要的結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"long-term sustainability","meaning":"長期可持續性","examples":[{"en":"The long-term sustainability of the region depends on controlling climate change.","zh":"該地區的長期可持續性取決於控制氣候變化。"},{"en":"Long-term sustainability means the ability to continue safely and successfully far into the future.","zh":"Long-term sustainability 指在遙遠未來仍能安全和成功持續的能力。"},{"en":"A school’s long-term sustainability depends on good teaching, stable finances, and student trust.","zh":"學校的長期可持續性取決於良好教學、穩定財政和學生信任。"},{"en":"If water, land, and health systems fail, a region cannot remain sustainable.","zh":"如果水、土地和健康系統失效，一個地區就不能保持可持續。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on survival and success over many years.","zh":"這個片語集中於多年後的生存和成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"within tolerable bounds","meaning":"在可承受範圍內","examples":[{"en":"Climate change must be kept within tolerable bounds.","zh":"氣候變化必須被控制在可承受範圍內。"},{"en":"Within tolerable bounds means within limits that people, ecosystems, or systems can still cope with.","zh":"Within tolerable bounds 指在人類、生態系統或制度仍可應付的界限內。"},{"en":"Noise in a classroom should be kept within tolerable bounds so students can concentrate.","zh":"課室噪音應保持在可承受範圍內，讓學生能專注。"},{"en":"If warming exceeds tolerable limits, adaptation may become much harder.","zh":"如果變暖超出可承受界限，適應可能變得困難得多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping a problem within manageable limits.","zh":"這個片語描述把問題保持在可管理界限內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"current understanding of","meaning":"對……的現有理解","examples":[{"en":"Current understanding of safe limits points to urgent action.","zh":"對安全界限的現有理解表明需要緊急行動。"},{"en":"Current understanding of something means what people or experts know about it now.","zh":"Current understanding of something 指人們或專家目前對某事的認識。"},{"en":"Current understanding of child development affects how teachers design lessons.","zh":"對兒童發展的現有理解會影響老師如何設計課堂。"},{"en":"If current understanding changes, policies may need to change too.","zh":"如果現有理解改變，政策也可能需要改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to knowledge available at the present time.","zh":"這個片語指目前可用的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"safe limits","meaning":"安全界限","examples":[{"en":"Safe limits suggest the need for prompt international action.","zh":"安全界限顯示需要迅速國際行動。"},{"en":"Safe limits are boundaries beyond which risk becomes too high.","zh":"Safe limits 是超出後風險會過高的界線。"},{"en":"A medicine label gives safe limits so people do not take too much.","zh":"藥物標籤提供安全界限，讓人們不會服用過量。"},{"en":"If climate change goes beyond safe limits, damage may become difficult to control.","zh":"如果氣候變化超出安全界限，損害可能變得難以控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes thresholds that should not be crossed.","zh":"這個片語描述不應跨越的門檻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"point to the need for","meaning":"表明有需要……","examples":[{"en":"Scientific understanding points to the need for urgent agreement.","zh":"科學理解表明有需要達成緊急協議。"},{"en":"To point to the need for something means to show that it is necessary.","zh":"To point to the need for something 指顯示某事是必要的。"},{"en":"Falling test scores may point to the need for more reading practice.","zh":"測驗分數下降可能表明有需要更多閱讀練習。"},{"en":"If evidence shows rising risk, it points to the need for early action.","zh":"如果證據顯示風險上升，就表明有需要及早行動。"},{"en":"This phrase links evidence with a necessary response.","zh":"這個片語把證據與必要回應連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"prompt international agreement","meaning":"迅速的國際協議","examples":[{"en":"Prompt international agreement is needed to cut emissions.","zh":"需要迅速的國際協議來削減排放。"},{"en":"Prompt international agreement means countries quickly reaching a shared decision or plan.","zh":"Prompt international agreement 指各國快速達成共同決定或計劃。"},{"en":"During a health crisis, prompt international agreement can help countries share medicine faster.","zh":"在健康危機期間，迅速的國際協議可以幫助國家更快分享藥物。"},{"en":"If emissions must fall quickly, delayed agreement may make targets harder to reach.","zh":"如果排放必須快速下降，延遲協議可能令目標更難達成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fast cooperation between countries.","zh":"這個片語描述國家之間快速合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"drastic cuts in","meaning":"大幅削減","examples":[{"en":"Drastic cuts in greenhouse gas emissions are required.","zh":"需要大幅削減溫室氣體排放。"},{"en":"Drastic cuts in something are very large reductions in it.","zh":"Drastic cuts in something 是對某事物非常大幅的減少。"},{"en":"A family may need drastic cuts in spending if income suddenly falls.","zh":"如果收入突然下降，家庭可能需要大幅削減開支。"},{"en":"If emissions must fall quickly, small reductions may not be enough.","zh":"如果排放必須迅速下降，小幅減少可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong and serious reduction.","zh":"這個片語描述強力而嚴重的削減。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"stabilise atmospheric concentrations","meaning":"穩定大氣濃度","examples":[{"en":"Emissions cuts are needed to stabilise atmospheric concentrations of greenhouse gases.","zh":"需要削減排放，以穩定溫室氣體的大氣濃度。"},{"en":"To stabilise atmospheric concentrations means to stop the amount of gases in the air from rising further.","zh":"To stabilise atmospheric concentrations 指阻止空氣中氣體含量進一步上升。"},{"en":"A doctor may try to stabilise a patient’s blood sugar so it stops rising and falling sharply.","zh":"醫生可能嘗試穩定病人血糖，讓它不再大幅升跌。"},{"en":"If greenhouse gas concentrations stabilise, climate risks may become easier to manage.","zh":"如果溫室氣體濃度穩定，氣候風險可能較容易管理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping gas levels steady in the atmosphere.","zh":"這個片語描述令大氣中氣體水平保持穩定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"complete the flow-chart","meaning":"完成流程圖","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the flow-chart using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成流程圖。"},{"en":"To complete the flow-chart means to fill in missing steps in a diagram showing a process.","zh":"To complete the flow-chart 指填補展示過程的圖表中的缺失步驟。"},{"en":"Students may complete a flow-chart showing how drought leads to crop failure.","zh":"學生可能完成一張顯示乾旱如何導致農作物歉收的流程圖。"},{"en":"If one step is wrong, the whole cause-and-effect chain may become unclear.","zh":"如果其中一步錯誤，整個因果鏈可能變得不清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in reading tasks.","zh":"這個片語是閱讀題常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個詞","examples":[{"en":"The instructions say to write no more than three words.","zh":"指示說寫不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"No more than three words 指答案必須包含三個或更少英文單詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “greenhouse gases,” it uses two words and fits the rule.","zh":"如果答案是 “greenhouse gases”，它用了兩個詞，符合規則。"},{"en":"If students write four words, they may lose the mark even if the idea is right.","zh":"如果學生寫四個詞，即使意思正確，也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit for exam answers.","zh":"這個片語為考試答案給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"which paragraph contains","meaning":"哪一段包含","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which paragraph contains specific information.","zh":"學生識別哪一段包含特定資料。"},{"en":"Which paragraph contains asks students to find the paragraph where information appears.","zh":"Which paragraph contains 要求學生找出資料出現在哪一段。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may scan topic sentences to see which paragraph contains the answer.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能掃讀主題句，看哪一段包含答案。"},{"en":"If students confuse similar paragraphs, they may choose the wrong location.","zh":"如果學生混淆相似段落，他們可能選錯位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in paragraph-location questions.","zh":"這個片語用於段落定位題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"the following information","meaning":"以下資料","examples":[{"en":"The task asks students to locate the following information.","zh":"題目要求學生定位以下資料。"},{"en":"The following information means the details listed after the instruction.","zh":"The following information 指指示後列出的資料細節。"},{"en":"Students should underline names and dates in the following information before scanning the passage.","zh":"學生掃讀文章前，應在以下資料中劃出名字和日期。"},{"en":"If the information is paraphrased in the text, students must match meaning, not just words.","zh":"如果資料在文章中被改寫，學生必須配對意思，而不只是字詞。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the details students need to find.","zh":"這個片語引出學生需要尋找的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"human intervention","meaning":"人為干預","examples":[{"en":"Human intervention can worsen or help address environmental problems.","zh":"人為干預可以惡化或幫助處理環境問題。"},{"en":"Human intervention means actions taken by people to change or manage a situation.","zh":"Human intervention 指人類採取行動去改變或管理某情況。"},{"en":"Planting trees is human intervention that can help protect soil.","zh":"種樹是一種可以幫助保護土壤的人為干預。"},{"en":"If people overuse land, human intervention can also make environmental damage worse.","zh":"如果人們過度使用土地，人為干預也可以令環境損害更差。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to helpful action or harmful interference.","zh":"這個片語可以指有幫助的行動，也可以指有害干涉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"potential solution to","meaning":"……的潛在解決方法","examples":[{"en":"Human intervention may be a potential solution to disaster.","zh":"人為干預可能是災難的潛在解決方法。"},{"en":"A potential solution to something is a possible way to solve or reduce a problem.","zh":"Potential solution to something 是解決或減少某問題的可能方法。"},{"en":"Extra buses may be a potential solution to overcrowding at a school gate.","zh":"增加巴士可能是學校門口擁擠的潛在解決方法。"},{"en":"If desertification can be slowed by better land management, that becomes a possible solution.","zh":"如果荒漠化可以透過更好土地管理減慢，那就成為可能解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an option that may work but still needs action or testing.","zh":"這個片語描述可能有效但仍需行動或測試的選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"the rate of climate change","meaning":"氣候變化的速度","examples":[{"en":"The rate of climate change is expected to accelerate.","zh":"氣候變化的速度預計會加快。"},{"en":"The rate of climate change is the speed at which the climate is changing.","zh":"The rate of climate change 是氣候正在改變的速度。"},{"en":"Teachers may explain rate by comparing how fast two students finish the same task.","zh":"老師可能透過比較兩名學生完成同一任務的速度來解釋 rate。"},{"en":"If the rate increases, communities have less time to adapt.","zh":"如果速度增加，社區就有較少時間適應。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on speed, not just the fact of change.","zh":"這個片語集中於速度，而不只是變化本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"be set to accelerate dramatically","meaning":"將會急劇加快","examples":[{"en":"The rate of climate change is set to accelerate dramatically.","zh":"氣候變化的速度將會急劇加快。"},{"en":"To be set to accelerate dramatically means to be expected to become much faster.","zh":"To be set to accelerate dramatically 指預計會變得快得多。"},{"en":"A school construction project may be set to accelerate dramatically after new funding arrives.","zh":"新資金到位後，學校建設項目可能會急劇加快。"},{"en":"If climate change accelerates dramatically, slow planning may no longer be enough.","zh":"如果氣候變化急劇加快，緩慢規劃可能不再足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase predicts a sharp increase in speed.","zh":"這個片語預測速度大幅增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"seldom enough information","meaning":"很少有足夠資料","examples":[{"en":"There is seldom enough information to track past environmental change.","zh":"很少有足夠資料去追蹤過去的環境變化。"},{"en":"Seldom enough information means there is rarely enough data or evidence.","zh":"Seldom enough information 指很少有足夠數據或證據。"},{"en":"A teacher may have seldom enough information to judge a new student after only one lesson.","zh":"老師只上一堂課後，很少有足夠資料去評估新學生。"},{"en":"If records are missing, past environmental change becomes hard to measure.","zh":"如果紀錄缺失，過去環境變化就難以量度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a frequent shortage of useful information.","zh":"這個片語描述經常缺乏有用資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"track how fast","meaning":"追蹤……有多快","examples":[{"en":"Data can help scientists track how fast degradation has occurred.","zh":"數據可以幫助科學家追蹤退化發生得有多快。"},{"en":"To track how fast something happens means to measure or follow its speed over time.","zh":"To track how fast something happens 指隨時間量度或跟進某事的速度。"},{"en":"A teacher may track how fast students read by timing them each month.","zh":"老師可能透過每月計時來追蹤學生閱讀有多快。"},{"en":"If scientists track degradation speed, they can judge whether action is urgent.","zh":"如果科學家追蹤退化速度，他們可以判斷行動是否緊急。"},{"en":"This phrase describes monitoring the rate of change.","zh":"這個片語描述監察變化速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"effects of climate change","meaning":"氣候變化的影響","examples":[{"en":"The effects of climate change may vary across regions.","zh":"氣候變化的影響可能因地區而異。"},{"en":"Effects of climate change are the results caused by changes in climate patterns.","zh":"Effects of climate change 是由氣候模式變化造成的結果。"},{"en":"One city may face flooding, while another may face drought.","zh":"一座城市可能面對水浸，另一座城市可能面對乾旱。"},{"en":"If climate effects differ by region, local planning must also differ.","zh":"如果氣候影響因地區而異，本地規劃也必須不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the consequences of a changing climate.","zh":"這個片語描述氣候變化的後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"happen in the past","meaning":"在過去發生","examples":[{"en":"Some areas lack data showing how degradation happened in the past.","zh":"一些地區缺乏顯示退化在過去如何發生的數據。"},{"en":"Happen in the past means to occur before the present time.","zh":"Happen in the past 指在現在之前發生。"},{"en":"Historians study what happened in the past by reading records and objects.","zh":"歷史學家透過閱讀紀錄和研究物件來研究過去發生的事。"},{"en":"If we know how damage happened in the past, we may prevent it in the future.","zh":"如果我們知道損害在過去如何發生，就可能在未來防止它。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event before now.","zh":"這個片語把事件放在現在之前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"be attributable to","meaning":"可歸因於……","examples":[{"en":"Desertification is attributable to a number of factors.","zh":"荒漠化可歸因於多項因素。"},{"en":"To be attributable to something means to be caused by or explained by it.","zh":"To be attributable to something 指由某事造成或由某事解釋。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be attributable to regular practice and better sleep.","zh":"學生進步可能可歸因於定期練習和更好睡眠。"},{"en":"If land degradation is attributable to poor irrigation, changing water use may help.","zh":"如果土地退化可歸因於欠佳灌溉，改變用水方式可能有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the causes behind a result.","zh":"這個片語指出結果背後的成因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"a number of factors","meaning":"多項因素","examples":[{"en":"Desertification is attributable to a number of factors.","zh":"荒漠化可歸因於多項因素。"},{"en":"A number of factors means several causes or influences.","zh":"A number of factors 指幾個成因或影響。"},{"en":"A student’s stress may come from a number of factors, including exams, sleep, and family pressure.","zh":"學生壓力可能來自多項因素，包括考試、睡眠和家庭壓力。"},{"en":"If several factors create a problem, one solution may not be enough.","zh":"如果幾個因素造成問題，單一解決方法可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the cause is not single or simple.","zh":"這個片語顯示原因不是單一或簡單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary with words from the list.","zh":"學生使用列表中的詞語完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill missing words in a short version of the passage.","zh":"To complete the summary 指在文章簡短版本中填補缺失字詞。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole summary first before choosing words.","zh":"學生選詞前應先閱讀整段摘要。"},{"en":"If the grammar around a blank requires a noun, a verb will not fit.","zh":"如果空格前後文法需要名詞，動詞就不合適。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in reading exams.","zh":"這個片語是閱讀考試中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"catastrophic effects","meaning":"災難性影響","examples":[{"en":"Climate change may have catastrophic effects on people and animals.","zh":"氣候變化可能對人類和動物有災難性影響。"},{"en":"Catastrophic effects are extremely serious and destructive consequences.","zh":"Catastrophic effects 是極其嚴重和具破壞性的後果。"},{"en":"A major dam failure could have catastrophic effects on villages downstream.","zh":"大型水壩崩塌可能對下游村莊造成災難性影響。"},{"en":"If sea levels rise and crops fail, the effects can become catastrophic.","zh":"如果海平面上升且農作物歉收，影響可以變成災難性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damage on a disaster level.","zh":"這個片語描述災難級別的損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"the human and animal world","meaning":"人類和動物世界","examples":[{"en":"Climate change may affect both the human and animal world.","zh":"氣候變化可能同時影響人類和動物世界。"},{"en":"The human and animal world means people together with animals and their habitats.","zh":"Human and animal world 指人類、動物及其棲息地。"},{"en":"A polluted river affects the human and animal world by harming drinking water and fish.","zh":"受污染河流會透過傷害食水和魚類來影響人類和動物世界。"},{"en":"If climate change damages food chains, both humans and animals may suffer.","zh":"如果氣候變化破壞食物鏈，人類和動物都可能受苦。"},{"en":"This phrase connects human society with the natural world.","zh":"這個片語把人類社會與自然世界連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"as glaciers melt","meaning":"隨着冰川融化","examples":[{"en":"As glaciers melt, sea levels will rise.","zh":"隨着冰川融化，海平面將上升。"},{"en":"As glaciers melt means while large bodies of land ice are turning into water.","zh":"As glaciers melt 指當大型陸地冰體正在變成水時。"},{"en":"As ice melts in a glass, the water level may rise if the ice was sitting above the water.","zh":"當玻璃杯中的冰融化，如果冰原本在水面之上，水位可能上升。"},{"en":"If glacier water flows into the ocean, it adds water to the sea.","zh":"如果冰川水流入海洋，它會為海洋增加水量。"},{"en":"This phrase links ice melt with its result.","zh":"這個片語把冰融化與其結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"extensive flooding","meaning":"大範圍水浸","examples":[{"en":"Sea-level rise may cause extensive flooding.","zh":"海平面上升可能造成大範圍水浸。"},{"en":"Extensive flooding means flooding that covers a large area.","zh":"Extensive flooding 是覆蓋大片地區的水浸。"},{"en":"After days of rain, a town may face extensive flooding in streets, schools, and shops.","zh":"連日大雨後，城鎮可能在街道、學校和商店面對大範圍水浸。"},{"en":"If coastal water rises higher, floods may spread farther inland.","zh":"如果沿海水位升得更高，水浸可能更深入內陸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes widespread water damage.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛水害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"land loss","meaning":"土地流失","examples":[{"en":"Sea-level rise can cause flooding and land loss.","zh":"海平面上升可以造成水浸和土地流失。"},{"en":"Land loss means land disappears, is eroded, or becomes unusable.","zh":"Land loss 指土地消失、被侵蝕或變得不可使用。"},{"en":"A village may face land loss if the riverbank collapses every rainy season.","zh":"如果河岸每個雨季倒塌，村莊可能面對土地流失。"},{"en":"If coastal land is lost, homes, roads, and farms may disappear too.","zh":"如果沿海土地流失，房屋、道路和農場也可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the loss of usable physical land.","zh":"這個片語描述可用實體土地的喪失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"another consequence of","meaning":"……的另一個後果","examples":[{"en":"Another consequence of global warming is desertification.","zh":"全球變暖的另一個後果是荒漠化。"},{"en":"Another consequence of something means one more result caused by it.","zh":"Another consequence of something 指由某事造成的另一個結果。"},{"en":"Another consequence of poor sleep is weaker memory during lessons.","zh":"睡眠不足的另一個後果是課堂記憶力較弱。"},{"en":"If global warming changes rainfall, desertification may be one result among many.","zh":"如果全球變暖改變降雨，荒漠化可能是眾多結果之一。"},{"en":"This phrase adds an extra effect to a list of results.","zh":"這個片語把額外影響加入結果清單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"areas known as drylands","meaning":"稱為乾旱地的地區","examples":[{"en":"Desertification affects areas known as drylands.","zh":"荒漠化影響稱為乾旱地的地區。"},{"en":"Areas known as drylands are regions that are officially or commonly called drylands.","zh":"Areas known as drylands 是正式或普遍被稱為乾旱地的地區。"},{"en":"A map may mark areas known as drylands so students can see where rainfall is limited.","zh":"地圖可能標示稱為乾旱地的地區，讓學生看見降雨有限的地方。"},{"en":"If these areas become drier, the risk of land degradation increases.","zh":"如果這些地區變得更乾，土地退化風險會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the name used for a type of region.","zh":"這個片語引出某類地區的名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"be subject to","meaning":"受……影響；易受……影響","examples":[{"en":"Drylands are subject to irregular weather patterns.","zh":"乾旱地易受不規則天氣模式影響。"},{"en":"To be subject to something means to be affected by it or likely to experience it.","zh":"To be subject to something 指受某事影響或很可能經歷某事。"},{"en":"Outdoor sports lessons are subject to weather conditions.","zh":"戶外體育課受天氣狀況影響。"},{"en":"If drylands are subject to erratic rain, farming becomes difficult to plan.","zh":"如果乾旱地受不穩定降雨影響，農業就難以規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase shows vulnerability or dependence on a condition.","zh":"這個片語顯示脆弱性或對某條件的依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"irregular weather patterns","meaning":"不規則天氣模式","examples":[{"en":"Drylands are subject to irregular weather patterns.","zh":"乾旱地受不規則天氣模式影響。"},{"en":"Irregular weather patterns are weather behaviours that do not follow normal or predictable timing.","zh":"Irregular weather patterns 是不遵循正常或可預測時間的天氣行為。"},{"en":"Farmers may struggle when rain comes in irregular patterns instead of a clear rainy season.","zh":"如果雨水以不規則模式出現，而不是清晰雨季，農民可能很吃力。"},{"en":"If weather becomes irregular, planting and harvesting schedules may fail.","zh":"如果天氣變得不規則，播種和收割時間表可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unpredictable weather.","zh":"這個片語描述難以預測的天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"human intervention or neglect","meaning":"人為干預或疏忽","examples":[{"en":"Drylands also suffer from human intervention or neglect.","zh":"乾旱地也受人為干預或疏忽之苦。"},{"en":"Human intervention or neglect means damage caused by active human actions or by failing to care properly.","zh":"Human intervention or neglect 指由人類主動行動或未能妥善照顧所造成的損害。"},{"en":"A school garden may suffer from neglect if no one waters it during holidays.","zh":"如果假期沒有人澆水，學校花園可能因疏忽而受損。"},{"en":"If people overuse land or ignore its condition, degradation can worsen.","zh":"如果人們過度使用土地或忽視其狀況，退化可以惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both harmful action and harmful inaction.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋有害行動和有害不作為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"inadequate irrigation systems","meaning":"不足的灌溉系統","examples":[{"en":"Inadequate irrigation systems can worsen land degradation.","zh":"不足的灌溉系統可以惡化土地退化。"},{"en":"Inadequate irrigation systems are watering systems that are not good enough for the land’s needs.","zh":"Inadequate irrigation systems 是不足以滿足土地需要的澆水系統。"},{"en":"A farm with broken pipes and uneven watering has an inadequate irrigation system.","zh":"有破裂水管和澆水不均的農場，擁有不足的灌溉系統。"},{"en":"If irrigation is inadequate, some crops may dry out while others are overwatered.","zh":"如果灌溉不足，一些作物可能乾枯，而另一些則澆水過多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes poor water delivery for farming.","zh":"這個片語描述農業中欠佳的供水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"inefficient irrigation systems","meaning":"低效的灌溉系統","examples":[{"en":"Inefficient irrigation systems can damage dryland environments.","zh":"低效的灌溉系統可以破壞乾旱地環境。"},{"en":"Inefficient irrigation systems waste water or fail to deliver it properly to crops.","zh":"Inefficient irrigation systems 會浪費水或未能妥善把水送到作物。"},{"en":"A leaking pipe system is inefficient because water is lost before reaching the field.","zh":"漏水管道系統是低效的，因為水在到達田地前已流失。"},{"en":"If irrigation wastes water in a dry region, soil and crops may both suffer.","zh":"如果灌溉在乾燥地區浪費水，土壤和作物都可能受害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes water systems that use resources poorly.","zh":"這個片語描述資源使用不良的供水系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"list of words","meaning":"詞語列表","examples":[{"en":"The list of words contains more choices than the summary needs.","zh":"詞語列表包含比摘要所需更多的選項。"},{"en":"A list of words is a set of possible answers provided for a task.","zh":"List of words 是為題目提供的一組可能答案。"},{"en":"Students should read the list of words carefully before choosing answers.","zh":"學生選答案前應仔細閱讀詞語列表。"},{"en":"If there are extra words, students must select by meaning and grammar, not guessing.","zh":"如果有額外詞語，學生必須根據意思和文法選擇，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the answer bank in a reading exercise.","zh":"這個片語描述閱讀練習中的答案庫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"choose from the list","meaning":"從列表中選擇","examples":[{"en":"Students choose suitable words from the list.","zh":"學生從列表中選擇合適詞語。"},{"en":"To choose from the list means to select answers from the provided options.","zh":"To choose from the list 指從提供的選項中選擇答案。"},{"en":"In a vocabulary exercise, students may choose from the list instead of writing their own words.","zh":"在詞彙練習中，學生可能從列表中選擇，而不是自己寫字。"},{"en":"If the list has extra choices, students need to check context carefully.","zh":"如果列表有多餘選項，學生需要仔細檢查語境。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an instruction to use only the supplied options.","zh":"這個片語指示只能使用所提供選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"there are more words than needed","meaning":"詞語比所需更多","examples":[{"en":"There are more words than needed to complete the summary.","zh":"詞語比完成摘要所需更多。"},{"en":"There are more words than needed means the list includes extra options that should not be used.","zh":"There are more words than needed 指列表包含不應使用的額外選項。"},{"en":"In a matching task, there may be more headings than needed, so students cannot use every one.","zh":"在配對題中，標題可能比所需更多，所以學生不能每個都用。"},{"en":"If extra words are included, students must reject distractors carefully.","zh":"如果包含額外詞語，學生必須仔細排除干擾項。"},{"en":"This phrase warns students that not every option is correct.","zh":"這個片語提醒學生並非每個選項都正確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 80 - LONG-TERM FORECAST - HOT AND DRY.pdf","sourcePage":26}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 81":[{"front":"migrants and refugees","meaning":"移民和難民","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses migrants and refugees in relation to discrimination and xenophobia.","zh":"文章討論移民和難民與歧視及仇外心理的關係。"},{"en":"Migrants and refugees are people who move from one place to another, often for work, safety, or survival.","zh":"migrants and refugees 指從一地遷往另一地的人，通常是為了工作、安全或生存。"},{"en":"A city may need extra language services when many migrants and refugees arrive.","zh":"當大量移民和難民到達，城市可能需要額外語言服務。"},{"en":"If migrants and refugees are not protected by law, they may face unfair treatment at work or in housing.","zh":"如果移民和難民不受法律保護，他們可能在工作或住屋上受到不公平對待。"},{"en":"The phrase often appears in discussions about human rights, borders, and social inclusion.","zh":"這個片語常出現在人權、邊界和社會共融的討論中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"racial discrimination","meaning":"種族歧視","examples":[{"en":"Racial discrimination affects many migrants, refugees and other non-nationals.","zh":"種族歧視影響許多移民、難民和其他非本國公民。"},{"en":"Racial discrimination means unfair treatment based on race, colour, descent, or ethnic origin.","zh":"racial discrimination 指基於種族、膚色、血統或族裔出身的不公平對待。"},{"en":"A job applicant may face racial discrimination if an employer rejects him only because of his background.","zh":"如果僱主只因求職者背景而拒絕他，該求職者可能面對種族歧視。"},{"en":"Racial discrimination can make people feel unsafe, excluded, and unable to access equal opportunities.","zh":"種族歧視可以令人感到不安全、被排斥，並無法獲得平等機會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unfair treatment linked to race or origin, not ordinary disagreement.","zh":"這個片語描述與種族或出身有關的不公平對待，而不是普通分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"xenophobia","meaning":"仇外心理；排外心理","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobia is often directed against people regarded as foreigners or outsiders.","zh":"仇外心理常針對被視為外國人或外來者的人。"},{"en":"Xenophobia means fear, dislike, or hostility toward people seen as foreign.","zh":"xenophobia 指對被視為外來者的人產生恐懼、厭惡或敵意。"},{"en":"A migrant family may experience xenophobia if neighbours blame them for local problems without evidence.","zh":"如果鄰居沒有證據就把本地問題怪罪於移民家庭，該家庭可能經歷仇外心理。"},{"en":"Xenophobia can grow when people feel insecure about jobs, housing, or national identity.","zh":"當人們對工作、住屋或國家身份感到不安時，仇外心理可能增長。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on hostility toward outsiders, even when they look physically similar to the majority.","zh":"這個片語集中於對外來者的敵意，即使他們在身體特徵上與主流群體相似。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one in every 50","meaning":"每50個中就有1個","examples":[{"en":"Today, one in every 50 human beings is a migrant worker, a refugee, an asylum seeker or an immigrant.","zh":"今天，每50個人中就有1個是移民工人、難民、尋求庇護者或移民。"},{"en":"One in every 50 means one person out of each group of fifty people.","zh":"one in every 50 指每五十人中有一人。"},{"en":"If one in every 50 students needs language support, a school must plan extra help carefully.","zh":"如果每50個學生中就有1個需要語言支援，學校必須仔細計劃額外幫助。"},{"en":"A figure like one in every 50 shows that migration is not a rare issue.","zh":"像每50個中就有1個這樣的數字，顯示移民不是罕見議題。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to express a proportion in a simple, memorable way.","zh":"這個片語用簡單而易記的方式表達比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"human beings","meaning":"人類；人","examples":[{"en":"One in every 50 human beings lives as a migrant worker, refugee, asylum seeker or immigrant.","zh":"每50個人中就有1個以移民工人、難民、尋求庇護者或移民身份生活。"},{"en":"Human beings means people, especially when stressing shared humanity.","zh":"human beings 指人，尤其強調共同人性時使用。"},{"en":"Policies about migration affect real human beings, not just numbers on a chart.","zh":"移民政策影響真實的人，而不只是圖表上的數字。"},{"en":"If human beings are treated only as statistics, their suffering may be ignored.","zh":"如果人類只被視為統計數字，他們的痛苦可能被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds readers that social issues concern people’s lives.","zh":"這個片語提醒讀者，社會議題關乎人的生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"migrant worker","meaning":"移民工人","examples":[{"en":"A migrant worker may live temporarily or permanently outside his or her country of origin.","zh":"移民工人可能暫時或永久居於其原籍國以外。"},{"en":"A migrant worker is a person who moves to another place or country to work.","zh":"migrant worker 指為工作而遷往另一地方或國家的人。"},{"en":"A restaurant may hire migrant workers when there are not enough local staff.","zh":"當本地員工不足，餐廳可能聘請移民工人。"},{"en":"Migrant workers may face exploitation if they do not understand local laws or language.","zh":"如果移民工人不明白本地法律或語言，可能面對剝削。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on migration for employment.","zh":"這個片語集中於為就業而遷移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"refugee","meaning":"難民","examples":[{"en":"A refugee may be forced to live outside his or her country of origin.","zh":"難民可能被迫居於其原籍國以外。"},{"en":"A refugee is a person who leaves their country because it is unsafe to stay.","zh":"refugee 指因留在本國不安全而離開的人。"},{"en":"A refugee family may need shelter, legal help, language support, and school places for children.","zh":"難民家庭可能需要住所、法律協助、語言支援和兒童學位。"},{"en":"War, persecution, or serious danger can force people to become refugees.","zh":"戰爭、迫害或嚴重危險可以迫使人成為難民。"},{"en":"The phrase usually stresses forced movement, not voluntary travel.","zh":"這個片語通常強調被迫遷移，而不是自願旅行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"asylum seeker","meaning":"尋求庇護者","examples":[{"en":"An asylum seeker is one of the migrant groups discussed in the passage.","zh":"尋求庇護者是文章討論的移民群體之一。"},{"en":"An asylum seeker is a person who asks another country for protection but has not yet been officially accepted as a refugee.","zh":"asylum seeker 指向另一國請求保護，但尚未正式被接納為難民的人。"},{"en":"An asylum seeker may wait months or years for a decision on their case.","zh":"尋求庇護者可能等候數月或數年才知道個案結果。"},{"en":"If an asylum seeker is refused protection, they may be asked to leave the country.","zh":"如果尋求庇護者被拒絕保護，可能被要求離開該國。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a legal status during the request for safety.","zh":"這個片語描述請求安全期間的法律身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"immigrant","meaning":"移民","examples":[{"en":"An immigrant may live in a foreign country temporarily or permanently.","zh":"移民可能暫時或永久居於外國。"},{"en":"An immigrant is a person who comes to live in a country that is not their original country.","zh":"immigrant 指來到非自己原籍國家居住的人。"},{"en":"An immigrant student may need time to learn the language and school routines.","zh":"移民學生可能需要時間學習語言和學校日常程序。"},{"en":"People may become immigrants for work, education, marriage, safety, or family reunion.","zh":"人們可能因工作、教育、婚姻、安全或家庭團聚而成為移民。"},{"en":"The phrase is broad and does not always imply danger or forced movement.","zh":"這個片語範圍較廣，不一定暗示危險或被迫遷移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"live in a foreign country","meaning":"居於外國","examples":[{"en":"Many immigrants live in a foreign country for work, safety or family reasons.","zh":"許多移民因工作、安全或家庭原因居於外國。"},{"en":"Live in a foreign country means reside in a country other than one’s own.","zh":"live in a foreign country 指居住在非自己本國的國家。"},{"en":"A student may live in a foreign country for university and then return home after graduation.","zh":"學生可能為讀大學而居於外國，畢業後再回家。"},{"en":"Living in a foreign country can create language challenges and cultural adjustment.","zh":"居於外國可以帶來語言挑戰和文化適應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes residence abroad, not simply a short holiday.","zh":"這個片語描述在海外居住，而不只是短暫假期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"current estimates","meaning":"目前估算","examples":[{"en":"Current estimates suggest that about 150 million people live outside their countries of origin.","zh":"目前估算顯示，約1.5億人居於其原籍國以外。"},{"en":"Current estimates are the latest approximate figures based on available information.","zh":"current estimates 指根據現有資料得出的最新約略數字。"},{"en":"Current estimates of school demand help officials decide how many classrooms are needed.","zh":"對學位需求的目前估算幫助官員決定需要多少課室。"},{"en":"If migration is difficult to measure exactly, current estimates may change over time.","zh":"如果移民難以準確量度，目前估算可能隨時間改變。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the number is approximate, not perfectly exact.","zh":"這個片語表示數字是約數，而不是完全精確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the United Nations","meaning":"聯合國","examples":[{"en":"The United Nations provides estimates about international migration.","zh":"聯合國提供關於國際移民的估算。"},{"en":"The United Nations is an international organisation of countries that works on peace, development, rights, and global cooperation.","zh":"the United Nations 指由各國組成、處理和平、發展、權利和全球合作的國際組織。"},{"en":"Schools may use United Nations reports when discussing poverty, migration, or climate change.","zh":"學校討論貧窮、移民或氣候變化時，可能使用聯合國報告。"},{"en":"If the United Nations publishes migration data, governments may use it for policy planning.","zh":"如果聯合國發表移民數據，政府可能用它作政策規劃。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a major global institution.","zh":"這個片語指一個主要全球機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"International Organisation for Migration","meaning":"國際移民組織","examples":[{"en":"The International Organisation for Migration estimates the number of people living outside their countries of origin.","zh":"國際移民組織估算居於原籍國以外的人數。"},{"en":"The International Organisation for Migration is an organisation that studies and supports migration issues.","zh":"International Organisation for Migration 指研究並支援移民議題的組織。"},{"en":"A government may consult the International Organisation for Migration when planning support for migrant workers.","zh":"政府規劃移民工人支援時，可能諮詢國際移民組織。"},{"en":"Migration data from international organisations can help show the scale of movement across borders.","zh":"國際組織提供的移民數據可以幫助顯示跨境流動的規模。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specialist organisation focused on migration.","zh":"這個片語指出專注移民的專門組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"indicate that","meaning":"顯示","examples":[{"en":"Current estimates indicate that millions of people live outside their countries of origin.","zh":"目前估算顯示，數以百萬計的人居於其原籍國以外。"},{"en":"Indicate that means show, suggest, or point to a fact or conclusion.","zh":"indicate that 指顯示、表明或指向某事實或結論。"},{"en":"Dark clouds may indicate that heavy rain is coming.","zh":"烏雲可能顯示大雨快將來臨。"},{"en":"If survey results indicate that students are stressed, schools may need to adjust workloads.","zh":"如果調查結果顯示學生有壓力，學校可能需要調整功課量。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence-based information.","zh":"這個片語引出有證據支持的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"some 150 million people","meaning":"約1.5億人","examples":[{"en":"Some 150 million people live temporarily or permanently outside their countries of origin.","zh":"約1.5億人暫時或永久居於其原籍國以外。"},{"en":"Some 150 million people means approximately 150 million people.","zh":"some 150 million people 指約一億五千萬人。"},{"en":"If some 500 students attend a school, the exact number may be slightly higher or lower.","zh":"如果約500名學生就讀某校，實際人數可能稍多或稍少。"},{"en":"Large approximate numbers help readers understand the scale of migration quickly.","zh":"大型約數幫助讀者快速理解移民規模。"},{"en":"The word “some” before a number signals approximation.","zh":"數字前的 some 表示約略。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"temporarily or permanently","meaning":"暫時或永久地","examples":[{"en":"Many migrants live temporarily or permanently outside their original countries.","zh":"許多移民暫時或永久居於其原本國家以外。"},{"en":"Temporarily or permanently means for a short or limited time, or forever or for a very long time.","zh":"temporarily or permanently 指短期或有限時間，或永遠／非常長期地。"},{"en":"A worker may move abroad temporarily for a contract or permanently after settling with family.","zh":"工人可能因合約暫時移居海外，或因與家庭定居而永久移居。"},{"en":"If migration is temporary, people may return home; if permanent, they may build a new life elsewhere.","zh":"如果移民是暫時的，人們可能回國；如果是永久的，則可能在別處建立新生活。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts short-term and long-term residence.","zh":"這個片語對比短期和長期居住。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"outside their countries of origin","meaning":"在其原籍國以外","examples":[{"en":"Millions of people live outside their countries of origin.","zh":"數以百萬計的人居於其原籍國以外。"},{"en":"Outside their countries of origin means not living in the countries where they originally come from.","zh":"outside their countries of origin 指不住在自己原本來自的國家。"},{"en":"University students may study outside their countries of origin for several years.","zh":"大學生可能在其原籍國以外讀書數年。"},{"en":"If people live outside their countries of origin, they may need visas, work permits, or protection.","zh":"如果人們居於其原籍國以外，可能需要簽證、工作許可或保護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes residence away from one’s original country.","zh":"這個片語描述離開原籍國居住。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"country of origin","meaning":"原籍國","examples":[{"en":"A migrant’s country of origin is the country he or she originally comes from.","zh":"移民的原籍國是他或她原本來自的國家。"},{"en":"Country of origin means the country where a person, product, or group originally comes from.","zh":"country of origin 指某人、產品或群體原本來自的國家。"},{"en":"A school form may ask a new student for their country of origin.","zh":"學校表格可能要求新生填寫其原籍國。"},{"en":"If a refugee cannot safely return to the country of origin, another country may offer protection.","zh":"如果難民無法安全返回原籍國，另一國可能提供保護。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies original national background.","zh":"這個片語指出原本的國家背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"of these","meaning":"在這些人當中","examples":[{"en":"Of these, an estimated 80–97 million are migrant workers and members of their families.","zh":"在這些人當中，估計有8,000萬至9,700萬人是移民工人及其家庭成員。"},{"en":"Of these means among the people or things just mentioned.","zh":"of these 指在剛才提到的人或事物當中。"},{"en":"A school has 300 students; of these, 40 take the bus every day.","zh":"一所學校有300名學生；在這些學生當中，40人每天乘巴士。"},{"en":"The phrase helps break a large number into smaller groups.","zh":"這個片語有助把大數字分成較小群體。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining statistics clearly.","zh":"它在清楚解釋統計資料時很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an estimated","meaning":"估計","examples":[{"en":"An estimated 80–97 million people are migrant workers and family members.","zh":"估計有8,000萬至9,700萬人是移民工人和家庭成員。"},{"en":"An estimated means the number is approximate, based on calculation or available data.","zh":"an estimated 指數字是根據計算或現有資料得出的約數。"},{"en":"An estimated 2,000 people attended the community event.","zh":"估計有2,000人參加社區活動。"},{"en":"If exact records are incomplete, reports often use estimated figures.","zh":"如果準確記錄不完整，報告通常使用估算數字。"},{"en":"The phrase tells readers not to treat the number as exact.","zh":"這個片語提醒讀者不要把數字視為精確數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"members of their families","meaning":"其家庭成員","examples":[{"en":"Migrant workers and members of their families make up a large migrant group.","zh":"移民工人及其家庭成員構成大型移民群體。"},{"en":"Members of their families means relatives such as spouses, children, parents, or dependants.","zh":"members of their families 指配偶、子女、父母或受供養親屬等家人。"},{"en":"A worker moving abroad may bring members of their family if the visa allows it.","zh":"如果簽證容許，移居海外工作的工人可能帶同家庭成員。"},{"en":"If migrant workers’ family members also move, schools and health services may need extra planning.","zh":"如果移民工人的家庭成員也遷移，學校和醫療服務可能需要額外規劃。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that migration affects whole families, not only workers.","zh":"這個片語顯示移民影響整個家庭，而不只是工人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"refugees outside their countries of origin","meaning":"身處原籍國以外的難民","examples":[{"en":"Another 12 million are refugees outside their countries of origin.","zh":"另有1,200萬人是身處原籍國以外的難民。"},{"en":"Refugees outside their countries of origin are people forced to seek safety beyond the country they came from.","zh":"refugees outside their countries of origin 指被迫到原籍國以外尋求安全的人。"},{"en":"Refugees outside their countries of origin may need legal protection, housing, and medical care.","zh":"身處原籍國以外的難民可能需要法律保護、住屋和醫療照顧。"},{"en":"If danger continues at home, refugees may be unable to return safely.","zh":"如果家鄉危險仍然持續，難民可能無法安全返回。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses displacement across national borders.","zh":"這個片語強調跨越國界的流離失所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"these figures do not include","meaning":"這些數字並不包括","examples":[{"en":"These figures do not include internally displaced persons.","zh":"這些數字並不包括境內流離失所者。"},{"en":"These figures do not include means the numbers leave out a particular group or category.","zh":"these figures do not include 指這些數字排除了某一群體或類別。"},{"en":"A school report may say exam results do not include absent students.","zh":"學校報告可能說考試結果並不包括缺席學生。"},{"en":"If figures exclude some groups, the real scale of the problem may be larger.","zh":"如果數字排除某些群體，問題的真實規模可能更大。"},{"en":"The phrase warns readers about the limits of statistics.","zh":"這個片語提醒讀者統計數字的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"internally displaced persons","meaning":"境內流離失所者","examples":[{"en":"Internally displaced persons are forced to move within their own country.","zh":"境內流離失所者被迫在自己國家境內遷移。"},{"en":"Internally displaced persons are people who flee their homes but do not cross an international border.","zh":"internally displaced persons 指逃離家園但沒有跨越國際邊界的人。"},{"en":"A family escaping violence may become internally displaced if they move to another province in the same country.","zh":"逃避暴力的家庭如果搬到同一國家的另一省，就可能成為境內流離失所者。"},{"en":"Because they remain inside their country, internally displaced persons may be less visible internationally.","zh":"因為他們仍留在國內，境內流離失所者在國際上可能較不顯眼。"},{"en":"The phrase differs from refugees, who cross borders.","zh":"這個片語不同於跨越邊界的難民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"forcibly displaced","meaning":"被迫流離失所","examples":[{"en":"Millions of people are forcibly displaced within their own country.","zh":"數以百萬計的人在自己國家境內被迫流離失所。"},{"en":"Forcibly displaced means forced to leave home because of danger, conflict, disaster, or pressure.","zh":"forcibly displaced 指因危險、衝突、災害或壓力而被迫離家。"},{"en":"Families may be forcibly displaced when fighting reaches their village.","zh":"當戰鬥蔓延到村莊，家庭可能被迫流離失所。"},{"en":"Forced displacement can break education, work, family life, and community ties.","zh":"被迫遷移可以中斷教育、工作、家庭生活和社區連繫。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that people did not move by free choice.","zh":"這個片語強調人們並非自由選擇遷移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"within their own country","meaning":"在自己國家境內","examples":[{"en":"Internally displaced persons are displaced within their own country.","zh":"境內流離失所者在自己國家境內流離失所。"},{"en":"Within their own country means inside the borders of the country they belong to or live in.","zh":"within their own country 指在自己所屬或居住國家的邊界之內。"},{"en":"A worker may move within their own country from a small town to a capital city.","zh":"工人可能在自己國家境內由小鎮搬到首都。"},{"en":"If people move within their own country, they may still face hardship without becoming international migrants.","zh":"如果人們在自己國家境內遷移，仍可能面對困難，但不會成為國際移民。"},{"en":"The phrase describes internal movement rather than cross-border migration.","zh":"這個片語描述內部移動，而不是跨境移民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"tens of millions of","meaning":"數以千萬計的……","examples":[{"en":"The figures do not include tens of millions of additional internal migrants.","zh":"這些數字並不包括數以千萬計的額外內部移民。"},{"en":"Tens of millions of means many millions, usually at least twenty million or more.","zh":"tens of millions of 指許多百萬，通常至少二千萬或以上。"},{"en":"Tens of millions of people may use public transport in a large country every day.","zh":"在大國中，每天可能有數以千萬計的人使用公共交通。"},{"en":"A number this large shows that internal migration is a major social reality.","zh":"如此龐大的數字顯示內部移民是重大的社會現實。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses very large scale without giving an exact figure.","zh":"這個片語強調非常大的規模，而不給出精確數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"internal migrants","meaning":"內部移民","examples":[{"en":"Internal migrants move from one area of a country to another.","zh":"內部移民從一個國家的一個地區遷往另一個地區。"},{"en":"Internal migrants are people who relocate within the same country, often for work, study, or safety.","zh":"internal migrants 指在同一國家境內遷居的人，通常為工作、學習或安全。"},{"en":"A young person who moves from a rural village to a city for work is an internal migrant.","zh":"從農村遷往城市工作的年輕人就是內部移民。"},{"en":"Internal migration can increase pressure on housing, schools, and transport in cities.","zh":"內部移民可以增加城市住屋、學校和交通壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement inside a country’s borders.","zh":"這個片語描述國界內部的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rural to urban","meaning":"由農村遷往城市","examples":[{"en":"Many internal migrants move mainly from rural to urban areas.","zh":"許多內部移民主要由農村遷往城市地區。"},{"en":"Rural to urban means from the countryside to towns or cities.","zh":"rural to urban 指從鄉郊前往城鎮或城市。"},{"en":"A student may move from a rural to an urban area to attend university.","zh":"學生可能由農村遷往城市地區讀大學。"},{"en":"Rural-to-urban migration can happen when city jobs pay more than farm work.","zh":"當城市工作比農務收入高時，農村到城市遷移可能發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common direction of internal migration.","zh":"這個片語描述內部移民的常見方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"around the world","meaning":"世界各地","examples":[{"en":"Internal migration occurs in countries around the world.","zh":"內部移民發生在世界各地的國家。"},{"en":"Around the world means in many countries or regions globally.","zh":"around the world 指在全球許多國家或地區。"},{"en":"Students around the world use mobile phones for learning and communication.","zh":"世界各地的學生使用手機學習和溝通。"},{"en":"If a problem happens around the world, it is not limited to one country.","zh":"如果一個問題發生在世界各地，它就不限於某一國家。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a global scope.","zh":"這個片語給出全球範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ethnic and racial diversity","meaning":"族裔和種族多元性","examples":[{"en":"Migration increases the ethnic and racial diversity of societies.","zh":"移民增加社會的族裔和種族多元性。"},{"en":"Ethnic and racial diversity means the presence of people from different ethnic groups and racial backgrounds.","zh":"ethnic and racial diversity 指社會中存在來自不同族裔群體和種族背景的人。"},{"en":"A classroom with students from many backgrounds has ethnic and racial diversity.","zh":"一個有許多背景學生的課室具有族裔和種族多元性。"},{"en":"Diversity can enrich society, but it also requires fair rules and mutual respect.","zh":"多元性可以豐富社會，但也需要公平規則和互相尊重。"},{"en":"The phrase describes social variety in ancestry, culture, and race.","zh":"這個片語描述祖源、文化和種族上的社會多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"inevitable consequence of","meaning":"……的必然結果","examples":[{"en":"The increasing diversity of societies is an inevitable consequence of migration.","zh":"社會日益多元是移民的必然結果。"},{"en":"An inevitable consequence of something is a result that naturally or unavoidably follows from it.","zh":"inevitable consequence of something 指自然或不可避免地由某事帶來的結果。"},{"en":"More homework may be an inevitable consequence of choosing an exam-heavy course.","zh":"選擇考試繁重的課程，更多功課可能是必然結果。"},{"en":"If people move across borders, societies will naturally become more diverse.","zh":"如果人們跨越邊界流動，社會自然會變得更為多元。"},{"en":"The phrase links an action with a result that is hard to avoid.","zh":"這個片語把行動與難以避免的結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"increasing migration","meaning":"日益增加的移民","examples":[{"en":"Increasing migration has made many states more multi-ethnic.","zh":"日益增加的移民令許多國家變得更多族裔。"},{"en":"Increasing migration means a rising movement of people between places or countries.","zh":"increasing migration 指人們在地方或國家之間的流動不斷增加。"},{"en":"A city may need more translation services because of increasing migration.","zh":"城市可能因日益增加的移民而需要更多翻譯服務。"},{"en":"Increasing migration can change labour markets, schools, neighbourhoods, and public services.","zh":"日益增加的移民可以改變勞動市場、學校、社區和公共服務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes migration growing in scale.","zh":"這個片語描述移民規模上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a growing number of","meaning":"越來越多的……","examples":[{"en":"A growing number of states are becoming more multi-ethnic.","zh":"越來越多國家正變得更多族裔。"},{"en":"A growing number of means more and more over time.","zh":"a growing number of 指隨時間越來越多。"},{"en":"A growing number of students use online notes before exams.","zh":"越來越多學生在考試前使用網上筆記。"},{"en":"If a growing number of countries face migration pressures, the issue becomes global.","zh":"如果越來越多國家面對移民壓力，該議題就變成全球性問題。"},{"en":"The phrase shows an increasing trend.","zh":"這個片語顯示上升趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"multi-ethnic","meaning":"多族裔的","examples":[{"en":"Many states have become or are becoming multi-ethnic.","zh":"許多國家已經或正在變成多族裔社會。"},{"en":"Multi-ethnic means made up of people from several different ethnic groups.","zh":"multi-ethnic 指由幾個不同族裔群體的人組成。"},{"en":"A multi-ethnic school may celebrate several languages, festivals, and food traditions.","zh":"多族裔學校可能慶祝幾種語言、節日和飲食傳統。"},{"en":"Multi-ethnic societies need laws and habits that protect equality and respect.","zh":"多族裔社會需要保護平等和尊重的法律及習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes diversity within a community or country.","zh":"這個片語描述社區或國家內部的多元性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be confronted with","meaning":"面對……","examples":[{"en":"Many states are confronted with the challenge of accommodating different groups.","zh":"許多國家面對容納不同群體的挑戰。"},{"en":"Be confronted with means face a difficult situation or problem directly.","zh":"be confronted with 指直接面對困難情況或問題。"},{"en":"A school may be confronted with overcrowding when many new families move into the area.","zh":"當大量新家庭搬入區內，學校可能面對過度擠迫問題。"},{"en":"If governments are confronted with diversity, they must decide how to manage it fairly.","zh":"如果政府面對多元性，就必須決定如何公平管理。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a serious issue that cannot be ignored.","zh":"這個片語暗示不能忽視的嚴重問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the challenge of","meaning":"……的挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Governments face the challenge of accommodating people of different cultures and races.","zh":"政府面對容納不同文化和種族人士的挑戰。"},{"en":"The challenge of something means the difficulty involved in doing or managing it.","zh":"the challenge of something 指做某事或管理某事所涉及的困難。"},{"en":"Teachers face the challenge of helping students with very different English levels.","zh":"老師面對幫助英文程度很不同學生的挑戰。"},{"en":"If a society becomes more diverse, the challenge of fairness becomes more urgent.","zh":"如果社會變得更多元，公平的挑戰就更迫切。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a difficult task.","zh":"這個片語引出困難任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"accommodating people of different cultures","meaning":"容納不同文化背景的人","examples":[{"en":"States must accommodate people of different cultures, races, religions and languages.","zh":"國家必須容納不同文化、種族、宗教和語言的人。"},{"en":"Accommodating people of different cultures means making space for people with different customs and ways of life.","zh":"accommodating people of different cultures 指為有不同習俗和生活方式的人提供空間。"},{"en":"A school accommodates different cultures by respecting food rules, languages, and festivals.","zh":"學校透過尊重飲食規則、語言和節日來容納不同文化。"},{"en":"If a society fails to accommodate cultural differences, tension and exclusion may grow.","zh":"如果社會未能容納文化差異，緊張和排斥可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical inclusion, not only polite words.","zh":"這個片語描述實際包容，而不只是禮貌言語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"different cultures, races, religions and languages","meaning":"不同文化、種族、宗教和語言","examples":[{"en":"Migration brings together people of different cultures, races, religions and languages.","zh":"移民使不同文化、種族、宗教和語言的人聚在一起。"},{"en":"Different cultures, races, religions and languages means diverse backgrounds in identity, belief, appearance, and communication.","zh":"different cultures, races, religions and languages 指身份、信仰、外貌和溝通方式上的多元背景。"},{"en":"A hospital may serve patients of different cultures, races, religions and languages every day.","zh":"醫院每天可能服務不同文化、種族、宗教和語言的病人。"},{"en":"Such diversity can enrich society, but it also requires respectful communication.","zh":"這種多元性可以豐富社會，但也需要尊重地溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase lists major forms of human difference.","zh":"這個片語列出人類差異的主要形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"addressing the reality of","meaning":"處理……的現實","examples":[{"en":"Addressing the reality of increased diversity requires effective social mechanisms.","zh":"處理多元性增加的現實需要有效社會機制。"},{"en":"Addressing the reality of something means dealing honestly and practically with a situation that already exists.","zh":"addressing the reality of something 指誠實而實際地處理已存在的情況。"},{"en":"Schools must address the reality of students using phones rather than pretending phones do not exist.","zh":"學校必須處理學生使用手機的現實，而不是假裝手機不存在。"},{"en":"If governments address diversity seriously, they create laws and services that match real social needs.","zh":"如果政府認真處理多元性，就會制定配合真實社會需要的法律和服務。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses practical response to facts.","zh":"這個片語強調對事實作出實際回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"increased diversity","meaning":"日益增加的多元性","examples":[{"en":"Increased diversity requires political, legal, social and economic responses.","zh":"日益增加的多元性需要政治、法律、社會和經濟回應。"},{"en":"Increased diversity means a society contains a wider range of groups, identities, or backgrounds than before.","zh":"increased diversity 指社會比以前包含更廣泛的群體、身份或背景。"},{"en":"A school with increased diversity may need more language support and cultural understanding.","zh":"多元性增加的學校可能需要更多語言支援和文化理解。"},{"en":"Increased diversity can create opportunity, but poor management can create tension.","zh":"日益增加的多元性可以帶來機會，但管理不善可以造成緊張。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a rise in social variety.","zh":"這個片語描述社會多樣性上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"political, legal, social and economic mechanisms","meaning":"政治、法律、社會和經濟機制","examples":[{"en":"Societies need political, legal, social and economic mechanisms to manage diversity.","zh":"社會需要政治、法律、社會和經濟機制來管理多元性。"},{"en":"Political, legal, social and economic mechanisms are systems, rules, and institutions used to manage society.","zh":"political, legal, social and economic mechanisms 指用來管理社會的制度、規則和機構。"},{"en":"Anti-discrimination laws, language services, job protections, and community programmes are examples of such mechanisms.","zh":"反歧視法、語言服務、工作保障和社區計劃都是這類機制的例子。"},{"en":"Without these mechanisms, diversity may be left unmanaged and conflict may grow.","zh":"如果沒有這些機制，多元性可能無人管理，衝突可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical tools for social organisation.","zh":"這個片語指社會組織的實際工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ensure mutual respect","meaning":"確保互相尊重","examples":[{"en":"Effective mechanisms are needed to ensure mutual respect.","zh":"需要有效機制來確保互相尊重。"},{"en":"Ensure mutual respect means make sure different people treat one another with dignity and fairness.","zh":"ensure mutual respect 指確保不同的人以尊嚴和公平對待彼此。"},{"en":"Classroom rules can ensure mutual respect during debates on sensitive topics.","zh":"課室規則可以確保學生在敏感議題辯論中互相尊重。"},{"en":"If people feel respected, they are less likely to treat difference as a threat.","zh":"如果人們感到被尊重，就較不容易把差異視為威脅。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating conditions for fair relationships.","zh":"這個片語描述創造公平關係的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mediate relations across differences","meaning":"調解差異之間的關係","examples":[{"en":"Governments need mechanisms to mediate relations across differences.","zh":"政府需要機制來調解差異之間的關係。"},{"en":"Mediate relations across differences means help people from different backgrounds manage disagreement and live together fairly.","zh":"mediate relations across differences 指幫助不同背景的人處理分歧並公平共處。"},{"en":"A school counsellor may mediate relations between students from different groups after an argument.","zh":"學生爭執後，學校輔導員可能調解不同群體學生之間的關係。"},{"en":"If no one helps groups communicate, small misunderstandings can become larger conflicts.","zh":"如果沒有人幫助群體溝通，小誤會可能變成較大衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on managing relationships across social difference.","zh":"這個片語集中於管理跨越社會差異的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"become evident in","meaning":"在……中變得明顯","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobia and racism have become evident in some societies.","zh":"仇外心理和種族主義在一些社會中變得明顯。"},{"en":"Become evident in means become clear or noticeable in a particular place or situation.","zh":"become evident in 指在某地方或情況中變得清楚或可察覺。"},{"en":"Stress may become evident in students when exams are close.","zh":"考試臨近時，壓力可能在學生身上變得明顯。"},{"en":"If racism becomes evident in housing or hiring, authorities should investigate it.","zh":"如果種族主義在住屋或招聘中變得明顯，當局應調查。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something hidden becoming visible.","zh":"這個片語描述隱藏的事情變得可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"substantial numbers of","meaning":"大量的……","examples":[{"en":"Some countries have received substantial numbers of immigrants.","zh":"有些國家接收了大量移民。"},{"en":"Substantial numbers of means large enough numbers to be important or noticeable.","zh":"substantial numbers of 指數量大到重要或明顯。"},{"en":"A school may need more teachers if it receives substantial numbers of new students.","zh":"如果學校接收大量新學生，可能需要更多老師。"},{"en":"When a country receives many newcomers, public services may need adjustment.","zh":"當國家接收大量新來者，公共服務可能需要調整。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a significant quantity, not just a few.","zh":"這個片語暗示數量顯著，而不只是少數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"asylum-seekers","meaning":"尋求庇護者","examples":[{"en":"Some immigrants arrive as workers or as asylum-seekers.","zh":"有些移民以工人或尋求庇護者身份抵達。"},{"en":"Asylum-seekers are people who ask another country for protection from danger or persecution.","zh":"asylum-seekers 指向另一國請求保護以逃避危險或迫害的人。"},{"en":"Asylum-seekers may need interpreters when explaining why they cannot return home.","zh":"尋求庇護者解釋自己為何不能回家時，可能需要傳譯員。"},{"en":"If their applications are accepted, asylum-seekers may be recognised as refugees.","zh":"如果申請獲接納，尋求庇護者可能被承認為難民。"},{"en":"The phrase describes people requesting safety under law.","zh":"這個片語描述依法請求安全的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"become the targets in","meaning":"成為……中的目標","examples":[{"en":"Migrants have become the targets in internal disputes about national identity.","zh":"移民已成為關於國家身份內部爭議中的目標。"},{"en":"Become the targets in means become the people blamed, attacked, or focused on in a conflict.","zh":"become the targets in 指在衝突中成為被責怪、攻擊或集中針對的人。"},{"en":"New students may become the targets in class arguments if others unfairly blame them for change.","zh":"如果其他人不公平地把改變怪罪於新同學，新同學可能成為班中爭執的目標。"},{"en":"When society argues about identity, outsiders may be blamed for deeper problems.","zh":"當社會就身份爭論，外來者可能被責怪為深層問題的原因。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being made the object of hostility or blame.","zh":"這個片語描述成為敵意或責怪的對象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"internal disputes","meaning":"內部爭議","examples":[{"en":"Migrants may become targets in internal disputes about national identity.","zh":"移民可能成為關於國家身份內部爭議中的目標。"},{"en":"Internal disputes are disagreements within a country, group, organisation, or community.","zh":"internal disputes 指國家、群體、組織或社區內部的分歧。"},{"en":"A school may have internal disputes over homework policy or class allocation.","zh":"學校可能就功課政策或分班安排出現內部爭議。"},{"en":"If internal disputes are unresolved, leaders may blame outsiders to avoid deeper discussion.","zh":"如果內部爭議未解決，領袖可能責怪外來者以逃避深層討論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes conflict inside a group, not between separate outsiders.","zh":"這個片語描述群體內部衝突，而不是與外部者之間的衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"national identity","meaning":"國家身份認同","examples":[{"en":"Migration can become part of disputes about national identity.","zh":"移民可以成為國家身份認同爭議的一部分。"},{"en":"National identity is how people understand what their nation is and who belongs to it.","zh":"national identity 指人們如何理解自己的國家是甚麼，以及誰屬於它。"},{"en":"Flags, language, history lessons, and public holidays can shape national identity.","zh":"旗幟、語言、歷史課和公眾假日可以塑造國家身份認同。"},{"en":"If immigration changes a society, people may argue over whether national identity should change too.","zh":"如果移民改變社會，人們可能爭論國家身份認同是否也應改變。"},{"en":"The phrase connects belonging, culture, history, and citizenship.","zh":"這個片語連結歸屬、文化、歷史和公民身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in the last few decades","meaning":"在過去數十年","examples":[{"en":"In the last few decades, new nation states have often emerged.","zh":"在過去數十年，新民族國家經常出現。"},{"en":"In the last few decades means during the most recent several tens of years.","zh":"in the last few decades 指在最近幾個十年期間。"},{"en":"In the last few decades, mobile phones have changed communication and daily life.","zh":"在過去數十年，手機改變了溝通和日常生活。"},{"en":"If a change happens over several decades, it may affect more than one generation.","zh":"如果變化跨越數十年，它可能影響不止一代人。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a recent historical time frame.","zh":"這個片語給出近代歷史時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the emergence of","meaning":"……的出現","examples":[{"en":"The emergence of new nation states has often been accompanied by ethnic exclusion.","zh":"新民族國家的出現往往伴隨族裔排斥。"},{"en":"The emergence of means the appearance or development of something new.","zh":"the emergence of 指某新事物的出現或發展。"},{"en":"The emergence of online learning changed how students attend lessons.","zh":"網上學習的出現改變了學生上課方式。"},{"en":"When new states emerge, questions about citizenship and belonging may become intense.","zh":"當新國家出現，關於公民身份和歸屬的問題可能變得強烈。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something coming into existence or becoming important.","zh":"這個片語描述某事出現或變得重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"new nation states","meaning":"新民族國家","examples":[{"en":"The emergence of new nation states has sometimes led to ethnic exclusion.","zh":"新民族國家的出現有時導致族裔排斥。"},{"en":"New nation states are newly formed countries that define themselves as nations.","zh":"new nation states 指新成立並以民族身份界定自己的國家。"},{"en":"A new nation state may need a flag, constitution, schools, and official language policy.","zh":"新民族國家可能需要國旗、憲法、學校和官方語言政策。"},{"en":"If a new state defines belonging narrowly, some ethnic groups may be excluded.","zh":"如果新國家狹窄地界定歸屬，有些族裔群體可能被排除。"},{"en":"The phrase links political independence with national identity.","zh":"這個片語把政治獨立與國家身份連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be accompanied by","meaning":"伴隨着……","examples":[{"en":"The emergence of new nation states has often been accompanied by ethnic exclusion.","zh":"新民族國家的出現往往伴隨着族裔排斥。"},{"en":"Be accompanied by means happen together with something else.","zh":"be accompanied by 指與另一件事同時發生。"},{"en":"A new school policy may be accompanied by extra training for teachers.","zh":"新學校政策可能伴隨額外教師培訓。"},{"en":"If political change is accompanied by exclusion, some groups may lose rights or recognition.","zh":"如果政治變化伴隨排斥，有些群體可能失去權利或承認。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that two events occur together.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩件事同時出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ethnic exclusion","meaning":"族裔排斥","examples":[{"en":"Ethnic exclusion has accompanied the emergence of some new nation states.","zh":"族裔排斥伴隨着一些新民族國家的出現。"},{"en":"Ethnic exclusion means keeping people out of rights, services, or belonging because of their ethnic identity.","zh":"ethnic exclusion 指因族裔身份而把人排除於權利、服務或歸屬之外。"},{"en":"A school would practise ethnic exclusion if it refused students from one ethnic group.","zh":"如果學校拒收某一族裔群體的學生，就是實行族裔排斥。"},{"en":"Ethnic exclusion can create resentment, fear, and long-term social division.","zh":"族裔排斥可以造成怨恨、恐懼和長期社會分裂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes exclusion based on ethnicity.","zh":"這個片語描述基於族裔的排除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"grapple with","meaning":"努力應對……","examples":[{"en":"Governments grapple with the new realities of their multi-ethnic societies.","zh":"政府努力應對多族裔社會的新現實。"},{"en":"Grapple with means struggle to deal with a difficult problem.","zh":"grapple with 指努力處理困難問題。"},{"en":"Teachers may grapple with how to help a class where students have very different English levels.","zh":"老師可能努力應對如何幫助英文程度很不同的班級。"},{"en":"If governments grapple poorly with diversity, discrimination may worsen.","zh":"如果政府未能好好應對多元性，歧視可能惡化。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests serious effort, not an easy solution.","zh":"這個片語暗示認真努力，而不是容易解決。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"new realities","meaning":"新現實","examples":[{"en":"Governments must grapple with the new realities of multi-ethnic societies.","zh":"政府必須努力應對多族裔社會的新現實。"},{"en":"New realities are changed conditions that people must now accept and manage.","zh":"new realities 指人們現在必須接受和管理的已改變情況。"},{"en":"Online learning created new realities for teachers, students, and parents.","zh":"網上學習為老師、學生和家長創造了新現實。"},{"en":"If migration changes neighbourhoods, public services must respond to those new realities.","zh":"如果移民改變社區，公共服務必須回應那些新現實。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changed social facts.","zh":"這個片語描述已改變的社會事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a marked increase in","meaning":"……的明顯增加","examples":[{"en":"There has been a marked increase in discrimination and violence against migrants.","zh":"針對移民的歧視和暴力出現明顯增加。"},{"en":"A marked increase in means a clear and noticeable rise in something.","zh":"a marked increase in 指某事清楚而明顯地上升。"},{"en":"A school may see a marked increase in absences during flu season.","zh":"流感季節期間，學校可能見到缺席人數明顯增加。"},{"en":"If reports of abuse rise sharply, authorities should investigate the causes.","zh":"如果虐待報告急劇上升，當局應調查原因。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a rise that is too obvious to ignore.","zh":"這個片語描述明顯到不能忽視的上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"discrimination and violence","meaning":"歧視和暴力","examples":[{"en":"Discrimination and violence are often directed against migrants and refugees.","zh":"歧視和暴力常針對移民和難民。"},{"en":"Discrimination and violence mean unfair treatment and physical or verbal harm.","zh":"discrimination and violence 指不公平對待以及身體或言語傷害。"},{"en":"A worker may face discrimination and violence if colleagues insult or attack them because of origin.","zh":"如果同事因出身侮辱或攻擊某工人，該工人可能面對歧視和暴力。"},{"en":"Discrimination can create exclusion, while violence creates direct fear and danger.","zh":"歧視可以造成排斥，而暴力造成直接恐懼和危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both unfair systems and harmful actions.","zh":"這個片語描述不公平制度和有害行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be directed against","meaning":"針對……","examples":[{"en":"Violence is sometimes directed against migrants, refugees and other non-nationals.","zh":"暴力有時針對移民、難民和其他非本國公民。"},{"en":"Be directed against means be aimed at or targeted at a person or group.","zh":"be directed against 指以某人或某群體為目標。"},{"en":"Online abuse may be directed against a student because of their accent.","zh":"網絡辱罵可能因學生口音而針對他。"},{"en":"If anger is directed against outsiders, deeper social problems may remain unsolved.","zh":"如果憤怒針對外來者，深層社會問題可能仍未解決。"},{"en":"The phrase describes who receives hostility or attack.","zh":"這個片語描述敵意或攻擊的承受者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"other non-nationals","meaning":"其他非本國公民","examples":[{"en":"Other non-nationals may also face discrimination and violence.","zh":"其他非本國公民也可能面對歧視和暴力。"},{"en":"Other non-nationals are people living in a country who are not citizens of that country.","zh":"other non-nationals 指居於某國但不是該國公民的人。"},{"en":"Foreign students, temporary workers, and visitors may be considered non-nationals.","zh":"外國學生、臨時工人和訪客都可能被視為非本國公民。"},{"en":"If non-nationals lack political rights, they may find it harder to defend themselves.","zh":"如果非本國公民缺乏政治權利，他們可能較難保護自己。"},{"en":"The phrase includes foreigners beyond migrants and refugees.","zh":"這個片語包括移民和難民以外的外國人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"extremist groups","meaning":"極端組織","examples":[{"en":"Extremist groups have attacked migrants and refugees in many parts of the world.","zh":"極端組織在世界許多地區攻擊移民和難民。"},{"en":"Extremist groups are groups with extreme political or social beliefs that may support hatred or violence.","zh":"extremist groups 指持有極端政治或社會信念，可能支持仇恨或暴力的組織。"},{"en":"Police may monitor extremist groups if they threaten minority communities.","zh":"如果極端組織威脅少數族裔社區，警方可能監察它們。"},{"en":"When fear of outsiders spreads, extremist groups may exploit it to gain support.","zh":"當對外來者的恐懼擴散，極端組織可能利用它來獲得支持。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised groups far outside moderate views.","zh":"這個片語描述遠離溫和觀點的有組織群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in many parts of the world","meaning":"在世界許多地區","examples":[{"en":"Discrimination against migrants occurs in many parts of the world.","zh":"針對移民的歧視發生在世界許多地區。"},{"en":"In many parts of the world means in many different regions or countries globally.","zh":"in many parts of the world 指在全球許多不同地區或國家。"},{"en":"In many parts of the world, schools now teach students to use digital tools.","zh":"在世界許多地區，學校現在教學生使用數碼工具。"},{"en":"If a problem appears in many regions, it needs international attention, not only local action.","zh":"如果問題出現在許多地區，就需要國際關注，而不只是本地行動。"},{"en":"The phrase broadens the issue beyond one place.","zh":"這個片語把議題擴展到不止一個地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"systematic documentation","meaning":"系統性記錄","examples":[{"en":"The lack of systematic documentation makes the scale of abuse unclear.","zh":"缺乏系統性記錄令虐待規模不清楚。"},{"en":"Systematic documentation means organised, regular recording of facts and cases.","zh":"systematic documentation 指有組織而定期地記錄事實和個案。"},{"en":"A school needs systematic documentation of bullying reports to see whether the problem is growing.","zh":"學校需要對欺凌報告作系統性記錄，才能判斷問題是否惡化。"},{"en":"Without systematic documentation, serious problems may remain hidden or underestimated.","zh":"沒有系統性記錄，嚴重問題可能仍然隱藏或被低估。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses careful record-keeping.","zh":"這個片語強調仔細保存記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"research over time","meaning":"長期研究","examples":[{"en":"Research over time is needed to measure changes in abuse and reporting.","zh":"需要長期研究來量度虐待和舉報的變化。"},{"en":"Research over time means studying something repeatedly across a period, not only once.","zh":"research over time 指在一段時間中反覆研究某事，而不是只研究一次。"},{"en":"Teachers need research over time to know whether a new method really helps students.","zh":"老師需要長期研究，才知道新方法是否真正幫到學生。"},{"en":"If abuse is measured only once, changes in the problem may be missed.","zh":"如果虐待只量度一次，問題變化可能被錯過。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long-term study.","zh":"這個片語描述長期研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"make it unclear whether","meaning":"令……是否……變得不清楚","examples":[{"en":"The lack of research makes it unclear whether abuse has really increased.","zh":"缺乏研究令虐待是否真的增加變得不清楚。"},{"en":"Make it unclear whether means create uncertainty about whether something is true.","zh":"make it unclear whether 指令某事是否屬實變得不確定。"},{"en":"Missing attendance records make it unclear whether a student was absent often or only once.","zh":"缺少出席紀錄會令學生是經常缺席還是只缺席一次變得不清楚。"},{"en":"If reporting improves, higher numbers may reflect better reporting, not more abuse.","zh":"如果舉報改善，較高數字可能反映舉報較完善，而不是虐待更多。"},{"en":"The phrase shows uncertainty caused by incomplete evidence.","zh":"這個片語顯示由證據不足造成的不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the level of abuse","meaning":"虐待程度","examples":[{"en":"It is unclear whether the level of abuse has increased.","zh":"虐待程度是否增加仍不清楚。"},{"en":"The level of abuse means how much abuse is happening or how serious it is.","zh":"the level of abuse 指虐待發生的多少或嚴重程度。"},{"en":"A school may track the level of bullying by recording complaints each term.","zh":"學校可能透過每學期記錄投訴來追蹤欺凌程度。"},{"en":"If the level of abuse rises, more protection and investigation may be needed.","zh":"如果虐待程度上升，可能需要更多保護和調查。"},{"en":"The phrase measures amount or seriousness of mistreatment.","zh":"這個片語量度不當對待的數量或嚴重性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"exposure and reporting","meaning":"曝光和舉報","examples":[{"en":"Higher exposure and reporting may make abuse appear more common.","zh":"更高的曝光和舉報可能令虐待看起來更常見。"},{"en":"Exposure and reporting means public attention to a problem and formal recording of cases.","zh":"exposure and reporting 指問題受到公眾關注以及個案被正式記錄。"},{"en":"More media exposure and school reporting can make bullying seem newly common, even if it existed before.","zh":"更多媒體曝光和學校舉報可以令欺凌看似新近常見，即使它以前已存在。"},{"en":"If people report abuse more often, recorded numbers may rise.","zh":"如果人們更常舉報虐待，記錄數字可能上升。"},{"en":"The phrase helps explain why statistics can change.","zh":"這個片語有助解釋統計數字為何改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"more than enough","meaning":"綽綽有餘；非常足夠","examples":[{"en":"There is more than enough anecdotal evidence of human rights violations.","zh":"關於侵犯人權的個案證據已經綽綽有餘。"},{"en":"More than enough means more than sufficient for a purpose.","zh":"more than enough 指超過所需，十分足夠。"},{"en":"If a teacher gives five clear examples, that may be more than enough for students to understand the phrase.","zh":"如果老師給出五個清楚例子，可能已非常足夠讓學生理解片語。"},{"en":"More than enough evidence can justify concern even before perfect statistics exist.","zh":"即使尚未有完美統計，足夠多的證據也能支持關注。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses sufficiency and abundance.","zh":"這個片語強調充足和豐富。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"anecdotal evidence","meaning":"軼事證據；個案證據","examples":[{"en":"Anecdotal evidence suggests that many migrants experience abuse.","zh":"軼事證據顯示，許多移民經歷虐待。"},{"en":"Anecdotal evidence is evidence based on individual stories or reported experiences rather than large systematic data.","zh":"anecdotal evidence 指基於個別故事或經驗報告，而不是大型系統數據的證據。"},{"en":"A teacher may hear anecdotal evidence from students that homework is taking too long.","zh":"老師可能從學生口中聽到功課需時太長的個案證據。"},{"en":"Anecdotal evidence can reveal problems, but it may not show their full scale accurately.","zh":"軼事證據可以揭示問題，但未必準確顯示其完整規模。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to case-based evidence.","zh":"這個片語指以個案為基礎的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"violations of human rights","meaning":"侵犯人權","examples":[{"en":"Violations of human rights are a defining feature of international migration today.","zh":"侵犯人權是當今國際移民的界定特徵。"},{"en":"Violations of human rights are actions that deny people basic freedoms, dignity, or protection.","zh":"violations of human rights 指否定人們基本自由、尊嚴或保護的行為。"},{"en":"Denying workers safe housing or legal pay can be a violation of human rights.","zh":"拒絕給工人安全住所或合法工資可以是侵犯人權。"},{"en":"If migrants cannot report abuse safely, human rights violations may continue unnoticed.","zh":"如果移民無法安全舉報虐待，侵犯人權可能持續而不被注意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious breaches of basic human protections.","zh":"這個片語描述對基本人類保障的嚴重違反。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"so generalised, widespread and commonplace that","meaning":"普遍、廣泛和常見到……","examples":[{"en":"These violations are so generalised, widespread and commonplace that they define migration today.","zh":"這些侵犯普遍、廣泛和常見到足以界定當今移民現象。"},{"en":"So generalised, widespread and commonplace that means so common across many places that it becomes a major feature.","zh":"so generalised, widespread and commonplace that 指某事在許多地方都非常常見，以致成為主要特徵。"},{"en":"If exam stress is so widespread and commonplace that every class is affected, schools must respond seriously.","zh":"如果考試壓力普遍而常見到每班都受影響，學校必須認真回應。"},{"en":"When abuse appears everywhere, it cannot be dismissed as a few isolated cases.","zh":"當虐待到處出現，就不能被視為少數孤立個案。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly emphasises scale and frequency.","zh":"這個片語強烈強調規模和頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"generalised","meaning":"普遍的","examples":[{"en":"Human rights violations against migrants are described as generalised.","zh":"針對移民的侵犯人權被描述為普遍的。"},{"en":"Generalised means spread across many cases rather than limited to one small example.","zh":"generalised 指分布於許多個案，而不是限於一個小例子。"},{"en":"A generalised lack of sleep among students means many students are affected, not just one class.","zh":"學生普遍睡眠不足表示許多學生受影響，而不只是一班。"},{"en":"If abuse is generalised, solutions must address the whole system.","zh":"如果虐待是普遍的，解決方案必須處理整個制度。"},{"en":"The word suggests broad presence.","zh":"這個詞暗示廣泛存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"widespread","meaning":"廣泛的","examples":[{"en":"Abuse of migrants is widespread in many societies.","zh":"移民受虐在許多社會中是廣泛的。"},{"en":"Widespread means existing in many places or affecting many people.","zh":"widespread 指存在於許多地方或影響許多人。"},{"en":"If a flu outbreak is widespread, many schools and workplaces may be affected.","zh":"如果流感爆發廣泛，許多學校和工作場所可能受影響。"},{"en":"Widespread discrimination requires public policy, not only individual kindness.","zh":"廣泛歧視需要公共政策，而不只是個人善意。"},{"en":"The word stresses broad distribution.","zh":"這個詞強調分布廣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"commonplace","meaning":"常見的","examples":[{"en":"Discrimination against migrants has become commonplace.","zh":"針對移民的歧視已變得常見。"},{"en":"Commonplace means ordinary, frequent, or no longer unusual.","zh":"commonplace 指普通、頻繁或不再罕見。"},{"en":"Online homework has become commonplace in many schools.","zh":"網上功課在許多學校已變得常見。"},{"en":"If discrimination becomes commonplace, people may stop noticing how serious it is.","zh":"如果歧視變得常見，人們可能停止注意其嚴重性。"},{"en":"The word can describe something sadly normalised.","zh":"這個詞可以描述令人遺憾地被正常化的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a defining feature of","meaning":"……的界定特徵","examples":[{"en":"Human rights violations are a defining feature of international migration today.","zh":"侵犯人權是當今國際移民的界定特徵。"},{"en":"A defining feature of something is a key characteristic that helps identify it.","zh":"defining feature of something 指幫助識別某事的核心特徵。"},{"en":"Clear feedback is a defining feature of good teaching.","zh":"清楚回饋是良好教學的界定特徵。"},{"en":"If abuse is a defining feature of migration, it is central rather than minor.","zh":"如果虐待是移民現象的界定特徵，它就是核心而非次要問題。"},{"en":"The phrase points to what makes something recognisable.","zh":"這個片語指出令某事可被辨認的特點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"international migration","meaning":"國際移民","examples":[{"en":"International migration is often linked with human rights concerns.","zh":"國際移民常與人權關注有關。"},{"en":"International migration means people moving from one country to another to live, work, or seek safety.","zh":"international migration 指人們從一個國家遷往另一個國家生活、工作或尋求安全。"},{"en":"International migration may bring workers to cities that need labour.","zh":"國際移民可能把工人帶到需要勞動力的城市。"},{"en":"If countries manage international migration poorly, migrants may face exploitation or exclusion.","zh":"如果國家管理國際移民不善，移民可能面對剝削或排斥。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement across national borders.","zh":"這個片語描述跨越國界的流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the extent of","meaning":"……的程度","examples":[{"en":"The extent of racial discrimination is often played down.","zh":"種族歧視的程度常被淡化。"},{"en":"The extent of something means how large, serious, or widespread it is.","zh":"the extent of something 指某事的規模、嚴重性或廣泛程度。"},{"en":"A school must understand the extent of bullying before deciding what action to take.","zh":"學校在決定採取甚麼行動前，必須了解欺凌的程度。"},{"en":"If the extent of discrimination is hidden, victims may not receive enough support.","zh":"如果歧視程度被隱藏，受害者可能得不到足夠支援。"},{"en":"The phrase measures scale or seriousness.","zh":"這個片語量度規模或嚴重性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be played down","meaning":"被淡化","examples":[{"en":"The seriousness of xenophobia is often played down by authorities.","zh":"仇外心理的嚴重性常被當局淡化。"},{"en":"Be played down means be made to seem less serious or less important than it really is.","zh":"be played down 指被說成比實際較不嚴重或較不重要。"},{"en":"A company may play down customer complaints to protect its image.","zh":"公司可能淡化顧客投訴以保護形象。"},{"en":"If discrimination is played down, victims may feel that no one believes them.","zh":"如果歧視被淡化，受害者可能覺得沒有人相信他們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes minimising a problem.","zh":"這個片語描述把問題說輕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be denied by authorities","meaning":"被當局否認","examples":[{"en":"The extent of discrimination is sometimes denied by authorities.","zh":"歧視的程度有時被當局否認。"},{"en":"Be denied by authorities means officials say something is not true or not happening.","zh":"be denied by authorities 指官員聲稱某事不是真的或沒有發生。"},{"en":"A pollution problem may be denied by authorities until residents provide strong evidence.","zh":"污染問題可能被當局否認，直到居民提供有力證據。"},{"en":"If discrimination is denied, victims may find it harder to seek justice.","zh":"如果歧視被否認，受害者可能更難尋求公義。"},{"en":"The phrase describes official refusal to accept a problem.","zh":"這個片語描述官方拒絕承認問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be defined in international law as","meaning":"在國際法中被定義為","examples":[{"en":"Racial discrimination is defined in international law as unequal treatment based on race or origin.","zh":"種族歧視在國際法中被定義為基於種族或出身的不平等對待。"},{"en":"Be defined in international law as means be officially described by global legal rules in a particular way.","zh":"be defined in international law as 指根據全球法律規則被正式描述為某種意思。"},{"en":"A crime may be defined in law as an action that harms another person or society.","zh":"罪行在法律中可被定義為傷害他人或社會的行為。"},{"en":"When discrimination is defined in law, victims have clearer grounds to complain.","zh":"當歧視在法律中被定義，受害者就有更清楚的投訴基礎。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an official legal definition.","zh":"這個片語引出正式法律定義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"international law","meaning":"國際法","examples":[{"en":"International law defines racial discrimination in broad terms.","zh":"國際法以廣泛方式定義種族歧視。"},{"en":"International law is the body of rules and agreements that govern relations between countries and protect basic rights.","zh":"international law 指管理國與國關係並保護基本權利的一套規則和協議。"},{"en":"Human rights treaties are part of international law.","zh":"人權條約是國際法的一部分。"},{"en":"If national laws are weak, international law can still provide standards for protection.","zh":"如果國內法律薄弱，國際法仍可提供保護標準。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to law beyond one country.","zh":"這個片語指超越單一國家的法律。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"distinction, exclusion, restriction or preference","meaning":"區別、排斥、限制或偏好","examples":[{"en":"Racial discrimination may involve distinction, exclusion, restriction or preference.","zh":"種族歧視可能涉及區別、排斥、限制或偏好。"},{"en":"Distinction, exclusion, restriction or preference means different forms of unequal treatment or selection.","zh":"distinction, exclusion, restriction or preference 指不同形式的不平等對待或選擇。"},{"en":"A club may discriminate if it excludes people from joining because of ethnic origin.","zh":"如果學會因族裔出身而排除某些人加入，就是歧視。"},{"en":"Restrictions or preferences can limit people’s rights even without open violence.","zh":"限制或偏好即使沒有公開暴力，也可以限制人的權利。"},{"en":"The phrase lists ways discrimination can operate.","zh":"這個片語列出歧視運作的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"基於……","examples":[{"en":"Racial discrimination is based on race, colour, descent or origin.","zh":"種族歧視基於種族、膚色、血統或出身。"},{"en":"Be based on means have something as the reason, foundation, or cause.","zh":"be based on 指以某事作為理由、基礎或原因。"},{"en":"A fair decision should be based on evidence, not rumours.","zh":"公平決定應基於證據，而不是謠言。"},{"en":"If treatment is based on race rather than ability, it becomes discriminatory.","zh":"如果待遇基於種族而不是能力，就變成歧視。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the basis of judgement or action.","zh":"這個片語指出判斷或行動的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"race, colour, descent or origin","meaning":"種族、膚色、血統或出身","examples":[{"en":"International law refers to race, colour, descent or national or ethnic origin.","zh":"國際法提到種族、膚色、血統或國籍／族裔出身。"},{"en":"Race, colour, descent or origin are identity markers sometimes used unfairly to treat people differently.","zh":"race, colour, descent or origin 指有時被不公平用來區別對待人的身份標記。"},{"en":"A housing agent should not reject a tenant because of race, colour, descent or origin.","zh":"地產代理不應因租客的種族、膚色、血統或出身而拒絕他。"},{"en":"When these factors affect access to rights, discrimination may occur.","zh":"當這些因素影響權利享有時，歧視可能出現。"},{"en":"The phrase lists protected identity characteristics.","zh":"這個片語列出受保護的身份特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"national or ethnic origin","meaning":"國籍或族裔出身","examples":[{"en":"Discrimination may be based on national or ethnic origin.","zh":"歧視可能基於國籍或族裔出身。"},{"en":"National or ethnic origin means the country or ethnic group a person comes from or is associated with.","zh":"national or ethnic origin 指某人來自或相關聯的國家或族裔群體。"},{"en":"A person should not be denied a job because of national or ethnic origin.","zh":"一個人不應因國籍或族裔出身而被拒絕工作。"},{"en":"If people are treated as outsiders because of origin, equal rights are weakened.","zh":"如果人們因出身被視為外來者，平等權利就被削弱。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies background linked to nationality or ethnicity.","zh":"這個片語指出與國籍或族裔有關的背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have the purpose or effect of","meaning":"具有……目的或效果","examples":[{"en":"Discrimination may have the purpose or effect of impairing human rights.","zh":"歧視可能具有損害人權的目的或效果。"},{"en":"Have the purpose or effect of means either intend to do something or produce that result in practice.","zh":"have the purpose or effect of 指有意做某事，或實際上產生該結果。"},{"en":"A rule may have the effect of excluding poorer students even if that was not its stated purpose.","zh":"一條規則即使聲稱目的不是排斥較貧窮學生，也可能產生排斥效果。"},{"en":"If a policy limits rights in practice, it can be discriminatory even without openly hateful wording.","zh":"如果政策在實際上限制權利，即使沒有公開仇恨字眼，也可能具歧視性。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both intention and outcome.","zh":"這個片語同時涵蓋意圖和結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"nullify or impair","meaning":"使……失效或受損","examples":[{"en":"Racial discrimination can nullify or impair the exercise of human rights.","zh":"種族歧視可以使人權的行使失效或受損。"},{"en":"Nullify or impair means cancel, weaken, or seriously damage something.","zh":"nullify or impair 指取消、削弱或嚴重損害某事。"},{"en":"A school rule can impair equal opportunity if only wealthy students can meet its requirements.","zh":"如果只有富裕學生能符合校規要求，該校規可以損害平等機會。"},{"en":"If discrimination stops people from using their rights, those rights become meaningless in practice.","zh":"如果歧視阻止人們使用權利，那些權利在實際上就變得無意義。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weakening or destroying the effect of rights.","zh":"這個片語描述削弱或破壞權利的效力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"recognition, enjoyment or exercise","meaning":"承認、享有或行使","examples":[{"en":"Discrimination affects the recognition, enjoyment or exercise of human rights.","zh":"歧視影響人權的承認、享有或行使。"},{"en":"Recognition, enjoyment or exercise means having rights accepted, benefiting from them, and using them in real life.","zh":"recognition, enjoyment or exercise 指權利被承認、從中受益，並在現實生活中使用。"},{"en":"A student’s right to education is not fully enjoyed if they are allowed to enrol but bullied every day.","zh":"如果學生被允許入學但每天被欺凌，其受教育權就沒有被充分享有。"},{"en":"Rights must be recognised in law and exercised in practice to be meaningful.","zh":"權利必須在法律上被承認，並在實際中被行使，才有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase lists different ways rights can be affected.","zh":"這個片語列出權利受影響的不同方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on an equal footing","meaning":"在平等基礎上","examples":[{"en":"People should enjoy human rights on an equal footing.","zh":"人們應在平等基礎上享有人權。"},{"en":"On an equal footing means with the same status, rights, or opportunities as others.","zh":"on an equal footing 指與其他人具有相同地位、權利或機會。"},{"en":"In a fair classroom, every student should ask questions on an equal footing.","zh":"在公平課室中，每位學生都應在平等基礎上提問。"},{"en":"If migrants cannot access services on an equal footing, discrimination may be present.","zh":"如果移民不能在平等基礎上獲得服務，可能存在歧視。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses equal treatment.","zh":"這個片語強調平等待遇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"human rights and fundamental freedoms","meaning":"人權和基本自由","examples":[{"en":"Discrimination can impair human rights and fundamental freedoms.","zh":"歧視可以損害人權和基本自由。"},{"en":"Human rights and fundamental freedoms are basic protections and liberties that all people should have.","zh":"human rights and fundamental freedoms 指所有人都應享有的基本保障和自由。"},{"en":"Freedom from violence and the right to fair treatment are human rights and fundamental freedoms.","zh":"免於暴力的自由和受到公平對待的權利都是人權和基本自由。"},{"en":"If these freedoms are not protected, vulnerable groups may live in fear.","zh":"如果這些自由不受保護，弱勢群體可能生活在恐懼中。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to basic rights central to dignity.","zh":"這個片語指與尊嚴核心相關的基本權利。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"public life","meaning":"公共生活","examples":[{"en":"Racial discrimination can occur in many fields of public life.","zh":"種族歧視可以發生在公共生活的許多領域。"},{"en":"Public life means areas of society outside private family life, such as work, education, politics, and services.","zh":"public life 指私人家庭生活以外的社會領域，例如工作、教育、政治和服務。"},{"en":"A person participates in public life when they vote, work, study, or use public services.","zh":"一個人投票、工作、學習或使用公共服務時，就是參與公共生活。"},{"en":"If discrimination appears in public life, it affects people’s opportunities and social belonging.","zh":"如果歧視出現在公共生活中，就會影響人的機會和社會歸屬。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to shared social and civic spaces.","zh":"這個片語指共同的社會和公民空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"distinct phenomena","meaning":"不同現象","examples":[{"en":"Racism and xenophobia are distinct phenomena, although they often overlap.","zh":"種族主義和仇外心理是不同現象，雖然它們常有重疊。"},{"en":"Distinct phenomena are separate things or events with different features.","zh":"distinct phenomena 指具有不同特徵的獨立事物或事件。"},{"en":"Stress and tiredness are distinct phenomena, although they can happen together.","zh":"壓力和疲倦是不同現象，雖然它們可以同時發生。"},{"en":"If two problems overlap, we still need to understand how they differ.","zh":"如果兩個問題有重疊，我們仍需要理解它們如何不同。"},{"en":"The phrase helps separate related but different concepts.","zh":"這個片語幫助區分相關但不同的概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"overlap","meaning":"重疊","examples":[{"en":"Racism and xenophobia often overlap in real situations.","zh":"種族主義和仇外心理在現實情況中常有重疊。"},{"en":"Overlap means partly cover the same area, meaning, or situation.","zh":"overlap 指部分覆蓋同一範圍、意思或情況。"},{"en":"Two school clubs may overlap if both organise language activities.","zh":"如果兩個學會都舉辦語言活動，它們可能有重疊。"},{"en":"Racism and xenophobia can overlap when foreigners are attacked because of both origin and appearance.","zh":"當外國人因出身和外貌同時受到攻擊時，種族主義和仇外心理可以重疊。"},{"en":"The word shows that categories can share features.","zh":"這個詞顯示分類可以共享特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"generally imply","meaning":"一般意味著","examples":[{"en":"Racism generally implies a distinction based on physical characteristics.","zh":"種族主義一般意味著基於身體特徵的區別。"},{"en":"Generally imply means usually suggest or mean something, though not in every single case.","zh":"generally imply 指通常暗示或表示某事，但不一定每個個案都如此。"},{"en":"A silent classroom generally implies that students are working, but it may also mean they are confused.","zh":"安靜的課室一般意味著學生在工作，但也可能表示他們困惑。"},{"en":"If racism generally implies physical distinction, xenophobia may focus more on perceived foreignness.","zh":"如果種族主義一般意味著身體差異，仇外心理可能更集中於被認為是外來者。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a usual meaning without making it absolute.","zh":"這個片語給出通常意思，但不把它絕對化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a distinction based on","meaning":"基於……的區別","examples":[{"en":"Racism implies a distinction based on physical characteristics.","zh":"種族主義意味著基於身體特徵的區別。"},{"en":"A distinction based on means a difference or separation made because of a particular factor.","zh":"a distinction based on 指因某特定因素而作出的差異或分隔。"},{"en":"A school should not make a distinction based on family income when giving basic support.","zh":"學校在提供基本支援時，不應基於家庭收入作出區別。"},{"en":"If treatment is based on appearance, unfair separation may occur.","zh":"如果待遇基於外貌，不公平區隔可能出現。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the reason behind a difference in treatment.","zh":"這個片語解釋差別對待背後的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"physical characteristics","meaning":"身體特徵","examples":[{"en":"Racism is often linked to differences in physical characteristics.","zh":"種族主義常與身體特徵差異有關。"},{"en":"Physical characteristics are visible body features such as skin colour, hair type, or facial features.","zh":"physical characteristics 指可見的身體特徵，例如膚色、髮質或面部特徵。"},{"en":"People should not be judged at school or work by physical characteristics.","zh":"人們不應在學校或工作中因身體特徵被評價。"},{"en":"When physical characteristics are used to rank people, discrimination can result.","zh":"當身體特徵被用來為人排序，就可能導致歧視。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to bodily features, not personality or ability.","zh":"這個片語指身體特徵，而不是性格或能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"skin colour","meaning":"膚色","examples":[{"en":"Skin colour is one example of a physical characteristic.","zh":"膚色是身體特徵的一個例子。"},{"en":"Skin colour means the natural colour or shade of a person’s skin.","zh":"skin colour 指一個人皮膚的自然顏色或色調。"},{"en":"A fair employer should not treat applicants differently because of skin colour.","zh":"公平僱主不應因膚色而區別對待求職者。"},{"en":"If skin colour becomes a reason for exclusion, racial discrimination is present.","zh":"如果膚色成為排斥理由，就存在種族歧視。"},{"en":"The phrase is often discussed in relation to racism.","zh":"這個片語常在種族主義相關討論中出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hair type","meaning":"髮質；頭髮類型","examples":[{"en":"Hair type may be treated as a physical characteristic in racist thinking.","zh":"在種族主義思維中，髮質可能被視為身體特徵。"},{"en":"Hair type means the natural texture or form of hair, such as straight, curly, or tightly coiled.","zh":"hair type 指頭髮的自然質感或形態，例如直髮、鬈髮或緊密卷曲髮。"},{"en":"School rules about hair type can be unfair if they target one ethnic group.","zh":"如果校規針對某一族裔群體的髮質，可能不公平。"},{"en":"If people are judged by hair type, appearance becomes a tool of exclusion.","zh":"如果人們因髮質被評價，外貌就成為排斥工具。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a visible bodily feature.","zh":"這個片語指可見的身體特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"facial features","meaning":"面部特徵","examples":[{"en":"Facial features are sometimes used to mark racial difference.","zh":"面部特徵有時被用來標示種族差異。"},{"en":"Facial features are parts and shapes of the face, such as eyes, nose, mouth, and bone structure.","zh":"facial features 指臉部的部分和形狀，例如眼睛、鼻、嘴和骨骼結構。"},{"en":"People should not be treated differently because of facial features.","zh":"人們不應因面部特徵而受到區別對待。"},{"en":"If facial features are used to label someone as foreign, prejudice may follow.","zh":"如果面部特徵被用來標籤某人為外來者，偏見可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to visible features of the face.","zh":"這個片語指臉部可見特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"denote behaviour","meaning":"表示……行為","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobia denotes behaviour based on the idea that someone is foreign.","zh":"仇外心理表示基於某人是外來者這一想法的行為。"},{"en":"Denote behaviour means refer to or indicate a type of action or conduct.","zh":"denote behaviour 指表示或指涉某種行動或舉止。"},{"en":"In school rules, “bullying” denotes behaviour such as repeated insults or threats.","zh":"在校規中，“bullying” 表示重複侮辱或威脅等行為。"},{"en":"If a term denotes behaviour, it describes what people do, not only what they think.","zh":"如果某詞表示行為，它描述的是人們做甚麼，而不只是想甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase helps define an idea through actions.","zh":"這個片語透過行動幫助界定概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"based on the perception that","meaning":"基於……的看法","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobia is based on the perception that a person is foreign.","zh":"仇外心理基於某人是外來者的看法。"},{"en":"Based on the perception that means caused by or built on the belief that something is true.","zh":"based on the perception that 指由某事是真實的信念造成或建立在該信念上。"},{"en":"A student may be excluded based on the perception that newcomers are unfriendly, even if this is false.","zh":"即使這是錯的，學生也可能因「新來者不友善」這種看法而被排斥。"},{"en":"If people perceive someone as foreign, they may treat that person differently.","zh":"如果人們把某人視為外來者，可能以不同方式對待那人。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses belief or perception, not necessarily fact.","zh":"這個片語強調信念或看法，而不一定是事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the other","meaning":"他者；被視為外來者的人","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobia treats “the other” as foreign or outside the community.","zh":"仇外心理把「他者」視為外國人或社區外的人。"},{"en":"The other means a person or group seen as different from “us” and not fully belonging.","zh":"the other 指被視為與「我們」不同且不完全屬於其中的人或群體。"},{"en":"New students may be treated as the other if classmates refuse to include them.","zh":"如果同學拒絕接納新生，新生可能被視為他者。"},{"en":"When society divides people into “us” and “the other,” prejudice becomes easier.","zh":"當社會把人分成「我們」和「他者」，偏見就更容易出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes social separation and exclusion.","zh":"這個片語描述社會區隔和排斥。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be foreign to","meaning":"對……而言是外來的","examples":[{"en":"The person may be seen as foreign to the community or nation.","zh":"該人可能被視為對社區或國家而言是外來的。"},{"en":"Be foreign to means be regarded as outside, unfamiliar, or not belonging to a group.","zh":"be foreign to 指被視為外部、不熟悉或不屬於某群體。"},{"en":"A new teaching method may feel foreign to students who are used to memorisation.","zh":"對習慣背誦的學生而言，新教學方法可能感覺陌生。"},{"en":"If someone is seen as foreign to a community, they may be excluded from trust and support.","zh":"如果某人被視為對社區而言是外來的，可能被排除於信任和支援之外。"},{"en":"The phrase describes perceived outsider status.","zh":"這個片語描述被感知為外來者的身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"originate from outside","meaning":"源自……之外","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobia targets people perceived to originate from outside the community.","zh":"仇外心理針對被認為源自社區之外的人。"},{"en":"Originate from outside means come from beyond a particular place or group.","zh":"originate from outside 指來自某特定地方或群體之外。"},{"en":"A rumour may be distrusted if people think it originated from outside the school.","zh":"如果人們認為謠言源自學校以外，就可能不信任它。"},{"en":"If people believe newcomers originate from outside, they may question whether they belong.","zh":"如果人們相信新來者源自外部，可能質疑他們是否屬於這裡。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on perceived source or origin.","zh":"這個片語集中於被感知的來源或出身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"community or nation","meaning":"社群或國家","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobia is directed at people seen as outsiders to a community or nation.","zh":"仇外心理針對被視為社群或國家外來者的人。"},{"en":"Community or nation means a local group of people or a whole country.","zh":"community or nation 指本地群體或整個國家。"},{"en":"A person may belong strongly to a neighbourhood community and also to a nation.","zh":"一個人可以強烈屬於某社區，也屬於一個國家。"},{"en":"If people are treated as outsiders to both community and nation, exclusion can be severe.","zh":"如果人們在社群和國家層面都被視為外來者，排斥可以很嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both local and national belonging.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋本地和國家層面的歸屬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"by the standard dictionary definition","meaning":"按照標準字典定義","examples":[{"en":"By the standard dictionary definition, xenophobia is dislike or fear of foreigners.","zh":"按照標準字典定義，仇外心理是對外國人的厭惡或恐懼。"},{"en":"By the standard dictionary definition means according to the usual meaning given in a dictionary.","zh":"by the standard dictionary definition 指根據字典中給出的通常意思。"},{"en":"By the standard dictionary definition, a refugee is someone forced to leave for safety.","zh":"按照標準字典定義，難民是因安全原因被迫離開的人。"},{"en":"Dictionary definitions help clarify basic meaning before deeper discussion begins.","zh":"字典定義有助在深入討論前澄清基本意思。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a common, formal definition.","zh":"這個片語引出常見而正式的定義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"intense dislike or fear of","meaning":"對……的強烈厭惡或恐懼","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobia is the intense dislike or fear of people from other countries.","zh":"仇外心理是對來自其他國家的人產生強烈厭惡或恐懼。"},{"en":"Intense dislike or fear of means very strong negative feeling toward someone or something.","zh":"intense dislike or fear of 指對某人或某事有非常強烈的負面感受。"},{"en":"A child may have an intense fear of dogs after being bitten.","zh":"孩子被狗咬後，可能對狗有強烈恐懼。"},{"en":"If intense dislike is directed at foreigners, social hostility can grow quickly.","zh":"如果強烈厭惡指向外國人，社會敵意可以迅速增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong emotional reaction.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈情緒反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"strangers or people from other countries","meaning":"陌生人或來自其他國家的人","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobia involves fear of strangers or people from other countries.","zh":"仇外心理涉及對陌生人或來自其他國家的人產生恐懼。"},{"en":"Strangers or people from other countries means unfamiliar people or foreigners.","zh":"strangers or people from other countries 指不熟悉的人或外國人。"},{"en":"A child may feel shy around strangers, but that is not the same as xenophobia.","zh":"孩子在陌生人附近可能害羞，但這不等於仇外心理。"},{"en":"When fear of strangers becomes hostility toward whole groups, it becomes socially dangerous.","zh":"當對陌生人的恐懼變成對整個群體的敵意，就會在社會上變得危險。"},{"en":"The phrase explains who xenophobic fear may target.","zh":"這個片語解釋仇外恐懼可能針對誰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as a sociologist puts it","meaning":"正如一位社會學家所說","examples":[{"en":"As a sociologist puts it, xenophobia is hostility against non-natives.","zh":"正如一位社會學家所說，仇外心理是對非本地人的敵意。"},{"en":"As a sociologist puts it means in the words or explanation of a sociologist.","zh":"as a sociologist puts it 指用一位社會學家的話語或解釋來說。"},{"en":"As a teacher puts it, grammar is a tool for making meaning clear.","zh":"正如一位老師所說，文法是令意思清楚的工具。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an expert’s wording rather than the writer’s own wording.","zh":"這個片語引出專家的措辭，而不是作者自己的措辭。"},{"en":"It is useful when quoting or paraphrasing a specialist view.","zh":"它在引用或轉述專家觀點時很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"attitudinal orientation","meaning":"態度取向","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobia can be described as an attitudinal orientation of hostility.","zh":"仇外心理可被描述為一種敵意的態度取向。"},{"en":"Attitudinal orientation means a general direction or pattern in a person’s attitudes.","zh":"attitudinal orientation 指一個人在態度上的整體方向或模式。"},{"en":"A student with a positive attitudinal orientation toward mistakes sees errors as chances to learn.","zh":"對錯誤有正面態度取向的學生，會把錯誤看成學習機會。"},{"en":"If a population has an orientation of hostility toward outsiders, xenophobia may become common.","zh":"如果某人口群體對外來者有敵意取向，仇外心理可能變得常見。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and refers to a pattern of attitude.","zh":"這個片語較正式，指態度模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hostility against","meaning":"對……的敵意","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobia involves hostility against non-natives.","zh":"仇外心理涉及對非本地人的敵意。"},{"en":"Hostility against means unfriendly, aggressive, or hateful feeling or behaviour toward someone.","zh":"hostility against 指對某人的不友善、攻擊性或仇恨感受或行為。"},{"en":"Hostility against new classmates can make them afraid to join group activities.","zh":"對新同學的敵意可以令他們害怕參加小組活動。"},{"en":"If hostility against migrants grows, verbal abuse may turn into violence.","zh":"如果對移民的敵意增長，言語辱罵可能變成暴力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active negative feeling toward a target.","zh":"這個片語描述針對某目標的主動負面感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"non-natives","meaning":"非本地人","examples":[{"en":"Non-natives may become targets of xenophobic attitudes.","zh":"非本地人可能成為仇外態度的目標。"},{"en":"Non-natives are people who are not originally from a particular place or community.","zh":"non-natives 指並非原本來自某特定地方或社群的人。"},{"en":"A non-native speaker may need extra time to understand fast local speech.","zh":"非母語說話者可能需要更多時間理解快速本地說話。"},{"en":"If non-natives are treated with suspicion, they may struggle to feel they belong.","zh":"如果非本地人受到猜疑，他們可能難以感到歸屬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes origin relative to a place.","zh":"這個片語描述相對於某地方的出身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in a given population","meaning":"在某個特定人口群體中","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobia may exist in a given population.","zh":"仇外心理可能存在於某個特定人口群體中。"},{"en":"In a given population means within a particular group of people being discussed or studied.","zh":"in a given population 指在正在討論或研究的特定人群之中。"},{"en":"A health survey may study stress levels in a given population of secondary students.","zh":"健康調查可能研究某個中學生人口群體中的壓力水平。"},{"en":"If hostility is common in a given population, researchers may examine social and economic causes.","zh":"如果敵意在某特定人口群體中常見，研究人員可能檢視社會和經濟原因。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows discussion to one defined group.","zh":"這個片語把討論收窄到一個被界定的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"differentiation from","meaning":"與……的區分","examples":[{"en":"The differentiation of xenophobia from racism is still evolving.","zh":"仇外心理與種族主義的區分仍在發展。"},{"en":"Differentiation from means the process of distinguishing one thing from another.","zh":"differentiation from 指把一件事與另一件事區分開來的過程。"},{"en":"Students learn differentiation of “affect” from “effect” through examples and practice.","zh":"學生透過例子和練習學習區分 affect 和 effect。"},{"en":"If two concepts overlap, differentiating them clearly may take time.","zh":"如果兩個概念有重疊，清楚區分它們可能需要時間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes drawing a boundary between ideas.","zh":"這個片語描述在觀念之間劃出界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"still evolving","meaning":"仍在發展","examples":[{"en":"The definition of xenophobia is still evolving.","zh":"仇外心理的定義仍在發展。"},{"en":"Still evolving means continuing to develop, change, or become clearer.","zh":"still evolving 指仍在發展、改變或變得更清晰。"},{"en":"A student’s writing style is still evolving if each essay shows new strengths.","zh":"如果學生每篇文章都展示新強項，其寫作風格仍在發展。"},{"en":"If social problems change, the language used to describe them may also evolve.","zh":"如果社會問題改變，描述它們的語言也可能演變。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a process is not yet complete.","zh":"這個片語暗示過程尚未完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"regional Preparatory Meetings","meaning":"區域籌備會議","examples":[{"en":"Regional Preparatory Meetings suggested definitions of racism and xenophobia.","zh":"區域籌備會議提出了種族主義和仇外心理的定義。"},{"en":"Regional Preparatory Meetings are meetings held in different regions to prepare for a larger conference or decision.","zh":"regional Preparatory Meetings 指在不同地區舉行、為大型會議或決定作準備的會議。"},{"en":"A school may hold preparatory meetings before a major open day.","zh":"學校可能在大型開放日前舉行籌備會議。"},{"en":"Such meetings can help collect views before final definitions are agreed.","zh":"這類會議可以在最終定義達成前收集意見。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised meetings before a bigger event.","zh":"這個片語指大型活動前有組織的會議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"World Conference","meaning":"世界會議","examples":[{"en":"A recent World Conference considered definitions of racism and xenophobia.","zh":"最近一次世界會議考慮了種族主義和仇外心理的定義。"},{"en":"A World Conference is a large international meeting where participants discuss a major global issue.","zh":"World Conference 指參與者討論重大全球議題的大型國際會議。"},{"en":"A World Conference on education may bring together governments, teachers, and researchers.","zh":"教育世界會議可能聚集政府、老師和研究人員。"},{"en":"If a World Conference defines key terms, those definitions may influence policy.","zh":"如果世界會議界定關鍵術語，這些定義可能影響政策。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a high-level global meeting.","zh":"這個片語描述高層全球會議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"suggest the following","meaning":"提出以下內容","examples":[{"en":"One meeting suggested the following definition of racism.","zh":"一次會議提出以下種族主義定義。"},{"en":"Suggest the following means introduce or propose the information that comes next.","zh":"suggest the following 指引入或提出接下來的資訊。"},{"en":"A teacher may suggest the following structure before students write an essay.","zh":"老師可能在學生寫文章前提出以下結構。"},{"en":"When a report suggests the following definition, it prepares readers for exact wording.","zh":"當報告提出以下定義，它讓讀者準備閱讀準確措辭。"},{"en":"The phrase points forward to a list, definition, or proposal.","zh":"這個片語指向接下來的列表、定義或建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ideological construct","meaning":"意識形態建構","examples":[{"en":"Racism is described as an ideological construct.","zh":"種族主義被描述為一種意識形態建構。"},{"en":"An ideological construct is an idea or belief system created to explain or justify social relations.","zh":"ideological construct 指被創造出來用以解釋或合理化社會關係的觀念或信念系統。"},{"en":"The belief that one group deserves more power can be an ideological construct.","zh":"相信某一群體應擁有更多權力，可以是一種意識形態建構。"},{"en":"If an ideology ranks people, it can support unequal treatment.","zh":"如果意識形態把人排序，就能支持不平等對待。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and describes a built system of ideas.","zh":"這個片語較正式，描述被建立起來的一套觀念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"assign someone to a position of power over","meaning":"將某人置於凌駕於……的權力位置","examples":[{"en":"Racism assigns one group to a position of power over others.","zh":"種族主義將一個群體置於凌駕於其他群體的權力位置。"},{"en":"Assign someone to a position of power over means place a person or group above others in authority or status.","zh":"assign someone to a position of power over 指把某人或群體放在高於其他人的權威或地位上。"},{"en":"A school should not assign one group of students power over others because of family background.","zh":"學校不應因家庭背景而把某組學生置於凌駕其他學生的權力位置。"},{"en":"If one group is placed above another, inequality becomes built into the system.","zh":"如果一個群體被置於另一群體之上，不平等就被建入制度中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving dominance to one side.","zh":"這個片語描述賦予一方支配地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a position of power over","meaning":"凌駕於……的權力位置","examples":[{"en":"Racism places one group in a position of power over other groups.","zh":"種族主義把一個群體置於凌駕其他群體的權力位置。"},{"en":"A position of power over means a place of control, authority, or dominance above others.","zh":"position of power over 指高於他人的控制、權威或支配位置。"},{"en":"A manager has a position of power over staff and should use it fairly.","zh":"經理對員工有權力位置，應公平使用。"},{"en":"If power is based on race, the system becomes discriminatory.","zh":"如果權力基於種族，制度就變得具歧視性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unequal authority.","zh":"這個片語描述不平等權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"on the basis of","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"Racism assigns power on the basis of physical and cultural attributes.","zh":"種族主義根據身體和文化特徵分配權力。"},{"en":"On the basis of means because of or according to a particular factor.","zh":"on the basis of 指因為或根據某特定因素。"},{"en":"A student should be graded on the basis of work, not popularity.","zh":"學生應根據作品評分，而不是根據受歡迎程度。"},{"en":"If rights are given on the basis of race, equality is destroyed.","zh":"如果權利根據種族授予，平等就被破壞。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the reason for a decision or judgement.","zh":"這個片語指出決定或判斷的理由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"physical and cultural attributes","meaning":"身體和文化特徵","examples":[{"en":"Racism may be based on physical and cultural attributes.","zh":"種族主義可能基於身體和文化特徵。"},{"en":"Physical and cultural attributes are bodily features and cultural traits such as language, dress, or customs.","zh":"physical and cultural attributes 指身體特徵，以及語言、服飾或習俗等文化特徵。"},{"en":"People should not be excluded because of physical and cultural attributes.","zh":"人們不應因身體和文化特徵而被排除。"},{"en":"If a society ranks people by appearance and culture, discrimination becomes systematic.","zh":"如果社會按外貌和文化把人排序，歧視就變得制度化。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both visible features and cultural markers.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋可見特徵和文化標記。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"economic wealth","meaning":"經濟財富","examples":[{"en":"Economic wealth may also be involved in racist power structures.","zh":"經濟財富也可能涉及種族主義權力結構。"},{"en":"Economic wealth means money, property, and financial resources.","zh":"economic wealth 指金錢、財產和財務資源。"},{"en":"A family with more economic wealth may afford private tutoring and better housing.","zh":"擁有更多經濟財富的家庭可能負擔得起私人補習和較好住屋。"},{"en":"If wealth is concentrated in one group, social power may become unequal.","zh":"如果財富集中在某一群體，社會權力可能變得不平等。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to material and financial advantage.","zh":"這個片語指物質和財政優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"hierarchical relations","meaning":"等級關係","examples":[{"en":"Racism involves hierarchical relations between groups.","zh":"種族主義涉及群體之間的等級關係。"},{"en":"Hierarchical relations are relationships arranged in higher and lower levels of power or status.","zh":"hierarchical relations 指按權力或地位高低排列的關係。"},{"en":"A workplace has hierarchical relations when managers make decisions and junior staff follow them.","zh":"當經理作決定而初級員工跟從，工作場所就有等級關係。"},{"en":"If one ethnic group is placed above another, hierarchy becomes discriminatory.","zh":"如果一個族群被置於另一族群之上，等級就變成歧視。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unequal ranking between groups.","zh":"這個片語描述群體之間不平等排序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the superior race","meaning":"優越種族","examples":[{"en":"Racist ideology imagines a superior race exercising control over others.","zh":"種族主義意識形態想像一個優越種族對其他群體行使控制。"},{"en":"The superior race is a false racist idea that one racial group is naturally better than others.","zh":"superior race 是一種錯誤的種族主義觀念，認為某一種族天生比其他種族優越。"},{"en":"A fair history lesson should challenge the myth of a superior race.","zh":"公平歷史課應挑戰優越種族這個神話。"},{"en":"Belief in a superior race can justify domination, exclusion, and violence.","zh":"相信優越種族可以合理化支配、排斥和暴力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a racist claim, not a factual truth.","zh":"這個片語描述種族主義主張，而不是事實真相。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"exercise domination and control over","meaning":"對……行使支配和控制","examples":[{"en":"A so-called superior race may exercise domination and control over others.","zh":"所謂優越種族可能對其他群體行使支配和控制。"},{"en":"Exercise domination and control over means use power to rule, limit, or command others.","zh":"exercise domination and control over 指使用權力去統治、限制或命令他人。"},{"en":"A bully may exercise control over classmates by threatening them.","zh":"欺凌者可能透過威脅同學來對他們行使控制。"},{"en":"If one group controls another’s movement, work, and rights, domination is present.","zh":"如果一個群體控制另一群體的移動、工作和權利，就存在支配。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active use of power over people.","zh":"這個片語描述主動對人使用權力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"attitudes, prejudices and behaviour","meaning":"態度、偏見和行為","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobia describes attitudes, prejudices and behaviour that reject outsiders.","zh":"仇外心理描述拒絕外來者的態度、偏見和行為。"},{"en":"Attitudes, prejudices and behaviour means what people feel, assume, and do toward others.","zh":"attitudes, prejudices and behaviour 指人們對他人的感受、假設和行動。"},{"en":"A school may address attitudes, prejudices and behaviour through discussion and clear rules.","zh":"學校可能透過討論和清楚規則處理態度、偏見和行為。"},{"en":"If prejudice becomes behaviour, words and beliefs may turn into exclusion or violence.","zh":"如果偏見變成行為，言語和信念可能轉化成排斥或暴力。"},{"en":"The phrase connects inner beliefs with outward actions.","zh":"這個片語把內在信念與外在行動連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reject, exclude and vilify","meaning":"拒絕、排斥和詆毀","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobic behaviour may reject, exclude and vilify people seen as foreigners.","zh":"仇外行為可能拒絕、排斥和詆毀被視為外國人的人。"},{"en":"Reject, exclude and vilify means refuse to accept, push out, and insult or attack someone’s reputation.","zh":"reject, exclude and vilify 指拒絕接受、排擠出去，並侮辱或攻擊某人的名譽。"},{"en":"A group of students may reject and exclude a new classmate by refusing to sit with her.","zh":"一群學生拒絕與新同學同坐，就是拒絕和排斥她。"},{"en":"If media vilifies migrants, the public may become more hostile toward them.","zh":"如果媒體詆毀移民，公眾可能對他們更有敵意。"},{"en":"The phrase shows increasing forms of hostility.","zh":"這個片語顯示逐步加劇的敵意形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be perceived as outsiders","meaning":"被視為外來者","examples":[{"en":"People may be perceived as outsiders even when they share physical characteristics.","zh":"即使人們有相同身體特徵，也可能被視為外來者。"},{"en":"Be perceived as outsiders means be seen or treated as not belonging to a group.","zh":"be perceived as outsiders 指被看作或對待成不屬於某群體的人。"},{"en":"A student who speaks with a different accent may be perceived as an outsider in class.","zh":"說話帶不同口音的學生可能在班中被視為外來者。"},{"en":"If people are perceived as outsiders, they may be excluded even without visible differences.","zh":"如果人們被視為外來者，即使沒有可見差異，也可能被排斥。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how others see someone.","zh":"這個片語集中於別人如何看待某人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"outsiders or foreigners","meaning":"外來者或外國人","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobia targets people seen as outsiders or foreigners.","zh":"仇外心理針對被視為外來者或外國人的人。"},{"en":"Outsiders or foreigners are people regarded as not belonging to the local group or nation.","zh":"outsiders or foreigners 指被認為不屬於本地群體或國家的人。"},{"en":"New workers may feel like outsiders if no one explains workplace routines to them.","zh":"如果沒有人解釋工作場所慣例，新員工可能覺得自己像外來者。"},{"en":"When outsiders or foreigners are blamed for problems, prejudice can spread.","zh":"當外來者或外國人被怪罪為問題來源，偏見可能擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase describes people viewed as outside the community.","zh":"這個片語描述被視為社群外的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"distinguish between","meaning":"區分……","examples":[{"en":"It can be difficult to distinguish between racism and xenophobia.","zh":"區分種族主義和仇外心理可能很困難。"},{"en":"Distinguish between means recognise the difference between two things.","zh":"distinguish between 指辨認兩件事之間的差異。"},{"en":"Students must distinguish between “false” and “not given” in reading exams.","zh":"學生在閱讀考試中必須區分 “false” 和 “not given”。"},{"en":"If two ideas overlap, clear examples help people distinguish between them.","zh":"如果兩個概念有重疊，清楚例子能幫助人們區分它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes separating similar things in meaning.","zh":"這個片語描述在意思上分辨相似事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"motivations for behaviour","meaning":"行為動機","examples":[{"en":"Racism and xenophobia may both be motivations for behaviour.","zh":"種族主義和仇外心理都可能是行為動機。"},{"en":"Motivations for behaviour are the reasons or feelings that cause people to act in a certain way.","zh":"motivations for behaviour 指導致人們以某方式行動的原因或感受。"},{"en":"A student’s motivation for studying may be curiosity, fear of exams, or family expectations.","zh":"學生學習的動機可能是好奇心、對考試的恐懼或家庭期望。"},{"en":"If fear of outsiders motivates behaviour, it may lead to exclusion or violence.","zh":"如果對外來者的恐懼成為行為動機，可能導致排斥或暴力。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why people act.","zh":"這個片語解釋人們為何行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be assumed to","meaning":"被假定為","examples":[{"en":"Physical differences are often assumed to separate a person from the common identity.","zh":"身體差異常被假定為會把一個人與共同身份分開。"},{"en":"Be assumed to means be believed to be true without full proof.","zh":"be assumed to 指在沒有充分證據下被認為是真的。"},{"en":"Quiet students are sometimes assumed to understand everything, even when they need help.","zh":"安靜學生有時被假定為甚麼都明白，即使他們需要幫助。"},{"en":"If appearance is assumed to show belonging, people may be judged unfairly.","zh":"如果外貌被假定為顯示歸屬，人們可能被不公平評價。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an untested belief.","zh":"這個片語描述未經驗證的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"common identity","meaning":"共同身份","examples":[{"en":"Physical characteristics may be used to distinguish someone from the common identity.","zh":"身體特徵可能被用來把某人與共同身份區分開來。"},{"en":"Common identity means the shared sense of belonging within a group, community, or nation.","zh":"common identity 指群體、社區或國家內共同的歸屬感。"},{"en":"A school uniform can create a common identity among students.","zh":"校服可以在學生之間創造共同身份。"},{"en":"If people are excluded from a common identity, they may feel they do not belong.","zh":"如果人們被排除於共同身份之外，可能覺得自己不屬於其中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shared belonging.","zh":"這個片語描述共同歸屬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"manifestations of xenophobia","meaning":"仇外心理的表現","examples":[{"en":"Manifestations of xenophobia can be directed against people with shared ancestry.","zh":"仇外心理的表現可以針對有共同祖先的人。"},{"en":"Manifestations of xenophobia are visible forms or examples of anti-outsider attitudes and actions.","zh":"manifestations of xenophobia 指反外來者態度和行為的可見形式或例子。"},{"en":"Hate speech, exclusion, and attacks can be manifestations of xenophobia.","zh":"仇恨言論、排斥和攻擊都可以是仇外心理的表現。"},{"en":"If xenophobia appears in daily behaviour, it becomes easier to identify and challenge.","zh":"如果仇外心理出現在日常行為中，就更容易識別和挑戰。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to how xenophobia shows itself.","zh":"這個片語指仇外心理如何顯現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"identical physical characteristics","meaning":"相同身體特徵","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobia may target people of identical physical characteristics.","zh":"仇外心理可能針對具有相同身體特徵的人。"},{"en":"Identical physical characteristics means the same visible bodily features.","zh":"identical physical characteristics 指相同的可見身體特徵。"},{"en":"Two siblings may have nearly identical physical characteristics but very different personalities.","zh":"兩兄弟姊妹可能有幾乎相同的身體特徵，但性格很不同。"},{"en":"If people look physically similar but one group is seen as foreign, xenophobia may still occur.","zh":"如果人們外貌相似，但其中一群被視為外來者，仇外心理仍可能發生。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that xenophobia is not always based on visible difference.","zh":"這個片語顯示仇外心理不一定基於可見差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"shared ancestry","meaning":"共同祖先","examples":[{"en":"People with shared ancestry may still be treated as outsiders.","zh":"有共同祖先的人仍可能被視為外來者。"},{"en":"Shared ancestry means common family, ethnic, or historical roots.","zh":"shared ancestry 指共同的家庭、族裔或歷史根源。"},{"en":"Two families may share ancestry if their grandparents came from the same village.","zh":"如果兩個家庭的祖父母來自同一村莊，他們可能有共同祖先。"},{"en":"Even shared ancestry may not protect people from exclusion if they are seen as newcomers.","zh":"如果人們被視為新來者，即使有共同祖先也未必能免於排斥。"},{"en":"The phrase describes common origin across generations.","zh":"這個片語描述跨世代的共同來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"arrive, return or migrate to","meaning":"到達、返回或遷移到","examples":[{"en":"People may face xenophobia when they arrive, return or migrate to certain areas.","zh":"人們到達、返回或遷移到某些地區時，可能面對仇外心理。"},{"en":"Arrive, return or migrate to means come to a place, come back to it, or move there to live.","zh":"arrive, return or migrate to 指來到某地、回到某地，或遷往某地居住。"},{"en":"A worker may arrive in a city, return to a hometown, or migrate to another country for work.","zh":"工人可能到達城市、返回家鄉，或為工作遷往另一國。"},{"en":"Movement into an area can trigger suspicion if local residents see newcomers as outsiders.","zh":"進入某地的流動可能引發猜疑，如果本地居民把新來者視為外來者。"},{"en":"The phrase covers several ways people enter a community.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋人們進入社區的幾種方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"occupants consider them outsiders","meaning":"居民視他們為外來者","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobia may occur when occupants consider newcomers outsiders.","zh":"當居民視新來者為外來者時，仇外心理可能出現。"},{"en":"Occupants consider them outsiders means people already living in a place see newcomers as not belonging.","zh":"occupants consider them outsiders 指已居於某地的人把新來者視為不屬於該地。"},{"en":"Long-time residents may consider new tenants outsiders if they do not speak the local language.","zh":"如果新租戶不說本地語言，長期居民可能視他們為外來者。"},{"en":"If occupants treat newcomers as outsiders, social distance and hostility can grow.","zh":"如果居民把新來者當作外來者，社會距離和敵意可能增長。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how exclusion begins from local perception.","zh":"這個片語解釋排斥如何由本地看法開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete each sentence with","meaning":"用……完成每句句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete each sentence with the correct ending.","zh":"考生用正確句尾完成每句句子。"},{"en":"Complete each sentence with means finish each sentence by adding the required word, phrase, or ending.","zh":"complete each sentence with 指加入所需字詞、片語或句尾，使每句完整。"},{"en":"Students complete each sentence with a verb form when practising grammar.","zh":"學生練習文法時，會用動詞形式完成每句句子。"},{"en":"If the ending does not match the sentence meaning, the answer becomes wrong.","zh":"如果句尾與句意不配合，答案就會錯。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the correct ending","meaning":"正確句尾","examples":[{"en":"The correct ending should match the meaning of the sentence.","zh":"正確句尾應配合句子的意思。"},{"en":"The correct ending is the option that completes a sentence accurately in meaning and grammar.","zh":"correct ending 指在意思和文法上準確完成句子的選項。"},{"en":"A student should check whether the correct ending fits the subject and verb.","zh":"學生應檢查正確句尾是否配合主語和動詞。"},{"en":"If two endings look possible, the passage meaning helps decide.","zh":"如果兩個句尾看似可行，文章意思有助決定。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the right final part of a sentence.","zh":"這個片語指句子的正確最後部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"write the correct letter","meaning":"寫上正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the correct letter in the spaces below.","zh":"考生在下方空格中寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"Write the correct letter means record the letter that matches the chosen answer.","zh":"write the correct letter 指寫下與所選答案相配的字母。"},{"en":"If option C is correct, students should write C, not the whole sentence.","zh":"如果 C 選項正確，學生應寫 C，而不是整句。"},{"en":"Writing the wrong letter can lose the mark even when the student understands the idea.","zh":"即使學生理解意思，寫錯字母也可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase is a practical exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是實際考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in the spaces below","meaning":"在下方空格中","examples":[{"en":"The answers should be written in the spaces below.","zh":"答案應寫在下方空格中。"},{"en":"In the spaces below means in the blank areas provided under the questions.","zh":"in the spaces below 指在題目下方提供的空白位置。"},{"en":"Students should write their answers in the spaces below each question, not in the margin.","zh":"學生應把答案寫在每題下方空格中，而不是頁邊。"},{"en":"If answers are placed in the wrong space, marking may become difficult.","zh":"如果答案放在錯誤位置，批改可能變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase tells candidates where to write.","zh":"這個片語告訴考生在哪裡書寫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"an upward trend in","meaning":"……的上升趨勢","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to an upward trend in violence against non-national groups.","zh":"題目提到針對非本國群體暴力的上升趨勢。"},{"en":"An upward trend in means a general increase over time.","zh":"upward trend in 指隨時間整體增加。"},{"en":"A school may see an upward trend in late arrivals during winter.","zh":"學校可能在冬季見到遲到人數有上升趨勢。"},{"en":"If violence shows an upward trend, preventive action becomes urgent.","zh":"如果暴力呈上升趨勢，預防行動就變得迫切。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a rising pattern, not one isolated increase.","zh":"這個片語描述上升模式，而不是一次單獨增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"violence perpetrated against","meaning":"針對……施行的暴力","examples":[{"en":"The statement discusses violence perpetrated against non-national minority groups.","zh":"該陳述討論針對非本國少數族裔群體施行的暴力。"},{"en":"Violence perpetrated against means violent acts committed against a person or group.","zh":"violence perpetrated against 指針對某人或某群體犯下的暴力行為。"},{"en":"Violence perpetrated against workers should be reported and investigated immediately.","zh":"針對工人施行的暴力應立即被舉報和調查。"},{"en":"If violence is perpetrated against minorities, fear may spread through the whole community.","zh":"如果暴力針對少數群體，恐懼可能擴散到整個社區。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and focuses on the victims of violence.","zh":"這個片語較正式，集中於暴力受害者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"non-national minority groups","meaning":"非本國少數族裔群體","examples":[{"en":"Non-national minority groups may suffer discrimination and violence.","zh":"非本國少數族裔群體可能遭受歧視和暴力。"},{"en":"Non-national minority groups are small groups of people in a country who are not citizens of that country.","zh":"non-national minority groups 指在某國內不是該國公民的少數群體。"},{"en":"Foreign domestic workers may be a non-national minority group in some societies.","zh":"在一些社會中，外籍家庭工人可能是非本國少數族裔群體。"},{"en":"If such groups lack political voice, abuse may be harder to challenge.","zh":"如果這些群體缺乏政治聲音，虐待可能更難被挑戰。"},{"en":"The phrase combines citizenship status and minority position.","zh":"這個片語結合公民身份和少數群體位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"radical nationals","meaning":"激進本國國民","examples":[{"en":"Radical nationals may direct violence against non-national minority groups.","zh":"激進本國國民可能把暴力指向非本國少數族裔群體。"},{"en":"Radical nationals are citizens with extreme nationalist views.","zh":"radical nationals 指持極端民族主義觀點的本國公民。"},{"en":"Radical nationals may blame foreigners for unemployment or social change without evidence.","zh":"激進本國國民可能在沒有證據下把失業或社會變化怪罪於外國人。"},{"en":"If radical nationalism grows, minority groups may become targets of hostility.","zh":"如果激進民族主義增長，少數群體可能成為敵意目標。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extreme members of the local national group.","zh":"這個片語描述本地民族群體中的極端成員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"where racism occurs","meaning":"在種族主義發生的地方","examples":[{"en":"Where racism occurs, one group may dominate others.","zh":"在種族主義發生的地方，一個群體可能支配其他群體。"},{"en":"Where racism occurs means in situations or places where racist beliefs or actions appear.","zh":"where racism occurs 指在種族主義信念或行為出現的情況或地方。"},{"en":"Where bullying occurs, schools must protect victims and correct behaviour.","zh":"在欺凌發生的地方，學校必須保護受害者並糾正行為。"},{"en":"If racism occurs in hiring, qualified people may be rejected unfairly.","zh":"如果種族主義出現在招聘中，合資格人士可能被不公平拒絕。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the condition under which a result happens.","zh":"這個片語引出某結果發生的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"dominant group","meaning":"主導群體","examples":[{"en":"The dominant group may promote a hierarchical system.","zh":"主導群體可能推動等級制度。"},{"en":"A dominant group is the group with the most power, influence, or control in a society.","zh":"dominant group 指在社會中擁有最多權力、影響力或控制力的群體。"},{"en":"In a classroom, a dominant group of students may influence what others feel safe to say.","zh":"在課室中，主導學生群體可能影響其他人是否敢發言。"},{"en":"If the dominant group controls laws and resources, minority voices may be ignored.","zh":"如果主導群體控制法律和資源，少數聲音可能被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the group in a stronger social position.","zh":"這個片語描述處於較強社會位置的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"promote a hierarchical system","meaning":"推動等級制度","examples":[{"en":"Racist ideology can promote a hierarchical system.","zh":"種族主義意識形態可以推動等級制度。"},{"en":"Promote a hierarchical system means encourage an order where some groups are placed above others.","zh":"promote a hierarchical system 指鼓勵某些群體被置於其他群體之上的秩序。"},{"en":"A school should not promote a hierarchy where wealthy students receive better treatment.","zh":"學校不應推動富裕學生獲得較好待遇的等級制度。"},{"en":"If a system ranks groups by race or origin, inequality becomes normalised.","zh":"如果制度按種族或出身排列群體，不平等就被正常化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes supporting unequal social ranking.","zh":"這個片語描述支持不平等的社會排序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"controlling hand in the affairs of","meaning":"對……的事務有控制權","examples":[{"en":"One group may have a controlling hand in the affairs of another group.","zh":"一個群體可能對另一群體的事務有控制權。"},{"en":"A controlling hand in the affairs of means power to influence or direct another group’s decisions and life.","zh":"controlling hand in the affairs of 指有權影響或指揮另一群體的決定和生活。"},{"en":"Parents should guide children, but not have a controlling hand in every friendship they form.","zh":"父母應引導孩子，但不應對孩子建立的每段友誼都有控制權。"},{"en":"If one community controls another’s schools, jobs, and rights, domination is present.","zh":"如果一個社群控制另一社群的學校、工作和權利，就存在支配。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong interference or control.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈干預或控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"sections of society","meaning":"社會階層；社會群體","examples":[{"en":"Racism can place one section of society above another.","zh":"種族主義可以把一個社會群體置於另一個之上。"},{"en":"Sections of society are different groups within a society, such as workers, migrants, students, or ethnic communities.","zh":"sections of society 指社會中的不同群體，例如工人、移民、學生或族裔社群。"},{"en":"Public policy should consider different sections of society, not only wealthy voters.","zh":"公共政策應考慮不同社會群體，而不只是富裕選民。"},{"en":"If one section is given more rights than another, social fairness is damaged.","zh":"如果某一群體比另一群體享有更多權利，社會公平就受損。"},{"en":"The phrase divides society into groups for discussion.","zh":"這個片語把社會分成群體來討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"culturally or physically distinct","meaning":"在文化或身體上不同","examples":[{"en":"Some victims may not be culturally or physically distinct from the majority.","zh":"有些受害者在文化或身體上未必與大多數人不同。"},{"en":"Culturally or physically distinct means different in customs, language, appearance, or bodily features.","zh":"culturally or physically distinct 指在習俗、語言、外貌或身體特徵上不同。"},{"en":"A newcomer may not look physically distinct but may still speak a different home language.","zh":"新來者外貌上未必不同，但可能在家說不同語言。"},{"en":"Xenophobia can occur even when victims are not visibly different from the majority.","zh":"即使受害者與大多數人沒有可見差異，仇外心理仍可能發生。"},{"en":"The phrase compares cultural and bodily differences.","zh":"這個片語比較文化和身體差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the majority","meaning":"大多數人；主流群體","examples":[{"en":"A person may be treated as an outsider even if he or she resembles the majority.","zh":"即使某人看起來像大多數人，也可能被視為外來者。"},{"en":"The majority means the larger or dominant part of a group or society.","zh":"majority 指群體或社會中較大或主導的部分。"},{"en":"In a class of thirty students, the majority may prefer group work while a few prefer writing alone.","zh":"在三十人的班級中，大多數人可能偏好小組工作，而少數人偏好獨自寫作。"},{"en":"If the majority controls social norms, minorities may feel pressure to hide difference.","zh":"如果主流群體控制社會規範，少數群體可能感到需要隱藏差異。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the larger group, not necessarily the fairest one.","zh":"這個片語指較大群體，但不一定代表最公平的一方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"find oneself the victim of","meaning":"發現自己成為……的受害者","examples":[{"en":"A person may still find himself or herself the victim of xenophobic behaviour.","zh":"一個人仍可能發現自己成為仇外行為的受害者。"},{"en":"Find oneself the victim of means unexpectedly become affected or harmed by something.","zh":"find oneself the victim of 指意外地受某事影響或傷害。"},{"en":"A student may find herself the victim of online rumours after one photo is shared.","zh":"一張照片被分享後，學生可能發現自己成為網絡謠言的受害者。"},{"en":"If people are labelled outsiders, they may become victims of hostility even without doing anything wrong.","zh":"如果人們被標籤為外來者，即使沒有做錯事，也可能成為敵意的受害者。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the experience of becoming a victim.","zh":"這個片語強調成為受害者的經歷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"xenophobic behaviour","meaning":"仇外行為；排外行為","examples":[{"en":"Xenophobic behaviour can target people perceived as outsiders.","zh":"仇外行為可以針對被視為外來者的人。"},{"en":"Xenophobic behaviour means actions that show fear, dislike, or hostility toward foreigners or outsiders.","zh":"xenophobic behaviour 指表現出對外國人或外來者恐懼、厭惡或敵意的行為。"},{"en":"Refusing to serve a customer because they sound foreign is xenophobic behaviour.","zh":"因顧客聽起來像外國人而拒絕服務，就是仇外行為。"},{"en":"If xenophobic behaviour is ignored, it may become normal in a community.","zh":"如果仇外行為被忽視，它可能在社區中正常化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes action, not only attitude.","zh":"這個片語描述行動，而不只是態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"differ from","meaning":"與……不同","examples":[{"en":"Racism differs from xenophobia in its usual basis for discrimination.","zh":"種族主義與仇外心理在其通常歧視基礎上不同。"},{"en":"Differ from means be different from something else.","zh":"differ from 指與另一事物不同。"},{"en":"Spoken English can differ from written English in grammar and tone.","zh":"口語英語在文法和語氣上可以與書面英語不同。"},{"en":"If two concepts differ, students should learn the exact point of difference.","zh":"如果兩個概念不同，學生應學會準確差異點。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to compare differences clearly.","zh":"這個片語用來清楚比較差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"victims of the former","meaning":"前者的受害者","examples":[{"en":"Victims of the former may be targeted because of physical characteristics.","zh":"前者的受害者可能因身體特徵而被針對。"},{"en":"Victims of the former means people harmed by the first of two things just mentioned.","zh":"victims of the former 指受剛才提到的兩件事中前者傷害的人。"},{"en":"If stress and bullying are discussed, victims of the former means victims of stress.","zh":"如果討論壓力和欺凌，victims of the former 指壓力的受害者。"},{"en":"The phrase helps avoid repeating a long noun phrase.","zh":"這個片語有助避免重複很長的名詞片語。"},{"en":"In this context, “the former” refers to racism, not xenophobia.","zh":"在這個語境中，“the former” 指種族主義，而不是仇外心理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"perpetrators of acts of wrongdoing","meaning":"不當行為的施害者","examples":[{"en":"The perpetrators of acts of wrongdoing may target people seen as outsiders.","zh":"不當行為的施害者可能針對被視為外來者的人。"},{"en":"Perpetrators of acts of wrongdoing are people who commit harmful, illegal, or immoral acts.","zh":"perpetrators of acts of wrongdoing 指作出有害、違法或不道德行為的人。"},{"en":"Police investigate perpetrators of wrongdoing after an attack or fraud.","zh":"攻擊或欺詐後，警方會調查不當行為的施害者。"},{"en":"If perpetrators are not held responsible, victims may lose trust in justice.","zh":"如果施害者不用負責，受害者可能失去對公義的信任。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and refers to people who do wrong.","zh":"這個片語較正式，指作惡的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"share a likeness with","meaning":"與……有相似之處","examples":[{"en":"Some victims may share a likeness with the perpetrators of the crime.","zh":"有些受害者可能與犯罪施害者有相似之處。"},{"en":"Share a likeness with means look similar to or have features in common with someone.","zh":"share a likeness with 指與某人外貌相似或有共同特徵。"},{"en":"A child may share a likeness with a parent in face shape or smile.","zh":"孩子可能在臉形或笑容上與父母有相似之處。"},{"en":"If victims look similar to attackers but are still targeted, the cause may be perceived outsider status.","zh":"如果受害者與攻擊者外貌相似但仍被針對，原因可能是被視為外來者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes similarity in appearance or features.","zh":"這個片語描述外貌或特徵上的相似。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"total submission","meaning":"完全服從","examples":[{"en":"A dominated group may be forced into a position of total submission.","zh":"被支配的群體可能被迫處於完全服從的位置。"},{"en":"Total submission means complete obedience and lack of power to resist.","zh":"total submission 指完全服從，沒有反抗權力。"},{"en":"A child should not be forced into total submission; discipline should still allow dignity.","zh":"孩子不應被迫完全服從；紀律仍應保留尊嚴。"},{"en":"If one group controls another completely, the weaker group loses freedom and voice.","zh":"如果一個群體完全控制另一群體，較弱群體就失去自由和聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extreme domination.","zh":"這個片語描述極端支配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for each multiple-choice question.","zh":"考生為每條選擇題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choose the correct letter means select the answer option that matches the passage or question.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選出與文章或題目相符的答案選項字母。"},{"en":"If answer B matches the text, candidates should choose B.","zh":"如果 B 答案符合文章，考生應選 B。"},{"en":"Students should compare every option carefully before choosing the correct letter.","zh":"學生在選出正確字母前，應仔細比較每個選項。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard multiple-choice instruction.","zh":"這個片語是標準選擇題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"which of the following","meaning":"以下哪一項","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which of the following migrant groups is the largest.","zh":"題目問以下哪一個移民群體最大。"},{"en":"Which of the following means choose one option from the list given.","zh":"which of the following 指從所給列表中選出一項。"},{"en":"In a reading test, “which of the following” tells students to compare the answer choices.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，“which of the following” 提示學生比較答案選項。"},{"en":"If several options look similar, students must locate evidence in the passage.","zh":"如果幾個選項看似相似，學生必須在文章中定位證據。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a multiple-choice question.","zh":"這個片語引出選擇題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"migrant groups","meaning":"移民群體","examples":[{"en":"The passage compares several migrant groups.","zh":"文章比較幾個移民群體。"},{"en":"Migrant groups are categories of people who move from one place to another, such as workers, refugees, or immigrants.","zh":"migrant groups 指從一地遷往另一地的人的不同類別，例如工人、難民或移民。"},{"en":"A government may design different services for different migrant groups.","zh":"政府可能為不同移民群體設計不同服務。"},{"en":"If migrant groups have different legal statuses, their rights and needs may differ.","zh":"如果移民群體有不同法律身份，他們的權利和需要可能不同。"},{"en":"The phrase helps classify different kinds of migrants.","zh":"這個片語幫助分類不同種類的移民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the largest","meaning":"最大的","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which migrant group is the largest.","zh":"題目問哪個移民群體最大。"},{"en":"The largest means the biggest in number, size, or amount.","zh":"the largest 指在數量、大小或程度上最大。"},{"en":"The largest class in a school may need a bigger classroom.","zh":"學校中最大的班級可能需要較大的課室。"},{"en":"If one migrant group is the largest, it may require the most policy attention.","zh":"如果某移民群體最大，它可能最需要政策關注。"},{"en":"The phrase compares size or number.","zh":"這個片語比較大小或數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the author of the text","meaning":"文章作者","examples":[{"en":"The author of the text discusses racism, xenophobia and migration.","zh":"文章作者討論種族主義、仇外心理和移民。"},{"en":"The author of the text means the person who wrote the passage or article.","zh":"author of the text 指寫作該篇章或文章的人。"},{"en":"Students should identify what the author of the text claims before answering attitude questions.","zh":"學生回答態度題前，應識別文章作者主張甚麼。"},{"en":"If the author uses cautious language, students should not exaggerate the writer’s view.","zh":"如果作者使用謹慎語言，學生不應誇大作者觀點。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the writer behind the passage.","zh":"這個片語指篇章背後的寫作者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"emigrate","meaning":"移居外國","examples":[{"en":"People emigrate when they leave their country to live elsewhere.","zh":"人們離開自己的國家到別處居住時，就是移居外國。"},{"en":"Emigrate means leave one’s own country to live in another country.","zh":"emigrate 指離開自己的國家，到另一個國家生活。"},{"en":"A young nurse may emigrate to find better pay and training.","zh":"年輕護士可能為了更好薪酬和培訓而移居外國。"},{"en":"People may emigrate because of work, safety, education, or family reasons.","zh":"人們可能因工作、安全、教育或家庭原因移居外國。"},{"en":"The word focuses on leaving the home country.","zh":"這個詞集中於離開本國。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"exploitation of minority groups","meaning":"剝削少數群體","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions the exploitation of minority groups.","zh":"題目提到剝削少數群體。"},{"en":"Exploitation of minority groups means using less powerful groups unfairly for profit, labour, or political gain.","zh":"exploitation of minority groups 指為了利益、勞力或政治好處而不公平地利用較弱勢群體。"},{"en":"Employers may exploit minority workers by paying them less because they fear complaining.","zh":"僱主可能因少數族裔工人害怕投訴而少付工資剝削他們。"},{"en":"If exploitation continues, inequality and resentment can deepen.","zh":"如果剝削持續，不平等和怨恨可能加深。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unfair use of vulnerable groups.","zh":"這個片語描述不公平利用弱勢群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"minority groups","meaning":"少數群體","examples":[{"en":"Minority groups may be vulnerable to discrimination.","zh":"少數群體可能容易受到歧視。"},{"en":"Minority groups are groups smaller or less powerful than the majority in a society.","zh":"minority groups 指在社會中比主流群體人數較少或權力較弱的群體。"},{"en":"A school may create support programmes for minority groups who face language barriers.","zh":"學校可能為面對語言障礙的少數群體設立支援計劃。"},{"en":"If minority groups lack protection, they may face exclusion in work, housing, or education.","zh":"如果少數群體缺乏保護，可能在工作、住屋或教育中受排斥。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to groups with less social power or smaller numbers.","zh":"這個片語指社會權力較少或人數較少的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"deter someone from","meaning":"阻止某人做……","examples":[{"en":"Exploitation may deter some people from migrating.","zh":"剝削可能阻止一些人移民。"},{"en":"Deter someone from means discourage or prevent someone from doing something.","zh":"deter someone from 指使某人打消念頭或阻止某人做某事。"},{"en":"High tuition fees may deter students from applying to overseas universities.","zh":"高昂學費可能阻止學生申請海外大學。"},{"en":"If migrants hear many stories of abuse, they may hesitate to move.","zh":"如果移民聽到許多虐待故事，可能會猶豫是否遷移。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stopping action by fear, cost, or difficulty.","zh":"這個片語描述由恐懼、成本或困難阻止行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"within minority groups","meaning":"在少數群體內部","examples":[{"en":"The option discusses whether xenophobia exists within minority groups.","zh":"該選項討論仇外心理是否存在於少數群體內部。"},{"en":"Within minority groups means among people who themselves belong to smaller or less powerful groups.","zh":"within minority groups 指在本身屬於較小或較弱勢群體的人之間。"},{"en":"Conflicts can happen within minority groups when language, religion, or class differences exist.","zh":"當語言、宗教或階級差異存在，少數群體內部也可能有衝突。"},{"en":"If xenophobia exists within minority groups, discrimination is not only a majority problem.","zh":"如果仇外心理存在於少數群體內部，歧視就不只是主流群體的問題。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows the focus to relations inside minority communities.","zh":"這個片語把焦點收窄到少數族群內部關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no real way of knowing","meaning":"沒有真正方法知道","examples":[{"en":"There is no real way of knowing the exact number of abused migrants.","zh":"沒有真正方法知道受虐移民的確實數目。"},{"en":"No real way of knowing means there is no reliable method to know something for certain.","zh":"no real way of knowing 指沒有可靠方法確定知道某事。"},{"en":"If no attendance records were kept, there may be no real way of knowing how many students missed class.","zh":"如果沒有保留出席紀錄，就可能沒有真正方法知道多少學生缺課。"},{"en":"When abuse is hidden and unreported, exact numbers become impossible to confirm.","zh":"當虐待被隱藏且未被舉報，確實數字就變得無法確認。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses uncertainty caused by missing evidence.","zh":"這個片語表達由證據缺失造成的不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be discriminated against","meaning":"受到歧視","examples":[{"en":"Many migrants may be discriminated against in host societies.","zh":"許多移民可能在接收社會中受到歧視。"},{"en":"Be discriminated against means be treated unfairly because of identity, background, or status.","zh":"be discriminated against 指因身份、背景或地位而受到不公平對待。"},{"en":"A worker may be discriminated against if they are paid less because of nationality.","zh":"如果工人因國籍而被少付工資，就是受到歧視。"},{"en":"If people are discriminated against, they may lose access to jobs, housing, or services.","zh":"如果人們受到歧視，可能失去工作、住屋或服務機會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being the victim of unfair treatment.","zh":"這個片語描述成為不公平對待的受害者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"racial abuse cases","meaning":"種族虐待個案","examples":[{"en":"Not all racial abuse cases are documented or investigated.","zh":"並非所有種族虐待個案都被記錄或調查。"},{"en":"Racial abuse cases are incidents of insult, threat, attack, or mistreatment linked to race or origin.","zh":"racial abuse cases 指與種族或出身有關的侮辱、威脅、攻擊或不當對待事件。"},{"en":"A school should record racial abuse cases so repeated patterns are not ignored.","zh":"學校應記錄種族虐待個案，避免重複模式被忽視。"},{"en":"If cases are not reported, authorities may underestimate the problem.","zh":"如果個案沒有被舉報，當局可能低估問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to individual incidents of racial mistreatment.","zh":"這個片語指個別種族不當對待事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be documented or looked into","meaning":"被記錄或調查","examples":[{"en":"Some abuse cases are never documented or looked into.","zh":"有些虐待個案從未被記錄或調查。"},{"en":"Be documented or looked into means be officially recorded or investigated.","zh":"be documented or looked into 指被正式記錄或調查。"},{"en":"A complaint should be documented and looked into if it involves student safety.","zh":"如果投訴涉及學生安全，就應被記錄和調查。"},{"en":"If abuse is not documented or investigated, victims may feel abandoned.","zh":"如果虐待沒有被記錄或調查，受害者可能感到被遺棄。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recording and examining a problem.","zh":"這個片語描述記錄並檢視問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"at an alarming rate","meaning":"以驚人速度","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that the number of migrants is increasing at an alarming rate.","zh":"該選項暗示移民人數正以驚人速度增加。"},{"en":"At an alarming rate means increasing or changing so quickly that it causes worry.","zh":"at an alarming rate 指增加或改變得非常快，以致令人擔心。"},{"en":"If student absences rise at an alarming rate, the school must find out why.","zh":"如果學生缺席以驚人速度上升，學校必須找出原因。"},{"en":"Rapid change can alarm people when services and housing cannot keep up.","zh":"當服務和住屋追不上時，快速變化可能令人不安。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses speed and concern.","zh":"這個片語強調速度和憂慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complain about being abused","meaning":"投訴受到虐待","examples":[{"en":"Some victims may not complain about being abused.","zh":"有些受害者可能不會投訴受到虐待。"},{"en":"Complain about being abused means report or speak out about being mistreated or harmed.","zh":"complain about being abused 指舉報或說出自己受到不當對待或傷害。"},{"en":"A worker may not complain about being abused if they fear losing their job.","zh":"如果工人害怕失去工作，可能不會投訴受到虐待。"},{"en":"If victims stay silent, official records may show fewer cases than reality.","zh":"如果受害者保持沉默，官方記錄可能比現實顯示更少個案。"},{"en":"The phrase describes speaking up about mistreatment.","zh":"這個片語描述就不當對待發聲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"serious cases","meaning":"嚴重個案","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to whether only serious cases are documented.","zh":"該選項提到是否只有嚴重個案被記錄。"},{"en":"Serious cases are incidents that are severe, harmful, or urgent enough to require attention.","zh":"serious cases 指嚴重、有害或緊急到需要關注的事件。"},{"en":"Hospitals prioritise serious cases when many patients arrive at once.","zh":"當大量病人同時到達，醫院會優先處理嚴重個案。"},{"en":"If only serious cases are recorded, everyday abuse may be ignored.","zh":"如果只有嚴重個案被記錄，日常虐待可能被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to cases with high severity.","zh":"這個片語指嚴重程度高的個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"people in authority","meaning":"掌權者；當局人士","examples":[{"en":"People in authority sometimes deny that discrimination is a problem.","zh":"掌權者有時否認歧視是一個問題。"},{"en":"People in authority are officials or leaders who have power to make decisions.","zh":"people in authority 指有權作決定的官員或領導者。"},{"en":"Students may report bullying to people in authority, such as teachers or principals.","zh":"學生可能向老師或校長等掌權者舉報欺凌。"},{"en":"If people in authority deny a problem, victims may be less willing to speak up.","zh":"如果掌權者否認問題，受害者可能更不願發聲。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to those with official power.","zh":"這個片語指擁有官方權力的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"exaggerate the seriousness of","meaning":"誇大……的嚴重性","examples":[{"en":"Some people may exaggerate the seriousness of a social problem.","zh":"有些人可能誇大社會問題的嚴重性。"},{"en":"Exaggerate the seriousness of means make a problem sound worse than it really is.","zh":"exaggerate the seriousness of 指把問題說得比實際更嚴重。"},{"en":"A student may exaggerate the seriousness of a small mistake and feel unnecessary panic.","zh":"學生可能誇大小錯誤的嚴重性，並產生不必要恐慌。"},{"en":"If officials accuse victims of exaggerating abuse, real harm may be dismissed.","zh":"如果官員指責受害者誇大虐待，真實傷害可能被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase describes overstating severity.","zh":"這個片語描述過度強調嚴重程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"deny there is a problem","meaning":"否認有問題存在","examples":[{"en":"Authorities sometimes deny there is a problem.","zh":"當局有時否認有問題存在。"},{"en":"Deny there is a problem means refuse to accept that something harmful or serious exists.","zh":"deny there is a problem 指拒絕承認有害或嚴重事情存在。"},{"en":"A school may deny there is a bullying problem until parents demand action.","zh":"學校可能否認存在欺凌問題，直到家長要求行動。"},{"en":"If leaders deny a problem, they may delay solutions and deepen public mistrust.","zh":"如果領袖否認問題，可能延誤解決方案並加深公眾不信任。"},{"en":"The phrase describes refusal to acknowledge reality.","zh":"這個片語描述拒絕承認現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be eager to solve","meaning":"急於解決","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether authorities are eager to solve the problem.","zh":"該選項問當局是否急於解決問題。"},{"en":"Be eager to solve means strongly want to fix or deal with a problem.","zh":"be eager to solve 指強烈希望解決或處理問題。"},{"en":"A good teacher is eager to solve confusion before it spreads through the class.","zh":"好老師會急於在困惑蔓延全班前解決它。"},{"en":"If authorities are eager to solve discrimination, they will collect evidence and act quickly.","zh":"如果當局急於解決歧視，就會收集證據並迅速行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active willingness to help.","zh":"這個片語描述主動幫助的意願。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether statements agree with the information given.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與所給資料一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the information given means match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the text says migrants face discrimination, a statement with the same meaning agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文本說移民面對歧視，意思相同的陳述就與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students must check meaning carefully, not only repeated words.","zh":"學生必須仔細檢查意思，而不只是重複字詞。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in TRUE, FALSE and NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個片語常見於 TRUE、FALSE 和 NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章中的資料矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradict the information means say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章內容相反的意思。"},{"en":"If the passage says abuse is underreported, a statement saying all abuse is recorded contradicts it.","zh":"如果文章說虐待舉報不足，而陳述說所有虐待都被記錄，就是與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should choose FALSE only when the conflict is clear.","zh":"學生只有在衝突清楚時才應選 FALSE。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct disagreement with the text.","zh":"這個片語描述與文本直接不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"The answer is not given if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果沒有這方面的資料，答案就是 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not provide evidence about the statement.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有提供關於該陳述的證據。"},{"en":"If a passage discusses migration numbers but not migrants’ ages, there is no information on age.","zh":"如果文章討論移民數字但沒有談年齡，就沒有年齡方面的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when the text gives no information.","zh":"當文本沒有資料時，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"The phrase explains when NOT GIVEN is appropriate.","zh":"這個片語解釋何時適合選 NOT GIVEN。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"flee one’s country of origin","meaning":"逃離原籍國","examples":[{"en":"Some migrants may flee their country of origin because of danger.","zh":"有些移民可能因危險而逃離原籍國。"},{"en":"Flee one’s country of origin means escape from one’s original country to avoid danger or persecution.","zh":"flee one’s country of origin 指為避開危險或迫害而逃離原本國家。"},{"en":"A family may flee its country of origin when fighting reaches their town.","zh":"當戰鬥蔓延到城鎮，家庭可能逃離原籍國。"},{"en":"If people flee rather than choose freely to leave, they may need protection as refugees.","zh":"如果人們是逃離而不是自由選擇離開，可能需要難民保護。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses urgent and forced departure.","zh":"這個片語強調緊急和被迫離開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"political or social disorder","meaning":"政治或社會動亂","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to political or social disorder in a country.","zh":"該陳述提到一個國家的政治或社會動亂。"},{"en":"Political or social disorder means instability, conflict, unrest, or breakdown in public life.","zh":"political or social disorder 指公共生活中的不穩、衝突、動盪或秩序崩潰。"},{"en":"Strikes, riots, government collapse, or armed conflict can create political or social disorder.","zh":"罷工、暴動、政府瓦解或武裝衝突都可以造成政治或社會動亂。"},{"en":"If disorder becomes severe, people may leave home to seek safety elsewhere.","zh":"如果動亂變得嚴重，人們可能離家到別處尋求安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes instability in a society or state.","zh":"這個片語描述社會或國家的不穩定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"leave the countryside for the cities","meaning":"離開農村前往城市","examples":[{"en":"Many internal migrants leave the countryside for the cities.","zh":"許多內部移民離開農村前往城市。"},{"en":"Leave the countryside for the cities means move from rural areas to urban areas.","zh":"leave the countryside for the cities 指從鄉郊地區遷往城市地區。"},{"en":"Young adults may leave the countryside for the cities to find work or education.","zh":"年輕成年人可能為工作或教育離開農村前往城市。"},{"en":"If many people move to cities, urban housing and transport may become crowded.","zh":"如果許多人搬到城市，城市住屋和交通可能變得擁擠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rural-to-urban migration.","zh":"這個片語描述由農村到城市的遷移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be reluctant to acknowledge","meaning":"不願承認","examples":[{"en":"Governments may be reluctant to acknowledge discrimination and xenophobia.","zh":"政府可能不願承認歧視和仇外心理。"},{"en":"Be reluctant to acknowledge means be unwilling or slow to admit that something is true.","zh":"be reluctant to acknowledge 指不願或遲遲不承認某事是真實的。"},{"en":"A school may be reluctant to acknowledge bullying because it fears bad publicity.","zh":"學校可能因害怕負面宣傳而不願承認欺凌。"},{"en":"If leaders avoid admitting a problem, solutions may come too late.","zh":"如果領袖避免承認問題，解決方案可能來得太遲。"},{"en":"The phrase describes hesitation to accept reality.","zh":"這個片語描述對承認現實的猶豫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"acknowledge that","meaning":"承認","examples":[{"en":"Authorities may fail to acknowledge that discrimination exists.","zh":"當局可能未能承認歧視存在。"},{"en":"Acknowledge that means accept or admit that something is true.","zh":"acknowledge that 指接受或承認某事是真的。"},{"en":"A teacher may acknowledge that a lesson was too difficult and explain it again.","zh":"老師可能承認某課太難，並再次解釋。"},{"en":"If officials acknowledge that discrimination exists, they can begin to measure and address it.","zh":"如果官員承認歧視存在，就能開始量度和處理它。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an admission or recognition.","zh":"這個片語引出承認或認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"create a sense of insecurity","meaning":"造成不安全感","examples":[{"en":"Migration may create a sense of insecurity for some groups.","zh":"移民可能為某些群體造成不安全感。"},{"en":"Create a sense of insecurity means make people feel uncertain, threatened, or unsafe.","zh":"create a sense of insecurity 指令人感到不確定、受威脅或不安全。"},{"en":"Sudden staff changes can create a sense of insecurity in a workplace.","zh":"突然的人事變動可以在工作場所造成不安全感。"},{"en":"If people fear losing jobs or identity, they may react negatively to newcomers.","zh":"如果人們害怕失去工作或身份，可能對新來者作出負面反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a feeling of fear or instability.","zh":"這個片語描述恐懼或不穩定的感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"extremist groups","meaning":"極端組織","examples":[{"en":"Extremist groups may exploit fear and hostility toward migrants.","zh":"極端組織可能利用對移民的恐懼和敵意。"},{"en":"Extremist groups are organisations that hold extreme views and may encourage hatred or violence.","zh":"extremist groups 指持有極端觀點並可能鼓勵仇恨或暴力的組織。"},{"en":"Extremist groups often use simple slogans to blame complex problems on one target.","zh":"極端組織常使用簡單口號，把複雜問題怪罪於單一目標。"},{"en":"If fear spreads, extremist groups may gain members by promising easy answers.","zh":"如果恐懼擴散，極端組織可能透過承諾簡單答案來吸納成員。"},{"en":"The phrase describes groups that reject moderate democratic debate.","zh":"這個片語描述拒絕溫和民主辯論的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"uneducated and hostile","meaning":"教育程度低且帶敵意的","examples":[{"en":"The statement describes racist or xenophobic people as uneducated and hostile.","zh":"該陳述把種族主義或仇外的人描述為教育程度低且帶敵意。"},{"en":"Uneducated and hostile means lacking education and showing aggressive dislike or opposition.","zh":"uneducated and hostile 指缺乏教育並表現出攻擊性厭惡或反對。"},{"en":"A person can be educated but still hostile, so students should be careful with broad labels.","zh":"一個人可以受過教育但仍帶敵意，所以學生應小心使用概括標籤。"},{"en":"Hostility may grow from fear, propaganda, or social pressure, not only lack of schooling.","zh":"敵意可能來自恐懼、宣傳或社會壓力，而不只是缺乏教育。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a negative characterisation of people’s attitude and background.","zh":"這個片語描述對人的態度和背景的負面定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"return to one’s country of ancestry","meaning":"返回祖籍國","examples":[{"en":"People may return to their country of ancestry and still face exclusion.","zh":"人們可能返回祖籍國，卻仍面對排斥。"},{"en":"Return to one’s country of ancestry means go back to the country where one’s ancestors came from.","zh":"return to one’s country of ancestry 指回到自己祖先來自的國家。"},{"en":"A grandchild of emigrants may return to their country of ancestry to study language and culture.","zh":"移民後代可能返回祖籍國學習語言和文化。"},{"en":"Even if someone has ancestral roots in a place, locals may still see them as outsiders.","zh":"即使某人在某地有祖先根源，本地人仍可能視他為外來者。"},{"en":"The phrase connects movement with family or ethnic origin.","zh":"這個片語把遷移與家族或族裔來源連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"face xenophobia","meaning":"面對仇外心理","examples":[{"en":"People considered outsiders may face xenophobia.","zh":"被視為外來者的人可能面對仇外心理。"},{"en":"Face xenophobia means experience fear, dislike, or hostility because one is seen as foreign.","zh":"face xenophobia 指因被視為外國人而經歷恐懼、厭惡或敵意。"},{"en":"A new worker may face xenophobia if colleagues mock their accent and exclude them.","zh":"如果同事嘲笑新員工口音並排斥他，他可能面對仇外心理。"},{"en":"If people face xenophobia repeatedly, they may feel unsafe and isolated.","zh":"如果人們反覆面對仇外心理，可能感到不安全和孤立。"},{"en":"The phrase describes experiencing anti-outsider hostility.","zh":"這個片語描述經歷反外來者敵意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"forms of animal protein","meaning":"動物蛋白形式","examples":[{"en":"Some forms of animal protein require less water than others.","zh":"有些動物蛋白形式比其他形式需要較少水。"},{"en":"Forms of animal protein are different animal-based foods that provide protein, such as beef, chicken, fish, eggs, or dairy.","zh":"forms of animal protein 指提供蛋白質的不同動物性食物，例如牛肉、雞肉、魚、蛋或奶製品。"},{"en":"A family may choose different forms of animal protein depending on price, health needs, and culture.","zh":"家庭可能根據價格、健康需要和文化選擇不同動物蛋白形式。"},{"en":"If one form of animal protein needs more grain and water, it has a heavier environmental cost.","zh":"如果某種動物蛋白需要更多穀物和水，其環境成本就更高。"},{"en":"The phrase compares different protein sources from animals.","zh":"這個片語比較不同動物來源的蛋白質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"offer huge potential for","meaning":"為……提供巨大潛力","examples":[{"en":"Water-efficient technologies offer huge potential for raising productivity.","zh":"節水科技為提高生產力提供巨大潛力。"},{"en":"Offer huge potential for means provide a very strong possibility of improving or achieving something.","zh":"offer huge potential for 指為改善或達成某事提供非常大的可能性。"},{"en":"Online lessons offer huge potential for helping students who live far from schools.","zh":"網上課堂為幫助住得離學校很遠的學生提供巨大潛力。"},{"en":"If technology saves water, farmers may produce more food with fewer resources.","zh":"如果科技節省用水，農民可能用較少資源生產更多食物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a promising opportunity.","zh":"這個片語描述有前景的機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"these shifts","meaning":"這些轉變","examples":[{"en":"These shifts will move faster if water prices reflect real value.","zh":"如果水價反映真正價值，這些轉變會更快進行。"},{"en":"These shifts means the changes or transitions just mentioned.","zh":"these shifts 指剛才提到的變化或轉型。"},{"en":"These shifts in study habits may continue if students find online tools useful.","zh":"如果學生覺得網上工具有用，這些學習習慣轉變可能持續。"},{"en":"If prices and policies support change, shifts in farming and consumption can speed up.","zh":"如果價格和政策支持改變，農業和消費轉變可以加快。"},{"en":"The phrase points back to earlier changes in the text.","zh":"這個片語指回文中較早提到的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"more closely reflect","meaning":"更貼近地反映","examples":[{"en":"The price of water should more closely reflect its real value.","zh":"水價應更貼近地反映其真正價值。"},{"en":"More closely reflect means show or match something more accurately.","zh":"more closely reflect 指更準確地顯示或配合某事。"},{"en":"Exam grades should more closely reflect what students can actually do.","zh":"考試成績應更貼近地反映學生實際能做甚麼。"},{"en":"If water prices reflect real scarcity, people may waste less water.","zh":"如果水價反映真實稀缺性，人們可能較少浪費水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a better match between price, measure, or reality.","zh":"這個片語描述價格、量度或現實之間更準確配合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"real value","meaning":"真正價值","examples":[{"en":"The price of water should reflect its real value.","zh":"水價應反映其真正價值。"},{"en":"Real value means the true worth or importance of something, not just its current price.","zh":"real value 指某事真正的價值或重要性，而不只是目前價格。"},{"en":"The real value of sleep becomes clear when tired students cannot concentrate.","zh":"當疲倦學生無法集中精神，睡眠的真正價值就變得清楚。"},{"en":"If water is priced below its real value, people may waste it more easily.","zh":"如果水價低於其真正價值，人們可能更容易浪費水。"},{"en":"The phrase separates true importance from surface cost.","zh":"這個片語把真正重要性與表面成本分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所提供資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements agree with the information given in the passage.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與文章所提供資料一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the information given means match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the passage says beef uses more water, a statement with the same meaning agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說牛肉使用更多水，意思相同的陳述就與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should rely on the passage, not their own outside knowledge.","zh":"學生應依據文章，而不是自己的外部知識。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"if the statement agrees with","meaning":"如果陳述與……一致","examples":[{"en":"Students write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information.","zh":"如果陳述與資料一致，學生寫 TRUE。"},{"en":"If the statement agrees with means if the sentence matches what the passage says.","zh":"if the statement agrees with 指如果句子與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If a statement agrees with the text, students should not choose FALSE just because the wording is different.","zh":"如果陳述與文本一致，學生不應只因措辭不同而選 FALSE。"},{"en":"Meaning matters more than repeated words in reading questions.","zh":"在閱讀題中，意思比重複字詞更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the condition for choosing TRUE.","zh":"這個片語引出選 TRUE 的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"Students write FALSE if the statement contradicts the information.","zh":"如果陳述與資料相矛盾，學生寫 FALSE。"},{"en":"Contradict the information means say the opposite of the passage.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章相反的意思。"},{"en":"If the passage says water use increases, a statement saying it decreases contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說用水增加，而陳述說用水減少，就是與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should look for direct conflict before choosing FALSE.","zh":"學生在選 FALSE 前應尋找直接衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase marks disagreement with the text.","zh":"這個片語標示與文本不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"Students write NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果沒有這方面的資料，學生寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not tell us whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有告訴我們陳述是真還是假。"},{"en":"If the passage discusses water use but not food prices, there is no information on food prices.","zh":"如果文章討論用水但沒有討論食物價格，就沒有食物價格方面的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when evidence is missing.","zh":"當證據缺失時，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase explains when to choose NOT GIVEN.","zh":"這個片語解釋何時選 NOT GIVEN。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"vegetarians","meaning":"素食者","examples":[{"en":"Vegetarians usually avoid eating meat.","zh":"素食者通常避免吃肉。"},{"en":"Vegetarians are people who do not eat meat, though some may eat eggs or dairy products.","zh":"vegetarians 指不吃肉的人，不過有些可能吃蛋或奶製品。"},{"en":"A school canteen may offer vegetarian meals for students who do not eat meat.","zh":"學校飯堂可能為不吃肉的學生提供素食餐。"},{"en":"If more people become vegetarians, demand for meat may decrease.","zh":"如果更多人成為素食者，肉類需求可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people’s diet choices.","zh":"這個片語指人的飲食選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"meat eaters","meaning":"肉食者","examples":[{"en":"The statement compares vegetarians with meat eaters.","zh":"該陳述把素食者與肉食者作比較。"},{"en":"Meat eaters are people who regularly eat meat as part of their diet.","zh":"meat eaters 指日常飲食中經常吃肉的人。"},{"en":"Meat eaters may choose beef, chicken, pork, or fish depending on culture and price.","zh":"肉食者可能根據文化和價格選擇牛肉、雞肉、豬肉或魚。"},{"en":"A high number of meat eaters can increase demand for livestock and grain.","zh":"大量肉食者可以增加對牲畜和穀物的需求。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts with vegetarians.","zh":"這個片語與素食者形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"a typical Indian diet","meaning":"典型印度飲食","examples":[{"en":"A typical Indian diet requires less grain than a typical USA diet.","zh":"典型印度飲食比典型美國飲食需要較少穀物。"},{"en":"A typical Indian diet means the common pattern of food eaten by many people in India, though diets vary widely.","zh":"typical Indian diet 指許多印度人常見的飲食模式，雖然飲食差異很大。"},{"en":"A typical Indian diet may include rice, lentils, vegetables, spices, and less meat than some Western diets.","zh":"典型印度飲食可能包括米飯、扁豆、蔬菜、香料，肉類比某些西方飲食少。"},{"en":"If a diet uses less meat, it may require less grain to feed livestock.","zh":"如果飲食使用較少肉類，就可能需要較少穀物去飼養牲畜。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a general dietary pattern, not every individual meal.","zh":"這個片語描述一般飲食模式，而不是每個人的每餐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"a typical USA diet","meaning":"典型美國飲食","examples":[{"en":"A typical USA diet is often rich in livestock products.","zh":"典型美國飲食通常含有豐富畜產品。"},{"en":"A typical USA diet means a common American eating pattern, often including more meat and dairy than some other diets.","zh":"typical USA diet 指常見美國飲食模式，通常比某些其他飲食包含更多肉類和奶製品。"},{"en":"A typical USA diet may include burgers, beef, chicken, cheese, and processed foods.","zh":"典型美國飲食可能包括漢堡、牛肉、雞肉、芝士和加工食品。"},{"en":"If a diet contains many livestock products, it may require more grain and water indirectly.","zh":"如果飲食包含許多畜產品，就可能間接需要更多穀物和水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a general national diet pattern, not every American’s diet.","zh":"這個片語描述一般國家飲食模式，而不是每個美國人的飲食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"growing grain","meaning":"種植穀物","examples":[{"en":"Growing grain requires large quantities of water.","zh":"種植穀物需要大量水。"},{"en":"Growing grain means cultivating crops such as wheat, rice, maize, or barley.","zh":"growing grain 指種植小麥、稻米、粟米或大麥等作物。"},{"en":"Farmers growing grain must consider rainfall, irrigation, soil quality, and pests.","zh":"種植穀物的農民必須考慮降雨、灌溉、土壤質素和害蟲。"},{"en":"If grain is used to feed livestock, water is used indirectly to produce meat.","zh":"如果穀物用來飼養牲畜，水就被間接用於生產肉類。"},{"en":"The phrase describes crop production for food or animal feed.","zh":"這個片語描述用作食物或飼料的作物生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"raising beef","meaning":"飼養肉牛","examples":[{"en":"Raising beef is often linked with high grain and water use.","zh":"飼養肉牛常與高穀物和高用水量有關。"},{"en":"Raising beef means keeping cattle for meat production.","zh":"raising beef 指飼養牛隻以生產牛肉。"},{"en":"Farmers raising beef need land, feed, water, veterinary care, and transport.","zh":"飼養肉牛的農民需要土地、飼料、水、獸醫護理和運輸。"},{"en":"Because cattle eat grain or grass, beef production can require large amounts of water.","zh":"因為牛吃穀物或草，牛肉生產可能需要大量水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes producing beef from cattle.","zh":"這個片語描述由牛隻生產牛肉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"move from the country to the city","meaning":"從鄉村搬到城市","examples":[{"en":"People who move from the country to the city may use more water.","zh":"從鄉村搬到城市的人可能使用更多水。"},{"en":"Move from the country to the city means leave rural areas and settle in urban areas.","zh":"move from the country to the city 指離開鄉郊地區並定居城市地區。"},{"en":"A young worker may move from the country to the city for a factory job.","zh":"年輕工人可能為工廠工作從鄉村搬到城市。"},{"en":"City life can change water use because people may use piped water, industry, and urban services more often.","zh":"城市生活可以改變用水量，因為人們可能更常使用自來水、工業和城市服務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rural-to-urban migration.","zh":"這個片語描述由鄉村到城市的遷移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"increase water consumption considerably","meaning":"大幅增加用水量","examples":[{"en":"Urban living may increase water consumption considerably.","zh":"城市生活可能大幅增加用水量。"},{"en":"Increase water consumption considerably means make the amount of water used much higher.","zh":"increase water consumption considerably 指令用水量大幅上升。"},{"en":"Installing many new showers in a sports centre can increase water consumption considerably.","zh":"在體育中心安裝許多新淋浴設備可以大幅增加用水量。"},{"en":"If people move into cities and use more services, total water demand may rise sharply.","zh":"如果人們搬入城市並使用更多服務，總用水需求可能急升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large rise in water use.","zh":"這個片語描述用水量大幅上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"future conflicts","meaning":"未來衝突","examples":[{"en":"Future conflicts may be linked to water and food shortages.","zh":"未來衝突可能與水和糧食短缺有關。"},{"en":"Future conflicts are disagreements, struggles, or wars that may happen later.","zh":"future conflicts 指日後可能發生的分歧、鬥爭或戰爭。"},{"en":"Future conflicts over housing may grow if cities do not build enough homes.","zh":"如果城市不建足夠房屋，未來關於住屋的衝突可能增加。"},{"en":"If water becomes scarce, countries or communities may compete more fiercely.","zh":"如果水變得稀缺，國家或社區可能更激烈競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase points to possible problems ahead.","zh":"這個片語指向將來可能出現的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"as much over…as over…","meaning":"因……而爆發的程度與因……一樣","examples":[{"en":"Future conflicts may be fought as much over food as over oil.","zh":"未來衝突可能因糧食而爆發的程度與因石油而爆發一樣。"},{"en":"As much over A as over B means A may be just as important a cause as B.","zh":"as much over A as over B 指 A 可能與 B 一樣是重要成因。"},{"en":"Family arguments may be as much over respect as over money.","zh":"家庭爭執可能因尊重而起的程度與因金錢而起一樣。"},{"en":"If food becomes scarce, it may cause conflict as seriously as fuel does.","zh":"如果糧食變得稀缺，它造成衝突的嚴重程度可能與燃料一樣。"},{"en":"The phrase compares two causes and says both matter greatly.","zh":"這個片語比較兩個成因，並表示兩者都非常重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"import something annually","meaning":"每年進口某物","examples":[{"en":"Some countries import large quantities of grain annually.","zh":"有些國家每年進口大量穀物。"},{"en":"Import something annually means bring goods from another country every year.","zh":"import something annually 指每年從另一國帶入商品。"},{"en":"A supermarket may import fruit annually from countries with warmer climates.","zh":"超級市場可能每年從較溫暖國家進口水果。"},{"en":"If a country imports grain every year, it may depend on global markets for food security.","zh":"如果一個國家每年進口穀物，可能依賴全球市場維持糧食安全。"},{"en":"The phrase combines trade with yearly repetition.","zh":"這個片語結合貿易和每年重複。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"paragraph contains information about","meaning":"段落包含關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which paragraph contains information about a topic.","zh":"學生識別哪一段包含關於某課題的資料。"},{"en":"Paragraph contains information about means a paragraph includes details related to a particular idea.","zh":"paragraph contains information about 指某段包含與特定想法相關的細節。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students scan each paragraph to see which one contains information about a given issue.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生快速瀏覽每段，看哪一段包含關於指定議題的資料。"},{"en":"If the exact words are different, students must still match the meaning.","zh":"即使用詞不同，學生仍必須配對意思。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in paragraph-location questions.","zh":"這個片語用於段落定位題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"threats to water supplies","meaning":"對水源供應的威脅","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses several threats to water supplies.","zh":"文章討論幾種對水源供應的威脅。"},{"en":"Threats to water supplies are dangers that may reduce the amount, quality, or reliability of available water.","zh":"threats to water supplies 指可能減少可用水的數量、質素或可靠性的危險。"},{"en":"Pollution, overuse, drought, and leaking pipes can be threats to water supplies.","zh":"污染、過度使用、乾旱和漏水管都可以是對水源供應的威脅。"},{"en":"If water supplies are threatened, farming, health, and daily life may suffer.","zh":"如果水源供應受威脅，農業、健康和日常生活可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes risks to water availability.","zh":"這個片語描述對水可用性的風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"the volume of water","meaning":"水量","examples":[{"en":"The volume of water needed for grain production is very large.","zh":"穀物生產所需水量非常大。"},{"en":"The volume of water means the amount of water measured by capacity.","zh":"volume of water 指按容量量度的水的數量。"},{"en":"A swimming pool holds a much larger volume of water than a bathtub.","zh":"游泳池的水量遠比浴缸大。"},{"en":"If grain production needs huge water volumes, dry countries may struggle to grow enough crops.","zh":"如果穀物生產需要巨大水量，乾旱國家可能難以種出足夠農作物。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on amount, not cleanliness or speed.","zh":"這個片語集中於數量，而不是潔淨度或速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"needed for irrigation","meaning":"灌溉所需的","examples":[{"en":"Huge volumes of water are needed for irrigation.","zh":"灌溉需要巨大水量。"},{"en":"Needed for irrigation means required to supply water to crops or farmland.","zh":"needed for irrigation 指供應農作物或農地用水所必需的。"},{"en":"Farmers use pipes, canals, or sprinklers when water is needed for irrigation.","zh":"當需要灌溉用水，農民會使用水管、渠道或灑水器。"},{"en":"If rainfall is low, more water may be needed for irrigation.","zh":"如果降雨少，灌溉所需水量可能更多。"},{"en":"The phrase explains agricultural water demand.","zh":"這個片語解釋農業用水需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"grain production","meaning":"穀物生產","examples":[{"en":"Water is essential for grain production.","zh":"水對穀物生產至關重要。"},{"en":"Grain production means growing crops such as rice, wheat, maize, and barley.","zh":"grain production 指種植稻米、小麥、粟米和大麥等作物。"},{"en":"A country with strong grain production may depend less on food imports.","zh":"穀物生產強的國家可能較少依賴糧食進口。"},{"en":"If water becomes scarce, grain production may fall and food prices may rise.","zh":"如果水變得稀缺，穀物生產可能下降，食物價格可能上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the farming of staple crops.","zh":"這個片語描述主糧作物的種植。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"underground water supplies","meaning":"地下水供應","examples":[{"en":"Over-pumping threatens underground water supplies.","zh":"過度抽水威脅地下水供應。"},{"en":"Underground water supplies are water stored below the ground in aquifers or rock layers.","zh":"underground water supplies 指儲存在地下含水層或岩層中的水。"},{"en":"Villages may depend on underground water supplies when rivers dry up.","zh":"當河流乾涸，村莊可能依賴地下水供應。"},{"en":"If groundwater is pumped faster than it is replaced, wells may run dry.","zh":"如果地下水抽取速度快於補充速度，水井可能乾涸。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to hidden water resources beneath the surface.","zh":"這個片語指地表以下隱藏的水資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"be responsible for","meaning":"對……負責；造成","examples":[{"en":"Population growth will be responsible for new water pressures.","zh":"人口增長將造成新的水資源壓力。"},{"en":"Be responsible for means be the cause of something or have duty over it.","zh":"be responsible for 指是某事的原因，或對某事有責任。"},{"en":"Poor planning can be responsible for traffic jams near a school.","zh":"規劃不善可以造成學校附近交通擠塞。"},{"en":"If population rises, more people need drinking water, food, and sanitation.","zh":"如果人口上升，更多人需要飲用水、食物和衛生設施。"},{"en":"In this context, the phrase means cause or create.","zh":"在這個語境中，這個片語意思是造成或產生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"water-related poverty","meaning":"與水相關的貧困","examples":[{"en":"Population growth may create a new type of water-related poverty.","zh":"人口增長可能造成一種新的與水相關的貧困。"},{"en":"Water-related poverty is poverty made worse by lack of safe, affordable, or reliable water.","zh":"water-related poverty 指因缺乏安全、可負擔或可靠水源而惡化的貧困。"},{"en":"A family may face water-related poverty if it spends hours collecting water instead of working or studying.","zh":"如果家庭花數小時取水而不能工作或學習，就可能面對與水相關的貧困。"},{"en":"If water becomes expensive or scarce, poor communities may suffer first.","zh":"如果水變得昂貴或稀缺，貧困社區可能首先受害。"},{"en":"The phrase links poverty with water access.","zh":"這個片語把貧困與取水問題連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"demand greater water supplies","meaning":"需要更多水源供應","examples":[{"en":"Industrialisation demands greater water supplies.","zh":"工業化需要更多水源供應。"},{"en":"Demand greater water supplies means require more water to support activity or growth.","zh":"demand greater water supplies 指需要更多水來支持活動或增長。"},{"en":"A growing hospital may demand greater water supplies for cleaning, cooking, and patient care.","zh":"擴大的醫院可能需要更多水源供應，用於清潔、煮食和病人護理。"},{"en":"If factories expand, they often need more water for production and cooling.","zh":"如果工廠擴張，通常需要更多水作生產和冷卻。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rising need for water.","zh":"這個片語描述用水需求上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"考生為每條題目選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choose the correct letter means select the option letter that gives the right answer.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇給出正確答案的選項字母。"},{"en":"Students should check A, B, C and D before choosing the correct letter.","zh":"學生應先檢查 A、B、C 和 D，再選出正確字母。"},{"en":"If two choices seem close, evidence from the passage decides the answer.","zh":"如果兩個選項看似相近，文章證據決定答案。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard instruction for multiple-choice questions.","zh":"這個片語是選擇題的標準指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"water supply is running low","meaning":"水源供應正在減少","examples":[{"en":"Our water supply is running low because demand is increasing.","zh":"由於需求增加，我們的水源供應正在減少。"},{"en":"Water supply is running low means the available amount of water is becoming insufficient.","zh":"water supply is running low 指可用水量正變得不足。"},{"en":"A campsite may warn visitors that the water supply is running low after several dry weeks.","zh":"乾旱幾週後，營地可能警告遊客水源供應正在減少。"},{"en":"If demand rises and rainfall falls, water supply may run low quickly.","zh":"如果需求上升而降雨下降，水源供應可能很快變少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shortage developing.","zh":"這個片語描述短缺正在形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"exported globally","meaning":"全球出口","examples":[{"en":"Grain is exported globally through international markets.","zh":"穀物透過國際市場全球出口。"},{"en":"Exported globally means sold and sent to many countries around the world.","zh":"exported globally 指被出售並運往世界許多國家。"},{"en":"A successful local product may be exported globally if overseas demand grows.","zh":"如果海外需求增加，成功本地產品可能全球出口。"},{"en":"If grain is exported globally, food supply in one country can depend on harvests elsewhere.","zh":"如果穀物全球出口，一國糧食供應可能依賴其他地方的收成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes worldwide trade.","zh":"這個片語描述全球貿易。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"increase rapidly","meaning":"急速增加","examples":[{"en":"The world’s population continues to increase rapidly.","zh":"世界人口持續急速增加。"},{"en":"Increase rapidly means grow or rise very quickly.","zh":"increase rapidly 指非常快速地增長或上升。"},{"en":"A school’s waiting list may increase rapidly after exam results improve.","zh":"學校考試成績改善後，輪候名單可能急速增加。"},{"en":"If population increases rapidly, demand for water, food, and housing rises too.","zh":"如果人口急速增加，對水、食物和住屋的需求也會上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fast growth.","zh":"這個片語描述快速增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"waste water foolishly","meaning":"愚蠢地浪費水","examples":[{"en":"Some people argue that societies waste water foolishly.","zh":"有些人認為社會愚蠢地浪費水。"},{"en":"Waste water foolishly means use water carelessly or without good reason.","zh":"waste water foolishly 指粗心或沒有好理由地使用水。"},{"en":"Leaving the tap running while brushing teeth wastes water foolishly.","zh":"刷牙時讓水龍頭一直開着，就是愚蠢地浪費水。"},{"en":"If water is cheap, people may waste it without noticing its real value.","zh":"如果水很便宜，人們可能在沒有注意其真正價值下浪費它。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises careless water use.","zh":"這個片語批評粗心用水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"high-meat diet","meaning":"高肉食飲食","examples":[{"en":"A high-meat diet requires more grain and water.","zh":"高肉食飲食需要更多穀物和水。"},{"en":"A high-meat diet is an eating pattern that includes large amounts of meat.","zh":"high-meat diet 指包含大量肉類的飲食模式。"},{"en":"A person on a high-meat diet may eat meat at most meals.","zh":"採用高肉食飲食的人可能大多數餐都吃肉。"},{"en":"Because livestock often need feed and water, high-meat diets can increase resource use.","zh":"由於牲畜通常需要飼料和水，高肉食飲食可以增加資源使用。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts with plant-based or low-meat diets.","zh":"這個片語與植物性或低肉食飲食形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"cause more water to be used","meaning":"導致使用更多水","examples":[{"en":"A high-meat diet can cause more water to be used.","zh":"高肉食飲食可以導致使用更多水。"},{"en":"Cause more water to be used means lead to higher water consumption directly or indirectly.","zh":"cause more water to be used 指直接或間接導致用水量增加。"},{"en":"Long showers cause more water to be used at home.","zh":"長時間淋浴會導致家中使用更多水。"},{"en":"If meat production needs grain and livestock care, more water may be used before food reaches the table.","zh":"如果肉類生產需要穀物和牲畜照顧，食物到餐桌前可能已使用更多水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an increase in water demand.","zh":"這個片語描述用水需求增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"feed livestock","meaning":"飼養牲畜","examples":[{"en":"It takes grain to feed livestock.","zh":"飼養牲畜需要穀物。"},{"en":"Feed livestock means give farm animals food so they can grow and produce meat, milk, or eggs.","zh":"feed livestock 指餵養農場動物，使牠們成長並生產肉、奶或蛋。"},{"en":"Farmers may feed livestock with grain, grass, hay, or mixed feed.","zh":"農民可能用穀物、草、乾草或混合飼料飼養牲畜。"},{"en":"If more grain is used to feed livestock, less grain may be available directly for people.","zh":"如果更多穀物用來飼養牲畜，可直接供人食用的穀物可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes feeding farm animals.","zh":"這個片語描述餵養農場動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"industrial processes","meaning":"工業過程","examples":[{"en":"Industrial processes often require large amounts of water.","zh":"工業過程通常需要大量水。"},{"en":"Industrial processes are steps used in factories or industries to make, clean, cool, or package products.","zh":"industrial processes 指工廠或工業中用來製造、清潔、冷卻或包裝產品的步驟。"},{"en":"Washing, heating, cooling, and chemical treatment can be industrial processes.","zh":"清洗、加熱、冷卻和化學處理都可以是工業過程。"},{"en":"If industry expands, water demand may rise because many processes depend on water.","zh":"如果工業擴張，由於許多過程依賴水，用水需求可能上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes production-related operations.","zh":"這個片語描述與生產有關的操作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"produce meat","meaning":"生產肉類","examples":[{"en":"Some processes are used to produce meat products.","zh":"有些過程用來生產肉類產品。"},{"en":"Produce meat means raise, process, or prepare animal products for food.","zh":"produce meat 指飼養、加工或準備動物產品作食物。"},{"en":"Farms, slaughterhouses, and factories may all be involved in producing meat.","zh":"農場、屠宰場和工廠都可能參與生產肉類。"},{"en":"Producing meat can require water for animals, cleaning, processing, and packaging.","zh":"生產肉類可能需要水來供動物飲用、清潔、加工和包裝。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to making meat available as food.","zh":"這個片語指使肉類成為可食用食品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"packaging of meat products","meaning":"肉類產品包裝","examples":[{"en":"The packaging of meat products may involve several processes.","zh":"肉類產品包裝可能涉及幾個過程。"},{"en":"Packaging of meat products means wrapping, sealing, labelling, and preparing meat for sale or transport.","zh":"packaging of meat products 指包裹、密封、貼標籤和準備肉類供銷售或運輸。"},{"en":"Supermarkets need careful packaging of meat products to keep food clean and safe.","zh":"超級市場需要仔細包裝肉類產品，以保持食物清潔和安全。"},{"en":"Packaging may use water indirectly through cleaning equipment and factory processes.","zh":"包裝可能透過清洗設備和工廠過程間接使用水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the final preparation of meat for consumers.","zh":"這個片語描述肉類給消費者前的最後準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"intensive washing process","meaning":"密集清洗程序","examples":[{"en":"An intensive washing process uses a lot of water.","zh":"密集清洗程序使用大量水。"},{"en":"An intensive washing process is a thorough cleaning procedure that requires repeated or heavy washing.","zh":"intensive washing process 指需要反覆或大量清洗的徹底清潔程序。"},{"en":"A hospital laundry may use an intensive washing process to remove germs from sheets.","zh":"醫院洗衣房可能使用密集清洗程序，以去除床單上的細菌。"},{"en":"If factories use intensive washing, water consumption can increase quickly.","zh":"如果工廠使用密集清洗，用水量可以迅速增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cleaning that is heavy and water-demanding.","zh":"這個片語描述大量用水的清潔程序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"reduce the use of water","meaning":"減少用水","examples":[{"en":"Some policies can reduce the use of water.","zh":"有些政策可以減少用水。"},{"en":"Reduce the use of water means lower the amount of water consumed.","zh":"reduce the use of water 指降低用水量。"},{"en":"Installing low-flow taps can reduce the use of water in school toilets.","zh":"安裝低流量水龍頭可以減少學校洗手間用水。"},{"en":"If farmers use drip irrigation, they may reduce water use without lowering crop output.","zh":"如果農民使用滴灌，可能在不降低農作物產量下減少用水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes saving water.","zh":"這個片語描述節約水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"without adversely affecting","meaning":"在不對……造成不良影響的情況下","examples":[{"en":"The aim is to reduce water use without adversely affecting food supply.","zh":"目標是在不對糧食供應造成不良影響的情況下減少用水。"},{"en":"Without adversely affecting means without harming or damaging something.","zh":"without adversely affecting 指不傷害或損害某事。"},{"en":"A school may reduce homework without adversely affecting exam preparation if tasks become more focused.","zh":"如果任務更集中，學校可以減少功課，而不對考試準備造成不良影響。"},{"en":"If water use falls but food supply stays stable, the policy is more acceptable.","zh":"如果用水下降但糧食供應保持穩定，政策就更容易被接受。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a desired change without negative side effects.","zh":"這個片語顯示希望改變但沒有負面副作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"food supply","meaning":"糧食供應","examples":[{"en":"Governments worry that water shortages may damage the food supply.","zh":"政府擔心水資源短缺可能損害糧食供應。"},{"en":"Food supply means the amount and availability of food for a population.","zh":"food supply 指供應給人口的食物數量和可得性。"},{"en":"A city’s food supply depends on farms, transport, storage, and markets.","zh":"城市糧食供應依賴農場、運輸、儲存和市場。"},{"en":"If drought reduces harvests, food supply may become unstable.","zh":"如果乾旱減少收成，糧食供應可能變得不穩。"},{"en":"The phrase describes whether people can get enough food.","zh":"這個片語描述人們能否獲得足夠食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"growing fewer crops","meaning":"種植較少農作物","examples":[{"en":"Growing fewer crops would reduce food production.","zh":"種植較少農作物會減少糧食生產。"},{"en":"Growing fewer crops means cultivating a smaller amount or fewer kinds of crops.","zh":"growing fewer crops 指種植較少數量或較少種類的農作物。"},{"en":"A farmer may grow fewer crops during a drought to save water.","zh":"農民可能在乾旱期間種植較少農作物以節省水。"},{"en":"If fewer crops are grown, food prices may rise and supply may fall.","zh":"如果種植較少農作物，食物價格可能上升，供應可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a reduction in agricultural output.","zh":"這個片語描述農業產出的減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"falling population levels","meaning":"人口水平下降","examples":[{"en":"Falling population levels would reduce pressure on water resources.","zh":"人口水平下降會減少水資源壓力。"},{"en":"Falling population levels means the number of people in a place is decreasing.","zh":"falling population levels 指某地人口數量正在減少。"},{"en":"A town with falling population levels may have fewer students and empty shops.","zh":"人口水平下降的城鎮可能有較少學生和空置商店。"},{"en":"If population falls, demand for water, food, housing, and transport may decline.","zh":"如果人口下降，對水、食物、住屋和交通的需求可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes demographic decrease.","zh":"這個片語描述人口減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"water war","meaning":"水資源戰爭","examples":[{"en":"A water war would be difficult to win.","zh":"水資源戰爭會很難取勝。"},{"en":"A water war is a conflict fought over access to water resources.","zh":"water war 指為取得水資源而爆發的衝突。"},{"en":"Two villages might argue over water before a true water war ever begins.","zh":"在真正水資源戰爭開始之前，兩條村可能已因用水而爭執。"},{"en":"If rivers, lakes, or aquifers become scarce, water can become a source of conflict.","zh":"如果河流、湖泊或地下水變得稀缺，水可以成為衝突來源。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that water scarcity can become politically dangerous.","zh":"這個片語警告水資源短缺可能在政治上變得危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"the driest countries","meaning":"最乾旱的國家","examples":[{"en":"The driest countries may face the greatest water pressure.","zh":"最乾旱的國家可能面對最大水資源壓力。"},{"en":"The driest countries are countries with very low rainfall or limited freshwater resources.","zh":"driest countries 指降雨很少或淡水資源有限的國家。"},{"en":"The driest countries may depend on wells, desalination, or imported food.","zh":"最乾旱的國家可能依賴水井、海水化淡或進口糧食。"},{"en":"If rainfall is low and population grows, water stress becomes more severe.","zh":"如果降雨低而人口增長，水資源壓力就變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies countries most exposed to water scarcity.","zh":"這個片語指出最容易受水資源短缺影響的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"the richest countries","meaning":"最富有的國家","examples":[{"en":"The richest countries may have an advantage in grain markets.","zh":"最富有的國家可能在穀物市場中有優勢。"},{"en":"The richest countries are countries with the greatest economic wealth and purchasing power.","zh":"richest countries 指擁有最大經濟財富和購買力的國家。"},{"en":"The richest countries can often buy food, fuel, or technology more easily than poorer countries.","zh":"最富有的國家通常比貧窮國家更容易購買食物、燃料或科技。"},{"en":"If grain becomes scarce, rich countries may outbid poorer countries for imports.","zh":"如果穀物變得稀缺，富國可能以更高價格搶購進口糧食。"},{"en":"The phrase compares countries by economic strength.","zh":"這個片語按經濟實力比較國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"more forceful","meaning":"更強硬的","examples":[{"en":"The question compares richer countries with more forceful countries.","zh":"題目把較富有國家與更強硬國家作比較。"},{"en":"More forceful means stronger, more aggressive, or more willing to use pressure.","zh":"more forceful 指更強勢、更具攻擊性或更願意施壓。"},{"en":"A more forceful student may dominate a group discussion if the teacher does not manage turn-taking.","zh":"如果老師不管理發言次序，較強勢的學生可能主導小組討論。"},{"en":"In resource conflicts, more forceful countries may try to secure supplies through pressure.","zh":"在資源衝突中，更強硬的國家可能試圖透過施壓保障供應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strength of action, not necessarily fairness.","zh":"這個片語描述行動力度，而不一定代表公平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"the biggest population","meaning":"最大人口","examples":[{"en":"Countries with the biggest population may have high water demand.","zh":"擁有最大人口的國家可能有高用水需求。"},{"en":"The biggest population means the largest number of people living in a country or area.","zh":"biggest population 指居住在某國家或地區的人數最多。"},{"en":"A city with the biggest population in a region usually needs the most schools and hospitals.","zh":"一個地區中人口最大的城市通常需要最多學校和醫院。"},{"en":"If a country has a huge population, even small increases in water use per person can create major pressure.","zh":"如果一個國家人口巨大，即使每人用水少量增加，也會造成重大壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase compares places by number of people.","zh":"這個片語按人口數量比較地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 81 - Migrants and Refugees - Racial Discrimination and Xenophobia.pdf","sourcePage":25}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 82":[{"front":"population growth","meaning":"人口增長","examples":[{"en":"Population growth is increasing pressure on the world’s water resources.","zh":"人口增長正在增加世界水資源的壓力。"},{"en":"Population growth means an increase in the number of people living in a place.","zh":"人口增長指某地居住人口數目的增加。"},{"en":"A city may need more schools and hospitals when population growth is fast.","zh":"當人口增長迅速，城市可能需要更多學校和醫院。"},{"en":"Population growth can create higher demand for food, housing, jobs and water.","zh":"人口增長可以造成對食物、房屋、工作和水的更高需求。"},{"en":"If population growth is not planned for, public services may become overcrowded.","zh":"如果沒有為人口增長作規劃，公共服務可能變得過度擠迫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sentence millions to","meaning":"令數以百萬計的人陷入……","examples":[{"en":"Population growth is sentencing millions of people to hydrological poverty.","zh":"人口增長正在令數以百萬計的人陷入水資源貧困。"},{"en":"To sentence millions to a condition means to force millions of people into a difficult situation.","zh":"sentence millions to 某種狀況，指迫使數以百萬計的人陷入困難處境。"},{"en":"Poor housing policy can sentence thousands of families to years of overcrowded living.","zh":"差劣房屋政策可以令數以千計家庭陷入多年擠迫生活。"},{"en":"If water systems fail, communities may be sentenced to daily shortages and long queues.","zh":"如果供水系統失效，社區可能被迫陷入每日缺水和長時間排隊。"},{"en":"The phrase is strong because it suggests people are trapped as if by a punishment.","zh":"這個短語語氣很強，因為它暗示人們像受懲罰一樣被困住。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hydrological poverty","meaning":"水資源貧困","examples":[{"en":"Hydrological poverty is a local form of poverty that is difficult to escape.","zh":"水資源貧困是一種難以擺脫的地方性貧困。"},{"en":"Hydrological poverty means poverty caused or deepened by not having enough usable water.","zh":"水資源貧困指因缺乏足夠可用水而造成或加深的貧困。"},{"en":"A farming village may fall into hydrological poverty if wells dry up and crops fail.","zh":"如果水井乾涸、農作物失收，農村可能陷入水資源貧困。"},{"en":"Hydrological poverty can keep children out of school when they must spend hours collecting water.","zh":"當孩子必須花數小時取水，水資源貧困可以令他們無法上學。"},{"en":"Unlike a short drought, hydrological poverty can become a long-term trap.","zh":"不同於短暫乾旱，水資源貧困可能成為長期困局。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"at a time when","meaning":"在……的時候","examples":[{"en":"At a time when drought is in the news, more serious water shortages are emerging.","zh":"在乾旱成為新聞焦點的時候，更嚴重的水資源短缺正在出現。"},{"en":"At a time when means during a period in which something important is happening.","zh":"at a time when 指在某件重要事情正在發生的一段時期。"},{"en":"At a time when exams are near, students need sleep as much as extra revision.","zh":"在考試臨近的時候，學生需要睡眠，程度不亞於額外溫習。"},{"en":"This phrase often connects a current situation with a deeper problem.","zh":"這個短語常把當前情況與更深層問題連起來。"},{"en":"It helps readers see why the writer is discussing the issue now.","zh":"它幫助讀者明白作者為何現在討論這個議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"drought","meaning":"乾旱","examples":[{"en":"Drought in several countries has recently been in the news.","zh":"幾個國家的乾旱最近成為新聞焦點。"},{"en":"Drought is a long period with too little rain, causing dry land and water shortages.","zh":"乾旱是長時間雨量太少，導致土地乾燥和水資源短缺。"},{"en":"Farmers may lose crops during a drought because the soil has too little moisture.","zh":"乾旱期間，農民可能因泥土水分太少而失去收成。"},{"en":"A severe drought can force cities to restrict garden watering and car washing.","zh":"嚴重乾旱可以迫使城市限制花園澆水和洗車。"},{"en":"Drought is dangerous because it affects food, health and daily water use.","zh":"乾旱危險，因為它影響食物、健康和日常用水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be in the news","meaning":"成為新聞焦點","examples":[{"en":"Drought in the United States, Ethiopia, and Afghanistan is in the news.","zh":"美國、埃塞俄比亞和阿富汗的乾旱成為新聞焦點。"},{"en":"To be in the news means to be reported and discussed by newspapers, television or online media.","zh":"be in the news 指被報章、電視或網上媒體報道和討論。"},{"en":"A school closure may be in the news if many families are affected.","zh":"如果許多家庭受影響，學校關閉可能成為新聞焦點。"},{"en":"When an issue is in the news, people notice it more, but not always deeply.","zh":"當一個議題成為新聞焦點，人們會更注意它，但未必深入理解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes public media attention.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾媒體關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"it is easy to forget that","meaning":"很容易忘記……","examples":[{"en":"It is easy to forget that far more serious water shortages are emerging.","zh":"人們很容易忘記，更嚴重得多的水資源短缺正在出現。"},{"en":"It is easy to forget that means people may overlook an important fact.","zh":"it is easy to forget that 指人們可能忽略一個重要事實。"},{"en":"It is easy to forget that quiet students may still understand the lesson deeply.","zh":"人們很容易忘記，安靜學生仍可能深刻理解課堂。"},{"en":"News about one visible problem can make people forget a slower, larger problem.","zh":"關於一個明顯問題的新聞，可以令人忘記一個較慢但更大的問題。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds readers to notice something important but easily missed.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者注意重要但容易被忽略的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"far more serious","meaning":"嚴重得多的","examples":[{"en":"Far more serious water shortages are emerging in many countries.","zh":"嚴重得多的水資源短缺正在許多國家出現。"},{"en":"Far more serious means much more severe or important than another problem.","zh":"far more serious 指比另一個問題嚴重或重要得多。"},{"en":"A broken pencil is annoying, but a lost exam paper is far more serious.","zh":"斷鉛筆令人煩惱，但遺失試卷嚴重得多。"},{"en":"A far more serious problem usually needs faster and stronger action.","zh":"嚴重得多的問題通常需要更快、更有力的行動。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a big difference in seriousness.","zh":"這個短語顯示嚴重程度上的巨大差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"water shortages","meaning":"水資源短缺","examples":[{"en":"Many countries are facing serious water shortages.","zh":"許多國家正面對嚴重水資源短缺。"},{"en":"Water shortages happen when there is not enough water for people, farms or industries.","zh":"水資源短缺指沒有足夠水供人、農場或工業使用。"},{"en":"A housing estate may face water shortages if pipes break during a heatwave.","zh":"如果熱浪期間水管爆裂，屋苑可能面對水資源短缺。"},{"en":"Water shortages can raise food prices when farmers cannot irrigate crops.","zh":"當農民無法灌溉農作物，水資源短缺可以推高食物價格。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a situation where demand for water is greater than available supply.","zh":"這個短語描述用水需求大於可用供應的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"emerge as","meaning":"逐漸出現為；形成","examples":[{"en":"Water shortages are emerging as demand outruns supply.","zh":"隨着需求超過供應，水資源短缺正在逐漸形成。"},{"en":"To emerge as something means to gradually appear or become recognised as that thing.","zh":"emerge as 某事，指逐漸出現或被認定為該事物。"},{"en":"A quiet student may emerge as a leader during a group project.","zh":"安靜學生可能在小組項目中逐漸成為領袖。"},{"en":"A small problem can emerge as a crisis if no one deals with it early.","zh":"如果沒有人早期處理，小問題可以逐漸形成危機。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a gradual development into a clearer condition or role.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸發展成更清楚的狀況或角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the demand for water","meaning":"對水的需求","examples":[{"en":"The demand for water is rising in many countries.","zh":"許多國家對水的需求正在上升。"},{"en":"The demand for water means how much water people, farms and industries need or want to use.","zh":"demand for water 指人、農場和工業需要或想使用多少水。"},{"en":"The demand for water increases when more homes have bathrooms, gardens and washing machines.","zh":"當更多家庭有浴室、花園和洗衣機，對水的需求會增加。"},{"en":"Higher demand can strain rivers, reservoirs and underground supplies.","zh":"更高需求可以令河流、水庫和地下水供應受壓。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on water needed by users, not the water available.","zh":"這個短語重點在使用者需要的水，而不是可供應的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"outrun the supply","meaning":"超過供應","examples":[{"en":"The demand for water in many countries simply outruns the supply.","zh":"許多國家對水的需求簡直超過供應。"},{"en":"To outrun the supply means to become greater than what is available.","zh":"outrun the supply 指變得大於可用供應量。"},{"en":"If students order more lunches than the canteen prepared, demand outruns the supply.","zh":"如果學生訂的午餐多於飯堂準備的數量，需求就超過供應。"},{"en":"When demand outruns supply, prices rise, queues form or shortages appear.","zh":"當需求超過供應，價格會上升、隊伍會形成，或短缺會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a gap where need grows faster than availability.","zh":"這個短語描述需求增長快過供應的差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"water tables","meaning":"地下水位","examples":[{"en":"Water tables are now falling on every continent.","zh":"地下水位現在在每個大洲下降。"},{"en":"Water tables are the underground levels below which the ground is filled with water.","zh":"water tables 是地下某一水平，低於該水平的土地充滿水。"},{"en":"Farmers worry when water tables fall because wells must be dug deeper.","zh":"當地下水位下降，農民會擔心，因為水井必須挖得更深。"},{"en":"Falling water tables show that groundwater is being used faster than it is replaced.","zh":"地下水位下降顯示地下水使用速度快過補充速度。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the height of underground water.","zh":"這個短語指地下水的高度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fall on every continent","meaning":"在每個大洲下降","examples":[{"en":"Water tables are falling on every continent.","zh":"地下水位正在每個大洲下降。"},{"en":"To fall on every continent means to decline across all major land regions of the world.","zh":"fall on every continent 指在世界所有主要陸地區域下降。"},{"en":"If wildlife numbers fall on every continent, the problem is global, not local.","zh":"如果野生動物數量在每個大洲下降，問題就是全球性，而非地方性。"},{"en":"A trend found on every continent shows wide and serious pressure.","zh":"在每個大洲都出現的趨勢顯示廣泛而嚴重的壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the decline is worldwide.","zh":"這個短語強調下降是世界性的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"literally scores of","meaning":"確實有數十個……","examples":[{"en":"Literally scores of countries are facing water shortages.","zh":"確實有數十個國家正面對水資源短缺。"},{"en":"Literally scores of means truly dozens of, not just a few.","zh":"literally scores of 指確實有幾十個，而不是只有少數。"},{"en":"Literally scores of students may join a school club if the activity is useful and fun.","zh":"如果活動有用又有趣，確實可能有數十名學生加入學會。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises that the number is large and real.","zh":"這個短語強調數量很大而且是真實的。"},{"en":"It is used when the writer wants readers to feel the scale.","zh":"當作者想讀者感受到規模時，會使用它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"face water shortages","meaning":"面對水資源短缺","examples":[{"en":"Scores of countries are facing water shortages.","zh":"數十個國家正面對水資源短缺。"},{"en":"To face water shortages means to experience or be threatened by not having enough water.","zh":"face water shortages 指經歷或受到缺乏足夠水的威脅。"},{"en":"A small town may face water shortages if its reservoir stays low for months.","zh":"如果水庫連續數月水位低，小鎮可能面對水資源短缺。"},{"en":"Countries facing water shortages may restrict farming, industry and household use.","zh":"面對水資源短缺的國家可能限制農業、工業和家居用水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a direct challenge caused by limited water supply.","zh":"這個短語描述由有限供水造成的直接挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"wells go dry","meaning":"水井乾涸","examples":[{"en":"Many wells go dry as water tables fall.","zh":"隨着地下水位下降，許多水井乾涸。"},{"en":"When wells go dry, they no longer contain enough water to draw out.","zh":"當 wells go dry，意思是水井不再有足夠水可抽取。"},{"en":"A village may panic when its main well goes dry during a hot summer.","zh":"炎熱夏天中，如果主要水井乾涸，村莊可能恐慌。"},{"en":"Wells go dry when underground water is used faster than nature can replace it.","zh":"當地下水使用速度快過自然補充，水井就會乾涸。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a visible sign of groundwater shortage.","zh":"這個短語描述地下水短缺的可見跡象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a water-challenged world","meaning":"水資源緊張的世界","examples":[{"en":"We live in a water-challenged world.","zh":"我們生活在一個水資源緊張的世界。"},{"en":"A water-challenged world is a world where many places struggle to secure enough water.","zh":"water-challenged world 指許多地方難以取得足夠水的世界。"},{"en":"In a water-challenged world, schools may teach children to save water from a young age.","zh":"在水資源緊張的世界，學校可能從小教孩子節約用水。"},{"en":"Climate, population and farming pressure can make the world more water-challenged.","zh":"氣候、人口和農業壓力可以令世界水資源更加緊張。"},{"en":"The phrase describes global difficulty in managing water.","zh":"這個短語描述全球管理水資源的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"become more so","meaning":"變得更加如此","examples":[{"en":"The world is water-challenged and is becoming more so each year.","zh":"世界水資源緊張，而且每年變得更加如此。"},{"en":"To become more so means to become even more like the condition just described.","zh":"become more so 指變得更加像剛剛描述的狀況。"},{"en":"The city is crowded and becomes more so during holidays.","zh":"這座城市很擠迫，假日期間變得更加如此。"},{"en":"If demand keeps rising, a difficult situation can become more so over time.","zh":"如果需求持續上升，困難情況會隨時間變得更加如此。"},{"en":"The phrase avoids repeating the same adjective again.","zh":"這個短語避免再次重複同一個形容詞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"additional people","meaning":"新增人口","examples":[{"en":"Millions of additional people are using the Earth’s water resources.","zh":"數以百萬計新增人口正在使用地球水資源。"},{"en":"Additional people are extra people added to an existing population or group.","zh":"additional people 是加入現有人口或群體的額外人數。"},{"en":"A school may need more desks when additional students join mid-year.","zh":"如果年中有新增學生加入，學校可能需要更多書桌。"},{"en":"Additional people increase demand for space, food, transport and water.","zh":"新增人口會增加對空間、食物、交通和水的需求。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the extra number added beyond those already there.","zh":"這個短語重點在原有人數以外增加的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stake one’s claims to","meaning":"聲稱有權使用……","examples":[{"en":"Additional people stake their claims to the Earth’s water resources.","zh":"新增人口聲稱有權使用地球水資源。"},{"en":"To stake one’s claims to something means to assert a right to use or own part of it.","zh":"stake one’s claims to 某物，指宣稱有權使用或擁有其中一部分。"},{"en":"New residents may stake their claims to public housing, school places and clinic services.","zh":"新居民可能聲稱有權使用公屋、學位和診所服務。"},{"en":"When more people claim the same limited resource, competition increases.","zh":"當更多人要求同一有限資源，競爭會增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes people saying, directly or indirectly, that they need their share.","zh":"這個短語描述人們直接或間接表示自己需要一份資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Earth’s water resources","meaning":"地球水資源","examples":[{"en":"Population growth increases pressure on the Earth’s water resources.","zh":"人口增長增加地球水資源的壓力。"},{"en":"The Earth’s water resources are the rivers, lakes, groundwater, glaciers and other water supplies on the planet.","zh":"Earth’s water resources 是地球上的河流、湖泊、地下水、冰川和其他水源。"},{"en":"Families use the Earth’s water resources when they drink, cook, wash and grow food.","zh":"家庭在飲水、煮食、洗滌和種植食物時，都在使用地球水資源。"},{"en":"These resources are limited, so wasteful use can harm people far away.","zh":"這些資源有限，所以浪費用水可以傷害遠方的人。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the planet’s available water.","zh":"這個短語指地球可用的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"projected","meaning":"預計的","examples":[{"en":"Nearly all the projected population growth will occur in water-short countries.","zh":"幾乎所有預計的人口增長都會發生在缺水國家。"},{"en":"Projected means predicted or estimated for the future based on current information.","zh":"projected 指根據現有資料對未來作出的預測或估算。"},{"en":"A school may hire teachers based on projected student numbers next year.","zh":"學校可能根據明年預計學生人數聘請老師。"},{"en":"Projected figures can change if birth rates, migration or policy changes.","zh":"如果出生率、移民或政策改變，預計數字也可能改變。"},{"en":"The word describes an informed forecast, not a confirmed fact.","zh":"這個詞描述有根據的預測，而不是已確認事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"over the next half-century","meaning":"在未來半個世紀","examples":[{"en":"Three billion people may be added over the next half-century.","zh":"在未來半個世紀，人口可能增加三十億。"},{"en":"Over the next half-century means during the coming fifty years.","zh":"over the next half-century 指在未來五十年期間。"},{"en":"Over the next half-century, many cities may need to redesign transport and housing.","zh":"在未來半個世紀，許多城市可能需要重新設計交通和房屋。"},{"en":"A change over fifty years can feel slow each year but huge in total.","zh":"五十年間的改變每年可能感覺緩慢，但總量巨大。"},{"en":"The phrase places a prediction in a long future period.","zh":"這個短語把預測放在長遠未來時段中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be born in countries that","meaning":"出生於……的國家","examples":[{"en":"Many children will be born in countries that already face water shortages.","zh":"許多孩子將出生於已經面對水資源短缺的國家。"},{"en":"To be born in countries that have a problem means to enter life in places already facing that condition.","zh":"be born in countries that have a problem 指在人生開始時就身處已面對該狀況的地方。"},{"en":"Children born in countries that lack schools may face educational barriers from the start.","zh":"出生於缺乏學校的國家的孩子，可能一開始就面對教育障礙。"},{"en":"Birthplace matters because local resources shape early life chances.","zh":"出生地重要，因為本地資源會塑造早期人生機會。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a person’s birth with the conditions of their country.","zh":"這個短語把人的出生與其國家的狀況連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"experience water shortages","meaning":"經歷水資源短缺","examples":[{"en":"Many countries are already experiencing water shortages.","zh":"許多國家已經經歷水資源短缺。"},{"en":"To experience water shortages means to actually suffer from not having enough water.","zh":"experience water shortages 指實際遭受缺乏足夠水的情況。"},{"en":"A hospital may experience water shortages if supply pipes are damaged.","zh":"如果供水管受損，醫院可能經歷水資源短缺。"},{"en":"Places experiencing water shortages may ration water or close some services.","zh":"經歷水資源短缺的地方可能配給用水或關閉部分服務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shortage being felt in real life, not just predicted.","zh":"這個短語描述短缺正在現實中被感受到，而不只是預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lack enough water to","meaning":"缺乏足夠的水去……","examples":[{"en":"Many people lack enough water to drink and produce food.","zh":"許多人缺乏足夠的水去飲用和生產糧食。"},{"en":"To lack enough water to do something means not to have sufficient water for that purpose.","zh":"lack enough water to do something 指沒有足夠水作該用途。"},{"en":"A school may lack enough water to clean classrooms properly after a pipe failure.","zh":"水管故障後，學校可能缺乏足夠的水去妥善清潔課室。"},{"en":"When people lack enough water to farm, food supplies become less secure.","zh":"當人們缺乏足夠的水去耕作，糧食供應就較不穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase shows both shortage and the action that becomes difficult.","zh":"這個短語同時顯示短缺和因此變得困難的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"satisfy hygienic needs","meaning":"滿足衞生需要","examples":[{"en":"Many people lack enough water to satisfy hygienic needs.","zh":"許多人缺乏足夠的水來滿足衞生需要。"},{"en":"To satisfy hygienic needs means to provide enough water for washing, cleaning and preventing disease.","zh":"satisfy hygienic needs 指提供足夠水作洗滌、清潔和預防疾病之用。"},{"en":"A clinic needs water to satisfy hygienic needs such as handwashing and cleaning equipment.","zh":"診所需要水來滿足洗手和清潔設備等衞生需要。"},{"en":"If hygienic needs are not met, illness can spread more easily.","zh":"如果衞生需要得不到滿足，疾病可以更容易傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to water needed for basic health and cleanliness.","zh":"這個短語指基本健康和清潔所需的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"produce food","meaning":"生產糧食","examples":[{"en":"Water is needed to produce food.","zh":"生產糧食需要水。"},{"en":"To produce food means to grow, raise or make food for people to eat.","zh":"produce food 指種植、飼養或製造供人食用的食物。"},{"en":"Farmers produce food by growing rice, vegetables, fruit and grain.","zh":"農民透過種植米、蔬菜、水果和穀物來生產糧食。"},{"en":"Food production needs water for crops, animals, cleaning and processing.","zh":"糧食生產需要水來灌溉農作物、飼養動物、清潔和加工。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the work of creating food supplies.","zh":"這個短語描述創造食物供應的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be projected to add","meaning":"預計增加","examples":[{"en":"India is projected to add 519 million people by 2050.","zh":"印度預計到2050年增加5.19億人口。"},{"en":"To be projected to add a number means to be expected to increase by that amount.","zh":"be projected to add 某數量，指預計增加該數量。"},{"en":"A school is projected to add 300 students if a new housing estate opens nearby.","zh":"如果附近新屋苑落成，學校預計增加300名學生。"},{"en":"Projected additions help governments plan for future services.","zh":"預計增加數字幫助政府規劃未來服務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a forecast increase.","zh":"這個短語描述預測中的增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at present","meaning":"目前","examples":[{"en":"Pakistan has 151 million people at present.","zh":"巴基斯坦目前有1.51億人口。"},{"en":"At present means now or at the current time.","zh":"at present 指現在或目前這個時間。"},{"en":"At present, the school library closes at 5 p.m.","zh":"目前，學校圖書館下午五時關閉。"},{"en":"The phrase often contrasts the current situation with future change.","zh":"這個短語常把當前情況與未來變化作對比。"},{"en":"It tells readers that the information may change later.","zh":"它告訴讀者該資訊之後可能改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be slated to","meaning":"預定；預計會","examples":[{"en":"Egypt, Iran, and Mexico are slated to increase their populations by more than half.","zh":"埃及、伊朗和墨西哥預計人口會增加超過一半。"},{"en":"To be slated to do something means to be scheduled, expected or planned to do it.","zh":"be slated to do something 指被安排、預期或計劃會做某事。"},{"en":"A new hospital is slated to open next year if construction finishes on time.","zh":"如果工程準時完成，新醫院預計明年啟用。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used for future developments that appear likely.","zh":"這個短語常用於看來很可能發生的未來發展。"},{"en":"It suggests that the event is already expected in a plan or forecast.","zh":"它暗示事件已在計劃或預測中被預期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"increase their populations by more than half","meaning":"人口增加超過一半","examples":[{"en":"Some countries are slated to increase their populations by more than half by 2050.","zh":"有些國家預計到2050年人口增加超過一半。"},{"en":"To increase a population by more than half means to grow by over 50 percent.","zh":"increase a population by more than half 指增長超過百分之五十。"},{"en":"A school of 600 students would increase its population by more than half if 350 more students joined.","zh":"一所600人的學校如果多了350名學生，就是人口增加超過一半。"},{"en":"Such growth can put heavy pressure on housing, transport and water supplies.","zh":"這種增長可以對房屋、交通和水源供應造成沉重壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a very large population rise.","zh":"這個短語描述非常大的人口上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"water-short countries","meaning":"缺水國家","examples":[{"en":"Population growth is especially dangerous in water-short countries.","zh":"人口增長在缺水國家尤其危險。"},{"en":"Water-short countries are countries that do not have enough water for their people and economy.","zh":"water-short countries 是沒有足夠水供人民和經濟使用的國家。"},{"en":"Water-short countries may struggle to provide farms, homes and factories with reliable water.","zh":"缺水國家可能難以為農場、家庭和工廠提供可靠水源。"},{"en":"When population grows in water-short countries, each person’s share of water may fall.","zh":"當缺水國家人口增長，每人的水份額可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes countries where water is already limited.","zh":"這個短語描述水本來已有限的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a local form of poverty","meaning":"一種地方性的貧困","examples":[{"en":"Hydrological poverty is a local form of poverty.","zh":"水資源貧困是一種地方性的貧困。"},{"en":"A local form of poverty is poverty shaped by conditions in a particular place.","zh":"local form of poverty 是由某特定地方條件塑造的貧困。"},{"en":"A mountain village may have a local form of poverty caused by poor transport access.","zh":"山村可能有一種由交通不便造成的地方性貧困。"},{"en":"Local poverty can persist when geography, water or services limit opportunity.","zh":"當地理、水源或服務限制機會，地方性貧困可以持續。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that poverty is not always caused by income alone.","zh":"這個短語顯示貧困不一定只由收入造成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"difficult to escape","meaning":"難以擺脫","examples":[{"en":"Hydrological poverty is difficult to escape.","zh":"水資源貧困難以擺脫。"},{"en":"Difficult to escape means hard to leave, solve or recover from.","zh":"difficult to escape 指難以離開、解決或恢復。"},{"en":"Debt can be difficult to escape if interest keeps increasing every month.","zh":"如果利息每月持續增加，債務可能難以擺脫。"},{"en":"A problem becomes difficult to escape when it reduces the resources needed to solve it.","zh":"當問題削弱解決它所需的資源時，它會變得難以擺脫。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a trap-like situation.","zh":"這個短語描述像陷阱一樣的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"even with","meaning":"即使有；即使在……情況下","examples":[{"en":"Even with today’s population, the world has a huge water deficit.","zh":"即使以今天的人口計算，世界已有巨大的水資源赤字。"},{"en":"Even with means despite already having or considering something.","zh":"even with 指即使已擁有或考慮某事。"},{"en":"Even with extra revision, a student may struggle if she does not understand the basics.","zh":"即使有額外溫習，如果學生不理解基礎，仍可能吃力。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a problem exists despite a condition that might seem enough.","zh":"這個短語顯示即使有看似足夠的條件，問題仍然存在。"},{"en":"It often makes the warning stronger.","zh":"它常令警告更強烈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a huge water deficit","meaning":"巨大的水資源赤字","examples":[{"en":"The world has a huge water deficit.","zh":"世界有巨大的水資源赤字。"},{"en":"A huge water deficit means water use is much greater than sustainable water supply.","zh":"huge water deficit 指用水量遠大於可持續供水量。"},{"en":"A household has a water deficit if it uses more stored water than rain can replace.","zh":"如果家庭用掉的儲水多於雨水能補充的量，就有水資源赤字。"},{"en":"A huge deficit can force communities to cut farming, import food or dig deeper wells.","zh":"巨大赤字可以迫使社區減少耕作、進口糧食或挖更深水井。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large gap between water demand and water renewal.","zh":"這個短語描述用水需求與水源更新之間的巨大差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"using data on","meaning":"使用關於……的數據","examples":[{"en":"The author uses data on over-pumping in several regions.","zh":"作者使用關於幾個地區過度抽取地下水的數據。"},{"en":"Using data on something means relying on recorded information about that topic.","zh":"using data on 某事，指依靠關於該主題的記錄資料。"},{"en":"A school may use data on attendance to find students who need support.","zh":"學校可能使用關於出席率的數據，找出需要支援的學生。"},{"en":"Good data can make an argument clearer and less emotional.","zh":"好數據可以令論點更清楚、較少情緒化。"},{"en":"The phrase shows what evidence a writer or researcher is using.","zh":"這個短語顯示作者或研究者正在使用甚麼證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"over-pumping","meaning":"過度抽取地下水","examples":[{"en":"Over-pumping is causing the annual depletion of aquifers.","zh":"過度抽取地下水正在造成含水層每年耗損。"},{"en":"Over-pumping means taking water from underground faster than nature can replace it.","zh":"over-pumping 指從地下取水的速度快過自然補充速度。"},{"en":"A farm may cause over-pumping if it runs deep wells day and night during dry seasons.","zh":"如果農場在旱季日夜運行深井，可能造成過度抽取地下水。"},{"en":"Over-pumping lowers water tables and can make wells go dry.","zh":"過度抽取地下水會降低地下水位，並可能令水井乾涸。"},{"en":"The phrase describes excessive groundwater extraction.","zh":"這個短語描述過量開採地下水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"author of","meaning":"……的作者","examples":[{"en":"Sandra Postel is the author of Pillar of Sand.","zh":"Sandra Postel 是《Pillar of Sand》的作者。"},{"en":"The author of a book is the person who wrote it.","zh":"author of 一本書，是寫作該書的人。"},{"en":"A student should name the author of an article when quoting it in an essay.","zh":"學生在文章中引用資料時，應寫出文章作者。"},{"en":"Knowing the author helps readers judge the source and perspective.","zh":"知道作者有助讀者判斷來源和角度。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who created a written work.","zh":"這個短語指出誰創作了書面作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"irrigation miracle","meaning":"灌溉奇蹟","examples":[{"en":"The book asks whether the irrigation miracle can last.","zh":"這本書問灌溉奇蹟能否持續。"},{"en":"An irrigation miracle is a dramatic increase in food production made possible by watering farmland.","zh":"irrigation miracle 是透過灌溉農地而實現的糧食產量大幅增加。"},{"en":"A dry region may seem to have an irrigation miracle when canals turn desert into farmland.","zh":"當運河把沙漠變成農田，乾旱地區可能看似出現灌溉奇蹟。"},{"en":"Such a miracle may fail if the water source is used faster than it is renewed.","zh":"如果水源使用速度快過更新速度，這種奇蹟可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests impressive agricultural success that may not be sustainable.","zh":"這個短語暗示令人印象深刻但未必可持續的農業成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"annual depletion of aquifers","meaning":"含水層每年耗損","examples":[{"en":"Sandra Postel reports the annual depletion of aquifers at 160 billion cubic metres.","zh":"Sandra Postel 報告含水層每年耗損達1600億立方米。"},{"en":"Annual depletion of aquifers means the amount of underground water lost from aquifers each year.","zh":"annual depletion of aquifers 指含水層每年失去的地下水量。"},{"en":"A region can measure annual depletion of aquifers by comparing water pumped out with water naturally refilled.","zh":"地區可以透過比較抽出水量與自然補充水量來量度含水層每年耗損。"},{"en":"Large annual depletion means groundwater is being used like savings, not income.","zh":"大量每年耗損意味地下水被當作儲蓄而非收入使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes yearly loss from underground water stores.","zh":"這個短語描述地下水儲存的年度流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"aquifers","meaning":"含水層","examples":[{"en":"Aquifers are being depleted by over-pumping.","zh":"含水層正因過度抽取地下水而被耗損。"},{"en":"Aquifers are underground layers of rock or soil that hold water.","zh":"aquifers 是能儲水的地下岩層或土層。"},{"en":"Villages often depend on aquifers when rivers are far away or unreliable.","zh":"當河流遙遠或不可靠，村莊常依賴含水層。"},{"en":"If aquifers are emptied too quickly, wells become deeper and more expensive.","zh":"如果含水層被太快抽空，水井會變得更深、更昂貴。"},{"en":"The word refers to natural underground water stores.","zh":"這個詞指天然地下水儲存層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cubic metres","meaning":"立方米","examples":[{"en":"The annual depletion of aquifers is measured in cubic metres.","zh":"含水層每年耗損以立方米量度。"},{"en":"Cubic metres are units used to measure volume, especially large amounts of water or space.","zh":"cubic metres 是用來量度體積的單位，尤其是大量水或空間。"},{"en":"A swimming pool’s capacity can be measured in cubic metres.","zh":"游泳池容量可以用立方米量度。"},{"en":"Measuring water in cubic metres helps compare use across farms, cities and countries.","zh":"以立方米量度水，有助比較農場、城市和國家的用量。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a standard measure of volume.","zh":"這個短語指標準體積量度單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"rule of thumb","meaning":"經驗法則","examples":[{"en":"A useful rule of thumb is that it takes 1,000 tons of water to produce 1 ton of grain.","zh":"一個有用的經驗法則是，生產1噸穀物需要1000噸水。"},{"en":"A rule of thumb is a simple practical guideline, not an exact scientific rule.","zh":"rule of thumb 是簡單實用指引，而不是精確科學規則。"},{"en":"A common rule of thumb is to start revising early rather than the night before an exam.","zh":"一個常見經驗法則是早點開始溫習，而不是考試前一晚才溫習。"},{"en":"Rules of thumb help people make quick estimates when exact data are not needed.","zh":"當不需要精確數據時，經驗法則幫助人快速估算。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a rough but useful guide.","zh":"這個短語描述粗略但有用的指引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"it takes…to produce…","meaning":"需要……才可生產……","examples":[{"en":"It takes 1,000 tons of water to produce 1 ton of grain.","zh":"需要1000噸水才可生產1噸穀物。"},{"en":"It takes X to produce Y means X is required in order to make Y.","zh":"it takes X to produce Y 指需要X才能製造Y。"},{"en":"It takes flour, water and yeast to produce bread.","zh":"需要麵粉、水和酵母才可生產麵包。"},{"en":"If a product takes many resources to produce, wasting it also wastes those resources.","zh":"如果產品需要許多資源才可生產，浪費它也等於浪費那些資源。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the input needed for an output.","zh":"這個短語解釋產出所需的投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"water deficit","meaning":"水資源赤字","examples":[{"en":"The water deficit is equal to 160 million tons of grain.","zh":"水資源赤字相等於1.6億噸穀物。"},{"en":"A water deficit is a gap between water used and water sustainably available.","zh":"water deficit 是用水量與可持續可用水量之間的差距。"},{"en":"A household has a water deficit if it uses stored water faster than the tank is refilled.","zh":"如果家庭用掉儲水的速度快過水箱補充速度，就有水資源赤字。"},{"en":"A water deficit can appear as lower reservoirs, dry wells or reduced crop production.","zh":"水資源赤字可以表現為水庫水位下降、水井乾涸或作物減產。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shortage measured as a balance problem.","zh":"這個短語描述以平衡問題量度的短缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be equal to","meaning":"等於","examples":[{"en":"The water deficit is equal to one-half of the US grain harvest.","zh":"水資源赤字等於美國穀物收成的一半。"},{"en":"To be equal to something means to have the same amount, value or effect.","zh":"be equal to 某物，指有相同數量、價值或效果。"},{"en":"Ten dollars is equal to two five-dollar notes.","zh":"十元等於兩張五元紙幣。"},{"en":"Comparing one amount with another can make a large figure easier to understand.","zh":"把一個數量與另一個比較，可以令大數字更容易理解。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that two quantities match.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個數量相等。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"grain harvest","meaning":"穀物收成","examples":[{"en":"The water deficit is equal to one-half the US grain harvest.","zh":"水資源赤字等於美國穀物收成的一半。"},{"en":"Grain harvest means the amount of grain collected from farms after crops mature.","zh":"grain harvest 指農作物成熟後從農場收集到的穀物數量。"},{"en":"A poor grain harvest can raise bread and noodle prices.","zh":"穀物收成差可以推高麵包和麵價。"},{"en":"Weather, water and soil conditions all affect the grain harvest.","zh":"天氣、水和土壤狀況都會影響穀物收成。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to harvested cereal crops such as wheat, rice and corn.","zh":"這個短語指小麥、米和粟米等穀類作物的收成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"average world grain consumption","meaning":"全球人均穀物消耗量","examples":[{"en":"Average world grain consumption is just over 300 kilograms per person per year.","zh":"全球人均穀物消耗量為每人每年剛超過300公斤。"},{"en":"Average world grain consumption means the typical amount of grain used by each person globally.","zh":"average world grain consumption 指全球每人通常使用的穀物數量。"},{"en":"Researchers use average consumption to estimate how many people a harvest can feed.","zh":"研究人員使用平均消耗量來估算收成可養活多少人。"},{"en":"If average grain consumption rises, more water is needed to produce food.","zh":"如果平均穀物消耗量上升，就需要更多水來生產糧食。"},{"en":"The phrase describes global grain use divided by population.","zh":"這個短語描述全球穀物使用量按人口平均計算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"just over","meaning":"剛超過","examples":[{"en":"Average world grain consumption is just over 300 kilograms per person per year.","zh":"全球人均穀物消耗量為每人每年剛超過300公斤。"},{"en":"Just over means slightly more than a stated amount.","zh":"just over 指比所說數量稍多一點。"},{"en":"The lesson lasted just over an hour, so students had a short break afterwards.","zh":"課堂剛超過一小時，所以學生之後有短暫休息。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate number that is a little above the figure mentioned.","zh":"這個短語給出略高於所提數字的約數。"},{"en":"It is useful when exact precision is not necessary.","zh":"當不需要完全精確時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"per person per year","meaning":"每人每年","examples":[{"en":"Average grain consumption is measured per person per year.","zh":"平均穀物消耗量以每人每年計算。"},{"en":"Per person per year means for each individual in one year.","zh":"per person per year 指每一個人在一年內。"},{"en":"A school may calculate paper use per student per year to reduce waste.","zh":"學校可能計算每名學生每年用紙量，以減少浪費。"},{"en":"This measure helps compare countries with different population sizes.","zh":"這種量度幫助比較人口規模不同的國家。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how a total amount is averaged over people and time.","zh":"這個短語顯示總量如何按人和時間平均。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"stated otherwise","meaning":"換句話說","examples":[{"en":"Stated otherwise, many people are being fed through unsustainable water use.","zh":"換句話說，許多人正透過不可持續用水方式被養活。"},{"en":"Stated otherwise means expressed in a different way to make the same idea clearer.","zh":"stated otherwise 指以另一種方式表達同一想法，使其更清楚。"},{"en":"The class failed to meet the deadline; stated otherwise, the plan was too ambitious.","zh":"全班未能趕上截止日期；換句話說，計劃太進取。"},{"en":"This phrase helps reframe a number or fact so readers understand its meaning.","zh":"這個短語幫助重新表達數字或事實，讓讀者理解其意思。"},{"en":"It signals that the next sentence says the same idea more plainly.","zh":"它標示下一句會以較直接方式說出同一想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be fed with","meaning":"以……養活","examples":[{"en":"Millions of people are being fed with grain produced through unsustainable water use.","zh":"數以百萬計的人正以透過不可持續用水生產的穀物養活。"},{"en":"To be fed with something means to receive food from that source.","zh":"be fed with 某物，指從該來源獲得食物。"},{"en":"Schoolchildren may be fed with meals prepared by volunteers during an emergency.","zh":"緊急情況下，學童可能以義工準備的膳食被養活。"},{"en":"If people are fed with food produced unsustainably, hidden environmental costs remain.","zh":"如果人們以不可持續生產的食物養活，隱藏環境成本仍然存在。"},{"en":"The phrase links people’s food supply with its source.","zh":"這個短語把人的糧食供應與其來源連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"produced through","meaning":"透過……生產","examples":[{"en":"Some grain is produced through the unsustainable use of water.","zh":"有些穀物是透過不可持續用水方式生產的。"},{"en":"Produced through means made by means of a particular process or resource.","zh":"produced through 指透過某個過程或資源製造。"},{"en":"Bread is produced through mixing, kneading, rising and baking dough.","zh":"麵包是透過混合、搓揉、發酵和烘焗麵團生產的。"},{"en":"If food is produced through wasteful methods, its true cost may be higher than its price.","zh":"如果食物透過浪費方法生產，其真實成本可能高於價格。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how something is made.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物如何被製造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"unsustainable use of water","meaning":"不可持續的用水方式","examples":[{"en":"Millions of people depend on the unsustainable use of water.","zh":"數以百萬計的人依賴不可持續的用水方式。"},{"en":"Unsustainable use of water means using water faster than it can naturally or safely be replaced.","zh":"unsustainable use of water 指用水速度快過自然或安全補充速度。"},{"en":"A farm that pumps groundwater every day without recharge may rely on unsustainable use of water.","zh":"每天抽取地下水而沒有補充的農場，可能依賴不可持續用水方式。"},{"en":"Such use can create short-term food but long-term water loss.","zh":"這種用法可以創造短期糧食，但造成長期水資源流失。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that the current pattern cannot continue safely.","zh":"這個短語警告目前模式不能安全地持續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a new phenomenon","meaning":"新現象","examples":[{"en":"Over-pumping is a new phenomenon.","zh":"過度抽取地下水是一種新現象。"},{"en":"A new phenomenon is something that has appeared recently or become important only in recent times.","zh":"new phenomenon 是最近出現或近年才變得重要的事物。"},{"en":"Online learning was once a new phenomenon in many schools.","zh":"網上學習曾是許多學校中的新現象。"},{"en":"New phenomena often spread before society fully understands their consequences.","zh":"新現象常在社會完全理解其後果前已經擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a recent development or trend.","zh":"這個短語描述近期發展或趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be largely confined to","meaning":"主要限於……","examples":[{"en":"Over-pumping is largely confined to the last half century.","zh":"過度抽取地下水主要限於過去半個世紀。"},{"en":"To be largely confined to a period or place means to happen mainly within that limit.","zh":"be largely confined to 某時期或地方，指主要發生在該範圍內。"},{"en":"A school’s serious flooding may be largely confined to the rainy season.","zh":"學校嚴重水浸可能主要限於雨季。"},{"en":"If a problem is confined to one period, history can help explain why it appeared then.","zh":"如果問題限於某一時期，歷史可以幫助解釋它為何在那時出現。"},{"en":"The phrase sets the main boundary of a situation.","zh":"這個短語設定情況的主要界限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the last half century","meaning":"過去半個世紀","examples":[{"en":"Over-pumping has mainly occurred in the last half century.","zh":"過度抽取地下水主要發生在過去半個世紀。"},{"en":"The last half century means the previous fifty years.","zh":"last half century 指過去五十年。"},{"en":"The last half century has seen huge changes in phones, computers and transport.","zh":"過去半個世紀見證了電話、電腦和交通的巨大變化。"},{"en":"A trend over fifty years can reshape everyday life without people noticing each step.","zh":"五十年間的趨勢可以重塑日常生活，而人們未必注意每一步。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a recent but long historical period.","zh":"這個短語指近期但較長的歷史時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the development of","meaning":"……的發展","examples":[{"en":"The development of powerful pumps has made over-pumping possible.","zh":"強力水泵的發展令過度抽取地下水成為可能。"},{"en":"The development of something means the process by which it is created, improved or made widely usable.","zh":"development of 某物，指它被創造、改良或變得可廣泛使用的過程。"},{"en":"The development of online payment changed how people shop and travel.","zh":"網上支付的發展改變了人們購物和出行的方式。"},{"en":"New technology can solve one problem while creating another.","zh":"新科技可以解決一個問題，同時創造另一個問題。"},{"en":"The phrase links progress in a tool or idea with later effects.","zh":"這個短語把工具或想法的進步與後來影響連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"diesel- and electrically driven pumps","meaning":"柴油和電力驅動的水泵","examples":[{"en":"Diesel- and electrically driven pumps can draw water from aquifers quickly.","zh":"柴油和電力驅動的水泵可以快速從含水層抽水。"},{"en":"Diesel- and electrically driven pumps are machines powered by diesel fuel or electricity to move water.","zh":"diesel- and electrically driven pumps 是以柴油燃料或電力推動來移動水的機器。"},{"en":"A farm may use electrically driven pumps to lift water from a deep well.","zh":"農場可能使用電力驅動水泵，從深井抽水。"},{"en":"Powerful pumps can make irrigation easier but may also speed up groundwater loss.","zh":"強力水泵可以令灌溉更容易，但也可能加速地下水流失。"},{"en":"The phrase names the technology that allows rapid water extraction.","zh":"這個短語指出容許快速抽水的科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have the capacity to","meaning":"有能力去……","examples":[{"en":"Modern pumps have the capacity to draw water from aquifers rapidly.","zh":"現代水泵有能力快速從含水層抽水。"},{"en":"To have the capacity to do something means to have the ability or power to do it.","zh":"have the capacity to do something 指有能力或力量做某事。"},{"en":"A school hall may have the capacity to hold 500 students.","zh":"學校禮堂可能有能力容納500名學生。"},{"en":"Capacity matters because ability can create both benefits and risks.","zh":"能力很重要，因為它可以同時創造好處和風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what something is able to do.","zh":"這個短語描述某物能做到甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"draw water from aquifers","meaning":"從含水層抽水","examples":[{"en":"Powerful pumps draw water from aquifers faster than nature can replace it.","zh":"強力水泵從含水層抽水的速度快過自然補充速度。"},{"en":"To draw water from aquifers means to pump underground water out of natural storage layers.","zh":"draw water from aquifers 指從天然地下儲水層抽出地下水。"},{"en":"Villages draw water from aquifers when surface rivers are dry.","zh":"當地面河流乾涸，村莊會從含水層抽水。"},{"en":"Drawing too much water from aquifers can lower water tables.","zh":"從含水層抽太多水可以降低地下水位。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extracting groundwater for use.","zh":"這個短語描述抽取地下水供使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"faster than","meaning":"比……更快","examples":[{"en":"Pumps can draw water faster than it is replenished by precipitation.","zh":"水泵抽水的速度可以比降水補充速度更快。"},{"en":"Faster than compares the speed of one action with another.","zh":"faster than 比較一個行動與另一個行動的速度。"},{"en":"A student may spend money faster than she earns it if she buys snacks every day.","zh":"如果學生每天買零食，她花錢可能比賺錢更快。"},{"en":"When use happens faster than replacement, shortage can follow.","zh":"當使用速度比補充速度更快，短缺可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights an imbalance in speed.","zh":"這個短語突出速度上的不平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be replenished by","meaning":"由……補充","examples":[{"en":"Groundwater is replenished by precipitation.","zh":"地下水由降水補充。"},{"en":"To be replenished by something means to be filled up again by that source.","zh":"be replenished by 某物，指由該來源再次補滿。"},{"en":"A school water tank may be replenished by rainwater collected from the roof.","zh":"學校水箱可能由屋頂收集的雨水補充。"},{"en":"If water is used faster than it is replenished, the supply declines.","zh":"如果用水速度快過補充速度，供應就會下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how a resource is renewed.","zh":"這個短語描述資源如何被更新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"precipitation","meaning":"降水","examples":[{"en":"Aquifers are replenished by precipitation.","zh":"含水層由降水補充。"},{"en":"Precipitation is water that falls from the sky, such as rain, snow or hail.","zh":"precipitation 是從天空落下的水，例如雨、雪或冰雹。"},{"en":"Farmers depend on precipitation when they do not have irrigation systems.","zh":"沒有灌溉系統時，農民依賴降水。"},{"en":"Low precipitation over many months can lead to drought.","zh":"多個月降水量低可以導致乾旱。"},{"en":"The word refers to natural water falling from the atmosphere.","zh":"這個詞指從大氣自然落下的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"water consumed worldwide","meaning":"全球消耗的水","examples":[{"en":"Most water consumed worldwide is used for irrigation.","zh":"全球消耗的大部分水用於灌溉。"},{"en":"Water consumed worldwide means the total water used by people across the planet.","zh":"water consumed worldwide 指全球人類使用的總水量。"},{"en":"Researchers compare water consumed worldwide by homes, farms and factories.","zh":"研究人員比較家庭、農場和工廠全球消耗的水。"},{"en":"Knowing global water use helps identify where saving efforts matter most.","zh":"了解全球用水有助找出節水努力最重要的地方。"},{"en":"The phrase describes total human water use around the world.","zh":"這個短語描述全世界人類用水總量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"diverted from rivers","meaning":"從河流引走","examples":[{"en":"Some water used for irrigation is diverted from rivers.","zh":"有些灌溉用水是從河流引走的。"},{"en":"Diverted from rivers means taken away from rivers and directed somewhere else.","zh":"diverted from rivers 指從河流取走並引向其他地方。"},{"en":"A canal may carry water diverted from a river to nearby farms.","zh":"運河可能把從河流引走的水帶到附近農場。"},{"en":"Diverting too much river water can harm fish, wetlands and downstream communities.","zh":"引走太多河水可以傷害魚類、濕地和下游社區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing the natural path of river water.","zh":"這個短語描述改變河水的自然流向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pumped from underground","meaning":"從地下抽取","examples":[{"en":"Some irrigation water is pumped from underground.","zh":"有些灌溉水是從地下抽取的。"},{"en":"Pumped from underground means drawn up from below the ground by a pump.","zh":"pumped from underground 指用水泵從地面以下抽上來。"},{"en":"A rural school may use water pumped from underground when no public pipe is available.","zh":"如果沒有公共水管，鄉村學校可能使用從地下抽取的水。"},{"en":"Pumping underground water can be useful, but excessive pumping lowers water tables.","zh":"抽取地下水可以有用，但過度抽取會降低地下水位。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extracting water from beneath the surface.","zh":"這個短語描述從地表以下取水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be used for irrigation","meaning":"用於灌溉","examples":[{"en":"About 70 percent of water consumed worldwide is used for irrigation.","zh":"全球消耗的水約有百分之七十用於灌溉。"},{"en":"To be used for irrigation means to be used to water crops and farmland.","zh":"be used for irrigation 指被用來澆灌農作物和農田。"},{"en":"A farm pond may be used for irrigation during dry weeks.","zh":"旱季幾星期內，農場池塘可能用於灌溉。"},{"en":"Water used for irrigation helps produce food but can reduce supplies for other uses.","zh":"用於灌溉的水幫助生產糧食，但可能減少其他用途的供應。"},{"en":"The phrase links water use with agriculture.","zh":"這個短語把用水與農業連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"residential purposes","meaning":"住宅用途；家居用途","examples":[{"en":"About 10 percent of water is used for residential purposes.","zh":"約百分之十的水用於住宅用途。"},{"en":"Residential purposes are uses connected with homes and daily household life.","zh":"residential purposes 是與家庭和日常家居生活相關的用途。"},{"en":"Cooking, bathing, toilet flushing and laundry are residential purposes for water use.","zh":"煮食、洗澡、沖廁和洗衣都是用水的家居用途。"},{"en":"Better household appliances can reduce water used for residential purposes.","zh":"更好的家電可以減少住宅用途用水。"},{"en":"The phrase separates home use from farm or industrial use.","zh":"這個短語把家居用水與農業或工業用水分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"increasingly intense competition for","meaning":"對……日益激烈的競爭","examples":[{"en":"There is increasingly intense competition for water among sectors.","zh":"各行業之間對水的競爭日益激烈。"},{"en":"Increasingly intense competition for something means rivalry for it is becoming stronger over time.","zh":"increasingly intense competition for 某物，指爭奪它的競爭隨時間變得更強。"},{"en":"There is increasingly intense competition for school places in popular districts.","zh":"熱門地區對學位的競爭日益激烈。"},{"en":"When a resource is limited and demand grows, competition becomes more intense.","zh":"當資源有限而需求增長，競爭會變得更激烈。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rising pressure between groups seeking the same resource.","zh":"這個短語描述爭取同一資源的群體之間壓力上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"among sectors","meaning":"在各行業之間","examples":[{"en":"Competition for water among sectors is becoming more intense.","zh":"各行業之間對水的競爭正變得更激烈。"},{"en":"Among sectors means between different parts of the economy, such as farming, industry and households.","zh":"among sectors 指在經濟不同部分之間，例如農業、工業和家庭。"},{"en":"Government funding may be divided among sectors like education, health and transport.","zh":"政府資金可能分配在教育、醫療和交通等行業之間。"},{"en":"Competition among sectors grows when each sector needs more of the same resource.","zh":"當每個行業都需要更多同一資源，行業之間競爭就會增加。"},{"en":"The phrase compares different economic or social areas.","zh":"這個短語比較不同經濟或社會範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"agriculture almost always loses","meaning":"農業幾乎總是落敗","examples":[{"en":"In the competition for water, agriculture almost always loses.","zh":"在用水競爭中，農業幾乎總是落敗。"},{"en":"Agriculture almost always loses means farming usually receives less water when other sectors compete for it.","zh":"agriculture almost always loses 指當其他行業爭水時，農業通常得到較少水。"},{"en":"A city may take water from farms because homes and factories can pay more.","zh":"城市可能從農場取水，因為家庭和工廠能付更高價格。"},{"en":"When agriculture loses water, food production may fall.","zh":"當農業失去水，糧食生產可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that farming is often weaker in resource competition.","zh":"這個短語顯示農業在資源競爭中常較弱勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"industrial output","meaning":"工業產出","examples":[{"en":"The same water can be used to expand industrial output.","zh":"同樣的水可以用來擴大工業產出。"},{"en":"Industrial output means the goods or value produced by factories and industries.","zh":"industrial output 指工廠和工業生產的貨品或價值。"},{"en":"A factory may increase industrial output when it buys new machines.","zh":"工廠購買新機器時，可能增加工業產出。"},{"en":"Water used in industry can create high economic value but reduce water available for farming.","zh":"工業用水可以創造高經濟價值，但減少農業可用水。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to production from the industrial sector.","zh":"這個短語指工業部門的生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"this ratio helps explain why","meaning":"這比例有助解釋為何……","examples":[{"en":"This ratio helps explain why farmers sell irrigation water rights.","zh":"這比例有助解釋為何農民出售灌溉用水權。"},{"en":"This ratio helps explain why means the comparison makes the reason easier to understand.","zh":"this ratio helps explain why 指該比較令原因更容易理解。"},{"en":"If one bus carries as many people as forty cars, this ratio helps explain why cities support buses.","zh":"如果一架巴士可載的人數等於四十架私家車，這比例有助解釋為何城市支持巴士。"},{"en":"Ratios can make hidden economic choices clearer.","zh":"比例可以令隱藏的經濟選擇更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an explanation based on numbers.","zh":"這個短語引出基於數字的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the American West","meaning":"美國西部","examples":[{"en":"The sale of irrigation water rights is common in the American West.","zh":"灌溉用水權出售在美國西部很常見。"},{"en":"The American West refers to the western region of the United States.","zh":"American West 指美國西部地區。"},{"en":"The American West includes many dry areas where water rights are economically important.","zh":"美國西部包括許多乾旱地區，因此水權在經濟上很重要。"},{"en":"In dry regions, control over water can shape farming, cities and industry.","zh":"在乾旱地區，對水的控制可以塑造農業、城市和工業。"},{"en":"The phrase names a region where water competition is especially visible.","zh":"這個短語指出一個水資源競爭尤其明顯的地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"irrigation water rights","meaning":"灌溉用水權","examples":[{"en":"Farmers in the American West sell irrigation water rights to cities.","zh":"美國西部的農民把灌溉用水權賣給城市。"},{"en":"Irrigation water rights are legal rights to use water for watering crops.","zh":"irrigation water rights 是使用水灌溉農作物的法律權利。"},{"en":"A farmer may sell irrigation water rights if a city is willing to pay more for the water.","zh":"如果城市願意為水支付更高價格，農民可能出售灌溉用水權。"},{"en":"Selling these rights can bring money to farmers but reduce local food production.","zh":"出售這些權利可以為農民帶來金錢，但減少本地糧食生產。"},{"en":"The phrase connects water use with legal ownership or entitlement.","zh":"這個短語把用水與法律擁有權或使用權連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an almost daily occurrence","meaning":"幾乎每天發生的事","examples":[{"en":"The sale of irrigation water rights is an almost daily occurrence.","zh":"灌溉用水權出售幾乎每天發生。"},{"en":"An almost daily occurrence is something that happens very frequently, nearly every day.","zh":"almost daily occurrence 是非常頻繁、幾乎每天發生的事。"},{"en":"Traffic jams are an almost daily occurrence near the school gate at dismissal time.","zh":"放學時間校門附近交通擠塞幾乎每天發生。"},{"en":"When an event becomes almost daily, it is no longer unusual.","zh":"當事件幾乎每天發生，它就不再不尋常。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises high frequency.","zh":"這個短語強調高頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in addition to","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"In addition to population growth, urbanisation also expands water demand.","zh":"除了人口增長之外，城市化也擴大用水需求。"},{"en":"In addition to means besides or as well as something already mentioned.","zh":"in addition to 指除了已提及的事物之外。"},{"en":"In addition to homework, students may need to prepare for a presentation.","zh":"除了功課之外，學生可能還需要準備匯報。"},{"en":"The phrase adds another factor to an explanation.","zh":"這個短語為解釋加入另一因素。"},{"en":"It helps show that a problem has more than one cause.","zh":"它幫助顯示問題有多於一個原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"urbanisation and industrialisation","meaning":"城市化和工業化","examples":[{"en":"Urbanisation and industrialisation expand the demand for water.","zh":"城市化和工業化擴大對水的需求。"},{"en":"Urbanisation is city growth, while industrialisation is the growth of factories and industry.","zh":"城市化是城市增長，而工業化是工廠和工業增長。"},{"en":"When villagers move to cities and factories expand, urbanisation and industrialisation both increase water use.","zh":"當村民搬到城市而工廠擴張，城市化和工業化都會增加用水量。"},{"en":"These processes create demand for homes, machines, cleaning, cooling and production.","zh":"這些過程產生對住房、機器、清潔、冷卻和生產的需求。"},{"en":"The phrase describes two major development changes that raise resource demand.","zh":"這個短語描述兩項會提高資源需求的主要發展變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"expand the demand for","meaning":"擴大對……的需求","examples":[{"en":"Industrialisation expands the demand for water.","zh":"工業化擴大對水的需求。"},{"en":"To expand the demand for something means to increase how much of it people or industries need.","zh":"expand the demand for 某物，指增加人們或行業對它的需要量。"},{"en":"Online shopping expands the demand for delivery workers and warehouse space.","zh":"網上購物擴大對送貨員和倉庫空間的需求。"},{"en":"Demand expands when more people or activities depend on the same resource.","zh":"當更多人或活動依賴同一資源，需求就會擴大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growth in need.","zh":"這個短語描述需要的增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"traditionally reliant on","meaning":"傳統上依賴……","examples":[{"en":"Many villagers are traditionally reliant on the village well.","zh":"許多村民傳統上依賴村裏的水井。"},{"en":"Traditionally reliant on means depending on something as a long-established habit or practice.","zh":"traditionally reliant on 指長久以來作為習慣或做法而依靠某物。"},{"en":"Some families are traditionally reliant on grandparents for childcare.","zh":"有些家庭傳統上依賴祖父母照顧孩子。"},{"en":"When people move or technology changes, traditional reliance may weaken.","zh":"當人們搬遷或科技改變，傳統依賴可能減弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dependence shaped by custom and history.","zh":"這個短語描述由習俗和歷史形成的依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the village well","meaning":"村裏的水井","examples":[{"en":"Villagers in developing countries are often reliant on the village well.","zh":"發展中國家的村民常依賴村裏的水井。"},{"en":"The village well is a shared water source where villagers draw water.","zh":"village well 是村民取水的共用水源。"},{"en":"Children may walk to the village well every morning before school.","zh":"孩子可能每天上學前走到村裏的水井取水。"},{"en":"If the village well dries up, daily cooking, washing and farming become difficult.","zh":"如果村裏的水井乾涸，日常煮食、洗滌和耕作都變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a central community water source.","zh":"這個短語指社區中心式水源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"move to","meaning":"搬到……","examples":[{"en":"Villagers may move to urban high-rise apartment buildings.","zh":"村民可能搬到城市高層住宅大廈。"},{"en":"To move to a place means to change where one lives, works or stays.","zh":"move to 某地，指改變居住、工作或停留的地方。"},{"en":"A family may move to another district to be closer to school.","zh":"家庭可能搬到另一區，以便更接近學校。"},{"en":"Moving to a city can change water use, transport habits and living costs.","zh":"搬到城市可以改變用水、交通習慣和生活成本。"},{"en":"The phrase describes relocation from one place to another.","zh":"這個短語描述從一地遷往另一地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"urban high-rise apartment buildings","meaning":"城市高層住宅大廈","examples":[{"en":"Urban high-rise apartment buildings often have indoor plumbing.","zh":"城市高層住宅大廈通常有室內供水及排水系統。"},{"en":"Urban high-rise apartment buildings are tall residential buildings in cities.","zh":"urban high-rise apartment buildings 是城市中的高層住宅建築。"},{"en":"Many families in dense cities live in urban high-rise apartment buildings.","zh":"在人口密集城市，許多家庭住在城市高層住宅大廈。"},{"en":"Such buildings usually provide water through pipes rather than village wells.","zh":"這類大廈通常透過水管供水，而不是依靠村井。"},{"en":"The phrase describes modern city housing with many floors.","zh":"這個短語描述有許多樓層的現代城市住房。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"indoor plumbing","meaning":"室內供水及排水系統","examples":[{"en":"Indoor plumbing can greatly increase residential water use.","zh":"室內供水及排水系統可以大幅增加家居用水量。"},{"en":"Indoor plumbing is a system of pipes that brings water into a building and removes wastewater.","zh":"indoor plumbing 是把水帶入建築物並排走污水的管道系統。"},{"en":"Homes with indoor plumbing make bathing, flushing toilets and washing clothes easier.","zh":"有室內供水及排水系統的家庭，洗澡、沖廁和洗衣更方便。"},{"en":"Easy access to tap water can increase how much water households use.","zh":"容易取得自來水可以增加家庭用水量。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to built-in water and drainage systems inside buildings.","zh":"這個短語指建築物內置的供水和排水系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"residential water use","meaning":"家居用水量","examples":[{"en":"Residential water use can triple when villagers move to urban flats.","zh":"當村民搬到城市單位，家居用水量可以增加至三倍。"},{"en":"Residential water use means water used in homes for drinking, washing, cooking and cleaning.","zh":"residential water use 指家庭用於飲水、洗滌、煮食和清潔的水。"},{"en":"A family’s residential water use rises when they take longer showers every day.","zh":"如果一家人每天洗澡時間更長，家居用水量會上升。"},{"en":"More appliances and indoor taps can increase residential water use.","zh":"更多電器和室內水喉可以增加家居用水量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes household water consumption.","zh":"這個短語描述家庭用水消耗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"easily triple","meaning":"輕易增加至三倍","examples":[{"en":"Residential water use can easily triple after people move to cities.","zh":"人們搬到城市後，家居用水量可以輕易增加至三倍。"},{"en":"To easily triple means to become three times as much without much difficulty.","zh":"easily triple 指不太困難地變成三倍。"},{"en":"A café’s electricity bill can easily triple if it adds many refrigerators.","zh":"如果咖啡店增加許多雪櫃，電費可以輕易增加至三倍。"},{"en":"Use can easily triple when access becomes more convenient.","zh":"當使用變得更方便，用量可以輕易增加至三倍。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises a large increase that can happen readily.","zh":"這個短語強調很容易發生的大幅增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rising affluence","meaning":"日益富裕","examples":[{"en":"Rising affluence generates additional demand for water.","zh":"日益富裕產生對水的額外需求。"},{"en":"Rising affluence means people or societies are becoming wealthier.","zh":"rising affluence 指人們或社會變得更富裕。"},{"en":"Rising affluence may lead families to buy cars, washing machines and larger homes.","zh":"日益富裕可能令家庭購買汽車、洗衣機和更大的家居。"},{"en":"As people become richer, their consumption often increases.","zh":"當人們變得更富裕，消費通常會增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growing wealth and its effects.","zh":"這個短語描述財富增長及其影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in itself","meaning":"本身","examples":[{"en":"Rising affluence in itself generates additional demand for water.","zh":"日益富裕本身就產生對水的額外需求。"},{"en":"In itself means considered alone, without needing another factor.","zh":"in itself 指單獨考慮時，不需要另一因素。"},{"en":"A long commute in itself can make a student tired, even before homework begins.","zh":"長途通勤本身就可以令學生疲倦，即使功課還未開始。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one factor is enough to create an effect.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個因素已足以造成影響。"},{"en":"It separates the effect of one cause from other causes.","zh":"它把一個原因的效果與其他原因分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"generate additional demand for","meaning":"產生對……的額外需求","examples":[{"en":"Rising affluence generates additional demand for water.","zh":"日益富裕產生對水的額外需求。"},{"en":"To generate additional demand for something means to create extra need for it.","zh":"generate additional demand for 某物，指創造對它的額外需要。"},{"en":"A new housing estate can generate additional demand for buses and clinics.","zh":"新屋苑可以產生對巴士和診所的額外需求。"},{"en":"Extra demand appears when more people use a service or use it more often.","zh":"當更多人使用某服務或更頻繁使用，額外需求就會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how change creates new pressure on supply.","zh":"這個短語描述改變如何對供應造成新壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"move up the food chain","meaning":"轉向較高層次的飲食","examples":[{"en":"People use more grain as they move up the food chain.","zh":"隨着人們轉向較高層次的飲食，他們會使用更多穀物。"},{"en":"To move up the food chain means to eat more animal products and fewer simple plant staples.","zh":"move up the food chain 指吃更多動物產品，較少依賴簡單植物主食。"},{"en":"A family may move up the food chain when rising income lets them buy more meat and dairy.","zh":"當收入上升讓家庭購買更多肉類和奶類，他們可能轉向較高層次的飲食。"},{"en":"Eating more animal products requires more grain because animals must be fed first.","zh":"吃更多動物產品需要更多穀物，因為動物必須先被餵養。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shift toward a richer, more resource-heavy diet.","zh":"這個短語描述轉向更富裕、更耗資源的飲食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"consume more","meaning":"消耗更多","examples":[{"en":"People consume more meat and dairy products as they become wealthier.","zh":"隨着人們變得更富裕，他們消耗更多肉類和奶類產品。"},{"en":"To consume more means to use, eat or buy a larger amount.","zh":"consume more 指使用、食用或購買更大數量。"},{"en":"Students may consume more electricity when they use air conditioning all afternoon.","zh":"如果學生整個下午使用冷氣，他們可能消耗更多電力。"},{"en":"Consuming more can improve comfort but also increase pressure on resources.","zh":"消耗更多可以改善舒適度，但也增加資源壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an increase in use.","zh":"這個短語描述使用量增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"livestock products","meaning":"畜產品","examples":[{"en":"A diet rich in livestock products requires more grain.","zh":"富含畜產品的飲食需要更多穀物。"},{"en":"Livestock products are foods from farm animals, such as meat, milk and eggs.","zh":"livestock products 是來自農場動物的食物，例如肉、奶和蛋。"},{"en":"Families buy livestock products when they choose chicken, beef, cheese or yoghurt.","zh":"家庭購買雞肉、牛肉、芝士或乳酪時，就是購買畜產品。"},{"en":"Producing livestock products often requires grain, water, land and animal care.","zh":"生產畜產品通常需要穀物、水、土地和動物照料。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to animal-based food products.","zh":"這個短語指動物來源的食物產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"require grain per person a year","meaning":"每人每年需要穀物","examples":[{"en":"A US diet requires 800 kilograms of grain per person a year.","zh":"美國式飲食每人每年需要800公斤穀物。"},{"en":"To require grain per person a year means each person’s diet needs that amount of grain annually.","zh":"require grain per person a year 指每個人的飲食每年需要該數量的穀物。"},{"en":"A meat-heavy diet may require more grain per person a year because animals eat grain too.","zh":"肉類較多的飲食可能每人每年需要更多穀物，因為動物也吃穀物。"},{"en":"This measure includes grain eaten directly and grain used to feed livestock.","zh":"這種量度包括直接食用的穀物和用來餵養牲畜的穀物。"},{"en":"The phrase links diet with yearly grain demand.","zh":"這個短語把飲食與年度穀物需求連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be dominated by","meaning":"以……為主","examples":[{"en":"Indian diets are often dominated by a starchy food staple such as rice.","zh":"印度飲食常以米等澱粉類主食為主。"},{"en":"To be dominated by something means to be mainly made up of or strongly controlled by it.","zh":"be dominated by 某物，指主要由它構成或強烈受它控制。"},{"en":"A student’s timetable may be dominated by exam revision in April.","zh":"學生四月的時間表可能以考試溫習為主。"},{"en":"If a diet is dominated by one staple, most calories come from that food.","zh":"如果飲食以一種主食為主，大部分熱量就來自該食物。"},{"en":"The phrase shows what takes the largest role.","zh":"這個短語顯示甚麼佔最大角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"starchy food staple","meaning":"澱粉類主食","examples":[{"en":"Rice is a starchy food staple in many diets.","zh":"米是許多飲食中的澱粉類主食。"},{"en":"A starchy food staple is a basic food rich in starch and eaten regularly.","zh":"starchy food staple 是富含澱粉並經常食用的基本食物。"},{"en":"Rice, bread, potatoes and noodles can be starchy food staples.","zh":"米、麵包、薯仔和麵都可以是澱粉類主食。"},{"en":"Such staples provide energy and often form the centre of daily meals.","zh":"這類主食提供能量，並常構成日常膳食中心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a main carbohydrate food.","zh":"這個短語描述主要碳水化合物食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"typically need only","meaning":"通常只需要","examples":[{"en":"Indian diets typically need only 200 kilograms of grain per person a year.","zh":"印度飲食通常每人每年只需要200公斤穀物。"},{"en":"Typically need only means usually require no more than a relatively small amount.","zh":"typically need only 指通常只需要相對較少的數量。"},{"en":"A short presentation typically needs only three clear points.","zh":"短匯報通常只需要三個清楚重點。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the normal requirement is limited.","zh":"這個短語顯示正常需要量有限。"},{"en":"It often contrasts with another case that needs much more.","zh":"它常與需要多得多的另一情況作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"four times as much","meaning":"四倍之多","examples":[{"en":"Using four times as much grain means using four times as much water.","zh":"使用四倍之多的穀物，意味使用四倍之多的水。"},{"en":"Four times as much means an amount that is four times larger.","zh":"four times as much 指數量大四倍。"},{"en":"If one class uses four times as much paper as another, it creates much more waste.","zh":"如果一個班用紙量是另一班的四倍，就會造成多得多的浪費。"},{"en":"When resource use becomes four times as much, pressure on supply rises sharply.","zh":"當資源使用量變成四倍，供應壓力會急劇上升。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses a clear numerical comparison.","zh":"這個短語表達清楚的數字比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"once a localised phenomenon","meaning":"曾經是地方性現象","examples":[{"en":"Water scarcity was once a localised phenomenon.","zh":"水資源匱乏曾經是地方性現象。"},{"en":"Once a localised phenomenon means something used to happen only in limited places.","zh":"once a localised phenomenon 指某事過去只在有限地方發生。"},{"en":"Online bullying was once seen as a localised phenomenon, but it now affects many schools.","zh":"網絡欺凌曾被視為地方性現象，但現在影響許多學校。"},{"en":"A localised problem can spread when trade, travel or technology connects places.","zh":"當貿易、旅行或科技把地方連起來，地方性問題可以擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts a past local issue with a wider present issue.","zh":"這個短語把過去的地方問題與現在更廣泛的問題作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"water scarcity","meaning":"水資源匱乏","examples":[{"en":"Water scarcity is now crossing national borders.","zh":"水資源匱乏現在正跨越國界。"},{"en":"Water scarcity means there is not enough water to meet people’s needs.","zh":"water scarcity 指沒有足夠水滿足人們的需要。"},{"en":"A region faces water scarcity when rivers are low and wells cannot supply enough water.","zh":"當河流水位低而水井無法供應足夠水，地區就面對水資源匱乏。"},{"en":"Water scarcity can affect farming, health, schools and economic growth.","zh":"水資源匱乏可以影響農業、健康、學校和經濟增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shortage of usable water.","zh":"這個短語描述可用水短缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cross national borders","meaning":"跨越國界","examples":[{"en":"Water scarcity is crossing national borders through grain trade.","zh":"水資源匱乏正透過穀物貿易跨越國界。"},{"en":"To cross national borders means to move or spread from one country to another.","zh":"cross national borders 指從一個國家移動或擴散到另一個國家。"},{"en":"A disease can cross national borders when people travel widely.","zh":"當人們廣泛旅行，疾病可以跨越國界。"},{"en":"Problems cross borders when countries depend on one another for goods or resources.","zh":"當國家彼此依賴貨品或資源，問題就會跨越國界。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an issue becoming international.","zh":"這個短語描述議題變成國際性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"via","meaning":"透過","examples":[{"en":"Water scarcity is spreading via the international grain trade.","zh":"水資源匱乏正透過國際穀物貿易擴散。"},{"en":"Via means through or by means of a particular route or method.","zh":"via 指透過某特定路線或方法。"},{"en":"Students can submit homework via an online platform.","zh":"學生可以透過網上平台提交功課。"},{"en":"Problems can spread via trade, travel, media or technology.","zh":"問題可以透過貿易、旅行、媒體或科技擴散。"},{"en":"The word shows the channel through which something happens.","zh":"這個詞顯示某事發生的渠道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"international grain trade","meaning":"國際穀物貿易","examples":[{"en":"Water scarcity now affects the international grain trade.","zh":"水資源匱乏現在影響國際穀物貿易。"},{"en":"International grain trade is the buying and selling of grain between countries.","zh":"international grain trade 是國家之間買賣穀物。"},{"en":"A country may rely on international grain trade when local harvests are too small.","zh":"當本地收成太少，國家可能依賴國際穀物貿易。"},{"en":"Water shortages can increase grain imports and change world prices.","zh":"水資源短缺可以增加穀物進口並改變世界價格。"},{"en":"The phrase links food supply with global markets.","zh":"這個短語把糧食供應與全球市場連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the fastest-growing grain import market","meaning":"增長最快的穀物進口市場","examples":[{"en":"North Africa and the Middle East form the world’s fastest-growing grain import market.","zh":"北非和中東形成世界增長最快的穀物進口市場。"},{"en":"The fastest-growing grain import market is the region where grain imports are increasing most quickly.","zh":"fastest-growing grain import market 是穀物進口增長最快的地區。"},{"en":"A city can become the fastest-growing market for electric buses if orders rise sharply.","zh":"如果訂單急升，一座城市可以成為電動巴士增長最快的市場。"},{"en":"Rapid growth in imports often shows local production cannot meet demand.","zh":"進口快速增長通常顯示本地生產無法滿足需求。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where import demand is rising fastest.","zh":"這個短語指出進口需求上升最快的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"grain import market","meaning":"穀物進口市場","examples":[{"en":"The region has become a major grain import market.","zh":"該地區已成為主要穀物進口市場。"},{"en":"A grain import market is a place or region that buys grain from other countries.","zh":"grain import market 是從其他國家購買穀物的地方或地區。"},{"en":"A drought-hit country may become a grain import market when its harvest fails.","zh":"當收成失敗，受乾旱打擊的國家可能成為穀物進口市場。"},{"en":"Grain import markets depend on global prices and shipping routes.","zh":"穀物進口市場依賴全球價格和航運路線。"},{"en":"The phrase describes demand for grain from abroad.","zh":"這個短語描述對外國穀物的需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"simultaneously experiencing","meaning":"同時經歷","examples":[{"en":"Many countries are simultaneously experiencing water shortages and population growth.","zh":"許多國家正同時經歷水資源短缺和人口增長。"},{"en":"Simultaneously experiencing means going through two or more things at the same time.","zh":"simultaneously experiencing 指同時經歷兩件或以上事情。"},{"en":"A student may be simultaneously experiencing exam pressure and family stress.","zh":"學生可能同時經歷考試壓力和家庭壓力。"},{"en":"When problems happen simultaneously, each one can make the other harder to manage.","zh":"當問題同時發生，每一個都可以令另一個更難處理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes overlapping experiences.","zh":"這個短語描述重疊的經歷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rapid population growth","meaning":"急速人口增長","examples":[{"en":"Rapid population growth increases pressure on water supplies.","zh":"急速人口增長增加水源供應壓力。"},{"en":"Rapid population growth means the number of people is rising quickly.","zh":"rapid population growth 指人口數目快速上升。"},{"en":"A town with rapid population growth may need new schools before planners expected.","zh":"急速人口增長的小鎮可能比規劃者預期更早需要新學校。"},{"en":"Fast growth can make water, housing and transport systems fall behind demand.","zh":"快速增長可以令水、房屋和交通系統追不上需求。"},{"en":"The phrase describes quick expansion in population size.","zh":"這個短語描述人口規模快速擴大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the region’s cities and industries","meaning":"該區的城市和工業","examples":[{"en":"The region’s cities and industries are increasing demand for water.","zh":"該區的城市和工業正在增加對水的需求。"},{"en":"The region’s cities and industries means the urban areas and economic production sectors in that area.","zh":"region’s cities and industries 指該地區的城市區域和經濟生產部門。"},{"en":"A coastal region’s cities and industries may both need clean water every day.","zh":"沿海地區的城市和工業可能每天都需要清潔水源。"},{"en":"When cities and industries expand together, water demand can rise sharply.","zh":"當城市和工業一起擴張，用水需求可以急升。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies two major sources of demand in a region.","zh":"這個短語指出一個地區中兩個主要需求來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be typically satisfied by","meaning":"通常透過……滿足","examples":[{"en":"Urban demand is typically satisfied by diverting water from irrigation.","zh":"城市需求通常透過從灌溉中調走水源來滿足。"},{"en":"To be typically satisfied by something means to be usually met through that method.","zh":"be typically satisfied by 某方法，指通常透過該方式被滿足。"},{"en":"A school’s demand for extra chairs may be typically satisfied by borrowing from the hall.","zh":"學校對額外椅子的需求通常透過從禮堂借用來滿足。"},{"en":"When one demand is satisfied by taking resources from another use, a trade-off appears.","zh":"當一項需求靠從另一用途取走資源來滿足，取捨就會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the usual way a need is met.","zh":"這個短語描述需求通常如何被滿足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"divert water from irrigation","meaning":"從灌溉中調走水源","examples":[{"en":"Cities often divert water from irrigation to meet their needs.","zh":"城市常從灌溉中調走水源以滿足需要。"},{"en":"To divert water from irrigation means to take water away from farming and use it elsewhere.","zh":"divert water from irrigation 指把水從農業灌溉中取走，改作其他用途。"},{"en":"A government may divert water from irrigation to supply a growing city during drought.","zh":"乾旱期間，政府可能從灌溉中調走水源供應增長中的城市。"},{"en":"Diverting irrigation water can reduce crop production.","zh":"調走灌溉用水可以減少農作物產量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shifting water from farms to another use.","zh":"這個短語描述把水由農場轉向另一用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"food production capacity","meaning":"糧食生產能力","examples":[{"en":"Diverting water from irrigation reduces food production capacity.","zh":"從灌溉中調走水源會降低糧食生產能力。"},{"en":"Food production capacity is the ability of farms or a region to produce food.","zh":"food production capacity 是農場或地區生產糧食的能力。"},{"en":"A village’s food production capacity falls if farmland lacks water.","zh":"如果農田缺水，村莊的糧食生產能力會下降。"},{"en":"Lower capacity means a country may need to import more food.","zh":"能力下降意味着國家可能需要進口更多食物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how much food can be produced.","zh":"這個短語描述能生產多少糧食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be offset by","meaning":"由……抵銷","examples":[{"en":"The loss in food production capacity is offset by importing grain.","zh":"糧食生產能力的損失由進口穀物抵銷。"},{"en":"To be offset by something means to be balanced or compensated for by it.","zh":"be offset by 某事，指由它平衡或補償。"},{"en":"A higher electricity bill may be offset by savings from using less petrol.","zh":"較高電費可能由較少使用汽油的節省抵銷。"},{"en":"Offsetting a loss does not remove the problem; it only balances part of its effect.","zh":"抵銷損失並不等於消除問題；它只是平衡部分影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes compensation for a negative change.","zh":"這個短語描述對負面變化的補償。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"import grain from abroad","meaning":"從外國進口穀物","examples":[{"en":"Countries can offset food losses by importing grain from abroad.","zh":"國家可以透過從外國進口穀物來抵銷糧食損失。"},{"en":"To import grain from abroad means to buy grain from other countries.","zh":"import grain from abroad 指從其他國家購買穀物。"},{"en":"A country may import grain from abroad after drought damages its own harvest.","zh":"乾旱破壞本地收成後，國家可能從外國進口穀物。"},{"en":"Importing grain can protect food supply but makes a country depend on global markets.","zh":"進口穀物可以保護糧食供應，但令國家依賴全球市場。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bringing in grain from outside the country.","zh":"這個短語描述從國外引入穀物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"represent","meaning":"代表；相當於","examples":[{"en":"One ton of grain represents 1,000 tons of water.","zh":"一噸穀物代表1000噸水。"},{"en":"To represent something means to stand for it or be equal to it in meaning or value.","zh":"represent 某物，指代表它或在意思或價值上相當於它。"},{"en":"A school badge represents the identity and history of the school.","zh":"校徽代表學校的身份和歷史。"},{"en":"In this passage, grain represents hidden water because water was used to grow it.","zh":"在這篇文章中，穀物代表隱藏的水，因為種植它使用了水。"},{"en":"The word helps show what is indirectly contained in a product.","zh":"這個詞幫助顯示產品中間接包含甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the most efficient way to","meaning":"最有效率的方法去……","examples":[{"en":"Importing grain becomes the most efficient way to import water.","zh":"進口穀物成為進口水資源最有效率的方法。"},{"en":"The most efficient way to do something is the method that achieves it with the least waste or effort.","zh":"most efficient way to do something 是以最少浪費或努力達成目標的方法。"},{"en":"Taking one direct bus may be the most efficient way to reach school.","zh":"乘坐一程直達巴士可能是到校最有效率的方法。"},{"en":"An efficient method saves time, money, energy or resources.","zh":"有效率的方法會節省時間、金錢、能源或資源。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the best practical method for a goal.","zh":"這個短語指出達成目標的最佳實用方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"import water","meaning":"進口水資源","examples":[{"en":"Importing grain is, in effect, a way to import water.","zh":"進口穀物實際上是一種進口水資源的方式。"},{"en":"To import water, in this context, means to obtain water indirectly through products made with water.","zh":"import water 在這個語境中，指透過用水製成的產品間接取得水。"},{"en":"A dry country imports water indirectly when it buys rice grown with foreign irrigation water.","zh":"乾旱國家購買以外國灌溉水種植的米時，就是間接進口水資源。"},{"en":"Importing food can reduce pressure on local water supplies.","zh":"進口食物可以減少本地水源供應壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase explains hidden water trade through food.","zh":"這個短語解釋透過食物進行的隱性水貿易。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"imported wheat","meaning":"進口小麥","examples":[{"en":"Iran imported 7 million tons of wheat last year.","zh":"伊朗去年進口了700萬噸小麥。"},{"en":"Imported wheat is wheat bought from another country and brought in for use.","zh":"imported wheat 是從另一個國家購買並帶入使用的小麥。"},{"en":"A bakery may depend on imported wheat if local wheat is too expensive or unavailable.","zh":"如果本地小麥太貴或沒有供應，麵包店可能依賴進口小麥。"},{"en":"Imported wheat can help feed people when local harvests fail.","zh":"當本地收成失敗，進口小麥可以幫助養活人民。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to foreign wheat entering a country’s food supply.","zh":"這個短語指進入一國糧食供應的外國小麥。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"eclipse","meaning":"超越","examples":[{"en":"Iran eclipsed Japan to become the world’s leading wheat importer.","zh":"伊朗超越日本，成為全球最大小麥進口國。"},{"en":"To eclipse someone means to surpass them and become more important, larger or more noticeable.","zh":"eclipse 某人，指超越對方並變得更重要、更大或更受注意。"},{"en":"A new student may eclipse last year’s champion by scoring higher in every subject.","zh":"新學生可能每科分數都更高，從而超越去年的冠軍。"},{"en":"When one country eclipses another in imports, it buys more than the previous leader.","zh":"當一個國家在進口上超越另一國，它購買量超過之前的領先者。"},{"en":"The word describes overtaking and overshadowing.","zh":"這個詞描述趕過並蓋過對方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the world’s leading wheat importer","meaning":"全球最大小麥進口國","examples":[{"en":"Iran became the world’s leading wheat importer.","zh":"伊朗成為全球最大小麥進口國。"},{"en":"The world’s leading wheat importer is the country that imports more wheat than any other country.","zh":"world’s leading wheat importer 是進口小麥量多於任何其他國家的國家。"},{"en":"A country may become the leading importer when local production cannot satisfy demand.","zh":"當本地生產不能滿足需求，國家可能成為最大進口國。"},{"en":"Being the leading importer can reveal pressure on land, water or food systems.","zh":"成為最大進口國可以揭示土地、水或糧食系統的壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the top country in wheat imports.","zh":"這個短語指出小麥進口量最高的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be projected to move ahead of","meaning":"預計超越……","examples":[{"en":"Egypt is projected to move ahead of Japan as a wheat importer.","zh":"埃及預計會在小麥進口方面超越日本。"},{"en":"To be projected to move ahead of someone means to be expected to overtake them in rank or amount.","zh":"be projected to move ahead of 某人，指預計在排名或數量上超越對方。"},{"en":"A school team is projected to move ahead of its rival if it wins the next match.","zh":"如果校隊贏得下一場比賽，就預計會超越對手。"},{"en":"Forecasts like this show how rankings may change in the future.","zh":"這類預測顯示排名未來可能如何改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes expected future overtaking.","zh":"這個短語描述預期中的未來超越。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"nearly 70 million people each","meaning":"各有接近七千萬人口","examples":[{"en":"Iran and Egypt have nearly 70 million people each.","zh":"伊朗和埃及各有接近七千萬人口。"},{"en":"Nearly 70 million people each means each country has close to 70 million people.","zh":"nearly 70 million people each 指每個國家都有接近七千萬人口。"},{"en":"If two cities have nearly two million people each, both need large transport systems.","zh":"如果兩座城市各有接近二百萬人口，兩者都需要大型交通系統。"},{"en":"Large populations create large demand for food, water and jobs.","zh":"大人口會創造對食物、水和工作的巨大需求。"},{"en":"The phrase compares two places with similar population size.","zh":"這個短語比較兩地相似的人口規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"increase by more than","meaning":"增加超過","examples":[{"en":"Both populations are increasing by more than a million a year.","zh":"兩國人口每年都增加超過一百萬。"},{"en":"To increase by more than a number means to grow by an amount greater than that number.","zh":"increase by more than 某數字，指增長量大於該數字。"},{"en":"A school’s online followers may increase by more than 1,000 after a successful event.","zh":"學校在成功活動後，網上追蹤者可能增加超過一千。"},{"en":"Large yearly increases can create planning pressure.","zh":"大幅年度增長可以造成規劃壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growth beyond a stated amount.","zh":"這個短語描述超過所述數量的增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"press against the limits of","meaning":"逼近……的極限","examples":[{"en":"Both countries are pressing against the limits of their water supplies.","zh":"兩國都正在逼近其水源供應的極限。"},{"en":"To press against the limits of something means to come close to the maximum it can handle.","zh":"press against the limits of 某物，指接近它能承受的最大限度。"},{"en":"A school presses against the limits of its classrooms when every room is full.","zh":"當每間課室都滿座，學校就逼近課室容量的極限。"},{"en":"When a system reaches its limits, small extra demand can cause failure.","zh":"當系統達到極限，小小額外需求也可能造成失效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pressure near a boundary.","zh":"這個短語描述接近邊界的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"water supplies","meaning":"水源供應","examples":[{"en":"Population growth is pressing against the limits of water supplies.","zh":"人口增長正逼近水源供應的極限。"},{"en":"Water supplies are the sources and systems that provide water to people and activities.","zh":"water supplies 是向人和活動提供水的來源和系統。"},{"en":"A city’s water supplies may include reservoirs, rivers, wells and pipes.","zh":"城市的水源供應可能包括水庫、河流、水井和水管。"},{"en":"When water supplies are limited, governments may restrict use or search for new sources.","zh":"當水源供應有限，政府可能限制使用或尋找新來源。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to available water and the systems delivering it.","zh":"這個短語指可用水以及輸送它的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"foodstuffs","meaning":"食品；糧食產品","examples":[{"en":"The region imports grain and other foodstuffs.","zh":"該地區進口穀物和其他食品。"},{"en":"Foodstuffs are substances used as food or ingredients.","zh":"foodstuffs 是用作食物或食材的物質。"},{"en":"Rice, flour, cooking oil and beans are common foodstuffs in a market.","zh":"米、麵粉、食油和豆類都是市場中的常見食品。"},{"en":"Importing foodstuffs can support a country when local production is too low.","zh":"當本地生產太低，進口食品可以支援一個國家。"},{"en":"The word is a formal way to refer to food products.","zh":"這個詞是指食物產品的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"roughly equal to","meaning":"大致相等於","examples":[{"en":"The water required was roughly equal to the annual flow of the Nile River.","zh":"所需的水大致相等於尼羅河的年流量。"},{"en":"Roughly equal to means approximately the same as, not exactly identical.","zh":"roughly equal to 指大約相同，而不是完全一模一樣。"},{"en":"A student’s monthly transport cost may be roughly equal to two textbooks.","zh":"學生每月交通費可能大致相等於兩本教科書。"},{"en":"Rough comparisons help readers understand large numbers more easily.","zh":"粗略比較幫助讀者更容易理解大數字。"},{"en":"The phrase signals an approximate comparison.","zh":"這個短語標示近似比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"annual flow","meaning":"年流量","examples":[{"en":"The imported food represented water equal to the annual flow of the Nile River.","zh":"進口食物代表的水量等於尼羅河的年流量。"},{"en":"Annual flow is the amount of water a river carries in one year.","zh":"annual flow 是河流一年內承載的水量。"},{"en":"Engineers study a river’s annual flow before planning reservoirs.","zh":"工程師規劃水庫前會研究河流年流量。"},{"en":"Low annual flow can reduce irrigation, shipping and drinking-water supply.","zh":"年流量低可以減少灌溉、航運和飲用水供應。"},{"en":"The phrase measures water movement over a year.","zh":"這個短語量度一年內的水流量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the Nile River","meaning":"尼羅河","examples":[{"en":"The region’s water deficit is compared with the Nile River.","zh":"該地區的水資源赤字與尼羅河作比較。"},{"en":"The Nile River is a major river in Africa often used as a reference for large water flows.","zh":"Nile River 是非洲一條主要河流，常被用作大型水流量的參照。"},{"en":"Textbooks may mention the Nile River when explaining ancient farming societies.","zh":"教科書解釋古代農業社會時，可能提及尼羅河。"},{"en":"Comparing water demand with the Nile River helps readers imagine the scale.","zh":"把用水需求與尼羅河比較，幫助讀者想像規模。"},{"en":"The phrase names a well-known river used for comparison.","zh":"這個短語指出一條用作比較的著名河流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"fast-growing water deficit","meaning":"快速增長的水資源赤字","examples":[{"en":"The region has a fast-growing water deficit.","zh":"該地區有快速增長的水資源赤字。"},{"en":"A fast-growing water deficit is a shortage gap that is increasing quickly.","zh":"fast-growing water deficit 是快速增加的短缺差距。"},{"en":"A household has a fast-growing budget deficit if expenses rise every week while income stays the same.","zh":"如果家庭開支每星期上升而收入不變，就有快速增長的預算赤字。"},{"en":"Fast-growing deficits are dangerous because delay makes later correction harder.","zh":"快速增長的赤字很危險，因為延誤會令後來修正更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a rapidly worsening imbalance between water use and supply.","zh":"這個短語描述用水與供應之間迅速惡化的不平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in the form of","meaning":"以……形式","examples":[{"en":"Water is entering the region in the form of imported grain.","zh":"水正以進口穀物形式進入該地區。"},{"en":"In the form of means appearing as or being provided through a particular type of thing.","zh":"in the form of 指以某種事物的類型出現或被提供。"},{"en":"A teacher may give feedback in the form of written comments.","zh":"老師可能以書面評語形式給予回饋。"},{"en":"Support can come in the form of money, advice or extra time.","zh":"支援可以以金錢、建議或額外時間形式出現。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the shape or medium through which something appears.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物出現的形態或媒介。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"imported grain","meaning":"進口穀物","examples":[{"en":"Imported grain can be understood as imported water.","zh":"進口穀物可以被理解為進口水資源。"},{"en":"Imported grain is grain bought from another country and brought into the local food supply.","zh":"imported grain 是從另一國購買並帶入本地糧食供應的穀物。"},{"en":"A country may rely on imported grain when drought reduces its harvest.","zh":"當乾旱減少收成，國家可能依賴進口穀物。"},{"en":"Imported grain carries hidden water because water was used to grow it abroad.","zh":"進口穀物帶有隱藏水資源，因為它是在外國用水種植的。"},{"en":"The phrase connects foreign food supply with local resource shortages.","zh":"這個短語把外國糧食供應與本地資源短缺連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"future wars","meaning":"未來戰爭","examples":[{"en":"Some people say future wars may be fought over water.","zh":"有些人說未來戰爭可能因水而爆發。"},{"en":"Future wars are conflicts that may happen in the years ahead.","zh":"future wars 是未來年份可能發生的衝突。"},{"en":"Experts discuss future wars when they consider resources, borders and technology.","zh":"專家考慮資源、邊界和科技時，會討論未來戰爭。"},{"en":"If essential resources become scarce, they may create political tension.","zh":"如果必要資源變得稀缺，它們可能造成政治緊張。"},{"en":"The phrase points to possible conflicts, not events that have already happened.","zh":"這個短語指可能發生的衝突，而不是已發生的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be fought over","meaning":"因爭奪……而爆發","examples":[{"en":"Future wars may be fought over water rather than oil.","zh":"未來戰爭可能因爭奪水而不是石油而爆發。"},{"en":"To be fought over something means the conflict is caused by competition for that thing.","zh":"be fought over 某物，指衝突由爭奪該物造成。"},{"en":"Families may argue over inheritance, but countries may fight over land or resources.","zh":"家庭可能因遺產爭執，但國家可能因土地或資源開戰。"},{"en":"When something is essential and scarce, it can become a reason for conflict.","zh":"當某物必要又稀缺，它可以成為衝突原因。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what the struggle is about.","zh":"這個短語指出爭鬥圍繞甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"given the difficulty in","meaning":"鑑於……的困難","examples":[{"en":"Given the difficulty in winning a water war, competition may occur in grain markets.","zh":"鑑於贏得水戰的困難，競爭可能發生在穀物市場。"},{"en":"Given the difficulty in something means considering how hard that thing is.","zh":"given the difficulty in 某事，指考慮到該事有多困難。"},{"en":"Given the difficulty in finding parking, many teachers take the bus to school.","zh":"鑑於找車位的困難，許多老師乘巴士上學。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a reason based on practical difficulty.","zh":"這個短語引出基於實際困難的原因。"},{"en":"It helps explain why people choose an alternative path.","zh":"它幫助解釋為何人們選擇替代途徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"competition for","meaning":"對……的競爭","examples":[{"en":"Competition for water may take place in world grain markets.","zh":"對水的競爭可能在世界穀物市場發生。"},{"en":"Competition for something means different people or groups are trying to get the same limited thing.","zh":"competition for 某物，指不同人或群體試圖取得同一有限事物。"},{"en":"There is competition for good school places in crowded districts.","zh":"在擁擠地區，對好學位有競爭。"},{"en":"Competition becomes stronger when demand rises and supply is limited.","zh":"當需求上升而供應有限，競爭會變得更強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rivalry over a resource or opportunity.","zh":"這個短語描述對資源或機會的爭奪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take place in","meaning":"在……發生","examples":[{"en":"The competition for water may take place in world grain markets.","zh":"對水的競爭可能在世界穀物市場發生。"},{"en":"To take place in a setting means to happen there.","zh":"take place in 某環境，指在那裏發生。"},{"en":"The school debate will take place in the hall after lunch.","zh":"學校辯論會在午飯後於禮堂舉行。"},{"en":"Knowing where an event takes place helps readers understand its form and participants.","zh":"知道事件在哪裏發生，有助讀者理解其形式和參與者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the location or arena of an event.","zh":"這個短語描述事件的地點或場域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"world grain markets","meaning":"世界穀物市場","examples":[{"en":"Water shortages may affect world grain markets.","zh":"水資源短缺可能影響世界穀物市場。"},{"en":"World grain markets are global systems where grain is bought and sold between countries.","zh":"world grain markets 是國家之間買賣穀物的全球系統。"},{"en":"A poor harvest in one major country can raise prices in world grain markets.","zh":"一個主要國家收成差，可以推高世界穀物市場價格。"},{"en":"When many countries import more grain, world grain markets can become unstable.","zh":"當許多國家進口更多穀物，世界穀物市場可能變得不穩。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to international trade in grain.","zh":"這個短語指穀物的國際貿易市場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"financially strongest","meaning":"財力最強的","examples":[{"en":"The financially strongest countries may win the competition for grain.","zh":"財力最強的國家可能贏得穀物競爭。"},{"en":"Financially strongest means having the most money or economic power.","zh":"financially strongest 指擁有最多金錢或經濟力量。"},{"en":"Financially strongest families may afford private tutoring more easily.","zh":"財力最強的家庭可能更容易負擔私人補習。"},{"en":"In markets, financially strong buyers can often outbid weaker buyers.","zh":"在市場中，財力強的買家常能出價高過較弱買家。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strength based on money rather than force.","zh":"這個短語描述基於金錢而非武力的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"militarily strongest","meaning":"軍事上最強的","examples":[{"en":"The winners may not be the militarily strongest countries.","zh":"勝出者未必是軍事上最強的國家。"},{"en":"Militarily strongest means having the greatest armed forces or military power.","zh":"militarily strongest 指擁有最大武裝力量或軍事力量。"},{"en":"A militarily strongest country may still struggle if it cannot afford food imports.","zh":"軍事上最強的國家如果無法負擔糧食進口，仍可能吃力。"},{"en":"In grain markets, money may matter more than military strength.","zh":"在穀物市場中，金錢可能比軍事力量更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strength based on armed power.","zh":"這個短語描述基於武力的強大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"grow larger with each year","meaning":"逐年擴大","examples":[{"en":"The world water deficit grows larger with each year.","zh":"世界水資源赤字逐年擴大。"},{"en":"To grow larger with each year means to increase year after year.","zh":"grow larger with each year 指一年一年增加。"},{"en":"A student’s vocabulary grows larger with each year of reading.","zh":"學生詞彙量會隨每年閱讀逐年擴大。"},{"en":"If a deficit grows each year, delaying action makes the problem harder to solve.","zh":"如果赤字逐年擴大，延遲行動會令問題更難解決。"},{"en":"The phrase describes steady annual increase.","zh":"這個短語描述穩定的年度增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"potentially more difficult to manage","meaning":"可能更難管理","examples":[{"en":"The growing water deficit is potentially more difficult to manage.","zh":"不斷增長的水資源赤字可能更難管理。"},{"en":"Potentially more difficult to manage means it may become harder to control or solve.","zh":"potentially more difficult to manage 指可能變得更難控制或解決。"},{"en":"A small classroom conflict is potentially more difficult to manage if teachers ignore it for weeks.","zh":"如果老師幾星期不理會，小小課室衝突可能更難管理。"},{"en":"Problems become harder to manage when they grow larger and affect more people.","zh":"當問題變大並影響更多人，它會更難處理。"},{"en":"The phrase warns about a possible increase in difficulty.","zh":"這個短語警告困難程度可能增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"decide abruptly to","meaning":"突然決定去……","examples":[{"en":"If governments decided abruptly to pump less water, grain production would fall.","zh":"如果政府突然決定減少抽水，穀物生產會下降。"},{"en":"To decide abruptly to do something means to make a sudden decision without gradual preparation.","zh":"decide abruptly to do something 指在沒有逐步準備下突然作出決定。"},{"en":"A school may create confusion if it decides abruptly to change the exam timetable.","zh":"如果學校突然決定更改考試時間表，可能造成混亂。"},{"en":"Abrupt decisions can solve one problem but create shocks elsewhere.","zh":"突然決定可以解決一個問題，但在其他地方造成衝擊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a sudden policy or action.","zh":"這個短語描述突然的政策或行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"stabilise water tables","meaning":"穩定地下水位","examples":[{"en":"Governments may need to stabilise water tables.","zh":"政府可能需要穩定地下水位。"},{"en":"To stabilise water tables means to stop underground water levels from continuing to fall.","zh":"stabilise water tables 指阻止地下水位繼續下降。"},{"en":"A farming region can stabilise water tables by pumping less and allowing rain to refill aquifers.","zh":"農業地區可以透過減少抽水並讓雨水補充含水層來穩定地下水位。"},{"en":"Stabilising water tables protects wells and future water supply.","zh":"穩定地下水位可以保護水井和未來供水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes keeping groundwater levels steady.","zh":"這個短語描述保持地下水水平穩定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"pump less water","meaning":"減少抽水","examples":[{"en":"Pumping less water would reduce the world grain harvest.","zh":"減少抽水會降低世界穀物收成。"},{"en":"To pump less water means to extract a smaller amount of water by machine.","zh":"pump less water 指用機器抽取較少水。"},{"en":"A farm may pump less water by using drip irrigation instead of flooding fields.","zh":"農場可以使用滴灌而不是淹灌田地，從而減少抽水。"},{"en":"Pumping less water can protect aquifers but may reduce crop output.","zh":"減少抽水可以保護含水層，但可能降低農作物產量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lowering water extraction.","zh":"這個短語描述降低取水量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"grain harvest would fall by","meaning":"穀物收成會下降……","examples":[{"en":"The world grain harvest would fall by about 160 million tons.","zh":"世界穀物收成會下降約1.6億噸。"},{"en":"Grain harvest would fall by a number means the amount of grain collected would decrease by that amount.","zh":"grain harvest would fall by 某數量，指收集到的穀物會減少該數量。"},{"en":"A farm’s rice harvest would fall by half if irrigation stopped during the growing season.","zh":"如果生長季節停止灌溉，農場米收成可能下降一半。"},{"en":"A falling harvest can raise food prices and increase imports.","zh":"收成下降可以推高食物價格並增加進口。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a predicted drop in crop output.","zh":"這個短語描述作物產量的預計下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"grain prices","meaning":"穀物價格","examples":[{"en":"Grain prices would rise sharply if the harvest fell.","zh":"如果收成下降，穀物價格會急升。"},{"en":"Grain prices are the market prices of crops such as wheat, rice and corn.","zh":"grain prices 是小麥、米和粟米等作物的市場價格。"},{"en":"Families may pay more for bread and noodles when grain prices rise.","zh":"當穀物價格上升，家庭可能為麵包和麵支付更多。"},{"en":"Poor harvests, war and transport problems can increase grain prices.","zh":"收成差、戰爭和運輸問題可以提高穀物價格。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the cost of staple grains in markets.","zh":"這個短語指市場中主食穀物的成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"go off the chart","meaning":"飆升至極高水平","examples":[{"en":"Grain prices would go off the chart.","zh":"穀物價格會飆升至極高水平。"},{"en":"To go off the chart means to rise to an extremely high level.","zh":"go off the chart 指上升到極高水平。"},{"en":"A school’s electricity bill may go off the chart during a long heatwave.","zh":"長時間熱浪期間，學校電費可能飆升至極高水平。"},{"en":"When prices go off the chart, ordinary families may struggle to afford basics.","zh":"當價格飆升至極高水平，普通家庭可能難以負擔基本用品。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and emphasises a dramatic increase.","zh":"這個短語較口語，強調劇烈上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"continue to widen","meaning":"繼續擴大","examples":[{"en":"If the deficit continues to widen, the eventual adjustment will be greater.","zh":"如果赤字繼續擴大，最終調整會更大。"},{"en":"To continue to widen means to keep becoming larger or more serious.","zh":"continue to widen 指持續變大或變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"If the gap between strong and weak students continues to widen, extra support is needed.","zh":"如果強弱學生之間的差距繼續擴大，就需要額外支援。"},{"en":"A widening deficit becomes harder to correct later.","zh":"不斷擴大的赤字之後更難修正。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an increasing gap.","zh":"這個短語描述增大的差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"eventual adjustment","meaning":"最終調整","examples":[{"en":"The eventual adjustment will be greater if the deficit widens.","zh":"如果赤字擴大，最終調整會更大。"},{"en":"Eventual adjustment is the correction that must happen later after a problem has grown.","zh":"eventual adjustment 是問題擴大後之後必須發生的修正。"},{"en":"If a student avoids revision all term, the eventual adjustment before exams will be painful.","zh":"如果學生整個學期逃避溫習，考試前的最終調整會很痛苦。"},{"en":"Delayed adjustment is often harder because the gap has become larger.","zh":"延遲調整通常更困難，因為差距已變得更大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a later correction or change.","zh":"這個短語描述後來的修正或改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"unless governments act quickly to","meaning":"除非政府迅速行動去……","examples":[{"en":"Unless governments act quickly to stabilise populations, shortages may worsen.","zh":"除非政府迅速行動穩定人口，短缺可能惡化。"},{"en":"Unless governments act quickly to do something means if they do not take fast action, a bad result may follow.","zh":"unless governments act quickly to do something 指如果政府不快速採取行動，壞結果可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"Unless schools act quickly to stop bullying, the victim may feel unsafe for months.","zh":"除非學校迅速行動制止欺凌，受害者可能幾個月都感到不安全。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a warning and a necessary response.","zh":"這個短語引出警告和必要回應。"},{"en":"It shows that delay can make the problem worse.","zh":"它顯示延誤可以令問題更差。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"stabilise their populations","meaning":"穩定人口","examples":[{"en":"Water-short countries need to stabilise their populations.","zh":"缺水國家需要穩定人口。"},{"en":"To stabilise their populations means to slow population growth until the number becomes more stable.","zh":"stabilise their populations 指減慢人口增長，直到人口數目更穩定。"},{"en":"A city may try to stabilise its population by balancing housing, jobs and family planning services.","zh":"城市可能透過平衡房屋、工作和家庭計劃服務來穩定人口。"},{"en":"Stable population size can make water, schools and hospitals easier to plan.","zh":"穩定人口規模可以令水、學校和醫院較易規劃。"},{"en":"The phrase describes controlling rapid demographic growth.","zh":"這個短語描述控制急速人口增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"raise water productivity","meaning":"提高水資源生產力","examples":[{"en":"Governments need to raise water productivity.","zh":"政府需要提高水資源生產力。"},{"en":"To raise water productivity means to produce more value or food from each unit of water.","zh":"raise water productivity 指每單位水創造更多價值或糧食。"},{"en":"A farm can raise water productivity by using drip irrigation instead of wasting water in open channels.","zh":"農場可以使用滴灌而不是在露天水渠浪費水，從而提高水資源生產力。"},{"en":"Higher water productivity reduces pressure on rivers and aquifers.","zh":"較高水資源生產力可以減少河流和含水層壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using water more efficiently.","zh":"這個短語描述更有效率地用水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"may soon become","meaning":"可能很快變成","examples":[{"en":"Water shortages may soon become food shortages.","zh":"水資源短缺可能很快變成糧食短缺。"},{"en":"May soon become means could change into another problem in the near future.","zh":"may soon become 指在不久將來可能轉變成另一問題。"},{"en":"A small cough may soon become a serious illness if it is ignored.","zh":"如果被忽視，小咳嗽可能很快變成嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that one problem can develop into another quickly.","zh":"這個短語警告一個問題可以快速發展成另一個問題。"},{"en":"It connects present risk with likely future consequence.","zh":"它把目前風險與可能的未來後果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"food shortages","meaning":"糧食短缺","examples":[{"en":"Water shortages may lead to food shortages.","zh":"水資源短缺可能導致糧食短缺。"},{"en":"Food shortages happen when there is not enough food for people’s needs.","zh":"food shortages 指沒有足夠食物滿足人們需要。"},{"en":"A city may face food shortages if transport is blocked after a storm.","zh":"暴風雨後如果交通受阻，城市可能面對糧食短缺。"},{"en":"Food shortages can raise prices and leave poor families hungry.","zh":"糧食短缺可以推高價格，令貧困家庭挨餓。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a lack of available food.","zh":"這個短語描述可用食物不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the growing number of","meaning":"日益增加的……數目","examples":[{"en":"The growing number of water-short countries may overwhelm grain supplies.","zh":"日益增加的缺水國家數目可能壓倒穀物供應。"},{"en":"The growing number of something means an increasing count of those things.","zh":"growing number of 某事物，指該事物數量不斷增加。"},{"en":"The growing number of elderly residents may increase demand for clinics.","zh":"日益增加的長者居民數目可能增加對診所的需求。"},{"en":"When the number of affected places grows, pressure on shared systems rises.","zh":"當受影響地方數目增加，共同系統的壓力會上升。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights increase in how many cases exist.","zh":"這個短語突出個案數量的增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"population giants","meaning":"人口大國","examples":[{"en":"China and India are population giants with rising grain-import needs.","zh":"中國和印度是人口大國，穀物進口需求正在上升。"},{"en":"Population giants are countries with extremely large populations.","zh":"population giants 是人口極大的國家。"},{"en":"A population giant can affect world markets because even small per-person changes become huge in total.","zh":"人口大國可以影響世界市場，因為人均小改變加起來也很巨大。"},{"en":"When population giants import more food, global supply can feel the pressure.","zh":"當人口大國進口更多食物，全球供應會感受到壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes countries whose population size gives them major influence.","zh":"這個短語描述因人口規模而有重大影響力的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"rising grain-import needs","meaning":"日益增加的穀物進口需求","examples":[{"en":"Water-short countries may have rising grain-import needs.","zh":"缺水國家可能有日益增加的穀物進口需求。"},{"en":"Rising grain-import needs means increasing need to buy grain from other countries.","zh":"rising grain-import needs 指從其他國家購買穀物的需要增加。"},{"en":"A country may have rising grain-import needs when drought reduces local harvests.","zh":"當乾旱減少本地收成，國家可能有日益增加的穀物進口需求。"},{"en":"Rising import needs can push up prices in world grain markets.","zh":"進口需求上升可以推高世界穀物市場價格。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growing dependence on foreign grain.","zh":"這個短語描述對外國穀物依賴增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"overwhelm the exportable supply","meaning":"壓倒可供出口的供應量","examples":[{"en":"Rising demand may overwhelm the exportable supply in food-surplus countries.","zh":"上升的需求可能壓倒糧食盈餘國家的可供出口供應量。"},{"en":"To overwhelm the exportable supply means demand becomes greater than the amount available for export.","zh":"overwhelm the exportable supply 指需求大於可供出口的數量。"},{"en":"If too many schools order laptops at once, demand may overwhelm the supplier’s stock.","zh":"如果太多學校同時訂購手提電腦，需求可能壓倒供應商庫存。"},{"en":"When exportable supply is overwhelmed, prices rise and poorer buyers lose access.","zh":"當可供出口供應量被壓倒，價格會上升，較貧窮買家會失去取得機會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes demand exceeding what can be sold abroad.","zh":"這個短語描述需求超過可售往外國的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"exportable supply","meaning":"可供出口的供應量","examples":[{"en":"Food-surplus countries may not have enough exportable supply.","zh":"糧食盈餘國家可能沒有足夠可供出口的供應量。"},{"en":"Exportable supply is the amount of goods a country can sell to other countries after meeting its own needs.","zh":"exportable supply 是一個國家滿足自身需要後可賣給其他國家的貨物數量。"},{"en":"A rice-producing country may have little exportable supply if local demand is high.","zh":"如果本地需求高，產米國可能只有很少可供出口供應量。"},{"en":"Exportable supply can shrink after drought, war or transport problems.","zh":"乾旱、戰爭或運輸問題後，可供出口供應量可以縮小。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the share available for export.","zh":"這個短語指可出口的份額。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"food-surplus countries","meaning":"糧食盈餘國家","examples":[{"en":"The United States, Canada, and Australia are food-surplus countries.","zh":"美國、加拿大和澳洲是糧食盈餘國家。"},{"en":"Food-surplus countries produce more food than they need for their own people.","zh":"food-surplus countries 生產的糧食多於本國人民所需。"},{"en":"A food-surplus country can sell extra grain to countries facing shortages.","zh":"糧食盈餘國家可以把額外穀物賣給面對短缺的國家。"},{"en":"The world depends on food-surplus countries when many regions experience poor harvests.","zh":"當許多地區收成差，世界會依賴糧食盈餘國家。"},{"en":"The phrase describes countries with extra food available.","zh":"這個短語描述有額外食物可用的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in turn","meaning":"進而","examples":[{"en":"Rising grain imports could, in turn, destabilise world grain markets.","zh":"穀物進口上升進而可能令世界穀物市場不穩。"},{"en":"In turn means as the next result in a chain of effects.","zh":"in turn 指作為一連串影響中的下一個結果。"},{"en":"Poor sleep reduces attention, which in turn lowers exam performance.","zh":"睡眠不足降低注意力，進而降低考試表現。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how one effect becomes the cause of another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個結果如何成為另一個結果的原因。"},{"en":"It helps explain a sequence of consequences.","zh":"它幫助解釋後果的連鎖次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"destabilise world grain markets","meaning":"令世界穀物市場不穩","examples":[{"en":"Rising import demand could destabilise world grain markets.","zh":"進口需求上升可能令世界穀物市場不穩。"},{"en":"To destabilise world grain markets means to make global grain trade less steady and predictable.","zh":"destabilise world grain markets 指令全球穀物貿易變得不穩定和難以預測。"},{"en":"A sudden export ban can destabilise world grain markets by reducing supply.","zh":"突然的出口禁令可以透過減少供應令世界穀物市場不穩。"},{"en":"Unstable grain markets can cause sharp price rises and food insecurity.","zh":"不穩定的穀物市場可以造成價格急升和糧食不安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes damage to the stability of global food trade.","zh":"這個短語描述對全球糧食貿易穩定性的破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"risk of delay in","meaning":"延遲處理……的風險","examples":[{"en":"There is a risk of delay in dealing with the water deficit.","zh":"處理水資源赤字存在延遲風險。"},{"en":"Risk of delay in something means the danger that action will happen too late.","zh":"risk of delay in 某事，指行動可能太遲發生的危險。"},{"en":"There is a risk of delay in treating illness if symptoms are ignored.","zh":"如果症狀被忽視，治療疾病就有延遲風險。"},{"en":"Delay can make a manageable problem become serious.","zh":"延遲可以令可處理問題變得嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that late action may create harm.","zh":"這個短語警告遲行動可能造成傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"deal with the deficit","meaning":"處理赤字","examples":[{"en":"Governments must deal with the deficit before it worsens.","zh":"政府必須在赤字惡化前處理它。"},{"en":"To deal with the deficit means to take action to reduce or solve the shortage gap.","zh":"deal with the deficit 指採取行動減少或解決短缺差距。"},{"en":"A school must deal with a budget deficit by cutting waste or finding new funding.","zh":"學校必須透過減少浪費或尋找新資金來處理預算赤字。"},{"en":"Ignoring a deficit usually makes later solutions more painful.","zh":"忽視赤字通常會令後來解決方法更痛苦。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active management of a shortfall.","zh":"這個短語描述主動管理短缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"low-income, water-short countries","meaning":"低收入缺水國家","examples":[{"en":"Low-income, water-short countries may not afford imported grain.","zh":"低收入缺水國家可能負擔不起進口穀物。"},{"en":"Low-income, water-short countries are poor countries that also lack enough water.","zh":"low-income, water-short countries 是同時貧窮又缺乏足夠水的國家。"},{"en":"Such countries may struggle to buy food when world grain prices rise.","zh":"當世界穀物價格上升，這類國家可能難以購買食物。"},{"en":"Poverty and water shortage together make food insecurity harder to escape.","zh":"貧窮和缺水一起出現，令糧食不安全更難擺脫。"},{"en":"The phrase describes countries facing both financial and water limits.","zh":"這個短語描述同時面對財政和水資源限制的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"afford to import","meaning":"負擔得起進口……","examples":[{"en":"Some countries may not be able to afford to import needed grain.","zh":"有些國家可能無法負擔得起進口所需穀物。"},{"en":"To afford to import something means to have enough money to buy it from abroad.","zh":"afford to import 某物，指有足夠金錢從外國購買它。"},{"en":"A small shop may not afford to import expensive ingredients every week.","zh":"小店可能無法每星期負擔得起進口昂貴食材。"},{"en":"If prices rise, poor countries may lose the ability to import essential food.","zh":"如果價格上升，貧窮國家可能失去進口必要食物的能力。"},{"en":"The phrase links foreign buying with financial ability.","zh":"這個短語把外國購買與財政能力連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"needed grain","meaning":"所需穀物","examples":[{"en":"Low-income countries may struggle to import needed grain.","zh":"低收入國家可能難以進口所需穀物。"},{"en":"Needed grain is the grain required to feed people or maintain food supply.","zh":"needed grain 是養活人民或維持糧食供應所需的穀物。"},{"en":"After a poor harvest, a country may buy needed grain from abroad.","zh":"收成差後，國家可能從外國購買所需穀物。"},{"en":"If needed grain is too expensive, families may face hunger.","zh":"如果所需穀物太昂貴，家庭可能面對飢餓。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to grain that is necessary, not optional.","zh":"這個短語指必要而非可有可無的穀物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"trap millions of people in","meaning":"令數以百萬計的人陷入……","examples":[{"en":"Water shortages may trap millions of people in hydrological poverty.","zh":"水資源短缺可能令數以百萬計的人陷入水資源貧困。"},{"en":"To trap millions of people in a condition means to keep huge numbers of people stuck there.","zh":"trap millions of people in 某狀況，指令大量人被困在其中。"},{"en":"Poor education can trap many children in low-paid work later in life.","zh":"差劣教育可以令許多孩子日後陷入低薪工作。"},{"en":"A trap is harder to escape when the problem removes the tools needed for escape.","zh":"當問題奪走逃脫所需的工具，陷阱會更難擺脫。"},{"en":"The phrase describes large-scale human suffering that becomes self-reinforcing.","zh":"這個短語描述大規模且會自我強化的人類苦難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"thirsty and hungry","meaning":"又渴又餓","examples":[{"en":"People trapped in hydrological poverty may be thirsty and hungry.","zh":"陷入水資源貧困的人可能又渴又餓。"},{"en":"Thirsty and hungry means lacking both enough water and enough food.","zh":"thirsty and hungry 指同時缺乏足夠水和足夠食物。"},{"en":"Children may become thirsty and hungry if a long school trip has no water or lunch break.","zh":"如果長途學校旅行沒有水和午飯休息，孩子可能又渴又餓。"},{"en":"Water shortages can make people hungry because farms need water to grow food.","zh":"水資源短缺可以令人飢餓，因為農場需要水種植食物。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the link between water insecurity and food insecurity.","zh":"這個短語顯示水不安全與糧食不安全之間的聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"unable to escape","meaning":"無法逃脫","examples":[{"en":"Millions may be unable to escape hydrological poverty.","zh":"數以百萬計的人可能無法逃脫水資源貧困。"},{"en":"Unable to escape means not able to get out of a difficult situation.","zh":"unable to escape 指不能脫離困難處境。"},{"en":"A family may be unable to escape debt if medical bills keep rising.","zh":"如果醫療費持續上升，家庭可能無法逃脫債務。"},{"en":"People are unable to escape when every solution requires resources they do not have.","zh":"當每個解決方法都需要他們沒有的資源，人們就無法逃脫。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being trapped by circumstances.","zh":"這個短語描述被環境困住。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"opportunities for developing","meaning":"發展……的機會","examples":[{"en":"There are still some opportunities for developing new water resources.","zh":"仍然有一些發展新水資源的機會。"},{"en":"Opportunities for developing something are chances to create, improve or expand it.","zh":"opportunities for developing 某物，是創造、改善或擴展它的機會。"},{"en":"A school may have opportunities for developing new language programmes after receiving funding.","zh":"學校獲得資助後，可能有發展新語言課程的機會。"},{"en":"Opportunities matter because they show possible solutions still exist.","zh":"機會重要，因為它們顯示可能的解決方法仍然存在。"},{"en":"The phrase describes chances for future improvement or growth.","zh":"這個短語描述未來改善或增長的機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"new water resources","meaning":"新水資源","examples":[{"en":"Some opportunities remain for developing new water resources.","zh":"發展新水資源仍有一些機會。"},{"en":"New water resources are additional sources of usable water, such as treated wastewater or captured rainwater.","zh":"new water resources 是額外可用水源，例如經處理污水或收集雨水。"},{"en":"A city may develop new water resources by recycling wastewater for parks and farms.","zh":"城市可能透過回收污水供公園和農場使用來發展新水資源。"},{"en":"New resources can reduce pressure on rivers and aquifers.","zh":"新資源可以減少河流和含水層壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extra water sources made available for use.","zh":"這個短語描述可供使用的額外水源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"restore the balance between","meaning":"恢復……之間的平衡","examples":[{"en":"Governments must restore the balance between water use and sustainable supply.","zh":"政府必須恢復用水量與可持續供應之間的平衡。"},{"en":"To restore the balance between two things means to bring them back into a healthy relationship.","zh":"restore the balance between 兩件事，指把它們帶回健康關係。"},{"en":"A student may restore the balance between study and rest by planning breaks.","zh":"學生可能透過安排休息，恢復學習與休息之間的平衡。"},{"en":"Balance is restored when use no longer exceeds what can be replaced.","zh":"當使用量不再超過可補充量，平衡就會恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase describes correcting an unhealthy imbalance.","zh":"這個短語描述修正不健康的不平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"water use","meaning":"用水量","examples":[{"en":"Water use must be balanced with sustainable supply.","zh":"用水量必須與可持續供應保持平衡。"},{"en":"Water use is the amount and way water is consumed by people, farms and industries.","zh":"water use 是人、農場和工業消耗水的數量和方式。"},{"en":"A family can reduce water use by taking shorter showers and fixing leaks.","zh":"家庭可以透過縮短洗澡時間和修理漏水來減少用水量。"},{"en":"High water use becomes dangerous when rivers and aquifers cannot recover.","zh":"當河流和含水層無法恢復，高用水量就變得危險。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to how much water is used and for what purposes.","zh":"這個短語指使用多少水以及用於甚麼用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"sustainable supply","meaning":"可持續供應","examples":[{"en":"Water use must not exceed a sustainable supply.","zh":"用水量不得超過可持續供應。"},{"en":"Sustainable supply is the amount that can be used without damaging future availability.","zh":"sustainable supply 是可以使用而不損害未來可用性的數量。"},{"en":"A forest has a sustainable supply of wood only if trees regrow as fast as they are cut.","zh":"只有當樹木再生速度與砍伐速度相若，森林才有可持續木材供應。"},{"en":"If use exceeds sustainable supply, shortages will eventually appear.","zh":"如果使用量超過可持續供應，短缺最終會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes supply that can continue over time.","zh":"這個短語描述能隨時間持續的供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"depend primarily on","meaning":"主要取決於","examples":[{"en":"Restoring the balance will depend primarily on demand-side initiatives.","zh":"恢復平衡將主要取決於需求管理措施。"},{"en":"Depend primarily on means rely mainly on one factor or method.","zh":"depend primarily on 指主要依賴一個因素或方法。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may depend primarily on regular practice, not expensive books.","zh":"學生進步可能主要取決於定期練習，而不是昂貴書本。"},{"en":"If success depends primarily on one action, that action deserves special attention.","zh":"如果成功主要取決於一項行動，該行動就值得特別注意。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main requirement for success.","zh":"這個短語指出成功的主要條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"demand-side initiatives","meaning":"需求管理措施","examples":[{"en":"Demand-side initiatives include stabilising population and raising water productivity.","zh":"需求管理措施包括穩定人口和提高水資源生產力。"},{"en":"Demand-side initiatives are actions that reduce or manage how much people need to use.","zh":"demand-side initiatives 是減少或管理人們需要使用多少資源的行動。"},{"en":"A city may use demand-side initiatives by encouraging shorter showers and efficient appliances.","zh":"城市可能透過鼓勵較短洗澡時間和高效電器來使用需求管理措施。"},{"en":"These initiatives focus on lowering demand instead of only finding more supply.","zh":"這些措施重點在降低需求，而不只是尋找更多供應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes policies that manage consumption.","zh":"這個短語描述管理消耗的政策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"stabilising population","meaning":"穩定人口","examples":[{"en":"Stabilising population is one way to reduce pressure on water supplies.","zh":"穩定人口是減少水源供應壓力的一種方法。"},{"en":"Stabilising population means slowing population growth until the number becomes steady.","zh":"stabilising population 指減慢人口增長，直到人數變得穩定。"},{"en":"Better education and healthcare can help communities stabilise population over time.","zh":"更好的教育和醫療可以幫助社區隨時間穩定人口。"},{"en":"Stable population growth makes it easier to plan water, housing and schools.","zh":"穩定人口增長令規劃水、住房和學校更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reducing pressure by controlling population growth.","zh":"這個短語描述透過控制人口增長來減壓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no longer separate","meaning":"不能再把……分開","examples":[{"en":"Governments can no longer separate population policy from water supply.","zh":"政府不能再把人口政策與水源供應分開。"},{"en":"No longer separate means must stop treating two issues as unrelated.","zh":"no longer separate 指必須停止把兩個議題視為無關。"},{"en":"Schools can no longer separate mental health from academic performance.","zh":"學校不能再把心理健康與學業表現分開。"},{"en":"When two problems affect each other, planning them separately becomes unrealistic.","zh":"當兩個問題互相影響，分開規劃就變得不現實。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that connection has become unavoidable.","zh":"這個短語顯示連繫已不可避免。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"population policy","meaning":"人口政策","examples":[{"en":"Population policy must be linked to water supply.","zh":"人口政策必須與水源供應連繫起來。"},{"en":"Population policy is government planning about population size, growth, family support and migration.","zh":"population policy 是政府關於人口規模、增長、家庭支援和移民的規劃。"},{"en":"A country may change population policy by improving family planning and education.","zh":"國家可能透過改善家庭計劃和教育來改變人口政策。"},{"en":"Good population policy considers whether schools, hospitals and water systems can cope.","zh":"好的人口政策會考慮學校、醫院和供水系統能否承受。"},{"en":"The phrase describes policy that affects demographic change.","zh":"這個短語描述影響人口變化的政策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the supply of water","meaning":"水的供應","examples":[{"en":"Governments must consider the supply of water when making population policy.","zh":"政府制定人口政策時，必須考慮水的供應。"},{"en":"The supply of water is the amount of water available for use.","zh":"supply of water 是可供使用的水量。"},{"en":"A school checks the supply of water before holding an outdoor sports day.","zh":"學校舉辦戶外運動日前會檢查水的供應。"},{"en":"If water supply is limited, population and development plans must be realistic.","zh":"如果水供應有限，人口和發展計劃必須現實。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on available water rather than demand.","zh":"這個短語重點在可用水，而不是需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"turn to","meaning":"轉向","examples":[{"en":"The world must now turn to raising water productivity.","zh":"世界現在必須轉向提高水資源生產力。"},{"en":"To turn to something means to begin using it or focusing on it as a solution.","zh":"turn to 某事，指開始使用或專注於它作為解決方法。"},{"en":"A student may turn to past papers when ordinary revision notes are not enough.","zh":"當普通溫習筆記不足，學生可能轉向歷屆試題。"},{"en":"People turn to a new approach when old methods cannot solve the problem.","zh":"當舊方法不能解決問題，人們會轉向新做法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shifting attention toward a solution.","zh":"這個短語描述把注意力轉向解決方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"raising land productivity","meaning":"提高土地生產力","examples":[{"en":"The world turned to raising land productivity half a century ago.","zh":"世界在半個世紀前轉向提高土地生產力。"},{"en":"Raising land productivity means producing more food or value from each area of land.","zh":"raising land productivity 指每片土地生產更多食物或價值。"},{"en":"Farmers raise land productivity by using better seeds, fertiliser and farming methods.","zh":"農民透過使用更好種子、肥料和耕作方法來提高土地生產力。"},{"en":"Higher land productivity can reduce the need to clear more land.","zh":"較高土地生產力可以減少開墾更多土地的需要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making land produce more efficiently.","zh":"這個短語描述令土地更有效率地生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a half century ago","meaning":"半個世紀前","examples":[{"en":"The world faced agricultural limits a half century ago.","zh":"世界在半個世紀前面對農業限制。"},{"en":"A half century ago means fifty years ago.","zh":"a half century ago 指五十年前。"},{"en":"A half century ago, most students did not use computers for homework.","zh":"半個世紀前，大多數學生不會用電腦做功課。"},{"en":"The phrase helps compare past problems with present ones.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較過去問題與現在問題。"},{"en":"It points to a long but understandable historical distance.","zh":"它指出一段長但容易理解的歷史距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the frontiers of agricultural settlement","meaning":"農業開墾邊界","examples":[{"en":"The frontiers of agricultural settlement disappeared.","zh":"農業開墾邊界消失了。"},{"en":"The frontiers of agricultural settlement are the edges of land still available for new farming communities.","zh":"frontiers of agricultural settlement 是仍可供新農業社群開墾的土地邊緣。"},{"en":"When all nearby farmland is already used, a village has reached its agricultural frontier.","zh":"當附近所有農地已被使用，村莊就到達其農業開墾邊界。"},{"en":"Once these frontiers disappear, food growth must come from better productivity, not more land.","zh":"一旦這些邊界消失，糧食增長必須來自更高生產力，而不是更多土地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the limit of expanding farming into new areas.","zh":"這個短語描述向新地區擴展農業的界限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the first step toward","meaning":"朝……邁出的第一步","examples":[{"en":"The first step toward this goal is to eliminate water subsidies.","zh":"朝這個目標邁出的第一步是取消用水補貼。"},{"en":"The first step toward something is the first action needed to begin reaching a goal.","zh":"first step toward 某事，是開始達成目標所需的第一個行動。"},{"en":"The first step toward better writing is understanding what the question asks.","zh":"朝更好寫作邁出的第一步，是理解題目要求甚麼。"},{"en":"A clear first step turns a large goal into something manageable.","zh":"清晰第一步把大目標變成可處理的事情。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the starting action in a plan.","zh":"這個短語引出計劃中的起始行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"eliminate water subsidies","meaning":"取消用水補貼","examples":[{"en":"Governments should eliminate water subsidies that foster inefficiency.","zh":"政府應取消助長低效率的用水補貼。"},{"en":"To eliminate water subsidies means to remove financial support that makes water artificially cheap.","zh":"eliminate water subsidies 指取消令水價被人為壓低的財政支援。"},{"en":"A government may eliminate water subsidies if cheap water encourages wasteful farming.","zh":"如果廉價水鼓勵浪費性農業，政府可能取消用水補貼。"},{"en":"Removing subsidies can push users to save water, but it may hurt poor families if done badly.","zh":"取消補貼可以推動使用者節水，但如果做得差，可能傷害貧困家庭。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ending policy support for low water prices.","zh":"這個短語描述終止低水價政策支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"water subsidies","meaning":"用水補貼","examples":[{"en":"Water subsidies can encourage inefficient water use.","zh":"用水補貼可以鼓勵低效率用水。"},{"en":"Water subsidies are government support that lowers the price users pay for water.","zh":"water subsidies 是政府支援，用來降低使用者支付的水價。"},{"en":"Farmers may use more water than necessary if water subsidies make irrigation very cheap.","zh":"如果用水補貼令灌溉非常便宜，農民可能使用多於必要的水。"},{"en":"Subsidies can help poor users, but they can also encourage waste.","zh":"補貼可以幫助貧困使用者，但也可以鼓勵浪費。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to financial support for water use.","zh":"這個短語指對用水的財政支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"foster inefficiency","meaning":"助長低效率","examples":[{"en":"Water subsidies can foster inefficiency.","zh":"用水補貼可以助長低效率。"},{"en":"To foster inefficiency means to encourage wasteful or poorly organised use of resources.","zh":"foster inefficiency 指鼓勵浪費或組織不善的資源使用。"},{"en":"Free printing can foster inefficiency if students print every draft without checking it.","zh":"如果學生不檢查草稿就每份都打印，免費打印可以助長低效率。"},{"en":"When people do not see the true cost of a resource, they may waste it.","zh":"當人們看不到資源真實成本，就可能浪費它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes policies or habits that make poor use more likely.","zh":"這個短語描述令低效使用更可能出現的政策或習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"raise the price of water","meaning":"提高水價","examples":[{"en":"The second step is to raise the price of water.","zh":"第二步是提高水價。"},{"en":"To raise the price of water means to make users pay more for using water.","zh":"raise the price of water 指令使用者為用水支付更多。"},{"en":"A city may raise the price of water to discourage waste and repair pipes.","zh":"城市可能提高水價，以阻止浪費並維修水管。"},{"en":"Higher prices can reduce use, but protections may be needed for poor households.","zh":"較高價格可以減少使用，但可能需要為貧困家庭提供保障。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using price to change behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述用價格改變行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"reflect its cost","meaning":"反映其成本","examples":[{"en":"The price of water should reflect its cost.","zh":"水價應反映其成本。"},{"en":"To reflect its cost means the price should show the real expense of providing and protecting it.","zh":"reflect its cost 指價格應顯示提供和保護它的真實開支。"},{"en":"A lunch price should reflect its cost, including ingredients, staff and rent.","zh":"午餐價格應反映其成本，包括食材、員工和租金。"},{"en":"If prices do not reflect costs, people may overuse the product.","zh":"如果價格不反映成本，人們可能過度使用產品。"},{"en":"The phrase links price with true resource expense.","zh":"這個短語把價格與資源真實成本連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"shift to","meaning":"轉向","examples":[{"en":"Countries should shift to more water-efficient technologies.","zh":"國家應轉向更節水的技術。"},{"en":"To shift to something means to change from one method or system to another.","zh":"shift to 某事，指從一種方法或系統改為另一種。"},{"en":"A school may shift to online notices to reduce paper waste.","zh":"學校可能轉向網上通告，以減少紙張浪費。"},{"en":"Shifting to efficient technology can save money and resources over time.","zh":"轉向高效技術可以隨時間節省金錢和資源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving toward a new approach.","zh":"這個短語描述走向新方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"water-efficient technologies","meaning":"節水技術","examples":[{"en":"Water-efficient technologies can help raise water productivity.","zh":"節水技術可以幫助提高水資源生產力。"},{"en":"Water-efficient technologies are tools or systems that use less water to achieve the same result.","zh":"water-efficient technologies 是用較少水達成相同效果的工具或系統。"},{"en":"Drip irrigation is a water-efficient technology because it sends water directly to plant roots.","zh":"滴灌是一種節水技術，因為它把水直接送到植物根部。"},{"en":"These technologies can reduce waste in farms, factories and homes.","zh":"這些技術可以減少農場、工廠和家庭的浪費。"},{"en":"The phrase describes technology designed to save water.","zh":"這個短語描述為節約用水而設計的科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"water-efficient crops","meaning":"節水農作物","examples":[{"en":"Water-efficient crops offer potential for saving water.","zh":"節水農作物有節約用水的潛力。"},{"en":"Water-efficient crops are crops that need less water to grow well.","zh":"water-efficient crops 是需要較少水也能良好生長的農作物。"},{"en":"Farmers may choose water-efficient crops in dry regions to reduce irrigation needs.","zh":"在乾旱地區，農民可能選擇節水農作物來減少灌溉需要。"},{"en":"Growing such crops can protect water supplies while still producing food.","zh":"種植這類作物可以在仍生產糧食的同時保護水源供應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes plants that produce useful harvests with lower water demand.","zh":"這個短語描述以較低用水需求產生有用收成的植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 82 - Population growth sentencing millions to hydrological poverty.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 83":[{"front":"the field of sleep research","meaning":"睡眠研究領域","examples":[{"en":"The field of sleep research is still relatively new.","zh":"睡眠研究領域仍然相對較新。"},{"en":"The field of sleep research is the area of science that studies why and how people sleep.","zh":"睡眠研究領域是研究人為何睡覺以及如何睡覺的科學範疇。"},{"en":"A university may open a laboratory in the field of sleep research to study insomnia and dreams.","zh":"大學可能開設睡眠研究實驗室，研究失眠和夢境。"},{"en":"Because the field is young, scientists still disagree about some functions of sleep.","zh":"因為這個領域仍年輕，科學家對睡眠某些功能仍有分歧。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a scientific area, not simply personal opinions about sleeping.","zh":"這個短語指一個科學範疇，而不只是個人對睡覺的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be still relatively new","meaning":"仍然相對較新","examples":[{"en":"Sleep research is still relatively new.","zh":"睡眠研究仍然相對較新。"},{"en":"If something is still relatively new, it has not existed or been studied for a very long time.","zh":"如果某事仍然相對較新，表示它存在或被研究的時間尚不算很長。"},{"en":"Online learning is still relatively new in some schools, so teachers are still improving their methods.","zh":"在某些學校，網上學習仍然相對較新，所以老師仍在改進方法。"},{"en":"When a field is still relatively new, many questions may remain unanswered.","zh":"當一個領域仍然相對較新，許多問題可能仍未解答。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something is developing and not yet fully mature.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事仍在發展，尚未完全成熟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have yet to determine","meaning":"尚未確定","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have yet to determine exactly why people sleep.","zh":"科學家尚未確定人們究竟為何需要睡眠。"},{"en":"To have yet to determine something means still not to have found or decided the answer.","zh":"尚未確定某事，是指仍未找到或決定答案。"},{"en":"Doctors have yet to determine why some patients recover faster than others.","zh":"醫生尚未確定為何有些病人比其他人康復得更快。"},{"en":"If researchers have yet to determine a cause, more evidence and experiments are needed.","zh":"如果研究人員尚未確定原因，就需要更多證據和實驗。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a question remains unresolved.","zh":"這個短語顯示問題仍未解決。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"determine exactly why","meaning":"確切判定原因","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are trying to determine exactly why people need sleep.","zh":"研究人員正嘗試確切判定人們為何需要睡眠。"},{"en":"To determine exactly why means to find the precise reason for something.","zh":"確切判定原因，是指找出某事的精確原因。"},{"en":"A teacher may try to determine exactly why a student keeps making the same grammar mistake.","zh":"老師可能嘗試確切判定為何學生不斷犯同一個文法錯誤。"},{"en":"Knowing exactly why a problem happens helps people choose the right solution.","zh":"確切知道問題原因，有助人們選擇正確解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses precise explanation, not rough guessing.","zh":"這個短語強調精確解釋，而不是粗略猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, people can survive longer without food than without sleep.","zh":"事實上，人們在沒有食物的情況下能比沒有睡眠存活更久。"},{"en":"In fact introduces a true point that supports, explains, or surprises the reader.","zh":"事實上，用來引入支持、解釋或令讀者驚訝的真實重點。"},{"en":"Many people think water is always harmless; in fact, drinking too much too quickly can be dangerous.","zh":"許多人以為水永遠無害；事實上，太快喝太多水也可能危險。"},{"en":"Writers use “in fact” to correct an assumption or add stronger evidence.","zh":"作者使用 in fact 來修正假設或加入更有力證據。"},{"en":"This phrase often signals that the next sentence is important.","zh":"這個短語通常表示下一句很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"survive longer without","meaning":"在沒有……的情況下存活更久","examples":[{"en":"People can survive longer without food than without sleep.","zh":"人們在沒有食物的情況下能比沒有睡眠存活更久。"},{"en":"To survive longer without something means to stay alive for more time while lacking it.","zh":"在沒有某物的情況下存活更久，是指缺少它時仍能維持生命更長時間。"},{"en":"A plant may survive longer without sunlight than without water.","zh":"植物在沒有陽光的情況下，可能比沒有水時存活更久。"},{"en":"Comparing what people can survive without shows which needs are most urgent.","zh":"比較人們缺少甚麼仍能存活多久，可以顯示哪些需要最迫切。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how long life can continue when something essential is missing.","zh":"這個短語描述缺少重要事物時生命能維持多久。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be alone in this need","meaning":"並非唯一有這種需要","examples":[{"en":"People are not alone in this need for sleep.","zh":"人類並非唯一有睡眠這種需要。"},{"en":"To be alone in this need means to be the only one that has this requirement.","zh":"唯一有這種需要，是指只有某一方有這個需求。"},{"en":"Humans are not alone in the need for clean water; animals need it too.","zh":"人類並非唯一需要清潔食水；動物也需要。"},{"en":"If many species share the same need, scientists may think it serves an important function.","zh":"如果許多物種都有同一需要，科學家可能認為它有重要功能。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a need is shared, not unique.","zh":"這個短語顯示某需要是共享的，而不是獨有的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mammals, reptiles and birds","meaning":"哺乳動物、爬蟲類動物和鳥類","examples":[{"en":"All mammals, reptiles and birds sleep.","zh":"所有哺乳動物、爬蟲類動物和鳥類都會睡覺。"},{"en":"Mammals, reptiles and birds are three large groups of animals with different body features.","zh":"哺乳動物、爬蟲類動物和鳥類，是具有不同身體特徵的三大動物類別。"},{"en":"Dogs, lizards and pigeons are examples of mammals, reptiles and birds.","zh":"狗、蜥蜴和鴿子分別是哺乳動物、爬蟲類動物和鳥類的例子。"},{"en":"Since all these animals sleep, sleep appears to be a basic biological need.","zh":"既然這些動物都會睡覺，睡眠看來是一種基本生物需要。"},{"en":"This phrase groups several kinds of animals together.","zh":"這個短語把幾類動物放在一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"propose theories on","meaning":"就……提出理論","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have proposed several theories on why humans require sleep.","zh":"科學家已就人類為何需要睡眠提出幾種理論。"},{"en":"To propose theories on something means to suggest possible explanations for it.","zh":"就某事提出理論，是指為它提出可能解釋。"},{"en":"Economists may propose theories on why prices rise in a city.","zh":"經濟學家可能就城市物價上升提出理論。"},{"en":"When scientists propose different theories, they are trying to explain evidence in a logical way.","zh":"當科學家提出不同理論，他們是在嘗試用合邏輯方式解釋證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes offering possible scientific explanations.","zh":"這個短語描述提出可能的科學解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"require sleep","meaning":"需要睡眠","examples":[{"en":"Humans require sleep for several possible reasons.","zh":"人類需要睡眠可能有幾個原因。"},{"en":"To require sleep means to need sleep in order to function properly.","zh":"需要睡眠，是指為了正常運作而必須睡覺。"},{"en":"Students require sleep to concentrate, remember information and control their mood.","zh":"學生需要睡眠來集中精神、記住資料和控制情緒。"},{"en":"If people do not get the sleep they require, their health and performance can suffer.","zh":"如果人們沒有得到所需睡眠，健康和表現都可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sleep as a real need, not a luxury.","zh":"這個短語把睡眠描述為真正需要，而不是奢侈享受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a way of recharging the brain","meaning":"為大腦重新充電的方法","examples":[{"en":"Sleep may be a way of recharging the brain.","zh":"睡眠可能是為大腦重新充電的方法。"},{"en":"A way of recharging the brain means a method that helps the brain regain energy or function.","zh":"為大腦重新充電的方法，是幫助大腦恢復能量或功能的方法。"},{"en":"A short break can sometimes feel like a way of recharging the brain after long study.","zh":"長時間溫習後，小休有時像是為大腦重新充電的方法。"},{"en":"Sleep may restore the brain so people can think more clearly the next day.","zh":"睡眠可能恢復大腦，使人第二天思考更清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the brain to a battery that needs renewal.","zh":"這個短語把大腦比作需要更新能量的電池。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have a chance to","meaning":"有機會去……","examples":[{"en":"The brain has a chance to shut down during sleep.","zh":"大腦在睡眠期間有機會暫停運作。"},{"en":"To have a chance to do something means to get an opportunity to do it.","zh":"有機會做某事，是指得到做該事的機會。"},{"en":"After exams, students finally have a chance to rest and meet friends.","zh":"考試後，學生終於有機會休息和見朋友。"},{"en":"If the brain has a chance to pause, it may recover from the work of the day.","zh":"如果大腦有機會暫停，它可能從一天的工作中恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an opportunity created by a situation.","zh":"這個短語描述由某情況帶來的機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"shut down","meaning":"暫停運作","examples":[{"en":"The brain has a chance to shut down and repair neurons.","zh":"大腦有機會暫停運作並修復神經元。"},{"en":"To shut down means to stop operating fully or to reduce activity for a time.","zh":"暫停運作，是指停止全面運行或暫時降低活動。"},{"en":"A computer may shut down automatically when its battery is too low.","zh":"電腦在電量太低時可能自動關機。"},{"en":"During sleep, parts of the brain may reduce activity so recovery can take place.","zh":"睡眠期間，大腦某些部分可能降低活動，以便恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a pause or major reduction in activity.","zh":"這個短語描述活動暫停或大幅減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"repair neurons","meaning":"修復神經元","examples":[{"en":"Sleep allows the brain to repair neurons.","zh":"睡眠讓大腦修復神經元。"},{"en":"To repair neurons means to help nerve cells recover from damage or daily wear.","zh":"修復神經元，是指幫助神經細胞從損傷或日常耗損中恢復。"},{"en":"A mechanic repairs a car, but the body repairs cells through biological processes.","zh":"機械師修理汽車，而身體透過生物過程修復細胞。"},{"en":"If neurons are repaired during sleep, the brain may work better when a person wakes up.","zh":"如果神經元在睡眠期間被修復，人醒來時大腦可能運作得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes biological recovery in the nervous system.","zh":"這個短語描述神經系統中的生物恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"neuronal connections","meaning":"神經連接","examples":[{"en":"Sleep may exercise important neuronal connections.","zh":"睡眠可能鍛鍊重要神經連接。"},{"en":"Neuronal connections are links between nerve cells that allow information to pass through the brain.","zh":"神經連接是神經細胞之間的連結，讓資訊在大腦中傳遞。"},{"en":"Learning a new word may strengthen neuronal connections related to language.","zh":"學習新單詞可能強化與語言相關的神經連接。"},{"en":"If important connections are used and maintained, memories and skills may be preserved.","zh":"如果重要連接被使用和維持，記憶和技能可能得以保存。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to communication links inside the brain.","zh":"這個短語指大腦內部的溝通連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"might otherwise deteriorate","meaning":"否則可能會退化","examples":[{"en":"Some neuronal connections might otherwise deteriorate.","zh":"某些神經連接否則可能會退化。"},{"en":"Might otherwise deteriorate means might become worse if the helpful action did not happen.","zh":"否則可能會退化，是指如果沒有某種有幫助的行動，它可能變差。"},{"en":"Without regular practice, a student’s speaking skills might otherwise deteriorate.","zh":"沒有定期練習，學生的口語能力否則可能會退步。"},{"en":"Sleep may protect brain connections that could weaken through lack of use.","zh":"睡眠可能保護那些可能因缺乏使用而變弱的大腦連接。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible decline prevented by another factor.","zh":"這個短語描述另一因素所防止的可能衰退。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"deteriorate due to","meaning":"因……而退化","examples":[{"en":"Neuronal connections may deteriorate due to lack of activity.","zh":"神經連接可能因缺乏活動而退化。"},{"en":"To deteriorate due to something means to become worse because of that cause.","zh":"因某事而退化，是指由於該原因而變差。"},{"en":"A building may deteriorate due to rain, heat and poor maintenance.","zh":"建築物可能因雨水、高溫和缺乏保養而老化。"},{"en":"Skills can deteriorate due to lack of practice over a long period.","zh":"技能可能因長期缺乏練習而退步。"},{"en":"This phrase connects decline with its cause.","zh":"這個短語把衰退與其原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lack of activity","meaning":"缺乏活動","examples":[{"en":"Neuronal connections may deteriorate because of lack of activity.","zh":"神經連接可能因缺乏活動而退化。"},{"en":"Lack of activity means not enough movement, use or stimulation.","zh":"缺乏活動，是指沒有足夠運動、使用或刺激。"},{"en":"A person’s muscles may weaken because of lack of activity after staying in bed for weeks.","zh":"一個人臥床數星期後，肌肉可能因缺乏活動而變弱。"},{"en":"When something is not used, it may become weaker over time.","zh":"當某物不被使用，它可能隨時間變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inactivity as a cause of decline.","zh":"這個短語描述不活動作為衰退原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have an opportunity to","meaning":"有機會去……","examples":[{"en":"Sleep gives the brain an opportunity to reorganise data.","zh":"睡眠給大腦機會去重新整理資料。"},{"en":"To have an opportunity to do something means to get a chance to do it.","zh":"有機會做某事，是指得到做該事的機會。"},{"en":"A student has an opportunity to ask questions when the teacher stays after class.","zh":"老師課後留下時，學生有機會提問。"},{"en":"Sleep may create quiet conditions in which the brain can sort information.","zh":"睡眠可能創造安靜條件，讓大腦整理資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a useful chance created by time or situation.","zh":"這個短語描述由時間或情況創造的有用機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reorganise data","meaning":"重新整理資料","examples":[{"en":"The brain may reorganise data during sleep.","zh":"大腦可能在睡眠期間重新整理資料。"},{"en":"To reorganise data means to sort information into a clearer or more useful order.","zh":"重新整理資料，是指把資訊整理成更清楚或更有用的次序。"},{"en":"A student may reorganise notes by topic before revising for an exam.","zh":"學生可能在考試溫習前按主題重新整理筆記。"},{"en":"If the brain reorganises information, memories may become easier to use later.","zh":"如果大腦重新整理資訊，記憶之後可能更容易使用。"},{"en":"This phrase compares mental work to sorting files.","zh":"這個短語把心智工作比作整理檔案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"find a solution to problems","meaning":"找到問題的解決方法","examples":[{"en":"Sleep may help the brain find a solution to problems.","zh":"睡眠可能幫助大腦找到問題的解決方法。"},{"en":"To find a solution to problems means to discover a way to deal with difficulties.","zh":"找到問題的解決方法，是指發現處理困難的方法。"},{"en":"After resting, a student may find a solution to a maths question that seemed impossible at night.","zh":"休息後，學生可能找到前一晚看似不可能的數學題解法。"},{"en":"Sleep may allow the brain to connect ideas in new ways.","zh":"睡眠可能讓大腦以新方式連接想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes solving difficulties rather than simply thinking about them.","zh":"這個短語描述解決困難，而不只是思考困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"process newly learned information","meaning":"處理新學到的資料","examples":[{"en":"Sleep helps the brain process newly learned information.","zh":"睡眠幫助大腦處理新學到的資料。"},{"en":"To process newly learned information means to understand, organise and absorb information recently received.","zh":"處理新學到的資料，是指理解、整理和吸收最近接收的資訊。"},{"en":"After a language lesson, sleep may help students process new vocabulary.","zh":"語言課後，睡眠可能幫助學生處理新詞彙。"},{"en":"If new information is processed well, it may become easier to remember later.","zh":"如果新資料被良好處理，之後可能更容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the brain working on recent learning.","zh":"這個短語描述大腦處理近期學習內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"organise and archive memories","meaning":"整理並儲存記憶","examples":[{"en":"The brain may organise and archive memories during sleep.","zh":"大腦可能在睡眠期間整理並儲存記憶。"},{"en":"To organise and archive memories means to arrange memories and store them for later use.","zh":"整理並儲存記憶，是指安排記憶並把它們保存起來以供日後使用。"},{"en":"A worker may organise and archive emails so important messages can be found later.","zh":"員工可能整理並儲存電郵，使重要訊息之後能被找到。"},{"en":"Sleep may help the brain decide which memories to keep and how to store them.","zh":"睡眠可能幫助大腦決定哪些記憶要保留，以及如何儲存。"},{"en":"This phrase compares memory to a filing system.","zh":"這個短語把記憶比作檔案系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lower someone’s metabolic rate","meaning":"降低某人的代謝率","examples":[{"en":"Sleep lowers a person’s metabolic rate.","zh":"睡眠會降低一個人的代謝率。"},{"en":"To lower someone’s metabolic rate means to reduce the speed at which the body uses energy.","zh":"降低某人的代謝率，是指降低身體使用能量的速度。"},{"en":"Resting quietly can lower a person’s energy use compared with running.","zh":"與跑步相比，安靜休息可以降低一個人的能量使用。"},{"en":"When metabolic rate falls, the body burns less energy for a time.","zh":"當代謝率下降，身體會暫時燃燒較少能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reduction in the body’s energy-use speed.","zh":"這個短語描述身體能量使用速度下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"energy consumption","meaning":"能量消耗","examples":[{"en":"Sleep lowers a person’s energy consumption.","zh":"睡眠會降低一個人的能量消耗。"},{"en":"Energy consumption means the amount of energy used by a person, machine or system.","zh":"能量消耗，是人、機器或系統所使用的能量數量。"},{"en":"Turning off lights reduces a household’s energy consumption.","zh":"關燈可以降低家庭能量消耗。"},{"en":"During sleep, the body’s energy consumption drops because many activities slow down.","zh":"睡眠期間，因為許多活動減慢，身體能量消耗下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how much energy is used.","zh":"這個短語描述使用了多少能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the cardiovascular system","meaning":"心血管系統","examples":[{"en":"The cardiovascular system gets a break during sleep.","zh":"心血管系統在睡眠期間得到休息。"},{"en":"The cardiovascular system is the heart and blood vessels that move blood around the body.","zh":"心血管系統是把血液運送到全身的心臟和血管。"},{"en":"Exercise trains the cardiovascular system because the heart must pump more blood.","zh":"運動會訓練心血管系統，因為心臟必須泵出更多血液。"},{"en":"During sleep, lower heart rate and blood pressure may reduce stress on this system.","zh":"睡眠期間，較低心率和血壓可能減少這個系統的負擔。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the body system connected with heart and circulation.","zh":"這個短語指與心臟和血液循環相關的身體系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get a break","meaning":"得到休息","examples":[{"en":"The cardiovascular system gets a break during sleep.","zh":"心血管系統在睡眠期間得到休息。"},{"en":"To get a break means to have a period of rest from work or pressure.","zh":"得到休息，是指從工作或壓力中有一段休息時間。"},{"en":"A busy cashier finally gets a break after serving customers all morning.","zh":"忙碌的收銀員服務顧客一整個早上後，終於得到休息。"},{"en":"Sleep gives body systems a break because activity and pressure are reduced.","zh":"睡眠讓身體系統得到休息，因為活動和壓力降低。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a chance to rest.","zh":"這個短語描述休息機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"normal or high blood pressure","meaning":"正常或高血壓","examples":[{"en":"People with normal or high blood pressure may experience a reduction during sleep.","zh":"正常或高血壓的人可能在睡眠期間出現下降。"},{"en":"Normal or high blood pressure means blood pressure that is either within the usual range or above it.","zh":"正常或高血壓，是指血壓處於一般範圍內或高於一般範圍。"},{"en":"A doctor may check whether a patient has normal or high blood pressure during a health examination.","zh":"醫生可能在健康檢查中檢查病人血壓是正常還是偏高。"},{"en":"Blood pressure often falls during sleep, giving the cardiovascular system a rest.","zh":"血壓通常在睡眠期間下降，讓心血管系統得到休息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two possible blood-pressure conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述兩種可能的血壓狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"experience a reduction in","meaning":"出現……下降","examples":[{"en":"People experience a reduction in blood pressure during sleep.","zh":"人們在睡眠期間出現血壓下降。"},{"en":"To experience a reduction in something means to have less of it than before.","zh":"出現某事下降，是指該事比之前減少。"},{"en":"A shop may experience a reduction in customers during heavy rain.","zh":"商店可能在大雨期間出現顧客數量下降。"},{"en":"A reduction in blood pressure can reduce strain on the heart for part of the night.","zh":"血壓下降可以在夜間部分時間減少心臟負擔。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a measurable decrease.","zh":"這個短語描述可量度的減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"blood pressure","meaning":"血壓","examples":[{"en":"Blood pressure falls during sleep.","zh":"血壓在睡眠期間下降。"},{"en":"Blood pressure is the force of blood pushing against the walls of blood vessels.","zh":"血壓是血液推向血管壁的力量。"},{"en":"Nurses often measure blood pressure during a health check.","zh":"護士通常在健康檢查中量度血壓。"},{"en":"High blood pressure can make the heart work harder over time.","zh":"高血壓會隨時間令心臟工作更吃力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an important measure of cardiovascular health.","zh":"這個短語指心血管健康的重要指標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"heart rate","meaning":"心率","examples":[{"en":"Heart rate is reduced during sleep.","zh":"心率在睡眠期間降低。"},{"en":"Heart rate means how many times the heart beats in a minute.","zh":"心率是心臟每分鐘跳動的次數。"},{"en":"A fitness watch can measure a runner’s heart rate during exercise.","zh":"健身手錶可以量度跑步者運動時的心率。"},{"en":"A lower heart rate during sleep shows that the body is resting.","zh":"睡眠期間較低心率顯示身體正在休息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the speed of the heartbeat.","zh":"這個短語描述心跳速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"replace chemicals","meaning":"更替化學物質","examples":[{"en":"The body has a chance to replace chemicals during sleep.","zh":"身體在睡眠期間有機會更替化學物質。"},{"en":"To replace chemicals means to restore or renew substances the body has used up.","zh":"更替化學物質，是指恢復或更新身體已使用的物質。"},{"en":"After heavy exercise, the body needs time to replace chemicals used by muscles.","zh":"劇烈運動後，身體需要時間更替肌肉使用過的化學物質。"},{"en":"Sleep may help the body rebuild supplies needed for healthy functioning.","zh":"睡眠可能幫助身體重建健康運作所需的儲備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes internal renewal of body substances.","zh":"這個短語描述體內物質的更新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"repair muscles","meaning":"修復肌肉","examples":[{"en":"The body repairs muscles during sleep.","zh":"身體在睡眠期間修復肌肉。"},{"en":"To repair muscles means to fix small damage in muscle tissue after use or strain.","zh":"修復肌肉，是指修補肌肉組織在使用或拉傷後的小損傷。"},{"en":"Athletes need sleep because training can create tiny tears in muscles that must be repaired.","zh":"運動員需要睡眠，因為訓練會在肌肉中造成需要修復的微小撕裂。"},{"en":"If muscles are not repaired well, a person may feel weak or sore the next day.","zh":"如果肌肉沒有良好修復，人第二天可能感到無力或痠痛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical recovery during rest.","zh":"這個短語描述休息期間的身體恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"other tissues","meaning":"其他組織","examples":[{"en":"The body repairs muscles and other tissues during sleep.","zh":"身體在睡眠期間修復肌肉和其他組織。"},{"en":"Other tissues means other body materials, such as skin, organs or connective tissue.","zh":"其他組織，是指皮膚、器官或結締組織等其他身體材料。"},{"en":"After a cut, the body repairs skin and other tissues around the wound.","zh":"受傷割傷後，身體會修復傷口周圍的皮膚和其他組織。"},{"en":"Sleep may support healing because the body can focus on repair.","zh":"睡眠可能支持癒合，因為身體可以專注修復。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to body parts beyond the one already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指已提及部分之外的其他身體部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ageing or dead cells","meaning":"老化或死亡細胞","examples":[{"en":"The body repairs ageing or dead cells during sleep.","zh":"身體在睡眠期間修復老化或死亡細胞。"},{"en":"Ageing or dead cells are cells that are becoming old, damaged or no longer alive.","zh":"老化或死亡細胞，是正在變老、受損或不再存活的細胞。"},{"en":"Skin constantly replaces ageing or dead cells as part of normal body maintenance.","zh":"皮膚會不斷更替老化或死亡細胞，這是正常身體維護的一部分。"},{"en":"Removing and replacing old cells helps tissues stay healthy.","zh":"移除和更替舊細胞有助組織保持健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cells that need repair or replacement.","zh":"這個短語描述需要修復或替換的細胞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"growth hormones","meaning":"生長荷爾蒙","examples":[{"en":"Growth hormones are released during deep sleep.","zh":"生長荷爾蒙在深層睡眠期間釋放。"},{"en":"Growth hormones are chemical messengers that help the body grow and repair tissue.","zh":"生長荷爾蒙是幫助身體生長和修復組織的化學訊使。"},{"en":"Children and teenagers need growth hormones as their bones and muscles develop.","zh":"兒童和青少年在骨骼和肌肉發展時需要生長荷爾蒙。"},{"en":"Deep sleep is important because some body-building processes happen then.","zh":"深層睡眠很重要，因為一些身體建構過程在此時發生。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to hormones linked with growth and repair.","zh":"這個短語指與生長和修復有關的荷爾蒙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be released during deep sleep","meaning":"在深層睡眠期間釋放","examples":[{"en":"In children and teenagers, growth hormones are released during deep sleep.","zh":"在兒童和青少年身上，生長荷爾蒙在深層睡眠期間釋放。"},{"en":"To be released during deep sleep means to be produced and sent into the body during the deepest sleep stages.","zh":"在深層睡眠期間釋放，是指在最深睡眠階段中被製造並送入身體。"},{"en":"Certain body chemicals may be released during rest when the body is not busy moving.","zh":"某些身體化學物質可能在休息時釋放，因為身體沒有忙於活動。"},{"en":"If deep sleep is disturbed, some repair and growth processes may be affected.","zh":"如果深層睡眠受干擾，一些修復和生長過程可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a body process with a sleep stage.","zh":"這個短語把身體過程與睡眠階段連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fall asleep","meaning":"入睡","examples":[{"en":"When a person falls asleep is influenced by circadian rhythm.","zh":"一個人何時入睡受晝夜節律影響。"},{"en":"To fall asleep means to move from being awake into sleep.","zh":"入睡，是指由清醒進入睡眠。"},{"en":"A student may fall asleep quickly after a long day of classes and sports.","zh":"學生經過一整天上課和運動後，可能很快入睡。"},{"en":"Light, stress and routine can affect how easily someone falls asleep.","zh":"光線、壓力和日常作息會影響某人是否容易入睡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述睡眠的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"wake up","meaning":"醒來","examples":[{"en":"When a person wakes up is also influenced by circadian rhythm.","zh":"一個人何時醒來也受晝夜節律影響。"},{"en":"To wake up means to stop sleeping and become conscious again.","zh":"醒來，是指停止睡眠並再次有意識。"},{"en":"Some people wake up naturally at the same time every morning.","zh":"有些人每天早上在同一時間自然醒來。"},{"en":"A stable sleep rhythm can make waking up easier and less unpleasant.","zh":"穩定睡眠節律可以令醒來更容易、較不難受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the end of sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述睡眠的結束。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be largely determined by","meaning":"主要由……決定","examples":[{"en":"Sleep timing is largely determined by circadian rhythm.","zh":"睡眠時間主要由晝夜節律決定。"},{"en":"To be largely determined by something means to be mostly decided or controlled by it.","zh":"主要由某事決定，是指大部分由它決定或控制。"},{"en":"A student’s route to school may be largely determined by where the bus stops are.","zh":"學生上學路線可能主要由巴士站位置決定。"},{"en":"If sleep is largely determined by body rhythm, ignoring that rhythm can cause problems.","zh":"如果睡眠主要由身體節律決定，忽視該節律可能造成問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the main controlling factor.","zh":"這個短語顯示主要控制因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"circadian rhythm","meaning":"晝夜節律","examples":[{"en":"A circadian rhythm is a day-night cycle of about 24 hours.","zh":"晝夜節律是一個約二十四小時的日夜週期。"},{"en":"Circadian rhythm is the body’s internal clock that helps control sleep and wakefulness.","zh":"晝夜節律是身體內部時鐘，幫助控制睡眠和清醒。"},{"en":"A person who always sleeps at midnight and wakes at seven has a regular circadian rhythm.","zh":"一個總是在午夜睡覺、七點醒來的人，有規律晝夜節律。"},{"en":"Bright light at night can disturb circadian rhythm and make sleep harder.","zh":"夜間強光可以干擾晝夜節律，使睡眠更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the body’s natural daily timing system.","zh":"這個短語指身體自然的每日時間系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a day-night cycle","meaning":"日夜週期","examples":[{"en":"A circadian rhythm is a day-night cycle of about 24 hours.","zh":"晝夜節律是一個約二十四小時的日夜週期。"},{"en":"A day-night cycle is a repeating pattern linked to daytime and nighttime.","zh":"日夜週期是與白天和夜晚相關的重複模式。"},{"en":"Plants may open flowers during the day and close them at night as part of a day-night cycle.","zh":"植物可能白天開花、夜晚合上，這是日夜週期的一部分。"},{"en":"A regular day-night cycle helps the body know when to sleep and wake.","zh":"規律日夜週期幫助身體知道何時睡覺和醒來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a pattern that repeats every day.","zh":"這個短語描述每天重複的模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"greatly influence","meaning":"大大影響","examples":[{"en":"Circadian rhythms greatly influence the timing and quality of sleep.","zh":"晝夜節律大大影響睡眠時間和睡眠質素。"},{"en":"To greatly influence something means to affect it strongly.","zh":"大大影響某事，是指強烈影響它。"},{"en":"A teacher’s feedback can greatly influence a student’s confidence.","zh":"老師的回饋可以大大影響學生信心。"},{"en":"If body rhythms are disturbed, sleep timing and sleep quality may change a lot.","zh":"如果身體節律受干擾，睡眠時間和睡眠質素可能大幅改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong effect.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the timing, amount and quality of sleep","meaning":"睡眠時間、睡眠量和睡眠質素","examples":[{"en":"Circadian rhythms influence the timing, amount and quality of sleep.","zh":"晝夜節律影響睡眠時間、睡眠量和睡眠質素。"},{"en":"The timing, amount and quality of sleep means when people sleep, how much they sleep and how well they sleep.","zh":"睡眠時間、睡眠量和睡眠質素，是指人何時睡、睡多久和睡得多好。"},{"en":"A student may sleep at the wrong time, get too few hours and still feel tired after poor-quality sleep.","zh":"學生可能睡眠時間不對、睡眠時數太少，而且睡眠質素差，醒來仍疲倦。"},{"en":"Good routines can improve not just bedtime, but also sleep length and sleep depth.","zh":"良好作息不只改善就寢時間，也改善睡眠長度和深度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes three key aspects of sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述睡眠的三個關鍵方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"small mammals","meaning":"小型哺乳動物","examples":[{"en":"Sleep has particular benefits for many small mammals.","zh":"睡眠對許多小型哺乳動物有特別好處。"},{"en":"Small mammals are small warm-blooded animals that feed their young with milk.","zh":"小型哺乳動物是體型細小、以乳汁餵養幼崽的恆溫動物。"},{"en":"Mice, hamsters and squirrels are examples of small mammals.","zh":"老鼠、倉鼠和松鼠都是小型哺乳動物的例子。"},{"en":"Because small mammals lose heat easily, rest and shelter can help them save energy.","zh":"因為小型哺乳動物容易散熱，休息和藏身處可以幫助牠們節省能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a group of small animals, not human beings.","zh":"這個短語描述一類小動物，而不是人類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"particular benefits","meaning":"特別好處","examples":[{"en":"Sleep has particular benefits for rodents.","zh":"睡眠對齧齒類動物有特別好處。"},{"en":"Particular benefits are special advantages for a specific group or situation.","zh":"特別好處，是對特定群體或情況尤其有用的優勢。"},{"en":"Online lessons have particular benefits for students who live far from school.","zh":"網上課堂對住得離學校很遠的學生有特別好處。"},{"en":"Sleep benefits small animals by giving rest and helping them conserve heat.","zh":"睡眠透過提供休息和幫助保溫，令小動物受益。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights advantages that are especially relevant to one group.","zh":"這個短語突出對某一群體特別相關的優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"rodents","meaning":"齧齒類動物","examples":[{"en":"Rodents gain physical rest during sleep.","zh":"齧齒類動物在睡眠期間得到身體休息。"},{"en":"Rodents are small mammals such as rats, mice and squirrels, usually with front teeth that keep growing.","zh":"齧齒類動物是老鼠、家鼠和松鼠等小型哺乳動物，通常有不斷生長的門牙。"},{"en":"A science class may study rodents to understand animal behaviour.","zh":"科學課可能研究齧齒類動物，以理解動物行為。"},{"en":"Many rodents sleep in nests, which can help protect them and conserve warmth.","zh":"許多齧齒類動物睡在巢中，這可以幫助保護牠們並保存熱量。"},{"en":"This word refers to a group of small mammals.","zh":"這個詞指一類小型哺乳動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"provide the only real opportunity for","meaning":"提供唯一真正……的機會","examples":[{"en":"Sleep provides the only real opportunity for physical rest.","zh":"睡眠提供唯一真正身體休息的機會。"},{"en":"To provide the only real opportunity for something means to be the only genuine chance for it to happen.","zh":"提供唯一真正某事的機會，是指成為該事真正發生的唯一機會。"},{"en":"Lunch break may provide the only real opportunity for a busy nurse to sit down.","zh":"午膳時間可能提供忙碌護士唯一真正坐下來的機會。"},{"en":"For some small animals, sleep may be the only time when the body fully rests.","zh":"對某些小動物而言，睡眠可能是身體完全休息的唯一時間。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that there are no other practical chances.","zh":"這個短語強調沒有其他實際機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"physical rest","meaning":"身體休息","examples":[{"en":"Sleep provides physical rest for many small mammals.","zh":"睡眠為許多小型哺乳動物提供身體休息。"},{"en":"Physical rest means rest for the body, especially muscles, organs and energy systems.","zh":"身體休息是身體的休息，尤其是肌肉、器官和能量系統。"},{"en":"After a long hike, a person needs physical rest before walking again.","zh":"長途遠足後，人需要身體休息才再走路。"},{"en":"Physical rest helps the body recover from movement and effort.","zh":"身體休息幫助身體從活動和用力中恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bodily recovery, not mental relaxation only.","zh":"這個短語描述身體恢復，而不只是心理放鬆。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"confine the animal to","meaning":"把動物限制在……","examples":[{"en":"Sleep confines the animal to the thermal insulation of a nest.","zh":"睡眠把動物限制在巢穴的保溫隔熱環境中。"},{"en":"To confine the animal to a place means to keep it within that place or limit its movement there.","zh":"把動物限制在某處，是指讓牠停留在該地方，或限制牠在那裡活動。"},{"en":"A pet owner may confine a sick rabbit to a warm cage so it can recover safely.","zh":"寵物主人可能把生病兔子限制在溫暖籠子中，讓牠安全康復。"},{"en":"Staying in a nest during sleep can reduce heat loss and protect the animal.","zh":"睡眠期間留在巢中可以減少熱量流失並保護動物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping an animal within a limited safe area.","zh":"這個短語描述把動物留在有限而安全的區域內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"thermal insulation","meaning":"保溫隔熱","examples":[{"en":"A nest provides thermal insulation for a sleeping animal.","zh":"巢穴為睡眠中的動物提供保溫隔熱。"},{"en":"Thermal insulation is material or protection that keeps heat in and cold out.","zh":"保溫隔熱，是把熱量留住並阻擋寒冷的材料或保護。"},{"en":"A thick winter coat provides thermal insulation for people in cold weather.","zh":"厚冬衣在寒冷天氣中為人提供保溫隔熱。"},{"en":"Thermal insulation helps small animals save energy by staying warm while they sleep.","zh":"保溫隔熱幫助小動物在睡眠時保持溫暖，從而節省能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protection against heat loss.","zh":"這個短語描述防止熱量流失的保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in these respects","meaning":"在這些方面","examples":[{"en":"In these respects, sleep conserves much energy in small mammals.","zh":"在這些方面，睡眠為小型哺乳動物節省大量能量。"},{"en":"In these respects means in the ways just mentioned.","zh":"在這些方面，是指在剛才提到的那些方式上。"},{"en":"A library is useful because it is quiet and free; in these respects, it helps students study.","zh":"圖書館有用，因為它安靜且免費；在這些方面，它幫助學生學習。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a conclusion to earlier points.","zh":"這個短語把結論與早前重點連接起來。"},{"en":"It is used to refer back to specific aspects already discussed.","zh":"它用來回指已討論的具體方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"conserve much energy","meaning":"節省大量能量","examples":[{"en":"Sleep conserves much energy in small mammals.","zh":"睡眠為小型哺乳動物節省大量能量。"},{"en":"To conserve much energy means to save a large amount of energy instead of using it.","zh":"節省大量能量，是指保存大量能量而不是使用它。"},{"en":"Turning off air conditioning when no one is home can conserve energy.","zh":"家中無人時關掉冷氣可以節省能量。"},{"en":"Small mammals conserve energy by sleeping in warm nests and reducing activity.","zh":"小型哺乳動物透過睡在溫暖巢穴和減少活動來節省能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes avoiding unnecessary energy loss.","zh":"這個短語描述避免不必要能量流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"develop into a torpor","meaning":"發展成低代謝休眠狀態","examples":[{"en":"Sleep can develop into a torpor in some small mammals.","zh":"某些小型哺乳動物的睡眠可以發展成低代謝休眠狀態。"},{"en":"To develop into a torpor means to change into a state of greatly reduced body activity.","zh":"發展成低代謝休眠狀態，是指變成身體活動大幅降低的狀態。"},{"en":"Some small animals enter a low-energy state when food is scarce or temperatures are low.","zh":"某些小動物在食物稀少或氣溫低時，會進入低能量狀態。"},{"en":"This change helps animals survive when staying active would use too much energy.","zh":"這種變化幫助動物在保持活躍會消耗太多能量時生存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sleep becoming a deeper energy-saving state.","zh":"這個短語描述睡眠變成更深層的節能狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"torpor","meaning":"低代謝休眠狀態","examples":[{"en":"Torpor is a state in which the metabolic rate drops significantly.","zh":"低代謝休眠狀態是代謝率大幅下降的狀態。"},{"en":"Torpor is a low-activity state in which an animal uses much less energy.","zh":"低代謝休眠狀態是一種低活動狀態，動物在其中使用少得多的能量。"},{"en":"A small mammal may enter torpor during cold weather when food is difficult to find.","zh":"小型哺乳動物可能在寒冷天氣、食物難尋時進入低代謝休眠狀態。"},{"en":"Torpor helps animals survive by slowing body processes for a short period.","zh":"低代謝休眠狀態透過短時間減慢身體過程，幫助動物生存。"},{"en":"This word describes a temporary energy-saving state, not ordinary sleep only.","zh":"這個詞描述暫時節能狀態，而不只是普通睡眠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the metabolic rate drops significantly","meaning":"代謝率大幅下降","examples":[{"en":"In torpor, the metabolic rate drops significantly.","zh":"在低代謝休眠狀態中，代謝率大幅下降。"},{"en":"When the metabolic rate drops significantly, the body uses much less energy than usual.","zh":"當代謝率大幅下降，身體使用的能量比平常少很多。"},{"en":"During deep rest, some animals’ bodies slow down to save fuel.","zh":"在深度休息期間，某些動物的身體會減慢以保存能量。"},{"en":"A large drop in metabolic rate can help an animal survive cold or hunger.","zh":"代謝率大幅下降可以幫助動物在寒冷或飢餓中生存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major reduction in body energy use.","zh":"這個短語描述身體能量使用大幅減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"during the sleep period","meaning":"在睡眠期間","examples":[{"en":"The metabolic rate may drop for a few hours during the sleep period.","zh":"代謝率可能在睡眠期間下降數小時。"},{"en":"During the sleep period means while the animal or person is asleep.","zh":"在睡眠期間，是指在人或動物睡着的時候。"},{"en":"A child’s body may release certain hormones during the sleep period.","zh":"兒童身體可能在睡眠期間釋放某些荷爾蒙。"},{"en":"What happens during sleep can affect energy, growth and memory after waking.","zh":"睡眠期間發生的事情會影響醒來後的能量、生長和記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes events that occur while sleeping.","zh":"這個短語描述睡眠時發生的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"On the other hand, humans can rest adequately while awake.","zh":"另一方面，人類在清醒時也能充分休息。"},{"en":"On the other hand introduces a contrasting point.","zh":"另一方面，用來引入對比的觀點。"},{"en":"Online lessons are convenient; on the other hand, students may miss face-to-face discussion.","zh":"網上課堂很方便；另一方面，學生可能會錯過面對面討論。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare two different sides of an issue.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較一個議題的兩面。"},{"en":"It signals that the next idea balances or contrasts with the previous one.","zh":"它表示下一個想法會平衡或對比前一個想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rest and relax adequately","meaning":"充分休息和放鬆","examples":[{"en":"Humans can usually rest and relax adequately during wakefulness.","zh":"人類通常可以在清醒狀態期間充分休息和放鬆。"},{"en":"To rest and relax adequately means to get enough physical and mental relaxation.","zh":"充分休息和放鬆，是指得到足夠身體和心理放鬆。"},{"en":"A worker may rest and relax adequately by sitting quietly during lunch.","zh":"員工可能透過午飯時安靜坐着來充分休息和放鬆。"},{"en":"Because humans can rest while awake, sleep may save less energy for them than for small mammals.","zh":"因為人類在清醒時也能休息，睡眠對人類節省的能量可能少於小型哺乳動物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes getting sufficient rest without necessarily sleeping.","zh":"這個短語描述未必睡覺也能得到足夠休息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"during wakefulness","meaning":"在清醒狀態期間","examples":[{"en":"Humans can rest and relax during wakefulness.","zh":"人類可以在清醒狀態期間休息和放鬆。"},{"en":"During wakefulness means while a person is awake and conscious.","zh":"在清醒狀態期間，是指人醒着並有意識的時候。"},{"en":"A student may daydream during wakefulness even though they are not asleep.","zh":"學生可能在清醒狀態期間發白日夢，即使他沒有睡着。"},{"en":"Rest during wakefulness can reduce tiredness but is not the same as sleep.","zh":"清醒期間的休息可以減少疲倦，但不等同於睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the state of being awake.","zh":"這個短語描述醒着的狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"modest further energy saving","meaning":"額外節省的能量有限","examples":[{"en":"Sleeping gives humans only a modest further energy saving.","zh":"睡眠只給人類帶來有限的額外能量節省。"},{"en":"Modest further energy saving means only a small additional reduction in energy use.","zh":"額外節省的能量有限，是指能量使用只再小幅減少。"},{"en":"Turning a fan from high to medium may give only a modest energy saving.","zh":"把風扇由高速調到中速，可能只節省有限能量。"},{"en":"Humans do not save as much energy by sleeping as animals that enter torpor.","zh":"人類透過睡眠節省的能量不如進入低代謝休眠狀態的動物多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a limited extra benefit.","zh":"這個短語描述有限的額外好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"to be gained by","meaning":"可透過……獲得","examples":[{"en":"Only a modest energy saving is to be gained by sleeping.","zh":"透過睡眠只能獲得有限能量節省。"},{"en":"To be gained by something means can be obtained as a result of doing it.","zh":"可透過某事獲得，是指做該事後可以取得某結果。"},{"en":"Confidence is to be gained by practising speaking regularly.","zh":"信心可以透過定期練習說話獲得。"},{"en":"If only a small benefit is gained, the activity must have other important purposes.","zh":"如果只能獲得小好處，該活動一定還有其他重要目的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what can be obtained from an action.","zh":"這個短語描述可從某行動中取得的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"enter torpor","meaning":"進入低代謝休眠狀態","examples":[{"en":"Humans do not enter torpor.","zh":"人類不會進入低代謝休眠狀態。"},{"en":"To enter torpor means to go into a low-energy state where body activity slows greatly.","zh":"進入低代謝休眠狀態，是指進入身體活動大幅減慢的低能量狀態。"},{"en":"Some small animals enter torpor during cold nights to save energy.","zh":"某些小動物在寒冷夜晚進入低代謝休眠狀態以節省能量。"},{"en":"Humans sleep, but their bodies do not usually slow down as dramatically as in torpor.","zh":"人類會睡覺，但身體通常不會像低代謝休眠那樣大幅減慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving into a special low-metabolism state.","zh":"這個短語描述進入特殊低代謝狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lying at rest while awake","meaning":"清醒時躺着休息","examples":[{"en":"A sleeping adult uses only slightly less energy than someone lying at rest while awake.","zh":"睡眠中的成人只比清醒時躺着休息的人使用稍少能量。"},{"en":"Lying at rest while awake means resting on a bed or sofa without sleeping.","zh":"清醒時躺着休息，是指沒有睡着地躺在床或梳化上休息。"},{"en":"A tired student may lie at rest while awake after school before starting homework.","zh":"疲倦學生放學後可能清醒地躺着休息，然後才開始做功課。"},{"en":"If sleeping saves only slightly more energy than awake rest, sleep must serve other functions too.","zh":"如果睡眠只比清醒休息多節省一點能量，睡眠一定還有其他功能。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts quiet waking rest with actual sleep.","zh":"這個短語對比安靜清醒休息和真正睡眠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a sizeable portion of","meaning":"相當大一部分","examples":[{"en":"A sizeable portion of the workforce consists of shift workers.","zh":"相當大一部分勞動人口由輪班工作者組成。"},{"en":"A sizeable portion of something means a fairly large part of it.","zh":"相當大一部分，是指某整體中頗大的一部分。"},{"en":"A sizeable portion of a class may choose science subjects in senior secondary school.","zh":"一班中相當大一部分學生可能在高中選讀理科。"},{"en":"If a sizeable portion of workers do shifts, sleep disruption becomes a public health issue.","zh":"如果相當大一部分工人輪班工作，睡眠受干擾就成為公共健康問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large but not necessarily majority part.","zh":"這個短語描述很大但不一定過半的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the workforce","meaning":"勞動人口","examples":[{"en":"A sizeable portion of the workforce works in shifts.","zh":"相當大一部分勞動人口從事輪班工作。"},{"en":"The workforce is all the people who are working or available for work in an economy or organisation.","zh":"勞動人口是經濟體或機構中正在工作或可工作的所有人。"},{"en":"The healthcare workforce includes doctors, nurses, cleaners and technicians.","zh":"醫護勞動人口包括醫生、護士、清潔工和技術人員。"},{"en":"Changes in the workforce can affect services, business costs and family routines.","zh":"勞動人口的變化會影響服務、企業成本和家庭作息。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to workers as a group.","zh":"這個短語指作為整體的工人群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"consist of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"The workforce consists partly of shift workers.","zh":"勞動人口部分由輪班工作者組成。"},{"en":"To consist of something means to be made up of those parts.","zh":"由某物組成，是指由那些部分構成。"},{"en":"A healthy meal may consist of rice, vegetables and protein.","zh":"健康一餐可以由米飯、蔬菜和蛋白質組成。"},{"en":"If a group consists of different types of workers, their needs may differ.","zh":"如果一個群體由不同類型工人組成，他們的需要可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what something is composed of.","zh":"這個短語描述某物由甚麼構成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"shift workers","meaning":"輪班工作者","examples":[{"en":"Shift workers work against their bodies’ natural sleep-wake cycle.","zh":"輪班工作者違背身體自然睡眠覺醒週期工作。"},{"en":"Shift workers are people who work at changing times, often at night or very early morning.","zh":"輪班工作者是在不同時間工作的人，通常包括夜班或清晨班。"},{"en":"Nurses, security guards and factory workers may be shift workers.","zh":"護士、保安員和工廠工人都可能是輪班工作者。"},{"en":"Shift work can disturb sleep because the body expects darkness for sleep and light for waking.","zh":"輪班工作會干擾睡眠，因為身體預期黑暗時睡覺、光亮時醒來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes workers whose schedules do not follow a normal daytime pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述工作時間不跟正常日間模式的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"work and sleep against","meaning":"違背……來工作和睡覺","examples":[{"en":"Shift workers work and sleep against their natural cycle.","zh":"輪班工作者違背自然週期來工作和睡覺。"},{"en":"To work and sleep against a cycle means to follow a schedule that conflicts with the body’s usual rhythm.","zh":"違背某週期來工作和睡覺，是指遵循與身體通常節律衝突的時間表。"},{"en":"A night-shift worker may sleep during daylight and work when the body expects rest.","zh":"夜班工作者可能在白天睡覺，在身體預期休息時工作。"},{"en":"Going against the natural cycle can lead to poor sleep and tiredness.","zh":"違背自然週期可能導致睡眠差和疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes conflict between schedule and body rhythm.","zh":"這個短語描述時間表與身體節律之間的衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"natural sleep-wake cycle","meaning":"自然睡眠覺醒週期","examples":[{"en":"Shift workers often disturb their natural sleep-wake cycle.","zh":"輪班工作者常常干擾自己的自然睡眠覺醒週期。"},{"en":"A natural sleep-wake cycle is the body’s normal pattern of feeling sleepy and awake across the day.","zh":"自然睡眠覺醒週期，是身體一天中感到想睡和清醒的正常模式。"},{"en":"A child with a regular bedtime usually has a more stable sleep-wake cycle.","zh":"有規律睡覺時間的孩子通常有較穩定的睡眠覺醒週期。"},{"en":"Working at night can disturb this cycle and make daytime sleep difficult.","zh":"夜間工作可以干擾這個週期，令日間睡眠變困難。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the body’s ordinary daily sleep rhythm.","zh":"這個短語指身體普通每日睡眠節律。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cannot be ignored or reprogrammed","meaning":"不能被忽視或重新設定","examples":[{"en":"A person’s circadian rhythm cannot be ignored or reprogrammed.","zh":"一個人的晝夜節律不能被忽視或重新設定。"},{"en":"Cannot be ignored or reprogrammed means cannot simply be dismissed or reset like a machine.","zh":"不能被忽視或重新設定，是指不能像機器一樣簡單地不理會或重置。"},{"en":"A student cannot ignore hunger all day and expect to study well.","zh":"學生不能整天忽視飢餓，卻期望自己學得好。"},{"en":"Body rhythms can adjust a little, but they cannot be changed instantly by willpower.","zh":"身體節律可以稍作調整，但不能單靠意志力立即改變。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that natural biology has limits.","zh":"這個短語提醒人自然生理有其限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be altered by","meaning":"被……改變","examples":[{"en":"The sleep-wake cycle can be altered by the timing of naps and exercise.","zh":"睡眠覺醒週期可以被小睡和運動的時間安排改變。"},{"en":"To be altered by something means to be changed because of it.","zh":"被某事改變，是指因它而產生變化。"},{"en":"A student’s mood can be altered by lack of sleep or good news.","zh":"學生的心情可以被睡眠不足或好消息改變。"},{"en":"Light exposure, travel and naps can alter when a person feels sleepy.","zh":"接觸光線、旅行和小睡都可以改變一個人何時感到想睡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes change caused by a factor.","zh":"這個短語描述由某因素造成的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the timing of","meaning":"……的時間安排","examples":[{"en":"The timing of bedtime can alter the sleep-wake cycle.","zh":"就寢時間安排可以改變睡眠覺醒週期。"},{"en":"The timing of something means when it happens.","zh":"某事的時間安排，是指它何時發生。"},{"en":"The timing of lunch matters if students have sports practice in the afternoon.","zh":"如果學生下午有運動訓練，午餐的時間安排就很重要。"},{"en":"Poor timing of naps can make it harder to fall asleep at night.","zh":"小睡時間安排不當會令人晚上更難入睡。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the time at which an action occurs.","zh":"這個短語聚焦行動發生的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"naps","meaning":"小睡","examples":[{"en":"Naps can affect a person’s sleep-wake cycle.","zh":"小睡可以影響一個人的睡眠覺醒週期。"},{"en":"Naps are short periods of sleep, usually during the day.","zh":"小睡是短時間睡眠，通常在日間發生。"},{"en":"A student may take a nap after school if they feel very tired.","zh":"如果學生很疲倦，放學後可能小睡一會兒。"},{"en":"A short nap can refresh someone, but a late nap may disturb nighttime sleep.","zh":"短小睡可以令人恢復精神，但太晚小睡可能干擾夜間睡眠。"},{"en":"This word refers to brief daytime sleep.","zh":"這個詞指短暫日間睡眠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"time zone","meaning":"時區","examples":[{"en":"Travel to a different time zone can alter the sleep cycle.","zh":"前往不同時區可以改變睡眠週期。"},{"en":"A time zone is a region where people use the same standard time.","zh":"時區是人們使用相同標準時間的地區。"},{"en":"Flying from Hong Kong to London moves a traveller into a different time zone.","zh":"從香港飛往倫敦會令旅客進入不同時區。"},{"en":"Time-zone changes can cause jet lag because the body clock does not adjust immediately.","zh":"時區變化會造成時差，因為生理時鐘不會立即調整。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a geographical time setting.","zh":"這個短語描述地理上的時間設定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"exposure to light","meaning":"接觸光線","examples":[{"en":"Exposure to light can alter a person’s sleep-wake cycle.","zh":"接觸光線可以改變一個人的睡眠覺醒週期。"},{"en":"Exposure to light means being in contact with light or having light reach the eyes or body.","zh":"接觸光線，是指身處光線中，或光線到達眼睛或身體。"},{"en":"Looking at a bright phone screen at night increases exposure to light.","zh":"晚上看明亮手機螢幕會增加接觸光線。"},{"en":"Light tells the body it may be daytime, so night-time exposure can delay sleep.","zh":"光線告訴身體可能是白天，所以夜間接觸光線會延遲睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes contact with light as a biological signal.","zh":"這個短語描述光線接觸作為生物訊號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stable and consistent","meaning":"穩定而一致","examples":[{"en":"The more stable and consistent the cycle is, the better the person sleeps.","zh":"週期越穩定而一致，人就睡得越好。"},{"en":"Stable and consistent means steady, regular and not changing much.","zh":"穩定而一致，是指穩定、有規律且不常改變。"},{"en":"A stable and consistent study timetable helps students build habits.","zh":"穩定而一致的溫習時間表幫助學生建立習慣。"},{"en":"Regular sleep and wake times can make the body clock more reliable.","zh":"規律的睡覺和起床時間可以令生理時鐘更可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a pattern that stays steady over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間保持穩定的模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"disruption of circadian rhythms","meaning":"晝夜節律受干擾","examples":[{"en":"Disruption of circadian rhythms can affect mental health.","zh":"晝夜節律受干擾可以影響心理健康。"},{"en":"Disruption of circadian rhythms means disturbance of the body’s normal daily timing system.","zh":"晝夜節律受干擾，是指身體正常每日時間系統受到破壞。"},{"en":"Working night shifts for many weeks can cause disruption of circadian rhythms.","zh":"連續多星期上夜班可能造成晝夜節律受干擾。"},{"en":"When body rhythms are disrupted, mood, sleep and concentration may suffer.","zh":"當身體節律受干擾，情緒、睡眠和專注力都可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damage to the body’s natural time pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述身體自然時間模式受破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cause mania","meaning":"導致躁狂","examples":[{"en":"Disruption of circadian rhythms can cause mania in some people.","zh":"晝夜節律受干擾可在某些人身上導致躁狂。"},{"en":"To cause mania means to trigger a period of abnormally high energy, mood or activity.","zh":"導致躁狂，是指觸發一段異常高能量、情緒或活動水平的時期。"},{"en":"Severe sleep loss can sometimes worsen mood problems in vulnerable people.","zh":"嚴重睡眠不足有時會加重易受影響人士的情緒問題。"},{"en":"If disrupted rhythms contribute to mania, keeping regular sleep may be especially important.","zh":"如果節律受干擾會促成躁狂，保持規律睡眠便尤其重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible mental-health effect.","zh":"這個短語描述一種可能的心理健康影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bipolar disorder","meaning":"躁鬱症","examples":[{"en":"People with bipolar disorder may be affected by disrupted circadian rhythms.","zh":"躁鬱症患者可能受晝夜節律干擾影響。"},{"en":"Bipolar disorder is a mental health condition involving strong mood changes, including depression and mania.","zh":"躁鬱症是一種心理健康狀況，涉及強烈情緒變化，包括抑鬱和躁狂。"},{"en":"A person with bipolar disorder may need medical treatment and regular daily routines.","zh":"躁鬱症患者可能需要醫療治療和規律日常作息。"},{"en":"Sleep disruption can be important because mood and body rhythm may be connected.","zh":"睡眠受干擾很重要，因為情緒和身體節律可能有關。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific mental health condition.","zh":"這個短語指特定心理健康狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the seven deadly sins","meaning":"七宗罪","examples":[{"en":"The seven deadly sins included sloth.","zh":"七宗罪包括怠惰。"},{"en":"The seven deadly sins are traditional Christian categories of serious moral faults.","zh":"七宗罪是基督教傳統中嚴重道德過失的分類。"},{"en":"In a history lesson, students may learn that pride and greed are among the seven deadly sins.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生可能學到驕傲和貪婪屬於七宗罪。"},{"en":"Mentioning the seven deadly sins shows how sleep and laziness have sometimes been confused morally.","zh":"提及七宗罪顯示睡眠和懶惰有時在道德上被混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a religious and moral classification.","zh":"這個短語指宗教和道德分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be formulated by","meaning":"由……制定","examples":[{"en":"The seven deadly sins were formulated by medieval monks.","zh":"七宗罪由中世紀修士制定。"},{"en":"To be formulated by someone means to be created, organised or expressed by them.","zh":"由某人制定，是指由他們創造、組織或表述。"},{"en":"School rules may be formulated by teachers and administrators.","zh":"校規可能由老師和行政人員制定。"},{"en":"When an idea is formulated by a group, that group shapes how the idea is understood.","zh":"當一個想法由某群體制定，該群體會塑造人們如何理解它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes who created or organised a concept.","zh":"這個短語描述誰創造或組織某概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"medieval monks","meaning":"中世紀修士","examples":[{"en":"Medieval monks included sloth among the seven deadly sins.","zh":"中世紀修士把怠惰列入七宗罪之中。"},{"en":"Medieval monks were religious men who lived in monasteries during the Middle Ages.","zh":"中世紀修士是在中世紀住在修道院中的宗教男性。"},{"en":"Medieval monks often copied books, prayed and followed strict routines.","zh":"中世紀修士常抄寫書籍、祈禱並遵守嚴格作息。"},{"en":"Their moral teachings influenced how later societies thought about work and laziness.","zh":"他們的道德教導影響後來社會如何看待工作和懶惰。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to religious figures from the medieval period.","zh":"這個短語指中世紀的宗教人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sloth","meaning":"怠惰；懶惰","examples":[{"en":"Sloth was included among the seven deadly sins.","zh":"怠惰被列入七宗罪之中。"},{"en":"Sloth means laziness or unwillingness to work when work is needed.","zh":"怠惰是需要工作時仍懶惰或不願工作。"},{"en":"A student who refuses to do any revision out of laziness may be showing sloth.","zh":"學生如果出於懶惰完全拒絕溫習，可能是在表現怠惰。"},{"en":"The passage separates sloth from the healthy need for sleep.","zh":"篇章把怠惰與健康睡眠需要區分開。"},{"en":"This word describes moral laziness, not ordinary tiredness.","zh":"這個詞描述道德上的懶惰，而不是普通疲倦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a more nuanced understanding of","meaning":"對……更細緻的理解","examples":[{"en":"A more nuanced understanding of sloth sees it as unwillingness to work.","zh":"對怠惰更細緻的理解，把它看作不願工作。"},{"en":"A more nuanced understanding of something is a more careful view that includes important distinctions.","zh":"對某事更細緻的理解，是包含重要區分的更仔細看法。"},{"en":"A more nuanced understanding of poor grades may consider stress, teaching and family problems.","zh":"對成績差更細緻的理解，可能考慮壓力、教學和家庭問題。"},{"en":"Nuance helps people avoid simple but unfair judgements.","zh":"細緻理解幫助人避免簡單但不公平的判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a more detailed and balanced interpretation.","zh":"這個短語描述更詳細和平衡的解讀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"disinclination to labour or work","meaning":"不願勞動或工作","examples":[{"en":"Sloth can be understood as a disinclination to labour or work.","zh":"怠惰可以理解為不願勞動或工作。"},{"en":"Disinclination to labour or work means unwillingness to make effort or do necessary work.","zh":"不願勞動或工作，是指不願付出努力或做必要工作。"},{"en":"A worker who avoids every task without reason may show disinclination to work.","zh":"無故避開所有任務的員工，可能表現出不願工作。"},{"en":"This attitude can reduce productivity and place more burden on others.","zh":"這種態度會降低生產力，並把更多負擔加在他人身上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unwillingness, not inability.","zh":"這個短語描述不願意，而不是沒有能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the desire for healthy sleep","meaning":"對健康睡眠的需要","examples":[{"en":"Sloth is not the same as the desire for healthy sleep.","zh":"怠惰不等同於對健康睡眠的需要。"},{"en":"The desire for healthy sleep means a natural and reasonable need to rest properly.","zh":"對健康睡眠的需要，是自然且合理地想要充分休息。"},{"en":"A student who wants eight hours of sleep before an exam is showing a desire for healthy sleep.","zh":"學生考試前想睡八小時，是表現出對健康睡眠的需要。"},{"en":"Wanting enough sleep can improve work, study and emotional control.","zh":"想要充足睡眠可以改善工作、學習和情緒控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a legitimate health need, not laziness.","zh":"這個短語描述正當健康需要，而不是懶惰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be the same as","meaning":"與……相同","examples":[{"en":"Sloth is not the same as healthy sleep.","zh":"怠惰不等同於健康睡眠。"},{"en":"To be the same as something means to be equal to it in meaning or nature.","zh":"與某事相同，是指在意思或本質上等同於它。"},{"en":"Being quiet is not the same as being rude.","zh":"安靜不等同於無禮。"},{"en":"The phrase helps separate two ideas that people may confuse.","zh":"這個短語幫助區分人們可能混淆的兩個概念。"},{"en":"It is useful when making a clear distinction.","zh":"它適合用於作清楚區分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on the contrary","meaning":"相反","examples":[{"en":"On the contrary, people need rest in order to work well.","zh":"相反，人們需要休息才能工作得好。"},{"en":"On the contrary introduces the opposite of what someone might expect or claim.","zh":"相反，用來引入與某人可能預期或聲稱相反的內容。"},{"en":"Some think breaks waste time; on the contrary, short breaks can improve focus.","zh":"有些人認為小休浪費時間；相反，短休可以改善專注。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly corrects a wrong idea.","zh":"這個短語強烈修正錯誤想法。"},{"en":"It is useful when the next point reverses the previous assumption.","zh":"當下一點推翻之前假設時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rest periods","meaning":"休息時段","examples":[{"en":"A person cannot work properly without rest periods.","zh":"一個人沒有休息時段就不能正常工作。"},{"en":"Rest periods are planned or natural times when a person stops working and recovers.","zh":"休息時段是人停止工作並恢復的計劃性或自然時間。"},{"en":"Office workers may need short rest periods to avoid eye strain from screens.","zh":"辦公室員工可能需要短休息時段，以避免螢幕造成眼睛疲勞。"},{"en":"Without rest periods, mistakes and tiredness can increase.","zh":"沒有休息時段，錯誤和疲倦可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes breaks that support performance.","zh":"這個短語描述支持表現的小休。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"operate at top performance","meaning":"保持最佳表現","examples":[{"en":"No one can operate at top performance without adequate sleep.","zh":"沒有人能在沒有充足睡眠下保持最佳表現。"},{"en":"To operate at top performance means to function as well as possible.","zh":"保持最佳表現，是指以最好的狀態運作。"},{"en":"An athlete cannot operate at top performance after only three hours of sleep.","zh":"運動員只睡三小時後，不可能保持最佳表現。"},{"en":"Adequate sleep helps people concentrate, react quickly and make better decisions.","zh":"充足睡眠幫助人集中精神、快速反應並作出更好決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes working at one’s best level.","zh":"這個短語描述以最佳水平工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"adequate sleep","meaning":"充足睡眠","examples":[{"en":"People need adequate sleep to perform well.","zh":"人們需要充足睡眠才能表現良好。"},{"en":"Adequate sleep means enough sleep for health, energy and proper functioning.","zh":"充足睡眠，是對健康、精力和正常運作足夠的睡眠。"},{"en":"A teenager may need adequate sleep to concentrate during morning lessons.","zh":"青少年可能需要充足睡眠，才能在早上課堂集中精神。"},{"en":"Without adequate sleep, memory, mood and reaction time can worsen.","zh":"沒有充足睡眠，記憶、情緒和反應時間都可能變差。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sleep that is sufficient, not excessive.","zh":"這個短語描述足夠的睡眠，而不是過量睡眠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Puritan work ethic","meaning":"清教徒工作倫理","examples":[{"en":"The Puritan work ethic can still respect healthy sleep.","zh":"清教徒工作倫理仍可以尊重健康睡眠。"},{"en":"The Puritan work ethic is a belief that hard work, discipline and duty are morally important.","zh":"清教徒工作倫理是一種信念，認為勤奮、紀律和責任在道德上重要。"},{"en":"A family with a strong work ethic may expect children to finish homework before entertainment.","zh":"有強烈工作倫理的家庭可能期望孩子先完成功課，再娛樂。"},{"en":"The passage suggests that valuing work does not require rejecting sleep.","zh":"篇章暗示重視工作不需要否定睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strict moral attitude toward work.","zh":"這個短語描述對工作的嚴格道德態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be adhered to","meaning":"得到遵守","examples":[{"en":"The Puritan work ethic can be adhered to without rejecting sleep.","zh":"清教徒工作倫理可以在不否定睡眠的情況下得到遵守。"},{"en":"To be adhered to means to be followed or obeyed.","zh":"得到遵守，是指被跟從或服從。"},{"en":"School safety rules must be adhered to during laboratory experiments.","zh":"學校安全規則在實驗室實驗期間必須得到遵守。"},{"en":"A work ethic can be followed while still allowing enough rest.","zh":"人可以遵守工作倫理，同時仍容許足夠休息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes following a rule, belief or principle.","zh":"這個短語描述遵循規則、信念或原則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pay respect to","meaning":"重視；尊重","examples":[{"en":"Respect can still be paid to the sleep needs of healthy humans.","zh":"人們仍可以重視健康人類的睡眠需要。"},{"en":"To pay respect to something means to recognise its importance and treat it properly.","zh":"重視或尊重某事，是指承認其重要性並妥善對待。"},{"en":"A company should pay respect to employees’ need for meal breaks.","zh":"公司應重視員工用膳休息的需要。"},{"en":"Respecting sleep needs helps people work better instead of less seriously.","zh":"尊重睡眠需要幫助人工作得更好，而不是更不認真。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving proper recognition to a need or value.","zh":"這個短語描述對需要或價值給予適當承認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sleep needs","meaning":"睡眠需要","examples":[{"en":"Healthy humans have real sleep needs.","zh":"健康人類有真正的睡眠需要。"},{"en":"Sleep needs are the amount and quality of sleep a person requires to function well.","zh":"睡眠需要，是人為了良好運作所需的睡眠量和睡眠質素。"},{"en":"A teenager’s sleep needs may be greater than an adult’s.","zh":"青少年的睡眠需要可能比成人更大。"},{"en":"Ignoring sleep needs can harm concentration, mood and health.","zh":"忽視睡眠需要會損害專注力、情緒和健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the body’s real requirement for sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述身體對睡眠的真正需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"see something as","meaning":"把……視為","examples":[{"en":"It is wrong to see sleep as a shameful activity.","zh":"把睡眠視為可恥活動是錯的。"},{"en":"To see something as something means to regard or interpret it in that way.","zh":"把某事視為某物，是指以那種方式看待或理解它。"},{"en":"A teacher should not see mistakes as failure, but as chances to learn.","zh":"老師不應把錯誤視為失敗，而應視為學習機會。"},{"en":"Seeing sleep as laziness can make people ignore their health needs.","zh":"把睡眠視為懶惰，會令人忽視健康需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how people judge or understand something.","zh":"這個短語描述人們如何判斷或理解某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a shameful activity","meaning":"可恥的活動","examples":[{"en":"Sleep should not be treated as a shameful activity.","zh":"睡眠不應被當成可恥的活動。"},{"en":"A shameful activity is something people feel embarrassed or morally wrong about doing.","zh":"可恥的活動，是令人感到尷尬或道德上錯誤的事情。"},{"en":"Asking for help should not be treated as a shameful activity in school.","zh":"在學校中，求助不應被當成可恥的活動。"},{"en":"If sleep is treated as shameful, people may push themselves until they become unhealthy.","zh":"如果睡眠被視為可恥，人們可能逼自己到不健康的程度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an activity wrongly associated with disgrace.","zh":"這個短語描述被錯誤地與羞恥聯繫起來的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pass through five stages","meaning":"經過五個階段","examples":[{"en":"Sleepers usually pass through five stages of sleep.","zh":"睡眠者通常經過五個睡眠階段。"},{"en":"To pass through five stages means to move step by step through five parts of a process.","zh":"經過五個階段，是指一步一步通過一個過程的五個部分。"},{"en":"A student may pass through several stages when writing an essay: planning, drafting, revising and checking.","zh":"學生寫文章時可能經過幾個階段：計劃、起草、修改和檢查。"},{"en":"Sleep is not one simple state because the brain and body change across stages.","zh":"睡眠不是單一簡單狀態，因為大腦和身體會隨階段改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement through a sequence.","zh":"這個短語描述通過一連串階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"REM sleep","meaning":"快速眼動睡眠","examples":[{"en":"REM sleep follows the first four stages.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠在前四個階段之後出現。"},{"en":"REM sleep is a sleep stage with rapid eye movement, active brain waves and frequent dreaming.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠是一個睡眠階段，具有快速眼動、活躍腦電波和頻繁做夢。"},{"en":"A person awakened during REM sleep may remember a vivid dream.","zh":"一個人在快速眼動睡眠期間被喚醒，可能記得生動夢境。"},{"en":"REM sleep is important because it is linked with dreaming, learning and memory.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠很重要，因為它與做夢、學習和記憶有關。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific stage of the sleep cycle.","zh":"這個短語指睡眠週期中的特定階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rapid eye movement","meaning":"快速眼動","examples":[{"en":"REM stands for rapid eye movement.","zh":"REM 代表快速眼動。"},{"en":"Rapid eye movement means quick movements of the eyes during a particular stage of sleep.","zh":"快速眼動，是指睡眠某一階段中眼睛快速移動。"},{"en":"Doctors may monitor rapid eye movement when studying a patient’s sleep cycle.","zh":"醫生研究病人睡眠週期時，可能監察快速眼動。"},{"en":"Rapid eye movement gives REM sleep its name and helps identify that stage.","zh":"快速眼動令 REM 睡眠得名，並幫助識別該階段。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visible sign of REM sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述快速眼動睡眠的可見特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"progress cyclically","meaning":"循環推進","examples":[{"en":"The stages progress cyclically from stage 1 to REM.","zh":"這些階段由第一階段至快速眼動睡眠循環推進。"},{"en":"To progress cyclically means to move through a repeated cycle rather than in a straight line once only.","zh":"循環推進，是指通過一個重複週期，而不是只直線前進一次。"},{"en":"A school timetable may progress cyclically from Monday to Friday and then repeat the next week.","zh":"學校時間表可能由星期一到星期五循環推進，然後下星期重複。"},{"en":"Sleep stages repeat several times during the night.","zh":"睡眠階段在夜間會重複幾次。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated movement through a sequence.","zh":"這個短語描述在序列中反覆前進。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a complete sleep cycle","meaning":"完整睡眠週期","examples":[{"en":"A complete sleep cycle takes an average of 90 to 110 minutes.","zh":"完整睡眠週期平均需時九十至一百一十分鐘。"},{"en":"A complete sleep cycle is one full round through the main sleep stages.","zh":"完整睡眠週期，是通過主要睡眠階段的一整輪。"},{"en":"A person may pass through several complete sleep cycles in one night.","zh":"一個人一晚可能經過幾個完整睡眠週期。"},{"en":"If a cycle is interrupted, the person may wake up feeling less rested.","zh":"如果週期被打斷，人醒來時可能較不覺得休息充足。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one full pattern of sleep stages.","zh":"這個短語描述睡眠階段的一整個模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"take an average of","meaning":"平均需時","examples":[{"en":"A complete sleep cycle takes an average of 90 to 110 minutes.","zh":"完整睡眠週期平均需時九十至一百一十分鐘。"},{"en":"To take an average of a certain time means to usually require about that amount of time.","zh":"平均需時某段時間，是指通常需要大約該時間。"},{"en":"The bus journey takes an average of thirty minutes on a normal school day.","zh":"在普通上學日，巴士車程平均需時三十分鐘。"},{"en":"Averages help describe typical timing, but individual cases may vary.","zh":"平均值幫助描述典型時間，但個別情況可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the usual amount of time needed.","zh":"這個短語給出通常所需時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"relatively short REM periods","meaning":"相對較短的快速眼動睡眠期","examples":[{"en":"The first sleep cycles have relatively short REM periods.","zh":"最初的睡眠週期有相對較短的快速眼動睡眠期。"},{"en":"Relatively short REM periods are REM stages that are shorter compared with later ones.","zh":"相對較短的快速眼動睡眠期，是與較後階段相比較短的 REM 階段。"},{"en":"A student’s first break may be relatively short, while later breaks are longer.","zh":"學生第一次小休可能相對較短，而之後的小休較長。"},{"en":"Early in the night, deep sleep is longer and REM sleep is shorter.","zh":"夜間早段，深層睡眠較長而快速眼動睡眠較短。"},{"en":"This phrase describes REM sleep in comparison with other parts of the night.","zh":"這個短語以夜間其他部分作比較描述 REM 睡眠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"long periods of deep sleep","meaning":"長時間深層睡眠","examples":[{"en":"Early sleep cycles have long periods of deep sleep.","zh":"早期睡眠週期有長時間深層睡眠。"},{"en":"Long periods of deep sleep are extended times spent in the deepest sleep stages.","zh":"長時間深層睡眠，是在最深睡眠階段中停留較長時間。"},{"en":"After a tiring day, a person may spend longer in deep sleep early in the night.","zh":"經過疲倦一天後，人可能在夜間早段花更長時間進入深層睡眠。"},{"en":"Deep sleep supports physical repair and is harder to wake from.","zh":"深層睡眠支持身體修復，也較難被喚醒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extended time in restorative sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述長時間處於恢復性睡眠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"later in the night","meaning":"在晚間較後時段","examples":[{"en":"Later in the night, REM periods become longer.","zh":"在晚間較後時段，快速眼動睡眠期變得更長。"},{"en":"Later in the night means during the later part of the sleeping period.","zh":"在晚間較後時段，是指睡眠期間的較後部分。"},{"en":"A person may dream more vividly later in the night when REM periods are longer.","zh":"當快速眼動睡眠期較長，人可能在晚間較後時段做更生動的夢。"},{"en":"Sleep stages change as the night continues.","zh":"睡眠階段會隨夜晚推進而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes timing within the night.","zh":"這個短語描述夜間內部的時間位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lengthen","meaning":"變長","examples":[{"en":"REM periods lengthen later in the night.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠期在晚間較後時段變長。"},{"en":"To lengthen means to become longer or make something longer.","zh":"變長，是指變得更長或令某物更長。"},{"en":"A teacher may lengthen a lesson if students need more practice.","zh":"如果學生需要更多練習，老師可能延長課堂。"},{"en":"REM periods lengthen as sleep cycles repeat through the night.","zh":"隨着睡眠週期在夜間重複，快速眼動睡眠期會變長。"},{"en":"This word describes an increase in duration or size.","zh":"這個詞描述時間長度或尺寸增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"deep sleep time decreases","meaning":"深層睡眠時間減少","examples":[{"en":"Deep sleep time decreases later in the night.","zh":"深層睡眠時間在晚間較後時段減少。"},{"en":"Deep sleep time decreases means the amount of time spent in deep sleep becomes smaller.","zh":"深層睡眠時間減少，是指花在深層睡眠中的時間變少。"},{"en":"A student’s screen time may decrease during exam week if they focus on revision.","zh":"如果學生專注溫習，考試週的螢幕時間可能減少。"},{"en":"As REM periods become longer, deep sleep often becomes shorter.","zh":"當快速眼動睡眠期變長，深層睡眠通常變短。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reduction in time spent in one sleep stage.","zh":"這個短語描述某睡眠階段所佔時間減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"light sleep","meaning":"淺睡","examples":[{"en":"Stage 1 is light sleep.","zh":"第一階段是淺睡。"},{"en":"Light sleep is a shallow stage of sleep from which a person can wake easily.","zh":"淺睡是較淺的睡眠階段，人可以容易醒來。"},{"en":"A person in light sleep may hear a door closing and wake up.","zh":"處於淺睡的人可能聽到關門聲就醒來。"},{"en":"Light sleep often marks the transition between wakefulness and deeper sleep.","zh":"淺睡通常標誌着清醒與更深睡眠之間的過渡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sleep that is not yet deep.","zh":"這個短語描述尚未進入深層的睡眠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"drift in and out of sleep","meaning":"半睡半醒","examples":[{"en":"In stage 1, people drift in and out of sleep.","zh":"在第一階段，人們會半睡半醒。"},{"en":"To drift in and out of sleep means to move gently between being awake and asleep.","zh":"半睡半醒，是指在清醒和睡着之間輕輕來回。"},{"en":"A tired passenger may drift in and out of sleep on a long bus ride.","zh":"疲倦乘客可能在長途巴士車程中半睡半醒。"},{"en":"During this state, a small sound may wake the person easily.","zh":"在這種狀態中，小聲音也可能容易把人喚醒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes half-sleep rather than deep sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述半睡狀態，而不是深層睡眠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be awakened easily","meaning":"容易被喚醒","examples":[{"en":"People in stage 1 can be awakened easily.","zh":"處於第一階段的人容易被喚醒。"},{"en":"To be awakened easily means to wake up with little noise, touch or disturbance.","zh":"容易被喚醒，是指很小聲音、觸碰或干擾也會醒來。"},{"en":"A baby may be awakened easily if the room door closes loudly.","zh":"如果房門關得很大聲，嬰兒可能容易被喚醒。"},{"en":"Light sleep is fragile because the sleeper has not entered deep sleep yet.","zh":"淺睡很脆弱，因為睡眠者尚未進入深層睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sleep that is easy to interrupt.","zh":"這個短語描述容易被打斷的睡眠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"muscle activity slows","meaning":"肌肉活動減慢","examples":[{"en":"Muscle activity slows during stage 1.","zh":"肌肉活動在第一階段減慢。"},{"en":"Muscle activity slows means the muscles move less and become more relaxed.","zh":"肌肉活動減慢，是指肌肉移動較少並變得更放鬆。"},{"en":"After lying down for a while, a person’s muscle activity may slow as they become sleepy.","zh":"躺下一會兒後，人變得想睡時，肌肉活動可能減慢。"},{"en":"Slower muscle activity helps the body move from wakefulness into sleep.","zh":"肌肉活動減慢幫助身體由清醒進入睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reduced body movement.","zh":"這個短語描述身體活動減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sudden muscle contractions","meaning":"突然肌肉收縮","examples":[{"en":"Many people experience sudden muscle contractions during stage 1.","zh":"許多人在第一階段經歷突然肌肉收縮。"},{"en":"Sudden muscle contractions are quick, unexpected tightening movements of muscles.","zh":"突然肌肉收縮，是肌肉快速、意外地繃緊或抽動。"},{"en":"A person may suddenly jerk while falling asleep because of a muscle contraction.","zh":"一個人在入睡時可能因肌肉收縮而突然抽動。"},{"en":"These contractions can make someone feel as if they are falling.","zh":"這些收縮可以令人感覺好像正在跌落。"},{"en":"This phrase describes brief involuntary body movements.","zh":"這個短語描述短暫而非自願的身體動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be preceded by","meaning":"之前先出現……","examples":[{"en":"Sudden muscle contractions may be preceded by a sensation of falling.","zh":"突然肌肉收縮之前可能先出現跌落感。"},{"en":"To be preceded by something means to happen after that thing comes first.","zh":"某事之前先出現另一事，是指另一事先發生，然後該事發生。"},{"en":"A loud alarm may be preceded by a flashing warning light.","zh":"巨大警報聲之前可能先出現閃爍警告燈。"},{"en":"In light sleep, the feeling of falling may come before a body jerk.","zh":"在淺睡中，跌落感可能在身體抽動前出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an earlier event in a sequence.","zh":"這個短語描述序列中較早發生的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a sensation of falling","meaning":"跌落感","examples":[{"en":"Some people feel a sensation of falling during light sleep.","zh":"有些人在淺睡期間感到跌落感。"},{"en":"A sensation of falling is the feeling that the body is dropping, even when it is not.","zh":"跌落感是身體正在下墜的感覺，即使實際上沒有下墜。"},{"en":"A student dozing on the sofa may suddenly feel a sensation of falling and wake up.","zh":"在梳化上打瞌睡的學生可能突然感到跌落感並醒來。"},{"en":"This feeling can trigger a sudden muscle jerk.","zh":"這種感覺可以觸發突然肌肉抽動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common feeling during early sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述早期睡眠中的常見感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"brain waves","meaning":"腦電波","examples":[{"en":"Brain waves become slower in stage 2.","zh":"腦電波在第二階段變慢。"},{"en":"Brain waves are patterns of electrical activity produced by the brain.","zh":"腦電波是大腦產生的電活動模式。"},{"en":"Sleep researchers use machines to record brain waves during the night.","zh":"睡眠研究人員使用機器記錄夜間腦電波。"},{"en":"Different brain-wave patterns help identify different stages of sleep.","zh":"不同腦電波模式幫助識別不同睡眠階段。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to measurable brain activity.","zh":"這個短語指可量度的大腦活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"occasional burst of","meaning":"偶爾爆發的……","examples":[{"en":"Stage 2 includes an occasional burst of rapid brain waves.","zh":"第二階段包括偶爾爆發的快速腦電波。"},{"en":"An occasional burst of something is a short event that happens from time to time.","zh":"偶爾爆發的某事，是時不時短暫出現的事件。"},{"en":"A quiet classroom may have an occasional burst of laughter when students hear a joke.","zh":"安靜課室在學生聽到笑話時，可能偶爾爆發笑聲。"},{"en":"In stage 2 sleep, mostly slow brain waves may be interrupted by short fast bursts.","zh":"在第二階段睡眠中，主要較慢的腦電波可能被短暫快速爆發打斷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes brief, irregular appearances.","zh":"這個短語描述短暫、不規則的出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rapid brain waves","meaning":"快速腦電波","examples":[{"en":"Stage 2 includes occasional rapid brain waves.","zh":"第二階段包括偶爾出現的快速腦電波。"},{"en":"Rapid brain waves are quick patterns of electrical activity in the brain.","zh":"快速腦電波是大腦中快速的電活動模式。"},{"en":"A sleep monitor may show rapid brain waves during certain sleep stages.","zh":"睡眠監測器可能在某些睡眠階段顯示快速腦電波。"},{"en":"Rapid brain waves help scientists distinguish one stage from another.","zh":"快速腦電波幫助科學家區分不同階段。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fast brain activity patterns.","zh":"這個短語描述快速大腦活動模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"extremely slow brain waves","meaning":"極慢腦電波","examples":[{"en":"Stage 3 includes extremely slow brain waves called delta waves.","zh":"第三階段包括稱為 delta 波的極慢腦電波。"},{"en":"Extremely slow brain waves are very low-frequency electrical patterns in the brain.","zh":"極慢腦電波是大腦中頻率很低的電活動模式。"},{"en":"Deep sleep is often linked with slower brain-wave activity.","zh":"深層睡眠通常與較慢的腦電波活動有關。"},{"en":"These waves show that the brain has entered a deeper sleep stage.","zh":"這些腦電波顯示大腦已進入更深睡眠階段。"},{"en":"This phrase describes brain activity during deep sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述深層睡眠中的大腦活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"delta waves","meaning":"delta 波","examples":[{"en":"Delta waves appear during deep sleep.","zh":"delta 波在深層睡眠期間出現。"},{"en":"Delta waves are very slow brain waves linked with deep stages of sleep.","zh":"delta 波是與深層睡眠階段相關的非常慢腦電波。"},{"en":"A sleep scientist may identify deep sleep by looking for delta waves.","zh":"睡眠科學家可能透過尋找 delta 波來識別深層睡眠。"},{"en":"When delta waves dominate, it can be difficult to wake the sleeper.","zh":"當 delta 波佔主導時，要叫醒睡眠者可能很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase names a brain-wave pattern associated with deep sleep.","zh":"這個短語命名與深層睡眠相關的腦電波模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be interspersed with","meaning":"夾雜着……","examples":[{"en":"Delta waves are interspersed with smaller, faster waves.","zh":"delta 波夾雜着較小、較快的腦電波。"},{"en":"To be interspersed with something means to have those things mixed in among the main pattern.","zh":"夾雜着某物，是指那些東西混在主要模式之中。"},{"en":"A long lecture may be interspersed with short questions to keep students engaged.","zh":"長講座可能夾雜着短問題，以保持學生投入。"},{"en":"In stage 3, slow waves appear together with some faster waves.","zh":"在第三階段，慢波與一些較快腦電波一同出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one thing being mixed among another.","zh":"這個短語描述一種東西混在另一種之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"smaller, faster waves","meaning":"較小、較快的腦電波","examples":[{"en":"In stage 3, delta waves are mixed with smaller, faster waves.","zh":"在第三階段，delta 波與較小、較快的腦電波混合。"},{"en":"Smaller, faster waves are brain waves that are lower in size but quicker than delta waves.","zh":"較小、較快的腦電波，是比 delta 波幅度較小但速度較快的腦電波。"},{"en":"A sound recording may show small fast waves mixed with larger slow waves.","zh":"聲音記錄可能顯示小而快的波與大而慢的波混在一起。"},{"en":"Their presence shows that stage 3 is not made only of delta waves.","zh":"它們的存在顯示第三階段不只由 delta 波組成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a contrasting brain-wave pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述一種形成對比的腦電波模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"almost exclusively","meaning":"幾乎完全","examples":[{"en":"In stage 4, the brain produces delta waves almost exclusively.","zh":"在第四階段，大腦幾乎完全產生 delta 波。"},{"en":"Almost exclusively means almost only, with very few other things included.","zh":"幾乎完全，是指幾乎只有某事，幾乎沒有其他東西。"},{"en":"A vegetarian restaurant may serve plant-based food almost exclusively.","zh":"素食餐廳可能幾乎完全提供植物性食物。"},{"en":"If delta waves appear almost exclusively, the sleep stage is very deep.","zh":"如果 delta 波幾乎完全出現，該睡眠階段非常深。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that dominates nearly completely.","zh":"這個短語描述某事幾乎完全佔主導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be referred to as","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"Stages 3 and 4 are referred to as deep sleep.","zh":"第三和第四階段被稱為深層睡眠。"},{"en":"To be referred to as something means to be called or described by that name.","zh":"被稱為某物，是指以該名稱被稱呼或描述。"},{"en":"A school’s main hall may be referred to as the assembly hall.","zh":"學校主禮堂可能被稱為集會禮堂。"},{"en":"Naming stages helps students understand and compare sleep patterns.","zh":"命名階段有助學生理解和比較睡眠模式。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the term used for something.","zh":"這個短語引入某事物所使用的名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"wake someone from","meaning":"把某人從……中喚醒","examples":[{"en":"It is very difficult to wake someone from deep sleep.","zh":"要把某人從深層睡眠中喚醒非常困難。"},{"en":"To wake someone from a state means to cause them to stop sleeping or leave that state.","zh":"把某人從某狀態中喚醒，是指令他們停止睡眠或離開該狀態。"},{"en":"It may be hard to wake a tired child from a deep afternoon nap.","zh":"要把疲倦孩子從深沉午睡中叫醒可能很困難。"},{"en":"Deep sleep is harder to interrupt than light sleep.","zh":"深層睡眠比淺睡更難被打斷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bringing someone out of sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述把某人帶離睡眠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bedwetting","meaning":"尿床","examples":[{"en":"Some children experience bedwetting during deep sleep.","zh":"有些兒童在深層睡眠期間會尿床。"},{"en":"Bedwetting means accidentally urinating while asleep, usually in bed.","zh":"尿床是睡着時意外排尿，通常發生在床上。"},{"en":"A young child may experience bedwetting even after learning to use the toilet in the day.","zh":"年幼孩子即使日間已學會如廁，也可能尿床。"},{"en":"Bedwetting can happen during deep sleep because the child may not wake easily.","zh":"尿床可能在深層睡眠期間發生，因為孩子不容易醒來。"},{"en":"This word describes an involuntary sleep-related event.","zh":"這個詞描述與睡眠相關的非自願事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sleepwalking","meaning":"夢遊","examples":[{"en":"Some children experience sleepwalking during deep sleep.","zh":"有些兒童在深層睡眠期間會夢遊。"},{"en":"Sleepwalking means walking or moving around while still asleep.","zh":"夢遊是人在仍睡着時行走或活動。"},{"en":"A sleepwalking child may leave the bedroom without remembering it the next morning.","zh":"夢遊中的孩子可能離開睡房，第二天早上卻不記得。"},{"en":"Because sleepwalking happens during deep sleep, the person may be hard to wake.","zh":"因為夢遊發生在深層睡眠期間，當事人可能很難被喚醒。"},{"en":"This word describes movement while asleep.","zh":"這個詞描述睡眠中的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"night terrors","meaning":"夜驚","examples":[{"en":"Some children experience night terrors during deep sleep.","zh":"有些兒童在深層睡眠期間會出現夜驚。"},{"en":"Night terrors are episodes of intense fear during sleep, often with shouting or sudden movement.","zh":"夜驚是睡眠期間出現的強烈恐懼發作，通常伴隨叫喊或突然動作。"},{"en":"A child having night terrors may look frightened but not remember the event clearly later.","zh":"出現夜驚的孩子可能看起來很害怕，但之後未必清楚記得事件。"},{"en":"Night terrors can worry parents because they seem dramatic and difficult to interrupt.","zh":"夜驚會令父母擔心，因為它看起來很劇烈且難以打斷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a frightening sleep disturbance.","zh":"這個短語描述令人害怕的睡眠干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in the REM period","meaning":"在快速眼動睡眠期","examples":[{"en":"In the REM period, breathing becomes more rapid and irregular.","zh":"在快速眼動睡眠期，呼吸變得更急促和不規則。"},{"en":"In the REM period means during the rapid-eye-movement stage of sleep.","zh":"在快速眼動睡眠期，是指在睡眠的快速眼動階段期間。"},{"en":"A sleep monitor may show different breathing patterns in the REM period.","zh":"睡眠監測器可能顯示快速眼動睡眠期中的不同呼吸模式。"},{"en":"REM sleep differs from deep sleep because the brain and body become more active in some ways.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠不同於深層睡眠，因為大腦和身體在某些方面變得更活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific time within the sleep cycle.","zh":"這個短語指出睡眠週期中的特定時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"become more rapid, irregular and shallow","meaning":"變得更急促、不規則而淺","examples":[{"en":"Breathing becomes more rapid, irregular and shallow during REM sleep.","zh":"呼吸在快速眼動睡眠期間變得更急促、不規則而淺。"},{"en":"To become more rapid, irregular and shallow means to become faster, less even and less deep.","zh":"變得更急促、不規則而淺，是指變得更快、較不平均且較不深入。"},{"en":"A nervous speaker’s breathing may become rapid, irregular and shallow before a presentation.","zh":"緊張演講者在匯報前呼吸可能變得急促、不規則而淺。"},{"en":"Changes in breathing help researchers identify different sleep stages.","zh":"呼吸變化幫助研究人員識別不同睡眠階段。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a noticeable change in breathing pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述呼吸模式的明顯變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"jerk rapidly","meaning":"快速抽動","examples":[{"en":"The eyes jerk rapidly during REM sleep.","zh":"眼睛在快速眼動睡眠期間快速抽動。"},{"en":"To jerk rapidly means to move suddenly and quickly in short movements.","zh":"快速抽動，是指以短促動作突然快速移動。"},{"en":"A person’s hand may jerk rapidly if they touch something very hot.","zh":"如果人碰到很熱的東西，手可能快速抽動。"},{"en":"Rapid eye jerks are one reason REM sleep can be identified.","zh":"眼睛快速抽動是識別 REM 睡眠的原因之一。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quick, sudden movement.","zh":"這個短語描述快速而突然的動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"limb muscles","meaning":"四肢肌肉","examples":[{"en":"Limb muscles are temporarily paralysed during REM sleep.","zh":"四肢肌肉在快速眼動睡眠期間暫時麻痺。"},{"en":"Limb muscles are the muscles in the arms and legs.","zh":"四肢肌肉是手臂和腿部的肌肉。"},{"en":"A runner uses limb muscles heavily during training.","zh":"跑步者在訓練期間大量使用四肢肌肉。"},{"en":"During REM sleep, limb muscles are paralysed so the person does not act out dreams.","zh":"在快速眼動睡眠期間，四肢肌肉會麻痺，使人不會把夢中的動作做出來。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to muscles used for arm and leg movement.","zh":"這個短語指用於手臂和腿部活動的肌肉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be temporarily paralysed","meaning":"暫時麻痺","examples":[{"en":"Limb muscles are temporarily paralysed during REM sleep.","zh":"四肢肌肉在快速眼動睡眠期間暫時麻痺。"},{"en":"To be temporarily paralysed means to be unable to move for a short time.","zh":"暫時麻痺，是指短時間內無法移動。"},{"en":"A foot may feel temporarily paralysed after sitting on it for too long.","zh":"如果坐壓腳太久，腳可能暫時麻痺。"},{"en":"Temporary paralysis during REM sleep may protect the body from acting out dreams.","zh":"REM 睡眠期間的暫時麻痺可能保護身體，避免把夢境動作做出來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a short-term loss of movement.","zh":"這個短語描述短期失去活動能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"increase to levels experienced when","meaning":"上升至……時的水平","examples":[{"en":"Brain waves increase to levels experienced when a person is awake.","zh":"腦電波上升至人在清醒時所經歷的水平。"},{"en":"To increase to levels experienced when something happens means to rise until they match that condition.","zh":"上升至某情況時的水平，是指升高到與該情況相同的程度。"},{"en":"A student’s heart rate may increase to levels experienced during exercise when they feel panic.","zh":"學生恐慌時，心率可能上升至運動時的水平。"},{"en":"In REM sleep, brain activity can look surprisingly similar to waking activity.","zh":"在快速眼動睡眠中，大腦活動可以出奇地接近清醒時活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rising to a comparable level.","zh":"這個短語描述上升至可比較的水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"heart rate increases","meaning":"心率上升","examples":[{"en":"Heart rate increases during REM sleep.","zh":"心率在快速眼動睡眠期間上升。"},{"en":"Heart rate increases means the heart beats more times per minute.","zh":"心率上升，是指心臟每分鐘跳動次數增加。"},{"en":"A person’s heart rate increases when they run up stairs.","zh":"人跑上樓梯時心率會上升。"},{"en":"During REM sleep, rising heart rate shows that the body is not completely inactive.","zh":"在快速眼動睡眠期間，心率上升顯示身體並非完全不活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rise in heartbeat speed.","zh":"這個短語描述心跳速度上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"blood pressure rises","meaning":"血壓上升","examples":[{"en":"Blood pressure rises during REM sleep.","zh":"血壓在快速眼動睡眠期間上升。"},{"en":"Blood pressure rises means the force of blood against blood vessels becomes higher.","zh":"血壓上升，是指血液對血管壁的壓力變高。"},{"en":"Blood pressure may rise when a person is stressed or frightened.","zh":"當人感到壓力或害怕時，血壓可能上升。"},{"en":"REM sleep can involve body changes that are closer to wakefulness than deep sleep.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠可能涉及較接近清醒而非深層睡眠的身體變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increase in a cardiovascular measure.","zh":"這個短語描述心血管指標上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lose some of the ability to","meaning":"失去部分……能力","examples":[{"en":"The body loses some of the ability to regulate its temperature.","zh":"身體失去部分調節體溫的能力。"},{"en":"To lose some of the ability to do something means to become less able to do it.","zh":"失去部分做某事的能力，是指變得較不能做到該事。"},{"en":"A tired driver may lose some of the ability to react quickly.","zh":"疲倦司機可能失去部分快速反應的能力。"},{"en":"During REM sleep, the body becomes less effective at temperature control.","zh":"在快速眼動睡眠期間，身體控制體溫的能力變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a partial loss of function.","zh":"這個短語描述功能的部分喪失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"regulate its temperature","meaning":"調節體溫","examples":[{"en":"The body loses some of the ability to regulate its temperature.","zh":"身體失去部分調節體溫的能力。"},{"en":"To regulate its temperature means to control body heat so it stays within a safe range.","zh":"調節體溫，是指控制身體熱量，使其保持在安全範圍內。"},{"en":"Sweating helps the body regulate its temperature on a hot day.","zh":"在炎熱日子流汗幫助身體調節體溫。"},{"en":"If temperature regulation weakens, the body may become too hot or too cold more easily.","zh":"如果體溫調節變弱，身體可能更容易過熱或過冷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes internal heat control.","zh":"這個短語描述內部熱量控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"dreams occur","meaning":"夢境出現","examples":[{"en":"Most dreams occur during REM sleep.","zh":"大多數夢境在快速眼動睡眠期間出現。"},{"en":"Dreams occur means dreams happen or take place.","zh":"夢境出現，是指夢發生。"},{"en":"Strange dreams may occur when a person is stressed or overtired.","zh":"當人有壓力或過度疲倦時，可能出現奇怪夢境。"},{"en":"Because many dreams occur in REM sleep, people awakened then often remember them.","zh":"因為許多夢在快速眼動睡眠中出現，人們在那時被喚醒通常能記得夢境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes when dreams happen.","zh":"這個短語描述夢何時發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"if awakened during","meaning":"如果在……期間被喚醒","examples":[{"en":"If awakened during REM sleep, a person can remember their dreams.","zh":"如果在快速眼動睡眠期間被喚醒，一個人可以記得自己的夢。"},{"en":"If awakened during something means if a person is woken up while that stage or event is happening.","zh":"如果在某期間被喚醒，是指人在該階段或事件發生時被叫醒。"},{"en":"If awakened during a deep nap, a child may feel confused.","zh":"如果孩子在深沉午睡期間被喚醒，可能會感到迷糊。"},{"en":"Waking during REM sleep can make dream memories easier to recall.","zh":"在快速眼動睡眠期間醒來，可以令夢境記憶較容易回想起。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what happens when sleep is interrupted at a particular time.","zh":"這個短語描述睡眠在特定時間被打斷時發生甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"remember their dreams","meaning":"記得自己的夢","examples":[{"en":"People can often remember their dreams after waking during REM sleep.","zh":"人們在快速眼動睡眠期間醒來後，通常可以記得自己的夢。"},{"en":"To remember their dreams means to recall dream images, events or feelings after waking.","zh":"記得自己的夢，是指醒來後回想起夢中的畫面、事件或感覺。"},{"en":"A student may remember a dream clearly and tell it to friends at breakfast.","zh":"學生可能清楚記得一個夢，並在早餐時告訴朋友。"},{"en":"People may forget dreams quickly if they wake at another stage or do not think about them.","zh":"如果人在其他階段醒來或沒有回想夢境，可能很快忘記。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recalling dreams after sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述睡眠後回憶夢境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"intervals of REM sleep","meaning":"快速眼動睡眠時段","examples":[{"en":"Most people experience three to five intervals of REM sleep each night.","zh":"大多數人每晚經歷三至五段快速眼動睡眠時段。"},{"en":"Intervals of REM sleep are separate periods of REM sleep within the night.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠時段，是夜間分開出現的 REM 睡眠期間。"},{"en":"A student may have several study intervals with short breaks between them.","zh":"學生可能有幾段溫習時段，中間有短休息。"},{"en":"REM intervals usually repeat as sleep cycles progress.","zh":"隨着睡眠週期推進，快速眼動睡眠時段通常會重複出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated periods of REM sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆出現的 REM 睡眠期間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"infants","meaning":"嬰兒","examples":[{"en":"Infants spend almost 50% of their time in REM sleep.","zh":"嬰兒接近百分之五十的睡眠時間處於快速眼動睡眠。"},{"en":"Infants are very young babies, usually in the first year of life.","zh":"嬰兒是非常年幼的寶寶，通常指生命第一年內。"},{"en":"Parents of infants often wake at night because babies sleep and feed frequently.","zh":"嬰兒父母常在夜間醒來，因為寶寶睡眠和吃奶都很頻密。"},{"en":"Infants spend much time in REM sleep because their brains are developing rapidly.","zh":"嬰兒花很多時間在快速眼動睡眠中，因為他們的大腦快速發展。"},{"en":"This word refers to very young children.","zh":"這個詞指非常年幼的孩子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"spend nearly half of","meaning":"花接近一半……於","examples":[{"en":"Adults spend nearly half of their sleep time in stage 2.","zh":"成人花接近一半睡眠時間於第二階段。"},{"en":"To spend nearly half of something on or in something means to use almost 50% of it that way.","zh":"花接近一半某事於某處，是指以那種方式使用接近百分之五十。"},{"en":"A student may spend nearly half of Saturday revising before a test.","zh":"學生可能在測驗前花接近一半星期六時間溫習。"},{"en":"If adults spend nearly half of sleep in stage 2, that stage is a major part of sleep.","zh":"如果成人睡眠接近一半處於第二階段，該階段就是睡眠的重要部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large proportion close to one half.","zh":"這個短語描述接近一半的大比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be divided between","meaning":"分配在……之間","examples":[{"en":"The remaining sleep time is divided between the other three stages.","zh":"剩餘睡眠時間分配在其他三個階段之間。"},{"en":"To be divided between things means to be shared among them.","zh":"分配在幾件事之間，是指在它們之間分享或分配。"},{"en":"A family’s weekend time may be divided between shopping, homework and visiting relatives.","zh":"家庭週末時間可能分配在購物、功課和探親之間。"},{"en":"If time is divided between stages, each stage receives only part of the total.","zh":"如果時間分配在幾個階段之間，每個階段只得到總量的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distribution among several options.","zh":"這個短語描述在幾個選項之間分配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"older adults","meaning":"年長成人","examples":[{"en":"Older adults spend progressively less time in REM sleep.","zh":"年長成人在快速眼動睡眠中的時間逐漸減少。"},{"en":"Older adults are people in later adulthood, often elderly or approaching old age.","zh":"年長成人是處於較後成年階段的人，通常指長者或接近老年的人。"},{"en":"Older adults may need different sleep routines from teenagers or young adults.","zh":"年長成人可能需要不同於青少年或年輕成人的睡眠作息。"},{"en":"Age can affect sleep structure, including the amount of REM sleep.","zh":"年齡可以影響睡眠結構，包括快速眼動睡眠量。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to adults in an older age group.","zh":"這個短語指較年長年齡組別的成人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"progressively less time","meaning":"逐漸減少的時間","examples":[{"en":"Older adults spend progressively less time in REM sleep.","zh":"年長成人花在快速眼動睡眠中的時間逐漸減少。"},{"en":"Progressively less time means gradually decreasing time over a period.","zh":"逐漸減少的時間，是指在一段時期中慢慢變少的時間。"},{"en":"As exams get closer, a student may spend progressively less time on games.","zh":"隨着考試臨近，學生可能花在遊戲上的時間逐漸減少。"},{"en":"If REM time becomes progressively less, the change happens step by step.","zh":"如果快速眼動睡眠時間逐漸減少，變化是一點一點發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gradual reduction in time.","zh":"這個短語描述時間逐步減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a relatively young field","meaning":"相對年輕的領域","examples":[{"en":"Sleep research is a relatively young field.","zh":"睡眠研究是一個相對年輕的領域。"},{"en":"A relatively young field is an area of study that has not been established for very long.","zh":"相對年輕的領域，是建立時間尚不算很長的研究範疇。"},{"en":"Artificial intelligence ethics is a relatively young field compared with mathematics.","zh":"與數學相比，人工智能倫理是一個相對年輕的領域。"},{"en":"Young fields often change quickly as new tools and discoveries appear.","zh":"年輕領域通常隨新工具和新發現出現而快速變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an area of knowledge still developing.","zh":"這個短語描述仍在發展的知識範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"discover REM sleep","meaning":"發現快速眼動睡眠","examples":[{"en":"Scientists did not discover REM sleep until 1953.","zh":"科學家直到 1953 年才發現快速眼動睡眠。"},{"en":"To discover REM sleep means to identify and recognise the rapid-eye-movement stage of sleep scientifically.","zh":"發現快速眼動睡眠，是指科學地識別並確認睡眠中的快速眼動階段。"},{"en":"Researchers may discover a new sleep pattern when better monitoring machines become available.","zh":"當更好的監測機器出現，研究人員可能發現新的睡眠模式。"},{"en":"The discovery of REM sleep changed how people understood the sleeping brain.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠的發現改變了人們對睡眠中大腦的理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major scientific finding about sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述關於睡眠的重要科學發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"not...until","meaning":"直到……才……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists did not discover REM sleep until 1953.","zh":"科學家直到 1953 年才發現快速眼動睡眠。"},{"en":"Not...until means something happened only at a later time, not before then.","zh":"not...until 是指某事到較後時間才發生，在那之前沒有發生。"},{"en":"The student did not understand the grammar rule until the teacher gave examples.","zh":"學生直到老師給例子後才理解文法規則。"},{"en":"This structure emphasises how late something happened.","zh":"這個結構強調某事發生得多晚。"},{"en":"It is useful for showing a delayed event or discovery.","zh":"它適合表示延遲發生的事件或發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"machines were developed to","meaning":"機器被研發出來以……","examples":[{"en":"New machines were developed to monitor brain activity.","zh":"新機器被研發出來以監察大腦活動。"},{"en":"Machines were developed to do something means machines were created for that purpose.","zh":"機器被研發出來以做某事，是指機器為該目的而被創造。"},{"en":"New machines were developed to help hospitals scan patients more safely.","zh":"新機器被研發出來，以幫助醫院更安全地掃描病人。"},{"en":"Better machines can make new scientific discoveries possible.","zh":"更好的機器可以使新科學發現成為可能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes technology created to perform a task.","zh":"這個短語描述為執行任務而創造的科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"monitor brain activity","meaning":"監察大腦活動","examples":[{"en":"New machines allowed researchers to monitor brain activity.","zh":"新機器讓研究人員監察大腦活動。"},{"en":"To monitor brain activity means to record and observe what the brain is doing.","zh":"監察大腦活動，是指記錄和觀察大腦正在做甚麼。"},{"en":"Doctors may monitor brain activity when checking a patient with sleep problems.","zh":"醫生檢查有睡眠問題的病人時，可能監察大腦活動。"},{"en":"Monitoring brain activity helps scientists identify sleep stages.","zh":"監察大腦活動幫助科學家識別睡眠階段。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful measurement of the brain’s electrical patterns.","zh":"這個短語描述對大腦電活動模式的仔細量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"before this discovery","meaning":"在這項發現之前","examples":[{"en":"Before this discovery, people misunderstood sleep.","zh":"在這項發現之前，人們誤解睡眠。"},{"en":"Before this discovery means in the period before the new finding was made.","zh":"在這項發現之前，是指新發現出現前的一段時期。"},{"en":"Before the discovery of germs, people misunderstood how many diseases spread.","zh":"在細菌被發現之前，人們誤解許多疾病如何傳播。"},{"en":"A major discovery can change what people believe about a familiar topic.","zh":"重大發現可以改變人們對熟悉主題的看法。"},{"en":"This phrase sets up a contrast between old and new understanding.","zh":"這個短語建立舊理解與新理解之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"it was believed that","meaning":"人們當時認為","examples":[{"en":"It was believed that most brain activity ceased during sleep.","zh":"人們當時認為大部分大腦活動在睡眠期間停止。"},{"en":"It was believed that means people generally thought something was true.","zh":"人們當時認為，是指人們普遍以為某事為真。"},{"en":"It was once believed that heavy objects fall faster than light ones.","zh":"人們曾經認為重物比輕物下跌得更快。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces an old belief that later evidence may challenge.","zh":"這個短語常引入後來證據可能挑戰的舊觀念。"},{"en":"It helps show how scientific understanding changes over time.","zh":"它有助顯示科學理解如何隨時間改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"brain activity ceased","meaning":"大腦活動停止","examples":[{"en":"Scientists once believed that brain activity ceased during sleep.","zh":"科學家曾認為大腦活動在睡眠期間停止。"},{"en":"Brain activity ceased means the brain stopped being active.","zh":"大腦活動停止，是指大腦不再活動。"},{"en":"A machine display may show that activity has ceased when the line becomes flat.","zh":"當機器顯示線變平，可能表示活動已停止。"},{"en":"REM research showed that the brain remains active during parts of sleep.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠研究顯示，大腦在睡眠部分階段仍保持活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a complete stopping of brain activity.","zh":"這個短語描述大腦活動完全停止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"disprove the idea that","meaning":"推翻……的想法","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have disproved the idea that REM deprivation causes insanity.","zh":"科學家已推翻剝奪快速眼動睡眠會導致精神錯亂的想法。"},{"en":"To disprove the idea that something is true means to show with evidence that it is false.","zh":"推翻某想法，是指用證據顯示它是錯誤的。"},{"en":"A fair experiment may disprove the idea that boys always learn maths faster than girls.","zh":"公平實驗可能推翻男生總是比女生學數學快的想法。"},{"en":"When evidence disproves an idea, scientists must reject or revise it.","zh":"當證據推翻一個想法，科學家必須拒絕或修訂它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using evidence to overturn a belief.","zh":"這個短語描述用證據推翻信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"deprivation of REM sleep","meaning":"剝奪快速眼動睡眠","examples":[{"en":"Scientists studied the effects of deprivation of REM sleep.","zh":"科學家研究剝奪快速眼動睡眠的影響。"},{"en":"Deprivation of REM sleep means being prevented from getting REM sleep.","zh":"剝奪快速眼動睡眠，是指被阻止進入或獲得 REM 睡眠。"},{"en":"Sleep researchers may wake participants whenever REM sleep begins to study its effects.","zh":"睡眠研究人員可能在參加者一進入 REM 睡眠時叫醒他們，以研究其影響。"},{"en":"REM deprivation can affect mood, memory and dream recall.","zh":"REM 睡眠剝奪可以影響情緒、記憶和夢境回憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the loss or blocking of a sleep stage.","zh":"這個短語描述某個睡眠階段的失去或被阻止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lead to insanity","meaning":"導致精神錯亂","examples":[{"en":"Scientists disproved the idea that REM sleep deprivation can lead to insanity.","zh":"科學家推翻了剝奪快速眼動睡眠會導致精神錯亂的想法。"},{"en":"To lead to insanity means to cause severe mental disorder or loss of normal thinking.","zh":"導致精神錯亂，是指造成嚴重精神障礙或正常思考喪失。"},{"en":"Extreme stress may harm mental health, but it does not automatically lead to insanity.","zh":"極端壓力可能損害心理健康，但不會自動導致精神錯亂。"},{"en":"The passage says the idea about REM deprivation and insanity was disproved.","zh":"篇章指出 REM 睡眠剝奪與精神錯亂的說法已被推翻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a claimed serious mental consequence.","zh":"這個短語描述一種被聲稱的嚴重心理後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lack of REM sleep","meaning":"缺乏快速眼動睡眠","examples":[{"en":"Lack of REM sleep can alleviate clinical depression.","zh":"缺乏快速眼動睡眠可以紓緩臨床抑鬱症。"},{"en":"Lack of REM sleep means not getting enough rapid-eye-movement sleep.","zh":"缺乏快速眼動睡眠，是指沒有得到足夠 REM 睡眠。"},{"en":"A person may experience lack of REM sleep if their sleep is repeatedly interrupted.","zh":"如果一個人的睡眠反覆被打斷，可能出現快速眼動睡眠不足。"},{"en":"The passage notes an unusual finding that REM sleep loss may relieve depression in some cases.","zh":"篇章提到一項不尋常發現：在某些情況下，缺乏 REM 睡眠可能紓緩抑鬱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shortage of a specific sleep stage.","zh":"這個短語描述特定睡眠階段不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"alleviate clinical depression","meaning":"紓緩臨床抑鬱症","examples":[{"en":"Lack of REM sleep can alleviate clinical depression.","zh":"缺乏快速眼動睡眠可以紓緩臨床抑鬱症。"},{"en":"To alleviate clinical depression means to reduce the symptoms or severity of diagnosed depression.","zh":"紓緩臨床抑鬱症，是指減輕已診斷抑鬱症的症狀或嚴重程度。"},{"en":"Proper treatment may alleviate clinical depression when guided by medical professionals.","zh":"在醫療專業人士指導下，適當治療可能紓緩臨床抑鬱症。"},{"en":"If a condition alleviates depression, it makes symptoms less severe, not necessarily cured forever.","zh":"如果某條件能紓緩抑鬱，它是令症狀較輕，不一定永久治癒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes easing a serious mental health condition.","zh":"這個短語描述減輕嚴重心理健康狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"link REM sleep to","meaning":"將快速眼動睡眠與……聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"Recent theories link REM sleep to learning and memory.","zh":"近期理論將快速眼動睡眠與學習和記憶聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To link REM sleep to something means to connect it with that process or result.","zh":"將快速眼動睡眠與某事聯繫起來，是指把它與該過程或結果連接。"},{"en":"Researchers may link regular exercise to better sleep quality.","zh":"研究人員可能把規律運動與更好睡眠質素聯繫起來。"},{"en":"If REM sleep is linked to memory, losing it may affect how well people learn.","zh":"如果 REM 睡眠與記憶有關，失去它可能影響學習效果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a proposed relationship between two things.","zh":"這個短語描述兩件事之間被提出的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"learning and memory","meaning":"學習和記憶","examples":[{"en":"Recent theories link REM sleep to learning and memory.","zh":"近期理論將快速眼動睡眠與學習和記憶聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Learning and memory are the processes of gaining new information and storing it for later use.","zh":"學習和記憶，是獲得新資訊並把它儲存以供日後使用的過程。"},{"en":"Students rely on learning and memory when preparing for vocabulary tests.","zh":"學生準備詞彙測驗時依靠學習和記憶。"},{"en":"Sleep may support learning and memory by helping the brain process information.","zh":"睡眠可能透過幫助大腦處理資訊來支持學習和記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two connected mental functions.","zh":"這個短語描述兩個相關心智功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"考生為每題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option that matches the passage.","zh":"選出正確字母，是指選擇與文章相符的答案選項。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice question, students may choose A, B, C or D.","zh":"在多項選擇題中，學生可能選 A、B、C 或 D。"},{"en":"Students must understand the text carefully because similar options can be misleading.","zh":"學生必須仔細理解文本，因為相似選項可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction about answer format.","zh":"這個短語是關於答案格式的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"among other functions","meaning":"在其他功能之外","examples":[{"en":"Among other functions, sleep re-energises parts of the brain.","zh":"在其他功能之外，睡眠為大腦部分區域重新注入能量。"},{"en":"Among other functions means besides other jobs or purposes.","zh":"在其他功能之外，是指除了其他作用或目的之外。"},{"en":"A school library, among other functions, gives students a quiet place to read.","zh":"學校圖書館在其他功能之外，也給學生一個安靜閱讀地方。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the listed function is only one of several.","zh":"這個短語暗示列出的功能只是幾個功能之一。"},{"en":"It is useful when a thing has more than one purpose.","zh":"當某物有多於一個目的時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"serve to","meaning":"起……作用","examples":[{"en":"Sleep serves to re-energise parts of the brain.","zh":"睡眠起着為大腦部分區域重新注入能量的作用。"},{"en":"To serve to do something means to have the function or effect of doing it.","zh":"起某種作用，是指具有做該事的功能或效果。"},{"en":"A school bell serves to tell students when a lesson begins or ends.","zh":"學校鐘聲起着告訴學生課堂何時開始或結束的作用。"},{"en":"Sleep may serve to restore the brain after a day of activity.","zh":"睡眠可能起着在一天活動後恢復大腦的作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes function or purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述功能或目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"develop physically","meaning":"身體發育","examples":[{"en":"Children’s bodies develop physically during sleep.","zh":"兒童身體在睡眠期間發育。"},{"en":"To develop physically means to grow or change in the body.","zh":"身體發育，是指身體成長或改變。"},{"en":"Teenagers develop physically as their bones, muscles and organs mature.","zh":"青少年隨着骨骼、肌肉和器官成熟而身體發育。"},{"en":"Sleep supports physical development because growth hormones are released during deep sleep.","zh":"睡眠支持身體發育，因為生長荷爾蒙在深層睡眠期間釋放。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bodily growth and maturation.","zh":"這個短語描述身體成長和成熟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"push daily problems from our minds","meaning":"暫時拋開日常煩惱","examples":[{"en":"Some people think sleep can push daily problems from our minds.","zh":"有些人認為睡眠可以讓我們暫時拋開日常煩惱。"},{"en":"To push daily problems from our minds means to stop thinking about everyday worries for a while.","zh":"暫時拋開日常煩惱，是指一段時間不再想着日常憂慮。"},{"en":"A walk after school may push homework stress from a student’s mind for a short time.","zh":"放學後散步可能讓學生暫時拋開功課壓力。"},{"en":"Sleep may give people a break from worries, even if it does not solve them directly.","zh":"睡眠可能讓人暫時避開憂慮，即使它不直接解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes temporarily moving worries out of attention.","zh":"這個短語描述暫時把煩惱移出注意力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"accelerate the learning process","meaning":"加快學習過程","examples":[{"en":"Sleep may support learning, but the passage does not say it significantly accelerates the learning process.","zh":"睡眠可能支持學習，但篇章沒有說它顯著加快學習過程。"},{"en":"To accelerate the learning process means to make learning happen faster.","zh":"加快學習過程，是指令學習更快發生。"},{"en":"Clear examples can accelerate the learning process because students understand grammar more quickly.","zh":"清楚例子可以加快學習過程，因為學生更快理解文法。"},{"en":"Good sleep may support learning, but it is different from directly speeding up every lesson.","zh":"良好睡眠可能支持學習，但這不同於直接加快每一堂課。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making learning quicker.","zh":"這個短語描述令學習更快。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"re-energise parts of the brain","meaning":"為大腦部分區域重新注入能量","examples":[{"en":"Sleep may re-energise parts of the brain.","zh":"睡眠可能為大腦部分區域重新注入能量。"},{"en":"To re-energise parts of the brain means to restore mental energy or function in some brain areas.","zh":"為大腦部分區域重新注入能量，是指恢復某些腦區的心理能量或功能。"},{"en":"A short rest may re-energise a tired student before evening revision.","zh":"短暫休息可能在晚上溫習前為疲倦學生重新注入能量。"},{"en":"If the brain is re-energised, concentration and thinking may improve after sleep.","zh":"如果大腦重新獲得能量，睡醒後專注力和思考可能改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental renewal.","zh":"這個短語描述心理更新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be described as","meaning":"可被描述為","examples":[{"en":"Torpor can be described as a state of reduced metabolic activity.","zh":"低代謝休眠狀態可被描述為代謝活動降低的狀態。"},{"en":"To be described as something means to be explained or characterised in that way.","zh":"可被描述為某物，是指可以用那種方式解釋或形容。"},{"en":"A quiet student may be described as thoughtful rather than shy.","zh":"安靜學生可以被描述為深思熟慮，而不是害羞。"},{"en":"Description helps learners understand a term by giving its main features.","zh":"描述透過給出主要特徵，幫助學習者理解術語。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an explanation or label.","zh":"這個短語引入解釋或標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"unlike small mammals","meaning":"與小型哺乳動物不同","examples":[{"en":"Unlike small mammals, humans save only a small amount of energy by sleeping.","zh":"與小型哺乳動物不同，人類透過睡眠只節省少量能量。"},{"en":"Unlike small mammals means different from small mammals.","zh":"與小型哺乳動物不同，是指不同於小型哺乳動物。"},{"en":"Unlike young children, adults may not need an afternoon nap every day.","zh":"與年幼兒童不同，成人未必每天需要午睡。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast between two groups.","zh":"這個短語引入兩個群體之間的對比。"},{"en":"It helps show that the same behaviour can have different effects in different species.","zh":"它幫助顯示同一行為在不同物種中可能有不同效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"conserve energy","meaning":"保存能量；節省能量","examples":[{"en":"Small mammals may sleep partly to conserve energy.","zh":"小型哺乳動物睡眠可能部分是為了保存能量。"},{"en":"To conserve energy means to save energy and avoid wasting it.","zh":"保存能量或節省能量，是指保留能量並避免浪費。"},{"en":"People conserve energy at home by switching off unused lights.","zh":"人們在家關掉不用的燈來節省能量。"},{"en":"Animals may conserve energy by sleeping, staying warm and reducing movement.","zh":"動物可能透過睡眠、保持溫暖和減少活動來保存能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using less energy to survive or operate efficiently.","zh":"這個短語描述使用較少能量以生存或有效運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"show no decrease in","meaning":"沒有顯示……下降","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether humans show no decrease in metabolic rate when they sleep.","zh":"題目問人類睡覺時是否沒有顯示代謝率下降。"},{"en":"To show no decrease in something means not to show any reduction in it.","zh":"沒有顯示某事下降，是指沒有顯示它有任何減少。"},{"en":"A shop may show no decrease in sales even after raising prices.","zh":"商店即使加價後，銷售也可能沒有顯示下降。"},{"en":"If humans showed no decrease in metabolic rate, sleep would not save energy at all.","zh":"如果人類沒有顯示代謝率下降，睡眠就完全不會節省能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the absence of reduction.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"an alternation of","meaning":"……的交替","examples":[{"en":"Stage 3 includes an alternation of delta waves and smaller, faster waves.","zh":"第三階段包括 delta 波與較小、較快腦電波的交替。"},{"en":"An alternation of two things means they appear or happen one after the other.","zh":"兩件事的交替，是指它們一個接一個出現或發生。"},{"en":"A lesson may include an alternation of teacher explanation and student practice.","zh":"課堂可能包括老師講解與學生練習的交替。"},{"en":"Alternation shows that the pattern is mixed, not made of one thing only.","zh":"交替顯示模式是混合的，而不只由一種東西構成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes switching between two forms.","zh":"這個短語描述兩種形式之間的轉換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete the flow-chart below","meaning":"完成以下流程圖","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the flow-chart below using words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成以下流程圖。"},{"en":"To complete the flow-chart below means to fill in missing steps in the diagram under the question.","zh":"完成以下流程圖，是指填上題目下方圖表中缺失的步驟。"},{"en":"Students may complete a flow-chart to show the process of making tea or solving a problem.","zh":"學生可能完成流程圖，以顯示泡茶或解題的過程。"},{"en":"A flow-chart tests whether students understand sequence and cause-effect relationships.","zh":"流程圖測試學生是否理解順序和因果關係。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction for filling gaps in a process diagram.","zh":"這個短語是填寫過程圖空格的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個詞","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write no more than three words for each answer.","zh":"考生每個答案寫不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain one, two or three words only.","zh":"不多於三個詞，是指答案只能包含一個、兩個或三個英文詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “rapid eye movement,” it follows the rule because it has three words.","zh":"如果答案是 “rapid eye movement”，它符合規則，因為有三個詞。"},{"en":"Writing four words can make the answer wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫四個詞也可能令答案錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit in an exam.","zh":"這個短語在考試中給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the stages of sleep","meaning":"睡眠階段","examples":[{"en":"The flow-chart describes the stages of sleep.","zh":"流程圖描述睡眠階段。"},{"en":"The stages of sleep are the different phases people pass through while sleeping.","zh":"睡眠階段是人們睡覺時經過的不同階段。"},{"en":"A sleep chart may show light sleep, deep sleep and REM sleep as different stages.","zh":"睡眠圖表可能把淺睡、深層睡眠和快速眼動睡眠顯示為不同階段。"},{"en":"Understanding sleep stages helps explain why sleep changes during the night.","zh":"理解睡眠階段有助解釋睡眠為何在夜間變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the organised parts of the sleep cycle.","zh":"這個短語描述睡眠週期中有組織的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"drift in and out of consciousness","meaning":"半清醒半入睡","examples":[{"en":"In light sleep, the individual drifts in and out of consciousness.","zh":"在淺睡中，個人會半清醒半入睡。"},{"en":"To drift in and out of consciousness means to move gently between awareness and sleep.","zh":"半清醒半入睡，是指在有意識和睡眠之間輕輕來回。"},{"en":"A sick person may drift in and out of consciousness while resting in bed.","zh":"生病的人躺床休息時，可能半清醒半入睡。"},{"en":"During light sleep, small sounds may pull a person back into awareness.","zh":"在淺睡期間，小聲音可能把人拉回清醒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unstable state between waking and sleeping.","zh":"這個短語描述清醒與睡眠之間不穩定的狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be woken up easily","meaning":"容易被喚醒","examples":[{"en":"A person in light sleep can be woken up easily.","zh":"處於淺睡的人容易被喚醒。"},{"en":"To be woken up easily means to wake after a small disturbance.","zh":"容易被喚醒，是指受到小干擾就醒來。"},{"en":"A sleeping baby may be woken up easily by a ringing phone.","zh":"睡着的嬰兒可能容易被電話鈴聲喚醒。"},{"en":"Light sleep is easy to interrupt because it is not deep.","zh":"淺睡容易被打斷，因為它不是深層睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fragile sleep.","zh":"這個短語描述脆弱睡眠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reduced muscle activity","meaning":"肌肉活動減少","examples":[{"en":"Light sleep involves reduced muscle activity.","zh":"淺睡涉及肌肉活動減少。"},{"en":"Reduced muscle activity means the muscles move less than when a person is awake.","zh":"肌肉活動減少，是指肌肉比人清醒時活動較少。"},{"en":"When someone relaxes on a sofa, reduced muscle activity may make the body feel heavy.","zh":"當人躺在梳化上放鬆，肌肉活動減少可能令身體感到沉重。"},{"en":"Reduced movement helps the body enter sleep more fully.","zh":"活動減少幫助身體更充分進入睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lower physical activity.","zh":"這個短語描述身體活動較低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"tend to stop","meaning":"往往會停止","examples":[{"en":"In stage 2, all movement of the eyes tends to stop.","zh":"在第二階段，所有眼部活動往往會停止。"},{"en":"To tend to stop means to usually stop, though not necessarily every single time.","zh":"往往會停止，是指通常會停止，但不一定每次都絕對如此。"},{"en":"Students tend to stop talking when the teacher begins giving instructions.","zh":"當老師開始給指示，學生往往會停止說話。"},{"en":"Eye movement stopping is one sign that the sleeper has moved beyond stage 1.","zh":"眼部活動停止是睡眠者已超越第一階段的跡象之一。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a usual pattern, not an absolute rule.","zh":"這個短語描述通常模式，而不是絕對規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be dominated by","meaning":"由……主導","examples":[{"en":"Brain activity is dominated by delta waves in deeper sleep.","zh":"在更深睡眠中，大腦活動由 delta 波主導。"},{"en":"To be dominated by something means to be mainly controlled or filled by it.","zh":"由某事主導，是指主要被它控制或充滿。"},{"en":"A meeting may be dominated by one topic if everyone keeps discussing it.","zh":"如果每個人都不斷討論同一主題，會議可能由該主題主導。"},{"en":"When brain activity is dominated by delta waves, the sleep stage is very deep.","zh":"當大腦活動由 delta 波主導，睡眠階段非常深。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what is most common or powerful in a situation.","zh":"這個短語描述某情況中最常見或最有力的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a scattering of","meaning":"少量零星的……","examples":[{"en":"Delta waves may appear with a scattering of smaller, faster waves.","zh":"delta 波可能與少量零星的較小、較快腦電波一同出現。"},{"en":"A scattering of something means a small number spread among other things.","zh":"少量零星的某物，是指少量東西分散在其他東西之中。"},{"en":"A beach may have a scattering of shells across the sand.","zh":"沙灘上可能有少量零星貝殼散落在沙上。"},{"en":"In stage 3, smaller waves appear only here and there among delta waves.","zh":"在第三階段，較小腦電波只在 delta 波之間零星出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small, scattered amount.","zh":"這個短語描述少量而分散的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"in evidence","meaning":"可見；存在","examples":[{"en":"Smaller, faster waves are also in evidence during stage 3.","zh":"較小、較快腦電波在第三階段也可見。"},{"en":"In evidence means visible, present or clearly noticeable.","zh":"可見或存在，是指可以被看見、出現或清楚注意到。"},{"en":"Exam stress may be in evidence when students look tired and anxious.","zh":"當學生看起來疲倦和焦慮，考試壓力可能清楚可見。"},{"en":"If smaller waves are in evidence, they can be detected in the brain-wave pattern.","zh":"如果較小腦電波可見，代表它們能在腦電波模式中被偵測到。"},{"en":"This phrase means something can be seen or observed.","zh":"這個短語意思是某事能被看見或觀察到。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"emit delta waves","meaning":"發出 delta 波","examples":[{"en":"In stage 4, the brain emits delta waves almost exclusively.","zh":"在第四階段，大腦幾乎完全發出 delta 波。"},{"en":"To emit delta waves means to produce or give off delta brain-wave patterns.","zh":"發出 delta 波，是指產生或釋放 delta 腦電波模式。"},{"en":"A radio emits signals, and the brain emits electrical patterns that machines can record.","zh":"收音機發出訊號，而大腦發出機器可以記錄的電模式。"},{"en":"When the brain emits mostly delta waves, the sleeper is in deep sleep.","zh":"當大腦主要發出 delta 波，睡眠者處於深層睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the brain producing a particular wave pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述大腦產生特定波形模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a temporary state of paralysis","meaning":"暫時癱瘓狀態","examples":[{"en":"Limb muscles enter a temporary state of paralysis during REM sleep.","zh":"四肢肌肉在快速眼動睡眠期間進入暫時癱瘓狀態。"},{"en":"A temporary state of paralysis is a short period when muscles cannot move.","zh":"暫時癱瘓狀態，是肌肉在短時間內不能移動的狀態。"},{"en":"A person’s arm may feel temporarily paralysed after being slept on for too long.","zh":"如果手臂被壓着睡太久，可能感覺暫時麻痺。"},{"en":"During REM sleep, temporary paralysis helps prevent the body from acting out dreams.","zh":"在 REM 睡眠期間，暫時癱瘓幫助防止身體把夢境動作做出來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a short-term inability to move.","zh":"這個短語描述短時間無法移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the summary using words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill missing words into a shortened version of the text.","zh":"完成摘要，是指在文本的簡短版本中填入缺失字詞。"},{"en":"Students may complete a summary after reading a passage about sleep stages.","zh":"學生可能在閱讀有關睡眠階段的篇章後完成摘要。"},{"en":"Summary completion tests whether students understand the main ideas and key details.","zh":"摘要填空測試學生是否理解主旨和關鍵細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個詞","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose no more than two words from the passage.","zh":"考生從文章中選擇不多於兩個詞。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must contain one or two words only.","zh":"不多於兩個詞，是指答案只能包含一個或兩個英文詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “deep sleep,” it follows the instruction because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “deep sleep”，它符合指示，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Using three words may break the rule even if the meaning is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，使用三個詞也可能違反規則。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict answer-length limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格答案長度限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"so essential that","meaning":"如此重要以致","examples":[{"en":"Sleep is so essential that people can survive longer without food than without sleep.","zh":"睡眠如此重要，以致人們在沒有食物的情況下能比沒有睡眠存活更久。"},{"en":"So essential that means so necessary that it produces the result described after “that”.","zh":"如此重要以致，是指重要到會造成 that 後面描述的結果。"},{"en":"Water is so essential that people cannot survive long without it.","zh":"水如此重要，以致人不能長時間沒有它而生存。"},{"en":"This structure shows a strong cause-and-effect relationship.","zh":"這個結構顯示強烈因果關係。"},{"en":"It is useful when emphasising how important something is.","zh":"它適合強調某事有多重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"go longer without","meaning":"在沒有……的情況下維持更久","examples":[{"en":"A person can go longer without food than without sleep.","zh":"一個人在沒有食物的情況下能比沒有睡眠維持更久。"},{"en":"To go longer without something means to manage for more time without having it.","zh":"在沒有某物的情況下維持更久，是指缺少它時仍能撐更長時間。"},{"en":"A phone can go longer without charging if the screen brightness is low.","zh":"如果螢幕亮度低，手機在沒有充電的情況下可以維持更久。"},{"en":"If people cannot go long without sleep, sleep must be biologically important.","zh":"如果人不能長時間沒有睡眠，睡眠一定在生物上很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how long something can continue without a need being met.","zh":"這個短語比較某需要未被滿足時，某事能持續多久。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"do repair work on","meaning":"對……進行修復工作","examples":[{"en":"The brain can do repair work on neuronal connections during sleep.","zh":"大腦可以在睡眠期間對神經連接進行修復工作。"},{"en":"To do repair work on something means to fix damage or restore it to better condition.","zh":"對某事進行修復工作，是指修補損傷或令它恢復較好狀態。"},{"en":"A technician may do repair work on a school computer after it stops working.","zh":"技術員可能在學校電腦停止運作後對它進行修復工作。"},{"en":"If the brain repairs connections during sleep, sleep helps maintain mental function.","zh":"如果大腦在睡眠期間修復連接，睡眠就有助維持心智功能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active fixing or restoration.","zh":"這個短語描述主動修補或恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"in a state of inactivity","meaning":"處於不活動狀態","examples":[{"en":"Neuronal connections may deteriorate in a state of inactivity.","zh":"神經連接處於不活動狀態時可能退化。"},{"en":"In a state of inactivity means not being used, moved or stimulated.","zh":"處於不活動狀態，是指沒有被使用、移動或刺激。"},{"en":"Muscles can weaken in a state of inactivity if a person stays in bed for weeks.","zh":"如果人臥床數星期，肌肉處於不活動狀態可能會變弱。"},{"en":"Lack of activity can cause systems to become weaker over time.","zh":"缺乏活動會令系統隨時間變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a condition of not being active.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有活動的狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"during this rest period","meaning":"在這段休息期間","examples":[{"en":"During this rest period, metabolic rate and energy consumption drop.","zh":"在這段休息期間，代謝率和能量消耗下降。"},{"en":"During this rest period means while the body is resting in the period being discussed.","zh":"在這段休息期間，是指身體在所討論的時段中休息時。"},{"en":"During a school break, students may eat, stretch and recover before the next lesson.","zh":"在學校小休期間，學生可能進食、伸展並在下一堂前恢復。"},{"en":"Sleep is a rest period in which several body processes slow down.","zh":"睡眠是一段休息期間，其中幾個身體過程會減慢。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a period of rest already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語回指已提及的一段休息時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"have a much-needed rest","meaning":"得到非常需要的休息","examples":[{"en":"The cardiovascular system has a much-needed rest during sleep.","zh":"心血管系統在睡眠期間得到非常需要的休息。"},{"en":"To have a much-needed rest means to get rest that is clearly necessary.","zh":"得到非常需要的休息，是指得到明顯必要的休息。"},{"en":"After working double shifts, a nurse may finally have a much-needed rest.","zh":"連續上雙班後，護士可能終於得到非常需要的休息。"},{"en":"Sleep gives the heart and blood vessels a break after many hours of daytime activity.","zh":"睡眠讓心臟和血管在多小時日間活動後得到休息。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the rest is important and overdue.","zh":"這個短語強調休息很重要，而且早已需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"fall into torpor","meaning":"進入低代謝休眠狀態","examples":[{"en":"Humans do not fall into torpor during deep sleep.","zh":"人類在深層睡眠期間不會進入低代謝休眠狀態。"},{"en":"To fall into torpor means to enter a low-metabolism, low-activity state.","zh":"進入低代謝休眠狀態，是指進入低代謝、低活動狀態。"},{"en":"Some small animals may fall into torpor when nights become cold.","zh":"某些小動物在夜晚變冷時可能進入低代謝休眠狀態。"},{"en":"Humans may sleep deeply, but their bodies do not usually enter this extreme energy-saving state.","zh":"人類可能深睡，但身體通常不會進入這種極端節能狀態。"},{"en":"This phrase describes entering torpor, often naturally and gradually.","zh":"這個短語描述自然且逐步地進入 torpor。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a cycle of 24 hours","meaning":"二十四小時週期","examples":[{"en":"A cycle of 24 hours is known as a circadian rhythm.","zh":"二十四小時週期被稱為晝夜節律。"},{"en":"A cycle of 24 hours is a pattern that repeats roughly once each day.","zh":"二十四小時週期，是大約每天重複一次的模式。"},{"en":"Many people feel sleepy at night and alert in the morning because of a 24-hour cycle.","zh":"許多人晚上想睡、早上清醒，是因為二十四小時週期。"},{"en":"A stable 24-hour cycle helps the body organise sleep, hunger and energy.","zh":"穩定的二十四小時週期幫助身體安排睡眠、飢餓感和能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a daily repeating rhythm.","zh":"這個短語描述每日重複的節律。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the amount and type of sleep","meaning":"睡眠量和睡眠類型","examples":[{"en":"Circadian rhythm influences the amount and type of sleep a person gets.","zh":"晝夜節律影響一個人獲得的睡眠量和睡眠類型。"},{"en":"The amount and type of sleep means how much sleep a person gets and which stages of sleep occur.","zh":"睡眠量和睡眠類型，是指一個人睡多久，以及出現哪些睡眠階段。"},{"en":"A student may get enough hours but still lack deep sleep or REM sleep.","zh":"學生可能睡眠時數足夠，但仍缺乏深層睡眠或快速眼動睡眠。"},{"en":"Body rhythm can affect both sleep length and the balance of sleep stages.","zh":"身體節律可以同時影響睡眠長度和睡眠階段的平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quantity and sleep-stage pattern together.","zh":"這個短語同時描述數量和睡眠階段模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 83 - SLEEP.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 84":[{"front":"latchkey children","meaning":"鑰匙兒童","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the social problem of latchkey children.","zh":"文章討論鑰匙兒童這個社會問題。"},{"en":"Latchkey children are children who return home without an adult and use their own key to enter.","zh":"鑰匙兒童是指放學後沒有成人陪同，並用自己的鎖匙回家的孩子。"},{"en":"A latchkey child may come home from school, unlock the door, and wait alone until a parent returns.","zh":"鑰匙兒童可能放學回家後自行開門，然後獨自等待父母回來。"},{"en":"Latchkey children may feel independent, but they may also feel lonely or unsafe without supervision.","zh":"鑰匙兒童可能感到獨立，但在沒有監督下也可能感到孤單或不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a childcare situation, not simply a child who owns a key.","zh":"這個短語描述一種兒童照顧情況，而不只是指擁有鎖匙的孩子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the term was coined","meaning":"這個詞被創造出來","examples":[{"en":"The term “latchkey child” was coined to describe children who carried house keys.","zh":"“latchkey child” 這個詞被創造出來，用來描述帶家門匙的兒童。"},{"en":"The term was coined means the word or expression was newly created.","zh":"the term was coined 指某個字詞或表達被新創造出來。"},{"en":"The term “screen time” was coined to describe the time people spend looking at digital screens.","zh":"“screen time” 這個詞被創造出來，用來描述人們看數碼螢幕的時間。"},{"en":"A new term is often coined when society needs a name for a new problem or habit.","zh":"當社會需要為新問題或新習慣命名時，常會創造新詞。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the creation of a word, not the problem itself.","zh":"這個短語集中於詞語的創造，而不是問題本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"describe children who","meaning":"描述……的兒童","examples":[{"en":"The term was coined to describe children who returned home alone.","zh":"這個詞被創造出來，用來描述獨自回家的兒童。"},{"en":"To describe children who do something means to explain what kind of children they are by their behaviour or situation.","zh":"describe children who do something 指透過行為或處境說明某類兒童。"},{"en":"A teacher may describe children who read every day as independent learners.","zh":"老師可能把每天閱讀的兒童描述為獨立學習者。"},{"en":"Descriptions help people understand a group by giving clear features or examples.","zh":"描述透過提供清楚特徵或例子，幫助人理解某一群體。"},{"en":"This phrase usually introduces the type of children being discussed.","zh":"這個短語通常引出正在討論的是哪一類兒童。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"carry house keys to school","meaning":"帶家門匙上學","examples":[{"en":"Some children carried house keys to school.","zh":"有些兒童帶家門匙上學。"},{"en":"To carry house keys to school means to bring home keys to school so the child can enter the house later.","zh":"carry house keys to school 指把家門匙帶到學校，以便之後能進入家中。"},{"en":"A child may carry house keys to school if no adult will be home after class.","zh":"如果放學後沒有成人在家，孩子可能需要帶家門匙上學。"},{"en":"Carrying keys gives the child access to home, but it also shows that the child may be alone.","zh":"帶鎖匙讓孩子能進入家門，但也顯示孩子可能會獨自一人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical sign of being a latchkey child.","zh":"這個短語描述鑰匙兒童的一個實際跡象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"let themselves into","meaning":"自行進入……","examples":[{"en":"The children could let themselves into their home after school.","zh":"兒童放學後可以自行進入家中。"},{"en":"To let themselves into a place means to enter it by opening the door themselves.","zh":"let themselves into a place 指自己開門進入某地方。"},{"en":"A teenager may let herself into the flat if her parents are still at work.","zh":"如果父母仍在工作，青少年可能自行進入單位。"},{"en":"Children who let themselves in need to know how to lock the door safely afterwards.","zh":"自行進入家中的孩子需要知道之後如何安全鎖門。"},{"en":"This phrase shows independent entry without an adult opening the door.","zh":"這個短語顯示沒有成人開門下的獨立進入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"return from school","meaning":"放學回來","examples":[{"en":"They let themselves into their home when they returned from school.","zh":"他們放學回來時自行進入家中。"},{"en":"To return from school means to come back home after classes have ended.","zh":"return from school 指課堂結束後回家。"},{"en":"Many children return from school in the afternoon and look for a snack.","zh":"許多孩子下午放學回來後會找零食吃。"},{"en":"What happens when children return from school matters if no adult is there to supervise them.","zh":"如果沒有成人監督，孩子放學回來後發生甚麼就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the after-school period.","zh":"這個短語標示放學後的時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"come into use","meaning":"開始被使用","examples":[{"en":"The term came into use during the Second World War.","zh":"這個詞在第二次世界大戰期間開始被使用。"},{"en":"To come into use means to start being used by people.","zh":"come into use 指開始被人使用。"},{"en":"The phrase “online learning” came into use more widely when schools moved lessons onto the internet.","zh":"當學校把課堂搬到網上，“online learning” 這個短語開始更廣泛被使用。"},{"en":"Words often come into use when society changes and new situations need names.","zh":"當社會改變，新情況需要名稱時，詞語常會開始被使用。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on when a word, tool, or practice starts to be used.","zh":"這個短語集中於某個詞、工具或做法何時開始使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the Second World War","meaning":"第二次世界大戰","examples":[{"en":"The term came into use during the Second World War.","zh":"這個詞在第二次世界大戰期間開始被使用。"},{"en":"The Second World War was a major global war from 1939 to 1945.","zh":"Second World War 指1939年至1945年的一場重大世界戰爭。"},{"en":"During the Second World War, many families changed their daily routines because adults were working or fighting.","zh":"第二次世界大戰期間，許多家庭因成人工作或參戰而改變日常生活。"},{"en":"War can change family life because parents may be absent from home for long hours.","zh":"戰爭可以改變家庭生活，因為父母可能長時間不在家。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the historical background for the rise of latchkey children.","zh":"這個短語提供鑰匙兒童出現的歷史背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"go off to war","meaning":"從軍參戰；奔赴戰場","examples":[{"en":"Many fathers had gone off to war.","zh":"許多父親已從軍參戰。"},{"en":"To go off to war means to leave home in order to fight in a war.","zh":"go off to war 指離家去參與戰爭。"},{"en":"A father who goes off to war may be away from his family for months or years.","zh":"從軍參戰的父親可能離開家人數月甚至數年。"},{"en":"When many men go off to war, families and workplaces must adjust quickly.","zh":"當許多男性奔赴戰場，家庭和工作場所都必須迅速調整。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests separation from home because of military duty.","zh":"這個短語暗示因軍事責任而離家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"go into industry","meaning":"投身工業生產","examples":[{"en":"Many mothers had gone into industry during the war.","zh":"戰爭期間，許多母親投身工業生產。"},{"en":"To go into industry means to start working in factories or industrial production.","zh":"go into industry 指開始在工廠或工業生產中工作。"},{"en":"A student who studies engineering may later go into industry instead of academic research.","zh":"讀工程的學生日後可能投身工業，而不是做學術研究。"},{"en":"During wartime, women went into industry because factories needed workers.","zh":"戰時女性投身工業生產，因為工廠需要工人。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a move into practical production work.","zh":"這個短語顯示轉向實際生產工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"make tanks and planes","meaning":"製造坦克和飛機","examples":[{"en":"Mothers worked in factories making tanks and planes.","zh":"母親們在工廠製造坦克和飛機。"},{"en":"To make tanks and planes means to manufacture military vehicles and aircraft.","zh":"make tanks and planes 指製造軍用車輛和飛機。"},{"en":"A wartime factory may make tanks and planes instead of ordinary cars.","zh":"戰時工廠可能製造坦克和飛機，而不是普通汽車。"},{"en":"When factories make war equipment, workers may need to work long shifts.","zh":"當工廠製造戰爭裝備，工人可能需要長時間輪班工作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the industrial work connected with the war effort.","zh":"這個短語顯示與戰時支援工作相關的工業工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"soldiers needed","meaning":"士兵所需要的","examples":[{"en":"Factories produced the uniforms and bullets that soldiers needed.","zh":"工廠生產士兵所需要的制服和子彈。"},{"en":"Soldiers needed means required by soldiers in order to fight or serve.","zh":"soldiers needed 指士兵為作戰或服役所需要的東西。"},{"en":"Soldiers needed warm clothing, food, medicine, and equipment during winter campaigns.","zh":"士兵在冬季戰役中需要保暖衣物、食物、藥物和裝備。"},{"en":"When soldiers need supplies, civilians may work in factories to produce them.","zh":"當士兵需要補給，平民可能在工廠生產它們。"},{"en":"This phrase connects military needs with production at home.","zh":"這個短語把軍事需要與後方生產連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on chains","meaning":"掛在鏈子上","examples":[{"en":"Some children wore keys on chains around their necks.","zh":"有些兒童把鎖匙掛在頸上的鏈子上。"},{"en":"On chains means attached to metal chains so the item can be worn or carried safely.","zh":"on chains 指固定在金屬鏈上，以便安全佩戴或攜帶。"},{"en":"A nurse may keep an ID card on a chain around her neck.","zh":"護士可能把職員證掛在頸上的鏈子上。"},{"en":"Children wore keys on chains so they would not easily lose them.","zh":"兒童把鎖匙掛在鏈子上，這樣較不容易遺失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how small objects are carried visibly and securely.","zh":"這個短語描述小物件如何被可見且安全地攜帶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a piece of string","meaning":"一條繩子","examples":[{"en":"Some children carried keys on a piece of string.","zh":"有些兒童用一條繩子帶着鎖匙。"},{"en":"A piece of string is a short length of thin cord or thread.","zh":"a piece of string 指一小段幼繩或線。"},{"en":"A child may tie a name tag to a schoolbag with a piece of string.","zh":"孩子可能用一條繩子把名牌綁在書包上。"},{"en":"String is used when people need a simple, cheap way to attach something.","zh":"當人們需要簡單便宜的方法固定物件時，會使用繩子。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a plain and practical object, not a formal chain.","zh":"這個短語顯示普通實用物件，而不是正式鏈子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tied around their necks","meaning":"綁在他們頸上","examples":[{"en":"The keys were tied around their necks.","zh":"鎖匙被綁在他們頸上。"},{"en":"Tied around their necks means fastened with string or a chain so the object hangs from the neck.","zh":"tied around their necks 指用繩子或鏈子固定，使物件掛在頸上。"},{"en":"A small whistle may be tied around a child’s neck during a school trip.","zh":"學校旅行時，小哨子可能被綁在孩子頸上。"},{"en":"Parents may tie important items this way so children do not lose them.","zh":"父母可能用這種方法綁住重要物件，以免孩子遺失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a way of carrying something safely on the body.","zh":"這個短語描述把物件安全帶在身上的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"work the night shift","meaning":"上夜班","examples":[{"en":"Some mothers chose to work the night shift.","zh":"有些母親選擇上夜班。"},{"en":"To work the night shift means to work during the night instead of the day.","zh":"work the night shift 指在夜間而不是日間工作。"},{"en":"Nurses, security guards, and factory workers may work the night shift.","zh":"護士、保安和工廠工人都可能上夜班。"},{"en":"Parents who work the night shift may sleep during the day and miss evening family time.","zh":"上夜班的父母可能日間睡覺，並錯過晚上的家庭時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a work schedule that can affect childcare.","zh":"這個短語描述一種會影響兒童照顧的工作時間表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"swing shift","meaning":"晚班；夜班","examples":[{"en":"The night shift was called the “swing shift”.","zh":"夜班被稱為 “swing shift”。"},{"en":"Swing shift means a work shift that usually falls between the day shift and the night shift, or refers to evening work in some contexts.","zh":"swing shift 通常指介乎日班和夜班之間的工作時段，在某些語境中也可指晚班。"},{"en":"A factory may use a swing shift when machines need to operate for many hours a day.","zh":"當工廠機器需要每天運作很長時間，工廠可能安排晚班。"},{"en":"Shift work can make family routines harder because parents work at unusual times.","zh":"輪班工作會令家庭常規更困難，因為父母在非正常時間工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is connected with factory schedules and non-standard working hours.","zh":"這個短語與工廠時間表和非標準工作時間有關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tuck someone into bed","meaning":"安頓某人上床睡覺","examples":[{"en":"Some mothers tucked their children into bed before going to work.","zh":"有些母親在上班前安頓孩子上床睡覺。"},{"en":"To tuck someone into bed means to help them settle comfortably in bed, often by covering them with blankets.","zh":"tuck someone into bed 指幫某人舒服地躺好，通常替他蓋好被子。"},{"en":"A parent may tuck a child into bed after reading a bedtime story.","zh":"父母可能讀完睡前故事後安頓孩子上床睡覺。"},{"en":"Tucking a child into bed can make them feel safe before the parent leaves.","zh":"安頓孩子上床可以讓孩子在父母離開前感到安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a caring bedtime action.","zh":"這個短語描述一個照顧性的睡前動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lock the door","meaning":"鎖門","examples":[{"en":"The mothers locked the door and went to the factory.","zh":"母親們鎖門後去工廠上班。"},{"en":"To lock the door means to close it securely with a key or lock.","zh":"lock the door 指用鎖匙或門鎖把門安全關上。"},{"en":"A student should lock the door before leaving home if no one else is inside.","zh":"如果家中沒有人，學生離家前應該鎖門。"},{"en":"Locking the door can protect the home, but it can also leave children alone inside.","zh":"鎖門可以保護家居，但也可能令孩子獨自留在屋內。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a basic safety action.","zh":"這個短語描述基本安全行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"go to the factory","meaning":"去工廠上班","examples":[{"en":"Some mothers went to the factory after putting their children to bed.","zh":"有些母親把孩子安頓上床後去工廠上班。"},{"en":"To go to the factory means to leave for work at an industrial workplace.","zh":"go to the factory 指前往工業工作場所上班。"},{"en":"A worker may go to the factory before sunrise if the early shift begins at six.","zh":"如果早班六點開始，工人可能日出前就去工廠上班。"},{"en":"When parents go to the factory at night, children may be left without direct care.","zh":"當父母晚上去工廠，孩子可能缺乏直接照顧。"},{"en":"This phrase connects work outside the home with childcare issues.","zh":"這個短語把外出工作與兒童照顧問題連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the country’s response","meaning":"國家的回應","examples":[{"en":"The country’s response was prompt and comprehensive.","zh":"國家的回應迅速而全面。"},{"en":"The country’s response means the actions taken by the nation, government, or society to deal with a problem.","zh":"country’s response 指國家、政府或社會為處理問題而採取的行動。"},{"en":"A country’s response to a typhoon may include shelters, food, and rescue teams.","zh":"國家對颱風的回應可能包括避難所、食物和救援隊。"},{"en":"A strong response can reduce harm when a social problem appears.","zh":"當社會問題出現，強而有力的回應可以減少傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collective action, not one family’s decision.","zh":"這個短語描述集體行動，而不是單一家庭的決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prompt and comprehensive","meaning":"迅速而全面","examples":[{"en":"The response to the problem was prompt and comprehensive.","zh":"對這個問題的回應迅速而全面。"},{"en":"Prompt and comprehensive means quick and covering many necessary parts.","zh":"prompt and comprehensive 指快速，而且涵蓋許多必要部分。"},{"en":"A school’s response to bullying is prompt and comprehensive if it protects the victim, investigates the case, and educates students.","zh":"如果學校保護受害者、調查事件並教育學生，對欺凌的回應就是迅速而全面。"},{"en":"Quick action prevents delay, while comprehensive action prevents gaps.","zh":"快速行動避免延誤，全面行動避免漏洞。"},{"en":"This phrase praises a response that is both fast and complete.","zh":"這個短語讚揚既快又完整的回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"programmes were set up","meaning":"計劃被設立","examples":[{"en":"Programmes were set up to care for children during the war.","zh":"戰爭期間設立了照顧兒童的計劃。"},{"en":"Programmes were set up means organised plans or services were created.","zh":"programmes were set up 指有組織的計劃或服務被創立。"},{"en":"After many students struggled with homework, support classes were set up after school.","zh":"當許多學生在功課上有困難，學校設立了課後支援班。"},{"en":"Programmes are often set up when a problem affects many people.","zh":"當問題影響許多人，計劃常會被設立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating organised help.","zh":"這個短語描述建立有組織的幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"community centres","meaning":"社區中心","examples":[{"en":"Programmes were organised in schools, factories, and community centres.","zh":"計劃在學校、工廠和社區中心組織。"},{"en":"Community centres are local places where people can join activities, classes, or support services.","zh":"community centres 指本地居民可參加活動、課程或支援服務的地方。"},{"en":"A community centre may offer homework help, sports clubs, and elderly services.","zh":"社區中心可能提供功課輔導、運動班和長者服務。"},{"en":"Community centres can support families when parents are busy or working long hours.","zh":"當父母忙碌或長時間工作，社區中心可以支援家庭。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to shared local spaces for public support.","zh":"這個短語指供公眾支援使用的本地共享空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"care for children","meaning":"照顧兒童","examples":[{"en":"The programmes were designed to care for children whose parents were busy.","zh":"這些計劃是為照顧父母忙碌的兒童而設計的。"},{"en":"To care for children means to look after their safety, needs, and daily activities.","zh":"care for children 指照顧兒童的安全、需要和日常活動。"},{"en":"A babysitter cares for children by preparing food, checking homework, and keeping them safe.","zh":"保姆透過準備食物、檢查功課和確保安全來照顧兒童。"},{"en":"Good childcare helps children avoid danger and loneliness when parents are away.","zh":"良好兒童照顧幫助孩子在父母不在時避免危險和孤單。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical protection and attention given to children.","zh":"這個短語描述給予兒童的實際保護和關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"whose parents were busy","meaning":"其父母忙於……的","examples":[{"en":"The programmes helped children whose parents were busy with the war effort.","zh":"這些計劃幫助父母忙於戰爭工作的兒童。"},{"en":"Whose parents were busy means the children’s parents did not have enough time because of work or duties.","zh":"whose parents were busy 指兒童的父母因工作或責任而沒有足夠時間。"},{"en":"After-school clubs help children whose parents are busy until evening.","zh":"課後活動幫助父母忙到晚上的孩子。"},{"en":"When parents are busy, children may need other adults or programmes for support.","zh":"當父母忙碌，孩子可能需要其他成人或計劃提供支援。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies children by their parents’ situation.","zh":"這個短語按父母情況辨認兒童。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the war effort","meaning":"戰爭工作；戰時支援工作","examples":[{"en":"Many parents were busy with the war effort.","zh":"許多父母忙於戰爭工作。"},{"en":"The war effort means the work done by a country’s people to support a war.","zh":"war effort 指一個國家的人民為支援戰爭而做的工作。"},{"en":"During a war, factory work, nursing, fundraising, and food rationing can all be part of the war effort.","zh":"戰爭期間，工廠工作、護理、籌款和食物配給都可以是戰時支援工作的一部分。"},{"en":"When adults join the war effort, family routines may change sharply.","zh":"當成人參與戰爭工作，家庭常規可能急劇改變。"},{"en":"This phrase connects civilian work with military needs.","zh":"這個短語把平民工作與軍事需要連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"close promptly","meaning":"迅速關閉","examples":[{"en":"These programmes closed promptly when the war ended.","zh":"戰爭結束時，這些計劃迅速關閉。"},{"en":"To close promptly means to shut down quickly and without delay.","zh":"close promptly 指快速而不拖延地關閉。"},{"en":"A temporary shelter may close promptly after the storm danger has passed.","zh":"風暴危險過後，臨時庇護中心可能迅速關閉。"},{"en":"Programmes that close too quickly can leave families without support.","zh":"計劃太快關閉可能令家庭失去支援。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something ended soon after the need seemed to disappear.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事在需求看似消失後很快結束。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"when the war ended","meaning":"戰爭結束時","examples":[{"en":"The childcare programmes closed when the war ended.","zh":"戰爭結束時，兒童照顧計劃關閉了。"},{"en":"When the war ended means at the time the war came to a finish.","zh":"when the war ended 指戰爭完結的時候。"},{"en":"When the school term ended, many temporary study groups stopped meeting.","zh":"學期結束時，許多臨時溫習小組停止聚會。"},{"en":"Major endings often change what services people think are necessary.","zh":"重大結束常改變人們認為哪些服務仍然必要。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the point when wartime conditions stopped.","zh":"這個短語標示戰時狀況停止的時間點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"resume their roles as","meaning":"恢復……的角色","examples":[{"en":"Women resumed their roles as housewives after the war.","zh":"戰後，女性恢復家庭主婦的角色。"},{"en":"To resume their roles as something means to return to a previous social or family role.","zh":"resume their roles as something 指回到以前的社會或家庭角色。"},{"en":"After a business trip, a parent may resume her role as the main caregiver at home.","zh":"出差後，家長可能恢復在家中作為主要照顧者的角色。"},{"en":"When people resume old roles, society may expect routines to return to normal.","zh":"當人們恢復舊角色，社會可能期待日常生活回復正常。"},{"en":"This phrase describes going back to a role held before.","zh":"這個短語描述回到過去擔任的角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"housewives","meaning":"家庭主婦","examples":[{"en":"Many women resumed their roles as housewives.","zh":"許多女性恢復家庭主婦的角色。"},{"en":"Housewives are women whose main work is managing the home and family rather than paid employment outside.","zh":"housewives 指主要負責管理家庭和家人，而不是在外受薪工作的女性。"},{"en":"A housewife may cook meals, clean the home, manage shopping, and care for children.","zh":"家庭主婦可能煮飯、清潔家居、安排購物和照顧孩子。"},{"en":"The role of housewives can change when economic pressure or war changes family needs.","zh":"當經濟壓力或戰爭改變家庭需要，家庭主婦的角色也可能改變。"},{"en":"This word describes a domestic role, not a lack of work.","zh":"這個字描述家庭角色，而不是沒有工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"more than sixty years on","meaning":"六十多年後","examples":[{"en":"More than sixty years on, many mothers are working again.","zh":"六十多年後，許多母親再次工作。"},{"en":"More than sixty years on means over sixty years later.","zh":"more than sixty years on 指六十多年之後。"},{"en":"More than ten years on, the old school project is still remembered by students.","zh":"十多年後，那個舊學校項目仍被學生記住。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a later time with an earlier historical moment.","zh":"這個短語把較後時間與較早歷史時刻比較。"},{"en":"It helps show that a similar issue has returned after many years.","zh":"它有助顯示相似問題多年後再次出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"large numbers of","meaning":"大量","examples":[{"en":"There are large numbers of working mothers today.","zh":"今日有大量在職母親。"},{"en":"Large numbers of something means many of them.","zh":"large numbers of something 指數量很多。"},{"en":"Large numbers of students use public transport to get to school.","zh":"大量學生使用公共交通上學。"},{"en":"When large numbers of parents work, childcare becomes a wider social issue.","zh":"當大量父母工作，兒童照顧就成為更廣泛的社會問題。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses quantity and scale.","zh":"這個短語強調數量和規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"working mothers","meaning":"在職母親","examples":[{"en":"There are large numbers of working mothers in modern society.","zh":"現代社會有大量在職母親。"},{"en":"Working mothers are mothers who have paid jobs while also raising children.","zh":"working mothers 指一邊受薪工作、一邊撫養孩子的母親。"},{"en":"A working mother may finish office work and then help her child with homework at night.","zh":"在職母親可能下班後晚上還要幫孩子做功課。"},{"en":"Working mothers may need childcare support when school ends before their workday does.","zh":"當學校放學時間早於工作結束時間，在職母親可能需要兒童照顧支援。"},{"en":"This phrase connects employment with parenting responsibilities.","zh":"這個短語把就業與育兒責任連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"unlike in wartime","meaning":"不像戰時","examples":[{"en":"Unlike in wartime, the country is not organised to care for their children.","zh":"不像戰時，國家沒有有系統地安排照顧她們的孩子。"},{"en":"Unlike in wartime means different from the situation during war.","zh":"unlike in wartime 指與戰爭期間的情況不同。"},{"en":"Unlike in exam season, the school library closes early during holidays.","zh":"不像考試季，學校圖書館在假期會提早關門。"},{"en":"This phrase sets up a contrast between two time periods or situations.","zh":"這個短語建立兩個時期或情況之間的對比。"},{"en":"It shows that today’s support system is different from the wartime one.","zh":"它顯示今日支援制度與戰時制度不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be organised to","meaning":"有系統地安排去","examples":[{"en":"The country is not organised to care for the children of working mothers.","zh":"國家沒有有系統地安排去照顧在職母親的孩子。"},{"en":"To be organised to do something means to have systems, people, and plans arranged for that purpose.","zh":"be organised to do something 指為某目的安排好制度、人員和計劃。"},{"en":"A school is organised to handle emergencies if it has drills, staff roles, and clear exits.","zh":"如果學校有演習、人員分工和清楚出口，就是有系統地安排去處理緊急情況。"},{"en":"Without organisation, many families may face the same problem alone.","zh":"沒有組織安排，許多家庭可能要獨自面對同一問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planned collective support.","zh":"這個短語描述有計劃的集體支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"finding young children at home","meaning":"發現年幼兒童在家","examples":[{"en":"Finding young children at home without supervision has become common.","zh":"發現年幼兒童在家而沒有監督已變得常見。"},{"en":"Finding young children at home means discovering or seeing children at home in a particular situation.","zh":"finding young children at home 指發現或看見兒童處於家中某種情況。"},{"en":"A neighbour may be worried after finding young children at home alone after school.","zh":"鄰居在放學後發現年幼兒童獨自在家，可能會擔心。"},{"en":"This situation becomes a social concern when it happens regularly in many families.","zh":"當這種情況在許多家庭定期發生，它就成為社會關注。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the observation that children are present at home without adults.","zh":"這個短語集中於觀察到兒童在沒有成人下留在家中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"without adult supervision","meaning":"沒有成人監督","examples":[{"en":"Young children are often at home without adult supervision.","zh":"年幼兒童經常在沒有成人監督下留在家中。"},{"en":"Without adult supervision means no responsible adult is watching, guiding, or protecting the child.","zh":"without adult supervision 指沒有負責任成人看顧、指導或保護孩子。"},{"en":"Children should not use a gas stove without adult supervision.","zh":"兒童不應在沒有成人監督下使用煤氣爐。"},{"en":"Without supervision, small problems can quickly become dangerous.","zh":"沒有監督時，小問題可能很快變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the absence of adult care or monitoring.","zh":"這個短語突出成人照顧或監察的缺席。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"much too commonplace","meaning":"太過常見","examples":[{"en":"This problem has become much too commonplace.","zh":"這個問題已變得太過常見。"},{"en":"Much too commonplace means far too common and no longer rare enough to ignore.","zh":"much too commonplace 指太普遍，已不再罕見到可以忽視。"},{"en":"Online scams have become much too commonplace among elderly phone users.","zh":"網上騙案在長者手機用戶之間已變得太過常見。"},{"en":"When a problem becomes commonplace, people may wrongly stop feeling shocked by it.","zh":"當問題變得常見，人們可能錯誤地不再感到震驚。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises a situation for happening too often.","zh":"這個短語批評某情況發生得太頻繁。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"among the lower classes","meaning":"在下層階級之中","examples":[{"en":"Latchkey children were once found only among the lower classes.","zh":"鑰匙兒童曾經只出現在下層階級之中。"},{"en":"Among the lower classes means within poorer or less socially advantaged groups.","zh":"among the lower classes 指在較貧窮或社會優勢較少的群體中。"},{"en":"A social problem may first appear among the lower classes because they have fewer resources.","zh":"社會問題可能先在下層階級出現，因為他們資源較少。"},{"en":"Class-based patterns can change when the same pressure spreads to richer families.","zh":"當相同壓力蔓延到較富裕家庭，階級模式可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where a social issue was once concentrated.","zh":"這個短語描述某社會問題曾經集中出現的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"gradually spread to","meaning":"逐漸蔓延至","examples":[{"en":"The situation has gradually spread to the middle and upper classes.","zh":"這種情況已逐漸蔓延至中上階層。"},{"en":"To gradually spread to a group means to slowly begin affecting that group too.","zh":"gradually spread to a group 指慢慢開始也影響某群體。"},{"en":"A new fashion may gradually spread from teenagers to adults.","zh":"新潮流可能從青少年逐漸蔓延至成年人。"},{"en":"Social problems spread when the causes become common across society.","zh":"當成因在社會各處變得普遍，社會問題就會蔓延。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow expansion from one group to another.","zh":"這個短語描述從一個群體到另一個群體的緩慢擴展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"middle and upper classes","meaning":"中上階層","examples":[{"en":"Latchkey children are now found in the middle and upper classes.","zh":"鑰匙兒童現在也出現在中上階層。"},{"en":"Middle and upper classes are social groups with moderate to high income, education, or social status.","zh":"middle and upper classes 指收入、教育或社會地位中等至較高的社會群體。"},{"en":"A problem in the middle and upper classes may be less visible because families have more privacy.","zh":"中上階層中的問題可能較不明顯，因為家庭有更多私隱。"},{"en":"When a problem reaches these classes, it shows the issue is not limited to poverty.","zh":"當問題到達這些階層，便顯示議題不限於貧窮。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies more socially or economically advantaged groups.","zh":"這個短語辨認社會或經濟上較有優勢的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the same is true of","meaning":"……也是如此","examples":[{"en":"The same is true of adolescent violence.","zh":"青少年暴力也是如此。"},{"en":"The same is true of something means the same pattern or point applies to that thing too.","zh":"the same is true of something 指相同模式或觀點也適用於某事。"},{"en":"Many adults need enough sleep; the same is true of teenagers.","zh":"許多成人需要足夠睡眠；青少年也是如此。"},{"en":"This phrase links one example to another with a shared pattern.","zh":"這個短語把一個例子與另一個有共同模式的例子連起來。"},{"en":"It helps writers avoid repeating a full explanation.","zh":"它幫助作者避免重複完整解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"adolescent violence","meaning":"青少年暴力","examples":[{"en":"Adolescent violence has spread across society.","zh":"青少年暴力已蔓延至整個社會。"},{"en":"Adolescent violence means violent behaviour by teenagers or young people.","zh":"adolescent violence 指青少年或年輕人的暴力行為。"},{"en":"School fights, gang attacks, and serious threats may be forms of adolescent violence.","zh":"校園打鬥、幫派襲擊和嚴重威脅都可能是青少年暴力形式。"},{"en":"Adolescent violence can grow when young people feel angry, isolated, or unsupervised.","zh":"當年輕人感到憤怒、孤立或無人監督，青少年暴力可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on violence during the teenage years.","zh":"這個短語集中於青少年時期的暴力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"shootings and stabbings","meaning":"槍擊和刺傷事件","examples":[{"en":"Shootings and stabbings were once associated mainly with poor areas.","zh":"槍擊和刺傷事件曾經主要與貧困地區有關。"},{"en":"Shootings and stabbings are violent incidents involving guns or knives.","zh":"shootings and stabbings 指涉及槍械或刀具的暴力事件。"},{"en":"A news report about shootings and stabbings usually suggests serious public safety problems.","zh":"關於槍擊和刺傷事件的新聞報道通常暗示嚴重公共安全問題。"},{"en":"Such violence creates fear because it can cause severe injury or death.","zh":"這類暴力令人恐懼，因為它可造成重傷或死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to extreme physical violence.","zh":"這個短語指極端身體暴力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be associated primarily with","meaning":"主要與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Violence was associated primarily with inner-city areas.","zh":"暴力主要與市中心貧困地區有關。"},{"en":"To be associated primarily with something means to be mainly linked with it.","zh":"be associated primarily with something 指主要與某事相連。"},{"en":"Exam stress is associated primarily with older students, although younger students can feel it too.","zh":"考試壓力主要與較年長學生有關，雖然年幼學生也可能感受到。"},{"en":"When a problem spreads, it may no longer be associated primarily with one group.","zh":"當問題蔓延，它可能不再主要與一個群體有關。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main connection people make.","zh":"這個短語指出人們作出的主要聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"inner-city areas","meaning":"市中心貧困地區","examples":[{"en":"Teen violence was once linked to inner-city areas.","zh":"青少年暴力曾經與市中心貧困地區有關。"},{"en":"Inner-city areas are older central urban districts, often with poverty or social problems in this context.","zh":"inner-city areas 在此語境中指較舊的城市中心區，常伴隨貧窮或社會問題。"},{"en":"Some inner-city areas have crowded housing and fewer safe spaces for young people.","zh":"有些市中心貧困地區住房擠迫，且給年輕人的安全空間較少。"},{"en":"Social problems in these areas may grow when schools, families, and services are under pressure.","zh":"當學校、家庭和服務承受壓力，這些地區的社會問題可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to central city districts, not simply any city area.","zh":"這個短語指城市中心區，而不只是任何城市地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"poverty-stricken areas","meaning":"貧困地區","examples":[{"en":"Violence was once associated with poverty-stricken areas.","zh":"暴力曾經與貧困地區有關。"},{"en":"Poverty-stricken areas are places where many people are very poor.","zh":"poverty-stricken areas 指許多人非常貧窮的地方。"},{"en":"A poverty-stricken area may lack safe housing, good schools, and enough public services.","zh":"貧困地區可能缺乏安全住房、良好學校和足夠公共服務。"},{"en":"Poverty can increase stress and reduce support, but it does not explain every social problem.","zh":"貧窮可以增加壓力並減少支援，但不能解釋每一個社會問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severe economic hardship in a place.","zh":"這個短語描述某地嚴重經濟困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be permeated with","meaning":"充斥着","examples":[{"en":"Some areas were permeated with abusive families and neglectful schools.","zh":"有些地區充斥着施虐家庭和疏於照顧學生的學校。"},{"en":"To be permeated with something means to be filled with it throughout.","zh":"be permeated with something 指到處充滿某事物。"},{"en":"A workplace may be permeated with fear if staff are constantly criticised.","zh":"如果員工不斷被批評，工作場所可能充斥着恐懼。"},{"en":"When a community is permeated with neglect, children may see harmful behaviour as normal.","zh":"當社區充斥忽視，孩子可能把有害行為視為正常。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a problem is widespread and deeply present.","zh":"這個短語暗示問題廣泛且深入存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"abusive families","meaning":"施虐家庭","examples":[{"en":"Some children grow up in abusive families.","zh":"有些兒童在施虐家庭中長大。"},{"en":"Abusive families are families where members are harmed physically, emotionally, or verbally.","zh":"abusive families 指家庭成員在身體、情緒或言語上受到傷害的家庭。"},{"en":"A child in an abusive family may feel afraid to speak honestly at home.","zh":"生活在施虐家庭的孩子可能害怕在家中誠實說話。"},{"en":"Abuse can damage a child’s trust, confidence, and emotional control.","zh":"虐待可以傷害孩子的信任、自信和情緒控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harmful family environments, not ordinary family conflict.","zh":"這個短語描述有害家庭環境，而不是普通家庭衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"neglectful schools","meaning":"疏於照顧學生的學校","examples":[{"en":"Violence was linked to abusive families and neglectful schools.","zh":"暴力與施虐家庭和疏於照顧學生的學校有關。"},{"en":"Neglectful schools are schools that fail to give students enough care, guidance, or protection.","zh":"neglectful schools 指未能給學生足夠照顧、指導或保護的學校。"},{"en":"A neglectful school may ignore bullying complaints until students stop feeling safe.","zh":"疏於照顧學生的學校可能忽視欺凌投訴，直到學生不再感到安全。"},{"en":"When schools neglect students, problems at home may become worse.","zh":"當學校忽視學生，家庭問題可能變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes institutional failure to care for children.","zh":"這個短語描述機構未能照顧兒童。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in recent times","meaning":"近年來","examples":[{"en":"In recent times, teen violence has penetrated every economic level.","zh":"近年來，青少年暴力已滲透到各個經濟階層。"},{"en":"In recent times means in the period close to the present.","zh":"in recent times 指接近現在的一段時期。"},{"en":"In recent times, many students have used online tools to study vocabulary.","zh":"近年來，許多學生使用網上工具學習詞彙。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts modern developments with older patterns.","zh":"這個短語把現代發展與舊有模式作對比。"},{"en":"It helps show that a situation has changed lately.","zh":"它有助顯示情況最近已改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"teen violence epidemic","meaning":"青少年暴力問題蔓延","examples":[{"en":"The teen violence epidemic has affected many parts of society.","zh":"青少年暴力問題蔓延已影響社會許多部分。"},{"en":"A teen violence epidemic means teen violence has become widespread like a serious social outbreak.","zh":"teen violence epidemic 指青少年暴力像嚴重社會爆發一樣廣泛出現。"},{"en":"A school district may worry about a teen violence epidemic if fights and weapon incidents rise sharply.","zh":"如果打鬥和武器事件急升，學區可能擔心青少年暴力問題蔓延。"},{"en":"Calling it an epidemic suggests the problem is spreading and needs urgent attention.","zh":"把它稱為 epidemic 暗示問題正在擴散，需要緊急關注。"},{"en":"This phrase is metaphorical; violence is not a disease, but it spreads socially.","zh":"這個短語是比喻；暴力不是疾病，但會在社會中擴散。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"penetrate society","meaning":"滲透社會","examples":[{"en":"The epidemic has penetrated society at every economic level.","zh":"這個問題已在各個經濟階層滲透社會。"},{"en":"To penetrate society means to spread deeply into many parts of society.","zh":"penetrate society 指深入蔓延至社會許多部分。"},{"en":"Smartphone use has penetrated society so deeply that even small shops use mobile payment.","zh":"智能手機使用已深深滲透社會，以致小店也使用手機支付。"},{"en":"When a problem penetrates society, it is no longer limited to one group.","zh":"當問題滲透社會，它就不再限於某一群體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep and widespread entry into social life.","zh":"這個短語描述深入且廣泛進入社會生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at every economic level","meaning":"在各個經濟階層","examples":[{"en":"Teen violence now appears at every economic level.","zh":"青少年暴力現在出現在各個經濟階層。"},{"en":"At every economic level means among poor, middle-income, and wealthy groups alike.","zh":"at every economic level 指在貧窮、中等收入和富裕群體中都存在。"},{"en":"Stress can affect students at every economic level, though the causes may differ.","zh":"壓力可以影響各個經濟階層的學生，雖然原因可能不同。"},{"en":"A problem found at every level cannot be explained only by poverty.","zh":"如果問題出現在各個階層，就不能只用貧窮來解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that all income groups are involved.","zh":"這個短語強調所有收入群體都涉及其中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"an increase in","meaning":"……的增加","examples":[{"en":"An increase in working mothers has contributed to the problem.","zh":"在職母親的增加促成了這個問題。"},{"en":"An increase in something means there is more of it than before.","zh":"an increase in something 指某事物比以前更多。"},{"en":"An increase in homework may leave students with less time to sleep.","zh":"功課增加可能令學生睡眠時間減少。"},{"en":"When working mothers increase, demand for childcare may also increase.","zh":"當在職母親增加，兒童照顧需求也可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a rising factor.","zh":"這個短語引出正在上升的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"single-parent families","meaning":"單親家庭","examples":[{"en":"Single-parent families are one factor behind the rise of latchkey children.","zh":"單親家庭是鑰匙兒童增加背後的一個因素。"},{"en":"Single-parent families are families where one parent raises the child or children.","zh":"single-parent families 指由一位父母撫養孩子的家庭。"},{"en":"A single-parent family may depend on one adult’s income and schedule.","zh":"單親家庭可能依賴一名成人的收入和時間表。"},{"en":"If the only parent works long hours, children may spend more time alone.","zh":"如果唯一照顧者長時間工作，孩子可能更多時間獨處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes family structure, not parenting quality.","zh":"這個短語描述家庭結構，而不是育兒質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"extended families","meaning":"大家庭","examples":[{"en":"Extended families once helped with childcare.","zh":"大家庭曾經幫忙照顧兒童。"},{"en":"Extended families include relatives beyond parents and children, such as grandparents, aunts, uncles, and cousins.","zh":"extended families 指父母和子女以外的親屬，包括祖父母、叔伯姨舅和表兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"In an extended family, a grandmother may collect children from school while parents work.","zh":"在大家庭中，祖母可能在父母工作時接孩子放學。"},{"en":"When extended families live far apart, parents may lose informal childcare support.","zh":"當大家庭成員住得很遠，父母可能失去非正式照顧支援。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts wider family networks with the nuclear family.","zh":"這個短語把更廣泛家庭網絡與核心家庭作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"help with childcare","meaning":"幫忙照顧兒童","examples":[{"en":"Extended families used to help with childcare.","zh":"大家庭過去會幫忙照顧兒童。"},{"en":"To help with childcare means to assist in looking after children.","zh":"help with childcare 指協助照顧孩子。"},{"en":"A neighbour may help with childcare by watching a child until the parent returns from work.","zh":"鄰居可能幫忙照顧兒童，看顧孩子直到父母下班回來。"},{"en":"Childcare support reduces the time children spend alone.","zh":"兒童照顧支援減少孩子獨處的時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical help with supervision, safety, and daily routines.","zh":"這個短語描述在監督、安全和日常常規上的實際幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"contribute to","meaning":"導致；促成","examples":[{"en":"Several social changes have contributed to the growing ranks of latchkey kids.","zh":"幾項社會變化促成鑰匙兒童群體日益增加。"},{"en":"To contribute to something means to help cause it or add to it.","zh":"contribute to something 指幫助造成或增加某事。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can contribute to poor concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致課堂專注力差。"},{"en":"A social problem often has several factors contributing to it at the same time.","zh":"社會問題常由幾個因素同時促成。"},{"en":"This phrase shows partial cause, not always the only cause.","zh":"這個短語表示部分原因，不一定是唯一原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"growing ranks of","meaning":"日益增加的……群體","examples":[{"en":"Social changes have contributed to the growing ranks of latchkey children.","zh":"社會變化促成鑰匙兒童群體日益增加。"},{"en":"Growing ranks of a group means the number of people in that group is increasing.","zh":"growing ranks of a group 指某群體的人數正在增加。"},{"en":"Online learning has added to the growing ranks of students studying from home.","zh":"網上學習令在家學習的學生群體日益增加。"},{"en":"When the ranks of a group grow, society may need new services for them.","zh":"當某群體人數增加，社會可能需要為他們提供新服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an expanding group of people.","zh":"這個短語描述不斷擴大的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"latchkey kids","meaning":"鑰匙兒童","examples":[{"en":"Many latchkey kids go home to an empty house.","zh":"許多鑰匙兒童回到空無一人的房子。"},{"en":"Latchkey kids are children who regularly return home without an adult present.","zh":"latchkey kids 指經常在沒有成人在家的情況下回家的孩子。"},{"en":"A latchkey kid may heat food, watch television, and wait alone until evening.","zh":"鑰匙兒童可能自己加熱食物、看電視，並獨自等到晚上。"},{"en":"Some latchkey kids manage well, but others may feel isolated or unsafe.","zh":"有些鑰匙兒童適應良好，但另一些可能感到孤立或不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is a more informal version of “latchkey children.”","zh":"這個短語是 “latchkey children” 較口語的說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"according to one census","meaning":"根據一項人口普查","examples":[{"en":"According to one census, many school-age children are latchkey kids.","zh":"根據一項人口普查，許多學齡兒童是鑰匙兒童。"},{"en":"According to one census means based on data collected in one official population survey.","zh":"according to one census 指根據一項官方人口調查收集的資料。"},{"en":"According to one census, a city may have more elderly residents than young children.","zh":"根據一項人口普查，一座城市的長者居民可能多於幼兒。"},{"en":"Census data helps writers support claims with numbers rather than guesses.","zh":"人口普查資料幫助作者用數字而不是猜測支持說法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces statistical evidence.","zh":"這個短語引出統計證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"school-age children","meaning":"學齡兒童","examples":[{"en":"One-third of school-age children are latchkey kids for part of the week.","zh":"三分之一學齡兒童在一星期某些時間是鑰匙兒童。"},{"en":"School-age children are children old enough to attend school.","zh":"school-age children 指已達上學年齡的兒童。"},{"en":"School-age children often need supervision after classes end but before parents finish work.","zh":"學齡兒童常在放學後、父母下班前需要監督。"},{"en":"Support programmes for school-age children can reduce loneliness and risk.","zh":"為學齡兒童而設的支援計劃可以減少孤單和風險。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies children by their stage of education.","zh":"這個短語按教育階段辨認兒童。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"for some part of the week","meaning":"一星期中某些時間","examples":[{"en":"Some children are home alone for some part of the week.","zh":"有些孩子在一星期中某些時間獨自在家。"},{"en":"For some part of the week means during certain hours or days, but not the whole week.","zh":"for some part of the week 指在某些時段或日子，但不是整個星期。"},{"en":"A student may attend tutoring for some part of the week and sports training on other days.","zh":"學生可能一星期中某些時間補習，其他日子參加運動訓練。"},{"en":"Even occasional time alone can matter if the child is young or anxious.","zh":"即使只是偶爾獨處，如果孩子年幼或焦慮，也可能很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the situation happens part-time, not constantly.","zh":"這個短語顯示情況是部分時間發生，而不是持續發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"go home to","meaning":"回到……","examples":[{"en":"Latchkey children go home to an empty house or apartment.","zh":"鑰匙兒童回到空無一人的房子或單位。"},{"en":"To go home to something means to return home and find that situation waiting there.","zh":"go home to something 指回家後面對某種情況。"},{"en":"A child may go home to a warm meal if a grandparent is there.","zh":"如果祖父母在家，孩子可能回到一頓熱飯。"},{"en":"Going home to an empty flat can make a child feel lonely after school.","zh":"放學後回到空無一人的單位，可能令孩子感到孤單。"},{"en":"This phrase connects returning home with the condition found at home.","zh":"這個短語把回家與家中狀況連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"an empty house or apartment","meaning":"空無一人的房子或單位","examples":[{"en":"Many latchkey children return to an empty house or apartment.","zh":"許多鑰匙兒童回到空無一人的房子或單位。"},{"en":"An empty house or apartment means no one is home when the child arrives.","zh":"empty house or apartment 指孩子到家時沒有任何人在家。"},{"en":"A teenager may return to an empty apartment if both parents work late.","zh":"如果父母都工作到很晚，青少年可能回到空無一人的單位。"},{"en":"Empty homes can feel quiet and unsafe for young children.","zh":"對年幼兒童來說，空無一人的家可能顯得安靜且不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the absence of people, not a house without furniture.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有人在家，而不是沒有家具的房子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the total number","meaning":"總數","examples":[{"en":"The total number may be between five and seven million children.","zh":"總數可能介乎五百萬至七百萬名兒童之間。"},{"en":"The total number means the complete count of all people or things included.","zh":"total number 指所有包括在內的人或物的完整數量。"},{"en":"A teacher checks the total number of students before leaving for a school trip.","zh":"老師在出發校外旅行前會檢查學生總數。"},{"en":"Total numbers help people understand the scale of a problem.","zh":"總數幫助人們理解問題規模。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the whole amount, not one small group.","zh":"這個短語集中於整體數量，而不是某小群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"between five and seven million","meaning":"五百萬至七百萬之間","examples":[{"en":"The number may be between five and seven million.","zh":"數字可能在五百萬至七百萬之間。"},{"en":"Between five and seven million means not less than five million and not more than seven million.","zh":"between five and seven million 指不少於五百萬且不多於七百萬。"},{"en":"A city project may cost between five and seven million dollars if the final design is not fixed.","zh":"如果最終設計未定，城市項目可能花費五百萬至七百萬美元。"},{"en":"A range is used when the exact number is uncertain.","zh":"當確切數字不確定時，就會使用範圍。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an estimated numerical range.","zh":"這個短語給出估計數字範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"close to","meaning":"接近","examples":[{"en":"Marian Wright Edelman thinks the number is close to 16 million.","zh":"Marian Wright Edelman 認為數字接近一千六百萬。"},{"en":"Close to a number means almost that number but not necessarily exactly equal to it.","zh":"close to a number 指幾乎達到某數字，但不一定完全相等。"},{"en":"A student who scores 78 is close to 80.","zh":"得78分的學生接近80分。"},{"en":"Estimates use close to when the exact figure may not be known.","zh":"當確切數字可能未知時，估計會使用 close to。"},{"en":"This phrase signals approximate quantity.","zh":"這個短語表示近似數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Census Bureau","meaning":"人口普查局","examples":[{"en":"The Census Bureau collected information about children left alone.","zh":"人口普查局收集了關於獨自留在家中兒童的資料。"},{"en":"The Census Bureau is a government office that collects population data.","zh":"Census Bureau 指收集人口資料的政府部門。"},{"en":"A Census Bureau may ask families about age, work, housing, and household size.","zh":"人口普查局可能詢問家庭關於年齡、工作、住屋和住戶人數的資料。"},{"en":"Census data helps governments plan schools, transport, and social services.","zh":"人口普查資料幫助政府規劃學校、交通和社會服務。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an official statistics agency.","zh":"這個短語指官方統計機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"home alone before school","meaning":"上學前獨自在家","examples":[{"en":"Some children were home alone before school.","zh":"有些兒童上學前獨自在家。"},{"en":"Home alone before school means alone at home in the morning before going to school.","zh":"home alone before school 指早上上學前獨自在家。"},{"en":"A child may be home alone before school if a parent starts work very early.","zh":"如果父母很早上班，孩子可能上學前獨自在家。"},{"en":"Morning loneliness can be risky if children must prepare breakfast or leave on time by themselves.","zh":"如果孩子要自己準備早餐或準時出門，早上獨處可能有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies an unsupervised period before the school day begins.","zh":"這個短語指出上學日開始前無人監督的時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"after school","meaning":"放學後","examples":[{"en":"Most children were home alone after school.","zh":"大多數兒童放學後獨自在家。"},{"en":"After school means during the time after classes finish.","zh":"after school 指課堂結束後的時間。"},{"en":"Many students attend clubs or tutoring after school.","zh":"許多學生放學後參加學會或補習。"},{"en":"The after-school period can be risky if children have no supervision or activities.","zh":"如果孩子沒有監督或活動，放學後時段可能有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the afternoon period between school and parents’ return.","zh":"這個短語標示學校放學與父母回家之間的下午時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at night","meaning":"晚上","examples":[{"en":"Some children were home alone at night.","zh":"有些兒童晚上獨自在家。"},{"en":"At night means during the evening or nighttime hours.","zh":"at night 指在晚上或夜間時段。"},{"en":"A child home alone at night may feel more afraid than during daylight.","zh":"晚上獨自在家的孩子可能比日間更害怕。"},{"en":"Nighttime alone can be more worrying because fewer neighbours or services may be available.","zh":"夜間獨處可能更令人擔心，因為可求助的鄰居或服務可能較少。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the time when supervision may be especially important.","zh":"這個短語指出監督可能特別重要的時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"presumably","meaning":"大概；相信是","examples":[{"en":"Presumably, the children at home at night have parents who work night shifts.","zh":"大概晚上在家的兒童，其父母是上夜班的。"},{"en":"Presumably means probably, based on what seems reasonable from the evidence.","zh":"presumably 指根據證據看來合理地推測「大概」。"},{"en":"If a classroom is dark and empty, presumably the lesson has finished.","zh":"如果課室又黑又空，大概課堂已經結束。"},{"en":"This word introduces a likely explanation, not a proven fact.","zh":"這個字引出可能解釋，而不是已證明事實。"},{"en":"It is useful when the writer is making a careful assumption.","zh":"當作者作出謹慎假設時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"work night shifts","meaning":"上夜班","examples":[{"en":"Some parents work night shifts.","zh":"有些父母上夜班。"},{"en":"To work night shifts means to work regularly during the night.","zh":"work night shifts 指定期在夜間工作。"},{"en":"Hospital staff may work night shifts because patients need care all day and night.","zh":"醫院職員可能上夜班，因為病人日夜都需要照顧。"},{"en":"Parents who work night shifts may have difficulty supervising children in the evening.","zh":"上夜班的父母可能難以在晚上監督孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a schedule that can affect family life.","zh":"這個短語描述一種會影響家庭生活的工作時間表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"aged 12 to 14","meaning":"年齡介乎 12 至 14 歲","examples":[{"en":"Many children aged 12 to 14 are home alone each week.","zh":"許多年齡介乎12至14歲的兒童每星期都獨自在家。"},{"en":"Aged 12 to 14 means between twelve and fourteen years old.","zh":"aged 12 to 14 指十二至十四歲之間。"},{"en":"Students aged 12 to 14 are often in early secondary school.","zh":"年齡介乎12至14歲的學生通常在初中。"},{"en":"Children in this age range may seem independent but still need guidance.","zh":"這個年齡層的孩子可能看似獨立，但仍需要指導。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific age group.","zh":"這個短語指出特定年齡組別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on average","meaning":"平均而言","examples":[{"en":"Some children are home alone for an average of seven hours a week.","zh":"有些兒童平均每星期獨自在家七小時。"},{"en":"On average means when the total amount is divided into a typical amount.","zh":"on average 指把總量換算成典型數量。"},{"en":"On average, a student may spend thirty minutes travelling to school.","zh":"平均而言，學生可能花三十分鐘上學。"},{"en":"An average does not mean every child has exactly the same experience.","zh":"平均數不代表每個孩子都有完全相同經歷。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a general numerical pattern.","zh":"這個短語給出一般數字模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"seven hours a week","meaning":"每星期七小時","examples":[{"en":"Some children are home alone for seven hours a week.","zh":"有些兒童每星期獨自在家七小時。"},{"en":"Seven hours a week means a total of seven hours across one week.","zh":"seven hours a week 指一星期總共七小時。"},{"en":"A student who studies English seven hours a week practises one hour a day on average.","zh":"每星期學英文七小時的學生，平均每天練習一小時。"},{"en":"Time alone can add up even if each day only includes a short period.","zh":"即使每天只是短時間獨處，加起來也可以很多。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a weekly amount of time.","zh":"這個短語給出每週時間總量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the very poor","meaning":"極貧人士","examples":[{"en":"The very poor are less likely to leave their children alone at home.","zh":"極貧人士較不可能把孩子獨自留在家中。"},{"en":"The very poor means people living in extreme poverty.","zh":"the very poor 指生活在極端貧窮中的人。"},{"en":"The very poor may rely on relatives, neighbours, or informal help because paid childcare is too expensive.","zh":"極貧人士可能依賴親戚、鄰居或非正式幫助，因為付費托兒太昂貴。"},{"en":"Poverty can limit choices, but it may also keep families close to home or shared housing.","zh":"貧窮會限制選擇，但也可能令家庭更接近家中或共同居住。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the poorest group in society.","zh":"這個短語指出社會中最貧窮的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be less likely to","meaning":"較不可能","examples":[{"en":"Very poor families are less likely to leave their children alone.","zh":"極貧家庭較不可能把孩子獨自留下。"},{"en":"To be less likely to do something means to have a lower chance of doing it.","zh":"be less likely to do something 指做某事的機會較低。"},{"en":"Students who sleep well are less likely to make careless mistakes.","zh":"睡眠充足的學生較不可能犯粗心錯誤。"},{"en":"A family may be less likely to leave children alone if grandparents live nearby.","zh":"如果祖父母住在附近，家庭較不可能讓孩子獨處。"},{"en":"This phrase compares probability between groups or situations.","zh":"這個短語比較不同群體或情況的可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"allow them to","meaning":"容許他們去","examples":[{"en":"Some families allow children to go home alone.","zh":"有些家庭容許孩子獨自回家。"},{"en":"To allow them to do something means to permit them to do it.","zh":"allow them to do something 指准許他們做某事。"},{"en":"Parents may allow teenagers to take the bus alone when they trust their judgement.","zh":"當父母信任青少年的判斷，可能容許他們獨自坐巴士。"},{"en":"Permission can be reasonable when the child is mature and the environment is safe.","zh":"當孩子成熟且環境安全時，許可可以是合理的。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that someone has been given permission.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人被給予許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"earn twice their level of income","meaning":"賺取他們兩倍收入","examples":[{"en":"Families who earn twice their income are more likely to leave children alone.","zh":"賺取他們兩倍收入的家庭較可能把孩子獨自留下。"},{"en":"To earn twice someone’s level of income means to make double the amount of money that person or group earns.","zh":"earn twice someone’s level of income 指賺取某人或某群體收入的兩倍。"},{"en":"A family earning twice another family’s income may still struggle if childcare is expensive.","zh":"收入是另一家庭兩倍的家庭，如果托兒很昂貴，仍可能感到吃力。"},{"en":"Income affects childcare choices because families with different earnings use different support systems.","zh":"收入影響兒童照顧選擇，因為不同收入家庭會使用不同支援系統。"},{"en":"This phrase compares income levels between groups.","zh":"這個短語比較群體之間的收入水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"less safe neighbourhoods","meaning":"較不安全的社區","examples":[{"en":"The very poor often live in less safe neighbourhoods.","zh":"極貧人士常住在較不安全的社區。"},{"en":"Less safe neighbourhoods are areas where crime, danger, or poor conditions are more common.","zh":"less safe neighbourhoods 指罪案、危險或惡劣環境較常見的地區。"},{"en":"A parent may worry if a child walks home alone through a less safe neighbourhood.","zh":"如果孩子要獨自走過較不安全的社區回家，家長可能會擔心。"},{"en":"Neighbourhood safety affects whether children can be left alone or travel alone.","zh":"社區安全會影響孩子能否獨處或獨自出行。"},{"en":"This phrase compares safety between communities.","zh":"這個短語比較不同社區的安全程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in an emergency","meaning":"在緊急情況下","examples":[{"en":"Some families have fewer friends who can help in an emergency.","zh":"有些家庭在緊急情況下可求助的朋友較少。"},{"en":"In an emergency means during a sudden dangerous or urgent situation.","zh":"in an emergency 指在突然危險或迫切情況中。"},{"en":"In an emergency, a child should know which adult to call first.","zh":"在緊急情況下，孩子應知道先打電話給哪位成人。"},{"en":"Families with support nearby can respond faster when something goes wrong.","zh":"附近有支援的家庭在出事時能更快回應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes situations that require immediate help.","zh":"這個短語描述需要即時幫助的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in spite of","meaning":"儘管","examples":[{"en":"In spite of the hours spent on the job, working mothers spend time with their children.","zh":"儘管花了許多時間工作，在職母親仍會花時間陪伴孩子。"},{"en":"In spite of means although something is true, another thing still happens.","zh":"in spite of 指雖然某事屬實，另一件事仍然發生。"},{"en":"In spite of heavy rain, students arrived on time for the exam.","zh":"儘管下大雨，學生仍準時到達考試。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast between difficulty and action.","zh":"這個短語引出困難與行動之間的對比。"},{"en":"It shows that one fact does not completely prevent another.","zh":"它顯示一個事實不會完全阻止另一件事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hours spent on the job","meaning":"花在工作上的時間","examples":[{"en":"Working mothers spend many hours on the job.","zh":"在職母親花許多時間在工作上。"},{"en":"Hours spent on the job means the amount of time used for paid work.","zh":"hours spent on the job 指用於受薪工作的時間。"},{"en":"A nurse may spend long hours on the job during a busy hospital shift.","zh":"醫院繁忙輪班期間，護士可能花很長時間在工作上。"},{"en":"Long work hours can reduce the time available for rest and family care.","zh":"長工時可以減少休息和照顧家庭的時間。"},{"en":"This phrase measures work time, not total daily activity.","zh":"這個短語量度工作時間，而不是每日所有活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"spend an average of","meaning":"平均花費","examples":[{"en":"Working mothers spend an average of five and a half hours a day with their children.","zh":"在職母親平均每天花五個半小時陪伴孩子。"},{"en":"To spend an average of an amount means to use that typical amount of time or money.","zh":"spend an average of an amount 指使用某個典型時間或金錢數量。"},{"en":"Students may spend an average of twenty minutes a day reviewing vocabulary.","zh":"學生可能平均每天花二十分鐘複習詞彙。"},{"en":"Averages help compare groups, but individual cases can be higher or lower.","zh":"平均數有助比較群體，但個別情況可以高於或低於平均。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a typical measured amount.","zh":"這個短語引出典型量度數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"five and a half hours a day","meaning":"每天五個半小時","examples":[{"en":"Working mothers spend five and a half hours a day with their children.","zh":"在職母親每天花五個半小時陪伴孩子。"},{"en":"Five and a half hours a day means five hours and thirty minutes every day.","zh":"five and a half hours a day 指每天五小時三十分鐘。"},{"en":"A student who studies five and a half hours a day is working very intensively.","zh":"每天學習五個半小時的學生學習量非常密集。"},{"en":"Daily time matters because small differences add up across a week.","zh":"每日時間很重要，因為小差異一星期下來會累積。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a specific daily amount of time.","zh":"這個短語給出具體每日時間量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"function well","meaning":"運作良好；適應良好","examples":[{"en":"When latchkey children function well, we do not hear about them.","zh":"當鑰匙兒童適應良好時，我們通常不會聽聞他們。"},{"en":"To function well means to manage daily life successfully without serious problems.","zh":"function well 指能成功處理日常生活而沒有嚴重問題。"},{"en":"A student functions well when they attend school, finish work, and handle stress calmly.","zh":"學生能上學、完成功課並冷靜處理壓力，就是適應良好。"},{"en":"Children who function well alone may still need regular emotional support.","zh":"獨處時適應良好的孩子，仍可能需要定期情感支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical adjustment, not perfect happiness.","zh":"這個短語描述實際適應，而不是完美快樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hear about","meaning":"聽聞；得知","examples":[{"en":"We usually hear about latchkey children only when problems arise.","zh":"我們通常只有在問題出現時才聽聞鑰匙兒童。"},{"en":"To hear about something means to receive news or information about it.","zh":"hear about something 指收到關於某事的消息或資訊。"},{"en":"Parents may hear about a school problem through a teacher’s phone call.","zh":"家長可能透過老師電話得知學校問題。"},{"en":"People often hear about a group only when something goes wrong.","zh":"人們常只在出事時才聽聞某個群體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming aware of an issue.","zh":"這個短語描述開始知道某議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"child welfare agencies","meaning":"兒童福利機構","examples":[{"en":"Many complaints to child welfare agencies involve latchkey children.","zh":"許多向兒童福利機構作出的投訴涉及鑰匙兒童。"},{"en":"Child welfare agencies are organisations that protect children’s safety and wellbeing.","zh":"child welfare agencies 指保護兒童安全和福祉的機構。"},{"en":"A child welfare agency may investigate if a child is often left alone in unsafe conditions.","zh":"如果孩子經常在不安全情況下被獨自留下，兒童福利機構可能調查。"},{"en":"These agencies become involved when families cannot protect children adequately.","zh":"當家庭未能充分保護兒童，這些機構就會介入。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal services for child protection.","zh":"這個短語指正式兒童保護服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"complaints to","meaning":"向……作出的投訴","examples":[{"en":"One-third of complaints to child welfare agencies involve latchkey children.","zh":"向兒童福利機構作出的投訴中，三分之一涉及鑰匙兒童。"},{"en":"Complaints to an organisation are reports made to that organisation about a problem.","zh":"complaints to an organisation 指向某機構報告問題。"},{"en":"Complaints to a school may concern bullying, safety, or unfair treatment.","zh":"向學校作出的投訴可能涉及欺凌、安全或不公平對待。"},{"en":"Complaints help agencies know which problems need investigation.","zh":"投訴幫助機構知道哪些問題需要調查。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where concerns are officially reported.","zh":"這個短語指出關注事項正式報告到哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"involve latchkey children","meaning":"涉及鑰匙兒童","examples":[{"en":"Many complaints involve latchkey children.","zh":"許多投訴涉及鑰匙兒童。"},{"en":"To involve latchkey children means to include them as part of the problem or case.","zh":"involve latchkey children 指把鑰匙兒童包括在問題或個案之中。"},{"en":"A police report may involve teenagers if they were present during an incident.","zh":"如果青少年在事件中在場，警方報告可能涉及青少年。"},{"en":"When many complaints involve one group, that group may need more support.","zh":"當許多投訴涉及同一群體，該群體可能需要更多支援。"},{"en":"This phrase shows who is connected with the reported issue.","zh":"這個短語顯示誰與被報告問題相關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"do poorly in school","meaning":"在學校表現欠佳","examples":[{"en":"Many latchkey children are doing poorly in school.","zh":"許多鑰匙兒童在學校表現欠佳。"},{"en":"To do poorly in school means to have weak academic performance or school behaviour.","zh":"do poorly in school 指學業表現或在校行為較弱。"},{"en":"A child may do poorly in school if they are tired, anxious, or unsupported at home.","zh":"如果孩子疲倦、焦慮或在家缺乏支援，可能在學校表現欠佳。"},{"en":"Lack of supervision after school can affect homework, sleep, and concentration.","zh":"放學後缺乏監督可以影響功課、睡眠和專注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes school difficulties, not low intelligence.","zh":"這個短語描述學校困難，而不是智力低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the number one cause of","meaning":"……的首要原因","examples":[{"en":"Teachers believe being alone at home is the number one cause of school failure.","zh":"老師認為獨自在家是學業失敗的首要原因。"},{"en":"The number one cause of something means the main or most important reason for it.","zh":"number one cause of something 指某事的主要或最重要原因。"},{"en":"For many students, lack of revision is the number one cause of weak test results.","zh":"對許多學生而言，缺乏溫習是測驗成績差的首要原因。"},{"en":"Calling something the number one cause suggests it matters more than other factors.","zh":"把某事稱為首要原因，暗示它比其他因素更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the leading cause.","zh":"這個短語指出最主要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"school failure","meaning":"學業失敗","examples":[{"en":"Being alone at home may contribute to school failure.","zh":"獨自在家可能促成學業失敗。"},{"en":"School failure means serious difficulty in succeeding academically or staying on track at school.","zh":"school failure 指在學業上嚴重難以成功或跟上學校進度。"},{"en":"A student facing school failure may miss homework, fail tests, and lose motivation.","zh":"面臨學業失敗的學生可能欠交功課、考試不合格並失去動力。"},{"en":"School failure can result from family stress, poor support, health problems, or learning gaps.","zh":"學業失敗可以由家庭壓力、支援不足、健康問題或學習缺口造成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes educational breakdown, not just one bad grade.","zh":"這個短語描述教育上的崩潰，而不只是一次低分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"afternoon hours","meaning":"下午時段","examples":[{"en":"The afternoon hours are the peak time for juvenile crime.","zh":"下午時段是青少年犯罪的高峰時間。"},{"en":"Afternoon hours means the period after noon and before evening.","zh":"afternoon hours 指中午之後、晚上之前的時間。"},{"en":"The afternoon hours after school may leave children free but unsupervised.","zh":"放學後的下午時段可能令孩子有空但無人監督。"},{"en":"When adults are still at work, the afternoon hours can become a risky gap.","zh":"當成人仍在工作，下午時段可能變成有風險的空檔。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a time period with special importance.","zh":"這個短語指出具有特殊重要性的時間段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"peak time for","meaning":"……的高峰時間","examples":[{"en":"Afternoon is the peak time for juvenile crime.","zh":"下午是青少年犯罪的高峰時間。"},{"en":"Peak time for something means the period when it happens most often.","zh":"peak time for something 指某事最常發生的時段。"},{"en":"Morning rush hour is the peak time for crowded trains.","zh":"早上繁忙時間是列車最擁擠的高峰時間。"},{"en":"Knowing the peak time helps people plan supervision or prevention.","zh":"知道高峰時間有助人們安排監督或預防。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the highest-risk or busiest period.","zh":"這個短語指出最高風險或最繁忙的時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"juvenile crime","meaning":"青少年犯罪","examples":[{"en":"Juvenile crime has increased sharply.","zh":"青少年犯罪急劇增加。"},{"en":"Juvenile crime means crimes committed by young people who are not yet adults.","zh":"juvenile crime 指未成年年輕人所犯的罪行。"},{"en":"Shoplifting, vandalism, or assault by teenagers may be counted as juvenile crime.","zh":"青少年偷竊、破壞公物或襲擊可能被計算為青少年犯罪。"},{"en":"Juvenile crime may increase when young people are unsupervised and disconnected from support.","zh":"當年輕人無人監督並與支援脫節，青少年犯罪可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on crime by minors.","zh":"這個短語集中於未成年人犯罪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"increase 48 per cent","meaning":"增加百分之四十八","examples":[{"en":"Juvenile crime has increased 48 per cent in 11 years.","zh":"青少年犯罪在十一年間增加百分之四十八。"},{"en":"To increase 48 per cent means to rise by 48 per cent compared with the earlier level.","zh":"increase 48 per cent 指與較早水平相比上升百分之四十八。"},{"en":"If a club grows from 100 to 148 members, it has increased 48 per cent.","zh":"如果學會由100名會員增至148名，就是增加百分之四十八。"},{"en":"Percent increases help show how quickly a problem is growing.","zh":"百分比增幅有助顯示問題增長得有多快。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a measured rise over time.","zh":"這個短語給出一段時間內的量化上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"adolescent development","meaning":"青少年發展","examples":[{"en":"The Carnegie Council on Adolescent Development studied teenagers’ behaviour.","zh":"Carnegie Council on Adolescent Development 研究青少年行為。"},{"en":"Adolescent development means the physical, emotional, social, and mental growth of teenagers.","zh":"adolescent development 指青少年的身體、情緒、社交和心理成長。"},{"en":"Teachers consider adolescent development when deciding how much independence students can handle.","zh":"老師決定學生能承受多少獨立性時，會考慮青少年發展。"},{"en":"During adolescence, young people rethink identity, values, friends, and risk.","zh":"在青春期，年輕人會重新思考身份、價值觀、朋友和風險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to growth during the teenage years.","zh":"這個短語指青少年時期的成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"eighth-graders","meaning":"八年級學生","examples":[{"en":"Eighth-graders who are alone for many hours are at greater risk.","zh":"長時間獨處的八年級學生面對較大風險。"},{"en":"Eighth-graders are students in the eighth year of formal schooling, usually around age thirteen or fourteen.","zh":"eighth-graders 指正式教育第八年的學生，通常約十三或十四歲。"},{"en":"Eighth-graders may want independence but still need adult guidance.","zh":"八年級學生可能想要獨立，但仍需要成人指導。"},{"en":"If eighth-graders spend long hours alone, peer pressure and boredom may become stronger risks.","zh":"如果八年級學生長時間獨處，同輩壓力和沉悶可能成為更大風險。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific school grade group.","zh":"這個短語指出特定年級群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"twice as likely to","meaning":"可能性高出一倍","examples":[{"en":"Children who are alone after school are twice as likely to abuse drugs.","zh":"放學後獨處的兒童濫用毒品的可能性高出一倍。"},{"en":"Twice as likely to do something means having double the chance of doing it.","zh":"twice as likely to do something 指做某事的機會是兩倍。"},{"en":"Students who skip revision may be twice as likely to fail a vocabulary quiz.","zh":"跳過溫習的學生在詞彙測驗不合格的可能性可能高出一倍。"},{"en":"This phrase compares risk between two groups.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個群體之間的風險。"},{"en":"It does not mean the behaviour is certain; it means the probability is higher.","zh":"它不代表行為一定發生，而是機會較高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"abuse drugs","meaning":"濫用毒品","examples":[{"en":"Some adolescents are more likely to abuse drugs.","zh":"有些青少年較可能濫用毒品。"},{"en":"To abuse drugs means to use illegal drugs or misuse medicine in a harmful way.","zh":"abuse drugs 指使用非法毒品或以有害方式誤用藥物。"},{"en":"A teenager may abuse drugs if they take pills not prescribed to them.","zh":"如果青少年服用並非開給自己的藥丸，可能屬於濫用藥物。"},{"en":"Drug abuse can harm health, school performance, and family relationships.","zh":"濫用毒品可以傷害健康、學校表現和家庭關係。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dangerous substance use, not normal medical treatment.","zh":"這個短語描述危險物質使用，而不是正常醫療治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"busy after school","meaning":"放學後有事可做","examples":[{"en":"Adolescents who are busy after school are less likely to abuse drugs.","zh":"放學後有事可做的青少年較不可能濫用毒品。"},{"en":"Busy after school means having organised activities or responsibilities after classes end.","zh":"busy after school 指放學後有安排好的活動或責任。"},{"en":"A student busy after school with football practice may have less time to wander around unsupervised.","zh":"放學後忙於足球訓練的學生，較少時間在無人監督下閒逛。"},{"en":"Structured activities can reduce risky behaviour by giving young people purpose and supervision.","zh":"有結構的活動可以透過給年輕人目標和監督來減少高風險行為。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts active routines with empty free time.","zh":"這個短語把有活動的常規與空白自由時間作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"unsupervised children","meaning":"無人監督的兒童","examples":[{"en":"Unsupervised children are more likely to become depressed.","zh":"無人監督的兒童較可能變得抑鬱。"},{"en":"Unsupervised children are children who are not watched or guided by an adult.","zh":"unsupervised children 指沒有成人看顧或指導的兒童。"},{"en":"Unsupervised children may spend hours online without anyone checking what they see.","zh":"無人監督的兒童可能連續幾小時上網，而沒有人檢查他們看了甚麼。"},{"en":"Without guidance, children may feel lonely, unsafe, or pressured by peers.","zh":"沒有指導時，孩子可能感到孤單、不安全或受到同輩壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the absence of adult care.","zh":"這個短語突出成人照顧的缺席。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"become depressed","meaning":"變得抑鬱","examples":[{"en":"Unsupervised children are more likely to become depressed.","zh":"無人監督的兒童較可能變得抑鬱。"},{"en":"To become depressed means to develop deep sadness, low mood, or loss of interest over time.","zh":"become depressed 指隨時間出現深層悲傷、情緒低落或失去興趣。"},{"en":"A child may become depressed if they feel lonely every afternoon and have no one to talk to.","zh":"如果孩子每天下午都感到孤單且無人傾訴，可能變得抑鬱。"},{"en":"Depression can affect sleep, schoolwork, appetite, and motivation.","zh":"抑鬱可以影響睡眠、功課、食慾和動力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious emotional change, not just one bad day.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重情緒變化，而不是單日心情差。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"smoke cigarettes and marijuana","meaning":"吸煙和吸食大麻","examples":[{"en":"Unsupervised children are more likely to smoke cigarettes and marijuana.","zh":"無人監督的兒童較可能吸煙和吸食大麻。"},{"en":"To smoke cigarettes and marijuana means to use tobacco and cannabis by inhaling smoke.","zh":"smoke cigarettes and marijuana 指透過吸入煙霧使用煙草和大麻。"},{"en":"Teenagers may try smoking if friends pressure them and no adult is present.","zh":"如果朋友施壓且沒有成人在場，青少年可能嘗試吸煙。"},{"en":"Smoking can harm health and may become a habit that is hard to stop.","zh":"吸煙可以傷害健康，並可能變成難以停止的習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes risky substance use among young people.","zh":"這個短語描述年輕人的高風險物質使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"drink alcohol","meaning":"飲酒","examples":[{"en":"Unsupervised children are more likely to drink alcohol.","zh":"無人監督的兒童較可能飲酒。"},{"en":"To drink alcohol means to consume beer, wine, spirits, or other alcoholic drinks.","zh":"drink alcohol 指飲用啤酒、葡萄酒、烈酒或其他含酒精飲品。"},{"en":"Teenagers may drink alcohol at a party if no responsible adult is supervising them.","zh":"如果沒有負責任成人監督，青少年可能在派對上飲酒。"},{"en":"Alcohol can affect judgement, safety, and health, especially for young people.","zh":"酒精可以影響判斷、安全和健康，尤其對年輕人而言。"},{"en":"This phrase describes behaviour that may be illegal or risky for minors.","zh":"這個短語描述未成年人可能違法或高風險的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be victims of crimes","meaning":"成為罪案受害者","examples":[{"en":"Latchkey children are more likely to be victims of crimes.","zh":"鑰匙兒童較可能成為罪案受害者。"},{"en":"To be victims of crimes means to suffer harm because someone commits a crime against them.","zh":"be victims of crimes 指因有人對他們犯罪而受到傷害。"},{"en":"A child alone at home may be a victim of burglary, threats, or online scams.","zh":"獨自在家的孩子可能成為入屋盜竊、威脅或網上騙案的受害者。"},{"en":"Lack of adult protection can make children easier targets.","zh":"缺乏成人保護可以令兒童更容易成為目標。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that children may suffer from crime, not only commit it.","zh":"這個短語顯示兒童不只可能犯罪，也可能受犯罪傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"when home alone","meaning":"獨自在家時","examples":[{"en":"When home alone, latchkey children often watch television.","zh":"獨自在家時，鑰匙兒童常常看電視。"},{"en":"When home alone means during the time a person is at home without anyone else there.","zh":"when home alone 指一個人在沒有其他人在家的時候。"},{"en":"A child may feel nervous when home alone during a thunderstorm.","zh":"雷暴期間獨自在家時，孩子可能感到緊張。"},{"en":"What children do when home alone can affect their safety and habits.","zh":"孩子獨自在家時做甚麼，可以影響其安全和習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on behaviour during unsupervised time at home.","zh":"這個短語集中於在家無人監督時的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"watch television","meaning":"看電視","examples":[{"en":"Latchkey children generally watch television when home alone.","zh":"鑰匙兒童獨自在家時通常看電視。"},{"en":"To watch television means to look at TV programmes or videos on a screen.","zh":"watch television 指觀看電視節目或螢幕上的影片。"},{"en":"A child may watch television after school because it is easy and requires no adult help.","zh":"孩子放學後可能看電視，因為這很容易且不需要成人幫助。"},{"en":"Too much television can replace homework, reading, exercise, or conversation.","zh":"看太多電視可以取代功課、閱讀、運動或對話。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common passive activity at home.","zh":"這個短語描述在家常見的被動活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"eat snacks","meaning":"吃零食","examples":[{"en":"Some latchkey children eat snacks after school.","zh":"有些鑰匙兒童放學後吃零食。"},{"en":"To eat snacks means to eat small amounts of food between meals.","zh":"eat snacks 指在正餐之間吃少量食物。"},{"en":"A child may eat snacks after school because dinner is still hours away.","zh":"孩子放學後可能吃零食，因為距離晚餐還有幾小時。"},{"en":"Without supervision, children may choose sweets and crisps instead of healthier food.","zh":"沒有監督下，孩子可能選糖果和薯片，而不是較健康食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common after-school habit.","zh":"這個短語描述常見放學後習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"play with pets","meaning":"與寵物玩耍","examples":[{"en":"Some children play with pets when they are home alone.","zh":"有些孩子獨自在家時與寵物玩耍。"},{"en":"To play with pets means to spend time with animals such as dogs, cats, or rabbits for fun.","zh":"play with pets 指為了娛樂而與狗、貓或兔等動物相處。"},{"en":"A child may play with a dog after school to feel less lonely.","zh":"孩子放學後可能與狗玩耍，以減少孤單感。"},{"en":"Pets can provide comfort, but they cannot replace adult supervision.","zh":"寵物可以提供安慰，但不能取代成人監督。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple home activity involving animals.","zh":"這個短語描述一種涉及動物的簡單家居活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fight with siblings","meaning":"與兄弟姊妹打架","examples":[{"en":"Latchkey children may fight with siblings when home alone.","zh":"鑰匙兒童獨自在家時可能與兄弟姊妹打架。"},{"en":"To fight with siblings means to argue or physically struggle with brothers or sisters.","zh":"fight with siblings 指與兄弟姊妹爭吵或肢體衝突。"},{"en":"Two children may fight with siblings over the television remote when no adult is present.","zh":"沒有成人在場時，兩個孩子可能因電視遙控器而與兄弟姊妹打架。"},{"en":"Small conflicts can become bigger if no adult helps children calm down.","zh":"如果沒有成人幫助孩子冷靜，小衝突可能變大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes conflict between children in the same family.","zh":"這個短語描述同一家庭兒童之間的衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fall under the classification of","meaning":"屬於……分類","examples":[{"en":"Some adolescents fall under the classification of latchkey children.","zh":"有些青少年屬於鑰匙兒童分類。"},{"en":"To fall under the classification of something means to belong to that category.","zh":"fall under the classification of something 指屬於某個類別。"},{"en":"A student who studies at home full-time may fall under the classification of homeschooler.","zh":"全日在家學習的學生可能屬於在家教育者分類。"},{"en":"Classifications help researchers group similar cases together.","zh":"分類幫助研究者把相似個案歸在一起。"},{"en":"This phrase describes category membership.","zh":"這個短語描述類別歸屬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"of the same age group","meaning":"同一年齡組別的","examples":[{"en":"They are more likely than others of the same age group to feel isolated.","zh":"他們比同一年齡組別的其他人更可能感到孤立。"},{"en":"Of the same age group means belonging to a group of people around the same age.","zh":"of the same age group 指屬於大約相同年齡的一群人。"},{"en":"A twelve-year-old may compare herself with classmates of the same age group.","zh":"十二歲孩子可能把自己與同一年齡組別的同學比較。"},{"en":"Comparing people of the same age group makes the comparison fairer.","zh":"比較同一年齡組別的人會令比較更公平。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies peers by age.","zh":"這個短語按年齡辨認同輩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"experience feelings of","meaning":"經歷……的感覺","examples":[{"en":"Some latchkey children experience feelings of rage and isolation.","zh":"有些鑰匙兒童經歷憤怒和孤立感。"},{"en":"To experience feelings of something means to feel that emotion strongly or repeatedly.","zh":"experience feelings of something 指強烈或反覆感受到某種情緒。"},{"en":"A new student may experience feelings of loneliness during the first week of school.","zh":"新學生在開學第一週可能經歷孤單感。"},{"en":"Repeated emotional experiences can affect behaviour and confidence.","zh":"反覆的情緒經歷可以影響行為和自信。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the emotions someone goes through.","zh":"這個短語引出某人所經歷的情緒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rage and isolation","meaning":"憤怒和孤立感","examples":[{"en":"Latchkey adolescents may feel rage and isolation.","zh":"鑰匙青少年可能感到憤怒和孤立感。"},{"en":"Rage and isolation mean intense anger and a painful sense of being alone or cut off from others.","zh":"rage and isolation 指強烈憤怒，以及痛苦地覺得自己孤單或與他人隔絕。"},{"en":"A teenager who feels ignored at home may experience rage and isolation.","zh":"在家中感到被忽視的青少年可能經歷憤怒和孤立感。"},{"en":"These feelings can become dangerous if the child has no safe way to talk about them.","zh":"如果孩子沒有安全方式談論這些感受，這些情緒可能變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase combines emotional anger with social loneliness.","zh":"這個短語結合情緒憤怒與社交孤單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"express emotions","meaning":"表達情緒","examples":[{"en":"Some adolescents express their emotions in an aggressive manner.","zh":"有些青少年以攻擊性方式表達情緒。"},{"en":"To express emotions means to show or communicate feelings.","zh":"express emotions 指展示或傳達感受。"},{"en":"A child may express emotions by crying, talking, drawing, or shouting.","zh":"孩子可能透過哭泣、說話、畫畫或大叫來表達情緒。"},{"en":"Healthy expression helps children manage feelings before they become harmful behaviour.","zh":"健康表達有助孩子在情緒變成有害行為前處理它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how inner feelings become visible.","zh":"這個短語描述內在感受如何變得可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in a physically aggressive manner","meaning":"以身體攻擊性的方式","examples":[{"en":"They may express their emotions in a physically aggressive manner.","zh":"他們可能以身體攻擊性的方式表達情緒。"},{"en":"In a physically aggressive manner means through actions such as hitting, pushing, kicking, or damaging things.","zh":"in a physically aggressive manner 指透過打人、推撞、踢人或破壞物件等行動。"},{"en":"A child who throws chairs is reacting in a physically aggressive manner.","zh":"掟椅子的孩子就是以身體攻擊性的方式反應。"},{"en":"Physical aggression can harm others and may require adult intervention.","zh":"身體攻擊可以傷害他人，並可能需要成人介入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bodily violence rather than verbal anger only.","zh":"這個短語描述肢體暴力，而不只是言語憤怒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"genetic and biological factors","meaning":"遺傳及生物因素","examples":[{"en":"Genetic and biological factors may influence aggressive behaviour.","zh":"遺傳及生物因素可能影響攻擊性行為。"},{"en":"Genetic and biological factors are inherited traits and body-related conditions that affect behaviour.","zh":"genetic and biological factors 指影響行為的遺傳特質和身體相關條件。"},{"en":"Some children may react more strongly to stress because of biological differences.","zh":"有些孩子可能因生物差異而對壓力反應更強。"},{"en":"These factors can influence behaviour, but environment and learning also matter.","zh":"這些因素可以影響行為，但環境和學習也很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to nature-based influences, not social causes alone.","zh":"這個短語指基於天性的影響，而不只是社會原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be involved in","meaning":"牽涉於","examples":[{"en":"Genetic and biological factors are involved in adolescent behaviour.","zh":"遺傳及生物因素牽涉於青少年行為。"},{"en":"To be involved in something means to play a part in it or be connected with it.","zh":"be involved in something 指在某事中起作用或與之相關。"},{"en":"Sleep, diet, and stress are involved in a student’s ability to concentrate.","zh":"睡眠、飲食和壓力都牽涉於學生專注能力。"},{"en":"Many factors can be involved in one behaviour at the same time.","zh":"一種行為可以同時牽涉許多因素。"},{"en":"This phrase shows connection without saying something is the only cause.","zh":"這個短語顯示關聯，而不是說某事是唯一原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the development of","meaning":"……的發展","examples":[{"en":"Several factors are involved in the development of aggression.","zh":"幾個因素牽涉於攻擊性的發展。"},{"en":"The development of something means the process by which it grows or forms over time.","zh":"development of something 指某事隨時間成長或形成的過程。"},{"en":"The development of a child’s confidence depends on practice, praise, and safe mistakes.","zh":"孩子自信的發展取決於練習、讚賞和安全地犯錯。"},{"en":"Aggression can develop when emotions, biology, family, and environment interact.","zh":"當情緒、生物因素、家庭和環境互相作用，攻擊性可能發展出來。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how something gradually comes into being.","zh":"這個短語集中於某事如何逐漸形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"propensity towards","meaning":"……的傾向","examples":[{"en":"Some adolescents develop a propensity towards acting out their feelings.","zh":"有些青少年發展出以行為表現情緒的傾向。"},{"en":"A propensity towards something is a tendency or natural leaning to do it.","zh":"propensity towards something 指做某事的傾向或自然偏向。"},{"en":"A student with a propensity towards worry may feel anxious before every test.","zh":"有憂慮傾向的學生可能每次測驗前都感到焦慮。"},{"en":"A tendency can become stronger if behaviour is repeated and not corrected.","zh":"如果行為反覆出現且沒有被糾正，傾向可能變強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated inclination, not a single action.","zh":"這個短語描述重複傾向，而不是單一行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"act out feelings","meaning":"以行為表現情緒","examples":[{"en":"Some adolescents act out their feelings of rage and isolation.","zh":"有些青少年以行為表現憤怒和孤立感。"},{"en":"To act out feelings means to show emotions through behaviour rather than words.","zh":"act out feelings 指透過行為而不是言語表達情緒。"},{"en":"A child may act out sadness by refusing to speak or breaking small objects.","zh":"孩子可能透過拒絕說話或打破小物件來以行為表現悲傷。"},{"en":"Acting out feelings can cause trouble if adults only punish the behaviour and ignore the emotion.","zh":"如果成人只懲罰行為而忽視情緒，以行為表現情緒可能引發麻煩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotions being expressed through actions.","zh":"這個短語描述情緒透過行動表達出來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"play a key role in","meaning":"在……中扮演關鍵角色","examples":[{"en":"Environment also plays a key role in adolescent behaviour.","zh":"環境也在青少年行為中扮演關鍵角色。"},{"en":"To play a key role in something means to be a very important factor in it.","zh":"play a key role in something 指在某事中是非常重要的因素。"},{"en":"Sleep plays a key role in memory and mood.","zh":"睡眠在記憶和情緒中扮演關鍵角色。"},{"en":"Family, school, and neighbourhood can shape how young people behave.","zh":"家庭、學校和社區可以塑造年輕人的行為。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a major influence.","zh":"這個短語指出主要影響因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in this arena","meaning":"在這個範疇","examples":[{"en":"Environment plays a key role in this arena.","zh":"環境在這個範疇中扮演關鍵角色。"},{"en":"In this arena means in this area of discussion, activity, or problem.","zh":"in this arena 指在這個討論、活動或問題範圍中。"},{"en":"In the arena of school discipline, communication between teachers and parents matters greatly.","zh":"在學校紀律這個範疇中，老師與家長之間的溝通非常重要。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the writer is focusing on a particular field.","zh":"這個短語表示作者正在集中於某一特定領域。"},{"en":"It is more formal than simply saying “in this area.”","zh":"它比簡單說 “in this area” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sociologists have found that","meaning":"社會學家發現","examples":[{"en":"Sociologists have found that many latchkey children come from dysfunctional families.","zh":"社會學家發現許多鑰匙兒童來自功能失調家庭。"},{"en":"Sociologists have found that means researchers who study society have discovered this through research.","zh":"sociologists have found that 指研究社會的學者透過研究發現某事。"},{"en":"Sociologists have found that loneliness can affect people in both rich and poor communities.","zh":"社會學家發現孤單可以影響富裕和貧窮社群中的人。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a research-based social observation.","zh":"這個短語引出基於研究的社會觀察。"},{"en":"It gives more authority than a personal opinion.","zh":"它比個人意見更具權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"dysfunctional families","meaning":"功能失調家庭","examples":[{"en":"Many latchkey children are raised in dysfunctional families.","zh":"許多鑰匙兒童在功能失調家庭中長大。"},{"en":"Dysfunctional families are families with serious problems in communication, care, safety, or emotional support.","zh":"dysfunctional families 指在溝通、照顧、安全或情感支援上有嚴重問題的家庭。"},{"en":"In a dysfunctional family, children may learn to hide feelings instead of asking for help.","zh":"在功能失調家庭中，孩子可能學會隱藏感受，而不是求助。"},{"en":"Family dysfunction can affect a child’s trust, behaviour, and school performance.","zh":"家庭功能失調可以影響孩子的信任、行為和學校表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unhealthy family systems, not ordinary disagreements.","zh":"這個短語描述不健康的家庭系統，而不是普通分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be taught by example","meaning":"透過榜樣被教懂","examples":[{"en":"Children may be taught by example to behave in unhealthy ways.","zh":"兒童可能透過榜樣被教懂以不健康方式行事。"},{"en":"To be taught by example means to learn by watching what others do.","zh":"be taught by example 指透過觀察他人的行為來學習。"},{"en":"A child may be taught by example to say thank you if adults around them always do so.","zh":"如果身邊成人總是說謝謝，孩子可能透過榜樣學會說謝謝。"},{"en":"Bad examples can teach children harmful behaviour even without direct instruction.","zh":"壞榜樣即使沒有直接教導，也可以教會孩子有害行為。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that behaviour can be learned through observation.","zh":"這個短語顯示行為可以透過觀察學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"manipulative","meaning":"操控別人的","examples":[{"en":"Some latchkey children learn to be manipulative.","zh":"有些鑰匙兒童學會操控別人。"},{"en":"Manipulative means using people or situations unfairly to get what one wants.","zh":"manipulative 指不公平地利用人或情況來得到自己想要的東西。"},{"en":"A manipulative person may pretend to be helpless so others will do their work.","zh":"操控別人的人可能假裝無助，讓他人替自己做事。"},{"en":"Children may become manipulative if hiding truth helps them avoid punishment at home.","zh":"如果隱瞞真相有助孩子避開家中懲罰，他們可能變得操控別人。"},{"en":"This word describes controlling behaviour, not healthy persuasion.","zh":"這個字描述控制他人的行為，而不是健康說服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"secretive","meaning":"隱瞞的；秘密的","examples":[{"en":"Some children become secretive about their living situation.","zh":"有些孩子對自己的生活狀況變得隱瞞。"},{"en":"Secretive means unwilling to share information or feelings openly.","zh":"secretive 指不願公開分享資訊或感受。"},{"en":"A student may become secretive if they fear being judged by classmates.","zh":"如果學生害怕被同學評價，可能變得隱瞞。"},{"en":"Children may hide their home situation if they feel ashamed or unsafe.","zh":"如果孩子感到羞恥或不安全，可能隱瞞家庭情況。"},{"en":"This word describes a pattern of keeping things hidden.","zh":"這個字描述把事情藏起來的模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unpredictable","meaning":"難以預測的","examples":[{"en":"Dysfunctional family environments may make children unpredictable.","zh":"功能失調家庭環境可能令孩子變得難以預測。"},{"en":"Unpredictable means difficult to know or guess in advance.","zh":"unpredictable 指難以事先知道或猜測。"},{"en":"An unpredictable child may be calm one moment and angry the next.","zh":"難以預測的孩子可能上一刻冷靜，下一刻憤怒。"},{"en":"Unstable environments can make behaviour harder to predict because children are always reacting to stress.","zh":"不穩定環境可以令行為更難預測，因為孩子總是在回應壓力。"},{"en":"This word describes irregular or uncertain behaviour.","zh":"這個字描述不規律或不確定的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"instinctively develop","meaning":"本能地發展出","examples":[{"en":"Some children instinctively develop ways to hide the truth.","zh":"有些孩子本能地發展出隱瞞真相的方法。"},{"en":"To instinctively develop something means to form it naturally without being formally taught.","zh":"instinctively develop something 指在沒有正式教導下自然形成某物。"},{"en":"A shy child may instinctively develop quiet ways to avoid attention.","zh":"害羞孩子可能本能地發展出安靜避開注意的方法。"},{"en":"Children in stressful homes may develop protective habits before they can explain them.","zh":"壓力家庭中的孩子可能在能解釋前已發展出保護自己的習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes natural adaptation to a situation.","zh":"這個短語描述對情況的自然適應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a sense of timing","meaning":"時機感","examples":[{"en":"Some children develop a sense of timing and emotional control.","zh":"有些孩子發展出時機感和情緒控制。"},{"en":"A sense of timing means knowing when to say or do something.","zh":"sense of timing 指知道何時說或做某事。"},{"en":"A student with a good sense of timing knows when to ask a teacher for help.","zh":"有良好時機感的學生知道何時向老師求助。"},{"en":"Children may learn timing if speaking at the wrong moment causes trouble at home.","zh":"如果在錯誤時刻說話會在家中引起麻煩，孩子可能學會掌握時機。"},{"en":"This phrase describes judgement about the right moment.","zh":"這個短語描述對合適時刻的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"manage their emotions","meaning":"管理自己的情緒","examples":[{"en":"Latchkey children may learn to manage their emotions carefully.","zh":"鑰匙兒童可能學會小心管理自己的情緒。"},{"en":"To manage emotions means to control, understand, or respond to feelings in a suitable way.","zh":"manage emotions 指以合適方式控制、理解或回應情緒。"},{"en":"A student manages anger well if they breathe deeply instead of shouting.","zh":"如果學生深呼吸而不是大叫，就是良好管理憤怒。"},{"en":"Children may learn emotional control when they must avoid conflict at home.","zh":"當孩子必須避免家中衝突，可能學會情緒控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes handling feelings, not pretending they do not exist.","zh":"這個短語描述處理感受，而不是假裝感受不存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be directly used to","meaning":"可被直接用來","examples":[{"en":"These skills can be directly used to create a false image.","zh":"這些技能可被直接用來製造假象。"},{"en":"To be directly used to do something means to be applied for that purpose without many extra steps.","zh":"be directly used to do something 指不用許多額外步驟，直接應用於某目的。"},{"en":"A phone camera can be directly used to scan homework pages.","zh":"手機相機可被直接用來掃描功課頁。"},{"en":"Skills learned in one situation may later be used for helpful or harmful purposes.","zh":"在一種情況學到的技能，日後可能被用於有益或有害目的。"},{"en":"This phrase shows practical application.","zh":"這個短語顯示實際應用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"portray a false picture of","meaning":"描繪……的假象","examples":[{"en":"Children may portray a false picture of themselves.","zh":"兒童可能描繪自己的假象。"},{"en":"To portray a false picture of something means to present it in a misleading or untrue way.","zh":"portray a false picture of something 指以誤導或不真實方式呈現某事。"},{"en":"A student may portray a false picture of confidence while feeling anxious inside.","zh":"學生可能表現出自信的假象，但內心感到焦慮。"},{"en":"People sometimes create false pictures to avoid shame, punishment, or questions.","zh":"人們有時製造假象，以避免羞恥、懲罰或追問。"},{"en":"This phrase describes showing an image that hides the truth.","zh":"這個短語描述展示掩蓋真相的形象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"living situation","meaning":"生活狀況","examples":[{"en":"They may hide the truth about their living situation.","zh":"他們可能隱瞞關於自己生活狀況的真相。"},{"en":"Living situation means the conditions in which someone lives at home.","zh":"living situation 指某人在家中的生活條件。"},{"en":"A child’s living situation includes who is at home, how safe the home is, and whether support is available.","zh":"孩子的生活狀況包括誰在家、家是否安全，以及是否有支援。"},{"en":"Difficult living situations can affect schoolwork, mood, and behaviour.","zh":"困難生活狀況可以影響功課、情緒和行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes home circumstances, not only the building itself.","zh":"這個短語描述家庭處境，而不只是建築物本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make the decision","meaning":"作出決定","examples":[{"en":"Parents must make the decision about whether a child is ready to be alone.","zh":"父母必須作出孩子是否準備好獨處的決定。"},{"en":"To make the decision means to choose after thinking about the situation.","zh":"make the decision 指思考情況後作出選擇。"},{"en":"A parent may make the decision to let a teenager walk to school alone.","zh":"家長可能作出決定，讓青少年獨自步行上學。"},{"en":"Important decisions should consider safety, maturity, and available support.","zh":"重要決定應考慮安全、成熟程度和可用支援。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises responsibility for choosing.","zh":"這個短語強調作出選擇的責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be ready to","meaning":"準備好去","examples":[{"en":"Some children are ready to be home alone earlier than others.","zh":"有些孩子比其他孩子更早準備好獨自在家。"},{"en":"To be ready to do something means to have enough ability, maturity, or preparation to do it safely.","zh":"be ready to do something 指有足夠能力、成熟程度或準備安全地做某事。"},{"en":"A child may be ready to cross the road alone only after learning traffic rules.","zh":"孩子可能只有在學懂交通規則後，才準備好獨自過馬路。"},{"en":"Readiness depends on the child and the situation, not age alone.","zh":"準備程度取決於孩子和情況，而不只是年齡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparedness for responsibility.","zh":"這個短語描述對責任的準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"home alone","meaning":"獨自在家","examples":[{"en":"Parents must decide when a child is ready to be home alone.","zh":"父母必須決定孩子何時準備好獨自在家。"},{"en":"Home alone means at home without any other person there to supervise or help.","zh":"home alone 指在家中沒有其他人監督或幫助。"},{"en":"A child home alone should know how to call a parent or emergency service.","zh":"獨自在家的孩子應知道如何打電話給父母或緊急服務。"},{"en":"Being home alone can build independence, but it can also create risks.","zh":"獨自在家可以建立獨立性，但也可能帶來風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a child’s unsupervised time at home.","zh":"這個短語描述孩子在家中無人監督的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"personality characteristics","meaning":"性格特徵","examples":[{"en":"Personality characteristics are useful criteria for judging readiness.","zh":"性格特徵是判斷準備程度的有用標準。"},{"en":"Personality characteristics are stable features of how a person thinks, feels, and behaves.","zh":"personality characteristics 指一個人思考、感受和行為方式中較穩定的特徵。"},{"en":"Calmness, honesty, and responsibility are personality characteristics parents may consider.","zh":"冷靜、誠實和責任感都是父母可能考慮的性格特徵。"},{"en":"A child’s personality affects how they respond when alone or under pressure.","zh":"孩子的性格會影響他們獨處或受壓時如何反應。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to personal traits, not academic results.","zh":"這個短語指個人特質，而不是學業成績。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"maturity","meaning":"成熟程度","examples":[{"en":"Maturity helps determine whether a child can stay home alone.","zh":"成熟程度有助判斷孩子能否獨自在家。"},{"en":"Maturity means the ability to behave sensibly, responsibly, and calmly.","zh":"maturity 指明智、負責和冷靜行事的能力。"},{"en":"A mature child tells an adult when something goes wrong instead of hiding it.","zh":"成熟的孩子出事時會告訴成人，而不是隱瞞。"},{"en":"Maturity matters because being alone requires judgement and self-control.","zh":"成熟程度很重要，因為獨處需要判斷力和自制力。"},{"en":"This word describes readiness beyond age.","zh":"這個字描述超越年齡的準備程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"useful criteria for","meaning":"判斷……的有用標準","examples":[{"en":"Skills and maturity are useful criteria for determining readiness.","zh":"技能和成熟程度是判斷準備程度的有用標準。"},{"en":"Useful criteria for something are helpful standards for judging it.","zh":"useful criteria for something 指有助判斷某事的標準。"},{"en":"Attendance, effort, and improvement are useful criteria for judging a student’s progress.","zh":"出席、努力和進步是判斷學生進展的有用標準。"},{"en":"Clear criteria help people make fairer and safer decisions.","zh":"清楚標準幫助人作出較公平和安全的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the standards used in evaluation.","zh":"這個短語描述評估時使用的標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"determine readiness","meaning":"判斷準備程度","examples":[{"en":"Parents need to determine a child’s readiness to be home alone.","zh":"父母需要判斷孩子獨自在家的準備程度。"},{"en":"To determine readiness means to judge whether someone is prepared for a task or responsibility.","zh":"determine readiness 指判斷某人是否已準備好承擔任務或責任。"},{"en":"A teacher may determine readiness for an exam by checking practice results.","zh":"老師可能透過檢查練習結果來判斷學生考試準備程度。"},{"en":"Readiness should be judged before giving a child new independence.","zh":"給孩子新的獨立性前，應先判斷準備程度。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on careful assessment before action.","zh":"這個短語集中於行動前的仔細評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"generally change much with age","meaning":"通常不會隨年齡大幅改變","examples":[{"en":"Personality does not generally change much with age.","zh":"性格通常不會隨年齡大幅改變。"},{"en":"Does not generally change much with age means usually stays fairly stable as someone gets older.","zh":"does not generally change much with age 指隨着年齡增長通常仍相當穩定。"},{"en":"A shy child may become more confident, but the basic tendency may not change much with age.","zh":"害羞孩子可能變得更有信心，但基本傾向未必隨年齡大幅改變。"},{"en":"Some reactions can be modified even when personality remains stable.","zh":"即使性格保持穩定，有些反應仍可以被調整。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests age alone may not transform a child’s character.","zh":"這個短語暗示單靠年齡未必能改變孩子性格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"learn to modify","meaning":"學會調整","examples":[{"en":"Children can learn to modify some of their reactions.","zh":"兒童可以學會調整自己的一些反應。"},{"en":"To learn to modify something means to learn how to change or adjust it.","zh":"learn to modify something 指學會如何改變或調整某事。"},{"en":"A student can learn to modify their tone so they sound more polite in discussions.","zh":"學生可以學會調整語氣，使討論時聽起來更有禮貌。"},{"en":"Children may not change their personality completely, but they can adjust behaviour.","zh":"孩子未必完全改變性格，但可以調整行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning controlled change.","zh":"這個短語描述學習有控制的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"what is expected of them","meaning":"別人對他們的期望","examples":[{"en":"Children learn what is expected of them as they grow.","zh":"孩子隨着成長會學會別人對他們的期望。"},{"en":"What is expected of them means the behaviour, responsibility, or standard others want from them.","zh":"what is expected of them 指別人希望他們有的行為、責任或標準。"},{"en":"A student learns what is expected of them when a teacher explains homework rules clearly.","zh":"當老師清楚解釋功課規則，學生就會知道別人對他們的期望。"},{"en":"Clear expectations help children behave more responsibly.","zh":"清楚期望幫助孩子更負責地行事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social or family expectations.","zh":"這個短語描述社會或家庭期望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"find it difficult to","meaning":"覺得……很困難","examples":[{"en":"Some children find it very difficult to be alone.","zh":"有些孩子覺得獨處很困難。"},{"en":"To find it difficult to do something means to feel that doing it is hard.","zh":"find it difficult to do something 指覺得做某事很困難。"},{"en":"A shy student may find it difficult to speak in front of the class.","zh":"害羞學生可能覺得在全班面前說話很困難。"},{"en":"Children who find being alone difficult may need gradual practice and reassurance.","zh":"覺得獨處困難的孩子可能需要逐步練習和安撫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes personal difficulty, not impossibility.","zh":"這個短語描述個人困難，而不是不可能做到。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"gradual exposure to","meaning":"逐步接觸","examples":[{"en":"Some children need gradual exposure to being alone.","zh":"有些孩子需要逐步接觸獨處。"},{"en":"Gradual exposure to something means slowly becoming familiar with it step by step.","zh":"gradual exposure to something 指一步一步慢慢熟悉某事。"},{"en":"A nervous swimmer may need gradual exposure to deep water before swimming alone.","zh":"緊張的游泳者可能需要逐步接觸深水，才獨自游泳。"},{"en":"Gradual exposure can reduce fear because the child learns the situation is manageable.","zh":"逐步接觸可以減少恐懼，因為孩子學到情況是可應付的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow, careful introduction to something difficult.","zh":"這個短語描述對困難事物的緩慢而小心引入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"become accustomed to","meaning":"習慣於","examples":[{"en":"Some children need time to become accustomed to being by themselves.","zh":"有些孩子需要時間習慣獨自一人。"},{"en":"To become accustomed to something means to get used to it.","zh":"become accustomed to something 指逐漸習慣某事。"},{"en":"A student may need a few weeks to become accustomed to a new school timetable.","zh":"學生可能需要幾星期來習慣新的學校時間表。"},{"en":"Children become more comfortable when new experiences are introduced slowly.","zh":"當新經驗慢慢引入，孩子會變得較自在。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adjustment over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間適應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"being by themselves","meaning":"獨自一人","examples":[{"en":"Some children need time to become comfortable being by themselves.","zh":"有些孩子需要時間習慣獨自一人。"},{"en":"Being by themselves means being alone without other people nearby.","zh":"being by themselves 指身邊沒有其他人陪同。"},{"en":"A child may practise being by themselves for ten minutes while a parent stays nearby.","zh":"孩子可能先練習獨自一人十分鐘，而父母留在附近。"},{"en":"Being alone can feel different depending on age, confidence, and safety.","zh":"獨處感受會因年齡、自信和安全程度而不同。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the experience of solitude.","zh":"這個短語集中於獨處的經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"adapt easily","meaning":"容易適應","examples":[{"en":"Some children adapt easily to being home alone.","zh":"有些孩子容易適應獨自在家。"},{"en":"To adapt easily means to adjust to a new situation without much difficulty.","zh":"adapt easily 指毫不困難地適應新情況。"},{"en":"A student who adapts easily to a new class quickly learns routines and makes friends.","zh":"容易適應新班級的學生會很快學會常規並結交朋友。"},{"en":"Children who adapt easily may still need safety rules and check-ins.","zh":"容易適應的孩子仍需要安全規則和定期聯絡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes smooth adjustment.","zh":"這個短語描述順利適應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"fearful","meaning":"害怕的","examples":[{"en":"A child who is ready to be alone is not fearful.","zh":"準備好獨處的孩子不會害怕。"},{"en":"Fearful means feeling afraid or easily frightened.","zh":"fearful 指感到害怕或容易受驚。"},{"en":"A fearful child may panic when hearing an unexpected sound at home.","zh":"害怕的孩子在家中聽到意外聲音時可能驚慌。"},{"en":"Fear can make it harder for children to make calm decisions when alone.","zh":"恐懼會令孩子獨處時更難作出冷靜決定。"},{"en":"This word describes emotional readiness, not physical ability.","zh":"這個字描述情緒準備，而不是身體能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"feel at ease","meaning":"感到自在","examples":[{"en":"A ready child feels at ease in the world.","zh":"準備好的孩子在世界中感到自在。"},{"en":"To feel at ease means to feel calm, comfortable, and not anxious.","zh":"feel at ease 指感到冷靜、舒服和不焦慮。"},{"en":"A student feels at ease in class when they know mistakes will be treated kindly.","zh":"當學生知道錯誤會被友善對待，就會在課堂中感到自在。"},{"en":"Children who feel at ease are more likely to respond calmly to small problems.","zh":"感到自在的孩子更可能冷靜回應小問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional comfort and security.","zh":"這個短語描述情緒上的舒適和安全感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"self-confident","meaning":"有自信的","examples":[{"en":"A child who is ready to be alone is self-confident.","zh":"準備好獨處的孩子是有自信的。"},{"en":"Self-confident means believing in one’s ability to handle situations.","zh":"self-confident 指相信自己有能力處理情況。"},{"en":"A self-confident student can ask for help without feeling ashamed.","zh":"有自信的學生可以求助而不感到羞恥。"},{"en":"Confidence helps children stay calm when a minor problem happens at home.","zh":"自信幫助孩子在家中出現小問題時保持冷靜。"},{"en":"This word describes inner belief in one’s own ability.","zh":"這個字描述對自己能力的內在信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be calm","meaning":"保持冷靜","examples":[{"en":"A ready child is calm when something unexpected happens.","zh":"準備好的孩子在意外事情發生時會保持冷靜。"},{"en":"To be calm means to stay controlled and not panic.","zh":"be calm 指保持控制而不驚慌。"},{"en":"A calm student reads the question again instead of crying when they do not understand it.","zh":"冷靜的學生不明白題目時，會重新讀題，而不是哭。"},{"en":"Calmness helps children follow safety rules during small emergencies.","zh":"冷靜有助孩子在小型緊急情況中遵守安全規則。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled behaviour under pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述壓力下受控的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be excitable","meaning":"容易激動的","examples":[{"en":"A child who is too excitable may not be ready to stay alone.","zh":"太容易激動的孩子可能未準備好獨處。"},{"en":"To be excitable means to become excited, upset, or emotional very easily.","zh":"be excitable 指很容易變得興奮、不安或情緒化。"},{"en":"An excitable child may shout or run around when something surprising happens.","zh":"容易激動的孩子在驚訝事情發生時可能大叫或四處跑。"},{"en":"High excitability can make it harder to think clearly in an emergency.","zh":"高度易激動會令人在緊急情況中更難清楚思考。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a temperament that may affect readiness.","zh":"這個短語描述可能影響準備程度的性情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"something unexpected happens","meaning":"意外事情發生","examples":[{"en":"A mature child stays calm when something unexpected happens.","zh":"成熟的孩子在意外事情發生時會保持冷靜。"},{"en":"Something unexpected happens means an event occurs without warning or planning.","zh":"something unexpected happens 指某事件在沒有預警或計劃下發生。"},{"en":"A child may need to know what to do if the lights go out unexpectedly.","zh":"如果突然停電，孩子可能需要知道應該怎樣做。"},{"en":"Unexpected events test whether a child can think clearly without an adult nearby.","zh":"意外事件會測試孩子在沒有成人附近時能否清楚思考。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sudden situations that require judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述需要判斷的突發情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"outgoing","meaning":"外向的","examples":[{"en":"An outgoing child may talk more readily about feelings.","zh":"外向的孩子可能較願意談論感受。"},{"en":"Outgoing means friendly, sociable, and willing to speak with others.","zh":"outgoing 指友善、善於社交並願意與他人說話。"},{"en":"An outgoing student may join group activities quickly in a new class.","zh":"外向學生在新班級中可能很快參與小組活動。"},{"en":"Outgoing children may find it easier to tell adults when something worries them.","zh":"外向孩子可能較容易告訴成人自己擔心的事。"},{"en":"This word describes social openness.","zh":"這個字描述社交上的開放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"talk about feelings and thoughts","meaning":"談論感受和想法","examples":[{"en":"Children should be able to talk about their feelings and thoughts.","zh":"兒童應能談論自己的感受和想法。"},{"en":"To talk about feelings and thoughts means to express emotions and ideas in words.","zh":"talk about feelings and thoughts 指用語言表達情緒和想法。"},{"en":"A child who can say “I feel scared” is talking about feelings clearly.","zh":"能說「我感到害怕」的孩子，就是清楚談論感受。"},{"en":"Communication helps adults notice problems before they become serious.","zh":"溝通幫助成人在問題變嚴重前察覺它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional and mental communication.","zh":"這個短語描述情緒和思想上的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"readily with parents","meaning":"樂意與父母……","examples":[{"en":"A ready child talks readily with parents and others.","zh":"準備好的孩子樂意與父母和其他人交談。"},{"en":"Readily with parents means willingly and easily with parents.","zh":"readily with parents 指願意且容易地與父母溝通。"},{"en":"A child who speaks readily with parents may ask for help before taking a risk.","zh":"樂意與父母交談的孩子可能會在冒險前先求助。"},{"en":"Easy communication makes being home alone safer because problems can be reported quickly.","zh":"容易溝通令獨自在家更安全，因為問題可以迅速報告。"},{"en":"This phrase describes open communication with trusted adults.","zh":"這個短語描述與可信成人的開放溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"admit wrongdoing","meaning":"承認錯事","examples":[{"en":"A mature child admits wrongdoing.","zh":"成熟的孩子會承認錯事。"},{"en":"To admit wrongdoing means to say honestly that one has done something wrong.","zh":"admit wrongdoing 指誠實承認自己做錯了事。"},{"en":"A student admits wrongdoing when they tell the teacher they copied homework.","zh":"學生告訴老師自己抄功課，就是承認錯事。"},{"en":"Admitting mistakes helps adults correct problems before they become dangerous.","zh":"承認錯誤幫助成人在問題變危險前糾正它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows honesty and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語顯示誠實和責任感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"expect disapproval","meaning":"預期會被責備","examples":[{"en":"A child may admit wrongdoing even when expecting disapproval.","zh":"孩子即使預期會被責備，也可能承認錯事。"},{"en":"To expect disapproval means to believe others will criticise or be unhappy with what you did.","zh":"expect disapproval 指相信他人會批評或不滿自己所做的事。"},{"en":"A student may expect disapproval after breaking a classroom rule.","zh":"學生違反課室規則後，可能預期會被責備。"},{"en":"Admitting the truth despite expected disapproval shows maturity.","zh":"即使預期會被責備仍承認真相，顯示成熟。"},{"en":"This phrase describes anticipating criticism.","zh":"這個短語描述預料會受到批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"have courage enough to","meaning":"有足夠勇氣去","examples":[{"en":"A mature child has courage enough to resist pressure.","zh":"成熟的孩子有足夠勇氣去抵抗壓力。"},{"en":"To have courage enough to do something means to be brave enough to do it.","zh":"have courage enough to do something 指有足夠勇氣做某事。"},{"en":"A student has courage enough to say no when friends ask them to cheat.","zh":"當朋友要求作弊，學生有足夠勇氣拒絕。"},{"en":"Courage matters when doing the right thing may upset others.","zh":"當做正確的事可能令他人不滿，勇氣就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bravery in a difficult choice.","zh":"這個短語描述在困難選擇中的勇氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"resist pressure from","meaning":"抵抗來自……的壓力","examples":[{"en":"A ready child can resist pressure from friends and others.","zh":"準備好的孩子能抵抗來自朋友和其他人的壓力。"},{"en":"To resist pressure from someone means to refuse to do something just because they push you to do it.","zh":"resist pressure from someone 指拒絕只因他人施壓而做某事。"},{"en":"A teenager resists pressure from friends when they refuse to smoke.","zh":"青少年拒絕吸煙時，就是抵抗來自朋友的壓力。"},{"en":"Children who can resist pressure are safer when adults are not nearby.","zh":"能抵抗壓力的孩子在成人不在附近時更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes standing firm against influence.","zh":"這個短語描述面對影響仍堅持立場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in many communities","meaning":"在許多社區","examples":[{"en":"In many communities, activities are available for school-age children.","zh":"在許多社區，有供學齡兒童參加的活動。"},{"en":"In many communities means in many local areas or neighbourhoods.","zh":"in many communities 指在許多本地區域或社區中。"},{"en":"In many communities, libraries provide free reading programmes for children.","zh":"在許多社區，圖書館為兒童提供免費閱讀計劃。"},{"en":"Community resources can reduce the risks children face after school.","zh":"社區資源可以減少孩子放學後面對的風險。"},{"en":"This phrase points to support available across different local places.","zh":"這個短語指出不同本地地方可用的支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"school-age children","meaning":"學齡兒童","examples":[{"en":"There are activities for school-age children whose parents work.","zh":"有些活動是為父母工作的學齡兒童而設。"},{"en":"School-age children are children old enough to attend school.","zh":"school-age children 指已達上學年齡的兒童。"},{"en":"School-age children may need after-school care because parents are still at work.","zh":"學齡兒童可能需要課後照顧，因為父母仍在工作。"},{"en":"Activities for this age group should match their safety, learning, and social needs.","zh":"為這個年齡群體而設的活動應符合其安全、學習和社交需要。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies children by schooling stage.","zh":"這個短語按上學階段辨認兒童。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"whose parents work","meaning":"父母工作的","examples":[{"en":"Some children need afternoon activities because their parents work.","zh":"有些孩子因父母工作而需要下午活動。"},{"en":"Whose parents work means children whose parents have jobs and may not be home.","zh":"whose parents work 指父母有工作、可能不在家的孩子。"},{"en":"A student whose parents work late may stay in an after-school centre until evening.","zh":"父母工作到很晚的學生可能留在課後中心直到晚上。"},{"en":"Parental work schedules can create gaps in supervision.","zh":"父母工作時間表可能造成監督空檔。"},{"en":"This phrase links children’s needs with parents’ employment.","zh":"這個短語把兒童需要與父母就業連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"cannot be at home","meaning":"不能在家","examples":[{"en":"Some parents cannot be at home in the afternoon.","zh":"有些父母下午不能在家。"},{"en":"Cannot be at home means are unable to stay at home because of work or other duties.","zh":"cannot be at home 指因工作或其他責任而無法留在家中。"},{"en":"A parent who works in a hospital cannot be at home when the afternoon shift begins.","zh":"在醫院工作的父母若下午班開始，就不能在家。"},{"en":"If parents cannot be at home, children may need supervised activities elsewhere.","zh":"如果父母不能在家，孩子可能需要在其他地方參加受監督活動。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why outside support may be necessary.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何外部支援可能必要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in the afternoon","meaning":"在下午","examples":[{"en":"Some children need supervision in the afternoon.","zh":"有些孩子在下午需要監督。"},{"en":"In the afternoon means during the time after noon and before evening.","zh":"in the afternoon 指中午之後、晚上之前的時間。"},{"en":"A child may attend a homework club in the afternoon while parents work.","zh":"父母工作時，孩子可能在下午參加功課班。"},{"en":"Afternoon supervision matters because school often ends before the workday ends.","zh":"下午監督很重要，因為學校常比工作日更早結束。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a key after-school time period.","zh":"這個短語指出關鍵課後時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the importance of","meaning":"……的重要性","examples":[{"en":"Professionals stress the importance of looking into these activities.","zh":"專業人士強調了解這些活動的重要性。"},{"en":"The importance of something means why it matters or why it should be taken seriously.","zh":"importance of something 指某事為何重要或為何應被認真對待。"},{"en":"Teachers stress the importance of sleep before exams.","zh":"老師強調考試前睡眠的重要性。"},{"en":"When adults understand the importance of activities, they are more likely to arrange them for children.","zh":"當成人理解活動的重要性，他們更可能為孩子安排活動。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the value or seriousness of something.","zh":"這個短語引出某事的價值或嚴重性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"look into","meaning":"了解；調查","examples":[{"en":"Parents should look into after-school activities.","zh":"父母應該了解課後活動。"},{"en":"To look into something means to investigate or find out more about it.","zh":"look into something 指調查或進一步了解某事。"},{"en":"A parent may look into a tutoring centre before enrolling a child.","zh":"家長可能在為孩子報名前先了解補習中心。"},{"en":"Looking into options helps families choose safe and suitable support.","zh":"了解不同選項幫助家庭選擇安全且合適的支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful checking before making a decision.","zh":"這個短語描述作決定前的仔細查核。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be stressed by","meaning":"由……強調","examples":[{"en":"The importance of these activities is stressed by child development professionals.","zh":"這些活動的重要性由兒童發展專業人士強調。"},{"en":"To be stressed by someone means to be emphasised strongly by that person or group.","zh":"be stressed by someone 指被某人或某群體強烈強調。"},{"en":"The need for regular sleep is stressed by doctors and teachers.","zh":"規律睡眠的需要由醫生和老師強調。"},{"en":"When experts stress a point, they want people to take it seriously.","zh":"當專家強調某點，他們希望人們認真看待它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows who emphasises an idea.","zh":"這個短語顯示誰在強調某想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"child development professionals","meaning":"兒童發展專業人士","examples":[{"en":"Child development professionals recommend supervised activities.","zh":"兒童發展專業人士建議受監督的活動。"},{"en":"Child development professionals are experts who study children’s growth, behaviour, learning, and emotional needs.","zh":"child development professionals 指研究兒童成長、行為、學習和情感需要的專家。"},{"en":"A child development professional may advise parents on whether a child is ready to be alone.","zh":"兒童發展專業人士可能建議父母孩子是否準備好獨處。"},{"en":"Their advice helps families make decisions based on children’s needs, not convenience only.","zh":"他們的建議幫助家庭根據孩子需要，而不只是方便程度作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to specialists in children’s development.","zh":"這個短語指兒童發展方面的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"re-examine attitudes and values","meaning":"重新審視態度和價值觀","examples":[{"en":"Young people re-examine their attitudes and values between ages 10 and 15.","zh":"年輕人在10至15歲之間會重新審視自己的態度和價值觀。"},{"en":"To re-examine attitudes and values means to think again about one’s beliefs and what matters.","zh":"re-examine attitudes and values 指重新思考自己的信念和重視的事物。"},{"en":"A teenager may re-examine values after meeting friends with different backgrounds.","zh":"青少年遇到不同背景的朋友後，可能重新審視價值觀。"},{"en":"This process can make young people more open, but also more vulnerable to pressure.","zh":"這個過程可以令年輕人更開放，但也更容易受壓力影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a normal part of growing up.","zh":"這個短語描述成長中的正常部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be pressured by peers","meaning":"受到同輩壓力","examples":[{"en":"Young people are being pressured by peers.","zh":"年輕人正受到同輩壓力。"},{"en":"To be pressured by peers means to feel pushed by people of the same age group to act in a certain way.","zh":"be pressured by peers 指被同一年齡群體推動去以某種方式行事。"},{"en":"A teenager may be pressured by peers to skip class or try smoking.","zh":"青少年可能受到同輩壓力去逃課或嘗試吸煙。"},{"en":"Peer pressure can be stronger when no trusted adult is nearby.","zh":"當沒有可信成人在旁，同輩壓力可能更強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social influence from friends or classmates.","zh":"這個短語描述來自朋友或同學的社會影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"responsible adults","meaning":"負責任的成年人","examples":[{"en":"Young people need protection from responsible adults.","zh":"年輕人需要負責任的成年人保護。"},{"en":"Responsible adults are adults who can guide, protect, and make sensible decisions for children.","zh":"responsible adults 指能指導、保護並為兒童作出明智決定的成年人。"},{"en":"A coach, teacher, parent, or neighbour can be a responsible adult after school.","zh":"教練、老師、父母或鄰居都可以成為課後負責任的成年人。"},{"en":"Responsible adults help young people judge risks and resist harmful pressure.","zh":"負責任的成年人幫助年輕人判斷風險並抵抗有害壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises safe adult guidance.","zh":"這個短語強調安全的成人指導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"examine and counter","meaning":"審視並抵制","examples":[{"en":"Adults help children examine and counter harmful attitudes.","zh":"成人幫助孩子審視並抵制有害態度。"},{"en":"To examine and counter something means to think about it carefully and then resist or challenge it.","zh":"examine and counter something 指仔細思考某事，然後抵抗或挑戰它。"},{"en":"A teacher helps students examine and counter racist jokes by discussing why they hurt people.","zh":"老師透過討論種族笑話為何傷害人，幫助學生審視並抵制它們。"},{"en":"Children need guidance to recognise harmful ideas before accepting them.","zh":"孩子在接受有害想法前，需要指導去辨認它們。"},{"en":"This phrase combines understanding with resistance.","zh":"這個短語結合理解和抵抗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"harmful attitudes","meaning":"有害態度","examples":[{"en":"Young people may need help countering harmful attitudes.","zh":"年輕人可能需要幫助去抵制有害態度。"},{"en":"Harmful attitudes are beliefs or ways of thinking that can hurt people or lead to bad behaviour.","zh":"harmful attitudes 指可能傷害他人或導致壞行為的信念或思考方式。"},{"en":"Thinking that violence proves strength is a harmful attitude.","zh":"認為暴力證明力量是一種有害態度。"},{"en":"Harmful attitudes can spread through peers, media, or family examples.","zh":"有害態度可以透過同輩、媒體或家庭榜樣傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to dangerous ideas, not just unpopular opinions.","zh":"這個短語指危險想法，而不只是冷門意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"activities available","meaning":"可供參加的活動","examples":[{"en":"The activities available vary in cost and popularity.","zh":"可供參加的活動在費用和受歡迎程度上各有不同。"},{"en":"Activities available are the activities people can choose or join.","zh":"activities available 指人們可以選擇或參加的活動。"},{"en":"Activities available after school may include sports, music, tutoring, or library clubs.","zh":"放學後可供參加的活動可能包括運動、音樂、補習或圖書館小組。"},{"en":"When more activities are available, children have safer ways to spend time.","zh":"當有更多活動可供參加，孩子就有更安全的方式消磨時間。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on options that can actually be accessed.","zh":"這個短語集中於實際可接觸的選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"vary in cost","meaning":"費用各有不同","examples":[{"en":"After-school programmes vary in cost.","zh":"課後計劃費用各有不同。"},{"en":"To vary in cost means to have different prices.","zh":"vary in cost 指價格不同。"},{"en":"Sports clubs may vary in cost depending on equipment, teachers, and venue fees.","zh":"運動班可能因器材、教師和場地費而費用各有不同。"},{"en":"If activities vary in cost, some families may have fewer choices.","zh":"如果活動費用各有不同，有些家庭可能選擇較少。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how expensive different options are.","zh":"這個短語比較不同選項有多昂貴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"rewarding","meaning":"有益的；有回報的","examples":[{"en":"Some activities are more rewarding than others.","zh":"有些活動比其他活動更有益。"},{"en":"Rewarding means useful, satisfying, or worth the effort.","zh":"rewarding 指有用、令人滿足或值得付出努力。"},{"en":"Volunteering can be rewarding because students learn responsibility and empathy.","zh":"做義工可以很有回報，因為學生學到責任感和同理心。"},{"en":"Rewarding activities give children skills, confidence, or meaningful enjoyment.","zh":"有益的活動給孩子技能、自信或有意義的樂趣。"},{"en":"This word describes value beyond simple entertainment.","zh":"這個字描述超越單純娛樂的價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be preferable to","meaning":"比……更可取","examples":[{"en":"All these activities are preferable to sitting at home.","zh":"所有這些活動都比坐在家中更可取。"},{"en":"To be preferable to something means to be better or more desirable than it.","zh":"be preferable to something 指比某事更好或更值得選擇。"},{"en":"A supervised study room is preferable to wandering around the street after school.","zh":"受監督的自修室比放學後在街上閒逛更可取。"},{"en":"An option is preferable when it is safer, healthier, or more useful.","zh":"當一個選項更安全、更健康或更有用，它就更可取。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly compares two choices.","zh":"這個短語清楚比較兩個選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"sitting at home","meaning":"坐在家中","examples":[{"en":"Supervised activities are better than sitting at home.","zh":"受監督活動比坐在家中更好。"},{"en":"Sitting at home means staying at home with little active or purposeful activity.","zh":"sitting at home 指留在家中，沒有多少主動或有目的活動。"},{"en":"A teenager may spend the whole afternoon sitting at home and scrolling on a phone.","zh":"青少年可能整個下午坐在家中滑手機。"},{"en":"Too much unstructured time at home can lead to boredom and loneliness.","zh":"太多沒有結構的家中時間可以導致沉悶和孤單。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests passivity or lack of engagement.","zh":"這個短語常暗示被動或缺乏參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"in front of the television","meaning":"在電視機前","examples":[{"en":"Children should not spend all afternoon in front of the television.","zh":"兒童不應整個下午都在電視機前度過。"},{"en":"In front of the television means sitting or staying where one watches TV.","zh":"in front of the television 指坐在或留在觀看電視的位置。"},{"en":"A child may spend hours in front of the television if no adult sets limits.","zh":"如果沒有成人設限，孩子可能在電視機前待上幾小時。"},{"en":"Too much time in front of the television can reduce exercise, homework, and conversation.","zh":"太多時間在電視機前會減少運動、功課和對話。"},{"en":"This phrase describes passive screen time.","zh":"這個短語描述被動螢幕時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"depending upon","meaning":"視乎","examples":[{"en":"Some programmes are free, depending upon the activity and the child’s age.","zh":"有些計劃免費，視乎活動和孩子年齡而定。"},{"en":"Depending upon means based on or determined by something.","zh":"depending upon 指根據或取決於某事。"},{"en":"A bus fare may change depending upon distance and passenger age.","zh":"巴士費可能視乎距離和乘客年齡而改變。"},{"en":"Costs vary because different activities need different staff, equipment, and spaces.","zh":"費用會不同，因為不同活動需要不同人手、器材和空間。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the factors that affect a result.","zh":"這個短語引出影響結果的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"particular activity","meaning":"特定活動","examples":[{"en":"The cost depends on the particular activity.","zh":"費用取決於特定活動。"},{"en":"A particular activity means the specific activity being discussed.","zh":"particular activity 指正在討論的某一項具體活動。"},{"en":"Swimming may cost more than reading club because that particular activity needs a pool and instructors.","zh":"游泳可能比閱讀會昂貴，因為該特定活動需要泳池和教練。"},{"en":"Different activities have different requirements, so prices may vary.","zh":"不同活動有不同要求，所以價格可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows attention to one specific option.","zh":"這個短語把注意力收窄到一個具體選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"offer the opportunity to","meaning":"提供機會去","examples":[{"en":"After-school programmes offer the opportunity to acquire skills.","zh":"課後計劃提供機會去獲得技能。"},{"en":"To offer the opportunity to do something means to give someone a chance to do it.","zh":"offer the opportunity to do something 指給某人機會做某事。"},{"en":"A debate club offers the opportunity to practise public speaking.","zh":"辯論學會提供機會去練習公開演說。"},{"en":"Opportunities matter because children cannot learn skills they never get to practise.","zh":"機會很重要，因為孩子無法學會從未練習過的技能。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a chance for growth or learning.","zh":"這個短語突出成長或學習的機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"acquire skills and knowledge","meaning":"獲得技能和知識","examples":[{"en":"Children can acquire skills and knowledge through activities.","zh":"兒童可以透過活動獲得技能和知識。"},{"en":"To acquire skills and knowledge means to gain abilities and understanding through learning or practice.","zh":"acquire skills and knowledge 指透過學習或練習獲得能力和理解。"},{"en":"A child can acquire teamwork skills and sports knowledge by joining a basketball club.","zh":"孩子參加籃球會可以獲得團隊合作技能和運動知識。"},{"en":"Skills and knowledge grow when children practise regularly in meaningful activities.","zh":"當孩子在有意義活動中定期練習，技能和知識會增長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning useful abilities and information.","zh":"這個短語描述學習有用能力和資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"throughout life","meaning":"一生中","examples":[{"en":"Some skills are useful throughout life.","zh":"有些技能一生中都有用。"},{"en":"Throughout life means during the whole course of a person’s life.","zh":"throughout life 指在人一生的整個過程中。"},{"en":"Communication skills are useful throughout life, from school to work and family relationships.","zh":"溝通技巧一生中都有用，從學校到工作和家庭關係都是如此。"},{"en":"Skills learned in childhood can support decisions many years later.","zh":"童年學到的技能可以在多年後支援決策。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long-term usefulness.","zh":"這個短語強調長期有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"at a distinct disadvantage","meaning":"處於明顯劣勢","examples":[{"en":"Children who are not learning anything are at a distinct disadvantage.","zh":"沒有學到任何東西的兒童處於明顯劣勢。"},{"en":"At a distinct disadvantage means clearly in a worse position than others.","zh":"at a distinct disadvantage 指明顯處於比別人差的位置。"},{"en":"A student without internet access may be at a distinct disadvantage in an online course.","zh":"沒有網絡的學生在網上課程中可能處於明顯劣勢。"},{"en":"Children without enriching activities may fall behind peers who gain skills after school.","zh":"沒有有益活動的孩子，可能落後於放學後獲得技能的同輩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear unfair weakness or loss of opportunity.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚的不公平弱勢或機會損失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"compared to","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Inactive children are at a disadvantage compared to children in enriching activities.","zh":"與參與有益身心活動的兒童相比，不活躍兒童處於劣勢。"},{"en":"Compared to means when measured or considered against another person or thing.","zh":"compared to 指與另一人或事物比較來看。"},{"en":"Compared to walking, cycling may get a student to school faster.","zh":"與步行相比，騎單車可能讓學生更快到校。"},{"en":"Comparisons help show difference in advantage, risk, or result.","zh":"比較有助顯示優勢、風險或結果上的差異。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the standard being used for comparison.","zh":"這個短語引出比較標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"engaged in","meaning":"參與","examples":[{"en":"Some children are engaged in enriching activities after school.","zh":"有些孩子放學後參與有益身心的活動。"},{"en":"To be engaged in something means to be actively involved in it.","zh":"be engaged in something 指積極參與某事。"},{"en":"A student engaged in drama club practises lines, listens to others, and performs on stage.","zh":"參與戲劇學會的學生會練習台詞、聆聽他人並上台表演。"},{"en":"Active engagement gives children structure and purpose after school.","zh":"積極參與給孩子放學後的結構和目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes participation, not passive presence.","zh":"這個短語描述參與，而不是被動在場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"enriching activities","meaning":"有益身心的活動","examples":[{"en":"Children benefit from enriching activities.","zh":"兒童從有益身心的活動中受益。"},{"en":"Enriching activities are activities that help children learn, grow, and develop useful skills.","zh":"enriching activities 指幫助兒童學習、成長和發展有用技能的活動。"},{"en":"Music lessons, sports, volunteering, and reading clubs can be enriching activities.","zh":"音樂課、運動、義工服務和閱讀會都可以是有益身心的活動。"},{"en":"Such activities can build confidence, discipline, friendship, and knowledge.","zh":"這類活動可以建立自信、紀律、友誼和知識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes activities that add value to a child’s development.","zh":"這個短語描述對孩子發展增值的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"in the words of","meaning":"用……的話來說","examples":[{"en":"In the words of T. Berry Brazelton, children need constructive activities.","zh":"用 T. Berry Brazelton 的話來說，孩子需要有建設性的活動。"},{"en":"In the words of someone means using that person’s exact or remembered expression.","zh":"in the words of someone 指使用某人的原話或記得的表達。"},{"en":"In the words of my teacher, “practice turns fear into confidence.”","zh":"用我老師的話來說，「練習會把恐懼變成信心。」"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to quote or refer to an authority’s wording.","zh":"作者使用這個短語來引用或提及權威人士的措辭。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces another person’s viewpoint or phrasing.","zh":"這個短語引入另一個人的觀點或說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"all-important bridge years","meaning":"極重要的過渡歲月","examples":[{"en":"The years between childhood and adulthood are all-important bridge years.","zh":"童年與成年之間的歲月是極重要的過渡歲月。"},{"en":"All-important bridge years are extremely important transition years between two life stages.","zh":"all-important bridge years 指兩個人生階段之間極其重要的過渡年份。"},{"en":"The first year of secondary school can be a bridge year between primary habits and teenage independence.","zh":"中一可以是小學習慣與青少年獨立之間的過渡年。"},{"en":"What children learn during bridge years can shape later confidence and behaviour.","zh":"孩子在過渡歲月中學到的東西，可以塑造日後自信和行為。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that transition periods matter greatly.","zh":"這個短語強調過渡期非常重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"childhood and adulthood","meaning":"童年與成年","examples":[{"en":"Adolescence is a bridge between childhood and adulthood.","zh":"青春期是童年與成年之間的橋樑。"},{"en":"Childhood and adulthood are the life stages of being a child and being an adult.","zh":"childhood and adulthood 指作為兒童和作為成年人的人生階段。"},{"en":"Teenagers stand between childhood and adulthood because they want freedom but still need guidance.","zh":"青少年處於童年與成年之間，因為他們想要自由但仍需要指導。"},{"en":"This transition can be confusing because expectations change quickly.","zh":"這個過渡可能令人困惑，因為期望迅速改變。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the two stages adolescence connects.","zh":"這個短語標示青春期所連接的兩個階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"something constructive to do","meaning":"有建設性的事情可做","examples":[{"en":"Children need something constructive to do.","zh":"孩子需要有建設性的事情可做。"},{"en":"Something constructive to do means an activity that builds skills, confidence, or good habits.","zh":"something constructive to do 指能建立技能、自信或良好習慣的活動。"},{"en":"A child may need something constructive to do after school, such as sports or homework club.","zh":"孩子放學後可能需要有建設性的事情可做，例如運動或功課班。"},{"en":"Constructive activities reduce boredom and give young people purpose.","zh":"有建設性的活動減少沉悶，並給年輕人目標。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts useful activity with empty or harmful time.","zh":"這個短語把有用活動與空白或有害時間作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"have their activities supervised","meaning":"活動受到監督","examples":[{"en":"Children still need to have their activities supervised.","zh":"兒童仍需要活動受到監督。"},{"en":"To have activities supervised means to have an adult watch, guide, or check what children are doing.","zh":"have activities supervised 指有成人看顧、指導或檢查孩子正在做甚麼。"},{"en":"A sports coach supervises activities to make sure children play safely.","zh":"運動教練監督活動，以確保孩子安全地玩。"},{"en":"Supervision helps prevent accidents, bullying, and risky choices.","zh":"監督有助防止意外、欺凌和高風險選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adult oversight of children’s activities.","zh":"這個短語描述成人對兒童活動的看顧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"most of all","meaning":"最重要的是","examples":[{"en":"Most of all, children need to know that their parents care about them.","zh":"最重要的是，孩子需要知道父母關心他們。"},{"en":"Most of all means more importantly than anything else.","zh":"most of all 指比任何其他事情都更重要。"},{"en":"A student needs books and practice, but most of all they need steady effort.","zh":"學生需要書本和練習，但最重要的是穩定努力。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the writer’s most important point.","zh":"這個短語突出作者最重要的觀點。"},{"en":"It often comes before a final emotional or practical priority.","zh":"它常放在最終情感或實際優先事項之前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be involved in their lives","meaning":"參與他們的生活","examples":[{"en":"Children need parents who are involved in their lives.","zh":"孩子需要參與他們生活的父母。"},{"en":"To be involved in their lives means to take an active interest in what they do, feel, and need.","zh":"be involved in their lives 指積極關心他們做甚麼、感受甚麼和需要甚麼。"},{"en":"Parents are involved in a child’s life when they know their friends, schoolwork, and worries.","zh":"父母了解孩子朋友、功課和憂慮時，就是參與孩子生活。"},{"en":"Involvement helps children feel noticed, guided, and valued.","zh":"參與讓孩子感到被注意、被指導和被重視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active parental presence, not just living in the same home.","zh":"這個短語描述父母主動在場，而不只是住在同一屋簷下。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"have their best interests at heart","meaning":"真心為他們着想","examples":[{"en":"Parents should have their children’s best interests at heart.","zh":"父母應真心為孩子着想。"},{"en":"To have someone’s best interests at heart means to genuinely want what is best for them.","zh":"have someone’s best interests at heart 指真心希望對方得到最好的結果。"},{"en":"A teacher has students’ best interests at heart when she gives honest but kind feedback.","zh":"老師給予誠實但友善的回饋，就是為學生着想。"},{"en":"Children trust adults more when they believe adults truly care about their wellbeing.","zh":"當孩子相信成人真心關心他們的福祉，他們會更信任成人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sincere concern, not control for selfish reasons.","zh":"這個短語描述真誠關心，而不是出於自私原因的控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"choose three letters","meaning":"選出三個字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose three letters from the list.","zh":"考生從列表中選出三個字母。"},{"en":"To choose three letters means to select three answer options marked by letters.","zh":"choose three letters 指選出三個以字母標示的答案選項。"},{"en":"In a reading exam, students may choose three letters such as A, C, and F.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生可能選出 A、C 和 F 等三個字母。"},{"en":"Students should check the passage before choosing, because extra options may distract them.","zh":"學生選擇前應核對文章，因為額外選項可能造成干擾。"},{"en":"This phrase is an instruction about answer format.","zh":"這個短語是關於答案格式的指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"may be given in any order","meaning":"可以任何次序作答","examples":[{"en":"The answers may be given in any order.","zh":"答案可以任何次序作答。"},{"en":"May be given in any order means the sequence of the answers does not matter.","zh":"may be given in any order 指答案次序並不重要。"},{"en":"If the correct letters are A, D, and F, writing F, A, D may still be accepted.","zh":"如果正確字母是 A、D 和 F，寫成 F、A、D 也可能被接受。"},{"en":"This instruction reduces pressure because students do not need to rank the answers.","zh":"這個指示減少壓力，因為學生不需要排列答案次序。"},{"en":"This phrase tells candidates that content matters more than order.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生內容比次序重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be mentioned in the text","meaning":"在文章中被提及","examples":[{"en":"Students identify statements that are mentioned in the text.","zh":"學生辨認在文章中被提及的陳述。"},{"en":"To be mentioned in the text means to be stated or referred to in the passage.","zh":"be mentioned in the text 指在文章中被說明或提到。"},{"en":"An answer should not be chosen if it sounds reasonable but is not mentioned in the text.","zh":"如果某答案聽起來合理但文章沒有提及，就不應選擇。"},{"en":"Reading tasks often test whether students can separate text evidence from personal opinion.","zh":"閱讀題常測試學生能否分清文本證據與個人意見。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what the passage actually says.","zh":"這個短語集中於文章實際說了甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be attributable to","meaning":"可歸因於","examples":[{"en":"Youth crime is not always attributable to economic background.","zh":"青少年犯罪並不總是可歸因於經濟背景。"},{"en":"To be attributable to something means to be caused by or explained by it.","zh":"be attributable to something 指由某事造成或可由某事解釋。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be attributable to poor sleep rather than laziness.","zh":"學生疲倦可能可歸因於睡眠不足，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"Social problems are often not attributable to one single factor.","zh":"社會問題通常不可歸因於單一因素。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a possible cause or explanation.","zh":"這個短語引出可能原因或解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"economic background","meaning":"經濟背景","examples":[{"en":"Teen violence now occurs across different economic backgrounds.","zh":"青少年暴力現在出現在不同經濟背景中。"},{"en":"Economic background means a person’s or family’s financial and social-economic situation.","zh":"economic background 指個人或家庭的財政和社會經濟情況。"},{"en":"Students from different economic backgrounds may have different access to private tutoring.","zh":"來自不同經濟背景的學生可能有不同機會接受私人補習。"},{"en":"If a problem appears across backgrounds, money alone cannot explain it.","zh":"如果問題出現在不同背景，金錢本身就不能完全解釋它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes financial and class context.","zh":"這個短語描述財政和階級背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"the greatest cause for concern","meaning":"最大的憂慮","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to the greatest cause for concern.","zh":"該選項提到最大的憂慮。"},{"en":"The greatest cause for concern means the most worrying issue.","zh":"greatest cause for concern 指最令人擔心的問題。"},{"en":"In a school safety report, bullying may be the greatest cause for concern.","zh":"在學校安全報告中，欺凌可能是最大的憂慮。"},{"en":"Identifying the greatest concern helps people decide what to address first.","zh":"找出最大憂慮有助人們決定先處理甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase ranks one problem as the most serious worry.","zh":"這個短語把一個問題列為最嚴重的擔心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"alcohol-abuse problems","meaning":"酗酒問題","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions parents with alcohol-abuse problems.","zh":"該選項提到有酗酒問題的父母。"},{"en":"Alcohol-abuse problems are difficulties caused by harmful or uncontrolled drinking.","zh":"alcohol-abuse problems 指由有害或失控飲酒造成的困難。"},{"en":"A parent with alcohol-abuse problems may forget appointments or become unsafe around children.","zh":"有酗酒問題的父母可能忘記約定，或在孩子身邊變得不安全。"},{"en":"Alcohol abuse can affect family stability, money, and emotional safety.","zh":"酗酒可以影響家庭穩定、金錢和情感安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious drinking-related problems, not occasional social drinking.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重飲酒相關問題，而不是偶爾社交飲酒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"unsupervised at home","meaning":"在家中無人監督","examples":[{"en":"Some children are left unsupervised at home.","zh":"有些兒童被留在家中無人監督。"},{"en":"Unsupervised at home means at home without an adult watching or guiding them.","zh":"unsupervised at home 指在家中沒有成人看顧或指導。"},{"en":"A child unsupervised at home may not know what to do if someone knocks on the door.","zh":"在家中無人監督的孩子可能不知道有人敲門時該怎樣做。"},{"en":"Being unsupervised can increase risk if the child is too young or anxious.","zh":"如果孩子太年幼或焦慮，無人監督會增加風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lack of adult monitoring inside the home.","zh":"這個短語描述家中缺乏成人監察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"safer neighbourhood","meaning":"較安全的社區","examples":[{"en":"The option compares neighbourhood safety with adolescent crime.","zh":"該選項把社區安全與青少年犯罪作比較。"},{"en":"A safer neighbourhood is an area with lower danger, crime, or public disorder.","zh":"safer neighbourhood 指危險、罪案或公共混亂較少的地區。"},{"en":"Parents may feel more comfortable letting older children walk home in a safer neighbourhood.","zh":"在較安全的社區，父母可能較放心讓較年長孩子步行回家。"},{"en":"Neighbourhood safety affects how much independence children can safely have.","zh":"社區安全影響孩子能安全擁有多少獨立性。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one community’s safety with another’s.","zh":"這個短語比較一個社區與另一個社區的安全程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"crime rate","meaning":"犯罪率","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to the crime rate among adolescents.","zh":"該陳述提到青少年之間的犯罪率。"},{"en":"Crime rate means how often crimes occur in a group or area.","zh":"crime rate 指某群體或地區中罪案發生的頻率。"},{"en":"A city may increase street lighting if the crime rate rises at night.","zh":"如果夜間犯罪率上升，城市可能增加街燈。"},{"en":"Crime rates help people see whether a problem is growing or shrinking.","zh":"犯罪率幫助人們看出問題正在增加還是減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the measured frequency of crime.","zh":"這個短語描述罪案的量化頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"financial considerations","meaning":"財政考慮","examples":[{"en":"Financial considerations may affect access to activities.","zh":"財政考慮可能影響參加活動的機會。"},{"en":"Financial considerations are money-related factors that influence a decision.","zh":"financial considerations 指影響決定的金錢相關因素。"},{"en":"A family may choose a free library club because of financial considerations.","zh":"家庭可能因財政考慮而選擇免費圖書館小組。"},{"en":"If activities cost too much, poorer children may be excluded.","zh":"如果活動費用太高，較貧窮兒童可能被排除在外。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how money affects choices.","zh":"這個短語顯示金錢如何影響選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"have access to","meaning":"可使用；可參加","examples":[{"en":"Some children have access to community activities.","zh":"有些兒童可參加社區活動。"},{"en":"To have access to something means to be able to use or join it.","zh":"have access to something 指能夠使用或參加某事。"},{"en":"Students with library cards have access to books, computers, and study spaces.","zh":"有圖書證的學生可使用書本、電腦和自修空間。"},{"en":"Access matters because a good programme cannot help children who cannot join it.","zh":"可及性很重要，因為孩子無法參加的好計劃幫不到他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes real availability, not just existence.","zh":"這個短語描述實際可使用，而不只是存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"community activities","meaning":"社區活動","examples":[{"en":"Community activities can support children after school.","zh":"社區活動可以在放學後支援兒童。"},{"en":"Community activities are organised local events or programmes that people can join.","zh":"community activities 指人們可參加的本地有組織活動或計劃。"},{"en":"Community activities may include sports clubs, art classes, reading groups, or volunteer work.","zh":"社區活動可包括運動會、藝術班、閱讀小組或義工服務。"},{"en":"These activities give children safe places to learn and socialise.","zh":"這些活動給孩子安全地方學習和社交。"},{"en":"This phrase describes local support beyond the family.","zh":"這個短語描述家庭以外的本地支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be drawn to crime","meaning":"被犯罪吸引；走向犯罪","examples":[{"en":"Latchkey children may be drawn to crime.","zh":"鑰匙兒童可能被犯罪吸引。"},{"en":"To be drawn to crime means to be attracted or pulled toward criminal behaviour.","zh":"be drawn to crime 指被吸引或拉向犯罪行為。"},{"en":"A bored teenager may be drawn to crime if older peers make shoplifting seem exciting.","zh":"如果年長同輩把偷竊說得刺激，沉悶青少年可能被犯罪吸引。"},{"en":"Lack of supervision can make risky behaviour feel more tempting.","zh":"缺乏監督可以令高風險行為更具誘惑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attraction toward wrongdoing, not being physically pulled.","zh":"這個短語描述被錯誤行為吸引，而不是被實際拉走。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"victims of crime","meaning":"罪案受害者","examples":[{"en":"Latchkey children can also be victims of crime.","zh":"鑰匙兒童也可能成為罪案受害者。"},{"en":"Victims of crime are people harmed by criminal actions.","zh":"victims of crime 指受到犯罪行為傷害的人。"},{"en":"A child may become a victim of crime if someone breaks into the home while they are alone.","zh":"如果孩子獨自在家時有人入屋盜竊，孩子可能成為罪案受害者。"},{"en":"Children can be affected by crime even when they have done nothing wrong.","zh":"即使孩子沒有做錯事，也可能受罪案影響。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on people who suffer harm from crime.","zh":"這個短語集中於受犯罪傷害的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"should not be a factor in","meaning":"不應成為……的因素","examples":[{"en":"Expense should not be a factor in allowing children to join activities.","zh":"費用不應成為容許孩子參加活動的因素。"},{"en":"Should not be a factor in something means should not influence that decision.","zh":"should not be a factor in something 指不應影響該決定。"},{"en":"A student’s family income should not be a factor in whether they can join a school trip.","zh":"學生家庭收入不應成為他們能否參加學校旅行的因素。"},{"en":"If cost controls access, children from poorer families may lose opportunities.","zh":"如果費用控制可及性，較貧窮家庭的孩子可能失去機會。"},{"en":"This phrase argues that one consideration should be excluded.","zh":"這個短語主張某個考慮因素應被排除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"out-of-school activities","meaning":"課外活動","examples":[{"en":"Children can benefit from out-of-school activities.","zh":"兒童可以從課外活動中受益。"},{"en":"Out-of-school activities are activities children do outside normal classroom hours.","zh":"out-of-school activities 指兒童在正常課堂時間以外參加的活動。"},{"en":"Sports training, music lessons, and community service are out-of-school activities.","zh":"運動訓練、音樂課和社區服務都是課外活動。"},{"en":"These activities can build skills, friendships, and confidence after lessons end.","zh":"這些活動可以在課堂結束後建立技能、友誼和自信。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to learning and development beyond regular school classes.","zh":"這個短語指常規學校課堂以外的學習和發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"knowing how to say no","meaning":"懂得如何拒絕","examples":[{"en":"Knowing how to say no to peers is a sign of maturity.","zh":"懂得如何拒絕同輩是成熟的跡象。"},{"en":"Knowing how to say no means being able to refuse clearly and safely.","zh":"knowing how to say no 指能清楚而安全地拒絕。"},{"en":"A teenager who says no to smoking knows how to protect their own limits.","zh":"拒絕吸煙的青少年懂得如何保護自己的界線。"},{"en":"Saying no can be difficult when friends laugh or apply pressure.","zh":"當朋友嘲笑或施壓，說不可能很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes refusal skills, not rudeness.","zh":"這個短語描述拒絕技巧，而不是無禮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"one’s peers","meaning":"同輩","examples":[{"en":"Adolescents often face pressure from their peers.","zh":"青少年常面對來自同輩的壓力。"},{"en":"One’s peers are people of similar age, status, or social group.","zh":"one’s peers 指年齡、身份或社交群體相近的人。"},{"en":"A student’s peers may include classmates, teammates, and friends from the neighbourhood.","zh":"學生的同輩可能包括同學、隊友和社區朋友。"},{"en":"Peers can influence clothing, language, habits, and risk-taking.","zh":"同輩可以影響衣着、語言、習慣和冒險行為。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people at a similar stage, not adults in authority.","zh":"這個短語指相近階段的人，而不是有權威的成人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"a sign of maturity","meaning":"成熟的跡象","examples":[{"en":"Resisting peer pressure is a sign of maturity.","zh":"抵抗同輩壓力是成熟的跡象。"},{"en":"A sign of maturity is behaviour showing that someone is becoming responsible and sensible.","zh":"sign of maturity 指顯示某人正在變得負責和明智的行為。"},{"en":"Admitting a mistake without being forced is a sign of maturity.","zh":"沒有被迫也承認錯誤，是成熟的跡象。"},{"en":"Mature behaviour helps adults trust children with more independence.","zh":"成熟行為幫助成人更信任孩子，給予更多獨立性。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies evidence of growing responsibility.","zh":"這個短語指出責任感增長的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"考生為每條題目選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option marked by the right letter.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選出以正確字母標示的答案選項。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may choose A, B, C, or D after checking the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生核對文章後可能選 A、B、C 或 D。"},{"en":"Correct letters must match the text evidence, not personal opinion.","zh":"正確字母必須符合文本證據，而不是個人意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據","examples":[{"en":"Students answer the question according to the passage.","zh":"學生根據文章回答問題。"},{"en":"According to means based on what a source says.","zh":"according to 指基於某來源所說。"},{"en":"According to the timetable, the bus leaves at eight o’clock.","zh":"根據時間表，巴士八點開出。"},{"en":"In reading exams, students must answer according to the text, not outside knowledge.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生必須根據文本回答，而不是外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the source of information.","zh":"這個短語指出資訊來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"during the war","meaning":"戰爭期間","examples":[{"en":"The writer compares childcare during the war with childcare today.","zh":"作者把戰爭期間的兒童照顧與今日的兒童照顧作比較。"},{"en":"During the war means in the period when the war was happening.","zh":"during the war 指戰爭正在發生的時期。"},{"en":"During the war, many families changed work patterns and childcare arrangements.","zh":"戰爭期間，許多家庭改變工作模式和兒童照顧安排。"},{"en":"Comparing wartime and modern childcare shows how social support has changed.","zh":"比較戰時和現代兒童照顧，可以顯示社會支援如何改變。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event in a wartime period.","zh":"這個短語把事件放在戰爭時期中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"absent from the home","meaning":"不在家中","examples":[{"en":"Some children’s parents were absent from the home because of work or war.","zh":"有些孩子的父母因工作或戰爭而不在家中。"},{"en":"Absent from the home means not present at home.","zh":"absent from the home 指不在家中。"},{"en":"A parent may be absent from the home during a hospital night shift.","zh":"家長上醫院夜班時可能不在家中。"},{"en":"When adults are absent from the home, children may lack supervision.","zh":"當成人不在家中，孩子可能缺乏監督。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical absence from the household.","zh":"這個短語描述身體上不在家庭之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"present-day children","meaning":"現今的兒童","examples":[{"en":"Present-day children in the same situation may receive less organised support.","zh":"處於相同情況的現今兒童可能得到較少有組織支援。"},{"en":"Present-day children are children living today.","zh":"present-day children 指今日生活的兒童。"},{"en":"Present-day children may face new risks such as online contact and screen addiction.","zh":"現今兒童可能面對網上接觸和螢幕成癮等新風險。"},{"en":"Comparing present-day children with wartime children shows changes in family and social support.","zh":"比較現今兒童與戰時兒童，可以顯示家庭和社會支援的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to children of the current period.","zh":"這個短語指當代兒童。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"in the same situation","meaning":"處於相同情況","examples":[{"en":"Children today may be in the same situation as wartime latchkey children.","zh":"今日兒童可能處於與戰時鑰匙兒童相同的情況。"},{"en":"In the same situation means facing similar conditions or problems.","zh":"in the same situation 指面對相似條件或問題。"},{"en":"Two students may be in the same situation if both parents work late and no one is home after school.","zh":"如果兩名學生的父母都工作到很晚，放學後家中無人，他們就處於相同情況。"},{"en":"Recognising similar situations helps people compare solutions across time.","zh":"辨認相似情況有助人們跨時代比較解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase links separate cases by shared circumstances.","zh":"這個短語以共同處境連接不同個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"slow to react to","meaning":"對……反應緩慢","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether the country was slow to react to the problem.","zh":"該選項問國家是否對這個問題反應緩慢。"},{"en":"To be slow to react to something means to respond late or not quickly enough.","zh":"slow to react to something 指回應太遲或不夠快。"},{"en":"A school is slow to react to bullying if it waits months before investigating.","zh":"如果學校等了幾個月才調查欺凌，就是對欺凌反應緩慢。"},{"en":"Slow reaction can allow a problem to grow worse.","zh":"反應緩慢可以令問題變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises delayed response.","zh":"這個短語批評延遲回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"the role of the housewife","meaning":"家庭主婦的角色","examples":[{"en":"The role of the housewife changed during the war.","zh":"家庭主婦的角色在戰爭期間改變。"},{"en":"The role of the housewife means the expected duties and social position of a woman managing the home.","zh":"role of the housewife 指管理家庭女性被期望承擔的職責和社會位置。"},{"en":"The role of the housewife may include cooking, cleaning, budgeting, and caring for children.","zh":"家庭主婦的角色可能包括煮飯、清潔、理財和照顧孩子。"},{"en":"War changed this role when women entered factories and public work.","zh":"當女性進入工廠和公共工作，戰爭改變了這個角色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a social role, not one fixed natural duty.","zh":"這個短語描述社會角色，而不是固定天職。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"be expected to","meaning":"被期望去","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether all wives were expected to work in industry.","zh":"該選項問是否所有妻子都被期望去工業界工作。"},{"en":"To be expected to do something means others believe or require that someone should do it.","zh":"be expected to do something 指他人相信或要求某人應該做某事。"},{"en":"Students are expected to arrive on time for exams.","zh":"學生被期望準時到達考試。"},{"en":"Social expectations can influence how people behave, even without written rules.","zh":"社會期望即使沒有明文規則，也能影響人們行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pressure or duty created by expectations.","zh":"這個短語描述由期望造成的壓力或責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"according to the Census Bureau","meaning":"根據人口普查局","examples":[{"en":"According to the Census Bureau, most children were left alone after school.","zh":"根據人口普查局，大多數兒童放學後被獨自留下。"},{"en":"According to the Census Bureau means based on information from the official population statistics agency.","zh":"according to the Census Bureau 指根據官方人口統計機構的資料。"},{"en":"According to the Census Bureau, a city may have more working parents than before.","zh":"根據人口普查局，某城市在職父母可能比以前更多。"},{"en":"This phrase gives authority to a claim by naming the data source.","zh":"這個短語透過指出資料來源來增加說法的權威。"},{"en":"It tells readers the statement is based on official figures.","zh":"它告訴讀者該陳述基於官方數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"be left alone","meaning":"被獨自留下","examples":[{"en":"Many children were left alone after school.","zh":"許多兒童放學後被獨自留下。"},{"en":"To be left alone means to be without company or supervision.","zh":"be left alone 指沒有陪伴或監督。"},{"en":"A young child should not be left alone near a swimming pool.","zh":"年幼孩子不應被獨自留在泳池附近。"},{"en":"Being left alone can be safe or unsafe depending on age, maturity, and environment.","zh":"被獨自留下是否安全取決於年齡、成熟程度和環境。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the absence of another person.","zh":"這個短語突出他人陪伴的缺席。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"all day","meaning":"整天","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether children were left alone all day.","zh":"題目問兒童是否整天被獨自留下。"},{"en":"All day means for the whole day, not just a few hours.","zh":"all day 指整個白天，而不只是幾小時。"},{"en":"A child who is sick may stay in bed all day.","zh":"生病的孩子可能整天躺在床上。"},{"en":"Being alone all day is more serious than being alone briefly after school.","zh":"整天獨處比放學後短暫獨處更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes total daily duration.","zh":"這個短語描述整日持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether statements agree with the information given.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與所給資料相符。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文章所說內容一致。"},{"en":"If the text says most children were alone after school, a matching statement agrees with the information given.","zh":"如果文本說大多數兒童放學後獨處，吻合的陳述就與所給資料相符。"},{"en":"Students should check exact wording before deciding.","zh":"學生作決定前應檢查準確措辭。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文本相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says programmes closed after the war, a statement saying they continued would contradict the information.","zh":"如果文章說計劃在戰後關閉，而陳述說它們繼續，就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be clear from the passage, not guessed from outside knowledge.","zh":"矛盾必須從文章清楚看出，而不是靠外部知識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct conflict with text evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述與文本證據直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students choose “NOT GIVEN” when there is no information on this.","zh":"當沒有相關資料時，學生選擇 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not say enough to decide.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文章沒有提供足夠資料作判斷。"},{"en":"If the text never mentions a child’s exact age, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文本從未提到孩子確實年齡，就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not invent answers when the passage is silent.","zh":"當文章沒有說明，學生不應自行編造答案。"},{"en":"This phrase signals missing evidence.","zh":"這個短語表示證據缺失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"experts at hiding the truth","meaning":"隱瞞真相的高手","examples":[{"en":"Some latchkey children can be experts at hiding the truth.","zh":"有些鑰匙兒童可能是隱瞞真相的高手。"},{"en":"Experts at hiding the truth are people who are very skilled at concealing what is really happening.","zh":"experts at hiding the truth 指非常擅長隱藏真實情況的人。"},{"en":"A child may become an expert at hiding the truth if honesty often leads to punishment.","zh":"如果誠實常導致懲罰，孩子可能成為隱瞞真相的高手。"},{"en":"Hiding the truth can protect a child temporarily but make help harder to receive.","zh":"隱瞞真相可以暫時保護孩子，但令他們更難得到幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a learned survival skill in difficult situations.","zh":"這個短語描述困難情況中學會的生存技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"leave home at an early age","meaning":"早年離家","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether latchkey children leave home at an early age.","zh":"該陳述問鑰匙兒童是否早年離家。"},{"en":"To leave home at an early age means to stop living with one’s family while still young.","zh":"leave home at an early age 指年紀尚輕時停止與家人同住。"},{"en":"A teenager may leave home at an early age if family conflict becomes unbearable.","zh":"如果家庭衝突變得難以忍受，青少年可能早年離家。"},{"en":"Leaving home early can create risks if the young person lacks money or support.","zh":"如果年輕人缺乏金錢或支援，早年離家可能帶來風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes early separation from the family home.","zh":"這個短語描述早期離開家庭住所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"aggressive emotional responses","meaning":"攻擊性的情緒反應","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses aggressive emotional responses in adolescents.","zh":"文章討論青少年的攻擊性情緒反應。"},{"en":"Aggressive emotional responses are angry reactions shown through threatening or harmful behaviour.","zh":"aggressive emotional responses 指透過威脅或有害行為表現出來的憤怒反應。"},{"en":"A student who shouts, pushes, or throws objects may show aggressive emotional responses.","zh":"大叫、推人或丟東西的學生可能表現出攻擊性情緒反應。"},{"en":"Such responses can appear when feelings are intense and poorly managed.","zh":"當情緒強烈且管理不善，這類反應可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase links emotion with outward aggression.","zh":"這個短語把情緒與外在攻擊性連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"be due principally to","meaning":"主要由……造成","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether aggressive responses are due principally to biology.","zh":"該陳述問攻擊性反應是否主要由生物因素造成。"},{"en":"To be due principally to something means to be caused mainly by it.","zh":"be due principally to something 指主要由某事造成。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be due principally to lack of sleep, not lack of effort.","zh":"學生疲倦可能主要由睡眠不足造成，而不是努力不足。"},{"en":"Saying something is due principally to one cause reduces the role of other causes.","zh":"說某事主要由一個原因造成，會降低其他原因的重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main cause being proposed.","zh":"這個短語指出被提出的主要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"biological make-up","meaning":"生理構成","examples":[{"en":"An adolescent’s biological make-up may affect behaviour.","zh":"青少年的生理構成可能影響行為。"},{"en":"Biological make-up means the physical and genetic features that form a person’s body and nervous system.","zh":"biological make-up 指構成一個人身體和神經系統的身體及遺傳特徵。"},{"en":"A child’s biological make-up may affect energy level, sleep needs, or stress reaction.","zh":"孩子的生理構成可能影響精力水平、睡眠需要或壓力反應。"},{"en":"Biology can influence behaviour, but it interacts with family, school, and environment.","zh":"生物因素可以影響行為，但會與家庭、學校和環境互相作用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to body-based characteristics.","zh":"這個短語指基於身體的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"communication skills","meaning":"溝通技巧","examples":[{"en":"Good communication skills can show readiness to be left alone.","zh":"良好溝通技巧可以顯示孩子準備好被獨自留下。"},{"en":"Communication skills are the abilities used to express ideas, feelings, needs, and problems clearly.","zh":"communication skills 指清楚表達想法、感受、需要和問題的能力。"},{"en":"A child with good communication skills can call a parent and explain what happened.","zh":"有良好溝通技巧的孩子可以打電話給父母並解釋發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"These skills matter because children alone must report danger or ask for help.","zh":"這些技巧很重要，因為獨處兒童必須報告危險或求助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical speaking and listening ability.","zh":"這個短語描述實際說話和聆聽能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"a measure of","meaning":"……的衡量標準","examples":[{"en":"Communication skills are a measure of a child’s readiness.","zh":"溝通技巧是孩子準備程度的衡量標準。"},{"en":"A measure of something is a way to judge or assess it.","zh":"a measure of something 指判斷或評估某事的方法。"},{"en":"Homework completion can be a measure of a student’s study habits.","zh":"功課完成情況可以是學生學習習慣的衡量標準。"},{"en":"Measures help adults make decisions based on evidence rather than guesswork.","zh":"衡量標準幫助成人根據證據而不是猜測作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies something used for assessment.","zh":"這個短語指出用於評估的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"be left unsupervised","meaning":"被無人監督地留下","examples":[{"en":"Some children may be left unsupervised at home.","zh":"有些孩子可能被無人監督地留在家中。"},{"en":"To be left unsupervised means to be left without an adult watching or guiding them.","zh":"be left unsupervised 指被留下時沒有成人看顧或指導。"},{"en":"A child should not be left unsupervised near a busy road.","zh":"孩子不應被無人監督地留在繁忙馬路附近。"},{"en":"Whether a child can be left unsupervised depends on age, maturity, and safety.","zh":"孩子能否在無人監督下被留下，取決於年齡、成熟程度和安全。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights lack of adult oversight.","zh":"這個短語突出缺乏成人看顧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the summary using words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill missing words in a shortened version of the text.","zh":"complete the summary 指在文本的簡短版本中填入缺失字詞。"},{"en":"A student should check grammar and meaning before choosing words for a summary.","zh":"學生為摘要選字前應檢查文法和意思。"},{"en":"Summary completion tests whether students can locate and fit information accurately.","zh":"完成摘要測試學生能否準確定位並填入資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common reading exam task.","zh":"這個短語描述常見閱讀考試任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不超過兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Students choose no more than two words from the passage.","zh":"學生從文章中選擇不超過兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must contain one or two words only.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案只可包含一個或兩個字。"},{"en":"If the answer is “night shifts,” adding “the night shifts” may break the word limit.","zh":"如果答案是 “night shifts”，加入 “the night shifts” 可能違反字數限制。"},{"en":"Word limits matter because extra words can make a correct idea wrong.","zh":"字數限制很重要，因為多餘字詞可以令正確意思變錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict exam answer rule.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格考試作答規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"give rise to","meaning":"引起；導致","examples":[{"en":"The Second World War gave rise to the phenomenon of the latchkey child.","zh":"第二次世界大戰引起鑰匙兒童這一現象。"},{"en":"To give rise to something means to cause it to appear or develop.","zh":"give rise to something 指造成某事出現或發展。"},{"en":"Long working hours can give rise to stress and family conflict.","zh":"長工時可以引起壓力和家庭衝突。"},{"en":"Major social changes often give rise to new terms and new problems.","zh":"重大社會變化常會引起新詞語和新問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows cause and development.","zh":"這個短語顯示原因和發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"the phenomenon of","meaning":"……的現象","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains the phenomenon of the latchkey child.","zh":"文章解釋鑰匙兒童的現象。"},{"en":"The phenomenon of something means a noticeable social, natural, or behavioural pattern.","zh":"phenomenon of something 指可被注意到的社會、自然或行為模式。"},{"en":"The phenomenon of students studying with phones beside them is now common.","zh":"學生把手機放在旁邊溫習的現象現在很常見。"},{"en":"Calling something a phenomenon suggests it is widespread enough to study.","zh":"把某事稱為現象，暗示它廣泛到值得研究。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an observable pattern or issue.","zh":"這個短語引出可觀察的模式或議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"abandon traditional duties","meaning":"放棄傳統職責","examples":[{"en":"During the war, many mothers abandoned traditional duties.","zh":"戰爭期間，許多母親放棄傳統職責。"},{"en":"To abandon traditional duties means to stop doing roles that society previously expected.","zh":"abandon traditional duties 指停止履行社會過去期望的角色。"},{"en":"A family member may abandon traditional duties if they must take a paid job urgently.","zh":"如果家庭成員急需受薪工作，可能放棄傳統職責。"},{"en":"War can force people to change old gender roles and household routines.","zh":"戰爭可以迫使人們改變舊有性別角色和家庭常規。"},{"en":"This phrase describes leaving expected roles behind.","zh":"這個短語描述離開被期待的角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"fill the places of","meaning":"填補……的位置","examples":[{"en":"Mothers filled the places of men in industry.","zh":"母親們填補了男性在工業中的位置。"},{"en":"To fill the places of someone means to take over their roles or positions.","zh":"fill the places of someone 指接替他們的角色或位置。"},{"en":"A substitute teacher fills the place of a teacher who is sick.","zh":"代課老師填補生病老師的位置。"},{"en":"During wartime, women filled men’s places in factories because many men were away fighting.","zh":"戰時許多男性參戰離開，因此女性填補男性在工廠的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes replacing someone in a role.","zh":"這個短語描述在角色上取代某人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"by the authorities","meaning":"由當局","examples":[{"en":"There was a quick response by the authorities.","zh":"當局作出了快速回應。"},{"en":"By the authorities means done or organised by official bodies or people in power.","zh":"by the authorities 指由官方機構或掌權人士執行或組織。"},{"en":"A road closure by the authorities may happen after a serious accident.","zh":"嚴重交通意外後，當局可能封路。"},{"en":"Official action can coordinate resources that families cannot organise alone.","zh":"官方行動可以協調家庭無法單獨組織的資源。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who took formal action.","zh":"這個短語指出誰採取正式行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"left at home unsupervised","meaning":"被無人監督地留在家中","examples":[{"en":"The programmes helped ensure children were not left at home unsupervised.","zh":"這些計劃有助確保兒童不會被無人監督地留在家中。"},{"en":"Left at home unsupervised means left in the house without an adult watching them.","zh":"left at home unsupervised 指被留在家中時沒有成人看顧。"},{"en":"A young child left at home unsupervised may face risks from cooking, strangers, or accidents.","zh":"年幼孩子被無人監督地留在家中，可能面對煮食、陌生人或意外風險。"},{"en":"Supervised programmes reduce the need to leave children alone at home.","zh":"受監督計劃減少孩子需要獨自留在家中的情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unsafe or worrying childcare gap.","zh":"這個短語描述不安全或令人擔心的兒童照顧缺口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"this type of support","meaning":"這類支援","examples":[{"en":"This type of support disappeared after the war.","zh":"這類支援在戰後消失。"},{"en":"This type of support means this particular kind of help or service.","zh":"this type of support 指這種特定幫助或服務。"},{"en":"Free after-school care is one type of support for working parents.","zh":"免費課後照顧是在職父母的一種支援。"},{"en":"When support disappears, families may have to solve problems alone.","zh":"當支援消失，家庭可能要獨自解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a specific help system already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指回前面已提及的特定幫助系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"without supervision","meaning":"沒有監督","examples":[{"en":"The problem of children being alone without supervision is common.","zh":"兒童沒有監督下獨處的問題很常見。"},{"en":"Without supervision means without someone responsible watching or guiding them.","zh":"without supervision 指沒有負責任的人看顧或指導。"},{"en":"Children using the internet without supervision may see unsafe content.","zh":"孩子沒有監督下上網，可能看見不安全內容。"},{"en":"Lack of supervision can turn ordinary free time into a risky period.","zh":"缺乏監督可以把普通自由時間變成有風險的時段。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the absence of adult oversight.","zh":"這個短語突出成人看顧的缺席。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"perform poorly at school","meaning":"在學校表現欠佳","examples":[{"en":"Latchkey children may perform poorly at school.","zh":"鑰匙兒童可能在學校表現欠佳。"},{"en":"To perform poorly at school means to have weak grades, behaviour, or participation.","zh":"perform poorly at school 指成績、行為或參與度較弱。"},{"en":"A child may perform poorly at school if they are tired from being alone and anxious after school.","zh":"如果孩子放學後獨處而焦慮疲倦，可能在學校表現欠佳。"},{"en":"Poor performance can signal problems outside the classroom.","zh":"表現欠佳可以反映課室以外的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes school results and behaviour that are below expectation.","zh":"這個短語描述低於期望的學校成績和行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"display aggressive behaviour","meaning":"表現出攻擊性行為","examples":[{"en":"Some latchkey children display aggressive behaviour.","zh":"有些鑰匙兒童表現出攻擊性行為。"},{"en":"To display aggressive behaviour means to show hostile or violent actions.","zh":"display aggressive behaviour 指表現出敵意或暴力行動。"},{"en":"A student displays aggressive behaviour when they threaten classmates or damage desks.","zh":"學生威脅同學或破壞書桌時，就是表現出攻擊性行為。"},{"en":"Aggressive behaviour may appear when anger, isolation, and poor supervision combine.","zh":"當憤怒、孤立和監督不足結合，攻擊性行為可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible harmful behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述可見的有害行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":27},{"front":"take up smoking","meaning":"開始吸煙","examples":[{"en":"Unsupervised children may take up smoking.","zh":"無人監督的兒童可能開始吸煙。"},{"en":"To take up smoking means to start smoking as a habit.","zh":"take up smoking 指開始把吸煙變成習慣。"},{"en":"A teenager may take up smoking if close friends smoke after school.","zh":"如果親近朋友放學後吸煙，青少年可能開始吸煙。"},{"en":"Starting to smoke young can create long-term health problems.","zh":"年輕時開始吸煙可以造成長期健康問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes beginning a harmful habit.","zh":"這個短語描述開始有害習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":27},{"front":"play a part in","meaning":"在……中起作用","examples":[{"en":"Personality and maturity play a part in how a child copes.","zh":"性格和成熟程度在孩子如何應付中起作用。"},{"en":"To play a part in something means to have some influence on it.","zh":"play a part in something 指對某事有一定影響。"},{"en":"Sleep plays a part in how well students remember new words.","zh":"睡眠在學生記住新詞的能力中起作用。"},{"en":"Many factors can play a part in a child’s readiness to be alone.","zh":"許多因素可以在孩子是否準備好獨處中起作用。"},{"en":"This phrase shows partial influence, not the only cause.","zh":"這個短語顯示部分影響，而不是唯一原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":27},{"front":"cope with","meaning":"應付","examples":[{"en":"Children differ in how they cope with being latchkey children.","zh":"孩子在如何應付成為鑰匙兒童方面有所不同。"},{"en":"To cope with something means to manage a difficult situation.","zh":"cope with something 指處理困難情況。"},{"en":"A student copes with exam stress by planning revision and taking breaks.","zh":"學生透過計劃溫習和休息來應付考試壓力。"},{"en":"Children cope better when they have rules, support, and someone to call.","zh":"當孩子有規則、支援和可致電的人，他們會應付得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes handling difficulty rather than avoiding it.","zh":"這個短語描述處理困難，而不是逃避困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":27},{"front":"the remedy for","meaning":"……的補救方法","examples":[{"en":"Experts say the remedy for this situation is more parental involvement.","zh":"專家說這種情況的補救方法是更多父母參與。"},{"en":"The remedy for a problem means the solution or treatment for it.","zh":"remedy for a problem 指問題的解決方法或處理方法。"},{"en":"The remedy for constant lateness may be an earlier bedtime and a clearer morning routine.","zh":"經常遲到的補救方法可能是早點睡和更清楚的早晨常規。"},{"en":"A remedy should address the real cause, not only the visible symptom.","zh":"補救方法應處理真正原因，而不只是表面症狀。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what may fix or reduce a problem.","zh":"這個短語引出可能修正或減少問題的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":27},{"front":"parental involvement","meaning":"父母參與","examples":[{"en":"Experts recommend more parental involvement in children’s lives.","zh":"專家建議父母更多參與子女生活。"},{"en":"Parental involvement means parents actively taking part in their children’s education, activities, feelings, and decisions.","zh":"parental involvement 指父母積極參與孩子的教育、活動、感受和決定。"},{"en":"Parental involvement can include checking homework, attending school meetings, and talking after dinner.","zh":"父母參與可以包括檢查功課、出席學校會議和晚飯後聊天。"},{"en":"Children often feel safer when parents know what is happening in their lives.","zh":"當父母知道孩子生活中發生甚麼，孩子通常會更有安全感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active care, not just providing money or housing.","zh":"這個短語描述主動照顧，而不只是提供金錢或住所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":27},{"front":"interest in their children’s lives","meaning":"對子女生活的關心","examples":[{"en":"Children need parents to show interest in their lives.","zh":"孩子需要父母表現出對子女生活的關心。"},{"en":"Interest in their children’s lives means real curiosity and care about what children do, feel, and experience.","zh":"interest in their children’s lives 指真心好奇和關心孩子做甚麼、感受甚麼和經歷甚麼。"},{"en":"A parent shows interest by asking about school, friends, worries, and plans.","zh":"父母詢問學校、朋友、憂慮和計劃，就是表現出關心。"},{"en":"Children who feel noticed may be more willing to share problems early.","zh":"感到被注意的孩子可能更願意及早分享問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional attention from parents.","zh":"這個短語描述父母在情感上的關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 84 - LATCHKEY CHILDREN.pdf","sourcePage":27}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 85":[{"front":"a master of political and diplomatic juggling","meaning":"政治與外交斡旋高手","examples":[{"en":"The article questions whether Bismarck was a master of political and diplomatic juggling.","zh":"文章質疑 Bismarck 是否是政治與外交斡旋高手。"},{"en":"A master of political and diplomatic juggling is someone very skilled at managing power, alliances, conflicts, and negotiations at the same time.","zh":"a master of political and diplomatic juggling 指非常擅長同時處理權力、同盟、衝突和談判的人。"},{"en":"A school principal may need to be a master of political and diplomatic juggling when parents, teachers, and students all want different things.","zh":"當家長、老師和學生都有不同要求時，校長可能需要成為政治與外交斡旋高手。"},{"en":"If a leader balances several powerful groups successfully, people may call him a master of political and diplomatic juggling.","zh":"如果領袖成功平衡幾個強大群體，人們可能稱他為政治與外交斡旋高手。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests clever coordination, but it can also imply manipulation.","zh":"這個短語暗示聰明協調，但也可能帶有操控意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"political and diplomatic juggling","meaning":"政治與外交斡旋","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck’s political and diplomatic juggling helped him achieve many of his goals.","zh":"Bismarck 的政治與外交斡旋幫助他達成許多目標。"},{"en":"Political and diplomatic juggling means handling political power and international relations carefully at the same time.","zh":"political and diplomatic juggling 指同時小心處理政治權力和國際關係。"},{"en":"A government may need political and diplomatic juggling when it wants trade with one country but security support from another.","zh":"當政府想與一國貿易，又想從另一國取得安全支援時，可能需要政治與外交斡旋。"},{"en":"Such juggling can succeed if each side feels it has gained something.","zh":"如果各方都覺得自己有所收穫，這種斡旋可能成功。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests difficult balancing between competing interests.","zh":"這個短語常暗示在互相競爭的利益之間作艱難平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rise up the political ladder","meaning":"在政壇迅速晉升","examples":[{"en":"Otto von Bismarck’s rise up the political ladder was swift and relentless.","zh":"Otto von Bismarck 在政壇迅速晉升，而且過程迅速而毫不鬆懈。"},{"en":"To rise up the political ladder means to move quickly to higher and more powerful political positions.","zh":"rise up the political ladder 指晉升至更高、更有權力的政治職位。"},{"en":"A young councillor may rise up the political ladder if she gains public trust and party support.","zh":"如果年輕議員取得公眾信任和政黨支持，她可能在政壇迅速晉升。"},{"en":"Strong speeches, alliances, and timing can help someone rise up the political ladder.","zh":"有力演說、同盟和時機都可以幫助人在政壇晉升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes career advancement in politics.","zh":"這個短語描述政治生涯上的向上發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"swift and relentless","meaning":"迅速而毫不鬆懈的","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck’s rise to power was swift and relentless.","zh":"Bismarck 的掌權過程迅速而毫不鬆懈。"},{"en":"Swift and relentless means fast and continuing without stopping or weakening.","zh":"swift and relentless 指快速，而且持續不停、不減弱。"},{"en":"A company’s expansion can be swift and relentless if it opens new shops every month.","zh":"如果公司每月開新店，它的擴張可以是迅速而毫不鬆懈的。"},{"en":"Swift and relentless progress can impress people, but it may also create pressure on others.","zh":"迅速而毫不鬆懈的進展可以令人印象深刻，但也可能給其他人壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes speed combined with unstoppable determination.","zh":"這個短語描述速度加上不可阻擋的決心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"enter parliament","meaning":"進入議會","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck entered parliament in 1847.","zh":"Bismarck 在 1847 年進入議會。"},{"en":"To enter parliament means to become a member of a country’s law-making body.","zh":"enter parliament 指成為國家立法機構的一員。"},{"en":"A local politician may enter parliament after winning a national election.","zh":"本地政治人物在贏得全國選舉後，可能進入議會。"},{"en":"Entering parliament gives a politician a formal platform to debate laws and policy.","zh":"進入議會讓政治人物有正式平台辯論法律和政策。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the beginning of a formal political career.","zh":"這個短語標誌正式政治生涯的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"harbour lofty ambitions","meaning":"懷有遠大抱負","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck always harboured lofty ambitions.","zh":"Bismarck 一直懷有遠大抱負。"},{"en":"To harbour lofty ambitions means to keep strong and high-level goals in one’s mind for a long time.","zh":"harbour lofty ambitions 指長期在心中保有強烈而高遠的目標。"},{"en":"A student may harbour lofty ambitions of becoming a doctor, even while struggling with science at school.","zh":"學生即使在學校讀科學吃力，也可能懷有成為醫生的遠大抱負。"},{"en":"Lofty ambitions can drive hard work, but they can also lead to impatience.","zh":"遠大抱負可以推動努力，但也可能導致急躁。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests big goals that are deeply held.","zh":"這個短語暗示深藏心中的宏大目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"chief among them","meaning":"其中最重要的是","examples":[{"en":"He had many ambitions, chief among them the reunification of Germany.","zh":"他有許多抱負，其中最重要的是德國統一。"},{"en":"Chief among them means the most important one among several things.","zh":"chief among them 指在幾件事之中最重要的一項。"},{"en":"A school may have many goals, chief among them improving students’ reading ability.","zh":"學校可能有許多目標，其中最重要的是提升學生閱讀能力。"},{"en":"When one aim is chief among them, it guides many later decisions.","zh":"當一個目標是其中最重要的，它會引導許多後續決定。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the top priority in a group of aims or problems.","zh":"這個短語突出一組目標或問題中的最高優先事項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the reunification of Germany","meaning":"德國統一","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck wanted the reunification of Germany into one strong state.","zh":"Bismarck 希望德國統一成為一個強大國家。"},{"en":"The reunification of Germany means bringing separate German states or territories together again as one country.","zh":"the reunification of Germany 指把分散的德意志邦國或領土重新結合成一個國家。"},{"en":"A history lesson may discuss the reunification of Germany when explaining nationalism in Europe.","zh":"歷史課解釋歐洲民族主義時，可能討論德國統一。"},{"en":"Reunification can create a stronger state, but it may also shift the balance of power.","zh":"統一可以建立更強大的國家，但也可能改變權力平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a major political process of joining divided parts together.","zh":"這個短語指把分裂部分結合起來的重大政治過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a centrally controlled state","meaning":"中央集權國家","examples":[{"en":"He wanted Germany to become one strong, centrally controlled state.","zh":"他希望德國成為一個強大而中央集權的國家。"},{"en":"A centrally controlled state is a country where major decisions are made by a strong central government.","zh":"a centrally controlled state 指主要決定由強大中央政府作出的國家。"},{"en":"A centrally controlled state may set the same school rules for every province.","zh":"中央集權國家可能為每個省份制定相同校規。"},{"en":"Central control can make decisions faster, but it may reduce local freedom.","zh":"中央控制可以令決策更快，但可能減少地方自由。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts national authority with regional independence.","zh":"這個短語把全國權威與地方自主作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"personal thirst for power","meaning":"個人權力慾","examples":[{"en":"His personal thirst for power was arguably even stronger than his nationalist ambition.","zh":"他的個人權力慾可以說比民族主義抱負更強。"},{"en":"Personal thirst for power means a strong personal desire to gain and keep authority.","zh":"personal thirst for power 指個人強烈渴望取得並保持權力。"},{"en":"A manager with a personal thirst for power may refuse to let team members make decisions.","zh":"有個人權力慾的經理可能拒絕讓團隊成員作決定。"},{"en":"Such thirst can push someone to work hard, but it can also make them controlling.","zh":"這種慾望可以推動人努力，但也可能令他變得控制欲強。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests ambition driven by self-interest.","zh":"這個短語暗示由私利推動的野心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"arguably even stronger","meaning":"可以說更強烈","examples":[{"en":"His desire for power was arguably even stronger.","zh":"他的權力慾可以說更強烈。"},{"en":"Arguably even stronger means it can reasonably be claimed to be stronger, though people may debate it.","zh":"arguably even stronger 指可以合理地說更強，但人們可能仍會爭論。"},{"en":"Her speaking skills are impressive, but her listening skills are arguably even stronger.","zh":"她的口語能力令人印象深刻，但聆聽能力可以說更強。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when making a careful but confident comparison.","zh":"作者在作出謹慎但有信心的比較時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase leaves room for disagreement while still giving a clear judgement.","zh":"這個短語保留分歧空間，同時給出清楚判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on becoming","meaning":"在成為……後","examples":[{"en":"On becoming Prussian Chancellor, Bismarck set about fulfilling his ambitions.","zh":"在成為普魯士首相後，Bismarck 開始着手實現自己的抱負。"},{"en":"On becoming means immediately after becoming or once someone has taken a position.","zh":"on becoming 指在成為某身份後立即或一旦取得某職位。"},{"en":"On becoming class monitor, a student may try to improve classroom routines.","zh":"學生成為班長後，可能嘗試改善課室常規。"},{"en":"A new role often gives someone the power to act on earlier plans.","zh":"新角色常給予某人實行早前計劃的權力。"},{"en":"This phrase links a new position with the actions that follow.","zh":"這個短語把新職位與之後的行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Prussian Chancellor","meaning":"普魯士首相","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck became Prussian Chancellor before leading German unification.","zh":"Bismarck 在領導德國統一前成為普魯士首相。"},{"en":"The Prussian Chancellor was the leading government official of Prussia.","zh":"Prussian Chancellor 指普魯士政府的主要官員。"},{"en":"In a history essay, students may explain how the Prussian Chancellor gained influence over German politics.","zh":"在歷史作文中，學生可能解釋普魯士首相如何取得對德國政治的影響力。"},{"en":"Holding this office gave Bismarck authority to shape policy and diplomacy.","zh":"擔任此職位讓 Bismarck 有權力塑造政策和外交。"},{"en":"This phrase names a powerful political position in Prussia.","zh":"這個短語命名普魯士一個有權勢的政治職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"set about doing something","meaning":"開始着手做某事","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck set about fulfilling his ambitions.","zh":"Bismarck 開始着手實現自己的抱負。"},{"en":"To set about doing something means to begin doing it with purpose and effort.","zh":"set about doing something 指有目的和努力地開始做某事。"},{"en":"After receiving feedback, a student set about rewriting her essay.","zh":"收到回饋後，學生開始着手重寫作文。"},{"en":"People set about a task when they have decided what they want to achieve.","zh":"當人們已決定想達成甚麼，就會開始着手處理任務。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active, deliberate action.","zh":"這個短語暗示積極而有意識的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fulfil one’s ambitions","meaning":"實現某人的抱負","examples":[{"en":"He set about fulfilling his political ambitions.","zh":"他開始着手實現自己的政治抱負。"},{"en":"To fulfil one’s ambitions means to achieve the goals one has strongly wanted.","zh":"fulfil one’s ambitions 指達成自己強烈渴望的目標。"},{"en":"A student may fulfil her ambitions by entering the university she has worked toward for years.","zh":"學生多年努力後進入理想大學，可能就是實現自己的抱負。"},{"en":"Ambitions are fulfilled through planning, effort, opportunity, and sometimes luck.","zh":"抱負透過計劃、努力、機會，有時還有運氣而實現。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on turning long-held goals into reality.","zh":"這個短語著重把長期目標變成現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"prove oneself to be","meaning":"證明自己是……","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck proved himself to be a skilful diplomat.","zh":"Bismarck 證明自己是一名熟練外交家。"},{"en":"To prove oneself to be something means to show through actions that one has that quality or ability.","zh":"prove oneself to be something 指透過行動顯示自己具有某品質或能力。"},{"en":"A new teacher may prove herself to be patient by helping weak students calmly every day.","zh":"新老師每天冷靜幫助能力弱的學生，可能證明自己有耐性。"},{"en":"People prove themselves through results, not only through promises.","zh":"人們透過結果證明自己，而不只是透過承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes earning a reputation through evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述透過證據贏得名聲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a diplomat of considerable skill","meaning":"頗有才能的外交家","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck proved himself to be a diplomat of considerable skill.","zh":"Bismarck 證明自己是頗有才能的外交家。"},{"en":"A diplomat of considerable skill is someone highly capable in negotiation and international relations.","zh":"a diplomat of considerable skill 指在談判和國際關係方面很有能力的人。"},{"en":"A company representative can be a diplomat of considerable skill if she calms angry partners and keeps a deal alive.","zh":"如果公司代表能安撫憤怒合作伙伴並保住交易，她可以是頗有才能的外交家。"},{"en":"Such skill helps when different sides distrust one another.","zh":"當不同方面互不信任，這種能力會有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase praises a person’s ability to manage sensitive relationships.","zh":"這個短語讚揚某人處理敏感關係的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the Austro-Prussian War","meaning":"普奧戰爭","examples":[{"en":"Victory in the Austro-Prussian War strengthened Prussia’s position.","zh":"普奧戰爭的勝利強化了普魯士的地位。"},{"en":"The Austro-Prussian War was a conflict between Austria and Prussia that changed German power politics.","zh":"the Austro-Prussian War 指奧地利與普魯士之間、改變德國權力政治的衝突。"},{"en":"Students study the Austro-Prussian War to understand how Prussia became dominant among German states.","zh":"學生研究普奧戰爭，以理解普魯士如何在德意志邦國中取得主導。"},{"en":"A victory in such a war can change alliances, borders, and political influence.","zh":"這類戰爭中的勝利可以改變同盟、邊界和政治影響力。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major nineteenth-century European conflict.","zh":"這個短語命名十九世紀歐洲一場重大衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"effectively end","meaning":"實際上終結","examples":[{"en":"Victory effectively ended Austria as a factor in German affairs.","zh":"勝利實際上終結了奧地利作為德國事務因素的角色。"},{"en":"To effectively end something means to bring it to an end in practice, even if not formally.","zh":"effectively end something 指在實際上結束某事，即使並非正式結束。"},{"en":"A new school app effectively ended the need for paper notices.","zh":"新學校應用程式實際上終結了紙本通告的需要。"},{"en":"Something can effectively end when it loses real influence or usefulness.","zh":"當某事失去實際影響力或用途，它可以說是實際上終結。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical result rather than official wording.","zh":"這個短語著重實際結果，而不是官方措辭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as a factor in","meaning":"作為……中的因素","examples":[{"en":"Austria ceased to be an important factor in German affairs.","zh":"奧地利不再是德國事務中的重要因素。"},{"en":"As a factor in something means as an influence or element affecting that situation.","zh":"as a factor in something 指作為影響該情況的因素或元素。"},{"en":"Sleep is a major factor in a student’s concentration.","zh":"睡眠是學生專注力中的主要因素。"},{"en":"If a group stops being a factor in a decision, it no longer shapes the outcome.","zh":"如果某群體不再是決策中的因素，它就不再塑造結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that affects what happens.","zh":"這個短語描述會影響事情發展的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"German affairs","meaning":"德國事務","examples":[{"en":"Austria was no longer a major factor in German affairs.","zh":"奧地利不再是德國事務中的主要因素。"},{"en":"German affairs means political, social, or diplomatic matters concerning Germany or German states.","zh":"German affairs 指與德國或德意志邦國有關的政治、社會或外交事務。"},{"en":"A historian may study German affairs to understand how European alliances changed.","zh":"歷史學家可能研究德國事務，以理解歐洲同盟如何改變。"},{"en":"Control over German affairs mattered because it shaped power in central Europe.","zh":"對德國事務的控制很重要，因為它塑造中歐權力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to matters connected with Germany’s political life.","zh":"這個短語指與德國政治生活相關的事務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be taken a step further","meaning":"被推進一步","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck’s political juggling was taken a step further in 1870.","zh":"Bismarck 的政治斡旋在 1870 年被推進一步。"},{"en":"To be taken a step further means to be developed or pushed to a more advanced or extreme stage.","zh":"be taken a step further 指被發展或推向更進一步或更極端的階段。"},{"en":"A school’s recycling plan was taken a step further when students began measuring waste each week.","zh":"當學生開始每週量度廢物，學校的回收計劃被推進一步。"},{"en":"An idea is taken further when someone moves from planning to active action.","zh":"當某人由計劃轉向實際行動，想法就被推進一步。"},{"en":"This phrase shows progress to the next level.","zh":"這個短語顯示進入下一層次。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"orchestrate a situation","meaning":"精心策劃一個局面","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck orchestrated a situation in which France declared war.","zh":"Bismarck 精心策劃了一個令法國宣戰的局面。"},{"en":"To orchestrate a situation means to carefully arrange events so that a particular result happens.","zh":"orchestrate a situation 指仔細安排事件，使某特定結果出現。"},{"en":"A manager may orchestrate a meeting so that two departments agree on a shared plan.","zh":"經理可能精心策劃一場會議，令兩個部門同意共同計劃。"},{"en":"Orchestrating a situation can be clever, but it may also be manipulative.","zh":"精心策劃局面可以很聰明，但也可能帶操控意味。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful behind-the-scenes planning.","zh":"這個短語暗示幕後仔細策劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"declare war on","meaning":"向……宣戰","examples":[{"en":"France declared war on Germany in 1870.","zh":"法國在 1870 年向德國宣戰。"},{"en":"To declare war on a country means to officially announce that a state of war exists with it.","zh":"declare war on a country 指正式宣布與某國進入戰爭狀態。"},{"en":"In history lessons, students learn why governments declare war on other states.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生學習政府為何向其他國家宣戰。"},{"en":"Declaring war can turn a political dispute into open military conflict.","zh":"宣戰可以把政治爭端變成公開軍事衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a formal act by a government.","zh":"這個短語描述政府的正式行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make someone seem responsible for","meaning":"使某人看似要為……負責","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck made the French seem responsible for the conflict.","zh":"Bismarck 使法國人看似要為衝突負責。"},{"en":"To make someone seem responsible for something means to create the impression that they caused it.","zh":"make someone seem responsible for something 指製造印象，令人覺得某人造成某事。"},{"en":"A student may make a classmate seem responsible for a mistake by hiding part of the story.","zh":"學生可能透過隱瞞部分故事，使同學看似要為錯誤負責。"},{"en":"This tactic can shift blame even when the full facts are more complicated.","zh":"這種手法可以轉移責任，即使完整事實更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests manipulation of public perception.","zh":"這個短語常暗示操控公眾觀感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be responsible for a conflict","meaning":"對衝突負責","examples":[{"en":"The French were made to seem responsible for the conflict.","zh":"法國人被塑造成看似要對衝突負責。"},{"en":"To be responsible for a conflict means to be seen as having caused or started it.","zh":"be responsible for a conflict 指被視為造成或引發衝突。"},{"en":"In a classroom argument, one student may be blamed as responsible for the conflict.","zh":"在課室爭執中，一名學生可能被怪責要對衝突負責。"},{"en":"Being seen as responsible can damage a group’s reputation and justify action against it.","zh":"被視為負責可以損害群體聲譽，並合理化針對它的行動。"},{"en":"This phrase connects blame with the start of a dispute.","zh":"這個短語把責任與爭端開始連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"intend to create","meaning":"打算製造","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck had always intended to create the conflict.","zh":"Bismarck 一直打算製造這場衝突。"},{"en":"To intend to create something means to plan or aim to make it happen.","zh":"intend to create something 指計劃或意圖令某事發生。"},{"en":"A teacher may intend to create discussion by asking a difficult opening question.","zh":"老師可能打算透過提出困難開場問題來製造討論。"},{"en":"Intention matters because it shows whether an outcome was accidental or planned.","zh":"意圖很重要，因為它顯示結果是意外還是計劃之中。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights deliberate purpose.","zh":"這個短語突出有意識的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"following another swift military triumph","meaning":"在另一場迅速軍事勝利之後","examples":[{"en":"Following another swift military triumph, the German Empire was proclaimed.","zh":"在另一場迅速軍事勝利之後，德意志帝國被宣告成立。"},{"en":"Following another swift military triumph means after another quick victory in war.","zh":"following another swift military triumph 指在另一場快速軍事勝利之後。"},{"en":"Following another successful debate performance, the student was chosen as team captain.","zh":"在又一次成功辯論表現之後，該學生被選為隊長。"},{"en":"A victory can create the confidence and political conditions for a major announcement.","zh":"勝利可以創造信心和政治條件，讓重大宣布出現。"},{"en":"This phrase links a fast success with what happened next.","zh":"這個短語把快速成功與之後發生的事連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"military triumph","meaning":"軍事勝利","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck gained another military triumph over the French.","zh":"Bismarck 對法國取得另一場軍事勝利。"},{"en":"A military triumph is a major victory in war or battle.","zh":"military triumph 指戰爭或戰役中的重大勝利。"},{"en":"A country may celebrate a military triumph with speeches, parades, and monuments.","zh":"一個國家可能用演說、巡遊和紀念碑慶祝軍事勝利。"},{"en":"Military triumphs can strengthen a leader’s position, but they can also create future enemies.","zh":"軍事勝利可以強化領袖地位，但也可能製造未來敵人。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses success in armed conflict.","zh":"這個短語強調武裝衝突中的成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be proclaimed","meaning":"被宣告成立","examples":[{"en":"The German Empire was proclaimed in January 1871.","zh":"德意志帝國於 1871 年 1 月被宣告成立。"},{"en":"To be proclaimed means to be officially announced in a public or formal way.","zh":"be proclaimed 指以公開或正式方式被宣布。"},{"en":"A new holiday may be proclaimed after parliament approves it.","zh":"議會批准後，新假期可能被正式宣布。"},{"en":"Proclamation gives an event public and official recognition.","zh":"宣告賦予事件公開和正式承認。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a formal announcement, often of political importance.","zh":"這個短語描述正式宣布，常涉及政治重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in little more than","meaning":"在僅僅多於……的時間內","examples":[{"en":"In little more than nine years, Bismarck realised his lifelong ambition.","zh":"在僅僅多於九年的時間內，Bismarck 實現了畢生抱負。"},{"en":"In little more than means in only slightly more than a stated period of time.","zh":"in little more than 指只比所提時間稍微多一點。"},{"en":"In little more than six months, the small café became a popular local meeting place.","zh":"在僅僅多於六個月的時間內，小咖啡店成為受歡迎的本地聚會地點。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that something happened surprisingly quickly.","zh":"這個短語強調某事發生得出乎意料地快。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing a short time with a major achievement.","zh":"當短時間與重大成就作比較時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"realise one’s lifelong ambition","meaning":"實現畢生抱負","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck realised his lifelong ambition by unifying Germany.","zh":"Bismarck 透過統一德國實現畢生抱負。"},{"en":"To realise one’s lifelong ambition means to achieve a goal one has wanted for most of one’s life.","zh":"realise one’s lifelong ambition 指達成一個人生大部分時間都渴望的目標。"},{"en":"A singer may realise her lifelong ambition when she performs on a major stage.","zh":"歌手在大型舞台演出時，可能實現畢生抱負。"},{"en":"Lifelong ambitions often require years of preparation and sacrifice.","zh":"畢生抱負通常需要多年準備和犧牲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the fulfilment of a deeply held dream.","zh":"這個短語描述深藏夢想的實現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"steer someone to","meaning":"引領……走向","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck steered Germany to reunification.","zh":"Bismarck 引領德國走向統一。"},{"en":"To steer someone or something to a result means to guide it carefully toward that outcome.","zh":"steer someone or something to a result 指小心引導其走向某結果。"},{"en":"A good tutor can steer a weak student to clearer writing by giving step-by-step feedback.","zh":"好導師可以透過逐步回饋，引領能力弱的學生寫得更清楚。"},{"en":"Leaders steer groups by choosing direction, timing, and strategy.","zh":"領袖透過選擇方向、時機和策略來引領群體。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active guidance toward a goal.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動引導走向目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"defeat someone in quick succession","meaning":"接連擊敗某人","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck defeated Austria and France in quick succession.","zh":"Bismarck 接連擊敗奧地利和法國。"},{"en":"To defeat someone in quick succession means to beat several opponents one after another in a short time.","zh":"defeat someone in quick succession 指在短時間內一個接一個擊敗幾個對手。"},{"en":"A debate team defeated three schools in quick succession during the tournament.","zh":"辯論隊在比賽中接連擊敗三間學校。"},{"en":"Quick successive victories can make a leader appear unusually powerful.","zh":"接連快速勝利可以令領袖顯得異常強大。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses repeated success with little time between victories.","zh":"這個短語強調勝利之間相隔很短的反覆成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"create a power vacuum","meaning":"造成權力真空","examples":[{"en":"Defeating Austria and France created a power vacuum in Europe.","zh":"擊敗奧地利和法國在歐洲造成權力真空。"},{"en":"To create a power vacuum means to remove a powerful force and leave no clear replacement.","zh":"create a power vacuum 指移除一股強大力量，卻沒有清楚替代者。"},{"en":"When a strong manager suddenly resigns, it may create a power vacuum in the office.","zh":"當強勢經理突然辭職，辦公室可能出現權力真空。"},{"en":"A power vacuum can lead to competition because several groups want control.","zh":"權力真空可以導致競爭，因為幾個群體都想取得控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an empty space in authority or influence.","zh":"這個短語描述權威或影響力上的空缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mainland Europe","meaning":"歐洲大陸","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck wanted to fill the power vacuum on mainland Europe.","zh":"Bismarck 想填補歐洲大陸上的權力真空。"},{"en":"Mainland Europe means the main continental part of Europe, not islands such as Britain or Ireland.","zh":"mainland Europe 指歐洲的主要大陸部分，不包括英國或愛爾蘭等島嶼。"},{"en":"Train travel is easier across mainland Europe because many countries are connected by land.","zh":"在歐洲大陸，火車旅行較方便，因為許多國家由陸地相連。"},{"en":"In political history, mainland Europe often refers to the central arena of continental power struggles.","zh":"在政治歷史中，歐洲大陸常指大陸權力鬥爭的中心舞台。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts continental Europe with island territories.","zh":"這個短語把歐洲大陸與島嶼領土作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be determined to","meaning":"決心……","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck was determined to fill the power vacuum himself.","zh":"Bismarck 決心親自填補權力真空。"},{"en":"To be determined to do something means to have a firm decision and strong will to do it.","zh":"be determined to do something 指有堅定決定和強烈意志去做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be determined to improve after failing an important exam.","zh":"學生在重要考試失敗後，可能決心改進。"},{"en":"Determination can help people continue even when obstacles appear.","zh":"決心可以幫助人在障礙出現時繼續前進。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong commitment to a goal.","zh":"這個短語顯示對目標的強烈承諾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"political and diplomatic cunning","meaning":"政治與外交手腕","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck demonstrated considerable political and diplomatic cunning.","zh":"Bismarck 展現出相當的政治與外交手腕。"},{"en":"Political and diplomatic cunning means clever, strategic, and sometimes manipulative skill in politics and foreign relations.","zh":"political and diplomatic cunning 指在政治和外交關係中聰明、策略性，有時帶操控意味的能力。"},{"en":"A negotiator shows diplomatic cunning when she gets two rivals to accept the same compromise.","zh":"當談判者令兩個對手接受同一妥協方案，她就展現外交手腕。"},{"en":"Cunning can achieve results quickly, but it may make others distrust the person using it.","zh":"手腕可以快速取得結果，但也可能令他人不信任使用它的人。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests intelligence mixed with craftiness.","zh":"這個短語暗示智慧加上狡黠技巧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a dictatorial Germany","meaning":"獨裁式德國","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck set about creating a dictatorial Germany.","zh":"Bismarck 開始着手建立一個獨裁式德國。"},{"en":"A dictatorial Germany means a Germany governed with strong central power and limited political opposition.","zh":"a dictatorial Germany 指以強大中央權力統治、政治反對受限制的德國。"},{"en":"A dictatorial school system would give students and teachers little say in decisions.","zh":"獨裁式學校制度會讓學生和老師在決策中幾乎沒有發言權。"},{"en":"Dictatorial rule can look efficient, but it often weakens freedom and accountability.","zh":"獨裁統治可能看似有效率，但常削弱自由和問責。"},{"en":"This phrase describes government controlled by authority rather than broad democratic debate.","zh":"這個短語描述由權威控制，而非廣泛民主辯論的政府。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"head of parliament","meaning":"議會首腦","examples":[{"en":"As head of the Prussian parliament, he gained enormous influence.","zh":"作為普魯士議會首腦，他取得巨大影響力。"},{"en":"The head of parliament is the person who holds a leading role in a legislative body.","zh":"head of parliament 指在立法機構中擔任領導角色的人。"},{"en":"The head of a student council may control meeting agendas and guide discussion.","zh":"學生會主席可能控制會議議程並引導討論。"},{"en":"A leading position in parliament can give someone power over laws and political timing.","zh":"議會中的領導職位可以給予某人對法律和政治時機的權力。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a powerful leadership role inside a representative institution.","zh":"這個短語指出代表機構內的強大領導角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"automatically become","meaning":"自動成為","examples":[{"en":"He would automatically become chancellor of the German Empire.","zh":"他會自動成為德意志帝國首相。"},{"en":"To automatically become something means to enter a role without a separate decision or extra process.","zh":"automatically become something 指無需另作決定或額外程序就進入某角色。"},{"en":"The vice-captain may automatically become captain if the captain leaves the team.","zh":"如果隊長離隊，副隊長可能自動成為隊長。"},{"en":"Automatic promotion can make succession predictable and easier to manage.","zh":"自動晉升可以令繼任安排可預測且較易管理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a result that follows by rule or structure.","zh":"這個短語描述按規則或結構自然產生的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"draft a constitution","meaning":"起草憲法","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck drafted a new German constitution.","zh":"Bismarck 起草了一部新的德國憲法。"},{"en":"To draft a constitution means to write the first formal version of a country’s basic political rules.","zh":"draft a constitution 指撰寫一個國家基本政治規則的正式初稿。"},{"en":"A student club may draft a constitution to explain elections, duties, and membership rules.","zh":"學生學會可能起草章程，解釋選舉、職責和會員規則。"},{"en":"Drafting a constitution shapes who has power and how decisions are made.","zh":"起草憲法會塑造誰擁有權力，以及決策如何進行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes writing the framework for governance.","zh":"這個短語描述撰寫管治框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"suit one’s own purposes","meaning":"配合某人自己的目的","examples":[{"en":"He drafted a constitution to suit his own purposes.","zh":"他起草憲法，以配合自己的目的。"},{"en":"To suit one’s own purposes means to be arranged in a way that serves one’s own aims.","zh":"suit one’s own purposes 指被安排成服務某人自己目標的樣子。"},{"en":"A manager may design a meeting schedule to suit his own purposes rather than the team’s needs.","zh":"經理可能設計會議時間表以配合自己的目的，而不是團隊需要。"},{"en":"Rules made to suit one person’s purposes can look fair while protecting that person’s power.","zh":"為配合某人目的而制定的規則，可以看似公平，同時保護該人的權力。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests self-serving design.","zh":"這個短語常暗示自利安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"maintain a veneer of democracy","meaning":"維持民主表象","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck maintained a veneer of democracy in the new empire.","zh":"Bismarck 在新帝國中維持民主表象。"},{"en":"To maintain a veneer of democracy means to keep the appearance of democratic rule while real power is limited or controlled.","zh":"maintain a veneer of democracy 指保留民主統治的外表，但實際權力受到限制或控制。"},{"en":"A school committee may maintain a veneer of democracy if students vote but leaders ignore the result.","zh":"如果學生有投票但領袖忽視結果，學校委員會可能只是維持民主表象。"},{"en":"A democratic appearance can make strong control seem more acceptable.","zh":"民主外表可以令強力控制看起來較可接受。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts surface appearance with real political power.","zh":"這個短語把表面外觀與真實政治權力作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"effectively powerless to","meaning":"實際上無力……","examples":[{"en":"The German parliament was effectively powerless to oppose him.","zh":"德國議會實際上無力反對他。"},{"en":"Effectively powerless to do something means unable to do it in practice, even if some formal role exists.","zh":"effectively powerless to do something 指即使形式上有角色，實際上仍不能做到某事。"},{"en":"A class representative is effectively powerless to change school rules if teachers ignore every suggestion.","zh":"如果老師忽視所有建議，班代表實際上無力改變校規。"},{"en":"People may seem included in a system but still be powerless to affect decisions.","zh":"人們可能看似被納入制度，但仍無力影響決定。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights practical weakness behind formal structure.","zh":"這個短語突出形式結構背後的實際弱勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"oppose someone","meaning":"反對某人","examples":[{"en":"The parliament was unable to oppose Bismarck effectively.","zh":"議會無法有效反對 Bismarck。"},{"en":"To oppose someone means to disagree with them and try to stop or limit their actions.","zh":"oppose someone 指不同意某人，並試圖阻止或限制其行動。"},{"en":"Parents may oppose a school plan if they think it harms students.","zh":"如果家長認為學校計劃傷害學生，可能反對校方。"},{"en":"Opposition matters only if people have enough power to make their objections count.","zh":"只有當人們有足夠權力令反對意見有效時，反對才有影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active resistance, not quiet dislike.","zh":"這個短語描述主動抵抗，而不是安靜不喜歡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"slow to support","meaning":"遲遲未支持","examples":[{"en":"Provinces that were slow to support him were offered bribes.","zh":"遲遲未支持他的省份被提供賄賂。"},{"en":"Slow to support means hesitant or taking a long time to give help or approval.","zh":"slow to support 指猶豫或花很長時間才給予幫助或認可。"},{"en":"Some students may be slow to support a new club until they know who will join.","zh":"有些學生可能遲遲未支持新學會，直到知道誰會加入。"},{"en":"If groups are slow to support a leader, he may try to persuade or pressure them.","zh":"如果群體遲遲未支持領袖，他可能嘗試說服或施壓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes delayed backing.","zh":"這個短語描述支持來得很慢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be enticed with bribes","meaning":"被賄賂引誘","examples":[{"en":"Some provinces were enticed with bribes.","zh":"有些省份被賄賂引誘。"},{"en":"To be enticed with bribes means to be tempted to act through dishonest payments or rewards.","zh":"be enticed with bribes 指被不誠實的付款或回報誘惑而行動。"},{"en":"A dishonest company may entice officials with bribes to win a contract.","zh":"不誠實公司可能用賄賂引誘官員以取得合約。"},{"en":"Bribes can change decisions by replacing fair judgement with private gain.","zh":"賄賂可以以私人利益取代公平判斷，從而改變決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes corruption through temptation.","zh":"這個短語描述透過誘惑造成的腐敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"before long","meaning":"不久之後","examples":[{"en":"Before long, the German Empire was his to command.","zh":"不久之後，德意志帝國由他掌控。"},{"en":"Before long means after a short time.","zh":"before long 指過了一段短時間之後。"},{"en":"A new student may feel shy at first, but before long she may make friends.","zh":"新學生起初可能害羞，但不久之後可能交到朋友。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that a change happens fairly quickly.","zh":"這個短語暗示變化相當快地發生。"},{"en":"It connects an earlier action with a soon-after result.","zh":"它把早前行動與很快出現的結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be someone’s to command","meaning":"由某人掌控","examples":[{"en":"The German Empire was Bismarck’s to command.","zh":"德意志帝國由 Bismarck 掌控。"},{"en":"If something is someone’s to command, that person has strong control over it.","zh":"be someone’s to command 指某人對某事擁有強大控制權。"},{"en":"A team may become a coach’s to command if players follow every instruction without question.","zh":"如果球員毫無疑問地跟從每項指示，球隊可能由教練掌控。"},{"en":"Such control can make action efficient, but it may reduce others’ freedom.","zh":"這種控制可以令行動有效率，但可能減少其他人的自由。"},{"en":"This phrase describes power to direct people or institutions.","zh":"這個短語描述指揮人或機構的權力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a testament to","meaning":"……的證明","examples":[{"en":"His achievements were a testament to his political skill.","zh":"他的成就是其政治技巧的證明。"},{"en":"A testament to something is clear evidence that a quality or effort exists.","zh":"a testament to something 指清楚證明某種品質或努力存在的事物。"},{"en":"A student’s improved essays are a testament to months of careful practice.","zh":"學生進步了的作文，是數月仔細練習的證明。"},{"en":"Strong results can act as a testament to planning, discipline, and skill.","zh":"強勁成果可以成為計劃、紀律和技巧的證明。"},{"en":"This phrase praises something by presenting it as proof.","zh":"這個短語透過把某事呈現為證據來讚揚它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"political skill","meaning":"政治技巧","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck’s political skill allowed him to achieve much quickly.","zh":"Bismarck 的政治技巧讓他迅速取得很多成就。"},{"en":"Political skill is the ability to understand power, persuade people, and manage public decisions.","zh":"political skill 指理解權力、說服他人和管理公共決策的能力。"},{"en":"A class leader shows political skill when she gets rival groups to support the same event.","zh":"班長令對立群體支持同一活動時，就展現政治技巧。"},{"en":"Political skill can help a leader pass laws, build alliances, or survive criticism.","zh":"政治技巧可以幫助領袖通過法律、建立同盟或承受批評。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical ability in handling politics.","zh":"這個短語描述處理政治的實際能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"achieve so much so quickly","meaning":"如此迅速地取得這麼多成就","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck achieved so much so quickly that his skill was widely recognised.","zh":"Bismarck 如此迅速地取得這麼多成就，以致其才能廣受承認。"},{"en":"To achieve so much so quickly means to accomplish many important things in a short time.","zh":"achieve so much so quickly 指在短時間內完成許多重要事情。"},{"en":"A new manager may achieve so much so quickly that other departments begin copying her methods.","zh":"新經理可能如此迅速地取得這麼多成就，以致其他部門開始模仿她的方法。"},{"en":"Rapid achievement can bring respect, but it can also create jealousy or resistance.","zh":"快速成就可以帶來尊重，但也可能製造嫉妒或抵抗。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses both scale and speed.","zh":"這個短語同時強調規模和速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at this point in","meaning":"在……這個階段","examples":[{"en":"At this point in his career, he seemed highly successful.","zh":"在其事業這個階段，他看起來非常成功。"},{"en":"At this point in something means at this particular stage of a process or period.","zh":"at this point in something 指在某過程或時期的這個特定階段。"},{"en":"At this point in the course, students should understand the basic grammar rules.","zh":"在課程這個階段，學生應已理解基本文法規則。"},{"en":"Looking at one point in a career may not show how the full story ends.","zh":"只看事業某一階段，未必能顯示整個故事如何結束。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a specific moment in a longer development.","zh":"這個短語標記較長發展中的某個具體時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"colourful political career","meaning":"多姿多彩的政治生涯","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck had a colourful political career.","zh":"Bismarck 有一段多姿多彩的政治生涯。"},{"en":"A colourful political career is a political life full of dramatic events, conflicts, achievements, or controversy.","zh":"colourful political career 指充滿戲劇性事件、衝突、成就或爭議的政治人生。"},{"en":"A mayor with scandals, reforms, and election victories may have a colourful political career.","zh":"一位有醜聞、改革和選舉勝利的市長，可能有多姿多彩的政治生涯。"},{"en":"Such a career attracts attention because it is not ordinary or predictable.","zh":"這類生涯會吸引注意，因為它並不平凡或可預測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lively and eventful public life.","zh":"這個短語描述活躍而多事的公共人生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for all intents and purposes","meaning":"實際上；從各方面看","examples":[{"en":"He appeared, for all intents and purposes, to be a master strategist.","zh":"從各方面看，他似乎是一名戰略大師。"},{"en":"For all intents and purposes means in all practical ways, even if not officially or perfectly.","zh":"for all intents and purposes 指在所有實際意義上，即使並非正式或完全如此。"},{"en":"A student who runs every meeting is, for all intents and purposes, the team leader.","zh":"負責每次會議的學生，實際上就是團隊領袖。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when the practical reality matters more than the formal label.","zh":"當實際現實比正式標籤更重要時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It means something is effectively true in real life.","zh":"它表示某事在現實生活中實際上是真的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"challenges lay ahead","meaning":"挑戰仍在前方","examples":[{"en":"Despite his early success, challenges lay ahead.","zh":"儘管他早期成功，挑戰仍在前方。"},{"en":"Challenges lay ahead means difficulties were waiting in the future.","zh":"challenges lay ahead 指困難正在未來等待。"},{"en":"After passing the first exam, a student may still know that harder challenges lay ahead.","zh":"通過第一次考試後，學生可能仍知道更困難的挑戰在前方。"},{"en":"Early success does not remove future problems.","zh":"早期成功不會消除未來問題。"},{"en":"This phrase prepares the reader for later difficulties.","zh":"這個短語讓讀者準備好面對後續困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"deem something too powerful","meaning":"認為某事物過於強大","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck deemed the Catholic Church too powerful.","zh":"Bismarck 認為天主教會過於強大。"},{"en":"To deem something too powerful means to judge that it has more influence than is safe or acceptable.","zh":"deem something too powerful 指判斷某事物的影響力超出安全或可接受程度。"},{"en":"A principal may deem a student group too powerful if it controls school events unfairly.","zh":"如果學生組織不公平地控制學校活動，校長可能認為它過於強大。"},{"en":"Seeing another organisation as too powerful can lead a leader to restrict it.","zh":"把另一組織視為過於強大，可能令領袖限制它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a judgement about excessive influence.","zh":"這個短語描述對過度影響力的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a threat to","meaning":"對……的威脅","examples":[{"en":"He saw the Catholic Church as a threat to his political dominance.","zh":"他把天主教會視為對其政治支配地位的威脅。"},{"en":"A threat to something is a danger that may weaken, damage, or challenge it.","zh":"a threat to something 指可能削弱、破壞或挑戰某事的危險。"},{"en":"Poor attendance is a threat to a student’s progress.","zh":"出席率低是對學生進步的威脅。"},{"en":"Leaders may act aggressively when they see another group as a threat to their power.","zh":"當領袖把另一群體視為對其權力的威脅，可能採取強硬行動。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what is being endangered.","zh":"這個短語指出甚麼正受到危害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"political dominance","meaning":"政治支配地位","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck wanted to protect his political dominance.","zh":"Bismarck 想保護自己的政治支配地位。"},{"en":"Political dominance means having strong control or influence over political life.","zh":"political dominance 指對政治生活擁有強大控制或影響力。"},{"en":"A party may gain political dominance if it wins elections for many years.","zh":"如果政黨連續多年勝出選舉，可能取得政治支配地位。"},{"en":"Political dominance can make decision-making easier, but it can weaken opposition.","zh":"政治支配地位可以令決策更容易，但可能削弱反對力量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a superior position in politics.","zh":"這個短語描述政治中的優勢地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"proceed to enact","meaning":"接着頒布","examples":[{"en":"He proceeded to enact a series of laws.","zh":"他接着頒布一系列法律。"},{"en":"To proceed to enact laws means to go on to officially make laws.","zh":"proceed to enact laws 指接着正式制定法律。"},{"en":"After months of debate, the council proceeded to enact new safety rules.","zh":"經過數月辯論後，議會接着頒布新的安全規則。"},{"en":"Leaders enact laws when they want policy to become enforceable action.","zh":"當領袖想把政策變成可執行行動，就會頒布法律。"},{"en":"This phrase links a decision with formal legal action.","zh":"這個短語把決定與正式法律行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a series of laws","meaning":"一系列法律","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck enacted a series of laws against the Catholic Church.","zh":"Bismarck 頒布一系列針對天主教會的法律。"},{"en":"A series of laws means several laws introduced one after another around the same issue.","zh":"a series of laws 指圍繞同一議題先後推出的幾項法律。"},{"en":"A government may pass a series of laws to improve road safety.","zh":"政府可能通過一系列法律來改善道路安全。"},{"en":"Several related laws can create stronger pressure than one single rule.","zh":"幾項相關法律可以比單一規則造成更強壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated legal action.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆的法律行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"erode the power of","meaning":"削弱……的權力","examples":[{"en":"The laws seriously eroded the power of the church.","zh":"這些法律嚴重削弱教會的權力。"},{"en":"To erode the power of someone or something means to gradually weaken their influence or authority.","zh":"erode the power of someone or something 指逐漸削弱其影響力或權威。"},{"en":"Repeated complaints can erode the power of a school rule if students stop respecting it.","zh":"如果學生不再尊重某校規，反覆投訴可能削弱該校規的權力。"},{"en":"Power is eroded when support, money, legal rights, or public trust decline.","zh":"當支持、金錢、法律權利或公眾信任下降，權力就會被削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow weakening rather than sudden destruction.","zh":"這個短語描述慢慢削弱，而不是突然摧毀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"backfire","meaning":"適得其反","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck’s plans against the church backfired.","zh":"Bismarck 針對教會的計劃適得其反。"},{"en":"If a plan backfires, it produces the opposite result from what was intended.","zh":"backfire 指計劃產生與原意相反的結果。"},{"en":"A strict phone ban may backfire if students become more secretive instead of more focused.","zh":"嚴格禁手機可能適得其反，令學生變得更秘密，而不是更專注。"},{"en":"Plans backfire when leaders misjudge how people will react.","zh":"當領袖錯判人們反應，計劃就可能適得其反。"},{"en":"This word describes a strategy going wrong and hurting the person who used it.","zh":"這個詞描述策略出錯並傷害使用者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be forced to","meaning":"被迫……","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck was forced to make a political U-turn.","zh":"Bismarck 被迫作出政治轉軚。"},{"en":"To be forced to do something means to have no real choice but to do it.","zh":"be forced to do something 指沒有真正選擇，只能做某事。"},{"en":"A shop may be forced to close early if the power fails.","zh":"如果停電，商店可能被迫提早關門。"},{"en":"People are forced to change plans when pressure or circumstances leave no better option.","zh":"當壓力或情況不留下更好選擇，人們就被迫改變計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase shows action caused by necessity rather than free preference.","zh":"這個短語顯示行動由必要性造成，而不是自由偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"make a political U-turn","meaning":"作出政治轉軚","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck was forced to make a political U-turn.","zh":"Bismarck 被迫作出政治轉軚。"},{"en":"To make a political U-turn means to reverse a political position or policy.","zh":"make a political U-turn 指逆轉政治立場或政策。"},{"en":"A mayor may make a political U-turn after public protests against a transport plan.","zh":"市長可能在公眾抗議交通計劃後作出政治轉軚。"},{"en":"Political U-turns can reduce damage, but they may also make a leader look weak.","zh":"政治轉軚可以減少損害，但也可能令領袖顯得軟弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major change in political direction.","zh":"這個短語描述政治方向的重大改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"save face","meaning":"保全面子","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck somehow managed to save face after the failure.","zh":"Bismarck 在失敗後不知怎樣仍設法保全面子。"},{"en":"To save face means to avoid public shame or embarrassment after a mistake or defeat.","zh":"save face 指在錯誤或失敗後避免公開羞辱或尷尬。"},{"en":"A teacher may let a student correct an answer quietly so the student can save face.","zh":"老師可能讓學生悄悄更正答案，好讓學生保全面子。"},{"en":"People try to save face when their reputation is at risk.","zh":"當名聲有風險，人們會嘗試保全面子。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on protecting dignity in front of others.","zh":"這個短語著重在他人面前保護尊嚴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"damage to one’s reputation","meaning":"對某人名聲的損害","examples":[{"en":"The damage to his reputation was limited.","zh":"對他名聲的損害有限。"},{"en":"Damage to one’s reputation means harm done to how other people view or respect someone.","zh":"damage to one’s reputation 指對他人如何看待或尊重某人造成傷害。"},{"en":"A company can suffer damage to its reputation if it treats customers unfairly.","zh":"如果公司不公平對待顧客，它的名聲可能受損。"},{"en":"Reputation damage may reduce trust even after the original problem is fixed.","zh":"即使原本問題已解決，名聲損害仍可能減少信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes loss of public respect.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾尊重的流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"by the late 1870s","meaning":"到十九世紀七十年代末","examples":[{"en":"By the late 1870s, Bismarck had won over the church.","zh":"到十九世紀七十年代末，Bismarck 已爭取到教會支持。"},{"en":"By the late 1870s means before or around the final years of the 1870s.","zh":"by the late 1870s 指在 1870 年代最後幾年之前或其間。"},{"en":"By the late 2020s, many schools may use more digital textbooks.","zh":"到二十一世紀二十年代末，許多學校可能使用更多電子教材。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a historical time marker for when a change had happened.","zh":"這個短語給出變化已發生的歷史時間標記。"},{"en":"It helps readers place events in sequence.","zh":"它幫助讀者排列事件先後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"win over","meaning":"爭取……支持","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck managed to win over the church.","zh":"Bismarck 設法爭取到教會支持。"},{"en":"To win over someone means to persuade them to support or accept you.","zh":"win over someone 指說服某人支持或接受你。"},{"en":"A new teacher can win over a difficult class by being fair and consistent.","zh":"新老師可以透過公平和一致來爭取難教班級的支持。"},{"en":"People are won over when trust replaces suspicion.","zh":"當信任取代懷疑，人們就會被爭取過來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing someone from resistance to support.","zh":"這個短語描述把某人由抗拒轉為支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"view something as","meaning":"把某事物視為……","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck viewed the Social Democratic Party as a threat.","zh":"Bismarck 把社會民主黨視為威脅。"},{"en":"To view something as something means to see or judge it in that way.","zh":"view something as something 指以某方式看待或判斷某事。"},{"en":"Some parents view homework as useful practice, while others view it as unnecessary pressure.","zh":"有些家長把功課視為有用練習，另一些則視為不必要壓力。"},{"en":"How people view an issue affects how they respond to it.","zh":"人們如何看待議題，會影響他們如何回應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes perception or judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述看法或判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the growing popularity of","meaning":"……日益受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The growing popularity of the Social Democratic Party worried Bismarck.","zh":"社會民主黨日益受歡迎令 Bismarck 擔心。"},{"en":"The growing popularity of something means more and more people are supporting or liking it.","zh":"the growing popularity of something 指越來越多人支持或喜歡某事物。"},{"en":"The growing popularity of online lessons has changed how schools plan courses.","zh":"網上課堂日益受歡迎，改變了學校如何規劃課程。"},{"en":"Growing popularity can worry opponents because it may lead to greater influence.","zh":"日益受歡迎可以令對手擔心，因為它可能帶來更大影響力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing public support.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾支持增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the Social Democratic Party","meaning":"社會民主黨","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck tried to weaken the Social Democratic Party.","zh":"Bismarck 試圖削弱社會民主黨。"},{"en":"The Social Democratic Party was a political party associated with socialist and workers’ interests.","zh":"the Social Democratic Party 指與社會主義和工人利益相關的政黨。"},{"en":"A history essay may discuss the Social Democratic Party when explaining German domestic politics.","zh":"歷史作文解釋德國內政時，可能討論社會民主黨。"},{"en":"A growing political party can threaten leaders who want to control opposition.","zh":"日益壯大的政黨可以威脅想控制反對力量的領袖。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific political organisation in the passage.","zh":"這個短語命名文章中的一個特定政治組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a serious threat","meaning":"嚴重威脅","examples":[{"en":"He regarded the party as a serious threat.","zh":"他把該黨視為嚴重威脅。"},{"en":"A serious threat is a danger that could cause major harm or loss of control.","zh":"a serious threat 指可能造成重大傷害或失控的危險。"},{"en":"A sudden illness can be a serious threat to a student’s exam preparation.","zh":"突發疾病可以是對學生考試準備的嚴重威脅。"},{"en":"Leaders may take strong action when they believe a threat is serious.","zh":"當領袖相信威脅嚴重，可能採取強硬行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes danger that should not be ignored.","zh":"這個短語描述不應被忽視的危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bide one’s time","meaning":"等待時機","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck bided his time before attacking the socialists.","zh":"Bismarck 在攻擊社會主義者前等待時機。"},{"en":"To bide one’s time means to wait patiently for the right moment to act.","zh":"bide one’s time 指耐心等待合適行動時刻。"},{"en":"A student may bide her time before asking a difficult question until the teacher finishes explaining.","zh":"學生可能等待老師解釋完，才提出困難問題。"},{"en":"Waiting can be strategic if acting too early would fail.","zh":"如果太早行動會失敗，等待可以是一種策略。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests patience with a purpose.","zh":"這個短語暗示有目的的耐心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"attempted assassination","meaning":"暗殺未遂","examples":[{"en":"The attempted assassination of the Kaiser gave Bismarck an excuse.","zh":"對皇帝的暗殺未遂給了 Bismarck 一個藉口。"},{"en":"An attempted assassination is an effort to kill an important person that does not succeed.","zh":"attempted assassination 指試圖殺死重要人物但沒有成功。"},{"en":"Security may be increased after an attempted assassination of a political leader.","zh":"政治領袖遭暗殺未遂後，保安可能加強。"},{"en":"Such an event can create fear and justify harsh government action.","zh":"這類事件可以製造恐懼，並合理化強硬政府行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a failed murder attempt against a public figure.","zh":"這個短語描述針對公眾人物的失敗謀殺企圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"use something as an excuse to","meaning":"以某事作為藉口去……","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck used the attempted assassination as an excuse to attack the socialists.","zh":"Bismarck 以暗殺未遂作為藉口去攻擊社會主義者。"},{"en":"To use something as an excuse to do something means to use an event as a reason for an action one already wanted to take.","zh":"use something as an excuse to do something 指利用某事件作理由，去做本來已想做的事。"},{"en":"A manager may use one late arrival as an excuse to punish the whole team.","zh":"經理可能以一次遲到作為藉口去懲罰整個團隊。"},{"en":"People may use a crisis as an excuse to introduce stricter rules.","zh":"人們可能以危機作為藉口去引入更嚴格規則。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests the stated reason is not the real reason.","zh":"這個短語常暗示表面理由不是真正理由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"blame someone for","meaning":"因……責怪某人","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck blamed the socialists for the attempt on the Kaiser’s life.","zh":"Bismarck 因對皇帝的暗殺企圖而責怪社會主義者。"},{"en":"To blame someone for something means to say they caused it or are responsible for it.","zh":"blame someone for something 指說某人造成某事或要為某事負責。"},{"en":"A teacher should not blame a whole class for one student’s mistake.","zh":"老師不應因一名學生的錯誤而責怪全班。"},{"en":"Blame can turn public anger toward a chosen target.","zh":"責怪可以把公眾憤怒轉向某個指定目標。"},{"en":"This phrase connects responsibility with accusation.","zh":"這個短語把責任與指控連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the attempt on someone’s life","meaning":"對某人的暗殺企圖","examples":[{"en":"The attempt on the Kaiser’s life was blamed on the socialists.","zh":"對皇帝的暗殺企圖被歸咎於社會主義者。"},{"en":"An attempt on someone’s life is an effort to kill that person.","zh":"attempt on someone’s life 指試圖殺死某人。"},{"en":"After an attempt on a president’s life, the whole country may enter a period of fear.","zh":"總統遭暗殺企圖後，整個國家可能進入恐懼時期。"},{"en":"Such an attempt can be used politically if leaders blame an enemy group.","zh":"如果領袖把責任歸咎於敵對群體，這種企圖可以被政治利用。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal way to describe an assassination attempt.","zh":"這個短語是描述暗殺企圖的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"arrest the leaders","meaning":"逮捕領袖","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck immediately arrested the leaders.","zh":"Bismarck 立即逮捕領袖。"},{"en":"To arrest the leaders means to take the people in charge into legal custody.","zh":"arrest the leaders 指把負責人依法拘留。"},{"en":"Police may arrest the leaders of a violent group after an attack.","zh":"警方可能在襲擊後逮捕暴力組織的領袖。"},{"en":"Arresting leaders can weaken an organisation by removing its direction.","zh":"逮捕領袖可以透過移除指揮來削弱組織。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct state action against leadership.","zh":"這個短語描述國家針對領導層的直接行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ban party meetings","meaning":"禁止政黨會議","examples":[{"en":"He banned party meetings after the assassination attempt.","zh":"他在暗殺企圖後禁止政黨會議。"},{"en":"To ban party meetings means to officially forbid a political party from gathering.","zh":"ban party meetings 指正式禁止某政黨集會。"},{"en":"A government may ban meetings during an emergency, but such bans can limit political freedom.","zh":"政府可能在緊急狀態下禁止會議，但這類禁令可以限制政治自由。"},{"en":"Banning meetings makes it harder for a party to organise supporters.","zh":"禁止會議會令政黨更難組織支持者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes restricting political activity.","zh":"這個短語描述限制政治活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"suppress newspapers","meaning":"壓制報章","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck suppressed socialist newspapers.","zh":"Bismarck 壓制社會主義報章。"},{"en":"To suppress newspapers means to stop or control publications so they cannot freely spread ideas.","zh":"suppress newspapers 指阻止或控制出版物，使其不能自由傳播想法。"},{"en":"A government suppresses newspapers when it closes them or censors their reports.","zh":"政府關閉報章或審查報道時，就是壓制報章。"},{"en":"Suppressing newspapers can silence opposition but may also create public resentment.","zh":"壓制報章可以使反對聲音沉默，但也可能製造公眾怨恨。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limiting press freedom.","zh":"這個短語描述限制新聞自由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"efforts to destroy","meaning":"摧毀……的努力","examples":[{"en":"His efforts to destroy the socialist movement failed.","zh":"他摧毀社會主義運動的努力失敗了。"},{"en":"Efforts to destroy something are attempts to eliminate or break it completely.","zh":"efforts to destroy something 指試圖完全消除或破壞某事的努力。"},{"en":"A company’s efforts to destroy a competitor may fail if customers trust the competitor more.","zh":"如果顧客更信任競爭對手，公司摧毀對手的努力可能失敗。"},{"en":"Strong attacks can sometimes make a movement more united instead of weaker.","zh":"強烈攻擊有時會令運動更團結，而不是更弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deliberate attempts at complete removal.","zh":"這個短語描述有意完全消除的嘗試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the socialist movement","meaning":"社會主義運動","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck tried to destroy the socialist movement.","zh":"Bismarck 試圖摧毀社會主義運動。"},{"en":"The socialist movement is a political movement that seeks greater equality and stronger rights for workers.","zh":"socialist movement 指追求更大平等和更強工人權利的政治運動。"},{"en":"A history class may study the socialist movement to understand industrial workers’ demands.","zh":"歷史課可能研究社會主義運動，以理解工業工人的要求。"},{"en":"A growing movement can challenge leaders who depend on traditional elites.","zh":"日益壯大的運動可以挑戰依賴傳統精英的領袖。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised political activity around socialist ideas.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞社會主義思想的有組織政治活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"treble","meaning":"增至三倍","examples":[{"en":"The party’s popularity had trebled by 1890.","zh":"到 1890 年，該黨受歡迎程度已增至三倍。"},{"en":"To treble means to become three times as large or as much.","zh":"treble 指變成原來的三倍大或三倍多。"},{"en":"A small club’s membership may treble after a successful open day.","zh":"小型學會在成功開放日後，會員人數可能增至三倍。"},{"en":"If support trebles, opponents may become much more worried.","zh":"如果支持率增至三倍，對手可能變得更擔心。"},{"en":"This word describes a threefold increase.","zh":"這個詞描述三倍增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"by 1890","meaning":"到1890年","examples":[{"en":"By 1890, the socialist movement had become more popular.","zh":"到 1890 年，社會主義運動已變得更受歡迎。"},{"en":"By 1890 means before or at the year 1890.","zh":"by 1890 指在 1890 年之前或到 1890 年時。"},{"en":"By the end of the term, students should be able to write a full essay plan.","zh":"到學期末，學生應能寫出完整作文大綱。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a deadline or time point for a completed change.","zh":"這個短語為已完成變化設定期限或時間點。"},{"en":"It helps readers understand when a development had already happened.","zh":"它幫助讀者理解某發展何時已經發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"intervention with","meaning":"對……的干預","examples":[{"en":"His intervention with the church had not gone as planned.","zh":"他對教會的干預未如計劃般發展。"},{"en":"Intervention with a group means active involvement in its affairs to change or control it.","zh":"intervention with a group 指主動介入該群體事務，以改變或控制它。"},{"en":"A principal’s intervention with a troubled class may include new rules and extra counselling.","zh":"校長對問題班級的干預可能包括新規則和額外輔導。"},{"en":"Interventions can help if well planned, but they can fail if people resist them.","zh":"干預如果規劃良好可以有幫助，但如果人們抗拒就可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deliberate interference or involvement.","zh":"這個短語描述有意干涉或介入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not go as planned","meaning":"未如計劃般發展","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck’s attack on the socialists did not go as planned.","zh":"Bismarck 對社會主義者的攻擊未如計劃般發展。"},{"en":"If something does not go as planned, it develops differently from what people expected or intended.","zh":"not go as planned 指某事發展與人們預期或意圖不同。"},{"en":"A school trip may not go as planned if heavy rain closes the outdoor area.","zh":"如果大雨令戶外區域關閉，學校旅行可能未如計劃般發展。"},{"en":"Plans fail when conditions, people, or timing behave differently from expectations.","zh":"當環境、人或時機與預期不同，計劃就會失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gap between intention and result.","zh":"這個短語描述意圖與結果之間的落差。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fail to achieve one’s objective","meaning":"未能達成目標","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck failed to achieve his objective.","zh":"Bismarck 未能達成目標。"},{"en":"To fail to achieve one’s objective means not to reach the goal one intended.","zh":"fail to achieve one’s objective 指未能達到原本意圖的目標。"},{"en":"A student may fail to achieve her objective if she revises only the easiest topics.","zh":"如果學生只溫習最容易的課題，可能未能達成自己的目標。"},{"en":"Failure to reach an objective can force someone to change strategy.","zh":"未能達成目標可以迫使人改變策略。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the gap between goal and outcome.","zh":"這個短語著重目標與結果之間的落差。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"to one’s credit","meaning":"值得肯定的是","examples":[{"en":"To his credit, Bismarck still held on to power.","zh":"值得肯定的是，Bismarck 仍保住權力。"},{"en":"To one’s credit means someone deserves some praise for a good quality or achievement.","zh":"to one’s credit 指某人因良好品質或成就而值得得到一些讚賞。"},{"en":"To her credit, the student admitted her mistake and corrected it quickly.","zh":"值得肯定的是，該學生承認錯誤並迅速更正。"},{"en":"This phrase gives fair recognition even when the wider situation is negative.","zh":"這個短語即使在整體負面情況中，也給予公平肯定。"},{"en":"It often introduces a positive point after criticism.","zh":"它常在批評後引入一個正面點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hold on to power","meaning":"保住權力","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck managed to hold on to power.","zh":"Bismarck 設法保住權力。"},{"en":"To hold on to power means to keep control or authority despite challenges.","zh":"hold on to power 指在面對挑戰時仍保持控制或權威。"},{"en":"A class leader may hold on to power if classmates still trust her after a mistake.","zh":"如果同學在班長犯錯後仍信任她，她可能保住權力。"},{"en":"Leaders hold on to power through support, strategy, rules, or pressure.","zh":"領袖透過支持、策略、規則或壓力保住權力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping authority rather than gaining it for the first time.","zh":"這個短語描述保持權威，而不是首次取得權力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"domestic position","meaning":"國內政治地位","examples":[{"en":"His domestic position was relatively secure after 1871.","zh":"1871 年後，他的國內政治地位相對穩固。"},{"en":"Domestic position means a leader’s standing and power within his own country.","zh":"domestic position 指領袖在自己國家內的地位和權力。"},{"en":"A prime minister’s domestic position may weaken if voters lose trust at home.","zh":"如果本國選民失去信任，首相的國內政治地位可能削弱。"},{"en":"A secure domestic position gives a leader more freedom to focus on foreign affairs.","zh":"穩固的國內政治地位讓領袖更有自由專注外交事務。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to internal political strength.","zh":"這個短語指國內政治實力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"relatively secure","meaning":"相對穩固","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck’s domestic position was relatively secure.","zh":"Bismarck 的國內政治地位相對穩固。"},{"en":"Relatively secure means fairly safe or stable compared with possible alternatives.","zh":"relatively secure 指相比其他可能情況較安全或穩定。"},{"en":"A student’s place in a course may be relatively secure if she has already passed the main assessment.","zh":"如果學生已通過主要評核，她在課程中的位置可能相對穩固。"},{"en":"Something relatively secure can still face risk, but the risk is not immediate or severe.","zh":"相對穩固的事物仍可能面對風險，但風險並非即時或嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a careful, not absolute, judgement of safety.","zh":"這個短語給出謹慎而非絕對的安全判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"devote time to","meaning":"投放時間於……","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck devoted much of his time to foreign policy.","zh":"Bismarck 把大量時間投放於外交政策。"},{"en":"To devote time to something means to spend a lot of time and attention on it.","zh":"devote time to something 指把大量時間和注意力投放於某事。"},{"en":"A student may devote time to vocabulary every morning before school.","zh":"學生可能每天上學前把時間投放於詞彙。"},{"en":"People devote time to what they believe is important or urgent.","zh":"人們會把時間投放於自己認為重要或迫切的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase shows priority through time spent.","zh":"這個短語透過所花時間顯示優先次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"foreign policy","meaning":"外交政策","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck focused heavily on foreign policy after 1871.","zh":"1871 年後，Bismarck 非常集中於外交政策。"},{"en":"Foreign policy is a government’s plan for dealing with other countries.","zh":"foreign policy 指政府處理與其他國家關係的計劃。"},{"en":"A country’s foreign policy may include trade agreements, alliances, and peace talks.","zh":"一個國家的外交政策可能包括貿易協議、同盟和和平談判。"},{"en":"Foreign policy matters because decisions abroad can affect security and the economy at home.","zh":"外交政策很重要，因為海外決策可以影響本國安全和經濟。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to international strategy by a state.","zh":"這個短語指國家的國際策略。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"unite Germany","meaning":"統一德國","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck had used war to unite Germany.","zh":"Bismarck 曾用戰爭統一德國。"},{"en":"To unite Germany means to bring separate German states together into one country.","zh":"unite Germany 指把分散的德意志邦國結合成一個國家。"},{"en":"A history textbook may explain how military victories helped unite Germany.","zh":"歷史教科書可能解釋軍事勝利如何幫助統一德國。"},{"en":"Uniting divided territories can create national strength but also new tensions.","zh":"統一分裂領土可以創造國家力量，但也可能帶來新緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the political act of forming one German state.","zh":"這個短語描述形成一個德國國家的政治行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make a country great","meaning":"使一個國家強大","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck used war to make Germany great.","zh":"Bismarck 用戰爭使德國強大。"},{"en":"To make a country great means to increase its power, status, wealth, or influence.","zh":"make a country great 指提升一國的力量、地位、財富或影響力。"},{"en":"Some leaders try to make a country great through education, trade, and technology.","zh":"有些領袖嘗試透過教育、貿易和科技使國家強大。"},{"en":"A country may become stronger, but the method used can shape its future problems.","zh":"國家可能變得更強，但所用方法可以塑造其未來問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes national strengthening, often with political ambition.","zh":"這個短語描述國家強化，常帶政治野心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be best served by","meaning":"最能透過……達成","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck believed his ambitions were best served by peace.","zh":"Bismarck 相信自己的抱負最能透過和平達成。"},{"en":"To be best served by something means to be helped most effectively by it.","zh":"be best served by something 指最有效地受到某事幫助。"},{"en":"A student’s progress may be best served by regular practice rather than last-minute revision.","zh":"學生進步最能透過定期練習達成，而不是臨急溫習。"},{"en":"If a goal is best served by peace, war would damage rather than help it.","zh":"如果目標最能透過和平達成，戰爭就會造成損害而非幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the most useful method for an aim.","zh":"這個短語指出達成目標最有用的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"isolate a hostile France","meaning":"孤立敵對的法國","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck wanted to isolate a hostile France.","zh":"Bismarck 想孤立敵對的法國。"},{"en":"To isolate a hostile France means to keep France, seen as an enemy, without strong allies.","zh":"isolate a hostile France 指使被視為敵人的法國缺乏強大盟友。"},{"en":"A team may try to isolate a strong rival by persuading others not to support it.","zh":"團隊可能透過說服其他人不要支持強大對手，來孤立它。"},{"en":"Isolation can weaken an opponent by reducing its options and support.","zh":"孤立可以透過減少選擇和支持來削弱對手。"},{"en":"This phrase describes diplomatic containment of an enemy.","zh":"這個短語描述對敵人的外交遏制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"require diplomatic skills","meaning":"需要外交技巧","examples":[{"en":"His plan required considerable diplomatic skills.","zh":"他的計劃需要相當的外交技巧。"},{"en":"To require diplomatic skills means to need the ability to negotiate carefully and manage sensitive relationships.","zh":"require diplomatic skills 指需要小心談判和處理敏感關係的能力。"},{"en":"Solving a dispute between two departments may require diplomatic skills.","zh":"解決兩個部門之間的爭端可能需要外交技巧。"},{"en":"Diplomatic skills are needed when direct pressure would make people more resistant.","zh":"當直接施壓會令人更抗拒，就需要外交技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that success depends on tact and negotiation.","zh":"這個短語顯示成功取決於圓滑和談判。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the Dreikaiserbund agreement","meaning":"三皇同盟協議","examples":[{"en":"The Dreikaiserbund agreement was signed in 1873.","zh":"三皇同盟協議於 1873 年簽訂。"},{"en":"The Dreikaiserbund agreement was an alliance involving the emperors of Germany, Austria-Hungary, and Russia.","zh":"the Dreikaiserbund agreement 指涉及德國、奧匈和俄國皇帝的同盟。"},{"en":"Students may study the Dreikaiserbund agreement when learning how Bismarck tried to isolate France.","zh":"學生學習 Bismarck 如何試圖孤立法國時，可能研究三皇同盟協議。"},{"en":"Such agreements can reduce conflict by linking powerful states together.","zh":"這類協議可以透過連結強國來減少衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific diplomatic agreement.","zh":"這個短語命名一項特定外交協議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a first step towards","meaning":"邁向……的第一步","examples":[{"en":"The agreement was a first step towards isolating France.","zh":"該協議是邁向孤立法國的第一步。"},{"en":"A first step towards something is the beginning action that moves a plan in that direction.","zh":"a first step towards something 指使計劃朝某方向前進的起始行動。"},{"en":"Saving a small amount each week can be a first step towards buying a computer.","zh":"每週儲蓄一小筆錢可以是邁向購買電腦的第一步。"},{"en":"First steps matter because they turn an intention into action.","zh":"第一步很重要，因為它把意圖變成行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the starting point of a larger goal.","zh":"這個短語描述更大目標的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the Balkan crisis","meaning":"巴爾幹危機","examples":[{"en":"The Balkan crisis severely tested Bismarck’s diplomacy.","zh":"巴爾幹危機嚴峻考驗了 Bismarck 的外交。"},{"en":"The Balkan crisis was a conflict in southeastern Europe involving competing powers and national interests.","zh":"the Balkan crisis 指歐洲東南部涉及競爭強權和民族利益的衝突。"},{"en":"A history class may discuss the Balkan crisis to show how local disputes can affect major powers.","zh":"歷史課可能討論巴爾幹危機，以顯示本地爭端如何影響大國。"},{"en":"Crises in unstable regions can test whether alliances are strong or fragile.","zh":"不穩定地區的危機可以考驗同盟是強還是脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a major diplomatic challenge in Europe.","zh":"這個短語指歐洲一場重大外交挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a conflict involving","meaning":"涉及……的衝突","examples":[{"en":"The Balkan crisis was a conflict involving Russia and Austria-Hungary.","zh":"巴爾幹危機是一場涉及俄國和奧匈帝國的衝突。"},{"en":"A conflict involving several parties is a dispute or struggle in which those parties take part.","zh":"a conflict involving several parties 指那些方面參與其中的爭端或鬥爭。"},{"en":"A workplace conflict involving managers and staff may need mediation.","zh":"涉及經理和員工的職場衝突可能需要調解。"},{"en":"More parties in a conflict can make settlement harder because interests multiply.","zh":"衝突中參與方越多，解決越困難，因為利益會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who is part of a dispute.","zh":"這個短語指出誰參與爭端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"severely test","meaning":"嚴峻考驗","examples":[{"en":"The crisis severely tested his diplomatic credentials.","zh":"這場危機嚴峻考驗了他的外交能力。"},{"en":"To severely test something means to challenge it in a very serious way.","zh":"severely test something 指以非常嚴重的方式挑戰某能力或事物。"},{"en":"A sudden family illness can severely test a student’s ability to keep up with schoolwork.","zh":"突發家庭疾病可以嚴峻考驗學生跟上學業的能力。"},{"en":"Difficult situations reveal whether skills are real or only claimed.","zh":"困難情況會揭示能力是真的，還是只是聲稱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong challenge to ability or strength.","zh":"這個短語描述對能力或力量的強烈挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"diplomatic credentials","meaning":"外交能力；外交資歷","examples":[{"en":"The Balkan crisis tested Bismarck’s diplomatic credentials.","zh":"巴爾幹危機考驗了 Bismarck 的外交能力。"},{"en":"Diplomatic credentials are the skills, experience, and reputation that show someone can handle diplomacy.","zh":"diplomatic credentials 指顯示某人能處理外交的技能、經驗和聲譽。"},{"en":"A negotiator’s diplomatic credentials grow when she resolves difficult disputes fairly.","zh":"當談判者公平解決困難爭端，她的外交資歷會增強。"},{"en":"Credentials are tested when a real crisis requires careful judgement.","zh":"當真正危機需要仔細判斷，資歷就會受到考驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes proof of diplomatic ability.","zh":"這個短語描述外交能力的證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"offer oneself as","meaning":"自薦擔任……","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck offered himself as an honest broker.","zh":"Bismarck 自薦擔任公正調停人。"},{"en":"To offer oneself as something means to present oneself as willing to take on that role.","zh":"offer oneself as something 指把自己呈現為願意承擔某角色。"},{"en":"A senior student may offer herself as a mediator when two classmates argue.","zh":"當兩名同學爭執，高年級學生可能自薦擔任調解人。"},{"en":"Offering oneself as a helper can build trust if others believe the person is fair.","zh":"如果其他人相信該人公平，自薦擔任幫助者可以建立信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes volunteering for a role.","zh":"這個短語描述自願承擔某角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"an honest broker","meaning":"公正調停人","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck presented himself as an honest broker in the dispute.","zh":"Bismarck 在爭端中把自己呈現為公正調停人。"},{"en":"An honest broker is a neutral person who helps opposing sides reach an agreement.","zh":"honest broker 指幫助對立雙方達成協議的中立人士。"},{"en":"A teacher can act as an honest broker when two student groups argue over shared space.","zh":"當兩組學生爭奪共用空間，老師可以擔任公正調停人。"},{"en":"An honest broker must appear fair, or neither side will trust the process.","zh":"公正調停人必須看起來公平，否則雙方都不會信任過程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a trusted mediator.","zh":"這個短語描述可信任的調解者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"resolve the dispute","meaning":"解決爭端","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck tried to help resolve the dispute.","zh":"Bismarck 試圖幫助解決爭端。"},{"en":"To resolve the dispute means to settle a disagreement so that the parties can move on.","zh":"resolve the dispute 指解決分歧，讓各方可以繼續前進。"},{"en":"A manager may resolve the dispute by giving both teams a clear schedule for using the room.","zh":"經理可能透過給兩隊清楚房間使用時間表來解決爭端。"},{"en":"Disputes are resolved when the main source of disagreement is dealt with.","zh":"當主要分歧來源得到處理，爭端就被解決。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ending conflict through agreement or decision.","zh":"這個短語描述透過協議或決定結束衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the subsequent Congress of Berlin","meaning":"隨後的柏林會議","examples":[{"en":"The subsequent Congress of Berlin strengthened his reputation.","zh":"隨後的柏林會議強化了他的聲譽。"},{"en":"The subsequent Congress of Berlin means the Berlin conference that followed the crisis or earlier events.","zh":"subsequent Congress of Berlin 指危機或早前事件後舉行的柏林會議。"},{"en":"Students may mention the subsequent Congress of Berlin when explaining Bismarck’s diplomatic success.","zh":"學生解釋 Bismarck 的外交成功時，可能提到隨後的柏林會議。"},{"en":"A later conference can change how people judge a leader’s handling of a crisis.","zh":"後來的會議可以改變人們如何評價領袖處理危機的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a later diplomatic meeting.","zh":"這個短語指出後續的外交會議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"host a congress","meaning":"主辦會議","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck hosted the Congress of Berlin.","zh":"Bismarck 主辦柏林會議。"},{"en":"To host a congress means to organise and receive participants for a major formal meeting.","zh":"host a congress 指組織並接待大型正式會議的參與者。"},{"en":"A university may host a congress on education reform and invite experts from many countries.","zh":"大學可能主辦教育改革會議，邀請多國專家。"},{"en":"Hosting a congress can increase a city’s or leader’s prestige.","zh":"主辦會議可以提升城市或領袖的聲望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking responsibility for a formal gathering.","zh":"這個短語描述負責正式集會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"an outstanding success","meaning":"極大成功","examples":[{"en":"The Congress of Berlin was an outstanding success.","zh":"柏林會議是一次極大成功。"},{"en":"An outstanding success is a very impressive achievement.","zh":"outstanding success 指非常令人印象深刻的成就。"},{"en":"A school concert may be an outstanding success if tickets sell out and students perform confidently.","zh":"如果學校音樂會門票售罄，學生又自信演出，它可能是極大成功。"},{"en":"Outstanding success usually improves confidence, reputation, or support.","zh":"極大成功通常會提升信心、聲譽或支持。"},{"en":"This phrase gives strong praise for a result.","zh":"這個短語對結果給予高度讚賞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"serve to reinforce","meaning":"有助鞏固","examples":[{"en":"The congress served to reinforce Bismarck’s reputation.","zh":"該會議有助鞏固 Bismarck 的聲譽。"},{"en":"To serve to reinforce something means to help strengthen it.","zh":"serve to reinforce something 指有助加強某事。"},{"en":"A student’s strong final essay can serve to reinforce the teacher’s confidence in her progress.","zh":"學生出色的期末作文可以鞏固老師對她進步的信心。"},{"en":"Repeated success reinforces reputation because people see a pattern.","zh":"反覆成功會鞏固聲譽，因為人們看見一種模式。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how an event strengthens an existing idea or image.","zh":"這個短語顯示事件如何加強既有想法或形象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reputation as","meaning":"作為……的聲譽","examples":[{"en":"The event reinforced his reputation as a shrewd diplomat.","zh":"該事件鞏固了他作為精明外交家的聲譽。"},{"en":"Reputation as something means the public image of being that kind of person.","zh":"reputation as something 指作為某類人的公眾形象。"},{"en":"A teacher may build a reputation as a patient and clear explainer.","zh":"老師可能建立作為有耐性且解釋清楚者的聲譽。"},{"en":"A reputation grows when people repeatedly see the same quality in action.","zh":"當人們反覆看到同一品質在行動中出現，聲譽就會形成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how someone is known by others.","zh":"這個短語描述某人在他人眼中如何被認識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a shrewd diplomat","meaning":"精明的外交家","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck was regarded as a shrewd diplomat.","zh":"Bismarck 被視為精明的外交家。"},{"en":"A shrewd diplomat is someone clever and practical in handling negotiations and international relationships.","zh":"shrewd diplomat 指在處理談判和國際關係時聰明而務實的人。"},{"en":"A shrewd diplomat may keep both sides talking even when they dislike each other.","zh":"精明的外交家可能在雙方互不喜歡時仍令他們保持對話。"},{"en":"Shrewd diplomacy can prevent conflict by giving each side something to accept.","zh":"精明外交可以透過給各方一些可接受之處來防止衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase praises sharp judgement in diplomacy.","zh":"這個短語讚揚外交中的敏銳判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"continue in this vein","meaning":"沿着這種方式繼續","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck’s foreign policy continued in this vein.","zh":"Bismarck 的外交政策沿着這種方式繼續。"},{"en":"To continue in this vein means to keep following the same style, method, or direction.","zh":"continue in this vein 指繼續遵循同一風格、方法或方向。"},{"en":"If a teacher’s examples are clear and useful, she should continue in this vein.","zh":"如果老師的例子清晰有用，她應沿着這種方式繼續。"},{"en":"A policy continues in this vein when later actions repeat the same approach.","zh":"當後續行動重複同一方法，政策就是沿着這種方式繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase links a later pattern to an earlier one.","zh":"這個短語把後來模式與早前模式連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"throughout one’s reign","meaning":"在某人執政期間","examples":[{"en":"His foreign policy continued throughout his reign as Chancellor.","zh":"他的外交政策在其擔任首相期間一直延續。"},{"en":"Throughout one’s reign means during the whole period when someone is ruling or holding power.","zh":"throughout one’s reign 指在某人統治或掌權的整段期間。"},{"en":"A principal may promote reading throughout her reign as head of the school.","zh":"校長在其擔任學校首長期間可能一直推動閱讀。"},{"en":"A policy lasting throughout a reign shows long-term priority.","zh":"一項政策若在整段執政期間持續，顯示它是長期優先事項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continuity during a period of leadership.","zh":"這個短語描述領導時期中的連續性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"build up strategic alliances","meaning":"建立戰略同盟","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck built up strategic alliances with major powers.","zh":"Bismarck 與主要強國建立戰略同盟。"},{"en":"To build up strategic alliances means to gradually create useful partnerships for long-term advantage.","zh":"build up strategic alliances 指逐步建立有利於長遠利益的有用合作關係。"},{"en":"A small business may build up strategic alliances with suppliers, schools, and community groups.","zh":"小企業可能與供應商、學校和社區團體建立戰略同盟。"},{"en":"Strong alliances can protect a group when challenges appear.","zh":"強大同盟可以在挑戰出現時保護一個群體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planned relationship-building for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述有目的的關係建立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the big powers","meaning":"大國","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck sought alliances with the big powers.","zh":"Bismarck 尋求與大國結盟。"},{"en":"The big powers are the strongest and most influential countries in a region or period.","zh":"big powers 指某地區或時期中最強大、最有影響力的國家。"},{"en":"Smaller countries may watch the big powers carefully before choosing alliances.","zh":"小國在選擇同盟前，可能仔細觀察大國。"},{"en":"Decisions by big powers can affect the security of many weaker states.","zh":"大國的決定可以影響許多較弱國家的安全。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to major states with significant influence.","zh":"這個短語指具有重大影響力的主要國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in the hope that","meaning":"希望……","examples":[{"en":"He built alliances in the hope that he could isolate France and Britain.","zh":"他建立同盟，希望能孤立法國和英國。"},{"en":"In the hope that means doing something because one wants a particular result to happen.","zh":"in the hope that 指因希望某特定結果發生而做某事。"},{"en":"A student may join a study group in the hope that she will stay motivated.","zh":"學生可能加入溫習小組，希望自己保持動力。"},{"en":"People act in the hope that their effort will lead to a desired outcome.","zh":"人們行動，是希望努力會帶來想要的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase connects action with expectation.","zh":"這個短語把行動與期望連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"main threats","meaning":"主要威脅","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck saw France and Britain as his main threats.","zh":"Bismarck 把法國和英國視為主要威脅。"},{"en":"Main threats are the most important dangers or opponents someone faces.","zh":"main threats 指某人面對的最重要危險或對手。"},{"en":"A small shop may see rising rent and online competition as its main threats.","zh":"小店可能把租金上升和網上競爭視為主要威脅。"},{"en":"Identifying main threats helps leaders decide where to focus attention.","zh":"找出主要威脅有助領袖決定把注意力放在哪裡。"},{"en":"This phrase names the biggest sources of danger.","zh":"這個短語命名最大危險來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"keep someone isolated","meaning":"使某人被孤立","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck hoped to keep France and Britain isolated.","zh":"Bismarck 希望使法國和英國被孤立。"},{"en":"To keep someone isolated means to prevent them from gaining support or close contact with others.","zh":"keep someone isolated 指阻止某人取得支持或與其他人建立密切接觸。"},{"en":"A bully may try to keep a classmate isolated by stopping others from talking to him.","zh":"欺凌者可能透過阻止其他人與同學說話，使該同學被孤立。"},{"en":"Diplomatic isolation weakens a rival by reducing its friends and options.","zh":"外交孤立透過減少朋友和選擇來削弱對手。"},{"en":"This phrase describes maintaining separation from support networks.","zh":"這個短語描述維持與支援網絡分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in truth","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In truth, Bismarck’s reign confirmed his diplomatic skill.","zh":"事實上，Bismarck 的執政確認了他的外交技巧。"},{"en":"In truth means in reality or when the facts are considered carefully.","zh":"in truth 指在現實中，或仔細考慮事實後。"},{"en":"The plan looked simple, but in truth it required months of preparation.","zh":"計劃看似簡單，但事實上需要數月準備。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to correct or clarify a surface impression.","zh":"作者使用這個短語來更正或澄清表面印象。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a more accurate judgement.","zh":"這個短語引入更準確的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reign as chancellor","meaning":"擔任首相期間","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck’s reign as chancellor showed his political ability.","zh":"Bismarck 擔任首相期間展現了他的政治能力。"},{"en":"Reign as chancellor means the period during which someone served as chancellor.","zh":"reign as chancellor 指某人擔任首相的期間。"},{"en":"A historian may judge a leader’s reign as chancellor by reforms, crises, and long-term effects.","zh":"歷史學家可能根據改革、危機和長遠影響來評價領袖擔任首相期間。"},{"en":"A period in office can reveal strengths that earlier speeches only promised.","zh":"任職期間可以揭示早前演說只承諾過的能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes time spent holding the office of chancellor.","zh":"這個短語描述擔任首相職位的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"confirm one’s status as","meaning":"確認某人作為……的地位","examples":[{"en":"His achievements confirmed his status as a shrewd politician.","zh":"他的成就確認了他作為精明政治家的地位。"},{"en":"To confirm one’s status as something means to prove that a person deserves that reputation or position.","zh":"confirm one’s status as something 指證明某人配得上該聲譽或地位。"},{"en":"A student’s consistent top marks may confirm her status as the strongest writer in the class.","zh":"學生持續取得最高分，可能確認她作為班中最強寫作者的地位。"},{"en":"Repeated success confirms status because it gives others evidence to trust.","zh":"反覆成功會確認地位，因為它給他人可信證據。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a reputation becoming firmly established.","zh":"這個短語顯示聲譽變得穩固。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"shrewd and wily","meaning":"精明而狡黠的","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck was a shrewd and wily diplomat.","zh":"Bismarck 是一名精明而狡黠的外交家。"},{"en":"Shrewd and wily means clever, practical, and skilled at getting advantages, sometimes through indirect methods.","zh":"shrewd and wily 指聰明、務實，並擅長取得優勢，有時透過間接方法。"},{"en":"A shrewd and wily negotiator may notice what each side secretly wants.","zh":"精明而狡黠的談判者可能注意到各方暗中想要甚麼。"},{"en":"Such people can solve problems, but others may also fear being manipulated by them.","zh":"這類人可以解決問題，但其他人也可能害怕被他們操控。"},{"en":"This phrase mixes admiration for intelligence with suspicion of craftiness.","zh":"這個短語把對智慧的欣賞與對狡猾的懷疑混合起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"objectives were broadly achieved","meaning":"目標大致達成","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck’s objectives were broadly achieved.","zh":"Bismarck 的目標大致達成。"},{"en":"Objectives were broadly achieved means the main goals were mostly reached, even if not perfectly.","zh":"objectives were broadly achieved 指主要目標大多達成，即使並不完美。"},{"en":"A school project’s objectives were broadly achieved if students learned the key skills but missed some details.","zh":"如果學生學到關鍵技能但錯過一些細節，學校項目的目標就算大致達成。"},{"en":"Broad achievement suggests success in the main areas, not complete success in every area.","zh":"大致達成暗示主要範圍成功，而不是每方面完全成功。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a balanced judgement of success.","zh":"這個短語給出平衡的成功判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"so-called","meaning":"所謂的","examples":[{"en":"The article questions whether his so-called juggling was successful.","zh":"文章質疑他所謂的斡旋是否成功。"},{"en":"So-called is used when the writer doubts, questions, or distances themselves from a label.","zh":"so-called 用於作者懷疑、質疑或與某標籤保持距離時。"},{"en":"A shop’s so-called discount may not be real if prices were raised first.","zh":"如果商店先加價，所謂的折扣可能並不真實。"},{"en":"This word can make a description sound suspicious or ironic.","zh":"這個詞可以令描述聽起來可疑或諷刺。"},{"en":"It suggests the label may not be fully accurate.","zh":"它暗示該標籤未必完全準確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a less than perfect legacy","meaning":"不盡完美的遺產","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck left a less than perfect legacy.","zh":"Bismarck 留下不盡完美的遺產。"},{"en":"A less than perfect legacy is an inheritance of results that includes both achievements and serious problems.","zh":"less than perfect legacy 指留下的結果既有成就，也有嚴重問題。"},{"en":"A principal may leave a less than perfect legacy if exam results improve but teacher morale falls.","zh":"如果校長令考試成績改善但教師士氣下降，可能留下不盡完美的遺產。"},{"en":"A legacy can be impressive in the short term but harmful in the long term.","zh":"遺產可以短期令人印象深刻，但長期有害。"},{"en":"This phrase gives mixed rather than total praise.","zh":"這個短語給出混合評價，而不是完全讚揚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the ultimate say in","meaning":"對……有最終決定權","examples":[{"en":"The Kaiser had the ultimate say in domestic affairs.","zh":"皇帝對內政有最終決定權。"},{"en":"The ultimate say in something is the final power to decide it.","zh":"ultimate say in something 指對某事擁有最終決定權。"},{"en":"In a family business, the founder may still have the ultimate say in major spending.","zh":"在家族企業中，創辦人可能仍對重大開支有最終決定權。"},{"en":"When one person has the ultimate say, others may advise but cannot make the final decision.","zh":"當一個人有最終決定權，其他人可以建議，但不能作最後決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes final authority.","zh":"這個短語描述最終權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"domestic affairs","meaning":"內政","examples":[{"en":"The Kaiser had great power over domestic affairs.","zh":"皇帝對內政擁有很大權力。"},{"en":"Domestic affairs are matters inside a country, such as laws, taxes, education, and public order.","zh":"domestic affairs 指一國內部事務，例如法律、稅收、教育和公共秩序。"},{"en":"A government may focus on domestic affairs when housing and healthcare become urgent problems.","zh":"當房屋和醫療成為迫切問題，政府可能集中於內政。"},{"en":"Control over domestic affairs affects daily life more directly than many foreign issues.","zh":"對內政的控制比許多外交議題更直接影響日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to internal national matters.","zh":"這個短語指國家內部事務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"wield power","meaning":"行使權力","examples":[{"en":"The Kaiser could wield far too much power.","zh":"皇帝可以行使過多權力。"},{"en":"To wield power means to use authority or influence.","zh":"wield power 指使用權威或影響力。"},{"en":"A school principal can wield power by deciding budgets, rules, and staff duties.","zh":"校長可以透過決定預算、規則和員工職責來行使權力。"},{"en":"Power becomes dangerous when one person can wield it without enough checks.","zh":"當一個人可以在缺乏制衡下行使權力，權力就會變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active use of authority.","zh":"這個短語描述主動使用權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"should he choose to","meaning":"如果他選擇……","examples":[{"en":"The Kaiser had too much power should he choose to wield it.","zh":"如果皇帝選擇行使權力，他擁有過多權力。"},{"en":"Should he choose to means if he decides to do so.","zh":"should he choose to 指如果他決定這樣做。"},{"en":"The team captain could change the training schedule, should she choose to use her authority.","zh":"如果隊長選擇使用權威，她可以改變訓練時間表。"},{"en":"This structure suggests a possibility that depends on one person’s decision.","zh":"這個結構暗示某可能性取決於一個人的決定。"},{"en":"It is a formal way of saying “if he chooses to.”","zh":"它是 “if he chooses to” 的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"largely depend on","meaning":"很大程度上取決於","examples":[{"en":"The empire’s future largely depended on the Kaiser.","zh":"帝國的未來很大程度上取決於皇帝。"},{"en":"To largely depend on something means to be mainly determined by it.","zh":"largely depend on something 指主要由某事決定。"},{"en":"A student’s exam result may largely depend on daily revision rather than one night of study.","zh":"學生考試成績可能很大程度上取決於每日溫習，而不是一晚苦讀。"},{"en":"If a system depends largely on one person, it becomes vulnerable to that person’s weaknesses.","zh":"如果一個制度很大程度上取決於一個人，它就容易受該人的弱點影響。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the main source of influence or risk.","zh":"這個短語顯示主要影響或風險來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"strength and character","meaning":"能力與性格","examples":[{"en":"The future depended on the strength and character of one man.","zh":"未來取決於一個人的能力與性格。"},{"en":"Strength and character means a person’s ability, judgement, courage, and moral qualities.","zh":"strength and character 指一個人的能力、判斷、勇氣和道德品質。"},{"en":"A school’s recovery after a crisis may depend on the strength and character of its principal.","zh":"學校在危機後的恢復，可能取決於校長的能力與性格。"},{"en":"Strong institutions are safer than systems that rely too much on one person’s character.","zh":"強大制度比過度依賴一個人性格的制度更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes personal qualities that affect leadership.","zh":"這個短語描述影響領導的個人特質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"disastrous for","meaning":"對……造成災難性後果","examples":[{"en":"A weak Kaiser would be disastrous for the country.","zh":"軟弱的皇帝會對國家造成災難性後果。"},{"en":"Disastrous for something means causing very serious damage to it.","zh":"disastrous for something 指對某事造成非常嚴重損害。"},{"en":"A long transport strike could be disastrous for small shops that depend on daily customers.","zh":"長時間交通罷工可能對依賴每日顧客的小店造成災難性後果。"},{"en":"Weak leadership can be disastrous when a system gives one person too much power.","zh":"當制度給一人過多權力，軟弱領導可以造成災難性後果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a result that would be extremely harmful.","zh":"這個短語描述極有害的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the country’s welfare","meaning":"國家福祉","examples":[{"en":"A weak Kaiser would harm the country’s welfare.","zh":"軟弱的皇帝會損害國家福祉。"},{"en":"The country’s welfare means the general well-being, safety, and prosperity of the nation and its people.","zh":"the country’s welfare 指國家及人民整體的福祉、安全和繁榮。"},{"en":"Public health, education, and stable jobs all affect a country’s welfare.","zh":"公共衛生、教育和穩定工作都影響國家福祉。"},{"en":"Bad leadership can damage the country’s welfare by weakening trust and services.","zh":"差劣領導可以透過削弱信任和服務來損害國家福祉。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to national well-being, not only money.","zh":"這個短語指國家整體福祉，而不只是金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"so it would soon prove","meaning":"事實很快證明如此","examples":[{"en":"A weak Kaiser would be dangerous, and so it would soon prove.","zh":"軟弱的皇帝會很危險，而事實很快證明如此。"},{"en":"So it would soon prove means later events quickly showed that the statement was true.","zh":"so it would soon prove 指後來事件很快顯示該說法是真的。"},{"en":"The school warned that the roof was unsafe, and so it would soon prove when heavy rain caused damage.","zh":"學校警告屋頂不安全，而大雨造成損壞時，事實很快證明如此。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to foreshadow confirmation by later events.","zh":"作者使用這個短語預示後來事件會證實說法。"},{"en":"This phrase links prediction with later proof.","zh":"這個短語把預測與後來證明連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in the final analysis","meaning":"歸根究底","examples":[{"en":"In the final analysis, Bismarck restored Germany as a great power.","zh":"歸根究底，Bismarck 使德國恢復為強國。"},{"en":"In the final analysis means after considering all the evidence and arguments.","zh":"in the final analysis 指在考慮所有證據和論點之後。"},{"en":"In the final analysis, a study plan works only if the student actually follows it.","zh":"歸根究底，學習計劃只有在學生真正執行時才有效。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a final balanced judgement after discussion.","zh":"這個短語在討論後引入最終平衡判斷。"},{"en":"It signals the writer’s overall conclusion.","zh":"它表示作者的整體結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"put something back on the map","meaning":"使……重新受到重視","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck put Germany back on the map as a great power.","zh":"Bismarck 使德國作為強國重新受到重視。"},{"en":"To put something back on the map means to make it important, noticed, or respected again.","zh":"put something back on the map 指令某事物再次變得重要、受注意或受尊重。"},{"en":"A successful food festival can put a small town back on the map.","zh":"成功的美食節可以使小鎮重新受到重視。"},{"en":"Strong achievement can restore attention to a place or organisation that had been overlooked.","zh":"強大成就可以令被忽視的地方或組織重新受到關注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes renewed importance or recognition.","zh":"這個短語描述重新取得重要性或認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a great power","meaning":"強國","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck made Germany a great power in Europe.","zh":"Bismarck 使德國成為歐洲強國。"},{"en":"A great power is a country with major military, political, economic, or diplomatic influence.","zh":"great power 指在軍事、政治、經濟或外交上有重大影響力的國家。"},{"en":"Students study great powers to understand why their decisions affect smaller states.","zh":"學生研究強國，以理解為何其決定影響較小國家。"},{"en":"Becoming a great power can bring security, status, and rivalry.","zh":"成為強國可以帶來安全、地位和競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a highly influential state.","zh":"這個短語指高度有影響力的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"during one’s reign","meaning":"在某人執政期間","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck strengthened Germany during his reign.","zh":"Bismarck 在其執政期間強化了德國。"},{"en":"During one’s reign means while someone was ruling or holding high office.","zh":"during one’s reign 指在某人統治或擔任高位期間。"},{"en":"During her reign as principal, the school built a new library and improved exam results.","zh":"在她擔任校長期間，學校興建了新圖書館並改善考試成績。"},{"en":"A leader’s actions during his reign shape how history remembers him.","zh":"領袖在執政期間的行動，塑造歷史如何記住他。"},{"en":"This phrase marks events within a period of leadership.","zh":"這個短語標示領導時期中的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"we should not forget that","meaning":"我們不應忘記","examples":[{"en":"We should not forget that Bismarck created serious future problems.","zh":"我們不應忘記，Bismarck 造成了嚴重未來問題。"},{"en":"We should not forget that means the writer wants readers to remember an important balancing point.","zh":"we should not forget that 指作者希望讀者記住一個重要平衡點。"},{"en":"We should not forget that good exam results can still hide student stress.","zh":"我們不應忘記，好考試成績仍可能隱藏學生壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when adding a warning after praise.","zh":"這個短語在讚揚後加入警告時很有用。"},{"en":"It reminds readers not to judge too simply.","zh":"它提醒讀者不要過於簡單地判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"create the political situation","meaning":"造成政治局面","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck created the political situation that later harmed Germany.","zh":"Bismarck 造成了後來損害德國的政治局面。"},{"en":"To create the political situation means to produce the conditions of power, rules, and relationships that shape later events.","zh":"create the political situation 指造成會塑造後來事件的權力、規則和關係條件。"},{"en":"A school board can create the political situation for conflict if it excludes teachers from decisions.","zh":"如果校董會把老師排除在決策外，可能造成衝突的政治局面。"},{"en":"Political situations created today may cause problems years later.","zh":"今天造成的政治局面可能多年後引發問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on setting up the conditions for future outcomes.","zh":"這個短語著重建立未來結果的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the downfall of","meaning":"……的衰落；垮台","examples":[{"en":"His system contributed to the downfall of his country.","zh":"他的制度促成了其國家的衰落。"},{"en":"The downfall of someone or something is its loss of power, success, or stability.","zh":"the downfall of someone or something 指其失去權力、成功或穩定。"},{"en":"Poor financial planning can lead to the downfall of a small business.","zh":"差劣財務規劃可以導致小企業垮台。"},{"en":"Downfall often follows when hidden weaknesses finally become serious.","zh":"當隱藏弱點終於變嚴重，衰落常隨之而來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collapse or serious decline.","zh":"這個短語描述崩潰或嚴重下滑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"cannot be considered","meaning":"不能被視為","examples":[{"en":"His juggling cannot be considered a total success.","zh":"他的斡旋不能被視為完全成功。"},{"en":"Cannot be considered means should not be judged or described in that way.","zh":"cannot be considered 指不應被判斷或描述為那樣。"},{"en":"A project cannot be considered successful if it saves money but harms students.","zh":"如果項目省了錢卻傷害學生，就不能被視為成功。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a careful negative judgement.","zh":"這個短語引入謹慎的負面判斷。"},{"en":"It shows that the evidence does not support a certain conclusion.","zh":"它顯示證據不支持某結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a total success","meaning":"完全成功","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck’s political strategy was not a total success.","zh":"Bismarck 的政治策略並非完全成功。"},{"en":"A total success is a result with no major failure or serious negative consequence.","zh":"total success 指沒有重大失敗或嚴重負面後果的結果。"},{"en":"A school event is not a total success if many students enjoy it but safety rules are ignored.","zh":"如果許多學生享受活動但安全規則被忽視，學校活動就不是完全成功。"},{"en":"Something can be partly successful without being a total success.","zh":"某事可以部分成功，但不是完全成功。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete success, not mixed achievement.","zh":"這個短語描述完整成功，而不是混合成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"choose the correct answer","meaning":"選出正確答案","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct answer for each question.","zh":"考生為每題選出正確答案。"},{"en":"To choose the correct answer means to select the option that best matches the information or question.","zh":"choose the correct answer 指選出最符合資料或題目的選項。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should return to the passage before choosing the correct answer.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應回到文章再選出正確答案。"},{"en":"Careless guessing can lead to wrong answers even when the passage is understood.","zh":"即使理解文章，粗心猜測仍可能導致錯誤答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"succeed in doing something","meaning":"成功做到某事","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck succeeded in reuniting Germany.","zh":"Bismarck 成功統一德國。"},{"en":"To succeed in doing something means to manage to do it successfully.","zh":"succeed in doing something 指成功完成某事。"},{"en":"A student may succeed in improving grammar by correcting one mistake pattern each week.","zh":"學生可能透過每週改正一種錯誤模式，成功改善文法。"},{"en":"Success usually comes from clear goals, effort, and useful feedback.","zh":"成功通常來自清楚目標、努力和有用回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on achieving a specific action.","zh":"這個短語著重達成某個具體行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"suppress the Socialist party","meaning":"壓制社會黨","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck tried to suppress the Socialist party.","zh":"Bismarck 試圖壓制社會黨。"},{"en":"To suppress the Socialist party means to restrict, weaken, or silence that political party.","zh":"suppress the Socialist party 指限制、削弱或使該政黨沉默。"},{"en":"A government may suppress a party by banning meetings and controlling its newspapers.","zh":"政府可能透過禁止會議和控制其報章來壓制政黨。"},{"en":"Suppression can sometimes make supporters more determined rather than less active.","zh":"壓制有時會令支持者更堅定，而不是更不活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes political pressure against an opposition group.","zh":"這個短語描述針對反對群體的政治壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"abolish the parliament","meaning":"廢除議會","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether Bismarck abolished the parliament.","zh":"該選項問 Bismarck 是否廢除議會。"},{"en":"To abolish the parliament means to formally end or remove the legislative body.","zh":"abolish the parliament 指正式終止或移除立法機構。"},{"en":"A dictator may abolish the parliament to rule without elected representatives.","zh":"獨裁者可能廢除議會，以在沒有民選代表下統治。"},{"en":"Abolishing parliament removes an important check on executive power.","zh":"廢除議會會移除對行政權力的重要制衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ending a political institution.","zh":"這個短語描述終止一個政治機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"enact laws to weaken","meaning":"頒布法律以削弱……","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck enacted laws to weaken the Catholic Church.","zh":"Bismarck 頒布法律以削弱天主教會。"},{"en":"To enact laws to weaken something means to pass official rules designed to reduce its power.","zh":"enact laws to weaken something 指通過旨在減少其權力的正式規則。"},{"en":"A government may enact laws to weaken organised crime by cutting off illegal money flows.","zh":"政府可能頒布法律以透過切斷非法資金流來削弱有組織犯罪。"},{"en":"Laws can weaken an institution by limiting its rights, money, or public role.","zh":"法律可以透過限制權利、金錢或公共角色來削弱機構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using legal power to reduce influence.","zh":"這個短語描述使用法律權力來減少影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"make someone an ally","meaning":"使某人成為盟友","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck later made the church an ally.","zh":"Bismarck 後來使教會成為盟友。"},{"en":"To make someone an ally means to turn that person or group into a supporter or partner.","zh":"make someone an ally 指把某人或某群體變成支持者或合作伙伴。"},{"en":"A class leader may make a former critic an ally by listening to his concerns.","zh":"班長可能透過聆聽批評者的關注，使昔日批評者成為盟友。"},{"en":"Turning opponents into allies can strengthen a leader’s position.","zh":"把對手變成盟友可以強化領袖地位。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing a relationship from opposition to cooperation.","zh":"這個短語描述把關係由反對轉為合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"someone’s influence weakened","meaning":"某人的影響力被削弱","examples":[{"en":"The option says that Bismarck’s influence was severely weakened.","zh":"該選項說 Bismarck 的影響力被嚴重削弱。"},{"en":"Someone’s influence weakened means that person became less able to affect decisions or people.","zh":"someone’s influence weakened 指某人影響決定或他人的能力下降。"},{"en":"A coach’s influence may weaken if players stop trusting his judgement.","zh":"如果球員不再信任教練判斷，教練的影響力可能被削弱。"},{"en":"Influence weakens when support, authority, or credibility declines.","zh":"當支持、權威或公信力下降，影響力就會削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reduction in power over others.","zh":"這個短語描述對他人的權力減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"rise threefold","meaning":"增加三倍","examples":[{"en":"The Socialist party’s popularity had risen threefold by 1890.","zh":"到 1890 年，社會黨受歡迎程度已增加三倍。"},{"en":"To rise threefold means to increase to three times the original amount.","zh":"rise threefold 指增加至原來數量的三倍。"},{"en":"A club’s membership may rise threefold after it starts offering free workshops.","zh":"學會開始提供免費工作坊後，會員人數可能增加三倍。"},{"en":"A threefold rise can turn a small movement into a serious force.","zh":"三倍增長可以把小型運動變成重要力量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large numerical increase.","zh":"這個短語描述大幅數字增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"take power from","meaning":"從……手中奪權","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether the party took power from Bismarck.","zh":"該選項問該黨是否從 Bismarck 手中奪權。"},{"en":"To take power from someone means to remove their control and gain it oneself.","zh":"take power from someone 指移除某人的控制並由自己取得權力。"},{"en":"A board may take power from a manager if he repeatedly breaks company rules.","zh":"如果經理反覆違反公司規則，董事會可能從他手中奪權。"},{"en":"Taking power usually requires support, authority, or force.","zh":"奪權通常需要支持、權威或武力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a transfer of control.","zh":"這個短語描述控制權轉移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lose one’s influence","meaning":"失去影響力","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether the Socialist party lost its influence.","zh":"該選項問社會黨是否失去影響力。"},{"en":"To lose one’s influence means to become less able to affect people, decisions, or events.","zh":"lose one’s influence 指影響他人、決定或事件的能力下降。"},{"en":"A student leader may lose influence if classmates stop believing her promises.","zh":"如果同學不再相信學生領袖的承諾，她可能失去影響力。"},{"en":"Influence can be lost through failure, scandal, or changing public opinion.","zh":"影響力可以因失敗、醜聞或公眾意見改變而失去。"},{"en":"This phrase describes declining power to shape outcomes.","zh":"這個短語描述塑造結果的能力下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"after reuniting Germany","meaning":"在統一德國後","examples":[{"en":"After reuniting Germany, Bismarck focused on foreign policy.","zh":"在統一德國後，Bismarck 專注於外交政策。"},{"en":"After reuniting Germany means following the successful joining of Germany into one state.","zh":"after reuniting Germany 指在成功把德國結合成一個國家之後。"},{"en":"After completing a major school project, a student may focus on exam revision.","zh":"完成重大學校項目後，學生可能專注於考試溫習。"},{"en":"Completing one major goal often shifts attention to the next priority.","zh":"完成一個主要目標後，注意力常轉向下一個優先事項。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a completed achievement with later action.","zh":"這個短語把已完成成就與後續行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"wage war with","meaning":"與……開戰","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that Bismarck needed to wage war with threatening countries.","zh":"該選項暗示 Bismarck 需要與構成威脅的國家開戰。"},{"en":"To wage war with a country means to fight a war against it.","zh":"wage war with a country 指與某國進行戰爭。"},{"en":"Governments may wage war with enemies when diplomacy fails completely.","zh":"當外交完全失敗，政府可能與敵人開戰。"},{"en":"War can solve one problem while creating new human and political costs.","zh":"戰爭可以解決一個問題，同時造成新的人道和政治代價。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sustained armed conflict.","zh":"這個短語描述持續的武裝衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"pose a military threat","meaning":"構成軍事威脅","examples":[{"en":"Some countries posed a military threat to Germany.","zh":"有些國家對德國構成軍事威脅。"},{"en":"To pose a military threat means to create danger through possible armed attack or military pressure.","zh":"pose a military threat 指透過可能的武裝攻擊或軍事壓力造成危險。"},{"en":"A neighbouring state may pose a military threat if it moves troops to the border.","zh":"如果鄰國把軍隊調到邊境，可能構成軍事威脅。"},{"en":"Military threats can push countries to form alliances or increase defence spending.","zh":"軍事威脅可以促使國家結盟或增加國防開支。"},{"en":"This phrase describes danger from armed power.","zh":"這個短語描述來自武裝力量的危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"preserve the peace","meaning":"維持和平","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck believed that preserving the peace would benefit him.","zh":"Bismarck 相信維持和平會對他有利。"},{"en":"To preserve the peace means to keep a situation free from war or serious conflict.","zh":"preserve the peace 指使情況保持沒有戰爭或嚴重衝突。"},{"en":"A teacher may preserve the peace by separating two angry students before an argument grows.","zh":"老師可能在爭吵擴大前分開兩名憤怒學生，以維持和平。"},{"en":"Peace is preserved when tension is managed before it becomes open conflict.","zh":"當緊張在變成公開衝突前受到管理，和平就得以維持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes maintaining stability.","zh":"這個短語描述維持穩定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"form a powerful alliance","meaning":"結成強大同盟","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions forming a powerful alliance with France.","zh":"該選項提到與法國結成強大同盟。"},{"en":"To form a powerful alliance means to create a strong partnership for protection, influence, or shared goals.","zh":"form a powerful alliance 指建立強大的伙伴關係，以取得保護、影響力或共同目標。"},{"en":"Small shops may form a powerful alliance to negotiate cheaper rent together.","zh":"小店可能結成強大同盟，一起談判較低租金。"},{"en":"Powerful alliances can change the balance between competing groups.","zh":"強大同盟可以改變競爭群體之間的平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes building a strong cooperative relationship.","zh":"這個短語描述建立強大合作關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"leave a positive legacy","meaning":"留下正面遺產","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Bismarck left a positive legacy.","zh":"題目問 Bismarck 是否留下正面遺產。"},{"en":"To leave a positive legacy means to leave behind results that later people regard as beneficial.","zh":"leave a positive legacy 指留下後人視為有益的成果。"},{"en":"A principal leaves a positive legacy if students, teachers, and the community remain stronger after she leaves.","zh":"如果校長離任後學生、老師和社區都更強，她就留下正面遺產。"},{"en":"A legacy is judged over time because short-term success may create long-term problems.","zh":"遺產需要隨時間評價，因為短期成功可能造成長期問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the good effects remembered after someone’s rule or work.","zh":"這個短語描述某人統治或工作後被記住的良好影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be tolerant of","meaning":"對……寬容","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether Bismarck was tolerant of opposing views.","zh":"該選項問 Bismarck 是否對反對意見寬容。"},{"en":"To be tolerant of something means to allow or accept it even when one disagrees.","zh":"be tolerant of something 指即使不同意也容許或接受某事。"},{"en":"A teacher is tolerant of different opinions when she lets students debate respectfully.","zh":"當老師讓學生尊重地辯論，就是對不同意見寬容。"},{"en":"Tolerance can reduce conflict because people feel heard rather than silenced.","zh":"寬容可以減少衝突，因為人們感到被聽見，而不是被壓制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes openness toward difference or disagreement.","zh":"這個短語描述對差異或分歧的開放態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"different opinions","meaning":"不同意見","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to people who had different opinions.","zh":"該選項指有不同意見的人。"},{"en":"Different opinions are views that do not agree with one another.","zh":"different opinions 指彼此不同意的看法。"},{"en":"Students may have different opinions about whether school uniforms are useful.","zh":"學生對校服是否有用可能有不同意見。"},{"en":"Different opinions can improve discussion if people support them with reasons.","zh":"如果人們用理由支持不同意見，討論可以變得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disagreement or variety in viewpoints.","zh":"這個短語描述觀點上的分歧或多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"not actually","meaning":"實際上並非","examples":[{"en":"The article asks whether Bismarck was not actually a master of political juggling.","zh":"文章問 Bismarck 實際上是否並非政治斡旋高手。"},{"en":"Not actually means not really, despite what may appear to be true.","zh":"not actually 指實際上不是，儘管表面可能看似如此。"},{"en":"A student may look confident but not actually understand the topic.","zh":"學生可能看起來有信心，但實際上並不理解課題。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects an impression that may be misleading.","zh":"這個短語更正可能具誤導性的印象。"},{"en":"It signals doubt about a surface claim.","zh":"它表示對表面聲稱有所懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether the statements agree with the information in the passage.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與文章資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information means to match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"In a reading test, an answer agrees with the information only if the text clearly supports it.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，答案只有在文本清楚支持時才與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge if the passage gives different information.","zh":"如果文章給出不同資料，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE、FALSE、NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"FALSE 陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage states.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章所述相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says the meeting was in Berlin, an option saying it was in Paris contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說會議在柏林舉行，選項說在巴黎舉行，就是與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should choose FALSE only when the statement clearly conflicts with the text.","zh":"只有當陳述與文本清楚衝突，學生才應選 FALSE。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct disagreement with given information.","zh":"這個短語描述與所給資料直接相反。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Readers choose this option when there is no information on this point.","zh":"當這一點沒有相關資料時，讀者選擇這個選項。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not say enough to confirm or deny the statement.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有提供足夠資料去確認或否定陳述。"},{"en":"If a text describes a king’s policies but not his childhood, there is no information on his childhood habits.","zh":"如果文本描述國王政策但沒有描述童年，關於其童年習慣就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when the passage gives no information.","zh":"當文章沒有提供資料，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase explains when NOT GIVEN is the correct answer.","zh":"這個短語解釋何時 NOT GIVEN 是正確答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a great personal success","meaning":"個人重大成功","examples":[{"en":"The Congress of Berlin was a great personal success for Bismarck.","zh":"柏林會議對 Bismarck 來說是個人重大成功。"},{"en":"A great personal success is an achievement that strongly improves one individual’s reputation or position.","zh":"great personal success 指大大提升某個人聲譽或地位的成就。"},{"en":"Winning a public speaking competition can be a great personal success for a shy student.","zh":"贏得公開演說比賽，對害羞學生來說可以是個人重大成功。"},{"en":"Personal success may matter because it changes how others judge someone’s ability.","zh":"個人成功很重要，因為它改變他人如何評價某人的能力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on benefit to the individual.","zh":"這個短語著重對個人的好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"refuse to build alliances","meaning":"拒絕建立同盟","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Bismarck refused to build alliances.","zh":"該陳述問 Bismarck 是否拒絕建立同盟。"},{"en":"To refuse to build alliances means to choose not to form partnerships with others.","zh":"refuse to build alliances 指選擇不與他人建立伙伴關係。"},{"en":"A small club may struggle if it refuses to build alliances with teachers or other societies.","zh":"如果小型學會拒絕與老師或其他學會建立同盟，可能會很吃力。"},{"en":"Refusing alliances can leave a person or group isolated.","zh":"拒絕同盟可以令個人或群體被孤立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rejecting cooperation.","zh":"這個短語描述拒絕合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"consider one’s reign a failure","meaning":"認為自己的執政失敗","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Bismarck considered his reign a failure.","zh":"該陳述問 Bismarck 是否認為自己的執政失敗。"},{"en":"To consider one’s reign a failure means to judge one’s own period in power as unsuccessful.","zh":"consider one’s reign a failure 指判斷自己掌權時期不成功。"},{"en":"A principal may consider her leadership a failure if exam results improve but students feel unsafe.","zh":"如果考試成績改善但學生感到不安全，校長可能認為自己的領導失敗。"},{"en":"Leaders rarely admit failure unless the results clearly contradict their aims.","zh":"除非結果明顯違背目標，領袖很少承認失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes self-judgement about a period of rule.","zh":"這個短語描述對執政時期的自我判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct heading for each paragraph.","zh":"考生為每段選出正確標題。"},{"en":"To choose the correct heading means to select the title that best summarises the whole paragraph.","zh":"choose the correct heading 指選出最能概括整段的標題。"},{"en":"Students should find the main idea before choosing the correct heading.","zh":"學生應先找出主旨，再選出正確標題。"},{"en":"A heading is wrong if it matches only one small detail.","zh":"如果標題只符合一個小細節，它就是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in paragraph-matching reading tasks.","zh":"這個短語是段落配對閱讀題常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The list of headings contains possible paragraph summaries.","zh":"標題列表包含可能的段落摘要。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a set of possible titles used to match paragraphs.","zh":"list of headings 指用來配對段落的一組可能標題。"},{"en":"In IELTS reading, students compare each paragraph with the list of headings.","zh":"在 IELTS 閱讀中，學生把每段與標題列表比較。"},{"en":"Similar headings can confuse students if they read only keywords.","zh":"如果學生只看關鍵詞，相似標題可能令他們混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the answer choices in a heading task.","zh":"這個短語指標題題中的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"critical analysis","meaning":"批判性分析","examples":[{"en":"The final paragraph gives a critical analysis of Bismarck’s legacy.","zh":"最後一段對 Bismarck 的遺產作出批判性分析。"},{"en":"Critical analysis is careful judgement that examines strengths, weaknesses, causes, and consequences.","zh":"critical analysis 指仔細判斷優點、弱點、原因和後果。"},{"en":"A literature essay needs critical analysis, not just a summary of the story.","zh":"文學作文需要批判性分析，而不只是故事摘要。"},{"en":"Critical analysis helps readers see both achievement and damage.","zh":"批判性分析幫助讀者同時看見成就和傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes thoughtful evaluation rather than simple praise or blame.","zh":"這個短語描述深思熟慮的評價，而不是單純讚揚或責備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"early career and rise to power","meaning":"早期事業與掌權過程","examples":[{"en":"The first paragraph describes Bismarck’s early career and rise to power.","zh":"第一段描述 Bismarck 的早期事業與掌權過程。"},{"en":"Early career and rise to power means the beginning of someone’s working life and the process by which they gained authority.","zh":"early career and rise to power 指某人工作生涯開始及其取得權力的過程。"},{"en":"A biography may begin with a leader’s early career and rise to power.","zh":"傳記可能以領袖的早期事業與掌權過程開始。"},{"en":"Understanding early career helps explain later ambitions and methods.","zh":"理解早期事業有助解釋後來的抱負和方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first stage of a political life.","zh":"這個短語描述政治人生的最初階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"foreign policy","meaning":"外交政策","examples":[{"en":"One heading focuses on Bismarck’s foreign policy.","zh":"一個標題集中於 Bismarck 的外交政策。"},{"en":"Foreign policy is a state’s strategy for managing relations with other countries.","zh":"foreign policy 指國家管理與其他國家關係的策略。"},{"en":"A country may change foreign policy after a war, election, or economic crisis.","zh":"一個國家可能在戰爭、選舉或經濟危機後改變外交政策。"},{"en":"Foreign policy can involve alliances, trade, diplomacy, and military planning.","zh":"外交政策可以涉及同盟、貿易、外交和軍事規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a government’s international direction.","zh":"這個短語描述政府的國際方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"powerful friends","meaning":"有權勢的盟友","examples":[{"en":"The heading refers to Bismarck’s powerful friends and alliances.","zh":"該標題指 Bismarck 有權勢的盟友和同盟。"},{"en":"Powerful friends are influential allies who can offer support, protection, or advantage.","zh":"powerful friends 指能提供支持、保護或優勢的有影響力盟友。"},{"en":"A small business with powerful friends may get better advice and useful contacts.","zh":"有權勢盟友的小企業可能得到更好建議和有用人脈。"},{"en":"Powerful friends can strengthen a leader, but they may also expect something in return.","zh":"有權勢的盟友可以強化領袖，但也可能期待回報。"},{"en":"This phrase describes support from people or states with influence.","zh":"這個短語描述來自有影響力人士或國家的支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"separating church and state","meaning":"政教分離","examples":[{"en":"The heading refers to conflict between political power and church influence.","zh":"該標題指政治權力與教會影響之間的衝突。"},{"en":"Separating church and state means keeping religious institutions and government authority apart.","zh":"separating church and state 指把宗教機構與政府權威分開。"},{"en":"A country separates church and state when religious leaders do not control public laws.","zh":"當宗教領袖不控制公共法律，一個國家就是政教分離。"},{"en":"This separation can reduce conflict when citizens follow different religions.","zh":"當公民信奉不同宗教，這種分離可以減少衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the boundary between religion and government.","zh":"這個短語描述宗教與政府之間的界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"socialist threat","meaning":"社會主義威脅","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck viewed the Social Democratic Party as a socialist threat.","zh":"Bismarck 把社會民主黨視為社會主義威脅。"},{"en":"A socialist threat is a danger that leaders believe comes from socialist ideas or movements.","zh":"socialist threat 指領袖認為來自社會主義思想或運動的危險。"},{"en":"A government may see organised workers as a socialist threat if they demand major political change.","zh":"如果有組織工人要求重大政治改變，政府可能視他們為社會主義威脅。"},{"en":"Calling a group a threat can justify restrictions against it.","zh":"把群體稱為威脅，可以合理化對它的限制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a perceived political danger.","zh":"這個短語描述被感知的政治危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"political decline","meaning":"政治衰落","examples":[{"en":"The heading suggests a decline in political power.","zh":"該標題暗示政治權力衰落。"},{"en":"Political decline means a reduction in political influence, control, or success.","zh":"political decline 指政治影響力、控制力或成功下降。"},{"en":"A party may enter political decline after losing several elections.","zh":"政黨在連續輸掉幾次選舉後，可能進入政治衰落。"},{"en":"Political decline can happen slowly as supporters move away.","zh":"當支持者逐漸離開，政治衰落可以慢慢發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weakening political strength.","zh":"這個短語描述政治力量削弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"creating a virtual dictatorship","meaning":"建立實質上的獨裁統治","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck’s constitution helped him create a virtual dictatorship.","zh":"Bismarck 的憲法幫助他建立實質上的獨裁統治。"},{"en":"Creating a virtual dictatorship means building a system that looks partly democratic but gives one person almost complete control.","zh":"creating a virtual dictatorship 指建立一個看似部分民主，但讓一人幾乎完全控制的制度。"},{"en":"A club creates a virtual dictatorship if elections exist but one leader controls every decision.","zh":"如果學會有選舉但所有決定都由一名領袖控制，就是建立實質上的獨裁統治。"},{"en":"Such systems can hide concentrated power behind formal procedures.","zh":"這類制度可以把集中權力隱藏在正式程序背後。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical dictatorship under a softer appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述較柔和外表下的實際獨裁。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a change of mind","meaning":"改變主意","examples":[{"en":"Bismarck’s political U-turn showed a change of mind.","zh":"Bismarck 的政治轉軚顯示他改變主意。"},{"en":"A change of mind means a decision to think differently from before.","zh":"change of mind 指決定以不同於以前的方式思考。"},{"en":"A student may have a change of mind after hearing stronger evidence from a classmate.","zh":"學生聽到同學更有力的證據後，可能改變主意。"},{"en":"A change of mind can happen when the original plan fails or new facts appear.","zh":"當原本計劃失敗或新事實出現，人們可能改變主意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift in opinion or decision.","zh":"這個短語描述意見或決定的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 85 - Bismarck - A Master of Political and Diplomatic Juggling?.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 86":[{"front":"making a sound investment decision","meaning":"作出明智的投資決定","examples":[{"en":"The passage gives advice on making a sound investment decision.","zh":"文章就作出明智的投資決定提供建議。"},{"en":"Making a sound investment decision means choosing where to put money after careful research and realistic thinking.","zh":"making a sound investment decision 指經過仔細研究和務實思考後，選擇把錢投放在哪裏。"},{"en":"A family makes a sound investment decision when they compare prices, risks, and future income before buying a flat.","zh":"一個家庭在買樓前比較價格、風險和未來收入，就是作出明智的投資決定。"},{"en":"Careful planning can lead to a sound investment decision, while emotional buying can lead to losses.","zh":"仔細規劃可以帶來明智的投資決定，而情緒化購買可能導致損失。"},{"en":"A sound investment decision is based on evidence, not excitement.","zh":"明智的投資決定建基於證據，而不是興奮情緒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sound investment decision","meaning":"明智的投資決定","examples":[{"en":"A sound investment decision should be based on careful research.","zh":"明智的投資決定應建基於仔細研究。"},{"en":"A sound investment decision is a wise and well-judged choice about where to invest money.","zh":"sound investment decision 指關於投資金錢去向的明智而判斷良好的選擇。"},{"en":"Buying a small shop after checking rent, location, and repair costs can be a sound investment decision.","zh":"在檢查租金、地點和維修成本後買入小商舖，可以是明智的投資決定。"},{"en":"A sound investment decision can protect people from overpaying or borrowing too much.","zh":"明智的投資決定可以保護人避免支付過高價格或借貸過多。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests good judgement, not just luck.","zh":"這個短語暗示良好判斷，而不只是運氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"investors","meaning":"投資者","examples":[{"en":"Many investors are looking for alternatives to the stock market.","zh":"許多投資者正在尋找股市以外的選擇。"},{"en":"Investors are people or organisations that put money into something to make a profit.","zh":"investors 指把錢投放到某事物中，希望賺取利潤的人或機構。"},{"en":"A teacher may become an investor by buying a small flat to rent out.","zh":"老師買入小單位出租，也可以成為投資者。"},{"en":"Investors can lose money if they ignore risk and follow trends blindly.","zh":"如果投資者忽視風險並盲目跟風，可能會虧錢。"},{"en":"The word describes people who use money with the hope of future return.","zh":"這個詞描述希望未來獲得回報而使用金錢的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tire of","meaning":"對……感到厭倦","examples":[{"en":"Investors may tire of stock market instability.","zh":"投資者可能對股市不穩定感到厭倦。"},{"en":"To tire of something means to become bored, annoyed, or exhausted by it over time.","zh":"tire of something 指隨時間對某事感到厭煩、惱怒或疲累。"},{"en":"Students may tire of repeated grammar drills if every exercise looks the same.","zh":"如果每個練習都一樣，學生可能對反覆文法操練感到厭倦。"},{"en":"When people tire of uncertainty, they often look for safer or more stable choices.","zh":"當人們厭倦不確定性，他們通常會尋找較安全或穩定的選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests gradual loss of patience or interest.","zh":"這個短語暗示耐性或興趣逐漸消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"stock market instability","meaning":"股市不穩定","examples":[{"en":"Some investors are tired of stock market instability.","zh":"有些投資者厭倦股市不穩定。"},{"en":"Stock market instability means frequent and unpredictable changes in share prices.","zh":"stock market instability 指股票價格頻繁而難以預測地變動。"},{"en":"A worker saving for retirement may worry about stock market instability when prices rise and fall sharply.","zh":"為退休儲蓄的工人，在股價大升大跌時可能擔心股市不穩定。"},{"en":"Instability can make investors seek property, bonds, or savings accounts instead.","zh":"不穩定可能令投資者轉而尋找物業、債券或儲蓄戶口。"},{"en":"The phrase describes uncertainty in the share market.","zh":"這個短語描述股票市場中的不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the idea of","meaning":"……這個想法","examples":[{"en":"The idea of owning property is gaining in popularity.","zh":"擁有物業這個想法越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"The idea of something means the thought, plan, or possibility of doing it.","zh":"the idea of something 指做某事的想法、計劃或可能性。"},{"en":"The idea of studying abroad may excite a student who wants independence.","zh":"對想獨立的學生來說，出國讀書這個想法可能令人興奮。"},{"en":"When the idea of an activity becomes attractive, more people begin considering it seriously.","zh":"當某活動的想法變得吸引，更多人會開始認真考慮。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a concept rather than the action itself.","zh":"這個短語引入一個概念，而不是行動本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"owning a piece of real estate","meaning":"擁有一項房地產","examples":[{"en":"Owning a piece of real estate is becoming more popular.","zh":"擁有一項房地產正變得越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"Owning a piece of real estate means possessing land, a flat, a house, or another property.","zh":"owning a piece of real estate 指擁有土地、單位、房屋或其他物業。"},{"en":"A young couple may dream of owning a piece of real estate instead of renting forever.","zh":"年輕夫婦可能夢想擁有一項房地產，而不是永遠租屋。"},{"en":"Owning property can create rental income, but it also brings costs and responsibilities.","zh":"擁有物業可以創造租金收入，但也帶來成本和責任。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to property ownership in a practical investment sense.","zh":"這個短語指實際投資意義上的物業擁有權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"real estate","meaning":"房地產","examples":[{"en":"Real estate can become a good source of income.","zh":"房地產可以成為良好收入來源。"},{"en":"Real estate means land, houses, flats, shops, offices, and other property.","zh":"real estate 指土地、房屋、單位、商舖、辦公室和其他物業。"},{"en":"A family may buy real estate to live in, rent out, or sell later at a higher price.","zh":"家庭可能買入房地產作自住、出租，或日後以更高價格出售。"},{"en":"Real estate can produce income through rent, but it can also lose value.","zh":"房地產可以透過租金產生收入，但也可能貶值。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to property, not movable items like cars or furniture.","zh":"這個短語指物業，而不是汽車或家具等可移動物品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"gaining in popularity","meaning":"越來越受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The idea of investing in real estate is gaining in popularity.","zh":"投資房地產這個想法越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"Gaining in popularity means becoming more liked, accepted, or common over time.","zh":"gaining in popularity 指隨時間變得更受喜愛、更被接受或更常見。"},{"en":"Online English lessons are gaining in popularity because students can study at home.","zh":"網上英文課因學生可以在家學習而越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"A trend gains in popularity when more people see benefits in it.","zh":"當更多人看見某趨勢的好處，它就會越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growing public interest.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾興趣增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have what it takes to","meaning":"具備……所需條件","examples":[{"en":"Not everyone has what it takes to become a landlord.","zh":"不是每個人都具備成為業主所需條件。"},{"en":"To have what it takes to do something means to have the qualities, skills, money, or patience needed to succeed.","zh":"have what it takes to do something 指具備成功完成某事所需的素質、技能、金錢或耐性。"},{"en":"A student has what it takes to pass an exam if she studies steadily and handles pressure well.","zh":"如果學生穩定溫習並能承受壓力，她就具備通過考試所需條件。"},{"en":"Property investment requires discipline, so people without patience may not have what it takes.","zh":"物業投資需要紀律，所以沒有耐性的人可能不具備所需條件。"},{"en":"The phrase asks whether someone is truly suitable for a difficult role.","zh":"這個短語是在問某人是否真正適合困難角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"become a landlord","meaning":"成為業主","examples":[{"en":"Not everyone has what it takes to become a landlord.","zh":"不是每個人都具備成為業主所需條件。"},{"en":"To become a landlord means to own property and rent it to tenants.","zh":"become a landlord 指擁有物業並把它出租給租客。"},{"en":"A retiree may become a landlord by renting out a spare flat for monthly income.","zh":"退休人士可能透過出租空置單位取得月入而成為業主。"},{"en":"Becoming a landlord brings income, but it also means handling repairs, tenants, and legal duties.","zh":"成為業主帶來收入，但也意味要處理維修、租客和法律責任。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving from property owner to rental-property manager.","zh":"這個短語描述由物業持有人轉為出租物業管理者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"make a go of it","meaning":"成功做好某事","examples":[{"en":"Property investment can be profitable if you can make a go of it.","zh":"如果你能成功做好，物業投資可以有利可圖。"},{"en":"To make a go of it means to succeed in something after effort, planning, and persistence.","zh":"make a go of it 指經過努力、規劃和堅持後成功做好某事。"},{"en":"A small café can make a go of it if it controls costs and keeps regular customers happy.","zh":"如果小咖啡店控制成本並令常客滿意，它可以成功經營下去。"},{"en":"Investors make a go of property when rental income covers costs and leaves profit.","zh":"當租金收入覆蓋成本並留下利潤，投資者就是成功做好物業投資。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests practical success, not just trying.","zh":"這個短語暗示實際成功，而不只是嘗試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"has the potential to","meaning":"有潛力去……","examples":[{"en":"Real estate has the potential to become a good money-earner.","zh":"房地產有潛力成為賺錢的好方法。"},{"en":"Has the potential to means may be able to become something in the future.","zh":"has the potential to 指未來可能能夠成為某事物。"},{"en":"A quiet student has the potential to become a strong speaker with enough practice.","zh":"安靜學生若有足夠練習，有潛力成為出色講者。"},{"en":"A property has the potential to earn money if the location, rent, and costs are favourable.","zh":"如果地點、租金和成本有利，物業就有潛力賺錢。"},{"en":"The phrase shows possibility, not guaranteed success.","zh":"這個短語顯示可能性，而不是保證成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"good money-earner","meaning":"賺錢的好方法；有利可圖的東西","examples":[{"en":"A rental property can become a good money-earner.","zh":"出租物業可以成為賺錢的好方法。"},{"en":"A good money-earner is something that regularly brings in useful income or profit.","zh":"good money-earner 指能定期帶來有用收入或利潤的事物。"},{"en":"A weekend tutoring class can be a good money-earner if many students enrol.","zh":"如果很多學生報讀，週末補習班可以是賺錢的好方法。"},{"en":"A property becomes a good money-earner when rent is higher than mortgage and maintenance costs.","zh":"當租金高於按揭和維修成本，物業就成為有利可圖的東西。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something profitable, not merely expensive.","zh":"這個短語描述能賺錢的事物，而不只是昂貴的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"successful real-estate mogul","meaning":"成功的房地產大亨","examples":[{"en":"Janet Anderson is described as a successful real-estate mogul.","zh":"Janet Anderson 被形容為成功的房地產大亨。"},{"en":"A successful real-estate mogul is a wealthy and influential person who has made money through property.","zh":"successful real-estate mogul 指透過物業賺錢並有財富和影響力的人。"},{"en":"A businesswoman who owns many rental buildings may be called a real-estate mogul.","zh":"擁有多幢出租大廈的女商人可能被稱為房地產大亨。"},{"en":"Successful real-estate moguls usually understand prices, locations, timing, and risk.","zh":"成功的房地產大亨通常理解價格、地點、時機和風險。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests power and success in the property business.","zh":"這個短語暗示在房地產生意中的權力和成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"start building up","meaning":"開始逐步建立","examples":[{"en":"Investors can start building up their property portfolio.","zh":"投資者可以開始逐步建立他們的物業投資組合。"},{"en":"To start building up something means to begin developing or increasing it gradually.","zh":"start building up something 指開始逐漸發展或增加某事物。"},{"en":"A student can start building up vocabulary by learning five useful phrases each day.","zh":"學生可以每天學五個實用短語，開始逐步建立詞彙量。"},{"en":"Investors build up a portfolio slowly because buying too much too soon can be risky.","zh":"投資者慢慢建立投資組合，因為太快買太多可能有風險。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests gradual growth over time.","zh":"這個短語暗示隨時間逐步增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"property portfolio","meaning":"物業投資組合","examples":[{"en":"Janet gives tips on how to build up a property portfolio.","zh":"Janet 提供如何建立物業投資組合的建議。"},{"en":"A property portfolio is a collection of properties owned by one person or company as investments.","zh":"property portfolio 指由一個人或公司作投資用途持有的一組物業。"},{"en":"A landlord with two flats and one small shop has a property portfolio.","zh":"擁有兩個單位和一間小商舖的業主有一個物業投資組合。"},{"en":"A larger portfolio can spread risk, but it also creates more management work.","zh":"較大的投資組合可以分散風險，但也創造更多管理工作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to multiple property investments held together.","zh":"這個短語指一併持有的多項物業投資。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"According to Janet, foreclosures can be good bargains.","zh":"根據 Janet 所說，銀主盤可以是划算交易。"},{"en":"According to someone means based on what that person says or believes.","zh":"according to someone 指根據某人所說或所相信的內容。"},{"en":"According to the teacher, students should read the question before reading the options.","zh":"根據老師所說，學生應先讀題目再讀選項。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the source of information or opinion.","zh":"這個短語顯示資訊或觀點的來源。"},{"en":"It does not prove the statement is true; it tells us who said it.","zh":"它不證明該說法真實；它告訴我們是誰說的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"identify a bargain","meaning":"找出便宜貨；找出划算交易","examples":[{"en":"One way to identify a bargain is to look for foreclosures.","zh":"找出划算交易的一個方法是尋找銀主盤。"},{"en":"To identify a bargain means to recognise something that is worth more than its price.","zh":"identify a bargain 指辨認出價值高於價格的東西。"},{"en":"A shopper identifies a bargain when she finds a good winter coat at half price.","zh":"購物者以半價找到一件好冬天外套，就是找出便宜貨。"},{"en":"Careful comparison helps investors identify bargains instead of overpaying.","zh":"仔細比較幫助投資者找出划算交易，而不是支付過高價格。"},{"en":"The phrase means spotting real value, not simply buying something cheap.","zh":"這個短語指看出真正價值，而不只是買便宜東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hunt for","meaning":"搜尋；尋找","examples":[{"en":"Investors can hunt for foreclosures to find bargains.","zh":"投資者可以搜尋銀主盤以找出划算交易。"},{"en":"To hunt for something means to search carefully and actively for it.","zh":"hunt for something 指仔細而主動地尋找某物。"},{"en":"Students may hunt for useful examples in newspapers before writing an essay.","zh":"學生寫作文前可能在報紙中尋找有用例子。"},{"en":"Investors hunt for bargains because good deals are not always easy to find.","zh":"投資者尋找划算交易，因為好交易不一定容易找到。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests active searching, not waiting passively.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動搜尋，而不是被動等待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"foreclosures","meaning":"被銀行收回的物業；銀主盤","examples":[{"en":"Foreclosures are properties repossessed by banks.","zh":"銀主盤是被銀行收回的物業。"},{"en":"Foreclosures are homes or properties taken back by lenders because owners failed to keep up payments.","zh":"foreclosures 指因業主未能持續供款而被貸款機構收回的住宅或物業。"},{"en":"An investor may buy foreclosures at auction if banks want to sell them quickly.","zh":"如果銀行想快速出售，投資者可能在拍賣中買入銀主盤。"},{"en":"Foreclosures can be cheaper, but buyers must still check the condition and legal risks.","zh":"銀主盤可能較便宜，但買家仍須檢查狀況和法律風險。"},{"en":"The word refers to property taken back after mortgage problems.","zh":"這個詞指因按揭問題而被收回的物業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"properties","meaning":"物業","examples":[{"en":"Foreclosures are properties that banks have repossessed.","zh":"銀主盤是銀行已收回的物業。"},{"en":"Properties are pieces of land, houses, flats, shops, or buildings that can be owned.","zh":"properties 指可被擁有的土地、房屋、單位、商舖或建築物。"},{"en":"A landlord may own several properties and rent them to different tenants.","zh":"業主可能擁有幾項物業，並出租給不同租客。"},{"en":"Properties can rise or fall in value depending on location, demand, and maintenance.","zh":"物業價值可以因地點、需求和保養而上升或下降。"},{"en":"The word refers to real-estate assets.","zh":"這個詞指房地產資產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"repossessed","meaning":"被收回；被取回","examples":[{"en":"The bank repossessed the property after the owner missed payments.","zh":"業主錯過供款後，銀行收回該物業。"},{"en":"Repossessed means taken back by a lender because the borrower failed to pay what was owed.","zh":"repossessed 指貸款人因借款人未能償還欠款而取回資產。"},{"en":"A car can be repossessed if the buyer stops making loan payments.","zh":"如果買家停止償還車貸，汽車可能被收回。"},{"en":"When a property is repossessed, the lender may sell it to recover money.","zh":"當物業被收回，貸款人可能出售它以取回款項。"},{"en":"The word describes legal recovery of an asset after non-payment.","zh":"這個詞描述因未付款而合法收回資產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"unable to","meaning":"無法……","examples":[{"en":"The owners were unable to meet the mortgage repayments.","zh":"業主無法支付按揭供款。"},{"en":"Unable to do something means not able to do it because of a problem or limitation.","zh":"unable to do something 指因問題或限制而不能做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be unable to attend class if she is ill.","zh":"學生若生病，可能無法上課。"},{"en":"Owners who are unable to pay their mortgage may risk losing the property.","zh":"無法償還按揭的業主可能面臨失去物業的風險。"},{"en":"The phrase shows lack of ability, not lack of desire only.","zh":"這個短語顯示缺乏能力，而不只是缺乏意願。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"meet the mortgage repayments","meaning":"支付按揭供款","examples":[{"en":"Some owners are unable to meet the mortgage repayments.","zh":"有些業主無法支付按揭供款。"},{"en":"To meet the mortgage repayments means to pay the required mortgage instalments on time.","zh":"meet the mortgage repayments 指準時支付所需的按揭分期供款。"},{"en":"A family may struggle to meet the mortgage repayments if one parent loses a job.","zh":"如果其中一名家長失業，家庭可能難以支付按揭供款。"},{"en":"Failure to meet repayments can lead to penalties, stress, or repossession.","zh":"未能支付供款可能導致罰款、壓力或物業被收回。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to keeping up with home-loan payments.","zh":"這個短語指持續償還房屋貸款。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mortgage repayments","meaning":"按揭供款","examples":[{"en":"Failure to make mortgage repayments can lead to repossession.","zh":"未能作出按揭供款可能導致物業被收回。"},{"en":"Mortgage repayments are regular payments made to repay a loan used to buy property.","zh":"mortgage repayments 指為償還購買物業貸款而定期支付的款項。"},{"en":"A homeowner may pay mortgage repayments every month for twenty years.","zh":"業主可能每月支付按揭供款，持續二十年。"},{"en":"If repayments are too high, the owner may have little money left for repairs or savings.","zh":"如果供款太高，業主可能很少錢剩下作維修或儲蓄。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to scheduled home-loan payments.","zh":"這個短語指預定的房屋貸款還款。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"quick sale","meaning":"快速出售","examples":[{"en":"Banks often want a quick sale on foreclosed properties.","zh":"銀行通常希望快速出售銀主盤。"},{"en":"A quick sale is a sale completed fast, often because the seller wants money back quickly.","zh":"quick sale 指快速完成的出售，通常因賣方想盡快取回金錢。"},{"en":"A shop may offer a discount for a quick sale before closing down.","zh":"商店結業前可能為快速出售而提供折扣。"},{"en":"A quick sale can lower the price because speed matters more than maximum profit.","zh":"快速出售可能降低價格，因為速度比最大利潤更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights urgency in selling.","zh":"這個短語突出出售時的急切性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cut their losses","meaning":"止蝕；減少損失","examples":[{"en":"Banks want to cut their losses and recover their money.","zh":"銀行想止蝕並取回款項。"},{"en":"To cut one’s losses means to accept a smaller loss now to avoid a bigger loss later.","zh":"cut one’s losses 指現在接受較小損失，以避免日後更大損失。"},{"en":"A student may cut her losses by dropping one weak elective and focusing on stronger subjects.","zh":"學生可能放棄一科弱選修科，集中較強科目，以減少損失。"},{"en":"Banks sell repossessed property quickly because waiting may create more costs and risk.","zh":"銀行快速出售被收回物業，因為等待可能產生更多成本和風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limiting damage before it gets worse.","zh":"這個短語描述在情況惡化前限制損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get their money back","meaning":"取回本金","examples":[{"en":"Banks want to get their money back as quickly as possible.","zh":"銀行想盡快取回本金。"},{"en":"To get their money back means to recover money that was lent, spent, or invested.","zh":"get their money back 指取回已借出、花費或投資的金錢。"},{"en":"A customer may ask to get her money back if a product is broken.","zh":"如果產品損壞，顧客可能要求退款。"},{"en":"Lenders sell repossessed assets so they can recover at least part of the loan.","zh":"貸款機構出售被收回資產，以便至少取回部分貸款。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on recovering funds.","zh":"這個短語重點是收回資金。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as quickly as possible","meaning":"盡快","examples":[{"en":"Banks try to sell repossessed properties as quickly as possible.","zh":"銀行嘗試盡快出售被收回物業。"},{"en":"As quickly as possible means with the least possible delay.","zh":"as quickly as possible 指以最少可能延誤完成。"},{"en":"A school may send typhoon updates as quickly as possible so parents can plan safely.","zh":"學校可能盡快發出颱風更新，讓家長安全安排。"},{"en":"Acting quickly can reduce losses when holding an asset costs money.","zh":"當持有資產會產生成本，迅速行動可以減少損失。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses speed and urgency.","zh":"這個短語強調速度和急切性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"developing a network","meaning":"建立人脈網絡","examples":[{"en":"Developing a network can help investors identify bargains.","zh":"建立人脈網絡可以幫助投資者找出划算交易。"},{"en":"Developing a network means building useful relationships with people who can share information or support.","zh":"developing a network 指與能分享資訊或支援的人建立有用關係。"},{"en":"A job seeker develops a network by meeting classmates, teachers, and former colleagues.","zh":"求職者透過認識同學、老師和前同事來建立人脈網絡。"},{"en":"A good network can reveal opportunities before they become widely known.","zh":"良好人脈網絡可以在機會廣為人知前揭示它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes relationship-building for practical advantage.","zh":"這個短語描述為實際好處而建立關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"making connections with","meaning":"與……建立聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Investors can make connections with city clerks and bank employees.","zh":"投資者可以與市政文員和銀行職員建立聯繫。"},{"en":"Making connections with people means building relationships with them, often for future information or help.","zh":"making connections with people 指與人建立關係，通常為了日後資訊或幫助。"},{"en":"A student makes connections with alumni by attending a careers talk.","zh":"學生透過參加就業講座與校友建立聯繫。"},{"en":"Good connections can help people hear about opportunities earlier.","zh":"良好聯繫可以幫助人更早聽到機會。"},{"en":"The phrase means forming useful social or professional links.","zh":"這個短語指建立有用的社交或專業連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"city clerks","meaning":"市政文員","examples":[{"en":"City clerks may know which properties are about to be sold.","zh":"市政文員可能知道哪些物業即將出售。"},{"en":"City clerks are local government office workers who handle records, forms, and administrative information.","zh":"city clerks 指處理紀錄、表格和行政資訊的地方政府辦公室職員。"},{"en":"A city clerk may help residents file property documents or check public records.","zh":"市政文員可能幫居民提交物業文件或查核公共紀錄。"},{"en":"Clerks can be useful contacts because they may know official procedures and upcoming sales.","zh":"文員可以是有用聯絡人，因為他們可能知道官方程序和即將出售的物業。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to municipal administrative staff.","zh":"這個短語指市政行政人員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"bank employees","meaning":"銀行職員","examples":[{"en":"Bank employees may know about upcoming property sales.","zh":"銀行職員可能知道即將舉行的物業出售。"},{"en":"Bank employees are people who work for banks and handle loans, accounts, payments, or customer service.","zh":"bank employees 指在銀行工作並處理貸款、戶口、付款或客戶服務的人。"},{"en":"A bank employee may explain mortgage terms to a first-time buyer.","zh":"銀行職員可能向首次置業者解釋按揭條款。"},{"en":"Bank staff may hear about repossessed properties before they are widely advertised.","zh":"銀行職員可能在被收回物業廣泛刊登前已聽聞消息。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to workers inside a bank.","zh":"這個短語指銀行內工作的員工。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"about to be sold","meaning":"即將被出售","examples":[{"en":"Some repossessed properties are about to be sold.","zh":"一些被收回物業即將被出售。"},{"en":"About to be sold means going to be sold very soon.","zh":"about to be sold 指很快將會出售。"},{"en":"A used textbook marked with a low price may be about to be sold to the first student who pays.","zh":"標上低價的二手課本，可能即將售予第一個付款的學生。"},{"en":"Investors who hear early that a property is about to be sold may prepare a bid quickly.","zh":"投資者若早知某物業即將被出售，可能迅速準備出價。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that is close to happening.","zh":"這個短語描述某事接近發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"an excellent way to","meaning":"……的極佳方法","examples":[{"en":"Networking can be an excellent way to identify bargains.","zh":"建立人脈可以是找出划算交易的極佳方法。"},{"en":"An excellent way to do something means a very effective method for achieving it.","zh":"an excellent way to do something 指達成某事的非常有效方法。"},{"en":"Reading model essays is an excellent way to learn useful sentence patterns.","zh":"閱讀範文是學習有用句式的極佳方法。"},{"en":"A method becomes excellent when it works reliably and saves time or effort.","zh":"當方法可靠有效並節省時間或力氣，它就變得極佳。"},{"en":"The phrase recommends a strong practical approach.","zh":"這個短語推薦一種強而實用的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"prove to be","meaning":"證明是……","examples":[{"en":"Foreclosures can prove to be real bargains.","zh":"銀主盤可以證明是真正划算交易。"},{"en":"To prove to be something means to turn out to be that thing after experience or evidence.","zh":"prove to be something 指經過經驗或證據後結果證明是某事物。"},{"en":"A difficult teacher may prove to be very helpful once students understand her method.","zh":"嚴格老師在學生理解其方法後，可能證明是非常有幫助。"},{"en":"A property proves to be a bargain if it later produces strong rental income.","zh":"如果物業日後產生強勁租金收入，它就證明是划算交易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a result becoming clear over time.","zh":"這個短語描述結果隨時間變得清楚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"recent fire-sale auction","meaning":"最近一次賤價拍賣","examples":[{"en":"A recent fire-sale auction included a heavily discounted house.","zh":"最近一次賤價拍賣包括一間大幅折扣的房子。"},{"en":"A recent fire-sale auction is a recent event where assets were sold quickly and cheaply.","zh":"recent fire-sale auction 指最近一次快速而廉價出售資產的活動。"},{"en":"A company closing down may hold a fire-sale auction to sell furniture and computers fast.","zh":"結業公司可能舉行賤價拍賣，快速出售家具和電腦。"},{"en":"Fire-sale auctions can attract buyers because prices are often below normal market levels.","zh":"賤價拍賣可以吸引買家，因為價格通常低於正常市場水平。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights both timing and urgency.","zh":"這個短語同時突出時間和急切性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fire-sale auction","meaning":"賤價拍賣","examples":[{"en":"A fire-sale auction is used to dispose of repossessed assets quickly.","zh":"賤價拍賣用來快速處置被收回資產。"},{"en":"A fire-sale auction is an auction where items are sold cheaply and urgently, often because the seller wants quick cash.","zh":"fire-sale auction 指物品被廉價而急切拍賣的活動，通常因賣方想快速套現。"},{"en":"A landlord may attend a fire-sale auction to find discounted office furniture.","zh":"業主可能參加賤價拍賣，以尋找折扣辦公室家具。"},{"en":"Because speed matters, fire-sale auctions can produce unusually low prices.","zh":"因為速度重要，賤價拍賣可以產生異常低價。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests urgent selling at bargain prices.","zh":"這個短語暗示以便宜價格急售。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the phrase that has been coined","meaning":"被創造出來的說法","examples":[{"en":"The phrase “fire-sale auction” has been coined to describe these events.","zh":"“fire-sale auction” 這個說法被創造出來形容這些活動。"},{"en":"A phrase that has been coined is a newly created expression used to name an idea or situation.","zh":"phrase that has been coined 指新創造出來、用來命名某想法或情況的表達。"},{"en":"Teachers may coin a phrase to help students remember a common grammar mistake.","zh":"老師可能創造一個說法來幫學生記住常見文法錯誤。"},{"en":"New phrases are coined when people need a short way to describe a repeated pattern.","zh":"當人們需要簡短方式描述反覆出現的模式，新短語就會被創造出來。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on language being created for a specific use.","zh":"這個短語重點是語言為特定用途而被創造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"coined to describe","meaning":"被創造出來形容……","examples":[{"en":"The phrase was coined to describe auctions of repossessed assets.","zh":"這個短語被創造出來形容被收回資產的拍賣。"},{"en":"Coined to describe means newly invented as a phrase for explaining or naming something.","zh":"coined to describe 指作為解釋或命名某事的新短語而被創造。"},{"en":"The term “doomscrolling” was coined to describe endlessly reading bad news online.","zh":"“doomscrolling” 這個詞被創造出來形容不停在網上看壞消息。"},{"en":"A phrase is coined when an existing word is not precise enough for a new situation.","zh":"當現有詞語不足以準確描述新情況，短語就會被創造出來。"},{"en":"The phrase shows why a new expression was created.","zh":"這個短語顯示新表達被創造的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"auction-room events","meaning":"拍賣場活動","examples":[{"en":"Fire-sale auctions are auction-room events for repossessed assets.","zh":"賤價拍賣是為被收回資產而設的拍賣場活動。"},{"en":"Auction-room events are organised sales where people bid for items in an auction setting.","zh":"auction-room events 指人們在拍賣環境中競投物品的有組織銷售活動。"},{"en":"A charity may hold an auction-room event where guests bid for paintings and donated gifts.","zh":"慈善機構可能舉辦拍賣場活動，讓賓客競投畫作和捐贈禮品。"},{"en":"Competitive bidding can raise prices, but urgent selling can keep them low.","zh":"競爭性出價可以推高價格，但急售可以令價格保持低。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to formal events where goods are sold by bidding.","zh":"這個短語指透過出價出售貨品的正式活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dedicated entirely to","meaning":"完全專門用於……","examples":[{"en":"The auction was dedicated entirely to the disposal of repossessed assets.","zh":"該拍賣完全專門用於處置被收回資產。"},{"en":"Dedicated entirely to something means used only for that purpose.","zh":"dedicated entirely to something 指只用於某個目的。"},{"en":"A study room dedicated entirely to silent reading should not be used for group discussion.","zh":"完全專門用於安靜閱讀的自修室，不應用作小組討論。"},{"en":"When an event is dedicated entirely to one purpose, all its activities support that aim.","zh":"當活動完全專門用於一個目的，所有活動都支持該目標。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses complete focus.","zh":"這個短語強調完全集中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"disposal of repossessed assets","meaning":"處置被收回資產","examples":[{"en":"The auction was held for the disposal of repossessed assets.","zh":"該拍賣是為處置被收回資產而舉行。"},{"en":"Disposal of repossessed assets means selling or getting rid of assets taken back by a lender.","zh":"disposal of repossessed assets 指出售或處理被貸款人收回的資產。"},{"en":"A bank may arrange disposal of repossessed assets after borrowers stop paying loans.","zh":"借款人停止還款後，銀行可能安排處置被收回資產。"},{"en":"Quick disposal helps lenders recover money and reduce storage or holding costs.","zh":"快速處置幫助貸款人取回款項並減少儲存或持有成本。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and refers to selling off recovered property.","zh":"這個短語較正式，指出售收回的財產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"repossessed assets","meaning":"被收回的資產","examples":[{"en":"Repossessed assets may be sold at fire-sale auctions.","zh":"被收回的資產可能在賤價拍賣中出售。"},{"en":"Repossessed assets are valuable items or properties taken back because payments were not made.","zh":"repossessed assets 指因未付款而被收回的有價值物品或物業。"},{"en":"A repossessed car may be sold cheaply if the finance company wants quick cash.","zh":"如果財務公司想快速套現，被收回的汽車可能被廉價出售。"},{"en":"These assets are often sold so lenders can reduce losses.","zh":"這些資產通常被出售，以便貸款人減少損失。"},{"en":"The phrase covers property, vehicles, or other financed goods taken back by lenders.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋被貸款人收回的物業、車輛或其他融資貨品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"market value","meaning":"市值","examples":[{"en":"The house had a market value nearing $1,000,000.","zh":"該房子的市值接近一百萬美元。"},{"en":"Market value is the price something is likely to sell for in the current market.","zh":"market value 指某物在當前市場中可能售出的價格。"},{"en":"A flat’s market value may rise if a new train station opens nearby.","zh":"如果附近開設新鐵路站，單位市值可能上升。"},{"en":"Investors compare market value with auction price to decide whether a deal is cheap.","zh":"投資者比較市值和拍賣價，以決定交易是否便宜。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to realistic selling price, not emotional value.","zh":"這個短語指現實售價，而不是情感價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"nearing","meaning":"接近……","examples":[{"en":"The property had a market value nearing one million dollars.","zh":"該物業市值接近一百萬美元。"},{"en":"Nearing means getting close to a particular number, time, or condition.","zh":"nearing 指接近某個數字、時間或狀況。"},{"en":"A student nearing graduation may begin applying for jobs.","zh":"接近畢業的學生可能開始申請工作。"},{"en":"A price nearing one million dollars may still be slightly below that figure.","zh":"接近一百萬美元的價格可能仍略低於該數字。"},{"en":"The word describes approaching a point, not reaching it exactly.","zh":"這個詞描述接近某點，而不是完全達到。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"reserve price","meaning":"底價；保留價","examples":[{"en":"The house had a low reserve price to attract bidders.","zh":"該房子有低底價，以吸引競投者。"},{"en":"A reserve price is the minimum price a seller is willing to accept at an auction.","zh":"reserve price 指賣方在拍賣中願意接受的最低價格。"},{"en":"If no one bids above the reserve price, the owner may refuse to sell the item.","zh":"如果沒有人出價高於底價，物主可能拒絕出售該物品。"},{"en":"A low reserve price can encourage more people to join the bidding.","zh":"低底價可以鼓勵更多人參與競投。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the seller’s minimum acceptable auction price.","zh":"這個短語指賣方可接受的最低拍賣價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"designed to encourage","meaning":"旨在鼓勵……","examples":[{"en":"The low reserve price was designed to encourage bidders.","zh":"低底價旨在鼓勵競投者。"},{"en":"Designed to encourage means planned in order to make people more willing to do something.","zh":"designed to encourage 指為了令人更願意做某事而設計或安排。"},{"en":"A free trial lesson is designed to encourage students to join a course.","zh":"免費試堂旨在鼓勵學生報讀課程。"},{"en":"Lower prices can encourage buyers by reducing their fear of overpaying.","zh":"較低價格可以透過降低買家對支付過高價格的恐懼來鼓勵他們。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the purpose behind a design or policy.","zh":"這個短語解釋設計或政策背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bidders","meaning":"競投者","examples":[{"en":"A low reserve price can encourage bidders at an auction.","zh":"低底價可以鼓勵拍賣中的競投者。"},{"en":"Bidders are people who offer money to buy something at an auction.","zh":"bidders 指在拍賣中出價購買某物的人。"},{"en":"Several bidders may compete for the same flat if the starting price is attractive.","zh":"如果起拍價吸引，幾名競投者可能競爭同一個單位。"},{"en":"More bidders can push the final selling price higher.","zh":"更多競投者可以推高最終售價。"},{"en":"The word refers to auction participants who make offers.","zh":"這個詞指在拍賣中出價的參與者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"secure a quick sale","meaning":"確保快速成交","examples":[{"en":"The low reserve price helped secure a quick sale.","zh":"低底價幫助確保快速成交。"},{"en":"To secure a quick sale means to make sure something is sold quickly.","zh":"secure a quick sale 指確保某物快速售出。"},{"en":"A shop may lower prices to secure a quick sale before moving location.","zh":"商店搬遷前可能降價，以確保快速成交。"},{"en":"Sellers may accept less money if speed is more important than the highest price.","zh":"如果速度比最高價格更重要，賣方可能接受較少金錢。"},{"en":"The phrase connects pricing strategy with fast completion.","zh":"這個短語把定價策略與快速完成交易連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"went for","meaning":"以……價格售出","examples":[{"en":"The house went for $450,000 at auction.","zh":"該房子在拍賣中以45萬美元售出。"},{"en":"Went for means was sold for a particular price.","zh":"went for 指以某特定價格售出。"},{"en":"The old piano went for only $200 at the school charity auction.","zh":"那部舊鋼琴在學校慈善拍賣中只以200美元售出。"},{"en":"If a property goes for far below market value, it may be a bargain.","zh":"如果物業以遠低於市值的價格售出，它可能是划算交易。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and commonly used for auction selling prices.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，常用於拍賣售價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"whopping discount","meaning":"驚人的折扣","examples":[{"en":"The buyer received a whopping 55% discount.","zh":"買家獲得驚人的55%折扣。"},{"en":"A whopping discount is a very large and impressive price reduction.","zh":"whopping discount 指非常大而令人印象深刻的減價。"},{"en":"A student may buy a laptop with a whopping discount during a clearance sale.","zh":"學生可能在清貨減價時以驚人折扣買到手提電腦。"},{"en":"Huge discounts can attract buyers quickly, especially when sellers need fast cash.","zh":"巨大折扣可以快速吸引買家，尤其當賣方需要快速套現。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds informal and emphasises how surprisingly big the discount is.","zh":"這個短語語氣較非正式，強調折扣大得令人驚訝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be realistic","meaning":"現實一點；務實","examples":[{"en":"Investors must be realistic about how much they can afford.","zh":"投資者必須現實地看待自己負擔得起多少。"},{"en":"To be realistic means to judge a situation according to facts and limits, not wishes.","zh":"be realistic 指根據事實和限制，而不是願望來判斷情況。"},{"en":"A student should be realistic about how many essays she can finish in one night.","zh":"學生應現實地看待一晚可以完成多少篇作文。"},{"en":"Being realistic prevents people from borrowing too much or planning beyond their ability.","zh":"務實可以防止人借貸過多或作超出能力的計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase encourages practical thinking.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵實際思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"stretch yourself too far financially","meaning":"令自己財政負擔過重","examples":[{"en":"Investors should not stretch themselves too far financially.","zh":"投資者不應令自己財政負擔過重。"},{"en":"To stretch yourself too far financially means to spend or borrow so much that money becomes dangerously tight.","zh":"stretch yourself too far financially 指花費或借款過多，以致財政變得危險地緊張。"},{"en":"A family stretches itself too far financially if almost all income goes to rent and loan payments.","zh":"如果家庭幾乎所有收入都用於租金和貸款供款，就是令自己財政負擔過重。"},{"en":"Financial overextension can leave people unable to handle repairs, illness, or job loss.","zh":"財政過度拉緊可以令人無法應付維修、疾病或失業。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against taking on more financial pressure than you can safely bear.","zh":"這個短語警告不要承擔超出安全承受能力的財政壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the biggest mistake","meaning":"最大錯誤","examples":[{"en":"The biggest mistake is to borrow too much.","zh":"最大錯誤是借貸過多。"},{"en":"The biggest mistake means the most serious error someone can make in a situation.","zh":"the biggest mistake 指人在某情況中可能犯下的最嚴重錯誤。"},{"en":"In exam preparation, the biggest mistake may be memorising answers without understanding the question.","zh":"在備考中，最大錯誤可能是不理解題目就背答案。"},{"en":"In investment, one major mistake can damage finances for many years.","zh":"在投資中，一個重大錯誤可以損害多年財務狀況。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the error people should avoid most carefully.","zh":"這個短語突出人們最應小心避免的錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"borrow too much","meaning":"借貸過多","examples":[{"en":"First-time investors should avoid borrowing too much.","zh":"首次投資者應避免借貸過多。"},{"en":"To borrow too much means to take on more debt than one can safely repay.","zh":"borrow too much 指承擔超過自己能安全償還的債務。"},{"en":"A student should not borrow too much for a course if the future income is uncertain.","zh":"如果未來收入不確定，學生不應為課程借貸過多。"},{"en":"Borrowing too much can make small problems turn into serious financial stress.","zh":"借貸過多可以令小問題變成嚴重財務壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against excessive debt.","zh":"這個短語警告不要過度負債。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in other words","meaning":"換言之","examples":[{"en":"To borrow too much is, in other words, to overborrow.","zh":"借貸過多，換言之，就是過度借貸。"},{"en":"In other words introduces a simpler or clearer way to say the same idea.","zh":"in other words 用來引入同一想法的更簡單或更清楚說法。"},{"en":"The essay lacks focus; in other words, it tries to answer too many questions at once.","zh":"這篇作文缺乏焦點；換言之，它同時試圖回答太多問題。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when they want to restate a point more directly.","zh":"當作者想更直接重述重點時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It helps readers understand by giving a second version of the idea.","zh":"它透過給出第二種說法幫助讀者理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"overborrow","meaning":"過度借貸","examples":[{"en":"Janet warns first-time investors not to overborrow.","zh":"Janet 警告首次投資者不要過度借貸。"},{"en":"To overborrow means to borrow more money than is safe or manageable.","zh":"overborrow 指借入超過安全或可管理範圍的金錢。"},{"en":"A family may overborrow if it takes a large mortgage without saving for emergencies.","zh":"如果家庭承擔大額按揭卻沒有應急儲蓄，就是過度借貸。"},{"en":"Overborrowing can lead to missed payments, stress, and repossession.","zh":"過度借貸可以導致錯過供款、壓力和物業被收回。"},{"en":"The word is a strong warning about excessive debt.","zh":"這個詞是關於過量債務的強烈警告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"first-time investors","meaning":"首次投資者","examples":[{"en":"Lenders often demand bigger down payments from first-time investors.","zh":"貸款機構通常要求首次投資者支付較高首期。"},{"en":"First-time investors are people investing in something for the first time.","zh":"first-time investors 指首次投資某事物的人。"},{"en":"A first-time investor may need advice before buying a rental flat.","zh":"首次投資者在買入出租單位前可能需要建議。"},{"en":"Because they have no proven record, first-time investors may face stricter borrowing conditions.","zh":"因為他們沒有已證明往績，首次投資者可能面對更嚴格借款條件。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights inexperience in investment.","zh":"這個短語突出投資方面缺乏經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lenders","meaning":"貸款機構；放款人","examples":[{"en":"Lenders usually demand bigger down payments from new investors.","zh":"貸款機構通常要求新投資者支付較高首期。"},{"en":"Lenders are banks, companies, or people that lend money to borrowers.","zh":"lenders 指向借款人借出金錢的銀行、公司或人士。"},{"en":"A lender may check a borrower’s income before approving a mortgage.","zh":"貸款人可能在批准按揭前檢查借款人的收入。"},{"en":"Lenders reduce their risk by asking for deposits, documents, and repayment plans.","zh":"貸款機構透過要求訂金、文件和還款計劃來降低風險。"},{"en":"The word refers to those who provide loans.","zh":"這個詞指提供貸款的人或機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"demand bigger down payments","meaning":"要求較高首期","examples":[{"en":"Lenders may demand bigger down payments from first-time investors.","zh":"貸款機構可能要求首次投資者支付較高首期。"},{"en":"To demand bigger down payments means to require buyers to pay more money at the beginning of a purchase.","zh":"demand bigger down payments 指要求買家在購買開始時支付更多金錢。"},{"en":"A bank may demand a bigger down payment if the borrower has unstable income.","zh":"如果借款人收入不穩定，銀行可能要求較高首期。"},{"en":"Bigger down payments reduce the lender’s risk but increase the buyer’s upfront burden.","zh":"較高首期降低貸款人的風險，但增加買家的前期負擔。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stricter lending requirements.","zh":"這個短語描述較嚴格的貸款要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"down payments","meaning":"首期付款","examples":[{"en":"First-time investors often need to make bigger down payments.","zh":"首次投資者通常需要支付較高首期。"},{"en":"Down payments are the money paid at the beginning of a purchase before the rest is financed by a loan.","zh":"down payments 指購買開始時支付的款項，其餘部分由貸款融資。"},{"en":"A flat buyer may pay a down payment and borrow the remaining amount from a bank.","zh":"買樓者可能支付首期，然後向銀行借餘下金額。"},{"en":"A larger down payment lowers the loan amount but ties up more of the buyer’s cash.","zh":"較高首期會降低貸款額，但也綁住買家更多現金。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to upfront payment in a purchase.","zh":"這個短語指購買中的前期付款。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"proven track record","meaning":"已證明的往績","examples":[{"en":"First-time investors do not have a proven track record.","zh":"首次投資者沒有已證明的往績。"},{"en":"A proven track record is evidence from past performance showing that someone has succeeded before.","zh":"proven track record 指過往表現證明某人曾成功的證據。"},{"en":"A tutor with a proven track record can show students’ past exam improvements.","zh":"有已證明往績的導師可以展示學生過往考試進步。"},{"en":"Lenders trust borrowers more when they have a proven record of successful repayment.","zh":"當借款人有成功還款往績，貸款人會更信任他們。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to reliable proof from experience.","zh":"這個短語指來自經驗的可靠證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"money on the table","meaning":"已投入並承受風險的資金","examples":[{"en":"A larger down payment means more of your money is on the table.","zh":"較高首期意味你有更多資金已投入並承受風險。"},{"en":"Money on the table means money already committed to a deal and exposed to risk.","zh":"money on the table 指已投入某交易並暴露於風險中的金錢。"},{"en":"If a family pays a large deposit for a flat, they have a lot of money on the table.","zh":"如果家庭為單位支付大額訂金，他們就有很多資金已投入並承受風險。"},{"en":"The more money you put into a risky deal, the more you may lose if it fails.","zh":"你投入高風險交易的錢越多，交易失敗時可能損失越多。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights personal financial exposure.","zh":"這個短語突出個人財務風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"should anything go wrong","meaning":"萬一出現問題","examples":[{"en":"Should anything go wrong, the investor may suffer a major loss.","zh":"萬一出現問題，投資者可能遭受重大損失。"},{"en":"Should anything go wrong means if any problem happens.","zh":"should anything go wrong 指如果有任何問題發生。"},{"en":"Should anything go wrong during the school trip, teachers must contact parents immediately.","zh":"萬一學校旅行中出現問題，老師必須立即聯絡家長。"},{"en":"Investors need spare cash because problems such as repairs or vacancies can happen suddenly.","zh":"投資者需要備用現金，因為維修或空置等問題可能突然出現。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to introduce a possible bad situation.","zh":"這個短語是引入可能壞情況的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be in for","meaning":"將要面對……","examples":[{"en":"If the investment fails, you may be in for a big financial hit.","zh":"如果投資失敗，你可能將要面對巨大財務打擊。"},{"en":"To be in for something means to be likely to experience something, often unpleasant.","zh":"be in for something 指很可能經歷某事，通常是不愉快的事。"},{"en":"A student who has not revised may be in for a difficult exam.","zh":"沒有溫習的學生可能將要面對一場困難考試。"},{"en":"Investors who overborrow may be in for trouble when interest rates rise.","zh":"過度借貸的投資者在利率上升時可能將要面對麻煩。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that a consequence is coming.","zh":"這個短語警告某後果將會到來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"big financial hit","meaning":"巨大財務打擊","examples":[{"en":"A failed property deal can result in a big financial hit.","zh":"失敗的物業交易可以導致巨大財務打擊。"},{"en":"A big financial hit is a serious loss of money.","zh":"big financial hit 指嚴重金錢損失。"},{"en":"A family may take a big financial hit if a business closes after they invested their savings.","zh":"如果家庭把積蓄投資到一盤生意後該生意倒閉，他們可能遭受巨大財務打擊。"},{"en":"Large deposits and high loans increase the size of the possible financial hit.","zh":"大額訂金和高額貸款會增加可能財務打擊的規模。"},{"en":"The phrase describes painful money loss.","zh":"這個短語描述痛苦的金錢損失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"business partner","meaning":"生意夥伴","examples":[{"en":"James Nylles is Janet Anderson’s business partner.","zh":"James Nylles 是 Janet Anderson 的生意夥伴。"},{"en":"A business partner is a person who shares ownership, responsibility, or work in a business.","zh":"business partner 指在生意中分享所有權、責任或工作的人。"},{"en":"Two friends may become business partners when they open a language centre together.","zh":"兩位朋友一起開語言中心時，可能成為生意夥伴。"},{"en":"Good business partners need trust because they share risks and decisions.","zh":"好生意夥伴需要信任，因為他們共同承擔風險和決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a professional relationship in running a business.","zh":"這個短語描述經營生意中的專業關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in complete agreement","meaning":"完全同意","examples":[{"en":"James is in complete agreement with Janet on this point.","zh":"James 在這一點上完全同意 Janet。"},{"en":"To be in complete agreement means to fully share the same opinion.","zh":"in complete agreement 指完全持有相同意見。"},{"en":"The teachers were in complete agreement that students needed more writing practice.","zh":"老師們完全同意學生需要更多寫作練習。"},{"en":"Complete agreement can strengthen advice because different experts support the same warning.","zh":"完全同意可以加強建議，因為不同專家支持同一警告。"},{"en":"The phrase means no meaningful disagreement remains.","zh":"這個短語表示沒有實質分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"on this point","meaning":"在這一點上","examples":[{"en":"James agrees with Janet on this point.","zh":"James 在這一點上同意 Janet。"},{"en":"On this point means about this particular issue or idea.","zh":"on this point 指關於這個特定議題或想法。"},{"en":"Two teachers may disagree about homework, but they agree on this point: students need clear feedback.","zh":"兩位老師可能對功課有不同意見，但在這一點上同意：學生需要清楚回饋。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows agreement or disagreement to one specific matter.","zh":"這個短語把同意或不同意收窄到某一具體事項。"},{"en":"It helps avoid suggesting that people agree about everything.","zh":"它避免暗示人們對所有事情都同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"highlights the fact that","meaning":"強調……這個事實","examples":[{"en":"James highlights the fact that deposits are only part of the cost.","zh":"James 強調訂金只是成本一部分這個事實。"},{"en":"To highlight the fact that means to draw attention to an important truth.","zh":"highlight the fact that 指提醒人注意一個重要事實。"},{"en":"A teacher may highlight the fact that good writing needs planning, not only grammar.","zh":"老師可能強調好寫作需要構思，而不只是文法這個事實。"},{"en":"Highlighting a fact helps people notice a risk they might otherwise ignore.","zh":"強調某事實幫助人注意到本來可能忽略的風險。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a point the speaker wants readers to remember.","zh":"這個短語引入說話者希望讀者記住的重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"mortgage payments","meaning":"按揭供款","examples":[{"en":"Mortgage payments are only part of the long-term cost.","zh":"按揭供款只是長期成本的一部分。"},{"en":"Mortgage payments are regular payments made to repay a property loan.","zh":"mortgage payments 指為償還物業貸款而定期支付的款項。"},{"en":"A landlord must pay mortgage payments even if the flat has no tenant for a month.","zh":"即使單位一個月沒有租客，業主仍必須支付按揭供款。"},{"en":"High mortgage payments can reduce profit from rental income.","zh":"高按揭供款可以減少租金收入帶來的利潤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to continuing loan payments after buying property.","zh":"這個短語指買入物業後持續支付的貸款供款。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"deposits","meaning":"訂金；首期款項","examples":[{"en":"Deposits are only part of the cost of buying rental property.","zh":"訂金只是購買出租物業成本的一部分。"},{"en":"Deposits are upfront payments made to secure a purchase, rental, or agreement.","zh":"deposits 指為確保購買、租賃或協議而預先支付的款項。"},{"en":"A tenant may pay a deposit before moving into a flat.","zh":"租客入住單位前可能支付訂金。"},{"en":"Paying a deposit ties up cash, so investors must keep money for later costs too.","zh":"支付訂金會佔用現金，所以投資者也必須保留日後成本所需資金。"},{"en":"The word often refers to money paid at the beginning of a deal.","zh":"這個詞通常指交易開始時支付的金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"only part of","meaning":"只是……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Mortgage payments are only part of the long-term cost.","zh":"按揭供款只是長期成本的一部分。"},{"en":"Only part of something means not the whole thing, but just one element within it.","zh":"only part of something 指不是整體，而只是其中一個元素。"},{"en":"Tuition fees are only part of the cost of studying overseas.","zh":"學費只是海外升學成本的一部分。"},{"en":"If people focus on only one cost, they may underestimate the total expense.","zh":"如果人們只集中一項成本，可能低估總開支。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that there are other factors to consider.","zh":"這個短語提醒還有其他因素需要考慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"long-term cost","meaning":"長期成本","examples":[{"en":"Investors must consider the long-term cost of buying rental property.","zh":"投資者必須考慮購買出租物業的長期成本。"},{"en":"Long-term cost means expenses that continue over many months or years.","zh":"long-term cost 指持續多個月或多年的開支。"},{"en":"A car’s long-term cost includes insurance, repairs, fuel, and maintenance.","zh":"汽車的長期成本包括保險、維修、燃油和保養。"},{"en":"Ignoring long-term costs can make a cheap purchase expensive later.","zh":"忽視長期成本可以令便宜購買日後變得昂貴。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on total future expense, not only the initial price.","zh":"這個短語重點是未來總開支，而不只是初始價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rental property","meaning":"出租物業","examples":[{"en":"A rental property involves many long-term costs.","zh":"出租物業涉及許多長期成本。"},{"en":"A rental property is a property bought or owned in order to rent it to tenants.","zh":"rental property 指為出租給租客而購買或持有的物業。"},{"en":"A small flat near a university can be a rental property for students.","zh":"大學附近的小單位可以成為出租給學生的物業。"},{"en":"Rental property can produce monthly income, but repairs and vacancies reduce profit.","zh":"出租物業可以產生月租收入，但維修和空置會減少利潤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to property used as an income-generating rental.","zh":"這個短語指用作產生租金收入的物業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"administration and maintenance","meaning":"行政和維修保養","examples":[{"en":"Repairs, administration and maintenance all cost money.","zh":"維修、行政和保養都需要金錢。"},{"en":"Administration and maintenance are the management tasks and repair work needed to keep something running properly.","zh":"administration and maintenance 指讓某事物正常運作所需的管理任務和維修工作。"},{"en":"A school building needs administration and maintenance, from paying bills to fixing lights.","zh":"學校建築需要行政和維修保養，由繳付帳單到修理燈光都包括在內。"},{"en":"Poor maintenance can increase costs later because small problems become major repairs.","zh":"保養差可以令日後成本增加，因為小問題會變成大維修。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to ongoing management and upkeep.","zh":"這個短語指持續管理和保養。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"property manager’s fees","meaning":"物業經理費用","examples":[{"en":"Property manager’s fees are part of the long-term cost.","zh":"物業經理費用是長期成本的一部分。"},{"en":"Property manager’s fees are payments made to a person or company that manages rental property for the owner.","zh":"property manager’s fees 指支付給為業主管理出租物業的人或公司的費用。"},{"en":"A landlord may pay property manager’s fees so someone else handles tenants and repairs.","zh":"業主可能支付物業經理費用，讓其他人處理租客和維修。"},{"en":"These fees reduce profit, so investors must include them in calculations.","zh":"這些費用會減少利潤，所以投資者必須把它們納入計算。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to management-service costs.","zh":"這個短語指管理服務成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"and so on","meaning":"等等","examples":[{"en":"Repairs, insurance and so on all require money in reserve.","zh":"維修、保險等等都需要備用資金。"},{"en":"And so on means and other similar things.","zh":"and so on 指以及其他類似事物。"},{"en":"Students need pens, notebooks, folders and so on for the new school year.","zh":"新學年學生需要筆、筆記簿、文件夾等等。"},{"en":"The phrase avoids listing every item when the category is already clear.","zh":"當類別已清楚，這個短語避免逐一列出每項。"},{"en":"It signals that the examples given are not the full list.","zh":"它表示所給例子不是完整清單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"require someone to","meaning":"要求某人……","examples":[{"en":"These costs require investors to hold money in reserve.","zh":"這些成本要求投資者保留備用資金。"},{"en":"To require someone to do something means to make it necessary for them to do it.","zh":"require someone to do something 指令某人有必要做某事。"},{"en":"School rules require students to arrive before the bell.","zh":"校規要求學生在鐘聲前到達。"},{"en":"Extra costs require investors to keep spare cash because unexpected bills may appear.","zh":"額外成本要求投資者保留備用現金，因為意外帳單可能出現。"},{"en":"The phrase shows necessity or obligation.","zh":"這個短語顯示必要性或責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"significant amount of","meaning":"大量的……","examples":[{"en":"Investors need a significant amount of money in reserve.","zh":"投資者需要大量備用資金。"},{"en":"A significant amount of something means a large or important quantity of it.","zh":"significant amount of something 指大量或重要數量的某物。"},{"en":"A school trip requires a significant amount of planning before students can travel safely.","zh":"學校旅行需要大量規劃，學生才能安全出行。"},{"en":"A significant amount of spare cash helps investors survive unexpected expenses.","zh":"大量備用現金幫助投資者應付意外開支。"},{"en":"The phrase means more than a small amount.","zh":"這個短語意思是超過小量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"money in reserve","meaning":"備用資金","examples":[{"en":"Investors should hold money in reserve for unexpected costs.","zh":"投資者應保留備用資金以應付意外成本。"},{"en":"Money in reserve is spare money kept aside for future needs or emergencies.","zh":"money in reserve 指留作未來需要或緊急情況的備用金錢。"},{"en":"A family may keep money in reserve in case the washing machine breaks.","zh":"家庭可能保留備用資金，以防洗衣機壞掉。"},{"en":"Without reserve money, one repair bill can create financial stress.","zh":"沒有備用資金，一張維修帳單就可以造成財政壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to emergency or backup funds.","zh":"這個短語指應急或後備資金。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"failure to factor these in","meaning":"未能把這些因素計算在內","examples":[{"en":"Failure to factor these in can lead to disaster.","zh":"未能把這些因素計算在內可以導致災難性後果。"},{"en":"Failure to factor these in means not including these costs or risks in your planning.","zh":"failure to factor these in 指沒有把這些成本或風險納入規劃。"},{"en":"A student’s study plan may fail if it does not factor in travel time and tiredness.","zh":"如果學習計劃沒有把交通時間和疲倦計算在內，它可能會失敗。"},{"en":"Investors who ignore maintenance, insurance, and management fees may badly underestimate costs.","zh":"忽視維修、保險和管理費的投資者可能嚴重低估成本。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against leaving important details out of calculations.","zh":"這個短語警告不要把重要細節排除在計算之外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"factor something in","meaning":"將……計算在內","examples":[{"en":"Investors must factor repair costs into their calculations.","zh":"投資者必須把維修成本計算在內。"},{"en":"To factor something in means to include it when making a calculation, plan, or decision.","zh":"factor something in 指在計算、計劃或決定時納入某因素。"},{"en":"A student should factor in commuting time before choosing an evening course.","zh":"學生選擇夜校課程前，應把通勤時間計算在內。"},{"en":"If investors factor in all costs, they can judge profit more accurately.","zh":"如果投資者把所有成本計算在內，就能更準確判斷利潤。"},{"en":"The phrase means not forgetting an important part of the situation.","zh":"這個短語意思是不要忘記情況中的重要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"calculating","meaning":"計算","examples":[{"en":"Investors must be careful when calculating mortgage repayments.","zh":"投資者計算按揭供款時必須小心。"},{"en":"Calculating means working out a number by using information and arithmetic.","zh":"calculating 指使用資訊和算術推算數字。"},{"en":"A family calculates monthly expenses before deciding whether to buy a car.","zh":"家庭在決定是否買車前會計算每月開支。"},{"en":"Wrong calculations can make a purchase look affordable when it is not.","zh":"錯誤計算可以令一項購買看似負擔得起，但實際上不是。"},{"en":"The word stresses careful numerical thinking.","zh":"這個詞強調仔細的數字思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"afford to part with","meaning":"負擔得起付出……","examples":[{"en":"You must know how much you can afford to part with each month.","zh":"你必須知道自己每月負擔得起付出多少。"},{"en":"To afford to part with money means to be able to give or spend it without serious financial trouble.","zh":"afford to part with money 指能夠付出或花掉金錢，而不造成嚴重財務問題。"},{"en":"A student should know how much pocket money she can afford to part with before buying concert tickets.","zh":"學生買演唱會門票前，應知道自己負擔得起付出多少零用錢。"},{"en":"Spending more than you can afford to part with can create debt or stress.","zh":"花超過自己負擔得起付出的金額，可以造成債務或壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on money you can safely let go.","zh":"這個短語重點是你能安全放手的金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lead to disaster","meaning":"導致災難性後果","examples":[{"en":"Poor financial planning can lead to disaster.","zh":"差劣財務規劃可以導致災難性後果。"},{"en":"To lead to disaster means to cause a very serious bad result.","zh":"lead to disaster 指造成非常嚴重的壞結果。"},{"en":"Ignoring safety rules in a laboratory can lead to disaster.","zh":"在實驗室忽視安全規則可以導致災難性後果。"},{"en":"In investment, borrowing too much and ignoring costs can create severe financial harm.","zh":"在投資中，借貸過多和忽視成本可以造成嚴重財務傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase is a strong warning about serious consequences.","zh":"這個短語是關於嚴重後果的強烈警告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"one of the biggest traps","meaning":"最大陷阱之一","examples":[{"en":"One of the biggest traps is paying too much for a property.","zh":"最大陷阱之一是為物業支付過高價格。"},{"en":"One of the biggest traps means one of the most serious mistakes or dangers people easily fall into.","zh":"one of the biggest traps 指人們容易跌入的最嚴重錯誤或危險之一。"},{"en":"One of the biggest traps in studying is spending hours highlighting notes without practising questions.","zh":"學習中最大陷阱之一，是花數小時間螢光筆畫筆記卻不做題。"},{"en":"A trap is dangerous because it may look attractive at first.","zh":"陷阱之所以危險，是因為它起初可能看起來吸引。"},{"en":"The phrase warns about a common and costly mistake.","zh":"這個短語警告常見且代價高昂的錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"temptation to","meaning":"……的誘惑","examples":[{"en":"Investors must resist the temptation to pay over the odds.","zh":"投資者必須抵抗支付過高價格的誘惑。"},{"en":"Temptation to do something means a strong desire to do something that may be unwise.","zh":"temptation to do something 指想做某事的強烈慾望，但該事可能不明智。"},{"en":"A student may feel the temptation to check her phone instead of revising.","zh":"學生可能感到查看手機而不是溫習的誘惑。"},{"en":"In auctions, competition can create the temptation to bid higher than planned.","zh":"在拍賣中，競爭可以造成出價高於原計劃的誘惑。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests an attractive but risky urge.","zh":"這個短語暗示吸引但有風險的衝動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pay over the odds","meaning":"付出過高價格","examples":[{"en":"Some buyers pay over the odds to get the property they want.","zh":"有些買家為得到想要的物業而付出過高價格。"},{"en":"To pay over the odds means to pay more than something is really worth.","zh":"pay over the odds 指支付超過某物真正價值的金額。"},{"en":"A parent may pay over the odds for a rare textbook before exams.","zh":"家長可能在考試前為稀有教科書付出過高價格。"},{"en":"Emotional buying can make people pay over the odds and regret it later.","zh":"情緒化購買可以令人付出過高價格並日後後悔。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against overpaying.","zh":"這個短語警告不要多付錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the property you desire","meaning":"你渴望得到的物業","examples":[{"en":"Buyers may overpay for the property they desire.","zh":"買家可能為自己渴望得到的物業支付過高價格。"},{"en":"The property you desire is the flat, house, or building you strongly want to buy.","zh":"the property you desire 指你非常想買入的單位、房屋或建築物。"},{"en":"A family may desire a flat near a famous school even if it is expensive.","zh":"家庭可能渴望得到名校附近的單位，即使它很昂貴。"},{"en":"Strong desire can make buyers ignore price, condition, or future return.","zh":"強烈渴望可以令買家忽視價格、狀況或未來回報。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds investors that wanting something is not the same as judging it wisely.","zh":"這個短語提醒投資者，想要某物不等於明智判斷它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get carried away","meaning":"一時衝動；忘乎所以","examples":[{"en":"Buyers often get carried away in the auction room.","zh":"買家在拍賣場中常常一時衝動。"},{"en":"To get carried away means to become so excited or emotional that you lose control or good judgement.","zh":"get carried away 指因太興奮或情緒化而失去控制或良好判斷。"},{"en":"A student may get carried away in a discussion and forget to answer the actual question.","zh":"學生可能在討論中太投入，忘記回答真正題目。"},{"en":"In an auction, excitement can make buyers bid more than they planned.","zh":"在拍賣中，興奮可以令買家出價高於原定計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against letting emotion take over.","zh":"這個短語警告不要讓情緒接管。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"auction-room setting","meaning":"拍賣場環境","examples":[{"en":"The auction-room setting can become highly competitive.","zh":"拍賣場環境可以變得高度競爭。"},{"en":"An auction-room setting is the environment where people gather and bid against one another.","zh":"auction-room setting 指人們聚集並互相競投的環境。"},{"en":"In an auction-room setting, buyers may feel pressure when others keep raising bids.","zh":"在拍賣場環境中，當其他人不斷加價，買家可能感到壓力。"},{"en":"The setting can influence behaviour because public competition affects emotions.","zh":"環境可以影響行為，因為公開競爭會影響情緒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the atmosphere and situation of an auction.","zh":"這個短語描述拍賣的氣氛和情境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"quite competitive","meaning":"相當具競爭性","examples":[{"en":"Property auctions can get quite competitive.","zh":"物業拍賣可以變得相當具競爭性。"},{"en":"Quite competitive means involving fairly strong competition between people or groups.","zh":"quite competitive 指人或群體之間有頗強競爭。"},{"en":"School debate team selection can be quite competitive when many students apply.","zh":"當很多學生申請，學校辯論隊選拔可以相當具競爭性。"},{"en":"Competitive situations may push people to try harder, but they can also cause overreaction.","zh":"競爭性情況可能推動人更努力，但也可能造成過度反應。"},{"en":"The phrase means more competitive than calm or easy.","zh":"這個短語意思是比平靜或容易的情況更具競爭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"descend into","meaning":"淪為……","examples":[{"en":"The auction can descend into a racket of one-upmanship.","zh":"拍賣可以淪為互相攀比的混亂競爭。"},{"en":"To descend into something means to become worse and turn into an unpleasant situation.","zh":"descend into something 指情況變差並轉化為不愉快局面。"},{"en":"A class discussion can descend into shouting if students stop listening to one another.","zh":"如果學生停止互相聆聽，課堂討論可能淪為吵鬧。"},{"en":"Auctions may descend into irrational bidding when buyers focus on beating each other.","zh":"當買家集中於擊敗對方，拍賣可能淪為不理性出價。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a negative change from order to disorder.","zh":"這個短語描述由秩序變成混亂的負面變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a racket of one-upmanship","meaning":"互相攀比的混亂競爭","examples":[{"en":"The auction became a racket of one-upmanship among buyers.","zh":"拍賣變成買家之間互相攀比的混亂競爭。"},{"en":"A racket of one-upmanship is noisy, confused competition where people try to outdo each other.","zh":"a racket of one-upmanship 指人們互相超越對方而形成嘈雜混亂的競爭。"},{"en":"A parents’ group can become a racket of one-upmanship if everyone boasts about their child’s achievements.","zh":"如果每個人都炫耀孩子成就，家長群組可以變成互相攀比的混亂競爭。"},{"en":"One-upmanship can push people to spend, speak, or act beyond good sense.","zh":"互相攀比可以推動人花費、說話或行動超出理智。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises competitive showing-off.","zh":"這個短語批評競爭式炫耀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"one-upmanship","meaning":"爭強好勝；互相較勁","examples":[{"en":"One-upmanship can push buyers to bid higher than planned.","zh":"爭強好勝可以推動買家出價高於原定計劃。"},{"en":"One-upmanship is behaviour where people try to prove they are better than others.","zh":"one-upmanship 指人們試圖證明自己比別人強的行為。"},{"en":"In class, one-upmanship happens when students answer only to show they are smarter.","zh":"在課堂中，當學生回答只是為了顯示自己更聰明，就是爭強好勝。"},{"en":"One-upmanship can make decisions emotional because people focus on winning rather than value.","zh":"爭強好勝可以令決定情緒化，因為人們集中於勝出而不是價值。"},{"en":"The word describes competitive showing-off.","zh":"這個詞描述競爭式炫耀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"end up","meaning":"最終……","examples":[{"en":"Some buyers end up paying top dollar.","zh":"有些買家最終付出高價。"},{"en":"To end up doing something means to finally do or experience it, often after a process or mistake.","zh":"end up doing something 指經過一個過程或錯誤後，最後做某事或經歷某事。"},{"en":"A student who leaves homework until midnight may end up sleeping too little.","zh":"把功課拖到午夜的學生，最終可能睡得太少。"},{"en":"Buyers who keep bidding emotionally may end up paying far more than planned.","zh":"持續情緒化出價的買家，最終可能支付遠高於原定計劃的金額。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the final result of earlier actions.","zh":"這個短語顯示早前行動的最終結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"paying top dollar","meaning":"付出最高價；付出高價","examples":[{"en":"Buyers may end up paying top dollar for a property.","zh":"買家可能最終為物業付出高價。"},{"en":"Paying top dollar means paying a very high price, often the highest market price.","zh":"paying top dollar 指支付非常高的價格，通常是市場最高價。"},{"en":"A parent may pay top dollar for a private tutor before an important exam.","zh":"家長可能在重要考試前為私人導師付出高價。"},{"en":"Paying top dollar reduces investment return because the starting cost is already high.","zh":"付出高價會降低投資回報，因為起始成本已經很高。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that high price can damage profit.","zh":"這個短語警告高價格可以損害利潤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"landing themselves in","meaning":"令自己陷入……","examples":[{"en":"Overpaying can land investors in a difficult financial situation.","zh":"支付過高價格可以令投資者陷入困難財務狀況。"},{"en":"To land oneself in a situation means to cause oneself to end up in that situation, usually a bad one.","zh":"land oneself in a situation 指令自己最終處於某種情況，通常是不好的情況。"},{"en":"A student may land herself in trouble by missing several deadlines.","zh":"學生若錯過幾個截止日期，可能令自己陷入麻煩。"},{"en":"Investors can land themselves in debt if they ignore costs and borrow too much.","zh":"如果投資者忽視成本並借貸過多，可能令自己陷入債務。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights self-caused difficulty.","zh":"這個短語突出由自己造成的困境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"financial situation","meaning":"財務狀況","examples":[{"en":"Overpaying may put investors in a poor financial situation.","zh":"支付過高價格可能令投資者處於差劣財務狀況。"},{"en":"Financial situation means a person’s or organisation’s overall money position, including income, debts, savings, and costs.","zh":"financial situation 指個人或機構整體金錢狀況，包括收入、債務、儲蓄和成本。"},{"en":"A family’s financial situation may worsen if rent rises and income stays the same.","zh":"如果租金上升而收入不變，家庭財務狀況可能惡化。"},{"en":"Good planning improves financial situation by keeping debt and spending under control.","zh":"良好規劃透過控制債務和開支改善財務狀況。"},{"en":"The phrase describes overall money health.","zh":"這個短語描述整體金錢健康。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"can ill afford to","meaning":"實在負擔不起……","examples":[{"en":"Some buyers land themselves in a situation they can ill afford to be in.","zh":"有些買家令自己陷入實在負擔不起的情況。"},{"en":"Can ill afford to do something means can hardly afford it because the cost or risk is too high.","zh":"can ill afford to do something 指因成本或風險太高而幾乎負擔不起某事。"},{"en":"A student can ill afford to miss lessons two weeks before the exam.","zh":"考試前兩星期，學生實在負擔不起缺課。"},{"en":"Investors with little reserve cash can ill afford expensive repairs or months without rent.","zh":"備用現金很少的投資者實在負擔不起昂貴維修或數月沒有租金。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that someone is in no position to take the risk.","zh":"這個短語強調某人根本不適合承擔該風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the property game","meaning":"房地產投資活動","examples":[{"en":"Investors enter the property game to make money.","zh":"投資者進入房地產投資活動是為了賺錢。"},{"en":"The property game means the business or activity of buying, selling, and renting property for profit.","zh":"property game 指為賺取利潤而買賣和出租物業的商業或活動。"},{"en":"A young investor may enter the property game by buying one small rental flat.","zh":"年輕投資者可能透過買入一個小出租單位進入房地產投資活動。"},{"en":"The property game can reward careful planning but punish emotional decisions.","zh":"房地產投資活動可以回報仔細規劃，但懲罰情緒化決定。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and presents property investment as a competitive activity.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，把物業投資呈現為競爭性活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pay up front","meaning":"預先支付","examples":[{"en":"The more you pay up front, the lower your potential return may be.","zh":"你預先支付越多，潛在回報可能越低。"},{"en":"To pay up front means to pay money at the beginning before receiving full benefit.","zh":"pay up front 指在獲得全部好處之前，於開始時先付款。"},{"en":"A student may pay up front for a six-month course to get a discount.","zh":"學生可能預先支付六個月課程費用以取得折扣。"},{"en":"Paying too much up front leaves less cash for emergencies and lowers possible return.","zh":"預先支付太多會留下較少應急現金，並降低可能回報。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to advance payment.","zh":"這個短語指預先付款。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"less likely to","meaning":"較不可能……","examples":[{"en":"The more you overpay, the less likely you are to recoup your investment.","zh":"你支付過高價格越多，就越不可能收回投資。"},{"en":"Less likely to means having a lower chance of doing or experiencing something.","zh":"less likely to 指做某事或經歷某事的機會較低。"},{"en":"Students who practise speaking daily are less likely to panic in an oral exam.","zh":"每天練習口語的學生，在口試中較不可能驚慌。"},{"en":"Investors who pay too much are less likely to earn enough rent to recover costs.","zh":"支付過高價格的投資者較不可能賺取足夠租金收回成本。"},{"en":"The phrase compares probability.","zh":"這個短語比較可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"recoup your investment","meaning":"收回投資","examples":[{"en":"Investors need enough rental income to recoup their investment.","zh":"投資者需要足夠租金收入來收回投資。"},{"en":"To recoup your investment means to earn back the money you originally spent or invested.","zh":"recoup your investment 指賺回你最初花費或投資的金錢。"},{"en":"A shop owner may need two years of sales to recoup the investment in renovation.","zh":"店主可能需要兩年銷售額來收回裝修投資。"},{"en":"If purchase costs are too high, it takes longer to recoup the investment.","zh":"如果購買成本太高，收回投資所需時間會更長。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on recovering the original invested money.","zh":"這個短語重點是取回原本投入的金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in the long run","meaning":"長遠來說","examples":[{"en":"Overpaying can hurt returns in the long run.","zh":"長遠來說，支付過高價格可以損害回報。"},{"en":"In the long run means over a long period of time, after immediate effects have passed.","zh":"in the long run 指在長時間後，當即時影響已過去。"},{"en":"Sleeping enough helps students more in the long run than studying all night once.","zh":"長遠來說，充足睡眠比偶爾通宵讀書更幫到學生。"},{"en":"A decision that feels exciting now may create problems in the long run.","zh":"現在感覺令人興奮的決定，長遠來說可能造成問題。"},{"en":"The phrase shifts attention from short-term feelings to future results.","zh":"這個短語把注意力由短期感受轉向未來結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the good news","meaning":"好消息是……","examples":[{"en":"The good news is that the housing market is not very hot now.","zh":"好消息是樓市現在不太熾熱。"},{"en":"The good news is introduces a positive point in a situation that may seem worrying.","zh":"the good news is 用來在看似令人擔心的情況中引入正面重點。"},{"en":"The good news is that you made grammar mistakes we can fix quickly.","zh":"好消息是你犯的是我們可以快速修正的文法錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase helps balance bad news with a hopeful or useful fact.","zh":"這個短語幫助用有希望或有用的事實平衡壞消息。"},{"en":"It prepares readers for a reassuring point.","zh":"它讓讀者準備接受令人安心的重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"housing market","meaning":"樓市；房地產市場","examples":[{"en":"The housing market is not very hot at the moment.","zh":"目前樓市不太熾熱。"},{"en":"The housing market is the buying, selling, renting, and pricing of homes in an area.","zh":"housing market 指某地區住宅的買賣、租賃和定價情況。"},{"en":"A city’s housing market may become expensive when many people want to live there.","zh":"當很多人想住在某城市，該城市樓市可能變得昂貴。"},{"en":"A cooler housing market can reduce pressure on buyers and lower the risk of overpaying.","zh":"較冷卻的樓市可以減少買家壓力並降低支付過高價格的風險。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the market for homes and residential property.","zh":"這個短語指住宅和居住物業市場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not very hot","meaning":"不太熾熱","examples":[{"en":"The housing market is not very hot at the moment.","zh":"目前樓市不太熾熱。"},{"en":"Not very hot means not extremely active, competitive, or fast-rising.","zh":"not very hot 指不是非常活躍、競爭激烈或快速上升。"},{"en":"The restaurant market is not very hot if few new shops are opening.","zh":"如果很少新店開張，餐飲市場就是不太熾熱。"},{"en":"When a market is not very hot, buyers may have more time to compare options.","zh":"當市場不太熾熱，買家可能有更多時間比較選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a cooler, less intense market condition.","zh":"這個短語描述較冷卻、較不激烈的市場狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at the moment","meaning":"目前","examples":[{"en":"The danger of overpaying is not so great at the moment.","zh":"目前支付過高價格的風險沒有那麼大。"},{"en":"At the moment means now or during the present period.","zh":"at the moment 指現在或目前這段時間。"},{"en":"At the moment, many students are preparing for final exams.","zh":"目前，許多學生正在準備期末考試。"},{"en":"Market conditions can change, so what is true at the moment may not remain true later.","zh":"市場情況可以改變，所以目前真實的情況未必日後仍然真實。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the current situation.","zh":"這個短語重點是當前情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"danger of overpaying","meaning":"支付過高價格的風險","examples":[{"en":"A cooler housing market reduces the danger of overpaying.","zh":"較冷卻的樓市降低支付過高價格的風險。"},{"en":"The danger of overpaying is the risk of paying more than something is worth.","zh":"danger of overpaying 指支付超過某物價值金額的風險。"},{"en":"A shopper faces the danger of overpaying if she buys the first laptop without comparing prices.","zh":"如果購物者不比較價格就買第一部手提電腦，她會面對支付過高價格的風險。"},{"en":"Competitive bidding increases the danger of overpaying because buyers become emotional.","zh":"競爭性出價增加支付過高價格的風險，因為買家變得情緒化。"},{"en":"The phrase warns about paying too much.","zh":"這個短語警告不要支付過多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"set emotions to one side","meaning":"把情緒放到一旁","examples":[{"en":"Investors should set emotions to one side when buying property.","zh":"投資者買物業時應把情緒放到一旁。"},{"en":"To set emotions to one side means to stop feelings from controlling a decision.","zh":"set emotions to one side 指不讓感受控制決定。"},{"en":"A teacher may set emotions to one side when marking a favourite student’s essay.","zh":"老師批改喜愛學生的作文時，可能需要把情緒放到一旁。"},{"en":"Investors who set emotions aside can compare price, rent, and risk more clearly.","zh":"把情緒放到一旁的投資者能更清楚比較價格、租金和風險。"},{"en":"The phrase encourages objective judgement.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵客觀判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"purely business perspective","meaning":"純粹商業角度","examples":[{"en":"Investors should think from a purely business perspective.","zh":"投資者應從純粹商業角度思考。"},{"en":"A purely business perspective means judging something only by costs, risks, income, and profit.","zh":"purely business perspective 指只用成本、風險、收入和利潤來判斷某事。"},{"en":"A landlord may dislike a flat’s design but still buy it from a business perspective if rent is strong.","zh":"業主可能不喜歡單位設計，但如果租金強勁，從商業角度仍會買入。"},{"en":"This perspective reduces emotional mistakes because it focuses on numbers and returns.","zh":"這種角度因集中於數字和回報而減少情緒化錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts investment logic with personal taste.","zh":"這個短語把投資邏輯與個人喜好作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"liking or disliking","meaning":"喜歡或不喜歡","examples":[{"en":"Your liking or disliking the property is irrelevant.","zh":"你喜歡或不喜歡該物業並不相關。"},{"en":"Liking or disliking means personal preference or emotional reaction toward something.","zh":"liking or disliking 指對某事的個人偏好或情緒反應。"},{"en":"A student’s liking or disliking a topic should not decide whether it is important for the exam.","zh":"學生喜歡或不喜歡某主題，不應決定該主題對考試是否重要。"},{"en":"In investment, personal taste can distract people from profit and risk.","zh":"在投資中，個人喜好可以令人分心，忽視利潤和風險。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on subjective feeling.","zh":"這個短語重點是主觀感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"irrelevant","meaning":"不相關；無關重要","examples":[{"en":"Whether you like the property is irrelevant to the investment decision.","zh":"你是否喜歡該物業，與投資決定無關。"},{"en":"Irrelevant means not connected to or not important for the issue being considered.","zh":"irrelevant 指與正在考慮的議題沒有關係或不重要。"},{"en":"A student’s handwriting style is irrelevant if the online exam is typed.","zh":"如果網上考試是打字，學生字體風格就無關重要。"},{"en":"In property investment, personal taste may be irrelevant if tenants will like the flat.","zh":"在物業投資中，如果租客會喜歡該單位，個人口味可能不相關。"},{"en":"The word tells readers to ignore a point because it does not affect the decision.","zh":"這個詞告訴讀者某點不影響決定，因此應忽略。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as Nylles points out","meaning":"正如 Nylles 指出","examples":[{"en":"As Nylles points out, the investor will not be living there.","zh":"正如 Nylles 指出，投資者不會住在那裏。"},{"en":"As someone points out introduces an observation or reminder made by that person.","zh":"as someone points out 用來引入某人提出的觀察或提醒。"},{"en":"As the teacher points out, a beautiful sentence is useless if it does not answer the question.","zh":"正如老師指出，如果一句漂亮句子沒有回答題目，它就沒有用。"},{"en":"The phrase gives credit to the source of a useful point.","zh":"這個短語把有用重點歸功於來源。"},{"en":"It often introduces a practical reminder.","zh":"它常引入實際提醒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"made in the cold, hard light of day","meaning":"在冷靜務實的情況下作出","examples":[{"en":"Business decisions are made in the cold, hard light of day.","zh":"商業決定是在冷靜務實的情況下作出的。"},{"en":"Made in the cold, hard light of day means made calmly and realistically, without emotion or illusion.","zh":"made in the cold, hard light of day 指在冷靜、現實、不受情緒或幻想影響下作出。"},{"en":"A school should decide budgets in the cold, hard light of day, not because one department complains loudly.","zh":"學校應在冷靜務實的情況下決定預算，而不是因某部門大聲投訴。"},{"en":"Clear facts can prevent people from making decisions based on excitement or fear.","zh":"清楚事實可以防止人基於興奮或恐懼作決定。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses tough, objective judgement.","zh":"這個短語強調嚴格而客觀的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"objective","meaning":"目標","examples":[{"en":"Your objective is to minimise your outlay and maximise your return.","zh":"你的目標是將支出減至最低並將回報最大化。"},{"en":"An objective is a goal or purpose that someone is trying to achieve.","zh":"objective 指某人試圖達成的目標或目的。"},{"en":"A student’s objective may be to improve writing accuracy before the final exam.","zh":"學生的目標可能是在期末考前改善寫作準確度。"},{"en":"Clear objectives help people choose actions that support the main goal.","zh":"清楚目標幫助人選擇支持主要目標的行動。"},{"en":"The word refers to what you are trying to accomplish.","zh":"這個詞指你正在努力完成的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"minimise your outlay","meaning":"將支出減至最低","examples":[{"en":"The investor’s objective is to minimise outlay.","zh":"投資者的目標是將支出減至最低。"},{"en":"To minimise your outlay means to reduce the amount of money you have to spend at the beginning or overall.","zh":"minimise your outlay 指減少你一開始或整體需要花費的金錢。"},{"en":"A small business may minimise outlay by renting equipment instead of buying it.","zh":"小企業可能透過租用設備而不是購買設備來將支出減至最低。"},{"en":"Lower outlay can improve returns because less money is tied up in the investment.","zh":"較低支出可以改善回報，因為較少金錢被綁在投資中。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on keeping costs as low as possible.","zh":"這個短語重點是把成本保持到盡可能低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"maximise your return","meaning":"將回報最大化","examples":[{"en":"The investor’s objective is to maximise return.","zh":"投資者的目標是將回報最大化。"},{"en":"To maximise your return means to make the profit or benefit from an investment as high as possible.","zh":"maximise your return 指把投資所得利潤或好處提高到最高。"},{"en":"A café may maximise return by keeping rent low and attracting regular customers.","zh":"咖啡店可能透過保持低租金並吸引常客來將回報最大化。"},{"en":"Investors maximise return when income rises and unnecessary costs fall.","zh":"當收入上升而不必要成本下降，投資者就能將回報最大化。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on getting the greatest possible gain.","zh":"這個短語重點是取得最大可能收益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"secure a huge home","meaning":"成功買入一間大屋","examples":[{"en":"An investor may secure a huge home in pristine condition.","zh":"投資者可能成功買入一間狀態嶄新完好的大屋。"},{"en":"To secure a huge home means to successfully buy or obtain a very large house.","zh":"secure a huge home 指成功買入或取得一間非常大的房子。"},{"en":"A family may secure a huge home after winning a competitive bidding process.","zh":"家庭可能在競爭性出價過程後成功買入一間大屋。"},{"en":"Securing a large property may feel impressive, but it is not always the best investment.","zh":"成功買入大型物業可能感覺令人印象深刻，但不一定是最佳投資。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on successfully obtaining the property.","zh":"這個短語重點是成功取得該物業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"pristine condition","meaning":"嶄新完好的狀態","examples":[{"en":"The house was in pristine condition.","zh":"該房子處於嶄新完好的狀態。"},{"en":"Pristine condition means perfectly clean, fresh, undamaged, and almost new.","zh":"pristine condition 指非常乾淨、新淨、沒有損壞，幾乎像新的狀態。"},{"en":"A second-hand textbook in pristine condition may look as if no one has used it.","zh":"狀態嶄新完好的二手教科書可能看起來像沒有人用過。"},{"en":"A property in pristine condition may need fewer repairs, but it may also cost more.","zh":"狀態完好的物業可能需要較少維修，但也可能價格較高。"},{"en":"The phrase describes excellent physical condition.","zh":"這個短語描述極佳實物狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"barely enough room to","meaning":"幾乎沒有足夠空間去……","examples":[{"en":"The flat had barely enough room to stretch out.","zh":"該小單位幾乎沒有足夠空間伸展身體。"},{"en":"Barely enough room to do something means just enough space to do it, with almost no extra space.","zh":"barely enough room to do something 指剛好有足夠空間做某事，幾乎沒有額外空間。"},{"en":"The classroom had barely enough room for thirty students and their bags.","zh":"課室幾乎沒有足夠空間容納三十名學生和他們的書包。"},{"en":"A tiny flat may be uncomfortable, but it can still be profitable if demand is high.","zh":"小單位可能不舒服，但如果需求高，仍可以有利可圖。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses limited space.","zh":"這個短語強調空間有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stretch out","meaning":"伸展身體","examples":[{"en":"The tiny flat had barely enough room to stretch out.","zh":"該細小單位幾乎沒有足夠空間伸展身體。"},{"en":"To stretch out means to extend your body, arms, or legs comfortably.","zh":"stretch out 指舒適地伸展身體、手臂或雙腿。"},{"en":"After sitting in class all morning, students may want to stretch out during lunch.","zh":"坐了一整個上午課後，學生可能想在午飯時伸展身體。"},{"en":"A room too small to stretch out in may feel cramped and uncomfortable.","zh":"太小而不能伸展身體的房間，可能令人感到狹窄不舒服。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests needing more physical space.","zh":"這個短語常暗示需要更多身體空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"return on your investment","meaning":"投資回報","examples":[{"en":"The tiny flat may give a better return on your investment.","zh":"該細小單位可能給你更好的投資回報。"},{"en":"Return on your investment is the profit or benefit you receive compared with the money you put in.","zh":"return on your investment 指你相對於投入金錢所得到的利潤或好處。"},{"en":"A course gives a good return on investment if it helps a student get a better job.","zh":"如果課程幫助學生找到更好工作，它就有良好投資回報。"},{"en":"A cheap flat with steady rent may give a better return than an expensive house.","zh":"有穩定租金的便宜單位，可能比昂貴大屋有更好回報。"},{"en":"The phrase measures gain against cost.","zh":"這個短語量度收益相對於成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the choice is a no-brainer","meaning":"選擇很明顯；不用多想","examples":[{"en":"The better investment choice is a no-brainer.","zh":"較好的投資選擇很明顯，不用多想。"},{"en":"The choice is a no-brainer means the correct decision is very obvious and requires little thought.","zh":"the choice is a no-brainer 指正確決定非常明顯，幾乎不用思考。"},{"en":"If one phone is cheaper, newer, and has a longer warranty, the choice is a no-brainer.","zh":"如果一部電話較便宜、較新，而且保養期更長，選擇就很明顯。"},{"en":"A clear difference in return can make one investment obviously better than another.","zh":"回報上的清楚差異可以令一項投資明顯優於另一項。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and means the answer is easy.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，意思是答案很容易。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"last of all","meaning":"最後","examples":[{"en":"Last of all, investors should do their homework.","zh":"最後，投資者應做足資料搜集。"},{"en":"Last of all introduces the final point in a list or explanation.","zh":"last of all 用來引入清單或解釋中的最後一點。"},{"en":"Last of all, students should check spelling before handing in an essay.","zh":"最後，學生交作文前應檢查串字。"},{"en":"The phrase helps organise advice by showing that the final recommendation is coming.","zh":"這個短語透過顯示最後建議即將出現來幫助組織意見。"},{"en":"It means “finally”.","zh":"它意思是「最後」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"do your homework","meaning":"做足資料搜集","examples":[{"en":"Investors must do their homework before buying property.","zh":"投資者買物業前必須做足資料搜集。"},{"en":"To do your homework means to research carefully before making a decision.","zh":"do your homework 指在作決定前仔細研究。"},{"en":"A student choosing a university should do her homework on fees, courses, and career support.","zh":"選大學的學生應做足資料搜集，了解學費、課程和就業支援。"},{"en":"Investors who do their homework can avoid bad locations and hidden costs.","zh":"做足資料搜集的投資者可以避開差地點和隱藏成本。"},{"en":"The phrase means preparing properly, not only completing school assignments.","zh":"這個短語指妥善準備，而不只是完成學校功課。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"get to know","meaning":"了解；熟悉","examples":[{"en":"You have to get to know the location before investing.","zh":"你投資前必須了解該地點。"},{"en":"To get to know something means to become familiar with it through time, research, or experience.","zh":"get to know something 指透過時間、研究或經驗逐漸熟悉某事。"},{"en":"A new teacher needs to get to know the class before choosing the best teaching method.","zh":"新老師需要了解班級，才選擇最佳教學方法。"},{"en":"Investors who know an area well can judge rent, demand, and risk more accurately.","zh":"熟悉某地區的投資者能更準確判斷租金、需求和風險。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests gradual understanding.","zh":"這個短語暗示逐步理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"invest in","meaning":"投資於……","examples":[{"en":"You need to know the location in which you are going to invest.","zh":"你需要了解自己將會投資於的地點。"},{"en":"To invest in something means to put money, time, or effort into it in the hope of future benefit.","zh":"invest in something 指把金錢、時間或努力投放到某事，希望日後有好處。"},{"en":"Parents may invest in English lessons because they believe language skills will help their child.","zh":"父母可能投資於英文課程，因為他們相信語言能力會幫到孩子。"},{"en":"Investing in a poor location can reduce rental income and future resale value.","zh":"投資於差地點可以降低租金收入和未來轉售價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes committing resources for expected return.","zh":"這個短語描述為預期回報而投入資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"look out for","meaning":"留意；尋找","examples":[{"en":"Investors should look out for areas earmarked for government investment.","zh":"投資者應留意被指定用於政府投資的地區。"},{"en":"To look out for something means to watch carefully for it because it may be useful, important, or risky.","zh":"look out for something 指仔細留意某事，因為它可能有用、重要或有風險。"},{"en":"Students should look out for keywords when reading exam questions.","zh":"學生閱讀考試題目時應留意關鍵字。"},{"en":"Investors look out for signs of future growth, such as new transport or renewal projects.","zh":"投資者留意未來增長跡象，例如新交通或重建項目。"},{"en":"The phrase means actively paying attention.","zh":"這個短語意思是主動留神。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"earmarked for","meaning":"被指定用於……","examples":[{"en":"Some areas are earmarked for government investment.","zh":"一些地區被指定用於政府投資。"},{"en":"Earmarked for something means officially set aside or chosen for a particular purpose.","zh":"earmarked for something 指被正式預留或選定作某特定用途。"},{"en":"A classroom may be earmarked for after-school homework support.","zh":"一間課室可能被指定用於課後功課支援。"},{"en":"Areas earmarked for investment may become more attractive as facilities improve.","zh":"被指定投資的地區可能隨設施改善而變得更吸引。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests planned future use.","zh":"這個短語暗示有計劃的未來用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"government investment","meaning":"政府投資","examples":[{"en":"Urban renewal areas may be earmarked for government investment.","zh":"市區重建地區可能被指定用於政府投資。"},{"en":"Government investment is money spent by the state on projects, infrastructure, or public services.","zh":"government investment 指國家花在項目、基礎設施或公共服務上的金錢。"},{"en":"A new railway station is an example of government investment in transport.","zh":"新鐵路站是政府在交通方面投資的例子。"},{"en":"Government investment can raise property values by improving roads, parks, schools, or safety.","zh":"政府投資可以透過改善道路、公園、學校或治安來提高物業價值。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to public money used for development.","zh":"這個短語指用於發展的公共資金。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"urban renewal areas","meaning":"市區重建地區","examples":[{"en":"Urban renewal areas are often attractive to investors.","zh":"市區重建地區通常對投資者有吸引力。"},{"en":"Urban renewal areas are city districts selected for improvement, rebuilding, or redevelopment.","zh":"urban renewal areas 指被選定作改善、重建或重新發展的城市地區。"},{"en":"An old neighbourhood may become an urban renewal area if buildings are unsafe or services are weak.","zh":"如果建築物不安全或服務薄弱，舊社區可能成為市區重建地區。"},{"en":"Renewal can raise property values because transport, shops, and public spaces may improve.","zh":"重建可以提高物業價值，因為交通、商店和公共空間可能改善。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to older city areas planned for upgrading.","zh":"這個短語指計劃升級的舊城市地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"attractive","meaning":"有吸引力的","examples":[{"en":"Urban renewal areas can be attractive to property investors.","zh":"市區重建地區可以對物業投資者有吸引力。"},{"en":"Attractive means appealing or likely to interest people because of benefits or qualities.","zh":"attractive 指因好處或特質而吸引人或可能令人感興趣。"},{"en":"A course with flexible hours and clear materials is attractive to busy adults.","zh":"有彈性時間和清楚教材的課程，對忙碌成年人有吸引力。"},{"en":"An area becomes attractive to investors when prices are low but future growth looks likely.","zh":"當某區價格低但未來增長看似可能，它就對投資者有吸引力。"},{"en":"The word describes practical appeal, not only physical beauty.","zh":"這個詞描述實際吸引力，而不只是外表美。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"house and rental prices","meaning":"樓價和租金","examples":[{"en":"House and rental prices may rise in urban renewal areas.","zh":"市區重建地區的樓價和租金可能上升。"},{"en":"House and rental prices are the prices of buying homes and the cost of renting them.","zh":"house and rental prices 指購買住宅的價格和租住住宅的成本。"},{"en":"House and rental prices often rise when a new railway line makes an area easier to reach.","zh":"當新鐵路線令某區更易到達，樓價和租金通常會上升。"},{"en":"Rising prices can increase investment returns but make housing less affordable for residents.","zh":"價格上升可以增加投資回報，但令居民較難負擔住房。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both sale prices and rent levels.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋售價和租金水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"low right now","meaning":"現在偏低","examples":[{"en":"Prices in renewal areas may be low right now.","zh":"重建地區的價格現在可能偏低。"},{"en":"Low right now means cheap or below expected levels at the present time.","zh":"low right now 指目前便宜或低於預期水平。"},{"en":"Air tickets may be low right now before the holiday season begins.","zh":"假期季節開始前，機票價格現在可能偏低。"},{"en":"Investors may buy when prices are low now and hope they rise later.","zh":"投資者可能在價格現在偏低時買入，並希望日後上升。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a temporary current condition.","zh":"這個短語強調暫時的當前狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"can be expected to","meaning":"可以預期會……","examples":[{"en":"House and rental prices can be expected to rise.","zh":"樓價和租金可以預期會上升。"},{"en":"Can be expected to means it is reasonable to predict that something will happen.","zh":"can be expected to 指合理預測某事將會發生。"},{"en":"If a new school opens nearby, local traffic can be expected to increase.","zh":"如果附近開設新學校，本地交通可以預期會增加。"},{"en":"Prices can be expected to rise when demand grows and supply stays limited.","zh":"當需求增長而供應保持有限，價格可以預期會上升。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a logical forecast.","zh":"這個短語引入合乎邏輯的預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rise","meaning":"上升","examples":[{"en":"Rental prices may rise in the not too distant future.","zh":"租金價格可能在不久的將來上升。"},{"en":"To rise means to increase or go up.","zh":"rise 指增加或向上。"},{"en":"Bus fares may rise if fuel costs become higher.","zh":"如果燃油成本變高，巴士車費可能上升。"},{"en":"When demand for flats increases, rents often rise.","zh":"當單位需求增加，租金通常會上升。"},{"en":"The word describes upward movement in price, number, or level.","zh":"這個詞描述價格、數字或水平向上移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in the not too distant future","meaning":"在不久的將來","examples":[{"en":"Prices may rise in the not too distant future.","zh":"價格可能在不久的將來上升。"},{"en":"In the not too distant future means fairly soon, though not immediately.","zh":"in the not too distant future 指相當快，但不是立即。"},{"en":"Students may need digital skills in the not too distant future even in ordinary office jobs.","zh":"在不久的將來，即使普通辦公室工作，學生也可能需要數碼技能。"},{"en":"Investors consider future change because today’s low price may not last long.","zh":"投資者考慮未來變化，因為今天的低價未必會長久。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a near future period.","zh":"這個短語指向較近的未來時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"range of local amenities","meaning":"本地配套設施的範圍","examples":[{"en":"The range of local amenities is an important factor.","zh":"本地配套設施的範圍是一個重要因素。"},{"en":"Range of local amenities means the variety of nearby facilities and services people can use.","zh":"range of local amenities 指附近可供人使用的設施和服務種類。"},{"en":"A flat near schools, clinics, parks, and supermarkets has a strong range of local amenities.","zh":"靠近學校、診所、公園和超級市場的單位，有良好的本地配套設施範圍。"},{"en":"Better amenities can attract tenants and support higher rent.","zh":"更好的配套設施可以吸引租客並支持較高租金。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the spread of useful facilities in an area.","zh":"這個短語描述某區有用設施的種類和分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"local amenities","meaning":"本地配套設施","examples":[{"en":"Local amenities can affect rental income.","zh":"本地配套設施可以影響租金收入。"},{"en":"Local amenities are useful nearby facilities such as shops, schools, parks, clinics, and transport links.","zh":"local amenities 指附近有用設施，例如商店、學校、公園、診所和交通連接。"},{"en":"Tenants often prefer flats with local amenities within walking distance.","zh":"租客通常偏好步行距離內有本地配套設施的單位。"},{"en":"Good amenities can make an area more convenient and attractive.","zh":"良好配套設施可以令地區更方便和吸引。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical neighbourhood facilities.","zh":"這個短語指實用社區設施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the state of","meaning":"……的狀況","examples":[{"en":"The state of the local economy is an important factor.","zh":"本地經濟的狀況是一個重要因素。"},{"en":"The state of something means its current condition or situation.","zh":"the state of something 指某事物目前的情況或狀態。"},{"en":"A doctor checks the state of a patient’s health before choosing treatment.","zh":"醫生在選擇治療前會檢查病人健康狀況。"},{"en":"The state of the local economy affects jobs, wages, spending, and rent demand.","zh":"本地經濟狀況影響職位、工資、消費和租屋需求。"},{"en":"The phrase asks how good or bad something currently is.","zh":"這個短語詢問某事目前好壞如何。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"local economy","meaning":"本地經濟","examples":[{"en":"The state of the local economy affects property investment.","zh":"本地經濟狀況影響物業投資。"},{"en":"The local economy is the jobs, businesses, wages, spending, and production in a particular area.","zh":"local economy 指某一地區的職位、企業、工資、消費和生產。"},{"en":"A town with new factories and growing shops has a stronger local economy.","zh":"有新工廠和增長中商店的城鎮，有較強本地經濟。"},{"en":"A weak local economy can reduce rent demand because fewer people can afford housing.","zh":"薄弱本地經濟可以降低租屋需求，因為較少人負擔得起住房。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to economic life in one area.","zh":"這個短語指某地區的經濟生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"important factors to consider","meaning":"需要考慮的重要因素","examples":[{"en":"Safety and local amenities are important factors to consider.","zh":"安全和本地配套設施是需要考慮的重要因素。"},{"en":"Important factors to consider are key points that should be included before making a decision.","zh":"important factors to consider 指作決定前應納入的關鍵重點。"},{"en":"When choosing a school, location, fees, teachers, and class size are important factors to consider.","zh":"選學校時，地點、學費、老師和班級大小都是需要考慮的重要因素。"},{"en":"Ignoring important factors can lead to poor decisions even if one feature looks attractive.","zh":"即使某個特徵看似吸引，忽視重要因素仍可能導致差決定。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds people to think carefully before choosing.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們選擇前要仔細思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"as the old saying goes","meaning":"正如俗語所說","examples":[{"en":"As the old saying goes, location is everything in property.","zh":"正如俗語所說，物業最重要的是地點。"},{"en":"As the old saying goes introduces a familiar traditional phrase or common piece of wisdom.","zh":"as the old saying goes 用來引入熟悉的傳統說法或常見智慧。"},{"en":"As the old saying goes, practice makes perfect.","zh":"正如俗語所說，熟能生巧。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to connect advice with widely recognised experience.","zh":"作者使用這個短語，把建議與廣為人知的經驗連起來。"},{"en":"It signals that the following words are a well-known saying.","zh":"它表示接下來的話是眾所周知的說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"location, location, location","meaning":"地點最重要","examples":[{"en":"The old saying “location, location, location” stresses the importance of place.","zh":"俗語 “location, location, location” 強調地點的重要性。"},{"en":"Location, location, location means that where a property is located is the most important factor in its value.","zh":"location, location, location 指物業所在位置是其價值中最重要因素。"},{"en":"A small flat near a train station may rent better than a larger flat in an inconvenient area.","zh":"近鐵路站的小單位，可能比不方便地區的大單位更容易出租。"},{"en":"Good location can raise demand, rental income, and resale value.","zh":"好地點可以提高需求、租金收入和轉售價值。"},{"en":"The repeated word emphasises that place matters above almost everything else.","zh":"重複這個詞強調地點幾乎比所有其他因素都重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"rental income","meaning":"租金收入","examples":[{"en":"A good location can maximise your rental income.","zh":"好地點可以將你的租金收入最大化。"},{"en":"Rental income is money received from tenants who pay to use a property.","zh":"rental income 指從租客支付使用物業費用中收到的金錢。"},{"en":"A landlord earns rental income when a tenant pays monthly rent for a flat.","zh":"當租客每月支付單位租金，業主就賺取租金收入。"},{"en":"Higher rental income helps investors cover mortgage payments and other costs.","zh":"較高租金收入幫助投資者支付按揭供款和其他成本。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to income from renting out property.","zh":"這個短語指出租物業所得收入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"answer the questions below","meaning":"回答以下問題","examples":[{"en":"Students answer the questions below using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞回答以下問題。"},{"en":"Answer the questions below means respond to the following questions in the test or exercise.","zh":"answer the questions below 指回答測驗或練習中接下來的問題。"},{"en":"Students should answer the questions below after locating the relevant lines in the passage.","zh":"學生應在文章中找到相關行數後回答以下問題。"},{"en":"Reading the instructions carefully prevents answers that break the word limit.","zh":"仔細閱讀指示可以避免答案違反字數限制。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should use no more than three words.","zh":"每個答案應使用不多於三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain one, two, or three words only.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案只能包含一個、兩個或三個詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “stock market instability”, it fits because it has three words.","zh":"如果答案是 “stock market instability”，它符合要求，因為有三個詞。"},{"en":"Writing extra words can make an otherwise correct answer wrong.","zh":"寫多餘字詞可以令本來正確的答案變錯。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語設定嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"for each answer","meaning":"每個答案","examples":[{"en":"Students should use no more than three words for each answer.","zh":"學生每個答案應使用不多於三個字。"},{"en":"For each answer means separately for every answer written.","zh":"for each answer 指對所寫的每個答案分別而言。"},{"en":"For each answer, students should check spelling and word limit.","zh":"每個答案，學生都應檢查串字和字數限制。"},{"en":"The phrase prevents students from applying the rule to only one question.","zh":"這個短語防止學生只把規則套用於其中一題。"},{"en":"It means the instruction applies every time.","zh":"它意思是指示每次都適用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"getting fed up with","meaning":"對……感到厭煩","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what investors are getting fed up with.","zh":"題目問投資者對甚麼感到厭煩。"},{"en":"Getting fed up with something means becoming annoyed or tired because it has continued too long.","zh":"getting fed up with something 指因某事持續太久而變得厭煩或疲累。"},{"en":"Students may get fed up with slow internet during online lessons.","zh":"學生可能對網課期間網速慢感到厭煩。"},{"en":"Investors getting fed up with unstable markets may look for property instead.","zh":"對不穩定市場感到厭煩的投資者，可能轉向物業。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and shows frustration.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，表示挫敗感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"involved in the sale of property","meaning":"從事物業買賣","examples":[{"en":"Janet Anderson is involved in the sale of property.","zh":"Janet Anderson 從事物業買賣。"},{"en":"Involved in the sale of property means taking part professionally in buying, selling, or arranging property deals.","zh":"involved in the sale of property 指專業參與買賣或安排物業交易。"},{"en":"A real-estate agent is involved in the sale of property when she shows flats to buyers.","zh":"地產代理帶買家看樓時，就是從事物業買賣。"},{"en":"People involved in property sales often understand market prices and buyer behaviour.","zh":"從事物業買賣的人通常理解市場價格和買家行為。"},{"en":"The phrase describes participation in real-estate business.","zh":"這個短語描述參與房地產業務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"another phrase used to describe","meaning":"用來描述……的另一個短語","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for another phrase used to describe this business.","zh":"題目要求找出用來描述這類業務的另一個短語。"},{"en":"Another phrase used to describe something means a different expression with a similar meaning.","zh":"another phrase used to describe something 指另一個意思相近的表達。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask for another phrase used to describe “very tired”, such as “exhausted”.","zh":"老師可能要求學生找出用來描述 “very tired” 的另一個短語，例如 “exhausted”。"},{"en":"This type of question tests whether students can connect meanings across the passage.","zh":"這類題目測試學生能否連接文章中的意思。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on alternative wording.","zh":"這個短語重點是替代表達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"this type of business","meaning":"這類業務","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to the business of selling property.","zh":"題目指的是買賣物業這類業務。"},{"en":"This type of business means this particular kind of commercial activity.","zh":"this type of business 指這一特定種類的商業活動。"},{"en":"Private tutoring is this type of business if the discussion is about paid education services.","zh":"如果討論的是收費教育服務，私人補習就是這類業務。"},{"en":"Naming the type of business helps readers know which industry the question is about.","zh":"命名業務類型幫助讀者知道題目關於哪個行業。"},{"en":"The phrase points back to a business already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指回已提及的業務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"one of the best ways to","meaning":"……的最佳方法之一","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for one of the best ways to identify a bargain.","zh":"題目問找出划算交易的最佳方法之一。"},{"en":"One of the best ways to do something means one of the most effective methods for achieving it.","zh":"one of the best ways to do something 指達成某事最有效的方法之一。"},{"en":"One of the best ways to improve speaking is to record yourself and listen again.","zh":"改善口語的最佳方法之一，是錄下自己說話並重新聆聽。"},{"en":"A method becomes one of the best when it works reliably in real situations.","zh":"當方法在真實情況中可靠有效，它就成為最佳方法之一。"},{"en":"The phrase recommends a strong practical strategy.","zh":"這個短語推薦強而實用的策略。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"property market","meaning":"物業市場","examples":[{"en":"Investors look for bargains in the property market.","zh":"投資者在物業市場尋找划算交易。"},{"en":"The property market is the system of buying, selling, renting, and pricing property.","zh":"property market 指買賣、租賃和定價物業的系統。"},{"en":"The property market may become active when interest rates fall.","zh":"當利率下降，物業市場可能變得活躍。"},{"en":"A weak property market can create bargains for buyers with enough cash.","zh":"疲弱物業市場可以為有足夠現金的買家創造划算交易。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to real-estate buying and selling conditions.","zh":"這個短語指房地產買賣情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"failure to meet","meaning":"未能支付……","examples":[{"en":"Failure to meet mortgage repayments can lead to repossession.","zh":"未能支付按揭供款可能導致物業被收回。"},{"en":"Failure to meet something means not managing to satisfy a duty, payment, rule, or requirement.","zh":"failure to meet something 指未能履行責任、付款、規則或要求。"},{"en":"Failure to meet a deadline can cause a student to lose marks.","zh":"未能趕上截止日期可以令學生失分。"},{"en":"Failure to meet mortgage payments can make a lender take back the property.","zh":"未能支付按揭供款可以令貸款人收回物業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes not fulfilling an obligation.","zh":"這個短語描述未履行義務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"cause your home to be repossessed","meaning":"導致你的住宅被收回","examples":[{"en":"Missing mortgage payments can cause your home to be repossessed.","zh":"錯過按揭供款可以導致你的住宅被收回。"},{"en":"To cause your home to be repossessed means to lead the lender to take back your property because payments were not made.","zh":"cause your home to be repossessed 指因未付款而導致貸款人收回你的物業。"},{"en":"A family may risk repossession if several mortgage payments are missed.","zh":"如果家庭錯過幾期按揭供款，可能面臨住宅被收回的風險。"},{"en":"Repossession happens because the home was used as security for the loan.","zh":"收回物業之所以發生，是因為住宅被用作貸款抵押。"},{"en":"The phrase warns about the serious result of failing to pay a mortgage.","zh":"這個短語警告未能償還按揭的嚴重後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"foreclosed properties","meaning":"被銀行收回的物業；銀主盤","examples":[{"en":"Banks want quick sales on foreclosed properties.","zh":"銀行希望快速出售銀主盤。"},{"en":"Foreclosed properties are properties taken back by lenders after owners fail to make mortgage payments.","zh":"foreclosed properties 指業主未能支付按揭後被貸款人收回的物業。"},{"en":"Investors may search for foreclosed properties because some are sold below market value.","zh":"投資者可能尋找銀主盤，因為有些以低於市值出售。"},{"en":"Banks often sell foreclosed properties quickly to recover money and reduce losses.","zh":"銀行通常快速出售銀主盤，以取回款項並減少損失。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to repossessed real estate.","zh":"這個短語指被收回的房地產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"developing networks","meaning":"建立人脈網絡","examples":[{"en":"Developing networks can help investors find bargains.","zh":"建立人脈網絡可以幫助投資者找到划算交易。"},{"en":"Developing networks means building relationships with people who can provide information, support, or opportunities.","zh":"developing networks 指與能提供資訊、支援或機會的人建立關係。"},{"en":"A graduate develops networks by attending career events and contacting alumni.","zh":"畢業生透過參加就業活動和聯絡校友建立人脈網絡。"},{"en":"Investors with strong networks may hear about property sales earlier than others.","zh":"有強大人脈的投資者可能比其他人更早聽到物業出售消息。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on creating useful connections.","zh":"這個短語重點是建立有用聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"error of judgement","meaning":"判斷錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Overborrowing is a serious error of judgement.","zh":"過度借貸是嚴重判斷錯誤。"},{"en":"An error of judgement is a mistake caused by poor decision-making rather than lack of information only.","zh":"error of judgement 指由差劣決策造成的錯誤，而不只是缺乏資訊。"},{"en":"Choosing an expensive course without checking the teacher’s quality can be an error of judgement.","zh":"沒有檢查老師質素就選擇昂貴課程，可能是判斷錯誤。"},{"en":"In investment, one error of judgement can create long-term financial pressure.","zh":"在投資中，一個判斷錯誤可以造成長期財務壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a bad decision.","zh":"這個短語描述差劣決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"according to Anderson","meaning":"根據 Anderson 所說","examples":[{"en":"According to Anderson, the biggest mistake is borrowing too much.","zh":"根據 Anderson 所說，最大錯誤是借貸過多。"},{"en":"According to Anderson means based on what Anderson says or believes.","zh":"according to Anderson 指根據 Anderson 所說或所相信的內容。"},{"en":"According to the coach, the team lost because it stopped communicating.","zh":"根據教練所說，球隊落敗是因為停止溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of an opinion or explanation.","zh":"這個短語指出觀點或解釋的來源。"},{"en":"It tells readers whose view is being reported.","zh":"它告訴讀者正在報告誰的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與文章資料一致","examples":[{"en":"The statements may agree with the information in the passage.","zh":"這些陳述可能與文章資料一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the information means match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the passage says banks want quick sales, the same statement agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說銀行想快速出售，同樣的陳述就與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students must check the text carefully before deciding an answer agrees.","zh":"學生必須仔細檢查文本，才決定答案是否一致。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in reading comprehension questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀理解題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"views of the writer","meaning":"作者的觀點","examples":[{"en":"Students judge whether a statement agrees with the views of the writer.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與作者的觀點一致。"},{"en":"Views of the writer means the opinions, attitudes, or claims expressed by the author.","zh":"views of the writer 指作者表達的意見、態度或主張。"},{"en":"A student should not use personal opinion when a question asks for the writer’s views.","zh":"當題目問作者觀點，學生不應使用個人意見。"},{"en":"Identifying the writer’s view requires reading tone, examples, and direct statements.","zh":"識別作者觀點需要閱讀語氣、例子和直接陳述。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on author opinion, not general fact only.","zh":"這個短語重點是作者意見，而不只是一般事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradicts the views of the writer","meaning":"與作者觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A “NO” answer means the statement contradicts the views of the writer.","zh":"“NO” 答案表示陳述與作者觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradicts the views of the writer means says the opposite of what the author believes or claims.","zh":"contradicts the views of the writer 指說出與作者相信或主張相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the writer says investors should avoid emotion, saying emotion is useful may contradict the writer’s views.","zh":"如果作者說投資者應避免情緒化，說情緒有用可能與作者觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students need clear textual evidence before choosing NO.","zh":"學生選 NO 前需要清楚文本證據。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in YES, NO, NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語用於 YES、NO、NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"“NOT GIVEN” means it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"“NOT GIVEN” 表示無法判斷作者怎樣想。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide confidently.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資訊作出有信心判斷。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions the investor’s age, it is impossible to say whether she is young or old.","zh":"如果文章從未提到投資者年齡，就無法判斷她年輕還是年老。"},{"en":"Students should choose NOT GIVEN when the text gives no evidence either way.","zh":"當文本兩邊都沒有證據，學生應選 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against guessing.","zh":"這個短語警告不要猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"demand larger deposits","meaning":"要求較高訂金／首期","examples":[{"en":"Banks may demand larger deposits from first-time property investors.","zh":"銀行可能要求首次物業投資者支付較高訂金或首期。"},{"en":"To demand larger deposits means to require more money to be paid at the start of a deal.","zh":"demand larger deposits 指要求在交易開始時支付更多金錢。"},{"en":"A landlord may demand a larger deposit from a tenant with no rental history.","zh":"業主可能要求沒有租住紀錄的租客支付較高訂金。"},{"en":"Larger deposits protect the lender or owner but increase the buyer’s financial burden.","zh":"較高訂金保護貸款人或業主，但增加買家的財務負擔。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stricter upfront payment requirements.","zh":"這個短語描述較嚴格的前期付款要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"personal financial risk","meaning":"個人財務風險","examples":[{"en":"A larger deposit may increase personal financial risk.","zh":"較高訂金可能增加個人財務風險。"},{"en":"Personal financial risk is the chance that an individual may lose money or face financial pressure.","zh":"personal financial risk 指個人可能損失金錢或面對財務壓力的機會。"},{"en":"A student takes personal financial risk if she borrows heavily for a course with uncertain job value.","zh":"如果學生為就業價值不確定的課程大額借貸，她就是承擔個人財務風險。"},{"en":"Bigger upfront payments increase risk because more personal money is exposed.","zh":"更大前期付款會增加風險，因為更多個人金錢暴露於風險中。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on money danger faced by one person.","zh":"這個短語重點是個人面對的金錢危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"take into consideration","meaning":"將……納入考慮","examples":[{"en":"Investors must take long-term costs into consideration.","zh":"投資者必須將長期成本納入考慮。"},{"en":"To take something into consideration means to include it when thinking or deciding.","zh":"take something into consideration 指在思考或決定時把某事納入。"},{"en":"A student should take travel time into consideration before joining an evening class.","zh":"學生報讀夜校課程前，應把交通時間納入考慮。"},{"en":"Considering all costs helps people avoid decisions that only look cheap at first.","zh":"考慮所有成本幫助人避免只在初看時便宜的決定。"},{"en":"The phrase means not ignoring an important factor.","zh":"這個短語意思是不要忽視重要因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"before purchasing","meaning":"在購買……之前","examples":[{"en":"Investors should consider long-term costs before purchasing a rental property.","zh":"投資者在購買出租物業之前應考慮長期成本。"},{"en":"Before purchasing means before buying something.","zh":"before purchasing 指在買入某物之前。"},{"en":"Customers should compare warranty terms before purchasing an expensive laptop.","zh":"顧客在購買昂貴手提電腦前，應比較保養條款。"},{"en":"Checking details before purchasing can prevent regret and hidden costs.","zh":"購買前檢查細節可以防止後悔和隱藏成本。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a step that should happen before buying.","zh":"這個短語設定買入前應發生的步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"hold a lot of money in reserve","meaning":"保留大量備用資金","examples":[{"en":"Investors may need to hold a lot of money in reserve.","zh":"投資者可能需要保留大量備用資金。"},{"en":"To hold a lot of money in reserve means to keep a large amount of spare cash for future needs.","zh":"hold a lot of money in reserve 指保留大量備用現金以應付未來需要。"},{"en":"A family may hold money in reserve before starting home renovation.","zh":"家庭開始家居裝修前，可能保留備用資金。"},{"en":"Reserve money helps investors handle repairs, empty rental periods, or higher interest rates.","zh":"備用資金幫助投資者應付維修、出租空置期或更高利率。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses financial preparation.","zh":"這個短語強調財務準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"tempted to pay more than they should","meaning":"被誘惑而支付過高價格","examples":[{"en":"Many investors are tempted to pay more than they should.","zh":"許多投資者被誘惑而支付過高價格。"},{"en":"Tempted to pay more than they should means strongly drawn to overpay, even though it is unwise.","zh":"tempted to pay more than they should 指被強烈吸引去多付錢，即使這樣不明智。"},{"en":"A fan may be tempted to pay more than she should for concert tickets.","zh":"粉絲可能被誘惑而為演唱會門票支付過高價格。"},{"en":"Competition and excitement can tempt buyers to ignore their budget.","zh":"競爭和興奮可以誘惑買家忽視預算。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that desire can defeat good judgement.","zh":"這個短語警告慾望可以打敗良好判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"investment properties","meaning":"投資物業","examples":[{"en":"Investors should not overpay for investment properties.","zh":"投資者不應為投資物業支付過高價格。"},{"en":"Investment properties are properties bought mainly to make money, not mainly to live in.","zh":"investment properties 指主要為賺錢而非主要自住而買入的物業。"},{"en":"A small flat bought for rental income is an investment property.","zh":"為租金收入而買入的小單位是投資物業。"},{"en":"The value of an investment property depends on rent, costs, location, and resale potential.","zh":"投資物業的價值取決於租金、成本、地點和轉售潛力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to property as a financial asset.","zh":"這個短語指作為財務資產的物業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"extremely high in general","meaning":"整體上極高","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether house prices are extremely high in general.","zh":"該陳述問樓價是否整體上極高。"},{"en":"Extremely high in general means very high overall, not only in one special case.","zh":"extremely high in general 指整體非常高，而不只是某個特殊個案。"},{"en":"Tuition fees may be extremely high in general if most schools charge far more than families can afford.","zh":"如果大多數學校收費遠超家庭負擔能力，學費可能整體上極高。"},{"en":"If prices are high only in a few districts, they may not be extremely high in general.","zh":"如果價格只在少數地區高，就未必是整體上極高。"},{"en":"The phrase asks about the broad situation, not one example.","zh":"這個短語問的是廣泛情況，而不是單一例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"urban renewal projects","meaning":"市區重建項目","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to urban renewal projects earmarked by the government.","zh":"題目提到由政府指定的市區重建項目。"},{"en":"Urban renewal projects are planned efforts to improve, rebuild, or redevelop older city areas.","zh":"urban renewal projects 指有計劃地改善、重建或重新發展舊城市地區的工作。"},{"en":"An urban renewal project may replace unsafe buildings with new housing and public spaces.","zh":"市區重建項目可能把危險建築物換成新住宅和公共空間。"},{"en":"These projects can raise local property values if transport and amenities improve.","zh":"如果交通和配套設施改善，這些項目可以提高本地物業價值。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised redevelopment in city districts.","zh":"這個短語指城市地區中有組織的重新發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"earmarked by the government","meaning":"由政府指定的","examples":[{"en":"Some projects may be earmarked by the government.","zh":"一些項目可能由政府指定。"},{"en":"Earmarked by the government means officially chosen or set aside by the state for a particular purpose.","zh":"earmarked by the government 指由國家正式選定或預留作某特定用途。"},{"en":"A piece of land may be earmarked by the government for a new hospital.","zh":"一幅土地可能由政府指定用作新醫院。"},{"en":"Government earmarking can signal future development and attract investor attention.","zh":"政府指定可以顯示未來發展，並吸引投資者注意。"},{"en":"The phrase shows official planning or designation.","zh":"這個短語顯示官方規劃或指定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 86 - Making a sound Investment Decision.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 87":[{"front":"burgeoning budget-holiday attraction","meaning":"正迅速興起的廉價旅行熱點","examples":[{"en":"Austria is becoming a burgeoning budget-holiday attraction.","zh":"奧地利正成為一個迅速興起的廉價旅行熱點。"},{"en":"A burgeoning budget-holiday attraction is a cheap travel destination that is growing quickly in popularity.","zh":"burgeoning budget-holiday attraction 指一個低成本旅行目的地正快速變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"A small seaside town may become a burgeoning budget-holiday attraction after cheap trains make it easy to reach.","zh":"當廉價火車令小海濱城鎮容易到達，它可能成為迅速興起的廉價旅行熱點。"},{"en":"When prices fall and more travellers hear about a place, it can quickly attract budget tourists.","zh":"當價格下降且更多旅客聽說某地，它就可以快速吸引預算有限的遊客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a low-cost destination is newly becoming fashionable.","zh":"當低成本目的地新近變得流行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"trips to Austria","meaning":"前往奧地利的旅行","examples":[{"en":"Trips to Austria are often associated with commerce or winter skiing.","zh":"前往奧地利的旅行常與商貿或冬季滑雪聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Trips to Austria means journeys or holidays made to Austria.","zh":"trips to Austria 指前往奧地利的旅程或假期。"},{"en":"A family may book trips to Austria in summer to hike, visit lakes, and enjoy mountain scenery.","zh":"家庭可能在夏天預訂前往奧地利的旅行，去行山、遊湖和欣賞山景。"},{"en":"The image of a destination can change when travellers discover new reasons to go there.","zh":"當旅客發現前往某地的新理由，目的地形象就可以改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing travel to a specific country.","zh":"討論前往特定國家的旅行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be commonly associated with","meaning":"通常與……聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"Austria is more commonly associated with winter skiing than summertime fun.","zh":"奧地利通常較多與冬季滑雪聯繫起來，而不是夏日樂趣。"},{"en":"Be commonly associated with something means people usually connect it with that thing.","zh":"be commonly associated with something 指人們通常把某事物與另一事物連繫起來。"},{"en":"Libraries are commonly associated with quiet study, books, and exams.","zh":"圖書館通常與安靜溫習、書本和考試聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Strong associations shape what people expect before they visit or buy something.","zh":"強烈聯想會塑造人們在到訪或購買前的期待。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a familiar public image.","zh":"描述熟悉的公眾形象時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"commerce","meaning":"商貿；商業活動","examples":[{"en":"Trips to Austria are often associated with commerce.","zh":"前往奧地利的旅行常與商貿聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Commerce means business activity, especially buying, selling, trade, and commercial exchange.","zh":"commerce 指商業活動，尤其是買賣、貿易和商業交流。"},{"en":"A city with many offices, banks, and trade fairs is strongly linked to commerce.","zh":"擁有許多辦公室、銀行和貿易展覽的城市，與商貿有強烈關係。"},{"en":"When commerce grows, hotels, transport, and restaurants may also benefit.","zh":"當商貿增長，酒店、交通和餐廳也可能受惠。"},{"en":"This word is useful when travel is connected with business rather than leisure.","zh":"當旅行與商業而不是休閒有關時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"winter skiing","meaning":"冬季滑雪","examples":[{"en":"Austria has long been associated with winter skiing.","zh":"奧地利長久以來與冬季滑雪聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Winter skiing means skiing on snow during the winter season.","zh":"winter skiing 指在冬季雪地上滑雪。"},{"en":"A family may travel to mountain resorts for winter skiing during school holidays.","zh":"家庭可能在學校假期前往山區度假村冬季滑雪。"},{"en":"Places famous for skiing may struggle to attract visitors in warmer months.","zh":"以滑雪聞名的地方，可能在較溫暖月份難以吸引遊客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing seasonal mountain tourism.","zh":"描述季節性山區旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"summertime fun and entertainment","meaning":"夏日樂趣和娛樂","examples":[{"en":"Austria is not usually associated with summertime fun and entertainment.","zh":"奧地利通常不會與夏日樂趣和娛樂聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Summertime fun and entertainment means enjoyable activities people do during the summer holidays.","zh":"summertime fun and entertainment 指人們在暑假期間進行的愉快活動。"},{"en":"Beach games, outdoor concerts, hiking trips, and boat rides can all be summertime fun and entertainment.","zh":"沙灘遊戲、戶外演唱會、行山旅行和划船都可以是夏日樂趣和娛樂。"},{"en":"A destination can attract new visitors when it shows that summer is also enjoyable there.","zh":"當目的地展示夏天同樣好玩，它就可以吸引新訪客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting summer leisure with winter tourism.","zh":"對比夏季消閒和冬季旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the last year or so","meaning":"在過去一年左右","examples":[{"en":"In the last year or so, a surprising trend has begun to develop.","zh":"在過去一年左右，一個令人意外的趨勢開始形成。"},{"en":"In the last year or so means during the past year or approximately that period.","zh":"in the last year or so 指在過去一年或大約這段時間內。"},{"en":"In the last year or so, many students have started using AI tools for revision.","zh":"在過去一年左右，許多學生開始使用人工智能工具溫習。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a recent change, but the timing is not perfectly exact.","zh":"這個短語表示近期變化，但時間不需要完全精確。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing a trend that has appeared quite recently.","zh":"描述相當近期出現的趨勢時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a surprising trend","meaning":"令人意外的趨勢","examples":[{"en":"A surprising trend has begun to develop in the British holiday market.","zh":"一個令人意外的趨勢已在英國旅行市場開始形成。"},{"en":"A surprising trend is a pattern of change that people did not expect.","zh":"surprising trend 指人們沒有預期到的變化模式。"},{"en":"A surprising trend may appear when teenagers start choosing libraries over shopping malls after school.","zh":"當青少年放學後開始選擇圖書館而不是商場，就可能出現令人意外的趨勢。"},{"en":"Trends feel surprising when they go against old habits or common assumptions.","zh":"當趨勢違反舊習慣或常見假設，就會令人意外。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a new pattern catches people off guard.","zh":"當新模式令人措手不及時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"begin to develop","meaning":"開始形成","examples":[{"en":"A new holiday trend has begun to develop.","zh":"一個新的旅行趨勢已開始形成。"},{"en":"Begin to develop means start to form, grow, or become noticeable.","zh":"begin to develop 指開始形成、增長或變得可見。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may begin to develop after several successful speaking practices.","zh":"學生在幾次成功口語練習後，信心可能開始形成。"},{"en":"Small early signs can later become a clear pattern if they continue.","zh":"小小早期跡象如果持續，後來可以變成清晰模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is just starting to grow.","zh":"當某事剛開始成長時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the British foreign holiday market","meaning":"英國海外旅行市場","examples":[{"en":"A new trend has appeared in the British foreign holiday market.","zh":"一個新趨勢已出現在英國海外旅行市場。"},{"en":"The British foreign holiday market is the business of selling overseas holidays to British travellers.","zh":"British foreign holiday market 指向英國旅客銷售海外假期的商業市場。"},{"en":"Travel companies study the British foreign holiday market to see where families want to go next.","zh":"旅遊公司研究英國海外旅行市場，以了解家庭下一步想去哪裏。"},{"en":"When demand changes, airlines and hotels may adjust prices and packages.","zh":"當需求改變，航空公司和酒店可能調整價格和套票。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing British tourists travelling abroad.","zh":"討論英國遊客出國旅行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tour operators","meaning":"旅行社營辦商；旅遊營辦商","examples":[{"en":"Tour operators have identified a new desire among holiday-goers.","zh":"旅行社營辦商發現度假人士之中有一種新需求。"},{"en":"Tour operators are companies that organise and sell holiday packages, transport, hotels, and activities.","zh":"tour operators 指組織和銷售旅行套票、交通、酒店和活動的公司。"},{"en":"A tour operator may arrange flights, hotel rooms, meals, and local guides for a family trip.","zh":"旅遊營辦商可能為家庭旅行安排航班、酒店房間、餐膳和本地導遊。"},{"en":"When travellers want something new, tour operators create packages to match that demand.","zh":"當旅客想要新東西，旅行社營辦商會創造套票來配合需求。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the business side of travel.","zh":"討論旅遊業商業面時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"identify a desire among","meaning":"發現……之中有一種需求","examples":[{"en":"Tour operators have identified a desire among holiday-goers to try new destinations.","zh":"旅行社營辦商發現度假人士之中有嘗試新目的地的需求。"},{"en":"Identify a desire among a group means notice that people in that group want something.","zh":"identify a desire among a group 指注意到某群人想要某事物。"},{"en":"A school may identify a desire among students for more speaking practice.","zh":"學校可能發現學生之中有更多口語練習的需求。"},{"en":"Once a desire is identified, organisations can design services to meet it.","zh":"一旦需求被發現，組織就可以設計服務來滿足它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when businesses or institutions detect demand.","zh":"當企業或機構察覺需求時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"holiday-goers","meaning":"旅行人士；度假人士","examples":[{"en":"Holiday-goers are looking for less crowded destinations.","zh":"度假人士正在尋找較少人群的目的地。"},{"en":"Holiday-goers are people who travel for holidays or leisure.","zh":"holiday-goers 指為假期或休閒而旅行的人。"},{"en":"Holiday-goers may choose quieter towns if famous beaches become too crowded.","zh":"如果著名海灘變得太擠迫，度假人士可能選擇較安靜城鎮。"},{"en":"Their preferences affect flights, hotels, restaurants, and local tourism businesses.","zh":"他們的偏好會影響航班、酒店、餐廳和本地旅遊業。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing people who travel for pleasure.","zh":"討論為娛樂而旅行的人時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"budget travellers","meaning":"預算有限的旅客","examples":[{"en":"Even budget travellers are looking for new destinations.","zh":"即使預算有限的旅客也在尋找新目的地。"},{"en":"Budget travellers are people who try to travel without spending too much money.","zh":"budget travellers 指嘗試不花太多錢旅行的人。"},{"en":"Students are often budget travellers because they compare hostels, cheap flights, and meal costs carefully.","zh":"學生常是預算有限的旅客，因為他們仔細比較青年旅舍、廉航和餐費。"},{"en":"When cheap options become available, budget travellers may explore places once seen as expensive.","zh":"當廉價選項出現，預算有限的旅客可能探索曾被視為昂貴的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing low-cost tourism.","zh":"討論低成本旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"package-holiday devotees","meaning":"套票旅行愛好者","examples":[{"en":"Package-holiday devotees are beginning to broaden their horizons.","zh":"套票旅行愛好者正開始擴闊眼界。"},{"en":"Package-holiday devotees are people who strongly prefer holidays where flights, hotels, and services are sold together.","zh":"package-holiday devotees 指非常偏好航班、酒店和服務合併出售的旅行方式的人。"},{"en":"A busy parent may become a package-holiday devotee because one booking solves most travel details.","zh":"忙碌家長可能成為套票旅行愛好者，因為一次預訂能解決大部分旅行細節。"},{"en":"Such travellers may still want variety if the same beach trips become boring.","zh":"如果相同海灘旅行變得沉悶，這類旅客仍可能想要變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing loyal users of package holidays.","zh":"描述套票旅行的忠實使用者時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"broaden their horizons","meaning":"擴闊眼界","examples":[{"en":"Travellers want to broaden their horizons beyond traditional beach resorts.","zh":"旅客想把眼界擴闊到傳統海灘度假村以外。"},{"en":"To broaden their horizons means to gain wider experience, knowledge, or understanding.","zh":"broaden their horizons 指獲得更廣泛的經驗、知識或理解。"},{"en":"Students can broaden their horizons by joining exchange programmes or volunteering in new communities.","zh":"學生可以透過參加交流計劃或在新社區做義工來擴闊眼界。"},{"en":"New experiences help people see that their usual choices are not the only possibilities.","zh":"新體驗幫助人看見慣常選擇不是唯一可能。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when people expand their view of life.","zh":"當人們擴展人生視野時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"somewhat beyond","meaning":"稍為超越……","examples":[{"en":"Holiday-goers are looking somewhat beyond Spain and the Canary Islands.","zh":"度假人士正在稍為超越西班牙和加那利群島尋找選擇。"},{"en":"Somewhat beyond means a little further than the usual limit or familiar choice.","zh":"somewhat beyond 指稍微超出慣常界限或熟悉選擇。"},{"en":"A student may read somewhat beyond the textbook by looking at simple news articles.","zh":"學生可能透過閱讀簡單新聞文章，稍為超越課本。"},{"en":"Small steps beyond the familiar can lead to wider confidence and curiosity.","zh":"稍微走出熟悉範圍，可以帶來更大信心和好奇心。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when change is moderate, not extreme.","zh":"當變化溫和而非極端時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"traditional haunts","meaning":"傳統常去之地","examples":[{"en":"Spain and the Canary Islands are traditional haunts for British holiday-goers.","zh":"西班牙和加那利群島是英國度假人士的傳統常去之地。"},{"en":"Traditional haunts are places people have regularly visited for a long time.","zh":"traditional haunts 指人們長時間以來經常到訪的地方。"},{"en":"A café near school may become a traditional haunt for students after exams.","zh":"學校附近的咖啡店可能在考試後成為學生的傳統常去之地。"},{"en":"When people tire of their usual haunts, they may search for fresh alternatives.","zh":"當人們厭倦慣常去處，他們可能尋找新替代選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing familiar favourite places.","zh":"描述熟悉而常去的喜愛地方時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the Canary Islands","meaning":"加那利群島","examples":[{"en":"The Canary Islands have long been a traditional holiday destination.","zh":"加那利群島長久以來是傳統旅行目的地。"},{"en":"The Canary Islands are a group of Spanish islands off the northwest coast of Africa.","zh":"Canary Islands 指位於非洲西北海岸外的一組西班牙島嶼。"},{"en":"Many tourists visit the Canary Islands for warm weather, beaches, and resort hotels.","zh":"許多遊客到加那利群島享受溫暖天氣、海灘和度假酒店。"},{"en":"A destination can become traditional when generations of travellers return there regularly.","zh":"當幾代旅客定期回到某地，它就可以成為傳統目的地。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing popular European holiday places.","zh":"討論歐洲熱門旅行地點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"less crowded destinations","meaning":"較少人群的目的地","examples":[{"en":"Travellers are looking for new, less crowded destinations.","zh":"旅客正在尋找新的、較少人群的目的地。"},{"en":"Less crowded destinations are places with fewer tourists or visitors.","zh":"less crowded destinations 指遊客或訪客較少的地方。"},{"en":"A family may choose a quiet lake town instead of a crowded theme park.","zh":"家庭可能選擇安靜湖邊小鎮，而不是擁擠主題公園。"},{"en":"Less crowded places can feel calmer, cheaper, and more authentic.","zh":"較少人群的地方可以感覺更平靜、更便宜、更真實。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when travellers want space and comfort.","zh":"當旅客想要空間和舒適時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"enter the Austrian package holiday","meaning":"奧地利套票旅行登場","examples":[{"en":"Enter the Austrian package holiday, the answer to the tour operators’ prayers.","zh":"奧地利套票旅行登場，成為旅行社營辦商夢寐以求的解決方法。"},{"en":"Enter the Austrian package holiday means the Austrian package holiday appears as the new solution or option.","zh":"enter the Austrian package holiday 指奧地利套票旅行作為新解決方法或選項出現。"},{"en":"After years of boring school trips, enter the outdoor adventure camp, a fresh choice for students.","zh":"在多年沉悶學校旅行後，戶外歷險營登場，成為學生的新選擇。"},{"en":"This dramatic phrase introduces something as if it is arriving on a stage.","zh":"這個戲劇化短語把某事物介紹得像在舞台上登場。"},{"en":"It is useful when a new option suddenly solves an old problem.","zh":"當新選項突然解決舊問題時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the answer to someone’s prayers","meaning":"某人夢寐以求的解決方法","examples":[{"en":"The Austrian package holiday was the answer to the tour operators’ prayers.","zh":"奧地利套票旅行是旅行社營辦商夢寐以求的解決方法。"},{"en":"The answer to someone’s prayers means exactly the solution someone has been hoping for.","zh":"answer to someone’s prayers 指正是某人一直希望得到的解決方法。"},{"en":"A new bus route may be the answer to commuters’ prayers if they used to walk far to work.","zh":"如果通勤者以前要走很遠上班，新巴士路線可能是他們夢寐以求的解決方法。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when a solution arrives after frustration or difficulty.","zh":"當解決方法在挫折或困難後出現，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something feels perfectly helpful.","zh":"當某事感覺非常有幫助時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"for all its natural beauty","meaning":"儘管有自然美景","examples":[{"en":"For all its natural beauty, Austria traditionally attracted tourists mainly in winter.","zh":"儘管有自然美景，奧地利傳統上主要在冬季吸引遊客。"},{"en":"For all its natural beauty means although it has great natural beauty.","zh":"for all its natural beauty 指雖然它擁有出色自然美景。"},{"en":"For all its beautiful parks, a city may still fail to attract visitors if transport is poor.","zh":"儘管一個城市有美麗公園，如果交通差，它仍可能未能吸引遊客。"},{"en":"This phrase creates contrast between a positive quality and an unexpected limitation.","zh":"這個短語在正面特質和意外限制之間建立對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when something good does not produce the expected result.","zh":"當好特質沒有產生預期結果時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fare well in","meaning":"在……方面表現良好","examples":[{"en":"Austria has traditionally fared well in attracting tourists during the ski season.","zh":"奧地利傳統上在滑雪季節吸引遊客方面表現良好。"},{"en":"Fare well in something means perform successfully in that area.","zh":"fare well in something 指在某方面表現成功。"},{"en":"A student may fare well in speaking exams but struggle in writing tasks.","zh":"學生可能在口試方面表現良好，但在寫作任務上吃力。"},{"en":"A place fares well when its strengths match what people want at that time.","zh":"當一個地方的強項配合人們當時想要的東西，它就表現良好。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing performance in a particular area.","zh":"比較某方面表現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"attract tourists","meaning":"吸引遊客","examples":[{"en":"Austria attracts many tourists during the winter ski season.","zh":"奧地利在冬季滑雪季節吸引許多遊客。"},{"en":"To attract tourists means to make visitors want to come to a place.","zh":"attract tourists 指令訪客想來某地方。"},{"en":"A town may attract tourists with night markets, museums, clean beaches, and good transport.","zh":"城鎮可能透過夜市、博物館、潔淨海灘和良好交通吸引遊客。"},{"en":"Tourist attractions can create jobs for hotels, restaurants, guides, and shops.","zh":"旅遊吸引力可以為酒店、餐廳、導遊和商店創造工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing why people visit a destination.","zh":"討論人們為何到訪目的地時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"during the winter ski season","meaning":"在冬季滑雪季節","examples":[{"en":"Austria traditionally attracted tourists during the winter ski season.","zh":"奧地利傳統上在冬季滑雪季節吸引遊客。"},{"en":"During the winter ski season means in the period when snow conditions are suitable for skiing.","zh":"during the winter ski season 指雪況適合滑雪的時期。"},{"en":"Mountain hotels may be fully booked during the winter ski season.","zh":"山區酒店在冬季滑雪季節可能被完全訂滿。"},{"en":"Seasonal demand can raise prices when many visitors arrive at the same time.","zh":"當許多遊客同時到來，季節性需求可以推高價格。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when tourism depends on snow and winter sports.","zh":"當旅遊依賴雪和冬季運動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"foreign tourists especially","meaning":"尤其是外國遊客","examples":[{"en":"During the summer, foreign tourists especially neglected Austria’s mountain scenery.","zh":"在夏季，尤其是外國遊客忽視奧地利的山區景色。"},{"en":"Foreign tourists especially means visitors from other countries in particular.","zh":"foreign tourists especially 指特別是來自其他國家的遊客。"},{"en":"Foreign tourists especially may avoid a town if signs, transport, and websites are not in familiar languages.","zh":"如果標誌、交通和網站沒有熟悉語言，尤其是外國遊客可能避開某城鎮。"},{"en":"When foreign tourists overlook a place, local businesses may lose summer income.","zh":"當外國遊客忽視某地，本地企業可能失去夏季收入。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one visitor group is more affected than others.","zh":"當某一訪客群體比其他群體更受影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lush mountain meadows","meaning":"翠綠的山間草甸","examples":[{"en":"Austria has lush mountain meadows, fresh air and wildlife.","zh":"奧地利擁有翠綠的山間草甸、清新空氣和野生動物。"},{"en":"Lush mountain meadows are green, healthy grasslands high in the mountains.","zh":"lush mountain meadows 指山上的翠綠、茂盛草地。"},{"en":"Visitors may walk through lush mountain meadows full of flowers during a summer hike.","zh":"遊客在夏季遠足時，可能走過滿是花朵的翠綠山間草甸。"},{"en":"Beautiful landscapes can attract travellers who want nature rather than beaches.","zh":"美麗景觀可以吸引想要自然環境而非海灘的旅客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing rich mountain scenery.","zh":"描述豐富山區景色時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fresh air and wildlife","meaning":"清新空氣和野生動物","examples":[{"en":"Tourists often neglect Austria’s fresh air and wildlife in summer.","zh":"遊客常在夏季忽視奧地利的清新空氣和野生動物。"},{"en":"Fresh air and wildlife means clean outdoor air and animals living naturally in the area.","zh":"fresh air and wildlife 指潔淨戶外空氣和在該地自然生活的動物。"},{"en":"Families may visit a country park for fresh air and wildlife after a stressful week in the city.","zh":"一星期城市壓力後，家庭可能去郊野公園享受清新空氣和野生動物。"},{"en":"Natural attractions can make holidays healthier and more active.","zh":"自然景點可以令假期更健康和更活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing outdoor appeal.","zh":"描述戶外吸引力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in favour of","meaning":"轉而選擇；寧願選擇","examples":[{"en":"Tourists neglected Austria in favour of cheap beach holidays.","zh":"遊客忽視奧地利，轉而選擇廉價海灘旅行。"},{"en":"In favour of means choosing one thing instead of another.","zh":"in favour of 指選擇一件事而不是另一件事。"},{"en":"A student may skip a party in favour of resting before an important exam.","zh":"學生可能不去派對，轉而選擇在重要考試前休息。"},{"en":"This phrase shows preference and often implies that another option is rejected.","zh":"這個短語顯示偏好，並常暗示另一個選項被放棄。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing competing choices.","zh":"比較互相競爭的選擇時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cheap beach holidays","meaning":"廉價海灘旅行","examples":[{"en":"Many tourists preferred cheap beach holidays to summer trips in Austria.","zh":"許多遊客較喜歡廉價海灘旅行，而不是夏季奧地利旅行。"},{"en":"Cheap beach holidays are low-cost vacations focused on sun, sea, sand, and simple relaxation.","zh":"cheap beach holidays 指以陽光、大海、沙灘和簡單放鬆為主的低成本假期。"},{"en":"Students may choose cheap beach holidays because flights and hotels are included in one package.","zh":"學生可能選擇廉價海灘旅行，因為航班和酒店包括在一個套票中。"},{"en":"Low prices can attract crowds even if the experience becomes repetitive.","zh":"即使體驗變得重複，低價仍可以吸引人群。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing budget seaside tourism.","zh":"描述預算有限的海濱旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"drench themselves in","meaning":"讓自己浸滿；沉浸於","examples":[{"en":"Some tourists drench themselves in drink and suntan.","zh":"有些遊客讓自己沉浸於酒精和日曬之中。"},{"en":"To drench themselves in something means to cover themselves heavily in it or indulge in it excessively.","zh":"drench themselves in something 指大量覆蓋自己於某物之中，或過度沉溺其中。"},{"en":"On holiday, some people drench themselves in perfume before going out at night.","zh":"度假時，有些人晚上外出前會噴很多香水，好像讓自己浸滿其中。"},{"en":"The phrase can sound humorous or critical when people overdo something.","zh":"當人們做得過火，這個短語可以帶幽默或批評意味。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing excessive enjoyment or exposure.","zh":"描述過度享受或暴露時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in equal measures of","meaning":"同等程度地","examples":[{"en":"Tourists drenched themselves in equal measures of drink and suntan.","zh":"遊客同等程度地沉浸於酒精和日曬之中。"},{"en":"In equal measures of A and B means with the same amount or degree of both things.","zh":"in equal measures of A and B 指 A 和 B 兩者有相同數量或程度。"},{"en":"A good teacher needs equal measures of patience and firmness.","zh":"好老師需要同等程度的耐性和堅定。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two elements are present to a similar extent.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個元素以相似程度存在。"},{"en":"It is useful when balancing two qualities or behaviours.","zh":"平衡兩種特質或行為時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"for a week or so","meaning":"大約一星期","examples":[{"en":"Some tourists spend a week or so on cheap beach holidays.","zh":"有些遊客花大約一星期在廉價海灘旅行上。"},{"en":"For a week or so means for about one week, not exactly one week.","zh":"for a week or so 指大約一星期，而不一定剛好一星期。"},{"en":"A student may revise intensely for a week or so before a major exam.","zh":"學生可能在重要考試前密集溫習大約一星期。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate time without sounding too exact.","zh":"這個短語給出大約時間，而不顯得太精確。"},{"en":"It is useful when the duration is rough but clear enough.","zh":"當持續時間是粗略但足夠清楚時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"return home strawberry-red","meaning":"曬得通紅後回家","examples":[{"en":"Some beach tourists return home strawberry-red after too much sun.","zh":"有些海灘遊客曬太多太陽後，曬得通紅回家。"},{"en":"Return home strawberry-red means go back home with skin made very red by sunburn.","zh":"return home strawberry-red 指因曬傷而皮膚很紅地回家。"},{"en":"A child may return home strawberry-red after forgetting sunscreen at the beach.","zh":"孩子在海灘忘記塗防曬後，可能曬得通紅回家。"},{"en":"Too much sun can turn a relaxing holiday into an uncomfortable one.","zh":"過量日曬可以把放鬆假期變成不舒服的經歷。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when humorously describing severe sunburn.","zh":"幽默地描述嚴重曬傷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cultural experience","meaning":"文化體驗","examples":[{"en":"The writer suggests that some beach holidays offer little cultural experience.","zh":"作者暗示有些海灘旅行提供很少文化體驗。"},{"en":"Cultural experience means contact with a place’s history, customs, food, language, art, or daily life.","zh":"cultural experience 指接觸某地的歷史、習俗、食物、語言、藝術或日常生活。"},{"en":"A student gains cultural experience by staying with a host family rather than only visiting shopping malls.","zh":"學生住在寄宿家庭而不只是逛商場，可以獲得文化體驗。"},{"en":"Holidays feel richer when travellers learn something about local people and traditions.","zh":"當旅客了解本地人和傳統，假期會感覺更豐富。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when travel involves learning, not just relaxing.","zh":"當旅行涉及學習而不只是放鬆時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have something to tell someone about","meaning":"有……可以跟某人講述","examples":[{"en":"They had very little cultural experience to tell the neighbours about.","zh":"他們幾乎沒有甚麼文化體驗可以跟鄰居講述。"},{"en":"Have something to tell someone about means have an interesting experience or story to share.","zh":"have something to tell someone about 指有有趣經歷或故事可以分享。"},{"en":"After volunteering at a farm, a student had plenty to tell classmates about.","zh":"在農場做義工後，學生有很多事情可以跟同學講。"},{"en":"Memorable experiences give people stories that ordinary routines do not provide.","zh":"難忘體驗給人故事，而普通日常生活未必能提供。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when travel creates shareable memories.","zh":"當旅行創造可分享回憶時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"how do I put this politely","meaning":"我該怎樣禮貌地說呢","examples":[{"en":"The writer says, “How do I put this politely?” before using a euphemism.","zh":"作者在使用委婉語前說：「我該怎樣禮貌地說呢？」"},{"en":"How do I put this politely means the speaker wants to say something awkward in a softer way.","zh":"how do I put this politely 指說話者想用較柔和方式說出尷尬事情。"},{"en":"A teacher might say, “How do I put this politely? Your essay needs much clearer examples.”","zh":"老師可能說：「我該怎樣禮貌地說呢？你的文章需要更清晰例子。」"},{"en":"The phrase prepares listeners for criticism, humour, or a sensitive comment.","zh":"這個短語讓聽者準備接受批評、幽默或敏感評論。"},{"en":"It is useful when someone wants to avoid sounding too rude.","zh":"當某人想避免聽起來太無禮時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"posterior","meaning":"臀部；屁股","examples":[{"en":"The writer humorously refers to a person’s posterior.","zh":"作者幽默地提到一個人的臀部。"},{"en":"Posterior is a polite or formal word for the part of the body someone sits on.","zh":"posterior 是指人坐下時使用的身體部位的較禮貌或正式說法。"},{"en":"A doctor may use the word posterior instead of a more casual word in a medical note.","zh":"醫生可能在醫療紀錄中使用 posterior，而不是較口語的詞。"},{"en":"Formal words can make embarrassing topics sound less direct.","zh":"正式詞語可以令尷尬話題聽起來較不直接。"},{"en":"This word is useful when humorous politeness is needed.","zh":"當需要幽默而禮貌地表達時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cheap and cheerful","meaning":"價廉但令人開心的","examples":[{"en":"The cheap and cheerful package holiday has often had narrow horizons.","zh":"價廉但令人開心的套票旅行常常選擇有限。"},{"en":"Cheap and cheerful means inexpensive but still pleasant, simple, or enjoyable.","zh":"cheap and cheerful 指便宜但仍令人愉快、簡單或開心。"},{"en":"A cheap and cheerful café may serve basic food quickly with friendly service.","zh":"價廉但令人開心的咖啡店可能快速提供基本食物和友善服務。"},{"en":"Something cheap and cheerful may satisfy simple needs but lack depth or variety.","zh":"價廉但令人開心的東西可能滿足簡單需要，但缺乏深度或變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when low cost is positive but not luxurious.","zh":"當低價是正面但不是豪華時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"package holiday","meaning":"套票旅行","examples":[{"en":"The package holiday has traditionally offered limited destination choices.","zh":"套票旅行傳統上提供有限的目的地選擇。"},{"en":"A package holiday is a holiday sold as one deal including things such as flights, hotels, and sometimes meals.","zh":"package holiday 指以一個方案出售的假期，包括航班、酒店，有時還包括餐膳。"},{"en":"A busy family may choose a package holiday because it saves planning time.","zh":"忙碌家庭可能選擇套票旅行，因為它節省規劃時間。"},{"en":"Package holidays can be convenient, but they may feel predictable if destinations are always similar.","zh":"套票旅行可以方便，但如果目的地總是相似，就可能感覺可預測。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when travel services are bundled together.","zh":"當旅遊服務被捆綁出售時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"narrow horizons","meaning":"視野狹窄；選擇有限","examples":[{"en":"The writer says package holidays have always had narrow horizons.","zh":"作者說套票旅行一直視野狹窄。"},{"en":"Narrow horizons means limited choices, experience, imagination, or understanding.","zh":"narrow horizons 指選擇、經驗、想像力或理解有限。"},{"en":"A student has narrow horizons if they only read one type of book and refuse all others.","zh":"如果學生只讀一類書並拒絕其他所有書，他就視野狹窄。"},{"en":"Narrow choices can make people bored and stop them discovering better possibilities.","zh":"有限選擇會令人沉悶，並阻止人發現更好可能性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when criticising limited vision or variety.","zh":"批評視野或變化有限時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"members of the ordinary public","meaning":"普羅大眾","examples":[{"en":"Members of the ordinary public were tired of predictable beach holidays.","zh":"普羅大眾已厭倦可預測的海灘旅行。"},{"en":"Members of the ordinary public are regular people, not experts, officials, celebrities, or the very rich.","zh":"members of the ordinary public 指普通人，而不是專家、官員、名人或超級富豪。"},{"en":"Members of the ordinary public may complain if train fares rise too quickly.","zh":"如果火車票價上升太快，普羅大眾可能投訴。"},{"en":"Their choices matter because they make up most customers in many markets.","zh":"他們的選擇很重要，因為他們構成許多市場中的大多數顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about normal people as a group.","zh":"把普通人作為群體討論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be traumatised by","meaning":"因……而受創；受夠了……","examples":[{"en":"Some travellers were traumatised by years of meaningless beach holidays.","zh":"有些旅客因多年毫無意義的海灘旅行而受夠了。"},{"en":"Be traumatised by something means be deeply upset or affected by a bad experience, often exaggerated here for humour.","zh":"be traumatised by something 指因糟糕經歷而深受困擾或影響，這裏常帶幽默誇張。"},{"en":"A student may feel traumatised by a terrible exam, though friends may use the word jokingly.","zh":"學生可能覺得被一場糟糕考試「傷害」，雖然朋友可能只是開玩笑地用這個詞。"},{"en":"The phrase can be serious, but in light writing it may strongly exaggerate boredom or dislike.","zh":"這個短語可以很嚴肅，但在輕鬆文章中可能強烈誇張沉悶或厭惡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an experience leaves a strong negative impression.","zh":"當經歷留下強烈負面印象時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"years spent holidaying","meaning":"多年來旅行的經歷","examples":[{"en":"Years spent holidaying on similar beaches made travellers want a change.","zh":"多年來在相似海灘旅行的經歷，令旅客想要改變。"},{"en":"Years spent holidaying means many years used for taking holidays in a particular way or place.","zh":"years spent holidaying 指多年用於以某種方式或在某地方度假。"},{"en":"Years spent eating at the same restaurant may make a family want to try somewhere new.","zh":"多年在同一間餐廳吃飯，可能令家庭想嘗試新地方。"},{"en":"Repeated experiences can become boring when they no longer feel fresh.","zh":"當重複經歷不再新鮮，就可能變得沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when long repetition creates a desire for change.","zh":"當長期重複創造改變欲望時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a meaningless beach","meaning":"毫無意義的海灘","examples":[{"en":"The writer describes the traditional package holiday as a meaningless beach somewhere in Malaga.","zh":"作者把傳統套票旅行描述為 Malaga 某處毫無意義的海灘。"},{"en":"A meaningless beach means a beach holiday that feels empty, repetitive, or without cultural value.","zh":"meaningless beach 指感覺空洞、重複或缺乏文化價值的海灘假期。"},{"en":"A traveller may call a resort meaningless if every day is only sunbathing, drinking, and shopping.","zh":"如果每天只是日光浴、飲酒和購物，旅客可能說某度假村毫無意義。"},{"en":"Holidays can feel meaningless when they create no memory, learning, or real connection with a place.","zh":"當假期沒有創造回憶、學習或與地方的真實連繫，就可能感覺毫無意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when criticising shallow tourism.","zh":"批評膚淺旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have sand coming out of their ears","meaning":"對海灘旅行厭倦透頂","examples":[{"en":"After many beach holidays, travellers have sand coming out of their ears.","zh":"經歷許多海灘旅行後，旅客已對海灘旅行厭倦透頂。"},{"en":"Have sand coming out of their ears is a humorous way to say people are completely tired of beach holidays.","zh":"have sand coming out of their ears 是幽默說法，表示人們完全厭倦海灘假期。"},{"en":"After a week of worksheets, students may joke that they have grammar coming out of their ears.","zh":"做了一星期工作紙後，學生可能開玩笑說自己滿腦子都是文法。"},{"en":"The phrase exaggerates repeated exposure until it feels excessive.","zh":"這個短語誇張地描述重複接觸某事，直到感覺過量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone has had far too much of the same thing.","zh":"當某人已經受夠同一件事時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at this stage","meaning":"到這個階段","examples":[{"en":"At this stage, many travellers wanted a different kind of holiday.","zh":"到這個階段，許多旅客想要另一種旅行。"},{"en":"At this stage means at this point in a process, situation, or story.","zh":"at this stage 指在某過程、情況或故事的這一刻。"},{"en":"At this stage of revision, students should practise full papers rather than only read notes.","zh":"到溫習這個階段，學生應練習整份試卷，而不只是讀筆記。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show how needs change as time passes.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示需要如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing a turning point in development.","zh":"描述發展中的轉捩點時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"clearly a change was needed","meaning":"顯然需要改變","examples":[{"en":"Clearly a change was needed in the package-holiday market.","zh":"套票旅行市場顯然需要改變。"},{"en":"Clearly a change was needed means it was obvious that the old situation could not continue well.","zh":"clearly a change was needed 指舊情況明顯不能良好持續。"},{"en":"If students keep failing the same grammar point, clearly a change is needed in teaching method.","zh":"如果學生一直在同一文法點失分，教學方法顯然需要改變。"},{"en":"Repeated dissatisfaction often shows that a system needs a new approach.","zh":"重複出現的不滿常顯示系統需要新方法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the need for reform is obvious.","zh":"當改革需要很明顯時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"who would have thought of","meaning":"誰會想到……","examples":[{"en":"Who would have thought of Austria as the perfect alternative?","zh":"誰會想到奧地利會是完美替代選擇？"},{"en":"Who would have thought of something means it is surprising that someone considered or discovered that idea.","zh":"who would have thought of something 指某人想到或發現某想法令人驚訝。"},{"en":"Who would have thought of using a quiet library as the best place for a birthday party?","zh":"誰會想到使用安靜圖書館作為生日派對的最佳地點？"},{"en":"The phrase shows surprise because the answer was not obvious at first.","zh":"這個短語顯示驚訝，因為答案起初並不明顯。"},{"en":"It is useful when an unexpected choice turns out to work.","zh":"當意想不到的選擇最後有效時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the perfect alternative","meaning":"完美替代選擇","examples":[{"en":"Austria became the perfect alternative to beach holidays.","zh":"奧地利成為海灘旅行的完美替代選擇。"},{"en":"The perfect alternative is another choice that solves the problem especially well.","zh":"perfect alternative 指能特別好地解決問題的另一個選擇。"},{"en":"A quiet café may be the perfect alternative to a noisy library for group study.","zh":"對小組溫習來說，安靜咖啡店可能是嘈雜圖書館的完美替代選擇。"},{"en":"An alternative feels perfect when it offers what the old option lacks.","zh":"當替代選擇提供舊選項缺乏的東西，它就感覺完美。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one choice replaces another successfully.","zh":"當一個選擇成功取代另一個時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the domain of","meaning":"……的領域；……專屬的地方","examples":[{"en":"Austria was seen as the domain of the rich ski crowd.","zh":"奧地利被視為富有滑雪族群的專屬地方。"},{"en":"The domain of a group means an area, activity, or world strongly associated with that group.","zh":"domain of a group 指與某群體強烈相關的範圍、活動或世界。"},{"en":"Luxury watch shops may seem like the domain of wealthy collectors.","zh":"名貴手錶店可能看似富有收藏家的領域。"},{"en":"When prices fall, a place once linked to rich people can become accessible to ordinary travellers.","zh":"當價格下降，曾與富人相關的地方可以變得讓普通旅客也能前往。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something feels reserved for a certain group.","zh":"當某事感覺只屬於某群體時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"rich and privileged","meaning":"富有且享有特權的","examples":[{"en":"Ski holidays were associated with rich and privileged travellers.","zh":"滑雪假期與富有且享有特權的旅客聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Rich and privileged means wealthy and enjoying advantages that many ordinary people do not have.","zh":"rich and privileged 指富裕並享有許多普通人沒有的優勢。"},{"en":"A private school may seem designed for rich and privileged families if fees are extremely high.","zh":"如果學費極高，私立學校可能看似為富有且享有特權的家庭而設。"},{"en":"When an activity is linked with privilege, ordinary people may assume it is not for them.","zh":"當活動與特權聯繫起來，普通人可能假設它不屬於自己。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when wealth and social advantage are connected.","zh":"當財富和社會優勢相連時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ski crowd","meaning":"滑雪族群","examples":[{"en":"Austria was traditionally associated with the ski crowd.","zh":"奧地利傳統上與滑雪族群聯繫起來。"},{"en":"The ski crowd means people who regularly go skiing, especially as a fashionable or wealthy group.","zh":"ski crowd 指經常滑雪的人，尤其是作為時尚或富裕群體。"},{"en":"A mountain resort may design its hotels and shops for the ski crowd in winter.","zh":"山區度假村可能在冬季為滑雪族群設計酒店和商店。"},{"en":"If a place wants new visitors, it must show that it is not only for one crowd.","zh":"如果地方想吸引新遊客，就必須顯示它不只屬於一個族群。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a specific travel group.","zh":"描述特定旅行群體時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pay a small fortune","meaning":"花一大筆錢","examples":[{"en":"Many people assumed they had to pay a small fortune to fly to Austria.","zh":"許多人以為自己必須花一大筆錢才能飛往奧地利。"},{"en":"Pay a small fortune means spend a very large amount of money.","zh":"pay a small fortune 指花非常大量金錢。"},{"en":"A parent may feel they pay a small fortune for school uniforms every year.","zh":"家長可能覺得每年要為校服花一大筆錢。"},{"en":"High expected costs can stop people from even considering an option.","zh":"預期成本高可以阻止人甚至考慮某選項。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something seems very expensive.","zh":"當某事看似很昂貴時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mountain resorts","meaning":"山區度假村","examples":[{"en":"Austrian mountain resorts charge high prices in winter.","zh":"奧地利山區度假村在冬季收費高昂。"},{"en":"Mountain resorts are holiday places in mountain areas, often offering hotels, views, skiing, hiking, and outdoor activities.","zh":"mountain resorts 指位於山區的度假地，通常提供酒店、景色、滑雪、行山和戶外活動。"},{"en":"A mountain resort may be busy in winter for skiing and in summer for hiking.","zh":"山區度假村冬季可能因滑雪而繁忙，夏季則因行山而繁忙。"},{"en":"Resorts depend on seasons because weather changes what visitors want to do.","zh":"度假村依賴季節，因為天氣會改變遊客想做的事。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing tourism in mountain regions.","zh":"討論山區旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"charge a pretty penny","meaning":"收費昂貴","examples":[{"en":"Austrian resorts charge a pretty penny for accommodation in winter.","zh":"奧地利度假村在冬季住宿收費昂貴。"},{"en":"Charge a pretty penny means ask customers to pay a high price.","zh":"charge a pretty penny 指向顧客收取高價。"},{"en":"A hotel with a famous sea view may charge a pretty penny during summer holidays.","zh":"有著名海景的酒店在暑假可能收費昂貴。"},{"en":"Prices rise when demand is high and rooms are limited.","zh":"當需求高而房間有限，價格就會上升。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something costs more than ordinary people expect.","zh":"當某事成本高於普通人預期時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"accommodation","meaning":"住宿","examples":[{"en":"Accommodation in Austrian mountain resorts can be expensive in winter.","zh":"奧地利山區度假村的住宿在冬季可能很昂貴。"},{"en":"Accommodation means a place where travellers stay, such as a hotel, hostel, apartment, or guesthouse.","zh":"accommodation 指旅客住宿的地方，例如酒店、青年旅舍、公寓或民宿。"},{"en":"Students may choose cheap accommodation to save money during a study trip.","zh":"學生在學習旅行期間可能選擇便宜住宿來省錢。"},{"en":"Accommodation costs can decide whether a holiday is affordable or too expensive.","zh":"住宿成本可以決定假期是可負擔還是太昂貴。"},{"en":"This word is useful when planning travel budgets.","zh":"規劃旅行預算時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in snowier times","meaning":"在多雪季節","examples":[{"en":"In snowier times, Austrian holidays are much more expensive.","zh":"在多雪季節，奧地利假期昂貴得多。"},{"en":"In snowier times means during periods or seasons with more snow.","zh":"in snowier times 指在有更多雪的時期或季節。"},{"en":"Mountain roads may become harder to use in snowier times.","zh":"在多雪季節，山路可能變得較難使用。"},{"en":"More snow can increase demand for skiing and push winter prices higher.","zh":"更多雪可以增加滑雪需求，並推高冬季價格。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when snow affects travel conditions or costs.","zh":"當雪影響旅行條件或成本時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cost an arm and several legs","meaning":"貴得離譜","examples":[{"en":"Winter holidays in Austria can cost an arm and several legs.","zh":"奧地利冬季假期可能貴得離譜。"},{"en":"Cost an arm and several legs is a humorous exaggeration meaning cost an extremely large amount of money.","zh":"cost an arm and several legs 是幽默誇張說法，指花費極大量金錢。"},{"en":"A family may joke that a new laptop costs an arm and several legs.","zh":"家庭可能開玩笑說新手提電腦貴得離譜。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests the price is far beyond normal expectations.","zh":"這個短語暗示價格遠超正常預期。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when complaining humorously about very high prices.","zh":"幽默抱怨價格非常高時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"nothing in comparison","meaning":"相比之下不算甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Summer accommodation costs almost nothing in comparison with winter prices.","zh":"夏季住宿費與冬季價格相比，幾乎不算甚麼。"},{"en":"Nothing in comparison means much smaller, cheaper, or less serious when compared with something else.","zh":"nothing in comparison 指與另一事物相比小得多、便宜得多或不嚴重。"},{"en":"The cost of a bus ticket is nothing in comparison with a long taxi ride across the city.","zh":"與橫跨城市的長途的士相比，巴士票價不算甚麼。"},{"en":"Comparison can make a price or problem seem minor.","zh":"比較可以令價格或問題顯得較小。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one thing is tiny beside another.","zh":"當一件事與另一件相比很微不足道時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"come spring and summer","meaning":"到了春夏季","examples":[{"en":"Prices fall come spring and summer.","zh":"到了春夏季，價格就會下降。"},{"en":"Come spring and summer means when spring and summer arrive.","zh":"come spring and summer 指當春天和夏天到來時。"},{"en":"Come exam season, students often spend more time in the library.","zh":"到了考試季，學生常花更多時間在圖書館。"},{"en":"This structure highlights what happens when a particular time arrives.","zh":"這個結構突出某段時間到來時會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"It is useful when seasons or periods change behaviour.","zh":"當季節或時期改變行為時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"snow-covered winter","meaning":"白雪覆蓋的冬季","examples":[{"en":"The Austrian Alps are beautiful in the snow-covered winter.","zh":"奧地利阿爾卑斯山在白雪覆蓋的冬季很美。"},{"en":"Snow-covered winter means a winter landscape where snow lies over mountains, buildings, or land.","zh":"snow-covered winter 指雪覆蓋山脈、建築或土地的冬季景觀。"},{"en":"A village may look magical in a snow-covered winter, especially under street lights.","zh":"在白雪覆蓋的冬季，村莊在街燈下可能看起來很夢幻。"},{"en":"Snowy scenery can attract skiers and raise winter tourism prices.","zh":"雪景可以吸引滑雪者並提高冬季旅遊價格。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing winter beauty.","zh":"描述冬季美景時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the Austrian Alps","meaning":"奧地利阿爾卑斯山","examples":[{"en":"The Austrian Alps are beautiful in both summer and winter.","zh":"奧地利阿爾卑斯山在夏季和冬季都很美。"},{"en":"The Austrian Alps are the part of the Alps mountain range located in Austria.","zh":"Austrian Alps 指位於奧地利境內的阿爾卑斯山脈部分。"},{"en":"Tourists may visit the Austrian Alps for skiing, hiking, lakes, and mountain villages.","zh":"遊客可能到奧地利阿爾卑斯山滑雪、行山、遊湖和參觀山村。"},{"en":"Their beauty in different seasons makes them suitable for more than one kind of holiday.","zh":"它們在不同季節的美景，使它們適合多於一種假期。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing Austria’s mountain tourism.","zh":"討論奧地利山區旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"enable someone to","meaning":"使某人能夠","examples":[{"en":"This realisation enabled tour operators to create a new holiday package.","zh":"這個認識使旅行社營辦商能夠創造新的旅行套票。"},{"en":"Enable someone to do something means make it possible for them to do it.","zh":"enable someone to do something 指令某人能夠做某事。"},{"en":"Online booking enables travellers to compare hotel prices quickly.","zh":"網上預訂使旅客能夠快速比較酒店價格。"},{"en":"New information can enable businesses to design better services.","zh":"新資訊可以使企業能夠設計更好服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one factor makes action possible.","zh":"當一個因素令行動變得可能時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"come up with something new","meaning":"想出新點子","examples":[{"en":"Package holiday companies came up with something new.","zh":"套票旅行公司想出了新點子。"},{"en":"Come up with something new means think of or create a new idea, product, or solution.","zh":"come up with something new 指想到或創造新的想法、產品或解決方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may come up with something new when students get bored with old exercises.","zh":"當學生厭倦舊練習，老師可能想出新點子。"},{"en":"New ideas often appear when an old market stops satisfying people.","zh":"當舊市場不再令人滿足，新想法常會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when creativity solves a problem.","zh":"當創意解決問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be awash with","meaning":"充斥着","examples":[{"en":"The internet was awash with cheap summer holiday alternatives.","zh":"互聯網充斥着廉價夏季旅行替代選擇。"},{"en":"Be awash with something means be full of or flooded with a large amount of it.","zh":"be awash with something 指充滿或大量湧現某事物。"},{"en":"After exam results are released, social media may be awash with advice for students.","zh":"考試成績公布後，社交媒體可能充斥着給學生的建議。"},{"en":"When many options appear at once, people may feel excited but also overwhelmed.","zh":"當許多選項同時出現，人們可能既興奮又感到眼花繚亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when there is a lot of something everywhere.","zh":"當某事物到處大量存在時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"holiday alternatives","meaning":"旅行替代選擇","examples":[{"en":"Tour operators offered cheap summer holiday alternatives in Austria.","zh":"旅行社營辦商在奧地利提供廉價夏季旅行替代選擇。"},{"en":"Holiday alternatives are other travel choices people can take instead of their usual holidays.","zh":"holiday alternatives 指人們可以用來取代慣常假期的其他旅行選擇。"},{"en":"A family bored with shopping trips may look for camping or cycling holiday alternatives.","zh":"厭倦購物旅行的家庭可能尋找露營或單車旅行替代選擇。"},{"en":"Alternatives become attractive when the old choice feels too crowded, expensive, or predictable.","zh":"當舊選擇感覺太擠迫、昂貴或可預測，替代選擇就變得吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when travellers want different options.","zh":"當旅客想要不同選項時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"seven nights in","meaning":"在……住七晚","examples":[{"en":"Some packages offered seven nights in the Austrian Alps.","zh":"有些套票提供在奧地利阿爾卑斯山住七晚。"},{"en":"Seven nights in a place means staying there for seven overnight periods.","zh":"seven nights in a place 指在某地過夜七次。"},{"en":"A couple may book seven nights in a quiet village to rest properly.","zh":"一對夫婦可能預訂在安靜村莊住七晚，好好休息。"},{"en":"The number of nights affects the total price, schedule, and activities of a holiday.","zh":"晚數會影響假期總價、日程和活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing travel packages.","zh":"描述旅行套票時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"three- and four-star hotels","meaning":"三星及四星酒店","examples":[{"en":"The packages included three- and four-star hotels.","zh":"這些套票包括三星及四星酒店。"},{"en":"Three- and four-star hotels are mid-range or higher-standard hotels with more comfort and services than basic accommodation.","zh":"three- and four-star hotels 指中等或較高標準酒店，比基本住宿提供更多舒適和服務。"},{"en":"A family may choose a three-star hotel to save money or a four-star hotel for extra comfort.","zh":"家庭可能選擇三星酒店省錢，或選擇四星酒店獲得額外舒適。"},{"en":"Hotel quality affects how travellers judge whether a package is good value.","zh":"酒店質素會影響旅客判斷套票是否物有所值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing accommodation standards.","zh":"描述住宿標準時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"full board","meaning":"全膳住宿","examples":[{"en":"Some Austrian holiday packages offered full board.","zh":"有些奧地利旅行套票提供全膳住宿。"},{"en":"Full board means accommodation includes all main meals, usually breakfast, lunch, and dinner.","zh":"full board 指住宿包括所有正餐，通常是早餐、午餐和晚餐。"},{"en":"Parents may choose full board because it saves time finding restaurants for children.","zh":"家長可能選擇全膳住宿，因為它省卻為孩子找餐廳的時間。"},{"en":"Including all meals can make holiday budgeting easier and more predictable.","zh":"包括所有餐膳可以令旅行預算更容易和更可預測。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing hotel meal plans.","zh":"比較酒店餐膳安排時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"half board","meaning":"半膳住宿","examples":[{"en":"Half board was typically provided as standard.","zh":"半膳住宿通常作為標準配套提供。"},{"en":"Half board means accommodation includes breakfast and one other main meal, usually dinner.","zh":"half board 指住宿包括早餐和另一餐正餐，通常是晚餐。"},{"en":"Travellers may choose half board if they want lunch outside while sightseeing.","zh":"如果旅客想在觀光時外出吃午餐，可能選擇半膳住宿。"},{"en":"Half board balances convenience with freedom to explore local food.","zh":"半膳住宿在方便和自由探索本地食物之間取得平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing what meals are included in a hotel package.","zh":"討論酒店套票包括哪些餐膳時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"provided as standard","meaning":"作為標準配套提供","examples":[{"en":"Half board was typically provided as standard in the packages.","zh":"半膳住宿通常在套票中作為標準配套提供。"},{"en":"Provided as standard means included automatically without needing an extra request or special payment.","zh":"provided as standard 指自動包括在內，不需要額外要求或特別付款。"},{"en":"Wi-Fi is provided as standard in many modern hotels.","zh":"許多現代酒店把 Wi-Fi 作為標準配套提供。"},{"en":"Standard features make customers feel the package offers better value.","zh":"標準配套功能會令顧客覺得套票更物有所值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is automatically included.","zh":"當某事自動包括在內時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hoteliers and restaurateurs","meaning":"酒店業者和餐廳業者","examples":[{"en":"Austrian hoteliers and restaurateurs welcomed the new summer demand.","zh":"奧地利酒店業者和餐廳業者歡迎新的夏季需求。"},{"en":"Hoteliers and restaurateurs are people who own or manage hotels and restaurants.","zh":"hoteliers and restaurateurs 指擁有或管理酒店和餐廳的人。"},{"en":"Hoteliers and restaurateurs may work together to attract visitors during quiet seasons.","zh":"酒店業者和餐廳業者可能合作，在淡季吸引遊客。"},{"en":"More tourists can increase room bookings, meals sold, and local employment.","zh":"更多遊客可以增加房間預訂、餐膳銷售和本地就業。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing hospitality businesses.","zh":"討論款待業企業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"gear up for","meaning":"為……作好準備","examples":[{"en":"Hotels had geared up for seasonal winter trade.","zh":"酒店已為季節性冬季生意作好準備。"},{"en":"To gear up for something means to prepare for it seriously.","zh":"gear up for something 指認真為某事作準備。"},{"en":"A school gears up for exam season by arranging revision classes and mock tests.","zh":"學校透過安排溫習課和模擬試，為考試季作好準備。"},{"en":"Businesses prepare early when they expect a busy period.","zh":"當企業預期繁忙時期，它們會提早準備。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when people or organisations get ready for demand.","zh":"當人或組織為需求作準備時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"seasonal winter trade","meaning":"季節性冬季生意","examples":[{"en":"Austrian hotels relied heavily on seasonal winter trade.","zh":"奧地利酒店高度依賴季節性冬季生意。"},{"en":"Seasonal winter trade is business that mainly happens during the winter season.","zh":"seasonal winter trade 指主要在冬季發生的生意。"},{"en":"A ski shop depends on seasonal winter trade when most customers arrive after snow falls.","zh":"當大多數顧客在下雪後到來，滑雪用品店就依賴季節性冬季生意。"},{"en":"Businesses based on one season may need new income sources during quiet months.","zh":"依賴單一季節的企業，在淡季可能需要新收入來源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when sales depend strongly on winter demand.","zh":"當銷售強烈依賴冬季需求時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be only too happy to","meaning":"非常樂意","examples":[{"en":"Businesses were only too happy to satisfy summertime demand.","zh":"商戶非常樂意滿足夏季需求。"},{"en":"Be only too happy to do something means be very willing and pleased to do it.","zh":"be only too happy to do something 指非常願意且樂於做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may be only too happy to help a student who asks sincere questions.","zh":"對真誠提問的學生，老師可能非常樂意幫助。"},{"en":"People are eager to act when the action brings benefit or relief.","zh":"當行動帶來好處或紓緩，人們就會很願意去做。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when willingness is strong.","zh":"當意願很強時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"satisfy demand","meaning":"滿足需求","examples":[{"en":"Hotels were happy to satisfy the new summertime demand.","zh":"酒店樂於滿足新的夏季需求。"},{"en":"To satisfy demand means provide enough goods or services for what people want.","zh":"satisfy demand 指提供足夠商品或服務，以回應人們想要的東西。"},{"en":"A bakery may hire more staff to satisfy demand for bread before a festival.","zh":"麵包店可能在節日前聘請更多員工，以滿足麵包需求。"},{"en":"If businesses cannot satisfy demand, customers may go elsewhere.","zh":"如果企業不能滿足需求，顧客可能轉到其他地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when supply responds to customer needs.","zh":"當供應回應顧客需要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"summertime demand","meaning":"夏季需求","examples":[{"en":"Austria saw new summertime demand from budget travellers.","zh":"奧地利看到來自預算有限旅客的新夏季需求。"},{"en":"Summertime demand is the need or desire for products or services during summer.","zh":"summertime demand 指夏季期間對產品或服務的需要或渴望。"},{"en":"Ice-cream shops often see strong summertime demand when the weather becomes hot.","zh":"天氣變熱時，雪糕店常看到強烈夏季需求。"},{"en":"New summer demand can help businesses that usually rely on winter customers.","zh":"新夏季需求可以幫助通常依賴冬季顧客的企業。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when seasonal interest appears in summer.","zh":"當季節性興趣在夏季出現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at reduced prices","meaning":"以減價價格","examples":[{"en":"Hotels offered rooms at reduced prices in summer.","zh":"酒店在夏季以減價價格提供房間。"},{"en":"At reduced prices means at lower prices than usual.","zh":"at reduced prices 指以比平常較低的價格。"},{"en":"A shop may sell winter coats at reduced prices after the cold season ends.","zh":"寒冷季節結束後，商店可能以減價價格出售冬季外套。"},{"en":"Lower prices can attract customers during slow periods.","zh":"較低價格可以在淡季吸引顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discounts make something more affordable.","zh":"當折扣令某物更可負擔時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"vacant rooms","meaning":"空置房間","examples":[{"en":"Any profit was better than vacant rooms.","zh":"任何利潤都比空置房間好。"},{"en":"Vacant rooms are rooms that are empty and not being used or booked.","zh":"vacant rooms 指空着、未被使用或未被預訂的房間。"},{"en":"A hotel may lower prices if it has many vacant rooms on weekdays.","zh":"如果酒店平日有很多空置房間，可能會降低價格。"},{"en":"Empty rooms earn nothing, so even lower-paying guests may help the business.","zh":"空房不能賺錢，所以即使付費較低的住客也可能幫助生意。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing hotel occupancy.","zh":"討論酒店入住率時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"look on something as","meaning":"把……視為","examples":[{"en":"Hotel owners looked on summer profits as a bonus.","zh":"酒店東主把夏季利潤視為額外收益。"},{"en":"To look on something as something means to regard or treat it in that way.","zh":"look on something as something 指把某事視作或當作某種東西。"},{"en":"A student may look on feedback as help rather than criticism.","zh":"學生可能把回饋視為幫助，而不是批評。"},{"en":"How people look on a situation affects whether they feel grateful, worried, or annoyed.","zh":"人們如何看待情況，會影響他們感到感激、擔心還是煩惱。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing attitude or interpretation.","zh":"描述態度或詮釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a bonus","meaning":"額外收益","examples":[{"en":"Summer profits were regarded as a bonus.","zh":"夏季利潤被視為額外收益。"},{"en":"A bonus is something extra and welcome, beyond what was expected or needed.","zh":"bonus 指超出預期或需要之外、令人歡迎的額外事物。"},{"en":"A worker may treat free lunch at a meeting as a bonus.","zh":"員工可能把會議中的免費午餐視為額外好處。"},{"en":"Extra income feels like a bonus when the main income source is already secure.","zh":"當主要收入來源已穩定，額外收入就感覺像額外收益。"},{"en":"This word is useful when something additional is pleasant.","zh":"當額外事物令人愉快時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be too greedy","meaning":"太貪心","examples":[{"en":"Hotels did not need to be too greedy with prices.","zh":"酒店不需要在價格上太貪心。"},{"en":"Be too greedy means want too much money, profit, or advantage.","zh":"be too greedy 指想要太多金錢、利潤或好處。"},{"en":"A shop may lose customers if it becomes too greedy and raises prices sharply.","zh":"如果商店太貪心並大幅加價，可能失去顧客。"},{"en":"Greedy pricing can discourage people from buying or visiting.","zh":"貪心定價可以令人不想購買或到訪。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when excessive profit-seeking becomes harmful.","zh":"當過度追求利潤變得有害時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"put people off coming","meaning":"令人不想前來","examples":[{"en":"High prices would put people off coming.","zh":"高價格會令人不想前來。"},{"en":"Put people off coming means discourage people from visiting or attending.","zh":"put people off coming 指令人不想來訪或參加。"},{"en":"A long waiting time may put patients off coming to a clinic for minor problems.","zh":"長時間等候可能令病人不想因小問題到診所。"},{"en":"If prices, distance, or inconvenience feel too great, people may choose another option.","zh":"如果價格、距離或不便感覺太大，人們可能選擇另一個選項。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something reduces interest in visiting.","zh":"當某事降低到訪興趣時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"besides","meaning":"況且；此外","examples":[{"en":"Besides, winter business was their main source of income.","zh":"況且，冬季生意是他們的主要收入來源。"},{"en":"Besides means in addition, or used to add another reason.","zh":"besides 指此外，或用來加入另一個理由。"},{"en":"The café is close to school; besides, the food is cheap.","zh":"那間咖啡店靠近學校；此外，食物也便宜。"},{"en":"This word helps add a supporting point after the main reason.","zh":"這個詞幫助在主要原因後加入支持點。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving an extra explanation.","zh":"給予額外解釋時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bread and butter","meaning":"主要收入來源；飯碗","examples":[{"en":"Winter business was the bread and butter of Austrian hotels.","zh":"冬季生意是奧地利酒店的主要收入來源。"},{"en":"Bread and butter means the main source of income or the basic work that keeps something going.","zh":"bread and butter 指主要收入來源，或讓某事維持運作的基本工作。"},{"en":"Regular local customers are the bread and butter of a small restaurant.","zh":"固定本地顧客是小餐廳的飯碗。"},{"en":"A business protects its bread and butter because it depends on it for survival.","zh":"企業會保護自己的主要收入來源，因為它依賴它生存。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing core income.","zh":"討論核心收入時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not going anywhere","meaning":"不會消失","examples":[{"en":"The winter business was not going anywhere.","zh":"冬季生意不會消失。"},{"en":"Not going anywhere means not likely to disappear or stop soon.","zh":"not going anywhere 指不太可能很快消失或停止。"},{"en":"Online learning is not going anywhere because many students find it convenient.","zh":"網上學習不會消失，因為許多學生覺得它方便。"},{"en":"If demand remains strong, a business can take risks in other areas.","zh":"如果需求仍然強勁，企業可以在其他範疇冒一些風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is stable and likely to continue.","zh":"當某事穩定且可能持續時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"budget flights","meaning":"廉價航班","examples":[{"en":"Numerous new budget flights were also appearing.","zh":"許多新廉價航班也正在出現。"},{"en":"Budget flights are low-cost flights sold at cheaper prices, often with fewer extras.","zh":"budget flights 指以較便宜價格出售、通常附加服務較少的低成本航班。"},{"en":"Students may choose budget flights to save money for food and activities during a trip.","zh":"學生可能選擇廉價航班，把錢省下來用於旅行中的食物和活動。"},{"en":"Cheap flights can make previously expensive destinations accessible to ordinary travellers.","zh":"廉價航班可以令以往昂貴的目的地變得讓普通旅客也能前往。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when low airfares change travel habits.","zh":"當低機票價格改變旅行習慣時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"direct return flights","meaning":"直航來回機票","examples":[{"en":"Ryanair offered direct return flights to Salzburg.","zh":"Ryanair 提供前往薩爾斯堡的直航來回機票。"},{"en":"Direct return flights are flights to a destination and back again without needing to change planes.","zh":"direct return flights 指前往目的地和返回時都不需要轉機的航班。"},{"en":"A family may prefer direct return flights because they are simpler for children and luggage.","zh":"家庭可能較喜歡直航來回航班，因為對孩子和行李較簡單。"},{"en":"Easier transport can make a new destination more attractive.","zh":"更方便的交通可以令新目的地更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing convenient air travel.","zh":"討論便利航空旅行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for little more than","meaning":"只比……多一點","examples":[{"en":"Flights to Salzburg cost little more than £50.","zh":"前往薩爾斯堡的航班只需比50英鎊多一點。"},{"en":"For little more than an amount means for only slightly above that amount.","zh":"for little more than an amount 指只比某金額稍高。"},{"en":"A student may buy a second-hand desk for little more than £20.","zh":"學生可能以只比20英鎊多一點的價格買二手書桌。"},{"en":"When prices are only slightly above a small amount, people may see the deal as affordable.","zh":"當價格只比小額金錢稍高，人們可能覺得交易可負擔。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing low cost.","zh":"強調低成本時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"including taxes","meaning":"包括稅項","examples":[{"en":"The flights cost little more than £50, including taxes.","zh":"這些航班只需比50英鎊多一點，包括稅項。"},{"en":"Including taxes means the stated price already contains required tax charges.","zh":"including taxes 指所列價格已包含必要稅項。"},{"en":"A hotel room advertised at £80 including taxes is clearer than one with extra charges added later.","zh":"標明80英鎊包括稅項的酒店房，比之後再加額外費用的房價更清楚。"},{"en":"Including taxes helps travellers understand the real cost before booking.","zh":"包括稅項有助旅客在預訂前理解真實成本。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing total prices.","zh":"描述總價格時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"vacationers","meaning":"旅行人士","examples":[{"en":"Vacationers suddenly had an alternative to beach holidays.","zh":"旅行人士突然有了海灘旅行以外的替代選擇。"},{"en":"Vacationers are people who are on holiday or planning a holiday.","zh":"vacationers 指正在度假或計劃度假的人。"},{"en":"Vacationers may compare beaches, mountains, cities, and countryside before choosing a trip.","zh":"旅行人士可能在選擇旅程前比較海灘、山區、城市和鄉村。"},{"en":"Their choices shape what airlines, hotels, and tour operators offer.","zh":"他們的選擇會塑造航空公司、酒店和旅行社營辦商提供的產品。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing leisure travellers.","zh":"討論休閒旅客時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the same old","meaning":"一成不變的","examples":[{"en":"Travellers wanted an alternative to the same old sandy monotony.","zh":"旅客想要一成不變的單調沙灘旅行以外的選擇。"},{"en":"The same old means the usual thing that has become boring because it is repeated too often.","zh":"the same old 指因重複太多而變得沉悶的慣常事物。"},{"en":"A student may get tired of the same old grammar worksheets every week.","zh":"學生可能厭倦每星期一成不變的文法工作紙。"},{"en":"People often search for change when the same old routine stops feeling enjoyable.","zh":"當一成不變的日常不再令人享受，人們常尋求改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when complaining about repetition.","zh":"抱怨重複時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sandy monotony","meaning":"單調乏味的沙灘旅行","examples":[{"en":"Austria offered an alternative to sandy monotony.","zh":"奧地利提供了單調乏味的沙灘旅行以外的選擇。"},{"en":"Sandy monotony means the dull repetition of similar beach holidays.","zh":"sandy monotony 指相似海灘假期的沉悶重複。"},{"en":"A traveller may complain of sandy monotony after visiting almost identical resorts for ten summers.","zh":"旅客在十個夏天到訪幾乎一樣的度假村後，可能抱怨沙灘旅行單調乏味。"},{"en":"Repetition can make even pleasant beaches feel boring over time.","zh":"隨着時間過去，重複可以令即使愉快的海灘也變得沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when criticising predictable seaside tourism.","zh":"批評可預測的海濱旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"given how","meaning":"考慮到……","examples":[{"en":"The response was surprising given how budget travellers are depicted in the media.","zh":"考慮到預算有限旅客在媒體中如何被描繪，這種反應令人驚訝。"},{"en":"Given how means considering the way or degree to which something is true.","zh":"given how 指考慮到某事情是真實的方式或程度。"},{"en":"The student’s speech was impressive given how nervous he had been the day before.","zh":"考慮到那學生前一天多緊張，他的演講令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a result seems surprising or understandable.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何某結果顯得令人驚訝或可理解。"},{"en":"It is useful when judging something in context.","zh":"在語境中判斷某事時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be depicted in the media","meaning":"在媒體中被描繪成","examples":[{"en":"Budget travellers are often depicted negatively in the media.","zh":"預算有限的旅客常在媒體中被負面描繪。"},{"en":"Be depicted in the media means be shown or described by newspapers, television, websites, or social media.","zh":"be depicted in the media 指被報章、電視、網站或社交媒體展示或描述。"},{"en":"Teenagers are sometimes depicted in the media as lazy, even when many are hardworking.","zh":"青少年有時在媒體中被描繪成懶惰，即使很多人很勤奮。"},{"en":"Media depictions can shape public opinion, fairly or unfairly.","zh":"媒體描繪可以公平或不公平地塑造公眾意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing public image created by media.","zh":"討論由媒體創造的公眾形象時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ignorant, undiscerning folk","meaning":"無知且缺乏鑑賞力的人","examples":[{"en":"The media sometimes depicts budget travellers as ignorant, undiscerning folk.","zh":"媒體有時把預算有限的旅客描繪成無知且缺乏鑑賞力的人。"},{"en":"Ignorant, undiscerning folk means people unfairly described as knowing little and lacking judgement or taste.","zh":"ignorant, undiscerning folk 指被不公平地描述為知識少、缺乏判斷或品味的人。"},{"en":"A cheap-food customer should not be dismissed as ignorant and undiscerning simply because they watch their budget.","zh":"不能只因顧客注重預算，就把廉價食物顧客貶低為無知且缺乏鑑賞力的人。"},{"en":"Stereotypes can make people underestimate others’ curiosity and good taste.","zh":"刻板印象可以令人低估他人的好奇心和好品味。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when criticising a negative stereotype.","zh":"批評負面刻板印象時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"embrace this new opportunity","meaning":"欣然接受這個新機會","examples":[{"en":"Many budget travellers wanted to embrace this new opportunity.","zh":"許多預算有限的旅客想欣然接受這個新機會。"},{"en":"To embrace this new opportunity means to accept and use a new chance gladly.","zh":"embrace this new opportunity 指高興地接受並利用新的機會。"},{"en":"A student may embrace a new opportunity to study abroad if funding becomes available.","zh":"如果資助出現，學生可能欣然接受到海外學習的新機會。"},{"en":"People welcome opportunities when they offer something better than old limitations.","zh":"當機會提供比舊限制更好的東西，人們就會歡迎它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone responds positively to change.","zh":"當某人正面回應改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"discard their sandals and lilos","meaning":"拋開涼鞋和吹氣浮床","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of Britons discarded their sandals and lilos.","zh":"數以千計英國人拋開涼鞋和吹氣浮床。"},{"en":"Discard their sandals and lilos means give up the usual beach-holiday symbols and choose another style of holiday.","zh":"discard their sandals and lilos 指放棄慣常海灘旅行象徵，選擇另一種旅行方式。"},{"en":"A family may discard its beach towels and buy hiking bags for a mountain trip instead.","zh":"家庭可能拋開沙灘毛巾，改買行山背包去山區旅行。"},{"en":"Changing equipment can symbolise a deeper change in holiday habits.","zh":"裝備改變可以象徵旅行習慣上的更深改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when travellers move from beach leisure to active travel.","zh":"當旅客由海灘休閒轉向活躍旅行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"don hiking boots","meaning":"穿上行山靴","examples":[{"en":"Britons donned their hiking boots instead of beachwear.","zh":"英國人穿上行山靴，而不是沙灘服裝。"},{"en":"To don hiking boots means to put on boots suitable for walking in hills or mountains.","zh":"don hiking boots 指穿上適合在山丘或山區步行的靴。"},{"en":"Before a country walk, students may don hiking boots to avoid slipping on muddy paths.","zh":"郊遊前，學生可能穿上行山靴，以免在泥路上滑倒。"},{"en":"Wearing the right equipment makes outdoor activities safer and more comfortable.","zh":"穿着合適裝備令戶外活動更安全和舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when preparing for active travel.","zh":"準備活躍旅行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"yodel-ley-he-hoo","meaning":"約德爾唱法的幽默叫聲","examples":[{"en":"The writer jokingly ends the paragraph with “Yodel-ley-he-hoo.”","zh":"作者以 “Yodel-ley-he-hoo” 這句玩笑式叫聲結束該段。"},{"en":"Yodel-ley-he-hoo is a playful imitation of yodelling, a singing style associated with Alpine regions.","zh":"yodel-ley-he-hoo 是對約德爾唱法的俏皮模仿，這種唱法與阿爾卑斯地區有關。"},{"en":"A student may shout “yodel-ley-he-hoo” jokingly after seeing a mountain scene in a film.","zh":"學生在電影中看到山景後，可能開玩笑地喊 “yodel-ley-he-hoo”。"},{"en":"The phrase adds humour and connects the holiday image with the Alps.","zh":"這個短語加入幽默，並把旅行形象與阿爾卑斯山連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when creating a light, comic Alpine mood.","zh":"當想營造輕鬆滑稽的阿爾卑斯氣氛時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"continue to grow","meaning":"繼續增長","examples":[{"en":"The popularity of Austria may continue to grow.","zh":"奧地利的受歡迎程度可能繼續增長。"},{"en":"Continue to grow means keep increasing or becoming more important.","zh":"continue to grow 指持續增加或變得更重要。"},{"en":"A school club may continue to grow if older students invite younger students to join.","zh":"如果高年級學生邀請低年級學生加入，學校學會可能繼續增長。"},{"en":"Growth continues when demand stays strong and more people hear positive stories.","zh":"當需求保持強勁且更多人聽到正面故事，增長就會持續。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a trend is expected to keep rising.","zh":"當趨勢預期持續上升時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"over the coming years","meaning":"在未來數年","examples":[{"en":"The trend may continue over the coming years.","zh":"這個趨勢可能在未來數年繼續。"},{"en":"Over the coming years means during the next several years.","zh":"over the coming years 指在接下來幾年期間。"},{"en":"Over the coming years, more schools may use digital textbooks.","zh":"在未來數年，更多學校可能使用電子課本。"},{"en":"This phrase points to future development rather than immediate change only.","zh":"這個短語指向未來發展，而不只是即時變化。"},{"en":"It is useful when predicting gradual change.","zh":"預測逐步變化時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"health experts","meaning":"健康專家","examples":[{"en":"Health experts see Austria’s popularity as a positive development.","zh":"健康專家把奧地利受歡迎視為正面發展。"},{"en":"Health experts are people with professional knowledge about health, medicine, fitness, or public well-being.","zh":"health experts 指在健康、醫學、健身或公共福祉方面有專業知識的人。"},{"en":"Health experts may advise schools to give children more outdoor exercise.","zh":"健康專家可能建議學校給孩子更多戶外運動。"},{"en":"Their opinions matter when lifestyle changes affect public health.","zh":"當生活方式改變影響公共健康，他們的意見很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing expert views on health.","zh":"討論健康方面的專家看法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a huge turning point","meaning":"巨大轉捩點","examples":[{"en":"This trend could be a huge turning point in the health of the nation.","zh":"這個趨勢可能是國民健康的一個巨大轉捩點。"},{"en":"A huge turning point is a major moment when a situation begins to change in an important way.","zh":"huge turning point 指情況開始以重要方式改變的重大時刻。"},{"en":"A child’s first successful speech may be a huge turning point in their confidence.","zh":"孩子第一次成功演講，可能是其信心上的巨大轉捩點。"},{"en":"Turning points matter because they mark a clear shift from the old pattern.","zh":"轉捩點重要，因為它標誌從舊模式清楚轉變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when change feels large and decisive.","zh":"當改變感覺重大而關鍵時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the health of our nation","meaning":"國民健康","examples":[{"en":"The trend could improve the health of the nation.","zh":"這個趨勢可能改善國民健康。"},{"en":"The health of our nation means the general physical and mental well-being of people in a country.","zh":"health of our nation 指一個國家人民整體的身體和心理健康。"},{"en":"More parks, cleaner air, and better diets can improve the health of a nation.","zh":"更多公園、更清潔空氣和更好飲食可以改善國民健康。"},{"en":"When many people become more active, public healthcare pressure may fall.","zh":"當許多人變得更活躍，公共醫療壓力可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when individual habits are discussed at a national level.","zh":"當個人習慣在國家層面討論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"there is really no comparison between","meaning":"兩者實在不能相比","examples":[{"en":"There is really no comparison between a static beach holiday and an active Alpine holiday.","zh":"靜態海灘旅行和活躍阿爾卑斯山旅行實在不能相比。"},{"en":"There is really no comparison between two things means one is clearly much better or very different from the other.","zh":"there is really no comparison between two things 指兩者非常不同，或其中一個明顯好得多。"},{"en":"There is really no comparison between guessing vocabulary and learning it through clear examples.","zh":"猜詞彙和透過清晰例子學詞彙，兩者實在不能相比。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly favours one option and dismisses the other as weaker.","zh":"這個短語強烈偏向一個選項，並把另一個視為較弱。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when making a strong contrast.","zh":"作出強烈對比時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"drink-fuelled","meaning":"以飲酒為主的","examples":[{"en":"A drink-fuelled beach holiday is less healthy than an active holiday.","zh":"以飲酒為主的海灘旅行比活躍旅行較不健康。"},{"en":"Drink-fuelled means driven or dominated by alcohol consumption.","zh":"drink-fuelled 指由飲酒推動或以飲酒為主。"},{"en":"A drink-fuelled party may become noisy, unsafe, and difficult to control.","zh":"以飲酒為主的派對可能變得嘈雜、不安全且難以控制。"},{"en":"Alcohol-centred activities can reduce rest, safety, and health during a holiday.","zh":"以酒精為中心的活動可以減少假期中的休息、安全和健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when criticising excessive drinking.","zh":"批評過度飲酒時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"static beach holiday","meaning":"靜態海灘旅行","examples":[{"en":"A static beach holiday involves little physical activity.","zh":"靜態海灘旅行涉及很少體能活動。"},{"en":"A static beach holiday is a holiday where people mostly sit, lie down, and do very little movement.","zh":"static beach holiday 指人們主要坐着、躺着且很少活動的假期。"},{"en":"A person may spend a static beach holiday moving only between a sunbed, bar, and hotel room.","zh":"一個人可能在靜態海灘旅行中只在太陽椅、酒吧和酒店房間之間移動。"},{"en":"Too little movement can make a holiday less healthy, even if it feels relaxing.","zh":"太少活動可以令假期較不健康，即使它感覺放鬆。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting passive holidays with active ones.","zh":"對比被動假期和活躍假期時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"what the Alps have to offer","meaning":"阿爾卑斯山所能提供的","examples":[{"en":"There is no comparison between beach holidays and what the Alps have to offer.","zh":"海灘旅行和阿爾卑斯山所能提供的東西實在不能相比。"},{"en":"What the Alps have to offer means the activities, scenery, culture, and experiences available in the Alps.","zh":"what the Alps have to offer 指阿爾卑斯山可提供的活動、景色、文化和體驗。"},{"en":"Families may enjoy what the mountains have to offer, such as hiking, lakes, and clean air.","zh":"家庭可能享受山區所能提供的東西，例如行山、湖泊和清新空氣。"},{"en":"A destination becomes attractive when people understand the full range of things it offers.","zh":"當人們理解目的地提供的完整範圍，它就變得吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a place’s advantages.","zh":"描述地方優勢時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"holiday phenomenon","meaning":"旅行現象","examples":[{"en":"The Austrian holiday phenomenon may encourage healthier lifestyles.","zh":"奧地利旅行現象可能鼓勵更健康的生活方式。"},{"en":"A holiday phenomenon is a travel trend that becomes noticeable and widely discussed.","zh":"holiday phenomenon 指變得明顯並被廣泛討論的旅行趨勢。"},{"en":"Short weekend city trips became a holiday phenomenon when cheap flights became common.","zh":"當廉價航班變得普遍，週末城市短途旅行成為一種旅行現象。"},{"en":"A travel phenomenon can influence businesses, media, and public habits.","zh":"旅行現象可以影響企業、媒體和公眾習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a holiday trend becomes socially significant.","zh":"當旅行趨勢變得有社會意義時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"just the tonic","meaning":"正是所需的良方","examples":[{"en":"The Austrian holiday phenomenon is just the tonic health workers had hoped for.","zh":"奧地利旅行現象正是醫療工作者一直希望得到的良方。"},{"en":"Just the tonic means exactly the thing needed to improve health, mood, or a situation.","zh":"just the tonic 指正是改善健康、心情或情況所需的事物。"},{"en":"A quiet weekend may be just the tonic for a student exhausted by exams.","zh":"對被考試弄得疲憊的學生來說，安靜週末可能正是所需良方。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when something gives welcome relief or improvement.","zh":"當某事帶來受歡迎的紓緩或改善，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a solution feels refreshing and helpful.","zh":"當解決方法令人精神一振且有幫助時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"healthcare","meaning":"醫療保健","examples":[{"en":"People who work in healthcare welcome more active holidays.","zh":"從事醫療保健的人歡迎更多活躍假期。"},{"en":"Healthcare means services and work related to protecting and improving people’s health.","zh":"healthcare 指與保護和改善人們健康有關的服務和工作。"},{"en":"Doctors, nurses, clinics, hospitals, and health educators are all part of healthcare.","zh":"醫生、護士、診所、醫院和健康教育者都是醫療保健的一部分。"},{"en":"Healthcare workers may support active holidays because exercise can reduce long-term illness.","zh":"醫療工作者可能支持活躍假期，因為運動可以減少長期疾病。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing health services and public well-being.","zh":"討論健康服務和公共福祉時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"leaflets and brochures","meaning":"傳單和小冊子","examples":[{"en":"Hotels give guests leaflets and brochures about outdoor activities.","zh":"酒店向住客提供關於戶外活動的傳單和小冊子。"},{"en":"Leaflets and brochures are small printed materials that give information, advice, or advertising.","zh":"leaflets and brochures 指提供資訊、建議或廣告的小型印刷材料。"},{"en":"A school may give parents leaflets and brochures about summer courses.","zh":"學校可能向家長派發關於暑期課程的傳單和小冊子。"},{"en":"Clear printed information can encourage people to try activities they did not know about.","zh":"清晰印刷資訊可以鼓勵人嘗試原本不知道的活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when information is distributed to visitors.","zh":"當資訊被分發給訪客時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"outdoor activities","meaning":"戶外活動","examples":[{"en":"Austrian holidays encourage guests to try outdoor activities.","zh":"奧地利假期鼓勵住客嘗試戶外活動。"},{"en":"Outdoor activities are things people do outside, often involving movement, nature, or sport.","zh":"outdoor activities 指人們在戶外做的事情，常涉及活動、自然或運動。"},{"en":"Hiking, cycling, fishing, camping, and football are outdoor activities.","zh":"行山、踩單車、釣魚、露營和足球都是戶外活動。"},{"en":"Outdoor activities can improve fitness, mood, and confidence.","zh":"戶外活動可以改善體能、心情和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing active leisure outside buildings.","zh":"描述建築物外的活躍休閒時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hiking","meaning":"行山","examples":[{"en":"Hiking is one of the outdoor activities offered in Austria.","zh":"行山是奧地利提供的戶外活動之一。"},{"en":"Hiking means walking for pleasure or exercise, usually in the countryside, hills, or mountains.","zh":"hiking 指為樂趣或運動而步行，通常在鄉郊、山丘或山區進行。"},{"en":"A family may go hiking on a marked trail during a weekend trip.","zh":"家庭可能在週末旅行中沿標示路線行山。"},{"en":"Hiking can strengthen the body and help people enjoy natural scenery.","zh":"行山可以強健身體，並幫助人享受自然景色。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing active holidays.","zh":"討論活躍假期時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hill walking","meaning":"山野步行","examples":[{"en":"Hill walking is a popular activity in the Austrian Alps.","zh":"山野步行是奧地利阿爾卑斯山的熱門活動。"},{"en":"Hill walking means walking in hilly areas, usually less extreme than mountain climbing.","zh":"hill walking 指在多山丘地區步行，通常不如登山那麼極端。"},{"en":"Older travellers may prefer hill walking because it is active but not too dangerous.","zh":"年長旅客可能較喜歡山野步行，因為它活躍但不太危險。"},{"en":"Gentle walking routes can make mountain holidays accessible to more people.","zh":"溫和步行路線可以令更多人能享受山區假期。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing moderate outdoor exercise.","zh":"描述中等強度戶外運動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"horse riding","meaning":"騎馬","examples":[{"en":"Families can try horse riding during an Austrian holiday.","zh":"家庭可以在奧地利假期中嘗試騎馬。"},{"en":"Horse riding means sitting on and controlling a horse for sport, travel, or enjoyment.","zh":"horse riding 指為運動、旅行或享受而騎乘和控制馬匹。"},{"en":"A child may try horse riding for the first time at a countryside activity centre.","zh":"孩子可能在鄉郊活動中心第一次嘗試騎馬。"},{"en":"Trying horse riding can make a holiday feel adventurous and memorable.","zh":"嘗試騎馬可以令假期感覺冒險且難忘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing outdoor leisure activities.","zh":"討論戶外休閒活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mountain biking","meaning":"山地單車","examples":[{"en":"Mountain biking is one of the activities promoted to visitors.","zh":"山地單車是向訪客推廣的活動之一。"},{"en":"Mountain biking means riding a bicycle on rough outdoor paths, hills, or mountain trails.","zh":"mountain biking 指在崎嶇戶外路徑、山丘或山路上踩單車。"},{"en":"A teenager may enjoy mountain biking because it feels fast, active, and challenging.","zh":"青少年可能喜歡山地單車，因為它感覺快速、活躍且有挑戰性。"},{"en":"Safety equipment matters because mountain biking can involve uneven ground and steep slopes.","zh":"安全裝備很重要，因為山地單車可能涉及不平地面和陡坡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing active adventure sports.","zh":"討論活躍冒險運動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"you name it","meaning":"諸如此類；應有盡有","examples":[{"en":"Guests can try hiking, horse riding, mountain biking, fishing, boating, you name it.","zh":"住客可以嘗試行山、騎馬、山地單車、釣魚、划船，諸如此類。"},{"en":"You name it means there are many examples, almost any example you can think of.","zh":"you name it 指例子很多，幾乎你能想到的都有。"},{"en":"The new community centre offers music, dance, chess, yoga, cooking, you name it.","zh":"新社區中心提供音樂、舞蹈、棋藝、瑜伽、烹飪，應有盡有。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests variety and abundance without listing everything.","zh":"這個短語暗示種類繁多，而不需要列出所有東西。"},{"en":"It is useful when choices are wide and easy to imagine.","zh":"當選擇廣泛且容易想像時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be encouraged to try out","meaning":"被鼓勵嘗試","examples":[{"en":"Guests are encouraged to try out healthy activities.","zh":"住客被鼓勵嘗試健康活動。"},{"en":"Be encouraged to try out something means be invited or motivated to test an activity for the first time.","zh":"be encouraged to try out something 指被邀請或推動去首次試某活動。"},{"en":"Students are encouraged to try out drama club before deciding whether to join.","zh":"學生被鼓勵先試試戲劇學會，再決定是否加入。"},{"en":"Encouragement lowers fear and makes new experiences feel easier to start.","zh":"鼓勵可以降低恐懼，令新體驗感覺更容易開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when people are gently pushed toward new activities.","zh":"當人們被溫和推向新活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"healthy activities","meaning":"健康活動","examples":[{"en":"Austria offers many healthy activities for travellers.","zh":"奧地利為旅客提供許多健康活動。"},{"en":"Healthy activities are activities that support physical or mental well-being.","zh":"healthy activities 指支持身體或心理健康的活動。"},{"en":"Walking, swimming, cycling, stretching, and outdoor games are healthy activities.","zh":"步行、游泳、踩單車、伸展和戶外遊戲都是健康活動。"},{"en":"Regular healthy activities can improve energy, mood, and long-term health.","zh":"定期進行健康活動可以改善精力、心情和長期健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when leisure is good for the body or mind.","zh":"當休閒對身體或心靈有益時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make permanent lifestyle changes","meaning":"作出永久生活方式改變","examples":[{"en":"The holiday may encourage people to make permanent lifestyle changes.","zh":"這個假期可能鼓勵人們作出永久生活方式改變。"},{"en":"To make permanent lifestyle changes means to change daily habits in a lasting way.","zh":"make permanent lifestyle changes 指以持久方式改變日常習慣。"},{"en":"After a health scare, a parent may make permanent lifestyle changes such as walking daily and eating less sugar.","zh":"經歷健康警號後，家長可能作出永久生活方式改變，例如每天步行和少吃糖。"},{"en":"Temporary experiences can become important if they lead to long-term habits.","zh":"如果短暫體驗導致長期習慣，它就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a short event changes daily life.","zh":"當短期事件改變日常生活時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"continue to be active","meaning":"繼續保持活躍","examples":[{"en":"Travellers may continue to be active after returning home.","zh":"旅客回家後可能繼續保持活躍。"},{"en":"Continue to be active means keep doing physical movement or exercise regularly.","zh":"continue to be active 指持續定期進行身體活動或運動。"},{"en":"A student who enjoys a hiking trip may continue to be active by walking after school.","zh":"享受行山旅行的學生，可能透過放學後步行來繼續保持活躍。"},{"en":"Active habits become healthier when they continue beyond one special event.","zh":"活躍習慣在超越一次特別活動後，會變得更健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when exercise becomes a lasting habit.","zh":"當運動變成持久習慣時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"return home from their holidays","meaning":"旅行後回家","examples":[{"en":"People may stay active when they return home from their holidays.","zh":"人們旅行後回家時，可能仍保持活躍。"},{"en":"Return home from their holidays means come back to normal life after a trip.","zh":"return home from their holidays 指旅行後回到正常生活。"},{"en":"A family may return home from their holidays with new photos, stories, and healthier habits.","zh":"家庭旅行後回家時，可能帶着新照片、故事和更健康習慣。"},{"en":"What people do after a holiday shows whether the experience had a lasting effect.","zh":"人們旅行後做甚麼，顯示該體驗是否有持久影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing life after travel.","zh":"討論旅行後生活時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"East Ender","meaning":"倫敦東區人","examples":[{"en":"Ed Brown is described as an East Ender.","zh":"Ed Brown 被描述為倫敦東區人。"},{"en":"An East Ender is a person from the East End of London.","zh":"East Ender 指來自倫敦東區的人。"},{"en":"An East Ender may speak with a local accent and feel strong pride in the neighbourhood.","zh":"倫敦東區人可能有本地口音，並對社區有強烈自豪感。"},{"en":"Mentioning someone’s background can make their holiday story feel more personal and ordinary.","zh":"提及某人的背景可以令其旅行故事感覺更個人化和貼近普通人。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying a person by their London community.","zh":"以倫敦社區身份識別某人時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"local musician and teacher","meaning":"本地音樂人兼教師","examples":[{"en":"Ed Brown is a local musician and teacher.","zh":"Ed Brown 是本地音樂人兼教師。"},{"en":"A local musician and teacher is someone who works in music and education within a community.","zh":"local musician and teacher 指在社區內從事音樂和教育工作的人。"},{"en":"A local musician and teacher may give piano lessons and perform at school events.","zh":"本地音樂人兼教師可能教授鋼琴，並在學校活動中表演。"},{"en":"Such a background suggests an ordinary working person, not a wealthy luxury traveller.","zh":"這種背景暗示他是普通工作人士，而不是富裕奢華旅客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing someone’s role in community life.","zh":"描述某人在社區生活中的角色時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"holiday experience","meaning":"旅行經歷","examples":[{"en":"Ed Brown describes his Austrian holiday experience.","zh":"Ed Brown 描述他的奧地利旅行經歷。"},{"en":"Holiday experience means what someone did, felt, and remembered during a holiday.","zh":"holiday experience 指某人在假期中做了甚麼、感受到甚麼和記住甚麼。"},{"en":"A student may write about their holiday experience after visiting a farm for the first time.","zh":"學生第一次參觀農場後，可能寫下自己的旅行經歷。"},{"en":"Good holiday experiences can change what people want from future travel.","zh":"好的旅行經歷可以改變人們未來對旅行的期望。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing personal travel memories.","zh":"討論個人旅行回憶時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on my salary","meaning":"以我的薪金","examples":[{"en":"On his salary, Ed Brown could only afford package trips in the past.","zh":"以他的薪金，Ed Brown 過去只能負擔套票旅行。"},{"en":"On my salary means based on the amount of money I earn from work.","zh":"on my salary 指根據我從工作賺到的金額。"},{"en":"On my salary, I can rent a small flat but not buy a large apartment.","zh":"以我的薪金，我能租細單位，但買不起大公寓。"},{"en":"Income limits what people can realistically afford.","zh":"收入限制人們實際能負擔甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining financial limits.","zh":"解釋財務限制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"afford to go on","meaning":"負擔得起去……","examples":[{"en":"He could never afford to go on anything but a package trip.","zh":"他除了套票旅行之外，從來負擔不起去其他旅行。"},{"en":"Afford to go on a trip means have enough money to pay for that trip.","zh":"afford to go on a trip 指有足夠金錢支付該旅行。"},{"en":"A student may not afford to go on an overseas tour without saving for months.","zh":"學生如果不儲蓄幾個月，可能負擔不起去海外旅行團。"},{"en":"When cheaper options appear, people can afford trips they once thought impossible.","zh":"當較便宜選項出現，人們可以負擔以前認為不可能的旅行。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when travel depends on cost.","zh":"當旅行取決於成本時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"anything but","meaning":"除了……之外甚麼都不","examples":[{"en":"He could never afford anything but a package trip.","zh":"他除了套票旅行之外，甚麼都負擔不起。"},{"en":"Anything but means anything except, or not at all the thing mentioned, depending on context.","zh":"anything but 指除了某事之外任何事，或根本不是某事，視乎語境而定。"},{"en":"A tired student may want anything but another long worksheet.","zh":"疲倦學生可能甚麼都想要，就是不想再做一份長工作紙。"},{"en":"In this sentence, the phrase shows that package trips were the only affordable option.","zh":"在這句中，這個短語顯示套票旅行是唯一可負擔選項。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when excluding all other choices.","zh":"排除所有其他選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"package trip","meaning":"套票旅行","examples":[{"en":"Package trips were the only holidays Ed Brown could afford.","zh":"套票旅行是 Ed Brown 唯一負擔得起的假期。"},{"en":"A package trip is a holiday sold as one combined deal, usually including travel and accommodation.","zh":"package trip 指以一個組合方案出售的假期，通常包括交通和住宿。"},{"en":"A family may choose a package trip because the flight, hotel, and transfers are arranged together.","zh":"家庭可能選擇套票旅行，因為航班、酒店和接送都一併安排。"},{"en":"Package trips reduce planning stress but may limit flexibility.","zh":"套票旅行減少規劃壓力，但可能限制彈性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing organised holiday deals.","zh":"討論有組織旅行優惠時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"過去","examples":[{"en":"In the past, Ed Brown could not afford to visit the Alps.","zh":"過去，Ed Brown 負擔不起到訪阿爾卑斯山。"},{"en":"In the past means before now or during an earlier time.","zh":"in the past 指現在以前或較早時期。"},{"en":"In the past, students used paper dictionaries more often than phone apps.","zh":"過去，學生較常使用紙本字典，而不是手機應用程式。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare earlier situations with the present.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較早前情況和現在。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing change over time.","zh":"顯示隨時間變化時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"never envisaged","meaning":"從未想像過","examples":[{"en":"He never envisaged being able to go to the Alps.","zh":"他從未想像過自己能到阿爾卑斯山。"},{"en":"Never envisaged means never imagined or expected something could happen.","zh":"never envisaged 指從未想像或預期某事可能發生。"},{"en":"A shy student may never have envisaged speaking confidently on stage.","zh":"害羞學生可能從未想像過自己能在台上自信演講。"},{"en":"When barriers fall, people may experience things they once thought impossible.","zh":"當障礙消失，人們可能經歷以前認為不可能的事。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a later reality was once unimaginable.","zh":"當後來現實曾經不可想像時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be able to","meaning":"能夠","examples":[{"en":"He never thought he would be able to take his daughter horse riding.","zh":"他從未想過自己能夠帶女兒去騎馬。"},{"en":"Be able to means have the ability, chance, or resources to do something.","zh":"be able to 指有能力、機會或資源做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be able to join a trip if the school offers financial help.","zh":"如果學校提供經濟幫助，學生可能能夠參加旅行。"},{"en":"Opportunity often depends on money, time, health, and access.","zh":"機會常取決於金錢、時間、健康和取得途徑。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing possibility or ability.","zh":"討論可能性或能力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"within budget","meaning":"在預算之內","examples":[{"en":"Beach package holidays were the only thing within budget.","zh":"海灘套票旅行是唯一在預算之內的東西。"},{"en":"Within budget means affordable because it does not exceed the money available.","zh":"within budget 指價格可負擔，因為沒有超出可用金錢。"},{"en":"A school trip is within budget if the class can pay for transport, tickets, and food.","zh":"如果班級能支付交通、門票和食物，學校旅行就在預算之內。"},{"en":"When something is within budget, people can choose it without financial stress.","zh":"當某事在預算之內，人們可以在沒有財務壓力下選擇它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing cost with available money.","zh":"比較成本和可用金錢時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"go on them anyway","meaning":"還是去那些旅行","examples":[{"en":"They did not like beach holidays but used to go on them anyway.","zh":"他們不喜歡海灘旅行，但以前還是去那些旅行。"},{"en":"Go on them anyway means still take those holidays despite not really wanting to.","zh":"go on them anyway 指即使不太想去，仍然參加那些旅行。"},{"en":"A student may dislike revision classes but go on them anyway because parents paid for them.","zh":"學生可能不喜歡補習班，但因父母已付款還是去上。"},{"en":"People sometimes choose imperfect options when alternatives are too expensive or unavailable.","zh":"當其他選擇太貴或不可取得，人們有時會選擇不完美的選項。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone does something despite dislike.","zh":"當某人不喜歡但仍做某事時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"such an adventure","meaning":"如此精彩的歷險","examples":[{"en":"Ed Brown and his family had been on such an adventure.","zh":"Ed Brown 和他的家人經歷了如此精彩的歷險。"},{"en":"Such an adventure means a very exciting, unusual, or memorable experience.","zh":"such an adventure 指非常刺激、不尋常或難忘的經歷。"},{"en":"A child may call a camping trip such an adventure after sleeping under the stars.","zh":"孩子在星空下露營後，可能說那是如此精彩的歷險。"},{"en":"Adventures feel special because they involve new places, small risks, and strong memories.","zh":"歷險感覺特別，因為它涉及新地方、小風險和強烈回憶。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a trip feels exciting and different from ordinary life.","zh":"當旅行感覺刺激且不同於日常生活時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"drive to the top of","meaning":"駛到……頂部","examples":[{"en":"They drove to the top of Austria’s highest mountain.","zh":"他們駛到奧地利最高山的頂部。"},{"en":"Drive to the top of something means travel by car or vehicle to the highest point or upper part of it.","zh":"drive to the top of something 指乘車到達某物的最高點或上部。"},{"en":"A family may drive to the top of a hill to watch the sunset.","zh":"家庭可能駛到山丘頂部看日落。"},{"en":"Reaching a high viewpoint can make a trip feel dramatic and memorable.","zh":"到達高處觀景點可以令旅行感覺壯觀且難忘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing travel to a summit or high place.","zh":"描述前往山頂或高處時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"highest mountain","meaning":"最高的山","examples":[{"en":"The family visited Austria’s highest mountain.","zh":"這家人到訪奧地利最高的山。"},{"en":"The highest mountain is the mountain that rises higher than all others in a country or area.","zh":"highest mountain 指在某國家或地區中高度高於所有其他山的山。"},{"en":"Tourists may visit the highest mountain in a region for views and photographs.","zh":"遊客可能到訪某地區最高的山，以欣賞景色和拍照。"},{"en":"High mountains often become landmarks because they are easy to identify and remember.","zh":"高山常成為地標，因為它們容易識別和記住。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a major natural attraction.","zh":"描述主要自然景點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"hike on a glacier","meaning":"在冰川上遠足","examples":[{"en":"They hiked on a glacier during the holiday.","zh":"他們在假期中在冰川上遠足。"},{"en":"To hike on a glacier means to walk across a large body of slow-moving ice, usually with proper safety support.","zh":"hike on a glacier 指在大型緩慢移動的冰體上步行，通常需要適當安全支援。"},{"en":"Travellers may need a guide and special boots to hike safely on a glacier.","zh":"旅客可能需要導遊和特殊靴子，才能安全地在冰川上遠足。"},{"en":"Glacier hiking feels memorable because it is very different from ordinary walking.","zh":"冰川遠足令人難忘，因為它與普通步行非常不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing unusual mountain activities.","zh":"描述不尋常山區活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bring a picnic","meaning":"帶野餐","examples":[{"en":"The family went hill walking and brought a picnic.","zh":"這家人去山野步行並帶了野餐。"},{"en":"Bring a picnic means take prepared food to eat outdoors during a trip or activity.","zh":"bring a picnic 指帶備食物，在旅行或活動期間戶外進食。"},{"en":"Students may bring a picnic to the park instead of buying lunch outside.","zh":"學生可能帶野餐去公園，而不是在外面買午餐。"},{"en":"Bringing food can save money and make an outdoor day more relaxed.","zh":"帶食物可以省錢，並令戶外日子更放鬆。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing simple outdoor meals.","zh":"討論簡單戶外餐食時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"could not get over","meaning":"對……感到難以置信","examples":[{"en":"Ed Brown could not get over the warm weather.","zh":"Ed Brown 對溫暖天氣感到難以置信。"},{"en":"Could not get over something means was very surprised by it and kept thinking about it.","zh":"could not get over something 指對某事非常驚訝，並一直想着它。"},{"en":"A student could not get over how quiet the library was during exam week.","zh":"學生可能對考試週圖書館多安靜感到難以置信。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when something is more surprising than expected.","zh":"當某事比預期更令人驚訝，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It is useful when a strong impression remains in the mind.","zh":"當強烈印象留在腦海中時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"hire a boat","meaning":"租船","examples":[{"en":"They hired a boat and went out on the lake.","zh":"他們租了一艘船，然後到湖上遊玩。"},{"en":"Hire a boat means pay to use a boat for a period of time.","zh":"hire a boat 指付錢在一段時間內使用船。"},{"en":"A family may hire a boat for one hour to explore a lake safely.","zh":"家庭可能租船一小時，安全地探索湖泊。"},{"en":"Renting equipment allows travellers to try activities without owning expensive gear.","zh":"租用設備讓旅客不用擁有昂貴器材，也能嘗試活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when people pay temporarily to use leisure equipment.","zh":"當人們暫時付費使用休閒設備時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"go out on the lake","meaning":"到湖上遊玩","examples":[{"en":"The family hired a boat and went out on the lake.","zh":"這家人租了一艘船，到湖上遊玩。"},{"en":"Go out on the lake means travel onto the surface of a lake, usually by boat.","zh":"go out on the lake 指通常乘船到湖面上活動。"},{"en":"Friends may go out on the lake in a small rowing boat during a summer afternoon.","zh":"朋友可能在夏日下午乘小划艇到湖上遊玩。"},{"en":"Lake activities can make a mountain holiday feel peaceful and varied.","zh":"湖上活動可以令山區假期感覺平靜且多樣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing boating or lake leisure.","zh":"描述划船或湖上休閒時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"hire a guide","meaning":"聘請導遊","examples":[{"en":"They hired a guide to take them through the hills.","zh":"他們聘請導遊帶他們穿越山丘。"},{"en":"Hire a guide means pay a knowledgeable person to lead or explain a trip.","zh":"hire a guide 指付錢請有知識的人帶領或講解旅程。"},{"en":"Tourists may hire a guide in an old city to understand its history and hidden streets.","zh":"遊客可能在古城聘請導遊，以了解其歷史和隱藏街道。"},{"en":"Guides can make unfamiliar places safer, clearer, and more meaningful.","zh":"導遊可以令陌生地方更安全、更清楚和更有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when travellers need local knowledge.","zh":"當旅客需要本地知識時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"on horseback","meaning":"騎馬","examples":[{"en":"The guide took them on horseback through the hills.","zh":"導遊帶他們騎馬穿越山丘。"},{"en":"On horseback means riding on a horse.","zh":"on horseback 指騎在馬背上。"},{"en":"Visitors may travel on horseback along a quiet country path.","zh":"訪客可能騎馬沿安靜鄉郊小路前行。"},{"en":"Riding on horseback can make a journey feel slower, closer to nature, and more adventurous.","zh":"騎馬可以令旅程感覺較慢、更接近自然和更具冒險感。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing travel by horse.","zh":"描述騎馬旅行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"through the hills","meaning":"穿越山丘","examples":[{"en":"The family travelled on horseback through the hills.","zh":"這家人騎馬穿越山丘。"},{"en":"Through the hills means across or among a series of raised natural land areas.","zh":"through the hills 指穿過或在一連串自然高地之間前行。"},{"en":"Hikers may walk through the hills before reaching a small village.","zh":"行山人士可能穿越山丘，然後到達小村莊。"},{"en":"Travelling through hills gives people changing views, slopes, and a sense of exploration.","zh":"穿越山丘給人不斷變化的景色、斜坡和探索感。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing movement across hilly countryside.","zh":"描述穿過多山鄉郊的移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"what a good time","meaning":"多麼愉快的時光","examples":[{"en":"Ed Brown said, “What a good time!”","zh":"Ed Brown 說：「多麼愉快的時光！」"},{"en":"What a good time means the experience was very enjoyable.","zh":"what a good time 指經歷非常愉快。"},{"en":"After a picnic, a child may say, “What a good time!” because the whole day felt happy.","zh":"野餐後，孩子可能說「多麼愉快的時光！」因為整天都感覺開心。"},{"en":"People say this when an activity gives them pleasure and strong memories.","zh":"當活動帶來快樂和強烈回憶，人們會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when expressing simple enjoyment.","zh":"表達簡單享受時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"step off the plane","meaning":"走下飛機","examples":[{"en":"Mark Jones spoke as he stepped off the plane.","zh":"Mark Jones 走下飛機時說話。"},{"en":"Step off the plane means walk down from an aircraft after landing.","zh":"step off the plane 指飛機降落後從機上走下來。"},{"en":"A traveller may feel excited as they step off the plane in a country they have never visited.","zh":"旅客走下飛機到達從未到訪過的國家時，可能感到興奮。"},{"en":"First impressions often begin the moment people leave the aircraft.","zh":"第一印象常在人們離開飛機那一刻開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing arrival after a flight.","zh":"描述乘飛機抵達後，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be impressed by","meaning":"對……印象深刻","examples":[{"en":"Mark Jones was impressed by Austria.","zh":"Mark Jones 對奧地利印象深刻。"},{"en":"Be impressed by something means feel admiration or surprise because it is good, beautiful, or effective.","zh":"be impressed by something 指因某事好、美麗或有效而感到欣賞或驚喜。"},{"en":"A parent may be impressed by a school if teachers explain the curriculum clearly.","zh":"如果老師清楚解釋課程，家長可能對學校印象深刻。"},{"en":"Good experiences can change someone’s opinion of a place or service.","zh":"良好體驗可以改變某人對地方或服務的看法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something creates a strong positive reaction.","zh":"當某事帶來強烈正面反應時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"point back towards","meaning":"指向後方的……","examples":[{"en":"He pointed back towards the plane as he spoke.","zh":"他說話時指向後方的飛機。"},{"en":"Point back towards something means gesture with a finger or hand in the direction behind you.","zh":"point back towards something 指用手指或手勢指向身後某方向。"},{"en":"A student may point back towards the classroom to show where they left their bag.","zh":"學生可能指向後方的課室，表示自己把書包留在那裏。"},{"en":"Pointing helps listeners understand which place or object the speaker means.","zh":"指向能幫助聽者理解說話者指的是哪個地方或物件。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing physical direction.","zh":"描述實際方向時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"to tell you the truth","meaning":"老實說","examples":[{"en":"To tell you the truth, he used to enjoy the beach.","zh":"老實說，他以前喜歡海灘。"},{"en":"To tell you the truth means honestly speaking or to be frank.","zh":"to tell you the truth 指誠實地說或坦白說。"},{"en":"To tell you the truth, I was nervous before the interview.","zh":"老實說，我面試前很緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase prepares the listener for an honest admission or personal feeling.","zh":"這個短語讓聽者準備接受誠實承認或個人感受。"},{"en":"It is useful when someone wants to sound sincere.","zh":"當某人想顯得真誠時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lounge around","meaning":"懶洋洋地消磨時間","examples":[{"en":"After work, it is nice to lounge around and relax.","zh":"工作後，懶洋洋地消磨時間和放鬆是很舒服的。"},{"en":"Lounge around means spend time resting lazily without doing much.","zh":"lounge around 指懶散地休息，不做太多事情。"},{"en":"After exams, students may lounge around at home watching films and eating snacks.","zh":"考試後，學生可能在家懶洋洋地看電影和吃零食。"},{"en":"Lounging around can feel pleasant, but too much of it may become boring or unhealthy.","zh":"懶洋洋地休息可以愉快，但太多可能變得沉悶或不健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing lazy relaxation.","zh":"描述懶散放鬆時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"relax","meaning":"放鬆","examples":[{"en":"Many people go to the beach to relax.","zh":"許多人去海灘放鬆。"},{"en":"Relax means rest, calm down, and reduce stress or tension.","zh":"relax 指休息、平靜下來並減少壓力或緊張。"},{"en":"A student may relax by listening to music after finishing homework.","zh":"學生完成功課後，可能透過聽音樂放鬆。"},{"en":"Relaxation helps people recover energy before returning to work or study.","zh":"放鬆幫助人在回到工作或學習前恢復精力。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing rest and stress relief.","zh":"討論休息和減壓時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"do this for the kids","meaning":"為孩子做這件事","examples":[{"en":"Mark Jones wanted to do this for the kids.","zh":"Mark Jones 想為孩子做這件事。"},{"en":"Do this for the kids means choose or do something mainly for the children’s benefit.","zh":"do this for the kids 指主要為孩子的利益而選擇或做某事。"},{"en":"Parents may visit a science museum because they want to do something for the kids.","zh":"父母可能參觀科學博物館，因為他們想為孩子做點事。"},{"en":"Adults sometimes accept inconvenience if the experience helps children learn or enjoy life.","zh":"如果體驗有助孩子學習或享受生活，成年人有時會接受不便。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when children are the main reason for a decision.","zh":"當孩子是決定的主要原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"show someone there was more to life than","meaning":"讓某人知道人生不只是……","examples":[{"en":"He wanted to show his children that there was more to life than sunbathing.","zh":"他想讓孩子知道人生不只是日光浴。"},{"en":"Show someone there is more to life than something means help them realise life offers richer possibilities than one limited activity or value.","zh":"show someone there is more to life than something 指幫助某人明白人生有比某一有限活動或價值更豐富的可能。"},{"en":"A teacher may show students there is more to life than exam marks.","zh":"老師可能讓學生知道人生不只是考試分數。"},{"en":"New experiences can widen children’s view of what is enjoyable, meaningful, or possible.","zh":"新體驗可以擴闊孩子對甚麼是愉快、有意義或可能的理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when challenging a narrow view of life.","zh":"挑戰狹窄人生觀時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"sunbathing","meaning":"日光浴","examples":[{"en":"Mark Jones wanted his children to experience more than sunbathing.","zh":"Mark Jones 希望孩子體驗日光浴以外的事情。"},{"en":"Sunbathing means lying or sitting in the sun to become tanned or enjoy warmth.","zh":"sunbathing 指躺或坐在陽光下曬黑或享受溫暖。"},{"en":"Tourists may spend hours sunbathing beside a hotel pool.","zh":"遊客可能在酒店泳池旁花幾小時日光浴。"},{"en":"Too much sunbathing can cause sunburn and make a holiday less healthy.","zh":"過多日光浴可以造成曬傷，令假期較不健康。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing beach holidays and passive relaxation.","zh":"討論海灘旅行和被動放鬆時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"loved every moment of it","meaning":"享受當中的每一刻","examples":[{"en":"The children loved every moment of the holiday.","zh":"孩子們享受假期中的每一刻。"},{"en":"Loved every moment of it means enjoyed the whole experience from beginning to end.","zh":"loved every moment of it 指從開始到結束都享受整個經歷。"},{"en":"A child may love every moment of a school camp if the activities are exciting and friendly.","zh":"如果活動刺激且氣氛友善，孩子可能享受學校營的每一刻。"},{"en":"Strong enjoyment can make a trip memorable long after it ends.","zh":"強烈享受可以令旅行在結束很久後仍令人記得。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone enjoys an experience completely.","zh":"當某人完全享受某經歷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"stranger still","meaning":"更奇怪的是","examples":[{"en":"Stranger still, Mark Jones enjoyed the active holiday too.","zh":"更奇怪的是，Mark Jones 也享受這個活躍假期。"},{"en":"Stranger still means even more surprising than what was just mentioned.","zh":"stranger still 指比剛才提到的事情更令人驚訝。"},{"en":"The shy student joined the debate team; stranger still, he became team captain.","zh":"害羞學生加入了辯論隊；更奇怪的是，他成為隊長。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a second surprise that goes further than the first.","zh":"這個短語引入第二個驚喜，而且比第一個更進一步。"},{"en":"It is useful when a situation becomes unexpectedly more unusual.","zh":"當情況變得意外地更不尋常時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"run around all week","meaning":"整星期四處活動","examples":[{"en":"He had been running around all week but still felt refreshed.","zh":"他整星期四處活動，但仍感到精神煥發。"},{"en":"Run around all week means spend the whole week being physically busy and active.","zh":"run around all week 指整個星期身體上很忙碌、到處活動。"},{"en":"A parent may run around all week taking children to school, lessons, and appointments.","zh":"家長可能整星期四處奔走，接送孩子上學、上課和看診。"},{"en":"Being busy usually makes people tired, so feeling refreshed afterwards can be surprising.","zh":"忙碌通常令人疲倦，所以之後感到精神煥發可能令人驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a week full of movement and activity.","zh":"描述充滿移動和活動的一星期時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"feel more refreshed than","meaning":"感到比……更精神","examples":[{"en":"He felt more refreshed than he ever did on a beach holiday.","zh":"他感到比任何海灘旅行後都更精神。"},{"en":"Feel more refreshed than means feel more rested, energetic, or mentally renewed compared with something else.","zh":"feel more refreshed than 指相比另一事物感到更休息充分、更有活力或精神更新。"},{"en":"A student may feel more refreshed after a walk than after scrolling on a phone for an hour.","zh":"學生散步後可能比滑手機一小時後更精神。"},{"en":"Active rest can sometimes restore energy better than passive rest.","zh":"活躍休息有時比被動休息更能恢復精力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing different kinds of recovery.","zh":"比較不同恢復方式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"sitting on my sunbed","meaning":"坐在太陽椅上","examples":[{"en":"He felt more refreshed than he did sitting on his sunbed.","zh":"他感覺比坐在太陽椅上時更精神。"},{"en":"Sitting on my sunbed means resting on a reclining outdoor chair, usually while sunbathing.","zh":"sitting on my sunbed 指坐或躺在戶外斜躺椅上，通常是在日光浴。"},{"en":"A tourist may spend the afternoon sitting on a sunbed beside the hotel pool.","zh":"遊客可能整個下午坐在酒店泳池旁的太陽椅上。"},{"en":"Sitting still can feel relaxing, but it may not give the same energy as active outdoor movement.","zh":"靜坐可以感覺放鬆，但未必像活躍戶外活動那樣帶來精力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing passive beach relaxation.","zh":"描述被動海灘放鬆時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生為每題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choose the correct letter means select the option letter that matches the right answer.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇與正確答案相配的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may choose the correct letter after checking the relevant paragraph.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能查看相關段落後選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choosing carefully matters because similar options may contain small traps.","zh":"謹慎選擇很重要，因為相似選項可能包含小陷阱。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in multiple-choice exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於多項選擇考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"which of the following statements is accurate","meaning":"以下哪項陳述正確","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which of the following statements is accurate.","zh":"題目問以下哪項陳述正確。"},{"en":"Which of the following statements is accurate means which option is true according to the information given.","zh":"which of the following statements is accurate 指哪個選項根據所給資料是真確的。"},{"en":"Students should check each option against the passage before deciding which statement is accurate.","zh":"學生應把每個選項與文章核對，再決定哪項陳述正確。"},{"en":"An accurate statement must match the text, not simply sound reasonable.","zh":"正確陳述必須符合文本，而不只是聽起來合理。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading-comprehension questions.","zh":"這個短語適用於閱讀理解題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"enjoy a reputation as","meaning":"享有……的名聲","examples":[{"en":"The option says Austria has enjoyed a reputation as a wealthy summer destination.","zh":"這個選項說奧地利享有富裕夏季目的地的名聲。"},{"en":"Enjoy a reputation as something means be widely regarded or known in that way.","zh":"enjoy a reputation as something 指廣泛被視為或被知道是某種形象。"},{"en":"A school may enjoy a reputation as a caring place if teachers support students well.","zh":"如果老師很好地支援學生，學校可能享有關愛校園的名聲。"},{"en":"Reputation affects what people expect before they have direct experience.","zh":"名聲會影響人們在直接經驗前的期待。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing public image.","zh":"討論公眾形象時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"more of a seasonal holiday destination","meaning":"更像季節性旅行目的地","examples":[{"en":"The option describes Austria as more of a seasonal holiday destination.","zh":"這個選項把奧地利描述為更像季節性旅行目的地。"},{"en":"More of a seasonal holiday destination means a place is mainly popular during one particular season.","zh":"more of a seasonal holiday destination 指某地方主要在某一特定季節受歡迎。"},{"en":"A ski village is more of a seasonal holiday destination if most visitors come only in winter.","zh":"如果大多數訪客只在冬季到來，滑雪村就更像季節性旅行目的地。"},{"en":"Seasonal destinations may need new attractions to bring visitors at other times of year.","zh":"季節性目的地可能需要新景點，在一年其他時間吸引訪客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a place’s tourism depends on season.","zh":"當地方旅遊依賴季節時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"good-value holiday destination","meaning":"物有所值的旅行目的地","examples":[{"en":"The option describes Austria as a good-value holiday destination.","zh":"這個選項把奧地利描述為物有所值的旅行目的地。"},{"en":"A good-value holiday destination is a place that offers a satisfying holiday for a reasonable price.","zh":"good-value holiday destination 指以合理價格提供令人滿意假期的地方。"},{"en":"A town with cheap hotels, beautiful scenery, and safe transport can be a good-value holiday destination.","zh":"擁有便宜酒店、美麗景色和安全交通的城鎮，可以是物有所值的旅行目的地。"},{"en":"Good value matters when travellers want quality without spending too much.","zh":"當旅客想要質素但不想花太多錢，物有所值就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when judging cost and experience together.","zh":"同時判斷成本和體驗時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"traditionally attracted","meaning":"傳統上吸引","examples":[{"en":"Austria has traditionally attracted more foreign tourists in winter.","zh":"奧地利傳統上在冬季吸引更多外國遊客。"},{"en":"Traditionally attracted means has usually drawn or brought in visitors over a long period.","zh":"traditionally attracted 指長期以來通常吸引或帶來訪客。"},{"en":"A market has traditionally attracted local families on Sunday mornings.","zh":"市集傳統上在星期日上午吸引本地家庭。"},{"en":"Traditional visitor patterns can change when prices, transport, or tastes shift.","zh":"當價格、交通或品味改變，傳統訪客模式也可以改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing long-established tourism habits.","zh":"描述長久形成的旅遊習慣時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"what does the writer mean when","meaning":"作者說……是甚麼意思","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what the writer means by “narrow horizons.”","zh":"題目問作者說 “narrow horizons” 是甚麼意思。"},{"en":"What does the writer mean when asks students to explain the intended meaning behind a phrase or statement.","zh":"what does the writer mean when 指要求學生解釋短語或陳述背後的真正意思。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask what the writer means when he calls a city “a living classroom.”","zh":"老師可能問作者稱一座城市為「活的課室」是甚麼意思。"},{"en":"These questions test interpretation, not just dictionary meaning.","zh":"這類題目測試詮釋，而不只是字典意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading questions about implied meaning.","zh":"這個短語適用於關於隱含意思的閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be targeted at","meaning":"以……為目標對象","examples":[{"en":"The option says package holidays are targeted at people with little money.","zh":"這個選項說套票旅行以金錢不多的人為目標對象。"},{"en":"Be targeted at a group means be designed or marketed for that group.","zh":"be targeted at a group 指為某群體設計或推廣。"},{"en":"A beginner English course may be targeted at adults who lack confidence in speaking.","zh":"初級英文課程可能以缺乏說話信心的成人為目標對象。"},{"en":"Targeting affects price, language, design, and advertising.","zh":"目標對象會影響價格、語言、設計和廣告。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing intended customers or audiences.","zh":"描述預期顧客或受眾時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"very few and very similar choices","meaning":"很少且非常相似的選擇","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests package holidays offer very few and very similar choices.","zh":"這個選項暗示套票旅行提供很少且非常相似的選擇。"},{"en":"Very few and very similar choices means there are not many options, and the options that exist are almost the same.","zh":"very few and very similar choices 指選項不多，而且現有選項幾乎相同。"},{"en":"A school canteen offers very few and very similar choices if every lunch is rice with one meat dish.","zh":"如果學校飯堂每餐都是飯配一款肉，選擇就很少且非常相似。"},{"en":"Limited and repetitive choices can make people bored and eager for alternatives.","zh":"有限且重複的選擇會令人厭倦並渴望替代方案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when criticising lack of variety.","zh":"批評缺乏多樣性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"far-off destinations","meaning":"遙遠目的地","examples":[{"en":"Some package holidays are rarely offered to far-off destinations.","zh":"有些套票旅行很少提供前往遙遠目的地的選擇。"},{"en":"Far-off destinations are places that are distant or difficult to reach.","zh":"far-off destinations 指距離遙遠或難以到達的地方。"},{"en":"A small travel agency may avoid far-off destinations because flights are expensive and complicated.","zh":"小旅行社可能避免遙遠目的地，因為航班昂貴且複雜。"},{"en":"Distant places may feel exciting but harder to include in cheap packages.","zh":"遙遠地方可能感覺刺激，但較難納入廉價套票。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing long-distance travel.","zh":"討論長途旅行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"well planned or organised","meaning":"計劃或組織妥善","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to holidays that are not well planned or organised.","zh":"這個選項指計劃或組織不妥善的旅行。"},{"en":"Well planned or organised means arranged carefully, clearly, and efficiently.","zh":"well planned or organised 指被仔細、清楚且有效地安排。"},{"en":"A school trip is well planned and organised when transport, meals, tickets, and emergency contacts are ready.","zh":"當交通、餐膳、門票和緊急聯絡都準備好，學校旅行就是計劃和組織妥善。"},{"en":"Poor organisation can make even an exciting trip stressful.","zh":"組織差可以令即使刺激的旅行也變得有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when judging how smoothly an event is arranged.","zh":"判斷活動安排是否順暢時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"typical summer holiday package","meaning":"典型夏季旅行套票","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what a typical summer holiday package to Austria offers.","zh":"題目問前往奧地利的典型夏季旅行套票提供甚麼。"},{"en":"A typical summer holiday package is the usual set of travel services sold for summer tourists.","zh":"typical summer holiday package 指為夏季遊客出售的慣常旅行服務組合。"},{"en":"A typical package may include flights, hotel rooms, meals, and some local activities.","zh":"典型套票可能包括航班、酒店房間、餐膳和一些本地活動。"},{"en":"Knowing what is typical helps travellers compare value and avoid misunderstandings.","zh":"知道甚麼是典型安排，有助旅客比較價值並避免誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing standard travel deals.","zh":"描述標準旅行優惠時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"luxury accommodation","meaning":"豪華住宿","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions luxury accommodation.","zh":"這個選項提到豪華住宿。"},{"en":"Luxury accommodation means expensive, high-quality places to stay with extra comfort and services.","zh":"luxury accommodation 指昂貴、高質素並提供額外舒適和服務的住宿。"},{"en":"A honeymoon couple may choose luxury accommodation with a private pool and mountain view.","zh":"蜜月夫婦可能選擇有私人泳池和山景的豪華住宿。"},{"en":"Luxury lodging raises the price of a trip but can make it feel special.","zh":"豪華住宿會提高旅程價格，但可以令它感覺特別。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing high-end travel.","zh":"討論高端旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"included in the price","meaning":"已包括在價格內","examples":[{"en":"Some meals may be included in the price.","zh":"有些餐膳可能已包括在價格內。"},{"en":"Included in the price means already covered by the amount paid, with no extra charge.","zh":"included in the price 指已由所支付金額涵蓋，不需額外收費。"},{"en":"Breakfast is included in the price at some hotels.","zh":"有些酒店早餐已包括在價格內。"},{"en":"Included items make it easier for customers to calculate the real cost.","zh":"已包括項目令顧客更容易計算真實成本。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining what a deal contains.","zh":"解釋優惠包含甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"all meals included","meaning":"包括所有餐膳","examples":[{"en":"Full board means all meals are included.","zh":"全膳住宿指包括所有餐膳。"},{"en":"All meals included means breakfast, lunch, and dinner are covered in the package price.","zh":"all meals included 指早餐、午餐和晚餐都包含在套票價格內。"},{"en":"A camp with all meals included is easier for parents to budget for.","zh":"包括所有餐膳的營地，讓家長更容易預算。"},{"en":"Including all meals reduces the need to search for food each day.","zh":"包括所有餐膳可以減少每天找食物的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining full-board arrangements.","zh":"解釋全膳安排時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"standard half-board basis","meaning":"標準半膳形式","examples":[{"en":"Austrian packages are usually offered on a standard half-board basis.","zh":"奧地利套票通常以標準半膳形式提供。"},{"en":"Standard half-board basis means the usual package includes accommodation plus breakfast and one main meal.","zh":"standard half-board basis 指慣常套票包括住宿、早餐和一餐正餐。"},{"en":"A family may choose a standard half-board basis so they can eat lunch while sightseeing.","zh":"家庭可能選擇標準半膳形式，這樣可以在觀光時外出吃午餐。"},{"en":"This arrangement keeps costs lower than full board while still providing convenience.","zh":"這種安排比全膳成本低，同時仍提供方便。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a common hotel meal plan.","zh":"描述常見酒店餐膳計劃時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in some cases","meaning":"在某些情況下","examples":[{"en":"Full board is offered in some cases.","zh":"在某些情況下會提供全膳住宿。"},{"en":"In some cases means in certain situations, but not all.","zh":"in some cases 指在某些情況下，但不是所有情況。"},{"en":"In some cases, students need extra speaking practice before interviews.","zh":"在某些情況下，學生面試前需要額外口語練習。"},{"en":"This phrase prevents overgeneralisation by showing that a point applies only sometimes.","zh":"這個短語顯示某點只在部分情況適用，防止過度概括。"},{"en":"It is useful when a rule has exceptions.","zh":"當規則有例外時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be willing to","meaning":"願意","examples":[{"en":"Hotel and restaurant owners were willing to lower their prices.","zh":"酒店和餐廳東主願意降低價格。"},{"en":"Be willing to do something means be ready or prepared to do it.","zh":"be willing to do something 指準備好或願意做某事。"},{"en":"A student who wants to improve must be willing to practise even after making mistakes.","zh":"想進步的學生必須願意在犯錯後仍繼續練習。"},{"en":"People are more willing to act when they see clear benefits.","zh":"當人們看見清楚好處，就更願意行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing readiness or openness.","zh":"討論準備程度或開放態度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"lower their prices","meaning":"降低價格","examples":[{"en":"Austrian businesses lowered their prices in summer.","zh":"奧地利商戶在夏季降低價格。"},{"en":"Lower their prices means reduce how much customers have to pay.","zh":"lower their prices 指減少顧客需要支付的金額。"},{"en":"A shop may lower its prices after a festival to sell remaining stock.","zh":"商店可能在節日後降低價格，以售出剩餘存貨。"},{"en":"Lower prices can attract customers who would otherwise choose cheaper alternatives.","zh":"較低價格可以吸引原本會選擇更便宜替代品的顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing discounts and affordability.","zh":"討論折扣和可負擔性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"slow at that time of year","meaning":"一年中那時生意淡靜","examples":[{"en":"Business was slow at that time of year.","zh":"一年中那時生意淡靜。"},{"en":"Slow at that time of year means there were fewer customers or sales during that season.","zh":"slow at that time of year 指在該季節顧客或銷售較少。"},{"en":"A tutoring centre may be slow during summer if students travel abroad.","zh":"如果學生到海外旅行，補習中心在夏季可能生意淡靜。"},{"en":"Businesses often reduce prices or create promotions during slow periods.","zh":"企業常在淡季減價或創造促銷活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when demand changes by season.","zh":"當需求因季節改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"extra custom","meaning":"額外客源","examples":[{"en":"Any extra custom in summer was welcomed.","zh":"夏季任何額外客源都受到歡迎。"},{"en":"Extra custom means additional customers or business.","zh":"extra custom 指額外顧客或生意。"},{"en":"A café near a school welcomes extra custom when parents attend sports day.","zh":"當家長參加運動會，學校附近咖啡店會歡迎額外客源。"},{"en":"Extra customers can turn an otherwise quiet period into a profitable one.","zh":"額外顧客可以把原本淡靜時期變成有利可圖時期。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when businesses receive more visitors than usual.","zh":"當企業獲得比平常更多訪客時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be offset by","meaning":"被……抵銷","examples":[{"en":"Losses could be offset by profits in winter.","zh":"損失可以被冬季利潤抵銷。"},{"en":"Be offset by something means be balanced or compensated for by it.","zh":"be offset by something 指被某事平衡或補償。"},{"en":"Higher rent may be offset by better sales if a shop moves to a busier street.","zh":"如果商店搬到更繁忙街道後銷售更好，較高租金可能被抵銷。"},{"en":"One source of income can reduce the damage caused by another weak area.","zh":"一個收入來源可以減少另一弱項造成的損害。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one factor balances another.","zh":"當一個因素平衡另一個因素時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"profits in winter","meaning":"冬季利潤","examples":[{"en":"Winter profits helped support Austrian tourism businesses.","zh":"冬季利潤幫助支撐奧地利旅遊企業。"},{"en":"Profits in winter are the money businesses earn after costs during the winter season.","zh":"profits in winter 指企業在冬季扣除成本後賺到的金錢。"},{"en":"A ski-rental shop may depend on profits in winter to survive the quiet summer months.","zh":"滑雪租賃店可能依賴冬季利潤來度過淡靜夏季。"},{"en":"Strong winter earnings can let businesses accept lower prices in other seasons.","zh":"強勁冬季收入可以讓企業在其他季節接受較低價格。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when seasonal income supports a business.","zh":"當季節性收入支撐企業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"at the levels it used to be","meaning":"達到以往的水平","examples":[{"en":"The option says winter trade was not at the levels it used to be.","zh":"這個選項說冬季生意沒有達到以往的水平。"},{"en":"At the levels it used to be means as high or strong as it was in the past.","zh":"at the levels it used to be 指像過去那樣高或強。"},{"en":"A restaurant’s lunchtime business may no longer be at the levels it used to be after offices move away.","zh":"辦公室搬走後，餐廳午市生意可能不再達到以往水平。"},{"en":"Falling below former levels can force businesses to find new customers.","zh":"跌破過去水平可以迫使企業尋找新顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing present performance with past performance.","zh":"比較現在和過去表現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"infer about","meaning":"推斷出……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what we can infer about the writer’s experience.","zh":"題目問我們可以推斷出作者的經歷是怎樣的。"},{"en":"Infer about something means work out information that is suggested but not directly stated.","zh":"infer about something 指推斷被暗示但沒有直接說出的資料。"},{"en":"If a student keeps yawning, a teacher may infer that the student is tired.","zh":"如果學生一直打呵欠，老師可能推斷學生很累。"},{"en":"Inference requires evidence, not random guessing.","zh":"推斷需要證據，而不是隨便猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading questions about implied meaning.","zh":"這個短語適用於關於隱含意思的閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"traditional package holidays","meaning":"傳統套票旅行","examples":[{"en":"The writer criticises traditional package holidays.","zh":"作者批評傳統套票旅行。"},{"en":"Traditional package holidays are older-style holiday deals, often to familiar resort destinations.","zh":"traditional package holidays 指較舊式的旅行套票，通常前往熟悉度假區。"},{"en":"A traditional package holiday may include a flight, hotel, beach resort, and little local exploration.","zh":"傳統套票旅行可能包括航班、酒店、海灘度假村和很少本地探索。"},{"en":"Such holidays can feel convenient but repetitive if the choices never change.","zh":"這類旅行可以方便，但如果選擇從不改變，就會感覺重複。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing older mass-tourism habits.","zh":"討論較舊的大眾旅遊習慣時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"pleasant experience","meaning":"愉快經驗","examples":[{"en":"The option describes package holidays as a pleasant experience.","zh":"這個選項把套票旅行描述為愉快經驗。"},{"en":"A pleasant experience is something enjoyable, comfortable, or agreeable.","zh":"pleasant experience 指令人享受、舒適或滿意的經歷。"},{"en":"A short walk by the river can be a pleasant experience after a stressful day.","zh":"壓力大的一天後，河邊短暫散步可以是愉快經驗。"},{"en":"Pleasant experiences make people more likely to repeat an activity.","zh":"愉快經驗令人更可能重複某活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing mild enjoyment.","zh":"描述溫和享受時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"providing good value for money","meaning":"物有所值","examples":[{"en":"The option says package holidays provide good value for money.","zh":"這個選項說套票旅行物有所值。"},{"en":"Providing good value for money means giving enough quality or benefit for the price paid.","zh":"providing good value for money 指以所付價格提供足夠質素或好處。"},{"en":"A lunch set provides good value for money if it is tasty, filling, and reasonably priced.","zh":"如果午餐套餐好吃、飽肚且價格合理，它就是物有所值。"},{"en":"Value depends on both cost and what customers receive in return.","zh":"價值取決於成本和顧客得到的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when judging whether a purchase is worth the price.","zh":"判斷購買是否值得時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be particularly fond of","meaning":"特別喜歡","examples":[{"en":"The writer does not seem particularly fond of beach holidays.","zh":"作者似乎不是特別喜歡海灘旅行。"},{"en":"Be particularly fond of something means like it very much.","zh":"be particularly fond of something 指非常喜歡某事物。"},{"en":"A student may be particularly fond of history because they enjoy stories about real people.","zh":"學生可能特別喜歡歷史，因為他享受關於真人的故事。"},{"en":"If someone is not fond of an activity, they may welcome alternatives.","zh":"如果某人不喜歡一項活動，他可能歡迎替代選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing personal preference.","zh":"描述個人偏好時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"seaside holiday destinations","meaning":"海邊旅行目的地","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to popular seaside holiday destinations.","zh":"題目提到熱門海邊旅行目的地。"},{"en":"Seaside holiday destinations are places by the sea where people go for holidays.","zh":"seaside holiday destinations 指位於海邊、供人度假的地方。"},{"en":"A town with beaches, seafood restaurants, and hotels can be a seaside holiday destination.","zh":"擁有海灘、海鮮餐廳和酒店的城鎮，可以是海邊旅行目的地。"},{"en":"Seaside destinations can become crowded when many travellers seek sun and sand.","zh":"當許多旅客追求陽光和沙灘，海邊目的地可能變得擠迫。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing beach-based tourism.","zh":"討論以海灘為基礎的旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"unimaginative and boring","meaning":"缺乏想像力且沉悶","examples":[{"en":"The writer finds traditional package holidays unimaginative and boring.","zh":"作者認為傳統套票旅行缺乏想像力且沉悶。"},{"en":"Unimaginative and boring means lacking creativity, variety, or interest.","zh":"unimaginative and boring 指缺乏創意、變化或趣味。"},{"en":"A lesson can become unimaginative and boring if every class uses the same worksheet.","zh":"如果每堂課都用同一份工作紙，課堂可能變得缺乏想像力且沉悶。"},{"en":"Repetition without new ideas makes people lose attention and enthusiasm.","zh":"沒有新想法的重複會令人失去注意力和熱情。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when criticising dull routines.","zh":"批評沉悶常規時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"until now","meaning":"直到現在","examples":[{"en":"The option says such holidays were enjoyed by the wealthy until now.","zh":"這個選項說這類旅行直到現在都由富人享受。"},{"en":"Until now means up to the present moment, with a possible change beginning now.","zh":"until now 指直到目前這一刻，而現在可能開始有變化。"},{"en":"Until now, the club met only online, but next month it will meet in person.","zh":"直到現在，這個學會只在網上聚會，但下月會面對面聚會。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a contrast between the past situation and a new development.","zh":"這個短語突出過去情況與新發展之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when something is starting to change.","zh":"當某事開始改變時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"suggest is surprising","meaning":"暗示令人驚訝的是","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what the writer suggests is surprising.","zh":"題目問作者暗示令人驚訝的是甚麼。"},{"en":"Suggest is surprising means imply that something is unexpected or contrary to assumptions.","zh":"suggest is surprising 指暗示某事出乎意料或違反假設。"},{"en":"A teacher may suggest it is surprising that the quietest student gave the strongest speech.","zh":"老師可能暗示令人驚訝的是最安靜的學生作出了最有力演講。"},{"en":"Writers often signal surprise when events do not match stereotypes.","zh":"當事件不符合刻板印象，作者常會暗示驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reading for implied attitude.","zh":"閱讀作者隱含態度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"welcome the opportunity to","meaning":"歡迎……的機會","examples":[{"en":"Budget travellers welcomed the opportunity to try a new vacation.","zh":"預算有限的旅客歡迎嘗試新假期的機會。"},{"en":"Welcome the opportunity to do something means be pleased to have the chance to do it.","zh":"welcome the opportunity to do something 指高興有機會做某事。"},{"en":"A student may welcome the opportunity to speak with native English speakers.","zh":"學生可能歡迎與英語母語者交談的機會。"},{"en":"People welcome opportunities when they feel fresh, useful, or previously unavailable.","zh":"當機會感覺新鮮、有用或以前無法得到，人們就會歡迎它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone responds positively to a new chance.","zh":"當某人正面回應新機會時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"try out a new kind of vacation","meaning":"嘗試一種新旅行方式","examples":[{"en":"Many travellers tried out a new kind of vacation in Austria.","zh":"許多旅客在奧地利嘗試一種新旅行方式。"},{"en":"Try out a new kind of vacation means test or experience a different style of holiday for the first time.","zh":"try out a new kind of vacation 指首次測試或體驗不同風格的假期。"},{"en":"A family used to beach trips may try out a farm holiday to see whether the children enjoy it.","zh":"習慣海灘旅行的家庭，可能嘗試農場假期，看看孩子是否喜歡。"},{"en":"Trying something new can change future travel habits if the experience is positive.","zh":"如果體驗正面，嘗試新事物可以改變未來旅行習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when travellers experiment with holiday style.","zh":"當旅客實驗旅行風格時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be true to the stereotype","meaning":"符合刻板印象","examples":[{"en":"The option says travellers were true to the stereotype.","zh":"這個選項說旅客符合刻板印象。"},{"en":"Be true to the stereotype means behave exactly as people unfairly or simply expect that group to behave.","zh":"be true to the stereotype 指行為完全符合人們對某群體的不公平或簡化期待。"},{"en":"A teenager who is lazy in class may seem true to a stereotype, but many teenagers work hard.","zh":"上課懶散的青少年可能看似符合刻板印象，但許多青少年很勤奮。"},{"en":"Stereotypes can be misleading because real people often behave differently.","zh":"刻板印象可能誤導，因為真實的人常有不同表現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing whether behaviour matches a public image.","zh":"討論行為是否符合公眾形象時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"portrayed by the media","meaning":"被媒體描繪","examples":[{"en":"Budget travellers are often portrayed by the media in a negative way.","zh":"預算有限的旅客常被媒體以負面方式描繪。"},{"en":"Portrayed by the media means shown or described by newspapers, television, websites, or social platforms.","zh":"portrayed by the media 指被報章、電視、網站或社交平台展示或描述。"},{"en":"Young people are sometimes portrayed by the media as careless, even when many are responsible.","zh":"年輕人有時被媒體描繪成粗心，即使許多人很負責任。"},{"en":"Media portrayals can shape public judgement before people meet the group themselves.","zh":"媒體描繪可以在人們親身接觸該群體前塑造公眾判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing image and representation.","zh":"討論形象和呈現方式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be prepared to pay more money","meaning":"願意付更多錢","examples":[{"en":"The option says travellers were prepared to pay more money.","zh":"這個選項說旅客願意付更多錢。"},{"en":"Be prepared to pay more money means be willing to spend extra for something better or different.","zh":"be prepared to pay more money 指願意為更好或不同的東西花額外金錢。"},{"en":"Parents may be prepared to pay more money for a safer school bus service.","zh":"家長可能願意付更多錢，以獲得更安全的校巴服務。"},{"en":"People accept higher prices when they believe the added value is worth it.","zh":"當人們相信額外價值值得，就會接受較高價格。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing willingness to spend extra.","zh":"討論額外付費意願時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"better-quality holiday","meaning":"質素較高的旅行","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to a better-quality holiday.","zh":"這個選項指質素較高的旅行。"},{"en":"A better-quality holiday is a holiday that offers better comfort, activities, service, scenery, or overall experience.","zh":"better-quality holiday 指提供更好舒適度、活動、服務、景色或整體體驗的假期。"},{"en":"A family may pay extra for a better-quality holiday with safer transport and cleaner rooms.","zh":"家庭可能額外付費，選擇交通更安全、房間更乾淨的質素較高旅行。"},{"en":"Higher quality can make a trip more relaxing, meaningful, and memorable.","zh":"較高質素可以令旅程更放鬆、有意義和難忘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing holiday standards.","zh":"比較假期標準時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"show good taste","meaning":"顯示有品味","examples":[{"en":"The travellers showed good taste by choosing Austria.","zh":"旅客選擇奧地利，顯示有品味。"},{"en":"Show good taste means make a choice that seems stylish, thoughtful, or culturally refined.","zh":"show good taste 指作出看似有格調、有想法或有文化修養的選擇。"},{"en":"A student may show good taste by choosing a simple, elegant design for a presentation.","zh":"學生為簡報選擇簡潔優雅的設計，可能顯示有品味。"},{"en":"Good taste is often judged by how carefully someone chooses, not by how much they spend.","zh":"好品味常由選擇有多仔細來判斷，而不是花了多少錢。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when praising someone’s choice.","zh":"讚賞某人的選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be credited with having","meaning":"被認為擁有……","examples":[{"en":"Budget travellers are not often credited with having good taste.","zh":"預算有限的旅客不常被認為擁有好品味。"},{"en":"Be credited with having something means be recognised as possessing that quality or achievement.","zh":"be credited with having something 指被承認擁有某特質或成就。"},{"en":"A quiet student may not be credited with having leadership skills until a group project reveals them.","zh":"安靜學生在小組專題顯示能力前，可能不被認為擁有領導才能。"},{"en":"People can be underestimated when others judge them by stereotypes.","zh":"當別人按刻板印象判斷，人們可能被低估。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when recognition is given or denied.","zh":"當承認被給予或被否定時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"health-conscious","meaning":"注重健康的","examples":[{"en":"The option describes travellers as health-conscious people.","zh":"這個選項把旅客描述為注重健康的人。"},{"en":"Health-conscious means careful about choices that affect health, such as exercise, food, sleep, and alcohol.","zh":"health-conscious 指重視影響健康的選擇，例如運動、飲食、睡眠和酒精。"},{"en":"A health-conscious student may choose water and a walk instead of sugary drinks and screen time.","zh":"注重健康的學生可能選擇喝水和散步，而不是含糖飲品和螢幕時間。"},{"en":"Health-conscious people often prefer activities that keep them active and well.","zh":"注重健康的人常較喜歡令自己保持活躍和健康的活動。"},{"en":"This word is useful when describing people who care about healthy living.","zh":"描述重視健康生活的人時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"as a rule","meaning":"一般而言","examples":[{"en":"The option says they are health-conscious as a rule.","zh":"這個選項說他們一般而言都注重健康。"},{"en":"As a rule means generally or in most cases.","zh":"as a rule 指一般而言或在大多數情況下。"},{"en":"As a rule, students learn vocabulary better when they see clear examples.","zh":"一般而言，學生看到清晰例子時，詞彙學得更好。"},{"en":"The phrase allows for exceptions while describing a normal pattern.","zh":"這個短語在描述一般模式時容許例外。"},{"en":"It is useful when making a general statement.","zh":"作一般陳述時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"match each statement to","meaning":"把每句陳述配對至……","examples":[{"en":"Students match each statement to the correct person.","zh":"學生把每句陳述配對至正確人物。"},{"en":"Match each statement to something means connect each sentence with the person, place, or idea it belongs to.","zh":"match each statement to something 指把每個句子連接到它所屬的人、地方或想法。"},{"en":"In a reading task, students may match each statement to the paragraph that contains the same idea.","zh":"在閱讀任務中，學生可能把每句陳述配對至包含相同意思的段落。"},{"en":"Matching requires careful evidence, not simply guessing by keywords.","zh":"配對需要仔細證據，而不是只靠關鍵字猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"use any letter more than once","meaning":"可多於一次使用任何字母","examples":[{"en":"Students may use any letter more than once.","zh":"學生可多於一次使用任何字母。"},{"en":"Use any letter more than once means the same answer option can be chosen for several questions.","zh":"use any letter more than once 指同一答案選項可以用於幾條題目。"},{"en":"In a matching exercise, two statements may both match person B, so students can use B twice.","zh":"在配對練習中，兩句陳述可能都配對人物 B，所以學生可以用 B 兩次。"},{"en":"This instruction prevents students from wrongly forcing each option to appear only once.","zh":"這個指示防止學生錯誤地強迫每個選項只出現一次。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in matching-task directions.","zh":"這個短語適用於配對題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"permanently alter","meaning":"永久改變","examples":[{"en":"Holiday experiences might encourage people to permanently alter their lifestyles.","zh":"旅行經歷可能鼓勵人們永久改變生活方式。"},{"en":"Permanently alter means change something in a lasting way, not just briefly.","zh":"permanently alter 指以持久方式改變某事，而不是短暫改變。"},{"en":"A serious illness may permanently alter a person’s eating and exercise habits.","zh":"嚴重疾病可能永久改變一個人的飲食和運動習慣。"},{"en":"Lasting change happens when a new experience becomes part of daily life.","zh":"當新體驗成為日常生活一部分，持久改變就會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a change is long-term.","zh":"當改變是長期的，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the way in which they live","meaning":"他們的生活方式","examples":[{"en":"The holiday may alter the way in which people live.","zh":"這個假期可能改變人們的生活方式。"},{"en":"The way in which they live means their lifestyle, habits, routines, and daily choices.","zh":"way in which they live 指他們的生活方式、習慣、日常規律和日常選擇。"},{"en":"A person may change the way they live by walking to work and cooking healthier meals.","zh":"一個人可能透過步行上班和煮更健康的飯菜來改變生活方式。"},{"en":"New experiences can influence daily behaviour after the original event ends.","zh":"新體驗可以在原本事件結束後影響日常行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing lifestyle change.","zh":"討論生活方式改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"another type of holiday","meaning":"另一類旅行","examples":[{"en":"One person used to go on another type of holiday for financial reasons.","zh":"有一個人過去因財務原因而去另一類旅行。"},{"en":"Another type of holiday means a different kind of vacation from the one currently being discussed.","zh":"another type of holiday 指不同於目前討論內容的另一種假期。"},{"en":"A family used to camping may try another type of holiday, such as a city break.","zh":"習慣露營的家庭可能嘗試另一類旅行，例如城市短途假期。"},{"en":"People choose different holiday types depending on money, interests, health, and family needs.","zh":"人們根據金錢、興趣、健康和家庭需要選擇不同旅行類型。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing travel styles.","zh":"比較旅行風格時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"could not afford the alternatives","meaning":"負擔不起其他選擇","examples":[{"en":"He chose beach holidays because he could not afford the alternatives.","zh":"他選擇海灘旅行，因為他負擔不起其他選擇。"},{"en":"Could not afford the alternatives means did not have enough money to choose the other options.","zh":"could not afford the alternatives 指沒有足夠金錢選擇其他選項。"},{"en":"A student may buy second-hand textbooks because they cannot afford the alternatives.","zh":"學生可能購買二手課本，因為負擔不起其他選擇。"},{"en":"Limited budgets can force people to choose what is cheapest rather than what they prefer.","zh":"有限預算可以迫使人選擇最便宜的，而不是自己最喜歡的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when financial limits control choice.","zh":"當財務限制控制選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"enjoy relaxing by the sea","meaning":"喜歡在海邊放鬆","examples":[{"en":"One person enjoys relaxing by the sea.","zh":"有一個人喜歡在海邊放鬆。"},{"en":"Enjoy relaxing by the sea means like resting near the ocean, often while sitting, walking, or sunbathing.","zh":"enjoy relaxing by the sea 指喜歡在海邊休息，通常是坐着、散步或日光浴。"},{"en":"A tired worker may enjoy relaxing by the sea because the waves feel calming.","zh":"疲倦工人可能喜歡在海邊放鬆，因為海浪令人平靜。"},{"en":"Relaxing by the sea can reduce stress, but it may become boring if every holiday is the same.","zh":"在海邊放鬆可以減壓，但如果每個假期都一樣，就可能變得沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a preference for seaside rest.","zh":"描述對海邊休息的偏好時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"illustrate to their children that","meaning":"向子女說明","examples":[{"en":"He wanted to illustrate to his children that other holidays were possible.","zh":"他想向子女說明其他類型的旅行也是可能的。"},{"en":"Illustrate to their children that means show children clearly through example or experience.","zh":"illustrate to their children that 指透過例子或經驗向孩子清楚展示某事。"},{"en":"Parents may illustrate to their children that reading is enjoyable by reading together every night.","zh":"父母可能透過每晚一起閱讀，向子女說明閱讀是愉快的。"},{"en":"Children often understand ideas better when adults show them, not just tell them.","zh":"當成年人展示而不只是告訴，孩子常更能理解想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when teaching through experience.","zh":"透過經驗教導時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"other types of holidays","meaning":"其他類型的旅行","examples":[{"en":"He wanted his children to experience other types of holidays.","zh":"他希望孩子體驗其他類型的旅行。"},{"en":"Other types of holidays are different styles of vacation, such as mountain trips, city breaks, or cultural tours.","zh":"other types of holidays 指不同風格的假期，例如山區旅行、城市短途假期或文化遊。"},{"en":"A family may try other types of holidays after becoming bored with beach resorts.","zh":"家庭厭倦海灘度假村後，可能嘗試其他類型的旅行。"},{"en":"Different holiday types can teach children different skills, interests, and ways to relax.","zh":"不同旅行類型可以教孩子不同技能、興趣和放鬆方式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing travel choices.","zh":"比較旅行選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"find it hard to explain","meaning":"覺得難以解釋","examples":[{"en":"One person found it hard to explain why he did not feel tired.","zh":"有一個人覺得難以解釋為何自己不累。"},{"en":"Find it hard to explain means have difficulty giving a clear reason for something.","zh":"find it hard to explain 指很難清楚說明某事的原因。"},{"en":"A student may find it hard to explain why they understand grammar in class but forget it in exams.","zh":"學生可能覺得難以解釋為何在課堂懂文法，但考試時忘記。"},{"en":"Some experiences are surprising because they do not match what people expect.","zh":"有些經歷令人驚訝，因為它們不符合人們預期。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when feelings or results are difficult to describe.","zh":"當感受或結果難以描述時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"feel drained","meaning":"感到筋疲力盡","examples":[{"en":"He did not feel drained despite a very active week.","zh":"儘管一星期非常活躍，他並沒有感到筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"Feel drained means feel extremely tired, as if all energy has been used up.","zh":"feel drained 指感到極度疲倦，好像所有精力都用完。"},{"en":"A nurse may feel drained after a long night shift with little rest.","zh":"護士在休息很少的長夜班後，可能感到筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"People usually feel drained after heavy work, so feeling refreshed after activity can be surprising.","zh":"人們通常在辛苦工作後筋疲力盡，所以活動後反而精神可以令人驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing physical or mental exhaustion.","zh":"描述身體或精神疲憊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"despite how busy","meaning":"儘管多麼忙碌","examples":[{"en":"He felt refreshed despite how busy his week was.","zh":"儘管那一星期多麼忙碌，他仍感到精神煥發。"},{"en":"Despite how busy means although the amount of activity or work was great.","zh":"despite how busy 指雖然活動或工作量很大。"},{"en":"Despite how busy the exam week was, the student still found time to exercise.","zh":"儘管考試週多麼忙碌，學生仍找到時間運動。"},{"en":"This phrase creates contrast between heavy activity and an unexpected result.","zh":"這個短語在大量活動和意外結果之間建立對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when something good happens even with a demanding schedule.","zh":"當行程繁重但仍有好結果時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"weather conditions","meaning":"天氣情況","examples":[{"en":"One person found the weather conditions better than expected.","zh":"有一個人覺得天氣情況比預期好。"},{"en":"Weather conditions are the state of the weather, such as temperature, rain, wind, sunshine, or snow.","zh":"weather conditions 指天氣狀態，例如溫度、雨、風、陽光或雪。"},{"en":"A school picnic may be cancelled if weather conditions become unsafe.","zh":"如果天氣情況變得不安全，學校野餐可能取消。"},{"en":"Good weather conditions can make outdoor holidays more enjoyable and easier to plan.","zh":"良好天氣情況可以令戶外假期更愉快和更容易規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when weather affects activities.","zh":"當天氣影響活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"more favourable than expected","meaning":"比預期更理想","examples":[{"en":"The weather was more favourable than expected.","zh":"天氣比預期更理想。"},{"en":"More favourable than expected means better or more helpful than people thought it would be.","zh":"more favourable than expected 指比人們原本以為的更好或更有幫助。"},{"en":"A student may find the interview more favourable than expected if the questions are friendly.","zh":"如果問題友善，學生可能覺得面試比預期更理想。"},{"en":"Positive surprises can change how people remember an experience.","zh":"正面驚喜可以改變人們如何記住一段經歷。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reality is better than prediction.","zh":"當現實比預測更好時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與資料相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether statements agree with the information in the passage.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與文章資料相符。"},{"en":"Agree with the information means match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information 指符合文章所說內容。"},{"en":"A statement agrees with the information if the text clearly supports it.","zh":"如果文本清楚支持某陳述，它就與資料相符。"},{"en":"Students should check the exact meaning, not just similar words.","zh":"學生應檢查準確意思，而不只是相似字眼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語適用於 TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the views of the writer","meaning":"作者的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The final questions ask about the views of the writer.","zh":"最後幾題詢問作者的觀點。"},{"en":"The views of the writer are the opinions, attitudes, or arguments expressed by the author.","zh":"views of the writer 指作者表達的意見、態度或論點。"},{"en":"Students identify the writer’s views by looking at tone, examples, and clear statements.","zh":"學生透過語氣、例子和明確陳述來辨認作者觀點。"},{"en":"Understanding the writer’s view helps readers choose between TRUE, FALSE, and NOT GIVEN.","zh":"理解作者觀點有助讀者在 TRUE、FALSE 和 NOT GIVEN 之間選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when questions test opinion rather than simple facts.","zh":"當題目測試意見而不是簡單事實時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the views of the writer.","zh":"一個陳述可能與作者觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradict the views of someone means express the opposite of that person’s opinion or argument.","zh":"contradict the views of someone 指表達與某人意見或論點相反的意思。"},{"en":"If a writer praises active holidays, a statement saying he dislikes them may contradict his views.","zh":"如果作者讚賞活躍假期，而陳述說他不喜歡它們，就可能與其觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students must find clear disagreement in the passage before choosing FALSE or NO.","zh":"學生必須在文章中找到清楚分歧，才選 FALSE 或 NO。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when checking whether a statement opposes the author.","zh":"檢查陳述是否反對作者時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Students write NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"如果無法判斷作者想法，學生寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide clearly.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資料清楚判斷。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions ticket refunds, it is impossible to say whether tourists received them.","zh":"如果文章從未提到機票退款，就無法判斷遊客是否收到退款。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from background knowledge when the text gives no evidence.","zh":"當文本沒有證據時，學生不應根據背景知識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the answer cannot be proven from the passage.","zh":"當答案不能由文章證明時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"a reduction in the cost of","meaning":"……成本下降","examples":[{"en":"A reduction in the cost of flying helped Austria attract budget travellers.","zh":"飛行成本下降幫助奧地利吸引預算有限的旅客。"},{"en":"A reduction in the cost of something means it becomes cheaper.","zh":"reduction in the cost of something 指某事變得較便宜。"},{"en":"A reduction in the cost of textbooks can help more students buy their own copies.","zh":"課本成本下降可以幫助更多學生購買自己的課本。"},{"en":"Lower costs can open opportunities to people who were previously priced out.","zh":"成本降低可以為以前因價格而被排除的人打開機會。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when cheaper prices change behaviour.","zh":"當較低價格改變行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"play a role in","meaning":"在……中起作用","examples":[{"en":"Budget flights played a role in Austria’s popularity.","zh":"廉價航班在奧地利受歡迎方面起了作用。"},{"en":"Play a role in something means be one of the factors that contributes to it.","zh":"play a role in something 指作為促成某事的其中一個因素。"},{"en":"Good teachers play a role in helping students gain confidence.","zh":"好老師在幫助學生建立信心方面起作用。"},{"en":"A result usually has several causes, and each may play a different role.","zh":"一個結果通常有幾個原因，而每個原因可能有不同作用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining contributing factors.","zh":"解釋促成因素時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"overtake traditional beach package holidays","meaning":"超越傳統海灘套票旅行","examples":[{"en":"The statement says Austrian holidays have overtaken traditional beach holidays.","zh":"這個陳述說奧地利旅行已超越傳統海灘套票旅行。"},{"en":"Overtake traditional beach package holidays means become more popular or successful than the usual beach package trips.","zh":"overtake traditional beach package holidays 指變得比慣常海灘套票旅行更受歡迎或更成功。"},{"en":"Online courses may overtake printed workbooks if students find them cheaper and clearer.","zh":"如果學生覺得網上課程更便宜和更清楚，它們可能超越紙本工作冊。"},{"en":"To overtake an old option, a new option must attract more users or customers.","zh":"要超越舊選項，新選項必須吸引更多使用者或顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing popularity between old and new choices.","zh":"比較新舊選擇受歡迎程度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"in terms of popularity","meaning":"就受歡迎程度而言","examples":[{"en":"The statement compares holidays in terms of popularity.","zh":"這個陳述就受歡迎程度而言比較不同旅行。"},{"en":"In terms of popularity means judged by how many people like, choose, or talk about something.","zh":"in terms of popularity 指根據有多少人喜歡、選擇或談論某事來判斷。"},{"en":"In terms of popularity, bubble tea may be stronger than ordinary tea among teenagers.","zh":"就受歡迎程度而言，珍珠奶茶在青少年之中可能比普通茶更強。"},{"en":"Popularity can change quickly when prices, fashion, or social media attention change.","zh":"當價格、潮流或社交媒體關注改變，受歡迎程度可以快速改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing how widely liked things are.","zh":"比較事物受喜愛程度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"聚焦於","examples":[{"en":"The statement says beach holidays are less focused on drinking.","zh":"這個陳述說海灘旅行較少聚焦於飲酒。"},{"en":"Focus on something means give main attention to it.","zh":"focus on something 指把主要注意力放在某事上。"},{"en":"A school may focus on reading skills before moving to writing practice.","zh":"學校可能先聚焦於閱讀技巧，再轉向寫作練習。"},{"en":"What a holiday focuses on affects whether it feels active, cultural, relaxing, or unhealthy.","zh":"假期聚焦於甚麼，會影響它感覺活躍、文化化、放鬆還是不健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the main emphasis of an activity.","zh":"描述活動主要重點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"unhealthy activities","meaning":"不健康活動","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to drinking and other unhealthy activities.","zh":"這個陳述提到飲酒和其他不健康活動。"},{"en":"Unhealthy activities are actions that can harm the body or mind if done often or excessively.","zh":"unhealthy activities 指如果經常或過度進行，可能傷害身心的行為。"},{"en":"Staying up late, drinking too much alcohol, and sitting all day are unhealthy activities.","zh":"熬夜、過量飲酒和整天坐着都是不健康活動。"},{"en":"Too many unhealthy activities can reduce energy and increase long-term health risks.","zh":"太多不健康活動可以降低精力並增加長期健康風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing habits that damage well-being.","zh":"討論損害身心健康的習慣時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"provide a wider choice of","meaning":"提供更廣泛的……選擇","examples":[{"en":"The statement says beach holidays provide a wider choice of activities.","zh":"這個陳述說海灘旅行提供更廣泛的活動選擇。"},{"en":"Provide a wider choice of something means offer more different options.","zh":"provide a wider choice of something 指提供更多不同選項。"},{"en":"A school can provide a wider choice of clubs by adding drama, chess, coding, and hiking.","zh":"學校可以透過加入戲劇、棋藝、編程和行山，提供更廣泛的學會選擇。"},{"en":"More choice can make people feel freer and more likely to find something they enjoy.","zh":"更多選擇可以令人感覺更自由，也更可能找到自己享受的事。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when variety is being compared.","zh":"比較多樣性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"in general","meaning":"一般而言","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to beach holidays in general.","zh":"這個陳述一般而言提到海灘旅行。"},{"en":"In general means usually, overall, or without focusing on special cases.","zh":"in general 指通常、整體而言，或不聚焦於特殊個案。"},{"en":"In general, students learn better when examples are clear and connected to daily life.","zh":"一般而言，當例子清楚並連接日常生活，學生會學得更好。"},{"en":"General statements may have exceptions, so readers should not treat them as absolute rules.","zh":"一般陳述可能有例外，所以讀者不應把它們視為絕對規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when making a broad point.","zh":"作出廣泛觀點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 87 - Austria - The burgeoning budget holiday attraction.pdf","sourcePage":22}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 88":[{"front":"continents collide","meaning":"大陸碰撞","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains what happens when continents collide.","zh":"文章解釋大陸碰撞時會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"When continents collide, huge landmasses push against each other over millions of years.","zh":"當大陸碰撞時，巨大陸塊會在數百萬年間互相擠壓。"},{"en":"In geography class, students may draw two plates moving together to show how continents collide.","zh":"在地理課中，學生可能畫出兩個板塊靠近，以展示大陸碰撞。"},{"en":"When continents collide, rocks can fold, rise, and form mountain ranges.","zh":"當大陸碰撞時，岩石會褶皺、上升並形成山脈。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a slow but powerful geological crash, not a sudden accident.","zh":"這個短語描述緩慢但強大的地質碰撞，而不是突然意外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the idea that","meaning":"……這一想法","examples":[{"en":"The idea that the continents are moving was first proposed by Alfred Wegener.","zh":"大陸正在移動這一想法最初由 Alfred Wegener 提出。"},{"en":"The idea that introduces a belief, theory, or claim.","zh":"「the idea that」用來引出一個信念、理論或主張。"},{"en":"The idea that students learn better through practice is common among teachers.","zh":"學生透過練習學得更好這一想法，在老師之間很常見。"},{"en":"If the idea that something is true gains evidence, more people may accept it.","zh":"如果某一想法獲得證據支持，更多人可能接受它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for introducing a theory clearly.","zh":"這個短語適合用來清楚引入理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"continents are moving","meaning":"大陸正在移動","examples":[{"en":"The idea that the continents are moving changed geology.","zh":"大陸正在移動這一想法改變了地質學。"},{"en":"Continents are moving means the Earth’s large landmasses slowly change position over time.","zh":"「continents are moving」意思是地球上的巨大陸塊會隨時間慢慢改變位置。"},{"en":"Students can see evidence that continents are moving by comparing matching coastlines.","zh":"學生可以透過比較相配的海岸線，看見大陸正在移動的證據。"},{"en":"Because continents are moving, oceans can open and mountains can form.","zh":"因為大陸正在移動，海洋可以打開，山脈可以形成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extremely slow movement across geological time.","zh":"這個短語描述地質時間中的極慢移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be first proposed by","meaning":"最初由……提出","examples":[{"en":"The theory was first proposed by a German meteorologist.","zh":"該理論最初由一位德國氣象學家提出。"},{"en":"To be first proposed by someone means to be originally suggested by that person.","zh":"「be first proposed by」某人，意思是最初由該人提出。"},{"en":"A new school rule may be first proposed by a teacher before the principal approves it.","zh":"新校規可能先由老師提出，再由校長批准。"},{"en":"If an idea is first proposed without enough evidence, people may reject it at first.","zh":"如果一個想法最初提出時證據不足，人們可能一開始拒絕它。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the original source of an idea.","zh":"這個短語指出想法的原始來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"German meteorologist","meaning":"德國氣象學家","examples":[{"en":"Alfred Wegener was a German meteorologist.","zh":"Alfred Wegener 是一位德國氣象學家。"},{"en":"A German meteorologist is a weather scientist from Germany.","zh":"「German meteorologist」是來自德國的天氣科學家。"},{"en":"A meteorologist studies weather, climate, air pressure, winds, and storms.","zh":"氣象學家研究天氣、氣候、氣壓、風和暴風雨。"},{"en":"Although Wegener studied weather, his idea became important in geology.","zh":"雖然 Wegener 研究天氣，他的想法後來在地質學中變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes Wegener’s nationality and scientific background.","zh":"這個短語描述 Wegener 的國籍和科學背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Alfred Wegener","meaning":"阿爾弗雷德・魏格納","examples":[{"en":"Alfred Wegener proposed that the continents were moving.","zh":"Alfred Wegener 提出大陸正在移動。"},{"en":"Alfred Wegener was the scientist who developed the early theory of continental drift.","zh":"Alfred Wegener 是發展早期大陸漂移理論的科學家。"},{"en":"In a geology lesson, Wegener is often introduced before plate tectonics.","zh":"在地質課中，Wegener 通常在板塊構造論之前被介紹。"},{"en":"His theory was rejected at first because he could not explain the force behind the movement.","zh":"他的理論最初被拒絕，因為他無法解釋移動背後的力量。"},{"en":"The name is linked with one of the great turning points in Earth science.","zh":"這個名字與地球科學的一個重大轉折點有關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a book published in","meaning":"於……出版的書","examples":[{"en":"Wegener presented his idea in a book published in 1915.","zh":"Wegener 在一本於1915年出版的書中提出其想法。"},{"en":"A book published in a year is a book that came out in that year.","zh":"「a book published in」某年，是在該年面世的書。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to read a novel published in the nineteenth century.","zh":"老師可能要求學生閱讀一本於十九世紀出版的小說。"},{"en":"If an idea appears in a book, it can reach a wider scientific audience.","zh":"如果想法出現在書中，它可以接觸更廣泛的科學讀者。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the date when a written work became public.","zh":"這個短語提供書面作品公開面世的日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"gather a great deal of","meaning":"收集大量……","examples":[{"en":"Wegener had gathered a great deal of careful evidence.","zh":"Wegener 已收集大量仔細證據。"},{"en":"To gather a great deal of something means to collect a large amount of it.","zh":"「gather a great deal of」某物，意思是收集大量該物。"},{"en":"A student may gather a great deal of information before writing a research report.","zh":"學生在寫研究報告前可能收集大量資料。"},{"en":"If scientists gather enough evidence, a weak idea can become more convincing.","zh":"如果科學家收集足夠證據，一個薄弱想法可以變得更有說服力。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses careful collection in large quantity.","zh":"這個短語強調大量而仔細的收集。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"careful and tantalising evidence","meaning":"仔細而引人入勝的證據","examples":[{"en":"He gathered careful and tantalising evidence for continental movement.","zh":"他為大陸移動收集了仔細而引人入勝的證據。"},{"en":"Careful and tantalising evidence is detailed evidence that strongly suggests something interesting but may not yet prove everything.","zh":"「careful and tantalising evidence」是詳細而強烈暗示某有趣事情、但未必完全證明一切的證據。"},{"en":"A detective may find careful and tantalising evidence that points to a suspect.","zh":"偵探可能找到仔細而引人入勝的證據，指向某個嫌疑人。"},{"en":"If evidence is tantalising, people want to know more because it hints at a bigger truth.","zh":"如果證據引人入勝，人們會想知道更多，因為它暗示更大的真相。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence that is both serious and intriguing.","zh":"這個短語描述既嚴謹又令人好奇的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the most obvious being","meaning":"最明顯的是","examples":[{"en":"He offered several clues, the most obvious being the shape of the continents.","zh":"他提出了幾個線索，最明顯的是大陸的形狀。"},{"en":"The most obvious being introduces the clearest example among several points.","zh":"「the most obvious being」用來引出多點之中最清楚的例子。"},{"en":"The school has many problems, the most obvious being the lack of classrooms.","zh":"學校有許多問題，最明顯的是課室不足。"},{"en":"If one clue is easy to see, writers may present it as the most obvious evidence.","zh":"如果一個線索很容易看見，作者可能把它作為最明顯證據。"},{"en":"The phrase helps highlight the strongest or clearest example.","zh":"這個短語幫助突出最強或最清楚的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"simple observation","meaning":"簡單觀察","examples":[{"en":"The theory began with a simple observation about landmasses.","zh":"該理論始於對陸塊的一個簡單觀察。"},{"en":"A simple observation is something easy to notice by looking carefully.","zh":"「simple observation」是仔細觀看後容易注意到的事情。"},{"en":"A student may make a simple observation that plants near the window grow faster.","zh":"學生可能作出一個簡單觀察：靠近窗邊的植物長得更快。"},{"en":"Simple observations can lead to big questions when people think deeply about them.","zh":"當人們深入思考，簡單觀察可以引出重大問題。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that science can begin with something ordinary.","zh":"這個短語顯示科學可以始於平凡事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"great landmasses","meaning":"巨大陸塊","examples":[{"en":"The great landmasses of the world seem to fit together.","zh":"世界上的巨大陸塊看似能拼合在一起。"},{"en":"Great landmasses are very large areas of land, such as continents.","zh":"「great landmasses」是非常大片的土地，例如大陸。"},{"en":"On a world map, students can compare great landmasses like Africa and South America.","zh":"在世界地圖上，學生可以比較非洲和南美洲等巨大陸塊。"},{"en":"If large landmasses seem to match, scientists may ask whether they were once joined.","zh":"如果大型陸塊看似相配，科學家可能會問它們是否曾經相連。"},{"en":"The phrase describes huge pieces of Earth’s land surface.","zh":"這個短語描述地球陸地表面的巨大部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"seem to fit together","meaning":"看似能拼合在一起","examples":[{"en":"The continents seem to fit together like pieces of a puzzle.","zh":"大陸看似像拼圖碎片一樣能拼合在一起。"},{"en":"To seem to fit together means to appear as if separate parts match in shape or position.","zh":"「seem to fit together」意思是分開的部分看起來在形狀或位置上相配。"},{"en":"Two broken pieces of a cup may seem to fit together when their edges match.","zh":"當邊緣吻合時，杯子的兩塊碎片可能看似能拼合在一起。"},{"en":"If coastlines seem to fit together, they may suggest a shared geological past.","zh":"如果海岸線看似能拼合在一起，它們可能暗示共同地質過去。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visual matching, not final proof by itself.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺上的相配，本身不是最終證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"jigsaw-like","meaning":"像拼圖一樣","examples":[{"en":"The continents fit together in a jigsaw-like way.","zh":"大陸以像拼圖一樣的方式拼合。"},{"en":"Jigsaw-like means resembling pieces of a puzzle that can fit together.","zh":"「jigsaw-like」意思是像能拼合在一起的拼圖碎片。"},{"en":"A broken plate may have jigsaw-like edges after it falls on the floor.","zh":"碟子跌在地上後，破裂邊緣可能像拼圖一樣。"},{"en":"If coastlines look jigsaw-like, they appear to match across an ocean.","zh":"如果海岸線像拼圖一樣，它們看似跨越海洋互相吻合。"},{"en":"The phrase uses a puzzle image to describe matching shapes.","zh":"這個短語用拼圖意象描述相配形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a striking example","meaning":"顯著例子","examples":[{"en":"The Atlantic coastlines provide a striking example.","zh":"大西洋海岸線提供了一個顯著例子。"},{"en":"A striking example is an example that is very clear, noticeable, or impressive.","zh":"「a striking example」是非常清楚、明顯或令人印象深刻的例子。"},{"en":"A school with no library is a striking example of poor educational resources.","zh":"沒有圖書館的學校，是教育資源不足的顯著例子。"},{"en":"If an example is striking, it helps readers understand the argument quickly.","zh":"如果例子顯著，它能幫助讀者快速理解論點。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence that is hard to ignore.","zh":"這個短語引出難以忽視的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the coastlines of either side of","meaning":"……兩邊的海岸線","examples":[{"en":"The coastlines of either side of the Atlantic Ocean seem to match.","zh":"大西洋兩邊的海岸線看似相配。"},{"en":"The coastlines of either side of something means the shorelines on both sides of it.","zh":"「the coastlines of either side of」某物，意思是它兩邊的海岸線。"},{"en":"Students can compare the coastlines of either side of a narrow sea on a map.","zh":"學生可以在地圖上比較狹窄海域兩邊的海岸線。"},{"en":"If coastlines on two sides match, they may suggest the land was once connected.","zh":"如果兩邊海岸線相配，它們可能暗示陸地曾經相連。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on matching edges across a body of water.","zh":"這個短語集中於水域兩側相配的邊緣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the Atlantic Ocean","meaning":"大西洋","examples":[{"en":"The coastlines on either side of the Atlantic Ocean seem to fit together.","zh":"大西洋兩邊的海岸線看似能拼合在一起。"},{"en":"The Atlantic Ocean is the large ocean between the Americas and Europe and Africa.","zh":"「the Atlantic Ocean」是位於美洲與歐洲、非洲之間的大洋。"},{"en":"On a map, the Atlantic Ocean separates South America from Africa.","zh":"在地圖上，大西洋把南美洲與非洲分隔開。"},{"en":"If the two sides of the Atlantic seem to match, they can support continental-drift ideas.","zh":"如果大西洋兩邊看似相配，它們可以支持大陸漂移的想法。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major ocean used in Wegener’s evidence.","zh":"這個短語指出 Wegener 證據中使用的一個主要海洋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be able to theorise","meaning":"能夠提出理論認為","examples":[{"en":"Wegener was able to theorise that the continents were once joined.","zh":"Wegener 能夠提出理論認為大陸曾經相連。"},{"en":"To be able to theorise means to form a reasoned explanation from evidence.","zh":"「be able to theorise」意思是能根據證據形成有理據的解釋。"},{"en":"A doctor may be able to theorise the cause of illness after seeing several symptoms.","zh":"醫生看見幾個症狀後，可能能夠提出病因理論。"},{"en":"If evidence points in one direction, scientists can develop a theory from it.","zh":"如果證據指向同一方向，科學家可以由此發展理論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes building an explanation, not merely guessing.","zh":"這個短語描述建立解釋，而不只是猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be assembled into","meaning":"被組合成","examples":[{"en":"All the continents were once assembled into a supercontinent.","zh":"所有大陸曾經被組合成一個超級大陸。"},{"en":"To be assembled into something means to be brought together to form a larger whole.","zh":"「be assembled into」某物，意思是被聚集起來形成更大的整體。"},{"en":"Several desks can be assembled into one large table for group work.","zh":"幾張書桌可以被組合成一張大桌，供小組活動使用。"},{"en":"If many landmasses are assembled into one body, a supercontinent forms.","zh":"如果許多陸塊被組合成一體，就會形成超級大陸。"},{"en":"The phrase describes separate parts being joined together.","zh":"這個短語描述分開部分被合併。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a supercontinent","meaning":"超級大陸","examples":[{"en":"Pangaea was a supercontinent made up of all the continents.","zh":"盤古大陸是一個由所有大陸組成的超級大陸。"},{"en":"A supercontinent is a huge landmass formed when most or all continents are joined.","zh":"「a supercontinent」是當大多數或所有大陸相連時形成的巨大陸塊。"},{"en":"In a geography lesson, Pangaea is often used as the example of a supercontinent.","zh":"在地理課中，盤古大陸常被用作超級大陸的例子。"},{"en":"When a supercontinent breaks apart, new oceans and continents can form.","zh":"當超級大陸分裂時，新的海洋和大陸可以形成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a continent much larger than any modern one.","zh":"這個短語描述比任何現代大陸都大得多的大陸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Pangaea","meaning":"盤古大陸","examples":[{"en":"Pangaea later broke up into Laurasia and Gondwana.","zh":"盤古大陸後來分裂成勞亞古陸和岡瓦納古陸。"},{"en":"Pangaea was an ancient supercontinent that included the world’s major landmasses.","zh":"「Pangaea」是一個古代超級大陸，包含世界主要陸塊。"},{"en":"Students may draw Pangaea to understand how modern continents once fitted together.","zh":"學生可能畫出盤古大陸，以理解現代大陸曾如何拼合。"},{"en":"When Pangaea broke apart, the continents slowly moved toward their present positions.","zh":"當盤古大陸分裂，各大陸慢慢移向今天的位置。"},{"en":"The name is central to the theory of continental drift.","zh":"這個名稱是大陸漂移理論的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"break up into","meaning":"分裂成","examples":[{"en":"Pangaea broke up into Laurasia and Gondwana.","zh":"盤古大陸分裂成勞亞古陸和岡瓦納古陸。"},{"en":"To break up into parts means to divide into smaller pieces or groups.","zh":"「break up into」幾部分，意思是分成較小部分或小組。"},{"en":"A large class may break up into smaller groups for discussion.","zh":"大班可能分裂成較小小組進行討論。"},{"en":"When a landmass breaks up, separate pieces can move in different directions.","zh":"當陸塊分裂，分開的部分可以向不同方向移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes division from one whole into several parts.","zh":"這個短語描述由一個整體分成幾部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Laurasia","meaning":"勞亞古陸","examples":[{"en":"Laurasia later became North America and Eurasia.","zh":"勞亞古陸後來成為北美洲和歐亞大陸。"},{"en":"Laurasia was the northern part of the ancient supercontinent after Pangaea split.","zh":"「Laurasia」是盤古大陸分裂後的北部古陸。"},{"en":"In geology, Laurasia helps explain links between northern continents.","zh":"在地質學中，勞亞古陸幫助解釋北方大陸之間的關聯。"},{"en":"If fossils match across areas once in Laurasia, they can support ancient connections.","zh":"如果曾屬勞亞古陸的地區有相配化石，它們可以支持古代連結。"},{"en":"The name refers to an old landmass, not a modern country.","zh":"這個名稱指古陸，而不是現代國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Gondwana","meaning":"岡瓦納古陸","examples":[{"en":"Gondwana later became the remaining southern continents.","zh":"岡瓦納古陸後來成為其餘南方大陸。"},{"en":"Gondwana was a southern ancient landmass formed after Pangaea split.","zh":"「Gondwana」是盤古大陸分裂後形成的南方古陸。"},{"en":"South America, Africa, Antarctica, India, and Australia were linked to Gondwana.","zh":"南美洲、非洲、南極洲、印度和澳洲都與岡瓦納古陸有關。"},{"en":"Similar fossils across these areas helped scientists infer Gondwana’s existence.","zh":"這些地區相似化石幫助科學家推斷岡瓦納古陸存在。"},{"en":"The word names an ancient continent important to Earth history.","zh":"這個詞指出地球歷史中重要的古大陸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the remaining continents","meaning":"其餘大陸","examples":[{"en":"Gondwana became the remaining continents.","zh":"岡瓦納古陸成為其餘大陸。"},{"en":"The remaining continents means the continents left after others have been mentioned or separated.","zh":"「the remaining continents」意思是在其他大陸已被提及或分出後剩下的大陸。"},{"en":"If North America and Eurasia are discussed first, the remaining continents include others such as Africa and Australia.","zh":"如果先討論北美洲和歐亞大陸，其餘大陸包括非洲和澳洲等。"},{"en":"In a classification task, “remaining” helps avoid listing the same items again.","zh":"在分類任務中，“remaining” 有助避免再次列出相同項目。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what is left in a group.","zh":"這個短語指一組中剩下的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"propulsive force","meaning":"推動力","examples":[{"en":"Wegener could not propose a propulsive force for continental movement.","zh":"Wegener 無法為大陸移動提出推動力。"},{"en":"A propulsive force is a force that pushes or drives something forward.","zh":"「propulsive force」是推動或驅動某物向前的力量。"},{"en":"In a boat, the engine provides the propulsive force that moves it through water.","zh":"在船上，引擎提供使船穿過水面的推動力。"},{"en":"If a theory cannot explain the force behind movement, scientists may doubt it.","zh":"如果理論不能解釋移動背後的力量，科學家可能懷疑它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the power that causes motion.","zh":"這個短語描述造成運動的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"apart from","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"He had no explanation apart from a vague suggestion about centrifugal force.","zh":"除了關於離心力的模糊說法外，他沒有解釋。"},{"en":"Apart from means except for or other than.","zh":"「apart from」意思是除了或不同於。"},{"en":"Apart from one grammar mistake, the essay was very clear.","zh":"除了一個文法錯誤外，文章非常清楚。"},{"en":"If a person has no evidence apart from a guess, the argument remains weak.","zh":"如果某人除了一個猜測外沒有證據，論點仍然薄弱。"},{"en":"The phrase separates one exception from the rest.","zh":"這個短語把一個例外與其餘部分分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"vague and erroneous suggestion","meaning":"模糊而錯誤的說法","examples":[{"en":"His explanation involved a vague and erroneous suggestion.","zh":"他的解釋包含一個模糊而錯誤的說法。"},{"en":"A vague and erroneous suggestion is an unclear idea that is also wrong.","zh":"「vague and erroneous suggestion」是不清楚而且錯誤的想法。"},{"en":"Saying “study more somehow” is vague, and saying grammar does not matter is erroneous.","zh":"說「總之多溫習」很模糊，而說文法不重要則是錯誤的。"},{"en":"If an explanation is vague and wrong, it will not convince careful readers.","zh":"如果解釋模糊又錯誤，它不能說服仔細的讀者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a weak and inaccurate proposal.","zh":"這個短語描述薄弱而不準確的提議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"centrifugal force","meaning":"離心力","examples":[{"en":"Wegener suggested that centrifugal force might move the continents.","zh":"Wegener 提出離心力可能移動大陸。"},{"en":"Centrifugal force is the apparent outward force felt when something moves in a circle.","zh":"「centrifugal force」是物體作圓周運動時感覺到的向外表觀力。"},{"en":"On a fast roundabout, riders may feel pushed outward by centrifugal force.","zh":"在快速旋轉木馬上，乘客可能感到被離心力向外推。"},{"en":"Wegener’s use of this force was not enough to explain continental movement.","zh":"Wegener 使用這種力量不足以解釋大陸移動。"},{"en":"The phrase names a physical force linked with circular motion.","zh":"這個短語指出與圓周運動有關的物理力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"severely overestimate","meaning":"嚴重高估","examples":[{"en":"Wegener severely overestimated the speed of continental motion.","zh":"Wegener 嚴重高估了大陸運動的速度。"},{"en":"To severely overestimate something means to judge it as much larger, faster, or greater than it really is.","zh":"「severely overestimate」某事，意思是把它判斷得比實際大、快或多得多。"},{"en":"A student may severely overestimate how much revision can be done in one night.","zh":"學生可能嚴重高估一晚可以完成多少溫習。"},{"en":"If scientists overestimate a speed, their model may become less credible.","zh":"如果科學家高估速度，其模型可能變得較不可信。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a serious error in judgment.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重判斷錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the speed of this motion","meaning":"這種運動的速度","examples":[{"en":"He overestimated the speed of this motion.","zh":"他高估了這種運動的速度。"},{"en":"The speed of this motion means how fast this movement happens.","zh":"「the speed of this motion」意思是這種移動發生得有多快。"},{"en":"A science student may measure the speed of a toy car’s motion on a ramp.","zh":"科學學生可能量度玩具車在斜坡上運動的速度。"},{"en":"If the motion is extremely slow, people may not notice it in daily life.","zh":"如果運動極慢，人們在日常生活中可能察覺不到。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the rate of movement.","zh":"這個短語集中於移動速率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"upon publishing his ideas","meaning":"在發表其想法後","examples":[{"en":"Upon publishing his ideas, Wegener faced hostility from scientists.","zh":"在發表其想法後，Wegener 面對科學家的敵意。"},{"en":"Upon publishing his ideas means when or after he made his ideas public in writing.","zh":"「upon publishing his ideas」意思是當他或在他以書面公開想法後。"},{"en":"Upon publishing her research, a scientist may receive questions from other experts.","zh":"在發表研究後，科學家可能收到其他專家的提問。"},{"en":"If an idea challenges accepted beliefs, publication can lead to criticism.","zh":"如果想法挑戰既有信念，發表後可能引來批評。"},{"en":"The phrase marks what happened immediately after an idea was shared.","zh":"這個短語標示想法被分享後立即發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the scientific community","meaning":"科學界","examples":[{"en":"The scientific community was hostile to Wegener’s theory.","zh":"科學界對 Wegener 的理論持敵視態度。"},{"en":"The scientific community means scientists as a group, especially those working in related fields.","zh":"「the scientific community」意思是科學家作為一個群體，尤其是相關領域的科學家。"},{"en":"The scientific community may debate a new medical discovery before accepting it.","zh":"科學界可能在接受新醫學發現前進行辯論。"},{"en":"If the scientific community rejects an idea, it may take years for it to gain support.","zh":"如果科學界拒絕某想法，它可能需要多年才獲支持。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the collective world of scientists.","zh":"這個短語指科學家的整體世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"resolutely and implacably hostile","meaning":"堅決而毫不讓步地敵視","examples":[{"en":"The scientific community was resolutely and implacably hostile to his ideas.","zh":"科學界堅決而毫不讓步地敵視他的想法。"},{"en":"Resolutely and implacably hostile means firmly and unyieldingly opposed.","zh":"「resolutely and implacably hostile」意思是堅定而不讓步地反對。"},{"en":"A committee may be resolutely hostile to a proposal if it believes the plan is dangerous.","zh":"如果委員會認為計劃危險，可能會堅決敵視該提議。"},{"en":"If people are implacably hostile, ordinary persuasion may not change their minds.","zh":"如果人們毫不讓步地敵視，普通說服可能不能改變他們想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes very strong resistance.","zh":"這個短語描述非常強烈的抗拒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a not-uncommon case","meaning":"並非罕見的情況","examples":[{"en":"Wegener’s story is a not-uncommon case in science.","zh":"Wegener 的故事在科學中並非罕見的情況。"},{"en":"A not-uncommon case means a situation that happens fairly often, even if it sounds unusual.","zh":"「a not-uncommon case」意思是即使聽起來特別，仍相當常見的情況。"},{"en":"It is a not-uncommon case for a student to understand a topic only after several attempts.","zh":"學生嘗試幾次後才理解題目，並非罕見的情況。"},{"en":"If good ideas are rejected at first, history may later prove them correct.","zh":"如果好想法一開始被拒絕，歷史可能後來證明它正確。"},{"en":"The phrase means the case is not rare.","zh":"這個短語意思是該情況並不稀少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be fundamentally correct","meaning":"基本上正確","examples":[{"en":"Wegener was fundamentally correct about continental movement.","zh":"Wegener 關於大陸移動的觀點基本上正確。"},{"en":"To be fundamentally correct means to be right in the most basic or important way.","zh":"「be fundamentally correct」意思是在最基本或最重要方面是正確的。"},{"en":"A student’s answer may be fundamentally correct even if the wording is not perfect.","zh":"學生的答案即使用字不完美，也可能基本上正確。"},{"en":"If the central idea is true, later evidence can correct smaller errors.","zh":"如果核心想法正確，後來證據可以修正較小錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase separates the main truth from minor mistakes.","zh":"這個短語把主要真相與小錯誤分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be denied recognition","meaning":"不獲承認","examples":[{"en":"He was denied recognition in his lifetime.","zh":"他在有生之年不獲承認。"},{"en":"To be denied recognition means not to receive the respect or credit one deserves.","zh":"「be denied recognition」意思是沒有得到應有的尊重或肯定。"},{"en":"A hardworking employee may be denied recognition if managers ignore their contribution.","zh":"如果經理忽視員工貢獻，勤奮員工可能不獲承認。"},{"en":"If a scientist is denied recognition, their work may only be valued after death.","zh":"如果科學家不獲承認，其工作可能在死後才被重視。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unfair lack of acknowledgement.","zh":"這個短語描述不公平地缺乏肯定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in his lifetime","meaning":"在他有生之年","examples":[{"en":"Wegener received little recognition in his lifetime.","zh":"Wegener 在他有生之年幾乎沒有得到認可。"},{"en":"In his lifetime means during the period when he was alive.","zh":"「in his lifetime」意思是在他仍然活着的期間。"},{"en":"Some artists become famous only after death, not in their lifetime.","zh":"有些藝術家不是在有生之年，而是在死後才成名。"},{"en":"If a person is not recognised in their lifetime, later praise can feel tragic.","zh":"如果一個人在有生之年不獲承認，後來的讚賞會顯得悲哀。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the time frame of a person’s life.","zh":"這個短語給出某人生命期間的時間範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"advocate the washing of hands","meaning":"提倡洗手","examples":[{"en":"Semmelweis advocated the washing of hands before surgery.","zh":"Semmelweis 提倡手術前洗手。"},{"en":"To advocate the washing of hands means to publicly support handwashing as an important practice.","zh":"「advocate the washing of hands」意思是公開支持洗手作為重要做法。"},{"en":"A nurse may advocate handwashing to prevent infections in a clinic.","zh":"護士可能在診所提倡洗手，以防感染。"},{"en":"If doctors wash their hands, fewer germs may pass to patients.","zh":"如果醫生洗手，較少細菌會傳給病人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes promoting a hygiene practice.","zh":"這個短語描述推廣衛生做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"before surgery","meaning":"手術前","examples":[{"en":"Doctors were advised to wash their hands before surgery.","zh":"醫生被建議在手術前洗手。"},{"en":"Before surgery means before an operation is performed.","zh":"「before surgery」意思是在進行手術之前。"},{"en":"Patients may be asked not to eat before surgery.","zh":"病人可能被要求手術前不要進食。"},{"en":"If hygiene is poor before surgery, infection risk can increase.","zh":"如果手術前衛生欠佳，感染風險可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the preparation stage before an operation.","zh":"這個短語指手術前的準備階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reduce hospital fatalities","meaning":"減少醫院死亡個案","examples":[{"en":"Handwashing could reduce hospital fatalities.","zh":"洗手可以減少醫院死亡個案。"},{"en":"To reduce hospital fatalities means to lower the number of deaths in hospitals.","zh":"「reduce hospital fatalities」意思是降低醫院死亡人數。"},{"en":"Better emergency training can reduce hospital fatalities during serious accidents.","zh":"更好的急救培訓可以在嚴重事故中減少醫院死亡個案。"},{"en":"If infection is prevented, fewer patients may die after treatment.","zh":"如果感染被預防，治療後死亡的病人可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes saving lives in a medical setting.","zh":"這個短語描述在醫療環境中拯救生命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"die unexpectedly","meaning":"意外去世","examples":[{"en":"Wegener died unexpectedly on an expedition in Greenland.","zh":"Wegener 在格陵蘭探險期間意外去世。"},{"en":"To die unexpectedly means to die suddenly or without warning.","zh":"「die unexpectedly」意思是突然或毫無預警地去世。"},{"en":"A healthy-looking person may die unexpectedly from a hidden heart problem.","zh":"看似健康的人可能因隱藏心臟問題而意外去世。"},{"en":"If someone dies unexpectedly, their work may be left unfinished.","zh":"如果某人意外去世，其工作可能未完成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a death that was not predicted.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有被預料到的死亡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on an expedition","meaning":"在探險期間","examples":[{"en":"He died while on an expedition in Greenland.","zh":"他在格陵蘭探險期間去世。"},{"en":"On an expedition means taking part in a journey made for exploration or research.","zh":"「on an expedition」意思是參與以探索或研究為目的的旅程。"},{"en":"Scientists on an expedition may collect rock, ice, or plant samples.","zh":"在探險期間，科學家可能收集岩石、冰或植物樣本。"},{"en":"If weather changes suddenly on an expedition, the team may face danger.","zh":"如果探險期間天氣突然改變，團隊可能面對危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being involved in a serious journey of investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述參與一趟認真調查旅程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"probably of a heart attack","meaning":"可能死於心臟病發","examples":[{"en":"Wegener probably died of a heart attack.","zh":"Wegener 可能死於心臟病發。"},{"en":"Probably of a heart attack means the most likely cause was a sudden failure of the heart.","zh":"「probably of a heart attack」意思是最可能的原因是心臟突然出問題。"},{"en":"If a report says someone died probably of a heart attack, the cause is likely but not completely certain.","zh":"如果報告說某人可能死於心臟病發，原因很可能如此，但並非完全確定。"},{"en":"A heart attack can kill quickly if help is not available.","zh":"如果沒有救援，心臟病發可以迅速致命。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses a likely medical cause of death.","zh":"這個短語表達可能的醫學死因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be left out in the cold","meaning":"被冷落；不受重視","examples":[{"en":"In death as in life, Wegener was left out in the cold.","zh":"生前如此，死後亦然，Wegener 被冷落。"},{"en":"To be left out in the cold means to be ignored, excluded, or not given support.","zh":"「be left out in the cold」意思是被忽視、排除或得不到支持。"},{"en":"A student may feel left out in the cold if group members make decisions without them.","zh":"如果小組成員不與某學生商量便作決定，他可能感到被冷落。"},{"en":"If a scientist’s work is ignored, they may receive no credit for an important discovery.","zh":"如果科學家的工作被忽視，他可能得不到重要發現的功勞。"},{"en":"The phrase describes social or professional exclusion.","zh":"這個短語描述社交或專業上的排除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"first hints of","meaning":"……的最初線索","examples":[{"en":"The first hints of Gondwana’s existence came from fossil evidence.","zh":"岡瓦納古陸存在的最初線索來自化石證據。"},{"en":"The first hints of something are the earliest signs that it may be true or real.","zh":"「first hints of」某事，是它可能真實或存在的最早跡象。"},{"en":"The first hints of illness may be tiredness and a slight fever.","zh":"疾病的最初線索可能是疲倦和輕微發燒。"},{"en":"If early clues appear, researchers can begin asking deeper questions.","zh":"如果早期線索出現，研究者可以開始提出更深問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the beginning of evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述證據的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Gondwana’s existence","meaning":"岡瓦納古陸的存在","examples":[{"en":"Fossils provided early evidence of Gondwana’s existence.","zh":"化石提供了岡瓦納古陸存在的早期證據。"},{"en":"Gondwana’s existence means the fact that the ancient landmass Gondwana once existed.","zh":"「Gondwana’s existence」意思是岡瓦納這片古陸曾經存在的事實。"},{"en":"Geology students study Gondwana’s existence by comparing fossils and rocks.","zh":"地質學生透過比較化石和岩石研究岡瓦納古陸的存在。"},{"en":"If matching fossils are found on separated continents, they can support the idea of Gondwana.","zh":"如果分離的大陸上發現相配化石，它們可以支持岡瓦納古陸的想法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to proof that an ancient continent was real.","zh":"這個短語指證明古大陸真實存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fossil plants and animals","meaning":"植物和動物化石","examples":[{"en":"Similar fossil plants and animals were found across several continents.","zh":"相似的植物和動物化石在幾個大陸被發現。"},{"en":"Fossil plants and animals are preserved remains or traces of ancient living things.","zh":"「fossil plants and animals」是古代生物保存下來的遺骸或痕跡。"},{"en":"A museum may display fossil plants and animals to show what life was like millions of years ago.","zh":"博物館可能展示植物和動物化石，以顯示數百萬年前生命的樣貌。"},{"en":"If the same fossils appear on distant continents, scientists may infer the lands were once connected.","zh":"如果同樣化石出現在遙遠大陸，科學家可能推斷陸地曾經相連。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ancient biological evidence preserved in rocks.","zh":"這個短語描述保存在岩石中的古代生物證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the same geological period","meaning":"同一地質時期","examples":[{"en":"The fossils came from the same geological period.","zh":"這些化石來自同一地質時期。"},{"en":"The same geological period means the same time interval in Earth’s deep history.","zh":"「the same geological period」意思是地球深遠歷史中的同一時間段。"},{"en":"Rocks from the same geological period may contain similar fossils.","zh":"來自同一地質時期的岩石可能含有相似化石。"},{"en":"If fossils are from the same period, comparison between continents becomes more meaningful.","zh":"如果化石來自同一時期，大陸之間的比較就更有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase helps connect evidence by age.","zh":"這個短語幫助按年代連結證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be found across","meaning":"遍佈……被發現","examples":[{"en":"Similar fossils were found across South America, Africa and Australia.","zh":"相似化石遍佈南美洲、非洲和澳洲被發現。"},{"en":"To be found across an area means to appear in many places throughout that area.","zh":"「be found across」某區，意思是在該區許多地方出現。"},{"en":"The same school rule may be found across all campuses in a school group.","zh":"同一校規可能遍佈一個辦學團體的所有校園。"},{"en":"If one type of fossil is found across several continents, it may suggest a shared past.","zh":"如果一種化石在幾個大陸被發現，可能暗示共同過去。"},{"en":"The phrase describes wide distribution.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"South America","meaning":"南美洲","examples":[{"en":"Fossils in South America helped support the theory of Gondwana.","zh":"南美洲的化石幫助支持岡瓦納古陸理論。"},{"en":"South America is the continent that includes countries such as Brazil, Argentina, and Chile.","zh":"「South America」是包括巴西、阿根廷和智利等國家的大陸。"},{"en":"On a map, South America lies west of the Atlantic Ocean.","zh":"在地圖上，南美洲位於大西洋以西。"},{"en":"If South American fossils match African fossils, scientists may infer an ancient connection.","zh":"如果南美洲化石與非洲化石相配，科學家可能推斷古代連結。"},{"en":"The phrase names one of the continents used in continental-drift evidence.","zh":"這個短語指出大陸漂移證據中的其中一個大陸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Africa","meaning":"非洲","examples":[{"en":"Fossils found in Africa matched those from other continents.","zh":"在非洲發現的化石與其他大陸的化石相配。"},{"en":"Africa is a large continent east of the Atlantic Ocean and south of Europe.","zh":"「Africa」是位於大西洋以東、歐洲以南的大洲。"},{"en":"Africa’s west coast is often compared with the east coast of South America.","zh":"非洲西岸常與南美洲東岸作比較。"},{"en":"Matching rocks and fossils in Africa can support ideas about ancient land connections.","zh":"非洲相配的岩石和化石可以支持古代陸地連結的想法。"},{"en":"The word names a key continent in Wegener’s evidence.","zh":"這個詞指出 Wegener 證據中的關鍵大陸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Antarctica","meaning":"南極洲","examples":[{"en":"Antarctica was once part of Gondwana.","zh":"南極洲曾經是岡瓦納古陸的一部分。"},{"en":"Antarctica is the icy continent around the South Pole.","zh":"「Antarctica」是圍繞南極的冰封大陸。"},{"en":"Students may be surprised that Antarctica was once linked to warmer continents.","zh":"學生可能驚訝於南極洲曾與較溫暖的大陸相連。"},{"en":"Fossils in Antarctica can reveal that its past climate was very different.","zh":"南極洲的化石可以揭示其過去氣候非常不同。"},{"en":"The phrase names a continent important to ancient supercontinent evidence.","zh":"這個短語指出古代超級大陸證據中的重要大陸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"India","meaning":"印度","examples":[{"en":"India was once connected to other parts of Gondwana.","zh":"印度曾經與岡瓦納古陸其他部分相連。"},{"en":"India here refers to the Indian landmass or plate, not only the modern country.","zh":"這裡的「India」指印度陸塊或板塊，不只是現代國家。"},{"en":"In geology, India is important because it moved north and collided with Asia.","zh":"在地質學中，印度很重要，因為它向北移動並與亞洲碰撞。"},{"en":"If India had remained in Gondwana, the Himalayas would not have formed in the same way.","zh":"如果印度仍留在岡瓦納古陸，喜馬拉雅山脈就不會以同樣方式形成。"},{"en":"The word can refer to both a modern country and an ancient moving landmass.","zh":"這個詞可指現代國家，也可指古代移動陸塊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Australia","meaning":"澳洲","examples":[{"en":"Australia was one of the continents linked to Gondwana.","zh":"澳洲是與岡瓦納古陸有關的大陸之一。"},{"en":"Australia is both a country and a continent in the Southern Hemisphere.","zh":"「Australia」既是一個國家，也是在南半球的一個大陸。"},{"en":"Fossils in Australia can help scientists compare its ancient history with Antarctica and India.","zh":"澳洲的化石可以幫助科學家把其古代歷史與南極洲和印度比較。"},{"en":"If Australia was once connected to Gondwana, its rocks may share features with other southern lands.","zh":"如果澳洲曾與岡瓦納古陸相連，其岩石可能與其他南方陸地有共同特徵。"},{"en":"The word names a modern continent with ancient geological links.","zh":"這個詞指出一個具有古代地質連結的現代大陸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the composition and nature of","meaning":"……的成分和性質","examples":[{"en":"The composition and nature of rocks supported Wegener’s theory.","zh":"岩石的成分和性質支持 Wegener 的理論。"},{"en":"The composition and nature of something means what it is made of and what qualities it has.","zh":"「the composition and nature of」某物，意思是它由甚麼組成，以及具有甚麼特質。"},{"en":"A scientist may study the composition and nature of soil before deciding what crops to grow.","zh":"科學家可能先研究泥土的成分和性質，再決定種植甚麼作物。"},{"en":"If rocks on two coastlines have the same composition, they may share an origin.","zh":"如果兩條海岸線上的岩石成分相同，它們可能有共同來源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both material content and characteristics.","zh":"這個短語描述材料內容和特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"corresponding coastlines","meaning":"相對應的海岸線","examples":[{"en":"Rocks along corresponding coastlines told the same story.","zh":"相對應海岸線上的岩石說明同一件事。"},{"en":"Corresponding coastlines are coastlines on separate landmasses that match or relate to each other.","zh":"「corresponding coastlines」是分開陸塊上互相吻合或有關聯的海岸線。"},{"en":"Students may compare corresponding coastlines on opposite sides of an ocean.","zh":"學生可能比較海洋兩邊相對應的海岸線。"},{"en":"If rocks on corresponding coastlines match, they can support continental drift.","zh":"如果相對應海岸線上的岩石相配，它們可以支持大陸漂移。"},{"en":"The phrase describes coastlines that appear to belong together.","zh":"這個短語描述看似本來相連的海岸線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tell the same story","meaning":"說明同一件事；提供相同證據","examples":[{"en":"The fossils and rocks told the same story about ancient continents.","zh":"化石和岩石都說明關於古代大陸的同一件事。"},{"en":"To tell the same story means to support the same explanation or conclusion.","zh":"「tell the same story」意思是支持同一解釋或結論。"},{"en":"If a student’s notes, attendance, and test results all tell the same story, the teacher can identify the problem.","zh":"如果學生筆記、出席率和測驗成績都說明同一件事，老師就能找出問題。"},{"en":"When different kinds of evidence agree, an argument becomes stronger.","zh":"當不同證據互相吻合，論點會變得更強。"},{"en":"The phrase means separate clues point to the same idea.","zh":"這個短語意思是不同線索指向同一想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"scientifically credible","meaning":"在科學上可信","examples":[{"en":"The theory needed more evidence to become scientifically credible.","zh":"該理論需要更多證據才變得在科學上可信。"},{"en":"Scientifically credible means believable because it is supported by reliable scientific evidence.","zh":"「scientifically credible」意思是因有可靠科學證據支持而可信。"},{"en":"A health claim becomes scientifically credible only after careful studies support it.","zh":"健康聲稱只有在仔細研究支持後，才變得在科學上可信。"},{"en":"If a theory lacks evidence, scientists may not treat it as credible.","zh":"如果理論缺乏證據，科學家可能不把它視為可信。"},{"en":"The phrase describes trustworthiness in science.","zh":"這個短語描述科學上的可信度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"evidence of","meaning":"……的證據","examples":[{"en":"Scientists wanted evidence of a force that could move continents.","zh":"科學家想要能移動大陸的力量的證據。"},{"en":"Evidence of something is proof or information showing that it exists or happened.","zh":"「evidence of」某事，是顯示它存在或發生的證明或資料。"},{"en":"A teacher may look for evidence of effort in a student’s draft work.","zh":"老師可能在學生草稿中尋找努力的證據。"},{"en":"If there is no evidence of improvement, a study plan may need to change.","zh":"如果沒有進步的證據，學習計劃可能需要改變。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces what the evidence is supposed to show.","zh":"這個短語引出證據要顯示的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"such huge continents","meaning":"如此巨大的大陸","examples":[{"en":"A powerful force was needed to move such huge continents.","zh":"需要強大力量才能移動如此巨大的大陸。"},{"en":"Such huge continents means continents of this extremely large size.","zh":"「such huge continents」意思是如此極其巨大的大陸。"},{"en":"Moving such huge objects requires far more energy than moving small stones.","zh":"移動如此巨大的物體，需要比移動小石頭多得多的能量。"},{"en":"If continents are enormous, any theory about their movement must explain a strong force.","zh":"如果大陸極其巨大，任何關於其移動的理論都必須解釋強大力量。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises the great size of the landmasses.","zh":"這個短語強調陸塊非常巨大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the same way that","meaning":"正如……一樣","examples":[{"en":"Wegener’s idea needed evidence in the same way that Semmelweis’s idea needed germ theory.","zh":"Wegener 的想法需要證據，正如 Semmelweis 的想法需要細菌理論一樣。"},{"en":"In the same way that means similarly to how another situation works.","zh":"「in the same way that」意思是以與另一情況相似的方式。"},{"en":"A student needs practice in the same way that an athlete needs training.","zh":"學生需要練習，正如運動員需要訓練一樣。"},{"en":"If two cases share a pattern, this phrase helps compare them clearly.","zh":"如果兩個個案有共同模式，這個短語有助清楚比較。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a comparison of logic or situation.","zh":"這個短語引入邏輯或情況上的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"germ theory of disease","meaning":"疾病細菌理論","examples":[{"en":"Semmelweis’s idea later gained support from the germ theory of disease.","zh":"Semmelweis 的想法後來得到疾病細菌理論支持。"},{"en":"The germ theory of disease is the idea that many diseases are caused by microorganisms.","zh":"「germ theory of disease」是指許多疾病由微生物引起的想法。"},{"en":"In biology class, students learn that germ theory explains why handwashing prevents infection.","zh":"在生物課中，學生學到細菌理論解釋為何洗手能預防感染。"},{"en":"If germs cause disease, hygiene becomes a scientific necessity, not just a habit.","zh":"如果細菌導致疾病，衛生就成為科學必要，而不只是習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major medical theory.","zh":"這個短語指出一項重要醫學理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"decades after","meaning":"在……數十年後","examples":[{"en":"Hard evidence appeared decades after Wegener’s death.","zh":"確鑿證據在 Wegener 去世數十年後出現。"},{"en":"Decades after means many tens of years later.","zh":"「decades after」意思是數十年之後。"},{"en":"A writer may become famous decades after publishing their first book.","zh":"作家可能在出版第一本書數十年後才成名。"},{"en":"If evidence appears decades later, the original thinker may never see their idea accepted.","zh":"如果證據數十年後才出現，原本的思想家可能永遠看不到其想法被接受。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a long delay.","zh":"這個短語描述長時間延遲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hard evidence","meaning":"確鑿證據","examples":[{"en":"Hard evidence for Wegener’s theory began to accumulate in the 1960s.","zh":"支持 Wegener 理論的確鑿證據在1960年代開始累積。"},{"en":"Hard evidence is strong, reliable proof that supports a claim.","zh":"「hard evidence」是支持某主張的強而可靠的證明。"},{"en":"A teacher needs hard evidence before accusing a student of copying homework.","zh":"老師在指控學生抄功課前需要確鑿證據。"},{"en":"If hard evidence appears, sceptical people may start to change their minds.","zh":"如果確鑿證據出現，持懷疑態度的人可能開始改變想法。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts solid proof with weak guesses.","zh":"這個短語把堅實證明與薄弱猜測作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"begin to accumulate","meaning":"開始累積","examples":[{"en":"Evidence for continental movement began to accumulate.","zh":"大陸移動的證據開始累積。"},{"en":"To begin to accumulate means to start building up gradually in amount.","zh":"「begin to accumulate」意思是數量開始逐漸增加。"},{"en":"Homework can begin to accumulate if a student delays small tasks every day.","zh":"如果學生每天拖延小任務，功課可以開始累積。"},{"en":"When evidence accumulates, a theory becomes harder to dismiss.","zh":"當證據累積，理論就更難被否定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual increase over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間逐漸增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"become overwhelming","meaning":"變得壓倒性；非常充分","examples":[{"en":"The evidence eventually became overwhelming.","zh":"證據最終變得壓倒性。"},{"en":"To become overwhelming means to become so strong or great that it is difficult to reject.","zh":"「become overwhelming」意思是變得非常強大或充分，以致難以拒絕。"},{"en":"If many students complain about the same timetable problem, the evidence becomes overwhelming.","zh":"如果許多學生投訴同一時間表問題，證據就變得非常充分。"},{"en":"When evidence is overwhelming, disagreement becomes much harder to defend.","zh":"當證據壓倒性，反對意見就更難辯護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence becoming extremely convincing.","zh":"這個短語描述證據變得極具說服力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"plate tectonics","meaning":"板塊構造論","examples":[{"en":"The modern theory is called plate tectonics.","zh":"現代理論稱為板塊構造論。"},{"en":"Plate tectonics is the theory that Earth’s outer shell is divided into moving plates.","zh":"「plate tectonics」是地球外層分裂成移動板塊的理論。"},{"en":"Geography students use plate tectonics to explain earthquakes, volcanoes, and mountains.","zh":"地理學生用板塊構造論解釋地震、火山和山脈。"},{"en":"If plates move, collide, or separate, major geological features can form.","zh":"如果板塊移動、碰撞或分離，重大地質特徵可以形成。"},{"en":"The phrase names the modern explanation for continental movement.","zh":"這個短語指出大陸移動的現代解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be proven that","meaning":"被證明","examples":[{"en":"It was proven that the Earth’s surface is fractured into plates.","zh":"地球表面被證明裂成板塊。"},{"en":"To be proven that means evidence has shown something to be true.","zh":"「be proven that」意思是證據已顯示某事為真。"},{"en":"It was proven that regular sleep improves concentration in many students.","zh":"有證據證明規律睡眠能改善許多學生的專注力。"},{"en":"If something is proven, it moves beyond simple opinion.","zh":"如果某事被證明，它就超越單純意見。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a conclusion supported by evidence.","zh":"這個短語引入由證據支持的結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the Earth’s surface","meaning":"地球表面","examples":[{"en":"The Earth’s surface is divided into tectonic plates.","zh":"地球表面分為構造板塊。"},{"en":"The Earth’s surface is the outer layer of the planet where land and oceans lie.","zh":"「the Earth’s surface」是地球外層，陸地和海洋位於其上。"},{"en":"Maps show only the Earth’s surface, not the deep interior beneath it.","zh":"地圖只顯示地球表面，不顯示其下的深層內部。"},{"en":"If the surface is broken into plates, movement below can affect land above.","zh":"如果表面裂成板塊，下面的移動可以影響上方陸地。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the planet’s outer visible or near-visible layer.","zh":"這個短語指地球外部可見或近可見的一層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be fractured into","meaning":"裂成","examples":[{"en":"The Earth’s surface is fractured into plates.","zh":"地球表面裂成板塊。"},{"en":"To be fractured into parts means to be broken or divided into separate pieces.","zh":"「be fractured into」幾部分，意思是被破裂或分成分開的碎片。"},{"en":"A dropped tile may be fractured into several sharp pieces.","zh":"掉落的瓷磚可能裂成幾塊尖銳碎片。"},{"en":"If Earth’s outer layer is fractured, the pieces can move against one another.","zh":"如果地球外層裂開，各部分可以互相移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes breaking into distinct sections.","zh":"這個短語描述裂成明確部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tectonic plates","meaning":"構造板塊","examples":[{"en":"Tectonic plates move slowly across the Earth’s surface.","zh":"構造板塊在地球表面緩慢移動。"},{"en":"Tectonic plates are huge pieces of Earth’s outer shell that move over time.","zh":"「tectonic plates」是地球外殼中會隨時間移動的巨大部分。"},{"en":"Students may use cardboard pieces to model tectonic plates in class.","zh":"學生可能在課堂上用卡紙片模擬構造板塊。"},{"en":"When tectonic plates collide, mountains or earthquakes can occur.","zh":"當構造板塊碰撞，山脈或地震可能出現。"},{"en":"The phrase names the moving sections of Earth’s crust.","zh":"這個短語指出地殼中移動的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"bump and grind","meaning":"碰撞和摩擦","examples":[{"en":"The plates bump and grind as they move.","zh":"板塊移動時會碰撞和摩擦。"},{"en":"To bump and grind means to collide and rub against each other roughly.","zh":"「bump and grind」意思是粗糙地互相碰撞和摩擦。"},{"en":"Two shopping trolleys may bump and grind when pushed through a crowded aisle.","zh":"在擠迫通道中，兩架購物車可能碰撞和摩擦。"},{"en":"When plates grind together, pressure can build and later release as earthquakes.","zh":"當板塊互相摩擦，壓力可以累積並之後以地震形式釋放。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rough contact between moving objects.","zh":"這個短語描述移動物體之間的粗糙接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"steadily move","meaning":"穩定移動","examples":[{"en":"Tectonic plates steadily move in given directions.","zh":"構造板塊朝特定方向穩定移動。"},{"en":"To steadily move means to move continuously and gradually, without stopping suddenly.","zh":"「steadily move」意思是持續而逐漸地移動，不是突然停止。"},{"en":"A student can steadily move toward better writing by practising a little every day.","zh":"學生可以透過每天少量練習，穩定地邁向更好寫作。"},{"en":"If plates move steadily for millions of years, small movement can produce huge results.","zh":"如果板塊數百萬年穩定移動，小移動也能產生巨大結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow, consistent progress or motion.","zh":"這個短語描述緩慢而持續的進展或運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"infinitesimally slow speeds","meaning":"極其緩慢的速度","examples":[{"en":"The plates move at infinitesimally slow speeds.","zh":"板塊以極其緩慢的速度移動。"},{"en":"Infinitesimally slow speeds are speeds so tiny that they are almost impossible to notice directly.","zh":"「infinitesimally slow speeds」是細微到幾乎無法直接察覺的速度。"},{"en":"A plant grows at a very slow speed, but plate movement is even slower to human eyes.","zh":"植物生長速度很慢，但對人眼而言，板塊移動更慢。"},{"en":"If motion is infinitesimally slow, it may still change the planet over millions of years.","zh":"如果運動極其緩慢，它仍可在數百萬年間改變地球。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises extreme slowness.","zh":"這個短語強調極端緩慢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in given directions","meaning":"朝特定方向","examples":[{"en":"The plates move slowly in given directions.","zh":"板塊朝特定方向緩慢移動。"},{"en":"In given directions means along particular or specified paths.","zh":"「in given directions」意思是沿着特定或指定路徑。"},{"en":"During a fire drill, students must move in given directions toward the exits.","zh":"火警演習期間，學生必須朝特定方向前往出口。"},{"en":"If plates move in different directions, they may collide, separate, or slide past one another.","zh":"如果板塊朝不同方向移動，它們可能碰撞、分離或互相擦過。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement with a particular direction.","zh":"這個短語描述有特定方向的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be driven by","meaning":"由……推動","examples":[{"en":"The plates are driven by convection currents.","zh":"板塊由對流推動。"},{"en":"To be driven by something means to be caused, powered, or strongly influenced by it.","zh":"「be driven by」某物，意思是由它造成、驅動或強烈影響。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be driven by daily practice and honest feedback.","zh":"學生進步可能由每日練習和誠實回饋推動。"},{"en":"If plate motion is driven by forces below the surface, we cannot see the cause directly.","zh":"如果板塊運動由地表下力量推動，我們不能直接看見原因。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the force or reason behind movement.","zh":"這個短語指出運動背後的力量或原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"convection currents","meaning":"對流","examples":[{"en":"Convection currents help drive the movement of tectonic plates.","zh":"對流有助推動構造板塊移動。"},{"en":"Convection currents are circular movements caused when hot material rises and cooler material sinks.","zh":"「convection currents」是熱物質上升、較冷物質下沉造成的循環流動。"},{"en":"In boiling soup, convection currents move hot liquid upward and cooler liquid downward.","zh":"在沸騰湯中，對流令熱液體上升、較冷液體下沉。"},{"en":"Inside Earth, similar circulation can help move tectonic plates above.","zh":"在地球內部，相似循環可以幫助推動上方構造板塊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes heat-driven circulation.","zh":"這個短語描述由熱力驅動的循環。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"vast circulation of","meaning":"……的大規模循環","examples":[{"en":"Convection currents involve the vast circulation of superheated rock.","zh":"對流涉及過熱岩石的大規模循環。"},{"en":"Vast circulation of something means very large-scale movement around a system.","zh":"「vast circulation of」某物，意思是在系統中非常大規模的流動。"},{"en":"The vast circulation of air around the planet affects weather patterns.","zh":"地球周圍空氣的大規模循環影響天氣模式。"},{"en":"If rock circulates on a huge scale, it can create forces under tectonic plates.","zh":"如果岩石大規模循環，它可以在構造板塊下方產生力量。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises large, continuous movement.","zh":"這個短語強調大型而持續的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"superheated rock","meaning":"過熱岩石","examples":[{"en":"Superheated rock circulates beneath the Earth’s surface.","zh":"過熱岩石在地球表面下循環。"},{"en":"Superheated rock is rock heated to extremely high temperatures deep inside Earth.","zh":"「superheated rock」是在地球深處被加熱至極高溫的岩石。"},{"en":"Students may compare superheated rock to thick hot syrup moving very slowly.","zh":"學生可能把過熱岩石比作非常緩慢移動的濃熱糖漿。"},{"en":"When superheated rock moves, it can help transfer heat inside the planet.","zh":"當過熱岩石移動，它可以幫助地球內部傳遞熱量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extremely hot material below the surface.","zh":"這個短語描述地表下極熱材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"molten interior","meaning":"熔融內部","examples":[{"en":"The Earth’s molten interior produces convection currents.","zh":"地球的熔融內部產生對流。"},{"en":"Molten interior means the hot, partly melted material inside Earth.","zh":"「molten interior」意思是地球內部高溫、部分熔化的物質。"},{"en":"A volcano gives visible evidence that Earth has very hot material inside.","zh":"火山提供可見證據，顯示地球內部有非常熱的物質。"},{"en":"If the interior is molten or extremely hot, material can circulate slowly.","zh":"如果內部是熔融或極熱的，物質可以慢慢循環。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the hot inner part of the planet.","zh":"這個短語描述地球的高溫內部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cool as it nears","meaning":"在接近……時冷卻","examples":[{"en":"The material cools as it nears the surface.","zh":"該物質在接近地表時冷卻。"},{"en":"To cool as it nears something means to lose heat while moving closer to it.","zh":"「cool as it nears」某物，意思是在靠近它時失去熱量。"},{"en":"Hot tea cools as it nears room temperature after being left on a desk.","zh":"熱茶放在書桌上後，在接近室溫時冷卻。"},{"en":"When hot rock moves upward, it may cool because the upper layers are less hot.","zh":"當熱岩石向上移動時，因上層較不熱，它可能冷卻。"},{"en":"The phrase describes temperature change during movement.","zh":"這個短語描述移動中的溫度變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sink once again towards","meaning":"再次下沉至……","examples":[{"en":"The cooled material sinks once again towards the centre.","zh":"冷卻的物質再次下沉至中心。"},{"en":"To sink once again towards something means to move downward again after cooling or becoming denser.","zh":"「sink once again towards」某處，意思是在冷卻或變得較密後再次向下移動。"},{"en":"In soup, cooler liquid may sink again toward the bottom of the pot.","zh":"在湯中，較冷液體可能再次下沉至鍋底。"},{"en":"If hot material rises and cool material sinks, circulation continues.","zh":"如果熱物質上升而冷物質下沉，循環就會持續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the downward part of a cycle.","zh":"這個短語描述循環中的下沉部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the rotation of the Earth","meaning":"地球自轉","examples":[{"en":"The rotation of the Earth adds to the complexity of plate movement.","zh":"地球自轉增加板塊運動的複雜性。"},{"en":"The rotation of the Earth is the spinning of the planet around its axis.","zh":"「the rotation of the Earth」是地球繞其軸心旋轉。"},{"en":"Day and night happen because of the rotation of the Earth.","zh":"日夜變化是因為地球自轉。"},{"en":"If rotation affects moving material, plate movement becomes harder to model simply.","zh":"如果自轉影響移動物質，板塊運動就更難簡單建模。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to Earth’s spinning motion.","zh":"這個短語指地球的旋轉運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"barely understood","meaning":"幾乎未被理解","examples":[{"en":"The system of molten rock movement is barely understood.","zh":"熔融岩石運動系統幾乎未被理解。"},{"en":"Barely understood means understood only a little or not well enough.","zh":"「barely understood」意思是只理解少許或理解得不夠好。"},{"en":"A difficult grammar pattern may be barely understood after one quick lesson.","zh":"困難文法模式在一堂快速課後可能幾乎未被理解。"},{"en":"If a process is barely understood, scientists need more data and better models.","zh":"如果過程幾乎未被理解，科學家需要更多數據和更好模型。"},{"en":"The phrase shows limited understanding.","zh":"這個短語顯示理解有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cyclic swirls","meaning":"循環旋流","examples":[{"en":"Cyclic swirls of molten rock affect tectonic plates.","zh":"熔融岩石的循環旋流影響構造板塊。"},{"en":"Cyclic swirls are repeated circular movements that happen in a cycle.","zh":"「cyclic swirls」是以循環方式反覆出現的圓形流動。"},{"en":"Stirring soup can create small cyclic swirls in the pot.","zh":"攪拌湯時，鍋中可以產生小型循環旋流。"},{"en":"If molten rock moves in cyclic swirls, it can create complex forces below plates.","zh":"如果熔融岩石以循環旋流移動，它可以在板塊下方產生複雜力量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated spinning movement.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆旋轉移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"molten rock","meaning":"熔岩；熔融岩石","examples":[{"en":"Molten rock produces drags and pulls on tectonic plates.","zh":"熔融岩石對構造板塊產生拖力和拉力。"},{"en":"Molten rock is rock that has become liquid or partly liquid because of extreme heat.","zh":"「molten rock」是因極高熱力變成液態或半液態的岩石。"},{"en":"Lava is molten rock that has reached the surface.","zh":"熔岩是已到達地表的熔融岩石。"},{"en":"If molten rock moves below the crust, it can influence plate movement.","zh":"如果熔融岩石在地殼下方移動，它可以影響板塊運動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rock in a melted state.","zh":"這個短語描述熔化狀態的岩石。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"drags and pulls","meaning":"拖力和拉力","examples":[{"en":"Drags and pulls act on each tectonic plate.","zh":"拖力和拉力作用於每個構造板塊。"},{"en":"Drags and pulls are forces that slow, pull, or move something in different directions.","zh":"「drags and pulls」是令某物減慢、被拉動或向不同方向移動的力量。"},{"en":"A heavy bag creates drag and pull on a student’s shoulder.","zh":"沉重書包會對學生肩膀產生拖力和拉力。"},{"en":"If several forces act together, the final movement may be difficult to predict.","zh":"如果幾種力量一起作用，最終移動可能難以預測。"},{"en":"The phrase describes combined forces acting on an object.","zh":"這個短語描述作用於物體的組合力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the sum of which","meaning":"其總和","examples":[{"en":"These forces act together, the sum of which results in migration.","zh":"這些力量共同作用，其總和導致遷移。"},{"en":"The sum of which means the total effect of the things just mentioned.","zh":"「the sum of which」意思是剛提到事物的總體效果。"},{"en":"Sleep, practice, and feedback all help learning, the sum of which improves exam performance.","zh":"睡眠、練習和回饋都有助學習，其總和改善考試表現。"},{"en":"If many small forces combine, their total effect can move a plate.","zh":"如果許多小力量結合，其總效果可以移動板塊。"},{"en":"The phrase links several factors to one combined result.","zh":"這個短語把幾個因素連結到一個綜合結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"result in","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"The forces result in the steady migration of plates.","zh":"這些力量導致板塊穩定遷移。"},{"en":"To result in something means to cause it to happen.","zh":"「result in」某事，意思是導致它發生。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can result in weak concentration during lessons.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致上課專注力弱。"},{"en":"If forces beneath Earth continue, they can result in plate movement over time.","zh":"如果地球下方力量持續，它們可以隨時間導致板塊移動。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a cause with an outcome.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"steady migration","meaning":"穩定遷移","examples":[{"en":"The forces create a steady migration of tectonic plates.","zh":"這些力量造成構造板塊的穩定遷移。"},{"en":"Steady migration means slow, continuous movement from one place toward another.","zh":"「steady migration」意思是從一處向另一處緩慢而持續移動。"},{"en":"A family may make a steady migration from a crowded city to quieter suburbs over several years.","zh":"一個家庭可能在幾年間穩定地由擠迫城市遷往較寧靜郊區。"},{"en":"If plates migrate steadily, their effects become visible only over very long periods.","zh":"如果板塊穩定遷移，其效果只會在很長時間後變得可見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual but persistent movement.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸但持續的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"typically at the speed at which","meaning":"通常以……的速度","examples":[{"en":"Plate motion is typically at the speed at which fingernails grow.","zh":"板塊運動通常以指甲生長的速度進行。"},{"en":"Typically at the speed at which means usually moving as fast as a familiar process.","zh":"「typically at the speed at which」意思是通常以某個熟悉過程的速度移動。"},{"en":"A plant may grow at roughly the speed at which a teacher can notice change week by week.","zh":"植物可能以老師每週可察覺變化的速度生長。"},{"en":"Comparing plate movement with fingernails helps students imagine slow movement.","zh":"把板塊移動與指甲生長比較，幫助學生想像慢速移動。"},{"en":"The phrase uses comparison to explain speed.","zh":"這個短語用比較解釋速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fingernails grow","meaning":"指甲生長","examples":[{"en":"Tectonic plates often move at the speed at which fingernails grow.","zh":"構造板塊通常以指甲生長的速度移動。"},{"en":"Fingernails grow means the hard nails at the ends of fingers slowly become longer.","zh":"「fingernails grow」意思是手指末端的硬甲慢慢變長。"},{"en":"People may notice fingernails grow only after several days or weeks.","zh":"人們通常要幾天或幾星期後才注意到指甲生長。"},{"en":"If plate movement is like fingernail growth, it is extremely slow but continuous.","zh":"如果板塊移動像指甲生長，它就是極慢但持續的。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a familiar comparison for geological motion.","zh":"這個短語為地質運動提供熟悉比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at its fastest","meaning":"在最快的時候","examples":[{"en":"At its fastest, plate movement is about the rate at which hair grows.","zh":"在最快的時候，板塊移動約為頭髮生長的速度。"},{"en":"At its fastest means when something reaches its highest speed.","zh":"「at its fastest」意思是某物達到最高速度時。"},{"en":"At its fastest, a delivery service may bring food in fifteen minutes.","zh":"在最快的時候，送餐服務可能十五分鐘內把食物送到。"},{"en":"Even at its fastest, plate movement is still slow by human standards.","zh":"即使在最快的時候，板塊移動以人類標準仍然很慢。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the maximum speed.","zh":"這個短語標示最高速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the rate at which","meaning":"……的速度","examples":[{"en":"The plates may move at the rate at which hair grows.","zh":"板塊可能以頭髮生長的速度移動。"},{"en":"The rate at which something happens means how quickly it happens.","zh":"「the rate at which」某事發生，意思是它發生得有多快。"},{"en":"The rate at which students improve depends on practice and feedback.","zh":"學生進步的速度取決於練習和回饋。"},{"en":"If a process happens at a slow rate, results may take years to appear.","zh":"如果過程以緩慢速度發生，結果可能多年後才出現。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a measure of speed or pace.","zh":"這個短語引入速度或步伐的量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"consistent and essentially unstoppable","meaning":"持續而基本上無法阻止","examples":[{"en":"Plate movement is consistent and essentially unstoppable.","zh":"板塊移動持續而基本上無法阻止。"},{"en":"Consistent and essentially unstoppable means steady and almost impossible to stop.","zh":"「consistent and essentially unstoppable」意思是穩定持續且幾乎不能停止。"},{"en":"A small daily habit can become consistent and difficult to break after many months.","zh":"每日小習慣持續多月後，可以變得穩定且難以打破。"},{"en":"If plate movement cannot be stopped, humans must understand and prepare for its effects.","zh":"如果板塊移動不能停止，人類就必須理解並準備其影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement that continues with great persistence.","zh":"這個短語描述非常持久的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the results can be spectacular","meaning":"結果可以非常壯觀","examples":[{"en":"The results can be spectacular when plates meet.","zh":"當板塊相遇時，結果可以非常壯觀。"},{"en":"The results can be spectacular means the effects can be dramatic and impressive.","zh":"「the results can be spectacular」意思是效果可以戲劇性而令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"If a school art project succeeds, the results can be spectacular in the exhibition hall.","zh":"如果學校藝術項目成功，展覽廳中的結果可以非常壯觀。"},{"en":"When huge natural forces combine, they can produce mountains, volcanoes, and earthquakes.","zh":"當巨大自然力量結合，它們可以產生山脈、火山和地震。"},{"en":"The phrase prepares readers for impressive outcomes.","zh":"這個短語讓讀者準備看到令人驚嘆的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"particularly when","meaning":"特別是在……時","examples":[{"en":"Plate movement becomes dramatic particularly when plates meet.","zh":"板塊移動特別是在板塊相遇時變得劇烈。"},{"en":"Particularly when means especially in the situation where something happens.","zh":"「particularly when」意思是尤其在某情況發生時。"},{"en":"Students feel nervous particularly when an exam decides their future school place.","zh":"學生特別是在考試決定未來學校名額時感到緊張。"},{"en":"If plates simply move slowly apart, the effect may be less dramatic than when they collide.","zh":"如果板塊只是慢慢分開，其效果可能沒有碰撞時那麼劇烈。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights one important condition.","zh":"這個短語突出一個重要條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the release of heat","meaning":"熱量釋放","examples":[{"en":"The release of heat can trigger geological events.","zh":"熱量釋放可以觸發地質事件。"},{"en":"The release of heat means heat energy is let out or transferred.","zh":"「the release of heat」意思是熱能被放出或轉移。"},{"en":"A laptop may slow down if the release of heat is blocked by dust.","zh":"如果熱量釋放被灰塵阻塞，手提電腦可能變慢。"},{"en":"In Earth, released heat can help melt rock and drive movement.","zh":"在地球內部，釋放的熱量可以幫助熔化岩石並推動移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes heat leaving or becoming active in a system.","zh":"這個短語描述熱量離開或在系統中變得活躍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"resulting buckling and melting","meaning":"隨之而來的彎曲變形和熔化","examples":[{"en":"The resulting buckling and melting create dramatic geological features.","zh":"隨之而來的彎曲變形和熔化形成劇烈地質特徵。"},{"en":"Resulting buckling and melting means bending and melting that happen as a result of pressure and heat.","zh":"「resulting buckling and melting」意思是由壓力和熱力造成的彎曲變形和熔化。"},{"en":"A plastic ruler may buckle near heat, but rocks buckle on a much larger scale.","zh":"塑膠尺遇熱可能彎曲，但岩石會在大得多的尺度上彎曲。"},{"en":"When plates collide, pressure bends rocks and heat may melt some material.","zh":"當板塊碰撞，壓力使岩石彎曲，熱力可能熔化某些物質。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical changes caused by tectonic forces.","zh":"這個短語描述由構造力量造成的物理變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"give rise to","meaning":"引起；產生","examples":[{"en":"Plate collisions give rise to earthquakes and mountains.","zh":"板塊碰撞引起地震和山脈。"},{"en":"To give rise to something means to cause it to happen or appear.","zh":"「give rise to」某事，意思是導致它發生或出現。"},{"en":"Poor communication can give rise to misunderstandings in a group project.","zh":"溝通不良可以在小組專題中引起誤會。"},{"en":"When plates push together, pressure can give rise to earthquakes.","zh":"當板塊互相擠壓，壓力可以引起地震。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a cause with a new result.","zh":"這個短語把原因與新結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"geological events","meaning":"地質事件","examples":[{"en":"Earthquakes are major geological events.","zh":"地震是重大地質事件。"},{"en":"Geological events are natural events related to Earth’s structure, rocks, and internal forces.","zh":"「geological events」是與地球結構、岩石和內部力量有關的自然事件。"},{"en":"Volcanic eruptions and earthquakes are geological events students often study in geography.","zh":"火山爆發和地震是學生在地理課常研究的地質事件。"},{"en":"If geological events happen near cities, they can cause serious damage.","zh":"如果地質事件發生在城市附近，可能造成嚴重破壞。"},{"en":"The phrase describes major Earth processes or incidents.","zh":"這個短語描述重大地球過程或事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"geological features","meaning":"地質特徵","examples":[{"en":"Mountains and volcanoes are geological features.","zh":"山脈和火山是地質特徵。"},{"en":"Geological features are physical landforms or structures created by Earth processes.","zh":"「geological features」是由地球過程造成的實體地貌或結構。"},{"en":"Valleys, ridges, cliffs, and trenches are geological features.","zh":"山谷、山脊、懸崖和海溝都是地質特徵。"},{"en":"If plates collide or separate, new geological features can form over time.","zh":"如果板塊碰撞或分離，新的地質特徵可以隨時間形成。"},{"en":"The phrase names visible results of Earth’s history.","zh":"這個短語指出地球歷史的可見結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"earthquakes","meaning":"地震","examples":[{"en":"Earthquakes often occur near plate boundaries.","zh":"地震常發生在板塊邊界附近。"},{"en":"Earthquakes are sudden shaking movements of the ground caused by energy release in Earth’s crust.","zh":"「earthquakes」是地殼中能量釋放造成的地面突然震動。"},{"en":"Schools in earthquake zones practise safety drills regularly.","zh":"位於地震帶的學校會定期進行安全演習。"},{"en":"When pressure builds along a fault, an earthquake may occur.","zh":"當壓力沿斷層累積，地震可能發生。"},{"en":"The word describes one of the most dangerous geological events.","zh":"這個詞描述最危險的地質事件之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"volcanoes","meaning":"火山","examples":[{"en":"Volcanoes often form near plate boundaries.","zh":"火山常在板塊邊界附近形成。"},{"en":"Volcanoes are openings or mountains where molten rock, ash, and gas can reach the surface.","zh":"「volcanoes」是熔融岩石、火山灰和氣體可以到達地表的開口或山。"},{"en":"Tourists may visit inactive volcanoes, but active ones require careful monitoring.","zh":"遊客可能參觀休眠火山，但活火山需要仔細監測。"},{"en":"If molten rock rises through cracks, a volcano may form or erupt.","zh":"如果熔融岩石透過裂縫上升，火山可能形成或爆發。"},{"en":"The word describes a landform linked with Earth’s internal heat.","zh":"這個詞描述與地球內部熱量有關的地貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"oceanic ridges and trenches","meaning":"海洋中脊和海溝","examples":[{"en":"Plate movement creates oceanic ridges and trenches.","zh":"板塊移動形成海洋中脊和海溝。"},{"en":"Oceanic ridges and trenches are raised and deep features on the ocean floor.","zh":"「oceanic ridges and trenches」是海底上的隆起和深陷特徵。"},{"en":"A map of the seabed may show long oceanic ridges and very deep trenches.","zh":"海床地圖可能顯示長長的海洋中脊和非常深的海溝。"},{"en":"If plates move apart, ridges may form; if one plate sinks, trenches may form.","zh":"如果板塊分開，可能形成中脊；如果一個板塊下沉，可能形成海溝。"},{"en":"The phrase names major underwater geological features.","zh":"這個短語指出主要海底地質特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"plate boundaries","meaning":"板塊邊界","examples":[{"en":"Plate boundaries see most of the world’s active volcanoes.","zh":"世界上大多數活火山出現在板塊邊界。"},{"en":"Plate boundaries are the edges where tectonic plates meet, separate, or slide past each other.","zh":"「plate boundaries」是構造板塊相遇、分離或互相滑過的邊緣。"},{"en":"Geography students mark plate boundaries on maps to explain earthquakes.","zh":"地理學生在地圖上標示板塊邊界，以解釋地震。"},{"en":"If people live near plate boundaries, they may face higher volcanic or earthquake risk.","zh":"如果人們住在板塊邊界附近，可能面對較高火山或地震風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the active edges of tectonic plates.","zh":"這個短語描述構造板塊活躍的邊緣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"active volcanoes","meaning":"活火山","examples":[{"en":"Most active volcanoes occur along plate boundaries.","zh":"大多數活火山出現在板塊邊界沿線。"},{"en":"Active volcanoes are volcanoes that are erupting now or may erupt again in the future.","zh":"「active volcanoes」是正在爆發或未來可能再次爆發的火山。"},{"en":"Scientists monitor active volcanoes for gas, heat, and ground movement.","zh":"科學家監測活火山的氣體、熱量和地面移動。"},{"en":"If an active volcano shows warning signs, nearby residents may need to evacuate.","zh":"如果活火山顯示警號，附近居民可能需要疏散。"},{"en":"The phrase describes volcanoes that still pose a real risk.","zh":"這個短語描述仍然構成真實風險的火山。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the Pacific Plate","meaning":"太平洋板塊","examples":[{"en":"The Pacific Plate is associated with the Ring of Fire.","zh":"太平洋板塊與環太平洋火山帶有關。"},{"en":"The Pacific Plate is a huge tectonic plate beneath much of the Pacific Ocean.","zh":"「the Pacific Plate」是位於大部分太平洋下方的巨大構造板塊。"},{"en":"On a plate map, students can see that the Pacific Plate touches many other plates.","zh":"在板塊地圖上，學生可以看到太平洋板塊接觸許多其他板塊。"},{"en":"Because its edges are active, many earthquakes and volcanoes occur around it.","zh":"因為其邊緣活躍，周圍發生許多地震和火山活動。"},{"en":"The phrase names one of Earth’s major tectonic plates.","zh":"這個短語指出地球主要構造板塊之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Ring of Fire","meaning":"環太平洋火山帶","examples":[{"en":"The Pacific Plate’s Ring of Fire is a good example of volcanic activity.","zh":"太平洋板塊的環太平洋火山帶是火山活動的好例子。"},{"en":"The Ring of Fire is a zone around the Pacific Ocean with many volcanoes and earthquakes.","zh":"「Ring of Fire」是環繞太平洋、擁有許多火山和地震的地帶。"},{"en":"Japan, Indonesia, and parts of the Americas lie near the Ring of Fire.","zh":"日本、印尼和美洲部分地區位於環太平洋火山帶附近。"},{"en":"If plates around the Pacific move, the Ring of Fire remains highly active.","zh":"如果太平洋周圍板塊移動，環太平洋火山帶仍非常活躍。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major belt of geological activity.","zh":"這個短語指出一條主要地質活動帶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"volcanism","meaning":"火山活動","examples":[{"en":"Volcanism may sometimes occur in the middle of plates.","zh":"火山活動有時可能發生在板塊中間。"},{"en":"Volcanism means the processes connected with volcano formation, magma movement, and eruptions.","zh":"「volcanism」意思是與火山形成、岩漿移動和爆發有關的過程。"},{"en":"Geography students study volcanism to understand lava, ash, and volcanic islands.","zh":"地理學生研究火山活動，以理解熔岩、火山灰和火山島。"},{"en":"If magma rises through the crust, volcanism can create new landforms.","zh":"如果岩漿穿過地殼上升，火山活動可以創造新地貌。"},{"en":"The word describes volcanic activity as a geological process.","zh":"這個詞把火山活動描述為地質過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"occur in the middle of","meaning":"發生在……中間","examples":[{"en":"Volcanism can occur in the middle of tectonic plates.","zh":"火山活動可以發生在構造板塊中間。"},{"en":"To occur in the middle of something means to happen away from the edges or boundaries.","zh":"「occur in the middle of」某物，意思是發生在遠離邊緣或邊界的位置。"},{"en":"A traffic jam can occur in the middle of a tunnel if a car breaks down.","zh":"如果汽車拋錨，交通擠塞可以發生在隧道中間。"},{"en":"If volcanoes form in the middle of a plate, scientists need another explanation besides plate boundaries.","zh":"如果火山在板塊中間形成，科學家需要除板塊邊界以外的解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes location inside an area rather than at its edge.","zh":"這個短語描述在某區內部而非邊緣的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be theorised to be","meaning":"被理論上解釋為","examples":[{"en":"This type of volcanism has been theorised to be caused by hotspots.","zh":"這種火山活動被理論上解釋為由熱點造成。"},{"en":"To be theorised to be means scientists have proposed that something is the case.","zh":"「be theorised to be」意思是科學家提出某事可能如此。"},{"en":"Some memory problems are theorised to be linked to lack of sleep.","zh":"有些記憶問題被理論上解釋為與睡眠不足有關。"},{"en":"If something is only theorised, more evidence may still be needed.","zh":"如果某事只是理論上提出，可能仍需要更多證據。"},{"en":"The phrase presents an explanation as a scientific theory, not final certainty.","zh":"這個短語把解釋呈現為科學理論，而非最終確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a result of","meaning":"……的結果","examples":[{"en":"Mid-plate volcanism may be a result of hotspots.","zh":"板塊中部火山活動可能是熱點的結果。"},{"en":"A result of something is something caused by it.","zh":"「a result of」某事，是由它造成的結果。"},{"en":"Poor marks may be a result of weak planning rather than low ability.","zh":"成績差可能是規劃薄弱的結果，而不是能力低。"},{"en":"If hot material rises under a plate, volcanism may be the result.","zh":"如果熱物質在板塊下方上升，火山活動可能就是結果。"},{"en":"The phrase links an effect to its cause.","zh":"這個短語把結果與原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hotspots","meaning":"熱點","examples":[{"en":"Hotspots are unusually hot areas of interior rock.","zh":"熱點是地球內部岩石中異常高溫的區域。"},{"en":"Hotspots are places beneath Earth’s crust where heat is unusually concentrated.","zh":"「hotspots」是地殼下方熱量異常集中的地方。"},{"en":"In geology, hotspots can explain volcanoes that are far from plate boundaries.","zh":"在地質學中，熱點可以解釋遠離板塊邊界的火山。"},{"en":"If a plate moves over a hotspot, a chain of volcanic islands may form.","zh":"如果板塊移過熱點，可能形成一串火山島。"},{"en":"The word describes a hot geological source below the surface.","zh":"這個詞描述地表下的高溫地質來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"anomalously hot areas","meaning":"異常高溫區域","examples":[{"en":"Hotspots are anomalously hot areas beneath the crust.","zh":"熱點是地殼下方的異常高溫區域。"},{"en":"Anomalously hot areas are places that are much hotter than expected or normal.","zh":"「anomalously hot areas」是比預期或正常情況熱得多的地方。"},{"en":"A doctor may notice an anomalously hot area on the skin during an infection.","zh":"感染時，醫生可能注意到皮膚上有異常高溫區域。"},{"en":"If rock below the crust is unusually hot, it may melt and rise.","zh":"如果地殼下方岩石異常高溫，它可能熔化並上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes heat that is abnormal for its location.","zh":"這個短語描述某位置中不正常的高熱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"interior rock","meaning":"地球內部岩石","examples":[{"en":"Interior rock can melt through a plate.","zh":"地球內部岩石可以熔穿板塊。"},{"en":"Interior rock is rock located deep inside Earth rather than at the surface.","zh":"「interior rock」是位於地球深處而非地表的岩石。"},{"en":"Scientists cannot easily see interior rock, so they study indirect evidence.","zh":"科學家不能輕易看見地球內部岩石，所以研究間接證據。"},{"en":"If interior rock becomes hot enough, it may melt and move upward.","zh":"如果地球內部岩石變得足夠熱，它可能熔化並向上移動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to rock from within the planet.","zh":"這個短語指來自地球內部的岩石。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"melt through","meaning":"熔穿","examples":[{"en":"Hot interior rock may melt through the plate.","zh":"熱的地球內部岩石可能熔穿板塊。"},{"en":"To melt through something means to pass through it by melting or burning a path.","zh":"「melt through」某物，意思是透過熔化或燒出路徑穿過它。"},{"en":"A hot object can melt through thin plastic if it is left there too long.","zh":"如果熱物體放在薄塑膠上太久，可能熔穿它。"},{"en":"If very hot rock melts through crust, volcanic activity may reach the surface.","zh":"如果極熱岩石熔穿地殼，火山活動可能到達地表。"},{"en":"The phrase describes heat creating a passage through material.","zh":"這個短語描述熱力在材料中形成通道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"force an escape to the surface","meaning":"迫使……逃逸至地表","examples":[{"en":"Hot rock forces an escape to the surface.","zh":"熱岩石迫使物質逃逸至地表。"},{"en":"To force an escape to the surface means to push material upward until it reaches the outside.","zh":"「force an escape to the surface」意思是把物質向上推，直到它到達外部。"},{"en":"Pressure in a shaken bottle can force liquid to escape to the surface when opened.","zh":"搖晃過的瓶子被打開時，壓力可以迫使液體衝出表面。"},{"en":"If hot rock cannot stay below, pressure may drive it upward as magma.","zh":"如果熱岩石不能留在下方，壓力可能把它作為岩漿向上推。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pressure pushing something out.","zh":"這個短語描述壓力把某物推出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"come in three types","meaning":"分為三種類型","examples":[{"en":"Plate boundaries come in three types.","zh":"板塊邊界分為三種類型。"},{"en":"To come in three types means to be divided into three main categories.","zh":"「come in three types」意思是分成三個主要類別。"},{"en":"This grammar exercise comes in three types: correction, completion, and rewriting.","zh":"這個文法練習分為三種類型：改錯、填充和改寫。"},{"en":"If students know the three types, they can classify examples more easily.","zh":"如果學生知道三種類型，就能更容易分類例子。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a simple classification.","zh":"這個短語引入簡單分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"transform boundaries","meaning":"轉形邊界","examples":[{"en":"Transform boundaries occur where plates grind past each other.","zh":"轉形邊界出現在板塊互相擦過的地方。"},{"en":"Transform boundaries are plate boundaries where two plates slide horizontally past one another.","zh":"「transform boundaries」是兩個板塊水平互相滑過的板塊邊界。"},{"en":"Students may model transform boundaries by sliding two books side by side in opposite directions.","zh":"學生可以用兩本書並排向相反方向滑動來模擬轉形邊界。"},{"en":"When plates grind at transform boundaries, earthquakes can occur.","zh":"當板塊在轉形邊界摩擦，地震可能發生。"},{"en":"The phrase names one type of plate boundary.","zh":"這個短語指出一種板塊邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"grind past each other","meaning":"互相擦過","examples":[{"en":"At transform boundaries, plates grind past each other.","zh":"在轉形邊界，板塊互相擦過。"},{"en":"To grind past each other means to rub against one another while moving in opposite or different directions.","zh":"「grind past each other」意思是在相反或不同方向移動時互相摩擦。"},{"en":"Two heavy boxes may grind past each other in a narrow storeroom.","zh":"兩個重箱在狹窄儲物室中可能互相擦過。"},{"en":"If plates grind together, friction can build up stress.","zh":"如果板塊互相摩擦，摩擦力可以累積壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rough sideways movement.","zh":"這個短語描述粗糙的橫向移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"it was once thought that","meaning":"人們曾經認為","examples":[{"en":"It was once thought that the Aegir Ridge was active.","zh":"人們曾經認為埃吉爾海嶺是活躍的。"},{"en":"It was once thought that means people believed something in the past, but it may no longer be accepted.","zh":"「it was once thought that」意思是人們過去相信某事，但它現在未必再被接受。"},{"en":"It was once thought that children learned best only through memorisation.","zh":"人們曾經認為孩子只靠背誦學得最好。"},{"en":"If new evidence appears, old beliefs may be corrected.","zh":"如果新證據出現，舊信念可能被修正。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a former belief.","zh":"這個短語引入過去的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"well-known","meaning":"著名的","examples":[{"en":"The well-known Aegir Ridge was once thought to be a transform boundary.","zh":"著名的埃吉爾海嶺曾被認為是轉形邊界。"},{"en":"Well-known means familiar to many people or widely recognised.","zh":"「well-known」意思是許多人熟悉或廣泛認識。"},{"en":"A well-known teacher may attract students because of strong exam results.","zh":"著名老師可能因出色考試成績而吸引學生。"},{"en":"If a place is well-known, writers may not need to explain it in detail.","zh":"如果某地方很著名，作者可能不需要詳細解釋它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes public familiarity or recognition.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾熟悉度或認知度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Aegir Ridge","meaning":"埃吉爾海嶺","examples":[{"en":"The Aegir Ridge was later shown to have never been active.","zh":"埃吉爾海嶺後來被證明從未活躍。"},{"en":"The Aegir Ridge is an oceanic ridge once discussed in relation to plate boundaries.","zh":"「Aegir Ridge」是一條曾在板塊邊界相關討論中出現的海洋中脊。"},{"en":"In a geology question, the Aegir Ridge may be used as an example of an earlier mistaken view.","zh":"在地質題中，埃吉爾海嶺可能被用作早期錯誤觀點的例子。"},{"en":"If later evidence shows a ridge was inactive, earlier classification must change.","zh":"如果後來證據顯示海嶺不活躍，早期分類就必須改變。"},{"en":"The name refers to a specific geological feature.","zh":"這個名稱指一個特定地質特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"whereas","meaning":"然而；相比之下","examples":[{"en":"The Aegir Ridge was inactive, whereas the San Andreas Fault shows the opposite case.","zh":"埃吉爾海嶺並不活躍，然而聖安德烈亞斯斷層顯示正好相反的情況。"},{"en":"Whereas means while, but in contrast.","zh":"「whereas」意思是然而、相比之下。"},{"en":"Some students learn best by reading, whereas others need spoken explanation.","zh":"有些學生透過閱讀學得最好，而另一些則需要口頭解釋。"},{"en":"If one example is inactive whereas another is active, the contrast becomes clear.","zh":"如果一個例子不活躍，而另一個活躍，對比就變得清楚。"},{"en":"The word is used to compare two different situations.","zh":"這個詞用來比較兩種不同情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"periodic earthquakes","meaning":"週期性地震","examples":[{"en":"Periodic earthquakes occur along the San Andreas Fault.","zh":"週期性地震沿聖安德烈亞斯斷層發生。"},{"en":"Periodic earthquakes are earthquakes that happen from time to time at repeated intervals.","zh":"「periodic earthquakes」是每隔一段時間反覆發生的地震。"},{"en":"A city near an active fault may prepare for periodic earthquakes through regular drills.","zh":"位於活躍斷層附近的城市可能透過定期演習準備週期性地震。"},{"en":"If pressure builds and releases repeatedly, earthquakes may occur periodically.","zh":"如果壓力反覆累積和釋放，地震可能週期性發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recurring earthquake activity.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆出現的地震活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"San Andreas Fault","meaning":"聖安德烈亞斯斷層","examples":[{"en":"The San Andreas Fault is an active example of a transform boundary.","zh":"聖安德烈亞斯斷層是轉形邊界的活躍例子。"},{"en":"The San Andreas Fault is a major fault in California where two plates slide past each other.","zh":"「San Andreas Fault」是加州一條主要斷層，兩個板塊在那裡互相滑過。"},{"en":"Students often study the San Andreas Fault when learning about earthquake risk.","zh":"學生學習地震風險時，常研究聖安德烈亞斯斷層。"},{"en":"Because the fault is active, pressure along it can produce earthquakes.","zh":"因為該斷層活躍，沿線壓力可以造成地震。"},{"en":"The phrase names a famous geological fault.","zh":"這個短語指出一條著名地質斷層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the very opposite case","meaning":"正好相反的情況","examples":[{"en":"The San Andreas Fault shows the very opposite case.","zh":"聖安德烈亞斯斷層顯示正好相反的情況。"},{"en":"The very opposite case means a situation that is completely different from the one just mentioned.","zh":"「the very opposite case」意思是與剛提及情況完全相反的情況。"},{"en":"One student studies too little; another studies all night without rest, the very opposite case.","zh":"一個學生溫習太少；另一個通宵不休息地溫習，正好相反。"},{"en":"If one ridge is inactive and another fault is active, they illustrate opposing examples.","zh":"如果一條海嶺不活躍，而另一條斷層活躍，它們展示相反例子。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly highlights contrast.","zh":"這個短語強烈突出對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"divergent boundaries","meaning":"張裂型邊界","examples":[{"en":"Divergent boundaries occur where two plates slide apart.","zh":"張裂型邊界出現在兩個板塊分離滑開的地方。"},{"en":"Divergent boundaries are plate boundaries where plates move away from each other.","zh":"「divergent boundaries」是板塊彼此遠離的板塊邊界。"},{"en":"Students can model divergent boundaries by pulling two pieces of paper apart.","zh":"學生可以拉開兩張紙來模擬張裂型邊界。"},{"en":"When plates separate, magma may rise and form new crust.","zh":"當板塊分離，岩漿可能上升並形成新地殼。"},{"en":"The phrase names a boundary type based on separation.","zh":"這個短語指出基於分離的邊界類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"slide apart from each other","meaning":"彼此分離滑開","examples":[{"en":"At divergent boundaries, two plates slide apart from each other.","zh":"在張裂型邊界，兩個板塊彼此分離滑開。"},{"en":"To slide apart from each other means to move away from one another while sliding.","zh":"「slide apart from each other」意思是滑動時彼此遠離。"},{"en":"Two books on a desk can slide apart from each other if pushed in opposite directions.","zh":"如果兩本書在桌上被向相反方向推，它們可以彼此分離滑開。"},{"en":"If plates slide apart, new material may rise between them.","zh":"如果板塊分離滑開，新物質可能在它們之間上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes separation by smooth movement.","zh":"這個短語描述透過滑動而分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"mid-oceanic ridges","meaning":"大洋中脊","examples":[{"en":"Mid-oceanic ridges can form at divergent boundaries.","zh":"大洋中脊可以在張裂型邊界形成。"},{"en":"Mid-oceanic ridges are long raised mountain-like features on the ocean floor.","zh":"「mid-oceanic ridges」是海底上長長隆起、像山脈的地貌。"},{"en":"A seabed map may show mid-oceanic ridges running through the middle of oceans.","zh":"海床地圖可能顯示大洋中脊穿過海洋中部。"},{"en":"If plates move apart under the sea, new crust can build these ridges.","zh":"如果板塊在海底分離，新地殼可以建立這些中脊。"},{"en":"The phrase names underwater ridges formed by plate separation.","zh":"這個短語指出由板塊分離形成的海底山脊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"active rift zones","meaning":"活躍裂谷帶","examples":[{"en":"Active rift zones are examples of divergent boundaries.","zh":"活躍裂谷帶是張裂型邊界的例子。"},{"en":"Active rift zones are areas where Earth’s crust is being pulled apart now or in recent geological time.","zh":"「active rift zones」是地殼正在或在近地質時期被拉開的地區。"},{"en":"In geography, East Africa is often discussed as an active rift zone.","zh":"在地理中，東非常被討論為活躍裂谷帶。"},{"en":"If a rift zone is active, earthquakes and volcanic activity may occur there.","zh":"如果裂谷帶活躍，當地可能發生地震和火山活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a place where land is splitting apart.","zh":"這個短語描述陸地正在裂開的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"East Africa","meaning":"東非","examples":[{"en":"East Africa contains active rift zones.","zh":"東非包含活躍裂谷帶。"},{"en":"East Africa is the eastern region of the African continent.","zh":"「East Africa」是非洲大陸東部地區。"},{"en":"Geography students study East Africa because its rift system shows plates pulling apart.","zh":"地理學生研究東非，因為其裂谷系統顯示板塊正在拉開。"},{"en":"If rifting continues, parts of the region may slowly change shape over millions of years.","zh":"如果裂谷活動持續，該地區部分地方可能在數百萬年間慢慢改變形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase names a region important in plate-boundary examples.","zh":"這個短語指出板塊邊界例子中的重要地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"convergent boundaries","meaning":"聚合型邊界","examples":[{"en":"Convergent boundaries occur where two plates move towards each other.","zh":"聚合型邊界出現在兩個板塊彼此靠近的地方。"},{"en":"Convergent boundaries are plate boundaries where plates move together and collide or one sinks beneath another.","zh":"「convergent boundaries」是板塊互相靠近並碰撞，或一個板塊沉到另一個下方的邊界。"},{"en":"Students can model convergent boundaries by pushing two books toward each other.","zh":"學生可以把兩本書互相推近來模擬聚合型邊界。"},{"en":"When plates converge, mountains, trenches, or volcanoes may form.","zh":"當板塊聚合，山脈、海溝或火山可能形成。"},{"en":"The phrase names a boundary type based on coming together.","zh":"這個短語指出基於靠近的邊界類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"slide towards each other","meaning":"彼此靠近滑動","examples":[{"en":"At convergent boundaries, two plates slide towards each other.","zh":"在聚合型邊界，兩個板塊彼此靠近滑動。"},{"en":"To slide towards each other means to move closer together while sliding.","zh":"「slide towards each other」意思是滑動時彼此靠近。"},{"en":"Two chairs can slide towards each other if pushed across a smooth floor.","zh":"如果在平滑地板上推動，兩張椅子可以彼此靠近滑動。"},{"en":"If plates slide towards each other, pressure builds between them.","zh":"如果板塊彼此靠近滑動，它們之間會累積壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement that leads to collision or compression.","zh":"這個短語描述導致碰撞或擠壓的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"form either…or…","meaning":"形成……或……","examples":[{"en":"Convergent boundaries can form either a subduction zone or a continental collision.","zh":"聚合型邊界可以形成隱沒帶或大陸碰撞。"},{"en":"Form either A or B means produce one of two possible results.","zh":"「form either A or B」意思是產生兩種可能結果之一。"},{"en":"A school club can form either a debate team or a drama group depending on student interest.","zh":"學校學會可以按學生興趣形成辯論隊或戲劇組。"},{"en":"If different plate types meet, the boundary may develop in different ways.","zh":"如果不同板塊類型相遇，邊界可能以不同方式發展。"},{"en":"The phrase presents two possible outcomes.","zh":"這個短語呈現兩種可能結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"subduction zone","meaning":"隱沒帶","examples":[{"en":"A subduction zone forms when one plate moves underneath another.","zh":"當一個板塊移到另一個板塊下方時，隱沒帶形成。"},{"en":"A subduction zone is an area where one tectonic plate sinks below another plate.","zh":"「subduction zone」是一個構造板塊沉到另一板塊下方的地區。"},{"en":"Students may draw a subduction zone to show oceanic crust descending beneath continental crust.","zh":"學生可能畫出隱沒帶，以展示海洋地殼沉到大陸地殼下方。"},{"en":"If a plate descends, heat and pressure can cause volcanism and trenches.","zh":"如果板塊下沉，熱力和壓力可以造成火山活動和海溝。"},{"en":"The phrase names a boundary process involving sinking.","zh":"這個短語指出涉及下沉的邊界過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"move underneath","meaning":"移到……下方","examples":[{"en":"One plate may move underneath another plate.","zh":"一個板塊可能移到另一個板塊下方。"},{"en":"To move underneath something means to pass or slide below it.","zh":"「move underneath」某物，意思是移到或滑到其下面。"},{"en":"A cat may move underneath a table to hide.","zh":"貓可能移到桌子下方躲藏。"},{"en":"If one plate moves underneath another, a subduction zone can form.","zh":"如果一個板塊移到另一個下方，隱沒帶可以形成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes downward movement below another object.","zh":"這個短語描述移到另一物體下方的向下移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"continental collision","meaning":"大陸碰撞","examples":[{"en":"A continental collision occurs when continental plates push together.","zh":"當大陸板塊互相擠壓時，大陸碰撞發生。"},{"en":"Continental collision is the meeting and compression of two continental plates.","zh":"「continental collision」是兩個大陸板塊相遇並被擠壓。"},{"en":"Students often study India and Asia as a famous example of continental collision.","zh":"學生常研究印度與亞洲，作為大陸碰撞的著名例子。"},{"en":"When continental plates collide, neither plate easily sinks, so land may rise into mountains.","zh":"當大陸板塊碰撞，兩者都不容易下沉，因此陸地可能上升成山脈。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the plate process that builds major mountain ranges.","zh":"這個短語描述建立主要山脈的板塊過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"deep marine trenches","meaning":"深海海溝","examples":[{"en":"Deep marine trenches are formed in a subduction zone.","zh":"深海海溝在隱沒帶形成。"},{"en":"Deep marine trenches are long, very deep valleys on the ocean floor.","zh":"「deep marine trenches」是海底上又長又非常深的谷地。"},{"en":"A world map of the seabed may show deep marine trenches near plate boundaries.","zh":"世界海床地圖可能顯示板塊邊界附近的深海海溝。"},{"en":"If one plate sinks under another, the ocean floor can bend downward into a trench.","zh":"如果一個板塊沉到另一個下方，海底可以向下彎曲成海溝。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extremely deep underwater landforms.","zh":"這個短語描述極深的海底地貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in the former case","meaning":"在前一種情況下","examples":[{"en":"In the former case, deep marine trenches are formed.","zh":"在前一種情況下，深海海溝會形成。"},{"en":"In the former case means in the first of the two situations just mentioned.","zh":"「in the former case」意思是在剛提及兩種情況中的第一種。"},{"en":"A school may offer online and face-to-face lessons; in the former case, students need a stable internet connection.","zh":"學校可能提供網課和面授課；在前一種情況下，學生需要穩定網絡。"},{"en":"If two options are listed, this phrase refers back to the first option.","zh":"如果列出兩個選項，這個短語指回第一個選項。"},{"en":"The phrase helps organise comparison between two cases.","zh":"這個短語幫助組織兩種情況的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"descending plate","meaning":"下沉板塊","examples":[{"en":"The descending plate is heated in the Earth’s interior.","zh":"下沉板塊在地球內部被加熱。"},{"en":"A descending plate is a tectonic plate moving downward beneath another plate.","zh":"「descending plate」是移到另一個板塊下方的構造板塊。"},{"en":"In a diagram of subduction, the descending plate is usually shown sloping into the mantle.","zh":"在隱沒作用圖中，下沉板塊通常被畫成斜斜進入地幔。"},{"en":"As the plate descends, heat and pressure increase.","zh":"當板塊下沉，熱力和壓力會增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the sinking plate in a subduction zone.","zh":"這個短語描述隱沒帶中的下沉板塊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be heated in","meaning":"在……中被加熱","examples":[{"en":"The descending plate is heated in the Earth’s interior.","zh":"下沉板塊在地球內部被加熱。"},{"en":"To be heated in a place means to become hotter while inside that place.","zh":"「be heated in」某地方，意思是在該處內部變熱。"},{"en":"Food is heated in an oven until it is ready to eat.","zh":"食物在焗爐中被加熱，直到可以食用。"},{"en":"If a plate sinks into Earth’s interior, it is exposed to intense heat.","zh":"如果板塊沉入地球內部，它會暴露於強烈熱力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where heating happens.","zh":"這個短語描述加熱發生的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"trapped water","meaning":"被困住的水","examples":[{"en":"The descending plate releases trapped water.","zh":"下沉板塊釋放被困住的水。"},{"en":"Trapped water is water held inside rocks, spaces, or materials and unable to escape easily.","zh":"「trapped water」是被保存在岩石、空隙或材料中，難以逃出的水。"},{"en":"Trapped water inside a wall can cause damp marks and damage paint.","zh":"牆內被困住的水可以造成潮濕痕跡並損壞油漆。"},{"en":"If a descending plate releases trapped water, melting processes may be affected.","zh":"如果下沉板塊釋放被困住的水，熔化過程可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes water locked inside material.","zh":"這個短語描述被鎖在材料內的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"immense heat and pressure","meaning":"巨大的熱力和壓力","examples":[{"en":"Immense heat and pressure rise to the surface.","zh":"巨大的熱力和壓力升至地表。"},{"en":"Immense heat and pressure means extremely great temperature and force.","zh":"「immense heat and pressure」意思是極高溫度和極大力量。"},{"en":"Deep underground rocks can change form under immense heat and pressure.","zh":"地底深處岩石可以在巨大熱力和壓力下改變形態。"},{"en":"If heat and pressure are high enough, rock may melt or deform.","zh":"如果熱力和壓力足夠高，岩石可能熔化或變形。"},{"en":"The phrase describes powerful physical conditions inside Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述地球內部強大的物理條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rise to the surface","meaning":"升至地表","examples":[{"en":"Heat and pressure rise to the surface.","zh":"熱力和壓力升至地表。"},{"en":"To rise to the surface means to move upward until reaching the outside or top layer.","zh":"「rise to the surface」意思是向上移動直到到達外部或最上層。"},{"en":"Oil may rise to the surface of soup because it is lighter than water.","zh":"油可能因比水輕而升至湯的表面。"},{"en":"If magma rises to the surface, a volcano may erupt.","zh":"如果岩漿升至地表，火山可能爆發。"},{"en":"The phrase describes upward movement from inside to outside.","zh":"這個短語描述由內部向外部的上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"causing something to form","meaning":"導致……形成","examples":[{"en":"Heat and pressure rise to the surface, causing mountains to form.","zh":"熱力和壓力升至地表，導致山脈形成。"},{"en":"Causing something to form means making something develop, appear, or take shape.","zh":"「causing something to form」意思是令某物發展、出現或成形。"},{"en":"Cold air can cause ice to form on a car window.","zh":"冷空氣可以導致汽車窗上形成冰。"},{"en":"If tectonic pressure pushes land upward, it can cause mountains to form.","zh":"如果構造壓力把陸地向上推，它可以導致山脈形成。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a cause with the creation of something.","zh":"這個短語把原因與某物形成連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the Andes","meaning":"安第斯山脈","examples":[{"en":"The Andes were formed by tectonic processes.","zh":"安第斯山脈由構造過程形成。"},{"en":"The Andes are a long mountain range along the western edge of South America.","zh":"「the Andes」是沿南美洲西部邊緣延伸的長山脈。"},{"en":"Geography students study the Andes as an example of mountains linked to plate movement.","zh":"地理學生研究安第斯山脈，作為與板塊移動有關的山脈例子。"},{"en":"If oceanic crust subducts near a continent, mountain ranges like the Andes can form.","zh":"如果海洋地殼在大陸附近隱沒，像安第斯山脈這樣的山脈可以形成。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major mountain system.","zh":"這個短語指出一個主要山脈系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the best example of","meaning":"……的最佳例子","examples":[{"en":"The Indian plate is the best example of a continental collision.","zh":"印度板塊是大陸碰撞的最佳例子。"},{"en":"The best example of something is the clearest or most useful case for explaining it.","zh":"「the best example of」某事，是最清楚或最有用來解釋它的個案。"},{"en":"A student’s improved essay may be the best example of how feedback helps learning.","zh":"學生改善後的文章可能是回饋如何幫助學習的最佳例子。"},{"en":"If one case shows a process very clearly, teachers often use it as the main example.","zh":"如果一個個案非常清楚顯示過程，老師常用它作主要例子。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the strongest illustration of an idea.","zh":"這個短語引入某想法的最強例證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the Indian plate","meaning":"印度板塊","examples":[{"en":"The Indian plate is moving into Central Asia.","zh":"印度板塊正移入中亞。"},{"en":"The Indian plate is the tectonic plate carrying India northward into Asia.","zh":"「the Indian plate」是承載印度向北移向亞洲的構造板塊。"},{"en":"Students learn about the Indian plate when studying the formation of the Himalayas.","zh":"學生研究喜馬拉雅山形成時會學習印度板塊。"},{"en":"As the Indian plate pushes into Asia, land is forced upward into mountains.","zh":"當印度板塊擠入亞洲，陸地被迫向上形成山脈。"},{"en":"The phrase names the moving plate behind the Himalayan collision.","zh":"這個短語指出喜馬拉雅碰撞背後的移動板塊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"steadily and implacably migrating","meaning":"穩定而不可阻擋地遷移","examples":[{"en":"The Indian plate is steadily and implacably migrating into Central Asia.","zh":"印度板塊正穩定而不可阻擋地遷移進入中亞。"},{"en":"Steadily and implacably migrating means moving continuously and unstoppably toward a place.","zh":"「steadily and implacably migrating」意思是持續而無法阻止地移向某地。"},{"en":"A city may steadily expand into nearby villages as its population grows.","zh":"隨着人口增長，城市可能穩定地擴展到附近村莊。"},{"en":"If a plate moves implacably, the pressure it creates cannot simply be avoided.","zh":"如果板塊不可阻擋地移動，它造成的壓力不能簡單避免。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow movement with unstoppable force.","zh":"這個短語描述帶有不可阻擋力量的緩慢移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"straight into","meaning":"直接進入；直衝向","examples":[{"en":"The Indian plate is moving straight into Central Asia.","zh":"印度板塊正直衝向中亞。"},{"en":"Straight into means directly toward and into something.","zh":"「straight into」意思是直接朝向並進入某物。"},{"en":"A student who is late may walk straight into the classroom without stopping outside.","zh":"遲到的學生可能沒有在外面停下，而是直接走進課室。"},{"en":"If one plate moves straight into another landmass, collision becomes unavoidable.","zh":"如果一個板塊直接移向另一片陸塊，碰撞就不可避免。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises direct movement.","zh":"這個短語強調直接移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Central Asia","meaning":"中亞","examples":[{"en":"The Indian plate is colliding with Central Asia.","zh":"印度板塊正與中亞碰撞。"},{"en":"Central Asia is the inland region of Asia north of India and west of China.","zh":"「Central Asia」是位於印度以北、中國以西的亞洲內陸地區。"},{"en":"Geography students may locate Central Asia before studying the Himalayan collision zone.","zh":"地理學生研究喜馬拉雅碰撞帶前，可能先定位中亞。"},{"en":"If the Indian plate pushes into Central Asia, mountain ranges can rise along the collision zone.","zh":"如果印度板塊擠入中亞，山脈可以沿碰撞帶上升。"},{"en":"The phrase names a region central to this geological process.","zh":"這個短語指出此地質過程中的核心地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the Himalayas","meaning":"喜馬拉雅山脈","examples":[{"en":"The Himalayas formed as a result of continental collision.","zh":"喜馬拉雅山脈因大陸碰撞而形成。"},{"en":"The Himalayas are a vast mountain range in Asia containing the world’s highest peaks.","zh":"「the Himalayas」是亞洲一條龐大山脈，包含世界最高山峰。"},{"en":"Students often study the Himalayas to understand how plate collisions build mountains.","zh":"學生常研究喜馬拉雅山脈，以理解板塊碰撞如何造山。"},{"en":"Because the Indian plate is still pushing north, the Himalayas are still changing.","zh":"因為印度板塊仍向北擠壓，喜馬拉雅山脈仍在改變。"},{"en":"The phrase names one of the clearest results of continental collision.","zh":"這個短語指出大陸碰撞最清楚的結果之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Nepal and northern India","meaning":"尼泊爾和印度北部","examples":[{"en":"The Himalayas stretch across Nepal and northern India.","zh":"喜馬拉雅山脈橫跨尼泊爾和印度北部。"},{"en":"Nepal and northern India are regions along the southern side of the Himalayas.","zh":"「Nepal and northern India」是位於喜馬拉雅山脈南側的地區。"},{"en":"Climbers often travel through Nepal and northern India to reach Himalayan areas.","zh":"登山者常經尼泊爾和印度北部前往喜馬拉雅地區。"},{"en":"If mountains rise in this region, rivers and settlements below are affected.","zh":"如果這個地區山脈上升，下方河流和聚落會受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies places connected with the Himalayan range.","zh":"這個短語指出與喜馬拉雅山脈相關的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the Karakoram Ranges","meaning":"喀喇崑崙山脈","examples":[{"en":"The Karakoram Ranges are part of the collision zone.","zh":"喀喇崑崙山脈是碰撞帶的一部分。"},{"en":"The Karakoram Ranges are high mountain ranges northwest of the Himalayas.","zh":"「the Karakoram Ranges」是位於喜馬拉雅山西北方的高山山脈。"},{"en":"Geography students may study the Karakoram Ranges alongside the Himalayas.","zh":"地理學生可能把喀喇崑崙山脈與喜馬拉雅山一起研究。"},{"en":"If the collision zone continues to rise, nearby ranges may remain geologically active.","zh":"如果碰撞帶持續上升，附近山脈可能仍具地質活躍性。"},{"en":"The phrase names another major mountain system linked to continental collision.","zh":"這個短語指出另一個與大陸碰撞有關的主要山脈系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"northern Pakistan","meaning":"巴基斯坦北部","examples":[{"en":"The Karakoram Ranges lie in northern Pakistan.","zh":"喀喇崑崙山脈位於巴基斯坦北部。"},{"en":"Northern Pakistan is the northern part of Pakistan, close to major Asian mountain ranges.","zh":"「northern Pakistan」是巴基斯坦北部，靠近亞洲主要山脈。"},{"en":"Travellers may visit northern Pakistan for mountain scenery and high passes.","zh":"旅客可能前往巴基斯坦北部欣賞山景和高山隘口。"},{"en":"If a mountain range lies in northern Pakistan, it is part of a complex highland region.","zh":"如果山脈位於巴基斯坦北部，它就是複雜高地地區的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the geographical location of the Karakoram Ranges.","zh":"這個短語指出喀喇崑崙山脈的地理位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the highlands of Afghanistan","meaning":"阿富汗高地","examples":[{"en":"The highlands of Afghanistan are part of the complex fold system.","zh":"阿富汗高地是複雜褶皺系統的一部分。"},{"en":"The highlands of Afghanistan are elevated mountainous areas within Afghanistan.","zh":"「the highlands of Afghanistan」是阿富汗境內較高的山區。"},{"en":"A map of Central Asia may show the highlands of Afghanistan near other major ranges.","zh":"中亞地圖可能顯示阿富汗高地靠近其他主要山脈。"},{"en":"If a collision affects a broad region, highlands far from the main peaks may also form.","zh":"如果碰撞影響廣大地區，遠離主要高峰的高地也可能形成。"},{"en":"The phrase names mountainous terrain linked to the collision zone.","zh":"這個短語指出與碰撞帶有關的山地地形。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be part of","meaning":"是……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"These mountain ranges are part of a complex fold system.","zh":"這些山脈是複雜褶皺系統的一部分。"},{"en":"To be part of something means to belong to a larger whole.","zh":"「be part of」某物，意思是屬於一個較大整體。"},{"en":"A school library is part of the learning support system.","zh":"學校圖書館是學習支援系統的一部分。"},{"en":"If one range is part of a larger fold system, it should not be studied alone.","zh":"如果一條山脈是較大褶皺系統的一部分，就不應孤立研究它。"},{"en":"The phrase connects one item to a bigger structure.","zh":"這個短語把一個項目連接到更大結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complex fold system","meaning":"複雜褶皺系統","examples":[{"en":"The collision produced a complex fold system.","zh":"碰撞產生了一個複雜褶皺系統。"},{"en":"A complex fold system is a large arrangement of folded rock layers created by pressure.","zh":"「complex fold system」是由壓力造成的大型褶皺岩層排列。"},{"en":"Students may fold layers of paper to model a simple fold system.","zh":"學生可能摺疊幾層紙來模擬簡單褶皺系統。"},{"en":"If plates push together for millions of years, rocks can fold into complicated mountain structures.","zh":"如果板塊數百萬年互相擠壓，岩石可以褶皺成複雜山脈結構。"},{"en":"The phrase describes folded geological structures on a large scale.","zh":"這個短語描述大尺度的褶皺地質結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"result from","meaning":"由……造成","examples":[{"en":"The fold system resulted from the collision of the Indian plate.","zh":"該褶皺系統由印度板塊碰撞造成。"},{"en":"To result from something means to be caused by it.","zh":"「result from」某事，意思是由它造成。"},{"en":"Poor exam performance may result from lack of sleep rather than lack of intelligence.","zh":"考試表現差可能由睡眠不足造成，而不是智力不足。"},{"en":"If mountains result from plate collision, their shape reflects deep pressure.","zh":"如果山脈由板塊碰撞造成，其形態反映深層壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase links an effect back to its cause.","zh":"這個短語把結果連回原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the highest peaks in the world","meaning":"世界最高山峰之一","examples":[{"en":"The collision produced some of the highest peaks in the world.","zh":"這次碰撞形成了一些世界最高山峰。"},{"en":"The highest peaks in the world are the tallest mountain summits on Earth.","zh":"「the highest peaks in the world」是地球上最高的山峰頂部。"},{"en":"Mount Everest is one of the highest peaks in the world.","zh":"珠穆朗瑪峰是世界最高山峰之一。"},{"en":"If continental collision continues, very high peaks can rise over geological time.","zh":"如果大陸碰撞持續，非常高的山峰可以在地質時間中上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mountains of extreme height.","zh":"這個短語描述極高山峰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"deep valleys","meaning":"深谷","examples":[{"en":"The collision zone also contains deep valleys.","zh":"碰撞帶也包含深谷。"},{"en":"Deep valleys are low areas between mountains or hills with steep sides.","zh":"「deep valleys」是山或丘陵之間兩側陡峭的低地。"},{"en":"A river may flow through a deep valley between two mountain ranges.","zh":"河流可能流經兩條山脈之間的深谷。"},{"en":"If mountains rise high, erosion and rivers can cut deep valleys between them.","zh":"如果山脈升得很高，侵蝕和河流可以在其間切出深谷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes low, narrow landforms within mountainous areas.","zh":"這個短語描述山區內低而狹長的地貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"receive meltwater runoff","meaning":"接收融雪徑流","examples":[{"en":"Deep valleys receive meltwater runoff from the mountains.","zh":"深谷接收來自山脈的融雪徑流。"},{"en":"To receive meltwater runoff means to collect water flowing down from melting snow or ice.","zh":"「receive meltwater runoff」意思是接收由融雪或融冰流下來的水。"},{"en":"A valley village may receive meltwater runoff during spring as snow melts.","zh":"春季積雪融化時，山谷村莊可能接收融雪徑流。"},{"en":"If mountains hold much snow, their runoff can feed rivers below.","zh":"如果山脈有大量積雪，其徑流可以補給下方河流。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how valleys get water from melting ice or snow.","zh":"這個短語描述山谷如何從融冰或融雪取得水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"meltwater runoff","meaning":"融雪徑流","examples":[{"en":"Meltwater runoff helps feed major rivers.","zh":"融雪徑流有助補給主要河流。"},{"en":"Meltwater runoff is water that flows away after snow or ice melts.","zh":"「meltwater runoff」是冰雪融化後流走的水。"},{"en":"In spring, meltwater runoff can fill streams and reservoirs.","zh":"在春季，融雪徑流可以填滿溪流和水塘。"},{"en":"If glaciers shrink, the amount of meltwater runoff may change over time.","zh":"如果冰川縮小，融雪徑流的水量可能隨時間改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes flowing water from melted snow or ice.","zh":"這個短語描述來自融冰或融雪的流動水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the far side of","meaning":"……的另一邊","examples":[{"en":"Water flows from the far side of these mountains.","zh":"水從這些山脈的另一邊流出。"},{"en":"The far side of something means the side that is farther away from the speaker or reference point.","zh":"「the far side of」某物，意思是離說話者或參考點較遠的一邊。"},{"en":"The school gate is on the far side of the playground.","zh":"校門在操場的另一邊。"},{"en":"If rivers begin on the far side of mountains, they may flow into different regions.","zh":"如果河流始於山脈另一邊，它們可能流入不同地區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a side across or beyond something.","zh":"這個短語描述跨過或超越某物的一側。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"mighty rivers","meaning":"大河；壯闊河流","examples":[{"en":"The mountains feed mighty rivers such as the Indus and the Mekong.","zh":"這些山脈補給印度河和湄公河等大河。"},{"en":"Mighty rivers are very large and powerful rivers.","zh":"「mighty rivers」是非常巨大而有力量的河流。"},{"en":"The Amazon and the Nile are often described as mighty rivers.","zh":"亞馬遜河和尼羅河常被描述為壯闊河流。"},{"en":"If mountains supply meltwater, mighty rivers can support farms, cities, and transport.","zh":"如果山脈提供融雪水，大河可以支持農田、城市和交通。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rivers with great size and importance.","zh":"這個短語描述規模和重要性都很大的河流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the Indus","meaning":"印度河","examples":[{"en":"The Indus receives water from the mountains.","zh":"印度河接收來自山脈的水。"},{"en":"The Indus is a major river flowing through parts of Asia, especially Pakistan.","zh":"「the Indus」是流經亞洲部分地區，尤其巴基斯坦的重要河流。"},{"en":"Geography students may study the Indus when learning about mountain-fed river systems.","zh":"地理學生學習由山脈補給的河流系統時，可能研究印度河。"},{"en":"If Himalayan meltwater changes, rivers like the Indus may also be affected.","zh":"如果喜馬拉雅融雪水改變，印度河等河流也可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase names an important river linked to mountain runoff.","zh":"這個短語指出與山脈徑流有關的重要河流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the Irrawaddy","meaning":"伊洛瓦底江","examples":[{"en":"The Irrawaddy is one of the rivers mentioned in the passage.","zh":"伊洛瓦底江是文章提及的河流之一。"},{"en":"The Irrawaddy is a major river in Myanmar.","zh":"「the Irrawaddy」是緬甸的一條主要河流。"},{"en":"A geography class may study the Irrawaddy when learning about Southeast Asian river systems.","zh":"地理課學習東南亞河流系統時，可能研究伊洛瓦底江。"},{"en":"If mountain runoff feeds a river, communities downstream may depend on it.","zh":"如果山脈徑流補給河流，下游社區可能依靠它。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major Asian river.","zh":"這個短語指出一條亞洲主要河流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the Mekong","meaning":"湄公河","examples":[{"en":"The Mekong receives runoff from mountainous regions.","zh":"湄公河接收來自山區的徑流。"},{"en":"The Mekong is a major river flowing through parts of Southeast Asia.","zh":"「the Mekong」是流經東南亞部分地區的一條主要河流。"},{"en":"Farmers and fishing communities depend on the Mekong for water and food.","zh":"農民和漁業社區依靠湄公河取得水和食物。"},{"en":"If mountain water changes, the Mekong’s flow may affect millions of people downstream.","zh":"如果山水改變，湄公河流量可能影響下游數百萬人。"},{"en":"The phrase names an important river system in Asia.","zh":"這個短語指出亞洲一條重要河流系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"still growing","meaning":"仍在上升；仍在增長","examples":[{"en":"The Himalayas are still growing.","zh":"喜馬拉雅山脈仍在上升。"},{"en":"Still growing means continuing to increase in size, height, or development.","zh":"「still growing」意思是大小、高度或發展仍在增加。"},{"en":"A young child is still growing, so shoes may become too small quickly.","zh":"年幼孩子仍在長大，所以鞋子可能很快不合穿。"},{"en":"If a mountain range is still growing, tectonic forces are still active there.","zh":"如果山脈仍在增長，當地構造力量仍然活躍。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an ongoing process, not a finished one.","zh":"這個短語描述仍在進行、尚未完成的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the summit of Mount Everest","meaning":"珠穆朗瑪峰峰頂","examples":[{"en":"The summit of Mount Everest may be higher than it was in 1953.","zh":"珠穆朗瑪峰峰頂可能比1953年時更高。"},{"en":"The summit of Mount Everest is the very top of the world’s highest mountain.","zh":"「the summit of Mount Everest」是世界最高山的最頂端。"},{"en":"Climbers aim to reach the summit of Mount Everest after weeks of preparation.","zh":"登山者經過數星期準備後，目標是到達珠穆朗瑪峰峰頂。"},{"en":"If the mountain is still rising, its summit may slowly become higher.","zh":"如果山脈仍在上升，其峰頂可能慢慢變高。"},{"en":"The phrase names the highest point of Everest.","zh":"這個短語指出珠峰的最高點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a couple of metres higher","meaning":"高幾米左右","examples":[{"en":"Mount Everest may now be a couple of metres higher.","zh":"珠穆朗瑪峰現在可能高幾米左右。"},{"en":"A couple of metres higher means about two metres higher.","zh":"「a couple of metres higher」意思是高約兩米。"},{"en":"A new school fence may be a couple of metres higher than the old one.","zh":"新學校圍欄可能比舊圍欄高幾米左右。"},{"en":"If a mountain rises only a little each year, the change may still add up over time.","zh":"如果山每年只上升一點，變化仍可能隨時間累積。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate small increase in height.","zh":"這個短語提供大約的小幅高度增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"when people first stood there","meaning":"當人們首次站在那裏時","examples":[{"en":"Everest may be higher now than when people first stood there.","zh":"珠峰現在可能比人們首次站在那裏時更高。"},{"en":"When people first stood there means at the time humans first reached that exact place.","zh":"「when people first stood there」意思是在人類首次到達該確切地點時。"},{"en":"A classroom may look different now from when students first studied there years ago.","zh":"課室現在看起來可能與學生多年前首次在那裡上課時不同。"},{"en":"If a summit changes after the first climb, measurements from different years may differ.","zh":"如果山頂在首次登頂後改變，不同年份的量度可能不同。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the present with the first human arrival.","zh":"這個短語把現在與人類首次到達作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"presumably","meaning":"推測；大概","examples":[{"en":"Presumably, the mountain is now slightly harder to climb.","zh":"推測這座山現在稍微更難攀登。"},{"en":"Presumably means something is probably true based on what we know.","zh":"「presumably」意思是根據已知資料，某事大概是真的。"},{"en":"If the lights are off, presumably the office is closed.","zh":"如果燈關了，辦公室大概已關門。"},{"en":"If Everest is higher, it is presumably a little harder to reach the top.","zh":"如果珠峰更高，它大概稍微更難登頂。"},{"en":"The word signals a reasonable assumption, not absolute proof.","zh":"這個詞表示合理假設，而不是絕對證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"just that little bit harder","meaning":"就是稍微更難一點","examples":[{"en":"The increase in height makes Everest just that little bit harder to reach.","zh":"高度增加令珠峰就是稍微更難到達。"},{"en":"Just that little bit harder means slightly more difficult than before.","zh":"「just that little bit harder」意思是比以前稍微困難一點。"},{"en":"A longer bus route makes arriving on time just that little bit harder.","zh":"較長巴士路線令準時到達稍微更難一點。"},{"en":"If a mountain grows even slightly, reaching the summit becomes a little more demanding.","zh":"如果山即使只上升少許，到達峰頂也會更吃力一點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small increase in difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述難度小幅增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"harder to reach","meaning":"更難到達","examples":[{"en":"Mount Everest may now be harder to reach.","zh":"珠穆朗瑪峰現在可能更難到達。"},{"en":"Harder to reach means more difficult to get to or arrive at.","zh":"「harder to reach」意思是更難去到或抵達。"},{"en":"A school may be harder to reach if the nearest bus stop closes.","zh":"如果最近的巴士站關閉，學校可能更難到達。"},{"en":"If a summit becomes higher, climbers need more effort to reach it.","zh":"如果山頂變得更高，登山者需要更多努力才能到達。"},{"en":"The phrase describes increased difficulty in access.","zh":"這個短語描述抵達難度增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the sentences","meaning":"完成句子","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the sentences with words from the passage.","zh":"學生用文章中的詞語完成句子。"},{"en":"To complete the sentences means to fill in missing words so the sentences make sense.","zh":"「complete the sentences」意思是填入缺失詞語，使句子意思完整。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete the sentences by copying exact words from the text.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過抄寫文本原字完成句子。"},{"en":"If the wrong word is chosen, the grammar or meaning may not fit.","zh":"如果選錯詞，文法或意思可能不吻合。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose one word from","meaning":"從……中選一個字","examples":[{"en":"Students choose one word from the passage for each answer.","zh":"學生為每個答案從文章中選一個字。"},{"en":"Choose one word from means select a single word from a given text or source.","zh":"「choose one word from」意思是從指定文本或來源選出單一詞語。"},{"en":"In a vocabulary task, students may choose one word from a box to complete a sentence.","zh":"在詞彙任務中，學生可能從方框中選一個字完成句子。"},{"en":"If the instruction says one word, adding extra words may make the answer wrong.","zh":"如果指示說一個字，加入額外詞語可能令答案錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict source and length rule.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格來源和長度規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the combination of","meaning":"……的組合","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the combination of North America and Eurasia.","zh":"題目問北美洲和歐亞大陸的組合。"},{"en":"The combination of things means the joining or grouping of them together.","zh":"「the combination of」幾件事，意思是它們連結或組合在一起。"},{"en":"The combination of sleep, practice, and feedback helps students improve.","zh":"睡眠、練習和回饋的組合幫助學生進步。"},{"en":"If two landmasses are combined in an ancient continent, their later separation matters.","zh":"如果兩個陸塊在古大陸中合併，其後來分離就很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes things put together as one group.","zh":"這個短語描述幾件事被放在一起成為一組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"North America and Eurasia","meaning":"北美洲和歐亞大陸","examples":[{"en":"North America and Eurasia were linked to Laurasia.","zh":"北美洲和歐亞大陸與勞亞古陸有關。"},{"en":"North America and Eurasia are major northern landmasses in the modern world.","zh":"「North America and Eurasia」是現代世界中的主要北方陸塊。"},{"en":"On a world map, students can locate North America west of the Atlantic and Eurasia to the east.","zh":"在世界地圖上，學生可以找到大西洋以西的北美洲和以東的歐亞大陸。"},{"en":"If both were once part of Laurasia, their geological histories may be connected.","zh":"如果兩者曾是勞亞古陸一部分，其地質歷史可能相連。"},{"en":"The phrase names two landmasses important in supercontinent history.","zh":"這個短語指出超級大陸歷史中的兩個重要陸塊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生為每題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choose the correct letter means select the letter that matches the right answer option.","zh":"「choose the correct letter」意思是選出與正確答案選項相配的字母。"},{"en":"If answer B is correct, students should write B, not the whole sentence.","zh":"如果答案 B 正確，學生應寫 B，而不是整句。"},{"en":"If students choose the wrong letter, the answer will not match the option.","zh":"如果學生選錯字母，答案就不符合選項。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common multiple-choice instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見多項選擇指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"dislike someone’s idea","meaning":"不喜歡某人的想法","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists disliked Wegener’s idea because he lacked a clear force.","zh":"有些科學家不喜歡 Wegener 的想法，因為他缺乏清楚力量解釋。"},{"en":"To dislike someone’s idea means to disagree with it or feel it is weak or wrong.","zh":"「dislike someone’s idea」意思是不同意它，或覺得它薄弱或錯誤。"},{"en":"A teacher may dislike a student’s idea if it has no evidence.","zh":"如果學生想法沒有證據，老師可能不喜歡該想法。"},{"en":"If people dislike an idea, they may ask for stronger proof before accepting it.","zh":"如果人們不喜歡某想法，可能要求更強證據才接受。"},{"en":"The phrase describes negative reaction to a proposal.","zh":"這個短語描述對提議的負面反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"make simple observations","meaning":"作出簡單觀察","examples":[{"en":"Scientists should not dismiss ideas simply because they begin with simple observations.","zh":"科學家不應只因想法始於簡單觀察便否定它們。"},{"en":"To make simple observations means to notice basic facts by looking carefully.","zh":"「make simple observations」意思是透過仔細觀看注意到基本事實。"},{"en":"A child may make simple observations about which plants grow better in sunlight.","zh":"孩子可能作出簡單觀察，看看哪些植物在陽光下長得更好。"},{"en":"If simple observations are followed by careful testing, they can lead to strong science.","zh":"如果簡單觀察之後有仔細測試，它們可以通向強有力的科學。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the first step of noticing patterns.","zh":"這個短語描述注意到模式的第一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"make too many suggestions","meaning":"提出太多建議","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that Wegener made too many suggestions.","zh":"該選項暗示 Wegener 提出太多建議。"},{"en":"To make too many suggestions means to offer more ideas than are useful or manageable.","zh":"「make too many suggestions」意思是提出比有用或可處理數量更多的想法。"},{"en":"In a group project, one student may make too many suggestions before the team chooses a direction.","zh":"在小組專題中，一名學生可能在團隊選方向前提出太多建議。"},{"en":"If too many suggestions are given, the main argument can become unclear.","zh":"如果建議太多，主要論點可能變得不清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes excessive proposing of ideas.","zh":"這個短語描述過度提出想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"die prematurely","meaning":"早逝","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether both scientists died prematurely.","zh":"題目問兩位科學家是否都早逝。"},{"en":"To die prematurely means to die earlier than expected or before old age.","zh":"「die prematurely」意思是比預期更早或未到老年便去世。"},{"en":"A writer who dies prematurely may leave several books unfinished.","zh":"早逝的作家可能留下幾本未完成的書。"},{"en":"If a scientist dies prematurely, they may never see their theory accepted.","zh":"如果科學家早逝，他們可能永遠看不到自己的理論被接受。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an early death.","zh":"這個短語描述早期死亡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"lack crucial evidence","meaning":"缺乏關鍵證據","examples":[{"en":"Both Wegener and Semmelweis lacked crucial evidence at first.","zh":"Wegener 和 Semmelweis 一開始都缺乏關鍵證據。"},{"en":"To lack crucial evidence means to not have the most important proof needed.","zh":"「lack crucial evidence」意思是沒有最重要、最需要的證明。"},{"en":"A student’s argument may lack crucial evidence if it gives opinions without examples.","zh":"如果學生論點只有意見沒有例子，就可能缺乏關鍵證據。"},{"en":"If a theory lacks crucial evidence, people may reject it even if it is later proven right.","zh":"如果理論缺乏關鍵證據，即使後來被證明正確，人們起初也可能拒絕它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes missing key support.","zh":"這個短語描述缺少核心支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be given recognition","meaning":"獲得認可","examples":[{"en":"Important scientists are not always given recognition during their lifetimes.","zh":"重要科學家不一定在有生之年獲得認可。"},{"en":"To be given recognition means to receive respect, credit, or public acknowledgement.","zh":"「be given recognition」意思是得到尊重、功勞或公開肯定。"},{"en":"A quiet student may finally be given recognition after doing excellent group work.","zh":"安靜學生在小組工作中表現出色後，可能終於獲得認可。"},{"en":"If someone’s contribution is recognised late, their earlier struggle may seem unfair.","zh":"如果某人的貢獻很晚才被承認，其早期掙扎可能顯得不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase describes receiving deserved acknowledgement.","zh":"這個短語描述獲得應得肯定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the motion of tectonic plates","meaning":"構造板塊的運動","examples":[{"en":"The motion of tectonic plates is slow but powerful.","zh":"構造板塊的運動緩慢但強大。"},{"en":"The motion of tectonic plates means the movement of Earth’s large outer plates.","zh":"「the motion of tectonic plates」意思是地球大型外層板塊的移動。"},{"en":"Students may use arrows on a map to show the motion of tectonic plates.","zh":"學生可能在地圖上用箭咀表示構造板塊的運動。"},{"en":"If plate motion continues for millions of years, continents and mountains can change shape.","zh":"如果板塊運動持續數百萬年，大陸和山脈可以改變形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how tectonic plates move over time.","zh":"這個短語描述構造板塊隨時間如何移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be well understood","meaning":"被充分理解","examples":[{"en":"The movement of molten rock is not fully well understood.","zh":"熔融岩石的運動尚未被完全充分理解。"},{"en":"To be well understood means to be clearly and thoroughly known or explained.","zh":"「be well understood」意思是被清楚而全面地認識或解釋。"},{"en":"A grammar rule is well understood when students can explain and use it correctly.","zh":"當學生能正確解釋和使用文法規則時，該規則就是被充分理解。"},{"en":"If a process is not well understood, scientists may disagree about its details.","zh":"如果過程未被充分理解，科學家可能對細節有分歧。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a high level of understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述高程度理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"start cyclic swirls","meaning":"引發循環旋流","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether plate motion can start cyclic swirls.","zh":"題目問板塊運動是否可以引發循環旋流。"},{"en":"To start cyclic swirls means to begin repeated circular movements in a material.","zh":"「start cyclic swirls」意思是在某材料中開始反覆圓形流動。"},{"en":"Stirring a cup of tea can start cyclic swirls in the liquid.","zh":"攪拌一杯茶可以在液體中引發循環旋流。"},{"en":"If heat and rotation affect molten material, swirling motion may develop.","zh":"如果熱力和旋轉影響熔融物質，旋流可能形成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes causing repeated circular flow.","zh":"這個短語描述造成反覆圓形流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be formed away from","meaning":"在遠離……的地方形成","examples":[{"en":"Volcanoes can be formed away from plate boundaries.","zh":"火山可以在遠離板塊邊界的地方形成。"},{"en":"To be formed away from something means to be created at a distance from it.","zh":"「be formed away from」某物，意思是在距離它較遠的位置被形成。"},{"en":"New shops may be formed away from the town centre when rent becomes too high.","zh":"當租金太高，新商店可能在遠離市中心的地方形成。"},{"en":"If volcanoes form away from boundaries, hotspots may explain them.","zh":"如果火山在遠離邊界處形成，熱點可能解釋它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formation outside the expected location.","zh":"這個短語描述在預期位置以外形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"due to","meaning":"由於","examples":[{"en":"Some volcanoes form away from boundaries due to hotspots.","zh":"有些火山由於熱點而在遠離邊界處形成。"},{"en":"Due to means because of.","zh":"「due to」意思是由於、因為。"},{"en":"The school picnic was cancelled due to heavy rain.","zh":"學校旅行由於大雨而取消。"},{"en":"If volcanic activity happens due to hotspots, the cause is below the plate rather than at its edge.","zh":"如果火山活動由熱點造成，其原因在板塊下方，而不是邊緣。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a cause or reason.","zh":"這個短語引入原因或理由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"heated regions","meaning":"受熱區域","examples":[{"en":"Heated regions beneath plates can produce volcanic activity.","zh":"板塊下方的受熱區域可以產生火山活動。"},{"en":"Heated regions are areas made hot by energy from below or around them.","zh":"「heated regions」是由下方或周圍能量加熱的區域。"},{"en":"A heated region on a pan may cook food faster than cooler parts.","zh":"平底鍋上的受熱區域可能比較冷部分更快煮熟食物。"},{"en":"If heated regions exist under a plate, rock may melt and rise.","zh":"如果板塊下有受熱區域，岩石可能熔化並上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes areas affected by high temperature.","zh":"這個短語描述受高溫影響的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete the diagram","meaning":"完成圖表","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the diagram using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的詞語完成圖表。"},{"en":"To complete the diagram means to fill missing labels or information in a picture or chart.","zh":"「complete the diagram」意思是在圖片或圖表中填入缺失標籤或資料。"},{"en":"In science class, students complete the diagram of the eye with labels such as retina and lens.","zh":"在科學課中，學生用 retina 和 lens 等標籤完成人眼圖表。"},{"en":"If students understand the process, they can label the diagram accurately.","zh":"如果學生理解過程，就能準確標示圖表。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common visual-question instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見圖像題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不超過兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Students choose no more than two words for each answer.","zh":"學生為每個答案選擇不超過兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must contain two words or fewer.","zh":"「no more than two words」意思是答案必須包含兩個詞或更少。"},{"en":"If the answer is “tectonic plates”, it fits because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “tectonic plates”，它符合要求，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"If students write three words, the answer may break the instruction.","zh":"如果學生寫三個詞，答案可能違反指示。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"tectonic forces at work","meaning":"構造力量的運作","examples":[{"en":"The diagram shows tectonic forces at work.","zh":"圖表顯示構造力量的運作。"},{"en":"Tectonic forces at work means Earth’s plate forces are actively operating and causing change.","zh":"「tectonic forces at work」意思是地球板塊力量正在運作並造成變化。"},{"en":"A model with pushing blocks can show tectonic forces at work in a classroom.","zh":"用推動積木的模型可以在課室展示構造力量的運作。"},{"en":"When these forces act over time, rocks may fold, break, or rise.","zh":"當這些力量長時間作用，岩石可能褶皺、斷裂或上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes geological forces in action.","zh":"這個短語描述正在發揮作用的地質力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete the table","meaning":"完成表格","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the table with information from the passage.","zh":"學生用文章中的資料完成表格。"},{"en":"To complete the table means to fill missing cells with correct information.","zh":"「complete the table」意思是用正確資料填入缺失格子。"},{"en":"Students may complete a table by matching each boundary type with its example.","zh":"學生可能透過把每種邊界類型與其例子配對來完成表格。"},{"en":"If one box is filled with the wrong detail, the comparison becomes confusing.","zh":"如果某格填入錯誤細節，比較就會變得混亂。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-task instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀任務指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不超過三個字","examples":[{"en":"Students choose no more than three words from the passage.","zh":"學生從文章中選擇不超過三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"「no more than three words」意思是答案必須包含三個詞或更少。"},{"en":"If the answer is “deep marine trenches”, it fits because it has three words.","zh":"如果答案是 “deep marine trenches”，它符合要求，因為有三個詞。"},{"en":"If students add unnecessary words, they may lose marks despite understanding the idea.","zh":"如果學生加入不必要詞語，即使理解意思，也可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict answer-length rule.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格答案長度規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"type of boundary","meaning":"邊界類型","examples":[{"en":"The table asks for the type of boundary.","zh":"表格要求填寫邊界類型。"},{"en":"Type of boundary means the category of edge where plates meet, separate, or slide.","zh":"「type of boundary」意思是板塊相遇、分離或滑過位置的類別。"},{"en":"In a geography worksheet, students may identify each type of boundary from a diagram.","zh":"在地理工作紙中，學生可能從圖中辨認每種邊界類型。"},{"en":"If the movement direction is known, the boundary type is easier to name.","zh":"如果已知移動方向，邊界類型就較容易命名。"},{"en":"The phrase asks students to classify a boundary.","zh":"這個短語要求學生分類邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"related example","meaning":"相關例子","examples":[{"en":"The table gives a related example for each boundary type.","zh":"表格為每種邊界類型提供相關例子。"},{"en":"A related example is an example connected to the category or idea being discussed.","zh":"「related example」是與正在討論的類別或想法有關的例子。"},{"en":"If the topic is divergent boundaries, a related example may be a mid-oceanic ridge.","zh":"如果題目是張裂型邊界，相關例子可能是大洋中脊。"},{"en":"Examples help students connect abstract categories with real places.","zh":"例子幫助學生把抽象類別與真實地方連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an example that supports a specific point.","zh":"這個短語描述支持特定重點的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"resulting in","meaning":"導致；結果是","examples":[{"en":"The collision created Central Asian ranges, resulting in tall mountains and deep valleys.","zh":"這次碰撞造成中亞山脈，導致高山和深谷形成。"},{"en":"Resulting in means causing something to happen as a consequence.","zh":"「resulting in」意思是作為後果造成某事發生。"},{"en":"Heavy rain blocked the road, resulting in long delays for commuters.","zh":"大雨阻塞道路，導致通勤者長時間延誤。"},{"en":"If continental plates collide, pressure may build, resulting in folded mountains.","zh":"如果大陸板塊碰撞，壓力可能累積，結果形成褶皺山脈。"},{"en":"The phrase links an action or process to its outcome.","zh":"這個短語把行動或過程連到結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"tall mountains","meaning":"高山","examples":[{"en":"Continental collision can produce tall mountains.","zh":"大陸碰撞可以形成高山。"},{"en":"Tall mountains are mountains with great height above the surrounding land.","zh":"「tall mountains」是比周圍土地高很多的山。"},{"en":"Climbers need training before attempting tall mountains because oxygen and weather can be dangerous.","zh":"登山者嘗試攀登高山前需要訓練，因為氧氣和天氣可能危險。"},{"en":"If plates push land upward for millions of years, tall mountains may form.","zh":"如果板塊數百萬年把陸地向上推，高山可能形成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes high landforms created by geological forces.","zh":"這個短語描述由地質力量形成的高大地貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"several mighty rivers","meaning":"幾條大河","examples":[{"en":"The collision zone produced deep valleys and several mighty rivers.","zh":"碰撞帶形成深谷和幾條大河。"},{"en":"Several mighty rivers means a number of very large and powerful rivers.","zh":"「several mighty rivers」意思是幾條非常巨大而有力量的河流。"},{"en":"A mountain range may feed several mighty rivers that support farms and cities below.","zh":"山脈可能補給幾條大河，支持下方農田和城市。"},{"en":"If snowmelt flows through deep valleys, great rivers can develop downstream.","zh":"如果融雪流經深谷，下游可以形成大河。"},{"en":"The phrase describes multiple major river systems.","zh":"這個短語描述多條主要河流系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"Central Asian ranges","meaning":"中亞山脈","examples":[{"en":"The Central Asian ranges were formed by continental collision.","zh":"中亞山脈由大陸碰撞形成。"},{"en":"Central Asian ranges are mountain ranges in or near Central Asia.","zh":"「Central Asian ranges」是位於中亞或附近的山脈。"},{"en":"Students may study Central Asian ranges when learning how the Indian plate changed Asia’s landscape.","zh":"學生學習印度板塊如何改變亞洲地貌時，可能研究中亞山脈。"},{"en":"If continental collision continues, these ranges may remain high and geologically complex.","zh":"如果大陸碰撞持續，這些山脈可能保持高大且地質複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to mountain systems produced by major tectonic forces.","zh":"這個短語指由重大構造力量形成的山脈系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 88 - Continents Collide!.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 89":[{"front":"organisational conflict and change","meaning":"組織衝突與變革","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses organisational conflict and change.","zh":"文章討論組織衝突與變革。"},{"en":"Organisational conflict and change means disagreement and adjustment inside a company, school, or institution.","zh":"組織衝突與變革，指公司、學校或機構內部的分歧和調整。"},{"en":"A school may face organisational conflict and change when it introduces a new timetable.","zh":"當學校推出新時間表，可能面對組織衝突與變革。"},{"en":"If people disagree about new rules, conflict may appear before the organisation adapts.","zh":"如果人們對新規則有分歧，組織適應前可能先出現衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase links internal disagreement with the process of transformation.","zh":"這個短語把內部分歧與轉變過程連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a natural process","meaning":"自然過程","examples":[{"en":"Change is a natural process.","zh":"變化是一個自然過程。"},{"en":"A natural process is something that happens normally as part of life or development.","zh":"自然過程，是生命或發展中正常發生的事情。"},{"en":"Children growing taller each year is a natural process.","zh":"孩子每年長高是一個自然過程。"},{"en":"If organisations grow and adapt, change becomes expected rather than strange.","zh":"如果組織會成長和適應，變化就變得可以預期，而不是奇怪。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that change should not automatically be feared.","zh":"這個短語暗示不應自動害怕變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"grow, mature and decline","meaning":"成長、成熟和衰退","examples":[{"en":"Humans grow, mature and decline over time.","zh":"人類會隨時間成長、成熟和衰退。"},{"en":"To grow, mature and decline means to develop, reach a stronger stage, and later become weaker.","zh":"成長、成熟和衰退，指發展、到達更成熟階段，然後變弱。"},{"en":"A small business may grow, mature and decline if it fails to keep up with customers.","zh":"如果小企業未能跟上顧客需要，可能會成長、成熟然後衰退。"},{"en":"If an organisation stops learning after maturity, decline may begin.","zh":"如果組織成熟後停止學習，衰退可能開始。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a full life cycle.","zh":"這個短語描述完整生命週期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"eventually die","meaning":"最終死亡；最終消亡","examples":[{"en":"Organisations, like humans, may eventually die.","zh":"組織像人類一樣，可能最終消亡。"},{"en":"To eventually die means to stop existing after a period of time.","zh":"最終死亡或消亡，指經過一段時間後停止存在。"},{"en":"A shop may eventually die if no customers visit it for years.","zh":"如果一間店多年沒有顧客，可能最終倒閉。"},{"en":"If an organisation cannot adapt to change, it may close or disappear.","zh":"如果組織不能適應變化，可能關閉或消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes final decline, not a temporary problem.","zh":"這個短語描述最終衰亡，而不是暫時問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on a bigger scale","meaning":"從更大層面來看","examples":[{"en":"On a bigger scale, modern existence is in constant change.","zh":"從更大層面來看，現代生活處於不斷變化之中。"},{"en":"On a bigger scale means when looking at a larger level or wider situation.","zh":"從更大層面來看，指從較大層次或更廣情況去看。"},{"en":"A student may worry about one test, but on a bigger scale, study habits matter more.","zh":"學生可能擔心一次測驗，但從更大層面來看，學習習慣更重要。"},{"en":"If we move from one company to society as a whole, change looks even more constant.","zh":"如果我們由一間公司轉到整個社會，變化看起來更加持續。"},{"en":"The phrase widens the discussion.","zh":"這個短語擴闊討論範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"modern existence","meaning":"現代生活；現代存在狀態","examples":[{"en":"Modern existence is similarly in a constant state of flux.","zh":"現代生活同樣處於不斷變動的狀態。"},{"en":"Modern existence means life in today’s world, including work, technology, family, and society.","zh":"現代生活指今日世界中的生活，包括工作、科技、家庭和社會。"},{"en":"Online banking, remote work, and social media are parts of modern existence.","zh":"網上銀行、遙距工作和社交媒體都是現代生活的一部分。"},{"en":"If modern existence changes quickly, people must keep learning new habits.","zh":"如果現代生活變化很快，人們就必須持續學習新習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to present-day life as a whole.","zh":"這個短語指整體當代生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be in a constant state of flux","meaning":"處於不斷變動的狀態","examples":[{"en":"Modern existence is in a constant state of flux.","zh":"現代生活處於不斷變動的狀態。"},{"en":"To be in a constant state of flux means to be changing all the time.","zh":"處於不斷變動的狀態，指一直在改變。"},{"en":"A school timetable may be in a state of flux during exam season.","zh":"考試季期間，學校時間表可能處於變動狀態。"},{"en":"If rules, technology, and customer needs keep changing, an organisation cannot stay fixed.","zh":"如果規則、科技和顧客需要不斷改變，組織就不能保持固定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continuous instability or movement.","zh":"這個短語描述持續不穩或變動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lifestyle change","meaning":"生活方式的改變","examples":[{"en":"Lifestyle change is constantly upon us.","zh":"生活方式的改變不斷出現在我們身邊。"},{"en":"Lifestyle change means a change in daily habits, routines, work, diet, or leisure.","zh":"生活方式的改變，指日常習慣、作息、工作、飲食或休閒的改變。"},{"en":"A person may experience lifestyle change after starting a new job.","zh":"一個人開始新工作後，可能經歷生活方式的改變。"},{"en":"If technology changes how people shop and communicate, lifestyle change follows.","zh":"如果科技改變人們購物和溝通方式，生活方式就會隨之改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to changes in how people live day to day.","zh":"這個短語指人們日常生活方式的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"personal change","meaning":"個人改變","examples":[{"en":"Personal change is part of modern existence.","zh":"個人改變是現代生活的一部分。"},{"en":"Personal change means change in an individual’s habits, beliefs, goals, or behaviour.","zh":"個人改變，指個人習慣、信念、目標或行為上的變化。"},{"en":"A student may go through personal change after moving to a new school.","zh":"學生轉到新學校後，可能經歷個人改變。"},{"en":"If someone gains confidence, their decisions and relationships may change too.","zh":"如果某人建立信心，其決定和人際關係也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on change inside a person’s life.","zh":"這個短語強調個人生活中的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be constantly upon us","meaning":"不斷臨近；不斷出現在身邊","examples":[{"en":"Global change and personal change are constantly upon us.","zh":"全球變化和個人改變不斷出現在我們身邊。"},{"en":"To be constantly upon us means to be always present or repeatedly happening around us.","zh":"不斷出現在身邊，指一直存在或反覆在周圍發生。"},{"en":"New phone updates are constantly upon us, so users must keep learning features.","zh":"手機更新不斷出現在我們身邊，所以用戶必須持續學習新功能。"},{"en":"If change is constantly upon us, ignoring it is not a realistic strategy.","zh":"如果變化不斷出現，忽視它就不是實際策略。"},{"en":"The phrase makes change feel close and unavoidable.","zh":"這個短語令變化顯得接近且不可避免。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the current rate of","meaning":"目前……的速度","examples":[{"en":"The current rate of technological advance is extremely fast.","zh":"目前科技進步的速度極快。"},{"en":"The current rate of something means how quickly it is happening now.","zh":"目前某事的速度，指它現在發生得有多快。"},{"en":"The current rate of price increase makes daily shopping more expensive.","zh":"目前物價上升的速度令日常購物更昂貴。"},{"en":"If the current rate of change is high, organisations must adapt faster.","zh":"如果目前變化速度很高，組織就必須更快適應。"},{"en":"The phrase measures present speed.","zh":"這個短語量度當前速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"technological advance","meaning":"科技進步","examples":[{"en":"Technological advance is making change happen faster.","zh":"科技進步正在令變化發生得更快。"},{"en":"Technological advance means progress in machines, digital tools, systems, or scientific methods.","zh":"科技進步，指機器、數碼工具、系統或科學方法上的進展。"},{"en":"Online payment is one technological advance that changed shopping habits.","zh":"網上支付是一項改變購物習慣的科技進步。"},{"en":"If technology advances quickly, old working methods may become outdated.","zh":"如果科技迅速進步，舊工作方法可能變得過時。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to improvement in technology over time.","zh":"這個短語指科技隨時間改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at a faster pace","meaning":"以更快速度","examples":[{"en":"Change is now happening at a faster pace.","zh":"變化現在正以更快速度發生。"},{"en":"At a faster pace means more quickly than before.","zh":"以更快速度，指比以前更快。"},{"en":"Students may learn at a faster pace when examples are clear and practical.","zh":"當例子清楚而實用，學生可能以更快速度學習。"},{"en":"If customers change habits quickly, companies must respond at a faster pace too.","zh":"如果顧客迅速改變習慣，公司也必須以更快速度回應。"},{"en":"The phrase compares speed across time or situations.","zh":"這個短語比較不同時間或情況下的速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"putting it simply","meaning":"簡單來說","examples":[{"en":"Putting it simply, life is change.","zh":"簡單來說，生命就是變化。"},{"en":"Putting it simply means saying an idea in a clear and uncomplicated way.","zh":"簡單來說，指用清楚而不複雜的方式表達想法。"},{"en":"Putting it simply, good writing needs clear ideas and enough evidence.","zh":"簡單來說，好寫作需要清楚想法和足夠證據。"},{"en":"If a topic is complicated, this phrase helps introduce a short summary.","zh":"如果題目複雜，這個短語有助引入簡短總結。"},{"en":"The phrase prepares readers for a simplified explanation.","zh":"這個短語讓讀者準備接受簡化解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"life is change","meaning":"生命就是變化","examples":[{"en":"The writer argues that life is change.","zh":"作者認為生命就是變化。"},{"en":"Life is change means change is an unavoidable part of being alive.","zh":"生命就是變化，指變化是活着不可避免的一部分。"},{"en":"A child becomes an adult, a student becomes a worker, and families move through different stages.","zh":"孩子成為成人，學生成為工作者，家庭經歷不同階段。"},{"en":"If life constantly changes, organisations must also expect change.","zh":"如果生命不斷變化，組織也必須預期變化。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses a broad idea about existence.","zh":"這個短語表達關於存在的廣泛想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in a manner never before experienced","meaning":"以前所未有的方式","examples":[{"en":"Change is happening in a manner never before experienced.","zh":"變化正以前所未有的方式發生。"},{"en":"In a manner never before experienced means in a way people have not faced before.","zh":"以前所未有的方式，指以人們過去未曾面對過的方式。"},{"en":"Online lessons changed education in a manner many teachers had never before experienced.","zh":"網課以前許多老師未曾經歷的方式改變教育。"},{"en":"If technology changes work completely, old experience may not be enough.","zh":"如果科技完全改變工作，舊經驗可能不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the newness of the situation.","zh":"這個短語強調情況的新穎性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be analogous to","meaning":"與……相似；可類比為……","examples":[{"en":"Organisations are analogous to organisms.","zh":"組織可類比為生物體。"},{"en":"To be analogous to something means to be similar enough to be compared with it.","zh":"與某物相似或可類比，指相似到足以作比較。"},{"en":"A school can be analogous to a small community because people share rules and responsibilities.","zh":"學校可以類比為小社區，因為人們共享規則和責任。"},{"en":"If organisations grow, adapt, and decline, they can be compared to living things.","zh":"如果組織會成長、適應和衰退，就可以與生物作比較。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a useful comparison.","zh":"這個短語引入有用比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"organisms","meaning":"生物體","examples":[{"en":"Organisations are compared to organisms.","zh":"組織被比作生物體。"},{"en":"Organisms are living things, such as humans, animals, plants, and bacteria.","zh":"生物體是有生命的東西，例如人類、動物、植物和細菌。"},{"en":"A plant is an organism because it grows, needs resources, and can die.","zh":"植物是生物體，因為它會生長、需要資源並可能死亡。"},{"en":"If an organisation behaves like an organism, it must adapt to survive.","zh":"如果組織表現得像生物體，就必須適應才能生存。"},{"en":"The word helps create a biological comparison.","zh":"這個詞有助建立生物學比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"suffer injury and crises","meaning":"遭受損害和危機","examples":[{"en":"Organisations can suffer injury and crises.","zh":"組織可能遭受損害和危機。"},{"en":"To suffer injury and crises means to experience damage, serious problems, or emergency situations.","zh":"遭受損害和危機，指經歷傷害、嚴重問題或緊急情況。"},{"en":"A company may suffer injury when a major product fails and customers lose trust.","zh":"當主要產品失敗、顧客失去信任，公司可能遭受損害。"},{"en":"If an organisation faces repeated crises, its survival may be at risk.","zh":"如果組織反覆面對危機，其生存可能受威脅。"},{"en":"The phrase treats organisational problems like harm to a living body.","zh":"這個短語把組織問題像生物受傷一樣處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"may well","meaning":"很可能","examples":[{"en":"An organisation may well die if it fails to adapt.","zh":"如果組織未能適應，很可能會消亡。"},{"en":"May well means is quite likely to happen.","zh":"很可能，指相當有可能發生。"},{"en":"A student who never practises speaking may well struggle in an oral exam.","zh":"從不練口語的學生，很可能在口試中吃力。"},{"en":"If a company ignores major market change, failure becomes quite likely.","zh":"如果公司忽視重大市場變化，失敗就相當可能。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses strong possibility.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"become bankrupt","meaning":"破產","examples":[{"en":"A company may die by becoming bankrupt.","zh":"公司可能因破產而消亡。"},{"en":"To become bankrupt means to be legally unable to pay debts.","zh":"破產，指在法律上無法償還債務。"},{"en":"A shop may become bankrupt if sales fall but rent stays high.","zh":"如果銷售下跌但租金仍高，商店可能破產。"},{"en":"If bankruptcy happens, the business may close and workers may lose jobs.","zh":"如果破產發生，企業可能關閉，員工可能失業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes financial failure.","zh":"這個短語描述財務失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the implications of","meaning":"……的含意","examples":[{"en":"The implications of the new change paradigm are serious.","zh":"新變革範式的含意很嚴重。"},{"en":"The implications of something are the possible results, meanings, or consequences it has.","zh":"某事的含意，是它可能帶來的結果、意思或後果。"},{"en":"The implications of longer school hours include tired students and less family time.","zh":"更長上課時間的含意包括學生疲倦和家庭時間減少。"},{"en":"If change is unavoidable, organisations must rethink how they are managed.","zh":"如果變化不可避免，組織就必須重新思考如何管理。"},{"en":"The phrase asks what a fact means for the future.","zh":"這個短語問某事實對未來意味着甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"change paradigm","meaning":"變革範式；變革模式","examples":[{"en":"The new change paradigm challenges old organisational systems.","zh":"新的變革範式挑戰舊有組織系統。"},{"en":"A change paradigm is a basic way of understanding how change works.","zh":"變革範式，是理解變化如何運作的基本方式。"},{"en":"A school that sees learning as lifelong has a different education paradigm from one focused only on exams.","zh":"把學習視為終身過程的學校，與只專注考試的學校有不同教育範式。"},{"en":"If the change paradigm shifts, old stable systems may no longer be enough.","zh":"如果變革範式轉變，舊有穩定系統可能不再足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a broad model for thinking about change.","zh":"這個短語指思考變革的廣泛模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stable structures","meaning":"穩定架構","examples":[{"en":"Stable structures once made organisations strong.","zh":"穩定架構曾令組織強大。"},{"en":"Stable structures are systems, rules, or arrangements that remain steady over time.","zh":"穩定架構是隨時間保持穩定的系統、規則或安排。"},{"en":"A school with clear departments and regular routines has stable structures.","zh":"有清楚部門和固定日常流程的學校，擁有穩定架構。"},{"en":"If the environment changes too quickly, stable structures may become too rigid.","zh":"如果環境變得太快，穩定架構可能變得太僵化。"},{"en":"The phrase can be positive or negative depending on context.","zh":"這個短語視乎語境可正可負。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"static systems","meaning":"靜態系統；固定不變的制度","examples":[{"en":"Static systems can now contribute to organisational decline.","zh":"靜態系統現在可能促成組織衰退。"},{"en":"Static systems are systems that stay fixed and do not adapt.","zh":"靜態系統，是保持固定而不適應的系統。"},{"en":"A company using the same customer-service process for twenty years may have a static system.","zh":"一間公司二十年使用同一套客戶服務流程，可能有靜態系統。"},{"en":"If a system cannot respond to new needs, it may become harmful.","zh":"如果系統不能回應新需要，它可能變得有害。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises lack of movement or flexibility.","zh":"這個短語批評缺乏變動或彈性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"在過去","examples":[{"en":"In the past, stable systems often made organisations strong.","zh":"在過去，穩定系統常令組織強大。"},{"en":"In the past means during an earlier time, not now.","zh":"在過去，指較早時間，而不是現在。"},{"en":"In the past, students often used paper dictionaries instead of phone apps.","zh":"在過去，學生常使用紙本字典，而不是手機應用程式。"},{"en":"If something worked in the past, it may still fail in a changed world.","zh":"如果某事在過去有效，在已改變的世界中仍可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts earlier conditions with the present.","zh":"這個短語把以往情況與現在作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"contribute to decline","meaning":"導致衰落；促成衰退","examples":[{"en":"Old structures may now contribute to organisational decline.","zh":"舊架構現在可能促成組織衰退。"},{"en":"To contribute to decline means to help cause weakening, failure, or loss of performance.","zh":"促成衰退，指幫助造成變弱、失敗或表現下降。"},{"en":"Poor communication can contribute to the decline of a school club.","zh":"溝通差可以促成學會衰落。"},{"en":"If old rules slow every decision, they may weaken the organisation.","zh":"如果舊規則拖慢每個決定，它們可能削弱組織。"},{"en":"The phrase shows one cause of deterioration.","zh":"這個短語顯示退化的一個原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"textbooks cite examples of","meaning":"教科書列舉……的例子","examples":[{"en":"Textbooks cite many examples of institutions that failed to change.","zh":"教科書列舉了許多未能變革的機構例子。"},{"en":"To cite examples of something means to mention specific cases as evidence.","zh":"列舉某事的例子，指提及具體個案作為證據。"},{"en":"A teacher may cite examples of good essays to show students what works.","zh":"老師可能列舉好作文的例子，向學生展示甚麼有效。"},{"en":"If textbooks cite failed companies, readers can learn from real cases.","zh":"如果教科書列舉失敗公司，讀者可以從真實個案學習。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces supporting evidence.","zh":"這個短語引入支持證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"monolithic institutions","meaning":"龐大而僵化的機構","examples":[{"en":"Large monolithic institutions often struggled to respond to change.","zh":"龐大而僵化的機構常難以回應變化。"},{"en":"Monolithic institutions are large organisations that are rigid, unified, and difficult to change.","zh":"龐大而僵化的機構，是大型、僵硬、統一且難以改變的組織。"},{"en":"A huge department with one fixed rule for every situation may become monolithic.","zh":"如果巨大部門對每種情況只用一條固定規則，可能變得僵化。"},{"en":"If an institution is too rigid, it may fail to adapt to local needs.","zh":"如果機構太僵硬，可能未能適應本地需要。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests size, unity, and inflexibility.","zh":"這個短語暗示規模大、統一和缺乏彈性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fail to respond to","meaning":"未能回應……","examples":[{"en":"Some organisations failed to respond to external circumstances.","zh":"一些組織未能回應外部環境。"},{"en":"To fail to respond to something means not to react or adapt when action is needed.","zh":"未能回應某事，指在需要行動時沒有反應或適應。"},{"en":"A restaurant may fail to respond to customer complaints if it keeps serving poor food.","zh":"如果餐廳繼續供應差劣食物，就是未能回應顧客投訴。"},{"en":"If an organisation ignores warning signs, problems may grow worse.","zh":"如果組織忽視警號，問題可能惡化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes missed or inadequate reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述錯失或不足的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"external circumstances","meaning":"外部環境；外在情況","examples":[{"en":"Organisations must respond to external circumstances.","zh":"組織必須回應外部環境。"},{"en":"External circumstances are outside conditions that affect an organisation, such as laws, markets, technology, or public opinion.","zh":"外部環境，是影響組織的外在條件，例如法律、市場、科技或公眾意見。"},{"en":"A school may change policy because of external circumstances like a new health rule.","zh":"學校可能因新的健康規則等外部環境而改變政策。"},{"en":"If external circumstances shift, internal systems may need adjustment.","zh":"如果外部環境轉變，內部系統可能需要調整。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to forces outside the organisation.","zh":"這個短語指組織外部的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"former government monopolies","meaning":"前政府壟斷企業","examples":[{"en":"Many examples were former government monopolies.","zh":"許多例子都是前政府壟斷企業。"},{"en":"Former government monopolies are organisations that were once state-controlled and had little or no competition.","zh":"前政府壟斷企業，是曾由政府控制且幾乎或完全沒有競爭的組織。"},{"en":"A public utility may be a former government monopoly if it used to be the only provider.","zh":"如果公共事業公司過去是唯一供應者，它可能是前政府壟斷企業。"},{"en":"If competition appears later, such organisations may struggle to adapt.","zh":"如果後來出現競爭，這類組織可能難以適應。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to old state-backed dominant organisations.","zh":"這個短語指舊有由國家支持的主導機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"break-up into smaller divisions","meaning":"拆分成較小部門","examples":[{"en":"Their break-up into smaller divisions was one attempt to solve the problem.","zh":"將它們拆分成較小部門，是解決問題的一次嘗試。"},{"en":"Break-up into smaller divisions means splitting a large organisation into smaller units.","zh":"拆分成較小部門，指把大型組織分成較小單位。"},{"en":"A school may break a large department into smaller teams to improve communication.","zh":"學校可能把大型部門拆成較小團隊，以改善溝通。"},{"en":"If one huge organisation is too slow, smaller divisions may respond faster.","zh":"如果一個巨大組織太慢，較小部門可能回應更快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes restructuring by splitting.","zh":"這個短語描述透過拆分進行重組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"one attempt to deal with","meaning":"處理……的一次嘗試","examples":[{"en":"The break-up was one attempt to deal with the issue.","zh":"拆分是處理該問題的一次嘗試。"},{"en":"One attempt to deal with something is one action tried in order to solve or manage a problem.","zh":"處理某事的一次嘗試，是為解決或管理問題而試行的一項行動。"},{"en":"Extra tutoring may be one attempt to deal with weak exam results.","zh":"額外補習可能是處理考試成績弱的一次嘗試。"},{"en":"If one attempt fails, organisations may need another strategy.","zh":"如果一次嘗試失敗，組織可能需要另一策略。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a solution is tried but not guaranteed.","zh":"這個短語顯示解決方法被嘗試，但不保證成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"respond to change","meaning":"回應變化","examples":[{"en":"Organisations must respond to change or fail to thrive.","zh":"組織必須回應變化，否則未能蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"To respond to change means to adjust actions, rules, or systems when conditions become different.","zh":"回應變化，指當情況變得不同時調整行動、規則或系統。"},{"en":"A shop may respond to change by offering online orders.","zh":"商店可能透過提供網上訂購來回應變化。"},{"en":"If a company does not respond to new customer habits, competitors may overtake it.","zh":"如果公司不回應新顧客習慣，競爭對手可能超越它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active adaptation.","zh":"這個短語描述主動適應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fail to thrive","meaning":"未能蓬勃發展","examples":[{"en":"Organisations that do not adapt may fail to thrive.","zh":"不適應的組織可能未能蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"To fail to thrive means to survive poorly or not develop successfully.","zh":"未能蓬勃發展，指生存狀況差或未能成功發展。"},{"en":"A student may fail to thrive in a class where they receive no feedback.","zh":"如果學生在沒有回饋的課堂中學習，可能未能茁壯成長。"},{"en":"If an organisation stays alive but stops improving, it may still be failing to thrive.","zh":"如果組織仍存在但停止進步，仍可能算是未能蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"The phrase means more than not dying; it means not growing well.","zh":"這個短語不只是沒有死亡，而是沒有良好成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"promote resistance among","meaning":"在……之中引發抗拒","examples":[{"en":"Change promotes resistance among people.","zh":"變化會在人們之中引發抗拒。"},{"en":"To promote resistance among people means to cause people to oppose or hesitate about something.","zh":"在人們之中引發抗拒，指令他們反對或猶豫接受某事。"},{"en":"A sudden school rule can promote resistance among students if no explanation is given.","zh":"如果學校突然推出規則而沒有解釋，可能在學生中引發抗拒。"},{"en":"If workers fear losing status, change may make them resist.","zh":"如果員工害怕失去地位，變革可能令他們抗拒。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that change can create opposition.","zh":"這個短語顯示變化可以造成反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a degree of discomfort","meaning":"某程度的不適","examples":[{"en":"Change brings a degree of discomfort.","zh":"變化帶來某程度的不適。"},{"en":"A degree of discomfort means some level of unease, difficulty, or awkwardness.","zh":"某程度的不適，指一定程度的不安、困難或尷尬。"},{"en":"Moving to a new class may bring a degree of discomfort until students know one another.","zh":"轉到新班級可能帶來某程度的不適，直到學生互相熟悉。"},{"en":"If routines are disrupted, people may feel uncertain and uneasy.","zh":"如果日常流程被打亂，人們可能感到不確定和不安。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests discomfort exists but may not be extreme.","zh":"這個短語暗示有不適，但未必極端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in turn","meaning":"繼而；反過來","examples":[{"en":"Discomfort in turn results in conflict.","zh":"不適繼而導致衝突。"},{"en":"In turn means as the next result in a chain of events.","zh":"繼而，指作為一連串事件中的下一個結果。"},{"en":"Poor sleep reduces concentration, which in turn lowers study efficiency.","zh":"睡眠差會降低專注力，繼而降低學習效率。"},{"en":"If change causes discomfort, that discomfort may then create conflict.","zh":"如果變化造成不適，那種不適可能接着產生衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase links one result to the next.","zh":"這個短語把一個結果與下一個結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"result in conflict","meaning":"導致衝突","examples":[{"en":"Change can result in conflict.","zh":"變化可以導致衝突。"},{"en":"To result in conflict means to lead to disagreement, tension, or argument.","zh":"導致衝突，指引起分歧、緊張或爭論。"},{"en":"A new seating plan may result in conflict if friends are separated without explanation.","zh":"如果新座位安排沒有解釋就拆散朋友，可能導致衝突。"},{"en":"If people feel ignored during change, arguments may follow.","zh":"如果人們在變革中感到被忽視，爭執可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a cause-and-effect relationship.","zh":"這個短語顯示因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"so too is","meaning":"……亦然","examples":[{"en":"Since change is constant, so too is conflict.","zh":"既然變化是持續的，衝突亦然。"},{"en":"So too is means the second thing is also true in the same way.","zh":"……亦然，指第二件事也以同樣方式成立。"},{"en":"If practice is necessary, so too is rest.","zh":"如果練習是必要的，休息亦然。"},{"en":"If change never disappears, conflict may also remain part of organisational life.","zh":"如果變化永不消失，衝突也可能仍是組織生活的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a parallel between two ideas.","zh":"這個短語在兩個想法之間建立平行關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"negative connotations","meaning":"負面含義","examples":[{"en":"The word “conflict” has negative connotations.","zh":"「衝突」一詞帶有負面含義。"},{"en":"Negative connotations are unpleasant associations or feelings connected with a word or idea.","zh":"負面含義，是與某詞或想法相關的不愉快聯想或感覺。"},{"en":"The word “failure” has negative connotations, even though it can lead to learning.","zh":"「失敗」一詞帶有負面含義，即使它可以帶來學習。"},{"en":"If conflict suggests anger and damage, people may avoid it too quickly.","zh":"如果衝突令人想到憤怒和破壞，人們可能太快避免它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to emotional meaning beyond dictionary definition.","zh":"這個短語指超出字典定義的情感意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"deservedly so","meaning":"這也是理所當然的","examples":[{"en":"Conflict has negative connotations, and deservedly so.","zh":"衝突帶有負面含義，這也是理所當然的。"},{"en":"Deservedly so means this judgement is fair or justified.","zh":"這也是理所當然的，指這種判斷是公平或有理由的。"},{"en":"Cheating has a bad reputation, and deservedly so, because it is unfair to others.","zh":"作弊名聲差，這也是理所當然的，因為它對其他人不公平。"},{"en":"If destructive conflict wastes resources and damages trust, its bad image is understandable.","zh":"如果破壞性衝突浪費資源並破壞信任，其負面形象是可以理解的。"},{"en":"The phrase confirms that a negative view has reason behind it.","zh":"這個短語確認負面看法背後有原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"negative forces","meaning":"負面力量","examples":[{"en":"Conflict is often the result of negative forces.","zh":"衝突往往是負面力量的結果。"},{"en":"Negative forces are harmful pressures, feelings, or actions that damage a situation.","zh":"負面力量是會破壞情況的有害壓力、情緒或行動。"},{"en":"Jealousy and poor communication can be negative forces in a team project.","zh":"嫉妒和溝通差可以成為小組項目中的負面力量。"},{"en":"If negative forces dominate, conflict becomes destructive rather than useful.","zh":"如果負面力量佔主導，衝突就變成破壞性而非有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes harmful influences.","zh":"這個短語描述有害影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"resources are diverted","meaning":"資源被轉移","examples":[{"en":"Resources are diverted when conflict becomes destructive.","zh":"當衝突變得具破壞性，資源會被轉移。"},{"en":"When resources are diverted, money, time, people, or attention are moved away from their original purpose.","zh":"資源被轉移時，金錢、時間、人手或注意力會離開原本目的。"},{"en":"A school may divert resources from teaching to handling complaints.","zh":"學校可能把資源由教學轉向處理投訴。"},{"en":"If managers spend all their time fighting internal conflict, less energy goes to customers.","zh":"如果管理層把所有時間花在內部衝突上，投放給顧客的精力就會減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes wasteful redirection of support.","zh":"這個短語描述支援被浪費性地重新分配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"judgements are distorted","meaning":"判斷被扭曲","examples":[{"en":"Judgements are distorted by unhealthy conflict.","zh":"不健康衝突會扭曲判斷。"},{"en":"If judgements are distorted, people no longer think clearly or fairly.","zh":"如果判斷被扭曲，人們就不再清楚或公平地思考。"},{"en":"A teacher’s judgement may be distorted if they are angry with one student.","zh":"如果老師對某學生生氣，其判斷可能被扭曲。"},{"en":"If conflict becomes personal, people may reject good ideas simply because they dislike the speaker.","zh":"如果衝突變成人身問題，人們可能只因不喜歡發言者而拒絕好想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes damaged decision-making.","zh":"這個短語描述受損的決策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"co-ordination is reduced","meaning":"協調被削弱","examples":[{"en":"Co-ordination is reduced when conflict is badly managed.","zh":"當衝突管理不善，協調會被削弱。"},{"en":"If co-ordination is reduced, people work together less smoothly.","zh":"如果協調被削弱，人們合作起來就較不順暢。"},{"en":"A sports team with poor communication has reduced co-ordination on the field.","zh":"溝通差的運動隊在場上協調會被削弱。"},{"en":"If departments stop sharing information, projects may slow down.","zh":"如果部門停止分享資料，項目可能拖慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weaker teamwork.","zh":"這個短語描述團隊合作變弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ill-feeling is generated","meaning":"產生惡感；產生不滿情緒","examples":[{"en":"Ill-feeling is generated by destructive conflict.","zh":"破壞性衝突會產生惡感。"},{"en":"If ill-feeling is generated, resentment, anger, or dislike develops between people.","zh":"如果產生惡感，人與人之間會形成怨氣、憤怒或厭惡。"},{"en":"Unfair group work can generate ill-feeling among classmates.","zh":"不公平的小組工作可以在同學之間產生不滿情緒。"},{"en":"If people feel attacked during meetings, trust may fall and resentment may grow.","zh":"如果人們在會議中感到被攻擊，信任可能下降，怨氣可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes negative emotions being created.","zh":"這個短語描述負面情緒被製造出來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not necessarily unwelcome","meaning":"不一定不受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Conflict is not necessarily unwelcome.","zh":"衝突不一定不受歡迎。"},{"en":"Not necessarily unwelcome means something is not always bad or unwanted.","zh":"不一定不受歡迎，指某事並非總是壞或不想要的。"},{"en":"Criticism in class is not necessarily unwelcome if it helps students improve.","zh":"課堂批評如果幫助學生進步，就不一定不受歡迎。"},{"en":"If disagreement produces better ideas, conflict can be useful.","zh":"如果分歧產生更好想法，衝突可以有用。"},{"en":"The phrase challenges an automatic negative reaction.","zh":"這個短語挑戰自動負面反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"Conflict can, in fact, be necessary.","zh":"事實上，衝突可以是必要的。"},{"en":"In fact introduces information that is true, often surprising or stronger than expected.","zh":"事實上，引入真實資料，通常是令人意外或比預期更強的資訊。"},{"en":"The quiet student is, in fact, the best writer in the class.","zh":"那位安靜學生事實上是班中最好的寫作者。"},{"en":"If people assume all conflict is bad, this phrase corrects that assumption.","zh":"如果人們假設所有衝突都是壞的，這個短語就糾正該假設。"},{"en":"The phrase strengthens or clarifies a point.","zh":"這個短語加強或澄清觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be necessary","meaning":"是必要的","examples":[{"en":"Some conflict may be necessary for better decisions.","zh":"某些衝突對更好決策可能是必要的。"},{"en":"To be necessary means to be needed for a purpose or result.","zh":"是必要的，指為某目的或結果所需要。"},{"en":"Practice is necessary if students want to speak fluently.","zh":"如果學生想流利說話，練習是必要的。"},{"en":"If disagreement reveals weak ideas, some conflict becomes useful for decision-making.","zh":"如果分歧揭示薄弱想法，某些衝突對決策就變得有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something required, not merely optional.","zh":"這個短語描述必需的東西，而不只是可選。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"crucial fact","meaning":"關鍵事實","examples":[{"en":"We must first accept one crucial fact about decision-making.","zh":"我們必須先接受一個關於決策的關鍵事實。"},{"en":"A crucial fact is a very important truth that affects how we understand a situation.","zh":"關鍵事實，是影響我們如何理解情況的非常重要真相。"},{"en":"In exam preparation, one crucial fact is that practice must come before speed.","zh":"在考試準備中，一個關鍵事實是練習必須先於速度。"},{"en":"If a crucial fact is ignored, later decisions may be built on a weak basis.","zh":"如果關鍵事實被忽視，後來決定可能建立在薄弱基礎上。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a key point.","zh":"這個短語引入要點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"new era of","meaning":"……的新時代","examples":[{"en":"Modern organisations operate in a new era of increasing change.","zh":"現代組織在日益變化的新時代中運作。"},{"en":"A new era of something means a new period defined by that condition or development.","zh":"某事的新時代，指由該條件或發展界定的新時期。"},{"en":"Online shopping created a new era of convenience for consumers.","zh":"網上購物為消費者創造了便利的新時代。"},{"en":"If organisations enter a new era, old rules may no longer fit.","zh":"如果組織進入新時代，舊規則可能不再適合。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a major shift in time or conditions.","zh":"這個短語標示時間或條件上的重大轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"increasing change and complexity","meaning":"日益增加的變化與複雜性","examples":[{"en":"Decision-making is difficult in an era of increasing change and complexity.","zh":"在日益增加的變化與複雜性時代，決策很困難。"},{"en":"Increasing change and complexity means situations are becoming less stable and more complicated.","zh":"日益增加的變化與複雜性，指情況變得較不穩定且更複雜。"},{"en":"A school faces increasing complexity when it must manage online learning, special needs, and parent expectations.","zh":"當學校必須管理網上學習、特殊需要和家長期望，就面對日益增加的複雜性。"},{"en":"If information grows and conditions shift quickly, decisions become harder.","zh":"如果資料增加且情況迅速轉變，決策就變得更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why simple top-down decisions may fail.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何簡單由上而下的決策可能失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"accurate and considered decision-making","meaning":"準確而審慎的決策","examples":[{"en":"Accurate and considered decision-making is critical.","zh":"準確而審慎的決策至關重要。"},{"en":"Accurate and considered decision-making means making decisions carefully, correctly, and after thinking about evidence.","zh":"準確而審慎的決策，指仔細、正確並在考慮證據後作出決定。"},{"en":"A doctor needs accurate and considered decision-making before choosing treatment.","zh":"醫生選擇治療前需要準確而審慎的決策。"},{"en":"If decisions are rushed or based on incomplete information, mistakes become more likely.","zh":"如果決策倉促或基於不完整資料，錯誤就更可能發生。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both correctness and careful thought.","zh":"這個短語同時強調正確和仔細思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be critical","meaning":"至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Good decision-making is critical in modern organisations.","zh":"良好決策在現代組織中至關重要。"},{"en":"To be critical means to be extremely important for success or safety.","zh":"至關重要，指對成功或安全極其重要。"},{"en":"Clear instructions are critical during a fire drill.","zh":"在火警演習中，清楚指示至關重要。"},{"en":"If decision-making is poor, an organisation may waste time and money.","zh":"如果決策差，組織可能浪費時間和金錢。"},{"en":"The phrase means essential, not merely useful.","zh":"這個短語指必要，而不只是有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"can no longer be considered","meaning":"不再可被視為","examples":[{"en":"Decision-making can no longer be considered the province of one person.","zh":"決策不再可被視為一個人的專屬範圍。"},{"en":"Can no longer be considered means should not be seen in that way anymore.","zh":"不再可被視為，指不應再用那種方式看待。"},{"en":"Online safety can no longer be considered only a problem for computer teachers.","zh":"網絡安全不再可被視為只屬電腦老師的問題。"},{"en":"If decisions need many kinds of knowledge, one person alone is no longer enough.","zh":"如果決策需要多種知識，單靠一個人已不再足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a change in how something should be understood.","zh":"這個短語標示理解方式的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the province of","meaning":"……的專屬範圍","examples":[{"en":"Decision-making is not the province of just one person.","zh":"決策並不是單一個人的專屬範圍。"},{"en":"The province of someone means an area of responsibility, authority, or special control.","zh":"某人的專屬範圍，指責任、權力或特殊控制的領域。"},{"en":"In a hospital, surgery is the province of trained doctors, not visitors.","zh":"在醫院中，手術是受訓醫生的專屬範圍，而不是訪客的。"},{"en":"If decision-making becomes too complex, it should not remain the province of one manager.","zh":"如果決策變得太複雜，就不應仍是單一經理的專屬範圍。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who controls or is responsible for something.","zh":"這個短語指出誰控制或負責某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"too much information to be processed","meaning":"有太多資料需要處理","examples":[{"en":"There is too much information to be processed by one person.","zh":"有太多資料需要由一個人處理。"},{"en":"Too much information to be processed means the amount of data is too large for someone to handle effectively.","zh":"有太多資料需要處理，指數據量太大，某人無法有效處理。"},{"en":"A student may face too much information to process if they revise five subjects in one night.","zh":"如果學生一晚溫習五科，可能有太多資料需要處理。"},{"en":"If one manager must read every report alone, important details may be missed.","zh":"如果一位經理必須獨自閱讀每份報告，重要細節可能被錯過。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why teamwork may be needed.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何可能需要團隊合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"within the capability of","meaning":"在……的能力範圍內","examples":[{"en":"The task is not within the capability of a single individual.","zh":"這項任務不在單一個人的能力範圍內。"},{"en":"Within the capability of someone means possible for them to do with their skills, time, and resources.","zh":"在某人的能力範圍內，指以其技能、時間和資源而言可以做到。"},{"en":"Finishing one worksheet may be within the capability of a beginner, but writing a full essay may not.","zh":"完成一份工作紙可能在初學者能力範圍內，但寫完整文章可能不在。"},{"en":"If a task exceeds one person’s ability, a group may be needed.","zh":"如果任務超出一人能力，就可能需要團隊。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the limit of what someone can do.","zh":"這個短語標示某人能做甚麼的界限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"any single individual","meaning":"任何單一個人","examples":[{"en":"No single individual can process all the necessary information.","zh":"任何單一個人都不能處理所有必要資料。"},{"en":"Any single individual means one person alone, without help from others.","zh":"任何單一個人，指沒有其他人幫助下的一個人。"},{"en":"No single individual can run a large hospital without nurses, cleaners, and administrators.","zh":"任何單一個人都不能在沒有護士、清潔工和行政人員下營運大型醫院。"},{"en":"If knowledge is spread across many people, decisions should involve more than one person.","zh":"如果知識分散在多人之中，決策就應涉及多於一人。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises the limits of one person.","zh":"這個短語強調一個人的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, decision-making is now based on group discussion.","zh":"因此，決策現在以小組討論為基礎。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what was just mentioned.","zh":"因此，指因為剛才提到的事情。"},{"en":"The bus was late; as a result, many students missed the first lesson.","zh":"巴士遲到；因此，許多學生錯過第一課。"},{"en":"If one person cannot process all information, group discussion becomes necessary.","zh":"如果一個人不能處理所有資料，小組討論就變得必要。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a consequence.","zh":"這個短語引出結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"以……為基礎","examples":[{"en":"Modern decision-making is based on group discussions.","zh":"現代決策以小組討論為基礎。"},{"en":"To be based on something means to use it as the foundation or main support.","zh":"以某物為基礎，指使用它作為根基或主要支持。"},{"en":"A good essay should be based on evidence, not only opinion.","zh":"好作文應以證據為基礎，而不只是意見。"},{"en":"If decisions are based on group discussion, many views influence the final choice.","zh":"如果決策以小組討論為基礎，許多觀點會影響最終選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the foundation of an action or idea.","zh":"這個短語指出行動或想法的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"group discussions","meaning":"小組討論","examples":[{"en":"Group discussions allow different perspectives to be exchanged.","zh":"小組討論容許不同觀點交流。"},{"en":"Group discussions are conversations among several people who share ideas on a topic.","zh":"小組討論是幾個人就某題目分享想法的對話。"},{"en":"Students may use group discussions to plan a presentation.","zh":"學生可能透過小組討論計劃匯報。"},{"en":"If group discussions are well managed, quiet members can also contribute.","zh":"如果小組討論管理得好，安靜成員也可以貢獻。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to collective thinking through conversation.","zh":"這個短語指透過對話進行集體思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"meetings and presentations","meaning":"會議和匯報","examples":[{"en":"Meetings and presentations are used in modern decision-making.","zh":"會議和匯報被用於現代決策。"},{"en":"Meetings and presentations are formal ways to share information, explain ideas, and discuss decisions.","zh":"會議和匯報，是分享資料、解釋想法和討論決定的正式方式。"},{"en":"A company may use meetings and presentations before launching a new product.","zh":"公司推出新產品前，可能使用會議和匯報。"},{"en":"If information is complex, presentations can help people understand it more clearly.","zh":"如果資料複雜，匯報可以幫助人們更清楚理解。"},{"en":"The phrase names common workplace communication formats.","zh":"這個短語指出常見工作場所溝通形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"allow the exchange of","meaning":"容許……交流","examples":[{"en":"Meetings allow the exchange of different perspectives.","zh":"會議容許不同觀點交流。"},{"en":"To allow the exchange of something means to make it possible for people to share it with one another.","zh":"容許某物交流，指讓人們可以彼此分享它。"},{"en":"A class debate allows the exchange of ideas between students.","zh":"課堂辯論容許學生之間交流想法。"},{"en":"If a meeting allows real exchange, people do more than listen silently.","zh":"如果會議容許真正交流，人們就不只是安靜聆聽。"},{"en":"The phrase describes two-way sharing.","zh":"這個短語描述雙向分享。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a variety of perspectives","meaning":"多種觀點","examples":[{"en":"Organisations need a variety of perspectives from qualified people.","zh":"組織需要來自合資格人士的多種觀點。"},{"en":"A variety of perspectives means several different viewpoints or ways of seeing a problem.","zh":"多種觀點，指幾種不同看法或理解問題的方式。"},{"en":"A school policy improves when teachers, students, and parents offer a variety of perspectives.","zh":"當老師、學生和家長提供多種觀點，學校政策會改善。"},{"en":"If only one perspective is heard, important risks may be missed.","zh":"如果只聽到一種觀點，重要風險可能被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase values diversity of thought.","zh":"這個短語重視思想多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"appropriately qualified people","meaning":"具適當資格的人","examples":[{"en":"Decision-making should involve appropriately qualified people.","zh":"決策應涉及具適當資格的人。"},{"en":"Appropriately qualified people are people with the right knowledge, training, or experience for a task.","zh":"具適當資格的人，是對某任務有合適知識、訓練或經驗的人。"},{"en":"A hospital should ask appropriately qualified doctors before changing medical procedures.","zh":"醫院更改醫療程序前，應詢問具適當資格的醫生。"},{"en":"If decisions involve technology, technical staff should be included.","zh":"如果決策涉及科技，就應包括技術人員。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that expertise should match the issue.","zh":"這個短語強調專業知識應配合議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"such gatherings","meaning":"這類聚會；這類會議","examples":[{"en":"Such gatherings are often affected by groupthink.","zh":"這類會議常受到群體迷思影響。"},{"en":"Such gatherings means meetings or group situations just mentioned.","zh":"這類會議，指剛才提到的會議或小組情境。"},{"en":"Staff meetings, project briefings, and committee discussions are such gatherings.","zh":"員工會議、項目簡報和委員會討論都是這類會議。"},{"en":"If people meet in groups, social pressure may affect what they say.","zh":"如果人們以小組形式見面，社會壓力可能影響他們說甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to the gatherings already described.","zh":"這個短語回指已描述的聚會或會議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be affected by","meaning":"受到……影響","examples":[{"en":"Decision-making groups can be affected by groupthink.","zh":"決策小組可能受到群體迷思影響。"},{"en":"To be affected by something means to be influenced or changed by it.","zh":"受到某事影響，指被它影響或改變。"},{"en":"Students’ concentration can be affected by noise outside the classroom.","zh":"學生專注力可能受到課室外噪音影響。"},{"en":"If a group is affected by pressure to agree, decisions may become weaker.","zh":"如果小組受到一致同意的壓力影響，決策可能變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase shows an external or internal influence.","zh":"這個短語顯示外部或內部影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"groupthink","meaning":"群體迷思","examples":[{"en":"Groupthink can damage the quality of decisions.","zh":"群體迷思可以損害決策質素。"},{"en":"Groupthink happens when people agree with the group too easily and stop thinking critically.","zh":"群體迷思發生在人們太容易同意群體，並停止批判思考時。"},{"en":"In a class project, groupthink may occur if everyone follows the loudest student without questioning.","zh":"在班級項目中，如果人人不加質疑地跟隨最大聲的學生，就可能出現群體迷思。"},{"en":"If disagreement is suppressed, mistakes may remain hidden.","zh":"如果分歧被壓制，錯誤可能保持隱藏。"},{"en":"The word describes unhealthy agreement.","zh":"這個詞描述不健康的一致同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tightly-knit cohorts","meaning":"關係緊密的小群體","examples":[{"en":"Groupthink occurs in tightly-knit cohorts of workers.","zh":"群體迷思出現在關係緊密的小群體員工之中。"},{"en":"Tightly-knit cohorts are close groups whose members know and support one another strongly.","zh":"關係緊密的小群體，是成員彼此熟悉並強烈支持對方的小組。"},{"en":"A small team that eats lunch together every day may become tightly knit.","zh":"每天一起吃午飯的小團隊可能變得關係緊密。"},{"en":"If a close group values harmony too much, members may avoid honest disagreement.","zh":"如果親密小組過分重視和諧，成員可能避免誠實分歧。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests closeness that can become pressure.","zh":"這個短語暗示親密可能變成壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"uncritically accept","meaning":"不加批判地接受","examples":[{"en":"Workers may uncritically accept the feelings of the group.","zh":"員工可能不加批判地接受群體感受。"},{"en":"To uncritically accept something means to agree without questioning or examining it.","zh":"不加批判地接受某事，指不質疑或檢視就同意。"},{"en":"Students should not uncritically accept an answer just because the top student says it.","zh":"學生不應只因尖子說某答案，就不加批判地接受。"},{"en":"If people stop asking questions, wrong ideas may pass as agreement.","zh":"如果人們停止發問，錯誤想法可能被當作共識通過。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against thoughtless acceptance.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要盲目接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"feelings of the group","meaning":"群體感受","examples":[{"en":"Groupthink means accepting the feelings of the group.","zh":"群體迷思意味着接受群體感受。"},{"en":"Feelings of the group are the shared mood, preference, or emotional direction within a group.","zh":"群體感受，是小組內共同的情緒、偏好或情感方向。"},{"en":"A class may have strong group feelings against a new homework policy.","zh":"班級可能對新功課政策有強烈群體感受。"},{"en":"If group feelings replace evidence, decisions can become emotional rather than accurate.","zh":"如果群體感受取代證據，決策可能變得情緒化而非準確。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to collective emotion.","zh":"這個短語指集體情緒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Workers may accept group feelings rather than fight out disagreements.","zh":"員工可能接受群體感受，而不是把分歧辯清楚。"},{"en":"Rather than shows that one thing is chosen or true instead of another.","zh":"而不是，顯示選擇或成立的是一件事，而非另一件事。"},{"en":"A student should explain mistakes rather than hide them.","zh":"學生應解釋錯誤，而不是隱藏它們。"},{"en":"If people choose harmony rather than debate, weak ideas may survive.","zh":"如果人們選擇和諧而不是辯論，薄弱想法可能留下來。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a clear contrast.","zh":"這個短語建立清楚對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fight it out","meaning":"爭論到底；把問題辯清楚","examples":[{"en":"Group members may avoid fighting it out.","zh":"小組成員可能避免把問題辯清楚。"},{"en":"To fight it out means to argue or debate until a disagreement is fully dealt with.","zh":"爭論到底，指辯論或爭論直到分歧被充分處理。"},{"en":"Two classmates may need to fight out different ideas before choosing a project topic.","zh":"兩名同學可能需要把不同想法辯清楚，才選擇項目題目。"},{"en":"If a disagreement is never fought out, hidden tension may remain.","zh":"如果分歧從未被辯清楚，隱藏緊張可能仍然存在。"},{"en":"The phrase can mean intense discussion, not physical fighting.","zh":"這個短語可以指激烈討論，而不是肢體打鬥。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"individual dissent","meaning":"個人異議","examples":[{"en":"Individual dissent is squashed in groupthink.","zh":"在群體迷思中，個人異議會被壓制。"},{"en":"Individual dissent means one person’s disagreement with the group view.","zh":"個人異議，是一個人對群體觀點的不同意見。"},{"en":"A student shows individual dissent when they politely challenge a group answer.","zh":"當學生有禮貌地質疑小組答案時，就是表達個人異議。"},{"en":"If dissent is punished, people may stop offering honest views.","zh":"如果異議被懲罰，人們可能停止提出真實看法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to personal disagreement inside a group.","zh":"這個短語指小組內個人的不同意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be squashed","meaning":"被壓制","examples":[{"en":"Dissent can be squashed by pressure to agree.","zh":"異議可能被一致同意的壓力壓制。"},{"en":"To be squashed means to be pressed down, silenced, or stopped.","zh":"被壓制，指被壓下、被噤聲或被阻止。"},{"en":"A student’s question may be squashed if the teacher laughs at it.","zh":"如果老師嘲笑學生問題，該問題可能被壓制。"},{"en":"If disagreement is squashed, the group may look united but think poorly.","zh":"如果分歧被壓制，小組可能看起來團結，但思考質素差。"},{"en":"The phrase describes suppression.","zh":"這個短語描述壓抑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a pool of thinking individuals","meaning":"一群會思考的人","examples":[{"en":"Good decisions should come from a pool of thinking individuals.","zh":"好決策應來自一群會思考的人。"},{"en":"A pool of thinking individuals means a group of people who each think carefully and independently.","zh":"一群會思考的人，指每個人都仔細和獨立思考的小組。"},{"en":"A good project team needs thinking individuals, not members who simply nod.","zh":"好項目團隊需要會思考的人，而不是只會點頭的成員。"},{"en":"If each person contributes real judgement, the group can make better decisions.","zh":"如果每個人都貢獻真正判斷，小組就能作出更好決策。"},{"en":"The phrase values independent minds within a group.","zh":"這個短語重視群體中的獨立頭腦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"valuable insights","meaning":"有價值的見解","examples":[{"en":"Each individual may contribute valuable insights.","zh":"每個個人都可能貢獻有價值的見解。"},{"en":"Valuable insights are useful understandings that help people see a situation more clearly.","zh":"有價值的見解，是幫助人更清楚看見情況的有用理解。"},{"en":"A quiet student may offer valuable insights during a group discussion.","zh":"安靜學生可能在小組討論中提出有價值的見解。"},{"en":"If different people share insights, hidden problems may become visible.","zh":"如果不同人分享見解，隱藏問題可能變得可見。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to useful ideas, not just opinions.","zh":"這個短語指有用想法，而不只是意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"collective desire to","meaning":"共同想要……的願望","examples":[{"en":"The group may have a collective desire to promote harmony.","zh":"小組可能有共同想要促進和諧的願望。"},{"en":"A collective desire to do something is a shared wish among group members.","zh":"共同想要做某事的願望，是小組成員共享的願望。"},{"en":"A class may have a collective desire to finish a project quickly before the holiday.","zh":"班級可能有共同想在假期前快速完成項目的願望。"},{"en":"If everyone wants harmony too strongly, disagreement may be avoided.","zh":"如果人人太強烈希望和諧，就可能避免分歧。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a group-level wish.","zh":"這個短語描述群體層面的願望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"promote harmony","meaning":"促進和諧","examples":[{"en":"Groupthink may simply promote harmony.","zh":"群體迷思可能只是促進和諧。"},{"en":"To promote harmony means to encourage peace, agreement, and smooth relationships.","zh":"促進和諧，指鼓勵和平、一致和順暢關係。"},{"en":"A class monitor may promote harmony by helping classmates solve small arguments.","zh":"班長可能透過幫同學解決小爭執來促進和諧。"},{"en":"If harmony is promoted at the cost of truth, decisions may become weaker.","zh":"如果和諧是以真相為代價來促進，決策可能變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase can be positive, but here it may hide disagreement.","zh":"這個短語可以是正面，但在此可能隱藏分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be likely to","meaning":"很可能","examples":[{"en":"Groupthink is not likely to produce the best decision.","zh":"群體迷思不太可能產生最佳決定。"},{"en":"To be likely to do something means to have a good chance of doing it.","zh":"很可能做某事，指有相當機會做該事。"},{"en":"A student who practises daily is likely to improve.","zh":"每天練習的學生很可能進步。"},{"en":"If nobody questions weak ideas, the group is unlikely to make the best choice.","zh":"如果沒有人質疑薄弱想法，小組就不太可能作出最佳選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses probability.","zh":"這個短語表達可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"optimise the chances of","meaning":"最大化……的機會","examples":[{"en":"Groupthink does not optimise the chances of making the best decision.","zh":"群體迷思不能最大化作出最佳決定的機會。"},{"en":"To optimise the chances of something means to make success as likely as possible.","zh":"最大化某事的機會，指令成功盡可能有可能發生。"},{"en":"Sleeping well and practising past papers can optimise the chances of exam success.","zh":"睡得好和練習歷屆試題可以最大化考試成功機會。"},{"en":"If a team welcomes honest disagreement, it improves its chance of finding the best answer.","zh":"如果團隊歡迎誠實分歧，就提高找到最佳答案的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase means maximise the likelihood of a good result.","zh":"這個短語指最大化好結果出現的可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make the best decision","meaning":"作出最佳決定","examples":[{"en":"Organisations need conflict to make the best decision.","zh":"組織需要衝突來作出最佳決定。"},{"en":"To make the best decision means to choose the option that is most suitable after careful thinking.","zh":"作出最佳決定，指經仔細思考後選擇最合適選項。"},{"en":"A family may compare price, distance, and quality to make the best school choice.","zh":"家庭可能比較價錢、距離和質素，以作出最佳學校選擇。"},{"en":"If different views are heard, mistakes can be corrected before the final decision.","zh":"如果不同觀點被聽見，錯誤可以在最終決定前被糾正。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on quality of choice.","zh":"這個短語強調選擇的質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bring together","meaning":"結合起來","examples":[{"en":"When these two facts are brought together, they lead to a conclusion.","zh":"當這兩個事實被結合起來，它們會導向一個結論。"},{"en":"To bring together ideas means to combine them and consider them at the same time.","zh":"把想法結合起來，指把它們合併並同時考慮。"},{"en":"A student can bring together evidence from two paragraphs to answer a reading question.","zh":"學生可以把兩段的證據結合起來回答閱讀題。"},{"en":"If two facts point in the same direction, combining them strengthens the argument.","zh":"如果兩個事實指向同一方向，把它們結合會加強論點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes combining information.","zh":"這個短語描述合併資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lead to the conclusion that","meaning":"得出……的結論","examples":[{"en":"The two facts lead to the conclusion that some conflict is necessary.","zh":"這兩個事實得出某些衝突是必要的結論。"},{"en":"To lead to the conclusion that something is true means to make that conclusion logical.","zh":"導向某結論，指令該結論在邏輯上成立。"},{"en":"Repeated lateness and poor preparation may lead a teacher to the conclusion that a student needs support.","zh":"反覆遲到和準備不足，可能令老師得出學生需要支援的結論。"},{"en":"If one-person decisions are weak and groupthink is dangerous, some disagreement becomes useful.","zh":"如果一人決策薄弱而群體迷思危險，某些分歧就變得有用。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a reasoned final idea.","zh":"這個短語引出經推理得出的最終想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"some degree of conflict","meaning":"某程度的衝突","examples":[{"en":"Some degree of conflict is necessary for better decision-making.","zh":"某程度的衝突對更好決策是必要的。"},{"en":"Some degree of conflict means a certain amount of disagreement or tension.","zh":"某程度的衝突，指一定數量的分歧或緊張。"},{"en":"A project team may need some degree of conflict to test weak ideas.","zh":"項目團隊可能需要某程度的衝突來測試薄弱想法。"},{"en":"If there is no disagreement at all, people may simply be hiding their views.","zh":"如果完全沒有分歧，人們可能只是隱藏看法。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests limited conflict can be healthy.","zh":"這個短語暗示有限度衝突可以健康。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in order to","meaning":"為了","examples":[{"en":"Some conflict is needed in order to improve decision-making.","zh":"為了改善決策，需要某些衝突。"},{"en":"In order to means for the purpose of doing something.","zh":"為了，指以做某事為目的。"},{"en":"Students practise pronunciation in order to speak more clearly.","zh":"學生練習發音，是為了說得更清楚。"},{"en":"If conflict is managed well, it can serve the purpose of better thinking.","zh":"如果衝突管理得好，它可以服務於更好思考的目的。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces purpose.","zh":"這個短語引入目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ultimately","meaning":"最終","examples":[{"en":"Better decision-making can ultimately improve organisational performance.","zh":"更好的決策最終可以改善組織表現。"},{"en":"Ultimately means in the end or after all effects are considered.","zh":"最終，指到最後或考慮所有影響後。"},{"en":"Daily reading may feel slow, but it ultimately improves writing.","zh":"每天閱讀可能感覺慢，但最終會改善寫作。"},{"en":"If conflict improves decisions, it may finally help the whole organisation.","zh":"如果衝突改善決策，它最終可能幫助整個組織。"},{"en":"The word points to the final result.","zh":"這個詞指向最後結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"higher organisational performance","meaning":"更高的組織表現","examples":[{"en":"Conflict may ultimately produce higher organisational performance.","zh":"衝突最終可能產生更高的組織表現。"},{"en":"Higher organisational performance means better results, efficiency, quality, or success for an organisation.","zh":"更高的組織表現，指組織有更好的結果、效率、質素或成功。"},{"en":"A school shows higher organisational performance when students learn better and teachers co-operate well.","zh":"當學生學得更好且老師合作良好，學校就顯示更高的組織表現。"},{"en":"If conflict leads to better decisions, the organisation may perform more strongly.","zh":"如果衝突帶來更好決策，組織可能表現更強。"},{"en":"The phrase measures how well an organisation works.","zh":"這個短語衡量組織運作得有多好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"extending this further","meaning":"進一步說","examples":[{"en":"Extending this further, very low conflict may be worrying.","zh":"進一步說，非常低水平的衝突可能令人擔心。"},{"en":"Extending this further means taking the same idea one step beyond what was just said.","zh":"進一步說，指把剛才的想法再推前一步。"},{"en":"If practice improves writing, extending this further, feedback can improve it even more.","zh":"如果練習改善寫作，進一步說，回饋可以令它改善更多。"},{"en":"If some conflict is useful, then no conflict at all may signal another problem.","zh":"如果某些衝突有用，那麼完全沒有衝突可能顯示另一問題。"},{"en":"The phrase develops an argument further.","zh":"這個短語進一步發展論點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"somewhat paradoxically","meaning":"有點矛盾的是","examples":[{"en":"Somewhat paradoxically, an absence of conflict may be a warning sign.","zh":"有點矛盾的是，缺乏衝突可能是一個警號。"},{"en":"Somewhat paradoxically means in a way that seems contradictory at first.","zh":"有點矛盾的是，指以起初看似自相矛盾的方式。"},{"en":"Somewhat paradoxically, failing an easy test can help a student take study more seriously.","zh":"有點矛盾的是，簡單測驗不合格可以幫助學生更認真學習。"},{"en":"If conflict seems bad, it may feel surprising that no conflict can also be bad.","zh":"如果衝突看似壞事，完全沒有衝突也可能不好就令人意外。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an apparently opposite idea.","zh":"這個短語引入表面相反的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"very low levels of","meaning":"非常低水平的……","examples":[{"en":"Very low levels of conflict may indicate a problem.","zh":"非常低水平的衝突可能顯示問題。"},{"en":"Very low levels of something means there is only a small amount of it.","zh":"非常低水平的某事，指它只有很少數量。"},{"en":"Very low levels of participation in class may worry a teacher.","zh":"課堂參與度非常低可能令老師擔心。"},{"en":"If conflict levels are extremely low, people may be silent rather than satisfied.","zh":"如果衝突水平極低，人們可能是沉默，而不是滿意。"},{"en":"The phrase measures a small amount.","zh":"這個短語量度很少的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"absence of conflict","meaning":"缺乏衝突","examples":[{"en":"An absence of conflict may actually be worrying.","zh":"缺乏衝突其實可能令人擔心。"},{"en":"Absence of conflict means there is no visible disagreement or tension.","zh":"缺乏衝突，指沒有可見分歧或緊張。"},{"en":"In a group project, total absence of conflict may mean no one cares enough to speak.","zh":"在小組項目中，完全缺乏衝突可能意味沒有人關心得想發言。"},{"en":"If problems exist but nobody argues, the issues may be hidden.","zh":"如果問題存在但沒有人爭論，問題可能被隱藏。"},{"en":"The phrase does not always mean peace; it may mean silence.","zh":"這個短語不一定代表和平；也可能代表沉默。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"may actually be worrying","meaning":"其實可能令人擔心","examples":[{"en":"A lack of conflict may actually be worrying.","zh":"缺乏衝突其實可能令人擔心。"},{"en":"May actually be worrying means may be a real cause for concern, even if it seems fine at first.","zh":"其實可能令人擔心，指即使起初看似沒問題，也可能真正值得憂慮。"},{"en":"A class that never asks questions may actually be worrying because students may not understand.","zh":"從不發問的班級其實可能令人擔心，因為學生可能不明白。"},{"en":"If silence hides fear, the situation is less healthy than it looks.","zh":"如果沉默掩蓋恐懼，情況就沒有表面上那麼健康。"},{"en":"The phrase challenges a surface impression.","zh":"這個短語挑戰表面印象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"indicate a lack of","meaning":"顯示缺乏……","examples":[{"en":"Low conflict may indicate a lack of staff involvement.","zh":"低衝突可能顯示缺乏職員參與。"},{"en":"To indicate a lack of something means to show that something may be missing or insufficient.","zh":"顯示缺乏某物，指顯示某物可能不存在或不足。"},{"en":"Poor attendance may indicate a lack of interest in the activity.","zh":"出席率低可能顯示缺乏對活動的興趣。"},{"en":"If workers never speak up, it may show they are not involved.","zh":"如果員工從不發聲，可能顯示他們沒有參與。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a sign with a possible absence.","zh":"這個短語把跡象與可能缺失連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"staff involvement","meaning":"職員參與","examples":[{"en":"Very little conflict may suggest low staff involvement.","zh":"很少衝突可能暗示職員參與度低。"},{"en":"Staff involvement means employees actively take part in discussions, decisions, or activities.","zh":"職員參與，指員工主動參加討論、決策或活動。"},{"en":"A school has high staff involvement when teachers help design new policies.","zh":"當老師幫助設計新政策，學校就有高職員參與度。"},{"en":"If staff involvement is low, change may be decided without useful frontline knowledge.","zh":"如果職員參與度低，變革可能在沒有前線有用知識下被決定。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to active participation by workers.","zh":"這個短語指員工主動參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"staff interest","meaning":"職員興趣；職員關注","examples":[{"en":"An absence of conflict may indicate a lack of staff interest.","zh":"缺乏衝突可能顯示缺乏職員關注。"},{"en":"Staff interest means employees care about what is happening in the organisation.","zh":"職員關注，指員工關心組織正在發生的事情。"},{"en":"High staff interest can be seen when workers ask questions about new plans.","zh":"當員工就新計劃發問，就可看見高度職員關注。"},{"en":"If staff show no interest, they may not challenge weak decisions.","zh":"如果職員沒有興趣，他們可能不會質疑薄弱決定。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to concern and attention from employees.","zh":"這個短語指員工的關心和注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"problems are being hidden","meaning":"問題正被隱藏","examples":[{"en":"Low conflict may suggest that problems are being hidden.","zh":"低衝突可能暗示問題正被隱藏。"},{"en":"Problems are being hidden means difficulties exist but are not being openly discussed.","zh":"問題正被隱藏，指困難存在但沒有被公開討論。"},{"en":"If students never complain but marks keep falling, classroom problems may be hidden.","zh":"如果學生從不投訴但成績持續下跌，課堂問題可能被隱藏。"},{"en":"When people fear punishment, they may hide problems instead of solving them.","zh":"當人們害怕懲罰，他們可能隱藏問題而不是解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that silence may not equal success.","zh":"這個短語提醒沉默不等於成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"new ideas are being stifled","meaning":"新意念正被壓制","examples":[{"en":"An absence of conflict may mean that new ideas are being stifled.","zh":"缺乏衝突可能意味着新意念正被壓制。"},{"en":"New ideas are being stifled means fresh suggestions are being suppressed or prevented from developing.","zh":"新意念正被壓制，指新建議被壓下或被阻止發展。"},{"en":"A teacher may stifle new ideas if every unusual answer is immediately rejected.","zh":"如果老師立即否定每個不尋常答案，可能壓制新意念。"},{"en":"If people stop proposing changes, the organisation may become less creative.","zh":"如果人們停止提出改變，組織可能變得較缺乏創意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creativity being blocked.","zh":"這個短語描述創意被阻塞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"morale is low","meaning":"士氣低落","examples":[{"en":"Very little conflict may suggest that morale is low.","zh":"很少衝突可能暗示士氣低落。"},{"en":"Morale is low means people feel discouraged, unmotivated, or unhappy about the group.","zh":"士氣低落，指人們對群體感到灰心、缺乏動力或不快。"},{"en":"A team with low morale may stop volunteering for extra tasks.","zh":"士氣低落的團隊可能停止自願承擔額外工作。"},{"en":"If staff no longer care enough to disagree, morale may be poor.","zh":"如果職員已不再關心得提出不同意見，士氣可能很差。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weak group spirit.","zh":"這個短語描述薄弱的團隊精神。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the focus shifts to","meaning":"焦點轉移至……","examples":[{"en":"The focus shifts to conflict management.","zh":"焦點轉移至衝突管理。"},{"en":"The focus shifts to something means attention moves from one issue to another.","zh":"焦點轉移至某事，指注意力由一個議題移到另一個。"},{"en":"After students understand vocabulary, the focus shifts to using it in speaking.","zh":"學生理解詞彙後，焦點轉移至在口語中使用它。"},{"en":"If conflict cannot be removed completely, attention should move to managing it well.","zh":"如果衝突不能完全消除，注意力就應轉到好好管理它。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a change in priority.","zh":"這個短語標示優先事項改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"conflict management","meaning":"衝突管理","examples":[{"en":"Organisations should focus on conflict management, not conflict removal.","zh":"組織應專注於衝突管理，而不是消除衝突。"},{"en":"Conflict management means handling disagreement so that it becomes useful or at least less harmful.","zh":"衝突管理，指處理分歧，使它變得有用或至少較少有害。"},{"en":"A teacher uses conflict management when helping two students discuss a problem calmly.","zh":"老師幫助兩名學生冷靜討論問題時，就是在進行衝突管理。"},{"en":"If conflict is managed well, it may produce better ideas instead of anger.","zh":"如果衝突管理得好，它可能產生更好想法，而不是憤怒。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on controlling conflict, not pretending it does not exist.","zh":"這個短語強調控制衝突，而不是假裝它不存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as deemed optimum","meaning":"按被視為最理想的情況","examples":[{"en":"Conflict should be reduced or created as deemed optimum for the organisation.","zh":"衝突應按被視為對組織最理想的情況而被減少或創造。"},{"en":"As deemed optimum means according to what is judged to be the best level or condition.","zh":"按被視為最理想的情況，指根據被判斷為最佳水平或狀態的標準。"},{"en":"A teacher may adjust homework as deemed optimum for students’ workload.","zh":"老師可能按學生工作量最理想的情況調整功課。"},{"en":"If conflict is too high, reduce it; if it is too low, encourage honest debate.","zh":"如果衝突太高，就減少它；如果太低，就鼓勵誠實辯論。"},{"en":"The phrase means based on what seems most suitable.","zh":"這個短語指根據看似最合適的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"conflict removal","meaning":"消除衝突","examples":[{"en":"The aim is conflict management rather than conflict removal.","zh":"目標是衝突管理，而不是消除衝突。"},{"en":"Conflict removal means trying to eliminate all disagreement or tension.","zh":"消除衝突，指試圖除去所有分歧或緊張。"},{"en":"A classroom that bans all disagreement may achieve conflict removal but lose discussion quality.","zh":"禁止所有分歧的課室，可能達到消除衝突，但失去討論質素。"},{"en":"If all conflict is removed, useful criticism may disappear too.","zh":"如果所有衝突被消除，有用批評也可能消失。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts with managing conflict productively.","zh":"這個短語與有效管理衝突形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"significant resistance and conflict","meaning":"重大的抗拒與衝突","examples":[{"en":"Change causes significant resistance and conflict.","zh":"變革造成重大的抗拒與衝突。"},{"en":"Significant resistance and conflict means strong opposition and serious disagreement.","zh":"重大的抗拒與衝突，指強烈反對和嚴重分歧。"},{"en":"A new workplace pay system may create significant resistance and conflict if workers feel treated unfairly.","zh":"如果員工覺得不公平，新的工作場所薪酬制度可能造成重大抗拒與衝突。"},{"en":"If change threatens people’s routines or security, strong resistance may follow.","zh":"如果變革威脅人們的日常流程或安全感，強烈抗拒可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a major reaction to change.","zh":"這個短語描述對變革的重大反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"constructive and necessary","meaning":"具建設性且必要","examples":[{"en":"Some conflict is constructive and necessary.","zh":"某些衝突具建設性且必要。"},{"en":"Constructive and necessary means useful for improvement and needed for a good result.","zh":"具建設性且必要，指對改善有用並對好結果有需要。"},{"en":"Honest feedback on an essay can be constructive and necessary.","zh":"對作文的誠實回饋可以是具建設性且必要的。"},{"en":"If disagreement exposes a weak plan, it helps the group improve.","zh":"如果分歧揭示薄弱計劃，它就幫助小組改善。"},{"en":"The phrase separates healthy conflict from destructive conflict.","zh":"這個短語把健康衝突與破壞性衝突區分開來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"impede progress","meaning":"阻礙進展","examples":[{"en":"Some conflict impedes progress.","zh":"某些衝突會阻礙進展。"},{"en":"To impede progress means to slow down or block improvement or movement forward.","zh":"阻礙進展，指拖慢或阻止改善或向前推進。"},{"en":"Constant arguments in a group project can impede progress toward the deadline.","zh":"小組項目中持續爭吵，可以阻礙按限期完成的進展。"},{"en":"If conflict becomes personal, work may stop moving forward.","zh":"如果衝突變成人身問題，工作可能停止前進。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that gets in the way of improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述阻擋改善的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"originate from","meaning":"源自","examples":[{"en":"Resistance can originate from rational people.","zh":"抗拒可以源自理性的人。"},{"en":"To originate from something means to begin or come from that source.","zh":"源自某物，指從該來源開始或出現。"},{"en":"A misunderstanding may originate from unclear instructions.","zh":"誤解可能源自不清楚的指示。"},{"en":"If resistance originates from reasonable concerns, managers should listen carefully.","zh":"如果抗拒源自合理憂慮，管理者應仔細聆聽。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of something.","zh":"這個短語指出某事的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"level-headed","meaning":"冷靜理智的","examples":[{"en":"Even level-headed people can resist change.","zh":"即使冷靜理智的人也可能抗拒變化。"},{"en":"Level-headed means calm, sensible, and able to think clearly.","zh":"冷靜理智的，指沉着、明智並能清楚思考。"},{"en":"A level-headed student stays calm during an exam and reads questions carefully.","zh":"冷靜理智的學生在考試中保持鎮定並仔細讀題。"},{"en":"If even calm people resist change, the resistance may have real reasons.","zh":"如果連冷靜的人也抗拒變革，這種抗拒可能有真實原因。"},{"en":"The word describes balanced judgement.","zh":"這個詞描述平衡判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"open-minded","meaning":"思想開明的","examples":[{"en":"Open-minded people may still feel resistance to change.","zh":"思想開明的人仍可能對變革感到抗拒。"},{"en":"Open-minded means willing to consider new ideas or different opinions.","zh":"思想開明的，指願意考慮新想法或不同意見。"},{"en":"An open-minded teacher listens to students’ suggestions before deciding.","zh":"思想開明的老師在決定前會聆聽學生建議。"},{"en":"If an open-minded person resists a change, their concern may deserve attention.","zh":"如果思想開明的人抗拒某變化，其憂慮可能值得注意。"},{"en":"The word describes mental flexibility.","zh":"這個詞描述思想彈性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rational people","meaning":"理性的人","examples":[{"en":"Even rational people can produce conflict.","zh":"即使是理性的人也可能產生衝突。"},{"en":"Rational people are people who try to think logically and use reasons.","zh":"理性的人，是嘗試邏輯思考並使用理由的人。"},{"en":"Rational people may still disagree if they have different information.","zh":"如果理性的人掌握不同資料，仍可能有分歧。"},{"en":"If rational workers resist change, managers should not assume they are simply difficult.","zh":"如果理性員工抗拒變革，管理者不應假設他們只是難相處。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds us that conflict can come from reasonable thought.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，衝突可以來自合理思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"change agents","meaning":"變革推動者","examples":[{"en":"Change agents need strategies for dealing with resistance.","zh":"變革推動者需要處理抗拒的策略。"},{"en":"Change agents are people who help plan, lead, or support change in an organisation.","zh":"變革推動者，是幫助規劃、領導或支援組織變革的人。"},{"en":"A school principal can be a change agent when introducing a new teaching system.","zh":"當校長引入新教學制度時，可以是變革推動者。"},{"en":"If change agents ignore people’s fears, resistance may grow.","zh":"如果變革推動者忽視人們的恐懼，抗拒可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people who drive change.","zh":"這個短語指推動變革的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"deal with it","meaning":"處理它","examples":[{"en":"Change agents must know how to deal with resistance.","zh":"變革推動者必須知道如何處理抗拒。"},{"en":"To deal with it means to manage or handle a problem effectively.","zh":"處理它，指有效管理或應對問題。"},{"en":"If a student receives criticism, they need to deal with it calmly and learn from it.","zh":"如果學生收到批評，就需要冷靜處理它並從中學習。"},{"en":"If resistance appears, ignoring it will not make it disappear.","zh":"如果抗拒出現，忽視它不會令它消失。"},{"en":"The phrase means respond practically to a difficulty.","zh":"這個短語指實際回應困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"essential strategy","meaning":"重要策略","examples":[{"en":"One essential strategy is to listen to everyone involved.","zh":"一個重要策略是聆聽所有相關人士。"},{"en":"An essential strategy is a very important method needed for success.","zh":"重要策略，是成功所需的非常重要方法。"},{"en":"For language learning, one essential strategy is practising little and often.","zh":"對語言學習而言，一個重要策略是少量但經常練習。"},{"en":"If managers listen before deciding, resistance may become easier to handle.","zh":"如果管理者在決定前聆聽，抗拒可能較容易處理。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a key method.","zh":"這個短語指出關鍵方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"all those involved","meaning":"所有相關人士","examples":[{"en":"A change agent should listen to all those involved.","zh":"變革推動者應聆聽所有相關人士。"},{"en":"All those involved means everyone who takes part in or is affected by the situation.","zh":"所有相關人士，指所有參與或受該情況影響的人。"},{"en":"Before changing school lunch rules, leaders should listen to students, parents, and staff.","zh":"在更改學校午餐規則前，領導者應聆聽學生、家長和員工。"},{"en":"If affected people are excluded, they may resist the change.","zh":"如果受影響的人被排除，他們可能抗拒變化。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses inclusion.","zh":"這個短語強調包容參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"strident","meaning":"言辭激烈的","examples":[{"en":"A change agent should listen even to strident people.","zh":"變革推動者即使對言辭激烈的人也應聆聽。"},{"en":"Strident means loud, forceful, and often angry in expressing opinions.","zh":"言辭激烈的，指表達意見時聲音大、強硬且常帶憤怒。"},{"en":"A strident parent may speak very strongly at a school meeting.","zh":"言辭激烈的家長可能在學校會議上非常強硬地發言。"},{"en":"If someone sounds strident, their tone may be difficult but their point may still matter.","zh":"如果某人聽起來言辭激烈，其語氣可能難接受，但觀點仍可能重要。"},{"en":"The word describes manner of expression, not whether the person is right.","zh":"這個詞描述表達方式，而不是此人是否正確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"after all","meaning":"畢竟","examples":[{"en":"A difficult person may be right, after all.","zh":"難相處的人畢竟可能是對的。"},{"en":"After all means despite what was first thought, this may still be true.","zh":"畢竟，指儘管起初有其他想法，這仍可能是真的。"},{"en":"A quiet student’s answer may be correct, after all, even if others disagree.","zh":"即使其他人不同意，安靜學生的答案畢竟可能是正確的。"},{"en":"If a difficult critic notices a real problem, managers should not ignore them.","zh":"如果難相處的批評者注意到真正問題，管理者不應忽視他們。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a reminder or reconsideration.","zh":"這個短語引入提醒或重新考慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"concur with","meaning":"同意；認同","examples":[{"en":"A useful strategy is to concur with what is factually accurate.","zh":"一個有用策略是認同事實上準確的內容。"},{"en":"To concur with something means to agree with it.","zh":"認同某事，指同意它。"},{"en":"A teacher may concur with a student’s point even if the full essay is weak.","zh":"即使整篇文章薄弱，老師仍可能認同學生某個觀點。"},{"en":"If managers agree with accurate concerns, people may feel heard.","zh":"如果管理者同意準確憂慮，人們可能感到被聽見。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and means agree.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"factually accurate","meaning":"事實上準確的","examples":[{"en":"Change agents should agree with what is factually accurate.","zh":"變革推動者應同意事實上準確的內容。"},{"en":"Factually accurate means correct according to facts, not just feelings or opinions.","zh":"事實上準確的，指根據事實正確，而不只是感受或意見。"},{"en":"If a student says the deadline is Friday and the notice confirms it, the statement is factually accurate.","zh":"如果學生說截止日期是星期五，而通告確認了，該陳述就是事實上準確的。"},{"en":"Agreeing with accurate details builds trust even during disagreement.","zh":"即使有分歧，同意準確細節也能建立信任。"},{"en":"The phrase separates facts from emotion.","zh":"這個短語把事實與情緒分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"find it difficult to argue with","meaning":"覺得難以與……爭辯","examples":[{"en":"People find it difficult to argue with those who agree with them.","zh":"人們覺得難以與同意自己的人爭辯。"},{"en":"To find it difficult to argue with someone means to have less reason or ability to fight their point.","zh":"覺得難以與某人爭辯，指較少理由或能力反駁其觀點。"},{"en":"A student may find it difficult to argue with feedback that first recognises their effort.","zh":"如果回饋先承認學生努力，學生可能較難與之爭辯。"},{"en":"If managers agree with true concerns, resistance may become softer.","zh":"如果管理者同意真實憂慮，抗拒可能變得較柔和。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how agreement can reduce defensiveness.","zh":"這個短語顯示同意如何減少防衛心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"resistance is reduced","meaning":"抗拒被減少","examples":[{"en":"Resistance is reduced when people feel heard.","zh":"當人們感到被聽見，抗拒會減少。"},{"en":"If resistance is reduced, opposition becomes weaker or less intense.","zh":"如果抗拒被減少，反對就變得較弱或較不激烈。"},{"en":"Students may resist a new rule less when the teacher explains the reason clearly.","zh":"當老師清楚解釋原因，學生可能較少抗拒新規則。"},{"en":"If people feel respected, they may still disagree but become less hostile.","zh":"如果人們感到被尊重，他們可能仍不同意，但敵意較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes opposition being lowered.","zh":"這個短語描述反對程度下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"communication is enhanced","meaning":"溝通得到加強","examples":[{"en":"Communication is enhanced when agreement is acknowledged.","zh":"當認同被承認時，溝通會得到加強。"},{"en":"If communication is enhanced, people share information and understand one another better.","zh":"如果溝通得到加強，人們更好地分享資料和理解彼此。"},{"en":"In class, communication is enhanced when students are allowed to ask questions.","zh":"在課堂中，當學生被允許發問，溝通會得到加強。"},{"en":"If both sides recognise accurate points, discussion becomes more open.","zh":"如果雙方承認準確觀點，討論會變得更開放。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improved communication.","zh":"這個短語描述溝通改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"insights into the situation","meaning":"對情況的深入理解","examples":[{"en":"Insights into the situation will emerge through better communication.","zh":"透過更好溝通，對情況的深入理解會出現。"},{"en":"Insights into the situation are deeper understandings of what is really happening.","zh":"對情況的深入理解，是對真正發生事情的更深認識。"},{"en":"A teacher may gain insights into a class problem by talking privately with students.","zh":"老師可能透過私下與學生談話，獲得對班級問題的深入理解。"},{"en":"If communication improves, hidden fears and practical problems may become clear.","zh":"如果溝通改善，隱藏恐懼和實際問題可能變得清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to deeper understanding of a specific context.","zh":"這個短語指對特定語境的更深理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"will emerge","meaning":"會浮現；會出現","examples":[{"en":"Useful insights will emerge when communication improves.","zh":"當溝通改善，有用見解會浮現。"},{"en":"Will emerge means will appear, become clear, or become known.","zh":"會浮現，指會出現、變清楚或變得為人所知。"},{"en":"New problems may emerge after a school changes its timetable.","zh":"學校更改時間表後，新問題可能會出現。"},{"en":"If people speak honestly, hidden concerns may emerge.","zh":"如果人們誠實發言，隱藏憂慮可能浮現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something becoming visible or known.","zh":"這個短語描述某事變得可見或為人所知。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"remind themselves of","meaning":"提醒自己……","examples":[{"en":"Change agents should remind themselves of two basic facts.","zh":"變革推動者應提醒自己兩個基本事實。"},{"en":"To remind themselves of something means to make themselves remember it again.","zh":"提醒自己某事，指令自己再次記起它。"},{"en":"Students should remind themselves of the marking criteria before writing an essay.","zh":"學生寫作文前應提醒自己評分準則。"},{"en":"If managers remember human limits, they may handle conflict more patiently.","zh":"如果管理者記住人的限制，就可能更有耐性地處理衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deliberate remembering.","zh":"這個短語描述有意識地記住。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"complete rationality","meaning":"完全理性","examples":[{"en":"Change agents should not expect complete rationality from others.","zh":"變革推動者不應期望他人完全理性。"},{"en":"Complete rationality means perfect logical thinking without emotion, bias, or weakness.","zh":"完全理性，指沒有情緒、偏見或弱點的完美邏輯思考。"},{"en":"It is unrealistic to expect complete rationality from students during a stressful exam.","zh":"在壓力大的考試中期望學生完全理性是不現實的。"},{"en":"If people feel threatened, their reactions may not be fully logical.","zh":"如果人們感到受威脅，其反應未必完全合乎邏輯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an ideal that humans rarely reach.","zh":"這個短語描述人類很少達到的理想狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at all times","meaning":"在任何時候","examples":[{"en":"People do not show complete rationality at all times.","zh":"人們不會在任何時候都表現出完全理性。"},{"en":"At all times means always, without exception.","zh":"在任何時候，指永遠、沒有例外。"},{"en":"A teacher cannot watch every student at all times during a large school event.","zh":"在大型學校活動中，老師不能在任何時候都看着每個學生。"},{"en":"If humans are not rational at all times, managers should expect emotional reactions.","zh":"如果人類不是任何時候都理性，管理者就應預期情緒反應。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses continuous and total consistency.","zh":"這個短語強調持續且完全一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ideal behaviour","meaning":"理想行為","examples":[{"en":"Expecting ideal behaviour from people is itself irrational.","zh":"期望人們有理想行為本身就是不理性的。"},{"en":"Ideal behaviour means perfect behaviour that matches what people should do in theory.","zh":"理想行為，指在理論上完全符合應做之事的完美行為。"},{"en":"In group work, ideal behaviour would include listening, sharing tasks, and meeting deadlines.","zh":"在小組工作中，理想行為包括聆聽、分工和遵守限期。"},{"en":"If managers expect perfect behaviour from stressed workers, they may misunderstand reality.","zh":"如果管理者期望受壓員工有完美行為，可能誤解現實。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a standard that may be too perfect for real life.","zh":"這個短語描述對現實生活可能太完美的標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"itself irrational","meaning":"本身就是不理性的","examples":[{"en":"Expecting perfect rationality is itself irrational.","zh":"期望完美理性本身就是不理性的。"},{"en":"Itself irrational means the expectation or action is unreasonable in its own nature.","zh":"本身就是不理性的，指該期望或行動本質上不合理。"},{"en":"Demanding that students never feel nervous is itself irrational.","zh":"要求學生永遠不緊張，本身就是不理性的。"},{"en":"If humans naturally have emotions, expecting emotionless decisions is not reasonable.","zh":"如果人類天然有情緒，期望無情緒決策並不合理。"},{"en":"The phrase turns criticism back onto the expectation itself.","zh":"這個短語把批評轉回期望本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"resign oneself to","meaning":"接受；認命於","examples":[{"en":"Managers must resign themselves to the inevitability of human failings.","zh":"管理者必須接受人性弱點的不可避免性。"},{"en":"To resign oneself to something means to accept something unpleasant because it cannot be avoided.","zh":"接受某事，指因無法避免而接受令人不快的事情。"},{"en":"A student may resign herself to retaking a test after missing the deadline.","zh":"學生錯過限期後，可能只好接受重考。"},{"en":"If managers accept that people are imperfect, conflict becomes easier to manage.","zh":"如果管理者接受人並不完美，衝突就較容易管理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reluctant acceptance.","zh":"這個短語描述不情願但必要的接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the inevitability of","meaning":"……的不可避免性","examples":[{"en":"Accepting the inevitability of human failings makes conflict manageable.","zh":"接受人性弱點的不可避免性，會令衝突較易管理。"},{"en":"The inevitability of something means the fact that it cannot be avoided.","zh":"某事的不可避免性，指它無法避免這一事實。"},{"en":"Students must accept the inevitability of mistakes when learning a new language.","zh":"學生學習新語言時，必須接受錯誤的不可避免性。"},{"en":"If human weakness cannot be avoided, systems should be designed to manage it.","zh":"如果人性弱點無法避免，制度就應被設計來管理它。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses unavoidable reality.","zh":"這個短語強調不可避免的現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"human failings","meaning":"人性的弱點；人的缺點","examples":[{"en":"Human failings make conflict unavoidable.","zh":"人性的弱點令衝突不可避免。"},{"en":"Human failings are weaknesses in people, such as fear, pride, bias, or impatience.","zh":"人性的弱點，是人的弱處，例如恐懼、驕傲、偏見或缺乏耐性。"},{"en":"A team may struggle because of human failings like jealousy or poor listening.","zh":"團隊可能因嫉妒或不善聆聽等人性弱點而陷入困難。"},{"en":"If managers expect human failings, they can design better communication systems.","zh":"如果管理者預期人性弱點，就可以設計更好的溝通系統。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to ordinary imperfections in people.","zh":"這個短語指人的普通不完美。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"more manageable","meaning":"較易管理","examples":[{"en":"Conflict becomes more manageable when human failings are expected.","zh":"當人性弱點被預期，衝突會變得較易管理。"},{"en":"More manageable means easier to control, handle, or deal with.","zh":"較易管理，指較容易控制、處理或應對。"},{"en":"A large project becomes more manageable when it is divided into smaller tasks.","zh":"大型項目被分成較小任務後，會變得較易管理。"},{"en":"If managers expect emotional reactions, they can prepare for them calmly.","zh":"如果管理者預期情緒反應，就可以冷靜準備。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something becoming easier to handle.","zh":"這個短語描述某事變得更容易處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"human beliefs","meaning":"人的信念","examples":[{"en":"Human beliefs are not necessarily encapsulations of the truth.","zh":"人的信念不一定是真理的體現。"},{"en":"Human beliefs are ideas people hold about themselves, others, or the world.","zh":"人的信念，是人們對自己、他人或世界持有的想法。"},{"en":"A student may believe they are bad at English even after improving.","zh":"即使進步後，學生仍可能相信自己英文差。"},{"en":"If beliefs protect people’s self-image, they may resist facts that threaten them.","zh":"如果信念保護人的自我形象，他們可能抗拒威脅它們的事實。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what people believe, not always what is true.","zh":"這個短語指人們相信的東西，而不一定是真相。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"not necessarily","meaning":"不一定","examples":[{"en":"Beliefs are not necessarily the same as truth.","zh":"信念不一定等同真相。"},{"en":"Not necessarily means not always or not in every case.","zh":"不一定，指不是總是如此或不是每種情況都如此。"},{"en":"A quiet student is not necessarily bored; they may be thinking carefully.","zh":"安靜學生不一定覺得沉悶；他可能正在仔細思考。"},{"en":"If something feels true, it is not necessarily supported by evidence.","zh":"如果某事感覺真實，它不一定有證據支持。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against automatic assumptions.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要自動假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"encapsulations of the truth","meaning":"真理的體現","examples":[{"en":"Human beliefs are not necessarily encapsulations of the truth.","zh":"人的信念不一定是真理的體現。"},{"en":"Encapsulations of the truth are statements or beliefs that perfectly contain what is real.","zh":"真理的體現，是完美包含現實的陳述或信念。"},{"en":"A rumour may feel convincing, but it is not an encapsulation of the truth.","zh":"謠言可能感覺可信，但它不是真理的體現。"},{"en":"If beliefs are shaped by fear or pride, they may protect the self more than reflect reality.","zh":"如果信念由恐懼或驕傲塑造，它們可能更保護自我，而不是反映現實。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and means complete expressions of truth.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是完整表達真相。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"constructions of the mind","meaning":"心智建構出來的東西","examples":[{"en":"Beliefs are often constructions of the mind.","zh":"信念往往是心智建構出來的東西。"},{"en":"Constructions of the mind are ideas created by thought, memory, fear, or interpretation.","zh":"心智建構出來的東西，是由思想、記憶、恐懼或解讀創造的想法。"},{"en":"A student’s belief that “everyone is judging me” may be a construction of the mind.","zh":"學生相信「所有人都在評判我」，可能是心智建構出來的想法。"},{"en":"If beliefs are mentally constructed, they can feel real without being fully true.","zh":"如果信念由心智建構，它們可以感覺真實，但不完全為真。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ideas made inside the mind.","zh":"這個短語描述在腦海中製造出來的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"serve to maximise","meaning":"用以最大化……","examples":[{"en":"Beliefs may serve to maximise the security of the self.","zh":"信念可能用以最大化自我安全感。"},{"en":"To serve to maximise something means to function in a way that increases it as much as possible.","zh":"用以最大化某事，指以某種方式運作，使它盡可能增加。"},{"en":"A strict timetable may serve to maximise study efficiency before exams.","zh":"嚴格時間表可能用以最大化考試前的學習效率。"},{"en":"If a belief protects someone’s self-image, it may make them feel safer.","zh":"如果信念保護某人的自我形象，它可能令他感到更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the function or purpose of something.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事的功能或目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the security of the self","meaning":"自我安全感","examples":[{"en":"People may construct beliefs to maximise the security of the self.","zh":"人們可能建構信念以最大化自我安全感。"},{"en":"The security of the self means a person’s feeling that their identity, worth, and safety are protected.","zh":"自我安全感，指一個人感到自己的身份、價值和安全受到保護。"},{"en":"A student may avoid feedback because criticism threatens the security of the self.","zh":"學生可能避免回饋，因為批評威脅自我安全感。"},{"en":"If change challenges who people think they are, they may defend old beliefs.","zh":"如果變化挑戰人們對自己的看法，他們可能捍衛舊信念。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to psychological safety around identity.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞身份的心理安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"encounter difficulties in","meaning":"在……方面遇到困難","examples":[{"en":"Change agents may encounter difficulties in implementing change.","zh":"變革推動者在推行變革方面可能遇到困難。"},{"en":"To encounter difficulties in something means to face problems while doing it.","zh":"在某事方面遇到困難，指做該事時面對問題。"},{"en":"Students may encounter difficulties in writing essays if they lack examples.","zh":"如果學生缺乏例子，可能在寫作文方面遇到困難。"},{"en":"If workers resist a new system, managers may struggle to introduce it.","zh":"如果員工抗拒新系統，管理者可能難以引入它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes problems met during a task.","zh":"這個短語描述任務中遇到的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"implementing change","meaning":"推行變革","examples":[{"en":"Managers often face resistance when implementing change.","zh":"管理者在推行變革時常面對抗拒。"},{"en":"Implementing change means putting a new plan, system, or policy into practice.","zh":"推行變革，指把新計劃、系統或政策付諸實行。"},{"en":"A school implements change when it replaces paper homework with an online platform.","zh":"當學校用網上平台取代紙本功課時，就是推行變革。"},{"en":"If implementation is rushed, people may feel confused and resist.","zh":"如果推行過急，人們可能感到混亂並抗拒。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on carrying out change, not just planning it.","zh":"這個短語強調執行變革，而不只是規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"there is a good chance that","meaning":"很有可能","examples":[{"en":"There is a good chance that stakeholders are protecting their beliefs.","zh":"很有可能持份者正在保護自己的信念。"},{"en":"There is a good chance that means it is quite likely that something is true or will happen.","zh":"很有可能，指某事相當可能是真的或會發生。"},{"en":"If a student has not slept, there is a good chance that they will lose focus.","zh":"如果學生沒有睡覺，很有可能會失去專注力。"},{"en":"If people strongly resist change, they may be defending something important to them.","zh":"如果人們強烈抗拒變革，他們可能在保護對自己重要的東西。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses a strong possibility.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"stakeholders","meaning":"持份者","examples":[{"en":"Stakeholders may protect beliefs that give them security.","zh":"持份者可能保護令他們有安全感的信念。"},{"en":"Stakeholders are people or groups affected by a decision or able to influence it.","zh":"持份者，是受某決定影響或能影響該決定的人或群體。"},{"en":"In a school reform, stakeholders include students, parents, teachers, and administrators.","zh":"在學校改革中，持份者包括學生、家長、老師和行政人員。"},{"en":"If stakeholders are ignored, they may resist even useful changes.","zh":"如果持份者被忽視，即使有用變革也可能遭抗拒。"},{"en":"The word refers to people with an interest in the outcome.","zh":"這個詞指對結果有利益或關注的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take into account","meaning":"考慮到","examples":[{"en":"Change agents should take these beliefs into account.","zh":"變革推動者應考慮到這些信念。"},{"en":"To take something into account means to consider it before deciding or acting.","zh":"考慮到某事，指在決定或行動前把它納入考量。"},{"en":"A teacher should take students’ workload into account before setting homework.","zh":"老師設定功課前應考慮到學生工作量。"},{"en":"If beliefs shape resistance, managers must consider them during change.","zh":"如果信念塑造抗拒，管理者在變革中必須考慮它們。"},{"en":"The phrase means include a factor in thinking.","zh":"這個短語指把某因素納入思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"experienced change agent","meaning":"有經驗的變革推動者","examples":[{"en":"An experienced change agent examines everyone’s perspective.","zh":"有經驗的變革推動者會審視每個人的觀點。"},{"en":"An experienced change agent is someone skilled at leading or supporting change because they have done it before.","zh":"有經驗的變革推動者，是因過往做過而擅長領導或支援變革的人。"},{"en":"An experienced principal may guide a school through curriculum reform more calmly.","zh":"有經驗的校長可能更冷靜地帶領學校進行課程改革。"},{"en":"If a change agent has experience, they know resistance may contain useful information.","zh":"如果變革推動者有經驗，就知道抗拒可能包含有用資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase combines change leadership with practical experience.","zh":"這個短語把變革領導與實際經驗結合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"perspective needs to be examined","meaning":"觀點需要被審視","examples":[{"en":"Everyone’s perspective needs to be examined with an open mind.","zh":"每個人的觀點都需要以開放心態被審視。"},{"en":"If a perspective needs to be examined, it should be considered carefully instead of dismissed quickly.","zh":"如果某觀點需要被審視，就應被仔細考慮，而不是很快否定。"},{"en":"A teacher should examine a student’s perspective before judging why homework is late.","zh":"老師判斷學生為何遲交功課前，應審視學生的觀點。"},{"en":"If different perspectives are examined, hidden causes of resistance may become clear.","zh":"如果不同觀點被審視，抗拒的隱藏原因可能變得清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses careful consideration of viewpoints.","zh":"這個短語強調仔細考慮觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"with an open mind","meaning":"以開放的心態","examples":[{"en":"A change agent should examine viewpoints with an open mind.","zh":"變革推動者應以開放的心態審視觀點。"},{"en":"With an open mind means being willing to consider new or different ideas fairly.","zh":"以開放的心態，指願意公平考慮新想法或不同想法。"},{"en":"Students should read opposing arguments with an open mind before writing an essay.","zh":"學生寫作文前，應以開放心態閱讀相反論點。"},{"en":"If managers listen openly, they may discover that resistance is reasonable.","zh":"如果管理者開放地聆聽，可能發現抗拒是合理的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fair and flexible thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述公平而有彈性的思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"conflicting viewpoints","meaning":"互相衝突的觀點","examples":[{"en":"Conflicting viewpoints should be promoted in a healthy way.","zh":"互相衝突的觀點應以健康方式被鼓勵。"},{"en":"Conflicting viewpoints are opinions that disagree with one another.","zh":"互相衝突的觀點，是彼此不同意的意見。"},{"en":"In a debate, students present conflicting viewpoints on whether homework should be reduced.","zh":"在辯論中，學生就是否應減少功課提出互相衝突的觀點。"},{"en":"If conflicting views are discussed respectfully, a group may reach a better decision.","zh":"如果衝突觀點被尊重地討論，小組可能作出更好決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes disagreement in ideas.","zh":"這個短語描述想法上的分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be promoted in a healthy way","meaning":"以健康方式被鼓勵","examples":[{"en":"Conflict should be promoted in a healthy way.","zh":"衝突應以健康方式被鼓勵。"},{"en":"To be promoted in a healthy way means to be encouraged safely, respectfully, and productively.","zh":"以健康方式被鼓勵，指以安全、尊重和有成效的方式被推動。"},{"en":"Class debate can be promoted in a healthy way if students criticise ideas, not people.","zh":"如果學生批評想法而不是人，課堂辯論就可以以健康方式被鼓勵。"},{"en":"If conflict is encouraged without respect, it may become destructive.","zh":"如果鼓勵衝突但沒有尊重，它可能變成破壞性。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that encouragement needs limits and rules.","zh":"這個短語顯示鼓勵需要界限和規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be disarmed","meaning":"放下戒心；被消除敵意","examples":[{"en":"People should be disarmed before discussing conflict.","zh":"人們在討論衝突前應先放下戒心。"},{"en":"To be disarmed means to become less defensive, hostile, or ready to fight.","zh":"放下戒心或被消除敵意，指變得較少防衛、敵意或準備爭鬥。"},{"en":"A sincere apology can disarm an angry customer.","zh":"真誠道歉可以令憤怒顧客放下戒心。"},{"en":"If people feel respected first, they may discuss conflict more calmly.","zh":"如果人們先感到被尊重，可能更冷靜討論衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reducing emotional defensiveness.","zh":"這個短語描述減少情緒防衛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"react as a result of","meaning":"因……而反應","examples":[{"en":"People may react as a result of ill-feeling or malice.","zh":"人們可能因惡感或惡意而反應。"},{"en":"To react as a result of something means to respond because that cause is influencing them.","zh":"因某事而反應，指因該原因正在影響他們而作出回應。"},{"en":"A student may react angrily as a result of embarrassment.","zh":"學生可能因尷尬而憤怒反應。"},{"en":"If people react from hurt feelings, the discussion may become less rational.","zh":"如果人們出於受傷感受而反應，討論可能變得較不理性。"},{"en":"The phrase links behaviour with its emotional cause.","zh":"這個短語把行為與其情緒原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"ill-feeling or malice","meaning":"惡感或惡意","examples":[{"en":"Ill-feeling or malice can produce unhealthy conflict.","zh":"惡感或惡意可以產生不健康的衝突。"},{"en":"Ill-feeling or malice means resentment, hostility, or a wish to harm someone.","zh":"惡感或惡意，指怨氣、敵意或想傷害某人的意圖。"},{"en":"A team project can suffer if members act from ill-feeling rather than fairness.","zh":"如果成員出於惡感而非公平行事，小組項目可能受損。"},{"en":"If disagreement becomes personal and malicious, it stops helping decision-making.","zh":"如果分歧變成人身和惡意，它就不再幫助決策。"},{"en":"The phrase describes harmful emotions behind conflict.","zh":"這個短語描述衝突背後的有害情緒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"emotions emerge","meaning":"情緒浮現","examples":[{"en":"When such emotions emerge, they need to be understood.","zh":"當這些情緒浮現時，它們需要被理解。"},{"en":"When emotions emerge, feelings appear or become clear in people’s words or actions.","zh":"情緒浮現時，感受會在人們的說話或行動中出現或變清楚。"},{"en":"In a class discussion, anger may emerge when students feel treated unfairly.","zh":"在課堂討論中，當學生覺得被不公平對待，憤怒可能浮現。"},{"en":"If emotions emerge during change, managers should not ignore them.","zh":"如果情緒在變革中浮現，管理者不應忽視它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes feelings becoming visible.","zh":"這個短語描述感受變得可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"understand where they come from","meaning":"理解它們從何而來","examples":[{"en":"Managers should understand where emotional reactions come from.","zh":"管理者應理解情緒反應從何而來。"},{"en":"To understand where they come from means to identify the cause or background of those feelings.","zh":"理解它們從何而來，指識別那些感受的原因或背景。"},{"en":"A teacher should understand where a student’s anger comes from before punishing them.","zh":"老師懲罰學生前，應理解學生憤怒從何而來。"},{"en":"If fear comes from job insecurity, managers can address that concern directly.","zh":"如果恐懼來自工作不穩定，管理者就可以直接處理該憂慮。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on finding the source of a reaction.","zh":"這個短語強調找出反應來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"how to handle them","meaning":"如何處理它們","examples":[{"en":"Change agents need to know how to handle emotional reactions.","zh":"變革推動者需要知道如何處理情緒反應。"},{"en":"How to handle them means how to manage or deal with them effectively.","zh":"如何處理它們，指如何有效管理或應對它們。"},{"en":"A teacher needs to know how to handle students who panic before exams.","zh":"老師需要知道如何處理考試前恐慌的學生。"},{"en":"If emotions are handled badly, conflict may become more intense.","zh":"如果情緒處理不善，衝突可能變得更激烈。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on practical management.","zh":"這個短語強調實際管理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"constructive rather than destructive paths","meaning":"建設性而非破壞性的路線","examples":[{"en":"Managers should follow constructive rather than destructive paths.","zh":"管理者應遵循建設性而非破壞性的路線。"},{"en":"Constructive rather than destructive paths are ways of acting that build improvement instead of causing damage.","zh":"建設性而非破壞性的路線，是帶來改善而不是造成損害的行動方式。"},{"en":"In a disagreement, asking questions is more constructive than insulting classmates.","zh":"在分歧中，發問比侮辱同學更具建設性。"},{"en":"If conflict is channelled into problem-solving, it helps instead of harms.","zh":"如果衝突被引導至解決問題，它就會幫助而非傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts helpful action with damaging action.","zh":"這個短語把有幫助的行動與有破壞性的行動作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"certainly possible","meaning":"絕對可能","examples":[{"en":"Managing conflict well is not easy, but it is certainly possible.","zh":"好好管理衝突並不容易，但絕對可能。"},{"en":"Certainly possible means definitely achievable, even if it is difficult.","zh":"絕對可能，指即使困難，也肯定可以達成。"},{"en":"Improving speaking in six months is certainly possible with regular practice.","zh":"只要定期練習，六個月內改善口語絕對可能。"},{"en":"If managers use listening, fairness, and structure, conflict can be handled better.","zh":"如果管理者使用聆聽、公平和結構，衝突可以被處理得更好。"},{"en":"The phrase gives realistic encouragement.","zh":"這個短語給出現實的鼓勵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生為每條問題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the option letter that matches the answer.","zh":"選出正確字母，指選擇符合答案的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice question, students may choose A, B, C, or D.","zh":"在選擇題中，學生可能選 A、B、C 或 D。"},{"en":"If students understand the passage evidence, they can choose more accurately.","zh":"如果學生理解文章證據，就能更準確選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be similar to","meaning":"與……相似","examples":[{"en":"Organisations are similar to living things.","zh":"組織與生物相似。"},{"en":"To be similar to something means to share some important features with it.","zh":"與某物相似，指與它共享一些重要特徵。"},{"en":"A classroom is similar to a workplace because both need rules and cooperation.","zh":"課室與工作場所相似，因為兩者都需要規則和合作。"},{"en":"If organisations grow and decline, they are similar to organisms in that way.","zh":"如果組織會成長和衰退，它們在這方面與生物相似。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces comparison.","zh":"這個短語引入比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"living things","meaning":"生物；有生命的東西","examples":[{"en":"The passage compares organisations to living things.","zh":"文章把組織比作生物。"},{"en":"Living things are organisms that grow, need resources, respond to surroundings, and may die.","zh":"生物是會成長、需要資源、回應環境並可能死亡的有生命東西。"},{"en":"Plants, animals, and humans are living things.","zh":"植物、動物和人類都是生物。"},{"en":"If an organisation behaves like a living thing, it must adapt to its environment.","zh":"如果組織像生物一樣運作，就必須適應環境。"},{"en":"The phrase supports a biological comparison.","zh":"這個短語支援生物學比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"come and go","meaning":"來來去去；時有時無","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that conflict may come and go.","zh":"該選項暗示衝突可能時有時無。"},{"en":"To come and go means to appear for a time and then disappear again.","zh":"來來去去，指出現一段時間後又消失。"},{"en":"A headache may come and go during a stressful week.","zh":"在壓力大的一週，頭痛可能時有時無。"},{"en":"If conflict comes and goes, it may not stay constant but can return.","zh":"如果衝突時有時無，它可能不是一直存在，但會再回來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something temporary or repeated.","zh":"這個短語描述暫時或反覆出現的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"lead to wrong decisions","meaning":"導致錯誤決定","examples":[{"en":"Groupthink can lead to wrong decisions.","zh":"群體迷思可以導致錯誤決定。"},{"en":"To lead to wrong decisions means to cause people to choose badly or inaccurately.","zh":"導致錯誤決定，指令人作出差劣或不準確的選擇。"},{"en":"Copying a friend’s answer without checking can lead to wrong decisions in a test.","zh":"在測驗中不檢查就抄朋友答案，可能導致錯誤決定。"},{"en":"If nobody challenges weak ideas, the group may choose the wrong plan.","zh":"如果沒有人挑戰薄弱想法，小組可能選錯計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a harmful result of poor thinking.","zh":"這個短語顯示思考不佳的有害結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"warning sign","meaning":"警號","examples":[{"en":"Very little conflict can be a warning sign.","zh":"很少衝突可以是一個警號。"},{"en":"A warning sign is something that shows a possible problem before it becomes worse.","zh":"警號是在問題變得更嚴重前顯示可能有問題的跡象。"},{"en":"Falling attendance is a warning sign that a club may be losing members’ interest.","zh":"出席率下降是一個警號，顯示學會可能正在失去成員興趣。"},{"en":"If nobody speaks up in meetings, managers should ask whether people feel unsafe.","zh":"如果會議中沒有人發聲，管理者應問人們是否感到不安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an early signal of danger or weakness.","zh":"這個短語描述危險或弱點的早期信號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete the flow chart","meaning":"完成流程圖","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the flow chart using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成流程圖。"},{"en":"To complete the flow chart means to fill in missing steps or labels in a process diagram.","zh":"完成流程圖，指填寫過程圖中缺失的步驟或標籤。"},{"en":"Students may complete a flow chart showing how a complaint becomes a policy change.","zh":"學生可能完成一個展示投訴如何變成政策改變的流程圖。"},{"en":"If the chart shows causes and results, each answer must fit the sequence.","zh":"如果圖表顯示原因和結果，每個答案都必須符合次序。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個詞","examples":[{"en":"The answer should use no more than three words from the passage.","zh":"答案應使用文章中不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"不多於三個詞，指答案必須包含三個詞或以下。"},{"en":"“staff involvement” is acceptable, but a long sentence is not.","zh":"“staff involvement” 可以接受，但完整長句不可以。"},{"en":"If students write four words, the answer may be marked wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"如果學生寫四個詞，即使意思正確，答案也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"answer the questions","meaning":"回答問題","examples":[{"en":"Students answer the questions using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞回答問題。"},{"en":"To answer the questions means to provide the required responses to the task.","zh":"回答問題，指提供題目所要求的答案。"},{"en":"In reading practice, students should answer the questions only after finding evidence.","zh":"在閱讀練習中，學生應先找到證據才回答問題。"},{"en":"If the answer must use passage words, invented synonyms may be wrong.","zh":"如果答案必須使用文章字詞，自創同義詞可能錯。"},{"en":"The phrase is a general exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是一般考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"even rational people","meaning":"即使是理性的人","examples":[{"en":"Even rational people can produce resistance and conflict.","zh":"即使是理性的人也可以產生抗拒和衝突。"},{"en":"Even rational people means people who think logically can still do this unexpected thing.","zh":"即使是理性的人，指連邏輯思考的人也仍會做出這種意外事情。"},{"en":"Even rational students may panic when an exam starts unexpectedly.","zh":"即使是理性的學生，當考試突然開始時也可能恐慌。"},{"en":"If sensible workers resist change, their reasons should be examined.","zh":"如果明智員工抗拒變革，其理由應被審視。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that resistance is not limited to unreasonable people.","zh":"這個短語強調抗拒不限於不理性的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"what sort of information","meaning":"哪一類資料","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what sort of information a change agent should agree with.","zh":"題目問變革推動者應同意哪一類資料。"},{"en":"What sort of information means what kind or type of information.","zh":"哪一類資料，指甚麼種類或類型的資料。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask what sort of information students need before writing a report.","zh":"老師可能問學生寫報告前需要哪一類資料。"},{"en":"If the information is factually accurate, agreeing with it may reduce resistance.","zh":"如果資料事實上準確，同意它可能減少抗拒。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for a category, not a full explanation.","zh":"這個短語問的是類別，而不是完整解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agree with","meaning":"同意；認同","examples":[{"en":"A change agent should agree with factually accurate information.","zh":"變革推動者應同意事實上準確的資料。"},{"en":"To agree with something means to accept that it is true, right, or reasonable.","zh":"同意某事，指接受它是真的、正確或合理。"},{"en":"A teacher may agree with a student’s example but not their conclusion.","zh":"老師可能同意學生的例子，但不同意其結論。"},{"en":"If managers agree with accurate points, workers may feel respected.","zh":"如果管理者認同準確觀點，員工可能感到被尊重。"},{"en":"The phrase describes acceptance of an idea or statement.","zh":"這個短語描述接受某個想法或陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"what quality","meaning":"哪種特質","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what quality does not constantly come from people.","zh":"題目問哪種特質不會持續來自人們。"},{"en":"What quality means what characteristic or feature.","zh":"哪種特質，指甚麼特徵或特點。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask what quality makes a good leader trustworthy.","zh":"老師可能問哪種特質令好領袖值得信任。"},{"en":"If the answer is “complete rationality,” students must find that exact idea in the passage.","zh":"如果答案是「完全理性」，學生必須在文章中找到該準確想法。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for a specific characteristic.","zh":"這個短語詢問特定特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"constantly come from people","meaning":"持續來自人們","examples":[{"en":"Complete rationality does not constantly come from people.","zh":"完全理性不會持續來自人們。"},{"en":"To constantly come from people means to appear from people all the time without interruption.","zh":"持續來自人們，指一直不中斷地由人表現出來。"},{"en":"Perfect patience does not constantly come from teachers because they are human too.","zh":"完美耐性不會持續來自老師，因為他們也是人。"},{"en":"If rationality does not always appear, emotional reactions should be expected.","zh":"如果理性不總是出現，就應預期情緒反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something being produced consistently by people.","zh":"這個短語描述某事由人持續產生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"construct beliefs","meaning":"建構信念","examples":[{"en":"People often construct beliefs to protect themselves.","zh":"人們常建構信念來保護自己。"},{"en":"To construct beliefs means to build ideas in the mind about what is true or safe.","zh":"建構信念，指在心中建立關於甚麼是真實或安全的想法。"},{"en":"A student may construct the belief that they are “bad at speaking” after one embarrassing moment.","zh":"學生可能在一次尷尬經歷後建構「自己不擅長口語」的信念。"},{"en":"If beliefs protect self-esteem, people may resist evidence that challenges them.","zh":"如果信念保護自尊，人們可能抗拒挑戰它們的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mental building of beliefs.","zh":"這個短語描述在心中建立信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"enhance a feeling","meaning":"增強某種感覺","examples":[{"en":"Beliefs may enhance a feeling of security.","zh":"信念可能增強安全感。"},{"en":"To enhance a feeling means to make that feeling stronger.","zh":"增強某種感覺，指令該感覺變得更強。"},{"en":"Clear instructions can enhance a feeling of safety during a school trip.","zh":"清楚指示可以在學校旅行中增強安全感。"},{"en":"If a belief makes someone feel protected, they may hold onto it tightly.","zh":"如果某信念令某人感到受保護，他們可能緊抓着它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strengthening an emotion or sense.","zh":"這個短語描述加強情緒或感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"unhealthy conflict","meaning":"不健康的衝突","examples":[{"en":"Ill-feeling and malice can produce unhealthy conflict.","zh":"惡感和惡意可以產生不健康的衝突。"},{"en":"Unhealthy conflict is disagreement that damages relationships, decisions, or progress.","zh":"不健康的衝突，是損害關係、決策或進展的分歧。"},{"en":"A group project has unhealthy conflict when members insult one another instead of solving the task.","zh":"當小組成員互相侮辱而不是解決任務，項目就有不健康的衝突。"},{"en":"If conflict comes from malice, it is less likely to improve decisions.","zh":"如果衝突來自惡意，它較不可能改善決策。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts harmful conflict with constructive disagreement.","zh":"這個短語把有害衝突與建設性分歧作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 89 - Organisational Conflict and Change.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 90":[{"front":"the mother of all languages","meaning":"所有語言之母","examples":[{"en":"The passage explores the idea of the mother of all languages.","zh":"文章探討所有語言之母這個想法。"},{"en":"The mother of all languages means the original language from which all later languages may have developed.","zh":"the mother of all languages 指所有後來語言可能由其發展而來的最原始語言。"},{"en":"A teacher may call Latin the mother of many European languages, but not the mother of all languages.","zh":"老師可能稱拉丁語為許多歐洲語言之母，但不是所有語言之母。"},{"en":"If many languages share one ancient source, linguists may search for that source as a mother language.","zh":"如果許多語言共享同一古老源頭，語言學家可能會尋找那個源頭作為母語。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing the deepest possible origin of human speech.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論人類語言最深層的可能起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be stationed in","meaning":"被派駐於……","examples":[{"en":"William Jones was a British judge stationed in India.","zh":"William Jones 是一名被派駐於印度的英國法官。"},{"en":"To be stationed in a place means to be officially sent to work or serve there.","zh":"be stationed in a place 指被正式派往某地工作或服務。"},{"en":"A police officer may be stationed in a busy district during a public event.","zh":"警員可能在公眾活動期間被派駐於繁忙地區。"},{"en":"If a government worker is stationed abroad, they may learn local languages and customs.","zh":"如果政府人員被派駐海外，他們可能學習當地語言和習俗。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for judges, soldiers, diplomats, or officials posted somewhere.","zh":"這個片語常用於法官、士兵、外交官或官員被派往某地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be ranked as","meaning":"被列為","examples":[{"en":"Jones made what must be ranked as one of the most amazing discoveries of all time.","zh":"Jones 作出了一項必須被列為有史以來最驚人發現之一的發現。"},{"en":"To be ranked as something means to be judged or placed in a particular position or category.","zh":"be ranked as something 指被評定或置於某個位置或類別。"},{"en":"A school may be ranked as one of the best in the district because of strong exam results.","zh":"學校可能因考試成績優秀而被列為區內最佳學校之一。"},{"en":"If a discovery changes an entire field, people may rank it among the greatest discoveries.","zh":"如果一項發現改變整個領域，人們可能把它列為最偉大的發現之一。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evaluation by importance, quality, or position.","zh":"這個片語描述按重要性、質素或位置作評價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one of the most amazing discoveries of all time","meaning":"有史以來最驚人的發現之一","examples":[{"en":"Jones made one of the most amazing discoveries of all time.","zh":"Jones 作出了有史以來最驚人的發現之一。"},{"en":"One of the most amazing discoveries of all time means a discovery that is among the greatest ever made.","zh":"one of the most amazing discoveries of all time 指歷來最偉大發現之一。"},{"en":"The discovery of penicillin is often seen as one of the most amazing discoveries of all time.","zh":"青黴素的發現常被視為有史以來最驚人的發現之一。"},{"en":"If a discovery changes how people understand history, science, or language, it may earn this description.","zh":"如果一項發現改變人們對歷史、科學或語言的理解，它可能獲得這種描述。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly praises the importance of a discovery.","zh":"這個片語強烈讚揚一項發現的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be little known outside of","meaning":"在……以外鮮為人知","examples":[{"en":"The discovery is little known outside of linguistic circles.","zh":"這項發現在語言學界以外鮮為人知。"},{"en":"To be little known outside of a group means few people beyond that group know about it.","zh":"be little known outside of a group 指在某群體以外很少人知道。"},{"en":"A useful teaching method may be little known outside of specialist education circles.","zh":"一種有用教學方法可能在專門教育界以外鮮為人知。"},{"en":"If an idea is technical, it may remain famous among experts but unknown to the public.","zh":"如果一個想法很專門，它可能在專家之間有名，但公眾並不知道。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts specialist knowledge with general public awareness.","zh":"這個片語把專門知識與一般公眾認知作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"linguistic circles","meaning":"語言學界","examples":[{"en":"Jones’s discovery is famous within linguistic circles.","zh":"Jones 的發現在語言學界很有名。"},{"en":"Linguistic circles are groups of people who study or work with language scientifically.","zh":"linguistic circles 是科學地研究或處理語言的人群。"},{"en":"A new theory about grammar may be discussed widely in linguistic circles before reaching textbooks.","zh":"關於文法的新理論可能先在語言學界廣泛討論，才進入教科書。"},{"en":"If something is known only in linguistic circles, ordinary readers may not have heard of it.","zh":"如果某事只在語言學界為人所知，普通讀者可能未聽過。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the academic or professional world of language study.","zh":"這個片語指語言研究的學術或專業圈子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Sanskrit","meaning":"梵文","examples":[{"en":"Jones was studying Sanskrit, an ancient Indian language.","zh":"Jones 當時正在研究梵文，一種古印度語言。"},{"en":"Sanskrit is an ancient Indian language used in many classical and religious texts.","zh":"Sanskrit 是一種古印度語言，用於許多古典和宗教文本。"},{"en":"A student of Indian history may learn Sanskrit to read old poems and sacred writings.","zh":"研究印度歷史的學生可能學習梵文，以閱讀古詩和神聖文獻。"},{"en":"If scholars compare Sanskrit with Greek and Latin, they can notice deep historical links.","zh":"如果學者把梵文與希臘語和拉丁語比較，就能注意到深層歷史連繫。"},{"en":"This word names a major ancient language important in linguistic study.","zh":"這個詞指語言學研究中重要的一種主要古代語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"long-dead language","meaning":"早已不再作日常使用的語言","examples":[{"en":"Sanskrit was described as a long-dead Indian language.","zh":"梵文被描述為一種早已不再作日常使用的印度語言。"},{"en":"A long-dead language is a language that has not been used as an everyday spoken language for a very long time.","zh":"long-dead language 指很久以來不再作日常口語使用的語言。"},{"en":"Students may study a long-dead language through old manuscripts rather than conversation practice.","zh":"學生可能透過古手稿學習一種早已不再作日常使用的語言，而不是練習對話。"},{"en":"If a language is long-dead, scholars may depend on texts to understand its grammar and vocabulary.","zh":"如果語言早已不作日常使用，學者可能依靠文本理解其語法和詞彙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a language preserved mainly through writing, not daily speech.","zh":"這個片語描述主要透過文字保存，而不是日常說話保存的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"classical texts","meaning":"古典文本","examples":[{"en":"Sanskrit was used in classical texts.","zh":"梵文被用於古典文本。"},{"en":"Classical texts are important old writings that are respected as part of a literary or cultural tradition.","zh":"classical texts 是被視為文學或文化傳統一部分的重要古老作品。"},{"en":"Students may read classical texts to understand how earlier societies thought and wrote.","zh":"學生可能閱讀古典文本，以理解早期社會如何思考和寫作。"},{"en":"If a language appears in classical texts, it can remain important long after everyday use declines.","zh":"如果一種語言出現在古典文本中，即使日常使用下降，它仍可保持重要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to old writings of lasting cultural value.","zh":"這個片語指具有持久文化價值的古老作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"liturgical texts","meaning":"禮拜儀式文本；宗教儀式文本","examples":[{"en":"Sanskrit was used in classical or liturgical texts.","zh":"梵文被用於古典或宗教儀式文本。"},{"en":"Liturgical texts are writings used in religious worship, prayer, or ceremony.","zh":"liturgical texts 是用於宗教崇拜、祈禱或儀式的文本。"},{"en":"A temple may preserve liturgical texts that guide chants and rituals.","zh":"寺廟可能保存指導吟誦和儀式的宗教儀式文本。"},{"en":"If a language is used in liturgical texts, it can remain sacred even when people no longer speak it daily.","zh":"如果一種語言用於宗教儀式文本，即使人們不再日常說它，它仍可保持神聖地位。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to religious texts used in formal worship.","zh":"這個片語指正式崇拜中使用的宗教文本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"upon examining","meaning":"在仔細研究……時","examples":[{"en":"Upon examining many words, Jones noticed their similarity to Greek and Latin.","zh":"在仔細研究許多詞語時，Jones 注意到它們與希臘語和拉丁語的相似性。"},{"en":"Upon examining means when someone carefully looks at or studies something.","zh":"upon examining 指當某人仔細查看或研究某事時。"},{"en":"Upon examining the essay, the teacher noticed that the examples were too general.","zh":"老師在仔細研究作文時，注意到例子太籠統。"},{"en":"If researchers examine data carefully, they may notice patterns that casual readers miss.","zh":"如果研究人員仔細檢查數據，可能會注意到普通讀者錯過的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces a discovery made after close study.","zh":"這個片語常引入仔細研究後作出的發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be struck by","meaning":"被……深深打動；突然注意到","examples":[{"en":"Jones was struck by the similarity between Sanskrit, Greek, and Latin.","zh":"Jones 突然注意到梵文、希臘語和拉丁語之間的相似性。"},{"en":"To be struck by something means to suddenly notice it strongly or feel impressed by it.","zh":"be struck by something 指突然強烈注意到某事，或對它留下深刻印象。"},{"en":"A visitor may be struck by how quiet a library is compared with a busy street.","zh":"訪客可能突然注意到圖書館與繁忙街道相比有多安靜。"},{"en":"If a researcher is struck by a pattern, they may investigate it more deeply.","zh":"如果研究人員被某種模式吸引，他們可能更深入調查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong moment of noticing or realisation.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈注意或頓悟的一刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"similarity to","meaning":"與……的相似性","examples":[{"en":"Many Sanskrit words showed similarity to Greek and Latin.","zh":"許多梵文字詞顯示出與希臘語和拉丁語的相似性。"},{"en":"Similarity to something means likeness or shared features with it.","zh":"similarity to something 指與某物相似或具有共同特徵。"},{"en":"A child may notice the similarity between two songs if the melody sounds almost the same.","zh":"如果兩首歌旋律聽起來幾乎一樣，孩子可能注意到它們之間的相似性。"},{"en":"If words in different languages show similarity, linguists may ask whether they share an origin.","zh":"如果不同語言中的詞語顯示相似性，語言學家可能會問它們是否有共同起源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes resemblance between two things.","zh":"這個片語描述兩件事之間的相似。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the most ancient languages known at that time","meaning":"當時已知最古老的語言","examples":[{"en":"Greek and Latin were among the most ancient languages known at that time.","zh":"希臘語和拉丁語屬於當時已知最古老的語言。"},{"en":"The most ancient languages known at that time were the oldest languages scholars then knew about.","zh":"the most ancient languages known at that time 指當時學者所知道最古老的語言。"},{"en":"In an old history class, students may learn what people once considered the oldest known civilisations.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生可能學到人們曾認為哪些文明是最古老的已知文明。"},{"en":"If scholars discover older evidence later, ideas about what is most ancient can change.","zh":"如果後來學者發現更古老證據，人們對最古老事物的看法可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase depends on the knowledge available in a particular period.","zh":"這個片語取決於某一時期可得的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a stronger affinity with","meaning":"與……有更密切的關係","examples":[{"en":"Sanskrit had a stronger affinity with Greek and Latin than expected.","zh":"梵文與希臘語和拉丁語之間的關係比預期更密切。"},{"en":"A stronger affinity with something means a closer relationship or greater similarity to it.","zh":"stronger affinity with something 指與某物有更接近的關係或更大相似性。"},{"en":"A student may feel a stronger affinity with history than mathematics because stories feel more natural to them.","zh":"學生可能對歷史比對數學有更強親近感，因為故事對他來說更自然。"},{"en":"If two languages show strong affinity, they may share deep historical roots.","zh":"如果兩種語言顯示密切關係，它們可能共享深層歷史根源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes closeness in nature, origin, or feeling.","zh":"這個片語描述性質、起源或感受上的接近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be produced by accident","meaning":"由偶然造成","examples":[{"en":"The similarity could not possibly have been produced by accident.","zh":"這種相似不可能由偶然造成。"},{"en":"To be produced by accident means to happen by chance rather than through a real connection or cause.","zh":"be produced by accident 指由碰巧發生，而不是由真實連繫或原因造成。"},{"en":"If two students write exactly the same unusual sentence, the similarity may not have been produced by accident.","zh":"如果兩名學生寫出完全相同而少見的句子，這種相似可能不是偶然造成。"},{"en":"When many patterns match, researchers often look for a deeper explanation.","zh":"當許多模式吻合，研究人員通常會尋找更深層解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts random coincidence with meaningful cause.","zh":"這個片語把隨機巧合與有意義原因作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"draw the conclusion that","meaning":"得出……的結論","examples":[{"en":"Jones drew the conclusion that Greek, Latin, and Sanskrit were related.","zh":"Jones 得出希臘語、拉丁語和梵文有關聯的結論。"},{"en":"To draw the conclusion that means to decide something after considering evidence.","zh":"draw the conclusion that 指在考慮證據後判斷某事。"},{"en":"After seeing many late submissions, a teacher may draw the conclusion that the deadline was unclear.","zh":"老師看到許多遲交功課後，可能得出截止日期不清楚的結論。"},{"en":"If evidence points in the same direction, researchers can draw a stronger conclusion.","zh":"如果證據指向同一方向，研究人員可以得出更有力的結論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reasoning from evidence to judgement.","zh":"這個片語描述由證據推理到判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Germanic languages","meaning":"日耳曼語族","examples":[{"en":"English belongs to the Germanic languages.","zh":"英語屬於日耳曼語族。"},{"en":"Germanic languages are a branch of the Indo-European language family that includes English, German, Dutch, and related languages.","zh":"Germanic languages 是印歐語系的一個分支，包括英語、德語、荷蘭語及相關語言。"},{"en":"A student may compare English and German to see similar basic words.","zh":"學生可能比較英語和德語，以看見相似的基本詞。"},{"en":"If two languages are Germanic, they may share grammar patterns and old vocabulary.","zh":"如果兩種語言屬於日耳曼語族，它們可能共享語法模式和古老詞彙。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to one major group of related European languages.","zh":"這個片語指歐洲相關語言的一個主要群組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be related to","meaning":"與……有關聯","examples":[{"en":"Greek and Latin were related to Sanskrit.","zh":"希臘語和拉丁語與梵文有關聯。"},{"en":"To be related to something means to share a connection, origin, or family relationship with it.","zh":"be related to something 指與某物共享連繫、起源或家族關係。"},{"en":"Spanish is related to French because both developed from Latin.","zh":"西班牙語與法語有關，因為兩者都由拉丁語發展而來。"},{"en":"If languages are related, learning one may help students notice patterns in another.","zh":"如果語言有關聯，學習其中一種可能幫助學生注意另一種中的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a historical or structural connection.","zh":"這個片語描述歷史或結構上的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"thus","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"The languages were related; thus, they probably evolved from an earlier language.","zh":"這些語言有關聯；因此，它們很可能由更早期語言演變而來。"},{"en":"Thus means therefore or as a result.","zh":"thus 指因此或作為結果。"},{"en":"The road was closed; thus, students had to take a longer route to school.","zh":"道路封閉；因此，學生必須走較長路線上學。"},{"en":"If evidence shows a connection, thus researchers can form a new explanation.","zh":"如果證據顯示有連繫，研究人員因此可以形成新解釋。"},{"en":"This word links a reason to a logical result.","zh":"這個詞把原因與合乎邏輯的結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"logically","meaning":"從邏輯上說","examples":[{"en":"Logically, all of these languages must have evolved from a single earlier language.","zh":"從邏輯上說，所有這些語言必然由一種更早期的單一語言演變而來。"},{"en":"Logically means according to reason and evidence.","zh":"logically 指根據理性和證據來看。"},{"en":"Logically, if the train leaves at eight and you arrive at eight-ten, you will miss it.","zh":"從邏輯上說，如果火車八點開出，而你八點十分才到，你就會錯過。"},{"en":"If several facts point to the same answer, a logical conclusion becomes stronger.","zh":"如果幾個事實指向同一答案，合乎邏輯的結論會更有力。"},{"en":"This word introduces a conclusion that follows from reasoning.","zh":"這個詞引入由推理得出的結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"necessarily have evolved from","meaning":"必然由……演變而來","examples":[{"en":"These languages must necessarily have evolved from a single earlier language.","zh":"這些語言必然由一種更早期的單一語言演變而來。"},{"en":"Necessarily have evolved from means must have developed from something earlier because the evidence strongly requires it.","zh":"necessarily have evolved from 指因證據強烈要求如此，所以必定由更早事物發展而來。"},{"en":"If two school rules use identical wording, one may necessarily have evolved from the other.","zh":"如果兩條校規用字完全相同，其中一條可能必然由另一條演變而來。"},{"en":"When many languages share deep grammar and vocabulary, scholars may argue they came from one source.","zh":"當許多語言共享深層語法和詞彙，學者可能主張它們來自同一源頭。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a strong logical claim about origin.","zh":"這個片語表達關於起源的強烈邏輯主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a single earlier language","meaning":"一種更早期的單一語言","examples":[{"en":"Greek, Latin, and Sanskrit may have evolved from a single earlier language.","zh":"希臘語、拉丁語和梵文可能由一種更早期的單一語言演變而來。"},{"en":"A single earlier language means one older language that later developed into several different languages.","zh":"single earlier language 指一種較古老語言，後來發展成幾種不同語言。"},{"en":"A local dialect and a neighbouring dialect may both come from a single earlier speech form.","zh":"本地方言和鄰近方言可能都來自一種更早期的說話形式。"},{"en":"If many languages share one earlier language, they belong to the same historical family.","zh":"如果許多語言共享一種早期語言，它們就屬於同一歷史語系。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common linguistic ancestor.","zh":"這個片語描述共同語言祖先。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"subsequent scholars","meaning":"後來的學者","examples":[{"en":"Subsequent scholars were able to confirm Jones’s conclusion.","zh":"後來的學者能夠證實 Jones 的結論。"},{"en":"Subsequent scholars are researchers who come later and continue studying the same topic.","zh":"subsequent scholars 是後來出現並繼續研究同一主題的研究者。"},{"en":"A scientist may make an early claim, and subsequent scholars may test it with better data.","zh":"科學家可能提出早期主張，而後來的學者用更好數據測試它。"},{"en":"If later scholars confirm a discovery, the original idea becomes more widely accepted.","zh":"如果後來學者證實一項發現，原來想法就會更廣泛被接受。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to researchers from later periods.","zh":"這個片語指較後時期的研究者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be able to confirm","meaning":"能夠證實","examples":[{"en":"Scholars were able to confirm the relationship between these languages.","zh":"學者能夠證實這些語言之間的關係。"},{"en":"To be able to confirm something means to have enough evidence to show that it is true.","zh":"be able to confirm something 指有足夠證據顯示某事屬實。"},{"en":"A doctor may be able to confirm an illness after reading test results.","zh":"醫生閱讀測試結果後，可能能夠證實疾病。"},{"en":"If more evidence appears, researchers can confirm or reject an earlier theory.","zh":"如果更多證據出現，研究人員可以證實或否定早期理論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes proving something with stronger support.","zh":"這個片語描述用更強支持證明某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"linguistic family","meaning":"語系；語言家族","examples":[{"en":"Scholars added more languages to the same linguistic family.","zh":"學者把更多語言加入同一語系。"},{"en":"A linguistic family is a group of languages that developed from a common ancestor.","zh":"linguistic family 是由共同祖先發展而來的一組語言。"},{"en":"French, Spanish, and Italian belong to the same language family branch because they developed from Latin.","zh":"法語、西班牙語和意大利語屬於同一語系分支，因為它們由拉丁語發展而來。"},{"en":"If languages are in one family, their basic words and grammar may show similarities.","zh":"如果語言屬於同一家族，其基本詞彙和語法可能顯示相似性。"},{"en":"This phrase helps classify languages by historical origin.","zh":"這個片語幫助按歷史起源分類語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Romance languages","meaning":"羅曼語族","examples":[{"en":"French and Spanish are Romance languages.","zh":"法語和西班牙語屬於羅曼語族。"},{"en":"Romance languages are languages that developed from Latin, including French, Spanish, Italian, and Portuguese.","zh":"Romance languages 是由拉丁語發展而來的語言，包括法語、西班牙語、意大利語和葡萄牙語。"},{"en":"A student who knows Spanish may find some Italian words familiar.","zh":"懂西班牙語的學生可能覺得一些意大利語詞語熟悉。"},{"en":"If languages come from Latin, they often share related vocabulary and grammar patterns.","zh":"如果語言來自拉丁語，它們通常共享相關詞彙和語法模式。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major branch of the Indo-European family.","zh":"這個片語指出印歐語系中的一個主要分支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Slavic languages","meaning":"斯拉夫語族","examples":[{"en":"Russian and Czech are Slavic languages.","zh":"俄語和捷克語屬於斯拉夫語族。"},{"en":"Slavic languages are a group of related Indo-European languages spoken mainly in eastern, central, and southeastern Europe.","zh":"Slavic languages 是一組相關的印歐語言，主要在東歐、中歐和東南歐使用。"},{"en":"A traveller who learns basic Russian may notice some familiar words in other Slavic countries.","zh":"學過基本俄語的旅客，可能在其他斯拉夫國家注意到熟悉詞語。"},{"en":"If two languages are Slavic, they may share sound patterns, grammar, or old roots.","zh":"如果兩種語言屬於斯拉夫語族，它們可能共享音系模式、語法或古老詞根。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major European language branch.","zh":"這個片語指出歐洲一個主要語言分支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Indo-Iranian languages","meaning":"印度—伊朗語族","examples":[{"en":"Persian belongs to the Indo-Iranian languages.","zh":"波斯語屬於印度—伊朗語族。"},{"en":"Indo-Iranian languages are a branch of Indo-European languages that includes Persian, Hindi, Urdu, and related languages.","zh":"Indo-Iranian languages 是印歐語系的一個分支，包括波斯語、印地語、烏爾都語及相關語言。"},{"en":"A linguistics class may compare Persian and Sanskrit to study old Indo-Iranian roots.","zh":"語言學課可能比較波斯語和梵文，以研究古老印度—伊朗詞根。"},{"en":"If languages belong to this branch, they may share deep historical connections.","zh":"如果語言屬於這一分支，它們可能共享深層歷史連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a large language group in South and West Asia.","zh":"這個片語指南亞和西亞的一大語言群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hundreds of languages and dialects","meaning":"數以百計的語言和方言","examples":[{"en":"There are hundreds of languages and dialects in this family.","zh":"這個語系中有數以百計的語言和方言。"},{"en":"Hundreds of languages and dialects means a very large number of related speech forms.","zh":"hundreds of languages and dialects 指非常大量相關的說話形式。"},{"en":"A country may contain many dialects even when schools use one official language.","zh":"一個國家即使學校使用一種官方語言，也可能包含許多方言。"},{"en":"If a language family has hundreds of members, its history must be very complex.","zh":"如果一個語系有數百個成員，其歷史必然非常複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the size and diversity of a language group.","zh":"這個片語強調語言群的規模和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"all over","meaning":"遍及","examples":[{"en":"Related languages are found all over Europe, Iran, and South Asia.","zh":"相關語言遍及歐洲、伊朗和南亞。"},{"en":"All over means throughout many parts of a place or region.","zh":"all over 指遍布某地方或地區的許多部分。"},{"en":"Posters for the school concert were placed all over the campus.","zh":"學校音樂會海報貼滿校園各處。"},{"en":"If a language family is found all over a continent, it must have spread widely over time.","zh":"如果一個語系遍及整個大陸，它必然隨時間廣泛傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad distribution.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ancestry","meaning":"祖源；源流","examples":[{"en":"The ancestry of many languages can be traced to Proto-Indo-European.","zh":"許多語言的祖源可追溯至原始印歐語。"},{"en":"Ancestry means origin, family background, or line of descent.","zh":"ancestry 指起源、家族背景或傳承脈絡。"},{"en":"A person may study family ancestry by reading old birth records.","zh":"一個人可能透過閱讀舊出生紀錄研究家族祖源。"},{"en":"If a language’s ancestry is known, scholars can understand how it changed over time.","zh":"如果一種語言的源流已知，學者就能理解它如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"This word describes historical roots.","zh":"這個詞描述歷史根源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be traced to","meaning":"可追溯至……","examples":[{"en":"The ancestry of these languages can be traced to an original Indo-European language.","zh":"這些語言的祖源可追溯至一種原始印歐語。"},{"en":"To be traced to something means to be followed back to an earlier source or cause.","zh":"be traced to something 指被追尋回較早源頭或原因。"},{"en":"A school rule may be traced to an accident that happened many years ago.","zh":"一條校規可能可追溯至多年前發生的一宗意外。"},{"en":"If a word can be traced to an ancient language, its history becomes clearer.","zh":"如果一個詞可追溯至古代語言，其歷史就更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finding the origin of something.","zh":"這個片語描述尋找某事起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"original Indo-European language","meaning":"原始印歐語","examples":[{"en":"Many languages can be traced to an original Indo-European language.","zh":"許多語言可追溯至原始印歐語。"},{"en":"The original Indo-European language means the earlier language from which the Indo-European family developed.","zh":"original Indo-European language 指印歐語系由其發展而來的較早語言。"},{"en":"A linguistics class may use reconstructed words to imagine this original language.","zh":"語言學課可能用重建詞語想像這種原始語言。"},{"en":"If many languages come from one original source, their similarities become easier to explain.","zh":"如果許多語言來自同一原始源頭，它們的相似性就更易解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the proposed common ancestor of many languages.","zh":"這個片語指許多語言被提出的共同祖先。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Proto-Indo-European","meaning":"原始印歐語","examples":[{"en":"Proto-Indo-European is often shortened to PIE.","zh":"Proto-Indo-European 常被縮寫為 PIE。"},{"en":"Proto-Indo-European is the reconstructed ancestor language of the Indo-European language family.","zh":"Proto-Indo-European 是印歐語系的重建祖語。"},{"en":"Students cannot listen to a recording of Proto-Indo-European because it was spoken before sound recording existed.","zh":"學生不能聽原始印歐語錄音，因為它在錄音技術出現前已被使用。"},{"en":"If scholars reconstruct Proto-Indo-European, they use patterns from later languages as evidence.","zh":"如果學者重建原始印歐語，他們會使用後來語言的模式作證據。"},{"en":"This term names a proposed ancient language, not a directly recorded one.","zh":"這個術語指一種被提出的古代語言，而不是有直接記錄的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"for short","meaning":"簡稱","examples":[{"en":"Proto-Indo-European is called PIE for short.","zh":"Proto-Indo-European 簡稱 PIE。"},{"en":"For short means as a shorter name or abbreviation.","zh":"for short 指作為較短名稱或縮寫。"},{"en":"Alexander is often called Alex for short.","zh":"Alexander 常簡稱 Alex。"},{"en":"If a technical term is long, people may use a shorter form to make discussion easier.","zh":"如果技術術語很長，人們可能使用較短形式令討論更方便。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a shortened name.","zh":"這個片語引入簡短名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"According to linguistic theory, proto-languages are spoken in limited areas.","zh":"根據語言學理論，原始語言通常在有限地區使用。"},{"en":"According to means based on what a person, source, rule, or theory says.","zh":"according to 指根據某人、來源、規則或理論所說。"},{"en":"According to the timetable, the last bus leaves at eleven.","zh":"根據時間表，最後一班巴士十一點開出。"},{"en":"If a claim is made according to a theory, it depends on that theory’s assumptions.","zh":"如果某主張根據一套理論提出，它取決於該理論的假設。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the source of information.","zh":"這個片語引入資訊來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"linguistic theory","meaning":"語言學理論","examples":[{"en":"Linguistic theory describes how proto-languages may have been spoken.","zh":"語言學理論描述原始語言可能如何被使用。"},{"en":"Linguistic theory is a set of ideas used to explain how languages work, change, and relate to one another.","zh":"linguistic theory 是用來解釋語言如何運作、改變和彼此相關的一套想法。"},{"en":"A student may use linguistic theory to understand why children learn grammar naturally.","zh":"學生可能使用語言學理論來理解孩子為何自然學會文法。"},{"en":"If theory explains language change well, it can help scholars reconstruct older languages.","zh":"如果理論能很好解釋語言變化，它可以幫助學者重建較古老語言。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to academic explanations of language.","zh":"這個片語指關於語言的學術解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"proto-languages","meaning":"原始語言","examples":[{"en":"Proto-languages are usually spoken by relatively small communities.","zh":"原始語言通常由相對小型社群使用。"},{"en":"Proto-languages are reconstructed earlier languages from which later related languages developed.","zh":"proto-languages 是被重建出來、後來相關語言由其發展而來的較早語言。"},{"en":"A teacher may compare proto-languages to grandparents in a language family tree.","zh":"老師可能把原始語言比作語言家族樹中的祖父母。"},{"en":"If several daughter languages share patterns, scholars may reconstruct a proto-language behind them.","zh":"如果幾種子語言共享模式，學者可能重建其背後的原始語言。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to proposed ancestral languages.","zh":"這個片語指被提出的祖語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"over relatively limited geographical areas","meaning":"在相對有限的地理範圍內","examples":[{"en":"Proto-languages are usually spoken over relatively limited geographical areas.","zh":"原始語言通常在相對有限的地理範圍內使用。"},{"en":"Over relatively limited geographical areas means within fairly small physical regions.","zh":"over relatively limited geographical areas 指在相當小的實體地區內。"},{"en":"A local dialect may be spoken over a limited area around one valley.","zh":"一種本地方言可能只在某個山谷附近的有限範圍內使用。"},{"en":"If a language is spoken only in a small area, contact with neighbours can shape it strongly.","zh":"如果一種語言只在小地區使用，與鄰近群體接觸可以強烈塑造它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes restricted geographical spread.","zh":"這個片語描述受限制的地理分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"over a short time span","meaning":"在短時間範圍內","examples":[{"en":"Proto-languages are usually spoken over a short time span.","zh":"原始語言通常在短時間範圍內被使用。"},{"en":"Over a short time span means during a relatively brief period.","zh":"over a short time span 指在相對短暫的一段期間內。"},{"en":"A school campaign may change student habits over a short time span if the message is clear.","zh":"如果訊息清晰，學校活動可能在短時間內改變學生習慣。"},{"en":"If a language changes quickly, its earlier form may exist only for a limited period.","zh":"如果語言快速改變，其較早形式可能只存在有限時期。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited duration.","zh":"這個片語描述有限持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tightly-knit community","meaning":"關係緊密的社群","examples":[{"en":"A proto-language is usually spoken by a tightly-knit community.","zh":"原始語言通常由關係緊密的社群使用。"},{"en":"A tightly-knit community is a group whose members know and support one another closely.","zh":"tightly-knit community 是成員彼此熟悉並密切支持的群體。"},{"en":"A small village can be tightly knit if families share work, festivals, and daily help.","zh":"如果小村莊中的家庭共同工作、過節並在日常互助，它可以是關係緊密的社群。"},{"en":"If a community is tightly knit, language habits may remain stable for longer.","zh":"如果社群關係緊密，語言習慣可能更長時間保持穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong social closeness.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈社會親密度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the implication is simple but stunning","meaning":"其含意簡單但驚人","examples":[{"en":"The implication of linguistic theory is simple but stunning.","zh":"語言學理論的含意簡單但驚人。"},{"en":"The implication is simple but stunning means the meaning that follows from the idea is easy to state but surprising in importance.","zh":"the implication is simple but stunning 指由某想法推出的含意容易說明，但重要性令人驚訝。"},{"en":"If one missed bus makes a student fail the interview, the implication is simple but serious: punctuality matters.","zh":"如果錯過一班巴士令學生面試失敗，其含意簡單但嚴重：準時很重要。"},{"en":"If many languages share one ancestor, the conclusion is simple but historically enormous.","zh":"如果許多語言共享同一祖先，結論很簡單但歷史意義巨大。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a small logical step with a powerful result.","zh":"這個片語突出一個小小邏輯步驟帶來強大結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ancient tribe","meaning":"古代部落","examples":[{"en":"A single ancient tribe may have spoken Proto-Indo-European.","zh":"一個單一古代部落可能曾使用原始印歐語。"},{"en":"An ancient tribe is a very old community or people group sharing language, culture, and way of life.","zh":"ancient tribe 是非常古老、共享語言、文化和生活方式的社群或民族群體。"},{"en":"A museum may display tools believed to belong to an ancient tribe.","zh":"博物館可能展示被認為屬於古代部落的工具。"},{"en":"If one ancient tribe spread widely, its language could influence many later peoples.","zh":"如果一個古代部落廣泛擴散，其語言可能影響許多後來民族。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a prehistoric social group.","zh":"這個片語指史前社會群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"eventually take over","meaning":"最終佔據；接管","examples":[{"en":"This ancient tribe eventually took over much of Eurasia.","zh":"這個古代部落最終佔據了歐亞大陸大部分地區。"},{"en":"To eventually take over a place means to gradually gain control or dominance there over time.","zh":"eventually take over a place 指隨時間逐漸取得該地控制權或主導地位。"},{"en":"A small shop may eventually take over a market if customers prefer its service.","zh":"如果顧客較喜歡某小店的服務，它可能最終接管市場。"},{"en":"If a group spreads with better tools or food supply, it may become dominant in nearby areas.","zh":"如果一個群體帶着較好工具或食物供應擴散，它可能在附近地區變得佔主導。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual expansion into control.","zh":"這個片語描述逐步擴張至取得控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Eurasian landmass","meaning":"歐亞大陸","examples":[{"en":"The tribe spread across the middle and western Eurasian landmass.","zh":"該部落擴散到歐亞大陸中部和西部。"},{"en":"The Eurasian landmass is the large continuous land area made up of Europe and Asia.","zh":"Eurasian landmass 是由歐洲和亞洲組成的巨大連續陸地。"},{"en":"Trade routes once connected many peoples across the Eurasian landmass.","zh":"貿易路線曾連接歐亞大陸上許多民族。"},{"en":"If a language spreads across this landmass, it can reach many climates, cultures, and societies.","zh":"如果一種語言在這片大陸擴散，它可以到達許多氣候、文化和社會。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the huge connected continent of Europe and Asia.","zh":"這個片語指歐洲和亞洲相連的巨大大陸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"spread their language with them","meaning":"隨着他們傳播自己的語言","examples":[{"en":"The tribe spread their language with them as they migrated.","zh":"該部落遷徙時也隨着他們傳播自己的語言。"},{"en":"To spread their language with them means to carry and pass on their language as they move to new places.","zh":"spread their language with them 指移往新地方時帶同並傳承自己的語言。"},{"en":"Migrant families may spread their language with them when they form communities abroad.","zh":"移民家庭在海外形成社群時，可能也把自己的語言帶到當地。"},{"en":"If a group settles widely, their children and neighbours may learn their speech.","zh":"如果一個群體廣泛定居，他們的孩子和鄰居可能學會他們的說話方式。"},{"en":"This phrase connects migration with language transmission.","zh":"這個片語把遷徙與語言傳播連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"subsequently evolved into","meaning":"其後演變成……","examples":[{"en":"The original language subsequently evolved into many others.","zh":"原本的語言其後演變成許多其他語言。"},{"en":"Subsequently evolved into means later developed into a different form or several new forms.","zh":"subsequently evolved into 指後來發展成另一形式或幾種新形式。"},{"en":"A small after-school club may subsequently evolve into a full school programme.","zh":"小型課後社團其後可能演變成完整學校計劃。"},{"en":"If a language spreads to different regions, it may gradually become several separate languages.","zh":"如果語言擴散到不同地區，它可能逐漸變成幾種分開的語言。"},{"en":"This phrase describes later development after an earlier stage.","zh":"這個片語描述早期階段之後的後續發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"over the course of time","meaning":"隨着時間推移","examples":[{"en":"The language evolved into many others over the course of time.","zh":"隨着時間推移，該語言演變成許多其他語言。"},{"en":"Over the course of time means gradually as time passes.","zh":"over the course of time 指隨時間逐漸發生。"},{"en":"A shy student may become confident over the course of time with regular practice.","zh":"害羞學生透過定期練習，可能隨着時間推移變得自信。"},{"en":"If communities live far apart, their speech may change over time in different directions.","zh":"如果社群相隔很遠，他們的說話方式可能隨時間朝不同方向改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow development across a period.","zh":"這個片語描述一段時間內的緩慢發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"language family","meaning":"語系；語言家族","examples":[{"en":"Proto-Indo-European created a language family with many speakers.","zh":"原始印歐語形成了一個有許多使用者的語系。"},{"en":"A language family is a group of languages that share a common ancestor.","zh":"language family 是共享共同祖先的一組語言。"},{"en":"English, German, and Dutch are in the same broad language family branch.","zh":"英語、德語和荷蘭語屬於同一大語系分支。"},{"en":"If languages belong to one family, old sound changes can explain many similarities.","zh":"如果語言屬於同一家族，古老音變可以解釋許多相似性。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise languages by ancestry.","zh":"這個片語幫助按祖源組織語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the greatest number of speakers","meaning":"最多使用者","examples":[{"en":"This language family now has the greatest number of speakers in the world.","zh":"這個語系現在擁有世界上最多使用者。"},{"en":"The greatest number of speakers means more users than any other comparable language family or group.","zh":"greatest number of speakers 指使用者數量多於任何可比較語系或群體。"},{"en":"A social media app with the greatest number of users can influence online habits strongly.","zh":"擁有最多用戶的社交媒體應用程式，可以強烈影響網上習慣。"},{"en":"If a language family has many speakers, its cultural and political influence may be wide.","zh":"如果一個語系有許多使用者，其文化和政治影響可能很廣。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the size of speaker populations.","zh":"這個片語比較使用者人口規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the big question concerns","meaning":"重大問題關乎……","examples":[{"en":"The big question concerns who the Proto-Indo-Europeans were.","zh":"重大問題關乎原始印歐人到底是誰。"},{"en":"The big question concerns something means the most important issue is about that thing.","zh":"the big question concerns something 指最重要的問題是關於某事。"},{"en":"In a school reform, the big question concerns whether students actually learn better.","zh":"在學校改革中，重大問題關乎學生是否真的學得更好。"},{"en":"If evidence is incomplete, the biggest question may remain difficult to answer.","zh":"如果證據不完整，最重大問題可能仍難以回答。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the central problem in a discussion.","zh":"這個片語引入討論中的核心問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ancestral homeland","meaning":"祖居地","examples":[{"en":"Scholars debate where the ancestral homeland of the Proto-Indo-Europeans lay.","zh":"學者爭論原始印歐人的祖居地在哪裡。"},{"en":"An ancestral homeland is the original home area of a people’s ancestors.","zh":"ancestral homeland 是一個民族祖先原本居住的地區。"},{"en":"A family may visit an ancestral homeland to learn where grandparents once lived.","zh":"家庭可能探訪祖居地，以了解祖父母曾經住在哪裡。"},{"en":"If scholars identify a group’s ancestral homeland, they can better explain migration routes.","zh":"如果學者確定某群體的祖居地，就能更好解釋遷徙路線。"},{"en":"This phrase connects origin, land, and ancestry.","zh":"這個片語連接起源、土地和祖先。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"archaeologists","meaning":"考古學家","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists have examined many prehistoric sites.","zh":"考古學家考察了許多史前遺址。"},{"en":"Archaeologists are experts who study past human life through objects, buildings, bones, and sites.","zh":"archaeologists 是透過物件、建築、骨骼和遺址研究過去人類生活的專家。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may dig carefully in old settlements to find tools and pottery.","zh":"考古學家可能在古老聚落中小心挖掘，以尋找工具和陶器。"},{"en":"If archaeologists find evidence of farming or horses, it may help explain ancient migrations.","zh":"如果考古學家找到農耕或馬匹證據，它可能幫助解釋古代遷徙。"},{"en":"This word refers to researchers who study human history through material remains.","zh":"這個詞指透過物質遺存研究人類歷史的研究者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"examine sites","meaning":"考察遺址","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists have examined many sites of European prehistory.","zh":"考古學家考察了許多歐洲史前遺址。"},{"en":"To examine sites means to study physical places carefully for evidence.","zh":"examine sites 指仔細研究實體地點以尋找證據。"},{"en":"Fire officers may examine sites after a fire to understand how it started.","zh":"消防人員可能在火災後考察現場，以了解火災如何開始。"},{"en":"If archaeologists examine sites systematically, they may find patterns of settlement and movement.","zh":"如果考古學家有系統地考察遺址，他們可能發現定居和遷移模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful investigation of locations.","zh":"這個片語描述對地點作仔細調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"European prehistory","meaning":"歐洲史前時代","examples":[{"en":"Many sites of European prehistory have been examined.","zh":"許多歐洲史前時代的遺址已被考察。"},{"en":"European prehistory refers to the period in Europe before written historical records.","zh":"European prehistory 指歐洲文字歷史紀錄出現以前的時期。"},{"en":"A museum exhibit on European prehistory may show stone tools, burial sites, and early farming remains.","zh":"關於歐洲史前時代的博物館展覽可能展示石器、墓地和早期農耕遺存。"},{"en":"If a period lacks written records, archaeologists must rely more on objects and sites.","zh":"如果某時期缺乏文字紀錄，考古學家就必須更多依靠物件和遺址。"},{"en":"This phrase describes Europe’s ancient past before writing.","zh":"這個片語描述歐洲文字出現前的古代過去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"identify something as","meaning":"把某物確定為……","examples":[{"en":"Some archaeologists have identified certain sites as the homeland of the PIE population.","zh":"一些考古學家把某些遺址確定為原始印歐語族群的家園。"},{"en":"To identify something as something else means to say what it is after study or evidence.","zh":"identify something as something else 指經研究或證據後指出某物是甚麼。"},{"en":"A doctor may identify a rash as an allergic reaction.","zh":"醫生可能把皮疹確定為過敏反應。"},{"en":"If scholars identify a site as a homeland, they must explain why the evidence fits.","zh":"如果學者把某遺址確定為祖居地，他們必須解釋為何證據吻合。"},{"en":"This phrase describes naming or classifying something based on evidence.","zh":"這個片語描述根據證據命名或分類某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the PIE population","meaning":"原始印歐語族群","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists have searched for the homeland of the PIE population.","zh":"考古學家一直尋找原始印歐語族群的祖居地。"},{"en":"The PIE population means the people believed to have spoken Proto-Indo-European.","zh":"PIE population 指被認為曾使用原始印歐語的人群。"},{"en":"A map of the PIE population would try to show where these ancient speakers may have lived.","zh":"原始印歐語族群地圖會嘗試顯示這些古代使用者可能住在哪裡。"},{"en":"If scholars locate this population, they can better explain how the language spread.","zh":"如果學者定位這個族群，就能更好解釋語言如何傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a proposed prehistoric speech community.","zh":"這個片語指被提出的史前語言社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"nationalistic overtones","meaning":"民族主義色彩","examples":[{"en":"Some claims are made with nationalistic overtones.","zh":"一些主張帶有民族主義色彩。"},{"en":"Nationalistic overtones are hints of strong national pride or political bias in a claim.","zh":"nationalistic overtones 是主張中帶有強烈民族自豪或政治偏見的暗示。"},{"en":"A history textbook may have nationalistic overtones if it presents one country as always heroic.","zh":"如果歷史教科書把一個國家描寫成永遠英雄，它可能帶有民族主義色彩。"},{"en":"If scholarship has nationalistic overtones, other researchers may question its fairness.","zh":"如果學術研究帶有民族主義色彩，其他研究者可能質疑其公正性。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that an argument may be shaped by national pride.","zh":"這個片語提醒某論點可能受民族自豪塑造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"arouse the anger of","meaning":"激起……的憤怒","examples":[{"en":"These claims sometimes arouse the anger of other scholars.","zh":"這些主張有時會激起其他學者的憤怒。"},{"en":"To arouse the anger of someone means to make them angry.","zh":"arouse the anger of someone 指令某人生氣。"},{"en":"A school decision may arouse the anger of parents if it feels unfair.","zh":"如果學校決定令人覺得不公平，可能激起家長憤怒。"},{"en":"If a theory appears politically biased, it may anger experts in the field.","zh":"如果理論看似帶有政治偏見，可能激怒該領域專家。"},{"en":"This phrase describes causing strong negative reaction.","zh":"這個片語描述引起強烈負面反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"others in this field","meaning":"這個領域中的其他人","examples":[{"en":"The claims have angered others in this field.","zh":"這些主張激怒了這個領域中的其他人。"},{"en":"Others in this field means other people working or researching in the same area.","zh":"others in this field 指在同一範疇工作或研究的其他人。"},{"en":"A new teaching theory may be criticised by others in the field of education.","zh":"新教學理論可能受到教育領域中其他人的批評。"},{"en":"If experts in the same field disagree, debate may continue for many years.","zh":"如果同一領域的專家意見不合，爭論可能持續多年。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to colleagues or specialists in the same discipline.","zh":"這個片語指同一學科中的同僚或專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"there remains controversy over","meaning":"對……仍有爭議","examples":[{"en":"There still remains controversy over each claim.","zh":"對每一項主張仍然存在爭議。"},{"en":"There remains controversy over something means people still disagree about it.","zh":"there remains controversy over something 指人們對某事仍有分歧。"},{"en":"There remains controversy over whether exams should be the only way to assess students.","zh":"對考試是否應是評估學生的唯一方式仍有爭議。"},{"en":"If evidence is incomplete, controversy may continue even among experts.","zh":"如果證據不完整，即使在專家之間，爭議也可能持續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unresolved debate.","zh":"這個片語描述尚未解決的爭論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"each claim","meaning":"每一項聲稱；每一個主張","examples":[{"en":"There is controversy over each claim about the PIE homeland.","zh":"關於原始印歐語祖居地的每一項主張都有爭議。"},{"en":"Each claim means every separate statement or argument being made.","zh":"each claim 指每一個分開提出的陳述或論點。"},{"en":"In a debate, students should check the evidence behind each claim.","zh":"在辯論中，學生應檢查每一項主張背後的證據。"},{"en":"If each claim is tested carefully, weak arguments become easier to spot.","zh":"如果每一項主張都被仔細測試，薄弱論點就更容易被看出。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that every individual assertion matters.","zh":"這個片語強調每個個別主張都重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"linguistic evidence","meaning":"語言學證據","examples":[{"en":"Linguistic evidence may provide more definite clues.","zh":"語言學證據可能提供更明確的線索。"},{"en":"Linguistic evidence is evidence from language, such as vocabulary, grammar, sound patterns, or word history.","zh":"linguistic evidence 是來自語言的證據，例如詞彙、語法、聲音模式或詞源歷史。"},{"en":"Similar words in two languages can provide linguistic evidence of a shared origin.","zh":"兩種語言中的相似詞語可以提供共同起源的語言學證據。"},{"en":"If archaeological evidence is unclear, linguistic evidence may help narrow the possibilities.","zh":"如果考古證據不清楚，語言學證據可能幫助縮小可能性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to language-based proof or clues.","zh":"這個片語指基於語言的證據或線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"provide more definite clues","meaning":"提供較明確的線索","examples":[{"en":"Linguistic evidence provides more definite clues than archaeology.","zh":"語言學證據比考古學提供較明確的線索。"},{"en":"To provide more definite clues means to give clearer hints or evidence.","zh":"provide more definite clues 指給出更清晰的提示或證據。"},{"en":"A student’s repeated mistakes may provide more definite clues about which grammar point is weak.","zh":"學生反覆犯錯可能提供較明確線索，顯示哪個文法點薄弱。"},{"en":"If one type of evidence is clearer, researchers may trust it more when forming a theory.","zh":"如果某類證據更清晰，研究人員在形成理論時可能更信任它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence that helps reduce uncertainty.","zh":"這個片語描述有助減少不確定性的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"similarities in vocabulary","meaning":"詞彙上的相似之處","examples":[{"en":"Similarities in vocabulary help linguists reconstruct earlier languages.","zh":"詞彙上的相似之處幫助語言學家重建較早語言。"},{"en":"Similarities in vocabulary are likenesses between words in different languages.","zh":"similarities in vocabulary 是不同語言中的詞語相似之處。"},{"en":"English father and German Vater show a similarity in basic family vocabulary.","zh":"英語 father 和德語 Vater 顯示基本家庭詞彙上的相似。"},{"en":"If many basic words look related, linguists may suspect a common ancestor.","zh":"如果許多基本詞看似相關，語言學家可能懷疑有共同祖先。"},{"en":"This phrase describes word-level evidence of connection.","zh":"這個片語描述詞語層面的連繫證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"daughter languages","meaning":"派生語言；子語言","examples":[{"en":"PIE’s daughter languages include many languages of Europe and Asia.","zh":"原始印歐語的子語言包括許多歐洲和亞洲語言。"},{"en":"Daughter languages are languages that developed from an earlier parent language.","zh":"daughter languages 是由較早母語發展而來的語言。"},{"en":"Spanish and French can be seen as daughter languages of Latin.","zh":"西班牙語和法語可被視為拉丁語的子語言。"},{"en":"If daughter languages spread far apart, they may become very different over time.","zh":"如果子語言擴散到很遠的地方，它們隨時間可能變得非常不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes languages descended from an older source.","zh":"這個片語描述由較古老源頭派生的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"allow someone to deduce","meaning":"使某人能推斷","examples":[{"en":"Vocabulary similarities allow linguists to deduce a probable grammar.","zh":"詞彙相似使語言學家能推斷可能的語法。"},{"en":"To allow someone to deduce something means to make it possible for them to work it out by reasoning.","zh":"allow someone to deduce something 指使某人能透過推理得出某事。"},{"en":"Footprints in the hallway may allow a teacher to deduce where students walked after lunch.","zh":"走廊上的腳印可能使老師推斷學生午飯後走過哪裡。"},{"en":"If evidence is detailed enough, researchers can infer facts that were not directly recorded.","zh":"如果證據足夠詳細，研究人員可以推斷未被直接記錄的事實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reasoning from clues.","zh":"這個片語描述由線索推理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"probable grammar","meaning":"可能的語法","examples":[{"en":"Linguists have deduced a probable grammar for PIE.","zh":"語言學家已推斷出原始印歐語的可能語法。"},{"en":"Probable grammar means the likely system of rules a language used, based on evidence.","zh":"probable grammar 指根據證據推測某語言可能使用的規則系統。"},{"en":"If students reconstruct an old dialect, they may suggest a probable grammar from surviving phrases.","zh":"如果學生重建一種舊方言，他們可能從留存片語提出可能語法。"},{"en":"Because no one recorded PIE directly, scholars can only propose its most likely grammar.","zh":"因為沒有人直接記錄原始印歐語，學者只能提出其最可能的語法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reasoned but not absolutely certain reconstruction.","zh":"這個片語描述有理據但非絕對確定的重建。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fairly extensive vocabulary","meaning":"相當廣泛的詞彙","examples":[{"en":"Linguists have reconstructed a fairly extensive vocabulary.","zh":"語言學家已重建出相當廣泛的詞彙。"},{"en":"A fairly extensive vocabulary means quite a large set of words.","zh":"fairly extensive vocabulary 指相當大量的詞語。"},{"en":"A student with a fairly extensive vocabulary can discuss school, work, travel, and daily problems clearly.","zh":"擁有相當廣泛詞彙的學生，可以清楚討論學校、工作、旅遊和日常問題。"},{"en":"If scholars reconstruct many words, they can infer what objects and ideas mattered to ancient speakers.","zh":"如果學者重建出許多詞，就可以推斷哪些物件和想法對古代使用者重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a vocabulary that is broad but not complete.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛但不完整的詞彙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"it is tempting to","meaning":"很容易想去……","examples":[{"en":"It is tempting to read a lifestyle and location into the vocabulary.","zh":"人們很容易想從詞彙中解讀出生活方式和地點。"},{"en":"It is tempting to do something means it is attractive or easy to want to do it.","zh":"it is tempting to do something 指某事很吸引人或令人容易想去做。"},{"en":"It is tempting to guess an answer quickly when two options look similar.","zh":"當兩個選項看起來相似，很容易想快速猜答案。"},{"en":"If evidence seems to suggest a story, researchers may be tempted to go beyond what it proves.","zh":"如果證據似乎暗示一個故事，研究人員可能被誘惑超出證據能證明的範圍。"},{"en":"This phrase often warns that an attractive idea may still be risky.","zh":"這個片語常提醒吸引人的想法仍可能有風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"read into","meaning":"從……中解讀出","examples":[{"en":"Scholars may read a tentative lifestyle into the reconstructed vocabulary.","zh":"學者可能從重建詞彙中解讀出初步推測的生活方式。"},{"en":"To read something into evidence means to interpret it as showing that thing, sometimes too strongly.","zh":"read something into evidence 指把證據詮釋為顯示某事，有時可能過度。"},{"en":"A teacher should not read laziness into one late homework submission without asking the reason.","zh":"老師不應只因一次遲交功課，就解讀成學生懶惰，而不先詢問原因。"},{"en":"If scholars read too much into a few words, their conclusion may become speculative.","zh":"如果學者從少數詞語中解讀太多，結論可能變得推測性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes interpretation, often with a warning about overinterpretation.","zh":"這個片語描述詮釋，常帶有過度詮釋的提醒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tentative lifestyle","meaning":"初步推測的生活方式","examples":[{"en":"The vocabulary may suggest a tentative lifestyle.","zh":"詞彙可能暗示一種初步推測的生活方式。"},{"en":"A tentative lifestyle is a cautious reconstruction of how people may have lived.","zh":"tentative lifestyle 是對人們可能如何生活作出的謹慎重建。"},{"en":"From old tools, archaeologists may suggest a tentative lifestyle of fishing and small-scale farming.","zh":"從舊工具中，考古學家可能提出一種以捕魚和小規模農耕為主的初步生活方式。"},{"en":"If evidence is limited, any lifestyle description must remain tentative.","zh":"如果證據有限，任何生活方式描述都必須保持試探性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a careful, uncertain picture of daily life.","zh":"這個片語描述一幅謹慎而不確定的日常生活圖像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"quaint proviso","meaning":"有點有趣的附帶條件","examples":[{"en":"The idea comes with the quaint proviso that it remains speculative.","zh":"這個想法帶有一個有點有趣的附帶條件：它仍然是推測性的。"},{"en":"A quaint proviso is an unusual or slightly old-fashioned condition added to a statement.","zh":"quaint proviso 是加在陳述上的不尋常或略帶古雅感的條件。"},{"en":"A teacher might praise a student’s theory with the proviso that more evidence is needed.","zh":"老師可能讚賞學生的理論，但附帶條件是需要更多證據。"},{"en":"If a claim comes with a proviso, readers should notice its limits.","zh":"如果主張帶有附帶條件，讀者應注意其限制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a condition or warning attached to an attractive idea.","zh":"這個片語描述附加在吸引人想法上的條件或警告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at best","meaning":"充其量；頂多","examples":[{"en":"The conclusion is, at best, highly speculative.","zh":"這個結論充其量是高度推測性的。"},{"en":"At best means even in the most favourable interpretation.","zh":"at best 指即使從最有利角度理解也只是如此。"},{"en":"If a student writes only one example, the essay is at best incomplete.","zh":"如果學生只寫一個例子，文章充其量是不完整的。"},{"en":"When evidence is weak, a conclusion can be at best a careful guess.","zh":"當證據薄弱時，結論頂多只能是謹慎猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase limits how strong or positive a judgement can be.","zh":"這個片語限制判斷能有多強或多正面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"highly speculative","meaning":"高度推測性的","examples":[{"en":"The proposed lifestyle remains highly speculative.","zh":"所提出的生活方式仍然高度推測性。"},{"en":"Highly speculative means based on limited evidence and therefore uncertain.","zh":"highly speculative 指基於有限證據，因此不確定。"},{"en":"A rumour about a new school policy is highly speculative until the principal confirms it.","zh":"關於新校政的傳聞在校長確認前都是高度推測性的。"},{"en":"If a theory depends on many guesses, researchers should present it carefully.","zh":"如果理論依賴許多猜測，研究人員應謹慎呈現。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that an idea is possible but not firmly proven.","zh":"這個片語提醒某想法可能成立，但未被堅實證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"looking at just one example","meaning":"只看其中一個例子","examples":[{"en":"Looking at just one example, PIE has words for temperate trees.","zh":"只看其中一個例子，原始印歐語有表示溫帶樹木的詞。"},{"en":"Looking at just one example means using one case to illustrate a larger point.","zh":"looking at just one example 指用一個例子說明更大的觀點。"},{"en":"Looking at just one example, a late bus can show why transport planning matters.","zh":"只看其中一個例子，一班遲到巴士可以顯示交通規劃為何重要。"},{"en":"If one example is clear, it can help students understand a difficult argument.","zh":"如果一個例子清楚，它可以幫助學生理解困難論點。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a single illustration, not the whole proof.","zh":"這個片語引入單一說明，而不是完整證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"temperate trees","meaning":"溫帶樹木","examples":[{"en":"PIE includes words for temperate trees.","zh":"原始印歐語包括表示溫帶樹木的詞。"},{"en":"Temperate trees are trees that grow in mild or cool climates, not tropical regions.","zh":"temperate trees 是生長在溫和或寒涼氣候，而非熱帶地區的樹木。"},{"en":"Oaks and beeches are examples of temperate trees found in many northern regions.","zh":"橡樹和山毛櫸是在許多北方地區發現的溫帶樹木例子。"},{"en":"If an ancient language has words for temperate trees, it may suggest where its speakers lived.","zh":"如果古代語言有溫帶樹木詞彙，可能暗示其使用者住在哪裡。"},{"en":"This phrase links vocabulary with climate and geography.","zh":"這個片語把詞彙與氣候和地理連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the Northern Hemisphere","meaning":"北半球","examples":[{"en":"These words refer to trees of the Northern Hemisphere.","zh":"這些詞指北半球的樹木。"},{"en":"The Northern Hemisphere is the half of the Earth north of the equator.","zh":"Northern Hemisphere 是地球赤道以北的一半。"},{"en":"Europe, North America, and much of Asia are in the Northern Hemisphere.","zh":"歐洲、北美和亞洲大部分都位於北半球。"},{"en":"If a language has words linked to northern plants, scholars may consider a northern homeland.","zh":"如果一種語言有與北方植物相關的詞，學者可能考慮北方祖居地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major geographical half of the planet.","zh":"這個片語描述地球的一個主要地理半球。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tropical varieties","meaning":"熱帶品種","examples":[{"en":"PIE lacks words for tropical varieties of trees.","zh":"原始印歐語缺乏表示熱帶樹木品種的詞。"},{"en":"Tropical varieties are types of plants or trees that grow in hot, wet tropical regions.","zh":"tropical varieties 是生長在炎熱潮濕熱帶地區的植物或樹木類型。"},{"en":"Mango and palm trees are familiar tropical varieties in many warm countries.","zh":"芒果樹和棕櫚樹是許多炎熱國家常見的熱帶品種。"},{"en":"If an ancient language lacks tropical tree words, its speakers may not have lived in the tropics.","zh":"如果古代語言缺乏熱帶樹木詞，使用者可能不住在熱帶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes kinds found in tropical climates.","zh":"這個片語描述熱帶氣候中的種類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Mediterranean varieties","meaning":"地中海品種","examples":[{"en":"PIE lacks words for Mediterranean varieties.","zh":"原始印歐語缺乏表示地中海品種的詞。"},{"en":"Mediterranean varieties are types of plants or trees associated with the Mediterranean climate and region.","zh":"Mediterranean varieties 是與地中海氣候和地區相關的植物或樹木種類。"},{"en":"Olive trees and some grape varieties are often linked with Mediterranean landscapes.","zh":"橄欖樹和一些葡萄品種常與地中海景觀相連。"},{"en":"If a language lacks such words, scholars may question whether its speakers lived near the Mediterranean.","zh":"如果一種語言缺乏這些詞，學者可能質疑其使用者是否住在地中海附近。"},{"en":"This phrase connects plant vocabulary with a specific regional climate.","zh":"這個片語把植物詞彙與特定地區氣候連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"indicate a northern European location","meaning":"顯示位於北歐","examples":[{"en":"The vocabulary indicates a northern European location.","zh":"詞彙顯示起源地位於北歐。"},{"en":"To indicate a northern European location means to suggest that the place was in northern Europe.","zh":"indicate a northern European location 指暗示地點在北歐。"},{"en":"If a shopping receipt uses local currency, it may indicate where the buyer was.","zh":"如果購物收據使用當地貨幣，它可能顯示買家曾在哪裡。"},{"en":"If words refer to cold-climate trees, they may point to a northern homeland.","zh":"如果詞語指寒冷氣候樹木，它們可能指向北方祖居地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence suggesting a geographical area.","zh":"這個片語描述證據暗示某個地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cold climate","meaning":"寒冷氣候","examples":[{"en":"The words suggest a cold climate.","zh":"這些詞暗示寒冷氣候。"},{"en":"A cold climate is a climate with low temperatures, especially for much of the year.","zh":"cold climate 是氣溫低，尤其是一年中很多時間都寒冷的氣候。"},{"en":"People in a cold climate may need thick clothing, heating, and stored food in winter.","zh":"生活在寒冷氣候中的人可能需要厚衣、暖氣和冬季儲存食物。"},{"en":"If a language has many words for snow or cold-weather trees, climate may have shaped its vocabulary.","zh":"如果一種語言有許多雪或寒地樹木詞，氣候可能塑造了其詞彙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes environmental conditions linked to low temperature.","zh":"這個片語描述與低溫相關的環境條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"detailed linguistic analysis","meaning":"詳細的語言學分析","examples":[{"en":"Detailed linguistic analysis supports the Caspian Steppe theory.","zh":"詳細的語言學分析支持裏海草原理論。"},{"en":"Detailed linguistic analysis is careful study of language evidence, including sounds, words, grammar, and history.","zh":"detailed linguistic analysis 是對語言證據的仔細研究，包括聲音、詞語、語法和歷史。"},{"en":"A teacher may use detailed analysis to show why two similar answers are not equally correct.","zh":"老師可能用詳細分析說明為何兩個相似答案並非同樣正確。"},{"en":"If analysis is detailed, it can support a theory more strongly than vague comparison.","zh":"如果分析詳細，它比籠統比較更能有力支持理論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes close, evidence-based language study.","zh":"這個片語描述細緻、以證據為本的語言研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the most widely accepted theory","meaning":"最廣為接受的理論","examples":[{"en":"The most widely accepted theory places the PIE origin in the Caspian Steppe.","zh":"最廣為接受的理論把原始印歐語起源地定位於裏海草原。"},{"en":"The most widely accepted theory is the explanation supported by the largest number of experts or evidence.","zh":"most widely accepted theory 是得到最多專家或證據支持的解釋。"},{"en":"In science class, students learn the most widely accepted theory before studying alternative ideas.","zh":"在科學課中，學生先學最廣為接受的理論，再研究其他想法。"},{"en":"If a theory is widely accepted, it still may change when new evidence appears.","zh":"如果理論被廣泛接受，當新證據出現時，它仍可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the current mainstream explanation.","zh":"這個片語描述目前的主流解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"place the origin in","meaning":"把起源地定位於……","examples":[{"en":"The theory places the PIE origin in the Caspian Steppe.","zh":"該理論把原始印歐語起源地定位於裏海草原。"},{"en":"To place the origin in a location means to identify that place as where something began.","zh":"place the origin in a location 指把某地確定為某事開始的地方。"},{"en":"Historians may place the origin of a festival in an old farming ritual.","zh":"歷史學家可能把節日的起源定位於古老農耕儀式。"},{"en":"If scholars place a language’s origin in one region, they must explain how it spread elsewhere.","zh":"如果學者把語言起源定位於某地區，就必須解釋它如何傳到其他地方。"},{"en":"This phrase links a beginning with a specific place.","zh":"這個片語把起點與特定地方連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the Caspian Steppe","meaning":"裏海草原","examples":[{"en":"The Caspian Steppe is often identified as the origin of PIE.","zh":"裏海草原常被確定為原始印歐語的起源地。"},{"en":"The Caspian Steppe is a large grassland region near the Caspian and Black Sea areas.","zh":"Caspian Steppe 是靠近裏海和黑海地區的一大片草原。"},{"en":"A map can help students see why the Caspian Steppe could connect Europe and Asia.","zh":"地圖可以幫助學生看見為何裏海草原可能連接歐洲和亞洲。"},{"en":"If a people lived on open steppe land, horses and movement may have been important.","zh":"如果一個民族生活在開闊草原，馬匹和移動可能很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major proposed homeland for Proto-Indo-European.","zh":"這個片語指出原始印歐語的一個主要被提出祖居地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a vast region of","meaning":"一大片……地區","examples":[{"en":"The Caspian Steppe is a vast region of grass and shrubland.","zh":"裏海草原是一大片草地和灌木地區。"},{"en":"A vast region of something means a very large area covered by that kind of landscape or feature.","zh":"vast region of something 指被某種景觀或特徵覆蓋的非常大區域。"},{"en":"A desert is a vast region of sand, rock, and dry air.","zh":"沙漠是一大片沙、岩石和乾燥空氣的地區。"},{"en":"If people live across a vast region, their communities may spread out and move often.","zh":"如果人們生活在一大片地區，他們的社群可能分散並經常移動。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the large size of an area.","zh":"這個片語強調區域面積巨大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"temperate grass and shrubland","meaning":"溫帶草原和灌木地","examples":[{"en":"The Caspian Steppe consists of temperate grass and shrubland.","zh":"裏海草原由溫帶草原和灌木地組成。"},{"en":"Temperate grass and shrubland is land with grasses and low bushes in a mild or cool climate.","zh":"temperate grass and shrubland 是溫和或寒涼氣候中有草和低矮灌木的土地。"},{"en":"Herders may use grassland for animals when there is enough open space.","zh":"當有足夠開闊空間，牧民可能用草原放牧動物。"},{"en":"If a region is mostly grass and shrubland, farming, herding, and travel may develop differently from forest life.","zh":"如果地區主要是草原和灌木地，農耕、畜牧和旅行可能與森林生活不同地發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a particular natural environment.","zh":"這個片語描述一種特定自然環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"north of","meaning":"在……以北","examples":[{"en":"The Caspian Steppe lies north of the Black Sea.","zh":"裏海草原位於黑海以北。"},{"en":"North of a place means located above it on a map, toward the north.","zh":"north of a place 指在地圖上位於該地上方、向北的位置。"},{"en":"The school is north of the train station, so students walk uphill from the station.","zh":"學校在火車站以北，所以學生從車站步行上坡。"},{"en":"If a region lies north of another, climate and travel routes may differ.","zh":"如果一個地區位於另一地以北，氣候和交通路線可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase gives relative geographical location.","zh":"這個片語給出相對地理位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"present-day Ukraine","meaning":"現今的烏克蘭","examples":[{"en":"The region includes present-day Ukraine, southern Russia, and Kazakhstan.","zh":"該地區包括現今的烏克蘭、俄羅斯南部和哈薩克。"},{"en":"Present-day Ukraine means the country known as Ukraine today, as opposed to ancient or historical boundaries.","zh":"present-day Ukraine 指今天稱為烏克蘭的國家，而不是古代或歷史邊界。"},{"en":"A history map may show that an ancient empire covered parts of present-day Turkey.","zh":"歷史地圖可能顯示古代帝國覆蓋現今土耳其的部分地區。"},{"en":"If scholars describe ancient regions using modern countries, readers can locate them more easily.","zh":"如果學者用現代國家描述古代地區，讀者就更容易定位。"},{"en":"This phrase connects ancient geography with today’s map.","zh":"這個片語把古代地理與今天地圖連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"southern Russia","meaning":"俄羅斯南部","examples":[{"en":"The Caspian Steppe stretches across southern Russia.","zh":"裏海草原橫跨俄羅斯南部。"},{"en":"Southern Russia means the southern part of Russia, closer to the Black Sea, Caspian Sea, or Caucasus regions.","zh":"southern Russia 指俄羅斯南部地區，較接近黑海、裏海或高加索地區。"},{"en":"A geography lesson may compare southern Russia with Siberia to show climate differences.","zh":"地理課可能比較俄羅斯南部與西伯利亞，以顯示氣候差異。"},{"en":"If a steppe crosses southern Russia, it can connect several neighbouring regions.","zh":"如果草原橫跨俄羅斯南部，它可以連接幾個鄰近地區。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a broad regional location inside Russia.","zh":"這個片語給出俄羅斯內部的大致地區位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"around 4000 BC","meaning":"約公元前 4000 年","examples":[{"en":"The PIE language was spoken around 4000 BC.","zh":"原始印歐語約在公元前 4000 年被使用。"},{"en":"Around 4000 BC means approximately four thousand years before the traditional birth year of Christ.","zh":"around 4000 BC 指大約在傳統基督出生年份前四千年。"},{"en":"A museum label may say a pot was made around 2000 BC if the date is approximate.","zh":"如果日期只是大約，博物館標籤可能寫某陶器約在公元前 2000 年製成。"},{"en":"If dates are very ancient, scholars often use around because exact dating is difficult.","zh":"如果年代非常久遠，學者常用 around，因為確切定年困難。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate ancient date.","zh":"這個片語給出大約的古代日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"plus or minus a millennium","meaning":"上下相差約一千年","examples":[{"en":"The date is around 4000 BC, plus or minus a millennium.","zh":"日期約為公元前 4000 年，上下相差約一千年。"},{"en":"Plus or minus a millennium means the date could be about one thousand years earlier or later.","zh":"plus or minus a millennium 指日期可能早或晚大約一千年。"},{"en":"For very old remains, an estimate may be 8000 years old, plus or minus several centuries.","zh":"對非常古老的遺骸，估算可能是八千年前，上下相差數百年。"},{"en":"If evidence is ancient and indirect, the possible date range can be wide.","zh":"如果證據古老且間接，可能日期範圍可以很闊。"},{"en":"This phrase shows uncertainty in dating.","zh":"這個片語顯示定年上的不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"exact dates","meaning":"確切日期","examples":[{"en":"Exact dates are impossible at such an early stage.","zh":"在如此早期階段，確切日期是不可能的。"},{"en":"Exact dates are precise days, years, or periods without uncertainty.","zh":"exact dates 是沒有不確定性的精確日子、年份或時期。"},{"en":"A school event needs exact dates so parents can plan ahead.","zh":"學校活動需要確切日期，讓家長可以提前安排。"},{"en":"For prehistoric language, exact dates are hard because there are no written records.","zh":"對史前語言而言，確切日期很難，因為沒有文字紀錄。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts precision with approximate dating.","zh":"這個片語把精確與大約定年作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at such an early stage","meaning":"在如此早期階段","examples":[{"en":"Exact dates are impossible at such an early stage in European prehistory.","zh":"在歐洲史前時代如此早期階段，確切日期是不可能的。"},{"en":"At such an early stage means during such a very early period in development or history.","zh":"at such an early stage 指在發展或歷史中如此早的一段時期。"},{"en":"At such an early stage of a project, it is hard to know the final cost.","zh":"在項目如此早期階段，很難知道最終成本。"},{"en":"If a period is extremely early, evidence may be rare or damaged.","zh":"如果時期極早，證據可能稀少或受損。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why certainty is difficult.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何難以確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"enable someone to","meaning":"使某人能夠","examples":[{"en":"Scholars ask what enabled the tribe to advance outwards.","zh":"學者問是甚麼使該部落能夠向外擴張。"},{"en":"To enable someone to do something means to make it possible for them to do it.","zh":"enable someone to do something 指使某人能夠做某事。"},{"en":"Online lessons enable students in remote areas to study with good teachers.","zh":"網上課堂使偏遠地區學生能夠跟好老師學習。"},{"en":"If horses enabled a tribe to travel faster, expansion would become easier.","zh":"如果馬匹使部落能夠更快旅行，擴張就會變得更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with new ability.","zh":"這個片語把原因與新能力連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"advance outwards","meaning":"向外擴張","examples":[{"en":"The tribe may have advanced outwards across Eurasia.","zh":"該部落可能向外擴張，橫越歐亞大陸。"},{"en":"To advance outwards means to move or expand away from an original centre.","zh":"advance outwards 指從原本中心向外移動或擴展。"},{"en":"A city may advance outwards as new housing estates are built beyond the old town.","zh":"隨着新屋苑建在舊城外，城市可能向外擴張。"},{"en":"If a population grows, people may move outward to find land, food, or work.","zh":"如果人口增長，人們可能向外移動以尋找土地、食物或工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes expansion from a starting point.","zh":"這個片語描述從起點向外擴展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"geneticists","meaning":"遺傳學家","examples":[{"en":"Geneticists have suggested explanations for the tribe’s expansion.","zh":"遺傳學家提出了解釋該部落擴張的說法。"},{"en":"Geneticists are scientists who study genes, heredity, and biological ancestry.","zh":"geneticists 是研究基因、遺傳和生物祖源的科學家。"},{"en":"Geneticists may use DNA evidence to study how ancient populations moved.","zh":"遺傳學家可能使用 DNA 證據研究古代人口如何遷移。"},{"en":"If geneticists compare modern and ancient DNA, they may trace migration patterns.","zh":"如果遺傳學家比較現代和古代 DNA，他們可能追蹤遷徙模式。"},{"en":"This word refers to scientists who study inherited biological information.","zh":"這個詞指研究遺傳生物資訊的科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"domestication of the horse","meaning":"馬匹馴化","examples":[{"en":"The domestication of the horse may have given the tribe military superiority.","zh":"馬匹馴化可能給予該部落軍事優勢。"},{"en":"Domestication of the horse means humans began controlling, breeding, and using horses for work, travel, or war.","zh":"domestication of the horse 指人類開始控制、繁殖和使用馬匹作工作、交通或戰爭用途。"},{"en":"A history teacher may explain how horse domestication changed transport and warfare.","zh":"歷史老師可能解釋馬匹馴化如何改變交通和戰爭。"},{"en":"If a group could ride horses while others could not, it might move and fight more effectively.","zh":"如果一個群體能騎馬而其他群體不能，它可能更有效移動和作戰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of turning wild horses into useful human partners.","zh":"這個片語描述把野馬變成人類有用伙伴的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hitherto unheard-of","meaning":"迄今未有過的","examples":[{"en":"The horse may have given the tribe hitherto unheard-of military superiority.","zh":"馬匹可能給予該部落迄今未有過的軍事優勢。"},{"en":"Hitherto unheard-of means never known or experienced before that time.","zh":"hitherto unheard-of 指在那時以前從未被知道或經歷過。"},{"en":"A school may achieve hitherto unheard-of exam results after changing its teaching system.","zh":"學校改變教學系統後，可能取得迄今未有過的考試成績。"},{"en":"If a new tool gives one group an advantage never seen before, it can change power relations.","zh":"如果新工具給予某群體前所未見的優勢，它可以改變權力關係。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises novelty and surprise.","zh":"這個片語強烈強調新奇和驚人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"military superiority","meaning":"軍事優勢","examples":[{"en":"Horse domestication may have given the tribe military superiority.","zh":"馬匹馴化可能給予該部落軍事優勢。"},{"en":"Military superiority means having greater fighting power, weapons, mobility, or strategy than opponents.","zh":"military superiority 指比對手有更強作戰力量、武器、機動性或策略。"},{"en":"An army with faster transport may have military superiority over one that must walk.","zh":"擁有更快交通工具的軍隊，可能比必須步行的軍隊有軍事優勢。"},{"en":"If one group has military superiority, it may conquer or influence neighbouring groups.","zh":"如果一個群體有軍事優勢，它可能征服或影響鄰近群體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes advantage in war or conflict.","zh":"這個片語描述戰爭或衝突中的優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"many thousands of years later","meaning":"數千年後","examples":[{"en":"The Huns and the Mongols used similar advantages many thousands of years later.","zh":"數千年後，匈人和蒙古人使用了相似優勢。"},{"en":"Many thousands of years later means a very long time after the earlier event.","zh":"many thousands of years later 指在較早事件之後非常久遠的時間。"},{"en":"Ancient farming began long before machines transformed agriculture many thousands of years later.","zh":"古代農耕早已開始，數千年後機器才改變農業。"},{"en":"If a strategy works again much later, it may reveal a repeated pattern in history.","zh":"如果某策略在很久之後再次有效，它可能揭示歷史中的重複模式。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a huge gap in time.","zh":"這個片語突出巨大的時間距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the discovery of farming","meaning":"農耕的發現","examples":[{"en":"The discovery of farming may have driven the tribe’s expansion.","zh":"農耕的發現可能推動了該部落的擴張。"},{"en":"The discovery of farming means humans learned to grow crops and produce food instead of only gathering or hunting.","zh":"discovery of farming 指人類學會種植作物和生產食物，而不只是採集或狩獵。"},{"en":"A lesson on early villages often begins with the discovery of farming.","zh":"關於早期村落的一課通常由農耕的發現開始。"},{"en":"If people can farm, they may produce more reliable food and support larger populations.","zh":"如果人們能農耕，就可能生產更可靠食物並支持更大人口。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major turning point in human history.","zh":"這個片語描述人類歷史中的重大轉折。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the impetus of","meaning":"……的推動力","examples":[{"en":"Farming may have been the impetus of the tribe’s advance.","zh":"農耕可能是該部落向外推進的推動力。"},{"en":"The impetus of something is the force or reason that drives it forward.","zh":"impetus of something 是推動某事向前的力量或原因。"},{"en":"A bad test result may become the impetus of a student’s serious revision plan.","zh":"一次差劣測驗成績可能成為學生認真溫習計劃的推動力。"},{"en":"If farming provided food security, it could push a population to grow and move outward.","zh":"如果農耕提供食物安全，它可以推動人口增長並向外移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the driving force behind an action or change.","zh":"這個片語描述行動或變化背後的驅動力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stable and steady food supply","meaning":"穩定的食物供應","examples":[{"en":"Farming provided a stable and steady food supply.","zh":"農耕提供了穩定的食物供應。"},{"en":"A stable and steady food supply means food is available regularly and reliably.","zh":"stable and steady food supply 指食物能定期而可靠地獲得。"},{"en":"A family with a steady income can keep a stable food supply at home.","zh":"有穩定收入的家庭可以在家中保持穩定食物供應。"},{"en":"If a community has reliable food, more children can survive and the population may grow.","zh":"如果社群有可靠食物，更多兒童可以存活，人口可能增長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes food security.","zh":"這個片語描述糧食安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at hand","meaning":"在手邊；可隨時取得","examples":[{"en":"The tribe had a stable food supply at hand.","zh":"該部落有可隨時取得的穩定食物供應。"},{"en":"At hand means nearby, available, or ready to use.","zh":"at hand 指在附近、可用或準備好使用。"},{"en":"A student should keep a dictionary at hand when reading difficult articles.","zh":"學生閱讀困難文章時，應把字典放在手邊。"},{"en":"If food is at hand, people spend less time searching for it and more time building communities.","zh":"如果食物可隨時取得，人們花較少時間尋找食物，能用更多時間建立社群。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something accessible and ready.","zh":"這個片語描述可接觸且可使用的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at the expense of","meaning":"以犧牲……為代價","examples":[{"en":"The tribe may have expanded at the expense of other groups.","zh":"該部落可能以犧牲其他群體為代價而擴張。"},{"en":"At the expense of someone or something means causing loss, harm, or sacrifice to them.","zh":"at the expense of someone or something 指對某人或某事造成損失、傷害或犧牲。"},{"en":"A student should not improve grades at the expense of sleep and health.","zh":"學生不應以犧牲睡眠和健康為代價來提高成績。"},{"en":"If one population expands into another group’s land, the second group may lose resources.","zh":"如果一個人口擴張到另一群體的土地，後者可能失去資源。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one side’s gain may create another side’s loss.","zh":"這個片語顯示一方得益可能造成另一方損失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fragmented hunter-gathering tribes","meaning":"分散的狩獵採集部落","examples":[{"en":"Other fragmented hunter-gathering tribes roamed Eurasia.","zh":"其他分散的狩獵採集部落在歐亞大陸遊蕩。"},{"en":"Fragmented hunter-gathering tribes are scattered groups that live by hunting animals and gathering wild plants.","zh":"fragmented hunter-gathering tribes 是靠狩獵動物和採集野生植物生活的分散群體。"},{"en":"Small forest groups may move often to find food rather than farm one fixed field.","zh":"小型森林群體可能經常移動尋找食物，而不是耕種固定田地。"},{"en":"If tribes are fragmented, they may be less able to resist a larger expanding population.","zh":"如果部落分散，它們可能較難抵抗更大且正在擴張的人口。"},{"en":"This phrase describes scattered non-farming communities.","zh":"這個片語描述分散的非農耕社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"roam the wilds of","meaning":"在……的荒野中遊蕩","examples":[{"en":"Hunter-gathering tribes roamed the wilds of Eurasia.","zh":"狩獵採集部落在歐亞大陸的荒野中遊蕩。"},{"en":"To roam the wilds of a place means to move through its natural, uncultivated areas without settling permanently.","zh":"roam the wilds of a place 指在某地自然、未開墾地區中移動，而不永久定居。"},{"en":"Hikers may roam the wilds of a national park during a long camping trip.","zh":"徒步者可能在長途露營期間於國家公園荒野中漫遊。"},{"en":"If tribes roam wild areas, their lives depend on animals, plants, seasons, and movement.","zh":"如果部落在荒野中遊蕩，其生活取決於動物、植物、季節和移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes free movement through natural landscapes.","zh":"這個片語描述在自然景觀中的自由移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"move alongside","meaning":"伴隨……一起移動","examples":[{"en":"PIE may have moved alongside the outward spread of agriculture.","zh":"原始印歐語可能伴隨農業向外傳播而一起移動。"},{"en":"To move alongside something means to spread or develop at the same time as it.","zh":"move alongside something 指與某事同時傳播或發展。"},{"en":"New shops may move alongside a new railway line as more passengers arrive.","zh":"隨着更多乘客到來，新商店可能伴隨新鐵路線一起出現。"},{"en":"If farming spreads, language may spread with the farmers who carry it.","zh":"如果農耕擴散，語言可能隨着攜帶該語言的農民一起傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two developments happening together.","zh":"這個片語描述兩種發展同步發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"outward spread of agriculture","meaning":"農業向外傳播","examples":[{"en":"The language may have spread with the outward spread of agriculture.","zh":"該語言可能隨着農業向外傳播而擴散。"},{"en":"Outward spread of agriculture means farming moved from an original area into surrounding regions.","zh":"outward spread of agriculture 指農耕從原本地區移向周邊地區。"},{"en":"A history map may show the outward spread of rice farming from river valleys to nearby plains.","zh":"歷史地圖可能展示稻作農業如何從河谷向附近平原傳播。"},{"en":"If agriculture spreads outward, population, settlements, and languages may spread too.","zh":"如果農業向外傳播，人口、聚落和語言也可能一起傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase connects farming expansion with wider social change.","zh":"這個片語把農耕擴張與更廣泛社會變化連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rapidly expanding population","meaning":"快速擴張的人口","examples":[{"en":"The language spread with a rapidly expanding population.","zh":"該語言隨着快速擴張的人口而傳播。"},{"en":"A rapidly expanding population is a population that is growing quickly in number and area.","zh":"rapidly expanding population 是數量和分布地區迅速增長的人口。"},{"en":"A town with many new families may become a rapidly expanding population centre.","zh":"有許多新家庭遷入的小鎮可能成為快速擴張的人口中心。"},{"en":"If a population grows quickly, it may need more land, food, and settlements.","zh":"如果人口快速增長，它可能需要更多土地、食物和聚落。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fast demographic growth.","zh":"這個片語描述快速人口增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"interbreeding population","meaning":"相互通婚繁衍的人口","examples":[{"en":"The tribe may have spread with an interbreeding population.","zh":"該部落可能隨着相互通婚繁衍的人口而擴散。"},{"en":"An interbreeding population is a group whose members have children with one another and share genes over time.","zh":"interbreeding population 是成員彼此生育後代並隨時間共享基因的群體。"},{"en":"In a small village, families may form an interbreeding population across generations.","zh":"在小村莊中，家庭可能經過幾代形成相互通婚繁衍的人口。"},{"en":"If populations interbreed as they spread, genetic evidence may show movement and contact.","zh":"如果人口在擴散時互相通婚，遺傳證據可能顯示移動和接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes biological mixing within or between groups.","zh":"這個片語描述群體內或群體之間的生物混合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"audacious linguists","meaning":"大膽的語言學家","examples":[{"en":"Audacious linguists are digging deeper into the past.","zh":"大膽的語言學家正在更深入追溯過去。"},{"en":"Audacious linguists are bold language scholars willing to make difficult or risky arguments.","zh":"audacious linguists 是願意提出困難或具風險論點的大膽語言學者。"},{"en":"An audacious researcher may ask questions that more cautious scholars avoid.","zh":"大膽研究者可能提出較謹慎學者會避免的問題。"},{"en":"If linguists look beyond well-supported evidence, their ideas may be exciting but controversial.","zh":"如果語言學家超出證據充分支持的範圍，其想法可能令人興奮但具爭議。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bold scholars in language study.","zh":"這個片語描述語言研究中的大膽學者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"dig deeper into the past","meaning":"更深入追溯過去","examples":[{"en":"Linguists are digging deeper into the past to find earlier languages.","zh":"語言學家正更深入追溯過去，以尋找更早期語言。"},{"en":"To dig deeper into the past means to investigate older and older periods of history.","zh":"dig deeper into the past 指調查越來越古老的歷史時期。"},{"en":"A student may dig deeper into family history by interviewing grandparents and reading old letters.","zh":"學生可能透過訪問祖父母和閱讀舊信，更深入追溯家族歷史。"},{"en":"If researchers dig too deep without enough evidence, conclusions may become uncertain.","zh":"如果研究人員在證據不足下追溯得太深，結論可能變得不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deeper historical investigation.","zh":"這個片語描述更深入的歷史調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"give birth to","meaning":"產生；孕育出","examples":[{"en":"PIE gave birth to a large family of languages.","zh":"原始印歐語孕育出一大語系。"},{"en":"To give birth to something means to produce it or cause it to begin.","zh":"give birth to something 指產生某事或令某事開始。"},{"en":"A small student idea can give birth to a successful school club.","zh":"一個學生小想法可以孕育出成功的學校社團。"},{"en":"If one ancient language gives birth to many later languages, it becomes their ancestor.","zh":"如果一種古代語言孕育出許多後來語言，它就成為它們的祖先。"},{"en":"This phrase uses birth as a metaphor for origin.","zh":"這個片語用出生作為起源的比喻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a large family of languages","meaning":"一大語系","examples":[{"en":"PIE gave birth to a large family of languages.","zh":"原始印歐語孕育出一大語系。"},{"en":"A large family of languages is a broad group of related languages with many members.","zh":"large family of languages 是包含許多成員的廣泛相關語言群。"},{"en":"A language tree can show how a large family of languages branches into smaller groups.","zh":"語言樹可以顯示一大語系如何分成較小分支。"},{"en":"If a family is large, its languages may be spoken across many countries.","zh":"如果語系很大，其語言可能在許多國家被使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a wide group of historically related languages.","zh":"這個片語描述一大組歷史上相關的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Afro-Asiatic","meaning":"亞非語系","examples":[{"en":"Afro-Asiatic is another major language family.","zh":"亞非語系是另一個主要語系。"},{"en":"Afro-Asiatic is a language family that includes languages spoken in parts of Africa and western Asia.","zh":"Afro-Asiatic 是包括非洲部分地區和西亞一些語言的語系。"},{"en":"Arabic belongs to the Afro-Asiatic family.","zh":"阿拉伯語屬於亞非語系。"},{"en":"If scholars compare major language families, Afro-Asiatic is often discussed alongside Indo-European.","zh":"如果學者比較主要語系，亞非語系常與印歐語系一起被討論。"},{"en":"This term names a large family of related languages.","zh":"這個術語指出一大相關語言家族。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"include Arabic","meaning":"包括阿拉伯語","examples":[{"en":"Afro-Asiatic includes Arabic.","zh":"亞非語系包括阿拉伯語。"},{"en":"To include Arabic means that Arabic is one member or part of the group being described.","zh":"include Arabic 指阿拉伯語是所描述群體中的一個成員或部分。"},{"en":"A language course may include Arabic if many students are interested in Middle Eastern culture.","zh":"如果許多學生對中東文化感興趣，語言課程可能包括阿拉伯語。"},{"en":"If a family includes Arabic, scholars may compare Arabic with other related languages.","zh":"如果一個語系包括阿拉伯語，學者可能把阿拉伯語與其他相關語言比較。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that Arabic belongs inside a larger category.","zh":"這個片語顯示阿拉伯語屬於更大類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Dravidian","meaning":"達羅毗荼語系","examples":[{"en":"Dravidian comprises many languages of Southern India.","zh":"達羅毗荼語系包括印度南部許多語言。"},{"en":"Dravidian is a language family spoken mainly in southern India and nearby regions.","zh":"Dravidian 是主要在印度南部和附近地區使用的語系。"},{"en":"Tamil is one well-known Dravidian language.","zh":"泰米爾語是一種著名達羅毗荼語言。"},{"en":"If a language belongs to Dravidian, it is not part of the Indo-European family in the usual classification.","zh":"如果一種語言屬於達羅毗荼語系，按通常分類它不屬於印歐語系。"},{"en":"This term names a major South Asian language family.","zh":"這個術語指出南亞一個主要語系。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"comprise","meaning":"包括；由……組成","examples":[{"en":"Dravidian comprises many languages of Southern India.","zh":"達羅毗荼語系包括印度南部許多語言。"},{"en":"To comprise something means to include or be made up of it.","zh":"comprise something 指包括某物或由某物組成。"},{"en":"A school lunch may comprise rice, vegetables, soup, and fruit.","zh":"學校午餐可能包括米飯、蔬菜、湯和水果。"},{"en":"If a language family comprises many languages, it contains several related members.","zh":"如果一個語系包括許多語言，它就包含幾個相關成員。"},{"en":"This word is a formal way to say include or consist of.","zh":"這個詞是表示包括或由……組成的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Southern India","meaning":"印度南部","examples":[{"en":"Many Dravidian languages are spoken in Southern India.","zh":"許多達羅毗荼語言在印度南部使用。"},{"en":"Southern India means the southern part of India, including regions where many Dravidian languages are used.","zh":"Southern India 指印度南部，包括許多達羅毗荼語言被使用的地區。"},{"en":"A travel programme may show the food, temples, and languages of Southern India.","zh":"旅遊節目可能展示印度南部的食物、寺廟和語言。"},{"en":"If a language is common in Southern India, it may have a different history from northern Indo-Aryan languages.","zh":"如果一種語言在印度南部常見，它可能有不同於北方印度—雅利安語言的歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a broad geographical location.","zh":"這個片語給出大致地理位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Altaic","meaning":"阿爾泰語系","examples":[{"en":"Altaic has been proposed as another language family.","zh":"阿爾泰語系被提出為另一個語系。"},{"en":"Altaic is a proposed language family that some scholars have used to group several Eurasian languages.","zh":"Altaic 是一個被提出的語系，一些學者曾用它把幾種歐亞語言歸類。"},{"en":"A linguistics class may discuss Altaic as an example of a debated classification.","zh":"語言學課可能討論阿爾泰語系，把它作為有爭議分類的例子。"},{"en":"If a language family is only proposed, scholars may disagree about whether it is real.","zh":"如果語系只是被提出，學者可能不同意它是否真實存在。"},{"en":"This term refers to a controversial language-family proposal.","zh":"這個術語指一項有爭議的語系提案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"belong to","meaning":"屬於","examples":[{"en":"Some language families may belong to a macro-family.","zh":"一些語系可能屬於一個大語系。"},{"en":"To belong to something means to be a member or part of that larger group.","zh":"belong to something 指成為較大群體的成員或部分。"},{"en":"A student may belong to a debate club and a music club at the same time.","zh":"學生可能同時屬於辯論學會和音樂學會。"},{"en":"If a language family belongs to a larger macro-family, its history may be even deeper.","zh":"如果一個語系屬於更大的宏語系，其歷史可能更加深遠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes membership or classification.","zh":"這個片語描述成員關係或分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"macro-family","meaning":"大語系；宏語系","examples":[{"en":"Proto-Nostratic has been proposed as a macro-family.","zh":"原始諾斯特拉語被提出為一個宏語系。"},{"en":"A macro-family is a proposed very large language family that includes several smaller language families.","zh":"macro-family 是被提出的超大型語系，包括幾個較小語系。"},{"en":"A teacher may compare a macro-family to a very large family tree with many branches.","zh":"老師可能把宏語系比作有許多分支的巨大族譜。"},{"en":"If a macro-family is proposed, scholars must show evidence linking distant language groups.","zh":"如果有人提出宏語系，學者必須展示連接遙遠語言群的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very broad language classification.","zh":"這個片語描述非常廣泛的語言分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Proto-Nostratic","meaning":"原始諾斯特拉語","examples":[{"en":"Some linguists call the proposed macro-family Proto-Nostratic.","zh":"一些語言學家把這個被提出的大語系稱為原始諾斯特拉語。"},{"en":"Proto-Nostratic is a proposed ancient ancestor language or macro-family behind several major language families.","zh":"Proto-Nostratic 是被提出的古代祖語或宏語系，位於幾個主要語系背後。"},{"en":"A linguistics textbook may mention Proto-Nostratic as a debated idea rather than a settled fact.","zh":"語言學教科書可能把原始諾斯特拉語作為有爭議想法，而非既定事實提及。"},{"en":"If evidence for Proto-Nostratic is weak, many scholars will remain sceptical.","zh":"如果支持原始諾斯特拉語的證據薄弱，許多學者會保持懷疑。"},{"en":"This term refers to a highly controversial deep-origin language hypothesis.","zh":"這個術語指高度具爭議的深層語言起源假說。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"maintain that","meaning":"堅持認為","examples":[{"en":"Most linguists maintain that the claim is difficult to prove.","zh":"大多數語言學家堅持認為這項主張很難證明。"},{"en":"To maintain that something is true means to continue to argue or believe it.","zh":"maintain that something is true 指繼續主張或相信某事屬實。"},{"en":"A teacher may maintain that daily reading is more useful than last-minute memorisation.","zh":"老師可能堅持認為每日閱讀比臨急背誦更有用。"},{"en":"If experts maintain a position, they usually have reasons for not changing their view.","zh":"如果專家堅持某立場，他們通常有理由不改變看法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a firmly held opinion.","zh":"這個片語引入堅定持有的意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"theoretically possible","meaning":"理論上可能","examples":[{"en":"It is theoretically possible that such an original language existed.","zh":"這樣一種原始語言理論上可能存在。"},{"en":"Theoretically possible means possible in theory, even if there is not enough proof or practical evidence.","zh":"theoretically possible 指在理論上可能，即使沒有足夠證據或實際支持。"},{"en":"It is theoretically possible to finish a project overnight, but the quality may be poor.","zh":"一晚完成項目理論上可能，但質素可能很差。"},{"en":"If an idea is only theoretically possible, researchers still need evidence before accepting it.","zh":"如果想法只是理論上可能，研究人員仍需要證據才接受。"},{"en":"This phrase separates possibility from proof.","zh":"這個片語把可能性與證明分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"original language","meaning":"原始語言","examples":[{"en":"Some scholars propose that an original language existed before PIE.","zh":"一些學者提出，在原始印歐語之前曾存在一種原始語言。"},{"en":"An original language is an earlier source language from which later languages may have developed.","zh":"original language 是後來語言可能由其發展而來的較早源頭語言。"},{"en":"A family may speak a home dialect that is closer to the original language of their village.","zh":"家庭可能說一種家庭方言，較接近其村莊的原始語言。"},{"en":"If scholars search for an original language, they are looking for deeper linguistic ancestry.","zh":"如果學者尋找原始語言，他們是在尋找更深層語言祖源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a proposed starting point for later languages.","zh":"這個片語描述後來語言被提出的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"next to impossible to prove","meaning":"幾乎不可能證明","examples":[{"en":"The existence of Proto-Nostratic is next to impossible to prove.","zh":"原始諾斯特拉語的存在幾乎不可能證明。"},{"en":"Next to impossible to prove means almost impossible to show with convincing evidence.","zh":"next to impossible to prove 指幾乎無法用有說服力的證據證明。"},{"en":"It is next to impossible to prove who first used a playground nickname years ago.","zh":"要證明多年前誰最先使用某個操場綽號幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"If evidence has disappeared, even a true idea may be nearly impossible to prove.","zh":"如果證據已消失，即使想法是真的，也可能幾乎不可能證明。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extreme difficulty in proving a claim.","zh":"這個片語描述證明某主張極度困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"resemblances among languages","meaning":"語言之間的相似之處","examples":[{"en":"Resemblances among languages can be due to chance.","zh":"語言之間的相似之處可能由偶然造成。"},{"en":"Resemblances among languages are similarities in sound, words, or grammar between different languages.","zh":"resemblances among languages 是不同語言在聲音、詞語或語法上的相似。"},{"en":"Two unrelated languages may have similar-sounding words by coincidence.","zh":"兩種無關語言可能因巧合有發音相似的詞。"},{"en":"If similarities are only surface-level, they may not prove common origin.","zh":"如果相似只停留在表面，它們未必證明共同起源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes language similarities that need careful interpretation.","zh":"這個片語描述需要謹慎詮釋的語言相似性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be due to chance","meaning":"由偶然造成","examples":[{"en":"Some resemblances among languages may be due to chance.","zh":"一些語言之間的相似可能由偶然造成。"},{"en":"To be due to chance means to happen accidentally rather than because of a real connection.","zh":"be due to chance 指因偶然而發生，而不是因真實連繫。"},{"en":"Two students may choose the same essay title purely due to chance.","zh":"兩名學生可能純粹因偶然選擇同一作文題目。"},{"en":"If a similarity is due to chance, it should not be treated as strong evidence.","zh":"如果相似由偶然造成，就不應被視為強證據。"},{"en":"This phrase separates coincidence from meaningful cause.","zh":"這個片語把巧合與有意義原因分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"remain sceptical of","meaning":"對……仍持懷疑態度","examples":[{"en":"Most linguists remain sceptical of the Proto-Nostratic claim.","zh":"大多數語言學家對原始諾斯特拉語的主張仍持懷疑態度。"},{"en":"To remain sceptical of something means to continue doubting it.","zh":"remain sceptical of something 指繼續懷疑某事。"},{"en":"A parent may remain sceptical of a miracle study plan until they see real improvement.","zh":"家長在看到真正進步前，可能對神奇學習計劃仍持懷疑態度。"},{"en":"If evidence is weak, experts may remain sceptical even when the idea is attractive.","zh":"如果證據薄弱，即使想法吸引，專家仍可能保持懷疑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continued doubt.","zh":"這個片語描述持續懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"such a claim","meaning":"這樣的主張","examples":[{"en":"Linguists are sceptical of such a claim.","zh":"語言學家對這樣的主張持懷疑態度。"},{"en":"Such a claim means a statement or argument of the type just mentioned.","zh":"such a claim 指剛提到那類陳述或論點。"},{"en":"If someone says one week is enough to master English, teachers may question such a claim.","zh":"如果有人說一星期足以精通英語，老師可能質疑這樣的主張。"},{"en":"If a claim is very large, it needs strong evidence before experts accept it.","zh":"如果主張非常重大，它需要強證據才會被專家接受。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a claim already described.","zh":"這個片語回指已描述的主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"mind-boggling","meaning":"令人難以置信的；令人震驚的","examples":[{"en":"It is mind-boggling that many languages may share one source.","zh":"許多語言可能共享同一源頭，這令人難以置信。"},{"en":"Mind-boggling means extremely surprising, difficult to imagine, or hard to fully understand.","zh":"mind-boggling 指極令人驚訝、難以想像或難以完全理解。"},{"en":"It is mind-boggling to think that a phone can store thousands of books.","zh":"想到一部電話可以儲存數千本書，令人震驚。"},{"en":"If almost all languages came from one source, the scale of language history is astonishing.","zh":"如果幾乎所有語言來自同一源頭，語言歷史的規模令人驚訝。"},{"en":"This word describes something that overwhelms the mind.","zh":"這個詞描述令人腦袋難以承受的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"almost every single language on Earth","meaning":"地球上幾乎每一種語言","examples":[{"en":"Almost every single language on Earth may trace back to one source.","zh":"地球上幾乎每一種語言可能追溯到同一源頭。"},{"en":"Almost every single language on Earth means nearly all languages spoken anywhere in the world.","zh":"almost every single language on Earth 指世界各地幾乎所有被使用的語言。"},{"en":"A claim about almost every language on Earth is extremely broad and needs strong evidence.","zh":"關於地球上幾乎每一種語言的主張非常廣泛，需要強證據。"},{"en":"If nearly all languages share one source, human speech may have a common deep history.","zh":"如果幾乎所有語言共享同一源頭，人類語言可能有共同深層歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses an almost complete global scale.","zh":"這個片語強調幾乎完整的全球規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ultimately be traced back to","meaning":"最終可追溯至……","examples":[{"en":"Many languages may ultimately be traced back to a single source.","zh":"許多語言最終可追溯至單一源頭。"},{"en":"To ultimately be traced back to something means to be followed back to the deepest or final origin.","zh":"ultimately be traced back to something 指被一路追溯到最深或最終起源。"},{"en":"A family tradition may ultimately be traced back to one grandparent’s habit.","zh":"家庭傳統最終可能追溯至某位祖父母的習慣。"},{"en":"If languages are traced back far enough, scholars may find older and older shared roots.","zh":"如果語言被追溯得足夠遠，學者可能找到越來越古老的共同詞根。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching the deepest known source.","zh":"這個片語描述到達最深的已知源頭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a single source","meaning":"單一源頭","examples":[{"en":"Many languages may have come from a single source.","zh":"許多語言可能來自單一源頭。"},{"en":"A single source is one origin from which several things develop.","zh":"single source 是幾件事物由其發展而來的一個起源。"},{"en":"Several rumours in a school may come from a single source, such as one misunderstood message.","zh":"學校裡幾個傳聞可能來自單一源頭，例如一個被誤解的訊息。"},{"en":"If many languages share one source, their differences developed later.","zh":"如果許多語言共享一個源頭，它們的差異是後來發展出來的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one common origin.","zh":"這個片語描述一個共同起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a small group of individuals","meaning":"一小群人","examples":[{"en":"The original language may have been spoken by a small group of individuals.","zh":"原始語言可能由一小群人使用。"},{"en":"A small group of individuals means a limited number of people.","zh":"small group of individuals 指有限數量的人。"},{"en":"A small group of students may start a club before it grows into a school-wide activity.","zh":"一小群學生可能先創立社團，然後它發展成全校活動。"},{"en":"If a language begins with a small group, migration and population growth can spread it widely.","zh":"如果語言始於一小群人，遷徙和人口增長可以使它廣泛傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on a limited original community.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於有限的原始社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Proto-Human","meaning":"原始人類語言","examples":[{"en":"Proto-Human is sometimes called the mother of all languages.","zh":"原始人類語言有時被稱為所有語言之母。"},{"en":"Proto-Human is a proposed original human language from which all later languages may have developed.","zh":"Proto-Human 是被提出的一種原始人類語言，所有後來語言可能由其發展而來。"},{"en":"A linguistics teacher may present Proto-Human as a fascinating idea that is very hard to prove.","zh":"語言學老師可能把原始人類語言介紹為一個迷人但極難證明的想法。"},{"en":"If Proto-Human existed, all languages would share one extremely ancient ancestor.","zh":"如果原始人類語言曾存在，所有語言就共享一個極古老祖先。"},{"en":"This term refers to a speculative deep-origin language.","zh":"這個術語指一種推測性的深層起源語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"one interesting theory","meaning":"一個有趣的理論","examples":[{"en":"One interesting theory links language development to a catastrophe.","zh":"一個有趣的理論把語言發展與一場災難連繫起來。"},{"en":"One interesting theory means one explanation or idea that is worth attention.","zh":"one interesting theory 指一個值得注意的解釋或想法。"},{"en":"One interesting theory about sleep is that the brain uses it to organise memories.","zh":"關於睡眠的一個有趣理論是，大腦利用睡眠整理記憶。"},{"en":"If a theory connects language with disaster, it may make students think about history differently.","zh":"如果一個理論把語言與災難連接起來，它可能令學生以不同方式思考歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a noteworthy but not necessarily proven idea.","zh":"這個片語引入值得注意但不一定已被證明的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be posited by","meaning":"由……提出","examples":[{"en":"One theory has been posited by geologists.","zh":"一個理論由地質學家提出。"},{"en":"To be posited by someone means to be suggested or proposed by them as an idea.","zh":"be posited by someone 指由某人作為想法提出或假設。"},{"en":"A new explanation for student stress may be posited by school counsellors.","zh":"關於學生壓力的新解釋可能由學校輔導員提出。"},{"en":"If a theory is posited by experts in another field, it may bring a fresh perspective.","zh":"如果理論由另一領域專家提出，它可能帶來新視角。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an idea being formally proposed.","zh":"這個片語描述想法被正式提出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"geologists","meaning":"地質學家","examples":[{"en":"Geologists have posited a theory about Mount Toba.","zh":"地質學家提出了一個關於多巴火山的理論。"},{"en":"Geologists are scientists who study rocks, Earth history, volcanoes, and geological processes.","zh":"geologists 是研究岩石、地球歷史、火山和地質過程的科學家。"},{"en":"Geologists may examine volcanic ash to understand ancient eruptions.","zh":"地質學家可能檢查火山灰，以理解古代火山爆發。"},{"en":"If geologists study a huge eruption, they can estimate its effects on climate and life.","zh":"如果地質學家研究巨大火山爆發，他們可以估算其對氣候和生命的影響。"},{"en":"This word refers to scientists who study the Earth.","zh":"這個詞指研究地球的科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"huge catastrophe","meaning":"巨大災難","examples":[{"en":"A huge catastrophe may have occurred about 70,000 years ago.","zh":"約七萬年前可能發生了一場巨大災難。"},{"en":"A huge catastrophe is a very large disaster that causes major damage or change.","zh":"huge catastrophe 是造成重大破壞或變化的非常大災難。"},{"en":"A massive earthquake can be a huge catastrophe for a city.","zh":"大地震可以成為城市的巨大災難。"},{"en":"If a catastrophe affects the whole planet, it may change population, climate, and history.","zh":"如果災難影響整個星球，它可能改變人口、氣候和歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a disaster of enormous scale.","zh":"這個片語描述規模極大的災難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"occur in","meaning":"發生於","examples":[{"en":"A catastrophe may have occurred in the not-so-distant past.","zh":"一場災難可能發生於不算太遙遠的過去。"},{"en":"To occur in a period or place means to happen there or then.","zh":"occur in a period or place 指在某時期或地點發生。"},{"en":"A power cut may occur in a school during a storm.","zh":"暴風雨期間，學校可能發生停電。"},{"en":"If an event occurred long ago, researchers need evidence to reconstruct it.","zh":"如果事件發生在很久以前，研究人員需要證據來重建它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where or when something happens.","zh":"這個片語描述某事發生的地點或時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the not-so-distant past","meaning":"不算太遙遠的過去","examples":[{"en":"The catastrophe occurred in the not-so-distant past.","zh":"這場災難發生於不算太遙遠的過去。"},{"en":"The not-so-distant past means a past time that is old, but not extremely ancient in human history.","zh":"not-so-distant past 指過去的某個時期，雖然久遠，但在人類歷史中不算極古老。"},{"en":"In the not-so-distant past, many students still submitted homework only on paper.","zh":"在不算太遙遠的過去，許多學生仍只交紙本功課。"},{"en":"If an event happened in the not-so-distant past, some traces may still remain.","zh":"如果事件發生於不算太遠的過去，一些痕跡可能仍然存在。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the past feel closer than expected.","zh":"這個片語令過去感覺比預期更接近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be linked to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The catastrophe was linked to the volcanic eruption of Mount Toba.","zh":"這場災難與多巴火山爆發有關。"},{"en":"To be linked to something means to be connected with it as a cause, result, or related event.","zh":"be linked to something 指與某事作為原因、結果或相關事件有連繫。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is often linked to lower concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足常與課堂專注力下降有關。"},{"en":"If a population decline is linked to an eruption, climate effects may be part of the explanation.","zh":"如果人口下降與火山爆發有關，氣候影響可能是解釋的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a meaningful connection.","zh":"這個片語描述有意義的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"volcanic eruption","meaning":"火山爆發","examples":[{"en":"The volcanic eruption of Mount Toba may have changed human history.","zh":"多巴火山爆發可能改變了人類歷史。"},{"en":"A volcanic eruption is an event in which lava, ash, gases, or rock are released from a volcano.","zh":"volcanic eruption 是火山釋放熔岩、火山灰、氣體或岩石的事件。"},{"en":"A volcanic eruption can close airports if ash spreads into the sky.","zh":"如果火山灰擴散到天空，火山爆發可以令機場關閉。"},{"en":"If an eruption is huge, it can affect climate, food supply, and human survival.","zh":"如果爆發規模巨大，它可以影響氣候、食物供應和人類生存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a powerful geological event.","zh":"這個片語描述強大的地質事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Mount Toba","meaning":"多巴火山","examples":[{"en":"Mount Toba is a volcano in Indonesia.","zh":"多巴火山是位於印尼的一座火山。"},{"en":"Mount Toba is the volcano linked to a huge ancient eruption in the theory discussed.","zh":"Mount Toba 是該理論中與巨大古代爆發相關的火山。"},{"en":"Students may locate Mount Toba on a map to understand where the eruption occurred.","zh":"學生可能在地圖上找出多巴火山，以理解爆發發生在哪裡。"},{"en":"If Mount Toba affected global climate, its eruption would have had worldwide consequences.","zh":"如果多巴火山影響全球氣候，其爆發就會帶來世界性後果。"},{"en":"This phrase names the volcanic site central to the theory.","zh":"這個片語指出該理論中的核心火山地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"according to this theory","meaning":"根據這個理論","examples":[{"en":"According to this theory, the eruption reduced the world population.","zh":"根據這個理論，火山爆發使世界人口減少。"},{"en":"According to this theory means based on this particular explanation or claim.","zh":"according to this theory 指根據這個特定解釋或主張。"},{"en":"According to this theory, students learn better when examples come before rules.","zh":"根據這個理論，學生先看例子再學規則會學得更好。"},{"en":"If a sentence begins this way, the writer is reporting a theory, not necessarily proven fact.","zh":"如果句子以這種說法開始，作者是在報道理論，不一定是已證實事實。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces information from a specific explanation.","zh":"這個片語引入來自特定解釋的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"reduce the world population to","meaning":"使世界人口減少至……","examples":[{"en":"The eruption may have reduced the world population to a small band of survivors.","zh":"火山爆發可能使世界人口減少至一小群倖存者。"},{"en":"To reduce the world population to a number or group means to cause it to fall to that level.","zh":"reduce the world population to a number or group 指使世界人口下降到某個水平。"},{"en":"A disease outbreak in a story might reduce a village population to only a few families.","zh":"故事中的疾病爆發可能使村莊人口減少至只剩幾個家庭。"},{"en":"If a disaster reduces a population sharply, later generations may all descend from fewer survivors.","zh":"如果災難令人口急劇減少，後來世代可能都由較少倖存者繁衍而來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a dramatic decrease in population.","zh":"這個片語描述人口劇烈下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a small band of survivors","meaning":"一小群倖存者","examples":[{"en":"The world population may have been reduced to a small band of survivors.","zh":"世界人口可能被減少至一小群倖存者。"},{"en":"A small band of survivors is a small group of people who remain alive after a disaster.","zh":"small band of survivors 是災難後仍然活着的一小群人。"},{"en":"After a shipwreck in a novel, a small band of survivors may reach an island.","zh":"在小說中的船難後，一小群倖存者可能到達一個島。"},{"en":"If only a small group survives, their language and genes may shape later populations strongly.","zh":"如果只有一小群人存活，他們的語言和基因可能強烈塑造後來人口。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a tiny surviving group after catastrophe.","zh":"這個片語描述災難後的小型倖存群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"give rise to","meaning":"產生；引致","examples":[{"en":"The Proto-Human language may have given rise to all subsequent languages.","zh":"原始人類語言可能產生了所有後來語言。"},{"en":"To give rise to something means to cause it to appear, develop, or begin.","zh":"give rise to something 指導致某事出現、發展或開始。"},{"en":"A small classroom argument can give rise to a wider discussion about fairness.","zh":"課室中一場小爭論可以引發關於公平的更廣泛討論。"},{"en":"If one language gives rise to many later languages, it becomes their common source.","zh":"如果一種語言產生許多後來語言，它就成為它們的共同源頭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes origin and cause.","zh":"這個片語描述起源和原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"subsequent languages","meaning":"後來的語言","examples":[{"en":"The survivors’ language may have given rise to all subsequent languages.","zh":"倖存者的語言可能產生所有後來的語言。"},{"en":"Subsequent languages are languages that developed later after an earlier language.","zh":"subsequent languages 是在較早語言之後發展出來的語言。"},{"en":"Latin influenced many subsequent languages in Europe.","zh":"拉丁語影響了歐洲許多後來的語言。"},{"en":"If one early language shaped subsequent languages, later speech forms may still carry traces of it.","zh":"如果一種早期語言塑造後來語言，後來說話形式可能仍保留其痕跡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes languages that come afterward.","zh":"這個片語描述其後出現的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"if this is true","meaning":"如果這是真的","examples":[{"en":"If this is true, the catastrophe shaped the languages we speak today.","zh":"如果這是真的，那場災難塑造了我們今天所說的語言。"},{"en":"If this is true means if the claim or theory is correct.","zh":"if this is true 指如果該主張或理論正確。"},{"en":"If this is true, the school may need to change its homework policy quickly.","zh":"如果這是真的，學校可能需要迅速改變功課政策。"},{"en":"When writers use this phrase, they often explore the consequences of an uncertain idea.","zh":"作者使用這個片語時，常探討一個不確定想法的後果。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a possible result based on a condition.","zh":"這個片語根據條件引入可能結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"it is intriguing to think that","meaning":"想到……實在耐人尋味","examples":[{"en":"It is intriguing to think that we might otherwise speak totally different languages.","zh":"想到否則我們今天可能說完全不同的語言，實在耐人尋味。"},{"en":"It is intriguing to think that means it is interesting and thought-provoking to imagine that.","zh":"it is intriguing to think that 指想像某事令人感興趣並引人深思。"},{"en":"It is intriguing to think that one small decision can change a person’s whole career.","zh":"想到一個小決定可以改變一個人的整個事業，實在耐人尋味。"},{"en":"If a theory changes how we imagine history, it can feel intellectually exciting.","zh":"如果理論改變我們想像歷史的方式，它會令人感到智性上的興奮。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a fascinating possibility.","zh":"這個片語引入令人着迷的可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"had that catastrophe not occurred","meaning":"如果那場災難沒有發生","examples":[{"en":"Had that catastrophe not occurred, languages might have developed differently.","zh":"如果那場災難沒有發生，語言可能會以不同方式發展。"},{"en":"Had that catastrophe not occurred means if that disaster had not happened.","zh":"had that catastrophe not occurred 指如果那場災難沒有發生。"},{"en":"Had the train not been delayed, the students would have arrived on time.","zh":"如果火車沒有延誤，學生本來會準時到達。"},{"en":"This structure imagines a different past and its possible result.","zh":"這種結構想像一個不同的過去及其可能結果。"},{"en":"It is a formal conditional pattern used for unreal past situations.","zh":"這是一種用於非真實過去情況的正式條件句式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"totally different languages","meaning":"完全不同的語言","examples":[{"en":"We might all be speaking totally different languages today.","zh":"我們今天可能全都在說完全不同的語言。"},{"en":"Totally different languages means languages that are completely unlike the ones we now know or use.","zh":"totally different languages 指與我們現在知道或使用的語言完全不同的語言。"},{"en":"If history had changed, a country might speak a totally different official language today.","zh":"如果歷史改變，一個國家今天可能使用完全不同的官方語言。"},{"en":"If early human groups had survived differently, later languages might not resemble modern ones.","zh":"如果早期人類群體以不同方式存活，後來語言可能不像現代語言。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses complete difference.","zh":"這個片語強調完全差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete the sentences","meaning":"完成句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the sentences with words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用篇章中的字詞完成句子。"},{"en":"To complete the sentences means to fill in missing words so each sentence becomes whole and grammatical.","zh":"complete the sentences 指填入缺失字詞，使每句完整且合乎文法。"},{"en":"Students should read before and after each blank before completing the sentence.","zh":"學生完成句子前，應閱讀每個空格前後內容。"},{"en":"If the answer does not fit the grammar, it is probably wrong.","zh":"如果答案不符合文法，它很可能是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案應不多於兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must use one or two words only.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案只可使用一個或兩個英文詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “linguistic circles”, students should not add extra explanation.","zh":"如果答案是 “linguistic circles”，學生不應加入額外解釋。"},{"en":"If students write three words, the answer may be marked wrong even if the meaning is close.","zh":"如果學生寫三個詞，即使意思接近，也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit for exam answers.","zh":"這個片語給出考試答案的嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"findings","meaning":"研究發現","examples":[{"en":"William Jones’s findings are important in linguistics.","zh":"William Jones 的研究發現在語言學中很重要。"},{"en":"Findings are results or conclusions discovered through research or investigation.","zh":"findings 是透過研究或調查發現的結果或結論。"},{"en":"A school survey’s findings may show that students want more reading time.","zh":"學校調查的研究發現可能顯示學生想有更多閱讀時間。"},{"en":"If findings are strong, they can change how experts understand a subject.","zh":"如果研究發現有力，它們可以改變專家對某主題的理解。"},{"en":"This word refers to what research discovers.","zh":"這個詞指研究發現了甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be mostly known within","meaning":"主要在……內為人所知","examples":[{"en":"Jones’s findings are mostly known within linguistic circles.","zh":"Jones 的研究發現主要在語言學界內為人所知。"},{"en":"To be mostly known within a group means mainly people in that group know about it.","zh":"be mostly known within a group 指主要由該群體的人知道。"},{"en":"A useful classroom technique may be mostly known within teacher-training circles.","zh":"一種有用課堂技巧可能主要在教師培訓圈內為人所知。"},{"en":"If a discovery is technical, it may be known among experts but not the public.","zh":"如果發現很專門，它可能在專家中知名，但公眾不知道。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited specialist awareness.","zh":"這個片語描述有限的專門認知。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"speak a proto-language","meaning":"使用原始語言","examples":[{"en":"A community may speak a proto-language over a limited area.","zh":"一個社群可能在有限地區使用原始語言。"},{"en":"To speak a proto-language means to use an earlier ancestor form of a group of later languages.","zh":"speak a proto-language 指使用一組後來語言的較早祖先形式。"},{"en":"A small ancient community may have spoken a language that later developed into several dialects.","zh":"小型古代社群可能曾使用一種後來發展成幾種方言的語言。"},{"en":"If one community speaks a proto-language, later migration can spread and change it.","zh":"如果一個社群使用原始語言，後來遷徙可以使它傳播並改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the use of an ancestral language.","zh":"這個片語描述祖語的使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"might have come from","meaning":"可能來自……","examples":[{"en":"Proto-Indo-Europeans might have come from the Caspian Steppe.","zh":"原始印歐人可能來自裏海草原。"},{"en":"Might have come from means possibly originated in a place, but not with complete certainty.","zh":"might have come from 指可能起源於某地，但並非完全確定。"},{"en":"A family surname might have come from a village name or an old occupation.","zh":"家族姓氏可能來自村名或古老職業。"},{"en":"If evidence is incomplete, scholars use might to show uncertainty.","zh":"如果證據不完整，學者用 might 表示不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a cautious claim about origin.","zh":"這個片語表達關於起源的謹慎主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the site of","meaning":"……的地點","examples":[{"en":"Mount Toba was the site of a volcanic eruption.","zh":"多巴火山是一次火山爆發的地點。"},{"en":"The site of an event is the place where that event happened.","zh":"site of an event 是某事件發生的地方。"},{"en":"The playground was the site of the school’s sports day.","zh":"操場是學校運動日的地點。"},{"en":"If a volcano is the site of a huge eruption, scientists may study rocks and ash there.","zh":"如果一座火山是巨大爆發的地點，科學家可能研究那裡的岩石和火山灰。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the location of an event.","zh":"這個片語指出事件發生地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"write the correct letter","meaning":"寫出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the correct letter for each statement.","zh":"考生為每項陳述寫出正確字母。"},{"en":"To write the correct letter means to choose and record the answer option that matches.","zh":"write the correct letter 指選擇並寫下相配的答案選項字母。"},{"en":"In a matching exercise, students may write B if statement two matches paragraph B.","zh":"在配對練習中，如果第二項陳述配對段落 B，學生可能寫 B。"},{"en":"If the correct idea is found but the wrong letter is written, the answer may still be marked wrong.","zh":"如果找到正確意思但寫錯字母，答案仍可能被判錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"use each answer only once","meaning":"每個答案只可使用一次","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should use each answer only once.","zh":"考生應每個答案只可使用一次。"},{"en":"Use each answer only once means every option can be chosen one time and not repeated.","zh":"use each answer only once 指每個選項只能選一次，不能重複。"},{"en":"In a matching task, if answer A is already used, students must choose another option for the next item.","zh":"在配對題中，如果答案 A 已經使用，學生下一題必須選另一選項。"},{"en":"If students repeat an answer when repetition is not allowed, one response may be wrong.","zh":"如果不允許重複而學生重複使用答案，其中一個回應可能錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a rule about answer choices.","zh":"這個片語給出關於答案選項的規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reliable nutrition","meaning":"可靠的營養來源","examples":[{"en":"Reliable nutrition may help explain population growth and expansion.","zh":"可靠的營養來源可能有助解釋人口增長和擴張。"},{"en":"Reliable nutrition means a steady supply of food that gives people the energy and nutrients they need.","zh":"reliable nutrition 指穩定的食物供應，能提供人們所需能量和營養。"},{"en":"School lunches can provide reliable nutrition for children whose families struggle financially.","zh":"學校午餐可以為經濟困難家庭的孩子提供可靠營養來源。"},{"en":"If a community has reliable nutrition, more people may survive illness, childhood, and hard seasons.","zh":"如果社群有可靠營養來源，更多人可能熬過疾病、童年和艱難季節。"},{"en":"This phrase connects food security with health and population growth.","zh":"這個片語把糧食安全與健康和人口增長連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"categorise languages","meaning":"將語言分類","examples":[{"en":"Scholars have categorised many languages into families.","zh":"學者已將許多語言分類到不同語系。"},{"en":"To categorise languages means to sort them into groups according to shared features or ancestry.","zh":"categorise languages 指根據共同特徵或祖源把語言分組。"},{"en":"A teacher may categorise vocabulary into food, transport, health, and school topics.","zh":"老師可能把詞彙分類為食物、交通、健康和學校主題。"},{"en":"If languages are categorised correctly, their histories and relationships become clearer.","zh":"如果語言被正確分類，其歷史和關係就更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organising languages into meaningful groups.","zh":"這個片語描述把語言組織成有意義的群組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"face anger and controversy","meaning":"面對憤怒和爭議","examples":[{"en":"Some archaeologists face anger and controversy over their claims.","zh":"一些考古學家因其主張而面對憤怒和爭議。"},{"en":"To face anger and controversy means to receive strong criticism and disagreement.","zh":"face anger and controversy 指受到強烈批評和分歧。"},{"en":"A school principal may face anger and controversy after changing the uniform rules.","zh":"校長改變校服規則後，可能面對憤怒和爭議。"},{"en":"If a claim touches national identity, scholars may face stronger emotional reactions.","zh":"如果主張觸及民族身份，學者可能面對更強烈情緒反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes conflict caused by a disputed idea.","zh":"這個片語描述由具爭議想法引起的衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be sceptical about","meaning":"對……持懷疑態度","examples":[{"en":"Many linguists are sceptical about Proto-Nostratic.","zh":"許多語言學家對原始諾斯特拉語持懷疑態度。"},{"en":"To be sceptical about something means to doubt whether it is true or reliable.","zh":"be sceptical about something 指懷疑某事是否真實或可靠。"},{"en":"Parents may be sceptical about a study app that promises perfect grades in one week.","zh":"家長可能對聲稱一星期內成績滿分的學習應用程式持懷疑態度。"},{"en":"If evidence is weak, experts should be sceptical rather than accept the claim quickly.","zh":"如果證據薄弱，專家應保持懷疑，而不是快速接受主張。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful doubt.","zh":"這個片語描述謹慎懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"speculate about","meaning":"推測；猜想","examples":[{"en":"Geologists have speculated about a disaster in the past.","zh":"地質學家推測過去曾發生一場災難。"},{"en":"To speculate about something means to form ideas about it without complete proof.","zh":"speculate about something 指在沒有完整證明下形成關於某事的想法。"},{"en":"Students may speculate about why a teacher suddenly changed the seating plan.","zh":"學生可能猜想老師為何突然改變座位表。"},{"en":"If evidence is incomplete, speculation can suggest possibilities but not prove them.","zh":"如果證據不完整，推測可以提出可能性，但不能證明它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes thoughtful guessing.","zh":"這個片語描述有思考的猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"complete the flow chart","meaning":"完成流程圖","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the flow chart using words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用篇章中的字詞完成流程圖。"},{"en":"To complete the flow chart means to fill missing information into a diagram showing a process or sequence.","zh":"complete the flow chart 指把缺失資訊填入展示過程或次序的圖表中。"},{"en":"Students may complete a flow chart showing how a seed becomes a plant.","zh":"學生可能完成展示種子如何變成植物的流程圖。"},{"en":"If a flow chart shows language development, students should follow the order carefully.","zh":"如果流程圖展示語言發展，學生應仔細跟隨次序。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction for process information.","zh":"這個片語是過程資訊題中的常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the evolution of language","meaning":"語言的演變","examples":[{"en":"The flow chart shows the evolution of language.","zh":"流程圖展示語言的演變。"},{"en":"The evolution of language means the gradual development and change of language over time.","zh":"evolution of language 指語言隨時間逐漸發展和改變。"},{"en":"A class may study the evolution of English from older forms to modern usage.","zh":"課堂可能研究英語如何從較古老形式演變至現代用法。"},{"en":"If people migrate and communities separate, language evolution may produce new dialects and languages.","zh":"如果人們遷徙且社群分離，語言演變可能產生新方言和新語言。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how language changes across history.","zh":"這個片語描述語言如何跨越歷史變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for the final question.","zh":"考生為最後一題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the option letter that gives the right answer.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇給出正確答案的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice question, students should eliminate wrong letters before choosing the correct one.","zh":"在多項選擇題中，學生應先排除錯誤字母，再選正確答案。"},{"en":"If two letters seem possible, students must return to the passage for exact evidence.","zh":"如果兩個字母看似可能，學生必須回到篇章尋找精確證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the author thinks","meaning":"作者認為","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what the author thinks about the subject.","zh":"題目問作者對該主題有甚麼看法。"},{"en":"The author thinks means the writer’s opinion, attitude, or interpretation.","zh":"the author thinks 指作者的意見、態度或詮釋。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students must separate what the author thinks from what other people in the passage claim.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生必須把作者看法與文章中其他人的主張分開。"},{"en":"If the author’s tone is admiring, the answer may show interest or approval.","zh":"如果作者語氣帶欣賞，答案可能顯示興趣或認同。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about the writer’s viewpoint.","zh":"這個片語詢問作者觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complicated","meaning":"複雜的","examples":[{"en":"The history of language is complicated.","zh":"語言歷史是複雜的。"},{"en":"Complicated means involving many parts, details, or causes, so it is not easy to understand quickly.","zh":"complicated 指涉及許多部分、細節或原因，因此不容易快速理解。"},{"en":"A school timetable becomes complicated when teachers, rooms, and exam practice all need to fit together.","zh":"當老師、課室和考試練習都需要配合時，學校時間表會變得複雜。"},{"en":"If language history involves migration, climate, war, and culture, simple answers may be misleading.","zh":"如果語言歷史涉及遷徙、氣候、戰爭和文化，簡單答案可能誤導。"},{"en":"This word describes something with many connected details.","zh":"這個詞描述有許多互相關連細節的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"controversial","meaning":"具爭議性的","examples":[{"en":"The origin of Proto-Indo-European is controversial.","zh":"原始印歐語的起源具爭議性。"},{"en":"Controversial means causing disagreement, debate, or strong opposing opinions.","zh":"controversial 指引起分歧、辯論或強烈相反意見。"},{"en":"A school phone ban can be controversial if students and parents disagree strongly.","zh":"如果學生和家長強烈不同意，學校手機禁令可能具爭議性。"},{"en":"If evidence supports different interpretations, a topic may remain controversial for many years.","zh":"如果證據支持不同詮釋，主題可能多年來仍具爭議。"},{"en":"This word describes something people argue about.","zh":"這個詞描述人們會爭論的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"fascinating","meaning":"令人着迷的","examples":[{"en":"The author clearly finds the subject fascinating.","zh":"作者顯然覺得這個主題令人着迷。"},{"en":"Fascinating means extremely interesting and able to hold people’s attention.","zh":"fascinating 指極有趣，並能吸引人持續注意。"},{"en":"A student may find old maps fascinating because they show how cities changed.","zh":"學生可能覺得舊地圖令人着迷，因為它們展示城市如何改變。"},{"en":"If a topic connects language, history, migration, and human survival, it can feel fascinating.","zh":"如果主題連接語言、歷史、遷徙和人類生存，它會令人着迷。"},{"en":"This word describes something that strongly attracts curiosity.","zh":"這個詞描述強烈吸引好奇心的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 90 - The Mother of All Languages.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 91":[{"front":"waterfalls","meaning":"瀑布","examples":[{"en":"Waterfalls are places where rivers or streams flow over vertical drops.","zh":"瀑布是河流或溪流流過垂直落差的地方。"},{"en":"Waterfalls are natural places where water falls from a higher level to a lower level.","zh":"瀑布是水從較高位置落到較低位置的自然地方。"},{"en":"A family may visit waterfalls during a holiday because the sound and view are impressive.","zh":"一家人可能在假期參觀瀑布，因為聲音和景觀令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"Waterfalls form when flowing water reaches a sudden drop in the land.","zh":"當流動的水到達地面突然下降的地方，瀑布就會形成。"},{"en":"Small waterfalls may be peaceful, while giant waterfalls can feel powerful and dangerous.","zh":"小瀑布可能很平靜，而巨型瀑布則可以感覺強大而危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rivers or streams","meaning":"河流或溪流","examples":[{"en":"Rivers or streams may direct their flow over vertical drops.","zh":"河流或溪流可能使水流流過垂直落差。"},{"en":"Rivers or streams are natural channels of flowing water, with rivers usually larger than streams.","zh":"rivers or streams 指天然流水通道，其中河流通常比溪流較大。"},{"en":"Children may play near small streams, but large rivers can be deep and fast-moving.","zh":"孩子可能在小溪附近玩耍，但大河可以很深且水流很急。"},{"en":"When rivers or streams meet steep rock drops, waterfalls may form.","zh":"當河流或溪流遇上陡峭岩石落差，瀑布可能形成。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when describing moving water in natural landscapes.","zh":"這個片語適用於描述自然景觀中的流動水體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"direct their flow over","meaning":"使水流流過……","examples":[{"en":"Waterfalls occur where rivers direct their flow over vertical drops.","zh":"瀑布出現在河流使水流流過垂直落差的地方。"},{"en":"Direct their flow over means make water move across or down a particular surface or edge.","zh":"direct their flow over 指使水流經過或向下流過某個表面或邊緣。"},{"en":"Engineers may direct water flow over a channel to stop flooding in a street.","zh":"工程師可能把水流導過渠道，以防街道水浸。"},{"en":"If a river directs its flow over hard rock, erosion may be slower.","zh":"如果河流使水流流過堅硬岩石，侵蝕速度可能較慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the path taken by moving water.","zh":"這個片語描述流動水體所走的路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"vertical drops","meaning":"垂直落差","examples":[{"en":"Waterfalls form where water flows over vertical drops.","zh":"水流流過垂直落差的地方會形成瀑布。"},{"en":"Vertical drops are steep downward falls from one level to a much lower level.","zh":"vertical drops 指從一個高度陡直下降到較低位置的落差。"},{"en":"A hiking trail may be dangerous if it passes near vertical drops without fences.","zh":"如果遠足路線經過沒有圍欄的垂直落差附近，可能很危險。"},{"en":"When a river reaches a vertical drop, gravity pulls the water downward quickly.","zh":"當河流到達垂直落差，重力會迅速把水向下拉。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a sharp height difference in the land.","zh":"這個片語描述地形中明顯的高度差。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be a lure for","meaning":"對……有吸引力","examples":[{"en":"Waterfalls have always been a lure for visitors.","zh":"瀑布一直對遊客有吸引力。"},{"en":"Be a lure for means attract people strongly and make them want to come.","zh":"be a lure for 指強烈吸引人，使他們想前來。"},{"en":"A famous night market can be a lure for tourists who enjoy local food.","zh":"著名夜市可以對喜歡本地食物的遊客有吸引力。"},{"en":"If a place has dramatic views, it may become a lure for photographers and travellers.","zh":"如果一個地方有壯觀景色，可能成為攝影師和旅客的吸引點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong attraction, not physical pulling.","zh":"這個片語描述強大吸引力，而不是實際拉動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"scenic beauty","meaning":"優美景色","examples":[{"en":"Many waterfalls attract visitors because of their scenic beauty.","zh":"許多瀑布因優美景色而吸引遊客。"},{"en":"Scenic beauty means the attractive natural appearance of a place.","zh":"scenic beauty 指一個地方吸引人的自然外觀。"},{"en":"A mountain village may be famous for its scenic beauty, especially at sunrise.","zh":"山村可能因優美景色而聞名，尤其在日出時。"},{"en":"Scenic beauty can increase tourism and encourage people to protect natural sites.","zh":"優美景色可以增加旅遊業，並鼓勵人們保護自然景點。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used for landscapes such as beaches, forests, mountains, and waterfalls.","zh":"這個片語常用於海灘、森林、山脈和瀑布等景觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the case of","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"In the case of the biggest waterfalls, their power attracts visitors.","zh":"就最大的瀑布而言，吸引遊客的是它們的力量。"},{"en":"In the case of means when talking about one particular example or situation.","zh":"in the case of 指談到某個特定例子或情況時。"},{"en":"In the case of young learners, short examples are often more useful than long explanations.","zh":"就年幼學習者而言，短例子通常比長解釋更有用。"},{"en":"If the situation changes, the best solution may also change.","zh":"如果情況改變，最佳解決方法也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase helps narrow a general discussion to a specific case.","zh":"這個片語幫助把一般討論收窄到特定情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"showcase nature’s might and majesty","meaning":"展現大自然的力量與壯麗","examples":[{"en":"Large waterfalls showcase nature’s might and majesty.","zh":"大型瀑布展現大自然的力量與壯麗。"},{"en":"Showcase nature’s might and majesty means display the great power and beauty of the natural world.","zh":"showcase nature’s might and majesty 指展現自然世界巨大的力量和美。"},{"en":"A huge storm over the sea can showcase nature’s might and majesty.","zh":"海上的巨大風暴可以展現大自然的力量與壯麗。"},{"en":"When people see powerful natural scenes, they may feel respect and caution.","zh":"當人們看見強大的自然景象，可能會感到敬畏和謹慎。"},{"en":"The phrase is used for scenes that feel both beautiful and overwhelming.","zh":"這個片語用於既美麗又令人震撼的景象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on the border of","meaning":"位於……邊境","examples":[{"en":"Niagara Falls is on the border of Canada and America.","zh":"尼亞加拉瀑布位於加拿大和美國邊境。"},{"en":"On the border of means located at or near the line separating two countries or regions.","zh":"on the border of 指位於或靠近兩個國家或地區的分界線。"},{"en":"A town on the border of two provinces may use services from both sides.","zh":"位於兩省邊境的城鎮可能使用兩邊的服務。"},{"en":"Places on borders often attract visitors from more than one country.","zh":"位於邊境的地方常吸引來自不止一個國家的遊客。"},{"en":"The phrase describes geographical position.","zh":"這個片語描述地理位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"discharge the most water","meaning":"排出最多水量","examples":[{"en":"Niagara Falls discharges the most water of all waterfalls.","zh":"尼亞加拉瀑布在所有瀑布中排出最多水量。"},{"en":"Discharge the most water means release or carry the greatest volume of water over time.","zh":"discharge the most water 指在一段時間內釋放或帶走最大水量。"},{"en":"A large drain may discharge more water than a small pipe during heavy rain.","zh":"暴雨期間，大排水渠排出的水量可能比小水管多。"},{"en":"If a waterfall discharges huge amounts of water, it can be extremely powerful and noisy.","zh":"如果瀑布排出巨大水量，它可以極其有力且聲音很大。"},{"en":"The phrase is about water volume, not height.","zh":"這個片語關於水量，而不是高度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be a magnet for visitors","meaning":"對遊客有強大吸引力","examples":[{"en":"Niagara Falls is a magnet for visitors.","zh":"尼亞加拉瀑布對遊客有強大吸引力。"},{"en":"Be a magnet for visitors means attract many people strongly and continuously.","zh":"be a magnet for visitors 指持續而強烈地吸引大量遊客。"},{"en":"A shopping street with famous restaurants can be a magnet for visitors at weekends.","zh":"有著名餐廳的購物街在週末可以對遊客有強大吸引力。"},{"en":"If a natural site becomes famous online, it may become a magnet for tourists.","zh":"如果自然景點在網上成名，可能成為吸引遊客的熱點。"},{"en":"The phrase compares attraction to a magnet pulling metal.","zh":"這個片語把吸引力比作磁石吸引金屬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"straddle the international boundary between","meaning":"橫跨……之間的國際邊界","examples":[{"en":"Victoria Falls straddles the international boundary between Zimbabwe and Zambia.","zh":"維多利亞瀑布橫跨津巴布韋和贊比亞之間的國際邊界。"},{"en":"Straddle the international boundary between means extend across the border separating two countries.","zh":"straddle the international boundary between 指橫跨分隔兩國的邊界。"},{"en":"A bridge may straddle the boundary between two towns and serve both communities.","zh":"一座橋可能橫跨兩個城鎮之間的邊界，服務兩個社區。"},{"en":"If a landmark crosses a national boundary, both countries may share its tourism value.","zh":"如果地標跨越國界，兩個國家都可能分享其旅遊價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something lying on both sides of a border.","zh":"這個片語描述某物位於邊界兩側。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"present the single largest sheet of falling water","meaning":"呈現世界上最大的單一落水水幕","examples":[{"en":"Victoria Falls presents the single largest sheet of falling water in the world.","zh":"維多利亞瀑布呈現世界上最大的單一落水水幕。"},{"en":"Present the single largest sheet of falling water means display the widest continuous curtain of falling water.","zh":"present the single largest sheet of falling water 指展現最寬闊、連續的落水水幕。"},{"en":"A wide waterfall can look like a sheet when the water falls in one connected wall.","zh":"當水以一面相連的牆落下，寬闊瀑布看起來就像一張水幕。"},{"en":"If a waterfall forms one huge falling sheet, it creates a dramatic visual effect.","zh":"如果瀑布形成一大片巨大落水水幕，就會創造壯觀視覺效果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes appearance and scale together.","zh":"這個片語同時描述外觀和規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"remoteness and inaccessibility","meaning":"偏遠和難以到達","examples":[{"en":"The remoteness and inaccessibility of Angel Falls have not reduced its appeal.","zh":"安赫爾瀑布的偏遠和難以到達並沒有減低其吸引力。"},{"en":"Remoteness and inaccessibility mean being far away and difficult to reach.","zh":"remoteness and inaccessibility 指地點遙遠且難以到達。"},{"en":"A mountain village may suffer from remoteness and inaccessibility if there are no good roads.","zh":"如果沒有良好道路，山村可能受偏遠和難以到達影響。"},{"en":"If a place is hard to reach, visitors may need more time, money, and planning.","zh":"如果一個地方難以到達，遊客可能需要更多時間、金錢和計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests difficulty but also mystery and attraction.","zh":"這個片語常暗示困難，但也帶有神秘和吸引力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"located deep in","meaning":"位於……深處","examples":[{"en":"Angel Falls is located deep in the Venezuelan jungle.","zh":"安赫爾瀑布位於委內瑞拉叢林深處。"},{"en":"Located deep in means situated far inside a place, away from easy access.","zh":"located deep in 指位於某地方內部深處，遠離容易到達的位置。"},{"en":"A small temple located deep in the mountains may take hours to reach.","zh":"位於山中深處的小寺廟可能需要數小時才能到達。"},{"en":"If a tourist site is located deep in a jungle, transport and safety become important concerns.","zh":"如果旅遊景點位於叢林深處，交通和安全就成為重要考慮。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests remoteness within a larger area.","zh":"這個片語暗示在較大地區內的偏遠位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"top tourist attractions","meaning":"主要旅遊景點","examples":[{"en":"Angel Falls has become one of Venezuela’s top tourist attractions.","zh":"安赫爾瀑布已成為委內瑞拉主要旅遊景點之一。"},{"en":"Top tourist attractions are the most popular places visitors want to see.","zh":"top tourist attractions 指遊客最想參觀的熱門地方。"},{"en":"A museum, old market, or mountain viewpoint can become a top tourist attraction.","zh":"博物館、舊市場或山上觀景點都可以成為主要旅遊景點。"},{"en":"If a place becomes a top attraction, local transport and services may expand.","zh":"如果一個地方成為主要景點，本地交通和服務可能擴展。"},{"en":"The phrase is used for places that strongly draw travellers.","zh":"這個片語用於強烈吸引旅客的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"possible causes of","meaning":"……的可能成因","examples":[{"en":"There are many possible causes of waterfalls.","zh":"瀑布有許多可能成因。"},{"en":"Possible causes of something are different reasons that may explain why it happens.","zh":"possible causes of something 指可能解釋某事為何發生的不同原因。"},{"en":"Doctors look for possible causes of a headache before choosing treatment.","zh":"醫生在選擇治療前會尋找頭痛的可能成因。"},{"en":"If several causes are possible, scientists compare evidence carefully.","zh":"如果有幾個可能成因，科學家會仔細比較證據。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces more than one explanation.","zh":"這個片語引出多於一個解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"differences in rock type","meaning":"岩石種類的差異","examples":[{"en":"Differences in rock type are a common cause of waterfalls.","zh":"岩石種類的差異是瀑布的常見成因。"},{"en":"Differences in rock type mean that some rocks are harder, softer, or more easily eroded than others.","zh":"differences in rock type 指有些岩石較硬、較軟或較容易受侵蝕。"},{"en":"A builder checks rock type before choosing how to support a hillside road.","zh":"建築工人在選擇如何支撐山坡道路前會檢查岩石種類。"},{"en":"If hard rock and soft rock meet, water may erode them at different speeds.","zh":"如果硬岩和軟岩相接，水可能以不同速度侵蝕它們。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why land surfaces do not wear away evenly.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何地表不會均勻磨蝕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"flow over a resistant rock bed","meaning":"流過堅硬抗蝕的岩床","examples":[{"en":"A river may flow over a resistant rock bed.","zh":"河流可能流過堅硬抗蝕的岩床。"},{"en":"Flow over a resistant rock bed means move across a layer of hard rock that resists erosion.","zh":"flow over a resistant rock bed 指水流經過一層抵抗侵蝕的硬岩。"},{"en":"Water running over a concrete path moves differently from water running over loose soil.","zh":"水流過混凝土小徑與流過鬆散泥土時，情況不同。"},{"en":"If rock resists erosion, the riverbed may remain high while softer rock nearby is cut down.","zh":"如果岩石抗蝕，河床可能保持較高，而附近軟岩被切低。"},{"en":"The phrase helps explain the start of some waterfalls.","zh":"這個片語有助解釋某些瀑布如何開始形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"erosion is slow","meaning":"侵蝕速度緩慢","examples":[{"en":"Erosion is slow when water flows over resistant rock.","zh":"當水流過抗蝕岩石時，侵蝕速度緩慢。"},{"en":"Erosion is slow means rock or soil is worn away only gradually.","zh":"erosion is slow 指岩石或泥土只會逐漸被磨蝕。"},{"en":"A stone step may wear down slowly if only a few people walk on it each day.","zh":"如果每天只有少數人走過，石級可能慢慢磨損。"},{"en":"If erosion is slow on hard rock, softer nearby rock may disappear faster.","zh":"如果硬岩侵蝕緩慢，附近軟岩可能更快消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a gradual natural process.","zh":"這個片語描述逐漸發生的自然過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"complex geological faulting","meaning":"複雜的地質斷層作用","examples":[{"en":"Complex geological faulting can expose softer rock.","zh":"複雜的地質斷層作用可以暴露較軟岩石。"},{"en":"Complex geological faulting means complicated movement and cracking in Earth’s rocks.","zh":"complex geological faulting 指地球岩石中複雜的移動和裂開。"},{"en":"Engineers study geological faulting before building tunnels or bridges.","zh":"工程師在建隧道或橋樑前會研究地質斷層作用。"},{"en":"If faulting exposes soft rock, rivers may erode it more quickly.","zh":"如果斷層作用暴露軟岩，河流可能更快侵蝕它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to deep structural changes in the ground.","zh":"這個片語指地面深層結構變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Earth’s surface","meaning":"地球表面","examples":[{"en":"Geological faulting affects the Earth’s surface.","zh":"地質斷層作用影響地球表面。"},{"en":"The Earth’s surface is the outer part of the planet, including land and ocean floors.","zh":"the Earth’s surface 指地球最外層部分，包括陸地和海床。"},{"en":"Roads, rivers, forests, and cities all exist on the Earth’s surface.","zh":"道路、河流、森林和城市都存在於地球表面。"},{"en":"When forces below the ground move, the Earth’s surface can crack, rise, or sink.","zh":"當地下力量移動時，地球表面可以裂開、升起或下沉。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the visible outer layer of Earth.","zh":"這個片語描述地球可見的外層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"softer patches of rock","meaning":"較軟的岩石區","examples":[{"en":"Softer patches of rock can be exposed by geological faulting.","zh":"較軟的岩石區可以被地質斷層作用暴露出來。"},{"en":"Softer patches of rock are areas of rock that wear away more easily than surrounding harder rock.","zh":"softer patches of rock 指比周圍硬岩更容易被磨蝕的岩石區域。"},{"en":"A road built on softer rock may need stronger support.","zh":"建在較軟岩石上的道路可能需要更強支撐。"},{"en":"If a river reaches softer patches of rock, erosion may speed up.","zh":"如果河流到達較軟的岩石區，侵蝕可能加快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes uneven weakness in a rock layer.","zh":"這個片語描述岩層中不均勻的脆弱部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be exposed","meaning":"被暴露出來","examples":[{"en":"Softer rock can be exposed by geological processes.","zh":"較軟岩石可以被地質過程暴露出來。"},{"en":"Be exposed means be uncovered and made visible or reachable.","zh":"be exposed 指被揭開，變得可見或可接觸。"},{"en":"Old pipes may be exposed when workers dig up a road.","zh":"工人掘開道路時，舊水管可能被暴露出來。"},{"en":"If soft rock is exposed, water and weather can attack it more easily.","zh":"如果軟岩被暴露出來，水和天氣可以更容易侵蝕它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something hidden becoming uncovered.","zh":"這個片語描述隱藏的東西被揭開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cut into","meaning":"侵蝕；切入","examples":[{"en":"The water cuts into the softer rock.","zh":"水流侵蝕較軟岩石。"},{"en":"Cut into means wear, carve, or dig into a surface.","zh":"cut into 指磨蝕、刻入或挖入某表面。"},{"en":"A sharp knife cuts into bread when pressure is applied.","zh":"施加壓力時，鋒利刀子會切入麵包。"},{"en":"If water cuts into soft rock for a long time, a channel or drop may form.","zh":"如果水長時間切入軟岩，可能形成水道或落差。"},{"en":"The phrase often describes erosion by water.","zh":"這個片語常描述水造成的侵蝕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"resulting in","meaning":"導致……","examples":[{"en":"The water cuts into the rock, resulting in minor turbulence.","zh":"水流侵蝕岩石，導致輕微湍流。"},{"en":"Resulting in means causing something to happen as a consequence.","zh":"resulting in 指導致某事作為結果發生。"},{"en":"A late bus may make students arrive after the bell, resulting in missed instructions.","zh":"巴士遲到可能令學生鐘聲後才到達，導致錯過指示。"},{"en":"If water hits uneven rock, it can create turbulence and faster erosion.","zh":"如果水撞上不平岩石，就可能產生湍流和更快侵蝕。"},{"en":"The phrase links an action with its result.","zh":"這個片語把行動與結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"minor turbulence","meaning":"輕微湍流","examples":[{"en":"The river creates minor turbulence at the boundary.","zh":"河流在邊界處產生輕微湍流。"},{"en":"Minor turbulence is a small amount of rough, swirling, or disturbed movement in water or air.","zh":"minor turbulence 指水或空氣中少量粗糙、旋轉或受擾的流動。"},{"en":"Passengers may feel minor turbulence when a plane flies through uneven air.","zh":"飛機穿過不穩定氣流時，乘客可能感到輕微湍流。"},{"en":"If water becomes turbulent, it can stir up sand and small stones.","zh":"如果水流變得湍急，就能攪起沙和小石。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slight disturbance, not a violent storm.","zh":"這個片語描述輕微擾動，而不是猛烈風暴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at the boundary","meaning":"在邊界處","examples":[{"en":"Turbulence occurs at the boundary between different rock types.","zh":"湍流出現在不同岩石種類的邊界處。"},{"en":"At the boundary means at the line or area where two different things meet.","zh":"at the boundary 指在兩種不同事物相接的線或區域。"},{"en":"A fence may stand at the boundary between two gardens.","zh":"圍欄可能立在兩個花園的邊界處。"},{"en":"If hard rock meets soft rock at the boundary, water may behave differently there.","zh":"如果硬岩和軟岩在邊界處相接，水流在那裡可能有不同表現。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the meeting point between two areas.","zh":"這個片語標示兩個區域的相接點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stir up","meaning":"攪起；激起","examples":[{"en":"The water stirs up pebbles and grit from the riverbed.","zh":"水流從河床攪起小石和沙礫。"},{"en":"Stir up means lift or disturb small materials so they move around.","zh":"stir up 指把細小物質揚起或擾動，使其四處移動。"},{"en":"Children can stir up dust when they run across a dry playground.","zh":"孩子跑過乾燥操場時，可以攪起塵土。"},{"en":"If fast water stirs up stones and sand, these materials can scrape the riverbed.","zh":"如果急水攪起石頭和沙，這些物質可以刮擦河床。"},{"en":"The phrase often describes movement that disturbs settled material.","zh":"這個片語常描述擾動沉積物的動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pebbles and grit","meaning":"小石和沙礫","examples":[{"en":"Pebbles and grit increase the erosive capacity of the current.","zh":"小石和沙礫增加水流的侵蝕能力。"},{"en":"Pebbles and grit are small stones and rough grains of sand or rock.","zh":"pebbles and grit 指小石頭以及粗糙的沙或岩石顆粒。"},{"en":"Pebbles and grit on a path can make shoes dirty and slippery.","zh":"路上的小石和沙礫可以弄髒鞋並令人滑倒。"},{"en":"When water carries pebbles and grit, it can scrape rock like sandpaper.","zh":"當水帶着小石和沙礫時，就能像砂紙一樣刮擦岩石。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to small hard materials moved by water.","zh":"這個片語指由水搬運的小型堅硬物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the riverbed","meaning":"河床","examples":[{"en":"Pebbles and grit are stirred up from the riverbed.","zh":"小石和沙礫從河床被攪起。"},{"en":"The riverbed is the bottom surface over which a river flows.","zh":"riverbed 指河流流經的底部表面。"},{"en":"During a drought, people may see the dry riverbed clearly.","zh":"在乾旱期間，人們可能清楚看見乾涸河床。"},{"en":"If stones move along the riverbed, they can wear it down over time.","zh":"如果石頭沿河床移動，長時間下來會磨蝕河床。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the floor of a river.","zh":"這個片語指河流的底部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"increase the erosive capacity of","meaning":"增加……的侵蝕能力","examples":[{"en":"Pebbles and grit increase the erosive capacity of the current.","zh":"小石和沙礫增加水流的侵蝕能力。"},{"en":"Increase the erosive capacity of means make something better able to wear away rock or soil.","zh":"increase the erosive capacity of 指使某物更能磨蝕岩石或泥土。"},{"en":"Sand in strong wind can increase the erosive capacity of air against old walls.","zh":"強風中的沙可以增加空氣對舊牆的侵蝕能力。"},{"en":"If water carries hard particles, it can cut into rock more effectively.","zh":"如果水流帶有堅硬顆粒，就能更有效切入岩石。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why moving water becomes more destructive.","zh":"這個片語解釋流動的水為何變得更具破壞力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the current","meaning":"水流","examples":[{"en":"The current becomes more erosive when it carries grit.","zh":"當水流帶有沙礫時，侵蝕力會更強。"},{"en":"The current is the moving flow of water in a river, stream, or sea.","zh":"current 指河流、溪流或海中的流動水體。"},{"en":"Swimmers should avoid strong currents because they can pull people away from shore.","zh":"游泳者應避免強水流，因為它可以把人拉離岸邊。"},{"en":"If the current carries stones, it can wear down rock faster.","zh":"如果水流帶着石頭，就能更快磨蝕岩石。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving water, not electricity in this context.","zh":"在這個語境中，這個詞指流動的水，而不是電流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a process begins whereby","meaning":"由此開始一個……的過程","examples":[{"en":"A process begins whereby the river develops two levels.","zh":"由此開始一個河流形成兩層的過程。"},{"en":"A process begins whereby means a series of changes starts, through which something happens.","zh":"a process begins whereby 指一連串變化開始，某事由此發生。"},{"en":"If a student practises daily, a process begins whereby weak grammar slowly improves.","zh":"如果學生每天練習，就會開始一個文法弱點慢慢改善的過程。"},{"en":"When soft rock erodes faster than hard rock, the river may start to form a drop.","zh":"當軟岩比硬岩侵蝕得更快，河流可能開始形成落差。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a cause-and-development sequence.","zh":"這個片語引出因果和發展過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take on two tiers","meaning":"形成兩層","examples":[{"en":"The river takes on two tiers, and a waterfall is born.","zh":"河流形成兩層，瀑布由此誕生。"},{"en":"Take on two tiers means develop two different levels or steps.","zh":"take on two tiers 指發展出兩個不同層次或階級。"},{"en":"A classroom shelf may take on two tiers if a second level is added above the first.","zh":"如果在課室書架第一層上方加上第二層，它就形成兩層。"},{"en":"If a riverbed erodes unevenly, the water may flow from an upper tier to a lower tier.","zh":"如果河床侵蝕不均，水可能從上層流到下層。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change from one level to two levels.","zh":"這個片語描述由一層變成兩層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a waterfall is born","meaning":"瀑布由此形成","examples":[{"en":"When the river develops two tiers, a waterfall is born.","zh":"當河流形成兩層，瀑布由此形成。"},{"en":"A waterfall is born means a waterfall begins to form or come into existence.","zh":"a waterfall is born 指瀑布開始形成或出現。"},{"en":"A new school club is born when students, teachers, and a clear purpose come together.","zh":"當學生、老師和清楚目標聚在一起，一個新學會就誕生。"},{"en":"If erosion creates a sudden drop in a river, a waterfall may begin.","zh":"如果侵蝕在河流中創造突然落差，瀑布可能開始形成。"},{"en":"The phrase personifies formation, making the natural process easier to imagine.","zh":"這個片語把形成過程擬人化，使自然過程更易想像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"abrupt causes","meaning":"突然的成因","examples":[{"en":"Earthquakes and landslides are more abrupt causes of waterfalls.","zh":"地震和山泥傾瀉是瀑布較突然的成因。"},{"en":"Abrupt causes are causes that happen suddenly rather than gradually.","zh":"abrupt causes 指突然發生，而不是逐漸發生的原因。"},{"en":"A sudden power cut can be an abrupt cause of cancelled online lessons.","zh":"突然停電可以是網課取消的突然成因。"},{"en":"Unlike slow erosion, earthquakes can change land shape in a short time.","zh":"與緩慢侵蝕不同，地震可以在短時間內改變地形。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts sudden events with slow processes.","zh":"這個片語把突發事件與緩慢過程作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"earthquakes or landslides","meaning":"地震或山泥傾瀉","examples":[{"en":"Earthquakes or landslides can create waterfalls.","zh":"地震或山泥傾瀉可以形成瀑布。"},{"en":"Earthquakes or landslides are sudden natural events that can break land or move large amounts of rock and soil.","zh":"earthquakes or landslides 指突然發生、能令土地破裂或大量岩土移動的自然事件。"},{"en":"A road may close after landslides block the way with mud and stones.","zh":"山泥傾瀉以泥石堵塞道路後，道路可能關閉。"},{"en":"If an earthquake creates a fault or a landslide blocks a stream, water may be forced over a new drop.","zh":"如果地震形成斷層，或山泥傾瀉堵塞溪流，水可能被迫流過新的落差。"},{"en":"The phrase names two sudden geological causes.","zh":"這個片語指出兩種突然的地質成因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"create fault lines","meaning":"形成斷層線","examples":[{"en":"Earthquakes can create fault lines in the land.","zh":"地震可以在土地上形成斷層線。"},{"en":"Create fault lines means produce cracks or breaks where parts of Earth’s crust move.","zh":"create fault lines 指形成地殼不同部分移動處的裂縫或斷裂。"},{"en":"Engineers study fault lines before building tall buildings in earthquake zones.","zh":"工程師在地震帶建高樓前會研究斷層線。"},{"en":"If a fault line changes the height of land, a river may suddenly flow over a drop.","zh":"如果斷層線改變土地高度，河流可能突然流過落差。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one way earthquakes reshape land.","zh":"這個片語描述地震重塑地形的一種方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"divert watercourses","meaning":"改變水道方向","examples":[{"en":"Landslides can divert watercourses.","zh":"山泥傾瀉可以改變水道方向。"},{"en":"Divert watercourses means change the direction in which rivers or streams flow.","zh":"divert watercourses 指改變河流或溪流流動的方向。"},{"en":"Roadworks may divert traffic, and a landslide may divert a stream.","zh":"道路工程可以改道交通，而山泥傾瀉可以改變溪流方向。"},{"en":"If a watercourse is diverted over steep ground, a new waterfall may form.","zh":"如果水道被改向陡峭地面，就可能形成新瀑布。"},{"en":"The phrase describes redirecting natural water paths.","zh":"這個片語描述重新引導自然水流路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"respectively","meaning":"分別地","examples":[{"en":"Earthquakes and landslides create fault lines and divert watercourses, respectively.","zh":"地震和山泥傾瀉分別形成斷層線和改變水道方向。"},{"en":"Respectively means in the same order as the things just mentioned.","zh":"respectively 指按照剛提到的事物順序分別對應。"},{"en":"Tom and May scored 80 and 90 marks, respectively, meaning Tom scored 80 and May scored 90.","zh":"Tom 和 May 分別考得80和90分，意思是 Tom 80分、May 90分。"},{"en":"If two causes and two effects are listed, respectively shows which effect belongs to which cause.","zh":"如果列出兩個原因和兩個結果，respectively 顯示哪個結果屬於哪個原因。"},{"en":"The word prevents confusion in paired information.","zh":"這個詞防止配對資訊混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"during past ice ages","meaning":"在過去冰河時期","examples":[{"en":"During past ice ages, glaciers scoured out deep basins.","zh":"在過去冰河時期，冰川沖刷出深盆地。"},{"en":"During past ice ages means in earlier periods when much of Earth was colder and covered by ice.","zh":"during past ice ages 指在地球較寒冷且大片地區被冰覆蓋的早期時期。"},{"en":"Geography students study what happened during past ice ages to understand today’s valleys and lakes.","zh":"地理學生研究過去冰河時期發生的事情，以理解今天的山谷和湖泊。"},{"en":"If glaciers moved during ice ages, they could reshape the land deeply.","zh":"如果冰川在冰河時期移動，就可以深刻重塑土地。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a long-term geological time setting.","zh":"這個片語給出長期地質時間背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"glaciers","meaning":"冰川","examples":[{"en":"Glaciers created many deep basins during past ice ages.","zh":"冰川在過去冰河時期創造了許多深盆地。"},{"en":"Glaciers are huge, slow-moving masses of ice that can shape the land.","zh":"glaciers 指巨大而緩慢移動、能塑造土地的冰體。"},{"en":"Tourists may visit glaciers in mountain regions, but they must stay on safe marked routes.","zh":"遊客可能到山區參觀冰川，但必須留在安全標示路線上。"},{"en":"As glaciers move, they scrape rock and carry loose material away.","zh":"當冰川移動時，它們會刮擦岩石並帶走鬆散物質。"},{"en":"The word names a powerful natural force made of ice.","zh":"這個詞指出一種由冰構成的強大自然力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"scour out deep basins","meaning":"沖刷出深盆地","examples":[{"en":"Glaciers scoured out many deep basins.","zh":"冰川沖刷出許多深盆地。"},{"en":"Scour out deep basins means scrape and hollow out deep low areas in the land.","zh":"scour out deep basins 指刮蝕並挖出土地中的深低窪區。"},{"en":"Strong water can scour out a hole in soft soil under a leaking pipe.","zh":"漏水管下方的強水流可以在軟土中沖刷出洞。"},{"en":"If glaciers grind against rock for thousands of years, they can create deep depressions.","zh":"如果冰川數千年磨擦岩石，就可以形成深凹陷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes powerful scraping erosion.","zh":"這個片語描述強力刮蝕侵蝕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"feeder rivers","meaning":"支流；補給河流","examples":[{"en":"Feeder rivers may continue to flow into remaining depressions.","zh":"支流可能繼續流入殘留的低窪地。"},{"en":"Feeder rivers are smaller rivers that flow into a larger river, lake, basin, or waterfall system.","zh":"feeder rivers 指流入較大河流、湖泊、盆地或瀑布系統的小河。"},{"en":"A reservoir may receive water from several feeder rivers after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，水庫可能從幾條支流接收水。"},{"en":"If a feeder river flows into a deep basin, its water may fall as a waterfall.","zh":"如果支流流入深盆地，其水可能以瀑布形式落下。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rivers that supply water to a larger feature.","zh":"這個片語描述向較大地貌供水的河流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"continue to flow as","meaning":"繼續以……形式流動","examples":[{"en":"Feeder rivers can continue to flow as waterfalls.","zh":"支流可以繼續以瀑布形式流動。"},{"en":"Continue to flow as means keep moving in a particular form or pattern.","zh":"continue to flow as 指繼續以某特定形式或模式移動。"},{"en":"Water from a broken pipe may continue to flow as a thin stream until it is repaired.","zh":"破裂水管的水可能繼續以細流形式流動，直到修理好。"},{"en":"If a river reaches a deep basin left by ice, it may keep flowing as a waterfall.","zh":"如果河流到達冰川留下的深盆地，可能繼續以瀑布形式流下。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ongoing movement in a new form.","zh":"這個片語描述以新形式持續移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"remaining depressions","meaning":"殘留的低窪地","examples":[{"en":"Water may fall into remaining depressions left by glaciers.","zh":"水可能落入冰川留下的殘留低窪地。"},{"en":"Remaining depressions are low areas that are left behind after a geological process.","zh":"remaining depressions 指地質過程後留下的低窪區。"},{"en":"After roadworks, remaining depressions in the pavement may collect rainwater.","zh":"道路工程後，行人路上殘留的低窪處可能積水。"},{"en":"If glaciers leave deep depressions, rivers may later flow into them from higher ground.","zh":"如果冰川留下深凹地，河流日後可能從高地流入其中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes leftover low places in the landscape.","zh":"這個片語描述景觀中留下的低窪地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"come in a variety of shapes and sizes","meaning":"有各種形狀和大小","examples":[{"en":"Waterfalls come in a variety of shapes and sizes.","zh":"瀑布有各種形狀和大小。"},{"en":"Come in a variety of shapes and sizes means exist in many different forms and dimensions.","zh":"come in a variety of shapes and sizes 指以許多不同形式和尺寸存在。"},{"en":"School bags come in a variety of shapes and sizes for different ages and needs.","zh":"書包有各種形狀和大小，以配合不同年齡和需要。"},{"en":"If geology varies from place to place, waterfalls will also look different.","zh":"如果各地地質不同，瀑布外觀也會不同。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses diversity in appearance.","zh":"這個片語強調外觀上的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"local geology","meaning":"本地地質","examples":[{"en":"The shape of a waterfall depends on the local geology.","zh":"瀑布形狀取決於本地地質。"},{"en":"Local geology means the rock types, layers, faults, and land structure in a particular area.","zh":"local geology 指某特定地區的岩石種類、岩層、斷層和地形結構。"},{"en":"Builders study local geology before constructing tunnels or hillside roads.","zh":"建築工人在興建隧道或山坡道路前會研究本地地質。"},{"en":"If local geology includes hard and soft rock together, erosion may create unusual landforms.","zh":"如果本地地質同時包括硬岩和軟岩，侵蝕可能形成不尋常地貌。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why natural features differ from place to place.","zh":"這個片語解釋自然地貌為何因地而異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"result in an abundance of","meaning":"造成大量……","examples":[{"en":"The variety of waterfalls has resulted in an abundance of descriptive terms.","zh":"瀑布的多樣性造成大量描述性術語。"},{"en":"Result in an abundance of means produce a large number or supply of something.","zh":"result in an abundance of 指產生大量或豐富的某物。"},{"en":"A school with many activities may result in an abundance of choices for students.","zh":"活動很多的學校可能為學生造成大量選擇。"},{"en":"If waterfalls have many forms, people create many terms to describe them.","zh":"如果瀑布有很多形式，人們就會創造許多術語描述它們。"},{"en":"The phrase connects variety with plenty.","zh":"這個片語把多樣性與豐富連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"descriptive terms","meaning":"描述性術語","examples":[{"en":"There are many descriptive terms for different types of waterfalls.","zh":"不同類型瀑布有許多描述性術語。"},{"en":"Descriptive terms are words or phrases that name and explain features of something.","zh":"descriptive terms 指命名並解釋某物特徵的字詞或片語。"},{"en":"In grammar lessons, descriptive terms like “noun” and “verb” help students talk about language clearly.","zh":"在文法課中，noun 和 verb 等描述性術語幫助學生清楚談論語言。"},{"en":"If a subject has many types, useful descriptive terms help people classify them.","zh":"如果某主題有許多類型，有用的描述性術語能幫助人們分類。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to words that describe and organise information.","zh":"這個片語指用來描述和整理資訊的詞語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"refer simply to","meaning":"簡單指……","examples":[{"en":"The word “cataract” refers simply to a large powerful waterfall.","zh":"“cataract” 這個詞簡單指大型而水勢強勁的瀑布。"},{"en":"Refer simply to means mean only or directly mean something without extra complexity.","zh":"refer simply to 指只表示或直接表示某意思，沒有額外複雜性。"},{"en":"In a menu, “vegetarian” refers simply to food that does not contain meat.","zh":"在餐牌中，“vegetarian” 簡單指不含肉類的食物。"},{"en":"If a term refers simply to size and power, it does not describe every detail of shape.","zh":"如果術語只是指大小和力量，就不是描述形狀每個細節。"},{"en":"The phrase clarifies a word’s basic meaning.","zh":"這個片語澄清一個詞的基本意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cataract","meaning":"大瀑布；巨瀑","examples":[{"en":"A cataract is a large powerful waterfall.","zh":"cataract 是大型而水勢強勁的瀑布。"},{"en":"Cataract means a waterfall with great size, force, or volume of falling water.","zh":"cataract 指規模、力量或落水量很大的瀑布。"},{"en":"A travel guide may describe a huge roaring waterfall as a cataract.","zh":"旅遊指南可能把巨大轟鳴的瀑布描述為巨瀑。"},{"en":"If a waterfall carries a very large flow, it may be called a cataract rather than a small cascade.","zh":"如果瀑布水流量非常大，它可能被稱為 cataract，而不是小型階梯瀑布。"},{"en":"The word is a descriptive term for a powerful waterfall.","zh":"這個詞是描述強勁瀑布的術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"powerful waterfall","meaning":"水勢強勁的瀑布","examples":[{"en":"A cataract is a large powerful waterfall.","zh":"cataract 是大型而水勢強勁的瀑布。"},{"en":"A powerful waterfall is a waterfall with strong force, heavy flow, or great height.","zh":"powerful waterfall 指力量強、水流大或高度高的瀑布。"},{"en":"Visitors may hear a powerful waterfall long before they see it.","zh":"遊客可能在看見水勢強勁的瀑布前很久已聽到它。"},{"en":"If a waterfall is powerful, it can erode rock and create deep plunge pools.","zh":"如果瀑布水勢強勁，就能侵蝕岩石並形成深瀑布潭。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses strength rather than only beauty.","zh":"這個片語強調力量，而不只是美感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cascade","meaning":"階梯狀瀑布","examples":[{"en":"A cascade descends a series of rock steps.","zh":"階梯狀瀑布沿一連串岩石階梯下降。"},{"en":"A cascade is a waterfall or stream that falls down in small steps or stages.","zh":"cascade 指以小階梯或階段向下流的瀑布或溪流。"},{"en":"Water from a garden fountain may fall like a small cascade over several stones.","zh":"花園噴泉的水可能像小型階梯瀑布一樣流過幾塊石頭。"},{"en":"If rock steps slow the water, the fall may look gentler than a single vertical drop.","zh":"如果岩石階梯減慢水流，瀑布可能看起來比單一垂直落差溫和。"},{"en":"The word describes stepped falling water.","zh":"這個詞描述分階段下落的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"descend a series of","meaning":"沿一連串……下降","examples":[{"en":"A cascade descends a series of rock steps.","zh":"階梯狀瀑布沿一連串岩石階梯下降。"},{"en":"Descend a series of means move downward through several connected levels or stages.","zh":"descend a series of 指經過幾個相連層次或階段向下移動。"},{"en":"Hikers may descend a series of stone steps before reaching the beach.","zh":"遠足者可能沿一連串石級下降，才到達海灘。"},{"en":"If water descends several steps, the waterfall may be called a cascade or tiered fall.","zh":"如果水沿幾層階梯下降，瀑布可能被稱為階梯狀或分層瀑布。"},{"en":"The phrase describes downward movement through repeated parts.","zh":"這個片語描述經過重複部分向下移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rock steps","meaning":"岩石階梯","examples":[{"en":"A cascade falls down a series of rock steps.","zh":"階梯狀瀑布沿一連串岩石階梯流下。"},{"en":"Rock steps are natural step-like levels in rock over which water can flow.","zh":"rock steps 指岩石中自然形成、可讓水流經的階梯狀層面。"},{"en":"Hikers may use rock steps carefully when walking down a steep path.","zh":"遠足者沿陡路下行時，可能小心使用岩石階梯。"},{"en":"If water meets rock steps, it may fall in separate small drops.","zh":"如果水遇上岩石階梯，可能分成幾個小落差流下。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stepped rock surfaces in a landscape.","zh":"這個片語描述景觀中的階梯狀岩石表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"very distinct","meaning":"非常清晰分明","examples":[{"en":"If the steps are very distinct, the waterfall is called a tiered waterfall.","zh":"如果階梯非常清晰分明，該瀑布就稱為分層瀑布。"},{"en":"Very distinct means very clear and easy to separate or recognise.","zh":"very distinct 指非常清楚且容易分辨或辨認。"},{"en":"A teacher’s two examples are very distinct if students can easily tell the difference.","zh":"如果學生容易分辨差異，老師的兩個例子就是非常清晰分明。"},{"en":"If each step in a waterfall is clearly visible, the structure looks tiered.","zh":"如果瀑布每一層都清楚可見，其結構看起來就是分層的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong clarity or separation.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈清晰度或分隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tiered waterfall","meaning":"分層瀑布","examples":[{"en":"A tiered waterfall descends over distinct steps.","zh":"分層瀑布沿清晰階梯下降。"},{"en":"A tiered waterfall is a waterfall that falls down several clear levels.","zh":"tiered waterfall 指沿幾個清楚層次落下的瀑布。"},{"en":"A park may describe a stepped waterfall as a tiered waterfall on a visitor sign.","zh":"公園可能在遊客標示上把階梯狀瀑布描述為分層瀑布。"},{"en":"If separate drops are visible one after another, the waterfall has a tiered form.","zh":"如果一個接一個分開的落差清楚可見，該瀑布就有分層形態。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shape, not necessarily size.","zh":"這個片語描述形狀，而不一定描述大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"of approximately the same size","meaning":"大小大致相同","examples":[{"en":"In a multi-step waterfall, each step is of approximately the same size.","zh":"在多級瀑布中，每一級大小大致相同。"},{"en":"Of approximately the same size means nearly equal in measurement or scale.","zh":"of approximately the same size 指在尺寸或規模上接近相等。"},{"en":"A teacher may divide a class into groups of approximately the same size.","zh":"老師可能把全班分成大小大致相同的小組。"},{"en":"If waterfall steps are similar in size, the pattern looks more regular.","zh":"如果瀑布階級大小相近，圖案看起來更有規律。"},{"en":"The phrase allows small differences, not exact equality.","zh":"這個片語容許小差異，而不是完全相等。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a significant pool of water","meaning":"一大片水潭","examples":[{"en":"A multi-step waterfall has a significant pool of water at each base.","zh":"多級瀑布在每一層底部都有一大片水潭。"},{"en":"A significant pool of water is a fairly large and noticeable collection of water.","zh":"significant pool of water 指相當大且明顯的一片積水。"},{"en":"After heavy rain, a significant pool of water may form near a blocked drain.","zh":"大雨後，堵塞排水口附近可能形成一大片積水。"},{"en":"If water collects at the base of each step, the waterfall develops pools between drops.","zh":"如果水在每一級底部聚集，瀑布就會在各落差之間形成水潭。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests more than a small puddle.","zh":"這個片語暗示不只是小水窪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at each base","meaning":"在每一層底部","examples":[{"en":"There is a pool of water at each base of a multi-step waterfall.","zh":"多級瀑布在每一層底部都有水潭。"},{"en":"At each base means at the bottom of every level or section.","zh":"at each base 指在每一個層次或部分的底部。"},{"en":"In a shopping mall, signs may be placed at each base of the escalators.","zh":"商場可能在每條扶手電梯底部放置標示。"},{"en":"If water lands at each base, it can form separate pools between steps.","zh":"如果水落在每一層底部，就能在階級之間形成分開的水潭。"},{"en":"The phrase points to repeated bottom locations.","zh":"這個片語指重複出現的底部位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be known as","meaning":"被稱為……","examples":[{"en":"A waterfall with large equal steps is known as a multi-step waterfall.","zh":"有大型且相等階級的瀑布被稱為多級瀑布。"},{"en":"Be known as means be called or recognised by a particular name.","zh":"be known as 指被稱作或被認定為某個名稱。"},{"en":"Hong Kong is known as a busy international city.","zh":"香港被稱為繁忙的國際城市。"},{"en":"If a feature has a special shape, it may be known by a technical term.","zh":"如果某地貌有特殊形狀，可能被稱為技術術語。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a name or label.","zh":"這個片語引出名稱或標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"multi-step waterfall","meaning":"多級瀑布","examples":[{"en":"A multi-step waterfall has large steps and pools at each base.","zh":"多級瀑布有大型階級，並在每一層底部有水潭。"},{"en":"A multi-step waterfall is a waterfall that falls through several similar steps.","zh":"multi-step waterfall 指經過幾個相似階級落下的瀑布。"},{"en":"Visitors may enjoy a multi-step waterfall because each level creates a different view.","zh":"遊客可能喜歡多級瀑布，因為每一層都創造不同景觀。"},{"en":"If rock layers form repeated drops, water can fall as a multi-step waterfall.","zh":"如果岩層形成重複落差，水就可以以多級瀑布形式落下。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a waterfall with several large stages.","zh":"這個片語描述有幾個大型階段的瀑布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"remain in contact with","meaning":"與……保持接觸","examples":[{"en":"The falling water may remain in contact with the rock face.","zh":"落下的水可能與岩壁保持接觸。"},{"en":"Remain in contact with means continue touching something.","zh":"remain in contact with 指繼續接觸某物。"},{"en":"A phone charger must remain in contact with the socket to keep charging.","zh":"手機充電器必須與插座保持接觸，才能繼續充電。"},{"en":"If falling water stays against the rock, it may spread across the surface.","zh":"如果落水貼着岩石，可能沿表面擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continuous physical contact.","zh":"這個片語描述持續的物理接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rock face","meaning":"岩壁","examples":[{"en":"The water may fall while touching the rock face.","zh":"水可能在接觸岩壁的情況下落下。"},{"en":"A rock face is a steep exposed surface of rock, often on a cliff or mountain.","zh":"rock face 指陡峭而外露的岩石表面，常在懸崖或山上。"},{"en":"Climbers check the rock face carefully before choosing where to place their hands.","zh":"攀石者會仔細檢查岩壁，再選擇手放在哪裡。"},{"en":"If water stays against the rock face, the waterfall may look like a horsetail.","zh":"如果水貼着岩壁下落，瀑布可能看起來像馬尾瀑布。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a vertical or steep rock surface.","zh":"這個片語描述垂直或陡峭的岩石表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"widen","meaning":"變寬","examples":[{"en":"If the water remains in contact with the rock face, it often widens.","zh":"如果水與岩壁保持接觸，它通常會變寬。"},{"en":"Widen means become wider or spread over a larger width.","zh":"widen 指變得更寬或擴展到更大的寬度。"},{"en":"A road may widen near a bus stop so buses can stop safely.","zh":"道路可能在巴士站附近變寬，讓巴士安全停靠。"},{"en":"If water spreads across rock while falling, the waterfall may become broader.","zh":"如果水在落下時沿岩石擴散，瀑布可能變得更寬闊。"},{"en":"The word describes an increase in width.","zh":"這個詞描述寬度增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"horsetail waterfall","meaning":"馬尾瀑布","examples":[{"en":"A horsetail waterfall remains in contact with the rock face.","zh":"馬尾瀑布與岩壁保持接觸。"},{"en":"A horsetail waterfall is a waterfall whose falling water stays touching the rock and often spreads out.","zh":"horsetail waterfall 指落水貼着岩石並常向外散開的瀑布。"},{"en":"A visitor may recognise a horsetail waterfall because it looks like water brushing down a cliff.","zh":"遊客可能因它像水沿懸崖刷下來而辨認出馬尾瀑布。"},{"en":"If the water does not leap away from the rock, it is not a plunge waterfall.","zh":"如果水沒有離開岩石向外直落，它就不是直瀉式瀑布。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the waterfall’s shape and contact with rock.","zh":"這個片語描述瀑布形狀以及與岩石的接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not touch the rock face at all","meaning":"完全不接觸岩壁","examples":[{"en":"In a plunge waterfall, the water does not touch the rock face at all.","zh":"在直瀉式瀑布中，水完全不接觸岩壁。"},{"en":"Not touch the rock face at all means fall freely without contacting the cliff surface.","zh":"not touch the rock face at all 指自由落下，不接觸懸崖表面。"},{"en":"A rope hanging away from a wall does not touch the wall at all.","zh":"一條離牆懸掛的繩子完全不接觸牆壁。"},{"en":"If falling water clears the cliff edge, it drops straight down through the air.","zh":"如果落水越過崖邊，就會穿過空氣直接向下落。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses complete separation from the rock.","zh":"這個片語強調與岩石完全分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"plunge waterfall","meaning":"直瀉式瀑布","examples":[{"en":"A plunge waterfall drops without touching the rock face.","zh":"直瀉式瀑布落下時不接觸岩壁。"},{"en":"A plunge waterfall is a waterfall where water falls freely away from the cliff.","zh":"plunge waterfall 指水離開懸崖自由下落的瀑布。"},{"en":"Tourists often enjoy plunge waterfalls because the falling water creates a dramatic curtain.","zh":"遊客常喜歡直瀉式瀑布，因為落水形成壯觀水幕。"},{"en":"If the water shoots over an edge and falls through open air, it has a plunge form.","zh":"如果水越過邊緣並穿過空氣落下，它就具有直瀉形態。"},{"en":"The phrase describes free-falling water.","zh":"這個片語描述自由落下的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the most picturesque","meaning":"最如畫；最美麗","examples":[{"en":"Plunge waterfalls are often the most picturesque.","zh":"直瀉式瀑布往往最如畫。"},{"en":"The most picturesque means the most beautiful in a way that looks like a picture.","zh":"the most picturesque 指最美麗、最像圖畫般吸引人。"},{"en":"A village with old houses, trees, and a river may be the most picturesque stop on a trip.","zh":"有舊屋、樹木和河流的村莊，可能是旅程中最如畫的一站。"},{"en":"If falling water separates cleanly from a cliff, it can create a dramatic view.","zh":"如果落水清楚離開懸崖，就能創造壯觀景觀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong visual beauty.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈視覺美感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"regardless of","meaning":"不論……","examples":[{"en":"Regardless of their differences, all waterfalls have common features.","zh":"不論瀑布之間有何差異，所有瀑布都有共同特徵。"},{"en":"Regardless of means without being affected by a particular difference or condition.","zh":"regardless of 指不受某差異或條件影響。"},{"en":"Students should be treated fairly regardless of their background.","zh":"不論學生背景如何，都應受到公平對待。"},{"en":"Regardless of size, every waterfall has water, height, and movement.","zh":"不論大小，每個瀑布都有水、高度和流動。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a statement applies despite differences.","zh":"這個片語顯示某說法儘管有差異仍然適用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have in common","meaning":"共同擁有","examples":[{"en":"All waterfalls have vertical height and average flow in common.","zh":"所有瀑布都共同擁有垂直高度和平均水流量。"},{"en":"Have in common means share the same feature or quality.","zh":"have in common 指共有同一特徵或品質。"},{"en":"Two classmates may have music, basketball, and the same bus route in common.","zh":"兩名同學可能共同擁有音樂、籃球和同一條巴士路線作為共同點。"},{"en":"If several things have one feature in common, that feature helps compare them.","zh":"如果幾件事共同擁有一個特徵，該特徵就有助比較它們。"},{"en":"The phrase points to shared characteristics.","zh":"這個片語指出共同特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"vertical height","meaning":"垂直高度","examples":[{"en":"Every waterfall has a vertical height.","zh":"每個瀑布都有垂直高度。"},{"en":"Vertical height is the straight up-and-down distance from top to bottom.","zh":"vertical height 指從頂部到底部的垂直距離。"},{"en":"Builders measure the vertical height of a wall before ordering ladders.","zh":"建築工人在訂購梯子前會量度牆的垂直高度。"},{"en":"If a waterfall has great vertical height, the water falls farther and may look more dramatic.","zh":"如果瀑布垂直高度很大，水落得更遠，可能看起來更壯觀。"},{"en":"The phrase measures height, not width.","zh":"這個片語量度高度，而不是寬度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"average flow of water","meaning":"平均水流量","examples":[{"en":"The average flow of water helps measure a waterfall’s power.","zh":"平均水流量有助衡量瀑布的力量。"},{"en":"Average flow of water means the usual amount of water moving through a place over time.","zh":"average flow of water 指一段時間內通常流經某地的水量。"},{"en":"A city checks the average flow of water in drains before the rainy season.","zh":"雨季前，城市會檢查排水渠的平均水流量。"},{"en":"If average flow is high, a waterfall may be more powerful even if it is not the tallest.","zh":"如果平均水流量高，即使瀑布不是最高，也可能更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes water quantity over time.","zh":"這個片語描述隨時間計算的水量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"taken together","meaning":"合起來看","examples":[{"en":"These features, taken together, measure the waterfall’s power.","zh":"這些特徵合起來看，可以衡量瀑布的力量。"},{"en":"Taken together means considered as a group rather than separately.","zh":"taken together 指作為整體考慮，而不是分開看。"},{"en":"Attendance, homework, and test scores, taken together, show how a student is progressing.","zh":"出席、功課和測驗成績合起來看，可以顯示學生進步情況。"},{"en":"If height and flow are considered together, they give a fuller picture of waterfall power.","zh":"如果高度和水流量一起考慮，就能更完整呈現瀑布力量。"},{"en":"The phrase combines separate details into one judgement.","zh":"這個片語把分開細節合成一個判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a measure of","meaning":"衡量……的指標","examples":[{"en":"Height and flow are a measure of a waterfall’s power.","zh":"高度和水流量是衡量瀑布力量的指標。"},{"en":"A measure of something is an indicator that helps judge or compare it.","zh":"a measure of something 指幫助判斷或比較某事的指標。"},{"en":"Exam results are one measure of learning, but not the only one.","zh":"考試成績是衡量學習的一個指標，但不是唯一指標。"},{"en":"If a waterfall is high and carries much water, those facts measure its force.","zh":"如果瀑布很高且水量大，這些事實就能衡量其力量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a way to assess something.","zh":"這個片語描述評估某事的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be quantified using","meaning":"使用……量化","examples":[{"en":"A waterfall’s power is quantified using a ten-point scale.","zh":"瀑布力量使用十級尺度量化。"},{"en":"Be quantified using means be measured or expressed in numbers by a particular method.","zh":"be quantified using 指透過某方法以數字量度或表達。"},{"en":"Student progress can be quantified using test scores, attendance, and writing samples.","zh":"學生進步可以使用測驗分數、出席率和寫作樣本量化。"},{"en":"If something is quantified, people can compare examples more easily.","zh":"如果某事被量化，人們就能更容易比較不同例子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes turning qualities into measurable numbers.","zh":"這個片語描述把特質轉化為可量度數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ten-point logarithmic scale","meaning":"十級對數尺度","examples":[{"en":"Waterfall power is measured on a ten-point logarithmic scale.","zh":"瀑布力量以十級對數尺度量度。"},{"en":"A ten-point logarithmic scale is a scale from one to ten where each step represents a large mathematical increase.","zh":"ten-point logarithmic scale 指一個由一至十的尺度，其中每一級代表很大的數學增幅。"},{"en":"Earthquake strength is also often explained using scales where higher numbers mean much stronger events.","zh":"地震強度也常以較高數字代表強很多的尺度來解釋。"},{"en":"If a scale is logarithmic, moving up one level can mean a big increase, not just a small one.","zh":"如果尺度是對數的，上升一級可能代表大幅增加，而不只是少許增加。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a technical measurement system.","zh":"這個片語指一種技術性量度系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"giant falls","meaning":"巨型瀑布","examples":[{"en":"Giant falls such as Niagara are graded at the top of the scale.","zh":"像尼亞加拉這樣的巨型瀑布被評為尺度最高級別。"},{"en":"Giant falls are extremely large waterfalls with great height, flow, or power.","zh":"giant falls 指高度、水流量或力量極大的瀑布。"},{"en":"Tourists may travel across countries to see giant falls because they are rare and dramatic.","zh":"遊客可能跨國旅行去看巨型瀑布，因為它們罕見且壯觀。"},{"en":"If a waterfall has huge water volume and strong force, it may be ranked among giant falls.","zh":"如果瀑布水量巨大且力量強，可能被列為巨型瀑布。"},{"en":"The phrase describes very large waterfalls.","zh":"這個片語描述非常大型的瀑布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be graded at the very top of","meaning":"被評為……的最高級別","examples":[{"en":"Niagara is graded at the very top of the scale.","zh":"尼亞加拉被評為該尺度的最高級別。"},{"en":"Be graded at the very top of means receive the highest ranking or score in a system.","zh":"be graded at the very top of 指在某系統中獲得最高等級或分數。"},{"en":"A restaurant may be graded at the top of a hygiene scale if it meets all standards.","zh":"如果餐廳符合所有標準，可能被評為衛生尺度最高級別。"},{"en":"If a waterfall has exceptional height and flow, it may receive the highest grade.","zh":"如果瀑布高度和水流量都非常突出，可能獲得最高級別。"},{"en":"The phrase describes top-level classification.","zh":"這個片語描述最高層級分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"town creeks","meaning":"城鎮小溪","examples":[{"en":"Small falls may occur in town creeks.","zh":"小瀑布可能出現在城鎮小溪中。"},{"en":"Town creeks are small streams that flow through or near towns.","zh":"town creeks 指流經或靠近城鎮的小溪。"},{"en":"Children may see fish, leaves, and small stones in town creeks after rain.","zh":"雨後，孩子可能在城鎮小溪中看見魚、葉和小石。"},{"en":"If a town creek crosses a small drop, a tiny waterfall may form.","zh":"如果城鎮小溪流過小落差，就可能形成小瀑布。"},{"en":"The phrase describes small local waterways.","zh":"這個片語描述本地小型水道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"common feature","meaning":"常見特徵","examples":[{"en":"A plunge pool is another common feature of larger falls.","zh":"瀑布潭是較大型瀑布的另一個常見特徵。"},{"en":"A common feature is something often found in a particular type of place or thing.","zh":"common feature 指在某類地方或事物中常見的東西。"},{"en":"A playground is a common feature of many primary schools.","zh":"遊樂場是許多小學的常見特徵。"},{"en":"If many large waterfalls have plunge pools, the pool is considered a common feature.","zh":"如果許多大型瀑布都有瀑布潭，水潭就被視為常見特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a usual or repeated characteristic.","zh":"這個片語描述通常或重複出現的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"larger falls","meaning":"較大型瀑布","examples":[{"en":"Larger falls often have plunge pools.","zh":"較大型瀑布通常有瀑布潭。"},{"en":"Larger falls are waterfalls that are bigger in height, flow, width, or power.","zh":"larger falls 指在高度、水流量、寬度或力量上較大的瀑布。"},{"en":"Visitors may need to stay farther back from larger falls because spray and currents can be strong.","zh":"遊客可能需要與較大型瀑布保持更遠距離，因為水霧和水流可以很強。"},{"en":"If a fall is large and powerful, falling water can dig out a deep pool below.","zh":"如果瀑布大型且強勁，落水可以在下方挖出深水潭。"},{"en":"The phrase compares bigger waterfalls with smaller ones.","zh":"這個片語把較大的瀑布與較小瀑布比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"plunge pool","meaning":"瀑布潭","examples":[{"en":"A plunge pool forms at the base of larger waterfalls.","zh":"瀑布潭在較大型瀑布底部形成。"},{"en":"A plunge pool is a deep pool created where falling water hits the ground or riverbed.","zh":"plunge pool 指落水撞擊地面或河床處形成的深水潭。"},{"en":"Swimmers should be careful near plunge pools because currents may be hidden and strong.","zh":"游泳者在瀑布潭附近應小心，因為水流可能隱藏而強勁。"},{"en":"As falling water pounds the base, rocks and sand help deepen the pool.","zh":"當落水不斷衝擊底部，岩石和沙會幫助加深水潭。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a basin formed by waterfall erosion.","zh":"這個片語描述由瀑布侵蝕形成的盆地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rubble at the base of","meaning":"……底部的碎石","examples":[{"en":"The plunge pool is caused by rubble at the base of the falls.","zh":"瀑布潭由瀑布底部的碎石造成。"},{"en":"Rubble at the base of means broken rock pieces collected at the bottom of something.","zh":"rubble at the base of 指聚集在某物底部的破碎岩石。"},{"en":"After an old wall collapses, rubble may collect at the base of the building.","zh":"舊牆倒塌後，碎石可能聚集在建築物底部。"},{"en":"If rubble is moved around by water, it can grind against the riverbed.","zh":"如果碎石被水攪動，就能磨擦河床。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broken material lying at the bottom.","zh":"這個片語描述位於底部的破碎材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be stirred and broken into","meaning":"被攪動並碎成……","examples":[{"en":"The rubble is stirred and broken into smaller pieces.","zh":"碎石被攪動並碎成更小塊。"},{"en":"Be stirred and broken into means be moved around and smashed into smaller parts.","zh":"be stirred and broken into 指被攪動並撞碎成更小部分。"},{"en":"Biscuits may be stirred and broken into crumbs when mixed too roughly.","zh":"如果攪拌太粗暴，餅乾可能被攪動並碎成餅碎。"},{"en":"If rocks are stirred by strong water, they can hit one another and break apart.","zh":"如果岩石被強水流攪動，就會互相撞擊並破裂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement plus fragmentation.","zh":"這個片語描述移動加碎裂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"never-ending eddies and whirlpools","meaning":"不斷旋轉的渦流和漩渦","examples":[{"en":"Never-ending eddies and whirlpools help carve out the basin.","zh":"不斷旋轉的渦流和漩渦幫助挖出盆地。"},{"en":"Never-ending eddies and whirlpools are continuous circular water movements that keep spinning.","zh":"never-ending eddies and whirlpools 指持續不斷旋轉的圓形水流。"},{"en":"Water near a drain can form small whirlpools when it flows away quickly.","zh":"水快速流走時，排水口附近可以形成小漩渦。"},{"en":"If spinning currents keep moving stones, they can deepen a basin over time.","zh":"如果旋轉水流持續移動石頭，就能隨時間加深盆地。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests constant circular motion in water.","zh":"這個片語暗示水中持續的圓形運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"scour out a deep underwater basin","meaning":"沖刷出深水盆","examples":[{"en":"The pieces scour out a deep underwater basin.","zh":"這些碎塊沖刷出深水盆。"},{"en":"Scour out a deep underwater basin means scrape and hollow out a deep basin below the water.","zh":"scour out a deep underwater basin 指在水下刮蝕並挖出深盆地。"},{"en":"Fast water carrying sand can scour out holes near a bridge support.","zh":"帶沙急水可以在橋墩附近沖刷出洞。"},{"en":"If stones spin at the base of a waterfall, they can dig the bottom deeper.","zh":"如果石頭在瀑布底部旋轉，就能把底部挖得更深。"},{"en":"The phrase describes erosion beneath water.","zh":"這個片語描述水下侵蝕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"an interesting consequence","meaning":"一個有趣的結果","examples":[{"en":"An interesting consequence is that such falls are retreating.","zh":"一個有趣的結果是，這類瀑布正在後退。"},{"en":"An interesting consequence is a result that is notable or surprising.","zh":"an interesting consequence 指值得注意或令人意外的結果。"},{"en":"An interesting consequence of online lessons is that some quiet students ask more questions in chat.","zh":"網課的一個有趣結果是，有些安靜學生會在聊天欄問更多問題。"},{"en":"If plunge pools erode the base, the waterfall may slowly move backward.","zh":"如果瀑布潭侵蝕底部，瀑布可能慢慢向後移動。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a result worth noticing.","zh":"這個片語引出值得注意的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the process of retreat","meaning":"正在後退的過程中","examples":[{"en":"Large waterfalls are often in the process of retreat.","zh":"大型瀑布通常正在後退的過程中。"},{"en":"In the process of retreat means currently moving backward over time.","zh":"in the process of retreat 指目前隨時間向後移動。"},{"en":"A coastline may be in the process of retreat if waves keep removing sand.","zh":"如果海浪不斷帶走沙，海岸線可能正在後退的過程中。"},{"en":"If erosion cuts away rock behind a waterfall, the waterfall slowly moves upstream.","zh":"如果侵蝕削走瀑布後方岩石，瀑布就會慢慢向上游移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an ongoing backward movement.","zh":"這個片語描述正在進行的後退移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"softer material","meaning":"較軟的物質","examples":[{"en":"Softer material at the lower face is eroded more easily.","zh":"下部表面的較軟物質更容易被侵蝕。"},{"en":"Softer material means rock or soil that is less hard and easier to wear away.","zh":"softer material 指較不堅硬、較容易被磨蝕的岩石或泥土。"},{"en":"A pencil cuts into softer material like rubber more easily than into metal.","zh":"鉛筆比起金屬，更容易切入橡膠這類較軟物質。"},{"en":"If softer material lies below hard rock, water may undercut the base.","zh":"如果較軟物質位於硬岩下方，水可能侵蝕底部。"},{"en":"The phrase describes material that is more vulnerable to erosion.","zh":"這個片語描述較容易受侵蝕的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lower face","meaning":"下部表面","examples":[{"en":"The lower face suffers undercutting.","zh":"下部表面遭受底部侵蝕。"},{"en":"Lower face means the lower exposed surface of a cliff, rock wall, or waterfall edge.","zh":"lower face 指懸崖、岩壁或瀑布邊緣較低的外露表面。"},{"en":"Workers may inspect the lower face of a wall for cracks after flooding.","zh":"水浸後，工人可能檢查牆的下部表面是否有裂縫。"},{"en":"If water attacks the lower face first, the upper rock may eventually collapse.","zh":"如果水先侵蝕下部表面，上方岩石最終可能塌下。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the bottom part of a visible surface.","zh":"這個片語指可見表面的底部部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"suffer undercutting","meaning":"遭受底部侵蝕","examples":[{"en":"The softer material suffers undercutting.","zh":"較軟物質遭受底部侵蝕。"},{"en":"Suffer undercutting means be eroded from below or at the base.","zh":"suffer undercutting 指從下方或底部被侵蝕。"},{"en":"A riverbank may suffer undercutting if fast water removes soil from its lower edge.","zh":"如果急水移走河岸下緣泥土，河岸可能遭受底部侵蝕。"},{"en":"If the base is undercut, the rock above may lose support and collapse.","zh":"如果底部被侵蝕，上方岩石可能失去支撐並倒塌。"},{"en":"The phrase describes erosion that weakens something from below.","zh":"這個片語描述從下方削弱某物的侵蝕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"give rise to","meaning":"引致；產生","examples":[{"en":"Undercutting gives rise to rock shelters behind the water.","zh":"底部侵蝕產生落水後方的岩洞。"},{"en":"Give rise to means cause something to happen or develop.","zh":"give rise to 指導致某事發生或發展。"},{"en":"Poor communication can give rise to misunderstandings in a group project.","zh":"溝通差可以在小組項目中引致誤解。"},{"en":"If erosion removes rock below a waterfall, hollow spaces may form behind the falling water.","zh":"如果侵蝕移走瀑布下方岩石，落水後面可能形成中空空間。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a cause with a new result.","zh":"這個片語把原因與新結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rock shelters","meaning":"岩洞；岩石遮蔽處","examples":[{"en":"Rock shelters can form behind falling water.","zh":"岩洞可以在落水後方形成。"},{"en":"Rock shelters are hollow or protected spaces formed under or behind rock overhangs.","zh":"rock shelters 指在岩石突出部分下方或後方形成的中空或受保護空間。"},{"en":"Hikers may rest in rock shelters during sudden rain, but they must check for danger first.","zh":"遠足者遇上突然下雨時可能在岩石遮蔽處休息，但必須先檢查危險。"},{"en":"If undercutting grows deeper, a rock shelter behind a waterfall may become larger.","zh":"如果底部侵蝕加深，瀑布後方的岩洞可能變大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes natural sheltered spaces in rock.","zh":"這個片語描述岩石中的天然遮蔽空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"steadily become larger","meaning":"穩步變大","examples":[{"en":"The rock shelters steadily become larger.","zh":"岩洞穩步變大。"},{"en":"Steadily become larger means gradually increase in size over time.","zh":"steadily become larger 指隨時間逐漸增加大小。"},{"en":"A savings account can steadily become larger if money is added every month.","zh":"如果每月存錢，儲蓄戶口可以穩步變大。"},{"en":"If water continues to erode the rock, the hollow space behind the fall expands.","zh":"如果水持續侵蝕岩石，瀑布後方的中空空間就會擴大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow but continuous growth.","zh":"這個片語描述緩慢但持續的增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the roof collapses","meaning":"頂部塌下","examples":[{"en":"The shelter becomes larger until the roof collapses.","zh":"岩洞變得越來越大，直到頂部塌下。"},{"en":"The roof collapses means the top part falls down because it loses support.","zh":"the roof collapses 指頂部因失去支撐而倒塌。"},{"en":"A badly damaged old building may be unsafe if the roof collapses after heavy rain.","zh":"如果舊建築嚴重受損，大雨後屋頂塌下就會很危險。"},{"en":"If erosion removes too much support, the rock above can fall.","zh":"如果侵蝕移走太多支撐，上方岩石就可能跌落。"},{"en":"The phrase describes structural failure from above.","zh":"這個片語描述上方結構失效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"retreat significantly upstream","meaning":"大幅向上游後退","examples":[{"en":"The waterfall may retreat significantly upstream.","zh":"瀑布可能大幅向上游後退。"},{"en":"Retreat significantly upstream means move noticeably backward in the direction opposite the river’s flow.","zh":"retreat significantly upstream 指朝與河流流向相反的方向明顯後移。"},{"en":"If a riverbank erodes every year, the edge may retreat noticeably over time.","zh":"如果河岸每年被侵蝕，邊緣可能隨時間明顯後退。"},{"en":"When the cliff face collapses repeatedly, the waterfall shifts farther upstream.","zh":"當懸崖面反覆塌下，瀑布就會向更上游移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes major backward movement along a river.","zh":"這個片語描述沿河流的大幅後退。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"people at large","meaning":"一般大眾","examples":[{"en":"To people at large, a waterfall seems fixed and forever.","zh":"對一般大眾而言，瀑布看似固定而永恆。"},{"en":"People at large means ordinary people in general, not specialists.","zh":"people at large 指一般普通人，而不是專家。"},{"en":"To people at large, a school timetable may look simple, but teachers know it is hard to design.","zh":"對一般大眾而言，學校時間表可能看似簡單，但老師知道它很難設計。"},{"en":"If ordinary visitors cannot see slow erosion, they may think a waterfall never changes.","zh":"如果普通遊客看不見緩慢侵蝕，可能以為瀑布永不改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the general public.","zh":"這個片語指普羅大眾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"seem fixed and forever","meaning":"看似固定而永恆","examples":[{"en":"A waterfall may seem fixed and forever to ordinary observers.","zh":"對普通觀察者而言，瀑布可能看似固定而永恆。"},{"en":"Seem fixed and forever means appear unchanging and permanent.","zh":"seem fixed and forever 指看起來不變且永久。"},{"en":"A child may think a school building seems fixed and forever until it is renovated.","zh":"孩子可能覺得校舍看似固定而永恆，直到它被翻新。"},{"en":"If natural change is very slow, people may not notice it during one visit.","zh":"如果自然變化非常緩慢，人們一次到訪時可能注意不到。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts appearance with gradual change.","zh":"這個片語對比表象與逐漸變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"erosion is indeed a slow process","meaning":"侵蝕確實是一個緩慢過程","examples":[{"en":"Erosion is indeed a slow process.","zh":"侵蝕確實是一個緩慢過程。"},{"en":"Erosion is indeed a slow process means rock and soil are usually worn away gradually over long periods.","zh":"erosion is indeed a slow process 指岩石和泥土通常在長時間中逐漸被磨蝕。"},{"en":"A stone step may take years to show wear from people walking on it.","zh":"石級可能要多年才會顯示被人行走造成的磨損。"},{"en":"Because erosion is slow, changes in a waterfall may be hard to notice at first.","zh":"因為侵蝕緩慢，瀑布變化起初可能難以察覺。"},{"en":"The phrase confirms that erosion normally takes time.","zh":"這個片語確認侵蝕通常需要時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"given a sufficiently powerful waterfall","meaning":"假如有一個足夠強勁的瀑布","examples":[{"en":"Given a sufficiently powerful waterfall, retreat can be visible over time.","zh":"假如有一個足夠強勁的瀑布，後退可以隨時間變得可見。"},{"en":"Given a sufficiently powerful waterfall means if the waterfall is strong enough.","zh":"given a sufficiently powerful waterfall 指如果瀑布力量足夠強。"},{"en":"Given enough practice, a nervous student can become more confident in speaking.","zh":"假如有足夠練習，緊張的學生可以在說話方面變得更自信。"},{"en":"If a waterfall has enough force, it can erode rock quickly enough for people to notice.","zh":"如果瀑布有足夠力量，就能快到讓人注意到地侵蝕岩石。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a condition that makes something possible.","zh":"這個片語引出令某事成為可能的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the right sort of rock","meaning":"合適類型的岩石","examples":[{"en":"The retreat depends on the right sort of rock.","zh":"後退取決於合適類型的岩石。"},{"en":"The right sort of rock means a rock type with suitable hardness or weakness for a process.","zh":"the right sort of rock 指硬度或脆弱程度適合某過程的岩石類型。"},{"en":"Builders need the right sort of rock or ground before constructing a stable foundation.","zh":"建築工人在建穩固地基前，需要合適類型的岩石或地面。"},{"en":"If rock is too hard, retreat may be too slow to notice; if softer, erosion may be faster.","zh":"如果岩石太硬，後退可能慢得難以察覺；如果較軟，侵蝕可能較快。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that material conditions matter.","zh":"這個片語顯示材料條件很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"over a metre a year","meaning":"每年超過一米","examples":[{"en":"The retreat can be over a metre a year.","zh":"後退速度可以每年超過一米。"},{"en":"Over a metre a year means more than one metre in distance each year.","zh":"over a metre a year 指每年距離超過一米。"},{"en":"A fast-growing hedge may grow over a metre a year if it gets enough sun and water.","zh":"如果陽光和水分足夠，快速生長的樹籬每年可能長超過一米。"},{"en":"If a waterfall retreats over a metre yearly, the change can be measured within a human lifetime.","zh":"如果瀑布每年後退超過一米，變化可在人的一生中量度到。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a rate of movement or growth.","zh":"這個片語給出移動或生長速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"clearly observable","meaning":"清楚可見","examples":[{"en":"The retreat may be clearly observable over a lifetime.","zh":"後退在一生中可能清楚可見。"},{"en":"Clearly observable means easy to see, notice, or measure.","zh":"clearly observable 指容易看見、注意到或量度。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may be clearly observable after several months of speaking practice.","zh":"經過數月口語練習後，學生的信心可能清楚可見。"},{"en":"If erosion moves a waterfall far enough, people can see the change without special instruments.","zh":"如果侵蝕使瀑布移動得夠遠，人們不用特別儀器也能看見變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something visible and noticeable.","zh":"這個片語描述可見而明顯的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"over a person’s lifetime","meaning":"在一個人的一生中","examples":[{"en":"The change can be observed over a person’s lifetime.","zh":"這種變化可以在一個人的一生中被觀察到。"},{"en":"Over a person’s lifetime means during the years that one person lives.","zh":"over a person’s lifetime 指在一個人活着的年份中。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood can change greatly over a person’s lifetime as shops, roads, and housing change.","zh":"隨着商店、道路和房屋改變，社區可以在一個人的一生中大幅改變。"},{"en":"If geological change is visible within one lifetime, it is relatively fast.","zh":"如果地質變化在一生中可見，它就相對快速。"},{"en":"The phrase uses human life as a time scale.","zh":"這個片語以人的生命作為時間尺度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fast-motion view","meaning":"快鏡畫面","examples":[{"en":"A fast-motion view would show the waterfall moving backwards.","zh":"快鏡畫面會顯示瀑布向後移動。"},{"en":"A fast-motion view is a sped-up view that shows slow changes quickly.","zh":"fast-motion view 指加速播放的畫面，快速顯示緩慢變化。"},{"en":"A fast-motion view of a plant growing can show weeks of growth in a few seconds.","zh":"植物生長的快鏡畫面可以在數秒內顯示數週生長。"},{"en":"If decades of erosion are compressed into a short video, the waterfall’s retreat becomes obvious.","zh":"如果數十年的侵蝕被壓縮成短片，瀑布後退就會變得明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a way to make slow processes visible.","zh":"這個片語描述令緩慢過程可見的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"span several decades","meaning":"跨越數十年","examples":[{"en":"The fast-motion view would span several decades.","zh":"快鏡畫面會跨越數十年。"},{"en":"Span several decades means cover a period of many tens of years.","zh":"span several decades 指涵蓋很多十年組成的時期。"},{"en":"A family photo album may span several decades, from grandparents’ youth to today.","zh":"家庭相簿可能跨越數十年，從祖父母年輕時到今天。"},{"en":"If a process spans decades, one short observation is not enough to understand it.","zh":"如果過程跨越數十年，一次短暫觀察不足以理解它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a long time range.","zh":"這個片語描述長時間範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"essentially unchanged height","meaning":"基本不變的高度","examples":[{"en":"The waterfall may keep an essentially unchanged height.","zh":"瀑布可能保持基本不變的高度。"},{"en":"Essentially unchanged height means the height remains basically the same, even if small changes occur.","zh":"essentially unchanged height 指高度基本保持相同，即使有小變化。"},{"en":"A student’s score may stay essentially unchanged if practice methods do not improve.","zh":"如果練習方法沒有改善，學生分數可能保持基本不變。"},{"en":"If a waterfall moves backward into higher land while maintaining its drop, its height may remain similar.","zh":"如果瀑布向較高地形後退但保持落差，其高度可能仍然相近。"},{"en":"The phrase allows minor changes but stresses overall sameness.","zh":"這個片語容許小變化，但強調整體相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"burrow backwards","meaning":"向後鑽蝕","examples":[{"en":"The waterfall appears to burrow backwards over time.","zh":"瀑布看起來隨時間向後鑽蝕。"},{"en":"Burrow backwards means seem to dig or cut its way backward through rock or land.","zh":"burrow backwards 指看似在岩石或土地中向後挖掘或切入。"},{"en":"A mouse may burrow through soil, but a waterfall “burrows” by erosion.","zh":"老鼠可能在泥土中鑽洞，而瀑布則透過侵蝕「鑽蝕」。"},{"en":"If water keeps cutting away the rock behind the fall, the waterfall shifts upstream.","zh":"如果水持續切走瀑布後方岩石，瀑布就會向上游移動。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a vivid image of erosion moving backward.","zh":"這個片語生動描繪侵蝕向後移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"with surprising evenness","meaning":"以令人驚訝的均勻程度","examples":[{"en":"The waterfall retreats with surprising evenness.","zh":"瀑布以令人驚訝的均勻程度後退。"},{"en":"With surprising evenness means in an unexpectedly steady and regular way.","zh":"with surprising evenness 指以出乎意料地穩定和有規律的方式。"},{"en":"A student may improve with surprising evenness if they practise a little every day.","zh":"如果學生每天練習一點點，可能以令人驚訝的穩定程度進步。"},{"en":"If erosion happens evenly across the fall, the waterfall moves backward without losing its general shape.","zh":"如果侵蝕在整個瀑布上均勻發生，瀑布就會在不失去大致形狀下向後移動。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses regularity that people might not expect.","zh":"這個片語強調人們可能想不到的規律性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"towards higher elevations","meaning":"朝較高海拔方向","examples":[{"en":"The retreat is towards higher elevations.","zh":"後退朝較高海拔方向進行。"},{"en":"Towards higher elevations means in the direction of land that is higher above sea level.","zh":"towards higher elevations 指朝海拔較高的土地方向。"},{"en":"Hikers move towards higher elevations as they climb from a valley to a mountain ridge.","zh":"遠足者從山谷爬向山脊時，就是朝較高海拔方向移動。"},{"en":"If a waterfall retreats upstream, it may move into higher land.","zh":"如果瀑布向上游後退，可能移入更高地形。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement toward greater height.","zh":"這個片語描述朝更高高度移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"through more hilly terrain","meaning":"穿過較多山丘的地形","examples":[{"en":"The waterfall may retreat through more hilly terrain.","zh":"瀑布可能穿過較多山丘的地形向後退。"},{"en":"Through more hilly terrain means across land with more hills and uneven slopes.","zh":"through more hilly terrain 指穿過有更多山丘和不平斜坡的土地。"},{"en":"A bus route through hilly terrain may take longer than one on flat roads.","zh":"穿過多山地形的巴士路線可能比平路路線需時更長。"},{"en":"If a waterfall retreats into hilly land, its path may encounter many rock features.","zh":"如果瀑布後退進入多山地形，其路徑可能遇上許多岩石特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement across uneven elevated land.","zh":"這個片語描述穿過不平而較高的土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a host of","meaning":"大量；許多","examples":[{"en":"A host of geological features can lie in the waterfall’s path.","zh":"大量地質特徵可能位於瀑布路徑上。"},{"en":"A host of means a large number of something.","zh":"a host of 指大量或許多某物。"},{"en":"A school fair may offer a host of activities, from games to food stalls.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能提供許多活動，從遊戲到食物攤位都有。"},{"en":"If a landscape has many rock forms, a retreating waterfall may pass through several of them.","zh":"如果景觀中有許多岩石形態，後退中的瀑布可能穿過其中幾種。"},{"en":"The phrase simply means many.","zh":"這個片語簡單指很多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"geological features","meaning":"地質特徵","examples":[{"en":"Islands, gorges and rock formations are geological features.","zh":"島嶼、峽谷和岩層都是地質特徵。"},{"en":"Geological features are natural landforms or rock structures shaped by Earth processes.","zh":"geological features 指由地球過程塑造的自然地貌或岩石結構。"},{"en":"Caves, cliffs, valleys, and volcanoes are geological features that students may study in geography.","zh":"洞穴、懸崖、山谷和火山都是學生在地理中可能研究的地質特徵。"},{"en":"If water and rock interact for a long time, new geological features may form.","zh":"如果水和岩石長時間互相作用，新的地質特徵可能形成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical features of the Earth.","zh":"這個片語描述地球的實體特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lie in something’s path","meaning":"位於……的路徑上","examples":[{"en":"Geological features may lie in the waterfall’s retreating path.","zh":"地質特徵可能位於瀑布後退路徑上。"},{"en":"Lie in something’s path means be located in the route something will take.","zh":"lie in something’s path 指位於某物將會經過的路線上。"},{"en":"A fallen tree may lie in a cyclist’s path and create danger.","zh":"倒下的樹可能位於單車手路徑上，造成危險。"},{"en":"If islands or gorges lie in a waterfall’s path, they may shape how it retreats.","zh":"如果島嶼或峽谷位於瀑布路徑上，可能影響它如何後退。"},{"en":"The phrase describes position along a route.","zh":"這個片語描述在路線上的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"retreating path","meaning":"後退路徑","examples":[{"en":"Many features may lie in a waterfall’s retreating path.","zh":"許多特徵可能位於瀑布的後退路徑上。"},{"en":"A retreating path is the route along which something moves backward over time.","zh":"retreating path 指某物隨時間向後移動所經過的路線。"},{"en":"A shrinking shoreline may leave a retreating path visible in old maps and photos.","zh":"收縮中的海岸線可能在舊地圖和照片中留下後退路徑。"},{"en":"If a waterfall retreats upstream, its path can pass through gorges and rock formations.","zh":"如果瀑布向上游後退，其路徑可以穿過峽谷和岩層。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the route of backward movement.","zh":"這個片語描述向後移動的路線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a prime example","meaning":"典型例子","examples":[{"en":"Victoria Falls is a prime example of this process.","zh":"維多利亞瀑布是這個過程的典型例子。"},{"en":"A prime example is a very clear and strong example of something.","zh":"prime example 指非常清楚而有力的例子。"},{"en":"A student who improves through daily practice is a prime example of steady effort paying off.","zh":"透過每天練習而進步的學生，是穩定努力有回報的典型例子。"},{"en":"If one waterfall clearly shows retreat and geological features, it is a good example to study.","zh":"如果一個瀑布清楚顯示後退和地質特徵，就很適合研究。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the best or clearest example.","zh":"這個片語突出最好或最清楚的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lower reaches","meaning":"下游河段","examples":[{"en":"Victoria Falls has lower reaches with spectacular geological features.","zh":"維多利亞瀑布的下游河段有壯觀地質特徵。"},{"en":"Lower reaches are the downstream parts of a river, closer to where the river continues away from its source.","zh":"lower reaches 指河流較下游的部分，接近河流離開源頭後繼續流動的地方。"},{"en":"Flooding in the lower reaches of a river may affect towns far from the mountains.","zh":"河流下游河段水浸可能影響遠離山區的城鎮。"},{"en":"If waterfalls retreat, the lower reaches may contain gorges and older erosion features.","zh":"如果瀑布後退，下游河段可能有峽谷和較早侵蝕特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the lower downstream section of a river system.","zh":"這個片語描述河流系統較低的下游部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be characterised by","meaning":"以……為特徵","examples":[{"en":"Its lower reaches are characterised by islands, gorges and rock formations.","zh":"其下游河段以島嶼、峽谷和岩層為特徵。"},{"en":"Be characterised by means have particular features that make something recognisable.","zh":"be characterised by 指具有令某物可被辨認的特定特徵。"},{"en":"A good classroom is characterised by clear rules, respect, and active learning.","zh":"好課室以清楚規則、尊重和主動學習為特徵。"},{"en":"If a river section is full of gorges and rock shapes, these features define its appearance.","zh":"如果河段充滿峽谷和岩石形態，這些特徵就定義其外觀。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces key features.","zh":"這個片語引出主要特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"spectacular islands, gorges and rock formations","meaning":"壯觀的島嶼、峽谷和岩層","examples":[{"en":"Victoria Falls is characterised by spectacular islands, gorges and rock formations.","zh":"維多利亞瀑布以壯觀的島嶼、峽谷和岩層為特徵。"},{"en":"Spectacular islands, gorges and rock formations are visually impressive land features shaped by water and rock.","zh":"spectacular islands, gorges and rock formations 指由水和岩石塑造、視覺上令人驚嘆的地貌。"},{"en":"A national park may attract visitors with spectacular cliffs, valleys, and unusual rocks.","zh":"國家公園可能以壯觀懸崖、山谷和奇特岩石吸引遊客。"},{"en":"If a waterfall retreats through rocky terrain, it can leave dramatic landforms behind.","zh":"如果瀑布穿過多岩地形後退，就能在身後留下壯觀地貌。"},{"en":"The phrase describes scenery that is both geological and visually striking.","zh":"這個片語描述既具地質意義又視覺震撼的景色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"occasionally causes problems","meaning":"偶爾造成問題","examples":[{"en":"The retreat of a waterfall occasionally causes problems.","zh":"瀑布後退偶爾造成問題。"},{"en":"Occasionally causes problems means sometimes leads to difficulties, though not always.","zh":"occasionally causes problems 指有時導致困難，但不是經常如此。"},{"en":"Heavy homework occasionally causes problems when students also have exams and family duties.","zh":"當學生同時有考試和家庭責任時，繁重功課偶爾會造成問題。"},{"en":"If a waterfall moves backward, nearby borders, roads, or buildings may be affected.","zh":"如果瀑布向後移動，附近邊界、道路或建築物可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes problems that happen from time to time.","zh":"這個片語描述不時發生的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be seen with","meaning":"可在……看到","examples":[{"en":"This problem can be seen with Niagara Falls.","zh":"這個問題可在尼亞加拉瀑布看到。"},{"en":"Be seen with means be observed in the case of a particular example.","zh":"be seen with 指可在某個特定例子中被觀察到。"},{"en":"This difficulty can be seen with students who understand grammar but fear speaking.","zh":"這種困難可在明白文法但害怕說話的學生身上看到。"},{"en":"If a general process appears clearly in one case, that case helps explain it.","zh":"如果一般過程在某個案例中清楚出現，該案例就有助解釋它。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an example that shows a problem.","zh":"這個片語引出能顯示問題的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in just over ten millennia","meaning":"在一萬多年內","examples":[{"en":"Niagara Falls has moved almost 11 kilometres upstream in just over ten millennia.","zh":"尼亞加拉瀑布在一萬多年內向上游移動了接近十一公里。"},{"en":"In just over ten millennia means in a little more than ten thousand years.","zh":"in just over ten millennia 指在稍多於一萬年的時間內。"},{"en":"Human farming has changed landscapes in just over ten millennia in many regions.","zh":"在許多地區，人類農耕在一萬多年內改變了景觀。"},{"en":"For geology, movement over ten thousand years can be relatively fast.","zh":"對地質而言，一萬年內的移動可以算相對快速。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a long but specific time span.","zh":"這個片語給出漫長但具體的時間跨度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"almost 11 kilometres upstream","meaning":"向上游接近十一公里","examples":[{"en":"The falls have moved almost 11 kilometres upstream.","zh":"瀑布已向上游移動接近十一公里。"},{"en":"Almost 11 kilometres upstream means nearly eleven kilometres in the direction against the river’s flow.","zh":"almost 11 kilometres upstream 指沿河流相反方向接近十一公里。"},{"en":"A village almost 11 kilometres upstream may be far enough to avoid city floods.","zh":"向上游接近十一公里的村莊可能足夠遠，可避開城市水浸。"},{"en":"If a waterfall retreats this far, the landscape and border discussions can change.","zh":"如果瀑布後退這麼遠，景觀和邊界討論都可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes distance and direction along a river.","zh":"這個片語描述沿河的距離和方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"mark the border of","meaning":"標示……的邊界","examples":[{"en":"The Niagara River marks the border of Canada and America.","zh":"尼亞加拉河標示加拿大和美國的邊界。"},{"en":"Mark the border of means show or form the boundary between two places.","zh":"mark the border of 指顯示或形成兩個地方之間的邊界。"},{"en":"A fence may mark the border of a school playground and a public park.","zh":"圍欄可以標示學校操場和公共公園的邊界。"},{"en":"If a river marks a border, changes in the river can raise political questions.","zh":"如果河流標示邊界，河流變化可能引發政治問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a physical feature acting as a boundary.","zh":"這個片語描述實體特徵作為邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as agreed in","meaning":"如……所協定","examples":[{"en":"The river marks the border, as agreed in 1819.","zh":"該河標示邊界，如1819年所協定。"},{"en":"As agreed in means according to an agreement made at a particular time.","zh":"as agreed in 指根據某時所作的協議。"},{"en":"The school trip will start at 8 a.m., as agreed in the meeting.","zh":"學校旅行將於早上八時開始，如會議所協定。"},{"en":"If a border was agreed in an old treaty, later natural changes may create complications.","zh":"如果邊界在舊條約中協定，後來的自然變化可能造成複雜問題。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the source of an agreement.","zh":"這個片語指出協議來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"detectable retreat","meaning":"可察覺的後退","examples":[{"en":"The detectable retreat of the falls has affected the border argument.","zh":"瀑布可察覺的後退影響了邊界爭論。"},{"en":"Detectable retreat means backward movement that can be noticed or measured.","zh":"detectable retreat 指可以被注意到或量度的向後移動。"},{"en":"A doctor may look for detectable improvement after a patient starts treatment.","zh":"病人開始治療後，醫生可能尋找可察覺的改善。"},{"en":"If retreat becomes detectable, it can no longer be dismissed as invisible change.","zh":"如果後退變得可察覺，就不能再被視為不可見變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement that evidence can show.","zh":"這個片語描述證據能顯示的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"technically means that","meaning":"技術上意味着","examples":[{"en":"The retreat technically means that the frontier has shifted.","zh":"後退技術上意味着邊界已經移動。"},{"en":"Technically means that introduces a precise result that may be true in a legal, scientific, or strict sense.","zh":"technically means that 引出在法律、科學或嚴格意義上可能成立的精確結果。"},{"en":"If a student submits one minute late, it technically means that the deadline was missed.","zh":"如果學生遲交一分鐘，技術上意味着已錯過截止時間。"},{"en":"If a river boundary moves with the waterfall, the official interpretation may become complicated.","zh":"如果河流邊界隨瀑布移動，官方解讀可能變得複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase often contrasts strict meaning with practical reality.","zh":"這個片語常對比嚴格意思與實際現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Canadian frontier","meaning":"加拿大邊界","examples":[{"en":"The Canadian frontier has technically advanced because of the retreat.","zh":"加拿大邊界因瀑布後退而在技術上推進。"},{"en":"Canadian frontier means the boundary or border area associated with Canada.","zh":"Canadian frontier 指與加拿大有關的邊界或邊境地區。"},{"en":"Border officers work near a national frontier to control movement between countries.","zh":"邊境人員在國界附近工作，以管制國家之間的人流。"},{"en":"If a natural border shifts, people may argue that one country’s frontier has moved.","zh":"如果天然邊界移動，人們可能爭論某國邊界已經改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a national boundary from Canada’s side.","zh":"這個片語從加拿大一方描述國家邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"advance at the expense of","meaning":"以犧牲……為代價而推進","examples":[{"en":"The Canadian frontier has advanced at the expense of America.","zh":"加拿大邊界以犧美國為代價而推進。"},{"en":"Advance at the expense of means gain ground or advantage while another side loses.","zh":"advance at the expense of 指一方取得土地或優勢，而另一方有所損失。"},{"en":"A company may expand at the expense of small shops if it takes their customers.","zh":"如果公司搶走小店顧客，就可能以犧牲小店為代價而擴張。"},{"en":"If a border shifts toward one country, that country gains while the other loses territory.","zh":"如果邊界向某國方向移動，該國得益而另一國失去領土。"},{"en":"The phrase shows one side benefits while another pays the cost.","zh":"這個片語顯示一方得益而另一方付出代價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"cause disputes","meaning":"引起爭議","examples":[{"en":"This argument has caused disputes.","zh":"這個論點引起了爭議。"},{"en":"Cause disputes means lead to disagreements or arguments between people or groups.","zh":"cause disputes 指導致人或群體之間出現分歧或爭論。"},{"en":"Unclear homework rules can cause disputes between students and teachers.","zh":"不清楚的功課規則可以引起學生和老師之間的爭議。"},{"en":"If a border appears to move, neighbouring countries may argue over the result.","zh":"如果邊界看似移動，鄰國可能就結果爭論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something producing conflict.","zh":"這個片語描述某事產生衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"more practically","meaning":"從實際角度來說","examples":[{"en":"More practically, it is important to limit the erosion.","zh":"從實際角度來說，限制侵蝕是重要的。"},{"en":"More practically means from a more realistic or useful point of view.","zh":"more practically 指從更現實或有用的角度來看。"},{"en":"More practically, students should sleep early before exams rather than rewrite all their notes at midnight.","zh":"從實際角度來說，學生考試前應早睡，而不是午夜重寫所有筆記。"},{"en":"If a border argument is abstract, protecting roads and buildings may be the more practical issue.","zh":"如果邊界爭論較抽象，保護道路和建築物可能是更實際的問題。"},{"en":"The phrase shifts attention from theory to real action.","zh":"這個片語把注意力由理論轉向實際行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"infrastructure","meaning":"基礎設施","examples":[{"en":"Hotels, roads and bridges are forms of infrastructure.","zh":"酒店、道路和橋樑都是基礎設施。"},{"en":"Infrastructure means the basic physical systems a place needs, such as roads, bridges, water, and power.","zh":"infrastructure 指一個地方所需的基本實體系統，例如道路、橋樑、供水和電力。"},{"en":"Good infrastructure helps students reach school and workers reach offices safely.","zh":"良好基礎設施幫助學生安全上學，工人安全上班。"},{"en":"If erosion damages infrastructure near a waterfall, tourism and local services may suffer.","zh":"如果侵蝕破壞瀑布附近基礎設施，旅遊業和本地服務可能受影響。"},{"en":"The word refers to essential built systems.","zh":"這個詞指必要的建設系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"scenic viewpoints","meaning":"觀景點","examples":[{"en":"Scenic viewpoints have been built near the falls.","zh":"瀑布附近已建有觀景點。"},{"en":"Scenic viewpoints are places designed for people to enjoy and photograph attractive views.","zh":"scenic viewpoints 指設計給人欣賞和拍攝優美景色的地方。"},{"en":"A hilltop lookout can be a scenic viewpoint over a city or harbour.","zh":"山頂瞭望台可以是俯瞰城市或海港的觀景點。"},{"en":"If erosion changes the land near a viewpoint, safety barriers may need repair.","zh":"如果侵蝕改變觀景點附近土地，安全欄杆可能需要維修。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visitor spots for viewing scenery.","zh":"這個片語描述供遊客觀賞景色的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be rigidly established","meaning":"被固定地建立","examples":[{"en":"Infrastructure near the falls is rigidly established.","zh":"瀑布附近的基礎設施被固定地建立。"},{"en":"Be rigidly established means be fixed firmly in place and difficult to move or change.","zh":"be rigidly established 指被牢固固定在某位置，難以移動或改變。"},{"en":"A school timetable may be rigidly established if buses, lessons, and lunch times all depend on it.","zh":"如果校巴、課堂和午飯時間都依賴時間表，學校時間表可能被固定地建立。"},{"en":"If hotels and roads are fixed near a moving waterfall, erosion creates practical problems.","zh":"如果酒店和道路固定在移動中的瀑布附近，侵蝕就會造成實際問題。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests little flexibility.","zh":"這個片語暗示缺乏彈性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"remain important to","meaning":"仍然重要","examples":[{"en":"It remains important to limit the erosion.","zh":"限制侵蝕仍然重要。"},{"en":"Remain important to means continue to be necessary or valuable for a purpose.","zh":"remain important to 指對某目的而言繼續有必要或有價值。"},{"en":"It remains important to practise speaking even after students learn grammar rules.","zh":"即使學生學會文法規則，練習口語仍然重要。"},{"en":"If erosion continues, controlling it stays important for safety and tourism.","zh":"如果侵蝕持續，控制侵蝕對安全和旅遊仍然重要。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that importance has not disappeared.","zh":"這個片語顯示重要性沒有消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"limit the erosion","meaning":"限制侵蝕","examples":[{"en":"Engineers try to limit the erosion at Niagara Falls.","zh":"工程師嘗試限制尼亞加拉瀑布的侵蝕。"},{"en":"Limit the erosion means reduce how quickly rock, soil, or land is worn away.","zh":"limit the erosion 指減慢岩石、泥土或土地被磨蝕的速度。"},{"en":"Planting grass can limit erosion on a school slope after heavy rain.","zh":"在學校山坡種草可以在大雨後限制侵蝕。"},{"en":"If erosion is limited, nearby roads, bridges, and viewpoints may last longer.","zh":"如果侵蝕受到限制，附近道路、橋樑和觀景點可能維持更久。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slowing natural damage.","zh":"這個片語描述減慢自然損耗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"for this reason","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"For this reason, the exposed ridges have been strengthened.","zh":"因此，外露岩脊已被加固。"},{"en":"For this reason means because of the point just mentioned.","zh":"for this reason 指因為剛才提到的原因。"},{"en":"Many students forget new words quickly; for this reason, teachers give revision tasks.","zh":"許多學生很快忘記新詞；因此，老師會安排溫習任務。"},{"en":"If erosion threatens infrastructure, engineers take protective action.","zh":"如果侵蝕威脅基礎設施，工程師就會採取保護行動。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a reason with a response.","zh":"這個片語把原因與反應連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"exposed ridges","meaning":"外露的山脊；外露岩脊","examples":[{"en":"The exposed ridges of the falls have been strengthened.","zh":"瀑布的外露岩脊已被加固。"},{"en":"Exposed ridges are raised lines of rock or land that are uncovered and open to erosion or weather.","zh":"exposed ridges 指沒有遮蔽、容易受侵蝕或天氣影響的凸起岩石或地形線。"},{"en":"Hikers should avoid exposed ridges during strong winds.","zh":"遠足者在強風中應避免走外露山脊。"},{"en":"If ridges near a waterfall are exposed, water and weather may weaken them.","zh":"如果瀑布附近岩脊外露，水和天氣可能削弱它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes vulnerable raised rock features.","zh":"這個片語描述脆弱的凸起岩石特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be extensively strengthened","meaning":"被大規模加固","examples":[{"en":"The exposed ridges have been extensively strengthened.","zh":"外露岩脊已被大規模加固。"},{"en":"Be extensively strengthened means be reinforced widely or thoroughly.","zh":"be extensively strengthened 指被廣泛或徹底加強支撐。"},{"en":"An old school building may be extensively strengthened before it is reopened.","zh":"舊校舍重新開放前可能被大規模加固。"},{"en":"If rock near a waterfall is unstable, engineers may add support in many places.","zh":"如果瀑布附近岩石不穩定，工程師可能在多處加支撐。"},{"en":"The phrase describes large-scale reinforcement.","zh":"這個片語描述大規模強化工程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"underwater barriers","meaning":"水底屏障","examples":[{"en":"Underwater barriers help divert strong river currents.","zh":"水底屏障幫助分流強勁河流。"},{"en":"Underwater barriers are structures placed below the water to block, guide, or slow water movement.","zh":"underwater barriers 指放在水下、用來阻擋、引導或減慢水流的結構。"},{"en":"A harbour may use underwater barriers to reduce strong waves near boats.","zh":"港口可能使用水底屏障減少船隻附近的強浪。"},{"en":"If barriers redirect the strongest current, erosion at one point may be reduced.","zh":"如果屏障改變最強水流方向，某處侵蝕可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes hidden structures used to control water.","zh":"這個片語描述用來控制水流的隱藏結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be installed to","meaning":"被安裝以……","examples":[{"en":"Underwater barriers were installed to divert the strongest currents.","zh":"水底屏障被安裝以分流最強水流。"},{"en":"Be installed to means be put in place for a particular purpose.","zh":"be installed to 指為某特定目的而被放置或設置。"},{"en":"Cameras may be installed to improve safety in a school corridor.","zh":"攝影機可能被安裝以改善學校走廊安全。"},{"en":"If barriers are installed to change water flow, they are part of an engineering solution.","zh":"如果屏障被安裝以改變水流，它們就是工程解決方案的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase connects construction with purpose.","zh":"這個片語把建設與目的連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"divert the strongest river currents","meaning":"分流最強的河流","examples":[{"en":"Barriers divert the strongest river currents.","zh":"屏障分流最強的河流。"},{"en":"Divert the strongest river currents means redirect the most powerful water flows away from a vulnerable area.","zh":"divert the strongest river currents 指把最強水流重新導向，離開脆弱地區。"},{"en":"Drainage channels can divert stormwater away from houses during heavy rain.","zh":"排水渠可以在大雨期間把雨水分流，遠離房屋。"},{"en":"If strong currents are diverted, erosion may slow near the protected rock.","zh":"如果強水流被分流，受保護岩石附近的侵蝕可能減慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes controlling the direction of powerful water.","zh":"這個片語描述控制強大水流的方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ambitious erosion-control measure","meaning":"雄心最大的侵蝕控制措施","examples":[{"en":"The most ambitious erosion-control measure took place in 1969.","zh":"雄心最大的侵蝕控制措施在1969年進行。"},{"en":"An ambitious erosion-control measure is a large and difficult action designed to reduce erosion.","zh":"ambitious erosion-control measure 指旨在減少侵蝕的大型而困難行動。"},{"en":"A city may launch an ambitious flood-control measure by rebuilding an entire drainage system.","zh":"城市可能透過重建整個排水系統，推行雄心勃勃的防洪措施。"},{"en":"If erosion threatens a famous landmark, engineers may attempt a bold solution.","zh":"如果侵蝕威脅著名地標，工程師可能嘗試大膽解決方案。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both scale and purpose.","zh":"這個片語強調規模和目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"take place","meaning":"發生；進行","examples":[{"en":"The erosion-control measure took place in 1969.","zh":"侵蝕控制措施在1969年進行。"},{"en":"Take place means happen or be carried out.","zh":"take place 指發生或被進行。"},{"en":"The school concert will take place in the hall on Friday.","zh":"學校音樂會將於星期五在禮堂舉行。"},{"en":"If a major engineering project takes place, planning and safety checks are needed.","zh":"如果大型工程項目進行，就需要規劃和安全檢查。"},{"en":"The phrase simply describes when or where an event happens.","zh":"這個片語簡單描述事件何時或在哪裡發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"American Falls","meaning":"美國瀑布","examples":[{"en":"The 1969 project focused on Niagara’s American Falls.","zh":"1969年的項目集中處理尼亞加拉的美國瀑布。"},{"en":"American Falls is one section of Niagara Falls on the American side.","zh":"American Falls 指尼亞加拉瀑布中位於美國一側的部分。"},{"en":"Visitors may view American Falls from platforms and scenic paths nearby.","zh":"遊客可以從附近平台和觀景小徑觀看美國瀑布。"},{"en":"If erosion affects American Falls, it can raise concerns about land, tourism, and safety.","zh":"如果侵蝕影響美國瀑布，就可能引起關於土地、旅遊和安全的憂慮。"},{"en":"The phrase names a particular waterfall within Niagara Falls.","zh":"這個片語指出尼亞加拉瀑布中的特定瀑布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"nibble away at","meaning":"一點一點侵蝕","examples":[{"en":"The retreat was nibbling away at American territory.","zh":"瀑布後退正在一點一點侵蝕美國領土。"},{"en":"Nibble away at means gradually reduce or damage something bit by bit.","zh":"nibble away at 指一點一點逐漸減少或損害某物。"},{"en":"Small daily expenses can nibble away at a student’s savings.","zh":"每日小額開支可以一點一點消耗學生儲蓄。"},{"en":"If erosion removes land little by little, territory may slowly shrink.","zh":"如果侵蝕一點一點移走土地，領土可能慢慢縮小。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow, repeated loss.","zh":"這個片語描述緩慢而反覆的損失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"American territory","meaning":"美國領土","examples":[{"en":"The retreat was reducing American territory.","zh":"瀑布後退正在減少美國領土。"},{"en":"American territory means land belonging to or controlled by the United States.","zh":"American territory 指屬於或由美國控制的土地。"},{"en":"A national border decides where American territory begins or ends.","zh":"國界決定美國領土從哪裡開始或結束。"},{"en":"If a natural boundary changes, people may debate whether territory has technically shifted.","zh":"如果天然邊界改變，人們可能爭論領土是否在技術上移動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to land under American sovereignty.","zh":"這個片語指美國主權下的土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the branch of the Niagara River","meaning":"尼亞加拉河的支流","examples":[{"en":"The branch of the Niagara River feeding American Falls was dammed.","zh":"為美國瀑布供水的尼亞加拉河支流被築壩截流。"},{"en":"The branch of the Niagara River means one part or channel of the river separated from the main flow.","zh":"branch of the Niagara River 指尼亞加拉河從主流分出的其中一部分或水道。"},{"en":"A river branch may carry water to a smaller stream, island, or wetland.","zh":"河流支流可能把水帶到較小溪流、島嶼或濕地。"},{"en":"If one branch is blocked, water may be redirected to another channel.","zh":"如果一條支流被阻塞，水可能被重新導向另一條水道。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a divided part of a river system.","zh":"這個片語描述河流系統中分出的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"feed these subsidiary falls","meaning":"為這些附屬瀑布供水","examples":[{"en":"A branch of the river feeds these subsidiary falls.","zh":"一條河流支流為這些附屬瀑布供水。"},{"en":"Feed these subsidiary falls means supply water to these smaller or secondary waterfalls.","zh":"feed these subsidiary falls 指向這些較小或次要瀑布供應水。"},{"en":"A pipe feeds water to a garden fountain so it can keep running.","zh":"水管為花園噴泉供水，使它能持續運作。"},{"en":"If the branch is dammed, the smaller falls may temporarily dry out.","zh":"如果支流被築壩截流，較小瀑布可能暫時乾涸。"},{"en":"The phrase describes supplying water to a waterfall.","zh":"這個片語描述向瀑布供應水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"subsidiary falls","meaning":"附屬瀑布","examples":[{"en":"American Falls are described as subsidiary falls.","zh":"美國瀑布被描述為附屬瀑布。"},{"en":"Subsidiary falls are smaller or secondary waterfalls connected to a larger waterfall system.","zh":"subsidiary falls 指與較大瀑布系統相連的較小或次要瀑布。"},{"en":"A tourist map may label smaller side falls as subsidiary falls beside the main attraction.","zh":"旅遊地圖可能把主要景點旁邊較小的側瀑標示為附屬瀑布。"},{"en":"If water is diverted away from subsidiary falls, the main fall may receive extra flow.","zh":"如果水流從附屬瀑布分流走，主瀑布可能接收額外水量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes falls that are not the main central waterfall.","zh":"這個片語描述不是主要中心瀑布的瀑布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be dammed","meaning":"被築壩截流","examples":[{"en":"The branch of the river was dammed.","zh":"該河流支流被築壩截流。"},{"en":"Be dammed means be blocked by a dam so that water flow is stopped or controlled.","zh":"be dammed 指被水壩阻擋，使水流停止或受控制。"},{"en":"A small stream may be dammed to create a pond for irrigation.","zh":"小溪可能被築壩截流，以形成灌溉用池塘。"},{"en":"If a river branch is dammed, the water can be redirected elsewhere.","zh":"如果河流支流被築壩截流，水可以被重新導向其他地方。"},{"en":"The phrase describes water being controlled by a barrier.","zh":"這個片語描述水流被屏障控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"absorb the excess flow","meaning":"吸收額外水流","examples":[{"en":"The main Horseshoe Falls absorbed the excess flow.","zh":"主要的馬蹄瀑布吸收了額外水流。"},{"en":"Absorb the excess flow means receive and carry extra water that has been redirected from elsewhere.","zh":"absorb the excess flow 指接收並承載從其他地方轉移來的額外水。"},{"en":"A larger drain can absorb excess flow when a small pipe is blocked.","zh":"當小水管堵塞時，較大的排水渠可以吸收額外水流。"},{"en":"If one waterfall is shut off, another may receive more water than usual.","zh":"如果一個瀑布被截流，另一個瀑布可能接收比平時更多的水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes taking in additional water flow.","zh":"這個片語描述接收額外水流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the main Horseshoe Falls","meaning":"主要的馬蹄瀑布","examples":[{"en":"The main Horseshoe Falls absorbed the excess flow.","zh":"主要的馬蹄瀑布吸收了額外水流。"},{"en":"The main Horseshoe Falls is the largest and most powerful section of Niagara Falls.","zh":"main Horseshoe Falls 指尼亞加拉瀑布中最大且水勢最強的部分。"},{"en":"Visitors often recognise Horseshoe Falls by its curved shape.","zh":"遊客常因其彎曲形狀而辨認出馬蹄瀑布。"},{"en":"If extra water is diverted to Horseshoe Falls, its flow becomes even stronger.","zh":"如果額外水流被導向馬蹄瀑布，其水流會變得更強。"},{"en":"The phrase names the principal waterfall in the Niagara system.","zh":"這個片語指出尼亞加拉系統中的主要瀑布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"dry and exposed river bottom","meaning":"乾涸並外露的河床","examples":[{"en":"The dry and exposed river bottom allowed engineers to work.","zh":"乾涸並外露的河床讓工程師能夠工作。"},{"en":"A dry and exposed river bottom is the riverbed visible after water has been removed or diverted.","zh":"dry and exposed river bottom 指水被移走或分流後可見的河床。"},{"en":"During drought, a river bottom may become dry and exposed, showing stones and mud.","zh":"乾旱期間，河床可能乾涸並外露，露出石頭和泥。"},{"en":"If engineers can see the river bottom, they can inspect and repair unstable rock more safely.","zh":"如果工程師能看見河床，就能更安全地檢查和修復不穩定岩石。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a normally underwater area made visible.","zh":"這個片語描述平時在水下、現在可見的區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"cliff face","meaning":"懸崖面","examples":[{"en":"The exposed cliff face was strengthened by engineers.","zh":"外露的懸崖面由工程師加固。"},{"en":"A cliff face is a steep vertical or near-vertical rock surface.","zh":"cliff face 指陡直或接近垂直的岩石表面。"},{"en":"Climbers examine a cliff face for cracks before climbing.","zh":"攀登者在攀爬前會檢查懸崖面有沒有裂縫。"},{"en":"If a cliff face is weakened by erosion, rocks may fall and create danger.","zh":"如果懸崖面被侵蝕削弱，岩石可能掉落並造成危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the front surface of a steep rock wall.","zh":"這個片語描述陡峭岩壁的正面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a team of US Army engineers","meaning":"一隊美國陸軍工程師","examples":[{"en":"A team of US Army engineers strengthened the unstable rock.","zh":"一隊美國陸軍工程師加固了不穩定岩石。"},{"en":"A team of US Army engineers means a group of engineers from the United States Army.","zh":"a team of US Army engineers 指來自美國陸軍的一組工程師。"},{"en":"A team of engineers may be called in when a bridge, dam, or road is unsafe.","zh":"當橋樑、水壩或道路不安全時，可能會召來一隊工程師。"},{"en":"If rock near a waterfall is unstable, specialist engineers may need to secure it.","zh":"如果瀑布附近岩石不穩定，專業工程師可能需要固定它。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the professional group doing the work.","zh":"這個片語指出進行工作的專業團隊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"bolts, cement and brackets","meaning":"螺栓、水泥和支架","examples":[{"en":"The engineers used bolts, cement and brackets.","zh":"工程師使用螺栓、水泥和支架。"},{"en":"Bolts, cement and brackets are materials or fittings used to fasten, support, and strengthen structures.","zh":"bolts, cement and brackets 指用來固定、支撐和加固結構的材料或配件。"},{"en":"Workers may use bolts and brackets to secure a heavy shelf to a wall.","zh":"工人可能使用螺栓和支架把沉重書架固定在牆上。"},{"en":"If unstable rock is fixed with strong materials, it is less likely to collapse.","zh":"如果不穩定岩石用堅固材料固定，就較不容易塌下。"},{"en":"The phrase lists practical tools for reinforcement.","zh":"這個片語列出實際加固工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"strengthen unstable rock","meaning":"加固不穩定的岩石","examples":[{"en":"The engineers used materials to strengthen unstable rock.","zh":"工程師使用材料加固不穩定的岩石。"},{"en":"Strengthen unstable rock means make weak or unsafe rock more secure.","zh":"strengthen unstable rock 指使脆弱或不安全的岩石變得更穩固。"},{"en":"Workers may strengthen an unstable wall before allowing people to walk nearby.","zh":"工人可能在允許人們靠近前加固不穩定的牆。"},{"en":"If rock is strengthened, it is less likely to break away under water pressure.","zh":"如果岩石被加固，就較不容易在水壓下崩落。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making natural rock safer through engineering.","zh":"這個片語描述透過工程使天然岩石更安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"temporary dam","meaning":"臨時水壩","examples":[{"en":"The temporary dam was destroyed after five months.","zh":"臨時水壩在五個月後被摧毀。"},{"en":"A temporary dam is a short-term barrier built to hold back or divert water.","zh":"temporary dam 指為短期阻擋或分流水而建的屏障。"},{"en":"Workers may build a temporary dam before repairing a leaking river wall.","zh":"工人在修理漏水河牆前可能建造臨時水壩。"},{"en":"If a temporary dam blocks water, engineers can work on a normally wet area.","zh":"如果臨時水壩阻擋水流，工程師就能在平時濕的地方工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a dam not meant to last permanently.","zh":"這個片語描述並非永久使用的水壩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be destroyed with explosives","meaning":"被炸藥炸毀","examples":[{"en":"The temporary dam was destroyed with explosives.","zh":"臨時水壩被炸藥炸毀。"},{"en":"Be destroyed with explosives means be broken apart using controlled explosive materials.","zh":"be destroyed with explosives 指使用受控爆炸材料把某物炸開。"},{"en":"An unsafe old bridge may be destroyed with explosives after nearby people are moved away.","zh":"不安全舊橋可能在附近居民撤離後被炸藥炸毀。"},{"en":"If a dam must be removed quickly, explosives can break it open.","zh":"如果水壩必須快速移除，炸藥可以把它炸開。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a forceful method of demolition.","zh":"這個片語描述強力拆除方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"return water to","meaning":"使水流回到……","examples":[{"en":"Destroying the dam returned water to the falls.","zh":"炸毀水壩使水流回到瀑布。"},{"en":"Return water to means allow water to flow back to a place where it normally goes.","zh":"return water to 指讓水重新流回它通常會去的地方。"},{"en":"After repairs, workers opened the pipe to return water to the fountain.","zh":"維修後，工人打開水管，使水流回到噴泉。"},{"en":"If a temporary barrier is removed, the original flow can be restored.","zh":"如果臨時屏障被移除，原本水流就能恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase describes restoring water movement.","zh":"這個片語描述恢復水流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"inexorable erosion process","meaning":"無法阻擋的侵蝕過程","examples":[{"en":"The inexorable erosion process was considerably slowed.","zh":"無法阻擋的侵蝕過程被明顯減慢。"},{"en":"An inexorable erosion process is erosion that seems impossible to stop completely.","zh":"inexorable erosion process 指看似不可能完全停止的侵蝕。"},{"en":"Sea waves can create an inexorable erosion process along an unprotected coast.","zh":"海浪可以在沒有保護的海岸形成無法阻擋的侵蝕過程。"},{"en":"Even if engineers slow erosion, natural forces may continue working over time.","zh":"即使工程師減慢侵蝕，自然力量仍可能隨時間繼續作用。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the process is persistent and hard to resist.","zh":"這個片語強調該過程持續而難以抵抗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"considerably slowed","meaning":"明顯減慢","examples":[{"en":"The erosion process was considerably slowed.","zh":"侵蝕過程被明顯減慢。"},{"en":"Considerably slowed means made much slower than before.","zh":"considerably slowed 指比以前慢得多。"},{"en":"A student’s progress may be considerably slowed if they stop practising for several months.","zh":"如果學生幾個月停止練習，進步可能明顯減慢。"},{"en":"If engineers strengthen rock and divert currents, erosion can become much slower.","zh":"如果工程師加固岩石並分流水流，侵蝕可以大幅減慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a noticeable reduction in speed.","zh":"這個片語描述速度明顯下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"write TRUE, FALSE, or NOT GIVEN","meaning":"寫上 TRUE、FALSE 或 NOT GIVEN","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write TRUE, FALSE, or NOT GIVEN for the statements.","zh":"考生為各陳述寫上 TRUE、FALSE 或 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"Write TRUE, FALSE, or NOT GIVEN means decide whether each statement matches, contradicts, or is not covered by the passage.","zh":"write TRUE, FALSE, or NOT GIVEN 指判斷每句陳述是否符合、矛盾或文章沒有提及。"},{"en":"In reading exams, students should not use outside knowledge for TRUE, FALSE, or NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生不應用外部知識回答 TRUE、FALSE 或 NOT GIVEN 題。"},{"en":"If a statement is not mentioned, the answer should be NOT GIVEN, not a guess.","zh":"如果陳述沒有被提及，答案應是 NOT GIVEN，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個片語給出常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與資料一致","examples":[{"en":"A TRUE statement agrees with the information in the passage.","zh":"TRUE 陳述與文章中的資料一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the information means match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If a passage says erosion was slowed, a statement saying erosion was reduced in speed agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說侵蝕被減慢，而陳述說侵蝕速度降低，就是與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should check exact meaning, not just similar words.","zh":"學生應檢查準確意思，而不只是相似字詞。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct support from the text.","zh":"這個片語描述文本的直接支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A FALSE statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"FALSE 陳述與文章中的資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradict the information means say the opposite of what the passage states.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章所述相反的意思。"},{"en":"If the passage says a river was dammed, a statement saying it was never blocked contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說河流被築壩截流，而陳述說它從未被阻擋，就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should choose FALSE only when there is clear disagreement with the text.","zh":"學生只有在與文本清楚不一致時才應選 FALSE。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct conflict with the passage.","zh":"這個片語描述與文章直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"Write NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果沒有這方面的資料，則寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not tell us whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文章沒有告訴我們該陳述是真還是假。"},{"en":"If a passage describes a waterfall’s height but not ticket prices, there is no information on ticket prices.","zh":"如果文章描述瀑布高度但沒有提到票價，就沒有票價方面的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not infer beyond the passage when the answer is NOT GIVEN.","zh":"當答案是 NOT GIVEN 時，學生不應超出文章推斷。"},{"en":"The phrase explains when evidence is missing.","zh":"這個片語解釋證據缺失的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"international boundaries","meaning":"國際邊界","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions waterfalls on international boundaries.","zh":"題目提到位於國際邊界上的瀑布。"},{"en":"International boundaries are borders that separate one country from another.","zh":"international boundaries 指分隔一個國家與另一個國家的邊界。"},{"en":"Rivers, mountains, and fences can sometimes form international boundaries.","zh":"河流、山脈和圍欄有時可以形成國際邊界。"},{"en":"If a waterfall lies on an international boundary, more than one country may share responsibility for it.","zh":"如果瀑布位於國際邊界上，可能由多於一個國家共同負責。"},{"en":"The phrase describes borders between nations.","zh":"這個片語描述國與國之間的邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"create waterfalls faster than erosion","meaning":"比侵蝕更快形成瀑布","examples":[{"en":"Landslides can create waterfalls faster than slow erosion.","zh":"山泥傾瀉可以比緩慢侵蝕更快形成瀑布。"},{"en":"Create waterfalls faster than erosion means form waterfalls more quickly than the gradual wearing away of rock does.","zh":"create waterfalls faster than erosion 指形成瀑布的速度比岩石逐漸磨蝕更快。"},{"en":"A sudden road collapse can create a problem faster than ordinary wear and tear.","zh":"突然路陷可以比普通磨損更快造成問題。"},{"en":"If land shifts suddenly, water may be forced over a drop almost at once.","zh":"如果土地突然移動，水可能幾乎立刻被迫流過落差。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts sudden formation with slow natural change.","zh":"這個片語對比突然形成與緩慢自然變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"produce the most waterfalls","meaning":"形成最多瀑布","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether glaciers have produced the most waterfalls.","zh":"題目問冰川是否形成最多瀑布。"},{"en":"Produce the most waterfalls means create a greater number of waterfalls than other causes do.","zh":"produce the most waterfalls 指比其他成因創造更多瀑布。"},{"en":"A school activity that attracts the most students may be considered the most popular.","zh":"吸引最多學生的學校活動可以被視為最受歡迎。"},{"en":"If glaciers shape many basins and cliffs, they may create many waterfall sites.","zh":"如果冰川塑造許多盆地和懸崖，就可能創造許多瀑布地點。"},{"en":"The phrase compares which cause creates the greatest number.","zh":"這個片語比較哪個成因創造最多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a Grade Ten waterfall","meaning":"十級瀑布","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Niagara is a Grade Ten waterfall.","zh":"題目問尼亞加拉是否是十級瀑布。"},{"en":"A Grade Ten waterfall is a waterfall ranked at the highest level on a ten-point scale.","zh":"Grade Ten waterfall 指在十級尺度上被評為最高級別的瀑布。"},{"en":"A student receiving the highest grade has reached the top of the marking scale.","zh":"得到最高分的學生達到評分尺度頂級。"},{"en":"If a waterfall has exceptional height and flow, it may qualify for the highest grade.","zh":"如果瀑布高度和水流量極突出，就可能符合最高級別。"},{"en":"The phrase describes top-level classification of waterfall power.","zh":"這個片語描述瀑布力量的頂級分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete the diagrams","meaning":"完成圖表","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the diagrams using words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成圖表。"},{"en":"Complete the diagrams means fill labels or missing parts in pictures or charts.","zh":"complete the diagrams 指填寫圖像或圖表中的標籤或缺失部分。"},{"en":"In science class, students may complete diagrams of the water cycle with words like evaporation and rainfall.","zh":"在科學課中，學生可能用 evaporation 和 rainfall 等字完成水循環圖。"},{"en":"If a diagram shows a waterfall, students must match labels to the correct parts.","zh":"如果圖表顯示瀑布，學生必須把標籤配對到正確部分。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction for visual tasks.","zh":"這個片語是視覺題常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個詞","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose no more than three words from the passage.","zh":"考生從文章中選擇不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案必須包含三個詞或更少。"},{"en":"If the answer is “rock face,” it follows the three-word limit.","zh":"如果答案是 “rock face”，就符合三詞限制。"},{"en":"Writing four words when only three are allowed may make the answer wrong.","zh":"只允許三詞時寫四詞，可能令答案錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit for exam answers.","zh":"這個片語給出考試答案的嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"answer the questions","meaning":"回答問題","examples":[{"en":"Candidates answer the questions using words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞回答問題。"},{"en":"Answer the questions means provide the required information in response to each item.","zh":"answer the questions 指針對每一題提供所需資訊。"},{"en":"Students should read the question carefully before answering the questions in a test.","zh":"學生在測驗中回答問題前應仔細閱讀題目。"},{"en":"If answers must come from the passage, outside knowledge should not be used.","zh":"如果答案必須來自文章，就不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a basic exam task instruction.","zh":"這個片語給出基本考試任務指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個詞","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose no more than two words from the passage.","zh":"考生從文章中選擇不多於兩個詞。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must contain two words or fewer.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案必須包含兩個詞或更少。"},{"en":"“Plunge pool” is acceptable under a two-word limit.","zh":"“Plunge pool” 符合兩詞限制。"},{"en":"If students write an extra word, the answer may break the instruction.","zh":"如果學生多寫一個詞，答案可能違反指示。"},{"en":"The phrase tells students to keep answers short and exact.","zh":"這個片語告訴學生答案要短而準確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"examples of","meaning":"……的例子","examples":[{"en":"Gorges and rock formations are examples of geological features.","zh":"峽谷和岩層是地質特徵的例子。"},{"en":"Examples of means specific cases that show a larger category or idea.","zh":"examples of 指能展示較大類別或概念的具體例子。"},{"en":"Apples and oranges are examples of fruit.","zh":"蘋果和橙是水果的例子。"},{"en":"If students know examples of a concept, they can recognise it more easily in a passage.","zh":"如果學生知道某概念的例子，就更容易在文章中辨認它。"},{"en":"The phrase connects specific items to a general group.","zh":"這個片語把具體項目連接到一般群組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"benefit from","meaning":"從……中受益","examples":[{"en":"The question asks who has benefited from the erosion at Niagara Falls.","zh":"題目問誰從尼亞加拉瀑布的侵蝕中受益。"},{"en":"Benefit from means gain an advantage or receive something useful from a situation.","zh":"benefit from 指從某情況中獲得優勢或有用東西。"},{"en":"Students benefit from clear feedback because they know what to improve.","zh":"學生從清楚回饋中受益，因為他們知道要改善甚麼。"},{"en":"If erosion shifts a boundary, one side may gain territory while another loses it.","zh":"如果侵蝕移動邊界，一方可能獲得領土，而另一方失去領土。"},{"en":"The phrase describes receiving an advantage.","zh":"這個片語描述獲得好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"control water movements","meaning":"控制水流移動","examples":[{"en":"Underwater barriers are used to control some water movements.","zh":"水底屏障用來控制部分水流移動。"},{"en":"Control water movements means guide, slow, or redirect how water flows.","zh":"control water movements 指引導、減慢或改變水流方式。"},{"en":"City drains control water movements during heavy rain to prevent flooding.","zh":"城市排水渠在大雨期間控制水流移動，以防水浸。"},{"en":"If engineers control currents near a waterfall, they may reduce erosion in dangerous areas.","zh":"如果工程師控制瀑布附近水流，就可能減少危險地區侵蝕。"},{"en":"The phrase describes managing the direction and force of water.","zh":"這個片語描述管理水的方向和力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"geological parts","meaning":"地質部位","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which geological parts the 1969 project focused on.","zh":"題目問1969年項目集中處理哪些地質部位。"},{"en":"Geological parts are physical rock or land features involved in a natural formation.","zh":"geological parts 指自然地貌中涉及的實體岩石或土地部分。"},{"en":"In a volcano diagram, geological parts may include the crater, vent, and magma chamber.","zh":"在火山圖中，地質部位可能包括火山口、通道和岩漿房。"},{"en":"If engineers repair geological parts of a waterfall, they may work on the riverbed or cliff face.","zh":"如果工程師修復瀑布的地質部位，可能處理河床或懸崖面。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to natural structural components of the landscape.","zh":"這個片語指景觀中的天然結構組成部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"集中處理；聚焦於","examples":[{"en":"The 1969 project focused on the river bottom and cliff face.","zh":"1969年的項目集中處理河床和懸崖面。"},{"en":"Focus on means give most attention, effort, or resources to something.","zh":"focus on 指把大部分注意力、努力或資源放在某事上。"},{"en":"A student should focus on weak grammar points before an exam.","zh":"學生考試前應集中處理薄弱文法點。"},{"en":"If engineers focus on unstable rock, they can reduce the most serious risk first.","zh":"如果工程師集中處理不穩定岩石，就能先減少最嚴重風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes choosing a main target for attention.","zh":"這個片語描述選定主要關注目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 91 - Waterfalls.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 92":[{"front":"The Year Without a Summer","meaning":"無夏之年","examples":[{"en":"The year 1816 became known as the year without a summer.","zh":"1816年被稱為無夏之年。"},{"en":"The Year Without a Summer refers to a year when normal summer warmth almost disappeared.","zh":"The Year Without a Summer 指正常夏季暖意幾乎消失的一年。"},{"en":"A farmer would fear a year without a summer because crops need warmth to grow.","zh":"農民會害怕無夏之年，因為農作物需要溫暖天氣生長。"},{"en":"If temperatures stay low for months, harvests can fail and food prices can rise.","zh":"如果氣溫連續數月偏低，收成可能失敗，糧食價格也可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an extremely unusual cold year, not just a cool summer.","zh":"這個片語描述極不尋常的寒冷年份，而不只是較涼的夏天。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a strange year indeed","meaning":"確實是奇怪的一年","examples":[{"en":"1816 was a strange year indeed.","zh":"1816年確實是奇怪的一年。"},{"en":"A strange year indeed means a year that was truly unusual and difficult to explain.","zh":"A strange year indeed 指一年真的非常不尋常，而且難以解釋。"},{"en":"A school might call it a strange year indeed if exams, holidays, and lessons were all disrupted.","zh":"如果考試、假期和課堂全被打亂，學校可能稱那一年確實是奇怪的一年。"},{"en":"When normal patterns disappear, people may remember that year as strange indeed.","zh":"當正常模式消失，人們可能會記得那確實是奇怪的一年。"},{"en":"This phrase adds emphasis: the year was not just slightly odd, but clearly unusual.","zh":"這個片語加強語氣：那一年不只是有點奇怪，而是明顯不尋常。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in midsummer","meaning":"在盛夏","examples":[{"en":"Snow fell in midsummer in parts of America.","zh":"美國部分地區在盛夏下雪。"},{"en":"In midsummer means during the middle of summer, when weather is usually warm.","zh":"In midsummer 指在夏季中段，通常天氣溫暖的時候。"},{"en":"If people wear coats in midsummer, the weather is clearly unusual.","zh":"如果人們在盛夏穿大衣，天氣明顯不尋常。"},{"en":"Snow in midsummer can damage crops because plants expect warmth, not frost.","zh":"盛夏下雪可以破壞農作物，因為植物需要溫暖，而不是霜雪。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the surprising timing of an event.","zh":"這個片語突出事件發生時間令人意外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a dry fog","meaning":"乾霧","examples":[{"en":"A dry fog covered large areas of land.","zh":"乾霧覆蓋大片土地。"},{"en":"A dry fog is a thick haze that looks like fog but is not caused mainly by moisture.","zh":"Dry fog 是看似霧但主要不是由水分造成的濃霧狀煙霾。"},{"en":"People may notice a dry fog when smoke or dust makes the air look grey.","zh":"當煙或塵令空氣變灰，人們可能會注意到乾霧。"},{"en":"If a dry fog blocks sunlight, the day can feel darker and colder.","zh":"如果乾霧遮擋陽光，白天可能變得更暗和更冷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes poor visibility caused by particles in the air.","zh":"這個片語描述由空氣中粒子造成的能見度差。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cover the land so thickly that","meaning":"厚厚地覆蓋土地，以致……","examples":[{"en":"The fog covered the land so thickly that snow fell.","zh":"霧厚厚地覆蓋土地，以致下雪。"},{"en":"To cover the land so thickly that something happens means to spread over an area in a very heavy layer.","zh":"To cover the land so thickly that something happens 指以很厚的一層覆蓋某地，並造成結果。"},{"en":"Smoke can cover a neighbourhood so thickly that people keep windows closed.","zh":"煙霧可以厚厚地覆蓋社區，以致人們關上窗戶。"},{"en":"If ash covers fields so thickly, crops may receive too little sunlight.","zh":"如果火山灰厚厚地覆蓋田地，農作物可能得到太少陽光。"},{"en":"This structure shows that the covering is strong enough to cause a result.","zh":"這個結構顯示覆蓋程度強到足以造成結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"large parts of","meaning":"大部分……","examples":[{"en":"Large parts of the country were affected by unusual cold.","zh":"該國大部分地區受到異常寒冷影響。"},{"en":"Large parts of a place means many areas within that place.","zh":"Large parts of a place 指某地方內的許多地區。"},{"en":"Large parts of the city lost electricity after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，城市大部分地區停電。"},{"en":"If large parts of a country are affected, the problem becomes national rather than local.","zh":"如果一個國家大部分地區受影響，問題就變成全國性，而不是地方性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a wide area, not a single small location.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛地區，而不是單一小地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be gripped by","meaning":"被……籠罩；受……控制","examples":[{"en":"Large parts of the country were gripped by intense cold.","zh":"該國大部分地區被嚴寒籠罩。"},{"en":"To be gripped by something means to be strongly affected or held under its control.","zh":"To be gripped by something 指被某事強烈影響或控制。"},{"en":"A city may be gripped by fear after several serious accidents.","zh":"幾宗嚴重事故後，一座城市可能被恐懼籠罩。"},{"en":"If a region is gripped by cold, daily life, transport, and farming can all be disrupted.","zh":"如果一個地區被寒冷籠罩，日常生活、交通和農業都可能受干擾。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a powerful condition that people cannot easily escape.","zh":"這個片語暗示一種人們不易擺脫的強大狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an intense and lingering cold front","meaning":"強烈而持續不散的冷鋒","examples":[{"en":"The country was gripped by an intense and lingering cold front.","zh":"該國被一股強烈而持續不散的冷鋒籠罩。"},{"en":"An intense and lingering cold front is a strong mass of cold air that stays for a long time.","zh":"Intense and lingering cold front 是一股強烈且停留很久的冷空氣。"},{"en":"A lingering cold front can make people keep heating on even after spring begins.","zh":"持續不散的冷鋒可以令人即使春天開始後仍開暖氣。"},{"en":"If a cold front remains for weeks, crops may stop growing normally.","zh":"如果冷鋒停留數星期，農作物可能停止正常生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cold weather that is both strong and slow to leave.","zh":"這個片語描述既強烈又遲遲不離開的寒冷天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the situation was no better","meaning":"情況並沒有好轉","examples":[{"en":"The situation was no better in Great Britain and Europe.","zh":"英國和歐洲的情況並沒有好轉。"},{"en":"The situation was no better means conditions were just as bad somewhere else.","zh":"The situation was no better 指另一地方的情況同樣糟糕。"},{"en":"The train was delayed, and the situation was no better on the bus routes.","zh":"火車延誤，而巴士路線的情況也沒有好轉。"},{"en":"If one region suffers and another is no better, the problem is widespread.","zh":"如果一個地區受苦，而另一地也沒有好轉，問題就是廣泛的。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two places and shows both had serious difficulties.","zh":"這個片語比較兩地，並顯示兩者都有嚴重困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Great Britain and Europe","meaning":"英國和歐洲","examples":[{"en":"Great Britain and Europe also suffered from cold and wet weather.","zh":"英國和歐洲也遭受寒冷和潮濕天氣。"},{"en":"Great Britain and Europe refers to Britain together with the wider European region.","zh":"Great Britain and Europe 指英國以及更廣泛的歐洲地區。"},{"en":"A history lesson may compare weather effects in America with those in Great Britain and Europe.","zh":"歷史課可能比較美國與英國和歐洲所受的天氣影響。"},{"en":"If Great Britain and Europe both suffer crop failures, food supply can become unstable.","zh":"如果英國和歐洲都出現農作物歉收，糧食供應可能變得不穩。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the wider geographical area affected.","zh":"這個片語指出受影響的較廣泛地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cool temperatures","meaning":"涼冷的氣溫","examples":[{"en":"Cool temperatures persisted for months.","zh":"涼冷的氣溫持續數月。"},{"en":"Cool temperatures are lower-than-warm conditions, though not always freezing.","zh":"Cool temperatures 是低於溫暖水平的天氣，但不一定結冰。"},{"en":"Cool temperatures in summer may make beaches empty and outdoor cafés quiet.","zh":"夏季涼冷的氣溫可能令海灘冷清，戶外咖啡店安靜。"},{"en":"If cool temperatures last too long, plants may grow more slowly.","zh":"如果涼冷氣溫持續太久，植物可能生長較慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weather that is noticeably cooler than expected.","zh":"這個片語描述明顯比預期涼的天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"wet weather","meaning":"潮濕多雨的天氣","examples":[{"en":"Wet weather persisted for months in Europe.","zh":"歐洲潮濕多雨的天氣持續數月。"},{"en":"Wet weather means rainy, damp, or very moist weather.","zh":"Wet weather 指下雨、潮濕或水分很重的天氣。"},{"en":"Wet weather can make students bring umbrellas and arrive at school with wet shoes.","zh":"潮濕多雨的天氣會令學生帶傘，並穿着濕鞋到校。"},{"en":"If wet weather continues, farmers may struggle to dry crops or work in fields.","zh":"如果潮濕天氣持續，農民可能難以曬乾作物或在田裏工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weather with frequent rain or damp conditions.","zh":"這個片語描述經常下雨或潮濕的天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"persist for months","meaning":"持續數月","examples":[{"en":"Cool temperatures and wet weather persisted for months.","zh":"涼冷氣溫和潮濕多雨天氣持續數月。"},{"en":"To persist for months means to continue for several months without stopping.","zh":"To persist for months 指連續數月不停地持續。"},{"en":"If a leak persists for months, the wall may become damp and damaged.","zh":"如果漏水持續數月，牆身可能變潮濕並受損。"},{"en":"When bad weather persists for months, people may face transport and food problems.","zh":"當壞天氣持續數月，人們可能面對交通和食物問題。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that a condition lasts much longer than expected.","zh":"這個片語強調某狀況比預期持續更久。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"author of Frankenstein","meaning":"《科學怪人》的作者","examples":[{"en":"Mary Shelley was the author of Frankenstein.","zh":"Mary Shelley 是《科學怪人》的作者。"},{"en":"The author of Frankenstein is the writer who created the novel Frankenstein.","zh":"The author of Frankenstein 指創作小說《科學怪人》的作家。"},{"en":"A teacher may introduce Mary Shelley as the author of Frankenstein before discussing Gothic literature.","zh":"老師討論哥德文學前，可能介紹 Mary Shelley 是《科學怪人》的作者。"},{"en":"If students know the author, they can connect the book to the writer’s life and period.","zh":"如果學生知道作者，他們可以把作品與作家的生平和時代連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies Mary Shelley by her most famous work.","zh":"這個片語以 Mary Shelley 最著名的作品識別她。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"while holidaying in","meaning":"在……旅行期間","examples":[{"en":"Mary Shelley complained of rainfall while holidaying in Switzerland.","zh":"Mary Shelley 在瑞士旅行期間抱怨降雨。"},{"en":"While holidaying in a place means during the time someone is travelling there for leisure.","zh":"While holidaying in a place 指某人在該地休閒旅行期間。"},{"en":"A family may take photos while holidaying in Japan during winter.","zh":"一個家庭可能在日本冬季旅行期間拍照。"},{"en":"If bad weather arrives while people are holidaying, outdoor plans may be cancelled.","zh":"如果人們旅行期間遇上惡劣天氣，戶外計劃可能取消。"},{"en":"This phrase places an action during a trip or vacation.","zh":"這個片語把某行動放在旅遊期間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"complain of","meaning":"抱怨；訴說有……","examples":[{"en":"Mary Shelley complained of incessant rainfall.","zh":"Mary Shelley 抱怨連綿不斷的降雨。"},{"en":"To complain of something means to say that something unpleasant is happening or troubling you.","zh":"To complain of something 指說出某件不愉快的事正在發生或困擾自己。"},{"en":"A patient may complain of a headache after a long day at work.","zh":"病人工作一整天後可能訴說有頭痛。"},{"en":"If travellers complain of heavy rain, they may have spent too much time indoors.","zh":"如果旅客抱怨大雨，他們可能花太多時間留在室內。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for discomfort, illness, or unpleasant conditions.","zh":"這個片語常用於不適、疾病或不愉快狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"incessant rainfall","meaning":"連綿不斷的降雨","examples":[{"en":"Incessant rainfall may have influenced Mary Shelley’s mood.","zh":"連綿不斷的降雨可能影響了 Mary Shelley 的心情。"},{"en":"Incessant rainfall means rain that continues for a long time without stopping.","zh":"Incessant rainfall 指長時間不停的降雨。"},{"en":"Incessant rainfall can make a school sports day impossible to hold outdoors.","zh":"連綿不斷的降雨可以令學校運動會無法在戶外舉行。"},{"en":"If rain continues day after day, people may feel trapped and gloomy.","zh":"如果雨一天接一天地下，人們可能感到受困和陰鬱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rain that feels endless.","zh":"這個片語描述令人感到沒完沒了的雨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"put someone in the mood for","meaning":"令某人有心情去……","examples":[{"en":"The dark weather may have put Shelley in the mood for writing.","zh":"陰暗天氣可能令 Shelley 有心情寫作。"},{"en":"To put someone in the mood for something means to make them feel ready or willing to do it.","zh":"To put someone in the mood for something 指令某人感到準備好或願意做某事。"},{"en":"Soft music may put students in the mood for reading quietly.","zh":"柔和音樂可能令學生有心情安靜閱讀。"},{"en":"If gloomy weather affects emotions, it may put a writer in the mood for dark stories.","zh":"如果陰鬱天氣影響情緒，它可能令作家有心情寫黑暗故事。"},{"en":"This phrase links atmosphere with a person’s feeling or action.","zh":"這個片語把氣氛與人的感覺或行動連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"her most famous work","meaning":"她最著名的作品","examples":[{"en":"The weather may have influenced the writing of her most famous work.","zh":"天氣可能影響了她最著名作品的寫作。"},{"en":"Her most famous work means the book, artwork, or creation she is best known for.","zh":"Her most famous work 指她最為人熟知的書、藝術品或創作。"},{"en":"A museum may display an artist’s most famous work near the entrance.","zh":"博物館可能在入口附近展示藝術家最著名的作品。"},{"en":"If an experience shapes a writer’s most famous work, readers may study that background.","zh":"如果某經歷塑造了作家最著名的作品，讀者可能研究該背景。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the creation most strongly connected with a person.","zh":"這個片語指出與某人最密切相關的創作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"far more significant effects","meaning":"更加重大的影響","examples":[{"en":"There were far more significant effects of the year without a summer.","zh":"無夏之年有更加重大的影響。"},{"en":"Far more significant effects are much more important results or consequences.","zh":"Far more significant effects 是重要得多的結果或後果。"},{"en":"A school closure may cause far more significant effects than a cancelled picnic.","zh":"停課可能比取消野餐造成更加重大的影響。"},{"en":"If bad weather destroys crops, its effects are more serious than inconvenience alone.","zh":"如果惡劣天氣破壞農作物，其影響就比不方便更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase compares small effects with much more important ones.","zh":"這個片語把小影響與更重要的影響作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"become known as","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"The unusual year became known as the year without a summer.","zh":"這個不尋常年份被稱為無夏之年。"},{"en":"To become known as something means to receive that name because people commonly use it.","zh":"To become known as something 指因人們普遍使用某名稱而得到該稱呼。"},{"en":"A difficult exam may become known as “the nightmare paper” among students.","zh":"一份困難試卷可能在學生之間被稱為「噩夢卷」。"},{"en":"If an event is unusual enough, it may become known by a special name.","zh":"如果事件足夠不尋常，它可能被稱為一個特別名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how a name or label becomes widely accepted.","zh":"這個片語解釋名稱或標籤如何變得廣泛接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"where did the summer go?","meaning":"夏天去了哪裏？","examples":[{"en":"People wondered where the summer had gone.","zh":"人們想知道夏天去了哪裏。"},{"en":"Where did the summer go? is a question people ask when summer weather seems to disappear.","zh":"Where did the summer go? 是當夏天天氣似乎消失時，人們會問的問題。"},{"en":"If June is cold and rainy every day, people may ask where the summer went.","zh":"如果六月每天又冷又雨，人們可能會問夏天去了哪裏。"},{"en":"When expected warmth does not arrive, people feel confused and disappointed.","zh":"當預期中的溫暖沒有到來，人們會感到困惑和失望。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses surprise that normal summer conditions are missing.","zh":"這個片語表達對正常夏季情況消失的驚訝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the main culprit","meaning":"主要元兇；主因","examples":[{"en":"The main culprit was a volcano in Indonesia.","zh":"主要元兇是印尼的一座火山。"},{"en":"The main culprit is the main cause of a problem or harmful event.","zh":"Main culprit 是某問題或有害事件的主要原因。"},{"en":"If students are always sleepy, the main culprit may be late-night phone use.","zh":"如果學生總是很睏，主要元兇可能是深夜使用手機。"},{"en":"Finding the main culprit helps people solve the real problem, not just the symptoms.","zh":"找出主要元兇有助人們解決真正問題，而不只是表面症狀。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what is mainly responsible.","zh":"這個片語指出主要責任所在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"surprisingly","meaning":"令人意外地","examples":[{"en":"Surprisingly, the main cause was a volcano far away.","zh":"令人意外地，主因是一座遙遠的火山。"},{"en":"Surprisingly means in a way that is unexpected or causes surprise.","zh":"Surprisingly 指以出乎意料或令人驚訝的方式。"},{"en":"Surprisingly, the quiet student gave the strongest speech in class.","zh":"令人意外地，那位安靜的學生在班上作了最有力的演講。"},{"en":"If the cause is far away, it may surprisingly still affect local life.","zh":"如果原因在遙遠地方，它仍可能令人意外地影響本地生活。"},{"en":"This word prepares the reader for information that is not expected.","zh":"這個詞讓讀者準備接收意想不到的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on the other side of the planet","meaning":"在地球另一邊","examples":[{"en":"The volcano was on the other side of the planet.","zh":"那座火山在地球另一邊。"},{"en":"On the other side of the planet means very far away in another part of the world.","zh":"On the other side of the planet 指在世界另一部分，非常遙遠。"},{"en":"A storm on the other side of the planet can still affect flight schedules.","zh":"地球另一邊的風暴仍可以影響航班時間表。"},{"en":"If an event is large enough, its effects may travel far beyond its location.","zh":"如果事件足夠巨大，其影響可能遠遠超出發生地點。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses great geographical distance.","zh":"這個片語強調巨大的地理距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Mount Tambora","meaning":"坦博拉火山","examples":[{"en":"Mount Tambora erupted with colossal force in 1815.","zh":"坦博拉火山在1815年以巨大力量爆發。"},{"en":"Mount Tambora is the Indonesian volcano linked to the year without a summer.","zh":"Mount Tambora 是與無夏之年相關的印尼火山。"},{"en":"A geography teacher may use Mount Tambora to explain how volcanoes can change climate.","zh":"地理老師可能用坦博拉火山來解釋火山如何改變氣候。"},{"en":"When Mount Tambora erupted, ash entered the atmosphere and helped cool the planet.","zh":"當坦博拉火山爆發，火山灰進入大氣層，並幫助令地球降溫。"},{"en":"This name refers to the volcano at the centre of the 1816 climate disaster.","zh":"這個名稱指1816年氣候災難核心的火山。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"whose eruption","meaning":"其爆發","examples":[{"en":"Mount Tambora was the volcano whose eruption altered global climate.","zh":"坦博拉火山就是其爆發改變全球氣候的火山。"},{"en":"Whose eruption connects a volcano with the eruption that belonged to it.","zh":"Whose eruption 把某座火山與屬於它的爆發連接起來。"},{"en":"The factory whose fire damaged the street had ignored safety warnings.","zh":"那間其火災破壞街道的工廠曾忽視安全警告。"},{"en":"If a volcano’s eruption sends ash worldwide, that eruption can affect distant countries.","zh":"如果火山爆發把火山灰送往全球，其爆發可以影響遙遠國家。"},{"en":"This phrase helps join a thing with the event it caused.","zh":"這個片語幫助把事物與它造成的事件連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the previous year","meaning":"前一年","examples":[{"en":"The eruption had happened the previous year.","zh":"爆發發生在前一年。"},{"en":"The previous year means the year before the time being discussed.","zh":"The previous year 指所討論時間之前的一年。"},{"en":"If a student improved this year, the previous year may show how much progress was made.","zh":"如果學生今年進步，前一年的表現可以顯示進步幅度。"},{"en":"An event in the previous year can still create effects later.","zh":"前一年發生的事件仍可能在之後造成影響。"},{"en":"This phrase helps place events in time.","zh":"這個片語幫助安排事件時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"of such colossal magnitude that","meaning":"規模巨大到……","examples":[{"en":"The eruption was of such colossal magnitude that it altered global climate.","zh":"爆發規模巨大到改變了全球氣候。"},{"en":"Of such colossal magnitude that means so huge in scale that it caused a major result.","zh":"Of such colossal magnitude that 指規模如此巨大，以致造成重大結果。"},{"en":"The storm was of such magnitude that schools closed across the city.","zh":"風暴規模巨大到全城學校停課。"},{"en":"If a disaster is that large, its effects may spread far beyond the original area.","zh":"如果災難如此巨大，其影響可能遠遠超出原發地區。"},{"en":"This structure links extreme size with serious consequence.","zh":"這個結構把極大規模與嚴重後果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"alter global climate","meaning":"改變全球氣候","examples":[{"en":"The eruption altered global climate.","zh":"火山爆發改變了全球氣候。"},{"en":"To alter global climate means to change weather patterns and temperatures around the world.","zh":"To alter global climate 指改變世界各地的天氣模式和氣溫。"},{"en":"Large volcanic eruptions can alter climate by sending dust high into the atmosphere.","zh":"大型火山爆發可以透過把塵埃送入高層大氣來改變氣候。"},{"en":"If global climate changes suddenly, farmers may not know when to plant crops.","zh":"如果全球氣候突然改變，農民可能不知道何時種植作物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a worldwide environmental change.","zh":"這個片語描述全球性的環境變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the years leading to","meaning":"在……之前的數年間","examples":[{"en":"In the years leading to the major eruption, the mountain had experienced minor eruptions.","zh":"在重大爆發之前的數年間，該山曾經歷小型火山爆發。"},{"en":"In the years leading to an event means during the years before it happened.","zh":"In the years leading to an event 指某事件發生前的數年間。"},{"en":"In the years leading to graduation, students slowly build skills and confidence.","zh":"在畢業之前的數年間，學生逐步建立技能和信心。"},{"en":"If warning signs appear in the years leading to a disaster, experts may study them later.","zh":"如果災難前數年間出現警號，專家之後可能研究它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the period before a major event.","zh":"這個片語描述重大事件之前的一段時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"experience minor eruptions","meaning":"經歷小型火山爆發","examples":[{"en":"The mountain had experienced minor eruptions before the major event.","zh":"該山在重大事件前曾經歷小型火山爆發。"},{"en":"To experience minor eruptions means to have smaller volcanic outbursts before a larger one.","zh":"To experience minor eruptions 指在較大爆發前出現較小型的火山噴發。"},{"en":"A volcano may experience minor eruptions that warn scientists of growing pressure below.","zh":"火山可能經歷小型爆發，警告科學家地下壓力正在增加。"},{"en":"If minor eruptions increase, nearby residents may prepare for evacuation.","zh":"如果小型爆發增加，附近居民可能準備疏散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes smaller volcanic activity before or between major eruptions.","zh":"這個片語描述重大爆發之前或之間的較小火山活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the culmination","meaning":"頂點；最終結果","examples":[{"en":"The 1815 event was the culmination of earlier volcanic activity.","zh":"1815年的事件是早前火山活動的頂點。"},{"en":"The culmination is the final and most important result of a series of events.","zh":"Culmination 是一連串事件的最終和最重要結果。"},{"en":"A final performance can be the culmination of months of music practice.","zh":"最終演出可以是數月音樂練習的最終成果。"},{"en":"If small warnings build over time, a major crisis may become their culmination.","zh":"如果小警號隨時間累積，重大危機可能成為它們的最終結果。"},{"en":"This word describes the peak or final outcome of a process.","zh":"這個詞描述過程的高峰或最終結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"explosive outburst","meaning":"爆炸式噴發","examples":[{"en":"The eruption involved a huge explosive outburst.","zh":"火山爆發涉及一次巨大的爆炸式噴發。"},{"en":"An explosive outburst is a sudden violent release of energy, gas, ash, or material.","zh":"Explosive outburst 是能量、氣體、火山灰或物質突然猛烈釋放。"},{"en":"A burst pipe can cause an outburst of water, but a volcanic outburst is far more dangerous.","zh":"水管爆裂可以造成水突然噴出，但火山爆炸式噴發危險得多。"},{"en":"If pressure builds underground, an explosive outburst can throw material high into the air.","zh":"如果地下壓力累積，爆炸式噴發可以把物質拋上高空。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a violent and sudden release.","zh":"這個片語描述猛烈而突然的釋放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"central volcanic vent","meaning":"中央火山噴口","examples":[{"en":"The explosive outburst came from the central volcanic vent.","zh":"爆炸式噴發來自中央火山噴口。"},{"en":"A central volcanic vent is the main opening where volcanic material escapes.","zh":"Central volcanic vent 是火山物質噴出的主要開口。"},{"en":"Scientists may monitor a volcanic vent for gas, heat, and ash.","zh":"科學家可能監測火山噴口的氣體、熱力和火山灰。"},{"en":"If pressure rises below the vent, an eruption may become more likely.","zh":"如果噴口下方壓力上升，火山爆發可能更有可能。"},{"en":"This phrase names the main channel of a volcano.","zh":"這個片語命名火山的主要通道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"subsequent caldera collapse","meaning":"隨後的火山臼塌陷","examples":[{"en":"The eruption was followed by subsequent caldera collapse.","zh":"火山爆發後出現隨後的火山臼塌陷。"},{"en":"Subsequent caldera collapse means the volcano’s crater area collapsed after the eruption.","zh":"Subsequent caldera collapse 指火山爆發後，火山口區域塌陷。"},{"en":"After a large eruption, the ground above the empty magma chamber may collapse.","zh":"大型爆發後，空岩漿房上方地面可能塌陷。"},{"en":"If a caldera collapses, the landscape around the volcano can change dramatically.","zh":"如果火山臼塌陷，火山周邊地貌可以劇烈改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what happened after the explosive stage.","zh":"這個片語描述爆炸階段之後發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the vicinity","meaning":"在附近地區","examples":[{"en":"Over 70,000 people in the vicinity were killed.","zh":"附近地區超過70,000人死亡。"},{"en":"In the vicinity means in the nearby area.","zh":"In the vicinity 指在附近範圍內。"},{"en":"People in the vicinity of a fire may be told to close windows.","zh":"火災附近地區的人可能被要求關上窗戶。"},{"en":"If a volcano erupts, those in the vicinity face the greatest immediate danger.","zh":"如果火山爆發，附近地區的人面對最大即時危險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people or places close to an event.","zh":"這個片語指接近某事件的人或地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lava flows","meaning":"熔岩流","examples":[{"en":"Lava flows killed many people near the volcano.","zh":"熔岩流殺死了火山附近許多人。"},{"en":"Lava flows are streams of hot molten rock moving from a volcano.","zh":"Lava flows 是從火山流出的高溫熔融岩石流。"},{"en":"Residents may evacuate if lava flows move toward their village.","zh":"如果熔岩流流向村莊，居民可能疏散。"},{"en":"If lava flows cover roads, rescue teams may not reach the area easily.","zh":"如果熔岩流覆蓋道路，救援隊可能難以到達該區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one direct danger of volcanic eruptions.","zh":"這個片語描述火山爆發的一種直接危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tsunamis","meaning":"海嘯","examples":[{"en":"Tsunamis were among the deadly effects of the eruption.","zh":"海嘯是火山爆發的致命影響之一。"},{"en":"Tsunamis are large sea waves often caused by earthquakes, eruptions, or underwater landslides.","zh":"Tsunamis 是通常由地震、火山爆發或海底山泥傾瀉造成的大海浪。"},{"en":"Coastal schools may practise evacuation drills because tsunamis can arrive quickly.","zh":"沿岸學校可能進行疏散演習，因為海嘯可以很快到達。"},{"en":"If a tsunami reaches the shore, it can flood towns and destroy buildings.","zh":"如果海嘯到達岸邊，它可以淹浸城鎮並摧毀建築物。"},{"en":"This word describes dangerous waves that can affect coastal communities.","zh":"這個詞描述會影響沿岸社區的危險海浪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pumice and ash falls","meaning":"浮石和火山灰降落","examples":[{"en":"People were killed by pumice and ash falls.","zh":"人們被浮石和火山灰降落殺死。"},{"en":"Pumice and ash falls are falling pieces of volcanic rock and fine volcanic dust.","zh":"Pumice and ash falls 是火山岩碎片和細火山灰從空中落下。"},{"en":"After an eruption, pumice and ash falls can cover roofs, roads, and farms.","zh":"火山爆發後，浮石和火山灰可以覆蓋屋頂、道路和農田。"},{"en":"If ash becomes too heavy on rooftops, buildings may collapse.","zh":"如果屋頂上的火山灰太重，建築物可能倒塌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dangerous material falling from an eruption cloud.","zh":"這個片語描述從火山爆發雲中落下的危險物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"more significantly","meaning":"更重要的是","examples":[{"en":"More significantly, the eruption sent dust into the stratosphere.","zh":"更重要的是，火山爆發把塵埃送入平流層。"},{"en":"More significantly means more importantly than what has just been mentioned.","zh":"More significantly 指比剛提到的事情更重要。"},{"en":"The rain cancelled the picnic; more significantly, it flooded several homes.","zh":"雨取消了野餐；更重要的是，它淹浸了幾間房屋。"},{"en":"If a detail is more significant, it has a bigger effect on the main issue.","zh":"如果某細節更重要，它對主要問題有更大影響。"},{"en":"This phrase moves attention to the more important consequence.","zh":"這個片語把注意力轉向更重要的後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be acknowledged as","meaning":"被承認為","examples":[{"en":"The eruption is now acknowledged as the largest in recorded history.","zh":"這次爆發現在被承認為有紀錄以來最大。"},{"en":"To be acknowledged as something means to be accepted or recognised as that thing.","zh":"To be acknowledged as something 指被接受或認可為某種身份或事物。"},{"en":"A teacher may be acknowledged as an expert after years of successful teaching.","zh":"一位老師經多年成功教學後，可能被承認為專家。"},{"en":"If evidence is strong, an event may be acknowledged as historically important.","zh":"如果證據強，一件事件可能被承認為具有歷史重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase shows public or expert recognition.","zh":"這個片語顯示公眾或專家的認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the largest in recorded history","meaning":"有紀錄以來最大","examples":[{"en":"The Tambora eruption is regarded as the largest in recorded history.","zh":"坦博拉火山爆發被視為有紀錄以來最大。"},{"en":"The largest in recorded history means the biggest event of its kind found in written records.","zh":"The largest in recorded history 指書面記錄中同類事件最大的一次。"},{"en":"A flood may be called the largest in recorded history if no earlier written record shows a bigger one.","zh":"如果沒有較早文字記錄顯示更大的洪水，一場洪水可被稱為有紀錄以來最大。"},{"en":"If something is the largest recorded, its effects are likely to be severe.","zh":"如果某事是有紀錄以來最大，其影響很可能嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase compares an event with all documented examples before it.","zh":"這個片語把某事件與所有有文獻記載的例子作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"eject huge amounts of","meaning":"噴出大量……","examples":[{"en":"The eruption ejected huge amounts of dust into the atmosphere.","zh":"火山爆發把大量塵埃噴入大氣層。"},{"en":"To eject huge amounts of something means to force out a very large quantity.","zh":"To eject huge amounts of something 指強力排出非常大量某物。"},{"en":"A broken pipe can eject huge amounts of water into a basement.","zh":"爆裂水管可以把大量水噴入地下室。"},{"en":"If a volcano ejects huge amounts of ash, sunlight may be blocked.","zh":"如果火山噴出大量火山灰，陽光可能被阻擋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a powerful release of material.","zh":"這個片語描述物質被強力釋放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"volcanic dust","meaning":"火山塵","examples":[{"en":"Volcanic dust can remain in the atmosphere for years.","zh":"火山塵可以在大氣中停留多年。"},{"en":"Volcanic dust is fine material thrown into the air by a volcanic eruption.","zh":"Volcanic dust 是火山爆發拋入空中的細小物質。"},{"en":"Volcanic dust can settle on cars, roofs, and farms after an eruption.","zh":"火山爆發後，火山塵可以落在汽車、屋頂和農場上。"},{"en":"If volcanic dust reaches high air layers, it may affect sunlight and temperature.","zh":"如果火山塵到達高層大氣，它可能影響陽光和氣溫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes tiny eruption material carried by air.","zh":"這個片語描述由空氣攜帶的細小火山爆發物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the stratosphere","meaning":"平流層","examples":[{"en":"The eruption sent huge amounts of dust into the stratosphere.","zh":"火山爆發把大量塵埃送入平流層。"},{"en":"The stratosphere is a high layer of Earth’s atmosphere above the lower weather layer.","zh":"Stratosphere 是地球大氣中位於較低天氣層之上的高層。"},{"en":"Scientists study the stratosphere because particles there can spread widely and remain long.","zh":"科學家研究平流層，因為那裏的粒子可以廣泛散播並長時間停留。"},{"en":"If volcanic dust reaches the stratosphere, rain does not remove it quickly.","zh":"如果火山塵到達平流層，雨水不會很快把它清除。"},{"en":"This word names an atmospheric layer important in climate effects.","zh":"這個詞命名一個在氣候影響中重要的大氣層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"atmospheric layer","meaning":"大氣層","examples":[{"en":"The stratosphere is an atmospheric layer that can hold volcanic dust for a long time.","zh":"平流層是一個可以長時間保存火山塵的大氣層。"},{"en":"An atmospheric layer is one level or region of gases surrounding Earth.","zh":"Atmospheric layer 是包圍地球的氣體中的某一層或區域。"},{"en":"Weather forecasts mainly concern the lower atmospheric layer where clouds form.","zh":"天氣預報主要涉及雲形成的較低大氣層。"},{"en":"If dust enters a high atmospheric layer, it may travel far before falling out.","zh":"如果塵埃進入高層大氣，它可能在落下前傳到很遠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a level within the air around the planet.","zh":"這個片語描述地球周圍空氣中的一個層次。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be least affected by","meaning":"最少受……影響","examples":[{"en":"The stratosphere is least affected by rainfall.","zh":"平流層最少受降雨影響。"},{"en":"To be least affected by something means to be influenced by it less than other things are.","zh":"To be least affected by something 指比其他事物更少受某事影響。"},{"en":"A sheltered playground may be least affected by strong wind compared with open areas.","zh":"與空曠地方相比，有遮擋的操場可能最少受強風影響。"},{"en":"If an air layer is least affected by rain, dust there stays longer.","zh":"如果某大氣層最少受雨影響，那裏的塵埃會停留更久。"},{"en":"This phrase compares levels of influence or damage.","zh":"這個片語比較影響或損害程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take a relatively long time","meaning":"需要相對較長時間","examples":[{"en":"It takes a relatively long time for volcanic dust to be washed out.","zh":"火山塵需要相對較長時間才被沖刷掉。"},{"en":"To take a relatively long time means to need more time than expected or than similar processes.","zh":"To take a relatively long time 指比預期或類似過程需要更多時間。"},{"en":"Learning pronunciation may take a relatively long time because habits change slowly.","zh":"學習發音可能需要相對較長時間，因為習慣改變得慢。"},{"en":"If dust stays high in the air, it can take a long time to disappear.","zh":"如果塵埃停留在高空，它可能需要很久才消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a slow process.","zh":"這個片語描述緩慢過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be washed out","meaning":"被沖刷掉","examples":[{"en":"Volcanic dust may take years to be washed out of the atmosphere.","zh":"火山塵可能需要多年才從大氣中被沖刷掉。"},{"en":"To be washed out means to be removed by rain, water, or natural washing.","zh":"To be washed out 指被雨水、水流或自然沖洗移除。"},{"en":"Mud on the pavement may be washed out after several days of heavy rain.","zh":"行人路上的泥可能在幾天大雨後被沖刷掉。"},{"en":"If dust is too high for rain to reach easily, it will not be washed out quickly.","zh":"如果塵埃太高，雨水不易到達，它就不會很快被沖刷掉。"},{"en":"This phrase describes removal through water or rainfall.","zh":"這個片語描述透過水或雨水移除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dust particles","meaning":"塵埃粒子","examples":[{"en":"Fine dust particles can travel around the globe.","zh":"細小塵埃粒子可以環繞全球移動。"},{"en":"Dust particles are tiny pieces of solid material floating or moving in the air.","zh":"Dust particles 是在空氣中漂浮或移動的細小固體物質。"},{"en":"Dust particles in a classroom can make some students sneeze.","zh":"課室中的塵埃粒子可以令一些學生打噴嚏。"},{"en":"If particles are very small, wind can carry them a long distance.","zh":"如果粒子非常細小，風可以把它們帶到很遠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes tiny bits of matter suspended in air.","zh":"這個片語描述懸浮於空氣中的細小物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fine enough","meaning":"足夠細小","examples":[{"en":"If dust particles are fine enough, they can be blown around the globe.","zh":"如果塵埃粒子足夠細小，它們可以被吹到全球各地。"},{"en":"Fine enough means small or light enough for a particular result to happen.","zh":"Fine enough 指細小或輕到足以造成某結果。"},{"en":"Flour is fine enough to float in the air if a bag is dropped suddenly.","zh":"如果麵粉袋突然掉落，麵粉細到可以飄在空氣中。"},{"en":"If ash is fine enough, wind can carry it far from the volcano.","zh":"如果火山灰足夠細小，風可以把它帶離火山很遠。"},{"en":"This phrase links small size with what becomes possible.","zh":"這個片語把細小程度與可能發生的事連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be blown around the globe","meaning":"被吹到全球各地","examples":[{"en":"Fine volcanic particles can be blown around the globe.","zh":"細小火山粒子可以被吹到全球各地。"},{"en":"To be blown around the globe means to be carried by winds across the world.","zh":"To be blown around the globe 指被風帶到世界各地。"},{"en":"Smoke from a large fire can be blown far from its original area.","zh":"大火產生的煙可以被吹離原地很遠。"},{"en":"If volcanic particles are blown globally, distant countries may see unusual skies.","zh":"如果火山粒子被吹到全球各地，遙遠國家可能看見不尋常天空。"},{"en":"This phrase describes worldwide movement by wind.","zh":"這個片語描述由風造成的全球移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"remain there for years","meaning":"在那裏停留多年","examples":[{"en":"Volcanic dust can remain in the atmosphere for years.","zh":"火山塵可以在大氣中停留多年。"},{"en":"To remain there for years means to stay in that place for a very long time.","zh":"To remain there for years 指在該處停留很長時間。"},{"en":"A stain on a wall may remain there for years if nobody repairs it.","zh":"如果沒有人修理，牆上的污漬可能在那裏停留多年。"},{"en":"If dust remains in the atmosphere for years, it can affect climate for more than one season.","zh":"如果塵埃在大氣中停留多年，它可以影響不止一季的氣候。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long-term presence.","zh":"這個片語強調長期存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"on a somewhat benign note","meaning":"從較正面的角度來說","examples":[{"en":"On a somewhat benign note, the ash produced beautiful sunsets.","zh":"從較正面的角度來說，火山灰產生了美麗日落。"},{"en":"On a somewhat benign note means looking at a less harmful or more positive side.","zh":"On a somewhat benign note 指從較少傷害或較正面的角度來看。"},{"en":"After a difficult exam, on a benign note, students learned which topics need more practice.","zh":"一場困難考試後，從較正面角度來說，學生知道哪些題目需要更多練習。"},{"en":"If a disaster has one beautiful side effect, it may still not reduce the seriousness of the damage.","zh":"如果災難有一個美麗副作用，仍不會減低損害的嚴重性。"},{"en":"This phrase gently shifts from harm to a milder or positive point.","zh":"這個片語溫和地由傷害轉向較輕微或正面的重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"airborne ash","meaning":"空氣中的火山灰","examples":[{"en":"Airborne ash resulted in beautiful sunsets.","zh":"空氣中的火山灰造成美麗日落。"},{"en":"Airborne ash is volcanic ash floating or travelling through the air.","zh":"Airborne ash 是漂浮或在空氣中移動的火山灰。"},{"en":"Airborne ash can make people wear masks and keep windows closed.","zh":"空氣中的火山灰可以令人戴口罩並關窗。"},{"en":"If ash remains airborne, it can affect sunlight, air quality, and visibility.","zh":"如果火山灰停留在空氣中，它可以影響陽光、空氣質素和能見度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ash carried in the atmosphere.","zh":"這個片語描述由大氣攜帶的火山灰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"result in","meaning":"導致；造成","examples":[{"en":"The ash resulted in pastel-coloured sunsets.","zh":"火山灰導致粉彩色日落。"},{"en":"To result in something means to cause it to happen.","zh":"To result in something 指造成某事發生。"},{"en":"A broken traffic light can result in long queues at a junction.","zh":"交通燈故障可以導致路口出現長長車龍。"},{"en":"If heavy rain continues, it may result in flooding and travel delays.","zh":"如果大雨持續，它可能導致水浸和交通延誤。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with its consequence.","zh":"這個片語把原因與後果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pastel-coloured sunsets","meaning":"粉彩色的日落","examples":[{"en":"Airborne ash produced pastel-coloured sunsets.","zh":"空氣中的火山灰產生粉彩色的日落。"},{"en":"Pastel-coloured sunsets are sunsets with soft pale colours, such as pink, orange, or purple.","zh":"Pastel-coloured sunsets 是帶有柔和淡色，例如粉紅、橙色或紫色的日落。"},{"en":"People may stop to photograph pastel-coloured sunsets after a dusty day.","zh":"在多塵的一天後，人們可能停下來拍攝粉彩色日落。"},{"en":"If particles scatter sunlight, the sky can show unusual soft colours.","zh":"如果粒子散射陽光，天空可以出現不尋常的柔和顏色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gentle visual effect in the evening sky.","zh":"這個片語描述傍晚天空中的柔和視覺效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"extended twilights","meaning":"延長的黃昏餘暉","examples":[{"en":"The ash also produced extended twilights in Northern Europe.","zh":"火山灰也在北歐產生延長的黃昏餘暉。"},{"en":"Extended twilights are longer periods of soft light after sunset.","zh":"Extended twilights 是日落後柔和光線維持更久的時段。"},{"en":"Photographers may enjoy extended twilights because the sky stays colourful for longer.","zh":"攝影師可能喜歡延長的黃昏餘暉，因為天空顏色停留更久。"},{"en":"If particles remain in the air, evening light may linger unusually long.","zh":"如果粒子停留在空氣中，傍晚光線可能異常地久久不散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes twilight that lasts longer than normal.","zh":"這個片語描述比平常更長的黃昏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Northern Europe","meaning":"北歐","examples":[{"en":"Northern Europe experienced unusual sunsets and twilights.","zh":"北歐經歷了不尋常的日落和黃昏餘暉。"},{"en":"Northern Europe refers to the northern part of the European continent and nearby islands.","zh":"Northern Europe 指歐洲大陸北部及附近島嶼。"},{"en":"Travellers visiting Northern Europe may expect cool weather and long summer evenings.","zh":"到北歐旅行的人可能預期涼冷天氣和漫長夏夜。"},{"en":"If atmospheric dust spreads northward, Northern Europe may see unusual skies.","zh":"如果大氣塵埃向北擴散，北歐可能看見不尋常天空。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a broad region in Europe.","zh":"這個片語指出歐洲的一個廣泛地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"on a darker note","meaning":"從較負面的角度來說","examples":[{"en":"On a darker note, the ash helped create a volcanic winter.","zh":"從較負面的角度來說，火山灰幫助造成火山寒冬。"},{"en":"On a darker note means moving to a more serious, negative, or worrying point.","zh":"On a darker note 指轉向更嚴重、負面或令人擔憂的重點。"},{"en":"The festival was popular; on a darker note, several visitors became ill from spoiled food.","zh":"節日很受歡迎；從較負面的角度來說，幾名遊客因變壞食物而生病。"},{"en":"If a pleasant effect hides a serious danger, the writer may use this phrase to shift tone.","zh":"如果愉快效果掩蓋嚴重危險，作者可能用這個片語轉換語氣。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a more troubling side of the same topic.","zh":"這個片語引出同一題目的較令人不安一面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"quite literally","meaning":"頗為字面意義上地","examples":[{"en":"The darker effect was quite literally related to reduced sunlight.","zh":"這個較黑暗的影響頗為字面意義上與陽光減少有關。"},{"en":"Quite literally means actually and directly, not just as a figure of speech.","zh":"Quite literally 指實際而直接地，不只是比喻。"},{"en":"The classroom was quite literally freezing because the heater had broken.","zh":"課室真的冷得像結冰，因為暖氣壞了。"},{"en":"If ash blocks sunlight, the world becomes darker quite literally.","zh":"如果火山灰阻擋陽光，世界就頗為字面意義上變暗。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that a statement is physically true.","zh":"這個片語強調某說法在物理上是真的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"set into motion","meaning":"觸發；啟動","examples":[{"en":"The ash set into motion a volcanic winter.","zh":"火山灰觸發了火山寒冬。"},{"en":"To set something into motion means to start a process or chain of events.","zh":"To set something into motion 指開始一個過程或一連串事件。"},{"en":"One complaint can set into motion a full safety investigation at work.","zh":"一宗投訴可以啟動工作場所的完整安全調查。"},{"en":"If volcanic ash blocks sunlight, it can set climate changes into motion.","zh":"如果火山灰阻擋陽光，它可以觸發氣候變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes starting events that then continue to develop.","zh":"這個片語描述啟動之後繼續發展的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a volcanic winter","meaning":"火山冬天；火山寒冬","examples":[{"en":"A volcanic winter can occur when ash blocks sunlight.","zh":"當火山灰阻擋陽光時，可能出現火山寒冬。"},{"en":"A volcanic winter is a period of colder global weather caused by volcanic material in the atmosphere.","zh":"Volcanic winter 是由大氣中的火山物質造成的一段全球較寒冷天氣。"},{"en":"Farmers fear a volcanic winter because crops may receive too little warmth and light.","zh":"農民害怕火山寒冬，因為農作物可能得到太少溫暖和光照。"},{"en":"If ash reflects sunlight away from Earth, temperatures can fall.","zh":"如果火山灰把陽光反射離開地球，氣溫可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes climate cooling after a major volcanic eruption.","zh":"這個片語描述重大火山爆發後的氣候降溫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"due to","meaning":"由於","examples":[{"en":"The volcanic winter occurred due to the filtering of the sun’s rays.","zh":"火山寒冬由於太陽光線被過濾而發生。"},{"en":"Due to means because of.","zh":"Due to 指因為。"},{"en":"The lesson was cancelled due to a power failure.","zh":"課堂由於停電而取消。"},{"en":"If flights are delayed due to weather, passengers may miss connections.","zh":"如果航班由於天氣延誤，乘客可能錯過轉機。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the reason for a result.","zh":"這個片語引出結果的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"filtering of the sun’s rays","meaning":"過濾太陽光線","examples":[{"en":"The filtering of the sun’s rays reduced heat reaching Earth.","zh":"太陽光線被過濾，減少了到達地球的熱量。"},{"en":"Filtering of the sun’s rays means blocking or reducing sunlight before it reaches the ground.","zh":"Filtering of the sun’s rays 指太陽光到達地面前被阻擋或減弱。"},{"en":"Thick curtains filter the sun’s rays and make a room cooler.","zh":"厚窗簾會過濾太陽光線，使房間較涼。"},{"en":"If volcanic dust filters sunlight, less warmth reaches crops and people.","zh":"如果火山塵過濾陽光，較少熱力會到達農作物和人類。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how light can be weakened before reaching Earth.","zh":"這個片語解釋光線如何在到達地球前被削弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"increased reflectivity","meaning":"反射率增加","examples":[{"en":"Increased reflectivity caused more heat to be bounced back into space.","zh":"反射率增加令更多熱量被反射回太空。"},{"en":"Increased reflectivity means a surface or layer reflects more light or heat away.","zh":"Increased reflectivity 指表面或層次反射更多光或熱。"},{"en":"A white roof has increased reflectivity compared with a dark roof.","zh":"與深色屋頂相比，白色屋頂反射率較高。"},{"en":"If Earth’s atmosphere becomes more reflective, less solar energy may warm the ground.","zh":"如果地球大氣變得更能反射，較少太陽能可能加熱地面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a greater ability to send light or heat back.","zh":"這個片語描述把光或熱反射回去的能力增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be bounced back into space","meaning":"被反射回太空","examples":[{"en":"Heat and sunlight were bounced back into space.","zh":"熱量和陽光被反射回太空。"},{"en":"To be bounced back into space means to be reflected away from Earth and sent outward.","zh":"To be bounced back into space 指從地球反射出去並射向外太空。"},{"en":"A shiny car window can bounce sunlight back toward people’s eyes.","zh":"閃亮的車窗可以把陽光反射回人的眼睛。"},{"en":"If more sunlight is bounced back into space, Earth receives less warmth.","zh":"如果更多陽光被反射回太空，地球得到的熱量就較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reflection away from the planet.","zh":"這個片語描述光或熱被反射離開地球。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"what is intriguing","meaning":"令人感興趣的是","examples":[{"en":"What is intriguing is that the period was already unusually cold.","zh":"令人感興趣的是，該時期本來已異常寒冷。"},{"en":"What is intriguing means what is interesting, surprising, or worth thinking about.","zh":"What is intriguing 指令人感興趣、驚訝或值得思考的地方。"},{"en":"What is intriguing about the class results is that quiet students improved the most.","zh":"班級成績令人感興趣的是，安靜的學生進步最大。"},{"en":"If a detail seems unexpected, it may be intriguing because it changes the explanation.","zh":"如果某細節出乎意料，它可能令人感興趣，因為它改變了解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a point that invites curiosity.","zh":"這個片語引出令人好奇的重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"even without","meaning":"即使沒有……","examples":[{"en":"Even without the Tambora explosion, the period was already cold.","zh":"即使沒有坦博拉火山爆發，該時期本來已寒冷。"},{"en":"Even without something means that the situation would still be true if that thing were absent.","zh":"Even without something 指即使缺少某因素，情況仍然成立。"},{"en":"Even without extra homework, students may feel tired after a full day of lessons.","zh":"即使沒有額外功課，學生上完整天課後仍可能感到疲倦。"},{"en":"If the world was already cool even without Tambora, the eruption made an existing problem worse.","zh":"如果即使沒有坦博拉火山，世界已經較冷，爆發就是加劇已有問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor was not the only cause.","zh":"這個片語顯示某因素不是唯一原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"one of the coldest on record","meaning":"有紀錄以來最寒冷之一","examples":[{"en":"The period from 1790 to 1830 was one of the coldest on record.","zh":"1790年至1830年是有紀錄以來最寒冷的時期之一。"},{"en":"One of the coldest on record means among the coldest periods ever measured or documented.","zh":"One of the coldest on record 指在曾量度或記錄的時期中屬最寒冷之一。"},{"en":"A winter may be one of the coldest on record if temperatures break many old records.","zh":"如果氣溫打破許多舊紀錄，某個冬天可算是有紀錄以來最寒冷之一。"},{"en":"If a period is that cold, farming and health can be seriously affected.","zh":"如果一段時期如此寒冷，農業和健康都可能受嚴重影響。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a period with historical weather records.","zh":"這個片語把某段時期與歷史天氣紀錄作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"officially become known as","meaning":"正式被稱為","examples":[{"en":"This cold period officially became known as the Dalton Minimum.","zh":"這個寒冷時期正式被稱為道爾頓極小期。"},{"en":"To officially become known as something means to receive a recognised formal name.","zh":"To officially become known as something 指得到被認可的正式名稱。"},{"en":"A new school building may officially become known as the Science Centre after a ceremony.","zh":"新校舍在典禮後可能正式被稱為科學中心。"},{"en":"If experts use a name consistently, it can become the official label for a period.","zh":"如果專家一致使用某名稱，它可以成為某時期的正式標籤。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a formal naming, not just a casual nickname.","zh":"這個片語標示正式命名，而不只是隨意綽號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the Dalton Minimum","meaning":"道爾頓極小期","examples":[{"en":"The Dalton Minimum was a period of reduced solar activity.","zh":"道爾頓極小期是一段太陽活動減弱的時期。"},{"en":"The Dalton Minimum refers to a historical period when the sun showed fewer signs of activity.","zh":"Dalton Minimum 指太陽活動跡象較少的一段歷史時期。"},{"en":"Science students may study the Dalton Minimum when learning about climate and the sun.","zh":"科學學生學習氣候和太陽時，可能研究道爾頓極小期。"},{"en":"If solar activity decreases, some scientists ask whether Earth’s temperature may be affected.","zh":"如果太陽活動減少，一些科學家會問地球氣溫是否可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase names a cold historical period linked with lower solar activity.","zh":"這個片語命名一段與較低太陽活動相關的寒冷歷史時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"London-based meteorologist","meaning":"駐倫敦的氣象學家","examples":[{"en":"John Dalton was a London-based meteorologist.","zh":"John Dalton 是駐倫敦的氣象學家。"},{"en":"A London-based meteorologist is a weather scientist who works in London.","zh":"London-based meteorologist 是在倫敦工作的天氣科學家。"},{"en":"A Hong Kong-based teacher is a teacher who works mainly in Hong Kong.","zh":"Hong Kong-based teacher 是主要在香港工作的老師。"},{"en":"If a scientist is based in a city, their observations may be linked to that workplace.","zh":"如果科學家駐某城市，他的觀察可能與該工作地點有關。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both a person’s job and working location.","zh":"這個片語同時指出人的職業和工作地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sunspots","meaning":"太陽黑子","examples":[{"en":"John Dalton noticed fewer sunspots during that period.","zh":"John Dalton 注意到該時期太陽黑子較少。"},{"en":"Sunspots are darker areas on the sun’s surface linked with solar activity.","zh":"Sunspots 是太陽表面較暗、與太陽活動相關的區域。"},{"en":"Scientists observe sunspots to study changes in the sun.","zh":"科學家觀察太陽黑子，以研究太陽變化。"},{"en":"If fewer sunspots appear, researchers may wonder whether solar activity has weakened.","zh":"如果太陽黑子較少出現，研究人員可能懷疑太陽活動是否減弱。"},{"en":"This word names visible dark marks used in studying the sun.","zh":"這個詞命名研究太陽時使用的可見暗斑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"solar flares","meaning":"太陽耀斑","examples":[{"en":"The sun seemed less active in its production of solar flares.","zh":"太陽在產生太陽耀斑方面似乎較不活躍。"},{"en":"Solar flares are sudden bursts of energy from the sun’s surface.","zh":"Solar flares 是太陽表面突然爆發的能量。"},{"en":"A science teacher may explain that solar flares can affect satellites and radio signals.","zh":"科學老師可能解釋太陽耀斑可以影響衛星和無線電訊號。"},{"en":"If solar flares become less frequent, the sun may appear less active.","zh":"如果太陽耀斑變得較少，太陽可能顯得較不活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase names energetic events on the sun.","zh":"這個片語命名太陽上的能量事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"solar activity","meaning":"太陽活動","examples":[{"en":"Natural variations in solar activity may have affected temperatures.","zh":"太陽活動的自然變化可能影響了氣溫。"},{"en":"Solar activity refers to changes in the sun’s energy, sunspots, flares, and radiation.","zh":"Solar activity 指太陽能量、黑子、耀斑和輻射的變化。"},{"en":"Scientists track solar activity to understand how the sun changes over time.","zh":"科學家追蹤太陽活動，以了解太陽如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"If solar activity falls, some researchers study whether less energy reaches Earth.","zh":"如果太陽活動下降，一些研究人員會研究是否有較少能量到達地球。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how active the sun is.","zh":"這個片語描述太陽有多活躍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"whether there is a correlation between","meaning":"是否在……之間有關聯","examples":[{"en":"Scientists still debate whether there is a correlation between solar activity and radiation.","zh":"科學家仍在爭論太陽活動和輻射之間是否有關聯。"},{"en":"Whether there is a correlation between two things asks if they change together in a connected way.","zh":"Whether there is a correlation between two things 是問兩者是否以相關方式一起變化。"},{"en":"A teacher may study whether there is a correlation between sleep and test scores.","zh":"老師可能研究睡眠和測驗分數之間是否有關聯。"},{"en":"If two things rise and fall together, researchers may investigate a possible link.","zh":"如果兩件事一起升跌，研究人員可能調查可能的聯繫。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about a relationship, not necessarily direct causation.","zh":"這個片語詢問關係，而不一定是直接因果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"solar radiation","meaning":"太陽輻射","examples":[{"en":"The amount of solar radiation emitted by the sun may vary slightly.","zh":"太陽發出的太陽輻射量可能略有變化。"},{"en":"Solar radiation is energy from the sun that travels through space as light and heat.","zh":"Solar radiation 是太陽以光和熱形式穿過太空傳來的能量。"},{"en":"Solar panels use solar radiation to produce electricity.","zh":"太陽能板使用太陽輻射來發電。"},{"en":"If solar radiation decreases, less energy may reach Earth.","zh":"如果太陽輻射減少，較少能量可能到達地球。"},{"en":"This phrase names the sun’s energy reaching the planet.","zh":"這個片語命名到達地球的太陽能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be still unclear","meaning":"仍不清楚","examples":[{"en":"The connection between sunspots and solar radiation is still unclear.","zh":"太陽黑子和太陽輻射之間的關係仍不清楚。"},{"en":"To be still unclear means people do not yet fully understand or confirm something.","zh":"To be still unclear 指人們尚未完全理解或確認某事。"},{"en":"The reason for a student’s sudden absence may still be unclear if no one has contacted the family.","zh":"如果沒有人聯絡家長，學生突然缺席的原因可能仍不清楚。"},{"en":"If evidence is incomplete, the answer can remain unclear for years.","zh":"如果證據不完整，答案可能多年來仍不清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase shows uncertainty that continues.","zh":"這個片語顯示持續存在的不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a fraction of a percent","meaning":"百分之一中的一小部分","examples":[{"en":"The reduction may have been only a fraction of a percent.","zh":"減少幅度可能只是百分之一中的一小部分。"},{"en":"A fraction of a percent means a very small part of one percent.","zh":"A fraction of a percent 指百分之一中的極小部分。"},{"en":"A shop discount of a fraction of a percent would barely change the final price.","zh":"商店折扣如果只是百分之一中的一小部分，最終價格幾乎不會改變。"},{"en":"Even a tiny percentage change can matter if the system is very sensitive.","zh":"如果系統非常敏感，即使極小百分比變化也可能重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an extremely small amount.","zh":"這個片語描述極小數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"arguably significant","meaning":"可以說是重要的","examples":[{"en":"Even a tiny change in solar radiation may be arguably significant.","zh":"即使太陽輻射的微小變化也可以說是重要的。"},{"en":"Arguably significant means possibly important, though people may still debate it.","zh":"Arguably significant 指可能重要，但人們仍可討論。"},{"en":"A small improvement in exam scores may be arguably significant if every class shows the same pattern.","zh":"如果每班都出現同一模式，考試分數的小幅改善可以說是重要的。"},{"en":"If a tiny change affects a large system, its importance may be worth arguing for.","zh":"如果微小變化影響大型系統，它的重要性就值得提出討論。"},{"en":"This phrase presents importance cautiously.","zh":"這個片語以謹慎方式提出重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"orbit so far away","meaning":"在如此遙遠的位置運行","examples":[{"en":"Earth is a small planet orbiting far away from the sun.","zh":"地球是一顆在離太陽如此遙遠的位置運行的小行星。"},{"en":"To orbit so far away means to move around something at a very great distance.","zh":"To orbit so far away 指在很遠距離上圍繞某物運行。"},{"en":"A satellite orbiting far away from Earth needs strong signals to communicate.","zh":"在離地球很遠位置運行的衛星需要強訊號來通訊。"},{"en":"If Earth orbits far from the sun, even small changes in solar energy may matter.","zh":"如果地球在離太陽很遠的位置運行，即使太陽能量小變化也可能重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement around an object from a distant path.","zh":"這個片語描述在遠距離軌道上圍繞某物移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"add further complexity to","meaning":"令……更加複雜","examples":[{"en":"Other eruptions added further complexity to the issue.","zh":"其他火山爆發令這個問題更加複雜。"},{"en":"To add further complexity to something means to make it harder to explain or understand.","zh":"To add further complexity to something 指令某事更難解釋或理解。"},{"en":"A new bus timetable can add further complexity to students’ morning travel.","zh":"新巴士時間表可以令學生早上交通更加複雜。"},{"en":"If several causes act together, they add complexity to the problem.","zh":"如果幾個原因同時作用，它們會令問題更加複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making an issue less simple.","zh":"這個片語描述令議題不再簡單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the issue","meaning":"這個問題","examples":[{"en":"Several factors made the issue more difficult to explain.","zh":"幾個因素令這個問題更難解釋。"},{"en":"The issue means the main problem, question, or topic being discussed.","zh":"The issue 指正在討論的主要問題、疑問或題目。"},{"en":"If students keep arriving late, the issue may be transport rather than attitude.","zh":"如果學生不斷遲到，問題可能是交通，而不是態度。"},{"en":"Understanding the issue clearly helps people choose the right solution.","zh":"清楚理解問題有助人們選擇正確解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase points back to the central matter under discussion.","zh":"這個片語回指正在討論的核心事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"significant volcanic eruptions","meaning":"重大火山爆發","examples":[{"en":"There had been other significant volcanic eruptions before Tambora.","zh":"在坦博拉之前已有其他重大火山爆發。"},{"en":"Significant volcanic eruptions are eruptions large enough to cause serious effects.","zh":"Significant volcanic eruptions 是大到足以造成嚴重影響的火山爆發。"},{"en":"A significant volcanic eruption may close airports because ash can damage aircraft engines.","zh":"重大火山爆發可能令機場關閉，因為火山灰可損壞飛機引擎。"},{"en":"If several eruptions occur close together, their effects may combine.","zh":"如果幾次爆發接近發生，其影響可能結合起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes volcanic events that matter historically or environmentally.","zh":"這個片語描述在歷史或環境上重要的火山事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"prior to","meaning":"在……之前","examples":[{"en":"Several eruptions occurred prior to Tambora.","zh":"幾次火山爆發發生在坦博拉之前。"},{"en":"Prior to means before.","zh":"Prior to 指在……之前。"},{"en":"Students should revise key vocabulary prior to a reading test.","zh":"學生應在閱讀測驗之前溫習關鍵詞。"},{"en":"If warning signs appear prior to a disaster, experts may later connect them to the event.","zh":"如果警號在災難之前出現，專家之後可能把它們與事件連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal way to show earlier timing.","zh":"這個片語是表示較早時間的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the Caribbean","meaning":"加勒比地區","examples":[{"en":"There were volcanic eruptions in the Caribbean before Tambora.","zh":"在坦博拉之前，加勒比地區曾發生火山爆發。"},{"en":"The Caribbean is a region of islands and coastal areas around the Caribbean Sea.","zh":"The Caribbean 是加勒比海周邊島嶼和沿岸地區。"},{"en":"Travellers often associate the Caribbean with beaches, islands, and warm weather.","zh":"旅客常把加勒比地區與海灘、島嶼和溫暖天氣聯繫起來。"},{"en":"If volcanoes erupt in the Caribbean, ash may affect nearby islands and shipping routes.","zh":"如果加勒比地區火山爆發，火山灰可能影響附近島嶼和航運路線。"},{"en":"This phrase names a geographical region.","zh":"這個片語命名一個地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Japan","meaning":"日本","examples":[{"en":"Japan was one of the places with earlier volcanic eruptions.","zh":"日本是較早出現火山爆發的地點之一。"},{"en":"Japan is an island country in East Asia with many volcanoes and earthquakes.","zh":"Japan 是東亞島國，有許多火山和地震。"},{"en":"A geography class may study Japan to understand life in volcanic regions.","zh":"地理課可能研究日本，以理解火山地區的生活。"},{"en":"If volcanic activity occurs in Japan, transport and farming may be affected locally.","zh":"如果日本出現火山活動，當地交通和農業可能受影響。"},{"en":"This word names a country included in the passage’s list of eruption sites.","zh":"這個詞命名文章列出的火山爆發地點之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the Philippines","meaning":"菲律賓","examples":[{"en":"The Philippines experienced a destructive eruption before Tambora.","zh":"菲律賓在坦博拉之前經歷一次具破壞性的火山爆發。"},{"en":"The Philippines is an island country in Southeast Asia with active volcanoes.","zh":"The Philippines 是東南亞島國，有活火山。"},{"en":"A travel plan to the Philippines may include checking weather and volcanic alerts.","zh":"到菲律賓旅遊的計劃可能包括檢查天氣和火山警報。"},{"en":"If a volcano erupts in the Philippines, whole communities may need to evacuate.","zh":"如果菲律賓火山爆發，整個社區可能需要疏散。"},{"en":"This phrase names another eruption location mentioned in the passage.","zh":"這個片語命名文章提到的另一個爆發地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"massive dust clouds","meaning":"巨大的塵雲","examples":[{"en":"Earlier eruptions produced massive dust clouds.","zh":"較早的火山爆發產生巨大塵雲。"},{"en":"Massive dust clouds are very large clouds of dust or ash in the air.","zh":"Massive dust clouds 是空氣中非常大的塵埃或火山灰雲。"},{"en":"A construction site may create dust clouds, but volcanic dust clouds are much larger and more dangerous.","zh":"建築地盤可能產生塵雲，但火山塵雲大得多也危險得多。"},{"en":"If massive dust clouds reach high altitude, they can reduce sunlight over wide areas.","zh":"如果巨大塵雲到達高空，它們可以減少大片地區的陽光。"},{"en":"This phrase describes huge amounts of airborne particles.","zh":"這個片語描述空氣中大量粒子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the Philippine example","meaning":"菲律賓的例子","examples":[{"en":"The Philippine example shows that Tambora was not the only eruption.","zh":"菲律賓的例子顯示坦博拉不是唯一一次火山爆發。"},{"en":"The Philippine example means the case from the Philippines used to support a point.","zh":"Philippine example 指用來支持某觀點的菲律賓案例。"},{"en":"A teacher may use the Hong Kong example to explain how public transport works in a dense city.","zh":"老師可能用香港的例子解釋公共交通如何在密集城市運作。"},{"en":"If one example shows a pattern, other examples may strengthen the explanation.","zh":"如果一個例子顯示某模式，其他例子可能加強解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific case used as evidence.","zh":"這個片語指出用作證據的特定案例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"destructive eruption","meaning":"具破壞性的火山爆發","examples":[{"en":"Mount Mayon had a highly destructive eruption in 1814.","zh":"馬榮火山在1814年發生一次極具破壞性的火山爆發。"},{"en":"A destructive eruption is a volcanic eruption that causes serious damage or death.","zh":"Destructive eruption 是造成嚴重破壞或死亡的火山爆發。"},{"en":"A destructive eruption may bury homes, destroy farms, and force people to leave.","zh":"具破壞性的火山爆發可能掩埋房屋、摧毀農場並迫使人離開。"},{"en":"If eruption material falls on towns, buildings and roads can be badly damaged.","zh":"如果火山物質落在城鎮上，建築物和道路可能嚴重受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an eruption with harmful consequences.","zh":"這個片語描述有害後果的火山爆發。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Mount Mayon","meaning":"馬榮火山","examples":[{"en":"Mount Mayon produced a major eruption in 1814.","zh":"馬榮火山在1814年發生一次重大爆發。"},{"en":"Mount Mayon is a volcano in the Philippines mentioned as an earlier eruption example.","zh":"Mount Mayon 是菲律賓一座火山，在文章中作為較早火山爆發例子。"},{"en":"Students may study Mount Mayon when learning about volcanic hazards in Southeast Asia.","zh":"學生學習東南亞火山危害時，可能研究馬榮火山。"},{"en":"If Mount Mayon erupts violently, nearby communities can be buried by ash and rock.","zh":"如果馬榮火山猛烈爆發，附近社區可能被火山灰和岩石掩埋。"},{"en":"This name refers to the Philippine volcano discussed in the passage.","zh":"這個名稱指文章討論的菲律賓火山。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"bury whole towns and villages","meaning":"掩埋整個城鎮和村莊","examples":[{"en":"The eruption buried whole towns and villages.","zh":"火山爆發掩埋整個城鎮和村莊。"},{"en":"To bury whole towns and villages means to cover entire communities under ash, rock, mud, or debris.","zh":"To bury whole towns and villages 指用火山灰、岩石、泥或碎屑覆蓋整個社區。"},{"en":"A landslide can bury houses if it moves quickly down a hill.","zh":"如果山泥快速滑下山坡，它可以掩埋房屋。"},{"en":"If towns are buried, survivors may lose homes, roads, farms, and records.","zh":"如果城鎮被掩埋，生還者可能失去家園、道路、農場和記錄。"},{"en":"This phrase describes total physical destruction of communities.","zh":"這個片語描述社區在實體上被完全摧毀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"spew out","meaning":"噴出","examples":[{"en":"The volcano spewed out millions of tons of ash and rock.","zh":"火山噴出數百萬噸火山灰和岩石。"},{"en":"To spew out something means to force large amounts of it out violently.","zh":"To spew out something 指猛烈地噴出大量某物。"},{"en":"A broken machine may spew out smoke if it overheats.","zh":"如果機器過熱，壞掉的機器可能噴出煙。"},{"en":"If a volcano spews out ash, air quality can become dangerous.","zh":"如果火山噴出火山灰，空氣質素可能變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a violent release from inside something.","zh":"這個片語描述某物從內部猛烈釋放出來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"millions of tons of","meaning":"數百萬噸的……","examples":[{"en":"The volcano spewed out millions of tons of ash and rock.","zh":"火山噴出數百萬噸的火山灰和岩石。"},{"en":"Millions of tons of something means an extremely large weight of material.","zh":"Millions of tons of something 指重量極大的物質。"},{"en":"A busy port may handle millions of tons of goods each year.","zh":"繁忙港口每年可能處理數百萬噸貨物。"},{"en":"If millions of tons of ash enter the air, the atmosphere can be affected widely.","zh":"如果數百萬噸火山灰進入空氣，大氣可以受到廣泛影響。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises an enormous quantity.","zh":"這個片語強調巨大數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ash and rock","meaning":"火山灰和岩石","examples":[{"en":"The eruption sent ash and rock into the atmosphere.","zh":"火山爆發把火山灰和岩石送入大氣。"},{"en":"Ash and rock are volcanic materials thrown out during an eruption.","zh":"Ash and rock 是火山爆發期間噴出的火山物質。"},{"en":"After an eruption, roads may be covered with ash and rock.","zh":"火山爆發後，道路可能被火山灰和岩石覆蓋。"},{"en":"If ash and rock fall on houses, roofs can break and people may be injured.","zh":"如果火山灰和岩石落在房屋上，屋頂可能破裂，人們可能受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes solid material ejected by a volcano.","zh":"這個片語描述火山噴出的固體物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the high atmosphere","meaning":"高層大氣","examples":[{"en":"Ash and rock were thrown into the high atmosphere.","zh":"火山灰和岩石被拋入高層大氣。"},{"en":"The high atmosphere means the upper parts of the air around Earth.","zh":"High atmosphere 指地球周圍空氣的上層部分。"},{"en":"Weather balloons can carry instruments into the high atmosphere.","zh":"氣象氣球可以把儀器帶入高層大氣。"},{"en":"If ash reaches the high atmosphere, it may travel far before falling down.","zh":"如果火山灰到達高層大氣，它可能在落下前傳到很遠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes air layers far above the ground.","zh":"這個片語描述離地面很高的大氣層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"put all these factors together","meaning":"把所有這些因素結合起來","examples":[{"en":"When we put all these factors together, the sequence becomes clearer.","zh":"當我們把所有這些因素結合起來，事情的先後脈絡就更清楚。"},{"en":"To put all these factors together means to consider all causes or details as a connected whole.","zh":"To put all these factors together 指把所有原因或細節作為相連整體來考慮。"},{"en":"A teacher may put attendance, homework, and test scores together to understand a student’s progress.","zh":"老師可能把出席、功課和測驗分數結合起來，以理解學生進步。"},{"en":"If several small causes combine, the full explanation becomes clearer only when they are considered together.","zh":"如果幾個小原因結合，完整解釋只有在一起考慮時才更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes building a complete picture from many parts.","zh":"這個片語描述從多個部分建立完整圖像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the sequence is clearer","meaning":"事情的先後脈絡更清楚","examples":[{"en":"The sequence is clearer when all the factors are considered together.","zh":"當所有因素一起考慮，事情的先後脈絡更清楚。"},{"en":"The sequence is clearer means the order of events is easier to understand.","zh":"The sequence is clearer 指事件的先後次序更容易理解。"},{"en":"A timeline can make the sequence of a historical event clearer for students.","zh":"時間線可以令學生更清楚歷史事件的先後脈絡。"},{"en":"If causes and effects are placed in order, confusion is reduced.","zh":"如果原因和後果按次序排列，混亂就會減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a better understanding of how events followed one another.","zh":"這個片語描述對事件如何相繼發生有更好理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"suffer from lower temperatures","meaning":"受較低氣溫影響","examples":[{"en":"The world was already suffering from lower temperatures.","zh":"世界已經受較低氣溫影響。"},{"en":"To suffer from lower temperatures means to be harmed or troubled by colder conditions.","zh":"To suffer from lower temperatures 指因較寒冷環境而受害或受困擾。"},{"en":"A farm may suffer from lower temperatures if young plants cannot grow.","zh":"如果幼苗不能生長，農場可能受較低氣溫影響。"},{"en":"If people suffer from cold weather, heating costs and health risks may rise.","zh":"如果人們受寒冷天氣影響，取暖成本和健康風險可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that cold weather is causing difficulty.","zh":"這個片語顯示寒冷天氣正在造成困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"natural variations in","meaning":"……的自然變化","examples":[{"en":"Lower temperatures were linked to natural variations in solar activity.","zh":"較低氣溫與太陽活動的自然變化有關。"},{"en":"Natural variations in something are normal changes that occur without human control.","zh":"Natural variations in something 是不受人類控制而自然發生的正常變化。"},{"en":"Natural variations in rainfall can affect how much water a reservoir collects.","zh":"降雨的自然變化可以影響水塘收集多少水。"},{"en":"If natural variation changes sunlight slightly, climate may respond over time.","zh":"如果自然變化稍微改變陽光，氣候可能隨時間作出反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes normal changes within a natural system.","zh":"這個片語描述自然系統中的正常變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a series of severe volcanic eruptions","meaning":"一連串嚴重火山爆發","examples":[{"en":"A series of severe volcanic eruptions occurred before Tambora.","zh":"在坦博拉之前發生一連串嚴重火山爆發。"},{"en":"A series of severe volcanic eruptions means several serious eruptions happening one after another.","zh":"A series of severe volcanic eruptions 指幾次嚴重火山爆發相繼發生。"},{"en":"A series of accidents on the same road may lead the government to improve safety.","zh":"同一道路上一連串事故可能促使政府改善安全。"},{"en":"If several eruptions happen close together, ash can accumulate in the atmosphere.","zh":"如果幾次火山爆發接近發生，火山灰可以在大氣中積聚。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses repeated serious events, not one isolated event.","zh":"這個片語強調重複的嚴重事件，而不是單一孤立事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"accumulation of ash","meaning":"火山灰積聚","examples":[{"en":"The accumulation of ash in the stratosphere reached a historic high.","zh":"平流層中的火山灰積聚達到歷史高位。"},{"en":"Accumulation of ash means ash building up over time in one place or layer.","zh":"Accumulation of ash 指火山灰隨時間在某處或某層累積。"},{"en":"The accumulation of dust in a classroom can make cleaning harder.","zh":"課室中灰塵積聚會令清潔更困難。"},{"en":"If ash accumulates in the atmosphere, it may block more sunlight.","zh":"如果火山灰在大氣中積聚，它可能阻擋更多陽光。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual build-up of volcanic material.","zh":"這個片語描述火山物質逐漸累積。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rise to a historic high","meaning":"升至歷史高位","examples":[{"en":"The accumulation of ash rose to a historic high.","zh":"火山灰積聚升至歷史高位。"},{"en":"To rise to a historic high means to reach the highest level ever recorded in history.","zh":"To rise to a historic high 指達到有史以來記錄的最高水平。"},{"en":"School applications may rise to a historic high after the school wins a major award.","zh":"學校贏得大獎後，入學申請可能升至歷史高位。"},{"en":"If ash levels rise to a historic high, climate effects may become stronger.","zh":"如果火山灰水平升至歷史高位，氣候影響可能更強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching an exceptional record level.","zh":"這個片語描述達到異常紀錄水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mammoth Tambora explosion","meaning":"巨大的坦博拉火山爆發","examples":[{"en":"The mammoth Tambora explosion added greatly to the ash in the atmosphere.","zh":"巨大的坦博拉火山爆發大幅增加了大氣中的火山灰。"},{"en":"A mammoth explosion is an extremely huge and powerful explosion.","zh":"Mammoth explosion 是極其巨大而強力的爆炸。"},{"en":"A mammoth factory explosion would affect not only the building but the surrounding neighbourhood.","zh":"巨大的工廠爆炸不只影響建築本身，也會影響周邊社區。"},{"en":"If an eruption is mammoth in scale, its effects can extend far beyond the volcano.","zh":"如果火山爆發規模巨大，其影響可以遠超火山本身。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the enormous size of the Tambora event.","zh":"這個片語強調坦博拉事件的巨大規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"substantially add to","meaning":"大幅增加……","examples":[{"en":"The Tambora eruption substantially added to the atmospheric ash.","zh":"坦博拉火山爆發大幅增加了大氣火山灰。"},{"en":"To substantially add to something means to increase it by a large or meaningful amount.","zh":"To substantially add to something 指以大幅或有意義的數量增加某物。"},{"en":"A large donation can substantially add to a school’s library budget.","zh":"一筆大型捐款可以大幅增加學校圖書館預算。"},{"en":"If one eruption adds greatly to existing ash, cooling effects may intensify.","zh":"如果一次火山爆發大幅增加已有火山灰，降溫影響可能加劇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major addition, not a tiny increase.","zh":"這個片語描述重大增加，而不是微小增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"send a sharp cold spell across","meaning":"令一股強烈寒流席捲……","examples":[{"en":"The eruption sent a sharp cold spell across the globe.","zh":"火山爆發令一股強烈寒流席捲全球。"},{"en":"To send a sharp cold spell across an area means to cause a sudden period of cold weather to spread there.","zh":"To send a sharp cold spell across an area 指令一段突然寒冷天氣擴散到該地。"},{"en":"A winter storm can send a sharp cold spell across a whole city.","zh":"冬季風暴可以令一股強烈寒流席捲整座城市。"},{"en":"If cold spreads quickly across many regions, farming and transport can be disrupted.","zh":"如果寒冷迅速擴散到多個地區，農業和交通都可能受干擾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sudden wave of cold affecting a wide area.","zh":"這個片語描述一股突然寒冷影響廣泛地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cold spell","meaning":"一段寒冷天氣；寒流","examples":[{"en":"A sharp cold spell spread across the already cooler globe.","zh":"一股強烈寒流席捲已經較寒冷的全球。"},{"en":"A cold spell is a short or noticeable period of colder-than-usual weather.","zh":"Cold spell 是一段明顯比平常寒冷的天氣。"},{"en":"A cold spell can make families bring out winter clothes earlier than expected.","zh":"寒流可以令家庭比預期更早拿出冬衣。"},{"en":"If a cold spell arrives during planting season, young crops may die.","zh":"如果寒流在播種季節到來，幼苗可能死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a temporary period of unusual cold.","zh":"這個片語描述暫時性的異常寒冷時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the already cooler globe","meaning":"已經較寒冷的全球","examples":[{"en":"The eruption affected an already cooler globe.","zh":"火山爆發影響了一個已經較寒冷的全球。"},{"en":"The already cooler globe means the world was already colder before the new event happened.","zh":"The already cooler globe 指新事件發生前，世界已經較冷。"},{"en":"If a cold front arrives in an already cold city, conditions can become dangerous.","zh":"如果冷鋒到達一座已經寒冷的城市，情況可能變得危險。"},{"en":"When a new problem hits an already weakened system, the damage becomes worse.","zh":"當新問題打擊已經脆弱的系統，損害會更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the world was not starting from normal conditions.","zh":"這個片語顯示世界並非從正常狀態開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the consequences were dire","meaning":"後果十分嚴重","examples":[{"en":"The consequences of the eruption were dire.","zh":"火山爆發的後果十分嚴重。"},{"en":"Dire consequences are extremely serious and harmful results.","zh":"Dire consequences 是極其嚴重和有害的結果。"},{"en":"If a hospital loses power for hours, the consequences could be dire for patients.","zh":"如果醫院停電數小時，對病人的後果可能十分嚴重。"},{"en":"When crops fail across many regions, the consequences can include famine and unrest.","zh":"當多個地區農作物歉收，後果可以包括饑荒和動盪。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that the results were very severe.","zh":"這個片語警告結果非常嚴重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fall to near-freezing","meaning":"降至接近冰點","examples":[{"en":"Temperatures fell to near-freezing within hours.","zh":"氣溫在數小時內降至接近冰點。"},{"en":"To fall to near-freezing means to drop close to the temperature at which water freezes.","zh":"To fall to near-freezing 指下降到接近水會結冰的溫度。"},{"en":"If the temperature falls to near-freezing, people may protect pipes and bring plants indoors.","zh":"如果氣溫降至接近冰點，人們可能保護水管並把植物搬入室內。"},{"en":"Crops can be damaged if warm-weather plants suddenly face near-freezing temperatures.","zh":"如果溫暖天氣植物突然面對接近冰點的氣溫，農作物可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sharp drop close to zero degrees Celsius.","zh":"這個片語描述氣溫急跌至接近攝氏零度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"within hours","meaning":"在數小時內","examples":[{"en":"Temperatures dropped within hours.","zh":"氣溫在數小時內下降。"},{"en":"Within hours means in only a few hours or before many hours have passed.","zh":"Within hours 指只用幾小時或在不多小時過去前。"},{"en":"After the notice was posted, parents replied within hours.","zh":"通知貼出後，家長在數小時內回覆。"},{"en":"If temperature changes within hours, people may have little time to prepare.","zh":"如果氣溫在數小時內改變，人們可能沒有太多時間準備。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses speed and short timing.","zh":"這個片語強調速度和短時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"together with","meaning":"加上；連同","examples":[{"en":"Near-freezing temperatures came together with sudden summer frosts.","zh":"接近冰點的氣溫加上突如其來的夏季霜凍。"},{"en":"Together with means along with or in addition to.","zh":"Together with 指加上或連同。"},{"en":"A school trip may require a consent form together with payment.","zh":"學校旅行可能需要同意書連同付款。"},{"en":"If cold temperatures come together with heavy rain, the effect on crops can be worse.","zh":"如果寒冷氣溫加上大雨，對農作物的影響可能更差。"},{"en":"This phrase links two things happening or being considered together.","zh":"這個片語把兩件同時發生或被一起考慮的事連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sudden summer frosts","meaning":"突如其來的夏季霜凍","examples":[{"en":"Sudden summer frosts damaged crops.","zh":"突如其來的夏季霜凍破壞了農作物。"},{"en":"Sudden summer frosts are unexpected freezing conditions during the summer.","zh":"Sudden summer frosts 是夏季出現的意外結霜或冰凍情況。"},{"en":"A gardener may lose tomato plants if sudden summer frosts arrive overnight.","zh":"如果突如其來的夏季霜凍一夜之間出現，園丁可能失去番茄植物。"},{"en":"If frost comes in summer, crops are unprepared and may fail.","zh":"如果霜在夏季來臨，作物沒有準備，可能歉收。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cold damage at a season when warmth is expected.","zh":"這個片語描述在本應溫暖季節中的寒冷損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sustained drenching rainfall","meaning":"持續的傾盆大雨","examples":[{"en":"Sustained drenching rainfall damaged agricultural production.","zh":"持續的傾盆大雨破壞了農業生產。"},{"en":"Sustained drenching rainfall means heavy rain that continues for a long time and soaks everything.","zh":"Sustained drenching rainfall 指長時間持續、把一切浸濕的大雨。"},{"en":"Sustained drenching rainfall can flood playgrounds and cancel outdoor lessons.","zh":"持續的傾盆大雨可以淹浸操場並取消戶外課。"},{"en":"If fields stay soaked, farmers may be unable to harvest or plant properly.","zh":"如果田地長期浸濕，農民可能無法正常收割或播種。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-lasting heavy rain with damaging effects.","zh":"這個片語描述帶有破壞性影響的長時間大雨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"across the Northern Hemisphere","meaning":"橫跨北半球","examples":[{"en":"Extreme weather spread across the Northern Hemisphere.","zh":"極端天氣橫跨北半球擴散。"},{"en":"Across the Northern Hemisphere means over the half of Earth north of the equator.","zh":"Across the Northern Hemisphere 指遍及赤道以北的半個地球。"},{"en":"A cold wave across the Northern Hemisphere can affect Europe, Asia, and North America.","zh":"橫跨北半球的寒潮可以影響歐洲、亞洲和北美。"},{"en":"If a climate effect crosses the Northern Hemisphere, millions of people may be affected.","zh":"如果氣候影響橫跨北半球，數百萬人可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very wide geographical spread.","zh":"這個片語描述非常廣泛的地理擴散。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"staple crops","meaning":"主糧作物","examples":[{"en":"Staple crops such as maize and wheat failed to mature.","zh":"粟米和小麥等主糧作物未能成熟。"},{"en":"Staple crops are basic food crops that many people depend on for daily meals.","zh":"Staple crops 是許多人日常飲食依賴的基本糧食作物。"},{"en":"Rice is a staple crop in many Asian countries.","zh":"稻米是許多亞洲國家的主糧作物。"},{"en":"If staple crops fail, food shortages can quickly become serious.","zh":"如果主糧作物歉收，糧食短缺可以迅速變得嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to crops that support everyday survival.","zh":"這個片語指支撐日常生存的農作物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"maize and wheat","meaning":"粟米和小麥","examples":[{"en":"Maize and wheat were among the crops affected.","zh":"粟米和小麥是受影響的作物之一。"},{"en":"Maize and wheat are important grain crops used for food and animal feed.","zh":"Maize and wheat 是重要穀物作物，用於人類食物和動物飼料。"},{"en":"A bakery depends on wheat, while many farms use maize to feed animals.","zh":"麵包店依賴小麥，而許多農場用粟米餵飼動物。"},{"en":"If maize and wheat fail, both people and livestock may face food shortages.","zh":"如果粟米和小麥歉收，人和牲畜都可能面對糧食短缺。"},{"en":"This phrase names two major crops affected by bad weather.","zh":"這個片語命名兩種受惡劣天氣影響的主要作物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fail to mature","meaning":"未能成熟","examples":[{"en":"Many staple crops failed to mature.","zh":"許多主糧作物未能成熟。"},{"en":"To fail to mature means to not grow fully or become ready for harvest.","zh":"To fail to mature 指沒有完全生長或未能達到可收割狀態。"},{"en":"Fruit may fail to mature if the weather stays too cold.","zh":"如果天氣一直太冷，水果可能未能成熟。"},{"en":"If crops fail to mature, farmers may have little food to sell or store.","zh":"如果農作物未能成熟，農民可能幾乎沒有食物可出售或儲存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth stopping before completion.","zh":"這個片語描述生長在完成前停止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"livestock animals","meaning":"牲畜","examples":[{"en":"Many livestock animals were killed by the extreme weather.","zh":"許多牲畜被極端天氣殺死。"},{"en":"Livestock animals are farm animals kept for food, milk, wool, work, or sale.","zh":"Livestock animals 是農場飼養，用於食物、牛奶、羊毛、工作或出售的動物。"},{"en":"Cows, sheep, pigs, goats, and chickens are common livestock animals.","zh":"牛、羊、豬、山羊和雞都是常見牲畜。"},{"en":"If livestock animals die, families may lose food, income, and farming support.","zh":"如果牲畜死亡，家庭可能失去食物、收入和農業支援。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to animals raised as part of agriculture.","zh":"這個片語指作為農業一部分飼養的動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"agricultural production","meaning":"農業生產","examples":[{"en":"Agricultural production was already low before the final crisis.","zh":"在最後危機之前，農業生產已經偏低。"},{"en":"Agricultural production is the amount of food, crops, and farm goods produced.","zh":"Agricultural production 是生產出來的食物、農作物和農產品數量。"},{"en":"Drought can reduce agricultural production by damaging fields and water supplies.","zh":"乾旱可以透過破壞田地和水源來減少農業生產。"},{"en":"If agricultural production falls, food prices may rise and families may suffer.","zh":"如果農業生產下降，食物價格可能上升，家庭可能受苦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes farming output.","zh":"這個片語描述農業產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"due to the cooler preceding years","meaning":"由於之前數年較寒冷","examples":[{"en":"Agricultural production was low due to the cooler preceding years.","zh":"農業生產偏低，是由於之前數年較寒冷。"},{"en":"Due to the cooler preceding years means because the years before had been colder than usual.","zh":"Due to the cooler preceding years 指因為之前幾年比平常寒冷。"},{"en":"A poor harvest may occur due to the colder months before planting season.","zh":"收成差可能由於播種季節前幾個月較寒冷。"},{"en":"If several earlier years are cool, farms may enter a crisis already weakened.","zh":"如果早前幾年都較冷，農場可能在已經脆弱的狀態下面對危機。"},{"en":"This phrase links current weakness to earlier cold conditions.","zh":"這個片語把當前脆弱與早前寒冷情況連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"preceding years","meaning":"之前數年","examples":[{"en":"The preceding years had already weakened agricultural production.","zh":"之前數年已經削弱了農業生產。"},{"en":"Preceding years are the years that came before the time being discussed.","zh":"Preceding years 是所討論時間之前的幾年。"},{"en":"A student’s final grade may reflect effort in the preceding years, not just one exam.","zh":"學生最終成績可能反映之前數年的努力，而不只是一場考試。"},{"en":"If the preceding years were difficult, a community may have fewer reserves for a new crisis.","zh":"如果之前數年困難，一個社區面對新危機時可能較少儲備。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain earlier background conditions.","zh":"這個片語幫助解釋早前背景情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rudimentary road systems","meaning":"簡陋的道路系統","examples":[{"en":"Rudimentary road systems made food distribution difficult.","zh":"簡陋的道路系統令糧食分發困難。"},{"en":"Rudimentary road systems are basic, simple, and poorly developed road networks.","zh":"Rudimentary road systems 是基本、簡單且發展不足的道路網絡。"},{"en":"A village with rudimentary roads may be hard to reach after heavy rain.","zh":"道路簡陋的村莊在大雨後可能難以到達。"},{"en":"If roads are poor, emergency food cannot be moved quickly to people in need.","zh":"如果道路差，緊急糧食不能快速運到有需要的人手中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weak transport infrastructure.","zh":"這個片語描述薄弱的交通基礎設施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"importation and distribution","meaning":"進口和分發","examples":[{"en":"Importation and distribution of emergency food supplies were difficult.","zh":"緊急糧食供應的進口和分發很困難。"},{"en":"Importation and distribution means bringing goods into a country and sending them to different places.","zh":"Importation and distribution 指把貨物帶入一個國家，並送到不同地方。"},{"en":"A charity must plan importation and distribution before sending medicine overseas.","zh":"慈善機構向海外送藥前，必須規劃進口和分發。"},{"en":"If roads and ports are weak, food may arrive but still fail to reach hungry families.","zh":"如果道路和港口薄弱，食物可能到達卻仍未能送到饑餓家庭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both receiving supplies and delivering them.","zh":"這個片語同時描述接收物資和運送物資。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"emergency food supplies","meaning":"緊急糧食供應","examples":[{"en":"Emergency food supplies were difficult to transport.","zh":"緊急糧食供應難以運送。"},{"en":"Emergency food supplies are food reserves sent quickly to people during a crisis.","zh":"Emergency food supplies 是危機期間快速送給人們的糧食儲備。"},{"en":"After a typhoon, emergency food supplies may include rice, water, and canned food.","zh":"颱風後，緊急糧食供應可能包括米、水和罐頭食品。"},{"en":"If emergency food cannot reach affected areas, hunger can worsen rapidly.","zh":"如果緊急糧食不能到達受影響地區，饑餓可能迅速惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes urgent food aid for survival.","zh":"這個片語描述維持生存的緊急食物援助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the final blow","meaning":"最後一擊","examples":[{"en":"The failed harvest was the final blow.","zh":"收成失敗是最後一擊。"},{"en":"The final blow is the last serious problem that makes an already bad situation collapse.","zh":"The final blow 是令已經糟糕的情況崩潰的最後一個嚴重問題。"},{"en":"After months of poor sales, losing the main customer was the final blow for the shop.","zh":"經過數月銷售低迷後，失去主要顧客成為該店的最後一擊。"},{"en":"If a community is already weak, one more disaster can become the final blow.","zh":"如果社區已經脆弱，再一次災難可以成為最後一擊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the last damaging event in a chain of problems.","zh":"這個片語描述一連串問題中的最後破壞性事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"devastating","meaning":"毀滅性的","examples":[{"en":"The final blow was devastating for many communities.","zh":"這最後一擊對許多社區是毀滅性的。"},{"en":"Devastating means causing great damage, suffering, or emotional pain.","zh":"Devastating 指造成巨大破壞、痛苦或情感傷害。"},{"en":"A sudden factory closure can be devastating for workers and their families.","zh":"工廠突然關閉可以對工人和家庭造成毀滅性影響。"},{"en":"If a harvest fails completely, the effect can be devastating in poor farming areas.","zh":"如果收成完全失敗，對貧困農村地區的影響可以是毀滅性的。"},{"en":"This word describes harm that is severe and deeply felt.","zh":"這個詞描述嚴重且深刻的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"widespread malnutrition","meaning":"大範圍營養不良","examples":[{"en":"The crisis resulted in widespread malnutrition.","zh":"危機導致大範圍營養不良。"},{"en":"Widespread malnutrition means many people lack enough healthy food and nutrients.","zh":"Widespread malnutrition 指許多人缺乏足夠健康食物和營養。"},{"en":"Children may suffer from malnutrition if families cannot afford balanced meals.","zh":"如果家庭負擔不起均衡膳食，兒童可能營養不良。"},{"en":"If food shortages continue, malnutrition can weaken immunity and growth.","zh":"如果糧食短缺持續，營養不良可以削弱免疫力和成長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious health problem affecting many people.","zh":"這個片語描述影響許多人的嚴重健康問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"starvation","meaning":"饑餓；餓死","examples":[{"en":"Many people suffered from starvation after the crop failures.","zh":"農作物歉收後，許多人遭受饑餓。"},{"en":"Starvation is extreme hunger caused by not having enough food for a long time.","zh":"Starvation 是長時間沒有足夠食物造成的極度饑餓。"},{"en":"Refugees may face starvation if emergency food does not arrive.","zh":"如果緊急糧食未能到達，難民可能面對饑餓。"},{"en":"If harvests fail and food cannot be imported, starvation can spread.","zh":"如果收成失敗而食物不能進口，饑餓可能蔓延。"},{"en":"This word describes hunger severe enough to threaten life.","zh":"這個詞描述嚴重到威脅生命的饑餓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"outbreaks of diseases","meaning":"疾病爆發","examples":[{"en":"The crisis caused outbreaks of diseases such as typhus and cholera.","zh":"危機造成斑疹傷寒和霍亂等疾病爆發。"},{"en":"Outbreaks of diseases are sudden increases in cases of illness in a place.","zh":"Outbreaks of diseases 是某地方疾病個案突然增加。"},{"en":"A school may close temporarily after outbreaks of flu in several classes.","zh":"如果幾個班爆發流感，學校可能暫時停課。"},{"en":"If people are hungry and crowded together, disease outbreaks can spread more easily.","zh":"如果人們饑餓又擠在一起，疾病爆發更容易擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes illness appearing suddenly among many people.","zh":"這個片語描述疾病突然在許多人之中出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"typhus and cholera","meaning":"斑疹傷寒和霍亂","examples":[{"en":"Typhus and cholera spread during the famine.","zh":"斑疹傷寒和霍亂在饑荒期間蔓延。"},{"en":"Typhus and cholera are serious infectious diseases often linked with poor conditions and unsafe water.","zh":"Typhus and cholera 是常與惡劣環境和不安全食水相關的嚴重傳染病。"},{"en":"After floods, doctors may watch for diseases like cholera if clean water is limited.","zh":"水災後，如果清潔食水有限，醫生可能留意霍亂等疾病。"},{"en":"If sanitation breaks down, infectious diseases can spread quickly.","zh":"如果衛生設施崩潰，傳染病可以迅速擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase names two dangerous diseases associated with crisis conditions.","zh":"這個片語命名兩種與危機環境相關的危險疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"streams of starving refugees","meaning":"一批批捱餓難民","examples":[{"en":"The crisis created streams of starving refugees.","zh":"危機造成一批批捱餓難民。"},{"en":"Streams of starving refugees means many groups of hungry people forced to leave their homes.","zh":"Streams of starving refugees 指許多群饑餓而被迫離家的難民。"},{"en":"After a war, roads may fill with streams of refugees searching for safety.","zh":"戰爭後，道路可能滿是一批批尋找安全地方的難民。"},{"en":"If food disappears, people may leave their villages in large numbers.","zh":"如果食物消失，人們可能大量離開村莊。"},{"en":"This phrase creates an image of continuous movement by desperate people.","zh":"這個片語營造絕望人群不斷流動的畫面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"large shifts of population","meaning":"大規模人口遷移","examples":[{"en":"The famine caused large shifts of population.","zh":"饑荒造成大規模人口遷移。"},{"en":"Large shifts of population are major movements of people from one place to another.","zh":"Large shifts of population 是人們由一地遷往另一地的大規模移動。"},{"en":"Rising rents can cause shifts of population from city centres to cheaper districts.","zh":"租金上升可以造成由市中心遷往較便宜地區的人口轉移。"},{"en":"If famine hits rural areas, many families may move toward towns or other countries.","zh":"如果饑荒打擊農村地區，許多家庭可能移向城鎮或其他國家。"},{"en":"This phrase describes major changes in where people live.","zh":"這個片語描述人們居住地的大幅改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"riots","meaning":"暴亂","examples":[{"en":"Food shortages led to riots.","zh":"糧食短缺導致暴亂。"},{"en":"Riots are violent public disturbances involving groups of angry people.","zh":"Riots 是由憤怒人群造成的暴力公共混亂。"},{"en":"A city may face riots if people believe food prices are unfair and leaders ignore them.","zh":"如果人們認為食物價格不公平而領袖不理會，城市可能面對暴亂。"},{"en":"If hunger and fear increase, crowds may become harder to control.","zh":"如果饑餓和恐懼增加，人群可能更難控制。"},{"en":"This word describes serious disorder in public places.","zh":"這個詞描述公共場所中的嚴重混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"looting of food warehouses","meaning":"搶掠糧倉","examples":[{"en":"The crisis led to looting of food warehouses.","zh":"危機導致搶掠糧倉。"},{"en":"Looting of food warehouses means people stealing food from storage buildings during disorder.","zh":"Looting of food warehouses 指人們在混亂中從儲糧建築偷取食物。"},{"en":"During a severe shortage, desperate crowds may break into warehouses for grain.","zh":"在嚴重短缺期間，絕望人群可能闖入倉庫取穀物。"},{"en":"If official distribution fails, people may turn to looting to survive.","zh":"如果官方分發失敗，人們可能為求生存而搶掠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes theft linked to hunger and social breakdown.","zh":"這個片語描述與饑餓和社會崩潰相關的偷竊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"breakdowns of civic order","meaning":"公共秩序崩潰","examples":[{"en":"The famine caused breakdowns of civic order.","zh":"饑荒造成公共秩序崩潰。"},{"en":"Breakdowns of civic order are failures of normal public peace, rules, and social control.","zh":"Breakdowns of civic order 是正常公共和平、規則和社會控制失效。"},{"en":"After a major disaster, civic order may break down if food, police, and transport all fail.","zh":"重大災難後，如果食物、警力和交通全部失效，公共秩序可能崩潰。"},{"en":"If people cannot trust authorities to provide basics, public disorder may spread.","zh":"如果人們不能信任當局提供基本物資，公共混亂可能蔓延。"},{"en":"This phrase describes society losing normal order.","zh":"這個片語描述社會失去正常秩序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"an estimated","meaning":"估計","examples":[{"en":"An estimated 100,000 people died in Ireland alone.","zh":"估計單是在愛爾蘭已有100,000人死亡。"},{"en":"An estimated number is an approximate number based on available information.","zh":"An estimated number 是根據現有資料得出的約略數字。"},{"en":"An estimated 500 students attended the school fair.","zh":"估計有500名學生參加學校嘉年華。"},{"en":"If exact records are missing, historians may use estimated figures.","zh":"如果缺乏精確紀錄，歷史學家可能使用估計數字。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a number is approximate, not exact.","zh":"這個片語顯示數字是約略，而非精確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in Ireland alone","meaning":"單是在愛爾蘭","examples":[{"en":"About 100,000 people died in Ireland alone.","zh":"單是在愛爾蘭約有100,000人死亡。"},{"en":"In Ireland alone means only in Ireland, without counting other places.","zh":"In Ireland alone 指只計愛爾蘭，不包括其他地方。"},{"en":"The school raised HKD 20,000 in one class alone, before counting other classes.","zh":"單是一班已為學校籌得20,000港元，還未計其他班。"},{"en":"If many people died in one place alone, the total across all regions was likely much higher.","zh":"如果單一地方已有很多人死亡，所有地區總數很可能高得多。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the scale within a single location.","zh":"這個片語強調單一地點內的規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"many times that figure","meaning":"是那個數字的很多倍","examples":[{"en":"Many times that figure died on the European continent.","zh":"歐洲大陸死亡人數是那個數字的很多倍。"},{"en":"Many times that figure means a much larger number than the number just mentioned.","zh":"Many times that figure 指比剛提到的數字大得多。"},{"en":"If one shop sold 100 cakes, the whole chain may have sold many times that figure.","zh":"如果一間店賣出100個蛋糕，整個連鎖店可能賣出那數字的很多倍。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the total elsewhere was far greater.","zh":"這個片語顯示其他地方的總數遠遠更大。"},{"en":"It is used when the exact number may be unknown but the scale is clearly much larger.","zh":"當確實數字可能未知但規模明顯更大時，可使用這個片語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the European continent","meaning":"歐洲大陸","examples":[{"en":"Many more people died on the European continent.","zh":"歐洲大陸有更多人死亡。"},{"en":"The European continent refers to mainland Europe, usually excluding islands such as Britain and Ireland.","zh":"The European continent 指歐洲本土，通常不包括英國和愛爾蘭等島嶼。"},{"en":"A train journey across the European continent may pass through several countries.","zh":"橫跨歐洲大陸的火車旅程可能經過多個國家。"},{"en":"If famine spreads across the continent, many nations may be affected at once.","zh":"如果饑荒在大陸蔓延，多個國家可能同時受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies mainland Europe as a large geographical area.","zh":"這個片語指出歐洲本土這一大片地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"such mortality that","meaning":"死亡人數多到……","examples":[{"en":"There was such mortality that the famine is now considered the worst of the century.","zh":"死亡人數多到這場饑荒現在被認為是該世紀最嚴重的一次。"},{"en":"Such mortality that means so many deaths occurred that a serious conclusion follows.","zh":"Such mortality that 指死亡人數如此多，以致產生嚴重結論。"},{"en":"The disease caused such mortality that the hospital opened emergency wards.","zh":"疾病造成死亡人數多到醫院開設緊急病房。"},{"en":"If death numbers are extremely high, historians may classify the event as a major disaster.","zh":"如果死亡人數極高，歷史學家可能把事件歸類為重大災難。"},{"en":"This structure links a high death toll with its consequence.","zh":"這個結構把高死亡人數與其後果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the famine","meaning":"饑荒","examples":[{"en":"The famine is considered the worst of that century.","zh":"這場饑荒被認為是該世紀最嚴重的一次。"},{"en":"The famine means a severe shortage of food that causes hunger, illness, and death.","zh":"Famine 指嚴重糧食短缺，導致饑餓、疾病和死亡。"},{"en":"A region may face famine if crops fail and food cannot be imported.","zh":"如果農作物歉收而食物不能進口，一個地區可能面對饑荒。"},{"en":"If famine continues, people may migrate, riot, or suffer from disease.","zh":"如果饑荒持續，人們可能遷移、暴亂或患病。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major food crisis.","zh":"這個片語描述重大糧食危機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be considered the worst of","meaning":"被認為是……中最嚴重的","examples":[{"en":"The famine is considered the worst of the nineteenth century.","zh":"這場饑荒被認為是十九世紀最嚴重的。"},{"en":"To be considered the worst of something means to be judged as the most severe in that group or period.","zh":"To be considered the worst of something 指被判斷為某組或某時期中最嚴重。"},{"en":"A storm may be considered the worst of the decade if it causes record damage.","zh":"如果一場風暴造成破紀錄損害，它可能被認為是十年中最嚴重的。"},{"en":"If an event has the highest death toll, people may consider it the worst.","zh":"如果某事件死亡人數最高，人們可能認為它最嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a strong historical judgment.","zh":"這個片語表達強烈的歷史判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the question then is whether","meaning":"接下來的問題是是否","examples":[{"en":"The question then is whether such an event could happen again.","zh":"接下來的問題是，這樣的事件是否可能再次發生。"},{"en":"The question then is whether introduces the next logical question after earlier information.","zh":"The question then is whether 用來在前文資訊後引出下一個合乎邏輯的問題。"},{"en":"If students improve with practice, the question then is whether the method works for weaker learners too.","zh":"如果學生透過練習進步，接下來的問題是該方法是否也適用於較弱學生。"},{"en":"After understanding a past disaster, people naturally ask whether it could return.","zh":"理解過去災難後，人們自然會問它是否可能回來。"},{"en":"This phrase moves the discussion to the next issue.","zh":"這個片語把討論推向下一個問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"happen again","meaning":"再次發生","examples":[{"en":"A year without a summer could happen again.","zh":"無夏之年可能再次發生。"},{"en":"To happen again means to occur another time after happening before.","zh":"To happen again 指某事曾發生後再一次發生。"},{"en":"If a school power cut happened once, students may ask whether it could happen again.","zh":"如果學校曾停電一次，學生可能問它是否會再次發生。"},{"en":"Studying past disasters helps people prepare in case similar events happen again.","zh":"研究過去災難有助人們準備類似事件再次發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recurrence.","zh":"這個片語描述重現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"geological history","meaning":"地質歷史","examples":[{"en":"Similar events have happened many times in geological history.","zh":"類似事件在地質歷史中已發生多次。"},{"en":"Geological history is the long history of Earth’s rocks, volcanoes, climate, and landforms.","zh":"Geological history 是地球岩石、火山、氣候和地貌的漫長歷史。"},{"en":"A science museum may show fossils to explain geological history.","zh":"科學博物館可能展示化石來解釋地質歷史。"},{"en":"If an event appears many times in geological history, it is rare for humans but not impossible for Earth.","zh":"如果事件在地質歷史中出現多次，它對人類來說罕見，但對地球而言並非不可能。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to Earth’s deep natural past.","zh":"這個片語指地球深遠的自然過去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the most extreme case","meaning":"最極端的例子","examples":[{"en":"The most extreme case occurred about 70,000 years ago.","zh":"最極端的例子大約發生於70,000年前。"},{"en":"The most extreme case is the strongest or most severe example of a situation.","zh":"The most extreme case 是某情況中最強烈或最嚴重的例子。"},{"en":"In a class with many late students, the most extreme case may be someone who missed half the lesson.","zh":"在許多學生遲到的班上，最極端的例子可能是錯過半堂課的人。"},{"en":"If one eruption was the most extreme case, its effects were greater than all others discussed.","zh":"如果一次火山爆發是最極端例子，其影響就比其他討論例子更大。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the highest level of severity.","zh":"這個片語指出最高嚴重程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"occur about","meaning":"大約發生於","examples":[{"en":"The most extreme case occurred about 70,000 years ago.","zh":"最極端的例子大約發生於70,000年前。"},{"en":"Occur about a time means to happen approximately then.","zh":"Occur about a time 指大約在某個時間發生。"},{"en":"The school event occurred about ten years before the new building opened.","zh":"學校事件大約發生於新校舍開幕前十年。"},{"en":"If an ancient event occurred about 70,000 years ago, the date is approximate.","zh":"如果古代事件大約發生於70,000年前，日期是估計的。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an estimated time of occurrence.","zh":"這個片語給出事件發生的大約時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the world’s largest known eruption","meaning":"世界已知最大火山爆發","examples":[{"en":"The world’s largest known eruption took place at Lake Toba.","zh":"世界已知最大火山爆發發生於多巴湖。"},{"en":"The world’s largest known eruption means the biggest volcanic eruption that scientists know about.","zh":"The world’s largest known eruption 指科學家所知最大的一次火山爆發。"},{"en":"A science textbook may compare smaller eruptions with the world’s largest known eruption.","zh":"科學教科書可能把較小爆發與世界已知最大火山爆發比較。"},{"en":"If an eruption is that large, it can affect climate and life across huge areas.","zh":"如果一次火山爆發如此巨大，它可以影響大片地區的氣候和生命。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the greatest known volcanic event.","zh":"這個片語描述已知最大火山事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"take place at","meaning":"發生於","examples":[{"en":"The eruption took place at Lake Toba.","zh":"火山爆發發生於多巴湖。"},{"en":"To take place at somewhere means to happen at that location.","zh":"To take place at somewhere 指在某地發生。"},{"en":"The school concert will take place at the main hall.","zh":"學校音樂會將於禮堂舉行。"},{"en":"If an event takes place near a community, local people may be directly affected.","zh":"如果事件發生於社區附近，當地人可能直接受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where an event happens.","zh":"這個片語指出事件發生地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"Lake Toba","meaning":"多巴湖","examples":[{"en":"Lake Toba was the site of an enormous ancient eruption.","zh":"多巴湖是一場巨大古代火山爆發的地點。"},{"en":"Lake Toba is the place linked with a massive volcanic eruption in ancient history.","zh":"Lake Toba 是與古代一次巨大火山爆發相關的地方。"},{"en":"A geography teacher may use Lake Toba to explain super-eruptions.","zh":"地理老師可能用多巴湖來解釋超級火山爆發。"},{"en":"If a lake forms after a huge eruption, it may mark an old volcanic collapse.","zh":"如果湖泊在巨大爆發後形成，它可能標示舊火山塌陷。"},{"en":"This name identifies the location of the extreme ancient eruption.","zh":"這個名稱指出極端古代爆發的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"relatively close to","meaning":"相對接近……","examples":[{"en":"Lake Toba is relatively close to Tambora.","zh":"多巴湖相對接近坦博拉。"},{"en":"Relatively close to means near when compared with other possible distances.","zh":"Relatively close to 指與其他可能距離相比算是接近。"},{"en":"A school may be relatively close to a train station, even if students still need to walk ten minutes.","zh":"一間學校可能相對接近火車站，即使學生仍需步行十分鐘。"},{"en":"If two volcanic sites are relatively close, scientists may compare their geological settings.","zh":"如果兩個火山地點相對接近，科學家可能比較它們的地質環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes nearness in comparison, not necessarily next-door closeness.","zh":"這個片語描述相對上的接近，而不一定是隔壁那麼近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be thought to have","meaning":"被認為曾經……","examples":[{"en":"The eruption is thought to have triggered a volcanic winter.","zh":"這次火山爆發被認為曾經觸發火山寒冬。"},{"en":"To be thought to have done something means people believe it probably did that thing.","zh":"To be thought to have done something 指人們相信它很可能做過某事。"},{"en":"The old bridge is thought to have been built by local workers.","zh":"這座舊橋被認為曾由本地工人興建。"},{"en":"If evidence is incomplete, historians may say an event is thought to have caused a result.","zh":"如果證據不完整，歷史學家可能說某事件被認為曾造成某結果。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a careful belief rather than absolute certainty.","zh":"這個片語表達謹慎相信，而非絕對確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"plunge the planet into","meaning":"使地球陷入……","examples":[{"en":"The eruption may have plunged the planet into a volcanic winter.","zh":"火山爆發可能使地球陷入火山寒冬。"},{"en":"To plunge the planet into something means to push the whole world suddenly into a serious condition.","zh":"To plunge the planet into something 指突然把整個世界推入嚴重狀態。"},{"en":"A global financial crash can plunge many families into hardship.","zh":"全球金融崩潰可以令許多家庭陷入困境。"},{"en":"If an eruption blocks sunlight worldwide, it may plunge the planet into colder conditions.","zh":"如果火山爆發全球性阻擋陽光，它可能使地球陷入較寒冷狀況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sudden and severe shift into trouble.","zh":"這個片語描述突然且嚴重地陷入困境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"decade-long volcanic winter","meaning":"長達十年的火山寒冬","examples":[{"en":"The eruption may have caused a decade-long volcanic winter.","zh":"火山爆發可能造成長達十年的火山寒冬。"},{"en":"A decade-long volcanic winter is a volcanic winter lasting about ten years.","zh":"Decade-long volcanic winter 是持續約十年的火山寒冬。"},{"en":"A decade-long drought would change farming, water use, and daily life.","zh":"長達十年的乾旱會改變農業、用水和日常生活。"},{"en":"If volcanic cooling lasts a decade, societies may face repeated harvest failures.","zh":"如果火山降溫持續十年，社會可能面對反覆收成失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase combines duration with a severe climate condition.","zh":"這個片語把持續時間與嚴重氣候狀況結合起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"trigger the onset of","meaning":"觸發……的開始","examples":[{"en":"The eruption may have triggered the onset of the last ice age.","zh":"火山爆發可能觸發上一次冰河時期的開始。"},{"en":"To trigger the onset of something means to start the beginning of it.","zh":"To trigger the onset of something 指引發某事的開始。"},{"en":"A stressful event can trigger the onset of sleep problems.","zh":"壓力事件可以觸發睡眠問題的開始。"},{"en":"If a volcanic winter begins after an eruption, scientists may ask whether the eruption triggered it.","zh":"如果火山寒冬在爆發後開始，科學家可能問爆發是否觸發了它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes causing the start of a process.","zh":"這個片語描述造成某過程開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the last ice age","meaning":"上一次冰河時期","examples":[{"en":"The last ice age lasted many tens of thousands of years.","zh":"上一次冰河時期持續了數萬年。"},{"en":"The last ice age was a long period when large areas of Earth were much colder and covered by ice.","zh":"The last ice age 是地球大片地區更寒冷並被冰覆蓋的漫長時期。"},{"en":"Students may study the last ice age to understand climate change over deep time.","zh":"學生可能研究上一次冰河時期，以理解深遠時間尺度上的氣候變化。"},{"en":"If an ice age begins, plants, animals, and human groups must adapt or move.","zh":"如果冰河時期開始，植物、動物和人類群體必須適應或遷移。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major cold period in Earth’s past.","zh":"這個片語命名地球過去的一個重大寒冷時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a deep freeze of the planet","meaning":"地球的深度冰封期","examples":[{"en":"The last ice age was a deep freeze of the planet.","zh":"上一次冰河時期是地球的深度冰封期。"},{"en":"A deep freeze of the planet means a severe and long-lasting cooling of Earth.","zh":"Deep freeze of the planet 指地球嚴重而長時間降溫。"},{"en":"A deep freeze in a city can close schools, freeze pipes, and stop transport.","zh":"城市深度冰封可以令學校停課、水管結冰並令交通停頓。"},{"en":"If the planet enters a deep freeze, ecosystems can change dramatically.","zh":"如果地球進入深度冰封期，生態系統可以劇烈改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extreme global cold.","zh":"這個片語描述極端全球寒冷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"last many tens of thousands of years","meaning":"持續數萬年","examples":[{"en":"The deep freeze lasted many tens of thousands of years.","zh":"這段深度冰封持續數萬年。"},{"en":"To last many tens of thousands of years means to continue for a vast period of time.","zh":"To last many tens of thousands of years 指持續極其漫長的時間。"},{"en":"Some rock formations last many thousands of years because natural change is slow.","zh":"有些岩層因自然變化緩慢而持續數千年。"},{"en":"If a climate period lasts that long, it shapes evolution, migration, and landscapes.","zh":"如果氣候時期持續那麼久，它會塑造進化、遷移和地貌。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses an enormous timescale.","zh":"這個片語強調巨大的時間尺度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"some speculate","meaning":"有些人推測","examples":[{"en":"Some speculate that the eruption nearly wiped out the human race.","zh":"有些人推測這次火山爆發幾乎消滅人類。"},{"en":"Some speculate means some people suggest an idea without complete proof.","zh":"Some speculate 指有些人在沒有完整證據下提出某想法。"},{"en":"Some speculate that students learn better in the morning, but schools need evidence before changing timetables.","zh":"有些人推測學生早上學得更好，但學校改時間表前需要證據。"},{"en":"If evidence is limited, speculation should be treated carefully.","zh":"如果證據有限，推測應謹慎看待。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a possible but uncertain explanation.","zh":"這個片語引出可能但未確定的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"just about","meaning":"幾乎","examples":[{"en":"The eruption may have just about wiped out the human race.","zh":"火山爆發可能幾乎消滅人類。"},{"en":"Just about means almost or very nearly.","zh":"Just about 指幾乎或差不多。"},{"en":"I just about caught the bus because the driver was closing the doors.","zh":"我幾乎趕上巴士，因為司機正關門。"},{"en":"If a disaster just about destroys something, it leaves very little surviving.","zh":"如果災難幾乎摧毀某物，留下的倖存部分非常少。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something nearly happened completely.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事差點完全發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"wipe out the human race","meaning":"消滅人類","examples":[{"en":"The ancient eruption may have nearly wiped out the human race.","zh":"古代火山爆發可能幾乎消滅人類。"},{"en":"To wipe out the human race means to destroy all or nearly all humans.","zh":"To wipe out the human race 指消滅全部或幾乎全部人類。"},{"en":"Science-fiction films often imagine disasters that could wipe out humanity.","zh":"科幻電影常想像可能消滅人類的災難。"},{"en":"If a disaster threatens survival globally, it becomes more than a local crisis.","zh":"如果災難在全球層面威脅生存，它就不只是地方危機。"},{"en":"This phrase describes near-total destruction of humans.","zh":"這個片語描述對人類近乎完全的毀滅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"rest assured","meaning":"可以放心","examples":[{"en":"We can rest assured that such events are extremely rare.","zh":"我們可以放心，這類事件極為罕見。"},{"en":"Rest assured means feel confident and do not worry too much.","zh":"Rest assured 指可以有信心，不必太擔心。"},{"en":"Parents can rest assured that teachers will contact them if a child feels unwell.","zh":"家長可以放心，如果孩子不舒服，老師會聯絡他們。"},{"en":"If experts say an event is extremely rare, people may feel more reassured.","zh":"如果專家說某事件極為罕見，人們可能較安心。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to comfort someone with confidence.","zh":"這個片語用來以信心安慰別人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"extremely few and far between","meaning":"極為罕見","examples":[{"en":"Events of that scale are extremely few and far between.","zh":"那種規模的事件極為罕見。"},{"en":"Extremely few and far between means very rare and not happening often.","zh":"Extremely few and far between 指非常罕見且不常發生。"},{"en":"Truly free parking spaces in a busy city are few and far between.","zh":"在繁忙城市中，真正免費泊車位非常罕見。"},{"en":"If disasters of that scale are rare, most generations will never experience one.","zh":"如果那種規模的災難很罕見，大多數世代都不會經歷。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises rarity.","zh":"這個片語強烈強調罕見性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"for a long time to come","meaning":"在未來很長一段時間內","examples":[{"en":"People can enjoy summer holidays for a long time to come.","zh":"人們在未來很長一段時間內都可以享受暑假。"},{"en":"For a long time to come means for many years into the future.","zh":"For a long time to come 指未來很多年。"},{"en":"A well-built bridge can serve a community for a long time to come.","zh":"一座建得好的橋可以在未來很長一段時間內服務社區。"},{"en":"If extreme eruptions are rare, ordinary summers should continue for many years.","zh":"如果極端火山爆發罕見，普通夏天應會持續很多年。"},{"en":"This phrase looks forward over a long future period.","zh":"這個片語展望未來一段很長時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the flowchart","meaning":"完成流程圖","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the flowchart using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成流程圖。"},{"en":"To complete the flowchart means to fill missing steps in a diagram showing a process.","zh":"To complete the flowchart 指填補展示過程的圖表中的缺失步驟。"},{"en":"Students may complete a flowchart about how rainwater becomes drinking water.","zh":"學生可能完成一張關於雨水如何變成食水的流程圖。"},{"en":"If one step is wrong, the whole sequence may become confusing.","zh":"如果一步錯了，整個先後次序可能變得混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common reading-task instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見閱讀題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個詞","examples":[{"en":"The instructions say to choose no more than three words.","zh":"指示說選擇不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"No more than three words 指答案必須包含三個或更少英文單詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “volcanic dust,” it uses two words and fits the rule.","zh":"如果答案是 “volcanic dust”，它用了兩個詞，符合規則。"},{"en":"If students write four words, the answer may be marked wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"如果學生寫四個詞，即使意思正確，也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個片語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose from the passage","meaning":"從文章中選取","examples":[{"en":"Students choose answers from the passage.","zh":"學生從文章中選取答案。"},{"en":"To choose from the passage means to take the answer words directly from the reading text.","zh":"To choose from the passage 指直接從閱讀文章中選取答案字詞。"},{"en":"In a gap-fill task, students should copy words from the passage accurately.","zh":"在填空題中，學生應準確抄寫文章中的字詞。"},{"en":"If students use their own words when the task requires text words, they may lose marks.","zh":"如果題目要求使用文章字詞，而學生用自己的字，可能會失分。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds learners to rely on the source text.","zh":"這個片語提醒學習者依賴原文。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"answer the questions","meaning":"回答問題","examples":[{"en":"Students answer the questions by matching locations with events.","zh":"學生透過把地點與事件配對來回答問題。"},{"en":"To answer the questions means to provide the required responses to the task items.","zh":"To answer the questions 指為題目項目提供所需答案。"},{"en":"Students should read the instructions before they answer the questions.","zh":"學生回答問題前應先閱讀指示。"},{"en":"If they answer before checking evidence, they may choose a tempting wrong option.","zh":"如果未檢查證據就作答，他們可能選到有吸引力但錯誤的選項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the basic task of responding correctly.","zh":"這個片語描述正確回應題目的基本任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"write the correct letter next to","meaning":"在……旁寫上正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students write the correct letter next to each question.","zh":"學生在每條問題旁寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"To write the correct letter next to something means to place the matching answer letter beside that item.","zh":"To write the correct letter next to something 指把配對答案字母寫在該項旁邊。"},{"en":"If the answer to Question 3 is B, students write B next to Question 3.","zh":"如果第3題答案是B，學生就在第3題旁寫B。"},{"en":"If letters are placed beside the wrong questions, correct thinking may still lose marks.","zh":"如果字母寫在錯誤問題旁，即使思路正確也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in matching tasks.","zh":"這個片語用於配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"which location saw","meaning":"哪個地點見證了……","examples":[{"en":"The task asks which location saw each event.","zh":"題目問哪個地點見證了每件事件。"},{"en":"Which location saw an event means which place experienced or was linked to that event.","zh":"Which location saw an event 指哪個地方經歷或與該事件有關。"},{"en":"A history quiz may ask which city saw the first protest.","zh":"歷史小測可能問哪個城市見證了第一次抗議。"},{"en":"If several places are mentioned, students must match each event to the right location.","zh":"如果提到幾個地方，學生必須把每件事件配對到正確地點。"},{"en":"This phrase asks students to identify the place connected with an event.","zh":"這個片語要求學生識別與事件相關的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a positive effect of","meaning":"……的正面影響","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about a positive effect of a volcanic eruption.","zh":"題目問火山爆發的一個正面影響。"},{"en":"A positive effect of something is a good or beneficial result caused by it.","zh":"Positive effect of something 是由某事造成的好或有益結果。"},{"en":"A positive effect of walking to school is that students get more exercise.","zh":"步行上學的一個正面影響是學生得到更多運動。"},{"en":"Even harmful events can sometimes have one small positive effect.","zh":"即使有害事件有時也可能有一個小的正面影響。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for a good consequence, not the main damage.","zh":"這個片語問的是好後果，而不是主要損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"volcanic eruption","meaning":"火山爆發","examples":[{"en":"A volcanic eruption can affect weather around the world.","zh":"火山爆發可以影響世界各地的天氣。"},{"en":"A volcanic eruption happens when lava, ash, gas, or rock bursts out from a volcano.","zh":"Volcanic eruption 是熔岩、火山灰、氣體或岩石從火山爆出。"},{"en":"People living near a volcano may practise evacuation drills in case of eruption.","zh":"住在火山附近的人可能練習疏散演習，以防火山爆發。"},{"en":"If volcanic ash reaches the atmosphere, it can affect sunlight and air travel.","zh":"如果火山灰到達大氣層，它可以影響陽光和航空交通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the active release of material from a volcano.","zh":"這個片語描述物質從火山主動釋放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the biggest volcanic eruption","meaning":"最大型火山爆發","examples":[{"en":"The biggest volcanic eruption mentioned was connected with Lake Toba.","zh":"文中提到的最大型火山爆發與多巴湖有關。"},{"en":"The biggest volcanic eruption means the largest eruption among the examples discussed.","zh":"The biggest volcanic eruption 指所討論例子中規模最大的爆發。"},{"en":"A science worksheet may ask students to identify the biggest volcanic eruption in a passage.","zh":"科學工作紙可能要求學生找出文章中的最大型火山爆發。"},{"en":"If an eruption is the biggest, it may have the widest climate impact.","zh":"如果一次火山爆發最大，它可能有最廣泛的氣候影響。"},{"en":"This phrase compares eruption size.","zh":"這個片語比較火山爆發規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"scientific observation","meaning":"科學觀察","examples":[{"en":"Scientific observation helped identify reduced solar activity.","zh":"科學觀察幫助識別太陽活動減弱。"},{"en":"Scientific observation means carefully watching, measuring, and recording facts for study.","zh":"Scientific observation 指為研究而仔細觀察、量度和記錄事實。"},{"en":"Students practise scientific observation when they record plant growth every day.","zh":"學生每天記錄植物生長，就是在練習科學觀察。"},{"en":"If observations are repeated carefully, they can support a scientific explanation.","zh":"如果觀察被仔細重複，它們可以支持科學解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence gathered by watching and measuring.","zh":"這個片語描述透過觀察和量度收集的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a series of eruptions","meaning":"一連串火山爆發","examples":[{"en":"A series of eruptions occurred before the Tambora event.","zh":"坦博拉事件之前發生了一連串火山爆發。"},{"en":"A series of eruptions means several volcanic eruptions happening over a period of time.","zh":"A series of eruptions 指一段時間內發生幾次火山爆發。"},{"en":"A series of small earthquakes may warn people that a larger event is possible.","zh":"一連串小地震可能警告人們較大事件有可能發生。"},{"en":"If eruptions happen repeatedly, ash can build up in the atmosphere.","zh":"如果火山反覆爆發，火山灰可以在大氣中累積。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses repeated events rather than a single eruption.","zh":"這個片語強調重複事件，而不是單一爆發。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"buildings destroyed","meaning":"建築物被摧毀","examples":[{"en":"Buildings were destroyed when whole towns and villages were buried.","zh":"當整個城鎮和村莊被掩埋時，建築物被摧毀。"},{"en":"Buildings destroyed means homes, shops, or other structures were badly damaged or ruined.","zh":"Buildings destroyed 指房屋、商店或其他結構嚴重受損或毀壞。"},{"en":"A strong typhoon may leave many buildings destroyed along the coast.","zh":"強烈颱風可能令沿岸許多建築物被摧毀。"},{"en":"If buildings are destroyed, people may lose shelter, schools, and workplaces.","zh":"如果建築物被摧毀，人們可能失去住所、學校和工作場所。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severe physical damage to structures.","zh":"這個片語描述建築結構受到嚴重實體破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a book written","meaning":"一本書被寫成","examples":[{"en":"A book may have been written partly because of the gloomy weather.","zh":"一本書可能部分因陰鬱天氣而被寫成。"},{"en":"A book written means a literary work that was created or composed by an author.","zh":"A book written 指由作者創作或寫成的文學作品。"},{"en":"A book written during wartime may reflect fear, loss, and uncertainty.","zh":"戰時寫成的書可能反映恐懼、失去和不確定。"},{"en":"If weather shapes a writer’s mood, it may influence the book they write.","zh":"如果天氣塑造作家心情，它可能影響他所寫的書。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a completed written work and its possible background.","zh":"這個片語指完成的書面作品及其可能背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"America","meaning":"美國","examples":[{"en":"America experienced snow and intense cold in midsummer.","zh":"美國在盛夏經歷下雪和嚴寒。"},{"en":"America here refers to the parts of the United States affected by the abnormal weather.","zh":"America 在此指受異常天氣影響的美國部分地區。"},{"en":"A history passage may use America to discuss weather effects in New England and nearby regions.","zh":"歷史文章可能用 America 來討論新英格蘭及附近地區的天氣影響。"},{"en":"If America experienced snow in summer, the climate event was clearly unusual.","zh":"如果美國夏天下雪，該氣候事件明顯不尋常。"},{"en":"This word names one major region affected by the year without a summer.","zh":"這個詞命名無夏之年受影響的主要地區之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"Switzerland","meaning":"瑞士","examples":[{"en":"Mary Shelley was holidaying in Switzerland during the rainy period.","zh":"Mary Shelley 在多雨時期正在瑞士旅行。"},{"en":"Switzerland is a European country where Mary Shelley experienced gloomy summer weather.","zh":"Switzerland 是 Mary Shelley 經歷陰鬱夏季天氣的歐洲國家。"},{"en":"Travellers may visit Switzerland for lakes, mountains, and fresh air.","zh":"旅客可能到瑞士欣賞湖泊、山脈和清新空氣。"},{"en":"If constant rain traps visitors indoors, it can change the mood of a holiday.","zh":"如果連場大雨令旅客困在室內，它可以改變假期氣氛。"},{"en":"This place is linked in the passage with Shelley and Frankenstein.","zh":"這個地方在文章中與 Shelley 和《科學怪人》有關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"London","meaning":"倫敦","examples":[{"en":"John Dalton was a London-based meteorologist.","zh":"John Dalton 是駐倫敦的氣象學家。"},{"en":"London is the city where Dalton was based when he made weather-related observations.","zh":"London 是 Dalton 作出天氣相關觀察時所在的城市。"},{"en":"A scientist based in London may still study events affecting the wider world.","zh":"駐倫敦的科學家仍可能研究影響更廣泛世界的事件。"},{"en":"If observations made in London reveal fewer sunspots, they can help explain climate discussion.","zh":"如果在倫敦作出的觀察顯示太陽黑子較少，它們可以幫助解釋氣候討論。"},{"en":"This place is connected with scientific observation in the passage.","zh":"這個地方在文章中與科學觀察有關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"Tambora","meaning":"坦博拉","examples":[{"en":"Tambora was the volcano whose eruption helped cause the year without a summer.","zh":"坦博拉是其爆發幫助造成無夏之年的火山。"},{"en":"Tambora refers to Mount Tambora, the Indonesian volcano central to the passage.","zh":"Tambora 指坦博拉火山，即文章中的核心印尼火山。"},{"en":"Students may remember Tambora as the volcano linked with 1816’s abnormal cold.","zh":"學生可能記得坦博拉是與1816年異常寒冷相關的火山。"},{"en":"If Tambora sent ash into the stratosphere, global sunlight and temperature could be affected.","zh":"如果坦博拉把火山灰送入平流層，全球陽光和氣溫都可能受影響。"},{"en":"This name points to the main volcanic cause discussed.","zh":"這個名稱指文中討論的主要火山成因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the largest eruption","meaning":"最大規模的爆發","examples":[{"en":"The Tambora eruption was acknowledged as the largest in recorded history.","zh":"坦博拉火山爆發被承認為有紀錄以來最大規模的爆發。"},{"en":"The largest eruption means the biggest volcanic eruption in the comparison being made.","zh":"The largest eruption 指比較中規模最大的火山爆發。"},{"en":"A science chart may show the largest eruption at the top of a list.","zh":"科學圖表可能把最大規模的爆發列在清單頂端。"},{"en":"If an eruption is the largest recorded, its effects may be global rather than local.","zh":"如果一次爆發是有紀錄以來最大，它的影響可能是全球性而非地方性。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on eruption scale.","zh":"這個片語集中於爆發規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"Mount Tambora in Indonesia","meaning":"印尼坦博拉火山","examples":[{"en":"Mount Tambora in Indonesia was the main culprit behind the abnormal weather.","zh":"印尼坦博拉火山是異常天氣背後的主要元兇。"},{"en":"Mount Tambora in Indonesia identifies the exact volcano and country linked to the disaster.","zh":"Mount Tambora in Indonesia 指與災難相關的確切火山和國家。"},{"en":"A map can help students locate Mount Tambora in Indonesia before reading the passage.","zh":"閱讀文章前，地圖可以幫助學生找出印尼坦博拉火山的位置。"},{"en":"If a volcano in Indonesia affects Europe and America, the event must have been enormous.","zh":"如果印尼一座火山影響歐洲和美國，該事件必定非常巨大。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the specific location of the main cause.","zh":"這個片語給出主因的具體地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"book written in gloomy conditions","meaning":"在陰鬱天氣下寫成的書","examples":[{"en":"Frankenstein was written after Shelley experienced gloomy weather in Switzerland.","zh":"《科學怪人》是在 Shelley 於瑞士經歷陰鬱天氣後寫成的。"},{"en":"A book written in gloomy conditions is a work created during dark, rainy, or depressing circumstances.","zh":"Book written in gloomy conditions 是在陰暗、多雨或令人低落的情況下創作的作品。"},{"en":"A diary written in gloomy conditions may describe loneliness, bad weather, and fear.","zh":"在陰鬱環境下寫成的日記，可能描述孤獨、壞天氣和恐懼。"},{"en":"If conditions affect a writer’s mood, they may influence the atmosphere of the book.","zh":"如果環境影響作家心情，它們可能影響作品氣氛。"},{"en":"This phrase connects writing with the emotional setting around it.","zh":"這個片語把寫作與周圍的情緒環境連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"location matching task","meaning":"地點配對題","examples":[{"en":"The location matching task asks students to connect places with events.","zh":"地點配對題要求學生把地方與事件連接起來。"},{"en":"A location matching task is an exercise where learners match each event to the correct place.","zh":"Location matching task 是學習者把每件事件配對到正確地點的練習。"},{"en":"Students may match “Switzerland” with Mary Shelley and “London” with John Dalton.","zh":"學生可能把「瑞士」配對 Mary Shelley，把「倫敦」配對 John Dalton。"},{"en":"If a passage mentions many places, matching locations helps test careful reading.","zh":"如果文章提到許多地方，地點配對有助測試仔細閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reading question type based on places.","zh":"這個片語描述以地點為基礎的閱讀題型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"positive effect","meaning":"正面影響","examples":[{"en":"The colourful sunsets were a positive effect of airborne ash.","zh":"彩色日落是空氣中火山灰的一個正面影響。"},{"en":"A positive effect is a good result caused by something.","zh":"Positive effect 是由某事造成的好結果。"},{"en":"A positive effect of walking more is better physical health.","zh":"多步行的一個正面影響是身體更健康。"},{"en":"If a harmful event has one positive effect, that does not erase the damage.","zh":"如果有害事件有一個正面影響，那也不會抹去損害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a beneficial consequence.","zh":"這個片語描述有益後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"buildings destroyed by eruption","meaning":"被火山爆發摧毀的建築物","examples":[{"en":"The eruption destroyed buildings by burying whole towns and villages.","zh":"火山爆發透過掩埋整個城鎮和村莊摧毀建築物。"},{"en":"Buildings destroyed by eruption are structures ruined by lava, ash, rock, or volcanic force.","zh":"Buildings destroyed by eruption 是被熔岩、火山灰、岩石或火山力量摧毀的建築。"},{"en":"Homes near a volcano may be destroyed if ash and rock cover the area.","zh":"火山附近的房屋如果被火山灰和岩石覆蓋，可能被摧毀。"},{"en":"If buildings are destroyed, survivors need shelter, water, and medical help.","zh":"如果建築物被摧毀，生還者需要住所、水和醫療協助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical destruction caused by volcanic activity.","zh":"這個片語描述由火山活動造成的實體破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"scientific observation of sunspots","meaning":"對太陽黑子作出的科學觀察","examples":[{"en":"Dalton made scientific observations of sunspots and solar flares.","zh":"Dalton 對太陽黑子和太陽耀斑作出科學觀察。"},{"en":"Scientific observation of sunspots means carefully recording dark marks on the sun to study solar activity.","zh":"Scientific observation of sunspots 指仔細記錄太陽上的暗斑，以研究太陽活動。"},{"en":"Students can observe sunspots safely only with proper equipment and teacher guidance.","zh":"學生只有在有適當設備和老師指導下，才能安全觀察太陽黑子。"},{"en":"If sunspot numbers change, scientists may compare them with climate records.","zh":"如果太陽黑子數量改變，科學家可能把它們與氣候紀錄比較。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a careful study of visible solar features.","zh":"這個片語描述對可見太陽特徵的仔細研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"volcanic activity","meaning":"火山活動","examples":[{"en":"Volcanic activity before Tambora helped cool the globe.","zh":"坦博拉之前的火山活動幫助令全球降溫。"},{"en":"Volcanic activity refers to eruptions, gas release, tremors, and other signs of an active volcano.","zh":"Volcanic activity 指火山爆發、氣體釋放、震動和其他活火山跡象。"},{"en":"Scientists monitor volcanic activity to warn people before dangerous eruptions.","zh":"科學家監測火山活動，以在危險爆發前警告人們。"},{"en":"If volcanic activity increases, nearby communities may prepare to evacuate.","zh":"如果火山活動增加，附近社區可能準備疏散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes processes showing that a volcano is active.","zh":"這個片語描述顯示火山活躍的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"recorded history","meaning":"有紀錄以來的歷史","examples":[{"en":"The eruption was the largest in recorded history.","zh":"這次爆發是有紀錄以來最大的一次。"},{"en":"Recorded history means the period of the past for which written records exist.","zh":"Recorded history 指有文字記錄存在的過去時期。"},{"en":"A city may call a storm the worst in recorded history if old documents show no stronger one.","zh":"如果舊文件沒有顯示更強風暴，城市可能稱某風暴為有紀錄以來最嚴重。"},{"en":"If an event is unique in recorded history, it stands out in human records.","zh":"如果某事件在有紀錄以來的歷史中獨一無二，它就在人類紀錄中十分突出。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to history documented by people.","zh":"這個片語指由人記錄下來的歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"global climate effects","meaning":"全球氣候影響","examples":[{"en":"The eruption produced global climate effects.","zh":"火山爆發產生全球氣候影響。"},{"en":"Global climate effects are changes in weather or temperature that affect the whole world or many regions.","zh":"Global climate effects 是影響全世界或許多地區的天氣或氣溫變化。"},{"en":"A major change in ocean temperature can produce global climate effects.","zh":"海洋溫度重大變化可以產生全球氣候影響。"},{"en":"If volcanic dust blocks sunlight worldwide, global climate effects may follow.","zh":"如果火山塵在全球阻擋陽光，全球氣候影響可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes climate impact beyond one local area.","zh":"這個片語描述超出單一本地地區的氣候影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"atmospheric dust","meaning":"大氣塵埃","examples":[{"en":"Atmospheric dust can reduce sunlight and cool the planet.","zh":"大氣塵埃可以減少陽光並令地球降溫。"},{"en":"Atmospheric dust is fine dust floating in the air around Earth.","zh":"Atmospheric dust 是漂浮在地球周圍空氣中的細小塵埃。"},{"en":"After a dust storm, atmospheric dust may make the sky look pale or hazy.","zh":"沙塵暴後，大氣塵埃可能令天空看起來蒼白或朦朧。"},{"en":"If atmospheric dust reflects sunlight, less heat reaches the ground.","zh":"如果大氣塵埃反射陽光，較少熱量會到達地面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dust suspended in the atmosphere.","zh":"這個片語描述懸浮於大氣中的塵埃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"lower global temperatures","meaning":"較低的全球氣溫","examples":[{"en":"Lower global temperatures helped create the year without a summer.","zh":"較低的全球氣溫幫助造成無夏之年。"},{"en":"Lower global temperatures mean average temperatures around the world are reduced.","zh":"Lower global temperatures 指世界各地平均氣溫降低。"},{"en":"Lower global temperatures can shorten growing seasons in farming regions.","zh":"較低的全球氣溫可以縮短農業地區的生長季節。"},{"en":"If the whole planet cools, even distant countries may experience unusual weather.","zh":"如果整個地球降溫，即使遙遠國家也可能經歷異常天氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes worldwide cooling.","zh":"這個片語描述全球降溫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"crop failure","meaning":"農作物歉收","examples":[{"en":"Crop failure led to famine and social disorder.","zh":"農作物歉收導致饑荒和社會混亂。"},{"en":"Crop failure happens when crops do not grow or cannot be harvested successfully.","zh":"Crop failure 指農作物未能生長或未能成功收割。"},{"en":"A farmer may face crop failure if rain destroys the fields before harvest.","zh":"如果雨水在收割前破壞田地，農民可能面對農作物歉收。"},{"en":"If crop failure affects staple foods, hunger can spread quickly.","zh":"如果主糧作物歉收，饑餓可以迅速蔓延。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious farming loss.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重農業損失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"emergency distribution","meaning":"緊急物資分發","examples":[{"en":"Emergency distribution of food was difficult because of poor roads.","zh":"由於道路差，糧食緊急分發很困難。"},{"en":"Emergency distribution is the urgent delivery of supplies to people in crisis.","zh":"Emergency distribution 是向危機中的人緊急運送物資。"},{"en":"After a flood, emergency distribution may include food, blankets, and medicine.","zh":"水災後，緊急物資分發可能包括食物、毛氈和藥物。"},{"en":"If roads are blocked, emergency distribution becomes slow and uneven.","zh":"如果道路被堵塞，緊急分發會變慢且不平均。"},{"en":"This phrase describes urgent supply delivery during disasters.","zh":"這個片語描述災難期間的緊急物資運送。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"civic disorder","meaning":"公共秩序混亂","examples":[{"en":"Food shortages led to civic disorder.","zh":"糧食短缺導致公共秩序混亂。"},{"en":"Civic disorder means public unrest when normal social order breaks down.","zh":"Civic disorder 指正常社會秩序崩潰時出現的公共動盪。"},{"en":"A city may face civic disorder if people cannot buy basic food for weeks.","zh":"如果人們連續數星期買不到基本食物，城市可能面對公共秩序混亂。"},{"en":"If hunger, fear, and anger grow together, public order may collapse.","zh":"如果饑餓、恐懼和憤怒一起增加，公共秩序可能崩潰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disorder in community life.","zh":"這個片語描述社區生活中的混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"volcanic winter conditions","meaning":"火山寒冬狀況","examples":[{"en":"Volcanic winter conditions can last for years after a major eruption.","zh":"重大火山爆發後，火山寒冬狀況可以持續多年。"},{"en":"Volcanic winter conditions are cold, dark, and abnormal weather patterns caused by volcanic material in the atmosphere.","zh":"Volcanic winter conditions 是由大氣中火山物質造成的寒冷、陰暗和異常天氣模式。"},{"en":"Farmers may struggle under volcanic winter conditions because crops receive too little sunlight.","zh":"在火山寒冬狀況下，農民可能困難重重，因為作物得到太少陽光。"},{"en":"If these conditions last long, food production and health may suffer.","zh":"如果這些狀況持續很久，糧食生產和健康可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the climate situation after severe volcanic cooling.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重火山降溫後的氣候情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"unusually cold period","meaning":"異常寒冷時期","examples":[{"en":"The Dalton Minimum was an unusually cold period.","zh":"道爾頓極小期是一段異常寒冷時期。"},{"en":"An unusually cold period is a time when temperatures are much lower than normal.","zh":"Unusually cold period 是氣溫遠低於正常水平的一段時間。"},{"en":"An unusually cold period in spring can delay flowers and fruit growth.","zh":"春季異常寒冷時期可以延遲開花和水果生長。"},{"en":"If a cold period lasts for years, it can affect farming and health.","zh":"如果寒冷時期持續多年，它可以影響農業和健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weather that is colder than expected for a period of time.","zh":"這個片語描述某段時間比預期寒冷的天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"reduced solar activity","meaning":"太陽活動減弱","examples":[{"en":"Reduced solar activity may have contributed to colder global temperatures.","zh":"太陽活動減弱可能促成較低的全球氣溫。"},{"en":"Reduced solar activity means the sun is showing lower levels of activity than usual.","zh":"Reduced solar activity 指太陽活動水平低於平常。"},{"en":"Scientists may study reduced solar activity by counting sunspots.","zh":"科學家可能透過計算太陽黑子來研究太陽活動減弱。"},{"en":"If solar activity decreases, researchers may ask whether less solar energy reaches Earth.","zh":"如果太陽活動下降，研究人員可能問是否較少太陽能到達地球。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a quieter period in the sun’s behaviour.","zh":"這個片語描述太陽行為較安靜的時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"massive ash clouds","meaning":"巨大的火山灰雲","examples":[{"en":"Massive ash clouds from eruptions affected the atmosphere.","zh":"火山爆發產生的巨大火山灰雲影響了大氣。"},{"en":"Massive ash clouds are huge clouds of volcanic ash thrown into the air.","zh":"Massive ash clouds 是被拋入空中的巨大火山灰雲。"},{"en":"Massive ash clouds can close airports because aircraft engines may be damaged.","zh":"巨大的火山灰雲可以令機場關閉，因為飛機引擎可能受損。"},{"en":"If ash clouds spread widely, sunlight and visibility can both decrease.","zh":"如果火山灰雲廣泛擴散，陽光和能見度都可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very large volcanic ash formations in the sky.","zh":"這個片語描述天空中非常巨大的火山灰形成物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"historic accumulation","meaning":"歷史性的灰塵積聚","examples":[{"en":"The historic accumulation of ash worsened global cooling.","zh":"歷史性的火山灰積聚加劇了全球降溫。"},{"en":"Historic accumulation means a build-up that reaches an unusually high level in history.","zh":"Historic accumulation 指累積量達到歷史上異常高水平。"},{"en":"A historic accumulation of snow can block roads and close schools for days.","zh":"歷史性的積雪可以阻塞道路並令學校停課數日。"},{"en":"If ash accumulation becomes historic, the climate effects may be unusually strong.","zh":"如果火山灰積聚達歷史水平，氣候影響可能異常強烈。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a record-level build-up over time.","zh":"這個片語描述隨時間形成的紀錄級累積。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"global cooling","meaning":"全球降溫","examples":[{"en":"Global cooling followed the accumulation of volcanic ash.","zh":"火山灰積聚後出現全球降溫。"},{"en":"Global cooling means average temperatures around the world become lower.","zh":"Global cooling 指全球平均氣溫下降。"},{"en":"Global cooling can shorten growing seasons and increase heating needs.","zh":"全球降溫可以縮短生長季節並增加取暖需求。"},{"en":"If volcanic dust reflects sunlight, global cooling may follow.","zh":"如果火山塵反射陽光，全球降溫可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a worldwide drop in temperature.","zh":"這個片語描述全球氣溫下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"food crisis","meaning":"糧食危機","examples":[{"en":"The weather disaster created a serious food crisis.","zh":"天氣災難造成嚴重糧食危機。"},{"en":"A food crisis is a situation where people cannot get enough food safely or affordably.","zh":"Food crisis 是人們無法安全或負擔得起地取得足夠食物的情況。"},{"en":"A food crisis may occur after drought, war, floods, or crop failure.","zh":"糧食危機可能在乾旱、戰爭、水災或農作物歉收後出現。"},{"en":"If food prices rise and supplies fall, families may skip meals.","zh":"如果食物價格上升而供應下降，家庭可能減少用餐。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious shortage or access problem involving food.","zh":"這個片語描述涉及食物的嚴重短缺或取得問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"population displacement","meaning":"人口流離失所","examples":[{"en":"The famine caused population displacement across affected areas.","zh":"饑荒在受影響地區造成人口流離失所。"},{"en":"Population displacement means people are forced to leave their homes and move elsewhere.","zh":"Population displacement 指人們被迫離開家園並遷往其他地方。"},{"en":"Flooding can cause population displacement if homes become unsafe.","zh":"如果房屋變得不安全，水災可以造成人口流離失所。"},{"en":"If people cannot find food locally, they may move to other regions for survival.","zh":"如果人們在本地找不到食物，他們可能為生存遷往其他地區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes forced movement of communities.","zh":"這個片語描述社區被迫遷移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"extreme volcanic event","meaning":"極端火山事件","examples":[{"en":"An extreme volcanic event can change climate for years.","zh":"極端火山事件可以改變氣候多年。"},{"en":"An extreme volcanic event is a very large or powerful eruption with serious effects.","zh":"Extreme volcanic event 是具有嚴重影響的非常大型或強力火山爆發。"},{"en":"Emergency planners may prepare for extreme volcanic events in high-risk regions.","zh":"應急規劃人員可能在高風險地區準備應對極端火山事件。"},{"en":"If an event sends huge ash clouds into the atmosphere, weather may change far away.","zh":"如果事件把巨大火山灰雲送入大氣，遙遠地方的天氣可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a volcanic event beyond ordinary scale.","zh":"這個片語描述超出普通規模的火山事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"ancient eruption","meaning":"古代火山爆發","examples":[{"en":"The ancient eruption at Lake Toba may have nearly destroyed humanity.","zh":"多巴湖的古代火山爆發可能幾乎毀滅人類。"},{"en":"An ancient eruption is a volcanic eruption that happened in the very distant past.","zh":"Ancient eruption 是發生在非常遙遠過去的火山爆發。"},{"en":"Scientists study ancient eruptions by examining rocks, ash layers, and lake deposits.","zh":"科學家透過研究岩石、火山灰層和湖泊沉積物來研究古代火山爆發。"},{"en":"If an ancient eruption left thick ash layers, researchers can reconstruct its size.","zh":"如果古代火山爆發留下厚火山灰層，研究人員可以重建其規模。"},{"en":"This phrase connects volcanic history with deep time.","zh":"這個片語把火山歷史與深遠時間連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"long-term climatic impact","meaning":"長期氣候影響","examples":[{"en":"Major eruptions can have long-term climatic impact.","zh":"重大火山爆發可以有長期氣候影響。"},{"en":"Long-term climatic impact means effects on climate that last for years or longer.","zh":"Long-term climatic impact 指持續多年或更久的氣候影響。"},{"en":"Deforestation can have long-term climatic impact by changing rainfall and temperature patterns.","zh":"砍伐森林可以透過改變降雨和氣溫模式造成長期氣候影響。"},{"en":"If volcanic dust stays in the atmosphere, its climatic impact may continue after the eruption ends.","zh":"如果火山塵停留在大氣中，其氣候影響可能在火山爆發結束後仍繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lasting effects on climate.","zh":"這個片語描述對氣候的持久影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 92 - The Year Without a Summer.pdf","sourcePage":22}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 93":[{"front":"Cubism","meaning":"立體主義","examples":[{"en":"Cubism is a revolutionary art movement associated with Picasso and Braque.","zh":"立體主義是一場與 Picasso 和 Braque 相關的革命性藝術運動。"},{"en":"Cubism is an art style that shows objects from several viewpoints at once.","zh":"立體主義是一種同時從多個視角呈現物件的藝術風格。"},{"en":"A Cubism lesson may ask students to draw a face from the front and side together.","zh":"立體主義課堂可能要求學生同時畫出一張臉的正面和側面。"},{"en":"Because Cubism breaks normal perspective, its paintings can look fragmented at first.","zh":"因為立體主義打破正常透視，其畫作起初可能看起來支離破碎。"},{"en":"Cubism changed modern art by challenging the idea that pictures must copy reality.","zh":"立體主義透過挑戰圖畫必須複製現實這個想法，改變了現代藝術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"when someone’s name is mentioned","meaning":"當提到某人的名字時","examples":[{"en":"When Picasso’s name is mentioned, Cubism usually springs to mind.","zh":"當提到 Picasso 的名字時，立體主義通常會浮現在腦海中。"},{"en":"When someone’s name is mentioned means when people hear or refer to that person’s name.","zh":"when someone’s name is mentioned 指當人們聽到或提及某人的名字時。"},{"en":"When Einstein’s name is mentioned, many students think of science and genius.","zh":"當提到 Einstein 的名字時，許多學生會想到科學和天才。"},{"en":"A famous person’s name often brings a related idea to mind immediately.","zh":"名人名字常會立即帶出一個相關想法。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the moment a name triggers an association.","zh":"這個短語引出名字觸發聯想的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"spring to mind","meaning":"浮現在腦海中","examples":[{"en":"The concept of Cubism usually springs to mind when people hear Picasso’s name.","zh":"當人們聽到 Picasso 的名字，立體主義這個概念通常會浮現在腦海中。"},{"en":"To spring to mind means to appear suddenly in one’s thoughts.","zh":"spring to mind 指突然出現在腦海中。"},{"en":"When students hear “homework”, deadlines may spring to mind.","zh":"當學生聽到 “homework”，截止日期可能會浮現在腦海中。"},{"en":"Strong associations make certain ideas spring to mind very quickly.","zh":"強烈聯想會令某些想法很快浮現在腦海中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an immediate mental connection.","zh":"這個短語描述即時的心理聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"this indicates just how","meaning":"這正顯示……有多麼","examples":[{"en":"This indicates just how deep Cubism’s influence has been.","zh":"這正顯示立體主義的影響有多麼深遠。"},{"en":"This indicates just how means this clearly shows the degree or extent of something.","zh":"this indicates just how 指這清楚顯示某事的程度或範圍。"},{"en":"If every student remembers one teacher’s advice, this indicates just how powerful the advice was.","zh":"如果每個學生都記得一位老師的建議，這正顯示該建議有多麼有力。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when evidence reveals something strongly.","zh":"當證據強烈揭示某事時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It often prepares the reader for an explanation of importance or scale.","zh":"它常為讀者準備好理解某事的重要性或規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"deep and long-lasting influence","meaning":"深遠而持久的影響","examples":[{"en":"Cubism has had a deep and long-lasting influence on the art world.","zh":"立體主義對藝術世界有深遠而持久的影響。"},{"en":"A deep and long-lasting influence is an effect that is strong and continues for many years.","zh":"deep and long-lasting influence 是強烈並持續多年的影響。"},{"en":"A good primary-school teacher can have a deep and long-lasting influence on a child’s confidence.","zh":"好的小學老師可以對孩子信心有深遠而持久的影響。"},{"en":"Such influence remains visible when later people still follow or react to the original idea.","zh":"當後來的人仍跟隨或回應原本想法，這種影響仍然可見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes impact that is both powerful and enduring.","zh":"這個短語描述既強大又持久的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"influence on","meaning":"對……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Cubism has had a major influence on the world of art.","zh":"立體主義對藝術世界有重大影響。"},{"en":"Influence on something means the effect one thing has on another.","zh":"influence on 某事，指一件事對另一件事的效果。"},{"en":"Parents can have a strong influence on a child’s study habits.","zh":"父母可以對孩子的學習習慣有強烈影響。"},{"en":"An influence on a field can change how people work, think or create.","zh":"對某領域的影響可以改變人們工作、思考或創作的方式。"},{"en":"The phrase links a cause with the area it affects.","zh":"這個短語把原因與其影響範圍連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"yet although","meaning":"然而雖然","examples":[{"en":"Yet although many people know the name Cubism, few can explain it clearly.","zh":"然而雖然許多人知道立體主義這個名稱，卻很少人能清楚解釋它。"},{"en":"Yet although introduces a contrast between what seems true and what is also true.","zh":"yet although 引出看似成立的事與另一同時成立的事之間的對比。"},{"en":"Yet although many students know the word “grammar”, few can explain every rule.","zh":"然而雖然許多學生知道 “grammar” 這個詞，卻很少人能解釋每條規則。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that recognition does not always mean understanding.","zh":"這個短語顯示認得某事不一定代表理解。"},{"en":"It is useful when correcting a simple assumption.","zh":"它適合用來修正簡單假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"with any degree of familiarity","meaning":"帶有任何程度的熟悉","examples":[{"en":"Few people can speak about Cubism with any degree of familiarity.","zh":"很少人能帶有任何程度的熟悉去談論立體主義。"},{"en":"With any degree of familiarity means with even a small amount of real knowledge.","zh":"with any degree of familiarity 指帶有哪怕少量真正認識。"},{"en":"A student may know a composer’s name but cannot discuss his music with any degree of familiarity.","zh":"學生可能知道一位作曲家的名字，但不能帶有任何熟悉程度談論他的音樂。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that surface recognition is not enough.","zh":"這個短語暗示表面認識並不足夠。"},{"en":"It is often used to show limited understanding.","zh":"它常用來顯示理解有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be credited as","meaning":"被譽為；被認為是","examples":[{"en":"Georges Braque is now credited as an equal pioneer of Cubism.","zh":"Georges Braque 現在被譽為立體主義同等重要的先驅。"},{"en":"To be credited as something means to be recognised as having that role or achievement.","zh":"be credited as 某身分，指被認可擁有該角色或成就。"},{"en":"A student may be credited as the organiser of a charity project if she planned most of it.","zh":"如果學生策劃了慈善項目的大部分工作，她可能被認為是組織者。"},{"en":"Credit matters because it gives proper recognition for someone’s contribution.","zh":"給予功勞很重要，因為它適當承認某人的貢獻。"},{"en":"The phrase describes public or historical acknowledgement.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾或歷史上的認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an equal pioneer in","meaning":"……中同等重要的先驅","examples":[{"en":"Braque is credited as an equal pioneer in this revolutionary art movement.","zh":"Braque 被認為是這場革命性藝術運動中同等重要的先驅。"},{"en":"An equal pioneer in a field is someone whose early contribution is as important as another person’s.","zh":"equal pioneer in 某領域，是早期貢獻與另一人同樣重要的人。"},{"en":"Two teachers may be equal pioneers in a school’s new reading programme.","zh":"兩位老師可能是學校新閱讀計劃中同等重要的先驅。"},{"en":"Calling someone an equal pioneer corrects the idea that only one person mattered.","zh":"稱某人為同等重要的先驅，是修正只有一人重要的想法。"},{"en":"The phrase recognises shared importance at the beginning of a movement.","zh":"這個短語承認某運動初期的共同重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"revolutionary art movement","meaning":"革命性的藝術運動","examples":[{"en":"Cubism was a revolutionary art movement in the early twentieth century.","zh":"立體主義是二十世紀初一場革命性的藝術運動。"},{"en":"A revolutionary art movement is a major change in how artists create and think about art.","zh":"revolutionary art movement 是藝術家創作和思考藝術方式上的重大改變。"},{"en":"A school art club may study a revolutionary art movement to understand why old rules changed.","zh":"學校藝術學會可能研究一場革命性藝術運動，以理解舊規則為何改變。"},{"en":"Such movements often shock people at first but influence later artists.","zh":"這類運動起初常令人震驚，但會影響後來藝術家。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an artistic shift that changes tradition.","zh":"這個短語描述改變傳統的藝術轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"claiming that","meaning":"聲稱","examples":[{"en":"Claiming that Picasso and Braque alone created Cubism oversimplifies the issue.","zh":"聲稱 Picasso 和 Braque 單獨創造了立體主義，是過分簡化問題。"},{"en":"Claiming that means saying or arguing that something is true.","zh":"claiming that 指說或主張某事是真實的。"},{"en":"Claiming that one student did all the group work may be unfair if others also helped.","zh":"聲稱一名學生做了所有小組工作，如果其他人也有幫忙，可能不公平。"},{"en":"A claim can sound simple but still ignore important facts.","zh":"一項聲稱可以聽起來簡單，但仍忽略重要事實。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a statement that may need evidence or correction.","zh":"這個短語引出可能需要證據或修正的陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"these two artists alone","meaning":"單是這兩位藝術家","examples":[{"en":"These two artists alone did not fully create Cubism.","zh":"單是這兩位藝術家並沒有完全創造立體主義。"},{"en":"These two artists alone means only these two artists, without considering anyone else.","zh":"these two artists alone 指只看這兩位藝術家，而不考慮其他人。"},{"en":"These two students alone could not have organised the whole school fair without volunteers.","zh":"單是這兩名學生，如果沒有義工，不可能組織整個學校嘉年華。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that a wider group may have contributed.","zh":"這個短語提醒可能有更大群體作出貢獻。"},{"en":"It limits attention to two people and often invites correction.","zh":"它把注意力限制在兩人身上，並常引出修正。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"oversimplify a complex issue","meaning":"過分簡化一個複雜問題","examples":[{"en":"Saying that only Picasso and Braque created Cubism oversimplifies a complex issue.","zh":"說只有 Picasso 和 Braque 創造了立體主義，是過分簡化一個複雜問題。"},{"en":"To oversimplify a complex issue means to explain it too simply and miss important details.","zh":"oversimplify a complex issue 指把複雜問題解釋得太簡單，並漏掉重要細節。"},{"en":"Saying poor grades happen only because students are lazy oversimplifies a complex issue.","zh":"說成績差只因學生懶惰，是過分簡化一個複雜問題。"},{"en":"Complex issues usually have several causes, people and contexts behind them.","zh":"複雜問題背後通常有幾個原因、人物和語境。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against easy explanations that hide reality.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要使用掩蓋現實的簡單解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"defining Cubism itself","meaning":"界定立體主義本身","examples":[{"en":"Defining Cubism itself is difficult.","zh":"界定立體主義本身是困難的。"},{"en":"Defining Cubism itself means explaining exactly what Cubism is.","zh":"defining Cubism itself 指準確解釋立體主義是甚麼。"},{"en":"Defining “good teaching” itself can be difficult because students need different things.","zh":"界定「好教學」本身也可能困難，因為學生需要不同東西。"},{"en":"A concept is hard to define when it has many forms and changes over time.","zh":"當概念有許多形式並隨時間改變，它就難以界定。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the challenge of giving a clear definition.","zh":"這個短語重點在給出清晰定義的挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at its simplest","meaning":"最簡單來說","examples":[{"en":"At its simplest, Cubism breaks an object into pieces.","zh":"最簡單來說，立體主義把物件分解成碎片。"},{"en":"At its simplest means explained in the most basic and easy-to-understand way.","zh":"at its simplest 指以最基本、最容易理解的方式解釋。"},{"en":"At its simplest, budgeting means not spending more money than you have.","zh":"最簡單來說，預算就是不要花超過自己擁有的錢。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful before giving a basic explanation of a difficult idea.","zh":"這個短語適合在解釋困難想法前給出基本說法。"},{"en":"It signals that more details exist, but the core idea is simple.","zh":"它表示仍有更多細節，但核心想法簡單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"three-dimensional object","meaning":"三維物件；立體物件","examples":[{"en":"A three-dimensional object may be represented from several angles.","zh":"三維物件可以從幾個角度被呈現。"},{"en":"A three-dimensional object has height, width and depth.","zh":"three-dimensional object 有高度、闊度和深度。"},{"en":"A cup, a chair and a human face are three-dimensional objects.","zh":"杯、椅子和人臉都是三維物件。"},{"en":"Showing such an object on flat paper requires choices about viewpoint and perspective.","zh":"在平面紙上呈現這類物件，需要選擇視角和透視法。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts real solid objects with flat images.","zh":"這個短語把真實立體物件與平面圖像作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be broken into pieces","meaning":"被分解成碎片","examples":[{"en":"In Cubism, the object being painted can be broken into pieces.","zh":"在立體主義中，被畫的物件可以被分解成碎片。"},{"en":"To be broken into pieces means to be divided into smaller parts.","zh":"be broken into pieces 指被分成較小部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may break a difficult essay question into pieces so students can answer it step by step.","zh":"老師可能把困難作文題分解成幾部分，讓學生逐步回答。"},{"en":"Breaking something into pieces can make its structure easier to examine.","zh":"把某物分解成碎片可以令其結構更容易檢視。"},{"en":"The phrase can be literal or figurative, depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可按語境作字面或比喻用法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cube-shaped","meaning":"立方體形狀的","examples":[{"en":"Some of the pieces may be square or cube-shaped.","zh":"有些碎片可能是正方形或立方體形狀的。"},{"en":"Cube-shaped means having a form like a cube, with box-like sides.","zh":"cube-shaped 指形狀像立方體，有盒子般的面。"},{"en":"A dice is cube-shaped, so each side is a square.","zh":"骰子是立方體形狀的，所以每一面都是正方形。"},{"en":"Cube-shaped forms can make an image look geometric rather than natural.","zh":"立方體形狀可以令圖像看起來幾何化，而不是自然。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a solid, angular shape.","zh":"這個短語描述實心、有角的形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hence the name","meaning":"因此得名","examples":[{"en":"The pieces are sometimes cube-shaped, hence the name Cubism.","zh":"這些碎片有時呈立方體形狀，因此得名立體主義。"},{"en":"Hence the name means this is the reason for the name.","zh":"hence the name 指這就是該名稱的由來。"},{"en":"The shop sells only desserts, hence the name “Sweet Corner”.","zh":"那間店只賣甜品，因此得名 “Sweet Corner”。"},{"en":"This phrase links a feature directly to a name or label.","zh":"這個短語把一項特徵直接連到名稱或標籤。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining why something is called what it is.","zh":"它適合用來解釋某物為何如此命名。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be reassembled","meaning":"被重新組合","examples":[{"en":"The pieces are reassembled in a less-than-coherent order.","zh":"這些碎片以不太連貫的次序被重新組合。"},{"en":"To be reassembled means to be put back together after being separated.","zh":"be reassembled 指分開後再次被放在一起。"},{"en":"After cleaning a desk fan, its parts must be reassembled before use.","zh":"清潔座檯風扇後，其零件必須在使用前被重新組合。"},{"en":"Reassembling parts in a new order can change how the whole object looks.","zh":"以新次序重新組合各部分，可以改變整體外觀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes putting pieces together again.","zh":"這個短語描述把碎片再次組合起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"less-than-coherent order","meaning":"不太連貫的次序","examples":[{"en":"The parts may be arranged in a less-than-coherent order.","zh":"這些部分可能以不太連貫的次序排列。"},{"en":"A less-than-coherent order is an arrangement that does not seem clear, logical or easy to follow.","zh":"less-than-coherent order 是看起來不清楚、不合邏輯或不易跟隨的排列。"},{"en":"A student’s notes may be in a less-than-coherent order if ideas are written randomly.","zh":"如果學生隨機寫下想法，筆記可能呈不太連貫的次序。"},{"en":"Such order can confuse readers because connections are not obvious.","zh":"這種次序會令讀者困惑，因為聯繫不明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organisation that feels partly disorderly.","zh":"這個短語描述感覺有點混亂的組織方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at different angles","meaning":"從不同角度","examples":[{"en":"The pieces are often shown at different angles.","zh":"這些碎片常從不同角度呈現。"},{"en":"At different angles means from different directions or viewpoints.","zh":"at different angles 指從不同方向或視角。"},{"en":"A teacher may photograph a model at different angles so students can see its shape clearly.","zh":"老師可能從不同角度拍攝模型，讓學生清楚看見其形狀。"},{"en":"Looking at something from different angles can reveal details hidden from one view.","zh":"從不同角度看某物可以揭示單一視角隱藏的細節。"},{"en":"The phrase describes variation in viewpoint or direction.","zh":"這個短語描述視角或方向上的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"overlap","meaning":"重疊","examples":[{"en":"Different views of the subject can overlap in a Cubist painting.","zh":"在立體主義畫作中，主體的不同視角可以重疊。"},{"en":"To overlap means to cover or share part of the same space, time or idea.","zh":"overlap 指覆蓋或共享部分相同空間、時間或想法。"},{"en":"Two classes may overlap if one ends at 3:00 and another starts at 2:45.","zh":"如果一堂課3點結束，而另一堂2點45分開始，兩堂課就會重疊。"},{"en":"Overlapping images can make a painting look layered and complex.","zh":"重疊圖像可以令畫作看起來有層次且複雜。"},{"en":"The word describes partial crossing or sharing.","zh":"這個詞描述部分交叉或共享。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"more than one view","meaning":"多於一個視角","examples":[{"en":"More than one view is often presented at the same time.","zh":"多於一個視角常會同時呈現。"},{"en":"More than one view means two or more ways of seeing or understanding something.","zh":"more than one view 指兩種或以上觀看或理解某事的方式。"},{"en":"A debate helps students hear more than one view on the same issue.","zh":"辯論幫助學生聽到同一議題上的多於一個觀點。"},{"en":"Showing more than one view can make a topic richer but less simple.","zh":"呈現多於一個視角可以令主題更豐富，但也較不簡單。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses plurality rather than a single perspective.","zh":"這個短語強調多元，而不是單一視角。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"同時","examples":[{"en":"Several views can be shown at the same time in one picture.","zh":"幾個視角可以在同一幅圖中同時呈現。"},{"en":"At the same time means simultaneously or during the same moment.","zh":"at the same time 指同時或在同一時刻。"},{"en":"A student can listen to music and write notes at the same time, although it may reduce focus.","zh":"學生可以同時聽音樂和寫筆記，雖然可能降低專注。"},{"en":"When two things happen at the same time, they share one time period.","zh":"當兩件事同時發生，它們共享同一時段。"},{"en":"The phrase describes simultaneity.","zh":"這個短語描述同時性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"move beyond","meaning":"超越","examples":[{"en":"Cubism moves beyond the limits of a fixed observer.","zh":"立體主義超越固定觀察者的限制。"},{"en":"To move beyond something means to go past its usual limits or restrictions.","zh":"move beyond 某事，指超過其通常界限或限制。"},{"en":"A student moves beyond memorisation when she begins to explain ideas in her own words.","zh":"當學生開始用自己的話解釋想法，她就超越了背誦。"},{"en":"Moving beyond old limits can create new possibilities.","zh":"超越舊限制可以創造新可能性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes development past an earlier boundary.","zh":"這個短語描述越過早前界線的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the limits of","meaning":"……的限制","examples":[{"en":"Cubism moves beyond the limits of traditional perspective.","zh":"立體主義超越傳統透視法的限制。"},{"en":"The limits of something are the boundaries of what it can do or allow.","zh":"limits of 某事，是它能做到或容許做到的邊界。"},{"en":"A school budget sets the limits of what new equipment can be bought.","zh":"學校預算設定了可購買新設備的限制。"},{"en":"Understanding limits helps people see when a new method is needed.","zh":"理解限制幫助人看出何時需要新方法。"},{"en":"The phrase points to restrictions or boundaries.","zh":"這個短語指出限制或邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a fixed observer","meaning":"固定觀察者","examples":[{"en":"Cubism does not depend on the viewpoint of a fixed observer.","zh":"立體主義不依賴固定觀察者的視點。"},{"en":"A fixed observer is someone who sees an object from one unmoving position.","zh":"fixed observer 是從一個不移動位置觀看物件的人。"},{"en":"A student sitting at the front of the classroom is a fixed observer of the board.","zh":"坐在課室前方的學生，是白板的固定觀察者。"},{"en":"If an artist rejects a fixed observer, the picture can combine several viewpoints.","zh":"如果藝術家拒絕固定觀察者，圖畫就能結合幾個視角。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a single stable viewing position.","zh":"這個短語描述單一穩定觀看位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"multiple viewpoints","meaning":"多重視角","examples":[{"en":"Cubist paintings often use multiple viewpoints.","zh":"立體主義畫作常使用多重視角。"},{"en":"Multiple viewpoints are several different ways of seeing the same subject.","zh":"multiple viewpoints 是觀看同一主體的幾種不同方式。"},{"en":"In a group discussion, students hear multiple viewpoints before making a decision.","zh":"在小組討論中，學生在作決定前會聽到多重觀點。"},{"en":"Multiple viewpoints can make a painting or argument more complex.","zh":"多重視角可以令畫作或論點更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that one angle is not enough.","zh":"這個短語強調一個角度並不足夠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mobile perspectives","meaning":"流動視角","examples":[{"en":"The term mobile perspectives refers to views that shift across time and angle.","zh":"mobile perspectives 這個術語指會隨時間和角度轉變的視角。"},{"en":"Mobile perspectives are viewpoints that move rather than stay fixed.","zh":"mobile perspectives 是移動而不是固定的視點。"},{"en":"A video tour of a building gives mobile perspectives because the camera keeps changing position.","zh":"建築物影片導覽提供流動視角，因為鏡頭位置不斷改變。"},{"en":"Mobile perspectives can show more information than one still view.","zh":"流動視角可以比一個靜止視角顯示更多資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing viewpoints across space or time.","zh":"這個短語描述跨越空間或時間的變動視角。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the subject is captured","meaning":"主體被捕捉","examples":[{"en":"The subject is captured from different angles.","zh":"主體從不同角度被捕捉。"},{"en":"The subject is captured means the artist or camera represents the thing being shown.","zh":"the subject is captured 指藝術家或相機呈現正在展示的東西。"},{"en":"In a school photo, the class is captured standing on the playground.","zh":"在學校相片中，全班被捕捉在操場上站着。"},{"en":"How a subject is captured affects what viewers notice first.","zh":"主體如何被捕捉會影響觀眾最先注意甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the act of representing a person, object or scene.","zh":"這個短語描述呈現人物、物件或場景的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"from different angles","meaning":"從不同角度","examples":[{"en":"Cubist artists captured subjects from different angles.","zh":"立體主義藝術家從不同角度捕捉主體。"},{"en":"From different angles means from different positions, directions or ways of looking.","zh":"from different angles 指從不同位置、方向或觀看方式。"},{"en":"A doctor may examine an X-ray from different angles before making a decision.","zh":"醫生作決定前可能從不同角度檢視X光片。"},{"en":"Looking from different angles can reveal details missed from one side.","zh":"從不同角度觀看可以揭示單一面向漏掉的細節。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe physical viewpoint or different ways of thinking.","zh":"這個短語可描述物理視角或不同思考方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at different times","meaning":"在不同時間","examples":[{"en":"The subject may be captured at different times in one painting.","zh":"主體可能在同一幅畫中於不同時間被捕捉。"},{"en":"At different times means not all at once, but at separate moments.","zh":"at different times 指不是同時，而是在分開的時刻。"},{"en":"A diary records a student’s feelings at different times during the school year.","zh":"日記記錄學生在學年中不同時間的感受。"},{"en":"Showing different times together can make one image feel layered.","zh":"把不同時間一起呈現，可以令一個圖像有層次感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moments separated in time.","zh":"這個短語描述時間上分開的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"corresponding images","meaning":"對應的圖像","examples":[{"en":"The corresponding images are fused into a single picture.","zh":"對應的圖像被融合成單一畫面。"},{"en":"Corresponding images are related images that match or connect with each other.","zh":"corresponding images 是彼此配合或連繫的相關圖像。"},{"en":"In a textbook, a diagram and its corresponding image may help explain the same idea.","zh":"在教科書中，圖表及其對應圖像可能幫助解釋同一想法。"},{"en":"When corresponding images are combined, viewers can compare related views together.","zh":"當對應圖像被結合，觀眾可以一起比較相關視角。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to matching visual parts.","zh":"這個短語指互相配對的視覺部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be fused into","meaning":"被融合成","examples":[{"en":"Different images are fused into a single picture.","zh":"不同圖像被融合成單一畫面。"},{"en":"To be fused into something means to be joined together to form one whole.","zh":"be fused into 某物，指被結合起來形成一個整體。"},{"en":"Several class photos may be fused into one poster for graduation.","zh":"幾張班相可能被融合成一張畢業海報。"},{"en":"Fusion can create a new result that is different from each separate part.","zh":"融合可以創造出不同於各個單獨部分的新結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes combining elements into one unit.","zh":"這個短語描述把元素結合成一個單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a single picture","meaning":"單一畫面","examples":[{"en":"Multiple viewpoints can be fused into a single picture.","zh":"多重視角可以被融合成單一畫面。"},{"en":"A single picture is one complete image, not several separate images.","zh":"single picture 是一個完整圖像，而不是幾個分開圖像。"},{"en":"A poster may combine photos, text and drawings into a single picture.","zh":"海報可能把照片、文字和圖畫結合成單一畫面。"},{"en":"Putting many views into one picture can create density and complexity.","zh":"把許多視角放入一幅圖，可以創造密度和複雜性。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses unity despite multiple parts.","zh":"這個短語強調即使有多個部分仍形成整體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pre-war paintings","meaning":"戰前畫作","examples":[{"en":"Braque began experimenting with these ideas in his pre-war paintings.","zh":"Braque 開始在他的戰前畫作中嘗試這些想法。"},{"en":"Pre-war paintings are paintings made before a particular war.","zh":"pre-war paintings 是某場戰爭前創作的畫作。"},{"en":"A museum may compare an artist’s pre-war paintings with later works after the war changed his style.","zh":"博物館可能比較藝術家的戰前畫作與戰後改變風格的作品。"},{"en":"War can alter an artist’s themes, colours and emotional tone.","zh":"戰爭可以改變藝術家的主題、色彩和情緒語調。"},{"en":"The phrase places artworks in the period before war.","zh":"這個短語把藝術作品放在戰爭前的時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"experiment with","meaning":"嘗試；實驗","examples":[{"en":"Braque began experimenting with multiple viewpoints.","zh":"Braque 開始嘗試多重視角。"},{"en":"To experiment with something means to try it in order to discover what works.","zh":"experiment with 某事，指嘗試它以發現甚麼有效。"},{"en":"A student may experiment with different revision methods before an exam.","zh":"學生可能在考試前嘗試不同溫習方法。"},{"en":"Experimenting can lead to mistakes, but it can also produce new ideas.","zh":"嘗試可能導致錯誤，但也可以產生新想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes trying a method creatively or scientifically.","zh":"這個短語描述創意或科學地試用某方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"inevitably lead to","meaning":"無可避免地導致","examples":[{"en":"Braque’s experiments inevitably led to an association with Picasso.","zh":"Braque 的實驗無可避免地導致他與 Picasso 產生聯繫。"},{"en":"To inevitably lead to something means to cause a result that is very likely or unavoidable.","zh":"inevitably lead to 某事，指造成非常可能或不可避免的結果。"},{"en":"Ignoring a leaking roof will inevitably lead to more expensive repairs.","zh":"忽視漏水屋頂會無可避免地導致更昂貴維修。"},{"en":"When two artists explore similar ideas, comparison may inevitably lead to connection.","zh":"當兩位藝術家探索相似想法，比較可能自然導致聯繫。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a result that naturally follows.","zh":"這個短語描述自然隨之而來的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"an association with","meaning":"與……的聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Braque’s work led to an association with Picasso.","zh":"Braque 的作品導致他與 Picasso 產生聯繫。"},{"en":"An association with someone or something is a connection in people’s minds or in history.","zh":"association with 某人或某事，是在人們腦海或歷史中的連繫。"},{"en":"A school may have an association with music if its choir often wins prizes.","zh":"如果學校合唱團常得獎，該校可能與音樂產生聯繫。"},{"en":"Repeated collaboration can create a strong association between two names.","zh":"反覆合作可以在兩個名字之間創造強烈聯繫。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a recognised link.","zh":"這個短語描述被認可的連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dabble in","meaning":"涉獵；嘗試","examples":[{"en":"Picasso had also been dabbling in geometric forms.","zh":"Picasso 也一直在涉獵幾何形式。"},{"en":"To dabble in something means to try it casually or not yet fully seriously.","zh":"dabble in 某事，指較隨意地嘗試，而未必完全認真投入。"},{"en":"A student may dabble in photography before deciding whether to join the school club.","zh":"學生可能先嘗試攝影，再決定是否加入學校學會。"},{"en":"Dabbling can become serious work if interest grows.","zh":"如果興趣增長，初步涉獵可以變成認真工作。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests early exploration rather than full commitment.","zh":"這個短語暗示早期探索，而不是完全投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"render something as","meaning":"將……描繪成","examples":[{"en":"Picasso rendered three-dimensional views as two-dimensional geometric shapes.","zh":"Picasso 將三維視角描繪成二維幾何形狀。"},{"en":"To render something as something else means to represent it in a particular form.","zh":"render something as something else 指以特定形式呈現某物。"},{"en":"A designer may render a school building as a simple 3D model.","zh":"設計師可能將學校建築描繪成簡單3D模型。"},{"en":"How something is rendered changes how viewers understand it.","zh":"某物如何被呈現，會改變觀眾如何理解它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes turning an idea or object into a visual form.","zh":"這個短語描述把想法或物件轉化為視覺形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"three-dimensional views","meaning":"三維視角","examples":[{"en":"Picasso experimented with rendering three-dimensional views as flat shapes.","zh":"Picasso 嘗試把三維視角描繪成平面形狀。"},{"en":"Three-dimensional views show height, width and depth rather than only a flat surface.","zh":"three-dimensional views 顯示高度、闊度和深度，而不只是平面表面。"},{"en":"Students use three-dimensional views when they draw a box with visible depth.","zh":"當學生畫一個有可見深度的盒子時，就是使用三維視角。"},{"en":"Converting such views into flat shapes can make an image look abstract.","zh":"把這類視角轉化為平面形狀，可以令圖像看起來抽象。"},{"en":"The phrase describes viewpoints that suggest physical depth.","zh":"這個短語描述暗示實體深度的視角。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"two-dimensional geometric shapes","meaning":"二維幾何形狀","examples":[{"en":"Picasso turned three-dimensional views into two-dimensional geometric shapes.","zh":"Picasso 把三維視角轉化為二維幾何形狀。"},{"en":"Two-dimensional geometric shapes are flat shapes such as squares, triangles and circles.","zh":"two-dimensional geometric shapes 是正方形、三角形和圓形等平面形狀。"},{"en":"A maths worksheet may ask students to identify two-dimensional geometric shapes in a picture.","zh":"數學工作紙可能要求學生辨認圖片中的二維幾何形狀。"},{"en":"Using flat geometric shapes can simplify real objects into patterns.","zh":"使用平面幾何形狀可以把真實物件簡化成圖案。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to flat, measurable shapes.","zh":"這個短語指平面且可量度的形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be labelled","meaning":"被標籤為；被稱為","examples":[{"en":"Young Ladies of Avignon is often labelled proto-cubist.","zh":"《亞維農少女》常被稱為原始立體主義作品。"},{"en":"To be labelled something means to be described or classified with that name.","zh":"be labelled 某物，指被以該名稱描述或分類。"},{"en":"A student may be labelled quiet, even though she speaks confidently with close friends.","zh":"學生可能被標籤為安靜，即使她與好友說話很有信心。"},{"en":"Labels can help classification, but they may also oversimplify.","zh":"標籤可以幫助分類，但也可能過分簡化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving a category or name to something.","zh":"這個短語描述給某物一個類別或名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"proto-cubist","meaning":"原始立體主義的","examples":[{"en":"Some critics describe Young Ladies of Avignon as proto-cubist.","zh":"有些評論家把《亞維農少女》描述為原始立體主義的作品。"},{"en":"Proto-cubist means showing early features of Cubism before the style was fully developed.","zh":"proto-cubist 指在立體主義完全發展前，已顯示其早期特徵。"},{"en":"An early app design may be called proto-social-media if it contains basic sharing features.","zh":"如果早期應用程式包含基本分享功能，它可能被稱為原始社交媒體形式。"},{"en":"Proto-forms matter because they show how a movement began to take shape.","zh":"原始形式重要，因為它們顯示一場運動如何開始成形。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that comes before the mature form.","zh":"這個短語描述成熟形式之前的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the true beginning of","meaning":"……的真正開端","examples":[{"en":"Some consider this painting to be the true beginning of Cubism.","zh":"有些人認為這幅畫是立體主義的真正開端。"},{"en":"The true beginning of something is the real starting point of its development.","zh":"true beginning of 某事，是其發展的真正起點。"},{"en":"A teacher may say a student’s true beginning in writing came when she started revising seriously.","zh":"老師可能說學生寫作的真正開端，是她開始認真修改時。"},{"en":"Identifying a true beginning helps people understand how later changes grew.","zh":"找出真正開端有助人理解後來變化如何成長。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the moment something meaningfully starts.","zh":"這個短語標記某事真正有意義地開始的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"inspire someone to","meaning":"啟發某人去","examples":[{"en":"The painting inspired Braque to follow Picasso’s lead.","zh":"這幅畫啟發 Braque 跟隨 Picasso 的方向。"},{"en":"To inspire someone to do something means to encourage them to act or create.","zh":"inspire someone to do something 指鼓勵某人行動或創作。"},{"en":"A teacher’s praise may inspire a student to enter a writing competition.","zh":"老師的稱讚可能啟發學生參加寫作比賽。"},{"en":"Inspiration can turn interest into action.","zh":"啟發可以把興趣轉化為行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes motivation created by another person or work.","zh":"這個短語描述由他人或作品產生的動力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"follow its lead","meaning":"跟隨其方向","examples":[{"en":"Braque followed the painting’s lead and developed Cubist ideas further.","zh":"Braque 跟隨該畫的方向，並進一步發展立體主義想法。"},{"en":"To follow its lead means to use something as a guide or starting direction.","zh":"follow its lead 指把某物作為指引或起始方向。"},{"en":"A student may follow a model essay’s lead by using a clear introduction and topic sentences.","zh":"學生可能跟隨範文的方向，使用清楚引言和主題句。"},{"en":"Following a lead can help someone develop an idea without copying it completely.","zh":"跟隨方向可以幫助人發展想法，而不完全抄襲。"},{"en":"The phrase describes taking direction from an earlier example.","zh":"這個短語描述從早前例子取得方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"develop the movement towards","meaning":"推動該運動走向","examples":[{"en":"Braque helped develop the movement towards its trademark features.","zh":"Braque 幫助推動該運動走向其標誌性特徵。"},{"en":"To develop the movement towards something means to help it grow in a particular direction.","zh":"develop the movement towards 某事，指幫助它朝某方向成長。"},{"en":"A school leader may develop a club towards more student-led activities.","zh":"學校領袖可能推動學會走向更多學生主導活動。"},{"en":"Movements develop when repeated choices create clearer shared features.","zh":"當反覆選擇創造更清楚的共同特徵，運動就會發展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes guiding gradual change.","zh":"這個短語描述引導漸進改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"trademark features","meaning":"標誌性特徵","examples":[{"en":"The movement developed towards its trademark features.","zh":"該運動發展出其標誌性特徵。"},{"en":"Trademark features are distinctive qualities that make something easily recognised.","zh":"trademark features 是令某物容易被辨認的獨特特質。"},{"en":"A teacher’s trademark features may include clear examples and calm explanations.","zh":"老師的標誌性特徵可能包括清楚例子和平靜解釋。"},{"en":"When a style develops trademark features, people can identify it quickly.","zh":"當一種風格發展出標誌性特徵，人們就能快速辨認它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recognisable signature qualities.","zh":"這個短語描述可辨認的招牌特質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be influenced by","meaning":"受……影響","examples":[{"en":"Both Picasso and Braque were influenced by earlier painters.","zh":"Picasso 和 Braque 都受較早期畫家影響。"},{"en":"To be influenced by someone means to be affected by their ideas, style or actions.","zh":"be influenced by 某人，指受其想法、風格或行動影響。"},{"en":"A student’s speaking style may be influenced by a favourite teacher.","zh":"學生的說話風格可能受喜愛老師影響。"},{"en":"Influence can appear in small choices, such as colour, structure or method.","zh":"影響可以出現在顏色、結構或方法等小選擇中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how one person’s work shapes another’s.","zh":"這個短語描述一個人的作品如何塑造另一個人的作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"earlier painters","meaning":"較早期的畫家","examples":[{"en":"Earlier painters helped shape the development of Cubism.","zh":"較早期的畫家幫助塑造立體主義的發展。"},{"en":"Earlier painters are artists who worked before the painters being discussed.","zh":"earlier painters 是在所討論畫家之前工作的藝術家。"},{"en":"Modern designers often learn from earlier painters when studying colour and composition.","zh":"現代設計師研究色彩和構圖時，常向較早期畫家學習。"},{"en":"Earlier painters can influence later art even if they did not belong to the later movement.","zh":"較早期畫家即使不屬於後來運動，也可以影響後來藝術。"},{"en":"The phrase places artists in a historical sequence.","zh":"這個短語把藝術家放在歷史次序中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in particular","meaning":"尤其是","examples":[{"en":"The artists were influenced in particular by the later works of Cezanne.","zh":"這些藝術家尤其受 Cezanne 後期作品影響。"},{"en":"In particular means especially or more specifically than the others.","zh":"in particular 指尤其是，或比其他項目更具體地說。"},{"en":"Students often struggle with grammar, in particular articles and prepositions.","zh":"學生常在文法上吃力，尤其是冠詞和介詞。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows a general statement to one important example.","zh":"這個短語把一般陳述收窄到一個重要例子。"},{"en":"It helps readers know which item deserves special attention.","zh":"它幫助讀者知道哪一項值得特別注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"later works","meaning":"後期作品","examples":[{"en":"Cezanne’s later works influenced Cubist artists.","zh":"Cezanne 的後期作品影響了立體主義藝術家。"},{"en":"Later works are pieces created in the later part of an artist’s career.","zh":"later works 是藝術家事業後期創作的作品。"},{"en":"A writer’s later works may be calmer and deeper than his early novels.","zh":"作家的後期作品可能比早期小說更平靜和深刻。"},{"en":"Later works can show how an artist’s style changed over time.","zh":"後期作品可以顯示藝術家的風格如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts mature works with earlier creations.","zh":"這個短語把成熟作品與早期創作作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"divide the canvas into","meaning":"將畫布分成","examples":[{"en":"Cezanne was one of the first artists to divide the canvas into several views.","zh":"Cezanne 是最早將畫布分成幾個視角的藝術家之一。"},{"en":"To divide the canvas into parts means to separate the picture surface into sections.","zh":"divide the canvas into parts 指把畫面表面分成幾個部分。"},{"en":"A student may divide the canvas into four areas before painting different scenes.","zh":"學生可能先將畫布分成四個區域，再畫不同場景。"},{"en":"Dividing a canvas lets an artist show more than one idea or viewpoint.","zh":"分割畫布讓藝術家呈現多於一個想法或視角。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organising a picture surface.","zh":"這個短語描述組織畫面表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the canvas","meaning":"畫布","examples":[{"en":"Cezanne divided the canvas into several views.","zh":"Cezanne 將畫布分成幾個視角。"},{"en":"The canvas is the surface on which a painter paints.","zh":"canvas 是畫家作畫的表面。"},{"en":"In art class, students may stretch paper or cloth to create a canvas.","zh":"在美術課中，學生可能拉平紙張或布料來製作畫布。"},{"en":"How an artist uses the canvas affects the whole composition.","zh":"藝術家如何使用畫布會影響整體構圖。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to both the painting surface and the space of the picture.","zh":"這個短語既指作畫表面，也指畫面空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"several views","meaning":"幾個視角","examples":[{"en":"Cezanne presented several views within one painting.","zh":"Cezanne 在一幅畫中呈現幾個視角。"},{"en":"Several views means more than two ways of seeing the same subject.","zh":"several views 指觀看同一主體的多於兩種方式。"},{"en":"A travel brochure may show several views of a hotel room before guests book it.","zh":"旅遊小冊子可能在客人訂房前展示酒店房間的幾個視角。"},{"en":"Several views help people understand an object more completely.","zh":"幾個視角幫助人更完整地理解物件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes multiple visual perspectives.","zh":"這個短語描述多個視覺角度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"present natural objects","meaning":"呈現自然物件","examples":[{"en":"Cezanne began presenting natural objects in geometric figures.","zh":"Cezanne 開始以幾何圖形呈現自然物件。"},{"en":"To present natural objects means to show things from nature in a particular way.","zh":"present natural objects 指以特定方式展示自然界中的東西。"},{"en":"A child may present natural objects such as leaves and shells in a science poster.","zh":"孩子可能在科學海報中呈現葉子和貝殼等自然物件。"},{"en":"Presenting nature geometrically can make familiar things look structured and unusual.","zh":"以幾何方式呈現自然，可以令熟悉事物看起來有結構且不尋常。"},{"en":"The phrase describes artistic representation of natural things.","zh":"這個短語描述對自然事物的藝術呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"geometric figures","meaning":"幾何圖形","examples":[{"en":"Cezanne represented natural objects in geometric figures.","zh":"Cezanne 以幾何圖形呈現自然物件。"},{"en":"Geometric figures are shapes such as circles, triangles, cubes and cones.","zh":"geometric figures 是圓形、三角形、立方體和圓錐等形狀。"},{"en":"Maths teachers use geometric figures to explain area, volume and symmetry.","zh":"數學老師使用幾何圖形解釋面積、體積和對稱。"},{"en":"Artists use geometric figures to simplify complex forms.","zh":"藝術家使用幾何圖形來簡化複雜形態。"},{"en":"The phrase describes clear mathematical shapes.","zh":"這個短語描述清晰的數學形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"exhibit paintings","meaning":"展出畫作","examples":[{"en":"Several museums exhibited Cezanne’s paintings after his death.","zh":"幾間博物館在 Cezanne 死後展出他的畫作。"},{"en":"To exhibit paintings means to display them publicly, usually in a museum or gallery.","zh":"exhibit paintings 指公開展示畫作，通常在博物館或畫廊。"},{"en":"A school may exhibit paintings by students during an open day.","zh":"學校可能在開放日展出學生畫作。"},{"en":"Exhibiting paintings lets more people see, discuss and judge them.","zh":"展出畫作讓更多人觀看、討論和評價。"},{"en":"The phrase describes public display of artworks.","zh":"這個短語描述藝術作品的公開展示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a retrospective of","meaning":"……的回顧展","examples":[{"en":"Museums held a retrospective of Cezanne’s life and work.","zh":"博物館舉辦了 Cezanne 一生及作品的回顧展。"},{"en":"A retrospective of an artist is an exhibition that looks back over their career.","zh":"retrospective of 藝術家，是回顧其事業的展覽。"},{"en":"A cinema may hold a retrospective of an old director’s films.","zh":"戲院可能舉辦一位舊導演電影的回顧展。"},{"en":"Retrospectives help audiences see development across many years.","zh":"回顧展幫助觀眾看見多年來的發展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a backward-looking review of someone’s work.","zh":"這個短語描述對某人作品的回顧式展示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the artist’s life","meaning":"該藝術家的一生","examples":[{"en":"The retrospective presented paintings from the artist’s life.","zh":"回顧展呈現了該藝術家一生中的畫作。"},{"en":"The artist’s life means the period and experiences of an artist from youth to death.","zh":"artist’s life 指藝術家從年輕到死亡的時期和經歷。"},{"en":"A biography explains the artist’s life through family, training, success and struggle.","zh":"傳記透過家庭、訓練、成功和掙扎解釋該藝術家的一生。"},{"en":"Knowing the artist’s life can help viewers understand why the work changed.","zh":"了解藝術家的一生可以幫助觀眾理解作品為何改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the personal and professional history of an artist.","zh":"這個短語指藝術家的個人和專業歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Parisian art scene","meaning":"巴黎藝術圈","examples":[{"en":"Young painters in the Parisian art scene saw Cezanne’s works.","zh":"巴黎藝術圈中的年輕畫家看到了 Cezanne 的作品。"},{"en":"The Parisian art scene means the community of artists, galleries and exhibitions in Paris.","zh":"Parisian art scene 指巴黎的藝術家、畫廊和展覽社群。"},{"en":"A young painter may move to the Parisian art scene to meet other ambitious artists.","zh":"年輕畫家可能搬到巴黎藝術圈，以認識其他有抱負的藝術家。"},{"en":"A strong art scene spreads ideas quickly because artists see and discuss one another’s work.","zh":"強大的藝術圈會快速傳播想法，因為藝術家彼此觀看和討論作品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the cultural network of art in Paris.","zh":"這個短語描述巴黎藝術的文化網絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"would have seen","meaning":"很可能看過","examples":[{"en":"Picasso and Braque would have seen Cezanne’s works in the retrospective.","zh":"Picasso 和 Braque 很可能在回顧展中看過 Cezanne 的作品。"},{"en":"Would have seen means the writer believes they probably saw it, based on context.","zh":"would have seen 指作者根據語境認為他們很可能看過。"},{"en":"A student who attended the meeting would have heard the announcement about the trip.","zh":"參加會議的學生很可能聽過關於旅行的宣布。"},{"en":"The phrase is used for a likely past event that cannot be stated with complete certainty.","zh":"這個短語用於不能完全確定但很可能發生的過去事件。"},{"en":"It suggests informed probability, not direct proof.","zh":"它表示有根據的可能性，而不是直接證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"whilst not yet","meaning":"雖然尚未","examples":[{"en":"Whilst not yet fractured into cubes, Cezanne’s work showed underlying geometry.","zh":"雖然尚未被分裂成立方體，Cezanne 的作品已顯示潛在幾何結構。"},{"en":"Whilst not yet means although something had not reached that stage at the time.","zh":"whilst not yet 指雖然當時某事尚未達到該階段。"},{"en":"Whilst not yet fluent, the student could already hold simple English conversations.","zh":"雖然尚未流利，學生已能進行簡單英語對話。"},{"en":"The phrase shows an early stage before full development.","zh":"這個短語顯示完全發展前的早期階段。"},{"en":"It helps compare what is already present with what has not appeared yet.","zh":"它幫助比較已存在的東西與尚未出現的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be fractured into","meaning":"被分裂成","examples":[{"en":"Cezanne’s subjects were not yet fractured into facets or cubes.","zh":"Cezanne 的主體尚未被分裂成切面或立方體。"},{"en":"To be fractured into parts means to be broken visually or physically into separate pieces.","zh":"be fractured into 部分，指在視覺上或物理上被分成分開的碎片。"},{"en":"A cracked phone screen may be fractured into many small sections.","zh":"破裂的手機螢幕可能被分裂成許多小部分。"},{"en":"In art, fracturing a subject can make it look analysed rather than natural.","zh":"在藝術中，把主體分裂可以令它看起來像被分析，而非自然呈現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes division into angular parts.","zh":"這個短語描述分成有角部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"facets or cubes","meaning":"切面或立方體","examples":[{"en":"Cubist works often fracture objects into facets or cubes.","zh":"立體主義作品常把物件分裂成切面或立方體。"},{"en":"Facets or cubes are flat surfaces or box-like shapes used to break up a form.","zh":"facets or cubes 是用來分解形態的平面或盒狀形狀。"},{"en":"A jewellery drawing may show facets on a diamond to suggest many small surfaces.","zh":"珠寶圖可能畫出鑽石切面，以暗示許多小表面。"},{"en":"Using facets or cubes makes a natural object look geometric.","zh":"使用切面或立方體會令自然物件看起來幾何化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes angular parts in a fragmented image.","zh":"這個短語描述碎片化圖像中的有角部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"occasionally introduce","meaning":"偶爾引入","examples":[{"en":"Cezanne occasionally introduced an underlying geometry.","zh":"Cezanne 偶爾引入潛在幾何結構。"},{"en":"To occasionally introduce something means to bring it in from time to time, not constantly.","zh":"occasionally introduce 某事，指不時加入它，而不是一直使用。"},{"en":"A teacher may occasionally introduce games to make grammar practice lighter.","zh":"老師可能偶爾引入遊戲，令文法練習輕鬆一點。"},{"en":"Occasional use can signal an idea without making it dominate the whole work.","zh":"偶爾使用可以暗示一個想法，而不令它支配整件作品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something appearing sometimes.","zh":"這個短語描述某事有時出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"underlying geometry","meaning":"潛在的幾何結構","examples":[{"en":"The Bathers contains an underlying geometry.","zh":"《浴者》包含潛在的幾何結構。"},{"en":"Underlying geometry is a hidden structure of shapes beneath the surface of an image.","zh":"underlying geometry 是圖像表面之下隱藏的形狀結構。"},{"en":"A poster may look casual but still have underlying geometry that guides the viewer’s eyes.","zh":"海報可能看似隨意，但仍有引導觀眾視線的潛在幾何結構。"},{"en":"Such structure can make an artwork feel balanced even when it looks natural.","zh":"這種結構可以令藝術作品即使看起來自然，也感覺平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase points to hidden geometric order.","zh":"這個短語指出隱藏的幾何秩序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"unfinished painting","meaning":"未完成畫作","examples":[{"en":"The Bathers is one of Cezanne’s most famous unfinished paintings.","zh":"《浴者》是 Cezanne 最著名的未完成畫作之一。"},{"en":"An unfinished painting is a painting that the artist did not complete.","zh":"unfinished painting 是藝術家沒有完成的畫作。"},{"en":"A student’s unfinished painting may still show a strong idea in its early lines.","zh":"學生的未完成畫作仍可能在早期線條中顯示強烈想法。"},{"en":"Unfinished works can be valuable because they reveal the artist’s process.","zh":"未完成作品可以很有價值，因為它們揭示藝術家的創作過程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes artwork left incomplete.","zh":"這個短語描述未完成的藝術作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"break tradition","meaning":"打破傳統","examples":[{"en":"The Bathers breaks tradition in its unflattering portrait of women.","zh":"《浴者》以不加美化的女性描繪打破傳統。"},{"en":"To break tradition means to stop following the usual or accepted way of doing something.","zh":"break tradition 指不再跟隨通常或被接受的做法。"},{"en":"A school may break tradition by allowing students to design the graduation ceremony.","zh":"學校可能讓學生設計畢業典禮，從而打破傳統。"},{"en":"Breaking tradition can shock people but may open space for new ideas.","zh":"打破傳統可能令人震驚，但也可能為新想法開路。"},{"en":"The phrase describes challenging established practice.","zh":"這個短語描述挑戰既定做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"unflattering portrait","meaning":"不加美化的描繪","examples":[{"en":"The painting offers an unflattering portrait of the women.","zh":"這幅畫對女性作出不加美化的描繪。"},{"en":"An unflattering portrait shows someone in a way that is not beautified or pleasing.","zh":"unflattering portrait 指以不美化、不討好的方式呈現某人。"},{"en":"A photo taken in harsh light may become an unflattering portrait of a person.","zh":"在刺眼燈光下拍的相片，可能成為某人的不加美化肖像。"},{"en":"Artists may choose an unflattering portrait to challenge idealised beauty.","zh":"藝術家可能選擇不加美化的描繪，以挑戰理想化美感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a portrayal that does not try to make the subject attractive.","zh":"這個短語描述不嘗試令主體吸引的呈現方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"naked forms","meaning":"裸體形態","examples":[{"en":"The women’s naked forms are rendered in sharp symmetry.","zh":"女性的裸體形態被描繪成鮮明的對稱。"},{"en":"Naked forms are human bodies shown without clothing in art.","zh":"naked forms 是藝術中沒有衣服的人體。"},{"en":"In a life-drawing class, students study naked forms to understand body shape and proportion.","zh":"在人體素描課中，學生研究裸體形態以理解身體形狀和比例。"},{"en":"How naked forms are drawn can express beauty, vulnerability or discomfort.","zh":"裸體形態如何被畫出，可以表達美、脆弱或不安。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to unclothed bodies as artistic forms.","zh":"這個短語指作為藝術形態的裸體身體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be rendered in","meaning":"被描繪成","examples":[{"en":"The naked forms are rendered in sharp symmetry.","zh":"裸體形態被描繪成鮮明的對稱。"},{"en":"To be rendered in a style means to be shown or represented in that manner.","zh":"be rendered in 某風格，指以該方式被呈現或描繪。"},{"en":"A city skyline may be rendered in black and white for a dramatic poster.","zh":"城市天際線可能被描繪成黑白色，用於戲劇化海報。"},{"en":"The chosen style affects the mood and meaning of the image.","zh":"所選風格會影響圖像的氣氛和意思。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how something is visually presented.","zh":"這個短語描述某物如何被視覺呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sharp symmetry","meaning":"鮮明的對稱","examples":[{"en":"The figures are rendered in sharp symmetry.","zh":"這些人物被描繪成鮮明的對稱。"},{"en":"Sharp symmetry is clear, strong balance between matching sides or shapes.","zh":"sharp symmetry 是相配兩邊或形狀之間清晰而強烈的平衡。"},{"en":"A logo with sharp symmetry may look formal, stable and easy to recognise.","zh":"具有鮮明對稱的標誌可能看起來正式、穩定且易辨認。"},{"en":"Strong symmetry can make figures look organised rather than soft or natural.","zh":"強烈對稱可以令人像看起來有組織，而不是柔和或自然。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a precise visual balance.","zh":"這個短語描述精確的視覺平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"form a triangular pattern","meaning":"形成三角形圖案","examples":[{"en":"The women, river, and trees form a triangular pattern.","zh":"女性、河流和樹木形成三角形圖案。"},{"en":"To form a triangular pattern means to create a shape or arrangement like a triangle.","zh":"form a triangular pattern 指創造像三角形的形狀或排列。"},{"en":"Three students standing apart can form a triangular pattern on a stage.","zh":"三名學生分開站在舞台上，可以形成三角形圖案。"},{"en":"Triangular patterns can guide the viewer’s eyes through a picture.","zh":"三角形圖案可以引導觀眾視線穿過畫面。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visual arrangement into a triangle-like structure.","zh":"這個短語描述排列成類似三角形結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be said to have inspired","meaning":"據說啟發了","examples":[{"en":"The Bathers is said to have inspired Picasso’s similar work.","zh":"據說《浴者》啟發了 Picasso 的類似作品。"},{"en":"To be said to have inspired something means people believe it influenced that later work.","zh":"be said to have inspired 某物，指人們相信它影響了後來作品。"},{"en":"An old poem is said to have inspired a popular song if the song uses similar images.","zh":"如果一首流行歌使用相似意象，一首舊詩可說據說啟發了它。"},{"en":"This phrase is cautious because the influence may be widely believed but not directly proven.","zh":"這個短語較謹慎，因為影響可能被廣泛相信但未被直接證明。"},{"en":"It describes reported artistic influence.","zh":"它描述被報道或認為的藝術影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"similarly styled work","meaning":"風格相似的作品","examples":[{"en":"Picasso later produced a similarly styled work.","zh":"Picasso 後來創作了一件風格相似的作品。"},{"en":"A similarly styled work is another work that uses a similar visual approach or method.","zh":"similarly styled work 是使用相似視覺方式或方法的另一件作品。"},{"en":"A designer may create a similarly styled poster for the same school event series.","zh":"設計師可能為同一學校活動系列創作風格相似的海報。"},{"en":"Similar style can show influence, shared taste or deliberate reference.","zh":"相似風格可以顯示影響、共同品味或刻意引用。"},{"en":"The phrase compares works by appearance or method.","zh":"這個短語按外觀或方法比較作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"mentioned previously","meaning":"之前提及的","examples":[{"en":"The painting mentioned previously was Young Ladies of Avignon.","zh":"之前提及的畫作是《亞維農少女》。"},{"en":"Mentioned previously means already referred to earlier in the text or conversation.","zh":"mentioned previously 指在文本或對話較早部分已提及。"},{"en":"The teacher returned to the rule mentioned previously before giving new examples.","zh":"老師在給新例子前，回到之前提及的規則。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers connect back to earlier information.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者連回早前資訊。"},{"en":"It avoids repeating the full explanation again.","zh":"它避免再次重複完整解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"moving beyond","meaning":"超越；離開……階段","examples":[{"en":"Moving beyond the early years of Cubism, many artists explored related ideas.","zh":"離開立體主義早期階段後，許多藝術家探索相關想法。"},{"en":"Moving beyond something means going past an earlier stage or limit.","zh":"moving beyond 某事，指越過較早階段或限制。"},{"en":"Moving beyond basic grammar, students begin to write longer and more flexible sentences.","zh":"超越基本文法後，學生開始寫更長、更靈活的句子。"},{"en":"Once people move beyond an early stage, they can experiment more freely.","zh":"一旦人們超越早期階段，就能更自由地實驗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes progress away from an initial period.","zh":"這個短語描述離開初始時期的進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the early years of","meaning":"……的早期","examples":[{"en":"Many artists worked after the early years of Cubism.","zh":"許多藝術家在立體主義早期之後工作。"},{"en":"The early years of something are its beginning period.","zh":"early years of 某事，是其開始時期。"},{"en":"The early years of a business are often difficult because money and customers are limited.","zh":"企業早期常很困難，因為金錢和客戶有限。"},{"en":"Early years can shape the direction that later development follows.","zh":"早期可以塑造後來發展所跟隨的方向。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the first stage of a movement, career or organisation.","zh":"這個短語指運動、事業或組織的第一階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"explore the same idea","meaning":"探索同一理念","examples":[{"en":"Many artists were exploring the same idea in individual ways.","zh":"許多藝術家以個人方式探索同一理念。"},{"en":"To explore the same idea means to investigate or develop one shared concept.","zh":"explore the same idea 指研究或發展一個共同概念。"},{"en":"Several students may explore the same idea of friendship in different stories.","zh":"幾名學生可能在不同故事中探索友誼這個同一理念。"},{"en":"Shared ideas can lead to very different results when people approach them personally.","zh":"當人們以個人方式處理共同想法，結果可以非常不同。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creative work around one common theme.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞一個共同主題的創作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take something in individual directions","meaning":"將……帶向個人化方向","examples":[{"en":"Other artists took Cubism in individual directions.","zh":"其他藝術家將立體主義帶向個人化方向。"},{"en":"To take something in individual directions means to develop it in personal and different ways.","zh":"take something in individual directions 指以個人而不同的方式發展它。"},{"en":"Students may take the same project in individual directions by choosing different communities to study.","zh":"學生可以選擇研究不同社區，把同一項目帶向個人化方向。"},{"en":"Individual directions make a movement more varied and less controlled by one style.","zh":"個人化方向令一場運動更多樣，而較少被單一風格控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes personal development of a shared idea.","zh":"這個短語描述對共同想法的個人發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be unfairly considered","meaning":"被不公平地認為","examples":[{"en":"Some artists are unfairly considered less important.","zh":"有些藝術家被不公平地認為較不重要。"},{"en":"To be unfairly considered something means to be judged in a way that is not just or accurate.","zh":"be unfairly considered 某事，指被以不公正或不準確方式評價。"},{"en":"Quiet students may be unfairly considered less capable because they speak less in class.","zh":"安靜學生可能因在課堂少說話而被不公平地認為能力較弱。"},{"en":"Unfair judgement can hide real talent and contribution.","zh":"不公平判斷可以掩蓋真正才能和貢獻。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a biased or incomplete evaluation.","zh":"這個短語描述有偏見或不完整的評價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"play less significant roles","meaning":"扮演較不重要的角色","examples":[{"en":"Other Cubist artists are often said to have played less significant roles.","zh":"其他立體主義藝術家常被說成扮演較不重要的角色。"},{"en":"To play less significant roles means to be seen as less important in a process or event.","zh":"play less significant roles 指在某過程或事件中被視為較不重要。"},{"en":"In a group project, a student who writes notes may seem to play a less significant role than the presenter.","zh":"在小組項目中，負責寫筆記的學生可能看似比匯報者扮演較不重要角色。"},{"en":"Some roles look small but are still necessary for success.","zh":"有些角色看似較小，但仍是成功所必需。"},{"en":"The phrase compares levels of contribution or importance.","zh":"這個短語比較貢獻或重要性的程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"simply because","meaning":"只是因為","examples":[{"en":"They were overlooked simply because they did not follow Picasso and Braque closely.","zh":"他們被忽視，只是因為他們沒有緊密跟隨 Picasso 和 Braque。"},{"en":"Simply because means for only that reason, often suggesting the reason is not enough.","zh":"simply because 指只因為那個原因，常暗示該原因並不足夠。"},{"en":"A student should not be ignored simply because she is shy.","zh":"學生不應只是因為害羞就被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase can criticise unfair judgement based on one narrow factor.","zh":"這個短語可以批評基於單一狹窄因素的不公平判斷。"},{"en":"It emphasises that the cause is too simple or limited.","zh":"它強調原因太簡單或有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"adhere to","meaning":"遵從；堅持","examples":[{"en":"Some artists did not adhere to the strict perspectives of Braque or Picasso.","zh":"有些藝術家沒有遵從 Braque 或 Picasso 的嚴格視角。"},{"en":"To adhere to something means to follow it closely and consistently.","zh":"adhere to 某事，指緊密而持續地遵從它。"},{"en":"A school must adhere to safety rules during science experiments.","zh":"學校在科學實驗中必須遵守安全規則。"},{"en":"Artists who do not adhere to one style may create more personal work.","zh":"不遵從單一風格的藝術家可能創造更個人化的作品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strict following of rules, ideas or methods.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴格跟隨規則、想法或方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"strict perspectives","meaning":"嚴格的視角","examples":[{"en":"Not all Cubist artists followed the strict perspectives of Braque and Picasso.","zh":"並非所有立體主義藝術家都跟隨 Braque 和 Picasso 的嚴格視角。"},{"en":"Strict perspectives are fixed or tightly controlled ways of seeing or representing something.","zh":"strict perspectives 是固定或嚴格控制的觀看或呈現方式。"},{"en":"A teacher with strict perspectives may accept only one method for solving a problem.","zh":"具有嚴格視角的老師可能只接受一種解題方法。"},{"en":"Strict perspectives can create clarity, but they may also limit creativity.","zh":"嚴格視角可以創造清晰度，但也可能限制創意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes narrow or controlled viewpoints.","zh":"這個短語描述狹窄或受控制的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"conceivably","meaning":"可以想像地","examples":[{"en":"Conceivably, these artists developed their own understanding of Cubism through Cezanne.","zh":"可以想像地，這些藝術家主要透過 Cezanne 發展出自己對立體主義的理解。"},{"en":"Conceivably means possibly or in a way that can be imagined as true.","zh":"conceivably 指可能地，或可以被想像為真實地。"},{"en":"Conceivably, a quiet student may understand the lesson deeply but hesitate to speak.","zh":"可以想像地，安靜學生可能深刻理解課堂，只是不敢開口。"},{"en":"The word is used when an idea is possible but not certain.","zh":"當想法可能成立但不確定時，會使用這個詞。"},{"en":"It signals cautious speculation.","zh":"它標示謹慎推測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"their own understanding of","meaning":"對……自己的理解","examples":[{"en":"Many artists developed their own understanding of Cubism.","zh":"許多藝術家發展出自己對立體主義的理解。"},{"en":"Their own understanding of something is a personal interpretation based on experience and thought.","zh":"own understanding of 某事，是基於經驗和思考的個人詮釋。"},{"en":"Students may develop their own understanding of a poem after discussing it in class.","zh":"學生在課堂討論後，可能發展出自己對一首詩的理解。"},{"en":"Personal understanding can differ from the textbook explanation.","zh":"個人理解可以不同於教科書解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses individual interpretation.","zh":"這個短語強調個人詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"primarily through","meaning":"主要透過","examples":[{"en":"They developed their ideas primarily through Cezanne’s influence.","zh":"他們主要透過 Cezanne 的影響發展想法。"},{"en":"Primarily through means mainly by means of one source, method or influence.","zh":"primarily through 指主要藉由一個來源、方法或影響。"},{"en":"A student may improve primarily through daily reading rather than grammar drills.","zh":"學生可能主要透過每日閱讀而非文法操練來進步。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main route through which development happens.","zh":"這個短語指出發展發生的主要途徑。"},{"en":"It does not mean there were no other influences.","zh":"它並不表示沒有其他影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pervading influence","meaning":"瀰漫性的影響","examples":[{"en":"Cezanne had a pervading influence on the Parisian art scene.","zh":"Cezanne 對巴黎藝術圈有瀰漫性的影響。"},{"en":"A pervading influence is an influence that spreads widely through a place or group.","zh":"pervading influence 是在一個地方或群體中廣泛散布的影響。"},{"en":"A strict exam culture can have a pervading influence on how students study.","zh":"嚴格考試文化可以對學生如何學習有瀰漫性的影響。"},{"en":"When an influence pervades a community, many people absorb it even indirectly.","zh":"當一種影響瀰漫於社群，許多人甚至會間接受到它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes influence that is widespread and hard to avoid.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛且難以避免的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"almost universal influence","meaning":"幾乎普遍的影響","examples":[{"en":"Cezanne’s influence was almost universal in the Parisian art scene.","zh":"Cezanne 的影響在巴黎藝術圈中幾乎普遍。"},{"en":"Almost universal influence means an influence felt by nearly everyone in a group.","zh":"almost universal influence 指一個群體中幾乎人人都感受到的影響。"},{"en":"Smartphones have an almost universal influence on how students communicate.","zh":"智能手機對學生如何溝通有幾乎普遍的影響。"},{"en":"When influence is almost universal, it shapes the atmosphere of a whole community.","zh":"當影響幾乎普遍，它會塑造整個社群的氣氛。"},{"en":"The phrase describes very wide but not absolutely total influence.","zh":"這個短語描述非常廣泛但並非絕對全部的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"of that day","meaning":"當時的","examples":[{"en":"Cezanne influenced the Parisian art scene of that day.","zh":"Cezanne 影響了當時的巴黎藝術圈。"},{"en":"Of that day means existing during that particular historical period.","zh":"of that day 指存在於該特定歷史時期。"},{"en":"The teachers of that day used blackboards more than digital screens.","zh":"當時的老師使用黑板多於電子屏幕。"},{"en":"The phrase helps readers understand ideas within their original time.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者在原本時代中理解想法。"},{"en":"It points to the period being discussed.","zh":"它指出正在討論的時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"true innovators","meaning":"真正的創新者","examples":[{"en":"These artists should be considered true innovators in their own right.","zh":"這些藝術家應被視為本身就是的真正創新者。"},{"en":"True innovators are people who create genuinely new ideas or methods.","zh":"true innovators 是創造真正新想法或方法的人。"},{"en":"A small shop can be a true innovator if it invents a better way to serve customers.","zh":"如果小店發明更好的顧客服務方式，它也可以是真正創新者。"},{"en":"True innovators may not be recognised immediately because their work feels unfamiliar.","zh":"真正創新者未必立即被認可，因為其作品感覺陌生。"},{"en":"The phrase praises real originality.","zh":"這個短語稱讚真正的原創性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in their own right","meaning":"憑本身條件；本身就是","examples":[{"en":"Other Cubist artists were innovators in their own right.","zh":"其他立體主義藝術家本身就是創新者。"},{"en":"In their own right means because of their own qualities, not because of someone else.","zh":"in their own right 指因其自身特質，而不是因為別人。"},{"en":"A teaching assistant can be a skilled educator in her own right, not just a helper.","zh":"教學助理本身也可以是熟練教育工作者，而不只是助手。"},{"en":"The phrase gives independent value to a person or thing.","zh":"這個短語給予人或事物獨立價值。"},{"en":"It corrects the idea that importance comes only from association.","zh":"它修正重要性只來自關聯的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"remain little recognised","meaning":"仍然鮮為人認識","examples":[{"en":"Juan Gris produced important works but remains little recognised.","zh":"Juan Gris 創作了重要作品，但仍然鮮為人認識。"},{"en":"To remain little recognised means to continue receiving little public or professional recognition.","zh":"remain little recognised 指繼續很少得到公眾或專業認可。"},{"en":"A helpful school cleaner may remain little recognised even though daily life depends on her work.","zh":"有幫助的學校清潔工即使支撐日常生活，也可能仍然鮮為人認識。"},{"en":"Important contributions can remain hidden if attention goes to more famous people.","zh":"如果注意力集中在更有名的人身上，重要貢獻可以保持隱藏。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ongoing lack of recognition.","zh":"這個短語描述持續缺乏認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"compatriot of","meaning":"……的同胞","examples":[{"en":"As a compatriot of Picasso, Gris became acquainted with him.","zh":"作為 Picasso 的同胞，Gris 與他相識。"},{"en":"A compatriot of someone is a person from the same country.","zh":"compatriot of 某人，是與該人來自同一國家的人。"},{"en":"A Spanish student may feel comfortable meeting a compatriot of hers in a foreign university.","zh":"西班牙學生在外國大學遇到同胞時，可能感到自在。"},{"en":"Shared nationality can create an early connection between people.","zh":"共同國籍可以在人與人之間創造早期連結。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a link through country of origin.","zh":"這個短語指出透過原籍國形成的聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"become personally acquainted with","meaning":"與……私下相識","examples":[{"en":"Gris became personally acquainted with Picasso.","zh":"Gris 與 Picasso 私下相識。"},{"en":"To become personally acquainted with someone means to get to know them directly, not just by reputation.","zh":"become personally acquainted with 某人，指直接認識他，而不是只知道其名聲。"},{"en":"A student may become personally acquainted with a writer after attending a workshop.","zh":"學生參加工作坊後，可能與一位作家私下相識。"},{"en":"Personal acquaintance can lead to conversation, influence or collaboration.","zh":"私人認識可以帶來對話、影響或合作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct personal familiarity.","zh":"這個短語描述直接的個人熟悉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"well-known portrait","meaning":"著名肖像畫","examples":[{"en":"Gris painted his well-known Portrait of Picasso.","zh":"Gris 畫了他著名的《Picasso 肖像》。"},{"en":"A well-known portrait is a famous painting or image of a person.","zh":"well-known portrait 是一幅著名的人物畫像或圖像。"},{"en":"A school may display a well-known portrait of its founder in the hall.","zh":"學校可能在禮堂展示創校人的著名肖像。"},{"en":"Portraits become well-known when they capture a person in a memorable style.","zh":"當肖像以令人難忘的風格捕捉人物，它就會變得有名。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a recognised image of someone.","zh":"這個短語描述廣為人知的人物圖像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be regarded as","meaning":"被視為","examples":[{"en":"Portrait of Picasso is now regarded as a strong example of Cubism.","zh":"《Picasso 肖像》現在被視為立體主義的有力例子。"},{"en":"To be regarded as something means to be considered or seen in that way.","zh":"be regarded as 某物，指被認為或看作那樣。"},{"en":"A student may be regarded as reliable if she always submits work on time.","zh":"如果學生總是準時交功課，她可能被視為可靠。"},{"en":"How something is regarded can change as people understand it better.","zh":"隨着人們更了解某物，它被如何看待可以改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes public or expert judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾或專家的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"one of the best examples of","meaning":"……的最佳例子之一","examples":[{"en":"Portrait of Picasso is one of the best examples of the Cubist style.","zh":"《Picasso 肖像》是立體主義風格的最佳例子之一。"},{"en":"One of the best examples of something is a case that shows it very clearly and successfully.","zh":"one of the best examples of 某事，是非常清楚且成功展示它的案例。"},{"en":"A clear student essay may be one of the best examples of good paragraphing.","zh":"一篇清晰學生文章可能是良好分段的最佳例子之一。"},{"en":"Good examples help learners understand the main features of a style or idea.","zh":"好例子幫助學習者理解某風格或想法的主要特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a highly representative case.","zh":"這個短語指出高度具代表性的案例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Cubist style","meaning":"立體主義風格","examples":[{"en":"The painting is regarded as an excellent example of the Cubist style.","zh":"這幅畫被視為立體主義風格的優秀例子。"},{"en":"Cubist style is the visual style of Cubism, often using fragmented shapes and multiple viewpoints.","zh":"Cubist style 是立體主義的視覺風格，常使用碎片化形狀和多重視角。"},{"en":"In art class, students may imitate Cubist style by drawing a guitar from several angles.","zh":"在美術課中，學生可能透過從幾個角度畫結他來模仿立體主義風格。"},{"en":"The style can make ordinary objects look broken, geometric and reassembled.","zh":"這種風格可以令普通物件看起來被打碎、幾何化並重新組合。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the recognisable appearance of Cubist art.","zh":"這個短語指立體主義藝術可辨認的外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"venture beyond","meaning":"超越；突破","examples":[{"en":"Gris ventured beyond the monochromatic style of Picasso and Braque.","zh":"Gris 突破了 Picasso 和 Braque 的單色風格。"},{"en":"To venture beyond something means to go further than an established limit or style.","zh":"venture beyond 某事，指走得比既定限制或風格更遠。"},{"en":"A student may venture beyond simple sentences when she starts using clauses confidently.","zh":"當學生開始自信地使用從句，她就超越了簡單句。"},{"en":"Venturing beyond a familiar method can create risk but also originality.","zh":"突破熟悉方法可能有風險，但也能帶來原創性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bold movement past an existing boundary.","zh":"這個短語描述大膽越過現有界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"monochromatic","meaning":"單色的","examples":[{"en":"Picasso and Braque often employed a monochromatic approach.","zh":"Picasso 和 Braque 常使用單色做法。"},{"en":"Monochromatic means using one colour or one family of similar colours.","zh":"monochromatic 指使用一種顏色或同一色系。"},{"en":"A monochromatic poster may use only blue shades to create a calm mood.","zh":"單色海報可能只使用藍色調來營造平靜氣氛。"},{"en":"Limiting colour can make viewers focus more on shape and structure.","zh":"限制顏色可以令觀眾更集中於形狀和結構。"},{"en":"The word describes a single-colour visual approach.","zh":"這個詞描述單一色彩的視覺方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"single family of colours","meaning":"單一色系","examples":[{"en":"Monochromatic works use a single family of colours.","zh":"單色作品使用單一色系。"},{"en":"A single family of colours is a group of related shades from one main colour.","zh":"single family of colours 是來自一種主色的相關色調群。"},{"en":"A room decorated with light blue, dark blue and grey-blue uses a single family of colours.","zh":"用淺藍、深藍和灰藍裝飾的房間使用單一色系。"},{"en":"Using one colour family can make a design feel unified.","zh":"使用一個色系可以令設計感覺統一。"},{"en":"The phrase describes colour choices that stay within one range.","zh":"這個短語描述停留在同一範圍內的色彩選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be employed by","meaning":"被……使用","examples":[{"en":"Monochromatic colour schemes were employed by Picasso and Braque.","zh":"單色色彩方案被 Picasso 和 Braque 使用。"},{"en":"To be employed by someone means to be used by that person.","zh":"be employed by 某人，指被該人使用。"},{"en":"Clear diagrams are often employed by teachers to explain difficult grammar.","zh":"老師常使用清楚圖表來解釋困難文法。"},{"en":"A method is employed when someone chooses it for a purpose.","zh":"當某人為某目的選擇一種方法，它就被使用。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to say “used by”.","zh":"這個短語是 “used by” 的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"vibrant hues","meaning":"鮮明色調","examples":[{"en":"Gris combined vibrant hues in unusual ways.","zh":"Gris 以不尋常方式結合鮮明色調。"},{"en":"Vibrant hues are bright, strong and lively colours.","zh":"vibrant hues 是明亮、強烈而有活力的顏色。"},{"en":"A festival poster may use vibrant hues to attract attention from far away.","zh":"節日海報可能使用鮮明色調，以從遠處吸引注意。"},{"en":"Bright colours can create energy and emotion in a design.","zh":"明亮顏色可以在設計中創造活力和情緒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes vivid colour tones.","zh":"這個短語描述鮮艷的色彩色調。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"unusual combinations","meaning":"不尋常的組合","examples":[{"en":"Gris used bright colours in unusual combinations.","zh":"Gris 以不尋常的組合使用鮮艷色彩。"},{"en":"Unusual combinations are pairings or mixtures that people do not normally expect.","zh":"unusual combinations 是人們通常不預期的配搭或混合。"},{"en":"A café may create unusual combinations by mixing local tea with fruit flavours.","zh":"咖啡店可能把本地茶與水果味混合，創造不尋常組合。"},{"en":"Unusual combinations can surprise people and create a distinctive style.","zh":"不尋常的組合可以令人驚喜並創造獨特風格。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unexpected mixtures.","zh":"這個短語描述意想不到的混合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"still life","meaning":"靜物畫","examples":[{"en":"Newspaper and Fruit Dish is a still life by Gris.","zh":"《報紙與果盤》是 Gris 的一幅靜物畫。"},{"en":"A still life is an artwork showing arranged objects such as fruit, bottles or books.","zh":"still life 是展示水果、瓶子或書本等擺放物件的藝術作品。"},{"en":"Students may paint a still life of cups and apples in art class.","zh":"學生可能在美術課畫杯子和蘋果的靜物畫。"},{"en":"Still-life painting trains artists to study shape, light and composition.","zh":"靜物畫訓練藝術家研究形狀、光線和構圖。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to art focused on objects rather than people or landscapes.","zh":"這個短語指專注物件而非人物或風景的藝術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"become known as","meaning":"後來被稱為","examples":[{"en":"The Orphic Cubists later became known for bright colour and abstraction.","zh":"俄耳甫斯立體主義者後來以鮮艷色彩和抽象而聞名。"},{"en":"To become known as or for something means to gain a reputation connected with it.","zh":"become known as or for 某事，指獲得與其相關的名聲。"},{"en":"A school may become known for strong music programmes after years of concerts.","zh":"學校多年舉辦音樂會後，可能以強大的音樂課程聞名。"},{"en":"Repeated style or success can shape how people remember a group.","zh":"反覆風格或成功可以塑造人們如何記住一個群體。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the formation of reputation.","zh":"這個短語描述名聲的形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"similarly exploratory","meaning":"同樣具探索性的","examples":[{"en":"The Orphic Cubists were similarly exploratory in their use of colour.","zh":"俄耳甫斯立體主義者在色彩使用上同樣具探索性。"},{"en":"Similarly exploratory means also willing to try new ideas or methods.","zh":"similarly exploratory 指同樣願意嘗試新想法或方法。"},{"en":"A student may be similarly exploratory if she tests different ways to plan essays.","zh":"如果學生測試不同文章規劃方法，她也可以同樣具探索性。"},{"en":"Exploratory work can lead to new styles because people are not limited by old habits.","zh":"探索性工作可以帶來新風格，因為人們不受舊習慣限制。"},{"en":"The phrase compares two groups that both experiment.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個同樣實驗的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"move further towards","meaning":"進一步走向","examples":[{"en":"Some artists moved further towards abstraction.","zh":"有些藝術家進一步走向抽象。"},{"en":"To move further towards something means to become closer to that style, state or goal.","zh":"move further towards 某事，指更接近該風格、狀態或目標。"},{"en":"A student may move further towards independence when she plans her own revision schedule.","zh":"當學生自己規劃溫習時間表，她可能進一步走向獨立。"},{"en":"Gradual movement towards a goal can happen through repeated choices.","zh":"透過反覆選擇，可以逐漸朝目標前進。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continuing development in one direction.","zh":"這個短語描述朝一個方向持續發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"abstraction","meaning":"抽象","examples":[{"en":"Orphic Cubists moved further towards abstraction.","zh":"俄耳甫斯立體主義者進一步走向抽象。"},{"en":"Abstraction is art or thinking that moves away from realistic representation.","zh":"abstraction 是遠離寫實呈現的藝術或思考方式。"},{"en":"A painting of emotions using only colours and shapes is an example of abstraction.","zh":"只用顏色和形狀表達情緒的畫作就是抽象例子。"},{"en":"Abstraction can make viewers focus on feeling, form or idea rather than exact objects.","zh":"抽象可以令觀眾集中於感覺、形式或想法，而不是精確物件。"},{"en":"The word describes movement away from literal appearance.","zh":"這個詞描述遠離字面外觀的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"share someone’s use of","meaning":"共享某人的……用法","examples":[{"en":"The Orphic Cubists shared Gris’s use of bright colours.","zh":"俄耳甫斯立體主義者共享 Gris 對鮮艷色彩的用法。"},{"en":"To share someone’s use of something means to use the same technique or feature as that person.","zh":"share someone’s use of 某物，指使用與某人相同的技巧或特徵。"},{"en":"A student may share her teacher’s use of clear examples when explaining grammar to classmates.","zh":"學生向同學解釋文法時，可能採用老師使用清楚例子的做法。"},{"en":"Shared use can show influence or common artistic interest.","zh":"共同使用可以顯示影響或共同藝術興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes similarity in method.","zh":"這個短語描述方法上的相似。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"bright colours","meaning":"鮮艷色彩","examples":[{"en":"Some Cubists used bright colours to convey meaning.","zh":"有些立體主義者使用鮮艷色彩來傳達意義。"},{"en":"Bright colours are strong, vivid colours that attract attention.","zh":"bright colours 是強烈、鮮明並吸引注意的顏色。"},{"en":"A safety poster may use bright colours so people notice the warning quickly.","zh":"安全海報可能使用鮮艷色彩，令人快速注意警告。"},{"en":"Bright colours can create energy, joy, danger or contrast in an image.","zh":"鮮艷色彩可以在圖像中創造活力、喜悅、危險或對比。"},{"en":"The phrase describes colours that stand out clearly.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚突出的顏色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"convey meaning","meaning":"傳達意義","examples":[{"en":"Colours were used to convey meaning.","zh":"色彩被用來傳達意義。"},{"en":"To convey meaning means to communicate an idea, feeling or message.","zh":"convey meaning 指傳達想法、感覺或訊息。"},{"en":"A red warning sign conveys meaning quickly even before people read the words.","zh":"紅色警告標誌在人們讀字前已能快速傳達意義。"},{"en":"Artists can convey meaning through colour, shape, gesture or composition.","zh":"藝術家可以透過顏色、形狀、姿勢或構圖傳達意義。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how something communicates.","zh":"這個短語描述某物如何溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be blended in a way that","meaning":"以一種……的方式融合","examples":[{"en":"The colours were blended in a way that moved beyond the physical subject.","zh":"這些色彩以一種超越實際主體的方式融合。"},{"en":"To be blended in a way that means to be mixed so that a particular effect is created.","zh":"be blended in a way that 指被混合，以創造某種特定效果。"},{"en":"A drink may be blended in a way that makes sour fruit taste smooth.","zh":"飲品可以以一種令酸水果味道變順滑的方式調配。"},{"en":"How elements are blended can change the viewer’s feeling or interpretation.","zh":"元素如何融合可以改變觀眾的感受或詮釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mixing with a specific result.","zh":"這個短語描述具有特定結果的混合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"go beyond","meaning":"超越","examples":[{"en":"Orphic Cubist colour went beyond the physical subject.","zh":"俄耳甫斯立體主義色彩超越了實際主體。"},{"en":"To go beyond something means to move past its usual limits or literal meaning.","zh":"go beyond 某事，指越過其通常限制或字面意思。"},{"en":"A good apology goes beyond saying sorry because it includes changed behaviour.","zh":"好的道歉超越說對不起，因為它包括行為改變。"},{"en":"Art goes beyond description when it expresses emotion or ideas.","zh":"當藝術表達情緒或想法，它就超越了描述。"},{"en":"The phrase describes exceeding a basic level.","zh":"這個短語描述超過基本層次。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the physical subject","meaning":"實際主體","examples":[{"en":"The painting goes beyond the physical subject it represents.","zh":"這幅畫超越了它所代表的實際主體。"},{"en":"The physical subject is the actual object, person or scene shown in an artwork.","zh":"physical subject 是藝術作品中呈現的實際物件、人物或場景。"},{"en":"In a portrait, the physical subject may be a student sitting in a chair.","zh":"在肖像畫中，實際主體可能是坐在椅子上的學生。"},{"en":"Art can go beyond the physical subject by showing mood, memory or movement.","zh":"藝術可以透過呈現氣氛、記憶或動感來超越實際主體。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the real visible thing being represented.","zh":"這個短語指被呈現的真實可見事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"main proponent","meaning":"主要倡導者","examples":[{"en":"Robert Delaunay was the main proponent of Orphic Cubism.","zh":"Robert Delaunay 是俄耳甫斯立體主義的主要倡導者。"},{"en":"A main proponent is a leading supporter or promoter of an idea.","zh":"main proponent 是某想法的主要支持者或推動者。"},{"en":"A teacher may be the main proponent of using drama in language lessons.","zh":"老師可能是語文課使用戲劇的主要倡導者。"},{"en":"Main proponents spread ideas by explaining, practising and defending them.","zh":"主要倡導者透過解釋、實踐和捍衛想法來傳播它們。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the strongest advocate.","zh":"這個短語指出最主要的支持者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"together with","meaning":"與……一起","examples":[{"en":"Delaunay, together with his wife, exhibited regularly in Paris.","zh":"Delaunay 與他的妻子一起定期在巴黎展出。"},{"en":"Together with means along with or in addition to someone or something.","zh":"together with 指與某人或某物一起，或加上某人某物。"},{"en":"A student, together with her classmates, organised a charity sale.","zh":"一名學生與同學一起組織慈善義賣。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that people or things acted as a group.","zh":"這個短語顯示人或事物作為群體行動。"},{"en":"It adds another participant to the main subject.","zh":"它為主要主語加入另一參與者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"regularly exhibit","meaning":"定期展出","examples":[{"en":"Delaunay and his wife regularly exhibited in Parisian salons.","zh":"Delaunay 和他的妻子定期在巴黎沙龍展出作品。"},{"en":"To regularly exhibit means to display work publicly again and again over time.","zh":"regularly exhibit 指隨時間一次又一次公開展示作品。"},{"en":"A school art club may regularly exhibit student paintings in the library.","zh":"學校藝術學會可能定期在圖書館展出學生畫作。"},{"en":"Regular exhibition helps artists build recognition and reach audiences.","zh":"定期展出幫助藝術家建立認知度並接觸觀眾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated public showing of work.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆公開展示作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Parisian salons","meaning":"巴黎沙龍","examples":[{"en":"Artists exhibited their works in Parisian salons.","zh":"藝術家在巴黎沙龍展出作品。"},{"en":"Parisian salons were public or semi-public art exhibitions held in Paris.","zh":"Parisian salons 是在巴黎舉行的公開或半公開藝術展覽。"},{"en":"Young artists hoped to show their paintings in Parisian salons to gain attention.","zh":"年輕藝術家希望在巴黎沙龍展示畫作以獲得關注。"},{"en":"Salons mattered because critics, buyers and other artists could see new work there.","zh":"沙龍重要，因為評論家、買家和其他藝術家都能在那裏看見新作品。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to important Paris art exhibition spaces.","zh":"這個短語指巴黎重要藝術展覽空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"increasingly non-representational forms","meaning":"越來越非具象的形式","examples":[{"en":"Delaunay’s works used increasingly non-representational forms.","zh":"Delaunay 的作品使用越來越非具象的形式。"},{"en":"Increasingly non-representational forms are shapes that become less and less like real objects.","zh":"increasingly non-representational forms 是越來越不像真實物件的形狀。"},{"en":"A student’s drawing may move from a realistic tree to increasingly non-representational forms.","zh":"學生的畫可能從寫實樹木走向越來越非具象的形式。"},{"en":"As forms become less realistic, viewers focus more on colour, rhythm and structure.","zh":"當形式變得較不寫實，觀眾會更集中於色彩、節奏和結構。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a gradual movement toward abstraction.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸走向抽象的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"barely recognisable as","meaning":"幾乎看不出是","examples":[{"en":"Simultaneous Windows is barely recognisable as a window.","zh":"《同時的窗》幾乎看不出是窗。"},{"en":"Barely recognisable as something means almost impossible to identify as that thing.","zh":"barely recognisable as 某物，指幾乎不能辨認為該物。"},{"en":"A badly damaged sign may be barely recognisable as a school notice.","zh":"嚴重損壞的告示可能幾乎看不出是學校通告。"},{"en":"In abstract art, the original object may become hard to recognise.","zh":"在抽象藝術中，原本物件可能變得難以辨認。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an image that only slightly resembles its subject.","zh":"這個短語描述只略為像其主體的圖像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a blend of","meaning":"……的混合","examples":[{"en":"The painting is a blend of prismatic hues.","zh":"這幅畫是棱鏡般色調的混合。"},{"en":"A blend of things is a mixture of them.","zh":"blend of 某些事物，指它們的混合。"},{"en":"A good class discussion is a blend of teacher guidance and student ideas.","zh":"好的課堂討論是老師指導和學生想法的混合。"},{"en":"Blending elements can create a result that feels richer than one element alone.","zh":"融合元素可以創造比單一元素更豐富的結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a mixture or combination.","zh":"這個短語描述混合或結合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"prismatic hues","meaning":"棱鏡般的色調","examples":[{"en":"Simultaneous Windows contains a blend of prismatic hues.","zh":"《同時的窗》包含棱鏡般色調的混合。"},{"en":"Prismatic hues are bright colours like those seen when light passes through a prism.","zh":"prismatic hues 是像光線穿過棱鏡時出現的鮮明色彩。"},{"en":"A soap bubble may show prismatic hues when sunlight hits it.","zh":"肥皂泡在陽光照射下可能顯示棱鏡般的色調。"},{"en":"Such hues can make a painting feel luminous and energetic.","zh":"這類色調可以令畫作感覺明亮而有活力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rainbow-like colour tones.","zh":"這個短語描述彩虹般的色彩色調。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"prominent square","meaning":"顯眼的正方形","examples":[{"en":"The painting contains one prominent square.","zh":"這幅畫包含一個顯眼的正方形。"},{"en":"A prominent square is a square shape that stands out clearly.","zh":"prominent square 是清楚突出的正方形。"},{"en":"A poster may use a prominent square to frame the event date.","zh":"海報可能使用顯眼的正方形來框住活動日期。"},{"en":"A prominent shape guides the viewer’s attention to one part of the image.","zh":"顯眼形狀會把觀眾注意力引向圖像某部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a clearly noticeable square form.","zh":"這個短語描述明顯可見的正方形形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"give a hint of","meaning":"給人一點……的暗示","examples":[{"en":"The prominent square gives a hint of three-dimensionality.","zh":"顯眼的正方形給人一點三維感的暗示。"},{"en":"To give a hint of something means to suggest it slightly without showing it fully.","zh":"give a hint of 某事，指稍微暗示它，而不完全展示。"},{"en":"A dark cloud gives a hint of rain before the storm arrives.","zh":"暴風雨到來前，烏雲給人一點下雨的暗示。"},{"en":"Small visual clues can give a hint of depth, movement or emotion.","zh":"小小視覺線索可以給人深度、動感或情緒的暗示。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a subtle suggestion.","zh":"這個短語描述微妙提示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"three-dimensionality","meaning":"三維感；立體感","examples":[{"en":"The square gives a hint of three-dimensionality.","zh":"正方形給人一點三維感。"},{"en":"Three-dimensionality is the quality of seeming to have depth as well as height and width.","zh":"three-dimensionality 是看起來除了高度和闊度外還有深度的特質。"},{"en":"Shading can give a drawing three-dimensionality by making a flat circle look like a ball.","zh":"陰影可以令平面圓形看起來像球，從而給圖畫三維感。"},{"en":"Without three-dimensionality, an image may look completely flat.","zh":"沒有三維感，圖像可能看起來完全平面。"},{"en":"The word describes the visual feeling of depth.","zh":"這個詞描述視覺上的深度感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a personal form of","meaning":"個人化的……形式","examples":[{"en":"Léger followed a more personal form of Cubism.","zh":"Léger 跟隨一種更個人化的立體主義形式。"},{"en":"A personal form of something is an individual version shaped by one person’s style or ideas.","zh":"personal form of 某事，是由某人風格或想法塑造的個人版本。"},{"en":"A student may develop a personal form of note-taking that uses drawings and keywords.","zh":"學生可能發展出使用圖畫和關鍵詞的個人化筆記形式。"},{"en":"Personal forms allow shared ideas to become distinctive.","zh":"個人化形式讓共同想法變得獨特。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an individual version of a broader style.","zh":"這個短語描述更廣泛風格中的個人版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as with","meaning":"與……一樣","examples":[{"en":"As with most artists of his generation, Léger saw the Cezanne retrospective.","zh":"與他那一代的大多數藝術家一樣，Léger 看過 Cezanne 回顧展。"},{"en":"As with means as was also true of another person or group.","zh":"as with 指某情況對另一人或群體也同樣成立。"},{"en":"As with many students, she improved after receiving clear feedback.","zh":"與許多學生一樣，她在收到清楚回饋後進步。"},{"en":"The phrase compares one case with a wider pattern.","zh":"這個短語把一個個案與更廣泛模式比較。"},{"en":"It shows that the example is not isolated.","zh":"它顯示例子並非孤立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"most of his generation","meaning":"他那一代的大多數人","examples":[{"en":"Most of his generation had seen the Cezanne retrospective.","zh":"他那一代的大多數人都看過 Cezanne 回顧展。"},{"en":"Most of his generation means the majority of people about his age or artistic period.","zh":"most of his generation 指與他年齡或藝術時期相近的大多數人。"},{"en":"Most of her generation grew up using smartphones at school and at home.","zh":"她那一代的大多數人在學校和家中使用智能手機長大。"},{"en":"Generational experience can shape people’s habits, taste and ideas.","zh":"世代經驗可以塑造人們的習慣、品味和想法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a broad age or time group.","zh":"這個短語指廣泛的年齡或時代群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"enkindle interest in","meaning":"激發對……的興趣","examples":[{"en":"The retrospective enkindled interest in geometric experimentation.","zh":"回顧展激發了對幾何實驗的興趣。"},{"en":"To enkindle interest in something means to awaken or strongly encourage interest in it.","zh":"enkindle interest in 某事，指喚起或強烈鼓勵對它的興趣。"},{"en":"A museum visit may enkindle interest in history for a quiet student.","zh":"博物館參觀可能激發安靜學生對歷史的興趣。"},{"en":"A powerful example can turn mild curiosity into active exploration.","zh":"有力例子可以把輕微好奇轉化為主動探索。"},{"en":"The phrase describes interest being sparked.","zh":"這個短語描述興趣被點燃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"experimentation with","meaning":"對……的實驗","examples":[{"en":"Léger developed an interest in experimentation with geometric forms.","zh":"Léger 發展出對幾何形式實驗的興趣。"},{"en":"Experimentation with something means trying new ways of using it.","zh":"experimentation with 某事，指嘗試使用它的新方式。"},{"en":"A student may enjoy experimentation with sentence patterns when learning writing.","zh":"學生學寫作時可能享受對句式的實驗。"},{"en":"Experimentation can reveal possibilities that fixed rules hide.","zh":"實驗可以揭示固定規則所隱藏的可能性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active testing of forms, methods or materials.","zh":"這個短語描述對形式、方法或材料的主動測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"geometric forms","meaning":"幾何形式","examples":[{"en":"Léger experimented with geometric forms in his paintings.","zh":"Léger 在畫作中實驗幾何形式。"},{"en":"Geometric forms are shapes based on geometry, such as cubes, cones, circles and rectangles.","zh":"geometric forms 是基於幾何的形狀，例如立方體、圓錐、圓形和長方形。"},{"en":"A playground design may use geometric forms like circles and squares.","zh":"遊樂場設計可能使用圓形和正方形等幾何形式。"},{"en":"Geometric forms can make a picture look ordered, mechanical or abstract.","zh":"幾何形式可以令圖畫看起來有秩序、機械化或抽象。"},{"en":"The phrase describes structured mathematical shapes in design or art.","zh":"這個短語描述設計或藝術中的結構化數學形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"eventually lead to","meaning":"最終導致","examples":[{"en":"This experimentation eventually led to complete abstraction.","zh":"這種實驗最終導致完全抽象。"},{"en":"To eventually lead to something means to cause that result after some time.","zh":"eventually lead to 某事，指在一段時間後造成該結果。"},{"en":"Daily reading may eventually lead to stronger vocabulary.","zh":"每日閱讀可能最終導致更強詞彙量。"},{"en":"A process may not show results immediately, but repeated action can create change.","zh":"一個過程未必立即見效，但反覆行動可以創造改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a later result of earlier actions.","zh":"這個短語描述早前行動的後來結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"complete abstraction","meaning":"完全抽象","examples":[{"en":"Léger’s experiments eventually led to complete abstraction.","zh":"Léger 的實驗最終導致完全抽象。"},{"en":"Complete abstraction is art that no longer clearly represents real objects.","zh":"complete abstraction 是不再清楚代表真實物件的藝術。"},{"en":"A painting made only of lines, colours and shapes may show complete abstraction.","zh":"只由線條、顏色和形狀構成的畫作可能顯示完全抽象。"},{"en":"Complete abstraction asks viewers to respond to form and feeling rather than recognise objects.","zh":"完全抽象要求觀眾回應形式和感覺，而不是辨認物件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the far end of non-representational art.","zh":"這個短語描述非具象藝術的極端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"tubes, cones, and cubes","meaning":"圓管、圓錐和立方體","examples":[{"en":"Tubes, cones, and cubes are splayed on the canvas.","zh":"圓管、圓錐和立方體被鋪展在畫布上。"},{"en":"Tubes, cones and cubes are simple geometric solid shapes.","zh":"tubes, cones and cubes 是簡單的幾何立體形狀。"},{"en":"Children may use paper tubes, cones and cubes to build a model city.","zh":"孩子可能用紙圓管、圓錐和立方體建造模型城市。"},{"en":"In painting, these shapes can replace natural forms and make a scene look mechanical.","zh":"在繪畫中，這些形狀可以取代自然形態，令場景看起來機械化。"},{"en":"The phrase lists basic three-dimensional forms.","zh":"這個短語列出基本三維形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be splayed on","meaning":"被鋪展在……上","examples":[{"en":"Geometric forms are splayed on the canvas in bold colours.","zh":"幾何形式以大膽色彩被鋪展在畫布上。"},{"en":"To be splayed on something means to be spread out across a surface.","zh":"be splayed on 某物，指被攤開或鋪散在一個表面上。"},{"en":"Art supplies may be splayed on a classroom table before a project begins.","zh":"項目開始前，美術用品可能被鋪展在課室桌面上。"},{"en":"Splayed shapes can create a scattered or energetic visual effect.","zh":"鋪散的形狀可以創造分散或有活力的視覺效果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes elements spread outward over an area.","zh":"這個短語描述元素向外散布於某範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"bold primary colours","meaning":"大膽的原色","examples":[{"en":"Léger used bold primary colours in Railway Crossing.","zh":"Léger 在《鐵路交叉口》中使用大膽的原色。"},{"en":"Bold primary colours are strong versions of red, blue and yellow.","zh":"bold primary colours 是強烈版本的紅、藍和黃。"},{"en":"A children’s playground may use bold primary colours to feel lively and easy to notice.","zh":"兒童遊樂場可能使用大膽原色，使環境感覺活潑並容易注意。"},{"en":"Strong colours can create energy and make shapes stand out.","zh":"強烈顏色可以創造活力並令形狀突出。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bright basic colours used confidently.","zh":"這個短語描述被自信使用的鮮明基本色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in spite of","meaning":"儘管","examples":[{"en":"In spite of its non-representational quality, the work suggests modern alienation.","zh":"儘管該作品具有非具象特質，它仍暗示現代生活的疏離感。"},{"en":"In spite of means despite or although something is true.","zh":"in spite of 指儘管或雖然某事成立。"},{"en":"In spite of heavy rain, the students arrived at school on time.","zh":"儘管下大雨，學生仍準時到校。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a contrast between a difficulty and an unexpected result.","zh":"這個短語引出困難與意外結果之間的對比。"},{"en":"It shows that one fact does not prevent another.","zh":"它顯示一個事實不會阻止另一事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"non-representational quality","meaning":"非具象特質","examples":[{"en":"Railway Crossing has a non-representational quality.","zh":"《鐵路交叉口》具有非具象特質。"},{"en":"A non-representational quality means the work does not clearly show real objects or scenes.","zh":"non-representational quality 指作品沒有清楚呈現真實物件或場景。"},{"en":"An abstract poster with only colour blocks has a non-representational quality.","zh":"只有色塊的抽象海報具有非具象特質。"},{"en":"This quality can make viewers search for mood and structure instead of objects.","zh":"這種特質可以令觀眾尋找氣氛和結構，而不是物件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a move away from realistic representation.","zh":"這個短語描述遠離寫實呈現的特質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the suggestion of","meaning":"對……的暗示","examples":[{"en":"The painting contains the suggestion of harsh mechanisation.","zh":"這幅畫包含對冷酷機械化的暗示。"},{"en":"The suggestion of something is a hint or impression of it, not a direct statement.","zh":"suggestion of 某事，是對它的提示或印象，而不是直接說明。"},{"en":"A quiet scene with empty chairs may contain the suggestion of loneliness.","zh":"有空椅子的安靜場景可能包含對孤獨的暗示。"},{"en":"Suggestions let artists communicate ideas indirectly.","zh":"暗示讓藝術家間接傳達想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an implied meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述隱含意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"harsh mechanisation","meaning":"冷酷的機械化","examples":[{"en":"The painting suggests the harsh mechanisation of modern life.","zh":"這幅畫暗示現代生活中冷酷的機械化。"},{"en":"Harsh mechanisation is the cold, hard or dehumanising effect of machines and industrial systems.","zh":"harsh mechanisation 是機器和工業系統造成的冰冷、強硬或非人化效果。"},{"en":"A factory schedule that treats workers like parts of a machine may show harsh mechanisation.","zh":"把工人當成機器零件的工廠時間表，可能顯示冷酷的機械化。"},{"en":"Mechanisation can increase efficiency but also make life feel impersonal.","zh":"機械化可以提高效率，但也可以令生活感覺沒有人情味。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises the severe human cost of machine-like systems.","zh":"這個短語批評機械式系統帶來的嚴重人性代價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"alienation of modern life","meaning":"現代生活的疏離感","examples":[{"en":"Léger’s work suggests the alienation of modern life.","zh":"Léger 的作品暗示現代生活的疏離感。"},{"en":"Alienation of modern life means the loneliness or disconnection people may feel in modern society.","zh":"alienation of modern life 指人在現代社會中可能感到的孤獨或斷裂感。"},{"en":"A worker in a huge city may feel the alienation of modern life despite being surrounded by people.","zh":"大城市中的工人即使被人群包圍，也可能感到現代生活的疏離感。"},{"en":"Busy systems, machines and crowds can make individuals feel less connected.","zh":"忙碌系統、機器和人群可以令人感到較少連繫。"},{"en":"The phrase describes emotional distance in modern living.","zh":"這個短語描述現代生活中的情感距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"accentuate a theme","meaning":"強化一個主題","examples":[{"en":"The artist’s experience in World War One accentuated this theme.","zh":"藝術家在第一次世界大戰中的經歷強化了這個主題。"},{"en":"To accentuate a theme means to make an idea stronger, clearer or more noticeable.","zh":"accentuate a theme 指令一個想法更強、更清楚或更明顯。"},{"en":"A sad ending can accentuate a theme of loneliness in a story.","zh":"悲傷結局可以強化故事中的孤獨主題。"},{"en":"Personal experience often strengthens themes that artists already care about.","zh":"個人經歷常會加強藝術家本來關心的主題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a central idea more powerful.","zh":"這個短語描述令中心思想更有力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"World War One","meaning":"第一次世界大戰","examples":[{"en":"Léger’s experiences in World War One influenced his artistic themes.","zh":"Léger 在第一次世界大戰中的經歷影響了他的藝術主題。"},{"en":"World War One was a major global war fought from 1914 to 1918.","zh":"World War One 是1914年至1918年間爆發的一場重大世界戰爭。"},{"en":"Artists who lived through World War One often responded to violence, machines and loss.","zh":"經歷第一次世界大戰的藝術家常回應暴力、機器和失去。"},{"en":"War experiences can change how people view modern society.","zh":"戰爭經歷可以改變人們如何看待現代社會。"},{"en":"The phrase names a historical conflict that shaped twentieth-century culture.","zh":"這個短語指出一場塑造二十世紀文化的歷史衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"predate similar trends","meaning":"比類似趨勢早出現","examples":[{"en":"Léger’s work predates similar trends by decades.","zh":"Léger 的作品比類似趨勢早出現數十年。"},{"en":"To predate similar trends means to appear before later movements that look related.","zh":"predate similar trends 指早於後來看似相關的運動出現。"},{"en":"A teacher’s early online lessons may predate similar trends in digital education.","zh":"老師早期的網上課可能比數碼教育的類似趨勢更早出現。"},{"en":"Work that predates a trend can later look surprisingly modern.","zh":"早於趨勢的作品後來可能看起來出奇地現代。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being ahead of comparable developments.","zh":"這個短語描述早於可比較的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"by decades","meaning":"早了數十年","examples":[{"en":"His work predates pop art by decades.","zh":"他的作品比普普藝術早了數十年。"},{"en":"By decades means by many tens of years.","zh":"by decades 指相差許多個十年。"},{"en":"Some safety rules existed by decades before smartphones became common.","zh":"有些安全規則在智能手機普及前數十年已存在。"},{"en":"A work that is ahead by decades may not be fully understood at first.","zh":"超前數十年的作品起初可能未被完全理解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large time gap measured in decades.","zh":"這個短語描述以數十年計算的大時間差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"pop art","meaning":"普普藝術","examples":[{"en":"Léger’s work predates later trends such as pop art.","zh":"Léger 的作品比普普藝術等後來趨勢更早出現。"},{"en":"Pop art is an art movement that uses images from popular culture, advertising and everyday products.","zh":"pop art 是使用流行文化、廣告和日常產品圖像的藝術運動。"},{"en":"A pop art poster may turn a soup can or comic image into colourful art.","zh":"普普藝術海報可能把湯罐或漫畫圖像變成彩色藝術。"},{"en":"Pop art often blurs the line between fine art and mass culture.","zh":"普普藝術常模糊高雅藝術與大眾文化之間的界線。"},{"en":"The phrase names a later modern art movement.","zh":"這個短語指出一場較後期的現代藝術運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a complex art movement","meaning":"複雜的藝術運動","examples":[{"en":"Cubism was clearly a complex art movement.","zh":"立體主義明顯是一場複雜的藝術運動。"},{"en":"A complex art movement has many artists, styles, stages and ideas.","zh":"complex art movement 有許多藝術家、風格、階段和想法。"},{"en":"Students may find a complex art movement difficult until examples are grouped clearly.","zh":"學生可能覺得複雜藝術運動很難，直到例子被清楚分類。"},{"en":"Complexity grows when different artists develop related ideas in different directions.","zh":"當不同藝術家以不同方向發展相關想法，複雜性就會增加。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that the movement cannot be explained in one simple sentence.","zh":"這個短語提醒該運動不能用一句簡單說話解釋完。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"Analytical Cubism","meaning":"分析立體主義","examples":[{"en":"Analytical Cubism is one label used to describe Cubist works.","zh":"分析立體主義是用來描述立體主義作品的一個標籤。"},{"en":"Analytical Cubism refers to a phase of Cubism that breaks subjects into muted, fragmented forms.","zh":"Analytical Cubism 指立體主義中把主體分解成低調、碎片化形式的階段。"},{"en":"An art class may compare Analytical Cubism with later colourful Cubist styles.","zh":"美術課可能比較分析立體主義與後來色彩較豐富的立體主義風格。"},{"en":"The label helps organise works, but it was created after the art itself.","zh":"這個標籤有助組織作品，但它是在藝術本身之後才被創造。"},{"en":"The phrase names one category within Cubism.","zh":"這個短語指出立體主義中的一個類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"Synthetic Cubism","meaning":"綜合立體主義","examples":[{"en":"Synthetic Cubism is another later label for part of the movement.","zh":"綜合立體主義是該運動部分作品的另一個後來標籤。"},{"en":"Synthetic Cubism is a Cubist phase often linked with combining shapes, colours and collage-like elements.","zh":"Synthetic Cubism 是立體主義的一個階段，常與結合形狀、色彩和拼貼式元素相關。"},{"en":"Students may study Synthetic Cubism when learning how artists used paper, pattern and text.","zh":"學生學習藝術家如何使用紙張、圖案和文字時，可能研究綜合立體主義。"},{"en":"The term helps distinguish later Cubist works from earlier analytical ones.","zh":"這個術語幫助把後期立體主義作品與早期分析立體主義作品區分。"},{"en":"The phrase names a labelled stage of Cubism.","zh":"這個短語指出立體主義中被命名的一個階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"Orphic Cubism","meaning":"俄耳甫斯立體主義","examples":[{"en":"Orphic Cubism is associated with colour and abstraction.","zh":"俄耳甫斯立體主義與色彩和抽象相關。"},{"en":"Orphic Cubism is a form of Cubism that emphasises bright colour, rhythm and abstract forms.","zh":"Orphic Cubism 是一種強調鮮艷色彩、節奏和抽象形式的立體主義。"},{"en":"A teacher may use Orphic Cubism to show students how colour can carry meaning.","zh":"老師可能用俄耳甫斯立體主義向學生展示色彩如何承載意義。"},{"en":"Its focus on colour moved Cubism away from darker monochrome works.","zh":"它對色彩的重視令立體主義遠離較深沉的單色作品。"},{"en":"The phrase names a colourful branch of Cubism.","zh":"這個短語指出立體主義中較多彩的一支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"constructs","meaning":"建構出來的概念","examples":[{"en":"These names are constructs invented after the artworks were created.","zh":"這些名稱是在藝術作品創作後才發明的建構概念。"},{"en":"Constructs are ideas or categories created to organise and explain complex reality.","zh":"constructs 是為了組織和解釋複雜現實而創造的想法或類別。"},{"en":"“Beginner” and “advanced” are learning constructs that help teachers group students.","zh":"“beginner” 和 “advanced” 是幫助老師分類學生的學習建構概念。"},{"en":"Constructs can be useful, but they may not perfectly match real life.","zh":"建構概念可以有用，但未必完美符合現實生活。"},{"en":"The word describes made-up analytical categories.","zh":"這個詞描述被創造出來的分析類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"invented long after","meaning":"在……很久之後才被創造","examples":[{"en":"The labels were invented long after the artworks they describe.","zh":"這些標籤是在它們描述的藝術作品很久之後才被創造。"},{"en":"Invented long after means created much later than the thing being discussed.","zh":"invented long after 指比正在討論的事物晚很多才被創造。"},{"en":"The name of a school tradition may be invented long after students first began doing it.","zh":"一個學校傳統的名稱可能在學生最初開始做很久之後才被創造。"},{"en":"Later labels can help organise history, but they may simplify what actually happened.","zh":"後來標籤可以幫助組織歷史，但也可能簡化實際發生的事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a name or idea created after the fact.","zh":"這個短語描述事後才創造的名稱或想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"attempt to describe","meaning":"嘗試描述","examples":[{"en":"The labels attempt to describe a complex collective movement.","zh":"這些標籤嘗試描述一場複雜的集體運動。"},{"en":"To attempt to describe something means to try to explain or represent it in words.","zh":"attempt to describe 某事，指嘗試用文字解釋或呈現它。"},{"en":"A student may attempt to describe a difficult feeling in a diary.","zh":"學生可能嘗試在日記中描述一種困難感受。"},{"en":"Describing complex things is hard because one label may miss important differences.","zh":"描述複雜事物很難，因為一個標籤可能漏掉重要差異。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses effort rather than perfect success.","zh":"這個短語強調努力，而不是完美成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"appear to give","meaning":"似乎給予","examples":[{"en":"These labels appear to give coherent order to a messy movement.","zh":"這些標籤似乎給予一場混亂運動連貫秩序。"},{"en":"Appear to give means seem to provide something, even if the reality is more complicated.","zh":"appear to give 指似乎提供某物，即使現實更複雜。"},{"en":"A timetable may appear to give order to school life, though students still face surprises.","zh":"時間表似乎給予學校生活秩序，雖然學生仍會遇到突發事情。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that the effect may be partly superficial.","zh":"這個短語暗示效果可能部分只是表面。"},{"en":"It describes how something seems to organise or provide meaning.","zh":"它描述某物看似組織或提供意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"coherent order","meaning":"連貫秩序","examples":[{"en":"The labels give coherent order to a complex art movement.","zh":"這些標籤給予一場複雜藝術運動連貫秩序。"},{"en":"Coherent order is clear, logical arrangement that helps people understand connections.","zh":"coherent order 是清楚、有邏輯並幫助人理解聯繫的安排。"},{"en":"A teacher creates coherent order when she groups vocabulary by topic and use.","zh":"老師按主題和用法分類詞彙時，就是創造連貫秩序。"},{"en":"Without coherent order, students may see only disconnected facts.","zh":"沒有連貫秩序，學生可能只看到互不相連的事實。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organisation that makes sense.","zh":"這個短語描述有意義的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a collective movement","meaning":"集體運動","examples":[{"en":"Cubism was a collective movement involving many artists.","zh":"立體主義是一場涉及許多藝術家的集體運動。"},{"en":"A collective movement is a movement created by a group, not by one person alone.","zh":"collective movement 是由一個群體而非單一個人創造的運動。"},{"en":"A school environmental campaign can become a collective movement if many classes join.","zh":"如果許多班級加入，學校環保活動可以成為集體運動。"},{"en":"Collective movements develop through shared ideas and individual contributions.","zh":"集體運動透過共同想法和個人貢獻發展。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses group participation.","zh":"這個短語強調群體參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contribute","meaning":"作出貢獻","examples":[{"en":"Many individuals contributed to Cubism.","zh":"許多人對立體主義作出貢獻。"},{"en":"To contribute means to give help, ideas, work or influence to something larger.","zh":"contribute 指向更大的事物提供幫助、想法、工作或影響。"},{"en":"A student can contribute to a group project by researching, writing or presenting.","zh":"學生可以透過研究、寫作或匯報對小組項目作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Contributions may be small individually but important together.","zh":"貢獻個別看來可能很小，但合起來很重要。"},{"en":"The word describes adding value to a shared effort.","zh":"這個詞描述為共同努力增加價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"among all this confusion","meaning":"在這一切混亂之中","examples":[{"en":"Among all this confusion, the early twentieth century remains fascinating.","zh":"在這一切混亂之中，上世紀初期仍然令人着迷。"},{"en":"Among all this confusion means despite many unclear or complicated details.","zh":"among all this confusion 指儘管有許多不清楚或複雜細節。"},{"en":"Among all this confusion during exam season, a clear timetable helps students stay calm.","zh":"在考試季這一切混亂之中，清楚時間表幫助學生保持冷靜。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something valuable remains even when the situation is messy.","zh":"這個短語顯示即使情況混亂，仍有有價值的東西存在。"},{"en":"It introduces a point that survives complexity.","zh":"它引出一個在複雜中仍成立的重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"one does not doubt that","meaning":"毫無疑問","examples":[{"en":"One does not doubt that the Parisian art scene was fascinating.","zh":"毫無疑問，巴黎藝術圈令人着迷。"},{"en":"One does not doubt that means it is clear or strongly believable that something is true.","zh":"one does not doubt that 指某事明顯或非常可信地成立。"},{"en":"One does not doubt that good sleep helps students learn better.","zh":"毫無疑問，良好睡眠幫助學生學得更好。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses confidence without sounding overly casual.","zh":"這個短語表達信心，同時不太口語化。"},{"en":"It is often used before making a firm judgement.","zh":"它常用於作出堅定判斷前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"fascinating period","meaning":"令人着迷的時期","examples":[{"en":"The early years of the last century were a fascinating period in art.","zh":"上世紀初期是藝術中一段令人着迷的時期。"},{"en":"A fascinating period is a time that is especially interesting because many important things happened.","zh":"fascinating period 是因發生許多重要事情而特別有趣的時期。"},{"en":"The first year of a new school can be a fascinating period because students and teachers build new traditions.","zh":"新學校的第一年可以是令人着迷的時期，因為學生和老師建立新傳統。"},{"en":"Such periods attract study because they contain change, conflict and creativity.","zh":"這類時期吸引研究，因為它包含變化、衝突和創意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a time worth close attention.","zh":"這個短語描述值得仔細關注的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"answer the questions","meaning":"回答問題","examples":[{"en":"Candidates answer the questions by choosing the correct painter.","zh":"考生透過選擇正確畫家來回答問題。"},{"en":"To answer the questions means to provide responses to the task given.","zh":"answer the questions 指對所給任務提供答案。"},{"en":"Students should read the instructions carefully before they answer the questions.","zh":"學生回答問題前應仔細閱讀指示。"},{"en":"Good answers come from matching evidence with what the question asks.","zh":"好答案來自把證據與題目要求配對。"},{"en":"The phrase describes completing an exam or practice task.","zh":"這個短語描述完成考試或練習任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for each answer.","zh":"考生為每個答案選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choose the correct letter means select the option letter that matches the answer.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選出符合答案的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students choose the correct letter after checking evidence in the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生查核文章證據後選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Copying the wrong letter can lose marks even if the reasoning is right.","zh":"即使推理正確，抄錯字母也會失分。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common multiple-choice instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見多項選擇指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"for each answer","meaning":"每個答案","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose one letter for each answer.","zh":"考生為每個答案選擇一個字母。"},{"en":"For each answer means separately for every question or blank.","zh":"for each answer 指為每條題目或每個空格分別處理。"},{"en":"Students should check the word limit for each answer in a summary task.","zh":"學生在摘要題中應為每個答案檢查字數限制。"},{"en":"Treating each answer separately helps avoid careless copying mistakes.","zh":"分開處理每個答案有助避免粗心抄寫錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that every item needs its own response.","zh":"這個短語強調每一項都需要自己的回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"use an answer more than once","meaning":"可重複使用答案","examples":[{"en":"Candidates can use an answer more than once.","zh":"考生可以重複使用答案。"},{"en":"To use an answer more than once means the same option may be chosen for more than one question.","zh":"use an answer more than once 指同一選項可用於多於一條題目。"},{"en":"In a matching task, one paragraph may be used more than once if it contains several details.","zh":"在配對題中，如果一段包含幾個細節，同一段可以被使用多於一次。"},{"en":"This instruction prevents students from eliminating an option after one use.","zh":"這個指示防止學生在使用一次後排除某選項。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated use of the same answer option.","zh":"這個短語描述同一答案選項的重複使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"lead a new abstraction movement","meaning":"領導新的抽象運動","examples":[{"en":"One painter led a new abstraction movement.","zh":"一位畫家領導了新的抽象運動。"},{"en":"To lead a new abstraction movement means to be a main figure guiding a new abstract art direction.","zh":"lead a new abstraction movement 指成為引導新抽象藝術方向的主要人物。"},{"en":"A student may lead a new reading group if others follow her idea.","zh":"如果其他人跟隨她的想法，學生可能領導新的閱讀小組。"},{"en":"Leading a movement requires influence, activity and visible examples.","zh":"領導運動需要影響力、行動和可見例子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes guiding others toward a new abstract style.","zh":"這個短語描述引導他人走向新抽象風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the most influential","meaning":"最具影響力的","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which painter was the most influential.","zh":"題目問哪位畫家最具影響力。"},{"en":"The most influential means having the strongest effect on other people or later developments.","zh":"most influential 指對其他人或後來發展有最強影響。"},{"en":"A teacher may be the most influential person in a student’s choice of career.","zh":"老師可能是學生選擇事業時最具影響力的人。"},{"en":"Influence is shown when others copy, react to or develop someone’s ideas.","zh":"當其他人模仿、回應或發展某人的想法，影響力便顯現。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the person or thing with the greatest impact.","zh":"這個短語指出影響最大的人或事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be affected by","meaning":"受……影響","examples":[{"en":"One painter was affected by a global conflict.","zh":"一位畫家受全球衝突影響。"},{"en":"To be affected by something means to be changed or influenced by it.","zh":"be affected by 某事，指被它改變或影響。"},{"en":"Students may be affected by noise if construction happens beside the classroom.","zh":"如果課室旁施工，學生可能受噪音影響。"},{"en":"Major events can affect people’s work, emotions and decisions.","zh":"重大事件可以影響人的工作、情緒和決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes impact from an outside force.","zh":"這個短語描述外在力量帶來的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"global conflict","meaning":"全球衝突","examples":[{"en":"World War One was a global conflict that affected artists.","zh":"第一次世界大戰是一場影響藝術家的全球衝突。"},{"en":"A global conflict is a war or struggle involving many countries around the world.","zh":"global conflict 是涉及世界許多國家的戰爭或鬥爭。"},{"en":"A global conflict can disrupt families, schools, trade and culture.","zh":"全球衝突可以打亂家庭、學校、貿易和文化。"},{"en":"Artists may respond to global conflict by showing fear, machinery or loss.","zh":"藝術家可能透過呈現恐懼、機器或失去來回應全球衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase describes conflict on an international scale.","zh":"這個短語描述國際規模的衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"inevitably linked with","meaning":"無可避免地與……聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"Picasso is inevitably linked with Cubism.","zh":"Picasso 無可避免地與立體主義聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To be inevitably linked with something means to be so strongly connected that people almost always associate the two.","zh":"inevitably linked with 某事，指兩者連結強到人們幾乎總會聯想在一起。"},{"en":"A famous school principal may be inevitably linked with the school’s major reforms.","zh":"著名校長可能無可避免地與學校重大改革聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Repeated public association can make a link feel unavoidable.","zh":"反覆的公眾聯想可以令連結感覺不可避免。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong and lasting connection.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈而持久的聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"an art movement","meaning":"藝術運動","examples":[{"en":"Cubism is an art movement associated with several painters.","zh":"立體主義是一場與幾位畫家相關的藝術運動。"},{"en":"An art movement is a shared artistic direction followed by a group of artists.","zh":"art movement 是一群藝術家共同跟隨的藝術方向。"},{"en":"Students may study an art movement by comparing several artists’ works.","zh":"學生可能透過比較幾位藝術家的作品來研究藝術運動。"},{"en":"Art movements develop when artists share questions, methods or styles.","zh":"當藝術家分享問題、方法或風格，藝術運動就會發展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broad pattern in art history.","zh":"這個短語描述藝術史中的廣泛模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be married","meaning":"已婚","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which painter was married.","zh":"題目問哪位畫家已婚。"},{"en":"To be married means to have a husband or wife through a legal or recognised relationship.","zh":"be married 指透過法律或被承認的關係擁有丈夫或妻子。"},{"en":"A biography may mention whether an artist was married because family affected their work.","zh":"傳記可能提及藝術家是否已婚，因為家庭影響其作品。"},{"en":"Marriage can sometimes connect artists through collaboration or shared exhibitions.","zh":"婚姻有時可以透過合作或共同展覽把藝術家連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes marital status.","zh":"這個短語描述婚姻狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"use an answer only once","meaning":"只能使用答案一次","examples":[{"en":"In this section, candidates can use an answer only once.","zh":"在這部分，考生只能使用答案一次。"},{"en":"To use an answer only once means the same option cannot be repeated.","zh":"use an answer only once 指同一選項不可重複使用。"},{"en":"In a matching task, students must be careful if each answer can be used only once.","zh":"在配對題中，如果每個答案只能使用一次，學生必須小心。"},{"en":"This rule forces candidates to compare all choices before deciding.","zh":"這條規則迫使考生在決定前比較所有選項。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strict one-use answer rule.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴格的一次使用答案規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"confusing abstraction","meaning":"令人困惑的抽象畫","examples":[{"en":"The painting may appear to be a confusing abstraction.","zh":"這幅畫可能看起來是令人困惑的抽象畫。"},{"en":"A confusing abstraction is an abstract image or idea that is difficult to understand at first.","zh":"confusing abstraction 是起初難以理解的抽象圖像或想法。"},{"en":"A student may find a diagram a confusing abstraction if it uses shapes without labels.","zh":"如果圖表使用沒有標籤的形狀，學生可能覺得它是令人困惑的抽象圖。"},{"en":"Abstraction becomes confusing when viewers cannot connect forms with meaning.","zh":"當觀眾無法把形式與意義連起來，抽象就會令人困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes abstract work that puzzles the viewer.","zh":"這個短語描述令觀眾疑惑的抽象作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"in many colours","meaning":"以多種顏色","examples":[{"en":"Some Cubist works present abstraction in many colours.","zh":"有些立體主義作品以多種顏色呈現抽象。"},{"en":"In many colours means using a wide range of different colours.","zh":"in many colours 指使用大量不同顏色。"},{"en":"A school mural may show community life in many colours.","zh":"學校壁畫可能以多種顏色展示社區生活。"},{"en":"Many colours can create energy, variety and visual excitement.","zh":"多種顏色可以創造活力、多樣性和視覺興奮感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes colourful presentation.","zh":"這個短語描述色彩豐富的呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a darker view","meaning":"較陰暗的看法","examples":[{"en":"One painting gives a darker view of modern life.","zh":"一幅畫對現代生活給出較陰暗的看法。"},{"en":"A darker view is a more negative, serious or troubling interpretation.","zh":"darker view 是較負面、嚴肅或令人不安的詮釋。"},{"en":"A film about overwork may give a darker view of city success.","zh":"關於過勞的電影可能對城市成功給出較陰暗的看法。"},{"en":"Darker views often focus on loneliness, fear, pressure or loss.","zh":"較陰暗的看法常集中於孤獨、恐懼、壓力或失去。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a less optimistic perspective.","zh":"這個短語描述較不樂觀的視角。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"ahead of its time","meaning":"超前於時代","examples":[{"en":"Some works were ahead of their time.","zh":"有些作品超前於時代。"},{"en":"Ahead of its time means too advanced or original for most people of that period to understand fully.","zh":"ahead of its time 指對當時大多數人而言太先進或太原創，難以完全理解。"},{"en":"An early online school system may have been ahead of its time before remote learning became common.","zh":"在遙距學習普及前，早期網上學校系統可能超前於時代。"},{"en":"Works ahead of their time may be appreciated only years later.","zh":"超前於時代的作品可能多年後才被欣賞。"},{"en":"The phrase describes early originality.","zh":"這個短語描述早出的原創性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the first of its kind","meaning":"同類中的首創","examples":[{"en":"One painting may have been the first of its kind.","zh":"一幅畫可能是同類中的首創。"},{"en":"The first of its kind is the earliest example of a particular type.","zh":"first of its kind 是某一類型的最早例子。"},{"en":"A school may open the first of its kind language lab in the district.","zh":"學校可能開設區內同類中的首個語言實驗室。"},{"en":"Being first matters because later examples may follow its model.","zh":"成為首創很重要，因為後來例子可能跟隨其模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an original starting example.","zh":"這個短語描述原創的起始例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"intriguing and multi-chromatic","meaning":"引人入勝而多色彩的","examples":[{"en":"One work presents an intriguing and multi-chromatic view.","zh":"一件作品呈現引人入勝而多色彩的視角。"},{"en":"Intriguing and multi-chromatic means interesting and made with many colours.","zh":"intriguing and multi-chromatic 指有趣並由多種顏色構成。"},{"en":"A colourful science poster can be intriguing and multi-chromatic if it draws students into the topic.","zh":"如果彩色科學海報吸引學生進入主題，它可以是引人入勝而多色彩的。"},{"en":"Many colours can make a work visually rich and invite closer looking.","zh":"多種顏色可以令作品視覺上豐富，並吸引人仔細觀看。"},{"en":"The phrase combines curiosity with colour variety.","zh":"這個短語結合好奇感與色彩多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"multi-chromatic view","meaning":"多色彩視角","examples":[{"en":"Gris’s still life offers a multi-chromatic view.","zh":"Gris 的靜物畫提供多色彩視角。"},{"en":"A multi-chromatic view uses many colours to present a subject.","zh":"multi-chromatic view 是使用多種顏色呈現主體的方式。"},{"en":"A city map for children may use a multi-chromatic view to separate parks, roads and schools.","zh":"兒童城市地圖可能使用多色彩視角來區分公園、道路和學校。"},{"en":"Multiple colours can help organise information or create visual excitement.","zh":"多種顏色可以幫助組織資訊或創造視覺興奮感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a many-coloured way of seeing.","zh":"這個短語描述多色彩的觀看方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"representative of its type","meaning":"很能代表其類型的","examples":[{"en":"Portrait of Picasso is very representative of the Cubist style.","zh":"《Picasso 肖像》很能代表立體主義風格。"},{"en":"Representative of its type means clearly showing the main features of that category.","zh":"representative of its type 指清楚顯示該類別主要特徵。"},{"en":"A well-written report may be representative of strong academic writing.","zh":"寫得好的報告可能很能代表強學術寫作。"},{"en":"Representative examples help students learn what a style normally looks like.","zh":"具代表性的例子幫助學生學會某風格通常是甚麼樣子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a good example of a category.","zh":"這個短語描述某類別的好例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"an early painting","meaning":"早期畫作","examples":[{"en":"The Bathers was an early painting that influenced later Cubist work.","zh":"《浴者》是一幅影響後來立體主義作品的早期畫作。"},{"en":"An early painting is a work created before later developments or mature style.","zh":"early painting 是在後來發展或成熟風格之前創作的作品。"},{"en":"An artist’s early painting may contain ideas that become clearer in later works.","zh":"藝術家的早期畫作可能包含在後來作品中變得更清楚的想法。"},{"en":"Early paintings can influence others even if they are unfinished or experimental.","zh":"早期畫作即使未完成或具實驗性，也可以影響他人。"},{"en":"The phrase places a painting near the beginning of a development.","zh":"這個短語把畫作放在某發展的開始附近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"influence another","meaning":"影響另一作品","examples":[{"en":"One painting influenced another important work.","zh":"一幅畫影響了另一件重要作品。"},{"en":"To influence another work means to affect how that later work is made or understood.","zh":"influence another work 指影響後來作品如何被創作或理解。"},{"en":"A student’s essay may influence another student’s structure if it is used as a model.","zh":"如果學生文章被用作範本，它可能影響另一名學生的結構。"},{"en":"Influence can appear through theme, shape, colour or method.","zh":"影響可以透過主題、形狀、顏色或方法出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a connection between two works.","zh":"這個短語描述兩件作品之間的聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the Cezanne retrospective","meaning":"Cezanne 回顧展","examples":[{"en":"The Cezanne retrospective influenced young artists in Paris.","zh":"Cezanne 回顧展影響了巴黎的年輕藝術家。"},{"en":"The Cezanne retrospective was an exhibition looking back at Cezanne’s life and work.","zh":"Cezanne retrospective 是回顧 Cezanne 一生和作品的展覽。"},{"en":"Students may study the Cezanne retrospective to understand how later artists saw his paintings.","zh":"學生可能研究 Cezanne 回顧展，以理解後來藝術家如何看待他的畫。"},{"en":"A major retrospective can change how an artist is understood after death.","zh":"大型回顧展可以改變藝術家死後被理解的方式。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a key exhibition of Cezanne’s work.","zh":"這個短語指 Cezanne 作品的一場關鍵展覽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be attended by","meaning":"由……出席","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether the retrospective was attended by Cezanne.","zh":"題目問該回顧展是否由 Cezanne 出席。"},{"en":"To be attended by someone means that person was present at an event.","zh":"be attended by 某人，指該人出席某活動。"},{"en":"A school concert may be attended by parents, teachers and former students.","zh":"學校音樂會可能由家長、老師和舊生出席。"},{"en":"Attendance matters because it shows who was there to witness the event.","zh":"出席很重要，因為它顯示誰在場見證事件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes presence at an event.","zh":"這個短語描述在活動中的出席。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"Cubist paintings","meaning":"立體主義畫作","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether the retrospective showed Cubist paintings.","zh":"該選項問回顧展是否展示立體主義畫作。"},{"en":"Cubist paintings are paintings made in the style of Cubism.","zh":"Cubist paintings 是以立體主義風格創作的畫作。"},{"en":"Cubist paintings may show a violin from several angles at once.","zh":"立體主義畫作可能同時從幾個角度展示小提琴。"},{"en":"Their broken shapes and multiple views can make familiar objects look strange.","zh":"其破碎形狀和多重視角可以令熟悉物件看起來陌生。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to artworks belonging to or showing Cubist style.","zh":"這個短語指屬於或顯示立體主義風格的藝術作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"influence someone to","meaning":"影響某人去","examples":[{"en":"The retrospective influenced an artist to move towards abstraction.","zh":"回顧展影響一位藝術家走向抽象。"},{"en":"To influence someone to do something means to affect them so they begin or choose that action.","zh":"influence someone to do something 指影響某人，使其開始或選擇該行動。"},{"en":"A career talk may influence a student to study engineering.","zh":"職業講座可能影響學生去讀工程。"},{"en":"Influence can guide decisions without forcing them.","zh":"影響可以引導決定，而不是強迫。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one person or event shaping another person’s action.","zh":"這個短語描述某人或某事件如何塑造另一人的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"non-representational style","meaning":"非具象風格","examples":[{"en":"Léger moved towards a non-representational style.","zh":"Léger 走向非具象風格。"},{"en":"A non-representational style does not clearly show real people, objects or places.","zh":"non-representational style 不清楚呈現真實人物、物件或地方。"},{"en":"A painting made only of coloured lines may use a non-representational style.","zh":"只由彩色線條構成的畫作可能使用非具象風格。"},{"en":"This style asks viewers to focus on form, colour and feeling.","zh":"這種風格要求觀眾集中於形式、色彩和感受。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an abstract visual approach.","zh":"這個短語描述抽象視覺方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"Cubist innovators","meaning":"立體主義創新者","examples":[{"en":"Many Cubist innovators were not adequately recognised.","zh":"許多立體主義創新者未得到充分認可。"},{"en":"Cubist innovators are artists who created new ideas within Cubism.","zh":"Cubist innovators 是在立體主義中創造新想法的藝術家。"},{"en":"A school project may highlight Cubist innovators beyond Picasso and Braque.","zh":"學校項目可能介紹 Picasso 和 Braque 以外的立體主義創新者。"},{"en":"Innovators can be overlooked when history focuses on the most famous names.","zh":"當歷史集中於最有名的名字，創新者可能被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creative figures inside the Cubist movement.","zh":"這個短語描述立體主義運動中的創意人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"prefer still-life painting","meaning":"偏好靜物畫","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether Cubist innovators preferred still-life painting.","zh":"該選項問立體主義創新者是否偏好靜物畫。"},{"en":"To prefer still-life painting means to like painting arranged objects more than other subjects.","zh":"prefer still-life painting 指較喜歡畫擺放物件，而不是其他主題。"},{"en":"A student may prefer still-life painting because objects stay still and are easier to observe.","zh":"學生可能偏好靜物畫，因為物件不動並較容易觀察。"},{"en":"Preference for one subject can shape an artist’s practice and reputation.","zh":"對某主題的偏好可以塑造藝術家的實踐和名聲。"},{"en":"The phrase describes artistic choice of subject matter.","zh":"這個短語描述藝術家對題材的選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"favour monochrome","meaning":"偏好單色","examples":[{"en":"Some artists favoured monochrome, while others used bright colour.","zh":"有些藝術家偏好單色，而另一些使用鮮艷色彩。"},{"en":"To favour monochrome means to prefer using one colour or one colour family.","zh":"favour monochrome 指偏好使用一種顏色或一個色系。"},{"en":"A designer may favour monochrome for a formal business report.","zh":"設計師可能在正式商業報告中偏好單色。"},{"en":"Monochrome can create unity, seriousness or focus on shape.","zh":"單色可以創造統一、嚴肅或對形狀的集中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a preference for limited colour.","zh":"這個短語描述對有限色彩的偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"invent names for","meaning":"為……創造名稱","examples":[{"en":"The names for Cubist styles were invented later.","zh":"立體主義風格的名稱是後來被創造的。"},{"en":"To invent names for something means to create labels used to identify or classify it.","zh":"invent names for 某事，指創造用來辨認或分類它的標籤。"},{"en":"Students may invent names for different study methods so they can remember them easily.","zh":"學生可能為不同學習方法創造名稱，以便容易記住。"},{"en":"Names help organise ideas, but they can also make messy history look too neat.","zh":"名稱幫助組織想法，但也可以令混亂歷史看起來太整齊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating labels after noticing patterns.","zh":"這個短語描述在注意到模式後創造標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"adequately recognised","meaning":"得到充分認可","examples":[{"en":"Many Cubist innovators were not adequately recognised.","zh":"許多立體主義創新者未得到充分認可。"},{"en":"Adequately recognised means given enough attention, credit or respect.","zh":"adequately recognised 指得到足夠注意、功勞或尊重。"},{"en":"A helpful class monitor may not be adequately recognised if teachers only praise top marks.","zh":"如果老師只稱讚高分，有幫助的班長可能未得到充分認可。"},{"en":"Lack of recognition can make important contributions seem smaller than they were.","zh":"缺乏認可可以令重要貢獻看起來比實際小。"},{"en":"The phrase describes receiving the level of acknowledgement deserved.","zh":"這個短語描述得到應有程度的承認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"fairly easily explained","meaning":"相當容易解釋","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether Cubism is fairly easily explained.","zh":"該選項問立體主義是否相當容易解釋。"},{"en":"Fairly easily explained means not too difficult to describe in a clear way.","zh":"fairly easily explained 指不太難以清楚描述。"},{"en":"The school timetable is fairly easily explained if each colour represents one subject.","zh":"如果每種顏色代表一科，學校時間表就相當容易解釋。"},{"en":"Some topics look familiar but are not actually easy to explain.","zh":"有些題目看似熟悉，但其實不容易解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moderate ease in explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述解釋上的中等容易程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"incoherent order","meaning":"不連貫的次序","examples":[{"en":"Objects in Cubist paintings may appear in an incoherent order.","zh":"立體主義畫作中的物件可能以不連貫的次序出現。"},{"en":"Incoherent order is an arrangement that does not seem logical, clear or connected.","zh":"incoherent order 是看起來不合邏輯、不清楚或沒有連繫的排列。"},{"en":"A student’s essay may have incoherent order if examples appear before the main point.","zh":"如果例子出現在主旨前，學生文章可能有不連貫的次序。"},{"en":"Incoherent order can confuse readers or viewers because links are unclear.","zh":"不連貫次序會令讀者或觀眾困惑，因為連結不清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes disorganised arrangement.","zh":"這個短語描述混亂的排列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"different views of a subject","meaning":"主體的不同視角","examples":[{"en":"Cubism shows different views of a subject within one picture.","zh":"立體主義在一幅畫中展示主體的不同視角。"},{"en":"Different views of a subject are several ways of seeing the same person, object or issue.","zh":"different views of a subject 是觀看同一人物、物件或議題的幾種方式。"},{"en":"A classroom debate gives students different views of a subject such as homework policy.","zh":"課堂辯論讓學生得到關於功課政策等主題的不同觀點。"},{"en":"Several views can reveal complexity that one angle misses.","zh":"幾個視角可以揭示單一角度漏掉的複雜性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes multiple perspectives on one subject.","zh":"這個短語描述對同一主體的多重視角。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be created by","meaning":"由……創造","examples":[{"en":"The passage questions whether Cubism was created only by Picasso and Braque.","zh":"文章質疑立體主義是否只由 Picasso 和 Braque 創造。"},{"en":"To be created by someone means to be made, developed or brought into existence by that person.","zh":"be created by 某人，指由該人製作、發展或帶入存在。"},{"en":"A school mural may be created by students, teachers and local artists together.","zh":"學校壁畫可能由學生、老師和本地藝術家共同創造。"},{"en":"Asking who something was created by helps identify contribution and credit.","zh":"問某事由誰創造，有助辨認貢獻和功勞。"},{"en":"The phrase describes authorship or origin.","zh":"這個短語描述作者身分或來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 93 - Cubism.pdf","sourcePage":21}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 94":[{"front":"the International Space Station","meaning":"國際太空站","examples":[{"en":"The International Space Station can sometimes be seen from Earth.","zh":"國際太空站有時可以從地球看見。"},{"en":"The International Space Station is a large spacecraft where astronauts live and work in orbit.","zh":"國際太空站是一艘大型太空船，太空人在軌道上居住和工作。"},{"en":"Students may track the International Space Station online before watching it pass over their city.","zh":"學生可能先在網上追蹤國際太空站，然後觀看它經過自己城市上空。"},{"en":"Because the International Space Station reflects sunlight, it can look like a bright moving dot in the sky.","zh":"因為國際太空站反射陽光，它在天空中可能看似一個明亮移動的點。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the orbiting research station, not an ordinary satellite.","zh":"這個短語指在軌道上運行的研究太空站，而不是普通衛星。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"just before sunrise","meaning":"日出前不久","examples":[{"en":"Just before sunrise, the ISS may be visible in the sky.","zh":"日出前不久，國際太空站可能在天空中可見。"},{"en":"Just before sunrise means a short time before the sun appears in the morning.","zh":"日出前不久，是指太陽在早上出現前的一小段時間。"},{"en":"A runner may leave home just before sunrise to avoid the heat of the day.","zh":"跑步者可能在日出前不久出門，以避開白天炎熱天氣。"},{"en":"The ISS may be easier to see just before sunrise because the ground is still dark but the station is lit by the sun.","zh":"國際太空站在日出前不久可能較容易看見，因為地面仍然黑暗，但太空站被太陽照亮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a time very early in the morning.","zh":"這個短語描述清晨很早的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on a clear night","meaning":"在晴朗的晚上","examples":[{"en":"On a clear night, people may see the ISS passing overhead.","zh":"在晴朗的晚上，人們可能看見國際太空站從頭頂經過。"},{"en":"On a clear night means during a night when the sky has few clouds and good visibility.","zh":"在晴朗的晚上，是指天空少雲、能見度良好的夜晚。"},{"en":"Families may watch stars on a clear night because the sky is easier to see.","zh":"家庭可能在晴朗的晚上觀星，因為天空較容易看見。"},{"en":"If the sky is cloudy, people may miss the ISS even if it passes overhead.","zh":"如果天空多雲，即使國際太空站從頭頂經過，人們也可能錯過它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weather conditions that make sky-watching possible.","zh":"這個短語描述讓觀天成為可能的天氣條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"look up","meaning":"抬頭看","examples":[{"en":"Look up, and you may see the ISS moving across the sky.","zh":"抬頭看，你可能會看見國際太空站橫越天空。"},{"en":"To look up means to raise your eyes or head to see something above you.","zh":"抬頭看，是指抬起眼睛或頭部去看上方的東西。"},{"en":"A teacher may tell students to look up when a plane flies over the playground.","zh":"當飛機飛過操場上空，老師可能叫學生抬頭看。"},{"en":"If people do not look up at the right moment, they may miss the moving light.","zh":"如果人們沒有在正確時刻抬頭看，可能會錯過那道移動亮光。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the simple action of looking toward the sky or a higher place.","zh":"這個短語描述望向天空或較高位置的簡單動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"travel steadily across","meaning":"穩定地橫越……","examples":[{"en":"The ISS travels steadily across the dark sky.","zh":"國際太空站穩定地橫越漆黑天空。"},{"en":"To travel steadily across something means to move across it smoothly and at a regular speed.","zh":"穩定地橫越某處，是指平穩並以規律速度穿過它。"},{"en":"A ferry may travel steadily across the harbour on a calm morning.","zh":"渡輪可能在平靜早晨穩定地橫越海港。"},{"en":"The ISS appears to travel steadily because it follows a fixed orbit around Earth.","zh":"國際太空站看似穩定移動，因為它沿固定軌道繞地球運行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement that is even, continuous, and not sudden.","zh":"這個短語描述均勻、持續而不突然的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dark, starry sky","meaning":"漆黑而佈滿星星的天空","examples":[{"en":"The ISS can be seen against a dark, starry sky.","zh":"國際太空站可以在漆黑而佈滿星星的天空背景下被看見。"},{"en":"A dark, starry sky is a night sky that is black and filled with visible stars.","zh":"漆黑而佈滿星星的天空，是黑暗且能看見很多星星的夜空。"},{"en":"Campers may enjoy a dark, starry sky far away from city lights.","zh":"露營者可能喜歡遠離城市燈光的漆黑星空。"},{"en":"A dark, starry sky makes bright moving objects easier to notice.","zh":"漆黑而佈滿星星的天空使明亮移動物體較容易被注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear night sky suitable for watching stars or satellites.","zh":"這個短語描述適合觀星或看衛星的晴朗夜空。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"take about four minutes to","meaning":"需時約四分鐘去……","examples":[{"en":"The ISS takes about four minutes to pass across the sky.","zh":"國際太空站需時約四分鐘橫越天空。"},{"en":"To take about four minutes to do something means to need roughly four minutes to complete it.","zh":"需時約四分鐘做某事，是指大約需要四分鐘完成它。"},{"en":"It may take about four minutes to walk from a classroom to the school office.","zh":"從課室走到校務處可能需時約四分鐘。"},{"en":"Because the ISS moves quickly, viewers have only a short time to watch it cross the sky.","zh":"因為國際太空站移動很快，觀察者只有短時間觀看它橫越天空。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate time needed for an action.","zh":"這個短語給出某行動所需的大約時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"too fast to be","meaning":"太快而不可能是……","examples":[{"en":"The object is too fast to be a planet.","zh":"這個物體太快而不可能是行星。"},{"en":"Too fast to be something means it moves faster than that thing normally would.","zh":"太快而不可能是某物，是指它移動速度比該物通常速度更快。"},{"en":"A light crossing the sky in seconds is too fast to be an ordinary airplane far away.","zh":"幾秒內橫越天空的光點，太快而不可能是遠處的普通飛機。"},{"en":"Speed helps observers decide whether an object is a planet, satellite, plane, or meteor.","zh":"速度幫助觀察者判斷物體是行星、衛星、飛機還是流星。"},{"en":"This phrase uses speed to rule out one possible identity.","zh":"這個短語用速度排除其中一種可能身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"too slow to be","meaning":"太慢而不可能是……","examples":[{"en":"The object is too slow to be a shooting star.","zh":"這個物體太慢而不可能是流星。"},{"en":"Too slow to be something means it moves more slowly than that thing normally would.","zh":"太慢而不可能是某物，是指它移動速度比該物通常速度更慢。"},{"en":"A bright dot taking several minutes to cross the sky is too slow to be a shooting star.","zh":"一個亮點花幾分鐘橫越天空，太慢而不可能是流星。"},{"en":"When an object moves too slowly, observers may consider it a satellite instead of a meteor.","zh":"當物體移動太慢，觀察者可能認為它是衛星而不是流星。"},{"en":"This phrase uses slowness to reject an explanation.","zh":"這個短語用速度太慢來否定一個解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"shooting star","meaning":"流星","examples":[{"en":"The ISS is too slow to be a shooting star.","zh":"國際太空站太慢而不可能是流星。"},{"en":"A shooting star is a bright streak of light caused by a small object burning in Earth’s atmosphere.","zh":"流星是小物體在地球大氣中燃燒時產生的明亮光痕。"},{"en":"Children may make a wish when they see a shooting star at night.","zh":"孩子晚上看見流星時，可能會許願。"},{"en":"A shooting star usually appears and disappears quickly, unlike the ISS.","zh":"流星通常很快出現又消失，與國際太空站不同。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a meteor seen from Earth.","zh":"這個短語指從地球看見的 meteor。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on one of its orbits","meaning":"在其中一次軌道運行中","examples":[{"en":"The ISS is visible during one of its orbits around Earth.","zh":"國際太空站在其中一次繞地球軌道運行期間可見。"},{"en":"On one of its orbits means during one complete path it takes around a planet.","zh":"在其中一次軌道運行中，是指在它繞行星走完一圈的路徑期間。"},{"en":"A satellite may pass over a city on one of its orbits during the night.","zh":"衛星可能在夜間其中一次軌道運行中經過城市上空。"},{"en":"Because the ISS circles Earth many times a day, it may become visible during some passes.","zh":"因為國際太空站每天繞地球多次，所以某些經過期間可能可見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific trip around Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述繞地球的一次特定運行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"15 orbits per day","meaning":"每日十五次軌道運行","examples":[{"en":"The ISS completes about 15 orbits per day.","zh":"國際太空站每日完成約十五次軌道運行。"},{"en":"15 orbits per day means the station circles Earth about fifteen times every day.","zh":"每日十五次軌道運行，是指太空站每天繞地球約十五圈。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain that one orbit is one full trip around Earth.","zh":"老師可能解釋，一次軌道運行就是繞地球完整走一圈。"},{"en":"Because the ISS makes many orbits per day, it repeatedly passes over different parts of the planet.","zh":"因為國際太空站每日進行多次軌道運行，它會反覆經過地球不同地區上空。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how often the ISS circles Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述國際太空站繞地球的頻密程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"light something up","meaning":"照亮某物","examples":[{"en":"The sun’s light has lit the ISS up.","zh":"太陽光已照亮國際太空站。"},{"en":"To light something up means to make it bright or visible by shining light on it.","zh":"照亮某物，是指用光使它變亮或可見。"},{"en":"Street lamps light up the road so drivers can see at night.","zh":"街燈照亮道路，讓司機夜間能看見。"},{"en":"When sunlight lights up the ISS while the ground is dark, people can see it clearly.","zh":"當陽光照亮國際太空站而地面仍黑暗時，人們能清楚看見它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making something brighter.","zh":"這個短語描述令某物變亮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"surroundings remain dark","meaning":"周圍環境仍然漆黑","examples":[{"en":"The ISS is bright while the surroundings remain dark.","zh":"國際太空站很明亮，而周圍環境仍然漆黑。"},{"en":"Surroundings remain dark means the area around something is still without much light.","zh":"周圍環境仍然漆黑，是指某物周邊區域仍然沒有太多光。"},{"en":"A candle looks brighter when the surroundings remain dark.","zh":"當周圍環境仍然漆黑，蠟燭看起來更明亮。"},{"en":"The contrast between a lit object and dark surroundings makes the object easier to see.","zh":"被照亮物體和黑暗周圍之間的對比，令該物更容易看見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a situation where the background has not yet become bright.","zh":"這個短語描述背景尚未變亮的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"discount something as","meaning":"把某物視為……而不重視","examples":[{"en":"People should not discount the white dot as unimportant.","zh":"人們不應把那個白點視為不重要而不重視。"},{"en":"To discount something as something means to dismiss it or treat it as less important than it is.","zh":"把某物視為某事而不重視，是指低估它或認為它不重要。"},{"en":"A teacher should not discount a quiet student’s idea as useless before listening carefully.","zh":"老師不應在仔細聆聽前，就把安靜學生的想法視為無用。"},{"en":"If people discount the ISS as a simple white dot, they miss its scientific importance.","zh":"如果人們把國際太空站視為普通白點而不重視，就會錯過它的科學重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against undervaluing something too quickly.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要太快低估某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a white dot","meaning":"白點","examples":[{"en":"From Earth, the ISS may look like a white dot.","zh":"從地球看，國際太空站可能像一個白點。"},{"en":"A white dot is a very small bright spot that appears white.","zh":"白點是一個看起來是白色的很小亮點。"},{"en":"A distant airplane may look like a white dot before it comes closer.","zh":"遠處飛機在靠近前可能看起來像白點。"},{"en":"The ISS looks small from Earth because it is hundreds of kilometres above us.","zh":"國際太空站從地球看很小，因為它在我們上方數百公里。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a large object can appear tiny from far away.","zh":"這個短語描述大型物體從遠處看如何顯得很細小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"something inconsequential","meaning":"無關重要的東西","examples":[{"en":"The ISS should not be dismissed as something inconsequential.","zh":"國際太空站不應被視為無關重要的東西而被否定。"},{"en":"Something inconsequential is something that seems unimportant or without serious effect.","zh":"無關重要的東西，是看似不重要或沒有嚴重影響的東西。"},{"en":"A small typo may be inconsequential in a casual message but serious in a legal document.","zh":"在普通訊息中，小錯字可能無關重要，但在法律文件中可能很嚴重。"},{"en":"The ISS may look tiny, but it is not inconsequential because it represents huge scientific effort.","zh":"國際太空站可能看似細小，但它並非無關重要，因為它代表巨大科學努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something treated as having little importance.","zh":"這個短語描述被視為不太重要的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be spent on","meaning":"被花費在……上","examples":[{"en":"About $100 billion has been spent on the ISS so far.","zh":"到目前為止，約一千億美元已被花費在國際太空站上。"},{"en":"To be spent on something means money is used to pay for it.","zh":"被花費在某事上，是指金錢被用來支付該事。"},{"en":"School funds may be spent on books, computers, and classroom repairs.","zh":"學校資金可能被花費在書本、電腦和課室維修上。"},{"en":"When large sums are spent on a project, people may ask whether the benefits justify the cost.","zh":"當大筆金錢被花費在一個項目上，人們可能會問其好處是否值得成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where money is used.","zh":"這個短語描述金錢用在甚麼地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"so far","meaning":"到目前為止","examples":[{"en":"A huge amount of money has been spent on the ISS so far.","zh":"到目前為止，已有巨額金錢花在國際太空站上。"},{"en":"So far means up to now or up to this point in time.","zh":"到目前為止，是指直到現在或直到這個時間點。"},{"en":"So far, the class has finished three chapters of the book.","zh":"到目前為止，全班已完成這本書的三章。"},{"en":"Using “so far” suggests that the situation may continue or change later.","zh":"使用 so far 暗示情況之後可能繼續或改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what has happened up to the present moment.","zh":"這個短語描述到現在為止已發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"by the time","meaning":"到……的時候","examples":[{"en":"The ISS will need more money by the time it ceases operation.","zh":"到國際太空站停止運作的時候，它將需要更多金錢。"},{"en":"By the time means before or when a particular future point is reached.","zh":"到某時候，是指在到達某個未來時間點之前或之時。"},{"en":"By the time students finish the course, they should know the main grammar rules.","zh":"到學生完成課程的時候，他們應該知道主要文法規則。"},{"en":"This phrase connects one event with the time another event happens.","zh":"這個短語把一件事與另一件事發生的時間連接起來。"},{"en":"It is useful for showing a deadline or final point.","zh":"它適合顯示期限或終點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cease operation","meaning":"停止運作","examples":[{"en":"The ISS will need much more money before it ceases operation.","zh":"國際太空站在停止運作前將需要更多金錢。"},{"en":"To cease operation means to stop working or stop being used.","zh":"停止運作，是指停止工作或停止被使用。"},{"en":"An old bus route may cease operation if too few passengers use it.","zh":"如果乘客太少，一條舊巴士路線可能停止運作。"},{"en":"When a machine ceases operation, it may need to be repaired, replaced, or safely shut down.","zh":"當機器停止運作，它可能需要維修、更換或安全關閉。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and means stop operating.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是停止運行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"enormous cost","meaning":"巨額成本","examples":[{"en":"The enormous cost of the ISS could not be paid by one nation.","zh":"國際太空站的巨額成本不可能由一個國家支付。"},{"en":"Enormous cost means a very large amount of money needed for something.","zh":"巨額成本，是某事所需的非常大筆金錢。"},{"en":"Building a new hospital can involve enormous cost because it needs land, staff, and equipment.","zh":"興建新醫院可能涉及巨額成本，因為需要土地、人手和設備。"},{"en":"Enormous cost may force organisations to share expenses or seek outside funding.","zh":"巨額成本可能迫使機構分擔開支或尋求外部資金。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cost that is too large to ignore.","zh":"這個短語描述大得不能忽視的成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a joint effort","meaning":"共同努力；合作項目","examples":[{"en":"The ISS was necessarily a joint effort by several space agencies.","zh":"國際太空站必然是幾個太空機構共同努力的成果。"},{"en":"A joint effort is work done together by two or more people or organisations.","zh":"共同努力，是由兩個或多個人或機構一起完成的工作。"},{"en":"A school fair may be a joint effort by teachers, parents, and students.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能是老師、家長和學生共同努力的成果。"},{"en":"Large projects often need joint effort because no single group has enough money, skills, or time.","zh":"大型項目通常需要共同努力，因為單一群體沒有足夠金錢、技能或時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cooperation toward a shared goal.","zh":"這個短語描述為共同目標而合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"no fewer than","meaning":"不少於","examples":[{"en":"No fewer than five space agencies worked on the ISS.","zh":"不少於五個太空機構參與國際太空站項目。"},{"en":"No fewer than means at least that number, often suggesting the number is surprisingly large.","zh":"不少於，是指至少達到該數量，通常暗示數量出乎意料地大。"},{"en":"No fewer than thirty students joined the after-school science club.","zh":"不少於三十名學生參加了課後科學學會。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises that the number is not small.","zh":"這個短語強調數量不小。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing scale or importance.","zh":"它適合用來顯示規模或重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"space agencies","meaning":"太空機構","examples":[{"en":"Five different space agencies contributed to the ISS.","zh":"五個不同太空機構為國際太空站作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Space agencies are organisations that plan, fund, or carry out space exploration and research.","zh":"太空機構是規劃、資助或執行太空探索和研究的組織。"},{"en":"A national space agency may launch satellites, train astronauts, and study planets.","zh":"國家太空機構可能發射衛星、訓練太空人和研究行星。"},{"en":"Space agencies cooperate when projects are too large for one country alone.","zh":"當項目太大，單一國家無法獨自完成時，太空機構會合作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to official organisations involved in space work.","zh":"這個短語指參與太空工作的官方組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"European equivalent","meaning":"歐洲對應機構","examples":[{"en":"ESA is the European equivalent of the other space agencies.","zh":"ESA 是其他太空機構的歐洲對應機構。"},{"en":"A European equivalent is a European organisation, person, or thing that has a similar role to another one.","zh":"歐洲對應機構，是在歐洲具有相似角色的組織、人物或事物。"},{"en":"A European equivalent of a school exam board may set exams for several countries.","zh":"某個學校考試局的歐洲對應機構，可能為幾個國家制定考試。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare institutions that do similar work in different regions.","zh":"這個短語有助比較不同地區中做相似工作的機構。"},{"en":"It means the European version or counterpart.","zh":"它意思是歐洲版本或對應者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ferry payloads into","meaning":"將載荷運送到……","examples":[{"en":"It is difficult to ferry payloads into space.","zh":"將載荷運送到太空是困難的。"},{"en":"To ferry payloads into a place means to transport useful cargo there, usually repeatedly or with effort.","zh":"將載荷運送到某處，是指把有用貨物運到那裡，通常是反覆或費力地運送。"},{"en":"Trucks may ferry supplies into a remote village after a storm.","zh":"風暴後，貨車可能將補給品運送到偏遠村落。"},{"en":"Ferrying payloads into space is expensive because rockets must lift heavy cargo against gravity.","zh":"將載荷運送到太空很昂貴，因為火箭必須把重貨物送離地球引力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transporting equipment or materials to a difficult destination.","zh":"這個短語描述把設備或材料運送到困難目的地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"payloads","meaning":"有效載荷","examples":[{"en":"Spacecraft were used to ferry payloads to the ISS.","zh":"太空船被用來把有效載荷運送到國際太空站。"},{"en":"Payloads are the useful cargo carried by a vehicle, aircraft, or spacecraft.","zh":"有效載荷是車輛、飛機或太空船運載的有用貨物。"},{"en":"A delivery drone’s payload may be medicine for a patient in a remote area.","zh":"送貨無人機的有效載荷可能是給偏遠地區病人的藥物。"},{"en":"In space travel, payloads may include equipment, food, experiments, or station modules.","zh":"在太空旅行中，有效載荷可能包括設備、食物、實驗或太空站艙段。"},{"en":"This word refers to what is being carried, not the vehicle itself.","zh":"這個詞指被運載的東西，而不是運載工具本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a project of the scale of","meaning":"……這種規模的項目","examples":[{"en":"A project of the scale of the ISS could not be built by one country alone.","zh":"國際太空站這種規模的項目不可能由一個國家獨自建成。"},{"en":"A project of the scale of something means a project as large or complex as that example.","zh":"某事這種規模的項目，是指與該例子一樣龐大或複雜的項目。"},{"en":"A project of the scale of a new airport needs years of planning and many teams.","zh":"新機場這種規模的項目需要多年規劃和多個團隊。"},{"en":"Very large-scale projects often require shared funding and international cooperation.","zh":"非常大型的項目通常需要共同資金和國際合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a project’s great size and difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述項目的巨大規模和難度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ready-made station","meaning":"現成太空站","examples":[{"en":"The ISS could not be launched as a ready-made station.","zh":"國際太空站不可能作為現成太空站被發射。"},{"en":"A ready-made station is a station already complete before being moved or used.","zh":"現成太空站是移動或使用前已經完成的太空站。"},{"en":"A ready-made classroom building can be delivered in sections and used quickly.","zh":"現成課室建築可以分段運送並快速使用。"},{"en":"The ISS was too large to launch as one complete ready-made structure.","zh":"國際太空站太大，不可能作為一個完整現成結構發射。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something finished before installation or use.","zh":"這個短語描述在安裝或使用前已完成的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the earliest varieties","meaning":"最早期的種類","examples":[{"en":"The earliest varieties of space stations were simpler.","zh":"最早期的太空站種類較簡單。"},{"en":"The earliest varieties means the first types or versions of something.","zh":"最早期的種類，是某事物最初的類型或版本。"},{"en":"The earliest varieties of mobile phones were heavy and had few functions.","zh":"最早期的手提電話又重又功能少。"},{"en":"Early versions are often simpler because technology and experience are still limited.","zh":"早期版本通常較簡單，因為科技和經驗仍有限。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first forms of a thing.","zh":"這個短語描述某物最初的形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"module by module","meaning":"逐個組件地","examples":[{"en":"The ISS was built module by module.","zh":"國際太空站是逐個組件地建成的。"},{"en":"Module by module means one separate section at a time.","zh":"逐個組件地，是指一次建造一個獨立部分。"},{"en":"A website may be built module by module, starting with login and then adding payment.","zh":"網站可以逐個模組建成，先建立登入功能，再加入付款功能。"},{"en":"Building the ISS module by module allowed each part to be launched separately.","zh":"國際太空站逐個組件地建造，讓每部分能分開發射。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual construction from separate units.","zh":"這個短語描述由獨立單位逐步組成的建設方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be flown into space","meaning":"被送入太空","examples":[{"en":"Each module was flown into space before being attached.","zh":"每個組件在連接前都被送入太空。"},{"en":"To be flown into space means to be carried into space by a rocket or spacecraft.","zh":"被送入太空，是指由火箭或太空船運載到太空。"},{"en":"Scientific equipment may be flown into space for experiments on a station.","zh":"科學設備可能被送入太空，在太空站上進行實驗。"},{"en":"Because space cargo is difficult to transport, each item must be carefully planned before launch.","zh":"因為太空貨物難以運送，每件物品在發射前都必須仔細規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being transported from Earth to space.","zh":"這個短語描述由地球被運送到太空。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"intricately connected","meaning":"錯綜複雜地連接","examples":[{"en":"The modules were intricately connected in orbit.","zh":"這些組件在軌道上錯綜複雜地連接起來。"},{"en":"Intricately connected means joined together in a complicated and detailed way.","zh":"錯綜複雜地連接，是指以複雜而細緻的方式連接在一起。"},{"en":"The wires inside a computer are intricately connected to different parts.","zh":"電腦內的電線錯綜複雜地連接到不同部件。"},{"en":"If parts are intricately connected, damage to one part may affect others.","zh":"如果各部分錯綜複雜地連接，一個部分受損可能影響其他部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a complex connection between components.","zh":"這個短語描述組件之間的複雜連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"eventually became","meaning":"最終變成","examples":[{"en":"The ISS eventually became an awkward-looking structure.","zh":"國際太空站最終變成一個外形笨拙的結構。"},{"en":"Eventually became means finally changed into a particular state after a long process.","zh":"最終變成，是指經過長時間過程後，最後變成某種狀態。"},{"en":"A small tutoring group eventually became a full education centre.","zh":"一個小型補習小組最終變成完整教育中心。"},{"en":"Step-by-step construction can eventually create something much larger than the first part.","zh":"一步一步建造，最終可以創造出比最初部分大得多的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a final result after development over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間發展後的最終結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"awkward-looking conglomeration","meaning":"外形笨拙的組合體","examples":[{"en":"The ISS became an awkward-looking conglomeration of modules.","zh":"國際太空站變成由多個組件構成的外形笨拙組合體。"},{"en":"An awkward-looking conglomeration is a large, uneven collection of parts that looks complicated or ungainly.","zh":"外形笨拙的組合體，是由許多部分組成、看起來複雜或不靈巧的大型集合體。"},{"en":"A desk covered with cables, books, and devices may look like an awkward-looking conglomeration.","zh":"滿是電線、書本和裝置的書桌可能看起來像外形笨拙的組合體。"},{"en":"The ISS looks unusual because many modules and structures were added at different times.","zh":"國際太空站看起來不尋常，因為許多艙段和結構在不同時間被加入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something made of many joined parts that does not look smooth or simple.","zh":"這個短語描述由許多連接部分組成、外觀不流暢或不簡單的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"viewed with Earth in the background","meaning":"以地球作背景觀看時","examples":[{"en":"The station is impressive when viewed with Earth in the background.","zh":"當以地球作背景觀看時，太空站令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"Viewed with Earth in the background means seen with Earth behind it in the image or view.","zh":"以地球作背景觀看時，是指在圖像或視野中以地球在後方來觀看。"},{"en":"A mountain may look more dramatic when viewed with sunset in the background.","zh":"一座山以日落作背景觀看時，可能顯得更壯觀。"},{"en":"Seeing the ISS with Earth behind it helps people understand its size and position in orbit.","zh":"看見國際太空站以地球作背景，有助人們理解它的大小和軌道位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how the background changes the visual impression.","zh":"這個短語描述背景如何改變視覺印象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a grand and inspiring monument to","meaning":"對……宏偉而令人振奮的見證","examples":[{"en":"The ISS is a grand and inspiring monument to human ingenuity.","zh":"國際太空站是人類智慧和創造力的宏偉而令人振奮的見證。"},{"en":"A grand and inspiring monument to something is an impressive thing that shows respect for or proves that quality.","zh":"對某事的宏偉而令人振奮的見證，是令人印象深刻、展示或證明某種特質的事物。"},{"en":"A well-designed public library can be a monument to a city’s belief in education.","zh":"設計出色的公共圖書館，可以成為一座城市相信教育的見證。"},{"en":"The ISS inspires people because it shows what cooperation, science, and engineering can achieve.","zh":"國際太空站令人振奮，因為它顯示合作、科學和工程能達成甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase praises something as a powerful symbol of human achievement.","zh":"這個短語把某物讚揚為人類成就的有力象徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"humankind’s ingenuity","meaning":"人類的智慧和創造力","examples":[{"en":"The ISS shows humankind’s ingenuity.","zh":"國際太空站顯示人類的智慧和創造力。"},{"en":"Humankind’s ingenuity means the creativity and clever problem-solving ability of human beings.","zh":"人類的智慧和創造力，是人類的創意和巧妙解難能力。"},{"en":"Bridges, vaccines, and satellites all show humankind’s ingenuity.","zh":"橋樑、疫苗和衛星都顯示人類的智慧和創造力。"},{"en":"Ingenuity is needed when people solve problems that are too difficult for ordinary methods.","zh":"當人們解決普通方法無法處理的難題時，就需要智慧和創造力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes human cleverness in designing and building new things.","zh":"這個短語描述人類設計和建造新事物的聰明能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"break to pieces","meaning":"碎裂成多塊","examples":[{"en":"Such a construction would break to pieces under ordinary gravity.","zh":"這樣的構造在普通重力環境下會碎裂成多塊。"},{"en":"To break to pieces means to fall apart into many separate parts.","zh":"碎裂成多塊，是指分裂成許多獨立部分。"},{"en":"A glass cup may break to pieces if it falls onto a hard floor.","zh":"玻璃杯如果跌到硬地上，可能碎裂成多塊。"},{"en":"A structure that works in space may break to pieces on Earth because gravity pulls on it differently.","zh":"在太空中可行的結構，可能因地球重力以不同方式拉扯而碎裂成多塊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severe physical collapse or destruction.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重的實體崩塌或破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"under its own weight","meaning":"在自身重量下","examples":[{"en":"The structure would collapse under its own weight on Earth.","zh":"這個結構在地球上會在自身重量下倒塌。"},{"en":"Under its own weight means because it is too heavy to support itself.","zh":"在自身重量下，是指因太重而無法支撐自己。"},{"en":"A weak shelf may bend under its own weight even before books are placed on it.","zh":"薄弱書架即使未放書，也可能在自身重量下彎曲。"},{"en":"Gravity can make a large structure fail if it was not designed to support its own mass.","zh":"如果大型結構不是為支撐自身質量而設計，重力會令它失效。"},{"en":"This phrase explains collapse caused by the object’s heaviness.","zh":"這個短語解釋由物體自身重量造成的倒塌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ordinary gravity","meaning":"普通重力環境","examples":[{"en":"The ISS would not survive as one structure in ordinary gravity.","zh":"國際太空站在普通重力環境中無法作為一個整體結構存在。"},{"en":"Ordinary gravity means the normal gravitational force experienced on Earth.","zh":"普通重力環境，是地球上所感受到的正常重力。"},{"en":"A heavy table stands firmly in ordinary gravity, but a fragile space structure may not.","zh":"厚重桌子在普通重力中可以穩固站立，但脆弱太空結構可能不行。"},{"en":"In orbit, the ISS does not feel weight in the same way it would under ordinary gravity.","zh":"在軌道上，國際太空站不像在普通重力環境中那樣感受到重量。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts Earth-like gravity with weightlessness in space.","zh":"這個短語把地球式重力與太空失重作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be in orbit","meaning":"在軌道上運行","examples":[{"en":"The station is in orbit around Earth.","zh":"太空站在地球軌道上運行。"},{"en":"To be in orbit means to move repeatedly around a planet or other body in space.","zh":"在軌道上運行，是指在太空中反覆繞行星或其他天體移動。"},{"en":"The moon is in orbit around Earth.","zh":"月球在地球軌道上運行。"},{"en":"An object in orbit keeps falling toward Earth but also moving sideways fast enough to miss it.","zh":"在軌道上的物體不斷向地球下墜，但同時橫向移動夠快，所以不會撞上地球。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled motion around a celestial body.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞天體的受控運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"its weight is not felt","meaning":"其重量不被感受到","examples":[{"en":"Because the station is in orbit, its weight is not felt.","zh":"因為太空站在軌道上，它的重量不被感受到。"},{"en":"Its weight is not felt means it does not press downward in the usual way.","zh":"其重量不被感受到，是指它不以平常方式向下施壓。"},{"en":"Astronauts feel weightless because their bodies and the spacecraft are falling together.","zh":"太空人感到失重，因為他們的身體和太空船一起下墜。"},{"en":"When weight is not felt, people and objects can float inside the spacecraft.","zh":"當重量不被感受到，人和物件可以在太空船內漂浮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the experience of weightlessness in orbit.","zh":"這個短語描述軌道上的失重體驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"constantly free-falling","meaning":"不斷自由下墜","examples":[{"en":"The ISS is constantly free-falling around Earth.","zh":"國際太空站正不斷繞地球自由下墜。"},{"en":"Constantly free-falling means continuously falling under gravity without hitting the ground.","zh":"不斷自由下墜，是指持續在重力作用下下墜，但不撞到地面。"},{"en":"A lift dropping suddenly would make passengers feel as if they were briefly free-falling.","zh":"電梯突然下墜時，乘客可能感到自己短暫地自由下墜。"},{"en":"The ISS stays in orbit because it falls toward Earth while moving sideways very fast.","zh":"國際太空站留在軌道上，因為它向地球下墜，同時以很快橫向速度移動。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why astronauts feel weightless.","zh":"這個短語解釋太空人為何感到失重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"under Earth’s gravitational pull","meaning":"在地球引力作用下","examples":[{"en":"The station is free-falling under Earth’s gravitational pull.","zh":"太空站在地球引力作用下自由下墜。"},{"en":"Under Earth’s gravitational pull means affected by the force that pulls objects toward Earth.","zh":"在地球引力作用下，是指受到把物體拉向地球的力量影響。"},{"en":"A ball dropped from a window falls under Earth’s gravitational pull.","zh":"從窗邊掉下的球會在地球引力作用下下墜。"},{"en":"Even in orbit, the ISS is still affected by Earth’s gravity.","zh":"即使在軌道上，國際太空站仍受地球重力影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the force causing objects to fall toward Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述令物體向地球下墜的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"never hit the planet","meaning":"永不撞上地球","examples":[{"en":"The ISS keeps falling but never hits the planet.","zh":"國際太空站不斷下墜，但永不撞上地球。"},{"en":"To never hit the planet means not to crash into Earth despite being pulled by gravity.","zh":"永不撞上地球，是指即使被重力拉動，也不會撞向地球。"},{"en":"A satellite can keep missing Earth if it moves sideways fast enough.","zh":"如果衛星橫向移動夠快，它可以一直錯過地球。"},{"en":"The ISS avoids hitting the planet because its forward speed balances its fall.","zh":"國際太空站避免撞上地球，因為其前進速度平衡了下墜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how orbital motion prevents collision.","zh":"這個短語描述軌道運動如何防止碰撞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"due to","meaning":"由於","examples":[{"en":"The station avoids hitting Earth due to its lateral velocity.","zh":"太空站由於其橫向速度而避免撞上地球。"},{"en":"Due to means because of.","zh":"due to 意思是「由於」。"},{"en":"The picnic was cancelled due to heavy rain.","zh":"野餐由於大雨而取消。"},{"en":"In space, the ISS avoids collision due to its sideways motion around Earth.","zh":"在太空中，國際太空站由於圍繞地球的橫向運動而避免碰撞。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the reason for something.","zh":"這個短語引入某事的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lateral velocity","meaning":"橫向速度","examples":[{"en":"The ISS does not hit Earth because of its lateral velocity.","zh":"國際太空站因其橫向速度而不會撞上地球。"},{"en":"Lateral velocity is sideways speed, especially movement across rather than directly downward.","zh":"橫向速度是側向速度，尤其是橫向移動而不是直接向下。"},{"en":"A ball thrown sideways has lateral velocity as well as downward motion.","zh":"向側面拋出的球除了向下運動，也有橫向速度。"},{"en":"The ISS needs lateral velocity to keep missing Earth while gravity pulls it downward.","zh":"國際太空站需要橫向速度，在重力把它向下拉時一直錯過地球。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sideways motion that helps maintain orbit.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助維持軌道的側向運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not continue forever","meaning":"不會永遠持續","examples":[{"en":"The station’s orbit will not continue forever.","zh":"太空站的軌道不會永遠持續。"},{"en":"Not continue forever means it will eventually end or change.","zh":"不會永遠持續，是指它最終會結束或改變。"},{"en":"A phone battery will not continue forever if it is not recharged.","zh":"如果不充電，手機電池不會永遠持續。"},{"en":"The ISS orbit slowly decays, so it needs boosts to stay at the right height.","zh":"國際太空站軌道會慢慢衰減，所以需要推進以維持正確高度。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a situation is not permanent.","zh":"這個短語提醒某情況並非永久。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"low-Earth orbit","meaning":"低地球軌道","examples":[{"en":"The ISS travels in low-Earth orbit.","zh":"國際太空站在低地球軌道運行。"},{"en":"Low-Earth orbit is an orbit relatively close to Earth’s surface.","zh":"低地球軌道是相對接近地球表面的軌道。"},{"en":"Many communication and observation satellites are placed in low-Earth orbit.","zh":"許多通訊和觀測衛星被放置在低地球軌道。"},{"en":"Objects in low-Earth orbit may still experience slight atmospheric drag.","zh":"在低地球軌道上的物體仍可能受到輕微大氣阻力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the region of space where the ISS travels.","zh":"這個短語描述國際太空站運行的太空區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"aerodynamic drag","meaning":"空氣動力阻力","examples":[{"en":"Aerodynamic drag slowly reduces the speed of the ISS.","zh":"空氣動力阻力慢慢降低國際太空站的速度。"},{"en":"Aerodynamic drag is resistance from air or atmosphere that slows a moving object.","zh":"空氣動力阻力是空氣或大氣對移動物體造成的阻力，使其減慢。"},{"en":"A cyclist feels aerodynamic drag when riding fast against the air.","zh":"單車手高速騎行時會感受到空氣動力阻力。"},{"en":"Even the faint atmosphere in low-Earth orbit can create drag and slow the ISS.","zh":"即使低地球軌道中的稀薄大氣，也可以產生阻力並減慢國際太空站。"},{"en":"This phrase describes air resistance acting on a moving object.","zh":"這個短語描述作用於移動物體上的空氣阻力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"faint atmosphere","meaning":"稀薄大氣","examples":[{"en":"The ISS passes through a faint atmosphere.","zh":"國際太空站穿過稀薄大氣。"},{"en":"A faint atmosphere is a very thin layer of gas with much less air than near Earth’s surface.","zh":"稀薄大氣是非常薄的氣體層，空氣遠少於地球表面附近。"},{"en":"A mountaintop has thinner air than a city, but low-Earth orbit has a far fainter atmosphere.","zh":"山頂空氣比城市稀薄，但低地球軌道的大氣遠更稀薄。"},{"en":"Even a faint atmosphere can create drag when an object moves extremely fast.","zh":"即使稀薄大氣，在物體高速移動時仍可產生阻力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very thin atmospheric gas.","zh":"這個短語描述非常稀薄的大氣氣體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"continually plough through","meaning":"不斷穿越","examples":[{"en":"The station continually ploughs through the faint atmosphere.","zh":"太空站不斷穿越稀薄大氣。"},{"en":"To continually plough through something means to keep pushing through it with effort or resistance.","zh":"不斷穿越某物，是指持續費力或受到阻力地推進穿過它。"},{"en":"A bus may plough through heavy rain during a storm.","zh":"巴士可能在暴風雨中不斷穿越大雨。"},{"en":"The ISS loses speed because it keeps pushing through thin atmospheric particles.","zh":"國際太空站因持續穿過稀薄大氣粒子而失去速度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated movement through something that slows progress.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆穿過會減慢進展的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"result in","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"Aerodynamic drag results in a small loss of speed.","zh":"空氣動力阻力導致小幅速度流失。"},{"en":"To result in something means to cause it to happen.","zh":"導致某事，是指造成它發生。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can result in poor concentration during lessons.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致上課時專注力差。"},{"en":"In orbit, drag results in gradual slowing and orbital decay.","zh":"在軌道上，阻力導致逐漸減速和軌道衰減。"},{"en":"This phrase connects cause and effect.","zh":"這個短語連接原因和結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a small yet steady loss of speed","meaning":"細微但持續的速度流失","examples":[{"en":"The ISS experiences a small yet steady loss of speed.","zh":"國際太空站經歷細微但持續的速度流失。"},{"en":"A small yet steady loss of speed means a slight decrease that continues over time.","zh":"細微但持續的速度流失，是指速度輕微下降，但持續發生。"},{"en":"A bicycle with a soft tyre may suffer a small yet steady loss of speed.","zh":"輪胎偏軟的單車可能出現細微但持續的速度流失。"},{"en":"Even a small steady slowdown matters in orbit because it can lower the station’s path.","zh":"即使細微的持續減速，在軌道上也重要，因為它會降低太空站軌道。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual but continuous slowing.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸但持續的減速。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"perceptible loss of speed","meaning":"可察覺的速度流失","examples":[{"en":"The drag causes a perceptible loss of speed.","zh":"阻力造成可察覺的速度流失。"},{"en":"A perceptible loss of speed is a decrease in speed that can be noticed or measured.","zh":"可察覺的速度流失，是可以被注意或量度到的速度下降。"},{"en":"A car climbing a steep hill may show a perceptible loss of speed.","zh":"汽車爬陡斜坡時可能出現可察覺的速度流失。"},{"en":"When drag continues, a small slowdown can become perceptible over time.","zh":"當阻力持續，小幅減速會隨時間變得可察覺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes speed loss that is no longer invisible.","zh":"這個短語描述不再看不見的速度流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"consequent orbital decay","meaning":"隨之而來的軌道衰減","examples":[{"en":"The loss of speed causes consequent orbital decay.","zh":"速度流失導致隨之而來的軌道衰減。"},{"en":"Consequent orbital decay means the resulting gradual lowering or weakening of an orbit.","zh":"隨之而來的軌道衰減，是由此造成的軌道逐漸降低或變弱。"},{"en":"A satellite may need engine boosts to correct orbital decay.","zh":"衛星可能需要引擎推進來修正軌道衰減。"},{"en":"If an orbit decays too much, the object may fall lower and eventually re-enter the atmosphere.","zh":"如果軌道衰減太多，物體可能下降並最終重返大氣層。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the result of losing orbital speed.","zh":"這個短語描述失去軌道速度造成的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"contribute to this loss","meaning":"導致這種損失","examples":[{"en":"Tidal forces also contribute to this loss of speed.","zh":"潮汐力也導致這種速度流失。"},{"en":"To contribute to this loss means to be one of the causes that make the loss happen.","zh":"導致這種損失，是指成為造成該損失的其中一個原因。"},{"en":"Poor diet and lack of sleep can both contribute to a loss of energy.","zh":"飲食差和睡眠不足都可以導致精力流失。"},{"en":"Several small causes can contribute to one larger problem.","zh":"幾個小原因可以共同造成一個更大問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding to an existing loss or difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述增加現有損失或困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tidal forces","meaning":"潮汐力","examples":[{"en":"Tidal forces contribute to the ISS’s loss of speed.","zh":"潮汐力導致國際太空站速度流失。"},{"en":"Tidal forces are gravitational effects that stretch or pull different parts of an object differently.","zh":"潮汐力是重力效應，會以不同方式拉伸或拉扯物體不同部分。"},{"en":"The moon’s tidal forces help create ocean tides on Earth.","zh":"月球的潮汐力幫助形成地球海洋潮汐。"},{"en":"On a large space structure, tidal forces can make different parts flex slightly.","zh":"在大型太空結構上，潮汐力可以令不同部分輕微彎曲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gravity-related stretching forces.","zh":"這個短語描述與重力相關的拉伸力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"loosely connected","meaning":"鬆散連接的","examples":[{"en":"The ISS is large and loosely connected.","zh":"國際太空站很大，而且是鬆散連接的。"},{"en":"Loosely connected means joined together but not in one tight, solid block.","zh":"鬆散連接的，是指連接在一起，但不是一整塊緊密堅固的結構。"},{"en":"A temporary market stall may be loosely connected with ropes and metal poles.","zh":"臨時市集攤位可能用繩和金屬杆鬆散連接起來。"},{"en":"Loosely connected parts can move or flex more than tightly joined parts.","zh":"鬆散連接的部分比緊密連接的部分更容易移動或彎曲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a structure with flexible or less rigid connections.","zh":"這個短語描述具有彈性或較不剛性的連接結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"further from the Earth","meaning":"離地球較遠","examples":[{"en":"The parts further from the Earth flex more than the closer parts.","zh":"離地球較遠的部分比較接近的部分彎曲更多。"},{"en":"Further from the Earth means at a greater distance from Earth’s surface or centre.","zh":"離地球較遠，是指距離地球表面或中心更遠。"},{"en":"A satellite is further from the Earth than an airplane.","zh":"衛星比飛機離地球較遠。"},{"en":"Parts further from Earth may experience slightly different gravitational effects.","zh":"離地球較遠的部分可能受到略有不同的重力效應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relative distance from Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述與地球的相對距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"flex more than","meaning":"比……彎曲更多","examples":[{"en":"Some parts of the ISS flex more than others.","zh":"國際太空站某些部分比其他部分彎曲更多。"},{"en":"To flex more than something means to bend or move slightly more than it does.","zh":"比某物彎曲更多，是指比它更大程度地彎曲或輕微移動。"},{"en":"A thin ruler flexes more than a thick wooden board.","zh":"薄尺比厚木板彎曲更多。"},{"en":"If one part of a structure flexes more than another, energy can be lost through repeated movement.","zh":"如果結構某部分比另一部分彎曲更多，能量可能透過反覆移動而流失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relative bending or movement.","zh":"這個短語描述相對彎曲或移動程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"closer to","meaning":"較接近……","examples":[{"en":"The parts closer to Earth flex less.","zh":"較接近地球的部分彎曲較少。"},{"en":"Closer to something means nearer to it in distance.","zh":"較接近某物，是指距離它較近。"},{"en":"Students sitting closer to the board can usually read small writing more easily.","zh":"坐得較接近黑板的學生通常更容易看清細字。"},{"en":"In the ISS, parts closer to Earth experience slightly different forces from parts farther away.","zh":"在國際太空站中，較接近地球的部分受到的力與較遠部分略有不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shorter distance from a reference point.","zh":"這個短語描述距離參照點較短。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"use up energy","meaning":"消耗能量","examples":[{"en":"The flexing parts use up energy.","zh":"彎曲的部分會消耗能量。"},{"en":"To use up energy means to consume or spend energy until less is available.","zh":"消耗能量，是指使用或花費能量，使可用能量變少。"},{"en":"Running upstairs can use up energy quickly.","zh":"跑上樓梯可以很快消耗能量。"},{"en":"When station parts flex repeatedly, some orbital energy is gradually lost.","zh":"當太空站部分反覆彎曲，一些軌道能量會逐漸流失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes energy being consumed by an action.","zh":"這個短語描述行動消耗能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the largest component","meaning":"最大組件","examples":[{"en":"The largest component of the ISS is the Truss Structure.","zh":"國際太空站的最大組件是桁架結構。"},{"en":"The largest component is the biggest part of a larger system.","zh":"最大組件是較大系統中最大的部分。"},{"en":"The largest component of a school budget may be staff salaries.","zh":"學校預算的最大組件可能是員工薪酬。"},{"en":"Identifying the largest component helps people understand the structure of a complex whole.","zh":"識別最大組件有助人們理解複雜整體的結構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the biggest single part.","zh":"這個短語描述最大的單一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Truss Structure","meaning":"桁架結構","examples":[{"en":"The Truss Structure forms the main spine of the ISS.","zh":"桁架結構形成國際太空站的主要脊柱。"},{"en":"The Truss Structure is a long framework that supports equipment and holds major parts together.","zh":"桁架結構是支撐設備並把主要部分固定在一起的長形框架。"},{"en":"A bridge may use a truss structure to support weight across a wide gap.","zh":"橋樑可能使用桁架結構，以跨越寬闊距離並支撐重量。"},{"en":"On the ISS, the Truss Structure supports solar arrays and other external systems.","zh":"在國際太空站上，桁架結構支撐太陽能板陣列和其他外部系統。"},{"en":"This phrase names the main structural framework of the station.","zh":"這個短語命名太空站的主要結構框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"non-pressurised","meaning":"非加壓的","examples":[{"en":"The Truss Structure is a non-pressurised spine.","zh":"桁架結構是一條非加壓的主幹。"},{"en":"Non-pressurised means not filled with breathable air at safe pressure for humans.","zh":"非加壓的，是指沒有充滿適合人類安全呼吸壓力的空氣。"},{"en":"A storage area outside a spacecraft may be non-pressurised and unsafe without a spacesuit.","zh":"太空船外部儲物區可能是非加壓的，沒有太空衣就不安全。"},{"en":"Astronauts cannot live inside non-pressurised parts because there is no suitable atmosphere.","zh":"太空人不能住在非加壓部分，因為沒有合適大氣。"},{"en":"This word describes a space that is not made safe for human breathing.","zh":"這個詞描述未被設計成可供人呼吸的空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ten-segment spine","meaning":"十段式主幹","examples":[{"en":"The Truss Structure is a ten-segment spine.","zh":"桁架結構是一條十段式主幹。"},{"en":"A ten-segment spine is a backbone-like structure made of ten sections.","zh":"十段式主幹，是由十個部分組成、像脊柱一樣的支撐結構。"},{"en":"A long bridge may have a segmented spine that supports different platforms.","zh":"長橋可能有分段式主幹，以支撐不同平台。"},{"en":"Dividing a structure into segments makes it easier to launch, assemble, or repair.","zh":"把結構分成多段，可以令發射、組裝或維修更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the ISS’s long supporting framework.","zh":"這個短語描述國際太空站的長形支撐框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be connected to","meaning":"與……連接","examples":[{"en":"The solar arrays are connected to the Truss Structure.","zh":"太陽能板陣列與桁架結構連接。"},{"en":"To be connected to something means to be joined or attached to it.","zh":"與某物連接，是指與它接合或附着。"},{"en":"A printer may be connected to a computer by a cable or wireless network.","zh":"打印機可能透過電線或無線網絡與電腦連接。"},{"en":"If one part is connected to another, power, support, or information may pass between them.","zh":"如果一部分與另一部分連接，電力、支撐或資訊可能在兩者之間傳遞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical or functional linking.","zh":"這個短語描述實體或功能上的連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"extensive solar arrays","meaning":"大型太陽能板陣列","examples":[{"en":"The ISS has extensive solar arrays at one end.","zh":"國際太空站一端有大型太陽能板陣列。"},{"en":"Extensive solar arrays are large groups of solar panels that collect sunlight for power.","zh":"大型太陽能板陣列，是收集陽光發電的一大組太陽能板。"},{"en":"A school roof may have solar arrays to provide electricity for classrooms.","zh":"學校屋頂可能有太陽能板陣列，為課室供電。"},{"en":"The ISS needs extensive solar arrays because it relies on sunlight for electrical power.","zh":"國際太空站需要大型太陽能板陣列，因為它依靠陽光產生電力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large power-generating panel systems.","zh":"這個短語描述大型發電板系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"thermal radiators","meaning":"散熱器","examples":[{"en":"Thermal radiators are connected towards the centre of the structure.","zh":"散熱器連接在結構較接近中央的位置。"},{"en":"Thermal radiators are devices that release extra heat into space or the surrounding environment.","zh":"散熱器是把多餘熱量釋放到太空或周圍環境的裝置。"},{"en":"A car radiator helps remove heat from the engine so it does not overheat.","zh":"汽車散熱器幫助引擎散熱，避免過熱。"},{"en":"On the ISS, thermal radiators prevent equipment and living areas from becoming too hot.","zh":"在國際太空站上，散熱器防止設備和生活區變得太熱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes equipment used for heat control.","zh":"這個短語描述用於控制熱量的設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"towards the centre","meaning":"朝向中央；靠近中央","examples":[{"en":"The thermal radiators are positioned towards the centre.","zh":"散熱器被放置在靠近中央的位置。"},{"en":"Towards the centre means nearer to the middle part of something.","zh":"朝向中央或靠近中央，是指較接近某物的中間部分。"},{"en":"In a theatre, expensive seats are often towards the centre because the view is better.","zh":"在劇院中，昂貴座位通常靠近中央，因為視野較好。"},{"en":"Parts placed towards the centre may be easier to connect to several systems.","zh":"放在中央附近的部分可能較容易連接到多個系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direction or position nearer the middle.","zh":"這個短語描述方向或位置較接近中間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"perpendicular to","meaning":"與……成直角","examples":[{"en":"The pressurised modules are perpendicular to the Truss Structure.","zh":"加壓艙段與桁架結構成直角。"},{"en":"Perpendicular to something means at a right angle to it.","zh":"與某物成直角，是指與它呈九十度角。"},{"en":"The legs of a table are usually perpendicular to the floor.","zh":"桌腳通常與地面成直角。"},{"en":"If one structure is perpendicular to another, they cross or meet at about 90 degrees.","zh":"如果一個結構與另一個結構成直角，它們大約以九十度相交或連接。"},{"en":"This phrase describes geometric position.","zh":"這個短語描述幾何位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pressurised modules","meaning":"加壓艙段","examples":[{"en":"The crew live and work inside pressurised modules.","zh":"機組人員在加壓艙段內生活和工作。"},{"en":"Pressurised modules are sealed sections filled with breathable air at safe pressure.","zh":"加壓艙段是密封部分，內有適合安全呼吸壓力的空氣。"},{"en":"Passengers sit inside a pressurised cabin when flying at high altitude.","zh":"乘客在高空飛行時坐在加壓客艙內。"},{"en":"Astronauts need pressurised modules because space outside has no breathable atmosphere.","zh":"太空人需要加壓艙段，因為外太空沒有可呼吸大氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes human-safe living or working sections in a spacecraft.","zh":"這個短語描述太空船中適合人類安全生活或工作的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"begin with","meaning":"以……開始","examples":[{"en":"The station began with the Zarya module.","zh":"太空站以 Zarya 艙段開始。"},{"en":"To begin with something means to start with it as the first part or step.","zh":"以某事開始，是指把它作為第一部分或第一步。"},{"en":"A lesson may begin with a short question to get students thinking.","zh":"課堂可能以一個短問題開始，讓學生思考。"},{"en":"Large projects often begin with one basic part before other pieces are added.","zh":"大型項目通常以一個基本部分開始，然後再加入其他部分。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the starting point of a process.","zh":"這個短語指出過程的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"first launched","meaning":"首次發射","examples":[{"en":"Zarya was first launched in 1998.","zh":"Zarya 於 1998 年首次發射。"},{"en":"First launched means sent into space or introduced for the first time.","zh":"首次發射，是指第一次被送入太空或首次推出。"},{"en":"A new app was first launched in one city before becoming popular worldwide.","zh":"一個新應用程式可能先在一個城市首次推出，然後在全球流行。"},{"en":"The first launch of a module marks the beginning of construction in space.","zh":"一個艙段的首次發射標誌着太空建設的開始。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the starting date of a launch or release.","zh":"這個短語給出發射或推出的起始日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"directly attached to","meaning":"直接連接到……","examples":[{"en":"Unity was directly attached to Zarya.","zh":"Unity 直接連接到 Zarya。"},{"en":"Directly attached to something means joined to it without another part in between.","zh":"直接連接到某物，是指中間沒有其他部分地與它接合。"},{"en":"A handle may be directly attached to a door.","zh":"門把可能直接連接到門上。"},{"en":"Direct attachment can make two parts function as one connected unit.","zh":"直接連接可以令兩部分作為一個相連單位運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a close physical connection.","zh":"這個短語描述緊密的實體連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"notable feature","meaning":"顯著特色","examples":[{"en":"Unity’s most notable feature is the protruding Cupola.","zh":"Unity 最顯著特色是突出的穹頂艙。"},{"en":"A notable feature is an important or easily noticed characteristic.","zh":"顯著特色是重要或容易被注意到的特徵。"},{"en":"A library’s quiet study room may be its most notable feature.","zh":"圖書館的安靜自修室可能是其最顯著特色。"},{"en":"Notable features help people recognise or remember a place or object.","zh":"顯著特色幫助人們認出或記住一個地方或物件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a characteristic that stands out.","zh":"這個短語描述突出的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"protruding Cupola","meaning":"突出的穹頂艙","examples":[{"en":"The protruding Cupola is a large viewing room.","zh":"突出的穹頂艙是一個大型觀景艙。"},{"en":"A protruding Cupola is a dome-like section that sticks out from the main structure.","zh":"突出的穹頂艙，是從主體結構伸出的圓頂狀部分。"},{"en":"A balcony protruding from a building gives people a better view outside.","zh":"從建築物伸出的露台讓人更好地觀看外面。"},{"en":"The Cupola protrudes so astronauts can look out in several directions.","zh":"穹頂艙向外突出，使太空人可以向多個方向觀看。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the outward-projecting viewing area of the ISS.","zh":"這個短語描述國際太空站向外伸出的觀景區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"seven-windowed viewing room","meaning":"有七扇窗的觀景艙","examples":[{"en":"The Cupola is a seven-windowed viewing room.","zh":"穹頂艙是一個有七扇窗的觀景艙。"},{"en":"A seven-windowed viewing room is a room designed for looking out through seven windows.","zh":"有七扇窗的觀景艙，是設計來透過七扇窗向外觀看的房間。"},{"en":"A hotel may advertise a sea-view room with large windows for watching the harbour.","zh":"酒店可能宣傳有大窗可觀看海港的海景房。"},{"en":"The Cupola’s windows help astronauts observe Earth, space, and station operations.","zh":"穹頂艙的窗戶幫助太空人觀察地球、太空和太空站運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a special room built for observation.","zh":"這個短語描述為觀察而建的特殊房間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"absolutely essential for","meaning":"對……絕對必不可少","examples":[{"en":"The Cupola is absolutely essential for the crew’s wellbeing.","zh":"穹頂艙對機組人員的福祉絕對必不可少。"},{"en":"Absolutely essential for something means completely necessary for it.","zh":"對某事絕對必不可少，是指對它完全必要。"},{"en":"Clean water is absolutely essential for public health.","zh":"清潔食水對公共健康絕對必不可少。"},{"en":"The Cupola supports wellbeing because it gives astronauts light, views, and a connection with Earth.","zh":"穹頂艙支持福祉，因為它給太空人光線、景觀和與地球的連結。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that cannot be easily removed or ignored.","zh":"這個短語描述不能輕易移除或忽視的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"psychological wellbeing","meaning":"心理健康","examples":[{"en":"The Cupola supports the psychological wellbeing of the crew.","zh":"穹頂艙支持機組人員的心理健康。"},{"en":"Psychological wellbeing means mental and emotional health.","zh":"心理健康是精神和情緒上的健康。"},{"en":"Regular sleep, friendship, and quiet time can support a student’s psychological wellbeing.","zh":"規律睡眠、友誼和安靜時間可以支持學生心理健康。"},{"en":"In space, views of Earth may reduce stress and help astronauts feel less isolated.","zh":"在太空中，地球景觀可能減少壓力，幫助太空人感到較少孤立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how well someone is feeling mentally and emotionally.","zh":"這個短語描述某人在心理和情緒上感覺如何。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the crew","meaning":"機組人員","examples":[{"en":"The crew live and work on board the ISS.","zh":"機組人員在國際太空站上生活和工作。"},{"en":"The crew are the people who operate or work on a ship, aircraft, or spacecraft.","zh":"機組人員是在船、飛機或太空船上操作或工作的人。"},{"en":"The crew on a plane includes pilots and flight attendants.","zh":"飛機機組人員包括機師和空中服務員。"},{"en":"On the ISS, the crew must manage experiments, repairs, exercise, and daily living tasks.","zh":"在國際太空站上，機組人員必須管理實驗、維修、運動和日常生活任務。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the working team on board.","zh":"這個短語指在船上或機上工作的團隊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"almost two more years","meaning":"又差不多兩年","examples":[{"en":"It took almost two more years before Zvezda was attached.","zh":"又差不多兩年後，Zvezda 才被接上。"},{"en":"Almost two more years means nearly another two years after the previous event.","zh":"又差不多兩年，是指在前一事件之後再接近兩年。"},{"en":"After finishing secondary school, it may take almost two more years to complete an associate degree.","zh":"完成中學後，完成副學士課程可能又差不多需要兩年。"},{"en":"Large projects can move slowly because each new stage needs planning, testing, and approval.","zh":"大型項目可能進展緩慢，因為每個新階段都需要規劃、測試和批准。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a long additional waiting period.","zh":"這個短語描述很長的額外等待時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"opposite end","meaning":"另一端","examples":[{"en":"Zvezda was attached to Zarya’s opposite end.","zh":"Zvezda 被連接到 Zarya 的另一端。"},{"en":"The opposite end is the far end on the other side of an object.","zh":"另一端，是物件另一邊的遠端。"},{"en":"If the entrance is at one end of a corridor, the toilets may be at the opposite end.","zh":"如果入口在走廊一端，洗手間可能在另一端。"},{"en":"Attaching modules to opposite ends helps extend a structure in different directions.","zh":"把艙段接在不同端部，有助結構向不同方向延伸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position on the other side.","zh":"這個短語描述另一邊的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be fixed to","meaning":"被固定在……上","examples":[{"en":"The Truss Structure was fixed to the Unity Module.","zh":"桁架結構被固定在 Unity 艙段上。"},{"en":"To be fixed to something means to be firmly attached to it.","zh":"被固定在某物上，是指被牢固地連接到它上面。"},{"en":"A noticeboard may be fixed to a classroom wall with screws.","zh":"告示板可能用螺絲被固定在課室牆上。"},{"en":"Parts must be securely fixed to a spacecraft so they do not move dangerously.","zh":"部件必須牢固固定在太空船上，才不會危險地移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes firm physical attachment.","zh":"這個短語描述牢固的實體連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"followed by","meaning":"隨後是","examples":[{"en":"The Truss Structure was added, followed by the Harmony Module.","zh":"桁架結構被加入，隨後是 Harmony 艙段。"},{"en":"Followed by means coming next after something else.","zh":"隨後是，是指在另一事物之後接着出現。"},{"en":"The lesson began with vocabulary practice, followed by a short writing task.","zh":"課堂先進行詞彙練習，隨後是短寫作任務。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe the order of events or steps.","zh":"這個短語有助描述事件或步驟的順序。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining how a project developed over time.","zh":"它適合解釋項目如何隨時間發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"no less complicated","meaning":"同樣複雜","examples":[{"en":"The station’s interior is no less complicated.","zh":"太空站內部同樣複雜。"},{"en":"No less complicated means just as complicated as what has already been described.","zh":"同樣複雜，是指與剛描述的事物一樣複雜。"},{"en":"The outside of a computer looks simple, but its software is no less complicated.","zh":"電腦外觀看似簡單，但其軟件同樣複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that another part is also complex, not easier.","zh":"這個短語顯示另一部分也很複雜，而不是較容易。"},{"en":"It is used to extend a comparison.","zh":"它用來延伸比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"six-member crew","meaning":"六人機組","examples":[{"en":"A six-member crew may stay on board for months.","zh":"六人機組可能在太空站上停留數月。"},{"en":"A six-member crew is a working team made up of six people.","zh":"六人機組是由六個人組成的工作團隊。"},{"en":"A rescue boat may need a six-member crew to operate safely.","zh":"救援船可能需要六人機組才能安全操作。"},{"en":"On the ISS, each crew member has duties such as experiments, repairs, and exercise.","zh":"在國際太空站上，每名機組成員都有實驗、維修和運動等職責。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the size of the operating team.","zh":"這個短語描述操作團隊的大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stay on board","meaning":"留在……上","examples":[{"en":"The crew can stay on board the ISS for up to six months.","zh":"機組人員可以在國際太空站上停留長達六個月。"},{"en":"To stay on board means to remain inside or on a vehicle, ship, aircraft, or spacecraft.","zh":"留在某交通工具或太空站上，是指保持在船、飛機、太空船或太空站內或上面。"},{"en":"Passengers may be asked to stay on board a ferry until staff open the exit.","zh":"乘客可能被要求留在渡輪上，直到職員打開出口。"},{"en":"Astronauts stay on board the ISS for long periods because missions require continuous work.","zh":"太空人在國際太空站上長期停留，因為任務需要持續工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes remaining on a transport or station.","zh":"這個短語描述留在交通工具或站點上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"for up to","meaning":"長達","examples":[{"en":"The crew may remain on the station for up to six months.","zh":"機組人員可在太空站上停留長達六個月。"},{"en":"For up to means for a maximum period or amount of time.","zh":"長達，是指最長可達某段時間或某個數量。"},{"en":"A library book may be borrowed for up to three weeks.","zh":"圖書館書籍可借閱長達三星期。"},{"en":"Saying “for up to six months” means the stay may be shorter, but not longer than that limit.","zh":"說「長達六個月」表示停留時間可能較短，但不會超過該上限。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an upper limit.","zh":"這個短語給出最高限度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"life-support systems","meaning":"生命維持系統","examples":[{"en":"Life-support systems are crucial on the ISS.","zh":"生命維持系統在國際太空站上至關重要。"},{"en":"Life-support systems are machines and processes that keep people alive in dangerous environments.","zh":"生命維持系統是在危險環境中維持人類生命的機器和程序。"},{"en":"A submarine needs life-support systems to provide breathable air underwater.","zh":"潛艇需要生命維持系統在水下提供可呼吸空氣。"},{"en":"On the ISS, life-support systems manage oxygen, air pressure, carbon dioxide, and temperature.","zh":"在國際太空站上，生命維持系統管理氧氣、氣壓、二氧化碳和溫度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes systems that make survival possible.","zh":"這個短語描述令生存成為可能的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"airless and deadly vacuum of space","meaning":"無空氣且致命的太空真空環境","examples":[{"en":"The ISS operates in the airless and deadly vacuum of space.","zh":"國際太空站在無空氣且致命的太空真空環境中運作。"},{"en":"The airless and deadly vacuum of space is the space environment with no breathable air and extreme danger to humans.","zh":"無空氣且致命的太空真空環境，是沒有可呼吸空氣、對人類極度危險的太空環境。"},{"en":"Without a spacesuit, a person could not survive in the vacuum of space.","zh":"沒有太空衣，人無法在太空真空環境中生存。"},{"en":"Because space is airless and deadly, spacecraft must provide a safe internal atmosphere.","zh":"因為太空無空氣且致命，太空船必須提供安全內部大氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes why life-support systems are necessary.","zh":"這個短語描述為何生命維持系統是必要的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"atmospheric control","meaning":"大氣控制","examples":[{"en":"Atmospheric control is the most important element of spacecraft design.","zh":"大氣控制是太空船設計中最重要的元素。"},{"en":"Atmospheric control means managing air pressure, oxygen, carbon dioxide, and air quality.","zh":"大氣控制是管理氣壓、氧氣、二氧化碳和空氣質素。"},{"en":"A hospital room may need air control to protect patients from infection.","zh":"醫院病房可能需要空氣控制，以保護病人免受感染。"},{"en":"In spacecraft, atmospheric control keeps astronauts able to breathe and work safely.","zh":"在太空船中，大氣控制讓太空人能安全呼吸和工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes control of the air environment inside a closed space.","zh":"這個短語描述封閉空間內空氣環境的控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"maintain a stable atmosphere","meaning":"維持穩定大氣","examples":[{"en":"The systems maintain a stable Earth-like atmosphere.","zh":"這些系統維持穩定、類似地球的大氣。"},{"en":"To maintain a stable atmosphere means to keep air conditions safe and steady.","zh":"維持穩定大氣，是指保持空氣條件安全而穩定。"},{"en":"A greenhouse may maintain a stable atmosphere for plants by controlling temperature and humidity.","zh":"溫室可以透過控制溫度和濕度，為植物維持穩定大氣。"},{"en":"If atmosphere is not stable, astronauts may face breathing problems or health risks.","zh":"如果大氣不穩定，太空人可能面對呼吸問題或健康風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping internal air conditions under control.","zh":"這個短語描述保持內部空氣條件受控。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Earth-like atmosphere","meaning":"類似地球的大氣","examples":[{"en":"The ISS must maintain an Earth-like atmosphere.","zh":"國際太空站必須維持類似地球的大氣。"},{"en":"An Earth-like atmosphere is air with conditions similar to those humans breathe on Earth.","zh":"類似地球的大氣，是與人類在地球上呼吸的空氣條件相似的大氣。"},{"en":"A spacecraft needs an Earth-like atmosphere so astronauts can live without wearing spacesuits inside.","zh":"太空船需要類似地球的大氣，讓太空人在艙內不用穿太空衣也能生活。"},{"en":"Without an Earth-like atmosphere, pressure and oxygen levels would be unsafe.","zh":"沒有類似地球的大氣，氣壓和氧氣水平會不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes breathable air conditions similar to Earth’s.","zh":"這個短語描述類似地球的可呼吸空氣條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the most important element","meaning":"最重要的元素","examples":[{"en":"Atmospheric control is the most important element of life support.","zh":"大氣控制是生命維持系統中最重要的元素。"},{"en":"The most important element is the part that matters most in a system or situation.","zh":"最重要的元素，是系統或情況中最關鍵的部分。"},{"en":"In language learning, regular practice may be the most important element of progress.","zh":"在語言學習中，定期練習可能是進步最重要的元素。"},{"en":"If the most important element fails, the whole system may become unsafe or ineffective.","zh":"如果最重要的元素失效，整個系統可能變得不安全或無效。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the key part.","zh":"這個短語指出關鍵部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"present the greatest challenge","meaning":"帶來最大挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Atmospheric control has always presented the greatest challenge.","zh":"大氣控制一直帶來最大挑戰。"},{"en":"To present the greatest challenge means to be the most difficult problem to solve.","zh":"帶來最大挑戰，是指成為最難解決的問題。"},{"en":"For new teachers, managing a noisy class may present the greatest challenge.","zh":"對新老師而言，管理嘈雜班級可能帶來最大挑戰。"},{"en":"Spacecraft air control is difficult because astronauts depend on it every second.","zh":"太空船空氣控制很困難，因為太空人每一秒都依賴它。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the hardest part of a task.","zh":"這個短語突出任務中最困難的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"spacecraft design","meaning":"太空船設計","examples":[{"en":"Atmospheric control is a major challenge in spacecraft design.","zh":"大氣控制是太空船設計中的重大挑戰。"},{"en":"Spacecraft design is the planning and engineering of vehicles that travel in space.","zh":"太空船設計是規劃和工程設計能在太空中航行的載具。"},{"en":"Spacecraft design must consider air, power, heat, communication, and safety.","zh":"太空船設計必須考慮空氣、電力、熱量、通訊和安全。"},{"en":"Poor spacecraft design can endanger astronauts and damage equipment.","zh":"差劣太空船設計可能危及太空人並損壞設備。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to designing machines for space travel.","zh":"這個短語指為太空旅行而設計機器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pure-oxygen atmosphere","meaning":"純氧大氣","examples":[{"en":"Apollo 1 used a pure-oxygen atmosphere.","zh":"阿波羅1號使用純氧大氣。"},{"en":"A pure-oxygen atmosphere is an air environment made almost entirely of oxygen.","zh":"純氧大氣是幾乎完全由氧氣構成的空氣環境。"},{"en":"Pure oxygen can help breathing in some medical situations, but it can also increase fire risk.","zh":"純氧在某些醫療情況中可以幫助呼吸，但也會增加火災風險。"},{"en":"In Apollo 1, the pure-oxygen atmosphere made combustion much easier.","zh":"在阿波羅1號中，純氧大氣令燃燒更容易發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an atmosphere without the normal mixture of gases found on Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有地球正常混合氣體的大氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"tragic consequences","meaning":"悲劇性後果","examples":[{"en":"The use of pure oxygen had tragic consequences.","zh":"使用純氧造成悲劇性後果。"},{"en":"Tragic consequences are very sad and serious results, often involving death or suffering.","zh":"悲劇性後果是非常令人傷心和嚴重的結果，通常涉及死亡或痛苦。"},{"en":"Ignoring fire safety rules can have tragic consequences in a crowded building.","zh":"在擠迫建築物中忽視消防安全規則，可能造成悲劇性後果。"},{"en":"In the Apollo 1 case, the atmosphere choice helped create a deadly fire risk.","zh":"在阿波羅1號事件中，大氣選擇增加了致命火災風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes outcomes that are severe and heartbreaking.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重而令人心碎的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"allow a lower air pressure","meaning":"允許較低氣壓","examples":[{"en":"Pure oxygen allowed a lower air pressure.","zh":"純氧允許較低氣壓。"},{"en":"To allow a lower air pressure means to make it possible to use less pressure while still supporting breathing.","zh":"允許較低氣壓，是指使人在較低壓力下仍能呼吸成為可能。"},{"en":"Engineers may choose lower pressure to reduce stress on a sealed cabin.","zh":"工程師可能選擇較低氣壓，以減少密封艙承受的壓力。"},{"en":"Pure oxygen can support breathing at lower pressure, but it increases fire danger.","zh":"純氧可以在較低氣壓下支持呼吸，但會增加火災危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an engineering advantage with possible risk.","zh":"這個短語描述一項帶有風險的工程優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"from an engineering standpoint","meaning":"從工程角度來看","examples":[{"en":"A lower air pressure was better from an engineering standpoint.","zh":"從工程角度來看，較低氣壓較好。"},{"en":"From an engineering standpoint means when considered from the perspective of design, structure, or technical function.","zh":"從工程角度來看，是指從設計、結構或技術功能的角度考慮。"},{"en":"From an engineering standpoint, a lighter bridge may be cheaper to build.","zh":"從工程角度來看，較輕的橋樑可能較便宜建造。"},{"en":"A choice that seems good technically may still create safety or human problems.","zh":"技術上看似好的選擇，仍可能造成安全或人員問題。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a technical point of view.","zh":"這個短語引入技術觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"readily fuel combustion","meaning":"更容易助燃","examples":[{"en":"Pure oxygen more readily fuels combustion.","zh":"純氧更容易助燃。"},{"en":"To readily fuel combustion means to make burning happen more easily and intensely.","zh":"更容易助燃，是指令燃燒更容易和更猛烈地發生。"},{"en":"Dry paper can readily fuel combustion if it is near a flame.","zh":"乾紙如果接近火焰，可以很容易助燃。"},{"en":"A pure-oxygen atmosphere increases fire risk because flames can spread faster.","zh":"純氧大氣會增加火災風險，因為火焰可以更快蔓延。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making fire easier to start or continue.","zh":"這個短語描述令火更容易開始或持續燃燒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"random spark","meaning":"隨機火花","examples":[{"en":"A random spark started the fire.","zh":"一個隨機火花引發了火災。"},{"en":"A random spark is a sudden tiny flash of fire or electricity that occurs unexpectedly.","zh":"隨機火花是意外出現的細小火光或電火花。"},{"en":"A loose wire can create a random spark inside an old machine.","zh":"鬆脫電線可能在舊機器內產生隨機火花。"},{"en":"In an oxygen-rich environment, even a small spark can lead to a serious fire.","zh":"在富氧環境中，即使小火花也可以引發嚴重火災。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unexpected ignition source.","zh":"這個短語描述意外點火來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"race through","meaning":"迅速蔓延穿過","examples":[{"en":"The fire raced through the Apollo 1 craft.","zh":"火焰迅速蔓延穿過阿波羅1號太空船。"},{"en":"To race through a place means to move through it extremely quickly.","zh":"迅速穿過某處，是指以極快速度通過或蔓延其中。"},{"en":"News can race through a school when students share it online.","zh":"當學生在網上分享消息，消息可以迅速傳遍學校。"},{"en":"Fire can race through a small enclosed space if conditions help it spread.","zh":"如果條件有助火勢蔓延，火可以迅速穿過狹小封閉空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very rapid movement or spreading.","zh":"這個短語描述非常快速的移動或蔓延。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"crew members","meaning":"機組人員","examples":[{"en":"The fire killed all three crew members.","zh":"火災殺死了全部三名機組人員。"},{"en":"Crew members are the people who work together on a ship, aircraft, or spacecraft.","zh":"機組人員是在船、飛機或太空船上一起工作的人。"},{"en":"Crew members on a flight must check safety equipment before passengers board.","zh":"航班上的機組人員必須在乘客登機前檢查安全設備。"},{"en":"In dangerous missions, crew members depend on equipment and one another to survive.","zh":"在危險任務中，機組人員依靠設備和彼此生存。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to individuals in an operating team.","zh":"這個短語指操作團隊中的個別成員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the experiment was never repeated","meaning":"該實驗從未再重複","examples":[{"en":"The pure-oxygen experiment was never repeated.","zh":"純氧實驗從未再重複。"},{"en":"The experiment was never repeated means the same test or design choice was not used again.","zh":"該實驗從未再重複，是指同一測試或設計選擇沒有再被使用。"},{"en":"After a dangerous classroom activity causes an injury, the experiment may never be repeated.","zh":"如果危險課堂活動造成受傷，該實驗可能從未再重複。"},{"en":"A serious accident can make engineers abandon a risky method permanently.","zh":"嚴重事故可以令工程師永久放棄高風險方法。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a failure changed future practice.","zh":"這個短語顯示失敗改變了未來做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"main source of oxygen","meaning":"主要氧氣來源","examples":[{"en":"The Elektron system is the ISS’s main source of oxygen.","zh":"Elektron 系統是國際太空站的主要氧氣來源。"},{"en":"The main source of oxygen is the primary system or supply that provides breathable oxygen.","zh":"主要氧氣來源是提供可呼吸氧氣的主要系統或供應。"},{"en":"In a hospital, oxygen tanks may be a main source of oxygen for some patients.","zh":"在醫院中，氧氣瓶可能是某些病人的主要氧氣來源。"},{"en":"If the main source of oxygen fails in space, backup systems become essential.","zh":"如果太空中的主要氧氣來源失效，後備系統就變得必要。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where most oxygen comes from.","zh":"這個短語指出大部分氧氣來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"electric current","meaning":"電流","examples":[{"en":"The system uses an electric current to break apart water molecules.","zh":"這個系統使用電流分解水分子。"},{"en":"An electric current is the flow of electricity through a material or device.","zh":"電流是電力在材料或裝置中流動。"},{"en":"A phone charger sends an electric current into a battery.","zh":"手機充電器把電流送入電池。"},{"en":"In the Elektron system, electric current helps split water into oxygen and hydrogen.","zh":"在 Elektron 系統中，電流幫助把水分解成氧氣和氫氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving electricity used to power a process.","zh":"這個短語描述用來推動過程的流動電力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"break apart water molecules","meaning":"分解水分子","examples":[{"en":"The Elektron system breaks apart water molecules.","zh":"Elektron 系統分解水分子。"},{"en":"To break apart water molecules means to split water into its chemical parts.","zh":"分解水分子，是指把水分裂成其化學組成部分。"},{"en":"In a science demonstration, electricity can break apart water molecules into hydrogen and oxygen.","zh":"在科學示範中，電力可以把水分子分解成氫氣和氧氣。"},{"en":"Breaking apart water molecules allows the ISS to produce oxygen for astronauts.","zh":"分解水分子讓國際太空站為太空人製造氧氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a chemical process using water.","zh":"這個短語描述使用水的化學過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"water molecules","meaning":"水分子","examples":[{"en":"Water molecules are broken apart to produce oxygen.","zh":"水分子被分解以產生氧氣。"},{"en":"Water molecules are the tiny chemical units that make up water.","zh":"水分子是構成水的微小化學單位。"},{"en":"Each water molecule contains hydrogen and oxygen atoms.","zh":"每個水分子含有氫原子和氧原子。"},{"en":"If water molecules are split, oxygen can be collected for breathing.","zh":"如果水分子被分解，氧氣可以被收集作呼吸用途。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the basic chemical particles of water.","zh":"這個短語指水的基本化學粒子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be vented into","meaning":"被排入……","examples":[{"en":"The oxygen is vented into the pressurised modules.","zh":"氧氣被排入加壓艙段。"},{"en":"To be vented into a place means to be released or directed into it through a system.","zh":"被排入某處，是指透過系統被釋放或引導進入該處。"},{"en":"Cool air may be vented into a classroom through ceiling ducts.","zh":"冷空氣可能透過天花管道被排入課室。"},{"en":"Oxygen must be vented into crew areas so astronauts can breathe safely.","zh":"氧氣必須被排入機組區域，讓太空人安全呼吸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled release of gas into a space.","zh":"這個短語描述氣體被控制地釋放進某空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the oxygen produced","meaning":"產生的氧氣","examples":[{"en":"The oxygen produced is released into the crew areas.","zh":"產生的氧氣被釋放到機組人員區域。"},{"en":"The oxygen produced means the oxygen created by a process or machine.","zh":"產生的氧氣，是由某過程或機器製造出來的氧氣。"},{"en":"The oxygen produced by a medical machine may help a patient breathe.","zh":"醫療機器產生的氧氣可能幫助病人呼吸。"},{"en":"On the ISS, the oxygen produced from water supports daily life for the crew.","zh":"在國際太空站上，由水產生的氧氣支持機組人員日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to oxygen after it has been generated.","zh":"這個短語指已被製造出的氧氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"by-product","meaning":"副產品","examples":[{"en":"Hydrogen is the other by-product of the process.","zh":"氫氣是該過程的另一種副產品。"},{"en":"A by-product is something produced as a secondary result of a process.","zh":"副產品是某過程中作為次要結果產生的東西。"},{"en":"Heat can be a by-product of a machine running for a long time.","zh":"機器長時間運作時，熱量可以是副產品。"},{"en":"When water is split for oxygen, hydrogen is also produced as a by-product.","zh":"當水被分解以製造氧氣，氫氣也會作為副產品產生。"},{"en":"This word describes an additional product, not the main purpose.","zh":"這個詞描述額外產物，而不是主要目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be vented into space","meaning":"被排放到太空","examples":[{"en":"Hydrogen is vented into space.","zh":"氫氣被排放到太空。"},{"en":"To be vented into space means to be released outside the spacecraft into outer space.","zh":"被排放到太空，是指被釋放到太空船外的外太空中。"},{"en":"Waste gas from a spacecraft may be vented into space if it is no longer useful.","zh":"如果太空船中的廢氣不再有用，可能會被排放到太空。"},{"en":"Hydrogen is vented away because it is not needed in the crew’s breathing atmosphere.","zh":"氫氣被排走，因為機組人員的呼吸大氣不需要它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes releasing gas from a spacecraft into space.","zh":"這個短語描述從太空船把氣體釋放到太空。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"generate enough oxygen","meaning":"產生足夠氧氣","examples":[{"en":"The system generates enough oxygen for a six-member crew.","zh":"這個系統為六人機組產生足夠氧氣。"},{"en":"To generate enough oxygen means to produce a sufficient amount of oxygen.","zh":"產生足夠氧氣，是指製造出足夠數量的氧氣。"},{"en":"A hospital oxygen system must generate enough oxygen for patients who need breathing support.","zh":"醫院氧氣系統必須為需要呼吸支援的病人產生足夠氧氣。"},{"en":"If the ISS system cannot generate enough oxygen, astronauts must use backup supplies.","zh":"如果國際太空站系統不能產生足夠氧氣，太空人必須使用後備供應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes producing the amount needed for survival.","zh":"這個短語描述產生生存所需的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"prove unreliable","meaning":"證明不可靠","examples":[{"en":"The Elektron system has proven unreliable.","zh":"Elektron 系統已證明不可靠。"},{"en":"To prove unreliable means to show through experience that something cannot always be depended on.","zh":"證明不可靠，是指經驗顯示某物不能總是被依賴。"},{"en":"An old lift may prove unreliable if it stops working every week.","zh":"如果舊升降機每星期都停用，它可能證明不可靠。"},{"en":"If a life-support system proves unreliable, backup systems become very important.","zh":"如果生命維持系統證明不可靠，後備系統就變得非常重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that fails too often to be fully trusted.","zh":"這個短語描述某物故障太頻繁，不能完全信任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"emergency backups","meaning":"緊急後備系統","examples":[{"en":"The crew regularly need emergency backups.","zh":"機組人員經常需要緊急後備系統。"},{"en":"Emergency backups are extra systems or supplies used when the main system fails.","zh":"緊急後備系統，是在主要系統失效時使用的額外系統或供應。"},{"en":"A school may keep emergency backup lights in case the power goes out.","zh":"學校可能備有緊急後備燈，以防停電。"},{"en":"On the ISS, emergency backups protect astronauts if the oxygen system stops working.","zh":"在國際太空站上，如果氧氣系統停止運作，緊急後備系統會保護太空人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes safety support for serious failures.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重故障時的安全支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"bottled oxygen","meaning":"樽裝氧氣","examples":[{"en":"Bottled oxygen is one emergency backup.","zh":"樽裝氧氣是一種緊急後備。"},{"en":"Bottled oxygen is oxygen stored under pressure in tanks or bottles.","zh":"樽裝氧氣是儲存在氧氣樽或氣瓶中的加壓氧氣。"},{"en":"Ambulances may carry bottled oxygen for patients who have trouble breathing.","zh":"救護車可能攜帶樽裝氧氣，給呼吸困難的病人使用。"},{"en":"Bottled oxygen can serve as a backup when a regular oxygen system fails.","zh":"當常規氧氣系統失效時，樽裝氧氣可以作為後備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stored oxygen ready for use.","zh":"這個短語描述可隨時使用的儲存氧氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be ferried up by","meaning":"由……運送上去","examples":[{"en":"Bottled oxygen is ferried up by unmanned supply craft.","zh":"樽裝氧氣由無人補給太空船運送上去。"},{"en":"To be ferried up by something means to be transported upward or to space by that vehicle.","zh":"由某物運送上去，是指由該交通工具向上或到太空運送。"},{"en":"Supplies may be ferried up a mountain by cable car after heavy snow blocks roads.","zh":"暴雪封路後，補給品可能由纜車運送上山。"},{"en":"Oxygen must be ferried up to the ISS because the station cannot get supplies locally.","zh":"氧氣必須被運送上國際太空站，因為太空站不能在當地取得補給。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transport to a higher or more remote place.","zh":"這個短語描述運送到較高或較偏遠地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"unmanned supply craft","meaning":"無人補給太空船","examples":[{"en":"Unmanned supply craft deliver oxygen to the ISS.","zh":"無人補給太空船把氧氣運送到國際太空站。"},{"en":"An unmanned supply craft is a spacecraft that carries supplies without people on board.","zh":"無人補給太空船是沒有載人、負責運送補給品的太空船。"},{"en":"An unmanned delivery vehicle can bring food to a remote research station.","zh":"無人運送車可以把食物送到偏遠研究站。"},{"en":"Unmanned supply craft reduce risk because no crew must travel on the cargo vehicle.","zh":"無人補給太空船降低風險，因為貨運載具上不需要機組人員。"},{"en":"This phrase describes robotic cargo spacecraft.","zh":"這個短語描述機械化貨運太空船。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"solid-fuel oxygen generator","meaning":"固體燃料氧氣產生器","examples":[{"en":"The ISS has a solid-fuel oxygen generator as a backup.","zh":"國際太空站有固體燃料氧氣產生器作為後備。"},{"en":"A solid-fuel oxygen generator is a device that uses solid chemicals to produce oxygen.","zh":"固體燃料氧氣產生器，是使用固體化學物來產生氧氣的裝置。"},{"en":"Emergency oxygen generators on aircraft may provide air when cabin pressure fails.","zh":"飛機上的緊急氧氣產生器可能在客艙失壓時提供空氣。"},{"en":"On the ISS, a solid-fuel generator can supply oxygen if the main system breaks down.","zh":"在國際太空站上，如果主系統故障，固體燃料產生器可以供應氧氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a backup device for producing breathable oxygen.","zh":"這個短語描述產生可呼吸氧氣的後備裝置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"chemical one","meaning":"化學氧氣產生器","examples":[{"en":"The ISS also has a chemical oxygen generator.","zh":"國際太空站也有一個化學氧氣產生器。"},{"en":"A chemical one means a generator or system that works through a chemical reaction.","zh":"化學氧氣產生器，是透過化學反應運作的產生器或系統。"},{"en":"A chemical cleaner removes stains through chemical action rather than scrubbing alone.","zh":"化學清潔劑透過化學作用去除污漬，而不只是靠刷洗。"},{"en":"A chemical oxygen generator can produce oxygen when chemicals react in a controlled way.","zh":"化學氧氣產生器可以在化學物受控反應時產生氧氣。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a chemical version of a system already discussed.","zh":"這個短語指前文已討論系統的化學版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"respectively","meaning":"分別地","examples":[{"en":"The backups are located in the Zvezda and Zarya Modules, respectively.","zh":"這些後備系統分別位於 Zvezda 和 Zarya 艙段。"},{"en":"Respectively means in the same order as the items just mentioned.","zh":"respectively 是指按照剛提到項目的相同次序分別對應。"},{"en":"Tom and Mary scored 80 and 90 marks, respectively, meaning Tom scored 80 and Mary scored 90.","zh":"Tom 和 Mary 分別取得 80 和 90 分，意思是 Tom 得 80 分，Mary 得 90 分。"},{"en":"This word prevents confusion when matching two lists of information.","zh":"這個詞在配對兩組資料時避免混亂。"},{"en":"It is useful when each item corresponds to another item in order.","zh":"當每個項目按次序對應另一項目時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"output is circulated","meaning":"輸出物被循環輸送","examples":[{"en":"The oxygen output is circulated with strong fans.","zh":"氧氣輸出物由強力風扇循環輸送。"},{"en":"Output is circulated means the produced material is moved around through a system.","zh":"輸出物被循環輸送，是指產生出的物質透過系統被移動到各處。"},{"en":"Warm air from a heater is circulated around a room by a fan.","zh":"暖爐產生的暖空氣由風扇在房間中循環輸送。"},{"en":"Oxygen must be circulated so it does not stay in one area while other areas become unsafe.","zh":"氧氣必須被循環輸送，才不會停留在某一區而其他區域變得不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distributing something after it is produced.","zh":"這個短語描述某物產生後被分配到各處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"strong and noisy fans","meaning":"強力而嘈吵的風扇","examples":[{"en":"The output is circulated with strong and noisy fans.","zh":"輸出物由強力而嘈吵的風扇循環輸送。"},{"en":"Strong and noisy fans are powerful fans that move air forcefully but make a lot of sound.","zh":"強力而嘈吵的風扇，是能大力移動空氣但發出很多聲音的風扇。"},{"en":"A restaurant kitchen may use strong and noisy fans to remove smoke and heat.","zh":"餐廳廚房可能使用強力而嘈吵的風扇去除煙和熱。"},{"en":"On the ISS, fans must be strong because air does not naturally circulate well in weightlessness.","zh":"在國際太空站上，風扇必須強力，因為失重環境中空氣不會自然良好循環。"},{"en":"This phrase describes powerful air-moving equipment that may be uncomfortable to hear.","zh":"這個短語描述強力移動空氣但聲音可能令人不適的設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"without which","meaning":"沒有它的話","examples":[{"en":"The astronauts need fans, without which the air would stagnate.","zh":"太空人需要風扇，沒有它的話，空氣會停滯不流通。"},{"en":"Without which means without that thing, the result just mentioned would not be possible or would become worse.","zh":"without which 是指沒有那樣東西，剛提到的結果就不可能或會變差。"},{"en":"Students need clear instructions, without which they may complete the task incorrectly.","zh":"學生需要清楚指示，沒有它的話，他們可能錯誤完成任務。"},{"en":"Fans are necessary in the ISS because without them, exhaled air may stay around astronauts.","zh":"在國際太空站中，風扇是必要的，因為沒有風扇，呼出的空氣可能停留在太空人周圍。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a necessary tool with the problem it prevents.","zh":"這個短語把必要工具與它防止的問題連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"immobile astronauts","meaning":"靜止不動的太空人","examples":[{"en":"Air around immobile astronauts would stagnate without fans.","zh":"沒有風扇，靜止不動的太空人周圍空氣會停滯。"},{"en":"Immobile astronauts are astronauts who are not moving or are staying still.","zh":"靜止不動的太空人，是沒有移動或保持不動的太空人。"},{"en":"A patient lying immobile in bed may need nurses to check breathing and comfort.","zh":"躺在床上靜止不動的病人可能需要護士檢查呼吸和舒適程度。"},{"en":"In weightlessness, air around an immobile person may not move away naturally.","zh":"在失重環境中，靜止不動的人周圍的空氣可能不會自然散開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes astronauts who are physically still.","zh":"這個短語描述身體保持靜止的太空人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stagnate","meaning":"停滯不流通","examples":[{"en":"The air around an astronaut could stagnate.","zh":"太空人周圍的空氣可能停滯不流通。"},{"en":"To stagnate means to stop moving or developing.","zh":"停滯，是指停止流動或發展。"},{"en":"Water in a blocked drain can stagnate and begin to smell bad.","zh":"堵塞去水位中的水可能停滯並開始發臭。"},{"en":"If air stagnates around an astronaut, fresh oxygen may not reach them properly.","zh":"如果空氣在太空人周圍停滯，新鮮氧氣可能無法正常到達。"},{"en":"This word describes harmful stillness or lack of movement.","zh":"這個詞描述有害的靜止或缺乏流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a bubble of","meaning":"一團……","examples":[{"en":"A bubble of carbon dioxide could form around an astronaut.","zh":"一團二氧化碳可能在太空人周圍形成。"},{"en":"A bubble of something is a small surrounding pocket or area of that substance.","zh":"一團某物，是該物質形成的小型包圍區域或局部空間。"},{"en":"A bubble of warm air may form near a heater in a cold room.","zh":"在寒冷房間中，暖爐附近可能形成一團暖空氣。"},{"en":"In space, a bubble of exhaled carbon dioxide may stay near a person without air circulation.","zh":"在太空中，沒有空氣循環時，一團呼出的二氧化碳可能停留在人附近。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a local pocket of gas or liquid.","zh":"這個短語描述局部的一團氣體或液體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"exhaled carbon dioxide","meaning":"呼出的二氧化碳","examples":[{"en":"Astronauts may be surrounded by their own exhaled carbon dioxide.","zh":"太空人可能被自己呼出的二氧化碳包圍。"},{"en":"Exhaled carbon dioxide is the carbon dioxide people breathe out.","zh":"呼出的二氧化碳，是人呼氣時排出的二氧化碳。"},{"en":"In a crowded room with poor ventilation, exhaled carbon dioxide can build up.","zh":"在通風差的擠迫房間中，呼出的二氧化碳可以積聚。"},{"en":"If exhaled carbon dioxide stays near the face, breathing can become uncomfortable or unsafe.","zh":"如果呼出的二氧化碳停留在臉部附近，呼吸可能變得不舒服或不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes waste gas from breathing.","zh":"這個短語描述呼吸產生的廢氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"oxygen-deprived","meaning":"缺氧的","examples":[{"en":"Astronauts could become oxygen-deprived without air circulation.","zh":"沒有空氣循環，太空人可能變得缺氧。"},{"en":"Oxygen-deprived means lacking enough oxygen to breathe or function properly.","zh":"缺氧的，是指缺乏足夠氧氣去呼吸或正常運作。"},{"en":"A person trapped in a smoke-filled room may become oxygen-deprived.","zh":"被困在充滿煙霧房間的人可能變得缺氧。"},{"en":"Without fans, astronauts might breathe too much carbon dioxide and too little oxygen.","zh":"沒有風扇，太空人可能吸入太多二氧化碳和太少氧氣。"},{"en":"This word describes a dangerous shortage of oxygen.","zh":"這個詞描述危險的氧氣不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"struggle to breathe","meaning":"呼吸困難","examples":[{"en":"Without fans, astronauts could struggle to breathe.","zh":"沒有風扇，太空人可能呼吸困難。"},{"en":"To struggle to breathe means to have difficulty getting enough air.","zh":"呼吸困難，是指難以吸入足夠空氣。"},{"en":"A person with asthma may struggle to breathe during a serious attack.","zh":"哮喘患者在嚴重發作時可能呼吸困難。"},{"en":"If carbon dioxide builds up around the face, a person may struggle to breathe.","zh":"如果二氧化碳在臉部周圍積聚，人可能會呼吸困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious breathing difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重呼吸問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"indicate that","meaning":"顯示；表明","examples":[{"en":"The oxygen system indicates that life on the ISS is difficult.","zh":"氧氣系統顯示國際太空站上的生活很困難。"},{"en":"To indicate that means to show, suggest, or be a sign that something is true.","zh":"顯示或表明某事，是指展示、暗示或作為某事真實的跡象。"},{"en":"Dark clouds may indicate that rain is coming soon.","zh":"烏雲可能顯示快要下雨。"},{"en":"The need for complex oxygen systems indicates that space life is not simple or comfortable.","zh":"需要複雜氧氣系統，顯示太空生活並不簡單或舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces evidence or a sign.","zh":"這個短語引入證據或跡象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"no pleasure cruise","meaning":"並非輕鬆愉快的旅程","examples":[{"en":"Life on the ISS is no pleasure cruise.","zh":"國際太空站上的生活並非輕鬆愉快的旅程。"},{"en":"No pleasure cruise means not an easy, relaxing, or enjoyable experience.","zh":"並非輕鬆愉快的旅程，是指不是容易、放鬆或享受的經歷。"},{"en":"Preparing for final exams is no pleasure cruise if students have many subjects to revise.","zh":"如果學生有很多科要溫習，準備期末考並非輕鬆愉快的旅程。"},{"en":"The ISS may be exciting, but cramped space, strict rules, and danger make life hard.","zh":"國際太空站可能令人興奮，但狹窄空間、嚴格規則和危險令生活艱難。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that something is difficult, not comfortable.","zh":"這個短語強調某事困難，而不是舒適。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"close and cramped quarters","meaning":"狹小擠迫的居住空間","examples":[{"en":"The crew live in close and cramped quarters.","zh":"機組人員住在狹小擠迫的居住空間中。"},{"en":"Close and cramped quarters are small living spaces where people have little room to move.","zh":"狹小擠迫的居住空間，是人們幾乎沒有活動空間的小型生活區。"},{"en":"Six students sharing a tiny study room may feel they are in cramped quarters.","zh":"六名學生共用一間細小自修室，可能感到身處擠迫空間。"},{"en":"Cramped living conditions can increase stress and reduce privacy.","zh":"擠迫生活環境可以增加壓力並減少私隱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uncomfortable lack of space.","zh":"這個短語描述令人不舒服的空間不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"awkward and uncomfortable facilities","meaning":"笨拙而不舒適的設施","examples":[{"en":"The ISS has awkward and uncomfortable facilities.","zh":"國際太空站有笨拙而不舒適的設施。"},{"en":"Awkward and uncomfortable facilities are equipment or spaces that are difficult or unpleasant to use.","zh":"笨拙而不舒適的設施，是難以使用或使用時不愉快的設備或空間。"},{"en":"A badly designed toilet in a small café may be an awkward and uncomfortable facility.","zh":"小咖啡店中設計差的洗手間可能是笨拙而不舒適的設施。"},{"en":"In space, basic tasks such as washing and sleeping can become awkward because of weightlessness.","zh":"在太空中，洗漱和睡覺等基本任務會因失重而變得笨拙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes facilities that make daily life inconvenient.","zh":"這個短語描述令日常生活不方便的設施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"strict protocols","meaning":"嚴格規程","examples":[{"en":"Crew members follow strict eating, hygiene and exercise protocols.","zh":"機組人員遵守嚴格的飲食、衞生和運動規程。"},{"en":"Strict protocols are detailed rules that must be followed carefully.","zh":"嚴格規程是必須仔細遵守的詳細規則。"},{"en":"A hospital has strict protocols for washing hands before treating patients.","zh":"醫院有嚴格規程，要求治療病人前洗手。"},{"en":"In space, strict protocols reduce risk and keep crew members healthy.","zh":"在太空中，嚴格規程減少風險並保持機組人員健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes firm procedures rather than casual advice.","zh":"這個短語描述堅定程序，而不是隨意建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"hygiene protocols","meaning":"衞生規程","examples":[{"en":"Hygiene protocols are part of daily life on the ISS.","zh":"衞生規程是國際太空站日常生活的一部分。"},{"en":"Hygiene protocols are rules for keeping people, equipment, and living areas clean.","zh":"衞生規程是保持人、設備和生活區潔淨的規則。"},{"en":"Schools may use hygiene protocols such as handwashing before lunch.","zh":"學校可能使用午餐前洗手等衞生規程。"},{"en":"In a closed spacecraft, hygiene protocols help prevent illness from spreading.","zh":"在封閉太空船中，衞生規程有助防止疾病傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cleanliness rules and procedures.","zh":"這個短語描述清潔規則和程序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"two-hour-per-day exercise protocols","meaning":"每日兩小時的運動規程","examples":[{"en":"Astronauts follow two-hour-per-day exercise protocols.","zh":"太空人遵守每日兩小時的運動規程。"},{"en":"Two-hour-per-day exercise protocols are rules requiring exercise for two hours each day.","zh":"每日兩小時的運動規程，是要求每天運動兩小時的規則。"},{"en":"A sports team may have daily training protocols to maintain fitness.","zh":"運動隊可能有每日訓練規程，以保持體能。"},{"en":"Astronauts need long exercise routines because weightlessness weakens muscles and bones.","zh":"太空人需要長時間運動，因為失重會削弱肌肉和骨骼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fixed daily exercise requirement.","zh":"這個短語描述固定每日運動要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"dizziness and fatigue","meaning":"頭暈和疲勞","examples":[{"en":"Weightlessness can cause dizziness and fatigue.","zh":"失重可以造成頭暈和疲勞。"},{"en":"Dizziness and fatigue mean feeling light-headed and extremely tired.","zh":"頭暈和疲勞，是感到暈眩和非常疲倦。"},{"en":"A student may feel dizziness and fatigue after skipping breakfast and standing for too long.","zh":"學生不吃早餐又站太久後，可能感到頭暈和疲勞。"},{"en":"In space, the body must adapt to weightlessness, which can make astronauts feel unwell.","zh":"在太空中，身體必須適應失重，這可能令太空人感到不適。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical discomfort and tiredness.","zh":"這個短語描述身體不適和疲倦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be induced in","meaning":"在……中引起","examples":[{"en":"Dizziness and fatigue are induced in a weightless environment.","zh":"頭暈和疲勞在失重環境中被引起。"},{"en":"To be induced in a situation means to be caused or brought about by that situation.","zh":"在某情況中被引起，是指由該情況造成或帶來。"},{"en":"Stress may be induced in students during a very strict oral exam.","zh":"在非常嚴格的口試中，學生可能產生壓力。"},{"en":"Weightlessness can induce physical symptoms because the body is not used to floating.","zh":"失重可以引起身體症狀，因為身體不習慣漂浮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something being caused by a particular condition.","zh":"這個短語描述某事由特定條件造成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"weightless environment","meaning":"失重環境","examples":[{"en":"The ISS is a weightless environment.","zh":"國際太空站是一個失重環境。"},{"en":"A weightless environment is a place where people and objects seem to have no weight.","zh":"失重環境是人和物件看似沒有重量的地方。"},{"en":"Astronauts float in a weightless environment instead of standing on the floor.","zh":"太空人在失重環境中漂浮，而不是站在地板上。"},{"en":"Weightlessness affects eating, sleeping, exercise, and movement.","zh":"失重會影響進食、睡眠、運動和移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical conditions inside an orbiting spacecraft.","zh":"這個短語描述軌道太空船內的物理條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"long workday","meaning":"漫長工作日","examples":[{"en":"Astronauts have a long workday devoted to maintenance and experiments.","zh":"太空人有漫長工作日，專門用於維修保養和實驗。"},{"en":"A long workday is a day with many hours of work and few breaks.","zh":"漫長工作日，是工時很長、休息很少的一天。"},{"en":"A nurse may have a long workday during a busy hospital shift.","zh":"護士在繁忙醫院輪班中可能有漫長工作日。"},{"en":"Long workdays can cause tiredness, especially when the work is technical and important.","zh":"漫長工作日可以造成疲倦，尤其當工作技術性強而且重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an extended period of daily work.","zh":"這個短語描述延長的每日工作時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be devoted to","meaning":"投放於；專門用於","examples":[{"en":"The crew’s workday is devoted to maintenance and scientific experiments.","zh":"機組人員的工作日專門用於維修保養和科學實驗。"},{"en":"To be devoted to something means to be used mainly for that purpose.","zh":"專門用於某事，是指主要為該目的而使用。"},{"en":"Friday afternoon may be devoted to revision before an exam.","zh":"星期五下午可能專門用於考試前溫習。"},{"en":"If a day is devoted to repairs, there may be little time left for rest.","zh":"如果一天專門用於維修，剩下休息時間可能很少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how time or effort is mainly used.","zh":"這個短語描述時間或努力主要如何被使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"maintenance","meaning":"維修保養","examples":[{"en":"Much of the crew’s time is spent on maintenance.","zh":"機組人員很多時間花在維修保養上。"},{"en":"Maintenance is the work needed to keep machines, buildings, or systems in good condition.","zh":"維修保養是保持機器、建築物或系統良好狀態所需的工作。"},{"en":"A school needs regular maintenance to repair lights, air conditioners, and desks.","zh":"學校需要定期維修保養，以修理燈、冷氣和桌子。"},{"en":"Without maintenance, small problems can become dangerous failures.","zh":"沒有維修保養，小問題可能變成危險故障。"},{"en":"This word describes repair and care that keeps something working.","zh":"這個詞描述讓某物保持運作的修理和照顧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"scientific experiments","meaning":"科學實驗","examples":[{"en":"The crew conduct scientific experiments on the ISS.","zh":"機組人員在國際太空站上進行科學實驗。"},{"en":"Scientific experiments are tests designed to answer research questions using evidence.","zh":"科學實驗是用證據回答研究問題的測試。"},{"en":"Students may conduct scientific experiments to see which soil helps plants grow best.","zh":"學生可能進行科學實驗，看看哪種泥土最有利植物生長。"},{"en":"Experiments on the ISS can study effects that are difficult to observe on Earth.","zh":"國際太空站上的實驗可以研究在地球上難以觀察的效應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised research tests.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的研究測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"human isolation","meaning":"與人隔絕","examples":[{"en":"Human isolation can make life on the ISS stressful.","zh":"與人隔絕可以令國際太空站上的生活有壓力。"},{"en":"Human isolation means being separated from normal contact with other people.","zh":"與人隔絕，是指與正常人際接觸分離。"},{"en":"A student studying alone for weeks may feel human isolation if they rarely meet friends.","zh":"學生如果數星期獨自溫習且很少見朋友，可能感到與人隔絕。"},{"en":"Isolation can increase stress because people lack ordinary social comfort and support.","zh":"隔絕會增加壓力，因為人缺少普通社交安慰和支持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional and social separation.","zh":"這個短語描述情感和社交上的分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"strain relationships","meaning":"令關係緊張","examples":[{"en":"Difficult conditions can strain relationships.","zh":"困難條件可以令關係緊張。"},{"en":"To strain relationships means to put pressure on relationships and make them tense.","zh":"令關係緊張，是指對關係施加壓力，使其變得緊張。"},{"en":"Sharing a small flat can strain relationships if people have no privacy.","zh":"如果人們沒有私隱，共住細小單位可能令關係緊張。"},{"en":"Stress, tiredness, and limited space can make people argue more easily.","zh":"壓力、疲倦和有限空間會令人更容易爭吵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damage or pressure on personal connections.","zh":"這個短語描述對人際關係的傷害或壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"aggravate tensions","meaning":"加劇緊張","examples":[{"en":"Isolation can aggravate tensions among crew members.","zh":"隔絕可以加劇機組人員之間的緊張。"},{"en":"To aggravate tensions means to make existing stress or conflict worse.","zh":"加劇緊張，是指令已有壓力或衝突變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"A noisy neighbour can aggravate tensions in a crowded apartment building.","zh":"嘈吵鄰居可以加劇擠迫公寓大樓中的緊張。"},{"en":"If people are already tired, isolation may make small disagreements feel bigger.","zh":"如果人們已經疲倦，隔絕可能令小分歧感覺更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes worsening a tense situation.","zh":"這個短語描述令緊張情況惡化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"direct physical risk","meaning":"直接身體風險","examples":[{"en":"Solar radiation creates a direct physical risk.","zh":"太陽輻射造成直接身體風險。"},{"en":"A direct physical risk is an immediate danger to the body.","zh":"直接身體風險，是對身體的即時危險。"},{"en":"Broken glass on a playground is a direct physical risk to children.","zh":"操場上的碎玻璃對兒童是直接身體風險。"},{"en":"Solar radiation can harm astronauts because they are less protected than people on Earth.","zh":"太陽輻射可能傷害太空人，因為他們比地球上的人較少受到保護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a bodily danger, not just stress or discomfort.","zh":"這個短語描述身體危險，而不只是壓力或不適。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"solar radiation","meaning":"太陽輻射","examples":[{"en":"Astronauts face physical risk from solar radiation.","zh":"太空人面對來自太陽輻射的身體風險。"},{"en":"Solar radiation is energy from the sun that can include harmful particles and rays.","zh":"太陽輻射是來自太陽的能量，可能包括有害粒子和射線。"},{"en":"Sunscreen protects skin from some solar radiation during outdoor activities.","zh":"防曬霜在戶外活動時保護皮膚免受部分太陽輻射。"},{"en":"In space, solar radiation is more dangerous because astronauts are outside Earth’s protective atmosphere.","zh":"在太空中，太陽輻射更危險，因為太空人在地球保護大氣之外。"},{"en":"This phrase describes potentially harmful energy from the sun.","zh":"這個短語描述來自太陽、可能有害的能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"periodic flares","meaning":"週期性耀斑","examples":[{"en":"Periodic flares erupt from the sun’s surface.","zh":"週期性耀斑從太陽表面爆發。"},{"en":"Periodic flares are bursts of energy that happen from time to time.","zh":"週期性耀斑是時不時發生的能量爆發。"},{"en":"A warning system may check for periodic power surges in a building.","zh":"警報系統可能檢查建築物中的週期性電力突增。"},{"en":"Solar flares can increase radiation danger for astronauts in space.","zh":"太陽耀斑可以增加太空中太空人的輻射危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated bursts that occur at intervals.","zh":"這個短語描述間歇出現的反覆爆發。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"erupt from","meaning":"從……爆發","examples":[{"en":"Solar flares erupt from the sun’s surface.","zh":"太陽耀斑從太陽表面爆發。"},{"en":"To erupt from something means to burst out suddenly and forcefully from it.","zh":"從某物爆發，是指突然且猛烈地從中噴出或爆出。"},{"en":"Steam may erupt from a kettle if the lid is closed too tightly.","zh":"如果壺蓋蓋得太緊，蒸氣可能從水壺爆出。"},{"en":"Solar flares erupt when energy is suddenly released from the sun.","zh":"當能量突然從太陽釋放，太陽耀斑便會爆發。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sudden powerful burst outward.","zh":"這個短語描述突然猛烈向外爆出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the sun’s surface","meaning":"太陽表面","examples":[{"en":"Solar flares erupt from the sun’s surface.","zh":"太陽耀斑從太陽表面爆發。"},{"en":"The sun’s surface is the visible outer layer of the sun.","zh":"太陽表面是太陽可見的外層。"},{"en":"Scientists study the sun’s surface to understand sunspots and solar storms.","zh":"科學家研究太陽表面，以理解太陽黑子和太陽風暴。"},{"en":"Activity on the sun’s surface can affect satellites, astronauts, and communications.","zh":"太陽表面的活動可以影響衛星、太空人和通訊。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the outer visible part of the sun.","zh":"這個短語指太陽外部可見部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"returning crew member","meaning":"返航機組成員","examples":[{"en":"A returning crew member described the ISS as interesting but uncomfortable.","zh":"一名返航機組成員形容國際太空站有趣但不舒適。"},{"en":"A returning crew member is a person coming back after serving on a spacecraft or mission.","zh":"返航機組成員，是完成太空船或任務服務後返回的人。"},{"en":"A returning crew member from a ship may describe the voyage to new trainees.","zh":"從船上返航的機組成員可能向新學員描述航程。"},{"en":"Returning crew members can explain real living conditions because they experienced them directly.","zh":"返航機組成員能解釋真實生活條件，因為他們親身經歷過。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone who has come back from a mission.","zh":"這個短語描述從任務回來的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"an interesting place for a visit","meaning":"值得一訪的有趣地方","examples":[{"en":"The ISS is an interesting place for a visit.","zh":"國際太空站是值得一訪的有趣地方。"},{"en":"An interesting place for a visit is somewhere worth seeing for a short time.","zh":"值得一訪的有趣地方，是值得短時間參觀的地方。"},{"en":"A museum may be an interesting place for a visit, even if people would not want to live there.","zh":"博物館可能是值得一訪的有趣地方，即使人們不想住在那裡。"},{"en":"The ISS may fascinate visitors because it offers rare views and unusual experiences.","zh":"國際太空站可能令訪客着迷，因為它提供罕見景觀和不尋常經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests short-term interest, not long-term comfort.","zh":"這個短語暗示短期興趣，而不是長期舒適。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"would not want to live there","meaning":"不會想在那裏生活","examples":[{"en":"The crew member said that people would not want to live there.","zh":"該機組成員說，人們不會想在那裏生活。"},{"en":"Would not want to live there means would not choose to make that place one’s home.","zh":"不會想在那裏生活，是指不會選擇把那個地方當成自己的家。"},{"en":"A factory may be interesting to visit, but most people would not want to live there.","zh":"工廠可能值得參觀，但大多數人不會想在那裏生活。"},{"en":"The ISS is uncomfortable because it is cramped, noisy, strict, and isolated.","zh":"國際太空站不舒適，因為它擠迫、嘈吵、規矩嚴格且與人隔絕。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts visiting a place with living there long term.","zh":"這個短語對比短暫參觀和長期居住。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"answer the questions","meaning":"回答問題","examples":[{"en":"Candidates answer the questions using words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞回答問題。"},{"en":"To answer the questions means to give the required responses to a task or test.","zh":"回答問題，是指對任務或測驗給出所需答案。"},{"en":"Students should read the passage carefully before they answer the questions.","zh":"學生應仔細閱讀篇章，然後回答問題。"},{"en":"If candidates answer using words outside the passage, they may lose marks in this task.","zh":"如果考生使用文章以外的字詞回答，這類題目可能會失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is a basic exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是基本考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案應包含不多於兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means one or two words only, not three or more.","zh":"不多於兩個字，是指只可用一個或兩個英文詞，而不是三個或更多。"},{"en":"If the answer is “white dot,” it follows the rule because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “white dot”，它符合規則，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing too many words can make an answer wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫太多字也可能令答案錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"physically look like","meaning":"實際外觀看起來像","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what the ISS physically looks like from Earth.","zh":"題目問國際太空站從地球看實際外觀看起來像甚麼。"},{"en":"Physically look like means appear in shape, size, or visible form.","zh":"實際外觀看起來像，是指在形狀、大小或可見形式上呈現如何。"},{"en":"From far away, a large building may physically look like a small box.","zh":"從遠處看，大型建築物實際外觀可能像一個小盒子。"},{"en":"The ISS physically looks tiny from Earth because it is very far away.","zh":"國際太空站從地球看實際外觀很小，因為它非常遠。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about appearance, not function or meaning.","zh":"這個短語問的是外觀，而不是功能或意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"from Earth","meaning":"從地球看","examples":[{"en":"The ISS looks like a small white dot from Earth.","zh":"從地球看，國際太空站像一個小白點。"},{"en":"From Earth means as seen or considered by people on Earth.","zh":"從地球看，是指由地球上的人觀看或考慮。"},{"en":"The moon looks bright from Earth because it reflects sunlight.","zh":"從地球看，月球因反射陽光而顯得明亮。"},{"en":"An object can look small from Earth even if it is large in space.","zh":"即使某物在太空中很大，從地球看也可能很小。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the viewpoint of observers on our planet.","zh":"這個短語描述我們星球上觀察者的視角。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"from space","meaning":"從太空看","examples":[{"en":"The ISS looks like a complex structure from space.","zh":"從太空看，國際太空站像一個複雜結構。"},{"en":"From space means as seen from outside Earth’s surface or atmosphere.","zh":"從太空看，是指從地球表面或大氣之外觀看。"},{"en":"From space, cities may look like networks of lights at night.","zh":"從太空看，城市在夜間可能像燈光網絡。"},{"en":"The ISS looks more detailed from space because it is viewed much closer.","zh":"從太空看，國際太空站更有細節，因為觀看距離近得多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a viewpoint outside Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述地球之外的視角。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"force someone to work together","meaning":"迫使某人合作","examples":[{"en":"The enormous cost forced several space agencies to work together.","zh":"巨額成本迫使幾個太空機構合作。"},{"en":"To force someone to work together means to make cooperation necessary.","zh":"迫使某人合作，是指令合作變得必要。"},{"en":"A small business may be forced to work with partners if a project is too expensive to handle alone.","zh":"如果項目太昂貴，小企業可能被迫與伙伴合作，無法獨自處理。"},{"en":"High cost can force organisations to share money, skills, and responsibility.","zh":"高成本可以迫使機構分享金錢、技能和責任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pressure that makes cooperation unavoidable.","zh":"這個短語描述令合作不可避免的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"original space stations","meaning":"最初的太空站","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what the original space stations were like.","zh":"題目問最初的太空站是怎樣的。"},{"en":"Original space stations are the earliest versions of stations built for humans to live or work in space.","zh":"最初的太空站，是最早為人類在太空生活或工作而建的太空站版本。"},{"en":"Early mobile phones were simpler than modern smartphones, just as original space stations were simpler than the ISS.","zh":"早期手提電話比現代智能手機簡單，就像最初的太空站比國際太空站簡單。"},{"en":"Comparing original space stations with the ISS shows how space technology became more complex.","zh":"比較最初的太空站和國際太空站，可以顯示太空科技如何變得更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the first types of space stations.","zh":"這個短語指太空站的最早類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"strike the Earth","meaning":"撞擊地球","examples":[{"en":"The ISS does not strike the Earth because of its lateral velocity.","zh":"國際太空站因橫向速度而不會撞擊地球。"},{"en":"To strike the Earth means to hit or crash into the planet.","zh":"撞擊地球，是指擊中或撞上這個星球。"},{"en":"A meteor may strike the Earth if it survives the atmosphere and reaches the ground.","zh":"如果流星穿過大氣後仍到達地面，它可能撞擊地球。"},{"en":"The ISS avoids striking Earth because it moves sideways fast enough to remain in orbit.","zh":"國際太空站避免撞擊地球，因為它橫向移動夠快，能維持在軌道上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collision with Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述與地球碰撞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"label the diagram","meaning":"標示圖表","examples":[{"en":"Candidates label the diagram with terms from the passage.","zh":"考生用文章中的術語標示圖表。"},{"en":"To label the diagram means to write names or terms on parts of a picture.","zh":"標示圖表，是指在圖片各部分寫上名稱或術語。"},{"en":"In biology, students may label a diagram of the heart with words such as artery and valve.","zh":"在生物課中，學生可能用 artery 和 valve 等字標示心臟圖。"},{"en":"Diagram labelling tests whether students can match visual parts with exact terms.","zh":"標示圖表測試學生能否把視覺部分與準確術語配對。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction for identifying parts of an image.","zh":"這個短語是辨認圖片部分的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"specific terms","meaning":"具體術語","examples":[{"en":"The diagram must be labelled with specific terms from the passage.","zh":"圖表必須用文章中的具體術語標示。"},{"en":"Specific terms are exact words or phrases used for particular things.","zh":"具體術語是用於特定事物的準確字詞或短語。"},{"en":"In a science test, students may need specific terms such as “thermal radiator” or “solar array.”","zh":"在科學測驗中，學生可能需要 “thermal radiator” 或 “solar array” 等具體術語。"},{"en":"Using specific terms prevents vague answers and shows accurate understanding.","zh":"使用具體術語可避免含糊答案，並顯示準確理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes precise vocabulary.","zh":"這個短語描述精確詞彙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the table","meaning":"完成表格","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the table by giving causes.","zh":"考生透過提供原因完成表格。"},{"en":"To complete the table means to fill in missing information in a table.","zh":"完成表格，是指在表格中填上缺失資料。"},{"en":"Students may complete the table by writing dates, names, or reasons from the passage.","zh":"學生可能透過寫上文章中的日期、名稱或原因來完成表格。"},{"en":"Completing a table requires locating the right information and placing it in the correct box.","zh":"完成表格需要定位正確資訊並把它放入正確格子。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"give the cause of","meaning":"說明……的原因","examples":[{"en":"The table asks candidates to give the cause of each effect.","zh":"表格要求考生說明每個影響的原因。"},{"en":"To give the cause of something means to state the reason why it happened.","zh":"說明某事的原因，是指說出它為何發生。"},{"en":"A science worksheet may ask students to give the cause of rust on metal.","zh":"科學工作紙可能要求學生說明金屬生鏽的原因。"},{"en":"Giving the correct cause shows that students understand the relationship between events.","zh":"說明正確原因顯示學生理解事件之間的關係。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for a reason, not just a description.","zh":"這個短語要求原因，而不只是描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"effect or incident","meaning":"影響或事件","examples":[{"en":"Each effect or incident has one or more causes.","zh":"每個影響或事件都有一個或多個原因。"},{"en":"An effect or incident is a result, event, or happening that needs explanation.","zh":"影響或事件，是需要解釋的結果、事件或發生的事情。"},{"en":"A power cut in a school is an incident, and cancelled lessons may be an effect.","zh":"學校停電是一宗事件，而課堂取消可能是一種影響。"},{"en":"Identifying causes helps explain why an effect or incident occurred.","zh":"識別原因有助解釋影響或事件為何發生。"},{"en":"This phrase groups results and events that can be analysed.","zh":"這個短語把可分析的結果和事件歸為一類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"one cause","meaning":"一個原因","examples":[{"en":"The table gives one cause and asks for another.","zh":"表格給出一個原因，並要求另一個原因。"},{"en":"One cause is one reason why something happens.","zh":"一個原因，是某事發生的一個理由。"},{"en":"One cause of tiredness may be lack of sleep.","zh":"疲倦的一個原因可能是睡眠不足。"},{"en":"A problem may have more than one cause, so students must read carefully.","zh":"一個問題可能有多於一個原因，所以學生必須仔細閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a single reason among possible reasons.","zh":"這個短語指可能原因中的單一理由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"another cause","meaning":"另一個原因","examples":[{"en":"Candidates must identify another cause from the passage.","zh":"考生必須從文章中找出另一個原因。"},{"en":"Another cause means an additional reason apart from the one already given.","zh":"另一個原因，是除了已給出的原因之外的額外理由。"},{"en":"If poor sleep is one cause of tiredness, stress may be another cause.","zh":"如果睡眠差是疲倦的一個原因，壓力可能是另一個原因。"},{"en":"Finding another cause shows that a problem may have several contributing factors.","zh":"找出另一個原因顯示問題可能有幾個促成因素。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for an extra reason.","zh":"這個短語要求額外理由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"ISS slowing down","meaning":"國際太空站減速","examples":[{"en":"Aerodynamic drag contributes to the ISS slowing down.","zh":"空氣動力阻力導致國際太空站減速。"},{"en":"ISS slowing down means the International Space Station gradually loses speed.","zh":"國際太空站減速，是指國際太空站逐漸失去速度。"},{"en":"A bicycle slows down when friction and air resistance act against it.","zh":"單車受到摩擦和空氣阻力時會減速。"},{"en":"If the ISS slows down too much, its orbit can decay and move lower.","zh":"如果國際太空站減速太多，其軌道會衰減並下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gradual reduction in the station’s orbital speed.","zh":"這個短語描述太空站軌道速度逐漸降低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"Apollo 1 fire","meaning":"阿波羅1號火災","examples":[{"en":"The Apollo 1 fire had tragic consequences.","zh":"阿波羅1號火災造成悲劇性後果。"},{"en":"The Apollo 1 fire was a deadly fire connected with the Apollo 1 spacecraft.","zh":"阿波羅1號火災是與阿波羅1號太空船相關的致命火災。"},{"en":"A safety lesson may use the Apollo 1 fire to show why design choices matter.","zh":"安全課堂可能用阿波羅1號火災說明設計選擇為何重要。"},{"en":"The fire was made worse by a pure-oxygen atmosphere that helped flames spread.","zh":"純氧大氣助長火焰蔓延，使火災更加嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a serious spaceflight accident.","zh":"這個短語指一宗嚴重太空飛行事故。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"crew-member stress","meaning":"機組人員壓力","examples":[{"en":"Crew-member stress can result from difficult living conditions.","zh":"機組人員壓力可能源於困難生活條件。"},{"en":"Crew-member stress means pressure or mental strain experienced by people working on a crew.","zh":"機組人員壓力，是工作團隊成員所經歷的壓力或心理負擔。"},{"en":"Flight attendants may experience crew-member stress during long flights with difficult passengers.","zh":"空中服務員在長途航班中遇上難應付乘客時，可能經歷機組人員壓力。"},{"en":"On the ISS, cramped space, isolation, noise, and strict routines can increase stress.","zh":"在國際太空站上，擠迫空間、隔絕、噪音和嚴格日程都會增加壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stress affecting members of a working team.","zh":"這個短語描述影響工作團隊成員的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 94 - The International Space Station.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 95":[{"front":"the biggest impact","meaning":"最大的撞擊","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses what may have been the biggest impact in Earth’s history.","zh":"文章討論地球歷史上可能是最大的撞擊。"},{"en":"The biggest impact means the largest or most powerful collision.","zh":"the biggest impact 指最大或最強烈的碰撞。"},{"en":"A car crash involving several vehicles may be described as the biggest impact in a traffic report.","zh":"涉及多輛車的交通意外，可能在交通報告中被描述為最大的撞擊。"},{"en":"A huge impact can change the land, damage buildings, or affect many lives.","zh":"巨大撞擊可以改變地貌、損壞建築或影響許多生命。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when one collision is greater than all others being compared.","zh":"當一場碰撞比其他所有比較對象都大時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a team of researchers","meaning":"一隊研究人員","examples":[{"en":"A team of researchers were analysing soil samples at the KT boundary.","zh":"一隊研究人員正在分析 K-T 界線的泥土樣本。"},{"en":"A team of researchers is a group of people working together to study a question.","zh":"a team of researchers 指一組共同研究某問題的人。"},{"en":"A team of researchers may visit a hospital to study how patients recover after treatment.","zh":"一隊研究人員可能到醫院研究病人治療後如何康復。"},{"en":"Research teams divide tasks so that data can be collected and checked more carefully.","zh":"研究團隊會分工，使資料能更仔細地收集和檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses organised scientific work rather than one person acting alone.","zh":"這個短語強調有組織的科學工作，而不是一個人單獨行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"analysing soil samples","meaning":"分析泥土樣本","examples":[{"en":"The researchers were analysing soil samples from an ancient geological boundary.","zh":"研究人員正在分析來自古代地質界線的泥土樣本。"},{"en":"Analysing soil samples means studying pieces of soil to find out what they contain.","zh":"analysing soil samples 指研究泥土樣本，以找出其中含有甚麼。"},{"en":"Farmers may send soil to a lab for analysis before choosing fertiliser.","zh":"農民選擇肥料前，可能把泥土送到實驗室分析。"},{"en":"Soil analysis can reveal chemicals, minerals, pollution, or signs of past events.","zh":"泥土分析可以揭示化學物質、礦物、污染或過去事件的跡象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful scientific testing of earth material.","zh":"這個短語描述對泥土材料進行仔細科學測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"soil samples","meaning":"泥土樣本","examples":[{"en":"Soil samples at the KT boundary contained unusual evidence.","zh":"K-T 界線的泥土樣本含有不尋常證據。"},{"en":"Soil samples are small amounts of earth collected for testing or study.","zh":"soil samples 指為測試或研究而收集的小量泥土。"},{"en":"A gardener may test soil samples to see whether the ground is suitable for vegetables.","zh":"園丁可能測試泥土樣本，看看土地是否適合種菜。"},{"en":"Soil samples can help scientists understand climate, pollution, farming, or ancient events.","zh":"泥土樣本可以幫助科學家理解氣候、污染、農業或古代事件。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to pieces of soil used as evidence.","zh":"這個短語指用作證據的泥土片段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what was then known as","meaning":"當時被稱為……的","examples":[{"en":"The researchers studied what was then known as the KT boundary.","zh":"研究人員研究當時被稱為 K-T 界線的東西。"},{"en":"What was then known as means the name used for something at that time.","zh":"what was then known as 指某事在當時使用的名稱。"},{"en":"A city may study an area that was then known as the old market district.","zh":"城市可能研究當時被稱為舊市場區的地方。"},{"en":"Names can change later as knowledge, politics, or official terms change.","zh":"名稱後來可能因知識、政治或官方術語改變而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers understand the historical name used in the past.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者理解過去使用的歷史名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"KT boundary","meaning":"K-T 界線；白堊紀—第三紀界線","examples":[{"en":"The KT boundary marks the division between the Cretaceous and Tertiary eras.","zh":"K-T 界線標示白堊紀與第三紀之間的分界。"},{"en":"The KT boundary is a geological layer marking a major change in Earth’s history.","zh":"KT boundary 指標示地球歷史重大變化的地質層。"},{"en":"A science teacher may use the KT boundary to explain why many species disappeared.","zh":"科學老師可能用 K-T 界線解釋為何許多物種消失。"},{"en":"Such boundaries help geologists separate one time period from another.","zh":"這類界線幫助地質學家區分一個時期與另一個時期。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific geological boundary linked with mass extinction.","zh":"這個短語指出一條與大滅絕相關的特定地質界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"misleading","meaning":"具誤導性的","examples":[{"en":"The K in KT boundary is misleading.","zh":"K-T 界線中的 K 具誤導性。"},{"en":"Misleading means likely to make people understand something wrongly.","zh":"misleading 指容易令人錯誤理解某事。"},{"en":"A shop sign saying “free” can be misleading if customers must still pay a fee.","zh":"如果顧客仍須付費，寫着「免費」的商店標示就可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"Misleading information can cause wrong decisions because people trust the wrong clue.","zh":"誤導性資訊會令人依靠錯誤線索，從而作出錯誤決定。"},{"en":"This word describes something that points people toward a false idea.","zh":"這個字描述把人引向錯誤想法的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"refers to","meaning":"指的是……","examples":[{"en":"The K actually refers to the Cretaceous era.","zh":"K 實際上指的是白堊紀。"},{"en":"Refers to means points to, names, or represents something.","zh":"refers to 指指向、命名或代表某事。"},{"en":"In a timetable, “Mon” refers to Monday.","zh":"在時間表中，“Mon” 指的是星期一。"},{"en":"If a symbol is unclear, people may misunderstand what it refers to.","zh":"如果符號不清楚，人們可能誤解它指的是甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what a word, letter, or sign means.","zh":"這個短語解釋某個字、字母或標誌代表甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Cretaceous era","meaning":"白堊紀","examples":[{"en":"The K in KT refers to the Cretaceous era.","zh":"K-T 中的 K 指的是白堊紀。"},{"en":"The Cretaceous era was a geological period before the mass extinction discussed in the passage.","zh":"Cretaceous era 指文章所討論大滅絕之前的一個地質時期。"},{"en":"A museum may display dinosaur fossils from the Cretaceous era.","zh":"博物館可能展示來自白堊紀的恐龍化石。"},{"en":"Naming an era helps scientists organise fossils and rocks by time.","zh":"為時代命名有助科學家按時間整理化石和岩石。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific period in Earth’s ancient history.","zh":"這個短語指地球古代歷史中的特定時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Tertiary era","meaning":"第三紀","examples":[{"en":"The T in KT refers to the Tertiary era.","zh":"K-T 中的 T 指的是第三紀。"},{"en":"The Tertiary era was the geological period after the Cretaceous in the passage’s terminology.","zh":"Tertiary era 按文章術語指白堊紀之後的地質時期。"},{"en":"Students may learn that many mammals became more important during the Tertiary era.","zh":"學生可能學到許多哺乳類在第三紀變得更重要。"},{"en":"Geological eras help people discuss huge stretches of Earth’s history.","zh":"地質時代幫助人們討論地球歷史中的漫長時段。"},{"en":"This phrase names a time period after the extinction boundary.","zh":"這個短語指出滅絕界線之後的一個時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"geologists","meaning":"地質學家","examples":[{"en":"Geologists placed a boundary at that ancient point in time.","zh":"地質學家在那個古代時間點劃定界線。"},{"en":"Geologists are scientists who study rocks, Earth history, and geological processes.","zh":"geologists 指研究岩石、地球歷史和地質過程的科學家。"},{"en":"Geologists may examine cliffs to understand when different rock layers formed.","zh":"地質學家可能檢查峭壁，以了解不同岩層何時形成。"},{"en":"Their work helps explain earthquakes, volcanoes, fossils, and ancient climate.","zh":"他們的工作有助解釋地震、火山、化石和古代氣候。"},{"en":"This word refers to experts who study the Earth, not living animals directly.","zh":"這個字指研究地球的專家，而不是直接研究活體動物的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"placed a boundary at","meaning":"在……劃定界線","examples":[{"en":"Geologists placed a boundary at a point about 65 million years ago.","zh":"地質學家在大約六千五百萬年前的一個時間點劃定界線。"},{"en":"To place a boundary at a point means to mark that point as a division between two periods or areas.","zh":"place a boundary at a point 指把某一點標示為兩個時期或區域的分界。"},{"en":"A school may place a boundary at the edge of the playground to show where students can go.","zh":"學校可能在操場邊緣劃定界線，顯示學生可到達的範圍。"},{"en":"Boundaries help people separate one category, time, or space from another.","zh":"界線幫助人們區分一個類別、時期或空間與另一個。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating a clear dividing line.","zh":"這個短語描述建立清楚分界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"that distant point","meaning":"那個久遠的時間點","examples":[{"en":"Geologists placed the boundary at that distant point in Earth’s history.","zh":"地質學家把界線劃在地球歷史中那個久遠的時間點。"},{"en":"That distant point means a time very far in the past.","zh":"that distant point 指非常久遠的過去時間。"},{"en":"A historian may say that distant point marked the beginning of a new dynasty.","zh":"歷史學家可能說，那個久遠時間點標誌新王朝的開始。"},{"en":"Distant points in time are difficult to study because evidence is limited.","zh":"久遠時間點難以研究，因為證據有限。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers imagine a very remote moment in history.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者想像歷史中非常遙遠的一刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"some 65 million years ago","meaning":"大約六千五百萬年前","examples":[{"en":"A mass extinction occurred some 65 million years ago.","zh":"大約六千五百萬年前發生了一次大滅絕。"},{"en":"Some 65 million years ago means approximately 65 million years before the present.","zh":"some 65 million years ago 指距今約六千五百萬年前。"},{"en":"A museum label may say a fossil lived some 100 million years ago.","zh":"博物館標籤可能寫着某化石生活於大約一億年前。"},{"en":"“Some” here means “about”, not “a few.”","zh":"這裡的 some 解作「大約」，不是「一些」。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate ancient date.","zh":"這個短語給出古代的大約日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"mass extinction","meaning":"大滅絕","examples":[{"en":"A mass extinction caused many land and sea species to disappear.","zh":"大滅絕導致許多陸地和海洋物種消失。"},{"en":"A mass extinction is an event in which a very large number of species die out.","zh":"mass extinction 指大量物種滅絕的事件。"},{"en":"A science class may study mass extinction to understand how life on Earth changes suddenly.","zh":"科學課可能研究大滅絕，以理解地球生命如何突然改變。"},{"en":"Mass extinction can happen when climate, impacts, or other disasters disrupt ecosystems.","zh":"當氣候、撞擊或其他災難破壞生態系統，大滅絕可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to global biological loss, not one species disappearing.","zh":"這個短語指全球性的生物損失，而不是單一物種消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"occurred then","meaning":"在當時發生","examples":[{"en":"A major extinction occurred then, about 65 million years ago.","zh":"一次重大滅絕在當時發生，即大約六千五百萬年前。"},{"en":"Occurred then means happened at that particular time.","zh":"occurred then 指在那個特定時間發生。"},{"en":"If a fire alarm rang during lunch, the evacuation occurred then, not in the morning.","zh":"如果火警鐘在午飯時響起，疏散就是在當時發生，而不是早上。"},{"en":"This phrase links an event to a specific time already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語把事件連接到前面提及的特定時間。"},{"en":"It helps avoid confusion about when something happened.","zh":"它有助避免混淆事情何時發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"causing","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"The extinction caused over two-thirds of life to disappear.","zh":"這次滅絕導致超過三分之二的生命消失。"},{"en":"Causing means making something happen as a result.","zh":"causing 指使某事作為結果發生。"},{"en":"Heavy rain may cause traffic delays during the morning rush hour.","zh":"大雨可能導致早上繁忙時間交通延誤。"},{"en":"When one event causes another, it becomes the reason behind that result.","zh":"當一件事導致另一件事，它就成為該結果背後的原因。"},{"en":"This word is useful for showing cause and effect.","zh":"這個字適合用來表示因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"over two-thirds of","meaning":"超過三分之二的……","examples":[{"en":"Over two-thirds of all land and sea life disappeared.","zh":"超過三分之二的陸地和海洋生物消失了。"},{"en":"Over two-thirds of something means more than two out of every three parts.","zh":"over two-thirds of something 指每三份中超過兩份。"},{"en":"Over two-thirds of the class passed the test, so most students understood the topic.","zh":"超過三分之二的班級通過測驗，所以大多數學生理解該題目。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the majority is very large.","zh":"這個短語顯示大多數比例非常高。"},{"en":"It is used when the amount is greater than about 66 per cent.","zh":"當數量超過約百分之六十六時，可以使用它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"land and sea life","meaning":"陸地和海洋生物","examples":[{"en":"The extinction affected both land and sea life.","zh":"這次滅絕影響了陸地和海洋生物。"},{"en":"Land and sea life means living things found on land and in the oceans.","zh":"land and sea life 指生活在陸地和海洋中的生物。"},{"en":"Pollution can harm land and sea life if chemicals enter rivers and soil.","zh":"如果化學物進入河流和泥土，污染可以傷害陸地和海洋生物。"},{"en":"A global disaster affects many ecosystems when both land and sea life suffer.","zh":"當陸地和海洋生物都受害，全球災難就影響許多生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase covers living organisms in two major environments.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋兩大環境中的生命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"disappear","meaning":"消失；滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Many forms of life disappeared during the mass extinction.","zh":"許多生命形式在大滅絕中消失。"},{"en":"To disappear means to vanish, stop being seen, or no longer exist.","zh":"disappear 指消失、不再被看見或不再存在。"},{"en":"A phone may disappear from a desk if someone moves it without telling the owner.","zh":"如果有人不告知主人便移走手機，手機可能從桌上消失。"},{"en":"Species disappear when the last members die and no new ones are born.","zh":"當最後成員死亡且沒有新個體出生，物種就會滅絕。"},{"en":"This verb can describe physical loss or complete extinction.","zh":"這個動詞可描述實體消失或完全滅絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"including the dinosaurs","meaning":"包括恐龍在內","examples":[{"en":"The mass extinction caused many creatures to disappear, including the dinosaurs.","zh":"大滅絕導致許多生物消失，包括恐龍在內。"},{"en":"Including the dinosaurs means dinosaurs were part of the larger group affected.","zh":"including the dinosaurs 指恐龍是受影響的較大群體之一。"},{"en":"A school event may invite many clubs, including the debate team.","zh":"學校活動可能邀請許多學會，包括辯論隊在內。"},{"en":"This phrase adds an important example inside a broader category.","zh":"這個短語在較廣類別中加入重要例子。"},{"en":"It is often used when the example is famous or especially important.","zh":"當例子著名或特別重要時，常使用它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"more strictly","meaning":"更嚴格來說","examples":[{"en":"More strictly, all non-avian dinosaurs disappeared.","zh":"更嚴格來說，所有非鳥類恐龍都消失了。"},{"en":"More strictly means speaking more accurately or with a narrower definition.","zh":"more strictly 指更準確或以較狹窄定義來說。"},{"en":"People may say “I live in London,” but more strictly, they live just outside the city.","zh":"人們可能說「我住在倫敦」，但更嚴格來說，他們住在城外附近。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects or refines a previous statement.","zh":"這個短語修正或細化前一句說法。"},{"en":"It is useful when a general statement needs scientific precision.","zh":"當一般說法需要科學精確度時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"non-avian dinosaurs","meaning":"非鳥類恐龍","examples":[{"en":"All non-avian dinosaurs disappeared after the extinction event.","zh":"所有非鳥類恐龍在滅絕事件後消失。"},{"en":"Non-avian dinosaurs are dinosaurs that are not birds.","zh":"non-avian dinosaurs 指不是鳥類的恐龍。"},{"en":"A museum may explain that birds survived, while non-avian dinosaurs did not.","zh":"博物館可能解釋鳥類存活下來，而非鳥類恐龍沒有。"},{"en":"The term prevents confusion because modern birds are linked to dinosaur ancestry.","zh":"這個術語避免混淆，因為現代鳥類與恐龍祖先有關。"},{"en":"This phrase is more precise than simply saying “dinosaurs.”","zh":"這個短語比單純說「恐龍」更精確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"considered dinosaurs’ descendants","meaning":"被視為恐龍的後代","examples":[{"en":"Birds are now considered dinosaurs’ descendants.","zh":"鳥類現在被視為恐龍的後代。"},{"en":"Considered dinosaurs’ descendants means regarded as animals that evolved from dinosaurs.","zh":"considered dinosaurs’ descendants 指被認為是由恐龍演化而來的動物。"},{"en":"Students may be surprised to learn that modern birds are linked with ancient reptiles.","zh":"學生得知現代鳥類與古代爬蟲類有關時可能感到驚訝。"},{"en":"Scientific classification can change when new fossil evidence appears.","zh":"當新化石證據出現，科學分類可以改變。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how one group is understood to come from another.","zh":"這個短語解釋一個群體如何被理解為來自另一個群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"whilst","meaning":"雖然","examples":[{"en":"Whilst this was not the biggest extinction, it is the most famous.","zh":"雖然這不是最大規模的滅絕，但它最著名。"},{"en":"Whilst means although or while, depending on the sentence.","zh":"whilst 可解作「雖然」或「當……時」，視乎句子而定。"},{"en":"Whilst the course is difficult, many students find it useful.","zh":"雖然課程很困難，許多學生仍覺得它有用。"},{"en":"This word often introduces a contrast between two ideas.","zh":"這個字常引出兩個想法之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is more common in British English than American English.","zh":"它在英式英文中比美式英文更常見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the biggest extinction of all","meaning":"史上最大規模的滅絕","examples":[{"en":"This was not the biggest extinction of all.","zh":"這並不是史上最大規模的滅絕。"},{"en":"The biggest extinction of all means the largest extinction event when compared with every other one.","zh":"the biggest extinction of all 指與所有其他滅絕事件相比最大的一次。"},{"en":"A school’s largest sports day injury would not be the biggest accident of all in the city.","zh":"學校運動會最大宗受傷事件，也不會是全城最大事故。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one event with the whole set of similar events.","zh":"這個短語把一個事件與整組相似事件比較。"},{"en":"It stresses overall rank, not just importance or fame.","zh":"它強調整體排名，而不只是重要性或知名度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"definitely the most famous","meaning":"絕對是最著名的","examples":[{"en":"The KT extinction is definitely the most famous extinction event.","zh":"K-T 滅絕事件絕對是最著名的滅絕事件。"},{"en":"Definitely the most famous means clearly better known than all others.","zh":"definitely the most famous 指明顯比其他所有事物更為人熟知。"},{"en":"In many schools, Shakespeare is definitely the most famous English playwright.","zh":"在許多學校中，莎士比亞絕對是最著名的英文劇作家。"},{"en":"Something can be the most famous even if it is not the largest or most important.","zh":"某事即使不是最大或最重要，也可以是最著名的。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses strong certainty about public recognition.","zh":"這個短語強烈肯定其公眾知名度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what caused it","meaning":"是甚麼造成它","examples":[{"en":"Scientists wanted to know what caused the extinction.","zh":"科學家想知道是甚麼造成這次滅絕。"},{"en":"What caused it means the reason or event that made it happen.","zh":"what caused it 指令某事發生的原因或事件。"},{"en":"If a student’s grades suddenly fall, a teacher may ask what caused it.","zh":"如果學生分數突然下跌，老師可能會問是甚麼造成它。"},{"en":"Finding the cause helps people explain the result and prevent similar problems.","zh":"找出原因有助人們解釋結果並防止類似問題。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for the cause behind an event.","zh":"這個短語詢問事件背後的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"discovered that","meaning":"發現","examples":[{"en":"The researchers discovered that the layers contained unusual amounts of iridium.","zh":"研究人員發現這些地層含有不尋常數量的銥。"},{"en":"Discovered that means found out something after investigation or study.","zh":"discovered that 指經調查或研究後發現某事。"},{"en":"A doctor discovered that the patient’s tiredness was caused by low iron.","zh":"醫生發現病人的疲倦是由低鐵造成。"},{"en":"Discoveries often change how people understand a problem.","zh":"發現常會改變人們對問題的理解。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces new information found through evidence.","zh":"這個短語引出透過證據找到的新資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sedimentary layers","meaning":"沉積層","examples":[{"en":"Sedimentary layers at the KT boundary contained high levels of iridium.","zh":"K-T 界線的沉積層含有高水平的銥。"},{"en":"Sedimentary layers are layers of rock or soil formed from material deposited over time.","zh":"sedimentary layers 指由長時間沉積物形成的岩石或泥土層。"},{"en":"A cliff may show sedimentary layers like pages in Earth’s history book.","zh":"峭壁可能顯示像地球歷史書頁一樣的沉積層。"},{"en":"These layers can preserve fossils, minerals, and signs of ancient events.","zh":"這些地層可以保存化石、礦物和古代事件跡象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stacked geological evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述層層堆疊的地質證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"contained a concentration of","meaning":"含有……濃度","examples":[{"en":"The layers contained a concentration of iridium many times higher than normal.","zh":"這些地層含有比正常高出多倍的銥濃度。"},{"en":"Contained a concentration of means had a measured amount of a substance inside.","zh":"contained a concentration of 指內部有某種物質的可量度分量。"},{"en":"A water sample may contain a concentration of salt too high for drinking.","zh":"水樣本可能含有過高鹽分濃度，不適合飲用。"},{"en":"Unusual concentrations can alert scientists to pollution or rare events.","zh":"不尋常濃度可以提醒科學家注意污染或罕見事件。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a material with the amount of substance found in it.","zh":"這個短語把材料與其中發現的物質含量連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"concentration of iridium","meaning":"銥濃度","examples":[{"en":"The concentration of iridium at the KT boundary was unusually high.","zh":"K-T 界線的銥濃度異常高。"},{"en":"Concentration of iridium means the amount of iridium found in a particular material.","zh":"concentration of iridium 指某材料中發現的銥含量。"},{"en":"A lab report may measure the concentration of a metal in soil or water.","zh":"實驗室報告可能量度泥土或水中某金屬的濃度。"},{"en":"High iridium levels can suggest material from an asteroid or comet.","zh":"高銥水平可以暗示來自小行星或彗星的物質。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the measured amount of one element.","zh":"這個短語集中於某一元素的量度分量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"many times higher than normal","meaning":"比正常高出多倍","examples":[{"en":"The iridium level was many times higher than normal.","zh":"銥水平比正常高出多倍。"},{"en":"Many times higher than normal means far above the usual amount.","zh":"many times higher than normal 指遠高於平常數量。"},{"en":"A water bill many times higher than normal may show that a pipe is leaking.","zh":"如果水費比正常高出多倍，可能顯示水管漏水。"},{"en":"Very unusual levels often make people search for an explanation.","zh":"非常不尋常的水平常令人尋找解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a large difference from the expected level.","zh":"這個短語強調與預期水平之間的巨大差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"up to 120 times","meaning":"高達一百二十倍","examples":[{"en":"The iridium concentration was up to 120 times higher than normal.","zh":"銥濃度高達正常水平的一百二十倍。"},{"en":"Up to 120 times means reaching a maximum of 120 times the usual amount.","zh":"up to 120 times 指最高達到通常數量的一百二十倍。"},{"en":"A sale sign saying “up to 70% off” means the biggest discount is 70%.","zh":"折扣標示寫着 “up to 70% off”，意思是最高折扣為七折。"},{"en":"“Up to” gives the highest possible figure, not necessarily every case.","zh":"“up to” 給出最高可能數字，不代表每個個案都是如此。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights an extreme upper limit.","zh":"這個短語突出極端上限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"iridium","meaning":"銥","examples":[{"en":"Iridium is abundant in asteroids and comets.","zh":"銥在小行星和彗星中含量豐富。"},{"en":"Iridium is a rare metal element on Earth’s surface.","zh":"iridium 指在地球表面相當罕見的一種金屬元素。"},{"en":"A science teacher may mention iridium when explaining evidence for asteroid impacts.","zh":"科學老師解釋小行星撞擊證據時，可能提到銥。"},{"en":"High iridium in a rock layer can suggest material from space.","zh":"岩層中高銥含量可能暗示來自太空的物質。"},{"en":"This word names an element used as a clue in geology.","zh":"這個字指出一種在地質學中用作線索的元素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"disappeared when","meaning":"在……時消失","examples":[{"en":"Most iridium disappeared when the Earth was molten.","zh":"大部分銥在地球處於熔融狀態時消失。"},{"en":"Disappeared when means vanished or moved away at the time something else happened.","zh":"disappeared when 指在另一件事發生時消失或移走。"},{"en":"The lights disappeared when the power failed during the storm.","zh":"暴風雨中停電時，燈光消失了。"},{"en":"This phrase links disappearance with the condition that caused or accompanied it.","zh":"這個短語把消失與導致或伴隨它的情況連起來。"},{"en":"It helps show timing and cause together.","zh":"它有助同時顯示時間和原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the Earth was molten","meaning":"地球處於熔融狀態","examples":[{"en":"Most iridium sank when the Earth was molten.","zh":"當地球處於熔融狀態時，大部分銥沉了下去。"},{"en":"The Earth was molten means Earth’s material was hot enough to be liquid or partly liquid.","zh":"the Earth was molten 指地球物質熱到呈液態或部分液態。"},{"en":"Melted chocolate is molten, so it flows instead of staying solid.","zh":"融化朱古力是熔融的，所以會流動而不是保持固體。"},{"en":"When Earth was molten, heavy materials could sink toward the core.","zh":"當地球處於熔融狀態，重物質可以沉向地核。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an extremely hot early state of the planet.","zh":"這個短語描述地球早期極高溫狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sinking into","meaning":"沉入……","examples":[{"en":"Iridium sank into the Earth’s metallic core.","zh":"銥沉入地球的金屬地核。"},{"en":"Sinking into something means moving downward into it.","zh":"sinking into something 指向下移入某物之中。"},{"en":"A heavy coin may sink into soft mud after rain.","zh":"大雨後，沉重硬幣可能沉入軟泥中。"},{"en":"Heavy substances can sink into lower layers when materials are liquid.","zh":"當材料呈液態，重物質可以沉入較低層。"},{"en":"This phrase describes downward movement into another material.","zh":"這個短語描述向下進入另一種物質的動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"metallic core","meaning":"金屬地核","examples":[{"en":"Most iridium sank into the Earth’s metallic core.","zh":"大部分銥沉入地球的金屬地核。"},{"en":"The metallic core is the metal-rich centre of a planet.","zh":"metallic core 指行星富含金屬的中心部分。"},{"en":"A classroom model of Earth may show the core as the deepest layer.","zh":"地球課室模型可能把地核顯示為最深層。"},{"en":"Heavy metals tend to collect in the core during planetary formation.","zh":"在行星形成期間，重金屬往往聚集於地核。"},{"en":"This phrase names the central metal part of Earth.","zh":"這個短語指出地球中央的金屬部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"this element","meaning":"這種元素","examples":[{"en":"This element is abundant in asteroids and comets.","zh":"這種元素在小行星和彗星中含量豐富。"},{"en":"This element refers to the chemical element just mentioned.","zh":"this element 指剛才提及的化學元素。"},{"en":"In a science report, “this element” may refer back to oxygen, iron, or carbon.","zh":"在科學報告中，“this element” 可能指回氧、鐵或碳。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to avoid repeating the same element name too often.","zh":"作者使用這個短語以避免過度重複同一元素名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase depends on the previous sentence for its meaning.","zh":"這個短語的意思取決於前一句。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"abundant in","meaning":"在……中含量豐富","examples":[{"en":"Iridium is abundant in asteroids and comets.","zh":"銥在小行星和彗星中含量豐富。"},{"en":"Abundant in something means found there in large amounts.","zh":"abundant in something 指在某物中大量存在。"},{"en":"Oranges are abundant in vitamin C, so many people eat them when they want fruit.","zh":"橙含有豐富維他命 C，所以許多人想吃水果時會吃橙。"},{"en":"If a material is abundant in one place but rare elsewhere, it can become an important clue.","zh":"如果某物質在一處含量豐富但在其他地方罕見，它可以成為重要線索。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where something is plentiful.","zh":"這個短語描述某物在哪裡大量存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"asteroids and comets","meaning":"小行星和彗星","examples":[{"en":"Asteroids and comets contain abundant iridium.","zh":"小行星和彗星含有豐富的銥。"},{"en":"Asteroids and comets are small space objects that can orbit the Sun and sometimes approach planets.","zh":"asteroids and comets 指圍繞太陽運行、有時接近行星的小型太空物體。"},{"en":"A science museum may show models of asteroids and comets to explain space impacts.","zh":"科學博物館可能展示小行星和彗星模型，以解釋太空撞擊。"},{"en":"If such objects strike Earth, they can leave unusual chemical evidence.","zh":"如果這些物體撞擊地球，它們可以留下不尋常化學證據。"},{"en":"This phrase names two types of objects from space.","zh":"這個短語指出兩類來自太空的物體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"led to","meaning":"導致；引出","examples":[{"en":"The unusual iridium concentration led to an intriguing hypothesis.","zh":"不尋常的銥濃度引出一個引人入勝的假說。"},{"en":"Led to means caused or produced a result.","zh":"led to 指造成或產生某個結果。"},{"en":"Poor sleep led to careless mistakes in the student’s essay.","zh":"睡眠不足導致學生作文中出現粗心錯誤。"},{"en":"One piece of evidence can lead to a new question or theory.","zh":"一項證據可以引出新的問題或理論。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a cause-and-effect connection.","zh":"這個短語顯示因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"intriguing hypothesis","meaning":"引人入勝的假說","examples":[{"en":"The evidence led to an intriguing hypothesis about an asteroid impact.","zh":"證據引出一個關於小行星撞擊的引人入勝假說。"},{"en":"An intriguing hypothesis is an interesting possible explanation that needs testing.","zh":"intriguing hypothesis 指有趣而需要驗證的可能解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may offer an intriguing hypothesis about why students learn better in groups.","zh":"老師可能提出一個引人入勝的假說，解釋為何學生小組學習效果更好。"},{"en":"A hypothesis becomes stronger when evidence supports it repeatedly.","zh":"當證據反覆支持某假說，它就會變得更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a theory that attracts curiosity but still requires proof.","zh":"這個短語描述吸引好奇但仍需證明的理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"had struck the Earth","meaning":"曾撞擊地球","examples":[{"en":"Scientists suggested that an asteroid or comet had struck the Earth.","zh":"科學家提出一顆小行星或彗星曾撞擊地球。"},{"en":"Had struck the Earth means had hit the planet with force.","zh":"had struck the Earth 指曾以力量撞擊地球。"},{"en":"A meteor had struck the roof if the broken tiles and rock fragments match.","zh":"如果破瓦和岩石碎片吻合，可能是一顆隕石曾撞擊屋頂。"},{"en":"When something strikes Earth from space, it may leave craters or unusual materials.","zh":"當某物從太空撞擊地球，它可能留下隕石坑或不尋常物質。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a past collision with the planet.","zh":"這個短語描述過去與地球的碰撞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"causing the mass extinction","meaning":"造成大滅絕","examples":[{"en":"The impact may have caused the mass extinction.","zh":"這次撞擊可能造成大滅絕。"},{"en":"Causing the mass extinction means being the reason many species died out.","zh":"causing the mass extinction 指成為許多物種滅絕的原因。"},{"en":"A disease outbreak can cause a farm’s animals to die if it spreads unchecked.","zh":"如果疾病爆發不受控制地擴散，可以導致農場動物死亡。"},{"en":"In science, a cause must match the timing and evidence of the event.","zh":"在科學中，原因必須與事件的時間和證據相符。"},{"en":"This phrase links one disaster to a huge biological loss.","zh":"這個短語把一場災難與巨大生物損失連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"vaporised almost immediately","meaning":"幾乎立即氣化","examples":[{"en":"The object would have vaporised almost immediately upon impact.","zh":"該物體在撞擊時幾乎立即氣化。"},{"en":"Vaporised almost immediately means changed into gas almost at once.","zh":"vaporised almost immediately 指幾乎立刻變成氣體。"},{"en":"Water on a very hot pan may vaporise almost immediately.","zh":"水滴在極熱平底鍋上可能幾乎立即氣化。"},{"en":"Extreme heat from impact can turn solid rock into vapour.","zh":"撞擊產生的極端高溫可以把固體岩石變成蒸氣。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a rapid physical change caused by heat.","zh":"這個短語強調由熱力造成的快速物理變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"upon impact","meaning":"撞擊時","examples":[{"en":"The asteroid vaporised upon impact.","zh":"小行星在撞擊時氣化。"},{"en":"Upon impact means at the moment of hitting something.","zh":"upon impact 指撞上某物的一刻。"},{"en":"An airbag opens upon impact to protect passengers.","zh":"安全氣袋在撞擊時打開，以保護乘客。"},{"en":"What happens upon impact depends on speed, angle, and material.","zh":"撞擊時會發生甚麼取決於速度、角度和材料。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the instant a collision occurs.","zh":"這個短語標示碰撞發生的一瞬間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"throwing its contents into","meaning":"將其內容物拋入……","examples":[{"en":"The impact threw iridium-rich contents into the atmosphere.","zh":"撞擊將富含銥的物質拋入大氣層。"},{"en":"Throwing its contents into something means forcefully sending the material inside into another place.","zh":"throwing its contents into something 指把內部物質猛烈拋到另一地方。"},{"en":"A dropped bag may throw its contents into the street if it bursts open.","zh":"如果袋子掉落並爆開，可能把內容物拋到街上。"},{"en":"Powerful explosions can throw dust, ash, or debris high into the air.","zh":"強烈爆炸可以把塵埃、灰燼或碎片拋上高空。"},{"en":"This phrase describes violent movement of material.","zh":"這個短語描述物質的猛烈移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"iridium-rich contents","meaning":"富含銥的物質","examples":[{"en":"The object threw its iridium-rich contents into the atmosphere.","zh":"該物體把富含銥的物質拋入大氣層。"},{"en":"Iridium-rich contents are materials containing a high amount of iridium.","zh":"iridium-rich contents 指含有高量銥的物質。"},{"en":"A mineral sample may be iron-rich if it contains much more iron than usual.","zh":"如果礦物樣本含鐵量遠高於平常，它可以稱為富含鐵。"},{"en":"When iridium-rich material spreads globally, it can become a geological clue.","zh":"當富含銥的物質全球擴散，它可以成為地質線索。"},{"en":"This phrase describes material marked by unusually high iridium content.","zh":"這個短語描述銥含量異常高的物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"into the atmosphere","meaning":"進入大氣層","examples":[{"en":"The impact sent material into the atmosphere.","zh":"撞擊把物質送入大氣層。"},{"en":"Into the atmosphere means into the layer of gases surrounding Earth.","zh":"into the atmosphere 指進入圍繞地球的氣體層。"},{"en":"Smoke from a fire rises into the atmosphere.","zh":"火災的煙會升入大氣層。"},{"en":"Material in the atmosphere can affect sunlight, temperature, and air quality.","zh":"大氣層中的物質可以影響陽光、溫度和空氣質素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement upward into the air around the planet.","zh":"這個短語描述向上進入地球周圍空氣的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"settled across","meaning":"沉降遍佈……","examples":[{"en":"The material eventually settled across the entire planet.","zh":"這些物質最終沉降遍佈整個星球。"},{"en":"Settled across means fell down and spread over a wide area.","zh":"settled across 指降落並散布在廣闊範圍上。"},{"en":"Dust from nearby construction may settle across desks and windowsills.","zh":"附近工程的塵埃可能沉降在書桌和窗台上。"},{"en":"Material carried by air can settle far from where it began.","zh":"被空氣帶走的物質可以沉降在離源頭很遠的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual spreading and falling onto surfaces.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸散布並落在表面上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the entire planet","meaning":"整個星球","examples":[{"en":"Iridium-rich material settled across the entire planet.","zh":"富含銥的物質沉降遍佈整個星球。"},{"en":"The entire planet means the whole Earth.","zh":"the entire planet 指整個地球。"},{"en":"A global weather pattern can affect the entire planet in different ways.","zh":"全球天氣模式可以以不同方式影響整個星球。"},{"en":"When evidence is found worldwide, scientists may look for a global cause.","zh":"當證據在全球發現，科學家可能尋找全球性原因。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the effect was not local.","zh":"這個短語強調影響並非局部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"large enough to","meaning":"大到足以……","examples":[{"en":"An asteroid large enough to cause extinction would have left impact traces.","zh":"大到足以造成滅絕的小行星應會留下撞擊痕跡。"},{"en":"Large enough to do something means big enough for that result to be possible.","zh":"large enough to do something 指大到可使某結果成為可能。"},{"en":"A box large enough to hold all the books will be too heavy for one child.","zh":"大到足以裝下所有書的箱子，對一個孩子來說會太重。"},{"en":"Size matters because bigger objects can create stronger effects.","zh":"大小很重要，因為較大的物體可以造成較強效果。"},{"en":"This phrase connects size with ability or consequence.","zh":"這個短語把尺寸與能力或後果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"left traces of","meaning":"留下……的痕跡","examples":[{"en":"A large asteroid would have left traces of its impact.","zh":"一顆大型小行星應會留下其撞擊痕跡。"},{"en":"Left traces of something means left signs or evidence that it happened.","zh":"left traces of something 指留下某事發生過的跡象或證據。"},{"en":"Muddy shoes may leave traces of dirt across a clean floor.","zh":"沾滿泥的鞋可能在乾淨地板上留下泥跡。"},{"en":"Ancient events can leave traces in rocks, soil, or fossils.","zh":"古代事件可以在岩石、泥土或化石中留下痕跡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes remaining evidence after an event.","zh":"這個短語描述事件之後剩下的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"traces of its impact","meaning":"其撞擊痕跡","examples":[{"en":"Scientists expected to find traces of the asteroid’s impact.","zh":"科學家預期會找到該小行星的撞擊痕跡。"},{"en":"Traces of its impact are marks or evidence left by a collision.","zh":"traces of its impact 指碰撞留下的痕跡或證據。"},{"en":"A dent in a car door can be a trace of a parking accident.","zh":"車門凹痕可以是泊車意外的撞擊痕跡。"},{"en":"Impact traces can include craters, shocked rocks, or unusual minerals.","zh":"撞擊痕跡可包括隕石坑、受震岩石或不尋常礦物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to clues showing that something hit something else.","zh":"這個短語指顯示某物撞上另一物的線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Earth’s crust","meaning":"地殼","examples":[{"en":"Impact traces should have appeared in the Earth’s crust.","zh":"撞擊痕跡應該出現在地殼中。"},{"en":"Earth’s crust is the outer solid layer of the planet.","zh":"Earth’s crust 指地球最外層的固體層。"},{"en":"Students may compare Earth’s crust to the thin skin of an apple.","zh":"學生可能把地殼比作蘋果的薄皮。"},{"en":"Craters, faults, and rock layers are found in or on the crust.","zh":"隕石坑、斷層和岩層都在地殼中或地殼表面發現。"},{"en":"This phrase names the planet’s outer geological layer.","zh":"這個短語指出地球最外層的地質層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"known signs","meaning":"已知跡象","examples":[{"en":"At that time, there were no known signs of the impact.","zh":"當時，沒有已知的撞擊跡象。"},{"en":"Known signs are signs that people have already discovered or recognised.","zh":"known signs 指人們已經發現或認出的跡象。"},{"en":"A doctor may say there are no known signs of infection after checking a patient.","zh":"醫生檢查病人後可能說沒有已知感染跡象。"},{"en":"Lack of known signs does not always mean evidence does not exist.","zh":"缺乏已知跡象不一定代表證據不存在。"},{"en":"This phrase separates discovered evidence from evidence that may still be hidden.","zh":"這個短語把已發現證據與可能仍被隱藏的證據分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in actual fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In actual fact, evidence had already been noticed in Mexico.","zh":"事實上，證據早已在墨西哥被注意到。"},{"en":"In actual fact means actually or in reality.","zh":"in actual fact 指其實或在現實中。"},{"en":"I thought the class was cancelled; in actual fact, it had moved to another room.","zh":"我以為課堂取消了；事實上，它只是移到另一間課室。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects a mistaken impression.","zh":"這個短語修正錯誤印象。"},{"en":"It often introduces information that changes the reader’s understanding.","zh":"它常引出改變讀者理解的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"contractor","meaning":"承包商","examples":[{"en":"A contractor named Baltosser studied a gravity map.","zh":"一名叫 Baltosser 的承包商研究了一張重力圖。"},{"en":"A contractor is a person or company hired to do specific work for another organisation.","zh":"contractor 指受聘為另一機構完成特定工作的人或公司。"},{"en":"A school may hire a contractor to repair the roof during holidays.","zh":"學校可能在假期聘請承包商修理屋頂。"},{"en":"Contractors often work on projects without being permanent staff.","zh":"承包商通常參與項目工作，但不是永久員工。"},{"en":"This word describes someone hired for a task or service.","zh":"這個字描述受聘完成任務或服務的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"state-owned oil company","meaning":"國有石油公司","examples":[{"en":"Baltosser worked for a Mexican state-owned oil company.","zh":"Baltosser 為一間墨西哥國有石油公司工作。"},{"en":"A state-owned oil company is an oil company owned or controlled by the government.","zh":"state-owned oil company 指由政府擁有或控制的石油公司。"},{"en":"A country may use a state-owned company to manage important natural resources.","zh":"國家可能使用國有公司管理重要自然資源。"},{"en":"Government ownership can affect what information workers are allowed to release.","zh":"政府擁有權可以影響員工可否發放資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both ownership and industry.","zh":"這個短語同時描述所有權和行業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"gravity map","meaning":"重力圖","examples":[{"en":"Baltosser looked at a gravity map of the Yucatán Peninsula.","zh":"Baltosser 查看了尤卡坦半島的重力圖。"},{"en":"A gravity map shows variations in gravitational pull across an area.","zh":"gravity map 顯示某地區重力強度的變化。"},{"en":"Geologists may use a gravity map to locate hidden structures underground.","zh":"地質學家可能用重力圖尋找地下隱藏結構。"},{"en":"Unusual gravity patterns can suggest buried rock features or craters.","zh":"不尋常重力模式可能暗示埋藏岩石特徵或隕石坑。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a scientific map, not an ordinary road map.","zh":"這個短語指科學地圖，而不是普通道路地圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Yucatán Peninsula","meaning":"尤卡坦半島","examples":[{"en":"The Yucatán Peninsula lies near the Gulf of Mexico.","zh":"尤卡坦半島位於墨西哥灣附近。"},{"en":"The Yucatán Peninsula is a land area in southeastern Mexico.","zh":"Yucatán Peninsula 指墨西哥東南部的一片陸地。"},{"en":"A geography class may locate the Yucatán Peninsula on a map of North America.","zh":"地理課可能在北美洲地圖上找出尤卡坦半島。"},{"en":"Its location matters because the Chicxulub Crater was centred there.","zh":"它的位置很重要，因為希克蘇魯伯隕石坑以該地為中心。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific geographical region.","zh":"這個短語指出特定地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Gulf of Mexico","meaning":"墨西哥灣","examples":[{"en":"The Yucatán Peninsula is near the Gulf of Mexico.","zh":"尤卡坦半島位於墨西哥灣附近。"},{"en":"The Gulf of Mexico is a large body of water bordered by Mexico and the southern United States.","zh":"Gulf of Mexico 指由墨西哥和美國南部環繞的大型水域。"},{"en":"A weather report may mention storms forming over the Gulf of Mexico.","zh":"天氣報告可能提到在墨西哥灣形成的風暴。"},{"en":"Its seabed helped scientists study the buried impact structure.","zh":"其海床幫助科學家研究被埋藏的撞擊結構。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific sea region.","zh":"這個短語指出特定海域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"noticed","meaning":"留意到","examples":[{"en":"Baltosser noticed a large arc-shaped feature.","zh":"Baltosser 留意到一個大型弧形特徵。"},{"en":"Noticed means saw or became aware of something.","zh":"noticed 指看見或察覺到某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice that a student is quieter than usual.","zh":"老師可能留意到某學生比平常安靜。"},{"en":"Noticing small details can lead to important questions or discoveries.","zh":"留意小細節可以引出重要問題或發現。"},{"en":"This word describes becoming aware of evidence or change.","zh":"這個字描述察覺證據或變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"arc-shaped feature","meaning":"弧形特徵","examples":[{"en":"The map showed a large arc-shaped feature.","zh":"地圖顯示一個大型弧形特徵。"},{"en":"An arc-shaped feature is a structure or pattern shaped like part of a circle.","zh":"arc-shaped feature 指形狀像圓的一部分的結構或模式。"},{"en":"A rainbow is arc-shaped because it curves across the sky.","zh":"彩虹呈弧形，因為它彎曲橫跨天空。"},{"en":"A large arc in geological data may suggest a buried circular structure.","zh":"地質資料中的大型弧形可能暗示埋藏的圓形結構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shape and appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述形狀和外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"showing a symmetry","meaning":"顯示出對稱性","examples":[{"en":"The feature showed a symmetry that could not have occurred naturally.","zh":"該特徵顯示出不可能自然形成的對稱性。"},{"en":"Showing a symmetry means having balanced or matching parts on different sides.","zh":"showing a symmetry 指在不同側面有平衡或相配部分。"},{"en":"A butterfly’s wings show symmetry because the two sides look similar.","zh":"蝴蝶翅膀顯示出對稱性，因為兩邊看起來相似。"},{"en":"Strong symmetry in natural data may make scientists ask whether a special event caused it.","zh":"自然資料中強烈對稱可能令科學家追問是否由特殊事件造成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible balance in a pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述模式中的可見平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"occurred naturally","meaning":"自然形成","examples":[{"en":"The symmetry could not have occurred naturally.","zh":"這種對稱不可能自然形成。"},{"en":"Occurred naturally means happened through ordinary natural processes, without human action or unusual causes.","zh":"occurred naturally 指透過普通自然過程發生，而非人為行動或特殊原因造成。"},{"en":"A perfectly straight line of bricks did not occur naturally; someone placed them there.","zh":"一排完全筆直的磚不是自然形成的；有人把它們放在那裡。"},{"en":"If a pattern is unlikely to occur naturally, scientists look for another explanation.","zh":"如果某模式不大可能自然形成，科學家會尋找另一解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts natural formation with special or artificial causes.","zh":"這個短語把自然形成與特殊或人為原因作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"company policy","meaning":"公司政策","examples":[{"en":"Company policy prevented Baltosser from releasing his findings.","zh":"公司政策阻止 Baltosser 發表他的發現。"},{"en":"Company policy means official rules set by a company.","zh":"company policy 指公司制定的官方規則。"},{"en":"A company policy may require staff to keep client information private.","zh":"公司政策可能要求員工保密客戶資料。"},{"en":"Company policies can control what workers may share, wear, or do at work.","zh":"公司政策可以控制員工在工作中可分享、穿着或做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to rules from an organisation, not personal preference.","zh":"這個短語指組織規則，而不是個人偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"forbade him from","meaning":"禁止他……","examples":[{"en":"Company policy forbade him from releasing his findings.","zh":"公司政策禁止他發表自己的發現。"},{"en":"Forbade him from doing something means officially stopped or prohibited him from doing it.","zh":"forbade him from doing something 指正式阻止或禁止他做某事。"},{"en":"School rules forbade students from entering the laboratory without a teacher.","zh":"校規禁止學生在沒有老師的情況下進入實驗室。"},{"en":"A ban can prevent information, action, or behaviour from happening.","zh":"禁令可以阻止資訊、行動或行為發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong restriction.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"releasing his findings","meaning":"發表他的發現","examples":[{"en":"Baltosser was not allowed to release his findings.","zh":"Baltosser 不被允許發表他的發現。"},{"en":"Releasing his findings means making his discoveries or results publicly available.","zh":"releasing his findings 指把他的發現或結果公開。"},{"en":"A researcher may release her findings in a journal after checking the data.","zh":"研究者核對資料後，可能在期刊發表其發現。"},{"en":"If findings are not released, other scientists cannot examine or build on them.","zh":"如果發現沒有被發表，其他科學家就不能檢查或進一步研究它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sharing research results with others.","zh":"這個短語描述與他人分享研究結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"remained hidden","meaning":"一直被隱藏","examples":[{"en":"The secret remained hidden until 1978.","zh":"這個秘密一直被隱藏，直到1978年。"},{"en":"Remained hidden means continued to be unknown, unseen, or not public.","zh":"remained hidden 指持續不為人知、看不見或未公開。"},{"en":"A mistake in a report may remain hidden until someone checks the figures carefully.","zh":"報告中的錯誤可能一直被隱藏，直到有人仔細檢查數字。"},{"en":"Hidden information can delay understanding or decision-making.","zh":"隱藏資訊可以延誤理解或決策。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something staying concealed over time.","zh":"這個短語描述某事隨時間持續被隱藏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"geophysicists","meaning":"地球物理學家","examples":[{"en":"Two geophysicists discovered the same feature again.","zh":"兩名地球物理學家再次發現同一特徵。"},{"en":"Geophysicists are scientists who study Earth using physics, such as gravity, magnetism, and seismic waves.","zh":"geophysicists 指使用物理學研究地球的科學家，例如研究重力、磁力和地震波。"},{"en":"Geophysicists may help locate oil, minerals, or earthquake risks.","zh":"地球物理學家可能協助尋找石油、礦物或地震風險。"},{"en":"Their measurements can reveal hidden structures below the surface.","zh":"他們的量度可以揭示地表以下的隱藏結構。"},{"en":"This word refers to scientists studying Earth’s physical properties.","zh":"這個字指研究地球物理特性的科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"working for the same company","meaning":"為同一間公司工作","examples":[{"en":"Camargo and Penfield were working for the same company.","zh":"Camargo 和 Penfield 為同一間公司工作。"},{"en":"Working for the same company means being employed by one shared organisation.","zh":"working for the same company 指受僱於同一個組織。"},{"en":"Two engineers working for the same company may still work in different departments.","zh":"兩名為同一間公司工作的工程師，仍可能在不同部門工作。"},{"en":"Shared employment can give people access to the same data or equipment.","zh":"共同受僱可能讓人接觸相同資料或設備。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a workplace connection.","zh":"這個短語指出工作場所上的關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"discovered it again","meaning":"再次發現它","examples":[{"en":"Two geophysicists discovered the hidden feature again.","zh":"兩名地球物理學家再次發現這個隱藏特徵。"},{"en":"Discovered it again means found the same thing another time, often after it had been forgotten or hidden.","zh":"discovered it again 指再次找到同一事物，通常是在它被遺忘或隱藏之後。"},{"en":"A student may discover an old family photo again while cleaning a drawer.","zh":"學生清理抽屜時，可能再次發現一張舊家庭照片。"},{"en":"Rediscovery can make an old observation important in a new context.","zh":"重新發現可以令舊觀察在新背景中變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the finding was not completely new, but became visible again.","zh":"這個短語顯示該發現並非全新，而是再次變得可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the search for","meaning":"在尋找……時","examples":[{"en":"They found the feature in the search for oil-drilling sites.","zh":"他們在尋找石油鑽探地點時發現這個特徵。"},{"en":"In the search for something means while looking for it.","zh":"in the search for something 指在尋找某物的過程中。"},{"en":"A family may find old letters in the search for a lost passport.","zh":"家庭在尋找遺失護照時，可能發現舊信件。"},{"en":"People sometimes discover unexpected things while searching for something else.","zh":"人們有時在尋找其他東西時，意外發現不預期的事物。"},{"en":"This phrase links a discovery with the search activity that led to it.","zh":"這個短語把發現與導致它的搜尋活動連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"oil-drilling sites","meaning":"石油鑽探地點","examples":[{"en":"The company was searching for possible oil-drilling sites.","zh":"公司正在尋找可能的石油鑽探地點。"},{"en":"Oil-drilling sites are places where companies may drill into the ground or seabed to find oil.","zh":"oil-drilling sites 指公司可能鑽入地下或海床尋找石油的地方。"},{"en":"Engineers study maps before choosing safe oil-drilling sites.","zh":"工程師選擇安全石油鑽探地點前會研究地圖。"},{"en":"Choosing the wrong site can waste money and damage the environment.","zh":"選錯地點可能浪費金錢並破壞環境。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to locations for extracting oil.","zh":"這個短語指開採石油的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"examining magnetic surveys","meaning":"檢查磁力勘測資料","examples":[{"en":"The geophysicists were examining magnetic surveys in the Gulf of Mexico.","zh":"地球物理學家正在檢查墨西哥灣的磁力勘測資料。"},{"en":"Examining magnetic surveys means studying measurements of magnetic patterns in an area.","zh":"examining magnetic surveys 指研究某地區磁場模式的量度資料。"},{"en":"Scientists may examine magnetic surveys before digging underground tunnels.","zh":"科學家挖掘地下隧道前可能檢查磁力勘測資料。"},{"en":"Magnetic data can reveal buried rocks, metal objects, or geological structures.","zh":"磁力資料可以揭示埋藏岩石、金屬物或地質結構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful study of scientific survey data.","zh":"這個短語描述對科學勘測資料的仔細研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"magnetic surveys","meaning":"磁力勘測","examples":[{"en":"Magnetic surveys revealed an underwater arc.","zh":"磁力勘測揭示了一個水下弧形結構。"},{"en":"Magnetic surveys are measurements of magnetic patterns under land or sea.","zh":"magnetic surveys 指量度陸地或海底磁場模式的方法。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may use magnetic surveys to find buried walls without digging.","zh":"考古學家可能使用磁力勘測，在不挖掘下尋找埋藏牆壁。"},{"en":"Different rocks or structures can create different magnetic signals.","zh":"不同岩石或結構可以產生不同磁力訊號。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a scientific method for detecting hidden features.","zh":"這個短語指探測隱藏特徵的科學方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"revealed","meaning":"揭示","examples":[{"en":"The magnetic surveys revealed an underwater arc.","zh":"磁力勘測揭示了一個水下弧形結構。"},{"en":"Revealed means showed something that was hidden or not known before.","zh":"revealed 指顯示出之前被隱藏或未知的事物。"},{"en":"A blood test may reveal why a patient feels tired.","zh":"血液測試可能揭示病人為何疲倦。"},{"en":"Evidence reveals information when it makes a hidden fact visible.","zh":"當證據使隱藏事實變得可見，它就揭示資訊。"},{"en":"This word describes discovery through proof or observation.","zh":"這個字描述透過證據或觀察而發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"underwater arc","meaning":"水下弧形結構","examples":[{"en":"The surveys showed an underwater arc in the Gulf of Mexico.","zh":"勘測顯示墨西哥灣中有一個水下弧形結構。"},{"en":"An underwater arc is a curved structure or pattern beneath the water.","zh":"underwater arc 指水下的彎曲結構或模式。"},{"en":"Sonar may reveal an underwater arc on the seabed near a harbour.","zh":"聲納可能揭示港口附近海床上的水下弧形結構。"},{"en":"A curved seabed feature can suggest a buried circular structure.","zh":"彎曲海床特徵可能暗示埋藏的圓形結構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a hidden curve below the sea surface.","zh":"這個短語描述海面下隱藏的弧形。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sea-based and land-based","meaning":"海上和陸上的","examples":[{"en":"The sea-based and land-based arcs matched perfectly.","zh":"海上和陸上的弧形完全吻合。"},{"en":"Sea-based and land-based means located in the sea and on land.","zh":"sea-based and land-based 指位於海上和陸上。"},{"en":"A rescue plan may use both sea-based and land-based teams during a coastal emergency.","zh":"在沿海緊急情況中，救援計劃可能同時使用海上和陸上隊伍。"},{"en":"When features on sea and land match, they may be parts of one larger structure.","zh":"當海上和陸上的特徵吻合，它們可能是一個更大結構的部分。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two locations: ocean and land.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個位置：海洋和陸地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"matched perfectly","meaning":"完全吻合","examples":[{"en":"The two arcs matched perfectly.","zh":"兩個弧形完全吻合。"},{"en":"Matched perfectly means fitted together exactly or showed the same pattern.","zh":"matched perfectly 指精確配合或顯示相同模式。"},{"en":"Two puzzle pieces match perfectly when their edges fit without gaps.","zh":"兩塊拼圖邊緣沒有空隙地接合時，就是完全吻合。"},{"en":"Perfect matching can support the idea that two parts belong to one structure.","zh":"完全吻合可以支持兩部分屬於同一結構的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exact correspondence.","zh":"這個短語描述精確對應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a circle 180 kilometres wide","meaning":"直徑一百八十公里的圓形","examples":[{"en":"The two arcs showed a circle 180 kilometres wide.","zh":"兩個弧形顯示出一個直徑一百八十公里的圓形。"},{"en":"A circle 180 kilometres wide means a circular shape with a diameter of 180 kilometres.","zh":"a circle 180 kilometres wide 指直徑為一百八十公里的圓形。"},{"en":"A map may show a storm system as a circle hundreds of kilometres wide.","zh":"地圖可能把風暴系統顯示為直徑數百公里的圓形。"},{"en":"Such a huge circle suggests an enormous geological structure.","zh":"如此巨大的圓形暗示龐大的地質結構。"},{"en":"This phrase gives both shape and size.","zh":"這個短語同時給出形狀和大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"centred on","meaning":"以……為中心","examples":[{"en":"The circle was centred on the coastal village of Chicxulub.","zh":"這個圓形以沿海村落 Chicxulub 為中心。"},{"en":"Centred on means having its middle point at a particular place.","zh":"centred on 指中心點位於某特定地方。"},{"en":"A town festival may be centred on the main square.","zh":"城鎮節日可能以主廣場為中心。"},{"en":"When a structure is centred on a place, that place lies near its middle.","zh":"當一個結構以某地為中心，該地就位於其接近中間的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the central location of something.","zh":"這個短語指出某物的中心位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"coastal village","meaning":"沿海村落","examples":[{"en":"The crater was centred on a coastal village.","zh":"這個隕石坑以一個沿海村落為中心。"},{"en":"A coastal village is a small settlement near the sea.","zh":"coastal village 指靠近海的小型聚居地。"},{"en":"A coastal village may depend on fishing, tourism, or small boats for income.","zh":"沿海村落可能依靠捕魚、旅遊或小船維生。"},{"en":"Coastal places can be important in geology because land and sea evidence may meet there.","zh":"沿海地方在地質學中可能很重要，因為陸地和海洋證據可能在那裡相遇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both size and seaside location.","zh":"這個短語同時描述規模和海邊位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"became known as","meaning":"被稱為……","examples":[{"en":"The feature became known as the Chicxulub Crater.","zh":"這個特徵後來被稱為希克蘇魯伯隕石坑。"},{"en":"Became known as means later received or came to be recognised by a particular name.","zh":"became known as 指後來得到或被認可為某個名稱。"},{"en":"A quiet study corner may become known as the reading zone.","zh":"一個安靜自修角可能後來被稱為閱讀區。"},{"en":"Names often appear after people understand what a feature or event is.","zh":"名稱常在人們理解某特徵或事件後出現。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how something gained its name.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物如何獲得名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Chicxulub Crater","meaning":"希克蘇魯伯隕石坑","examples":[{"en":"The impact structure became known as the Chicxulub Crater.","zh":"這個撞擊結構後來被稱為希克蘇魯伯隕石坑。"},{"en":"The Chicxulub Crater is the buried impact crater linked with the KT extinction.","zh":"Chicxulub Crater 指與 K-T 滅絕相關的埋藏撞擊坑。"},{"en":"A science class may study the Chicxulub Crater to understand asteroid impacts.","zh":"科學課可能研究希克蘇魯伯隕石坑，以理解小行星撞擊。"},{"en":"Its size and age helped connect it to the mass extinction.","zh":"其大小和年代幫助把它與大滅絕連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific geological structure in Mexico.","zh":"這個短語指出墨西哥的一個特定地質結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"released their findings","meaning":"發表他們的發現","examples":[{"en":"Camargo and Penfield released their findings in 1981.","zh":"Camargo 和 Penfield 於1981年發表他們的發現。"},{"en":"Released their findings means made their research results public.","zh":"released their findings 指把研究結果公開。"},{"en":"Scientists may release their findings after other experts review the data.","zh":"科學家可能在其他專家審閱資料後發表他們的發現。"},{"en":"Public findings allow other researchers to test, challenge, or support the work.","zh":"公開發現讓其他研究者測試、挑戰或支持該研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sharing research with the wider world.","zh":"這個短語描述向外界分享研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the world was not listening","meaning":"外界沒有重視","examples":[{"en":"They released their findings, but the world was not listening.","zh":"他們發表了發現，但外界沒有重視。"},{"en":"The world was not listening means people generally ignored or failed to notice the message.","zh":"the world was not listening 指人們普遍忽視或沒有注意到該訊息。"},{"en":"A student may give a useful suggestion, but the class is not listening if everyone is distracted.","zh":"學生可能提出有用建議，但如果全班都分心，就沒有人重視。"},{"en":"Important ideas can be delayed when others do not pay attention.","zh":"當其他人不留意，重要想法可能被延誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lack of public or professional attention.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏公眾或專業關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"took over ten years","meaning":"花了十多年","examples":[{"en":"It took over ten years for scientists to begin accepting the findings.","zh":"科學家開始接受這些發現花了十多年。"},{"en":"Took over ten years means required more than ten years to happen.","zh":"took over ten years 指需要超過十年才發生。"},{"en":"It took over ten years for the old harbour to be rebuilt after the storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，重建舊港口花了十多年。"},{"en":"Long acceptance periods often show that strong evidence was needed.","zh":"長時間才被接受，常顯示需要強有力證據。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a slow process.","zh":"這個短語強調過程緩慢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"much more evidence","meaning":"更多證據","examples":[{"en":"Scientists needed much more evidence before accepting the findings.","zh":"科學家在接受這些發現前需要更多證據。"},{"en":"Much more evidence means a far larger amount of proof or support.","zh":"much more evidence 指多得多的證明或支持。"},{"en":"A teacher may need much more evidence before deciding that cheating occurred.","zh":"老師在判斷作弊發生前，可能需要更多證據。"},{"en":"Extraordinary claims often require more evidence than ordinary claims.","zh":"非比尋常的說法通常比普通說法需要更多證據。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that existing proof was not enough.","zh":"這個短語強調現有證據不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rock samples","meaning":"岩石樣本","examples":[{"en":"Rock samples helped support the impact theory.","zh":"岩石樣本幫助支持撞擊理論。"},{"en":"Rock samples are pieces of rock collected for testing or study.","zh":"rock samples 指為測試或研究而收集的岩石片段。"},{"en":"Geologists may collect rock samples from a cliff to identify minerals.","zh":"地質學家可能從峭壁收集岩石樣本，以辨認礦物。"},{"en":"Samples can reveal age, composition, heat damage, or impact evidence.","zh":"樣本可以揭示年代、成分、受熱損傷或撞擊證據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to physical rock evidence.","zh":"這個短語指實體岩石證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"drilling cores","meaning":"鑽探岩芯","examples":[{"en":"Drilling cores provided further evidence of the impact.","zh":"鑽探岩芯提供了進一步的撞擊證據。"},{"en":"Drilling cores are long cylindrical samples taken from underground or under the seabed.","zh":"drilling cores 指從地下或海床下取出的長圓柱形樣本。"},{"en":"Engineers may examine drilling cores before building a tunnel.","zh":"工程師建隧道前可能檢查鑽探岩芯。"},{"en":"Cores preserve layers in order, so scientists can study deep history.","zh":"岩芯按次序保存地層，所以科學家可以研究深層歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to evidence extracted by drilling.","zh":"這個短語指透過鑽探取得的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"dating of the seabed rocks","meaning":"海床岩石年代測定","examples":[{"en":"The dating of the seabed rocks pointed to 65 million years ago.","zh":"海床岩石年代測定指向六千五百萬年前。"},{"en":"Dating of the seabed rocks means determining the age of rocks from the ocean floor.","zh":"dating of the seabed rocks 指確定來自海床的岩石年代。"},{"en":"Scientists may date rocks to learn when a volcano erupted or a crater formed.","zh":"科學家可能測定岩石年代，以了解火山何時爆發或隕石坑何時形成。"},{"en":"If the rock age matches an extinction, the evidence becomes stronger.","zh":"如果岩石年代與滅絕事件吻合，證據就更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase connects age measurement with geological interpretation.","zh":"這個短語把年代量度與地質詮釋連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"seabed rocks","meaning":"海床岩石","examples":[{"en":"Seabed rocks helped date the crater.","zh":"海床岩石幫助測定隕石坑年代。"},{"en":"Seabed rocks are rocks found on or below the ocean floor.","zh":"seabed rocks 指在海床上或海床下發現的岩石。"},{"en":"A research ship may collect seabed rocks to study underwater volcanoes.","zh":"研究船可能收集海床岩石，以研究水下火山。"},{"en":"Rocks from the seabed can preserve evidence hidden below water.","zh":"海床岩石可以保存隱藏在水下的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes geological material from the sea floor.","zh":"這個短語描述來自海底的地質材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the magic figure of","meaning":"……這個關鍵數字","examples":[{"en":"The seabed rocks were dated to the magic figure of 65 million years.","zh":"海床岩石被測定為六千五百萬年這個關鍵數字。"},{"en":"The magic figure of a number means a number that is especially important because it matches key evidence.","zh":"the magic figure of a number 指因與關鍵證據吻合而特別重要的數字。"},{"en":"In a budget, the magic figure may be the amount needed to keep a project alive.","zh":"在預算中，關鍵數字可能是維持項目所需金額。"},{"en":"A number becomes “magic” when many clues point to it.","zh":"當多條線索都指向某數字，它就變得特別重要。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a number with special significance.","zh":"這個短語突出具有特殊意義的數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"begin accepting","meaning":"開始接受","examples":[{"en":"Scientists slowly began accepting the findings.","zh":"科學家慢慢開始接受這些發現。"},{"en":"To begin accepting something means to start believing it or treating it as likely true.","zh":"begin accepting something 指開始相信某事或把它視為可能真實。"},{"en":"A teacher may begin accepting a student’s explanation after seeing supporting messages.","zh":"老師看見支持訊息後，可能開始接受學生的解釋。"},{"en":"People often need evidence before they begin accepting a surprising claim.","zh":"人們通常需要證據，才開始接受令人驚訝的說法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gradual change in belief.","zh":"這個短語描述信念逐漸改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"widespread scepticism","meaning":"廣泛懷疑","examples":[{"en":"Widespread scepticism existed for many years.","zh":"廣泛懷疑存在了許多年。"},{"en":"Widespread scepticism means many people doubted or questioned something.","zh":"widespread scepticism 指許多人懷疑或質疑某事。"},{"en":"There may be widespread scepticism when a new school rule is announced without explanation.","zh":"如果新校規沒有解釋便宣布，可能出現廣泛懷疑。"},{"en":"Scepticism can slow acceptance until evidence becomes stronger.","zh":"懷疑可以減慢接受過程，直到證據變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad doubt among many people.","zh":"這個短語描述許多人之間的廣泛疑慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"to some extent","meaning":"在某程度上","examples":[{"en":"To some extent, scepticism remains today.","zh":"在某程度上，懷疑至今仍然存在。"},{"en":"To some extent means partly, but not completely.","zh":"to some extent 指部分地，但不是完全地。"},{"en":"To some extent, online lessons help shy students because they can type answers.","zh":"在某程度上，網上課堂幫助害羞學生，因為他們可以打字回答。"},{"en":"This phrase softens a statement by showing it is only partly true.","zh":"這個短語透過顯示某事只部分屬實來緩和說法。"},{"en":"It is useful when the situation is mixed rather than absolute.","zh":"當情況混合而非絕對時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"remains today","meaning":"至今仍然存在","examples":[{"en":"Some scepticism remains today.","zh":"有些懷疑至今仍然存在。"},{"en":"Remains today means still exists in the present.","zh":"remains today 指到現在仍然存在。"},{"en":"The old school building remains today, although many classrooms have changed.","zh":"舊校舍至今仍然存在，雖然許多課室已改變。"},{"en":"Some ideas remain today because not everyone accepts the same evidence.","zh":"有些想法至今仍然存在，因為不是每個人都接受同一證據。"},{"en":"This phrase links the past with the present.","zh":"這個短語把過去與現在連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"it is occasionally argued that","meaning":"偶爾有人主張","examples":[{"en":"It is occasionally argued that the impact was not the sole cause.","zh":"偶爾有人主張撞擊並非唯一原因。"},{"en":"It is occasionally argued that means some people sometimes make this argument.","zh":"it is occasionally argued that 指有些人有時提出這個論點。"},{"en":"It is occasionally argued that homework should be optional, though many teachers disagree.","zh":"偶爾有人主張功課應該自願完成，雖然許多老師不同意。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a minority or less frequent opinion.","zh":"這個短語引出少數或較不常見的意見。"},{"en":"It signals that the writer is reporting an argument, not necessarily agreeing with it.","zh":"它表示作者在報告一個論點，不一定同意它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sole reason","meaning":"唯一原因","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists argued that the impact was not the sole reason.","zh":"有些科學家認為撞擊不是唯一原因。"},{"en":"Sole reason means the only cause or explanation.","zh":"sole reason 指唯一原因或解釋。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep may not be the sole reason for poor exam results.","zh":"睡眠不足未必是考試成績差的唯一原因。"},{"en":"Complex problems often have several causes rather than one sole reason.","zh":"複雜問題通常有幾個原因，而不是一個唯一原因。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses exclusiveness: one reason and no others.","zh":"這個短語強調排他性：只有一個原因，沒有其他原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"contemporaneous impacts","meaning":"同時期的撞擊","examples":[{"en":"Some suggested that there were other contemporaneous impacts.","zh":"有些人提出可能還有其他同時期的撞擊。"},{"en":"Contemporaneous impacts are impacts that happened around the same time.","zh":"contemporaneous impacts 指在大約同一時期發生的撞擊。"},{"en":"Two accidents on the same road during the same storm may be contemporaneous events.","zh":"同一場暴風雨期間同一路上發生的兩宗事故，可以是同時期事件。"},{"en":"If several impacts occurred together, they could have combined effects.","zh":"如果幾次撞擊同時期發生，它們可能產生綜合影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes events sharing the same time period.","zh":"這個短語描述發生於同一時段的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"extensive volcanism","meaning":"大規模火山活動","examples":[{"en":"Extensive volcanism may also have contributed to the extinction.","zh":"大規模火山活動也可能促成滅絕。"},{"en":"Extensive volcanism means large-scale volcanic activity across a region or period.","zh":"extensive volcanism 指在某地區或時期內的大規模火山活動。"},{"en":"A science lesson may discuss extensive volcanism when many eruptions affect climate.","zh":"當許多火山爆發影響氣候，科學課可能討論大規模火山活動。"},{"en":"Volcanism can release gases and ash that change air and temperature.","zh":"火山活動可以釋放氣體和灰燼，改變空氣和溫度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes volcanic activity that is broad and significant.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛而重大的火山活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"climate and sea-level change","meaning":"氣候及海平面變化","examples":[{"en":"Climate and sea-level change were proposed as possible causes.","zh":"氣候及海平面變化被提出為可能原因。"},{"en":"Climate and sea-level change means changes in weather patterns and ocean height over time.","zh":"climate and sea-level change 指天氣模式和海洋高度隨時間出現變化。"},{"en":"Coastal towns worry about sea-level change because flooding may become more common.","zh":"沿海城鎮擔心海平面變化，因為水浸可能變得更常見。"},{"en":"Climate change can affect food, habitats, and survival conditions.","zh":"氣候變化可以影響食物、棲息地和生存條件。"},{"en":"This phrase names environmental changes that can affect life widely.","zh":"這個短語指出可廣泛影響生命的環境變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"real causes","meaning":"真正原因","examples":[{"en":"Some argued that volcanism or climate change were the real causes.","zh":"有些人認為火山活動或氣候變化才是真正原因。"},{"en":"Real causes are the true reasons behind an event, not just possible or surface explanations.","zh":"real causes 指事件背後的真正理由，而不只是可能或表面解釋。"},{"en":"If students are often late, the real causes may include transport problems or family duties.","zh":"如果學生經常遲到，真正原因可能包括交通問題或家庭責任。"},{"en":"Identifying real causes helps people avoid blaming the wrong thing.","zh":"找出真正原因有助人們避免責怪錯誤對象。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the actual explanation.","zh":"這個短語集中於實際解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"led to","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"The ongoing debate led to an international panel being convened.","zh":"持續爭論導致一個國際專家小組被召集。"},{"en":"Led to means caused something to happen as a result.","zh":"led to 指造成某事作為結果發生。"},{"en":"Repeated complaints led to a school meeting about lunch quality.","zh":"反覆投訴導致學校召開關於午餐質素的會議。"},{"en":"A debate can lead to action when people need a clear decision.","zh":"當人們需要明確決定，爭論可以導致行動。"},{"en":"This phrase connects one situation with the result it produced.","zh":"這個短語把一個情況與其產生的結果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"international panel","meaning":"國際專家小組","examples":[{"en":"An international panel of over 40 scientists examined the evidence.","zh":"一個由四十多名科學家組成的國際專家小組檢視了證據。"},{"en":"An international panel is a group of experts from different countries who review an issue.","zh":"international panel 指由來自不同國家的專家組成、審視某議題的小組。"},{"en":"An international panel may study climate data before giving policy advice.","zh":"國際專家小組可能研究氣候資料，然後提供政策建議。"},{"en":"Panels combine expertise so that a conclusion is not based on one person only.","zh":"專家小組結合專業知識，使結論不只基於一個人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a formal expert group with global membership.","zh":"這個短語描述具有全球成員的正式專家組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"being convened","meaning":"被召集","examples":[{"en":"The panel was convened to address the evidence.","zh":"該小組被召集來處理證據。"},{"en":"Being convened means being formally brought together for a meeting or purpose.","zh":"being convened 指為會議或目的而被正式召集在一起。"},{"en":"A school committee may be convened after a serious safety problem.","zh":"發生嚴重安全問題後，學校委員會可能被召集。"},{"en":"Groups are convened when a decision requires discussion by several people.","zh":"當一項決定需要多人討論，群體就會被召集。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal gathering for a task.","zh":"這個短語描述為任務而正式聚集。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in order to","meaning":"為了……","examples":[{"en":"The panel was convened in order to address the evidence.","zh":"該小組被召集，是為了處理證據。"},{"en":"In order to means for the purpose of doing something.","zh":"in order to 指為了做某事。"},{"en":"Students practise speaking in order to become more confident in interviews.","zh":"學生練習說話，是為了在面試中更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links an action with its purpose.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接行動與目的。"},{"en":"It is useful in formal explanation.","zh":"它適合用於正式解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"specifically address","meaning":"專門處理；專門審視","examples":[{"en":"The scientists were convened to specifically address the evidence.","zh":"科學家被召集來專門審視證據。"},{"en":"To specifically address something means to deal directly with that particular issue.","zh":"specifically address something 指直接處理某一特定問題。"},{"en":"A teacher may specifically address grammar mistakes after seeing them in many essays.","zh":"老師在許多作文中看見文法錯誤後，可能專門處理這些錯誤。"},{"en":"Focusing on one issue helps avoid vague discussion.","zh":"集中於一個議題有助避免空泛討論。"},{"en":"This phrase shows targeted attention.","zh":"這個短語顯示有針對性的關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the evidence","meaning":"證據","examples":[{"en":"The panel examined the evidence for the impact theory.","zh":"專家小組檢視了支持撞擊理論的證據。"},{"en":"The evidence means the facts, data, or signs used to support a claim.","zh":"the evidence 指用來支持某說法的事實、資料或跡象。"},{"en":"A teacher should check the evidence before accepting an excuse for missing homework.","zh":"老師在接受欠交功課的藉口前，應檢查證據。"},{"en":"Strong evidence makes an argument more convincing.","zh":"強證據令論點更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to proof, not personal opinion.","zh":"這個短語指證明，而不是個人意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"concluded that","meaning":"得出結論認為","examples":[{"en":"The scientists concluded that an asteroid impact caused the extinction.","zh":"科學家得出結論認為小行星撞擊造成了滅絕。"},{"en":"Concluded that means reached a final judgement after considering evidence.","zh":"concluded that 指考慮證據後得出最終判斷。"},{"en":"A doctor may conclude that a patient needs rest after reviewing test results.","zh":"醫生查看測試結果後，可能得出結論認為病人需要休息。"},{"en":"Conclusions are stronger when they are based on several kinds of evidence.","zh":"當結論基於多種證據，它會更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a reasoned decision.","zh":"這個短語引出有根據的決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"asteroid impact","meaning":"小行星撞擊","examples":[{"en":"The panel concluded that an asteroid impact caused the mass extinction.","zh":"專家小組得出結論，認為小行星撞擊造成大滅絕。"},{"en":"An asteroid impact is a collision between an asteroid and a planet or moon.","zh":"asteroid impact 指小行星與行星或月球之間的碰撞。"},{"en":"A science video may show an asteroid impact creating a crater.","zh":"科學影片可能展示小行星撞擊形成隕石坑。"},{"en":"Large impacts can release heat, dust, shock waves, and global environmental changes.","zh":"大型撞擊可以釋放熱力、塵埃、衝擊波和全球環境變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a space object striking a large body.","zh":"這個短語描述太空物體撞擊大型天體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as evidenced by","meaning":"正如……所證明","examples":[{"en":"The impact was evidenced by the Chicxulub Crater.","zh":"正如希克蘇魯伯隕石坑所證明，撞擊確實存在。"},{"en":"As evidenced by means as shown or supported by this evidence.","zh":"as evidenced by 指正如某證據所顯示或支持。"},{"en":"The student worked hard, as evidenced by detailed notes and corrected drafts.","zh":"正如詳細筆記和修改稿所證明，學生很努力。"},{"en":"This phrase links a claim to proof that supports it.","zh":"這個短語把說法與支持它的證據連起來。"},{"en":"It is formal and common in academic writing.","zh":"它較正式，常見於學術寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"indeed the cause of","meaning":"確實是……的原因","examples":[{"en":"The asteroid impact was indeed the cause of the mass extinction.","zh":"小行星撞擊確實是大滅絕的原因。"},{"en":"Indeed the cause of means truly or certainly the reason behind something.","zh":"indeed the cause of 指真正或確定是某事背後的原因。"},{"en":"After checking the pipes, the plumber found that a leak was indeed the cause of the wet floor.","zh":"水喉工檢查水管後，發現漏水確實是地板濕的原因。"},{"en":"This phrase confirms a cause after doubt or debate.","zh":"這個短語在懷疑或爭論後確認原因。"},{"en":"It adds emphasis to a conclusion.","zh":"它為結論加強語氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"trying to picture","meaning":"嘗試想像","examples":[{"en":"Trying to picture that event strains the imagination.","zh":"嘗試想像那次事件令人難以想像。"},{"en":"Trying to picture something means trying to imagine what it looked or felt like.","zh":"trying to picture something 指嘗試想像某事看起來或感覺如何。"},{"en":"Students may try to picture life before smartphones by asking grandparents for stories.","zh":"學生可能透過向祖父母詢問故事，嘗試想像智能手機出現前的生活。"},{"en":"Huge or unfamiliar events can be difficult to picture clearly.","zh":"巨大或陌生事件可能難以清楚想像。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental visualisation.","zh":"這個短語描述在腦中視覺化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the most powerful ever","meaning":"有史以來最強大的","examples":[{"en":"The impact was the most powerful event ever in Earth’s history.","zh":"這次撞擊是地球歷史上有史以來最強大的事件。"},{"en":"The most powerful ever means stronger than all others before or after it in the comparison.","zh":"the most powerful ever 指在比較中比之前或之後所有其他事件都強。"},{"en":"A storm may be described as the most powerful ever recorded in a region.","zh":"一場風暴可能被描述為某地區有記錄以來最強大的風暴。"},{"en":"Such a phrase is used only when the scale is extreme.","zh":"只有當規模極端時，才會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It stresses record-breaking force.","zh":"它強調破紀錄的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Earth’s history","meaning":"地球歷史","examples":[{"en":"The impact was one of the most dramatic events in Earth’s history.","zh":"這次撞擊是地球歷史中最劇烈的事件之一。"},{"en":"Earth’s history means the long record of events that have happened to the planet.","zh":"Earth’s history 指地球曾經發生的漫長事件記錄。"},{"en":"A science textbook may divide Earth’s history into geological periods.","zh":"科學教科書可能把地球歷史分成不同地質時期。"},{"en":"Rocks, fossils, and craters help scientists read Earth’s history.","zh":"岩石、化石和隕石坑幫助科學家閱讀地球歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the planet’s past, not human history only.","zh":"這個短語指地球的過去，而不只是人類歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"strains the imagination","meaning":"令人難以想像","examples":[{"en":"The power of the impact strains the imagination.","zh":"這次撞擊的力量令人難以想像。"},{"en":"Strains the imagination means is so extreme that it is difficult to imagine.","zh":"strains the imagination 指極端到難以想像。"},{"en":"The size of the universe strains the imagination because ordinary distances feel too small.","zh":"宇宙的大小令人難以想像，因為普通距離顯得太小。"},{"en":"Very large numbers or disasters can make the mind struggle to picture them.","zh":"非常巨大的數字或災難會令人難以在腦中描繪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something almost beyond mental grasp.","zh":"這個短語描述幾乎超出想像能力的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"begins with","meaning":"以……開始","examples":[{"en":"The event begins with a huge rock appearing from nowhere.","zh":"這次事件以一塊巨大岩石突然出現開始。"},{"en":"Begins with means starts with a particular action, scene, or situation.","zh":"begins with 指以某行動、場景或情況作開始。"},{"en":"A good lesson may begin with a simple question that makes students curious.","zh":"好課堂可能以一條簡單問題開始，令學生好奇。"},{"en":"How something begins can shape how people understand the whole event.","zh":"某事如何開始會影響人們如何理解整個事件。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the first stage.","zh":"這個短語引出第一階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"10–15-kilometre-wide rock","meaning":"闊十至十五公里的岩石","examples":[{"en":"The event began with a 10–15-kilometre-wide rock striking Earth.","zh":"這次事件始於一塊闊十至十五公里的岩石撞擊地球。"},{"en":"A 10–15-kilometre-wide rock is an enormous rock with a width of ten to fifteen kilometres.","zh":"10–15-kilometre-wide rock 指寬度達十至十五公里的巨大岩石。"},{"en":"A city map helps students imagine how huge a ten-kilometre object would be.","zh":"城市地圖可以幫助學生想像十公里大的物體有多巨大。"},{"en":"Such a large object would carry immense energy if moving at high speed.","zh":"如此大型物體若高速移動，會帶有巨大能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the size of the impact object.","zh":"這個短語描述撞擊物體的尺寸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"appearing from nowhere","meaning":"突然出現；不知從何而來","examples":[{"en":"The rock seemed to appear from nowhere.","zh":"那塊岩石似乎突然出現。"},{"en":"Appearing from nowhere means suddenly becoming visible without warning.","zh":"appearing from nowhere 指毫無預警地突然變得可見。"},{"en":"A cyclist may appear from nowhere if a driver is not checking side streets.","zh":"如果司機沒有留意橫街，單車手可能突然出現。"},{"en":"Sudden appearance can make an event feel shocking and unavoidable.","zh":"突然出現會令事件感覺震撼且難以避免。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unexpected arrival.","zh":"這個短語描述意外到來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"almost instantaneously","meaning":"幾乎瞬間","examples":[{"en":"The rock almost instantaneously vaporised.","zh":"那塊岩石幾乎瞬間氣化。"},{"en":"Almost instantaneously means almost immediately, with almost no delay.","zh":"almost instantaneously 指幾乎立即，幾乎沒有延遲。"},{"en":"A message can arrive almost instantaneously on a phone.","zh":"手機訊息可以幾乎瞬間到達。"},{"en":"Extreme heat can cause water droplets to disappear almost instantaneously.","zh":"極端高溫可以令水滴幾乎瞬間消失。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses very rapid timing.","zh":"這個短語強調非常快速的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"releasing over","meaning":"釋放超過……","examples":[{"en":"The impact released over two million times the energy of an atomic bomb.","zh":"這次撞擊釋放出超過一枚原子彈二百萬倍的能量。"},{"en":"Releasing over a number means giving off more than that amount.","zh":"releasing over a number 指釋放出多於某數量。"},{"en":"A factory may release over the legal limit of smoke if filters fail.","zh":"如果過濾器失效，工廠可能釋放超過法定上限的煙。"},{"en":"Energy release can cause heat, shock waves, and destruction.","zh":"能量釋放可以造成熱力、衝擊波和破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an amount greater than a stated figure.","zh":"這個短語引出高於某數字的分量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"two million times the energy of","meaning":"……能量的二百萬倍","examples":[{"en":"The impact released two million times the energy of an atomic bomb.","zh":"這次撞擊釋放出一枚原子彈能量的二百萬倍。"},{"en":"Two million times the energy of something means energy two million times greater than that reference point.","zh":"two million times the energy of something 指能量是某參照物的二百萬倍。"},{"en":"A comparison like this helps readers understand an otherwise unimaginable scale.","zh":"這類比較幫助讀者理解原本難以想像的規模。"},{"en":"Very large comparisons show that ordinary examples are too small.","zh":"非常巨大的比較顯示普通例子太小。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses extreme magnitude through comparison.","zh":"這個短語透過比較表達極端規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"atomic bomb","meaning":"原子彈","examples":[{"en":"The impact released far more energy than an atomic bomb.","zh":"這次撞擊釋放的能量遠超一枚原子彈。"},{"en":"An atomic bomb is a powerful nuclear weapon that releases enormous energy.","zh":"atomic bomb 指釋放巨大能量的核武器。"},{"en":"History lessons may mention atomic bombs when discussing twentieth-century warfare.","zh":"歷史課討論二十世紀戰爭時可能提到原子彈。"},{"en":"Comparing an impact with an atomic bomb helps show how destructive it was.","zh":"把撞擊與原子彈比較，有助顯示其破壞力有多大。"},{"en":"This phrase is used as a reference point for extreme energy.","zh":"這個短語常用作極端能量的參照點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"immediate effect","meaning":"即時影響","examples":[{"en":"The immediate effect was a cloud of superheated dust, ash and steam.","zh":"即時影響是一團過熱塵埃、灰燼和蒸汽。"},{"en":"Immediate effect means the result that happens right away.","zh":"immediate effect 指立刻發生的結果。"},{"en":"The immediate effect of turning off the lights is that the room becomes dark.","zh":"關燈的即時影響是房間變暗。"},{"en":"Immediate effects appear before slower, long-term consequences.","zh":"即時影響出現在較慢的長期後果之前。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the first result after an event.","zh":"這個短語指出事件後的第一個結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"superheated dust","meaning":"過熱塵埃","examples":[{"en":"A cloud of superheated dust expanded outwards.","zh":"一團過熱塵埃向外擴散。"},{"en":"Superheated dust is dust heated to an extremely high temperature.","zh":"superheated dust 指被加熱到極高溫的塵埃。"},{"en":"Hot ash from a fire can burn skin because tiny particles carry heat.","zh":"火災中的熱灰可以灼傷皮膚，因為微粒帶有熱力。"},{"en":"Superheated material can ignite fires when it spreads through the air.","zh":"過熱物質在空氣中擴散時可以引發火災。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dust made dangerously hot.","zh":"這個短語描述變得危險高溫的塵埃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ash and steam","meaning":"灰燼和蒸汽","examples":[{"en":"The impact produced dust, ash and steam.","zh":"這次撞擊產生塵埃、灰燼和蒸汽。"},{"en":"Ash and steam are burnt particles and hot water vapour.","zh":"ash and steam 指燃燒後的微粒和熱水蒸氣。"},{"en":"A volcanic eruption can send ash and steam high into the sky.","zh":"火山爆發可以把灰燼和蒸汽送上高空。"},{"en":"Ash can block light, while steam shows that water or wet rock has been heated.","zh":"灰燼可以阻擋光線，而蒸汽顯示水或潮濕岩石被加熱。"},{"en":"This phrase names materials produced by heat and explosion.","zh":"這個短語指出由熱力和爆炸產生的物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"expanding outwards","meaning":"向外擴散","examples":[{"en":"The cloud expanded outwards from the impact site.","zh":"這團雲從撞擊地點向外擴散。"},{"en":"Expanding outwards means spreading away from the centre in all directions.","zh":"expanding outwards 指從中心向各方向擴散。"},{"en":"Smoke from a fire may expand outwards through a hallway.","zh":"火災煙霧可能沿走廊向外擴散。"},{"en":"Outward expansion can make damage spread beyond the original location.","zh":"向外擴散可以令破壞超出原本地點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement away from a central point.","zh":"這個短語描述離開中心點的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"igniting fires","meaning":"引發火災","examples":[{"en":"The impact cloud ignited fires.","zh":"撞擊雲引發火災。"},{"en":"Igniting fires means starting fires, usually through heat, sparks, or flames.","zh":"igniting fires 指通常透過熱力、火花或火焰引起火災。"},{"en":"A dropped cigarette can ignite a fire in dry grass.","zh":"掉落的香煙可以在乾草中引發火災。"},{"en":"When many fires ignite at once, damage spreads quickly.","zh":"當許多火災同時引發，破壞會迅速擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of burning.","zh":"這個短語描述燃燒的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"broiling everything","meaning":"灼燒一切","examples":[{"en":"The superheated cloud broiled everything in its path.","zh":"過熱雲灼燒其路徑上的一切。"},{"en":"Broiling everything means burning or intensely heating everything nearby.","zh":"broiling everything 指灼燒或極度加熱附近一切。"},{"en":"Food left too close to a strong grill may be broiled until it burns.","zh":"食物放得太近強力烤爐，可能被烤到燒焦。"},{"en":"Extreme heat can destroy living things before flames even reach them.","zh":"極端高溫即使在火焰到達前，也能摧毀生物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severe heat damage.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重熱力傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in its path","meaning":"在其路徑上的","examples":[{"en":"The cloud destroyed everything in its path.","zh":"這團雲摧毀在其路徑上的一切。"},{"en":"In its path means in the direction where it is moving.","zh":"in its path 指在某物移動方向上的位置。"},{"en":"A falling tree can damage anything in its path.","zh":"倒下的樹可以損壞在其路徑上的任何東西。"},{"en":"Things in a moving force’s path are most likely to be hit or destroyed.","zh":"位於移動力量路徑上的東西最可能被撞擊或摧毀。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the area directly affected by movement.","zh":"這個短語指出直接受移動影響的範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a series of shock waves","meaning":"一連串衝擊波","examples":[{"en":"A series of shock waves followed a split second later.","zh":"瞬間之後，一連串衝擊波接着出現。"},{"en":"A series of shock waves means several powerful waves of pressure moving through air, water, or ground.","zh":"a series of shock waves 指幾道強大壓力波穿過空氣、水或地面。"},{"en":"An explosion can create shock waves that break windows nearby.","zh":"爆炸可以產生衝擊波，震碎附近窗戶。"},{"en":"Shock waves can carry destructive force far from the original blast.","zh":"衝擊波可以把破壞力帶到遠離原本爆炸的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated waves of sudden pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述重複出現的突然壓力波。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"split second later","meaning":"瞬間之後","examples":[{"en":"The shock waves followed a split second later.","zh":"衝擊波在瞬間之後接着出現。"},{"en":"A split second later means almost immediately after something happens.","zh":"split second later 指某事發生後幾乎立即。"},{"en":"The glass fell, and a split second later it shattered on the floor.","zh":"玻璃杯掉下來，瞬間之後在地上碎裂。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an extremely short time gap.","zh":"這個短語顯示極短時間間隔。"},{"en":"It is useful when events happen almost together.","zh":"當事件幾乎同時發生時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"travelling across","meaning":"橫越……","examples":[{"en":"Shock waves travelled across the surface of the globe.","zh":"衝擊波橫越地球表面。"},{"en":"Travelling across means moving over a wide area from one side to another.","zh":"travelling across 指在廣闊範圍內從一邊移動到另一邊。"},{"en":"News can travel across a school quickly when students share messages.","zh":"當學生分享訊息，消息可以很快傳遍學校。"},{"en":"A wave travelling across a surface can affect places far from its origin.","zh":"橫越表面的波可以影響遠離源頭的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement over distance.","zh":"這個短語描述跨距離移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"surface of the globe","meaning":"地球表面","examples":[{"en":"The shock waves travelled across the surface of the globe.","zh":"衝擊波橫越地球表面。"},{"en":"The surface of the globe means the outer surface of Earth.","zh":"surface of the globe 指地球的外部表面。"},{"en":"Maps show the surface of the globe as countries, oceans, mountains, and deserts.","zh":"地圖把地球表面顯示為國家、海洋、山脈和沙漠。"},{"en":"Events affecting the surface of the globe can spread across continents and oceans.","zh":"影響地球表面的事件可以跨越大陸和海洋擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes Earth’s outer visible layer.","zh":"這個短語描述地球外部可見層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"triggering earthquakes","meaning":"引發地震","examples":[{"en":"The shock waves triggered earthquakes.","zh":"衝擊波引發地震。"},{"en":"Triggering earthquakes means causing earthquakes to start.","zh":"triggering earthquakes 指造成地震開始。"},{"en":"Heavy construction rarely triggers earthquakes, but it can cause small vibrations.","zh":"大型工程很少引發地震，但可能造成小震動。"},{"en":"Powerful forces can disturb the ground and set off movement along faults.","zh":"強大力量可以擾動地面並觸發斷層移動。"},{"en":"This phrase links an outside force with the start of earthquakes.","zh":"這個短語把外部力量與地震開始連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"volcanic eruptions","meaning":"火山爆發","examples":[{"en":"The impact triggered earthquakes and volcanic eruptions.","zh":"這次撞擊引發地震和火山爆發。"},{"en":"Volcanic eruptions are events in which lava, ash, or gases burst from a volcano.","zh":"volcanic eruptions 指熔岩、灰燼或氣體從火山噴出的事件。"},{"en":"A volcanic eruption can force nearby residents to leave their homes.","zh":"火山爆發可以迫使附近居民離開家園。"},{"en":"Eruptions can affect air quality, farming, travel, and climate.","zh":"火山爆發可以影響空氣質素、農業、交通和氣候。"},{"en":"This phrase describes major volcanic activity.","zh":"這個短語描述重大火山活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"mega-tsunami","meaning":"超級海嘯","examples":[{"en":"A mega-tsunami followed the impact.","zh":"撞擊後出現超級海嘯。"},{"en":"A mega-tsunami is an extremely large tsunami caused by a massive disturbance.","zh":"mega-tsunami 指由巨大擾動造成的極大型海嘯。"},{"en":"A landslide into a lake can create a local wave, but a mega-tsunami is far larger.","zh":"山泥傾瀉入湖可以造成局部巨浪，但超級海嘯大得多。"},{"en":"Mega-tsunamis can destroy coastlines because the water rises and moves with huge force.","zh":"超級海嘯可以摧毀海岸線，因為海水以巨大力量上升和移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a tsunami of extraordinary scale.","zh":"這個短語描述規模非比尋常的海嘯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"thousands of metres high","meaning":"高達數千米","examples":[{"en":"The mega-tsunami was thousands of metres high.","zh":"超級海嘯高達數千米。"},{"en":"Thousands of metres high means reaching several thousand metres in height.","zh":"thousands of metres high 指高度達數千米。"},{"en":"A mountain thousands of metres high can be covered with snow even in warm regions.","zh":"高達數千米的山即使在溫暖地區也可能覆蓋積雪。"},{"en":"Such height is used to show an almost unimaginable scale.","zh":"這種高度用來顯示幾乎難以想像的規模。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extreme vertical size.","zh":"這個短語描述極端垂直高度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ripping coastlines apart","meaning":"撕裂海岸線","examples":[{"en":"The mega-tsunami ripped coastlines apart.","zh":"超級海嘯撕裂海岸線。"},{"en":"Ripping coastlines apart means violently tearing and destroying coastal areas.","zh":"ripping coastlines apart 指猛烈撕裂並摧毀沿海地區。"},{"en":"A strong storm can rip apart a weak seaside wall.","zh":"強烈風暴可以撕裂脆弱的海邊牆。"},{"en":"Powerful waves can remove beaches, trees, houses, and roads.","zh":"強大海浪可以移走沙灘、樹木、房屋和道路。"},{"en":"This phrase describes violent destruction along the shore.","zh":"這個短語描述沿岸的猛烈破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"stirring up the oceans","meaning":"攪動海洋","examples":[{"en":"The tsunami stirred up the oceans.","zh":"海嘯攪動海洋。"},{"en":"Stirring up the oceans means violently disturbing ocean water and sediment.","zh":"stirring up the oceans 指猛烈擾動海水和沉積物。"},{"en":"A child stirring soup makes the liquid and ingredients move around.","zh":"孩子攪拌湯時，液體和材料會四處移動。"},{"en":"Huge waves can stir up the seabed and make water muddy and chaotic.","zh":"巨浪可以攪動海床，使海水變得混濁混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong disturbance in the sea.","zh":"這個短語描述海洋中的強烈擾動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"huge amounts of","meaning":"大量的……","examples":[{"en":"The impact released huge amounts of carbon dioxide.","zh":"這次撞擊釋放大量二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Huge amounts of something means very large quantities of it.","zh":"huge amounts of something 指非常大的數量。"},{"en":"A busy restaurant may throw away huge amounts of food if it plans badly.","zh":"如果規劃不善，繁忙餐廳可能丟棄大量食物。"},{"en":"Huge amounts of gas or dust can change the environment quickly.","zh":"大量氣體或塵埃可以快速改變環境。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses quantity.","zh":"這個短語強調數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"carbon dioxide","meaning":"二氧化碳","examples":[{"en":"Carbon dioxide from vaporised rock heated the Earth.","zh":"氣化岩石釋放出的二氧化碳使地球升溫。"},{"en":"Carbon dioxide is a gas that can trap heat in the atmosphere.","zh":"carbon dioxide 指能在大氣中留住熱力的氣體。"},{"en":"Cars, factories, and fires can release carbon dioxide.","zh":"汽車、工廠和火災都可以釋放二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Extra carbon dioxide can affect climate by increasing heat retention.","zh":"額外二氧化碳可以透過增加熱量保留而影響氣候。"},{"en":"This phrase names an important atmospheric gas.","zh":"這個短語指出一種重要大氣氣體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"vaporisation of carbonate rock","meaning":"碳酸鹽岩的氣化","examples":[{"en":"The vaporisation of carbonate rock released carbon dioxide.","zh":"碳酸鹽岩的氣化釋放了二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Vaporisation of carbonate rock means carbonate rock was heated so strongly that it turned into gas and released material.","zh":"vaporisation of carbonate rock 指碳酸鹽岩被強烈加熱，變成氣體並釋放物質。"},{"en":"In a lab, intense heat can change some solids into vapour.","zh":"在實驗室中，強熱可以把某些固體變成蒸氣。"},{"en":"When carbonate rocks vaporise, carbon dioxide can be released into the air.","zh":"當碳酸鹽岩氣化，二氧化碳可以被釋放到空氣中。"},{"en":"This phrase links extreme heat with gas release.","zh":"這個短語把極端熱力與氣體釋放連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"carbonate rock","meaning":"碳酸鹽岩","examples":[{"en":"Carbonate rock released carbon dioxide when vaporised.","zh":"碳酸鹽岩氣化時釋放二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Carbonate rock is rock containing carbonate minerals, often formed from ancient marine material.","zh":"carbonate rock 指含有碳酸鹽礦物的岩石，常由古代海洋物質形成。"},{"en":"Limestone is a common type of carbonate rock.","zh":"石灰岩是一種常見碳酸鹽岩。"},{"en":"Carbonate rocks can release carbon dioxide under extreme heat.","zh":"碳酸鹽岩在極端高溫下可以釋放二氧化碳。"},{"en":"This phrase names a type of rock important in the impact story.","zh":"這個短語指出撞擊故事中重要的一類岩石。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"heat the Earth","meaning":"使地球升溫","examples":[{"en":"Carbon dioxide from the impact heated the Earth.","zh":"撞擊釋放的二氧化碳使地球升溫。"},{"en":"To heat the Earth means to raise the planet’s temperature.","zh":"heat the Earth 指提高地球溫度。"},{"en":"A greenhouse traps heat and warms the plants inside.","zh":"溫室會困住熱力，使裡面的植物變暖。"},{"en":"Gases that trap heat can make the planet warmer over time.","zh":"能困住熱力的氣體可以隨時間使地球升溫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes global warming caused by heat-trapping effects.","zh":"這個短語描述由保熱效應造成的全球升溫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"choked with dust","meaning":"被塵埃充塞","examples":[{"en":"The atmosphere was choked with dust for years.","zh":"大氣層多年來被塵埃充塞。"},{"en":"Choked with dust means filled so heavily with dust that normal conditions are blocked or harmed.","zh":"choked with dust 指充滿大量塵埃，以致正常狀況被阻礙或受損。"},{"en":"A classroom can feel choked with dust after old cupboards are moved.","zh":"搬動舊櫃後，課室可能感覺被塵埃充塞。"},{"en":"Dust-filled air can block light and make breathing difficult.","zh":"充滿塵埃的空氣可以阻擋光線並令人呼吸困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extreme dust pollution.","zh":"這個短語描述極端塵埃污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"sunlight is blocked","meaning":"陽光被阻擋","examples":[{"en":"Sunlight was blocked by dust in the atmosphere.","zh":"陽光被大氣中的塵埃阻擋。"},{"en":"Sunlight is blocked means light from the Sun is prevented from reaching a place.","zh":"sunlight is blocked 指太陽光被阻止到達某地方。"},{"en":"Thick curtains block sunlight and make a room darker.","zh":"厚窗簾會阻擋陽光，使房間變暗。"},{"en":"If sunlight is blocked for a long time, plants cannot photosynthesise properly.","zh":"如果陽光長時間被阻擋，植物就不能正常進行光合作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a barrier between sunlight and the surface.","zh":"這個短語描述陽光與表面之間出現阻隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"killing off plants","meaning":"使植物大量死亡","examples":[{"en":"The lack of sunlight killed off plants.","zh":"缺乏陽光使植物大量死亡。"},{"en":"Killing off plants means causing many plants to die.","zh":"killing off plants 指導致大量植物死亡。"},{"en":"A garden may lose vegetables if frost kills off young plants overnight.","zh":"如果霜凍一夜之間殺死幼苗，菜園可能失去蔬菜。"},{"en":"When plants die, animals depending on them also lose food.","zh":"當植物死亡，依賴植物的動物也會失去食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes widespread plant death.","zh":"這個短語描述植物大範圍死亡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"ultimately plunging","meaning":"最終令……陷入","examples":[{"en":"The blocked sunlight ultimately plunged the Earth into winter.","zh":"陽光被阻擋最終令地球陷入寒冬。"},{"en":"Ultimately plunging means finally causing a sudden fall into a bad condition.","zh":"ultimately plunging 指最終導致突然陷入糟糕狀況。"},{"en":"Repeated overspending can ultimately plunge a small business into debt.","zh":"反覆超支可以最終令小企業陷入債務。"},{"en":"“Ultimately” shows the final result after earlier steps.","zh":"“ultimately” 顯示較早步驟之後的最終結果。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a process with a severe final outcome.","zh":"這個短語把過程與嚴重最終後果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"plunged the Earth into winter","meaning":"令地球陷入寒冬","examples":[{"en":"The impact plunged the Earth into winter.","zh":"這次撞擊令地球陷入寒冬。"},{"en":"Plunged the Earth into winter means suddenly made the planet cold and dark like a long winter.","zh":"plunged the Earth into winter 指突然使地球變得寒冷陰暗，如同漫長冬天。"},{"en":"A power failure can plunge a building into darkness.","zh":"停電可以令建築物陷入黑暗。"},{"en":"Dust blocking sunlight can lower temperatures and disrupt plant growth.","zh":"塵埃阻擋陽光可以降低溫度並破壞植物生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sudden global shift into cold conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述全球突然轉入寒冷狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"entire biosphere","meaning":"整個生物圈","examples":[{"en":"The event threw the entire biosphere into chaos.","zh":"這次事件令整個生物圈陷入混亂。"},{"en":"The entire biosphere means all living things and ecosystems on Earth.","zh":"entire biosphere 指地球上所有生物和生態系統。"},{"en":"A major environmental disaster can affect the biosphere by harming plants, animals, and habitats.","zh":"重大環境災難可以透過傷害植物、動物和棲息地來影響生物圈。"},{"en":"When the biosphere is disrupted, food chains can collapse.","zh":"當生物圈受破壞，食物鏈可能崩潰。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the whole living system of the planet.","zh":"這個短語指地球整個生命系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"absolute chaos","meaning":"徹底混亂","examples":[{"en":"The biosphere was plunged into absolute chaos.","zh":"生物圈陷入徹底混亂。"},{"en":"Absolute chaos means complete disorder and confusion.","zh":"absolute chaos 指完全失序和混亂。"},{"en":"A classroom can fall into absolute chaos if the teacher leaves without instructions.","zh":"如果老師沒有指示就離開，課室可能陷入徹底混亂。"},{"en":"Chaos makes survival difficult because normal systems stop working.","zh":"混亂令生存困難，因為正常系統停止運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a situation with almost no order.","zh":"這個短語描述幾乎沒有秩序的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"surprising fact","meaning":"令人驚訝的事實","examples":[{"en":"The surprising fact is that so many creatures survived.","zh":"令人驚訝的事實是，竟有這麼多生物存活下來。"},{"en":"A surprising fact is a true piece of information that people may not expect.","zh":"surprising fact 指令人意想不到的真實資訊。"},{"en":"A surprising fact about sleep is that too little of it can weaken memory.","zh":"關於睡眠的一個令人驚訝事實是，睡眠不足可以削弱記憶。"},{"en":"Surprising facts make readers rethink what they assumed.","zh":"令人驚訝的事實會令讀者重新思考自己的假設。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces unexpected truth.","zh":"這個短語引出意料之外的真相。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"became extinct","meaning":"滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Many creatures became extinct after the impact.","zh":"許多生物在撞擊後滅絕。"},{"en":"Became extinct means died out completely, with no living members remaining.","zh":"became extinct 指完全消亡，沒有在世成員留下。"},{"en":"A plant species may become extinct if its habitat is destroyed and no seeds survive.","zh":"如果棲息地被摧毀且沒有種子存活，植物物種可能滅絕。"},{"en":"Extinction is permanent unless the term is being used loosely or revival is possible for languages.","zh":"對物種而言，滅絕通常是永久的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete disappearance of a species or group.","zh":"這個短語描述物種或群體完全消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"survived","meaning":"存活下來","examples":[{"en":"Many species survived despite the catastrophic impact.","zh":"儘管發生災難性撞擊，許多物種仍存活下來。"},{"en":"Survived means continued living after danger, disaster, or difficulty.","zh":"survived 指在危險、災難或困難後繼續活着。"},{"en":"A tree may survive a storm if its roots are strong.","zh":"如果根部強壯，樹木可能在暴風雨後存活下來。"},{"en":"Survival often depends on protection, flexibility, and available food.","zh":"存活通常取決於保護、適應能力和可用食物。"},{"en":"This word contrasts with dying or becoming extinct.","zh":"這個字與死亡或滅絕形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"global disruption","meaning":"全球性破壞","examples":[{"en":"Global disruption to plant communities affected many animals.","zh":"植物群落的全球性破壞影響了許多動物。"},{"en":"Global disruption means serious disturbance across the whole world.","zh":"global disruption 指遍及全球的嚴重擾亂。"},{"en":"A global disruption to shipping can delay goods in many countries.","zh":"全球航運受到破壞可以延誤許多國家的貨物。"},{"en":"When one global system is disrupted, many connected systems suffer too.","zh":"當一個全球系統受破壞，許多相連系統也會受害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large-scale disturbance.","zh":"這個短語描述大規模擾亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"plant communities","meaning":"植物群落","examples":[{"en":"Plant communities were badly disrupted after the impact.","zh":"撞擊後，植物群落受到嚴重破壞。"},{"en":"Plant communities are groups of plants living together in an ecosystem.","zh":"plant communities 指在同一生態系統中一起生長的植物群體。"},{"en":"A forest, grassland, or wetland contains different plant communities.","zh":"森林、草原或濕地包含不同植物群落。"},{"en":"When plant communities are damaged, animals lose food and shelter.","zh":"當植物群落受損，動物會失去食物和庇護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes plants as connected ecological groups.","zh":"這個短語把植物描述為相互連結的生態群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"herbivorous dinosaurs","meaning":"草食性恐龍","examples":[{"en":"The herbivorous dinosaurs died quickly after plants were destroyed.","zh":"植物被摧毀後，草食性恐龍很快死亡。"},{"en":"Herbivorous dinosaurs were dinosaurs that ate plants.","zh":"herbivorous dinosaurs 指以植物為食的恐龍。"},{"en":"A cow is herbivorous because it feeds mainly on plants.","zh":"牛是草食性的，因為它主要以植物為食。"},{"en":"Plant-eating animals suffer first when plant food disappears.","zh":"當植物食物消失，食植物動物會首先受害。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies dinosaurs by diet.","zh":"這個短語按飲食方式辨認恐龍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"predators","meaning":"捕食者","examples":[{"en":"The predators soon followed after their prey disappeared.","zh":"當獵物消失後，捕食者很快跟着滅絕。"},{"en":"Predators are animals that hunt and eat other animals.","zh":"predators 指捕獵並吃其他動物的動物。"},{"en":"Cats are predators when they hunt mice or birds.","zh":"貓捕捉老鼠或鳥時，就是捕食者。"},{"en":"Predators suffer when the animals they eat disappear.","zh":"當捕食者所吃的動物消失，它們也會受害。"},{"en":"This word describes animals higher in a food chain.","zh":"這個字描述食物鏈中較高層的動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"soon followed","meaning":"很快接着發生","examples":[{"en":"The predators soon followed the herbivorous dinosaurs into extinction.","zh":"捕食者很快接着草食性恐龍走向滅絕。"},{"en":"Soon followed means happened shortly after another event.","zh":"soon followed 指在另一事件後不久發生。"},{"en":"The first student left the club, and several friends soon followed.","zh":"第一名學生離開學會後，幾個朋友很快也跟着離開。"},{"en":"In food chains, one group’s collapse can soon be followed by another’s.","zh":"在食物鏈中，一個群體崩潰後，另一個群體可能很快接着崩潰。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a quick sequence of events.","zh":"這個短語顯示事件快速連續發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"sea-based life","meaning":"海洋生物","examples":[{"en":"Sea-based life suffered disastrously after the impact.","zh":"撞擊後，海洋生物遭受災難性打擊。"},{"en":"Sea-based life means organisms that live in the ocean or depend on marine environments.","zh":"sea-based life 指生活在海洋中或依賴海洋環境的生物。"},{"en":"Coral, fish, turtles, and plankton are examples of sea-based life.","zh":"珊瑚、魚、海龜和浮游生物都是海洋生物例子。"},{"en":"Ocean disruption can affect sea-based life by changing food, temperature, and water quality.","zh":"海洋擾動可以透過改變食物、溫度和水質影響海洋生物。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on marine living things.","zh":"這個短語集中於海洋中的生命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"suffered disastrously","meaning":"遭受災難性打擊","examples":[{"en":"Sea-based life suffered disastrously.","zh":"海洋生物遭受災難性打擊。"},{"en":"Suffered disastrously means was harmed in an extremely severe way.","zh":"suffered disastrously 指受到極其嚴重的傷害。"},{"en":"A town may suffer disastrously if a flood destroys homes, roads, and hospitals.","zh":"如果洪水摧毀房屋、道路和醫院，城鎮可能遭受災難性打擊。"},{"en":"Severe suffering can affect whole systems, not just individuals.","zh":"嚴重打擊可以影響整個系統，而不只是個體。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses extreme damage.","zh":"這個短語強調極端破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"giant marine reptiles","meaning":"巨型海洋爬行動物","examples":[{"en":"All giant marine reptiles disappeared.","zh":"所有巨型海洋爬行動物都消失了。"},{"en":"Giant marine reptiles were large reptile-like animals that lived in the sea.","zh":"giant marine reptiles 指生活在海洋中的大型爬行類動物。"},{"en":"A museum may display fossils of giant marine reptiles beside dinosaur fossils.","zh":"博物館可能把巨型海洋爬行動物化石與恐龍化石一起展示。"},{"en":"Large sea animals can be vulnerable when ocean food chains collapse.","zh":"當海洋食物鏈崩潰，大型海洋動物可能很脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ancient large reptiles of marine environments.","zh":"這個短語描述古代海洋環境中的大型爬行動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"ancestors of crocodiles","meaning":"鱷魚的祖先","examples":[{"en":"The ancestors of crocodiles survived the extinction.","zh":"鱷魚的祖先在滅絕中存活下來。"},{"en":"Ancestors of crocodiles are earlier animals from which modern crocodiles developed.","zh":"ancestors of crocodiles 指現代鱷魚演化來源的早期動物。"},{"en":"A family tree shows ancestors before the present generation.","zh":"家譜顯示現代世代以前的祖先。"},{"en":"Studying ancestors helps scientists explain why modern animals have certain features.","zh":"研究祖先幫助科學家解釋現代動物為何具有某些特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase links ancient animals with modern crocodiles.","zh":"這個短語把古代動物與現代鱷魚連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"it is theorised that","meaning":"有理論認為","examples":[{"en":"It is theorised that crocodile ancestors survived because they were semi-aquatic.","zh":"有理論認為鱷魚祖先因半水棲而存活。"},{"en":"It is theorised that means scientists or thinkers propose this as a possible explanation.","zh":"it is theorised that 指科學家或思想者提出某事作為可能解釋。"},{"en":"It is theorised that sleep helps the brain organise memories.","zh":"有理論認為睡眠幫助大腦整理記憶。"},{"en":"A theory still needs evidence and may change with new findings.","zh":"理論仍需要證據，並可能因新發現而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a scientific explanation that is not presented as simple fact.","zh":"這個短語引出科學解釋，而不是把它當作簡單事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"modern crocodiles","meaning":"現代鱷魚","examples":[{"en":"Modern crocodiles are semi-aquatic animals.","zh":"現代鱷魚是半水棲動物。"},{"en":"Modern crocodiles are crocodile species living today.","zh":"modern crocodiles 指今日仍存在的鱷魚物種。"},{"en":"Modern crocodiles spend time in water but can also move on land.","zh":"現代鱷魚會在水中活動，也能在陸地移動。"},{"en":"Their habits help scientists think about how ancient relatives may have survived.","zh":"牠們的習性幫助科學家思考古代親屬可能如何存活。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts living crocodiles with ancient ancestors.","zh":"這個短語把現存鱷魚與古代祖先作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"semi-aquatic","meaning":"半水棲的","examples":[{"en":"Crocodile ancestors were semi-aquatic and could shelter in water.","zh":"鱷魚祖先是半水棲的，可以躲在水中。"},{"en":"Semi-aquatic means living partly in water and partly on land.","zh":"semi-aquatic 指部分生活在水中、部分生活在陸上。"},{"en":"Frogs are semi-aquatic because they can live in ponds and on land.","zh":"青蛙是半水棲的，因為牠們能在池塘和陸地生活。"},{"en":"Semi-aquatic animals may escape some land dangers by entering water.","zh":"半水棲動物可以進入水中，避開部分陸地危險。"},{"en":"This word describes a lifestyle shared between two environments.","zh":"這個字描述在兩種環境之間生活的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"shelter in the water","meaning":"躲在水中避難","examples":[{"en":"Some reptiles could shelter in the water from fires.","zh":"有些爬行動物可以躲在水中避開火災。"},{"en":"To shelter in the water means to use water as protection from danger.","zh":"shelter in the water 指利用水作為保護來避開危險。"},{"en":"During extreme heat, animals may shelter near water to cool down.","zh":"在極端高溫中，動物可能躲近水源降溫。"},{"en":"Water can protect against fire, heat, and flying debris in some situations.","zh":"在某些情況下，水可以抵擋火、熱力和飛散碎片。"},{"en":"This phrase describes seeking safety in water.","zh":"這個短語描述在水中尋求安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"fires and blast damage","meaning":"火災和爆炸破壞","examples":[{"en":"Water protected some animals from fires and blast damage.","zh":"水保護了一些動物免受火災和爆炸破壞。"},{"en":"Fires and blast damage means burning and destruction caused by an explosion or impact.","zh":"fires and blast damage 指由爆炸或撞擊造成的燃燒和破壞。"},{"en":"After a gas explosion, buildings may suffer fires and blast damage.","zh":"煤氣爆炸後，建築物可能遭受火災和爆炸破壞。"},{"en":"Animals protected from heat and pressure may have a better chance of survival.","zh":"受保護免受熱力和壓力傷害的動物，存活機會可能較高。"},{"en":"This phrase combines two kinds of violent harm.","zh":"這個短語結合兩種猛烈傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"scavenge on land","meaning":"在陸地覓食腐肉","examples":[{"en":"Crocodile ancestors could scavenge on land after the disaster.","zh":"災難後，鱷魚祖先可以在陸地覓食腐肉。"},{"en":"To scavenge on land means to search land for dead animals or leftover food.","zh":"scavenge on land 指在陸地尋找死去動物或剩餘食物。"},{"en":"Crows may scavenge on land near rubbish bins or roads.","zh":"烏鴉可能在垃圾桶或道路附近覓食腐肉。"},{"en":"Scavenging helps animals survive when fresh prey is scarce.","zh":"當新鮮獵物稀少，食腐有助動物存活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes feeding from available dead matter on land.","zh":"這個短語描述在陸地利用可得死亡物質進食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"abundant dead animals","meaning":"大量死去的動物","examples":[{"en":"There were abundant dead animals after the impact.","zh":"撞擊後有大量死去的動物。"},{"en":"Abundant dead animals means many animal bodies were available.","zh":"abundant dead animals 指有許多動物屍體可見或可利用。"},{"en":"After a fish die-off, birds may find abundant dead fish along the shore.","zh":"魚類大量死亡後，鳥類可能在岸邊找到大量死魚。"},{"en":"Scavengers can survive better when dead animals provide food.","zh":"當死去動物提供食物，食腐動物更能存活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a grim but plentiful food source.","zh":"這個短語描述令人沉重但豐富的食物來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"for years afterwards","meaning":"其後多年","examples":[{"en":"Some animals fed on dead matter for years afterwards.","zh":"有些動物其後多年以死亡物質為食。"},{"en":"For years afterwards means for several years after an event.","zh":"for years afterwards 指事件之後的好幾年。"},{"en":"After a factory closed, the town struggled economically for years afterwards.","zh":"工廠關閉後，該城鎮其後多年在經濟上掙扎。"},{"en":"Some consequences last long after the original event ends.","zh":"有些後果在原事件結束很久後仍持續。"},{"en":"This phrase shows extended effects after a major event.","zh":"這個短語顯示重大事件之後的長期影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"similarly","meaning":"同樣地","examples":[{"en":"Similarly, insects and worms could feed on dead matter.","zh":"同樣地，昆蟲和蠕蟲可以以死亡物質為食。"},{"en":"Similarly means in a similar way or for the same kind of reason.","zh":"similarly 指以相似方式或基於同類理由。"},{"en":"Some students learn well from diagrams; similarly, others understand better through pictures.","zh":"有些學生透過圖表學得好；同樣地，另一些學生透過圖片理解得更好。"},{"en":"This word connects two points that share a pattern.","zh":"這個字連接兩個具有相同模式的觀點。"},{"en":"It helps show comparison between examples.","zh":"它有助顯示例子之間的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"insects, worms and molluscs","meaning":"昆蟲、蠕蟲和軟體動物","examples":[{"en":"Insects, worms and molluscs could feed on dead plant and animal matter.","zh":"昆蟲、蠕蟲和軟體動物可以以死去的植物和動物物質為食。"},{"en":"Insects, worms and molluscs are small animal groups, many of which can feed on decaying material.","zh":"insects, worms and molluscs 指小型動物群體，其中許多能以腐爛物質為食。"},{"en":"Earthworms help gardens by breaking down dead leaves in the soil.","zh":"蚯蚓透過分解泥土中的枯葉幫助花園。"},{"en":"Small creatures can survive disasters if food remains available in dead matter.","zh":"如果死亡物質仍提供食物，小型生物可以在災難中存活。"},{"en":"This phrase names groups low in the food chain.","zh":"這個短語指出食物鏈較低層的動物群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"feed on","meaning":"以……為食","examples":[{"en":"Many creatures could feed on dead plant and animal matter.","zh":"許多生物可以以死去的植物和動物物質為食。"},{"en":"To feed on something means to eat it as a food source.","zh":"feed on something 指把某物作為食物來源。"},{"en":"Bees feed on nectar from flowers.","zh":"蜜蜂以花蜜為食。"},{"en":"What animals feed on affects whether they can survive after an environment changes.","zh":"動物以甚麼為食會影響牠們能否在環境改變後存活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a regular food relationship.","zh":"這個短語描述常規食物關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"dead plant and animal matter","meaning":"死去的植物和動物物質","examples":[{"en":"Some small creatures survived by feeding on dead plant and animal matter.","zh":"有些小型生物靠進食死去的植物和動物物質存活。"},{"en":"Dead plant and animal matter means remains of plants and animals that have died.","zh":"dead plant and animal matter 指已死亡植物和動物的殘留物。"},{"en":"Compost is made when dead plant matter breaks down into soil nutrients.","zh":"堆肥是死去植物物質分解成泥土養分後形成的。"},{"en":"Dead matter can become food for worms, insects, fungi, and scavengers.","zh":"死亡物質可以成為蠕蟲、昆蟲、真菌和食腐動物的食物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to decaying biological material.","zh":"這個短語指正在腐爛的生物材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"those that fed on","meaning":"以……為食的那些動物","examples":[{"en":"Animals that fed on these creatures could also survive.","zh":"以這些生物為食的動物也能存活。"},{"en":"Those that fed on something means the animals or people that ate that food source.","zh":"those that fed on something 指以某食物來源為食的動物或人。"},{"en":"Birds that feed on insects may stay in a garden if insects are plentiful.","zh":"如果昆蟲很多，以昆蟲為食的鳥可能留在花園。"},{"en":"If one food source survives, animals depending on it may survive too.","zh":"如果一種食物來源存活，依賴它的動物也可能存活。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a group by what it eats.","zh":"這個短語按飲食辨認一個群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"consequently","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"Consequently, insectivores, scavengers and omnivores were preserved.","zh":"因此，食蟲動物、食腐動物和雜食動物得以存活。"},{"en":"Consequently means as a result.","zh":"consequently 指因此或作為結果。"},{"en":"The school added more buses; consequently, fewer students were late.","zh":"學校增加巴士；因此，較少學生遲到。"},{"en":"This word shows that one fact follows logically from another.","zh":"這個字顯示一個事實在邏輯上由另一個事實導出。"},{"en":"It is useful for explaining cause and effect.","zh":"它適合用來解釋因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"insectivores","meaning":"食蟲動物","examples":[{"en":"Insectivores survived because insects remained available as food.","zh":"食蟲動物因昆蟲仍可作食物而存活。"},{"en":"Insectivores are animals that eat insects.","zh":"insectivores 指以昆蟲為食的動物。"},{"en":"Some birds and bats are insectivores because they feed mainly on insects.","zh":"有些鳥類和蝙蝠是食蟲動物，因為牠們主要吃昆蟲。"},{"en":"If insects survive a disaster, insectivores still have food.","zh":"如果昆蟲在災難中存活，食蟲動物仍有食物。"},{"en":"This word identifies animals by their insect-based diet.","zh":"這個字按昆蟲飲食辨認動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"scavengers","meaning":"食腐動物","examples":[{"en":"Scavengers could survive by feeding on dead animals.","zh":"食腐動物可以靠吃死去動物存活。"},{"en":"Scavengers are animals that eat dead animals or leftover organic matter.","zh":"scavengers 指吃死去動物或剩餘有機物的動物。"},{"en":"Vultures are scavengers because they feed on carcasses.","zh":"禿鷹是食腐動物，因為牠們以動物屍體為食。"},{"en":"Scavengers are important because they clean up dead matter in ecosystems.","zh":"食腐動物很重要，因為牠們清理生態系統中的死亡物質。"},{"en":"This word describes animals that survive by using remains.","zh":"這個字描述靠利用遺骸存活的動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"omnivorous eating habits","meaning":"雜食性的飲食習慣","examples":[{"en":"Animals with omnivorous eating habits had a better chance of survival.","zh":"具有雜食性飲食習慣的動物有較高存活機會。"},{"en":"Omnivorous eating habits mean eating both plants and animals.","zh":"omnivorous eating habits 指同時吃植物和動物。"},{"en":"Humans are often omnivorous because many diets include vegetables, grains, meat, or fish.","zh":"人類通常是雜食性的，因為許多飲食包括蔬菜、穀物、肉或魚。"},{"en":"Omnivores may survive better when one food source disappears.","zh":"當一種食物來源消失，雜食動物可能更易存活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a flexible diet.","zh":"這個短語描述靈活的飲食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"mammals","meaning":"哺乳類動物","examples":[{"en":"Mammals survived and later came to dominate the land.","zh":"哺乳類動物存活下來，後來支配陸地。"},{"en":"Mammals are warm-blooded animals that usually have hair and feed their young with milk.","zh":"mammals 指通常有毛髮並以乳汁餵養幼體的溫血動物。"},{"en":"Humans, cats, whales, and bats are mammals.","zh":"人類、貓、鯨魚和蝙蝠都是哺乳類動物。"},{"en":"After dinosaurs declined, mammals had more space to diversify.","zh":"恐龍衰落後，哺乳類有更多空間多樣化發展。"},{"en":"This word names a major class of animals.","zh":"這個字指出一大類動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"smaller bird-like reptiles","meaning":"較小型、像鳥的爬行動物","examples":[{"en":"Smaller bird-like reptiles were among the animals preserved.","zh":"較小型、像鳥的爬行動物是存活下來的動物之一。"},{"en":"Smaller bird-like reptiles were small reptiles with features similar to birds.","zh":"smaller bird-like reptiles 指具有類似鳥類特徵的小型爬行動物。"},{"en":"A fossil with feathers and a light body may look bird-like.","zh":"具有羽毛和輕巧身體的化石可能看起來像鳥。"},{"en":"Smaller animals often need less food, which may help them survive disasters.","zh":"較小動物通常需要較少食物，這可能幫助牠們在災難中存活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a group by size and appearance.","zh":"這個短語按大小和外觀描述群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"were preserved","meaning":"得以保存；存活下來","examples":[{"en":"Some groups of animals were preserved after the extinction.","zh":"有些動物群體在滅絕後得以保存。"},{"en":"Were preserved means survived or were kept from disappearing.","zh":"were preserved 指存活下來或避免消失。"},{"en":"Old letters were preserved in a box, so the family history was not lost.","zh":"舊信件被保存在盒中，所以家族歷史沒有失去。"},{"en":"In biology, a preserved group continues while others die out.","zh":"在生物學中，得以保存的群體會延續，而其他群體滅絕。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean physically kept safe or biologically survived.","zh":"這個短語可以指實體保存，也可以指生物存活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"as we know them","meaning":"我們所認識的……","examples":[{"en":"The dinosaurs as we know them were almost gone.","zh":"我們所認識的恐龍幾乎全部消失了。"},{"en":"As we know them means in the form that is familiar to us.","zh":"as we know them 指以我們熟悉的形式而言。"},{"en":"Schools as we know them changed greatly when online lessons became common.","zh":"當網上課堂變得普遍，我們所認識的學校大大改變。"},{"en":"This phrase allows for a familiar idea while admitting there may be technical exceptions.","zh":"這個短語容許使用熟悉概念，同時承認可能有技術性例外。"},{"en":"It means “in the usual sense people understand.”","zh":"它的意思是「以人們通常理解的意思來說」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"dominant land animal","meaning":"佔主導地位的陸地動物","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs had been the dominant land animal for 135 million years.","zh":"恐龍曾是一億三千五百萬年來佔主導地位的陸地動物。"},{"en":"A dominant land animal is the animal group that is most powerful, common, or influential on land.","zh":"dominant land animal 指在陸地上最強大、常見或有影響力的動物群。"},{"en":"Humans are now a dominant land species because they reshape habitats worldwide.","zh":"人類現在是佔主導地位的陸地物種，因為人類重塑全球棲息地。"},{"en":"Dominance can end when disasters remove food, space, or survival advantages.","zh":"當災難移除食物、空間或生存優勢，主導地位可能結束。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ecological control on land.","zh":"這個短語描述陸地上的生態控制地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"all but gone","meaning":"幾乎全部消失","examples":[{"en":"The dinosaurs were all but gone after the extinction.","zh":"滅絕後，恐龍幾乎全部消失。"},{"en":"All but gone means almost completely gone.","zh":"all but gone 指幾乎完全消失。"},{"en":"By midnight, the cakes at the school fair were all but gone.","zh":"到午夜時，學校賣物會的蛋糕幾乎全部售罄。"},{"en":"This phrase allows a tiny exception while stressing near-total disappearance.","zh":"這個短語在強調接近完全消失時，仍容許極少例外。"},{"en":"It means “nearly gone”, not “all except gone.”","zh":"它意思是「幾乎消失」，不是「除了 gone 之外全部」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"allowed mammals to","meaning":"使哺乳類得以……","examples":[{"en":"The disappearance of dinosaurs allowed mammals to diversify.","zh":"恐龍消失使哺乳類得以多樣化發展。"},{"en":"Allowed mammals to means made it possible for mammals to do something.","zh":"allowed mammals to 指使哺乳類能夠做某事。"},{"en":"A new library allowed students to study after school.","zh":"新圖書館使學生得以放學後自修。"},{"en":"When competition disappears, other groups may have space to grow.","zh":"當競爭消失，其他群體可能有空間成長。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how one change creates opportunity.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個變化如何創造機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"burrowing cat-like creatures","meaning":"會掘洞、像貓的小型生物","examples":[{"en":"Early mammals were small burrowing cat-like creatures.","zh":"早期哺乳類是會掘洞、像貓的小型生物。"},{"en":"Burrowing cat-like creatures are small animals that look somewhat like cats and dig or live in holes.","zh":"burrowing cat-like creatures 指外形有點像貓，並會挖洞或住在洞中的小動物。"},{"en":"Rabbits are burrowing animals because they can dig homes underground.","zh":"兔子是會掘洞的動物，因為牠們能在地下挖家。"},{"en":"Burrowing can protect animals from heat, fire, and predators.","zh":"掘洞可以保護動物免受高溫、火災和捕食者傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes body shape and survival behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述身體形態和生存行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"attributes","meaning":"特徵；屬性","examples":[{"en":"Their attributes helped ensure their survival.","zh":"牠們的特徵有助確保牠們存活。"},{"en":"Attributes are qualities or features that a person, animal, or thing has.","zh":"attributes 指人、動物或事物具有的品質或特徵。"},{"en":"Patience and clear speech are useful attributes for a teacher.","zh":"耐性和清楚表達是老師有用的特徵。"},{"en":"An animal’s attributes can decide whether it survives in a changing environment.","zh":"動物的特徵可以決定牠能否在變化環境中存活。"},{"en":"This word means characteristics, not possessions.","zh":"這個字指特性，而不是財物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"helped ensure","meaning":"有助確保","examples":[{"en":"Burrowing helped ensure the survival of early mammals.","zh":"掘洞有助確保早期哺乳類存活。"},{"en":"Helped ensure means made a result more likely or more secure.","zh":"helped ensure 指令某結果更可能或更穩妥。"},{"en":"Regular revision helps ensure students remember vocabulary before an exam.","zh":"定期溫習有助確保學生在考試前記得詞彙。"},{"en":"Safety checks help ensure equipment does not fail during use.","zh":"安全檢查有助確保設備使用時不會故障。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor supports a desired result.","zh":"這個短語顯示某因素支援期望結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"survival throughout","meaning":"在……期間存活","examples":[{"en":"Their attributes helped ensure survival throughout the disaster.","zh":"牠們的特徵有助確保在整場災難期間存活。"},{"en":"Survival throughout something means continuing to live during the whole period of danger.","zh":"survival throughout something 指在整段危險時期中持續活下來。"},{"en":"A business’s savings may help ensure survival throughout an economic downturn.","zh":"企業儲備可能有助確保在經濟低迷期間存活。"},{"en":"To survive throughout a crisis, living things need protection and resources.","zh":"要在危機期間存活，生物需要保護和資源。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses endurance from beginning to end.","zh":"這個短語強調從開始到結束的持續忍耐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"emerge from","meaning":"從……冒出","examples":[{"en":"Mammals emerged from the undergrowth after the disaster.","zh":"災難後，哺乳類從低矮植被中冒出。"},{"en":"To emerge from something means to come out from it or become visible after being hidden.","zh":"emerge from something 指從某物中出來或在隱藏後變得可見。"},{"en":"A child may emerge from a crowded classroom once the bell rings.","zh":"下課鐘響後，孩子可能從擁擠課室中走出來。"},{"en":"After danger passes, hidden animals may emerge to search for food.","zh":"危險過後，隱藏的動物可能冒出來尋找食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes coming out into view.","zh":"這個短語描述從某處出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"undergrowth","meaning":"低矮植被；灌木叢","examples":[{"en":"Mammals emerged from the undergrowth and spread.","zh":"哺乳類從低矮植被中冒出並擴散。"},{"en":"Undergrowth is low plant growth under trees or bushes.","zh":"undergrowth 指樹木或灌木下方的低矮植物。"},{"en":"A hiker may find it hard to walk through thick undergrowth.","zh":"行山者可能覺得很難穿過濃密灌木叢。"},{"en":"Small animals can hide in undergrowth to avoid predators.","zh":"小動物可以躲在低矮植被中避開捕食者。"},{"en":"This word describes dense low vegetation.","zh":"這個字描述濃密低層植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"diversify","meaning":"多樣化發展","examples":[{"en":"Mammals diversified after dinosaurs disappeared.","zh":"恐龍消失後，哺乳類多樣化發展。"},{"en":"To diversify means to develop into many different types.","zh":"diversify 指發展成許多不同類型。"},{"en":"A company may diversify by selling food, drinks, and household products instead of only one item.","zh":"公司可以透過不只售賣一種貨品，而是售賣食物、飲品和家居用品來多樣化。"},{"en":"Animals diversify when new habitats or opportunities become available.","zh":"當新棲息地或機會出現，動物會多樣化發展。"},{"en":"This word describes growth in variety.","zh":"這個字描述種類增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"eventually rule the land","meaning":"最終統治陸地","examples":[{"en":"Mammals eventually ruled the land.","zh":"哺乳類最終統治陸地。"},{"en":"To eventually rule the land means finally become the dominant animals on land.","zh":"eventually rule the land 指最終成為陸地上佔主導地位的動物。"},{"en":"A small shop may eventually lead the market if it grows steadily for years.","zh":"如果小店多年穩定成長，可能最終領導市場。"},{"en":"“Eventually” shows that the change took time, not that it happened immediately.","zh":"“eventually” 顯示變化需要時間，不是立即發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a later rise to dominance.","zh":"這個短語描述後來取得主導地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"ironic consequence","meaning":"諷刺的結果","examples":[{"en":"In an ironic consequence, the extinction helped lead to humans.","zh":"諷刺的是，這次滅絕有助導向人類出現。"},{"en":"An ironic consequence is an unexpected result that seems opposite to what one might expect.","zh":"ironic consequence 指令人意外、似乎與預期相反的結果。"},{"en":"A cancelled class may have the ironic consequence of giving students time to finish homework.","zh":"取消課堂可能產生諷刺的結果：學生有時間完成功課。"},{"en":"Destructive events can sometimes create opportunities for other groups.","zh":"破壞性事件有時會為其他群體創造機會。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a surprising twist in cause and effect.","zh":"這個短語突出因果關係中的意外轉折。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"that class of animal","meaning":"那一類動物","examples":[{"en":"That class of animal ultimately led to Homo sapiens.","zh":"那一類動物最終演化出智人。"},{"en":"That class of animal means the animal group just mentioned.","zh":"that class of animal 指剛才提及的動物群。"},{"en":"In biology, mammals are a class of animal with shared features such as milk production.","zh":"在生物學中，哺乳類是具有產乳等共同特徵的一類動物。"},{"en":"A class of animal can include many different species.","zh":"一類動物可以包括許多不同物種。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a broad biological group.","zh":"這個短語指回一個廣泛生物群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"ultimately led to","meaning":"最終導致；最終演化出","examples":[{"en":"Mammals ultimately led to the species Homo sapiens.","zh":"哺乳類最終演化出智人這個物種。"},{"en":"Ultimately led to means eventually resulted in something after a long process.","zh":"ultimately led to 指經過長時間過程後最終導致某結果。"},{"en":"Years of practice ultimately led to the student’s confident speaking.","zh":"多年練習最終令學生能自信說話。"},{"en":"Long chains of causes can lead to results that seem surprising at first.","zh":"長因果鏈可以導致一開始看似意外的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase connects early developments with final outcomes.","zh":"這個短語把早期發展與最終結果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"species Homo sapiens","meaning":"智人這個物種","examples":[{"en":"Homo sapiens is the species name for human beings.","zh":"Homo sapiens 是人類的物種名稱。"},{"en":"Species Homo sapiens means the biological species to which modern humans belong.","zh":"species Homo sapiens 指現代人類所屬的生物物種。"},{"en":"A science textbook may use Homo sapiens instead of simply saying humans.","zh":"科學教科書可能使用 Homo sapiens，而不只是說 humans。"},{"en":"Scientific names help people avoid confusion between everyday and biological terms.","zh":"科學名稱幫助人們避免日常用語和生物學術語之間的混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies humans in formal biological language.","zh":"這個短語以正式生物學語言辨認人類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"human beings","meaning":"人類","examples":[{"en":"Human beings might not exist without the ancient extinction.","zh":"若沒有那次古代滅絕，人類可能不會存在。"},{"en":"Human beings means people as a biological and social species.","zh":"human beings 指作為生物和社會物種的人。"},{"en":"Human beings use language, tools, memory, and cooperation to survive.","zh":"人類使用語言、工具、記憶和合作來生存。"},{"en":"Events in Earth’s history shaped the conditions that allowed human beings to appear.","zh":"地球歷史中的事件塑造了讓人類出現的條件。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal way to say humans or people.","zh":"這個短語是 humans 或 people 的較正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"were it not for","meaning":"若非……；要不是……","examples":[{"en":"Were it not for that extinction, humans might not be here today.","zh":"若非那次滅絕，人類今天可能不會存在。"},{"en":"Were it not for means if it had not been for.","zh":"were it not for 指如果不是因為某事。"},{"en":"Were it not for my teacher’s advice, I might have given up the course.","zh":"若非老師的建議，我可能已放棄課程。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a condition that changed the outcome.","zh":"這個短語引出改變結果的條件。"},{"en":"It is a formal way to express “without.”","zh":"它是表達 “without” 的正式方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"disastrous extinction","meaning":"災難性滅絕","examples":[{"en":"That disastrous extinction changed the course of life on Earth.","zh":"那次災難性滅絕改變了地球生命的進程。"},{"en":"A disastrous extinction is an extinction event causing enormous loss and damage.","zh":"disastrous extinction 指造成巨大損失和破壞的滅絕事件。"},{"en":"A disastrous fire can destroy a town’s homes, schools, and shops.","zh":"災難性火災可以摧毀城鎮的房屋、學校和商店。"},{"en":"Disastrous events can still create unexpected changes in the long term.","zh":"災難性事件長遠仍可能造成意想不到的改變。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the terrible scale of loss.","zh":"這個短語強調損失規模可怕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"would not be here today","meaning":"今天就不會存在","examples":[{"en":"Without that extinction, human beings would not be here today.","zh":"沒有那次滅絕，人類今天就不會存在。"},{"en":"Would not be here today means would not exist now or be present now.","zh":"would not be here today 指現在不會存在或出現在這裡。"},{"en":"Without early support, the school library project would not be here today.","zh":"沒有早期支持，學校圖書館項目今天就不會存在。"},{"en":"This phrase links present existence to a past condition.","zh":"這個短語把現在的存在與過去條件連起來。"},{"en":"It is often used to show how important a past event was.","zh":"它常用來顯示過去事件有多重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"reading passage","meaning":"閱讀文章","examples":[{"en":"The reading passage has seven paragraphs.","zh":"這篇閱讀文章有七段。"},{"en":"A reading passage is a text that students read and answer questions about.","zh":"reading passage 指學生閱讀並回答問題的文本。"},{"en":"In an exam, a reading passage may be followed by multiple-choice and matching questions.","zh":"在考試中，閱讀文章後可能有多項選擇和配對題。"},{"en":"Students should understand the passage structure before answering detailed questions.","zh":"學生回答細節題前應先理解文章結構。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the text used for reading practice or assessment.","zh":"這個短語指用於閱讀練習或評估的文本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The list of headings contains more headings than needed.","zh":"標題列表包含比所需更多的標題。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a set of possible titles for paragraphs or sections.","zh":"list of headings 指段落或章節可能標題的一組選項。"},{"en":"In IELTS reading, students often match paragraphs with headings from a list.","zh":"在 IELTS 閱讀中，學生常把段落與列表中的標題配對。"},{"en":"Extra headings make the task harder because some options are distractors.","zh":"額外標題令題目更難，因為有些選項是干擾項。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to title choices in a reading task.","zh":"這個短語指閱讀題中的標題選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct heading for each paragraph.","zh":"學生為每段選出正確標題。"},{"en":"To choose the correct heading means to select the title that best matches the main idea.","zh":"choose the correct heading 指選出最符合主旨的標題。"},{"en":"A student should read the whole paragraph before choosing its heading.","zh":"學生應讀完整段後才選標題。"},{"en":"The correct heading usually reflects the paragraph’s overall purpose, not one small detail.","zh":"正確標題通常反映段落整體目的，而不是一個小細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common reading exam task.","zh":"這個短語描述常見閱讀考試任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"write the correct number","meaning":"寫上正確編號","examples":[{"en":"Students write the correct number for each answer.","zh":"學生為每個答案寫上正確編號。"},{"en":"To write the correct number means to record the number that matches the right option.","zh":"write the correct number 指記下與正確選項相符的編號。"},{"en":"In a matching task, students may write Roman numerals beside paragraph letters.","zh":"在配對題中，學生可能在段落字母旁寫上羅馬數字。"},{"en":"Writing the wrong number loses marks even if the idea is understood.","zh":"即使理解意思，寫錯編號也會失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction about answer format.","zh":"這個短語是關於答案格式的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"mystery of the border","meaning":"邊界之謎","examples":[{"en":"The example heading describes the mystery of the KT boundary.","zh":"範例標題描述 K-T 界線的邊界之謎。"},{"en":"Mystery of the border means an unexplained question about a boundary or dividing line.","zh":"mystery of the border 指關於界線或分界的未解問題。"},{"en":"A teacher may discuss the mystery of a school boundary if old maps show different limits.","zh":"如果舊地圖顯示不同範圍，老師可能討論學校邊界之謎。"},{"en":"The mystery exists because evidence at the border needs explanation.","zh":"這個謎存在，是因為邊界上的證據需要解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase frames a boundary as something puzzling.","zh":"這個短語把邊界描述成令人困惑的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"first piece of evidence","meaning":"第一項證據","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes the first piece of evidence for the impact theory.","zh":"文章描述支持撞擊理論的第一項證據。"},{"en":"First piece of evidence means the earliest clue supporting an idea.","zh":"first piece of evidence 指支持某想法的最早線索。"},{"en":"A teacher may see the first piece of evidence of cheating when two answers are exactly the same.","zh":"當兩份答案完全相同，老師可能看見作弊的第一項證據。"},{"en":"One clue can start a larger investigation.","zh":"一條線索可以開始更大規模的調查。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the beginning of an evidence chain.","zh":"這個短語指出證據鏈的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"unexpected element","meaning":"意想不到的元素","examples":[{"en":"The unexpected element in the soil was iridium.","zh":"泥土中的意想不到元素是銥。"},{"en":"An unexpected element is a chemical element found where people did not expect it.","zh":"unexpected element 指在不預期位置發現的化學元素。"},{"en":"A lab may find an unexpected element in drinking water during testing.","zh":"實驗室在測試飲用水時，可能發現意想不到的元素。"},{"en":"Unexpected elements can lead scientists to ask where the material came from.","zh":"意想不到的元素可以令科學家追問物質來自哪裡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a surprising chemical clue.","zh":"這個短語描述令人驚訝的化學線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"company procedures","meaning":"公司程序","examples":[{"en":"Company procedures prevented the early discovery from being released.","zh":"公司程序阻止早期發現被公開。"},{"en":"Company procedures are official steps and rules workers must follow.","zh":"company procedures 指員工必須遵守的官方步驟和規則。"},{"en":"Company procedures may require approval before staff publish technical reports.","zh":"公司程序可能要求員工發布技術報告前先獲批准。"},{"en":"Procedures can protect business interests but may also delay information sharing.","zh":"程序可以保護商業利益，但也可能延誤資訊分享。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal workplace processes.","zh":"這個短語指正式工作場所流程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"final decision","meaning":"最終決定","examples":[{"en":"The panel reached a final decision about the impact theory.","zh":"專家小組就撞擊理論作出最終決定。"},{"en":"A final decision is the conclusion made after discussion or review is complete.","zh":"final decision 指討論或審查完成後得出的結論。"},{"en":"A school committee may reach a final decision after hearing teachers, parents, and students.","zh":"學校委員會在聽取老師、家長和學生意見後，可能作出最終決定。"},{"en":"Final decisions end uncertainty, at least for the people making them.","zh":"最終決定會結束不確定性，至少對作決定的人而言如此。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the last official judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述最後的正式判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"heated debate","meaning":"激烈爭論","examples":[{"en":"There was heated debate about the true cause of the extinction.","zh":"關於滅絕真正原因曾有激烈爭論。"},{"en":"Heated debate is strong, emotional, or intense disagreement.","zh":"heated debate 指強烈、情緒化或激烈的分歧。"},{"en":"A new school uniform rule may cause heated debate among parents and students.","zh":"新校服規定可能在家長和學生之間引起激烈爭論。"},{"en":"Heated debate happens when people care deeply and evidence is disputed.","zh":"當人們非常關心某事且證據有爭議時，激烈爭論就會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes argument with strong feeling.","zh":"這個短語描述帶強烈情緒的爭論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"fortunate consequence","meaning":"幸運的後果","examples":[{"en":"The extinction had a fortunate consequence for mammals.","zh":"這次滅絕對哺乳類有一個幸運的後果。"},{"en":"A fortunate consequence is a good result that comes from an event, often unexpectedly.","zh":"fortunate consequence 指某事件帶來的好結果，通常是意外的。"},{"en":"A cancelled train may have the fortunate consequence of giving a student time to review notes.","zh":"火車取消可能有一個幸運後果，就是讓學生有時間複習筆記。"},{"en":"Bad events can sometimes create opportunities for other people or groups.","zh":"壞事件有時可以為其他人或群體創造機會。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a positive result from a difficult situation.","zh":"這個短語突出困難情況中的正面結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"preservation strategies","meaning":"保存／生存策略","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains preservation strategies that helped some animals survive.","zh":"文章解釋了幫助某些動物存活的生存策略。"},{"en":"Preservation strategies are ways of staying safe or avoiding disappearance.","zh":"preservation strategies 指保持安全或避免消失的方法。"},{"en":"A family may use preservation strategies such as saving water and storing emergency food during a storm season.","zh":"家庭在風季可能使用節約用水和儲存應急食物等生存策略。"},{"en":"Animals survive disasters when their habits protect them from danger or provide food.","zh":"當動物習性能保護牠們免受危險或提供食物，牠們就能在災難中存活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes methods that help survival.","zh":"這個短語描述有助生存的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"situation in the sea","meaning":"海洋中的情況","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the situation in the sea after the impact.","zh":"文章討論撞擊後海洋中的情況。"},{"en":"Situation in the sea means the conditions affecting ocean life and water after an event.","zh":"situation in the sea 指事件後影響海洋生物和海水的狀況。"},{"en":"After an oil spill, the situation in the sea may become dangerous for fish and birds.","zh":"漏油後，海洋中的情況可能對魚和鳥變得危險。"},{"en":"Sea conditions matter because marine food chains depend on water quality and sunlight.","zh":"海洋狀況很重要，因為海洋食物鏈依賴水質和陽光。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what happened in ocean environments.","zh":"這個短語集中於海洋環境中發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"first-hand view","meaning":"第一身觀察","examples":[{"en":"A first-hand view means an account from direct experience.","zh":"first-hand view 指來自直接經驗的描述。"},{"en":"A first-hand view is information from someone who saw or experienced something personally.","zh":"first-hand view 指由親眼看見或親身經歷某事的人提供的資訊。"},{"en":"A student who visited a refugee centre can give a first-hand view of the situation.","zh":"到訪過難民中心的學生可以提供該情況的第一身觀察。"},{"en":"First-hand views can feel vivid because they come from direct observation.","zh":"第一身觀察因來自直接觀察而可能感覺生動。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts direct experience with second-hand reports.","zh":"這個短語把直接經驗與二手報告作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill in missing words in a shortened version of the text.","zh":"complete the summary 指在文本的簡短版本中填入缺失字詞。"},{"en":"A student should read the summary grammar before choosing an answer.","zh":"學生選答案前應先讀摘要的文法。"},{"en":"Summary completion tests both meaning and exact wording.","zh":"完成摘要同時測試意思和準確字詞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common reading exam task.","zh":"這個短語描述常見閱讀考試任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"first half of the passage","meaning":"文章前半部分","examples":[{"en":"The summary focuses on the first half of the passage.","zh":"摘要集中於文章前半部分。"},{"en":"The first half of the passage means the earlier part of the reading text.","zh":"first half of the passage 指閱讀文本較早的一半。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to summarise only the first half of an article before reading the rest.","zh":"老師可能要求學生在閱讀餘下部分前，只總結文章前半部分。"},{"en":"Focusing on one half helps students locate answers faster.","zh":"集中於一半內容有助學生更快定位答案。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a section by position.","zh":"這個短語按位置指出文章部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should use no more than two words from the passage.","zh":"每個答案應使用文章中不多於兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must contain one or two words only.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案只能包含一個或兩個字。"},{"en":"“rock samples” fits the rule, but “the rock samples” may exceed the limit if extra words are not allowed.","zh":"“rock samples” 符合規則，但若不容許額外字詞，“the rock samples” 可能超出限制。"},{"en":"Word limits matter because extra words can make an answer wrong.","zh":"字數限制很重要，因為多寫字可能令答案錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict answer-length rule.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格答案長度規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"identify","meaning":"識別；辨認","examples":[{"en":"Baltosser was the first to identify the feature.","zh":"Baltosser 是第一個識別該特徵的人。"},{"en":"To identify something means to recognise what it is or point it out clearly.","zh":"identify something 指認出某物是甚麼或清楚指出它。"},{"en":"A teacher can identify a student’s common grammar mistake after reading several essays.","zh":"老師閱讀幾篇作文後，可以辨認學生的常見文法錯誤。"},{"en":"Identifying a feature is the first step before explaining its cause.","zh":"辨認特徵是解釋其成因前的第一步。"},{"en":"This word means more than simply seeing something; it means recognising it.","zh":"這個字不只是看見某物，而是認出它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"reveal this information","meaning":"透露這項資料","examples":[{"en":"Baltosser could not reveal this information because of company rules.","zh":"Baltosser 因公司規則不能透露這項資料。"},{"en":"To reveal this information means to make these facts known to others.","zh":"reveal this information 指把這些事實告知他人。"},{"en":"A school may not reveal student information without parental permission.","zh":"學校未經家長同意，不應透露學生資料。"},{"en":"Information may stay hidden if rules prevent people from sharing it.","zh":"如果規則阻止人分享資訊，資料可能保持隱藏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making facts public.","zh":"這個短語描述公開事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"added further evidence","meaning":"增加進一步證據","examples":[{"en":"The discovery added further evidence to the impact hypothesis.","zh":"這項發現為撞擊假說增加進一步證據。"},{"en":"Added further evidence means provided more proof or support for an idea.","zh":"added further evidence 指為某想法提供更多證明或支持。"},{"en":"A second witness added further evidence that the accident happened at the crossing.","zh":"第二名目擊者增加進一步證據，證明事故發生在過路處。"},{"en":"More evidence can turn a weak idea into a stronger theory.","zh":"更多證據可以把薄弱想法變成更有力理論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence building up.","zh":"這個短語描述證據逐步累積。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"showed the world","meaning":"向世人展示","examples":[{"en":"Camargo and Penfield finally showed the world the discovery.","zh":"Camargo 和 Penfield 最終向世人展示這項發現。"},{"en":"Showed the world means made something known to the wider public or scientific community.","zh":"showed the world 指把某事告知更廣泛公眾或科學界。"},{"en":"A young inventor may show the world a new device at a science fair.","zh":"年輕發明家可能在科學展向世人展示新裝置。"},{"en":"Public presentation allows others to judge the importance of a discovery.","zh":"公開展示讓其他人判斷發現的重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses bringing hidden work into public view.","zh":"這個短語強調把隱藏工作帶到公眾視野。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"nevertheless","meaning":"然而；儘管如此","examples":[{"en":"Nevertheless, they had to overcome scepticism.","zh":"然而，他們必須克服懷疑。"},{"en":"Nevertheless means despite what was just said.","zh":"nevertheless 指儘管剛才所說的情況如此。"},{"en":"The task was difficult; nevertheless, the students finished it on time.","zh":"任務很困難；然而，學生仍準時完成。"},{"en":"This word introduces a contrast after a previous point.","zh":"這個字在前一點之後引出對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when something happens despite an obstacle.","zh":"當某事在障礙下仍發生時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"overcome scepticism","meaning":"克服懷疑","examples":[{"en":"The scientists had to overcome widespread scepticism.","zh":"科學家必須克服廣泛懷疑。"},{"en":"To overcome scepticism means to persuade doubters through evidence or explanation.","zh":"overcome scepticism 指透過證據或解釋說服懷疑者。"},{"en":"A student can overcome scepticism about her idea by showing clear research.","zh":"學生可以透過展示清晰研究，克服別人對她想法的懷疑。"},{"en":"Strong evidence helps people move from doubt to acceptance.","zh":"強證據幫助人們從懷疑轉向接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes defeating doubt.","zh":"這個短語描述戰勝疑慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"international commission","meaning":"國際委員會","examples":[{"en":"An international commission can review scientific evidence.","zh":"國際委員會可以審視科學證據。"},{"en":"An international commission is an official group from different countries formed to study or decide an issue.","zh":"international commission 指由不同國家成員組成、用來研究或決定某議題的正式小組。"},{"en":"An international commission may investigate pollution that affects several nations.","zh":"國際委員會可能調查影響多國的污染。"},{"en":"Such commissions help make decisions feel more balanced and credible.","zh":"這類委員會有助令決定顯得更平衡和可信。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a formal multinational review body.","zh":"這個短語描述正式跨國審查機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"confirmed this event as","meaning":"確認這事件為……","examples":[{"en":"The panel confirmed the impact as the cause of the extinction.","zh":"專家小組確認這次撞擊為滅絕的原因。"},{"en":"Confirmed this event as something means officially accepted it as having that role.","zh":"confirmed this event as something 指正式接受該事件具有某角色。"},{"en":"Doctors confirmed the virus as the cause of the outbreak after testing samples.","zh":"醫生測試樣本後，確認病毒為疫情原因。"},{"en":"Confirmation usually comes after evidence has been reviewed.","zh":"確認通常在證據被審視後出現。"},{"en":"This phrase marks movement from possibility to accepted explanation.","zh":"這個短語標示從可能性轉向被接受的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"real reason for","meaning":"……的真正原因","examples":[{"en":"The impact was confirmed as the real reason for the extinction.","zh":"撞擊被確認為滅絕的真正原因。"},{"en":"Real reason for something means the true cause behind it.","zh":"real reason for something 指某事背後的真正原因。"},{"en":"The real reason for a student’s silence may be fear, not lack of ideas.","zh":"學生沉默的真正原因可能是害怕，而不是沒有想法。"},{"en":"Finding the real reason prevents people from solving the wrong problem.","zh":"找出真正原因可以避免人們解決錯誤問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the actual cause.","zh":"這個短語集中於實際原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each answer.","zh":"學生為每個答案選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the option marked by the right letter.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選出由正確字母標示的選項。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice question, students may choose A, B, C, or D.","zh":"在多項選擇題中，學生可能選 A、B、C 或 D。"},{"en":"Students should match the letter to the passage evidence, not personal knowledge.","zh":"學生應根據文章證據配對字母，而不是個人知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"after the asteroid struck","meaning":"小行星撞擊之後","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what happened after the asteroid struck Earth.","zh":"題目問小行星撞擊地球之後發生甚麼。"},{"en":"After the asteroid struck means following the moment the asteroid hit the planet.","zh":"after the asteroid struck 指小行星撞擊地球那一刻之後。"},{"en":"After a car struck a wall, people checked whether anyone was hurt.","zh":"汽車撞牆之後，人們會檢查是否有人受傷。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on consequences after an impact.","zh":"這個短語集中於撞擊後果。"},{"en":"It helps students order events correctly.","zh":"它幫助學生正確排列事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"shock wave","meaning":"衝擊波","examples":[{"en":"A shock wave followed shortly after the impact.","zh":"撞擊後不久出現衝擊波。"},{"en":"A shock wave is a powerful pressure wave created by an explosion, impact, or fast movement.","zh":"shock wave 指由爆炸、撞擊或高速移動產生的強大壓力波。"},{"en":"A loud explosion can create a shock wave that rattles windows.","zh":"巨大爆炸可以產生震動窗戶的衝擊波。"},{"en":"Shock waves can damage objects even far from the centre of the blast.","zh":"衝擊波可以損壞離爆炸中心很遠的物件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sudden pressure moving through air, water, or ground.","zh":"這個短語描述突然壓力穿過空氣、水或地面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"object’s vaporisation","meaning":"物體的氣化","examples":[{"en":"The object’s vaporisation happened almost immediately upon impact.","zh":"該物體的氣化在撞擊時幾乎立即發生。"},{"en":"Object’s vaporisation means the object changed into gas because of extreme heat.","zh":"object’s vaporisation 指物體因極端高溫變成氣體。"},{"en":"A drop of water on a hot pan can show simple vaporisation.","zh":"熱鍋上的一滴水可以顯示簡單氣化。"},{"en":"In a huge impact, heat can vaporise rock and spread material into the air.","zh":"在巨大撞擊中，熱力可以氣化岩石並把物質擴散到空氣中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rapid physical change of the object.","zh":"這個短語描述物體的快速物理變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"warmed before going cold","meaning":"先變暖後變冷","examples":[{"en":"The Earth warmed before going cold after the impact.","zh":"撞擊後，地球先變暖後變冷。"},{"en":"Warmed before going cold means temperature rose first and then fell later.","zh":"warmed before going cold 指溫度先上升，然後下降。"},{"en":"A room may warm before going cold if the heater runs briefly and then stops.","zh":"如果暖爐短暫運作後停止，房間可能先變暖後變冷。"},{"en":"Different effects can happen in sequence after one event.","zh":"一個事件之後可能依次出現不同效果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a two-stage temperature change.","zh":"這個短語描述兩階段溫度變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"plunged the atmosphere into chaos","meaning":"令大氣／生物圈陷入混亂","examples":[{"en":"The impact plunged the biosphere into chaos.","zh":"這次撞擊令生物圈陷入混亂。"},{"en":"Plunged the atmosphere into chaos means suddenly threw the air system into severe disorder.","zh":"plunged the atmosphere into chaos 指突然令大氣系統陷入嚴重混亂。"},{"en":"A factory explosion can plunge a neighbourhood into chaos if smoke and alarms spread everywhere.","zh":"如果煙霧和警報四處擴散，工廠爆炸可以令社區陷入混亂。"},{"en":"Dust, gases, and heat can disturb atmospheric conditions dramatically.","zh":"塵埃、氣體和熱力可以劇烈擾亂大氣狀況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sudden severe disruption.","zh":"這個短語描述突然的嚴重破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"in the aftermath of","meaning":"在……之後","examples":[{"en":"In the aftermath of the asteroid strike, dead animals became an important food source.","zh":"在小行星撞擊之後，死去動物成為重要食物來源。"},{"en":"In the aftermath of something means in the period after a major event, especially a damaging one.","zh":"in the aftermath of something 指重大事件，尤其災難之後的一段時期。"},{"en":"In the aftermath of a typhoon, families may repair homes and look for clean water.","zh":"颱風之後，家庭可能修理房屋並尋找清潔食水。"},{"en":"The aftermath often includes consequences that last longer than the event itself.","zh":"後續影響常比事件本身持續更久。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what happens after disaster.","zh":"這個短語集中於災難之後發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"asteroid strike","meaning":"小行星撞擊","examples":[{"en":"The asteroid strike caused catastrophic global changes.","zh":"小行星撞擊造成災難性全球變化。"},{"en":"An asteroid strike is the event of an asteroid hitting a planet or moon.","zh":"asteroid strike 指小行星撞擊行星或月球的事件。"},{"en":"A science animation may show an asteroid strike forming a crater.","zh":"科學動畫可能展示小行星撞擊形成隕石坑。"},{"en":"A large strike can throw dust into the air and change climate.","zh":"大型撞擊可以把塵埃拋入空氣並改變氣候。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a powerful space impact.","zh":"這個短語描述強大的太空撞擊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"dead animals","meaning":"死去的動物","examples":[{"en":"Dead animals were important for scavengers after the disaster.","zh":"災難後，死去的動物對食腐動物很重要。"},{"en":"Dead animals are animal bodies after life has ended.","zh":"dead animals 指生命結束後的動物屍體。"},{"en":"Vultures may feed on dead animals found in open land.","zh":"禿鷹可能以在開闊地發現的死去動物為食。"},{"en":"After a disaster, dead animals can become a food source for scavengers.","zh":"災難後，死去動物可以成為食腐動物的食物來源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to animal remains, not living prey.","zh":"這個短語指動物遺體，而不是活的獵物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"allowed shelter for","meaning":"為……提供庇護","examples":[{"en":"Water allowed some animals shelter from fire and blast damage.","zh":"水為一些動物提供庇護，使牠們避開火災和爆炸破壞。"},{"en":"Allowed shelter for means provided protection or a safe place for someone or something.","zh":"allowed shelter for 指為某人或某物提供保護或安全地方。"},{"en":"A covered bus stop allows shelter for passengers during heavy rain.","zh":"有蓋巴士站在大雨中為乘客提供庇護。"},{"en":"Shelter increases survival when danger comes from heat, wind, fire, or debris.","zh":"當危險來自熱力、風、火或碎片時，庇護會提高存活機會。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how a place or material provides protection.","zh":"這個短語顯示地方或物質如何提供保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"mammals of that time","meaning":"當時的哺乳類動物","examples":[{"en":"Mammals of that time were small burrowing creatures.","zh":"當時的哺乳類動物是會掘洞的小型生物。"},{"en":"Mammals of that time means mammals living during the period being discussed.","zh":"mammals of that time 指生活於正在討論時期的哺乳類。"},{"en":"Students studying the Ice Age may compare humans of that time with people today.","zh":"學生研究冰河時代時，可能比較當時的人類與今日人類。"},{"en":"Time-specific phrases help avoid confusing ancient animals with modern ones.","zh":"特定時間短語有助避免把古代動物與現代動物混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase places a group in a historical period.","zh":"這個短語把某群體放入歷史時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"consumed dead animals and plants","meaning":"食用死去的動植物","examples":[{"en":"Some creatures survived because they consumed dead animals and plants.","zh":"有些生物因食用死去的動植物而存活。"},{"en":"Consumed dead animals and plants means ate dead biological material.","zh":"consumed dead animals and plants 指吃死去的生物材料。"},{"en":"Worms consume dead leaves and help turn them into soil nutrients.","zh":"蠕蟲食用枯葉並幫助把它們變成泥土養分。"},{"en":"Animals that can eat dead matter may survive when fresh food is scarce.","zh":"能吃死亡物質的動物，在新鮮食物稀少時可能存活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes feeding on remains rather than living prey only.","zh":"這個短語描述以遺骸為食，而不只是吃活獵物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"lived in the shadows of trees","meaning":"生活在樹蔭下","examples":[{"en":"One option suggests that animals lived in the shadows of trees.","zh":"一個選項暗示動物生活在樹蔭下。"},{"en":"Lived in the shadows of trees means stayed under trees where shade was available.","zh":"lived in the shadows of trees 指停留在有陰影的樹下。"},{"en":"During summer, students may sit in the shadows of trees to avoid the sun.","zh":"夏天時，學生可能坐在樹蔭下避開陽光。"},{"en":"Shade can protect animals from heat, but it would not solve every disaster problem.","zh":"陰影可以保護動物免受高溫，但不能解決所有災難問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shaded habitat or shelter.","zh":"這個短語描述有樹蔭的棲息或庇護環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"a special class of animals","meaning":"一個特殊的動物類別","examples":[{"en":"Mammals became a special class of animals in evolutionary history.","zh":"哺乳類成為演化歷史中一個特殊的動物類別。"},{"en":"A special class of animals means a distinct animal group with important shared features.","zh":"special class of animals 指具有重要共同特徵的獨特動物群。"},{"en":"Birds are a special class of animals because feathers and flight shape many of their lives.","zh":"鳥類是一個特殊的動物類別，因為羽毛和飛行塑造了牠們許多生活方式。"},{"en":"A class becomes important when it develops many forms and affects ecosystems widely.","zh":"當一個類別發展出許多形式並廣泛影響生態系統，它就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a biologically significant group.","zh":"這個短語突出具有生物學重要性的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 95 - The Biggest Impact.pdf","sourcePage":25}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 96":[{"front":"the immunisation controversy","meaning":"免疫接種爭議","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the immunisation controversy and the anti-vaccination movement.","zh":"文章討論免疫接種爭議和反疫苗運動。"},{"en":"The immunisation controversy is the public argument about whether vaccines are safe, necessary, or trustworthy.","zh":"the immunisation controversy 指關於疫苗是否安全、必要或可信的公共爭論。"},{"en":"Parents may hear about the immunisation controversy when deciding whether to vaccinate a child.","zh":"父母在決定是否為孩子接種疫苗時，可能聽到免疫接種爭議。"},{"en":"The immunisation controversy can confuse people when false claims spread faster than medical evidence.","zh":"當虛假聲稱比醫學證據傳播得更快，免疫接種爭議可以令人困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a social and scientific dispute, not just a private medical choice.","zh":"這個短語描述社會和科學爭議，而不只是私人醫療選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lose ground to","meaning":"輸給；讓位於","examples":[{"en":"Science can lose ground to pseudoscience when people prefer comforting ideas.","zh":"當人們較喜歡令人安心的想法時，科學可能輸給偽科學。"},{"en":"To lose ground to something means to become less influential while the other side becomes stronger.","zh":"lose ground to something 指自己影響力減弱，而另一方變得更強。"},{"en":"A school’s healthy-eating campaign may lose ground to junk-food advertising if students see snacks everywhere.","zh":"如果學生到處都看到零食廣告，學校的健康飲食宣傳可能輸給垃圾食物廣告。"},{"en":"Clear facts can lose ground when emotional stories are repeated again and again.","zh":"當情緒化故事被反覆傳播，清晰事實可能讓位於那些故事。"},{"en":"This phrase shows one position becoming weaker in a competition of ideas.","zh":"這個短語顯示某立場在思想競爭中變弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pseudoscience","meaning":"偽科學","examples":[{"en":"Pseudoscience may seem more comforting than hard scientific evidence.","zh":"偽科學可能看起來比嚴謹科學證據更令人安心。"},{"en":"Pseudoscience is a belief or claim that sounds scientific but is not supported by proper evidence.","zh":"pseudoscience 指聽起來像科學，但沒有適當證據支持的信念或聲稱。"},{"en":"A product that claims to cure every illness without testing is an example of pseudoscience.","zh":"聲稱不用測試就能治癒所有疾病的產品，就是偽科學的例子。"},{"en":"Pseudoscience can mislead people because it uses scientific-sounding words without scientific proof.","zh":"偽科學可以誤導人，因為它使用聽似科學的詞語，卻沒有科學證明。"},{"en":"This word warns that something may look like science while failing to follow scientific methods.","zh":"這個詞提醒人，某事可能看似科學，卻沒有遵循科學方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"offer more comfort","meaning":"提供更多安慰","examples":[{"en":"Pseudoscience may offer more comfort than difficult scientific facts.","zh":"偽科學可能比困難的科學事實提供更多安慰。"},{"en":"To offer more comfort means to make people feel safer or less worried than another explanation does.","zh":"offer more comfort 指比另一種解釋更令人感到安全或較不擔心。"},{"en":"A simple excuse may offer more comfort than admitting that a student needs months of practice.","zh":"簡單藉口可能比承認學生需要數月練習提供更多安慰。"},{"en":"Comforting claims can attract people when the truth feels frightening or complicated.","zh":"當真相令人害怕或複雜，令人安心的聲稱可以吸引人。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why people may choose easy answers over accurate ones.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何人們可能選擇容易答案，而不是準確答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hard science","meaning":"嚴謹科學","examples":[{"en":"Hard science is sometimes less comforting than simple false claims.","zh":"嚴謹科學有時比簡單的虛假聲稱較不令人安心。"},{"en":"Hard science means careful scientific evidence based on testing, data, and logic.","zh":"hard science 指基於測試、數據和邏輯的仔細科學證據。"},{"en":"A doctor uses hard science when she explains treatment based on clinical studies.","zh":"醫生根據臨床研究解釋治療時，就是使用嚴謹科學。"},{"en":"Hard science may feel cold, but it helps people make safer decisions.","zh":"嚴謹科學可能感覺冷冰冰，但它幫助人作出更安全決定。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts evidence-based knowledge with guesses, rumours, or comforting myths.","zh":"這個短語把以證據為本的知識與猜測、謠言或令人安心的迷思作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"proven facts","meaning":"已證實的事實","examples":[{"en":"The writer argues that proven facts are often ignored.","zh":"作者認為已證實的事實常被忽視。"},{"en":"Proven facts are pieces of information shown to be true by strong evidence.","zh":"proven facts 指由有力證據顯示為真實的資料。"},{"en":"If a road is dangerous, accident records are proven facts that should guide safety plans.","zh":"如果某條道路危險，意外紀錄就是應指導安全計劃的已證實事實。"},{"en":"Ignoring proven facts can lead to poor decisions because people act on feelings instead of evidence.","zh":"忽視已證實的事實可以導致差劣決定，因為人們按感覺而非證據行事。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to information that has already been tested or confirmed.","zh":"這個短語指已經被測試或確認的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"indisputable logic","meaning":"無可爭辯的邏輯","examples":[{"en":"Indisputable logic is not always enough to persuade frightened parents.","zh":"無可爭辯的邏輯不一定足以說服受驚的父母。"},{"en":"Indisputable logic is reasoning that is so clear and strong that it is difficult to argue against.","zh":"indisputable logic 指非常清楚有力、難以反駁的推理。"},{"en":"A teacher may use indisputable logic to show why a student cannot pass without submitting assignments.","zh":"老師可能用無可爭辯的邏輯說明學生不交功課就不能合格。"},{"en":"Even strong logic may fail when people are afraid, angry, or misinformed.","zh":"即使邏輯有力，當人們害怕、憤怒或被誤導時，也可能失效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reasoning that should be convincing, though emotions may still resist it.","zh":"這個短語描述理應有說服力的推理，但情緒仍可能抗拒它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sufficiently consoling","meaning":"足以令人安心的","examples":[{"en":"Scientific facts may not feel sufficiently consoling to some people.","zh":"對有些人來說，科學事實可能不夠令人安心。"},{"en":"Sufficiently consoling means comforting enough to reduce fear, sadness, or anxiety.","zh":"sufficiently consoling 指足以減少恐懼、悲傷或焦慮。"},{"en":"A short apology may not be sufficiently consoling if a customer has lost a large amount of money.","zh":"如果顧客損失大筆金錢，簡短道歉可能不足以令人安心。"},{"en":"When facts are not emotionally comforting, people may look for easier explanations.","zh":"當事實在情緒上不令人安心，人們可能尋找更容易接受的解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether something gives enough emotional reassurance.","zh":"這個短語著重某事是否提供足夠情感安慰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"eliminate something from the equation","meaning":"把……排除在考慮之外","examples":[{"en":"Some people eliminate hard science from the equation.","zh":"有些人把嚴謹科學排除在考慮之外。"},{"en":"To eliminate something from the equation means to remove it from consideration when making a judgement.","zh":"eliminate something from the equation 指在作判斷時把某因素排除。"},{"en":"If a family ignores price completely, they eliminate cost from the equation when choosing a school.","zh":"如果家庭完全不理價格，他們選學校時就是把成本排除在考慮之外。"},{"en":"Removing evidence from the equation can make a decision feel easier but less accurate.","zh":"把證據排除在考慮之外，可以令決定感覺較容易，但較不準確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes leaving out an important factor.","zh":"這個短語描述把重要因素排除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"never has this been more distressing than","meaning":"從未有比……更令人痛心的情況","examples":[{"en":"Never has this been more distressing than with the anti-vaccination movement.","zh":"從未有比反疫苗運動更令人痛心的情況。"},{"en":"Never has this been more distressing than means this situation is the most upsetting example of a wider problem.","zh":"never has this been more distressing than 指這種情況是某個更大問題中最令人難過的例子。"},{"en":"Never has poor communication been more distressing than when families waited for hospital news.","zh":"當家屬等待醫院消息時，溝通不足從未有比這更令人痛心。"},{"en":"Writers use this structure to strongly emphasise a serious example.","zh":"作者使用這個結構來強烈突出嚴重例子。"},{"en":"This phrase means the case mentioned causes exceptional concern or sadness.","zh":"這個短語表示所提個案帶來特別大的憂慮或悲傷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"so-called","meaning":"所謂的","examples":[{"en":"The writer criticises the so-called anti-vaccination movement.","zh":"作者批評所謂的反疫苗運動。"},{"en":"So-called is used to show that a name or description may be doubtful, misleading, or not fully accepted.","zh":"so-called 用來表示某名稱或描述可能可疑、誤導或未被完全接受。"},{"en":"A shop’s so-called sale may not be real if prices were raised the week before.","zh":"如果商店上星期先加價，所謂的減價可能不是真減價。"},{"en":"Using so-called can signal criticism or distance from the label being used.","zh":"使用 so-called 可以表示批評或與該標籤保持距離。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests the writer does not fully respect the term.","zh":"這個短語常暗示作者並不完全認同該稱呼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"anti-vaccination movement","meaning":"反疫苗運動","examples":[{"en":"The anti-vaccination movement has influenced some parents.","zh":"反疫苗運動影響了一些父母。"},{"en":"The anti-vaccination movement is a group of beliefs and campaigns opposing vaccines.","zh":"anti-vaccination movement 指反對疫苗的一組信念和宣傳活動。"},{"en":"A parent may encounter the anti-vaccination movement through social media posts or online groups.","zh":"父母可能透過社交媒體帖文或網上群組接觸反疫苗運動。"},{"en":"This movement can reduce vaccination rates when fear spreads faster than evidence.","zh":"當恐懼比證據傳播得更快，這個運動可以降低疫苗接種率。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised opposition to vaccination, not normal questions asked before medical decisions.","zh":"這個短語指有組織地反對疫苗，而不是醫療決定前的正常提問。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the end result","meaning":"最終結果","examples":[{"en":"The end result has been the needless death of young children.","zh":"最終結果是不必要的幼童死亡。"},{"en":"The end result means the final outcome after a series of actions or events.","zh":"the end result 指一連串行動或事件之後的最終後果。"},{"en":"If students skip every practice test, the end result may be poor exam performance.","zh":"如果學生跳過每次練習測驗，最終結果可能是考試表現差。"},{"en":"Small choices can build up until the end result becomes serious.","zh":"小選擇可以累積，直到最終結果變得嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what finally happens, not only what people intended.","zh":"這個短語著重最終發生的事，而不只是人的原意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"needless death","meaning":"不必要的死亡","examples":[{"en":"The writer refers to the needless death of very young children.","zh":"作者提到非常年幼兒童的不必要死亡。"},{"en":"Needless death means death that could have been prevented.","zh":"needless death 指本可以避免的死亡。"},{"en":"A needless death may occur if a dangerous workplace ignores basic safety rules.","zh":"如果危險工作場所忽視基本安全規則，可能發生不必要的死亡。"},{"en":"Preventable illness can lead to needless deaths when people reject effective treatment.","zh":"當人們拒絕有效治療，可預防疾病可能導致不必要死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase carries moral weight because the loss did not have to happen.","zh":"這個短語帶有道德重量，因為這種損失本不必發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"helpless bystanders","meaning":"無助的旁觀受害者","examples":[{"en":"Very young children are described as the most helpless of bystanders.","zh":"非常年幼的孩子被描述為最無助的旁觀受害者。"},{"en":"Helpless bystanders are people affected by a situation but unable to protect themselves or control what happens.","zh":"helpless bystanders 指受情況影響，但無法保護自己或控制事情發展的人。"},{"en":"Children may become helpless bystanders when adults argue and make decisions for them.","zh":"當成年人爭論並替孩子作決定，孩子可能成為無助的旁觀受害者。"},{"en":"When public choices harm people who cannot choose, those people become helpless bystanders.","zh":"當公共選擇傷害無法選擇的人，那些人就成為無助的旁觀受害者。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses innocence, vulnerability, and lack of power.","zh":"這個短語強調無辜、脆弱和缺乏權力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"no end in sight","meaning":"看不到盡頭","examples":[{"en":"The writer fears that there is no end in sight.","zh":"作者擔心這件事看不到盡頭。"},{"en":"No end in sight means a problem seems likely to continue for a long time.","zh":"no end in sight 指問題似乎很可能長時間持續。"},{"en":"If complaints keep arriving every day, a school may feel there is no end in sight.","zh":"如果投訴每天不斷到來，學校可能覺得看不到盡頭。"},{"en":"A crisis feels worse when people cannot see when it will stop.","zh":"當人們看不到事情何時停止，危機會感覺更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses worry that a difficult situation will continue.","zh":"這個短語表達對困難情況會持續的憂慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"long and distinguished track record","meaning":"悠久而卓越的往績","examples":[{"en":"Vaccination has a long and distinguished track record.","zh":"疫苗接種有悠久而卓越的往績。"},{"en":"A long and distinguished track record is a history of strong, respected, and successful performance.","zh":"long and distinguished track record 指長期、受尊重且成功的表現紀錄。"},{"en":"A teacher with a long and distinguished track record has helped many students improve over many years.","zh":"有悠久而卓越往績的老師多年來幫助許多學生進步。"},{"en":"A strong track record builds trust because people can see past results.","zh":"強大的往績會建立信任，因為人們看得到過往成果。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when something has proved its value over time.","zh":"當某事物隨時間證明其價值時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be under assault","meaning":"受到攻擊","examples":[{"en":"Vaccination is now under assault from anti-vaccination groups.","zh":"疫苗接種現在受到反疫苗團體攻擊。"},{"en":"To be under assault means to be strongly attacked or criticised.","zh":"be under assault 指受到強烈攻擊或批評。"},{"en":"A school policy may be under assault if parents, newspapers, and politicians all attack it.","zh":"如果家長、報紙和政治人物都攻擊某校政，它可能受到攻擊。"},{"en":"When an idea is under assault, its supporters may need to explain it more clearly.","zh":"當某想法受到攻擊，其支持者可能需要更清楚解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes heavy pressure or criticism, not necessarily physical violence.","zh":"這個短語描述沉重壓力或批評，不一定是身體暴力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"smallpox","meaning":"天花","examples":[{"en":"Smallpox was eradicated through immunisation programmes.","zh":"天花透過免疫接種計劃被根除。"},{"en":"Smallpox was a serious infectious disease that caused fever, skin blisters, and many deaths.","zh":"smallpox 指一種嚴重傳染病，會造成發燒、皮膚水疱和大量死亡。"},{"en":"History lessons may discuss smallpox when explaining how vaccines changed public health.","zh":"歷史課解釋疫苗如何改變公共健康時，可能討論天花。"},{"en":"The removal of smallpox shows how organised vaccination can protect whole populations.","zh":"天花被消除顯示有組織疫苗接種如何保護整個人口。"},{"en":"This word refers to a disease that once killed many people but has been eliminated globally.","zh":"這個詞指曾殺死許多人但已在全球被消除的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"over half a billion","meaning":"超過五億","examples":[{"en":"Smallpox killed over half a billion human beings throughout history.","zh":"天花縱觀歷史殺死超過五億人。"},{"en":"Over half a billion means more than 500 million.","zh":"over half a billion 指超過五億。"},{"en":"Over half a billion people may use a popular app if it spreads across many countries.","zh":"如果一個熱門應用程式在許多國家傳播，可能有超過五億人使用。"},{"en":"Such a large number helps readers understand the enormous scale of the problem.","zh":"這麼大的數字幫助讀者理解問題規模極大。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for very large quantities.","zh":"這個短語用於非常大的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"throughout history","meaning":"縱觀歷史","examples":[{"en":"Smallpox killed huge numbers of people throughout history.","zh":"縱觀歷史，天花殺死了大量人口。"},{"en":"Throughout history means during many different periods in the past.","zh":"throughout history 指在過去許多不同時期中。"},{"en":"Throughout history, communities have used stories to teach children values.","zh":"縱觀歷史，社區一直用故事教孩子價值觀。"},{"en":"A problem that appears throughout history is not limited to one country or one generation.","zh":"縱觀歷史都出現的問題，並不限於一個國家或一代人。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a very long historical perspective.","zh":"這個短語給出很長遠的歷史視角。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be eradicated","meaning":"被根除","examples":[{"en":"Smallpox was eradicated through vaccination.","zh":"天花透過疫苗接種被根除。"},{"en":"To be eradicated means to be completely removed or destroyed.","zh":"be eradicated 指被完全消除或摧毀。"},{"en":"A city may try to eradicate mosquito breeding sites by removing standing water.","zh":"城市可能透過清除積水來根除蚊蟲滋生地。"},{"en":"A disease can be eradicated only when it no longer spreads anywhere.","zh":"只有當疾病不再在任何地方傳播，才可說它被根除。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete elimination, not just reduction.","zh":"這個短語描述完全消除，而不只是減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be removed from the face of the Earth","meaning":"從地球上被徹底消除","examples":[{"en":"Smallpox was completely removed from the face of the Earth.","zh":"天花從地球上被徹底消除。"},{"en":"To be removed from the face of the Earth means to disappear completely from the world.","zh":"be removed from the face of the Earth 指從世界上完全消失。"},{"en":"A harmful product may be removed from the market, but removing a disease from the Earth is much harder.","zh":"有害產品可能從市場下架，但把疾病從地球上徹底消除困難得多。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds dramatic because it describes total disappearance everywhere.","zh":"這個短語聽起來很強烈，因為它描述在所有地方完全消失。"},{"en":"It is stronger than saying something became rare.","zh":"它比說某事變得罕見更強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"via immunisation programmes","meaning":"透過免疫接種計劃","examples":[{"en":"Smallpox was eradicated via immunisation programmes.","zh":"天花透過免疫接種計劃被根除。"},{"en":"Via immunisation programmes means through organised plans to vaccinate people.","zh":"via immunisation programmes 指透過有組織地為人接種疫苗的計劃。"},{"en":"A country may reduce measles cases via immunisation programmes in schools and clinics.","zh":"一個國家可能透過學校和診所的免疫接種計劃減少麻疹個案。"},{"en":"These programmes work best when many people receive vaccines on time.","zh":"當許多人準時接種疫苗，這些計劃最有效。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the method used to prevent disease.","zh":"這個短語解釋預防疾病所使用的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"immunisation programmes","meaning":"免疫接種計劃","examples":[{"en":"Immunisation programmes helped eliminate smallpox.","zh":"免疫接種計劃幫助消除天花。"},{"en":"Immunisation programmes are organised public-health plans that provide vaccines to a population.","zh":"immunisation programmes 指向人口提供疫苗的有組織公共衛生計劃。"},{"en":"A school immunisation programme may remind parents when children need routine vaccines.","zh":"學校免疫接種計劃可能提醒家長孩子何時需要常規疫苗。"},{"en":"Strong programmes can protect people who are too young or too ill to be vaccinated.","zh":"強大的計劃可以保護太年幼或太病弱而不能接種疫苗的人。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to planned vaccination systems, not one isolated injection.","zh":"這個短語指有計劃的疫苗接種系統，而不是一次孤立注射。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"polio","meaning":"小兒麻痺症","examples":[{"en":"Polio is now virtually a thing of the past in many places.","zh":"小兒麻痺症現在在許多地方幾乎已成過去。"},{"en":"Polio is an infectious disease that can damage the nervous system and cause paralysis.","zh":"polio 指一種可損害神經系統並造成癱瘓的傳染病。"},{"en":"Public-health lessons may mention polio to show why vaccination campaigns matter.","zh":"公共衛生課可能提到小兒麻痺症，以顯示疫苗接種運動為何重要。"},{"en":"When vaccination rates are high, polio becomes rare in many communities.","zh":"當疫苗接種率高，小兒麻痺症在許多社區會變得罕見。"},{"en":"This word names a serious childhood disease once feared by many families.","zh":"這個詞命名一種曾令許多家庭恐懼的嚴重兒童疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rubella","meaning":"德國麻疹；風疹","examples":[{"en":"Rubella is one of the diseases controlled by vaccination.","zh":"德國麻疹是由疫苗控制的疾病之一。"},{"en":"Rubella is an infectious disease also known as German measles.","zh":"rubella 指一種傳染病，又稱德國麻疹或風疹。"},{"en":"A health clinic may offer vaccines that protect against rubella and other diseases.","zh":"健康診所可能提供預防德國麻疹和其他疾病的疫苗。"},{"en":"Controlling rubella is important because infection during pregnancy can harm unborn babies.","zh":"控制德國麻疹很重要，因為懷孕期間感染可能傷害胎兒。"},{"en":"This word refers to a preventable disease included in the MMR vaccine.","zh":"這個詞指 MMR 疫苗涵蓋的一種可預防疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"whooping cough","meaning":"百日咳","examples":[{"en":"Whooping cough once caused serious illness among children.","zh":"百日咳曾經在兒童中造成嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"Whooping cough is a contagious disease that causes severe coughing fits.","zh":"whooping cough 指一種會造成嚴重陣發性咳嗽的傳染病。"},{"en":"A baby with whooping cough may struggle to breathe after repeated coughing.","zh":"患百日咳的嬰兒在反覆咳嗽後可能呼吸困難。"},{"en":"Vaccination helps reduce the spread of whooping cough in schools and families.","zh":"疫苗接種有助減少百日咳在學校和家庭中傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase names a preventable disease that can be dangerous for young children.","zh":"這個短語命名一種對幼童可能危險的可預防疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"measles","meaning":"麻疹","examples":[{"en":"Measles can return when vaccination rates fall.","zh":"當疫苗接種率下降，麻疹可能再次出現。"},{"en":"Measles is a highly contagious disease that can cause fever, rash, and serious complications.","zh":"measles 指一種高度傳染性疾病，可造成發燒、皮疹和嚴重併發症。"},{"en":"A school may warn parents about measles if one infected child attends class.","zh":"如果一名受感染兒童上課，學校可能提醒家長注意麻疹。"},{"en":"Low vaccination rates make it easier for measles to spread through a community.","zh":"疫苗接種率低，會令麻疹更容易在社區傳播。"},{"en":"This word refers to a preventable disease that can become dangerous when outbreaks occur.","zh":"這個詞指一種可預防疾病，在爆發時可能變得危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a slew of","meaning":"大量；一連串","examples":[{"en":"A slew of diseases once decimated young people.","zh":"大量疾病曾經奪去年輕人的生命。"},{"en":"A slew of means a large number of something.","zh":"a slew of 指大量某物。"},{"en":"A student may face a slew of assignments before the end of term.","zh":"學期結束前，學生可能面對一連串功課。"},{"en":"When a slew of problems arrive together, people may feel overwhelmed.","zh":"當大量問題同時出現，人們可能感到不勝負荷。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and stresses quantity.","zh":"這個短語較口語，強調數量多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"routinely decimate","meaning":"經常大量奪去……的生命","examples":[{"en":"Several diseases routinely decimated young people in the past.","zh":"過去有幾種疾病經常大量奪去年輕人的生命。"},{"en":"To routinely decimate a group means to regularly destroy or kill a large part of it.","zh":"routinely decimate a group 指經常摧毀或殺死該群體的大部分。"},{"en":"Severe storms can routinely decimate crops in villages without proper flood protection.","zh":"在缺乏適當防洪的村莊，嚴重風暴可能經常大量摧毀農作物。"},{"en":"If disease routinely decimates a population, families experience repeated loss.","zh":"如果疾病經常大量奪去人口生命，家庭會反覆經歷喪失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frequent and serious destruction.","zh":"這個短語描述頻繁而嚴重的破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"virtually a thing of the past","meaning":"幾乎已成過去","examples":[{"en":"Some serious childhood diseases are now virtually things of the past.","zh":"有些嚴重兒童疾病現在幾乎已成過去。"},{"en":"Virtually a thing of the past means almost no longer present or common.","zh":"virtually a thing of the past 指幾乎不再存在或不再常見。"},{"en":"In some cities, paper bus tickets are virtually a thing of the past because people use cards or phones.","zh":"在一些城市，紙本巴士票幾乎已成過去，因為人們使用卡或手機。"},{"en":"A danger can become virtually a thing of the past when prevention works well.","zh":"當預防措施有效，某種危險可以幾乎已成過去。"},{"en":"This phrase means nearly gone, not completely impossible.","zh":"這個短語表示幾乎消失，而不是完全不可能發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"infant mortality","meaning":"嬰兒死亡率","examples":[{"en":"Vaccination helped reduce high infant mortality.","zh":"疫苗接種幫助降低高嬰兒死亡率。"},{"en":"Infant mortality is the death of babies before they reach their first birthday.","zh":"infant mortality 指嬰兒在一歲前死亡的情況。"},{"en":"Hospitals track infant mortality to understand whether newborn care is improving.","zh":"醫院追蹤嬰兒死亡率，以了解新生兒護理是否改善。"},{"en":"Better sanitation, vaccines, and medical care can reduce infant mortality.","zh":"更好的衛生、疫苗和醫療護理可以降低嬰兒死亡率。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in public health to measure how safe early life is.","zh":"這個短語用於公共衛生，以量度生命早期有多安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"short life spans","meaning":"短壽命","examples":[{"en":"Modern medicine helped end the days of short life spans.","zh":"現代醫學幫助終結短壽命的年代。"},{"en":"Short life spans are lives that end much earlier than expected because of disease, poverty, or poor conditions.","zh":"short life spans 指因疾病、貧窮或惡劣條件而遠早於預期結束的生命。"},{"en":"In the past, short life spans were common when infections could not be treated well.","zh":"在過去，當感染無法被妥善治療，短壽命很常見。"},{"en":"Better healthcare can increase life spans by preventing early deaths.","zh":"更好醫療可以透過預防早死來延長壽命。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the length of human life being unusually limited.","zh":"這個短語描述人的生命長度受到不尋常限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"nasty, brutish lives","meaning":"惡劣而艱苦的生活","examples":[{"en":"The writer contrasts modern health with nasty, brutish lives in the past.","zh":"作者把現代健康與過去惡劣而艱苦的生活作對比。"},{"en":"Nasty, brutish lives are lives that are harsh, unsafe, painful, and often short.","zh":"nasty, brutish lives 指嚴酷、不安全、痛苦且通常短暫的生活。"},{"en":"Before clean water and basic medicine, many poor families lived nasty, brutish lives.","zh":"在清潔食水和基本醫療出現前，許多貧困家庭過着惡劣而艱苦的生活。"},{"en":"Disease, hunger, and violence can make daily life nasty and brutish.","zh":"疾病、飢餓和暴力可以令日常生活變得惡劣而艱苦。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly describes life as unpleasant and cruel.","zh":"這個短語強烈描述生活令人痛苦而殘酷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"long gone","meaning":"早已過去","examples":[{"en":"The days of high infant mortality are long gone.","zh":"高嬰兒死亡率的日子早已過去。"},{"en":"Long gone means something ended or disappeared a long time ago.","zh":"long gone 指某事很久以前已經結束或消失。"},{"en":"In many offices, the days of sending every document by fax are long gone.","zh":"在許多辦公室，所有文件都用傳真發送的日子早已過去。"},{"en":"When a problem is long gone, younger people may not understand how serious it once was.","zh":"當問題早已過去，年輕人可能不明白它曾經有多嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses distance from the past.","zh":"這個短語強調與過去的距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"owe it all to","meaning":"全靠；都歸功於","examples":[{"en":"We owe much of this progress to disease prevention.","zh":"我們把這大部分進步都歸功於疾病預防。"},{"en":"To owe it all to something means to say that success happened because of that thing.","zh":"owe it all to something 指表示成功是因某事而出現。"},{"en":"A student may owe her improvement to daily reading and patient feedback.","zh":"學生可能把自己的進步歸功於每日閱讀和耐心回饋。"},{"en":"Public health progress often owes much to prevention, not only treatment.","zh":"公共衛生進步往往很大程度歸功於預防，而不只是治療。"},{"en":"This phrase shows gratitude or cause.","zh":"這個短語顯示感激或原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"crucial insight into","meaning":"對……的重要見解","examples":[{"en":"Vaccination was a crucial insight into disease prevention.","zh":"疫苗接種是對疾病預防的重要見解。"},{"en":"A crucial insight into something is an important understanding that changes how people deal with it.","zh":"crucial insight into something 指能改變人們處理某事方式的重要理解。"},{"en":"Realising that students fear mistakes can be a crucial insight into poor speaking performance.","zh":"意識到學生害怕犯錯，可能是理解口語表現差的重要見解。"},{"en":"A crucial insight can lead to better solutions because it reveals how a problem works.","zh":"重要見解可以帶來更好解決方法，因為它揭示問題如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important discovery or understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述重要發現或理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"disease prevention","meaning":"疾病預防","examples":[{"en":"Vaccination is an important form of disease prevention.","zh":"疫苗接種是疾病預防的重要形式。"},{"en":"Disease prevention means actions taken to stop illness before it starts or spreads.","zh":"disease prevention 指在疾病開始或傳播前阻止它的行動。"},{"en":"Washing hands, using clean water, and vaccination are forms of disease prevention.","zh":"洗手、使用清潔食水和接種疫苗都是疾病預防形式。"},{"en":"Prevention can save lives because it reduces the need for later treatment.","zh":"預防可以拯救生命，因為它減少之後治療的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on stopping illness early, not only curing it afterwards.","zh":"這個短語著重及早阻止疾病，而不只是事後治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"part of the problem","meaning":"問題的一部分","examples":[{"en":"The success of vaccination is part of the problem.","zh":"疫苗接種的成功是問題的一部分。"},{"en":"Part of the problem means one factor that helps create or continue a difficulty.","zh":"part of the problem 指造成或延續困難的其中一個因素。"},{"en":"If students never see accidents, their confidence may become part of the problem in safety training.","zh":"如果學生從未見過意外，他們的自信可能成為安全訓練中問題的一部分。"},{"en":"Success can become part of the problem when people forget why protection is still needed.","zh":"當人們忘記為何仍需要保護，成功可以成為問題的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that even something positive can create a hidden difficulty.","zh":"這個短語顯示即使正面事物也可能造成隱藏困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"once terrible epidemics","meaning":"曾經可怕的流行病","examples":[{"en":"Once terrible epidemics now lie outside human memory.","zh":"曾經可怕的流行病現在已超出人們的記憶範圍。"},{"en":"Once terrible epidemics are disease outbreaks that were frightening in the past but are no longer remembered by many people.","zh":"once terrible epidemics 指過去令人恐懼，但現在很多人已不記得的疾病爆發。"},{"en":"A village may forget once terrible floods after decades of good drainage.","zh":"一條村在數十年良好排水後，可能忘記曾經可怕的水災。"},{"en":"When past dangers disappear from memory, people may underestimate current protection.","zh":"當過去危險從記憶中消失，人們可能低估現有保護。"},{"en":"This phrase points to serious threats that have faded from public awareness.","zh":"這個短語指已從公眾意識淡出的嚴重威脅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lie outside human memory","meaning":"已超出人們的記憶範圍","examples":[{"en":"Many past epidemics now lie outside human memory.","zh":"許多過去的流行病現在已超出人們的記憶範圍。"},{"en":"To lie outside human memory means to be so far in the past that most living people do not remember it.","zh":"lie outside human memory 指事情久遠到大多數在世的人都不記得。"},{"en":"Some old wars lie outside human memory, so young people learn about them only from books.","zh":"有些舊戰爭已超出人們的記憶範圍，所以年輕人只能從書本學習。"},{"en":"When suffering lies outside memory, people may forget why safeguards exist.","zh":"當痛苦超出記憶範圍，人們可能忘記為何需要防護措施。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that direct personal memory has disappeared.","zh":"這個短語強調直接個人記憶已經消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a growing number of people","meaning":"越來越多人","examples":[{"en":"A growing number of people believe vaccinations are unnecessary.","zh":"越來越多人相信疫苗接種不再必要。"},{"en":"A growing number of people means more and more people over time.","zh":"a growing number of people 指隨時間越來越多的人。"},{"en":"A growing number of people now use mobile payment instead of cash.","zh":"越來越多人現在使用手機支付，而不是現金。"},{"en":"When a growing number of people accept a false idea, public action becomes harder.","zh":"當越來越多人接受錯誤想法，公共行動會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increasing group.","zh":"這個短語描述正在增加的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be convinced that","meaning":"深信","examples":[{"en":"Some people are convinced that vaccinations are no longer necessary.","zh":"有些人深信疫苗接種不再必要。"},{"en":"To be convinced that means to strongly believe something is true.","zh":"be convinced that 指強烈相信某事是真的。"},{"en":"A student may be convinced that practice is useless after failing one test.","zh":"學生可能在一次測驗失敗後深信練習沒有用。"},{"en":"People who are convinced of an idea may reject evidence that challenges it.","zh":"深信某想法的人可能拒絕挑戰該想法的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong belief, not necessarily correct belief.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈信念，不一定是正確信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"no longer necessary","meaning":"不再必要","examples":[{"en":"Some people wrongly believe vaccinations are no longer necessary.","zh":"有些人錯誤地相信疫苗接種不再必要。"},{"en":"No longer necessary means not needed anymore.","zh":"no longer necessary 指不再需要。"},{"en":"A printed timetable may be no longer necessary if everyone uses a school app.","zh":"如果人人都使用學校應用程式，紙本時間表可能不再必要。"},{"en":"Something can seem no longer necessary when its earlier success hides the original danger.","zh":"當早前成功掩蓋原本危險，某事可能看似不再必要。"},{"en":"This phrase should be used carefully when the need may only look absent.","zh":"當需要可能只是表面上消失時，這個短語應小心使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"adverse effects","meaning":"不良反應；副作用","examples":[{"en":"Some parents worry about the adverse effects of vaccines.","zh":"有些父母擔心疫苗的不良反應。"},{"en":"Adverse effects are unwanted or harmful effects after a medicine, treatment, or action.","zh":"adverse effects 指藥物、治療或行動之後出現的不想要或有害影響。"},{"en":"A patient should tell a doctor if a new medicine causes adverse effects.","zh":"如果新藥造成副作用，病人應告訴醫生。"},{"en":"Fear of adverse effects can make people hesitate, even when serious risks are very rare.","zh":"對不良反應的恐懼可以令人猶豫，即使嚴重風險非常罕見。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in medical or safety discussions.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於醫療或安全討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"outweigh the benefits","meaning":"大於其好處","examples":[{"en":"They believe the small risk of adverse effects outweighs the benefits.","zh":"他們相信不良反應的小風險大於其好處。"},{"en":"To outweigh the benefits means to be more important or serious than the good effects.","zh":"outweigh the benefits 指比好處更重要或更嚴重。"},{"en":"If a trip is extremely expensive and unsafe, the risks may outweigh the benefits.","zh":"如果旅行極昂貴又不安全，風險可能大於其好處。"},{"en":"People make poor decisions when they misjudge whether risks really outweigh benefits.","zh":"當人們錯誤判斷風險是否真的大於好處，就會作出差劣決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when comparing harm with advantage.","zh":"這個短語用於比較傷害與優點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"genetic disorders","meaning":"遺傳疾病","examples":[{"en":"Some genetic disorders emerge around the age of two.","zh":"有些遺傳疾病在大約兩歲時出現。"},{"en":"Genetic disorders are health conditions caused partly or fully by a person’s genes.","zh":"genetic disorders 指部分或完全由基因造成的健康狀況。"},{"en":"Doctors may test for genetic disorders when several relatives have the same condition.","zh":"當幾名親屬有同一疾病，醫生可能檢查遺傳疾病。"},{"en":"Some genetic disorders become visible only after a child grows older.","zh":"有些遺傳疾病只在孩子長大後才變得可見。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to conditions linked to inherited biology.","zh":"這個短語指與遺傳生物因素相關的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"brain impairment","meaning":"腦功能受損","examples":[{"en":"Some disorders related to brain impairment appear in early childhood.","zh":"有些與腦功能受損有關的疾病在幼兒期出現。"},{"en":"Brain impairment means reduced or damaged brain function.","zh":"brain impairment 指腦部功能減弱或受損。"},{"en":"A serious head injury may cause brain impairment that affects memory or movement.","zh":"嚴重頭部受傷可能造成影響記憶或活動的腦功能受損。"},{"en":"Early signs of brain impairment may lead doctors to recommend careful assessment.","zh":"腦功能受損的早期跡象可能令醫生建議仔細評估。"},{"en":"This phrase describes problems in how the brain works.","zh":"這個短語描述大腦運作方面的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"emerge at around","meaning":"在大約……時出現","examples":[{"en":"Some symptoms emerge at around two years of age.","zh":"有些症狀在大約兩歲時出現。"},{"en":"To emerge at around a time means to begin to appear approximately then.","zh":"emerge at around a time 指大約在該時間開始出現。"},{"en":"Reading problems may emerge at around Primary 2 when texts become longer.","zh":"當文章變長，閱讀問題可能在大約小二時出現。"},{"en":"When symptoms emerge around the same time as another event, people may wrongly connect them.","zh":"當症狀在與另一事件差不多時間出現，人們可能錯誤地把兩者連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate time of appearance.","zh":"這個短語給出大約出現時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"receive vaccinations","meaning":"接種疫苗","examples":[{"en":"Babies receive vaccinations during early childhood.","zh":"嬰兒在幼兒期接種疫苗。"},{"en":"To receive vaccinations means to be given vaccines to help protect against disease.","zh":"receive vaccinations 指接受疫苗，以幫助預防疾病。"},{"en":"Children may receive vaccinations at clinics, hospitals, or school health programmes.","zh":"兒童可能在診所、醫院或學校健康計劃中接種疫苗。"},{"en":"Receiving vaccinations on schedule helps build protection before exposure to disease.","zh":"按時接種疫苗有助在接觸疾病前建立保護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the act of being vaccinated.","zh":"這個短語描述接受疫苗接種的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"vaccinated group","meaning":"已接種疫苗的群體","examples":[{"en":"A vaccinated group may include children who later show symptoms of autism.","zh":"已接種疫苗的群體可能包括之後出現自閉症症狀的兒童。"},{"en":"A vaccinated group is a group of people who have received a vaccine.","zh":"vaccinated group 指已接受疫苗的一群人。"},{"en":"Researchers may compare a vaccinated group with an unvaccinated group to study disease rates.","zh":"研究人員可能比較已接種疫苗的群體和未接種群體，以研究疾病率。"},{"en":"If a health condition appears later in some members, that does not automatically prove the vaccine caused it.","zh":"如果某健康狀況之後在部分成員身上出現，這不會自動證明是疫苗造成。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a group by vaccination status.","zh":"這個短語按疫苗接種狀態識別群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be destined to develop","meaning":"注定會發展成","examples":[{"en":"Some children may be destined to develop autism for genetic reasons.","zh":"有些孩子可能因基因原因注定會發展成自閉症。"},{"en":"To be destined to develop something means to be very likely to develop it because of factors already present.","zh":"be destined to develop something 指因已存在的因素而很可能發展出某狀況。"},{"en":"A plant with weak roots may be destined to develop problems if it receives too much water.","zh":"根部弱的植物如果澆水太多，可能注定會發展出問題。"},{"en":"When a condition is already likely to appear, people may wrongly blame a nearby event.","zh":"當某狀況本來就很可能出現，人們可能錯誤怪責附近發生的事件。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an outcome was going to happen anyway.","zh":"這個短語暗示某結果本來就會發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"autism","meaning":"自閉症","examples":[{"en":"Autism may appear around the same age as routine vaccinations.","zh":"自閉症可能在與常規疫苗接種差不多的年齡出現。"},{"en":"Autism is a developmental condition that affects communication, behaviour, and social interaction in different ways.","zh":"autism 指一種發展狀況，會以不同方式影響溝通、行為和社交互動。"},{"en":"A child with autism may need support with language, routines, or sensory sensitivity.","zh":"有自閉症的孩子可能需要語言、日常規律或感官敏感方面的支援。"},{"en":"Because early signs often appear in childhood, timing can be misunderstood by worried parents.","zh":"因為早期跡象常在童年出現，憂心父母可能誤解時間上的巧合。"},{"en":"This word describes a neurodevelopmental condition, not a disease caused by ordinary parenting.","zh":"這個詞描述一種神經發展狀況，而不是由普通教養造成的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"observable symptoms","meaning":"可觀察到的症狀","examples":[{"en":"Observable symptoms may appear after a vaccination.","zh":"可觀察到的症狀可能在疫苗接種後出現。"},{"en":"Observable symptoms are signs of a condition that people can see or notice.","zh":"observable symptoms 指人們可以看見或注意到的狀況跡象。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice observable symptoms such as coughing, tiredness, or difficulty focusing.","zh":"老師可能注意到咳嗽、疲倦或難以集中等可觀察到的症狀。"},{"en":"Seeing symptoms after an event does not automatically mean the event caused them.","zh":"在某事件後看到症狀，不會自動表示該事件造成症狀。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on visible signs, not hidden causes.","zh":"這個短語著重可見跡象，而不是隱藏原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"distraught parents","meaning":"極度悲痛的父母","examples":[{"en":"Distraught parents may link one event to another.","zh":"極度悲痛的父母可能把一件事與另一件事聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Distraught parents are parents who are extremely upset, frightened, or emotionally overwhelmed.","zh":"distraught parents 指極度難過、害怕或情緒崩潰的父母。"},{"en":"Distraught parents may call the school immediately if their child is injured during a trip.","zh":"如果孩子在旅行中受傷，極度悲痛的父母可能立即致電學校。"},{"en":"Strong fear can make distraught parents search urgently for a clear explanation.","zh":"強烈恐懼可以令極度悲痛的父母急切尋找清楚解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional pain and panic, not careful scientific judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述情緒痛苦和恐慌，而不是仔細科學判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"link one event to another","meaning":"把一件事與另一件事聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"Parents may mistakenly link one event to another.","zh":"父母可能錯誤地把一件事與另一件事聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To link one event to another means to believe that two events are connected.","zh":"link one event to another 指相信兩件事之間有關聯。"},{"en":"A student may link a headache to a new food even if stress was the real cause.","zh":"學生可能把頭痛與新食物聯繫起來，即使真正原因是壓力。"},{"en":"People often link events wrongly when they happen close together in time.","zh":"當事件時間上接近，人們常錯誤地把它們聯繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes connecting events, correctly or incorrectly.","zh":"這個短語描述把事件連接起來，不論正確與否。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"misattribution","meaning":"錯誤歸因","examples":[{"en":"This misattribution is strengthened by misinformation online.","zh":"這種錯誤歸因因網上錯誤資訊而加強。"},{"en":"Misattribution means wrongly assigning a cause to something.","zh":"misattribution 指把某事錯誤歸因於某個原因。"},{"en":"If a student blames a bad grade on bad luck instead of not revising, that is misattribution.","zh":"如果學生把差成績歸咎於運氣差，而不是沒有溫習，那就是錯誤歸因。"},{"en":"Misattribution can spread when people share emotional stories without checking evidence.","zh":"當人們不核查證據就分享情緒化故事，錯誤歸因可以傳播。"},{"en":"This word describes blaming the wrong cause.","zh":"這個詞描述怪錯原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be compounded by","meaning":"因……而加劇","examples":[{"en":"The misattribution is compounded by the Internet.","zh":"這種錯誤歸因因互聯網而加劇。"},{"en":"To be compounded by something means to be made worse by it.","zh":"be compounded by something 指因某事而變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"A student’s stress may be compounded by poor sleep and family pressure.","zh":"學生壓力可能因睡眠差和家庭壓力而加劇。"},{"en":"False information is compounded when social media repeats it to more people.","zh":"當社交媒體把錯誤資訊傳給更多人，問題就會加劇。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an extra factor making a problem more serious.","zh":"這個短語顯示額外因素令問題更嚴重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"host a network of","meaning":"容納一個……網絡","examples":[{"en":"The Internet hosts a network of anti-vaccination websites.","zh":"互聯網容納一個反疫苗網站網絡。"},{"en":"To host a network of something means to provide a place where many connected groups or sites exist.","zh":"host a network of something 指提供地方，讓許多互相連接的群體或網站存在。"},{"en":"A university website may host a network of student clubs and project pages.","zh":"大學網站可能容納一個學生學會和項目頁面的網絡。"},{"en":"When a platform hosts harmful networks, false ideas can spread quickly between users.","zh":"當平台容納有害網絡，錯誤想法可以在用戶之間快速傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase describes providing space for connected activity.","zh":"這個短語描述為互相連接的活動提供空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sprawling network","meaning":"龐大而分散的網絡","examples":[{"en":"The Internet hosts a sprawling network of lobby groups and websites.","zh":"互聯網容納一個由游說團體和網站組成的龐大而分散的網絡。"},{"en":"A sprawling network is a large, spread-out, and loosely connected system.","zh":"sprawling network 指大型、分散且鬆散連接的系統。"},{"en":"A city may have a sprawling network of buses, minibuses, and train lines.","zh":"城市可能有由巴士、小巴和鐵路組成的龐大而分散交通網絡。"},{"en":"A sprawling online network can be hard to control because it has many separate parts.","zh":"龐大而分散的網上網絡可能難以控制，因為它有許多分開部分。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something large and widely spread.","zh":"這個短語暗示某物規模大且廣泛分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lobby groups","meaning":"游說團體","examples":[{"en":"Anti-vaccination lobby groups spread their claims online.","zh":"反疫苗游說團體在網上傳播其聲稱。"},{"en":"Lobby groups are organised groups that try to influence public opinion or government decisions.","zh":"lobby groups 指試圖影響公眾意見或政府決定的有組織團體。"},{"en":"Environmental lobby groups may ask the government to reduce plastic waste.","zh":"環保游說團體可能要求政府減少塑膠廢物。"},{"en":"Lobby groups can shape debate when they organise messages, websites, and campaigns.","zh":"當游說團體組織訊息、網站和宣傳活動，它們可以塑造辯論。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised pressure groups.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的壓力團體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"unsubstantiated claims","meaning":"未經證實的聲稱","examples":[{"en":"Many anti-vaccination websites are filled with unsubstantiated claims.","zh":"許多反疫苗網站充滿未經證實的聲稱。"},{"en":"Unsubstantiated claims are statements made without reliable evidence.","zh":"unsubstantiated claims 指沒有可靠證據支持的說法。"},{"en":"A shop should not advertise unsubstantiated claims about a product curing illness.","zh":"商店不應宣傳產品能治病的未經證實聲稱。"},{"en":"Such claims can spread fear because people may believe them before checking facts.","zh":"這類聲稱可以散播恐懼，因為人們可能在核查事實前就相信。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a statement has not been properly supported.","zh":"這個短語提醒某說法未獲適當支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fraudulent research","meaning":"欺詐性研究","examples":[{"en":"Some websites rely on fraudulent research.","zh":"有些網站依賴欺詐性研究。"},{"en":"Fraudulent research is research that involves deception, false data, or dishonest methods.","zh":"fraudulent research 指涉及欺騙、虛假數據或不誠實方法的研究。"},{"en":"A university may withdraw a paper if it discovers fraudulent research.","zh":"如果大學發現欺詐性研究，可能撤回論文。"},{"en":"Fraudulent research damages trust because readers think the findings were produced honestly.","zh":"欺詐性研究會損害信任，因為讀者以為研究結果是誠實產生的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research that is not merely wrong, but dishonest.","zh":"這個短語描述的不只是錯誤研究，而是不誠實研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"anecdotal evidence","meaning":"個別事例證據；軼事證據","examples":[{"en":"Anecdotal evidence is not the same as reliable scientific evidence.","zh":"個別事例證據不等於可靠科學證據。"},{"en":"Anecdotal evidence is information based on personal stories rather than systematic research.","zh":"anecdotal evidence 指基於個人故事，而不是系統研究的資料。"},{"en":"One person saying a diet worked for them is anecdotal evidence, not proof for everyone.","zh":"一個人說某飲食法對自己有效，是個別事例證據，不是對所有人的證明。"},{"en":"Anecdotal evidence can feel powerful because stories are emotional and easy to remember.","zh":"軼事證據可能感覺有力，因為故事有情緒且容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that personal examples cannot replace careful data.","zh":"這個短語提醒個人例子不能取代仔細數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"passionate tirades","meaning":"激烈的長篇批評","examples":[{"en":"The websites contain passionate tirades from angry supporters.","zh":"這些網站包含憤怒支持者的激烈長篇批評。"},{"en":"Passionate tirades are long, emotional, and angry speeches or writings.","zh":"passionate tirades 指長篇、情緒化且憤怒的演說或文字。"},{"en":"A customer may post a passionate tirade online after feeling ignored by a company.","zh":"顧客覺得被公司忽視後，可能在網上發布激烈長篇批評。"},{"en":"Passionate tirades can attract attention, but they may not provide reliable evidence.","zh":"激烈長篇批評可以吸引注意，但未必提供可靠證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes forceful emotional complaint.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈情緒化投訴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"multitudes","meaning":"大批人","examples":[{"en":"Multitudes of people are firmly convinced of their case.","zh":"大批人堅信自己的立場正確。"},{"en":"Multitudes means very large numbers of people.","zh":"multitudes 指非常大量的人。"},{"en":"Multitudes of commuters leave the station during the morning rush hour.","zh":"早上繁忙時間，大批通勤者離開車站。"},{"en":"When multitudes believe something, the idea can influence public behaviour.","zh":"當大批人相信某事，該想法可以影響公共行為。"},{"en":"This word emphasises a crowd or very large group.","zh":"這個詞強調人群或非常大的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be firmly convinced of","meaning":"堅信……","examples":[{"en":"Some people are firmly convinced of the correctness of their case.","zh":"有些人堅信自己立場的正確性。"},{"en":"To be firmly convinced of something means to believe it very strongly.","zh":"be firmly convinced of something 指非常強烈地相信某事。"},{"en":"A student may be firmly convinced of an answer even after the teacher asks for evidence.","zh":"即使老師要求證據，學生可能仍堅信某個答案。"},{"en":"Strong belief can make people resist changing their minds.","zh":"強烈信念可以令人抗拒改變想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes confidence in a view, not proof that the view is correct.","zh":"這個短語描述對看法有信心，而不是證明該看法正確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the correctness of their case","meaning":"他們立場的正確性","examples":[{"en":"They are convinced of the correctness of their case.","zh":"他們堅信自己立場的正確性。"},{"en":"The correctness of their case means the belief that their argument or position is right.","zh":"the correctness of their case 指相信自己的論點或立場是正確的。"},{"en":"A debate team may defend the correctness of its case by giving evidence and examples.","zh":"辯論隊可能透過證據和例子維護自己立場的正確性。"},{"en":"People who feel sure of their case may ignore weaknesses in their argument.","zh":"確信自己立場的人可能忽視自己論點中的弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on confidence that one’s own side is right.","zh":"這個短語著重對己方正確性的信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"authority is undermined","meaning":"權威受到削弱","examples":[{"en":"Scientific authority is undermined by online misinformation.","zh":"科學權威受到網上錯誤資訊削弱。"},{"en":"Authority is undermined when trust, respect, or power is weakened.","zh":"authority is undermined 指信任、尊重或權力受到削弱。"},{"en":"A teacher’s authority is undermined if school rules are enforced unfairly.","zh":"如果校規執行不公平，老師的權威會受到削弱。"},{"en":"Repeated false claims can undermine expert authority by making people doubt evidence.","zh":"反覆的虛假聲稱可以削弱專家權威，令人民懷疑證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a weakening of trust in a source of knowledge or power.","zh":"這個短語描述對知識或權力來源的信任被削弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"statistics are ignored","meaning":"統計數據被忽視","examples":[{"en":"Statistics are ignored when people follow propaganda.","zh":"當人們跟隨宣傳，統計數據會被忽視。"},{"en":"Statistics are ignored means numerical evidence is not considered or taken seriously.","zh":"statistics are ignored 指數字證據沒有被考慮或認真看待。"},{"en":"If a school ignores attendance statistics, it may miss signs of student stress.","zh":"如果學校忽視出席統計數據，可能錯過學生壓力的跡象。"},{"en":"Ignoring statistics can lead people to trust stories that are not typical.","zh":"忽視統計數據可以令人相信並不典型的故事。"},{"en":"This phrase shows evidence being pushed aside.","zh":"這個短語顯示證據被擱置一旁。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hard science is excluded","meaning":"嚴謹科學被排除","examples":[{"en":"Hard science is excluded from many anti-vaccination arguments.","zh":"嚴謹科學被排除在許多反疫苗論點之外。"},{"en":"Hard science is excluded means careful evidence and testing are left out of the discussion.","zh":"hard science is excluded 指仔細證據和測試被排除在討論之外。"},{"en":"A diet plan excludes hard science if it ignores medical studies and relies only on celebrity stories.","zh":"如果飲食計劃忽視醫學研究，只依賴名人故事，就是排除嚴謹科學。"},{"en":"When hard science is excluded, weak claims can sound more convincing than they deserve.","zh":"當嚴謹科學被排除，薄弱聲稱可能聽起來比實際更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes removing evidence-based reasoning from an argument.","zh":"這個短語描述把以證據為本的推理排除在論點外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"creationists","meaning":"創造論者","examples":[{"en":"The writer compares anti-vaccinationists with creationists.","zh":"作者把反疫苗人士與創造論者作比較。"},{"en":"Creationists are people who reject mainstream evolutionary science and believe life was specially created.","zh":"creationists 指拒絕主流進化科學，並相信生命是被特別創造的人。"},{"en":"A science teacher may explain why creationists disagree with evolution.","zh":"科學老師可能解釋為何創造論者不同意進化論。"},{"en":"The comparison suggests both groups may challenge scientific consensus.","zh":"這個比較暗示兩個群體都可能挑戰科學共識。"},{"en":"This word identifies a group by a belief about the origin of life.","zh":"這個詞根據對生命起源的信念識別一個群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"alternative medicine practitioners","meaning":"替代醫學從業者","examples":[{"en":"Some alternative medicine practitioners oppose vaccination.","zh":"有些替代醫學從業者反對疫苗接種。"},{"en":"Alternative medicine practitioners are people who provide health treatments outside mainstream medical practice.","zh":"alternative medicine practitioners 指提供主流醫學以外健康療法的人。"},{"en":"Some patients visit alternative medicine practitioners for herbal treatments or acupuncture.","zh":"有些病人會為草藥治療或針灸求診於替代醫學從業者。"},{"en":"Problems arise if practitioners reject evidence-based care and encourage unsafe choices.","zh":"如果從業者拒絕實證醫療並鼓勵不安全選擇，就會出現問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes providers of non-mainstream treatments.","zh":"這個短語描述非主流療法提供者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"gain respectability","meaning":"取得認受性","examples":[{"en":"Pseudoscientific groups can sometimes gain respectability.","zh":"偽科學團體有時可以取得認受性。"},{"en":"To gain respectability means to become seen as acceptable, serious, or socially trusted.","zh":"gain respectability 指變得被視為可接受、認真或值得社會信任。"},{"en":"A small charity can gain respectability by publishing clear accounts and working with schools.","zh":"小型慈善機構可以透過發布清楚帳目並與學校合作來取得認受性。"},{"en":"Harmful ideas may gain respectability if famous people repeat them.","zh":"如果名人重複有害想法，這些想法可能取得認受性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rise in public acceptance.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾接受度上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"widespread public and political support","meaning":"廣泛的公眾及政治支持","examples":[{"en":"Some unscientific movements gain widespread public and political support.","zh":"有些不科學運動取得廣泛的公眾及政治支持。"},{"en":"Widespread public and political support means many ordinary people and political leaders support something.","zh":"widespread public and political support 指許多普通人和政治領袖都支持某事。"},{"en":"A transport reform may gain widespread public and political support if it reduces fares and pollution.","zh":"如果交通改革降低票價和污染，可能取得廣泛的公眾及政治支持。"},{"en":"Support from both voters and politicians can make a movement powerful.","zh":"來自選民和政治人物的支持可以令運動變得強大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad backing across society and government.","zh":"這個短語描述社會和政府層面的廣泛支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the pseudoscience of","meaning":"……的偽科學","examples":[{"en":"The writer criticises the pseudoscience of the anti-vaccinationists.","zh":"作者批評反疫苗人士的偽科學。"},{"en":"The pseudoscience of a group means the false or weakly supported claims that the group presents as science.","zh":"the pseudoscience of a group 指該群體當作科學提出的虛假或證據薄弱聲稱。"},{"en":"Consumer groups may criticise the pseudoscience of companies selling miracle health products.","zh":"消費者組織可能批評銷售神奇健康產品公司的偽科學。"},{"en":"Pseudoscience becomes dangerous when people treat it as medical fact.","zh":"當人們把偽科學當成醫學事實，它就會變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the fake scientific basis behind an argument.","zh":"這個短語指出論點背後的假科學基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be faced with","meaning":"面對","examples":[{"en":"Parents are faced with a wave of propaganda.","zh":"父母面對一波宣傳攻勢。"},{"en":"To be faced with something means to have to deal with it.","zh":"be faced with something 指必須處理某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may be faced with a class of tired students after a school trip.","zh":"學校旅行後，老師可能面對一班疲倦的學生。"},{"en":"When people are faced with too much information, they may struggle to judge what is reliable.","zh":"當人們面對太多資訊，可能難以判斷甚麼可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a situation someone must confront.","zh":"這個短語描述某人必須面對的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a wave of propaganda","meaning":"一波宣傳攻勢","examples":[{"en":"Parents may be influenced by a wave of propaganda.","zh":"父母可能受到一波宣傳攻勢影響。"},{"en":"A wave of propaganda is a large amount of biased information designed to influence people.","zh":"a wave of propaganda 指大量旨在影響人的偏頗資訊。"},{"en":"During an election, voters may face a wave of propaganda on social media.","zh":"選舉期間，選民可能在社交媒體面對一波宣傳攻勢。"},{"en":"Propaganda can change behaviour when people hear the same emotional message repeatedly.","zh":"當人們反覆聽到同一情緒化訊息，宣傳可以改變行為。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests intense and widespread persuasion.","zh":"這個短語暗示密集而廣泛的說服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be motivated by","meaning":"受……推動","examples":[{"en":"Many parents are motivated by the desire to protect their children.","zh":"許多父母受保護子女的願望推動。"},{"en":"To be motivated by something means to act because of that reason or feeling.","zh":"be motivated by something 指因某個理由或感受而行動。"},{"en":"A student may be motivated by the wish to help her family in the future.","zh":"學生可能受將來幫助家人的願望推動。"},{"en":"Good motives can still lead to poor decisions if the information is false.","zh":"即使動機良好，如果資訊錯誤，仍可能導致差劣決定。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what drives a person’s action.","zh":"這個短語解釋推動某人行動的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"intense desire","meaning":"強烈願望","examples":[{"en":"Parents have an intense desire to protect their children.","zh":"父母有保護子女的強烈願望。"},{"en":"An intense desire is a very strong wish or need.","zh":"intense desire 指非常強烈的願望或需要。"},{"en":"A student may have an intense desire to pass after failing the same exam twice.","zh":"學生同一考試失敗兩次後，可能有合格的強烈願望。"},{"en":"Intense desire can make people act quickly, sometimes before checking facts.","zh":"強烈願望可以令人迅速行動，有時甚至未核查事實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a powerful emotional drive.","zh":"這個短語描述強大的情感推動力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"protect their children","meaning":"保護子女","examples":[{"en":"Parents naturally want to protect their children.","zh":"父母自然想保護子女。"},{"en":"To protect their children means to keep children safe from harm, danger, or illness.","zh":"protect their children 指讓孩子免受傷害、危險或疾病。"},{"en":"Parents protect their children by checking food allergies before a school trip.","zh":"父母在學校旅行前檢查食物過敏，就是保護子女。"},{"en":"The desire to protect children can make health decisions feel emotional and urgent.","zh":"保護子女的願望可以令健康決定變得情緒化且迫切。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a basic responsibility and instinct of parents.","zh":"這個短語描述父母的基本責任和本能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be influenced","meaning":"受到影響","examples":[{"en":"Some parents are influenced by anti-vaccination propaganda.","zh":"有些父母受到反疫苗宣傳影響。"},{"en":"To be influenced means to have one’s thoughts or actions affected by something.","zh":"be influenced 指思想或行動受到某事影響。"},{"en":"Students may be influenced by friends when choosing after-school activities.","zh":"學生選擇課外活動時，可能受到朋友影響。"},{"en":"People can be influenced without noticing, especially when messages are repeated often.","zh":"人們可能在不察覺下受到影響，尤其是訊息經常重複時。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being affected by outside ideas or pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述受到外來想法或壓力影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at this point","meaning":"在這一點上","examples":[{"en":"At this point, the writer clarifies the scientific evidence.","zh":"在這一點上，作者澄清科學證據。"},{"en":"At this point means at this stage in the discussion or situation.","zh":"at this point 指在討論或情況的這個階段。"},{"en":"At this point in the lesson, the teacher stops and explains the key grammar rule.","zh":"在課堂這一點上，老師停下來解釋關鍵文法規則。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to guide readers from one idea to the next.","zh":"作者使用這個短語，引導讀者由一個想法轉到下一個。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a moment when the argument changes direction or becomes clearer.","zh":"這個短語標示論點改變方向或變得更清楚的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"it must be clarified that","meaning":"必須澄清的是","examples":[{"en":"It must be clarified that the claims lack credible evidence.","zh":"必須澄清的是，這些聲稱缺乏可信證據。"},{"en":"It must be clarified that means an important point needs to be stated clearly to avoid misunderstanding.","zh":"it must be clarified that 指必須清楚說明某重要重點，以避免誤解。"},{"en":"It must be clarified that the school trip is optional, not compulsory.","zh":"必須澄清的是，學校旅行是自願參加，不是強制。"},{"en":"Clarifying a point can prevent rumours from spreading.","zh":"澄清重點可以防止謠言傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a correction or important explanation.","zh":"這個短語引入更正或重要解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"no credible evidence whatsoever","meaning":"完全沒有可信證據","examples":[{"en":"There is no credible evidence whatsoever to support the claim.","zh":"完全沒有可信證據支持這項聲稱。"},{"en":"No credible evidence whatsoever means there is absolutely no reliable proof.","zh":"no credible evidence whatsoever 指完全沒有可靠證明。"},{"en":"There is no credible evidence whatsoever that a phone app can cure serious illness.","zh":"完全沒有可信證據顯示手機應用程式可以治癒嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"Without credible evidence, a claim should not guide health decisions.","zh":"沒有可信證據，某聲稱就不應指導健康決定。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly rejects a claim because reliable support is absent.","zh":"這個短語因缺乏可靠支持而強烈否定某聲稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"support the claims","meaning":"支持這些聲稱","examples":[{"en":"No credible evidence supports the anti-vaccinationists’ claims.","zh":"沒有可信證據支持反疫苗人士的聲稱。"},{"en":"To support the claims means to provide evidence showing that the claims may be true.","zh":"support the claims 指提供證據顯示這些聲稱可能為真。"},{"en":"A student needs examples from the passage to support the claims in an essay.","zh":"學生需要文章中的例子來支持作文中的聲稱。"},{"en":"Claims become weak when no data, records, or reliable studies support them.","zh":"當沒有數據、紀錄或可靠研究支持聲稱，它們就會變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase connects statements with the evidence behind them.","zh":"這個短語把陳述與背後證據連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"over a score of","meaning":"二十多項","examples":[{"en":"Over a score of peer-reviewed studies have found no link.","zh":"二十多項經同行評審的研究發現沒有關聯。"},{"en":"Over a score of means more than twenty.","zh":"over a score of 指超過二十。"},{"en":"Over a score of students volunteered to help clean the beach.","zh":"二十多名學生自願幫忙清潔海灘。"},{"en":"Using this phrase gives a slightly formal or old-fashioned way to express quantity.","zh":"使用這個短語，是較正式或略帶舊式地表達數量。"},{"en":"It shows the number is not just one or two, but more than twenty.","zh":"它顯示數量不是一兩個，而是超過二十。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"peer-reviewed studies","meaning":"經同行評審的研究","examples":[{"en":"Peer-reviewed studies have found no link between the MMR vaccine and autism.","zh":"經同行評審的研究發現 MMR 疫苗與自閉症之間沒有關聯。"},{"en":"Peer-reviewed studies are research papers checked by other experts before or during publication.","zh":"peer-reviewed studies 指在發表前或發表期間由其他專家審查的研究論文。"},{"en":"A teacher may trust peer-reviewed studies more than anonymous online posts.","zh":"老師可能較信任經同行評審的研究，而不是匿名網上帖文。"},{"en":"Peer review helps catch weak methods, errors, or unsupported conclusions.","zh":"同行評審有助發現薄弱方法、錯誤或缺乏支持的結論。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to research that has passed expert checking.","zh":"這個短語指通過專家審查的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"no link between","meaning":"……之間沒有關聯","examples":[{"en":"Studies have found no link between the MMR vaccine and autism.","zh":"研究發現 MMR 疫苗與自閉症之間沒有關聯。"},{"en":"No link between two things means evidence does not show a connection between them.","zh":"no link between two things 指證據沒有顯示兩者之間有連繫。"},{"en":"A school survey may find no link between uniform colour and exam performance.","zh":"學校調查可能發現校服顏色與考試表現之間沒有關聯。"},{"en":"If careful studies find no link, people should be cautious about blaming one thing for another.","zh":"如果仔細研究發現沒有關聯，人們就應小心不要把一事歸咎於另一事。"},{"en":"This phrase rejects a claimed connection.","zh":"這個短語否定被聲稱的關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"MMR vaccine","meaning":"MMR疫苗；麻腮風三聯疫苗","examples":[{"en":"The MMR vaccine protects against measles, mumps and rubella.","zh":"MMR 疫苗預防麻疹、腮腺炎和德國麻疹。"},{"en":"The MMR vaccine is a combined vaccine that helps protect against three infectious diseases.","zh":"MMR vaccine 指一種幫助預防三種傳染病的混合疫苗。"},{"en":"Parents may receive information about the MMR vaccine before a child’s routine appointment.","zh":"父母可能在孩子常規預約前收到關於 MMR 疫苗的資料。"},{"en":"High uptake of the MMR vaccine helps reduce outbreaks in schools and communities.","zh":"MMR 疫苗接種率高，有助減少學校和社區爆發。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific vaccine, not vaccines in general.","zh":"這個短語命名一種特定疫苗，而不是泛指所有疫苗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"subtle neurological problems","meaning":"輕微的神經系統問題","examples":[{"en":"Studies found no link with subtle neurological problems.","zh":"研究發現與輕微神經系統問題沒有關聯。"},{"en":"Subtle neurological problems are small or not easily noticed problems related to the brain or nervous system.","zh":"subtle neurological problems 指與大腦或神經系統有關、細微或不易察覺的問題。"},{"en":"A child with subtle neurological problems may need careful assessment because signs are not obvious.","zh":"有輕微神經系統問題的孩子可能需要仔細評估，因為跡象不明顯。"},{"en":"Subtle problems can be misunderstood if people look only for simple causes.","zh":"如果人們只尋找簡單原因，細微問題可能被誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mild or hard-to-detect nervous-system issues.","zh":"這個短語描述輕微或難以偵測的神經系統問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"continuing vaccination","meaning":"繼續接種疫苗","examples":[{"en":"The studies support continuing vaccination.","zh":"這些研究支持繼續接種疫苗。"},{"en":"Continuing vaccination means keeping vaccination programmes going rather than stopping them.","zh":"continuing vaccination 指繼續推行疫苗接種計劃，而不是停止。"},{"en":"A clinic may recommend continuing vaccination when a disease remains a risk in the community.","zh":"當疾病在社區仍有風險，診所可能建議繼續接種疫苗。"},{"en":"Continuing vaccination helps maintain protection when infections can return.","zh":"當感染可能回來，繼續接種疫苗有助維持保護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing public-health action.","zh":"這個短語描述持續的公共衛生行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"so-called increase in autism","meaning":"所謂自閉症個案增加","examples":[{"en":"The so-called increase in autism results from more accurate diagnoses.","zh":"所謂自閉症個案增加，是由更準確診斷造成的。"},{"en":"So-called increase in autism means an apparent rise that may be partly due to how cases are identified or counted.","zh":"so-called increase in autism 指表面上的增加，可能部分源於個案如何被識別或計算。"},{"en":"A so-called increase in school bullying may happen after better reporting systems are introduced.","zh":"當更好的舉報系統推出後，所謂校園欺凌增加可能會出現。"},{"en":"When diagnosis improves, numbers may rise because hidden cases become visible.","zh":"當診斷改善，數字可能上升，因為隱藏個案變得可見。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the increase needs careful explanation, not quick blame.","zh":"這個短語暗示增加需要仔細解釋，而不是快速怪責。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be attributed to","meaning":"被歸因於","examples":[{"en":"The increase is often wrongly attributed to vaccinations.","zh":"這種增加常被錯誤歸因於疫苗接種。"},{"en":"To be attributed to something means to be explained as being caused by it.","zh":"be attributed to something 指被解釋為由某事造成。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be wrongly attributed to laziness when the real cause is poor sleep.","zh":"學生疲倦可能被錯誤歸因於懶惰，而真正原因是睡眠不足。"},{"en":"Wrong attribution can create fear because people blame the wrong factor.","zh":"錯誤歸因可以製造恐懼，因為人們怪錯因素。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a result with a supposed cause.","zh":"這個短語把結果與被認為的原因連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"more accurate diagnoses","meaning":"更準確的診斷","examples":[{"en":"The apparent increase results from more accurate diagnoses.","zh":"表面上的增加來自更準確的診斷。"},{"en":"More accurate diagnoses are better medical identifications of a condition.","zh":"more accurate diagnoses 指對某健康狀況更好的醫學識別。"},{"en":"More accurate diagnoses can help children receive support earlier.","zh":"更準確的診斷可以幫助孩子更早獲得支援。"},{"en":"When diagnosis improves, recorded case numbers may rise even if the condition itself has not suddenly become more common.","zh":"當診斷改善，記錄個案數可能上升，即使該狀況本身並沒有突然更普遍。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how better recognition can change statistics.","zh":"這個短語解釋更好識別如何改變統計數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be labelled as","meaning":"被標籤為","examples":[{"en":"Children in the past might have been labelled as “slow.”","zh":"過去的孩子可能被標籤為「遲鈍」。"},{"en":"To be labelled as something means to be described or classified in that way.","zh":"be labelled as something 指被描述或分類為某種樣子。"},{"en":"A quiet student may be unfairly labelled as lazy if teachers do not understand her anxiety.","zh":"如果老師不理解學生的焦慮，安靜學生可能被不公平地標籤為懶惰。"},{"en":"Labels can shape how people are treated, even when the label is too simple.","zh":"標籤可以影響人們如何被對待，即使該標籤過於簡化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a person is named or categorised by others.","zh":"這個短語描述一個人如何被他人命名或分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be identified as having","meaning":"被識別為患有","examples":[{"en":"Children are now identified as having one of the main grades of autism.","zh":"兒童現在被識別為患有自閉症其中一個主要級別。"},{"en":"To be identified as having a condition means to be recognised or diagnosed with it.","zh":"be identified as having a condition 指被識別或診斷為有某狀況。"},{"en":"A student may be identified as having dyslexia after a reading assessment.","zh":"學生在閱讀評估後，可能被識別為患有讀寫障礙。"},{"en":"Better identification can lead to earlier support and clearer understanding.","zh":"更好識別可以帶來更早支援和更清楚理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in health, education, and assessment contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於健康、教育和評估語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"main grades of autism","meaning":"自閉症的主要級別","examples":[{"en":"The passage refers to three main grades of autism.","zh":"文章提到自閉症的三個主要級別。"},{"en":"Main grades of autism means the broad categories or levels used to describe autistic conditions in the passage.","zh":"main grades of autism 指文章中用來描述自閉症狀況的主要類別或級別。"},{"en":"A teacher may need to understand different support needs rather than treat all autistic students the same.","zh":"老師可能需要理解不同支援需要，而不是把所有自閉症學生視為一樣。"},{"en":"Categories can help organise support, but individuals still differ.","zh":"分類可以幫助組織支援，但個別人士仍然不同。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to classification within autism.","zh":"這個短語指自閉症內部的分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"genetically determined","meaning":"由基因決定的","examples":[{"en":"Autism is described as probably genetically determined.","zh":"自閉症被描述為很可能由基因決定。"},{"en":"Genetically determined means strongly influenced or caused by genes.","zh":"genetically determined 指受到基因強烈影響或由基因造成。"},{"en":"Eye colour is largely genetically determined, though many traits are more complex.","zh":"眼睛顏色很大程度由基因決定，雖然許多特徵更複雜。"},{"en":"If a condition is genetically determined, blaming a recent event may be misleading.","zh":"如果某狀況由基因決定，怪責近期事件可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"This phrase points to inherited biological causes.","zh":"這個短語指向遺傳生物原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fall on deaf ears","meaning":"被充耳不聞","examples":[{"en":"The scientific argument falls on deaf ears.","zh":"科學論點被充耳不聞。"},{"en":"If an argument falls on deaf ears, people refuse to listen to it or take it seriously.","zh":"如果 an argument falls on deaf ears，人們拒絕聆聽或認真看待它。"},{"en":"A teacher’s warning may fall on deaf ears if students think the test is still far away.","zh":"如果學生覺得測驗還很遠，老師的提醒可能被充耳不聞。"},{"en":"Evidence can fall on deaf ears when people have already made up their minds.","zh":"當人們已經下定決心，證據可能被充耳不聞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ignored advice or ignored evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述被忽視的建議或證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"succeed in reducing","meaning":"成功降低","examples":[{"en":"Anti-vaccination campaigners have succeeded in reducing vaccination rates.","zh":"反疫苗運動人士成功降低疫苗接種率。"},{"en":"To succeed in reducing something means to manage to make it lower.","zh":"succeed in reducing something 指成功令某事下降。"},{"en":"A school may succeed in reducing lateness by changing the morning timetable.","zh":"學校可能透過改變早上時間表成功降低遲到率。"},{"en":"A campaign can reduce behaviour when its message changes people’s choices.","zh":"當宣傳訊息改變人們選擇，就可以降低某種行為。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on achieving a decrease, whether the result is good or harmful.","zh":"這個短語著重成功造成下降，不論結果好壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"vaccination rates","meaning":"疫苗接種率","examples":[{"en":"Vaccination rates fell in some communities.","zh":"一些社區的疫苗接種率下降了。"},{"en":"Vaccination rates are the percentage of people in a group who have received vaccines.","zh":"vaccination rates 指某群體中已接種疫苗者所佔的百分比。"},{"en":"A clinic may track vaccination rates among children before school begins.","zh":"診所可能在開學前追蹤兒童疫苗接種率。"},{"en":"Low vaccination rates can allow preventable diseases to spread again.","zh":"低疫苗接種率可以令可預防疾病再次傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase measures how widely vaccination has been taken up.","zh":"這個短語量度疫苗接種有多普及。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"to the extent that","meaning":"到了……的程度","examples":[{"en":"Rates fell to the extent that disease outbreaks occurred.","zh":"接種率下降到了疾病爆發的程度。"},{"en":"To the extent that means so much that a particular result happens.","zh":"to the extent that 指程度高到某結果發生。"},{"en":"The classroom became noisy to the extent that the teacher had to stop the lesson.","zh":"課室嘈吵到了老師不得不停課的程度。"},{"en":"When a problem grows to this extent, it starts producing visible consequences.","zh":"當問題發展到這個程度，它開始產生可見後果。"},{"en":"This phrase links degree with result.","zh":"這個短語把程度與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"outbreaks of preventable childhood illnesses","meaning":"可預防兒童疾病的爆發","examples":[{"en":"Outbreaks of preventable childhood illnesses began to occur.","zh":"可預防兒童疾病的爆發開始出現。"},{"en":"Outbreaks of preventable childhood illnesses are sudden increases in diseases that children could largely be protected from.","zh":"outbreaks of preventable childhood illnesses 指兒童本可大致受保護免患的疾病突然增加。"},{"en":"A measles outbreak in a school is an example of a preventable childhood illness spreading.","zh":"學校麻疹爆發，就是可預防兒童疾病傳播的例子。"},{"en":"Such outbreaks may happen when too few children are vaccinated.","zh":"當接種疫苗的兒童太少，這類爆發可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes avoidable disease spread among children.","zh":"這個短語描述兒童中可避免的疾病傳播。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"preventable childhood illnesses","meaning":"可預防的兒童疾病","examples":[{"en":"Measles and polio are examples of preventable childhood illnesses.","zh":"麻疹和小兒麻痺症是可預防兒童疾病的例子。"},{"en":"Preventable childhood illnesses are diseases affecting children that can often be avoided through vaccination or public-health measures.","zh":"preventable childhood illnesses 指影響兒童、通常可透過疫苗或公共衛生措施避免的疾病。"},{"en":"Schools may send reminders to reduce preventable childhood illnesses before term begins.","zh":"學校可能在學期開始前發提醒，以減少可預防兒童疾病。"},{"en":"When prevention is ignored, these illnesses can return and harm children.","zh":"當預防被忽視，這些疾病可以回來並傷害兒童。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that illness is not inevitable.","zh":"這個短語強調疾病並非不可避免。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the MMR controversy","meaning":"MMR疫苗爭議","examples":[{"en":"The MMR controversy is described as a sad case.","zh":"MMR 疫苗爭議被描述為令人難過的事件。"},{"en":"The MMR controversy is the public dispute over claims about the MMR vaccine.","zh":"the MMR controversy 指圍繞 MMR 疫苗相關聲稱的公共爭議。"},{"en":"A reading passage may use the MMR controversy to show how one study can influence public fear.","zh":"閱讀文章可能用 MMR 疫苗爭議來顯示一項研究如何影響公眾恐懼。"},{"en":"The controversy affected vaccination decisions even after later evidence rejected the claimed link.","zh":"即使後來證據否定所聲稱的關聯，該爭議仍影響疫苗接種決定。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific vaccine-related public debate.","zh":"這個短語命名一場與特定疫苗相關的公共辯論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a sad case","meaning":"令人難過的事件","examples":[{"en":"The writer calls the MMR controversy a sad case.","zh":"作者稱 MMR 疫苗爭議為令人難過的事件。"},{"en":"A sad case is an example that is upsetting because it caused harm or unnecessary suffering.","zh":"a sad case 指因造成傷害或不必要痛苦而令人難過的例子。"},{"en":"A school closure caused by poor planning can be a sad case if children lose support.","zh":"如果孩子失去支援，因規劃差而造成的學校停辦可以是令人難過的事件。"},{"en":"A sad case often teaches a serious lesson about what should not happen again.","zh":"令人難過的事件常教人嚴肅一課，提醒甚麼不應再次發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unfortunate example, not just a mildly disappointing one.","zh":"這個短語描述不幸例子，而不只是輕微令人失望的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"high-profile paper","meaning":"受高度關注的論文","examples":[{"en":"A high-profile paper linked the vaccine to autism.","zh":"一篇受高度關注的論文把疫苗與自閉症聯繫起來。"},{"en":"A high-profile paper is a research article that receives a lot of public or professional attention.","zh":"high-profile paper 指受到大量公眾或專業關注的研究文章。"},{"en":"A high-profile paper in education may change how schools think about homework.","zh":"教育領域一篇受高度關注的論文，可能改變學校如何看待功課。"},{"en":"If a high-profile paper is flawed, its influence can still cause widespread confusion.","zh":"如果受高度關注的論文有缺陷，其影響仍可能造成廣泛混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visibility and influence, not necessarily quality.","zh":"這個短語描述能見度和影響力，不一定代表質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"link something to","meaning":"把……與……聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"The paper linked the vaccine to autism.","zh":"該論文把疫苗與自閉症聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To link something to something else means to claim or show a connection between them.","zh":"link something to something else 指聲稱或顯示兩者之間有關聯。"},{"en":"A teacher may link poor sleep to weak concentration in class.","zh":"老師可能把睡眠不足與課堂專注力弱聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Linking two things without strong evidence can mislead readers.","zh":"沒有有力證據就把兩件事聯繫起來，可以誤導讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes connecting one thing with another.","zh":"這個短語描述把一件事與另一件事連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"it was later shown that","meaning":"後來證明","examples":[{"en":"It was later shown that the author had a conflict of interest.","zh":"後來證明作者有利益衝突。"},{"en":"It was later shown that means later evidence revealed something to be true.","zh":"it was later shown that 指後來的證據揭示某事為真。"},{"en":"It was later shown that the shop’s discount signs had been calculated incorrectly.","zh":"後來證明該商店的折扣標示計算錯誤。"},{"en":"New evidence can change how people judge an earlier claim.","zh":"新證據可以改變人們如何判斷早前聲稱。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces information discovered after the original event.","zh":"這個短語引入原事件之後才發現的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"receive funds from","meaning":"從……收取資金","examples":[{"en":"The author was receiving funds from groups involved in a lawsuit.","zh":"作者正從參與訴訟的團體收取資金。"},{"en":"To receive funds from someone means to get money or financial support from them.","zh":"receive funds from someone 指從某人或某機構取得金錢或財政支援。"},{"en":"A community centre may receive funds from the government to run youth programmes.","zh":"社區中心可能從政府收取資金來營辦青年計劃。"},{"en":"Funding sources matter because they may affect trust in a person’s work.","zh":"資金來源很重要，因為它可能影響人們對某人工作的信任。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where money comes from.","zh":"這個短語指出金錢從哪裡來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be engaged in a lawsuit against","meaning":"正參與針對……的訴訟","examples":[{"en":"Some groups were engaged in a lawsuit against vaccine manufacturers.","zh":"有些團體正參與針對疫苗製造商的訴訟。"},{"en":"To be engaged in a lawsuit against someone means to be involved in a legal case against them.","zh":"be engaged in a lawsuit against someone 指正參與針對某人的法律案件。"},{"en":"Tenants may be engaged in a lawsuit against a landlord over unsafe housing.","zh":"租戶可能因不安全住房而正參與針對業主的訴訟。"},{"en":"A lawsuit can create a conflict of interest if research findings may help one side financially.","zh":"如果研究結果可能在財務上幫助其中一方，訴訟可以造成利益衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal legal conflict.","zh":"這個短語描述正式法律衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"vaccine manufacturers","meaning":"疫苗製造商","examples":[{"en":"The lawsuit was against vaccine manufacturers.","zh":"該訴訟針對疫苗製造商。"},{"en":"Vaccine manufacturers are companies that produce vaccines.","zh":"vaccine manufacturers 指生產疫苗的公司。"},{"en":"Vaccine manufacturers must follow strict safety and quality standards.","zh":"疫苗製造商必須遵守嚴格安全和品質標準。"},{"en":"Public trust can be damaged if manufacturers are suspected of hiding information.","zh":"如果製造商被懷疑隱瞞資料，公眾信任可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the companies that make vaccines, not the doctors who give them.","zh":"這個短語指製造疫苗的公司，而不是接種疫苗的醫生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ethically and methodologically faulty","meaning":"在倫理和方法上都有缺陷","examples":[{"en":"The study was ethically and methodologically faulty.","zh":"該研究在倫理和方法上都有缺陷。"},{"en":"Ethically and methodologically faulty means wrong in both moral standards and research methods.","zh":"ethically and methodologically faulty 指在道德標準和研究方法上都有問題。"},{"en":"A student survey is methodologically faulty if questions lead people toward one answer.","zh":"如果學生調查問題引導人選某個答案，它在方法上就有缺陷。"},{"en":"Research is ethically faulty if participants are misled or harmed without proper protection.","zh":"如果參與者被誤導或在沒有適當保護下受傷害，研究在倫理上就有缺陷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious problems in how a study was conducted.","zh":"這個短語描述研究進行方式中的嚴重問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"data had been manipulated","meaning":"數據被操控","examples":[{"en":"Data had been manipulated in the study.","zh":"該研究中的數據被操控。"},{"en":"Data had been manipulated means information was changed or handled dishonestly to affect the result.","zh":"data had been manipulated 指資料被改動或不誠實處理，以影響結果。"},{"en":"Exam results are manipulated if a school removes weak scores to look better.","zh":"如果學校移除低分來讓自己看起來更好，考試成績就是被操控。"},{"en":"Manipulated data destroy trust because the conclusion no longer reflects reality.","zh":"被操控的數據會摧毀信任，因為結論不再反映現實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dishonest interference with evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述對證據的不誠實干預。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"results misreported","meaning":"結果被錯誤報告","examples":[{"en":"The results were misreported.","zh":"結果被錯誤報告。"},{"en":"Results are misreported when findings are described wrongly or misleadingly.","zh":"results are misreported 指研究發現被錯誤或誤導性地描述。"},{"en":"A survey is misreported if the headline says “all students agree” when only half agreed.","zh":"如果標題說「所有學生都同意」，但實際只有一半同意，調查結果就是被錯誤報告。"},{"en":"Misreported results can make readers believe a stronger conclusion than the data support.","zh":"被錯誤報告的結果可以令讀者相信比數據支持更強的結論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inaccurate reporting of findings.","zh":"這個短語描述對研究發現的不準確報告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"no link whatsoever","meaning":"完全沒有關聯","examples":[{"en":"Similar studies found no link whatsoever.","zh":"類似研究發現完全沒有關聯。"},{"en":"No link whatsoever means absolutely no connection was found.","zh":"no link whatsoever 指完全沒有發現任何連繫。"},{"en":"The school found no link whatsoever between desk colour and test scores.","zh":"學校發現書桌顏色與測驗分數完全沒有關聯。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly rejects the idea that two things are connected.","zh":"這個短語強烈否定兩件事有關聯的想法。"},{"en":"It is stronger than simply saying “no link.”","zh":"它比單純說 “no link” 更強烈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"medical journal","meaning":"醫學期刊","examples":[{"en":"The medical journal later retracted the article’s conclusion.","zh":"該醫學期刊後來撤回文章結論。"},{"en":"A medical journal is a publication that shares research and articles about medicine and health.","zh":"medical journal 指刊登醫學和健康研究文章的出版物。"},{"en":"Doctors may read a medical journal to learn about new treatments.","zh":"醫生可能閱讀醫學期刊，以了解新治療方法。"},{"en":"Journals can correct the record when a published article is found to be flawed.","zh":"當已發表文章被發現有缺陷，期刊可以更正紀錄。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a professional publication, not a general magazine.","zh":"這個短語指專業出版物，而不是一般雜誌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"publish the original article","meaning":"刊登原文","examples":[{"en":"The medical journal had published the original article.","zh":"該醫學期刊曾刊登原文。"},{"en":"To publish the original article means to release the first version of the article to readers.","zh":"publish the original article 指向讀者發布文章的最初版本。"},{"en":"A newspaper may publish the original article online before printing corrections later.","zh":"報紙可能先在網上刊登原文，之後再刊登更正。"},{"en":"Once an article is published, its claims can influence many people.","zh":"文章一旦發表，其聲稱可以影響許多人。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the first public release of a written work.","zh":"這個短語著重書面作品首次公開發布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"formally retract","meaning":"正式撤回","examples":[{"en":"The journal formally retracted its conclusion.","zh":"期刊正式撤回其結論。"},{"en":"To formally retract something means to officially withdraw it from the record.","zh":"formally retract something 指正式從紀錄中撤回某事。"},{"en":"A school may formally retract an accusation after evidence proves it was wrong.","zh":"當證據證明指控錯誤，學校可能正式撤回該指控。"},{"en":"Formal retraction helps correct misinformation, but it may not erase public memory.","zh":"正式撤回有助更正錯誤資訊，但未必能抹去公眾記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an official withdrawal of a statement or conclusion.","zh":"這個短語描述正式撤回聲明或結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in the subsequent years","meaning":"在隨後數年","examples":[{"en":"Vaccination rates dropped in the subsequent years.","zh":"在隨後數年，疫苗接種率下降。"},{"en":"In the subsequent years means in the years that followed.","zh":"in the subsequent years 指在之後的幾年中。"},{"en":"A school introduced a reading plan, and in the subsequent years exam scores improved.","zh":"學校推出閱讀計劃，而在隨後數年考試成績有所改善。"},{"en":"Looking at subsequent years helps people see the later effects of an event.","zh":"觀察隨後數年，有助人們看見某事件的後續影響。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an event with what happened afterwards.","zh":"這個短語把事件與之後發生的事連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"measles outbreak","meaning":"麻疹爆發","examples":[{"en":"A measles outbreak occurred in North Dublin.","zh":"北都柏林發生麻疹爆發。"},{"en":"A measles outbreak is a sudden spread of measles cases in a community.","zh":"measles outbreak 指社區中麻疹個案突然傳播。"},{"en":"A school may close temporarily if a measles outbreak affects many students.","zh":"如果麻疹爆發影響許多學生，學校可能暫時停課。"},{"en":"Outbreaks are more likely when vaccination levels are too low.","zh":"當疫苗接種水平太低，爆發更可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a local or regional rise in measles infections.","zh":"這個短語描述本地或地區麻疹感染增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as low as","meaning":"低至","examples":[{"en":"Vaccination rates were as low as 60 percent in North Dublin.","zh":"北都柏林的疫苗接種率低至 60%。"},{"en":"As low as means reaching a surprisingly low level.","zh":"as low as 指達到令人驚訝的低水平。"},{"en":"In a quiet month, shop sales may fall as low as half their usual level.","zh":"在淡季，商店銷售額可能低至平時的一半。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights that the number is worryingly or unusually low.","zh":"這個短語突出數字低得令人擔心或不尋常。"},{"en":"It is often used to stress a minimum figure.","zh":"它常用來強調最低數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"result in","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"The outbreak resulted in hospitalisations and deaths.","zh":"這次爆發導致住院和死亡。"},{"en":"To result in something means to cause it to happen.","zh":"result in something 指導致某事發生。"},{"en":"Heavy rain may result in traffic delays and school closures.","zh":"大雨可能導致交通延誤和學校停課。"},{"en":"Poor decisions can result in consequences that affect people beyond the decision-maker.","zh":"差劣決定可能導致影響決策者以外人士的後果。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with its outcome.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"hospitalisations","meaning":"住院個案","examples":[{"en":"The measles outbreak resulted in 100 hospitalisations.","zh":"麻疹爆發導致 100 宗住院個案。"},{"en":"Hospitalisations are cases in which people are admitted to hospital for treatment.","zh":"hospitalisations 指人們入院接受治療的個案。"},{"en":"A flu outbreak may increase hospitalisations among elderly people.","zh":"流感爆發可能增加長者住院個案。"},{"en":"Rising hospitalisations show that an illness is causing serious harm, not only mild symptoms.","zh":"住院個案上升顯示疾病造成嚴重傷害，而不只是輕微症狀。"},{"en":"This word counts people who need hospital care.","zh":"這個詞計算需要醫院護理的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"one of the key arguments","meaning":"其中一個主要論點","examples":[{"en":"One of the key arguments is the right to choose medication.","zh":"其中一個主要論點是選擇藥物的權利。"},{"en":"One of the key arguments means one of the main reasons used to support a position.","zh":"one of the key arguments 指用來支持某立場的主要理由之一。"},{"en":"One of the key arguments for longer library hours is that students need a quiet study place.","zh":"支持延長圖書館開放時間的其中一個主要論點，是學生需要安靜學習地方。"},{"en":"A key argument matters because it shapes how people defend their view.","zh":"主要論點很重要，因為它塑造人們如何捍衛看法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an important point in a debate.","zh":"這個短語引入辯論中的重要觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have the right to choose","meaning":"有權選擇","examples":[{"en":"Anti-vaccinationists argue that they have the right to choose.","zh":"反疫苗人士主張他們有權選擇。"},{"en":"To have the right to choose means to be allowed to make one’s own decision.","zh":"have the right to choose 指被允許自行作決定。"},{"en":"Students may have the right to choose some elective subjects at school.","zh":"學生可能有權選擇一些選修科目。"},{"en":"Personal choice becomes complicated when one person’s decision affects public safety.","zh":"當一個人的決定影響公共安全，個人選擇就會變得複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes freedom of decision-making.","zh":"這個短語描述作決定的自由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"medication","meaning":"藥物；醫療用藥","examples":[{"en":"Some people argue that they should choose their own medication.","zh":"有些人主張應該選擇自己的藥物。"},{"en":"Medication means medicine used to treat, prevent, or control a health problem.","zh":"medication 指用來治療、預防或控制健康問題的藥物。"},{"en":"A patient should tell a doctor before stopping medication suddenly.","zh":"病人在突然停藥前應告訴醫生。"},{"en":"Choosing medication without reliable advice can be risky.","zh":"在沒有可靠建議下選擇藥物可能有風險。"},{"en":"This word refers to medical drugs or treatment substances.","zh":"這個詞指醫療藥物或治療物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"attack what they see as","meaning":"攻擊他們眼中……的事物","examples":[{"en":"They attack what they see as an uncaring medical system.","zh":"他們攻擊他們眼中冷漠的醫療制度。"},{"en":"To attack what they see as something means to strongly criticise something because they believe it has that quality.","zh":"attack what they see as something 指因相信某事具有某特質而強烈批評它。"},{"en":"Parents may attack what they see as an unfair school policy.","zh":"家長可能攻擊他們眼中不公平的學校政策。"},{"en":"People may attack a system more fiercely when they feel ignored by it.","zh":"當人們覺得被制度忽視，可能更猛烈地攻擊該制度。"},{"en":"This phrase shows criticism based on perception.","zh":"這個短語顯示基於感知的批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"impersonal","meaning":"缺乏人情味的","examples":[{"en":"They see modern medical science as impersonal.","zh":"他們視現代醫學科學為缺乏人情味。"},{"en":"Impersonal means lacking warmth, human feeling, or personal attention.","zh":"impersonal 指缺乏溫度、人情味或個人關注。"},{"en":"A hospital visit may feel impersonal if no one explains what is happening.","zh":"如果沒有人解釋正在發生甚麼，醫院就診可能感覺缺乏人情味。"},{"en":"Impersonal service can make people distrust even a professional system.","zh":"缺乏人情味的服務可以令人不信任即使專業的系統。"},{"en":"This word describes something that feels distant or uncaring.","zh":"這個詞描述某事感覺疏遠或冷漠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"intrusive","meaning":"侵入性的；過分干預的","examples":[{"en":"They see modern medicine as intrusive.","zh":"他們視現代醫學為侵入性的。"},{"en":"Intrusive means entering too deeply into someone’s body, privacy, or personal choices.","zh":"intrusive 指過深地進入某人的身體、私隱或個人選擇。"},{"en":"Some students find repeated personal questions intrusive during counselling.","zh":"有些學生覺得輔導中反覆的私人問題過分干預。"},{"en":"Medical procedures may feel intrusive when patients do not understand why they are needed.","zh":"當病人不理解醫療程序為何需要，程序可能感覺侵入性。"},{"en":"This word describes something that feels too interfering.","zh":"這個詞描述某事感覺過度干預。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"uncaring","meaning":"冷漠的","examples":[{"en":"They describe modern medical science as uncaring.","zh":"他們把現代醫學科學描述為冷漠的。"},{"en":"Uncaring means not showing kindness, concern, or sympathy.","zh":"uncaring 指不表現善意、關心或同情。"},{"en":"A school may seem uncaring if it ignores a bullied student’s repeated complaints.","zh":"如果學校忽視被欺凌學生的反覆投訴，可能看似冷漠。"},{"en":"People may reject advice when they feel the person giving it is uncaring.","zh":"當人們覺得給建議的人冷漠，可能會拒絕其建議。"},{"en":"This word describes a lack of emotional concern.","zh":"這個詞描述缺乏情感關心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"edifice of modern medical science","meaning":"現代醫學科學體系","examples":[{"en":"They attack the edifice of modern medical science.","zh":"他們攻擊現代醫學科學體系。"},{"en":"The edifice of modern medical science means the large and established system of medical knowledge, institutions, and practices.","zh":"edifice of modern medical science 指龐大且已建立的醫學知識、機構和實踐系統。"},{"en":"A single scandal can make people question the whole edifice of a public system.","zh":"一宗醜聞可以令人質疑整個公共制度體系。"},{"en":"Attacking an edifice means challenging more than one rule or person; it challenges the whole structure.","zh":"攻擊一個體系，不只是挑戰一條規則或一個人，而是挑戰整個結構。"},{"en":"This phrase presents modern medicine as a large organised system.","zh":"這個短語把現代醫學呈現為大型有組織系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"depend on","meaning":"取決於","examples":[{"en":"The success of immunisation programmes depends on high vaccination rates.","zh":"免疫接種計劃的成功取決於高疫苗接種率。"},{"en":"To depend on something means to need that thing in order to work or succeed.","zh":"depend on something 指需要某事才能運作或成功。"},{"en":"A group project depends on every student doing their part.","zh":"小組項目取決於每名學生做好自己的部分。"},{"en":"If protection depends on high participation, one person’s choice can affect others.","zh":"如果保護取決於高參與率，一個人的選擇可以影響其他人。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what condition is necessary for success.","zh":"這個短語顯示成功所需條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a sufficiently high proportion of","meaning":"足夠高比例的……","examples":[{"en":"Immunisation requires a sufficiently high proportion of the population to be immune.","zh":"免疫接種需要足夠高比例的人口具有免疫力。"},{"en":"A sufficiently high proportion of means enough members of a group to make something work.","zh":"a sufficiently high proportion of 指群體中有足夠多成員，令某事能運作。"},{"en":"A school recycling plan needs a sufficiently high proportion of students to participate.","zh":"學校回收計劃需要足夠高比例的學生參與。"},{"en":"If the proportion is too low, the whole system may fail.","zh":"如果比例太低，整個系統可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on reaching the required level within a group.","zh":"這個短語著重在群體中達到所需水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be immune","meaning":"具有免疫力","examples":[{"en":"A high proportion of the population must be immune.","zh":"高比例人口必須具有免疫力。"},{"en":"To be immune means to be protected against a disease so infection is less likely or less severe.","zh":"be immune 指受到某疾病保護，使感染較不可能或較不嚴重。"},{"en":"After vaccination or past infection, some people may become immune to certain diseases.","zh":"接種疫苗或曾感染後，有些人可能對某些疾病具有免疫力。"},{"en":"When many people are immune, a disease has fewer chances to spread.","zh":"當許多人具有免疫力，疾病傳播機會就較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes biological protection.","zh":"這個短語描述生物上的保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"die out","meaning":"消失；絕跡","examples":[{"en":"The disease dies out when there are too few carriers.","zh":"當帶菌者太少，疾病就會消失。"},{"en":"To die out means to disappear gradually because it can no longer continue or spread.","zh":"die out 指因無法繼續或傳播而逐漸消失。"},{"en":"A local tradition may die out if young people stop learning it.","zh":"如果年輕人停止學習，本地傳統可能絕跡。"},{"en":"A disease can die out when it cannot find enough people to infect.","zh":"當疾病找不到足夠的人感染，就可以消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual disappearance.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lack of carriers","meaning":"缺乏帶菌者；缺乏傳播者","examples":[{"en":"A disease may die out through lack of carriers.","zh":"疾病可能因缺乏帶菌者而消失。"},{"en":"Lack of carriers means there are not enough infected or susceptible people to pass something on.","zh":"lack of carriers 指沒有足夠受感染或易感染的人去傳播某物。"},{"en":"A rumour may disappear through lack of carriers if no one repeats it.","zh":"如果沒有人重複謠言，謠言可能因缺乏傳播者而消失。"},{"en":"Diseases need carriers to move from person to person.","zh":"疾病需要帶菌者在人與人之間傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why transmission can stop.","zh":"這個短語解釋傳播為何會停止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"susceptible individuals","meaning":"易受感染人士","examples":[{"en":"Susceptible individuals can continue to spread disease.","zh":"易受感染人士可以繼續傳播疾病。"},{"en":"Susceptible individuals are people who can easily catch a disease because they are not protected.","zh":"susceptible individuals 指因沒有保護而容易感染疾病的人。"},{"en":"A newborn baby may be a susceptible individual before receiving certain vaccines.","zh":"新生嬰兒在接種某些疫苗前，可能是易受感染人士。"},{"en":"If many susceptible individuals remain in a community, outbreaks can continue.","zh":"如果社區中仍有許多易受感染人士，爆發可以持續。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people who are vulnerable to infection.","zh":"這個短語指容易受感染的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"chain of disease transmission","meaning":"疾病傳播鏈","examples":[{"en":"Susceptible individuals can provide a chain of disease transmission.","zh":"易受感染人士可以形成疾病傳播鏈。"},{"en":"A chain of disease transmission is the path by which a disease passes from one person to another.","zh":"chain of disease transmission 指疾病由一人傳到另一人的路徑。"},{"en":"One sick child may start a chain of disease transmission in a classroom.","zh":"一名患病兒童可能在課室開始一條疾病傳播鏈。"},{"en":"Breaking the chain can stop an outbreak before it reaches vulnerable people.","zh":"打斷傳播鏈可以在爆發到達弱勢人士前阻止它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how infection spreads step by step.","zh":"這個短語描述感染如何一步步傳播。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"safety is compromised","meaning":"安全受到威脅","examples":[{"en":"Public safety is compromised when vaccination rates fall.","zh":"當疫苗接種率下降，公共安全受到威脅。"},{"en":"Safety is compromised means safety is weakened or put at risk.","zh":"safety is compromised 指安全被削弱或置於風險中。"},{"en":"School safety is compromised if emergency exits are blocked.","zh":"如果緊急出口被堵塞，學校安全就受到威脅。"},{"en":"When safety is compromised, people may be harmed even if they personally did nothing wrong.","zh":"當安全受到威脅，人們即使自己沒有做錯事，也可能受傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protection becoming less secure.","zh":"這個短語描述保護變得較不穩固。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"for all","meaning":"對所有人而言","examples":[{"en":"Low vaccination rates compromise safety for all.","zh":"低疫苗接種率對所有人而言都威脅安全。"},{"en":"For all means for everyone, not just one person or one group.","zh":"for all 指對每個人，而不只是某一人或某一群體。"},{"en":"Clean public toilets improve daily life for all.","zh":"清潔公共洗手間改善所有人的日常生活。"},{"en":"Public-health choices can matter for all because infections move through communities.","zh":"公共衛生選擇可以對所有人都重要，因為感染會在社區中流動。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses shared impact.","zh":"這個短語強調共同影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"free choice","meaning":"自由選擇","examples":[{"en":"The writer argues that free choice should not be the main issue.","zh":"作者認為自由選擇不應是主要問題。"},{"en":"Free choice is the ability to decide for oneself without being forced.","zh":"free choice 指不被強迫而自行決定的能力。"},{"en":"Students may have free choice in selecting a book for a reading project.","zh":"學生可能在閱讀項目中有自由選擇書本的權利。"},{"en":"Free choice becomes complicated when one person’s choice creates risk for others.","zh":"當一個人的選擇為他人帶來風險，自由選擇就會變得複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on personal freedom in decision-making.","zh":"這個短語著重決策中的個人自由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"should not be an issue","meaning":"不應成為問題","examples":[{"en":"Free choice should not be an issue when public safety is at risk.","zh":"當公共安全有風險，自由選擇不應成為問題。"},{"en":"Should not be an issue means should not be treated as the main problem or deciding factor.","zh":"should not be an issue 指不應被視為主要問題或決定因素。"},{"en":"The colour of a uniform should not be an issue when the real concern is student safety.","zh":"當真正關注是學生安全，校服顏色不應成為問題。"},{"en":"Some questions become less important when a more serious risk appears.","zh":"當更嚴重風險出現，有些問題就變得較不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase pushes one concern aside because another concern matters more.","zh":"這個短語因另一個關注更重要而把某問題放到一旁。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"hard evidence","meaning":"確鑿證據","examples":[{"en":"The hard evidence presents an overwhelming case for vaccination.","zh":"確鑿證據提出支持疫苗接種的壓倒性理據。"},{"en":"Hard evidence is strong, reliable evidence based on facts, data, or careful observation.","zh":"hard evidence 指基於事實、數據或仔細觀察的有力可靠證據。"},{"en":"A school needs hard evidence before accusing a student of cheating.","zh":"學校在指控學生作弊前需要確鑿證據。"},{"en":"Hard evidence is more trustworthy than rumours because it can be checked.","zh":"確鑿證據比謠言更可信，因為它可以被核查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence that is difficult to dismiss.","zh":"這個短語描述難以否定的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"overwhelming case","meaning":"壓倒性的理據","examples":[{"en":"The evidence presents an overwhelming case for immunisation.","zh":"證據提出支持免疫接種的壓倒性理據。"},{"en":"An overwhelming case is an argument supported by so much evidence that it is very hard to reject.","zh":"overwhelming case 指有大量證據支持、非常難以拒絕的論點。"},{"en":"CCTV, witness reports, and receipts may present an overwhelming case in an investigation.","zh":"閉路電視、證人報告和收據可能在調查中提出壓倒性的理據。"},{"en":"When evidence is overwhelming, disagreement usually needs very strong counter-evidence.","zh":"當證據壓倒性，反對通常需要非常強的反證。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an extremely strong argument.","zh":"這個短語描述極有力的論點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"I would have thought that","meaning":"我本以為","examples":[{"en":"I would have thought that preventable deaths would change people’s minds.","zh":"我本以為可預防死亡會改變人們的想法。"},{"en":"I would have thought that means the speaker expected something to be true, but reality seems different.","zh":"I would have thought that 指說話者原本預期某事為真，但現實似乎不同。"},{"en":"I would have thought that a warning letter would make students submit homework on time.","zh":"我本以為警告信會令學生準時交功課。"},{"en":"This phrase often expresses surprise, disappointment, or disbelief.","zh":"這個短語常表達驚訝、失望或難以置信。"},{"en":"It shows that the speaker’s expectation has not been met.","zh":"它顯示說話者的預期沒有實現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"preventable diseases","meaning":"可預防疾病","examples":[{"en":"Children have died from preventable diseases.","zh":"兒童死於可預防疾病。"},{"en":"Preventable diseases are illnesses that can often be avoided through vaccines, hygiene, or other public-health measures.","zh":"preventable diseases 指通常可透過疫苗、衛生或其他公共衛生措施避免的疾病。"},{"en":"Clean water helps reduce preventable diseases in crowded communities.","zh":"清潔食水有助減少擁擠社區中的可預防疾病。"},{"en":"Deaths from preventable diseases are especially tragic because protection was possible.","zh":"因可預防疾病而死亡尤其悲慘，因為保護本來是可能的。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that illness or death did not have to happen.","zh":"這個短語強調疾病或死亡本不必發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"agendas at play","meaning":"有其他目的在背後運作","examples":[{"en":"The writer argues that there are other agendas at play.","zh":"作者認為有其他目的在背後運作。"},{"en":"Agendas at play are hidden aims or interests influencing what people say or do.","zh":"agendas at play 指影響人們言行的隱藏目標或利益。"},{"en":"In a school debate, there may be agendas at play if some students want popularity more than a fair solution.","zh":"在學校辯論中，如果有些學生想要人氣多於公平解決方法，就可能有其他目的在背後運作。"},{"en":"Hidden agendas can make a public argument less honest.","zh":"隱藏目的可以令公共爭論較不誠實。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests motives beyond the obvious explanation.","zh":"這個短語暗示明顯解釋以外還有其他動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"posture as","meaning":"擺出……姿態","examples":[{"en":"Some anti-vaccinationists posture as moral crusaders.","zh":"有些反疫苗人士擺出道德鬥士的姿態。"},{"en":"To posture as something means to present oneself in a role, often in an exaggerated or insincere way.","zh":"posture as something 指把自己呈現成某角色，常帶誇張或不真誠意味。"},{"en":"A company may posture as environmentally friendly while still wasting large amounts of plastic.","zh":"公司可能擺出環保姿態，同時仍浪費大量塑膠。"},{"en":"People posture as heroes when they want moral authority without accepting evidence.","zh":"當人們想取得道德權威而不接受證據，可能擺出英雄姿態。"},{"en":"This phrase often carries criticism of pretence.","zh":"這個短語常帶有對假裝的批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"moral crusaders","meaning":"道德鬥士","examples":[{"en":"Some campaigners present themselves as moral crusaders.","zh":"有些運動人士把自己呈現為道德鬥士。"},{"en":"Moral crusaders are people who see themselves as fighting for what is morally right.","zh":"moral crusaders 指把自己視為為道德正義而戰的人。"},{"en":"A community leader may act like a moral crusader when campaigning against child labour.","zh":"社區領袖反對童工時，可能像道德鬥士一樣行動。"},{"en":"The phrase can be admiring or critical, depending on whether the cause and methods are fair.","zh":"這個短語可以是讚賞或批評，視乎目標和方法是否公平。"},{"en":"In this context, it suggests people claiming moral superiority.","zh":"在這個語境中，它暗示人們聲稱自己道德上更高尚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"dismiss those who","meaning":"否定那些……的人","examples":[{"en":"They dismiss those who support immunisation.","zh":"他們否定那些支持免疫接種的人。"},{"en":"To dismiss those who do something means to reject or ignore those people and their views.","zh":"dismiss those who do something 指拒絕或忽視那些人及其看法。"},{"en":"A teacher should not dismiss students who ask basic questions.","zh":"老師不應否定那些問基本問題的學生。"},{"en":"Dismissing others can stop useful discussion because people feel attacked rather than heard.","zh":"否定他人可以阻礙有用討論，因為人們感到被攻擊而不是被聆聽。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rejecting people, not simply disagreeing with them.","zh":"這個短語描述拒絕人，而不只是不同意他們。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be in the pay of","meaning":"受……收買","examples":[{"en":"They claim supporters of immunisation are in the pay of pharmaceutical companies.","zh":"他們聲稱免疫接種支持者受製藥公司收買。"},{"en":"To be in the pay of someone means to be secretly or wrongly paid by them to support their interests.","zh":"be in the pay of someone 指秘密或不當地收取某人金錢，以支持其利益。"},{"en":"A journalist may be accused of being in the pay of a company if readers think his report is biased.","zh":"如果讀者認為記者報道偏頗，他可能被指受公司收買。"},{"en":"This accusation questions someone’s honesty and independence.","zh":"這種指控質疑某人的誠信和獨立性。"},{"en":"The phrase is strongly negative and suggests corruption.","zh":"這個短語強烈負面，暗示腐敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"big pharmaceutical companies","meaning":"大型製藥公司","examples":[{"en":"They accuse supporters of working for big pharmaceutical companies.","zh":"他們指控支持者為大型製藥公司工作。"},{"en":"Big pharmaceutical companies are large businesses that develop, produce, and sell medicines.","zh":"big pharmaceutical companies 指研發、生產和銷售藥物的大型企業。"},{"en":"Governments may negotiate with big pharmaceutical companies over drug prices.","zh":"政府可能與大型製藥公司就藥價談判。"},{"en":"Distrust of large companies can make some people suspicious of medical advice.","zh":"對大公司的不信任可以令人懷疑醫療建議。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to major drug companies, often with a critical tone.","zh":"這個短語指主要藥廠，常帶批評語氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"dishonest and immoral","meaning":"不誠實且不道德","examples":[{"en":"They view pharmaceutical companies as dishonest and immoral.","zh":"他們把製藥公司視為不誠實且不道德。"},{"en":"Dishonest and immoral means untruthful and ethically wrong.","zh":"dishonest and immoral 指不誠實並且在倫理上錯誤。"},{"en":"A business is dishonest and immoral if it hides safety risks to protect profit.","zh":"如果企業為保護利潤而隱瞞安全風險，就是不誠實且不道德。"},{"en":"Calling someone dishonest and immoral is a serious judgement about character and behaviour.","zh":"稱某人不誠實且不道德，是對品格和行為的嚴重判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase combines lack of truth with lack of ethics.","zh":"這個短語結合不真實與缺乏道德。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"talk show hosts","meaning":"清談節目主持人","examples":[{"en":"Talk show hosts may benefit from creating controversy.","zh":"清談節目主持人可能從製造爭議中得益。"},{"en":"Talk show hosts are people who lead radio, television, or online discussion programmes.","zh":"talk show hosts 指主持電台、電視或網上討論節目的人。"},{"en":"A talk show host may invite guests with opposing views to attract listeners.","zh":"清談節目主持人可能邀請持相反觀點的嘉賓，以吸引聽眾。"},{"en":"Some hosts gain attention when arguments become dramatic.","zh":"當爭論變得戲劇化，有些主持人會獲得關注。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to media presenters who guide public conversations.","zh":"這個短語指引導公共對話的媒體主持人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"paid experts","meaning":"受薪專家","examples":[{"en":"Paid experts may help create public controversy.","zh":"受薪專家可能幫助製造公共爭議。"},{"en":"Paid experts are specialists who receive money for giving opinions, advice, or analysis.","zh":"paid experts 指因提供意見、建議或分析而收取金錢的專家。"},{"en":"A court may invite paid experts to explain technical evidence.","zh":"法庭可能邀請受薪專家解釋技術證據。"},{"en":"Paid experts can be useful, but people may question their independence if payment affects their views.","zh":"受薪專家可以有用，但如果金錢影響其看法，人們可能質疑其獨立性。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on experts whose opinions are financially rewarded.","zh":"這個短語著重意見獲金錢回報的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"media celebrities","meaning":"傳媒名人","examples":[{"en":"Media celebrities can benefit from public controversy.","zh":"傳媒名人可以從公共爭議中得益。"},{"en":"Media celebrities are famous people known mainly through television, radio, newspapers, or online platforms.","zh":"media celebrities 指主要透過電視、電台、報紙或網上平台為人熟知的名人。"},{"en":"A media celebrity may gain followers by commenting on emotional public issues.","zh":"傳媒名人可能透過評論情緒化公共議題來增加追隨者。"},{"en":"Controversy can give media celebrities more attention, even when their claims are weak.","zh":"爭議可以給傳媒名人更多注意，即使其聲稱薄弱。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to fame created or maintained through media exposure.","zh":"這個短語指透過媒體曝光創造或維持的名氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"benefit from","meaning":"從……中得益","examples":[{"en":"Some public figures benefit from creating controversy.","zh":"有些公眾人物從製造爭議中得益。"},{"en":"To benefit from something means to gain an advantage from it.","zh":"benefit from something 指從某事中獲得好處。"},{"en":"Students benefit from clear feedback because they know what to improve.","zh":"學生從清楚回饋中得益，因為他們知道要改善甚麼。"},{"en":"People may benefit from controversy if it gives them attention, money, or influence.","zh":"如果爭議帶來關注、金錢或影響力，人們可能從中得益。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving a positive gain from a situation.","zh":"這個短語描述從某情況獲得正面利益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"create controversy where none exists","meaning":"在沒有爭議的地方製造爭議","examples":[{"en":"Some people create controversy where none exists.","zh":"有些人在沒有爭議的地方製造爭議。"},{"en":"To create controversy where none exists means to make people argue about something that is not truly disputed.","zh":"create controversy where none exists 指令人在本來沒有真正爭議的事情上爭論。"},{"en":"A blogger may create controversy where none exists by turning a small school rule into a scandal.","zh":"網誌作者可能把一條小校規變成醜聞，在沒有爭議的地方製造爭議。"},{"en":"This can waste public attention and make simple facts seem uncertain.","zh":"這可以浪費公眾注意力，並令簡單事實看似不確定。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises people who manufacture conflict.","zh":"這個短語批評那些製造衝突的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"snake-oil salesmen","meaning":"江湖郎中；兜售假藥的人","examples":[{"en":"The writer criticises snake-oil salesmen who oppose vaccination.","zh":"作者批評反對疫苗接種的江湖郎中。"},{"en":"Snake-oil salesmen are people who sell useless or dishonest cures while pretending they work.","zh":"snake-oil salesmen 指出售無用或不誠實療法，卻假裝有效的人。"},{"en":"A website selling miracle pills for every illness may be run by snake-oil salesmen.","zh":"出售能治所有疾病的神奇藥丸網站，可能由兜售假藥的人營運。"},{"en":"Snake-oil salesmen profit when frightened people buy unproven treatments.","zh":"當受驚的人購買未經證實療法，江湖郎中就能獲利。"},{"en":"This phrase is strongly critical and suggests fraud.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評，暗示欺詐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"oppose vaccination","meaning":"反對疫苗接種","examples":[{"en":"Some alternative medicine practitioners oppose vaccination.","zh":"有些替代醫學從業者反對疫苗接種。"},{"en":"To oppose vaccination means to disagree with or campaign against the use of vaccines.","zh":"oppose vaccination 指不同意或宣傳反對使用疫苗。"},{"en":"A person may oppose vaccination after reading frightening but unreliable stories online.","zh":"一個人在網上讀到嚇人但不可靠的故事後，可能反對疫苗接種。"},{"en":"Opposing vaccination can affect others if lower uptake allows diseases to spread.","zh":"如果較低接種率讓疾病傳播，反對疫苗接種可以影響他人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes resistance to vaccines.","zh":"這個短語描述對疫苗的抗拒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"pills, potions and treatments","meaning":"藥丸、藥水和療法","examples":[{"en":"Some sellers promote pills, potions and unproven treatments.","zh":"有些賣家推銷藥丸、藥水和未經證實的療法。"},{"en":"Pills, potions and treatments means various medicines, liquids, and health methods, often mentioned critically here.","zh":"pills, potions and treatments 指各種藥丸、液體和健康方法，在此常帶批評意味。"},{"en":"A dishonest seller may advertise pills, potions and treatments as quick cures for serious illness.","zh":"不誠實賣家可能把藥丸、藥水和療法宣傳成嚴重疾病的快速療法。"},{"en":"People should be careful when expensive products are promoted without reliable evidence.","zh":"當昂貴產品沒有可靠證據卻被推銷，人們應小心。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a mixed collection of questionable health products.","zh":"這個短語暗示一堆可疑健康產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"unproven expensive treatments","meaning":"未經證實的昂貴療法","examples":[{"en":"They promote unproven expensive treatments.","zh":"他們推銷未經證實的昂貴療法。"},{"en":"Unproven expensive treatments are costly treatments that have not been shown to work by reliable evidence.","zh":"unproven expensive treatments 指昂貴但未被可靠證據證明有效的療法。"},{"en":"A family may spend savings on unproven expensive treatments if they feel desperate.","zh":"如果家庭感到絕望，可能把積蓄花在未經證實的昂貴療法上。"},{"en":"These treatments can harm people financially and delay effective care.","zh":"這些療法可以在金錢上傷害人，並延誤有效治療。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that high price does not equal medical proof.","zh":"這個短語提醒高價不等於醫學證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"do the job better","meaning":"更有效地完成任務","examples":[{"en":"They believe their treatments do the job better.","zh":"他們相信自己的療法更有效地完成任務。"},{"en":"To do the job better means to perform the required task more effectively.","zh":"do the job better 指更有效地完成所需工作。"},{"en":"A reusable bottle may do the job better than a paper cup if students need water all day.","zh":"如果學生整天需要飲水，可重用水樽可能比紙杯更有效地完成任務。"},{"en":"Claims that something does the job better need evidence, not only confidence.","zh":"聲稱某物更有效地完成任務，需要證據，而不只是信心。"},{"en":"This phrase compares effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語比較有效性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"rational science","meaning":"理性科學","examples":[{"en":"The writer asks how rational science can prevail.","zh":"作者問理性科學如何能佔上風。"},{"en":"Rational science is science based on reason, evidence, and careful testing.","zh":"rational science 指基於理性、證據和仔細測試的科學。"},{"en":"A public-health campaign should use rational science rather than rumours or fear.","zh":"公共衛生宣傳應使用理性科學，而不是謠言或恐懼。"},{"en":"Rational science can protect people when decisions need reliable evidence.","zh":"當決定需要可靠證據，理性科學可以保護人。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts reasoned evidence with emotional or false claims.","zh":"這個短語把理性證據與情緒化或虛假聲稱作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"prevail","meaning":"佔上風；獲勝","examples":[{"en":"The writer wonders how rational science can prevail.","zh":"作者想知道理性科學如何能佔上風。"},{"en":"To prevail means to win, succeed, or become accepted after struggle or competition.","zh":"prevail 指在掙扎或競爭後勝出、成功或被接受。"},{"en":"In a class debate, the strongest evidence should prevail over loud opinions.","zh":"在課堂辯論中，最強證據應該壓過大聲意見而佔上風。"},{"en":"Science prevails when people value evidence more than fear.","zh":"當人們重視證據多於恐懼，科學就能獲勝。"},{"en":"This word describes one side winning influence or acceptance.","zh":"這個詞描述一方取得影響力或接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct heading for each paragraph.","zh":"學生為每段選出正確標題。"},{"en":"To choose the correct heading means to select the title that best summarises a paragraph.","zh":"choose the correct heading 指選出最能概括段落的標題。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should identify the main idea before choosing the heading.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先找出主旨，再選標題。"},{"en":"Wrong headings often focus on a detail rather than the whole paragraph.","zh":"錯誤標題常聚焦於細節，而不是整段。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in reading exams.","zh":"這個短語是閱讀考試常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The question provides a list of headings.","zh":"題目提供一個標題列表。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a set of possible paragraph titles for students to choose from.","zh":"list of headings 指供學生選擇的一組可能段落標題。"},{"en":"Students should read all items in the list of headings before matching them to paragraphs.","zh":"學生配對段落前，應閱讀標題列表中的所有項目。"},{"en":"Similar headings can confuse students if they do not identify the main idea carefully.","zh":"如果學生沒有仔細找主旨，相似標題可能令他們混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the answer options in a heading-matching task.","zh":"這個短語指標題配對題中的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"easy publicity","meaning":"輕易得到的宣傳","examples":[{"en":"One heading refers to easy publicity.","zh":"一個標題提到輕易得到的宣傳。"},{"en":"Easy publicity means attention that is gained quickly and with little effort.","zh":"easy publicity 指迅速且不用太多努力就得到的關注。"},{"en":"A celebrity can get easy publicity by making a shocking comment online.","zh":"名人可以透過在網上發表驚人言論輕易得到宣傳。"},{"en":"Easy publicity can reward people for creating noise rather than giving accurate information.","zh":"輕易得到的宣傳可能獎勵製造聲浪的人，而不是提供準確資訊的人。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests attention gained cheaply or irresponsibly.","zh":"這個短語常暗示廉價或不負責任地取得關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"increasing outbreaks of disease","meaning":"疾病爆發增加","examples":[{"en":"One heading refers to increasing outbreaks of disease.","zh":"一個標題提到疾病爆發增加。"},{"en":"Increasing outbreaks of disease means more frequent or more numerous disease outbreaks.","zh":"increasing outbreaks of disease 指疾病爆發變得更頻繁或數量更多。"},{"en":"A city may face increasing outbreaks of disease if sanitation and vaccination both decline.","zh":"如果衛生和疫苗接種都下降，城市可能面對疾病爆發增加。"},{"en":"Rising outbreaks warn that prevention systems are weakening.","zh":"爆發增加警告預防系統正在變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a worsening public-health pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述惡化中的公共衛生模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"some real reasons","meaning":"一些真正原因","examples":[{"en":"The question includes a heading about some real reasons.","zh":"題目包括一個關於一些真正原因的標題。"},{"en":"Some real reasons are actual causes behind a situation, not the reasons people merely claim.","zh":"some real reasons 指某情況背後的實際原因，而不是人們只是聲稱的原因。"},{"en":"Some real reasons for lateness may include poor transport and family duties, not laziness.","zh":"遲到的一些真正原因可能包括交通差和家庭責任，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"Looking for real reasons helps people avoid blaming the wrong group.","zh":"尋找真正原因幫助人避免怪責錯誤群體。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests deeper or more honest explanation.","zh":"這個短語暗示更深層或更誠實的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"all or nothing","meaning":"全有或全無；非黑即白","examples":[{"en":"One heading uses the phrase “all or nothing.”","zh":"一個標題使用 “all or nothing” 這個短語。"},{"en":"All or nothing means treating something as having only two extreme choices with no middle ground.","zh":"all or nothing 指把某事視為只有兩個極端選擇，沒有中間地帶。"},{"en":"A student may think revision is all or nothing: either study five hours or give up.","zh":"學生可能把溫習想成非黑即白：要麼讀五小時，要麼放棄。"},{"en":"All-or-nothing thinking can make decisions less flexible and less realistic.","zh":"非黑即白思維可以令決定較不靈活、較不現實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a black-and-white way of thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述黑白分明的思考方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"on the rise","meaning":"正在上升","examples":[{"en":"The heading suggests that autism is on the rise.","zh":"該標題暗示自閉症正在上升。"},{"en":"On the rise means increasing or becoming more common.","zh":"on the rise 指正在增加或變得更常見。"},{"en":"Online shopping is on the rise when more families buy groceries through apps.","zh":"當更多家庭透過應用程式買雜貨，網上購物就是正在上升。"},{"en":"When something is on the rise, people often ask what is causing the increase.","zh":"當某事正在上升，人們常會問是甚麼造成增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an upward trend.","zh":"這個短語描述上升趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"past successes","meaning":"過往成功例子","examples":[{"en":"One heading refers to the past successes of vaccination.","zh":"一個標題提到疫苗接種的過往成功例子。"},{"en":"Past successes are achievements that happened before and can be used as evidence or lessons.","zh":"past successes 指以前發生、可用作證據或教訓的成就。"},{"en":"A school may mention past successes to show that its reading programme works.","zh":"學校可能提到過往成功例子，以顯示閱讀計劃有效。"},{"en":"Past successes can build trust, but people may forget them when dangers disappear.","zh":"過往成功例子可以建立信任，但當危險消失時，人們可能忘記它們。"},{"en":"This phrase points to earlier achievements.","zh":"這個短語指早前成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a sad consequence","meaning":"令人難過的後果","examples":[{"en":"The example heading refers to a sad consequence.","zh":"例子標題提到令人難過的後果。"},{"en":"A sad consequence is an unhappy result of an action or situation.","zh":"a sad consequence 指某行動或情況帶來的不幸結果。"},{"en":"A sad consequence of bullying is that victims may stop enjoying school.","zh":"欺凌的一個令人難過後果，是受害者可能不再喜歡上學。"},{"en":"Consequences feel sadder when they could have been avoided.","zh":"當後果本可避免，它會更令人難過。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the painful result that follows.","zh":"這個短語著重隨後出現的痛苦結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"an unfortunate coincidence","meaning":"不幸的巧合","examples":[{"en":"One heading refers to an unfortunate coincidence.","zh":"一個標題提到不幸的巧合。"},{"en":"An unfortunate coincidence is when two events happen close together in a way that causes confusion or trouble.","zh":"an unfortunate coincidence 指兩件事接近發生，並因此造成混亂或麻煩。"},{"en":"It was an unfortunate coincidence that the fire alarm failed on the same day as a real emergency.","zh":"火警鐘在真正緊急事故同一天故障，是不幸的巧合。"},{"en":"Coincidence can lead people to assume cause when there is only timing.","zh":"巧合可以令人因時間接近而以為有因果關係。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bad luck in timing, not proof of connection.","zh":"這個短語描述時間上的壞運氣，而不是關聯證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a simple explanation","meaning":"簡單解釋","examples":[{"en":"The heading suggests that there is a simple explanation.","zh":"該標題暗示有一個簡單解釋。"},{"en":"A simple explanation is a clear reason that makes a confusing situation easier to understand.","zh":"a simple explanation 指令混亂情況較容易理解的清楚原因。"},{"en":"A simple explanation for a student’s tiredness may be that he slept only four hours.","zh":"學生疲倦的一個簡單解釋，可能是他只睡了四小時。"},{"en":"Simple explanations are useful when they are supported by evidence, not just attractive.","zh":"簡單解釋如果有證據支持就有用，而不只是吸引人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an easy-to-understand cause or answer.","zh":"這個短語描述容易理解的原因或答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"dubious evidence","meaning":"可疑證據","examples":[{"en":"One heading refers to dubious evidence.","zh":"一個標題提到可疑證據。"},{"en":"Dubious evidence is evidence that is doubtful, weak, or not fully trustworthy.","zh":"dubious evidence 指令人懷疑、薄弱或不完全可信的證據。"},{"en":"A screenshot without a source may be dubious evidence in a school complaint.","zh":"沒有來源的截圖在學校投訴中可能是可疑證據。"},{"en":"Dubious evidence can mislead people if it is presented with strong emotion.","zh":"如果可疑證據以強烈情緒呈現，它可以誤導人。"},{"en":"This phrase warns readers to question the reliability of the support given.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者質疑所給支持是否可靠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"choose three answers from","meaning":"從……中選出三個答案","examples":[{"en":"Students choose three answers from the list.","zh":"學生從列表中選出三個答案。"},{"en":"To choose three answers from a list means to select exactly three options provided.","zh":"choose three answers from a list 指從所提供選項中準確選出三個。"},{"en":"In an exam, students may lose marks if they choose two or four answers instead of three.","zh":"在考試中，如果學生選兩個或四個答案而不是三個，可能會失分。"},{"en":"Reading the whole list first helps students avoid choosing attractive but wrong options.","zh":"先閱讀整個列表，幫助學生避免選擇吸引但錯誤的選項。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the number and source of answers.","zh":"這個短語給出答案數量和來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"oppose vaccinations","meaning":"反對疫苗接種","examples":[{"en":"The question asks why anti-vaccinationists oppose vaccinations.","zh":"題目問為何反疫苗人士反對疫苗接種。"},{"en":"To oppose vaccinations means to disagree with or resist vaccine use.","zh":"oppose vaccinations 指不同意或抗拒使用疫苗。"},{"en":"Some people oppose vaccinations because they misunderstand how vaccines protect communities.","zh":"有些人反對疫苗接種，是因為誤解疫苗如何保護社區。"},{"en":"Opposition can lower vaccination rates if it spreads through families and online groups.","zh":"如果反對意見透過家庭和網上群組傳播，它可以降低疫苗接種率。"},{"en":"This phrase describes resistance to receiving or supporting vaccines.","zh":"這個短語描述抗拒接種或支持疫苗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"believe they cause problems","meaning":"相信它們會造成問題","examples":[{"en":"Some people oppose vaccinations because they believe they cause problems.","zh":"有些人反對疫苗接種，因為他們相信它們會造成問題。"},{"en":"To believe they cause problems means to think they create harm or trouble.","zh":"believe they cause problems 指認為它們會造成傷害或麻煩。"},{"en":"A parent may avoid a food if they believe it causes stomach problems for their child.","zh":"如果父母相信某種食物會令孩子腸胃不適，可能會避免它。"},{"en":"Beliefs about harm can change behaviour even when the belief is not supported by evidence.","zh":"關於傷害的信念可以改變行為，即使該信念沒有證據支持。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a reason for opposition.","zh":"這個短語解釋反對的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"freedom of choice","meaning":"選擇自由","examples":[{"en":"Some people oppose vaccination in the name of freedom of choice.","zh":"有些人以選擇自由之名反對疫苗接種。"},{"en":"Freedom of choice means the right to decide for oneself among different options.","zh":"freedom of choice 指在不同選項之間自行決定的權利。"},{"en":"Students may value freedom of choice when selecting books for a project.","zh":"學生在項目中選書時，可能重視選擇自由。"},{"en":"Freedom of choice has limits when private decisions create public risk.","zh":"當私人決定造成公共風險，選擇自由就有界限。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in debates about rights and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語常用於關於權利和責任的辯論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"drug manufacturers","meaning":"藥廠","examples":[{"en":"Some opponents do not trust drug manufacturers.","zh":"有些反對者不信任藥廠。"},{"en":"Drug manufacturers are companies that make medicines and medical products.","zh":"drug manufacturers 指製造藥物和醫療產品的公司。"},{"en":"A hospital buys medicines from drug manufacturers that meet safety standards.","zh":"醫院向符合安全標準的藥廠購買藥物。"},{"en":"Distrust of manufacturers can make people question products even when evidence supports them.","zh":"對藥廠的不信任可以令人質疑產品，即使證據支持它們。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to companies that produce drugs.","zh":"這個短語指生產藥物的公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the pain of vaccinations","meaning":"接種疫苗的痛楚","examples":[{"en":"One answer option mentions the pain of vaccinations.","zh":"一個答案選項提到接種疫苗的痛楚。"},{"en":"The pain of vaccinations means the brief discomfort caused by an injection.","zh":"the pain of vaccinations 指注射造成的短暫不適。"},{"en":"A child may cry because of the pain of vaccination, even though the pain usually passes quickly.","zh":"孩子可能因接種疫苗的痛楚而哭，即使痛楚通常很快過去。"},{"en":"Fear of a short injection can sometimes feel larger than the actual risk.","zh":"對短暫注射的恐懼，有時感覺比實際風險更大。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to physical discomfort, not the overall value of vaccination.","zh":"這個短語指身體不適，而不是疫苗接種的整體價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the influence of","meaning":"……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions the influence of creationists.","zh":"題目提到創造論者的影響。"},{"en":"The influence of someone or something is the effect they have on people’s ideas or actions.","zh":"the influence of someone or something 指他們對人們想法或行動造成的影響。"},{"en":"The influence of friends can affect what subjects a student chooses.","zh":"朋友的影響可以影響學生選擇哪些科目。"},{"en":"Strong influence can spread beliefs even when people do not fully understand them.","zh":"強大影響可以傳播信念，即使人們未完全理解那些信念。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on power to affect others.","zh":"這個短語著重影響他人的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"preferring alternative medicine","meaning":"較喜歡替代醫學","examples":[{"en":"Some people oppose vaccination because they prefer alternative medicine.","zh":"有些人反對疫苗接種，因為他們較喜歡替代醫學。"},{"en":"Preferring alternative medicine means choosing non-mainstream treatments over conventional medical care.","zh":"preferring alternative medicine 指選擇非主流療法，而不是常規醫療護理。"},{"en":"A patient may prefer alternative medicine because it feels more personal or natural.","zh":"病人可能較喜歡替代醫學，因為它感覺較個人化或自然。"},{"en":"Preference becomes risky when it replaces proven treatment for serious conditions.","zh":"當偏好取代嚴重疾病的已證實治療，就會變得有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a choice of treatment style.","zh":"這個短語描述治療方式的選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"most likely inherited","meaning":"很可能是遺傳的","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether autism is most likely inherited.","zh":"題目問自閉症是否很可能是遺傳的。"},{"en":"Most likely inherited means probably passed through genes from parents or family lines.","zh":"most likely inherited 指很可能透過基因從父母或家族傳下來。"},{"en":"A doctor may ask about relatives if a condition is most likely inherited.","zh":"如果某狀況很可能是遺傳的，醫生可能詢問親屬情況。"},{"en":"Inherited conditions can appear even when no recent event caused them.","zh":"遺傳狀況即使沒有近期事件造成，也可以出現。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a probable genetic explanation.","zh":"這個短語表達可能的基因解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"subtle neurological disorder","meaning":"輕微神經系統障礙","examples":[{"en":"One option describes autism as a subtle neurological disorder.","zh":"一個選項把自閉症描述為輕微神經系統障礙。"},{"en":"A subtle neurological disorder is a nervous-system condition with signs that may be mild or hard to notice.","zh":"subtle neurological disorder 指症狀可能輕微或不易察覺的神經系統狀況。"},{"en":"A child with a subtle neurological disorder may need careful observation before diagnosis.","zh":"有輕微神經系統障礙的孩子，可能需要仔細觀察才可診斷。"},{"en":"Subtle disorders can be misunderstood because their signs are not always obvious.","zh":"輕微障礙可能被誤解，因為其跡象不一定明顯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a condition affecting the nervous system in a less obvious way.","zh":"這個短語描述以較不明顯方式影響神經系統的狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the cause of falling vaccination rates","meaning":"疫苗接種率下降的原因","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether the paper was the cause of falling vaccination rates.","zh":"題目問該論文是否是疫苗接種率下降的原因。"},{"en":"The cause of falling vaccination rates means the reason why fewer people received vaccines.","zh":"the cause of falling vaccination rates 指較少人接種疫苗的原因。"},{"en":"Fearful news reports may become the cause of falling participation in a health programme.","zh":"令人恐懼的新聞報道可能成為健康計劃參與率下降的原因。"},{"en":"To identify a cause, people need evidence that one event led to the decrease.","zh":"要找出原因，人們需要證據顯示一件事導致下降。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on why a rate went down.","zh":"這個短語著重某比率為何下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be defended by","meaning":"得到……辯護","examples":[{"en":"The option says the paper was defended by the medical journal.","zh":"該選項說該論文得到醫學期刊辯護。"},{"en":"To be defended by someone means to be supported or protected against criticism by that person or organisation.","zh":"be defended by someone 指受到某人或機構支持或保護，以抵禦批評。"},{"en":"A school policy may be defended by the principal during a parents’ meeting.","zh":"校長可能在家長會上為學校政策辯護。"},{"en":"Defending a claim requires reasons and evidence, not only loyalty.","zh":"為某聲稱辯護需要理由和證據，而不只是忠誠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active support during criticism.","zh":"這個短語描述在批評中作出主動支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be verified by","meaning":"得到……證實","examples":[{"en":"The option says the paper was verified by other studies.","zh":"該選項說該論文得到其他研究證實。"},{"en":"To be verified by something means to be confirmed as true by that evidence or source.","zh":"be verified by something 指被該證據或來源證實為真。"},{"en":"A student’s answer is verified by the passage when the exact information appears there.","zh":"當文章中出現確切資料，學生答案就得到文章證實。"},{"en":"Claims become stronger when independent studies verify them.","zh":"當獨立研究證實聲稱，它們會變得更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes confirmation through checking.","zh":"這個短語描述透過核查得到確認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be funded by","meaning":"由……資助","examples":[{"en":"The option says the paper was funded by patients.","zh":"該選項說該論文由病人資助。"},{"en":"To be funded by someone means to receive money from them to support a project, study, or activity.","zh":"be funded by someone 指由某人提供金錢支持某項項目、研究或活動。"},{"en":"A school garden may be funded by parents and local shops.","zh":"學校花園可能由家長和本地商店資助。"},{"en":"Funding sources can affect how people judge independence and trustworthiness.","zh":"資金來源可以影響人們如何判斷獨立性和可信度。"},{"en":"This phrase explains who provided financial support.","zh":"這個短語解釋誰提供財政支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"supported by solid evidence","meaning":"得到可靠證據支持","examples":[{"en":"Vaccinations are supported by solid evidence.","zh":"疫苗接種得到可靠證據支持。"},{"en":"Supported by solid evidence means backed by strong, reliable proof.","zh":"supported by solid evidence 指由有力可靠證據支持。"},{"en":"A school policy is stronger when it is supported by solid evidence from student data.","zh":"當校政得到學生數據的可靠證據支持，它會更有力。"},{"en":"Solid evidence helps people distinguish reliable claims from rumours.","zh":"可靠證據幫助人們分辨可信聲稱和謠言。"},{"en":"This phrase means a claim has serious factual support.","zh":"這個短語表示某聲稱有嚴肅事實支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"no longer necessary","meaning":"不再必要","examples":[{"en":"One option claims that vaccinations are no longer necessary.","zh":"一個選項聲稱疫苗接種不再必要。"},{"en":"No longer necessary means no longer needed because circumstances have changed.","zh":"no longer necessary 指因情況改變而不再需要。"},{"en":"A paper map may be no longer necessary if a driver has a working GPS.","zh":"如果司機有能用的 GPS，紙本地圖可能不再必要。"},{"en":"In public health, something may appear unnecessary only because it has been working well.","zh":"在公共衛生中，某事可能只是因為一直有效運作而看似不再必要。"},{"en":"This phrase should be checked against evidence before being accepted.","zh":"這個短語在被接受前應以證據核查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"generally good","meaning":"一般而言是好的","examples":[{"en":"One option asks whether practitioners believe vaccinations are generally good.","zh":"一個選項問從業者是否相信疫苗接種一般而言是好的。"},{"en":"Generally good means good in most cases, though not necessarily perfect in every situation.","zh":"generally good 指在大多數情況下是好的，但不一定每個情況都完美。"},{"en":"A school rule may be generally good if it protects most students fairly.","zh":"如果校規公平地保護大多數學生，它可能一般而言是好的。"},{"en":"Saying something is generally good allows room for rare exceptions.","zh":"說某事一般而言是好的，容許存在少數例外。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a broad positive judgement.","zh":"這個短語給出廣泛正面判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"supported by politicians","meaning":"得到政客支持","examples":[{"en":"One option says alternative medicine practitioners are supported by politicians.","zh":"一個選項說替代醫學從業者得到政客支持。"},{"en":"Supported by politicians means backed, defended, or promoted by political figures.","zh":"supported by politicians 指得到政治人物支持、辯護或推廣。"},{"en":"A new transport plan may be supported by politicians from several parties.","zh":"一項新交通計劃可能得到幾個政黨的政客支持。"},{"en":"Political support can make an idea appear more acceptable to the public.","zh":"政治支持可以令某想法在公眾眼中看起來更可接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes backing from people in politics.","zh":"這個短語描述來自政治人物的支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"quite cheap","meaning":"相當便宜","examples":[{"en":"One option describes alternative medicine practitioners as quite cheap.","zh":"一個選項把替代醫學從業者描述為相當便宜。"},{"en":"Quite cheap means fairly low in price, though not necessarily the cheapest possible.","zh":"quite cheap 指價格頗低，但不一定是最低。"},{"en":"A lunch set may be quite cheap if it costs less than most nearby restaurants.","zh":"如果午餐套餐比附近大多數餐廳便宜，它可能相當便宜。"},{"en":"A treatment being quite cheap does not prove that it is effective or safe.","zh":"療法相當便宜並不能證明它有效或安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes price, not quality.","zh":"這個短語描述價格，而不是質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 96 - The Immunisation Controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 97":[{"front":"Are You Being Served?","meaning":"《有人招呼你嗎？》；標題文字遊戲：served 呼應 services，把「顧客服務」連到「服務業」","examples":[{"en":"The title Are You Being Served? hints at the growing importance of services.","zh":"標題《有人招呼你嗎？》暗示服務業的重要性正在上升。"},{"en":"Are You Being Served? is a title that plays on the idea of customer service and the wider services economy.","zh":"Are You Being Served? 是一個標題，利用「顧客服務」和更廣泛的服務型經濟之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"A shop assistant might ask, “Are you being served?” when checking whether a customer needs help.","zh":"店員可能會問 “Are you being served?”，以確認顧客是否需要幫忙。"},{"en":"The title is clever because “served” connects ordinary customer help with the economic idea of services.","zh":"這個標題巧妙之處在於 served 把普通顧客服務與經濟上的 services 連起來。"},{"en":"This title prepares readers to think about service work, not only factory production.","zh":"這個標題讓讀者準備思考服務工作，而不只是工廠生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the world’s factory","meaning":"世界工廠","examples":[{"en":"China is often described as the world’s factory.","zh":"中國常被形容為世界工廠。"},{"en":"The world’s factory means a country that produces a very large share of goods for global markets.","zh":"the world’s factory 指為全球市場生產大量貨品的國家。"},{"en":"A country may be called the world’s factory if many international brands make their products there.","zh":"如果許多國際品牌在某國生產產品，該國可能被稱為世界工廠。"},{"en":"This label focuses on manufacturing strength, but it can hide other parts of the economy.","zh":"這個標籤集中於製造業實力，但可能掩蓋經濟中的其他部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a production role, not literally one single factory.","zh":"這個短語描述生產角色，而不是字面上一間工廠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"it turns out","meaning":"原來；結果發現","examples":[{"en":"The world’s factory, it turns out, has a sizeable services sector.","zh":"原來，這個世界工廠有一個相當大的服務業。"},{"en":"It turns out introduces information that may be surprising or different from what people expected.","zh":"it turns out 用來引入可能令人驚訝，或與人們預期不同的資訊。"},{"en":"I thought the class was easy; it turns out many students found the listening task difficult.","zh":"我以為這班很容易教；結果發現許多學生覺得聆聽任務困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when new evidence changes the reader’s impression.","zh":"當新證據改變讀者印象時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It often signals that the real situation is more complex than the first assumption.","zh":"它常表示真實情況比最初假設更複雜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a sizeable canteen attached","meaning":"附帶一個相當大的飯堂","examples":[{"en":"The world’s factory has a sizeable canteen attached.","zh":"這個世界工廠附帶一個相當大的飯堂。"},{"en":"A sizeable canteen attached is a humorous image suggesting that a factory economy also has a large service side.","zh":"a sizeable canteen attached 是一個幽默意象，暗示工廠型經濟也有龐大服務業部分。"},{"en":"A school known for exams may also have a sizeable sports programme attached.","zh":"一所因考試聞名的學校，也可能附帶一個相當大的體育項目。"},{"en":"The phrase makes the services sector seem like an extra but important part of the main factory image.","zh":"這個短語令服務業看似是工廠形象旁邊的額外但重要部分。"},{"en":"It uses a canteen metaphor to show that production needs services around it.","zh":"它用飯堂比喻，顯示生產活動周圍也需要服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"not to mention","meaning":"更不用說","examples":[{"en":"China has a large canteen, not to mention an office block and shopping mall.","zh":"中國有一個大飯堂，更不用說辦公大樓和商場。"},{"en":"Not to mention introduces an extra point that makes the previous statement even stronger.","zh":"not to mention 用來加入額外重點，使前一句更有力。"},{"en":"The new campus has a library, not to mention a swimming pool and theatre.","zh":"新校園有圖書館，更不用說游泳池和劇場。"},{"en":"The phrase adds more evidence after the reader already has enough reason to agree.","zh":"這個短語在讀者已有足夠理由同意後，再加入更多證據。"},{"en":"It means “and also, importantly” rather than a point to ignore.","zh":"它意思是「而且還有重要的是」，不是叫人不要提。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"office block","meaning":"辦公大樓","examples":[{"en":"The services economy includes office blocks and shopping malls.","zh":"服務型經濟包括辦公大樓和商場。"},{"en":"An office block is a large building divided into offices for companies or organisations.","zh":"office block 指被分成辦公室、供公司或機構使用的大型建築物。"},{"en":"A growing business district may need more office blocks for accountants, lawyers, and consultants.","zh":"發展中的商業區可能需要更多辦公大樓給會計師、律師和顧問使用。"},{"en":"More office blocks can signal that professional services are expanding.","zh":"更多辦公大樓可以顯示專業服務正在擴張。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to workplace buildings, not factories or homes.","zh":"這個短語指工作場所建築，而不是工廠或住宅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"shopping mall","meaning":"商場","examples":[{"en":"A shopping mall is part of the expanding services economy.","zh":"商場是擴張中的服務型經濟的一部分。"},{"en":"A shopping mall is a large indoor or covered area with many shops, restaurants, and services.","zh":"shopping mall 指有許多商店、餐廳和服務的大型室內或有蓋購物區。"},{"en":"Families may spend weekends in a shopping mall to eat, shop, and watch films.","zh":"家庭可能週末到商場吃飯、購物和看電影。"},{"en":"When incomes rise, shopping malls often grow because people spend more on services and leisure.","zh":"當收入上升，商場通常會增長，因為人們在服務和休閒上花更多錢。"},{"en":"The phrase points to consumer services rather than manufacturing.","zh":"這個短語指向消費服務，而不是製造業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"official revision of","meaning":"對……的官方修訂","examples":[{"en":"The official revision of China’s GDP revealed a larger economy.","zh":"對中國 GDP 的官方修訂顯示經濟規模更大。"},{"en":"An official revision of a figure is a formal correction or update made by an authority.","zh":"official revision of a figure 指由權威機構正式作出的修正或更新。"},{"en":"A school may make an official revision of exam dates after a typhoon warning.","zh":"颱風警告後，學校可能對考試日期作官方修訂。"},{"en":"Revisions can change how people understand the size or direction of a situation.","zh":"修訂可以改變人們對某情況規模或方向的理解。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the change comes from an authorised source.","zh":"這個短語強調改動來自授權來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"gross domestic product","meaning":"本地生產總值","examples":[{"en":"China’s gross domestic product was revised upwards.","zh":"中國的本地生產總值被向上修訂。"},{"en":"Gross domestic product is the total value of goods and services produced in a country over a period of time.","zh":"gross domestic product 指一個國家在某段時間內生產的貨品和服務總值。"},{"en":"Governments use gross domestic product to compare the size of different economies.","zh":"政府使用本地生產總值比較不同經濟體的規模。"},{"en":"If services are undercounted, gross domestic product may look smaller than it really is.","zh":"如果服務業被低估，本地生產總值可能看起來比實際小。"},{"en":"The phrase is often shortened to GDP.","zh":"這個短語常縮寫為 GDP。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"reveal an economy worth","meaning":"顯示經濟規模達……","examples":[{"en":"The revision revealed an economy worth 16 trillion yuan.","zh":"這次修訂顯示經濟規模達16萬億元人民幣。"},{"en":"To reveal an economy worth a certain amount means to show that the economy’s measured value is that large.","zh":"reveal an economy worth a certain amount 指顯示該經濟體的量度價值有如此大。"},{"en":"A new survey may reveal a local food market worth millions of dollars a year.","zh":"新調查可能顯示本地食品市場每年規模達數百萬元。"},{"en":"Better data can reveal hidden economic activity that old systems missed.","zh":"更好數據可以揭示舊制度遺漏的隱藏經濟活動。"},{"en":"The phrase connects new information with the measured size of an economy.","zh":"這個短語把新資訊與經濟量度規模連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"previously thought","meaning":"先前所認為的","examples":[{"en":"The economy was larger than previously thought.","zh":"經濟規模比先前所認為的更大。"},{"en":"Previously thought means believed earlier, before new information appeared.","zh":"previously thought 指在新資訊出現前早先相信的看法。"},{"en":"The repair cost was lower than previously thought after the mechanic checked the car.","zh":"技工檢查汽車後，維修費比先前所認為的低。"},{"en":"New evidence can show that earlier estimates were wrong or incomplete.","zh":"新證據可以顯示早前估算錯誤或不完整。"},{"en":"The phrase compares old understanding with updated knowledge.","zh":"這個短語把舊理解與更新後知識作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be ascribed to","meaning":"被歸因於……","examples":[{"en":"Most of the increase was ascribed to the services sector.","zh":"大部分增幅被歸因於服務業。"},{"en":"To be ascribed to something means to be explained as being caused by it.","zh":"be ascribed to something 指被解釋為由某事造成。"},{"en":"A rise in exam scores may be ascribed to extra practice and clearer feedback.","zh":"考試分數上升可能被歸因於額外練習和更清楚回饋。"},{"en":"When statisticians ascribe growth to one sector, they identify where the change mainly came from.","zh":"當統計人員把增長歸因於某一行業，他們是在指出變化主要來自哪裏。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and means “be attributed to”.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是「歸因於」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the services sector","meaning":"服務業","examples":[{"en":"The services sector accounted for most of the newly measured activity.","zh":"服務業佔新量度經濟活動的大部分。"},{"en":"The services sector is the part of the economy that provides services rather than physical goods.","zh":"services sector 指提供服務而不是實體貨品的經濟部分。"},{"en":"Restaurants, schools, hospitals, banks, and transport firms belong to the services sector.","zh":"餐廳、學校、醫院、銀行和運輸公司都屬於服務業。"},{"en":"As people become richer, the services sector often grows because demand shifts beyond basic goods.","zh":"當人們變得更富裕，服務業通常會增長，因為需求轉向基本貨品以外。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts services with manufacturing and primary industries.","zh":"這個短語把服務與製造業和第一產業作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, services’ share of the economy increased sharply.","zh":"因此，服務業佔經濟的比重大幅上升。"},{"en":"As a result introduces the consequence of something just mentioned.","zh":"as a result 用來引入剛提到事情的結果。"},{"en":"The school added more speaking practice; as a result, students became more confident.","zh":"學校加入更多口語練習；因此，學生變得更有信心。"},{"en":"The phrase helps readers see cause and effect clearly.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者清楚看見因果關係。"},{"en":"It means “because of this”.","zh":"它意思是「因為這樣」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"share of the economy","meaning":"佔經濟的比重","examples":[{"en":"Services’ share of the economy jumped to 41%.","zh":"服務業佔經濟的比重躍升至41%。"},{"en":"Share of the economy means the percentage or part of total economic activity held by a sector.","zh":"share of the economy 指某行業在總經濟活動中所佔的百分比或部分。"},{"en":"Tourism’s share of a small island’s economy may be very large if most jobs depend on visitors.","zh":"如果大多數工作依賴遊客，旅遊業在小島經濟中的比重可能很大。"},{"en":"When a sector’s share rises, it becomes more important in the overall economy.","zh":"當一個行業比重上升，它在整體經濟中變得更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase measures relative weight, not absolute size alone.","zh":"這個短語量度相對份量，而不只是絕對規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"jump by nine percentage points","meaning":"上升九個百分點","examples":[{"en":"The services sector jumped by nine percentage points.","zh":"服務業上升九個百分點。"},{"en":"To jump by nine percentage points means to increase by nine points on a percentage scale.","zh":"jump by nine percentage points 指在百分比尺度上增加九個點。"},{"en":"If support for a policy rises from 30% to 39%, it jumps by nine percentage points.","zh":"如果某政策支持率由30%升至39%，就是上升九個百分點。"},{"en":"Percentage points measure the difference between two percentages, not a percentage of the old number.","zh":"百分點量度兩個百分比之間的差距，不是舊數字的百分比。"},{"en":"The phrase signals a clear statistical increase.","zh":"這個短語表示清楚的統計增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Services accounted for 41%, compared with 46% for manufacturing.","zh":"服務業佔41%，與製造業的46%相比。"},{"en":"Compared with introduces another figure or situation used for comparison.","zh":"compared with 用來引入另一個作比較的數字或情況。"},{"en":"The class average was 72%, compared with 65% last term.","zh":"班平均分是72%，與上學期的65%相比。"},{"en":"Comparison helps readers judge whether a number is high, low, larger, or smaller.","zh":"比較幫助讀者判斷數字是高、低、較大還是較小。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when two statistics are placed side by side.","zh":"當兩項統計並列時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"manufacturing","meaning":"製造業","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturing still accounted for a larger share than services.","zh":"製造業所佔比重仍大於服務業。"},{"en":"Manufacturing is the part of the economy that makes physical goods in factories or workshops.","zh":"manufacturing 指在工廠或工場製造實體貨品的經濟部分。"},{"en":"Making cars, phones, clothes, and furniture are examples of manufacturing.","zh":"製造汽車、電話、衣服和家具都是製造業例子。"},{"en":"Manufacturing creates goods, while services often involve helping, advising, transporting, or selling.","zh":"製造業創造貨品，而服務業通常涉及協助、建議、運輸或銷售。"},{"en":"The word refers to production of tangible products.","zh":"這個詞指有形產品的生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"primary industries","meaning":"第一產業","examples":[{"en":"Primary industries include mainly agriculture and mining.","zh":"第一產業主要包括農業和採礦業。"},{"en":"Primary industries are sectors that obtain raw materials directly from nature.","zh":"primary industries 指直接從自然界取得原材料的行業。"},{"en":"Farming vegetables, catching fish, and extracting coal are primary-industry activities.","zh":"種植蔬菜、捕魚和開採煤炭都是第一產業活動。"},{"en":"Primary industries provide basic resources that manufacturing and services may later use.","zh":"第一產業提供製造業和服務業後來可能使用的基本資源。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the first stage of economic production.","zh":"這個短語指經濟生產的第一階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"agriculture and mining","meaning":"農業和採礦業","examples":[{"en":"Agriculture and mining are examples of primary industries.","zh":"農業和採礦業是第一產業的例子。"},{"en":"Agriculture and mining are industries that produce food or extract natural resources.","zh":"agriculture and mining 指生產食物或開採自然資源的行業。"},{"en":"Agriculture supplies crops and livestock, while mining supplies coal, metal, and minerals.","zh":"農業供應農作物和牲畜，而採礦業供應煤、金屬和礦物。"},{"en":"These industries can support factories by providing raw materials.","zh":"這些行業可以透過提供原材料來支持工廠。"},{"en":"The phrase names two basic resource-producing sectors.","zh":"這個短語命名兩個基本資源生產行業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"where has all this extra activity come from?","meaning":"這些額外經濟活動從何而來？","examples":[{"en":"The article asks where all this extra activity has come from.","zh":"文章問這些額外經濟活動從何而來。"},{"en":"Where has all this extra activity come from? asks what caused newly measured economic activity to appear.","zh":"where has all this extra activity come from? 是問新量度到的經濟活動由甚麼造成。"},{"en":"A teacher might ask where all the extra homework mistakes came from after changing the worksheet format.","zh":"老師改變工作紙格式後，可能會問額外功課錯誤從何而來。"},{"en":"The question encourages readers to look for sources behind a surprising increase.","zh":"這個問題鼓勵讀者尋找驚人增幅背後的來源。"},{"en":"It is a way of moving from the number itself to the explanation behind it.","zh":"它是一種由數字本身轉向背後解釋的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the bulk of","meaning":"大部分","examples":[{"en":"The bulk of the extra activity is obvious to travellers in China.","zh":"大部分額外活動對中國旅客來說很明顯。"},{"en":"The bulk of something means most or the largest part of it.","zh":"the bulk of something 指某事物的大部分或最大部分。"},{"en":"The bulk of a student’s revision time may go to reading if vocabulary is weak.","zh":"如果詞彙較弱，學生大部分溫習時間可能用在閱讀上。"},{"en":"Identifying the bulk of a problem helps people focus on the main source, not small details.","zh":"找出問題的大部分來源，幫助人集中處理主要原因，而不是小細節。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the majority rather than every single part.","zh":"這個短語指大多數，而不是每一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"obvious to","meaning":"對……來說很明顯","examples":[{"en":"The growth of services is obvious to any traveller in China.","zh":"服務業增長對任何在中國旅行的人來說都很明顯。"},{"en":"If something is obvious to someone, that person can notice or understand it easily.","zh":"obvious to someone 指某人能容易注意到或理解某事。"},{"en":"The need for more buses is obvious to students who wait an hour after school.","zh":"放學後等一小時巴士的學生，很明顯需要更多巴士。"},{"en":"When change appears in streets, shops, and daily life, it becomes obvious to ordinary people.","zh":"當變化出現在街道、商店和日常生活中，它就會對普通人很明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something easy for a particular group to see.","zh":"這個短語描述某群體容易看見的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"grow wealthier","meaning":"變得更富裕","examples":[{"en":"As people grow wealthier, they demand more services.","zh":"隨着人們變得更富裕，他們會需求更多服務。"},{"en":"To grow wealthier means to become richer over time.","zh":"grow wealthier 指隨時間變得更有錢。"},{"en":"As families grow wealthier, they may spend more on travel, tutoring, and healthcare.","zh":"隨着家庭變得更富裕，他們可能在旅遊、補習和醫療上花更多錢。"},{"en":"Rising income often changes demand from basic goods to convenience, education, and leisure.","zh":"收入上升通常把需求由基本貨品轉向便利、教育和休閒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an increase in people’s financial ability.","zh":"這個短語描述人們財政能力增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"car dealerships","meaning":"汽車經銷店","examples":[{"en":"Car dealerships are one example of China’s expanding services.","zh":"汽車經銷店是中國擴張中服務業的一個例子。"},{"en":"Car dealerships are businesses that sell cars and often provide repair, finance, and after-sales services.","zh":"car dealerships 指售賣汽車，並通常提供維修、融資和售後服務的企業。"},{"en":"A family may visit several car dealerships before choosing a new vehicle.","zh":"家庭在選擇新車前，可能到訪幾間汽車經銷店。"},{"en":"More car dealerships may appear when more households can afford private cars.","zh":"當更多家庭買得起私家車，更多汽車經銷店可能出現。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to retail and service businesses around cars.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞汽車的零售和服務企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"private hospitals","meaning":"私家醫院","examples":[{"en":"Private hospitals have become more common as people grow wealthier.","zh":"隨着人們變得更富裕，私家醫院變得更常見。"},{"en":"Private hospitals are hospitals run by private organisations rather than directly by the state.","zh":"private hospitals 指由私人機構而不是由國家直接營運的醫院。"},{"en":"Some patients choose private hospitals because they want shorter waiting times or more personal service.","zh":"有些病人選擇私家醫院，因為他們想要較短輪候時間或更個人化服務。"},{"en":"Demand for private hospitals can rise when people have more income and higher expectations for care.","zh":"當人們收入較高且對照顧有更高期望，對私家醫院的需求可能上升。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts privately run healthcare with public hospitals.","zh":"這個短語把私人營運醫療與公立醫院作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"English language classes","meaning":"英文課程","examples":[{"en":"English language classes are part of the growing services sector.","zh":"英文課程是增長中服務業的一部分。"},{"en":"English language classes are lessons that teach people to read, write, listen, or speak English.","zh":"English language classes 指教人閱讀、寫作、聆聽或說英語的課程。"},{"en":"Parents may send children to English language classes to improve school results and future job options.","zh":"家長可能送孩子上英文課程，以改善學校成績和未來工作選擇。"},{"en":"Demand for English classes can grow when business and international travel increase.","zh":"當商業和國際旅遊增加，對英文課程的需求可能增長。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to education services, not factory production.","zh":"這個短語指教育服務，而不是工廠生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"beauty salons","meaning":"美容院","examples":[{"en":"Beauty salons are among the businesses that have expanded in China.","zh":"美容院是中國已經擴張的企業之一。"},{"en":"Beauty salons are shops that provide hair, skin, nail, or beauty treatments.","zh":"beauty salons 指提供頭髮、皮膚、指甲或美容護理的店舖。"},{"en":"A person may visit a beauty salon before a wedding or job interview.","zh":"一個人可能在婚禮或求職面試前到美容院。"},{"en":"As disposable income rises, people may spend more on personal-care services.","zh":"隨着可支配收入上升，人們可能在個人護理服務上花更多錢。"},{"en":"The phrase belongs to lifestyle services rather than manufacturing.","zh":"這個短語屬於生活方式服務，而不是製造業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"turnover and profits","meaning":"營業額和利潤","examples":[{"en":"Turnover and profits in many small businesses were not fully recorded.","zh":"許多小企業的營業額和利潤沒有被完全記錄。"},{"en":"Turnover is total sales income, while profits are the money left after costs are paid.","zh":"turnover 是總銷售收入，而 profits 是扣除成本後剩下的錢。"},{"en":"A small restaurant may have high turnover but low profits if rent and wages are expensive.","zh":"如果租金和工資昂貴，小餐廳可能營業額高但利潤低。"},{"en":"If turnover and profits are not recorded, official statistics may underestimate business activity.","zh":"如果營業額和利潤沒有被記錄，官方統計可能低估商業活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes key financial measures of a company.","zh":"這個短語描述公司的關鍵財務指標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be captured by","meaning":"被記錄；被計入","examples":[{"en":"Their profits had not previously been captured by the statistical system.","zh":"它們的利潤先前沒有被統計制度記錄。"},{"en":"To be captured by a system means to be recorded or included by it.","zh":"be captured by a system 指被某制度記錄或納入。"},{"en":"Cash payments in a small market may not be captured by official sales records.","zh":"小市場中的現金付款可能沒有被官方銷售紀錄計入。"},{"en":"If activity is not captured, the economy can look smaller or less active than it is.","zh":"如果活動沒有被記錄，經濟可能看起來比實際更小或更不活躍。"},{"en":"The phrase means “be counted”, not physically caught.","zh":"這個短語意思是「被計入」，不是被實際捉住。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"statistical system","meaning":"統計制度","examples":[{"en":"The statistical system was designed mainly to measure factory production.","zh":"統計制度主要被設計來衡量工廠生產。"},{"en":"A statistical system is the organised method a government or institution uses to collect and measure data.","zh":"statistical system 指政府或機構用來收集和量度數據的有組織方法。"},{"en":"A school’s statistical system may track attendance, grades, and exam pass rates.","zh":"學校的統計制度可能追蹤出席率、成績和考試合格率。"},{"en":"If a system is designed for factories, it may miss small service businesses.","zh":"如果制度為工廠而設計，它可能漏掉小型服務企業。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to data collection and measurement rules.","zh":"這個短語指數據收集和量度規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be geared to","meaning":"以……為目標；適合於……","examples":[{"en":"The old statistical system was geared to measuring factory production.","zh":"舊統計制度以衡量工廠生產為目標。"},{"en":"To be geared to something means to be designed or arranged mainly for that purpose.","zh":"be geared to something 指主要為某目的而設計或安排。"},{"en":"A beginner course is geared to students who need basic grammar and confidence.","zh":"初學者課程適合需要基本文法和信心的學生。"},{"en":"If a system is geared to one task, it may perform poorly when the economy changes.","zh":"如果制度只以某一任務為目標，當經濟改變時可能表現差。"},{"en":"The phrase describes purpose-built orientation.","zh":"這個短語描述為某目的而設的方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"measuring factory production","meaning":"衡量工廠生產","examples":[{"en":"The system was geared to measuring factory production rather than services.","zh":"這個制度適合衡量工廠生產，而不是服務。"},{"en":"Measuring factory production means counting the output or value of goods made in factories.","zh":"measuring factory production 指計算工廠製造貨品的產量或價值。"},{"en":"A company may measure factory production by counting how many phones are made each week.","zh":"公司可能透過計算每星期製造多少部手機來衡量工廠生產。"},{"en":"Measuring physical goods can be easier than measuring small service transactions.","zh":"衡量實體貨品可能比衡量小型服務交易更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on tracking manufactured output.","zh":"這個短語重點是追蹤製造業產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"small, often private companies","meaning":"小型而通常屬私人經營的公司","examples":[{"en":"Small, often private companies dominate many service businesses.","zh":"小型而通常屬私人經營的公司主導許多服務業。"},{"en":"Small, often private companies are businesses that are usually not large and are owned by private individuals or groups.","zh":"small, often private companies 指規模通常不大，並由私人個人或群體擁有的企業。"},{"en":"Local hair salons, tutoring centres, and delivery firms are often small private companies.","zh":"本地髮型屋、補習中心和送貨公司通常是小型私人公司。"},{"en":"Small private firms can be flexible, but they may be harder for statisticians to track.","zh":"小型私人公司可以靈活，但統計人員可能較難追蹤。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights business size and ownership.","zh":"這個短語突出企業規模和所有權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"dominate these areas","meaning":"主導這些領域","examples":[{"en":"Private companies dominate these areas of the services sector.","zh":"私人公司主導服務業的這些領域。"},{"en":"To dominate these areas means to have the largest influence or presence in those fields.","zh":"dominate these areas 指在這些領域中擁有最大影響力或存在感。"},{"en":"Small restaurants may dominate a neighbourhood food market if most customers eat locally.","zh":"如果大多數顧客在本區用餐，小餐廳可能主導社區食品市場。"},{"en":"When private firms dominate an area, government data may need better methods to measure them.","zh":"當私人公司主導某領域，政府數據可能需要更好方法去量度它們。"},{"en":"The phrase shows strong control or importance within a sector.","zh":"這個短語顯示在某行業中的強大控制或重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be at pains to","meaning":"煞費苦心去……","examples":[{"en":"Some companies have been at pains to escape notice.","zh":"有些公司煞費苦心去逃避注意。"},{"en":"To be at pains to do something means to make a careful or strong effort to do it.","zh":"be at pains to do something 指小心或努力地做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be at pains to explain that a late assignment was caused by illness, not laziness.","zh":"學生可能煞費苦心解釋遲交功課是因病而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"Companies may be at pains to hide income if they want to avoid taxes.","zh":"如果公司想避稅，它們可能煞費苦心隱藏收入。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests deliberate effort, often because something matters a lot.","zh":"這個短語暗示刻意努力，通常因為某事很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"escape notice","meaning":"逃避注意；不被發現","examples":[{"en":"Some small firms tried to escape notice and avoid taxes.","zh":"一些小公司試圖逃避注意並避稅。"},{"en":"To escape notice means to avoid being seen, recorded, or detected.","zh":"escape notice 指避免被看見、記錄或發現。"},{"en":"A spelling mistake may escape notice if the teacher checks the essay too quickly.","zh":"如果老師太快檢查作文，串字錯誤可能逃過注意。"},{"en":"Businesses that escape notice may not appear in official statistics.","zh":"逃避注意的企業可能不出現在官方統計中。"},{"en":"The phrase means remaining unnoticed, not physically running away.","zh":"這個短語指不被注意到，而不是實際逃跑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"and therefore taxes","meaning":"因而逃稅","examples":[{"en":"Some businesses escaped notice and therefore taxes.","zh":"有些企業逃避注意，因而逃稅。"},{"en":"And therefore taxes means that avoiding attention also allowed them to avoid paying taxes.","zh":"and therefore taxes 指避免被注意也讓它們避免繳稅。"},{"en":"A shop that hides cash sales may escape records and therefore taxes.","zh":"隱藏現金銷售的店舖可能逃過紀錄，因而逃稅。"},{"en":"If income is not reported, the government may collect less tax than it should.","zh":"如果收入沒有申報，政府可能收取少於應收的稅。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a cause-and-effect link between invisibility and tax avoidance.","zh":"這個短語顯示不被看見與逃稅之間的因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"commissioner of","meaning":"……的局長；專員","examples":[{"en":"Li Deshui was commissioner of China’s National Bureau of Statistics.","zh":"李德水是中國國家統計局局長。"},{"en":"Commissioner of an organisation means the official person in charge of it or holding a senior public role in it.","zh":"commissioner of an organisation 指負責該機構或在其中擔任高級公共職務的官員。"},{"en":"A commissioner of education may oversee school policy and public examinations.","zh":"教育專員可能監督學校政策和公開考試。"},{"en":"A commissioner’s statement can carry authority because it represents an official body.","zh":"專員的說法可能有權威，因為它代表官方機構。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a senior administrative position.","zh":"這個短語指出高級行政職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"National Bureau of Statistics","meaning":"國家統計局","examples":[{"en":"China’s National Bureau of Statistics revised the GDP figures.","zh":"中國國家統計局修訂了 GDP 數字。"},{"en":"The National Bureau of Statistics is a government agency responsible for collecting and publishing official statistics.","zh":"National Bureau of Statistics 指負責收集和公布官方統計數據的政府機構。"},{"en":"A statistics bureau may count population, wages, prices, and economic output.","zh":"統計局可能計算人口、工資、價格和經濟產出。"},{"en":"Official data from such a bureau can affect policy, investment, and public understanding.","zh":"來自這類機構的官方數據可以影響政策、投資和公眾理解。"},{"en":"The phrase names China’s official statistical authority.","zh":"這個短語命名中國官方統計機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"confirm that","meaning":"確認","examples":[{"en":"Li Deshui confirmed that the newly unearthed GDP came from three categories.","zh":"李德水確認新發現的 GDP 來自三個類別。"},{"en":"To confirm that means to state or prove that something is true.","zh":"confirm that 指聲明或證明某事屬實。"},{"en":"A teacher may confirm that the test will be open-book after students hear rumours.","zh":"學生聽到傳聞後，老師可能確認測驗可以開書。"},{"en":"Confirmation reduces uncertainty because it comes from a reliable source.","zh":"確認可以減少不確定性，因為它來自可靠來源。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces information that has been officially or clearly verified.","zh":"這個短語引入已被官方或清楚核實的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"newly unearthed GDP","meaning":"新發現的本地生產總值","examples":[{"en":"Most of the newly unearthed GDP came from services.","zh":"大部分新發現的本地生產總值來自服務業。"},{"en":"Newly unearthed GDP means economic output that has just been discovered or newly counted in official figures.","zh":"newly unearthed GDP 指剛被發現或新納入官方數字的經濟產出。"},{"en":"A city may find newly unearthed income when informal food stalls are finally included in statistics.","zh":"當非正式食品攤檔終於被納入統計，城市可能發現新被計入的收入。"},{"en":"When hidden activity is unearthed, the measured economy becomes larger.","zh":"當隱藏活動被發現，量度到的經濟規模就會變大。"},{"en":"The phrase uses an archaeological image to describe newly found economic data.","zh":"這個短語用考古意象來描述新發現的經濟數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"come from three categories","meaning":"來自三個類別","examples":[{"en":"The newly measured GDP came from three categories.","zh":"新量度到的 GDP 來自三個類別。"},{"en":"To come from three categories means to originate from three separate groups or types.","zh":"come from three categories 指源自三個分開的群組或類型。"},{"en":"A student’s final grade may come from three categories: homework, exams, and participation.","zh":"學生最終成績可能來自三個類別：功課、考試和課堂參與。"},{"en":"Dividing data into categories helps people see which source matters most.","zh":"把數據分成類別，幫助人看見哪個來源最重要。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the structure behind a total figure.","zh":"這個短語解釋總數背後的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"wholesale, retail and catering","meaning":"批發、零售及餐飲","examples":[{"en":"Wholesale, retail and catering made up one category of newly measured activity.","zh":"批發、零售及餐飲構成新量度活動的一個類別。"},{"en":"Wholesale, retail and catering refer to selling goods in large quantities, selling to individual customers, and providing food services.","zh":"wholesale, retail and catering 指大量銷售貨品、向個別顧客銷售，以及提供餐飲服務。"},{"en":"A supermarket, a clothing shop, and a noodle restaurant belong to this broad service category.","zh":"超級市場、服裝店和麵店都屬於這個廣泛服務類別。"},{"en":"These activities grow when people shop more, eat out more, and businesses trade more goods.","zh":"當人們購物更多、外出用餐更多、企業交易更多貨品，這些活動就會增長。"},{"en":"The phrase groups several everyday commercial services together.","zh":"這個短語把幾種日常商業服務歸為一類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"transport, storage, post and telecommunications","meaning":"運輸、倉儲、郵政及電訊","examples":[{"en":"Transport, storage, post and telecommunications formed another category.","zh":"運輸、倉儲、郵政及電訊形成另一個類別。"},{"en":"Transport, storage, post and telecommunications are services that move goods, keep goods, deliver messages, and connect people through communication networks.","zh":"transport, storage, post and telecommunications 指運送貨物、儲存貨物、傳遞訊息，以及透過通訊網絡連接人們的服務。"},{"en":"Delivery vans, warehouses, postal offices, and phone companies all fit this category.","zh":"送貨車、貨倉、郵局和電話公司都屬於這個類別。"},{"en":"These services expand when trade, online shopping, and communication needs increase.","zh":"當貿易、網購和通訊需要增加，這些服務就會擴張。"},{"en":"The phrase describes infrastructure services that support the wider economy.","zh":"這個短語描述支援更廣泛經濟的基礎服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"postal and telecoms services","meaning":"郵政和電訊服務","examples":[{"en":"Postal and telecoms services are still state-controlled.","zh":"郵政和電訊服務仍由國家控制。"},{"en":"Postal and telecoms services include mail delivery and communication services such as telephone or data networks.","zh":"postal and telecoms services 包括郵件派送和電話或數據網絡等通訊服務。"},{"en":"A business depends on postal and telecoms services to send parcels, call clients, and transfer information.","zh":"企業依賴郵政和電訊服務寄送包裹、聯絡客戶和傳送資訊。"},{"en":"Because these services connect the whole country, governments often regulate them closely.","zh":"因為這些服務連接整個國家，政府通常嚴密規管。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to communication and delivery networks.","zh":"這個短語指通訊和派送網絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"state-controlled","meaning":"由國家控制的","examples":[{"en":"Postal and telecoms services are still state-controlled.","zh":"郵政和電訊服務仍是由國家控制的。"},{"en":"State-controlled means managed, owned, or strongly directed by the government.","zh":"state-controlled 指由政府管理、擁有或強力指導。"},{"en":"A state-controlled railway may set prices according to public policy, not only profit.","zh":"由國家控制的鐵路可能根據公共政策而不只是利潤來定價。"},{"en":"State control can make activities easier to measure because official records are available.","zh":"國家控制可以令活動更容易量度，因為有官方紀錄。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts government control with private business ownership.","zh":"這個短語把政府控制與私人企業所有權作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"readily measured","meaning":"容易量度；容易統計","examples":[{"en":"State-controlled services are readily measured by statisticians.","zh":"由國家控制的服務容易被統計人員量度。"},{"en":"Readily measured means easy to count, record, or calculate.","zh":"readily measured 指容易計算、記錄或估算。"},{"en":"School attendance is readily measured because each student is marked present or absent every day.","zh":"學校出席率容易量度，因為每名學生每天被標記為出席或缺席。"},{"en":"Activities with clear records are easier to include in official statistics.","zh":"有清楚紀錄的活動更容易納入官方統計。"},{"en":"The phrase describes data that can be collected without much difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述不太困難就能收集的數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"trucking and removal companies","meaning":"貨運和搬運公司","examples":[{"en":"Small trucking and removal companies are harder to measure.","zh":"小型貨運和搬運公司較難量度。"},{"en":"Trucking and removal companies are businesses that transport goods or help people move items from one place to another.","zh":"trucking and removal companies 指運送貨物或幫人把物品從一地搬到另一地的企業。"},{"en":"A family may hire a removal company to move furniture to a new flat.","zh":"家庭可能聘請搬運公司把家具搬到新單位。"},{"en":"Small transport firms may be hard to measure if they use cash and keep weak records.","zh":"如果小型運輸公司使用現金並記錄薄弱，它們可能難以量度。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to road transport and moving services.","zh":"這個短語指道路運輸和搬遷服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"real estate","meaning":"房地產","examples":[{"en":"Real estate is one of the fastest-growing service activities.","zh":"房地產是增長最快的服務活動之一。"},{"en":"Real estate refers to land, buildings, property sales, rentals, and related services.","zh":"real estate 指土地、建築物、物業買賣、租賃及相關服務。"},{"en":"A family dealing with real estate may buy a flat, rent an office, or sell a shop.","zh":"涉及房地產的家庭可能買樓、租辦公室或出售店舖。"},{"en":"A real-estate boom can create demand for agents, lawyers, architects, and decorators.","zh":"房地產熱潮可以創造對地產代理、律師、建築師和裝修師傅的需求。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to property business, not only houses.","zh":"這個短語指物業生意，而不只是住宅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"boom particularly in","meaning":"尤其在……蓬勃發展","examples":[{"en":"Real estate is booming particularly in the coastal cities.","zh":"房地產尤其在沿海城市蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"To boom particularly in a place means to grow especially fast or strongly there.","zh":"boom particularly in a place 指在某地增長尤其快速或強勁。"},{"en":"Private tutoring may boom particularly in districts where parents worry about school competition.","zh":"私人補習可能尤其在家長擔心升學競爭的地區蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"A boom in one area can attract investors, workers, and supporting businesses.","zh":"某地熱潮可以吸引投資者、工人和配套企業。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a place where growth is especially noticeable.","zh":"這個短語指出增長特別明顯的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"coastal cities","meaning":"沿海城市","examples":[{"en":"Real estate has boomed in China’s coastal cities.","zh":"中國沿海城市的房地產蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"Coastal cities are cities located near the sea or along the coast.","zh":"coastal cities 指位於海邊或沿海地區的城市。"},{"en":"Coastal cities often grow quickly because ports, trade, tourism, and foreign investment are nearby.","zh":"沿海城市常因港口、貿易、旅遊和外國投資接近而快速增長。"},{"en":"When coastal cities become richer, property prices and service industries may rise.","zh":"當沿海城市變得更富裕，樓價和服務業可能上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes geography that can shape economic development.","zh":"這個短語描述能塑造經濟發展的地理位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"increasingly inland","meaning":"亦逐漸向內陸發展","examples":[{"en":"Real estate is booming in coastal cities and increasingly inland too.","zh":"房地產在沿海城市蓬勃發展，也逐漸向內陸發展。"},{"en":"Increasingly inland means more and more in areas away from the coast.","zh":"increasingly inland 指越來越多地在遠離海岸的內陸地區發生。"},{"en":"Shopping malls first appeared in major cities and then increasingly inland as smaller cities grew richer.","zh":"商場最初出現在大城市，之後隨着較小城市變富裕而逐漸向內陸發展。"},{"en":"When growth spreads inland, development is no longer limited to coastal regions.","zh":"當增長向內陸擴散，發展就不再限於沿海地區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a movement of activity toward interior areas.","zh":"這個短語描述活動向內部地區移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lead to an influx of","meaning":"導致……湧入","examples":[{"en":"The real-estate boom has led to an influx of private money.","zh":"房地產熱潮導致私人資金湧入。"},{"en":"To lead to an influx of something means to cause a large amount of it to enter a place or sector.","zh":"lead to an influx of something 指導致大量某物進入某地或某行業。"},{"en":"A new university can lead to an influx of students, cafés, and rental demand in a neighbourhood.","zh":"新大學可以導致學生、咖啡店和租屋需求湧入社區。"},{"en":"When investors expect high returns, money may flow quickly into that market.","zh":"當投資者預期高回報，資金可能快速流入該市場。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong incoming flow.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈流入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"private money","meaning":"私人資金","examples":[{"en":"Private money has flowed into China’s property market.","zh":"私人資金已流入中國房地產市場。"},{"en":"Private money means funds from individuals or private companies rather than the state.","zh":"private money 指來自個人或私人公司而非國家的資金。"},{"en":"A new school may be built with private money donated by parents and businesses.","zh":"新學校可能由家長和企業捐出的私人資金興建。"},{"en":"When private money enters a market, it can speed up growth and raise competition.","zh":"當私人資金進入市場，它可以加速增長並提高競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts private investment with government funding.","zh":"這個短語把私人投資與政府資金作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not least from","meaning":"尤其來自","examples":[{"en":"Private money came not least from overseas speculators.","zh":"私人資金尤其來自海外投機者。"},{"en":"Not least from means especially from, or importantly from, a particular source.","zh":"not least from 指尤其來自某來源，或某來源特別重要。"},{"en":"The school’s success came not least from parents who volunteered every week.","zh":"學校成功尤其來自每星期做義工的家長。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights one important source among several sources.","zh":"這個短語在多個來源中突出一個重要來源。"},{"en":"It tells readers that the named source should not be underestimated.","zh":"它告訴讀者不應低估所提到的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"overseas speculators","meaning":"海外投機者","examples":[{"en":"Overseas speculators invested in China’s property market.","zh":"海外投機者投資中國房地產市場。"},{"en":"Overseas speculators are foreign investors who buy assets hoping prices will rise quickly.","zh":"overseas speculators 指希望資產價格快速上升而購買資產的外國投資者。"},{"en":"Overseas speculators may buy flats in a city without intending to live there.","zh":"海外投機者可能買入城市中的單位，但沒有打算居住。"},{"en":"Speculation can push prices up if many investors chase the same property.","zh":"如果許多投資者追逐同一類物業，投機可以推高價格。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests investment for profit rather than long-term use.","zh":"這個短語暗示為利潤投資，而不是長期使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"property development","meaning":"房地產發展","examples":[{"en":"Property development has boosted demand for building services.","zh":"房地產發展推高了對建築及裝修服務的需求。"},{"en":"Property development is the process of building, improving, or selling land and buildings.","zh":"property development 指建造、改善或出售土地和建築物的過程。"},{"en":"A company may buy old land and begin property development by constructing apartment blocks.","zh":"公司可能買下舊土地，透過興建住宅大廈開始房地產發展。"},{"en":"Property development creates work for architects, engineers, decorators, and real-estate agents.","zh":"房地產發展為建築師、工程師、裝修師傅和地產代理創造工作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to creating or improving buildings for use or sale.","zh":"這個短語指為使用或出售而創造或改善建築物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in turn","meaning":"反過來；繼而","examples":[{"en":"Property development, in turn, boosted demand for architects.","zh":"房地產發展繼而推高對建築師的需求。"},{"en":"In turn means as the next result in a chain of cause and effect.","zh":"in turn 指作為一連串因果中的下一個結果。"},{"en":"Better transport brings more shoppers, which in turn helps small shops survive.","zh":"更好交通帶來更多購物者，繼而幫助小店生存。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one effect becomes the cause of another effect.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個結果又成為另一個結果的原因。"},{"en":"It helps readers follow a sequence of economic changes.","zh":"它幫助讀者跟隨一連串經濟變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"boost demand for","meaning":"推高對……的需求","examples":[{"en":"Property development boosted demand for architects and decorators.","zh":"房地產發展推高對建築師和裝修師傅的需求。"},{"en":"To boost demand for something means to increase people’s need or desire for it.","zh":"boost demand for something 指增加人們對某物或某服務的需要或需求。"},{"en":"A new housing estate can boost demand for buses, supermarkets, and schools nearby.","zh":"新屋苑可以推高附近對巴士、超市和學校的需求。"},{"en":"When an industry grows, it often boosts demand for related services.","zh":"當一個行業增長，它通常會推高對相關服務的需求。"},{"en":"The phrase connects growth in one area with increased need in another.","zh":"這個短語把某領域增長與另一領域需求增加連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"architects","meaning":"建築師","examples":[{"en":"The building boom created demand for architects.","zh":"建築熱潮創造了對建築師的需求。"},{"en":"Architects are professionals who design buildings and plan how spaces should be used.","zh":"architects 指設計建築物並規劃空間如何使用的專業人士。"},{"en":"A family may hire architects to design a safe and bright new home.","zh":"家庭可能聘請建築師設計安全明亮的新家。"},{"en":"More construction projects usually mean more work for architects.","zh":"更多建築項目通常代表建築師有更多工作。"},{"en":"The word refers to building designers, not construction workers alone.","zh":"這個詞指建築設計專業人士，而不只是建築工人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"decorators","meaning":"裝修師傅；室內裝修人員","examples":[{"en":"Decorators benefited from China’s property boom.","zh":"裝修師傅受惠於中國房地產熱潮。"},{"en":"Decorators are workers or specialists who improve the appearance and finish of indoor spaces.","zh":"decorators 指改善室內空間外觀和裝飾收尾的工人或專家。"},{"en":"A new flat owner may hire decorators to paint walls, install cupboards, and choose flooring.","zh":"新業主可能聘請裝修師傅油牆、安裝櫃子和選地板。"},{"en":"When many people buy homes, demand for decorators often rises.","zh":"當許多人買樓，對裝修師傅的需求通常會上升。"},{"en":"The word refers to interior finishing work, not building the whole structure.","zh":"這個詞指室內裝修收尾工作，而不是建造整棟建築。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"do-it-yourself stores","meaning":"家居裝修用品店","examples":[{"en":"Do-it-yourself stores expanded as property development increased.","zh":"隨着房地產發展增加，家居裝修用品店擴張。"},{"en":"Do-it-yourself stores sell tools, paint, furniture parts, and materials for people to repair or improve homes themselves.","zh":"do-it-yourself stores 售賣工具、油漆、家具部件和材料，讓人自己維修或改善家居。"},{"en":"A homeowner may visit a do-it-yourself store to buy shelves and paint for a bedroom.","zh":"業主可能到家居裝修用品店購買睡房用的層架和油漆。"},{"en":"Home ownership can increase demand for these stores because people want to decorate and repair flats.","zh":"置業可以增加對這類店舖的需求，因為人們想裝飾和維修單位。"},{"en":"The phrase is often shortened to DIY stores.","zh":"這個短語常縮寫為 DIY stores。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"building services","meaning":"建築及裝修服務","examples":[{"en":"Property development increased demand for building services.","zh":"房地產發展增加了對建築及裝修服務的需求。"},{"en":"Building services are professional and practical services connected with construction, repair, design, and decoration.","zh":"building services 指與建造、維修、設計和裝修相關的專業及實務服務。"},{"en":"Architects, plumbers, electricians, and decorators all provide building services.","zh":"建築師、水喉工、電工和裝修師傅都提供建築及裝修服務。"},{"en":"When more homes and offices are built, demand for building services grows.","zh":"當更多住宅和辦公室被興建，對建築服務的需求會增長。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to support work around buildings, not only physical materials.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞建築物的支援工作，而不只是實體材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"there is more to...than...","meaning":"……不只是……","examples":[{"en":"There is more to China’s services boom than restaurants and shops.","zh":"中國服務業繁榮不只是餐廳和商店。"},{"en":"There is more to A than B means A includes more than the simple or obvious part B.","zh":"there is more to A than B 指 A 包含的不只是簡單或明顯的 B 部分。"},{"en":"There is more to English learning than memorising vocabulary.","zh":"學英文不只是背詞彙。"},{"en":"The phrase pushes readers to look beyond the first easy explanation.","zh":"這個短語推動讀者看穿第一個簡單解釋。"},{"en":"It is useful when a topic is broader or deeper than it first appears.","zh":"當主題比表面上更廣或更深時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"services boom","meaning":"服務業繁榮","examples":[{"en":"China’s services boom includes technology, finance and education.","zh":"中國服務業繁榮包括科技、金融和教育。"},{"en":"A services boom is a period when service industries grow quickly and strongly.","zh":"services boom 指服務行業快速而強勁增長的時期。"},{"en":"A city may experience a services boom when tourism, tutoring, healthcare, and finance all expand.","zh":"當旅遊、補習、醫療和金融都擴張，城市可能經歷服務業繁榮。"},{"en":"A services boom can create new jobs outside factories.","zh":"服務業繁榮可以在工廠以外創造新工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rapid growth in service-based economic activity.","zh":"這個短語描述以服務為基礎的經濟活動快速增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"dish up stir-fries","meaning":"端出炒菜；提供中式小炒","examples":[{"en":"China’s services boom is about more than dishing up stir-fries.","zh":"中國服務業繁榮不只是端出炒菜。"},{"en":"To dish up stir-fries means to serve cooked Chinese dishes, especially in a restaurant setting.","zh":"dish up stir-fries 指端出已煮好的中式小炒，尤其在餐廳語境中。"},{"en":"A small café may dish up stir-fries quickly for office workers at lunchtime.","zh":"小茶餐廳可能在午飯時間快速為上班族端出小炒。"},{"en":"The phrase represents simple food service, but the article says services are much broader than that.","zh":"這個短語代表簡單餐飲服務，但文章說服務業比這廣泛得多。"},{"en":"It is a vivid way to refer to restaurant work.","zh":"它是一種生動方式，指餐廳工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ship boxes","meaning":"運送貨箱","examples":[{"en":"The services boom is about more than shipping boxes.","zh":"服務業繁榮不只是運送貨箱。"},{"en":"To ship boxes means to transport packages or goods from one place to another.","zh":"ship boxes 指把包裹或貨物從一地運到另一地。"},{"en":"An online shop may ship boxes to customers every afternoon.","zh":"網店可能每天下午把貨箱運送給顧客。"},{"en":"Delivery services grow when shopping, trade, and e-commerce increase.","zh":"當購物、貿易和電子商務增加，送貨服務會增長。"},{"en":"The phrase represents logistics work, but the services economy includes much more.","zh":"這個短語代表物流工作，但服務型經濟包含更多內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fit out apartments","meaning":"裝修住宅單位","examples":[{"en":"Decorators and shops help fit out apartments.","zh":"裝修師傅和商店幫助裝修住宅單位。"},{"en":"To fit out apartments means to furnish, decorate, and equip flats so people can live in them.","zh":"fit out apartments 指為住宅單位配備家具、裝飾和設備，使人可以居住。"},{"en":"A newly bought flat may need workers to fit out the kitchen, bathroom, and bedrooms.","zh":"新買單位可能需要工人裝修廚房、浴室和睡房。"},{"en":"Property growth creates demand for people who can fit out apartments.","zh":"房地產增長創造對能裝修住宅單位的人員的需求。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to preparing homes for practical use and appearance.","zh":"這個短語指把住宅準備好作實際使用並改善外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"recent years have seen","meaning":"近年出現了","examples":[{"en":"Recent years have seen a surge in media and technology services.","zh":"近年出現了媒體和科技服務的激增。"},{"en":"Recent years have seen means something has happened or become noticeable during the past few years.","zh":"recent years have seen 指某事在過去幾年發生或變得明顯。"},{"en":"Recent years have seen more students using online dictionaries and AI tools.","zh":"近年出現了更多學生使用網上字典和 AI 工具。"},{"en":"The phrase lets writers describe a trend without naming one exact date.","zh":"這個短語讓作者描述趨勢，而不用指出單一確切日期。"},{"en":"It is often used to introduce social or economic change.","zh":"它常用來引入社會或經濟變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a surge in","meaning":"……激增","examples":[{"en":"China has seen a surge in media and technology services.","zh":"中國出現媒體和科技服務激增。"},{"en":"A surge in something is a sudden or strong increase in it.","zh":"a surge in something 指某事突然或強烈增加。"},{"en":"A school may see a surge in library use before public exams.","zh":"公開考試前，學校圖書館使用量可能激增。"},{"en":"A surge often creates pressure for more staff, space, or regulation.","zh":"激增通常會造成對更多人手、空間或規管的壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growth that is noticeable and rapid.","zh":"這個短語描述明顯而快速的增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"media and technology services","meaning":"媒體和科技服務","examples":[{"en":"Media and technology services are growing quickly in China.","zh":"媒體和科技服務在中國快速增長。"},{"en":"Media and technology services include digital platforms, software, online content, advertising, and communication tools.","zh":"media and technology services 包括數碼平台、軟件、網上內容、廣告和通訊工具。"},{"en":"A company that designs apps or produces online videos provides media and technology services.","zh":"設計應用程式或製作網上影片的公司提供媒體和科技服務。"},{"en":"These services grow when people use more phones, internet platforms, and digital entertainment.","zh":"當人們使用更多手機、網絡平台和數碼娛樂，這些服務就會增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes modern service industries linked to information and technology.","zh":"這個短語描述與資訊和科技相關的現代服務業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"financial services","meaning":"金融服務","examples":[{"en":"Financial services such as leasing have expanded in China.","zh":"租賃等金融服務在中國擴張。"},{"en":"Financial services are services related to money, banking, investment, insurance, lending, and leasing.","zh":"financial services 指與金錢、銀行、投資、保險、借貸和租賃相關的服務。"},{"en":"A bank loan, credit card, insurance plan, and investment account are financial services.","zh":"銀行貸款、信用卡、保險計劃和投資戶口都是金融服務。"},{"en":"As companies grow, demand for financial services rises because they need funding and advice.","zh":"隨着公司增長，對金融服務的需求上升，因為它們需要資金和建議。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to money-related services rather than physical goods.","zh":"這個短語指與金錢相關的服務，而不是實體貨品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"leasing","meaning":"租賃服務","examples":[{"en":"Leasing is one example of a growing financial service.","zh":"租賃服務是增長中的金融服務之一。"},{"en":"Leasing means paying to use something for a period without buying it outright.","zh":"leasing 指支付費用在一段時間內使用某物，而不是一次過買下它。"},{"en":"A small business may use leasing to get a delivery van without paying the full price at once.","zh":"小企業可能使用租賃服務取得送貨車，而不用一次過支付全價。"},{"en":"Leasing can help companies expand while keeping upfront costs lower.","zh":"租賃可以幫助公司擴張，同時降低前期成本。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to renting equipment, property, or vehicles under an agreement.","zh":"這個短語指根據協議租用設備、物業或車輛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"education and leisure","meaning":"教育及休閒","examples":[{"en":"Education and leisure are part of China’s growing services sector.","zh":"教育及休閒是中國增長中服務業的一部分。"},{"en":"Education and leisure refer to learning services and free-time activities such as courses, travel, sports, and entertainment.","zh":"education and leisure 指學習服務和課程、旅遊、運動及娛樂等閒暇活動。"},{"en":"A family may spend money on education and leisure through tutoring, swimming lessons, and weekend trips.","zh":"家庭可能透過補習、游泳課和週末旅行在教育及休閒上花錢。"},{"en":"These services often grow when households have more income and more choices.","zh":"當家庭收入較高且選擇更多，這些服務通常會增長。"},{"en":"The phrase combines learning with activities people do for enjoyment.","zh":"這個短語把學習與人們為享受而做的活動結合起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in a small way","meaning":"在小規模上","examples":[{"en":"In a small way, China is starting to rival India in outsourcing.","zh":"在小規模上，中國開始在外判服務方面與印度競爭。"},{"en":"In a small way means to a limited extent, not yet on a large scale.","zh":"in a small way 指在有限程度上，尚未大規模。"},{"en":"In a small way, a class blog can help students practise writing outside lessons.","zh":"在小規模上，班級網誌可以幫助學生在課外練習寫作。"},{"en":"The phrase softens a claim by showing that the change is real but still limited.","zh":"這個短語透過顯示變化真實但仍有限，令說法較溫和。"},{"en":"It means “to some degree” rather than fully or completely.","zh":"它意思是「在某程度上」，而不是完全如此。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"start to rival","meaning":"開始與……競爭","examples":[{"en":"China is starting to rival India as an outsourcing hub.","zh":"中國開始作為外判服務中心與印度競爭。"},{"en":"To start to rival someone means to begin competing with them seriously.","zh":"start to rival someone 指開始與某人或某方認真競爭。"},{"en":"A small tutoring centre may start to rival a famous chain if its results are strong.","zh":"如果成績強，小型補習中心可能開始與著名連鎖機構競爭。"},{"en":"Rivalry begins when another player becomes good enough to challenge the leader.","zh":"當另一名參與者變得足以挑戰領先者，競爭就開始。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests growing competition, not complete equality yet.","zh":"這個短語暗示競爭正在增長，但尚未完全平起平坐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"outsourcing hub","meaning":"外判服務中心","examples":[{"en":"China is becoming an outsourcing hub for certain business tasks.","zh":"中國正在成為某些商業任務的外判服務中心。"},{"en":"An outsourcing hub is a place where companies send work to be done by outside firms or workers.","zh":"outsourcing hub 指公司把工作交給外部企業或工人完成的集中地。"},{"en":"A city with many call-centres and software firms can become an outsourcing hub.","zh":"擁有許多電話中心和軟件公司的城市可以成為外判服務中心。"},{"en":"Outsourcing hubs grow when they offer skilled workers, lower costs, and reliable services.","zh":"當地方提供熟練工人、較低成本和可靠服務，外判中心就會增長。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a centre for contracted business work.","zh":"這個短語指承接外判商業工作的中心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"call-centres","meaning":"客戶服務中心；電話中心","examples":[{"en":"China is less competitive in call-centres that require excellent English.","zh":"在要求出色英語的電話中心方面，中國競爭力較低。"},{"en":"Call-centres are offices where workers answer customer calls, provide support, or sell services by phone.","zh":"call-centres 指員工透過電話回答顧客來電、提供支援或銷售服務的辦公室。"},{"en":"A bank may use a call-centre to help customers reset passwords or report lost cards.","zh":"銀行可能使用電話中心幫助顧客重設密碼或報失信用卡。"},{"en":"Call-centres need clear communication, so language ability can affect competitiveness.","zh":"電話中心需要清楚溝通，所以語言能力可以影響競爭力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to telephone-based customer service operations.","zh":"這個短語指以電話為基礎的客戶服務運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"require excellent English","meaning":"要求出色英語","examples":[{"en":"Some outsourcing tasks require excellent English.","zh":"一些外判任務要求出色英語。"},{"en":"To require excellent English means to need very strong English ability to do the work well.","zh":"require excellent English 指需要很強英語能力才能做好工作。"},{"en":"A customer-service job for international clients may require excellent English.","zh":"面向國際客戶的客戶服務工作可能要求出色英語。"},{"en":"If workers lack the required language level, service quality may fall.","zh":"如果員工缺乏所需語言水平，服務質素可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase links a task with a high language requirement.","zh":"這個短語把任務與高語言要求連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"such tasks as","meaning":"例如……這類工作","examples":[{"en":"China is suitable for such tasks as preparing reports and patent filings.","zh":"中國適合例如準備報告和專利申請文件這類工作。"},{"en":"Such tasks as means tasks like the examples that follow.","zh":"such tasks as 指例如後面所列的工作。"},{"en":"A school assistant may handle such tasks as printing worksheets and arranging rooms.","zh":"學校助理可能處理例如列印工作紙和安排課室這類工作。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces examples without claiming the list is complete.","zh":"這個短語引入例子，但不表示清單完整。"},{"en":"It is useful when naming representative types of work.","zh":"當要列出具代表性的工作類型時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"prepare reports","meaning":"準備報告","examples":[{"en":"Outsourcing firms in China prepare reports for foreign companies.","zh":"中國外判公司為外國公司準備報告。"},{"en":"To prepare reports means to collect information, organise it, and write it in a formal document.","zh":"prepare reports 指收集資訊、整理資料並寫成正式文件。"},{"en":"A student may prepare a report on recycling after interviewing classmates.","zh":"學生訪問同學後，可能準備一份關於回收的報告。"},{"en":"Businesses prepare reports so managers can make decisions from clear information.","zh":"企業準備報告，讓經理可以根據清楚資訊作決策。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to structured writing for practical use.","zh":"這個短語指為實際用途而進行的有結構寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"patent filings","meaning":"專利申請文件","examples":[{"en":"Some outsourcing work involves preparing patent filings.","zh":"一些外判工作涉及準備專利申請文件。"},{"en":"Patent filings are official documents submitted to protect an invention legally.","zh":"patent filings 指為合法保護發明而提交的官方文件。"},{"en":"A technology company may prepare patent filings before launching a new device.","zh":"科技公司在推出新裝置前可能準備專利申請文件。"},{"en":"Good patent filings help prevent competitors from copying an invention without permission.","zh":"良好的專利申請文件幫助防止競爭者未經許可複製發明。"},{"en":"The phrase belongs to legal and technical business services.","zh":"這個短語屬於法律和技術商業服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take a stake in","meaning":"入股……","examples":[{"en":"Microsoft took a stake in a Chinese software firm.","zh":"Microsoft 入股一家中國軟件公司。"},{"en":"To take a stake in a company means to buy or acquire part ownership of it.","zh":"take a stake in a company 指購買或取得該公司部分所有權。"},{"en":"An investor may take a stake in a tutoring company if she believes it will grow.","zh":"如果投資者相信補習公司會增長，她可能入股該公司。"},{"en":"Taking a stake gives the investor a financial interest in the company’s success.","zh":"入股令投資者在公司成功中擁有財務利益。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to investment ownership, not simply supporting an idea.","zh":"這個短語指投資所有權，而不是單純支持某想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"software firm","meaning":"軟件公司","examples":[{"en":"Microsoft invested in a Chinese software firm in Dalian.","zh":"Microsoft 投資了大連一家中國軟件公司。"},{"en":"A software firm is a company that develops, sells, or supports computer programs and digital systems.","zh":"software firm 指開發、銷售或支援電腦程式和數碼系統的公司。"},{"en":"A school may hire a software firm to build an online homework platform.","zh":"學校可能聘請軟件公司建立網上功課平台。"},{"en":"Software firms grow when businesses need apps, databases, websites, and automation tools.","zh":"當企業需要應用程式、資料庫、網站和自動化工具，軟件公司就會增長。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a technology-services company.","zh":"這個短語指科技服務公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"north-east China","meaning":"中國東北部","examples":[{"en":"Dalian is a city in north-east China.","zh":"大連是中國東北部的一個城市。"},{"en":"North-east China is the region in the northeastern part of China.","zh":"north-east China 指中國東北方向的地區。"},{"en":"A geography lesson may locate north-east China by pointing to areas near Korea and Russia.","zh":"地理課可能透過指出接近韓國和俄羅斯的地區來定位中國東北部。"},{"en":"Regional location matters because trade links, language skills, and industries can differ by area.","zh":"地區位置很重要，因為貿易聯繫、語言能力和產業可以因地而異。"},{"en":"The phrase gives geographical position within China.","zh":"這個短語指出在中國內部的地理位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"thriving outsourcing industry","meaning":"蓬勃發展的外判服務業","examples":[{"en":"Dalian has a thriving outsourcing industry.","zh":"大連有蓬勃發展的外判服務業。"},{"en":"A thriving outsourcing industry is a successful and growing sector that handles work for other companies.","zh":"thriving outsourcing industry 指成功且增長中的行業，負責為其他公司處理工作。"},{"en":"A city with skilled programmers and language workers may build a thriving outsourcing industry.","zh":"有熟練程式員和語言人才的城市，可能建立蓬勃發展的外判服務業。"},{"en":"Such an industry can create office jobs and attract foreign clients.","zh":"這類行業可以創造辦公室工作並吸引外國客戶。"},{"en":"The phrase describes outsourcing work that is active, profitable, and expanding.","zh":"這個短語描述活躍、有利潤且正在擴張的外判工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tax returns","meaning":"報稅表","examples":[{"en":"Some firms in Dalian prepare tax returns for overseas companies.","zh":"大連一些公司為海外公司準備報稅表。"},{"en":"Tax returns are official forms that report income, expenses, and taxes owed to the government.","zh":"tax returns 指向政府申報收入、開支和應繳稅款的官方表格。"},{"en":"A small business may ask an accountant to prepare its tax return each year.","zh":"小企業可能每年請會計師準備報稅表。"},{"en":"Accurate tax returns help companies avoid fines and meet legal duties.","zh":"準確報稅表幫助公司避免罰款並履行法律責任。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to tax documents, not the money refunded only.","zh":"這個短語指稅務文件，而不只是退稅款項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"companies from Japan and South Korea","meaning":"來自日本和南韓的公司","examples":[{"en":"Dalian provides services for companies from Japan and South Korea.","zh":"大連為來自日本和南韓的公司提供服務。"},{"en":"Companies from Japan and South Korea are businesses based in those two countries.","zh":"companies from Japan and South Korea 指總部或來源在這兩個國家的企業。"},{"en":"A Chinese outsourcing firm may serve companies from Japan and South Korea if its staff know Japanese or Korean.","zh":"如果中國外判公司員工懂日語或韓語，它可能服務來自日本和南韓的公司。"},{"en":"Nearby geography and language skills can make cross-border service work easier.","zh":"接近的地理位置和語言能力可以令跨境服務工作更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies foreign business clients by country.","zh":"這個短語按國家指出外國商業客戶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rapid economic growth","meaning":"快速經濟增長","examples":[{"en":"China’s rapid economic growth is fuelling demand for professional services.","zh":"中國快速經濟增長正在推動對專業服務的需求。"},{"en":"Rapid economic growth means the economy is expanding quickly in output, income, jobs, or business activity.","zh":"rapid economic growth 指經濟在產出、收入、職位或商業活動方面快速擴張。"},{"en":"A city with rapid economic growth may build more offices, roads, and private schools.","zh":"有快速經濟增長的城市可能興建更多辦公室、道路和私立學校。"},{"en":"Fast growth creates more complex business needs, so professional services become more important.","zh":"快速增長創造更複雜商業需要，因此專業服務變得更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong economic expansion over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間出現的強勁經濟擴張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fuel demand for","meaning":"推動對……的需求","examples":[{"en":"Economic growth is fuelling demand for accountants and lawyers.","zh":"經濟增長正在推動對會計師和律師的需求。"},{"en":"To fuel demand for something means to make the need for it grow stronger.","zh":"fuel demand for something 指使對某物或某服務的需要變得更強。"},{"en":"More university applications can fuel demand for private tutors and admissions consultants.","zh":"更多大學申請可以推動對私人補習老師和升學顧問的需求。"},{"en":"When businesses expand, they often need more legal, financial, and marketing advice.","zh":"當企業擴張，它們通常需要更多法律、財務和市場建議。"},{"en":"The phrase uses “fuel” as a metaphor for making growth continue.","zh":"這個短語用 fuel 作比喻，表示令增長繼續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"accountants","meaning":"會計師","examples":[{"en":"China’s expanding economy needs more accountants.","zh":"中國擴張中的經濟需要更多會計師。"},{"en":"Accountants are professionals who record, check, and analyse financial information.","zh":"accountants 指記錄、檢查和分析財務資訊的專業人士。"},{"en":"A small business may hire accountants to prepare tax returns and manage budgets.","zh":"小企業可能聘請會計師準備報稅表和管理預算。"},{"en":"As companies grow, accountants help keep financial records accurate and legal.","zh":"隨着公司增長，會計師幫助保持財務紀錄準確和合法。"},{"en":"The word refers to finance and record-keeping specialists.","zh":"這個詞指財務和記錄保存專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lawyers","meaning":"律師","examples":[{"en":"Chinese companies need lawyers as they expand and restructure.","zh":"中國公司在擴張和重組時需要律師。"},{"en":"Lawyers are legal professionals who advise clients, prepare documents, and represent them in legal matters.","zh":"lawyers 指為客戶提供法律建議、準備文件並代表他們處理法律事務的專業人士。"},{"en":"A company may ask lawyers to review contracts before signing a partnership agreement.","zh":"公司在簽署合作協議前，可能請律師審閱合約。"},{"en":"Economic growth increases legal needs because businesses make more deals and face more rules.","zh":"經濟增長增加法律需要，因為企業進行更多交易並面對更多規則。"},{"en":"The word refers to specialists in law.","zh":"這個詞指法律專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"bankers","meaning":"銀行家","examples":[{"en":"Bankers are in demand as Chinese companies grow.","zh":"隨着中國公司增長，銀行家需求增加。"},{"en":"Bankers are professionals who work in banking, finance, lending, investment, or financial advice.","zh":"bankers 指在銀行、金融、借貸、投資或財務建議方面工作的專業人士。"},{"en":"A company may speak to bankers when it needs a loan to open new shops.","zh":"公司需要貸款開新店時，可能與銀行家商討。"},{"en":"Business expansion creates demand for bankers because firms need capital and financial planning.","zh":"商業擴張創造對銀行家的需求，因為企業需要資本和財務規劃。"},{"en":"The word refers to finance professionals connected with banks or financial markets.","zh":"這個詞指與銀行或金融市場相關的金融專業人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"all manner of consultants","meaning":"各式各樣的顧問","examples":[{"en":"China’s economy needs accountants, lawyers, bankers and all manner of consultants.","zh":"中國經濟需要會計師、律師、銀行家和各式各樣的顧問。"},{"en":"All manner of consultants means many different kinds of professional advisers.","zh":"all manner of consultants 指許多不同類型的專業顧問。"},{"en":"A growing school may hire consultants for curriculum design, marketing, finance, and technology.","zh":"發展中的學校可能聘請課程設計、市場推廣、財務和科技顧問。"},{"en":"As problems become more complex, businesses turn to consultants for specialised advice.","zh":"當問題變得更複雜，企業會求助顧問取得專門建議。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses variety and breadth.","zh":"這個短語強調種類多和範圍廣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"expand and restructure","meaning":"擴張和重組","examples":[{"en":"Chinese companies need advice as they expand and restructure.","zh":"中國公司在擴張和重組時需要建議。"},{"en":"To expand and restructure means to grow larger and reorganise how a company operates.","zh":"expand and restructure 指變得更大並重新組織公司運作方式。"},{"en":"A tutoring centre may expand and restructure by opening branches and changing staff roles.","zh":"補習中心可能透過開分校和改變員工職責來擴張和重組。"},{"en":"Expansion creates new opportunities, while restructuring helps the organisation manage growth.","zh":"擴張創造新機會，而重組幫助機構管理增長。"},{"en":"The phrase combines growth with internal reorganisation.","zh":"這個短語結合增長與內部重新組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"specialists in","meaning":"……方面的專家","examples":[{"en":"Specialists in marketing and advertising advise Chinese companies.","zh":"市場推廣和廣告方面的專家為中國公司提供建議。"},{"en":"Specialists in a field are people with deep knowledge or skill in that area.","zh":"specialists in a field 指在某領域有深入知識或技能的人。"},{"en":"A school may hire specialists in special education to support students with learning difficulties.","zh":"學校可能聘請特殊教育方面的專家，支援有學習困難的學生。"},{"en":"Specialists are useful when general knowledge is not enough to solve a problem.","zh":"當一般知識不足以解決問題，專家就很有用。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies experts by their area of expertise.","zh":"這個短語按專業領域指出專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"marketing, advertising and public relations","meaning":"市場推廣、廣告及公關","examples":[{"en":"Marketing, advertising and public relations are relatively new areas in China.","zh":"市場推廣、廣告及公關在中國是相對較新的領域。"},{"en":"Marketing, advertising and public relations are services that help organisations sell products, shape image, and communicate with the public.","zh":"marketing, advertising and public relations 指幫助機構銷售產品、塑造形象和與公眾溝通的服務。"},{"en":"A company may use marketing to understand customers, advertising to promote products, and public relations to manage reputation.","zh":"公司可能使用市場推廣了解顧客，用廣告推廣產品，用公關管理聲譽。"},{"en":"These services grow when companies compete for attention and brand trust.","zh":"當公司爭奪注意力和品牌信任，這些服務就會增長。"},{"en":"The phrase groups communication-based business services together.","zh":"這個短語把以溝通為基礎的商業服務歸在一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"advise on","meaning":"就……提供意見","examples":[{"en":"Consultants advise on marketing products and developing brands.","zh":"顧問就推銷產品和建立品牌提供意見。"},{"en":"To advise on something means to give professional suggestions about that subject.","zh":"advise on something 指就某主題提供專業建議。"},{"en":"A careers teacher may advise on university choices and interview preparation.","zh":"升學就業老師可能就大學選擇和面試準備提供意見。"},{"en":"Advice helps people avoid costly mistakes and make clearer decisions.","zh":"建議幫助人避免昂貴錯誤並作出更清楚決定。"},{"en":"The phrase usually introduces the topic of the advice.","zh":"這個短語通常引入建議的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"relatively new area","meaning":"相對較新的領域","examples":[{"en":"Brand development is a relatively new area for many Chinese companies.","zh":"品牌發展對許多中國公司而言是相對較新的領域。"},{"en":"A relatively new area is a field that has developed recently compared with older activities.","zh":"relatively new area 指與較舊活動相比，近年才發展起來的領域。"},{"en":"Online teaching was a relatively new area for many schools before they gained experience.","zh":"在學校累積經驗前，網上教學對許多學校而言是相對較新的領域。"},{"en":"New areas often need training, experimentation, and outside advice.","zh":"新領域通常需要培訓、實驗和外部建議。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a field that is not yet deeply established.","zh":"這個短語描述尚未深深建立的領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"market products","meaning":"推銷產品","examples":[{"en":"Companies need specialists to help them market products.","zh":"公司需要專家幫助它們推銷產品。"},{"en":"To market products means to promote and sell them to customers.","zh":"market products 指向顧客推廣和銷售產品。"},{"en":"A bakery may market products by offering samples and posting photos online.","zh":"麵包店可能透過提供試食和在網上發布照片來推銷產品。"},{"en":"Good marketing helps customers understand why a product is useful or desirable.","zh":"良好市場推廣幫助顧客理解產品為何有用或值得想要。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on selling through communication and strategy.","zh":"這個短語重點是透過溝通和策略銷售。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"develop brands","meaning":"建立品牌","examples":[{"en":"Companies hire consultants to help them develop brands.","zh":"公司聘請顧問幫助它們建立品牌。"},{"en":"To develop brands means to build a clear identity, reputation, and customer image for products or companies.","zh":"develop brands 指為產品或公司建立清楚身份、聲譽和顧客印象。"},{"en":"A small café may develop its brand through a clear logo, friendly service, and a consistent menu.","zh":"小咖啡店可能透過清晰標誌、友善服務和一致餐牌建立品牌。"},{"en":"Strong brands help customers remember and trust a company.","zh":"強大品牌幫助顧客記住並信任公司。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to building recognition and meaning around a business.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞企業建立辨識度和意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the new wealth","meaning":"新出現的財富","examples":[{"en":"The new wealth has created demand for luxury and personal services.","zh":"新出現的財富創造了對奢侈和個人服務的需求。"},{"en":"The new wealth means recently created money and purchasing power among people or households.","zh":"the new wealth 指人們或家庭中新近形成的金錢和購買力。"},{"en":"The new wealth in a city may lead to more private clubs, luxury shops, and international schools.","zh":"城市中新出現的財富可能帶來更多私人會所、奢侈品店和國際學校。"},{"en":"New wealth changes consumption because people can pay for comfort, status, and convenience.","zh":"新財富會改變消費，因為人們可以為舒適、地位和便利付款。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fresh prosperity, not inherited wealth only.","zh":"這個短語描述新近繁榮，而不只是繼承財富。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have consequences","meaning":"有後果；帶來影響","examples":[{"en":"The new wealth has other consequences too.","zh":"新出現的財富也有其他後果。"},{"en":"To have consequences means to produce results or effects after something happens.","zh":"have consequences 指某事發生後產生結果或影響。"},{"en":"A school’s decision to shorten lunch time may have consequences for student health and mood.","zh":"學校縮短午膳時間的決定，可能對學生健康和心情帶來影響。"},{"en":"Wealth can have consequences beyond spending, including changes in lifestyle and social demand.","zh":"財富可以帶來消費以外的後果，包括生活方式和社會需求變化。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds readers to look at effects, not only causes.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者看影響，而不只是原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"security guards","meaning":"保安員","examples":[{"en":"China now has nearly a million security guards.","zh":"中國現在有近一百萬名保安員。"},{"en":"Security guards are workers who protect buildings, people, property, or events.","zh":"security guards 指保護建築物、人員、財產或活動的工作人員。"},{"en":"A shopping mall may hire security guards to watch entrances and help during emergencies.","zh":"商場可能聘請保安員看守入口並在緊急情況協助。"},{"en":"More wealth and private property can increase demand for security guards.","zh":"更多財富和私人財產可以增加對保安員的需求。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to protective service workers.","zh":"這個短語指保護性服務工作者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"offer someone everything from...to...","meaning":"為某人提供從……到……的各種東西","examples":[{"en":"China can offer its new rich everything from cosmetic surgeons to pet salons.","zh":"中國可以為新富階層提供從整容外科醫生到寵物美容店的各種服務。"},{"en":"To offer someone everything from A to B means to provide a wide range of services or products.","zh":"offer someone everything from A to B 指為某人提供範圍廣泛的服務或產品。"},{"en":"A large shopping mall may offer families everything from supermarkets to children’s playrooms.","zh":"大型商場可能為家庭提供從超級市場到兒童遊樂室的各種東西。"},{"en":"The phrase shows variety by naming two examples from a broad range.","zh":"這個短語透過列出兩個例子來顯示廣泛種類。"},{"en":"It suggests that consumers have many choices.","zh":"它暗示消費者有許多選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the new rich","meaning":"新富階層","examples":[{"en":"The new rich can buy many luxury services.","zh":"新富階層可以購買許多奢侈服務。"},{"en":"The new rich are people who have recently become wealthy.","zh":"the new rich 指最近變得富有的人。"},{"en":"The new rich may spend on private schools, designer brands, travel, and personal services.","zh":"新富階層可能在私立學校、名牌、旅遊和個人服務上花錢。"},{"en":"When the new rich appear, markets for luxury goods and services often expand.","zh":"當新富階層出現，奢侈品和服務市場通常會擴張。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a newly wealthy social group.","zh":"這個短語描述新近富裕的社會群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cosmetic surgeons","meaning":"整容外科醫生","examples":[{"en":"Cosmetic surgeons serve China’s new rich.","zh":"整容外科醫生服務中國新富階層。"},{"en":"Cosmetic surgeons are doctors who perform operations to change or improve appearance.","zh":"cosmetic surgeons 指進行手術以改變或改善外貌的醫生。"},{"en":"A person may consult a cosmetic surgeon before deciding on eyelid or nose surgery.","zh":"一個人在決定做雙眼皮或鼻部手術前，可能諮詢整容外科醫生。"},{"en":"Demand for cosmetic surgeons can rise when people have more money for personal appearance.","zh":"當人們有更多錢用於個人外貌，對整容外科醫生的需求可能上升。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to medical specialists in appearance-related surgery.","zh":"這個短語指外貌相關手術的醫學專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pet salons","meaning":"寵物美容店","examples":[{"en":"Pet salons are one example of new lifestyle services.","zh":"寵物美容店是新生活方式服務的一個例子。"},{"en":"Pet salons are shops that wash, groom, trim, or style pets.","zh":"pet salons 指為寵物洗澡、梳理、修剪或造型的店舖。"},{"en":"A dog owner may visit a pet salon before a family photo day.","zh":"狗主人可能在家庭拍照日前到寵物美容店。"},{"en":"As households spend more on pets, demand for pet salons can grow.","zh":"隨着家庭在寵物上花更多錢，對寵物美容店的需求可以增長。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how services can expand into personal and leisure lifestyles.","zh":"這個短語顯示服務業可以擴展至個人和休閒生活方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"meanwhile","meaning":"與此同時","examples":[{"en":"Meanwhile, a huge new market is opening up for private education.","zh":"與此同時，一個巨大的私營教育新市場正在打開。"},{"en":"Meanwhile introduces another development happening at the same time.","zh":"meanwhile 用來引入同時發生的另一項發展。"},{"en":"The school improved its library; meanwhile, teachers also updated the writing curriculum.","zh":"學校改善圖書館；與此同時，老師也更新寫作課程。"},{"en":"The phrase helps writers move to a parallel point without losing the time connection.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者轉到平行重點，同時保留時間聯繫。"},{"en":"It means “at the same time” or “in another related area”.","zh":"它意思是「同時」或「在另一個相關領域」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a huge new market","meaning":"巨大的新市場","examples":[{"en":"A huge new market is opening up for private education.","zh":"一個巨大的新市場正在為私營教育打開。"},{"en":"A huge new market is a large and newly developing area of business demand.","zh":"huge new market 指大型而新近發展的商業需求領域。"},{"en":"Online tutoring became a huge new market when many students began studying from home.","zh":"當許多學生開始在家學習，網上補習成為巨大的新市場。"},{"en":"A new market opens when people suddenly need or want products that were less common before.","zh":"當人們突然需要或想要以前較少見的產品，新市場就會打開。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large business opportunity.","zh":"這個短語描述大型商業機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"open up for","meaning":"為……開拓；為……打開","examples":[{"en":"A new market is opening up for private education.","zh":"一個新市場正在為私營教育打開。"},{"en":"To open up for something means to become available or begin developing for that activity or sector.","zh":"open up for something 指為某活動或行業變得可用或開始發展。"},{"en":"New opportunities may open up for students who learn strong English and digital skills.","zh":"學會強英語和數碼技能的學生，可能有新機會打開。"},{"en":"When demand rises, space opens up for new companies to enter.","zh":"當需求上升，新公司就有進入市場的空間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a new possibility becoming available.","zh":"這個短語描述新可能性變得可用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"private education","meaning":"私營教育","examples":[{"en":"Private education is expanding rapidly in China.","zh":"私營教育在中國快速擴張。"},{"en":"Private education is education provided by private schools, tutors, training centres, or companies rather than the public system.","zh":"private education 指由私立學校、導師、培訓中心或公司，而非公營制度提供的教育。"},{"en":"Parents may pay for private education if they want smaller classes or extra exam support.","zh":"如果家長想要小班教學或額外考試支援，可能會為私營教育付款。"},{"en":"A weak public system can increase demand for private education.","zh":"質素欠佳的公營制度可以增加對私營教育的需求。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts paid private learning services with state-provided education.","zh":"這個短語把收費私人學習服務與國家提供的教育作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be fuelled by","meaning":"由……推動","examples":[{"en":"The private education market is fuelled by several factors.","zh":"私營教育市場由幾個因素推動。"},{"en":"To be fuelled by something means to be driven or made stronger by it.","zh":"be fuelled by something 指由某事推動或使其變得更強。"},{"en":"Demand for online classes may be fuelled by busy parents and long travel times.","zh":"對網課的需求可能由忙碌家長和長通勤時間推動。"},{"en":"A market grows faster when several forces fuel it at the same time.","zh":"當幾股力量同時推動市場，市場會增長得更快。"},{"en":"The phrase uses fuel as a metaphor for causes that power growth.","zh":"這個短語用燃料作比喻，表示推動增長的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the combination of","meaning":"……的結合","examples":[{"en":"The market is fuelled by the combination of public weakness and parental concern.","zh":"這個市場由公營制度薄弱和家長關注的結合所推動。"},{"en":"The combination of two things means those things working together.","zh":"combination of two things 指兩件事共同作用。"},{"en":"The combination of regular practice and clear feedback helps students improve faster.","zh":"定期練習和清楚回饋的結合，幫助學生更快進步。"},{"en":"When two causes combine, their effect can be stronger than either one alone.","zh":"當兩個原因結合，其影響可以比任何一個單獨因素更強。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights multiple factors acting together.","zh":"這個短語突出多個因素共同作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"poor public system","meaning":"質素欠佳的公營制度","examples":[{"en":"A poor public system helps fuel demand for private education.","zh":"質素欠佳的公營制度幫助推動對私營教育的需求。"},{"en":"A poor public system is a state-run service that is weak, underfunded, inefficient, or low in quality.","zh":"poor public system 指薄弱、資金不足、低效率或質素低的國家營辦服務。"},{"en":"If public schools are overcrowded, parents may turn to private tutoring.","zh":"如果公立學校過度擁擠，家長可能轉向私人補習。"},{"en":"Weak public services can create opportunities for private companies.","zh":"薄弱公營服務可以為私人公司創造機會。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises the quality of government-provided services.","zh":"這個短語批評政府提供服務的質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"preoccupation with","meaning":"對……的高度關注；念念不忘","examples":[{"en":"Middle-class parents have a preoccupation with giving their child the best chances.","zh":"中產父母高度關注給孩子最好的機會。"},{"en":"Preoccupation with something means strong and repeated concern about it.","zh":"preoccupation with something 指對某事強烈而反覆的關注。"},{"en":"A student’s preoccupation with grades may make her check exam rankings every day.","zh":"學生若對成績念念不忘，可能每天查看考試排名。"},{"en":"Strong parental concern can drive spending on tutors, books, and extra classes.","zh":"強烈家長關注可以推動在導師、書本和額外課程上的開支。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a worry or focus that occupies the mind.","zh":"這個短語暗示佔據心思的擔憂或焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"middle-class parents","meaning":"中產父母","examples":[{"en":"Middle-class parents spend heavily on education.","zh":"中產父母在教育上花費很大。"},{"en":"Middle-class parents are parents from households with moderate to relatively comfortable income and social status.","zh":"middle-class parents 指來自中等至相對舒適收入和社會地位家庭的父母。"},{"en":"Middle-class parents may pay for music lessons, tutoring, and overseas summer camps.","zh":"中產父母可能支付音樂課、補習和海外暑期營費用。"},{"en":"Their spending can expand private education markets because they have both concern and some ability to pay.","zh":"他們的開支可以擴大私營教育市場，因為他們既關心，也有一定支付能力。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a social group by family income and lifestyle.","zh":"這個短語按家庭收入和生活方式指出一個社會群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"give someone the best chances","meaning":"給某人最好的機會","examples":[{"en":"Parents want to give their only child the best chances.","zh":"父母想給獨生子女最好的機會。"},{"en":"To give someone the best chances means to provide the strongest opportunities for future success.","zh":"give someone the best chances 指為某人提供未來成功的最佳機會。"},{"en":"Parents may give a child the best chances by supporting reading, health, and confidence.","zh":"父母可以透過支持閱讀、健康和自信來給孩子最好的機會。"},{"en":"This desire can lead families to spend more on education and training.","zh":"這種願望可以導致家庭在教育和培訓上花更多錢。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on improving future opportunities.","zh":"這個短語重點是改善未來機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"demand from business","meaning":"來自商界的需求","examples":[{"en":"Demand from business also fuels the education market.","zh":"來自商界的需求也推動教育市場。"},{"en":"Demand from business means the need created by companies or employers.","zh":"demand from business 指由公司或僱主創造的需求。"},{"en":"Demand from business may increase English courses if companies need staff who can speak to foreign clients.","zh":"如果公司需要能與外國客戶溝通的員工，來自商界的需求可能增加英文課程。"},{"en":"When employers need new skills, training companies can grow quickly.","zh":"當僱主需要新技能，培訓公司可以快速增長。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies companies as a source of market demand.","zh":"這個短語指出公司是市場需求來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"spend more on...than on...","meaning":"在……上的花費比……更多","examples":[{"en":"Chinese families spend more on education than on anything except housing.","zh":"中國家庭在教育上的花費比除住房外任何東西都更多。"},{"en":"To spend more on A than on B means to use a larger amount of money for A than for B.","zh":"spend more on A than on B 指在 A 上使用的金錢比 B 更多。"},{"en":"Some families spend more on tutoring than on holidays during exam years.","zh":"有些家庭在考試年花在補習上的錢比假期更多。"},{"en":"Spending patterns show what households consider most important or urgent.","zh":"消費模式顯示家庭認為甚麼最重要或最迫切。"},{"en":"The phrase compares two categories of expenditure.","zh":"這個短語比較兩類開支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"except housing","meaning":"除住房外","examples":[{"en":"Education is the largest expense for many families except housing.","zh":"對許多家庭而言，除住房外，教育是最大開支。"},{"en":"Except housing means not including housing costs, which are treated as a separate larger category.","zh":"except housing 指不包括住房成本，因為它被視為另一個更大的獨立類別。"},{"en":"A family may spend most on rent, but except housing, education may be the biggest cost.","zh":"家庭可能租金開支最大，但除住房外，教育可能是最大成本。"},{"en":"The phrase helps compare spending while removing one unusually large item.","zh":"這個短語在排除一個特別大的項目後幫助比較開支。"},{"en":"It means housing is the only category above the one being discussed.","zh":"它意思是住房是唯一高於所討論項目的類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"courses, books and materials","meaning":"課程、書籍和教材","examples":[{"en":"The market for courses, books and materials has grown rapidly.","zh":"課程、書籍和教材市場快速增長。"},{"en":"Courses, books and materials are learning products and resources used for education or training.","zh":"courses, books and materials 指用於教育或培訓的學習產品和資源。"},{"en":"An English learner may buy courses, books and materials to prepare for an exam.","zh":"英文學習者可能購買課程、書籍和教材來準備考試。"},{"en":"When education demand rises, spending on these resources often rises too.","zh":"當教育需求上升，這些資源上的開支通常也會上升。"},{"en":"The phrase groups paid learning services and study resources together.","zh":"這個短語把收費學習服務和學習資源歸在一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"more than double","meaning":"增長超過一倍","examples":[{"en":"The education market more than doubled from 2002 levels.","zh":"教育市場較2002年水平增長超過一倍。"},{"en":"To more than double means to increase to more than twice the original size.","zh":"more than double 指增加至超過原本規模的兩倍。"},{"en":"If a class grows from 10 students to 23 students, it has more than doubled.","zh":"如果一班由10名學生增至23名學生，就是增長超過一倍。"},{"en":"Such growth shows very strong expansion, not a small increase.","zh":"這種增長顯示非常強勁擴張，而不是小幅增加。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to describe rapid numerical growth.","zh":"這個短語用來描述快速數字增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"from 2002 levels","meaning":"較2002年的水平","examples":[{"en":"The market more than doubled from 2002 levels.","zh":"該市場較2002年的水平增長超過一倍。"},{"en":"From 2002 levels means compared with the amount or size recorded in 2002.","zh":"from 2002 levels 指與2002年記錄的數量或規模相比。"},{"en":"School enrolment may have risen sharply from 2010 levels if more families moved nearby.","zh":"如果更多家庭搬到附近，學校收生可能較2010年水平大幅上升。"},{"en":"A base-year level helps readers understand how much change has occurred.","zh":"基準年份水平幫助讀者理解變化有多大。"},{"en":"The phrase sets the starting point for comparison.","zh":"這個短語設定比較起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"richer households","meaning":"較富裕的家庭","examples":[{"en":"Richer households have caused a tourism boom.","zh":"較富裕的家庭造成了旅遊業熱潮。"},{"en":"Richer households are families with more money to spend than before or than average families.","zh":"richer households 指比以前或比一般家庭有更多錢可花的家庭。"},{"en":"Richer households may buy better healthcare, private education, and overseas holidays.","zh":"較富裕的家庭可能購買更好醫療、私營教育和海外假期。"},{"en":"When households become richer, spending often shifts toward leisure and travel.","zh":"當家庭變得更富裕，開支通常轉向休閒和旅遊。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to families with higher purchasing power.","zh":"這個短語指購買力較高的家庭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tourism boom","meaning":"旅遊業熱潮","examples":[{"en":"China has experienced a tourism boom.","zh":"中國經歷了旅遊業熱潮。"},{"en":"A tourism boom is a rapid increase in travel, tourist spending, hotels, tours, and related services.","zh":"tourism boom 指旅遊、旅客消費、酒店、旅行團和相關服務快速增加。"},{"en":"A small town may have a tourism boom after a famous film is shot there.","zh":"著名電影在小鎮拍攝後，該地可能出現旅遊業熱潮。"},{"en":"A boom can create jobs but also put pressure on transport and local communities.","zh":"熱潮可以創造工作，但也會對交通和本地社區造成壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong growth in travel activity.","zh":"這個短語描述旅遊活動強勁增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"chiefly domestic","meaning":"主要屬本地；主要是國內","examples":[{"en":"The tourism boom is still chiefly domestic.","zh":"旅遊業熱潮仍主要屬國內。"},{"en":"Chiefly domestic means mainly within the country, rather than involving foreign travel.","zh":"chiefly domestic 指主要在國內，而不是涉及外國旅遊。"},{"en":"A country’s tourism market may be chiefly domestic if most visitors come from its own cities.","zh":"如果大多數旅客來自本國城市，一個國家的旅遊市場可能主要屬國內。"},{"en":"Domestic tourism can grow strongly before international tourism becomes large.","zh":"國內旅遊可以在國際旅遊變大之前強勁增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the main source or direction of tourism.","zh":"這個短語描述旅遊的主要來源或方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"mainlanders","meaning":"內地居民","examples":[{"en":"More mainlanders are venturing overseas.","zh":"更多內地居民正在前往海外。"},{"en":"Mainlanders means people from mainland China, especially when contrasted with Hong Kong, Macau, Taiwan, or overseas communities.","zh":"mainlanders 指來自中國內地的人，尤其是與香港、澳門、台灣或海外社群作對比時。"},{"en":"A travel agency may design tours for mainlanders visiting Europe for the first time.","zh":"旅行社可能為首次到歐洲旅遊的內地居民設計旅行團。"},{"en":"As incomes rise and visa rules loosen, more mainlanders may travel abroad.","zh":"隨着收入上升和簽證規則放寬，更多內地居民可能出國旅遊。"},{"en":"The word identifies people by origin within the Chinese context.","zh":"這個詞在中國語境中按來源識別人群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"venture overseas","meaning":"前往海外；涉足海外","examples":[{"en":"More Chinese tourists are venturing overseas.","zh":"更多中國旅客正在前往海外。"},{"en":"To venture overseas means to travel abroad, often with a sense of trying something new or less familiar.","zh":"venture overseas 指到外國去，通常帶有嘗試新事物或較陌生事物的感覺。"},{"en":"A student may venture overseas for university after years of studying locally.","zh":"學生在本地讀書多年後，可能前往海外升讀大學。"},{"en":"People may venture overseas when they have more income, confidence, and easier travel permission.","zh":"當人們有更多收入、信心和較容易的旅遊許可，他們可能前往海外。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests going beyond one’s usual home market or country.","zh":"這個短語暗示走出平常的本地市場或國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"visa restrictions","meaning":"簽證限制","examples":[{"en":"Visa restrictions are being lifted for Chinese travellers.","zh":"中國旅客的簽證限制正在被放寬。"},{"en":"Visa restrictions are rules that limit who can enter a country and under what conditions.","zh":"visa restrictions 指限制誰可以入境某國以及在甚麼條件下入境的規則。"},{"en":"Tourists may cancel a trip if visa restrictions make entry too difficult.","zh":"如果簽證限制令入境太困難，旅客可能取消旅程。"},{"en":"When restrictions are eased, more people can travel abroad.","zh":"當限制放寬，更多人可以出國旅遊。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to immigration and travel-entry rules.","zh":"這個短語指入境和旅遊簽證規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be lifted","meaning":"被取消；被放寬","examples":[{"en":"Visa restrictions are lifted as more Chinese people travel abroad.","zh":"隨着更多中國人出國旅遊，簽證限制被放寬。"},{"en":"To be lifted means to be removed, relaxed, or ended officially.","zh":"be lifted 指被正式取消、放寬或終止。"},{"en":"A school ban on playground use may be lifted after repairs are finished.","zh":"操場維修完成後，學校對使用操場的禁令可能被取消。"},{"en":"When restrictions are lifted, people have more freedom to act.","zh":"當限制被取消，人們有更多行動自由。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the removal of a rule or limit.","zh":"這個短語描述規則或限制被移除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"annual tourism market","meaning":"每年旅遊市場","examples":[{"en":"China’s annual tourism market is expected to grow rapidly.","zh":"中國每年旅遊市場預計會快速增長。"},{"en":"Annual tourism market means the total value of travel-related spending in one year.","zh":"annual tourism market 指一年內旅遊相關消費的總價值。"},{"en":"A city’s annual tourism market includes hotels, restaurants, tours, transport, and souvenirs.","zh":"城市每年旅遊市場包括酒店、餐廳、旅行團、交通和紀念品。"},{"en":"If more people travel and spend more per trip, the annual tourism market grows.","zh":"如果更多人旅遊且每次旅行花更多錢，每年旅遊市場就會增長。"},{"en":"The phrase measures yearly tourism activity in economic terms.","zh":"這個短語以經濟角度量度年度旅遊活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"more than triple","meaning":"增長超過三倍","examples":[{"en":"The tourism market may more than triple within a decade.","zh":"旅遊市場可能在十年內增長超過三倍。"},{"en":"To more than triple means to increase to more than three times the original size.","zh":"more than triple 指增加至超過原本規模的三倍。"},{"en":"If a club grows from 20 members to 70 members, it has more than tripled.","zh":"如果學會由20名成員增至70名成員，就是增長超過三倍。"},{"en":"More than tripling shows very rapid and substantial growth.","zh":"增長超過三倍顯示非常快速且大幅的增長。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when a number rises dramatically.","zh":"這個短語用於數字急劇上升時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"within a decade","meaning":"十年內","examples":[{"en":"China’s tourism market may reach $300 billion within a decade.","zh":"中國旅遊市場可能在十年內達到3000億美元。"},{"en":"Within a decade means within ten years.","zh":"within a decade 指在十年之內。"},{"en":"A small town may become a major tourist area within a decade if transport improves.","zh":"如果交通改善，小鎮可能在十年內成為主要旅遊區。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a future time limit for predicted change.","zh":"這個短語為預測變化設定未來時間限制。"},{"en":"It means the change may happen before ten years have passed.","zh":"它意思是變化可能在十年過去前發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"on this basis","meaning":"基於這一點","examples":[{"en":"On this basis, China’s services sector is well-developed.","zh":"基於這一點，中國服務業對其發展階段而言相當成熟。"},{"en":"On this basis means according to this evidence, comparison, or reasoning.","zh":"on this basis 指根據這個證據、比較或推理。"},{"en":"The student improved in every mock exam; on this basis, the teacher predicted a strong final result.","zh":"學生每次模擬考都有進步；基於這一點，老師預測最終成績會很好。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a conclusion follows from the information just given.","zh":"這個短語顯示結論來自剛給出的資訊。"},{"en":"It helps connect evidence to judgement.","zh":"它幫助把證據與判斷連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be well-developed","meaning":"發展成熟","examples":[{"en":"China’s services sector is well-developed for its stage of growth.","zh":"中國服務業就其發展階段而言發展成熟。"},{"en":"To be well-developed means to be advanced, organised, or mature compared with expectations.","zh":"be well-developed 指相對於預期而言先進、有組織或成熟。"},{"en":"A school’s online learning system is well-developed if lessons, homework, feedback, and records all work smoothly.","zh":"如果學校網上學習系統的課堂、功課、回饋和紀錄都順利運作，它就是發展成熟。"},{"en":"A well-developed sector usually has many firms, skilled workers, and steady demand.","zh":"發展成熟的行業通常有許多公司、熟練員工和穩定需求。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a high level of development.","zh":"這個短語描述高水平發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"roughly as large as","meaning":"大致與……一樣大","examples":[{"en":"China’s services sector is roughly as large as those of Japan and South Korea were.","zh":"中國服務業大致與日本和南韓當時的服務業一樣大。"},{"en":"Roughly as large as means approximately the same size as something else.","zh":"roughly as large as 指大約與另一事物同樣大小。"},{"en":"This year’s class is roughly as large as last year’s, with only two fewer students.","zh":"今年班級人數大致與去年一樣大，只少了兩名學生。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate comparison, not an exact equality.","zh":"這個短語給出大概比較，不是精確相等。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing economic size across countries or periods.","zh":"它適合用於比較不同國家或時期的經濟規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"at a similar stage of development","meaning":"在相似的發展階段","examples":[{"en":"China is compared with Japan and South Korea at a similar stage of development.","zh":"中國被拿來與在相似發展階段的日本和南韓比較。"},{"en":"At a similar stage of development means when countries or organisations are at roughly the same level of economic or institutional progress.","zh":"at a similar stage of development 指國家或機構處於大致相同的經濟或制度進展水平。"},{"en":"A new school should be compared with other schools at a similar stage of development, not with century-old elite schools.","zh":"新學校應與處於相似發展階段的學校比較，而不是與百年名校比較。"},{"en":"Fair comparison requires looking at similar starting points and growth levels.","zh":"公平比較需要看相似起點和增長水平。"},{"en":"The phrase makes comparison more reasonable.","zh":"這個短語令比較更合理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in reality","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In reality, China’s services sector is probably bigger still.","zh":"事實上，中國服務業可能還要更大。"},{"en":"In reality introduces what is actually true, especially when it differs from official figures or appearances.","zh":"in reality 用來引入實際真相，尤其是與官方數字或表面情況不同時。"},{"en":"The timetable looks simple; in reality, students still need help choosing the right classroom.","zh":"時間表看似簡單；事實上，學生仍需要幫助選對課室。"},{"en":"The phrase separates real conditions from what numbers or appearances suggest.","zh":"這個短語把真實情況與數字或表象所暗示的內容分開。"},{"en":"It means “actually”.","zh":"它意思是「實際上」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"bigger still","meaning":"還要更大","examples":[{"en":"The services sector is bigger still than the official figures suggest.","zh":"服務業比官方數字所顯示的還要更大。"},{"en":"Bigger still means even larger than already stated or expected.","zh":"bigger still 指比已說明或預期的還要更大。"},{"en":"The crowd looked large from the gate, but it was bigger still once we entered the hall.","zh":"從大門看人群已很大，但我們進入禮堂後發現還要更大。"},{"en":"Hidden activity can make a sector bigger than official numbers show.","zh":"隱藏活動可以令一個行業比官方數字顯示的更大。"},{"en":"The phrase strengthens the idea of size beyond an earlier estimate.","zh":"這個短語加強超出早前估算的規模概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"GDP revision","meaning":"本地生產總值修訂","examples":[{"en":"The GDP revision could not capture some informal activities.","zh":"GDP 修訂未能記錄一些非正式活動。"},{"en":"A GDP revision is an official update or correction to a country’s measured economic output.","zh":"GDP revision 指對一個國家量度經濟產出的官方更新或修正。"},{"en":"A government may make a GDP revision after finding better data on small businesses.","zh":"政府在找到更好的小企業數據後，可能作出 GDP 修訂。"},{"en":"Revisions can improve accuracy, but they may still miss informal activity.","zh":"修訂可以改善準確度，但仍可能遺漏非正式活動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a statistical adjustment of national output.","zh":"這個短語指對國民產出的統計調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"capture activities","meaning":"記錄經濟活動","examples":[{"en":"The GDP revision cannot capture all informal economic activities.","zh":"GDP 修訂不能記錄所有非正式經濟活動。"},{"en":"To capture activities means to record, count, or include them in a measurement system.","zh":"capture activities 指在量度制度中記錄、計算或納入活動。"},{"en":"A school survey may fail to capture students’ private tutoring if the question is unclear.","zh":"如果問題不清楚，學校問卷可能無法記錄學生私人補習情況。"},{"en":"If activities are not captured, the final data gives an incomplete picture.","zh":"如果活動沒有被記錄，最終數據會給出不完整圖像。"},{"en":"The phrase means to include activities in records, not to stop them.","zh":"這個短語意思是把活動納入紀錄，而不是阻止它們。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"kerbside lending","meaning":"路邊借貸；民間非正式借貸","examples":[{"en":"Kerbside lending is not fully captured in official GDP statistics.","zh":"路邊借貸沒有被官方 GDP 統計完全記錄。"},{"en":"Kerbside lending means informal lending outside official banks or financial institutions.","zh":"kerbside lending 指官方銀行或金融機構以外的非正式借貸。"},{"en":"A shopkeeper may borrow money from a local lender rather than a bank through kerbside lending.","zh":"店主可能透過民間借貸向本地貸款人借錢，而不是向銀行借。"},{"en":"Informal lending can escape official measurement because deals may be private and cash-based.","zh":"非正式借貸可能逃過官方量度，因為交易可能是私人和現金形式。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to unofficial borrowing and lending.","zh":"這個短語指非官方借貸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"tax-dodging cash transactions","meaning":"逃稅現金交易","examples":[{"en":"Tax-dodging cash transactions are common in some service industries.","zh":"逃稅現金交易在一些服務業中很常見。"},{"en":"Tax-dodging cash transactions are cash payments arranged to avoid being recorded and taxed.","zh":"tax-dodging cash transactions 指為避免被記錄和徵稅而安排的現金付款。"},{"en":"A repair worker who takes cash and gives no receipt may be involved in a tax-dodging cash transaction.","zh":"收現金但不開收據的維修工人，可能涉及逃稅現金交易。"},{"en":"Such transactions reduce reported income and make official statistics less accurate.","zh":"這類交易減少申報收入，令官方統計較不準確。"},{"en":"The phrase combines cash payment with tax avoidance.","zh":"這個短語結合現金付款和逃稅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"cash transactions","meaning":"現金交易","examples":[{"en":"Cash transactions in property and entertainment may escape official measurement.","zh":"房地產和娛樂業中的現金交易可能逃過官方量度。"},{"en":"Cash transactions are payments made with physical money rather than bank cards or electronic transfers.","zh":"cash transactions 指用實體金錢而不是銀行卡或電子轉帳付款。"},{"en":"A small street stall may rely mainly on cash transactions.","zh":"小街邊攤可能主要依賴現金交易。"},{"en":"Cash transactions can be harder to track if no receipt or digital record is kept.","zh":"如果沒有收據或數碼紀錄，現金交易可能較難追蹤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to money changing hands in cash.","zh":"這個短語指以現金交付款項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"property or entertainment","meaning":"房地產或娛樂業","examples":[{"en":"Some cash transactions occur in property or entertainment.","zh":"一些現金交易發生在房地產或娛樂業。"},{"en":"Property or entertainment refers to real-estate activities or leisure businesses such as clubs, shows, and performances.","zh":"property or entertainment 指房地產活動或會所、演出和表演等休閒娛樂業務。"},{"en":"Cash payments may occur when someone rents a flat or pays for a private event.","zh":"當有人租樓或支付私人活動費用時，可能出現現金付款。"},{"en":"These areas can include informal payments that are harder to measure.","zh":"這些領域可能包括較難量度的非正式付款。"},{"en":"The phrase names two service fields where hidden transactions may occur.","zh":"這個短語指出可能出現隱藏交易的兩個服務領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"chief Asia economist","meaning":"亞洲首席經濟師","examples":[{"en":"Dong Tao was chief Asia economist at CSFB.","zh":"陶冬是 CSFB 的亞洲首席經濟師。"},{"en":"A chief Asia economist is a senior expert who analyses Asian economies for a financial institution.","zh":"chief Asia economist 指為金融機構分析亞洲經濟的高級專家。"},{"en":"A bank may ask its chief Asia economist to explain growth trends in China, Japan, and India.","zh":"銀行可能請亞洲首席經濟師解釋中國、日本和印度的增長趨勢。"},{"en":"Such economists influence investor expectations because they interpret data and forecasts.","zh":"這類經濟師會影響投資者預期，因為他們解讀數據和預測。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a senior regional economics role.","zh":"這個短語指出高級地區經濟分析職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"reckon that","meaning":"認為；估計","examples":[{"en":"Dong Tao reckons that informal activity adds billions to the economy.","zh":"陶冬估計非正式活動為經濟增加數以十億計價值。"},{"en":"To reckon that means to think, estimate, or judge that something is true.","zh":"reckon that 指認為、估計或判斷某事屬實。"},{"en":"A teacher may reckon that a student needs two more weeks before taking the exam.","zh":"老師可能估計學生還需要兩星期才適合考試。"},{"en":"The phrase often introduces an informed estimate rather than exact proof.","zh":"這個短語常引入有根據的估算，而不是精確證明。"},{"en":"It means “believe” or “estimate” in a relatively informal way.","zh":"它以較非正式方式表示「相信」或「估計」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"add another...to","meaning":"為……再增加……","examples":[{"en":"Informal services may add another $220 billion to the economy.","zh":"非正式服務可能為經濟再增加2200億美元。"},{"en":"To add another amount to something means to increase the total by that extra amount.","zh":"add another amount to something 指把總數額外增加某個數量。"},{"en":"A weekend course may add another ten hours of practice to a student’s preparation.","zh":"週末課程可能為學生備考再增加十小時練習。"},{"en":"Hidden activity can add a large sum to an economy once it is counted.","zh":"隱藏活動一旦被計算，可以為經濟增加一大筆金額。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on extra addition to an existing total.","zh":"這個短語重點是對現有總數作額外增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"even so","meaning":"即使如此","examples":[{"en":"Even so, services remain below the level typical in developed countries.","zh":"即使如此，服務業仍低於發達國家常見水平。"},{"en":"Even so means despite what has just been said, the following point is still true.","zh":"even so 指儘管剛才所說成立，接下來的重點仍然成立。"},{"en":"The student improved a lot; even so, she still needs to practise timing.","zh":"學生進步很多；即使如此，她仍需要練習時間管理。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a limitation after a positive or strong statement.","zh":"這個短語在正面或強烈陳述後引入限制。"},{"en":"It helps keep the argument balanced.","zh":"它幫助論述保持平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"remain below","meaning":"仍低於","examples":[{"en":"China’s services share remains below that of many developed countries.","zh":"中國服務業比重仍低於許多發達國家。"},{"en":"To remain below means to continue to be lower than a certain level or comparison point.","zh":"remain below 指繼續低於某水平或比較點。"},{"en":"A student’s attendance may remain below the school requirement after several absences.","zh":"學生多次缺席後，出席率可能仍低於學校要求。"},{"en":"If a sector remains below developed-country levels, it still has room to grow.","zh":"如果一個行業仍低於發達國家水平，它仍有增長空間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continued lower position.","zh":"這個短語描述持續處於較低位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"typical in developed countries","meaning":"在發達國家常見","examples":[{"en":"A services share of 60–75% is typical in developed countries.","zh":"服務業比重達60%至75%在發達國家很常見。"},{"en":"Typical in developed countries means commonly found in wealthy, industrially advanced economies.","zh":"typical in developed countries 指在富裕且工業先進的經濟體中常見。"},{"en":"High spending on healthcare and education services is typical in developed countries.","zh":"醫療和教育服務高開支在發達國家很常見。"},{"en":"Comparing with what is typical elsewhere helps show whether a country is unusual or still catching up.","zh":"與其他地方常見情況比較，有助顯示一個國家是否不尋常或仍在追趕。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common pattern in richer economies.","zh":"這個短語描述較富裕經濟體中的常見模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"developed countries","meaning":"發達國家","examples":[{"en":"Services usually make up a larger share in developed countries.","zh":"在發達國家，服務業通常佔更大比重。"},{"en":"Developed countries are wealthier countries with advanced infrastructure, industries, institutions, and living standards.","zh":"developed countries 指基礎設施、產業、制度和生活水平先進的較富裕國家。"},{"en":"Developed countries often have large healthcare, finance, education, and leisure sectors.","zh":"發達國家通常有龐大的醫療、金融、教育和休閒行業。"},{"en":"As economies develop, services often become a bigger part of total output.","zh":"隨着經濟發展，服務業通常成為總產出中更大部分。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to countries at a high level of economic development.","zh":"這個短語指經濟發展水平高的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"smaller even than","meaning":"甚至比……更小","examples":[{"en":"China’s services sector is smaller even than India’s.","zh":"中國服務業甚至比印度的更小。"},{"en":"Smaller even than means surprisingly smaller than another thing used for comparison.","zh":"smaller even than 指出乎意料地比另一個比較對象更小。"},{"en":"The school’s playground is smaller even than the car park next door.","zh":"學校操場甚至比旁邊停車場更小。"},{"en":"The phrase adds emphasis because the comparison may be unexpected.","zh":"這個短語加強語氣，因為比較結果可能令人意外。"},{"en":"It highlights a surprising lower position.","zh":"它突出令人驚訝的較低位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"one reason for this","meaning":"這情況的一個原因","examples":[{"en":"One reason for this is a bias towards manufacturing.","zh":"這情況的一個原因是對製造業的偏重。"},{"en":"One reason for this introduces one cause that helps explain the situation just described.","zh":"one reason for this 用來引入解釋剛描述情況的一個原因。"},{"en":"Students may read slowly; one reason for this is limited vocabulary.","zh":"學生閱讀可能很慢；這情況的一個原因是詞彙有限。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the writer is moving from result to explanation.","zh":"這個短語表示作者正由結果轉向解釋。"},{"en":"It suggests there may be other reasons too.","zh":"它暗示也可能有其他原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"bias towards","meaning":"對……的偏重","examples":[{"en":"China has a bias towards manufacturing.","zh":"中國對製造業有偏重。"},{"en":"Bias towards something means a preference for it that may make other areas receive less attention.","zh":"bias towards something 指偏好某事，以致其他領域可能較少受到關注。"},{"en":"A school may have a bias towards exams if it ignores speaking, creativity, and wellbeing.","zh":"如果學校忽視口語、創意和身心健康，它可能對考試有偏重。"},{"en":"A bias can shape policy by directing money and respect toward one area.","zh":"偏重可以透過把資金和重視程度導向某一領域來塑造政策。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unequal preference, not always conscious prejudice.","zh":"這個短語描述不平衡偏好，不一定是有意識偏見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"real-men-make-stuff attitude","meaning":"「真正男子漢才造實物」的心態","examples":[{"en":"China has a “real-men-make-stuff” attitude toward manufacturing.","zh":"中國對製造業有一種「真正男子漢才造實物」的心態。"},{"en":"A real-men-make-stuff attitude is a belief that producing physical goods is more serious or valuable than providing services.","zh":"real-men-make-stuff attitude 指相信製造實體貨品比提供服務更認真或更有價值的想法。"},{"en":"A family business may have this attitude if it respects factory work more than design, branding, or customer service.","zh":"如果家族企業比設計、品牌或顧客服務更尊重工廠工作，它可能有這種心態。"},{"en":"Such an attitude can make policymakers undervalue service industries.","zh":"這種心態可以令政策制定者低估服務業。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises a narrow view of what counts as real economic work.","zh":"這個短語批評對真正經濟工作的狹窄看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"as someone puts it","meaning":"正如某人所說","examples":[{"en":"China has a manufacturing bias, as Gordon Orr puts it.","zh":"正如 Gordon Orr 所說，中國有一種製造業偏重。"},{"en":"As someone puts it means using another person’s wording or explanation.","zh":"as someone puts it 指使用某人的措辭或解釋。"},{"en":"The course is “practice before perfection,” as my teacher puts it.","zh":"正如我老師所說，這門課是「先練習，再追求完美」。"},{"en":"The phrase lets writers quote or paraphrase a memorable expression from someone else.","zh":"這個短語讓作者引用或轉述別人的有力表達。"},{"en":"It signals that the wording belongs to the named person.","zh":"它表示該措辭屬於被點名的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"This bias has led to many regulations for services.","zh":"這種偏重導致服務業有許多規例。"},{"en":"To lead to something means to cause it or help produce it.","zh":"lead to something 指造成某事或促成某事。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can lead to weak concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致課堂專注力差。"},{"en":"A policy preference can lead to rules that favour one industry over another.","zh":"政策偏好可以導致規則偏向某一行業而非另一行業。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses cause and result.","zh":"這個短語表達原因和結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a plethora of","meaning":"大量；過多","examples":[{"en":"China has a plethora of regulations for services.","zh":"中國對服務業有大量規例。"},{"en":"A plethora of something means a very large number of it, often too many.","zh":"a plethora of something 指非常多，通常甚至太多。"},{"en":"A student may feel lost when a website offers a plethora of revision notes with no clear order.","zh":"如果網站提供大量溫習筆記但沒有清楚次序，學生可能感到迷失。"},{"en":"Too many rules can slow business because firms spend time seeking approval instead of serving customers.","zh":"太多規則可以拖慢企業，因為公司要花時間尋求批准而不是服務顧客。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests excess, not just abundance.","zh":"這個短語通常暗示過量，而不只是充足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"ill-thought-through regulations","meaning":"考慮不周的規例","examples":[{"en":"Ill-thought-through regulations have slowed the development of services.","zh":"考慮不周的規例拖慢了服務業發展。"},{"en":"Ill-thought-through regulations are rules made without enough careful planning or understanding.","zh":"ill-thought-through regulations 指沒有足夠仔細規劃或理解就制定的規則。"},{"en":"A school rule banning all phones without planning emergency contact may be ill-thought-through.","zh":"如果學校禁用所有手機但沒有規劃緊急聯絡，這條校規可能考慮不周。"},{"en":"Poorly planned regulations can create delays, extra costs, and confusion.","zh":"規劃差的規例可以造成延誤、額外成本和混亂。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises rules that have not been properly considered.","zh":"這個短語批評未被妥善考慮的規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be made worse by","meaning":"因……而惡化","examples":[{"en":"The problem is made worse by suspicion of private business.","zh":"這個問題因對私營企業的懷疑而惡化。"},{"en":"To be made worse by something means to become more serious because of that factor.","zh":"be made worse by something 指因某因素而變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"Traffic congestion is made worse by illegal parking near schools.","zh":"學校附近違泊令交通擠塞惡化。"},{"en":"A small problem can become difficult to solve when another factor worsens it.","zh":"當另一因素令問題更壞，小問題可以變得難以解決。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies something that aggravates a problem.","zh":"這個短語指出令問題加劇的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"continuing suspicion of","meaning":"對……持續抱有懷疑","examples":[{"en":"China’s continuing suspicion of private business affects services.","zh":"中國對私營企業持續抱有懷疑，影響服務業。"},{"en":"Continuing suspicion of something means an ongoing lack of trust or confidence in it.","zh":"continuing suspicion of something 指對某事持續缺乏信任或信心。"},{"en":"A parent’s continuing suspicion of online learning may make them avoid digital courses.","zh":"家長若對網上學習持續抱有懷疑，可能會避開數碼課程。"},{"en":"Suspicion can slow cooperation because people hesitate to give freedom or support.","zh":"懷疑可以拖慢合作，因為人們猶豫是否給予自由或支持。"},{"en":"The phrase describes distrust that has not gone away.","zh":"這個短語描述尚未消失的不信任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"private business","meaning":"私營企業","examples":[{"en":"Private business is mostly concentrated in the services sector.","zh":"私營企業大多集中於服務業。"},{"en":"Private business means companies owned by individuals or private groups rather than the state.","zh":"private business 指由個人或私人團體而非國家擁有的公司。"},{"en":"A family-run restaurant and a tutoring centre are examples of private business.","zh":"家族經營餐廳和補習中心都是私營企業例子。"},{"en":"Private businesses often grow in services because they can respond quickly to customer needs.","zh":"私營企業常在服務業增長，因為它們能快速回應顧客需要。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts non-state enterprise with government-owned firms.","zh":"這個短語把非國有企業與政府擁有公司作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be concentrated in","meaning":"集中於……","examples":[{"en":"Private business is mostly concentrated in the services sector.","zh":"私營企業大多集中於服務業。"},{"en":"To be concentrated in a place or sector means to be found mainly there.","zh":"be concentrated in a place or sector 指主要出現在某地或某行業。"},{"en":"Many restaurants are concentrated in busy shopping districts.","zh":"許多餐廳集中於繁忙購物區。"},{"en":"When activity is concentrated in one sector, policies affecting that sector have wider impact.","zh":"當活動集中於某行業，影響該行業的政策會有更廣泛影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where something is mainly located or focused.","zh":"這個短語描述某物主要位於或集中在哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the lack of","meaning":"缺乏……","examples":[{"en":"The lack of a national trucking licence slows deliveries.","zh":"缺乏全國貨運牌照拖慢送貨。"},{"en":"The lack of something means that it is missing or not available.","zh":"lack of something 指某物缺失或不可用。"},{"en":"The lack of quiet study space can make homework difficult for students.","zh":"缺乏安靜自修空間可以令學生做功課困難。"},{"en":"When an important requirement is missing, work can become slower and more expensive.","zh":"當重要條件缺失，工作可以變得更慢和更昂貴。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies absence as a cause of a problem.","zh":"這個短語指出缺失是問題原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"national trucking licence","meaning":"全國貨運牌照","examples":[{"en":"Hauliers in China lack a national trucking licence.","zh":"中國貨運商缺乏全國貨運牌照。"},{"en":"A national trucking licence is a permit that allows transport companies to carry goods across the whole country.","zh":"national trucking licence 指允許運輸公司在全國運送貨物的牌照。"},{"en":"A delivery company with a national trucking licence could move goods between provinces more easily.","zh":"有全國貨運牌照的送貨公司，可以更容易在省份之間運貨。"},{"en":"Without a national licence, firms may need separate approvals in different regions.","zh":"如果沒有全國牌照，公司可能需要在不同地區取得個別批准。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a countrywide road-transport permit.","zh":"這個短語指全國適用的道路運輸許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"hauliers","meaning":"貨運商","examples":[{"en":"Hauliers must get approval from each province.","zh":"貨運商必須取得每個省份的批准。"},{"en":"Hauliers are companies or drivers that transport goods by road.","zh":"hauliers 指以道路運送貨物的公司或司機。"},{"en":"A supermarket may rely on hauliers to bring vegetables from farms to city stores.","zh":"超級市場可能依賴貨運商把蔬菜從農場送到城市分店。"},{"en":"If hauliers face too many approvals, deliveries become slower and more expensive.","zh":"如果貨運商面對太多批准程序，送貨會變得更慢和更昂貴。"},{"en":"The word refers to goods-transport operators.","zh":"這個詞指貨物運輸營運者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"get approval from","meaning":"取得……批准","examples":[{"en":"Hauliers must get approval from each province.","zh":"貨運商必須取得每個省份的批准。"},{"en":"To get approval from someone means to receive permission from that person or authority.","zh":"get approval from someone 指從某人或權威取得許可。"},{"en":"Students must get approval from a teacher before using the science lab after school.","zh":"學生放學後使用科學實驗室前，必須取得老師批准。"},{"en":"Requiring approval can protect safety, but too many approvals can delay work.","zh":"要求批准可以保護安全，但太多批准會延誤工作。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on receiving formal permission.","zh":"這個短語重點是取得正式許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"move goods across the country","meaning":"在全國各地運送貨物","examples":[{"en":"Hauliers need permission to move goods across the country.","zh":"貨運商需要許可在全國各地運送貨物。"},{"en":"To move goods across the country means to transport products from one region to another within the nation.","zh":"move goods across the country 指在國內把產品從一個地區運到另一個地區。"},{"en":"A logistics company may move goods across the country from coastal ports to inland shops.","zh":"物流公司可能把貨物從沿海港口運送到內陸商店。"},{"en":"Smooth national transport helps businesses deliver faster and reduce costs.","zh":"順暢的全國運輸幫助企業更快送貨並降低成本。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to domestic goods transportation.","zh":"這個短語指國內貨物運輸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"unload something on to","meaning":"將……卸到……上","examples":[{"en":"Goods may need to be unloaded on to different trucks at each border.","zh":"貨物可能需要在每個邊界被卸到不同貨車上。"},{"en":"To unload something on to another vehicle means to take it off one vehicle and put it onto another.","zh":"unload something on to another vehicle 指把某物從一輛車卸下，再放到另一輛車上。"},{"en":"Workers may unload boxes on to a smaller van for delivery through narrow streets.","zh":"工人可能把箱子卸到較小貨車上，以便在狹窄街道派送。"},{"en":"Repeated unloading can slow transport and increase the risk of damage or theft.","zh":"反覆卸貨可以拖慢運輸並增加損壞或偷竊風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes transferring goods from one carrier to another.","zh":"這個短語描述把貨物從一個運輸工具轉到另一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"at each border","meaning":"在每個邊界","examples":[{"en":"Goods may be unloaded at each provincial border.","zh":"貨物可能在每個省界被卸下。"},{"en":"At each border means at every boundary between regions or administrative areas.","zh":"at each border 指在地區或行政區之間的每一道邊界。"},{"en":"Drivers may need to show documents at each border when crossing several countries.","zh":"司機穿越幾個國家時，可能在每個邊界出示文件。"},{"en":"Repeated checks at borders can create delays and extra costs.","zh":"邊界上的反覆檢查可以造成延誤和額外成本。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises that the process happens again and again at every boundary.","zh":"這個短語強調程序在每個邊界都會重複發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"delay delivery","meaning":"延誤送貨","examples":[{"en":"These rules delay delivery and raise costs.","zh":"這些規則延誤送貨並提高成本。"},{"en":"To delay delivery means to make goods arrive later than expected.","zh":"delay delivery 指令貨物比預期更遲到達。"},{"en":"Bad weather can delay delivery of fresh vegetables to supermarkets.","zh":"惡劣天氣可以延誤新鮮蔬菜送到超級市場。"},{"en":"Delayed delivery can upset customers and increase storage or spoilage costs.","zh":"送貨延誤可以令顧客不滿，並增加儲存或損壞成本。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slower movement of goods to the final user.","zh":"這個短語描述貨物到達最終使用者的速度變慢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"increase spoilage and pilfering","meaning":"增加損耗和偷竊","examples":[{"en":"Frequent unloading increases spoilage and pilfering.","zh":"頻繁卸貨增加損耗和偷竊。"},{"en":"To increase spoilage and pilfering means to cause more goods to go bad or be stolen in small amounts.","zh":"increase spoilage and pilfering 指令更多貨物變壞或被小量偷走。"},{"en":"Moving fruit between trucks too often can increase spoilage and pilfering.","zh":"太頻繁在貨車之間搬動水果，可以增加損耗和偷竊。"},{"en":"Each extra transfer creates another chance for damage, delay, or theft.","zh":"每一次額外轉運都創造另一個損壞、延誤或偷竊機會。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the hidden cost of inefficient transport.","zh":"這個短語顯示低效率運輸的隱藏成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"spoilage","meaning":"貨物損壞；變壞","examples":[{"en":"Spoilage is a problem when goods are delayed in transport.","zh":"當貨物在運輸中延誤，損耗是一個問題。"},{"en":"Spoilage means goods, especially food, become damaged, rotten, or unusable.","zh":"spoilage 指貨物，尤其是食物，受損、腐爛或不能使用。"},{"en":"Milk and fruit can suffer spoilage if a delivery truck has no refrigeration.","zh":"如果送貨車沒有冷藏，牛奶和水果可能變壞。"},{"en":"Delays and poor storage increase spoilage and reduce profits.","zh":"延誤和差劣儲存會增加損耗並減少利潤。"},{"en":"The word refers to loss caused by goods going bad.","zh":"這個詞指貨物變壞造成的損失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"pilfering","meaning":"小偷小摸；偷竊","examples":[{"en":"Pilfering can increase when goods are moved between trucks.","zh":"當貨物在貨車之間搬動，偷竊可能增加。"},{"en":"Pilfering means stealing small amounts, often quietly or repeatedly.","zh":"pilfering 指小量、通常悄悄地或反覆地偷竊。"},{"en":"A warehouse may install cameras to stop pilfering of small electronic items.","zh":"貨倉可能安裝攝影機，以阻止小型電子產品被偷。"},{"en":"Frequent handling gives dishonest workers more chances to pilfer goods.","zh":"頻繁搬運給不誠實工人更多偷取貨物的機會。"},{"en":"The word refers to petty theft rather than large armed robbery.","zh":"這個詞指小偷小摸，而不是大型武裝搶劫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in retailing","meaning":"在零售業方面","examples":[{"en":"In retailing, local governments often maintain inefficient supply chains.","zh":"在零售業方面，地方政府常維持低效率供應鏈。"},{"en":"In retailing means in the business of selling goods directly to consumers.","zh":"in retailing 指在直接向消費者出售貨品的業務中。"},{"en":"In retailing, shop location and customer service can be as important as product price.","zh":"在零售業方面，店舖位置和顧客服務可以與產品價格同樣重要。"},{"en":"Retail rules affect how goods move from suppliers to shops and finally to customers.","zh":"零售規則影響貨物如何從供應商到商店，最後到顧客手中。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows the discussion to the retail sector.","zh":"這個短語把討論收窄到零售業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"local governments","meaning":"地方政府","examples":[{"en":"Local governments may protect inefficient supply chains.","zh":"地方政府可能保護低效率供應鏈。"},{"en":"Local governments are authorities that govern provinces, cities, districts, or towns rather than the whole country.","zh":"local governments 指管理省、市、區或城鎮，而不是全國的政府機關。"},{"en":"Local governments may manage roads, schools, markets, and business permits.","zh":"地方政府可能管理道路、學校、市場和商業許可。"},{"en":"Their decisions can affect local jobs, prices, and transport efficiency.","zh":"它們的決定可以影響本地工作、價格和運輸效率。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to regional or municipal authorities.","zh":"這個短語指地方或市政權力機關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"maintain inefficient supply chains","meaning":"維持低效率的供應鏈","examples":[{"en":"Some local governments maintain inefficient supply chains.","zh":"一些地方政府維持低效率的供應鏈。"},{"en":"To maintain inefficient supply chains means to keep using slow, costly, or poorly organised systems for moving goods.","zh":"maintain inefficient supply chains 指繼續使用緩慢、昂貴或組織差劣的貨物流動系統。"},{"en":"A shop may maintain an inefficient supply chain if it uses too many middlemen to receive products.","zh":"如果店舖用太多中間商收貨，它可能維持低效率供應鏈。"},{"en":"Inefficient supply chains raise costs and can make goods more expensive for customers.","zh":"低效率供應鏈會提高成本，並可能令顧客買到更貴商品。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises keeping a bad distribution system in place.","zh":"這個短語批評保留差劣分銷系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in part to","meaning":"部分是為了","examples":[{"en":"Local governments protect supply chains in part to protect local jobs.","zh":"地方政府保護供應鏈，部分是為了保護本地職位。"},{"en":"In part to means partly for the purpose of doing something.","zh":"in part to 指部分目的是為了做某事。"},{"en":"A school may keep a small class open in part to support students who need extra help.","zh":"學校可能保留小班，部分是為了支援需要額外幫助的學生。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that there is more than one reason behind the action.","zh":"這個短語暗示行動背後有多於一個原因。"},{"en":"It introduces one purpose, not necessarily the only purpose.","zh":"它引入其中一個目的，不一定是唯一目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"protect local jobs","meaning":"保護本地職位","examples":[{"en":"Inefficient supply chains may be maintained to protect local jobs.","zh":"低效率供應鏈可能被維持，以保護本地職位。"},{"en":"To protect local jobs means to preserve employment opportunities for people in the area.","zh":"protect local jobs 指保留該地區居民的就業機會。"},{"en":"A town may support small shops to protect local jobs from large chains.","zh":"城鎮可能支持小店，以保護本地職位免受大型連鎖店影響。"},{"en":"Protecting jobs can help families, but it may also preserve inefficient systems.","zh":"保護職位可以幫助家庭，但也可能保留低效率制度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes employment protection in a local community.","zh":"這個短語描述本地社區中的就業保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"head of","meaning":"……的主管","examples":[{"en":"David Wei was head of B&Q in China.","zh":"衛哲是 B&Q 中國業務的主管。"},{"en":"Head of an organisation means the person in charge of it.","zh":"head of an organisation 指負責該組織的人。"},{"en":"The head of a school department decides timetables, teaching plans, and staff duties.","zh":"學校部門主管決定時間表、教學計劃和員工職責。"},{"en":"A head of a company branch can explain how local business operations work.","zh":"公司分部主管可以解釋本地業務如何運作。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a leadership role.","zh":"這個短語指出領導職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"do-it-yourself stores on the mainland","meaning":"內地家居裝修用品店","examples":[{"en":"B&Q had 48 do-it-yourself stores on the mainland.","zh":"B&Q 在內地有48間家居裝修用品店。"},{"en":"Do-it-yourself stores on the mainland are home-improvement shops located in mainland China.","zh":"do-it-yourself stores on the mainland 指位於中國內地的家居改善用品店。"},{"en":"A homeowner may visit a mainland DIY store to buy paint, tiles, and tools.","zh":"業主可能到內地 DIY 店購買油漆、瓷磚和工具。"},{"en":"The number of such stores can show how property ownership and renovation services are growing.","zh":"這類店舖數量可以顯示置業和裝修服務如何增長。"},{"en":"The phrase connects retailing, property development, and mainland consumer demand.","zh":"這個短語把零售、房地產發展和內地消費需求連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be served by","meaning":"由……供應","examples":[{"en":"The stores are served by 1,800 suppliers.","zh":"這些店舖由1,800家供應商供應。"},{"en":"To be served by suppliers means to receive goods or support from those suppliers.","zh":"be served by suppliers 指從這些供應商接收貨品或支援。"},{"en":"A school cafeteria may be served by farms, bakeries, and drink companies.","zh":"學校飯堂可能由農場、麵包店和飲品公司供應。"},{"en":"If a store is served by too many suppliers, coordination can become difficult.","zh":"如果店舖由太多供應商供應，協調可能變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes supply relationships.","zh":"這個短語描述供應關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"The company has far more suppliers in China compared with Britain.","zh":"與英國相比，該公司在中國有多得多的供應商。"},{"en":"Compared with is used to show difference between two places, figures, or situations.","zh":"compared with 用來顯示兩個地方、數字或情況之間的差異。"},{"en":"Public transport is cheaper in this city compared with many overseas cities.","zh":"與許多海外城市相比，這個城市的公共交通較便宜。"},{"en":"The phrase helps readers understand scale by using a familiar comparison point.","zh":"這個短語透過使用熟悉比較點來幫助讀者理解規模。"},{"en":"It is useful for explaining contrast in business data.","zh":"它適合解釋商業數據中的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"take an early decision to","meaning":"早早決定去……","examples":[{"en":"China took an early decision to invite foreign investment into manufacturing.","zh":"中國早早決定引入外國投資到製造業。"},{"en":"To take an early decision to do something means to decide to act sooner than others or sooner than expected.","zh":"take an early decision to do something 指比其他人或比預期更早決定採取行動。"},{"en":"A school may take an early decision to move lessons online before a storm arrives.","zh":"學校可能在風暴到來前早早決定把課堂轉到網上。"},{"en":"Early decisions can shape long-term development because they set direction quickly.","zh":"早期決定可以塑造長期發展，因為它很快設定方向。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses timing and policy choice.","zh":"這個短語強調時機和政策選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"invite foreign direct investment into","meaning":"引入外國直接投資到……","examples":[{"en":"China invited foreign direct investment into manufacturing.","zh":"中國引入外國直接投資到製造業。"},{"en":"To invite foreign direct investment into a sector means to encourage overseas companies to invest directly in that industry.","zh":"invite foreign direct investment into a sector 指鼓勵海外公司直接投資某行業。"},{"en":"A government may invite foreign direct investment into renewable energy by offering clear rules and tax incentives.","zh":"政府可能透過清楚規則和稅務優惠，引入外國直接投資到可再生能源。"},{"en":"Foreign direct investment can bring money, technology, management skills, and competition.","zh":"外國直接投資可以帶來資金、技術、管理技能和競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to policy that opens an industry to overseas investors.","zh":"這個短語指向海外投資者開放某行業的政策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"foreign direct investment","meaning":"外國直接投資","examples":[{"en":"Foreign direct investment helped China’s manufacturing sector.","zh":"外國直接投資幫助了中國製造業。"},{"en":"Foreign direct investment is investment by overseas companies in businesses, factories, or operations inside another country.","zh":"foreign direct investment 指海外公司投資另一國內的企業、工廠或營運。"},{"en":"A carmaker building a factory abroad is making foreign direct investment.","zh":"汽車製造商在海外建廠，就是進行外國直接投資。"},{"en":"FDI can create jobs and transfer technology, but it may also increase competition for local firms.","zh":"外資可以創造職位和轉移技術，但也可能增加本地公司的競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to direct business investment across borders.","zh":"這個短語指跨境直接商業投資。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be reluctant to","meaning":"不願意……","examples":[{"en":"China has been reluctant to open up services.","zh":"中國一直不願意開放服務業。"},{"en":"To be reluctant to do something means to be unwilling or hesitant to do it.","zh":"be reluctant to do something 指不願意或猶豫去做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be reluctant to speak in class because she fears making mistakes.","zh":"學生可能因害怕犯錯而不願意在課堂發言。"},{"en":"Reluctance can slow change even when reform might bring benefits.","zh":"不願意改變可以拖慢改革，即使改革可能帶來好處。"},{"en":"The phrase describes hesitation, not impossibility.","zh":"這個短語描述猶豫，而不是不可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"open up services","meaning":"開放服務業","examples":[{"en":"China has been slower to open up services to foreign investors.","zh":"中國在向外國投資者開放服務業方面較慢。"},{"en":"To open up services means to allow more competition, private firms, or foreign investment in service industries.","zh":"open up services 指允許服務業有更多競爭、私人企業或外國投資。"},{"en":"A country may open up banking services by allowing foreign banks to operate branches.","zh":"一個國家可能透過允許外國銀行開設分行來開放銀行服務。"},{"en":"Opening up services can increase competition and improve quality, but it may threaten protected firms.","zh":"開放服務業可以增加競爭並改善質素，但也可能威脅受保護公司。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to liberalising service industries.","zh":"這個短語指放寬服務業限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"director of","meaning":"……的總監","examples":[{"en":"Diana Farrell was director of the McKinsey Global Institute.","zh":"Diana Farrell 是 McKinsey Global Institute 的總監。"},{"en":"Director of an organisation means a senior person responsible for leading or managing it.","zh":"director of an organisation 指負責領導或管理該機構的高級人士。"},{"en":"The director of a language centre may decide courses, teachers, and business strategy.","zh":"語言中心總監可能決定課程、老師和商業策略。"},{"en":"A director’s opinion can carry weight because they oversee research or operations.","zh":"總監的意見可能有分量，因為他們監督研究或營運。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a leadership position.","zh":"這個短語指出領導職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"consultancy’s think-tank","meaning":"顧問公司的智庫","examples":[{"en":"The McKinsey Global Institute is the consultancy’s think-tank.","zh":"McKinsey Global Institute 是該顧問公司的智庫。"},{"en":"A consultancy’s think-tank is its research group that studies problems and produces analysis or policy ideas.","zh":"consultancy’s think-tank 指顧問公司的研究小組，負責研究問題並提出分析或政策想法。"},{"en":"A business consultancy may use its think-tank to study labour trends and consumer behaviour.","zh":"商業顧問公司可能使用其智庫研究勞動趨勢和消費者行為。"},{"en":"Think-tanks influence debate by turning data into arguments and recommendations.","zh":"智庫透過把數據變成論點和建議來影響討論。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an organisation’s research and ideas unit.","zh":"這個短語指機構的研究和思想部門。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"argue that","meaning":"主張；認為","examples":[{"en":"Diana Farrell argues that foreign investment could improve services.","zh":"Diana Farrell 主張外國投資可以改善服務業。"},{"en":"To argue that means to state a view and support it with reasons.","zh":"argue that 指提出一個觀點並用理由支持。"},{"en":"A student may argue that school should start later because teenagers need more sleep.","zh":"學生可能主張學校應較遲上課，因為青少年需要更多睡眠。"},{"en":"An argument is stronger when it gives evidence, examples, and clear logic.","zh":"當論點提供證據、例子和清晰邏輯，它會更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a claim, not a quarrel only.","zh":"這個短語引入主張，不只是爭吵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"allow more foreign investment","meaning":"允許更多外國投資","examples":[{"en":"Allowing more foreign investment could improve the services sector.","zh":"允許更多外國投資可以改善服務業。"},{"en":"To allow more foreign investment means to permit more overseas companies or investors to put money into local businesses.","zh":"allow more foreign investment 指准許更多海外公司或投資者把資金投入本地企業。"},{"en":"A country may allow more foreign investment in hospitals to increase medical capacity.","zh":"一個國家可能允許更多外國投資進入醫院，以增加醫療容量。"},{"en":"More foreign investment can bring capital, skills, technology, and competition.","zh":"更多外國投資可以帶來資本、技能、技術和競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase describes opening markets to outside investors.","zh":"這個短語描述向外部投資者開放市場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"bring not just...but...","meaning":"帶來的不只是……還有……","examples":[{"en":"Foreign investment could bring not just capital and technology but competition.","zh":"外國投資帶來的不只是資本和技術，還有競爭。"},{"en":"Bring not just A but B means provide A and also an additional important thing B.","zh":"bring not just A but B 指帶來 A，也帶來另一項重要事物 B。"},{"en":"A good exchange programme brings not just language practice but confidence and cultural understanding.","zh":"好的交流計劃帶來的不只是語言練習，還有信心和文化理解。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises that the second benefit should not be overlooked.","zh":"這個短語強調第二項好處不應被忽視。"},{"en":"It is useful when one cause has several important effects.","zh":"當一個原因有幾個重要效果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"capital and technology","meaning":"資本和技術","examples":[{"en":"Foreign investors can bring capital and technology.","zh":"外國投資者可以帶來資本和技術。"},{"en":"Capital and technology mean money for investment and technical knowledge or equipment.","zh":"capital and technology 指投資資金以及技術知識或設備。"},{"en":"A new factory may need capital and technology before it can produce high-quality goods.","zh":"新工廠在生產高質素貨品前，可能需要資本和技術。"},{"en":"These inputs can help firms grow faster and become more productive.","zh":"這些投入可以幫助企業更快增長並提高生產力。"},{"en":"The phrase names two common benefits of foreign investment.","zh":"這個短語指出外國投資的兩項常見好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"competitive dynamic","meaning":"競爭動力","examples":[{"en":"Foreign investment could bring a competitive dynamic.","zh":"外國投資可以帶來競爭動力。"},{"en":"A competitive dynamic is the pressure and energy created when firms compete with one another.","zh":"competitive dynamic 指企業互相競爭時形成的壓力和活力。"},{"en":"A new café can create a competitive dynamic that pushes nearby cafés to improve service.","zh":"新咖啡店可以創造競爭動力，推動附近咖啡店改善服務。"},{"en":"Competition can force companies to innovate, lower prices, or become more efficient.","zh":"競爭可以迫使公司創新、降低價格或變得更有效率。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the active force of market competition.","zh":"這個短語描述市場競爭的活躍力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the presence of","meaning":"……的進入；……的存在","examples":[{"en":"The presence of Carrefour and Wal-Mart changed the retail market.","zh":"Carrefour 和 Wal-Mart 的進入改變了零售市場。"},{"en":"The presence of a company means its existence or operation in a place or market.","zh":"presence of a company 指某公司在某地或市場中的存在或營運。"},{"en":"The presence of a new supermarket can change how small shops price their goods.","zh":"新超級市場的出現可以改變小店如何定價。"},{"en":"When a major company enters a market, competitors may copy or improve their methods.","zh":"當大型公司進入市場，競爭者可能模仿或改善其方法。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the effect of a company being there.","zh":"這個短語重點是某公司存在於當地所產生的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"domestic copycats","meaning":"本地模仿者","examples":[{"en":"Foreign retailers have led to domestic copycats.","zh":"外國零售商催生了本地模仿者。"},{"en":"Domestic copycats are local companies that imitate the methods, style, or business model of foreign firms.","zh":"domestic copycats 指模仿外國公司方法、風格或商業模式的本地公司。"},{"en":"After a successful café chain opens, domestic copycats may copy its menu and design.","zh":"成功咖啡連鎖店開業後，本地模仿者可能複製其餐牌和設計。"},{"en":"Copycats can spread new business practices quickly, even if they are not original.","zh":"模仿者可以快速傳播新商業做法，即使它們不是原創。"},{"en":"The phrase can sound critical because it suggests imitation rather than innovation.","zh":"這個短語可以帶批評意味，因為它暗示模仿而不是創新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"create innovation","meaning":"創造創新","examples":[{"en":"Competition can create innovation and productivity growth.","zh":"競爭可以創造創新和生產力增長。"},{"en":"To create innovation means to produce new ideas, methods, products, or improvements.","zh":"create innovation 指產生新想法、新方法、新產品或改進。"},{"en":"A school competition may create innovation when students design new ways to save energy.","zh":"學校比賽可能在學生設計節能新方法時創造創新。"},{"en":"Competition can push firms to improve because standing still becomes risky.","zh":"競爭可以推動企業改善，因為停滯不前會變得有風險。"},{"en":"The phrase connects pressure with new solutions.","zh":"這個短語把壓力與新解決方法連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"productivity growth","meaning":"生產力增長","examples":[{"en":"Foreign competition may encourage productivity growth.","zh":"外國競爭可能鼓勵生產力增長。"},{"en":"Productivity growth means producing more output with the same or fewer resources.","zh":"productivity growth 指用相同或更少資源生產更多產出。"},{"en":"A restaurant achieves productivity growth if it serves more customers with the same number of staff.","zh":"如果餐廳用相同員工服務更多顧客，就是達成生產力增長。"},{"en":"Better technology, training, and management can increase productivity.","zh":"更好技術、培訓和管理可以提高生產力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improved efficiency in production or service.","zh":"這個短語描述生產或服務效率改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"for each question","meaning":"對每條題目而言","examples":[{"en":"For each question, only one of the choices is correct.","zh":"對每條題目而言，只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"For each question means separately for every question in the task.","zh":"for each question 指對任務中的每一道題分別而言。"},{"en":"For each question, students should read all options before choosing an answer.","zh":"對每條題目而言，學生應先讀完所有選項再選答案。"},{"en":"This instruction prevents students from assuming that several choices can be correct.","zh":"這項指示防止學生假設幾個選項都可以正確。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a rule that applies item by item.","zh":"這個短語設定逐題適用的規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"only one of the choices is correct","meaning":"只有一個選項正確","examples":[{"en":"The instructions say that only one of the choices is correct.","zh":"指示說只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct means students must select a single right answer from the options.","zh":"only one of the choices is correct 指學生必須從選項中選出唯一正確答案。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice reading question, choosing two letters is wrong if only one choice is correct.","zh":"在閱讀選擇題中，如果只有一個選項正確，選兩個字母就是錯。"},{"en":"This rule forces careful comparison between similar-looking options.","zh":"這條規則迫使學生仔細比較看似相似的選項。"},{"en":"The phrase warns students not to give multiple answers.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生不要給多個答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"corresponding letter","meaning":"相應字母","examples":[{"en":"Students write the corresponding letter in the answer box.","zh":"學生在答案格中寫上相應字母。"},{"en":"A corresponding letter is the letter that matches the correct answer option.","zh":"corresponding letter 指與正確答案選項相配的字母。"},{"en":"If the correct answer is option C, students should write the corresponding letter C.","zh":"如果正確答案是選項 C，學生應寫上相應字母 C。"},{"en":"Writing the wrong letter loses the mark even if the student understood the idea.","zh":"即使學生理解意思，寫錯字母也會失分。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in multiple-choice exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於選擇題考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"指的是","examples":[{"en":"The phrase “the world’s factory” refers to China.","zh":"“the world’s factory” 這個短語指的是中國。"},{"en":"To refer to something means to mean, mention, or point to it.","zh":"refer to something 指意思是、提到或指向某事物。"},{"en":"In the sentence “this city”, this may refer to Hong Kong if Hong Kong was just mentioned.","zh":"在 “this city” 這句中，如果剛提到香港，this 可能指香港。"},{"en":"Understanding what a phrase refers to helps readers avoid confusing the subject.","zh":"理解短語指的是甚麼，幫助讀者避免混淆主體。"},{"en":"The phrase is important in reading questions about meaning and reference.","zh":"這個短語在關於意思和指代的閱讀題中很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the total amount of goods produced","meaning":"生產貨品總量","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions the total amount of goods produced in the world.","zh":"該選項提到世界上生產貨品總量。"},{"en":"The total amount of goods produced means all physical products made within a stated area or period.","zh":"total amount of goods produced 指某地或某段時間內製造的所有實體產品。"},{"en":"A factory may record the total amount of goods produced each month to check efficiency.","zh":"工廠可能每月記錄生產貨品總量，以檢查效率。"},{"en":"This figure measures output, but it does not include all services people provide.","zh":"這個數字量度產出，但不包括人們提供的所有服務。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on manufactured products, not the whole economy.","zh":"這個短語重點是製造產品，而不是整個經濟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"state-owned companies","meaning":"國有企業","examples":[{"en":"State-owned companies are easier to measure than small private firms.","zh":"國有企業比小型私人公司更容易量度。"},{"en":"State-owned companies are businesses owned or controlled by the government.","zh":"state-owned companies 指由政府擁有或控制的企業。"},{"en":"A state-owned railway company may report its income and passenger numbers directly to the government.","zh":"國有鐵路公司可能直接向政府報告收入和乘客人數。"},{"en":"Because official records are usually clearer, state-owned firms can be easier to count in statistics.","zh":"因為官方紀錄通常較清楚，國有企業可能較容易被納入統計。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts government-owned businesses with private companies.","zh":"這個短語把政府擁有企業與私人公司作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"numerous small companies","meaning":"大量小型公司","examples":[{"en":"It is difficult to measure the finances of numerous small companies.","zh":"要量度大量小型公司的財務狀況很困難。"},{"en":"Numerous small companies means many businesses that are individually small in size.","zh":"numerous small companies 指數量很多但個別規模小的企業。"},{"en":"A street with many family-run shops may contain numerous small companies.","zh":"一條有許多家庭式店舖的街道，可能有大量小型公司。"},{"en":"When companies are numerous and small, collecting complete financial records becomes difficult.","zh":"當公司數量多而規模小，收集完整財務紀錄會變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both large number and small scale.","zh":"這個短語同時強調數量多和規模小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"measure the finances of","meaning":"量度……的財務狀況","examples":[{"en":"Statisticians find it hard to measure the finances of small firms.","zh":"統計人員覺得量度小公司的財務狀況很困難。"},{"en":"To measure the finances of a business means to record or estimate its income, costs, profits, and other money figures.","zh":"measure the finances of a business 指記錄或估算其收入、成本、利潤和其他金錢數字。"},{"en":"A school club may measure its finances by tracking ticket sales and spending on materials.","zh":"學校學會可能透過追蹤門票收入和材料開支來量度財務狀況。"},{"en":"Without clear records, it is hard to know how much money a business really makes.","zh":"沒有清楚紀錄，就難以知道企業真正賺多少錢。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to financial measurement and reporting.","zh":"這個短語指財務量度和報告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"increase the size of","meaning":"擴大……的規模","examples":[{"en":"Real estate helped increase the size of the service economy.","zh":"房地產幫助擴大服務型經濟的規模。"},{"en":"To increase the size of something means to make it larger in scale, value, or amount.","zh":"increase the size of something 指令某事物在規模、價值或數量上變大。"},{"en":"More students can increase the size of a language school’s business.","zh":"更多學生可以擴大語言學校的業務規模。"},{"en":"Growth in one industry can increase the size of related service sectors.","zh":"一個行業的增長可以擴大相關服務行業規模。"},{"en":"The phrase describes expansion.","zh":"這個短語描述擴張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"service economy","meaning":"服務型經濟","examples":[{"en":"Property development increased the size of the service economy.","zh":"房地產發展擴大了服務型經濟的規模。"},{"en":"A service economy is an economy where services make up a large or important share of activity.","zh":"service economy 指服務業佔很大或重要比重的經濟。"},{"en":"Banking, education, healthcare, transport, and tourism are parts of a service economy.","zh":"銀行、教育、醫療、運輸和旅遊都是服務型經濟的一部分。"},{"en":"A service economy grows when people and firms spend more on help, expertise, leisure, and convenience.","zh":"當人和企業在協助、專業知識、休閒和便利上花更多錢，服務型經濟就會增長。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts service-based activity with goods production.","zh":"這個短語把以服務為基礎的活動與貨品生產作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"involve investment from abroad","meaning":"涉及海外投資","examples":[{"en":"Real estate can involve investment from abroad.","zh":"房地產可能涉及海外投資。"},{"en":"To involve investment from abroad means to include money coming from foreign investors.","zh":"involve investment from abroad 指包括來自外國投資者的資金。"},{"en":"A new hotel project may involve investment from abroad if an overseas company helps fund it.","zh":"如果海外公司協助出資，新酒店項目可能涉及海外投資。"},{"en":"Foreign investment can increase the amount of money available for development.","zh":"外國投資可以增加可用於發展的資金。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights overseas financial participation.","zh":"這個短語突出海外財務參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"require services","meaning":"需要服務","examples":[{"en":"Developing real estate requires many supporting services.","zh":"發展房地產需要許多支援服務。"},{"en":"To require services means to need people or businesses to provide specialised help.","zh":"require services 指需要人或企業提供專門協助。"},{"en":"A wedding requires services such as catering, photography, transport, and venue management.","zh":"婚禮需要餐飲、攝影、交通和場地管理等服務。"},{"en":"Large projects create demand because they cannot be completed by goods alone.","zh":"大型項目創造需求，因為它們不能單靠貨品完成。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that economic activity often depends on service providers.","zh":"這個短語顯示經濟活動常依賴服務提供者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"largest portion of household spending","meaning":"家庭開支中最大部分","examples":[{"en":"The largest portion of household spending goes towards housing.","zh":"家庭開支中最大部分用於住房。"},{"en":"The largest portion of household spending means the biggest share of a family’s total expenses.","zh":"largest portion of household spending 指家庭總開支中最大的份額。"},{"en":"For many families, rent or mortgage payments form the largest portion of household spending.","zh":"對許多家庭而言，租金或按揭供款構成家庭開支中最大部分。"},{"en":"Knowing the largest spending category helps explain family financial pressure.","zh":"知道最大開支類別，有助解釋家庭財政壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase compares different parts of household expenses.","zh":"這個短語比較家庭開支的不同部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"household spending","meaning":"家庭開支","examples":[{"en":"Education and housing take up a large share of household spending.","zh":"教育和住房佔家庭開支很大比重。"},{"en":"Household spending is the money a family spends on living costs, services, and goods.","zh":"household spending 指家庭花在生活成本、服務和貨品上的金錢。"},{"en":"Food, rent, transport, school fees, and healthcare are parts of household spending.","zh":"食物、租金、交通、學費和醫療都是家庭開支的一部分。"},{"en":"When household spending rises faster than income, families may feel financial pressure.","zh":"當家庭開支升得比收入快，家庭可能感到財政壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to family-level expenditure.","zh":"這個短語指家庭層面的支出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"go towards","meaning":"用於……","examples":[{"en":"Much household spending goes towards housing and education.","zh":"許多家庭開支用於住房和教育。"},{"en":"To go towards something means to be used for that purpose or expense.","zh":"go towards something 指被用於某目的或開支。"},{"en":"Part of a student’s allowance may go towards transport and lunch.","zh":"學生零用錢的一部分可能用於交通和午餐。"},{"en":"Spending patterns show what families must pay for before they can save money.","zh":"消費模式顯示家庭在儲蓄前必須支付甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where money is directed.","zh":"這個短語描述金錢被投放到哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"accommodation","meaning":"住屋；住宿","examples":[{"en":"Accommodation is one of the biggest household expenses.","zh":"住屋是最大家庭開支之一。"},{"en":"Accommodation means housing or a place to live or stay.","zh":"accommodation 指住房或居住、停留的地方。"},{"en":"University students may spend a large part of their budget on accommodation.","zh":"大學生可能把預算很大部分花在住宿上。"},{"en":"When accommodation costs rise, families have less money for education, travel, or savings.","zh":"當住宿成本上升，家庭用於教育、旅遊或儲蓄的錢就較少。"},{"en":"The word can refer to permanent housing or temporary lodging.","zh":"這個詞可以指永久住屋或臨時住宿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"complete the following sentences","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the following sentences using words from the text.","zh":"學生使用文本中的字詞完成以下句子。"},{"en":"To complete the following sentences means to fill the blanks in the sentences that come next.","zh":"complete the following sentences 指填補接下來句子中的空格。"},{"en":"Students should read the full sentence before choosing words from the passage.","zh":"學生從文章選字前，應先讀完整句。"},{"en":"This task tests meaning, grammar, and exact wording.","zh":"這項任務測試意思、文法和準確措辭。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不超過三個字","examples":[{"en":"Students should use no more than three words from the text.","zh":"學生應使用文本中不超過三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain one, two, or three words only.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案只能包含一個、兩個或三個詞。"},{"en":"If the correct answer is “private education”, it fits because it has two words.","zh":"如果正確答案是 “private education”，它符合要求，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing four words may lose marks even if the meaning is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫四個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit for exam answers.","zh":"這個短語為考試答案給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"not really a rival to","meaning":"不算真正是……的對手","examples":[{"en":"China is not really a rival to India in some outsourcing areas.","zh":"在一些外判領域，中國不算真正是印度的對手。"},{"en":"Not really a rival to someone means not yet strong enough to compete seriously with them.","zh":"not really a rival to someone 指尚未強到可以與某人或某方認真競爭。"},{"en":"A new café is not really a rival to a famous chain if it has only one small shop.","zh":"如果新咖啡店只有一間小店，它不算真正是著名連鎖店的對手。"},{"en":"Weakness in language or experience can stop a country from becoming a true competitor.","zh":"語言或經驗弱點可以阻止一個國家成為真正競爭者。"},{"en":"The phrase softens a comparison by saying competition is limited.","zh":"這個短語透過說競爭有限來軟化比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"in the role of","meaning":"以……的角色","examples":[{"en":"China is growing in the role of an outsourcing hub.","zh":"中國正以外判服務中心的角色增長。"},{"en":"In the role of means acting as or developing as a particular kind of person, place, or organisation.","zh":"in the role of 指以某種人、地方或機構的身份發揮作用或發展。"},{"en":"A library may serve in the role of a community study centre after school.","zh":"圖書館放學後可以以社區學習中心的角色服務。"},{"en":"A place’s role can change as its skills, industries, and connections grow.","zh":"一個地方的角色可以隨着技能、產業和聯繫增長而改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes function or position.","zh":"這個短語描述功能或位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"real estate and leisure industries","meaning":"房地產和休閒行業","examples":[{"en":"Cash transactions occur in the real estate and leisure industries.","zh":"現金交易發生在房地產和休閒行業。"},{"en":"Real estate and leisure industries are property-related businesses and businesses connected with recreation or entertainment.","zh":"real estate and leisure industries 指物業相關業務，以及與休閒或娛樂相關的企業。"},{"en":"Property agents, hotels, cinemas, gyms, and clubs may belong to these broad industries.","zh":"地產代理、酒店、戲院、健身室和會所可能屬於這些廣泛行業。"},{"en":"Cash transactions in these industries can make official measurement less complete.","zh":"這些行業中的現金交易可以令官方量度較不完整。"},{"en":"The phrase groups property and enjoyment-related services together.","zh":"這個短語把物業和享樂相關服務歸在一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"that leads to","meaning":"這導致","examples":[{"en":"Cash transactions can lead to tax-dodging.","zh":"現金交易可以導致逃稅。"},{"en":"That leads to means that one situation causes another result.","zh":"that leads to 指某情況造成另一結果。"},{"en":"Missing basic grammar practice leads to repeated sentence errors.","zh":"缺少基本文法練習會導致句子錯誤反覆出現。"},{"en":"If payments leave no record, that can lead to tax avoidance.","zh":"如果付款沒有留下紀錄，這可以導致避稅。"},{"en":"The phrase links a cause to its consequence.","zh":"這個短語把原因與後果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"far less investment into","meaning":"投入……的投資少得多","examples":[{"en":"China has brought far less foreign investment into services.","zh":"中國引入服務業的外國投資少得多。"},{"en":"Far less investment into something means much smaller amounts of money have been put into that area.","zh":"far less investment into something 指投入某領域的資金少得多。"},{"en":"A school may receive far less investment into sports than into exam preparation.","zh":"學校投入體育的資源可能遠少於考試準備。"},{"en":"Less investment can slow development because firms lack capital, technology, and competition.","zh":"投資較少可以拖慢發展，因為企業缺乏資本、技術和競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a large gap in funding or investment.","zh":"這個短語顯示資金或投資上的巨大差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"slow development of","meaning":"減慢……的發展","examples":[{"en":"Restrictions can slow development of the services sector.","zh":"限制可以減慢服務業的發展。"},{"en":"To slow development of something means to make its growth or progress happen more slowly.","zh":"slow development of something 指令某事物的增長或進展變慢。"},{"en":"Too many approvals can slow development of a new school project.","zh":"太多批准程序可以減慢新學校項目的發展。"},{"en":"Regulations may slow development when they raise costs or delay decisions.","zh":"當規例提高成本或延誤決定，它們可能減慢發展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something blocking or reducing the speed of progress.","zh":"這個短語描述阻礙或降低進展速度的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"do the following statements agree with","meaning":"以下陳述是否與……相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements agree with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷以下陳述是否與文章相符。"},{"en":"Do the following statements agree with asks whether each statement matches the information in the text.","zh":"do the following statements agree with 是問每項陳述是否與文本資訊一致。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students must check whether each claim agrees with the passage, contradicts it, or is not given.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生必須檢查每項說法是否與文章一致、相矛盾，或沒有提及。"},{"en":"This task tests accuracy rather than personal opinion.","zh":"這項任務測試準確性，而不是個人意見。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN style question.","zh":"這個短語引入 TRUE、FALSE、NOT GIVEN 類型問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"information given in","meaning":"……中提供的資料","examples":[{"en":"The answers must agree with the information given in the passage.","zh":"答案必須與文章中提供的資料一致。"},{"en":"Information given in a passage means facts or claims actually stated in that text.","zh":"information given in a passage 指文本中實際陳述的事實或主張。"},{"en":"Students should answer according to the information given in the article, not outside knowledge.","zh":"學生應根據文章中提供的資料作答，而不是外部知識。"},{"en":"If the text does not provide evidence, the answer may be NOT GIVEN.","zh":"如果文本沒有提供證據，答案可能是 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds readers to stay inside the source.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者留在來源之內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章內容相反的說法。"},{"en":"If the passage says services are growing, a statement saying services are shrinking contradicts it.","zh":"如果文章說服務業正在增長，陳述說服務業正在萎縮就是與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"A contradiction must be supported by clear words in the text.","zh":"判斷矛盾必須由文本中的清楚字眼支持。"},{"en":"The phrase is central to TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語是 TRUE、FALSE、NOT GIVEN 題的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students write “NOT GIVEN” if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果沒有相關資料，學生寫 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not provide enough evidence to decide.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文章沒有提供足夠證據作判斷。"},{"en":"If the passage discusses GDP but never mentions workers’ salaries, there is no information on salaries.","zh":"如果文章討論 GDP 但從未提及工人工資，就沒有關於工資的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from background knowledge when the text is silent.","zh":"當文本沒有提及，學生不應憑背景知識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the claim cannot be proved or disproved from the passage.","zh":"這個短語表示該說法不能從文章證明或否定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"officially","meaning":"按官方數字","examples":[{"en":"Officially, manufacturing remains larger than services in China.","zh":"按官方數字，中國製造業仍大於服務業。"},{"en":"Officially means according to formal records, government figures, or authorised statements.","zh":"officially 指根據正式紀錄、政府數字或授權聲明。"},{"en":"Officially, the school day ends at 3:30, although many students stay for activities.","zh":"按官方規定，學校日於3:30結束，雖然許多學生會留下參加活動。"},{"en":"The word can contrast official data with what may be true in reality.","zh":"這個詞可以把官方數據與實際上可能真實的情況作對比。"},{"en":"It signals that the information comes from a formal source.","zh":"它表示資訊來自正式來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"newly discovered GDP","meaning":"新發現的本地生產總值","examples":[{"en":"Some of the newly discovered GDP came from service industries.","zh":"部分新發現的本地生產總值來自服務行業。"},{"en":"Newly discovered GDP means economic output that official statisticians have only recently identified or counted.","zh":"newly discovered GDP 指官方統計人員最近才識別或計算到的經濟產出。"},{"en":"A city may find newly discovered GDP when informal taxi services are added to official figures.","zh":"當非正式的士服務被加入官方數字，城市可能發現新的 GDP。"},{"en":"Newly discovered output can make an economy appear larger than earlier estimates.","zh":"新發現產出可以令經濟看起來比早前估算更大。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to GDP activity that was previously missed.","zh":"這個短語指先前被遺漏的 GDP 活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"education sector","meaning":"教育界","examples":[{"en":"The education sector is part of China’s growing services economy.","zh":"教育界是中國增長中服務型經濟的一部分。"},{"en":"The education sector includes schools, tutoring centres, training companies, books, courses, and learning services.","zh":"education sector 包括學校、補習中心、培訓公司、書籍、課程和學習服務。"},{"en":"A city’s education sector may grow when parents spend more on exam preparation.","zh":"當家長在備考上花更多錢，城市的教育界可能增長。"},{"en":"Education services expand when families and businesses demand more skills.","zh":"當家庭和企業要求更多技能，教育服務會擴張。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to education as an industry.","zh":"這個短語指作為行業的教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"successful outsourcing centre","meaning":"成功的外判服務中心","examples":[{"en":"Dalian is described as a successful outsourcing centre.","zh":"大連被描述為成功的外判服務中心。"},{"en":"A successful outsourcing centre is a place that attracts companies to send work there and completes that work effectively.","zh":"successful outsourcing centre 指吸引公司把工作外判到該地，並有效完成工作的地方。"},{"en":"A city can become a successful outsourcing centre if it has skilled workers, good internet, and reliable offices.","zh":"如果城市有熟練工人、良好網絡和可靠辦公室，它可以成為成功的外判服務中心。"},{"en":"Success in outsourcing can create jobs in software, accounting, reporting, and customer support.","zh":"外判成功可以在軟件、會計、報告和客戶支援方面創造職位。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong location for contracted business services.","zh":"這個短語描述承接商業外判服務的強大地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"as visa restrictions are lowered","meaning":"隨着簽證限制放寬","examples":[{"en":"More mainlanders travel overseas as visa restrictions are lowered.","zh":"隨着簽證限制放寬，更多內地居民到海外旅遊。"},{"en":"As visa restrictions are lowered means while or because entry rules become less strict.","zh":"as visa restrictions are lowered 指當入境規則變得較不嚴格時，或因為它們變得較不嚴格。"},{"en":"More students may join overseas summer camps as visa restrictions are lowered.","zh":"隨着簽證限制放寬，更多學生可能參加海外暑期營。"},{"en":"Easier visa rules reduce barriers and allow more people to travel.","zh":"較容易的簽證規則降低障礙，讓更多人旅遊。"},{"en":"The phrase links policy relaxation with increased travel.","zh":"這個短語把政策放寬與旅遊增加連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"be expected to spend","meaning":"預計會花費","examples":[{"en":"Chinese tourists are expected to spend more on tourism.","zh":"中國旅客預計會在旅遊上花更多錢。"},{"en":"To be expected to spend means people predict that someone will use a certain amount of money.","zh":"be expected to spend 指人們預測某人會使用某個金額。"},{"en":"Families are expected to spend more on school supplies before the new term begins.","zh":"新學期開始前，家庭預計會在學校用品上花更多錢。"},{"en":"Expected spending helps businesses plan stock, staff, and prices.","zh":"預計開支幫助企業規劃存貨、人手和價格。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a forecast about future expenditure.","zh":"這個短語引入關於未來支出的預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"about the same size as","meaning":"大小與……差不多","examples":[{"en":"China’s services sector is about the same size as Japan’s and South Korea’s at a similar stage.","zh":"中國服務業在相似階段的大小與日本和南韓差不多。"},{"en":"About the same size as means approximately equal in size, though not exactly identical.","zh":"about the same size as 指大小大約相等，但不是完全一樣。"},{"en":"This year’s debate club is about the same size as last year’s.","zh":"今年辯論學會大小與去年差不多。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when comparing two figures without claiming perfect equality.","zh":"這個短語適合比較兩個數字，而不聲稱完全相等。"},{"en":"It shows similarity in scale.","zh":"它顯示規模上的相似性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 97 - Are You Being Served?.pdf","sourcePage":24}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 98":[{"front":"experience economy","meaning":"體驗經濟","examples":[{"en":"In the new experience economy, people pay to do things rather than own things.","zh":"在新的體驗經濟中，人們付錢去做事情，而不是擁有東西。"},{"en":"The experience economy is an economy in which people spend money on memorable activities, feelings, and events.","zh":"experience economy 指人們把錢花在難忘活動、感受和事件上的經濟模式。"},{"en":"A family may spend money on a cooking class instead of buying another kitchen appliance.","zh":"一個家庭可能花錢上烹飪班，而不是再買一件廚房電器。"},{"en":"When basic goods become common, consumers may look for experiences that feel personal or special.","zh":"當基本商品變得普遍，消費者可能尋找感覺個人化或特別的體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing a shift from buying products to buying memories.","zh":"討論由購買產品轉向購買回憶時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"how we spend our money","meaning":"我們花錢的方式","examples":[{"en":"How we spend our money is changing.","zh":"我們花錢的方式正在改變。"},{"en":"How we spend our money means the choices we make about buying goods, services, or experiences.","zh":"how we spend our money 指我們在購買商品、服務或體驗時作出的選擇。"},{"en":"A student may spend money on online courses instead of new clothes.","zh":"學生可能把錢花在網上課程，而不是新衣服上。"},{"en":"When people’s income, values, or lifestyle change, their spending choices change too.","zh":"當人們的收入、價值觀或生活方式改變，他們的消費選擇也會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about consumer behaviour.","zh":"討論消費者行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pay to do things","meaning":"付錢去體驗事情","examples":[{"en":"In the experience economy, people pay to do things, not have things.","zh":"在體驗經濟中，人們付錢去體驗事情，而不是擁有東西。"},{"en":"Pay to do things means spend money on activities rather than physical possessions.","zh":"pay to do things 指把錢花在活動上，而不是實體物品上。"},{"en":"A couple may pay to do things like pottery, hiking tours, or dance lessons.","zh":"一對夫婦可能付錢去做陶藝、行山導賞或舞蹈課。"},{"en":"People may choose activities because they create stories to remember later.","zh":"人們可能選擇活動，因為它們創造日後可記住的故事。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when experiences matter more than ownership.","zh":"當體驗比擁有更重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"not have things","meaning":"而不是擁有東西","examples":[{"en":"The new economy values experiences, not simply having things.","zh":"新經濟重視體驗，而不是單純擁有東西。"},{"en":"Not have things means the focus is not on owning material objects.","zh":"not have things 指重點不在於擁有物質物品。"},{"en":"A child may prefer a trip to the zoo, not having another toy at home.","zh":"孩子可能更喜歡去動物園，而不是家中再多一件玩具。"},{"en":"When homes are already full of objects, people may want time, stories, and shared activities instead.","zh":"當家中已充滿物品，人們可能反而想要時間、故事和共同活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting experience with possession.","zh":"對比體驗與擁有時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"advertising supremo","meaning":"廣告界大人物","examples":[{"en":"Trevor Beattie is described as an advertising supremo.","zh":"Trevor Beattie 被描述為廣告界大人物。"},{"en":"An advertising supremo is a highly successful and influential person in the advertising industry.","zh":"advertising supremo 指廣告業中非常成功且有影響力的人。"},{"en":"An advertising supremo may create a campaign that makes a small brand famous overnight.","zh":"廣告界大人物可能創造一個宣傳活動，令小品牌一夜成名。"},{"en":"Such people are valued because they understand attention, emotion, and public reaction.","zh":"這類人受重視，因為他們理解注意力、情感和公眾反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a powerful figure in advertising.","zh":"描述廣告界有權威人物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"earn millions by","meaning":"透過……賺取數百萬","examples":[{"en":"He has earned millions by devising publicity campaigns.","zh":"他透過策劃宣傳活動賺取數百萬。"},{"en":"Earn millions by doing something means make a very large amount of money through that activity.","zh":"earn millions by doing something 指透過某活動賺取非常大量金錢。"},{"en":"A designer may earn millions by creating a popular app used around the world.","zh":"設計師可能透過創造全球使用的熱門應用程式賺取數百萬。"},{"en":"If a skill is rare and valuable, it can bring very high income.","zh":"如果一項技能稀有且有價值，它可以帶來很高收入。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an activity becomes financially successful.","zh":"當某活動帶來財務成功時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"devise publicity campaigns","meaning":"策劃宣傳活動","examples":[{"en":"Beattie earned money by devising original publicity campaigns.","zh":"Beattie 透過策劃原創宣傳活動賺錢。"},{"en":"To devise publicity campaigns means to plan creative ways to attract public attention to a product or idea.","zh":"devise publicity campaigns 指策劃有創意的方法，吸引公眾注意產品或想法。"},{"en":"A charity may devise a publicity campaign to encourage people to donate winter clothes.","zh":"慈善機構可能策劃宣傳活動，鼓勵人們捐出冬衣。"},{"en":"Good campaigns work because they make people notice, remember, and talk about the message.","zh":"好的宣傳活動有效，是因為它令人注意、記得並談論訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing advertising strategy.","zh":"討論廣告策略時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"original and controversial","meaning":"原創而具爭議性","examples":[{"en":"His agency created original and controversial publicity campaigns.","zh":"他的公司創造了原創而具爭議性的宣傳活動。"},{"en":"Original and controversial means new and unusual, but also likely to cause disagreement.","zh":"original and controversial 指新穎不尋常，但也可能引起分歧。"},{"en":"A school poster campaign may be original and controversial if it challenges parents’ old ideas about homework.","zh":"如果學校海報宣傳挑戰家長對功課的舊想法，它可能原創而具爭議性。"},{"en":"Controversy can attract attention, but it can also offend some people.","zh":"爭議可以吸引注意，但也可能冒犯一些人。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when creativity comes with public debate.","zh":"當創意伴隨公共辯論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"publicity campaigns","meaning":"宣傳活動","examples":[{"en":"The agency became known for its publicity campaigns.","zh":"這間公司因其宣傳活動而聞名。"},{"en":"Publicity campaigns are organised efforts to attract attention to a product, event, person, or cause.","zh":"publicity campaigns 指有組織地吸引人注意產品、活動、人物或理念的行動。"},{"en":"A museum may run publicity campaigns before opening a new exhibition.","zh":"博物館可能在新展覽開幕前進行宣傳活動。"},{"en":"Campaigns can increase awareness, shape opinion, and encourage people to act.","zh":"宣傳活動可以提高認知、塑造意見並鼓勵人行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing promotion and public attention.","zh":"討論推廣和公眾注意時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"assemble the logo","meaning":"設計出標誌","examples":[{"en":"His agency assembled the arresting FCUK logo for French Connection.","zh":"他的公司為 French Connection 設計出搶眼的 FCUK 標誌。"},{"en":"To assemble the logo means to design or put together the visual form of a brand symbol.","zh":"assemble the logo 指設計或組合品牌符號的視覺形式。"},{"en":"A design team may assemble the logo by choosing the letters, colours, and spacing carefully.","zh":"設計團隊可能透過仔細選擇字母、顏色和間距來設計標誌。"},{"en":"A strong logo can make a brand easier to recognise and remember.","zh":"強烈的標誌可以令品牌更容易被認出和記住。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing brand design.","zh":"討論品牌設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"arresting logo","meaning":"搶眼的標誌","examples":[{"en":"The FCUK logo was an arresting logo for French Connection.","zh":"FCUK 標誌是 French Connection 的搶眼標誌。"},{"en":"An arresting logo is a logo that immediately catches attention.","zh":"arresting logo 指能立即吸引注意的標誌。"},{"en":"A café with an arresting logo may make people stop and look even before they read the menu.","zh":"有搶眼標誌的咖啡店，可能令人未看餐牌前已停下來看。"},{"en":"A striking logo can increase brand recognition but may also create controversy.","zh":"醒目的標誌可以提高品牌辨識度，但也可能引起爭議。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when visual design strongly attracts attention.","zh":"當視覺設計強烈吸引注意時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"believe in","meaning":"相信；認同","examples":[{"en":"Beattie does not believe in amassing expensive emblems of success.","zh":"Beattie 不認同累積昂貴的成功象徵。"},{"en":"Believe in something means support it, trust it, or think it is the right thing to do.","zh":"believe in something 指支持、信任或認為某事是正確做法。"},{"en":"A teacher may believe in giving students many examples before asking them to write.","zh":"老師可能相信在要求學生寫作前，應先給他們很多例子。"},{"en":"What people believe in affects how they spend time and money.","zh":"人們相信甚麼會影響他們如何花時間和金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing values and choices.","zh":"討論價值觀和選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"amass expensive emblems of success","meaning":"累積昂貴的成功象徵","examples":[{"en":"He does not believe in amassing expensive emblems of success.","zh":"他不認同累積昂貴的成功象徵。"},{"en":"To amass expensive emblems of success means to collect costly objects that show wealth or status.","zh":"amass expensive emblems of success 指收集昂貴物品來展示財富或地位。"},{"en":"A manager may buy designer watches and luxury cars to amass emblems of success.","zh":"經理可能購買名牌手錶和豪華汽車，以累積成功象徵。"},{"en":"Some people prefer experiences because status objects can feel empty or predictable.","zh":"有些人較喜歡體驗，因為地位物品可能感覺空洞或可預測。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when criticising material displays of achievement.","zh":"批評物質化展示成就時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"emblems of success","meaning":"成功象徵","examples":[{"en":"Luxury cars can be seen as emblems of success.","zh":"豪華汽車可以被視為成功象徵。"},{"en":"Emblems of success are objects or signs that people associate with wealth, status, or achievement.","zh":"emblems of success 指人們與財富、地位或成就聯繫起來的物品或標誌。"},{"en":"A corner office, a large house, or an expensive watch may be treated as an emblem of success.","zh":"角落辦公室、大屋或昂貴手錶可能被視為成功象徵。"},{"en":"These symbols can impress others, but they do not always bring satisfaction.","zh":"這些象徵可以令人印象深刻，但不一定帶來滿足。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing status symbols.","zh":"討論地位象徵時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lavish a fortune on","meaning":"在……上揮霍財富","examples":[{"en":"He lavishes his fortune on unusual experiences.","zh":"他在不尋常體驗上揮霍財富。"},{"en":"To lavish a fortune on something means to spend a very large amount of money on it generously or extravagantly.","zh":"lavish a fortune on something 指慷慨或奢侈地在某事上花大量金錢。"},{"en":"A couple may lavish a fortune on a wedding banquet at a luxury hotel.","zh":"一對新人可能在豪華酒店婚宴上揮霍大量金錢。"},{"en":"People lavish money on what they believe will create special memories or status.","zh":"人們會在他們認為能創造特別回憶或地位的事物上花大錢。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when spending is large and emotional.","zh":"當花費巨大且帶有情感時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ephemeral things","meaning":"短暫的事物","examples":[{"en":"He spends money on ephemeral things such as flights in a MiG jet.","zh":"他把錢花在短暫的事物上，例如乘坐米格戰機飛行。"},{"en":"Ephemeral things are things that last only a short time.","zh":"ephemeral things 指只持續短時間的事物。"},{"en":"A concert, a fireworks show, or a special meal can be an ephemeral experience.","zh":"演唱會、煙花表演或特別晚餐都可以是短暫體驗。"},{"en":"Even short-lived experiences can become long-lasting memories.","zh":"即使短暫體驗也可以變成長久回憶。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something temporary is still valuable.","zh":"當某事短暫但仍有價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"flights in a MiG jet","meaning":"乘坐米格戰機飛行","examples":[{"en":"Flights in a MiG jet are examples of expensive experiences.","zh":"乘坐米格戰機飛行是昂貴體驗的例子。"},{"en":"Flights in a MiG jet means paid rides in a powerful military-style aircraft.","zh":"flights in a MiG jet 指付費乘坐強力軍用風格飛機飛行。"},{"en":"A thrill-seeker may choose a flight in a fighter jet instead of buying a luxury watch.","zh":"追求刺激的人可能選擇乘坐戰機飛行，而不是購買名貴手錶。"},{"en":"Such experiences are costly because they are rare, exciting, and difficult to arrange.","zh":"這類體驗昂貴，因為它們罕見、刺激且難以安排。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing extreme experience-based spending.","zh":"描述極端體驗式消費時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"flying his mum on Concorde","meaning":"讓母親乘坐協和式客機","examples":[{"en":"He spent money flying his mum on Concorde.","zh":"他花錢讓母親乘坐協和式客機。"},{"en":"Flying his mum on Concorde means paying for his mother to travel on the famous supersonic aircraft.","zh":"flying his mum on Concorde 指付錢讓母親乘坐著名超音速客機。"},{"en":"A son may choose a special trip for his mother instead of buying her jewellery.","zh":"兒子可能為母親選擇特別旅行，而不是買珠寶給她。"},{"en":"Shared experiences can feel more meaningful than objects because family members remember them together.","zh":"共同體驗可能比物品更有意義，因為家人會一起記住它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when spending money creates a memorable gift.","zh":"當花錢創造難忘禮物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the saddest thing in","meaning":"……中最可悲的事","examples":[{"en":"He says that buying a Porsche is the saddest thing in the history of money.","zh":"他說買一部保時捷是金錢史上最可悲的事。"},{"en":"The saddest thing in something means the most disappointing or emotionally empty example within that area.","zh":"saddest thing in something 指某範疇中最令人失望或情感上最空洞的例子。"},{"en":"A teacher might say wasting talent is the saddest thing in education.","zh":"老師可能說浪費天分是教育中最可悲的事。"},{"en":"This phrase uses exaggeration to show strong criticism.","zh":"這個短語用誇張方式表達強烈批評。"},{"en":"It is useful when someone wants to make a memorable judgement.","zh":"當某人想作出令人難忘的判斷時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in the history of money","meaning":"在金錢史上","examples":[{"en":"He calls buying a Porsche the saddest thing in the history of money.","zh":"他稱買保時捷為金錢史上最可悲的事。"},{"en":"In the history of money means in the whole story of how people have used or spent money.","zh":"in the history of money 指在人類使用或花費金錢的整個歷史中。"},{"en":"A charity leader might call wasting food one of the worst habits in the history of modern consumption.","zh":"慈善領袖可能稱浪費食物是現代消費史上最糟習慣之一。"},{"en":"The phrase is often humorous because it makes a personal opinion sound historically huge.","zh":"這個短語常帶幽默感，因為它把個人意見說得像歷史大事。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when making an exaggerated comment about spending.","zh":"對花錢方式作誇張評論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be not alone in","meaning":"並非唯一……的人","examples":[{"en":"Beattie is not alone in prizing memories above materialism.","zh":"Beattie 並非唯一重視回憶多於物質主義的人。"},{"en":"Be not alone in doing something means other people also do or believe the same thing.","zh":"be not alone in doing something 指其他人也做同樣事情或持同樣信念。"},{"en":"A student is not alone in feeling nervous before public speaking.","zh":"學生在公開演說前感到緊張，並非只有他一個人如此。"},{"en":"Knowing others share the same view can make an attitude seem part of a wider trend.","zh":"知道其他人有相同看法，可以令某態度看似更廣泛趨勢的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one person represents a larger pattern.","zh":"當一個人代表更大模式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"prize A above B","meaning":"重視A多於B","examples":[{"en":"Many people now prize memories above materialism.","zh":"許多人現在重視回憶多於物質主義。"},{"en":"To prize A above B means to value A more highly than B.","zh":"prize A above B 指認為 A 比 B 更有價值。"},{"en":"Some parents prize their children’s happiness above exam results.","zh":"有些父母重視子女快樂多於考試成績。"},{"en":"What people prize most affects how they choose gifts, holidays, and careers.","zh":"人們最重視甚麼會影響他們如何選擇禮物、假期和職業。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing values.","zh":"比較價值觀時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"memories above materialism","meaning":"回憶重於物質主義","examples":[{"en":"The experience economy values memories above materialism.","zh":"體驗經濟重視回憶多於物質主義。"},{"en":"Memories above materialism means experiences and remembered moments are valued more than owning expensive things.","zh":"memories above materialism 指體驗和可記住的時刻比擁有昂貴物品更受重視。"},{"en":"A family may choose a camping trip over a new television because they want shared memories.","zh":"一個家庭可能選擇露營旅行而不是新電視，因為他們想要共同回憶。"},{"en":"When people focus on memories, spending becomes more about stories than status.","zh":"當人們重視回憶，消費就更關乎故事而不是地位。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing anti-materialistic consumer choices.","zh":"描述反物質主義的消費選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a truly special birthday party","meaning":"真正特別的生日派對","examples":[{"en":"A truly special birthday party may now involve a unique experience.","zh":"真正特別的生日派對現在可能涉及獨特體驗。"},{"en":"A truly special birthday party is a celebration that feels memorable, personal, and different from an ordinary party.","zh":"truly special birthday party 指感覺難忘、個人化且不同於普通派對的慶祝活動。"},{"en":"A child may remember a birthday spent at a farm more than a room full of expensive gifts.","zh":"孩子可能更記得在農場度過的生日，而不是一屋昂貴禮物。"},{"en":"Special parties often succeed because guests share activities, surprises, and emotions.","zh":"特別派對常成功，因為賓客共享活動、驚喜和情感。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when celebration is judged by experience, not objects.","zh":"當慶祝由體驗而不是物品來判斷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a Ferrari in a ribbon","meaning":"綁上絲帶的法拉利","examples":[{"en":"A Ferrari in a ribbon is no longer enough for the super-rich.","zh":"對超級富豪來說，綁上絲帶的法拉利已不再足夠。"},{"en":"A Ferrari in a ribbon means a luxury car presented as an expensive gift.","zh":"Ferrari in a ribbon 指作為昂貴禮物呈現的豪華跑車。"},{"en":"A billionaire may find a wrapped sports car less exciting than a private concert.","zh":"億萬富豪可能覺得包裝好的跑車不如私人演唱會刺激。"},{"en":"When luxury goods become familiar, rich consumers may seek rarer experiences instead.","zh":"當奢侈品變得熟悉，富裕消費者可能改為尋找更罕有的體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing that even expensive objects may feel ordinary.","zh":"顯示即使昂貴物品也可能變得普通時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"no longer cut it","meaning":"不再足夠；不再管用","examples":[{"en":"A luxury car will no longer cut it as a special gift.","zh":"豪華汽車作為特別禮物已不再足夠。"},{"en":"No longer cut it means no longer be good enough or impressive enough.","zh":"no longer cut it 指不再夠好或不再令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"For a serious exam, reading notes once will no longer cut it; students need practice tests.","zh":"對重要考試來說，只讀一次筆記已不再管用；學生需要練習試題。"},{"en":"Standards rise when people become used to what once seemed special.","zh":"當人們習慣了昔日特別的東西，標準就會提高。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an old solution is no longer sufficient.","zh":"當舊方法不再足夠時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the super-rich","meaning":"超級富豪","examples":[{"en":"The super-rich may want private concerts or trips into space.","zh":"超級富豪可能想要私人演唱會或太空之旅。"},{"en":"The super-rich are people with extremely large amounts of money.","zh":"super-rich 指擁有極大量金錢的人。"},{"en":"The super-rich may pay for experiences that ordinary people can only imagine.","zh":"超級富豪可能為普通人只能想像的體驗付費。"},{"en":"When money is not a limit, rarity and uniqueness become more important.","zh":"當金錢不是限制，罕有性和獨特性變得更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing extreme wealth.","zh":"討論極端財富時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"private concert","meaning":"私人演唱會","examples":[{"en":"The super-rich may pay for their own private Rolling Stones concert.","zh":"超級富豪可能付錢舉辦自己的 Rolling Stones 私人演唱會。"},{"en":"A private concert is a performance arranged for a specific person or small group, not the general public.","zh":"private concert 指為特定人士或小群體安排，而非向公眾開放的表演。"},{"en":"A company may organise a private concert for important clients at an annual dinner.","zh":"公司可能在周年晚宴為重要客戶安排私人演唱會。"},{"en":"Private concerts feel special because access is limited and personal.","zh":"私人演唱會感覺特別，因為入場機會有限且個人化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing exclusive entertainment.","zh":"描述獨家娛樂時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a trip into space","meaning":"太空之旅","examples":[{"en":"A trip into space is an extreme example of paid experience.","zh":"太空之旅是付費體驗的極端例子。"},{"en":"A trip into space means travelling beyond Earth’s atmosphere, usually as a rare and expensive journey.","zh":"trip into space 指離開地球大氣層旅行，通常是罕有且昂貴的旅程。"},{"en":"A wealthy traveller may choose a trip into space instead of buying another holiday home.","zh":"富裕旅客可能選擇太空之旅，而不是再買一間度假屋。"},{"en":"Space tourism shows how far people may go to purchase unforgettable experiences.","zh":"太空旅遊顯示人們會為購買難忘體驗走到多遠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing luxury experiences beyond ordinary travel.","zh":"討論超越普通旅遊的奢華體驗時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"courtesy of","meaning":"由……提供","examples":[{"en":"A trip into space is available courtesy of Virgin Galactic.","zh":"太空之旅由 Virgin Galactic 提供。"},{"en":"Courtesy of means provided by or made possible by someone or an organisation.","zh":"courtesy of 指由某人或某組織提供或促成。"},{"en":"Free snacks at a school event may be courtesy of a local bakery.","zh":"學校活動中的免費小食可能由本地麵包店提供。"},{"en":"This phrase often gives credit to the provider of a service, gift, or opportunity.","zh":"這個短語常用來感謝服務、禮物或機會的提供者。"},{"en":"It is useful when naming who makes something available.","zh":"說明誰提供某事時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the rest of us","meaning":"我們其他人；一般人","examples":[{"en":"Even the rest of us do not particularly want more stuff.","zh":"即使我們其他人也不特別想要更多物品。"},{"en":"The rest of us means ordinary people other than the group just mentioned.","zh":"the rest of us 指剛才提到的群體以外的普通人。"},{"en":"Billionaires may buy private islands, but the rest of us usually plan cheaper holidays.","zh":"億萬富豪可能買私人島嶼，但我們其他人通常計劃較便宜的假期。"},{"en":"The phrase brings the discussion back from an extreme group to normal people.","zh":"這個短語把討論由極端群體帶回普通人。"},{"en":"It is useful when contrasting elites with everyone else.","zh":"對比精英和其他所有人時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"don’t particularly want","meaning":"並不特別想要","examples":[{"en":"Many consumers do not particularly want more material goods.","zh":"許多消費者並不特別想要更多物質商品。"},{"en":"Don’t particularly want means do not have a strong desire for something.","zh":"don’t particularly want 指對某事沒有強烈渴望。"},{"en":"A student may not particularly want another textbook if they already have enough study materials.","zh":"如果學生已有足夠學習材料，可能並不特別想要另一本課本。"},{"en":"When desire is weak, people may spend money on something more emotionally rewarding.","zh":"當渴望不強，人們可能把錢花在情感上更有回報的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when interest is low but not completely absent.","zh":"當興趣低但並非完全沒有時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"we’d rather","meaning":"我們寧願","examples":[{"en":"We would rather enjoy an experience than buy more things.","zh":"我們寧願享受一種體驗，也不想買更多東西。"},{"en":"We’d rather means we would prefer to do one thing instead of another.","zh":"we’d rather 指我們較想做一件事，而不是另一件事。"},{"en":"We’d rather eat at home tonight than wait in a crowded restaurant.","zh":"我們今晚寧願在家吃飯，也不想在擁擠餐廳等位。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly shows preference between two choices.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示兩個選擇之間的偏好。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining what people value more.","zh":"解釋人們更重視甚麼時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a day at the races","meaning":"賽馬日體驗","examples":[{"en":"Some people would rather enjoy a day at the races.","zh":"有些人寧願享受賽馬日體驗。"},{"en":"A day at the races means spending a day watching horse races and enjoying the atmosphere.","zh":"day at the races 指花一天觀看賽馬並享受現場氣氛。"},{"en":"A group of friends may choose a day at the races as a birthday celebration.","zh":"一群朋友可能選擇賽馬日作為生日慶祝。"},{"en":"Such outings are valued because they mix excitement, social time, and memory.","zh":"這類外出活動受重視，因為它結合刺激、社交時間和回憶。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a paid leisure experience.","zh":"描述付費休閒體驗時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a ride in a hot-air balloon","meaning":"乘坐熱氣球","examples":[{"en":"A ride in a hot-air balloon is part of the experience economy.","zh":"乘坐熱氣球是體驗經濟的一部分。"},{"en":"A ride in a hot-air balloon means travelling through the air in a large balloon basket for enjoyment.","zh":"ride in a hot-air balloon 指為享受而乘坐大型熱氣球吊籃在空中旅行。"},{"en":"A couple may book a hot-air balloon ride to celebrate an anniversary.","zh":"一對夫婦可能預訂熱氣球體驗來慶祝周年紀念。"},{"en":"People pay for this experience because it feels unusual, scenic, and memorable.","zh":"人們為這種體驗付費，因為它感覺不尋常、風景優美且難忘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing leisure activities people buy as experiences.","zh":"描述人們作為體驗購買的休閒活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"weekend cookery course","meaning":"週末烹飪課程","examples":[{"en":"A weekend cookery course can be sold as an experience.","zh":"週末烹飪課程可以作為一種體驗出售。"},{"en":"A weekend cookery course is a short cooking class held over a weekend.","zh":"weekend cookery course 指在週末舉行的短期烹飪課。"},{"en":"Friends may join a weekend cookery course to learn pasta-making together.","zh":"朋友可能一起參加週末烹飪課程，學習製作意大利麵。"},{"en":"Cooking courses create value because people learn, eat, socialise, and remember the activity.","zh":"烹飪課程創造價值，因為人們學習、用餐、社交並記住活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when skills are sold as enjoyable experiences.","zh":"當技能被包裝成愉快體驗出售時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Michelin-starred chef","meaning":"米芝蓮星級廚師","examples":[{"en":"A Michelin-starred chef may run a weekend cookery course.","zh":"米芝蓮星級廚師可能主持週末烹飪課程。"},{"en":"A Michelin-starred chef is a chef whose restaurant has received a Michelin star for high-quality cooking.","zh":"Michelin-starred chef 指其餐廳因高質素烹飪而獲得米芝蓮星級的廚師。"},{"en":"Food lovers may pay more to learn from a Michelin-starred chef than from an ordinary class.","zh":"美食愛好者可能願意付更多錢向米芝蓮星級廚師學習，而不是參加普通課程。"},{"en":"Famous expertise can make an experience feel rare and valuable.","zh":"著名專業能力可以令體驗感覺罕有且有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reputation adds value to food experiences.","zh":"當聲譽為美食體驗增加價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be symptomatic of","meaning":"是……的徵兆","examples":[{"en":"These purchases are symptomatic of the growing experience economy.","zh":"這些購買行為是不斷增長的體驗經濟的徵兆。"},{"en":"Be symptomatic of something means be a sign that a wider condition or trend exists.","zh":"be symptomatic of something 指是某種更廣泛狀況或趨勢存在的跡象。"},{"en":"Long queues outside dessert shops may be symptomatic of a new food trend among young people.","zh":"甜品店外長長人龍可能是年輕人中新飲食潮流的徵兆。"},{"en":"Small consumer choices can reveal larger social changes.","zh":"小小消費選擇可以揭示更大的社會變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an example points to a bigger pattern.","zh":"當例子指向更大模式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"growing experience economy","meaning":"不斷增長的體驗經濟","examples":[{"en":"The growing experience economy reflects changing consumer priorities.","zh":"不斷增長的體驗經濟反映消費者優先次序改變。"},{"en":"The growing experience economy means the expanding market for paid activities, memories, and personal experiences.","zh":"growing experience economy 指付費活動、回憶和個人體驗市場正在擴大。"},{"en":"More escape rooms, cooking classes, and travel packages show a growing experience economy.","zh":"更多密室逃脫、烹飪課和旅遊套票顯示體驗經濟不斷增長。"},{"en":"This growth happens when people have enough goods and want more meaningful activities.","zh":"當人們已有足夠商品並想要更有意義活動，這種增長就會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when experience-based spending is increasing.","zh":"當體驗式消費正在增加時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"evolve out of","meaning":"由……演變而來","examples":[{"en":"The experience economy has evolved out of mass affluence.","zh":"體驗經濟由大眾富裕演變而來。"},{"en":"Evolve out of something means gradually develop from an earlier condition or situation.","zh":"evolve out of something 指從早期條件或情況逐漸發展出來。"},{"en":"A school club may evolve out of a small group of students who meet after class.","zh":"學校學會可能由一小群課後聚會的學生演變而來。"},{"en":"New habits often evolve out of changes in income, technology, or social values.","zh":"新習慣常由收入、科技或社會價值變化演變而來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining origins over time.","zh":"解釋隨時間形成的起源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mass affluence","meaning":"大眾富裕","examples":[{"en":"The experience economy has grown from a culture of mass affluence.","zh":"體驗經濟從大眾富裕的文化中成長起來。"},{"en":"Mass affluence means many people in society have enough money to buy more than basic necessities.","zh":"mass affluence 指社會中許多人有足夠金錢購買超出基本需要的東西。"},{"en":"In a period of mass affluence, ordinary families may afford holidays, restaurants, and entertainment.","zh":"在大眾富裕時期，普通家庭可能負擔得起假期、餐廳和娛樂。"},{"en":"When more people become comfortable financially, consumer demand can shift beyond basic goods.","zh":"當更多人在財政上變得舒適，消費需求可以轉向基本商品以外。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing widespread wealth.","zh":"討論廣泛財富時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"basic needs satisfied","meaning":"基本需要得到滿足","examples":[{"en":"With basic needs satisfied, people become choosier about spending.","zh":"當基本需要得到滿足，人們對花錢變得更挑剔。"},{"en":"Basic needs satisfied means food, shelter, safety, and other essential needs have already been met.","zh":"basic needs satisfied 指食物、住所、安全和其他必要需要已經得到滿足。"},{"en":"After rent and food are covered, a worker may spend extra money on travel or hobbies.","zh":"當租金和食物已有着落，工人可能把額外金錢花在旅行或嗜好上。"},{"en":"When survival needs are met, people can focus more on enjoyment, identity, and meaning.","zh":"當生存需要得到滿足，人們可以更專注於享受、身份和意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why spending moves beyond necessities.","zh":"解釋消費為何超越必需品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"disposable income","meaning":"可支配收入","examples":[{"en":"The disposable income of Britons is double what it was in 1980.","zh":"英國人的可支配收入是1980年的兩倍。"},{"en":"Disposable income is the money people have left to spend or save after necessary payments and taxes.","zh":"disposable income 指人們支付必要開支和稅款後，可用來消費或儲蓄的金錢。"},{"en":"A worker with more disposable income may eat out more often or join a gym.","zh":"可支配收入較高的工人可能更常外出用餐或加入健身會。"},{"en":"Higher disposable income can increase spending on leisure and experiences.","zh":"較高可支配收入可以增加消閒和體驗開支。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing consumer spending power.","zh":"討論消費能力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"double what it was","meaning":"是以往的兩倍","examples":[{"en":"Disposable income is double what it was in 1980.","zh":"可支配收入是1980年的兩倍。"},{"en":"Double what it was means twice as much as before.","zh":"double what it was 指是以前的兩倍。"},{"en":"A shop’s rent may be double what it was ten years ago.","zh":"一間店舖的租金可能是十年前的兩倍。"},{"en":"When income doubles, people may feel freer to spend on non-essential items.","zh":"當收入翻倍，人們可能更自由地花錢在非必需品上。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing present and past amounts.","zh":"比較現在和過去數量時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"increasingly choosy about","meaning":"對……越來越挑剔","examples":[{"en":"Consumers are becoming increasingly choosy about how they spend money.","zh":"消費者對如何花錢變得越來越挑剔。"},{"en":"Increasingly choosy about something means becoming more selective and harder to satisfy over time.","zh":"increasingly choosy about something 指隨時間變得更有選擇性、更難滿足。"},{"en":"Parents may become increasingly choosy about schools if there are many options nearby.","zh":"如果附近有許多選擇，家長可能對學校越來越挑剔。"},{"en":"When people have more choices, they may demand better quality, service, or meaning.","zh":"當人們有更多選擇，他們可能要求更好質素、服務或意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when expectations are rising.","zh":"當期望正在提高時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"rather than upgrading","meaning":"而不是升級……","examples":[{"en":"Rather than upgrading a car, people may spend money on experiences.","zh":"人們可能把錢花在體驗上，而不是升級汽車。"},{"en":"Rather than upgrading means instead of buying a newer or better version of something.","zh":"rather than upgrading 指不是購買某物較新或較好的版本。"},{"en":"Rather than upgrading his phone, a student may save money for a graduation trip.","zh":"學生可能不是升級手機，而是存錢去畢業旅行。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that money is being redirected from possessions to another priority.","zh":"這個短語顯示金錢由物品轉向另一個優先事項。"},{"en":"It is useful when contrasting material improvement with experience.","zh":"對比物質升級和體驗時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"spend the cash in","meaning":"把錢花在……","examples":[{"en":"Consumers spend the cash in restaurants, hotels and sports clubs.","zh":"消費者把錢花在餐廳、酒店和運動會所。"},{"en":"Spend the cash in a place means use available money there.","zh":"spend the cash in a place 指在某地方使用可用金錢。"},{"en":"After getting a bonus, a worker may spend the cash in local cafés and bookshops.","zh":"工人得到花紅後，可能把錢花在本地咖啡店和書店。"},{"en":"Where people spend their cash shows which businesses benefit from changing habits.","zh":"人們把錢花在哪裏，顯示哪些企業受惠於習慣改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing where money flows.","zh":"討論金錢流向時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"coffee shops, hotels and restaurants","meaning":"咖啡店、酒店和餐廳","examples":[{"en":"People spend more money in coffee shops, hotels and restaurants.","zh":"人們在咖啡店、酒店和餐廳花更多錢。"},{"en":"Coffee shops, hotels and restaurants are service businesses that sell places to eat, stay, relax, or socialise.","zh":"coffee shops, hotels and restaurants 指售賣用餐、住宿、放鬆或社交空間的服務業。"},{"en":"A tourist may spend a weekend visiting coffee shops, hotels and restaurants rather than shopping for clothes.","zh":"遊客可能用週末去咖啡店、酒店和餐廳，而不是買衣服。"},{"en":"These businesses benefit when consumers value comfort, atmosphere, and experience.","zh":"當消費者重視舒適、氣氛和體驗，這些企業就會受惠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing spending on services.","zh":"討論服務消費時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sports clubs and theme parks","meaning":"運動會所和主題公園","examples":[{"en":"Sports clubs and theme parks benefit from the experience economy.","zh":"運動會所和主題公園受惠於體驗經濟。"},{"en":"Sports clubs and theme parks are places where people pay for activity, entertainment, fitness, or excitement.","zh":"sports clubs and theme parks 指人們付費進行活動、娛樂、健身或刺激體驗的地方。"},{"en":"A family may choose a theme park visit instead of buying more toys for the children.","zh":"家庭可能選擇參觀主題公園，而不是為孩子買更多玩具。"},{"en":"These places earn money because they provide memories and shared enjoyment.","zh":"這些地方能賺錢，因為它們提供回憶和共同享受。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing leisure businesses.","zh":"討論休閒企業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"splash out on","meaning":"花大錢於……","examples":[{"en":"Consumers splash out on European city breaks.","zh":"消費者花大錢於歐洲城市短途假期。"},{"en":"To splash out on something means to spend a lot of money on it, often as a treat.","zh":"splash out on something 指花很多錢在某事上，通常作為犒賞。"},{"en":"A student may splash out on a concert ticket after finishing exams.","zh":"學生完成考試後，可能花大錢買演唱會門票。"},{"en":"People often splash out when they think the experience will be rare or rewarding.","zh":"當人們認為體驗罕有或值得，他們常會花大錢。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing enjoyable but expensive spending.","zh":"描述愉快但昂貴的消費時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"European city breaks","meaning":"歐洲城市短途假期","examples":[{"en":"People may spend money on European city breaks.","zh":"人們可能花錢去歐洲城市短途假期。"},{"en":"European city breaks are short holidays in European cities, usually lasting a few days.","zh":"European city breaks 指在歐洲城市度過的短假期，通常只有幾天。"},{"en":"A couple may take a city break in Prague or Paris for food, museums, and walking tours.","zh":"一對夫婦可能到布拉格或巴黎短途旅行，享受食物、博物館和步行導賞。"},{"en":"Cheap flights and online booking make short city breaks easier to arrange.","zh":"廉價航班和網上預訂令城市短途假期更容易安排。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing short leisure trips.","zh":"討論短期休閒旅行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"walk the Inca Trail","meaning":"徒步走印加古道","examples":[{"en":"Some consumers splash out on walking the Inca Trail.","zh":"有些消費者花大錢徒步走印加古道。"},{"en":"To walk the Inca Trail means to hike the famous route in Peru leading toward Machu Picchu.","zh":"walk the Inca Trail 指徒步行走秘魯通往馬丘比丘的著名路線。"},{"en":"A traveller may spend months saving money to walk the Inca Trail with friends.","zh":"旅客可能儲錢幾個月，和朋友一起走印加古道。"},{"en":"People pay for such trips because the challenge and scenery create strong memories.","zh":"人們為這類旅行付費，因為挑戰和風景創造強烈回憶。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when travel itself is the purchased experience.","zh":"當旅行本身就是被購買的體驗時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in other words","meaning":"換句話說","examples":[{"en":"Experiences, in other words, are increasingly important.","zh":"換句話說，體驗變得越來越重要。"},{"en":"In other words means saying the same idea again in a clearer or simpler way.","zh":"in other words 指用更清楚或更簡單的方式重述同一想法。"},{"en":"He spends more on lessons than gadgets; in other words, he values skills over objects.","zh":"他花更多錢在課程而不是電子產品上；換句話說，他重視技能多於物件。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain a point again so readers understand the meaning.","zh":"這個短語幫助再次解釋重點，讓讀者理解意思。"},{"en":"It is useful when restating an idea.","zh":"重述想法時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as a proportion of","meaning":"佔……的比例","examples":[{"en":"Retail spending has fallen as a proportion of consumer spending.","zh":"零售開支佔消費開支的比例下降了。"},{"en":"As a proportion of means as a share or percentage of a larger total.","zh":"as a proportion of 指作為較大總數中的份額或百分比。"},{"en":"Rent may rise as a proportion of a family’s income if wages stay the same.","zh":"如果工資不變，租金佔家庭收入的比例可能上升。"},{"en":"A category can fall in proportion even if the actual amount spent does not fall.","zh":"即使實際花費沒有下降，某類別佔比也可以下降。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing shares of a total.","zh":"討論總額中的比例時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"consumer spending","meaning":"消費開支","examples":[{"en":"Retail goods now take a smaller share of consumer spending.","zh":"零售商品現在佔消費開支的較小份額。"},{"en":"Consumer spending is the money people spend on goods and services.","zh":"consumer spending 指人們花在商品和服務上的金錢。"},{"en":"Consumer spending may rise before holidays when families buy gifts and book meals.","zh":"假期前，家庭購買禮物和預訂餐廳，消費開支可能上升。"},{"en":"Changes in consumer spending show what people value and what businesses may grow.","zh":"消費開支的變化顯示人們重視甚麼，以及哪些企業可能增長。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the economy and buying habits.","zh":"討論經濟和購買習慣時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"go down","meaning":"下降","examples":[{"en":"Spending on retail goods has gone down as a proportion of total spending.","zh":"零售商品開支佔總開支的比例下降了。"},{"en":"Go down means decrease, fall, or become lower.","zh":"go down 指減少、下跌或變低。"},{"en":"A student’s stress may go down after they finish the hardest exam.","zh":"學生完成最難考試後，壓力可能下降。"},{"en":"Spending may go down when people choose cheaper options or shift money elsewhere.","zh":"當人們選擇較便宜選項或把錢轉到其他地方，開支可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a decrease.","zh":"描述減少時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the past ten years","meaning":"在過去十年","examples":[{"en":"Consumer spending patterns have changed in the past ten years.","zh":"消費開支模式在過去十年已經改變。"},{"en":"In the past ten years means during the most recent decade being discussed.","zh":"in the past ten years 指在所討論的最近十年期間。"},{"en":"In the past ten years, many students have started using online learning tools.","zh":"在過去十年，許多學生開始使用網上學習工具。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show that a change is recent rather than ancient.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示變化是近期的，而不是古代的。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing modern trends.","zh":"描述現代趨勢時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"migrate to","meaning":"轉移到……","examples":[{"en":"Money has migrated to restaurants, leisure and budget travel.","zh":"金錢已轉移到餐廳、消閒活動和廉價旅遊。"},{"en":"Migrate to means move from one place, area, or category to another.","zh":"migrate to 指由一個地方、範疇或類別移到另一個。"},{"en":"Students’ attention may migrate to videos if textbooks feel too difficult.","zh":"如果課本太難，學生注意力可能轉移到影片。"},{"en":"When spending migrates, some businesses grow while others lose customers.","zh":"當開支轉移，有些企業增長，另一些則失去顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when money, people, or attention shifts direction.","zh":"當金錢、人或注意力改變方向時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"leisure","meaning":"消閒活動","examples":[{"en":"More money has moved into leisure and travel.","zh":"更多金錢已流向消閒活動和旅遊。"},{"en":"Leisure means free-time activities done for rest, enjoyment, or personal interest.","zh":"leisure 指為休息、享受或個人興趣而進行的空閒時間活動。"},{"en":"Reading, hiking, gaming, swimming, and meeting friends can all be leisure activities.","zh":"閱讀、行山、打機、游泳和見朋友都可以是消閒活動。"},{"en":"When income rises, people often spend more on leisure because basic needs are already met.","zh":"當收入上升，人們常在基本需要已滿足後，把更多錢花在消閒活動上。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing non-work time.","zh":"討論非工作時間時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"budget travel","meaning":"廉價旅遊","examples":[{"en":"Budget travel has benefited from changes in consumer spending.","zh":"廉價旅遊受惠於消費開支變化。"},{"en":"Budget travel means travelling with low costs, often using cheap flights, simple hotels, or careful planning.","zh":"budget travel 指低成本旅遊，常使用廉價航班、簡單酒店或仔細規劃。"},{"en":"Students may choose budget travel so they can visit more cities with limited money.","zh":"學生可能選擇廉價旅遊，以有限金錢到訪更多城市。"},{"en":"Cheap travel options make experiences available to more ordinary consumers.","zh":"便宜旅遊選項令更多普通消費者能獲得體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing affordable tourism.","zh":"討論可負擔旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"acquisitional pursuit","meaning":"以獲取物品為目的的活動","examples":[{"en":"Shopping is described as an acquisitional pursuit.","zh":"購物被描述為以獲取物品為目的的活動。"},{"en":"An acquisitional pursuit is an activity focused on getting or owning things.","zh":"acquisitional pursuit 指集中於取得或擁有東西的活動。"},{"en":"Collecting designer shoes can become an acquisitional pursuit if the main goal is ownership.","zh":"如果主要目標是擁有，收集名牌鞋可以變成以獲取物品為目的的活動。"},{"en":"In the experience economy, shopping must offer more than simply acquiring products.","zh":"在體驗經濟中，購物必須提供不只是取得產品的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when criticising buying as mere possession.","zh":"批評購買只是為了擁有時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"wake up to","meaning":"意識到；醒覺到","examples":[{"en":"Shopping has had to wake up to the experience economy.","zh":"購物業不得不意識到體驗經濟。"},{"en":"Wake up to something means finally notice or understand an important change or reality.","zh":"wake up to something 指終於注意到或明白重要變化或現實。"},{"en":"Schools may wake up to students’ mental health needs after many report stress.","zh":"當許多學生表示有壓力，學校可能醒覺到學生心理健康需要。"},{"en":"Businesses that wake up late to a trend may lose customers to faster competitors.","zh":"對趨勢醒覺太遲的企業，可能把顧客輸給反應較快的競爭者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone becomes aware after delay.","zh":"當某人延遲後才意識到某事時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"shopping malls","meaning":"商場","examples":[{"en":"Shopping malls are changing their role in the experience economy.","zh":"商場正在體驗經濟中改變自己的角色。"},{"en":"Shopping malls are large indoor or partly indoor places with many shops, restaurants, and services.","zh":"shopping malls 指有許多商店、餐廳和服務的大型室內或半室內場所。"},{"en":"A family may spend a whole afternoon at a shopping mall eating, watching a film, and browsing shops.","zh":"一個家庭可能在商場花整個下午吃飯、看電影和逛店。"},{"en":"Malls add entertainment because buying goods alone may no longer attract enough visitors.","zh":"商場加入娛樂，因為單靠購買商品可能不再足以吸引訪客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing modern retail spaces.","zh":"討論現代零售空間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"acknowledge the arrival of","meaning":"承認……的到來","examples":[{"en":"Bluewater has acknowledged the arrival of the experience economy.","zh":"Bluewater 已承認體驗經濟的到來。"},{"en":"To acknowledge the arrival of something means to recognise that a new trend or situation has begun.","zh":"acknowledge the arrival of something 指承認一個新趨勢或情況已經開始。"},{"en":"A school may acknowledge the arrival of AI by teaching students how to use it responsibly.","zh":"學校可能透過教學生負責任地使用人工智能，承認人工智能時代的到來。"},{"en":"Recognising a change early helps organisations adapt before they fall behind.","zh":"及早認識變化有助組織在落後前適應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an institution accepts a new reality.","zh":"當機構接受新現實時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"restyle themselves as","meaning":"將自己重新定位為……","examples":[{"en":"Some shopping malls have restyled themselves as family destinations.","zh":"有些商場已將自己重新定位為家庭目的地。"},{"en":"To restyle themselves as something means to change their image or identity to fit a new role.","zh":"restyle themselves as something 指改變自身形象或身份，以配合新角色。"},{"en":"A library may restyle itself as a community learning hub rather than just a place for books.","zh":"圖書館可能把自己重新定位為社區學習中心，而不只是藏書地方。"},{"en":"Businesses restyle themselves when old images no longer attract customers.","zh":"當舊形象不再吸引顧客，企業就會重新定位自己。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when organisations reposition their public identity.","zh":"當組織重新塑造公眾身份時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"destinations for a family day out","meaning":"家庭一日遊目的地","examples":[{"en":"Shopping malls are becoming destinations for a family day out.","zh":"商場正成為家庭一日遊目的地。"},{"en":"Destinations for a family day out are places where families can spend several hours relaxing and doing activities together.","zh":"destinations for a family day out 指家庭可以花數小時一起放鬆和活動的地方。"},{"en":"A park with cafés, playgrounds, and events can become a destination for a family day out.","zh":"有咖啡店、遊樂場和活動的公園可以成為家庭一日遊目的地。"},{"en":"Places attract families when they offer food, entertainment, comfort, and safety together.","zh":"當地方同時提供食物、娛樂、舒適和安全，就能吸引家庭。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when retail spaces are treated like leisure venues.","zh":"當零售空間被視為休閒場地時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"browse, dine and take in a film","meaning":"瀏覽商店、用餐和看電影","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can browse, dine and take in a film at the mall.","zh":"訪客可以在商場瀏覽商店、用餐和看電影。"},{"en":"Browse, dine and take in a film means look around shops, eat a meal, and watch a movie.","zh":"browse, dine and take in a film 指逛店、吃飯和看一場電影。"},{"en":"Friends may go to a mall after school to browse, dine, and take in a film.","zh":"朋友放學後可能去商場瀏覽商店、用餐和看電影。"},{"en":"Combining activities makes a shopping trip feel like a fuller experience.","zh":"結合活動令購物行程感覺像更完整的體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a place offers several leisure options.","zh":"當一個地方提供多種休閒選項時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take in a film","meaning":"看一場電影","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can take in a film during a shopping trip.","zh":"訪客可以在購物行程中看一場電影。"},{"en":"To take in a film means to watch a movie, usually as part of a leisure outing.","zh":"take in a film 指看一部電影，通常作為休閒外出的一部分。"},{"en":"A family may take in a film after dinner at the mall.","zh":"一家人可能在商場晚飯後看一場電影。"},{"en":"Adding a film can turn a short shopping visit into a full afternoon activity.","zh":"加入電影可以把短暫購物變成整個下午的活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when movie-watching is part of a broader outing.","zh":"當看電影是更大外出活動的一部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"shopping is optional","meaning":"購物只是選擇之一","examples":[{"en":"At some malls, shopping is optional.","zh":"在有些商場，購物只是選擇之一。"},{"en":"Shopping is optional means visitors can enjoy the place without necessarily buying goods.","zh":"shopping is optional 指訪客可以享受該地方，而不一定要購買商品。"},{"en":"A teenager may go to a mall only to meet friends, eat, and watch a film.","zh":"青少年可能去商場只是為了見朋友、吃飯和看電影。"},{"en":"When shopping is optional, the mall becomes a leisure destination rather than just a retail centre.","zh":"當購物只是選擇之一，商場就變成休閒目的地，而不只是零售中心。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when buying is only one possible activity.","zh":"當購買只是可能活動之一時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"recognise the trend","meaning":"認識到這個趨勢","examples":[{"en":"Marks & Spencer recognises the trend towards experiential shopping.","zh":"Marks & Spencer 認識到體驗式購物的趨勢。"},{"en":"To recognise the trend means to notice and understand a pattern of change.","zh":"recognise the trend 指注意並理解一種變化模式。"},{"en":"A school may recognise the trend toward online learning and train teachers in digital tools.","zh":"學校可能認識到網上學習趨勢，並訓練老師使用數碼工具。"},{"en":"Businesses that recognise trends early can adapt products and services more quickly.","zh":"及早認識趨勢的企業，可以更快調整產品和服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when organisations respond to changing behaviour.","zh":"當組織回應行為變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"put coffee shops and bookshops in stores","meaning":"在店內設咖啡店和書店","examples":[{"en":"Retailers put coffee shops and bookshops in their stores.","zh":"零售商在店內設咖啡店和書店。"},{"en":"To put coffee shops and bookshops in stores means to add leisure spaces inside retail shops.","zh":"put coffee shops and bookshops in stores 指在零售店內加入休閒空間。"},{"en":"A department store may add a café so customers stay longer and feel more relaxed.","zh":"百貨公司可能加入咖啡店，讓顧客逗留更久並感覺更放鬆。"},{"en":"Extra experiences can increase customer time in the store and encourage spending.","zh":"額外體驗可以增加顧客在店內時間，並鼓勵消費。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when shops mix retail with leisure.","zh":"當商店把零售和休閒結合時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"end up taking home","meaning":"最後帶回家","examples":[{"en":"The shopping experience matters as much as what customers end up taking home.","zh":"購物體驗和顧客最後帶回家的東西同樣重要。"},{"en":"End up taking home means finally leave with or buy something after an activity.","zh":"end up taking home 指在活動後最終帶走或購買某物。"},{"en":"A customer may enjoy the bookstore café even if they end up taking home only one notebook.","zh":"顧客即使最後只帶走一本筆記簿，也可能享受書店咖啡店。"},{"en":"In experiential retail, the feeling during the visit can matter as much as the product purchased.","zh":"在體驗式零售中，到訪期間的感覺可以和購買的產品同樣重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the final purchase is only part of the value.","zh":"當最終購買只是價值的一部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be first predicted in","meaning":"最早在……被預測","examples":[{"en":"The experience economy was first predicted in a Harvard Business Review article.","zh":"體驗經濟最早在一篇《哈佛商業評論》文章中被預測。"},{"en":"Be first predicted in means be first described as a future development in a particular source.","zh":"be first predicted in 指某未來發展最早在某來源中被描述。"},{"en":"A new education trend may be first predicted in a research report before schools adopt it.","zh":"新教育趨勢可能最早在研究報告中被預測，然後學校才採用。"},{"en":"Early predictions can shape how businesses prepare for future change.","zh":"早期預測可以塑造企業如何準備未來變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when tracing where an idea first appeared.","zh":"追溯想法最早在哪裏出現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Harvard Business Review","meaning":"《哈佛商業評論》","examples":[{"en":"The idea appeared in an article in the Harvard Business Review.","zh":"這個想法出現在《哈佛商業評論》的一篇文章中。"},{"en":"Harvard Business Review is a well-known publication that discusses management, business strategy, and leadership.","zh":"Harvard Business Review 是討論管理、商業策略和領導力的知名刊物。"},{"en":"A manager may read Harvard Business Review to learn about customer experience and innovation.","zh":"經理可能閱讀《哈佛商業評論》，學習顧客體驗和創新。"},{"en":"Ideas published there can influence how companies think about markets and consumers.","zh":"在該刊物發表的想法可以影響公司如何看待市場和消費者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when referring to business writing.","zh":"提及商業寫作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"business consultant","meaning":"商業顧問","examples":[{"en":"James Gilmore is an American business consultant.","zh":"James Gilmore 是一位美國商業顧問。"},{"en":"A business consultant is a professional who advises companies on strategy, management, or improvement.","zh":"business consultant 指就策略、管理或改善向公司提供建議的專業人士。"},{"en":"A small shop may hire a business consultant to improve customer service and pricing.","zh":"小店可能聘請商業顧問改善顧客服務和定價。"},{"en":"Consultants are useful when outside advice helps a company see problems more clearly.","zh":"當外部建議幫助公司更清楚看見問題，顧問就有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing people who advise businesses.","zh":"描述為企業提供建議的人時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"advocate","meaning":"提倡；主張","examples":[{"en":"Gilmore advocates sleep deprivation as an idea booster.","zh":"Gilmore 提倡把睡眠不足作為激發意念的方法。"},{"en":"To advocate something means to publicly support or recommend it.","zh":"advocate something 指公開支持或推薦某事。"},{"en":"A doctor may advocate regular exercise as part of a healthier lifestyle.","zh":"醫生可能提倡把定期運動作為健康生活方式的一部分。"},{"en":"People advocate ideas when they believe those ideas will bring useful results.","zh":"當人們相信某想法會帶來有用結果，他們就會提倡它。"},{"en":"This word is useful when someone strongly supports a practice or policy.","zh":"當某人強烈支持某做法或政策時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sleep deprivation","meaning":"睡眠不足","examples":[{"en":"Gilmore advocates sleep deprivation as an idea booster.","zh":"Gilmore 提倡把睡眠不足作為激發意念的方法。"},{"en":"Sleep deprivation means not getting enough sleep.","zh":"sleep deprivation 指沒有得到足夠睡眠。"},{"en":"A student may suffer sleep deprivation after staying up late for several nights before exams.","zh":"學生考試前連續幾晚熬夜後，可能受睡眠不足影響。"},{"en":"Sleep deprivation can make people tired, emotional, and less able to concentrate.","zh":"睡眠不足可以令人疲倦、情緒化並較難集中。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the effects of lack of sleep.","zh":"討論缺乏睡眠的影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"idea booster","meaning":"激發意念的方法","examples":[{"en":"Sleep deprivation is described as an idea booster.","zh":"睡眠不足被描述為激發意念的方法。"},{"en":"An idea booster is something that helps people produce more ideas or think more creatively.","zh":"idea booster 指幫助人產生更多想法或更有創意地思考的東西。"},{"en":"A group discussion can be an idea booster when students are stuck on a project.","zh":"當學生在專題上卡住，小組討論可以是激發意念的方法。"},{"en":"Different boosters work for different people, such as music, walking, or quiet time.","zh":"不同方法適合不同人，例如音樂、散步或安靜時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something stimulates creativity.","zh":"當某物刺激創意時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be expanded into","meaning":"被擴展成","examples":[{"en":"The idea was later expanded into a book.","zh":"這個想法後來被擴展成一本書。"},{"en":"Be expanded into means be developed from a smaller idea or piece of writing into a larger form.","zh":"be expanded into 指由較小想法或文字發展成較大形式。"},{"en":"A short classroom speech may be expanded into a full essay.","zh":"一篇短課堂演講可以被擴展成完整文章。"},{"en":"Expansion allows writers to add examples, arguments, stories, and evidence.","zh":"擴展讓作者加入例子、論點、故事和證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an idea grows into a bigger work.","zh":"當想法成長為較大作品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"posit that","meaning":"提出；假定","examples":[{"en":"The book posits that we are in the middle of an economic shift.","zh":"這本書提出我們正處於經濟轉變之中。"},{"en":"To posit that means to state an idea or theory as something to consider or accept.","zh":"posit that 指提出某個想法或理論，讓人考慮或接受。"},{"en":"A researcher may posit that shorter lessons improve attention among young students.","zh":"研究人員可能提出較短課堂能改善年幼學生專注力。"},{"en":"This verb is often used when presenting a serious argument or theory.","zh":"這個動詞常用於呈現嚴肅論點或理論。"},{"en":"It is useful in academic or business writing.","zh":"它適用於學術或商業寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the middle of","meaning":"正處於……之中","examples":[{"en":"The book argues that we are in the middle of a profound economic shift.","zh":"這本書主張我們正處於深遠的經濟轉變之中。"},{"en":"In the middle of means currently experiencing or surrounded by a process, event, or situation.","zh":"in the middle of 指目前正在經歷或身處某過程、事件或情況之中。"},{"en":"A student in the middle of exam season may have little time for hobbies.","zh":"正處於考試季的學生可能很少有時間做嗜好。"},{"en":"When people are in the middle of a change, the final result may still be unclear.","zh":"當人們正處於變化之中，最終結果可能仍不清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is happening now, not already finished.","zh":"當某事正在發生而尚未完成時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"profound economic shift","meaning":"深遠的經濟轉變","examples":[{"en":"The experience economy represents a profound economic shift.","zh":"體驗經濟代表深遠的經濟轉變。"},{"en":"A profound economic shift is a deep and important change in how an economy works.","zh":"profound economic shift 指經濟運作方式上的深層而重要變化。"},{"en":"Moving from cash payments to digital wallets can be part of a profound economic shift.","zh":"由現金付款轉向電子錢包，可以是深遠經濟轉變的一部分。"},{"en":"Such shifts change business models, jobs, consumer habits, and expectations.","zh":"這類轉變會改變商業模式、工作、消費習慣和期望。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an economic change is major rather than minor.","zh":"當經濟變化重大而非輕微時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"just as","meaning":"正如","examples":[{"en":"Just as we moved from goods to services, we are now moving to experiences.","zh":"正如我們由商品轉向服務，現在也正在轉向體驗。"},{"en":"Just as means in the same way that or similar to the way something else happened.","zh":"just as 指以與另一件事相同或相似的方式。"},{"en":"Just as students need practice in writing, they also need practice in speaking.","zh":"正如學生需要寫作練習，他們也需要口語練習。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a comparison between two similar patterns.","zh":"這個短語在兩個相似模式之間建立比較。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining a new change by referring to an earlier one.","zh":"透過早前變化解釋新變化時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"move from A to B","meaning":"從A轉向B","examples":[{"en":"Society moved from a goods economy to a service economy.","zh":"社會由商品經濟轉向服務經濟。"},{"en":"Move from A to B means shift from one stage, place, system, or focus to another.","zh":"move from A to B 指由一個階段、地方、系統或重點轉向另一個。"},{"en":"A student may move from memorising phrases to creating their own sentences.","zh":"學生可能由背誦短語轉向創作自己的句子。"},{"en":"Moving from one stage to another often requires new skills and habits.","zh":"從一個階段轉向另一個階段，通常需要新技能和新習慣。"},{"en":"This structure is useful when describing change over time.","zh":"描述隨時間發生的變化時，這個結構很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"goods economy","meaning":"商品經濟","examples":[{"en":"The book describes a shift away from a goods economy.","zh":"這本書描述由商品經濟轉離的變化。"},{"en":"A goods economy is an economy mainly based on producing and selling physical products.","zh":"goods economy 指主要以生產和銷售實體產品為基礎的經濟。"},{"en":"Factories, supermarkets, and furniture shops are important in a goods economy.","zh":"工廠、超級市場和家具店在商品經濟中很重要。"},{"en":"When consumers already own many goods, companies may need to offer services or experiences instead.","zh":"當消費者已擁有許多商品，公司可能需要改為提供服務或體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing economic stages.","zh":"討論經濟階段時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"service economy","meaning":"服務經濟","examples":[{"en":"The service economy is being replaced by the experience economy.","zh":"服務經濟正在被體驗經濟取代。"},{"en":"A service economy is an economy mainly based on providing services rather than making goods.","zh":"service economy 指主要以提供服務而不是製造商品為基礎的經濟。"},{"en":"Banks, hotels, repair shops, tutors, and delivery companies are part of a service economy.","zh":"銀行、酒店、維修店、補習老師和速遞公司都是服務經濟的一部分。"},{"en":"Services become central when people pay for help, convenience, expertise, or care.","zh":"當人們為幫助、便利、專業知識或照顧付費，服務就變得核心。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing economic development beyond manufacturing.","zh":"討論製造業以外的經濟發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"shift from A to B","meaning":"由A轉向B","examples":[{"en":"We are shifting from a service economy to an experience economy.","zh":"我們正由服務經濟轉向體驗經濟。"},{"en":"Shift from A to B means gradually change from one thing to another.","zh":"shift from A to B 指逐漸由一件事轉向另一件事。"},{"en":"A school may shift from paper notices to online messages.","zh":"學校可能由紙本通告轉向網上訊息。"},{"en":"A shift often happens when old methods no longer fit people’s needs.","zh":"當舊方法不再符合人們需要，轉變常會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a broad transition.","zh":"描述廣泛過渡時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"accordingly","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"Accordingly, companies need to offer experiences to stand out.","zh":"因此，公司需要提供體驗以突圍而出。"},{"en":"Accordingly means as a result of what has just been said.","zh":"accordingly 指作為剛才所說事情的結果。"},{"en":"The class struggled with grammar; accordingly, the teacher added more practice lessons.","zh":"全班文法吃力；因此，老師加入更多練習課。"},{"en":"This word links a conclusion or action to an earlier reason.","zh":"這個詞把結論或行動與早前原因連接起來。"},{"en":"It is useful in formal explanations of cause and response.","zh":"在正式因果和回應解釋中，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stand out in the marketplace","meaning":"在市場上突圍而出","examples":[{"en":"Companies need experiences to stand out in the marketplace.","zh":"公司需要體驗來在市場上突圍而出。"},{"en":"To stand out in the marketplace means to be noticed by customers among many competing businesses.","zh":"stand out in the marketplace 指在眾多競爭企業中被顧客注意到。"},{"en":"A small café may stand out in the marketplace by offering live music and friendly service.","zh":"小咖啡店可能透過現場音樂和友善服務在市場上突圍而出。"},{"en":"If many products look similar, experience can become the reason customers choose one brand.","zh":"如果許多產品看起來相似，體驗可以成為顧客選擇某品牌的原因。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing competition and differentiation.","zh":"討論競爭和差異化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"offer not just…but…","meaning":"不只提供……而且提供……","examples":[{"en":"Companies need to offer not just goods and services but experiences.","zh":"公司需要不只提供商品和服務，而且提供體驗。"},{"en":"Offer not just A but B means provide B in addition to A, often because B is more important or surprising.","zh":"offer not just A but B 指除了 A 之外還提供 B，通常因為 B 更重要或更令人意外。"},{"en":"Good schools offer not just exam training but confidence, curiosity, and support.","zh":"好學校不只提供考試訓練，而且提供信心、好奇心和支援。"},{"en":"This structure highlights that the second element adds extra value.","zh":"這個結構突出第二項增加額外價值。"},{"en":"It is useful when expanding an idea beyond the obvious.","zh":"把想法擴展到明顯內容以外時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"mere suppliers","meaning":"純粹的供應商","examples":[{"en":"Companies are no longer mere suppliers.","zh":"公司不再只是純粹的供應商。"},{"en":"Mere suppliers are businesses that only provide products or services without creating a wider experience.","zh":"mere suppliers 指只提供產品或服務，而不創造更廣泛體驗的企業。"},{"en":"A bookstore is a mere supplier if it only sells books and offers no advice, events, or atmosphere.","zh":"如果書店只賣書，沒有建議、活動或氣氛，它就是純粹供應商。"},{"en":"In the experience economy, companies must do more than simply hand over goods.","zh":"在體驗經濟中，公司必須做得比單純交付商品更多。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting basic supply with richer customer experience.","zh":"對比基本供應和更豐富顧客體驗時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stagers of events","meaning":"活動策劃者；體驗製造者","examples":[{"en":"Companies are becoming stagers of events designed to be experienced.","zh":"公司正成為策劃可供體驗活動的體驗製造者。"},{"en":"Stagers of events are people or organisations that arrange experiences for others to take part in.","zh":"stagers of events 指安排體驗讓他人參與的人或組織。"},{"en":"A toy shop becomes a stager of events when it holds games, shows, and workshops for children.","zh":"當玩具店為兒童舉辦遊戲、表演和工作坊，它就成為活動策劃者。"},{"en":"Businesses stage events to create emotion, attention, and stronger customer memory.","zh":"企業策劃活動以創造情感、注意力和更強顧客記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when companies act like experience designers.","zh":"當公司像體驗設計者般行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"designed to be experienced","meaning":"被設計成可供體驗","examples":[{"en":"Retail events are designed to be experienced by consumers.","zh":"零售活動被設計成可供消費者體驗。"},{"en":"Designed to be experienced means created so people can feel, do, join, or remember something directly.","zh":"designed to be experienced 指被創造出來讓人直接感受、行動、參與或記住。"},{"en":"A museum room with sounds, lights, and objects to touch is designed to be experienced.","zh":"有聲音、燈光和可觸摸物件的博物館房間，就是被設計成可供體驗。"},{"en":"Direct participation can make a place more memorable than simple viewing or buying.","zh":"直接參與可以令地方比單純觀看或購買更難忘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when design focuses on feeling and participation.","zh":"當設計聚焦感受和參與時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"prove the point","meaning":"證明這一點","examples":[{"en":"The newest retail stores prove the point.","zh":"最新的零售店證明這一點。"},{"en":"To prove the point means to show that an argument or claim is true.","zh":"prove the point 指顯示某個論點或說法是真。"},{"en":"A student’s improved marks prove the point that regular practice works.","zh":"學生成績改善證明定期練習有效這一點。"},{"en":"Concrete examples make an argument more convincing than theory alone.","zh":"具體例子比單靠理論更能令論點有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence supports a claim.","zh":"當證據支持說法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"flagship store","meaning":"旗艦店","examples":[{"en":"The flagship Toys “R” Us shop is in Times Square.","zh":"Toys “R” Us 的旗艦店位於時代廣場。"},{"en":"A flagship store is a brand’s most important or most impressive store.","zh":"flagship store 指一個品牌最重要或最令人印象深刻的店舖。"},{"en":"A fashion brand may open a flagship store in a famous shopping district to show its image.","zh":"時裝品牌可能在著名購物區開旗艦店，以展示品牌形象。"},{"en":"Flagship stores often include special design, events, and experiences to attract attention.","zh":"旗艦店常包括特別設計、活動和體驗，以吸引注意。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing brand display and retail strategy.","zh":"討論品牌展示和零售策略時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Times Square","meaning":"時代廣場","examples":[{"en":"The flagship Toys “R” Us store is located in Times Square.","zh":"Toys “R” Us 旗艦店位於時代廣場。"},{"en":"Times Square is a famous commercial and entertainment area in New York City.","zh":"Times Square 指紐約市著名的商業和娛樂區。"},{"en":"A brand may choose Times Square for a flagship store because millions of visitors pass through it.","zh":"品牌可能選擇時代廣場開旗艦店，因為數以百萬計訪客會經過。"},{"en":"A famous location can make a shop feel more exciting and visible.","zh":"著名位置可以令店舖感覺更刺激和更顯眼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing high-profile retail locations.","zh":"討論高曝光零售地點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pile ’em high, sell ’em cheap","meaning":"大量堆貨、廉價銷售","examples":[{"en":"The store is not a “pile ’em high, sell ’em cheap” emporium.","zh":"這間店不是一間「大量堆貨、廉價銷售」的大型商店。"},{"en":"Pile ’em high, sell ’em cheap describes a shop strategy of stacking many products and selling them at low prices.","zh":"pile ’em high, sell ’em cheap 描述把大量商品堆起並以低價出售的商店策略。"},{"en":"A discount warehouse may pile goods high and sell them cheap to attract bargain hunters.","zh":"折扣貨倉可能大量堆貨、廉價銷售，以吸引尋找便宜貨的人。"},{"en":"This approach focuses on price and volume, not atmosphere or experience.","zh":"這種做法專注價格和數量，而不是氣氛或體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting cheap mass retail with experiential retail.","zh":"對比廉價大量零售和體驗式零售時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"emporium","meaning":"大型商店","examples":[{"en":"The store is more than a simple retail emporium.","zh":"這間店不只是簡單的大型零售商店。"},{"en":"An emporium is a large shop or store selling many kinds of goods.","zh":"emporium 指售賣多種類商品的大型商店。"},{"en":"A city-centre emporium may sell toys, clothes, stationery, and gifts under one roof.","zh":"市中心大型商店可能在同一屋簷下售賣玩具、衣服、文具和禮物。"},{"en":"In the experience economy, a large store may need attractions as well as products.","zh":"在體驗經濟中，大型商店除了產品，可能還需要景點。"},{"en":"This word is useful when describing a big retail space.","zh":"描述大型零售空間時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be immersed in","meaning":"沉浸於……","examples":[{"en":"Visitors are immersed in the Toys “R” Us experience.","zh":"訪客沉浸於 Toys “R” Us 的體驗之中。"},{"en":"Be immersed in something means be deeply surrounded by or involved in it.","zh":"be immersed in something 指被某事深深包圍或投入其中。"},{"en":"Children may be immersed in a science museum when they can touch exhibits and try experiments.","zh":"當孩子可以觸摸展品和做實驗，他們可能沉浸於科學博物館。"},{"en":"Immersion makes an experience stronger because people feel part of it.","zh":"沉浸感令體驗更強，因為人們覺得自己是其中一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an environment fully captures attention.","zh":"當環境完全吸引注意時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"encounter the Ferris wheel","meaning":"遇見摩天輪","examples":[{"en":"Visitors encounter the Ferris wheel at the front door.","zh":"訪客在正門遇見摩天輪。"},{"en":"To encounter the Ferris wheel means to come across or see the large rotating ride as part of the visit.","zh":"encounter the Ferris wheel 指在到訪過程中碰見或看見大型旋轉遊樂設施。"},{"en":"Children may encounter a giant display as soon as they enter a toy shop.","zh":"孩子一進玩具店就可能遇見巨型展示。"},{"en":"An unexpected attraction at the entrance can immediately create excitement.","zh":"入口處意想不到的景點可以立即創造興奮感。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when visitors meet a striking feature inside a place.","zh":"當訪客在地方內遇到搶眼特色時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at the front door","meaning":"在正門","examples":[{"en":"The Ferris wheel is placed at the front door.","zh":"摩天輪被放在正門。"},{"en":"At the front door means at or near the main entrance of a building or place.","zh":"at the front door 指在建築物或地方的主要入口處或附近。"},{"en":"A school may place welcome signs at the front door for new students.","zh":"學校可能在正門放置歡迎新生的標誌。"},{"en":"Things placed at the entrance shape visitors’ first impression.","zh":"放在入口的東西會塑造訪客第一印象。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing where something is positioned.","zh":"描述某物位置時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"other attractions include","meaning":"其他景點包括","examples":[{"en":"Other attractions include a Barbie house and an animatronic dinosaur.","zh":"其他景點包括 Barbie 屋和電動仿真恐龍。"},{"en":"Other attractions include means additional interesting features are part of the place or event.","zh":"other attractions include 指某地方或活動還有其他有趣特色。"},{"en":"Other attractions at the fair include food stalls, games, and a music stage.","zh":"嘉年華其他景點包括小食攤、遊戲和音樂舞台。"},{"en":"Adding more attractions gives visitors more reasons to stay longer.","zh":"加入更多景點給訪客更多理由逗留更久。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when listing extra features.","zh":"列出額外特色時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"two floors designed as","meaning":"兩層被設計成……","examples":[{"en":"Two floors are designed as a Barbie house.","zh":"兩層被設計成 Barbie 屋。"},{"en":"Two floors designed as something means two levels of a building are arranged to look or function like that thing.","zh":"two floors designed as something 指建築物兩層被安排成看起來或功能上像某物。"},{"en":"A museum may have two floors designed as an old village to help children learn history.","zh":"博物館可能有兩層被設計成舊村莊，幫助孩子學習歷史。"},{"en":"Large themed spaces make visitors feel they have entered another world.","zh":"大型主題空間令訪客感覺進入另一個世界。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing immersive design.","zh":"描述沉浸式設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"animatronic dinosaur","meaning":"電動仿真恐龍","examples":[{"en":"The store includes an animatronic dinosaur.","zh":"店內有一隻電動仿真恐龍。"},{"en":"An animatronic dinosaur is a mechanical dinosaur model that can move or make sounds.","zh":"animatronic dinosaur 指能移動或發聲的機械恐龍模型。"},{"en":"A theme park may use an animatronic dinosaur to make children feel as if the animal is alive.","zh":"主題公園可能使用電動仿真恐龍，令孩子感覺動物好像活着。"},{"en":"Moving displays create excitement because they feel more real than ordinary decorations.","zh":"會動的展示品令人興奮，因為它們比普通裝飾更真實。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when technology is used to create an attraction.","zh":"當科技被用來創造景點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"shoppers are called guests","meaning":"購物者被稱為賓客","examples":[{"en":"Shoppers are called guests in the new retail environment.","zh":"在新的零售環境中，購物者被稱為賓客。"},{"en":"Shoppers are called guests means customers are treated and described like visitors being hosted.","zh":"shoppers are called guests 指顧客被當作受款待訪客般對待和稱呼。"},{"en":"A hotel-style shop may call shoppers guests to make the service feel warmer.","zh":"酒店式商店可能稱購物者為賓客，令服務感覺更溫暖。"},{"en":"Language can change how staff behave and how customers feel.","zh":"語言可以改變員工行為和顧客感受。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when retail becomes more like hospitality.","zh":"當零售變得更像款客服務時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"foster an emotional attachment","meaning":"培養情感連繫","examples":[{"en":"The idea is to foster an emotional attachment between company and consumer.","zh":"這個想法是培養公司與消費者之間的情感連繫。"},{"en":"To foster an emotional attachment means to encourage a strong feeling of connection or loyalty.","zh":"foster an emotional attachment 指促進強烈連繫感或忠誠感。"},{"en":"A school can foster emotional attachment by making students feel known and supported.","zh":"學校可以透過令學生感到被認識和支持來培養情感連繫。"},{"en":"Customers who feel emotionally attached may return even when cheaper options exist.","zh":"有情感連繫的顧客即使有較便宜選項，也可能回來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when businesses try to build loyalty through feeling.","zh":"當企業嘗試透過感情建立忠誠時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"emotional attachment","meaning":"情感依附；情感連繫","examples":[{"en":"Companies want to create an emotional attachment with consumers.","zh":"公司想與消費者建立情感連繫。"},{"en":"Emotional attachment is a strong feeling of connection, affection, or loyalty toward someone or something.","zh":"emotional attachment 指對某人或某物有強烈連繫、喜愛或忠誠感。"},{"en":"A child may have an emotional attachment to an old toy because it reminds them of home.","zh":"孩子可能對舊玩具有情感依附，因為它令他想起家。"},{"en":"Brands build emotional attachment when customers connect them with happy memories.","zh":"當顧客把品牌與快樂回憶連接，品牌就建立了情感連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when feelings influence choices.","zh":"當感情影響選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"company and consumer","meaning":"公司與消費者","examples":[{"en":"The experience builds a bond between company and consumer.","zh":"這種體驗建立公司與消費者之間的連繫。"},{"en":"Company and consumer means the business and the person who buys or uses its products.","zh":"company and consumer 指企業和購買或使用其產品的人。"},{"en":"A friendly return policy can improve the relationship between company and consumer.","zh":"友善的退貨政策可以改善公司與消費者之間的關係。"},{"en":"Good experiences make consumers trust a company more deeply.","zh":"良好體驗令消費者更深入信任公司。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing business relationships.","zh":"討論商業關係時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"acquire a memento","meaning":"購買紀念品","examples":[{"en":"Guests may want to acquire a memento of the experience.","zh":"賓客可能想購買該體驗的紀念品。"},{"en":"To acquire a memento means to get or buy a small object that helps remember an event.","zh":"acquire a memento 指取得或購買一件幫助記住事件的小物件。"},{"en":"A tourist may acquire a memento such as a postcard after visiting a museum.","zh":"遊客參觀博物館後，可能購買明信片作紀念品。"},{"en":"Mementos matter because they connect a physical object with a memory.","zh":"紀念品重要，因為它把實體物件與回憶連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when souvenirs preserve experiences.","zh":"當紀念品保存體驗時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"remind someone of","meaning":"使某人想起……","examples":[{"en":"A memento reminds consumers of the experience.","zh":"紀念品使消費者想起那次體驗。"},{"en":"To remind someone of something means to make them remember it.","zh":"remind someone of something 指令某人記起某事。"},{"en":"A seashell on a desk may remind someone of a family beach holiday.","zh":"書桌上的貝殼可能使某人想起家庭海灘假期。"},{"en":"Objects connected with happy moments can bring those memories back later.","zh":"與快樂時刻相關的物件可以在日後帶回那些回憶。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something triggers memory.","zh":"當某物觸發記憶時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"warm fuzzy feelings","meaning":"溫暖愉快的感覺","examples":[{"en":"Consumers may buy products linked to warm fuzzy feelings.","zh":"消費者可能購買與溫暖愉快感覺相關的產品。"},{"en":"Warm fuzzy feelings are pleasant, comforting emotions that make people feel happy, safe, or affectionate.","zh":"warm fuzzy feelings 指令人感到快樂、安全或有愛意的愉快安慰情緒。"},{"en":"A childhood snack may give someone warm fuzzy feelings because it reminds them of family meals.","zh":"童年零食可能給人溫暖愉快感覺，因為它令人想起家庭飯局。"},{"en":"Brands use these feelings to make products seem more personal and lovable.","zh":"品牌利用這些感覺，使產品顯得更個人化和可愛。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when buying is driven by emotion.","zh":"當購買由情感推動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the hippest companies of the moment","meaning":"當下最時髦的公司","examples":[{"en":"Starbucks and Apple are among the hippest companies of the moment.","zh":"Starbucks 和 Apple 是當下最時髦的公司之一。"},{"en":"The hippest companies of the moment are the companies currently seen as fashionable, modern, and culturally attractive.","zh":"hippest companies of the moment 指目前被視為時尚、現代且有文化吸引力的公司。"},{"en":"Young consumers may talk about the hippest companies because their shops feel stylish and social.","zh":"年輕消費者可能談論最時髦的公司，因為它們的店感覺有格調和社交性。"},{"en":"Being hip can help a company charge more and attract loyal customers.","zh":"時髦形象可以幫助公司收取較高價格並吸引忠誠顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing fashionable brands.","zh":"描述時尚品牌時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"on a smaller scale","meaning":"規模較小地","examples":[{"en":"Innocent is admired on a smaller scale.","zh":"Innocent 以較小規模受到欣賞。"},{"en":"On a smaller scale means in a smaller size, amount, or level of influence.","zh":"on a smaller scale 指以較小大小、數量或影響層面。"},{"en":"A school fair can copy a theme park on a smaller scale with games and food stalls.","zh":"學校嘉年華可以用遊戲和小食攤，以較小規模模仿主題公園。"},{"en":"Smaller scale does not mean unimportant; it simply affects fewer people or uses fewer resources.","zh":"規模較小不代表不重要；它只是影響較少人或使用較少資源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing size or reach.","zh":"比較大小或影響範圍時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be admired within","meaning":"在……中受到欣賞","examples":[{"en":"These companies are admired within the business industry.","zh":"這些公司在商業界中受到欣賞。"},{"en":"Be admired within a group means be respected or looked up to by people in that field.","zh":"be admired within a group 指受到某領域人士尊重或仰慕。"},{"en":"A teacher may be admired within a school for helping weak students improve.","zh":"老師可能因幫助弱學生進步而在學校中受到欣賞。"},{"en":"Admiration within an industry can strengthen reputation and attract talent.","zh":"在行業內受到欣賞可以加強聲譽並吸引人才。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when respect comes from insiders.","zh":"當尊重來自圈內人士時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ability to connect emotionally with","meaning":"與……建立情感連繫的能力","examples":[{"en":"Successful brands connect emotionally with their consumers.","zh":"成功品牌能與消費者建立情感連繫。"},{"en":"Ability to connect emotionally with someone means the skill of creating feelings of trust, belonging, or affection.","zh":"ability to connect emotionally with someone 指創造信任、歸屬或喜愛感的能力。"},{"en":"A teacher’s ability to connect emotionally with students can make them feel safer in class.","zh":"老師與學生建立情感連繫的能力，可以令學生在課堂中感覺更安全。"},{"en":"Emotional connection can make people loyal even when cheaper options exist.","zh":"情感連繫可以令人忠誠，即使有較便宜選項。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when feelings strengthen relationships.","zh":"當感情加強關係時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"connect emotionally with consumers","meaning":"與消費者建立情感連繫","examples":[{"en":"Starbucks and Apple connect emotionally with consumers.","zh":"Starbucks 和 Apple 與消費者建立情感連繫。"},{"en":"To connect emotionally with consumers means to make customers feel a personal bond with a brand.","zh":"connect emotionally with consumers 指令顧客對品牌產生個人連繫。"},{"en":"A café may connect emotionally with consumers by remembering regular customers’ names.","zh":"咖啡店可能透過記住熟客名字來與消費者建立情感連繫。"},{"en":"Emotional connection can turn ordinary purchases into habits and identity statements.","zh":"情感連繫可以把普通購買變成習慣和身份表達。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when brands create loyalty through feeling.","zh":"當品牌透過感情創造忠誠時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pay a premium","meaning":"付出較高價格","examples":[{"en":"People will pay a premium to buy into a company’s world.","zh":"人們會付出較高價格來投入某公司的品牌世界。"},{"en":"Pay a premium means pay more than the basic or usual price.","zh":"pay a premium 指付出比基本或一般價格更高的價錢。"},{"en":"A customer may pay a premium for a hotel room with a sea view.","zh":"顧客可能為海景酒店房支付較高價格。"},{"en":"People pay extra when they believe quality, identity, service, or experience is better.","zh":"當人們相信質素、身份、服務或體驗更好，就會額外付費。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when higher prices are accepted.","zh":"當人們接受較高價格時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"buy into their world","meaning":"投入／認同其品牌世界","examples":[{"en":"Consumers pay more to buy into a brand’s world.","zh":"消費者付更多錢來投入某品牌的世界。"},{"en":"To buy into their world means to accept, join, or emotionally identify with a brand’s lifestyle and values.","zh":"buy into their world 指接受、加入或情感上認同品牌的生活方式和價值。"},{"en":"A teenager may buy into a sports brand’s world because it represents confidence and energy.","zh":"青少年可能投入某運動品牌的世界，因為它代表自信和活力。"},{"en":"Brands build worlds through design, language, shops, events, and community.","zh":"品牌透過設計、語言、店舖、活動和社群建立自己的世界。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when buying is also about identity.","zh":"當購買也關乎身份認同時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fruit smoothie","meaning":"水果沙冰","examples":[{"en":"An Innocent fruit smoothie costs more than a non-branded smoothie.","zh":"Innocent 水果沙冰比無品牌沙冰貴。"},{"en":"A fruit smoothie is a thick drink made by blending fruit, juice, milk, or yoghurt.","zh":"fruit smoothie 指把水果、果汁、牛奶或乳酪攪拌而成的濃稠飲品。"},{"en":"A student may buy a fruit smoothie after exercise instead of a fizzy drink.","zh":"學生運動後可能買水果沙冰，而不是汽水。"},{"en":"Branded smoothies may cost more because of packaging, image, and perceived quality.","zh":"有品牌沙冰可能因包裝、形象和被感知的質素而更貴。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing food products and branding.","zh":"討論食品和品牌時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"non-branded smoothie","meaning":"無品牌沙冰","examples":[{"en":"A non-branded smoothie costs less than an Innocent smoothie.","zh":"無品牌沙冰比 Innocent 沙冰便宜。"},{"en":"A non-branded smoothie is a smoothie sold without a famous brand name attached to it.","zh":"non-branded smoothie 指沒有著名品牌名稱的沙冰。"},{"en":"A small café may sell a non-branded smoothie made fresh behind the counter.","zh":"小咖啡店可能售賣在櫃台後即場製作的無品牌沙冰。"},{"en":"Without a strong brand image, the price may depend more on ingredients and location.","zh":"沒有強烈品牌形象時，價格可能更取決於材料和地點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing branded and unbranded products.","zh":"比較有品牌和無品牌產品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"magazine reviews of","meaning":"關於……的雜誌評論","examples":[{"en":"Magazine reviews of the iPod often criticise its price.","zh":"關於 iPod 的雜誌評論常批評其價格。"},{"en":"Magazine reviews of something are written evaluations published in magazines about that product or subject.","zh":"magazine reviews of something 指雜誌中對某產品或主題的書面評價。"},{"en":"Magazine reviews of restaurants may discuss food, service, price, and atmosphere.","zh":"關於餐廳的雜誌評論可能討論食物、服務、價格和氣氛。"},{"en":"Reviews influence consumers because they frame what is good or bad before people buy.","zh":"評論會影響消費者，因為它們在人們購買前界定甚麼好或不好。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing media evaluation.","zh":"討論媒體評價時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"battery life","meaning":"電池續航力","examples":[{"en":"Reviews often criticise the iPod’s battery life.","zh":"評論常批評 iPod 的電池續航力。"},{"en":"Battery life is the length of time a device can work before it needs charging again.","zh":"battery life 指裝置再次需要充電前可以運作的時間長度。"},{"en":"A student may choose a laptop with long battery life for a full day at school.","zh":"學生可能選擇電池續航力長的手提電腦，以應付整天上課。"},{"en":"Poor battery life can make a device inconvenient even if its design is attractive.","zh":"即使設計吸引，電池續航力差也會令裝置不方便。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing electronic products.","zh":"討論電子產品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"exorbitant price tag","meaning":"過高的標價","examples":[{"en":"The iPod was criticised for its exorbitant price tag.","zh":"iPod 因其過高標價而受到批評。"},{"en":"An exorbitant price tag is a price that seems unreasonably high.","zh":"exorbitant price tag 指看似不合理地高的價格。"},{"en":"A simple school bag with an exorbitant price tag may make parents choose a cheaper brand.","zh":"如果一個普通書包標價過高，家長可能選擇較便宜品牌。"},{"en":"High prices can be accepted only if customers believe the design, status, or experience is worth it.","zh":"只有當顧客相信設計、地位或體驗值得，高價才可能被接受。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when criticising expensive products.","zh":"批評昂貴產品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"inevitably forgiving","meaning":"難免寬容","examples":[{"en":"Reviewers are inevitably forgiving because of the iPod’s design.","zh":"評論者因 iPod 的設計而難免較寬容。"},{"en":"Inevitably forgiving means people naturally excuse faults because something else is attractive or impressive.","zh":"inevitably forgiving 指人們因另一方面吸引或令人印象深刻，自然地原諒缺點。"},{"en":"Parents may be forgiving of a child’s messy room if the child has been studying hard all week.","zh":"如果孩子整星期都努力溫習，父母可能對凌亂房間較寬容。"},{"en":"Strong design can make reviewers overlook weaknesses such as price or battery life.","zh":"強烈設計可以令評論者忽略價格或電池續航等弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when admiration softens criticism.","zh":"當欣賞軟化批評時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"iconic design","meaning":"標誌性設計","examples":[{"en":"The iPod is praised for its iconic design.","zh":"iPod 因其標誌性設計而受讚賞。"},{"en":"Iconic design is design that is easily recognised and strongly associated with a brand, product, or period.","zh":"iconic design 指容易被認出，並與某品牌、產品或時期強烈聯繫的設計。"},{"en":"A chair with iconic design may still be recognised decades after it was made.","zh":"有標誌性設計的椅子在製成數十年後仍可能被認出。"},{"en":"Iconic design can make customers love a product even when it has practical weaknesses.","zh":"標誌性設計可以令顧客喜愛產品，即使它有實用缺點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when design becomes a symbol.","zh":"當設計變成象徵時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"enduring affection for","meaning":"對……持久的喜愛","examples":[{"en":"Consumers show enduring affection for Apple’s image.","zh":"消費者對 Apple 的形象有持久喜愛。"},{"en":"Enduring affection for something means long-lasting liking or emotional attachment to it.","zh":"enduring affection for something 指對某事持久的喜歡或情感依附。"},{"en":"Many adults have enduring affection for cartoons they watched as children.","zh":"許多成年人對童年看的卡通片有持久喜愛。"},{"en":"Long-term affection helps brands survive criticism and competition.","zh":"長期喜愛幫助品牌承受批評和競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when emotional loyalty lasts over time.","zh":"當情感忠誠隨時間持續時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"perceived ability to","meaning":"被認為有能力去……","examples":[{"en":"Apple is admired for its perceived ability to do things differently.","zh":"Apple 因被認為有能力以不同方式做事而受欣賞。"},{"en":"Perceived ability to do something means the ability people believe someone or something has.","zh":"perceived ability to do something 指人們相信某人或某物具有的能力。"},{"en":"A school may attract parents because of its perceived ability to help shy students speak confidently.","zh":"學校可能因被認為有能力幫助害羞學生自信說話而吸引家長。"},{"en":"Perception matters because consumers may act on belief even before seeing proof.","zh":"感知很重要，因為消費者可能在看到證據前已按信念行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reputation influences judgement.","zh":"當聲譽影響判斷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"do things differently","meaning":"以不同方式做事","examples":[{"en":"Apple is seen as a company that does things differently.","zh":"Apple 被視為一間以不同方式做事的公司。"},{"en":"To do things differently means to use a method or style that is not the usual one.","zh":"do things differently 指使用不同於慣常做法的方法或風格。"},{"en":"A teacher may do things differently by teaching grammar through games and real conversations.","zh":"老師可能透過遊戲和真實對話教文法，以不同方式做事。"},{"en":"Different methods can make a brand or person seem creative and memorable.","zh":"不同方法可以令品牌或人物顯得有創意且令人記得。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing innovation or originality.","zh":"描述創新或原創性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"online concierge","meaning":"網上禮賓服務","examples":[{"en":"Apple visitors can use an online concierge to plan their trip.","zh":"Apple 訪客可以使用網上禮賓服務計劃行程。"},{"en":"An online concierge is a digital service that helps customers arrange visits, appointments, or support.","zh":"online concierge 指幫助顧客安排到訪、預約或支援的數碼服務。"},{"en":"A hotel may offer an online concierge so guests can book taxis and restaurant tables before arrival.","zh":"酒店可能提供網上禮賓服務，讓住客到達前預訂的士和餐廳。"},{"en":"Such services make customers feel guided rather than left alone.","zh":"這類服務令顧客感到有人引導，而不是被留下自己處理。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when online tools provide personalised assistance.","zh":"當網上工具提供個人化協助時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"plan their trip","meaning":"計劃行程","examples":[{"en":"The online concierge helps customers plan their trip.","zh":"網上禮賓服務幫助顧客計劃行程。"},{"en":"To plan their trip means to organise details such as time, transport, route, activities, or appointments.","zh":"plan their trip 指安排時間、交通、路線、活動或預約等細節。"},{"en":"A family may plan their trip by checking train times, ticket prices, and restaurant options.","zh":"家庭可能透過查火車時間、票價和餐廳選項來計劃行程。"},{"en":"Good planning can make a visit smoother and less stressful.","zh":"良好規劃可以令到訪更順暢、壓力更少。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when arranging a journey or visit.","zh":"安排行程或到訪時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"progressive companies","meaning":"進步的公司","examples":[{"en":"Progressive companies have embraced the hospitality concept.","zh":"進步的公司已接受款客服務概念。"},{"en":"Progressive companies are businesses that are open to new ideas and modern ways of working.","zh":"progressive companies 指願意接受新想法和現代工作方式的企業。"},{"en":"A progressive company may allow flexible work hours if it improves staff well-being.","zh":"如果彈性工作時間能改善員工身心健康，進步公司可能容許它。"},{"en":"Such companies adapt quickly because they notice changes in society and customers.","zh":"這類公司適應得快，因為它們注意社會和顧客的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing forward-looking businesses.","zh":"描述具前瞻性的企業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"buy fully into","meaning":"完全接受；完全投入","examples":[{"en":"Progressive companies have bought fully into the hospitality concept.","zh":"進步的公司已完全接受款客服務概念。"},{"en":"To buy fully into an idea means to accept and support it completely.","zh":"buy fully into an idea 指完全接受並支持某想法。"},{"en":"A school buys fully into project-based learning when every subject uses projects.","zh":"當每科都使用專題，學校就是完全投入專題式學習。"},{"en":"Full acceptance usually leads to real changes in behaviour, design, and spending.","zh":"完全接受通常會帶來行為、設計和開支上的真實改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when commitment is strong, not partial.","zh":"當承諾強烈而非部分接受時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hospitality concept","meaning":"款客服務概念","examples":[{"en":"Apple’s stores show the importance of the hospitality concept.","zh":"Apple 的店舖顯示款客服務概念的重要性。"},{"en":"The hospitality concept means treating customers like guests and making them feel welcomed, helped, and comfortable.","zh":"hospitality concept 指把顧客當作賓客款待，令他們感到受歡迎、被幫助和舒適。"},{"en":"A bank may use the hospitality concept by offering clear guidance and comfortable waiting areas.","zh":"銀行可能透過提供清晰指引和舒適等候區來使用款客服務概念。"},{"en":"Hospitality can change a store from a sales space into a place customers enjoy visiting.","zh":"款客服務可以把店舖由銷售空間變成顧客享受到訪的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when service feels like careful hosting.","zh":"當服務感覺像細心款待時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"conveyor belt of","meaning":"源源不絕的……","examples":[{"en":"The conveyor belt of business publishing reflects interest in customer experience.","zh":"商業出版源源不絕的作品反映人們對顧客體驗的興趣。"},{"en":"A conveyor belt of something means a continuous stream or steady production of similar things.","zh":"conveyor belt of something 指同類事物連續不斷地出現或被生產。"},{"en":"Exam season can bring a conveyor belt of assignments, quizzes, and revision tasks.","zh":"考試季可以帶來源源不絕的功課、測驗和溫習任務。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that many items are being produced one after another.","zh":"這個短語暗示許多項目一個接一個被製造出來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when output seems constant and repeated.","zh":"當產出持續且重複時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"business publishing","meaning":"商業出版","examples":[{"en":"Business publishing has produced many books on customer experience.","zh":"商業出版已產生許多關於顧客體驗的書。"},{"en":"Business publishing is the field of producing books, articles, and reports about business ideas and management.","zh":"business publishing 指出版關於商業理念和管理的書籍、文章和報告的領域。"},{"en":"Managers may follow business publishing to learn about leadership, branding, and consumer trends.","zh":"經理可能關注商業出版，以學習領導、品牌和消費趨勢。"},{"en":"Popular business books can spread new ideas quickly through companies.","zh":"受歡迎的商業書籍可以在公司之間快速傳播新想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing business-related books and media.","zh":"討論商業相關書籍和媒體時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"attest to","meaning":"證明；表明","examples":[{"en":"Business books attest to the importance of customer experience.","zh":"商業書籍證明顧客體驗的重要性。"},{"en":"To attest to something means to show, prove, or give evidence that it is true.","zh":"attest to something 指顯示、證明或提供證據說明某事為真。"},{"en":"Long queues outside a restaurant attest to its popularity.","zh":"餐廳外的長龍證明它很受歡迎。"},{"en":"Repeated examples can make a trend easier to believe.","zh":"重複出現的例子可以令趨勢更容易被相信。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something serves as evidence.","zh":"當某事物作為證據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"increasing importance of","meaning":"……日益增加的重要性","examples":[{"en":"These books attest to the increasing importance of the customer experience.","zh":"這些書證明顧客體驗日益增加的重要性。"},{"en":"Increasing importance of something means it is becoming more significant over time.","zh":"increasing importance of something 指某事隨時間變得更重要。"},{"en":"The increasing importance of digital skills has changed what schools teach.","zh":"數碼技能日益增加的重要性改變了學校教授的內容。"},{"en":"When something becomes more important, organisations usually spend more attention and money on it.","zh":"當某事變得更重要，組織通常會投入更多注意力和金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a trend is gaining influence.","zh":"當趨勢正在獲得影響力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"customer experience","meaning":"顧客體驗","examples":[{"en":"Customer experience has become central to business strategy.","zh":"顧客體驗已成為商業策略的核心。"},{"en":"Customer experience is how customers feel and what they go through when dealing with a company.","zh":"customer experience 指顧客與公司接觸時的感受和經歷。"},{"en":"A customer’s experience includes the shop layout, staff attitude, payment process, and after-sales support.","zh":"顧客體驗包括店舖佈局、員工態度、付款過程和售後支援。"},{"en":"Good customer experience can make people return even if prices are not the lowest.","zh":"良好顧客體驗可以令人回頭光顧，即使價格不是最低。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing service, loyalty, and brand image.","zh":"討論服務、忠誠和品牌形象時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"groundbreaking offering","meaning":"開創性的作品","examples":[{"en":"Pine and Gilmore’s book was a groundbreaking offering.","zh":"Pine 和 Gilmore 的書是一部開創性的作品。"},{"en":"A groundbreaking offering is a new work, product, or idea that changes how people think about a field.","zh":"groundbreaking offering 指改變人們如何看待某領域的新作品、產品或想法。"},{"en":"A teaching app may be a groundbreaking offering if it changes how students practise speaking.","zh":"如果一個教學應用程式改變學生練習口語的方式，它可能是開創性作品。"},{"en":"Groundbreaking work matters because others often copy, debate, or build on it.","zh":"開創性作品重要，因為其他人常會模仿、討論或在其基礎上發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is innovative and influential.","zh":"當某物具創新性和影響力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be followed by","meaning":"隨後出現","examples":[{"en":"Their book was followed by many similar business books.","zh":"他們的書隨後出現許多類似商業書籍。"},{"en":"Be followed by means come after something in time or sequence.","zh":"be followed by 指在時間或次序上接着某事出現。"},{"en":"A school talk may be followed by a question-and-answer session.","zh":"學校講座之後可能接着問答環節。"},{"en":"Successful ideas often lead to many later versions or responses.","zh":"成功想法常帶來許多後來版本或回應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing what comes next.","zh":"描述接下來發生甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tomes","meaning":"大部頭著作","examples":[{"en":"The subject produced such tomes as books on extraordinary experiences.","zh":"這個主題產生了關於非凡體驗等大部頭著作。"},{"en":"Tomes are large, serious, and often heavy books.","zh":"tomes 指大型、嚴肅且通常厚重的書。"},{"en":"A university library may contain tomes on law, medicine, and history.","zh":"大學圖書館可能有關於法律、醫學和歷史的大部頭著作。"},{"en":"Calling a book a tome can suggest it is long, detailed, or difficult to read.","zh":"稱一本書為 tome 可以暗示它很長、詳細或難讀。"},{"en":"This word is useful when describing substantial books.","zh":"描述厚重書籍時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"required reading","meaning":"指定讀物；必讀材料","examples":[{"en":"One book became required reading at IBM and Pizza Hut.","zh":"有一本書成為 IBM 和 Pizza Hut 的指定讀物。"},{"en":"Required reading is material that people are expected or told to read.","zh":"required reading 指人們被期望或被要求閱讀的材料。"},{"en":"A teacher may make a short story required reading before a literature lesson.","zh":"老師可能把一篇短篇故事列為文學課前必讀材料。"},{"en":"A book becomes required reading when an organisation thinks its ideas are important.","zh":"當組織認為一本書的想法重要，它就可能成為指定讀物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reading is officially expected.","zh":"當閱讀被正式要求時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ordinary products","meaning":"普通產品","examples":[{"en":"Companies try to turn ordinary products into extraordinary experiences.","zh":"公司嘗試把普通產品變成非凡體驗。"},{"en":"Ordinary products are normal everyday goods that do not seem special by themselves.","zh":"ordinary products 指本身看起來不特別的普通日常商品。"},{"en":"A notebook is an ordinary product, but a shop can make buying it feel special through design and service.","zh":"筆記簿是普通產品，但商店可以透過設計和服務令購買它感覺特別。"},{"en":"Experience design can add emotional value to simple goods.","zh":"體驗設計可以為簡單商品增加情感價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when basic items are made more attractive.","zh":"當基本物品被變得更吸引時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"extraordinary experiences","meaning":"非凡體驗","examples":[{"en":"Some books explain how to create extraordinary experiences.","zh":"有些書解釋如何創造非凡體驗。"},{"en":"Extraordinary experiences are experiences that feel unusual, memorable, and more impressive than normal activities.","zh":"extraordinary experiences 指感覺不尋常、難忘並比普通活動更令人印象深刻的體驗。"},{"en":"A restaurant may create an extraordinary experience through food, lighting, music, and personal service.","zh":"餐廳可能透過食物、燈光、音樂和個人化服務創造非凡體驗。"},{"en":"People remember extraordinary experiences because they involve emotion and surprise.","zh":"人們記得非凡體驗，因為它們包含情感和驚喜。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when normal services become special events.","zh":"當普通服務變成特別事件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"meaningful customer experiences","meaning":"有意義的顧客體驗","examples":[{"en":"Successful businesses deliver meaningful customer experiences.","zh":"成功企業提供有意義的顧客體驗。"},{"en":"Meaningful customer experiences are interactions that feel valuable, personal, memorable, or emotionally important to customers.","zh":"meaningful customer experiences 指令顧客感到有價值、個人化、難忘或情感上重要的互動。"},{"en":"A clinic creates a meaningful customer experience when staff explain treatment clearly and kindly.","zh":"當診所員工清楚而親切地解釋治療，它就創造有意義的顧客體驗。"},{"en":"Meaningful experiences can build trust and make customers return.","zh":"有意義的體驗可以建立信任並令顧客回來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when service has emotional or personal value.","zh":"當服務具有情感或個人價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"preach the same gospel","meaning":"宣揚同一套理念","examples":[{"en":"These books all preach the same gospel about customer experience.","zh":"這些書都宣揚同一套關於顧客體驗的理念。"},{"en":"Preach the same gospel means strongly promote the same belief or message.","zh":"preach the same gospel 指強烈推廣相同信念或訊息。"},{"en":"Several teachers may preach the same gospel that daily reading improves writing.","zh":"幾位老師可能都宣揚每日閱讀能改善寫作這同一套理念。"},{"en":"When many books repeat the same message, the idea can become influential.","zh":"當許多書重複同一訊息，該想法就可能變得有影響力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when different voices promote one shared doctrine.","zh":"當不同聲音推廣共同信條時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"contrary to","meaning":"與……相反","examples":[{"en":"Contrary to what companies think, consumers do not always want the cheapest product.","zh":"與公司所想相反，消費者不總是想要最便宜的產品。"},{"en":"Contrary to means opposite to or different from what was expected or believed.","zh":"contrary to 指與預期或相信的事情相反或不同。"},{"en":"Contrary to his fear, the interview was friendly and relaxed.","zh":"與他的擔心相反，面試友善而輕鬆。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a correction to a common assumption.","zh":"這個短語引入對常見假設的修正。"},{"en":"It is useful when reality differs from expectation.","zh":"當現實不同於預期時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"專注於","examples":[{"en":"Not all consumers focus on bagging the cheapest product.","zh":"並非所有消費者都專注於買到最便宜的產品。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give it most of your attention.","zh":"focus on something 指把大部分注意力放在某事上。"},{"en":"A student may focus on improving pronunciation rather than learning more grammar rules.","zh":"學生可能專注於改善發音，而不是學更多文法規則。"},{"en":"What people focus on affects what they notice, choose, and pay for.","zh":"人們專注於甚麼會影響他們注意、選擇和付費的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing priorities.","zh":"描述優先事項時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"bag the cheapest product","meaning":"買到最便宜的產品","examples":[{"en":"Consumers are not always focused on bagging the cheapest product.","zh":"消費者不總是專注於買到最便宜的產品。"},{"en":"To bag the cheapest product means to manage to buy the lowest-priced option.","zh":"bag the cheapest product 指成功買到價格最低的選項。"},{"en":"A shopper may spend an hour comparing prices to bag the cheapest rice cooker.","zh":"購物者可能花一小時比較價格，以買到最便宜的電飯煲。"},{"en":"Some consumers stop chasing the lowest price when service, design, or experience matters more.","zh":"當服務、設計或體驗更重要時，有些消費者會停止追求最低價。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when bargain-hunting is the main goal.","zh":"當尋找便宜貨是主要目標時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"buying experience","meaning":"購買體驗","examples":[{"en":"The buying experience is critical.","zh":"購買體驗至關重要。"},{"en":"Buying experience means what a customer feels and goes through while choosing and purchasing something.","zh":"buying experience 指顧客在選擇和購買某物時的感受和經歷。"},{"en":"A polite cashier, clear signs, and easy payment can improve the buying experience.","zh":"有禮貌的收銀員、清楚指示和簡易付款可以改善購買體驗。"},{"en":"A bad buying experience can stop customers returning, even if the product is good.","zh":"即使產品好，糟糕購買體驗也可以令顧客不再回來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the process of buying matters.","zh":"當購買過程很重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be critical","meaning":"至關重要","examples":[{"en":"The buying experience is critical to consumer choice.","zh":"購買體驗對消費者選擇至關重要。"},{"en":"Be critical means be extremely important or necessary.","zh":"be critical 指極其重要或必要。"},{"en":"Clear instructions are critical when students are doing an exam task.","zh":"當學生做考試題時，清楚指示至關重要。"},{"en":"If something is critical, ignoring it can cause failure or poor results.","zh":"如果某事至關重要，忽視它可能導致失敗或差劣結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing importance.","zh":"強調重要性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"switch to","meaning":"轉用；轉向","examples":[{"en":"Consumers have not all switched to Internet shopping.","zh":"消費者並沒有全部轉向網上購物。"},{"en":"Switch to means change from one option, method, or habit to another.","zh":"switch to 指由一個選項、方法或習慣轉到另一個。"},{"en":"A student may switch to digital notes after losing several paper worksheets.","zh":"學生遺失幾份紙本工作紙後，可能轉用數碼筆記。"},{"en":"People switch methods when the new option feels easier, cheaper, or more useful.","zh":"當新選項感覺更容易、更便宜或更有用，人們就會轉用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a change in behaviour.","zh":"描述行為改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Internet shopping","meaning":"網上購物","examples":[{"en":"Internet shopping may lack the buying experience customers value.","zh":"網上購物可能缺乏顧客重視的購買體驗。"},{"en":"Internet shopping means buying goods or services online rather than in a physical shop.","zh":"Internet shopping 指在網上而不是實體店購買商品或服務。"},{"en":"A parent may use Internet shopping to order school supplies without leaving home.","zh":"家長可能使用網上購物訂購學校用品，而不用離家。"},{"en":"Online shopping is convenient, but it may lack touch, atmosphere, and personal service.","zh":"網上購物方便，但可能缺乏觸摸、氣氛和個人服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing online and physical retail.","zh":"比較網上和實體零售時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"no-frills airlines","meaning":"廉航；無附加服務航空公司","examples":[{"en":"Not all consumers choose no-frills airlines.","zh":"並非所有消費者都選擇廉航。"},{"en":"No-frills airlines are low-cost airlines that offer basic service with few extras.","zh":"no-frills airlines 指提供基本服務、附加服務很少的低成本航空公司。"},{"en":"A traveller may choose a no-frills airline if they only need a cheap seat for a short flight.","zh":"如果旅客只需要短途航班的便宜座位，可能選擇廉航。"},{"en":"Some customers avoid no-frills airlines because they value comfort, service, or flexibility more than price.","zh":"有些顧客避免廉航，因為他們更重視舒適、服務或彈性多於價格。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing budget travel.","zh":"討論廉價旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the most notable aspect of","meaning":"……最值得注意的方面","examples":[{"en":"The most notable aspect of the experience economy is what people will pay for.","zh":"體驗經濟最值得注意的方面，是人們願意為甚麼付錢。"},{"en":"The most notable aspect of something is its most important or most noticeable feature.","zh":"most notable aspect of something 指某事最重要或最顯眼的特徵。"},{"en":"The most notable aspect of a good lesson may be how clearly examples explain the idea.","zh":"好課堂最值得注意的方面，可能是例子如何清楚解釋概念。"},{"en":"Identifying the most notable aspect helps readers focus on the main point.","zh":"找出最值得注意的方面，幫助讀者聚焦重點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when highlighting a key feature.","zh":"突出關鍵特徵時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be prepared to pay for","meaning":"願意為……付錢","examples":[{"en":"People are prepared to pay for non-material experiences.","zh":"人們願意為非物質體驗付錢。"},{"en":"Be prepared to pay for something means be willing to spend money on it.","zh":"be prepared to pay for something 指願意花錢購買某事物。"},{"en":"Parents may be prepared to pay for a good tutor if their child needs support.","zh":"如果孩子需要支援，家長可能願意為好補習老師付錢。"},{"en":"People pay when they believe the benefit, memory, or result is worth the cost.","zh":"當人們相信好處、回憶或結果值得成本，就會付錢。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing willingness to spend.","zh":"討論付費意願時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"purely non-material experience","meaning":"純非物質體驗","examples":[{"en":"A spa day is a purely non-material experience.","zh":"水療中心一日體驗是一種純非物質體驗。"},{"en":"A purely non-material experience is something people pay to feel or do, not to own physically.","zh":"purely non-material experience 指人們付錢去感受或做某事，而不是實體擁有它。"},{"en":"A meditation retreat can be a purely non-material experience because the value is calm and reflection.","zh":"冥想營可以是純非物質體驗，因為價值在於平靜和反思。"},{"en":"Such experiences may leave no object behind, but they can leave strong memories.","zh":"這類體驗可能不留下物件，但可以留下強烈回憶。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the purchased value is feeling rather than possession.","zh":"當購買價值在於感受而不是擁有時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a day in a spa","meaning":"水療中心一日體驗","examples":[{"en":"A day in a spa is an example of a non-material experience.","zh":"水療中心一日體驗是非物質體驗的一個例子。"},{"en":"A day in a spa means spending a day receiving relaxation, beauty, or wellness treatments.","zh":"day in a spa 指花一天接受放鬆、美容或健康護理療程。"},{"en":"A tired worker may book a day in a spa to rest after months of overtime.","zh":"疲倦工人可能在連續幾個月加班後，預訂水療中心一日體驗來休息。"},{"en":"People pay for spa experiences because they want calm, comfort, and personal care.","zh":"人們為水療體驗付錢，因為他們想要平靜、舒適和個人照顧。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing paid relaxation experiences.","zh":"討論付費放鬆體驗時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a trip to Prague","meaning":"布拉格之旅","examples":[{"en":"A trip to Prague is an example of a paid experience.","zh":"布拉格之旅是付費體驗的一個例子。"},{"en":"A trip to Prague means travelling to the Czech capital for tourism, culture, food, or leisure.","zh":"trip to Prague 指前往捷克首都旅遊、體驗文化、美食或休閒。"},{"en":"Friends may plan a trip to Prague to visit old streets, bridges, cafés, and museums.","zh":"朋友可能計劃布拉格之旅，參觀古老街道、橋樑、咖啡店和博物館。"},{"en":"A city trip creates value through sights, stories, photos, and shared memories.","zh":"城市旅行透過景點、故事、照片和共同回憶創造價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when travel is treated as an experience product.","zh":"當旅行被視為體驗產品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a collision of social trends","meaning":"多種社會趨勢的交匯","examples":[{"en":"A collision of social trends is responsible for this change.","zh":"多種社會趨勢的交匯導致這種改變。"},{"en":"A collision of social trends means several social changes come together and create a strong effect.","zh":"collision of social trends 指幾種社會變化匯合並產生強烈影響。"},{"en":"Remote work, online shopping, and high rent may collide to change city centres.","zh":"遙距工作、網上購物和高租金可能交匯起來改變市中心。"},{"en":"When trends combine, their effect can be stronger than any single trend alone.","zh":"當趨勢結合，其效果可以比任何單一趨勢更強。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when many social forces meet at once.","zh":"當許多社會力量同時相遇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be responsible for","meaning":"導致；是……的原因","examples":[{"en":"A number of social trends are responsible for the experience economy.","zh":"多個社會趨勢是體驗經濟的原因。"},{"en":"Be responsible for something means be the cause of it or have a role in making it happen.","zh":"be responsible for something 指是某事的原因，或在造成它方面有作用。"},{"en":"Poor lighting may be responsible for accidents on a dark staircase.","zh":"光線不足可能是黑暗樓梯上意外的原因。"},{"en":"When several factors are responsible, the result cannot be explained by one cause only.","zh":"當幾個因素都是原因，結果就不能只用單一原因解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying causes.","zh":"識別原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"this era is unique in","meaning":"這個時代的獨特之處在於……","examples":[{"en":"This era is unique in the coming together of several trends.","zh":"這個時代的獨特之處在於幾種趨勢的匯聚。"},{"en":"This era is unique in something means this period is special because of that feature.","zh":"this era is unique in something 指這個時期因某特徵而特別。"},{"en":"This era is unique in how quickly students can access information online.","zh":"這個時代的獨特之處在於學生可以多快在網上取得資訊。"},{"en":"A period becomes unique when several conditions appear together in a new way.","zh":"當幾種條件以新方式一起出現，一個時期就變得獨特。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining what makes a time period special.","zh":"解釋一個時代有何特別時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the coming together of","meaning":"……的匯聚","examples":[{"en":"The coming together of various trends has shaped consumer behaviour.","zh":"多種趨勢的匯聚塑造了消費者行為。"},{"en":"The coming together of things means different factors meet, combine, or happen at the same time.","zh":"coming together of things 指不同因素相遇、結合或同時發生。"},{"en":"The coming together of cheaper flights and online booking changed how students travel.","zh":"廉價航班和網上預訂的匯聚改變了學生如何旅行。"},{"en":"Combined trends can create a result that none of them would create alone.","zh":"結合起來的趨勢可以創造任何單一趨勢都不能獨自造成的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when several forces combine.","zh":"當幾種力量結合時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"globalism","meaning":"全球主義","examples":[{"en":"Globalism has helped expand the range of experiences available.","zh":"全球主義幫助擴大可取得體驗的範圍。"},{"en":"Globalism is the idea or process of the world becoming more connected through trade, culture, travel, and communication.","zh":"globalism 指世界透過貿易、文化、旅遊和溝通變得更互相連接的理念或過程。"},{"en":"Globalism allows people in one city to eat foreign food, watch foreign films, and buy international brands.","zh":"全球主義讓一個城市的人吃外國食物、看外國電影和購買國際品牌。"},{"en":"As the world connects, consumers become aware of more possible experiences.","zh":"隨着世界連接，消費者意識到更多可能體驗。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing worldwide connections.","zh":"討論全球連繫時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"multiculturalism","meaning":"多元文化主義","examples":[{"en":"Multiculturalism contributes to interest in different experiences.","zh":"多元文化主義促成人們對不同體驗的興趣。"},{"en":"Multiculturalism means different cultures living, interacting, and being recognised within one society.","zh":"multiculturalism 指不同文化在同一社會中生活、互動並被承認。"},{"en":"A multicultural school may celebrate festivals from several communities.","zh":"多元文化學校可能慶祝幾個社群的節日。"},{"en":"Exposure to different cultures can make people more curious about food, travel, music, and traditions.","zh":"接觸不同文化可以令人對食物、旅遊、音樂和傳統更好奇。"},{"en":"This word is useful when cultural diversity shapes behaviour.","zh":"當文化多樣性塑造行為時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"demographic shift","meaning":"人口結構轉變","examples":[{"en":"A demographic shift has helped change how people spend their money.","zh":"人口結構轉變幫助改變人們花錢的方式。"},{"en":"A demographic shift is a change in population patterns, such as age, family size, or life expectancy.","zh":"demographic shift 指人口模式的變化，例如年齡、家庭大小或預期壽命。"},{"en":"An ageing population is a demographic shift that can increase demand for healthcare.","zh":"人口老化是一種人口結構轉變，可以增加醫療需求。"},{"en":"When population structure changes, businesses must adjust what they offer.","zh":"當人口結構改變，企業必須調整提供的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when population changes affect society.","zh":"當人口變化影響社會時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"in terms of longevity","meaning":"就壽命而言","examples":[{"en":"The demographic shift is described in terms of longevity.","zh":"這個人口結構轉變是就壽命而言來描述的。"},{"en":"In terms of longevity means from the point of view of how long people live.","zh":"in terms of longevity 指從人們壽命長短的角度來看。"},{"en":"In terms of longevity, better healthcare has changed retirement planning.","zh":"就壽命而言，更好的醫療已改變退休規劃。"},{"en":"Longer lives affect work, savings, travel, and leisure choices.","zh":"更長壽命影響工作、儲蓄、旅遊和休閒選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when focusing on lifespan as the measure.","zh":"當以壽命作為衡量角度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"longevity","meaning":"長壽；壽命延長","examples":[{"en":"Greater longevity gives people more time to try different things.","zh":"壽命延長給人更多時間嘗試不同事物。"},{"en":"Longevity means long life or the length of time people live.","zh":"longevity 指長壽，或人們活着的時間長度。"},{"en":"Improved medicine and safer workplaces can contribute to greater longevity.","zh":"改善醫療和更安全工作場所可以促成壽命延長。"},{"en":"When people live longer, they may plan more travel, learning, and leisure after retirement.","zh":"當人們活得更長，他們可能在退休後計劃更多旅行、學習和休閒。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing life expectancy and ageing.","zh":"討論預期壽命和老化時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"leisure activities","meaning":"消閒活動","examples":[{"en":"There are more leisure activities today than twenty years ago.","zh":"今天的消閒活動比二十年前更多。"},{"en":"Leisure activities are things people do in their free time for enjoyment, rest, or interest.","zh":"leisure activities 指人們在空閒時間為享受、休息或興趣而做的事。"},{"en":"Yoga classes, hiking groups, board-game cafés, and weekend workshops are leisure activities.","zh":"瑜伽課、行山小組、桌遊咖啡店和週末工作坊都是消閒活動。"},{"en":"More leisure options give consumers more ways to spend money on experiences.","zh":"更多休閒選項給消費者更多方式把錢花在體驗上。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing free-time choices.","zh":"討論空閒時間選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be aware of","meaning":"知道；意識到","examples":[{"en":"Consumers are aware of more activities and cultures.","zh":"消費者知道更多活動和文化。"},{"en":"Be aware of something means know that it exists or understand it.","zh":"be aware of something 指知道某事存在或理解某事。"},{"en":"Students become aware of different careers when schools invite professionals to speak.","zh":"當學校邀請專業人士演講，學生會意識到不同職業。"},{"en":"Awareness often comes before interest, choice, and spending.","zh":"認知常出現在興趣、選擇和消費之前。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when people notice new possibilities.","zh":"當人們注意到新可能性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"other activities and cultures","meaning":"其他活動和文化","examples":[{"en":"People are aware of other activities and cultures.","zh":"人們知道其他活動和文化。"},{"en":"Other activities and cultures means different ways of spending time and different customs from one’s own society.","zh":"other activities and cultures 指不同的消閒方式和不同於自己社會的習俗。"},{"en":"Travel videos can introduce viewers to other activities and cultures, such as festivals, sports, and food traditions.","zh":"旅遊影片可以向觀眾介紹其他活動和文化，例如節日、運動和飲食傳統。"},{"en":"Awareness of difference can create curiosity and demand for new experiences.","zh":"對差異的認知可以創造好奇心和對新體驗的需求。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing cultural exposure.","zh":"討論文化接觸時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"have the money to","meaning":"有錢去……","examples":[{"en":"Many people now have the money to experience different cultures.","zh":"許多人現在有錢去體驗不同文化。"},{"en":"Have the money to do something means have enough money to afford it.","zh":"have the money to do something 指有足夠金錢負擔某事。"},{"en":"A worker may finally have the money to take driving lessons after saving for several months.","zh":"工人儲蓄幾個月後，可能終於有錢去上駕駛課。"},{"en":"When people have extra money, they can choose experiences beyond basic needs.","zh":"當人們有額外金錢，他們可以選擇基本需要以外的體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when ability depends on affordability.","zh":"當能力取決於負擔能力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"living longer","meaning":"活得更長","examples":[{"en":"People have more time for experiences because they are living longer.","zh":"人們有更多時間體驗，因為他們活得更長。"},{"en":"Living longer means having a longer life than people in earlier times or other groups.","zh":"living longer 指壽命比早期人群或其他群體更長。"},{"en":"Many retired people are living longer and may take courses, travel, or volunteer.","zh":"許多退休人士活得更長，可能上課、旅行或做義工。"},{"en":"Longer lives can increase demand for leisure, healthcare, and lifelong learning.","zh":"更長壽命可以增加對休閒、醫療和終身學習的需求。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when ageing changes behaviour.","zh":"當老化改變行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"try different things","meaning":"嘗試不同事物","examples":[{"en":"Longer lives give people more time to try different things.","zh":"更長壽命給人更多時間嘗試不同事物。"},{"en":"Try different things means experiment with activities, choices, or experiences that are new or varied.","zh":"try different things 指嘗試新的或多樣化的活動、選擇或體驗。"},{"en":"A student may try different things such as debating, painting, coding, and volunteering.","zh":"學生可能嘗試不同事物，例如辯論、繪畫、編程和義工服務。"},{"en":"Trying variety can help people discover what they enjoy and value.","zh":"嘗試多樣選擇可以幫助人發現自己享受和重視甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when people explore new possibilities.","zh":"當人們探索新可能性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"only one of the choices is correct","meaning":"只有其中一個選項正確","examples":[{"en":"For each question, only one of the choices is correct.","zh":"每題只有其中一個選項正確。"},{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct means just one option gives the right answer.","zh":"only one of the choices is correct 指只有一個選項是正確答案。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice reading question, students should not choose two answers if only one is correct.","zh":"在多項選擇閱讀題中，如果只有一個答案正確，學生不應選兩個。"},{"en":"This instruction helps prevent guessing too many options.","zh":"這個指示有助防止亂選太多選項。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in exam directions.","zh":"這個短語適用於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"corresponding letter","meaning":"相應字母","examples":[{"en":"Students write the corresponding letter on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生在答題紙上寫下相應字母。"},{"en":"The corresponding letter is the letter that matches the correct answer choice.","zh":"corresponding letter 指與正確答案選項相配的字母。"},{"en":"If option C is correct, students should write the corresponding letter C.","zh":"如果選項 C 正確，學生應寫下相應字母 C。"},{"en":"Writing the wrong letter loses marks even if the student understands the idea.","zh":"即使學生理解意思，寫錯字母也會失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in multiple-choice exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於多項選擇考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"appropriate box","meaning":"適當方格","examples":[{"en":"The answer should be written in the appropriate box.","zh":"答案應寫在適當方格內。"},{"en":"The appropriate box is the correct space on an answer sheet for a particular answer.","zh":"appropriate box 指答題紙上某答案應填寫的正確空格。"},{"en":"In an exam, students must write answer 12 in box 12, not beside another question.","zh":"在考試中，學生必須把第12題答案寫在第12格，而不是其他題目旁邊。"},{"en":"Correct placement matters because markers need to read answers quickly and accurately.","zh":"正確位置很重要，因為評卷員需要快速而準確地閱讀答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving form-filling or exam instructions.","zh":"給予填表或考試指示時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"least likely to","meaning":"最不可能","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what Trevor Beattie is least likely to do.","zh":"題目問 Trevor Beattie 最不可能做甚麼。"},{"en":"Least likely to means having the smallest chance of doing something.","zh":"least likely to 指做某事的機會最低。"},{"en":"A student who hates early mornings is least likely to choose a 7 a.m. class.","zh":"討厭早起的學生最不可能選擇早上七點的課。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare possibilities and identify the most unlikely one.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較可能性，並找出最不可能的一項。"},{"en":"It is useful in reading questions about behaviour or preference.","zh":"它適用於關於行為或偏好的閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"think of a good way of","meaning":"想出……的好方法","examples":[{"en":"Beattie is likely to think of a good way of advertising something.","zh":"Beattie 可能想出為某物賣廣告的好方法。"},{"en":"Think of a good way of doing something means create or find an effective method.","zh":"think of a good way of doing something 指創造或找到有效方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may think of a good way of explaining grammar through pictures.","zh":"老師可能想出透過圖片解釋文法的好方法。"},{"en":"Good methods solve the problem more clearly than ordinary or lazy approaches.","zh":"好方法比普通或懶散做法更清楚地解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing problem-solving and creativity.","zh":"討論解難和創意時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"advertising something","meaning":"為某物賣廣告","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to advertising something effectively.","zh":"題目指有效地為某物賣廣告。"},{"en":"Advertising something means promoting a product, service, event, or idea so people notice it.","zh":"advertising something 指推廣產品、服務、活動或想法，讓人注意到它。"},{"en":"A school may advertise an open day through posters, emails, and social media.","zh":"學校可能透過海報、電郵和社交媒體為開放日賣廣告。"},{"en":"Effective advertising makes the message clear and memorable to the right audience.","zh":"有效廣告令訊息對合適受眾清楚且難忘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing promotion.","zh":"討論推廣時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"fly in a military plane","meaning":"乘坐軍機飛行","examples":[{"en":"Beattie may pay to fly in a military plane.","zh":"Beattie 可能付錢乘坐軍機飛行。"},{"en":"To fly in a military plane means to travel as a passenger in an aircraft designed for military use.","zh":"fly in a military plane 指作為乘客乘坐為軍事用途設計的飛機。"},{"en":"A thrill-seeker may pay to fly in a military plane for speed and excitement.","zh":"追求刺激的人可能為速度和刺激感付錢乘坐軍機飛行。"},{"en":"Such experiences are unusual because ordinary travellers do not normally access military aircraft.","zh":"這類體驗不尋常，因為普通旅客通常不能接觸軍機。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing rare adventure experiences.","zh":"描述罕有冒險體驗時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"buy a nice, fast car","meaning":"買一部漂亮的跑車","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether he would buy a nice, fast car.","zh":"題目問他是否會買一部漂亮的跑車。"},{"en":"Buy a nice, fast car means purchase an attractive car with high speed or sporty performance.","zh":"buy a nice, fast car 指購買一部外觀吸引且速度快或性能好的車。"},{"en":"Someone may buy a nice, fast car to show success or enjoy driving.","zh":"有人可能買漂亮跑車來展示成功或享受駕駛。"},{"en":"In the passage, this choice contrasts with spending money on unusual experiences.","zh":"在文章中，這個選擇與把錢花在不尋常體驗上形成對比。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing material luxury.","zh":"討論物質奢華時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"has grown in Britain","meaning":"在英國發展起來","examples":[{"en":"The experience economy has grown in Britain.","zh":"體驗經濟已在英國發展起來。"},{"en":"Has grown in Britain means has become larger or more important within Britain.","zh":"has grown in Britain 指在英國變得更大或更重要。"},{"en":"Online food delivery has grown in Britain as more people use apps to order meals.","zh":"隨着更多人使用應用程式叫餐，網上外賣在英國發展起來。"},{"en":"Growth happens when more consumers spend money in a particular area.","zh":"當更多消費者在某範疇花錢，增長就會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing national trends.","zh":"討論國家趨勢時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"have enough things","meaning":"擁有足夠物品","examples":[{"en":"The experience economy has grown because most people have enough things.","zh":"體驗經濟發展起來，是因為大多數人已擁有足夠物品。"},{"en":"Have enough things means already own enough material goods to meet ordinary needs.","zh":"have enough things 指已擁有足夠物質商品來滿足普通需要。"},{"en":"A family with full wardrobes and working appliances may feel they have enough things.","zh":"衣櫃已滿且電器能用的家庭，可能覺得自己已擁有足夠物品。"},{"en":"When people already own many goods, they may prefer travel, meals, or learning experiences.","zh":"當人們已擁有許多商品，他們可能更喜歡旅行、用餐或學習體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why material buying becomes less exciting.","zh":"解釋為何物質購買變得較不吸引時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"consumer behaviour","meaning":"消費者行為","examples":[{"en":"Shopping malls have responded to changes in consumer behaviour.","zh":"商場已回應消費者行為的變化。"},{"en":"Consumer behaviour means the ways people choose, buy, use, and think about products or services.","zh":"consumer behaviour 指人們如何選擇、購買、使用和看待產品或服務。"},{"en":"A supermarket studies consumer behaviour by checking what shoppers buy before holidays.","zh":"超級市場透過查看顧客假期前買甚麼來研究消費者行為。"},{"en":"When consumer behaviour changes, businesses must change their design, prices, or services.","zh":"當消費者行為改變，企業必須改變設計、價格或服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how customers act.","zh":"討論顧客如何行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"present themselves","meaning":"展示／定位自己","examples":[{"en":"Shopping malls are changing the way they present themselves.","zh":"商場正在改變它們展示自己的方式。"},{"en":"Present themselves means show or describe their identity to the public in a particular way.","zh":"present themselves 指以某種方式向公眾展示或描述自己的身份。"},{"en":"A tutor may present themselves as friendly and practical rather than strict and old-fashioned.","zh":"補習老師可能把自己定位為友善和實用，而不是嚴厲和老派。"},{"en":"How an organisation presents itself affects what people expect from it.","zh":"組織如何展示自己會影響人們對它的期望。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing image and positioning.","zh":"討論形象和定位時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be slow to recognise","meaning":"對……反應遲緩","examples":[{"en":"Some businesses may be slow to recognise changes in consumer behaviour.","zh":"有些企業可能對消費者行為變化反應遲緩。"},{"en":"Be slow to recognise means take too long to notice or understand something important.","zh":"be slow to recognise 指太遲注意或理解重要事情。"},{"en":"A school may be slow to recognise that students are struggling with online homework.","zh":"學校可能太遲意識到學生在網上功課上遇到困難。"},{"en":"Slow recognition can cause missed opportunities and weaker responses.","zh":"反應遲緩可以造成錯失機會和較弱回應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when delayed awareness creates problems.","zh":"當延遲認知造成問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be unhappy with","meaning":"對……感到不滿","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that malls are unhappy with the experience economy.","zh":"這個選項暗示商場對體驗經濟感到不滿。"},{"en":"Be unhappy with something means feel dissatisfied, displeased, or negative about it.","zh":"be unhappy with something 指對某事感到不滿、不高興或負面。"},{"en":"Customers may be unhappy with a restaurant if food arrives cold and late.","zh":"如果食物又冷又遲才到，顧客可能對餐廳感到不滿。"},{"en":"Dissatisfaction often leads people to complain, leave, or demand improvement.","zh":"不滿常導致人投訴、離開或要求改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing negative reaction.","zh":"描述負面反應時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"focus more on","meaning":"更加重視","examples":[{"en":"Retailers are focusing more on experiences.","zh":"零售商更加重視體驗。"},{"en":"Focus more on something means give it greater attention than before.","zh":"focus more on something 指比以前給予某事更多注意。"},{"en":"A school may focus more on speaking practice after students perform poorly in interviews.","zh":"學生在面試中表現差後，學校可能更加重視口語練習。"},{"en":"Businesses shift focus when customer expectations change.","zh":"當顧客期望改變，企業會改變重點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when priorities increase.","zh":"當優先程度增加時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"aim to make sales","meaning":"旨在促成銷售","examples":[{"en":"Retailers still aim to make sales through experiences.","zh":"零售商仍然旨在透過體驗促成銷售。"},{"en":"Aim to make sales means intend to sell products or services and earn revenue.","zh":"aim to make sales 指意圖售賣產品或服務並賺取收入。"},{"en":"A café may offer free tastings because it aims to make sales of new desserts.","zh":"咖啡店可能提供免費試食，因為它旨在銷售新甜品。"},{"en":"Experiences can attract customers, but the business goal is often still selling.","zh":"體驗可以吸引顧客，但商業目標通常仍是銷售。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when commercial purpose remains behind an activity.","zh":"當活動背後仍有商業目的時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"marketing techniques","meaning":"市場推廣技巧","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to better marketing techniques.","zh":"這個選項提到更好的市場推廣技巧。"},{"en":"Marketing techniques are methods used to attract customers and encourage them to buy.","zh":"marketing techniques 指用來吸引顧客並鼓勵購買的方法。"},{"en":"Discounts, loyalty cards, social media videos, and product displays are marketing techniques.","zh":"折扣、會員卡、社交媒體影片和產品陳列都是市場推廣技巧。"},{"en":"Better techniques can change how customers see a product without changing the product itself.","zh":"更好的技巧可以改變顧客如何看待產品，即使產品本身沒有改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing sales strategy.","zh":"討論銷售策略時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"remind them of their experiences","meaning":"使他們想起自己的體驗","examples":[{"en":"Customers may buy things that remind them of their experiences.","zh":"顧客可能購買使他們想起自己體驗的東西。"},{"en":"Remind them of their experiences means make them remember activities or moments they enjoyed.","zh":"remind them of their experiences 指令他們記起自己享受過的活動或時刻。"},{"en":"A tourist may buy a mug that reminds them of their trip to a seaside town.","zh":"遊客可能購買一隻杯，讓自己想起海濱小鎮之旅。"},{"en":"Souvenirs connect objects with memories, so the object feels more meaningful.","zh":"紀念品把物件和回憶連接起來，因此物件感覺更有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when purchases act as memory triggers.","zh":"當購買物成為記憶觸發物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete the following sentences","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the following sentences using words from the text.","zh":"學生使用文章中的詞語完成以下句子。"},{"en":"Complete the following sentences means fill in missing parts of the sentences below the instruction.","zh":"complete the following sentences 指填寫指示下方句子的缺漏部分。"},{"en":"Students may complete the following sentences by choosing words that fit the grammar and meaning.","zh":"學生可能透過選擇符合文法和意思的詞語完成以下句子。"},{"en":"This task checks whether students understand both the passage and sentence structure.","zh":"這個任務檢查學生是否理解文章和句子結構。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading and grammar exercises.","zh":"這個短語適用於閱讀和文法練習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個詞","examples":[{"en":"The answer should use no more than two words from the text.","zh":"答案應使用文章中不多於兩個詞。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must contain one or two words only.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案只可包含一個或兩個詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “budget travel,” it follows the rule because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “budget travel”，它符合規則，因為它有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing three words can be marked wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫三個詞也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in exam instructions with strict word limits.","zh":"這個短語適用於有嚴格字數限制的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"for each gap","meaning":"每個空格","examples":[{"en":"Students write an answer for each gap.","zh":"學生為每個空格寫一個答案。"},{"en":"For each gap means for every blank space that must be filled.","zh":"for each gap 指為每一個需要填寫的空白位置。"},{"en":"In a summary task, students should check the grammar before writing a word for each gap.","zh":"在摘要填空題中，學生應先檢查文法，再為每個空格填詞。"},{"en":"Missing one gap can lose marks even if the other answers are correct.","zh":"即使其他答案正確，漏掉一個空格也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in fill-in-the-blank exercises.","zh":"這個短語適用於填空練習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"from the text","meaning":"來自文章","examples":[{"en":"The answers must come from the text.","zh":"答案必須來自文章。"},{"en":"From the text means the answer must be taken directly from the reading passage or source.","zh":"from the text 指答案必須直接取自閱讀篇章或來源。"},{"en":"Students should not use their own synonyms if the instruction says the answer is from the text.","zh":"如果指示說答案來自文章，學生不應使用自己的同義詞。"},{"en":"This rule ensures answers are based on evidence, not memory or outside knowledge.","zh":"這條規則確保答案基於證據，而不是記憶或外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading-comprehension instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於閱讀理解指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"become more creative","meaning":"變得更有創意","examples":[{"en":"Gilmore thinks people become more creative under certain conditions.","zh":"Gilmore 認為人在某些情況下會變得更有創意。"},{"en":"Become more creative means produce more original, useful, or imaginative ideas than before.","zh":"become more creative 指比以前產生更多原創、有用或具想像力的想法。"},{"en":"Students may become more creative when they are allowed to test several answers, not only one.","zh":"當學生被容許測試幾個答案，而不只是一個，他們可能變得更有創意。"},{"en":"Creativity can increase when people feel challenged, curious, or free to experiment.","zh":"當人們感到受挑戰、好奇或可自由實驗，創意可以增加。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how creativity develops.","zh":"討論創意如何發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be subjected to","meaning":"受到……影響；被置於……情況下","examples":[{"en":"People may become more creative when subjected to sleep deprivation.","zh":"當人們受到睡眠不足影響時，可能變得更有創意。"},{"en":"Be subjected to something means be made to experience something, often something difficult or unpleasant.","zh":"be subjected to something 指被迫經歷某事，通常是困難或不愉快的事。"},{"en":"Workers subjected to loud noise every day may need hearing protection.","zh":"每天受到噪音影響的工人可能需要聽力保護。"},{"en":"Being subjected to pressure can change how people think, feel, or behave.","zh":"被置於壓力下可以改變人們的思考、感受或行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone experiences a condition imposed on them.","zh":"當某人經歷被施加的情況時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"develop an emotional attachment with","meaning":"與……建立情感連繫","examples":[{"en":"Starbucks has developed an emotional attachment with its customers.","zh":"Starbucks 已與顧客建立情感連繫。"},{"en":"Develop an emotional attachment with someone means build a strong feeling of connection or loyalty over time.","zh":"develop an emotional attachment with someone 指隨時間建立強烈連繫感或忠誠感。"},{"en":"A school may develop an emotional attachment with graduates through traditions and reunions.","zh":"學校可能透過傳統和舊生聚會與畢業生建立情感連繫。"},{"en":"Emotional attachment grows when repeated experiences feel warm, personal, and reliable.","zh":"當重複體驗感覺溫暖、個人化且可靠，情感連繫就會增長。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when relationships deepen through feeling.","zh":"當關係透過感情加深時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"managed to develop","meaning":"成功建立","examples":[{"en":"Starbucks has managed to develop an emotional attachment with customers.","zh":"Starbucks 成功與顧客建立情感連繫。"},{"en":"Managed to develop means succeeded in building something, often after effort or planning.","zh":"managed to develop 指成功建立某事，通常經過努力或規劃。"},{"en":"A shy student managed to develop confidence after months of speaking practice.","zh":"害羞學生經過幾個月口語練習後，成功建立信心。"},{"en":"Success in developing something usually requires repeated action, feedback, and time.","zh":"成功建立某事通常需要反覆行動、回饋和時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when effort leads to growth.","zh":"當努力帶來成長時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"buying the cheapest product","meaning":"購買最便宜的產品","examples":[{"en":"Not all consumers focus on buying the cheapest product.","zh":"並非所有消費者都專注於購買最便宜的產品。"},{"en":"Buying the cheapest product means choosing the lowest-priced item available.","zh":"buying the cheapest product 指選擇可買到的最低價商品。"},{"en":"A shopper may compare several supermarkets before buying the cheapest rice.","zh":"購物者可能比較幾間超市後才購買最便宜的米。"},{"en":"Some people stop choosing the cheapest option when service, quality, or experience matters more.","zh":"當服務、質素或體驗更重要，有些人會停止選擇最便宜選項。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when price is only one part of consumer choice.","zh":"當價格只是消費選擇的一部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"lacks the buying experience","meaning":"缺乏購買體驗","examples":[{"en":"Internet shopping lacks the buying experience of physical retail.","zh":"網上購物缺乏實體零售的購買體驗。"},{"en":"Lacks the buying experience means does not provide the feelings, service, atmosphere, or interaction involved in buying in person.","zh":"lacks the buying experience 指沒有提供親身購買時的感受、服務、氣氛或互動。"},{"en":"Online clothes shopping may lack the buying experience because customers cannot touch the fabric or try items on.","zh":"網上買衣服可能缺乏購買體驗，因為顧客不能觸摸布料或試穿。"},{"en":"When experience is missing, some consumers still prefer real shops.","zh":"當缺少體驗，有些消費者仍偏好實體店。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing online and offline shopping.","zh":"比較網上和線下購物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"have time for","meaning":"有時間去……","examples":[{"en":"People have time for more experiences partly because they live longer.","zh":"人們有時間去體驗更多事情，部分原因是他們活得更長。"},{"en":"Have time for something means have enough available time to do it.","zh":"have time for something 指有足夠可用時間去做某事。"},{"en":"A worker may have time for evening classes if their job finishes earlier.","zh":"如果工作較早結束，工人可能有時間去上晚間課程。"},{"en":"More free time allows people to explore hobbies, travel, and leisure activities.","zh":"更多空閒時間讓人探索嗜好、旅遊和休閒活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when availability of time affects choices.","zh":"當時間是否充足影響選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"do the following statements agree with","meaning":"以下陳述是否與……一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the following statements agree with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷以下陳述是否與文章一致。"},{"en":"Do the following statements agree with means check whether each statement matches the information in the text.","zh":"do the following statements agree with 指檢查每個陳述是否符合文本資料。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students compare each statement carefully with the passage before answering.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生作答前會仔細把每個陳述與文章比較。"},{"en":"Agreement must be based on evidence in the text, not personal opinion.","zh":"一致與否必須基於文本證據，而不是個人意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語適用於 TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"information given in","meaning":"在……中給出的資料","examples":[{"en":"The statements must be checked against the information given in the passage.","zh":"這些陳述必須與文章中給出的資料核對。"},{"en":"Information given in a passage means the facts, details, or views that the text actually provides.","zh":"information given in a passage 指文本實際提供的事實、細節或觀點。"},{"en":"Students should answer according to the information given in the article, not outside knowledge.","zh":"學生應根據文章中給出的資料作答，而不是外部知識。"},{"en":"This instruction keeps answers grounded in the reading passage.","zh":"這個指示令答案以閱讀文章為根據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence must come from a source.","zh":"當證據必須來自來源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"if the statement agrees with","meaning":"如陳述與……一致","examples":[{"en":"Students write “TRUE” if the statement agrees with the information.","zh":"如陳述與資料一致，學生寫 TRUE。"},{"en":"If the statement agrees with means if the sentence matches what the text says.","zh":"if the statement agrees with 指如果句子符合文本所說內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says malls added cinemas, a matching statement agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說商場加入戲院，對應陳述就與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should choose TRUE only when the text clearly supports the statement.","zh":"只有當文本清楚支持陳述時，學生才應選 TRUE。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading-test instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"if the statement contradicts","meaning":"如陳述與……相反","examples":[{"en":"Students write “FALSE” if the statement contradicts the information.","zh":"如陳述與資料相反，學生寫 FALSE。"},{"en":"If the statement contradicts means if the sentence says the opposite of the text.","zh":"if the statement contradicts 指如果句子說出與文本相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says spending on experiences rose, a statement saying it fell may contradict it.","zh":"如果文章說體驗開支上升，而陳述說它下降，就可能與文章相反。"},{"en":"Students must find clear conflict in the passage before choosing FALSE.","zh":"學生必須在文章中找到清楚矛盾，才選 FALSE。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個短語適用於 TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students write “NOT GIVEN” if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文中沒有相關資料，學生寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not provide enough evidence to decide.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有提供足夠證據作出判斷。"},{"en":"If the text never mentions staff salaries, there is no information on whether workers are well paid.","zh":"如果文本從未提到員工薪金，就無法知道工人是否待遇好。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when the passage is silent about a point.","zh":"當文章沒有提及某點時，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence is missing.","zh":"當證據缺失時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"total amount of money spent on","meaning":"花在……上的總金額","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to the total amount of money spent on buying things.","zh":"這個陳述指花在購買物品上的總金額。"},{"en":"Total amount of money spent on something means the full sum used for that purpose.","zh":"total amount of money spent on something 指用於某目的的全部金額。"},{"en":"A family may calculate the total amount of money spent on eating out each month.","zh":"家庭可能計算每月花在外出用餐上的總金額。"},{"en":"Looking at the total amount helps people understand whether spending is rising or falling overall.","zh":"查看總金額幫助人理解整體開支是上升還是下降。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing spending data.","zh":"討論開支數據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"buying things","meaning":"購買物品","examples":[{"en":"The passage distinguishes buying things from buying experiences.","zh":"文章區分購買物品和購買體驗。"},{"en":"Buying things means spending money on physical goods that people can own.","zh":"buying things 指花錢購買人們可以擁有的實體商品。"},{"en":"Buying a phone, shoes, or a sofa is buying things rather than buying an experience.","zh":"買電話、鞋或梳化是購買物品，而不是購買體驗。"},{"en":"When people already own many objects, buying things may feel less exciting.","zh":"當人們已擁有許多物件，購買物品可能感覺較不刺激。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting possession with experience.","zh":"對比擁有和體驗時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"in the last ten years","meaning":"在過去十年","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to changes in the last ten years.","zh":"這個陳述提到過去十年的變化。"},{"en":"In the last ten years means during the most recent ten-year period being discussed.","zh":"in the last ten years 指在所討論的最近十年期間。"},{"en":"In the last ten years, many families have started ordering groceries online.","zh":"在過去十年，許多家庭開始在網上訂購雜貨。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show that a trend is recent and measurable.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示趨勢是近期且可量度的。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing current behaviour with the recent past.","zh":"比較目前行為與近期過去時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"enhance people’s shopping experience","meaning":"提升人們的購物體驗","examples":[{"en":"Some malls have cinemas to enhance people’s shopping experience.","zh":"有些商場設有戲院，以提升人們的購物體驗。"},{"en":"To enhance people’s shopping experience means to improve how enjoyable, comfortable, or memorable shopping feels.","zh":"enhance people’s shopping experience 指改善購物時的愉快、舒適或難忘程度。"},{"en":"A shop may enhance people’s shopping experience with music, seating, helpful staff, and clear displays.","zh":"商店可能透過音樂、座位、有幫助的員工和清晰陳列來提升人們的購物體驗。"},{"en":"Better experiences can make visitors stay longer and spend more.","zh":"更好體驗可以令訪客逗留更久並花更多錢。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when retail spaces add value beyond products.","zh":"當零售空間增加產品以外的價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be criticised for","meaning":"因……受到批評","examples":[{"en":"iPods are often criticised for being too expensive.","zh":"iPod 常因太昂貴而受到批評。"},{"en":"Be criticised for something means receive negative comments because of it.","zh":"be criticised for something 指因某事而受到負面評論。"},{"en":"A school may be criticised for giving students too much homework.","zh":"學校可能因給學生太多功課而受到批評。"},{"en":"Criticism often appears when people think a product, decision, or behaviour has a weakness.","zh":"當人們認為產品、決定或行為有弱點，批評常會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why people disapprove.","zh":"解釋人們為何不認同時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"too expensive","meaning":"太昂貴","examples":[{"en":"The iPod is often criticised for being too expensive.","zh":"iPod 常被批評太昂貴。"},{"en":"Too expensive means costing more than people think is reasonable or affordable.","zh":"too expensive 指價格高於人們認為合理或可負擔的水平。"},{"en":"A student may avoid a restaurant if the lunch set is too expensive.","zh":"如果午餐套餐太昂貴，學生可能避開那間餐廳。"},{"en":"A high price can reduce demand unless customers believe the product is worth it.","zh":"高價格可以降低需求，除非顧客相信產品值得。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing price objections.","zh":"討論價格反對意見時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be considered to be","meaning":"被認為是","examples":[{"en":"Apple is considered to be a creative company.","zh":"Apple 被認為是一間有創意的公司。"},{"en":"Be considered to be means be regarded or thought of as something by people.","zh":"be considered to be 指被人視為或認為是某種東西。"},{"en":"A student may be considered to be hardworking if they always prepare before class.","zh":"如果學生總是在課前準備，可能被認為是勤奮的。"},{"en":"Public reputation can influence how people judge products and services.","zh":"公眾聲譽可以影響人們如何判斷產品和服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing common opinion.","zh":"描述普遍看法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"creative company","meaning":"有創意的公司","examples":[{"en":"Apple is considered a creative company by many consumers.","zh":"Apple 被許多消費者認為是有創意的公司。"},{"en":"A creative company is a business known for original ideas, design, products, or ways of working.","zh":"creative company 指以原創想法、設計、產品或工作方式聞名的企業。"},{"en":"A creative company may redesign an ordinary service so customers enjoy using it.","zh":"有創意的公司可能重新設計普通服務，令顧客享受使用它。"},{"en":"Creativity helps companies stand out when competitors sell similar products.","zh":"當競爭者售賣相似產品，創意幫助公司突圍而出。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when innovation is part of a brand’s image.","zh":"當創新是品牌形象的一部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"clear limit to","meaning":"明確限制","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether companies believe there is a clear limit to spending.","zh":"這個陳述問公司是否相信消費有明確限制。"},{"en":"A clear limit to something is an obvious point beyond which it should not or cannot go.","zh":"clear limit to something 指一個明顯界線，超過它就不應或不能再繼續。"},{"en":"Parents may set a clear limit to how much money a child can spend on games each month.","zh":"父母可能為孩子每月可花在遊戲上的金錢設定明確限制。"},{"en":"Without clear limits, spending can rise until it becomes unreasonable or risky.","zh":"沒有明確限制，開支可以上升到不合理或有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing boundaries or maximum levels.","zh":"討論界線或最高水平時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"how much people will pay for","meaning":"人們願意為……付多少錢","examples":[{"en":"Companies are interested in how much people will pay for experiences.","zh":"公司對人們願意為體驗付多少錢感興趣。"},{"en":"How much people will pay for something means the amount customers are willing to spend on it.","zh":"how much people will pay for something 指顧客願意為某事花多少錢。"},{"en":"A gym may test how much people will pay for a weekend wellness workshop.","zh":"健身中心可能測試人們願意為週末健康工作坊付多少錢。"},{"en":"Knowing willingness to pay helps companies set prices and design packages.","zh":"了解付費意願有助公司定價和設計套票。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing pricing and demand.","zh":"討論定價和需求時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 98 - Are You Experienced?.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 99":[{"front":"charm your way into","meaning":"靠魅力成功進入……","examples":[{"en":"The article asks whether students can charm their way into Oxbridge.","zh":"文章問學生是否可以靠魅力成功進入牛津劍橋。"},{"en":"To charm your way into a place means to gain entry or acceptance by using confidence, manners, and personal appeal.","zh":"「charm your way into」某地方，意思是透過自信、禮貌和個人魅力取得進入或被接納的機會。"},{"en":"A job candidate may charm their way into a second interview by greeting everyone warmly and speaking clearly.","zh":"求職者可能靠熱情問候和清楚表達，靠魅力成功進入第二輪面試。"},{"en":"If a student relies only on charm without knowledge, the interviewers may quickly notice the weakness.","zh":"如果學生只靠魅力而沒有知識，面試官可能很快看出弱點。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests social skill can help, but it does not replace real ability.","zh":"這個短語暗示社交技巧有幫助，但不能取代真正能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Oxbridge","meaning":"牛津劍橋","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of applicants hope to gain a place at Oxbridge.","zh":"數以千計的申請人希望獲得牛津劍橋學位。"},{"en":"Oxbridge is a combined name for Oxford University and Cambridge University.","zh":"「Oxbridge」是 Oxford University 和 Cambridge University 的合稱。"},{"en":"A student applying to Oxbridge usually expects a demanding academic interview.","zh":"申請牛津劍橋的學生通常預期會有要求很高的學術面試。"},{"en":"If someone gains a place at Oxbridge, they have been accepted by one of the two universities.","zh":"如果某人獲得牛津劍橋學位，即表示他被兩所大學其中之一取錄。"},{"en":"The word is often used when discussing elite university admissions in Britain.","zh":"這個詞常用於討論英國精英大學收生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Oxbridge season","meaning":"牛津劍橋面試季","examples":[{"en":"Oxbridge season is the period when applicants wait for interview invitations.","zh":"牛津劍橋面試季是申請人等待面試邀請的時期。"},{"en":"Oxbridge season means the busy admissions period connected with Oxford and Cambridge interviews.","zh":"「Oxbridge season」意思是與牛津和劍橋面試有關的繁忙招生時期。"},{"en":"During Oxbridge season, teachers may spend extra time helping students practise difficult questions.","zh":"在牛津劍橋面試季，老師可能花額外時間幫助學生練習困難問題。"},{"en":"If interview invitations arrive, candidates often feel both excited and nervous.","zh":"如果面試邀請到達，候選人通常既興奮又緊張。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a specific time in the university application calendar.","zh":"這個短語描述大學申請日程中的特定時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"thousands of applicants","meaning":"數以千計的申請人","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of applicants are waiting to be called to interview.","zh":"數以千計的申請人正在等待被邀請參加面試。"},{"en":"Thousands of applicants means a very large number of people who have applied for something.","zh":"「thousands of applicants」意思是已申請某事的大量人士。"},{"en":"A popular scholarship may attract thousands of applicants from different schools.","zh":"受歡迎的獎學金可能吸引來自不同學校的數以千計申請人。"},{"en":"If thousands of applicants compete for limited places, the selection process becomes intense.","zh":"如果數以千計申請人競逐有限名額，甄選過程會變得激烈。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the scale of competition.","zh":"這個短語強調競爭規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"anxiously waiting to","meaning":"焦急地等待……","examples":[{"en":"Many applicants are anxiously waiting to be called to interview.","zh":"許多申請人正焦急地等待被邀請參加面試。"},{"en":"To be anxiously waiting to do something means to wait with worry, nervousness, or strong expectation.","zh":"「anxiously waiting to」做某事，意思是帶着憂慮、緊張或強烈期待等待。"},{"en":"Students may be anxiously waiting to receive their exam results.","zh":"學生可能焦急地等待收到考試成績。"},{"en":"If the result is important, waiting can feel stressful and difficult to ignore.","zh":"如果結果很重要，等待會令人感到壓力大，而且難以忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase shows emotional tension while waiting.","zh":"這個短語顯示等待時的情緒緊張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be called to interview","meaning":"被邀請參加面試","examples":[{"en":"Applicants are waiting to be called to interview.","zh":"申請人正在等待被邀請參加面試。"},{"en":"To be called to interview means to be invited to attend an interview after an application has been reviewed.","zh":"「be called to interview」意思是在申請被審視後，被邀請出席面試。"},{"en":"A job applicant may be called to interview after submitting a strong CV.","zh":"求職者提交出色履歷後，可能被邀請參加面試。"},{"en":"If a student is called to interview, the university wants to assess them in person or online.","zh":"如果學生被邀請參加面試，大學希望親身或網上評估他。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being selected for the next stage of an application.","zh":"這個短語描述被選入申請的下一階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"independent schools","meaning":"私立學校","examples":[{"en":"Independent schools often prepare their candidates carefully for Oxbridge interviews.","zh":"私立學校通常仔細準備其候選人參加牛津劍橋面試。"},{"en":"Independent schools are private schools that are not funded or managed in the same way as state schools.","zh":"「independent schools」是私立學校，並非以公營學校相同方式資助或管理。"},{"en":"Some independent schools offer small classes, extra coaching, and interview practice.","zh":"有些私立學校提供小班教學、額外指導和面試練習。"},{"en":"If a school has more resources, its students may receive more preparation for competitive admissions.","zh":"如果學校有更多資源，其學生可能得到更多競爭性收生準備。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to fee-paying schools in the British education context.","zh":"這個短語在英國教育語境中指收費學校。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"put the final polish on","meaning":"為……作最後潤飾","examples":[{"en":"Independent schools put the final polish on candidates before interview season.","zh":"私立學校在面試季前為候選人作最後潤飾。"},{"en":"To put the final polish on someone or something means to make the last improvements before an important event.","zh":"「put the final polish on」某人或某物，意思是在重要事件前作最後改善。"},{"en":"A student may put the final polish on an essay by checking grammar and word choice.","zh":"學生可能透過檢查文法和用詞，為文章作最後潤飾。"},{"en":"If candidates already have strong knowledge, final polish can help them present themselves better.","zh":"如果候選人已有強大知識，最後潤飾可以幫助他們更好地表現自己。"},{"en":"The phrase describes small finishing touches, not basic training from zero.","zh":"這個短語描述最後的小修飾，而不是由零開始的基礎訓練。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"candidates","meaning":"候選人；申請人","examples":[{"en":"The candidates are preparing for Oxbridge interviews.","zh":"候選人正在準備牛津劍橋面試。"},{"en":"Candidates are people who are applying for a job, course, prize, or position.","zh":"「candidates」是申請工作、課程、獎項或職位的人。"},{"en":"Exam candidates should read the instructions carefully before writing answers.","zh":"考生在寫答案前應仔細閱讀指示。"},{"en":"If candidates prepare well, they can show their abilities more clearly.","zh":"如果候選人準備充分，就能更清楚展示能力。"},{"en":"The word describes people being considered for selection.","zh":"這個詞描述正在被考慮甄選的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"may well have","meaning":"很可能已經……","examples":[{"en":"Some candidates may well have had a year’s intensive preparation.","zh":"有些候選人很可能已經接受了一年密集準備。"},{"en":"May well have means it is quite likely that something has happened.","zh":"「may well have」意思是某事很有可能已經發生。"},{"en":"A student who answers confidently may well have practised the topic many times.","zh":"答得很自信的學生，很可能已經練習該題目很多次。"},{"en":"If someone has had a year of preparation, they may perform more calmly in interview.","zh":"如果某人已有一年準備，他在面試中可能表現得更冷靜。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses strong possibility, not complete certainty.","zh":"這個短語表達很大可能性，而不是完全確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"intensive preparation","meaning":"密集準備","examples":[{"en":"Some applicants have already had a year’s intensive preparation.","zh":"有些申請人已經接受了一年的密集準備。"},{"en":"Intensive preparation means focused and serious practice over a period of time.","zh":"「intensive preparation」意思是在一段時間內進行專注而認真的練習。"},{"en":"A student may need intensive preparation before a public speaking competition.","zh":"學生在公開演講比賽前可能需要密集準備。"},{"en":"If preparation is intensive, candidates may improve knowledge, confidence, and presentation.","zh":"如果準備密集，候選人可能提升知識、信心和表達。"},{"en":"The phrase describes concentrated training rather than casual revision.","zh":"這個短語描述集中訓練，而不是隨意溫習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mock interview","meaning":"模擬面試","examples":[{"en":"A candidate might get a five-minute mock interview with a teacher.","zh":"候選人可能與老師進行五分鐘模擬面試。"},{"en":"A mock interview is a practice interview designed to prepare someone for a real one.","zh":"「mock interview」是為準備正式面試而設的練習面試。"},{"en":"A student may do a mock interview before applying for a scholarship.","zh":"學生在申請獎學金前可能進行模擬面試。"},{"en":"If a mock interview reveals weak answers, the candidate can improve before the real interview.","zh":"如果模擬面試揭示薄弱答案，候選人可以在正式面試前改善。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rehearsal under interview-like conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述在類似面試條件下排練。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"comprehensive school","meaning":"綜合中學","examples":[{"en":"The Cotswold School is a Gloucestershire comprehensive school.","zh":"The Cotswold School 是 Gloucestershire 的一所綜合中學。"},{"en":"A comprehensive school is a state school that accepts students of different academic abilities.","zh":"「comprehensive school」是接收不同學術能力學生的公營學校。"},{"en":"A comprehensive school may teach students who later choose university, work, or vocational training.","zh":"綜合中學可能教育日後選擇大學、工作或職業訓練的學生。"},{"en":"If a comprehensive school has fewer interview resources, outside workshops may help its students.","zh":"如果綜合中學面試資源較少，外來工作坊可能幫助學生。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a non-selective state secondary school in Britain.","zh":"這個短語在英國指非選拔制公營中學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a different story","meaning":"情況不同","examples":[{"en":"At the Cotswold School, it is a different story.","zh":"在 The Cotswold School，情況不同。"},{"en":"A different story means the situation is different from what has just been described.","zh":"「a different story」意思是情況與剛才描述的不同。"},{"en":"Some students have private tutors, but for poorer families it is a different story.","zh":"有些學生有私人補習，但對較貧困家庭而言，情況不同。"},{"en":"If one school has full preparation and another has little support, their candidates face different conditions.","zh":"如果一間學校有充分準備，而另一間支援很少，其候選人面對不同條件。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces contrast.","zh":"這個短語引出對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Oxbridge candidates","meaning":"牛津劍橋申請人","examples":[{"en":"The eight Oxbridge candidates are all boys.","zh":"八名牛津劍橋申請人全都是男生。"},{"en":"Oxbridge candidates are students applying to Oxford or Cambridge.","zh":"「Oxbridge candidates」是申請 Oxford 或 Cambridge 的學生。"},{"en":"Oxbridge candidates may need to prepare for subject questions, personal statements, and interviews.","zh":"牛津劍橋申請人可能需要準備學科問題、個人陳述和面試。"},{"en":"If candidates come from schools with less coaching, social-skills training may feel especially useful.","zh":"如果申請人來自面試指導較少的學校，社交技巧訓練可能特別有用。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies applicants to two highly competitive universities.","zh":"這個短語指出申請兩所高度競爭大學的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be given intensive social grooming","meaning":"接受密集社交禮儀訓練","examples":[{"en":"The boys are being given intensive social grooming before their interviews.","zh":"男生們在面試前正接受密集社交禮儀訓練。"},{"en":"To be given intensive social grooming means to receive focused training in manners, confidence, appearance, and social behaviour.","zh":"「be given intensive social grooming」意思是接受關於禮貌、自信、外表和社交行為的集中訓練。"},{"en":"A school team may be given social grooming before meeting important visitors.","zh":"學校團隊在接待重要訪客前，可能接受社交禮儀訓練。"},{"en":"If students learn how to greet people and sit properly, they may make a stronger first impression.","zh":"如果學生學會如何問候別人和坐得合適，他們可能留下更強第一印象。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical preparation for social situations.","zh":"這個短語描述為社交場合作實際準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"social grooming","meaning":"社交禮儀訓練","examples":[{"en":"Social grooming can help candidates make a better first impression.","zh":"社交禮儀訓練可以幫助候選人留下更好第一印象。"},{"en":"Social grooming is training in manners, appearance, confidence, and behaviour in social situations.","zh":"「social grooming」是在社交場合中的禮貌、外表、自信和行為訓練。"},{"en":"A teenager may receive social grooming before attending a formal dinner.","zh":"青少年在出席正式晚宴前可能接受社交禮儀訓練。"},{"en":"If someone learns polite greetings and body language, they may appear more confident.","zh":"如果某人學會禮貌問候和身體語言，可能顯得更有自信。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on social presentation, not academic knowledge.","zh":"這個短語集中於社交呈現，而不是學術知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"courtesy of","meaning":"由……提供","examples":[{"en":"The boys receive social grooming courtesy of Rachel Holland.","zh":"男生們接受由 Rachel Holland 提供的社交禮儀訓練。"},{"en":"Courtesy of means provided by or thanks to someone.","zh":"「courtesy of」意思是由某人提供，或多虧某人。"},{"en":"The school received new computers courtesy of a local charity.","zh":"學校收到由本地慈善機構提供的新電腦。"},{"en":"If a workshop is offered courtesy of a specialist, students benefit from outside expertise.","zh":"如果工作坊由專家提供，學生就能受惠於外部專業知識。"},{"en":"The phrase gives credit to the person or organisation providing something.","zh":"這個短語把提供某物的人或機構標示出來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"former independent-school maths teacher","meaning":"前私立學校數學老師","examples":[{"en":"Rachel Holland is a former independent-school maths teacher.","zh":"Rachel Holland 是前私立學校數學老師。"},{"en":"A former independent-school maths teacher is someone who used to teach mathematics at a private school.","zh":"「former independent-school maths teacher」是曾在私立學校教授數學的人。"},{"en":"A former maths teacher may understand how students behave in interviews and classrooms.","zh":"前數學老師可能了解學生在面試和課室中的行為。"},{"en":"If a tutor has worked in independent schools, she may know how their pupils are prepared.","zh":"如果導師曾在私立學校工作，她可能知道那裡的學生如何準備。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a person’s previous professional background.","zh":"這個短語描述某人以前的專業背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"housemistress","meaning":"女舍監","examples":[{"en":"Rachel Holland used to work as a housemistress.","zh":"Rachel Holland 以前曾擔任女舍監。"},{"en":"A housemistress is a woman responsible for looking after students in a school boarding house.","zh":"「housemistress」是負責照顧學校宿舍學生的女性。"},{"en":"A housemistress may check students’ behaviour, wellbeing, routines, and manners.","zh":"女舍監可能檢查學生的行為、身心狀況、日常規律和禮貌。"},{"en":"If she has supervised boarders, she may be used to teaching young people social expectations.","zh":"如果她曾管理寄宿生，她可能習慣教年輕人社交期望。"},{"en":"The word describes a pastoral role in boarding-school life.","zh":"這個詞描述寄宿學校生活中的照顧角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"clip along","meaning":"輕快地走來","examples":[{"en":"Rachel Holland clipped along in her high heels to give the boys tuition.","zh":"Rachel Holland 穿着高跟鞋輕快地走來，為男生授課。"},{"en":"To clip along means to walk quickly and energetically, often making a sharp sound with shoes.","zh":"「clip along」意思是快速而有活力地走，鞋子常發出清脆聲音。"},{"en":"A teacher clipped along the corridor when she was late for assembly.","zh":"老師因趕着去早會而在走廊輕快地走過。"},{"en":"If someone clips along in high heels, their movement may sound brisk and confident.","zh":"如果某人穿高跟鞋輕快走路，其動作可能聽起來爽快而自信。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a lively, purposeful way of walking.","zh":"這個短語描述活潑而有目的的走路方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"high heels","meaning":"高跟鞋","examples":[{"en":"She arrived in high heels and a smart outfit.","zh":"她穿着高跟鞋和端莊服裝到來。"},{"en":"High heels are shoes with raised heels, often worn for formal or stylish occasions.","zh":"「high heels」是鞋跟較高的鞋，通常在正式或時尚場合穿着。"},{"en":"A woman may wear high heels to a wedding or formal interview.","zh":"女性可能在婚禮或正式面試中穿高跟鞋。"},{"en":"If high heels are uncomfortable, walking confidently may become harder.","zh":"如果高跟鞋不舒服，自信地走路可能變得更難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a type of shoe associated with appearance and formality.","zh":"這個短語描述一種與外表和正式場合有關的鞋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"smart linen two-piece","meaning":"端莊的亞麻兩件套裝","examples":[{"en":"Rachel Holland wore a smart, pink linen two-piece.","zh":"Rachel Holland 穿着一套端莊的粉紅色亞麻兩件套裝。"},{"en":"A smart linen two-piece is a neat and stylish outfit made of two matching linen garments.","zh":"「smart linen two-piece」是一套由兩件相配亞麻衣物組成、整潔而時尚的服裝。"},{"en":"A candidate might wear a smart two-piece to look polished at an interview.","zh":"候選人可能穿端莊兩件套裝，以在面試中看起來利落。"},{"en":"If clothing looks smart but comfortable, it can help the wearer feel confident.","zh":"如果衣服既端莊又舒適，可以幫助穿着者感到自信。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formal, coordinated clothing.","zh":"這個短語描述正式而配襯的服裝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"give someone tuition in","meaning":"教授某人……","examples":[{"en":"She gave the boys tuition in social skills.","zh":"她教授男生社交技巧。"},{"en":"To give someone tuition in something means to teach or coach them in that subject or skill.","zh":"「give someone tuition in」某事，意思是教授或指導某人該科目或技能。"},{"en":"A tutor may give students tuition in grammar before an English exam.","zh":"導師可能在英文考試前教授學生文法。"},{"en":"If young people receive tuition in social skills, they may handle interviews more confidently.","zh":"如果年輕人接受社交技巧指導，他們可能更自信地應付面試。"},{"en":"The phrase describes focused teaching or coaching.","zh":"這個短語描述集中教學或指導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the lost arts of","meaning":"失傳的技巧","examples":[{"en":"She taught the lost arts of sitting, standing and making small talk.","zh":"她教授坐姿、站姿和寒暄這些失傳的技巧。"},{"en":"The lost arts of something are skills that people used to value but many no longer practise well.","zh":"「the lost arts of」某事，是以前被重視但現在許多人不再熟練實踐的技能。"},{"en":"Letter writing is sometimes called one of the lost arts of modern life.","zh":"寫信有時被稱為現代生活中失傳的技巧之一。"},{"en":"If young people rarely practise formal manners, simple social skills may feel unfamiliar.","zh":"如果年輕人很少練習正式禮儀，簡單社交技巧可能感到陌生。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests old skills that deserve to be learned again.","zh":"這個短語暗示值得重新學習的舊技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"making small talk","meaning":"閒談；寒暄","examples":[{"en":"The boys practised making small talk in pairs and groups.","zh":"男生們兩人或小組練習閒談。"},{"en":"Making small talk means having light, polite conversation about ordinary topics.","zh":"「making small talk」意思是就普通話題進行輕鬆而禮貌的對話。"},{"en":"At a school open day, students may practise making small talk with visiting parents.","zh":"在學校開放日，學生可能練習與來訪家長寒暄。"},{"en":"If people cannot make small talk, the beginning of a meeting may feel awkward.","zh":"如果人們不懂寒暄，會議開始時可能感到尷尬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes friendly conversation before serious discussion.","zh":"這個短語描述正式討論前的友好對話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"dressing well","meaning":"穿着得體","examples":[{"en":"The workshop included advice on dressing well for interviews.","zh":"工作坊包括面試時穿着得體的建議。"},{"en":"Dressing well means choosing clothes that are suitable, neat, and respectful for the situation.","zh":"「dressing well」意思是選擇適合、整潔並尊重場合的衣服。"},{"en":"A student dressing well for a presentation may wear a clean shirt and tidy shoes.","zh":"學生為匯報穿着得體，可能穿乾淨恤衫和整齊鞋子。"},{"en":"If someone dresses too casually for a formal interview, they may create the wrong impression.","zh":"如果某人正式面試時穿得太隨便，可能造成錯誤印象。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on appropriate appearance, not expensive fashion.","zh":"這個短語集中於合適外表，而不是昂貴時裝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hand round canapés","meaning":"傳遞小食","examples":[{"en":"The boys learned how to hand round canapés politely.","zh":"男生們學習如何有禮貌地傳遞小食。"},{"en":"To hand round canapés means to offer small party snacks to people in a polite way.","zh":"「hand round canapés」意思是有禮貌地向人提供派對小食。"},{"en":"At a school reception, students may hand round canapés to guests before speeches begin.","zh":"在學校招待會上，學生可能在演講開始前向賓客傳遞小食。"},{"en":"If someone serves food politely, they show confidence and awareness of others.","zh":"如果某人有禮貌地端送食物，就顯示自信和對他人的意識。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a formal social task.","zh":"這個短語描述正式社交任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it might sound the sort of thing that","meaning":"這聽起來像是……的事情","examples":[{"en":"It might sound the sort of thing that teenagers would not enjoy.","zh":"這聽起來像是青少年不會喜歡的事情。"},{"en":"It might sound the sort of thing that means it may seem like a particular kind of activity at first.","zh":"「it might sound the sort of thing that」意思是起初聽起來像某類活動。"},{"en":"Grammar practice might sound the sort of thing that students would find boring, but games can make it lively.","zh":"文法練習聽起來像是學生會覺得沉悶的事情，但遊戲可以令它生動。"},{"en":"If an activity sounds dull at first, good teaching can still make it useful and enjoyable.","zh":"如果活動起初聽起來沉悶，好的教學仍可令它有用又有趣。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an expected impression that may be wrong.","zh":"這個短語引出一種可能錯誤的預期印象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sceptical teenagers","meaning":"持懷疑態度的青少年","examples":[{"en":"Sceptical teenagers might roll their eyes at social-skills training.","zh":"持懷疑態度的青少年可能會對社交技巧訓練翻白眼。"},{"en":"Sceptical teenagers are young people who doubt whether something is useful or true.","zh":"「sceptical teenagers」是懷疑某事是否有用或真實的年輕人。"},{"en":"Sceptical teenagers may not believe a workshop will help until they try it themselves.","zh":"持懷疑態度的青少年可能在親自嘗試前，不相信工作坊有幫助。"},{"en":"If teenagers are sceptical, the teacher needs clear examples rather than long lectures.","zh":"如果青少年持懷疑態度，老師需要清楚例子，而不是長篇講課。"},{"en":"The phrase describes young people who are doubtful or unconvinced.","zh":"這個短語描述懷疑或未被說服的年輕人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"loll in chairs","meaning":"懶洋洋地癱坐在椅上","examples":[{"en":"Teenagers might be expected to loll in chairs during such a workshop.","zh":"人們可能預期青少年在這類工作坊中懶洋洋地癱坐在椅上。"},{"en":"To loll in chairs means to sit lazily or carelessly, often with poor posture.","zh":"「loll in chairs」意思是懶散或不端正地坐在椅上，通常姿勢不好。"},{"en":"A tired student may loll in a chair after a long sports lesson.","zh":"疲倦的學生在一節長體育課後可能懶洋洋地癱坐在椅上。"},{"en":"If a candidate lolls in a chair before an interview, they may look uninterested.","zh":"如果候選人在面試前癱坐在椅上，可能顯得不感興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes relaxed sitting that can appear rude in formal situations.","zh":"這個短語描述放鬆坐姿，但在正式場合可能顯得無禮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"roll one’s eyes skywards","meaning":"翻白眼望天","examples":[{"en":"Some teenagers might roll their eyes skywards at etiquette training.","zh":"有些青少年可能會對禮儀訓練翻白眼望天。"},{"en":"To roll one’s eyes skywards means to look upward in a way that shows annoyance, disbelief, or boredom.","zh":"「roll one’s eyes skywards」意思是向上翻眼，以表示厭煩、不相信或沉悶。"},{"en":"A student may roll their eyes skywards when reminded again to tidy the desk.","zh":"學生再次被提醒整理書桌時，可能翻白眼望天。"},{"en":"If teenagers roll their eyes, they may be showing that they think the lesson is unnecessary.","zh":"如果青少年翻白眼，他們可能在表示覺得課堂不必要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a visible sign of impatience or scepticism.","zh":"這個短語描述不耐煩或懷疑的可見表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"warm and engaging","meaning":"熱情而有吸引力","examples":[{"en":"Rachel Holland is described as warm and engaging.","zh":"Rachel Holland 被形容為熱情而有吸引力。"},{"en":"Warm and engaging means friendly, approachable, and able to hold people’s interest.","zh":"「warm and engaging」意思是友善、容易親近，並能吸引人注意。"},{"en":"A warm and engaging teacher can make shy students feel safe enough to speak.","zh":"熱情而有吸引力的老師可以令害羞學生感到安全，願意開口。"},{"en":"If a trainer is engaging, sceptical students may start to listen and participate.","zh":"如果導師有吸引力，持懷疑態度的學生可能開始聆聽和參與。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a pleasant and effective personal style.","zh":"這個短語描述令人舒服而有效的個人風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"funny and direct","meaning":"幽默而直接","examples":[{"en":"Her style is funny and direct.","zh":"她的風格幽默而直接。"},{"en":"Funny and direct means humorous but also clear and honest.","zh":"「funny and direct」意思是幽默，同時清楚而坦率。"},{"en":"A funny and direct coach can correct mistakes without making students feel attacked.","zh":"幽默而直接的教練可以糾正錯誤，而不令學生覺得被攻擊。"},{"en":"If advice is direct, learners understand quickly what they should change.","zh":"如果建議直接，學習者很快明白自己應改變甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes communication that is lively and straightforward.","zh":"這個短語描述生動而坦率的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tell someone bluntly","meaning":"直截了當地告訴某人","examples":[{"en":"She tells the boys bluntly that people judge others quickly.","zh":"她直截了當地告訴男生，人們很快評價別人。"},{"en":"To tell someone bluntly means to say something directly, without softening it much.","zh":"「tell someone bluntly」意思是直接說出某事，沒有太多修飾。"},{"en":"A doctor may tell a patient bluntly that smoking is damaging their lungs.","zh":"醫生可能直截了當地告訴病人，吸煙正在傷害肺部。"},{"en":"If advice is blunt, it may feel uncomfortable but can be very clear.","zh":"如果建議直率，可能令人不舒服，但可以非常清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes honest, direct speech.","zh":"這個短語描述坦白直接的說話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"judge others within a few seconds","meaning":"在幾秒內評價別人","examples":[{"en":"People often judge others within a few seconds of meeting them.","zh":"人們常在見面幾秒內評價別人。"},{"en":"To judge others within a few seconds means to form an opinion about someone almost immediately.","zh":"「judge others within a few seconds」意思是幾乎立即對某人形成看法。"},{"en":"Interviewers may judge a candidate within a few seconds from posture, greeting, and eye contact.","zh":"面試官可能在幾秒內根據姿勢、問候和眼神接觸評價候選人。"},{"en":"If first impressions form quickly, small details can affect how people are received.","zh":"如果第一印象很快形成，細節就會影響別人如何接收你。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why appearance and behaviour at the beginning matter.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何開頭的外表和行為重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"first impressions","meaning":"第一印象","examples":[{"en":"First impressions are vital in an interview.","zh":"第一印象在面試中至關重要。"},{"en":"First impressions are the early opinions people form when they first meet someone.","zh":"「first impressions」是人們首次見面時形成的早期看法。"},{"en":"A clean uniform and polite greeting can create a good first impression at school.","zh":"乾淨校服和禮貌問候可以在學校創造良好第一印象。"},{"en":"If the first impression is poor, the speaker may need extra effort to recover trust.","zh":"如果第一印象差，說話者可能需要額外努力恢復信任。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the immediate effect someone has on others.","zh":"這個短語描述某人對他人造成的即時效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be vital","meaning":"至關重要","examples":[{"en":"First impressions are vital when meeting interviewers.","zh":"與面試官見面時，第一印象至關重要。"},{"en":"To be vital means to be extremely important or necessary.","zh":"「be vital」意思是極其重要或必要。"},{"en":"Sleep is vital before an exam because tired students think less clearly.","zh":"考試前睡眠至關重要，因為疲倦學生思考較不清晰。"},{"en":"If a skill is vital, failing to practise it can seriously affect the result.","zh":"如果一項技能至關重要，不練習它會嚴重影響結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that matters greatly.","zh":"這個短語描述非常重要的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"step-by-step","meaning":"逐步地","examples":[{"en":"Step-by-step, Rachel Holland teaches the group how to meet people properly.","zh":"Rachel Holland 逐步地教導小組如何正確與人見面。"},{"en":"Step-by-step means gradually, one stage at a time.","zh":"「step-by-step」意思是逐漸地，一步一步進行。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain essay writing step-by-step, from planning to proofreading.","zh":"老師可能逐步地解釋作文，由規劃到校對。"},{"en":"If a difficult skill is taught step-by-step, students feel less overwhelmed.","zh":"如果困難技能逐步教授，學生就較不會感到不知所措。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a clear and ordered method.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚而有次序的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take someone through","meaning":"帶領某人學習……","examples":[{"en":"She takes the group through a good meet and greet.","zh":"她帶領小組學習良好的見面問候。"},{"en":"To take someone through something means to guide them carefully through each part of a process.","zh":"「take someone through」某事，意思是仔細帶領某人完成一個過程的每部分。"},{"en":"A coach may take new employees through the safety rules on their first day.","zh":"教練可能在新員工第一天帶領他們學習安全規則。"},{"en":"If students are taken through each step, they know exactly what to do.","zh":"如果學生被逐步帶領，他們就清楚知道要做甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes guided instruction.","zh":"這個短語描述有指引的教學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"meet and greet","meaning":"見面問候","examples":[{"en":"The boys practise a good meet and greet before entering the room.","zh":"男生們在進房前練習良好的見面問候。"},{"en":"A meet and greet is the first polite exchange when people meet, including smiling, greeting, and shaking hands.","zh":"「meet and greet」是人們見面時的最初禮貌交流，包括微笑、問候和握手。"},{"en":"At a school event, student helpers may do a meet and greet with visitors at the door.","zh":"在學校活動中，學生助手可能在門口與訪客見面問候。"},{"en":"If the meet and greet goes well, the conversation begins more smoothly.","zh":"如果見面問候順利，對話開始時會更流暢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the opening stage of meeting someone.","zh":"這個短語描述與人見面的開場階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"make eye contact","meaning":"眼神接觸","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should smile and make eye contact.","zh":"候選人應微笑並有眼神接觸。"},{"en":"To make eye contact means to look at another person’s eyes while communicating.","zh":"「make eye contact」意思是在溝通時看着對方眼睛。"},{"en":"A speaker can make eye contact with the audience to show confidence.","zh":"演講者可以與觀眾作眼神接觸，以顯示自信。"},{"en":"If a candidate never makes eye contact, they may appear nervous or uninterested.","zh":"如果候選人從不作眼神接觸，可能顯得緊張或不感興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common sign of attention and confidence.","zh":"這個短語描述注意力和自信的常見標誌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"give a firm handshake","meaning":"握手有力","examples":[{"en":"She teaches the boys how to give a firm handshake.","zh":"她教男生如何握手有力。"},{"en":"To give a firm handshake means to shake someone’s hand with steady, confident pressure.","zh":"「give a firm handshake」意思是以穩定而自信的力度與人握手。"},{"en":"At a job interview, a firm handshake can help create a professional first impression.","zh":"在求職面試中，有力握手可以幫助建立專業第一印象。"},{"en":"If a handshake is too weak or too forceful, it may feel awkward.","zh":"如果握手太弱或太用力，可能令人尷尬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a polite physical greeting.","zh":"這個短語描述一種禮貌的身體問候。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a no-no","meaning":"不應做的事；禁忌","examples":[{"en":"Lolling in chairs is a no-no before an interview.","zh":"面試前懶洋洋地癱坐在椅上是不應做的事。"},{"en":"A no-no is something that should not be done because it is inappropriate or unacceptable.","zh":"「a no-no」是不應做的事，因為它不合適或不可接受。"},{"en":"Checking your phone during a formal dinner is usually a no-no.","zh":"在正式晚宴中看電話通常是禁忌。"},{"en":"If candidates break a social no-no, they may appear careless or rude.","zh":"如果候選人觸犯社交禁忌，可能顯得粗心或無禮。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a clear social rule against an action.","zh":"這個短語描述反對某行動的清楚社交規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"interview room","meaning":"面試室","examples":[{"en":"Candidates may be judged before they enter the interview room.","zh":"候選人可能在進入面試室前已被評價。"},{"en":"An interview room is the place where an interview takes place.","zh":"「interview room」是面試進行的地方。"},{"en":"A student may wait outside the interview room until the panel is ready.","zh":"學生可能在面試室外等待，直到面試小組準備好。"},{"en":"If behaviour before entering the room is noticed, candidates should remain polite from the start.","zh":"如果進房前的行為也被注意，候選人一開始就應保持禮貌。"},{"en":"The phrase names the physical setting of an interview.","zh":"這個短語指出面試的實體場景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sit with one’s legs far apart","meaning":"雙腿分得很開地坐","examples":[{"en":"She tells the boys not to sit with their legs far apart.","zh":"她告訴男生不要雙腿分得很開地坐。"},{"en":"To sit with one’s legs far apart means to sit with the knees or feet widely spread.","zh":"「sit with one’s legs far apart」意思是坐着時膝蓋或雙腳張得很開。"},{"en":"On a crowded bus, sitting with legs far apart can seem rude because it takes extra space.","zh":"在擠迫巴士上，雙腿分得很開地坐可能顯得無禮，因為佔用額外空間。"},{"en":"If a candidate sits too casually, interviewers may think they lack respect for the occasion.","zh":"如果候選人坐得太隨便，面試官可能覺得他不尊重場合。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a posture that may appear too relaxed in formal settings.","zh":"這個短語描述在正式場合可能顯得太放鬆的姿勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"enter an interview room","meaning":"進入面試室","examples":[{"en":"Rachel Holland demonstrates how to enter an interview room.","zh":"Rachel Holland 示範如何進入面試室。"},{"en":"To enter an interview room means to go into the place where the interviewers are waiting.","zh":"「enter an interview room」意思是走進面試官等待的地方。"},{"en":"A candidate should pause, smile, and enter the interview room calmly.","zh":"候選人應停一停、微笑，然後冷靜地進入面試室。"},{"en":"If the entrance is confident, the interview can begin with a stronger first impression.","zh":"如果進場自信，面試就能以更強第一印象開始。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the first visible action in an interview situation.","zh":"這個短語描述面試情境中的第一個可見動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"demonstrate","meaning":"示範","examples":[{"en":"She demonstrates how to enter the room confidently.","zh":"她示範如何自信地進入房間。"},{"en":"To demonstrate means to show how something is done by doing it or explaining it clearly.","zh":"「demonstrate」意思是透過親自做或清楚解釋來展示某事如何進行。"},{"en":"A science teacher may demonstrate an experiment before students try it themselves.","zh":"科學老師可能在學生自己嘗試前示範實驗。"},{"en":"If a trainer demonstrates a skill, learners can copy the action more easily.","zh":"如果導師示範一項技能，學習者就能更容易模仿動作。"},{"en":"The word describes teaching by showing.","zh":"這個詞描述透過展示來教學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mime doing something","meaning":"用動作模仿做某事","examples":[{"en":"She mimes closing the door quietly behind her.","zh":"她用動作模仿在身後輕輕關門。"},{"en":"To mime doing something means to act it out without actually doing it or speaking.","zh":"「mime doing something」意思是不真正做或不說話，而用動作演出某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may mime opening an umbrella to teach the word “umbrella”.","zh":"老師可能用動作模仿打開雨傘，以教授 “umbrella” 這個詞。"},{"en":"If learners see a gesture, they may understand the action faster than through explanation alone.","zh":"如果學習者看見手勢，可能比單靠解釋更快理解動作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes silent acting of an action.","zh":"這個短語描述無聲地表演一個動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"close the door quietly","meaning":"輕輕關門","examples":[{"en":"A candidate should close the door quietly behind him or her.","zh":"候選人應在身後輕輕關門。"},{"en":"To close the door quietly means to shut it gently without making a loud sound.","zh":"「close the door quietly」意思是輕柔地關上門，不發出巨大聲響。"},{"en":"Students should close the classroom door quietly when a lesson has already started.","zh":"如果課堂已開始，學生應輕輕關上課室門。"},{"en":"If someone slams the door before an interview, it may create a poor first impression.","zh":"如果某人在面試前大力關門，可能造成差的第一印象。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small action that shows care and manners.","zh":"這個短語描述顯示細心和禮貌的小動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"smile warmly","meaning":"親切地微笑","examples":[{"en":"She enters the room while smiling warmly.","zh":"她親切地微笑着進入房間。"},{"en":"To smile warmly means to smile in a friendly and sincere way.","zh":"「smile warmly」意思是以友善而真誠的方式微笑。"},{"en":"A receptionist may smile warmly to make visitors feel welcome.","zh":"接待員可能親切地微笑，令訪客感到受歡迎。"},{"en":"If a candidate smiles warmly, the interview may begin with less tension.","zh":"如果候選人親切地微笑，面試開始時可能較少緊張。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a facial expression that creates friendliness.","zh":"這個短語描述營造友善感的面部表情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"walk confidently across","meaning":"自信地走過","examples":[{"en":"She walks confidently across the carpet.","zh":"她自信地走過地氈。"},{"en":"To walk confidently across a place means to move through it with steady posture and self-assurance.","zh":"「walk confidently across」某地，意思是以穩定姿勢和自信穿過它。"},{"en":"A speaker should walk confidently across the stage before beginning a presentation.","zh":"演講者在開始匯報前應自信地走過舞台。"},{"en":"If someone walks with confidence, others may assume they are prepared.","zh":"如果某人走路有自信，別人可能認為他已有準備。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement that signals self-belief.","zh":"這個短語描述傳達自信的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"shake each interviewer’s hand","meaning":"與每位面試官握手","examples":[{"en":"The candidate should shake each interviewer’s hand.","zh":"候選人應與每位面試官握手。"},{"en":"To shake each interviewer’s hand means to greet every interviewer individually with a handshake.","zh":"「shake each interviewer’s hand」意思是用握手逐一問候每位面試官。"},{"en":"At a panel interview, a candidate may shake each interviewer’s hand before sitting down.","zh":"在小組面試中，候選人可能坐下前與每位面試官握手。"},{"en":"If there are several interviewers, greeting each one can show confidence and respect.","zh":"如果有幾位面試官，逐一問候可顯示自信和尊重。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a formal greeting with every person present.","zh":"這個短語描述與在場每個人作正式問候。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"over and over again","meaning":"一遍又一遍地","examples":[{"en":"The boys practise the entrance over and over again.","zh":"男生們一遍又一遍地練習進場。"},{"en":"Over and over again means many times repeatedly.","zh":"「over and over again」意思是多次重複地。"},{"en":"A pianist plays the same difficult bar over and over again until it sounds smooth.","zh":"鋼琴學生一遍又一遍地彈同一段困難小節，直到聽起來流暢。"},{"en":"If students repeat a skill many times, it can become natural under pressure.","zh":"如果學生多次重複一項技能，在壓力下它就能變得自然。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated practice.","zh":"這個短語描述重複練習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"head up","meaning":"抬起頭","examples":[{"en":"Rachel reminds the boys to keep their head up.","zh":"Rachel 提醒男生們抬起頭。"},{"en":"To keep your head up means to hold your head upright instead of looking down.","zh":"「keep your head up」意思是把頭保持挺直，而不是低頭。"},{"en":"A speaker with their head up looks more confident than one staring at the floor.","zh":"抬起頭的演講者比盯着地板的人看起來更自信。"},{"en":"If a candidate keeps their head up, they can make better eye contact.","zh":"如果候選人抬起頭，就能有更好的眼神接觸。"},{"en":"The phrase describes posture that suggests confidence.","zh":"這個短語描述顯示自信的姿勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"don’t rush it","meaning":"不要急","examples":[{"en":"She tells the boys, “Don’t rush it.”","zh":"她告訴男生：「不要急。」"},{"en":"Don’t rush it means do not hurry through the action too quickly.","zh":"「Don’t rush it」意思是不要太快匆忙完成動作。"},{"en":"A teacher may say “Don’t rush it” when a student is reading instructions carelessly.","zh":"當學生粗心閱讀指示時，老師可能說「不要急」。"},{"en":"If candidates rush their entrance, they may seem nervous and uncontrolled.","zh":"如果候選人匆忙進場，可能顯得緊張和失控。"},{"en":"The phrase encourages calm and controlled timing.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵冷靜和受控制的節奏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"turn and sit down","meaning":"轉身坐下","examples":[{"en":"The boys practise how to turn and sit down properly.","zh":"男生們練習如何正確轉身坐下。"},{"en":"To turn and sit down means to rotate your body and take a seat in a controlled way.","zh":"「turn and sit down」意思是轉動身體並以受控方式坐下。"},{"en":"In a formal interview, a candidate should turn and sit down calmly after being invited.","zh":"在正式面試中，候選人應在獲邀後冷靜地轉身坐下。"},{"en":"If someone drops into a chair carelessly, they may look too casual.","zh":"如果某人隨便跌坐在椅上，可能顯得太隨便。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small movement that affects body language.","zh":"這個短語描述影響身體語言的小動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not until you’re invited to","meaning":"直到獲邀請才……","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should not sit down until they are invited to.","zh":"候選人應直到獲邀請才坐下。"},{"en":"Not until you’re invited to means only after someone gives permission.","zh":"「not until you’re invited to」意思是只有在別人給予許可後才做。"},{"en":"At a formal dinner, guests may not begin eating until they are invited to.","zh":"在正式晚宴上，客人可能要直到獲邀請才開始用餐。"},{"en":"If candidates wait to be invited, they show respect for the interview setting.","zh":"如果候選人等到獲邀請才坐下，就顯示尊重面試場合。"},{"en":"The phrase describes polite restraint.","zh":"這個短語描述有禮貌的克制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have had a bad day","meaning":"過了很糟的一天","examples":[{"en":"She asks the boys to imagine that their interviewers have had a bad day.","zh":"她要求男生想像面試官過了很糟的一天。"},{"en":"To have had a bad day means to have experienced a difficult, tiring, or unpleasant day.","zh":"「have had a bad day」意思是經歷了困難、疲倦或不愉快的一天。"},{"en":"A teacher who has had a bad day may still appreciate a student’s polite greeting.","zh":"過了很糟一天的老師，仍可能欣賞學生有禮貌的問候。"},{"en":"If interviewers are tired, a cheerful entrance can improve the atmosphere.","zh":"如果面試官疲倦，愉快的進場可以改善氣氛。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds candidates to consider other people’s mood.","zh":"這個短語提醒候選人考慮別人的心情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"brighten it up for someone","meaning":"令某人的一天變得愉快","examples":[{"en":"A confident candidate can brighten it up for the interviewers.","zh":"自信的候選人可以令面試官的一天變得愉快。"},{"en":"To brighten it up for someone means to make their day, mood, or situation more pleasant.","zh":"「brighten it up for someone」意思是令某人的一天、心情或情況更愉快。"},{"en":"A friendly thank-you note can brighten up a teacher’s difficult afternoon.","zh":"一張友善感謝便條可以令老師艱難的下午變得愉快。"},{"en":"If a candidate enters warmly, the room may feel more positive.","zh":"如果候選人親切進場，房間氣氛可能更正面。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improving someone’s mood or atmosphere.","zh":"這個短語描述改善某人的心情或氣氛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"announce to someone that","meaning":"向某人宣告……","examples":[{"en":"Your entrance should announce to the interviewers that you are present and confident.","zh":"你的進場應向面試官宣告你已到場並且自信。"},{"en":"To announce to someone that means to make something clearly known, either by words or behaviour.","zh":"「announce to someone that」意思是透過說話或行為清楚讓某人知道某事。"},{"en":"A tidy uniform can announce to teachers that a student takes the event seriously.","zh":"整齊校服可以向老師宣告學生認真看待活動。"},{"en":"If body language announces confidence, interviewers may pay closer attention.","zh":"如果身體語言宣告自信，面試官可能更留意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sending a clear message.","zh":"這個短語描述傳達清楚訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Here I am","meaning":"我來了","examples":[{"en":"A confident entrance says, “Here I am.”","zh":"自信的進場像是在說：「我來了。」"},{"en":"Here I am means I am present, ready, and asking to be noticed.","zh":"「Here I am」意思是我已到場、準備好了，並希望被注意。"},{"en":"A performer walking onto the stage with confidence seems to say, “Here I am.”","zh":"表演者自信地走上舞台時，似乎在說：「我來了。」"},{"en":"If a candidate’s entrance feels strong, it can show readiness before any answer is given.","zh":"如果候選人的進場有力量，未回答任何問題前已能顯示準備好。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses presence and self-assurance.","zh":"這個短語表達存在感和自信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"so-and-so","meaning":"某某人","examples":[{"en":"The candidate can say, “I’m so-and-so, and I’m pleased to see you.”","zh":"候選人可以說：「我是某某人，很高興見到你。」"},{"en":"So-and-so is a placeholder used instead of a person’s real name.","zh":"「so-and-so」是用來代替真人姓名的佔位詞。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “Imagine you are so-and-so in the story,” before a role-play.","zh":"老師在角色扮演前可能說：「想像你是故事中的某某人。」"},{"en":"If the real name is not important, “so-and-so” can stand in for any person.","zh":"如果真實姓名不重要，「so-and-so」可以代表任何人。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and means an unspecified person.","zh":"這個短語較口語，意思是未具名的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be pleased to see someone","meaning":"很高興見到某人","examples":[{"en":"A candidate should show that he or she is pleased to see the interviewers.","zh":"候選人應表現出很高興見到面試官。"},{"en":"To be pleased to see someone means to feel happy or glad to meet them.","zh":"「be pleased to see someone」意思是見到某人時感到高興。"},{"en":"A receptionist should look pleased to see visitors when they arrive.","zh":"接待員在訪客到達時應看起來很高興見到他們。"},{"en":"If candidates seem pleased to meet interviewers, the atmosphere becomes warmer.","zh":"如果候選人看似很高興見到面試官，氣氛會變得更溫暖。"},{"en":"The phrase describes friendly enjoyment at meeting someone.","zh":"這個短語描述見到某人時的友善喜悅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pay attention to me","meaning":"注意我","examples":[{"en":"The entrance should make the interviewers pay attention to the candidate.","zh":"進場應令面試官注意候選人。"},{"en":"Pay attention to me means notice me and focus on what I am doing or saying.","zh":"「pay attention to me」意思是留意我並專注於我正在做或說的事。"},{"en":"A student raising a hand calmly is asking the teacher to pay attention to them.","zh":"學生冷靜地舉手，是在要求老師注意他。"},{"en":"If a candidate enters confidently, interviewers may become more ready to listen.","zh":"如果候選人自信進場，面試官可能更準備聆聽。"},{"en":"The phrase describes attracting someone’s focus.","zh":"這個短語描述吸引某人的注意力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"want one’s place","meaning":"想獲得自己的學位","examples":[{"en":"A strong candidate gives the impression that he or she wants a place.","zh":"強勢候選人會給人一種他或她想獲得學位的印象。"},{"en":"To want one’s place means to strongly desire admission, acceptance, or a position.","zh":"「want one’s place」意思是強烈希望獲得取錄、接納或職位。"},{"en":"A scholarship applicant should show clearly that they want the place and understand the opportunity.","zh":"獎學金申請人應清楚顯示自己想獲得名額並理解機會。"},{"en":"If candidates look uninterested, interviewers may doubt their motivation.","zh":"如果候選人看起來不感興趣，面試官可能懷疑其動機。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visible desire for a position.","zh":"這個短語描述對位置的可見渴望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"set up","meaning":"創立；成立","examples":[{"en":"Rachel Holland set up a company to teach social skills.","zh":"Rachel Holland 創立了一間公司教授社交技巧。"},{"en":"To set up a company means to start or establish it.","zh":"「set up」公司，意思是創辦或成立它。"},{"en":"Two graduates may set up a tutoring business after leaving university.","zh":"兩名畢業生可能在大學畢業後創立補習業務。"},{"en":"If a service becomes popular, the founder may set up a company to offer it formally.","zh":"如果服務變得受歡迎，創辦人可能成立公司正式提供它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating an organisation or system.","zh":"這個短語描述建立組織或制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"social skills","meaning":"社交技巧","examples":[{"en":"Rachel Holland teaches social skills to young people.","zh":"Rachel Holland 向年輕人教授社交技巧。"},{"en":"Social skills are the abilities people use to communicate, behave politely, and interact with others.","zh":"「social skills」是人們用來溝通、有禮貌地行為和與他人互動的能力。"},{"en":"Group projects help students practise social skills such as listening and taking turns.","zh":"小組專題幫助學生練習聆聽和輪流發言等社交技巧。"},{"en":"If social skills are weak, interviews and formal events may feel more difficult.","zh":"如果社交技巧薄弱，面試和正式活動可能感覺更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical skills for dealing with people.","zh":"這個短語描述與人相處的實用技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"realise the popularity of","meaning":"意識到……受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"She realised the popularity of the workshops she had devised.","zh":"她意識到自己設計的工作坊很受歡迎。"},{"en":"To realise the popularity of something means to become aware that many people like or want it.","zh":"「realise the popularity of」某物，意思是察覺很多人喜歡或想要它。"},{"en":"A teacher may realise the popularity of a grammar game when students ask to play it again.","zh":"當學生要求再玩一次文法遊戲，老師可能意識到它受歡迎。"},{"en":"If a course becomes popular, the creator may decide to offer it more widely.","zh":"如果課程變得受歡迎，創作者可能決定更廣泛提供。"},{"en":"The phrase describes noticing demand or approval.","zh":"這個短語描述注意到需求或認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"devise workshops","meaning":"設計工作坊","examples":[{"en":"She devised workshops for pupils at Millfield.","zh":"她為 Millfield 的學生設計工作坊。"},{"en":"To devise workshops means to design and plan training sessions or learning activities.","zh":"「devise workshops」意思是設計和規劃培訓課或學習活動。"},{"en":"A school counsellor may devise workshops on stress management before exam season.","zh":"學校輔導員可能在考試季前設計壓力管理工作坊。"},{"en":"If students need practical skills, workshops can be designed around real situations.","zh":"如果學生需要實用技能，工作坊可以圍繞真實情境設計。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating structured learning sessions.","zh":"這個短語描述創造有結構的學習課程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pupils","meaning":"學生","examples":[{"en":"She first devised the workshops for school pupils.","zh":"她最初為學校學生設計這些工作坊。"},{"en":"Pupils are children or young people who are taught in a school.","zh":"「pupils」是在學校接受教育的兒童或年輕人。"},{"en":"Primary pupils may need simple examples when learning formal manners.","zh":"小學生學正式禮儀時，可能需要簡單例子。"},{"en":"If pupils practise social skills early, they may feel more confident later.","zh":"如果學生早些練習社交技巧，日後可能更有信心。"},{"en":"The word is common in British English for school students.","zh":"這個詞在英式英語中常指學校學生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"range from…to…","meaning":"範圍由……至……","examples":[{"en":"Her courses range from basic manners for children to etiquette for school leavers.","zh":"她的課程範圍由兒童基本禮貌至離校生禮儀。"},{"en":"Range from A to B means to include many types between two examples or limits.","zh":"「range from A to B」意思是包括兩個例子或界限之間的許多種類。"},{"en":"A school fair may include activities ranging from games to charity stalls.","zh":"學校嘉年華活動可能範圍由遊戲至慈善攤位。"},{"en":"If a course range is wide, students of different ages can find something useful.","zh":"如果課程範圍很廣，不同年齡學生都能找到有用內容。"},{"en":"The phrase shows variety across a scale.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個範圍上的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"three-hour workshop","meaning":"三小時工作坊","examples":[{"en":"One course is a three-hour workshop on basic manners.","zh":"其中一個課程是關於基本禮貌的三小時工作坊。"},{"en":"A three-hour workshop is a training session that lasts for three hours.","zh":"「three-hour workshop」是持續三小時的培訓課。"},{"en":"A school may run a three-hour workshop on interview skills after exams.","zh":"學校可能在考試後舉辦三小時面試技巧工作坊。"},{"en":"If a workshop is short but focused, students can learn practical steps quickly.","zh":"如果工作坊短但集中，學生可以快速學到實用步驟。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the length and format of a learning session.","zh":"這個短語描述學習課程的時長和形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"basic manners","meaning":"基本禮貌","examples":[{"en":"Younger children can take a workshop on basic manners.","zh":"較年幼的孩子可以參加基本禮貌工作坊。"},{"en":"Basic manners are simple polite behaviours such as saying please, listening, and greeting people properly.","zh":"「basic manners」是簡單有禮行為，例如說請、聆聽和正確問候別人。"},{"en":"Parents teach basic manners when they remind children to thank relatives for gifts.","zh":"父母提醒孩子為禮物感謝親人時，就是教授基本禮貌。"},{"en":"If children learn basic manners early, they handle school and social situations more smoothly.","zh":"如果孩子早些學習基本禮貌，他們會更順利應付學校和社交場合。"},{"en":"The phrase describes everyday politeness.","zh":"這個短語描述日常禮貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"one-term course","meaning":"一學期課程","examples":[{"en":"School leavers can take a one-term course on etiquette and life skills.","zh":"離校生可以修讀一學期禮儀和生活技能課程。"},{"en":"A one-term course is a course that lasts for one school term.","zh":"「one-term course」是持續一個學期的課程。"},{"en":"A language school may offer a one-term course in business English.","zh":"語言學校可能提供一學期商務英語課程。"},{"en":"If a topic needs practice over time, a one-term course may work better than a single lesson.","zh":"如果題目需要長時間練習，一學期課程可能比單一課堂更有效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a course length in a school calendar.","zh":"這個短語描述學校日曆中的課程長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"school leavers","meaning":"離校生","examples":[{"en":"School leavers may need practical social and life skills.","zh":"離校生可能需要實用社交和生活技能。"},{"en":"School leavers are young people who are about to leave school or have just left school.","zh":"「school leavers」是即將離校或剛離校的年輕人。"},{"en":"School leavers may need advice on interviews, work clothes, and managing money.","zh":"離校生可能需要面試、工作服裝和理財方面的建議。"},{"en":"If school leavers lack social confidence, entering work or university can feel harder.","zh":"如果離校生缺乏社交信心，進入工作或大學可能感覺更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to students at the transition from school to adult life.","zh":"這個短語指處於由學校過渡到成人生活階段的學生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"etiquette and life skills","meaning":"禮儀和生活技能","examples":[{"en":"The course teaches etiquette and life skills.","zh":"該課程教授禮儀和生活技能。"},{"en":"Etiquette and life skills are polite social rules and practical abilities needed in daily adult life.","zh":"「etiquette and life skills」是成人日常生活所需的社交禮貌規則和實用能力。"},{"en":"A course on etiquette and life skills may teach table manners, interview behaviour, and thank-you letters.","zh":"禮儀和生活技能課程可能教授餐桌禮儀、面試行為和感謝信。"},{"en":"If young people learn these skills, they may feel less lost in formal situations.","zh":"如果年輕人學會這些技能，在正式場合可能較不迷惘。"},{"en":"The phrase combines social manners with practical independence.","zh":"這個短語結合社交禮儀和實際獨立能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cover all aspects of","meaning":"涵蓋……的所有方面","examples":[{"en":"The course covers all aspects of modern life.","zh":"該課程涵蓋現代生活的所有方面。"},{"en":"To cover all aspects of something means to include every main part or area of it.","zh":"「cover all aspects of」某事，意思是包括它的每個主要部分或範疇。"},{"en":"A health course may cover all aspects of wellbeing, from sleep to diet and exercise.","zh":"健康課程可能涵蓋身心健康的所有方面，由睡眠到飲食和運動。"},{"en":"If a course covers many social situations, students can use the skills in real life.","zh":"如果課程涵蓋許多社交情境，學生就能在現實生活中使用技能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad and complete coverage.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛而完整的涵蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"modern life","meaning":"現代生活","examples":[{"en":"The course covers many social situations in modern life.","zh":"該課程涵蓋現代生活中的許多社交情況。"},{"en":"Modern life means the way people live today, including work, school, technology, and social habits.","zh":"「modern life」意思是今天人們的生活方式，包括工作、學校、科技和社交習慣。"},{"en":"Mobile phones are now a normal part of modern life.","zh":"手提電話現在是現代生活的正常部分。"},{"en":"If modern life includes more interviews and networking, social skills become more useful.","zh":"如果現代生活包括更多面試和人際網絡，社交技巧就變得更有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes present-day living conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述現今生活條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"accept a compliment","meaning":"接受讚美","examples":[{"en":"The course teaches students how to accept a compliment.","zh":"該課程教學生如何接受讚美。"},{"en":"To accept a compliment means to respond politely when someone says something positive about you.","zh":"「accept a compliment」意思是當別人說你正面好話時，有禮貌地回應。"},{"en":"If a teacher praises your presentation, you can accept the compliment by saying thank you.","zh":"如果老師稱讚你的匯報，你可以說謝謝來接受讚美。"},{"en":"If someone rejects every compliment, the other person may feel awkward.","zh":"如果某人拒絕每句讚美，對方可能感到尷尬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a polite response to praise.","zh":"這個短語描述對讚賞的禮貌回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"write a thank-you letter","meaning":"寫感謝信","examples":[{"en":"Students learn how to write a thank-you letter.","zh":"學生學習如何寫感謝信。"},{"en":"To write a thank-you letter means to send a written message expressing gratitude.","zh":"「write a thank-you letter」意思是寫一封表達感激的書面訊息。"},{"en":"After receiving work experience help, a student may write a thank-you letter to the company.","zh":"接受工作體驗幫助後，學生可能向公司寫感謝信。"},{"en":"If a letter is sincere and specific, it can strengthen a relationship.","zh":"如果信件真誠而具體，它可以加強關係。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formal written thanks.","zh":"這個短語描述正式書面感謝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"know when not to","meaning":"知道何時不應……","examples":[{"en":"Young people need to know when not to use a mobile phone.","zh":"年輕人需要知道何時不應使用手提電話。"},{"en":"To know when not to do something means to understand the situations where an action is inappropriate.","zh":"「know when not to」做某事，意思是明白在哪些情況下某行動不合適。"},{"en":"Students should know when not to joke, especially during serious announcements.","zh":"學生應知道何時不應開玩笑，尤其在嚴肅宣布期間。"},{"en":"If someone uses a phone at the wrong time, they may seem rude or distracted.","zh":"如果某人在錯誤時間使用電話，可能顯得無禮或分心。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on judgment and timing.","zh":"這個短語集中於判斷和時機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"no matter what their background","meaning":"無論背景如何","examples":[{"en":"Every child needs social skills, no matter what their background.","zh":"每個孩子都需要社交技巧，無論背景如何。"},{"en":"No matter what their background means regardless of family, class, school, culture, or experience.","zh":"「no matter what their background」意思是不論家庭、階級、學校、文化或經歷如何。"},{"en":"Every student deserves respect, no matter what their background.","zh":"每位學生都值得尊重，無論背景如何。"},{"en":"If social skills are useful for all children, they should not be limited to wealthy schools.","zh":"如果社交技巧對所有孩子都有用，就不應只限於富裕學校。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses inclusion across different groups.","zh":"這個短語強調涵蓋不同群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be given social skills","meaning":"獲教授社交技巧","examples":[{"en":"Every child needs to be given social skills.","zh":"每個孩子都需要獲教授社交技巧。"},{"en":"To be given social skills means to be taught how to communicate and behave appropriately with others.","zh":"「be given social skills」意思是被教導如何與他人適當溝通和行為。"},{"en":"A shy child can be given social skills through role-play and guided practice.","zh":"害羞孩子可以透過角色扮演和引導練習獲教授社交技巧。"},{"en":"If children are not taught these skills, formal situations may feel confusing later.","zh":"如果孩子沒有被教這些技能，日後正式場合可能感到困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes social ability as something that can be taught.","zh":"這個短語把社交能力描述為可以被教授的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"polite and well-mannered","meaning":"有禮貌和有教養","examples":[{"en":"Everyone needs to know how to be polite and well-mannered.","zh":"人人都需要知道如何有禮貌和有教養。"},{"en":"Polite and well-mannered means respectful, considerate, and socially appropriate.","zh":"「polite and well-mannered」意思是尊重人、體貼並符合社交禮儀。"},{"en":"A polite and well-mannered student listens before speaking and thanks people for help.","zh":"有禮貌和有教養的學生會先聽後說，並為別人的幫助道謝。"},{"en":"If someone is rude in an interview, their knowledge may not be enough to save the impression.","zh":"如果某人在面試中無禮，其知識可能不足以挽回印象。"},{"en":"The phrase describes behaviour that makes others feel respected.","zh":"這個短語描述令他人感到受尊重的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"once upon a time","meaning":"從前","examples":[{"en":"Once upon a time, teaching manners was considered a parents’ job.","zh":"從前，教導禮貌被視為父母的職責。"},{"en":"Once upon a time means in the past, often suggesting things were different then.","zh":"「once upon a time」意思是在過去，通常暗示當時情況不同。"},{"en":"Once upon a time, students wrote essays by hand instead of typing them.","zh":"從前，學生用手寫作文，而不是打字。"},{"en":"If society changes, responsibilities that once belonged to families may move into schools.","zh":"如果社會改變，曾屬於家庭的責任可能轉移到學校。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an earlier period, sometimes with a slightly story-like tone.","zh":"這個短語引入較早時期，有時帶一點故事語氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be considered a parents’ job","meaning":"被視為父母的職責","examples":[{"en":"Teaching these things was once considered a parents’ job.","zh":"教導這些事情曾被視為父母的職責。"},{"en":"To be considered a parents’ job means to be seen as something mothers and fathers should teach or handle.","zh":"「be considered a parents’ job」意思是被視為母親和父親應教導或處理的事。"},{"en":"Teaching children to say thank you is often considered a parents’ job.","zh":"教孩子說謝謝常被視為父母的職責。"},{"en":"If parents are busy or unsure, schools may need to support this learning.","zh":"如果父母忙碌或不確定，學校可能需要支援這種學習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a responsibility linked to parenting.","zh":"這個短語描述與育兒有關的責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as confused as","meaning":"和……一樣困惑","examples":[{"en":"Today’s parents are often as confused as their offspring.","zh":"今天的父母常和子女一樣困惑。"},{"en":"As confused as means equally unsure or puzzled as another person or group.","zh":"「as confused as」意思是與另一人或群體同樣不確定或困惑。"},{"en":"A teacher may be as confused as students when a new timetable is unclear.","zh":"當新時間表不清楚，老師可能和學生一樣困惑。"},{"en":"If parents are confused about modern etiquette, children may not receive clear guidance at home.","zh":"如果父母對現代禮儀感到困惑，孩子在家中可能得不到清晰指引。"},{"en":"The phrase makes an equal comparison of uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語對不確定程度作相等比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"offspring","meaning":"子女；後代","examples":[{"en":"Parents may be as confused as their offspring.","zh":"父母可能和子女一樣困惑。"},{"en":"Offspring means a person’s children or the young of an animal.","zh":"「offspring」意思是一個人的子女，或動物的幼崽。"},{"en":"Parents worry when their offspring leave home for university.","zh":"當子女離家上大學，父母會擔心。"},{"en":"If parents and offspring both lack social confidence, outside teaching may help.","zh":"如果父母和子女都缺乏社交信心，外來教學可能有幫助。"},{"en":"The word is more formal than “children”.","zh":"這個詞比 “children” 較正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"wear to interview","meaning":"面試時穿着","examples":[{"en":"Parents ask what their child should wear to interview.","zh":"父母問孩子面試時應穿甚麼。"},{"en":"What to wear to interview means what clothes are suitable for an interview.","zh":"「what to wear to interview」意思是面試時甚麼衣服合適。"},{"en":"A student may ask a teacher what to wear to interview for a scholarship.","zh":"學生可能問老師申請獎學金面試時穿甚麼。"},{"en":"If clothing is too casual or uncomfortable, it can distract the candidate.","zh":"如果衣服太隨便或不舒服，可能令候選人分心。"},{"en":"The phrase concerns appropriate dress for an interview situation.","zh":"這個短語關乎面試情境中的合適衣着。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"get lots of questions about","meaning":"收到很多關於……的問題","examples":[{"en":"Rachel gets lots of questions about eating and table manners.","zh":"Rachel 收到很多關於用餐和餐桌禮儀的問題。"},{"en":"To get lots of questions about something means to be asked about it many times.","zh":"「get lots of questions about」某事，意思是多次被問及它。"},{"en":"A school counsellor may get lots of questions about exam stress before finals.","zh":"學校輔導員在期末考前可能收到很多關於考試壓力的問題。"},{"en":"If many people ask the same question, the topic is probably confusing or important.","zh":"如果許多人問同一問題，該題目很可能令人困惑或重要。"},{"en":"The phrase shows common concern or interest.","zh":"這個短語顯示常見關注或興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cutlery","meaning":"餐具","examples":[{"en":"Young people worry about what to do when there is lots of cutlery.","zh":"年輕人擔心當有很多餐具時應怎樣做。"},{"en":"Cutlery means knives, forks, and spoons used for eating.","zh":"「cutlery」意思是用餐時使用的刀、叉和匙。"},{"en":"At a formal dinner, students may feel nervous if several pieces of cutlery are placed beside the plate.","zh":"在正式晚宴上，如果碟旁放了幾件餐具，學生可能感到緊張。"},{"en":"If people know which fork to use first, they feel less awkward at the table.","zh":"如果人們知道先用哪隻叉，在餐桌上就較不尷尬。"},{"en":"The word refers to eating tools, especially in formal meals.","zh":"這個詞指用餐工具，尤其在正式餐會中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the idea of","meaning":"……這個想法","examples":[{"en":"Some young people find the idea of eating with a future employer intimidating.","zh":"有些年輕人覺得與未來僱主用餐這個想法令人畏懼。"},{"en":"The idea of something means the thought or possibility of it.","zh":"「the idea of」某事，意思是對它的想法或可能性。"},{"en":"The idea of speaking in front of the whole school can make some students nervous.","zh":"在全校面前發言這個想法會令一些學生緊張。"},{"en":"If a situation sounds formal and unfamiliar, the idea alone may feel frightening.","zh":"如果情況聽起來正式又陌生，單是這個想法已可能令人害怕。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how people react to imagining something.","zh":"這個短語集中於人們想像某事時的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"future employer","meaning":"未來僱主","examples":[{"en":"A meal with a future employer can feel intimidating.","zh":"與未來僱主用餐可能令人感到畏懼。"},{"en":"A future employer is a person or organisation that may hire someone later.","zh":"「future employer」是日後可能聘用某人的個人或機構。"},{"en":"A student on work experience may meet a future employer at a networking event.","zh":"參與工作體驗的學生可能在交流活動中遇到未來僱主。"},{"en":"If you behave professionally with a future employer, you may improve your chances later.","zh":"如果你在未來僱主面前表現專業，日後機會可能提高。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a possible boss or workplace in the future.","zh":"這個短語指將來可能的上司或工作場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"find something intimidating","meaning":"覺得某事令人畏懼","examples":[{"en":"Young people may find formal meals intimidating.","zh":"年輕人可能覺得正式餐會令人畏懼。"},{"en":"To find something intimidating means to feel nervous or frightened because it seems difficult, formal, or powerful.","zh":"「find something intimidating」意思是因某事看似困難、正式或強大而感到緊張或害怕。"},{"en":"A shy student may find a large debate competition intimidating.","zh":"害羞學生可能覺得大型辯論比賽令人畏懼。"},{"en":"If people do not know the rules of a situation, it may feel more intimidating.","zh":"如果人們不知道某情況的規則，它可能感覺更令人畏懼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes feeling pressured by something.","zh":"這個短語描述被某事帶來壓力的感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be taught as a proper subject","meaning":"作為正式科目教授","examples":[{"en":"Rachel thinks social skills should be taught as a proper subject in schools.","zh":"Rachel 認為社交技巧應在學校作為正式科目教授。"},{"en":"To be taught as a proper subject means to be included formally in the school timetable and taken seriously.","zh":"「be taught as a proper subject」意思是被正式納入學校時間表並受到認真對待。"},{"en":"Some people think financial literacy should be taught as a proper subject.","zh":"有些人認為理財知識應作為正式科目教授。"},{"en":"If social skills are treated formally, students may practise them more consistently.","zh":"如果社交技巧被正式對待，學生可能更持續地練習。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts formal education with casual advice.","zh":"這個短語把正式教育與隨意建議作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"proper subject","meaning":"正式科目","examples":[{"en":"Social skills should be treated as a proper subject.","zh":"社交技巧應被視為正式科目。"},{"en":"A proper subject is a recognised area of study that is taught seriously and systematically.","zh":"「proper subject」是被認可、認真且有系統教授的學習範疇。"},{"en":"Coding has become a proper subject in many schools rather than an optional hobby.","zh":"編程在許多學校已成為正式科目，而不只是可選興趣。"},{"en":"If etiquette becomes a proper subject, students may receive structured lessons and feedback.","zh":"如果禮儀成為正式科目，學生可能得到有結構課堂和回饋。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests something deserves formal educational status.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事值得有正式教育地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"an add-on","meaning":"附加項目","examples":[{"en":"Rachel does not think social skills should be treated as an add-on.","zh":"Rachel 不認為社交技巧應被視為附加項目。"},{"en":"An add-on is something extra that is attached to the main thing but not treated as central.","zh":"「an add-on」是附加在主要事物之上，但不被視為核心的額外東西。"},{"en":"A school should not treat mental health support as a small add-on to academic lessons.","zh":"學校不應把心理健康支援視為學術課堂的小附加項目。"},{"en":"If social skills are only an add-on, they may be taught irregularly or ignored.","zh":"如果社交技巧只是附加項目，它可能被不定期教授或被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something supplementary rather than essential.","zh":"這個短語描述補充性而非必要性的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"come in from outside","meaning":"從外面進來；以外來者身份加入","examples":[{"en":"It helps that Rachel comes in from outside the school.","zh":"Rachel 以校外人士身份進來，這是有幫助的。"},{"en":"To come in from outside means to join or teach from outside an organisation rather than being part of it.","zh":"「come in from outside」意思是從組織外加入或教學，而不是本身屬於該組織。"},{"en":"A company may invite a trainer to come in from outside to teach customer service.","zh":"公司可能邀請外部培訓師進來教授客戶服務。"},{"en":"If an outside expert teaches a topic, students may listen differently from usual.","zh":"如果外來專家教授某題目，學生可能以不同方式聆聽。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an external person entering to help.","zh":"這個短語描述外部人士進入提供幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take one’s company into","meaning":"將自己的公司帶入……","examples":[{"en":"She has taken her new company into four independent schools.","zh":"她已將自己的新公司帶入四所私立學校。"},{"en":"To take one’s company into a place means to bring its services into that organisation or market.","zh":"「take one’s company into」某地方，意思是把公司的服務帶入該機構或市場。"},{"en":"A language tutor may take her company into local schools by offering after-school courses.","zh":"語言導師可能透過提供課後課程，把自己的公司帶入本地學校。"},{"en":"If a company enters schools, more students can access its training.","zh":"如果公司進入學校，更多學生就能接觸其培訓。"},{"en":"The phrase describes expanding a service into new institutions.","zh":"這個短語描述把服務擴展到新機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"try out one’s skills","meaning":"試用自己的技能","examples":[{"en":"She came to the Cotswold School to try out her skills in the state sector.","zh":"她來到 The Cotswold School，在公營教育界試用自己的技能。"},{"en":"To try out one’s skills means to test what one can do in a real or new situation.","zh":"「try out one’s skills」意思是在真實或新情況中測試自己的能力。"},{"en":"A student may try out their cooking skills by preparing dinner for the family.","zh":"學生可能透過為家人煮晚餐試用自己的烹飪技能。"},{"en":"If Rachel works with state-school students, she can see whether her methods work beyond private schools.","zh":"如果 Rachel 與公立學校學生合作，她可以了解其方法是否在私校以外也有效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical testing of ability.","zh":"這個短語描述實際測試能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"state sector","meaning":"公營教育界","examples":[{"en":"Rachel wanted to work with students in the state sector.","zh":"Rachel 想與公營教育界的學生合作。"},{"en":"The state sector means publicly funded schools or services run or supported by the government.","zh":"「state sector」意思是由政府營運或資助的公營學校或服務。"},{"en":"Teachers in the state sector often work with students from many social backgrounds.","zh":"公營教育界的老師常與來自不同社會背景的學生合作。"},{"en":"If training enters the state sector, it may reach students who cannot pay for private coaching.","zh":"如果培訓進入公營教育界，它可能接觸到無法支付私人指導費的學生。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts public education with private education.","zh":"這個短語把公營教育與私營教育作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"work with","meaning":"與……合作","examples":[{"en":"She worked with a small Oxbridge group at the school.","zh":"她與學校一個小型牛津劍橋申請小組合作。"},{"en":"To work with someone means to cooperate with them or teach them closely.","zh":"「work with」某人，意思是與他們合作或密切教導他們。"},{"en":"A coach may work with a small group of students before a speaking contest.","zh":"教練可能在演講比賽前與一小組學生合作。"},{"en":"If a trainer works with fewer students, she can give more personal feedback.","zh":"如果導師與較少學生合作，她可以給予更多個人回饋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes collaboration or guided teaching.","zh":"這個短語描述合作或有指導的教學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"run a workshop","meaning":"舉辦工作坊","examples":[{"en":"She also ran a larger workshop for 11-year-olds.","zh":"她也為11歲學生舉辦了較大型工作坊。"},{"en":"To run a workshop means to organise and lead a practical training session.","zh":"「run a workshop」意思是組織並帶領實用培訓課。"},{"en":"A teacher may run a workshop on essay planning before exam season.","zh":"老師可能在考試季前舉辦作文規劃工作坊。"},{"en":"If a workshop is well run, students practise skills rather than just listen.","zh":"如果工作坊辦得好，學生會練習技能，而不只是聆聽。"},{"en":"The phrase describes leading a structured learning activity.","zh":"這個短語描述帶領有結構的學習活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"headmistress","meaning":"女校長","examples":[{"en":"The headmistress came across Rachel Holland’s work through a family connection.","zh":"女校長透過家庭關係偶然得知 Rachel Holland 的工作。"},{"en":"A headmistress is the female head teacher or principal of a school.","zh":"「headmistress」是學校的女性校長或首席教師。"},{"en":"A headmistress may decide whether outside workshops are useful for her students.","zh":"女校長可能決定外來工作坊是否對學生有用。"},{"en":"If the headmistress supports a programme, teachers and parents may take it more seriously.","zh":"如果女校長支持某計劃，老師和家長可能更認真看待它。"},{"en":"The word describes the woman leading a school.","zh":"這個詞描述領導學校的女性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"come across","meaning":"偶然發現","examples":[{"en":"The headmistress came across Rachel Holland’s work through a family connection.","zh":"女校長透過家庭關係偶然發現 Rachel Holland 的工作。"},{"en":"To come across something means to find or discover it by chance.","zh":"「come across」某物，意思是偶然找到或發現它。"},{"en":"A student may come across a useful article while searching for homework information.","zh":"學生搜尋功課資料時，可能偶然發現一篇有用文章。"},{"en":"If someone comes across a good course, they may share it with colleagues.","zh":"如果某人偶然發現好課程，可能會與同事分享。"},{"en":"The phrase describes accidental discovery.","zh":"這個短語描述偶然發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"family connection","meaning":"家庭關係","examples":[{"en":"The headmistress learned about the workshop through a family connection.","zh":"女校長透過家庭關係得知該工作坊。"},{"en":"A family connection is a link between people through relatives or family relationships.","zh":"「family connection」是透過親戚或家庭關係建立的人際連結。"},{"en":"A student may find work experience through a family connection if an uncle knows a company manager.","zh":"如果叔叔認識公司經理，學生可能透過家庭關係找到工作體驗機會。"},{"en":"If opportunities come through family connections, not everyone has equal access.","zh":"如果機會透過家庭關係而來，不是人人都有平等接觸機會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a personal link based on family.","zh":"這個短語描述基於家庭的個人連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"for a minute","meaning":"一刻也","examples":[{"en":"Neither the headmistress nor the boys think for a minute that canapés are the key to Oxbridge.","zh":"女校長和男生一刻也不認為小食是進入牛津劍橋的關鍵。"},{"en":"Not think for a minute means not believe something at all, even briefly.","zh":"「not think for a minute」意思是完全不相信某事，哪怕一刻也不相信。"},{"en":"I do not think for a minute that one lesson can make someone fluent.","zh":"我一刻也不認為一堂課可以令人流利。"},{"en":"If people do not think etiquette alone wins admission, they still see it as useful support.","zh":"如果人們不認為禮儀單靠本身能贏得取錄，他們仍可能視它為有用支援。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly rejects an idea.","zh":"這個短語強烈否定一個想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the key to getting into","meaning":"進入……的關鍵","examples":[{"en":"They do not think etiquette is the key to getting into Oxbridge.","zh":"他們不認為禮儀是進入牛津劍橋的關鍵。"},{"en":"The key to getting into somewhere means the most important factor for gaining entry or acceptance.","zh":"「the key to getting into」某地方，意思是獲得進入或接納的最重要因素。"},{"en":"Consistent practice may be the key to getting into a competitive music school.","zh":"持續練習可能是進入競爭激烈音樂學校的關鍵。"},{"en":"If interviews test academic thinking, manners alone cannot be the key to admission.","zh":"如果面試測試學術思考，單靠禮貌不可能是取錄關鍵。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what matters most for success.","zh":"這個短語指出成功最重要的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"nevertheless","meaning":"儘管如此","examples":[{"en":"Nevertheless, the effect of the workshop is astonishing.","zh":"儘管如此，工作坊的效果令人驚訝。"},{"en":"Nevertheless means despite what has just been said.","zh":"「nevertheless」意思是儘管剛才所說如此。"},{"en":"The exam was difficult; nevertheless, the student stayed calm and finished it.","zh":"考試很困難；儘管如此，學生保持冷靜並完成它。"},{"en":"If etiquette is not the key to admission, it may nevertheless improve confidence.","zh":"如果禮儀不是取錄關鍵，它仍然可能改善信心。"},{"en":"The word introduces contrast with the previous idea.","zh":"這個詞引出與前一想法的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the effect of","meaning":"……的效果","examples":[{"en":"The effect of the workshop is astonishing.","zh":"工作坊的效果令人驚訝。"},{"en":"The effect of something means the result or change it causes.","zh":"「the effect of」某事，意思是它造成的結果或變化。"},{"en":"The effect of daily reading can be seen in better vocabulary and writing.","zh":"每日閱讀的效果可以在更好詞彙和寫作中看見。"},{"en":"If a workshop changes students’ confidence quickly, its effect is visible.","zh":"如果工作坊快速改變學生信心，其效果就是可見的。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on what happens because of something.","zh":"這個短語集中於某事造成甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"astonishing","meaning":"令人驚訝的","examples":[{"en":"The workshop has an astonishing effect on the candidates.","zh":"工作坊對候選人產生令人驚訝的效果。"},{"en":"Astonishing means very surprising or impressive.","zh":"「astonishing」意思是非常令人驚訝或印象深刻。"},{"en":"A quiet student’s confident speech can be astonishing to classmates.","zh":"安靜學生的自信演講可能令同學感到驚訝。"},{"en":"If a short workshop changes posture and confidence quickly, observers may be amazed.","zh":"如果短工作坊快速改變姿勢和信心，旁觀者可能驚訝。"},{"en":"The word describes something that strongly surprises people.","zh":"這個詞描述強烈令人意外的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"over the course of","meaning":"在……期間","examples":[{"en":"Over the course of the morning, the candidates become more confident.","zh":"在整個早上期間，候選人變得更自信。"},{"en":"Over the course of a period means during that period from beginning to end.","zh":"「over the course of」一段時間，意思是在該時段由開始到結束期間。"},{"en":"Over the course of a school term, students may improve their speaking confidence.","zh":"在一個學期期間，學生可能改善說話信心。"},{"en":"If skills are practised repeatedly during a morning, visible change can happen.","zh":"如果技能在一個早上反覆練習，可見變化可以發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual change within a time period.","zh":"這個短語描述某時段內的逐漸變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be transformed from…into…","meaning":"從……轉變成……","examples":[{"en":"The boys are transformed from lounging schoolboys into confident young men.","zh":"男生們從懶洋洋坐着的男學生轉變成自信的年輕人。"},{"en":"To be transformed from A into B means to change greatly from one state into another.","zh":"「be transformed from A into B」意思是由一種狀態大幅改變成另一種。"},{"en":"A messy paragraph can be transformed into a clear essay after careful editing.","zh":"經過仔細修改，混亂段落可以轉變成清晰文章。"},{"en":"If students practise posture and speech, they may change from nervous to confident.","zh":"如果學生練習姿勢和說話，他們可能從緊張轉變成自信。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong before-and-after change.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈的前後變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"amiable","meaning":"友善的","examples":[{"en":"The boys seem amiable before the workshop begins.","zh":"工作坊開始前，男生們看起來友善。"},{"en":"Amiable means friendly, pleasant, and easy to like.","zh":"「amiable」意思是友善、令人愉快和容易令人喜歡。"},{"en":"An amiable classmate makes group work more comfortable for everyone.","zh":"友善的同學令小組合作對每個人都更舒服。"},{"en":"If someone is amiable but lacks confidence, social training may help them show their strengths.","zh":"如果某人友善但缺乏自信，社交訓練可能幫助他展示優點。"},{"en":"The word describes a warm and friendly personality.","zh":"這個詞描述溫和友善的性格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lounging schoolboys","meaning":"懶洋洋坐着的男學生","examples":[{"en":"The candidates first appear as amiable, lounging schoolboys.","zh":"候選人起初看起來像友善但懶洋洋坐着的男學生。"},{"en":"Lounging schoolboys are boys sitting or standing in a relaxed, lazy, informal way.","zh":"「lounging schoolboys」是以放鬆、懶散、非正式方式坐着或站着的男學生。"},{"en":"After lunch, lounging schoolboys may lean back in chairs while chatting.","zh":"午飯後，懶洋洋的男學生可能靠在椅背上聊天。"},{"en":"If candidates look too relaxed, they may not seem ready for a formal interview.","zh":"如果候選人看起來太放鬆，可能不像準備好參加正式面試。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts casual student behaviour with polished interview behaviour.","zh":"這個短語把隨便學生行為與精緻面試表現作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"palpable presence","meaning":"明顯的存在感","examples":[{"en":"After the workshop, the boys have palpable presence.","zh":"工作坊後，男生們有明顯的存在感。"},{"en":"Palpable presence means a strong personal impact that other people can clearly feel or notice.","zh":"「palpable presence」意思是別人能清楚感受到或注意到的強烈個人影響力。"},{"en":"A confident speaker has palpable presence when the room becomes quiet and attentive.","zh":"當房間變得安靜而專注，自信演講者就有明顯存在感。"},{"en":"If posture, voice, and eye contact improve, a person’s presence becomes stronger.","zh":"如果姿勢、聲音和眼神接觸改善，一個人的存在感會變強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes noticeable personal force or confidence.","zh":"這個短語描述可感覺到的個人力量或自信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"charm and command your attention","meaning":"吸引並抓住你的注意力","examples":[{"en":"The boys learn to charm and command your attention.","zh":"男生們學會吸引並抓住你的注意力。"},{"en":"To charm and command your attention means to attract you pleasantly and hold your focus strongly.","zh":"「charm and command your attention」意思是以令人愉快的方式吸引你，並有力地抓住你的專注。"},{"en":"A good presenter can charm and command the audience’s attention with humour and clear structure.","zh":"好的匯報者可以用幽默和清晰結構吸引並抓住觀眾注意力。"},{"en":"If someone speaks confidently and warmly, listeners are more likely to stay focused.","zh":"如果某人說話自信而溫暖，聽者較可能保持專注。"},{"en":"The phrase combines likeability with authority.","zh":"這個短語結合可親魅力和權威感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"watch the action","meaning":"觀看現場情況","examples":[{"en":"The headmistress watches the action during the workshop.","zh":"女校長在工作坊期間觀看現場情況。"},{"en":"To watch the action means to observe what is happening, especially a lively activity.","zh":"「watch the action」意思是觀察正在發生的事情，尤其是生動活動。"},{"en":"Parents watched the action as students rehearsed for the school play.","zh":"當學生為學校戲劇排練時，家長觀看現場情況。"},{"en":"If someone watches a workshop closely, they can see whether it really changes behaviour.","zh":"如果某人仔細觀看工作坊，就能看出它是否真正改變行為。"},{"en":"The phrase describes observing an event in progress.","zh":"這個短語描述觀察進行中的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"straighten one’s back","meaning":"挺直背部","examples":[{"en":"The headmistress straightens her back in her chair.","zh":"女校長在椅上挺直背部。"},{"en":"To straighten one’s back means to sit or stand with the spine more upright.","zh":"「straighten one’s back」意思是坐或站時把脊背挺直。"},{"en":"A student may straighten their back before giving a presentation.","zh":"學生可能在匯報前挺直背部。"},{"en":"If people straighten their back, they often look more alert and confident.","zh":"如果人們挺直背部，通常看起來更精神和自信。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improving posture.","zh":"這個短語描述改善姿勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"practical stuff","meaning":"實用的東西","examples":[{"en":"The headmistress says the training is really practical stuff.","zh":"女校長說這訓練是真正實用的東西。"},{"en":"Practical stuff means useful knowledge or skills that can be applied in real life.","zh":"「practical stuff」意思是可在現實生活中應用的有用知識或技能。"},{"en":"Learning how to write emails is practical stuff for students preparing for work.","zh":"學習如何寫電郵對準備工作的學生而言是實用的東西。"},{"en":"If training is practical, students can use it immediately in interviews or meetings.","zh":"如果訓練實用，學生可以立即在面試或會議中使用。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts useful skills with abstract theory.","zh":"這個短語把有用技能與抽象理論作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"I only wish someone had told me","meaning":"我只希望當年有人告訴我","examples":[{"en":"She says, “I only wish someone had told me all this when I was young.”","zh":"她說：「我只希望當年有人在我年輕時告訴我這一切。」"},{"en":"I only wish someone had told me means I regret not receiving this advice earlier.","zh":"「I only wish someone had told me」意思是我遺憾沒有更早收到這些建議。"},{"en":"A graduate may say, “I only wish someone had told me how important internships were.”","zh":"畢業生可能說：「我只希望當年有人告訴我實習有多重要。」"},{"en":"If advice would have helped in the past, people often express regret this way.","zh":"如果某建議在過去本來會有幫助，人們常用這方式表達遺憾。"},{"en":"The phrase shows appreciation mixed with regret.","zh":"這個短語顯示感激與遺憾混合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"wide span of social backgrounds","meaning":"廣泛的社會背景","examples":[{"en":"The boys come from a wide span of social backgrounds.","zh":"男生們來自廣泛的社會背景。"},{"en":"A wide span of social backgrounds means a broad range of family, class, income, and life experiences.","zh":"「wide span of social backgrounds」意思是家庭、階級、收入和生活經驗範圍很廣。"},{"en":"A public school may teach students from a wide span of social backgrounds.","zh":"公立學校可能教育來自廣泛社會背景的學生。"},{"en":"If a group is socially mixed, training must be useful for different experiences and needs.","zh":"如果群體在社會背景上混合，訓練就必須適合不同經驗和需要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes social diversity.","zh":"這個短語描述社會多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"soak up","meaning":"充分吸收","examples":[{"en":"The boys soak up the non-stop stream of tips.","zh":"男生們充分吸收源源不絕的建議。"},{"en":"To soak up information means to absorb and learn it eagerly.","zh":"「soak up」資料，意思是熱切地吸收和學習它。"},{"en":"A child may soak up new words quickly when adults read aloud every night.","zh":"如果成年人每晚朗讀，孩子可能很快吸收新詞。"},{"en":"If students are interested, they remember advice more easily.","zh":"如果學生感興趣，他們更容易記住建議。"},{"en":"The phrase compares learning to a sponge absorbing water.","zh":"這個短語把學習比作海綿吸水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"non-stop stream of tips","meaning":"源源不絕的建議","examples":[{"en":"The boys receive a non-stop stream of tips.","zh":"男生們收到源源不絕的建議。"},{"en":"A non-stop stream of tips is a continuous flow of advice or suggestions.","zh":"「non-stop stream of tips」是連續不斷的建議或提示。"},{"en":"Before exams, teachers may give students a non-stop stream of tips about timing and mistakes.","zh":"考試前，老師可能給學生源源不絕的時間管理和錯誤提示。"},{"en":"If the advice comes quickly, students need to listen actively and remember the key points.","zh":"如果建議來得很快，學生需要主動聆聽並記住重點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes advice arriving continuously.","zh":"這個短語描述建議連續湧來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have fun doing something","meaning":"做某事時玩得開心","examples":[{"en":"The boys have fun swaggering up and down to music.","zh":"男生們伴着音樂神氣地來回走動時玩得開心。"},{"en":"To have fun doing something means to enjoy doing that activity.","zh":"「have fun doing something」意思是享受做某活動。"},{"en":"Students may have fun learning vocabulary through games and songs.","zh":"學生可能透過遊戲和歌曲學詞彙時玩得開心。"},{"en":"If learners enjoy a task, they may practise more willingly.","zh":"如果學習者享受任務，他們可能更願意練習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pleasure during an activity.","zh":"這個短語描述活動中的愉快感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"swagger up and down","meaning":"神氣地來回走動","examples":[{"en":"The boys practise swaggering up and down to music.","zh":"男生們伴着音樂練習神氣地來回走動。"},{"en":"To swagger up and down means to walk back and forth with exaggerated confidence.","zh":"「swagger up and down」意思是帶着誇張自信來回走動。"},{"en":"Actors may swagger up and down during rehearsal to practise a confident character.","zh":"演員可能在排練時神氣地來回走動，以練習自信角色。"},{"en":"If students overdo it, swagger can look arrogant rather than confident.","zh":"如果學生做得太誇張，神氣姿態可能看起來傲慢而不是自信。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bold, showy walking.","zh":"這個短語描述大膽而炫耀式的走路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"inject confidence into","meaning":"將信心注入……","examples":[{"en":"They try to inject more confidence into the way they walk.","zh":"他們嘗試將更多信心注入走路方式。"},{"en":"To inject confidence into something means to add a stronger feeling or appearance of self-assurance.","zh":"「inject confidence into」某事，意思是加入更強的自信感或自信外觀。"},{"en":"A speaker can inject confidence into a presentation by standing upright and slowing down.","zh":"演講者可以透過站直和放慢速度，將信心注入匯報。"},{"en":"If a person’s walk looks confident, others may take them more seriously.","zh":"如果一個人的走路方式看起來有自信，別人可能更認真看待他。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deliberately adding confidence to behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述刻意為行為加入信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"inject authority into","meaning":"將威嚴注入……","examples":[{"en":"They try to inject more authority into their walking.","zh":"他們嘗試將更多威嚴注入走路方式。"},{"en":"To inject authority into something means to make it seem stronger, more controlled, or more commanding.","zh":"「inject authority into」某事，意思是令它看起來更有力量、更受控制或更有指揮力。"},{"en":"A teacher can inject authority into instructions by using a calm, firm voice.","zh":"老師可以透過冷靜而堅定的聲音，將威嚴注入指示中。"},{"en":"If candidates walk with authority, they may appear more mature and prepared.","zh":"如果候選人走路有威嚴，可能顯得更成熟和準備充足。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adding a sense of control and seriousness.","zh":"這個短語描述加入控制感和嚴肅感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the way someone walks","meaning":"某人走路的方式","examples":[{"en":"Rachel teaches the boys to improve the way they walk.","zh":"Rachel 教男生改善他們走路的方式。"},{"en":"The way someone walks means their style of walking, including posture, speed, and confidence.","zh":"「the way someone walks」意思是某人的走路風格，包括姿勢、速度和自信。"},{"en":"A coach may change the way an athlete walks after an injury.","zh":"運動員受傷後，教練可能改變他走路的方式。"},{"en":"If the way someone walks looks nervous, people may notice before the person speaks.","zh":"如果某人走路方式看起來緊張，在他說話前別人可能已注意到。"},{"en":"The phrase describes body language shown through movement.","zh":"這個短語描述透過移動顯示的身體語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in twos and threes","meaning":"兩人或三人一組","examples":[{"en":"The boys practise small talk in twos and threes.","zh":"男生們兩人或三人一組練習閒談。"},{"en":"In twos and threes means in small groups of two or three people.","zh":"「in twos and threes」意思是以兩人或三人的小組形式。"},{"en":"Students may discuss a reading passage in twos and threes before sharing with the class.","zh":"學生可能兩人或三人一組討論閱讀篇章，再向全班分享。"},{"en":"If a task is social, small groups can make practice less frightening.","zh":"如果任務屬於社交性，小組練習可令它較不嚇人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small-group arrangement.","zh":"這個短語描述小組安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a tricky business","meaning":"棘手的事","examples":[{"en":"Making small talk can be a tricky business.","zh":"閒談可以是棘手的事。"},{"en":"A tricky business is something difficult to do well because it needs care, judgment, or practice.","zh":"「a tricky business」是因需要小心、判斷或練習而難以做好的一件事。"},{"en":"Explaining bad news politely can be a tricky business.","zh":"有禮貌地解釋壞消息可以是棘手的事。"},{"en":"If conversation topics are too personal or too dull, small talk may become awkward.","zh":"如果對話題目太私人或太沉悶，寒暄可能變得尷尬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a task that is harder than it first appears.","zh":"這個短語描述比起初看來更困難的任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"it’s hard work","meaning":"這很費力","examples":[{"en":"Rachel admits that making small talk is hard work.","zh":"Rachel 承認閒談很費力。"},{"en":"It’s hard work means it requires effort, concentration, or practice.","zh":"「it’s hard work」意思是某事需要努力、專注或練習。"},{"en":"Writing a good essay is hard work because planning, drafting, and editing all matter.","zh":"寫一篇好文章很費力，因為規劃、起稿和修改都重要。"},{"en":"If small talk feels natural only after practice, it is a skill rather than a gift.","zh":"如果寒暄只有在練習後才自然，它就是技能而不是天賦。"},{"en":"The phrase recognises that something takes real effort.","zh":"這個短語承認某事需要真正努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"store questions in your head","meaning":"在腦中儲備問題","examples":[{"en":"You need to store some questions in your head for small talk.","zh":"你需要在腦中儲備一些問題，以便閒談。"},{"en":"To store questions in your head means to prepare and remember possible questions before a conversation.","zh":"「store questions in your head」意思是在對話前準備並記住可能提出的問題。"},{"en":"Before meeting a guest speaker, students may store questions in their heads about the speaker’s career.","zh":"在見客席講者前，學生可能在腦中儲備關於講者職業的問題。"},{"en":"If conversation becomes quiet, prepared questions can help keep it moving.","zh":"如果對話變得安靜，預備好的問題可以幫助它繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mental preparation for speaking.","zh":"這個短語描述說話前的心理準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"fake it","meaning":"假裝出來","examples":[{"en":"Sometimes you have to fake confidence in social situations.","zh":"有時你在社交情況中要假裝有自信。"},{"en":"To fake it means to pretend to have a feeling or ability until you can act more naturally.","zh":"「fake it」意思是假裝有某種感覺或能力，直到你能更自然地表現。"},{"en":"A nervous speaker may fake confidence by standing straight and speaking slowly.","zh":"緊張的演講者可能透過站直和慢慢說話來假裝自信。"},{"en":"If the body looks calm, the mind may gradually feel calmer too.","zh":"如果身體看起來冷靜，心理也可能逐漸更冷靜。"},{"en":"The phrase describes acting confident even when you do not fully feel it.","zh":"這個短語描述即使未完全感受到，也先表現自信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"look relaxed and confident","meaning":"看起來放鬆而自信","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to look relaxed and confident.","zh":"候選人需要看起來放鬆而自信。"},{"en":"To look relaxed and confident means to appear calm, comfortable, and sure of yourself.","zh":"「look relaxed and confident」意思是外表顯得冷靜、自在和有把握。"},{"en":"A student who smiles, sits upright, and breathes steadily may look relaxed and confident.","zh":"微笑、坐直和穩定呼吸的學生可能看起來放鬆而自信。"},{"en":"If candidates look tense, interviewers may wonder whether pressure affects their performance.","zh":"如果候選人看起來緊張，面試官可能懷疑壓力是否影響其表現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the impression created by body language.","zh":"這個短語描述身體語言造成的印象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the most important thing","meaning":"最重要的事","examples":[{"en":"The most important thing is to smile.","zh":"最重要的事是微笑。"},{"en":"The most important thing means the point that matters more than all the others.","zh":"「the most important thing」意思是比其他所有事情都更重要的一點。"},{"en":"In an emergency, the most important thing is to stay safe before collecting belongings.","zh":"在緊急情況中，最重要的事是在收拾物品前先確保安全。"},{"en":"If many details are difficult to remember, one key action can guide behaviour.","zh":"如果許多細節難以記住，一個關鍵行動可以指導行為。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the main priority.","zh":"這個短語強調主要優先事項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"after a break","meaning":"小休後","examples":[{"en":"After a break, Rachel turns to clothes.","zh":"小休後，Rachel 開始談及衣着。"},{"en":"After a break means following a short pause or rest period.","zh":"「after a break」意思是在短暫暫停或休息時間之後。"},{"en":"After a break, students may return to class feeling more focused.","zh":"小休後，學生可能回到課堂時更專注。"},{"en":"If a long workshop includes breaks, learners can absorb information better.","zh":"如果長工作坊包括小休，學習者可以更好吸收資料。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a new stage after resting.","zh":"這個短語標示休息後的新階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"turn to","meaning":"轉到；開始談及","examples":[{"en":"After practising small talk, Rachel turns to clothes.","zh":"練習閒談後，Rachel 轉到衣着話題。"},{"en":"To turn to a topic means to start discussing or dealing with it.","zh":"「turn to」某話題，意思是開始討論或處理它。"},{"en":"After finishing vocabulary, the teacher turned to grammar practice.","zh":"完成詞彙後，老師轉到文法練習。"},{"en":"If a workshop covers several skills, the trainer turns to each topic in order.","zh":"如果工作坊涵蓋幾種技能，導師會按次序轉到每個題目。"},{"en":"The phrase signals a shift in focus.","zh":"這個短語表示焦點轉移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"buy the best quality someone can afford","meaning":"購買自己負擔得起的最好品質","examples":[{"en":"The boys are told to buy the best quality they can afford.","zh":"男生們被告知要購買自己負擔得起的最好品質。"},{"en":"To buy the best quality you can afford means to choose the best-made item within your budget.","zh":"「buy the best quality you can afford」意思是在預算內選擇造工最好的物品。"},{"en":"A student buying interview shoes should buy the best quality they can afford, not the flashiest pair.","zh":"學生買面試鞋時應購買自己負擔得起的最好品質，而不是最浮誇的一雙。"},{"en":"If clothes are better quality, they may fit better and last longer.","zh":"如果衣服質素較好，可能更合身並更耐用。"},{"en":"The phrase balances good appearance with realistic spending.","zh":"這個短語在良好外觀與現實開支之間取得平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"know one’s measurements","meaning":"知道自己的尺寸","examples":[{"en":"The boys are told to know their measurements.","zh":"男生們被告知要知道自己的尺寸。"},{"en":"To know one’s measurements means to know body sizes such as neck, chest, waist, and sleeve length.","zh":"「know one’s measurements」意思是知道頸圍、胸圍、腰圍和袖長等身體尺寸。"},{"en":"Someone ordering a suit online should know their measurements before choosing a size.","zh":"網上訂購西裝的人在選尺寸前應知道自己的尺寸。"},{"en":"If measurements are wrong, even expensive clothes may fit badly.","zh":"如果尺寸錯誤，即使昂貴衣服也可能不合身。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical knowledge needed for buying clothes.","zh":"這個短語描述買衣服所需的實用知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tape measure","meaning":"軟尺","examples":[{"en":"A tape measure is used to measure the boys.","zh":"軟尺被用來量度男生。"},{"en":"A tape measure is a flexible measuring tool used for body sizes, fabric, or furniture.","zh":"「tape measure」是用來量度身體尺寸、布料或家具的柔軟量度工具。"},{"en":"A tailor uses a tape measure to check sleeve length and waist size.","zh":"裁縫用軟尺檢查袖長和腰圍。"},{"en":"If measurements are taken with a tape measure, clothes can fit more accurately.","zh":"如果用軟尺量度尺寸，衣服可以更準確合身。"},{"en":"The phrase names a simple tool for measuring length.","zh":"這個短語指出一種簡單的量長工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be whipped out","meaning":"被迅速拿出來","examples":[{"en":"A tape measure is whipped out during the workshop.","zh":"工作坊期間，軟尺被迅速拿出來。"},{"en":"To be whipped out means to be taken out quickly and suddenly.","zh":"「be whipped out」意思是被快速而突然地拿出來。"},{"en":"A teacher whipped out a marker when a student asked for a diagram.","zh":"當學生要求圖解，老師迅速拿出白板筆。"},{"en":"If a tool is whipped out, the action feels quick, lively, and practical.","zh":"如果工具被迅速拿出來，動作感覺快速、生動和實用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fast removal from a bag, pocket, or case.","zh":"這個短語描述從袋、口袋或盒中快速拿出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sleeve length","meaning":"袖長","examples":[{"en":"The boys are measured for sleeve length.","zh":"男生們被量度袖長。"},{"en":"Sleeve length is the measurement from the shoulder or arm to where the sleeve should end.","zh":"「sleeve length」是從肩膀或手臂量到袖口應結束位置的尺寸。"},{"en":"A shirt with the wrong sleeve length may look untidy at an interview.","zh":"袖長不合適的恤衫在面試中可能顯得不整齊。"},{"en":"If sleeves are too long, they may cover the hands and look careless.","zh":"如果袖子太長，可能蓋住雙手並顯得粗心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one clothing measurement.","zh":"這個短語描述一項衣服尺寸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"neck size","meaning":"頸圍","examples":[{"en":"The boys are measured for neck size.","zh":"男生們被量度頸圍。"},{"en":"Neck size is the measurement around a person’s neck, often used when buying shirts.","zh":"「neck size」是圍繞頸部的尺寸，常用於購買恤衫。"},{"en":"A shirt with the right neck size feels comfortable when buttoned.","zh":"頸圍合適的恤衫扣上時會感到舒適。"},{"en":"If the neck size is too small, the collar may feel tight and distracting.","zh":"如果頸圍太小，衣領可能感到緊並令人分心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a clothing measurement for collars.","zh":"這個短語描述衣領相關的衣服尺寸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"buy a suit with vents at the back","meaning":"買背後有開衩的西裝","examples":[{"en":"Rachel advises the boys to buy a suit with vents at the back.","zh":"Rachel 建議男生買背後有開衩的西裝。"},{"en":"To buy a suit with vents at the back means to choose a jacket with openings at the rear for easier movement.","zh":"「buy a suit with vents at the back」意思是選擇後方有開口、方便活動的西裝外套。"},{"en":"A candidate may buy a suit with vents at the back so the jacket sits neatly when walking.","zh":"候選人可能買背後有開衩的西裝，使外套走路時保持整齊。"},{"en":"If a suit restricts movement, the wearer may look stiff or uncomfortable.","zh":"如果西裝限制活動，穿着者可能看起來僵硬或不舒服。"},{"en":"The phrase gives practical clothing advice.","zh":"這個短語提供實用服裝建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"vents at the back","meaning":"背後開衩","examples":[{"en":"A suit with vents at the back allows the wearer to move.","zh":"背後有開衩的西裝讓穿着者活動。"},{"en":"Vents at the back are openings in the rear of a jacket that allow easier movement.","zh":"「vents at the back」是外套後方的開口，讓人更容易活動。"},{"en":"A jacket with back vents is more comfortable when someone sits, turns, or walks.","zh":"有背後開衩的外套在坐下、轉身或走路時更舒適。"},{"en":"If the jacket has no vents, it may pull awkwardly when the wearer moves.","zh":"如果外套沒有開衩，穿着者移動時可能拉扯得很尷尬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a tailoring feature.","zh":"這個短語描述一項剪裁特色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"allow someone to move","meaning":"讓某人活動","examples":[{"en":"Vents at the back allow the wearer to move more easily.","zh":"背後開衩讓穿着者更容易活動。"},{"en":"To allow someone to move means to give them enough freedom or space for movement.","zh":"「allow someone to move」意思是給某人足夠自由或空間去活動。"},{"en":"Sports clothes allow athletes to move without feeling restricted.","zh":"運動服讓運動員活動時不覺受限制。"},{"en":"If interview clothes allow movement, candidates can sit and walk more naturally.","zh":"如果面試服裝讓人活動自如，候選人可以更自然地坐和走。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical comfort in clothing or space.","zh":"這個短語描述衣物或空間的實用舒適感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"make a difference","meaning":"帶來分別","examples":[{"en":"A good suit really makes a difference.","zh":"一套好西裝真的會帶來分別。"},{"en":"To make a difference means to have a noticeable effect or improvement.","zh":"「make a difference」意思是產生可見效果或改善。"},{"en":"Ten minutes of daily reading can make a difference to a student’s vocabulary.","zh":"每天閱讀十分鐘可以對學生詞彙帶來分別。"},{"en":"If clothes fit well, the wearer may look more confident and professional.","zh":"如果衣服合身，穿着者可能看起來更自信和專業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change that matters.","zh":"這個短語描述重要的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"evening dress","meaning":"晚禮服","examples":[{"en":"The boys are told when people wear evening dress.","zh":"男生們被告知人們何時穿晚禮服。"},{"en":"Evening dress is formal clothing worn for special events in the evening.","zh":"「evening dress」是在晚上特殊活動中穿着的正式服裝。"},{"en":"Guests may wear evening dress to a formal dinner, ball, or award ceremony.","zh":"客人可能在正式晚宴、舞會或頒獎禮中穿晚禮服。"},{"en":"If someone misunderstands a dress code, they may feel out of place.","zh":"如果某人誤解衣着要求，可能感到格格不入。"},{"en":"The phrase describes very formal evening clothing.","zh":"這個短語描述非常正式的晚間服裝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"smart casual","meaning":"端莊休閒服","examples":[{"en":"The boys learn what smart casual consists of.","zh":"男生們學習端莊休閒服由甚麼組成。"},{"en":"Smart casual is a dress style that is neat and tidy but not fully formal.","zh":"「smart casual」是一種整潔端莊但不完全正式的衣着風格。"},{"en":"A smart casual outfit may include a collared shirt, clean shoes, and trousers without a tie.","zh":"端莊休閒服可能包括有領恤衫、乾淨鞋子和西褲，但不用打呔。"},{"en":"If an invitation says smart casual, jeans and trainers may be too relaxed.","zh":"如果邀請寫着 smart casual，牛仔褲和波鞋可能太隨便。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a balanced style between formal and casual.","zh":"這個短語描述正式與休閒之間的平衡風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"consist of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"Rachel explains what smart casual consists of.","zh":"Rachel 解釋端莊休閒服由甚麼組成。"},{"en":"To consist of something means to be made up of particular parts or items.","zh":"「consist of」某物，意思是由特定部分或項目組成。"},{"en":"A simple school uniform may consist of a shirt, trousers, shoes, and a tie.","zh":"簡單校服可能由恤衫、長褲、鞋和領呔組成。"},{"en":"If students know what a dress code consists of, they can choose suitable clothes.","zh":"如果學生知道衣着要求由甚麼組成，就能選擇合適衣服。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the components of something.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物的組成部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"come as you are","meaning":"穿平日服裝出席","examples":[{"en":"A “come as you are” invitation may not mean exactly what it says.","zh":"“come as you are” 的邀請可能不完全是字面意思。"},{"en":"Come as you are means wear your ordinary clothes without dressing formally, though the phrase can be misleading.","zh":"「come as you are」意思是穿平日服裝而不用正式打扮，不過這說法可能有誤導性。"},{"en":"A party invitation that says “come as you are” may still expect guests to look tidy.","zh":"寫着 “come as you are” 的派對邀請，可能仍期望客人看起來整齊。"},{"en":"If people take the phrase too literally, they may dress too casually for the event.","zh":"如果人們太字面理解這短語，可能穿得對活動而言太隨便。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a relaxed dress code, but context matters.","zh":"這個短語描述較輕鬆衣着要求，但語境很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"tend not to mean what they say","meaning":"往往不是字面意思","examples":[{"en":"Some invitations tend not to mean what they say.","zh":"有些邀請往往不是字面意思。"},{"en":"To tend not to mean what they say means their literal words may not match the real social expectation.","zh":"「tend not to mean what they say」意思是字面文字可能不符合真正社交期望。"},{"en":"An invitation saying “informal” may still require guests to dress neatly.","zh":"寫着「非正式」的邀請，可能仍要求客人穿得整齊。"},{"en":"If social phrases are indirect, young people may need help interpreting them.","zh":"如果社交用語是間接的，年輕人可能需要幫助解讀。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that wording can hide unstated rules.","zh":"這個短語提醒字句背後可能有未明說規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"morning suit","meaning":"日間禮服","examples":[{"en":"Rachel asks the boys when someone would wear a morning suit.","zh":"Rachel 問男生甚麼時候會有人穿日間禮服。"},{"en":"A morning suit is formal daytime clothing, usually worn at weddings or very formal daytime events.","zh":"「morning suit」是正式日間服裝，通常在婚禮或非常正式的日間活動穿着。"},{"en":"A guest may wear a morning suit to a traditional wedding ceremony.","zh":"賓客可能在傳統婚禮儀式中穿日間禮服。"},{"en":"If someone wears a morning suit to a casual lunch, they may look overdressed.","zh":"如果某人穿日間禮服去隨便午餐，可能顯得打扮過度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a highly formal type of men’s daytime dress.","zh":"這個短語描述非常正式的男士日間服裝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"volunteer hopefully","meaning":"滿懷希望地自告奮勇回答","examples":[{"en":"The boys volunteer an answer hopefully.","zh":"男生們滿懷希望地自告奮勇回答。"},{"en":"To volunteer hopefully means to offer an answer while hoping it is correct.","zh":"「volunteer hopefully」意思是主動提供答案，同時希望它是正確的。"},{"en":"A student may volunteer hopefully when the teacher asks a difficult grammar question.","zh":"當老師問困難文法問題時，學生可能滿懷希望地自告奮勇回答。"},{"en":"If students are unsure but willing to try, they may learn from correction.","zh":"如果學生不確定但願意嘗試，他們可以從改正中學習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a tentative but eager response.","zh":"這個短語描述試探但熱切的回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"aspects of","meaning":"……的某些方面","examples":[{"en":"Some aspects of the workshop are not relevant to the boys’ lives.","zh":"工作坊的某些方面與男生的生活無關。"},{"en":"Aspects of something are particular parts, features, or sides of it.","zh":"「aspects of」某事，是它的特定部分、特徵或面向。"},{"en":"A course on health may cover aspects of sleep, diet, exercise, and stress.","zh":"健康課程可能涵蓋睡眠、飲食、運動和壓力等方面。"},{"en":"If some aspects of a lesson feel distant, students may still benefit from other parts.","zh":"如果課堂某些方面感覺遙遠，學生仍可能從其他部分受益。"},{"en":"The phrase helps discuss one part of a larger topic.","zh":"這個短語幫助討論較大題目中的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"top hat","meaning":"高禮帽","examples":[{"en":"Knowing when to wear a top hat is not very relevant to the boys.","zh":"知道何時戴高禮帽對男生而言不太相關。"},{"en":"A top hat is a tall formal hat traditionally worn with very formal clothing.","zh":"「top hat」是傳統上配非常正式服裝的高身正式帽子。"},{"en":"A top hat might appear at an old-fashioned wedding or ceremonial event.","zh":"高禮帽可能出現在復古婚禮或儀式活動中。"},{"en":"If students never attend such events, this knowledge may feel distant from daily life.","zh":"如果學生從不出席這類活動，這知識可能感覺與日常生活很遠。"},{"en":"The phrase names a traditional formal accessory.","zh":"這個短語指出一種傳統正式配飾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be clearly not relevant to","meaning":"明顯與……無關","examples":[{"en":"Some formal customs are clearly not relevant to their young lives.","zh":"有些正式習俗明顯與他們的年輕生活無關。"},{"en":"To be clearly not relevant to something means to have no obvious connection or usefulness for it.","zh":"「be clearly not relevant to」某事，意思是與它沒有明顯關係或用途。"},{"en":"Advanced tax law is clearly not relevant to most primary school pupils.","zh":"高階稅法明顯與大多數小學生無關。"},{"en":"If a topic does not connect with students’ lives, teachers may need to explain why it matters.","zh":"如果題目與學生生活沒有連繫，老師可能需要解釋它為何重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes obvious lack of relevance.","zh":"這個短語描述明顯缺乏相關性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"young lives","meaning":"年輕人的生活","examples":[{"en":"Some etiquette rules are not relevant to their young lives.","zh":"有些禮儀規則與他們年輕人的生活無關。"},{"en":"Young lives means the everyday experiences, needs, and situations of young people.","zh":"「young lives」意思是年輕人的日常經歷、需要和情況。"},{"en":"Social media, school pressure, and friendships are important parts of many young lives.","zh":"社交媒體、學校壓力和友誼是許多年輕人生活的重要部分。"},{"en":"If lessons connect with young lives, students may pay more attention.","zh":"如果課堂與年輕人生活有連繫，學生可能更留心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes life from the perspective of young people.","zh":"這個短語從年輕人角度描述生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be told what’s what","meaning":"被清楚告知該怎樣做","examples":[{"en":"The boys like being told what’s what.","zh":"男生們喜歡被清楚告知該怎樣做。"},{"en":"To be told what’s what means to be given clear, direct guidance about what is correct or expected.","zh":"「be told what’s what」意思是得到清楚直接的指引，知道甚麼正確或被期望。"},{"en":"New employees often like being told what’s what during their first week.","zh":"新員工在第一星期常喜歡被清楚告知該怎樣做。"},{"en":"If social rules are unclear, direct explanation can reduce anxiety.","zh":"如果社交規則不清楚，直接解釋可以減少焦慮。"},{"en":"The phrase describes receiving plain and practical instruction.","zh":"這個短語描述接受清楚實用的指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"wax enthusiastic","meaning":"變得熱情起來","examples":[{"en":"During a break, the boys wax enthusiastic about the workshop.","zh":"小休期間，男生們對工作坊變得熱情起來。"},{"en":"To wax enthusiastic means to start speaking with growing excitement and approval.","zh":"「wax enthusiastic」意思是開始越來越興奮而讚許地談論某事。"},{"en":"A student may wax enthusiastic about a book after discovering it is funny and easy to read.","zh":"學生發現一本書有趣又易讀後，可能對它變得熱情起來。"},{"en":"If learners enjoy a lesson, their attitude can change from doubt to excitement.","zh":"如果學習者享受課堂，他們的態度可以由懷疑變成興奮。"},{"en":"The phrase describes becoming openly positive about something.","zh":"這個短語描述對某事變得公開正面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"apply to read geography","meaning":"申請修讀地理","examples":[{"en":"Alex Green is applying to read geography at Cambridge.","zh":"Alex Green 正申請在劍橋修讀地理。"},{"en":"To apply to read geography means to apply to study geography as a university subject, especially in British English.","zh":"「apply to read geography」意思是申請在大學修讀地理，尤其是英式英語用法。"},{"en":"A student may apply to read history if they enjoy analysing past societies.","zh":"如果學生喜歡分析過去社會，可能申請修讀歷史。"},{"en":"If Alex applies to read geography, his interview may test how he thinks about places and environments.","zh":"如果 Alex 申請修讀地理，其面試可能測試他如何思考地方和環境。"},{"en":"The phrase uses “read” to mean study at university.","zh":"這個短語用 “read” 表示在大學修讀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"boost one’s confidence","meaning":"增強某人的信心","examples":[{"en":"The workshop has boosted Alex Green’s confidence.","zh":"工作坊增強了 Alex Green 的信心。"},{"en":"To boost one’s confidence means to increase someone’s belief in their own ability.","zh":"「boost one’s confidence」意思是增加某人對自己能力的信念。"},{"en":"A good mock interview can boost a student’s confidence before the real one.","zh":"好的模擬面試可以在正式面試前增強學生信心。"},{"en":"If candidates receive clear advice, they may feel more prepared and less afraid.","zh":"如果候選人得到清楚建議，他們可能感到更有準備、較少害怕。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making someone feel more self-assured.","zh":"這個短語描述令某人感到更有自信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"feel assured of oneself","meaning":"對自己更有信心","examples":[{"en":"Alex Green feels more assured of himself after the workshop.","zh":"工作坊後，Alex Green 對自己更有信心。"},{"en":"To feel assured of oneself means to feel confident and certain about one’s own ability or behaviour.","zh":"「feel assured of oneself」意思是對自己的能力或行為感到有信心和確定。"},{"en":"A student may feel more assured of herself after practising a speech several times.","zh":"學生練習演講幾次後，可能對自己更有信心。"},{"en":"If candidates know how to behave in the room, they may feel less nervous.","zh":"如果候選人知道在房間中如何行為，就可能較不緊張。"},{"en":"The phrase describes inner confidence.","zh":"這個短語描述內在自信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"control oneself in an interview","meaning":"在面試中控制自己","examples":[{"en":"He feels he knows how to control himself in an interview.","zh":"他覺得自己知道如何在面試中控制自己。"},{"en":"To control oneself in an interview means to manage one’s nerves, body language, and behaviour during the interview.","zh":"「control oneself in an interview」意思是在面試期間管理緊張、身體語言和行為。"},{"en":"A candidate can control himself by breathing slowly before answering a difficult question.","zh":"候選人可以在回答困難問題前慢慢呼吸，以控制自己。"},{"en":"If candidates cannot control their nerves, they may rush answers or forget key points.","zh":"如果候選人不能控制緊張，可能匆忙回答或忘記重點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes self-management under pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述壓力下的自我管理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"little things about","meaning":"關於……的小細節","examples":[{"en":"The little things about posture are really helpful.","zh":"關於姿勢的小細節真的很有幫助。"},{"en":"Little things about something are small details connected with it.","zh":"「little things about」某事，是與它有關的小細節。"},{"en":"The little things about email writing, such as subject lines and greetings, can affect professionalism.","zh":"關於電郵寫作的小細節，例如標題和問候語，可以影響專業感。"},{"en":"If small posture details improve confidence, they can have a large effect.","zh":"如果姿勢小細節改善信心，它們可以產生大影響。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that minor details can matter.","zh":"這個短語顯示微小細節也可以重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"posture","meaning":"姿勢；儀態","examples":[{"en":"Advice about posture can help candidates look more confident.","zh":"關於姿勢的建議可以幫助候選人看起來更自信。"},{"en":"Posture means the way a person holds their body when sitting, standing, or walking.","zh":"「posture」意思是人坐、站或走路時保持身體的方式。"},{"en":"Good posture during a presentation helps a speaker look alert and prepared.","zh":"匯報時良好姿勢幫助演講者看起來精神和準備充分。"},{"en":"If posture is poor, a confident answer may still appear weak.","zh":"如果姿勢不好，即使答案自信，仍可能顯得弱。"},{"en":"The word describes body position and its effect on impression.","zh":"這個詞描述身體位置及其對印象的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"really helpful","meaning":"非常有幫助","examples":[{"en":"The advice about posture is really helpful.","zh":"關於姿勢的建議非常有幫助。"},{"en":"Really helpful means genuinely useful and able to make a task easier or better.","zh":"「really helpful」意思是真正有用，能令任務更容易或更好。"},{"en":"A checklist before an exam can be really helpful for nervous students.","zh":"考試前的清單對緊張學生可以非常有幫助。"},{"en":"If advice leads to immediate improvement, students are more likely to trust it.","zh":"如果建議帶來即時改善，學生更可能信任它。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses strong practical usefulness.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈實用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"it’s like acting","meaning":"這就像演戲","examples":[{"en":"Alex Bexon says the workshop is really like acting.","zh":"Alex Bexon 說工作坊真的就像演戲。"},{"en":"It’s like acting means it involves performing a version of yourself through voice, posture, and behaviour.","zh":"「it’s like acting」意思是透過聲音、姿勢和行為表演某種版本的自己。"},{"en":"Giving a presentation can feel like acting because students must control expression and movement.","zh":"做匯報可能感覺像演戲，因為學生必須控制表情和動作。"},{"en":"If candidates practise confidence like a role, they may perform better even when nervous.","zh":"如果候選人像角色一樣練習自信，即使緊張也可能表現更好。"},{"en":"The phrase compares social performance with stage performance.","zh":"這個短語把社交表現與舞台表演作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"get one’s image across","meaning":"傳達自己的形象","examples":[{"en":"The workshop is about getting your image across.","zh":"工作坊關乎傳達自己的形象。"},{"en":"To get one’s image across means to communicate the impression or identity one wants others to see.","zh":"「get one’s image across」意思是傳達自己希望別人看見的印象或身份。"},{"en":"A student may get their image across by speaking calmly and dressing neatly at an interview.","zh":"學生可能在面試中透過冷靜說話和整潔衣着傳達自己的形象。"},{"en":"If your words and body language send different messages, your image may become unclear.","zh":"如果你的說話和身體語言傳達不同訊息，你的形象可能變得不清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes presenting yourself effectively.","zh":"這個短語描述有效呈現自己。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"for each question","meaning":"對於每題","examples":[{"en":"For each question, only one of the choices is correct.","zh":"對於每題，只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"For each question means for every individual question in a task or test.","zh":"「for each question」意思是對任務或測驗中的每一條問題。"},{"en":"For each question, students should underline the key words before choosing an answer.","zh":"對於每題，學生應在選答案前劃出關鍵詞。"},{"en":"If only one answer is correct, students must compare the options carefully.","zh":"如果只有一個答案正確，學生必須仔細比較選項。"},{"en":"The phrase gives instructions that apply to every question separately.","zh":"這個短語給出逐題適用的指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"only one of the choices is correct","meaning":"只有一個選項正確","examples":[{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct in this section.","zh":"在這部分中，只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct means students must select a single right answer from several options.","zh":"「only one of the choices is correct」意思是學生必須從幾個選項中選出唯一正確答案。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice grammar question, only one of the choices is correct because the others break the sentence pattern.","zh":"在文法選擇題中，只有一個選項正確，因為其他選項破壞句式。"},{"en":"If students choose two options, the answer may be marked wrong.","zh":"如果學生選兩個選項，答案可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strict multiple-choice rule.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴格的多項選擇規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"corresponding letter","meaning":"對應字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should write the corresponding letter in the appropriate box.","zh":"考生應在適當方格寫上對應字母。"},{"en":"A corresponding letter is the letter that matches the chosen answer or option.","zh":"「corresponding letter」是與所選答案或選項相配的字母。"},{"en":"If option C is correct, students should write the corresponding letter C.","zh":"如果 C 選項正確，學生應寫上對應字母 C。"},{"en":"If students write the word instead of the letter, the answer may not follow the instruction.","zh":"如果學生寫字詞而不是字母，答案可能不符合指示。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in exam answer formats.","zh":"這個短語用於考試答案格式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"appropriate box","meaning":"適當方格","examples":[{"en":"The answer should be written in the appropriate box.","zh":"答案應寫在適當方格內。"},{"en":"The appropriate box is the correct space or place where an answer should be written.","zh":"「appropriate box」是應寫入答案的正確空格或位置。"},{"en":"On a form, students must put their candidate number in the appropriate box.","zh":"在表格上，學生必須把考生編號寫在適當方格內。"},{"en":"If an answer is written in the wrong box, it may be hard to mark correctly.","zh":"如果答案寫在錯誤方格，可能難以正確評分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the correct answer location.","zh":"這個短語描述正確答案位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"on your answer sheet","meaning":"在答題紙上","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write their answers on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生在答題紙上寫下答案。"},{"en":"On your answer sheet means in the official place where answers must be recorded.","zh":"「on your answer sheet」意思是在必須記錄答案的正式位置。"},{"en":"In a public exam, students should check that every answer is written on the answer sheet.","zh":"在公開考試中，學生應檢查每個答案都寫在答題紙上。"},{"en":"If answers remain only on the question paper, they may not be marked.","zh":"如果答案只留在試題紙上，可能不會被評改。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an exam instruction about where to write.","zh":"這個短語給出關於寫在哪裡的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"advice does not include","meaning":"建議並不包括","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what Rachel Holland’s advice does not include.","zh":"題目問 Rachel Holland 的建議並不包括甚麼。"},{"en":"Advice does not include something means that thing is not part of the guidance given.","zh":"「advice does not include」某事，意思是該事不是所給指導的一部分。"},{"en":"A study plan may include reading and writing practice but not include private tutoring.","zh":"學習計劃可能包括閱讀和寫作練習，但不包括私人補習。"},{"en":"If a question asks what advice does not include, students must identify the option not mentioned or not supported.","zh":"如果題目問建議並不包括甚麼，學生必須找出沒有提及或不受支持的選項。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on exclusion.","zh":"這個短語集中於排除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"pass exams","meaning":"通過考試","examples":[{"en":"Her social-skills advice does not focus on how to pass exams.","zh":"她的社交技巧建議並不集中於如何通過考試。"},{"en":"To pass exams means to achieve the required marks to succeed in tests.","zh":"「pass exams」意思是在測驗中取得所需分數而成功。"},{"en":"Students usually need revision, practice, and time management to pass exams.","zh":"學生通常需要溫習、練習和時間管理來通過考試。"},{"en":"If a course teaches social skills, it may help interviews but not directly teach exam content.","zh":"如果課程教授社交技巧，它可能幫助面試，但不直接教授考試內容。"},{"en":"The phrase describes academic success in tests.","zh":"這個短語描述測驗中的學術成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"eat correctly","meaning":"正確用餐","examples":[{"en":"Some of her courses teach young people how to eat correctly in formal situations.","zh":"她的一些課程教年輕人在正式場合如何正確用餐。"},{"en":"To eat correctly means to use polite table manners appropriate to the setting.","zh":"「eat correctly」意思是使用符合場合的有禮餐桌禮儀。"},{"en":"At a formal dinner, eating correctly may include using the right cutlery and not speaking with food in your mouth.","zh":"在正式晚宴中，正確用餐可能包括使用合適餐具和不含着食物說話。"},{"en":"If young people know formal dining rules, they may feel less anxious at meals with employers.","zh":"如果年輕人知道正式用餐規則，與僱主用餐時可能較少焦慮。"},{"en":"The phrase describes socially acceptable eating behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述社交上可接受的用餐行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"talk about non-academic subjects","meaning":"談論非學術話題","examples":[{"en":"Small talk often involves talking about non-academic subjects.","zh":"閒談通常涉及談論非學術話題。"},{"en":"To talk about non-academic subjects means to discuss everyday topics not directly related to schoolwork or study.","zh":"「talk about non-academic subjects」意思是討論不直接與學業或學習相關的日常話題。"},{"en":"Students may talk about weather, hobbies, or travel as non-academic subjects before an interview.","zh":"學生可能在面試前談天氣、興趣或旅遊等非學術話題。"},{"en":"If conversation stays only on academic topics, it may feel stiff and unnatural.","zh":"如果對話只停留在學術題目，可能感覺僵硬不自然。"},{"en":"The phrase describes light social conversation topics.","zh":"這個短語描述輕鬆社交對話題目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"believe parents don’t teach","meaning":"認為父母沒有教授……","examples":[{"en":"Rachel believes parents do not always teach social skills effectively.","zh":"Rachel 認為父母不一定有效地教授社交技巧。"},{"en":"To believe parents don’t teach something means to think that parents fail to teach it or do not teach it enough.","zh":"「believe parents don’t teach」某事，意思是認為父母未能教授或教得不夠。"},{"en":"Some teachers believe parents do not always teach children how to manage screen time.","zh":"有些老師認為父母不一定教孩子如何管理屏幕時間。"},{"en":"If parents are unsure themselves, children may receive mixed guidance.","zh":"如果父母自己也不確定，孩子可能收到混亂指引。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses an opinion about gaps in parenting.","zh":"這個短語表達對育兒缺口的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"have so little time","meaning":"時間很少","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that parents may have so little time.","zh":"該選項暗示父母可能時間很少。"},{"en":"To have so little time means to have very limited time available.","zh":"「have so little time」意思是可用時間非常有限。"},{"en":"Working parents may have so little time that long conversations with children become difficult.","zh":"在職父母可能時間很少，以致難以與孩子長談。"},{"en":"If people have little time, important teaching may be rushed or forgotten.","zh":"如果人們時間很少，重要教導可能被匆忙帶過或忘記。"},{"en":"The phrase explains a possible reason for incomplete guidance.","zh":"這個短語解釋指導不完整的可能原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be well educated","meaning":"受過良好教育","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether parents have not been well educated.","zh":"該選項問父母是否未受過良好教育。"},{"en":"To be well educated means to have received a good level of education and knowledge.","zh":"「be well educated」意思是接受過良好程度的教育和知識。"},{"en":"A well-educated person may still feel unsure about modern social rules.","zh":"受過良好教育的人仍可能對現代社交規則感到不確定。"},{"en":"If parents are not confident in a subject, they may avoid teaching it.","zh":"如果父母對某題目沒有信心，可能避免教授它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes educational background, not moral quality.","zh":"這個短語描述教育背景，而不是道德品質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"making small talk well","meaning":"善於閒談","examples":[{"en":"Making small talk well involves preparing questions.","zh":"善於閒談涉及準備問題。"},{"en":"Making small talk well means holding light conversation smoothly and politely.","zh":"「making small talk well」意思是流暢而有禮地進行輕鬆對話。"},{"en":"A student makes small talk well when they ask simple questions and listen to the answers.","zh":"學生提出簡單問題並聆聽答案時，就是善於閒談。"},{"en":"If no one prepares topics, small talk can quickly become awkward silence.","zh":"如果沒有人準備話題，閒談很快會變成尷尬沉默。"},{"en":"The phrase describes skill in informal social conversation.","zh":"這個短語描述非正式社交對話的技巧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"involve asking questions","meaning":"涉及提問","examples":[{"en":"Making small talk well involves asking questions.","zh":"善於閒談涉及提問。"},{"en":"To involve asking questions means to include questions as an important part of the activity.","zh":"「involve asking questions」意思是把提問包括為活動的重要部分。"},{"en":"A good interview involves asking questions as well as answering them.","zh":"好面試涉及提問，也涉及回答問題。"},{"en":"If small talk includes questions, the other person has chances to speak.","zh":"如果閒談包括提問，對方就有機會說話。"},{"en":"The phrase explains one component of a process.","zh":"這個短語解釋過程的一個組成部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"remember what people say","meaning":"記住別人說的話","examples":[{"en":"Good conversation can involve remembering what people say.","zh":"好對話可能涉及記住別人說的話。"},{"en":"To remember what people say means to listen carefully and keep their words or ideas in mind.","zh":"「remember what people say」意思是仔細聆聽並把別人的說話或想法記在心中。"},{"en":"A good friend remembers what people say about their worries and asks about them later.","zh":"好朋友會記住別人說過的憂慮，並之後問候。"},{"en":"If you remember someone’s answer, your next question can feel more natural.","zh":"如果你記住對方的答案，下一個問題可以感覺更自然。"},{"en":"The phrase describes attentive listening.","zh":"這個短語描述用心聆聽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"walking correctly","meaning":"正確地走路","examples":[{"en":"The workshop also includes guidance on walking correctly.","zh":"工作坊也包括關於正確地走路的指導。"},{"en":"Walking correctly means moving with posture, pace, and body language suitable for the situation.","zh":"「walking correctly」意思是以適合情況的姿勢、步速和身體語言移動。"},{"en":"A drama teacher may teach students walking correctly for a formal stage entrance.","zh":"戲劇老師可能教學生為正式舞台進場而正確走路。"},{"en":"If someone walks too quickly or slouches, they may seem nervous or careless.","zh":"如果某人走得太快或彎腰駝背，可能顯得緊張或粗心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes controlled and appropriate movement.","zh":"這個短語描述受控制而合適的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the following sentences","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to complete the following sentences with words from the text.","zh":"考生需要用文本中的詞語完成以下句子。"},{"en":"To complete the following sentences means to fill the gaps in the sentences that come next.","zh":"「complete the following sentences」意思是填補接下來句子中的空格。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete the following sentences by copying exact words from the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過抄寫文章原字完成以下句子。"},{"en":"If students use too many words, their answers may not follow the instruction.","zh":"如果學生使用太多詞，答案可能不符合指示。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam task instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試任務指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should use no more than three words from the text.","zh":"每個答案應使用文本中不多於三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"「no more than three words」意思是答案必須包含三個詞或更少。"},{"en":"If the correct answer is “basic manners”, it fits because it has two words.","zh":"如果正確答案是 “basic manners”，它符合要求，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"If students write four words, the answer may be marked wrong even if the meaning is right.","zh":"如果學生寫四個詞，即使意思正確，答案也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word-limit rule.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格字數限制規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"from the text","meaning":"從文本中","examples":[{"en":"The missing words should be taken from the text.","zh":"缺失詞語應從文本中選取。"},{"en":"From the text means from the reading passage itself, not from outside knowledge.","zh":"「from the text」意思是來自閱讀文章本身，而不是外部知識。"},{"en":"In sentence-completion tasks, answers usually need words from the text exactly as written.","zh":"在句子填充題中，答案通常需要使用文本中原本寫法。"},{"en":"If students use their own wording, the answer may not match the required form.","zh":"如果學生使用自己的措辭，答案可能不符合要求形式。"},{"en":"The phrase tells students where the answer must come from.","zh":"這個短語告訴學生答案必須來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"for each gap","meaning":"每個空格","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should write a short answer for each gap.","zh":"考生應為每個空格寫下簡短答案。"},{"en":"For each gap means for every blank space where an answer is missing.","zh":"「for each gap」意思是對每個缺少答案的空白位置。"},{"en":"In a grammar exercise, students should check the verb form for each gap.","zh":"在文法練習中，學生應為每個空格檢查動詞形式。"},{"en":"If one gap is left empty, the sentence remains incomplete.","zh":"如果有一個空格留空，句子仍然不完整。"},{"en":"The phrase gives instructions for every blank separately.","zh":"這個短語給出逐個空格適用的指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"used to teach","meaning":"以前教","examples":[{"en":"Rachel Holland used to teach maths at an independent school.","zh":"Rachel Holland 以前在私立學校教數學。"},{"en":"Used to teach means taught in the past but does not necessarily teach that subject now.","zh":"「used to teach」意思是過去曾教，但現在未必仍教該科目。"},{"en":"My neighbour used to teach music before she became a school counsellor.","zh":"我的鄰居以前教音樂，後來成為學校輔導員。"},{"en":"If someone used to teach, they may still understand classroom behaviour well.","zh":"如果某人以前教書，他可能仍很了解課室行為。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a past habit or former job.","zh":"這個短語描述過去習慣或以前工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be taught to say","meaning":"被教導說出……","examples":[{"en":"The boys are taught to say their names clearly in the interview room.","zh":"男生們被教導在面試室中清楚說出自己的名字。"},{"en":"To be taught to say something means to be instructed to use certain words or speak in a certain way.","zh":"「be taught to say」某事，意思是被指導使用某些說話或以某種方式說話。"},{"en":"Children are taught to say “thank you” after receiving a gift.","zh":"孩子收到禮物後會被教導說「謝謝」。"},{"en":"If candidates say their names clearly, interviewers can recognise them with confidence.","zh":"如果候選人清楚說出名字，面試官就能有把握地認出他們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes spoken behaviour learned through instruction.","zh":"這個短語描述透過指導學會的說話行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"one of Rachel’s courses","meaning":"Rachel 的其中一個課程","examples":[{"en":"One of Rachel’s courses teaches basic manners to younger children.","zh":"Rachel 的其中一個課程向較年幼孩子教授基本禮貌。"},{"en":"One of Rachel’s courses means one course among the different courses Rachel offers.","zh":"「one of Rachel’s courses」意思是 Rachel 提供的不同課程中的其中一個。"},{"en":"One of a tutor’s courses may focus on writing, while another focuses on speaking.","zh":"導師的其中一個課程可能集中於寫作，另一個則集中於說話。"},{"en":"If a trainer offers several courses, each may target a different age group or skill.","zh":"如果導師提供幾個課程，每個可能針對不同年齡組或技能。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies one item from a larger set.","zh":"這個短語指出較大集合中的其中一項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"involve teaching","meaning":"涉及教授","examples":[{"en":"One course involves teaching basic manners to young children.","zh":"其中一個課程涉及向年幼孩子教授基本禮貌。"},{"en":"To involve teaching something means to include instruction in that skill or topic.","zh":"「involve teaching」某事，意思是包括該技能或題目的教學。"},{"en":"A first-aid course involves teaching students how to respond to injuries.","zh":"急救課程涉及教授學生如何應對受傷。"},{"en":"If a course involves teaching manners, students need practice as well as explanation.","zh":"如果課程涉及教授禮儀，學生需要練習，也需要解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what an activity includes.","zh":"這個短語描述某活動包括甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"younger children","meaning":"較年幼的孩子","examples":[{"en":"Younger children can learn basic manners in a short workshop.","zh":"較年幼的孩子可以在短工作坊中學習基本禮貌。"},{"en":"Younger children are children who are relatively young compared with older pupils or teenagers.","zh":"「younger children」是相比年長學生或青少年較年幼的孩子。"},{"en":"Younger children often learn best through games, stories, and simple role-play.","zh":"較年幼的孩子通常透過遊戲、故事和簡單角色扮演學得最好。"},{"en":"If younger children practise manners early, polite behaviour can become natural.","zh":"如果較年幼孩子早些練習禮貌，有禮行為可以變得自然。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a younger age group within school-age children.","zh":"這個短語描述學齡兒童中的較年幼組別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"put more confidence into","meaning":"將更多信心注入……","examples":[{"en":"Rachel teaches the boys how to put more confidence into their walking.","zh":"Rachel 教男生如何將更多信心注入走路方式。"},{"en":"To put more confidence into something means to make an action look or feel more self-assured.","zh":"「put more confidence into」某事，意思是令某行動看起來或感覺更有自信。"},{"en":"A student can put more confidence into a speech by speaking more slowly and clearly.","zh":"學生可以透過說得更慢更清楚，將更多信心注入演講。"},{"en":"If walking looks confident, the person may appear more ready for a formal situation.","zh":"如果走路看起來有自信，該人可能顯得更準備好面對正式場合。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adding self-assurance to behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述為行為加入自信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"do the following statements agree with","meaning":"以下陳述是否與……一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether the following statements agree with the passage.","zh":"考生判斷以下陳述是否與文章一致。"},{"en":"Do the following statements agree with asks whether each statement matches the information in the text.","zh":"「do the following statements agree with」是問每項陳述是否符合文本資料。"},{"en":"In a reading exam, students check the passage before deciding if a statement agrees with it.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生先檢查文章，再判斷陳述是否與它一致。"},{"en":"If a statement changes an important detail, it may not agree with the passage.","zh":"如果陳述改變重要細節，它可能不與文章一致。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a true, false, or not given task.","zh":"這個短語引入 true、false 或 not given 題型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"information given","meaning":"所給資料","examples":[{"en":"The statements must be checked against the information given in the passage.","zh":"陳述必須根據文章中所給資料核對。"},{"en":"Information given means the facts or details actually provided in the text.","zh":"「information given」意思是文本中實際提供的事實或細節。"},{"en":"Students should answer reading questions using the information given, not personal opinion.","zh":"學生應使用所給資料回答閱讀問題，而不是個人意見。"},{"en":"If information is not given, students should not guess from outside knowledge.","zh":"如果資料沒有給出，學生不應用外部知識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses evidence from the passage.","zh":"這個短語強調文章中的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"if the statement agrees with","meaning":"如果陳述與……一致","examples":[{"en":"Write true if the statement agrees with the information.","zh":"如果陳述與資料一致，則寫 true。"},{"en":"If the statement agrees with means if the statement matches what the text says.","zh":"「if the statement agrees with」意思是如果陳述符合文本所說。"},{"en":"If the statement agrees with the passage, students should choose TRUE.","zh":"如果陳述與文章一致，學生應選 TRUE。"},{"en":"If one word changes the meaning, the statement may no longer agree with the text.","zh":"如果一個詞改變意思，陳述可能不再與文本一致。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the condition for a TRUE answer.","zh":"這個短語解釋 TRUE 答案的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"if the statement contradicts","meaning":"如果陳述與……矛盾","examples":[{"en":"Write false if the statement contradicts the information.","zh":"如果陳述與資料矛盾，則寫 false。"},{"en":"If the statement contradicts means if it says the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"「if the statement contradicts」意思是如果它說出與文本相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says the workshop was useful, a statement saying it had no effect contradicts it.","zh":"如果文章說工作坊有用，而陳述說它沒有作用，就是與文章矛盾。"},{"en":"If a statement directly conflicts with the text, students should not choose NOT GIVEN.","zh":"如果陳述與文本直接衝突，學生不應選 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the condition for a FALSE answer.","zh":"這個短語解釋 FALSE 答案的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"Write not given if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果沒有這方面的資料，則寫 not given。"},{"en":"No information on this means the text does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"「no information on this」意思是文本沒有說明該陳述是真是假。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions a student’s age, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文章從未提及學生年齡，就沒有這方面的資料。"},{"en":"If evidence is missing, students should choose NOT GIVEN rather than guess.","zh":"如果缺乏證據，學生應選 NOT GIVEN，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase describes absence of textual support.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏文本支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"receive coaching from","meaning":"接受……的指導","examples":[{"en":"The Oxbridge candidates receive coaching from Rachel Holland.","zh":"牛津劍橋申請人接受 Rachel Holland 的指導。"},{"en":"To receive coaching from someone means to be trained or guided by that person.","zh":"「receive coaching from」某人，意思是接受該人的訓練或指導。"},{"en":"A football team may receive coaching from a former professional player.","zh":"足球隊可能接受前職業球員的指導。"},{"en":"If candidates receive coaching from an expert, they can practise skills more effectively.","zh":"如果候選人接受專家指導，就能更有效地練習技能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning through guided support.","zh":"這個短語描述透過引導支援學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"include tips on writing","meaning":"包括寫作建議","examples":[{"en":"Some of Rachel’s courses include tips on writing thank-you letters.","zh":"Rachel 的一些課程包括寫感謝信的建議。"},{"en":"To include tips on writing means to contain advice about how to write something well.","zh":"「include tips on writing」意思是包含如何寫好某類文字的建議。"},{"en":"An English course may include tips on writing introductions and conclusions.","zh":"英文課程可能包括寫引言和結論的建議。"},{"en":"If students learn writing tips, they may produce clearer and more polite messages.","zh":"如果學生學到寫作建議，他們可能寫出更清楚、更有禮貌的訊息。"},{"en":"The phrase describes advice included inside a course or guide.","zh":"這個短語描述課程或指南中包含的建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be more difficult if","meaning":"如果……會更困難","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Rachel’s job would be more difficult if she taught the boys normally.","zh":"題目問如果 Rachel 平常教這些男生，她的工作會否更困難。"},{"en":"Be more difficult if means become harder under a particular condition.","zh":"「be more difficult if」意思是在某條件下變得更困難。"},{"en":"Teaching speaking may be more difficult if students are afraid to make mistakes.","zh":"如果學生害怕犯錯，教授說話可能會更困難。"},{"en":"If Rachel were a regular teacher, students might react differently from how they react to an outside trainer.","zh":"如果 Rachel 是常規老師，學生的反應可能不同於面對外來導師。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a condition that could increase difficulty.","zh":"這個短語引入可能增加困難的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the key to getting an Oxbridge place","meaning":"獲得牛津劍橋學位的關鍵","examples":[{"en":"The workshop is useful, but it is not the key to getting an Oxbridge place.","zh":"工作坊有用，但它不是獲得牛津劍橋學位的關鍵。"},{"en":"The key to getting an Oxbridge place means the most important factor in being accepted by Oxford or Cambridge.","zh":"「the key to getting an Oxbridge place」意思是被牛津或劍橋取錄的最重要因素。"},{"en":"Strong academic thinking is more likely to be the key to getting an Oxbridge place than perfect table manners.","zh":"強大的學術思考比完美餐桌禮儀更可能是獲得牛津劍橋學位的關鍵。"},{"en":"If a workshop improves confidence, it can help but cannot replace subject knowledge.","zh":"如果工作坊改善信心，它可以幫助，但不能取代學科知識。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main factor behind admission success.","zh":"這個短語指出取錄成功背後的主要因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be interested in","meaning":"對……感興趣","examples":[{"en":"The boys become interested in many parts of the workshop.","zh":"男生們對工作坊的許多部分變得感興趣。"},{"en":"To be interested in something means to want to know more about it or pay attention to it.","zh":"「be interested in」某事，意思是想了解更多或注意它。"},{"en":"A student may become interested in history after hearing a story about ordinary people’s lives.","zh":"學生聽到關於普通人生活的故事後，可能對歷史感興趣。"},{"en":"If learners are interested in a topic, they participate more actively.","zh":"如果學習者對題目感興趣，他們會更積極參與。"},{"en":"The phrase describes curiosity or attention.","zh":"這個短語描述好奇或注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"things that are not relevant to them","meaning":"與他們無關的事情","examples":[{"en":"Some workshop topics are not relevant to the boys’ everyday lives.","zh":"有些工作坊題目與男生日常生活無關。"},{"en":"Things that are not relevant to them are topics or skills that do not connect clearly with their needs or experience.","zh":"「things that are not relevant to them」是與他們需要或經驗沒有清楚關係的題目或技能。"},{"en":"A lesson on mortgage law may not be relevant to young children.","zh":"按揭法律課可能與年幼孩子無關。"},{"en":"If students cannot see why a topic matters, they may still enjoy it if the teaching is lively.","zh":"如果學生看不出題目為何重要，只要教學有趣，他們仍可能享受它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes material that feels distant from someone’s life.","zh":"這個短語描述感覺與某人生活遙遠的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 99 - Can You Charm Your Way into Oxbridge?.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 100":[{"front":"look your age","meaning":"看起來符合實際年齡","examples":[{"en":"It can be hard to tell whether someone really looks their age.","zh":"有時很難判斷一個人是否真的看起來符合實際年齡。"},{"en":"To look your age means to appear as old as you actually are.","zh":"看起來符合實際年齡，指外表與真實年齡相符。"},{"en":"A healthy seventy-year-old may not look his age at all.","zh":"一位健康的七十歲長者可能完全不像實際年齡。"},{"en":"If stress affects your face, you may look older than your age.","zh":"如果壓力影響你的面容，你可能看起來比實際年齡老。"},{"en":"The phrase compares appearance with real age.","zh":"這個短語比較外貌與真實年齡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"guess someone’s exact age","meaning":"猜出某人的確實年齡","examples":[{"en":"It can be hard to guess someone’s exact age.","zh":"猜出某人的確實年齡可能很困難。"},{"en":"To guess someone’s exact age means to estimate precisely how old they are.","zh":"猜出某人的確實年齡，指準確估計他幾歲。"},{"en":"A teacher may guess a student’s age from their school year.","zh":"老師可能從學生的年級猜出其年齡。"},{"en":"If a person looks very young or mature, guessing their exact age becomes difficult.","zh":"如果某人看起來很年輕或成熟，猜出確實年齡就會變難。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on a precise age, not a rough age group.","zh":"這個短語強調準確年齡，而不是大概年齡組別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a range of factors","meaning":"一系列因素","examples":[{"en":"A range of factors may leave marks on our appearance.","zh":"一系列因素可能在我們的外貌上留下痕跡。"},{"en":"A range of factors means several different causes or influences.","zh":"一系列因素指幾種不同原因或影響。"},{"en":"Exam results can depend on a range of factors, including sleep, practice, and confidence.","zh":"考試成績可取決於一系列因素，包括睡眠、練習和信心。"},{"en":"If many factors affect appearance, no single reason explains ageing fully.","zh":"如果許多因素影響外貌，單一原因就不能完全解釋老化。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a situation has more than one cause.","zh":"這個短語顯示某情況有多於一個原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"leave marks on","meaning":"在……留下痕跡","examples":[{"en":"Lack of sleep can leave marks on our appearance.","zh":"睡眠不足可以在我們的外貌上留下痕跡。"},{"en":"To leave marks on something means to create visible effects or signs on it.","zh":"在某物上留下痕跡，指在其上造成可見影響或跡象。"},{"en":"A heavy schoolbag can leave marks on a student’s shoulders.","zh":"沉重書包可以在學生肩膀上留下痕跡。"},{"en":"If tiredness leaves marks on the face, people may notice dark circles.","zh":"如果疲倦在臉上留下痕跡，人們可能注意到黑眼圈。"},{"en":"The phrase can be physical or metaphorical.","zh":"這個短語可以是實際痕跡，也可以是抽象影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"our appearance","meaning":"我們的外貌","examples":[{"en":"Many factors can affect our appearance.","zh":"許多因素可以影響我們的外貌。"},{"en":"Our appearance means how we look to other people.","zh":"我們的外貌指別人看見我們時的樣子。"},{"en":"Clothes, posture, skin, and facial expression all form part of our appearance.","zh":"衣着、姿勢、皮膚和面部表情都構成我們外貌的一部分。"},{"en":"If our appearance changes suddenly, people may ask whether we are tired or unwell.","zh":"如果我們的外貌突然改變，人們可能問我們是否疲倦或不舒服。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to visible outward look.","zh":"這個短語指可見的外在樣子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"our view of ourselves","meaning":"我們對自己的看法","examples":[{"en":"Our view of ourselves may affect how old we look.","zh":"我們對自己的看法可能影響我們看起來有多老。"},{"en":"Our view of ourselves means how we think and feel about who we are.","zh":"我們對自己的看法，指我們如何理解和感受自己是誰。"},{"en":"A student with a positive view of herself may stand taller and speak more confidently.","zh":"對自己有正面看法的學生，可能站得更直、說話更有信心。"},{"en":"If people see themselves as old and tired, their posture and expression may change.","zh":"如果人們把自己看成老和疲累，其姿勢和表情可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase connects self-image with behaviour and appearance.","zh":"這個短語把自我形象與行為和外貌連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the good news is that","meaning":"好消息是","examples":[{"en":"The good news is that some lifestyle changes can make us look younger.","zh":"好消息是，一些生活方式改變可以令我們看起來更年輕。"},{"en":"The good news is that introduces a positive point after a problem.","zh":"好消息是，用來在問題之後引出正面一點。"},{"en":"The test was difficult, but the good news is that most students improved.","zh":"測驗很困難，但好消息是大部分學生都有進步。"},{"en":"If ageing has many causes, the good news is that some can be changed.","zh":"如果老化有許多原因，好消息是有些原因可以改變。"},{"en":"The phrase prepares readers for hope or reassurance.","zh":"這個短語讓讀者準備聽到希望或安慰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"add years to your appearance","meaning":"令你看起來老幾歲","examples":[{"en":"Stress and sun exposure can add years to your appearance.","zh":"壓力和日曬可以令你看起來老幾歲。"},{"en":"To add years to your appearance means to make you look older than you are.","zh":"令你看起來老幾歲，指令你看起來比實際年齡老。"},{"en":"Too little sleep before exams can add years to a student’s appearance.","zh":"考試前睡眠太少，可以令學生看起來老幾歲。"},{"en":"If smoking damages the skin, it may add years to the face.","zh":"如果吸煙損害皮膚，它可能令面容變老。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that visually ages a person.","zh":"這個短語描述令人在視覺上變老的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"it follows that","meaning":"由此可見","examples":[{"en":"If some factors add years to your appearance, it follows that others can take years off.","zh":"如果某些因素令你看起來老幾歲，由此可見其他因素可以令你看起來年輕幾歲。"},{"en":"It follows that means this conclusion is logical from what was just said.","zh":"由此可見，指這個結論可由剛才所說的內容合理推出。"},{"en":"If practice improves speaking, it follows that no practice may slow progress.","zh":"如果練習改善口語，由此可見不練習可能拖慢進步。"},{"en":"If diet affects skin, it follows that changing diet may affect appearance.","zh":"如果飲食影響皮膚，由此可見改變飲食可能影響外貌。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a logical result.","zh":"這個短語引出邏輯結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"take years off","meaning":"令……看起來年輕幾歲","examples":[{"en":"Healthy habits can take years off your appearance.","zh":"健康習慣可以令你的外貌看起來年輕幾歲。"},{"en":"To take years off means to make someone look younger.","zh":"令某人看起來年輕幾歲，指令某人外表更年輕。"},{"en":"Better sleep and fresh food can take years off a tired face.","zh":"更好的睡眠和新鮮食物可以令疲倦面容看起來年輕幾歲。"},{"en":"If exercise improves posture and skin tone, it may take years off your look.","zh":"如果運動改善姿勢和膚色，它可能令你看起來更年輕。"},{"en":"The phrase is about appearance, not changing real age.","zh":"這個短語關於外貌，而不是改變真實年齡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have control over","meaning":"對……有控制權","examples":[{"en":"We do not always have control over the social factors that affect our appearance.","zh":"我們不一定對影響外貌的社會因素有控制權。"},{"en":"To have control over something means to be able to influence or manage it.","zh":"對某事有控制權，指能影響或管理它。"},{"en":"Students have control over revision time but not over the exam questions.","zh":"學生可以控制溫習時間，但不能控制考試題目。"},{"en":"If you have control over diet and sleep, you can change some ageing factors.","zh":"如果你能控制飲食和睡眠，就能改變一些老化因素。"},{"en":"The phrase separates what we can change from what we cannot.","zh":"這個短語區分可改變和不可改變的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"social factors","meaning":"社會因素","examples":[{"en":"Social factors can influence how old people look.","zh":"社會因素可以影響人們看起來有多老。"},{"en":"Social factors are conditions connected with society, such as class, work, income, and stress.","zh":"社會因素是與社會有關的條件，例如階層、工作、收入和壓力。"},{"en":"A person’s job and housing may be social factors affecting health.","zh":"一個人的工作和住屋可能是影響健康的社會因素。"},{"en":"If social factors create long-term stress, they may affect appearance.","zh":"如果社會因素造成長期壓力，它們可能影響外貌。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to influences from society, not only personal choices.","zh":"這個短語指來自社會的影響，而不只是個人選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"take steps to","meaning":"採取措施去","examples":[{"en":"There are steps we can take to slow the effects of ageing.","zh":"我們可以採取一些措施去減慢老化影響。"},{"en":"To take steps to do something means to take practical actions toward a goal.","zh":"採取措施去做某事，指為達到目標而採取實際行動。"},{"en":"A school may take steps to reduce bullying by improving supervision.","zh":"學校可能透過改善監督來採取措施減少欺凌。"},{"en":"If you take steps to sleep better, your skin may look healthier.","zh":"如果你採取措施改善睡眠，皮膚可能看起來更健康。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests planned action, not just hope.","zh":"這個短語暗示有計劃的行動，而不只是希望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the ravages of age","meaning":"歲月的摧殘","examples":[{"en":"Good habits may help stop the ravages of age.","zh":"良好習慣可能有助阻止歲月的摧殘。"},{"en":"The ravages of age are the damaging effects ageing can have on the body and appearance.","zh":"歲月的摧殘，是老化對身體和外貌造成的損害。"},{"en":"Regular exercise may reduce the ravages of age on muscles and posture.","zh":"定期運動可能減少歲月對肌肉和姿勢的摧殘。"},{"en":"If people ignore health for years, the ravages of age may appear earlier.","zh":"如果人們多年忽視健康，歲月的摧殘可能更早出現。"},{"en":"The phrase presents ageing as something that slowly damages the body.","zh":"這個短語把老化呈現為慢慢損害身體的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"environmental factors","meaning":"環境因素","examples":[{"en":"The report studied environmental factors that affect facial ageing.","zh":"該報告研究影響面部老化的環境因素。"},{"en":"Environmental factors are outside conditions, such as sunlight, pollution, climate, and living environment.","zh":"環境因素是外在條件，例如陽光、污染、氣候和生活環境。"},{"en":"Air pollution and strong sun are environmental factors that may affect skin.","zh":"空氣污染和強烈陽光是可能影響皮膚的環境因素。"},{"en":"If environmental factors are harsh, the face may age faster.","zh":"如果環境因素惡劣，面部可能老化得更快。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to influences from surroundings.","zh":"這個短語指來自周遭環境的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"facial ageing","meaning":"面部老化","examples":[{"en":"The report examined the influence of environmental factors on facial ageing.","zh":"該報告研究環境因素對面部老化的影響。"},{"en":"Facial ageing means the visible ageing of the face, such as wrinkles, dryness, and sagging.","zh":"面部老化指臉部可見的老化，例如皺紋、乾燥和鬆弛。"},{"en":"Too much sun can speed up facial ageing around the eyes and cheeks.","zh":"過量日曬可以加速眼周和臉頰的面部老化。"},{"en":"If facial ageing begins early, people may look older than their real age.","zh":"如果面部老化提早開始，人們可能看起來比真實年齡老。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on ageing signs seen on the face.","zh":"這個短語強調臉上可見的老化跡象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"how we live","meaning":"我們的生活方式","examples":[{"en":"The study showed that how we live can affect how old we look.","zh":"研究顯示，我們的生活方式會影響我們看起來有多老。"},{"en":"How we live means our daily lifestyle, habits, work, rest, food, and stress levels.","zh":"我們的生活方式指日常生活習慣、工作、休息、飲食和壓力水平。"},{"en":"How we live changes when we sleep less, eat badly, or exercise more.","zh":"當我們睡得少、吃得差或多做運動，生活方式就會改變。"},{"en":"If how we live damages health, it may also damage appearance.","zh":"如果生活方式損害健康，也可能損害外貌。"},{"en":"The phrase points to lifestyle rather than genetics alone.","zh":"這個短語指向生活習慣，而不只是基因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"affect how old we look","meaning":"影響我們看起來有多老","examples":[{"en":"Social class and lifestyle can affect how old we look.","zh":"社會階層和生活方式可以影響我們看起來有多老。"},{"en":"To affect how old we look means to influence our perceived age.","zh":"影響我們看起來有多老，指影響我們的觀感年齡。"},{"en":"Good sleep can affect how old we look by reducing tired eyes.","zh":"良好睡眠可以透過減少疲倦眼神，影響我們看起來有多老。"},{"en":"If stress makes the face tense, it may make a person look older.","zh":"如果壓力令面部繃緊，它可能令人看起來更老。"},{"en":"The phrase links causes with apparent age.","zh":"這個短語把原因與外表年齡連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be photographed","meaning":"被拍照","examples":[{"en":"The twins were photographed for the ageing study.","zh":"這對雙胞胎為老化研究被拍照。"},{"en":"To be photographed means to have one’s picture taken with a camera.","zh":"被拍照，指被相機拍下照片。"},{"en":"Students may be photographed for school ID cards.","zh":"學生可能為學生證被拍照。"},{"en":"If participants are photographed, researchers can compare their appearance fairly.","zh":"如果參與者被拍照，研究者就能公平比較其外貌。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being recorded in a photo.","zh":"這個短語描述被相片記錄下來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"aged between","meaning":"年齡介乎……之間","examples":[{"en":"Ten female nurses aged between 25 and 46 took part in the study.","zh":"十名年齡介乎25至46歲的女護士參與研究。"},{"en":"Aged between X and Y means having ages from X to Y.","zh":"年齡介乎 X 與 Y 之間，指年齡由 X 至 Y。"},{"en":"The course is for children aged between 8 and 12.","zh":"該課程適合年齡介乎8至12歲的兒童。"},{"en":"If participants are aged between 25 and 46, the study covers young to middle adulthood.","zh":"如果參與者年齡介乎25至46歲，研究涵蓋青年至中年成人。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an age range.","zh":"這個短語給出年齡範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be asked to guess","meaning":"被要求猜測","examples":[{"en":"The nurses were asked to guess how old the models were.","zh":"護士被要求猜測模特兒幾歲。"},{"en":"To be asked to guess means to be invited to estimate something without full information.","zh":"被要求猜測，指在資料不完整下被邀請估計某事。"},{"en":"Students may be asked to guess a word’s meaning from context.","zh":"學生可能被要求從上下文猜測詞義。"},{"en":"If people are asked to guess age from photos, their answers show perceived age.","zh":"如果人們被要求從照片猜年齡，其答案就顯示觀感年齡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a task based on estimation.","zh":"這個短語描述基於估計的任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the results were intriguing","meaning":"結果耐人尋味","examples":[{"en":"The results were intriguing because several lifestyle factors affected perceived age.","zh":"結果耐人尋味，因為幾種生活方式因素影響觀感年齡。"},{"en":"Intriguing results are interesting because they raise questions or reveal unexpected patterns.","zh":"耐人尋味的結果，是因提出問題或揭示意外模式而有趣的結果。"},{"en":"A class survey may be intriguing if quiet students report the highest confidence online.","zh":"如果班中安靜學生在線上回報最高信心，班級調查結果可能耐人尋味。"},{"en":"If lifestyle affects perceived age, researchers may want to know why.","zh":"如果生活方式影響觀感年齡，研究者可能想知道原因。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that findings are interesting and worth further thought.","zh":"這個短語表示研究發現有趣並值得進一步思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"belong to a high social class","meaning":"屬於較高社會階層","examples":[{"en":"Belonging to a high social class can make people look younger.","zh":"屬於較高社會階層可以令人看起來更年輕。"},{"en":"To belong to a high social class means to be part of a wealthier or more privileged social group.","zh":"屬於較高社會階層，指身處較富裕或較有優勢的社會群體。"},{"en":"People in a high social class may have better housing, food, healthcare, and less physical hardship.","zh":"較高社會階層的人可能有較好住屋、食物、醫療和較少身體艱辛。"},{"en":"If social class affects stress and health, it may also affect appearance.","zh":"如果社會階層影響壓力和健康，也可能影響外貌。"},{"en":"The phrase describes social position, not personal character.","zh":"這個短語描述社會位置，而不是個人性格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"high social class","meaning":"較高社會階層","examples":[{"en":"A high social class was linked with a younger appearance.","zh":"較高社會階層與較年輕外貌有關。"},{"en":"High social class means a more privileged position in society, often connected with wealth, education, or status.","zh":"較高社會階層，指社會中較有優勢的位置，常與財富、教育或地位相關。"},{"en":"A person from a high social class may have easier access to healthcare.","zh":"較高社會階層的人可能較容易獲得醫療服務。"},{"en":"If high social class reduces daily hardship, it may help people look younger.","zh":"如果較高社會階層減少日常艱辛，它可能幫助人看起來更年輕。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to social advantage.","zh":"這個短語指社會優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"look up to four years younger","meaning":"看起來最多年輕四歲","examples":[{"en":"Some people can look up to four years younger.","zh":"有些人可以看起來最多年輕四歲。"},{"en":"To look up to four years younger means to appear as much as four years below one’s real age.","zh":"看起來最多年輕四歲，指外表比真實年齡最多少四歲。"},{"en":"A forty-year-old who looks thirty-six looks up to four years younger.","zh":"一位四十歲的人如果看起來三十六歲，就是看起來年輕四歲。"},{"en":"If healthy habits reduce visible ageing, a person may seem several years younger.","zh":"如果健康習慣減少可見老化，一個人可能看似年輕幾歲。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the maximum difference in apparent age.","zh":"這個短語給出外表年齡差距的最大值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lifestyle factors","meaning":"生活方式因素","examples":[{"en":"Many lifestyle factors were shown to affect the way we look.","zh":"許多生活方式因素被證明會影響我們的外貌。"},{"en":"Lifestyle factors are daily habits and choices, such as diet, sleep, exercise, and smoking.","zh":"生活方式因素是日常習慣和選擇，例如飲食、睡眠、運動和吸煙。"},{"en":"A doctor may ask about lifestyle factors before advising on skin health.","zh":"醫生給皮膚健康建議前，可能詢問生活方式因素。"},{"en":"If lifestyle factors are unhealthy, they may speed up visible ageing.","zh":"如果生活方式因素不健康，它們可能加速可見老化。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to changeable parts of daily life.","zh":"這個短語指日常生活中可改變的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"affect the way we look","meaning":"影響我們的外貌","examples":[{"en":"Diet, stress, and sun exposure can affect the way we look.","zh":"飲食、壓力和日曬可以影響我們的外貌。"},{"en":"To affect the way we look means to change our visible appearance.","zh":"影響我們的外貌，指改變我們可見的樣子。"},{"en":"A new haircut can affect the way we look immediately.","zh":"新髮型可以立即影響我們的外貌。"},{"en":"If poor diet dries the skin, it affects the way the face appears.","zh":"如果不良飲食令皮膚乾燥，就會影響面部看起來的樣子。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a cause with outward appearance.","zh":"這個短語把原因與外在樣子連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"look a full year younger","meaning":"看起來整整年輕一歲","examples":[{"en":"Having children was found to make men look a full year younger.","zh":"研究發現，有子女令男性看起來整整年輕一歲。"},{"en":"To look a full year younger means to appear exactly one year younger in perceived age.","zh":"看起來整整年輕一歲，指觀感年齡準確地少一歲。"},{"en":"If a thirty-five-year-old looks thirty-four, they look a full year younger.","zh":"如果三十五歲的人看起來三十四歲，就是看起來整整年輕一歲。"},{"en":"If family life improves mood or purpose, it may affect how old someone appears.","zh":"如果家庭生活改善心情或目標感，可能影響某人看起來有多老。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a complete one-year difference.","zh":"這個短語強調完整一年的差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have no effect on","meaning":"對……沒有影響","examples":[{"en":"Having children had no effect on women’s perceived age.","zh":"有子女對女性的觀感年齡沒有影響。"},{"en":"To have no effect on something means not to change or influence it.","zh":"對某事沒有影響，指不改變或不影響它。"},{"en":"Drinking water before a spelling test may have no effect on a student’s score.","zh":"默書前喝水可能對學生成績沒有影響。"},{"en":"If a factor has no effect, results stay the same whether it is present or not.","zh":"如果某因素沒有影響，不論它是否存在，結果都保持一樣。"},{"en":"The phrase means there is no noticeable influence.","zh":"這個短語指沒有明顯影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cancel out the benefit","meaning":"抵銷好處","examples":[{"en":"Having four or more children cancelled out the benefit for men.","zh":"有四名或以上子女抵銷了男性所得的好處。"},{"en":"To cancel out the benefit means to remove or neutralise a positive effect.","zh":"抵銷好處，指消除或中和正面效果。"},{"en":"Exercising is helpful, but eating too much junk food may cancel out the benefit.","zh":"運動有幫助，但吃太多垃圾食物可能抵銷好處。"},{"en":"If one factor makes people look younger but another adds stress, the advantage may disappear.","zh":"如果某因素令人看起來更年輕，但另一因素增加壓力，優勢可能消失。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a good effect can be lost.","zh":"這個短語顯示好效果可以被抵消。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"depression","meaning":"抑鬱","examples":[{"en":"Depression was one of the biggest factors in making people look older.","zh":"抑鬱是令 人看起來較老的最大因素之一。"},{"en":"Depression is a serious mental health condition involving long-lasting sadness, low energy, and loss of interest.","zh":"抑鬱是一種嚴重心理健康狀況，涉及長期悲傷、低能量和失去興趣。"},{"en":"A depressed student may stop sleeping well, eating well, or seeing friends.","zh":"抑鬱學生可能停止睡得好、吃得好或見朋友。"},{"en":"If depression affects sleep and facial expression, it can also affect appearance.","zh":"如果抑鬱影響睡眠和面部表情，也可以影響外貌。"},{"en":"The word refers to more than ordinary sadness.","zh":"這個詞不只是普通傷心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sun exposure","meaning":"日曬；陽光暴露","examples":[{"en":"Sun exposure can make people look old before their time.","zh":"日曬可以令人未老先衰。"},{"en":"Sun exposure means the skin being exposed to sunlight.","zh":"日曬指皮膚暴露在陽光下。"},{"en":"A worker outdoors all day has more sun exposure than an office worker.","zh":"整天在戶外工作的工人，比辦公室員工有更多日曬。"},{"en":"If sun exposure is excessive, the skin may develop wrinkles and dark spots earlier.","zh":"如果日曬過量，皮膚可能更早出現皺紋和色斑。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to contact with sunlight, especially on the skin.","zh":"這個短語指與陽光接觸，尤其是皮膚接觸陽光。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the biggest factors in","meaning":"……中最大的因素","examples":[{"en":"Depression and sun exposure were the biggest factors in making people look older.","zh":"抑鬱和日曬是令 人看起來較老的最大因素。"},{"en":"The biggest factors in something are the most important causes or influences.","zh":"某事中最大的因素，是最重要的原因或影響。"},{"en":"Sleep and practice are often the biggest factors in exam performance.","zh":"睡眠和練習常是考試表現中最大的因素。"},{"en":"If two factors have the strongest effect, they deserve the most attention.","zh":"如果兩個因素影響最強，就最值得注意。"},{"en":"The phrase ranks causes by importance.","zh":"這個短語按重要性排列原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"look old before your time","meaning":"未老先衰","examples":[{"en":"Too much sun exposure can make you look old before your time.","zh":"過量日曬可以令你未老先衰。"},{"en":"To look old before your time means to look older than expected for your age.","zh":"未老先衰，指看起來比該年齡應有樣子更老。"},{"en":"A young office worker under constant stress may look old before her time.","zh":"長期受壓的年輕辦公室員工可能未老先衰。"},{"en":"If skin is damaged early, the face may show ageing signs too soon.","zh":"如果皮膚早早受損，面部可能太早出現老化跡象。"},{"en":"The phrase describes premature visible ageing.","zh":"這個短語描述過早出現的可見老化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"add up to","meaning":"增加多達","examples":[{"en":"Depression added up to three and a half years to a woman’s perceived age.","zh":"抑鬱令女性觀感年齡增加多達三年半。"},{"en":"To add up to a number means to reach that total amount.","zh":"增加至某數量，指達到該總量。"},{"en":"Small daily expenses can add up to a large monthly bill.","zh":"小額日常開支可以累積成大筆每月帳單。"},{"en":"If several ageing factors add up, the face may look much older.","zh":"如果幾種老化因素累積，面容可能看起來老很多。"},{"en":"The phrase shows total accumulated effect.","zh":"這個短語顯示累積總效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"perceived age","meaning":"觀感年齡","examples":[{"en":"Depression can increase a person’s perceived age.","zh":"抑鬱可以增加一個人的觀感年齡。"},{"en":"Perceived age is how old someone appears to other people.","zh":"觀感年齡是某人在別人眼中看起來幾歲。"},{"en":"A forty-year-old may have a perceived age of thirty-five if they look younger.","zh":"如果四十歲的人看起來較年輕，其觀感年齡可能是三十五歲。"},{"en":"If stress changes the face, perceived age may rise even though real age has not changed.","zh":"如果壓力改變面容，即使真實年齡沒有改變，觀感年齡也可能上升。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to judged age, not actual age.","zh":"這個短語指被判斷出的年齡，而不是真實年齡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pile on","meaning":"增加；加上","examples":[{"en":"Sun exposure piled on at least an extra year.","zh":"日曬至少額外增加一年。"},{"en":"To pile on something means to add more of it, often in a heavy or noticeable way.","zh":"“Pile on” 某物，指增加更多，通常是明顯或沉重地增加。"},{"en":"A teacher should not pile on homework when students already have exams.","zh":"當學生已有考試，老師不應再加上大量功課。"},{"en":"If sun damage piles on extra years, the face appears older.","zh":"如果日曬傷害加上額外年齡，面容就顯得更老。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests adding an unwanted amount.","zh":"這個短語暗示增加不想要的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at least an extra year","meaning":"至少額外一年","examples":[{"en":"Sun exposure added at least an extra year to perceived age.","zh":"日曬令觀感年齡至少額外增加一年。"},{"en":"At least an extra year means one more year or possibly more.","zh":"至少額外一年，指多一年或可能更多。"},{"en":"A delayed project may need at least an extra year to finish.","zh":"延誤的項目可能需要至少額外一年完成。"},{"en":"If a habit adds at least an extra year to appearance, its effect is clearly visible.","zh":"如果一種習慣令外貌至少額外老一年，其效果就很明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a minimum additional amount of time.","zh":"這個短語給出額外時間的最低數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"smoking","meaning":"吸煙","examples":[{"en":"Smoking can make both men and women look older.","zh":"吸煙可以令男性和女性看起來較老。"},{"en":"Smoking means breathing in tobacco smoke from cigarettes, cigars, or similar products.","zh":"吸煙指吸入香煙、雪茄或類似產品的煙草煙霧。"},{"en":"A smoker may develop lines around the mouth after years of smoking.","zh":"吸煙者多年吸煙後，口部周圍可能出現皺紋。"},{"en":"If smoking reduces skin moisture and adds toxins, the face may age faster.","zh":"如果吸煙減少皮膚水分並加入毒素，面部可能老化得更快。"},{"en":"The word refers to a habit strongly linked with health risks.","zh":"這個詞指一種與健康風險密切相關的習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"put on six months","meaning":"令……看起來老六個月","examples":[{"en":"Smoking put on six months for a woman.","zh":"吸煙令女性看起來老六個月。"},{"en":"To put on six months means to make someone look six months older.","zh":"令某人看起來老六個月，指令其外表年齡增加六個月。"},{"en":"Constant tiredness may put on a few months in perceived age.","zh":"長期疲倦可能令觀感年齡增加幾個月。"},{"en":"If smoking adds visible lines, it can increase perceived age slightly.","zh":"如果吸煙增加可見皺紋，它可以稍微增加觀感年齡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small increase in apparent age.","zh":"這個短語描述外表年齡的小幅增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"high BMI","meaning":"高身體質量指數","examples":[{"en":"Having a high BMI was found to make people look younger.","zh":"研究發現，高身體質量指數會令人看起來較年輕。"},{"en":"A high BMI means a higher body mass index, often linked with higher body weight for height.","zh":"高 BMI 指較高的身體質量指數，通常與相對身高較高體重有關。"},{"en":"A doctor may calculate high BMI from a patient’s weight and height.","zh":"醫生可能用病人的體重和身高計算高 BMI。"},{"en":"If a person is not too thin, their face may look fuller and less aged.","zh":"如果一個人不太瘦，面部可能看起來較飽滿、不那麼老。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a measurement, not a full health judgement by itself.","zh":"這個短語指一項量度，本身不是完整健康判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"body mass index","meaning":"身體質量指數","examples":[{"en":"BMI stands for body mass index.","zh":"BMI 代表身體質量指數。"},{"en":"Body mass index is a number calculated from a person’s weight and height.","zh":"身體質量指數是由一個人的體重和身高計算出的數字。"},{"en":"Clinics often use body mass index as a quick screening tool.","zh":"診所常用身體質量指數作快速篩查工具。"},{"en":"If BMI is very high or very low, doctors may check health risks more carefully.","zh":"如果 BMI 非常高或非常低，醫生可能更仔細檢查健康風險。"},{"en":"The phrase is usually shortened to BMI.","zh":"這個短語通常縮寫為 BMI。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take a whole year off","meaning":"令……看起來年輕整整一年","examples":[{"en":"A high BMI was found to take a whole year off perceived age.","zh":"研究發現，高 BMI 令觀感年齡年輕整整一年。"},{"en":"To take a whole year off means to make someone look one full year younger.","zh":"令某人看起來年輕整整一年，指令外表年齡完整少一年。"},{"en":"Better sleep may take a whole year off a tired face.","zh":"更好睡眠可能令疲倦面容看起來年輕整整一年。"},{"en":"If a fuller face reduces visible lines, perceived age may decrease.","zh":"如果較飽滿面容減少可見皺紋，觀感年齡可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a complete one-year reduction in apparent age.","zh":"這個短語描述外表年齡完整減少一年。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not too skinny","meaning":"不太瘦","examples":[{"en":"Professor Christensen said that people do well if they are not too skinny.","zh":"Christensen 教授說，如果人不太瘦，情況就不錯。"},{"en":"Not too skinny means not excessively thin.","zh":"不太瘦，指不過分瘦削。"},{"en":"A healthy diet should help students stay fit, not too skinny or too heavy.","zh":"健康飲食應幫助學生保持健康，不太瘦也不太重。"},{"en":"If someone is too skinny, the face may look thinner and older.","zh":"如果某人太瘦，面部可能看起來更削瘦、更老。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a moderate body shape.","zh":"這個短語描述適中的身形。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be basically doing well","meaning":"基本上做得不錯","examples":[{"en":"If you are not depressed and not a smoker, you are basically doing well.","zh":"如果你沒有抑鬱，也不是吸煙者，你基本上做得不錯。"},{"en":"To be basically doing well means to be in a generally good situation, even if not perfect.","zh":"基本上做得不錯，指整體情況良好，即使不完美。"},{"en":"A student who attends class, sleeps enough, and practises regularly is basically doing well.","zh":"一個上課、睡得足和定期練習的學生，基本上做得不錯。"},{"en":"If someone avoids major risk factors, their health habits may already be fairly good.","zh":"如果某人避開主要風險因素，其健康習慣可能已經相當好。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a simple positive overall judgement.","zh":"這個短語給出簡單正面的整體判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"one of the report’s authors","meaning":"報告作者之一","examples":[{"en":"Professor Kaare Christensen was one of the report’s authors.","zh":"Kaare Christensen 教授是報告作者之一。"},{"en":"One of the report’s authors means one of the people who helped write the report.","zh":"報告作者之一，指幫助撰寫該報告的人之一。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask one of the project’s authors to explain the group’s conclusion.","zh":"老師可能請項目作者之一解釋小組結論。"},{"en":"If someone is an author of a report, their comments carry special relevance.","zh":"如果某人是報告作者，其評論就特別相關。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a contributor to a written study.","zh":"這個短語指出書面研究的參與撰寫者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"conclude that","meaning":"得出結論指","examples":[{"en":"The report concluded that looking older can be dangerous for health.","zh":"報告得出結論指，看起來較老可能對健康有危險。"},{"en":"To conclude that means to reach a final judgement after considering evidence.","zh":"得出結論指，指考慮證據後作出最終判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher may conclude that students need more practice after reading their essays.","zh":"老師閱讀學生作文後，可能得出結論指學生需要更多練習。"},{"en":"If research shows a strong link, the authors may state a conclusion.","zh":"如果研究顯示強烈關聯，作者可能陳述結論。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the result of reasoning or research.","zh":"這個短語引出推理或研究的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be dangerous for our health","meaning":"對我們的健康有危險","examples":[{"en":"Looking older than your actual age may be dangerous for your health.","zh":"看起來比實際年齡老，可能對你的健康有危險。"},{"en":"To be dangerous for our health means to create or signal risk to the body or mind.","zh":"對我們的健康有危險，指對身體或心理造成或顯示風險。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is dangerous for health because it affects mood, memory, and immunity.","zh":"睡眠不足對健康有危險，因為它影響情緒、記憶和免疫力。"},{"en":"If looking older reflects stress or illness, it may warn of health problems.","zh":"如果看起來較老反映壓力或疾病，它可能警告健康問題。"},{"en":"The phrase connects something with health risk.","zh":"這個短語把某事與健康風險連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"actually be","meaning":"實際上是","examples":[{"en":"It may be more dangerous to look a year older than to actually be a year older.","zh":"看起來老一歲，可能比實際上老一歲更危險。"},{"en":"Actually be means truly or really be something, not just appear to be it.","zh":"實際上是，指真正是某事，而不只是看起來像。"},{"en":"A student may look confident but actually be very nervous.","zh":"學生可能看起來有信心，但實際上很緊張。"},{"en":"If appearance suggests poor health, looking older may matter more than real age alone.","zh":"如果外貌暗示健康差，看起來較老可能比真實年齡本身更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts reality with appearance.","zh":"這個短語對比現實與外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"nutrition","meaning":"營養","examples":[{"en":"Nutrition may be the biggest change we can make fairly easily.","zh":"營養可能是我們相當容易作出的最大改變。"},{"en":"Nutrition means the food and nutrients the body receives for health and energy.","zh":"營養指身體為健康和能量所獲得的食物和營養素。"},{"en":"Good nutrition includes enough protein, fruit, vegetables, water, and healthy fats.","zh":"良好營養包括足夠蛋白質、水果、蔬菜、水分和健康脂肪。"},{"en":"If nutrition is poor, skin, energy, and immunity may suffer.","zh":"如果營養差，皮膚、能量和免疫力可能受損。"},{"en":"The word focuses on how food supports the body.","zh":"這個詞強調食物如何支援身體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the biggest change we can make","meaning":"我們可以作出的最大改變","examples":[{"en":"Nutrition is possibly the biggest change we can make easily.","zh":"營養可能是我們可以相對容易作出的最大改變。"},{"en":"The biggest change we can make means the most important adjustment within our power.","zh":"我們可以作出的最大改變，指我們能力範圍內最重要的調整。"},{"en":"For a tired student, sleeping earlier may be the biggest change they can make.","zh":"對疲倦學生而言，早點睡可能是他們可以作出的最大改變。"},{"en":"If diet strongly affects skin, improving nutrition can have a large visible effect.","zh":"如果飲食強烈影響皮膚，改善營養可以有很大可見效果。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the most powerful practical action.","zh":"這個短語突出最有力的實際行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fairly easily","meaning":"相當容易地","examples":[{"en":"People can improve their nutrition fairly easily.","zh":"人們可以相當容易地改善營養。"},{"en":"Fairly easily means without too much difficulty.","zh":"相當容易地，指沒有太大困難。"},{"en":"A student can fairly easily drink more water by carrying a bottle.","zh":"學生帶水樽後，可以相當容易地多喝水。"},{"en":"If a change is fairly easy, people are more likely to try it.","zh":"如果改變相當容易，人們就更可能嘗試。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests something is practical and manageable.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事實際可行且可管理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"prematurely age us","meaning":"令我們過早衰老","examples":[{"en":"Smoking and poor diet can prematurely age us.","zh":"吸煙和不良飲食可以令我們過早衰老。"},{"en":"To prematurely age us means to make us look or become older earlier than expected.","zh":"令我們過早衰老，指令我們比預期更早看起來或變得衰老。"},{"en":"Constant stress can prematurely age a person by damaging sleep and skin.","zh":"長期壓力可以透過損害睡眠和皮膚，令一個人過早衰老。"},{"en":"If unhealthy habits continue for years, ageing signs may appear too soon.","zh":"如果不健康習慣持續多年，老化跡象可能太早出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes early ageing caused by harmful factors.","zh":"這個短語描述有害因素造成的早衰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"too much alcohol","meaning":"過量酒精","examples":[{"en":"Too much alcohol is one factor that prematurely ages us.","zh":"過量酒精是令我們過早衰老的一個因素。"},{"en":"Too much alcohol means drinking more alcohol than is healthy or safe.","zh":"過量酒精，指飲用超過健康或安全水平的酒精。"},{"en":"A person who drinks heavily every night may have poorer sleep and drier skin.","zh":"每晚大量飲酒的人可能睡眠較差、皮膚較乾。"},{"en":"If alcohol dehydrates the body, it may make the face look tired.","zh":"如果酒精令身體脫水，它可能令面容看起來疲倦。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to excessive drinking.","zh":"這個短語指過度飲酒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lack of fresh fruit and vegetables","meaning":"缺乏新鮮水果和蔬菜","examples":[{"en":"Lack of fresh fruit and vegetables can make the skin look older.","zh":"缺乏新鮮水果和蔬菜可以令皮膚看起來較老。"},{"en":"Lack of fresh fruit and vegetables means not eating enough plant foods rich in vitamins and water.","zh":"缺乏新鮮水果和蔬菜，指沒有吃足夠富含維他命和水分的植物性食物。"},{"en":"A student who eats only instant noodles may lack fresh fruit and vegetables.","zh":"只吃即食麵的學生可能缺乏新鮮水果和蔬菜。"},{"en":"If the body lacks these foods, the skin may lose freshness and moisture.","zh":"如果身體缺少這些食物，皮膚可能失去清新感和水分。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a missing part of a healthy diet.","zh":"這個短語指出健康飲食中缺失的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"insufficient protein intake","meaning":"蛋白質攝取不足","examples":[{"en":"Insufficient protein intake is linked with premature ageing.","zh":"蛋白質攝取不足與過早衰老有關。"},{"en":"Insufficient protein intake means not getting enough protein from food.","zh":"蛋白質攝取不足，指從食物中得到的蛋白質不夠。"},{"en":"Someone who skips meals may have insufficient protein intake.","zh":"經常不吃正餐的人可能蛋白質攝取不足。"},{"en":"If the body lacks protein, it may struggle to repair tissue and maintain muscle.","zh":"如果身體缺乏蛋白質，可能難以修復組織和維持肌肉。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a nutritional shortage.","zh":"這個短語描述營養不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tell a smoker","meaning":"分辨出吸煙者","examples":[{"en":"You can often tell a smoker by the lines around the mouth and eyes.","zh":"你常可以從口部和眼睛周圍皺紋分辨出吸煙者。"},{"en":"To tell a smoker means to recognise that someone smokes from signs or clues.","zh":"分辨出吸煙者，指從跡象或線索認出某人吸煙。"},{"en":"A doctor may tell a smoker by smell, coughing, or skin changes.","zh":"醫生可能從氣味、咳嗽或皮膚變化分辨出吸煙者。"},{"en":"If smoking leaves visible lines, others may identify the habit from appearance.","zh":"如果吸煙留下可見皺紋，其他人可能從外貌辨認出這習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase means detect, not speak to a smoker.","zh":"這個短語意思是辨認，而不是跟吸煙者說話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lines around the mouth and eyes","meaning":"口部和眼睛周圍的皺紋","examples":[{"en":"Smokers often have lines around the mouth and eyes.","zh":"吸煙者常有口部和眼睛周圍的皺紋。"},{"en":"Lines around the mouth and eyes are wrinkles or creases near those areas.","zh":"口部和眼睛周圍的皺紋，是那些位置附近的紋路或摺痕。"},{"en":"A person who laughs often may have smile lines around the eyes.","zh":"經常笑的人可能眼周有笑紋。"},{"en":"If smoking dries the skin, lines may become deeper or more visible.","zh":"如果吸煙令皮膚乾燥，皺紋可能變得更深或更明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visible facial ageing marks.","zh":"這個短語描述可見的面部老化痕跡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be dehydrating to the body","meaning":"令身體脫水","examples":[{"en":"Smoking is dehydrating to the body.","zh":"吸煙會令身體脫水。"},{"en":"To be dehydrating to the body means to make the body lose or lack water.","zh":"令身體脫水，指使身體流失或缺乏水分。"},{"en":"Too much coffee can be dehydrating if a person drinks little water.","zh":"如果一個人喝水很少，喝太多咖啡可能令身體脫水。"},{"en":"If the body is dehydrated, skin may look dry and dull.","zh":"如果身體缺水，皮膚可能看起來乾燥暗啞。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why water becomes important.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何水分很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"inhale cigarette smoke","meaning":"吸入香煙煙霧","examples":[{"en":"Every time you inhale cigarette smoke, you take toxins into the body.","zh":"每次你吸入香煙煙霧，就把毒素帶入體內。"},{"en":"To inhale cigarette smoke means to breathe smoke from a cigarette into the lungs.","zh":"吸入香煙煙霧，指把香煙煙霧吸進肺部。"},{"en":"People nearby may inhale cigarette smoke if someone smokes in a small room.","zh":"如果有人在小房間吸煙，旁邊的人可能吸入香煙煙霧。"},{"en":"If smoke is inhaled repeatedly, harmful substances enter the body again and again.","zh":"如果反覆吸入煙霧，有害物質就一再進入身體。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the action of breathing in cigarette smoke.","zh":"這個短語描述吸入香煙煙霧的動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take toxins into the body","meaning":"把毒素吸入體內","examples":[{"en":"Smokers take toxins into the body when they inhale cigarette smoke.","zh":"吸煙者吸入香煙煙霧時，會把毒素吸入體內。"},{"en":"To take toxins into the body means to let harmful substances enter the body.","zh":"把毒素帶入體內，指讓有害物質進入身體。"},{"en":"Eating contaminated food can take toxins into the body.","zh":"吃受污染食物可以把毒素帶入體內。"},{"en":"If toxins enter the body, organs must work to process and remove them.","zh":"如果毒素進入身體，器官必須處理並移除它們。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the harmful intake of substances.","zh":"這個短語突出有害物質的攝入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be detoxified by","meaning":"由……解毒","examples":[{"en":"Toxins have to be detoxified by the liver and kidneys.","zh":"毒素必須由肝臟和腎臟解毒。"},{"en":"To be detoxified by an organ means to be processed so harmful substances are removed or made less harmful.","zh":"由某器官解毒，指被處理以移除有害物質或減低其害處。"},{"en":"The body detoxifies many waste products through the liver and kidneys.","zh":"身體透過肝臟和腎臟為許多廢物解毒。"},{"en":"If too many toxins enter, these organs may need to work harder.","zh":"如果太多毒素進入，這些器官可能需要更辛苦工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the body’s cleaning process.","zh":"這個短語描述身體的清理過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the liver and kidneys","meaning":"肝臟和腎臟","examples":[{"en":"The liver and kidneys help the body deal with toxins.","zh":"肝臟和腎臟幫助身體處理毒素。"},{"en":"The liver and kidneys are organs that process waste and help clean the blood.","zh":"肝臟和腎臟是處理廢物並幫助清潔血液的器官。"},{"en":"Doctors may check the liver and kidneys when a patient takes strong medicine.","zh":"當病人服用強效藥物，醫生可能檢查肝臟和腎臟。"},{"en":"If these organs are overworked, the body may struggle to remove harmful substances.","zh":"如果這些器官過度工作，身體可能難以移除有害物質。"},{"en":"The phrase names two important detoxifying organs.","zh":"這個短語指出兩個重要解毒器官。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be dependent on","meaning":"依賴……","examples":[{"en":"The liver and kidneys are dependent on fresh water to carry toxins away.","zh":"肝臟和腎臟依賴清水來帶走毒素。"},{"en":"To be dependent on something means to need it in order to work properly.","zh":"依賴某物，指需要它才能正常運作。"},{"en":"A school computer system is dependent on stable internet.","zh":"學校電腦系統依賴穩定網絡。"},{"en":"If the body lacks water, toxin removal may become less efficient.","zh":"如果身體缺水，毒素清除可能變得較低效。"},{"en":"The phrase shows necessary reliance.","zh":"這個短語顯示必要依靠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"plenty of fresh water","meaning":"大量清水","examples":[{"en":"The body needs plenty of fresh water to remove toxins.","zh":"身體需要大量清水來清除毒素。"},{"en":"Plenty of fresh water means a large enough amount of clean drinking water.","zh":"大量清水，指足夠多的乾淨飲用水。"},{"en":"Students should bring plenty of fresh water on a hot sports day.","zh":"學生在炎熱運動日應帶大量清水。"},{"en":"If a person drinks too little water, the skin and organs may suffer.","zh":"如果一個人喝水太少，皮膚和器官可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses enough clean water, not sugary drinks.","zh":"這個短語強調足夠清水，而不是含糖飲品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"carry toxins away","meaning":"帶走毒素","examples":[{"en":"Fresh water helps carry toxins away.","zh":"清水有助帶走毒素。"},{"en":"To carry toxins away means to help move harmful substances out of the body.","zh":"帶走毒素，指幫助把有害物質移出身體。"},{"en":"Drinking water supports the body as it removes waste through urine and sweat.","zh":"飲水支援身體透過尿液和汗水移除廢物。"},{"en":"If toxins are carried away efficiently, the body may feel and look healthier.","zh":"如果毒素有效被帶走，身體可能感覺和看起來更健康。"},{"en":"The phrase describes removal, not storage, of harmful substances.","zh":"這個短語描述移除有害物質，而不是儲存它們。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"anywhere near enough","meaning":"遠遠不夠","examples":[{"en":"Most smokers do not drink anywhere near enough water.","zh":"大多數吸煙者喝水遠遠不夠。"},{"en":"Anywhere near enough means not even close to the amount needed.","zh":"遠遠不夠，指甚至接近所需數量也沒有。"},{"en":"A student who revises for ten minutes has not done anywhere near enough for a major exam.","zh":"只溫習十分鐘的學生，對大型考試而言遠遠不夠。"},{"en":"If smokers need more water but drink very little, the shortage may affect skin.","zh":"如果吸煙者需要更多水但喝得很少，缺水可能影響皮膚。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly emphasises insufficiency.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"quick fix","meaning":"快速改善方法","examples":[{"en":"Eating more fresh fruit and vegetables is a quick fix.","zh":"多吃新鮮水果和蔬菜是一個快速改善方法。"},{"en":"A quick fix is a simple, fast solution that improves a problem quickly.","zh":"快速改善方法，是能迅速改善問題的簡單解決方法。"},{"en":"Drinking water may be a quick fix for mild dehydration.","zh":"喝水可能是輕微脫水的快速改善方法。"},{"en":"If diet lacks freshness, adding fruit and vegetables can improve it immediately.","zh":"如果飲食缺乏新鮮感，加入水果和蔬菜可立即改善。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests an easy improvement, not a complete cure for everything.","zh":"這個短語暗示容易改善，而不是治好一切的完整方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fresh fruit and vegetables","meaning":"新鮮水果和蔬菜","examples":[{"en":"Fresh fruit and vegetables can help the skin look healthier.","zh":"新鮮水果和蔬菜可以幫助皮膚看起來更健康。"},{"en":"Fresh fruit and vegetables are plant foods that are not stale, heavily processed, or preserved for long periods.","zh":"新鮮水果和蔬菜，是沒有變壞、沒有高度加工或長期保存的植物性食物。"},{"en":"Apples, oranges, carrots, and leafy greens are fresh fruit and vegetables.","zh":"蘋果、橙、胡蘿蔔和綠葉菜都是新鮮水果和蔬菜。"},{"en":"If people eat more fresh produce, they may get more vitamins, minerals, and water.","zh":"如果人們吃更多新鮮農產品，可能獲得更多維他命、礦物質和水分。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to basic healthy foods.","zh":"這個短語指基本健康食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fresh fruit and veg","meaning":"新鮮水果和蔬菜","examples":[{"en":"You can often see when someone does not eat enough fresh fruit and veg.","zh":"你常可以看出某人沒有吃足夠新鮮水果和蔬菜。"},{"en":"Fresh fruit and veg is an informal way to say fresh fruit and vegetables.","zh":"“Fresh fruit and veg” 是 fresh fruit and vegetables 的非正式說法。"},{"en":"A lunchbox with an apple and cucumber has some fresh fruit and veg.","zh":"有蘋果和青瓜的午餐盒，含有一些新鮮水果和蔬菜。"},{"en":"If someone rarely eats fresh fruit and veg, their diet may lack key nutrients.","zh":"如果某人很少吃新鮮水果和蔬菜，其飲食可能缺乏關鍵營養。"},{"en":"The phrase is casual and common in everyday speech.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常見於日常說話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in a minute","meaning":"很快；即刻","examples":[{"en":"You can see the difference in a minute.","zh":"你很快就能看出分別。"},{"en":"In a minute can mean very quickly or almost immediately.","zh":"“In a minute” 可以指很快或幾乎立即。"},{"en":"If a student drinks water after exercise, they may feel better in a minute.","zh":"如果學生運動後喝水，可能很快感覺好些。"},{"en":"If skin lacks freshness, the effect of poor diet may be visible quickly.","zh":"如果皮膚缺乏清新感，不良飲食的效果可能很快可見。"},{"en":"The phrase here means quickly, not exactly sixty seconds.","zh":"這個短語在此指很快，而不是準確六十秒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lack freshness and translucency","meaning":"缺乏清新感和通透感","examples":[{"en":"The skin lacks freshness and translucency when the diet is poor.","zh":"當飲食差，皮膚會缺乏清新感和通透感。"},{"en":"To lack freshness and translucency means to look dull, tired, and not naturally clear.","zh":"缺乏清新感和通透感，指看起來暗淡、疲倦且不自然清透。"},{"en":"After several nights of poor sleep, a student’s face may lack freshness.","zh":"連續幾晚睡不好後，學生面容可能缺乏清新感。"},{"en":"If the body lacks nutrients and water, the skin may lose its healthy glow.","zh":"如果身體缺乏營養和水分，皮膚可能失去健康光澤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes skin that looks less healthy and lively.","zh":"這個短語描述看起來較不健康和沒有生氣的皮膚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"translucency","meaning":"通透感","examples":[{"en":"Healthy skin often has freshness and translucency.","zh":"健康皮膚常有清新感和通透感。"},{"en":"Translucency means a clear, light quality that lets skin look naturally bright.","zh":"通透感指清透明亮、令皮膚看起來自然有光的特質。"},{"en":"Good hydration may give the face more translucency.","zh":"良好補水可能令面部更有通透感。"},{"en":"If skin becomes dry and dull, it loses translucency.","zh":"如果皮膚變乾和暗啞，就會失去通透感。"},{"en":"The word describes a soft clear glow, not literal transparency.","zh":"這個詞描述柔和清亮的光澤，而不是字面上的透明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the last organ to benefit from","meaning":"最後才受惠的器官","examples":[{"en":"The skin is the last organ to benefit from the nutrients you eat.","zh":"皮膚是最後才從你吃下的營養素中受惠的器官。"},{"en":"The last organ to benefit from something is the part that receives help only after other parts are supplied first.","zh":"最後才受惠的器官，指其他部分先獲供應後才得到幫助的部分。"},{"en":"In a family budget, entertainment may be the last thing to benefit after rent and food are paid.","zh":"在家庭預算中，娛樂可能在租金和食物付款後才最後受惠。"},{"en":"If vital organs get nutrients first, skin may show shortage early.","zh":"如果重要器官先獲得營養，皮膚可能較早顯示不足。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why poor diet can appear on the skin.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何不良飲食會反映在皮膚上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"nutrients","meaning":"營養素","examples":[{"en":"The skin needs sufficient nutrients to stay healthy.","zh":"皮膚需要足夠營養素才能保持健康。"},{"en":"Nutrients are useful substances in food that the body needs to grow, repair, and function.","zh":"營養素是食物中身體用來生長、修復和運作的有用物質。"},{"en":"Protein, vitamins, minerals, and healthy fats are nutrients.","zh":"蛋白質、維他命、礦物質和健康脂肪都是營養素。"},{"en":"If a diet lacks nutrients, energy, skin, and immunity may suffer.","zh":"如果飲食缺乏營養素，能量、皮膚和免疫力可能受損。"},{"en":"The word refers to the helpful parts of food.","zh":"這個詞指食物中有益的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the likes of","meaning":"例如……之類","examples":[{"en":"The likes of the brain, heart, and lungs get nutrients first.","zh":"例如大腦、心臟和肺部之類的器官會優先獲得營養素。"},{"en":"The likes of means examples such as these.","zh":"“The likes of” 指例如這些例子。"},{"en":"A school needs basic facilities, the likes of classrooms, toilets, and internet access.","zh":"學校需要基本設施，例如課室、洗手間和網絡之類。"},{"en":"If important organs like the brain and heart are supplied first, the skin may receive nutrients later.","zh":"如果像大腦和心臟這些重要器官先獲供應，皮膚可能較遲才得到營養。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces examples without listing everything.","zh":"這個短語引入例子，而不列出所有東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get the first share","meaning":"優先獲得","examples":[{"en":"The brain, heart, and lungs get the first share of nutrients.","zh":"大腦、心臟和肺部會優先獲得營養素。"},{"en":"To get the first share means to receive something before others do.","zh":"優先獲得，指比其他人或部位先得到某物。"},{"en":"In an emergency, hospitals may get the first share of medical supplies.","zh":"在緊急情況下，醫院可能優先獲得醫療物資。"},{"en":"If vital organs get nutrients first, skin may not receive enough when diet is poor.","zh":"如果重要器官優先獲得營養，而飲食又差，皮膚可能得不到足夠營養。"},{"en":"The phrase shows priority in distribution.","zh":"這個短語顯示分配中的優先次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be lacking in","meaning":"缺乏……","examples":[{"en":"If someone’s diet is lacking in fruit and veg, the skin may become dehydrated.","zh":"如果某人的飲食缺乏水果和蔬菜，皮膚可能變得缺水。"},{"en":"To be lacking in something means not to have enough of it.","zh":"缺乏某物，指沒有足夠該物。"},{"en":"A student’s essay may be lacking in examples if it only gives opinions.","zh":"如果學生作文只給意見，可能缺乏例子。"},{"en":"If a diet lacks fresh food, the body may miss water, vitamins, and fibre.","zh":"如果飲食缺乏新鮮食物，身體可能缺少水分、維他命和纖維。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what is missing or insufficient.","zh":"這個短語指出缺少或不足的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"become dehydrated","meaning":"變得缺水","examples":[{"en":"The skin can become dehydrated when the diet lacks fresh food.","zh":"當飲食缺乏新鮮食物，皮膚可以變得缺水。"},{"en":"To become dehydrated means to lose too much water or lack enough water.","zh":"變得缺水，指失去太多水分或沒有足夠水分。"},{"en":"A runner may become dehydrated after exercising in hot weather.","zh":"跑步者在炎熱天氣運動後可能變得缺水。"},{"en":"If skin becomes dehydrated, it may look dry, tight, and dull.","zh":"如果皮膚變得缺水，可能看起來乾、繃緊和暗啞。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a water shortage in the body or skin.","zh":"這個短語描述身體或皮膚水分不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sufficient nutrients","meaning":"足夠營養素","examples":[{"en":"Sufficient nutrients are needed for healthy-looking skin.","zh":"健康外觀的皮膚需要足夠營養素。"},{"en":"Sufficient nutrients means enough useful food substances for the body’s needs.","zh":"足夠營養素，指足以滿足身體需要的有用食物物質。"},{"en":"Children need sufficient nutrients to grow, concentrate, and fight illness.","zh":"孩子需要足夠營養素來成長、集中和抵抗疾病。"},{"en":"If the skin does not receive enough nutrients, it may look tired or dry.","zh":"如果皮膚沒有獲得足夠營養素，可能看起來疲倦或乾燥。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses adequacy, not excess.","zh":"這個短語強調足夠，而不是過量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be delivered","meaning":"被輸送","examples":[{"en":"Nutrients must be delivered to the skin.","zh":"營養素必須被輸送到皮膚。"},{"en":"To be delivered to a place means to be carried or supplied there.","zh":"被輸送到某處，指被運送或供應到那裡。"},{"en":"Food parcels may be delivered to elderly residents during bad weather.","zh":"惡劣天氣期間，食物包可能被送到長者居民家中。"},{"en":"If nutrients are delivered poorly, the skin may not benefit from what you eat.","zh":"如果營養素輸送不佳，皮膚可能無法從你吃的食物中受惠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement or supply to a destination.","zh":"這個短語描述移動或供應到目的地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"from an anti-ageing point of view","meaning":"從抗衰老角度來看","examples":[{"en":"From an anti-ageing point of view, raw food is important.","zh":"從抗衰老角度來看，生食很重要。"},{"en":"From an anti-ageing point of view means when considering how to slow visible ageing.","zh":"從抗衰老角度來看，指在考慮如何減慢可見老化時。"},{"en":"From a student’s point of view, sleep may be as important as revision.","zh":"從學生角度來看，睡眠可能與溫習同樣重要。"},{"en":"If raw food protects vitamins, it may matter for keeping skin youthful.","zh":"如果生食保護維他命，它可能對保持皮膚年輕很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase frames the discussion through one specific concern.","zh":"這個短語透過一個特定關注點來框定討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"anti-ageing","meaning":"抗衰老","examples":[{"en":"Anti-ageing advice often focuses on diet and skin care.","zh":"抗衰老建議常集中於飲食和皮膚護理。"},{"en":"Anti-ageing means intended to slow, reduce, or hide the signs of ageing.","zh":"抗衰老指旨在減慢、減少或掩蓋老化跡象。"},{"en":"Sunscreen is often part of an anti-ageing routine.","zh":"防曬霜常是抗衰老護理的一部分。"},{"en":"If a product claims anti-ageing effects, people expect fewer wrinkles or younger-looking skin.","zh":"如果產品聲稱有抗衰老效果，人們會期望皺紋較少或皮膚看起來較年輕。"},{"en":"The word refers to appearance and health strategies against ageing signs.","zh":"這個詞指對抗老化跡象的外貌和健康策略。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"live, fresh food","meaning":"新鮮、有生命力的食物","examples":[{"en":"Live, fresh food is important for healthy skin.","zh":"新鮮、有生命力的食物對健康皮膚很重要。"},{"en":"Live, fresh food means natural, fresh foods that still contain valuable nutrients and have not been heavily processed.","zh":"新鮮、有生命力的食物，指仍含有寶貴營養、沒有高度加工的天然新鮮食物。"},{"en":"A salad with fresh vegetables is closer to live, fresh food than a packet of crisps.","zh":"有新鮮蔬菜的沙律，比一包薯片更接近新鮮有生命力的食物。"},{"en":"If food is fresh and nutrient-rich, it may support clearer skin.","zh":"如果食物新鮮又富營養，可能支援更清透皮膚。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts fresh natural food with processed food.","zh":"這個短語把新鮮天然食物與加工食物作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"raw food","meaning":"生食；未經烹調的食物","examples":[{"en":"Raw food is vital from an anti-ageing point of view.","zh":"從抗衰老角度來看，生食至關重要。"},{"en":"Raw food is food that has not been cooked.","zh":"生食是沒有經過烹調的食物。"},{"en":"Carrot sticks, fresh fruit, and salad leaves are examples of raw food.","zh":"胡蘿蔔條、新鮮水果和沙律葉都是生食例子。"},{"en":"If cooking destroys some nutrients, raw food may help preserve them.","zh":"如果烹調破壞部分營養素，生食可能有助保存它們。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to uncooked food, especially plant foods.","zh":"這個短語指未經烹調的食物，尤其是植物性食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be vital","meaning":"至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Raw food is vital for maintaining a youthful appearance.","zh":"生食對維持年輕外貌至關重要。"},{"en":"To be vital means to be extremely important or necessary.","zh":"至關重要，指極其重要或必要。"},{"en":"Sleep is vital for students because memory improves during rest.","zh":"睡眠對學生至關重要，因為記憶會在休息期間改善。"},{"en":"If nutrients are vital for skin repair, a poor diet can affect appearance.","zh":"如果營養素對皮膚修復至關重要，不良飲食就會影響外貌。"},{"en":"The phrase shows something is not optional.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事不是可有可無。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"steaming","meaning":"蒸煮","examples":[{"en":"Steaming can retain some vitamins and minerals.","zh":"蒸煮可以保留一些維他命和礦物質。"},{"en":"Steaming is cooking food with hot steam rather than boiling it in water.","zh":"蒸煮是用熱蒸汽煮食物，而不是把食物放進水中煮。"},{"en":"A family may steam vegetables to keep them soft but not oily.","zh":"家庭可能蒸蔬菜，使它們柔軟但不油膩。"},{"en":"If vegetables are steamed gently, fewer nutrients may be lost than in long boiling.","zh":"如果蔬菜溫和蒸煮，可能比長時間水煮流失較少營養。"},{"en":"The word names a cooking method often considered healthy.","zh":"這個詞指出一種常被視為健康的烹調方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"retain vitamins and minerals","meaning":"保留維他命和礦物質","examples":[{"en":"Steaming helps retain vitamins and minerals.","zh":"蒸煮有助保留維他命和礦物質。"},{"en":"To retain vitamins and minerals means to keep these nutrients from being lost.","zh":"保留維他命和礦物質，指防止這些營養素流失。"},{"en":"Keeping fruit fresh helps retain vitamins better than leaving it cut for hours.","zh":"保持水果新鮮，比切開數小時更能保留維他命。"},{"en":"If cooking is too long or too harsh, food may lose more nutrients.","zh":"如果烹調時間太長或太猛烈，食物可能流失更多營養。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how food can stay nutritious.","zh":"這個短語解釋食物如何保持營養。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"vitamins and minerals","meaning":"維他命和礦物質","examples":[{"en":"Fresh food provides vitamins and minerals.","zh":"新鮮食物提供維他命和礦物質。"},{"en":"Vitamins and minerals are nutrients the body needs in small amounts to stay healthy.","zh":"維他命和礦物質是身體需要少量攝取以保持健康的營養素。"},{"en":"Oranges provide vitamin C, while leafy vegetables provide minerals such as iron.","zh":"橙提供維他命 C，而綠葉菜提供鐵等礦物質。"},{"en":"If a diet lacks vitamins and minerals, energy and skin health may suffer.","zh":"如果飲食缺乏維他命和礦物質，能量和皮膚健康可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to essential micronutrients.","zh":"這個短語指必需微量營養素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tend to miss out on","meaning":"往往忽略；未能攝取","examples":[{"en":"Many people tend to miss out on essential fatty acids.","zh":"許多人往往未能攝取必需脂肪酸。"},{"en":"To tend to miss out on something means to often fail to get or include it.","zh":"往往未能獲得某物，指經常沒有得到或包括它。"},{"en":"Busy students may miss out on breakfast when they wake up late.","zh":"忙碌學生起床太晚時，可能錯過早餐。"},{"en":"If people avoid all fats, they may fail to get healthy fats too.","zh":"如果人們避免所有脂肪，也可能未能攝取健康脂肪。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common pattern of missing something useful.","zh":"這個短語描述經常錯過有用事物的模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"diet-obsessed culture","meaning":"過分着重節食的文化","examples":[{"en":"People may avoid fats in a diet-obsessed culture.","zh":"在過分着重節食的文化中，人們可能避免脂肪。"},{"en":"A diet-obsessed culture is a society that focuses too much on dieting and losing weight.","zh":"過分着重節食的文化，是過度關注節食和減重的社會。"},{"en":"In a diet-obsessed culture, teenagers may fear normal foods like rice or oil.","zh":"在過分着重節食的文化中，青少年可能害怕米飯或油等正常食物。"},{"en":"If people think all fat is bad, they may miss essential fatty acids.","zh":"如果人們認為所有脂肪都是壞的，就可能錯過必需脂肪酸。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises unhealthy social pressure around dieting.","zh":"這個短語批評圍繞節食的不健康社會壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"adequate intake of","meaning":"足夠攝取……","examples":[{"en":"Adequate intake of essential fatty acids is important.","zh":"足夠攝取必需脂肪酸很重要。"},{"en":"Adequate intake of something means getting enough of it for health or normal function.","zh":"足夠攝取某物，指為健康或正常功能獲得足夠該物。"},{"en":"Children need adequate intake of calcium for strong bones.","zh":"兒童需要足夠攝取鈣質，以建立強健骨骼。"},{"en":"If intake is inadequate, the body may lack materials it cannot make itself.","zh":"如果攝取不足，身體可能缺少自己不能製造的材料。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses getting enough, not too much.","zh":"這個短語強調足夠，而不是過量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"essential fatty acids","meaning":"必需脂肪酸","examples":[{"en":"Essential fatty acids help give the skin a youthful feel.","zh":"必需脂肪酸有助令皮膚有年輕感。"},{"en":"Essential fatty acids are healthy fats the body needs but cannot make enough of by itself.","zh":"必需脂肪酸是身體需要但不能自行製造足夠的健康脂肪。"},{"en":"Oily fish, nuts, and seeds can provide essential fatty acids.","zh":"油性魚類、果仁和種子可以提供必需脂肪酸。"},{"en":"If people avoid all fats, skin and cells may not get enough of these important nutrients.","zh":"如果人們避免所有脂肪，皮膚和細胞可能得不到足夠這些重要營養素。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to necessary healthy fats.","zh":"這個短語指必要的健康脂肪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"oily fish, nuts, and seeds","meaning":"油性魚類、果仁和種子","examples":[{"en":"Essential fatty acids can come from oily fish, nuts, and seeds.","zh":"必需脂肪酸可以來自油性魚類、果仁和種子。"},{"en":"Oily fish, nuts, and seeds are foods rich in healthy fats.","zh":"油性魚類、果仁和種子是富含健康脂肪的食物。"},{"en":"Salmon, walnuts, almonds, and sunflower seeds are common examples.","zh":"三文魚、合桃、杏仁和葵花籽都是常見例子。"},{"en":"If people add these foods to meals, they may improve fatty-acid intake.","zh":"如果人們把這些食物加入餐單，可能改善脂肪酸攝取。"},{"en":"The phrase lists practical food sources.","zh":"這個短語列出實用食物來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be vital for","meaning":"對……至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Essential fatty acids are vital for prolonging life expectancy.","zh":"必需脂肪酸對延長預期壽命至關重要。"},{"en":"To be vital for something means to be extremely important for achieving or supporting it.","zh":"對某事至關重要，指對達成或支援該事極其重要。"},{"en":"Clean water is vital for public health.","zh":"清潔食水對公共健康至關重要。"},{"en":"If a nutrient is vital for cells, lacking it can affect the whole body.","zh":"如果某營養素對細胞至關重要，缺乏它可以影響全身。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something is necessary, not just helpful.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事是必要的，而不只是有幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"prolonging life expectancy","meaning":"延長預期壽命","examples":[{"en":"Essential fatty acids are vital for prolonging life expectancy.","zh":"必需脂肪酸對延長預期壽命至關重要。"},{"en":"Prolonging life expectancy means helping people live longer on average.","zh":"延長預期壽命，指幫助人們平均活得更久。"},{"en":"Better healthcare and cleaner water can help prolong life expectancy.","zh":"更好醫療和更清潔食水可以幫助延長預期壽命。"},{"en":"If nutrition protects the heart and cells, it may support longer life.","zh":"如果營養保護心臟和細胞，就可能支援更長壽命。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to increasing expected length of life.","zh":"這個短語指增加預期生命長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"every cell in the body","meaning":"身體每個細胞","examples":[{"en":"Every cell in the body has a protective bilayer.","zh":"身體每個細胞都有保護性雙分子層。"},{"en":"Every cell in the body means all the tiny living units that make up the body.","zh":"身體每個細胞，指構成身體的所有微小生命單位。"},{"en":"Skin, muscle, and blood are all made from cells.","zh":"皮膚、肌肉和血液都由細胞組成。"},{"en":"If cells need healthy fats, diet can affect the body at a very basic level.","zh":"如果細胞需要健康脂肪，飲食就能在非常基本的層面影響身體。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the effect is body-wide.","zh":"這個短語強調影響遍及全身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"phospholipid bilayer","meaning":"磷脂雙分子層","examples":[{"en":"Every cell in the body has a phospholipid bilayer.","zh":"身體每個細胞都有磷脂雙分子層。"},{"en":"A phospholipid bilayer is a two-layer membrane made of fat-like molecules around a cell.","zh":"磷脂雙分子層是圍繞細胞、由類脂肪分子組成的雙層膜。"},{"en":"Biology students learn that the phospholipid bilayer helps control what enters and leaves a cell.","zh":"生物學生學到磷脂雙分子層幫助控制物質進出細胞。"},{"en":"If cell membranes need healthy fats, fatty acids become important to health.","zh":"如果細胞膜需要健康脂肪，脂肪酸就對健康重要。"},{"en":"The phrase names a basic structure of cell membranes.","zh":"這個短語指出細胞膜的基本結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"give the skin a youthful feel","meaning":"令皮膚有年輕感","examples":[{"en":"Essential fatty acids give the skin a youthful feel.","zh":"必需脂肪酸令皮膚有年輕感。"},{"en":"To give the skin a youthful feel means to make skin feel soft, firm, and healthy.","zh":"令皮膚有年輕感，指令皮膚感覺柔軟、緊緻和健康。"},{"en":"Good hydration can give the skin a fresher feel after illness.","zh":"生病後良好補水可以令皮膚感覺較清新。"},{"en":"If healthy fats support cell membranes, skin may feel more elastic.","zh":"如果健康脂肪支援細胞膜，皮膚可能感覺更有彈性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes touch and appearance together.","zh":"這個短語同時描述觸感和外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dewy","meaning":"水潤的","examples":[{"en":"Healthy skin may have a dewy appearance.","zh":"健康皮膚可能有水潤外觀。"},{"en":"Dewy skin looks fresh, moist, and softly glowing.","zh":"水潤的皮膚看起來清新、濕潤並有柔和光澤。"},{"en":"After applying moisturiser, dry skin may look more dewy.","zh":"塗潤膚霜後，乾燥皮膚可能看起來更水潤。"},{"en":"If skin lacks water, it usually looks dull rather than dewy.","zh":"如果皮膚缺水，通常看起來暗啞而不是水潤。"},{"en":"The word describes a fresh, hydrated look.","zh":"這個詞描述清新、有水分的外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"bouncy","meaning":"有彈性的","examples":[{"en":"Essential fatty acids can give the skin a bouncy feel.","zh":"必需脂肪酸可以令皮膚有彈性感。"},{"en":"Bouncy skin feels firm, elastic, and able to spring back.","zh":"有彈性的皮膚感覺緊緻、有彈力並能回彈。"},{"en":"A healthy child’s cheeks may feel bouncy and soft.","zh":"健康孩子的臉頰可能感覺柔軟又有彈性。"},{"en":"If skin loses elasticity, it may feel less bouncy with age.","zh":"如果皮膚失去彈性，隨着年齡增長可能變得沒那麼有彈性。"},{"en":"The word describes youthful elasticity.","zh":"這個詞描述年輕的彈力感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"youthful feel","meaning":"年輕感","examples":[{"en":"Good nutrition can give the skin a youthful feel.","zh":"良好營養可以令皮膚有年輕感。"},{"en":"A youthful feel means a quality that makes skin seem young, fresh, and elastic.","zh":"年輕感，指令皮膚顯得年輕、清新和有彈性的特質。"},{"en":"Enough sleep may give the face a more youthful feel before an important meeting.","zh":"重要會議前，足夠睡眠可能令面部更有年輕感。"},{"en":"If skin becomes dry and flat, it loses some youthful feel.","zh":"如果皮膚變乾和扁塌，就會失去部分年輕感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the impression of youth in texture and appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述質感和外觀上的青春印象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"one of the worst things you can do","meaning":"你可以做的最壞事情之一","examples":[{"en":"One of the worst things you can do is go on a low-fat diet.","zh":"你可以做的最壞事情之一就是採用低脂飲食。"},{"en":"One of the worst things you can do means one of the most harmful choices available.","zh":"你可以做的最壞事情之一，指可選擇行為中最有害的一種。"},{"en":"Before an exam, one of the worst things you can do is stay awake all night.","zh":"考試前，你可以做的最壞事情之一就是整晚不睡。"},{"en":"If healthy fats are necessary, cutting them too much may damage skin and health.","zh":"如果健康脂肪是必要的，過度削減它們可能損害皮膚和健康。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly warns against an action.","zh":"這個短語強烈警告不要做某行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in terms of","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"In terms of looking old, a low-fat diet can be harmful.","zh":"就看起來老而言，低脂飲食可能有害。"},{"en":"In terms of means when considering a particular aspect or measure.","zh":"就某方面而言，指在考慮某特定方面或標準時。"},{"en":"In terms of cost, taking the bus is cheaper than taking a taxi.","zh":"就成本而言，乘巴士比乘的士便宜。"},{"en":"If we judge only appearance, a low-fat diet may not be helpful.","zh":"如果只以外貌判斷，低脂飲食可能沒有幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase limits the discussion to one angle.","zh":"這個短語把討論限制在一個角度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"go on a low-fat diet","meaning":"採用低脂飲食","examples":[{"en":"Going on a low-fat diet may make people look older.","zh":"採用低脂飲食可能令人看起來較老。"},{"en":"To go on a low-fat diet means to follow an eating plan that greatly reduces fat.","zh":"採用低脂飲食，指遵循大幅減少脂肪的飲食計劃。"},{"en":"A person may go on a low-fat diet because they think all fat is unhealthy.","zh":"一個人可能因認為所有脂肪都不健康而採用低脂飲食。"},{"en":"If healthy fats are removed, skin may lose softness and elasticity.","zh":"如果健康脂肪被移除，皮膚可能失去柔軟和彈性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes starting a diet that restricts fat.","zh":"這個短語描述開始限制脂肪的飲食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stress","meaning":"壓力","examples":[{"en":"Stress is another big factor in adding years to appearance.","zh":"壓力是另一個令外貌變老的重要因素。"},{"en":"Stress is pressure or worry that affects the mind and body.","zh":"壓力是影響心理和身體的壓迫感或憂慮。"},{"en":"Students may feel stress before public exams or presentations.","zh":"學生在公開考試或匯報前可能感到壓力。"},{"en":"If stress continues for months, sleep, posture, and facial expression may suffer.","zh":"如果壓力持續數月，睡眠、姿勢和面部表情可能受影響。"},{"en":"The word can refer to both mental pressure and physical effects.","zh":"這個詞可以指心理壓力，也可以指身體影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"another big one for","meaning":"另一個導致……的重要因素","examples":[{"en":"Stress is another big one for adding years.","zh":"壓力是另一個導致外貌變老的重要因素。"},{"en":"Another big one for something means another major factor causing that result.","zh":"另一個導致某結果的重要因素，指造成該結果的另一主要因素。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep is another big one for poor concentration.","zh":"睡眠不足是另一個導致專注力差的重要因素。"},{"en":"If several habits age the face, stress may be one of the most important.","zh":"如果幾種習慣令面容變老，壓力可能是其中最重要之一。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and points to a major cause.","zh":"這個短語較口語，指出主要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"adding years","meaning":"令外貌變老","examples":[{"en":"Stress is known for adding years to a person’s appearance.","zh":"壓力以令人的外貌變老而聞名。"},{"en":"Adding years means making someone look older than their actual age.","zh":"令外貌變老，指令人看起來比實際年齡老。"},{"en":"Dark circles can add years to a tired student’s face.","zh":"黑眼圈可以令疲倦學生的面容顯老。"},{"en":"If worry creates tension and poor sleep, it may visually age a person.","zh":"如果憂慮造成繃緊和睡眠差，可能令人在視覺上變老。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an increase in apparent age.","zh":"這個短語描述外表年齡增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"adrenal and thyroid glands","meaning":"腎上腺和甲狀腺","examples":[{"en":"Stress can affect the adrenal and thyroid glands.","zh":"壓力可以影響腎上腺和甲狀腺。"},{"en":"The adrenal and thyroid glands are organs that produce hormones affecting energy, stress, and metabolism.","zh":"腎上腺和甲狀腺是產生荷爾蒙、影響能量、壓力和新陳代謝的器官。"},{"en":"Doctors may check these glands when a patient feels constantly tired.","zh":"當病人長期疲倦，醫生可能檢查這些腺體。"},{"en":"If stress affects hormone systems, the body may show visible signs of strain.","zh":"如果壓力影響荷爾蒙系統，身體可能顯示可見緊張跡象。"},{"en":"The phrase names two hormone-related body parts.","zh":"這個短語指出兩個與荷爾蒙相關的身體部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take a hammering","meaning":"受到嚴重打擊","examples":[{"en":"The adrenal and thyroid glands take a hammering when we are stressed.","zh":"當我們受壓時，腎上腺和甲狀腺會受到嚴重打擊。"},{"en":"To take a hammering means to suffer a lot of pressure, damage, or strain.","zh":"受到嚴重打擊，指承受大量壓力、損害或負擔。"},{"en":"A student’s concentration may take a hammering after several nights without sleep.","zh":"幾晚不睡後，學生的專注力可能受到嚴重打擊。"},{"en":"If stress keeps attacking the body, important systems may become worn down.","zh":"如果壓力持續攻擊身體，重要系統可能被耗損。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and suggests serious strain.","zh":"這個短語較口語，暗示嚴重負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"when we are stressed","meaning":"當我們受壓時","examples":[{"en":"The body needs support when we are stressed.","zh":"當我們受壓時，身體需要支援。"},{"en":"When we are stressed means during periods of mental or physical pressure.","zh":"當我們受壓時，指處於心理或身體壓力期間。"},{"en":"When we are stressed, we may sleep badly and eat less carefully.","zh":"當我們受壓時，可能睡得差，飲食也較不小心。"},{"en":"If stress continues, the body may need more rest and nutrients.","zh":"如果壓力持續，身體可能需要更多休息和營養。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a condition that changes our needs.","zh":"這個短語描述一種會改變我們需要的狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"vitamin C and magnesium","meaning":"維他命 C 和鎂","examples":[{"en":"Vitamin C and magnesium can support the adrenal glands.","zh":"維他命 C 和鎂可以支援腎上腺。"},{"en":"Vitamin C and magnesium are nutrients that help different body functions.","zh":"維他命 C 和鎂是幫助不同身體功能的營養素。"},{"en":"Fruit can provide vitamin C, while nuts and leafy vegetables can provide magnesium.","zh":"水果可以提供維他命 C，而果仁和綠葉菜可以提供鎂。"},{"en":"If stress affects the body, these nutrients may help support normal function.","zh":"如果壓力影響身體，這些營養素可能幫助支援正常功能。"},{"en":"The phrase names two nutrients often discussed in health advice.","zh":"這個短語指出健康建議中常討論的兩種營養素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"support the thyroid","meaning":"支持甲狀腺功能","examples":[{"en":"Iodine, selenium, zinc, and B vitamins support the thyroid.","zh":"碘、硒、鋅和 B 族維他命支持甲狀腺功能。"},{"en":"To support the thyroid means to help this gland work normally.","zh":"支持甲狀腺功能，指幫助這個腺體正常運作。"},{"en":"A doctor may check thyroid function when someone feels unusually tired or cold.","zh":"當某人異常疲倦或怕冷，醫生可能檢查甲狀腺功能。"},{"en":"If the thyroid is not supported, energy and metabolism may be affected.","zh":"如果甲狀腺得不到支援，能量和新陳代謝可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase links nutrients with gland function.","zh":"這個短語把營養素與腺體功能連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"iodine","meaning":"碘","examples":[{"en":"Iodine is one nutrient that supports the thyroid.","zh":"碘是支持甲狀腺功能的一種營養素。"},{"en":"Iodine is a mineral the body needs for normal thyroid hormone production.","zh":"碘是身體製造正常甲狀腺荷爾蒙所需的礦物質。"},{"en":"Iodised salt is one common source of iodine.","zh":"加碘鹽是碘的一種常見來源。"},{"en":"If the body lacks iodine, thyroid function may be affected.","zh":"如果身體缺碘，甲狀腺功能可能受影響。"},{"en":"The word names a specific mineral nutrient.","zh":"這個詞指出一種特定礦物營養素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"selenium","meaning":"硒","examples":[{"en":"Selenium helps support the thyroid.","zh":"硒有助支持甲狀腺功能。"},{"en":"Selenium is a trace mineral needed in small amounts for body function.","zh":"硒是一種身體功能所需、只需少量的微量礦物質。"},{"en":"Brazil nuts and some seafood can contain selenium.","zh":"巴西果仁和一些海鮮可能含有硒。"},{"en":"If someone lacks selenium, thyroid-related processes may work less well.","zh":"如果某人缺乏硒，與甲狀腺相關的過程可能運作較差。"},{"en":"The word refers to a small but important nutrient.","zh":"這個詞指少量但重要的營養素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"zinc","meaning":"鋅","examples":[{"en":"Zinc is listed as a nutrient that supports the thyroid.","zh":"鋅被列為支持甲狀腺功能的營養素。"},{"en":"Zinc is a mineral involved in immunity, healing, and normal body function.","zh":"鋅是一種參與免疫、癒合和正常身體功能的礦物質。"},{"en":"Meat, seafood, beans, and nuts can provide zinc.","zh":"肉類、海鮮、豆類和果仁可以提供鋅。"},{"en":"If zinc intake is too low, the body may repair itself less effectively.","zh":"如果鋅攝取太低，身體自我修復可能較低效。"},{"en":"The word names an important mineral nutrient.","zh":"這個詞指出一種重要礦物營養素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"B vitamins","meaning":"B 族維他命","examples":[{"en":"B vitamins help support the thyroid.","zh":"B 族維他命有助支持甲狀腺功能。"},{"en":"B vitamins are a group of vitamins that help the body use energy from food.","zh":"B 族維他命是一組幫助身體使用食物能量的維他命。"},{"en":"Whole grains, eggs, meat, and beans can provide B vitamins.","zh":"全穀物、雞蛋、肉類和豆類可以提供 B 族維他命。"},{"en":"If someone lacks B vitamins, they may feel tired or low in energy.","zh":"如果某人缺乏 B 族維他命，可能感到疲倦或能量低。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to several related vitamins, not one single vitamin.","zh":"這個短語指幾種相關維他命，而不是單一維他命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"come to think of something as","meaning":"逐漸把某事視為……","examples":[{"en":"Many people have come to think of exercise as a slimming pursuit.","zh":"許多人逐漸把運動視為瘦身活動。"},{"en":"To come to think of something as something means to gradually start seeing it in that way.","zh":"逐漸把某事視為某物，指慢慢開始用那種方式看待它。"},{"en":"Some students come to think of English as only an exam subject.","zh":"一些學生逐漸把英語只視為考試科目。"},{"en":"If people see exercise only as weight loss, they may miss its anti-ageing benefits.","zh":"如果人們只把運動視為減重，可能忽略其抗衰老好處。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a developed way of thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步形成的思考方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pure slimming pursuit","meaning":"純粹瘦身活動","examples":[{"en":"Exercise should not be seen only as a pure slimming pursuit.","zh":"運動不應只被視為純粹瘦身活動。"},{"en":"A pure slimming pursuit is an activity done only to lose weight or become thinner.","zh":"純粹瘦身活動，是只為減重或變瘦而做的活動。"},{"en":"Some people go to the gym as a pure slimming pursuit and ignore strength or health.","zh":"有些人把去健身室當成純粹瘦身活動，忽略力量或健康。"},{"en":"If exercise builds muscle and supports ageing well, it is more than slimming.","zh":"如果運動建立肌肉並支持健康老化，它就不只是瘦身。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises a narrow view of exercise.","zh":"這個短語批評對運動的狹窄看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be rather scared of","meaning":"相當害怕……","examples":[{"en":"Some women are rather scared of lifting weights.","zh":"有些女性相當害怕舉重。"},{"en":"To be rather scared of something means to feel quite afraid or nervous about it.","zh":"相當害怕某事，指對它感到頗害怕或緊張。"},{"en":"A beginner may be rather scared of speaking English in front of the class.","zh":"初學者可能相當害怕在全班面前說英語。"},{"en":"If people fear weights, they may avoid useful strength training.","zh":"如果人們害怕重量訓練，可能避開有用的力量訓練。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mild but real fear.","zh":"這個短語描述輕度但真實的恐懼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lifting weights","meaning":"舉重；負重訓練","examples":[{"en":"Lifting weights can help build lean tissue.","zh":"舉重可以幫助建立瘦肌肉組織。"},{"en":"Lifting weights means exercising by moving heavy objects to strengthen muscles.","zh":"舉重指透過移動重物來鍛鍊肌肉的運動。"},{"en":"A beginner may lift light dumbbells before trying heavier weights.","zh":"初學者可能先舉輕啞鈴，再嘗試較重重量。"},{"en":"If people lift weights regularly, muscle tone and strength may improve.","zh":"如果人們定期舉重，肌肉線條和力量可能改善。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to resistance exercise, not simply carrying shopping bags.","zh":"這個短語指阻力運動，而不只是提購物袋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"build lean tissue","meaning":"建立瘦肌肉組織","examples":[{"en":"Weight-bearing exercise helps build lean tissue.","zh":"負重運動有助建立瘦肌肉組織。"},{"en":"To build lean tissue means to develop muscle and other non-fat body tissue.","zh":"建立瘦肌肉組織，指發展肌肉和其他非脂肪身體組織。"},{"en":"A person may build lean tissue by doing squats, push-ups, and resistance training.","zh":"一個人可以透過深蹲、掌上壓和阻力訓練建立瘦肌肉組織。"},{"en":"If lean tissue increases, the body may look firmer and stronger.","zh":"如果瘦肌肉組織增加，身體可能看起來更緊實和強壯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes building healthy muscle, not gaining fat.","zh":"這個短語描述建立健康肌肉，而不是增加脂肪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"weight-bearing exercise","meaning":"負重運動","examples":[{"en":"Weight-bearing exercise is key to keeping the years at bay.","zh":"負重運動是延緩衰老的關鍵。"},{"en":"Weight-bearing exercise is exercise where the body works against weight or gravity.","zh":"負重運動是身體對抗重量或重力的運動。"},{"en":"Walking, squats, and lifting weights are forms of weight-bearing exercise.","zh":"步行、深蹲和舉重都是負重運動。"},{"en":"If muscles and bones are challenged, they may stay stronger with age.","zh":"如果肌肉和骨骼受到挑戰，它們可能隨年齡增長仍保持較強。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to exercise that loads the body.","zh":"這個短語指讓身體承受負荷的運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be key to","meaning":"是……的關鍵","examples":[{"en":"Building lean tissue is key to looking younger.","zh":"建立瘦肌肉組織是看起來更年輕的關鍵。"},{"en":"To be key to something means to be very important for achieving it.","zh":"是某事的關鍵，指對達成該事非常重要。"},{"en":"Regular practice is key to improving pronunciation.","zh":"定期練習是改善發音的關鍵。"},{"en":"If muscle tone affects posture, exercise can be key to a younger appearance.","zh":"如果肌肉線條影響姿勢，運動就可以是年輕外貌的關鍵。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies an essential factor.","zh":"這個短語指出必要因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"keep the years at bay","meaning":"延緩衰老","examples":[{"en":"Weight-bearing exercise helps keep the years at bay.","zh":"負重運動有助延緩衰老。"},{"en":"To keep the years at bay means to delay visible ageing.","zh":"延緩衰老，指推遲可見老化。"},{"en":"Good sleep and exercise can help keep the years at bay during a stressful job.","zh":"良好睡眠和運動可以在壓力大的工作中幫助延緩衰老。"},{"en":"If muscles stay strong, the body may look and move younger for longer.","zh":"如果肌肉保持強壯，身體可能更長時間看起來和動起來較年輕。"},{"en":"The phrase means slow ageing, not stop time.","zh":"這個短語指減慢老化，而不是停止時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reduce the effects of ageing","meaning":"減少老化的影響","examples":[{"en":"Exercise can help reduce the effects of ageing.","zh":"運動可以幫助減少老化的影響。"},{"en":"To reduce the effects of ageing means to lessen the physical or visible changes caused by getting older.","zh":"減少老化的影響，指減輕年齡增長造成的身體或可見變化。"},{"en":"Strength training may reduce the effects of ageing on posture and muscle tone.","zh":"力量訓練可能減少老化對姿勢和肌肉線條的影響。"},{"en":"If activity keeps the body strong, ageing signs may appear more slowly.","zh":"如果活動令身體保持強壯，老化跡象可能較慢出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making ageing less severe.","zh":"這個短語描述令老化較不嚴重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"slow down the decline of","meaning":"減慢……的衰退","examples":[{"en":"Exercise slows down the decline of type II muscle fibres.","zh":"運動減慢第二類肌纖維的衰退。"},{"en":"To slow down the decline of something means to make its weakening or reduction happen more slowly.","zh":"減慢某物的衰退，指令其變弱或減少發生得更慢。"},{"en":"Reading daily can slow down the decline of vocabulary after a course ends.","zh":"課程結束後每日閱讀可以減慢詞彙衰退。"},{"en":"If muscles are trained, age-related loss may happen more slowly.","zh":"如果肌肉得到訓練，與年齡相關的流失可能發生得較慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes delaying deterioration.","zh":"這個短語描述延緩退化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"type II muscle fibres","meaning":"第二類肌纖維","examples":[{"en":"Type II muscle fibres respond to resistance work.","zh":"第二類肌纖維對阻力訓練有反應。"},{"en":"Type II muscle fibres are muscle fibres used for quick, powerful movements.","zh":"第二類肌纖維是用於快速、有力動作的肌纖維。"},{"en":"Sprinting and lifting weights use type II muscle fibres more than slow walking does.","zh":"短跑和舉重比慢走更常使用第二類肌纖維。"},{"en":"If these fibres are not challenged, they may deteriorate with age.","zh":"如果這些肌纖維沒有受到挑戰，可能隨年齡退化。"},{"en":"The phrase names fast-power muscle fibres.","zh":"這個短語指出快速力量型肌纖維。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"type I muscle fibres","meaning":"第一類肌纖維","examples":[{"en":"Type I muscle fibres deal with aerobic activities.","zh":"第一類肌纖維負責帶氧活動。"},{"en":"Type I muscle fibres are muscle fibres used for endurance and steady activity.","zh":"第一類肌纖維是用於耐力和穩定活動的肌纖維。"},{"en":"Long-distance walking or cycling uses type I muscle fibres strongly.","zh":"長距離步行或踩單車會大量使用第一類肌纖維。"},{"en":"If an activity is slow and continuous, type I fibres are usually important.","zh":"如果活動緩慢而持續，第一類肌纖維通常很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase names endurance-type muscle fibres.","zh":"這個短語指出耐力型肌纖維。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"aerobic activities","meaning":"帶氧活動","examples":[{"en":"Type I muscle fibres deal with aerobic activities.","zh":"第一類肌纖維負責帶氧活動。"},{"en":"Aerobic activities are exercises that use oxygen and can be continued for some time.","zh":"帶氧活動是使用氧氣並能持續一段時間的運動。"},{"en":"Jogging, swimming, and brisk walking are aerobic activities.","zh":"慢跑、游泳和急步行都是帶氧活動。"},{"en":"If you can breathe steadily during exercise, it is often aerobic.","zh":"如果你在運動中能穩定呼吸，它通常屬於帶氧運動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to endurance exercise.","zh":"這個短語指耐力運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"anaerobic activities","meaning":"無氧活動","examples":[{"en":"Type II muscle fibres deal with anaerobic activities.","zh":"第二類肌纖維負責無氧活動。"},{"en":"Anaerobic activities are short, intense exercises that do not rely mainly on oxygen during the effort.","zh":"無氧活動是短暫而高強度、發力時不主要依賴氧氣的運動。"},{"en":"Sprinting and heavy lifting are common anaerobic activities.","zh":"短跑和重型舉重是常見無氧活動。"},{"en":"If an exercise is explosive and brief, type II fibres are often used.","zh":"如果一項運動爆發力強而短暫，通常會用到第二類肌纖維。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to high-intensity activity.","zh":"這個短語指高強度活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"respond to","meaning":"對……有反應","examples":[{"en":"Type II muscle fibres respond to resistance work.","zh":"第二類肌纖維對阻力訓練有反應。"},{"en":"To respond to something means to react or change because of it.","zh":"對某事有反應，指因它而作出反應或改變。"},{"en":"Students often respond well to clear examples and patient feedback.","zh":"學生通常對清楚例子和耐心回饋反應良好。"},{"en":"If muscles respond to training, they may become stronger or firmer.","zh":"如果肌肉對訓練有反應，它們可能變得更強或更結實。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reaction to a stimulus or treatment.","zh":"這個短語描述對刺激或處理的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"resistance work","meaning":"阻力訓練","examples":[{"en":"Resistance work can improve muscle tone.","zh":"阻力訓練可以改善肌肉線條。"},{"en":"Resistance work is exercise where muscles push or pull against weight, bands, or body weight.","zh":"阻力訓練是肌肉對抗重量、彈力帶或自身体重的運動。"},{"en":"Push-ups, squats, and dumbbell exercises are forms of resistance work.","zh":"掌上壓、深蹲和啞鈴練習都是阻力訓練。"},{"en":"If muscles work against resistance, they may grow stronger.","zh":"如果肌肉對抗阻力工作，它們可能變得更強。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to strength-building exercise.","zh":"這個短語指建立力量的運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"improve muscle tone","meaning":"改善肌肉線條","examples":[{"en":"Resistance work helps improve muscle tone.","zh":"阻力訓練有助改善肌肉線條。"},{"en":"To improve muscle tone means to make muscles look and feel firmer.","zh":"改善肌肉線條，指令肌肉看起來和感覺更結實。"},{"en":"Regular strength exercises can improve muscle tone in the arms and legs.","zh":"定期力量訓練可以改善手臂和腿部肌肉線條。"},{"en":"If muscle tone improves, posture and body shape may look younger.","zh":"如果肌肉線條改善，姿勢和身形可能看起來更年輕。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on firmness rather than large muscle size.","zh":"這個短語強調結實感，而不是巨大肌肉量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"with ageing","meaning":"隨着年齡增長","examples":[{"en":"With ageing, habitual activity often decreases.","zh":"隨着年齡增長，慣常活動通常減少。"},{"en":"With ageing means as people get older.","zh":"隨着年齡增長，指當人變老時。"},{"en":"With ageing, some people need more time to recover after exercise.","zh":"隨着年齡增長，有些人運動後需要更多時間恢復。"},{"en":"If activity falls with ageing, muscles receive less regular stimulation.","zh":"如果活動量隨年齡減少，肌肉就得到較少定期刺激。"},{"en":"The phrase links a change to the process of growing older.","zh":"這個短語把變化與變老過程連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reduction in frequency, duration, and intensity","meaning":"頻率、持續時間和強度下降","examples":[{"en":"Ageing often brings a reduction in frequency, duration, and intensity of activity.","zh":"年齡增長常帶來活動頻率、持續時間和強度下降。"},{"en":"A reduction in frequency, duration, and intensity means doing something less often, for less time, and less strongly.","zh":"頻率、持續時間和強度下降，指做某事次數較少、時間較短、力度較低。"},{"en":"A student may show this reduction if they practise once a week instead of daily, for ten minutes instead of an hour.","zh":"如果學生由每天練習一小時變成每週練習十分鐘，就是出現這種下降。"},{"en":"If exercise becomes shorter, rarer, and easier, fitness may decline.","zh":"如果運動變得更短、更少和更輕鬆，體能可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes three ways activity can decrease.","zh":"這個短語描述活動減少的三種方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"habitual activity","meaning":"慣常活動","examples":[{"en":"Habitual activity tends to decline with ageing.","zh":"慣常活動往往隨着年齡增長而下降。"},{"en":"Habitual activity means the movement or exercise someone normally does as part of daily life.","zh":"慣常活動指某人日常生活中通常做的活動或運動。"},{"en":"Walking to school every day is a form of habitual activity.","zh":"每天步行上學是一種慣常活動。"},{"en":"If habitual activity falls, muscles may receive fewer daily challenges.","zh":"如果慣常活動減少，肌肉可能接受較少日常挑戰。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to regular everyday activity, not one special workout.","zh":"這個短語指規律日常活動，而不是一次特別訓練。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"deteriorate","meaning":"退化","examples":[{"en":"Type II muscle fibres deteriorate when they do not get enough stimuli.","zh":"第二類肌纖維如果得不到足夠刺激，就會退化。"},{"en":"To deteriorate means to become worse, weaker, or less effective.","zh":"退化指變差、變弱或變得較低效。"},{"en":"A student’s handwriting may deteriorate if they stop writing by hand for months.","zh":"如果學生數月不手寫，字體可能退化。"},{"en":"If muscles are not used, their strength and condition may decline.","zh":"如果肌肉不被使用，其力量和狀態可能下降。"},{"en":"The word describes gradual worsening.","zh":"這個詞描述逐漸惡化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"get enough stimuli","meaning":"獲得足夠刺激","examples":[{"en":"Muscle fibres deteriorate if they do not get enough stimuli.","zh":"肌纖維如果沒有獲得足夠刺激，就會退化。"},{"en":"To get enough stimuli means to receive enough signals or challenges to stay active.","zh":"獲得足夠刺激，指收到足夠信號或挑戰以保持活躍。"},{"en":"Students need enough mental stimuli, such as questions and tasks, to stay engaged.","zh":"學生需要足夠心理刺激，例如問題和任務，才能保持投入。"},{"en":"If muscles are not challenged by movement, they may weaken.","zh":"如果肌肉沒有被活動挑戰，可能變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that use and challenge help maintain function.","zh":"這個短語顯示使用和挑戰有助維持功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"skin care","meaning":"皮膚護理","examples":[{"en":"Good skin care should start early.","zh":"良好的皮膚護理應及早開始。"},{"en":"Skin care means habits and products used to clean, protect, and maintain the skin.","zh":"皮膚護理指用來清潔、保護和維持皮膚的習慣和產品。"},{"en":"Washing the face gently and using sunscreen are basic skin-care habits.","zh":"溫和洗面和使用防曬是基本皮膚護理習慣。"},{"en":"If skin care starts early, damage may be easier to prevent than repair.","zh":"如果皮膚護理及早開始，損害可能較容易預防而不是修復。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to regular care, not only expensive products.","zh":"這個短語指定期護理，而不只是昂貴產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"skin cream","meaning":"護膚霜","examples":[{"en":"Almost every skin cream promises to make people look younger.","zh":"幾乎每種護膚霜都承諾令 人看起來更年輕。"},{"en":"Skin cream is a product applied to the skin to moisturise, protect, or improve its appearance.","zh":"護膚霜是塗在皮膚上，用來保濕、保護或改善外觀的產品。"},{"en":"A person may use skin cream after washing their face at night.","zh":"一個人可能晚上洗面後使用護膚霜。"},{"en":"If skin cream is used too late, it may not repair long-term damage fully.","zh":"如果護膚霜太遲使用，可能無法完全修復長期損害。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a common skincare product.","zh":"這個短語指常見護膚產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"promise to","meaning":"承諾會","examples":[{"en":"Many skin creams promise to make users look younger.","zh":"許多護膚霜承諾會令用家看起來更年輕。"},{"en":"To promise to do something means to say that something will happen or be done.","zh":"承諾會做某事，指說某事將會發生或被完成。"},{"en":"A tutor may promise to give feedback after every writing task.","zh":"補習老師可能承諾每次寫作任務後給回饋。"},{"en":"If a product promises dramatic results, consumers should check the evidence.","zh":"如果產品承諾有戲劇性效果，消費者應檢查證據。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe a real promise or an advertising claim.","zh":"這個短語可以描述真實承諾，也可以描述廣告聲稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be seduced by","meaning":"被……吸引","examples":[{"en":"Many people are seduced by promises of younger-looking skin.","zh":"許多人被看起來更年輕的承諾吸引。"},{"en":"To be seduced by something means to be strongly attracted by it, sometimes unwisely.","zh":"被某事吸引，指被它強烈吸引，有時是不明智地被吸引。"},{"en":"Students may be seduced by easy shortcuts that promise high marks without practice.","zh":"學生可能被承諾不用練習就有高分的捷徑吸引。"},{"en":"If an advert offers quick youth, people may buy before thinking carefully.","zh":"如果廣告提供快速年輕效果，人們可能未仔細思考就購買。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that attraction can lead to poor judgement.","zh":"這個短語提醒吸引力可能導致判斷失誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"end up disappointed","meaning":"最後感到失望","examples":[{"en":"Many people end up disappointed after using skin creams too late.","zh":"許多人太遲使用護膚霜後，最後感到失望。"},{"en":"To end up disappointed means to finally feel unhappy because results did not meet expectations.","zh":"最後感到失望，指因結果不符期望而最終不開心。"},{"en":"A student may end up disappointed if they start revision the night before the exam.","zh":"如果學生考試前一晚才開始溫習，可能最後感到失望。"},{"en":"If people expect a cream to reverse years of damage, they may not get the result they want.","zh":"如果人們期望護膚霜逆轉多年損害，可能得不到想要的結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an unhappy final outcome.","zh":"這個短語描述不愉快的最終結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the problem is not that…, but that…","meaning":"問題不是……而是……","examples":[{"en":"The problem is not that products do not work, but that people start using them too late.","zh":"問題不是產品沒有效，而是人們太遲開始使用。"},{"en":"The problem is not that A, but that B means B is the real issue, not A.","zh":"問題不是 A，而是 B，指真正問題是 B，不是 A。"},{"en":"The problem is not that students are lazy, but that they do not know how to revise.","zh":"問題不是學生懶惰，而是他們不知道如何溫習。"},{"en":"If products help prevention more than repair, timing becomes the real problem.","zh":"如果產品更擅長預防而非修復，時間點就是真正問題。"},{"en":"The structure corrects a mistaken explanation.","zh":"這個結構糾正錯誤解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"start using something too late","meaning":"太遲開始使用某物","examples":[{"en":"Many people start using skin-care products too late.","zh":"許多人太遲開始使用護膚產品。"},{"en":"To start using something too late means to begin after the best time has passed.","zh":"太遲開始使用某物，指在最佳時間已過後才開始。"},{"en":"A student who starts using a planner only after missing deadlines starts too late.","zh":"只有在錯過限期後才開始用計劃表的學生，就是太遲開始。"},{"en":"If skin damage has already developed, products may be less effective.","zh":"如果皮膚損害已經形成，產品可能較沒有效。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights poor timing.","zh":"這個短語突出時間點不佳。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"skip good skin care","meaning":"忽略良好的皮膚護理","examples":[{"en":"Some people skip good skin care until they think they need it.","zh":"有些人會忽略良好的皮膚護理，直到他們認為自己需要它。"},{"en":"To skip good skin care means to avoid or neglect regular habits that protect the skin.","zh":"忽略良好的皮膚護理，指避免或疏忽保護皮膚的定期習慣。"},{"en":"A teenager may skip sunscreen because they do not see damage yet.","zh":"青少年可能因尚未看到損害而不用防曬。"},{"en":"If people skip care for years, prevention becomes harder later.","zh":"如果人們多年忽略護理，日後預防就更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes neglecting helpful routines.","zh":"這個短語描述忽視有用日常習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"by then","meaning":"到那時","examples":[{"en":"By then, it may already be too late.","zh":"到那時，可能已經太遲。"},{"en":"By then means by that later time.","zh":"到那時，指到那個較後時間為止。"},{"en":"A student may plan to study on Sunday, but by then the exam may be too close.","zh":"學生可能打算星期日才溫習，但到那時考試可能已經太近。"},{"en":"If skin care begins only after wrinkles appear, earlier prevention has been missed.","zh":"如果皮膚護理只在皺紋出現後開始，就錯過了早期預防。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a later moment when the situation may have changed.","zh":"這個短語指向較後、情況可能已改變的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the first to go","meaning":"最先變差","examples":[{"en":"In women, the skin around the eyes is the first to go.","zh":"對女性而言，眼周皮膚最先變差。"},{"en":"The first to go means the first part to weaken, fail, or show damage.","zh":"最先變差，指最早變弱、失效或顯示損害的部分。"},{"en":"In an old phone, the battery is often the first to go.","zh":"在舊手機中，電池通常最先變差。"},{"en":"If eye skin is delicate, it may show ageing before other areas.","zh":"如果眼周皮膚細嫩，它可能比其他位置更早顯示老化。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the earliest part to decline.","zh":"這個短語指出最早衰退的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the skin around the eyes","meaning":"眼周皮膚","examples":[{"en":"The skin around the eyes often shows ageing early.","zh":"眼周皮膚常較早顯示老化。"},{"en":"The skin around the eyes is the delicate skin surrounding the eye area.","zh":"眼周皮膚是圍繞眼睛區域的細嫩皮膚。"},{"en":"People may notice fine lines around the eyes after poor sleep.","zh":"睡眠不足後，人們可能注意到眼周細紋。"},{"en":"If this skin is thin, sun and dryness may affect it quickly.","zh":"如果這些皮膚很薄，陽光和乾燥可能很快影響它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a sensitive facial area.","zh":"這個短語指敏感面部區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a good routine","meaning":"良好的護理習慣","examples":[{"en":"A good skin-care routine should start early.","zh":"良好的皮膚護理習慣應及早開始。"},{"en":"A good routine is a regular set of helpful habits.","zh":"良好習慣是一套定期而有幫助的行為。"},{"en":"A student’s good study routine may include reading notes after each lesson.","zh":"學生良好的學習習慣可能包括每課後閱讀筆記。"},{"en":"If skin care becomes routine, protection happens before serious damage appears.","zh":"如果皮膚護理成為習慣，保護就會在嚴重損害出現前發生。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses consistency.","zh":"這個短語強調持續性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"maintenance is much easier than repair","meaning":"保養比修復容易得多","examples":[{"en":"Maintenance is much easier than repair when it comes to skin care.","zh":"說到皮膚護理，保養比修復容易得多。"},{"en":"Maintenance means keeping something in good condition, while repair means fixing damage after it happens.","zh":"保養指保持某物狀態良好，而修復指在損害發生後修補。"},{"en":"Brushing teeth daily is easier than repairing serious tooth decay later.","zh":"每天刷牙比日後修補嚴重蛀牙容易。"},{"en":"If skin is protected early, fewer problems need repairing later.","zh":"如果皮膚早期受到保護，日後需要修復的問題會較少。"},{"en":"The phrase teaches prevention before damage.","zh":"這個短語教人要在損害前預防。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"become more transparent","meaning":"變得更薄更透","examples":[{"en":"Your skin becomes more transparent as you get older.","zh":"隨着年齡增長，你的皮膚會變得更薄更透。"},{"en":"To become more transparent means to become thinner or more see-through in appearance.","zh":"變得更薄更透，指外觀上變薄或更透視。"},{"en":"Old paper may become more transparent when it becomes thin and worn.","zh":"舊紙張變薄和磨損後，可能變得更透。"},{"en":"If skin becomes thinner with age, veins and uneven colour may show more easily.","zh":"如果皮膚隨年齡變薄，血管和不均膚色可能更容易顯露。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a visible change in skin quality.","zh":"這個短語描述皮膚質素的可見改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as you get older","meaning":"隨着年齡增長","examples":[{"en":"You need to adapt your make-up as you get older.","zh":"隨着年齡增長，你需要調整化妝。"},{"en":"As you get older means while or when you age.","zh":"隨着年齡增長，指在人變老的過程中。"},{"en":"As people get older, they may need more time to recover after exercise.","zh":"隨着人們年齡增長，運動後可能需要更多恢復時間。"},{"en":"If skin changes with age, make-up and hair colour may need adjustment.","zh":"如果皮膚隨年齡改變，化妝和髮色可能需要調整。"},{"en":"The phrase links advice to ageing over time.","zh":"這個短語把建議與隨時間老化連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"adapt your make-up and hair colour","meaning":"調整化妝和髮色","examples":[{"en":"You need to adapt your make-up and hair colour accordingly.","zh":"你需要相應地調整化妝和髮色。"},{"en":"To adapt your make-up and hair colour means to change them to suit your current face, skin, or age.","zh":"調整化妝和髮色，指改變它們以配合目前面容、皮膚或年齡。"},{"en":"A person may use softer make-up and warmer hair colour as their skin changes.","zh":"隨着皮膚改變，一個人可能使用較柔和化妝和較暖髮色。"},{"en":"If old colours look harsh, adapting them can make the face look fresher.","zh":"如果舊顏色看起來刺眼，調整它們可以令面容更清新。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adjusting style to match changing appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述調整風格以配合變化中的外貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"accordingly","meaning":"相應地","examples":[{"en":"Skin changes with age, so make-up should be adapted accordingly.","zh":"皮膚隨年齡改變，所以化妝應相應地調整。"},{"en":"Accordingly means in a way that matches the situation just mentioned.","zh":"相應地，指以配合剛提及情況的方式。"},{"en":"If the weather is hot, students should dress accordingly.","zh":"如果天氣炎熱，學生應相應地穿衣。"},{"en":"If skin becomes thinner, foundation should be chosen accordingly.","zh":"如果皮膚變薄，粉底應相應地選擇。"},{"en":"The word shows that one action follows from a condition.","zh":"這個詞顯示某行動根據某情況而來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"foundation","meaning":"粉底","examples":[{"en":"Foundation should be lighter than you might expect.","zh":"粉底應比你預期的更淺色。"},{"en":"Foundation is a make-up product used on the face to even out skin tone.","zh":"粉底是一種塗在臉上用來均勻膚色的化妝品。"},{"en":"A person may apply foundation before powder or blush.","zh":"一個人可能先塗粉底，再上蜜粉或胭脂。"},{"en":"If foundation is too heavy or dark, it can make ageing skin look harsher.","zh":"如果粉底太厚或太深色，可以令老化皮膚看起來更生硬。"},{"en":"The word refers to a base layer of make-up.","zh":"這個詞指化妝中的底層產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"lighter than you would imagine","meaning":"比你想像中更淺色","examples":[{"en":"Foundation should be lighter than you would imagine.","zh":"粉底應比你想像中更淺色。"},{"en":"Lighter than you would imagine means paler or less heavy-looking than expected.","zh":"比你想像中更淺色，指比預期更淡或看起來更輕薄。"},{"en":"A teacher’s workload may be lighter than students imagine during holidays, but not always.","zh":"假期中老師工作量可能比學生想像中輕，但不一定。"},{"en":"If older skin is more transparent, a lighter foundation may look more natural.","zh":"如果年長皮膚更薄透，較淺色粉底可能看起來更自然。"},{"en":"The phrase corrects an expectation.","zh":"這個短語修正預期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"sheerer","meaning":"更薄透的","examples":[{"en":"Foundation should become lighter and sheerer with age.","zh":"隨着年齡增長，粉底應變得更淺色和更薄透。"},{"en":"Sheerer means thinner, lighter, and less opaque in appearance.","zh":"更薄透的，指外觀上更薄、更輕和較不遮蓋。"},{"en":"A sheer curtain lets more light through than a thick curtain.","zh":"薄紗窗簾比厚窗簾讓更多光線透過。"},{"en":"If foundation is sheerer, it may avoid looking heavy on ageing skin.","zh":"如果粉底更薄透，可能避免在老化皮膚上顯得厚重。"},{"en":"The word describes light coverage.","zh":"這個詞描述輕薄遮瑕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"cover grey","meaning":"遮蓋白髮","examples":[{"en":"Some people use hair dye to cover grey.","zh":"有些人使用染髮劑遮蓋白髮。"},{"en":"To cover grey means to hide grey or white hair with colour.","zh":"遮蓋白髮，指用顏色隱藏灰白頭髮。"},{"en":"A person may cover grey before a wedding or job interview.","zh":"一個人可能在婚禮或求職面試前遮蓋白髮。"},{"en":"If the dye is too dark, covering grey can make the face look harsher.","zh":"如果染髮劑太深色，遮蓋白髮可能令面容看起來更生硬。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to colouring grey hair.","zh":"這個短語指為白髮上色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be tempted to","meaning":"忍不住想……","examples":[{"en":"Do not be tempted to choose a too-dark hair colour.","zh":"不要忍不住選擇過深的髮色。"},{"en":"To be tempted to do something means to feel attracted to doing it, even if it may be unwise.","zh":"忍不住想做某事，指被吸引去做，即使可能不明智。"},{"en":"A tired student may be tempted to skip revision and watch videos.","zh":"疲倦學生可能忍不住想跳過溫習去看影片。"},{"en":"If dark hair dye seems youthful, people may choose it even when it looks harsh.","zh":"如果深色染髮看似年輕，人們可能即使它顯得生硬也會選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against a tempting but possibly poor choice.","zh":"這個短語警告不要作出誘人但可能差劣的選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"go for","meaning":"選擇","examples":[{"en":"Do not go for a hair colour that is too dark.","zh":"不要選擇太深的髮色。"},{"en":"To go for something means to choose or decide on it.","zh":"“Go for” 某物，指選擇或決定採用它。"},{"en":"At lunch, a student may go for noodles instead of rice.","zh":"午餐時，學生可能選擇麵而不是飯。"},{"en":"If you go for a softer hair colour, your face may look less harsh.","zh":"如果你選擇較柔和的髮色，面容可能看起來不那麼生硬。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and means choose.","zh":"這個短語較口語，意思是選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"too-dark hair colour","meaning":"過深的髮色","examples":[{"en":"A too-dark hair colour can look harsh.","zh":"過深的髮色可能看起來生硬。"},{"en":"A too-dark hair colour is a hair colour darker than suits the person’s skin and age.","zh":"過深的髮色，是比該人的膚色和年齡適合程度更深的髮色。"},{"en":"Someone with very pale skin may find black dye too harsh.","zh":"皮膚很白的人可能覺得黑色染髮太生硬。"},{"en":"If hair colour is too dark, it can draw attention to lines and shadows.","zh":"如果髮色太深，可能突出皺紋和陰影。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that darker is not always younger-looking.","zh":"這個短語提醒較深色不一定更顯年輕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"block colour","meaning":"單一實色","examples":[{"en":"Block colour may look less flattering than highlights.","zh":"單一實色可能不如挑染那麼修飾外貌。"},{"en":"Block colour is one solid, even colour without lighter or darker sections.","zh":"單一實色，是沒有深淺變化的一整片均勻顏色。"},{"en":"A wall painted entirely blue uses block colour.","zh":"整面牆塗成藍色，就是使用單一實色。"},{"en":"If hair is dyed one flat dark colour, the face may look harsher.","zh":"如果頭髮染成一整片深色，面容可能看起來更生硬。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts single colour with softer mixed tones.","zh":"這個短語把單一顏色與較柔和的混合色調作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"highlights","meaning":"挑染","examples":[{"en":"Highlights can look softer than block colour.","zh":"挑染可以比單一實色看起來更柔和。"},{"en":"Highlights are lighter sections added to hair to create depth and brightness.","zh":"挑染是加入頭髮中的較淺色部分，用來創造層次和亮度。"},{"en":"A hairdresser may add highlights around the face to soften the look.","zh":"髮型師可能在臉旁加入挑染，以柔和整體外觀。"},{"en":"If highlights break up a dark colour, the overall effect may look more natural.","zh":"如果挑染打破深色的單一感，整體效果可能更自然。"},{"en":"The word refers to lighter streaks in hair.","zh":"這個詞指頭髮中的較淺色髮束。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"apply moisturiser","meaning":"塗潤膚霜","examples":[{"en":"You should apply moisturiser around the back of the neck.","zh":"你應該在頸背周圍塗潤膚霜。"},{"en":"To apply moisturiser means to put a skin cream or lotion onto the skin.","zh":"塗潤膚霜，指把護膚霜或乳液塗在皮膚上。"},{"en":"People often apply moisturiser after washing their face or hands.","zh":"人們常在洗面或洗手後塗潤膚霜。"},{"en":"If the neck is dry, applying moisturiser may help keep the skin softer.","zh":"如果頸部乾燥，塗潤膚霜可能有助保持皮膚較柔軟。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using a skincare product on the body.","zh":"這個短語描述在身體上使用護膚產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the back of the neck","meaning":"頸背","examples":[{"en":"Do not forget to apply moisturiser around the back of the neck.","zh":"不要忘記在頸背周圍塗潤膚霜。"},{"en":"The back of the neck is the area behind the neck, below the hairline.","zh":"頸背是頸部後方、髮線以下的區域。"},{"en":"Sunscreen should be applied to the back of the neck when hiking.","zh":"遠足時應把防曬霜塗在頸背。"},{"en":"If this area is ignored, it may show ageing or sun damage.","zh":"如果這個位置被忽略，可能顯示老化或日曬損害。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a body area people often forget.","zh":"這個短語指出人們常忘記的身體部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be attached to a bone","meaning":"附着在骨頭上","examples":[{"en":"The skin at the back of the neck is attached to a bone.","zh":"頸背的皮膚附着在骨頭上。"},{"en":"To be attached to a bone means to be connected closely to bone or the structures around it.","zh":"附着在骨頭上，指與骨頭或其周圍結構緊密連接。"},{"en":"Tendons are attached to bones so muscles can move the body.","zh":"肌腱附着在骨頭上，使肌肉能移動身體。"},{"en":"If skin is attached tightly, sagging or tension may show differently there.","zh":"如果皮膚連接較緊，鬆弛或張力可能在那裡以不同方式出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a physical connection inside the body.","zh":"這個短語描述身體內的實際連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"look after","meaning":"照顧","examples":[{"en":"It is important to look after the skin around the neck.","zh":"照顧頸部周圍皮膚很重要。"},{"en":"To look after something means to care for it and keep it in good condition.","zh":"照顧某物，指關心它並保持其良好狀態。"},{"en":"Students should look after library books so others can use them.","zh":"學生應照顧圖書館書籍，讓其他人也能使用。"},{"en":"If you look after your skin early, repair may be easier later.","zh":"如果你及早照顧皮膚，日後修復可能較容易。"},{"en":"The phrase means care for, not simply look at.","zh":"這個短語意思是護理，而不只是觀看。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"avoid sagging","meaning":"避免鬆弛","examples":[{"en":"Moisturiser may help people avoid sagging skin.","zh":"潤膚霜可能幫助人避免皮膚鬆弛。"},{"en":"To avoid sagging means to prevent skin or tissue from becoming loose and hanging down.","zh":"避免鬆弛，指防止皮膚或組織變得鬆垂。"},{"en":"Good posture and muscle tone may help avoid sagging in some body areas.","zh":"良好姿勢和肌肉線條可能有助某些身體部位避免鬆弛。"},{"en":"If skin loses support and moisture, sagging may become more visible.","zh":"如果皮膚失去支撐和水分，鬆弛可能更明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preventing looseness caused by ageing or weakness.","zh":"這個短語描述防止因老化或無力造成的鬆垂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"corresponding letter","meaning":"相應字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the corresponding letter in the appropriate box.","zh":"考生在適當方格中寫上相應字母。"},{"en":"A corresponding letter is the letter that matches the correct answer or option.","zh":"相應字母，是與正確答案或選項相配的字母。"},{"en":"In a matching task, “B” may be the corresponding letter for the second statement.","zh":"在配對題中，“B” 可能是第二項陳述的相應字母。"},{"en":"If students choose the wrong letter, the answer will not match the evidence.","zh":"如果學生選錯字母，答案就不符合證據。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"appropriate box","meaning":"適當方格","examples":[{"en":"Students write the answer in the appropriate box on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生把答案寫在答題紙上的適當方格中。"},{"en":"The appropriate box is the correct space where an answer should be written.","zh":"適當方格，是應填寫答案的正確空格。"},{"en":"In a form, your phone number must go in the appropriate box.","zh":"在表格中，你的電話號碼必須填在適當方格。"},{"en":"If an answer is written in the wrong box, it may be marked incorrectly.","zh":"如果答案寫在錯誤方格，可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the right place for information.","zh":"這個短語指填寫資料的正確位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"according to surveys","meaning":"根據調查","examples":[{"en":"According to surveys, sun exposure can make a person look older.","zh":"根據調查，日曬可以令一個人看起來較老。"},{"en":"According to surveys means based on information collected from groups of people.","zh":"根據調查，指基於從群體中收集得來的資料。"},{"en":"According to surveys, many students sleep less before major exams.","zh":"根據調查，許多學生在大型考試前睡得較少。"},{"en":"If survey results show a pattern, researchers may investigate it further.","zh":"如果調查結果顯示某種模式，研究者可能進一步調查。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence from surveys.","zh":"這個短語引入來自調查的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"which of the following","meaning":"以下哪一項","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which of the following factors makes a person look older.","zh":"題目問以下哪一項因素會令人看起來較老。"},{"en":"Which of the following means choose one or more options from the list given.","zh":"以下哪一項，指從給出的列表中選擇一個或多個選項。"},{"en":"A test may ask, “Which of the following is a renewable energy source?”","zh":"測驗可能問：「以下哪一項是可再生能源？」"},{"en":"If a question says “which of the following,” students must compare the listed choices.","zh":"如果題目說「以下哪一項」，學生必須比較列出的選項。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard multiple-choice instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準選擇題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"make a person look older","meaning":"令一個人看起來較老","examples":[{"en":"Several social and lifestyle factors can make a person look older.","zh":"幾種社會和生活方式因素可以令一個人看起來較老。"},{"en":"To make a person look older means to increase their perceived age.","zh":"令一個人看起來較老，指增加其觀感年齡。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can make a person look older by creating dark circles.","zh":"睡眠不足可以透過造成黑眼圈，令一個人看起來較老。"},{"en":"If smoking and stress damage the skin, they may visually age the face.","zh":"如果吸煙和壓力損害皮膚，它們可能在視覺上令面部變老。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change in appearance, not actual age.","zh":"這個短語描述外貌改變，而不是真實年齡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"spend a long time in the sun","meaning":"長時間曬太陽","examples":[{"en":"Spending a long time in the sun can make the skin age faster.","zh":"長時間曬太陽可以令皮膚老化得更快。"},{"en":"To spend a long time in the sun means to stay under sunlight for many hours.","zh":"長時間曬太陽，指在陽光下停留很多小時。"},{"en":"Beach workers may spend a long time in the sun every day.","zh":"海灘工作者可能每天長時間曬太陽。"},{"en":"If the skin receives too much sunlight, wrinkles and spots may appear earlier.","zh":"如果皮膚接受太多陽光，皺紋和斑點可能更早出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extended sun exposure.","zh":"這個短語描述長時間日曬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"nutritional factors","meaning":"營養因素","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which nutritional factors make a person look older.","zh":"題目問哪些營養因素會令一個人看起來較老。"},{"en":"Nutritional factors are food-related influences on health and appearance.","zh":"營養因素是與食物相關、影響健康和外貌的因素。"},{"en":"Protein intake, water intake, and fruit consumption are nutritional factors.","zh":"蛋白質攝取、水分攝取和水果食用量都是營養因素。"},{"en":"If nutritional factors are poor, skin may lose freshness and elasticity.","zh":"如果營養因素差，皮膚可能失去清新感和彈性。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to diet-based causes.","zh":"這個短語指以飲食為基礎的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"not eating enough protein","meaning":"蛋白質攝取不足","examples":[{"en":"Not eating enough protein can prematurely age a person.","zh":"蛋白質攝取不足可以令一個人過早衰老。"},{"en":"Not eating enough protein means the diet does not provide enough protein for repair and muscle maintenance.","zh":"蛋白質攝取不足，指飲食沒有提供足夠蛋白質作修復和維持肌肉。"},{"en":"Someone who eats only snacks may not eat enough protein.","zh":"只吃零食的人可能沒有攝取足夠蛋白質。"},{"en":"If protein is too low, the body may struggle to maintain healthy skin and muscle.","zh":"如果蛋白質太低，身體可能難以維持健康皮膚和肌肉。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a specific dietary shortage.","zh":"這個短語描述特定飲食不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"eating lots of meat","meaning":"吃大量肉類","examples":[{"en":"The answer option mentions eating lots of meat.","zh":"答案選項提到吃大量肉類。"},{"en":"Eating lots of meat means consuming a large amount of meat regularly.","zh":"吃大量肉類，指定期攝取大量肉類。"},{"en":"A person who eats steak, sausages, and chicken at every meal eats lots of meat.","zh":"每餐都吃牛扒、香腸和雞肉的人，就是吃大量肉類。"},{"en":"If a question mentions this option, students must check whether the passage supports it.","zh":"如果題目提到這個選項，學生必須檢查文章是否支持它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes quantity, not automatically healthiness or unhealthiness.","zh":"這個短語描述數量，不自動代表健康或不健康。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"make a person look younger","meaning":"令一個人看起來較年輕","examples":[{"en":"Exercise and nutrition may help make a person look younger.","zh":"運動和營養可能幫助令一個人看起來較年輕。"},{"en":"To make a person look younger means to reduce their perceived age.","zh":"令一個人看起來較年輕，指降低其觀感年齡。"},{"en":"Better posture can make a person look younger in photos.","zh":"較好姿勢可以令一個人在照片中看起來較年輕。"},{"en":"If skin becomes fresher and muscles firmer, appearance may seem younger.","zh":"如果皮膚變得更清新、肌肉更緊實，外貌可能顯得更年輕。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to visual effect, not changing birth date.","zh":"這個短語指視覺效果，而不是改變出生日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"keep something in better condition","meaning":"令某物保持較好狀態","examples":[{"en":"Exercise helps keep type II muscle fibres in better condition.","zh":"運動有助令第二類肌纖維保持較好狀態。"},{"en":"To keep something in better condition means to maintain it so it stays healthier or works better.","zh":"令某物保持較好狀態，指維持它，使其較健康或運作更好。"},{"en":"Regular cleaning keeps classroom desks in better condition.","zh":"定期清潔可令課室書桌保持較好狀態。"},{"en":"If muscles are trained, they may stay stronger and deteriorate more slowly.","zh":"如果肌肉得到訓練，它們可能保持較強並退化得較慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes maintenance and protection.","zh":"這個短語描述保養和保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"increase oxygen flow","meaning":"增加氧氣流動","examples":[{"en":"Some exercise may increase oxygen flow in the body.","zh":"一些運動可能增加身體內的氧氣流動。"},{"en":"To increase oxygen flow means to improve the movement or supply of oxygen through the body.","zh":"增加氧氣流動，指改善氧氣在身體中的移動或供應。"},{"en":"Brisk walking can increase oxygen flow as breathing and heart rate rise.","zh":"急步行時呼吸和心跳加快，可以增加氧氣流動。"},{"en":"If oxygen flow improves, muscles and skin may receive better support.","zh":"如果氧氣流動改善，肌肉和皮膚可能得到更好支援。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improved circulation and breathing effect.","zh":"這個短語描述改善循環和呼吸的效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the main problem with","meaning":"……的主要問題","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the main problem with skincare products.","zh":"題目問護膚產品的主要問題。"},{"en":"The main problem with something is its most important weakness or difficulty.","zh":"某物的主要問題，是其最重要的弱點或困難。"},{"en":"The main problem with late revision is that there is not enough time to practise.","zh":"臨急溫習的主要問題是沒有足夠時間練習。"},{"en":"If products are used too late, timing may be the real weakness.","zh":"如果產品太遲使用，時間點可能是真正弱點。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for the central issue.","zh":"這個短語問核心問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"skincare products","meaning":"護膚產品","examples":[{"en":"Many people start using skincare products too late.","zh":"許多人太遲開始使用護膚產品。"},{"en":"Skincare products are creams, lotions, cleansers, or treatments used to care for the skin.","zh":"護膚產品是用來護理皮膚的面霜、乳液、潔面產品或療程。"},{"en":"Sunscreen and moisturiser are common skincare products.","zh":"防曬霜和潤膚霜是常見護膚產品。"},{"en":"If skincare products are used regularly and early, they may help prevent damage.","zh":"如果護膚產品定期及早使用，可能幫助預防損害。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to items used in skin-care routines.","zh":"這個短語指皮膚護理程序中使用的物品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"early enough","meaning":"夠早","examples":[{"en":"Many people do not use skincare products early enough.","zh":"許多人沒有夠早使用護膚產品。"},{"en":"Early enough means soon enough to be effective or useful.","zh":"夠早，指時間早到足以有效或有用。"},{"en":"Students who start revision early enough can practise instead of only memorising.","zh":"夠早開始溫習的學生可以練習，而不只是背誦。"},{"en":"If skin care does not begin before damage appears, prevention may be lost.","zh":"如果皮膚護理沒有在損害出現前開始，預防作用可能已失去。"},{"en":"The phrase judges whether the timing is soon enough.","zh":"這個短語判斷時間是否足夠早。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"spend too much money on","meaning":"在……花太多錢","examples":[{"en":"Some people worry that consumers spend too much money on skincare products.","zh":"有些人擔心消費者在護膚產品上花太多錢。"},{"en":"To spend too much money on something means to pay more for it than is necessary or sensible.","zh":"在某物上花太多錢，指花費超過必要或合理的金錢。"},{"en":"A student may spend too much money on stationery instead of using what they already have.","zh":"學生可能在文具上花太多錢，而不用已有物品。"},{"en":"If people buy many creams without changing habits, the money may not bring good results.","zh":"如果人們購買許多面霜卻不改變習慣，金錢可能帶不來好效果。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises excessive spending.","zh":"這個短語批評過度消費。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the following sentences","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the following sentences using words from the text.","zh":"考生使用文本中的字詞完成以下句子。"},{"en":"To complete the following sentences means to fill in the blanks in the sentences below.","zh":"完成以下句子，指填寫下面句子中的空格。"},{"en":"Students complete sentences by choosing words that fit the grammar and meaning.","zh":"學生透過選擇符合文法和意思的詞語完成句子。"},{"en":"If the answer must come from the text, students should not invent their own wording.","zh":"如果答案必須來自文本，學生不應自行創作措辭。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should use no more than three words from the text.","zh":"每個答案應使用文本中不多於三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"不多於三個字，指答案必須包含三個詞或以下。"},{"en":"“fresh fruit” is acceptable, but a five-word answer is too long.","zh":"“fresh fruit” 可以接受，但五個詞的答案太長。"},{"en":"If students exceed the word limit, the answer may be marked wrong.","zh":"如果學生超出字數限制，答案可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict answer-length rule.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格答案長度規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"for each gap","meaning":"每個空格","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose words from the text for each gap.","zh":"考生為每個空格從文本中選擇字詞。"},{"en":"For each gap means for every blank space in the exercise.","zh":"每個空格，指練習中每一個空白位置。"},{"en":"In a cloze task, students must read around each gap before answering.","zh":"在填充題中，學生作答前必須閱讀每個空格前後內容。"},{"en":"If one gap needs a noun and another needs a verb, answers must change accordingly.","zh":"如果一個空格需要名詞，另一個需要動詞，答案就必須相應改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to every missing-word position.","zh":"這個短語指每個缺詞位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"Danish survey","meaning":"丹麥調查","examples":[{"en":"The Danish survey used photographs of twins.","zh":"丹麥調查使用了雙胞胎的照片。"},{"en":"A Danish survey is a survey carried out in Denmark or by Danish researchers.","zh":"丹麥調查是在丹麥進行或由丹麥研究者進行的調查。"},{"en":"A Danish survey on health may collect answers from people living in Denmark.","zh":"關於健康的丹麥調查可能收集丹麥居民的答案。"},{"en":"If a survey uses twins, researchers can compare people with similar genes.","zh":"如果調查使用雙胞胎，研究者可以比較基因相似的人。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the origin or setting of the survey.","zh":"這個短語指出調查的來源或背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"use photographs of","meaning":"使用……的照片","examples":[{"en":"The researchers used photographs of twins in the survey.","zh":"研究者在調查中使用雙胞胎的照片。"},{"en":"To use photographs of people means to study or show their pictures as evidence.","zh":"使用某人的照片，指研究或展示其圖片作為證據。"},{"en":"A school project may use photographs of old streets to compare past and present.","zh":"學校項目可能使用舊街道照片比較過去與現在。"},{"en":"If nurses judge age from photographs, they assess appearance rather than medical records.","zh":"如果護士從照片判斷年齡，她們評估的是外貌，而不是醫療記錄。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using images as research material.","zh":"這個短語描述使用圖片作研究材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"relatively easily","meaning":"相對容易地","examples":[{"en":"The greatest difference people can make relatively easily is with nutrition.","zh":"人們可以相對容易地作出的最大改變在於營養。"},{"en":"Relatively easily means more easily compared with other possible changes.","zh":"相對容易地，指與其他可能改變相比較容易。"},{"en":"A student can relatively easily organise notes, but changing school policy is harder.","zh":"學生可以相對容易地整理筆記，但改變學校政策較難。"},{"en":"If diet is easier to change than social class, nutrition becomes a practical focus.","zh":"如果飲食比社會階層更容易改變，營養就成為實際焦點。"},{"en":"The phrase compares difficulty.","zh":"這個短語比較難度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"get rid of toxins","meaning":"清除毒素","examples":[{"en":"The human body uses the liver and kidneys to get rid of toxins.","zh":"人體使用肝臟和腎臟清除毒素。"},{"en":"To get rid of toxins means to remove harmful substances from the body.","zh":"清除毒素，指把有害物質從身體移除。"},{"en":"Drinking water helps the body get rid of waste products.","zh":"喝水幫助身體清除廢物。"},{"en":"If toxins are not removed effectively, the body may feel tired or stressed.","zh":"如果毒素沒有有效清除，身體可能感到疲倦或受壓。"},{"en":"The phrase describes clearing harmful substances away.","zh":"這個短語描述把有害物質清走。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"low-fat diet","meaning":"低脂飲食","examples":[{"en":"A low-fat diet can make people look older.","zh":"低脂飲食可以令人看起來較老。"},{"en":"A low-fat diet is an eating plan that reduces fat intake strongly.","zh":"低脂飲食是大幅減少脂肪攝取的飲食計劃。"},{"en":"Someone on a low-fat diet may avoid nuts, oily fish, and cooking oil.","zh":"採用低脂飲食的人可能避免果仁、油性魚類和食油。"},{"en":"If healthy fats are cut too much, skin may lose a youthful feel.","zh":"如果健康脂肪被削減太多，皮膚可能失去年輕感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a diet low in fat, not automatically a healthy diet.","zh":"這個短語描述脂肪含量低的飲食，不自動代表健康飲食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所提供資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements agree with the information given in the passage.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與文章所提供資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"與所提供資料一致，指符合文章所說內容。"},{"en":"If a passage says smoking ages the skin, a statement saying the same thing agrees with it.","zh":"如果文章說吸煙令皮膚老化，陳述相同內容就與文章一致。"},{"en":"If a statement adds unsupported details, it may not agree with the given information.","zh":"如果陳述加入未被支持的細節，可能不符合所提供資料。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個短語用於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement is false if it contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"如果陳述與文章資料相矛盾，就是 FALSE。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"與資料相矛盾，指說出與文章內容相反的意思。"},{"en":"If a text says exercise helps ageing, saying exercise has no benefit contradicts it.","zh":"如果文本說運動有助抗老，說運動沒有好處就是與之矛盾。"},{"en":"When an answer contradicts the passage, it should be marked false.","zh":"當答案與文章矛盾，就應被判為 false。"},{"en":"The phrase means conflict with the given evidence.","zh":"這個短語指與所給證據衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"Students write NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果沒有這方面的資料，學生寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not say enough to decide whether it is true or false.","zh":"沒有這方面的資料，指文章沒有足夠內容判斷真假。"},{"en":"If a passage discusses smoking but not coffee, a statement about coffee may be NOT GIVEN.","zh":"如果文章討論吸煙但沒有討論咖啡，關於咖啡的陳述可能是 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when the text gives no information.","zh":"當文本沒有資料時，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the answer cannot be judged from the passage.","zh":"這個短語表示答案不能根據文章判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"social class","meaning":"社會階層","examples":[{"en":"A person’s social class can affect how old they look.","zh":"一個人的社會階層可以影響他看起來有多老。"},{"en":"Social class is a person’s position in society, often linked to income, education, and job type.","zh":"社會階層是一個人在社會中的位置，常與收入、教育和工作類型相關。"},{"en":"People from different social classes may have different access to healthcare and rest.","zh":"來自不同社會階層的人，可能有不同醫療和休息機會。"},{"en":"If social class affects stress and lifestyle, it may also affect appearance.","zh":"如果社會階層影響壓力和生活方式，也可能影響外貌。"},{"en":"The phrase describes social position, not personal worth.","zh":"這個短語描述社會位置，而不是個人價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"have children","meaning":"有子女","examples":[{"en":"Having children was found to make men look younger.","zh":"研究發現，有子女會令男性看起來較年輕。"},{"en":"To have children means to be a parent.","zh":"有子女，指成為父母。"},{"en":"A man who has two sons and a daughter has children.","zh":"有兩個兒子和一個女兒的男人就是有子女。"},{"en":"If family life changes mood or behaviour, it may affect appearance in some groups.","zh":"如果家庭生活改變心情或行為，可能在某些群體中影響外貌。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to parenthood.","zh":"這個短語指為人父母。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"need to drink more water than","meaning":"需要比……喝更多水","examples":[{"en":"Smokers may need to drink more water than non-smokers.","zh":"吸煙者可能需要比非吸煙者喝更多水。"},{"en":"To need to drink more water than someone means to require a greater amount of water.","zh":"需要比某人喝更多水，指需要較大量水分。"},{"en":"A runner may need to drink more water than a person sitting indoors all day.","zh":"跑步者可能需要比整天坐在室內的人喝更多水。"},{"en":"If smoking dehydrates the body, smokers may need extra water to help remove toxins.","zh":"如果吸煙令身體脫水，吸煙者可能需要額外水分幫助清除毒素。"},{"en":"The phrase compares water needs between groups.","zh":"這個短語比較不同群體的水分需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"non-smokers","meaning":"非吸煙者","examples":[{"en":"Non-smokers are not exposed to cigarette smoke in the same way.","zh":"非吸煙者不會以同樣方式暴露於香煙煙霧。"},{"en":"Non-smokers are people who do not smoke cigarettes or tobacco products.","zh":"非吸煙者是不吸香煙或煙草產品的人。"},{"en":"A non-smoker may still breathe second-hand smoke if others smoke nearby.","zh":"如果附近有人吸煙，非吸煙者仍可能吸入二手煙。"},{"en":"If smokers need more water, non-smokers may not have the same toxin burden.","zh":"如果吸煙者需要更多水，非吸煙者可能沒有同樣毒素負擔。"},{"en":"The word contrasts people who smoke with those who do not.","zh":"這個詞把吸煙的人和不吸煙的人作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"get enough fatty acids","meaning":"攝取足夠脂肪酸","examples":[{"en":"Some people do not get enough fatty acids because they avoid fats.","zh":"有些人因避免脂肪而沒有攝取足夠脂肪酸。"},{"en":"To get enough fatty acids means to consume enough important fats for body function.","zh":"攝取足夠脂肪酸，指攝取足夠重要脂肪以支援身體功能。"},{"en":"Eating nuts and oily fish can help people get enough fatty acids.","zh":"吃果仁和油性魚類可以幫助人攝取足夠脂肪酸。"},{"en":"If people fear all fats, they may miss nutrients needed for skin and cells.","zh":"如果人們害怕所有脂肪，可能錯過皮膚和細胞所需營養。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on adequate intake of healthy fats.","zh":"這個短語強調足夠攝取健康脂肪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"contain vitamins","meaning":"含有維他命","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether most skin creams contain vitamins.","zh":"該陳述問大多數護膚霜是否含有維他命。"},{"en":"To contain vitamins means to include vitamins as ingredients or nutrients.","zh":"含有維他命，指包含維他命作為成分或營養素。"},{"en":"Some breakfast cereals contain vitamins added during production.","zh":"一些早餐穀物含有生產過程中加入的維他命。"},{"en":"If a cream contains vitamins, it may advertise them as skin-care benefits.","zh":"如果護膚霜含有維他命，它可能把這些維他命宣傳為護膚好處。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what is inside a product or food.","zh":"這個短語描述產品或食物內含甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 100 - Do You Look Your Age?.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 101":[{"front":"the fame machine","meaning":"名人製造機制","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes how the fame machine creates and sells modern celebrity.","zh":"文章描述名人製造機制如何創造並出售現代名人。"},{"en":"The fame machine means the system of media, agents, photographers and audiences that produces celebrity.","zh":"the fame machine 指由傳媒、經理人、攝影師和觀眾組成、製造名人的系統。"},{"en":"A singer may become famous not only through music but also through interviews, photos and reality shows.","zh":"歌手成名未必只靠音樂，也可能靠訪問、照片和真人騷。"},{"en":"If the fame machine works well, an ordinary person can become a profitable public figure.","zh":"如果名人製造機制運作良好，普通人也可以變成有利可圖的公眾人物。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that fame is manufactured, managed and sold like a product.","zh":"這個片語暗示名氣像產品一樣被製造、管理和出售。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fascination with","meaning":"對……着迷","examples":[{"en":"Fascination with rich and famous people is universal.","zh":"人們普遍對有錢和著名的人着迷。"},{"en":"Fascination with something means strong interest or attraction toward it.","zh":"fascination with something 指對某事有強烈興趣或吸引感。"},{"en":"Many teenagers have a fascination with pop stars because they seem glamorous and successful.","zh":"許多青少年對流行歌星着迷，因為他們看來有魅力又成功。"},{"en":"If people have a fascination with celebrities, magazines can sell stories about their lives.","zh":"如果人們對名人着迷，雜誌就能出售關於他們生活的故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep curiosity, not just casual interest.","zh":"這個片語描述深層好奇，而不只是普通興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a prolific producer of","meaning":"多產的……製作人","examples":[{"en":"Aaron Spelling was a prolific producer of American soap operas.","zh":"Aaron Spelling 是多產的美國肥皂劇製作人。"},{"en":"A prolific producer of something is someone who creates a large amount of it.","zh":"prolific producer of something 指大量創作某物的人。"},{"en":"A prolific writer may publish several novels and dozens of articles in one year.","zh":"多產作家一年可能出版幾本小說和數十篇文章。"},{"en":"If a producer is prolific, audiences see their work again and again.","zh":"如果製作人多產，觀眾會反覆看到他的作品。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises quantity as well as creative output.","zh":"這個片語強調數量，也強調創作產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"American soap operas","meaning":"美國肥皂劇","examples":[{"en":"Aaron Spelling produced many American soap operas.","zh":"Aaron Spelling 製作了多部美國肥皂劇。"},{"en":"American soap operas are long-running television dramas about relationships, family conflicts and personal problems.","zh":"American soap operas 是關於關係、家庭衝突和個人問題的長篇電視劇。"},{"en":"A soap opera may follow several families in the same town for many years.","zh":"肥皂劇可能多年來追蹤同一城鎮中幾個家庭的生活。"},{"en":"If audiences enjoy emotional twists, soap operas can keep them watching daily.","zh":"如果觀眾喜歡情感轉折，肥皂劇可以令他們每天追看。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a popular type of American television drama.","zh":"這個片語指一種受歡迎的美國電視劇類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rich people having problems that money can’t solve","meaning":"有錢也解決不了問題的富人","examples":[{"en":"Some audiences enjoy stories about rich people having problems that money can’t solve.","zh":"有些觀眾喜歡關於有錢也解決不了問題的富人的故事。"},{"en":"Rich people having problems that money can’t solve refers to wealthy people facing emotional, family or moral troubles.","zh":"rich people having problems that money can’t solve 指富人面對情感、家庭或道德困難。"},{"en":"A millionaire may still feel lonely if their children refuse to speak to them.","zh":"如果子女拒絕與他說話，百萬富翁仍可能感到孤獨。"},{"en":"If money cannot fix betrayal or illness, viewers may feel that rich people are human too.","zh":"如果金錢不能解決背叛或疾病，觀眾可能覺得富人也很人性化。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that wealth does not remove every difficulty.","zh":"這個片語顯示財富不能消除所有困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be universal","meaning":"普遍存在","examples":[{"en":"Fascination with celebrity problems is universal.","zh":"人們對名人問題的着迷普遍存在。"},{"en":"To be universal means to exist or be found everywhere or among almost everyone.","zh":"be universal 指到處存在，或幾乎所有人都有。"},{"en":"The need for friendship is universal, even though people express it differently.","zh":"對友誼的需要是普遍存在的，雖然不同人表達方式不同。"},{"en":"If a feeling is universal, stories about it can attract audiences across cultures.","zh":"如果某種感受是普遍的，關於它的故事就能吸引不同文化的觀眾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something common to people generally.","zh":"這個片語描述人類普遍共有的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"star-struck Britain","meaning":"崇拜明星的英國","examples":[{"en":"Star-struck Britain has a powerful fascination with celebrities.","zh":"崇拜明星的英國對名人有強烈着迷。"},{"en":"Star-struck Britain means Britain is strongly attracted to famous people and celebrity culture.","zh":"star-struck Britain 指英國強烈受名人和明星文化吸引。"},{"en":"A star-struck teenager may queue for hours just to see a singer for ten seconds.","zh":"崇拜明星的青少年可能排隊幾小時，只為看歌手十秒。"},{"en":"If a society is star-struck, celebrity news may become more important than serious news.","zh":"如果社會崇拜明星，名人新聞可能變得比嚴肅新聞更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a culture impressed by fame and glamour.","zh":"這個片語描述被名氣和魅力吸引的文化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have no equal","meaning":"無與倫比；無可匹敵","examples":[{"en":"Britain’s fascination with celebrity has no equal.","zh":"英國對名人的着迷無與倫比。"},{"en":"To have no equal means to be unmatched or greater than all others in a particular respect.","zh":"have no equal 指在某方面無人或無物能相比。"},{"en":"In a small school, one student’s speaking confidence may have no equal.","zh":"在小學校中，某學生的口語自信可能無可匹敵。"},{"en":"If a magazine’s sales have no equal, competitors may copy its style.","zh":"如果雜誌銷量無與倫比，競爭者可能模仿其風格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that stands above all comparisons.","zh":"這個片語描述某事物高於所有比較對象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a profusion of","meaning":"大量；眾多","examples":[{"en":"The country has a profusion of titles about celebrities.","zh":"該國有大量關於名人的刊物。"},{"en":"A profusion of something means a very large number or great abundance of it.","zh":"a profusion of something 指某物數量非常多或極豐富。"},{"en":"A supermarket may have a profusion of snacks near the checkout.","zh":"超級市場收銀處附近可能有大量零食。"},{"en":"If there is a profusion of celebrity magazines, readers can choose from many similar products.","zh":"如果有大量名人雜誌，讀者可以從許多相似產品中選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses abundance, sometimes more than necessary.","zh":"這個片語強調豐富，有時甚至多於需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"titles devoted to","meaning":"專門報道……的刊物","examples":[{"en":"Britain has many titles devoted to celebrity news.","zh":"英國有許多專門報道名人新聞的刊物。"},{"en":"Titles devoted to a topic are magazines, newspapers or publications focused mainly on that topic.","zh":"titles devoted to a topic 是主要聚焦某主題的雜誌、報紙或出版物。"},{"en":"A bookshop may have several titles devoted to cooking, travel or business.","zh":"書店可能有幾本專門關於烹飪、旅遊或商業的刊物。"},{"en":"If many titles are devoted to celebrity news, the market for gossip is clearly strong.","zh":"如果許多刊物專門報道名人新聞，八卦市場顯然很強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes publications built around a particular subject.","zh":"這個片語描述圍繞特定主題建立的出版物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"chronicling the doings of celebrities","meaning":"記錄名人的動態","examples":[{"en":"Many magazines are devoted to chronicling the doings of celebrities.","zh":"許多雜誌專門記錄名人的動態。"},{"en":"Chronicling the doings of celebrities means recording and reporting what famous people do.","zh":"chronicling the doings of celebrities 指記錄和報道名人做過的事情。"},{"en":"A fan account may chronicle a singer’s concerts, outfits and interviews.","zh":"粉絲帳戶可能記錄歌手的演唱會、服裝和訪問。"},{"en":"If magazines chronicle every movement of celebrities, private life becomes public entertainment.","zh":"如果雜誌記錄名人的每個動作，私生活就變成公共娛樂。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests detailed, continuous reporting of celebrity behaviour.","zh":"這個片語暗示對名人行為作詳細而持續的報道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the smallest doings of","meaning":"……最細微的動態","examples":[{"en":"Some magazines report even the smallest doings of celebrities.","zh":"一些雜誌甚至報道名人最細微的動態。"},{"en":"The smallest doings of someone means tiny, ordinary actions that are usually not important.","zh":"the smallest doings of someone 指某人細小而普通、通常不重要的行動。"},{"en":"A gossip page may report what a celebrity ate for lunch or bought at a shop.","zh":"八卦版可能報道名人午餐吃了甚麼，或在商店買了甚麼。"},{"en":"If readers want even tiny details, magazines can turn ordinary moments into news.","zh":"如果讀者連微小細節都想知道，雜誌可以把普通時刻變成新聞。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests excessive attention to minor actions.","zh":"這個片語暗示對小事過度關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"almost half as many...as","meaning":"數量接近……的一半","examples":[{"en":"Britons buy almost half as many celebrity magazines as Americans do.","zh":"英國人購買的名人雜誌數量接近美國人的一半。"},{"en":"Almost half as many A as B means the number of A is nearly half the number of B.","zh":"almost half as many A as B 指 A 的數量接近 B 的一半。"},{"en":"Our class borrowed almost half as many library books as the whole year group borrowed.","zh":"我們班借閱的圖書數量接近整個年級的一半。"},{"en":"If a smaller country buys almost half as many magazines as a bigger country, demand per person may be high.","zh":"如果較小國家購買的雜誌數量接近較大國家的一半，人均需求可能很高。"},{"en":"This phrase compares quantities between two groups.","zh":"這個片語比較兩個群體之間的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"celebrity magazines","meaning":"名人雜誌","examples":[{"en":"Britons buy many celebrity magazines.","zh":"英國人購買許多名人雜誌。"},{"en":"Celebrity magazines are magazines focused on famous people’s relationships, clothes, homes and scandals.","zh":"celebrity magazines 是聚焦名人關係、衣着、家居和醜聞的雜誌。"},{"en":"A hair salon may keep celebrity magazines for customers waiting for appointments.","zh":"髮型屋可能放置名人雜誌，供等候預約的顧客閱讀。"},{"en":"If readers enjoy gossip, celebrity magazines can sell stories about weddings and breakups.","zh":"如果讀者喜歡八卦，名人雜誌可以出售婚禮和分手故事。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to publications built around famous people’s private and public lives.","zh":"這個片語指出圍繞名人私生活和公眾生活的刊物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"despite having","meaning":"儘管擁有……","examples":[{"en":"Britons buy many celebrity magazines despite having a much smaller population.","zh":"英國人儘管人口少得多，仍購買許多名人雜誌。"},{"en":"Despite having means although someone or something has a particular condition.","zh":"despite having 指雖然某人或某事擁有某種情況。"},{"en":"A student may speak confidently despite having little preparation time.","zh":"學生儘管準備時間很少，仍可能自信發言。"},{"en":"If a small country buys many magazines despite having fewer people, interest is especially strong.","zh":"如果小國儘管人口較少仍購買許多雜誌，興趣就特別強烈。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast between expectation and reality.","zh":"這個片語引入預期與現實之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"one fifth the size","meaning":"五分之一大小","examples":[{"en":"Britain’s population is only one fifth the size of America’s.","zh":"英國人口只有美國人口的五分之一大小。"},{"en":"One fifth the size means only twenty percent as large as something else.","zh":"one fifth the size 指只有另一物的百分之二十大小。"},{"en":"A small classroom may be one fifth the size of the school hall.","zh":"小課室可能只有學校禮堂的五分之一大小。"},{"en":"If a market is one fifth the size but buys many products, demand per person is high.","zh":"如果市場只有五分之一大小卻購買許多產品，人均需求就很高。"},{"en":"This phrase compares size or population using a fraction.","zh":"這個片語用分數比較大小或人口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"celebrity news","meaning":"名人新聞","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity news often appears in British tabloids.","zh":"名人新聞常出現在英國小報中。"},{"en":"Celebrity news is news about famous people’s careers, relationships, appearances and private lives.","zh":"celebrity news 是關於名人事業、關係、外表和私生活的新聞。"},{"en":"A website may post celebrity news every morning to attract quick clicks.","zh":"網站可能每天早上發布名人新聞，以吸引快速點擊。"},{"en":"If celebrity news sells well, newspapers may give it more space than political stories.","zh":"如果名人新聞銷量好，報紙可能給它比政治新聞更多篇幅。"},{"en":"This phrase describes news focused on famous people.","zh":"這個片語描述聚焦名人的新聞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"make the front page of","meaning":"登上……頭版","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity news often makes the front page of British tabloid newspapers.","zh":"名人新聞常登上英國小報頭版。"},{"en":"To make the front page of a newspaper means to be important enough to appear on its first page.","zh":"make the front page of a newspaper 指重要到足以刊登在報紙第一版。"},{"en":"A school sports victory may make the front page of a local newspaper.","zh":"學校體育勝利可能登上本地報紙頭版。"},{"en":"If a celebrity scandal makes the front page, millions of readers may notice it immediately.","zh":"如果名人醜聞登上頭版，數百萬讀者可能立即注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving highly visible newspaper coverage.","zh":"這個片語描述獲得非常顯眼的報紙報道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tabloid newspapers","meaning":"小報","examples":[{"en":"British tabloid newspapers often carry stories about celebrities.","zh":"英國小報常刊登關於名人的報道。"},{"en":"Tabloid newspapers are newspapers with short, dramatic stories, large headlines and a focus on popular topics.","zh":"tabloid newspapers 是使用短篇誇張報道、大標題並聚焦大眾話題的報紙。"},{"en":"A tabloid may report a celebrity breakup with a huge headline and many photos.","zh":"小報可能用巨大標題和大量照片報道名人分手。"},{"en":"If tabloids compete for attention, stories may become more dramatic.","zh":"如果小報爭奪注意力，報道可能變得更誇張。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a popular newspaper format often linked with gossip and sensation.","zh":"這個片語指常與八卦和煽情相關的大眾報紙形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"provide a formidable distribution channel for","meaning":"為……提供強大的發行渠道","examples":[{"en":"Tabloid newspapers provide a formidable distribution channel for celebrity stories.","zh":"小報為名人報道提供強大的發行渠道。"},{"en":"To provide a formidable distribution channel for something means to give it a powerful way to reach many people.","zh":"provide a formidable distribution channel for something 指為某事提供接觸大量人群的強大方式。"},{"en":"Social media provides a formidable distribution channel for short videos.","zh":"社交媒體為短片提供強大的發行渠道。"},{"en":"If newspapers print celebrity stories daily, gossip can spread quickly across the country.","zh":"如果報紙每天刊登名人故事，八卦可以迅速傳遍全國。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong system for delivering content to an audience.","zh":"這個片語描述把內容傳送給觀眾的強大系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stories about celebrities","meaning":"關於名人的報道","examples":[{"en":"Tabloids provide a channel for stories about celebrities.","zh":"小報為關於名人的報道提供渠道。"},{"en":"Stories about celebrities are reports or articles about famous people’s lives and actions.","zh":"stories about celebrities 是關於名人生活和行動的報道或文章。"},{"en":"A magazine may publish stories about celebrities’ holidays, weddings or family problems.","zh":"雜誌可能刊登關於名人假期、婚禮或家庭問題的報道。"},{"en":"If these stories attract readers, publishers can sell more magazines and advertisements.","zh":"如果這些報道吸引讀者，出版商可以賣出更多雜誌和廣告。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to celebrity-focused media content.","zh":"這個片語指聚焦名人的媒體內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"new figures from","meaning":"來自……的新數字","examples":[{"en":"New figures from the Audit Bureau of Circulations show strong magazine sales.","zh":"來自發行量審計機構的新數字顯示雜誌銷量強勁。"},{"en":"New figures from a source are recently released numbers or statistics from that organisation.","zh":"new figures from a source 是某機構最近發布的數字或統計資料。"},{"en":"New figures from the school office may show that more students are joining clubs.","zh":"來自學校辦公室的新數字可能顯示更多學生加入社團。"},{"en":"If new figures show rising sales, companies may invest more in that market.","zh":"如果新數字顯示銷量上升，公司可能在該市場投資更多。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces fresh statistical evidence.","zh":"這個片語引入新的統計證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the Audit Bureau of Circulations","meaning":"Audit Bureau of Circulations；發行量審計機構","examples":[{"en":"The Audit Bureau of Circulations released figures about publication sales.","zh":"發行量審計機構發布了關於出版物銷量的數字。"},{"en":"The Audit Bureau of Circulations is an organisation that checks and reports circulation figures for publications.","zh":"Audit Bureau of Circulations 是核查並報告出版物發行量數字的機構。"},{"en":"Advertisers may look at circulation figures before buying space in a magazine.","zh":"廣告商在購買雜誌廣告位前，可能查看發行量數字。"},{"en":"If audited figures are high, a publication can claim strong market reach.","zh":"如果經審計數字很高，刊物就可以聲稱市場覆蓋力強。"},{"en":"This phrase names a body connected with publication sales data.","zh":"這個片語指出與出版物銷售數據相關的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"best-selling celebrity publications","meaning":"最暢銷的名人刊物","examples":[{"en":"The figures include the ten best-selling celebrity publications.","zh":"這些數字包括十本最暢銷的名人刊物。"},{"en":"Best-selling celebrity publications are celebrity magazines or papers with the highest sales.","zh":"best-selling celebrity publications 是銷量最高的名人雜誌或報紙。"},{"en":"A shop may place best-selling magazines near the entrance to attract buyers.","zh":"商店可能把最暢銷雜誌放在入口附近吸引買家。"},{"en":"If a publication is best-selling, rival publishers may copy its layout or tone.","zh":"如果刊物最暢銷，競爭出版商可能模仿其版面或語氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the most commercially successful celebrity titles.","zh":"這個片語描述商業上最成功的名人刊物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"most popular tabloids","meaning":"最受歡迎的小報","examples":[{"en":"The figures include the ten most popular tabloids.","zh":"這些數字包括十份最受歡迎的小報。"},{"en":"The most popular tabloids are tabloid newspapers with the largest readership or sales.","zh":"most popular tabloids 是讀者或銷量最多的小報。"},{"en":"A commuter may see the most popular tabloids at every train-station shop.","zh":"通勤者可能在每個火車站商店都看到最受歡迎的小報。"},{"en":"If popular tabloids focus on celebrities, celebrity stories reach huge audiences.","zh":"如果受歡迎小報聚焦名人，名人故事就能接觸龐大觀眾。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies widely read sensational newspapers.","zh":"這個片語指出被廣泛閱讀的煽情報紙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"combined circulation","meaning":"總發行量","examples":[{"en":"The publications have a combined circulation of 23 million.","zh":"這些刊物總發行量達二千三百萬。"},{"en":"Combined circulation is the total number of copies distributed by several publications together.","zh":"combined circulation 是幾份刊物合計發行的總份數。"},{"en":"Three school newsletters may have a combined circulation of 5,000 copies.","zh":"三份學校通訊的總發行量可能有五千份。"},{"en":"If combined circulation is huge, advertisers see a large potential audience.","zh":"如果總發行量很大，廣告商會看到龐大潛在受眾。"},{"en":"This phrase adds several circulation figures into one total.","zh":"這個片語把幾個發行量數字加成一個總數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"satisfy this voracious demand","meaning":"滿足這種龐大需求","examples":[{"en":"The industry tries to satisfy this voracious demand for celebrity news.","zh":"這個行業試圖滿足這種對名人新聞的龐大需求。"},{"en":"To satisfy this voracious demand means to meet a very strong and continuing desire for something.","zh":"satisfy this voracious demand 指滿足對某物非常強烈而持續的渴望。"},{"en":"A café may open earlier to satisfy strong demand for breakfast near an office district.","zh":"咖啡店可能提早開門，以滿足辦公區附近對早餐的強烈需求。"},{"en":"If readers constantly want new celebrity stories, publishers must produce content quickly.","zh":"如果讀者不斷想看新名人故事，出版商就必須快速生產內容。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that demand is hungry and hard to fill.","zh":"這個片語暗示需求很飢渴且難以填滿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"voracious demand","meaning":"巨大而強烈的需求","examples":[{"en":"There is a voracious demand for celebrity stories in Britain.","zh":"英國對名人故事有巨大而強烈的需求。"},{"en":"Voracious demand means an extremely strong appetite for something.","zh":"voracious demand 指對某物極強烈的需求。"},{"en":"During exam season, there may be a voracious demand for practice papers and marking services.","zh":"考試季期間，練習卷和批改服務可能有巨大需求。"},{"en":"If demand is voracious, suppliers may produce more even if quality falls.","zh":"如果需求強烈，供應者可能生產更多，即使質素下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intense, almost hungry demand.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈得近乎飢餓的需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"turn something into","meaning":"把……變成","examples":[{"en":"This demand has turned celebrity reporting into a major industry.","zh":"這種需求已把名人報道變成一個主要行業。"},{"en":"To turn something into something else means to change it into a different form or state.","zh":"turn something into something else 指把某物改變成另一種形式或狀態。"},{"en":"A hobby can turn into a business if many people are willing to pay for it.","zh":"如果許多人願意付費，興趣可以變成生意。"},{"en":"If gossip turns into an industry, it becomes organised, profitable and professional.","zh":"如果八卦變成行業，它就會變得有組織、有利可圖和專業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transformation.","zh":"這個片語描述轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what was once","meaning":"曾經是……的東西","examples":[{"en":"What was once an amateurish business has become an industry.","zh":"曾經是業餘生意的東西，已變成一個行業。"},{"en":"What was once means something that used to be true in the past.","zh":"what was once 指過去曾經如此的事物。"},{"en":"What was once a quiet village may become a busy tourist town.","zh":"曾經是寧靜村莊的地方，可能變成繁忙旅遊城鎮。"},{"en":"If what was once informal becomes commercial, rules and profits may appear.","zh":"如果曾經非正式的事物變成商業活動，規則和利潤可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the past with the present.","zh":"這個片語把過去與現在作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a shoddy, amateurish business","meaning":"粗劣而業餘的行業","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity reporting was once a shoddy, amateurish business.","zh":"名人報道曾經是一個粗劣而業餘的行業。"},{"en":"A shoddy, amateurish business is poorly made, badly organised and not professionally run.","zh":"shoddy, amateurish business 指質素差、組織差且不專業經營的行業。"},{"en":"A school event may look amateurish if no one plans the sound, signs or seating.","zh":"如果沒有人安排音響、指示牌或座位，學校活動可能顯得業餘。"},{"en":"If a business becomes profitable, it may move from shoddy work to professional systems.","zh":"如果生意變得有利可圖，它可能從粗劣工作轉向專業系統。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises low-quality, unprofessional work.","zh":"這個片語批評低質素、不專業的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"an entertainment industry in its own right","meaning":"本身就是一個娛樂產業","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity journalism has become an entertainment industry in its own right.","zh":"名人新聞本身已成為一個娛樂產業。"},{"en":"An industry in its own right is important and independent enough to be considered separately.","zh":"industry in its own right 指某領域已重要和獨立到可被單獨看待。"},{"en":"Online gaming has become an entertainment industry in its own right.","zh":"網上遊戲本身已成為一個娛樂產業。"},{"en":"If celebrity reporting makes money by itself, it no longer only supports films or music.","zh":"如果名人報道本身賺錢，它就不再只是支援電影或音樂。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something has become a full independent field.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事已成為完整獨立領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"business model","meaning":"商業模式","examples":[{"en":"The celebrity industry has a distinctive business model.","zh":"名人產業有一種獨特商業模式。"},{"en":"A business model is the way a company or industry creates value and earns money.","zh":"business model 是公司或行業創造價值並賺錢的方式。"},{"en":"A tutoring centre’s business model may depend on hourly lessons and exam packages.","zh":"補習中心的商業模式可能依賴按小時計算的課堂和考試套裝。"},{"en":"If a magazine earns money from celebrity photos, advertising and exclusives, that is part of its business model.","zh":"如果雜誌靠名人照片、廣告和獨家報道賺錢，那就是其商業模式的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how an activity becomes profitable.","zh":"這個片語解釋活動如何變得有利可圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"distinguishing features","meaning":"鮮明特點","examples":[{"en":"Its business model has two distinguishing features.","zh":"其商業模式有兩個鮮明特點。"},{"en":"Distinguishing features are qualities that make something different from others.","zh":"distinguishing features 是令某物與其他事物不同的特質。"},{"en":"A good language course may have two distinguishing features: clear feedback and realistic practice.","zh":"好語言課程可能有兩個鮮明特點：清晰回饋和真實練習。"},{"en":"If a product has no distinguishing features, customers may not notice it.","zh":"如果產品沒有鮮明特點，顧客可能不會注意到它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes characteristics that set something apart.","zh":"這個片語描述令某物突出的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"celebrity has become the product","meaning":"名人本身成為產品","examples":[{"en":"In this industry, celebrity has become the product.","zh":"在這個行業中，名人本身成為產品。"},{"en":"Celebrity has become the product means fame itself is what is bought, sold and packaged.","zh":"celebrity has become the product 指名氣本身就是被購買、出售和包裝的東西。"},{"en":"A reality-show contestant may sell interviews, photos and personal drama instead of a traditional skill.","zh":"真人騷參賽者可能出售訪問、照片和個人戲劇，而不是傳統技能。"},{"en":"If celebrity is the product, private life can become a source of income.","zh":"如果名人本身是產品，私生活就可以成為收入來源。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that fame can be commercialised directly.","zh":"這個片語顯示名氣可以被直接商品化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rather than just","meaning":"而不只是……","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity is the product rather than just a marketing device.","zh":"名人本身是產品，而不只是市場推廣手段。"},{"en":"Rather than just means not merely one thing, but something more important or different.","zh":"rather than just 指不僅僅是某物，而是更重要或不同的東西。"},{"en":"A school library should be a learning space rather than just a room with books.","zh":"學校圖書館應是學習空間，而不只是放書的房間。"},{"en":"If celebrity is more than promotion, magazines can sell fame itself.","zh":"如果名人不只是宣傳，雜誌就能出售名氣本身。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a contrast between a limited role and a larger role.","zh":"這個片語突出有限角色與更大角色之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a device for marketing","meaning":"用於推銷……的手段","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity used to be a device for marketing films or music.","zh":"名人過去是用於推銷電影或音樂的手段。"},{"en":"A device for marketing is a tool or method used to promote and sell something.","zh":"device for marketing 是用來推廣和銷售某物的工具或方法。"},{"en":"A famous athlete may be used as a marketing device for sports shoes.","zh":"著名運動員可能被用作推銷運動鞋的手段。"},{"en":"If celebrity only markets a film, fame supports another product rather than being the product itself.","zh":"如果名人只是推銷電影，名氣就是支援另一產品，而不是產品本身。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a promotional tool.","zh":"這個片語描述宣傳工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"owe its standing chiefly to","meaning":"主要靠……取得地位","examples":[{"en":"The talent owes its standing chiefly to the celebrity machine.","zh":"這名藝人主要靠名人製造機器取得地位。"},{"en":"To owe its standing chiefly to something means to gain its position mainly because of that thing.","zh":"owe its standing chiefly to something 指其地位主要由某事帶來。"},{"en":"A restaurant may owe its popularity chiefly to social media rather than food quality.","zh":"餐廳可能主要靠社交媒體而不是食物質素而受歡迎。"},{"en":"If someone owes fame to publicity, their status may depend on continued media attention.","zh":"如果某人靠宣傳成名，其地位可能依賴持續媒體關注。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the main source of status.","zh":"這個片語解釋地位的主要來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the celebrity machine","meaning":"名人製造機器","examples":[{"en":"The celebrity machine helps people become famous.","zh":"名人製造機器幫助人們成名。"},{"en":"The celebrity machine is the organised media and business system that creates, promotes and profits from fame.","zh":"celebrity machine 是創造、推廣並從名氣中獲利的有組織媒體和商業系統。"},{"en":"Reality shows, photographers, agents and magazines can all be parts of the celebrity machine.","zh":"真人騷、攝影師、經理人和雜誌都可以是名人製造機器的一部分。"},{"en":"If the celebrity machine promotes someone heavily, public attention can grow quickly.","zh":"如果名人製造機器大力宣傳某人，公眾關注可以迅速增加。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests fame is produced by a system, not only by talent.","zh":"這個片語暗示名氣由系統製造，而不只是由才華帶來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"particular gift","meaning":"特別才華","examples":[{"en":"Some celebrities owe their fame to the press rather than to any particular gift.","zh":"一些名人的名氣來自傳媒，而不是任何特別才華。"},{"en":"A particular gift is a special talent or natural ability.","zh":"particular gift 是特殊才能或天生能力。"},{"en":"A child may have a particular gift for languages if they learn pronunciation quickly.","zh":"如果孩子很快學會發音，他可能有語言方面的特別才華。"},{"en":"If fame comes without a particular gift, people may question why the person is famous.","zh":"如果名氣不是來自特別才華，人們可能質疑此人為何成名。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a recognisable special ability.","zh":"這個片語指可辨認的特殊能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"depend on the attentions of","meaning":"依賴……的關注","examples":[{"en":"Some celebrities depend on the attentions of the press to make money.","zh":"一些名人依賴傳媒關注來賺錢。"},{"en":"To depend on the attentions of someone means to rely on their notice, interest or coverage.","zh":"depend on the attentions of someone 指依靠某人的注意、興趣或報道。"},{"en":"A small café may depend on the attention of food bloggers to attract new customers.","zh":"小咖啡店可能依賴美食博客的關注來吸引新顧客。"},{"en":"If a celebrity depends on press attention, silence from the media can damage their income.","zh":"如果名人依賴傳媒關注，媒體沉默可能損害其收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reliance on being noticed.","zh":"這個片語描述對被注意的依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the press","meaning":"傳媒；新聞界","examples":[{"en":"The press plays a major role in creating celebrity.","zh":"傳媒在創造名人方面扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"The press means newspapers, magazines and news media generally.","zh":"the press 指報紙、雜誌和一般新聞媒體。"},{"en":"A school event may attract the press if a famous speaker attends.","zh":"如果著名講者出席學校活動，該活動可能吸引傳媒。"},{"en":"If the press repeats a story often, public interest can grow quickly.","zh":"如果傳媒經常重複某故事，公眾興趣可以迅速增加。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the media as a reporting institution.","zh":"這個片語指作為報道機構的媒體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"picture desks","meaning":"圖片編輯部","examples":[{"en":"Picture desks help select and sell images of celebrities.","zh":"圖片編輯部幫助選擇和出售名人圖片。"},{"en":"Picture desks are newspaper or magazine teams that choose, edit and manage photographs.","zh":"picture desks 是報紙或雜誌中選擇、編輯和管理照片的團隊。"},{"en":"A picture desk may decide which photo best matches a front-page story.","zh":"圖片編輯部可能決定哪張照片最適合頭版故事。"},{"en":"If picture desks want dramatic images, photographers may compete to capture them.","zh":"如果圖片編輯部想要戲劇性圖片，攝影師可能爭相拍攝。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the photo-editing side of media work.","zh":"這個片語指媒體工作的圖片編輯部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"an endless supply of","meaning":"源源不絕的……供應","examples":[{"en":"The industry creates an endless supply of celebrity news.","zh":"這個行業創造源源不絕的名人新聞供應。"},{"en":"An endless supply of something means a supply that seems never to stop.","zh":"endless supply of something 指看似永不停止的供應。"},{"en":"A busy school office may receive an endless supply of emails every morning.","zh":"繁忙的學校辦公室每天早上可能收到源源不絕的電郵。"},{"en":"If magazines need constant content, they create stories from even tiny events.","zh":"如果雜誌需要不斷有內容，它們會從微小事件中創造故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continuous availability.","zh":"這個片語描述持續可得的供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"work together","meaning":"合作","examples":[{"en":"Celebrities, agents, photographers and picture desks often work together.","zh":"名人、經理人、攝影師和圖片編輯部常常合作。"},{"en":"To work together means to cooperate to achieve a shared result.","zh":"work together 指為達成共同結果而合作。"},{"en":"Teachers and parents work together when they help a student improve behaviour.","zh":"老師和家長幫助學生改善行為時，就是合作。"},{"en":"If celebrities and magazines work together, publicity can be planned rather than accidental.","zh":"如果名人和雜誌合作，宣傳可以被計劃，而不是偶然發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cooperation between different people or groups.","zh":"這個片語描述不同人或群體之間的合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be based on intrusion","meaning":"建基於侵犯私生活","examples":[{"en":"The business used to be based on intrusion into private lives.","zh":"這門生意過去建基於侵犯私生活。"},{"en":"To be based on intrusion means to depend on entering people’s private space or affairs without welcome.","zh":"be based on intrusion 指依賴未經歡迎地進入他人私人空間或事務。"},{"en":"A news story based on intrusion may reveal family details that people wanted to keep private.","zh":"建基於侵犯私隱的新聞故事可能揭露人們想保密的家庭細節。"},{"en":"If a business relies on intrusion, it may damage trust and privacy.","zh":"如果生意依賴侵犯私生活，它可能損害信任和私隱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a business model built on unwanted interference.","zh":"這個片語描述建立在不受歡迎干擾上的商業模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a preference for collaboration","meaning":"對合作的偏好","examples":[{"en":"The industry has discovered a preference for collaboration.","zh":"這個行業發現了對合作的偏好。"},{"en":"A preference for collaboration means people or organisations prefer working together rather than acting separately or secretly.","zh":"preference for collaboration 指人或組織較喜歡合作，而不是分開或秘密行動。"},{"en":"A school may show a preference for collaboration by planning lessons with parents and community groups.","zh":"學校透過與家長和社區團體一起規劃課堂，可能顯示對合作的偏好。"},{"en":"If celebrities cooperate with photographers, both sides can share control and profit.","zh":"如果名人與攝影師合作，雙方都可以分享控制權和利潤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing cooperation as the better method.","zh":"這個片語描述選擇合作作為較好方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"expand abroad","meaning":"向海外擴展","examples":[{"en":"The British celebrity-magazine model is expanding abroad.","zh":"英國名人雜誌模式正在向海外擴展。"},{"en":"To expand abroad means to grow into foreign countries or overseas markets.","zh":"expand abroad 指發展到外國或海外市場。"},{"en":"A tutoring company may expand abroad by offering online lessons to students in other countries.","zh":"補習公司可能透過向其他國家的學生提供網課而向海外擴展。"},{"en":"If a magazine format works well at home, publishers may try it in new markets.","zh":"如果雜誌形式在本地成功，出版商可能在新市場嘗試它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes international business growth.","zh":"這個片語描述國際商業增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in the past few weeks","meaning":"在過去數星期","examples":[{"en":"In the past few weeks, a new American edition has been launched.","zh":"在過去數星期，一個新的美國版本已推出。"},{"en":"In the past few weeks means during the recent period of several weeks before now.","zh":"in the past few weeks 指在現在之前最近幾個星期內。"},{"en":"In the past few weeks, the school has received many applications for the new course.","zh":"在過去數星期，學校收到許多新課程申請。"},{"en":"If many changes happen in a few weeks, the market may be moving quickly.","zh":"如果幾星期內發生許多變化，市場可能正在快速變動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a recent short time period.","zh":"這個片語描述最近一段短時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"launch an American edition of","meaning":"推出……的美國版","examples":[{"en":"Northern & Shell launched an American edition of OK!.","zh":"Northern & Shell 推出了 OK! 的美國版。"},{"en":"To launch an American edition of a publication means to start publishing a version for the American market.","zh":"launch an American edition of a publication 指開始出版面向美國市場的版本。"},{"en":"A magazine may launch an American edition after becoming popular in Britain.","zh":"雜誌在英國受歡迎後，可能推出美國版。"},{"en":"If a title launches overseas, editors may adapt stories, language and celebrities for local readers.","zh":"如果刊物在海外推出，編輯可能為本地讀者調整故事、語言和名人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes introducing a regional version of a publication.","zh":"這個片語描述推出刊物的地區版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"celebrity magazine","meaning":"名人雜誌","examples":[{"en":"OK! is a celebrity magazine with several international editions.","zh":"OK! 是一本有幾個國際版本的名人雜誌。"},{"en":"A celebrity magazine is a magazine mainly about famous people’s lives, photos and relationships.","zh":"celebrity magazine 是主要關於名人生活、照片和關係的雜誌。"},{"en":"A waiting room may keep a celebrity magazine for readers who want light entertainment.","zh":"候診室可能放一本名人雜誌，供想看輕鬆娛樂的讀者閱讀。"},{"en":"If a celebrity magazine gets exclusive photos, sales may rise quickly.","zh":"如果名人雜誌取得獨家照片，銷量可能迅速上升。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a magazine built around fame and gossip.","zh":"這個片語指圍繞名氣和八卦建立的雜誌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Middle Eastern editions","meaning":"中東版本","examples":[{"en":"The magazine already has Australian, Chinese and Middle Eastern editions.","zh":"該雜誌已有澳洲版、中國版和中東版本。"},{"en":"Middle Eastern editions are versions of a publication made for readers in the Middle East.","zh":"Middle Eastern editions 是為中東讀者製作的刊物版本。"},{"en":"A fashion magazine may create Middle Eastern editions with local celebrities and cultural references.","zh":"時裝雜誌可能製作中東版本，加入本地名人和文化元素。"},{"en":"If a magazine enters a new region, it may adjust content to fit local tastes.","zh":"如果雜誌進入新地區，它可能調整內容以配合本地口味。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regional publishing versions for Middle Eastern markets.","zh":"這個片語描述面向中東市場的地區出版版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"publish a South African edition of","meaning":"出版……的南非版","examples":[{"en":"EMAP publishes a South African edition of Heat.","zh":"EMAP 出版 Heat 的南非版。"},{"en":"To publish a South African edition of a magazine means to produce a version for South African readers.","zh":"publish a South African edition of a magazine 指為南非讀者製作一個版本。"},{"en":"A children’s magazine may publish a South African edition with local animals and school stories.","zh":"兒童雜誌可能出版南非版，加入本地動物和校園故事。"},{"en":"If a publication adapts to a country, it may include local celebrities and advertisements.","zh":"如果刊物適應某國市場，它可能加入本地名人和廣告。"},{"en":"This phrase describes publishing a country-specific version.","zh":"這個片語描述出版特定國家版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a best-seller in Britain","meaning":"在英國的暢銷刊物","examples":[{"en":"Heat is a best-seller in Britain.","zh":"Heat 是英國的暢銷刊物。"},{"en":"A best-seller in Britain is a publication or product that sells extremely well in the British market.","zh":"best-seller in Britain 是在英國市場銷售極好的刊物或產品。"},{"en":"A novel may become a best-seller in Britain after winning a major prize.","zh":"小說在贏得重要獎項後，可能成為英國暢銷書。"},{"en":"If a magazine is a best-seller, publishers may try to export the format abroad.","zh":"如果雜誌是暢銷刊物，出版商可能嘗試把形式出口到海外。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong commercial success in Britain.","zh":"這個片語描述在英國的強勁商業成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"celebrity hounds","meaning":"追逐名人新聞的人","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity hounds from Britain are in demand abroad.","zh":"來自英國的追逐名人新聞的人在海外有需求。"},{"en":"Celebrity hounds are journalists or photographers who eagerly chase celebrity stories.","zh":"celebrity hounds 是熱切追逐名人故事的記者或攝影師。"},{"en":"A celebrity hound may wait outside a restaurant to photograph a famous actor.","zh":"追逐名人新聞的人可能在餐廳外等候，拍攝著名演員。"},{"en":"If foreign magazines want sharper gossip, they may hire experienced celebrity hounds.","zh":"如果外國雜誌想要更尖銳八卦，它們可能聘請有經驗的追星記者。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and suggests aggressive pursuit of fame-related news.","zh":"這個片語較口語，暗示積極追逐與名氣相關的新聞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cut their teeth in","meaning":"在……中初試身手；累積早期經驗","examples":[{"en":"Some celebrity journalists cut their teeth in Britain’s competitive market.","zh":"一些名人記者在英國競爭激烈的市場中累積早期經驗。"},{"en":"To cut one’s teeth in a place means to gain early experience and learn practical skills there.","zh":"cut one’s teeth in a place 指在某地獲得早期經驗並學習實用技能。"},{"en":"A young teacher may cut her teeth in a difficult school before moving to a larger role.","zh":"年輕老師可能先在困難學校初試身手，再轉往更大職位。"},{"en":"If journalists learn in a tough market, they may become fast, competitive and resourceful.","zh":"如果記者在艱難市場中學習，他們可能變得快速、有競爭力和機智。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where someone gains their first serious experience.","zh":"這個片語描述某人在哪裡獲得首次重要經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"competitive market","meaning":"競爭激烈的市場","examples":[{"en":"Britain has a competitive celebrity-news market.","zh":"英國有一個競爭激烈的名人新聞市場。"},{"en":"A competitive market is a market where many sellers fight for customers, attention or sales.","zh":"competitive market 是許多賣家爭奪顧客、注意力或銷量的市場。"},{"en":"Tutoring can be a competitive market when many centres offer similar exam courses.","zh":"當許多中心提供相似考試課程時，補習可以是競爭激烈的市場。"},{"en":"If a market is competitive, companies must work harder to stand out.","zh":"如果市場競爭激烈，公司必須更努力突圍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a business environment with strong rivalry.","zh":"這個片語描述有強烈競爭的商業環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be in demand abroad","meaning":"在海外有需求","examples":[{"en":"British celebrity journalists are in demand abroad.","zh":"英國名人記者在海外有需求。"},{"en":"To be in demand abroad means to be wanted by foreign employers, customers or markets.","zh":"be in demand abroad 指受到外國僱主、顧客或市場需要。"},{"en":"Experienced English teachers may be in demand abroad if they can teach online.","zh":"有經驗英文老師如果能網上教學，可能在海外有需求。"},{"en":"If workers have rare skills, companies in other countries may hire them.","zh":"如果工人擁有稀有技能，其他國家的公司可能聘請他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes international demand for people or services.","zh":"這個片語描述對人或服務的國際需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hard-nosed","meaning":"強硬務實的","examples":[{"en":"The National Enquirer is described as a hard-nosed scandal sheet.","zh":"The National Enquirer 被描述為一份強硬務實的醜聞小報。"},{"en":"Hard-nosed means tough, practical and not easily softened by emotion.","zh":"hard-nosed 指強硬、務實且不易受情感影響。"},{"en":"A hard-nosed manager may focus on results even when staff want more flexibility.","zh":"強硬務實的經理可能重視成果，即使員工想要更多彈性。"},{"en":"If a publication is hard-nosed, it may pursue stories aggressively.","zh":"如果刊物強硬務實，它可能積極追查故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a tough and commercially minded attitude.","zh":"這個片語描述強硬且商業導向的態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"scandal sheet","meaning":"專揭醜聞的小報","examples":[{"en":"The National Enquirer is a famous scandal sheet.","zh":"The National Enquirer 是著名的專揭醜聞小報。"},{"en":"A scandal sheet is a newspaper or magazine known for reporting shocking private stories and gossip.","zh":"scandal sheet 是以報道震撼私生活故事和八卦聞名的報紙或雜誌。"},{"en":"A scandal sheet may focus on affairs, arrests and family disputes.","zh":"專揭醜聞的小報可能聚焦婚外情、被捕和家庭糾紛。"},{"en":"If a publication earns money from scandal, it may push ethical limits.","zh":"如果刊物靠醜聞賺錢，它可能挑戰道德界限。"},{"en":"This phrase is critical and suggests sensational reporting.","zh":"這個片語帶批評意味，暗示煽情報道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"famed for","meaning":"以……聞名","examples":[{"en":"The magazine is famed for pushing back the boundaries of taste.","zh":"該雜誌以擴闊品味界限而聞名。"},{"en":"To be famed for something means to be well known for it.","zh":"be famed for something 指因某事而非常有名。"},{"en":"A restaurant may be famed for its handmade noodles.","zh":"餐廳可能以手工麵聞名。"},{"en":"If a magazine is famed for shocking stories, readers expect it to be bold or offensive.","zh":"如果雜誌以震撼故事聞名，讀者會預期它大膽或冒犯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong public reputation.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈公眾聲譽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"push back the boundaries of","meaning":"擴闊……的界限","examples":[{"en":"The magazine pushed back the boundaries of taste and free speech.","zh":"該雜誌擴闊了品味和言論自由的界限。"},{"en":"To push back the boundaries of something means to extend what is considered possible or acceptable.","zh":"push back the boundaries of something 指擴展被認為可能或可接受的範圍。"},{"en":"A filmmaker may push back the boundaries of documentary by mixing real interviews with animation.","zh":"電影製作人可能透過混合真實訪問和動畫，擴闊紀錄片界限。"},{"en":"If a publication pushes boundaries too far, it may offend readers or face legal trouble.","zh":"如果刊物過度挑戰界限，可能冒犯讀者或面對法律麻煩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes testing or expanding limits.","zh":"這個片語描述測試或擴展限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the boundaries of taste","meaning":"品味的界限","examples":[{"en":"The magazine challenged the boundaries of taste.","zh":"該雜誌挑戰了品味的界限。"},{"en":"The boundaries of taste are the limits of what people consider acceptable, decent or not offensive.","zh":"boundaries of taste 是人們認為可接受、得體或不冒犯的界限。"},{"en":"A joke may cross the boundaries of taste if it mocks tragedy.","zh":"如果笑話嘲諷悲劇，它可能越過品味的界限。"},{"en":"If media companies chase attention, they may test how much shock audiences will accept.","zh":"如果媒體公司追逐注意力，它們可能測試觀眾能接受多少震撼內容。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social limits on good judgement and decency.","zh":"這個片語描述良好判斷和得體程度上的社會限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"free speech","meaning":"言論自由","examples":[{"en":"The magazine also tested the boundaries of free speech.","zh":"該雜誌也測試了言論自由的界限。"},{"en":"Free speech is the right to express opinions without unfair censorship or punishment.","zh":"free speech 是表達意見而不受不公平審查或懲罰的權利。"},{"en":"Students practise free speech when they debate school policies respectfully.","zh":"學生尊重地辯論校政時，就是實踐言論自由。"},{"en":"If speech harms privacy or spreads lies, society may argue about its limits.","zh":"如果言論傷害私隱或散播謊言，社會可能爭論其限制。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to freedom of expression.","zh":"這個片語指表達自由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be relaunched","meaning":"重新推出","examples":[{"en":"The National Enquirer was relaunched by a British-led team.","zh":"The National Enquirer 由一支英國人帶領的團隊重新推出。"},{"en":"To be relaunched means to be introduced again with a new style, team or strategy.","zh":"be relaunched 指以新風格、團隊或策略再次推出。"},{"en":"A school website may be relaunched with clearer menus and better photos.","zh":"學校網站可能以更清晰選單和更好照片重新推出。"},{"en":"If a magazine is relaunched, publishers hope to attract new readers or revive sales.","zh":"如果雜誌重新推出，出版商希望吸引新讀者或重振銷量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fresh public restart.","zh":"這個片語描述新的公開重啟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a team led by","meaning":"由……帶領的團隊","examples":[{"en":"The magazine was relaunched by a team led by Paul Field.","zh":"該雜誌由 Paul Field 帶領的團隊重新推出。"},{"en":"A team led by someone is a group directed or managed by that person.","zh":"team led by someone 是由某人指揮或管理的小組。"},{"en":"A project team led by an experienced teacher may organise a school fair smoothly.","zh":"由有經驗老師帶領的項目團隊，可能順利組織學校市集。"},{"en":"If a team is led by someone from a successful newspaper, its style may reflect that background.","zh":"如果團隊由成功報紙出身的人帶領，其風格可能反映該背景。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the leader of a group.","zh":"這個片語指出團隊領袖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"formerly of","meaning":"以前任職於……","examples":[{"en":"Paul Field was formerly of The Sun.","zh":"Paul Field 以前任職於 The Sun。"},{"en":"Formerly of an organisation means someone previously worked for or belonged to that organisation.","zh":"formerly of an organisation 指某人以前在某機構工作或屬於該機構。"},{"en":"A coach formerly of a famous club may bring new methods to a school team.","zh":"以前任職於著名球會的教練，可能為學校球隊帶來新方法。"},{"en":"If an editor is formerly of a tabloid, their experience may shape a new magazine.","zh":"如果編輯以前任職小報，其經驗可能塑造新雜誌。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a person’s past professional connection.","zh":"這個片語交代某人過往職業關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be stuffed with","meaning":"充滿；大量加入","examples":[{"en":"The relaunched magazine was stuffed with alumni of British tabloids.","zh":"重新推出的雜誌充滿英國小報前員工。"},{"en":"To be stuffed with something means to be filled with a large number of it.","zh":"be stuffed with something 指大量充滿某物或某類人。"},{"en":"A classroom noticeboard may be stuffed with posters before open day.","zh":"開放日前，課室壁報板可能貼滿海報。"},{"en":"If a newsroom is stuffed with tabloid veterans, its reporting style may become more aggressive.","zh":"如果新聞編輯室充滿小報老手，其報道風格可能變得更進取。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a place or group is packed full of something.","zh":"這個片語暗示某地方或群體擠滿某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"alumni of","meaning":"……的前成員；前員工","examples":[{"en":"The team included alumni of British tabloids and magazines.","zh":"該團隊包括英國小報和雜誌的前員工。"},{"en":"Alumni of an organisation are former members, students or employees of it.","zh":"alumni of an organisation 是某機構的前成員、畢業生或前員工。"},{"en":"Alumni of a school may return to give career talks to students.","zh":"學校校友可能回校為學生作職業講座。"},{"en":"If a new company hires alumni of famous newspapers, it gains their experience and contacts.","zh":"如果新公司聘請著名報紙前員工，就能獲得他們的經驗和人脈。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people who previously belonged to a group.","zh":"這個片語指曾經屬於某群體的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"celebrity magazines were not a British invention","meaning":"名人雜誌並非英國發明","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity magazines were not a British invention.","zh":"名人雜誌並非英國發明。"},{"en":"This sentence means Britain did not create the idea of magazines about famous people.","zh":"這句話意思是，英國並沒有創造關於名人的雜誌這個概念。"},{"en":"A popular idea can become strongly associated with one country even if it began elsewhere.","zh":"一個受歡迎想法即使起源於別處，也可能與某個國家強烈連結。"},{"en":"If celebrity magazines existed earlier in Spain or America, Britain developed rather than invented the form.","zh":"如果名人雜誌更早存在於西班牙或美國，英國只是發展而非發明這種形式。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects a possible misunderstanding about origin.","zh":"這個片語糾正關於起源的可能誤解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"widely read","meaning":"被廣泛閱讀","examples":[{"en":"Hello! is still widely read.","zh":"Hello! 仍然被廣泛閱讀。"},{"en":"Widely read means read by many people in many places or groups.","zh":"widely read 指被許多地方或群體的人閱讀。"},{"en":"A school newsletter may become widely read if it includes useful exam tips.","zh":"如果學校通訊包含有用考試貼士，它可能被廣泛閱讀。"},{"en":"If a magazine is widely read, advertisers may be willing to pay more.","zh":"如果雜誌被廣泛閱讀，廣告商可能願意支付更多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad readership.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛讀者群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"wane of late","meaning":"近來逐漸衰落","examples":[{"en":"Hello! has been waning of late.","zh":"Hello! 近來逐漸衰落。"},{"en":"To wane of late means to become weaker or less popular recently.","zh":"wane of late 指最近變弱或變得較不受歡迎。"},{"en":"Interest in a once-popular game may wane of late when students move to new apps.","zh":"當學生轉向新應用程式，一款曾經流行的遊戲興趣可能近來逐漸衰落。"},{"en":"If a magazine’s popularity wanes, publishers may redesign it to win readers back.","zh":"如果雜誌受歡迎程度下降，出版商可能重新設計以挽回讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recent decline.","zh":"這個片語描述近期衰退。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"originate in","meaning":"起源於……","examples":[{"en":"Hello! originated in Spain.","zh":"Hello! 起源於西班牙。"},{"en":"To originate in a place means to begin or first develop there.","zh":"originate in a place 指在某地開始或最初發展。"},{"en":"A food tradition may originate in one village before spreading to the whole country.","zh":"一種飲食傳統可能起源於一條村，然後傳遍全國。"},{"en":"If a magazine format originates abroad, local versions may later adapt it.","zh":"如果雜誌形式起源於海外，本地版本日後可能加以改編。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where something began.","zh":"這個片語指出某事始於何處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"provide a hint of glamour to","meaning":"為……帶來一絲魅力","examples":[{"en":"Hola! provided a hint of glamour to women under Franco’s rule.","zh":"Hola! 為佛朗哥統治下的女性帶來一絲魅力。"},{"en":"To provide a hint of glamour to someone means to give them a small taste of elegance, beauty or exciting celebrity life.","zh":"provide a hint of glamour to someone 指給某人一點優雅、美感或刺激名人生活的感覺。"},{"en":"A bright window display can provide a hint of glamour to an ordinary shopping street.","zh":"明亮櫥窗展示可以為普通購物街帶來一絲魅力。"},{"en":"If daily life feels dull, glamorous magazines can offer readers escape and fantasy.","zh":"如果日常生活沉悶，華麗雜誌可以為讀者提供逃避和幻想。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a small but attractive touch of luxury.","zh":"這個片語暗示一點吸引人的奢華感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a hint of glamour","meaning":"一絲光彩；一點魅力","examples":[{"en":"The magazine offered a hint of glamour during a drab period.","zh":"該雜誌在沉悶時期提供了一絲光彩。"},{"en":"A hint of glamour is a small touch of elegance, excitement or luxury.","zh":"hint of glamour 是一點優雅、刺激或奢華感。"},{"en":"A simple dress may gain a hint of glamour with one beautiful necklace.","zh":"簡單裙子配上一條漂亮項鏈後，可能多了一點魅力。"},{"en":"If people live through hard times, even a small sign of glamour can feel attractive.","zh":"如果人們經歷艱難時期，即使一點光彩也會感到吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase means a little brightness in an otherwise plain situation.","zh":"這個片語指在平淡情況中的一點亮色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"under Franco’s drab reign","meaning":"在佛朗哥沉悶的統治下","examples":[{"en":"Hola! appeared under Franco’s drab reign.","zh":"Hola! 出現在佛朗哥沉悶的統治下。"},{"en":"Under Franco’s drab reign means during the dull and restrictive period when Franco ruled Spain.","zh":"under Franco’s drab reign 指在佛朗哥統治西班牙的沉悶而受限制時期。"},{"en":"Under a strict school principal, even small student clubs may feel controlled.","zh":"在嚴格校長管理下，即使小型學生社團也可能感到受控制。"},{"en":"If people live under a dull regime, colourful media may feel like escape.","zh":"如果人們生活在沉悶政權下，色彩繽紛的媒體可能像一種逃避。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a publication with a particular political period.","zh":"這個片語把刊物與特定政治時期連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"grow up around","meaning":"圍繞……發展起來","examples":[{"en":"Some magazines grew up around the film industry in America.","zh":"一些雜誌圍繞美國電影業發展起來。"},{"en":"To grow up around something means to develop alongside it and depend on it.","zh":"grow up around something 指與某事一起發展並依靠它。"},{"en":"Small cafés may grow up around a university because students need food and study spaces.","zh":"小咖啡店可能圍繞大學發展起來，因為學生需要食物和溫習空間。"},{"en":"If magazines grow around film studios, they may report stories that support the industry.","zh":"如果雜誌圍繞片廠發展，它們可能報道支持該行業的故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes development closely linked to another activity.","zh":"這個片語描述與另一活動密切相關的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the film industry","meaning":"電影業","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity magazines were connected to the film industry.","zh":"名人雜誌與電影業有關。"},{"en":"The film industry includes the companies and workers who produce, promote and distribute films.","zh":"film industry 包括製作、推廣和發行電影的公司與工作者。"},{"en":"Actors, directors, studios, cinemas and streaming platforms are all linked to the film industry.","zh":"演員、導演、片廠、戲院和串流平台都與電影業有關。"},{"en":"If celebrity news helps sell films, magazines and studios may depend on one another.","zh":"如果名人新聞有助推銷電影，雜誌和片廠可能互相依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the business world of cinema.","zh":"這個片語指電影的商業世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"report what someone wanted them to say","meaning":"報道某人希望它們說的內容","examples":[{"en":"Some magazines reported what the studios wanted them to say.","zh":"一些雜誌報道電影公司希望它們說的內容。"},{"en":"To report what someone wanted them to say means to publish information shaped by another party’s wishes.","zh":"report what someone wanted them to say 指刊登受另一方意願塑造的資料。"},{"en":"A school newsletter should not simply report what sponsors want it to say.","zh":"學校通訊不應只是報道贊助商希望它說的內容。"},{"en":"If magazines report only studio-approved stories, readers may not get honest criticism.","zh":"如果雜誌只報道片廠批准的故事，讀者可能得不到真實批評。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests controlled or influenced reporting.","zh":"這個片語暗示受控制或受影響的報道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the studios","meaning":"電影公司","examples":[{"en":"The studios influenced what some magazines reported.","zh":"電影公司影響了一些雜誌報道的內容。"},{"en":"The studios means film production companies that make and promote movies.","zh":"the studios 指製作和推廣電影的電影製作公司。"},{"en":"Large studios may control trailers, interviews and publicity photos.","zh":"大型電影公司可能控制預告片、訪問和宣傳照。"},{"en":"If studios influence magazines, celebrity news may become part of film marketing.","zh":"如果電影公司影響雜誌，名人新聞可能成為電影市場推廣的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to powerful companies in the movie business.","zh":"這個片語指電影業中有權力的公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"aim to","meaning":"旨在；意圖","examples":[{"en":"Confidential aimed to dish the dirt on the stars.","zh":"Confidential 旨在揭露明星醜聞。"},{"en":"To aim to do something means to intend or try to do it.","zh":"aim to do something 指意圖或嘗試做某事。"},{"en":"A school campaign may aim to reduce bullying by encouraging students to report problems.","zh":"學校活動可能旨在透過鼓勵學生舉報問題來減少欺凌。"},{"en":"If a magazine aims to expose scandal, it will search for shocking private details.","zh":"如果雜誌旨在揭露醜聞，它會尋找震撼私生活細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes purpose or intention.","zh":"這個片語描述目的或意圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dish the dirt on","meaning":"揭露……的醜聞","examples":[{"en":"Some magazines aimed to dish the dirt on the stars.","zh":"一些雜誌旨在揭露明星醜聞。"},{"en":"To dish the dirt on someone means to reveal gossip or embarrassing private information about them.","zh":"dish the dirt on someone 指揭露關於某人的八卦或令人尷尬的私生活資料。"},{"en":"A gossip account may dish the dirt on influencers after a public argument.","zh":"八卦帳戶可能在公開爭吵後揭露網紅醜聞。"},{"en":"If a magazine dishes the dirt, it may attract readers but damage reputations.","zh":"如果雜誌揭露醜聞，它可能吸引讀者，但損害名聲。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often negative.","zh":"這個片語較口語，通常帶負面意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the stars","meaning":"明星","examples":[{"en":"Confidential reported scandalous stories about the stars.","zh":"Confidential 報道關於明星的醜聞故事。"},{"en":"The stars means famous actors, singers or entertainers.","zh":"the stars 指著名演員、歌手或娛樂人物。"},{"en":"Fans may wait outside a theatre to see the stars after a show.","zh":"粉絲可能在劇院外等候，想在演出後見明星。"},{"en":"If stories about the stars sell well, magazines will keep reporting them.","zh":"如果關於明星的故事銷量好，雜誌會繼續報道。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to famous performers.","zh":"這個片語指著名表演者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be used to sell newspapers","meaning":"被用來促銷報紙","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity news has been used to sell newspapers for over a century.","zh":"名人新聞一個多世紀以來一直被用來促銷報紙。"},{"en":"To be used to sell newspapers means to attract buyers and increase sales through a topic or story.","zh":"be used to sell newspapers 指透過某主題或故事吸引買家並增加銷量。"},{"en":"A dramatic sports victory may be used to sell newspapers the next morning.","zh":"戲劇性的體育勝利可能在翌日被用來促銷報紙。"},{"en":"If readers buy papers for celebrity gossip, editors will place those stories prominently.","zh":"如果讀者為名人八卦購買報紙，編輯就會把這些故事放在顯眼位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using content as a sales tool.","zh":"這個片語描述把內容用作銷售工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"for more than a century","meaning":"超過一個世紀以來","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity news has sold British newspapers for more than a century.","zh":"超過一個世紀以來，名人新聞一直幫助英國報紙銷售。"},{"en":"For more than a century means for over one hundred years.","zh":"for more than a century 指超過一百年。"},{"en":"The school has served the neighbourhood for more than a century.","zh":"這所學校服務該社區超過一個世紀。"},{"en":"If a practice lasts more than a century, it is deeply rooted in public habits.","zh":"如果某做法持續超過一個世紀，它就深深扎根於公眾習慣中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very long historical duration.","zh":"這個片語描述很長的歷史時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"gleefully report","meaning":"津津樂道地報道","examples":[{"en":"The News of the World gleefully reported aristocratic scandals.","zh":"The News of the World 津津樂道地報道貴族醜聞。"},{"en":"To gleefully report something means to report it with obvious excitement or pleasure.","zh":"gleefully report something 指帶着明顯興奮或愉快地報道某事。"},{"en":"A gossip page may gleefully report a celebrity breakup with dramatic headlines.","zh":"八卦版可能用誇張標題津津樂道地報道名人分手。"},{"en":"If a newspaper reports scandal gleefully, it may care more about entertainment than dignity.","zh":"如果報紙津津樂道地報道醜聞，它可能更重視娛樂而非尊嚴。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests pleasure in exposing bad news.","zh":"這個片語暗示對揭露壞消息感到愉快。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"aristocratic scandals","meaning":"貴族醜聞","examples":[{"en":"The newspaper reported aristocratic scandals in the 19th century.","zh":"該報在十九世紀報道貴族醜聞。"},{"en":"Aristocratic scandals are shocking or embarrassing stories involving nobles or upper-class families.","zh":"aristocratic scandals 是涉及貴族或上流家庭的震撼或尷尬故事。"},{"en":"A secret affair involving a duke could become an aristocratic scandal.","zh":"涉及公爵的秘密婚外情可以成為貴族醜聞。"},{"en":"If ordinary readers enjoy stories about elite misbehaviour, such scandals can sell papers.","zh":"如果普通讀者喜歡看精英失德的故事，這類醜聞可以促銷報紙。"},{"en":"This phrase links social class with gossip and disgrace.","zh":"這個片語把社會階級與八卦和羞辱連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"first appear","meaning":"首次面世","examples":[{"en":"The News of the World first appeared in the same year as A Christmas Carol.","zh":"The News of the World 與《聖誕頌歌》同年首次面世。"},{"en":"To first appear means to be published, shown or seen for the first time.","zh":"first appear 指首次出版、展示或被看見。"},{"en":"A school magazine may first appear at the end of the academic year.","zh":"學校雜誌可能在學年末首次面世。"},{"en":"If a newspaper first appeared long ago, it has a long publishing history.","zh":"如果報紙很久以前首次面世，它就有悠久出版歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of public existence.","zh":"這個片語描述公開存在的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the same year as","meaning":"與……同年","examples":[{"en":"The newspaper appeared in the same year as Dickens’s A Christmas Carol.","zh":"該報與 Dickens 的《聖誕頌歌》同年面世。"},{"en":"In the same year as means during the same calendar year as another event.","zh":"in the same year as 指與另一事件在同一曆年發生。"},{"en":"The school opened in the same year as the town library.","zh":"學校與鎮圖書館同年開幕。"},{"en":"If two works appeared in the same year, comparing them can help show the historical context.","zh":"如果兩件作品同年出現，比較它們可以幫助顯示歷史背景。"},{"en":"This phrase links two events by date.","zh":"這個片語用日期連接兩個事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"give gossip a new sophistication","meaning":"令八卦新聞變得更精細","examples":[{"en":"Modern Britain has given gossip a new sophistication.","zh":"現代英國令八卦新聞變得更精細。"},{"en":"To give gossip a new sophistication means to make gossip more organised, professional or cleverly packaged.","zh":"give gossip a new sophistication 指令八卦變得更有組織、更專業或更巧妙包裝。"},{"en":"Social media analytics can give advertising a new sophistication by targeting exact audiences.","zh":"社交媒體分析可以透過精準鎖定受眾，令廣告變得更精細。"},{"en":"If gossip becomes sophisticated, it may involve contracts, staged photos and marketing plans.","zh":"如果八卦變得精細，它可能涉及合約、擺拍照片和市場計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a simple activity has become more refined and commercial.","zh":"這個片語顯示簡單活動變得更精緻和商業化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"part of the secret","meaning":"部分秘訣","examples":[{"en":"Part of the secret has been to separate celebrity revenue streams.","zh":"部分秘訣在於區分名人的收入來源。"},{"en":"Part of the secret means one reason behind success, especially one not obvious at first.","zh":"part of the secret 指成功背後的一個原因，尤其是起初不明顯的原因。"},{"en":"Part of the secret of a good lesson is using examples students recognise.","zh":"好課堂的部分秘訣是使用學生熟悉的例子。"},{"en":"If a business succeeds, part of the secret may be how it earns money from several sources.","zh":"如果生意成功，部分秘訣可能是它如何從幾個來源賺錢。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces one hidden factor behind success.","zh":"這個片語引入成功背後的一個隱藏因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"separate celebrity revenue streams","meaning":"區分名人的收入來源","examples":[{"en":"The industry separates celebrity revenue streams.","zh":"這個行業區分名人的收入來源。"},{"en":"To separate celebrity revenue streams means to divide the ways a celebrity earns money into different categories.","zh":"separate celebrity revenue streams 指把名人賺錢的方式分成不同類別。"},{"en":"A musician may separate income from concerts, streaming, sponsorships and merchandise.","zh":"音樂人可能區分演唱會、串流、贊助和商品收入。"},{"en":"If revenue streams are separated, each part of a celebrity’s life can be sold differently.","zh":"如果收入來源被區分，名人生活的每一部分都可以用不同方式出售。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organising fame into different sources of income.","zh":"這個片語描述把名氣組織成不同收入來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"revenue streams","meaning":"收入來源","examples":[{"en":"A celebrity can have more than one revenue stream.","zh":"名人可以有多於一個收入來源。"},{"en":"Revenue streams are different sources of income for a person or business.","zh":"revenue streams 是個人或企業不同的收入來源。"},{"en":"A tutor may have revenue streams from lessons, books and online courses.","zh":"導師可能有來自課堂、書籍和網上課程的收入來源。"},{"en":"If one revenue stream fails, another may help the business survive.","zh":"如果一個收入來源失效，另一個可能幫助生意生存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how money comes in from several directions.","zh":"這個片語描述金錢如何從幾個方向流入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"an agency for celebrities","meaning":"名人經理人公司","examples":[{"en":"Henry’s House is an agency for celebrities.","zh":"Henry’s House 是一間名人經理人公司。"},{"en":"An agency for celebrities is a company that represents famous people and manages work opportunities.","zh":"agency for celebrities 是代表名人並管理工作機會的公司。"},{"en":"A celebrity agency may arrange interviews, sponsorships and public appearances.","zh":"名人經理人公司可能安排訪問、贊助和公開露面。"},{"en":"If celebrities use an agency, they can turn attention into paid opportunities.","zh":"如果名人使用經理人公司，他們可以把關注轉化為付費機會。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a business that manages celebrity careers.","zh":"這個片語指管理名人事業的企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"distinguish between","meaning":"區分……","examples":[{"en":"Julian Henry distinguishes between a celebrity’s craft and celebrity rating.","zh":"Julian Henry 區分名人的本業和名人知名度評級。"},{"en":"To distinguish between two things means to recognise how they are different.","zh":"distinguish between two things 指認出兩者如何不同。"},{"en":"Students must distinguish between fact and opinion in reading questions.","zh":"學生必須在閱讀題中區分事實和意見。"},{"en":"If people distinguish between talent and fame, they may judge celebrities more carefully.","zh":"如果人們區分才華和名氣，就可能更仔細評價名人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes separating two ideas clearly.","zh":"這個片語描述清楚分開兩個概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a celebrity’s craft","meaning":"名人的本業；專門技藝","examples":[{"en":"A celebrity’s craft may include singing, modelling or sport.","zh":"名人的本業可能包括唱歌、模特兒工作或運動。"},{"en":"A celebrity’s craft is the actual skill or professional activity that the celebrity performs.","zh":"celebrity’s craft 是名人實際從事的技能或專業活動。"},{"en":"An actor’s craft includes voice, movement and emotional expression.","zh":"演員的專門技藝包括聲音、動作和情感表達。"},{"en":"If a celebrity’s craft is weak but fame is strong, publicity may matter more than skill.","zh":"如果名人的技藝薄弱但名氣很強，宣傳可能比技能更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase separates real work from public image.","zh":"這個片語把真實工作與公眾形象分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"celebrity rating","meaning":"名人知名度評級","examples":[{"en":"A celebrity rating can have a trajectory of its own.","zh":"名人知名度評級可以有其自身發展軌跡。"},{"en":"Celebrity rating means the level of public attention, popularity or media value a famous person has.","zh":"celebrity rating 指名人所擁有的公眾關注度、受歡迎程度或媒體價值。"},{"en":"A singer’s celebrity rating may rise after a viral interview, even without a new song.","zh":"歌手即使沒有新歌，也可能因爆紅訪問而知名度上升。"},{"en":"If celebrity rating falls, magazines may pay less for interviews and photos.","zh":"如果名人知名度下降，雜誌可能為訪問和照片支付較少。"},{"en":"This phrase measures fame as a marketable value.","zh":"這個片語把名氣量度為可出售價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a trajectory of its own","meaning":"有其自身發展軌跡","examples":[{"en":"A celebrity rating has a trajectory of its own.","zh":"名人知名度評級有其自身發展軌跡。"},{"en":"A trajectory of its own means an independent path of development over time.","zh":"trajectory of its own 指隨時間出現的獨立發展路線。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may have a trajectory of its own, separate from exam marks.","zh":"學生信心可能有其自身發展軌跡，與考試分數分開。"},{"en":"If fame follows its own trajectory, it may rise even when talent does not improve.","zh":"如果名氣有自己的發展軌跡，即使才華沒有改善，它也可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a separate pattern of growth or decline.","zh":"這個片語描述獨立的增長或下降模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"inverse relationship to","meaning":"與……成反比關係","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity rating often has an inverse relationship to talent.","zh":"名人知名度評級常與才華成反比。"},{"en":"An inverse relationship to something means one thing rises when the other falls, or they move in opposite directions.","zh":"inverse relationship to something 指一方上升時另一方下降，或兩者朝相反方向變化。"},{"en":"In some jobs, stress has an inverse relationship to sleep quality.","zh":"在一些工作中，壓力與睡眠質素成反比。"},{"en":"If fame rises as talent matters less, celebrity culture may reward attention more than skill.","zh":"如果才華越不重要名氣卻越上升，名人文化可能獎勵關注多於技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an opposite relationship between two things.","zh":"這個片語描述兩件事之間的相反關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a famous person","meaning":"名人","examples":[{"en":"A famous person may have more celebrity rating than talent.","zh":"名人可能有比才華更多的知名度評級。"},{"en":"A famous person is someone known by many people, often through media exposure.","zh":"famous person 是被許多人認識的人，通常透過媒體曝光成名。"},{"en":"A famous person may be recognised in restaurants, airports or shopping centres.","zh":"名人可能在餐廳、機場或商場被認出。"},{"en":"If someone is famous without clear achievement, people may question how fame was created.","zh":"如果某人沒有明顯成就卻成名，人們可能質疑名氣如何被創造。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a person with broad public recognition.","zh":"這個片語指具有廣泛公眾認知的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"become adept at","meaning":"變得擅長……","examples":[{"en":"Britain’s celebrity industry has become adept at creating celebrity value.","zh":"英國名人產業已變得擅長創造名人價值。"},{"en":"To become adept at something means to become skilled at doing it.","zh":"become adept at something 指變得熟練於做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher becomes adept at explaining grammar after years of correcting essays.","zh":"老師在多年批改作文後，會變得擅長解釋文法。"},{"en":"If an industry becomes adept at packaging fame, it can create profit from attention.","zh":"如果行業變得擅長包裝名氣，它就能從關注中創造利潤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growing practical skill.","zh":"這個片語描述實務技能增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"creating and selling","meaning":"創造並出售","examples":[{"en":"The industry has become adept at creating and selling celebrity rating.","zh":"這個行業已變得擅長創造並出售名人知名度評級。"},{"en":"Creating and selling means producing something and turning it into money through the market.","zh":"creating and selling 指製造某物，並透過市場把它轉化為金錢。"},{"en":"A designer may focus on creating and selling digital templates online.","zh":"設計師可能專注於在網上創造並出售數碼模板。"},{"en":"If celebrity rating can be created and sold, fame becomes a commercial asset.","zh":"如果名人知名度可以被創造並出售，名氣就成為商業資產。"},{"en":"This phrase connects production with profit.","zh":"這個片語把生產與利潤連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be to marry","meaning":"即將結婚","examples":[{"en":"Peter Andre and Katie Price are to marry later this month.","zh":"Peter Andre 和 Katie Price 即將在本月稍後結婚。"},{"en":"Be to marry means are scheduled or expected to get married.","zh":"be to marry 指按安排或預期將會結婚。"},{"en":"A couple are to marry next spring after five years together.","zh":"一對情侶在一起五年後，將於明年春天結婚。"},{"en":"If celebrities are to marry, magazines may compete for wedding photos.","zh":"如果名人即將結婚，雜誌可能爭奪婚禮照片。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal way to describe a planned future marriage.","zh":"這個片語是描述計劃中未來婚姻的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"later this month","meaning":"本月稍後","examples":[{"en":"The couple are to marry later this month.","zh":"這對情侶將於本月稍後結婚。"},{"en":"Later this month means at a future time before the current month ends.","zh":"later this month 指在本月結束前的未來某時間。"},{"en":"The school will hold a parents’ meeting later this month.","zh":"學校將於本月稍後舉行家長會。"},{"en":"If an event is happening later this month, publicity may start immediately.","zh":"如果活動在本月稍後舉行，宣傳可能立即開始。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a near future time within the same month.","zh":"這個片語表示同一月份內的近未來時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"better known as","meaning":"更為人熟悉的名字是……","examples":[{"en":"The model is better known as Jordan.","zh":"這名模特兒更為人熟悉的名字是 Jordan。"},{"en":"Better known as means more commonly recognised by another name.","zh":"better known as 指以另一個名字更常被人認識。"},{"en":"The singer’s real name is different, but she is better known by her stage name.","zh":"這名歌手真名不同，但她更為人熟悉的是其藝名。"},{"en":"If a public figure is better known by a nickname, media usually use that name.","zh":"如果公眾人物更常以綽號為人認識，媒體通常使用該名字。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the name most people recognise.","zh":"這個片語引入大多數人認得的名字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"careers were flagging","meaning":"事業正在走下坡","examples":[{"en":"Their careers were flagging when they met.","zh":"他們相遇時，事業正在走下坡。"},{"en":"Careers were flagging means their professional success and public attention were declining.","zh":"careers were flagging 指事業成功和公眾關注正在下降。"},{"en":"A singer’s career may be flagging if concerts sell poorly and new songs receive little attention.","zh":"如果演唱會銷量差，新歌又少人關注，歌手事業可能正在走下坡。"},{"en":"If careers are flagging, celebrities may use reality TV to regain visibility.","zh":"如果事業走下坡，名人可能利用真人騷重新獲得曝光。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a career losing energy or momentum.","zh":"這個片語描述事業失去活力或動力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reality TV show","meaning":"真人騷節目","examples":[{"en":"They met on a reality TV show.","zh":"他們在真人騷節目中相遇。"},{"en":"A reality TV show is a television programme that presents real people or celebrities in unscripted situations.","zh":"reality TV show 是展示真實人物或名人在非劇本情境中的電視節目。"},{"en":"A cooking competition can be a reality TV show if contestants are filmed under pressure.","zh":"如果參賽者在壓力下被拍攝，烹飪比賽也可以是真人騷。"},{"en":"If a reality show becomes popular, participants may become celebrities quickly.","zh":"如果真人騷受歡迎，參加者可能迅速成為名人。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to television built around real-life performance and personality.","zh":"這個片語指圍繞真實生活表現和個性的電視節目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an essential new cog in","meaning":"……中不可或缺的新齒輪","examples":[{"en":"Reality TV is an essential new cog in the celebrity machine.","zh":"真人騷是名人製造機器中不可或缺的新齒輪。"},{"en":"An essential new cog in a machine is a new but important part of a larger system.","zh":"essential new cog in a machine 指大型系統中新加入但重要的一部分。"},{"en":"Online booking became an essential new cog in the travel industry.","zh":"網上預訂成為旅遊業中不可或缺的新齒輪。"},{"en":"If reality TV supplies fresh personalities, it helps the celebrity machine keep working.","zh":"如果真人騷提供新鮮人物，它就幫助名人製造機器繼續運作。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one part of a system to a small but necessary machine part.","zh":"這個片語把系統中的一部分比作細小但必要的機械零件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sell rights to","meaning":"出售……的報道權","examples":[{"en":"The couple sold rights to their wedding.","zh":"這對情侶出售了婚禮報道權。"},{"en":"To sell rights to something means to allow someone to publish, film or use it in exchange for money.","zh":"sell rights to something 指收取金錢讓某人出版、拍攝或使用某事。"},{"en":"An author may sell film rights to a novel.","zh":"作家可能出售小說的電影版權。"},{"en":"If celebrities sell rights to a wedding, a magazine can publish exclusive photos and stories.","zh":"如果名人出售婚禮報道權，雜誌就可以刊登獨家照片和故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes turning access or permission into income.","zh":"這個片語描述把接觸權或許可轉化為收入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"build around a Cinderella theme","meaning":"圍繞灰姑娘主題設計","examples":[{"en":"The wedding was built around a Cinderella theme.","zh":"婚禮圍繞灰姑娘主題設計。"},{"en":"To be built around a theme means to be planned with that theme as the central idea.","zh":"be built around a theme 指以某主題作為核心概念來規劃。"},{"en":"A school party may be built around a space theme with stars, planets and costumes.","zh":"學校派對可能圍繞太空主題設計，有星星、行星和服裝。"},{"en":"If a celebrity wedding has a fairy-tale theme, magazines can market it as romantic fantasy.","zh":"如果名人婚禮有童話主題，雜誌可以把它包裝成浪漫幻想。"},{"en":"This phrase describes designing an event around one main concept.","zh":"這個片語描述圍繞一個主要概念設計活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as an exclusive to","meaning":"作為……的獨家報道","examples":[{"en":"The wedding was sold as an exclusive to OK!.","zh":"婚禮作為 OK! 的獨家報道出售。"},{"en":"As an exclusive to a publication means only that publication has the right to publish the story or photos first.","zh":"as an exclusive to a publication 指只有該刊物有權首先刊登故事或照片。"},{"en":"A newspaper may buy an interview as an exclusive so rival papers cannot print it.","zh":"報紙可能購買訪問作為獨家報道，讓競爭報紙不能刊登。"},{"en":"If a magazine gets an exclusive, readers may buy it for content they cannot find elsewhere.","zh":"如果雜誌取得獨家內容，讀者可能為別處看不到的內容而購買。"},{"en":"This phrase describes special media access given to one outlet.","zh":"這個片語描述給予某一媒體的特別接觸權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"for a small fortune","meaning":"以一大筆錢","examples":[{"en":"The wedding rights were sold for a small fortune.","zh":"婚禮報道權以一大筆錢出售。"},{"en":"For a small fortune means for a very large amount of money.","zh":"for a small fortune 指以非常大筆金錢。"},{"en":"A rare watch may sell for a small fortune at auction.","zh":"稀有手錶可能在拍賣中以一大筆錢售出。"},{"en":"If celebrity wedding photos sell for a small fortune, private events become commercial assets.","zh":"如果名人婚禮照片以高價出售，私人活動就成為商業資產。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the price is extremely high.","zh":"這個片語強調價格極高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the gossip press","meaning":"八卦傳媒","examples":[{"en":"The gossip press discussed the price of the deal.","zh":"八卦傳媒討論了該交易的價格。"},{"en":"The gossip press means newspapers and magazines focused on rumours, scandals and celebrity stories.","zh":"gossip press 指聚焦傳聞、醜聞和名人故事的報紙和雜誌。"},{"en":"The gossip press may follow a celebrity couple from dating to marriage and breakup.","zh":"八卦傳媒可能從拍拖到結婚再到分手，一直跟蹤一對名人情侶。"},{"en":"If the gossip press repeats a story, it can become part of public conversation.","zh":"如果八卦傳媒反覆報道某故事，它可以成為公共話題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to media built around personal and celebrity gossip.","zh":"這個片語指圍繞個人和名人八卦建立的媒體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be said to have","meaning":"據說已經……","examples":[{"en":"The price was said to have annoyed another celebrity.","zh":"據說該價格已令另一位名人不悅。"},{"en":"Be said to have done something means people report or claim that it happened, without presenting it as certain fact.","zh":"be said to have done something 指人們報稱或聲稱某事發生，但不把它當作確定事實。"},{"en":"The actor was said to have refused an interview, but no official statement was given.","zh":"據說該演員拒絕訪問，但沒有官方聲明。"},{"en":"If a story is only said to have happened, readers should treat it carefully.","zh":"如果故事只是據說發生，讀者應謹慎看待。"},{"en":"This phrase reports a claim indirectly.","zh":"這個片語間接報道一項聲稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"irk someone","meaning":"令某人不悅","examples":[{"en":"The price of the deal irked Victoria Beckham.","zh":"該交易價格令 Victoria Beckham 不悅。"},{"en":"To irk someone means to annoy or irritate them.","zh":"irk someone 指令某人惱怒或不快。"},{"en":"It may irk students when the timetable changes at the last minute.","zh":"當時間表在最後一刻改變，可能令學生不悅。"},{"en":"If one celebrity receives a larger payment, it may irk another who earned less.","zh":"如果一位名人收到更高報酬，可能令另一位收入較少的名人不快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mild but noticeable annoyance.","zh":"這個片語描述輕微但明顯的不悅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be covered by","meaning":"由……報道；由……涵蓋","examples":[{"en":"Victoria Beckham’s marriage was covered by a million-pound contract.","zh":"Victoria Beckham 的婚禮由一份百萬英鎊合約涵蓋。"},{"en":"To be covered by a contract means to be included under the rules, payment or protection of that contract.","zh":"be covered by a contract 指被包括在該合約的規則、付款或保障之內。"},{"en":"A phone repair may be covered by warranty if the damage is not caused by the user.","zh":"如果手機損壞不是由用戶造成，維修可能由保養涵蓋。"},{"en":"If a wedding is covered by a media contract, the magazine may receive publishing rights.","zh":"如果婚禮由媒體合約涵蓋，雜誌可能獲得出版權。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something included within an agreement.","zh":"這個片語描述某事被納入協議之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a million-pound contract","meaning":"百萬英鎊合約","examples":[{"en":"The wedding was covered by a million-pound contract.","zh":"婚禮由一份百萬英鎊合約涵蓋。"},{"en":"A million-pound contract is an agreement worth one million pounds.","zh":"million-pound contract 是價值一百萬英鎊的協議。"},{"en":"A footballer may sign a million-pound contract with a club.","zh":"足球員可能與球會簽訂百萬英鎊合約。"},{"en":"If a magazine pays a million pounds for wedding rights, it expects huge sales.","zh":"如果雜誌為婚禮報道權支付一百萬英鎊，它會期望巨大銷量。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the high financial value of an agreement.","zh":"這個片語強調協議的高金錢價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"such sums","meaning":"這樣的金額","examples":[{"en":"Such sums were once reserved for authentic stars.","zh":"這樣的金額曾經只留給真正的明星。"},{"en":"Such sums means amounts of money like those just mentioned.","zh":"such sums 指剛提到那樣的金錢數額。"},{"en":"A small charity rarely handles such sums unless it receives a major donation.","zh":"小型慈善機構除非收到重大捐款，否則很少處理這樣的金額。"},{"en":"If reality-show celebrities receive such sums, the definition of stardom may change.","zh":"如果真人騷名人收到這樣的金額，明星身份的定義可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to large amounts of money.","zh":"這個片語回指大筆金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be reserved for","meaning":"留給；專供……使用","examples":[{"en":"Large payments were once reserved for authentic stars.","zh":"大額付款曾經只留給真正的明星。"},{"en":"To be reserved for someone means to be kept specially for that person or group.","zh":"be reserved for someone 指特別留給某人或某群體。"},{"en":"Front-row seats may be reserved for parents during a school performance.","zh":"學校表演期間，前排座位可能留給家長。"},{"en":"If huge fees are no longer reserved for top actors, the celebrity economy has changed.","zh":"如果巨額費用不再只留給頂級演員，名人經濟已經改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exclusive use or special allocation.","zh":"這個片語描述專用或特別分配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"authentic stars","meaning":"真正的明星","examples":[{"en":"Such sums used to be reserved for authentic stars.","zh":"這樣的金額過去只留給真正的明星。"},{"en":"Authentic stars are genuinely famous performers with recognised talent or achievement.","zh":"authentic stars 是真正著名並擁有公認才華或成就的表演者。"},{"en":"An actor with decades of respected films may be seen as an authentic star.","zh":"擁有數十年受尊敬電影作品的演員，可能被視為真正明星。"},{"en":"If reality personalities earn the same sums, traditional star status becomes less exclusive.","zh":"如果真人騷人物賺取同樣金額，傳統明星地位就變得不再那麼專屬。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts lasting talent-based fame with manufactured celebrity.","zh":"這個片語把基於持久才華的名氣與被製造的名人作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"wedding snaps","meaning":"婚禮照片","examples":[{"en":"The deal included more than wedding snaps.","zh":"該交易包含的不只是婚禮照片。"},{"en":"Wedding snaps are informal photographs taken at a wedding.","zh":"wedding snaps 是婚禮上拍攝的非正式照片。"},{"en":"Guests may share wedding snaps with the couple after the ceremony.","zh":"賓客可能在婚禮後與新人分享婚禮照片。"},{"en":"If a media deal includes more than snaps, it may cover interviews, home life and future family events.","zh":"如果媒體交易包含的不只是照片，它可能涵蓋訪問、家庭生活和未來家庭事件。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and refers to wedding photos.","zh":"這個片語較口語，指婚禮照片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"over a year of","meaning":"超過一年時間的……","examples":[{"en":"The deal covered over a year of the couple’s life.","zh":"該交易涵蓋這對情侶超過一年時間的生活。"},{"en":"Over a year of something means a period longer than twelve months of it.","zh":"over a year of something 指某事超過十二個月的時間。"},{"en":"A research project may collect over a year of data before reporting results.","zh":"研究項目可能在報告結果前收集超過一年數據。"},{"en":"If a contract covers over a year of private life, many personal moments become media material.","zh":"如果合約涵蓋超過一年私生活，許多個人時刻就變成媒體材料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a duration longer than one year.","zh":"這個片語描述超過一年的持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"prenuptial nerves","meaning":"婚前緊張","examples":[{"en":"The deal covered everything from prenuptial nerves to family life.","zh":"該交易涵蓋從婚前緊張到家庭生活的一切。"},{"en":"Prenuptial nerves are feelings of anxiety or tension before marriage.","zh":"prenuptial nerves 是結婚前的焦慮或緊張感。"},{"en":"A bride may feel prenuptial nerves when planning the guest list and ceremony.","zh":"新娘在規劃賓客名單和儀式時，可能感到婚前緊張。"},{"en":"If magazines report prenuptial nerves, even private emotions become public entertainment.","zh":"如果雜誌報道婚前緊張，連私人情緒也變成公共娛樂。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to nervousness before a wedding.","zh":"這個片語指婚禮前的緊張感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"expected offspring","meaning":"即將出生的孩子","examples":[{"en":"The deal extended to the first birthday of the expected offspring.","zh":"該交易延伸至即將出生的孩子的一歲生日。"},{"en":"Expected offspring means a baby or child that is expected to be born.","zh":"expected offspring 指預期將會出生的嬰兒或孩子。"},{"en":"Parents may prepare a room for their expected offspring before the birth.","zh":"父母可能在孩子出生前為即將出生的孩子準備房間。"},{"en":"If media rights cover an expected child, family life is being commercialised before birth.","zh":"如果媒體權利涵蓋未出生孩子，家庭生活在出生前已被商業化。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal or slightly distant, meaning an unborn child.","zh":"這個片語較正式或疏離，意思是未出生的孩子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be bundled together","meaning":"被捆綁在一起","examples":[{"en":"Different parts of the couple’s life were bundled together.","zh":"這對情侶生活的不同部分被捆綁在一起。"},{"en":"To be bundled together means to be packaged or sold as one combined group.","zh":"be bundled together 指被包裝或作為一個組合出售。"},{"en":"A phone plan may bundle calls, data and streaming services together.","zh":"手機計劃可能把通話、數據和串流服務捆綁在一起。"},{"en":"If wedding, pregnancy and family photos are bundled together, private life becomes one media package.","zh":"如果婚禮、懷孕和家庭照片被捆綁在一起，私生活就成為一個媒體套裝。"},{"en":"This phrase describes combining separate items into one deal.","zh":"這個片語描述把分開項目合併成一項交易。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sold as a commodity","meaning":"作為商品出售","examples":[{"en":"The couple’s life was sold as a commodity.","zh":"這對情侶的生活被作為商品出售。"},{"en":"Sold as a commodity means treated as a product that can be bought and sold.","zh":"sold as a commodity 指被視為可以買賣的產品。"},{"en":"Personal data can be sold as a commodity when companies trade user information.","zh":"當公司交易用戶資訊，個人資料就可能被作為商品出售。"},{"en":"If a celebrity’s daily life is sold as a commodity, privacy becomes a source of profit.","zh":"如果名人的日常生活被作為商品出售，私隱就成為利潤來源。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises turning human experience into a market product.","zh":"這個片語批評把人的經驗轉化為市場產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sign a three-book deal with","meaning":"與……簽訂三本書合約","examples":[{"en":"Ms. Price signed a three-book deal with Random House.","zh":"Price 女士與 Random House 簽訂三本書合約。"},{"en":"To sign a three-book deal with a publisher means to agree to produce three books for that publisher.","zh":"sign a three-book deal with a publisher 指同意為該出版社製作三本書。"},{"en":"A popular teacher might sign a three-book deal to write grammar, speaking and writing guides.","zh":"受歡迎老師可能簽訂三本書合約，撰寫文法、口語和寫作指南。"},{"en":"If a celebrity signs a book deal, fame can be converted into publishing income.","zh":"如果名人簽訂書籍合約，名氣可以轉化為出版收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a publishing contract for three books.","zh":"這個片語描述三本書的出版合約。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"call this stuff","meaning":"把這類東西稱為……","examples":[{"en":"Paul Ashford calls this stuff “relationship journalism”.","zh":"Paul Ashford 把這類東西稱為「關係新聞」。"},{"en":"To call this stuff something means to give a name to a type of material or behaviour.","zh":"call this stuff something 指給某類材料或行為一個名稱。"},{"en":"A teacher may call repeated careless mistakes “exam technique problems”.","zh":"老師可能把反覆粗心錯誤稱為「考試技巧問題」。"},{"en":"If someone names a media pattern, readers can recognise it more easily.","zh":"如果有人為媒體模式命名，讀者就更容易認出它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a label for a practice.","zh":"這個片語引入對某種做法的標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"relationship journalism","meaning":"關係新聞；名人感情新聞","examples":[{"en":"Relationship journalism sells celebrity relationships as news.","zh":"關係新聞把名人關係作為新聞出售。"},{"en":"Relationship journalism is reporting that turns romance, marriage, breakup and family life into media content.","zh":"relationship journalism 是把戀愛、婚姻、分手和家庭生活變成媒體內容的報道。"},{"en":"A magazine story about every stage of a celebrity couple’s romance is relationship journalism.","zh":"關於名人情侶每個戀愛階段的雜誌故事就是關係新聞。"},{"en":"If relationship journalism sells well, celebrities may reveal emotions for money and attention.","zh":"如果關係新聞賣得好，名人可能為金錢和關注揭露情感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes media built around publicising private relationships.","zh":"這個片語描述圍繞公開私人關係而建立的媒體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be easy to spot","meaning":"很容易辨認","examples":[{"en":"Relationship journalism is pretty easy to spot.","zh":"關係新聞相當容易辨認。"},{"en":"To be easy to spot means to be simple to recognise or notice.","zh":"be easy to spot 指很容易認出或注意到。"},{"en":"A spelling mistake in a title is easy to spot because it is so visible.","zh":"標題中的串字錯誤很容易辨認，因為非常顯眼。"},{"en":"If a celebrity story focuses mainly on romance and family drama, relationship journalism is easy to identify.","zh":"如果名人故事主要聚焦戀情和家庭戲劇，關係新聞就很容易識別。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something obvious once you know what to look for.","zh":"這個片語描述一旦知道要看甚麼便很明顯的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the process has become so effective that","meaning":"這個過程變得如此有效，以致……","examples":[{"en":"The process has become so effective that it can manufacture major celebrities.","zh":"這個過程變得如此有效，以致它能製造主要名人。"},{"en":"This structure means the process works so well that it produces a strong result.","zh":"the process has become so effective that 指該過程非常有效，因此產生強烈結果。"},{"en":"The revision system became so effective that weaker students began passing consistently.","zh":"溫習系統變得如此有效，以致較弱學生開始穩定合格。"},{"en":"If celebrity production is this effective, fame can be created even without traditional achievement.","zh":"如果名人製造如此有效，即使沒有傳統成就也能創造名氣。"},{"en":"This phrase links high effectiveness with a surprising consequence.","zh":"這個片語把高效能與令人意外的後果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"insiders say","meaning":"內部人士表示","examples":[{"en":"Insiders say the top-selling celebrities were manufactured in this way.","zh":"內部人士表示，最暢銷的名人就是以這種方式被製造出來。"},{"en":"Insiders say means people with inside knowledge report or claim something.","zh":"insiders say 指掌握內部知識的人報稱或聲稱某事。"},{"en":"Insiders say a company may launch a new product before the official announcement.","zh":"內部人士可能在官方公布前表示公司將推出新產品。"},{"en":"If insiders speak, they may reveal how an industry really works behind the scenes.","zh":"如果內部人士發聲，他們可能揭示行業幕後真正如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces information from people close to the situation.","zh":"這個片語引入來自接近情況人士的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"shift most copies of","meaning":"令……賣出最多份","examples":[{"en":"Some celebrities shift most copies of OK!.","zh":"一些名人令 OK! 賣出最多份。"},{"en":"To shift most copies of a publication means to help sell the largest number of copies.","zh":"shift most copies of a publication 指幫助賣出最多刊物份數。"},{"en":"A famous actor on the cover may shift more copies of a magazine than an unknown model.","zh":"封面上的著名演員可能比陌生模特兒令雜誌賣出更多。"},{"en":"If one celebrity shifts many copies, editors may feature them repeatedly.","zh":"如果某名人帶來大量銷量，編輯可能反覆刊登他們。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and commercial, focusing on sales.","zh":"這個片語較口語且商業化，聚焦銷售。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be manufactured in this way","meaning":"以這種方式被製造出來","examples":[{"en":"Some celebrities have been manufactured in this way.","zh":"一些名人以這種方式被製造出來。"},{"en":"To be manufactured in this way means to be created through a planned media process rather than natural fame alone.","zh":"be manufactured in this way 指透過有計劃的媒體過程被創造，而不只是自然成名。"},{"en":"A reality-show contestant may be manufactured through interviews, photo deals and constant coverage.","zh":"真人騷參賽者可能透過訪問、照片交易和持續報道被製造出來。"},{"en":"If fame is manufactured this way, public image becomes carefully designed.","zh":"如果名氣以這種方式被製造，公眾形象就會被精心設計。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests celebrity is constructed, not simply earned.","zh":"這個片語暗示名人是被建構出來，而不只是靠成就獲得。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have a powerful effect on sales","meaning":"對銷量有強大影響","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity stories can have a powerful effect on sales.","zh":"名人故事可以對銷量有強大影響。"},{"en":"To have a powerful effect on sales means to strongly increase or decrease how much is sold.","zh":"have a powerful effect on sales 指強烈增加或減少銷售量。"},{"en":"A famous athlete’s endorsement can have a powerful effect on shoe sales.","zh":"著名運動員的代言可以對球鞋銷量有強大影響。"},{"en":"If a cover story boosts sales, magazines will produce similar stories again.","zh":"如果封面故事提升銷量，雜誌會再次製作相似故事。"},{"en":"This phrase links content or publicity with buying behaviour.","zh":"這個片語把內容或宣傳與購買行為連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"it is unsurprising that","meaning":"……並不令人意外","examples":[{"en":"It is unsurprising that celebrity stories are carefully manufactured.","zh":"名人故事被仔細製造並不令人意外。"},{"en":"It is unsurprising that means it is not surprising because the situation makes sense.","zh":"it is unsurprising that 指某事情合理，因此並不令人驚訝。"},{"en":"It is unsurprising that students improve when they receive clear feedback every week.","zh":"學生每週獲得清晰回饋時進步，並不令人意外。"},{"en":"If celebrity stories increase sales, it is logical that publishers design them carefully.","zh":"如果名人故事增加銷量，出版商仔細設計它們是合乎邏輯的。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an expected conclusion.","zh":"這個片語引入可預期的結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be left to chance","meaning":"任由運氣決定","examples":[{"en":"The manufacture of celebrity stories is not left to chance.","zh":"名人故事的製造並非任由運氣決定。"},{"en":"To be left to chance means to be allowed to happen randomly without planning.","zh":"be left to chance 指讓事情隨機發生而不作計劃。"},{"en":"A school open day should not be left to chance; staff need a clear plan.","zh":"學校開放日不應任由運氣決定，職員需要清晰計劃。"},{"en":"If celebrity stories affect profit, magazines will manage timing, images and access carefully.","zh":"如果名人故事影響利潤，雜誌會仔細管理時間、圖片和接觸權。"},{"en":"This phrase describes whether something is planned or random.","zh":"這個片語描述某事是有計劃還是隨機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"more egalitarian","meaning":"更平民化","examples":[{"en":"Modern celebrity in Britain is also more egalitarian.","zh":"英國現代名人也變得更平民化。"},{"en":"More egalitarian means less limited to elites and more open to ordinary people.","zh":"more egalitarian 指不再只限精英，而是更開放給普通人。"},{"en":"A school club becomes more egalitarian when beginners and top students both get chances to perform.","zh":"當初學者和尖子都有表演機會，學校社團就變得更平等。"},{"en":"If celebrity becomes more egalitarian, ordinary people can become famous without aristocratic background.","zh":"如果名人文化更平民化，普通人即使沒有貴族背景也能成名。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift toward wider access or equality.","zh":"這個片語描述朝向更廣泛參與或平等的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tittle-tattle about","meaning":"關於……的閒言閒語","examples":[{"en":"Tittle-tattle about dukes and duchesses is now less valuable.","zh":"關於公爵與公爵夫人的閒言閒語現在價值較低。"},{"en":"Tittle-tattle about someone means trivial gossip about them.","zh":"tittle-tattle about someone 指關於某人的瑣碎八卦。"},{"en":"Office tittle-tattle about who is dating whom can distract workers from serious tasks.","zh":"辦公室關於誰和誰拍拖的閒言閒語，可能令員工分心。"},{"en":"If gossip about aristocrats becomes less exciting, magazines may turn to ordinary celebrities.","zh":"如果關於貴族的八卦變得較不刺激，雜誌可能轉向普通名人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes light, often unimportant gossip.","zh":"這個片語描述輕微、通常不重要的八卦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"dukes and duchesses","meaning":"公爵與公爵夫人","examples":[{"en":"Stories about dukes and duchesses are worth less than before.","zh":"關於公爵與公爵夫人的故事價值低於以前。"},{"en":"Dukes and duchesses are high-ranking members of the aristocracy.","zh":"dukes and duchesses 是貴族階級中的高級成員。"},{"en":"A history lesson may discuss dukes and duchesses who owned large estates.","zh":"歷史課可能討論擁有大片莊園的公爵與公爵夫人。"},{"en":"If readers prefer ordinary celebrities, aristocratic titles may attract less attention.","zh":"如果讀者較喜歡普通名人，貴族頭銜可能吸引較少注意。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to noble men and women.","zh":"這個片語指貴族男性和女性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be worth less than","meaning":"價值低於……","examples":[{"en":"Aristocratic gossip is worth less than stories about ordinary people.","zh":"貴族八卦的價值低於關於普通人的故事。"},{"en":"To be worth less than something means to have lower value than it.","zh":"be worth less than something 指價值低於某物。"},{"en":"A used phone is usually worth less than a new one.","zh":"二手電話通常價值低於新電話。"},{"en":"If readers find ordinary people more interesting, aristocratic stories may earn less money.","zh":"如果讀者覺得普通人更有趣，貴族故事可能賺得較少。"},{"en":"This phrase compares value or market appeal.","zh":"這個片語比較價值或市場吸引力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ordinary folk","meaning":"普通人","examples":[{"en":"Ordinary folk make more colourful copy than aristocrats.","zh":"普通人比貴族更能成為生動有趣的報道題材。"},{"en":"Ordinary folk means ordinary people without special rank, title or fame.","zh":"ordinary folk 指沒有特殊地位、頭銜或名氣的普通人。"},{"en":"A documentary about ordinary folk can show how real families live and struggle.","zh":"關於普通人的紀錄片可以展示真實家庭如何生活和掙扎。"},{"en":"If ordinary people become celebrity subjects, fame feels more accessible to readers.","zh":"如果普通人成為名人題材，名氣對讀者而言感覺更可接近。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and refers to everyday people.","zh":"這個片語較口語，指日常普通人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make for more colourful copy","meaning":"令報道更生動有趣","examples":[{"en":"Ordinary folk make for more colourful copy.","zh":"普通人令報道更生動有趣。"},{"en":"To make for more colourful copy means to provide more interesting, lively material for writing.","zh":"make for more colourful copy 指提供更有趣、更生動的寫作材料。"},{"en":"A school trip with unexpected problems may make for more colourful copy in the newsletter.","zh":"一次出現意外問題的學校旅行，可能令通訊報道更生動有趣。"},{"en":"If ordinary people behave dramatically, their stories may be more entertaining than royal gossip.","zh":"如果普通人行為戲劇化，他們的故事可能比皇室八卦更具娛樂性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what makes writing vivid or marketable.","zh":"這個片語描述甚麼令文章生動或具市場價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"boost circulation by","meaning":"令發行量增加……","examples":[{"en":"The News of the World boosted circulation by 250,000.","zh":"The News of the World 令發行量增加二十五萬。"},{"en":"To boost circulation by a number means to increase the number of copies sold or distributed by that amount.","zh":"boost circulation by a number 指令售出或發行份數增加某數量。"},{"en":"A popular school interview may boost newsletter circulation by hundreds of copies.","zh":"一篇受歡迎的校園訪問可能令通訊發行量增加數百份。"},{"en":"If a celebrity scandal boosts circulation, editors may seek similar stories later.","zh":"如果名人醜聞令發行量增加，編輯日後可能尋找類似故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a measurable rise in publication sales.","zh":"這個片語描述出版物銷量的可量度上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"put someone on its cover","meaning":"把某人放上封面","examples":[{"en":"The newspaper put the Beckhams on its cover.","zh":"該報把 Beckham 夫婦放上封面。"},{"en":"To put someone on its cover means to place their picture or story on the front page or magazine cover.","zh":"put someone on its cover 指把某人的照片或故事放在頭版或雜誌封面。"},{"en":"A school magazine may put the debate team on its cover after a major victory.","zh":"學校雜誌可能在辯論隊重大勝利後把他們放上封面。"},{"en":"If a publication puts a celebrity on the cover, it hopes readers will notice and buy it.","zh":"如果刊物把名人放上封面，它希望讀者注意並購買。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using someone’s image as the main visual attraction.","zh":"這個片語描述使用某人形象作主要視覺吸引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be alleged to have","meaning":"被指稱曾經……","examples":[{"en":"David Beckham was alleged to have had a love affair.","zh":"David Beckham 被指稱曾經有婚外情。"},{"en":"Be alleged to have done something means someone is accused or claimed to have done it, but it is not proven in the sentence.","zh":"be alleged to have done something 指某人被指控或聲稱做過某事，但句子中未證實。"},{"en":"A student was alleged to have copied homework, but the teacher still needed evidence.","zh":"一名學生被指稱曾抄功課，但老師仍需要證據。"},{"en":"If a celebrity is alleged to have done something scandalous, tabloids may report it loudly.","zh":"如果名人被指稱做過醜聞事件，小報可能大肆報道。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for unproven claims or accusations.","zh":"這個片語用於未證實的聲稱或指控。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have a love affair","meaning":"有婚外情；有戀情","examples":[{"en":"David Beckham was alleged to have had a love affair.","zh":"David Beckham 被指稱曾經有婚外情。"},{"en":"To have a love affair means to have a romantic or sexual relationship, often outside marriage.","zh":"have a love affair 指有浪漫或性關係，常指婚姻以外的關係。"},{"en":"In a drama, a secret love affair can create conflict between families.","zh":"在劇集中，秘密戀情可以造成家庭之間的衝突。"},{"en":"If a married celebrity is accused of a love affair, public image may suffer.","zh":"如果已婚名人被指有婚外情，公眾形象可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in gossip, fiction and scandal reporting.","zh":"這個片語常出現在八卦、小說和醜聞報道中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"such cases show how","meaning":"這些例子顯示……如何","examples":[{"en":"Such cases show how participation can later damage celebrities.","zh":"這些例子顯示參與如何日後損害名人。"},{"en":"Such cases show how means examples like these demonstrate the way something happens.","zh":"such cases show how 指這類例子展示某事如何發生。"},{"en":"Students forgetting sources show how easy it is to lose marks for careless citation.","zh":"學生忘記標明資料來源，顯示粗心引用多麼容易失分。"},{"en":"If celebrities cooperate with media early on, later scandals may be harder to control.","zh":"如果名人早期與媒體合作，日後醜聞可能更難控制。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a lesson drawn from examples.","zh":"這個片語引入從例子得出的教訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"willing participation","meaning":"自願參與","examples":[{"en":"Celebrities’ willing participation may later create problems.","zh":"名人自願參與日後可能造成問題。"},{"en":"Willing participation means taking part voluntarily rather than being forced.","zh":"willing participation 指自願參與，而不是被迫。"},{"en":"A student’s willing participation in group work often improves the whole project.","zh":"學生自願參與小組工作，通常會改善整個項目。"},{"en":"If celebrities willingly share private life, media may expect even more access later.","zh":"如果名人自願分享私生活，媒體日後可能期待更多接觸權。"},{"en":"This phrase describes voluntary involvement.","zh":"這個片語描述自願投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"come back to haunt someone","meaning":"事後反過來困擾某人","examples":[{"en":"A celebrity’s earlier cooperation can come back to haunt them.","zh":"名人早前的合作可能事後反過來困擾他們。"},{"en":"To come back to haunt someone means a past action later causes trouble or regret.","zh":"come back to haunt someone 指過去行動日後造成麻煩或後悔。"},{"en":"A careless online comment can come back to haunt a student when applying for a job.","zh":"粗心的網上留言可能在學生求職時反過來困擾他。"},{"en":"If celebrities sell private stories, those stories may later be used against them.","zh":"如果名人出售私人故事，那些故事日後可能被用來對付他們。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that past choices can create future problems.","zh":"這個片語警告過去選擇可以造成未來問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"transgress","meaning":"越界；犯錯","examples":[{"en":"Celebrities may suffer if they transgress.","zh":"名人如果越界，可能會受苦。"},{"en":"To transgress means to break a rule, moral boundary or social expectation.","zh":"transgress 指違反規則、道德界限或社會期望。"},{"en":"A student transgresses when they cheat despite clear exam rules.","zh":"學生在考試規則清楚下作弊，就是犯錯越界。"},{"en":"If celebrities transgress after building a perfect image, the public reaction may be harsh.","zh":"如果名人建立完美形象後越界，公眾反應可能很嚴厲。"},{"en":"This word is formal and means to cross an accepted line.","zh":"這個詞較正式，意思是跨越被接受的界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"less common than you might think","meaning":"比你想像中少見","examples":[{"en":"Pure intrusion is less common than you might think.","zh":"純粹侵犯私生活比你想像中少見。"},{"en":"Less common than you might think means something happens less often than people expect.","zh":"less common than you might think 指某事發生得比人們預期少。"},{"en":"Perfect grammar in everyday speech is less common than learners might think.","zh":"日常說話中的完美文法比學習者想像中少見。"},{"en":"If staged photos are frequent, true invasion of privacy may be less common than it appears.","zh":"如果擺拍照片很常見，真正侵犯私隱可能比表面看來少。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects an assumption about frequency.","zh":"這個片語糾正對頻率的假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"plain intrusion into private lives","meaning":"明顯侵犯私生活","examples":[{"en":"Some photos look like plain intrusion into private lives.","zh":"一些照片看起來像明顯侵犯私生活。"},{"en":"Plain intrusion into private lives means obvious unwanted entry into personal matters or spaces.","zh":"plain intrusion into private lives 指明顯而不受歡迎地闖入個人事務或空間。"},{"en":"Photographing a family through a window would be plain intrusion into private life.","zh":"透過窗戶拍攝家庭，就是明顯侵犯私生活。"},{"en":"If media crosses this line, celebrities may lose control over personal dignity and safety.","zh":"如果媒體越過這條界線，名人可能失去對個人尊嚴和安全的控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clear invasion of privacy.","zh":"這個片語描述清楚侵犯私隱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"private lives","meaning":"私生活","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity magazines often appear to expose private lives.","zh":"名人雜誌常似乎揭露私生活。"},{"en":"Private lives are the personal parts of people’s lives outside public work or official roles.","zh":"private lives 是人們在公共工作或官方角色以外的個人生活部分。"},{"en":"Teachers have private lives outside the classroom, just like students have lives outside school.","zh":"老師在課室以外有私生活，就像學生在學校以外也有生活。"},{"en":"If private lives are constantly published, people may feel watched and pressured.","zh":"如果私生活不斷被公開，人們可能感到被監視和受壓。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to personal life that people may want to keep away from public attention.","zh":"這個片語指人們可能想遠離公眾關注的個人生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be staged","meaning":"被安排；被擺拍","examples":[{"en":"Many celebrity pictures are actually staged.","zh":"許多名人照片其實是被安排的。"},{"en":"To be staged means to be planned or arranged rather than happening naturally.","zh":"be staged 指經過計劃或安排，而不是自然發生。"},{"en":"A photo of students studying happily may be staged for a school brochure.","zh":"學校宣傳冊中學生快樂溫習的照片可能是擺拍的。"},{"en":"If paparazzi-style photos are staged, the celebrity keeps more control than readers realise.","zh":"如果狗仔隊風格照片是擺拍，名人比讀者想像中有更多控制權。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something deliberately set up.","zh":"這個片語描述某事被刻意安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"thanks to","meaning":"多虧；由於","examples":[{"en":"This is partly thanks to the profit motive.","zh":"這部分是由於利潤動機。"},{"en":"Thanks to means because of, often when explaining a cause.","zh":"thanks to 指因為某事，常用來解釋原因。"},{"en":"Thanks to careful revision, the student made fewer grammar mistakes.","zh":"多虧仔細溫習，學生犯較少文法錯誤。"},{"en":"If profits can be shared, celebrities and photographers have reason to cooperate.","zh":"如果利潤可以分享，名人和攝影師就有理由合作。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the reason something happens.","zh":"這個片語引入某事發生的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the profit motive","meaning":"利潤動機","examples":[{"en":"The profit motive encourages celebrities to cooperate.","zh":"利潤動機鼓勵名人合作。"},{"en":"The profit motive is the desire to make money from an activity.","zh":"profit motive 是從某活動賺錢的慾望。"},{"en":"A company may change its packaging because the profit motive pushes it to attract more buyers.","zh":"公司可能改變包裝，因為利潤動機推動它吸引更多買家。"},{"en":"If celebrities can earn from photos, they may agree to staged shoots.","zh":"如果名人能從照片賺錢，他們可能同意擺拍。"},{"en":"This phrase explains behaviour driven by financial gain.","zh":"這個片語解釋由金錢利益推動的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"give away their image","meaning":"免費交出自己的形象","examples":[{"en":"Many celebrities do not want to give away their image for free.","zh":"許多名人不想免費交出自己的形象。"},{"en":"To give away their image means to allow others to use their public likeness or identity without payment.","zh":"give away their image 指讓他人不付費使用自己的公眾外貌或身份。"},{"en":"A singer may refuse to give away their image for an advertisement unless a contract is signed.","zh":"歌手可能拒絕免費把形象給廣告使用，除非簽訂合約。"},{"en":"If an image has market value, celebrities try to control who uses it.","zh":"如果形象有市場價值，名人會嘗試控制誰使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes losing commercial control over personal publicity.","zh":"這個片語描述失去對個人宣傳的商業控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make money from","meaning":"從……賺錢","examples":[{"en":"Celebrities want to make money from their image.","zh":"名人想從自己的形象賺錢。"},{"en":"To make money from something means to earn income through it.","zh":"make money from something 指透過某物賺取收入。"},{"en":"A teacher may make money from online courses as well as face-to-face lessons.","zh":"老師可能從網上課程以及面授課堂賺錢。"},{"en":"If a celebrity’s image sells magazines, they may demand a share of the profit.","zh":"如果名人形象能賣雜誌，他們可能要求分享利潤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes turning an asset into income.","zh":"這個片語描述把資產轉化為收入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"run a photography agency","meaning":"經營一間攝影公司","examples":[{"en":"Darren Lyons runs a photography agency called Big Pictures.","zh":"Darren Lyons 經營一間名為 Big Pictures 的攝影公司。"},{"en":"To run a photography agency means to manage a business that produces, sells or licenses photographs.","zh":"run a photography agency 指管理一間製作、出售或授權照片的公司。"},{"en":"A photographer may run a small agency that supplies school event photos.","zh":"攝影師可能經營一間小型公司，提供學校活動照片。"},{"en":"If an agency sells celebrity pictures, it needs photographers, clients and media contacts.","zh":"如果公司出售名人照片，它需要攝影師、客戶和媒體人脈。"},{"en":"This phrase describes managing a photo-related business.","zh":"這個片語描述管理攝影相關企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"specialise in","meaning":"專門從事……","examples":[{"en":"The agency specialises in shooting celebrity pictures.","zh":"該公司專門拍攝名人照片。"},{"en":"To specialise in something means to focus mainly on that type of work or skill.","zh":"specialise in something 指主要專注於某類工作或技能。"},{"en":"A doctor may specialise in children’s health.","zh":"醫生可能專門從事兒童健康。"},{"en":"If an agency specialises in celebrity photos, it develops contacts and methods for that market.","zh":"如果公司專門拍攝名人照片，它會為該市場建立人脈和方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes focused expertise.","zh":"這個片語描述專門技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"shoot celebrities through long lenses","meaning":"用長鏡頭拍攝名人","examples":[{"en":"The agency shoots celebrities through long lenses.","zh":"該公司用長鏡頭拍攝名人。"},{"en":"To shoot celebrities through long lenses means to photograph them from far away using special camera lenses.","zh":"shoot celebrities through long lenses 指使用特殊相機鏡頭從遠處拍攝名人。"},{"en":"A wildlife photographer may use a long lens to photograph birds without disturbing them.","zh":"野生動物攝影師可能使用長鏡頭拍攝鳥類而不打擾牠們。"},{"en":"If celebrity photos are taken through long lenses, they can look secret or intrusive.","zh":"如果名人照片用長鏡頭拍攝，它們可以看似秘密或侵犯私隱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a paparazzi-style photography method.","zh":"這個片語描述狗仔隊風格的攝影方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"as if for","meaning":"好像是為了……","examples":[{"en":"The photos are taken as if for a paparazzi picture.","zh":"這些照片拍得好像是為了狗仔隊照片。"},{"en":"As if for means in a way that looks suitable for a particular purpose, even if that purpose may not be real.","zh":"as if for 指看起來適合某個目的，即使該目的未必真實。"},{"en":"A student may dress as if for a formal interview even on a normal presentation day.","zh":"學生即使只是普通匯報日，也可能穿得好像是為了正式面試。"},{"en":"If staged photos look as if for paparazzi, readers may believe they were captured secretly.","zh":"如果擺拍照片看似狗仔隊照片，讀者可能相信它們是偷拍所得。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an appearance or impression.","zh":"這個片語引入外觀或印象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"paparazzi picture","meaning":"狗仔隊照片","examples":[{"en":"The agency produces pictures that look like paparazzi pictures.","zh":"該公司製作看似狗仔隊照片的圖片。"},{"en":"A paparazzi picture is a photo of a celebrity, usually taken without formal posing and often from a distance.","zh":"paparazzi picture 是名人照片，通常不是正式擺拍，並常從遠處拍攝。"},{"en":"A paparazzi picture may show a singer leaving a restaurant at night.","zh":"狗仔隊照片可能展示歌手晚上離開餐廳。"},{"en":"If a staged photo looks like a paparazzi picture, it can feel more exciting and “real”.","zh":"如果擺拍照片看似狗仔隊照片，它會感覺更刺激和「真實」。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to celebrity photos associated with chasing and surprise.","zh":"這個片語指與追逐和突發拍攝相關的名人照片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"profits from the picture sales","meaning":"照片銷售所得利潤","examples":[{"en":"The profits from the picture sales are shared.","zh":"照片銷售所得利潤會被分享。"},{"en":"Profits from the picture sales are the money earned after photos are sold and costs are paid.","zh":"profits from the picture sales 是照片出售並扣除成本後賺得的金錢。"},{"en":"A school photo company may share profits from picture sales with the school.","zh":"學校攝影公司可能與學校分享照片銷售利潤。"},{"en":"If celebrities receive part of photo profits, they have a reason to cooperate.","zh":"如果名人獲得部分照片利潤，他們就有理由合作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to income generated by selling photographs.","zh":"這個片語指透過出售照片產生的收入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be split between","meaning":"在……之間分配","examples":[{"en":"The profits are split between the subject, the agency and the photographer.","zh":"利潤在被拍攝對象、公司和攝影師之間分配。"},{"en":"To be split between people means to be divided and shared among them.","zh":"be split between people 指在幾個人之間分配和分享。"},{"en":"Prize money may be split between team members after a competition.","zh":"比賽獎金可能在隊員之間分配。"},{"en":"If profits are split fairly, cooperation becomes more attractive.","zh":"如果利潤公平分配，合作會變得更有吸引力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sharing something among several parties.","zh":"這個片語描述把某物分給幾方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the subject","meaning":"被拍攝對象","examples":[{"en":"The subject of the photograph receives part of the profits.","zh":"照片的被拍攝對象會收到部分利潤。"},{"en":"The subject is the person or thing being photographed, studied or discussed.","zh":"subject 是被拍攝、研究或討論的人或事物。"},{"en":"In a portrait, the subject is usually the person sitting for the photo.","zh":"在肖像照中，被拍攝對象通常是坐下拍照的人。"},{"en":"If the subject receives profits, the photo is not purely an invasion of privacy.","zh":"如果被拍攝對象收到利潤，照片就不純粹是侵犯私隱。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who or what the image focuses on.","zh":"這個片語指出圖像聚焦於誰或甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"friendly paparazzi","meaning":"友善的狗仔隊","examples":[{"en":"The agency is almost known as the friendly paparazzi.","zh":"該公司幾乎被稱為友善的狗仔隊。"},{"en":"Friendly paparazzi means photographers who take celebrity-style photos but cooperate with the celebrity.","zh":"friendly paparazzi 指拍攝名人風格照片但與名人合作的攝影師。"},{"en":"A celebrity may prefer friendly paparazzi because the photos look spontaneous but are partly controlled.","zh":"名人可能較喜歡友善的狗仔隊，因為照片看似自然但部分受控。"},{"en":"If paparazzi become friendly, the line between intrusion and publicity becomes blurred.","zh":"如果狗仔隊變得友善，侵犯私隱與宣傳之間的界線會變得模糊。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts aggressive photographers with cooperative ones.","zh":"這個片語把進取攝影師與合作型攝影師作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"high-backed chair","meaning":"高背椅","examples":[{"en":"Mr. Lyons sat in a high-backed chair in his office.","zh":"Lyons 先生坐在辦公室的一張高背椅上。"},{"en":"A high-backed chair is a chair with a tall backrest that supports the upper back or head.","zh":"high-backed chair 是有高椅背、支撐上背或頭部的椅子。"},{"en":"A principal may sit in a high-backed chair behind a large desk.","zh":"校長可能坐在大書桌後的高背椅上。"},{"en":"If an office has a high-backed leather chair, it may create an image of authority.","zh":"如果辦公室有高背皮椅，它可能營造權威形象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical design of a chair.","zh":"這個片語描述椅子的實體設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"judicial chair","meaning":"法官椅","examples":[{"en":"The office contained a red leather judicial chair.","zh":"辦公室裡有一張紅色皮革法官椅。"},{"en":"A judicial chair is a chair that looks like one used by judges or in courtrooms.","zh":"judicial chair 是看起來像法官或法庭使用的椅子。"},{"en":"A theatre set may use a judicial chair to make a scene feel official and serious.","zh":"劇場布景可能使用法官椅，令場景感覺正式嚴肅。"},{"en":"If someone sits in a judicial chair, the setting may suggest power or judgement.","zh":"如果某人坐在法官椅上，場景可能暗示權力或裁決。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a chair with courtroom-like authority.","zh":"這個片語描述具有法庭權威感的椅子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a lion-skin rug","meaning":"獅皮地氈","examples":[{"en":"A lion-skin rug was spread across the floor.","zh":"一張獅皮地氈鋪在地板上。"},{"en":"A lion-skin rug is a floor covering made to look like or from the skin of a lion.","zh":"lion-skin rug 是看起來像獅皮或由獅皮製成的地面覆蓋物。"},{"en":"A film set may use a lion-skin rug to make a room look wealthy or dramatic.","zh":"電影布景可能使用獅皮地氈，令房間看起來富有或戲劇化。"},{"en":"If an office has such a rug, it may project power, luxury or theatrical taste.","zh":"如果辦公室有這種地氈，它可能展示權力、奢華或戲劇化品味。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an eye-catching decorative object.","zh":"這個片語描述引人注目的裝飾物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"retain some control over","meaning":"保留對……的部分控制權","examples":[{"en":"Collaboration allows celebrities to retain some control over their images.","zh":"合作讓名人保留對其形象的部分控制權。"},{"en":"To retain some control over something means to keep part of the power to decide how it is used.","zh":"retain some control over something 指保留部分決定某事如何使用的權力。"},{"en":"A student can retain control over a group project by keeping clear notes and deadlines.","zh":"學生可以透過保留清晰筆記和期限，對小組項目保持控制。"},{"en":"If celebrities cooperate with photographers, they may influence which pictures are published.","zh":"如果名人與攝影師合作，他們可能影響哪些照片被刊登。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping limited but important control.","zh":"這個片語描述保留有限但重要的控制權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"pictures that appear","meaning":"刊出的照片","examples":[{"en":"Celebrities can influence the pictures that appear.","zh":"名人可以影響刊出的照片。"},{"en":"Pictures that appear are photos that are published or shown to the public.","zh":"pictures that appear 是被出版或向公眾展示的照片。"},{"en":"A school may choose the pictures that appear in its annual report carefully.","zh":"學校可能仔細選擇年報中刊出的照片。"},{"en":"If celebrities help choose published pictures, they can protect their public image.","zh":"如果名人協助選擇刊出照片，他們可以保護公眾形象。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to images that finally reach an audience.","zh":"這個片語指最終到達觀眾眼前的圖像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"choosing the pictures","meaning":"選擇照片","examples":[{"en":"Celebrities may have some control over choosing the pictures.","zh":"名人可能對選擇照片有部分控制。"},{"en":"Choosing the pictures means selecting which images will be used, published or displayed.","zh":"choosing the pictures 指選擇哪些圖像會被使用、出版或展示。"},{"en":"A student may spend time choosing the pictures for a presentation so the examples are clear.","zh":"學生可能花時間為匯報選擇照片，讓例子更清楚。"},{"en":"If celebrities choose pictures, they can avoid images that make them look bad.","zh":"如果名人選擇照片，他們可以避免令自己形象差的圖片。"},{"en":"This phrase describes control over visual selection.","zh":"這個片語描述對視覺選擇的控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"for each question","meaning":"對於每一道題","examples":[{"en":"For each question, only one choice is correct.","zh":"對於每一道題，只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"For each question means separately for every question in a task or exam.","zh":"for each question 指對任務或考試中的每一道題分別適用。"},{"en":"For each question, students should read all options before choosing an answer.","zh":"對於每一道題，學生應先讀完所有選項再選答案。"},{"en":"If only one answer is correct for each question, guessing two choices will not help.","zh":"如果每題只有一個答案正確，猜兩個選項也沒有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an instruction that applies item by item.","zh":"這個片語給出逐題適用的指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"only one of the choices is correct","meaning":"只有其中一個選項正確","examples":[{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct in each multiple-choice question.","zh":"每道多項選擇題中只有其中一個選項正確。"},{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct means just a single option gives the right answer.","zh":"only one of the choices is correct 指只有一個選項給出正確答案。"},{"en":"In a grammar quiz, only one of the choices may fit the sentence naturally.","zh":"在文法測驗中，可能只有其中一個選項自然符合句子。"},{"en":"If two options look similar, students must check the exact meaning carefully.","zh":"如果兩個選項看似相似，學生必須仔細檢查確切意思。"},{"en":"This phrase warns learners not to choose more than one answer.","zh":"這個片語提醒學習者不要選多於一個答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"corresponding letter","meaning":"對應的字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the corresponding letter in the answer box.","zh":"考生在答案框中寫上對應的字母。"},{"en":"The corresponding letter is the letter that matches the correct option.","zh":"corresponding letter 是與正確選項相配的字母。"},{"en":"If the correct answer is option C, the corresponding letter is C.","zh":"如果正確答案是選項 C，對應字母就是 C。"},{"en":"If students write the full phrase instead of the required letter, they may lose marks.","zh":"如果學生寫完整詞組而不是所需字母，可能會失分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the answer code linked to a choice.","zh":"這個片語描述與選項相連的答案代碼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the appropriate box","meaning":"適當的方格","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the answer in the appropriate box.","zh":"考生在適當的方格中寫答案。"},{"en":"The appropriate box is the correct space where a particular answer should be written.","zh":"appropriate box 是應填寫某個答案的正確空格。"},{"en":"In an online form, students must type their phone number in the appropriate box.","zh":"在網上表格中，學生必須在適當方格輸入電話號碼。"},{"en":"If an answer is written in the wrong box, it may be marked incorrectly.","zh":"如果答案寫在錯誤方格，可能被判錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the correct place for entering information.","zh":"這個片語描述輸入資訊的正確位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"per head of population","meaning":"按人均計算","examples":[{"en":"Britons buy more celebrity magazines per head of population than Americans.","zh":"按人均計算，英國人比美國人購買更多名人雜誌。"},{"en":"Per head of population means for each person in the population, on average.","zh":"per head of population 指按人口中每人平均計算。"},{"en":"A small city may spend more on libraries per head of population than a larger city.","zh":"小城市按人均計算，圖書館開支可能高於大城市。"},{"en":"If sales are high per head of population, interest is strong even if the total population is small.","zh":"如果按人均計算銷量高，即使總人口小，興趣仍很強。"},{"en":"This phrase compares figures fairly by population size.","zh":"這個片語按人口大小公平比較數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a grand total of","meaning":"總共","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to a grand total of 23 million publications.","zh":"題目提到總共二千三百萬份刊物。"},{"en":"A grand total of something means the final total amount after everything is added together.","zh":"grand total of something 指所有東西加起來後的最終總數。"},{"en":"The charity event raised a grand total of 80,000 dollars.","zh":"慈善活動總共籌得八萬元。"},{"en":"If several magazines together reach a grand total of 23 million, their combined influence is large.","zh":"如果幾本雜誌加起來達二千三百萬份，其合計影響力很大。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the complete total.","zh":"這個片語強調完整總數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"each year","meaning":"每年","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether people buy that number each year.","zh":"該選項問人們是否每年購買那個數量。"},{"en":"Each year means every year or annually.","zh":"each year 指每一年。"},{"en":"The school awards scholarships to several students each year.","zh":"學校每年向幾名學生頒發獎學金。"},{"en":"If a magazine sells millions of copies each year, it has a stable market.","zh":"如果雜誌每年售出數百萬份，它就有穩定市場。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated yearly occurrence.","zh":"這個片語描述每年重複發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a tasteful magazine","meaning":"有品味的雜誌","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether The National Enquirer is a tasteful magazine.","zh":"題目問 The National Enquirer 是否是一本有品味的雜誌。"},{"en":"A tasteful magazine is a magazine considered refined, decent and not vulgar.","zh":"tasteful magazine 是被認為精緻、得體且不庸俗的雜誌。"},{"en":"A tasteful magazine may use elegant design and avoid cheap scandal.","zh":"有品味的雜誌可能使用優雅設計並避免低俗醜聞。"},{"en":"If a publication is a scandal sheet, readers may doubt whether it is tasteful.","zh":"如果刊物是專揭醜聞的小報，讀者可能懷疑它是否有品味。"},{"en":"This phrase judges a magazine’s style and standards.","zh":"這個片語評價雜誌的風格和標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be owned by","meaning":"由……擁有","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether the magazine is owned by British people.","zh":"該選項問該雜誌是否由英國人擁有。"},{"en":"To be owned by someone means to belong legally to that person or group.","zh":"be owned by someone 指在法律上屬於某人或某群體。"},{"en":"A family shop may be owned by three siblings.","zh":"家庭店舖可能由三兄弟姊妹擁有。"},{"en":"If a magazine is owned by a foreign company, its editorial direction may still be local.","zh":"如果雜誌由外國公司擁有，其編輯方向仍可能是本地的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes legal ownership.","zh":"這個片語描述法律上的擁有權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"employ many British journalists","meaning":"僱用很多英國記者","examples":[{"en":"The magazine employs many British journalists.","zh":"該雜誌僱用很多英國記者。"},{"en":"To employ many British journalists means to hire a large number of journalists from Britain.","zh":"employ many British journalists 指聘請大量來自英國的記者。"},{"en":"An international newspaper may employ British journalists for their tabloid experience.","zh":"國際報紙可能因英國記者的小報經驗而聘請他們。"},{"en":"If a magazine hires many British journalists, its tone may reflect British media habits.","zh":"如果雜誌僱用很多英國記者，其語氣可能反映英國媒體習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes staffing a publication with British reporters.","zh":"這個片語描述用英國記者組成刊物團隊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be published for over a hundred years","meaning":"已出版超過一百年","examples":[{"en":"The newspaper has been published for over a hundred years.","zh":"該報已出版超過一百年。"},{"en":"To be published for over a hundred years means to have appeared regularly for more than a century.","zh":"be published for over a hundred years 指定期出版超過一個世紀。"},{"en":"A local newspaper published for over a hundred years may hold important community memory.","zh":"出版超過一百年的本地報紙可能保存重要社區記憶。"},{"en":"If a publication lasts that long, it has survived many market and social changes.","zh":"如果刊物能持續這麼久，它已經經歷許多市場和社會變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long publication history.","zh":"這個片語描述悠久出版歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"publish extracts from","meaning":"刊登……的摘錄","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether the paper published extracts from A Christmas Carol.","zh":"該選項問該報是否刊登《聖誕頌歌》的摘錄。"},{"en":"To publish extracts from a work means to print selected short parts of it.","zh":"publish extracts from a work 指刊登某作品中選出的短部分。"},{"en":"A textbook may publish extracts from a novel so students can analyse the style.","zh":"教科書可能刊登小說摘錄，讓學生分析風格。"},{"en":"If a newspaper publishes extracts from a book, readers get a sample rather than the whole text.","zh":"如果報紙刊登書本摘錄，讀者得到的是樣本，而不是全文。"},{"en":"This phrase describes printing selected passages.","zh":"這個片語描述刊印選段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"work with celebrities","meaning":"與名人合作","examples":[{"en":"Darren Lyons works with celebrities through his photography agency.","zh":"Darren Lyons 透過其攝影公司與名人合作。"},{"en":"To work with celebrities means to cooperate professionally with famous people.","zh":"work with celebrities 指在專業上與名人合作。"},{"en":"A stylist may work with celebrities to prepare outfits for red-carpet events.","zh":"造型師可能與名人合作，準備紅地毯活動服裝。"},{"en":"If photographers work with celebrities, photos may be arranged rather than stolen.","zh":"如果攝影師與名人合作，照片可能是安排好的，而不是偷拍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes professional collaboration with famous people.","zh":"這個片語描述與名人的專業合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be disliked by","meaning":"被……討厭","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether Darren Lyons is disliked by many celebrities.","zh":"該選項問 Darren Lyons 是否被許多名人討厭。"},{"en":"To be disliked by someone means that person has a negative opinion of you.","zh":"be disliked by someone 指某人對你有負面看法。"},{"en":"A strict teacher may be disliked by students at first but respected later.","zh":"嚴格老師起初可能被學生討厭，但後來受到尊重。"},{"en":"If photographers invade privacy, they may be disliked by celebrities.","zh":"如果攝影師侵犯私隱，他們可能被名人討厭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being unpopular with a group.","zh":"這個片語描述不受某群體歡迎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"co-operate with","meaning":"與……合作","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether he co-operates with newspapers and magazines.","zh":"該選項問他是否與報紙和雜誌合作。"},{"en":"To co-operate with someone means to work together with them toward a shared aim.","zh":"co-operate with someone 指與某人合作以達成共同目標。"},{"en":"Parents and teachers co-operate with each other when helping a child improve.","zh":"家長和老師幫助孩子進步時彼此合作。"},{"en":"If agencies co-operate with magazines, celebrity photos can be sold more smoothly.","zh":"如果攝影公司與雜誌合作，名人照片可以更順利出售。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active collaboration.","zh":"這個片語描述積極協作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete the following sentences","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the following sentences using words from the text.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成以下句子。"},{"en":"To complete the following sentences means to fill in missing words in the sentences below.","zh":"complete the following sentences 指填寫下面句子中缺失的字詞。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students must copy the answer accurately from the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生必須準確從文章抄寫答案。"},{"en":"If the grammar around the blank does not fit, the chosen words may be wrong.","zh":"如果空格周圍文法不配合，所選字詞可能錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個詞","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should use no more than three words for each gap.","zh":"考生每個空格應使用不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain one, two or three words only.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案只可包含一個、兩個或三個英文詞。"},{"en":"If the correct answer is “reality TV show”, students must not add extra words.","zh":"如果正確答案是 “reality TV show”，學生不可加額外字詞。"},{"en":"Writing four words can lose marks even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫四個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個片語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"from the text","meaning":"從文章中","examples":[{"en":"The answers must come from the text.","zh":"答案必須來自文章。"},{"en":"From the text means taken directly from the passage, not invented or guessed from outside knowledge.","zh":"from the text 指直接取自篇章，而不是自行編造或用外部知識猜測。"},{"en":"In an IELTS reading task, students should choose words from the text exactly.","zh":"在 IELTS 閱讀題中，學生應準確選擇文章中的字詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is not in the text, students should not create their own wording.","zh":"如果答案不在文章中，學生不應自行創作措辭。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds candidates to rely on the source passage.","zh":"這個片語提醒考生依靠原文。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"for each gap","meaning":"每個空格","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write a short answer for each gap.","zh":"考生為每個空格寫一個簡短答案。"},{"en":"For each gap means separately for every blank space in the exercise.","zh":"for each gap 指對練習中的每個空白位置分別適用。"},{"en":"For each gap, students should check the grammar before writing the answer.","zh":"對每個空格，學生寫答案前應檢查文法。"},{"en":"If one gap needs a noun and another needs a verb, the answers must fit differently.","zh":"如果一個空格需要名詞，另一個需要動詞，答案就必須不同地配合。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an instruction that applies to every blank.","zh":"這個片語給出適用於每個空白的指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be good at","meaning":"擅長……","examples":[{"en":"Britain’s celebrity industry is good at creating celebrity value.","zh":"英國名人產業擅長創造名人價值。"},{"en":"To be good at something means to have skill or ability in doing it well.","zh":"be good at something 指有能力或技能做好某事。"},{"en":"A student may be good at speaking but weaker at writing.","zh":"學生可能擅長口語，但寫作較弱。"},{"en":"If an industry is good at creating value, it can turn attention into money.","zh":"如果行業擅長創造價值，它可以把關注轉化為金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ability in a particular activity.","zh":"這個片語描述某方面的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"increase sales","meaning":"增加銷量","examples":[{"en":"Some stars increase sales of OK!.","zh":"一些明星增加 OK! 的銷量。"},{"en":"To increase sales means to make more products or copies be bought.","zh":"increase sales 指令更多產品或刊物被購買。"},{"en":"A discount can increase sales in a shop during a quiet month.","zh":"折扣可以在淡季增加店舖銷量。"},{"en":"If a celebrity cover increases sales, editors may feature that celebrity again.","zh":"如果名人封面增加銷量，編輯可能再次刊登該名人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rise in the number sold.","zh":"這個片語描述售出數量上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"participate in","meaning":"參與……","examples":[{"en":"Some celebrities participate in relationship journalism.","zh":"一些名人參與關係新聞。"},{"en":"To participate in something means to take part in it.","zh":"participate in something 指參與某事。"},{"en":"Students participate in a debate by preparing arguments and speaking in front of others.","zh":"學生透過準備論點並公開發言來參與辯論。"},{"en":"If celebrities participate in media deals, they help create the stories sold about them.","zh":"如果名人參與媒體交易，他們就幫助創造關於自己的可出售故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active involvement.","zh":"這個片語描述積極投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"interesting subjects for stories","meaning":"有趣的報道題材","examples":[{"en":"Ordinary folk can make interesting subjects for stories.","zh":"普通人可以成為有趣的報道題材。"},{"en":"Interesting subjects for stories are people or topics that provide engaging material to write about.","zh":"interesting subjects for stories 是能提供吸引人寫作材料的人或主題。"},{"en":"A hardworking street cleaner may become an interesting subject for a community profile.","zh":"勤奮的街道清潔工可能成為社區人物專訪的有趣題材。"},{"en":"If readers relate to ordinary people, their lives can make strong stories.","zh":"如果讀者能代入普通人，他們的生活可以成為有力故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what or who can attract readers’ attention.","zh":"這個片語描述甚麼或誰能吸引讀者注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"with regard to","meaning":"關於；就……而言","examples":[{"en":"Collaboration gives celebrities control with regard to published photographs.","zh":"就刊登照片而言，合作給予名人控制權。"},{"en":"With regard to means concerning or about a particular matter.","zh":"with regard to 指關於某個特定事項。"},{"en":"With regard to homework, students want clearer instructions and fair deadlines.","zh":"關於功課，學生想要更清晰指示和公平期限。"},{"en":"If celebrities control matters with regard to photos, they can protect their image.","zh":"如果名人對照片相關事項有控制權，他們就能保護形象。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the specific area being discussed.","zh":"這個片語引入正在討論的特定範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be published","meaning":"被刊登","examples":[{"en":"Celebrities may influence which photographs are published.","zh":"名人可能影響哪些照片被刊登。"},{"en":"To be published means to be printed or released for the public to read or see.","zh":"be published 指被印刷或發布給公眾閱讀或觀看。"},{"en":"A student’s poem may be published in the school magazine.","zh":"學生的詩可能被刊登在學校雜誌中。"},{"en":"If a photo is published widely, it can shape how the public sees a person.","zh":"如果照片被廣泛刊登，它可以塑造公眾如何看待某人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making content public.","zh":"這個片語描述把內容公開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料一致","examples":[{"en":"A TRUE statement agrees with the information given in the passage.","zh":"TRUE 陳述與篇章所給資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指符合篇章所說內容。"},{"en":"If the text says a magazine originated in Spain, a statement saying the same thing agrees with it.","zh":"如果文本說某雜誌起源於西班牙，陳述同一件事就與資料一致。"},{"en":"If a statement changes the meaning, it does not agree even if some words are similar.","zh":"如果陳述改變意思，即使用字相似，也不一致。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in TRUE, FALSE and NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個片語用於 TRUE、FALSE 和 NOT GIVEN 題型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A FALSE statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"FALSE 陳述與篇章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文本相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says a magazine is British-led, saying it has no British staff may contradict the information.","zh":"如果篇章說某雜誌由英國人帶領，說它沒有英國員工可能與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"When a statement directly conflicts with the passage, it should be marked false.","zh":"當陳述與篇章直接衝突，就應標記為錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clear disagreement with the source text.","zh":"這個片語描述與來源文本明確不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"Write NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文中沒有這方面的資料，寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not give enough evidence to decide.","zh":"there is no information on this 指篇章沒有足夠證據作出判斷。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions a magazine’s owner, there is no information on ownership.","zh":"如果篇章從未提及雜誌擁有人，就沒有關於擁有權的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when the passage gives no evidence.","zh":"當篇章沒有證據時，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase explains when to choose NOT GIVEN.","zh":"這個片語解釋何時選擇 NOT GIVEN。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"produce many soap operas","meaning":"製作多部肥皂劇","examples":[{"en":"Aaron Spelling produced many American soap operas.","zh":"Aaron Spelling 製作了多部美國肥皂劇。"},{"en":"To produce many soap operas means to create or manage the making of many long-running television dramas.","zh":"produce many soap operas 指創作或管理多部長篇電視劇的製作。"},{"en":"A television company may produce many soap operas if audiences enjoy daily emotional stories.","zh":"如果觀眾喜歡每日情感故事，電視公司可能製作多部肥皂劇。"},{"en":"If a producer makes many successful shows, their name becomes important in the industry.","zh":"如果製作人創作許多成功節目，其名字就會在行業中變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes high output in television drama production.","zh":"這個片語描述電視劇製作中的高產量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"指的是……","examples":[{"en":"The word “talent” refers to the celebrity in the passage.","zh":"“talent” 這個詞在文章中指的是名人。"},{"en":"To refer to something means to point to, mean or identify it.","zh":"refer to something 指指向、表示或識別某事。"},{"en":"In a reading question, “this problem” may refer to the issue described in the previous sentence.","zh":"在閱讀題中，“this problem” 可能指上一句描述的問題。"},{"en":"If students misread what a pronoun refers to, they may choose the wrong answer.","zh":"如果學生誤解代詞指的是甚麼，可能選錯答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for understanding reference in texts.","zh":"這個片語有助理解文本中的指代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be first published","meaning":"首次出版","examples":[{"en":"The question asks when Confidential was first published.","zh":"題目問 Confidential 何時首次出版。"},{"en":"To be first published means to be printed or released to the public for the first time.","zh":"be first published 指首次被印刷或向公眾發布。"},{"en":"A novel may be first published in a magazine before becoming a book.","zh":"小說可能先在雜誌首次出版，再成為書本。"},{"en":"If students know when something was first published, they can place it in historical context.","zh":"如果學生知道某物何時首次出版，就能把它放在歷史背景中理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first public appearance of a written work.","zh":"這個片語描述書面作品首次公開面世。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be linked to","meaning":"與……有關聯","examples":[{"en":"A celebrity’s ability may not be directly linked to their celebrity rating.","zh":"名人能力未必與其知名度評級有直接關聯。"},{"en":"To be linked to something means to be connected with it.","zh":"be linked to something 指與某事有連繫。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is often linked to weaker concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足常與課堂專注力較弱有關。"},{"en":"If talent is not linked to celebrity rating, fame may depend more on publicity.","zh":"如果才華與知名度評級無關，名氣可能更依賴宣傳。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a relationship between two factors.","zh":"這個片語描述兩個因素之間的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"become more successful","meaning":"變得更成功","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Peter Andre and Katie Price were becoming more successful when they met.","zh":"題目問 Peter Andre 和 Katie Price 相遇時是否正在變得更成功。"},{"en":"To become more successful means to gain more achievement, popularity, money or recognition.","zh":"become more successful 指獲得更多成就、人氣、金錢或認可。"},{"en":"A small business may become more successful after improving service and online reviews.","zh":"小企業在改善服務和網上評價後可能變得更成功。"},{"en":"If celebrities are not becoming more successful, they may seek reality TV or media deals to revive attention.","zh":"如果名人沒有變得更成功，他們可能尋求真人騷或媒體交易來重振關注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rise in career or public success.","zh":"這個片語描述事業或公眾成功上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 101 - The Fame Machine.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 102":[{"front":"Learning about the Past","meaning":"認識過去","examples":[{"en":"Learning about the past can shape how people understand their national identity.","zh":"認識過去可以塑造人們如何理解自己的國家身份。"},{"en":"Learning about the past means studying history to understand how earlier events affect people today.","zh":"Learning about the past 指學習歷史，以理解早前事件如何影響今天的人。"},{"en":"Students learn about the past when they study old photographs, letters, wars, migrations, and family stories.","zh":"學生研究舊照片、書信、戰爭、遷徙和家庭故事時，就是在認識過去。"},{"en":"If people learn about the past honestly, they may understand both the proud and painful parts of their country’s story.","zh":"如果人們誠實地認識過去，就可能理解國家故事中值得自豪和痛苦的部分。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that history is not just memory; it shapes identity and judgement.","zh":"這個片語強調歷史不只是記憶；它會塑造身份和判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the past is a foreign country","meaning":"過去有如異國","examples":[{"en":"The passage begins with the idea that the past is a foreign country.","zh":"文章以「過去有如異國」這個想法開始。"},{"en":"The past is a foreign country means the past can feel strange because people then thought and lived differently.","zh":"the past is a foreign country 指過去可能感覺陌生，因為當時的人思想和生活方式不同。"},{"en":"A student may feel that the past is a foreign country when reading about old school rules and social customs.","zh":"學生閱讀舊校規和社會習俗時，可能覺得過去有如異國。"},{"en":"If people assume the past was just like today, they may misunderstand historical behaviour.","zh":"如果人們假定過去和今天一樣，就可能誤解歷史行為。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds readers that history needs imagination and careful interpretation.","zh":"這個片語提醒讀者，歷史需要想像和仔細解讀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the version that used to be taught","meaning":"以往教授的版本","examples":[{"en":"The version that used to be taught in Irish schools was much simpler.","zh":"愛爾蘭學校以往教授的版本簡單得多。"},{"en":"The version that used to be taught means the explanation or story students learned in the past.","zh":"the version that used to be taught 指學生過去學到的解釋或故事。"},{"en":"Older parents may remember the version that used to be taught before textbooks were updated.","zh":"年長家長可能記得教科書更新前以往教授的版本。"},{"en":"If new evidence appears, the version that used to be taught may become outdated.","zh":"如果新證據出現，以往教授的版本可能變得過時。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts earlier teaching with newer understanding.","zh":"這個片語把早期教學與較新的理解作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Irish schools","meaning":"愛爾蘭學校","examples":[{"en":"Irish schools once taught a simplified version of national history.","zh":"愛爾蘭學校曾教授簡化版國家歷史。"},{"en":"Irish schools are schools in Ireland or within the Irish education system.","zh":"Irish schools 指位於愛爾蘭或屬於愛爾蘭教育制度的學校。"},{"en":"Irish schools may teach students about language, religion, independence, and national memory.","zh":"愛爾蘭學校可能教學生語言、宗教、獨立和國家記憶。"},{"en":"If Irish schools change their history lessons, young people’s understanding of Ireland may also change.","zh":"如果愛爾蘭學校改變歷史課，年輕人對愛爾蘭的理解也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase names the educational setting where the history narrative was taught.","zh":"這個片語指出教授歷史敍事的教育場景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a simple landscape","meaning":"簡單的格局；簡化的面貌","examples":[{"en":"The old version of Irish history had a simple landscape.","zh":"舊版愛爾蘭歷史有一個簡化的面貌。"},{"en":"A simple landscape means a simplified picture of a situation, with few complications.","zh":"a simple landscape 指對某情況作簡化描繪，複雜之處很少。"},{"en":"A teacher gives a simple landscape of a topic first, then adds harder details later.","zh":"老師可能先給出某課題的簡單格局，之後再加入較難細節。"},{"en":"If history is reduced to good people and bad people, its landscape becomes too simple.","zh":"如果歷史被簡化成好人和壞人，其面貌就變得太簡單。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests an easy but incomplete view.","zh":"這個片語暗示容易理解但不完整的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the first invasion by","meaning":"由……首次入侵","examples":[{"en":"The story began with the first invasion by an English king.","zh":"這個故事由一位英格蘭國王首次入侵開始。"},{"en":"The first invasion by someone means the first time that person or power entered a place by force.","zh":"the first invasion by someone 指某人或某政權第一次以武力進入某地。"},{"en":"A history textbook may describe the first invasion by a foreign army before explaining later rule.","zh":"歷史課本可能先描述由外國軍隊首次入侵，再解釋後來統治。"},{"en":"If a national story begins with invasion, it often emphasises suffering and resistance.","zh":"如果國家故事由入侵開始，它通常強調受苦和反抗。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the starting point of a conflict narrative.","zh":"這個片語標示衝突敍事的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"suffer oppression","meaning":"遭受壓迫","examples":[{"en":"Ireland was presented as a country that had suffered oppression for centuries.","zh":"愛爾蘭被呈現為一個幾個世紀以來遭受壓迫的國家。"},{"en":"Suffer oppression means experience unfair control, cruelty, or denial of rights.","zh":"suffer oppression 指經歷不公平控制、殘酷對待或權利被剝奪。"},{"en":"Workers may suffer oppression if they are underpaid, threatened, and unable to complain.","zh":"如果工人被低薪、威脅且無法投訴，他們可能遭受壓迫。"},{"en":"If a group suffers oppression for generations, its identity may be shaped by pain and resistance.","zh":"如果一個群體幾代人遭受壓迫，其身份可能由痛苦和反抗塑造。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious and long-lasting unfair treatment.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重而長期的不公平對待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"at Easter 1916","meaning":"在1916年復活節","examples":[{"en":"At Easter 1916, Irish nationalists rose against British rule.","zh":"在1916年復活節，愛爾蘭民族主義者起義反抗英國統治。"},{"en":"At Easter 1916 refers to the period of the Easter Rising in Ireland in 1916.","zh":"at Easter 1916 指1916年愛爾蘭復活節起義的時期。"},{"en":"A history lesson may use “at Easter 1916” to locate a key nationalist rebellion in time.","zh":"歷史課可能用「在1916年復活節」來定位一次關鍵民族主義起義。"},{"en":"If a date becomes symbolic, it can shape how later generations remember independence.","zh":"如果某日期變得有象徵意義，就能塑造後代如何記住獨立。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a precise historical moment.","zh":"這個片語給出精確歷史時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rise against","meaning":"起義反抗……","examples":[{"en":"Irish rebels rose against the tyrant.","zh":"愛爾蘭叛軍起義反抗暴政者。"},{"en":"Rise against means rebel or take action against a ruler, system, or authority.","zh":"rise against 指反叛或採取行動反對統治者、制度或權威。"},{"en":"Citizens may rise against a government if they feel basic freedoms have been taken away.","zh":"如果公民覺得基本自由被奪走，可能會起義反抗政府。"},{"en":"If people rise against oppression, the conflict may become part of national memory.","zh":"如果人們起義反抗壓迫，該衝突可能成為國家記憶的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests active resistance, not quiet disagreement.","zh":"這個片語暗示主動抵抗，而不是安靜不同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the tyrant","meaning":"暴君；暴政者","examples":[{"en":"The old school narrative presented Britain as the tyrant.","zh":"舊學校敍事把英國呈現為暴政者。"},{"en":"A tyrant is a ruler or power that controls people harshly and unfairly.","zh":"tyrant 指嚴厲而不公平地控制人民的統治者或權力。"},{"en":"In a classroom story, a cruel king may be described as a tyrant if he punishes people for disagreeing.","zh":"在課堂故事中，如果殘酷國王因人民不同意而懲罰他們，他可能被描述為暴君。"},{"en":"If history presents one side as a tyrant, students may see the conflict as morally simple.","zh":"如果歷史把一方呈現為暴政者，學生可能把衝突看得過於道德簡單。"},{"en":"The word strongly suggests oppression and abuse of power.","zh":"這個詞強烈暗示壓迫和濫用權力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"their cause prevailed","meaning":"他們的事業最終勝利","examples":[{"en":"The rebels were killed, but their cause prevailed.","zh":"叛軍被殺，但他們的事業最終勝利。"},{"en":"Their cause prevailed means the aim they fought for eventually succeeded.","zh":"their cause prevailed 指他們為之奮鬥的目標最終成功。"},{"en":"A campaigner may die before a law changes, but their cause can prevail years later.","zh":"社運人士可能在法律改變前去世，但他們的事業多年後可以勝利。"},{"en":"If people remember defeated rebels as heroes, their ideas may win even after their deaths.","zh":"如果人們把失敗叛軍記作英雄，他們的理念即使在死後也可能勝出。"},{"en":"The phrase separates personal defeat from historical success.","zh":"這個片語把個人失敗與歷史成功分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"live happily ever after","meaning":"從此過着幸福生活","examples":[{"en":"The old history story suggested that Ireland lived happily ever after.","zh":"舊歷史故事暗示愛爾蘭從此過着幸福生活。"},{"en":"Live happily ever after means enjoy a perfect happy life after a struggle, like in fairy tales.","zh":"live happily ever after 指像童話一樣，在經歷鬥爭後享有完美幸福生活。"},{"en":"Children’s stories often end with the prince and princess living happily ever after.","zh":"童話故事常以王子和公主從此幸福生活作結。"},{"en":"If history is told as “and then everyone lived happily ever after,” later problems are ignored.","zh":"如果歷史被說成「然後所有人從此幸福生活」，後來問題就被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase can sound ironic when real life is much more complicated.","zh":"當現實生活複雜得多時，這個片語可以帶諷刺意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"awkward episodes","meaning":"尷尬的歷史片段","examples":[{"en":"Awkward episodes in Irish history were often ignored.","zh":"愛爾蘭歷史中尷尬的片段常被忽略。"},{"en":"Awkward episodes are events that are embarrassing, uncomfortable, or difficult to explain.","zh":"awkward episodes 指令人尷尬、不舒服或難以解釋的事件。"},{"en":"A school may avoid awkward episodes from its past if they involve unfair rules or scandals.","zh":"如果學校過去涉及不公平規則或醜聞，可能避免提起尷尬片段。"},{"en":"If awkward episodes are removed from lessons, students receive a cleaner but less honest history.","zh":"如果尷尬片段從課堂中移除，學生得到的是較乾淨但較不誠實的歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to uncomfortable parts of a story.","zh":"這個片語指故事中令人不舒服的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rival Irish nationalist groups","meaning":"互相敵對的愛爾蘭民族主義團體","examples":[{"en":"Rival Irish nationalist groups fought each other in 1922 and 1923.","zh":"互相敵對的愛爾蘭民族主義團體在1922和1923年互相作戰。"},{"en":"Rival Irish nationalist groups were competing groups that both supported Irish nationalism but disagreed with each other.","zh":"rival Irish nationalist groups 指同樣支持愛爾蘭民族主義但彼此不和的競爭團體。"},{"en":"Rival student groups may share a goal but argue over how to achieve it.","zh":"互相競爭的學生小組可能有共同目標，但就如何達成而爭論。"},{"en":"If nationalist groups fight one another, the story becomes more complex than foreign rule versus freedom.","zh":"如果民族主義團體互相作戰，故事就比外國統治對自由更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase shows division within one political movement.","zh":"這個片語顯示一個政治運動內部的分裂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be airbrushed away","meaning":"被淡化抹走","examples":[{"en":"The civil war was airbrushed away from school history.","zh":"內戰被從學校歷史中淡化抹走。"},{"en":"Be airbrushed away means be removed or hidden from a story to make it look cleaner.","zh":"be airbrushed away 指從故事中被移除或隱藏，使它看起來更乾淨。"},{"en":"A company may airbrush away past mistakes from its website to protect its image.","zh":"公司可能把過去錯誤從網站上淡化抹走，以保護形象。"},{"en":"If painful events are airbrushed away, students may never learn why society became divided.","zh":"如果痛苦事件被抹走，學生可能永遠不知道社會為何分裂。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests deliberate smoothing or erasing of history.","zh":"這個片語暗示刻意美化或刪除歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the civil war","meaning":"內戰","examples":[{"en":"The civil war was hardly mentioned in old Irish history lessons.","zh":"內戰在舊愛爾蘭歷史課中幾乎沒有被提及。"},{"en":"A civil war is a war fought between groups within the same country.","zh":"civil war 指同一國家內不同群體之間的戰爭。"},{"en":"A history teacher may explain that civil wars can divide families, towns, and political movements.","zh":"歷史老師可能解釋，內戰可以分裂家庭、城鎮和政治運動。"},{"en":"If a civil war follows independence, it complicates a simple story of national victory.","zh":"如果內戰在獨立後發生，它會令國家勝利的簡單故事變得複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase describes internal conflict, not war against a foreign enemy.","zh":"這個片語描述內部衝突，而不是對外國敵人的戰爭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an embarrassment","meaning":"令人尷尬的事","examples":[{"en":"The civil war was treated as an embarrassment.","zh":"內戰被視為令人尷尬的事。"},{"en":"An embarrassment is something that makes people feel ashamed, awkward, or uncomfortable.","zh":"an embarrassment 指令人感到羞愧、尷尬或不舒服的事情。"},{"en":"A school may see a past scandal as an embarrassment and avoid mentioning it publicly.","zh":"學校可能把過去醜聞視為尷尬事，並避免公開提及。"},{"en":"If a national story needs heroes, internal fighting may be treated as embarrassing.","zh":"如果國家故事需要英雄，內部爭鬥可能被視為尷尬。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests something people prefer not to discuss.","zh":"這個片語暗示人們寧願不討論某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be hardly mentioned","meaning":"幾乎沒有被提及","examples":[{"en":"The civil war was hardly mentioned in Irish schools.","zh":"內戰在愛爾蘭學校中幾乎沒有被提及。"},{"en":"Be hardly mentioned means be spoken about very little or almost not at all.","zh":"be hardly mentioned 指很少或幾乎完全沒有被談及。"},{"en":"Mental health may be hardly mentioned in a school until students begin asking for help.","zh":"在學生開始求助前，心理健康在學校中可能幾乎沒有被提及。"},{"en":"If an event is hardly mentioned, students may think it was unimportant.","zh":"如果事件幾乎沒有被提及，學生可能以為它不重要。"},{"en":"The phrase shows omission through silence.","zh":"這個片語顯示透過沉默造成的遺漏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"these days","meaning":"現今","examples":[{"en":"These days, Irish history lessons are more sophisticated.","zh":"現今，愛爾蘭歷史課更成熟細緻。"},{"en":"These days means nowadays or in the present period.","zh":"these days 指如今或目前這個時期。"},{"en":"These days, many students use online dictionaries as well as printed books.","zh":"現今，許多學生使用網上字典以及印刷書。"},{"en":"If lessons are more open these days, students may hear more than one side of history.","zh":"如果現今課堂更開放，學生可能聽到不只一面歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts the present with the past.","zh":"這個片語把現在與過去作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"more sophisticated","meaning":"更成熟細緻；更有深度","examples":[{"en":"Irish history lessons have become more sophisticated.","zh":"愛爾蘭歷史課已變得更成熟細緻。"},{"en":"More sophisticated means more complex, mature, and careful in understanding.","zh":"more sophisticated 指理解上更複雜、更成熟、更仔細。"},{"en":"A student’s essay becomes more sophisticated when it considers both advantages and disadvantages.","zh":"當學生文章考慮正反兩面時，就變得更有深度。"},{"en":"If history teaching becomes more sophisticated, it includes uncomfortable facts and different perspectives.","zh":"如果歷史教學變得更成熟細緻，就會包含令人不舒服的事實和不同角度。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests depth rather than simple slogans.","zh":"這個片語暗示深度，而不是簡單口號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"deal with facts","meaning":"處理事實","examples":[{"en":"Modern Irish history lessons deal with uncomfortable facts.","zh":"現代愛爾蘭歷史課處理令人不舒服的事實。"},{"en":"Deal with facts means face, discuss, and explain real information honestly.","zh":"deal with facts 指誠實面對、討論和解釋真實資料。"},{"en":"A teacher deals with facts when correcting a student’s mistake rather than hiding it.","zh":"老師糾正學生錯誤而不是隱瞞時，就是在處理事實。"},{"en":"If a society deals with facts, it may have to accept painful parts of its past.","zh":"如果社會處理事實，就可能必須接受過去痛苦的一面。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses honest handling of evidence.","zh":"這個片語強調誠實處理證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have no place in","meaning":"在……中沒有位置","examples":[{"en":"Some facts had no place in a plain tale of heroes and tyrants.","zh":"有些事實在一個英雄與暴君的簡單故事中沒有位置。"},{"en":"Have no place in means not fit into a particular story, system, or situation.","zh":"have no place in 指不適合某故事、制度或情況。"},{"en":"Personal insults have no place in a serious classroom debate.","zh":"人身攻擊在嚴肅課堂辯論中沒有位置。"},{"en":"If a history story allows only heroes and villains, complicated facts have no place in it.","zh":"如果歷史故事只容許英雄和壞人，複雜事實就沒有位置。"},{"en":"The phrase shows exclusion because something does not fit.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事因不合適而被排除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a plain tale of","meaning":"關於……的簡單故事","examples":[{"en":"The old version was a plain tale of heroes and tyrants.","zh":"舊版本是一個關於英雄與暴君的簡單故事。"},{"en":"A plain tale of something is a simple story with little complexity or nuance.","zh":"a plain tale of something 指缺乏複雜性或細微差別的簡單故事。"},{"en":"A teacher may first tell a plain tale of a conflict before adding the harder details.","zh":"老師可能先講一個關於衝突的簡單故事，再加入較難細節。"},{"en":"If national history is a plain tale of good and evil, students may miss internal disagreement.","zh":"如果國家歷史是善惡的簡單故事，學生可能錯過內部分歧。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a story that is easy but oversimplified.","zh":"這個片語暗示故事容易理解但過度簡化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"heroes and tyrants","meaning":"英雄與暴君","examples":[{"en":"The old narrative reduced history to heroes and tyrants.","zh":"舊敍事把歷史簡化為英雄與暴君。"},{"en":"Heroes and tyrants are good liberators and cruel oppressors in a simplified story.","zh":"heroes and tyrants 指簡化故事中的正義解放者和殘酷壓迫者。"},{"en":"Children’s stories often use heroes and tyrants because the moral conflict is easy to follow.","zh":"兒童故事常使用英雄與暴君，因為道德衝突容易理解。"},{"en":"If history is reduced to heroes and tyrants, ordinary people and mixed motives disappear.","zh":"如果歷史被簡化為英雄與暴君，普通人和複雜動機就會消失。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a black-and-white view of history.","zh":"這個片語顯示黑白分明的歷史觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Catholic and Protestant","meaning":"天主教徒和新教徒","examples":[{"en":"Catholic and Protestant Irish people fought for Britain during the wars.","zh":"天主教徒和新教徒愛爾蘭人在戰爭期間為英國作戰。"},{"en":"Catholic and Protestant refers to two major Christian traditions often linked to Irish identity and politics.","zh":"Catholic and Protestant 指兩大基督教傳統，常與愛爾蘭身份和政治有關。"},{"en":"A history class may discuss Catholic and Protestant communities when studying Ireland.","zh":"歷史課研究愛爾蘭時，可能討論天主教徒和新教徒社群。"},{"en":"If both Catholic and Protestant Irish people fought for Britain, the story is more complex than simple opposition.","zh":"如果天主教徒和新教徒愛爾蘭人都為英國作戰，故事就比簡單對抗更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase marks religious and social identities.","zh":"這個片語標示宗教和社會身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fight for Britain","meaning":"為英國作戰","examples":[{"en":"Many Irish people fought for Britain during the two world wars.","zh":"許多愛爾蘭人在兩次世界大戰期間為英國作戰。"},{"en":"Fight for Britain means serve or fight on Britain’s side in war.","zh":"fight for Britain 指在戰爭中為英國一方服役或作戰。"},{"en":"Soldiers may fight for a country even if their feelings about that country are complicated.","zh":"士兵即使對某國感情複雜，仍可能為該國作戰。"},{"en":"If Irish people fought for Britain, this challenges a simple story of Ireland only opposing Britain.","zh":"如果愛爾蘭人為英國作戰，就挑戰愛爾蘭只反對英國的簡單故事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes military service on Britain’s side.","zh":"這個片語描述站在英國一方的軍事服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"during the two world wars","meaning":"在兩次世界大戰期間","examples":[{"en":"Many Irish people fought for Britain during the two world wars.","zh":"許多愛爾蘭人在兩次世界大戰期間為英國作戰。"},{"en":"During the two world wars means in the periods of World War I and World War II.","zh":"during the two world wars 指在第一次世界大戰和第二次世界大戰期間。"},{"en":"Many families changed their lives during the two world wars because of rationing, fear, and military service.","zh":"許多家庭在兩次世界大戰期間因配給、恐懼和軍事服務而改變生活。"},{"en":"If a country’s people fought in both wars, its history cannot be separated from global conflict.","zh":"如果一個國家的人在兩次戰爭中作戰，其歷史就不能與全球衝突分開。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a major twentieth-century historical context.","zh":"這個片語給出二十世紀的重要歷史背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"become uneasy about","meaning":"對……感到不安","examples":[{"en":"Some people in Ireland became uneasy about a crude view of history.","zh":"愛爾蘭有些人開始對粗糙的歷史觀感到不安。"},{"en":"Become uneasy about means start to feel worried or uncomfortable about something.","zh":"become uneasy about 指開始對某事感到擔心或不舒服。"},{"en":"Parents may become uneasy about a school policy if it seems unfair to weaker students.","zh":"如果學校政策似乎對較弱學生不公平，家長可能感到不安。"},{"en":"If a simple history view fuels conflict, people may begin to question it.","zh":"如果簡化歷史觀加劇衝突，人們可能開始質疑它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growing discomfort or concern.","zh":"這個片語描述逐漸出現的不適或關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a crude view of","meaning":"對……的粗糙看法","examples":[{"en":"A crude view of national history was seen as dangerous.","zh":"對國家歷史的粗糙看法被視為危險。"},{"en":"A crude view of something is a rough, oversimplified, and insensitive understanding of it.","zh":"a crude view of something 指對某事粗略、過度簡化且不細緻的理解。"},{"en":"A crude view of poverty blames poor people without considering wages, housing, or health.","zh":"對貧窮的粗糙看法會責怪窮人，而不考慮工資、住屋或健康。"},{"en":"If history is taught crudely, students may learn slogans instead of causes and consequences.","zh":"如果歷史被粗糙地教授，學生可能學到口號而不是原因和後果。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises shallow understanding.","zh":"這個片語批評膚淺理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"national history","meaning":"國家歷史","examples":[{"en":"A simplified version of national history could fuel conflict.","zh":"簡化版國家歷史可能加劇衝突。"},{"en":"National history is the story a country tells about its past, people, struggles, and identity.","zh":"national history 指一個國家講述其過去、人民、鬥爭和身份的故事。"},{"en":"Students study national history when they learn about independence, wars, leaders, and social change.","zh":"學生學習獨立、戰爭、領袖和社會變革時，就是在學習國家歷史。"},{"en":"If national history ignores minorities, some citizens may feel excluded from the story.","zh":"如果國家歷史忽略少數群體，有些公民可能覺得自己被排除在故事之外。"},{"en":"The phrase connects the past with national identity.","zh":"這個片語把過去與國家身份連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fuel a conflict","meaning":"加劇衝突","examples":[{"en":"A crude view of history was fuelling a conflict in Northern Ireland.","zh":"粗糙的歷史觀正在加劇北愛爾蘭的衝突。"},{"en":"Fuel a conflict means make a disagreement or fight stronger and harder to stop.","zh":"fuel a conflict 指令分歧或爭鬥變得更強、更難停止。"},{"en":"Rumours can fuel a conflict between classmates if no one checks the facts.","zh":"如果沒有人核實事實，謠言可以加劇同學之間的衝突。"},{"en":"If history lessons present only blame and hatred, they may intensify political violence.","zh":"如果歷史課只呈現責怪和仇恨，可能加劇政治暴力。"},{"en":"The phrase compares conflict to a fire that grows when fuel is added.","zh":"這個片語把衝突比作被加燃料後變大的火。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the north of the island","meaning":"島的北部","examples":[{"en":"The conflict took place in the north of the island.","zh":"衝突發生在島的北部。"},{"en":"The north of the island means the northern part of an island.","zh":"the north of the island 指一個島嶼的北部地區。"},{"en":"A tourist map may show beaches in the south and mountains in the north of the island.","zh":"旅遊地圖可能顯示島南有海灘，島北有山脈。"},{"en":"If conflict is concentrated in one region, local history and identity may be especially important there.","zh":"如果衝突集中在某一地區，當地歷史和身份可能尤其重要。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a geographical location.","zh":"這個片語給出地理位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a fall in the influence of","meaning":"……影響力下降","examples":[{"en":"A fall in the influence of the Catholic church also changed history teaching.","zh":"天主教會影響力下降也改變了歷史教學。"},{"en":"A fall in the influence of something means it becomes less powerful or less respected.","zh":"a fall in the influence of something 指某事物變得較不有力或較不受尊重。"},{"en":"A fall in the influence of printed newspapers has changed how people get news.","zh":"印刷報紙影響力下降已改變人們獲取新聞的方式。"},{"en":"If a church loses influence, schools may become more willing to teach history in different ways.","zh":"如果教會影響力下降，學校可能更願意以不同方式教授歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase describes declining social power.","zh":"這個片語描述社會力量下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the Catholic church","meaning":"天主教會","examples":[{"en":"The Catholic church once had strong influence in Ireland.","zh":"天主教會曾在愛爾蘭有強大影響力。"},{"en":"The Catholic church is a major Christian institution historically important in many societies.","zh":"the Catholic church 指在許多社會中具有歷史重要性的主要基督宗教機構。"},{"en":"A history lesson may discuss how the Catholic church influenced education, family life, and politics.","zh":"歷史課可能討論天主教會如何影響教育、家庭生活和政治。"},{"en":"If a religious institution loses influence, national identity may become less tied to religion.","zh":"如果宗教機構失去影響力，國家身份可能較少與宗教綁在一起。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to both religious authority and social influence.","zh":"這個片語同時指宗教權威和社會影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rest on","meaning":"建基於……","examples":[{"en":"The church’s authority had rested on a fusion of religion and patriotism.","zh":"教會權威曾建基於宗教與愛國主義的融合。"},{"en":"Rest on means be based on or supported by something.","zh":"rest on 指以某事作為基礎或支撐。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may rest on steady practice rather than last-minute revision.","zh":"學生信心可能建基於穩定練習，而不是臨急抱佛腳。"},{"en":"If authority rests on one strong idea, that authority may weaken when the idea is questioned.","zh":"如果權威建基於一個強大觀念，當該觀念被質疑時，權威可能削弱。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the foundation of power or belief.","zh":"這個片語指出權力或信念的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a deft fusion between","meaning":"……之間巧妙的結合","examples":[{"en":"The church’s authority rested on a deft fusion between religion and patriotism.","zh":"教會權威建基於宗教與愛國主義之間巧妙的結合。"},{"en":"A deft fusion between two things is a skilful combination of them.","zh":"a deft fusion between two things 指把兩件事巧妙結合。"},{"en":"A good speech may use a deft fusion between personal story and public argument.","zh":"好演講可能把個人故事和公共論證巧妙結合。"},{"en":"If religion and patriotism are combined skilfully, people may see faith and nation as one identity.","zh":"如果宗教與愛國主義被巧妙結合，人們可能把信仰和國家視為同一身份。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses clever blending.","zh":"這個片語強調聰明而靈巧的融合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"religion and patriotism","meaning":"宗教與愛國主義","examples":[{"en":"Religion and patriotism were closely linked in traditional Irish identity.","zh":"宗教與愛國主義在傳統愛爾蘭身份中緊密相連。"},{"en":"Religion and patriotism are faith-based belief and love or loyalty toward one’s country.","zh":"religion and patriotism 指宗教信仰，以及對自己國家的愛或忠誠。"},{"en":"A national ceremony may mix religion and patriotism through prayers, flags, and songs.","zh":"國家典禮可能透過祈禱、旗幟和歌曲結合宗教與愛國主義。"},{"en":"If religion and patriotism become fused, disagreeing with one may feel like betraying the other.","zh":"如果宗教與愛國主義融合，反對其中一方可能感覺像背叛另一方。"},{"en":"The phrase describes two powerful sources of identity.","zh":"這個片語描述兩種強大的身份來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at work","meaning":"在發揮作用","examples":[{"en":"A broader social shift was also at work.","zh":"更廣泛的社會轉變也在發揮作用。"},{"en":"At work means operating or having an effect, even if it is not obvious.","zh":"at work 指正在運作或產生影響，即使未必明顯。"},{"en":"When students suddenly improve, quiet confidence may be at work behind the scenes.","zh":"當學生突然進步，背後可能是安靜的信心在發揮作用。"},{"en":"If social change is at work, school lessons may gradually change too.","zh":"如果社會變化在發揮作用，學校課程也可能逐漸改變。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a force influencing events.","zh":"這個片語指影響事件的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a broader shift","meaning":"更廣泛的轉變","examples":[{"en":"A broader shift made Ireland more open to complex history.","zh":"更廣泛的轉變令愛爾蘭更願意接受複雜歷史。"},{"en":"A broader shift is a wider change in society, not just one small event.","zh":"a broader shift 指社會中更廣泛的變化，而不是單一小事件。"},{"en":"A broader shift toward online learning changed how teachers give homework.","zh":"轉向網上學習的更廣泛轉變改變了老師派功課的方式。"},{"en":"If a whole society becomes richer and more confident, its history teaching may also change.","zh":"如果整個社會變得更富裕和自信，其歷史教學也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes large-scale change.","zh":"這個片語描述大規模變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rich, confident and cosmopolitan","meaning":"富裕、自信而國際化","examples":[{"en":"A rich, confident and cosmopolitan state needed fewer simple myths.","zh":"一個富裕、自信而國際化的國家較少需要簡單神話。"},{"en":"Rich, confident and cosmopolitan describes a society that is wealthy, self-assured, and open to the world.","zh":"rich, confident and cosmopolitan 指一個富裕、有自信且向世界開放的社會。"},{"en":"A cosmopolitan city may welcome people, food, languages, and ideas from many countries.","zh":"國際化城市可能歡迎來自許多國家的人民、食物、語言和思想。"},{"en":"If a country becomes more confident, it may feel less need to hide difficult history.","zh":"如果一個國家變得更自信，就可能較少需要隱藏困難歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests maturity and openness.","zh":"這個片語暗示成熟和開放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"see less need to","meaning":"較少覺得有需要……","examples":[{"en":"A confident state saw less need to teach simple nationalist ideas.","zh":"自信的國家較少覺得有需要教授簡單民族主義觀念。"},{"en":"See less need to means feel that something is less necessary than before.","zh":"see less need to 指覺得某事比以前較不必要。"},{"en":"A student who understands grammar may see less need to memorise every sentence.","zh":"理解文法的學生可能較少覺得有需要背誦每一句。"},{"en":"If society becomes more secure, it may rely less on simple patriotic myths.","zh":"如果社會變得更有安全感，就可能較少依賴簡單愛國神話。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reduced perceived necessity.","zh":"這個片語描述主觀上覺得必要性降低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"drum simple ideas into","meaning":"向……反覆灌輸簡單觀念","examples":[{"en":"The state saw less need to drum simple ideas into its youth.","zh":"國家較少覺得有需要向其年輕人反覆灌輸簡單觀念。"},{"en":"Drum simple ideas into someone means repeatedly teach simple ideas until people accept them.","zh":"drum simple ideas into someone 指反覆教授簡單觀念，直到人們接受。"},{"en":"A coach may drum basic safety rules into beginners before letting them train alone.","zh":"教練可能在初學者單獨訓練前，反覆灌輸基本安全規則。"},{"en":"If schools drum one national story into students, they may discourage independent thinking.","zh":"如果學校向學生反覆灌輸單一國家故事，可能壓抑獨立思考。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests repeated teaching that can feel forceful.","zh":"這個片語暗示重複且可能帶強迫性的教導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"its youth","meaning":"其年輕人","examples":[{"en":"The state no longer needed to drum simple ideas into its youth.","zh":"國家不再需要向其年輕人反覆灌輸簡單觀念。"},{"en":"Its youth means the young people of a country, society, or organisation.","zh":"its youth 指一個國家、社會或組織的年輕人。"},{"en":"A city invests in its youth by building libraries, sports centres, and training programmes.","zh":"城市透過建圖書館、體育中心和培訓計劃投資於其年輕人。"},{"en":"If a country teaches its youth narrow history, the next generation may inherit narrow views.","zh":"如果國家向其年輕人教授狹窄歷史，下一代可能繼承狹窄觀點。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to young citizens as a group.","zh":"這個片語指作為群體的年輕公民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"risk encouraging violence","meaning":"有鼓勵暴力的風險","examples":[{"en":"Simple historical ideas risked encouraging violence.","zh":"簡單歷史觀有鼓勵暴力的風險。"},{"en":"Risk encouraging violence means create a danger that people may become more willing to use force.","zh":"risk encouraging violence 指造成危險，使人們可能更願意使用武力。"},{"en":"Hate-filled slogans risk encouraging violence between rival groups.","zh":"充滿仇恨的口號有鼓勵敵對群體之間暴力的風險。"},{"en":"If history lessons teach only blame, they may make conflict seem justified.","zh":"如果歷史課只教責怪，可能令人覺得衝突合理。"},{"en":"The phrase warns about a dangerous possible result.","zh":"這個片語警告一種危險的可能結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"argue over","meaning":"就……爭論","examples":[{"en":"Countries often argue over what children should be taught.","zh":"各國常就孩子應學甚麼而爭論。"},{"en":"Argue over means disagree and debate about a particular issue.","zh":"argue over 指就某議題不同意並辯論。"},{"en":"Parents may argue over how much homework is healthy for children.","zh":"家長可能就多少功課對孩子健康而爭論。"},{"en":"If history shapes identity, countries will argue over which version schools should teach.","zh":"如果歷史塑造身份，國家就會爭論學校應教哪個版本。"},{"en":"The phrase describes disagreement about a topic.","zh":"這個片語描述圍繞某主題的分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"what to tell the children","meaning":"應該告訴孩子甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Many countries debate what to tell the children about the past.","zh":"許多國家爭論應該告訴孩子關於過去的甚麼。"},{"en":"What to tell the children means what version of events young people should be taught.","zh":"what to tell the children 指應教年輕人哪個事件版本。"},{"en":"Teachers must decide what to tell the children when a topic is painful but important.","zh":"當課題痛苦但重要時，老師必須決定應該告訴孩子甚麼。"},{"en":"If a society hides difficult history from children, they may learn a distorted story.","zh":"如果社會向孩子隱藏困難歷史，他們可能學到扭曲故事。"},{"en":"The phrase raises a question about education and responsibility.","zh":"這個片語提出關於教育和責任的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"collective past","meaning":"集體過去","examples":[{"en":"Countries argue about how to present their collective past.","zh":"各國爭論如何呈現自己的集體過去。"},{"en":"Collective past means the shared history of a group, nation, or community.","zh":"collective past 指一個群體、國家或社區共同擁有的歷史。"},{"en":"A family’s collective past may include migration, hardship, business, and celebration.","zh":"家庭的集體過去可能包括遷徙、艱辛、事業和慶祝。"},{"en":"If a collective past includes pain and shame, people may disagree over how to teach it.","zh":"如果集體過去包含痛苦和羞愧，人們可能就如何教授它意見不一。"},{"en":"The phrase connects memory with group identity.","zh":"這個片語把記憶與群體身份連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"look to Ireland enviously","meaning":"羨慕地看待愛爾蘭","examples":[{"en":"Many countries may look to Ireland enviously.","zh":"許多國家可能羨慕地看待愛爾蘭。"},{"en":"Look to Ireland enviously means view Ireland with admiration because it managed something difficult.","zh":"look to Ireland enviously 指因愛爾蘭成功處理困難事情而羨慕地看待它。"},{"en":"Schools may look to another school enviously if it handles exam reform smoothly.","zh":"如果另一所學校順利處理考試改革，學校可能羨慕地看待它。"},{"en":"If Ireland changed history teaching without serious conflict, other countries may wish they could do the same.","zh":"如果愛爾蘭在沒有嚴重衝突下改變歷史教學，其他國家可能希望自己也做到。"},{"en":"The phrase describes admiring comparison.","zh":"這個片語描述帶羨慕的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"seamless transition","meaning":"無縫過渡","examples":[{"en":"Ireland made a relatively seamless transition to a more open view of history.","zh":"愛爾蘭相對順利地無縫過渡至更開放的歷史觀。"},{"en":"A seamless transition is a smooth change from one state to another without obvious disruption.","zh":"seamless transition 指從一種狀態平順轉向另一種狀態，沒有明顯中斷。"},{"en":"A school makes a seamless transition to online lessons if students and teachers adapt quickly.","zh":"如果學生和老師很快適應，學校就能無縫過渡至網上課堂。"},{"en":"If a curriculum changes smoothly, there may be less public anger and confusion.","zh":"如果課程順利改變，公眾憤怒和混亂可能較少。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses smoothness in change.","zh":"這個片語強調改變中的平滑感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"nationalist view of history","meaning":"民族主義歷史觀","examples":[{"en":"Ireland moved away from a narrow nationalist view of history.","zh":"愛爾蘭逐漸擺脫狹窄的民族主義歷史觀。"},{"en":"A nationalist view of history explains the past mainly through national pride, struggle, and identity.","zh":"nationalist view of history 指主要透過民族自豪、鬥爭和身份來解釋過去。"},{"en":"A textbook with a nationalist view may emphasise heroes and independence but ignore internal conflict.","zh":"具有民族主義歷史觀的教科書可能強調英雄和獨立，但忽略內部衝突。"},{"en":"If history teaching moves away from a narrow nationalist view, it may include minorities and uncomfortable facts.","zh":"如果歷史教學擺脫狹窄民族主義觀，可能會包含少數群體和令人不舒服的事實。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a nation-centred interpretation of the past.","zh":"這個片語描述以民族為中心的歷史解讀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"open-minded view","meaning":"開明的看法","examples":[{"en":"Irish history teaching shifted towards a more open-minded view.","zh":"愛爾蘭歷史教學轉向更開明的看法。"},{"en":"An open-minded view is a willingness to consider different facts, perspectives, and interpretations.","zh":"open-minded view 指願意考慮不同事實、角度和解釋。"},{"en":"A student shows an open-minded view when they listen to both sides before judging.","zh":"學生在判斷前聆聽雙方時，就是展現開明看法。"},{"en":"If history is taught open-mindedly, students can compare evidence instead of memorising slogans.","zh":"如果歷史以開明方式教授，學生可以比較證據，而不是背誦口號。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests flexibility and fairness in thinking.","zh":"這個片語暗示思考上的彈性和公平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be an exception","meaning":"是例外","examples":[{"en":"Ireland’s transition is an exception.","zh":"愛爾蘭的轉變是例外。"},{"en":"Be an exception means be different from the usual rule or pattern.","zh":"be an exception 指不同於一般規則或模式。"},{"en":"Most students found the test difficult, but one student was an exception.","zh":"大多數學生覺得測驗困難，但有一名學生是例外。"},{"en":"If most countries fight over history teaching, a smooth transition is unusual.","zh":"如果大多數國家都為歷史教學爭論，順利過渡就不尋常。"},{"en":"The phrase marks something that does not follow the normal pattern.","zh":"這個片語標示不符合正常模式的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"history curriculum","meaning":"歷史課程","examples":[{"en":"A history curriculum can reveal how a nation sees itself.","zh":"歷史課程可以揭示一個國家如何看待自己。"},{"en":"A history curriculum is the planned content and approach used to teach history in schools.","zh":"history curriculum 指學校用來教授歷史的計劃內容和方法。"},{"en":"A school history curriculum may include ancient civilisations, national independence, wars, and social movements.","zh":"學校歷史課程可能包括古代文明、國家獨立、戰爭和社會運動。"},{"en":"If a curriculum changes, students may learn a different version of national identity.","zh":"如果課程改變，學生可能學到不同版本的國家身份。"},{"en":"The phrase connects education with public memory.","zh":"這個片語把教育與公共記憶連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a telling sign of","meaning":"……的明顯標誌","examples":[{"en":"A history curriculum is a telling sign of national self-image.","zh":"歷史課程是國家自我形象的明顯標誌。"},{"en":"A telling sign of something is a clear clue that reveals an important truth.","zh":"a telling sign of something 指揭示重要事實的清楚線索。"},{"en":"Empty desks can be a telling sign of students’ loss of interest in a course.","zh":"空書桌可以是學生對課程失去興趣的明顯標誌。"},{"en":"If a country teaches only heroic stories, that may reveal how it wants to see itself.","zh":"如果一個國家只教授英雄故事，這可能揭示它希望如何看待自己。"},{"en":"The phrase points to evidence that says more than it first appears to.","zh":"這個片語指出比表面看來更有意思的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a nation and its elites","meaning":"一個國家及其精英","examples":[{"en":"The curriculum shows how a nation and its elites see themselves.","zh":"課程顯示一個國家及其精英如何看待自己。"},{"en":"A nation and its elites means a country as a whole and its powerful political, cultural, or educational leaders.","zh":"a nation and its elites 指整個國家以及其有權力的政治、文化或教育領袖。"},{"en":"A national museum may reveal how a nation and its elites want history to be remembered.","zh":"國家博物館可能揭示一個國家及其精英希望歷史如何被記住。"},{"en":"If elites control textbooks, they can influence what children learn about the past.","zh":"如果精英控制教科書，他們就能影響孩子如何學習過去。"},{"en":"The phrase distinguishes ordinary society from powerful decision-makers.","zh":"這個片語區分普通社會與有權決策者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"see themselves as","meaning":"將自己視為……","examples":[{"en":"Nations may see themselves as victims or as imperial powers.","zh":"國家可能將自己視為受害者或帝國權力的實踐者。"},{"en":"See themselves as means understand or present their own identity in a particular way.","zh":"see themselves as 指以某特定方式理解或呈現自己的身份。"},{"en":"A student may see herself as weak at English until good feedback changes her confidence.","zh":"學生可能一直將自己視為英文弱，直到良好回饋改變她的信心。"},{"en":"If a country sees itself as a victim, it may teach history through suffering and resistance.","zh":"如果國家將自己視為受害者，可能透過受苦和反抗來教授歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase describes self-image.","zh":"這個片語描述自我形象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"victims of colonialism","meaning":"殖民主義的受害者","examples":[{"en":"Some nations see themselves as victims of colonialism.","zh":"有些國家將自己視為殖民主義的受害者。"},{"en":"Victims of colonialism are peoples or nations harmed by foreign rule, exploitation, or control.","zh":"victims of colonialism 指受到外國統治、剝削或控制傷害的人民或國家。"},{"en":"History classes may discuss victims of colonialism when studying land loss and cultural suppression.","zh":"歷史課研究土地喪失和文化壓制時，可能討論殖民主義的受害者。"},{"en":"If a nation sees itself this way, its history lessons may stress injustice and liberation.","zh":"如果一個國家這樣看待自己，其歷史課可能強調不公義和解放。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a historical identity shaped by colonial harm.","zh":"這個片語描述由殖民傷害塑造的歷史身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"practitioners of imperial power","meaning":"帝國權力的實踐者","examples":[{"en":"Other nations see themselves as practitioners of imperial power.","zh":"其他國家將自己視為帝國權力的實踐者。"},{"en":"Practitioners of imperial power are states or groups that have ruled, controlled, or dominated others.","zh":"practitioners of imperial power 指曾統治、控制或支配其他人的國家或群體。"},{"en":"A museum may examine how practitioners of imperial power justified conquest and trade control.","zh":"博物館可能檢視帝國權力的實踐者如何為征服和貿易控制辯護。"},{"en":"If a country once held empire, it may teach history with pride, regret, or defensiveness.","zh":"如果一個國家曾擁有帝國，它可能以自豪、懊悔或防衛心態教授歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase describes those who used imperial authority.","zh":"這個片語描述曾使用帝國權威的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"repentant or defiant","meaning":"懺悔的或抗拒認錯的","examples":[{"en":"Former imperial powers may be repentant or defiant.","zh":"前帝國強權可能是懺悔的，也可能是抗拒認錯的。"},{"en":"Repentant or defiant means sorry for past actions or stubbornly unwilling to apologise.","zh":"repentant or defiant 指為過去行為感到抱歉，或頑固地不願道歉。"},{"en":"A student caught cheating may be repentant and apologise, or defiant and blame the teacher.","zh":"被抓到作弊的學生可能懺悔並道歉，也可能抗拒承認並責怪老師。"},{"en":"If a country regrets empire, its textbooks may differ from those of a country that defends empire.","zh":"如果國家對帝國歷史感到後悔，其教科書可能與捍衛帝國的國家不同。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts apology with resistance.","zh":"這個片語對比道歉與抗拒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the modern history of","meaning":"在……的近代史中","examples":[{"en":"In the modern history of Mexico, textbook reform was a landmark.","zh":"在墨西哥近代史中，教科書改革是一個里程碑。"},{"en":"In the modern history of means within the recent historical development of a country or place.","zh":"in the modern history of 指在某國家或地方近期歷史發展中。"},{"en":"In the modern history of Hong Kong, education reform has changed how students prepare for exams.","zh":"在香港近代史中，教育改革改變了學生準備考試的方式。"},{"en":"If an event is important in modern history, it affects how people understand recent society.","zh":"如果事件在近代史中重要，它會影響人們如何理解近期社會。"},{"en":"The phrase places an event in a recent national timeline.","zh":"這個片語把事件放入近期國家時間線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a big landmark","meaning":"重要里程碑","examples":[{"en":"The introduction of new textbooks was a big landmark.","zh":"新教科書的引入是一個重要里程碑。"},{"en":"A big landmark is an important event that marks major change.","zh":"a big landmark 指標誌重大改變的重要事件。"},{"en":"A school’s first public exam success may be a big landmark in its development.","zh":"學校首次公開試成功可能是其發展中的重要里程碑。"},{"en":"If new textbooks change children’s view of history, the reform is a landmark.","zh":"如果新教科書改變孩子對歷史的看法，該改革就是里程碑。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a turning point.","zh":"這個片語突出轉捩點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the introduction of","meaning":"……的引入","examples":[{"en":"The introduction of less anti-American textbooks changed Mexican history teaching.","zh":"較少反美色彩教科書的引入改變了墨西哥歷史教學。"},{"en":"The introduction of something means the act of bringing it into use for the first time.","zh":"the introduction of something 指首次把某物投入使用的行動。"},{"en":"The introduction of online homework changed how teachers checked assignments.","zh":"網上功課的引入改變了老師檢查作業的方式。"},{"en":"If new textbooks are introduced, teachers and students may need to adjust.","zh":"如果新教科書被引入，老師和學生可能需要適應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the start of using something new.","zh":"這個片語描述開始使用新事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"textbooks","meaning":"教科書","examples":[{"en":"Textbooks can shape how children understand national history.","zh":"教科書可以塑造孩子如何理解國家歷史。"},{"en":"Textbooks are books used in schools to teach a subject in an organised way.","zh":"textbooks 指學校用來有系統教授某科目的書。"},{"en":"A history textbook may choose which events to include, shorten, or leave out.","zh":"歷史教科書可能選擇包含、簡化或省略哪些事件。"},{"en":"If textbooks change, students may learn different words for the same event.","zh":"如果教科書改變，學生可能學到描述同一事件的不同詞語。"},{"en":"The word refers to teaching materials that can influence memory and identity.","zh":"這個詞指會影響記憶和身份的教材。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a bit less anti-American","meaning":"較少反美色彩","examples":[{"en":"The new textbooks were a bit less anti-American.","zh":"新教科書較少反美色彩。"},{"en":"A bit less anti-American means slightly less hostile or critical toward America.","zh":"a bit less anti-American 指對美國稍為較少敵意或批判。"},{"en":"A newspaper article may be a bit less anti-government if it includes both criticism and praise.","zh":"如果報章文章同時包含批評和讚賞，它可能較少反政府色彩。"},{"en":"If textbooks become less hostile to a foreign power, they may reflect changing politics.","zh":"如果教科書對外國強權較少敵意，可能反映政治轉變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small shift in tone.","zh":"這個片語描述語氣上的小變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"history teaching","meaning":"歷史教學","examples":[{"en":"History teaching can serve political and educational purposes.","zh":"歷史教學可以服務政治和教育目的。"},{"en":"History teaching is the way schools teach students about the past.","zh":"history teaching 指學校教學生認識過去的方式。"},{"en":"Good history teaching asks students to read evidence, compare views, and explain causes.","zh":"良好歷史教學要求學生閱讀證據、比較觀點並解釋原因。"},{"en":"If history teaching becomes propaganda, students may memorise myths instead of thinking critically.","zh":"如果歷史教學變成宣傳，學生可能背誦神話而不是批判思考。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to both content and method.","zh":"這個片語同時指內容和方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"inculcation of","meaning":"灌輸……","examples":[{"en":"Some states use history teaching for the inculcation of foundation myths.","zh":"有些國家使用歷史教學來灌輸建國神話。"},{"en":"Inculcation of means repeated teaching intended to make people accept an idea deeply.","zh":"inculcation of 指透過反覆教導，使人深深接受某觀念。"},{"en":"The inculcation of discipline may happen through daily routines and strict rules.","zh":"紀律的灌輸可能透過每日常規和嚴格規則發生。"},{"en":"If schools repeatedly teach one national myth, students may accept it without question.","zh":"如果學校反覆教授單一國家神話，學生可能不加質疑地接受它。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests forceful or one-sided teaching.","zh":"這個片語常暗示強硬或單方面教導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"foundation myths","meaning":"建國神話","examples":[{"en":"Foundation myths help nations explain their origins.","zh":"建國神話幫助國家解釋其起源。"},{"en":"Foundation myths are stories about how a nation, group, or institution began.","zh":"foundation myths 指關於國家、群體或機構如何開始的故事。"},{"en":"A school may have a foundation story about one teacher starting classes in a tiny room.","zh":"學校可能有一個創校故事，講述某老師在細小課室開始上課。"},{"en":"If foundation myths are taught as pure truth, they may hide conflict and complexity.","zh":"如果建國神話被當成純粹真相教授，就可能隱藏衝突和複雜性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes origin stories that support identity.","zh":"這個片語描述支持身份的起源故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"strategic imperative","meaning":"戰略上的必要任務","examples":[{"en":"Some states see history teaching as a strategic imperative.","zh":"有些國家把歷史教學視為戰略上的必要任務。"},{"en":"A strategic imperative is something considered necessary for long-term political, social, or organisational goals.","zh":"strategic imperative 指被視為達成長遠政治、社會或組織目標所必需的事。"},{"en":"For a school, improving reading may be a strategic imperative if many subjects depend on it.","zh":"對學校而言，如果許多科目依賴閱讀能力，改善閱讀可能是戰略上的必要任務。"},{"en":"If leaders believe national unity depends on history lessons, they may treat the curriculum as strategic.","zh":"如果領袖相信國家團結取決於歷史課，就可能把課程視為戰略任務。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests urgency and importance.","zh":"這個片語暗示迫切性和重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"an exercise in","meaning":"一種……的訓練","examples":[{"en":"Other states see history as an exercise in teaching critical thinking.","zh":"其他國家把歷史視為一種教授批判思考的訓練。"},{"en":"An exercise in something is an activity designed to practise or develop a skill.","zh":"an exercise in something 指旨在練習或發展某技能的活動。"},{"en":"Writing a debate essay is an exercise in organising evidence and counterarguments.","zh":"寫辯論文章是一種組織證據和反駁的訓練。"},{"en":"If history is an exercise in critical thinking, students question sources rather than memorise stories.","zh":"如果歷史是批判思考訓練，學生會質疑資料來源，而不是背誦故事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the purpose of an activity.","zh":"這個片語描述活動的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"think for themselves","meaning":"獨立思考","examples":[{"en":"Some educators want children to think for themselves.","zh":"有些教育者希望孩子獨立思考。"},{"en":"Think for themselves means form their own judgement instead of simply accepting what others say.","zh":"think for themselves 指形成自己的判斷，而不是只接受別人所說。"},{"en":"Students think for themselves when they compare two sources before choosing an answer.","zh":"學生在選答案前比較兩個資料來源時，就是在獨立思考。"},{"en":"If history teaching encourages independent thought, students may question simple national myths.","zh":"如果歷史教學鼓勵獨立思考，學生可能質疑簡單國家神話。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses independent judgement.","zh":"這個片語強調自主判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the experience of","meaning":"……的經驗","examples":[{"en":"The experience of several countries suggests a limit to state control.","zh":"幾個國家的經驗顯示國家控制有限度。"},{"en":"The experience of a country means what has happened there and what can be learned from it.","zh":"the experience of a country 指某地發生過的事情以及可從中學到的教訓。"},{"en":"The experience of one school can help others avoid the same mistakes.","zh":"一所學校的經驗可以幫助其他學校避免同樣錯誤。"},{"en":"If several countries struggle to control history teaching, their experience becomes evidence.","zh":"如果幾個國家都難以控制歷史教學，它們的經驗就成為證據。"},{"en":"The phrase uses real cases as lessons.","zh":"這個片語把真實案例用作教訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"whatever educators and politicians might want","meaning":"不論教育者和政客想要甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Whatever educators and politicians might want, history teaching cannot be separated from society.","zh":"不論教育者和政客想要甚麼，歷史教學都不能與社會分開。"},{"en":"Whatever educators and politicians might want means no matter what teachers and leaders prefer.","zh":"whatever educators and politicians might want 指無論老師和領袖偏好甚麼。"},{"en":"Whatever parents might want, children still need sleep before exams.","zh":"不論家長想要甚麼，孩子考試前仍需要睡眠。"},{"en":"If society is divided, history lessons cannot simply ignore those divisions.","zh":"如果社會分裂，歷史課不能單純忽視那些分裂。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts wishes with reality.","zh":"這個片語對比願望與現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"there is a limit to","meaning":"……是有限度的","examples":[{"en":"There is a limit to how far history lessons can differ from society.","zh":"歷史課能與社會相差多遠是有限度的。"},{"en":"There is a limit to means something cannot continue beyond a certain point.","zh":"there is a limit to 指某事不能超過某一界線。"},{"en":"There is a limit to how much homework students can do before they lose focus.","zh":"學生能做多少功課才不失去專注是有限度的。"},{"en":"If school lessons contradict society too strongly, teachers may face resistance.","zh":"如果學校課堂與社會過度矛盾，老師可能面對阻力。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a boundary.","zh":"這個片語標示界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"diverge in tone from","meaning":"在語調上與……偏離","examples":[{"en":"History lessons cannot diverge too far in tone from society as a whole.","zh":"歷史課在語調上不能與整個社會偏離太遠。"},{"en":"Diverge in tone from means differ in attitude, style, or emotional direction from something else.","zh":"diverge in tone from 指在態度、風格或情感方向上與某事不同。"},{"en":"A school notice should not diverge too far in tone from the seriousness of an accident.","zh":"學校通告不應在語氣上與意外的嚴重性偏離太遠。"},{"en":"If society is already open-minded, school history can also become more open.","zh":"如果社會已經開明，學校歷史課也可以變得更開放。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on difference in attitude or mood.","zh":"這個片語集中於態度或氣氛上的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"society as a whole","meaning":"整個社會","examples":[{"en":"School history often reflects society as a whole.","zh":"學校歷史通常反映整個社會。"},{"en":"Society as a whole means the entire community or country, not just one group.","zh":"society as a whole 指整個社區或國家，而不是單一群體。"},{"en":"A policy may help one school but still be unfair to society as a whole.","zh":"一項政策可能幫助一所學校，但對整個社會仍不公平。"},{"en":"If society as a whole changes its values, schools usually change too.","zh":"如果整個社會改變價值觀，學校通常也會改變。"},{"en":"The phrase looks at the broader social picture.","zh":"這個片語着眼於更廣泛的社會圖像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"take Australia","meaning":"以澳洲為例","examples":[{"en":"Take Australia as an example of contested history teaching.","zh":"以澳洲作為歷史教學爭議的例子。"},{"en":"Take Australia means use Australia as an example for discussion.","zh":"take Australia 指用澳洲作為討論例子。"},{"en":"Take a school library as an example: quiet space can affect learning more than people expect.","zh":"以學校圖書館為例：安靜空間對學習的影響可能比人們預期大。"},{"en":"If a writer says “take Australia,” they are introducing a case to support a wider point.","zh":"如果作者說 “take Australia”，就是在引入案例支持更廣泛論點。"},{"en":"The phrase signals a concrete example.","zh":"這個片語標示具體例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"conservative prime minister","meaning":"保守派總理","examples":[{"en":"John Howard was a conservative prime minister.","zh":"John Howard 是一位保守派總理。"},{"en":"A conservative prime minister is a national leader who generally favours tradition, stability, and cautious change.","zh":"conservative prime minister 指通常重視傳統、穩定和謹慎改變的國家領袖。"},{"en":"A conservative school principal may prefer traditional uniforms and structured lessons.","zh":"保守派校長可能偏好傳統校服和有結構課堂。"},{"en":"If a conservative leader values national tradition, they may support a patriotic history curriculum.","zh":"如果保守派領袖重視國家傳統，可能支持愛國歷史課程。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies both political position and office.","zh":"這個片語同時指出政治立場和職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make history one of one’s favourite causes","meaning":"將歷史視為自己重視推動的議題之一","examples":[{"en":"John Howard made history one of his favourite causes.","zh":"John Howard 將歷史視為自己重視推動的議題之一。"},{"en":"Make something one of one’s favourite causes means treat it as an issue one strongly supports and promotes.","zh":"make something one of one’s favourite causes 指把某事視為自己強烈支持和推動的議題。"},{"en":"A teacher may make reading one of her favourite causes and start book clubs for students.","zh":"老師可能把閱讀視為自己重視推動的議題，並為學生開設讀書會。"},{"en":"If a leader makes history a favourite cause, curriculum debates can become political.","zh":"如果領袖把歷史視為重點議題，課程爭論可能變得政治化。"},{"en":"The phrase shows personal commitment to a public issue.","zh":"這個片語顯示對公共議題的個人投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"history summit","meaning":"歷史峰會","examples":[{"en":"A history summit was held to discuss Australia’s past.","zh":"一場歷史峰會被舉行，以討論澳洲的過去。"},{"en":"A history summit is a formal meeting where experts and officials discuss history policy or teaching.","zh":"history summit 指專家和官員討論歷史政策或教學的正式會議。"},{"en":"A school may hold a curriculum summit when teachers need to redesign a subject.","zh":"當老師需要重新設計科目時，學校可能舉行課程峰會。"},{"en":"If a government holds a history summit, it signals that history teaching has political importance.","zh":"如果政府舉行歷史峰會，就表示歷史教學具有政治重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a high-level meeting about history.","zh":"這個片語描述關於歷史的高層會議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"educators were urged to","meaning":"教育者被敦促去……","examples":[{"en":"Educators were urged to reestablish a structured narrative.","zh":"教育者被敦促去重新建立有結構的敍事。"},{"en":"Educators were urged to means teachers and education leaders were strongly encouraged or pressured to do something.","zh":"educators were urged to 指老師和教育領袖被強烈鼓勵或施壓去做某事。"},{"en":"Educators may be urged to reduce homework if students show serious stress.","zh":"如果學生表現出嚴重壓力，教育者可能被敦促去減少功課。"},{"en":"If politicians urge educators to change history lessons, teaching becomes part of public debate.","zh":"如果政客敦促教育者改變歷史課，教學就成為公共爭論的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests strong advice or pressure.","zh":"這個片語暗示強烈建議或壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reestablish a structured narrative","meaning":"重新建立有結構的敍事","examples":[{"en":"John Howard wanted to reestablish a structured narrative of national history.","zh":"John Howard 想重新建立國家歷史的有結構敍事。"},{"en":"Reestablish a structured narrative means bring back an organised story with a clear beginning, development, and meaning.","zh":"reestablish a structured narrative 指重新帶回有清楚開始、發展和意義的有組織故事。"},{"en":"A teacher may reestablish a structured narrative when students’ essays become a list of disconnected facts.","zh":"當學生文章變成一堆不相連事實時，老師可能重新建立有結構的敍事。"},{"en":"If history becomes too fragmented, some leaders may want one clear national story again.","zh":"如果歷史變得太零散，有些領袖可能想再次建立一個清楚國家故事。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests restoring order to a story.","zh":"這個片語暗示恢復故事秩序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be seen by critics as","meaning":"被評論者視為","examples":[{"en":"The proposal was seen by liberal critics as a doomed bid.","zh":"該建議被自由派評論者視為注定失敗的嘗試。"},{"en":"Be seen by critics as means be interpreted or judged in a particular way by critics.","zh":"be seen by critics as 指被評論者以某特定方式解讀或評價。"},{"en":"A new exam policy may be seen by teachers as unfair if it ignores weaker students.","zh":"如果新考試政策忽視較弱學生，可能被老師視為不公平。"},{"en":"If critics dislike a proposal, they may describe it as impossible or backward-looking.","zh":"如果評論者不喜歡某建議，可能形容它不可能成功或走回頭路。"},{"en":"The phrase reports how a group evaluates something.","zh":"這個片語報告某群體如何評價某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"liberal critics","meaning":"自由派評論者","examples":[{"en":"Liberal critics opposed the return to a romantic national narrative.","zh":"自由派評論者反對回到浪漫化的國家敍事。"},{"en":"Liberal critics are commentators who generally favour social openness, reform, and multiple perspectives.","zh":"liberal critics 指通常支持社會開放、改革和多元角度的評論者。"},{"en":"Liberal critics may question school rules that they see as too traditional or restrictive.","zh":"自由派評論者可能質疑他們視為太傳統或限制性的校規。"},{"en":"If history teaching becomes strongly patriotic, liberal critics may worry about exclusion.","zh":"如果歷史教學變得強烈愛國，自由派評論者可能擔心排斥。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies critics from a liberal political viewpoint.","zh":"這個片語指出來自自由派政治觀點的評論者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a doomed bid to","meaning":"注定失敗的嘗試","examples":[{"en":"Critics saw the summit as a doomed bid to revive an old vision.","zh":"評論者把峰會視為一次注定失敗、試圖重振舊想像的嘗試。"},{"en":"A doomed bid to do something is an attempt that is expected to fail.","zh":"a doomed bid to do something 指預計會失敗的嘗試。"},{"en":"Opening a shop without money, staff, or customers may be a doomed bid to start a business.","zh":"在沒有資金、員工或顧客下開店，可能是一次注定失敗的創業嘗試。"},{"en":"If society has already moved on, trying to restore an old story may fail.","zh":"如果社會已經向前走，試圖恢復舊故事可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests failure is almost certain.","zh":"這個片語暗示失敗幾乎必然。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"revive a romantic vision","meaning":"重新喚起浪漫化的想像","examples":[{"en":"The proposal tried to revive a romantic vision of white settlement.","zh":"該建議試圖重新喚起對白人殖民定居的浪漫化想像。"},{"en":"Revive a romantic vision means bring back an idealised and emotionally attractive picture of the past.","zh":"revive a romantic vision 指重新帶回對過去理想化而情感吸引的圖像。"},{"en":"A tourism campaign may revive a romantic vision of village life while ignoring poverty and hard work.","zh":"旅遊宣傳可能重新喚起鄉村生活的浪漫想像，卻忽略貧窮和辛勞。"},{"en":"If a curriculum revives a romantic vision, it may make settlement look noble and painless.","zh":"如果課程重振浪漫化想像，可能令定居看起來高尚而沒有痛苦。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests restoring an attractive but simplified image.","zh":"這個片語暗示恢復一種吸引但簡化的形象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"white settlement","meaning":"白人殖民定居","examples":[{"en":"The romantic story focused on white settlement in Australia.","zh":"這個浪漫化故事聚焦於澳洲的白人殖民定居。"},{"en":"White settlement refers to the arrival and establishment of European settlers in Australia.","zh":"white settlement 指歐洲定居者抵達並在澳洲建立社會。"},{"en":"A history class may contrast “white settlement” with “invasion” to show different viewpoints.","zh":"歷史課可能對比 “white settlement” 和 “invasion”，以顯示不同觀點。"},{"en":"If the term settlement is used alone, it may hide the violence experienced by Aboriginal peoples.","zh":"如果單獨使用 settlement 這個詞，可能隱藏原住民族所經歷的暴力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a colonial process from the settlers’ perspective.","zh":"這個片語從定居者角度描述殖民過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fade since","meaning":"自……以來逐漸淡化","examples":[{"en":"The romantic story has been fading since the 1980s.","zh":"這個浪漫化故事自1980年代以來逐漸淡化。"},{"en":"Fade since means become weaker or less common from a particular time onward.","zh":"fade since 指自某時起變得較弱或較少見。"},{"en":"Interest in a school club may fade since the main teacher left.","zh":"自主要老師離開後，學生對某學會的興趣可能逐漸淡化。"},{"en":"If a national story fades, newer interpretations may begin to replace it.","zh":"如果國家故事逐漸淡化，較新的解釋可能開始取代它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual decline after a starting point.","zh":"這個片語描述從某起點後逐漸衰退。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"revisionist view","meaning":"修正主義觀點","examples":[{"en":"A liberal revisionist view came to dominate curricula.","zh":"自由派修正主義觀點逐漸主導課程。"},{"en":"A revisionist view is a reinterpretation of history that challenges older accepted versions.","zh":"revisionist view 指挑戰舊有公認版本的歷史重新解讀。"},{"en":"A revisionist view of a school’s past may include students and staff once ignored.","zh":"對學校過去的修正主義觀點可能包括曾被忽略的學生和職員。"},{"en":"If new evidence shows victims’ experiences, historians may revise the old heroic story.","zh":"如果新證據顯示受害者經歷，歷史學家可能修正舊英雄故事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rethinking history.","zh":"這個片語描述重新思考歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"come to dominate","meaning":"逐漸主導","examples":[{"en":"The revisionist view came to dominate history curricula.","zh":"修正主義觀點逐漸主導歷史課程。"},{"en":"Come to dominate means gradually become the most powerful or common position.","zh":"come to dominate 指逐漸成為最有力或最常見的位置。"},{"en":"Online learning came to dominate some schools during long closures.","zh":"在長期停課期間，網上學習逐漸主導一些學校。"},{"en":"If one interpretation appears in most textbooks, it has come to dominate teaching.","zh":"如果一種解釋出現在大多數教科書中，它就已逐漸主導教學。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual rise to control or influence.","zh":"這個片語描述逐步取得控制或影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"replace settlement with invasion","meaning":"以「入侵」取代「定居」","examples":[{"en":"The curriculum replaced “settlement” with “invasion”.","zh":"課程以「入侵」取代「定居」。"},{"en":"Replace settlement with invasion means change the wording to show arrival as forceful occupation rather than peaceful settlement.","zh":"replace settlement with invasion 指改變用詞，把到來描述為武力佔領，而不是和平定居。"},{"en":"A teacher may replace “mistake” with “learning attempt” to change how students feel about errors.","zh":"老師可能以「學習嘗試」取代「錯誤」，以改變學生對錯誤的感受。"},{"en":"If a curriculum changes one key word, it can change the moral meaning of the whole event.","zh":"如果課程改變一個關鍵詞，就能改變整個事件的道德意義。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how language changes interpretation.","zh":"這個片語顯示語言如何改變解讀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for the first time","meaning":"首次","examples":[{"en":"The curriculum looked for the first time at the stories of Aboriginal peoples and women.","zh":"課程首次審視原住民族和女性的故事。"},{"en":"For the first time means something happened that had never happened before.","zh":"for the first time 指某事以前從未發生，現在首次發生。"},{"en":"A student may speak confidently in English for the first time after months of practice.","zh":"學生經過數月練習後，可能首次自信地用英文說話。"},{"en":"If ignored groups appear in textbooks for the first time, the national story becomes broader.","zh":"如果被忽略群體首次出現在教科書中，國家故事就變得更廣。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a new beginning.","zh":"這個片語標示新的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Aboriginal peoples and women","meaning":"原住民族和女性","examples":[{"en":"Modern curricula included the stories of Aboriginal peoples and women.","zh":"現代課程包括原住民族和女性的故事。"},{"en":"Aboriginal peoples and women refers to groups whose experiences were often left out of older national histories.","zh":"Aboriginal peoples and women 指經驗常被舊國家歷史排除在外的群體。"},{"en":"A fair history lesson includes Aboriginal peoples and women, not only male political leaders.","zh":"公平的歷史課包括原住民族和女性，而不只是男性政治領袖。"},{"en":"If textbooks include these groups, students can see how history affected different people.","zh":"如果教科書包括這些群體，學生就能看見歷史如何影響不同人。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights inclusion of previously marginalised voices.","zh":"這個片語突出納入以前被邊緣化的聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"policy battles","meaning":"政策爭議","examples":[{"en":"Australia’s policy battles affected the language of public debate.","zh":"澳洲的政策爭議影響了公共辯論的語言。"},{"en":"Policy battles are conflicts over what rules, laws, or official directions should be adopted.","zh":"policy battles 指圍繞應採用哪些規則、法律或官方方向的衝突。"},{"en":"A school may face policy battles over phones, uniforms, or homework limits.","zh":"學校可能因手機、校服或功課限制而面對政策爭議。"},{"en":"If policy battles continue, even the words people use can become politically sensitive.","zh":"如果政策爭議持續，甚至人們使用的字詞都可能變得政治敏感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes arguments over public decisions.","zh":"這個片語描述關於公共決策的爭論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cosmopolitan land","meaning":"國際化的地方","examples":[{"en":"Australia is described as a cosmopolitan land.","zh":"澳洲被描述為一個國際化的地方。"},{"en":"A cosmopolitan land is a place shaped by many cultures, peoples, languages, and global connections.","zh":"cosmopolitan land 指由多種文化、人民、語言和全球聯繫塑造的地方。"},{"en":"A cosmopolitan city may have restaurants, schools, and festivals from many traditions.","zh":"國際化城市可能有來自許多傳統的餐廳、學校和節日。"},{"en":"If a country is cosmopolitan, a single national story may not fit all citizens.","zh":"如果一個國家國際化，單一國家故事可能不適合所有公民。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses diversity and openness to the world.","zh":"這個片語強調多元性和對世界開放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"under Mr Howard’s government","meaning":"在 Howard 政府之下","examples":[{"en":"Some policy terms faded under Mr Howard’s government.","zh":"有些政策詞語在 Howard 政府之下淡出。"},{"en":"Under Mr Howard’s government means during the period when John Howard was in power.","zh":"under Mr Howard’s government 指在 John Howard 執政期間。"},{"en":"Under a new school principal, some old rules may disappear and new priorities may appear.","zh":"在新校長之下，有些舊規則可能消失，新優先事項可能出現。"},{"en":"If policy language changes under one government, it may reflect that government’s values.","zh":"如果政策語言在某政府之下改變，可能反映該政府的價值觀。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a political time frame.","zh":"這個片語給出政治時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"once had currency","meaning":"曾經流行；曾被廣泛使用","examples":[{"en":"The terms once had currency in public policy.","zh":"這些詞語曾在公共政策中被廣泛使用。"},{"en":"Once had currency means was once widely used, accepted, or influential.","zh":"once had currency 指曾經被廣泛使用、接受或具有影響力。"},{"en":"A slang word may once have had currency among teenagers but sound old-fashioned now.","zh":"一個俚語可能曾在青少年之間流行，但現在聽起來過時。"},{"en":"If a policy term loses currency, officials may stop using it even if teachers still do.","zh":"如果政策詞語失去流行度，官員可能停止使用，即使老師仍使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes former popularity or influence.","zh":"這個片語描述過去的流行或影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"policy lexicon","meaning":"政策詞彙","examples":[{"en":"Some terms faded from the policy lexicon.","zh":"有些詞語從政策詞彙中淡出。"},{"en":"Policy lexicon means the set of words commonly used in official policy discussion.","zh":"policy lexicon 指官方政策討論中常用的一套詞語。"},{"en":"Words like “assessment,” “inclusion,” and “accountability” may appear in an education policy lexicon.","zh":"“assessment”、“inclusion” 和 “accountability” 等詞可能出現在教育政策詞彙中。"},{"en":"If a term disappears from the policy lexicon, it may signal a shift in political priorities.","zh":"如果某詞從政策詞彙中消失，可能標示政治優先事項轉變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to official vocabulary.","zh":"這個片語指官方用語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fade from","meaning":"從……中淡出","examples":[{"en":"Terms such as multiculturalism faded from official language.","zh":"multiculturalism 等詞從官方語言中淡出。"},{"en":"Fade from means gradually disappear from a place, practice, or form of language.","zh":"fade from 指逐漸從某地方、做法或語言形式中消失。"},{"en":"A school slogan may fade from daily use after a new principal arrives.","zh":"新校長到任後，學校口號可能逐漸從日常使用中淡出。"},{"en":"If a word fades from official language, people may still use it in classrooms or public life.","zh":"如果一個詞從官方語言中淡出，人們仍可能在課室或公共生活中使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual disappearance.","zh":"這個片語描述逐漸消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not from classrooms","meaning":"但沒有從課室中消失","examples":[{"en":"The terms faded from policy language, but not from classrooms.","zh":"這些詞從政策語言中淡出，但沒有從課室中消失。"},{"en":"Not from classrooms means the words disappeared from one area but continued to be used in schools.","zh":"not from classrooms 指詞語從某領域消失，但仍在學校中使用。"},{"en":"A teaching method may disappear from official documents but not from classrooms where teachers still find it useful.","zh":"某教學方法可能從官方文件中消失，但沒有從仍覺得它有用的課室中消失。"},{"en":"If students and teachers keep using a term, government language cannot fully erase it.","zh":"如果學生和老師繼續使用某詞，政府語言不能完全抹走它。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts official policy with classroom reality.","zh":"這個片語對比官方政策與課室現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be controlled by the states","meaning":"由各州控制","examples":[{"en":"Australia’s curricula are controlled by the states.","zh":"澳洲的課程由各州控制。"},{"en":"Be controlled by the states means be managed by regional governments rather than one central authority.","zh":"be controlled by the states 指由地區政府而非單一中央權力管理。"},{"en":"School calendars may be controlled by local education authorities in some countries.","zh":"在某些國家，校曆可能由地方教育當局控制。"},{"en":"If curricula are controlled by states, national leaders may have limited power over classrooms.","zh":"如果課程由各州控制，國家領袖對課室的權力可能有限。"},{"en":"The phrase describes decentralised control.","zh":"這個片語描述分權控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rolled into","meaning":"併入……","examples":[{"en":"Many states have rolled Australian history into social studies courses.","zh":"許多州把澳洲歷史併入社會研究課程。"},{"en":"Rolled into means combined or merged into something larger.","zh":"rolled into 指被結合或合併到更大的事物中。"},{"en":"A school may roll grammar lessons into writing classes instead of teaching them separately.","zh":"學校可能把文法課併入寫作課，而不是分開教授。"},{"en":"If history is rolled into social studies, it may receive less separate attention.","zh":"如果歷史被併入社會研究，它可能得到較少獨立關注。"},{"en":"The phrase describes integration into a broader course or system.","zh":"這個片語描述整合到更廣泛課程或系統中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"social studies courses","meaning":"社會研究課程","examples":[{"en":"Australian history is often taught through social studies courses.","zh":"澳洲歷史常透過社會研究課程教授。"},{"en":"Social studies courses teach society, citizenship, geography, history, politics, and culture together.","zh":"social studies courses 指把社會、公民、地理、歷史、政治和文化一起教授的課程。"},{"en":"A social studies course may ask students to discuss elections, migration, and community problems.","zh":"社會研究課程可能要求學生討論選舉、移民和社區問題。"},{"en":"If history is taught through social studies, it may be connected with current social issues.","zh":"如果歷史透過社會研究教授，它可能與當前社會議題相連。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an interdisciplinary school subject.","zh":"這個片語指跨學科的學校科目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rather muddled","meaning":"相當混亂","examples":[{"en":"Some social studies courses are rather muddled.","zh":"有些社會研究課程相當混亂。"},{"en":"Rather muddled means somewhat confused, unclear, or poorly organised.","zh":"rather muddled 指有點混亂、不清楚或組織不佳。"},{"en":"A student’s essay may be rather muddled if every paragraph jumps to a new point.","zh":"如果學生文章每段都跳到新觀點，就可能相當混亂。"},{"en":"If a course mixes too many aims without structure, students may not know what they are learning.","zh":"如果課程在沒有結構下混合太多目標，學生可能不知道自己在學甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase politely criticises confusion.","zh":"這個片語較委婉地批評混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in its own right","meaning":"作為獨立科目","examples":[{"en":"In New South Wales, history is taught in its own right.","zh":"在新南威爾斯，歷史作為獨立科目教授。"},{"en":"In its own right means independently, not merely as part of something else.","zh":"in its own right 指獨立地，而不是只作為某物的一部分。"},{"en":"Grammar should sometimes be taught in its own right, not only corrected inside essays.","zh":"文法有時應作為獨立內容教授，而不只是作文中被糾正。"},{"en":"If history is taught in its own right, it receives separate time, structure, and assessment.","zh":"如果歷史作為獨立科目教授，它就有獨立時間、結構和評估。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses independent status.","zh":"這個片語強調獨立地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"promote a patriotic view of","meaning":"推廣對……的愛國觀點","examples":[{"en":"Mr Howard wanted to promote a patriotic view of history.","zh":"Howard 先生想推廣對歷史的愛國觀點。"},{"en":"Promote a patriotic view of history means encourage people to see history through national pride and loyalty.","zh":"promote a patriotic view of history 指鼓勵人們透過國家自豪和忠誠來看歷史。"},{"en":"A school ceremony may promote a patriotic view by focusing only on heroic national achievements.","zh":"學校典禮可能只聚焦英雄式國家成就，從而推廣愛國觀點。"},{"en":"If patriotic teaching ignores injustice, students may receive an incomplete picture.","zh":"如果愛國教學忽略不公義，學生可能得到不完整圖像。"},{"en":"The phrase describes encouraging national pride through interpretation.","zh":"這個片語描述透過解讀鼓勵民族自豪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"meet strong resistance","meaning":"遭遇強烈阻力","examples":[{"en":"The patriotic view of history meets strong resistance.","zh":"愛國歷史觀遭遇強烈阻力。"},{"en":"Meet strong resistance means face serious opposition.","zh":"meet strong resistance 指面對嚴重反對。"},{"en":"A new school rule may meet strong resistance if students think it is unfair.","zh":"如果學生認為新校規不公平，它可能遭遇強烈阻力。"},{"en":"If many teachers reject a political curriculum, reform becomes difficult.","zh":"如果許多老師反對政治化課程，改革就變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes forceful pushback.","zh":"這個片語描述有力反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"head of","meaning":"……的校長；主管","examples":[{"en":"Judy King is head of Riverside Girls High School.","zh":"Judy King 是 Riverside Girls High School 的校長。"},{"en":"Head of means the leader or person in charge of an organisation or department.","zh":"head of 指某組織或部門的領導者或負責人。"},{"en":"The head of a school makes decisions about staff, students, and curriculum.","zh":"學校校長負責決定員工、學生和課程事務。"},{"en":"If someone is head of history, they guide how the subject is taught.","zh":"如果某人是歷史科主任，就會指導該科如何教授。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies leadership responsibility.","zh":"這個片語指出領導責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ethnic groups","meaning":"族裔群體","examples":[{"en":"The school has students from more than 40 ethnic groups.","zh":"該校有來自40多個族裔群體的學生。"},{"en":"Ethnic groups are communities with shared ancestry, culture, language, or traditions.","zh":"ethnic groups 指擁有共同祖源、文化、語言或傳統的社群。"},{"en":"A city with many ethnic groups may celebrate different festivals and food cultures.","zh":"有許多族裔群體的城市可能慶祝不同節日和飲食文化。"},{"en":"If a classroom has many ethnic groups, one national story may not speak to every student.","zh":"如果課室中有許多族裔群體，單一國家故事未必能打動每位學生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cultural and ancestral diversity.","zh":"這個片語描述文化和祖源多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"present one story to","meaning":"向……呈現單一故事","examples":[{"en":"It is not possible to present one story to such diverse students.","zh":"向如此多元的學生呈現單一故事是不可能的。"},{"en":"Present one story to means offer a single version or explanation to a group.","zh":"present one story to 指向某群體提供單一版本或解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher should not present one story to a class if students’ family histories are very different.","zh":"如果學生家庭歷史非常不同，老師不應向全班呈現單一故事。"},{"en":"If a school presents only one story, some students may feel excluded or misrepresented.","zh":"如果學校只呈現一個故事，有些學生可能覺得被排除或被錯誤代表。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against one-size-fits-all teaching.","zh":"這個片語提醒不要用一刀切教學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"nor do we","meaning":"我們也不會這樣做","examples":[{"en":"It is not possible to present one story, and nor do we.","zh":"呈現單一故事是不可能的，我們也不會這樣做。"},{"en":"Nor do we means we also do not do the thing just mentioned.","zh":"nor do we 指我們也不做剛才提到的事情。"},{"en":"We do not force students to agree with one view, nor do we stop them asking questions.","zh":"我們不強迫學生同意單一觀點，也不阻止他們提問。"},{"en":"If a school says “nor do we,” it is rejecting a practice clearly and directly.","zh":"如果學校說 nor do we，就是清楚直接地拒絕某做法。"},{"en":"The phrase adds a negative statement that matches the previous one.","zh":"這個片語加入與前一句一致的否定說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"canvass all the terms","meaning":"全面討論各種說法","examples":[{"en":"The school canvasses all the terms for white settlement.","zh":"學校全面討論關於白人殖民定居的各種說法。"},{"en":"Canvass all the terms means discuss and examine all the possible words used for an issue.","zh":"canvass all the terms 指討論並檢視某議題所用的所有可能字詞。"},{"en":"A teacher may canvass all the terms for “poverty” before students write about inequality.","zh":"學生寫不平等前，老師可能全面討論 “poverty” 的各種說法。"},{"en":"If students examine words like settlement, invasion, and genocide, they learn how language shapes history.","zh":"如果學生檢視 settlement、invasion 和 genocide 等詞，就會學到語言如何塑造歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad discussion of wording and meaning.","zh":"這個片語描述對用詞和意思的廣泛討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"colonialism","meaning":"殖民主義","examples":[{"en":"Students discuss colonialism, invasion and genocide.","zh":"學生討論殖民主義、入侵和種族滅絕。"},{"en":"Colonialism is a system in which one country controls another land and its people.","zh":"colonialism 指一個國家控制另一片土地及其人民的制度。"},{"en":"History lessons on colonialism may include land loss, forced labour, cultural change, and resistance.","zh":"關於殖民主義的歷史課可能包括土地喪失、強迫勞動、文化變化和反抗。"},{"en":"If colonialism is described only as settlement, its violence may be hidden.","zh":"如果殖民主義只被描述為定居，其暴力可能被隱藏。"},{"en":"The word names a system of foreign control.","zh":"這個詞指出外國控制制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"invasion","meaning":"入侵","examples":[{"en":"The term invasion gives a different view of Australian history.","zh":"「入侵」一詞給出對澳洲歷史的不同看法。"},{"en":"Invasion means entering a place by force, often to control it.","zh":"invasion 指以武力進入某地，通常為了控制它。"},{"en":"A country may describe foreign troops entering its land as an invasion, not a visit.","zh":"一個國家可能把外國軍隊進入其土地描述為入侵，而不是訪問。"},{"en":"If “invasion” replaces “settlement,” the moral meaning of the event changes sharply.","zh":"如果 “invasion” 取代 “settlement”，事件的道德意義就會大幅改變。"},{"en":"The word stresses force and harm.","zh":"這個詞強調武力和傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"genocide","meaning":"種族滅絕","examples":[{"en":"The curriculum includes discussion of genocide.","zh":"課程包括對種族滅絕的討論。"},{"en":"Genocide is the deliberate destruction of a national, ethnic, racial, or religious group.","zh":"genocide 指蓄意摧毀一個民族、族裔、種族或宗教群體。"},{"en":"History teachers must handle genocide carefully because it involves extreme human suffering.","zh":"歷史老師必須小心處理種族滅絕，因為它涉及極端人類痛苦。"},{"en":"If students learn about genocide, they can understand how hatred and state power become deadly.","zh":"如果學生學習種族滅絕，就能理解仇恨和國家權力如何變得致命。"},{"en":"The word describes one of the gravest crimes in history.","zh":"這個詞描述歷史上最嚴重的罪行之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"are all views valid?","meaning":"所有觀點都有效嗎？","examples":[{"en":"Teachers may ask whether all views are valid.","zh":"老師可能問：所有觀點都有效嗎？"},{"en":"Are all views valid? asks whether every opinion is equally reasonable or supported by evidence.","zh":"are all views valid? 問是否每種意見都同樣合理或有證據支持。"},{"en":"In a classroom debate, students may ask whether all views are valid or whether some ignore facts.","zh":"在課堂辯論中，學生可能問所有觀點是否都有效，還是有些忽略事實。"},{"en":"If a view denies clear evidence, teachers may challenge it rather than treat it as equal.","zh":"如果某觀點否認清楚證據，老師可能會挑戰它，而不是把它視為同等有效。"},{"en":"The question encourages critical judgement, not automatic acceptance.","zh":"這個問題鼓勵批判判斷，而不是自動接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a single narrative","meaning":"單一敍事","examples":[{"en":"John Howard wanted a single narrative of national history.","zh":"John Howard 想要一個國家歷史的單一敍事。"},{"en":"A single narrative is one main story used to explain complex events.","zh":"single narrative 指用一個主要故事來解釋複雜事件。"},{"en":"A school should be careful about using a single narrative when students come from many backgrounds.","zh":"當學生來自許多背景時，學校應謹慎使用單一敍事。"},{"en":"If a single narrative dominates, alternative experiences may be pushed aside.","zh":"如果單一敍事佔主導，其他經驗可能被排擠。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests unity but can also imply oversimplification.","zh":"這個片語暗示統一，但也可能暗示過度簡化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"speaking as someone who","meaning":"作為一個……的人來說","examples":[{"en":"Speaking as someone who has taught history for decades, Judy King disagrees.","zh":"作為一個教歷史數十年的人來說，Judy King 不同意。"},{"en":"Speaking as someone who means giving an opinion based on personal experience or identity.","zh":"speaking as someone who 指基於個人經驗或身份發表意見。"},{"en":"Speaking as someone who has failed exams before, I know panic does not help.","zh":"作為一個曾經考試失敗的人來說，我知道恐慌沒有幫助。"},{"en":"If a teacher speaks from decades of experience, their disagreement carries practical weight.","zh":"如果老師根據數十年經驗發言，其反對意見具有實際分量。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a viewpoint grounded in experience.","zh":"這個片語引出基於經驗的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have a fight on one’s hands","meaning":"將面對一場艱難抗爭","examples":[{"en":"John Howard would have a fight on his hands.","zh":"John Howard 將面對一場艱難抗爭。"},{"en":"Have a fight on one’s hands means face strong opposition or a difficult struggle.","zh":"have a fight on one’s hands 指面對強烈反對或困難鬥爭。"},{"en":"A principal trying to ban all phones may have a fight on her hands with students and parents.","zh":"試圖全面禁止手機的校長可能會與學生和家長有一場硬仗。"},{"en":"If teachers resist a history reform, the leader promoting it will face a difficult battle.","zh":"如果老師反對歷史改革，推動它的領袖就會面對困難戰鬥。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious resistance ahead.","zh":"這個片語描述前方有嚴重阻力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"head of history","meaning":"歷史科主任","examples":[{"en":"Tom Ying is head of history at Burwood Girls High School.","zh":"Tom Ying 是 Burwood Girls High School 的歷史科主任。"},{"en":"Head of history means the teacher or leader responsible for the history department.","zh":"head of history 指負責歷史科部門的老師或領導。"},{"en":"The head of history may decide which sources, textbooks, and essay skills students practise.","zh":"歷史科主任可能決定學生練習哪些資料、教科書和作文技巧。"},{"en":"If the head of history supports multiple perspectives, students may learn a broader version of the past.","zh":"如果歷史科主任支持多角度，學生可能學到更廣闊的過去版本。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a school subject leader.","zh":"這個片語指出學校科目領導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"grow up as","meaning":"以……身份成長","examples":[{"en":"Tom Ying grew up as a Chinese child in white Australia.","zh":"Tom Ying 在白人主導的澳洲以華人孩子身份成長。"},{"en":"Grow up as means spend childhood with a particular identity or social position.","zh":"grow up as 指以某特定身份或社會位置度過童年。"},{"en":"A student may grow up as the only migrant child in a small town.","zh":"學生可能在小鎮中以唯一移民孩子身份成長。"},{"en":"If someone grows up as a minority, they may be sensitive to one-sided national stories.","zh":"如果某人以少數族裔身份成長，可能對單方面國家故事更敏感。"},{"en":"The phrase links childhood experience with identity.","zh":"這個片語把童年經驗與身份連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"white Australia","meaning":"白人主導的澳洲","examples":[{"en":"Tom Ying grew up in the white Australia of the 1950s.","zh":"Tom Ying 在1950年代白人主導的澳洲成長。"},{"en":"White Australia refers to a period or social order in which white people dominated Australian society and identity.","zh":"white Australia 指白人在澳洲社會和身份中佔主導的時期或社會秩序。"},{"en":"A history class may discuss white Australia when studying immigration restrictions and race.","zh":"歷史課研究移民限制和種族時，可能討論白人主導的澳洲。"},{"en":"If someone grew up in white Australia as a minority, they may understand exclusion personally.","zh":"如果某人作為少數族裔在白人主導的澳洲成長，可能親身理解排斥。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a racially dominant social context.","zh":"這個片語描述種族上佔主導的社會背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"non-English-speaking homes","meaning":"非英語家庭","examples":[{"en":"Most students at his school are from non-English-speaking homes.","zh":"他學校大多數學生來自非英語家庭。"},{"en":"Non-English-speaking homes are households where English is not the main language used at home.","zh":"non-English-speaking homes 指家中主要不使用英語的家庭。"},{"en":"Students from non-English-speaking homes may speak another language with parents and English at school.","zh":"來自非英語家庭的學生可能在家與父母說另一種語言，在學校說英語。"},{"en":"If a classroom includes many language backgrounds, one simple national story may feel too narrow.","zh":"如果課室包括許多語言背景，單一簡單國家故事可能顯得太狹窄。"},{"en":"The phrase describes linguistic diversity in families.","zh":"這個片語描述家庭中的語言多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"welcome an approach","meaning":"歡迎一種……的方法","examples":[{"en":"He welcomes an approach that includes difficult history.","zh":"他歡迎一種包括困難歷史的方法。"},{"en":"Welcome an approach means support or approve of a particular method.","zh":"welcome an approach 指支持或認同某種方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may welcome an approach that lets quiet students answer in writing first.","zh":"老師可能歡迎一種先讓安靜學生用文字回答的方法。"},{"en":"If a history approach includes painful facts, students may gain a more honest understanding.","zh":"如果歷史方法包含痛苦事實，學生可能得到更誠實的理解。"},{"en":"The phrase shows positive acceptance of a method.","zh":"這個片語顯示對某方法的正面接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the dark side of","meaning":"……黑暗的一面","examples":[{"en":"The curriculum includes the dark side of European settlement.","zh":"課程包括歐洲人殖民定居黑暗的一面。"},{"en":"The dark side of something is the harmful, painful, or morally troubling part of it.","zh":"the dark side of something 指某事有害、痛苦或道德上令人不安的一面。"},{"en":"A lesson about social media should include the dark side of online bullying and addiction.","zh":"關於社交媒體的課應包括網絡欺凌和沉迷的黑暗一面。"},{"en":"If history includes the dark side of settlement, it does not romanticise the past.","zh":"如果歷史包括定居的黑暗一面，就不會浪漫化過去。"},{"en":"The phrase reveals what a positive story often hides.","zh":"這個片語揭示正面故事常隱藏的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"European settlement","meaning":"歐洲人殖民定居","examples":[{"en":"European settlement had serious consequences for Aboriginal peoples.","zh":"歐洲人殖民定居對原住民族有嚴重後果。"},{"en":"European settlement refers to Europeans arriving and establishing communities in another land.","zh":"European settlement 指歐洲人到達另一片土地並建立社群。"},{"en":"In Australia, European settlement is debated because it also involved dispossession and violence.","zh":"在澳洲，歐洲人殖民定居具爭議，因為它也涉及剝奪和暴力。"},{"en":"If settlement is taught without Aboriginal experiences, students miss the full impact.","zh":"如果教授定居時不包括原住民族經驗，學生就會錯過完整影響。"},{"en":"The phrase may sound neutral, but its meaning depends on perspective.","zh":"這個片語可能聽起來中性，但其意思取決於角度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"one side of the story","meaning":"故事的一面之詞","examples":[{"en":"Students should not hear only one side of the story.","zh":"學生不應只聽故事的一面之詞。"},{"en":"One side of the story is one perspective or version of events, without other viewpoints.","zh":"one side of the story 指事件的一個角度或版本，而沒有其他觀點。"},{"en":"A teacher should hear both students before accepting one side of the story in an argument.","zh":"老師在學生爭執中接受一方說法前，應先聽雙方。"},{"en":"If history gives only one side, students may not understand why others disagree.","zh":"如果歷史只給出一面之詞，學生可能不明白為何其他人不同意。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against incomplete judgement.","zh":"這個片語提醒不要作不完整判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have an investment in","meaning":"對……有投入感；覺得與自己有關","examples":[{"en":"Immigrants, women and Aboriginal people need to have an investment in the story.","zh":"移民、女性和原住民族需要對這個故事有投入感。"},{"en":"Have an investment in means feel personally connected to and included in something.","zh":"have an investment in 指感到自己與某事有個人連繫並被包括其中。"},{"en":"Students have an investment in a class project when their own ideas are included.","zh":"當學生自己的想法被納入班級項目，他們就會對項目有投入感。"},{"en":"If minorities see themselves in history lessons, they are more likely to care about the national story.","zh":"如果少數群體在歷史課中看見自己，就更可能關心國家故事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes emotional and personal stake.","zh":"這個片語描述情感和個人利害關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"by world standards","meaning":"按世界標準來看","examples":[{"en":"Australia’s ideological effort is relatively gentle by world standards.","zh":"按世界標準來看，澳洲的意識形態努力相對溫和。"},{"en":"By world standards means compared with what is common in other countries.","zh":"by world standards 指與其他國家常見情況相比。"},{"en":"A city may be expensive locally but still affordable by world standards.","zh":"一個城市在本地可能昂貴，但按世界標準來看仍可負擔。"},{"en":"If a policy looks mild compared with harsher examples elsewhere, it is gentle by world standards.","zh":"如果某政策與其他地方更嚴厲例子相比顯得溫和，它就是按世界標準相對溫和。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an international comparison.","zh":"這個片語給出國際比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"re-impose","meaning":"重新強加","examples":[{"en":"Some leaders tried to re-impose a sort of national ideology.","zh":"有些領袖試圖重新強加某種國家意識形態。"},{"en":"Re-impose means put a rule, belief, or control back in place after it has weakened or disappeared.","zh":"re-impose 指在規則、信念或控制削弱或消失後重新施加。"},{"en":"A school may re-impose a uniform rule after students stop following the dress code.","zh":"當學生不再遵守服裝規定，學校可能重新強制校服規則。"},{"en":"If an old national story fades, leaders may try to force it back into classrooms.","zh":"如果舊國家故事淡化，領袖可能試圖把它重新強加到課室中。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests restoring control from above.","zh":"這個片語暗示由上而下恢復控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a sort of national ideology","meaning":"某種國家意識形態","examples":[{"en":"The policy tried to re-impose a sort of national ideology.","zh":"該政策試圖重新強加某種國家意識形態。"},{"en":"A sort of national ideology is a set of beliefs about what the nation is and how citizens should see it.","zh":"a sort of national ideology 指一套關於國家是甚麼以及公民應如何看待它的信念。"},{"en":"A school anthem may carry a sort of national ideology if it teaches loyalty and unity.","zh":"如果校歌教導忠誠和團結，它可能帶有某種國家意識形態。"},{"en":"If history lessons promote one official identity, they may become ideological.","zh":"如果歷史課推廣單一官方身份，就可能變得意識形態化。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a broad political belief system.","zh":"這個片語暗示廣泛的政治信念系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"look destined to fail","meaning":"看似注定失敗","examples":[{"en":"The effort looks destined to fail.","zh":"這項努力看似注定失敗。"},{"en":"Look destined to fail means seem very likely to be unsuccessful.","zh":"look destined to fail 指看起來很可能不成功。"},{"en":"A group project looks destined to fail if no one agrees on the topic or deadline.","zh":"如果沒有人同意題目或截止日期，小組項目看似注定失敗。"},{"en":"If teachers and students resist a policy strongly, it may never work in practice.","zh":"如果老師和學生強烈反對某政策，它實際上可能永遠行不通。"},{"en":"The phrase predicts failure based on visible signs.","zh":"這個片語根據可見跡象預測失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"by contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"Russia, by contrast, accepts a stronger national story.","zh":"相比之下，俄羅斯接受較強烈的國家故事。"},{"en":"By contrast means compared with the previous example, showing a difference.","zh":"by contrast 指與前一例子相比，顯示差異。"},{"en":"Some students like open discussion; by contrast, others prefer clear notes and model answers.","zh":"有些學生喜歡開放討論；相比之下，其他學生偏好清楚筆記和範文。"},{"en":"If Australia resists one national narrative but Russia accepts one, the contrast is clear.","zh":"如果澳洲抗拒單一國家敍事，而俄羅斯接受，對比就很清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces comparison through difference.","zh":"這個片語透過差異引出比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a toughly enforced ideology","meaning":"強硬執行的意識形態","examples":[{"en":"Russia still accepts a toughly enforced ideology.","zh":"俄羅斯仍接受一套強硬執行的意識形態。"},{"en":"A toughly enforced ideology is a belief system strongly imposed by authority.","zh":"toughly enforced ideology 指由權威強力施加的信念體系。"},{"en":"A school with a toughly enforced ideology may punish students for questioning official slogans.","zh":"有強硬執行意識形態的學校，可能懲罰質疑官方口號的學生。"},{"en":"If ideology is enforced harshly, history lessons may leave little room for debate.","zh":"如果意識形態被嚴厲執行，歷史課可能幾乎沒有辯論空間。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests strict control over belief.","zh":"這個片語暗示對信念的嚴格控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"national foundation story","meaning":"國家建基故事","examples":[{"en":"A national foundation story still seems natural to many Russians.","zh":"國家建基故事對許多俄羅斯人來說仍似乎自然。"},{"en":"A national foundation story is a story about how a nation began and what it stands for.","zh":"national foundation story 指關於一個國家如何開始及其代表甚麼的故事。"},{"en":"A school textbook may teach a national foundation story through heroes, battles, and symbols.","zh":"學校教科書可能透過英雄、戰役和象徵教授國家建基故事。"},{"en":"If people accept a foundation story as natural, they may not question what it leaves out.","zh":"如果人們把建基故事視為自然，就可能不質疑它遺漏了甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase connects origins with national identity.","zh":"這個片語把起源與國家身份連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"seem natural to","meaning":"對……來說似乎自然","examples":[{"en":"A national foundation story seems natural to many people.","zh":"國家建基故事對許多人來說似乎自然。"},{"en":"Seem natural to means appear normal, acceptable, or obvious to someone.","zh":"seem natural to 指對某人而言顯得正常、可接受或理所當然。"},{"en":"Wearing uniforms may seem natural to students who have done it since primary school.","zh":"對從小學起已穿校服的學生來說，穿校服可能似乎自然。"},{"en":"If a story is repeated for years, it may seem natural even if it is political.","zh":"如果一個故事被重複多年，即使它具政治性，也可能顯得自然。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how familiarity can make something feel normal.","zh":"這個片語顯示熟悉感如何令某事看起來正常。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the country’s elite","meaning":"國家精英","examples":[{"en":"The country’s elite often supports a national foundation story.","zh":"國家精英通常支持國家建基故事。"},{"en":"The country’s elite means the most powerful or influential people in politics, business, culture, or education.","zh":"the country’s elite 指在政治、商業、文化或教育中最有權力或影響力的人。"},{"en":"A country’s elite may shape museums, textbooks, universities, and public ceremonies.","zh":"國家精英可能塑造博物館、教科書、大學和公共典禮。"},{"en":"If elites support one national story, it may become official memory.","zh":"如果精英支持單一國家故事，它可能變成官方記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to influential groups at the top of society.","zh":"這個片語指社會頂層的有影響力群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a telling sign of","meaning":"……的明顯標誌","examples":[{"en":"The new holiday is a telling sign of how Putin views history.","zh":"新假日是 Putin 如何看待歷史的明顯標誌。"},{"en":"A telling sign of something is a clear clue that reveals a deeper attitude or truth.","zh":"a telling sign of something 指揭示更深層態度或真相的清楚線索。"},{"en":"A school’s choice of awards can be a telling sign of what it values most.","zh":"學校選擇頒發哪些獎項，可以明顯標示它最重視甚麼。"},{"en":"If a government chooses one historical date as a holiday, that choice reveals its priorities.","zh":"如果政府選擇某個歷史日期作假日，該選擇揭示其優先事項。"},{"en":"The phrase points to evidence with deeper meaning.","zh":"這個片語指出具有更深意義的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"imagine their past","meaning":"想像自己的過去","examples":[{"en":"The holiday shows how Russians are encouraged to imagine their past.","zh":"該假日顯示俄羅斯人被鼓勵如何想像自己的過去。"},{"en":"Imagine their past means form a picture or story about earlier national experience.","zh":"imagine their past 指形成關於早前國家經驗的圖像或故事。"},{"en":"Museums help visitors imagine their past through objects, photographs, and personal stories.","zh":"博物館透過物件、照片和個人故事幫助訪客想像自己的過去。"},{"en":"If people are encouraged to imagine the past as heroic defence, they may feel more united but less critical.","zh":"如果人們被鼓勵把過去想像成英勇防衛，可能更團結但較少批判。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shaping historical memory.","zh":"這個片語描述歷史記憶的塑造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"introduce a new national day","meaning":"引入新的國慶日","examples":[{"en":"President Putin introduced a new national day.","zh":"Putin 總統引入新的國慶日。"},{"en":"Introduce a new national day means officially create a new public holiday or commemorative date.","zh":"introduce a new national day 指官方創立新的公眾假日或紀念日。"},{"en":"A government may introduce a new national day to celebrate independence or unity.","zh":"政府可能引入新的國慶日，以慶祝獨立或團結。"},{"en":"If a new national day replaces an old one, the state may be changing how people remember history.","zh":"如果新的國家紀念日取代舊節日，國家可能正在改變人們記住歷史的方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes official creation of public memory.","zh":"這個片語描述官方創造公共記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"replace the old holiday","meaning":"取代舊假日","examples":[{"en":"The new national day replaced the old Revolution Day holiday.","zh":"新國慶日取代了舊革命紀念日假期。"},{"en":"Replace the old holiday means remove one public holiday and put another in its place.","zh":"replace the old holiday 指取消一個公眾假日，並以另一個取代。"},{"en":"A school may replace an old speech day with a new celebration of student service.","zh":"學校可能以新的學生服務慶典取代舊演講日。"},{"en":"If a holiday is replaced, the values being celebrated may also change.","zh":"如果假日被取代，被慶祝的價值也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase shows symbolic substitution.","zh":"這個片語顯示象徵性的替代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Revolution Day","meaning":"革命紀念日","examples":[{"en":"Revolution Day used to be celebrated on November 7.","zh":"革命紀念日過去在11月7日慶祝。"},{"en":"Revolution Day is a holiday that commemorates a revolution or revolutionary event.","zh":"Revolution Day 指紀念革命或革命事件的假日。"},{"en":"A country may celebrate Revolution Day with parades, speeches, and historical symbols.","zh":"國家可能以巡遊、演講和歷史象徵慶祝革命紀念日。"},{"en":"If Revolution Day is replaced, the state may be distancing itself from an older political identity.","zh":"如果革命紀念日被取代，國家可能正在與較舊政治身份保持距離。"},{"en":"The phrase names a politically symbolic holiday.","zh":"這個片語指出具政治象徵意義的假日。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"what the new date recalls","meaning":"新日期所紀念的是","examples":[{"en":"The new date recalls the expulsion of foreign forces from Moscow.","zh":"新日期所紀念的是外國軍隊被逐出莫斯科。"},{"en":"What the new date recalls means the historical event that the date is meant to remember.","zh":"what the new date recalls 指該日期旨在記住的歷史事件。"},{"en":"A school anniversary may recall the day the first students entered the building.","zh":"學校周年紀念日可能紀念第一批學生進入校舍的日子。"},{"en":"If a holiday recalls military victory, it may shape national feeling around defence and unity.","zh":"如果假日紀念軍事勝利，它可能圍繞防衛和團結塑造民族情感。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a date with memory.","zh":"這個片語把日期與記憶連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a period of chaos","meaning":"一段混亂時期","examples":[{"en":"The event followed a period of chaos in Russia.","zh":"該事件發生在俄羅斯一段混亂時期之後。"},{"en":"A period of chaos is a time when order breaks down and events become confused or unstable.","zh":"period of chaos 指秩序崩潰、事件變得混亂或不穩的時期。"},{"en":"A school may experience a period of chaos after a sudden fire alarm and timetable change.","zh":"突然火警鐘和時間表改變後，學校可能經歷一段混亂時期。"},{"en":"If a nation emerges from chaos, later leaders may celebrate the restoration of order.","zh":"如果國家從混亂中走出，後來領袖可能慶祝秩序恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase describes instability over time.","zh":"這個片語描述持續一段時間的不穩定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"drive someone out of","meaning":"將某人逐出……","examples":[{"en":"Russian forces drove the Catholic Poles and Lithuanians out of Moscow.","zh":"俄羅斯軍隊將天主教波蘭人和立陶宛人逐出莫斯科。"},{"en":"Drive someone out of means force people to leave a place.","zh":"drive someone out of 指迫使某人離開某地。"},{"en":"Rising rent can drive small shops out of a neighbourhood.","zh":"租金上升可以把小店逐出社區。"},{"en":"If foreign forces are driven out, the event may become a story of national defence.","zh":"如果外國軍隊被逐出，該事件可能成為國家防衛故事。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests forceful removal.","zh":"這個片語暗示強制移除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"despite the bonhomie of","meaning":"儘管……氣氛友好","examples":[{"en":"Despite the bonhomie of the meeting, the holiday carried a defensive message.","zh":"儘管會面氣氛友好，該假日仍帶有防衛性訊息。"},{"en":"Despite the bonhomie of means although the atmosphere seemed friendly and cheerful.","zh":"despite the bonhomie of 指雖然氣氛看起來友善而愉快。"},{"en":"Despite the bonhomie of the dinner, two colleagues still disagreed sharply about the project.","zh":"儘管晚餐氣氛友好，兩位同事仍對項目有尖銳分歧。"},{"en":"If a friendly meeting hides political tension, the public message may still be defensive.","zh":"如果友好會面掩蓋政治緊張，公共訊息仍可能具防衛性。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts friendliness with deeper conflict.","zh":"這個片語對比友善氣氛與深層衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a 25-minute chat","meaning":"25分鐘的談話","examples":[{"en":"Putin had a 25-minute chat with Pope Benedict XVI.","zh":"Putin 與教宗本篤十六世進行了25分鐘談話。"},{"en":"A 25-minute chat is a short informal conversation lasting twenty-five minutes.","zh":"a 25-minute chat 指持續二十五分鐘的短暫非正式談話。"},{"en":"A teacher may have a 25-minute chat with a parent about a student’s progress.","zh":"老師可能與家長進行25分鐘談話，討論學生進步。"},{"en":"If a short friendly chat occurs alongside defensive symbolism, the contrast can be striking.","zh":"如果短暫友好談話與防衛性象徵同時出現，對比可能很鮮明。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the length and informal nature of a conversation.","zh":"這個片語給出談話長度和非正式性質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Pope Benedict XVI","meaning":"教宗本篤十六世","examples":[{"en":"Pope Benedict XVI spoke with President Putin.","zh":"教宗本篤十六世與 Putin 總統交談。"},{"en":"Pope Benedict XVI was the head of the Catholic Church during his papacy.","zh":"Pope Benedict XVI 指他任教宗期間的天主教會領袖。"},{"en":"A history article may mention Pope Benedict XVI when discussing religion and international politics.","zh":"歷史文章討論宗教與國際政治時，可能提到教宗本篤十六世。"},{"en":"If a Russian leader meets the Pope but promotes an anti-Western symbol, the message becomes complex.","zh":"如果俄羅斯領袖與教宗會面，卻推動反西方象徵，訊息就變得複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major Catholic religious figure.","zh":"這個片語指出一位重要天主教宗教人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"promote a national day","meaning":"推動一個國家紀念日","examples":[{"en":"Putin promoted a national day with symbolic meaning.","zh":"Putin 推動一個具有象徵意義的國家紀念日。"},{"en":"Promote a national day means encourage public recognition and celebration of an official date.","zh":"promote a national day 指鼓勵公眾承認和慶祝官方日期。"},{"en":"A government may promote a national day through school ceremonies, speeches, and media campaigns.","zh":"政府可能透過學校典禮、演講和媒體宣傳推動國家紀念日。"},{"en":"If a national day is promoted strongly, it can shape how people remember the past.","zh":"如果國家紀念日被強力推動，它可以塑造人們如何記住過去。"},{"en":"The phrase describes official encouragement of commemoration.","zh":"這個片語描述官方鼓勵紀念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"signal isolation and defensiveness","meaning":"顯示孤立和防衛心態","examples":[{"en":"The national day signals isolation and defensiveness towards the West.","zh":"該國家紀念日顯示對西方的孤立和防衛心態。"},{"en":"Signal isolation and defensiveness means show a wish to stand apart and protect oneself from others.","zh":"signal isolation and defensiveness 指顯示想與他人保持距離並保護自己的心態。"},{"en":"A school that refuses all outside cooperation may signal isolation and defensiveness.","zh":"如果學校拒絕所有外部合作，可能顯示孤立和防衛心態。"},{"en":"If a holiday celebrates driving out Western forces, it may suggest suspicion toward the West.","zh":"如果假日慶祝逐出西方勢力，可能暗示對西方不信任。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the political message behind a symbol.","zh":"這個片語描述象徵背後的政治訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Western Christendom","meaning":"西方基督教世界","examples":[{"en":"The holiday suggests defensiveness towards Western Christendom.","zh":"該假日暗示對西方基督教世界的防衛心態。"},{"en":"Western Christendom refers to the Christian world historically associated with Western Europe and the Catholic or Western Christian tradition.","zh":"Western Christendom 指歷史上與西歐以及天主教或西方基督教傳統有關的基督教世界。"},{"en":"A history course may discuss Western Christendom when studying medieval Europe and church power.","zh":"歷史課研究中世紀歐洲和教會權力時，可能討論西方基督教世界。"},{"en":"If a holiday remembers expelling Catholic forces, it may carry a message about religious and cultural boundaries.","zh":"如果假日紀念逐出天主教勢力，可能帶有宗教和文化邊界的訊息。"},{"en":"The phrase links religion, region, and civilisation.","zh":"這個片語連結宗教、地區和文明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"white rule collapsed","meaning":"白人統治瓦解","examples":[{"en":"In South Africa, white rule collapsed.","zh":"在南非，白人統治瓦解。"},{"en":"White rule collapsed means political control by white rulers came to an end.","zh":"white rule collapsed 指由白人統治者掌握的政治控制結束。"},{"en":"A history teacher may describe how apartheid ended when white minority rule collapsed.","zh":"歷史老師可能描述白人少數統治瓦解時，種族隔離如何結束。"},{"en":"If a ruling system collapses, a country must create a new political story and curriculum.","zh":"如果統治制度瓦解，國家就必須創造新的政治故事和課程。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the end of racial political domination.","zh":"這個片語標示種族政治支配的終結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the authorities","meaning":"當局","examples":[{"en":"The authorities created a new national story.","zh":"當局創造了新的國家故事。"},{"en":"The authorities are the official people or organisations with power to make decisions.","zh":"the authorities 指有權作決定的官方人士或組織。"},{"en":"Local authorities may close roads during a storm for public safety.","zh":"地方當局可能在風暴期間封路，以保障公共安全。"},{"en":"If authorities control curriculum, they can influence how citizens remember the past.","zh":"如果當局控制課程，就能影響公民如何記住過去。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to those in official control.","zh":"這個片語指掌握官方控制權的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"do a better job at","meaning":"在……方面做得較好","examples":[{"en":"South Africa did a better job at forging a new national story.","zh":"南非在打造新國家敍事方面做得較好。"},{"en":"Do a better job at means perform more successfully in doing something.","zh":"do a better job at 指在做某事方面表現更成功。"},{"en":"A student may do a better job at writing conclusions after studying model essays.","zh":"學生研究範文後，可能在寫結論方面做得較好。"},{"en":"If a country avoids replacing one rigid ideology with another, it handles reform better.","zh":"如果國家避免以另一種僵化意識形態取代原有那種，就更好地處理改革。"},{"en":"The phrase compares performance or success.","zh":"這個片語比較表現或成功程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"forge a new national story","meaning":"打造新的國家敍事","examples":[{"en":"South Africa tried to forge a new national story after apartheid.","zh":"南非在種族隔離結束後嘗試打造新的國家敍事。"},{"en":"Forge a new national story means create a fresh shared account of a country’s identity and past.","zh":"forge a new national story 指創造一個關於國家身份和過去的新共同敍述。"},{"en":"A school may forge a new story about itself after merging with another school.","zh":"學校與另一所學校合併後，可能為自己打造新故事。"},{"en":"If a society changes completely, it may need a new story that includes previously excluded people.","zh":"如果社會完全改變，就可能需要一個包含以前被排除者的新故事。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests active creation of identity.","zh":"這個片語暗示主動創造身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"avoid the trap of","meaning":"避免陷入……的陷阱","examples":[{"en":"South Africa avoided the trap of replacing one rigid ideology with another.","zh":"南非避免陷入以另一種僵化意識形態取代原有那種的陷阱。"},{"en":"Avoid the trap of means not make a tempting but harmful mistake.","zh":"avoid the trap of 指避免犯下看似吸引但有害的錯誤。"},{"en":"Students should avoid the trap of memorising phrases without understanding them.","zh":"學生應避免陷入只背片語而不理解的陷阱。"},{"en":"If a new curriculum simply reverses old propaganda, it falls into the same problem.","zh":"如果新課程只是反轉舊宣傳，就會陷入同一問題。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against a common mistake.","zh":"這個片語提醒避開常見錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"one rigid ideology with another","meaning":"以另一種僵化意識形態取代原有那種","examples":[{"en":"The new curriculum avoided replacing one rigid ideology with another.","zh":"新課程避免以另一種僵化意識形態取代原有那種。"},{"en":"One rigid ideology with another means one fixed belief system is simply replaced by a different fixed belief system.","zh":"one rigid ideology with another 指一套固定信念系統只是被另一套不同但同樣固定的信念系統取代。"},{"en":"A school should not replace strict punishment with another rigid system that still ignores students’ needs.","zh":"學校不應以另一套仍忽略學生需要的僵化制度取代嚴厲懲罰。"},{"en":"If reform changes slogans but keeps closed thinking, the deeper problem remains.","zh":"如果改革只改口號卻保持封閉思維，深層問題仍然存在。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against changing sides without becoming more open.","zh":"這個片語提醒不要只是換邊站而沒有變得更開放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the main message of","meaning":"……的主要訊息","examples":[{"en":"The main message of the new curriculum is inclusion and reconciliation.","zh":"新課程的主要訊息是包容與和解。"},{"en":"The main message of something is its central idea or purpose.","zh":"the main message of something 指某事的核心思想或目的。"},{"en":"The main message of a school assembly may be that kindness matters in daily life.","zh":"學校早會的主要訊息可能是善意在日常生活中很重要。"},{"en":"If a curriculum’s main message is reconciliation, lessons should bring groups together rather than divide them.","zh":"如果課程主要訊息是和解，課堂就應讓不同群體走近，而不是分裂。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the core meaning.","zh":"這個片語指出核心意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"school curriculum","meaning":"學校課程","examples":[{"en":"The new school curriculum emphasises inclusion and reconciliation.","zh":"新學校課程強調包容與和解。"},{"en":"A school curriculum is the planned set of subjects, content, and learning goals in a school.","zh":"school curriculum 指學校中有計劃的科目、內容和學習目標。"},{"en":"A curriculum may include history, science, languages, arts, and civic education.","zh":"課程可能包括歷史、科學、語言、藝術和公民教育。"},{"en":"If a curriculum changes, classroom teaching and exams may change too.","zh":"如果課程改變，課堂教學和考試也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what schools officially teach.","zh":"這個片語指學校正式教授的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"inclusion and reconciliation","meaning":"包容與和解","examples":[{"en":"The curriculum promotes inclusion and reconciliation.","zh":"課程推動包容與和解。"},{"en":"Inclusion and reconciliation means bringing different groups into the shared story and helping them repair relationships.","zh":"inclusion and reconciliation 指把不同群體納入共同故事，並幫助他們修復關係。"},{"en":"A school promotes inclusion when migrant students see their cultures respected in class.","zh":"當移民學生在課堂中看見自己的文化受到尊重，學校就是在推動包容。"},{"en":"If history teaching includes former enemies and victims, it can support reconciliation.","zh":"如果歷史教學包括昔日敵人和受害者，就能支持和解。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses belonging and healing after division.","zh":"這個片語強調分裂後的歸屬和修復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"post-apartheid lessons","meaning":"種族隔離結束後的課程","examples":[{"en":"Linda Chisholm designed post-apartheid lessons.","zh":"Linda Chisholm 設計了種族隔離結束後的課程。"},{"en":"Post-apartheid lessons are lessons created after the end of apartheid in South Africa.","zh":"post-apartheid lessons 指南非種族隔離結束後創立的課程。"},{"en":"A post-apartheid history lesson may include voices once excluded by white rule.","zh":"種族隔離結束後的歷史課可能包括曾被白人統治排除的聲音。"},{"en":"If lessons are designed after a major political change, they may promote new values.","zh":"如果課程在重大政治變化後設計，可能推動新價值。"},{"en":"The phrase places education in the period after apartheid.","zh":"這個片語把教育放在種族隔離後的時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"handle primary sources","meaning":"處理一手資料","examples":[{"en":"Pupils are taught to handle primary sources.","zh":"學生被教導處理一手資料。"},{"en":"Handle primary sources means read, examine, and interpret original historical materials carefully.","zh":"handle primary sources 指仔細閱讀、檢視和解讀原始歷史材料。"},{"en":"Students handle primary sources when they study letters, photographs, speeches, or oral testimonies.","zh":"學生研究書信、照片、演講或口述證詞時，就是在處理一手資料。"},{"en":"If pupils handle sources themselves, they learn to judge evidence rather than simply trust textbooks.","zh":"如果學生親自處理資料，就會學會判斷證據，而不是只相信教科書。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an active historical skill.","zh":"這個片語描述主動的歷史技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"primary sources","meaning":"一手資料","examples":[{"en":"Primary sources include oral history and documents.","zh":"一手資料包括口述歷史和文件。"},{"en":"Primary sources are original materials from the time being studied.","zh":"primary sources 指來自所研究時期的原始材料。"},{"en":"Diaries, photographs, newspaper reports, speeches, and interview recordings can be primary sources.","zh":"日記、照片、報章報道、演講和訪談錄音都可以是一手資料。"},{"en":"If students use primary sources, they can see how real people experienced events.","zh":"如果學生使用一手資料，就能看見真實人物如何經歷事件。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts original evidence with later summaries.","zh":"這個片語把原始證據與後來摘要作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"oral history","meaning":"口述歷史","examples":[{"en":"Oral history can help pupils understand different experiences.","zh":"口述歷史可以幫助學生理解不同經歷。"},{"en":"Oral history is history collected through spoken memories and interviews.","zh":"oral history 指透過口述記憶和訪談收集的歷史。"},{"en":"Students may record oral history by interviewing grandparents about school life long ago.","zh":"學生可能透過訪問祖父母以前的學校生活來記錄口述歷史。"},{"en":"If textbooks ignore ordinary people, oral history can bring their voices into the classroom.","zh":"如果教科書忽略普通人，口述歷史可以把他們的聲音帶入課室。"},{"en":"The phrase values memory as historical evidence.","zh":"這個片語重視記憶作為歷史證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"spoon-feed someone on","meaning":"用……填鴨式教導某人","examples":[{"en":"Teachers avoid spoon-feeding pupils on textbooks.","zh":"老師避免用教科書對學生填鴨式教導。"},{"en":"Spoon-feed someone on something means give information too directly so learners do not think for themselves.","zh":"spoon-feed someone on something 指過度直接給資料，使學習者不用自己思考。"},{"en":"A tutor spoon-feeds students if he gives model answers but never explains why they work.","zh":"如果補習老師只給範文答案而不解釋原因，就是在填鴨式教學生。"},{"en":"If pupils are spoon-fed, they may memorise facts without learning to analyse sources.","zh":"如果學生被填鴨式教導，可能只背事實而不學會分析資料。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises passive learning.","zh":"這個片語批評被動學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"symbols and anniversaries","meaning":"象徵和周年紀念日","examples":[{"en":"Symbols and anniversaries have been redefined with skill.","zh":"象徵和周年紀念日已被巧妙地重新界定。"},{"en":"Symbols and anniversaries are public signs, ceremonies, and dates used to remember shared history.","zh":"symbols and anniversaries 指用來記住共同歷史的公共標誌、儀式和日期。"},{"en":"Flags, monuments, national days, and memorial services are symbols and anniversaries.","zh":"旗幟、紀念碑、國慶日和悼念儀式都是象徵和周年紀念日。"},{"en":"If a society changes, old symbols may need new meanings to include more people.","zh":"如果社會改變，舊象徵可能需要新意義來納入更多人。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to public memory tools.","zh":"這個片語指公共記憶工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be redefined with skill","meaning":"被巧妙地重新界定","examples":[{"en":"Old symbols have been redefined with skill.","zh":"舊象徵已被巧妙地重新界定。"},{"en":"Be redefined with skill means have one’s meaning changed carefully and effectively.","zh":"be redefined with skill 指某事物的意思被仔細而有效地改變。"},{"en":"A school may redefine an old prize with skill by turning it from competition into service recognition.","zh":"學校可能巧妙地重新界定舊獎項，把它由競爭轉為服務表揚。"},{"en":"If painful anniversaries are redefined well, they can support healing rather than division.","zh":"如果痛苦周年被妥善重新界定，就能支持療癒而不是分裂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful symbolic change.","zh":"這個片語描述仔細的象徵改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"white settlers","meaning":"白人殖民者","examples":[{"en":"The old anniversary remembered white settlers clashing with the Zulus.","zh":"舊周年紀念日紀念白人殖民者與祖魯人衝突。"},{"en":"White settlers were European-descended people who moved into and established homes in colonised lands.","zh":"white settlers 指歐洲裔人士遷入殖民土地並建立家園。"},{"en":"A history lesson may discuss white settlers alongside Indigenous communities to show both perspectives.","zh":"歷史課可能同時討論白人殖民者和原住民社群，以展示雙方角度。"},{"en":"If a holiday celebrates only white settlers, it may exclude those harmed by settlement.","zh":"如果假日只慶祝白人殖民者，可能排除被殖民定居傷害的人。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a colonial group.","zh":"這個片語指出殖民群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"clash with","meaning":"與……衝突","examples":[{"en":"White settlers clashed with the Zulus in 1838.","zh":"白人殖民者在1838年與祖魯人衝突。"},{"en":"Clash with means fight, conflict, or strongly disagree with another group.","zh":"clash with 指與另一群體打鬥、衝突或嚴重不同意。"},{"en":"Students may clash with parents over phone use and study time.","zh":"學生可能因手機使用和學習時間與父母衝突。"},{"en":"If two groups compete for land and power, they may clash violently.","zh":"如果兩個群體爭奪土地和權力，可能爆發暴力衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe physical conflict or serious disagreement.","zh":"這個片語可描述身體衝突或嚴重分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the Zulus","meaning":"祖魯人","examples":[{"en":"The Zulus were part of the historical memory of December 16.","zh":"祖魯人是12月16日歷史記憶的一部分。"},{"en":"The Zulus are a major ethnic group in southern Africa with a significant history and culture.","zh":"the Zulus 指南部非洲一個主要族群，具有重要歷史和文化。"},{"en":"A history lesson on South Africa may discuss the Zulus when studying colonial conflict.","zh":"南非歷史課研究殖民衝突時，可能討論祖魯人。"},{"en":"If a national holiday includes the Zulus only as enemies, the story may be too narrow.","zh":"如果國家假日只把祖魯人視為敵人，故事可能過於狹窄。"},{"en":"The phrase names a people central to South African history.","zh":"這個片語指出南非歷史中的重要民族。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the Day of Reconciliation","meaning":"和解日","examples":[{"en":"December 16 is now the Day of Reconciliation.","zh":"12月16日現在是和解日。"},{"en":"The Day of Reconciliation is a national day intended to promote healing and unity after division.","zh":"the Day of Reconciliation 指旨在分裂後促進療癒和團結的國家紀念日。"},{"en":"A school may mark a reconciliation day by inviting students to share family histories respectfully.","zh":"學校可能透過邀請學生尊重地分享家庭歷史來紀念和解日。"},{"en":"If an anniversary is renamed for reconciliation, its meaning changes from conflict to healing.","zh":"如果周年紀念日被重新命名為和解日，其意義就由衝突轉向療癒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a symbolic public holiday.","zh":"這個片語描述具有象徵意義的公眾假日。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"only one of the choices is correct","meaning":"只有一個選項正確","examples":[{"en":"For each question, only one of the choices is correct.","zh":"每條題目只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct means students must select a single right answer.","zh":"only one of the choices is correct 指學生必須選出唯一正確答案。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice question, students should not mark two answers if only one is correct.","zh":"在選擇題中，如果只有一個答案正確，學生不應標記兩個答案。"},{"en":"If two options look similar, the passage detail decides which one is correct.","zh":"如果兩個選項看似相似，文章細節決定哪一個正確。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語給出嚴格考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"corresponding letter","meaning":"相應字母","examples":[{"en":"Students write the corresponding letter in the answer box.","zh":"學生在答案框中寫上相應字母。"},{"en":"Corresponding letter means the letter that matches the chosen answer.","zh":"corresponding letter 指與所選答案配對的字母。"},{"en":"If option B is correct, the corresponding letter is B.","zh":"如果 B 選項正確，相應字母就是 B。"},{"en":"If students understand the answer but copy the wrong letter, they may lose the mark.","zh":"如果學生明白答案但抄錯字母，可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the answer code, not the full answer sentence.","zh":"這個片語指答案代碼，而不是完整答案句子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"appropriate box","meaning":"適當方格","examples":[{"en":"The answer should be written in the appropriate box.","zh":"答案應寫在適當方格內。"},{"en":"Appropriate box means the correct space or answer area for a particular question.","zh":"appropriate box 指某題對應的正確空格或答案位置。"},{"en":"Students should write question 5’s answer in the appropriate box, not beside question 6.","zh":"學生應把第5題答案寫在適當方格，而不是第6題旁邊。"},{"en":"If an answer is placed in the wrong box, it may be marked incorrectly.","zh":"如果答案放錯方格，可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a practical instruction about answer placement.","zh":"這個片語給出關於答案位置的實際指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"fit in with","meaning":"與……配合；符合","examples":[{"en":"The Irish Civil War did not fit in with a simple nationalist story.","zh":"愛爾蘭內戰與簡單民族主義故事不相配合。"},{"en":"Fit in with means match or suit a particular idea, plan, or pattern.","zh":"fit in with 指與某想法、計劃或模式相符或適合。"},{"en":"A student’s example may not fit in with the essay argument if it proves the opposite point.","zh":"如果學生例子證明相反觀點，就可能不符合文章論點。"},{"en":"If a civil war complicates the heroic story, it may be left out.","zh":"如果內戰令英雄故事變得複雜，它可能被省略。"},{"en":"The phrase describes whether something belongs naturally in a larger framework.","zh":"這個片語描述某事是否自然屬於更大框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"British rule","meaning":"英國統治","examples":[{"en":"Irish history was often told as a struggle against British rule.","zh":"愛爾蘭歷史常被講述成反抗英國統治的鬥爭。"},{"en":"British rule means political control by Britain over another place.","zh":"British rule 指英國對另一地方的政治控制。"},{"en":"History lessons may discuss British rule when studying colonies, laws, language, and resistance.","zh":"歷史課研究殖民地、法律、語言和反抗時，可能討論英國統治。"},{"en":"If a country defines itself against British rule, independence becomes central to its story.","zh":"如果國家以反對英國統治來定義自己，獨立就成為其故事核心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a period or system of British control.","zh":"這個片語描述英國控制的時期或制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"anger the British","meaning":"激怒英國人","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Irish people avoided the topic to avoid angering the British.","zh":"題目問愛爾蘭人是否為避免激怒英國人而避談該話題。"},{"en":"Anger the British means make British people or authorities angry.","zh":"anger the British 指令英國人或英國當局生氣。"},{"en":"A student may avoid a comment if they fear it will anger the teacher.","zh":"如果學生擔心一句評論會激怒老師，可能避免說出來。"},{"en":"If a topic is avoided only to avoid angering someone powerful, history becomes politically controlled.","zh":"如果避談某話題只是為了避免激怒有權者，歷史就變得受政治控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes causing offence or hostility.","zh":"這個片語描述造成冒犯或敵意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"favour teaching history","meaning":"支持以……方式教授歷史","examples":[{"en":"John Howard favours teaching history through a structured national narrative.","zh":"John Howard 支持以有結構的國家敍事方式教授歷史。"},{"en":"Favour teaching history in a way means prefer or support that method of history education.","zh":"favour teaching history in a way 指偏好或支持某種歷史教育方法。"},{"en":"Some teachers favour teaching history through source analysis rather than memorising dates.","zh":"有些老師支持透過資料分析教授歷史，而不是背誦日期。"},{"en":"If a leader favours one narrative, they may want textbooks to follow that structure.","zh":"如果領袖偏好一種敍事，可能希望教科書跟隨該結構。"},{"en":"The phrase describes support for a particular teaching approach.","zh":"這個片語描述對特定教學方法的支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"as it was taught before","meaning":"如以前那樣教授","examples":[{"en":"The question compares present teaching with how history was taught before the 1980s.","zh":"題目把現時教學與1980年代以前歷史如以前那樣教授的方式作比較。"},{"en":"As it was taught before means in the way the subject used to be taught in the past.","zh":"as it was taught before 指某科目過去被教授的方式。"},{"en":"Some parents prefer grammar as it was taught before, with more drills and rules.","zh":"有些家長偏好文法如以前那樣教授，有更多操練和規則。"},{"en":"If history is taught as before, newer perspectives may be excluded.","zh":"如果歷史如以前那樣教授，較新角度可能被排除。"},{"en":"The phrase compares older teaching with current teaching.","zh":"這個片語比較舊教學與現時教學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"appears to demonstrate that","meaning":"似乎顯示","examples":[{"en":"The new Russian holiday appears to demonstrate a link between history and ideology.","zh":"俄羅斯新假日似乎顯示歷史與意識形態之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"Appears to demonstrate that means seems to show something, though the wording remains cautious.","zh":"appears to demonstrate that 指似乎顯示某事，但措辭仍然謹慎。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement appears to demonstrate that regular feedback is helping.","zh":"學生進步似乎顯示定期回饋正在發揮作用。"},{"en":"If a holiday replaces an older political symbol, it may show a new ideological direction.","zh":"如果假日取代較舊政治象徵，可能顯示新的意識形態方向。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a cautious interpretation of evidence.","zh":"這個片語引出對證據的謹慎解讀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"become less authoritative","meaning":"變得較少威權","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether Russia is becoming less authoritative.","zh":"該選項問俄羅斯是否變得較少威權。"},{"en":"Become less authoritative means become less controlling, less strict, or less commanding.","zh":"become less authoritative 指變得較少控制、較不嚴格或較少命令式。"},{"en":"A teacher may become less authoritative if students are allowed to choose project topics.","zh":"如果學生被允許選擇項目題目，老師可能變得較少威權。"},{"en":"If a state still enforces ideology strongly, it has not become less authoritative.","zh":"如果國家仍強硬執行意識形態，它就沒有變得較少威權。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a reduction in control or authority.","zh":"這個片語描述控制或權威減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"strongly enforce a link between","meaning":"強力維繫……之間的聯繫","examples":[{"en":"The state can strongly enforce a link between ideology and history.","zh":"國家可以強力維繫意識形態與歷史之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"Strongly enforce a link between means actively make two ideas appear connected through rules, teaching, or propaganda.","zh":"strongly enforce a link between 指透過規則、教學或宣傳積極令兩種觀念看似相連。"},{"en":"A school may strongly enforce a link between discipline and success through assemblies and posters.","zh":"學校可能透過早會和海報強力維繫紀律與成功之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"If the state controls holidays and textbooks, it can connect national ideology with historical memory.","zh":"如果國家控制假日和教科書，就能把國家意識形態與歷史記憶連接起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes powerful official reinforcement of a connection.","zh":"這個片語描述官方強力加強某種連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"ideology and history","meaning":"意識形態與歷史","examples":[{"en":"In some countries, ideology and history are closely connected.","zh":"在有些國家，意識形態與歷史緊密相連。"},{"en":"Ideology and history refers to the relationship between political beliefs and the way the past is explained.","zh":"ideology and history 指政治信念與過去被如何解釋之間的關係。"},{"en":"A textbook may connect ideology and history by presenting one party as the natural defender of the nation.","zh":"教科書可能把某政黨呈現為國家的天然捍衛者，從而連接意識形態與歷史。"},{"en":"If ideology shapes history lessons, students may learn loyalty before analysis.","zh":"如果意識形態塑造歷史課，學生可能先學忠誠而不是分析。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how politics can influence memory.","zh":"這個片語顯示政治如何影響記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be opposed to the influence of","meaning":"反對……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The holiday suggests opposition to the influence of Western Christianity.","zh":"該假日暗示反對西方基督教的影響。"},{"en":"Be opposed to the influence of means resist or reject the effect of another group, belief, or culture.","zh":"be opposed to the influence of 指抗拒或拒絕另一群體、信念或文化的影響。"},{"en":"Some parents are opposed to the influence of violent games on young children.","zh":"有些家長反對暴力遊戲對幼童的影響。"},{"en":"If a national symbol rejects outside influence, it may strengthen a defensive identity.","zh":"如果國家象徵拒絕外來影響，可能加強防衛性身份。"},{"en":"The phrase describes resistance to external impact.","zh":"這個片語描述對外部影響的抵抗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"Western Christianity","meaning":"西方基督教","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to the influence of Western Christianity.","zh":"題目提到西方基督教的影響。"},{"en":"Western Christianity refers to Christian traditions historically linked to Western Europe, including Roman Catholicism and Protestantism.","zh":"Western Christianity 指歷史上與西歐有關的基督教傳統，包括羅馬天主教和新教。"},{"en":"A history lesson may mention Western Christianity when discussing Europe’s religious and political development.","zh":"歷史課討論歐洲宗教和政治發展時，可能提到西方基督教。"},{"en":"If a holiday celebrates victory over Catholic outsiders, it may carry a message about Western Christianity.","zh":"如果假日慶祝戰勝天主教外來者，可能帶有關於西方基督教的訊息。"},{"en":"The phrase links religion with Western historical identity.","zh":"這個片語把宗教與西方歷史身份連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"taught differently","meaning":"以不同方式教授","examples":[{"en":"History is now taught differently in South Africa.","zh":"歷史現在在南非以不同方式教授。"},{"en":"Taught differently means taught in a new or changed way.","zh":"taught differently 指以新的或改變了的方式教授。"},{"en":"Grammar may be taught differently if teachers use examples instead of memorisation.","zh":"如果老師使用例子而不是背誦，文法可能以不同方式教授。"},{"en":"If society changes after apartheid, history may be taught differently to include more voices.","zh":"如果社會在種族隔離後改變，歷史可能以不同方式教授，以包括更多聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change in teaching method or content.","zh":"這個片語描述教學方法或內容改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the collapse of apartheid","meaning":"種族隔離制度瓦解","examples":[{"en":"The collapse of apartheid changed history teaching in South Africa.","zh":"種族隔離制度瓦解改變了南非的歷史教學。"},{"en":"The collapse of apartheid means the ending of South Africa’s legal system of racial separation and white minority rule.","zh":"the collapse of apartheid 指南非法定種族隔離和白人少數統治制度的終結。"},{"en":"A history lesson may explain how the collapse of apartheid led to new elections and new public symbols.","zh":"歷史課可能解釋種族隔離制度瓦解如何帶來新選舉和新公共象徵。"},{"en":"If a political system collapses, schools may need new textbooks and new values.","zh":"如果政治制度瓦解，學校可能需要新教科書和新價值。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a major turning point in South African history.","zh":"這個片語標示南非歷史中的重大轉捩點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"rule by white people","meaning":"白人統治","examples":[{"en":"The collapse of rule by white people led to a new national story.","zh":"白人統治瓦解導致新的國家故事出現。"},{"en":"Rule by white people means political control held by white people, especially over other racial groups.","zh":"rule by white people 指由白人掌握政治控制，尤其控制其他種族群體。"},{"en":"In apartheid South Africa, rule by white people limited the rights of the black majority.","zh":"在種族隔離南非，白人統治限制了黑人多數的權利。"},{"en":"If such rule ends, public history may need to include those previously excluded.","zh":"如果這種統治結束，公共歷史可能需要包括以前被排除的人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes racial political domination.","zh":"這個片語描述種族政治支配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"complete the following sentences","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the following sentences using words from the text.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成以下句子。"},{"en":"Complete the following sentences means fill in the missing words in the sentences below.","zh":"complete the following sentences 指填入下列句子中的缺失字詞。"},{"en":"In reading exams, students must check grammar before completing sentences.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生完成句子前必須檢查文法。"},{"en":"If the answer must come from the text, students should copy the exact words allowed.","zh":"如果答案必須來自文章，學生應抄寫允許的準確字詞。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個詞","examples":[{"en":"The instructions say to use no more than three words.","zh":"指示說使用不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案必須包含三個詞或更少。"},{"en":"If the answer is “the civil war,” it follows the three-word limit.","zh":"如果答案是 “the civil war”，它符合三詞限制。"},{"en":"If students write four words when only three are allowed, the answer may be marked wrong.","zh":"如果只允許三詞而學生寫四詞，答案可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個片語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"from the text","meaning":"從文章中","examples":[{"en":"The answers should be taken from the text.","zh":"答案應從文章中取得。"},{"en":"From the text means using words or information found in the passage itself.","zh":"from the text 指使用文章本身找到的字詞或資料。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students should not use outside knowledge if the answer must come from the text.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，如果答案必須來自文章，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"If an answer is not supported by the text, it may be wrong even if it is true in real life.","zh":"如果答案不受文章支持，即使現實中是真的，也可能是錯的。"},{"en":"The phrase tells students the source of the answer.","zh":"這個片語告訴學生答案來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a simple view of history","meaning":"簡化的歷史觀","examples":[{"en":"A simple view of history can be politically dangerous.","zh":"簡化的歷史觀可以在政治上很危險。"},{"en":"A simple view of history is an oversimplified explanation that leaves out complexity and disagreement.","zh":"simple view of history 指省略複雜性和分歧的過度簡化解釋。"},{"en":"A student has a simple view of history if every event is reduced to heroes and villains.","zh":"如果學生把每件事都簡化成英雄和壞人，就是有簡化歷史觀。"},{"en":"If people accept a simple view of history, they may blame one group too easily.","zh":"如果人們接受簡化歷史觀，可能太容易責怪某一群體。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that easy stories can distort the past.","zh":"這個片語提醒，容易理解的故事可以扭曲過去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"in Northern Ireland","meaning":"在北愛爾蘭","examples":[{"en":"A crude view of history was linked to conflict in Northern Ireland.","zh":"粗糙的歷史觀與北愛爾蘭衝突有關。"},{"en":"In Northern Ireland means in the region in the north-east of the island of Ireland that is part of the United Kingdom.","zh":"in Northern Ireland 指在愛爾蘭島東北部、屬於英國的地區。"},{"en":"A history class may discuss conflict in Northern Ireland when studying identity, religion, and nationalism.","zh":"歷史課研究身份、宗教和民族主義時，可能討論北愛爾蘭衝突。"},{"en":"If historical stories fuel tension in Northern Ireland, teaching must be handled carefully.","zh":"如果歷史故事在北愛爾蘭加劇緊張，教學就必須小心處理。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the location of a political conflict.","zh":"這個片語給出政治衝突的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"history classes","meaning":"歷史課","examples":[{"en":"History classes often reveal how a country sees itself.","zh":"歷史課常揭示一個國家如何看待自己。"},{"en":"History classes are school lessons where students learn about past events and their meanings.","zh":"history classes 指學生學習過去事件及其意義的學校課堂。"},{"en":"Good history classes ask students to compare sources, not just memorise dates.","zh":"好的歷史課要求學生比較資料來源，而不只是背日期。"},{"en":"If history classes include many viewpoints, students may understand society more deeply.","zh":"如果歷史課包含多種觀點，學生可能更深入理解社會。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to formal school learning about the past.","zh":"這個片語指關於過去的正式學校學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"can still be found in","meaning":"仍可在……找到","examples":[{"en":"Some terms can still be found in Australian classrooms.","zh":"有些詞語仍可在澳洲課室中找到。"},{"en":"Can still be found in means continue to exist or be used in a place.","zh":"can still be found in 指繼續存在於或被使用於某地方。"},{"en":"Chalkboards can still be found in some older classrooms.","zh":"在一些較舊課室中仍可找到黑板。"},{"en":"If a term disappears from policy language but remains in classrooms, teachers may be keeping it alive.","zh":"如果某詞從政策語言中消失但仍留在課室，老師可能仍在延續它。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses continued presence.","zh":"這個片語強調持續存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"different standpoints","meaning":"不同立場","examples":[{"en":"Modern history teaching may look at events from different standpoints.","zh":"現代歷史教學可能從不同立場看事件。"},{"en":"Different standpoints are different positions or perspectives from which people view an issue.","zh":"different standpoints 指人們看待議題時所處的不同位置或角度。"},{"en":"A debate about school uniforms includes different standpoints from students, parents, and teachers.","zh":"關於校服的辯論包括學生、家長和老師的不同立場。"},{"en":"If history uses different standpoints, students can see why the same event has multiple meanings.","zh":"如果歷史使用不同立場，學生就能看見同一事件為何有多重意義。"},{"en":"The phrase encourages perspective-taking.","zh":"這個片語鼓勵換位思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"another rigid ideology","meaning":"另一種僵化意識形態","examples":[{"en":"South Africa avoided replacing apartheid ideology with another rigid ideology.","zh":"南非避免以另一種僵化意識形態取代種族隔離意識形態。"},{"en":"Another rigid ideology means a different but still inflexible belief system.","zh":"another rigid ideology 指另一套不同但仍不靈活的信念系統。"},{"en":"A school should not replace one harsh discipline policy with another rigid ideology that ignores student needs.","zh":"學校不應以另一種仍忽略學生需要的僵化意識形態取代嚴苛紀律政策。"},{"en":"If reform only changes who is praised and blamed, thinking may remain closed.","zh":"如果改革只改變誰被讚揚和責怪，思維可能仍然封閉。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against replacing one narrow system with another.","zh":"這個片語提醒不要以另一個狹窄制度取代原有制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"符合文中資料","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the information in the passage.","zh":"學生判斷每句陳述是否符合文章中的資料。"},{"en":"Agree with the information means match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"A True statement agrees with the information because it repeats the same meaning accurately.","zh":"True 陳述符合資料，因為它準確重述同一意思。"},{"en":"If a statement changes an important detail, it may no longer agree with the passage.","zh":"如果陳述改變重要細節，就可能不再符合文章。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in True, False, Not Given questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於 True, False, Not Given 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the information in the passage.","zh":"陳述可能與文章中的資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradict the information means say the opposite of what the passage states.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章所述相反的意思。"},{"en":"If a text says the curriculum became more open, a statement saying it became narrower contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說課程變得更開放，而陳述說它變得更狹窄，就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should choose False only when the passage directly disagrees with the statement.","zh":"學生只有在文章直接反對陳述時才應選 False。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a clear conflict with the text.","zh":"這個片語描述與文本清楚衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"If the passage gives no evidence, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文章沒有提供證據，文中就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文章沒有說明該陳述是真還是假。"},{"en":"If a passage discusses textbooks but not their price, there is no information on the price.","zh":"如果文章討論教科書但沒有討論價格，文中就沒有關於價格的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when there is no information in the passage.","zh":"當文章沒有資料時，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"The phrase explains when to choose Not Given.","zh":"這個片語解釋何時選 Not Given。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"as Ireland became richer","meaning":"隨着愛爾蘭變得更富裕","examples":[{"en":"As Ireland became richer, its view of history became less simplistic.","zh":"隨着愛爾蘭變得更富裕，它的歷史觀變得較不簡化。"},{"en":"As Ireland became richer means while Ireland grew more economically prosperous.","zh":"as Ireland became richer 指隨着愛爾蘭經濟上變得更繁榮。"},{"en":"As a family becomes richer, it may spend more on education, travel, and cultural activities.","zh":"隨着家庭變得更富裕，可能在教育、旅遊和文化活動上花更多錢。"},{"en":"If a country becomes richer and more confident, it may feel less need for simple national myths.","zh":"如果一個國家變得更富裕和更自信，可能較少需要簡單國家神話。"},{"en":"The phrase links economic change with changes in thinking.","zh":"這個片語把經濟變化與思想變化連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"become less interested in","meaning":"對……較少興趣","examples":[{"en":"A more confident society may become less interested in simple myths.","zh":"更自信的社會可能對簡單神話較少興趣。"},{"en":"Become less interested in means care about something less than before.","zh":"become less interested in 指比以前較少關心某事。"},{"en":"Students may become less interested in memorising model answers once they understand how to write independently.","zh":"一旦學生理解如何獨立寫作，可能對背誦範文較少興趣。"},{"en":"If people feel secure in their identity, they may need fewer simplified stories.","zh":"如果人們對自身身份有安全感，可能較少需要簡化故事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a decline in attention or desire.","zh":"這個片語描述注意或慾望下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"allow students to think for themselves","meaning":"讓學生獨立思考","examples":[{"en":"Some countries believe history should allow students to think for themselves.","zh":"有些國家相信歷史應讓學生獨立思考。"},{"en":"Allow students to think for themselves means give learners space to form their own evidence-based judgements.","zh":"allow students to think for themselves 指給學習者空間形成自己有證據支持的判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher allows students to think for themselves by asking questions instead of giving every answer.","zh":"老師透過提問而不是給出所有答案，讓學生獨立思考。"},{"en":"If history lessons include sources and debate, students practise independent judgement.","zh":"如果歷史課包括資料來源和辯論，學生就練習自主判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses autonomy in learning.","zh":"這個片語強調學習自主性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the meanings of words","meaning":"詞語的意思","examples":[{"en":"The meanings of words such as “settlement” and “invasion” are different.","zh":"“settlement” 和 “invasion” 等詞語的意思不同。"},{"en":"The meanings of words are the ideas, attitudes, and implications carried by particular terms.","zh":"meanings of words 指特定詞語承載的想法、態度和含意。"},{"en":"In history, the meanings of words can change how students judge an event.","zh":"在歷史中，詞語的意思可以改變學生如何判斷事件。"},{"en":"If one word sounds peaceful and another sounds violent, choosing between them matters.","zh":"如果一個詞聽起來和平，另一個聽起來暴力，選哪個詞就很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds learners that vocabulary is not neutral.","zh":"這個片語提醒學習者，詞彙不是中性的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"not the same","meaning":"並不相同","examples":[{"en":"The words “settlement” and “invasion” are not the same.","zh":"“settlement” 和 “invasion” 這兩個詞並不相同。"},{"en":"Not the same means different in meaning, effect, or nature.","zh":"not the same 指在意思、效果或性質上不同。"},{"en":"Being quiet and being rude are not the same.","zh":"安靜和無禮並不相同。"},{"en":"If two history terms are not the same, students should not use them interchangeably.","zh":"如果兩個歷史術語並不相同，學生不應互換使用。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses difference.","zh":"這個片語強調差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"an important part of","meaning":"……的重要部分","examples":[{"en":"A foundation story can be an important part of history classes.","zh":"建國故事可以是歷史課的重要部分。"},{"en":"An important part of means a significant element within a larger thing.","zh":"an important part of 指較大事物中的重要元素。"},{"en":"Feedback is an important part of learning because students need to know what to improve.","zh":"回饋是學習的重要部分，因為學生需要知道要改善甚麼。"},{"en":"If foundation stories shape identity, they become important parts of school history.","zh":"如果建國故事塑造身份，它們就成為學校歷史的重要部分。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies something that matters within a bigger whole.","zh":"這個片語指出較大整體中重要的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"include different standpoints","meaning":"包含不同立場","examples":[{"en":"The South African curriculum aims to include different standpoints.","zh":"南非課程旨在包含不同立場。"},{"en":"Include different standpoints means bring in more than one perspective or position.","zh":"include different standpoints 指納入多於一個角度或立場。"},{"en":"A fair debate lesson should include different standpoints before students write conclusions.","zh":"公平的辯論課在學生寫結論前應包含不同立場。"},{"en":"If a curriculum includes victims, rulers, ordinary people, and minorities, history becomes fuller.","zh":"如果課程包括受害者、統治者、普通人和少數群體，歷史就更完整。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses balanced and inclusive teaching.","zh":"這個片語強調平衡而具包容性的教學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"bring people together","meaning":"使人們團結起來","examples":[{"en":"The new curriculum aims to bring people together.","zh":"新課程旨在使人們團結起來。"},{"en":"Bring people together means unite people or help different groups feel connected.","zh":"bring people together 指團結人們，或幫助不同群體感到彼此相連。"},{"en":"A school fair can bring people together when parents, teachers, and students work on the same project.","zh":"當家長、老師和學生共同完成同一項目，學校嘉年華可以使人們團結起來。"},{"en":"If history teaching promotes reconciliation, it can reduce distance between former opponents.","zh":"如果歷史教學推動和解，就能減少昔日對立者之間的距離。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating unity after difference or division.","zh":"這個片語描述在差異或分裂後創造團結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 102 - Learning about the Past.pdf","sourcePage":21}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 103":[{"front":"black gold","meaning":"黑金；珍貴的黑色商品","examples":[{"en":"The title “Black Gold” suggests that dark chocolate has become highly valuable.","zh":"標題「黑金」暗示黑朱古力已變得非常有價值。"},{"en":"Black gold refers to a dark substance or product that has become extremely valuable.","zh":"Black gold 指一種黑色或深色物質或產品變得極具價值。"},{"en":"Coffee was once called black gold by traders because people were willing to pay high prices for it.","zh":"咖啡曾被商人稱為黑金，因為人們願意為它支付高價。"},{"en":"If demand rises sharply, an ordinary product can start to look like black gold.","zh":"如果需求急升，普通產品也可以開始看起來像黑金。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when a black or dark product becomes commercially precious.","zh":"這個片語常用於形容黑色或深色產品變得具有商業價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dark chocolate","meaning":"黑朱古力","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate used to be an acquired taste.","zh":"黑朱古力過去曾經是一種後天培養出來的喜好。"},{"en":"Dark chocolate is chocolate with a higher cocoa content and a less milky, often less sweet flavour.","zh":"Dark chocolate 是可可含量較高、奶味較少且通常不那麼甜的朱古力。"},{"en":"Some people prefer dark chocolate after they grow tired of very sweet snacks.","zh":"有些人吃厭很甜的零食後，會較喜歡黑朱古力。"},{"en":"Because dark chocolate contains more cocoa, it may need more cacao beans to produce.","zh":"因為黑朱古力含有更多可可，生產它可能需要更多可可豆。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the stronger, more cocoa-rich type of chocolate.","zh":"這個片語描述味道較濃、可可含量較高的朱古力種類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"used to be","meaning":"過去曾經是","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate used to be an acquired taste.","zh":"黑朱古力過去曾經是一種後天培養出來的喜好。"},{"en":"Used to be means something was true in the past but is no longer true now.","zh":"Used to be 指某事在過去是真的，但現在不再是這樣。"},{"en":"This street used to be quiet, but it is now full of cafés and tourists.","zh":"這條街過去曾經很安靜，但現在滿是咖啡店和遊客。"},{"en":"If a product used to be unpopular but becomes fashionable, companies may quickly promote it.","zh":"如果一種產品過去不受歡迎但後來變得流行，公司可能很快推廣它。"},{"en":"This phrase helps contrast the past with the present.","zh":"這個片語幫助對比過去和現在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an acquired taste","meaning":"後天培養出來的喜好","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate used to be an acquired taste.","zh":"黑朱古力過去曾經是一種後天培養出來的喜好。"},{"en":"An acquired taste is something people may dislike at first but learn to enjoy over time.","zh":"Acquired taste 是人們起初可能不喜歡，但隨時間學會欣賞的東西。"},{"en":"Black coffee can be an acquired taste because beginners often find it too bitter.","zh":"黑咖啡可以是一種後天培養出來的喜好，因為初學者常覺得它太苦。"},{"en":"If people repeatedly try a strong flavour, it may become an acquired taste.","zh":"如果人們反覆嘗試強烈味道，它可能變成後天培養出來的喜好。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for food, drink, music, or styles that take time to enjoy.","zh":"這個片語常用於食物、飲品、音樂或需要時間欣賞的風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the trouble is","meaning":"問題是","examples":[{"en":"The trouble is, we have all acquired a taste for dark chocolate.","zh":"問題是，我們全都培養出對黑朱古力的喜好。"},{"en":"The trouble is introduces the main problem in a situation.","zh":"The trouble is 用來引出某情況中的主要問題。"},{"en":"The trouble is, the school wants smaller classes but does not have enough teachers.","zh":"問題是，學校想要更小班教學，但教師不足。"},{"en":"If many people suddenly want the same product, the trouble is that supply may not keep up.","zh":"如果許多人突然想要同一產品，問題是供應可能跟不上。"},{"en":"This phrase is used before explaining what makes a situation difficult.","zh":"這個片語用於解釋某情況困難之處之前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"acquire a taste for","meaning":"培養出對……的喜好","examples":[{"en":"Many consumers have acquired a taste for dark chocolate.","zh":"許多消費者已培養出對黑朱古力的喜好。"},{"en":"To acquire a taste for something means to gradually learn to like it.","zh":"To acquire a taste for something 指逐漸學會喜歡某事物。"},{"en":"A student may acquire a taste for classical music after hearing it in films and concerts.","zh":"學生可能在電影和音樂會中聽到古典音樂後，培養出對它的喜好。"},{"en":"If consumers acquire a taste for bitter flavours, demand for sweeter products may fall.","zh":"如果消費者培養出對苦味的喜好，對較甜產品的需求可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a preference that develops over time.","zh":"這個片語描述隨時間發展出來的偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cocoa prices soar","meaning":"可可價格急升","examples":[{"en":"As cocoa prices soar, chocolate makers face higher costs.","zh":"隨着可可價格急升，朱古力生產商面對更高成本。"},{"en":"When cocoa prices soar, the price of cocoa rises very quickly and sharply.","zh":"Cocoa prices soar 指可可價格快速而大幅上升。"},{"en":"If wheat prices soar, bakeries may charge more for bread.","zh":"如果小麥價格急升，麵包店可能提高麵包價格。"},{"en":"Cocoa prices may soar when poor weather reduces supply and demand remains strong.","zh":"當惡劣天氣減少供應而需求仍強，可可價格可能急升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sudden and serious rise in cocoa costs.","zh":"這個片語描述可可成本突然大幅上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a shortage looms","meaning":"短缺迫在眉睫","examples":[{"en":"A shortage looms as demand for cocoa increases.","zh":"隨着可可需求增加，短缺迫在眉睫。"},{"en":"A shortage looms means a lack of supply seems likely to happen soon.","zh":"A shortage looms 指供應不足似乎很快會發生。"},{"en":"If many teachers resign before September, a school shortage may loom.","zh":"如果許多老師在九月前辭職，學校可能面臨人手短缺。"},{"en":"When demand grows faster than supply, a shortage can loom in the market.","zh":"當需求增長快過供應，市場短缺可能迫在眉睫。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a sense of warning about a coming shortage.","zh":"這個片語營造對即將出現短缺的警告感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"changing tastes","meaning":"不斷轉變的口味","examples":[{"en":"Changing tastes are increasing demand for dark chocolate.","zh":"不斷轉變的口味正在增加對黑朱古力的需求。"},{"en":"Changing tastes are shifts in what people like, buy, eat, or value.","zh":"Changing tastes 是人們喜歡、購買、食用或重視的東西出現變化。"},{"en":"Changing tastes among young people may make bubble tea shops more popular than old-style cafés.","zh":"年輕人口味轉變，可能令珍珠奶茶店比舊式咖啡店更受歡迎。"},{"en":"If tastes change quickly, businesses must update their products to keep customers.","zh":"如果口味快速轉變，商家必須更新產品以留住顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how consumer preferences move over time.","zh":"這個片語描述消費者偏好如何隨時間改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"threaten the source of","meaning":"威脅……的來源","examples":[{"en":"Our changing tastes could be threatening the source of our pleasure.","zh":"我們不斷轉變的口味可能正在威脅快樂的來源。"},{"en":"To threaten the source of something means to put the thing that provides it at risk.","zh":"To threaten the source of something 指令提供某事物的來源面臨風險。"},{"en":"Overfishing can threaten the source of a fishing village’s income.","zh":"過度捕魚可以威脅漁村收入的來源。"},{"en":"If chocolate demand damages cacao supply, our pleasure may undermine its own source.","zh":"如果朱古力需求破壞可可供應，我們的快樂可能會損害自身來源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harming the origin of something we value.","zh":"這個片語描述傷害我們重視之物的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the very source of","meaning":"……本身的來源","examples":[{"en":"Rising demand may threaten the very source of chocolate lovers’ pleasure.","zh":"需求上升可能威脅朱古力愛好者快樂本身的來源。"},{"en":"The very source of something means the exact basic origin from which it comes.","zh":"The very source of something 指某事物最根本、最直接的來源。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can attack the very source of a student’s concentration.","zh":"睡眠不足可以打擊學生專注力本身的來源。"},{"en":"If a business mistreats its loyal customers, it may damage the very source of its success.","zh":"如果企業惡待忠實顧客，它可能損害成功本身的來源。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the most important origin is being affected.","zh":"這個片語強調最重要的根源正在受影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a 25% jump in","meaning":"百分之二十五的急升","examples":[{"en":"A 25% jump in dark chocolate sales shows how popular it has become.","zh":"黑朱古力銷售百分之二十五的急升顯示它已變得多受歡迎。"},{"en":"A 25% jump in something means it has increased by one quarter.","zh":"A 25% jump in something 指某事物增加了四分之一。"},{"en":"A 25% jump in bus fares would make daily travel much more expensive for students.","zh":"巴士車費百分之二十五的急升會令學生每日交通昂貴得多。"},{"en":"If sales show a 25% jump, shops may order more stock next month.","zh":"如果銷售出現百分之二十五急升，商店下月可能訂更多貨。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large numerical increase.","zh":"這個片語描述大幅數字增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"speak for itself","meaning":"不言而喻","examples":[{"en":"The jump in dark chocolate sales pretty much speaks for itself.","zh":"黑朱古力銷售急升幾乎已不言而喻。"},{"en":"If something speaks for itself, it is so clear that little explanation is needed.","zh":"If something speaks for itself 指某事非常清楚，幾乎不需要解釋。"},{"en":"A student’s improved marks speak for themselves after months of steady practice.","zh":"學生經過數月穩定練習後成績進步，已不言而喻。"},{"en":"If customer complaints double, the problem speaks for itself.","zh":"如果顧客投訴增加一倍，問題就不言而喻。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when evidence is obvious.","zh":"這個片語用於證據很明顯的時候。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as a nation","meaning":"作為一個國家；全國而言","examples":[{"en":"As a nation, British consumers are turning away from milk chocolate.","zh":"全國而言，英國消費者正在遠離牛奶朱古力。"},{"en":"As a nation means considering the people of a country as a whole.","zh":"As a nation 指把一個國家的人民作為整體來看。"},{"en":"As a nation, people may start using public transport more when fuel becomes expensive.","zh":"全國而言，當燃油變得昂貴，人們可能開始更多使用公共交通。"},{"en":"If tastes change as a nation, the food industry may change quickly.","zh":"如果口味在全國層面改變，食品業可能迅速變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broad national pattern, not just individual behaviour.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛的全國模式，而不是個別行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"turn one’s back on","meaning":"背棄；不再接受","examples":[{"en":"Consumers are turning their backs on the bland taste of milk chocolate.","zh":"消費者正在背棄牛奶朱古力平淡的味道。"},{"en":"To turn one’s back on something means to reject it or stop supporting it.","zh":"To turn one’s back on something 指拒絕某事或停止支持它。"},{"en":"A student may turn his back on unhealthy snacks after joining a sports team.","zh":"學生加入運動隊後，可能不再接受不健康零食。"},{"en":"If shoppers turn their backs on a product, companies may redesign it or reduce its price.","zh":"如果購物者背棄某產品，公司可能重新設計它或減價。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests deliberate rejection or abandonment.","zh":"這個片語暗示有意識地拒絕或放棄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"bland taste","meaning":"平淡的味道","examples":[{"en":"Some consumers dislike the bland taste of milk chocolate.","zh":"有些消費者不喜歡牛奶朱古力平淡的味道。"},{"en":"A bland taste is mild, plain, and not very strong or interesting.","zh":"Bland taste 是溫和、普通，而且不太強烈或有趣的味道。"},{"en":"Soup may have a bland taste if the cook forgets to add salt or herbs.","zh":"如果廚師忘記加鹽或香草，湯可能有平淡的味道。"},{"en":"If customers want stronger flavours, a bland taste can make a product less attractive.","zh":"如果顧客想要更強烈味道，平淡的味道會令產品較不吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes food that lacks depth or character.","zh":"這個片語描述缺乏深度或特色的食物味道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"milk chocolate","meaning":"牛奶朱古力","examples":[{"en":"Many shoppers are choosing dark chocolate instead of milk chocolate.","zh":"許多購物者選擇黑朱古力，而不是牛奶朱古力。"},{"en":"Milk chocolate is chocolate made with milk and usually a sweeter, creamier taste.","zh":"Milk chocolate 是加入牛奶製成，通常味道較甜和較滑的朱古力。"},{"en":"Children often prefer milk chocolate because it tastes sweeter and less bitter.","zh":"孩子通常較喜歡牛奶朱古力，因為它較甜、不那麼苦。"},{"en":"If consumers move away from milk chocolate, demand for darker cocoa-rich products may rise.","zh":"如果消費者遠離牛奶朱古力，對可可含量較高的深色產品需求可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the milder, sweeter type of chocolate.","zh":"這個片語指較溫和、較甜的朱古力種類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be saturated with","meaning":"充滿；飽含","examples":[{"en":"Milk chocolate is often saturated with vegetable oil.","zh":"牛奶朱古力常充滿植物油。"},{"en":"To be saturated with something means to be filled or soaked with a large amount of it.","zh":"To be saturated with something 指充滿或浸透大量某物。"},{"en":"A sponge can be saturated with water after being left in the sink.","zh":"海綿放在洗手盆裏後，可能充滿水。"},{"en":"If a product is saturated with cheap oil, customers may see it as lower quality.","zh":"如果產品充滿廉價油，顧客可能視它為較低質素。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something contains a lot of a substance.","zh":"這個片語暗示某物含有大量某種物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"vegetable oil","meaning":"植物油","examples":[{"en":"Some milk chocolate is saturated with vegetable oil.","zh":"有些牛奶朱古力充滿植物油。"},{"en":"Vegetable oil is oil made from plants, such as sunflower, palm, or soybean oil.","zh":"Vegetable oil 是由植物製成的油，例如葵花籽油、棕櫚油或大豆油。"},{"en":"A family may use vegetable oil to fry eggs or cook vegetables at home.","zh":"家庭可能用植物油煎蛋或炒菜。"},{"en":"If too much vegetable oil is added to chocolate, it may change the texture and taste.","zh":"如果朱古力加入太多植物油，它可能改變口感和味道。"},{"en":"This phrase names a common cooking and food-manufacturing ingredient.","zh":"這個片語命名常見的烹調和食品製造材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"dominate counters","meaning":"佔據櫃枱主導位置","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate now dominates counters in many supermarkets.","zh":"黑朱古力現在在許多超級市場佔據櫃枱主導位置。"},{"en":"To dominate counters means to take up the most visible or largest space at shop counters.","zh":"To dominate counters 指在商店櫃枱上佔據最顯眼或最大空間。"},{"en":"During exam season, revision books may dominate counters in bookshops.","zh":"考試季期間，補充練習書可能在書店櫃枱佔主導位置。"},{"en":"If one product dominates counters, shoppers see it before they see alternatives.","zh":"如果一種產品佔據櫃枱主導位置，購物者會先看見它，再看見其他選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong physical presence in shops.","zh":"這個片語描述產品在商店中的強大實體存在感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"supermarket counters","meaning":"超級市場櫃枱","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate dominates supermarket counters in many shops.","zh":"黑朱古力在許多商店的超級市場櫃枱佔主導位置。"},{"en":"Supermarket counters are display or service areas in a supermarket where goods are shown or sold.","zh":"Supermarket counters 是超級市場中展示或售賣商品的展示或服務區。"},{"en":"Snacks near supermarket counters often attract customers waiting to pay.","zh":"超級市場櫃枱附近的零食常吸引等候付款的顧客。"},{"en":"If a product is placed on supermarket counters, shoppers may buy it impulsively.","zh":"如果產品放在超級市場櫃枱上，購物者可能衝動購買。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to visible selling spaces inside supermarkets.","zh":"這個片語指超級市場內顯眼的售賣空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"chocoholics","meaning":"朱古力迷","examples":[{"en":"Chocoholics should prepare for rising chocolate prices.","zh":"朱古力迷應為朱古力價格上升做好準備。"},{"en":"Chocoholics are people who love chocolate very much and eat it often.","zh":"Chocoholics 是非常喜歡朱古力並經常吃朱古力的人。"},{"en":"A chocoholic may keep chocolate in a desk drawer for afternoon snacks.","zh":"朱古力迷可能在書桌抽屜放朱古力作下午小食。"},{"en":"If chocolate prices rise, chocoholics may notice the change quickly because they buy it often.","zh":"如果朱古力價格上升，朱古力迷可能很快注意到變化，因為他們常買。"},{"en":"This informal word describes strong chocolate lovers, not a medical condition.","zh":"這個非正式詞語描述非常愛吃朱古力的人，而不是醫學病症。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"brace themselves","meaning":"做好心理準備","examples":[{"en":"Chocoholics should brace themselves for a possible shortage.","zh":"朱古力迷應為可能出現的短缺做好心理準備。"},{"en":"To brace themselves means to prepare mentally for something difficult or unpleasant.","zh":"To brace themselves 指為困難或不愉快的事情作心理準備。"},{"en":"Students may brace themselves before receiving difficult exam results.","zh":"學生收到困難考試成績前，可能會做好心理準備。"},{"en":"If prices are expected to rise, families may brace themselves by cutting other spending.","zh":"如果預期價格上升，家庭可能透過削減其他開支來做好準備。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests preparing for bad news or pressure.","zh":"這個片語暗示為壞消息或壓力作準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fears over","meaning":"對……的憂慮","examples":[{"en":"Fears over a global chocolate shortage have affected cocoa markets.","zh":"對全球朱古力短缺的憂慮已影響可可市場。"},{"en":"Fears over something are worries or concerns about a possible problem.","zh":"Fears over something 是對可能問題的擔心或關注。"},{"en":"Fears over rising rents may make families delay moving house.","zh":"對租金上升的憂慮，可能令家庭延遲搬屋。"},{"en":"If fears over supply grow, buyers may rush to purchase more early.","zh":"如果對供應的憂慮增加，買家可能提早搶購更多。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces public or market anxiety.","zh":"這個片語引出公眾或市場焦慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"global chocolate shortage","meaning":"全球朱古力短缺","examples":[{"en":"There are fears over a global chocolate shortage.","zh":"人們憂慮全球朱古力短缺。"},{"en":"A global chocolate shortage is a worldwide lack of enough chocolate or cocoa supply.","zh":"Global chocolate shortage 是全球缺乏足夠朱古力或可可供應。"},{"en":"A global chocolate shortage could make chocolate bars smaller or more expensive.","zh":"全球朱古力短缺可能令朱古力條變小或變貴。"},{"en":"If cacao harvests fail while demand rises, a global shortage may become likely.","zh":"如果可可收成失敗而需求上升，全球短缺可能變得很有可能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a supply problem affecting many countries.","zh":"這個片語描述影響多個國家的供應問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"spark a run on","meaning":"引發搶購潮","examples":[{"en":"The shortage fears have sparked a run on dark chocolate ingredients.","zh":"短缺憂慮已引發黑朱古力材料的搶購潮。"},{"en":"To spark a run on something means to trigger sudden heavy buying of it.","zh":"To spark a run on something 指觸發對某物的突然大量購買。"},{"en":"News of a coming typhoon can spark a run on bottled water and batteries.","zh":"颱風即將來臨的消息可以引發樽裝水和電池的搶購潮。"},{"en":"If buyers fear a shortage, they may rush to buy, making the shortage worse.","zh":"如果買家害怕短缺，他們可能搶購，令短缺更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes panic-driven or urgent buying.","zh":"這個片語描述恐慌或急切推動的購買。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the dark stuff","meaning":"黑朱古力；黑色那東西","examples":[{"en":"The phrase “the dark stuff” refers informally to dark chocolate.","zh":"“The dark stuff” 這個片語非正式地指黑朱古力。"},{"en":"The dark stuff is an informal way to refer to dark chocolate in this context.","zh":"在此語境中，the dark stuff 是非正式指黑朱古力的說法。"},{"en":"A shop assistant might say, “The dark stuff is on the top shelf,” when talking casually about chocolate.","zh":"店員閒談朱古力時可能說：「黑朱古力在最上層貨架。」"},{"en":"If a writer uses this phrase, the tone becomes more playful and conversational.","zh":"如果作者使用這個片語，語氣會變得較活潑和口語化。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and depends strongly on context.","zh":"這個片語屬非正式用語，十分依賴語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"world cocoa markets","meaning":"世界可可市場","examples":[{"en":"World cocoa markets have reacted to shortage fears.","zh":"世界可可市場已對短缺憂慮作出反應。"},{"en":"World cocoa markets are global places or systems where cocoa is bought, sold, and priced.","zh":"World cocoa markets 是全球買賣和定價可可的地方或系統。"},{"en":"Traders watch world cocoa markets to see whether chocolate-making costs will rise.","zh":"交易員觀察世界可可市場，以了解朱古力製造成本會否上升。"},{"en":"If harvests fail in major producer countries, world cocoa markets may respond quickly.","zh":"如果主要生產國收成失敗，世界可可市場可能迅速反應。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to international cocoa trading.","zh":"這個片語指國際可可交易。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"push up the price of","meaning":"推高……的價格","examples":[{"en":"High demand has pushed up the price of cacao beans.","zh":"高需求推高了可可豆的價格。"},{"en":"To push up the price of something means to make it become more expensive.","zh":"To push up the price of something 指令某物變得更昂貴。"},{"en":"A shortage of rental flats can push up the price of housing.","zh":"租盤短缺可以推高住屋價格。"},{"en":"If supply falls and demand remains strong, prices are likely to rise.","zh":"如果供應下降而需求仍強，價格很可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes upward pressure on prices.","zh":"這個片語描述對價格的上升壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cacao beans","meaning":"可可豆","examples":[{"en":"Cacao beans are used to make cocoa and chocolate.","zh":"可可豆被用來製造可可和朱古力。"},{"en":"Cacao beans are the seeds from the cacao tree, used as the basic ingredient of chocolate.","zh":"Cacao beans 是可可樹的種子，是製造朱古力的基本材料。"},{"en":"A chocolate factory buys cacao beans before roasting and processing them.","zh":"朱古力工廠在烘焙和加工前會購買可可豆。"},{"en":"If cacao bean harvests are poor, chocolate makers may face higher costs.","zh":"如果可可豆收成差，朱古力生產商可能面對更高成本。"},{"en":"This phrase names the raw material behind chocolate.","zh":"這個片語命名朱古力背後的原材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be used to make","meaning":"被用來製造","examples":[{"en":"Cacao beans are used to make cocoa.","zh":"可可豆被用來製造可可。"},{"en":"To be used to make something means to serve as a material or ingredient for producing it.","zh":"To be used to make something 指作為生產某物的材料或成分。"},{"en":"Flour is used to make bread, cakes, and noodles.","zh":"麵粉被用來製造麵包、蛋糕和麵條。"},{"en":"If an ingredient is used to make a popular product, demand for that ingredient may rise.","zh":"如果某成分被用來製造受歡迎產品，對該成分的需求可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose of a material.","zh":"這個片語解釋材料的用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"their highest level","meaning":"最高水平","examples":[{"en":"Cacao bean prices have reached their highest level for more than two years.","zh":"可可豆價格已達兩年多以來的最高水平。"},{"en":"Their highest level means the greatest point or amount reached within a period.","zh":"Their highest level 指在某段時間內達到的最高點或最大數量。"},{"en":"School attendance reached its highest level after the new bus service began.","zh":"新巴士服務開始後，學校出席率達到最高水平。"},{"en":"If prices reach their highest level, buyers may delay purchases or seek alternatives.","zh":"如果價格達到最高水平，買家可能延遲購買或尋找替代品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a record or peak point.","zh":"這個片語描述紀錄或高峰點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"for more than two years","meaning":"兩年多以來","examples":[{"en":"Cocoa prices reached their highest level for more than two years.","zh":"可可價格達到兩年多以來的最高水平。"},{"en":"For more than two years means for a period longer than two years.","zh":"For more than two years 指超過兩年的時間。"},{"en":"A student may study English with the same teacher for more than two years.","zh":"學生可能跟同一位老師學英文兩年多。"},{"en":"If prices are at their highest for more than two years, the rise is significant.","zh":"如果價格處於兩年多以來最高水平，升幅就很明顯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a period exceeding two years.","zh":"這個片語描述超過兩年的時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cocoa futures","meaning":"可可期貨","examples":[{"en":"The price of cocoa futures has climbed steadily.","zh":"可可期貨價格已穩步上升。"},{"en":"Cocoa futures are contracts to buy or sell cocoa at a future date at an agreed price.","zh":"Cocoa futures 是以約定價格在未來日期買入或賣出可可的合約。"},{"en":"Traders may buy cocoa futures if they expect cocoa prices to rise.","zh":"如果交易員預期可可價格上升，他們可能買入可可期貨。"},{"en":"If futures prices rise, markets may expect future cocoa supply to be tight.","zh":"如果期貨價格上升，市場可能預期未來可可供應緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to financial contracts linked to cocoa.","zh":"這個片語指與可可相關的金融合約。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be traded on","meaning":"在……上交易","examples":[{"en":"Cocoa futures are traded on world commodity markets.","zh":"可可期貨在世界商品市場上交易。"},{"en":"To be traded on a market means to be bought and sold there.","zh":"To be traded on a market 指在某市場上被買賣。"},{"en":"Company shares are traded on stock exchanges every working day.","zh":"公司股票每個工作日在證券交易所上交易。"},{"en":"If a product is traded globally, events in one country can affect prices elsewhere.","zh":"如果產品在全球交易，一個國家的事件可以影響其他地方的價格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where buying and selling happen.","zh":"這個片語描述買賣發生的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"world commodity markets","meaning":"世界商品市場","examples":[{"en":"Cocoa futures are traded on world commodity markets.","zh":"可可期貨在世界商品市場上交易。"},{"en":"World commodity markets are global trading systems for raw materials such as cocoa, oil, wheat, and metals.","zh":"World commodity markets 是交易可可、石油、小麥和金屬等原材料的全球系統。"},{"en":"Investors watch world commodity markets to understand changes in food and energy prices.","zh":"投資者觀察世界商品市場，以了解食品和能源價格變化。"},{"en":"If drought affects a crop, commodity markets may react before shoppers see price changes.","zh":"如果乾旱影響作物，商品市場可能在購物者看到價格變化前已作反應。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to international markets for basic goods.","zh":"這個片語指基本商品的國際市場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"climb steadily","meaning":"穩步上升","examples":[{"en":"The price of cocoa futures has climbed steadily since last November.","zh":"自去年十一月以來，可可期貨價格已穩步上升。"},{"en":"To climb steadily means to rise gradually and continuously.","zh":"To climb steadily 指逐漸而持續地上升。"},{"en":"A student’s marks may climb steadily after weekly practice and feedback.","zh":"學生經過每週練習和回饋後，成績可能穩步上升。"},{"en":"If prices climb steadily, buyers may expect the trend to continue.","zh":"如果價格穩步上升，買家可能預期趨勢會持續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a slow but consistent increase.","zh":"這個片語描述緩慢但穩定的增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"revive fears of","meaning":"重新引發對……的憂慮","examples":[{"en":"The recent price rise has revived fears of the cocoa crisis.","zh":"最近價格上升重新引發對可可危機的憂慮。"},{"en":"To revive fears of something means to bring back worries that people had before.","zh":"To revive fears of something 指重新帶回人們以前有過的憂慮。"},{"en":"A new flu outbreak may revive fears of school closures.","zh":"新一輪流感爆發可能重新引發對停課的憂慮。"},{"en":"If prices rise again after an old crisis, people may worry the same problem is returning.","zh":"如果舊危機後價格再次上升，人們可能擔心同一問題正在回來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes old anxieties becoming active again.","zh":"這個片語描述舊焦慮再次變得活躍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cocoa crisis","meaning":"可可危機","examples":[{"en":"The cocoa crisis of 2002 forced manufacturers to raise prices.","zh":"2002年的可可危機迫使生產商提高價格。"},{"en":"A cocoa crisis is a serious problem in cocoa supply, price, or production.","zh":"Cocoa crisis 是可可供應、價格或生產方面的嚴重問題。"},{"en":"A cocoa crisis can affect farmers, chocolate makers, shops, and consumers.","zh":"可可危機可以影響農民、朱古力生產商、商店和消費者。"},{"en":"If a cocoa crisis reduces supply, chocolate products may become more expensive.","zh":"如果可可危機減少供應，朱古力產品可能變得更昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major disruption in the cocoa industry.","zh":"這個片語描述可可行業中的重大干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"major manufacturers","meaning":"主要生產商","examples":[{"en":"Major manufacturers such as Nestlé were affected by the cocoa crisis.","zh":"雀巢等主要生產商受到可可危機影響。"},{"en":"Major manufacturers are large companies that produce goods on a big scale.","zh":"Major manufacturers 是大規模生產商品的大型公司。"},{"en":"Major manufacturers of phones may change prices when material costs rise.","zh":"主要手機生產商在材料成本上升時可能改變價格。"},{"en":"If major manufacturers face higher costs, the effect may reach ordinary consumers.","zh":"如果主要生產商面對更高成本，影響可能傳到普通消費者。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to large producers in an industry.","zh":"這個片語指某行業中的大型生產者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"hike the prices of","meaning":"大幅提高……的價格","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers had to hike the prices of some chocolate bars.","zh":"生產商不得不大幅提高一些朱古力條的價格。"},{"en":"To hike the prices of something means to raise prices sharply.","zh":"To hike the prices of something 指大幅提高價格。"},{"en":"A landlord may hike the price of rent after demand for flats increases.","zh":"當租盤需求增加，業主可能大幅提高租金。"},{"en":"If companies hike prices too much, customers may buy less or switch brands.","zh":"如果公司加價太多，顧客可能少買或轉品牌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sudden or noticeable price increase.","zh":"這個片語描述突然或明顯的加價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"chocolate bars","meaning":"朱古力條","examples":[{"en":"Some manufacturers raised the prices of their chocolate bars.","zh":"一些生產商提高了朱古力條的價格。"},{"en":"Chocolate bars are solid rectangular pieces of chocolate sold as snacks.","zh":"Chocolate bars 是作為零食出售的長方形固體朱古力。"},{"en":"Students may buy chocolate bars from a vending machine after school.","zh":"學生放學後可能從自動售賣機買朱古力條。"},{"en":"If cocoa becomes expensive, chocolate bars may cost more or become smaller.","zh":"如果可可變貴，朱古力條可能加價或變小。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a common packaged chocolate snack.","zh":"這個片語指常見的包裝朱古力零食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"speculators","meaning":"投機者","examples":[{"en":"Speculators have been blamed for pushing cocoa prices higher.","zh":"投機者被指責推高可可價格。"},{"en":"Speculators are investors who buy and sell assets hoping to profit from price changes.","zh":"Speculators 是希望從價格變動中獲利而買賣資產的投資者。"},{"en":"Speculators may buy property not to live in it, but to sell it later at a higher price.","zh":"投機者可能買樓不是為了居住，而是日後以更高價出售。"},{"en":"If speculators rush into a market, prices can rise faster than supply and demand alone would suggest.","zh":"如果投機者湧入市場，價格升幅可能比單靠供求所解釋的更快。"},{"en":"This word often suggests risky investment for profit.","zh":"這個詞常暗示為賺錢而作出的風險投資。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be fingered for","meaning":"被指責為","examples":[{"en":"Speculators have been fingered for pushing the price of cocoa higher.","zh":"投機者被指責為推高可可價格的原因。"},{"en":"To be fingered for something means to be identified or blamed as responsible for it.","zh":"To be fingered for something 指被指出或被責怪要為某事負責。"},{"en":"A student may be fingered for starting a rumour if classmates saw them sending the first message.","zh":"如果同學看到某學生傳出第一條訊息，他可能被指責為散播謠言的人。"},{"en":"If speculators are fingered for a price rise, people believe they helped cause it.","zh":"如果投機者被指為加價原因，人們相信他們助長了加價。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often suggests blame.","zh":"這個片語較非正式，常帶有責怪意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"push the price higher","meaning":"推高價格","examples":[{"en":"Speculators helped push the price of cocoa higher.","zh":"投機者幫助推高可可價格。"},{"en":"To push the price higher means to make a product or asset more expensive.","zh":"To push the price higher 指令產品或資產變得更昂貴。"},{"en":"A shortage of taxis can push the price of rides higher during heavy rain.","zh":"大雨期間的士短缺可以推高車費。"},{"en":"If many buyers compete for limited goods, their demand can push the price higher.","zh":"如果許多買家爭奪有限商品，他們的需求可以推高價格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes upward price pressure.","zh":"這個片語描述價格上升壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"chocolate aficionados","meaning":"朱古力愛好者","examples":[{"en":"British chocolate aficionados must share some of the blame.","zh":"英國朱古力愛好者必須分擔部分責任。"},{"en":"Chocolate aficionados are people who know, love, and care deeply about chocolate.","zh":"Chocolate aficionados 是了解、喜愛並非常重視朱古力的人。"},{"en":"A chocolate aficionado may compare cocoa origin, texture, bitterness, and aroma.","zh":"朱古力愛好者可能比較可可來源、口感、苦味和香氣。"},{"en":"If aficionados demand better chocolate, shops may stock more premium varieties.","zh":"如果愛好者要求更好的朱古力，商店可能入貨更多高級款式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious fans, not casual buyers.","zh":"這個片語描述認真的愛好者，而不是普通買家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"share some of the blame","meaning":"分擔部分責任","examples":[{"en":"Consumers must share some of the blame for rising cocoa prices.","zh":"消費者必須為可可價格上升分擔部分責任。"},{"en":"To share some of the blame means to be partly responsible for a problem.","zh":"To share some of the blame 指對某問題負有部分責任。"},{"en":"If a class is noisy, both students and weak classroom rules may share some of the blame.","zh":"如果課室嘈吵，學生和薄弱課堂規則可能都要分擔部分責任。"},{"en":"When demand rises because of consumer choices, consumers may share some responsibility for higher prices.","zh":"當價格因消費者選擇令需求上升而提高，消費者可能要負部分責任。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean full blame, but partial responsibility.","zh":"這個片語不是指全責，而是指部分責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the run on the bean","meaning":"對可可豆的搶購","examples":[{"en":"British demand helped create the run on the bean.","zh":"英國需求幫助造成對可可豆的搶購。"},{"en":"The run on the bean means a rush to buy cacao beans because buyers fear shortage or rising prices.","zh":"The run on the bean 指因買家害怕短缺或加價而急於購買可可豆。"},{"en":"A rumour of rice shortage can create a run on rice in supermarkets.","zh":"米短缺的傳聞可以造成超級市場中的搶米潮。"},{"en":"If everyone tries to buy beans at once, prices can rise even faster.","zh":"如果所有人同時嘗試買豆，價格可以升得更快。"},{"en":"This phrase uses “bean” to refer specifically to cacao beans.","zh":"這個片語用 “bean” 特別指可可豆。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"soaring demand for","meaning":"對……急升的需求","examples":[{"en":"Soaring demand for dark chocolate has raised cocoa prices.","zh":"對黑朱古力急升的需求推高了可可價格。"},{"en":"Soaring demand for something means demand is rising very quickly.","zh":"Soaring demand for something 指對某物的需求快速上升。"},{"en":"Soaring demand for online lessons may encourage more teachers to teach on video platforms.","zh":"對網上課堂急升的需求，可能鼓勵更多老師在影片平台教學。"},{"en":"If demand soars while supply stays limited, prices often increase.","zh":"如果需求急升而供應有限，價格通常會上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rapid growth in people wanting to buy something.","zh":"這個片語描述人們想購買某物的需求快速增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"put a rocket under","meaning":"令……急速上升","examples":[{"en":"Soaring demand has put a rocket under the global price of cacao beans.","zh":"急升的需求令可可豆全球價格急速上升。"},{"en":"To put a rocket under something means to make it rise or move very quickly.","zh":"To put a rocket under something 指令某事物快速上升或移動。"},{"en":"A popular celebrity review can put a rocket under sales of a small café’s dessert.","zh":"受歡迎名人的評論可以令小咖啡店甜品銷量急速上升。"},{"en":"If investors rush into a market, they can put a rocket under prices.","zh":"如果投資者湧入市場，他們可以令價格急速上升。"},{"en":"This informal phrase describes sudden acceleration or sharp increase.","zh":"這個非正式片語描述突然加速或大幅上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"global price","meaning":"全球價格","examples":[{"en":"The global price of cacao beans has increased sharply.","zh":"可可豆全球價格已大幅上升。"},{"en":"The global price is the price of a product across international markets.","zh":"Global price 是產品在國際市場上的價格。"},{"en":"The global price of oil can affect bus fares, airline tickets, and delivery costs.","zh":"石油全球價格可以影響巴士車費、機票和送貨成本。"},{"en":"If global prices rise, local shops may eventually charge customers more.","zh":"如果全球價格上升，本地商店最終可能向顧客收取更高價格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes worldwide pricing, not only one shop’s price.","zh":"這個片語描述全球定價，而不只是某間店的價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"compound the impact of","meaning":"加劇……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Demand has compounded the impact of drought in West Africa.","zh":"需求加劇了西非乾旱的影響。"},{"en":"To compound the impact of something means to make an existing problem worse.","zh":"To compound the impact of something 指令已有問題變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can compound the impact of exam stress on students.","zh":"睡眠不足可以加劇考試壓力對學生的影響。"},{"en":"If demand rises during a drought, the pressure on supply becomes even stronger.","zh":"如果乾旱期間需求上升，供應壓力會變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one problem making another problem more serious.","zh":"這個片語描述一個問題令另一問題更嚴重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"severe drought","meaning":"嚴重乾旱","examples":[{"en":"A severe drought in West Africa has reduced cocoa supply.","zh":"西非嚴重乾旱減少了可可供應。"},{"en":"A severe drought is a long and serious period with too little rain.","zh":"Severe drought 是長時間而嚴重缺雨的時期。"},{"en":"A severe drought can dry rivers, damage crops, and force farmers to use stored water.","zh":"嚴重乾旱可以令河流乾涸、破壞農作物，並迫使農民使用儲水。"},{"en":"If cacao trees receive too little rain, cocoa harvests may fall.","zh":"如果可可樹得到太少雨水，可可收成可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extreme dry weather with damaging effects.","zh":"這個片語描述帶有破壞性影響的極端乾燥天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"West Africa","meaning":"西非","examples":[{"en":"West Africa supplies much of the world’s cacao beans.","zh":"西非供應世界大量可可豆。"},{"en":"West Africa is the western region of the African continent, including several cacao-producing countries.","zh":"West Africa 是非洲大陸西部地區，包括幾個可可生產國。"},{"en":"A geography lesson may discuss West Africa when explaining global cocoa production.","zh":"地理課解釋全球可可生產時，可能討論西非。"},{"en":"If weather damages crops in West Africa, chocolate prices worldwide may be affected.","zh":"如果天氣破壞西非作物，全球朱古力價格可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase names an important region in the cocoa supply chain.","zh":"這個片語命名可可供應鏈中的重要地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be home to","meaning":"是……的所在地","examples":[{"en":"West Africa is home to much of the world’s supply of cacao beans.","zh":"西非是世界大量可可豆供應的所在地。"},{"en":"To be home to something means to contain it or be the place where it is found.","zh":"To be home to something 指包含某物或是某物所在的地方。"},{"en":"A library is home to thousands of books and quiet study spaces.","zh":"圖書館是數千本書和安靜自修空間的所在地。"},{"en":"If a region is home to a key crop, problems there can affect global supply.","zh":"如果某地區是關鍵作物的所在地，當地問題可以影響全球供應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where something exists or is concentrated.","zh":"這個片語描述某物存在或集中的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the world’s supply of","meaning":"世界……供應","examples":[{"en":"The region produces much of the world’s supply of cacao beans.","zh":"該地區生產世界可可豆供應中的大部分。"},{"en":"The world’s supply of something means the total amount available globally.","zh":"The world’s supply of something 指全球可用的總數量。"},{"en":"A poor harvest can reduce the world’s supply of wheat and raise food prices.","zh":"收成差可以減少世界小麥供應並推高食品價格。"},{"en":"If one region provides much of the world’s supply, the market depends heavily on that region.","zh":"如果一個地區提供世界供應的大部分，市場就高度依賴該地區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes global availability of a product.","zh":"這個片語描述產品的全球可用量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the rest of the food market","meaning":"其他食品市場","examples":[{"en":"Chocolate consumers are behaving as they do in the rest of the food market.","zh":"朱古力消費者的行為與他們在其他食品市場中的行為相似。"},{"en":"The rest of the food market means all the other parts of food buying and selling outside the product being discussed.","zh":"The rest of the food market 指所討論產品以外所有其他食品買賣範疇。"},{"en":"If organic fruit becomes popular, similar trends may appear in the rest of the food market.","zh":"如果有機水果變得流行，類似趨勢可能出現在其他食品市場。"},{"en":"When consumers seek quality in many foods, chocolate may follow the same pattern.","zh":"當消費者在許多食品中追求質素，朱古力可能跟隨同一模式。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one food category with wider food trends.","zh":"這個片語把某一食品類別與更廣泛食品趨勢作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"trade up","meaning":"轉買較高檔產品","examples":[{"en":"Consumers are trading up and buying better-quality chocolate.","zh":"消費者正在轉買較高檔產品，購買更高質素朱古力。"},{"en":"To trade up means to move from a cheaper or simpler product to a higher-quality one.","zh":"To trade up 指由較便宜或較簡單產品轉向較高質素產品。"},{"en":"A student may trade up from basic earphones to noise-cancelling headphones for online lessons.","zh":"學生可能由基本耳機轉買降噪耳機，以便上網課。"},{"en":"If customers trade up, shops may stock more premium goods.","zh":"如果顧客轉買較高檔產品，商店可能入貨更多高級商品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing a better and usually more expensive option.","zh":"這個片語描述選擇更好且通常更昂貴的選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be discerning about","meaning":"對……更有判斷力","examples":[{"en":"Consumers are being more discerning about what they buy.","zh":"消費者對自己購買的東西變得更有判斷力。"},{"en":"To be discerning about something means to judge it carefully and choose with good taste or understanding.","zh":"To be discerning about something 指仔細判斷並以品味或理解作選擇。"},{"en":"Parents may be discerning about the snacks they buy for young children.","zh":"家長可能對為幼兒購買的零食更有判斷力。"},{"en":"If shoppers become more discerning, low-quality products may sell less well.","zh":"如果購物者變得更有判斷力，低質產品可能賣得較差。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful and intelligent choice.","zh":"這個片語描述謹慎而聰明的選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"top supermarket chains","meaning":"主要連鎖超級市場","examples":[{"en":"Top supermarket chains have added premium dark chocolate varieties.","zh":"主要連鎖超級市場已加入高級黑朱古力款式。"},{"en":"Top supermarket chains are the major supermarket companies with many stores and strong market influence.","zh":"Top supermarket chains 是有許多分店並具強大市場影響力的主要超市公司。"},{"en":"Top supermarket chains can change consumer habits by promoting new products widely.","zh":"主要連鎖超級市場可以透過廣泛推廣新產品來改變消費習慣。"},{"en":"If top chains add premium chocolate, smaller shops may follow the trend.","zh":"如果主要連鎖店加入高級朱古力，小型商店可能跟隨趨勢。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to leading supermarket businesses.","zh":"這個片語指領先的超級市場企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"premium dark chocolate varieties","meaning":"高級黑朱古力款式","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets have added premium dark chocolate varieties to their ranges.","zh":"超級市場已在產品系列中加入高級黑朱古力款式。"},{"en":"Premium dark chocolate varieties are higher-quality types of dark chocolate, often with richer cocoa flavour.","zh":"Premium dark chocolate varieties 是較高質素的黑朱古力種類，通常可可味更濃。"},{"en":"A gift shop may sell premium dark chocolate varieties in small boxes for special occasions.","zh":"禮品店可能以小盒裝出售高級黑朱古力款式，用於特別場合。"},{"en":"If shoppers want stronger and more complex flavours, premium varieties may sell well.","zh":"如果購物者想要更濃和更複雜味道，高級款式可能賣得好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes high-end dark chocolate options.","zh":"這個片語描述高端黑朱古力選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"own-brand ranges","meaning":"自家品牌系列","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets have added dark chocolate to their own-brand ranges.","zh":"超級市場已把黑朱古力加入自家品牌系列。"},{"en":"Own-brand ranges are products sold under a shop’s own label rather than another company’s brand.","zh":"Own-brand ranges 是以商店自己品牌出售，而不是以其他公司品牌出售的產品。"},{"en":"A supermarket’s own-brand range may include bread, milk, biscuits, and cleaning products.","zh":"超級市場自家品牌系列可能包括麵包、牛奶、餅乾和清潔用品。"},{"en":"If a trend is strong, shops may create own-brand versions to capture demand.","zh":"如果某趨勢強勁，商店可能推出自家品牌版本來抓住需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes private-label product lines.","zh":"這個片語描述私人品牌產品線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in response to","meaning":"回應；因應","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets changed their products in response to rising demand.","zh":"超級市場因應需求上升而改變產品。"},{"en":"In response to something means as a reaction to it.","zh":"In response to something 指作為對某事的反應。"},{"en":"A school may open more revision classes in response to students’ exam worries.","zh":"學校可能因應學生的考試憂慮開設更多溫習班。"},{"en":"If customers ask for healthier snacks, shops may change stock in response to demand.","zh":"如果顧客要求更健康零食，商店可能因應需求改變存貨。"},{"en":"This phrase links an action to the reason behind it.","zh":"這個片語把行動與背後原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"this phenomenon","meaning":"這種現象","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets have responded to this phenomenon by expanding dark chocolate ranges.","zh":"超級市場透過擴大黑朱古力系列來回應這種現象。"},{"en":"This phenomenon means this noticeable trend or event that people can observe.","zh":"This phenomenon 指人們可以觀察到的明顯趨勢或事件。"},{"en":"Teachers may notice a phenomenon where students write better after reading more examples.","zh":"老師可能注意到一種現象：學生閱讀更多例子後寫得更好。"},{"en":"If a phenomenon becomes common, businesses and researchers may pay attention to it.","zh":"如果某種現象變得普遍，企業和研究人員可能會關注它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a trend already mentioned.","zh":"這個片語回指前面已提及的趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"expand the number of","meaning":"增加……的數量","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets have expanded the number of dark chocolate lines they stock.","zh":"超級市場已增加入貨的黑朱古力產品線數量。"},{"en":"To expand the number of something means to increase how many there are.","zh":"To expand the number of something 指增加某事物的數量。"},{"en":"A school may expand the number of reading clubs if many students want to join.","zh":"如果許多學生想加入，學校可能增加閱讀會的數量。"},{"en":"If product choices increase, shoppers have more options and may buy more.","zh":"如果產品選擇增加，購物者有更多選項，可能買得更多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a range larger.","zh":"這個片語描述擴大某個系列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"dark chocolate lines","meaning":"黑朱古力產品線","examples":[{"en":"Many supermarkets stock more dark chocolate lines than before.","zh":"許多超級市場入貨的黑朱古力產品線比以前更多。"},{"en":"Dark chocolate lines are different products or varieties of dark chocolate sold by a shop.","zh":"Dark chocolate lines 是商店售賣的不同黑朱古力產品或款式。"},{"en":"A shop may offer dark chocolate lines with orange, sea salt, almonds, or high cocoa content.","zh":"商店可能提供橙味、海鹽、杏仁或高可可含量的黑朱古力產品線。"},{"en":"If more lines are stocked, customers can choose different flavours and prices.","zh":"如果入貨更多產品線，顧客可以選擇不同味道和價格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes product varieties within dark chocolate.","zh":"這個片語描述黑朱古力中的產品款式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"stock","meaning":"備有；入貨","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets now stock many kinds of dark chocolate.","zh":"超級市場現在備有許多種黑朱古力。"},{"en":"To stock something means to keep it available for sale in a shop.","zh":"To stock something 指商店備有某物以供出售。"},{"en":"A school tuck shop may stock sandwiches, fruit, and bottled water.","zh":"學校小食部可能備有三文治、水果和樽裝水。"},{"en":"If shops stock more dark chocolate, customers see it as a normal choice.","zh":"如果商店入貨更多黑朱古力，顧客會把它視為正常選擇。"},{"en":"This verb describes what a shop keeps on its shelves.","zh":"這個動詞描述商店貨架上備有甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"dwarfing their milk chocolate variants","meaning":"令牛奶朱古力款式相形見絀","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate lines are dwarfing milk chocolate variants in some shops.","zh":"在一些商店中，黑朱古力產品線令牛奶朱古力款式相形見絀。"},{"en":"To dwarf other variants means to make them look much smaller or less important by comparison.","zh":"To dwarf other variants 指相比之下令其他款式顯得小得多或不重要。"},{"en":"A large new mall can dwarf the small shops around it.","zh":"大型新商場可以令周邊小店相形見絀。"},{"en":"If dark chocolate ranges become much bigger, milk chocolate options may seem limited.","zh":"如果黑朱古力系列變得大得多，牛奶朱古力選項可能顯得有限。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one category becoming far larger than another.","zh":"這個片語描述一個類別變得遠大於另一類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in some cases","meaning":"在某些情況下","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate ranges are larger than milk chocolate ranges in some cases.","zh":"在某些情況下，黑朱古力系列比牛奶朱古力系列更大。"},{"en":"In some cases means in certain situations, but not all situations.","zh":"In some cases 指在某些情況中，但不是所有情況。"},{"en":"In some cases, students learn better from examples than from rules alone.","zh":"在某些情況下，學生從例子中學得比只看規則更好。"},{"en":"If a statement is true only in some cases, we should avoid overgeneralising it.","zh":"如果陳述只在某些情況下成立，我們應避免過度概括。"},{"en":"This phrase limits a claim to particular situations.","zh":"這個片語把說法限制於特定情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"it takes more beans to","meaning":"需要更多可可豆去","examples":[{"en":"It takes more beans to produce a bar of dark chocolate.","zh":"生產一條黑朱古力需要更多可可豆。"},{"en":"It takes more beans to do something means more beans are needed for that process.","zh":"It takes more beans to do something 指某過程需要更多豆。"},{"en":"It takes more flour to bake a large cake than to make small biscuits.","zh":"烤一個大蛋糕比做小餅乾需要更多麵粉。"},{"en":"If dark chocolate needs more cacao beans, rising dark chocolate demand can strain supply.","zh":"如果黑朱古力需要更多可可豆，黑朱古力需求上升會令供應受壓。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the material requirement of production.","zh":"這個片語解釋生產所需材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at the root of the problem","meaning":"是問題的根源","examples":[{"en":"The need for more cacao beans is at the root of the problem.","zh":"需要更多可可豆是問題的根源。"},{"en":"At the root of the problem means being the deepest or main cause of the problem.","zh":"At the root of the problem 指某事是問題最深層或主要原因。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep may be at the root of a student’s poor concentration.","zh":"睡眠不足可能是學生專注力差的根源。"},{"en":"If the root problem is supply, raising prices alone will not solve it.","zh":"如果根本問題是供應不足，單靠加價不能解決。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the underlying cause.","zh":"這個片語指出深層原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"for delivery in July","meaning":"於七月交付的","examples":[{"en":"The cost of cacao beans for delivery in July rose sharply.","zh":"於七月交付的可可豆成本大幅上升。"},{"en":"For delivery in July means the goods are to be supplied or received in July.","zh":"For delivery in July 指貨物將於七月供應或接收。"},{"en":"A shop may order school uniforms for delivery in July before the new term begins.","zh":"商店可能在新學期前訂購於七月交付的校服。"},{"en":"If future delivery prices rise, buyers expect higher costs ahead.","zh":"如果未來交付價格上升，買家預期前方成本更高。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in trading and supply contracts.","zh":"這個片語常用於交易和供應合約。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"London cocoa exchange","meaning":"倫敦可可交易所","examples":[{"en":"Cacao bean prices rose on the London cocoa exchange.","zh":"可可豆價格在倫敦可可交易所上升。"},{"en":"The London cocoa exchange is a market where cocoa-related contracts are traded in London.","zh":"London cocoa exchange 是倫敦交易可可相關合約的市場。"},{"en":"Traders may watch the London cocoa exchange to judge cocoa price trends.","zh":"交易員可能觀察倫敦可可交易所，以判斷可可價格趨勢。"},{"en":"If prices rise on an exchange, chocolate companies may worry about future costs.","zh":"如果交易所價格上升，朱古力公司可能擔心未來成本。"},{"en":"This phrase names a trading venue for cocoa.","zh":"這個片語命名可可交易場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"shoot to","meaning":"急升至","examples":[{"en":"The price shot to £1,028 a tonne.","zh":"價格急升至每噸1,028英鎊。"},{"en":"To shoot to a price means to rise very quickly to that level.","zh":"To shoot to a price 指快速升至某個水平。"},{"en":"After a sudden shortage, mask prices may shoot to several times their normal level.","zh":"突然短缺後，口罩價格可能急升至正常水平的幾倍。"},{"en":"If a commodity price shoots up, buyers may hurry to secure supplies.","zh":"如果商品價格急升，買家可能趕緊確保供應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rapid jump to a specific number.","zh":"這個片語描述快速跳升到某一數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a tonne","meaning":"一噸","examples":[{"en":"The price rose to £1,028 a tonne.","zh":"價格升至每噸1,028英鎊。"},{"en":"A tonne is a unit of weight equal to 1,000 kilograms.","zh":"A tonne 是等於1,000公斤的重量單位。"},{"en":"A truck may carry several tonnes of rice to a warehouse.","zh":"一輛貨車可能把數噸米運到倉庫。"},{"en":"If cocoa is priced per tonne, buyers are usually dealing in large quantities.","zh":"如果可可以每噸計價，買家通常是在處理大量貨物。"},{"en":"This word is used for measuring heavy goods.","zh":"這個詞用於量度重型貨物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"exceptionally heavy trading","meaning":"異常活躍的交易","examples":[{"en":"The price rose on exceptionally heavy trading.","zh":"價格在異常活躍的交易中上升。"},{"en":"Exceptionally heavy trading means an unusually large amount of buying and selling.","zh":"Exceptionally heavy trading 指異常大量的買賣活動。"},{"en":"A company’s shares may rise during exceptionally heavy trading after major news is announced.","zh":"重大消息公布後，某公司股票可能在異常活躍的交易中上升。"},{"en":"If trading is heavy, it shows many buyers and sellers are active at the same time.","zh":"如果交易活躍，表示許多買家和賣家同時行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unusually intense market activity.","zh":"這個片語描述異常激烈的市場活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"up on the day","meaning":"當日上升","examples":[{"en":"The price was up £22 on the day.","zh":"價格當日上升22英鎊。"},{"en":"Up on the day means higher by the end of that trading day.","zh":"Up on the day 指在該交易日結束時變得更高。"},{"en":"A company’s share price may be up on the day after strong sales results.","zh":"公司公布強勁銷售結果後，股價可能當日上升。"},{"en":"If cocoa is up on the day, traders may see short-term buying pressure.","zh":"如果可可價格當日上升，交易員可能看到短期買入壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase reports a same-day price increase.","zh":"這個片語報告同日價格上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the highest price","meaning":"最高價格","examples":[{"en":"The crop fetched its highest price since November 2004.","zh":"該作物賣得自2004年11月以來的最高價格。"},{"en":"The highest price is the greatest amount paid or recorded for something in a period.","zh":"Highest price 是某段期間內某物被支付或記錄的最高金額。"},{"en":"A rare textbook may reach its highest price just before public exams.","zh":"罕見教科書可能在公開試前達到最高價格。"},{"en":"If a crop reaches the highest price in years, buyers may worry about shortage.","zh":"如果作物達到多年來最高價格，買家可能擔心短缺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a peak price.","zh":"這個片語描述價格高峰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fetch a price","meaning":"賣得某個價格","examples":[{"en":"The crop fetched its highest price for several years.","zh":"該作物賣得多年來最高價格。"},{"en":"To fetch a price means to be sold for that amount of money.","zh":"To fetch a price 指以某個金額出售。"},{"en":"An old comic book may fetch a high price if collectors want it badly.","zh":"如果收藏家非常想要，舊漫畫書可能賣得高價。"},{"en":"If cacao beans fetch higher prices, farmers may earn more but manufacturers pay more.","zh":"如果可可豆賣得更高價格，農民可能賺更多，但生產商要付更多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the selling price achieved.","zh":"這個片語描述達成的售價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at any point since","meaning":"自……以來任何時候","examples":[{"en":"The price was the highest at any point since November 2004.","zh":"該價格是自2004年11月以來任何時候的最高水平。"},{"en":"At any point since means at any time after a particular date.","zh":"At any point since 指在某日期之後的任何時間。"},{"en":"School attendance is higher now than at any point since the new policy began.","zh":"學校出席率現在高於新政策開始以來任何時候。"},{"en":"If a price is higher than at any point since a past date, it has reached a long-term peak.","zh":"如果價格高於某日期以來任何時候，它就達到長期高峰。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the present with every moment after a starting date.","zh":"這個片語把現在與某起始日期後每個時刻比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"canny investors","meaning":"精明投資者","examples":[{"en":"Canny investors placed record bets on rising prices.","zh":"精明投資者對價格上升下了破紀錄賭注。"},{"en":"Canny investors are clever and careful investors who try to spot profitable opportunities.","zh":"Canny investors 是聰明而謹慎、嘗試找出獲利機會的投資者。"},{"en":"A canny investor may buy shares when a strong company is temporarily unpopular.","zh":"精明投資者可能在強勁公司暫時不受歡迎時買入其股票。"},{"en":"If canny investors expect prices to rise, they may act before ordinary buyers notice the trend.","zh":"如果精明投資者預期價格上升，他們可能在普通買家注意趨勢前行動。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests shrewd market judgment.","zh":"這個片語暗示敏銳的市場判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"place record bets","meaning":"下破紀錄的賭注","examples":[{"en":"Investors have placed record bets that cocoa prices will keep rising.","zh":"投資者下了破紀錄的賭注，押注可可價格會持續上升。"},{"en":"To place record bets means to make the largest or unusually large wagers or investments on an outcome.","zh":"To place record bets 指對某結果作出最大或異常大的押注或投資。"},{"en":"Investors may place big bets on electric cars if they expect the industry to grow.","zh":"如果投資者預期電動車行業會增長，他們可能下大注。"},{"en":"If record bets are placed, markets may become more volatile.","zh":"如果出現破紀錄押注，市場可能變得更波動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very large speculative positions.","zh":"這個片語描述非常大的投機倉位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"keep rising","meaning":"持續上升","examples":[{"en":"Investors expect cocoa prices to keep rising.","zh":"投資者預期可可價格會持續上升。"},{"en":"To keep rising means to continue going up.","zh":"To keep rising 指繼續上升。"},{"en":"If school fees keep rising, more families may apply for financial help.","zh":"如果學費持續上升，更多家庭可能申請經濟援助。"},{"en":"When prices keep rising, buyers may purchase early to avoid higher costs later.","zh":"當價格持續上升，買家可能提早購買以避免之後成本更高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a continuing upward trend.","zh":"這個片語描述持續向上的趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hedge funds","meaning":"對沖基金","examples":[{"en":"Hedge funds have bought a large share of cocoa contracts.","zh":"對沖基金已買入大部分可可合約。"},{"en":"Hedge funds are investment funds that use complex strategies to try to make high returns.","zh":"Hedge funds 是使用複雜策略嘗試取得高回報的投資基金。"},{"en":"Hedge funds may buy or sell commodities, currencies, shares, or contracts.","zh":"對沖基金可能買賣商品、貨幣、股票或合約。"},{"en":"If hedge funds enter a small market heavily, prices may move quickly.","zh":"如果對沖基金大量進入小型市場，價格可能快速變動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to professional investment funds, not ordinary personal savings accounts.","zh":"這個片語指專業投資基金，而不是普通個人儲蓄戶口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make money by","meaning":"透過……賺錢","examples":[{"en":"Hedge funds make money by predicting price movements.","zh":"對沖基金透過預測價格變動賺錢。"},{"en":"To make money by doing something means to earn profit through that action.","zh":"To make money by doing something 指透過某行動賺取利潤。"},{"en":"A tutor may make money by teaching students online after work.","zh":"補習老師可能下班後透過網上教學生賺錢。"},{"en":"If investors correctly predict prices, they can make money by buying low and selling high.","zh":"如果投資者正確預測價格，他們可以透過低買高賣賺錢。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how profit is earned.","zh":"這個片語解釋利潤如何賺取。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"punt on whether","meaning":"押注……是否","examples":[{"en":"Hedge funds punt on whether commodity prices will rise or fall.","zh":"對沖基金押注商品價格會否上升或下跌。"},{"en":"To punt on whether something will happen means to make a risky bet on the outcome.","zh":"To punt on whether something will happen 指對某結果作風險押注。"},{"en":"A student should not punt on whether a topic will appear in the exam and ignore everything else.","zh":"學生不應押注某題目是否出現在考試中，然後忽略其他內容。"},{"en":"If investors punt on prices, they may gain a lot or lose a lot.","zh":"如果投資者押注價格，他們可能大賺，也可能大蝕。"},{"en":"This informal phrase describes speculative betting.","zh":"這個非正式片語描述投機押注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"commodity prices","meaning":"商品價格","examples":[{"en":"Hedge funds speculate on commodity prices.","zh":"對沖基金投機商品價格。"},{"en":"Commodity prices are the prices of raw materials such as cocoa, oil, wheat, and metals.","zh":"Commodity prices 是可可、石油、小麥和金屬等原材料的價格。"},{"en":"Rising commodity prices can make food, transport, and construction more expensive.","zh":"商品價格上升可以令食品、交通和建築更昂貴。"},{"en":"If commodity prices move sharply, businesses may struggle to plan costs.","zh":"如果商品價格大幅波動，企業可能難以規劃成本。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the market prices of basic goods.","zh":"這個片語指基本商品的市場價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"share prices","meaning":"股價","examples":[{"en":"Some investors bet on whether share prices will rise or fall.","zh":"有些投資者押注股價會上升還是下跌。"},{"en":"Share prices are the market prices of company shares.","zh":"Share prices 是公司股票的市場價格。"},{"en":"A company’s share price may rise after it reports strong profits.","zh":"公司公布強勁盈利後，股價可能上升。"},{"en":"If share prices fall sharply, investors may lose money quickly.","zh":"如果股價大幅下跌，投資者可能很快虧損。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the value of shares traded in financial markets.","zh":"這個片語指金融市場中交易股票的價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"swallow up","meaning":"大量買入；吞下","examples":[{"en":"Hedge funds have swallowed up a third of the cocoa contracts.","zh":"對沖基金已大量買入三分之一可可合約。"},{"en":"To swallow up something means to take in, buy, or use a very large amount of it.","zh":"To swallow up something 指吸收、買入或使用大量某物。"},{"en":"Rent can swallow up most of a student’s part-time income.","zh":"租金可以吞下學生兼職收入的大部分。"},{"en":"If investors swallow up available contracts, fewer may be left for other buyers.","zh":"如果投資者大量買入可用合約，留給其他買家的可能更少。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests one group taking a large share.","zh":"這個片語暗示某一群體取得很大份額。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cocoa contracts","meaning":"可可合約","examples":[{"en":"Cocoa contracts are traded in New York and London.","zh":"可可合約在紐約和倫敦交易。"},{"en":"Cocoa contracts are agreements to buy or sell cocoa under specified conditions.","zh":"Cocoa contracts 是按指定條件買入或賣出可可的協議。"},{"en":"A chocolate company may use cocoa contracts to lock in future supply.","zh":"朱古力公司可能使用可可合約鎖定未來供應。"},{"en":"If cocoa contracts become expensive, manufacturers may worry about production costs.","zh":"如果可可合約變貴，生產商可能擔心生產成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes financial or trade agreements involving cocoa.","zh":"這個片語描述涉及可可的金融或貿易協議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"main cocoa trading centre","meaning":"主要可可交易中心","examples":[{"en":"New York is another main cocoa trading centre.","zh":"紐約是另一個主要可可交易中心。"},{"en":"A main cocoa trading centre is an important place where cocoa contracts or products are bought and sold.","zh":"Main cocoa trading centre 是買賣可可合約或產品的重要地方。"},{"en":"A city can become a trading centre if many buyers, sellers, and financial firms gather there.","zh":"如果許多買家、賣家和金融公司聚集，一個城市可以成為交易中心。"},{"en":"If prices move in a main trading centre, global markets may notice quickly.","zh":"如果主要交易中心價格變動，全球市場可能很快注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major hub for cocoa trade.","zh":"這個片語描述可可貿易的主要樞紐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"industry buyers","meaning":"業內買家","examples":[{"en":"Industry buyers have not yet joined the buying frenzy.","zh":"業內買家尚未加入購買狂熱。"},{"en":"Industry buyers are companies or professionals who buy materials for use in their own industry.","zh":"Industry buyers 是為自己行業用途購買材料的公司或專業買家。"},{"en":"A bakery’s industry buyers may purchase flour, sugar, and packaging in large amounts.","zh":"麵包店的業內買家可能大量購買麵粉、糖和包裝材料。"},{"en":"If industry buyers start building stocks, demand in the market may rise further.","zh":"如果業內買家開始增加存貨，市場需求可能進一步上升。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to real business users, not casual consumers.","zh":"這個片語指真正的商業用戶，而不是普通消費者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"refrain from","meaning":"避免；克制不去","examples":[{"en":"Industry buyers have refrained from joining the frenzy.","zh":"業內買家一直避免加入狂熱行列。"},{"en":"To refrain from doing something means to deliberately avoid doing it.","zh":"To refrain from doing something 指有意識地避免做某事。"},{"en":"Students should refrain from checking their phones during a mock exam.","zh":"學生應避免在模擬考試期間查看手機。"},{"en":"If buyers refrain from panic buying, prices may stay calmer.","zh":"如果買家克制不恐慌購買，價格可能較平穩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled avoidance.","zh":"這個片語描述有控制地避免。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"join the frenzy","meaning":"加入狂熱行列","examples":[{"en":"Chocolate companies have not yet joined the frenzy.","zh":"朱古力公司尚未加入狂熱行列。"},{"en":"To join the frenzy means to take part in a period of excited, rushed, or uncontrolled activity.","zh":"To join the frenzy 指參與一段興奮、急促或失控的活動。"},{"en":"Shoppers may join the frenzy when a shop announces a huge one-day sale.","zh":"商店宣布大型一日促銷時，購物者可能加入狂熱搶購。"},{"en":"If companies join a buying frenzy, prices can rise even faster.","zh":"如果公司加入購買狂熱，價格可以升得更快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming part of a rush or craze.","zh":"這個片語描述成為搶購或熱潮的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"traders believe that","meaning":"交易員相信","examples":[{"en":"Traders believe that higher prices will make companies build up stocks.","zh":"交易員相信較高價格會令公司增加存貨。"},{"en":"Traders believe that means people who buy and sell in markets think something is likely.","zh":"Traders believe that 指市場買賣人士認為某事很可能發生。"},{"en":"Traders believe that bad weather will push vegetable prices higher next month.","zh":"交易員相信惡劣天氣會在下月推高蔬菜價格。"},{"en":"If traders believe prices will rise, they may buy early.","zh":"如果交易員相信價格會上升，他們可能提早買入。"},{"en":"This phrase reports market expectations.","zh":"這個片語報告市場預期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"prompt someone to","meaning":"促使某人去","examples":[{"en":"A jump in prices may prompt companies to build up their stocks.","zh":"價格急升可能促使公司增加存貨。"},{"en":"To prompt someone to do something means to cause or encourage them to act.","zh":"To prompt someone to do something 指造成或鼓勵某人採取行動。"},{"en":"A teacher’s feedback may prompt a student to rewrite an essay.","zh":"老師的回饋可能促使學生重寫作文。"},{"en":"If prices rise suddenly, companies may be prompted to secure supplies early.","zh":"如果價格突然上升，公司可能被促使提早確保供應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a trigger that leads to action.","zh":"這個片語描述引發行動的觸發因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"build up stocks","meaning":"增加存貨","examples":[{"en":"Chocolate companies may build up their stocks of cacao beans.","zh":"朱古力公司可能增加可可豆存貨。"},{"en":"To build up stocks means to increase stored supplies for future use.","zh":"To build up stocks 指增加儲存供應以便日後使用。"},{"en":"A family may build up stocks of rice and water before a typhoon.","zh":"家庭可能在颱風前增加米和水的存貨。"},{"en":"If companies build up stocks early, they can protect themselves from later shortages.","zh":"如果公司提早增加存貨，它們可以保護自己免受之後短缺影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing reserves.","zh":"這個片語描述增加儲備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rise nearly thirty per cent","meaning":"上升近三成","examples":[{"en":"Cocoa prices have risen nearly thirty per cent since December.","zh":"自十二月以來，可可價格已上升近三成。"},{"en":"To rise nearly thirty per cent means to increase by almost three tenths of the original amount.","zh":"To rise nearly thirty per cent 指增加接近原本數量的十分之三。"},{"en":"If school lunch prices rise nearly thirty per cent, many families will notice the change.","zh":"如果學校午餐價格上升近三成，許多家庭會注意到變化。"},{"en":"A rise of nearly thirty per cent can strongly affect budgets and buying decisions.","zh":"近三成升幅可以強烈影響預算和購買決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large percentage increase.","zh":"這個片語描述大幅百分比增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"since the beginning of","meaning":"自……開始以來","examples":[{"en":"Prices have risen sharply since the beginning of December.","zh":"自十二月開始以來，價格已大幅上升。"},{"en":"Since the beginning of a period means from the start of that time until now or another reference point.","zh":"Since the beginning of a period 指從某段時間開始至現在或另一參照點。"},{"en":"Since the beginning of term, the class has completed three writing tasks.","zh":"自學期開始以來，這班已完成三項寫作任務。"},{"en":"If prices rise from the beginning of a month, the trend may be tracked over time.","zh":"如果價格自月初開始上升，趨勢可以隨時間追蹤。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the starting point of a change.","zh":"這個片語標示變化的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"largely on","meaning":"主要由於","examples":[{"en":"Prices have risen largely on concern about drought.","zh":"價格上升主要由於對乾旱的憂慮。"},{"en":"Largely on means mainly because of or mainly based on something.","zh":"Largely on 指主要因為某事或主要建基於某事。"},{"en":"A shop’s success may depend largely on location and customer service.","zh":"商店成功可能主要取決於地點和顧客服務。"},{"en":"If a price rise is largely on fear, the market may react before real shortages appear.","zh":"如果價格上升主要由於恐懼，市場可能在真正短缺出現前已反應。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main reason behind a result.","zh":"這個片語指出結果背後的主要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"growing concern about","meaning":"對……日益增加的憂慮","examples":[{"en":"Growing concern about drought has pushed prices higher.","zh":"對乾旱日益增加的憂慮推高了價格。"},{"en":"Growing concern about something means increasing worry about it.","zh":"Growing concern about something 指對某事的擔憂越來越大。"},{"en":"Growing concern about student stress may lead schools to add counselling services.","zh":"對學生壓力日益增加的憂慮，可能令學校增加輔導服務。"},{"en":"If concern grows in a market, buyers may act before the problem is confirmed.","zh":"如果市場憂慮增加，買家可能在問題確認前行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes worry becoming stronger over time.","zh":"這個片語描述憂慮隨時間變強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Ivory Coast","meaning":"科特迪瓦","examples":[{"en":"Ivory Coast is the biggest cacao bean producer in West Africa.","zh":"科特迪瓦是西非最大的可可豆生產國。"},{"en":"Ivory Coast is a West African country strongly associated with cacao production.","zh":"Ivory Coast 是西非一個與可可生產密切相關的國家。"},{"en":"A geography lesson on chocolate supply may include Ivory Coast as a key producer.","zh":"關於朱古力供應的地理課可能把科特迪瓦列為重要生產國。"},{"en":"If weather harms cacao farms in Ivory Coast, cocoa prices may rise worldwide.","zh":"如果天氣損害科特迪瓦的可可農場，全球可可價格可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase names an important cocoa-producing country.","zh":"這個片語命名一個重要可可生產國。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the biggest producer","meaning":"最大生產國；最大生產者","examples":[{"en":"Ivory Coast is the biggest cacao bean producer in West Africa.","zh":"科特迪瓦是西非最大的可可豆生產國。"},{"en":"The biggest producer is the country, company, or region that makes the largest amount of a product.","zh":"Biggest producer 是生產某產品數量最多的國家、公司或地區。"},{"en":"A factory town may be the biggest producer of furniture in its region.","zh":"一個工業小鎮可能是其地區最大的家具生產者。"},{"en":"If the biggest producer has a bad harvest, the whole market may be affected.","zh":"如果最大生產者收成差，整個市場可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the largest source of production.","zh":"這個片語指出最大生產來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"dub something","meaning":"稱……為","examples":[{"en":"Farmers have dubbed it the worst drought in living memory.","zh":"農民稱它為仍在世的人記憶中最嚴重的乾旱。"},{"en":"To dub something a name means to give it that name or label.","zh":"To dub something a name 指給某事某個名稱或標籤。"},{"en":"Students may dub a difficult classroom “the ice room” if the air-conditioning is too cold.","zh":"如果課室冷氣太凍，學生可能稱那間困難課室為「冰房」。"},{"en":"If people dub an event “the worst” of its kind, they are stressing its severity.","zh":"如果人們稱某事件為同類中最嚴重，他們是在強調其嚴重性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes naming something in a memorable way.","zh":"這個片語描述以令人印象深刻方式命名某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in living memory","meaning":"在仍在世的人記憶中","examples":[{"en":"Farmers describe the drought as the worst in living memory.","zh":"農民把這次乾旱形容為仍在世的人記憶中最嚴重的一次。"},{"en":"In living memory means within the time that people still alive can remember.","zh":"In living memory 指仍然在世的人能記得的時間範圍內。"},{"en":"The flood was the worst in living memory for many villagers.","zh":"對許多村民來說，這次洪水是在仍在世的人記憶中最嚴重的一次。"},{"en":"If an event is the worst in living memory, it feels historically serious to the community.","zh":"如果某事件是在活人記憶中最嚴重的，社區會覺得它具有歷史嚴重性。"},{"en":"This phrase measures time by human memory, not exact dates.","zh":"這個片語用人的記憶而非精確日期來量度時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"to make matters worse","meaning":"更糟的是","examples":[{"en":"To make matters worse, demand is outstripping supply.","zh":"更糟的是，需求正在超過供應。"},{"en":"To make matters worse introduces an additional problem that makes a bad situation more serious.","zh":"To make matters worse 用來引出令壞情況更嚴重的額外問題。"},{"en":"The bus was late; to make matters worse, it started raining heavily.","zh":"巴士遲到；更糟的是，開始下大雨。"},{"en":"If supply is already damaged and demand also rises, matters become worse.","zh":"如果供應已受損而需求也上升，情況就更糟。"},{"en":"This phrase adds a further negative factor.","zh":"這個片語加入進一步負面因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"outstrip supply","meaning":"超過供應","examples":[{"en":"Demand is outstripping supply in the cocoa market.","zh":"可可市場中需求正在超過供應。"},{"en":"To outstrip supply means demand becomes greater than the amount available.","zh":"To outstrip supply 指需求超過可供應的數量。"},{"en":"If demand for school places outstrips supply, some children may not get their first choice.","zh":"如果對學位的需求超過供應，有些孩子可能不能入讀首選學校。"},{"en":"When demand outstrips supply, prices often rise.","zh":"當需求超過供應，價格通常會上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shortage caused by demand being too strong.","zh":"這個片語描述由需求過強造成的短缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"developing markets","meaning":"發展中市場","examples":[{"en":"Demand is rising as consumers in developing markets eat more chocolate.","zh":"隨着發展中市場的消費者吃更多朱古力，需求正在上升。"},{"en":"Developing markets are economies where incomes, industries, and consumer spending are still growing.","zh":"Developing markets 是收入、產業和消費開支仍在增長的經濟體。"},{"en":"Companies often enter developing markets when they see more young consumers with money to spend.","zh":"當公司看到更多年輕消費者有錢消費時，常進入發展中市場。"},{"en":"If developing markets buy more chocolate, global cocoa demand may increase.","zh":"如果發展中市場購買更多朱古力，全球可可需求可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to growing economies, not fully mature markets.","zh":"這個片語指成長中的經濟體，而不是完全成熟市場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"begin to sweeten","meaning":"開始嗜甜","examples":[{"en":"The teeth of consumers in developing markets are beginning to sweeten.","zh":"發展中市場消費者的口味開始嗜甜。"},{"en":"To begin to sweeten here means people are starting to enjoy sweet foods more.","zh":"To begin to sweeten 在此指人們開始更喜歡甜食。"},{"en":"Children may begin to sweeten after trying cakes and sweets at birthday parties.","zh":"孩子在生日會嘗過蛋糕和糖果後，可能開始嗜甜。"},{"en":"If consumers start liking sweeter snacks, chocolate demand may grow.","zh":"如果消費者開始喜歡較甜零食，朱古力需求可能增長。"},{"en":"This phrase is playful and connects taste with consumer behaviour.","zh":"這個片語帶玩味，把味覺與消費行為連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"predict a shortfall","meaning":"預測短缺","examples":[{"en":"The International Cocoa Organisation predicts a global cocoa shortfall.","zh":"國際可可組織預測全球可可短缺。"},{"en":"To predict a shortfall means to forecast that supply will be less than demand.","zh":"To predict a shortfall 指預測供應會少於需求。"},{"en":"A school may predict a shortfall in teachers if many retire in the same year.","zh":"如果許多老師同年退休，學校可能預測教師短缺。"},{"en":"If analysts predict a shortfall, buyers may try to secure supplies early.","zh":"如果分析師預測短缺，買家可能嘗試提早確保供應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes forecasting a shortage.","zh":"這個片語描述對短缺的預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"global cocoa shortfall","meaning":"全球可可短缺","examples":[{"en":"A global cocoa shortfall is expected this year.","zh":"今年預計會出現全球可可短缺。"},{"en":"A global cocoa shortfall means worldwide cocoa supply is expected to be lower than demand.","zh":"Global cocoa shortfall 指全球可可供應預計低於需求。"},{"en":"A global shortfall in rice would affect prices in many countries.","zh":"全球大米短缺會影響許多國家的價格。"},{"en":"If a global cocoa shortfall occurs, chocolate makers may compete for limited beans.","zh":"如果出現全球可可短缺，朱古力生產商可能爭奪有限可可豆。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an international cocoa shortage.","zh":"這個片語描述國際可可短缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"this year alone","meaning":"單是今年","examples":[{"en":"The shortfall may reach 100,000 tonnes this year alone.","zh":"單是今年，短缺量可能達到100,000噸。"},{"en":"This year alone means only within this single year, without counting other years.","zh":"This year alone 指只在這一年內，不計其他年份。"},{"en":"A school may receive hundreds of new applications this year alone.","zh":"學校單是今年可能收到數百份新申請。"},{"en":"If a shortage is large in one year alone, the market may feel pressure quickly.","zh":"如果短缺單在一年內已很大，市場可能很快感到壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the scale within one year.","zh":"這個片語強調一年內的規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"private forecasts","meaning":"私營機構預測","examples":[{"en":"Private forecasts warn that the deficit may be much larger.","zh":"私營機構預測警告短缺量可能大得多。"},{"en":"Private forecasts are predictions made by private companies, analysts, or organisations rather than public authorities.","zh":"Private forecasts 是由私人公司、分析師或組織，而不是公共當局作出的預測。"},{"en":"Private forecasts may predict housing prices before official figures are released.","zh":"私營機構預測可能在官方數字公布前預測樓價。"},{"en":"If private forecasts are more pessimistic, businesses may prepare for worse conditions.","zh":"如果私營機構預測較悲觀，企業可能為更差情況作準備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes non-government predictions.","zh":"這個片語描述非政府預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"warn that","meaning":"警告說","examples":[{"en":"Private forecasts warn that the deficit could be as much as 250,000 tonnes.","zh":"私營機構預測警告說短缺量可能多達250,000噸。"},{"en":"To warn that something may happen means to tell people about a possible danger or problem.","zh":"To warn that something may happen 指告訴人們可能出現的危險或問題。"},{"en":"Doctors may warn that too little sleep can harm memory and mood.","zh":"醫生可能警告說睡眠太少會損害記憶和情緒。"},{"en":"If experts warn that supply may fall, companies may change their plans.","zh":"如果專家警告說供應可能下降，公司可能改變計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a caution about a possible future problem.","zh":"這個片語引出對未來可能問題的警告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the deficit","meaning":"赤字；短缺量","examples":[{"en":"The deficit could be as much as 250,000 tonnes.","zh":"短缺量可能多達250,000噸。"},{"en":"The deficit is the amount by which demand is greater than supply, or spending is greater than income.","zh":"Deficit 是需求超過供應的差額，或開支超過收入的差額。"},{"en":"A school budget deficit appears when expenses are higher than available funding.","zh":"當開支高於可用資金時，學校預算會出現赤字。"},{"en":"If the cocoa deficit grows, chocolate makers may struggle to buy enough beans.","zh":"如果可可短缺量增加，朱古力生產商可能難以買到足夠可可豆。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gap or shortage.","zh":"這個片語描述差額或短缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as much as","meaning":"多達","examples":[{"en":"The cocoa deficit could be as much as 250,000 tonnes.","zh":"可可短缺量可能多達250,000噸。"},{"en":"As much as means up to a large amount or maximum possible amount.","zh":"As much as 指高達一個很大數量或最高可能數量。"},{"en":"A family may spend as much as HKD 1,000 a month on transport.","zh":"一個家庭每月交通費可能多達1,000港元。"},{"en":"If a deficit reaches as much as 250,000 tonnes, the shortage is very serious.","zh":"如果短缺量多達250,000噸，短缺就非常嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a high amount.","zh":"這個片語強調高數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"getting the right beans","meaning":"取得合適的可可豆","examples":[{"en":"Getting the right beans is becoming crucial in the chocolate market.","zh":"在朱古力市場中，取得合適的可可豆正變得至關重要。"},{"en":"Getting the right beans means obtaining cacao beans with the desired quality, flavour, and origin.","zh":"Getting the right beans 指取得具有理想質素、味道和來源的可可豆。"},{"en":"A coffee shop also needs the right beans if it wants a consistent flavour.","zh":"咖啡店如果想保持穩定味道，也需要合適的咖啡豆。"},{"en":"If chocolate makers cannot get the right beans, premium products may lose their special taste.","zh":"如果朱古力生產商無法取得合適可可豆，高級產品可能失去特殊味道。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the importance of choosing suitable raw ingredients.","zh":"這個片語描述選擇合適原材料的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"become crucial","meaning":"變得至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Bean quality has become crucial in premium chocolate.","zh":"可可豆質素在高級朱古力中已變得至關重要。"},{"en":"To become crucial means to become extremely important.","zh":"To become crucial 指變得極其重要。"},{"en":"Good internet access became crucial for students during online lessons.","zh":"網課期間，良好網絡連接對學生變得至關重要。"},{"en":"If flavour becomes crucial, companies must pay closer attention to ingredients.","zh":"如果味道變得至關重要，公司就必須更重視原料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something becoming essential to success.","zh":"這個片語描述某事對成功變得不可或缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fast following in the footsteps of","meaning":"快速步……後塵","examples":[{"en":"Chocolate is fast following in the footsteps of wine and coffee.","zh":"朱古力正快速步紅酒和咖啡的後塵。"},{"en":"To follow in the footsteps of something means to develop in a similar way to it.","zh":"To follow in the footsteps of something 指以相似方式發展。"},{"en":"Bubble tea may follow in the footsteps of coffee by becoming more specialised and premium.","zh":"珍珠奶茶可能步咖啡後塵，變得更專門和高級。"},{"en":"If chocolate follows wine and coffee, consumers may start caring about origin and flavour notes.","zh":"如果朱古力跟隨紅酒和咖啡，消費者可能開始關注產地和味道層次。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a newer trend with an earlier one.","zh":"這個片語把較新的趨勢與較早趨勢作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in terms of","meaning":"在……方面","examples":[{"en":"Chocolate is becoming like wine and coffee in terms of taste appreciation.","zh":"在味覺欣賞方面，朱古力正變得像紅酒和咖啡。"},{"en":"In terms of means when considering a particular aspect or area.","zh":"In terms of 指從某個特定方面或範疇來看。"},{"en":"In terms of price, public transport is often cheaper than owning a car.","zh":"在價格方面，公共交通通常比擁有汽車便宜。"},{"en":"If two products are similar in terms of quality, shoppers may compare brand and price.","zh":"如果兩種產品在質素方面相似，購物者可能比較品牌和價格。"},{"en":"This phrase limits the comparison to one aspect.","zh":"這個片語把比較限制在某一方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"appreciate its effect on the palate","meaning":"欣賞其對味覺的影響","examples":[{"en":"Consumers are learning to appreciate chocolate’s effect on the palate.","zh":"消費者正在學習欣賞朱古力對味覺的影響。"},{"en":"To appreciate its effect on the palate means to notice and enjoy how something tastes and feels in the mouth.","zh":"To appreciate its effect on the palate 指注意並享受某物在口中的味道和感覺。"},{"en":"Tea drinkers may learn to appreciate how different leaves affect the palate.","zh":"飲茶者可能學會欣賞不同茶葉如何影響味覺。"},{"en":"If consumers notice complex flavours, they may pay more for premium products.","zh":"如果消費者注意到複雜味道，他們可能願意為高級產品付更多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful enjoyment of taste.","zh":"這個片語描述對味道的細緻欣賞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the palate","meaning":"味覺；味蕾","examples":[{"en":"Premium chocolate appeals to the palate in complex ways.","zh":"高級朱古力以複雜方式吸引味覺。"},{"en":"The palate refers to a person’s sense of taste and the mouth’s experience of flavour.","zh":"Palate 指一個人的味覺，以及口腔對味道的體驗。"},{"en":"A spicy soup may be exciting to the palate but too strong for beginners.","zh":"辣湯對味覺可能很刺激，但對初學者太強烈。"},{"en":"If food affects the palate pleasantly, people may want to taste it again.","zh":"如果食物令人味覺愉悅，人們可能想再品嚐。"},{"en":"This word is often used when discussing refined taste.","zh":"這個詞常用於討論精緻味道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"experiment more with","meaning":"更願意嘗試","examples":[{"en":"People are willing to experiment more with food and drink.","zh":"人們更願意嘗試飲食。"},{"en":"To experiment more with something means to try new forms, flavours, or methods of it.","zh":"To experiment more with something 指嘗試某事物的新形式、味道或方法。"},{"en":"A family may experiment more with vegetarian meals after trying a good meat-free dish.","zh":"家庭嘗過一道好吃的無肉菜後，可能更願意嘗試素食餐。"},{"en":"If consumers experiment more, unusual products can become popular.","zh":"如果消費者更願意嘗試，不尋常產品可以變得流行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming more open to trying new options.","zh":"這個片語描述對新選項變得更開放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"food and drink","meaning":"飲食","examples":[{"en":"Consumers are experimenting more with food and drink.","zh":"消費者正更願意嘗試飲食。"},{"en":"Food and drink means the things people eat and drink.","zh":"Food and drink 指人們吃和喝的東西。"},{"en":"A school fair may sell food and drink to raise money for charity.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能售賣飲食，為慈善籌款。"},{"en":"If people become adventurous with food and drink, shops may offer more unusual flavours.","zh":"如果人們在飲食上變得更敢嘗試，商店可能提供更多不尋常味道。"},{"en":"This phrase refers broadly to eating and drinking products.","zh":"這個片語泛指吃喝產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rather like","meaning":"很像；有點像","examples":[{"en":"Chocolate is becoming rather like wine and coffee.","zh":"朱古力正變得很像紅酒和咖啡。"},{"en":"Rather like means quite similar to, though not exactly the same as.","zh":"Rather like 指相當相似，但不完全相同。"},{"en":"Learning pronunciation is rather like learning music because rhythm and sound matter.","zh":"學習發音有點像學音樂，因為節奏和聲音很重要。"},{"en":"If chocolate becomes rather like wine, people may discuss origin, flavour, and quality more seriously.","zh":"如果朱古力變得有點像紅酒，人們可能更認真討論產地、味道和質素。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a soft comparison.","zh":"這個片語作出溫和比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"varieties of chocolate","meaning":"朱古力種類","examples":[{"en":"Consumers are realising that there are many varieties of chocolate.","zh":"消費者正意識到朱古力有許多種類。"},{"en":"Varieties of chocolate are different types of chocolate with different flavours, ingredients, or cocoa levels.","zh":"Varieties of chocolate 是有不同味道、成分或可可含量的不同朱古力類型。"},{"en":"A shop may sell varieties of chocolate with nuts, fruit, chilli, or sea salt.","zh":"商店可能售賣加入果仁、水果、辣椒或海鹽的朱古力種類。"},{"en":"If consumers notice more varieties, they may become more selective.","zh":"如果消費者注意到更多種類，他們可能變得更挑剔。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the range of chocolate types available.","zh":"這個片語描述可供選擇的朱古力類型範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a niche","meaning":"小眾市場","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate used to be a niche product.","zh":"黑朱古力過去曾是小眾產品。"},{"en":"A niche is a small specialised market or interest area.","zh":"Niche 是小型而專門的市場或興趣範疇。"},{"en":"Handmade notebooks may be a niche product bought by people who love stationery.","zh":"手工筆記簿可能是文具愛好者購買的小眾產品。"},{"en":"If a niche product becomes mainstream, supply and marketing may expand quickly.","zh":"如果小眾產品變成主流，供應和市場推廣可能迅速擴大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something aimed at a limited group.","zh":"這個片語描述針對有限群體的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"not any longer","meaning":"不再是這樣","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate used to be a niche, but not any longer.","zh":"黑朱古力過去曾是小眾產品，但現在不再是這樣。"},{"en":"Not any longer means something was true before but is no longer true now.","zh":"Not any longer 指某事以前是真的，但現在不再是。"},{"en":"This shop used to close on Sundays, but not any longer.","zh":"這間店過去星期日關門，但現在不再是這樣。"},{"en":"If dark chocolate is no longer niche, supermarkets will treat it as a normal product.","zh":"如果黑朱古力不再是小眾，超級市場會把它視為普通產品。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a change from past to present.","zh":"這個片語強調從過去到現在的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"taste the cocoa","meaning":"品嚐可可本身","examples":[{"en":"With dark chocolate, consumers are tasting the cocoa itself.","zh":"吃黑朱古力時，消費者是在品嚐可可本身。"},{"en":"To taste the cocoa means to notice the natural flavour of cocoa rather than mainly sugar or milk.","zh":"To taste the cocoa 指注意可可的天然味道，而不是主要品嚐糖或牛奶。"},{"en":"Coffee lovers taste the beans when they drink coffee without too much milk or syrup.","zh":"咖啡愛好者在飲用沒有太多奶或糖漿的咖啡時，就是品嚐咖啡豆本身。"},{"en":"If people can taste the cocoa clearly, bean quality becomes more important.","zh":"如果人們能清楚品嚐可可本身，可可豆質素就變得更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes experiencing the core ingredient’s flavour.","zh":"這個片語描述體驗核心成分的味道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"taste the recipe","meaning":"品嚐配方味道","examples":[{"en":"With milk chocolate, consumers are often tasting the recipe.","zh":"吃牛奶朱古力時，消費者通常是在品嚐配方味道。"},{"en":"To taste the recipe means to taste the added ingredients and formula more than the main raw ingredient itself.","zh":"To taste the recipe 指品嚐添加成分和配方，多於品嚐主要原材料本身。"},{"en":"In a sweet drink, people may taste the recipe more than the tea leaves.","zh":"在甜飲中，人們可能品嚐配方味道多於茶葉本身。"},{"en":"If sugar, milk, and oil dominate, the original cocoa flavour may be hidden.","zh":"如果糖、奶和油佔主導，原本可可味可能被掩蓋。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts tasting a formula with tasting the raw ingredient.","zh":"這個片語把品嚐配方與品嚐原材料作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"flavour elements","meaning":"味道元素","examples":[{"en":"There are 450 different flavour elements in a single cacao bean.","zh":"一粒可可豆中有450種不同味道元素。"},{"en":"Flavour elements are individual taste or aroma components that together create a food’s overall flavour.","zh":"Flavour elements 是共同組成食物整體味道的個別味覺或香氣成分。"},{"en":"A bowl of soup may have flavour elements from salt, herbs, meat, and vegetables.","zh":"一碗湯可能有來自鹽、香草、肉和蔬菜的味道元素。"},{"en":"If a food has many flavour elements, people may describe it as complex.","zh":"如果食物有許多味道元素，人們可能形容它味道複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the small parts that build taste.","zh":"這個片語描述構成味道的小部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"vary in taste","meaning":"味道有所不同","examples":[{"en":"A cacao bean varies in taste depending on where it is grown.","zh":"可可豆的味道視乎種植地點而有所不同。"},{"en":"To vary in taste means to have different flavours in different cases.","zh":"To vary in taste 指在不同情況中有不同味道。"},{"en":"Apples vary in taste; some are sweet, while others are sharp and sour.","zh":"蘋果味道有所不同；有些很甜，有些酸味強烈。"},{"en":"If beans vary in taste by location, origin becomes important in premium chocolate.","zh":"如果可可豆味道因地點而不同，產地在高級朱古力中就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes flavour differences.","zh":"這個片語描述味道差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"depending on","meaning":"視乎","examples":[{"en":"The taste depends on where the cacao bean is grown.","zh":"味道視乎可可豆在哪裡種植。"},{"en":"Depending on something means being affected or decided by it.","zh":"Depending on something 指受某事影響或由某事決定。"},{"en":"A student may walk or take the bus depending on the weather.","zh":"學生可能視乎天氣選擇步行或乘巴士。"},{"en":"If taste depends on growing location, two beans can produce different chocolate flavours.","zh":"如果味道視乎種植地點，兩種可可豆可以產生不同朱古力味道。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor changes the result.","zh":"這個片語顯示某因素會改變結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"where it is grown","meaning":"它的種植地點","examples":[{"en":"The bean’s flavour changes according to where it is grown.","zh":"可可豆的味道會根據它的種植地點而改變。"},{"en":"Where it is grown means the place or region in which the crop is cultivated.","zh":"Where it is grown 指作物被種植的地方或地區。"},{"en":"Tea can taste different depending on where it is grown.","zh":"茶葉可以因種植地點不同而味道不同。"},{"en":"If soil, rain, and climate differ, where a crop is grown can shape its flavour.","zh":"如果土壤、雨量和氣候不同，作物的種植地點可以塑造其味道。"},{"en":"This phrase links agricultural location with product quality.","zh":"這個片語把農業地點與產品質素連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"seem peppery","meaning":"帶胡椒味","examples":[{"en":"Chocolate from Colombia might seem peppery.","zh":"來自哥倫比亞的朱古力可能帶胡椒味。"},{"en":"To seem peppery means to have a flavour or sensation that reminds people of pepper.","zh":"To seem peppery 指有令人想起胡椒的味道或感覺。"},{"en":"A soup may seem peppery if it leaves a warm spicy feeling on the tongue.","zh":"如果湯在舌頭上留下暖辣感，它可能帶胡椒味。"},{"en":"If chocolate seems peppery, consumers may describe its flavour as complex and unusual.","zh":"如果朱古力帶胡椒味，消費者可能形容其味道複雜而不尋常。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a taste impression, not necessarily actual pepper.","zh":"這個片語描述味覺印象，不一定真的有胡椒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"smell like vanilla","meaning":"聞起來像雲呢拿","examples":[{"en":"Chocolate from Venezuela might smell like vanilla.","zh":"來自委內瑞拉的朱古力可能聞起來像雲呢拿。"},{"en":"To smell like vanilla means to have an aroma similar to vanilla.","zh":"To smell like vanilla 指有類似雲呢拿的香氣。"},{"en":"A bakery may smell like vanilla when cakes are being baked.","zh":"蛋糕正在烘焙時，麵包店可能聞起來像雲呢拿。"},{"en":"If chocolate smells like vanilla, it may feel sweeter even before tasting.","zh":"如果朱古力聞起來像雲呢拿，即使未入口也可能感覺較甜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes aroma rather than actual ingredients.","zh":"這個片語描述香氣，而不一定指真正成分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"drive demand for","meaning":"推動對……的需求","examples":[{"en":"Complex flavours are driving demand for premium chocolate.","zh":"複雜味道正在推動對高級朱古力的需求。"},{"en":"To drive demand for something means to be a major reason why more people want it.","zh":"To drive demand for something 指成為更多人想要某物的主要原因。"},{"en":"Good reviews can drive demand for a new restaurant.","zh":"好評可以推動對新餐廳的需求。"},{"en":"If consumers love complex flavours, demand for premium chocolate may increase.","zh":"如果消費者喜愛複雜味道，對高級朱古力的需求可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what pushes more people to buy something.","zh":"這個片語描述推動更多人購買某物的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"uber-premium version","meaning":"超高端版本","examples":[{"en":"Single-estate chocolate is an uber-premium version of dark chocolate.","zh":"單一莊園朱古力是黑朱古力的超高端版本。"},{"en":"An uber-premium version is an extremely high-end and usually expensive form of a product.","zh":"Uber-premium version 是產品極高端且通常昂貴的形式。"},{"en":"A handmade leather bag may be an uber-premium version of an everyday school bag.","zh":"手工皮袋可能是日常書包的超高端版本。"},{"en":"If consumers want rare quality, brands may create uber-premium products.","zh":"如果消費者想要罕有質素，品牌可能創造超高端產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a product positioned above ordinary premium goods.","zh":"這個片語描述定位高於普通高級商品的產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"so-called","meaning":"所謂的","examples":[{"en":"The so-called single-estate chocolate bar uses beans from one location.","zh":"所謂的單一莊園朱古力條使用來自一個地點的可可豆。"},{"en":"So-called means known by that name, sometimes with a slightly questioning or explanatory tone.","zh":"So-called 指以該名稱為人所知，有時帶少許質疑或解釋語氣。"},{"en":"The so-called smart classroom still needs good teaching to be useful.","zh":"所謂的智能課室仍需要良好教學才有用。"},{"en":"If a product is so-called premium, consumers may check whether it truly deserves the label.","zh":"如果產品被稱為所謂高級，消費者可能檢查它是否真的配得上標籤。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a name or label.","zh":"這個片語引出名稱或標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"single-estate chocolate bar","meaning":"單一莊園朱古力條","examples":[{"en":"A single-estate chocolate bar sources beans from a single location.","zh":"單一莊園朱古力條從單一地點採購可可豆。"},{"en":"A single-estate chocolate bar is made from cacao beans grown on one estate or farm area.","zh":"Single-estate chocolate bar 是用同一莊園或農場地區種植的可可豆製成的朱古力條。"},{"en":"A chocolate lover may buy a single-estate bar to taste the flavour of one specific place.","zh":"朱古力愛好者可能購買單一莊園朱古力條，以品嚐某特定地方的味道。"},{"en":"If beans come from one estate, the chocolate’s flavour may be more distinctive.","zh":"如果可可豆來自同一莊園，朱古力味道可能更鮮明。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a high-end chocolate product linked to one origin.","zh":"這個片語描述與單一產地相關的高端朱古力產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"source beans from","meaning":"從……採購可可豆","examples":[{"en":"Single-estate chocolate sources its beans from a single location.","zh":"單一莊園朱古力從單一地點採購可可豆。"},{"en":"To source beans from a place means to obtain or buy beans from that place.","zh":"To source beans from a place 指從某地取得或購買豆。"},{"en":"A café may source coffee beans from a farm known for strong aroma.","zh":"咖啡店可能從以香氣濃郁聞名的農場採購咖啡豆。"},{"en":"If a company sources beans carefully, it can control flavour and quality better.","zh":"如果公司仔細採購可可豆，它可以更好控制味道和質素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where ingredients are obtained.","zh":"這個片語描述成分從哪裡取得。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a single location","meaning":"單一地點","examples":[{"en":"The beans are sourced from a single location.","zh":"這些可可豆從單一地點採購。"},{"en":"A single location means one specific place, not several different places.","zh":"Single location 指一個特定地方，而不是幾個不同地方。"},{"en":"A school trip may meet at a single location so no one gets lost.","zh":"學校旅行可能在單一地點集合，以免有人迷路。"},{"en":"If cacao beans come from a single location, their flavour may be more consistent.","zh":"如果可可豆來自單一地點，其味道可能更一致。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses one clear origin.","zh":"這個片語強調一個清楚來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"fall over themselves to","meaning":"爭先恐後地去","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are falling over themselves to complete studies on chocolate.","zh":"科學家正爭先恐後地完成關於朱古力的研究。"},{"en":"To fall over themselves to do something means to be extremely eager and compete to do it quickly.","zh":"To fall over themselves to do something 指非常急切並競相快速做某事。"},{"en":"Students may fall over themselves to join a popular teacher’s extra class.","zh":"學生可能爭先恐後地加入受歡迎老師的額外課堂。"},{"en":"If a topic becomes fashionable, researchers may rush to study it.","zh":"如果某題目變得流行，研究人員可能急着研究它。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests eagerness that is almost competitive.","zh":"這個片語暗示幾乎帶競爭性的急切。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete studies","meaning":"完成研究","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are trying to complete studies on chocolate’s health effects.","zh":"科學家正嘗試完成關於朱古力健康影響的研究。"},{"en":"To complete studies means to finish research projects or investigations.","zh":"To complete studies 指完成研究項目或調查。"},{"en":"University students must complete studies before submitting their final reports.","zh":"大學生必須完成研究後才提交最終報告。"},{"en":"If scientists complete studies, they can publish clearer evidence.","zh":"如果科學家完成研究，他們就能發表更清楚證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finishing research work.","zh":"這個片語描述完成研究工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"moderate consumption of","meaning":"適量食用……","examples":[{"en":"Moderate consumption of high-quality chocolate may be good for health.","zh":"適量食用高質素朱古力可能對健康有益。"},{"en":"Moderate consumption of something means eating or using a reasonable, not excessive, amount.","zh":"Moderate consumption of something 指食用或使用合理而不過量的份量。"},{"en":"Moderate consumption of coffee may be fine for many adults, but too much can affect sleep.","zh":"對許多成年人來說，適量飲用咖啡可能沒有問題，但太多會影響睡眠。"},{"en":"If people hear about health benefits, they still need to avoid overconsumption.","zh":"如果人們聽到健康益處，他們仍需要避免過量食用。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses balance rather than unlimited use.","zh":"這個片語強調平衡，而不是無限制使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"high-quality chocolate","meaning":"高質素朱古力","examples":[{"en":"Some studies suggest that high-quality chocolate can be good for you.","zh":"有些研究顯示高質素朱古力可能對你有益。"},{"en":"High-quality chocolate is chocolate made with better ingredients, richer cocoa, and careful production.","zh":"High-quality chocolate 是用較好原料、較濃可可和細心製作而成的朱古力。"},{"en":"A gift shop may sell high-quality chocolate in small handmade boxes.","zh":"禮品店可能以小型手工盒出售高質素朱古力。"},{"en":"If chocolate is high-quality, customers may accept a higher price.","zh":"如果朱古力質素高，顧客可能接受較高價格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes chocolate judged by ingredient and production standards.","zh":"這個片語描述以原料和製作標準評價的朱古力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be good for you","meaning":"對身體有益","examples":[{"en":"Moderate consumption of dark chocolate may be good for you.","zh":"適量食用黑朱古力可能對身體有益。"},{"en":"To be good for you means to benefit your health, body, or well-being.","zh":"To be good for you 指對健康、身體或身心狀態有好處。"},{"en":"Regular sleep is good for you because it supports mood and memory.","zh":"規律睡眠對身體有益，因為它支持情緒和記憶。"},{"en":"If a food is good for you only in small amounts, eating too much can still be harmful.","zh":"如果某食物只在少量時對身體有益，吃太多仍可能有害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes health benefit in everyday language.","zh":"這個片語以日常語言描述健康益處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"unveil research","meaning":"公布研究","examples":[{"en":"A Harvard professor unveiled research on cocoa nutrients.","zh":"一名哈佛教授公布了關於可可營養素的研究。"},{"en":"To unveil research means to publicly present or reveal new study findings.","zh":"To unveil research 指公開展示或揭示新的研究結果。"},{"en":"A university may unveil research on student sleep during a public lecture.","zh":"大學可能在公開講座中公布關於學生睡眠的研究。"},{"en":"If researchers unveil surprising results, media attention may increase.","zh":"如果研究人員公布令人驚訝的結果，傳媒關注可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making research known to the public.","zh":"這個片語描述把研究公開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"suggest that","meaning":"顯示；指出","examples":[{"en":"The research suggests that epicatechin could lower disease risks.","zh":"研究顯示表兒茶素可能降低疾病風險。"},{"en":"Suggest that means to indicate or point to a possible conclusion.","zh":"Suggest that 指顯示或指向一個可能結論。"},{"en":"A student’s repeated mistakes may suggest that they do not understand the grammar rule.","zh":"學生反覆犯錯可能顯示他不理解文法規則。"},{"en":"If research suggests a benefit, further studies may still be needed to confirm it.","zh":"如果研究顯示有好處，仍可能需要進一步研究確認。"},{"en":"This phrase presents evidence cautiously.","zh":"這個片語以謹慎方式呈現證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a nutrient in cocoa","meaning":"可可中的一種營養素","examples":[{"en":"Epicatechin is a nutrient in cocoa.","zh":"表兒茶素是可可中的一種營養素。"},{"en":"A nutrient in cocoa is a substance found in cocoa that may support body functions.","zh":"Nutrient in cocoa 是存在於可可中、可能支持身體功能的物質。"},{"en":"Vitamins and minerals are nutrients that people get from food.","zh":"維他命和礦物質是人們從食物中取得的營養素。"},{"en":"If a nutrient has health effects, scientists may study how much people need.","zh":"如果某營養素有健康影響，科學家可能研究人們需要多少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a health-related substance inside cocoa.","zh":"這個片語描述可可中與健康有關的物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"epicatechin","meaning":"表兒茶素","examples":[{"en":"Epicatechin may lower the risks of several diseases.","zh":"表兒茶素可能降低幾種疾病的風險。"},{"en":"Epicatechin is a plant compound found in cocoa and some other foods.","zh":"Epicatechin 是存在於可可和一些其他食物中的植物化合物。"},{"en":"Scientists may study epicatechin to understand why cocoa could have health effects.","zh":"科學家可能研究表兒茶素，以了解為何可可可能有健康影響。"},{"en":"If epicatechin affects blood vessels or cells, it may help explain some health claims about cocoa.","zh":"如果表兒茶素影響血管或細胞，它可能幫助解釋一些關於可可的健康主張。"},{"en":"This word names a specific nutrient discussed in chocolate research.","zh":"這個詞命名朱古力研究中討論的特定營養素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lower the risks of","meaning":"降低……的風險","examples":[{"en":"Epicatechin could lower the risks of cancer and heart disease.","zh":"表兒茶素可能降低癌症和心臟病風險。"},{"en":"To lower the risks of something means to reduce the chance that it will happen.","zh":"To lower the risks of something 指減少某事發生的機會。"},{"en":"Regular exercise can lower the risk of some health problems.","zh":"定期運動可以降低某些健康問題的風險。"},{"en":"If a food lowers disease risk, people may see it as healthier.","zh":"如果一種食物降低疾病風險，人們可能視它為較健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing probability, not removing danger completely.","zh":"這個片語描述降低可能性，而不是完全消除危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"cancer","meaning":"癌症","examples":[{"en":"Some research links cocoa nutrients with lower cancer risk.","zh":"一些研究把可可營養素與較低癌症風險聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Cancer is a serious disease in which abnormal cells grow uncontrollably.","zh":"Cancer 是異常細胞失控生長的嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"Doctors encourage screening because some cancers are easier to treat when found early.","zh":"醫生鼓勵篩查，因為有些癌症在早期發現時較容易治療。"},{"en":"If research mentions cancer risk, the claim should be treated carefully and scientifically.","zh":"如果研究提及癌症風險，該主張應以謹慎和科學方式處理。"},{"en":"This word names a major group of serious diseases.","zh":"這個詞命名一大類嚴重疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"strokes","meaning":"中風","examples":[{"en":"Epicatechin may help reduce the risk of strokes.","zh":"表兒茶素可能有助降低中風風險。"},{"en":"Strokes are serious medical events where blood flow to part of the brain is blocked or reduced.","zh":"Strokes 是流向大腦某部分的血液被阻塞或減少的嚴重醫療事件。"},{"en":"A person having a stroke may suddenly have trouble speaking or moving one side of the body.","zh":"中風的人可能突然說話困難或身體一邊難以活動。"},{"en":"If a nutrient reduces stroke risk, researchers will want clear medical evidence.","zh":"如果某營養素降低中風風險，研究人員會需要清楚醫學證據。"},{"en":"This word refers to dangerous brain-related health events.","zh":"這個詞指與大腦有關的危險健康事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"heart disease","meaning":"心臟病","examples":[{"en":"Cocoa nutrients may reduce the risk of heart disease.","zh":"可可營養素可能降低心臟病風險。"},{"en":"Heart disease refers to medical conditions that affect the heart and blood vessels.","zh":"Heart disease 指影響心臟和血管的醫療狀況。"},{"en":"Doctors often advise exercise, sleep, and balanced eating to reduce heart disease risk.","zh":"醫生常建議運動、睡眠和平衡飲食，以降低心臟病風險。"},{"en":"If food choices affect heart disease, diet becomes part of long-term health planning.","zh":"如果食物選擇影響心臟病，飲食就成為長期健康規劃的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major category of health problems.","zh":"這個片語命名一大類健康問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"diabetes","meaning":"糖尿病","examples":[{"en":"Some research suggests cocoa may lower the risk of diabetes.","zh":"一些研究顯示可可可能降低糖尿病風險。"},{"en":"Diabetes is a condition in which the body has problems controlling blood sugar.","zh":"Diabetes 是身體控制血糖出現問題的狀況。"},{"en":"A doctor may advise a patient with diabetes to monitor diet, exercise, and medication carefully.","zh":"醫生可能建議糖尿病患者仔細管理飲食、運動和藥物。"},{"en":"If a food is high in sugar, people worried about diabetes should be cautious.","zh":"如果食物糖分高，擔心糖尿病的人應謹慎。"},{"en":"This word names a common long-term health condition.","zh":"這個詞命名一種常見長期健康狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"base findings on","meaning":"將研究結果建基於","examples":[{"en":"Dr Hollenberg based his findings on a study of the Kuna people.","zh":"Hollenberg 博士將研究結果建基於對庫納人的研究。"},{"en":"To base findings on something means to use it as the evidence or foundation for conclusions.","zh":"To base findings on something 指以某事作為結論的證據或基礎。"},{"en":"A teacher may base findings about student progress on tests, homework, and class observations.","zh":"老師可能把關於學生進步的發現建基於測驗、功課和課堂觀察。"},{"en":"If findings are based on limited evidence, researchers should avoid overclaiming.","zh":"如果研究結果建基於有限證據，研究人員應避免過度聲稱。"},{"en":"This phrase explains where conclusions come from.","zh":"這個片語解釋結論來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"findings","meaning":"研究結果","examples":[{"en":"The professor’s findings were based on a study of the Kuna people.","zh":"該教授的研究結果建基於一項對庫納人的研究。"},{"en":"Findings are results or conclusions reached after research or investigation.","zh":"Findings 是研究或調查後得出的結果或結論。"},{"en":"A school survey’s findings may show that students want more quiet study space.","zh":"學校調查的結果可能顯示學生想要更多安靜自修空間。"},{"en":"If findings are reliable, they can guide decisions or further research.","zh":"如果研究結果可靠，它們可以指導決策或進一步研究。"},{"en":"This word describes what a study discovers.","zh":"這個詞描述研究發現了甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the Kuna people","meaning":"庫納人","examples":[{"en":"The Kuna people of Panama consume large amounts of cocoa.","zh":"巴拿馬的庫納人食用大量可可。"},{"en":"The Kuna people are an Indigenous people associated here with high cocoa consumption.","zh":"Kuna people 是一個原住民族群，在此與大量攝取可可有關。"},{"en":"Researchers may study the Kuna people to explore links between diet and health.","zh":"研究人員可能研究庫納人，以探索飲食與健康之間的關係。"},{"en":"If one community consumes much more cocoa than others, scientists may compare health patterns.","zh":"如果一個社群攝取可可遠多於其他群體，科學家可能比較健康模式。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific people discussed in the research.","zh":"這個片語命名研究中討論的特定族群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be weaned on","meaning":"自幼以……餵養","examples":[{"en":"The Kuna people are weaned on cocoa.","zh":"庫納人自幼以可可餵養。"},{"en":"To be weaned on something means to grow up consuming it from a very young age.","zh":"To be weaned on something 指從很小年紀開始食用某物長大。"},{"en":"A child may be weaned on rice soup if it is a common family food.","zh":"如果米粥是常見家庭食物，孩子可能自幼以米粥餵養。"},{"en":"If people are weaned on a food, it may become a normal part of daily life.","zh":"如果人們自幼接觸某食物，它可能成為日常生活的正常部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes early and regular exposure to food or drink.","zh":"這個片語描述對食物或飲品的早期和定期接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the stuff","meaning":"這東西；該飲品","examples":[{"en":"The Kuna people can drink up to 40 cups of the stuff a week.","zh":"庫納人每星期可以飲用多達40杯這東西。"},{"en":"The stuff is an informal way to refer to the substance already being discussed.","zh":"The stuff 是非正式地指前文正在討論的物質。"},{"en":"A tired student may say, “I need more of the stuff,” when pointing to coffee.","zh":"疲倦學生指着咖啡時可能說：「我需要更多這東西。」"},{"en":"If a writer uses “the stuff,” the tone becomes casual and conversational.","zh":"如果作者使用 “the stuff”，語氣會變得隨意和口語化。"},{"en":"This phrase depends on context to show what substance is meant.","zh":"這個片語依靠語境顯示所指物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"separate research","meaning":"另一項研究","examples":[{"en":"Separate research found another possible health benefit of dark chocolate.","zh":"另一項研究發現黑朱古力另一個可能健康益處。"},{"en":"Separate research means a different study or investigation from the one already mentioned.","zh":"Separate research 指不同於前文所提研究的另一項研究或調查。"},{"en":"Separate research may confirm a teacher’s observation that sleep affects test performance.","zh":"另一項研究可能確認老師的觀察，即睡眠影響測驗表現。"},{"en":"If separate research reaches a similar conclusion, the claim becomes stronger.","zh":"如果另一項研究得出相似結論，主張就變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces evidence from another study.","zh":"這個片語引出來自另一研究的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"snack on","meaning":"吃……作小食","examples":[{"en":"Snacking on dark chocolate may affect blood clot development.","zh":"吃黑朱古力作小食可能影響血栓形成。"},{"en":"To snack on something means to eat a small amount of it between meals.","zh":"To snack on something 指在正餐之間吃少量某物。"},{"en":"A student may snack on fruit while revising after school.","zh":"學生放學後溫習時，可能吃水果作小食。"},{"en":"If people snack on dark chocolate instead of very sugary sweets, their sugar intake may change.","zh":"如果人們吃黑朱古力作小食而不是很甜的糖果，糖分攝取可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes casual small eating, not a full meal.","zh":"這個片語描述隨意少量進食，而不是正餐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"decrease the development of","meaning":"減少……的形成","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate decreased the development of blood clots.","zh":"黑朱古力減少了血栓的形成。"},{"en":"To decrease the development of something means to reduce how much it forms or grows.","zh":"To decrease the development of something 指減少某物形成或增長的程度。"},{"en":"Better handwashing can decrease the development of illness in a classroom.","zh":"更好洗手習慣可以減少課室中疾病的形成和傳播。"},{"en":"If a food decreases clot development, scientists may study its effect on blood health.","zh":"如果某食物減少血栓形成，科學家可能研究它對血液健康的影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slowing or reducing formation.","zh":"這個片語描述減慢或減少形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"potentially fatal","meaning":"可能致命的","examples":[{"en":"The blood clots could be potentially fatal.","zh":"這些血栓可能是致命的。"},{"en":"Potentially fatal means able to cause death, even if it does not always do so.","zh":"Potentially fatal 指可能造成死亡，即使不一定每次如此。"},{"en":"A severe allergic reaction can be potentially fatal without quick treatment.","zh":"嚴重過敏反應如果沒有迅速治療，可能致命。"},{"en":"If a condition is potentially fatal, people should take it seriously.","zh":"如果某狀況可能致命，人們應認真看待。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious risk to life.","zh":"這個片語描述對生命的嚴重風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"blood clots","meaning":"血栓","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate may reduce the development of blood clots.","zh":"黑朱古力可能減少血栓形成。"},{"en":"Blood clots are thickened masses of blood that can block blood flow.","zh":"Blood clots 是變稠凝結的血塊，可能阻塞血流。"},{"en":"Doctors worry about blood clots because they can travel to the heart, lungs, or brain.","zh":"醫生擔心血栓，因為它們可以移動到心臟、肺部或大腦。"},{"en":"If blood clots block important vessels, they can cause serious illness.","zh":"如果血栓阻塞重要血管，它們可以造成嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"This phrase names a dangerous blood-related condition.","zh":"這個片語命名與血液有關的危險狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"proportionately more","meaning":"按比例更多","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate has proportionately more antioxidants than some other foods.","zh":"黑朱古力按比例比一些其他食物含有更多抗氧化物。"},{"en":"Proportionately more means more when compared according to size, amount, or share.","zh":"Proportionately more 指按大小、數量或份額比較時更多。"},{"en":"A small class may receive proportionately more teacher attention than a large class.","zh":"小班按比例可能比大班得到更多教師關注。"},{"en":"If dark chocolate has proportionately more antioxidants, a small amount may contain a notable share.","zh":"如果黑朱古力按比例有更多抗氧化物，少量也可能含有明顯份額。"},{"en":"This phrase compares relative amounts, not total volume only.","zh":"這個片語比較相對數量，而不只是總量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"antioxidants","meaning":"抗氧化物","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate contains many antioxidants.","zh":"黑朱古力含有許多抗氧化物。"},{"en":"Antioxidants are substances that help protect cells from certain kinds of damage.","zh":"Antioxidants 是有助保護細胞免受某些損害的物質。"},{"en":"Fruits, vegetables, tea, and cocoa may contain antioxidants.","zh":"水果、蔬菜、茶和可可可能含有抗氧化物。"},{"en":"If a food contains antioxidants, people may associate it with possible health benefits.","zh":"如果食物含有抗氧化物，人們可能把它與可能的健康益處聯繫起來。"},{"en":"This word names health-related compounds found in some foods.","zh":"這個詞命名一些食物中的健康相關化合物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"better known for","meaning":"以……更為人熟知","examples":[{"en":"Other foods are better known for their health-giving properties.","zh":"其他食物以其有益健康的特性更為人熟知。"},{"en":"Better known for something means more widely recognised because of that feature.","zh":"Better known for something 指因某特徵而更廣為人知。"},{"en":"Green tea is better known for health benefits than sugary soft drinks.","zh":"綠茶以健康益處比含糖汽水更為人熟知。"},{"en":"If a product is better known for one quality, consumers may overlook its other qualities.","zh":"如果產品以某一特質更為人熟知，消費者可能忽略它的其他特質。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what people commonly associate with something.","zh":"這個片語描述人們通常把某物與甚麼聯繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"health-giving properties","meaning":"有益健康的特性","examples":[{"en":"Red wine and green tea are known for their health-giving properties.","zh":"紅酒和綠茶以有益健康的特性聞名。"},{"en":"Health-giving properties are qualities that may support or improve health.","zh":"Health-giving properties 是可能支持或改善健康的特質。"},{"en":"Fresh fruit has health-giving properties because it contains vitamins and fibre.","zh":"新鮮水果有有益健康的特性，因為它含有維他命和纖維。"},{"en":"If a food is marketed for health-giving properties, people may buy it to feel better about their diet.","zh":"如果食物以有益健康的特性作市場推廣，人們可能為了對飲食感覺更好而購買。"},{"en":"This phrase describes possible health benefits of a food or drink.","zh":"這個片語描述食物或飲品的可能健康益處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"red wine","meaning":"紅酒","examples":[{"en":"Red wine is often associated with health-giving properties.","zh":"紅酒常與有益健康的特性聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Red wine is an alcoholic drink made from dark-coloured grapes.","zh":"Red wine 是由深色葡萄製成的酒精飲品。"},{"en":"Some adults drink red wine with dinner because they enjoy its flavour.","zh":"有些成年人晚餐時飲紅酒，因為喜歡它的味道。"},{"en":"If red wine is discussed in health contexts, moderation is still important.","zh":"如果紅酒在健康語境中被討論，適量仍然重要。"},{"en":"This phrase names a drink often compared with other antioxidant-rich foods.","zh":"這個片語命名一種常與其他富含抗氧化物食物比較的飲品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"green tea","meaning":"綠茶","examples":[{"en":"Green tea is better known than chocolate for health benefits.","zh":"綠茶比朱古力更以健康益處聞名。"},{"en":"Green tea is tea made from leaves that are not heavily fermented.","zh":"Green tea 是由沒有高度發酵的茶葉製成的茶。"},{"en":"Many people drink green tea because it tastes light and refreshing.","zh":"許多人飲綠茶，因為它味道清淡而清爽。"},{"en":"If green tea is seen as healthy, consumers may compare other foods with it.","zh":"如果綠茶被視為健康，消費者可能把其他食物與它比較。"},{"en":"This phrase names a drink widely linked with health-conscious habits.","zh":"這個片語命名一種廣泛與健康意識習慣相關的飲品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"berries","meaning":"莓果","examples":[{"en":"Berries are often known for their health-giving properties.","zh":"莓果常以其有益健康的特性聞名。"},{"en":"Berries are small fruits such as strawberries, blueberries, raspberries, and blackberries.","zh":"Berries 是小型水果，例如士多啤梨、藍莓、紅莓和黑莓。"},{"en":"A student may add berries to yoghurt for breakfast.","zh":"學生早餐可能把莓果加入乳酪。"},{"en":"If berries are rich in nutrients, people may see them as a healthy snack.","zh":"如果莓果含有豐富營養，人們可能把它們視為健康小食。"},{"en":"This word refers to a group of small fruits often linked with health.","zh":"這個詞指一類常與健康聯繫起來的小水果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"play a role","meaning":"發揮作用","examples":[{"en":"Health has probably played a role in dark chocolate’s popularity.","zh":"健康因素可能在黑朱古力受歡迎中發揮作用。"},{"en":"To play a role means to be one of the factors influencing a situation.","zh":"To play a role 指成為影響某情況的因素之一。"},{"en":"Good teaching can play a role in helping students enjoy grammar.","zh":"良好教學可以在幫助學生享受文法方面發揮作用。"},{"en":"If health claims play a role in sales, marketing may focus on them more.","zh":"如果健康主張在銷售中發揮作用，市場推廣可能更集中於它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes partial influence, not necessarily the only cause.","zh":"這個片語描述部分影響，不一定是唯一原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"more as…than anything else","meaning":"與其說是其他原因，不如說是……","examples":[{"en":"Health has played a role more as a justification for consumption than anything else.","zh":"健康因素發揮作用，與其說是其他原因，不如說是作為消費理由。"},{"en":"More as A than anything else means mainly in the role of A, rather than for other reasons.","zh":"More as A than anything else 指主要以A的角色發揮作用，而不是因其他原因。"},{"en":"A student may join a club more as a way to make friends than anything else.","zh":"學生加入社團，與其說是其他原因，不如說是為了交朋友。"},{"en":"If health works mainly as a justification, people may already want the product and use health to excuse buying it.","zh":"如果健康主要作為理由，人們可能本來已想買該產品，只是用健康來合理化購買。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the main function of something.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事的主要功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"justification for consumption","meaning":"消費的理由","examples":[{"en":"Health benefits may provide a justification for consumption.","zh":"健康益處可能提供消費的理由。"},{"en":"A justification for consumption is a reason people use to explain or defend buying or eating something.","zh":"Justification for consumption 是人們用來解釋或支持購買或食用某物的原因。"},{"en":"A student may use “I studied hard today” as a justification for buying dessert.","zh":"學生可能用「我今天很努力溫習」作為買甜品的理由。"},{"en":"If people feel guilty about a treat, a health claim can become a justification for consumption.","zh":"如果人們對享受零食有罪疚感，健康主張可以成為消費理由。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reason that makes consumption feel acceptable.","zh":"這個片語描述令人覺得消費可以接受的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"big selling point","meaning":"主要賣點","examples":[{"en":"One of dark chocolate’s big selling points is its lower sugar appeal.","zh":"黑朱古力的其中一個主要賣點是它低糖吸引力。"},{"en":"A big selling point is a feature that strongly attracts customers.","zh":"Big selling point 是強烈吸引顧客的特點。"},{"en":"A phone’s long battery life can be a big selling point for students.","zh":"手機電池續航長可以是對學生的主要賣點。"},{"en":"If a product has a clear selling point, it is easier to market.","zh":"如果產品有清晰賣點，它就更容易推廣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major reason people buy something.","zh":"這個片語描述人們購買某物的主要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"trap someone in","meaning":"令某人陷入","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate does not trap chocoholics in the same sugar-craving spiral.","zh":"黑朱古力不會令朱古力迷陷入同樣的糖分渴求循環。"},{"en":"To trap someone in something means to keep them stuck in a situation that is hard to escape.","zh":"To trap someone in something 指令某人困在難以擺脫的情況中。"},{"en":"Expensive rent can trap young workers in a cycle of saving very little.","zh":"昂貴租金可以令年輕員工陷入幾乎無法儲錢的循環。"},{"en":"If sugary snacks trap people in cravings, they may keep wanting more.","zh":"如果含糖零食令人在渴求中受困，他們可能一直想吃更多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being caught in an unhealthy or difficult pattern.","zh":"這個片語描述陷入不健康或困難模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"downward spiral","meaning":"惡性循環","examples":[{"en":"Milk chocolate can trap people in a downward sugar-craving spiral.","zh":"牛奶朱古力可以令人在對糖分渴求的惡性循環中受困。"},{"en":"A downward spiral is a situation that keeps getting worse because each problem creates another problem.","zh":"Downward spiral 是一種情況不斷惡化，因為每個問題又造成另一個問題。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can start a downward spiral of tiredness, bad mood, and weaker study.","zh":"睡眠不足可以開始疲倦、壞情緒和學習變弱的惡性循環。"},{"en":"If cravings lead to more sugar and more sugar leads to more cravings, a spiral forms.","zh":"如果渴求導致更多糖，而更多糖又導致更多渴求，循環就形成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a worsening cycle.","zh":"這個片語描述不斷惡化的循環。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"sugar-craving spiral","meaning":"對糖分渴求的循環","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate may avoid the sugar-craving spiral linked to milk chocolate.","zh":"黑朱古力可能避免與牛奶朱古力相關的糖分渴求循環。"},{"en":"A sugar-craving spiral is a cycle in which eating sugar makes a person want even more sugar.","zh":"Sugar-craving spiral 是吃糖令人更想吃糖的循環。"},{"en":"A child may enter a sugar-craving spiral after eating sweets every afternoon.","zh":"孩子每天下午吃糖後，可能進入對糖分渴求的循環。"},{"en":"If snacks are less sweet, they may reduce the urge to keep eating sugar.","zh":"如果零食沒那麼甜，它們可能減少繼續吃糖的衝動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated desire for sugar.","zh":"這個片語描述對糖分的反覆渴求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"bear this in mind","meaning":"記住這一點","examples":[{"en":"Parents should bear this in mind when buying snacks.","zh":"家長購買零食時應記住這一點。"},{"en":"To bear this in mind means to remember and consider this point when making a decision.","zh":"To bear this in mind 指在作決定時記住並考慮這一點。"},{"en":"Students should bear exam timing in mind when planning essay answers.","zh":"學生規劃作文答案時，應記住考試時間。"},{"en":"If parents bear sugar content in mind, they may choose snacks more carefully.","zh":"如果家長記住糖分含量，他們可能更仔細選擇零食。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to remind people to consider important information.","zh":"這個片語用來提醒人們考慮重要資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"shop for snacks","meaning":"購買零食","examples":[{"en":"Parents should consider this when they shop for snacks for their children.","zh":"家長為孩子購買零食時應考慮這一點。"},{"en":"To shop for snacks means to buy small foods eaten between meals.","zh":"To shop for snacks 指購買在正餐之間吃的小食。"},{"en":"A student may shop for snacks before a long study session.","zh":"學生可能在長時間自修前購買零食。"},{"en":"If people shop for snacks while hungry, they may buy more sugary food.","zh":"如果人們肚餓時購買零食，他們可能買更多含糖食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes buying light food, not full meals.","zh":"這個片語描述購買輕食，而不是正餐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a new breed of","meaning":"新一類","examples":[{"en":"A new breed of fashionable diets has promoted dark chocolate.","zh":"新一類流行飲食法推廣了黑朱古力。"},{"en":"A new breed of something means a new type or generation of it with different features.","zh":"A new breed of something 指具有不同特徵的新類型或新一代。"},{"en":"A new breed of teachers may use videos, games, and real-world tasks together.","zh":"新一類教師可能同時使用影片、遊戲和真實任務。"},{"en":"If a new breed of diets becomes popular, food marketing may change.","zh":"如果新一類飲食法變得流行，食品市場推廣可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a newer kind of something.","zh":"這個片語描述較新的類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"fashionable diets","meaning":"流行飲食法","examples":[{"en":"Fashionable diets have helped promote dark chocolate.","zh":"流行飲食法幫助推廣黑朱古力。"},{"en":"Fashionable diets are popular eating plans that many people follow for health, weight, or lifestyle reasons.","zh":"Fashionable diets 是許多人因健康、體重或生活方式原因追隨的熱門飲食計劃。"},{"en":"A fashionable diet may become popular after celebrities mention it online.","zh":"名人在網上提及後，某種流行飲食法可能變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"If a fashionable diet allows a food, that food may gain popularity.","zh":"如果流行飲食法允許某食物，該食物可能變得更受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trend-driven eating habits.","zh":"這個片語描述由潮流推動的飲食習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"promote the cause of","meaning":"推動……的支持","examples":[{"en":"Fashionable diets have helped promote the cause of dark chocolate.","zh":"流行飲食法幫助推動對黑朱古力的支持。"},{"en":"To promote the cause of something means to support it and help it become more accepted.","zh":"To promote the cause of something 指支持某事並幫助它更被接受。"},{"en":"A school campaign can promote the cause of recycling by making bins easier to use.","zh":"學校運動可以透過令回收箱更易使用，推動對回收的支持。"},{"en":"If health trends promote dark chocolate, more people may feel comfortable eating it.","zh":"如果健康潮流推動黑朱古力，更多人可能放心食用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes helping an idea, product, or movement gain support.","zh":"這個片語描述幫助某想法、產品或運動獲得支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"most dieticians agree that","meaning":"大部分營養師同意","examples":[{"en":"Most dieticians agree that a small treat can be useful.","zh":"大部分營養師同意少量獎勵性食物可以有用。"},{"en":"Most dieticians agree that means many nutrition experts share the same view.","zh":"Most dieticians agree that 指許多營養專家有相同看法。"},{"en":"Most dieticians agree that balanced meals are better than extreme restrictions.","zh":"大部分營養師同意均衡膳食比極端限制更好。"},{"en":"If experts agree on moderation, people may feel less guilty about occasional treats.","zh":"如果專家同意適度原則，人們可能對偶爾享受零食較少內疚。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a broad professional opinion.","zh":"這個片語引出廣泛專業意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a little of what you fancy","meaning":"少量自己喜歡的東西","examples":[{"en":"A little of what you fancy can be better than complete denial.","zh":"少量自己喜歡的東西可能比完全壓抑更好。"},{"en":"A little of what you fancy means a small amount of something you enjoy.","zh":"A little of what you fancy 指少量自己喜歡的東西。"},{"en":"A student may have a little of what they fancy, such as one biscuit, after finishing homework.","zh":"學生完成功課後，可能吃少量自己喜歡的東西，例如一塊餅乾。"},{"en":"If people allow small treats, they may avoid overeating later.","zh":"如果人們容許自己少量享受零食，他們之後可能避免過量進食。"},{"en":"This phrase supports moderation rather than strict deprivation.","zh":"這個片語支持適度，而不是嚴格剝奪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"does you more good than","meaning":"比……對你更有好處","examples":[{"en":"A small treat may do you more good than outright denial.","zh":"少量獎勵性食物可能比徹底壓抑對你更有好處。"},{"en":"If something does you more good than another thing, it benefits you more.","zh":"If something does you more good than another thing 指某事比另一事對你更有益。"},{"en":"A short rest may do you more good than forcing yourself to study while exhausted.","zh":"短暫休息可能比在疲憊時強迫自己溫習對你更有好處。"},{"en":"If complete denial causes stress, a small controlled treat may be healthier.","zh":"如果完全壓抑造成壓力，少量受控零食可能較健康。"},{"en":"This phrase compares which choice is more beneficial.","zh":"這個片語比較哪個選擇更有益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"outright denial","meaning":"完全壓抑；徹底否定","examples":[{"en":"Most dieticians do not support outright denial.","zh":"大部分營養師不支持完全壓抑。"},{"en":"Outright denial means completely refusing yourself something you want.","zh":"Outright denial 指完全拒絕自己想要的東西。"},{"en":"A person on a strict diet may practise outright denial by banning all desserts.","zh":"採取嚴格飲食法的人可能透過禁止所有甜品來完全壓抑自己。"},{"en":"If outright denial leads to frustration, people may give up the diet completely.","zh":"如果完全壓抑導致挫敗，人們可能徹底放棄飲食計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes total restriction rather than moderation.","zh":"這個片語描述完全限制，而不是適度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"products have got better","meaning":"產品變得更好","examples":[{"en":"More people may eat dark chocolate because the products have got better.","zh":"更多人可能吃黑朱古力，因為產品變得更好。"},{"en":"Products have got better means the items now have higher quality, taste, design, or performance than before.","zh":"Products have got better 指商品現在比以前有更高質素、味道、設計或性能。"},{"en":"Students may use tablets more often because the products have got better and lighter.","zh":"學生可能更常使用平板電腦，因為產品變得更好和更輕。"},{"en":"If dark chocolate products improve, people who disliked the old taste may try them again.","zh":"如果黑朱古力產品改善，不喜歡舊味道的人可能再次嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase explains rising popularity through improved quality.","zh":"這個片語透過質素改善解釋受歡迎程度上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the challenge with","meaning":"……的挑戰","examples":[{"en":"The challenge with higher cocoa variants is balancing bitterness and sweetness.","zh":"可可含量較高款式的挑戰是平衡苦味和甜味。"},{"en":"The challenge with something is the main difficulty involved in it.","zh":"The challenge with something 是某事涉及的主要困難。"},{"en":"The challenge with online learning is keeping students focused at home.","zh":"網上學習的挑戰是在家中保持學生專注。"},{"en":"If a product must be healthy and tasty, the challenge is balancing both needs.","zh":"如果產品必須健康又好吃，挑戰就是平衡兩種需要。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the difficult part of a task or product.","zh":"這個片語引出任務或產品的困難部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"higher cocoa variants","meaning":"可可含量較高的款式","examples":[{"en":"Higher cocoa variants contain more bitter-tasting cocoa.","zh":"可可含量較高的款式含有更多帶苦味的可可。"},{"en":"Higher cocoa variants are chocolate products with a greater percentage of cocoa.","zh":"Higher cocoa variants 是可可百分比較高的朱古力產品。"},{"en":"A 70% chocolate bar is a higher cocoa variant than a milk chocolate bar.","zh":"70%朱古力條比牛奶朱古力條是可可含量較高的款式。"},{"en":"If cocoa content rises, sweetness may fall and bitterness may increase.","zh":"如果可可含量上升，甜度可能下降而苦味可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes chocolate types with more cocoa.","zh":"這個片語描述含有更多可可的朱古力類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"get the right trade-off between","meaning":"在……之間取得適當平衡","examples":[{"en":"Makers must get the right trade-off between cocoa and sugar.","zh":"生產商必須在可可和糖之間取得適當平衡。"},{"en":"To get the right trade-off between two things means to balance them so neither causes too much loss.","zh":"To get the right trade-off between two things 指平衡兩者，令任何一方都不造成太大損失。"},{"en":"A student must get the right trade-off between study time and rest time.","zh":"學生必須在溫習時間和休息時間之間取得適當平衡。"},{"en":"If chocolate has too much cocoa, it may be too bitter; if it has too much sugar, it may lose cocoa flavour.","zh":"如果朱古力可可太多，可能太苦；如果糖太多，可能失去可可味。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finding the best balance between competing needs.","zh":"這個片語描述在互相競爭的需要之間找出最佳平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"bitter-tasting cocoa","meaning":"帶苦味的可可","examples":[{"en":"Bitter-tasting cocoa contains many good micronutrients.","zh":"帶苦味的可可含有許多良好微量營養素。"},{"en":"Bitter-tasting cocoa is cocoa with a strong, sharp flavour that is not sweet.","zh":"Bitter-tasting cocoa 是味道強烈、尖銳且不甜的可可。"},{"en":"A beginner may find bitter-tasting cocoa difficult to enjoy without sugar.","zh":"初學者可能覺得沒有糖的帶苦味可可難以享受。"},{"en":"If bitterness is too strong, companies may add vanilla or sweetness to soften it.","zh":"如果苦味太強，公司可能加入雲呢拿或甜味來軟化它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cocoa’s intense natural taste.","zh":"這個片語描述可可強烈的天然味道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"micronutrients","meaning":"微量營養素","examples":[{"en":"Good micronutrients come from the cocoa in dark chocolate.","zh":"良好微量營養素來自黑朱古力中的可可。"},{"en":"Micronutrients are vitamins, minerals, and other substances the body needs in small amounts.","zh":"Micronutrients 是身體少量需要的維他命、礦物質和其他物質。"},{"en":"Vegetables provide micronutrients that support normal body functions.","zh":"蔬菜提供支持身體正常功能的微量營養素。"},{"en":"If a food contains useful micronutrients, it may be nutritionally valuable even in small amounts.","zh":"如果食物含有有用微量營養素，即使少量也可能有營養價值。"},{"en":"This word describes nutrients needed in tiny quantities.","zh":"這個詞描述身體需要的微量營養。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"bitter and gritty-tasting","meaning":"苦澀而帶粗糙口感","examples":[{"en":"In the past, dark chocolate was bitter and gritty-tasting.","zh":"過去，黑朱古力苦澀而帶粗糙口感。"},{"en":"Bitter and gritty-tasting means sharp in flavour and rough or sandy in texture.","zh":"Bitter and gritty-tasting 指味道苦而強烈，口感粗糙或像有沙粒。"},{"en":"A badly made protein drink may be bitter and gritty-tasting if the powder does not mix well.","zh":"如果粉末混合不好，製作差的蛋白飲品可能苦澀而帶粗糙口感。"},{"en":"If chocolate feels gritty, consumers may think the product quality is poor.","zh":"如果朱古力口感粗糙，消費者可能認為產品質素差。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both taste and mouthfeel.","zh":"這個片語同時描述味道和口感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"gentle-tasting cocoa bean","meaning":"味道溫和的可可豆","examples":[{"en":"Some companies use a gentle-tasting cocoa bean.","zh":"有些公司使用味道溫和的可可豆。"},{"en":"A gentle-tasting cocoa bean has a softer, less harsh flavour.","zh":"Gentle-tasting cocoa bean 是味道較柔和、沒有那麼刺激的可可豆。"},{"en":"A café may choose gentle-tasting coffee beans for customers who dislike bitterness.","zh":"咖啡店可能為不喜歡苦味的顧客選擇味道溫和的咖啡豆。"},{"en":"If a cocoa bean tastes gentle, beginners may find dark chocolate easier to enjoy.","zh":"如果可可豆味道溫和，初學者可能更容易享受黑朱古力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a milder raw ingredient.","zh":"這個片語描述較溫和的原材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be new to","meaning":"對……不熟悉","examples":[{"en":"Gentle-tasting beans help people who are new to dark chocolate.","zh":"味道溫和的可可豆幫助對黑朱古力不熟悉的人。"},{"en":"To be new to something means to have little experience with it.","zh":"To be new to something 指對某事經驗很少。"},{"en":"A student who is new to IELTS may need simple examples before difficult strategies.","zh":"對 IELTS 不熟悉的學生可能需要簡單例子，再學困難策略。"},{"en":"If customers are new to a strong flavour, a milder version may help them start.","zh":"如果顧客對強烈味道不熟悉，較溫和版本可能幫助他們開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes beginners or first-time users.","zh":"這個片語描述初學者或首次使用者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"scare someone off","meaning":"嚇怕某人","examples":[{"en":"Strong bitterness may scare new consumers off.","zh":"強烈苦味可能嚇怕新消費者。"},{"en":"To scare someone off means to make someone avoid something because it seems unpleasant or difficult.","zh":"To scare someone off 指令某人因某事看似不愉快或困難而避開它。"},{"en":"A very long grammar explanation may scare beginners off.","zh":"非常長的文法解釋可能嚇怕初學者。"},{"en":"If the first experience is too harsh, customers may not try the product again.","zh":"如果第一次體驗太刺激，顧客可能不再嘗試該產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes discouraging someone from continuing.","zh":"這個片語描述令某人不想繼續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a hint of vanilla","meaning":"一點雲呢拿味","examples":[{"en":"Adding a hint of vanilla can soften dark chocolate.","zh":"加入一點雲呢拿味可以軟化黑朱古力。"},{"en":"A hint of vanilla means a small amount or slight flavour of vanilla.","zh":"A hint of vanilla 指少量或輕微的雲呢拿味。"},{"en":"A cake with a hint of lemon tastes fresh without becoming sour.","zh":"帶一點檸檬味的蛋糕會感覺清新，但不會變酸。"},{"en":"If a bitter product has a hint of sweetness or aroma, it may become easier to enjoy.","zh":"如果苦味產品有一點甜味或香氣，它可能變得更容易享受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a subtle flavour, not a strong one.","zh":"這個片語描述細微味道，而不是強烈味道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"act as a seasoning","meaning":"起調味作用","examples":[{"en":"Vanilla acts as a seasoning in dark chocolate.","zh":"雲呢拿在黑朱古力中起調味作用。"},{"en":"To act as a seasoning means to add flavour and improve the overall taste.","zh":"To act as a seasoning 指加入味道並改善整體口味。"},{"en":"A little salt can act as a seasoning in soup by bringing out other flavours.","zh":"少量鹽可以在湯中起調味作用，帶出其他味道。"},{"en":"If vanilla acts as a seasoning, it supports the cocoa rather than replacing it.","zh":"如果雲呢拿起調味作用，它支持可可味，而不是取代它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small ingredient that improves flavour balance.","zh":"這個片語描述改善味道平衡的小成分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"soften the bitter notes","meaning":"軟化苦味","examples":[{"en":"Vanilla can soften the bitter notes of cocoa.","zh":"雲呢拿可以軟化可可的苦味。"},{"en":"To soften the bitter notes means to make harsh bitter flavours feel gentler.","zh":"To soften the bitter notes 指令尖銳苦味變得較溫和。"},{"en":"Milk can soften the bitter notes of strong coffee.","zh":"牛奶可以軟化濃咖啡的苦味。"},{"en":"If bitter notes are softened, beginners may find the drink or food easier to accept.","zh":"如果苦味被軟化，初學者可能覺得該飲品或食物較容易接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing sharp bitterness without removing the flavour completely.","zh":"這個片語描述減低尖銳苦味，而不是完全除去味道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"bitter notes","meaning":"苦味調","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate often has bitter notes.","zh":"黑朱古力常有苦味調。"},{"en":"Bitter notes are slight bitter flavours within the overall taste of food or drink.","zh":"Bitter notes 是食物或飲品整體味道中的輕微苦味。"},{"en":"Strong tea may have bitter notes if it is brewed for too long.","zh":"如果茶沖泡太久，濃茶可能有苦味調。"},{"en":"If bitter notes are balanced with sweetness, the flavour can become more complex.","zh":"如果苦味調與甜味平衡，味道可以變得更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in tasting descriptions.","zh":"這個片語常用於品味描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"bring out the sweetness","meaning":"帶出甜味","examples":[{"en":"Vanilla can bring out the sweetness of cocoa.","zh":"雲呢拿可以帶出可可的甜味。"},{"en":"To bring out the sweetness means to make the sweet flavour easier to notice.","zh":"To bring out the sweetness 指令甜味更容易被注意到。"},{"en":"A little salt can bring out the sweetness of caramel.","zh":"少量鹽可以帶出焦糖的甜味。"},{"en":"If one ingredient brings out sweetness, the product may taste sweeter without adding much sugar.","zh":"如果某成分帶出甜味，產品可能不加太多糖也感覺更甜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes enhancing a flavour already present.","zh":"這個片語描述增強已有味道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"for each question","meaning":"對於每條問題","examples":[{"en":"For each question, only one of the choices is correct.","zh":"對於每條問題，只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"For each question means separately for every individual question.","zh":"For each question 指分別對每一條問題而言。"},{"en":"For each question in a reading test, students should check the evidence in the passage.","zh":"對於閱讀測驗中的每條問題，學生應檢查文章中的證據。"},{"en":"If instructions apply for each question, students must follow them every time.","zh":"如果指示適用於每條問題，學生每次都必須遵守。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights that the rule applies question by question.","zh":"這個片語強調規則逐題適用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"only one of the choices is correct","meaning":"只有一個選項正確","examples":[{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct for each question.","zh":"每條問題只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"Only one of the choices is correct means just one answer option is right.","zh":"Only one of the choices is correct 指只有一個答案選項是對的。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice grammar task, only one of the choices is usually correct.","zh":"在文法選擇題中，通常只有一個選項正確。"},{"en":"If students choose two answers when only one is correct, they may lose the mark.","zh":"如果學生在只有一個正確答案時選了兩個，可能會失分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語給出清楚考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"corresponding letter","meaning":"對應字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the corresponding letter in the answer box.","zh":"考生在答案方格中寫上對應字母。"},{"en":"The corresponding letter is the letter that matches the correct option.","zh":"Corresponding letter 是與正確選項相配的字母。"},{"en":"If option C is correct, students should write the corresponding letter C.","zh":"如果選項C正確，學生應寫上對應字母C。"},{"en":"If students write the wrong letter despite knowing the answer, they may lose marks.","zh":"如果學生即使知道答案卻寫錯字母，可能會失分。"},{"en":"This phrase links an answer choice with its letter.","zh":"這個片語把答案選項與其字母連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"appropriate box","meaning":"適當方格","examples":[{"en":"Students write the answer in the appropriate box on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生在答題紙上的適當方格內填寫答案。"},{"en":"The appropriate box is the correct space where an answer should be written.","zh":"Appropriate box 是應填寫答案的正確空格。"},{"en":"A student must write Question 5’s answer in the box for Question 5, not Question 6.","zh":"學生必須把第5題答案寫在第5題方格，而不是第6題。"},{"en":"If answers are written in the wrong boxes, correct answers may be marked wrong.","zh":"如果答案寫在錯誤方格中，正確答案也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the correct place for an answer.","zh":"這個片語描述答案應放的正確位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"answer sheet","meaning":"答題紙","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write their answers on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生把答案寫在答題紙上。"},{"en":"An answer sheet is the official paper or form where exam answers are recorded.","zh":"Answer sheet 是記錄考試答案的正式紙張或表格。"},{"en":"Students should check the answer sheet before time ends to avoid missing boxes.","zh":"學生應在時間結束前檢查答題紙，以避免漏填方格。"},{"en":"If the answer sheet is filled in carelessly, marks may be lost even when the thinking is correct.","zh":"如果答題紙填寫粗心，即使思路正確也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the document used for submitting answers.","zh":"這個片語指用來提交答案的文件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"people are eating more","meaning":"人們正在吃更多……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether people are eating more dark chocolate.","zh":"題目問人們是否正在吃更多黑朱古力。"},{"en":"People are eating more means consumption is increasing among consumers.","zh":"People are eating more 指消費者的食用量正在增加。"},{"en":"People are eating more takeaway food when they are too busy to cook.","zh":"當人們太忙沒時間煮飯，他們可能正在吃更多外賣。"},{"en":"If people are eating more of a product, demand for its ingredients may rise.","zh":"如果人們正在吃更多某產品，對其原料的需求可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rise in eating habits or consumption.","zh":"這個片語描述飲食習慣或消費量增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"rising for several reasons","meaning":"因多個原因上升","examples":[{"en":"Cocoa prices are rising for several reasons.","zh":"可可價格因多個原因上升。"},{"en":"Rising for several reasons means increasing because of more than one cause.","zh":"Rising for several reasons 指因不止一個原因而增加。"},{"en":"Transport costs may be rising for several reasons, including fuel, wages, and maintenance.","zh":"交通成本可能因燃油、工資和維修等多個原因上升。"},{"en":"If prices rise for several reasons, solving only one cause may not reduce them quickly.","zh":"如果價格因多個原因上升，只解決一個原因可能不能很快令價格下降。"},{"en":"This phrase explains that a trend has multiple causes.","zh":"這個片語解釋某趨勢有多重原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"water shortage","meaning":"水源短缺","examples":[{"en":"A water shortage in West Africa can affect cocoa production.","zh":"西非水源短缺可以影響可可生產。"},{"en":"A water shortage happens when there is not enough water for people, crops, or industry.","zh":"Water shortage 指沒有足夠水供人、農作物或工業使用。"},{"en":"A school may face a water shortage if pipes break before lunchtime.","zh":"如果水管在午飯前爆裂，學校可能面對水源短缺。"},{"en":"If farms face water shortages, crops may grow poorly or die.","zh":"如果農場面對水源短缺，作物可能生長不良或死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lack of available water.","zh":"這個片語描述可用水不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"transportation problems","meaning":"運輸問題","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether transportation problems caused the price rise.","zh":"題目問運輸問題是否造成價格上升。"},{"en":"Transportation problems are difficulties moving goods or people from one place to another.","zh":"Transportation problems 是把貨物或人從一地移到另一地時遇到的困難。"},{"en":"A broken railway line can create transportation problems for commuters.","zh":"鐵路線故障可以為通勤者造成運輸問題。"},{"en":"If transportation problems delay cacao beans, factories may face supply pressure.","zh":"如果運輸問題延誤可可豆，工廠可能面對供應壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes problems in moving things or people.","zh":"這個片語描述移動物件或人的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"far more than usual","meaning":"遠多於平常","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether buyers are purchasing far more cacao beans than usual.","zh":"該選項問買家是否購買遠多於平常的可可豆。"},{"en":"Far more than usual means much more than the normal amount.","zh":"Far more than usual 指比正常數量多很多。"},{"en":"A student may drink far more coffee than usual during exam week.","zh":"學生在考試週可能喝遠多於平常的咖啡。"},{"en":"If buyers purchase far more than usual, stocks can disappear quickly.","zh":"如果買家購買遠多於平常的數量，存貨可能很快消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unusually large increase.","zh":"這個片語描述異常大的增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"not yet responding to","meaning":"尚未對……作出回應","examples":[{"en":"Industry buyers are not yet responding strongly to the price rise.","zh":"業內買家尚未對價格上升作出強烈回應。"},{"en":"Not yet responding to something means they have not begun to react to it in a clear way.","zh":"Not yet responding to something 指他們尚未以清楚方式開始反應。"},{"en":"A school may not yet be responding to complaints if no meeting has been arranged.","zh":"如果學校尚未安排會議，它可能尚未對投訴作出回應。"},{"en":"If buyers are not yet responding, market behaviour may change later when pressure grows.","zh":"如果買家尚未回應，當壓力增加時市場行為可能之後改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a delayed or limited reaction.","zh":"這個片語描述延遲或有限的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"trying hard to prove","meaning":"努力證明","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are trying hard to prove that chocolate can be good for health.","zh":"科學家正努力證明朱古力可以對健康有益。"},{"en":"Trying hard to prove something means making a strong effort to show it is true.","zh":"Trying hard to prove something 指努力顯示某事是真的。"},{"en":"A student may try hard to prove that their answer is correct by quoting the passage.","zh":"學生可能透過引用文章，努力證明自己的答案正確。"},{"en":"If scientists try hard to prove a claim, they need careful evidence, not just enthusiasm.","zh":"如果科學家努力證明某主張，他們需要仔細證據，而不只是熱情。"},{"en":"This phrase describes determined effort to establish a point.","zh":"這個片語描述為確立觀點而作出的堅定努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"complete the following sentences","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the following sentences using words from the text.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成以下句子。"},{"en":"To complete the following sentences means to fill in missing parts of the sentences that come next.","zh":"To complete the following sentences 指填補接下來句子中的缺失部分。"},{"en":"Students should read the full sentence before choosing words from the passage.","zh":"學生應先閱讀整句，才從文章中選詞。"},{"en":"If the grammar around the gap is ignored, the answer may not fit.","zh":"如果忽略空格前後文法，答案可能不合適。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction for gap-fill reading tasks.","zh":"這個片語是填空閱讀題常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不超過三個字","examples":[{"en":"Students should use no more than three words for each gap.","zh":"學生每個空格應使用不超過三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain three words or fewer.","zh":"No more than three words 指答案必須包含三個或更少英文單詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “premium dark chocolate,” it uses three words and fits the rule.","zh":"如果答案是 “premium dark chocolate”，它用了三個字，符合規則。"},{"en":"If students write four words, the answer may be marked wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"如果學生寫四個字，即使意思正確，也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個片語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"from the text","meaning":"來自文章","examples":[{"en":"The answers must come from the text.","zh":"答案必須來自文章。"},{"en":"From the text means the words or information must be taken from the reading passage.","zh":"From the text 指字詞或資料必須取自閱讀文章。"},{"en":"In IELTS reading, students should not use outside knowledge when answers must come from the text.","zh":"在 IELTS 閱讀中，如果答案必須來自文章，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"If a word is not in the passage, it may not be accepted in a text-based gap-fill question.","zh":"如果某字不在文章中，在文章填空題中可能不被接受。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds students to rely on the source.","zh":"這個片語提醒學生依賴來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"for each gap","meaning":"每個空格","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose suitable words for each gap.","zh":"考生為每個空格選擇合適字詞。"},{"en":"For each gap means separately for every blank space in the question.","zh":"For each gap 指分別對每一個空白位置而言。"},{"en":"Students should check the grammar before and after each gap.","zh":"學生應檢查每個空格前後的文法。"},{"en":"If each gap needs a noun, choosing a verb may make the answer wrong.","zh":"如果每個空格需要名詞，選擇動詞可能令答案錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses attention on every individual blank.","zh":"這個片語把注意力集中在每個獨立空格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"worldwide shortfall","meaning":"全球短缺","examples":[{"en":"A worldwide shortfall in chocolate production is expected this year.","zh":"今年預計朱古力生產會出現全球短缺。"},{"en":"A worldwide shortfall is a global shortage where supply is less than demand.","zh":"Worldwide shortfall 是全球性短缺，即供應少於需求。"},{"en":"A worldwide shortfall in computer chips can delay phone and car production.","zh":"電腦晶片全球短缺可以延誤手機和汽車生產。"},{"en":"If a shortfall is worldwide, local shops may not solve it by changing suppliers easily.","zh":"如果短缺是全球性的，本地商店可能不容易透過更換供應商解決。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shortage affecting many countries.","zh":"這個片語描述影響許多國家的短缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"chocolate production","meaning":"朱古力生產","examples":[{"en":"A shortfall in chocolate production may occur this year.","zh":"今年可能出現朱古力生產短缺。"},{"en":"Chocolate production is the process of making chocolate from ingredients such as cacao beans, sugar, and milk.","zh":"Chocolate production 是用可可豆、糖和牛奶等材料製造朱古力的過程。"},{"en":"A factory may reduce chocolate production if cacao beans become too expensive.","zh":"如果可可豆變得太昂貴，工廠可能減少朱古力生產。"},{"en":"If production falls while demand rises, shortages and price increases may follow.","zh":"如果生產下降而需求上升，短缺和加價可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the manufacture of chocolate products.","zh":"這個片語描述朱古力產品的製造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"fresh tastes","meaning":"新鮮口味","examples":[{"en":"Consumers are looking for fresh tastes in chocolate.","zh":"消費者正在尋找朱古力中的新鮮口味。"},{"en":"Fresh tastes are new, different, or more interesting flavours.","zh":"Fresh tastes 是新的、不同的或更有趣的味道。"},{"en":"A café may attract young customers by offering fresh tastes such as yuzu tea or salted caramel.","zh":"咖啡店可能透過提供柚子茶或海鹽焦糖等新鮮口味吸引年輕顧客。"},{"en":"If consumers want fresh tastes, companies may experiment with new ingredients.","zh":"如果消費者想要新鮮口味，公司可能嘗試新成分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the desire for new flavour experiences.","zh":"這個片語描述對新味覺體驗的渴望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"prevent deadly blood clots","meaning":"防止致命血栓","examples":[{"en":"Dark chocolate may help prevent deadly blood clots.","zh":"黑朱古力可能有助防止致命血栓。"},{"en":"To prevent deadly blood clots means to stop dangerous clots from forming and threatening life.","zh":"To prevent deadly blood clots 指阻止危險血栓形成並威脅生命。"},{"en":"Doctors may prescribe medicine to prevent blood clots after certain operations.","zh":"醫生可能在某些手術後處方藥物防止血栓。"},{"en":"If a clot blocks blood flow to the brain or heart, it can be deadly.","zh":"如果血栓阻塞流向大腦或心臟的血液，它可能致命。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stopping a serious medical risk.","zh":"這個片語描述阻止嚴重醫療風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"disagree with the concept of","meaning":"不同意……的概念","examples":[{"en":"Most dieticians disagree with the concept of outright denial.","zh":"大部分營養師不同意完全壓抑這個概念。"},{"en":"To disagree with the concept of something means to reject the idea behind it.","zh":"To disagree with the concept of something 指拒絕某事背後的想法。"},{"en":"Many teachers disagree with the concept of learning only by memorising answers.","zh":"許多老師不同意只靠背答案學習這個概念。"},{"en":"If experts disagree with an idea, they may suggest a more balanced approach.","zh":"如果專家不同意某想法，他們可能建議較平衡做法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rejecting a general principle.","zh":"這個片語描述拒絕一般原則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"less bitter","meaning":"較少苦味","examples":[{"en":"Some companies have made their dark chocolate less bitter.","zh":"有些公司已令其黑朱古力較少苦味。"},{"en":"Less bitter means having a weaker or softer bitter taste.","zh":"Less bitter 指苦味較弱或較柔和。"},{"en":"Tea becomes less bitter if it is brewed for a shorter time.","zh":"如果茶沖泡時間較短，它會較少苦味。"},{"en":"If chocolate is less bitter, people new to dark chocolate may enjoy it more easily.","zh":"如果朱古力較少苦味，對黑朱古力不熟悉的人可能更容易享受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing sharpness in flavour.","zh":"這個片語描述減少味道中的尖銳感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether statements agree with the information given.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與所給資料相符。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"To agree with the information given 指與文章所說內容一致。"},{"en":"If the text says prices rose, a statement saying prices increased agrees with the information given.","zh":"如果文本說價格上升，而陳述說價格增加，它就與所給資料相符。"},{"en":"If a statement changes the meaning, it does not agree even if some words look similar.","zh":"如果陳述改變意思，即使有些字看似相似，也不算相符。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in True/False/Not Given tasks.","zh":"這個片語常見於 True/False/Not Given 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章中的資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"To contradict the information 指說出與文章相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says demand rose, a statement saying demand fell contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說需求上升，而陳述說需求下降，就是與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"When an option contradicts the text, students should mark it false.","zh":"當選項與文本相矛盾，學生應標示為 false。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a direct conflict with the source.","zh":"這個片語描述與來源直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students choose “NOT GIVEN” when there is no information on this.","zh":"當沒有相關資料時，學生選擇 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"No information on this 指文章沒有說該陳述是真或假。"},{"en":"If a passage mentions chocolate prices but not advertising budgets, there is no information on advertising budgets.","zh":"如果文章提到朱古力價格但沒有提到廣告預算，就沒有關於廣告預算的資料。"},{"en":"If there is no information, students should not guess from general knowledge.","zh":"如果沒有資料，學生不應用常識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the answer cannot be proved from the text.","zh":"這個片語表示答案不能從文本證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"increase the price of","meaning":"提高……的價格","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether companies have increased the price of chocolate bars.","zh":"該陳述問公司是否已提高朱古力條的價格。"},{"en":"To increase the price of something means to make it cost more.","zh":"To increase the price of something 指令某物售價更高。"},{"en":"A bus company may increase the price of tickets when fuel costs rise.","zh":"當燃油成本上升，巴士公司可能提高車票價格。"},{"en":"If manufacturers increase the price of chocolate, customers may buy fewer bars.","zh":"如果生產商提高朱古力價格，顧客可能購買較少朱古力條。"},{"en":"This phrase describes charging more than before.","zh":"這個片語描述比以前收取更高價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"move to higher-quality brands","meaning":"轉向較高質素品牌","examples":[{"en":"Chocolate consumers in Britain are moving to higher-quality brands.","zh":"英國朱古力消費者正轉向較高質素品牌。"},{"en":"To move to higher-quality brands means to switch from ordinary brands to better or more premium ones.","zh":"To move to higher-quality brands 指從普通品牌轉向更好或更高級品牌。"},{"en":"A student may move to higher-quality notebooks after cheap ones fall apart quickly.","zh":"如果便宜筆記簿很快散開，學生可能轉向較高質素品牌。"},{"en":"If consumers move to higher-quality brands, cheaper brands may lose market share.","zh":"如果消費者轉向較高質素品牌，較便宜品牌可能失去市場份額。"},{"en":"This phrase describes upgrading buying choices.","zh":"這個片語描述購買選擇升級。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"the biggest trading centres","meaning":"最大交易中心","examples":[{"en":"London and New York are major cocoa trading centres.","zh":"倫敦和紐約是主要可可交易中心。"},{"en":"The biggest trading centres are the most important places where a product or contract is bought and sold.","zh":"Biggest trading centres 是買賣某產品或合約最重要的地方。"},{"en":"A city may become one of the biggest trading centres if many banks and traders operate there.","zh":"如果許多銀行和交易員在某城市營運，它可能成為最大交易中心之一。"},{"en":"If prices move in the biggest trading centres, global buyers pay attention.","zh":"如果最大交易中心價格變動，全球買家會關注。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies leading market hubs.","zh":"這個片語指出領先市場樞紐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"depend on the climate","meaning":"取決於氣候","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether cacao taste depends on the climate where it is grown.","zh":"該陳述問可可味道是否取決於其種植地氣候。"},{"en":"To depend on the climate means to be affected by weather patterns such as rain, heat, and sunlight.","zh":"To depend on the climate 指受雨量、熱度和陽光等天氣模式影響。"},{"en":"Grape flavour can depend on the climate of the vineyard.","zh":"葡萄味道可能取決於葡萄園的氣候。"},{"en":"If crop quality depends on climate, unusual weather can change taste and harvest size.","zh":"如果作物質素取決於氣候，異常天氣可以改變味道和收成量。"},{"en":"This phrase links natural growing conditions with final quality.","zh":"這個片語把自然種植條件與最終質素連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"most types of dark chocolate","meaning":"大多數黑朱古力種類","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether vanilla is used in most types of dark chocolate.","zh":"該陳述問雲呢拿是否用於大多數黑朱古力種類。"},{"en":"Most types of dark chocolate means the majority of dark chocolate varieties.","zh":"Most types of dark chocolate 指黑朱古力款式中的大多數。"},{"en":"Most types of dark chocolate taste less sweet than milk chocolate.","zh":"大多數黑朱古力種類味道比牛奶朱古力不甜。"},{"en":"If an ingredient appears in most types, it is common rather than unusual.","zh":"如果某成分出現在大多數種類中，它就是常見而非不尋常。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what is true for the majority of dark chocolate products.","zh":"這個片語描述對大多數黑朱古力產品成立的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 103 - Black Gold.pdf","sourcePage":24}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 104":[{"front":"revolutionary bridges","meaning":"革命性的橋樑","examples":[{"en":"Robert Maillart is known for his revolutionary bridges.","zh":"Robert Maillart 以其革命性的橋樑聞名。"},{"en":"Revolutionary bridges are bridges with designs so new that they change how engineers think.","zh":"revolutionary bridges 指設計非常創新、能改變工程師思考方式的橋樑。"},{"en":"A city may become famous if it builds a revolutionary bridge that is both lighter and safer than older designs.","zh":"如果一座城市建造一條比舊設計更輕、更安全的革命性橋樑，它可能因此聞名。"},{"en":"Revolutionary bridges can influence later projects because other engineers copy or improve their ideas.","zh":"革命性的橋樑可以影響後來項目，因為其他工程師會模仿或改良其想法。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests not just beauty, but a major change in bridge design.","zh":"這個短語暗示的不只是美感，而是橋樑設計上的重大改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Swiss engineer","meaning":"瑞士工程師","examples":[{"en":"Robert Maillart was a Swiss engineer who designed remarkable bridges.","zh":"Robert Maillart 是一位設計非凡橋樑的瑞士工程師。"},{"en":"A Swiss engineer is an engineer from Switzerland or closely connected with Swiss engineering.","zh":"Swiss engineer 是來自瑞士或與瑞士工程密切相關的工程師。"},{"en":"A Swiss engineer may work on bridges, tunnels, railways or mountain roads.","zh":"瑞士工程師可能從事橋樑、隧道、鐵路或山區道路工程。"},{"en":"Mentioning Maillart as a Swiss engineer places his work within Switzerland’s strong engineering tradition.","zh":"稱 Maillart 為瑞士工程師，是把他的作品放在瑞士強大工程傳統中理解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both nationality and profession.","zh":"這個短語同時描述國籍和職業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"some of the greatest bridges","meaning":"一些最偉大的橋樑","examples":[{"en":"Maillart built some of the greatest bridges of the 20th century.","zh":"Maillart 建造了二十世紀一些最偉大的橋樑。"},{"en":"Some of the greatest bridges means several bridges that are among the most admired or important.","zh":"some of the greatest bridges 指幾座位列最受讚賞或最重要之中的橋樑。"},{"en":"A guidebook may list some of the greatest bridges in the world because of their design and history.","zh":"旅遊指南可能因橋樑的設計和歷史而列出世界上一些最偉大的橋樑。"},{"en":"Bridges are called great when they solve difficult problems and remain influential.","zh":"當橋樑解決困難問題並保持影響力，它們就會被稱為偉大。"},{"en":"The phrase praises a group of bridges without claiming they are the only great ones.","zh":"這個短語稱讚一組橋樑，但不是說它們是唯一偉大的橋樑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"elegantly solve","meaning":"巧妙地解決","examples":[{"en":"His designs elegantly solved a basic engineering problem.","zh":"他的設計巧妙地解決了一個基本工程難題。"},{"en":"To elegantly solve a problem means to solve it in a simple, clever and graceful way.","zh":"elegantly solve a problem 指以簡潔、聰明而優雅的方式解決問題。"},{"en":"A teacher elegantly solves a classroom problem by changing the seating plan instead of punishing everyone.","zh":"老師透過改變座位安排而不是懲罰所有人，巧妙地解決課室問題。"},{"en":"An elegant solution often uses fewer resources while producing a better result.","zh":"巧妙的解決方法常以較少資源帶來較好結果。"},{"en":"The phrase praises both the effectiveness and the beauty of a solution.","zh":"這個短語同時稱讚解決方法的有效性和美感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a basic engineering problem","meaning":"基本工程難題","examples":[{"en":"Maillart solved a basic engineering problem with reinforced concrete.","zh":"Maillart 用鋼筋混凝土解決了一個基本工程難題。"},{"en":"A basic engineering problem is a fundamental practical difficulty engineers must solve.","zh":"basic engineering problem 是工程師必須解決的根本實際困難。"},{"en":"Keeping a school roof strong during heavy rain is a basic engineering problem.","zh":"在暴雨中保持學校屋頂堅固，就是一個基本工程難題。"},{"en":"If a design cannot solve the basic engineering problem, it may look good but fail in use.","zh":"如果設計不能解決基本工程難題，它可能外觀好看但使用上失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a core technical challenge, not a small decorative issue.","zh":"這個短語指核心技術挑戰，而不是小小裝飾問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"support enormous weights","meaning":"支撐巨大重量","examples":[{"en":"A bridge must support enormous weights safely.","zh":"橋樑必須安全地支撐巨大重量。"},{"en":"To support enormous weights means to hold very heavy loads without collapsing.","zh":"support enormous weights 指承托非常重的負荷而不倒塌。"},{"en":"A warehouse floor must support enormous weights if heavy machines are stored there.","zh":"如果倉庫存放重型機器，地板必須支撐巨大重量。"},{"en":"If a structure cannot support enormous weights, people and vehicles may be in danger.","zh":"如果結構不能支撐巨大重量，人和車輛可能有危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a structure’s ability to carry heavy loads.","zh":"這個短語描述結構承載重物的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a slender arch","meaning":"纖幼拱形結構","examples":[{"en":"Maillart showed how a slender arch could support heavy loads.","zh":"Maillart 展示了纖幼拱形結構如何能支撐重負荷。"},{"en":"A slender arch is a thin, graceful curved structure that still has strength.","zh":"slender arch 是纖薄、優雅而仍具強度的弧形結構。"},{"en":"A modern footbridge may use a slender arch to look light while staying safe.","zh":"現代行人橋可能使用纖幼拱形結構，使外觀看來輕盈但仍安全。"},{"en":"If a slender arch is well designed, it can reduce material while carrying the necessary load.","zh":"如果纖幼拱形結構設計良好，就能減少材料而承載所需負荷。"},{"en":"The phrase combines visual lightness with structural function.","zh":"這個短語結合視覺輕盈感和結構功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"railway bridges","meaning":"鐵路橋","examples":[{"en":"Railway bridges were the great structural symbols of the 19th century.","zh":"鐵路橋是十九世紀偉大的結構象徵。"},{"en":"Railway bridges are bridges designed for trains and railway tracks.","zh":"railway bridges 是為火車和鐵路軌道而設計的橋樑。"},{"en":"A railway bridge must be strong enough to carry heavy trains at regular intervals.","zh":"鐵路橋必須足夠堅固，以定期承載重型火車。"},{"en":"Railway bridges became important because rail transport connected cities and industries.","zh":"鐵路橋變得重要，因為鐵路交通連接城市和工業。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to bridges built mainly for trains, not ordinary road traffic.","zh":"這個短語指主要為火車而建的橋樑，不是普通道路交通橋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"structural symbols","meaning":"結構象徵","examples":[{"en":"Railway bridges became structural symbols of the 19th century.","zh":"鐵路橋成為十九世紀的結構象徵。"},{"en":"Structural symbols are buildings or engineering works that represent an age, idea or technology.","zh":"structural symbols 是代表某時代、想法或科技的建築或工程作品。"},{"en":"A tall glass tower may become a structural symbol of a city’s financial growth.","zh":"高大的玻璃塔可能成為一座城市金融增長的結構象徵。"},{"en":"A structure becomes symbolic when people connect it with progress or power.","zh":"當人們把某結構與進步或力量連繫起來，它就成為象徵。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical structures that carry wider meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述承載更廣泛意義的實體結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"highway bridges","meaning":"公路橋","examples":[{"en":"Highway bridges became engineering emblems of the 20th century.","zh":"公路橋成為二十世紀的工程象徵。"},{"en":"Highway bridges are bridges designed to carry road traffic such as cars, buses and trucks.","zh":"highway bridges 是為承載汽車、巴士和貨車等道路交通而設計的橋樑。"},{"en":"A highway bridge can help commuters cross a river without entering city streets.","zh":"公路橋可以幫助通勤者不用進入市區街道也能跨過河流。"},{"en":"As car use increased, highway bridges became essential for connecting road networks.","zh":"隨着汽車使用增加，公路橋成為連接道路網絡的必要設施。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to road bridges rather than railway bridges.","zh":"這個短語指道路橋，而不是鐵路橋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"engineering emblems","meaning":"工程象徵","examples":[{"en":"Highway bridges were engineering emblems of the 20th century.","zh":"公路橋是二十世紀的工程象徵。"},{"en":"Engineering emblems are works that visibly represent engineering achievement.","zh":"engineering emblems 是明顯代表工程成就的作品。"},{"en":"A long tunnel under a harbour can be an engineering emblem of a modern city.","zh":"海港下的長隧道可以是一座現代城市的工程象徵。"},{"en":"Such emblems often show what technology allowed people to build at that time.","zh":"這類象徵常顯示當時科技讓人能建造甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes structures that stand for engineering progress.","zh":"這個短語描述象徵工程進步的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the invention of the automobile","meaning":"汽車的發明","examples":[{"en":"The invention of the automobile created demand for new roads and bridges.","zh":"汽車的發明產生了對新道路和橋樑的需求。"},{"en":"The invention of the automobile refers to the development of the motor car.","zh":"invention of the automobile 指汽車這種交通工具的發展。"},{"en":"The invention of the automobile changed daily travel because people could move farther and faster.","zh":"汽車的發明改變了日常出行，因為人們可以走得更遠更快。"},{"en":"New transport inventions often create demand for new infrastructure.","zh":"新交通發明常會產生對新基建的需求。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a technological change that reshaped road design.","zh":"這個短語指出一項重塑道路設計的科技變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"create an irresistible demand for","meaning":"產生對……無法抗拒的需求","examples":[{"en":"The automobile created an irresistible demand for paved roads.","zh":"汽車產生了對鋪砌道路無法抗拒的需求。"},{"en":"To create an irresistible demand for something means to make people need it so strongly that it cannot be ignored.","zh":"create an irresistible demand for 某物，指令人對它有強烈到不能忽視的需要。"},{"en":"Online shopping created an irresistible demand for faster delivery services.","zh":"網上購物產生了對更快送貨服務無法抗拒的需求。"},{"en":"When a new habit spreads widely, it can force cities and businesses to adapt.","zh":"當新習慣廣泛流行，它可以迫使城市和企業適應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes powerful demand caused by a major change.","zh":"這個短語描述由重大改變造成的強大需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"paved roads","meaning":"鋪砌道路","examples":[{"en":"The developed world needed more paved roads for automobiles.","zh":"已發展世界需要更多供汽車使用的鋪砌道路。"},{"en":"Paved roads are roads covered with hard material such as asphalt or concrete.","zh":"paved roads 是覆蓋瀝青或混凝土等堅硬材料的道路。"},{"en":"Buses and cars travel more safely on paved roads than on muddy tracks.","zh":"巴士和汽車在鋪砌道路上行駛，比在泥路上更安全。"},{"en":"Paved roads support regular transport because they are smoother and more durable.","zh":"鋪砌道路因較平滑和耐用而支援定期交通。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to properly surfaced roads suitable for vehicles.","zh":"這個短語指適合車輛使用的正式鋪面道路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"vehicular bridges","meaning":"車輛通行橋樑","examples":[{"en":"The spread of cars increased the need for vehicular bridges.","zh":"汽車普及增加了對車輛通行橋樑的需要。"},{"en":"Vehicular bridges are bridges designed for vehicles such as cars, buses and trucks.","zh":"vehicular bridges 是為汽車、巴士和貨車等車輛而設計的橋樑。"},{"en":"A city may build vehicular bridges to reduce traffic around a busy ferry crossing.","zh":"城市可能建造車輛通行橋樑，以減少繁忙渡口附近的交通。"},{"en":"More vehicles create more need for bridges that can handle road traffic safely.","zh":"車輛越多，越需要能安全處理道路交通的橋樑。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to bridges for vehicles rather than pedestrians or trains.","zh":"這個短語指供車輛使用的橋樑，而不是行人橋或鐵路橋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"throughout the developed world","meaning":"遍及已發展世界","examples":[{"en":"Paved roads and bridges were needed throughout the developed world.","zh":"鋪砌道路和橋樑遍及已發展世界都被需要。"},{"en":"Throughout the developed world means across industrialised or economically advanced countries.","zh":"throughout the developed world 指橫跨工業化或經濟較先進國家。"},{"en":"Public libraries are found throughout the developed world, although their services differ.","zh":"公共圖書館遍及已發展世界，雖然服務各有不同。"},{"en":"When a technology spreads through developed countries, supporting infrastructure often spreads with it.","zh":"當一種科技在已發展國家中擴散，支援基建通常也會一同擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a wide pattern across wealthy modern societies.","zh":"這個短語描述富裕現代社會中的廣泛模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fundamentally different from","meaning":"與……根本不同","examples":[{"en":"Highway bridges are fundamentally different from railway bridges.","zh":"公路橋與鐵路橋根本不同。"},{"en":"Fundamentally different from means different in basic nature, not just in small details.","zh":"fundamentally different from 指在基本性質上不同，而不只是小細節不同。"},{"en":"Learning a language is fundamentally different from memorising a list of random words.","zh":"學習一種語言與背誦隨機詞表根本不同。"},{"en":"When two things are fundamentally different, they may need different designs or methods.","zh":"當兩件事根本不同，它們可能需要不同設計或方法。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses deep, basic contrast.","zh":"這個短語強調深層、基本的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"locomotives","meaning":"火車頭","examples":[{"en":"Railway bridges must support heavy locomotives.","zh":"鐵路橋必須支撐沉重火車頭。"},{"en":"Locomotives are train engines that pull or push railway carriages.","zh":"locomotives 是拉動或推動鐵路車廂的火車引擎。"},{"en":"A locomotive is much heavier than an ordinary car, so railway bridges must be very strong.","zh":"火車頭比普通汽車重得多，所以鐵路橋必須非常堅固。"},{"en":"Heavy locomotives create large loads that affect bridge design.","zh":"沉重火車頭產生巨大負荷，會影響橋樑設計。"},{"en":"The word refers to the powerful engine part of a train.","zh":"這個詞指火車中有強大動力的引擎部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"carry lighter loads","meaning":"承載較輕負荷","examples":[{"en":"Most highway bridges carry lighter loads than railway bridges.","zh":"大多數公路橋比鐵路橋承載較輕負荷。"},{"en":"To carry lighter loads means to support less weight than another structure.","zh":"carry lighter loads 指比另一結構承托較少重量。"},{"en":"A small bookshelf carries lighter loads than a warehouse storage rack.","zh":"小書架比倉庫貨架承載較輕負荷。"},{"en":"If a bridge carries lighter loads, its design can sometimes be thinner or more flexible.","zh":"如果橋樑承載較輕負荷，其設計有時可以更薄或更靈活。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the amount of weight a structure must support.","zh":"這個短語比較結構必須支撐的重量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sharply curved","meaning":"急彎的","examples":[{"en":"Highway roadways can be sharply curved.","zh":"公路行車道可以是急彎的。"},{"en":"Sharply curved means bending strongly rather than gently.","zh":"sharply curved 指大幅彎曲，而不是輕微彎曲。"},{"en":"A mountain road may be sharply curved, so drivers must slow down.","zh":"山路可能是急彎的，所以司機必須減速。"},{"en":"Sharp curves create design challenges because vehicles need safe turning space.","zh":"急彎造成設計挑戰，因為車輛需要安全轉彎空間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong bend in a road or shape.","zh":"這個短語描述道路或形狀的強烈彎曲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"steeply sloping","meaning":"陡斜的","examples":[{"en":"Some roadways are steeply sloping.","zh":"有些行車道是陡斜的。"},{"en":"Steeply sloping means rising or falling at a sharp angle.","zh":"steeply sloping 指以很大的角度上升或下降。"},{"en":"A steeply sloping driveway can be difficult for elderly people to walk up.","zh":"陡斜的車道可能令長者難以走上去。"},{"en":"Steep slopes affect drainage, safety and vehicle control.","zh":"陡坡會影響排水、安全和車輛控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a surface that is strongly inclined.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈傾斜的表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"meet these needs","meaning":"滿足這些需要","examples":[{"en":"Bridge designers used reinforced concrete to meet these needs.","zh":"橋樑設計師使用鋼筋混凝土來滿足這些需要。"},{"en":"To meet these needs means to satisfy the requirements of a situation.","zh":"meet these needs 指滿足某情況的要求。"},{"en":"A school may hire more counsellors to meet students’ mental-health needs.","zh":"學校可能聘請更多輔導員，以滿足學生心理健康需要。"},{"en":"If old methods cannot meet new needs, designers must find better solutions.","zh":"如果舊方法不能滿足新需要，設計師必須尋找更好方案。"},{"en":"The phrase links a solution with the demands it answers.","zh":"這個短語把解決方案與它回應的需求連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"turn-of-the-century bridge designers","meaning":"世紀之交的橋樑設計師","examples":[{"en":"Turn-of-the-century bridge designers began using reinforced concrete.","zh":"世紀之交的橋樑設計師開始使用鋼筋混凝土。"},{"en":"Turn-of-the-century bridge designers were bridge designers working around the end of one century and the beginning of the next.","zh":"turn-of-the-century bridge designers 是在一個世紀末和下一個世紀初左右工作的橋樑設計師。"},{"en":"Turn-of-the-century architects often experimented with new materials and styles.","zh":"世紀之交的建築師常嘗試新材料和風格。"},{"en":"Designers at such a time may face both old traditions and new technologies.","zh":"在這樣的時期，設計師可能同時面對舊傳統和新科技。"},{"en":"The phrase places bridge designers in a historical transition period.","zh":"這個短語把橋樑設計師放在歷史過渡時期中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"building material","meaning":"建築材料","examples":[{"en":"Reinforced concrete was a new building material.","zh":"鋼筋混凝土是一種新建築材料。"},{"en":"A building material is a substance used to construct buildings or structures.","zh":"building material 是用來建造建築物或結構的物質。"},{"en":"Wood, steel, brick and concrete are common building materials.","zh":"木材、鋼、磚和混凝土都是常見建築材料。"},{"en":"New building materials can change what architects and engineers are able to design.","zh":"新建築材料可以改變建築師和工程師能設計的東西。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the physical substance used in construction.","zh":"這個短語指建造中使用的實體物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reinforced concrete","meaning":"鋼筋混凝土","examples":[{"en":"Maillart became a master of reinforced concrete.","zh":"Maillart 成為鋼筋混凝土的大師。"},{"en":"Reinforced concrete is concrete strengthened with steel bars or similar reinforcement.","zh":"reinforced concrete 是用鋼筋或類似加強物強化的混凝土。"},{"en":"Many schools, bridges and apartment blocks use reinforced concrete because it is strong and durable.","zh":"許多學校、橋樑和住宅大廈使用鋼筋混凝土，因為它堅固耐用。"},{"en":"Steel helps resist pulling forces, while concrete helps resist compression.","zh":"鋼筋幫助抵抗拉力，而混凝土幫助抵抗壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major modern construction material.","zh":"這個短語指出一種重要現代建築材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"steel bars embedded in","meaning":"嵌入……的鋼筋","examples":[{"en":"Reinforced concrete has steel bars embedded in it.","zh":"鋼筋混凝土中有嵌入其中的鋼筋。"},{"en":"Steel bars embedded in concrete are metal rods placed inside concrete to strengthen it.","zh":"steel bars embedded in concrete 是放在混凝土內部以加強它的金屬棒。"},{"en":"A building column may have steel bars embedded in it before concrete is poured.","zh":"建築柱在澆灌混凝土前，可能已有鋼筋嵌入其中。"},{"en":"Embedded steel helps the structure carry forces that plain concrete cannot handle well.","zh":"嵌入的鋼筋幫助結構承受普通混凝土難以處理的力量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reinforcement hidden inside a material.","zh":"這個短語描述隱藏在材料內部的加固物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the master of","meaning":"……的大師","examples":[{"en":"Maillart was the master of this new material.","zh":"Maillart 是這種新材料的大師。"},{"en":"The master of something is someone extremely skilled at using or understanding it.","zh":"master of 某物，是非常擅長使用或理解它的人。"},{"en":"A chef may be called the master of noodles if she can create many dishes from simple dough.","zh":"如果廚師能用簡單麵團做出多種菜式，她可被稱為麵條大師。"},{"en":"A master knows not only the rules but also how to use them creatively.","zh":"大師不只知道規則，也懂得創造性地運用規則。"},{"en":"The phrase praises exceptional skill in a field or material.","zh":"這個短語稱讚在某領域或材料上的卓越技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"structural engineer","meaning":"結構工程師","examples":[{"en":"Robert Maillart was a Swiss structural engineer.","zh":"Robert Maillart 是一位瑞士結構工程師。"},{"en":"A structural engineer designs structures so they can safely carry loads and resist forces.","zh":"structural engineer 設計結構，使其能安全承載負荷並抵抗力量。"},{"en":"A structural engineer checks whether a school building can withstand strong wind or heavy use.","zh":"結構工程師會檢查學校建築是否能承受強風或大量使用。"},{"en":"Without structural engineers, bridges and buildings may look attractive but be unsafe.","zh":"沒有結構工程師，橋樑和建築可能外觀吸引但不安全。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an engineer who focuses on strength, stability and safety.","zh":"這個短語指專注於強度、穩定性和安全的工程師。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"early in his career","meaning":"在事業早期","examples":[{"en":"Early in his career, Maillart developed a unique design method.","zh":"在事業早期，Maillart 發展出一種獨特設計方法。"},{"en":"Early in his career means during the first stage of his working life.","zh":"early in his career 指在他工作生涯的初期階段。"},{"en":"Early in her career, a teacher may experiment with different classroom methods.","zh":"在事業早期，老師可能嘗試不同課室方法。"},{"en":"Achievements made early can shape a person’s later professional direction.","zh":"早期取得的成就可以塑造一個人後來的專業方向。"},{"en":"The phrase places an event near the beginning of someone’s career.","zh":"這個短語把事件放在某人事業開始附近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"develop a unique method for","meaning":"發展出……的獨特方法","examples":[{"en":"Maillart developed a unique method for designing concrete structures.","zh":"Maillart 發展出設計混凝土結構的獨特方法。"},{"en":"To develop a unique method for something means to create a special way of doing it.","zh":"develop a unique method for 某事，指創造一種特別的做法。"},{"en":"A teacher may develop a unique method for helping weak students remember grammar.","zh":"老師可能發展出幫助弱學生記住文法的獨特方法。"},{"en":"Unique methods often appear when ordinary methods cannot solve a problem well.","zh":"當普通方法不能妥善解決問題時，獨特方法常會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating a distinctive approach.","zh":"這個短語描述創造具特色的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"concrete structures","meaning":"混凝土結構","examples":[{"en":"Maillart designed bridges, buildings and other concrete structures.","zh":"Maillart 設計橋樑、建築物和其他混凝土結構。"},{"en":"Concrete structures are buildings or engineering works made mainly from concrete.","zh":"concrete structures 是主要由混凝土建造的建築物或工程作品。"},{"en":"Car parks, water tanks and apartment blocks can all be concrete structures.","zh":"停車場、水箱和住宅大廈都可以是混凝土結構。"},{"en":"Concrete structures are common because concrete can be shaped and made strong.","zh":"混凝土結構很常見，因為混凝土可塑形並做得堅固。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to structures built using concrete as a main material.","zh":"這個短語指以混凝土為主要材料建造的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reject the analysis of","meaning":"拒絕採用對……的分析","examples":[{"en":"He rejected the complex mathematical analysis of loads and stresses.","zh":"他拒絕採用對負荷與應力的複雜數學分析。"},{"en":"To reject the analysis of something means to decide not to use or accept that kind of examination.","zh":"reject the analysis of 某事，指決定不使用或不接受那種檢視方式。"},{"en":"A manager may reject the analysis of sales figures if the data are incomplete.","zh":"如果數據不完整，經理可能拒絕採用銷售數字分析。"},{"en":"Rejecting an approach can lead someone to develop a different method.","zh":"拒絕一種方法可以促使某人發展另一種方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes refusing a particular way of studying a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述拒絕某種研究問題的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"complex mathematical analysis","meaning":"複雜數學分析","examples":[{"en":"Many engineers used complex mathematical analysis.","zh":"許多工程師使用複雜數學分析。"},{"en":"Complex mathematical analysis is detailed calculation using advanced mathematical methods.","zh":"complex mathematical analysis 是使用高階數學方法進行詳細計算。"},{"en":"Engineers may use complex mathematical analysis to test whether a roof can support heavy equipment.","zh":"工程師可能使用複雜數學分析，測試屋頂能否支撐重型設備。"},{"en":"Such analysis can improve safety, but it may also become difficult for non-specialists to understand.","zh":"這類分析可以提升安全，但也可能令非專家難以理解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes technical calculation rather than simple guessing.","zh":"這個短語描述技術性計算，而不是簡單猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"loads and stresses","meaning":"負荷與應力","examples":[{"en":"Engineers study loads and stresses when designing bridges.","zh":"工程師設計橋樑時會研究負荷與應力。"},{"en":"Loads and stresses are the weights and internal forces that a structure must handle.","zh":"loads and stresses 是結構必須承受的重量和內部力量。"},{"en":"A shelf must handle the load of books and the stress created by bending.","zh":"書架必須承受書本的負荷和彎曲造成的應力。"},{"en":"If loads and stresses are misjudged, a structure may crack, bend or collapse.","zh":"如果負荷與應力判斷錯誤，結構可能裂開、彎曲或倒塌。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to forces that affect structural safety.","zh":"這個短語指影響結構安全的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be enthusiastically adopted by","meaning":"被……熱烈採用","examples":[{"en":"Mathematical analysis was enthusiastically adopted by Maillart’s contemporaries.","zh":"數學分析被 Maillart 的同時代人熱烈採用。"},{"en":"To be enthusiastically adopted by people means to be accepted and used by them with strong approval.","zh":"be enthusiastically adopted by 某些人，指被他們熱烈認同並使用。"},{"en":"Online homework platforms were enthusiastically adopted by some schools during remote learning.","zh":"在遙距學習期間，網上功課平台被一些學校熱烈採用。"},{"en":"When a method seems modern and useful, professionals may quickly adopt it.","zh":"當一種方法看起來現代且有用，專業人士可能迅速採用它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes eager acceptance of an idea or method.","zh":"這個短語描述對想法或方法的熱切接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"contemporaries","meaning":"同時代的人","examples":[{"en":"Most of Maillart’s contemporaries preferred mathematical analysis.","zh":"Maillart 的大多數同時代人較喜歡數學分析。"},{"en":"Contemporaries are people who live or work during the same period.","zh":"contemporaries 是生活或工作於同一時期的人。"},{"en":"A writer’s contemporaries may include other authors publishing at the same time.","zh":"一位作家的同時代人可能包括同時期出版作品的其他作者。"},{"en":"Comparing someone with contemporaries shows whether they followed or challenged their age.","zh":"把某人與同時代人比較，可以顯示他是跟隨還是挑戰其時代。"},{"en":"The word refers to people from the same historical period.","zh":"這個詞指同一歷史時期的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"同時","examples":[{"en":"At the same time, Maillart avoided unnecessary decoration.","zh":"同時，Maillart 避免不必要的裝飾。"},{"en":"At the same time means meanwhile or simultaneously, often adding another related point.","zh":"at the same time 指同時或與此同時，常加入另一相關點。"},{"en":"A student can work hard and, at the same time, protect enough rest.","zh":"學生可以努力學習，同時保留足夠休息。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show that two things happened together or were both true.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示兩件事同時發生或同時成立。"},{"en":"It is useful for adding a second point without changing the topic completely.","zh":"它適合加入第二點，而不完全轉換主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"eschew","meaning":"避免；摒棄","examples":[{"en":"Maillart eschewed the decorative approach used by many bridge builders.","zh":"Maillart 摒棄了許多橋樑建造者使用的裝飾性做法。"},{"en":"To eschew something means to deliberately avoid or reject it.","zh":"eschew 某事，指有意避免或拒絕它。"},{"en":"A student may eschew memorising model answers and focus on understanding instead.","zh":"學生可能摒棄背誦範文答案，轉而專注理解。"},{"en":"People eschew a method when they believe it is unnecessary, harmful or unsuitable.","zh":"當人們認為某方法不必要、有害或不合適，就會摒棄它。"},{"en":"The word is formal and means to avoid by choice.","zh":"這個詞較正式，意思是有選擇地避免。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"decorative approach","meaning":"裝飾性做法","examples":[{"en":"Many bridge builders took a decorative approach.","zh":"許多橋樑建造者採用裝飾性做法。"},{"en":"A decorative approach focuses on adding visual features mainly for appearance.","zh":"decorative approach 重點在加入主要為外觀而設的視覺特徵。"},{"en":"A shop may take a decorative approach by adding lights and patterns to attract customers.","zh":"商店可能透過加入燈飾和圖案來吸引顧客，採用裝飾性做法。"},{"en":"If decoration does not support function, it may increase cost without improving use.","zh":"如果裝飾不支援功能，它可能增加成本而不改善使用。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts surface ornament with structural necessity.","zh":"這個短語把表面裝飾與結構必要性作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"bridge builders of his time","meaning":"他那個時代的橋樑建造者","examples":[{"en":"Maillart differed from many bridge builders of his time.","zh":"Maillart 與他那個時代的許多橋樑建造者不同。"},{"en":"Bridge builders of his time are the engineers and builders working in the same historical period.","zh":"bridge builders of his time 是與他同一歷史時期工作的工程師和建造者。"},{"en":"A designer may seem unusual when compared with builders of his time.","zh":"與他那個時代的建造者相比，設計師可能顯得不尋常。"},{"en":"This comparison helps readers see how original Maillart’s methods were.","zh":"這種比較幫助讀者看出 Maillart 的方法有多原創。"},{"en":"The phrase places people within the professional habits of a period.","zh":"這個短語把人物放在某時期的專業習慣中理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"resist imitating","meaning":"抗拒模仿","examples":[{"en":"He resisted imitating architectural styles.","zh":"他抗拒模仿建築風格。"},{"en":"To resist imitating something means to avoid copying it even when others do so.","zh":"resist imitating 某事，指即使其他人這樣做，也避免複製它。"},{"en":"A student may resist imitating a classmate’s essay style and develop her own voice.","zh":"學生可能抗拒模仿同學的文章風格，發展自己的聲音。"},{"en":"Resisting imitation can lead to more original work.","zh":"抗拒模仿可以帶來更原創的作品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes choosing independence instead of copying.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇獨立而不是抄襲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"architectural styles","meaning":"建築風格","examples":[{"en":"Maillart did not simply copy architectural styles.","zh":"Maillart 並沒有單純複製建築風格。"},{"en":"Architectural styles are recognisable ways of designing buildings or structures.","zh":"architectural styles 是可辨認的建築物或結構設計方式。"},{"en":"Gothic, modernist and classical designs are examples of architectural styles.","zh":"哥德式、現代主義和古典設計都是建築風格例子。"},{"en":"Copying a style may make a building look familiar, but it may not solve the real design problem.","zh":"複製風格可能令建築看起來熟悉，但未必解決真正設計問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to visual and design traditions in architecture.","zh":"這個短語指建築中的視覺和設計傳統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"design elements","meaning":"設計元素","examples":[{"en":"He avoided adding design elements purely for decoration.","zh":"他避免加入純粹為裝飾而設的設計元素。"},{"en":"Design elements are parts of a design, such as shape, colour, lines or structural details.","zh":"design elements 是設計中的部分，例如形狀、顏色、線條或結構細節。"},{"en":"A poster’s design elements may include headings, images and spacing.","zh":"海報的設計元素可能包括標題、圖片和留白。"},{"en":"Good design elements should help function, meaning or appearance.","zh":"好的設計元素應有助功能、意義或外觀。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the individual features that make up a design.","zh":"這個短語指構成設計的個別特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"solely for ornamentation","meaning":"純粹為了裝飾","examples":[{"en":"Maillart rejected details added solely for ornamentation.","zh":"Maillart 拒絕純粹為了裝飾而加入的細節。"},{"en":"Solely for ornamentation means only for decoration, not for function.","zh":"solely for ornamentation 指只為裝飾，而不是為功能。"},{"en":"A fake button on a jacket may exist solely for ornamentation.","zh":"外套上的假鈕扣可能純粹為了裝飾而存在。"},{"en":"Features added only for ornamentation can raise cost without improving performance.","zh":"只為裝飾而加入的特徵可能增加成本而不改善性能。"},{"en":"The phrase makes the contrast between decoration and practical purpose clear.","zh":"這個短語清楚對比裝飾與實際目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"creative intuition","meaning":"創造性直覺","examples":[{"en":"Maillart’s method was a form of creative intuition.","zh":"Maillart 的方法是一種創造性直覺。"},{"en":"Creative intuition is the ability to sense a good new solution without relying only on formal calculation.","zh":"creative intuition 是不只依靠正式計算，也能感覺出好新方案的能力。"},{"en":"A teacher may use creative intuition to explain grammar with an unexpected but clear example.","zh":"老師可能用創造性直覺，以意想不到但清楚的例子解釋文法。"},{"en":"Intuition becomes powerful when it is supported by experience and practical understanding.","zh":"當直覺由經驗和實際理解支持，它就會變得有力量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes imaginative judgement rather than random guessing.","zh":"這個短語描述有想像力的判斷，而不是隨機猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have a knack for","meaning":"有……的天分","examples":[{"en":"Maillart had a knack for conceiving new shapes.","zh":"Maillart 有構思新形狀的天分。"},{"en":"To have a knack for something means to have a natural or special ability to do it well.","zh":"have a knack for 某事，指有自然或特別能力把它做好。"},{"en":"A student may have a knack for explaining difficult ideas in simple words.","zh":"學生可能有用簡單詞語解釋困難想法的天分。"},{"en":"People with a knack often solve problems faster because they notice useful patterns.","zh":"有天分的人常因注意到有用模式而更快解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a talent that feels natural.","zh":"這個短語描述看起來自然的才能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"conceive new shapes","meaning":"構思新形狀","examples":[{"en":"He could conceive new shapes to solve engineering problems.","zh":"他能構思新形狀來解決工程問題。"},{"en":"To conceive new shapes means to imagine and design forms that did not exist before.","zh":"conceive new shapes 指想像並設計以前不存在的形態。"},{"en":"A product designer may conceive new shapes for a chair that is lighter and more comfortable.","zh":"產品設計師可能為椅子構思新形狀，使它更輕、更舒適。"},{"en":"New shapes can solve old problems when they distribute force or space differently.","zh":"當新形狀以不同方式分布力量或空間，它們可以解決舊問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creative design thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述創造性的設計思維。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"classic engineering problems","meaning":"經典工程難題","examples":[{"en":"Maillart used new forms to solve classic engineering problems.","zh":"Maillart 使用新形式來解決經典工程難題。"},{"en":"Classic engineering problems are long-standing technical challenges that many engineers face.","zh":"classic engineering problems 是許多工程師面對的長期技術挑戰。"},{"en":"Keeping a bridge strong while reducing material is a classic engineering problem.","zh":"在減少材料的同時保持橋樑堅固，就是經典工程難題。"},{"en":"Classic problems remain important because every generation must solve them with available technology.","zh":"經典問題仍然重要，因為每一代都要用當時可用科技解決它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes familiar but difficult challenges in engineering.","zh":"這個短語描述工程中熟悉但困難的挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a highly competitive field","meaning":"競爭激烈的領域","examples":[{"en":"Maillart worked in a highly competitive field.","zh":"Maillart 在一個競爭激烈的領域工作。"},{"en":"A highly competitive field is an area of work where many skilled people compete for success.","zh":"highly competitive field 是許多有能力的人爭取成功的工作範疇。"},{"en":"University admissions can be a highly competitive field when many students apply for few places.","zh":"當許多學生申請少量學額，大學入學可以是競爭激烈的領域。"},{"en":"In competitive fields, lower cost, stronger ideas or better quality can make a proposal win.","zh":"在競爭激烈的領域中，較低成本、更強想法或更好質素可以令方案勝出。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a professional area with strong rivalry.","zh":"這個短語描述有強烈競爭的專業範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"one of his goals was","meaning":"他的目標之一是","examples":[{"en":"One of his goals was economy.","zh":"他的目標之一是節省成本。"},{"en":"One of his goals was means one important aim among several was a particular result.","zh":"one of his goals was 指幾個重要目標之一是某個結果。"},{"en":"One of her goals was to help weaker students speak more confidently.","zh":"她的目標之一是幫助較弱學生更有信心地說話。"},{"en":"A designer may have several goals, such as safety, beauty and cost control.","zh":"設計師可能有幾個目標，例如安全、美感和成本控制。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces one aim without saying it is the only aim.","zh":"這個短語引出其中一個目標，而不是說它是唯一目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"economy","meaning":"節省成本；經濟效益","examples":[{"en":"Economy was an important aim in Maillart’s bridge designs.","zh":"節省成本是 Maillart 橋樑設計中的重要目標。"},{"en":"In this context, economy means saving money and materials while still achieving the purpose.","zh":"在這個語境中，economy 指在仍達到目的的同時節省金錢和材料。"},{"en":"A school renovation shows economy if it improves classrooms without wasting funds.","zh":"如果學校翻新改善課室而不浪費資金，就是有經濟效益。"},{"en":"Economy in design can make a project more likely to be approved.","zh":"設計上的節省成本可以令項目更可能獲批。"},{"en":"The word here means cost-effectiveness, not a country’s financial system.","zh":"這個詞在這裏指成本效益，而不是一個國家的經濟系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"design and construction contracts","meaning":"設計及建造合約","examples":[{"en":"Maillart won design and construction contracts with economical proposals.","zh":"Maillart 以經濟實惠的方案贏得設計及建造合約。"},{"en":"Design and construction contracts are agreements to plan and build a structure.","zh":"design and construction contracts 是規劃和建造結構的協議。"},{"en":"A company may win design and construction contracts for a new school hall.","zh":"公司可能贏得新學校禮堂的設計及建造合約。"},{"en":"Contractors often win such contracts by offering safe designs at reasonable prices.","zh":"承包商常透過提供安全且價格合理的設計贏得這類合約。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to formal work agreements covering both planning and building.","zh":"這個短語指涵蓋規劃和建造的正式工作協議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"reasonably priced","meaning":"價格合理的","examples":[{"en":"His structures were reasonably priced.","zh":"他的結構價格合理。"},{"en":"Reasonably priced means costing a fair amount, not too expensive for what is offered.","zh":"reasonably priced 指價格公平，就所提供內容而言不太昂貴。"},{"en":"A reasonably priced lunch is affordable but still filling and healthy.","zh":"價格合理的午餐是負擔得起，同時仍飽肚和健康。"},{"en":"If a design is reasonably priced, clients may choose it over a more expensive alternative.","zh":"如果設計價格合理，客戶可能選它而非更昂貴的替代方案。"},{"en":"The phrase describes good value rather than the cheapest possible price.","zh":"這個短語描述物有所值，而不是最便宜的價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"less costly than","meaning":"比……成本較低","examples":[{"en":"His proposals were often less costly than his rivals’ proposals.","zh":"他的方案常比競爭對手的方案成本較低。"},{"en":"Less costly than means cheaper than another option.","zh":"less costly than 指比另一選項便宜。"},{"en":"Taking the bus is often less costly than taking a taxi every day.","zh":"每天乘巴士通常比每天乘的士成本較低。"},{"en":"A less costly plan may win support if it still meets safety and quality needs.","zh":"如果較低成本的計劃仍符合安全和質素需要，它可能獲得支持。"},{"en":"The phrase compares options by cost.","zh":"這個短語按成本比較選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rivals’ proposals","meaning":"競爭對手的方案","examples":[{"en":"Maillart’s designs were cheaper than his rivals’ proposals.","zh":"Maillart 的設計比競爭對手的方案便宜。"},{"en":"Rivals’ proposals are plans submitted by competing people or companies.","zh":"rivals’ proposals 是由競爭者或競爭公司提交的計劃。"},{"en":"In a school design competition, one team compares its plan with its rivals’ proposals.","zh":"在學校設計比賽中，一隊會把自己的計劃與競爭對手的方案比較。"},{"en":"A proposal may win if it is safer, clearer or less expensive than rivals’ proposals.","zh":"如果方案比競爭對手的方案更安全、更清楚或更便宜，就可能勝出。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to competing plans.","zh":"這個短語指互相競爭的計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"first important bridge","meaning":"第一座重要橋樑","examples":[{"en":"Maillart’s first important bridge was built in Zuoz.","zh":"Maillart 的第一座重要橋樑建於 Zuoz。"},{"en":"A first important bridge is the earliest bridge in someone’s career that gains real significance.","zh":"first important bridge 是某人事業中最早具有真正重要性的橋樑。"},{"en":"A young architect’s first important building may bring attention from future clients.","zh":"年輕建築師的第一座重要建築可能帶來未來客戶的關注。"},{"en":"Early major projects can shape a designer’s reputation.","zh":"早期重大項目可以塑造設計師的聲譽。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the beginning of a person’s important professional achievements.","zh":"這個短語標記某人重要專業成就的開端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"local officials","meaning":"地方官員","examples":[{"en":"Local officials initially wanted a steel bridge.","zh":"地方官員最初想要一座鋼橋。"},{"en":"Local officials are people who hold authority in a town, district or local government.","zh":"local officials 是在城鎮、地區或地方政府中擁有權力的人。"},{"en":"Local officials may decide whether a new school road or bridge should be built.","zh":"地方官員可能決定是否興建新的學校道路或橋樑。"},{"en":"Their preferences can influence which design is approved.","zh":"他們的偏好可以影響哪個設計獲批。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to decision-makers at the local government level.","zh":"這個短語指地方政府層面的決策者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"initially wanted","meaning":"最初想要","examples":[{"en":"The officials initially wanted a steel bridge.","zh":"官員最初想要一座鋼橋。"},{"en":"Initially wanted means first wanted before later discussion or change.","zh":"initially wanted 指在後來討論或改變前最初想要。"},{"en":"A student may initially want to study medicine but later choose engineering.","zh":"學生可能最初想讀醫科，但後來選擇工程。"},{"en":"Initial preferences can change when people hear better arguments or see new evidence.","zh":"當人們聽到更好論據或看見新證據，最初偏好可以改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes someone’s first choice.","zh":"這個短語描述某人的第一選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"steel bridge","meaning":"鋼橋","examples":[{"en":"The town had first considered building a steel bridge.","zh":"該城鎮最初考慮建造一座鋼橋。"},{"en":"A steel bridge is a bridge built mainly from steel.","zh":"steel bridge 是主要由鋼建造的橋樑。"},{"en":"A railway may use a steel bridge because steel can carry heavy loads.","zh":"鐵路可能使用鋼橋，因為鋼能承載重負荷。"},{"en":"Steel bridges can be strong, but they may be more expensive or less suitable in some settings.","zh":"鋼橋可以很堅固，但在某些環境中可能較昂貴或較不合適。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a bridge by its main material.","zh":"這個短語按主要材料描述橋樑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"span the river","meaning":"跨越河流","examples":[{"en":"The bridge was designed to span the Inn River.","zh":"這座橋被設計用來跨越 Inn River。"},{"en":"To span a river means to stretch across it from one side to the other.","zh":"span a river 指由一邊延伸到另一邊，橫跨河流。"},{"en":"A footbridge can span a small river so students can walk to school safely.","zh":"行人橋可以跨越小河，讓學生安全步行上學。"},{"en":"Spanning a river solves a transport problem by connecting separated places.","zh":"跨越河流透過連接分隔地點來解決交通問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a bridge crossing over water.","zh":"這個短語描述橋樑橫跨水面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"argue that","meaning":"主張；認為","examples":[{"en":"Maillart argued that he could build a more elegant bridge.","zh":"Maillart 主張他能建造一座更優雅的橋。"},{"en":"To argue that something is true means to present reasons supporting that claim.","zh":"argue that 某事為真，指提出理由支持該主張。"},{"en":"A student may argue that school lunches should be healthier because concentration improves after good food.","zh":"學生可能主張學校午餐應更健康，因為良好食物能改善專注力。"},{"en":"Strong arguments use evidence, comparison or practical reasons.","zh":"有力論點會使用證據、比較或實際理由。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a position someone wants others to accept.","zh":"這個短語引出某人希望他人接受的立場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a more elegant bridge","meaning":"更優雅的橋樑","examples":[{"en":"He proposed a more elegant bridge made of reinforced concrete.","zh":"他提出一座由鋼筋混凝土製成的更優雅橋樑。"},{"en":"A more elegant bridge is a bridge that looks more graceful while still working well.","zh":"more elegant bridge 是外觀更優美而功能仍良好的橋樑。"},{"en":"A city may choose a more elegant bridge if it wants infrastructure to improve the landscape.","zh":"如果城市希望基建改善景觀，可能選擇更優雅的橋樑。"},{"en":"Elegance in bridge design often comes from simple forms and efficient use of material.","zh":"橋樑設計中的優雅常來自簡潔形式和有效使用材料。"},{"en":"The phrase combines visual beauty with engineering quality.","zh":"這個短語結合視覺美感與工程質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"for about the same cost","meaning":"成本大約相同","examples":[{"en":"He could build the bridge for about the same cost.","zh":"他可以以大約相同成本建造這座橋。"},{"en":"For about the same cost means at roughly the same price as another option.","zh":"for about the same cost 指價格與另一選項大致相同。"},{"en":"A family may buy a larger fridge for about the same cost as a smaller one during a sale.","zh":"減價期間，家庭可能以與小雪櫃大約相同的成本買到較大雪櫃。"},{"en":"If a better design costs about the same, clients have a strong reason to choose it.","zh":"如果更好的設計成本大約相同，客戶就有強理由選擇它。"},{"en":"The phrase compares price while allowing a small difference.","zh":"這個短語比較價格，同時容許小差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"crucial innovation","meaning":"關鍵創新","examples":[{"en":"Maillart’s crucial innovation was the hollow-box arch.","zh":"Maillart 的關鍵創新是空心箱形拱。"},{"en":"A crucial innovation is a new idea or design that is extremely important to success.","zh":"crucial innovation 是對成功極其重要的新想法或設計。"},{"en":"A school’s crucial innovation may be a simple system that lets teachers share lesson materials quickly.","zh":"學校的關鍵創新可能是一個讓老師快速分享教材的簡單系統。"},{"en":"Crucial innovations solve key problems and make later improvements possible.","zh":"關鍵創新解決核心問題，並使後來改良成為可能。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the most important new element.","zh":"這個短語突出最重要的新元素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"incorporate something into","meaning":"將某物併入……","examples":[{"en":"He incorporated the bridge’s arch and roadway into one form.","zh":"他將橋拱和行車道併入一個形式之中。"},{"en":"To incorporate something into something else means to include it as part of a larger whole.","zh":"incorporate something into something else 指把某物納入較大整體的一部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may incorporate games into a grammar lesson to make practice more active.","zh":"老師可能把遊戲併入文法課，使練習更主動。"},{"en":"Incorporating parts together can save space, reduce cost or create a clearer design.","zh":"把部分結合起來可以節省空間、降低成本或創造更清晰設計。"},{"en":"The phrase describes combining one element with another.","zh":"這個短語描述把一個元素與另一個結合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"roadway","meaning":"行車道","examples":[{"en":"The roadway was connected directly to the arch.","zh":"行車道直接連接到拱形結構。"},{"en":"A roadway is the part of a road or bridge where vehicles travel.","zh":"roadway 是道路或橋樑上供車輛行駛的部分。"},{"en":"Workers may close one lane of a roadway during bridge repairs.","zh":"橋樑維修期間，工人可能關閉行車道其中一條行車線。"},{"en":"The design of a roadway affects traffic flow and safety.","zh":"行車道設計影響交通流動和安全。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the vehicle-carrying surface.","zh":"這個短語指承載車輛行駛的表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a form called","meaning":"一種稱為……的形式","examples":[{"en":"He used a form called the hollow-box arch.","zh":"他使用一種稱為空心箱形拱的形式。"},{"en":"A form called something means a design or structure known by that name.","zh":"a form called 某物，指以該名稱為人所知的設計或結構。"},{"en":"A school may use a teaching form called peer review, where students comment on one another’s work.","zh":"學校可能使用一種稱為同儕評改的教學形式，讓學生評論彼此作品。"},{"en":"Naming the form helps readers recognise and discuss the design clearly.","zh":"命名該形式有助讀者清楚辨認和討論設計。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the name of a specific type or method.","zh":"這個短語引出特定類型或方法的名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hollow-box arch","meaning":"空心箱形拱","examples":[{"en":"The hollow-box arch reduced the amount of concrete needed.","zh":"空心箱形拱減少了所需混凝土數量。"},{"en":"A hollow-box arch is an arch form with empty box-like spaces built into the structure.","zh":"hollow-box arch 是結構中建有箱形空間的拱形形式。"},{"en":"A bridge using a hollow-box arch can be lighter because it avoids unnecessary solid material.","zh":"使用空心箱形拱的橋可以更輕，因為它避免不必要的實心材料。"},{"en":"The hollow spaces reduce weight while the connected surfaces still help carry loads.","zh":"空心空間減少重量，而相連表面仍有助承載負荷。"},{"en":"The phrase names Maillart’s important structural design.","zh":"這個短語指出 Maillart 的重要結構設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"substantially reduce","meaning":"大幅減少","examples":[{"en":"The new design substantially reduced the bridge’s expense.","zh":"新設計大幅減少了橋樑開支。"},{"en":"To substantially reduce something means to lower it by a large or meaningful amount.","zh":"substantially reduce 某事，指把它降低很多或降低到有意義的程度。"},{"en":"Turning off unused air conditioners can substantially reduce a school’s electricity bill.","zh":"關掉不用的冷氣可以大幅減少學校電費。"},{"en":"A design that substantially reduces cost can become attractive to clients.","zh":"能大幅降低成本的設計會對客戶變得有吸引力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a major decrease, not a tiny saving.","zh":"這個短語描述重大減少，而不是微小節省。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"minimise the amount of","meaning":"盡量減少……的數量","examples":[{"en":"The design minimised the amount of concrete needed.","zh":"該設計盡量減少所需混凝土的數量。"},{"en":"To minimise the amount of something means to reduce it as much as possible.","zh":"minimise the amount of 某物，指盡可能減少它。"},{"en":"A student may minimise the amount of paper used by submitting homework online.","zh":"學生可能透過網上交功課來盡量減少用紙量。"},{"en":"Minimising material can lower cost, reduce waste and make a design lighter.","zh":"盡量減少材料可以降低成本、減少浪費並使設計更輕。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on using as little as reasonably possible.","zh":"這個短語重點在合理地盡量少用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"concrete needed","meaning":"所需混凝土","examples":[{"en":"The hollow-box arch reduced the concrete needed for the bridge.","zh":"空心箱形拱減少了橋樑所需混凝土。"},{"en":"Concrete needed means the amount of concrete required to build something.","zh":"concrete needed 指建造某物所要求的混凝土數量。"},{"en":"A builder calculates the concrete needed before ordering materials for a floor.","zh":"建築工人在訂購地板材料前會計算所需混凝土。"},{"en":"Reducing the concrete needed can reduce cost and construction weight.","zh":"減少所需混凝土可以降低成本和建造重量。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the required quantity of concrete.","zh":"這個短語重點在混凝土所需數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"conventional arch bridge","meaning":"傳統拱橋","examples":[{"en":"A conventional arch bridge needs a relatively thick arch.","zh":"傳統拱橋需要相對厚的拱。"},{"en":"A conventional arch bridge is a traditional bridge type that uses an arch to carry loads.","zh":"conventional arch bridge 是使用拱形結構承載負荷的傳統橋樑類型。"},{"en":"Many old stone bridges are conventional arch bridges.","zh":"許多舊石橋都是傳統拱橋。"},{"en":"Conventional designs may be reliable, but they can use more material than newer designs.","zh":"傳統設計可能可靠，但會比新設計使用更多材料。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts traditional arch design with Maillart’s innovation.","zh":"這個短語把傳統拱形設計與 Maillart 的創新作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the weight of the roadway","meaning":"行車道的重量","examples":[{"en":"The weight of the roadway is transferred to the arch.","zh":"行車道的重量被傳遞到拱上。"},{"en":"The weight of the roadway means the load created by the road surface and anything it carries.","zh":"weight of the roadway 指道路表面及其所承載事物產生的負荷。"},{"en":"Engineers must calculate the weight of the roadway before designing bridge supports.","zh":"工程師設計橋樑支撐前，必須計算行車道重量。"},{"en":"If this weight is not transferred safely, the bridge may crack or fail.","zh":"如果這個重量沒有安全傳遞，橋樑可能裂開或失效。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to one major load in bridge design.","zh":"這個短語指橋樑設計中的一項主要負荷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be transferred by","meaning":"由……傳遞","examples":[{"en":"The load is transferred by columns to the arch.","zh":"負荷由柱傳遞到拱上。"},{"en":"To be transferred by something means to be carried or passed through that element.","zh":"be transferred by 某物，指由該元素承載或傳送。"},{"en":"In a building, the weight of a roof may be transferred by walls to the ground.","zh":"在建築物中，屋頂重量可能由牆傳遞到地面。"},{"en":"Safe transfer of forces is essential because loads must reach strong supporting parts.","zh":"安全傳遞力量很重要，因為負荷必須到達堅固支撐部分。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the path through which force moves.","zh":"這個短語解釋力量移動的路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"columns","meaning":"柱","examples":[{"en":"Columns transfer the weight of the roadway to the arch.","zh":"柱把行車道重量傳遞到拱上。"},{"en":"Columns are upright supports that carry loads in buildings or bridges.","zh":"columns 是建築物或橋樑中承載負荷的直立支撐物。"},{"en":"A school hall may have columns supporting the roof.","zh":"學校禮堂可能有柱支撐屋頂。"},{"en":"If columns are removed without proper design, the structure may become unsafe.","zh":"如果在沒有適當設計下移除柱，結構可能變得不安全。"},{"en":"The word refers to vertical supporting members.","zh":"這個詞指垂直支撐構件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"relatively thick","meaning":"相對厚的","examples":[{"en":"The arch in a conventional bridge must be relatively thick.","zh":"傳統橋中的拱必須相對厚。"},{"en":"Relatively thick means thick when compared with another object or design.","zh":"relatively thick 指與另一物件或設計相比較厚。"},{"en":"A winter coat is relatively thick compared with a summer shirt.","zh":"與夏天恤衫相比，冬天外套相對厚。"},{"en":"Thicker structural parts may carry more load but also use more material.","zh":"較厚的結構部分可能承載更多負荷，但也使用更多材料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes thickness through comparison.","zh":"這個短語透過比較描述厚度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be connected by","meaning":"由……連接","examples":[{"en":"The roadway and arch were connected by three vertical walls.","zh":"行車道和拱由三面垂直牆連接。"},{"en":"To be connected by something means to be joined through that part or element.","zh":"be connected by 某物，指透過該部分或元素連接起來。"},{"en":"Two school buildings may be connected by a covered walkway.","zh":"兩座學校大樓可能由有蓋通道連接。"},{"en":"Connections matter because they allow weight, people or information to move between parts.","zh":"連接很重要，因為它讓重量、人或資訊在不同部分之間移動。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what links two things together.","zh":"這個短語解釋甚麼把兩件事連在一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"vertical walls","meaning":"垂直牆","examples":[{"en":"Three vertical walls connected the roadway and arch.","zh":"三面垂直牆連接行車道和拱。"},{"en":"Vertical walls are walls standing upright, running up and down rather than sideways.","zh":"vertical walls 是直立的牆，方向上下延伸而不是橫向。"},{"en":"A classroom has vertical walls that support boards, shelves and windows.","zh":"課室有垂直牆支撐白板、架子和窗戶。"},{"en":"In a bridge, vertical walls can connect parts and help transfer loads.","zh":"在橋樑中，垂直牆可以連接部分並幫助傳遞負荷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes upright wall-like structural elements.","zh":"這個短語描述直立牆狀結構元素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"form two hollow boxes","meaning":"形成兩個空心箱","examples":[{"en":"The walls formed two hollow boxes under the roadway.","zh":"這些牆在行車道下形成兩個空心箱。"},{"en":"To form two hollow boxes means to create two empty box-like spaces inside the structure.","zh":"form two hollow boxes 指在結構內創造兩個箱形空間。"},{"en":"A cardboard divider can form two hollow boxes inside a package.","zh":"紙板隔板可以在包裹內形成兩個空心箱。"},{"en":"Hollow boxes reduce solid material while maintaining useful shape and strength.","zh":"空心箱減少實心材料，同時保持有用形狀和強度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how structural parts create empty compartments.","zh":"這個短語描述結構部分如何形成空腔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"running under","meaning":"在……下方延伸","examples":[{"en":"The hollow boxes ran under the roadway.","zh":"空心箱在行車道下方延伸。"},{"en":"Running under something means extending beneath it along its length.","zh":"running under 某物，指在其下方沿着長度延伸。"},{"en":"Water pipes may run under a school playground.","zh":"水管可能在學校操場下方延伸。"},{"en":"Parts running under a surface can support or supply it while remaining hidden.","zh":"在表面下方延伸的部分可以在隱藏狀態下支撐或供應它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes position and direction below another structure.","zh":"這個短語描述在另一結構下方的位置和方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the big advantage of","meaning":"……的一大優點","examples":[{"en":"The big advantage of the design was that the arch could be thinner.","zh":"該設計的一大優點是拱可以更薄。"},{"en":"The big advantage of something is its main or most important benefit.","zh":"big advantage of 某事，是其主要或最重要好處。"},{"en":"The big advantage of online notes is that students can update them quickly.","zh":"網上筆記的一大優點是學生可以快速更新。"},{"en":"A big advantage can make one design more attractive than another.","zh":"一大優點可以令一個設計比另一個更吸引。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the strongest positive point.","zh":"這個短語引出最強的正面重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bear the load alone","meaning":"獨自承受負荷","examples":[{"en":"The arch did not have to bear the load alone.","zh":"拱不必獨自承受負荷。"},{"en":"To bear the load alone means to carry all the weight without help from other parts.","zh":"bear the load alone 指在沒有其他部分幫助下承載全部重量。"},{"en":"One student should not bear the load alone in a group project.","zh":"在小組項目中，一名學生不應獨自承受負荷。"},{"en":"Sharing the load can reduce stress and make the whole system more stable.","zh":"分擔負荷可以減少壓力，並使整個系統更穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes carrying responsibility or weight without support.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有支援地承擔責任或重量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"much thinner","meaning":"薄得多","examples":[{"en":"Maillart’s arch could be much thinner than a conventional arch.","zh":"Maillart 的拱可以比傳統拱薄得多。"},{"en":"Much thinner means far less thick than another object or design.","zh":"much thinner 指厚度比另一物件或設計少很多。"},{"en":"A modern laptop is much thinner than an old desktop monitor.","zh":"現代手提電腦比舊桌面顯示器薄得多。"},{"en":"A thinner structure may look lighter and use less material if it remains safe.","zh":"如果較薄結構仍然安全，它可能看起來更輕盈並使用較少材料。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises a large difference in thickness.","zh":"這個短語強調厚度上的巨大差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as little as one-third as thick as","meaning":"厚度少至……的三分之一","examples":[{"en":"The arch could be as little as one-third as thick as a conventional arch.","zh":"拱的厚度可以少至傳統拱的三分之一。"},{"en":"As little as one-third as thick as means only about one third of the thickness of another thing.","zh":"as little as one-third as thick as 指只有另一物厚度大約三分之一。"},{"en":"A new phone screen protector may be as little as one-third as thick as an older model.","zh":"新手機保護貼的厚度可能少至舊款的三分之一。"},{"en":"Reducing thickness to one third can save material, but only if strength is maintained.","zh":"把厚度減至三分之一可以節省材料，但前提是保持強度。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses a striking reduction in thickness.","zh":"這個短語表達厚度上的顯著減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"first masterpiece","meaning":"第一件傑作","examples":[{"en":"The Tavanasa Bridge was Maillart’s first masterpiece.","zh":"Tavanasa Bridge 是 Maillart 的第一件傑作。"},{"en":"A first masterpiece is the first work that clearly shows someone’s exceptional talent.","zh":"first masterpiece 是第一件清楚顯示某人卓越才能的作品。"},{"en":"A young composer’s first masterpiece may make critics take her seriously.","zh":"年輕作曲家的第一件傑作可能令評論家認真看待她。"},{"en":"A masterpiece becomes important because it combines skill, originality and impact.","zh":"傑作之所以重要，是因為它結合技巧、原創性和影響力。"},{"en":"The phrase marks an early work of outstanding quality.","zh":"這個短語標記早期的優秀作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"over the Rhine River","meaning":"橫跨萊茵河","examples":[{"en":"The Tavanasa Bridge crossed over the Rhine River.","zh":"Tavanasa Bridge 橫跨萊茵河。"},{"en":"Over the Rhine River means across or above the Rhine River.","zh":"over the Rhine River 指跨過或位於萊茵河上方。"},{"en":"A railway line may pass over a river so trains do not need to stop at the water.","zh":"鐵路線可能跨過河流，使火車不用在水邊停下。"},{"en":"Crossing over a river connects communities separated by water.","zh":"橫跨河流可以連接被水分隔的社區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the bridge’s position above a specific river.","zh":"這個短語描述橋樑位於特定河流上方的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the Swiss Alps","meaning":"瑞士阿爾卑斯山","examples":[{"en":"The bridge stood in the Swiss Alps.","zh":"這座橋位於瑞士阿爾卑斯山。"},{"en":"The Swiss Alps are the Alpine mountain region in Switzerland.","zh":"Swiss Alps 是瑞士境內的阿爾卑斯山區。"},{"en":"Roads and bridges in the Swiss Alps often face snow, steep slopes and deep valleys.","zh":"瑞士阿爾卑斯山中的道路和橋樑常面對積雪、陡坡和深谷。"},{"en":"Mountain settings make bridge design more difficult but also more dramatic.","zh":"山區環境令橋樑設計更困難，但也更壯觀。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific mountainous region.","zh":"這個短語指出一個特定山區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"remove the parts of","meaning":"移除……的部分","examples":[{"en":"Maillart removed the parts of the vertical walls that carried no load.","zh":"Maillart 移除了垂直牆中不承受負荷的部分。"},{"en":"To remove the parts of something means to take away selected sections rather than the whole thing.","zh":"remove the parts of 某物，指拿走其中某些部分，而不是整個拿走。"},{"en":"A teacher may remove the parts of a worksheet that are too easy for advanced students.","zh":"老師可能移除工作紙中對高階學生太容易的部分。"},{"en":"Removing unnecessary parts can make a design lighter and clearer.","zh":"移除不必要部分可以令設計更輕和更清晰。"},{"en":"The phrase describes selective removal.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇性移除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not essential","meaning":"非必要的","examples":[{"en":"Some parts of the vertical walls were not essential.","zh":"垂直牆的某些部分並非必要。"},{"en":"Not essential means not necessary for the main purpose or function.","zh":"not essential 指對主要目的或功能而言並非必需。"},{"en":"A school trip may be enjoyable with souvenirs, but souvenirs are not essential.","zh":"學校旅行有紀念品可能很開心，但紀念品並非必要。"},{"en":"Removing non-essential parts can save time, money or material.","zh":"移除非必要部分可以節省時間、金錢或材料。"},{"en":"The phrase separates what is necessary from what can be removed.","zh":"這個短語把必要之物與可移除之物分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"carry no load","meaning":"不承受負荷","examples":[{"en":"The removed parts carried no load.","zh":"被移除的部分不承受負荷。"},{"en":"To carry no load means not to support any weight or force.","zh":"carry no load 指不支撐任何重量或力量。"},{"en":"A decorative plastic column in a shop may carry no load at all.","zh":"商店中的裝飾性塑膠柱可能完全不承受負荷。"},{"en":"If a part carries no load, removing it may not weaken the structure.","zh":"如果某部分不承受負荷，移除它未必會削弱結構。"},{"en":"The phrase explains that a part has no structural responsibility.","zh":"這個短語解釋某部分沒有結構責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"produce a slender form","meaning":"造就纖幼的形態","examples":[{"en":"The removal produced a slender, lighter-looking form.","zh":"這種移除造就了纖幼、看起來較輕盈的形態。"},{"en":"To produce a slender form means to create a thinner and more graceful shape.","zh":"produce a slender form 指創造更薄、更優雅的形狀。"},{"en":"A designer may remove bulky details to produce a slender form for a lamp.","zh":"設計師可能移除笨重細節，以為燈具造就纖幼形態。"},{"en":"A slender form can look elegant while also reducing material use.","zh":"纖幼形態可以看起來優雅，同時減少材料使用。"},{"en":"The phrase links design change with a lighter visual result.","zh":"這個短語把設計改變與更輕盈的視覺結果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lighter-looking form","meaning":"看起來較輕盈的形態","examples":[{"en":"The bridge had a slender, lighter-looking form.","zh":"這座橋有纖幼、看起來較輕盈的形態。"},{"en":"A lighter-looking form appears less heavy or bulky, even if it remains strong.","zh":"lighter-looking form 指外觀看來不那麼沉重或笨重，即使仍然堅固。"},{"en":"A chair with thin metal legs may have a lighter-looking form than a thick wooden chair.","zh":"有幼金屬腳的椅子可能比厚木椅看起來較輕盈。"},{"en":"Lighter appearance can make a structure fit more gracefully into its surroundings.","zh":"較輕盈的外觀可以令結構更優雅地融入周圍環境。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visual lightness rather than actual weight only.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺上的輕盈，而不只是實際重量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"perfectly meet","meaning":"完美符合","examples":[{"en":"The design perfectly met the bridge’s structural requirements.","zh":"該設計完美符合橋樑的結構要求。"},{"en":"To perfectly meet requirements means to satisfy them fully and exactly.","zh":"perfectly meet requirements 指完全而準確地滿足要求。"},{"en":"A student’s answer perfectly meets the question if it addresses every part clearly.","zh":"如果學生答案清楚回應題目的每個部分，就是完美符合題目要求。"},{"en":"When a design perfectly meets requirements, it is both suitable and efficient.","zh":"當設計完美符合要求，它就是合適且高效的。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses complete suitability.","zh":"這個短語強調完全合適。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"structural requirements","meaning":"結構要求","examples":[{"en":"The bridge met its structural requirements.","zh":"這座橋符合其結構要求。"},{"en":"Structural requirements are the strength, stability and safety conditions a structure must satisfy.","zh":"structural requirements 是結構必須滿足的強度、穩定性和安全條件。"},{"en":"A school roof must meet structural requirements before students can use the building.","zh":"學校屋頂必須符合結構要求，學生才能使用該建築。"},{"en":"If structural requirements are ignored, a beautiful design may become dangerous.","zh":"如果忽視結構要求，美麗設計可能變得危險。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to technical conditions needed for a safe structure.","zh":"這個短語指安全結構所需的技術條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"gain little favourable publicity","meaning":"幾乎沒有得到正面宣傳","examples":[{"en":"The Tavanasa Bridge gained little favourable publicity in Switzerland.","zh":"Tavanasa Bridge 在瑞士幾乎沒有得到正面宣傳。"},{"en":"To gain little favourable publicity means to receive very little positive public attention.","zh":"gain little favourable publicity 指得到很少正面公眾關注。"},{"en":"A useful school project may gain little favourable publicity if newspapers focus only on exam results.","zh":"如果報章只集中考試成績，有用的學校項目可能幾乎沒有得到正面宣傳。"},{"en":"Lack of publicity can delay recognition even when the work is excellent.","zh":"缺乏宣傳可以延遲認可，即使作品很出色。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limited positive notice from the public or media.","zh":"這個短語描述來自公眾或媒體的正面注意有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"on the contrary","meaning":"相反","examples":[{"en":"On the contrary, the bridge aroused strong objections.","zh":"相反，這座橋引起強烈反對。"},{"en":"On the contrary introduces the opposite of what might be expected or what was just stated.","zh":"on the contrary 引出與預期或剛說內容相反的情況。"},{"en":"The new rule did not reduce complaints; on the contrary, it created more confusion.","zh":"新規則沒有減少投訴；相反，它造成更多混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a clear contrast.","zh":"這個短語標誌清楚對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when the result is the reverse of what readers may expect.","zh":"當結果與讀者可能預期相反時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"arouse strong objections","meaning":"引起強烈反對","examples":[{"en":"The bridge aroused strong aesthetic objections.","zh":"這座橋引起強烈美學反對意見。"},{"en":"To arouse strong objections means to cause people to disagree strongly or complain.","zh":"arouse strong objections 指引起人們強烈不同意或投訴。"},{"en":"A plan to close a public library may arouse strong objections from residents.","zh":"關閉公共圖書館的計劃可能引起居民強烈反對。"},{"en":"Strong objections often appear when people feel a design threatens values they care about.","zh":"當人們覺得設計威脅他們重視的價值，強烈反對常會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes provoking serious opposition.","zh":"這個短語描述引發嚴重反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"aesthetic objections","meaning":"美學上的反對意見","examples":[{"en":"Public officials raised aesthetic objections to the bridge.","zh":"公職人員對這座橋提出美學上的反對意見。"},{"en":"Aesthetic objections are criticisms based on appearance or beauty.","zh":"aesthetic objections 是基於外觀或美感的批評。"},{"en":"Residents may raise aesthetic objections if a new sign looks ugly in a historic street.","zh":"如果新招牌在歷史街道上看起來醜陋，居民可能提出美學上的反對意見。"},{"en":"Aesthetic objections can block a design even when it is technically strong.","zh":"即使設計在技術上很強，美學反對意見也可能阻礙它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes opposition about visual appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述關於視覺外觀的反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"public officials","meaning":"公職人員","examples":[{"en":"Public officials preferred old-fashioned stone-faced bridges.","zh":"公職人員較喜歡老式石面橋。"},{"en":"Public officials are people who work in government or public administration.","zh":"public officials 是在政府或公共行政中工作的人。"},{"en":"Public officials may decide how public money is spent on roads, schools or parks.","zh":"公職人員可能決定公共資金如何用於道路、學校或公園。"},{"en":"Their opinions can shape which designs are accepted by a community.","zh":"他們的意見可以塑造哪些設計被社區接受。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people with official public responsibilities.","zh":"這個短語指有官方公共責任的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be more comfortable with","meaning":"對……較能接受","examples":[{"en":"Officials were more comfortable with old-fashioned bridge designs.","zh":"官員對老式橋樑設計較能接受。"},{"en":"To be more comfortable with something means to feel more familiar, confident or accepting toward it.","zh":"be more comfortable with 某事，指對它感到更熟悉、更有信心或更能接受。"},{"en":"A student may be more comfortable with handwritten notes than digital notes.","zh":"學生可能對手寫筆記比電子筆記較能接受。"},{"en":"People often prefer familiar methods because new ideas feel risky.","zh":"人們常偏好熟悉方法，因為新想法感覺有風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes emotional or practical acceptance.","zh":"這個短語描述情感或實際上的接受程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"old-fashioned","meaning":"老式的","examples":[{"en":"Many officials preferred old-fashioned stone-faced bridges.","zh":"許多官員較喜歡老式石面橋。"},{"en":"Old-fashioned means typical of the past and not modern.","zh":"old-fashioned 指具有過去特色而不現代。"},{"en":"An old-fashioned phone has buttons instead of a touchscreen.","zh":"老式電話有按鈕而不是觸控屏。"},{"en":"Old-fashioned designs can feel safe and familiar, but they may not solve new problems well.","zh":"老式設計可能令人感到安全和熟悉，但未必能妥善解決新問題。"},{"en":"The word describes something traditional or outdated in style.","zh":"這個詞描述風格上傳統或過時的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"stone-faced bridges","meaning":"石面橋","examples":[{"en":"Stone-faced bridges looked more traditional to public officials.","zh":"石面橋在公職人員眼中看起來更傳統。"},{"en":"Stone-faced bridges are bridges with stone on the visible outer surface.","zh":"stone-faced bridges 是外部可見表面有石材的橋樑。"},{"en":"A town may prefer stone-faced bridges because they match older buildings nearby.","zh":"城鎮可能偏好石面橋，因為它們與附近舊建築相襯。"},{"en":"Stone facing can make a bridge look traditional even if its inner structure is modern.","zh":"石面可以令橋看起來傳統，即使其內部結構是現代的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bridges by their visible stone appearance.","zh":"這個短語按可見石材外觀描述橋樑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"found one’s own firm","meaning":"創立自己的公司","examples":[{"en":"Maillart founded his own construction firm in 1902.","zh":"Maillart 於1902年創立自己的建築公司。"},{"en":"To found one’s own firm means to start and establish one’s own company.","zh":"found one’s own firm 指創辦並建立自己的公司。"},{"en":"An engineer may found her own firm after gaining enough experience in a large company.","zh":"工程師在大公司取得足夠經驗後，可能創立自己的公司。"},{"en":"Founding a firm gives more independence but also more financial risk.","zh":"創立公司帶來更多獨立性，但也帶來更多財務風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes starting a business professionally.","zh":"這個短語描述專業地創辦企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"construction firm","meaning":"建築公司","examples":[{"en":"Maillart ran his own construction firm.","zh":"Maillart 經營自己的建築公司。"},{"en":"A construction firm is a company that builds structures such as buildings, bridges or roads.","zh":"construction firm 是建造建築物、橋樑或道路等結構的公司。"},{"en":"A school may hire a construction firm to build a new sports hall.","zh":"學校可能聘請建築公司興建新體育館。"},{"en":"Construction firms must manage workers, materials, safety and deadlines.","zh":"建築公司必須管理工人、材料、安全和期限。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a business in the building industry.","zh":"這個短語指建築業中的企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be unable to","meaning":"無法……","examples":[{"en":"Maillart was unable to win any more bridge projects.","zh":"Maillart 無法贏得更多橋樑項目。"},{"en":"To be unable to do something means not to be able to do it.","zh":"be unable to do something 指不能做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be unable to attend class if she is seriously ill.","zh":"如果學生病得很嚴重，可能無法上課。"},{"en":"Being unable to do something can force a person to change plans.","zh":"無法做某事可以迫使人改變計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lack of ability, opportunity or permission.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏能力、機會或許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"win bridge projects","meaning":"贏得橋樑項目","examples":[{"en":"After Tavanasa, Maillart failed to win more bridge projects.","zh":"在 Tavanasa 之後，Maillart 未能贏得更多橋樑項目。"},{"en":"To win bridge projects means to be chosen to design or build bridges.","zh":"win bridge projects 指被選中設計或建造橋樑。"},{"en":"A company may win bridge projects by offering safe designs at a lower cost.","zh":"公司可能透過提供較低成本的安全設計贏得橋樑項目。"},{"en":"Winning projects matters because it gives engineers chances to test and develop ideas.","zh":"贏得項目很重要，因為它給工程師測試和發展想法的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes securing professional bridge work.","zh":"這個短語描述取得專業橋樑工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"shift one’s focus to","meaning":"將重心轉向……","examples":[{"en":"He shifted his focus to buildings and water tanks.","zh":"他將重心轉向建築物和水箱。"},{"en":"To shift one’s focus to something means to move attention or effort toward a new area.","zh":"shift one’s focus to 某事，指把注意力或努力轉向新範疇。"},{"en":"A student may shift her focus to speaking after improving her grammar.","zh":"學生改善文法後，可能將重心轉向說話。"},{"en":"People shift focus when old opportunities close or new needs appear.","zh":"當舊機會關閉或新需要出現，人們會轉移重心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing the main direction of work or attention.","zh":"這個短語描述改變工作或注意力的主要方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"water tanks","meaning":"水箱","examples":[{"en":"Maillart designed water tanks made of reinforced concrete.","zh":"Maillart 設計由鋼筋混凝土製成的水箱。"},{"en":"Water tanks are containers used to store water.","zh":"water tanks 是用來儲存水的容器。"},{"en":"A school may use water tanks to store water for toilets, cleaning or emergency use.","zh":"學校可能使用水箱儲水，供洗手間、清潔或緊急用途。"},{"en":"Water tanks must be strong because water is heavy and creates pressure on the walls.","zh":"水箱必須堅固，因為水很重並會對牆壁產生壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to storage structures for water.","zh":"這個短語指儲水結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"resume one’s work on","meaning":"恢復……方面的工作","examples":[{"en":"He did not resume his work on concrete bridges until the early 1920s.","zh":"他直到二十世紀二十年代初才恢復混凝土橋方面的工作。"},{"en":"To resume one’s work on something means to start working on it again after stopping.","zh":"resume one’s work on 某事，指停止後再次開始做該工作。"},{"en":"A student may resume her work on an essay after recovering from illness.","zh":"學生病癒後可能恢復文章寫作。"},{"en":"Resuming work can happen when conditions improve or new opportunities appear.","zh":"當情況改善或新機會出現，人們可能恢復工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes returning to a task or field.","zh":"這個短語描述回到某任務或領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"concrete bridges","meaning":"混凝土橋","examples":[{"en":"Maillart returned to designing concrete bridges in the 1920s.","zh":"Maillart 在二十世紀二十年代重新設計混凝土橋。"},{"en":"Concrete bridges are bridges built mainly with concrete or reinforced concrete.","zh":"concrete bridges 是主要由混凝土或鋼筋混凝土建造的橋樑。"},{"en":"Many road bridges are concrete bridges because the material can be strong and moulded into useful shapes.","zh":"許多道路橋都是混凝土橋，因為這種材料可以堅固並塑造成有用形狀。"},{"en":"Concrete bridges may cost less than some steel bridges if designed efficiently.","zh":"如果設計有效率，混凝土橋可能比某些鋼橋成本更低。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bridges by their main construction material.","zh":"這個短語按主要建造材料描述橋樑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"until the early 1920s","meaning":"直到二十世紀二十年代初","examples":[{"en":"He did not resume bridge work until the early 1920s.","zh":"他直到二十世紀二十年代初才恢復橋樑工作。"},{"en":"Until the early 1920s means not before the first years of the 1920s.","zh":"until the early 1920s 指不早於二十世紀二十年代最初幾年。"},{"en":"A school building may not be repaired until the early summer if funding arrives late.","zh":"如果資金遲到，學校建築可能直到初夏才維修。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a delay before an action finally happens.","zh":"這個短語顯示某行動最終發生前有延遲。"},{"en":"It places the event in a specific early part of a decade.","zh":"它把事件放在某十年的早期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"important breakthrough","meaning":"重要突破","examples":[{"en":"His most important breakthrough was the deck-stiffened arch.","zh":"他最重要的突破是橋面加勁拱。"},{"en":"An important breakthrough is a major advance that solves a difficult problem or opens new possibilities.","zh":"important breakthrough 是解決困難問題或開啟新可能的重大進展。"},{"en":"A new teaching method may be an important breakthrough if weak students finally understand grammar.","zh":"如果弱學生終於理解文法，新教學方法可能是重要突破。"},{"en":"Breakthroughs matter because they move a field beyond older limits.","zh":"突破重要，因為它把一個領域推到舊限制之外。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a significant step forward.","zh":"這個短語描述重大進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"during this period","meaning":"在這段時期","examples":[{"en":"During this period, Maillart developed the deck-stiffened arch.","zh":"在這段時期，Maillart 發展出橋面加勁拱。"},{"en":"During this period means within the time just mentioned or being discussed.","zh":"during this period 指在剛提及或正在討論的時間之內。"},{"en":"During this period, students revised grammar every morning before lessons began.","zh":"在這段時期，學生每天早上課前複習文法。"},{"en":"The phrase helps connect an event to a specific stage in a timeline.","zh":"這個短語幫助把事件連接到時間線中的特定階段。"},{"en":"It tells readers when something happened.","zh":"它告訴讀者某事何時發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the development of","meaning":"……的發展","examples":[{"en":"The development of the deck-stiffened arch was a major breakthrough.","zh":"橋面加勁拱的發展是一項重大突破。"},{"en":"The development of something means the process of creating, improving or bringing it into use.","zh":"development of 某物，指創造、改善或投入使用它的過程。"},{"en":"The development of online learning changed how many students access lessons.","zh":"網上學習的發展改變了許多學生接觸課堂的方式。"},{"en":"Development often takes time because ideas must be tested and refined.","zh":"發展通常需要時間，因為想法必須被測試和改良。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how something comes into existence or improves.","zh":"這個短語重點在某物如何出現或改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"deck-stiffened arch","meaning":"橋面加勁拱","examples":[{"en":"The deck-stiffened arch became one of Maillart’s key designs.","zh":"橋面加勁拱成為 Maillart 的關鍵設計之一。"},{"en":"A deck-stiffened arch is an arch bridge design in which the roadway helps stiffen and support the structure.","zh":"deck-stiffened arch 是一種拱橋設計，其中行車面有助加強和支撐結構。"},{"en":"In this design, the bridge deck is not just a surface for vehicles; it also helps the arch work.","zh":"在這種設計中，橋面不只是供車輛通行的表面；它也幫助拱發揮作用。"},{"en":"The method allows a thinner arch because different parts share structural responsibility.","zh":"這種方法容許較薄的拱，因為不同部分分擔結構責任。"},{"en":"The phrase names one of Maillart’s major bridge innovations.","zh":"這個短語指出 Maillart 的一項主要橋樑創新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the first example of","meaning":"……的首個例子","examples":[{"en":"The Flienglibach Bridge was the first example of the deck-stiffened arch.","zh":"Flienglibach Bridge 是橋面加勁拱的首個例子。"},{"en":"The first example of something is the earliest case showing that design, idea or method.","zh":"first example of 某事，是顯示該設計、想法或方法的最早案例。"},{"en":"A pilot class may be the first example of a new teaching approach in a school.","zh":"試驗班可能是一所學校中新教學方法的首個例子。"},{"en":"First examples are important because they test whether an idea works in real life.","zh":"首個例子很重要，因為它測試想法在現實中是否可行。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the earliest practical instance.","zh":"這個短語指出最早的實際案例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"somewhat like","meaning":"有點像","examples":[{"en":"An arch bridge is somewhat like an inverted cable.","zh":"拱橋有點像倒轉的纜索。"},{"en":"Somewhat like means partly similar to, but not exactly the same as.","zh":"somewhat like 指部分相似，但不完全相同。"},{"en":"A school timetable is somewhat like a map because it tells students where to go next.","zh":"學校時間表有點像地圖，因為它告訴學生下一步去哪裏。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain a difficult idea through a comparison.","zh":"這個短語透過比較幫助解釋困難想法。"},{"en":"It signals similarity while leaving room for differences.","zh":"它標示相似，同時保留差異空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"inverted cable","meaning":"倒轉的纜索","examples":[{"en":"An arch bridge can be compared to an inverted cable.","zh":"拱橋可以與倒轉的纜索比較。"},{"en":"An inverted cable is a cable shape turned upside down.","zh":"inverted cable 是上下倒轉的纜索形狀。"},{"en":"A hanging rope curves downward, but an inverted cable shape would curve upward.","zh":"懸掛的繩會向下彎曲，但倒轉的纜索形狀會向上彎曲。"},{"en":"This comparison helps explain why arches carry loads through compression.","zh":"這種比較幫助解釋為何拱透過壓力承載負荷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an upside-down cable-like curve.","zh":"這個短語描述上下倒轉的纜索狀曲線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"curve downward","meaning":"向下彎曲","examples":[{"en":"A cable curves downward when a weight is hung from it.","zh":"當重物掛在纜索上，它會向下彎曲。"},{"en":"To curve downward means to bend in a downward direction.","zh":"curve downward 指向下方彎曲。"},{"en":"A wet clothesline may curve downward when heavy towels are hung on it.","zh":"當沉重毛巾掛在濕晾衣繩上，繩可能向下彎曲。"},{"en":"Downward curvature shows how gravity pulls a flexible object.","zh":"向下彎曲顯示重力如何拉動柔性物體。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a bend that goes lower in the middle or along its length.","zh":"這個短語描述中間或沿長度方向向下的彎曲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hang a weight from","meaning":"把重物掛在……上","examples":[{"en":"A cable bends when a weight is hung from it.","zh":"當重物掛在纜索上，纜索會彎曲。"},{"en":"To hang a weight from something means to attach a heavy object so it pulls downward.","zh":"hang a weight from 某物，指把重物掛上去，使它向下拉。"},{"en":"A student may hang a weight from a spring to test how far it stretches.","zh":"學生可能把重物掛在彈簧上，測試它伸長多少。"},{"en":"Hanging weight creates force that can reveal how a material behaves.","zh":"掛上重量會產生力量，揭示材料如何表現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adding a downward load.","zh":"這個短語描述加入向下負荷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"curve upward","meaning":"向上彎曲","examples":[{"en":"An arch bridge curves upward to support the roadway.","zh":"拱橋向上彎曲以支撐行車道。"},{"en":"To curve upward means to bend in an upward direction.","zh":"curve upward 指向上方彎曲。"},{"en":"A rainbow curves upward from the horizon before falling again on the other side.","zh":"彩虹從地平線向上彎曲，然後在另一邊落下。"},{"en":"An upward curve can help direct weight toward supports at each end.","zh":"向上彎曲可以幫助把重量引向兩端支撐。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an arch-like rise.","zh":"這個短語描述拱形上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"compression in the arch","meaning":"拱內壓力","examples":[{"en":"The compression in the arch balances the bridge’s dead load.","zh":"拱內壓力平衡橋樑的恆載。"},{"en":"Compression in the arch is the pushing force inside an arch when it carries weight.","zh":"compression in the arch 是拱承重時內部產生的推壓力量。"},{"en":"A stack of books creates compression in the lower books because they are being squeezed.","zh":"一疊書會在下方書本中產生壓力，因為它們被擠壓。"},{"en":"Arches work well because stone or concrete can often resist compression strongly.","zh":"拱形結構有效，因為石材或混凝土通常能強力抵抗壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to internal squeezing force in an arch.","zh":"這個短語指拱內部的擠壓力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"balance the dead load","meaning":"平衡恆載","examples":[{"en":"The arch balances the dead load of the bridge.","zh":"拱平衡橋樑的恆載。"},{"en":"To balance the dead load means to support or counteract the fixed weight of the structure.","zh":"balance the dead load 指支撐或抵消結構的固定重量。"},{"en":"A building’s columns balance the dead load of floors and walls.","zh":"建築物的柱平衡樓板和牆的恆載。"},{"en":"If dead load is not balanced, the structure may deform or fail.","zh":"如果恆載未被平衡，結構可能變形或失效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes handling permanent structural weight.","zh":"這個短語描述處理永久結構重量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"dead load","meaning":"恆載；固定荷載","examples":[{"en":"The dead load of the bridge is balanced by compression in the arch.","zh":"橋樑的恆載由拱內壓力平衡。"},{"en":"Dead load is the permanent weight of a structure itself, such as the road deck and supports.","zh":"dead load 是結構本身的永久重量，例如橋面和支撐。"},{"en":"The weight of a school building’s walls and floors is part of its dead load.","zh":"學校建築牆壁和樓板的重量是其恆載的一部分。"},{"en":"Engineers must calculate dead load before adding people, furniture or vehicles.","zh":"工程師必須先計算恆載，再加入人、家具或車輛負荷。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts fixed structural weight with moving or temporary loads.","zh":"這個短語把固定結構重量與移動或臨時負荷作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"for aesthetic reasons","meaning":"出於美學原因","examples":[{"en":"For aesthetic reasons, Maillart wanted a thinner arch.","zh":"出於美學原因，Maillart 想要更薄的拱。"},{"en":"For aesthetic reasons means because of appearance, beauty or visual effect.","zh":"for aesthetic reasons 指因外觀、美感或視覺效果。"},{"en":"A café may choose wooden tables for aesthetic reasons, even if plastic tables are cheaper.","zh":"咖啡店可能出於美學原因選擇木桌，即使塑膠桌較便宜。"},{"en":"Aesthetic reasons can influence design, but safety and function still matter.","zh":"美學原因可以影響設計，但安全和功能仍然重要。"},{"en":"The phrase explains that beauty or appearance is the reason.","zh":"這個短語解釋美感或外觀是原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"transverse walls","meaning":"橫向牆","examples":[{"en":"Maillart connected the arch to the roadway with transverse walls.","zh":"Maillart 用橫向牆把拱連接到行車道。"},{"en":"Transverse walls are walls running across a structure rather than along its length.","zh":"transverse walls 是橫跨結構，而不是沿長度方向延伸的牆。"},{"en":"A storage box may have transverse dividers that split it into sections.","zh":"儲物箱可能有橫向隔板，把它分成幾個部分。"},{"en":"In a bridge, transverse walls can connect parts and help distribute load.","zh":"在橋樑中，橫向牆可以連接各部分並幫助分散負荷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes crosswise wall elements.","zh":"這個短語描述橫向牆狀元素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in this way","meaning":"透過這種方式","examples":[{"en":"In this way, Maillart justified making the arch thinner.","zh":"透過這種方式，Maillart 證明把拱做得更薄是合理的。"},{"en":"In this way means by doing the thing just described.","zh":"in this way 指透過剛描述的做法。"},{"en":"A student reviews mistakes after each essay; in this way, she improves faster.","zh":"學生每篇文章後都檢討錯誤；透過這種方式，她進步得更快。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a method with its result.","zh":"這個短語把方法與結果連起來。"},{"en":"It helps readers see how one action leads to another.","zh":"它幫助讀者看出一個行動如何導致另一結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"justify doing something","meaning":"證明做某事是合理的","examples":[{"en":"Maillart justified making the arch as thin as possible.","zh":"Maillart 證明把拱盡量做薄是合理的。"},{"en":"To justify doing something means to show that the action is reasonable or acceptable.","zh":"justify doing something 指顯示該行動是合理或可接受的。"},{"en":"A school must justify raising fees by explaining how students will benefit.","zh":"學校必須透過解釋學生如何受益，證明加學費是合理的。"},{"en":"Good justification uses evidence, cost, safety or clear need.","zh":"好的理由會使用證據、成本、安全或明確需要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving a reason that makes an action defensible.","zh":"這個短語描述給出使行動站得住腳的理由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as thin as he could reasonably build it","meaning":"薄至合理可建造的程度","examples":[{"en":"He made the arch as thin as he could reasonably build it.","zh":"他把拱做得薄至合理可建造的程度。"},{"en":"As thin as he could reasonably build it means as thin as possible while still remaining practical and safe.","zh":"as thin as he could reasonably build it 指在仍然實際和安全的情況下盡量薄。"},{"en":"A designer may make a laptop as thin as she can reasonably build it without overheating.","zh":"設計師可能把手提電腦做得薄至合理可製造的程度，而不令它過熱。"},{"en":"The word “reasonably” shows that the limit is controlled by safety and practicality.","zh":"“reasonably” 這個詞顯示限度受安全和實用性控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pushing a design to its sensible limit.","zh":"這個短語描述把設計推到合理極限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"accurately predict","meaning":"準確預測","examples":[{"en":"His analysis accurately predicted the behaviour of the bridge.","zh":"他的分析準確預測了橋樑的受力表現。"},{"en":"To accurately predict something means to say what will happen correctly.","zh":"accurately predict 某事，指正確說出將會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"A weather app accurately predicts rain if it warns students before the storm arrives.","zh":"如果天氣應用程式在暴雨到來前提醒學生，就是準確預測下雨。"},{"en":"Accurate prediction helps engineers prevent failure before construction begins.","zh":"準確預測幫助工程師在施工前防止失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes correct forecasting based on analysis or evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述基於分析或證據的正確預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"behaviour of the bridge","meaning":"橋樑的受力表現","examples":[{"en":"Maillart predicted the behaviour of the bridge under load.","zh":"Maillart 預測了橋樑在負荷下的受力表現。"},{"en":"The behaviour of the bridge means how the bridge responds to weight, force and movement.","zh":"behaviour of the bridge 指橋樑如何回應重量、力量和移動。"},{"en":"Engineers test the behaviour of a bridge when trucks pass over it.","zh":"工程師會在貨車駛過時測試橋樑的受力表現。"},{"en":"If the behaviour is not understood, hidden weaknesses may remain dangerous.","zh":"如果不了解這種表現，隱藏弱點可能仍然危險。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to structural response, not human behaviour.","zh":"這個短語指結構反應，而不是人的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"leading authorities","meaning":"權威人士","examples":[{"en":"The leading authorities of Swiss engineering opposed his methods.","zh":"瑞士工程界的權威人士反對他的方法。"},{"en":"Leading authorities are the most respected experts or organisations in a field.","zh":"leading authorities 是某領域中最受尊敬的專家或組織。"},{"en":"Leading authorities in medicine may issue guidance during a health crisis.","zh":"醫學界權威人士可能在健康危機期間發出指引。"},{"en":"When leading authorities oppose an idea, it may struggle to gain acceptance.","zh":"當權威人士反對一個想法，它可能難以被接受。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to powerful expert voices.","zh":"這個短語指有影響力的專家聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"argue against","meaning":"反對；提出反駁","examples":[{"en":"Swiss engineering authorities argued against Maillart’s methods.","zh":"瑞士工程權威人士反對 Maillart 的方法。"},{"en":"To argue against something means to give reasons opposing it.","zh":"argue against 某事，指提出理由反對它。"},{"en":"A parent may argue against too much homework if children have no time to rest.","zh":"如果孩子沒有時間休息，家長可能反對過多功課。"},{"en":"Arguments against a method may focus on safety, cost or tradition.","zh":"反對某方法的論點可能集中在安全、成本或傳統。"},{"en":"The phrase describes presenting opposition with reasons.","zh":"這個短語描述有理由地提出反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"for the next quarter of a century","meaning":"在接下來四分之一世紀","examples":[{"en":"Engineers argued against his methods for the next quarter of a century.","zh":"工程師在接下來四分之一世紀都反對他的方法。"},{"en":"For the next quarter of a century means for the following twenty-five years.","zh":"for the next quarter of a century 指在之後二十五年。"},{"en":"A school tradition may continue for the next quarter of a century if each generation preserves it.","zh":"如果每一代都保存某個學校傳統，它可能在接下來四分之一世紀繼續存在。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that opposition or influence lasted a very long time.","zh":"這個短語顯示反對或影響持續很長時間。"},{"en":"It describes a period of about twenty-five years after a starting point.","zh":"它描述由某起點之後約二十五年的時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"concentrate on","meaning":"專注於","examples":[{"en":"Maillart concentrated on refining the appearance of his bridges.","zh":"Maillart 專注於改良其橋樑的外觀。"},{"en":"To concentrate on something means to give it most of one’s attention and effort.","zh":"concentrate on 某事，指把大部分注意力和努力放在它上面。"},{"en":"A student may concentrate on pronunciation before preparing for a speaking exam.","zh":"學生可能在準備口試前專注於發音。"},{"en":"Concentration helps improve one area because energy is not spread too widely.","zh":"專注能改善一個範疇，因為精力沒有分散太廣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes focused attention.","zh":"這個短語描述集中注意力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"refine the visual appearance of","meaning":"改良……的視覺外觀","examples":[{"en":"He refined the visual appearance of the deck-stiffened arch.","zh":"他改良了橋面加勁拱的視覺外觀。"},{"en":"To refine the visual appearance of something means to improve how it looks through careful changes.","zh":"refine the visual appearance of 某物，指透過仔細改動改善其外觀。"},{"en":"A designer may refine the visual appearance of a poster by adjusting colour and spacing.","zh":"設計師可能透過調整顏色和留白來改良海報的視覺外觀。"},{"en":"Refinement can make a design clearer, lighter or more balanced.","zh":"改良可以令設計更清楚、更輕盈或更平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on improving appearance, not basic function alone.","zh":"這個短語重點在改善外觀，而不只是基本功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"visual appearance","meaning":"視覺外觀","examples":[{"en":"Maillart cared about the visual appearance of his bridges.","zh":"Maillart 重視其橋樑的視覺外觀。"},{"en":"Visual appearance is how something looks to the eye.","zh":"visual appearance 是某物在眼中看起來如何。"},{"en":"The visual appearance of a classroom can affect whether students feel calm and focused.","zh":"課室的視覺外觀可以影響學生是否感到平靜和專注。"},{"en":"Good visual appearance can make a useful object more welcome to the public.","zh":"良好的視覺外觀可以令有用物件更受公眾接受。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to outward look and visual impression.","zh":"這個短語指外在樣貌和視覺印象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"best-known structure","meaning":"最著名的結構","examples":[{"en":"The Salginatobel Bridge is Maillart’s best-known structure.","zh":"Salginatobel Bridge 是 Maillart 最著名的結構。"},{"en":"A best-known structure is the building or engineering work most widely recognised by the public.","zh":"best-known structure 是公眾最廣泛認識的建築或工程作品。"},{"en":"The Eiffel Tower is Paris’s best-known structure for many tourists.","zh":"對許多遊客來說，艾菲爾鐵塔是巴黎最著名的結構。"},{"en":"A structure becomes best-known when its design, location or history is memorable.","zh":"當一項結構的設計、位置或歷史令人難忘，它就會變得最著名。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the most famous work among several.","zh":"這個短語指出多個作品中最有名的一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"complete a structure","meaning":"完成一項結構工程","examples":[{"en":"The Salginatobel Bridge was completed in 1930.","zh":"Salginatobel Bridge 於1930年完成。"},{"en":"To complete a structure means to finish building it.","zh":"complete a structure 指完成建造該結構。"},{"en":"A school hall may be completed before the new term begins.","zh":"學校禮堂可能在新學期開始前完成。"},{"en":"Completion matters because the structure can then be inspected and used.","zh":"完成很重要，因為結構之後可以被檢查和使用。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the end of construction.","zh":"這個短語標記施工結束。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"win the competition for","meaning":"贏得……的競賽","examples":[{"en":"Maillart won the competition for the contract.","zh":"Maillart 贏得該合約的競賽。"},{"en":"To win the competition for something means to be selected over other competitors for it.","zh":"win the competition for 某事，指在競爭中勝過其他對手並被選中。"},{"en":"An architect may win the competition for a new library design.","zh":"建築師可能贏得新圖書館設計競賽。"},{"en":"Winning a competition can bring money, reputation and a chance to build the idea.","zh":"贏得競賽可以帶來金錢、聲譽和實現想法的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes success in a competitive selection process.","zh":"這個短語描述在競爭性甄選中的成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"contract","meaning":"合約","examples":[{"en":"His design won the contract for the Salginatobel Bridge.","zh":"他的設計贏得 Salginatobel Bridge 的合約。"},{"en":"A contract is a formal agreement to provide work, goods or services.","zh":"contract 是提供工作、貨品或服務的正式協議。"},{"en":"A school may sign a contract with a company to repair its roof.","zh":"學校可能與公司簽合約維修屋頂。"},{"en":"Contracts define cost, duties and deadlines, so both sides know what is expected.","zh":"合約訂明成本、職責和期限，令雙方知道預期內容。"},{"en":"The word refers to a binding work agreement.","zh":"這個詞指具約束力的工作協議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the least expensive of","meaning":"……之中最便宜的","examples":[{"en":"His design was the least expensive of the 19 submitted.","zh":"他的設計是19份提交方案之中最便宜的。"},{"en":"The least expensive of a group means the cheapest among all the options.","zh":"least expensive of 一組選項，指所有選項中最便宜的。"},{"en":"A student may choose the least expensive of three lunch sets if she wants to save money.","zh":"如果學生想省錢，可能選三個午餐套餐中最便宜的。"},{"en":"Being least expensive can help a proposal win if it still meets quality standards.","zh":"如果仍符合質素標準，最便宜可以幫助方案勝出。"},{"en":"The phrase compares one option with the whole group by price.","zh":"這個短語按價格把一個選項與整組比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"submitted","meaning":"提交的","examples":[{"en":"Nineteen designs were submitted for the bridge competition.","zh":"有19份設計提交給橋樑競賽。"},{"en":"Submitted means formally sent in for consideration, judgement or approval.","zh":"submitted 指正式遞交以供考慮、評審或批准。"},{"en":"Students must make sure their essays are submitted before the deadline.","zh":"學生必須確保文章在截止日期前提交。"},{"en":"Once a proposal is submitted, judges or officials can review it.","zh":"方案一旦提交，評審或官員便可審閱。"},{"en":"The word describes giving work officially to someone else.","zh":"這個詞描述把作品正式交給他人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"equivalent to","meaning":"相當於","examples":[{"en":"The cost was equivalent to about $3.5 million today.","zh":"該成本相當於今天約350萬美元。"},{"en":"Equivalent to means equal in value, amount, meaning or effect.","zh":"equivalent to 指在價值、數量、意思或效果上相等。"},{"en":"Ten thousand steps may be roughly equivalent to several kilometres of walking.","zh":"一萬步大約相當於步行數公里。"},{"en":"Historical costs are often converted into today’s money so readers can understand their scale.","zh":"歷史成本常被換算成今天金額，讓讀者理解其規模。"},{"en":"The phrase helps compare things measured in different times or forms.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較不同時間或形式量度的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"longest span","meaning":"最長跨度","examples":[{"en":"Salginatobel was Maillart’s longest span.","zh":"Salginatobel 是 Maillart 最長跨度的橋。"},{"en":"Longest span means the greatest distance covered between supports.","zh":"longest span 指支撐點之間覆蓋的最大距離。"},{"en":"A bridge with a long span can cross a wide valley without many columns below.","zh":"長跨度橋可以在下方沒有很多柱的情況下跨過寬闊山谷。"},{"en":"Longer spans are difficult because the structure must carry weight over a greater distance.","zh":"較長跨度很困難，因為結構必須在更大距離上承載重量。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the length of unsupported crossing.","zh":"這個短語指無支撐跨越的長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"dramatic setting","meaning":"壯觀的環境","examples":[{"en":"The bridge had the most dramatic setting of all his structures.","zh":"這座橋在他所有結構中擁有最壯觀的環境。"},{"en":"A dramatic setting is a striking or impressive location that makes something look more powerful.","zh":"dramatic setting 是令人震撼或印象深刻、令某物更有力量的位置。"},{"en":"A school built beside the sea may have a dramatic setting when waves crash nearby.","zh":"如果學校建在海邊，附近有海浪拍岸，就可能有壯觀的環境。"},{"en":"A dramatic setting can make a structure memorable even before people study its design.","zh":"壯觀環境可以在別人研究設計前，已令結構令人難忘。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the visual power of the surrounding place.","zh":"這個短語描述周圍地方的視覺力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"vault above","meaning":"拱跨於……上方","examples":[{"en":"The bridge vaulted 80 metres above the ravine.","zh":"這座橋拱跨於峽谷上方80米。"},{"en":"To vault above something means to arch high over it.","zh":"vault above 某物，指以拱形高高跨越它。"},{"en":"A footbridge may vault above a busy road so pedestrians can cross safely.","zh":"行人橋可能拱跨於繁忙道路上方，讓行人安全過路。"},{"en":"Vaulting above a deep space creates both structural challenge and visual drama.","zh":"拱跨於深空間上方同時帶來結構挑戰和視覺震撼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a high arched crossing.","zh":"這個短語描述高高的拱形跨越。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ravine","meaning":"峽谷","examples":[{"en":"The bridge rose above the ravine of the Salgina brook.","zh":"這座橋高於 Salgina 小溪的峽谷。"},{"en":"A ravine is a deep, narrow valley with steep sides.","zh":"ravine 是深而狹窄、兩側陡峭的山谷。"},{"en":"Hikers may need a bridge to cross a ravine safely.","zh":"遠足者可能需要橋樑安全跨越峽谷。"},{"en":"Ravines make construction difficult because the ground drops sharply.","zh":"峽谷令施工困難，因為地面急劇下跌。"},{"en":"The word describes a deep natural gap in the landscape.","zh":"這個詞描述地貌中的深天然缺口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"brook","meaning":"小溪","examples":[{"en":"The Salgina brook flowed below the bridge.","zh":"Salgina 小溪在橋下流過。"},{"en":"A brook is a small stream of water.","zh":"brook 是細小溪流。"},{"en":"Children may play near a brook in a village park, but they should stay safe after rain.","zh":"孩子可能在鄉村公園的小溪旁玩耍，但雨後應保持安全。"},{"en":"A brook can cut through land over time and create a small valley.","zh":"小溪可以隨時間切割土地並形成小山谷。"},{"en":"The word refers to a small natural watercourse.","zh":"這個詞指小型天然水道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be designated","meaning":"被指定為","examples":[{"en":"The bridge was designated an international historic landmark.","zh":"這座橋被指定為國際歷史地標。"},{"en":"To be designated something means to be officially named or classified as it.","zh":"be designated 某物，指被正式命名或分類為該物。"},{"en":"An old school building may be designated a protected heritage site.","zh":"一座舊校舍可能被指定為受保護文物地點。"},{"en":"Official designation can bring recognition and protection.","zh":"官方指定可以帶來認可和保護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formal naming or status.","zh":"這個短語描述正式命名或地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"international historic landmark","meaning":"國際歷史地標","examples":[{"en":"Salginatobel became an international historic landmark.","zh":"Salginatobel 成為國際歷史地標。"},{"en":"An international historic landmark is a place or structure recognised worldwide for historical importance.","zh":"international historic landmark 是因歷史重要性而在世界範圍受認可的地方或結構。"},{"en":"A famous bridge may become an international historic landmark if it changes engineering history.","zh":"如果著名橋樑改變工程史，它可能成為國際歷史地標。"},{"en":"Such landmarks attract visitors, researchers and preservation efforts.","zh":"這類地標會吸引遊客、研究人員和保育工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes heritage importance beyond one country.","zh":"這個短語描述超越一個國家的文化遺產重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"before his death","meaning":"在他去世前","examples":[{"en":"Before his death, Maillart completed other remarkable bridges.","zh":"在他去世前，Maillart 完成了其他非凡橋樑。"},{"en":"Before his death means during the period before he died.","zh":"before his death 指在他死亡之前的時期。"},{"en":"Before his death, a writer may finish several books that later become famous.","zh":"在作家去世前，他可能完成幾本後來成名的書。"},{"en":"This phrase helps place achievements near the end of someone’s life.","zh":"這個短語幫助把成就放在某人生命末期附近。"},{"en":"It introduces actions completed while the person was still alive.","zh":"它引出該人在世時完成的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"remarkable bridges","meaning":"非凡的橋樑","examples":[{"en":"Maillart completed several remarkable bridges.","zh":"Maillart 完成了幾座非凡的橋樑。"},{"en":"Remarkable bridges are bridges that are unusual, impressive or worth special attention.","zh":"remarkable bridges 是不尋常、令人印象深刻或值得特別注意的橋樑。"},{"en":"A bridge built with very little material but great strength may be remarkable.","zh":"用很少材料但有很大強度建成的橋可能很非凡。"},{"en":"Remarkable bridges often influence how later engineers design similar structures.","zh":"非凡的橋樑常影響後來工程師如何設計類似結構。"},{"en":"The phrase praises bridges for special quality or importance.","zh":"這個短語因橋樑的特殊質素或重要性而作出稱讚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"continue to refine","meaning":"繼續改良","examples":[{"en":"He continued to refine his bridge designs.","zh":"他繼續改良自己的橋樑設計。"},{"en":"To continue to refine something means to keep improving it through careful changes.","zh":"continue to refine 某物，指透過仔細改動持續改善它。"},{"en":"A student may continue to refine an essay after receiving teacher feedback.","zh":"學生可能在收到老師回饋後繼續改良文章。"},{"en":"Refinement over time can turn a good idea into an excellent one.","zh":"隨時間改良可以把好想法變成出色想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated improvement rather than one sudden change.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆改善，而不是一次突然改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"recognise the high quality of","meaning":"認可……的高質素","examples":[{"en":"Architects recognised the high quality of Maillart’s structures.","zh":"建築師認可 Maillart 結構的高質素。"},{"en":"To recognise the high quality of something means to understand and acknowledge that it is excellent.","zh":"recognise the high quality of 某物，指理解並承認它很出色。"},{"en":"A teacher may recognise the high quality of a student’s essay even if it is not flashy.","zh":"即使學生文章不花巧，老師也可能認可其高質素。"},{"en":"Recognition can arrive late when people need time to understand a new style.","zh":"當人們需要時間理解新風格，認可可能較遲到來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving deserved appreciation to excellence.","zh":"這個短語描述對卓越給予應有欣賞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"fellow engineers","meaning":"工程師同行","examples":[{"en":"Architects appreciated Maillart’s work before his fellow engineers did.","zh":"建築師比 Maillart 的工程師同行更早欣賞他的作品。"},{"en":"Fellow engineers are other engineers in the same profession or field.","zh":"fellow engineers 是同一專業或領域中的其他工程師。"},{"en":"A young engineer may present a new idea to fellow engineers at a conference.","zh":"年輕工程師可能在會議上向工程師同行展示新想法。"},{"en":"Support from fellow professionals can help an idea become accepted.","zh":"來自專業同行的支持可以幫助一個想法被接受。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to professional peers.","zh":"這個短語指專業同輩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"architectural section","meaning":"建築部門","examples":[{"en":"The architectural section of the Museum of Modern Art held an exhibition.","zh":"現代藝術博物館的建築部門舉辦了一場展覽。"},{"en":"An architectural section is a department or part of an institution focused on architecture.","zh":"architectural section 是機構中專注於建築的部門或部分。"},{"en":"A museum’s architectural section may collect drawings, models and photographs of buildings.","zh":"博物館的建築部門可能收藏建築圖、模型和照片。"},{"en":"Such a section helps the public understand design as culture, not only construction.","zh":"這類部門幫助公眾把設計理解為文化，而不只是施工。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the architecture-focused part of an organisation.","zh":"這個短語指組織中專注建築的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"devote an exhibition to","meaning":"為……舉辦展覽","examples":[{"en":"The museum devoted a major exhibition to Maillart’s works.","zh":"博物館為 Maillart 的作品舉辦大型展覽。"},{"en":"To devote an exhibition to someone or something means to make that person or topic the main focus of the exhibition.","zh":"devote an exhibition to 某人或某事，指把該人物或主題作為展覽的主要焦點。"},{"en":"A school may devote an exhibition to students’ environmental projects.","zh":"學校可能為學生環保項目舉辦展覽。"},{"en":"Devoting an exhibition to a figure signals that the work deserves serious attention.","zh":"為某人物舉辦展覽，顯示其作品值得認真關注。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dedicating a display to one subject.","zh":"這個短語描述把展示獻給一個主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"major exhibition","meaning":"大型展覽","examples":[{"en":"A major exhibition in New York focused entirely on Maillart’s work.","zh":"紐約一場大型展覽完全聚焦於 Maillart 的作品。"},{"en":"A major exhibition is a large and important public display.","zh":"major exhibition 是大型而重要的公開展示。"},{"en":"A museum may organise a major exhibition about ancient technology.","zh":"博物館可能舉辦關於古代科技的大型展覽。"},{"en":"Major exhibitions can change public awareness by presenting work in depth.","zh":"大型展覽可以透過深入呈現作品來改變公眾認知。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an exhibition of significant scale and importance.","zh":"這個短語描述規模和重要性都高的展覽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"entirely to","meaning":"完全獻給……","examples":[{"en":"The exhibition was devoted entirely to his works.","zh":"該展覽完全獻給他的作品。"},{"en":"Entirely to means completely to one person, topic or purpose.","zh":"entirely to 指完全給予某人、某主題或某目的。"},{"en":"A school assembly may be devoted entirely to student safety after several accidents.","zh":"幾宗意外後，學校早會可能完全獻給學生安全這一主題。"},{"en":"When time is given entirely to one topic, that topic receives full attention.","zh":"當時間完全用於一個主題，該主題就得到充分注意。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses complete focus.","zh":"這個短語強調完全聚焦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"in contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"In contrast, few American structural engineers knew of Maillart.","zh":"相比之下，很少美國結構工程師知道 Maillart。"},{"en":"In contrast introduces a clear difference from what has just been mentioned.","zh":"in contrast 引出與剛提及內容清楚不同的情況。"},{"en":"Some students love group work; in contrast, others prefer studying alone.","zh":"有些學生喜歡小組合作；相比之下，其他學生較喜歡獨自學習。"},{"en":"The phrase helps readers compare two different situations directly.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者直接比較兩種不同情況。"},{"en":"It signals that the next point is opposite or noticeably different.","zh":"它標誌下一點相反或明顯不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"have heard of","meaning":"聽說過","examples":[{"en":"Few American structural engineers had heard of Maillart.","zh":"很少美國結構工程師聽說過 Maillart。"},{"en":"To have heard of someone means to know that the person exists or is famous.","zh":"have heard of 某人，指知道這個人存在或有名。"},{"en":"A student may have heard of Shakespeare even before reading his plays.","zh":"學生可能在閱讀莎士比亞戲劇前已聽說過他。"},{"en":"If few people have heard of a designer, his influence may not yet have spread widely.","zh":"如果很少人聽說過某設計師，其影響力可能尚未廣泛傳開。"},{"en":"The phrase describes basic awareness of a person or thing.","zh":"這個短語描述對某人或某事的基本認識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in the following years","meaning":"在隨後幾年","examples":[{"en":"In the following years, engineers recognised Maillart’s technical skill.","zh":"在隨後幾年，工程師認可 Maillart 的技術能力。"},{"en":"In the following years means during the years after the time just mentioned.","zh":"in the following years 指在剛提及時間之後的幾年。"},{"en":"A school may introduce a new reading scheme, and in the following years exam results may improve.","zh":"學校可能推出新的閱讀計劃，而在隨後幾年考試成績可能改善。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that recognition or change happened later, not immediately.","zh":"這個短語顯示認可或改變是後來發生，而不是立即發生。"},{"en":"It helps organise events in time order.","zh":"它幫助按時間順序組織事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"more than just","meaning":"不只是","examples":[{"en":"His bridges were more than just aesthetically pleasing.","zh":"他的橋樑不只是美觀的。"},{"en":"More than just means not only that thing, but also something more important or additional.","zh":"more than just 指不只是某事，還有更重要或額外的東西。"},{"en":"A good school is more than just exam results; it also supports confidence and character.","zh":"好學校不只是考試成績；它也支援信心和品格。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show that a surface impression is incomplete.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示表面印象並不完整。"},{"en":"It adds deeper value beyond the first description.","zh":"它加入超越第一個描述的更深價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"aesthetically pleasing","meaning":"美觀的","examples":[{"en":"Maillart’s bridges were aesthetically pleasing and technically advanced.","zh":"Maillart 的橋樑美觀且技術先進。"},{"en":"Aesthetically pleasing means attractive or satisfying in appearance.","zh":"aesthetically pleasing 指外觀吸引或令人感到滿意。"},{"en":"A classroom can be aesthetically pleasing if colours, light and furniture feel balanced.","zh":"如果課室的顏色、光線和家具感覺平衡，它可以是美觀的。"},{"en":"Attractive design can make people more willing to accept and care for a public structure.","zh":"吸引人的設計可以令人更願意接受和愛護公共結構。"},{"en":"The phrase describes beauty or visual appeal.","zh":"這個短語描述美感或視覺吸引力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"technically unsurpassed","meaning":"技術上無與倫比","examples":[{"en":"Engineers realised that Maillart’s bridges were technically unsurpassed.","zh":"工程師意識到 Maillart 的橋樑在技術上無與倫比。"},{"en":"Technically unsurpassed means not bettered by others in technical quality or performance.","zh":"technically unsurpassed 指在技術質素或性能上沒有被其他作品超越。"},{"en":"A medical device may be technically unsurpassed if no rival is more accurate or reliable.","zh":"如果沒有競爭產品更準確或可靠，醫療設備可能在技術上無與倫比。"},{"en":"A design can be beautiful and still be judged mainly by its technical strength.","zh":"設計可以很美，但仍主要由其技術強度來評價。"},{"en":"The phrase gives very high praise for engineering quality.","zh":"這個短語對工程質素給予極高評價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"dominant design form","meaning":"主導設計形式","examples":[{"en":"The hollow-box arch became the dominant design form in the US.","zh":"空心箱形拱成為美國的主導設計形式。"},{"en":"A dominant design form is the main or most widely used style or method.","zh":"dominant design form 是主要或最廣泛使用的風格或方法。"},{"en":"Touchscreen phones became the dominant design form after older keypad phones declined.","zh":"舊鍵盤手機衰落後，觸控屏手機成為主導設計形式。"},{"en":"A form becomes dominant when many designers adopt it because it works well.","zh":"當許多設計師因某形式有效而採用它，它就會成為主導。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the design that leads or becomes standard.","zh":"這個短語描述領先或成為標準的設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"medium- and long-span concrete bridges","meaning":"中跨度及長跨度混凝土橋","examples":[{"en":"The design was used for medium- and long-span concrete bridges.","zh":"該設計用於中跨度及長跨度混凝土橋。"},{"en":"Medium- and long-span concrete bridges are concrete bridges that cross moderate or large distances between supports.","zh":"medium- and long-span concrete bridges 是支撐點之間跨越中等或較大距離的混凝土橋。"},{"en":"A city may need medium-span bridges over roads and long-span bridges over rivers or valleys.","zh":"城市可能需要跨道路的中跨度橋，以及跨河流或山谷的長跨度橋。"},{"en":"Longer spans require careful design because weight must be carried over greater distances.","zh":"較長跨度需要仔細設計，因為重量必須跨越更大距離被承載。"},{"en":"The phrase classifies concrete bridges by span length.","zh":"這個短語按跨度長度分類混凝土橋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"finally began to","meaning":"終於開始","examples":[{"en":"Swiss professors finally began to teach Maillart’s ideas.","zh":"瑞士教授終於開始教授 Maillart 的想法。"},{"en":"Finally began to means started doing something after a long delay or after earlier resistance.","zh":"finally began to 指經過長時間延遲或早前抗拒後開始做某事。"},{"en":"A student may finally begin to revise seriously after receiving a poor mock-exam result.","zh":"學生可能在模擬考成績差後終於開始認真溫習。"},{"en":"The word “finally” suggests that the change took time.","zh":"“finally” 這個詞暗示改變花了時間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a delayed beginning.","zh":"這個短語描述延遲後的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"influence a new generation of","meaning":"影響新一代……","examples":[{"en":"Maillart’s ideas influenced a new generation of designers.","zh":"Maillart 的想法影響了新一代設計師。"},{"en":"To influence a new generation of people means to shape the thinking or work of younger people who come later.","zh":"influence a new generation of 人，指塑造後來較年輕一代人的思想或工作。"},{"en":"A great teacher can influence a new generation of students long after leaving the school.","zh":"偉大老師即使離開學校多年後，仍可影響新一代學生。"},{"en":"Lasting influence appears when later people use, adapt or develop the original ideas.","zh":"當後來的人使用、改編或發展原有想法，持久影響就會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes impact across time.","zh":"這個短語描述跨時間的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a new generation of designers","meaning":"新一代設計師","examples":[{"en":"A new generation of designers learned from Maillart’s ideas.","zh":"新一代設計師從 Maillart 的想法中學習。"},{"en":"A new generation of designers means younger designers who begin working after an earlier group.","zh":"new generation of designers 指在較早一批人之後開始工作的年輕設計師。"},{"en":"A new generation of teachers may use technology more naturally than older staff.","zh":"新一代老師可能比年長職員更自然地使用科技。"},{"en":"New generations can carry forward ideas that were not fully accepted at first.","zh":"新一代可以延續起初未被完全接受的想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a later group entering the field.","zh":"這個短語描述後來進入該領域的一群人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reading passage","meaning":"閱讀篇章","examples":[{"en":"The reading passage has seven paragraphs.","zh":"閱讀篇章有七段。"},{"en":"A reading passage is a text used for reading practice or examination questions.","zh":"reading passage 是用於閱讀練習或考試題目的文本。"},{"en":"Students should skim the reading passage before answering detailed questions.","zh":"學生應在回答細節題前先略讀閱讀篇章。"},{"en":"Understanding the whole passage helps prevent mistakes caused by isolated keywords.","zh":"理解整篇文章有助防止因孤立關鍵詞造成錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the main text in a reading task.","zh":"這個短語指閱讀任務中的主要文本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the most suitable heading","meaning":"最合適的標題","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the most suitable heading for each paragraph.","zh":"考生為每段選出最合適的標題。"},{"en":"The most suitable heading is the title that best summarises the main idea.","zh":"most suitable heading 是最能概括主旨的標題。"},{"en":"In a reading exam, a heading about “causes” is not suitable if the paragraph only describes effects.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，如果段落只描述結果，關於「原因」的標題就不合適。"},{"en":"Choosing the best heading requires understanding the whole paragraph, not one word.","zh":"選最佳標題需要理解整段，而不是只看一個詞。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the best matching summary title.","zh":"這個短語指最相配的摘要式標題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"appropriate numbers","meaning":"適當的編號","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the appropriate numbers on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生在答題紙上寫上適當的編號。"},{"en":"Appropriate numbers are the correct numbers that match the answers required.","zh":"appropriate numbers 是符合所需答案的正確編號。"},{"en":"In a matching exercise, students must copy the appropriate numbers carefully.","zh":"在配對練習中，學生必須小心抄寫適當的編號。"},{"en":"A correct idea can still lose marks if the wrong number is written.","zh":"即使想法正確，如果寫錯編號仍可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the right numbered options.","zh":"這個短語指正確的編號選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"answer sheet","meaning":"答題紙","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write their answers on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生在答題紙上寫上答案。"},{"en":"An answer sheet is the official paper or digital form where exam answers are recorded.","zh":"answer sheet 是記錄考試答案的官方紙張或電子表格。"},{"en":"A student may know the answer but lose marks if she forgets to write it on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生可能知道答案，但如果忘記寫在答題紙上就會失分。"},{"en":"Exam instructions often stress answer sheets because only recorded answers are marked.","zh":"考試指示常強調答題紙，因為只有記錄下來的答案會被評分。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the place where final answers must be written.","zh":"這個短語指最終答案必須寫上的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The list of headings provides possible paragraph summaries.","zh":"標題列表提供可能的段落摘要。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a group of possible titles for paragraphs.","zh":"list of headings 是一組可供段落使用的可能標題。"},{"en":"Students should read the list of headings before matching them to paragraphs.","zh":"學生在把標題配對到段落前，應先閱讀標題列表。"},{"en":"Some headings may look similar, so students must compare main ideas carefully.","zh":"有些標題可能看似相似，所以學生必須仔細比較主旨。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to answer options in heading-matching tasks.","zh":"這個短語指標題配對題中的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"long-term impact","meaning":"長遠影響","examples":[{"en":"The final paragraph describes Maillart’s long-term impact.","zh":"最後一段描述 Maillart 的長遠影響。"},{"en":"Long-term impact is the effect something has over many years.","zh":"long-term impact 是某事在多年中產生的效果。"},{"en":"A good teacher can have long-term impact on students’ confidence and career choices.","zh":"好老師可以對學生信心和職業選擇產生長遠影響。"},{"en":"Long-term impact may appear only after later generations adopt the original idea.","zh":"長遠影響可能要到後來世代採用原有想法後才出現。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on lasting influence.","zh":"這個短語重點在持久影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a celebrated achievement","meaning":"備受讚揚的成就","examples":[{"en":"The Salginatobel Bridge was a celebrated achievement.","zh":"Salginatobel Bridge 是一項備受讚揚的成就。"},{"en":"A celebrated achievement is a success that is widely praised or admired.","zh":"celebrated achievement 是受到廣泛稱讚或欣賞的成功。"},{"en":"A student winning an international science prize may be a celebrated achievement for the school.","zh":"學生贏得國際科學獎，可能成為學校備受讚揚的成就。"},{"en":"Achievements become celebrated when people recognise their difficulty and value.","zh":"當人們認可成就的難度和價值，它就會備受讚揚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a success that receives honour and attention.","zh":"這個短語描述獲得榮譽和關注的成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"early brilliance passes unrecognised","meaning":"早期才華未受賞識","examples":[{"en":"Maillart’s early brilliance passed largely unrecognised.","zh":"Maillart 的早期才華大多未受賞識。"},{"en":"If early brilliance passes unrecognised, a person’s early talent is not properly noticed.","zh":"如果 early brilliance passes unrecognised，意思是某人早期才能沒有被適當注意。"},{"en":"A quiet student’s early brilliance may pass unrecognised if teachers only reward loud confidence.","zh":"如果老師只獎勵外露自信，安靜學生的早期才華可能未受賞識。"},{"en":"Recognition can arrive late when people are not ready to understand original work.","zh":"當人們尚未準備理解原創作品，認可可能很遲才來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes outstanding ability that is ignored at first.","zh":"這個短語描述出色能力起初被忽視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"outdated methods","meaning":"過時方法","examples":[{"en":"Some officials continued to prefer outdated methods.","zh":"有些官員繼續偏好過時方法。"},{"en":"Outdated methods are old ways of doing things that no longer fit current needs or knowledge.","zh":"outdated methods 是已不再符合現時需要或知識的舊做法。"},{"en":"A school using only memorisation may rely on outdated methods for language learning.","zh":"只使用背誦的學校可能依賴過時方法學語言。"},{"en":"Outdated methods can slow progress when better approaches are available.","zh":"當有更好方法可用，過時方法會拖慢進步。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises methods that belong to an earlier time.","zh":"這個短語批評屬於較早時代的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"retain popularity","meaning":"仍然受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Old-fashioned bridge styles retained popularity among officials.","zh":"老式橋樑風格在官員之中仍然受歡迎。"},{"en":"To retain popularity means to continue being liked or accepted.","zh":"retain popularity 指繼續受到喜愛或接受。"},{"en":"Paper notebooks retain popularity among students even though digital tools exist.","zh":"即使有電子工具，紙本筆記本在學生中仍然受歡迎。"},{"en":"Something may retain popularity because it feels familiar, reliable or traditional.","zh":"某物可能因感覺熟悉、可靠或傳統而仍然受歡迎。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continued approval over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間持續受到認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the basis of a new design","meaning":"新設計的基礎","examples":[{"en":"The hollow-box arch became the basis of a new design.","zh":"空心箱形拱成為新設計的基礎。"},{"en":"The basis of a new design is the main idea or foundation on which the design is built.","zh":"basis of a new design 是新設計所建基的主要想法或基礎。"},{"en":"A simple app layout may become the basis of a new school learning platform.","zh":"簡單應用程式版面可能成為新學習平台設計的基礎。"},{"en":"A strong basis helps later designers develop variations and improvements.","zh":"強大基礎幫助後來設計師發展變化和改良。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the foundation for further design.","zh":"這個短語描述進一步設計的根基。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be born","meaning":"誕生","examples":[{"en":"A new bridge design was born from Maillart’s innovation.","zh":"一種新橋樑設計由 Maillart 的創新中誕生。"},{"en":"To be born, in this context, means to begin or come into existence.","zh":"be born 在這個語境中指開始或出現。"},{"en":"A new school tradition may be born when students repeat a meaningful event every year.","zh":"當學生每年重複一項有意義活動，新學校傳統可能誕生。"},{"en":"New ideas are often born when someone solves an old problem differently.","zh":"新想法常在有人以不同方式解決舊問題時誕生。"},{"en":"The phrase is figurative and describes the beginning of something.","zh":"這個短語是比喻用法，描述某事的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"frustration at","meaning":"對……的挫敗感","examples":[{"en":"The heading refers to frustration at not perfecting a design.","zh":"該標題指對未能完善設計的挫敗感。"},{"en":"Frustration at something is annoyance or disappointment because of that situation.","zh":"frustration at 某事，是因該情況而產生的煩躁或失望。"},{"en":"A student may feel frustration at making the same grammar mistake again.","zh":"學生可能因再次犯同一文法錯誤而感到挫敗。"},{"en":"Frustration can push people to give up or to work harder on improvement.","zh":"挫敗感可以令人放棄，也可以推動人更努力改進。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the cause of someone’s disappointed feeling.","zh":"這個短語指出某人失望感的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"get the design right","meaning":"把設計做好","examples":[{"en":"Engineers often struggle to get a design right.","zh":"工程師常努力把設計做好。"},{"en":"To get the design right means to make the design work well in function, safety and appearance.","zh":"get the design right 指令設計在功能、安全和外觀上都表現良好。"},{"en":"A teacher may need several drafts to get a lesson plan right.","zh":"老師可能需要幾份草稿才把課程計劃做好。"},{"en":"Getting a design right usually requires testing, feedback and revision.","zh":"把設計做好通常需要測試、回饋和修改。"},{"en":"The phrase describes achieving a successful final design.","zh":"這個短語描述達成成功的最終設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"further refinements","meaning":"進一步改良","examples":[{"en":"Maillart made further refinements to his bridge designs.","zh":"Maillart 對其橋樑設計作出進一步改良。"},{"en":"Further refinements are additional small improvements made after the main design already exists.","zh":"further refinements 是主要設計已存在後再作的額外小改進。"},{"en":"A student may make further refinements to an essay by improving transitions and examples.","zh":"學生可能透過改善過渡和例子，對文章作出進一步改良。"},{"en":"Refinements can make a good piece of work clearer, lighter or more polished.","zh":"改良可以令好的作品更清楚、更輕巧或更成熟。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continued improvement after an initial version.","zh":"這個短語描述初版之後的持續改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"persistent objections","meaning":"持續反對","examples":[{"en":"His methods met persistent objections from Swiss engineering authorities.","zh":"他的方式遭到瑞士工程權威人士持續反對。"},{"en":"Persistent objections are repeated or continuing forms of opposition.","zh":"persistent objections 是反覆或持續的反對。"},{"en":"A school uniform change may face persistent objections from parents if costs are high.","zh":"如果成本高，校服改動可能面對家長持續反對。"},{"en":"Persistent objections can delay acceptance even when an idea later proves successful.","zh":"即使某想法後來證明成功，持續反對也可以延遲其被接受。"},{"en":"The phrase describes opposition that does not quickly disappear.","zh":"這個短語描述不會很快消失的反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"in all respects","meaning":"在各方面","examples":[{"en":"The new highway bridges were different from railway bridges in all respects.","zh":"新公路橋在各方面都與鐵路橋不同。"},{"en":"In all respects means in every important way or aspect.","zh":"in all respects 指在每個重要方面。"},{"en":"Online lessons are not the same as classroom lessons in all respects.","zh":"網上課在各方面都不等同於課室課堂。"},{"en":"If two things differ in all respects, one design cannot simply be copied for the other.","zh":"如果兩件事在各方面不同，一個設計就不能簡單複製到另一個。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses complete or broad difference.","zh":"這個短語強調完全或廣泛差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"look elsewhere","meaning":"另尋他處","examples":[{"en":"Some bridge-makers had to look elsewhere for new materials and methods.","zh":"有些橋樑建造者不得不另尋他處尋找新材料和方法。"},{"en":"To look elsewhere means to search in another place or direction for a solution.","zh":"look elsewhere 指在另一地方或方向尋找解決方案。"},{"en":"If a student cannot understand one textbook, she may look elsewhere for clearer explanations.","zh":"如果學生看不懂一本教科書，她可能另尋他處找更清楚解釋。"},{"en":"People look elsewhere when existing options fail to meet new needs.","zh":"當現有選項無法滿足新需要，人們就會另尋他處。"},{"en":"The phrase describes seeking alternatives.","zh":"這個短語描述尋找替代方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"transport developments","meaning":"交通發展","examples":[{"en":"Transport developments created a demand for new bridge designs.","zh":"交通發展產生了對新橋樑設計的需求。"},{"en":"Transport developments are changes or improvements in how people and goods move.","zh":"transport developments 是人和貨物移動方式的改變或改善。"},{"en":"The growth of electric buses is a transport development that may change city planning.","zh":"電動巴士增長是一種可能改變城市規劃的交通發展。"},{"en":"New transport systems often require new roads, stations, bridges or rules.","zh":"新交通系統常需要新道路、車站、橋樑或規則。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to progress or change in transport.","zh":"這個短語指交通方面的進步或變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"spark a major change","meaning":"觸發重大改變","examples":[{"en":"The automobile sparked a major change in bridge engineering.","zh":"汽車觸發了橋樑工程的重大改變。"},{"en":"To spark a major change means to cause an important change to begin.","zh":"spark a major change 指引發一項重要改變開始。"},{"en":"A new exam format can spark a major change in how teachers prepare lessons.","zh":"新考試形式可以觸發老師備課方式的重大改變。"},{"en":"One invention or event can trigger changes across an entire system.","zh":"一項發明或事件可以觸發整個系統的變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the starting cause of significant change.","zh":"這個短語描述重大改變的起始原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"complete the labels","meaning":"完成標籤","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the labels on the diagrams.","zh":"考生完成圖表上的標籤。"},{"en":"To complete the labels means to fill in the missing names or words on a diagram.","zh":"complete the labels 指填寫圖表上缺失的名稱或詞語。"},{"en":"In a science test, students may complete the labels of a plant diagram.","zh":"在科學測驗中，學生可能完成植物圖的標籤。"},{"en":"Correct labels show that students understand each part and its position.","zh":"正確標籤顯示學生理解每個部分及其位置。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction for diagram-completion questions.","zh":"這個短語是圖表填充題常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"using one or two words","meaning":"使用一至兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the labels using one or two words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的一至兩個字完成標籤。"},{"en":"Using one or two words means the answer must contain only one word or two words.","zh":"using one or two words 指答案只可包含一個或兩個英文詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “vertical walls,” it fits because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “vertical walls”，它符合要求，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing three words can make an answer wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使想法正確，寫三個詞也可能令答案錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit for exam answers.","zh":"這個短語給出考試答案的嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"from the reading passage","meaning":"來自閱讀篇章","examples":[{"en":"The answers must come from the reading passage.","zh":"答案必須來自閱讀篇章。"},{"en":"From the reading passage means taken directly from the text provided in the exam.","zh":"from the reading passage 指直接取自考試提供的文本。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge if the question says answers must come from the reading passage.","zh":"如果題目說答案必須來自閱讀篇章，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This instruction keeps answers grounded in the source text.","zh":"這個指示令答案緊扣來源文本。"},{"en":"The phrase tells candidates where to find the answer.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生在哪裏找答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"complete each statement","meaning":"完成每句陳述","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete each statement with the best ending.","zh":"考生用最佳句尾完成每句陳述。"},{"en":"To complete each statement means to finish every sentence by adding the missing part.","zh":"complete each statement 指透過加入缺失部分完成每個句子。"},{"en":"In a reading task, students complete each statement by choosing an ending that matches the passage.","zh":"在閱讀任務中，學生透過選擇符合文章的句尾來完成每句陳述。"},{"en":"Grammar and meaning must both fit for the statement to be correct.","zh":"文法和意思都必須合適，陳述才正確。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a sentence-completion task.","zh":"這個短語描述句子完成題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the best ending","meaning":"最佳句尾","examples":[{"en":"Each statement should be matched with the best ending.","zh":"每句陳述應配對最佳句尾。"},{"en":"The best ending is the option that completes the sentence most accurately and naturally.","zh":"best ending 是最準確且最自然地完成句子的選項。"},{"en":"A student should choose the best ending by checking both grammar and passage meaning.","zh":"學生應透過檢查文法和文章意思選擇最佳句尾。"},{"en":"Similar endings may be tempting, so careful comparison is necessary.","zh":"相似句尾可能很有迷惑性，所以必須仔細比較。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the most suitable sentence ending.","zh":"這個短語指最合適的句子結尾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"from the box below","meaning":"從下面方框中","examples":[{"en":"The endings are chosen from the box below.","zh":"句尾從下面方框中選出。"},{"en":"From the box below means the answers must be selected from the options shown underneath.","zh":"from the box below 指答案必須從下方列出的選項中選取。"},{"en":"Students should choose from the box below instead of writing their own endings.","zh":"學生應從下面方框中選擇，而不是自己寫句尾。"},{"en":"This instruction limits the answer choices and helps candidates focus.","zh":"這個指示限制答案選項，幫助考生集中注意。"},{"en":"The phrase tells students where the answer options are located.","zh":"這個短語告訴學生答案選項位於哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"prove someone wrong","meaning":"證明某人錯誤","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that Maillart wanted to prove local people wrong.","zh":"該選項暗示 Maillart 想證明當地人錯誤。"},{"en":"To prove someone wrong means to show through evidence or results that their belief was mistaken.","zh":"prove someone wrong 指透過證據或結果顯示某人的看法錯誤。"},{"en":"A student may prove critics wrong by improving after months of practice.","zh":"學生可能透過數月練習後進步來證明批評者錯誤。"},{"en":"Results can prove someone wrong more powerfully than arguments alone.","zh":"結果比單靠論辯更有力地證明某人錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes showing that another person’s judgement was incorrect.","zh":"這個短語描述顯示另一人的判斷不正確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"local people","meaning":"當地人","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to local people’s judgement of the bridge.","zh":"該選項指當地人對橋樑的判斷。"},{"en":"Local people are people who live in the area being discussed.","zh":"local people 是住在所討論地區的人。"},{"en":"Local people may know which roads flood after heavy rain.","zh":"當地人可能知道哪些道路在暴雨後會水浸。"},{"en":"Their views matter because they use and see public structures every day.","zh":"他們的看法重要，因為他們每天使用和看見公共結構。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to residents or community members of a place.","zh":"這個短語指某地的居民或社區成員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"find work in","meaning":"在……找到工作","examples":[{"en":"After Tavanasa, Maillart struggled to find work in bridge design.","zh":"在 Tavanasa 之後，Maillart 難以在橋樑設計中找到工作。"},{"en":"To find work in a field means to get paid jobs or projects in that area.","zh":"find work in 某領域，指在該範疇取得有薪工作或項目。"},{"en":"A graduate may find work in education after tutoring younger students.","zh":"畢業生在輔導低年級學生後，可能在教育界找到工作。"},{"en":"If clients reject someone’s style, it may be difficult to find work in that field.","zh":"如果客戶拒絕某人的風格，他可能難以在該領域找到工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes securing employment or commissions.","zh":"這個短語描述取得工作或委託。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"win more building commissions","meaning":"贏得更多建築委託","examples":[{"en":"Maillart later tried to win more building commissions.","zh":"Maillart 後來嘗試贏得更多建築委託。"},{"en":"To win more building commissions means to obtain more paid design or construction projects.","zh":"win more building commissions 指取得更多有薪設計或建造項目。"},{"en":"An architect may win more building commissions after one successful public project.","zh":"建築師在完成一個成功公共項目後，可能贏得更多建築委託。"},{"en":"Commissions bring income and chances to develop a professional reputation.","zh":"委託帶來收入，也帶來發展專業聲譽的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gaining more contracted building work.","zh":"這個短語描述取得更多合約式建築工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"reduce the amount of raw material required","meaning":"減少所需原材料數量","examples":[{"en":"The hollow-box arch reduced the amount of raw material required.","zh":"空心箱形拱減少了所需原材料數量。"},{"en":"To reduce the amount of raw material required means to use less basic building material for the same job.","zh":"reduce the amount of raw material required 指完成同一工作時使用較少基本建造材料。"},{"en":"A factory may redesign packaging to reduce the amount of raw material required.","zh":"工廠可能重新設計包裝，以減少所需原材料數量。"},{"en":"Using less raw material can lower cost, weight and waste.","zh":"使用較少原材料可以降低成本、重量和浪費。"},{"en":"The phrase describes material efficiency.","zh":"這個短語描述材料效率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"recognise one’s technical skills","meaning":"認可某人的技術能力","examples":[{"en":"Engineers were slow to recognise Maillart’s technical skills.","zh":"工程師很遲才認可 Maillart 的技術能力。"},{"en":"To recognise one’s technical skills means to acknowledge that someone has strong practical or engineering ability.","zh":"recognise one’s technical skills 指承認某人有強實用或工程能力。"},{"en":"A manager may recognise a worker’s technical skills after seeing her repair a complex machine.","zh":"經理看見員工修理複雜機器後，可能認可她的技術能力。"},{"en":"Recognition may be delayed if someone’s methods are unusual.","zh":"如果某人的方法不尋常，認可可能會延遲。"},{"en":"The phrase describes professional appreciation of ability.","zh":"這個短語描述對能力的專業欣賞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"capitalise on","meaning":"充分利用","examples":[{"en":"The Salginatobel Bridge allowed Maillart to capitalise on the spectacular terrain.","zh":"Salginatobel Bridge 讓 Maillart 充分利用壯觀地形。"},{"en":"To capitalise on something means to use it effectively to gain an advantage.","zh":"capitalise on 某事，指有效利用它來取得優勢。"},{"en":"A school can capitalise on its good library by running reading clubs there.","zh":"學校可以透過在優良圖書館舉辦閱讀會來充分利用它。"},{"en":"Maillart capitalised on the dramatic valley by designing a bridge that looked powerful in that setting.","zh":"Maillart 透過設計在該環境中看起來有力量的橋，充分利用壯觀山谷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making good use of an opportunity or feature.","zh":"這個短語描述善用機會或特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"spectacular terrain","meaning":"壯觀地形","examples":[{"en":"The bridge made use of spectacular terrain.","zh":"這座橋利用了壯觀地形。"},{"en":"Spectacular terrain is land or landscape that looks dramatic and impressive.","zh":"spectacular terrain 是看起來壯麗而令人印象深刻的土地或景觀。"},{"en":"A hiking trail through cliffs and waterfalls may pass through spectacular terrain.","zh":"穿過峭壁和瀑布的遠足徑可能經過壯觀地形。"},{"en":"Spectacular terrain can make construction difficult but visually memorable.","zh":"壯觀地形可以令施工困難，但在視覺上令人難忘。"},{"en":"The phrase describes powerful natural surroundings.","zh":"這個短語描述有力量的自然環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"improve the appearance of","meaning":"改善……的外觀","examples":[{"en":"Maillart refined his designs to improve the appearance of his bridges.","zh":"Maillart 改良自己的設計，以改善橋樑外觀。"},{"en":"To improve the appearance of something means to make it look better.","zh":"improve the appearance of 某物，指令它看起來更好。"},{"en":"A school may plant trees to improve the appearance of its entrance.","zh":"學校可能種樹以改善入口外觀。"},{"en":"Better appearance can make a useful structure more accepted by the public.","zh":"更好的外觀可以令有用結構更受公眾接受。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on visual improvement.","zh":"這個短語重點在視覺改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"design the hollow-box arch","meaning":"設計空心箱形拱","examples":[{"en":"Maillart designed the hollow-box arch to reduce material use.","zh":"Maillart 設計空心箱形拱以減少材料使用。"},{"en":"To design the hollow-box arch means to create the structural form with hollow box-like spaces in the arch system.","zh":"design the hollow-box arch 指創造在拱形系統中有箱形空腔的結構形式。"},{"en":"An engineer designs a new roof shape to reduce weight while keeping the building safe.","zh":"工程師設計新屋頂形狀，以減少重量同時保持建築安全。"},{"en":"Designing a hollow form can save material if the remaining parts still carry the load well.","zh":"如果剩餘部分仍能妥善承載負荷，設計空心形式可以節省材料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating a specific efficient bridge form.","zh":"這個短語描述創造一種特定高效橋樑形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"following the construction of","meaning":"在……建成後","examples":[{"en":"Following the construction of the Tavanasa Bridge, Maillart received little support.","zh":"在 Tavanasa Bridge 建成後，Maillart 幾乎沒有得到支持。"},{"en":"Following the construction of something means after it was built.","zh":"following the construction of 某物，指在它建成之後。"},{"en":"Following the construction of a new sports centre, more students joined after-school clubs.","zh":"在新體育中心建成後，更多學生參加課後活動。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show what happened after a building project was completed.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示建築項目完成後發生甚麼。"},{"en":"It marks a later result in the timeline.","zh":"它標記時間線中的後續結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"fail to","meaning":"未能……","examples":[{"en":"Maillart failed to win more bridge projects after Tavanasa.","zh":"Maillart 在 Tavanasa 之後未能贏得更多橋樑項目。"},{"en":"To fail to do something means not to succeed in doing it.","zh":"fail to do something 指未能成功做某事。"},{"en":"A student may fail to submit homework if she forgets the deadline.","zh":"如果學生忘記截止日期，可能未能提交功課。"},{"en":"Failing to get opportunities can force a person to change direction.","zh":"未能取得機會可以迫使人改變方向。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an unsuccessful attempt or outcome.","zh":"這個短語描述不成功的嘗試或結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"allow someone to","meaning":"使某人能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The transverse walls allowed Maillart to make the arch thinner.","zh":"橫向牆使 Maillart 能夠把拱做得更薄。"},{"en":"To allow someone to do something means to make it possible for that person to do it.","zh":"allow someone to do something 指使某人能夠做某事。"},{"en":"Online dictionaries allow students to check pronunciation quickly.","zh":"網上字典使學生能夠快速查發音。"},{"en":"A good design feature can allow an engineer to reduce material without losing strength.","zh":"好的設計特徵可以使工程師在不失去強度下減少材料。"},{"en":"The phrase links a condition or tool with a new possibility.","zh":"這個短語把條件或工具與新可能性連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"of all his bridges","meaning":"在他所有橋樑之中","examples":[{"en":"Of all his bridges, Salginatobel had the most dramatic setting.","zh":"在他所有橋樑之中，Salginatobel 的環境最壯觀。"},{"en":"Of all his bridges means when comparing every bridge he designed or built.","zh":"of all his bridges 指在比較他設計或建造的每一座橋時。"},{"en":"Of all her essays, the final one had the clearest argument.","zh":"在她所有文章之中，最後一篇論點最清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a comparison within one person’s whole set of works.","zh":"這個短語引出某人所有作品內部的比較。"},{"en":"It helps identify the strongest example among many.","zh":"它幫助在眾多例子中指出最強的一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 104 - The Revolutionary Bridges of Robert Maillart.pdf","sourcePage":22}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 105":[{"front":"talented or gifted","meaning":"有才華或有天賦的","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses what we mean by being talented or gifted.","zh":"篇章討論我們所說的有才華或有天賦是甚麼意思。"},{"en":"Someone who is talented or gifted has an unusually strong ability in one or more areas.","zh":"有才華或有天賦的人，在一個或多個範疇具有異常強的能力。"},{"en":"A talented or gifted student may learn music, maths, or sport much faster than classmates.","zh":"有才華或有天賦的學生可能在音樂、數學或運動方面比同學學得快很多。"},{"en":"Being talented or gifted can lead to special opportunities, but the person still needs practice and support.","zh":"有才華或有天賦可以帶來特別機會，但當事人仍需要練習和支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unusual ability, not automatic success.","zh":"這個短語描述非凡能力，而不是自動成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what do we mean by","meaning":"我們所指的是甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The writer asks what we mean by being talented or gifted.","zh":"作者問，我們所說的有才華或有天賦是甚麼意思。"},{"en":"What do we mean by something asks for the real meaning or definition of an idea.","zh":"我們所指的是甚麼，是要求說明某個概念的真正意思或定義。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask, “What do we mean by fairness?” before discussing school rules.","zh":"老師在討論校規前可能會問：「我們所說的公平是甚麼意思？」"},{"en":"This question is useful when a common word has several possible meanings.","zh":"當一個常用詞有幾種可能意思時，這個問題很有用。"},{"en":"It invites people to define an idea clearly before arguing about it.","zh":"它邀請人們在爭論前先清楚界定概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the most obvious way","meaning":"最明顯的方法","examples":[{"en":"The most obvious way is to look at the work someone does.","zh":"最明顯的方法是看某人所做的工作。"},{"en":"The most obvious way means the clearest and easiest method to think of first.","zh":"最明顯的方法，是最清楚、最容易首先想到的方法。"},{"en":"The most obvious way to check if a phone is charged is to look at the battery icon.","zh":"檢查手機是否有電，最明顯的方法是看電池圖示。"},{"en":"Starting with the most obvious way can save time before trying more complex methods.","zh":"先從最明顯的方法開始，可以在嘗試更複雜方法前節省時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first simple approach people naturally consider.","zh":"這個短語描述人們自然首先想到的簡單方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"look at","meaning":"看；考慮","examples":[{"en":"One way to judge talent is to look at the work someone does.","zh":"判斷才能的一種方法，是看某人所做的工作。"},{"en":"To look at something can mean to examine or consider it carefully.","zh":"look at 某事，可以指仔細檢視或考慮它。"},{"en":"A teacher may look at a student’s essays to understand their writing ability.","zh":"老師可能會看學生的作文，以了解其寫作能力。"},{"en":"If we look at results only, we may miss effort, training, or opportunity.","zh":"如果我們只看結果，可能會忽略努力、訓練或機會。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean more than seeing with the eyes; it can mean evaluating.","zh":"這個短語不只是用眼睛看，也可以指評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be capable of","meaning":"有能力……","examples":[{"en":"A person may be labelled talented if they are capable of significant success.","zh":"如果一個人有能力取得重大成功，他可能會被標籤為有才華。"},{"en":"To be capable of something means to have the ability to do it.","zh":"有能力做某事，是指具備做到該事的能力。"},{"en":"A hardworking student may be capable of passing a difficult exam with enough practice.","zh":"勤奮的學生在足夠練習下可能有能力通過困難考試。"},{"en":"Being capable of success does not mean success will happen without effort.","zh":"有能力成功不代表不用努力就一定成功。"},{"en":"This phrase describes potential or ability.","zh":"這個短語描述潛力或能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"significant success","meaning":"重大成功","examples":[{"en":"Talented people are often capable of significant success.","zh":"有才華的人通常有能力取得重大成功。"},{"en":"Significant success means important or impressive achievement, not just a small win.","zh":"重大成功，是重要或令人印象深刻的成就，而不只是小勝利。"},{"en":"Winning a national music competition would be significant success for a young pianist.","zh":"贏得全國音樂比賽，對年輕鋼琴家而言會是重大成功。"},{"en":"Significant success usually requires ability, effort, opportunity, and support.","zh":"重大成功通常需要能力、努力、機會和支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes achievement that is meaningful and noticeable.","zh":"這個短語描述有意義而明顯的成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"label someone as","meaning":"將某人標籤為……","examples":[{"en":"People may label successful individuals as talented.","zh":"人們可能將成功人士標籤為有才華。"},{"en":"To label someone as something means to describe or classify them in that way.","zh":"將某人標籤為某類人，是指用那種方式描述或分類他們。"},{"en":"A quiet child may be labelled as shy even if they are simply thinking carefully.","zh":"安靜的孩子可能被標籤為害羞，即使他只是正在仔細思考。"},{"en":"Labels can influence how teachers, parents, and classmates treat a person.","zh":"標籤會影響老師、父母和同學如何對待一個人。"},{"en":"This phrase can be neutral, but it may also suggest oversimplification.","zh":"這個短語可以是中性的，但也可能暗示過度簡化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"purely quantitative route","meaning":"純粹量化的方法","examples":[{"en":"The purely quantitative route looks at simple percentages.","zh":"純粹量化的方法看的是簡單百分比。"},{"en":"A purely quantitative route uses numbers only, rather than personal qualities or detailed judgement.","zh":"純粹量化的方法只使用數字，而不是個人特質或詳細判斷。"},{"en":"A school may take a purely quantitative route by choosing only the top 5% of test scores.","zh":"學校可能採用純粹量化的方法，只選測驗成績最高的百分之五學生。"},{"en":"This method is simple, but it may ignore creativity, effort, and different kinds of talent.","zh":"這種方法簡單，但可能忽略創造力、努力和不同種類的才能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a number-based approach.","zh":"這個短語描述以數字為基礎的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"percentage definition","meaning":"百分比定義","examples":[{"en":"The percentage definition labels the top part of the population as gifted.","zh":"百分比定義把人口中最高的一部分標籤為有天賦。"},{"en":"A percentage definition defines a group by using a fixed percentage.","zh":"百分比定義是用固定百分比來界定一個群體。"},{"en":"A school may call the top 10% of runners gifted under a percentage definition.","zh":"根據百分比定義，學校可能把最快的百分之十跑手稱為有天賦。"},{"en":"This definition is easy to apply, but it may not explain why those people are talented.","zh":"這種定義容易應用，但未必解釋那些人為何有才華。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a definition based on rank or proportion.","zh":"這個短語描述基於排名或比例的定義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"looks not at individuals, but at","meaning":"看的不是個人，而是……","examples":[{"en":"The percentage definition looks not at individuals, but at simple percentages.","zh":"百分比定義看的不是個人，而是簡單百分比。"},{"en":"Looks not at A, but at B means it focuses on B instead of A.","zh":"看的不是 A，而是 B，是指它聚焦 B 而不是 A。"},{"en":"A school ranking looks not at each child’s story, but at exam marks.","zh":"學校排名看的不是每個孩子的故事，而是考試分數。"},{"en":"This contrast shows what a method includes and what it leaves out.","zh":"這種對比顯示一種方法包括甚麼，又排除了甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when explaining a shift in focus.","zh":"這個短語適合用於解釋焦點轉移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"simple percentages","meaning":"簡單百分比","examples":[{"en":"The definition is based on simple percentages of the population.","zh":"這個定義以人口中的簡單百分比為基礎。"},{"en":"Simple percentages are basic numerical proportions, such as 5% or 10%.","zh":"簡單百分比是基本數字比例，例如百分之五或百分之十。"},{"en":"A teacher may use simple percentages to show how many students passed a test.","zh":"老師可能用簡單百分比顯示有多少學生通過測驗。"},{"en":"Simple percentages are easy to understand, but they may hide individual differences.","zh":"簡單百分比容易理解，但可能掩蓋個體差異。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to basic percentage figures, not detailed analysis.","zh":"這個短語指基本百分比數字，而不是詳細分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the top five per cent of","meaning":"最高的百分之五","examples":[{"en":"The top five per cent of the population may be labelled gifted.","zh":"人口中最高的百分之五可能被標籤為有天賦。"},{"en":"The top five per cent of a group means the highest-ranking 5% within that group.","zh":"某群體最高的百分之五，是該群體中排名最高的百分之五。"},{"en":"The top five per cent of students in a maths test may receive a special award.","zh":"數學測驗中最高的百分之五學生可能獲得特別獎。"},{"en":"This method selects a small elite group, but it may miss talents outside the measured area.","zh":"這種方法選出一小群精英，但可能錯過測量範圍以外的才能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the highest proportion within a larger group.","zh":"這個短語描述較大群體中的最高比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"by definition","meaning":"按定義來說","examples":[{"en":"The top five per cent are labelled gifted by definition.","zh":"按定義來說，最高的百分之五被標籤為有天賦。"},{"en":"By definition means according to the meaning or rule already chosen.","zh":"按定義來說，是指按照已選定的意思或規則。"},{"en":"By definition, a triangle has three sides.","zh":"按定義來說，三角形有三條邊。"},{"en":"If giftedness is defined as the top 5%, then those people are gifted by definition.","zh":"如果天賦被定義為最高百分之五，那些人按定義來說就是有天賦。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a conclusion follows from the definition itself.","zh":"這個短語顯示結論來自定義本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fallen from favour","meaning":"不再受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The percentage definition has fallen from favour.","zh":"百分比定義已不再受歡迎。"},{"en":"To have fallen from favour means to become less popular or less accepted than before.","zh":"不再受歡迎，是指比以前較不流行或較不被接受。"},{"en":"A teaching method may fall from favour if research shows it does not help students much.","zh":"如果研究顯示某教學方法對學生幫助不大，它可能不再受歡迎。"},{"en":"The percentage definition fell from favour as other ways of measuring ability became popular.","zh":"隨着其他能力測量方法變得流行，百分比定義不再受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a loss of approval over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間失去認同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"eclipsed by","meaning":"被……蓋過；被……取代","examples":[{"en":"The percentage definition was eclipsed by the advent of IQ tests.","zh":"百分比定義被智商測驗的出現蓋過。"},{"en":"To be eclipsed by something means to be overshadowed or replaced by something more influential.","zh":"被某物蓋過，是指被更有影響力的事物遮蓋或取代。"},{"en":"An old phone model may be eclipsed by a newer model with better features.","zh":"舊手機型號可能被功能更好的新型號取代。"},{"en":"The percentage definition lost attention when IQ tests became more popular.","zh":"當智商測驗變得更流行，百分比定義便失去注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one thing being pushed into the background by another.","zh":"這個短語描述一事物被另一事物推到背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the advent of","meaning":"……的出現","examples":[{"en":"The advent of IQ tests changed how talent was defined.","zh":"智商測驗的出現改變了才能如何被定義。"},{"en":"The advent of something means the arrival or beginning of something important.","zh":"某事的出現，是重要事物的到來或開始。"},{"en":"The advent of smartphones changed how people communicate.","zh":"智能手機的出現改變了人們溝通的方式。"},{"en":"The advent of a new tool can replace older ways of doing things.","zh":"新工具的出現可以取代較舊做法。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often describes major social or technological change.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常描述重大社會或科技變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"IQ tests","meaning":"智商測驗","examples":[{"en":"IQ tests became a popular way to assess intelligence.","zh":"智商測驗成為評估智力的流行方法。"},{"en":"IQ tests are tests designed to measure a person’s general intelligence score.","zh":"智商測驗是用來量度一個人一般智力分數的測驗。"},{"en":"A school psychologist may use IQ tests as one part of assessing a child’s learning needs.","zh":"學校心理學家可能把智商測驗作為評估孩子學習需要的一部分。"},{"en":"IQ tests can provide useful information, but they may not measure every kind of talent.","zh":"智商測驗可以提供有用資料，但未必量度每一種才能。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal tests of intellectual ability.","zh":"這個短語指正式的智力能力測驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"favoured by","meaning":"受……青睞","examples":[{"en":"IQ tests were favoured by luminaries such as Professor Hans Eysenck.","zh":"智商測驗受到 Hans Eysenck 教授等權威人物青睞。"},{"en":"To be favoured by someone means to be preferred or supported by them.","zh":"受某人青睞，是指被他們偏好或支持。"},{"en":"Online homework may be favoured by teachers because it is easy to collect.","zh":"網上功課可能受老師青睞，因為容易收集。"},{"en":"When a method is favoured by experts, it may become more widely used.","zh":"當某方法受專家青睞，它可能變得更廣泛使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes approval or preference.","zh":"這個短語描述認同或偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"luminaries such as","meaning":"……等權威人物","examples":[{"en":"The tests were favoured by luminaries such as Professor Hans Eysenck.","zh":"這些測驗受到 Hans Eysenck 教授等權威人物青睞。"},{"en":"Luminaries such as someone are famous and respected people in a field.","zh":"某些權威人物，是指某領域中著名且受尊敬的人。"},{"en":"A young scientist may be inspired by luminaries such as Marie Curie or Albert Einstein.","zh":"年輕科學家可能受到 Marie Curie 或 Albert Einstein 等權威人物啟發。"},{"en":"Support from luminaries can make an idea seem more credible.","zh":"權威人物的支持可以令某想法看起來更可信。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces respected examples of important people.","zh":"這個短語引入重要人物的受尊敬例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a series of","meaning":"一系列","examples":[{"en":"IQ tests use a series of written or verbal tests.","zh":"智商測驗使用一系列書面或口頭測驗。"},{"en":"A series of something means several things arranged one after another.","zh":"一系列某物，是指幾件事物一個接一個排列。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students a series of short quizzes before the final exam.","zh":"老師可能在期末試前給學生一系列小測驗。"},{"en":"A series of tests can measure ability from several angles.","zh":"一系列測驗可以從幾個角度量度能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes multiple connected items or events.","zh":"這個短語描述多個相連項目或事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"written or verbal tests","meaning":"書面或口頭測驗","examples":[{"en":"IQ tests include written or verbal tests of general intelligence.","zh":"智商測驗包括一般智力的書面或口頭測驗。"},{"en":"Written or verbal tests are tests answered in writing or by speaking.","zh":"書面或口頭測驗，是透過寫作或說話作答的測驗。"},{"en":"A language exam may include written tests for grammar and verbal tests for speaking.","zh":"語文考試可能包括測試文法的書面測驗和測試說話的口頭測驗。"},{"en":"Different test formats may reveal different strengths and weaknesses.","zh":"不同測驗形式可能揭示不同強項和弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two common ways of assessing ability.","zh":"這個短語描述評估能力的兩種常見方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"general intelligence","meaning":"一般智力","examples":[{"en":"IQ tests aim to measure general intelligence.","zh":"智商測驗旨在量度一般智力。"},{"en":"General intelligence means overall thinking ability, such as reasoning, understanding, and problem-solving.","zh":"一般智力是整體思考能力，例如推理、理解和解決問題。"},{"en":"A child with strong general intelligence may learn new school subjects quickly.","zh":"一般智力強的孩子可能很快學會新學科。"},{"en":"General intelligence is useful, but it is not the same as creativity, motivation, or artistic talent.","zh":"一般智力有用，但它不等同於創造力、動力或藝術才能。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to broad mental ability.","zh":"這個短語指廣泛心智能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"leads to","meaning":"導致；產生","examples":[{"en":"A series of tests leads to an intelligence score.","zh":"一系列測驗會產生一個智力分數。"},{"en":"To lead to something means to produce or result in it.","zh":"導致某事，是指產生或造成它。"},{"en":"Regular practice can lead to better exam performance.","zh":"定期練習可以帶來更好的考試表現。"},{"en":"In testing, several answers may lead to one final score.","zh":"在測驗中，多個答案可能產生一個最終分數。"},{"en":"This phrase shows cause and result.","zh":"這個短語顯示原因和結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"intelligence score","meaning":"智力分數","examples":[{"en":"IQ tests produce an intelligence score.","zh":"智商測驗產生一個智力分數。"},{"en":"An intelligence score is a number intended to represent a person’s measured mental ability.","zh":"智力分數是用來代表某人被量度心智能力的數字。"},{"en":"A student’s intelligence score may be used with other information to understand learning needs.","zh":"學生的智力分數可能與其他資料一起用來理解學習需要。"},{"en":"A score can be useful, but it cannot show every part of a person’s talent.","zh":"分數可以有用，但不能顯示一個人才能的每一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a numerical result from an intelligence test.","zh":"這個短語指智力測驗所得的數字結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"eclipsed in turn","meaning":"隨後又被取代","examples":[{"en":"The IQ test has been eclipsed in turn.","zh":"智商測驗隨後又被取代。"},{"en":"To be eclipsed in turn means to be replaced or overshadowed later by something else.","zh":"隨後又被取代，是指後來被另一事物蓋過或取代。"},{"en":"A popular app may be eclipsed in turn when a newer app becomes more useful.","zh":"一個受歡迎的應用程式可能在較新、更有用的應用出現後又被取代。"},{"en":"IQ tests were once influential, but later broader approaches challenged them.","zh":"智商測驗曾經有影響力，但後來更廣泛的方法挑戰了它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one dominant idea can later lose importance.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個主導想法後來也可能失去重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"studying intelligence and creativity","meaning":"研究智力和創造力","examples":[{"en":"Many researchers are studying intelligence and creativity.","zh":"許多研究人員正在研究智力和創造力。"},{"en":"Studying intelligence and creativity means researching how people think, solve problems, and produce original ideas.","zh":"研究智力和創造力，是研究人們如何思考、解決問題和產生原創想法。"},{"en":"A psychologist may study intelligence and creativity by observing children solving puzzles and drawing stories.","zh":"心理學家可能透過觀察兒童解謎和畫故事來研究智力和創造力。"},{"en":"This research can show that talent is broader than test scores.","zh":"這種研究可以顯示才能比測驗分數更廣泛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes academic investigation into mental ability and originality.","zh":"這個短語描述對心智能力和原創性的學術研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the new millennium","meaning":"在新千禧年代","examples":[{"en":"Researchers in the new millennium prefer a broader definition.","zh":"新千禧年代的研究人員較喜歡更廣泛的定義。"},{"en":"In the new millennium means in the period after the year 2000.","zh":"在新千禧年代，是指在 2000 年之後的時期。"},{"en":"In the new millennium, schools have used more digital tools in learning.","zh":"在新千禧年代，學校在學習中使用更多數碼工具。"},{"en":"New ideas in the new millennium may replace older ways of measuring talent.","zh":"新千禧年代的新想法可能取代較舊的才能測量方法。"},{"en":"This phrase places an idea in a modern time period.","zh":"這個短語把某想法放在現代時期中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prefer a broader definition","meaning":"較喜歡更廣泛的定義","examples":[{"en":"Modern researchers prefer a broader definition of talent.","zh":"現代研究人員較喜歡更廣泛的才能定義。"},{"en":"To prefer a broader definition means to choose a wider meaning that includes more examples or areas.","zh":"較喜歡更廣泛的定義，是指選擇涵蓋更多例子或範疇的較寬意思。"},{"en":"A teacher may prefer a broader definition of success that includes effort, progress, and confidence.","zh":"老師可能較喜歡更廣泛的成功定義，包括努力、進步和信心。"},{"en":"A broader definition of talent can include music, sport, leadership, and creativity.","zh":"更廣泛的才能定義可以包括音樂、運動、領導和創造力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving beyond a narrow meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述超越狹窄意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"multifaceted approach","meaning":"多方面的方法","examples":[{"en":"A multifaceted approach recognises talents in many areas.","zh":"多方面的方法承認許多範疇中的才能。"},{"en":"A multifaceted approach considers several different sides of a subject.","zh":"多方面的方法會考慮一個主題的幾個不同層面。"},{"en":"A school may use a multifaceted approach by looking at exams, projects, teamwork, and creativity.","zh":"學校可以透過考慮考試、專題、團隊合作和創造力來採用多方面的方法。"},{"en":"This approach can give a fairer picture because talent does not appear in only one form.","zh":"這種方法可以提供更公平的圖像，因為才能不只以一種形式出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broad, many-sided method.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛而多面向的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"talents in many areas","meaning":"多方面的才能","examples":[{"en":"Modern definitions recognise talents in many areas.","zh":"現代定義承認多方面的才能。"},{"en":"Talents in many areas means abilities in different fields, not only one subject.","zh":"多方面的才能，是指不同領域的能力，而不只是一個科目。"},{"en":"A child may show talents in many areas, such as drawing, sport, problem-solving, and speaking.","zh":"孩子可能在繪畫、運動、解難和說話等方面顯示多方面的才能。"},{"en":"Recognising many areas helps schools avoid judging students by exam marks alone.","zh":"承認多方面才能有助學校避免只用考試分數判斷學生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a wider view of ability.","zh":"這個短語描述對能力較廣泛的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be recognised","meaning":"被承認","examples":[{"en":"Talents in many areas are recognised in the broader definition.","zh":"在更廣泛的定義中，多方面的才能被承認。"},{"en":"To be recognised means to be noticed, accepted, or valued.","zh":"被承認，是指被注意、接受或重視。"},{"en":"A student’s leadership skills may be recognised when they organise a class event well.","zh":"當學生成功組織班級活動，他的領導能力可能被承認。"},{"en":"When different talents are recognised, more students can feel seen and encouraged.","zh":"當不同才能被承認，更多學生會感到被看見和被鼓勵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ability being acknowledged.","zh":"這個短語描述能力被認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Modern approaches recognise many talents rather than concentrating only on academic achievement.","zh":"現代方法承認多種才能，而不是只集中於學業成就。"},{"en":"Rather than introduces a contrast and means instead of.","zh":"rather than 引入對比，意思是「而不是」。"},{"en":"A student may revise regularly rather than wait until the night before the exam.","zh":"學生可以定期溫習，而不是等到考試前一晚。"},{"en":"Using “rather than” helps show which option is preferred or rejected.","zh":"使用 rather than 有助顯示哪個選擇被偏好或被拒絕。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing two choices or approaches.","zh":"這個短語適合比較兩個選擇或方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"purely concentrating on","meaning":"純粹集中於……","examples":[{"en":"The new approach avoids purely concentrating on academic achievement.","zh":"新方法避免純粹集中於學業成就。"},{"en":"Purely concentrating on something means focusing only on that one thing.","zh":"純粹集中於某事，是指只聚焦於那一件事。"},{"en":"If a school purely concentrates on exam marks, it may ignore art, sport, and kindness.","zh":"如果學校純粹集中於考試分數，可能會忽略藝術、運動和善良。"},{"en":"Purely concentrating on one measure can create an unfair picture of ability.","zh":"純粹集中於一種衡量標準，可能造成不公平的能力圖像。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a narrow focus.","zh":"這個短語描述狹窄焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"academic achievement","meaning":"學業成就","examples":[{"en":"Talent is no longer defined only by academic achievement.","zh":"才能不再只由學業成就界定。"},{"en":"Academic achievement means success in school subjects, exams, or formal study.","zh":"學業成就是在學校科目、考試或正式學習中的成功。"},{"en":"High grades in maths and science are examples of academic achievement.","zh":"數學和科學取得高分是學業成就的例子。"},{"en":"Academic achievement matters, but it does not include every kind of talent.","zh":"學業成就很重要，但並不包括每一種才能。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to success in education.","zh":"這個短語指教育方面的成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"assuming that","meaning":"假設","examples":[{"en":"The writer asks what follows if we are assuming that gifted individuals have many abilities.","zh":"作者問，如果我們假設有天賦的人具有多種能力，接下來會怎樣。"},{"en":"Assuming that means accepting something as true for the purpose of discussion.","zh":"假設，是指為了討論而把某事當作真實。"},{"en":"Assuming that the bus is late, we should leave earlier tomorrow.","zh":"假設巴士遲到，我們明天就應早點出門。"},{"en":"In an argument, assumptions shape what conclusions seem reasonable.","zh":"在論證中，假設會影響哪些結論看起來合理。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a condition or starting idea.","zh":"這個短語引入條件或起始想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"creative individuals","meaning":"有創造力的人","examples":[{"en":"Creative individuals may need to be assessed across a range of abilities.","zh":"有創造力的人可能需要從一系列能力方面被評估。"},{"en":"Creative individuals are people who can produce original ideas, solutions, or works.","zh":"有創造力的人是能產生原創想法、解決方法或作品的人。"},{"en":"A creative individual may solve a school project in an unexpected but effective way.","zh":"有創造力的人可能以意想不到但有效的方法完成學校專題。"},{"en":"Creativity can appear in art, business, science, writing, or everyday problem-solving.","zh":"創造力可以出現在藝術、商業、科學、寫作或日常解難中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people with originality, not just high test scores.","zh":"這個短語描述有原創性的人，而不只是測驗分數高的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"gifted individuals","meaning":"有天賦的人","examples":[{"en":"Gifted individuals may show ability in more than one area.","zh":"有天賦的人可能在多於一個範疇顯示能力。"},{"en":"Gifted individuals are people with unusually high ability or potential.","zh":"有天賦的人是具備異常高能力或潛力的人。"},{"en":"A gifted individual may be strong in music and also quick at solving problems.","zh":"有天賦的人可能在音樂方面很強，也很快解決問題。"},{"en":"Gifted individuals still need support because ability alone may not lead to success.","zh":"有天賦的人仍需要支援，因為能力本身未必帶來成功。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people with exceptional potential.","zh":"這個短語描述具有非凡潛力的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be assessed across","meaning":"從……各方面被評估","examples":[{"en":"Gifted individuals may need to be assessed across a range of abilities.","zh":"有天賦的人可能需要從一系列能力方面被評估。"},{"en":"To be assessed across several areas means to be evaluated in more than one field or skill.","zh":"從幾個範疇被評估，是指在多於一個領域或技能上接受評價。"},{"en":"A student may be assessed across reading, speaking, writing, and teamwork.","zh":"學生可能從閱讀、說話、寫作和團隊合作方面被評估。"},{"en":"Assessing across many areas can reveal strengths that one test may miss.","zh":"從多方面評估可以揭示單一測驗可能錯過的強項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad evaluation.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a range of abilities","meaning":"一系列能力","examples":[{"en":"Talent may need to be assessed across a range of abilities.","zh":"才能可能需要從一系列能力方面被評估。"},{"en":"A range of abilities means several different skills or capacities.","zh":"一系列能力，是指幾種不同技能或能力。"},{"en":"A good leader may need a range of abilities, including communication, planning, and patience.","zh":"好領袖可能需要一系列能力，包括溝通、規劃和耐性。"},{"en":"Looking at a range of abilities gives a fuller picture of a person’s talent.","zh":"觀察一系列能力，可以更完整地了解一個人的才能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes variety in skills.","zh":"這個短語描述技能上的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"run in families","meaning":"在家族中遺傳","examples":[{"en":"The writer asks whether intelligence can run in families.","zh":"作者問智力是否會在家族中遺傳。"},{"en":"If a trait runs in families, it appears often among relatives and may be inherited or shared through family environment.","zh":"如果某特質在家族中出現，是指它常在親屬之間出現，可能源於遺傳或家庭環境。"},{"en":"Musical ability may seem to run in families when several relatives play instruments well.","zh":"當幾位親戚都很會演奏樂器，音樂能力看似在家族中遺傳。"},{"en":"A trait that runs in families may come from genes, upbringing, or both.","zh":"在家族中出現的特質可能來自基因、成長環境，或兩者兼有。"},{"en":"This phrase describes patterns repeated among family members.","zh":"這個短語描述家庭成員之間反覆出現的模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"genetic tendency","meaning":"遺傳傾向","examples":[{"en":"Intelligence may be seen as a genetic tendency.","zh":"智力可能被視為一種遺傳傾向。"},{"en":"A genetic tendency is a likelihood that comes from inherited biological traits.","zh":"遺傳傾向是來自遺傳生物特徵的可能性。"},{"en":"Some families may have a genetic tendency towards tall height.","zh":"有些家庭可能有身材高大的遺傳傾向。"},{"en":"A genetic tendency can influence a person, but environment can still matter greatly.","zh":"遺傳傾向可以影響一個人，但環境仍可以非常重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inherited possibility, not fixed destiny.","zh":"這個短語描述遺傳可能性，而不是固定命運。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"inherited tendency","meaning":"遺傳得來的傾向","examples":[{"en":"The passage asks whether intelligence is an inherited tendency.","zh":"篇章問智力是否是一種遺傳得來的傾向。"},{"en":"An inherited tendency is a tendency passed from parents or ancestors to children.","zh":"遺傳得來的傾向，是由父母或祖先傳給子女的傾向。"},{"en":"A child may have an inherited tendency to be musical if many relatives are musicians.","zh":"如果許多親戚都是音樂家，孩子可能有音樂方面的遺傳傾向。"},{"en":"Inherited tendencies can be strengthened or weakened by environment and practice.","zh":"遺傳傾向可以被環境和練習加強或削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something received through family background.","zh":"這個短語描述透過家庭背景獲得的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mental dysfunction","meaning":"精神功能障礙","examples":[{"en":"Mental dysfunction can sometimes run in families.","zh":"精神功能障礙有時會在家族中出現。"},{"en":"Mental dysfunction refers to problems in thinking, emotion, or mental health that affect normal functioning.","zh":"精神功能障礙是影響正常運作的思考、情緒或心理健康問題。"},{"en":"Severe anxiety can become a mental dysfunction if it stops a person from studying or working normally.","zh":"如果嚴重焦慮阻止一個人正常學習或工作，它可能成為精神功能障礙。"},{"en":"If mental dysfunction appears often in a family, researchers may consider both genetic and environmental causes.","zh":"如果精神功能障礙常在家族中出現，研究人員可能同時考慮遺傳和環境原因。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficulty in mental functioning.","zh":"這個短語描述心理功能上的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"schizophrenia","meaning":"精神分裂症","examples":[{"en":"Schizophrenia is mentioned as an example of mental dysfunction.","zh":"精神分裂症被提及作為精神功能障礙的一個例子。"},{"en":"Schizophrenia is a serious mental disorder that can affect thought, perception, and behaviour.","zh":"精神分裂症是一種嚴重精神障礙，可能影響思想、感知和行為。"},{"en":"A person with schizophrenia may need medical treatment and long-term support.","zh":"患有精神分裂症的人可能需要醫療治療和長期支援。"},{"en":"The passage uses schizophrenia as an example when discussing whether mental traits can run in families.","zh":"篇章在討論精神特質是否會在家族中出現時，用精神分裂症作例子。"},{"en":"This word refers to a specific mental health condition.","zh":"這個詞指一種特定心理健康狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mental capacity","meaning":"心智能力","examples":[{"en":"The writer asks whether efficient mental capacity is passed from parent to child.","zh":"作者問高效心智能力是否由父母傳給子女。"},{"en":"Mental capacity means the ability to think, understand, learn, and make decisions.","zh":"心智能力是思考、理解、學習和作決定的能力。"},{"en":"A student needs mental capacity to solve problems and follow instructions.","zh":"學生需要心智能力來解決問題和跟從指示。"},{"en":"Mental capacity can be influenced by health, education, sleep, and environment.","zh":"心智能力可以受到健康、教育、睡眠和環境影響。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the mind’s ability to function.","zh":"這個短語指心智運作能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"passed on from parent to child","meaning":"由父母傳給子女","examples":[{"en":"Some abilities may be passed on from parent to child.","zh":"有些能力可能由父母傳給子女。"},{"en":"Passed on from parent to child means transmitted from one generation to the next.","zh":"由父母傳給子女，是指由一代傳到下一代。"},{"en":"A family recipe may be passed on from parent to child for many years.","zh":"家庭食譜可能多年來由父母傳給子女。"},{"en":"Traits may be passed on through genes, teaching, example, or family habits.","zh":"特質可以透過基因、教導、榜樣或家庭習慣傳承。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inheritance or transmission within families.","zh":"這個短語描述家庭內的繼承或傳遞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"animal experiments","meaning":"動物實驗","examples":[{"en":"Animal experiments throw some light on intelligence and environment.","zh":"動物實驗為智力和環境提供一些啟示。"},{"en":"Animal experiments are studies in which animals are used to test scientific questions.","zh":"動物實驗是使用動物來測試科學問題的研究。"},{"en":"Scientists may use animal experiments to study learning, memory, or behaviour.","zh":"科學家可能用動物實驗研究學習、記憶或行為。"},{"en":"Animal experiments can suggest ideas about humans, but the results must be interpreted carefully.","zh":"動物實驗可以為人類提供想法，但結果必須謹慎解讀。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to research using animals.","zh":"這個短語指使用動物的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"throw some light on","meaning":"令……更清楚；提供啟示","examples":[{"en":"Animal experiments throw some light on the question of inherited intelligence.","zh":"動物實驗為遺傳智力這個問題提供一些啟示。"},{"en":"To throw some light on something means to help make it clearer.","zh":"為某事提供啟示，是指幫助令它更清楚。"},{"en":"A teacher’s example can throw some light on a difficult grammar rule.","zh":"老師的例子可以令困難文法規則更清楚。"},{"en":"Evidence may not solve a problem completely, but it can throw some light on it.","zh":"證據未必完全解決問題，但可以為它提供啟示。"},{"en":"This phrase describes partial explanation or clarification.","zh":"這個短語描述部分解釋或澄清。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"on the whole area of","meaning":"對……整個範疇","examples":[{"en":"The experiments throw light on the whole area of genetics and environment.","zh":"這些實驗對遺傳和環境整個範疇提供啟示。"},{"en":"On the whole area of something means across the entire field or topic.","zh":"對某事整個範疇，是指橫跨整個領域或主題。"},{"en":"A report may provide evidence on the whole area of student mental health.","zh":"一份報告可能為學生心理健康整個範疇提供證據。"},{"en":"Looking at the whole area helps avoid focusing on one narrow detail only.","zh":"觀察整個範疇有助避免只聚焦一個狹窄細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broad field of discussion.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛討論領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"genetics","meaning":"遺傳因素","examples":[{"en":"The passage considers whether genetics influence intelligence.","zh":"篇章考慮遺傳因素是否影響智力。"},{"en":"Genetics refers to inherited biological information passed from parents to children.","zh":"遺傳因素是由父母傳給子女的生物遺傳資訊。"},{"en":"Genetics can affect eye colour, height, and some health risks.","zh":"遺傳因素可以影響眼睛顏色、身高和某些健康風險。"},{"en":"In talent development, genetics may matter, but environment and opportunity also matter.","zh":"在才能發展中，遺傳因素可能重要，但環境和機會也重要。"},{"en":"This word refers to biological inheritance.","zh":"這個詞指生物遺傳。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the environment","meaning":"環境","examples":[{"en":"The environment can influence intelligence and creative ability.","zh":"環境可以影響智力和創造能力。"},{"en":"The environment means the conditions and surroundings in which a person grows or lives.","zh":"環境是人在其中成長或生活的條件和周遭事物。"},{"en":"A quiet home, supportive parents, and good schools are part of a child’s environment.","zh":"安靜家庭、支持性父母和好學校都是孩子環境的一部分。"},{"en":"The environment can help talent develop or prevent it from growing.","zh":"環境可以幫助才能發展，也可以阻礙它成長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes external influences around a person.","zh":"這個短語描述人周圍的外在影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a combination of the two","meaning":"兩者的結合","examples":[{"en":"Intelligence may depend on genetics, the environment, or a combination of the two.","zh":"智力可能取決於遺傳因素、環境，或兩者的結合。"},{"en":"A combination of the two means both factors working together.","zh":"兩者的結合，是指兩個因素共同發揮作用。"},{"en":"A student’s success may come from natural ability, good teaching, or a combination of the two.","zh":"學生的成功可能來自天生能力、良好教學，或兩者的結合。"},{"en":"When two causes interact, it may be wrong to credit only one of them.","zh":"當兩個原因互相作用，只歸功於其中一個可能是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mixed explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述混合式解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"allows for","meaning":"使……成為可能","examples":[{"en":"The passage asks what allows for intelligence and creative ability.","zh":"篇章問甚麼使智力和創造能力成為可能。"},{"en":"To allow for something means to make it possible or create conditions for it.","zh":"使某事成為可能，是指令它能夠發生或創造條件讓它出現。"},{"en":"A quiet library allows for better concentration.","zh":"安靜的圖書館使更好專注成為可能。"},{"en":"Good teaching and encouragement may allow for talent to develop.","zh":"良好教學和鼓勵可能使才能發展成為可能。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what makes something possible.","zh":"這個短語解釋甚麼令某事能夠發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"creative ability","meaning":"創造能力","examples":[{"en":"The environment can influence creative ability.","zh":"環境可以影響創造能力。"},{"en":"Creative ability is the ability to produce original ideas, solutions, or artistic work.","zh":"創造能力是產生原創想法、解決方法或藝術作品的能力。"},{"en":"A child shows creative ability when they invent a new game using simple objects.","zh":"孩子用簡單物件創作新遊戲時，便顯示創造能力。"},{"en":"Creative ability can grow when people receive encouragement and freedom to experiment.","zh":"當人們得到鼓勵和實驗自由，創造能力可以成長。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to originality and imagination in action.","zh":"這個短語指行動中的原創性和想像力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"strains of rats","meaning":"不同品系的老鼠","examples":[{"en":"Different strains of rats show differences in intelligence.","zh":"不同品系的老鼠在智力方面顯示差異。"},{"en":"Strains of rats are groups of rats bred with particular inherited traits.","zh":"不同品系的老鼠，是帶有特定遺傳特徵而被繁殖出來的老鼠群體。"},{"en":"Scientists may compare different strains of rats to study learning ability.","zh":"科學家可能比較不同品系的老鼠，以研究學習能力。"},{"en":"If one strain performs better, researchers can ask whether genes or environment explain it.","zh":"如果某一品系表現較好，研究人員可以追問是基因還是環境解釋它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to genetically distinct groups of laboratory rats.","zh":"這個短語指實驗室老鼠中基因不同的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"show great differences in","meaning":"在……方面顯示很大差異","examples":[{"en":"Different strains of rats show great differences in intelligence.","zh":"不同品系的老鼠在智力方面顯示很大差異。"},{"en":"To show great differences in something means to display large variation in that area.","zh":"在某方面顯示很大差異，是指在該範疇表現出巨大變化。"},{"en":"Students may show great differences in reading speed even if they are the same age.","zh":"即使同齡，學生在閱讀速度方面也可能顯示很大差異。"},{"en":"Great differences can lead researchers to ask what causes them.","zh":"很大差異會令研究人員追問其成因。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clear variation between groups or people.","zh":"這個短語描述群體或個人之間的明顯變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rat reasoning","meaning":"老鼠推理能力","examples":[{"en":"The experiment tested what the writer calls rat reasoning.","zh":"這個實驗測試作者所說的老鼠推理能力。"},{"en":"Rat reasoning means the problem-solving ability shown by rats in an experiment.","zh":"老鼠推理能力，是老鼠在實驗中表現出的解難能力。"},{"en":"A rat shows rat reasoning when it learns the route through a maze to find food.","zh":"老鼠學會穿過迷宮找到食物時，就顯示老鼠推理能力。"},{"en":"Measuring rat reasoning helps researchers study learning in a controlled way.","zh":"量度老鼠推理能力有助研究人員以受控方式研究學習。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and refers to animal problem-solving.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，指動物解難能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"brought up in normal conditions","meaning":"在正常環境下被飼養","examples":[{"en":"The rats were brought up in normal conditions.","zh":"這些老鼠在正常環境下被飼養。"},{"en":"To be brought up in normal conditions means to be raised in ordinary surroundings.","zh":"在正常環境下被養大，是指在普通周遭條件中成長。"},{"en":"A child brought up in normal conditions has usual food, care, schooling, and safety.","zh":"在正常環境下長大的孩子有一般食物、照顧、上學和安全。"},{"en":"Normal conditions provide a baseline for comparing unusual environments.","zh":"正常環境為比較異常環境提供基準。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the standard upbringing or rearing environment.","zh":"這個短語描述標準成長或飼養環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"run through a maze","meaning":"穿過迷宮","examples":[{"en":"The rats were run through a maze to reach food.","zh":"這些老鼠被安排穿過迷宮以到達食物。"},{"en":"To run through a maze means to move through a confusing path system to find the way out or reach a goal.","zh":"穿過迷宮，是指在複雜路徑系統中移動，以找出口或達到目標。"},{"en":"Children may run through a maze at a playground and try to find the exit.","zh":"孩子可能在遊樂場穿過迷宮，嘗試找到出口。"},{"en":"In experiments, running through a maze can measure learning and memory.","zh":"在實驗中，穿過迷宮可以量度學習和記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes navigating a complicated route.","zh":"這個短語描述在複雜路線中導航。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"maze","meaning":"迷宮","examples":[{"en":"The rats had to run through a maze to reach food.","zh":"這些老鼠必須穿過迷宮才能到達食物。"},{"en":"A maze is a network of paths that makes it difficult to find the correct route.","zh":"迷宮是一個路徑網絡，使人難以找到正確路線。"},{"en":"A garden maze may have many turns and dead ends.","zh":"花園迷宮可能有許多轉彎和死路。"},{"en":"Mazes are useful in experiments because mistakes and learning can be counted.","zh":"迷宮在實驗中有用，因為錯誤和學習可以被計算。"},{"en":"This word describes a confusing path system.","zh":"這個詞描述令人困惑的路徑系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"food goal","meaning":"食物目標","examples":[{"en":"The rats ran through the maze to reach a food goal.","zh":"這些老鼠穿過迷宮以到達食物目標。"},{"en":"A food goal is food used as the target or reward in an experiment.","zh":"食物目標是在實驗中作為目標或獎勵的食物。"},{"en":"A dog may learn a trick faster if a small snack is used as a food goal.","zh":"如果小零食被用作食物目標，狗可能更快學會技巧。"},{"en":"A food goal motivates animals to move, search, and learn.","zh":"食物目標會激勵動物移動、尋找和學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the reward destination in a task.","zh":"這個短語描述任務中的獎勵目的地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"bright strain","meaning":"較聰明的品系","examples":[{"en":"The bright strain made fewer wrong turns.","zh":"較聰明的品系作出的錯誤轉向較少。"},{"en":"A bright strain is a group of animals bred or identified as quicker at learning in an experiment.","zh":"較聰明的品系，是在實驗中被培育或識別為學習較快的動物群體。"},{"en":"The bright strain of rats may remember the maze route faster.","zh":"較聰明的老鼠品系可能更快記住迷宮路線。"},{"en":"Calling them bright means they performed better on the task, not that they think like humans.","zh":"稱牠們較聰明，是指牠們在任務中表現較好，而不是像人類一樣思考。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the more successful experimental group.","zh":"這個短語描述較成功的實驗組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"dull ones","meaning":"較遲鈍的一類","examples":[{"en":"The dull ones made more wrong turns in a normal maze.","zh":"較遲鈍的一類在正常迷宮中作出更多錯誤轉向。"},{"en":"The dull ones are the animals or people described as slower at learning or less quick in a task.","zh":"較遲鈍的一類，是指在某任務中學習較慢或反應較不快的動物或人。"},{"en":"In the rat experiment, the dull ones needed more attempts to find the food.","zh":"在老鼠實驗中，較遲鈍的一類需要更多次嘗試才找到食物。"},{"en":"A dull label may reflect performance in one test, not total ability.","zh":"遲鈍這個標籤可能只反映一項測驗中的表現，而不是全部能力。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with the bright strain.","zh":"這個短語與較聰明的品系形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"far fewer wrong turns","meaning":"少得多的錯誤轉向","examples":[{"en":"The bright strain made far fewer wrong turns.","zh":"較聰明的品系作出的錯誤轉向少得多。"},{"en":"Far fewer wrong turns means many fewer mistakes in choosing direction.","zh":"少得多的錯誤轉向，是指選方向時犯的錯誤大幅減少。"},{"en":"After practising a route to school, a child may make far fewer wrong turns.","zh":"孩子練習上學路線後，可能作出少得多的錯誤轉向。"},{"en":"Fewer wrong turns suggest better memory, learning, or familiarity with the route.","zh":"較少錯誤轉向顯示較好的記憶、學習或路線熟悉度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes much better navigation performance.","zh":"這個短語描述好得多的導航表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"made dull and boring","meaning":"被變得沉悶乏味","examples":[{"en":"If the environment is made dull and boring, the number of errors becomes equal.","zh":"如果環境被變得沉悶乏味，錯誤次數便變得相等。"},{"en":"Made dull and boring means changed so that there is little interest, challenge, or stimulation.","zh":"被變得沉悶乏味，是指被改變成缺乏興趣、挑戰或刺激。"},{"en":"A classroom made dull and boring may reduce students’ motivation to participate.","zh":"被變得沉悶乏味的課室可能降低學生參與動機。"},{"en":"If an environment lacks stimulation, both bright and weaker learners may perform poorly.","zh":"如果環境缺乏刺激，較聰明和較弱的學習者都可能表現差。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an environment that discourages active learning.","zh":"這個短語描述阻礙主動學習的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the number of errors","meaning":"錯誤次數","examples":[{"en":"The number of errors became equal in a dull environment.","zh":"在沉悶環境中，錯誤次數變得相等。"},{"en":"The number of errors means how many mistakes were made.","zh":"錯誤次數，是指犯錯的數量。"},{"en":"A teacher may count the number of errors in a dictation exercise.","zh":"老師可能計算默書練習中的錯誤次數。"},{"en":"If the number of errors falls after practice, learning has probably improved.","zh":"如果練習後錯誤次數下降，學習可能已改善。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a count of mistakes.","zh":"這個短語指錯誤的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"becomes equal","meaning":"變得相等","examples":[{"en":"The number of errors becomes equal when the environment is dull.","zh":"當環境沉悶時，錯誤次數變得相等。"},{"en":"Becomes equal means changes until two or more amounts are the same.","zh":"變得相等，是指改變到兩個或多個數量相同。"},{"en":"If two teams score one goal each, their scores become equal.","zh":"如果兩隊各入一球，比分就變得相等。"},{"en":"In the experiment, equal errors meant the bright and dull rats no longer performed differently.","zh":"在實驗中，錯誤次數相等表示聰明和遲鈍老鼠表現不再不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a difference disappearing.","zh":"這個短語描述差異消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"exciting maze","meaning":"有刺激性的迷宮","examples":[{"en":"The discrepancy returned when the rats were placed in an exciting maze.","zh":"當老鼠被放入有刺激性的迷宮時，差異再次出現。"},{"en":"An exciting maze is a maze with more stimulation, interest, or challenge.","zh":"有刺激性的迷宮，是有更多刺激、趣味或挑戰的迷宮。"},{"en":"Children may enjoy an exciting maze more if it has colours, clues, and hidden paths.","zh":"如果迷宮有顏色、線索和隱藏路線，孩子可能更喜歡它。"},{"en":"A more exciting maze can bring out differences in learning and problem-solving.","zh":"更有刺激性的迷宮可以顯示學習和解難差異。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a stimulating testing environment.","zh":"這個短語描述具刺激性的測試環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"discrepancy","meaning":"差異","examples":[{"en":"The discrepancy returned when the environment became stimulating again.","zh":"當環境再次變得有刺激性，差異又回來了。"},{"en":"A discrepancy is a difference or mismatch between two things that should be compared.","zh":"差異是兩件應被比較的事物之間的不同或不一致。"},{"en":"A discrepancy between attendance records and classroom numbers may show that someone is missing.","zh":"出席紀錄和課室人數之間的差異可能顯示有人不在。"},{"en":"In the rat experiment, the discrepancy showed that one group performed better than the other.","zh":"在老鼠實驗中，差異顯示其中一組表現較好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a noticeable difference.","zh":"這個短語描述明顯不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as before","meaning":"像之前一樣","examples":[{"en":"The discrepancy returned as before.","zh":"差異像之前一樣再次出現。"},{"en":"As before means in the same way as earlier.","zh":"像之前一樣，是指以早前相同方式。"},{"en":"After the computer restarted, the screen looked as before.","zh":"電腦重新啟動後，螢幕看起來像之前一樣。"},{"en":"If a pattern returns as before, the earlier difference has appeared again.","zh":"如果某模式像之前一樣回來，早前的差異又再次出現。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a later situation with an earlier one.","zh":"這個短語把後來情況與早前情況連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in other words","meaning":"換言之","examples":[{"en":"In other words, environment can affect performance.","zh":"換言之，環境可以影響表現。"},{"en":"In other words introduces the same idea in a clearer or simpler way.","zh":"換言之，是用更清楚或更簡單的方式引入同一想法。"},{"en":"The bus is full; in other words, we need to wait for the next one.","zh":"巴士已滿；換言之，我們需要等下一班。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to explain a point again so readers understand it.","zh":"作者使用這個短語重新解釋重點，讓讀者明白。"},{"en":"This phrase signals restatement or clarification.","zh":"這個短語表示重述或澄清。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stimulating environment","meaning":"有刺激性的環境","examples":[{"en":"A dull rat in a stimulating environment can perform very well.","zh":"較遲鈍的老鼠在有刺激性的環境中可以表現很好。"},{"en":"A stimulating environment provides interest, challenge, and activity that encourage learning.","zh":"有刺激性的環境提供興趣、挑戰和活動，鼓勵學習。"},{"en":"A classroom with questions, projects, and discussion can be a stimulating environment.","zh":"有提問、專題和討論的課室可以是有刺激性的環境。"},{"en":"A stimulating environment may help weaker learners perform closer to stronger learners.","zh":"有刺激性的環境可能幫助較弱學習者表現接近較強學習者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes surroundings that encourage mental activity.","zh":"這個短語描述鼓勵心智活動的周遭環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"almost do as well as","meaning":"幾乎做得和……一樣好","examples":[{"en":"A dull rat in a stimulating environment will almost do as well as a bright rat.","zh":"較遲鈍的老鼠在有刺激性的環境中，幾乎做得和較聰明的老鼠一樣好。"},{"en":"To almost do as well as someone means to perform nearly at the same level.","zh":"幾乎做得和某人一樣好，是指表現接近同一水平。"},{"en":"With enough practice, a beginner may almost do as well as an experienced player.","zh":"經過足夠練習，初學者可能幾乎做得和有經驗的球員一樣好。"},{"en":"Supportive conditions can reduce the gap between weaker and stronger performers.","zh":"支持性條件可以縮小較弱和較強表現者之間的差距。"},{"en":"This phrase describes performance that is close but not exactly equal.","zh":"這個短語描述接近但不完全相等的表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"this principle applies to","meaning":"這個原則也適用於……","examples":[{"en":"This principle applies to humans too.","zh":"這個原則也適用於人類。"},{"en":"If a principle applies to something, it is relevant and true in that situation.","zh":"如果某原則適用於某事，表示它在該情況中相關且成立。"},{"en":"The rule about regular practice applies to music, sport, and language learning.","zh":"定期練習這個規則適用於音樂、運動和語言學習。"},{"en":"If environment affects rats, the writer suggests the same principle may apply to people.","zh":"如果環境影響老鼠，作者暗示同一原則也可能適用於人。"},{"en":"This phrase transfers an idea from one case to another.","zh":"這個短語把一個想法由一個情況轉移到另一個情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"innate intelligence","meaning":"天生智力","examples":[{"en":"Someone may be born with innate intelligence.","zh":"某人可能天生具有天生智力。"},{"en":"Innate intelligence is natural mental ability that a person seems to have from birth.","zh":"天生智力是人似乎出生時已具備的自然心智能力。"},{"en":"A child with innate intelligence may understand patterns quickly even before formal teaching.","zh":"具有天生智力的孩子即使在正式教學前，也可能很快理解規律。"},{"en":"Innate intelligence may help, but practice and environment still influence success.","zh":"天生智力可能有幫助，但練習和環境仍會影響成功。"},{"en":"This phrase describes natural ability rather than learned skill.","zh":"這個短語描述自然能力，而不是後天學到的技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have the final say over","meaning":"對……有最終決定權","examples":[{"en":"The environment probably has the final say over whether someone becomes creative.","zh":"環境可能對某人是否變得有創造力有最終決定權。"},{"en":"To have the final say over something means to be the deciding influence in the end.","zh":"對某事有最終決定權，是指最後成為決定性影響。"},{"en":"Parents may discuss a trip, but the school has the final say over safety rules.","zh":"家長可能討論旅行，但學校對安全規則有最終決定權。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that one factor may decide the final outcome after other factors matter.","zh":"這個短語暗示其他因素也重要，但某因素可能決定最終結果。"},{"en":"It describes final control or decisive influence.","zh":"它描述最終控制或決定性影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"become creative","meaning":"變得有創造力","examples":[{"en":"The environment may decide whether a person becomes creative.","zh":"環境可能決定一個人是否變得有創造力。"},{"en":"To become creative means to develop the ability to produce original ideas or work.","zh":"變得有創造力，是指發展出產生原創想法或作品的能力。"},{"en":"A child may become creative when adults encourage drawing, storytelling, and experimenting.","zh":"當成人鼓勵繪畫、講故事和實驗，孩子可能變得有創造力。"},{"en":"Creativity can grow when mistakes are allowed and curiosity is supported.","zh":"當錯誤被容許且好奇心得到支持，創造力可以成長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the development of originality over time.","zh":"這個短語描述原創性隨時間發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"even a genius","meaning":"甚至成為天才","examples":[{"en":"The environment may influence whether someone becomes creative or even a genius.","zh":"環境可能影響某人是否變得有創造力，甚至成為天才。"},{"en":"Even a genius means a person with extremely rare and outstanding ability.","zh":"甚至成為天才，是指成為具有極罕見和傑出能力的人。"},{"en":"A child may be clever, but becoming even a genius may require support, training, and opportunity.","zh":"孩子可能聰明，但甚至成為天才可能需要支援、訓練和機會。"},{"en":"The phrase raises the level from ordinary creativity to exceptional achievement.","zh":"這個短語把層次由普通創造力提升至非凡成就。"},{"en":"It emphasises an extreme form of talent.","zh":"它強調才能的極端形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"evidence now exists that","meaning":"現已有證據顯示","examples":[{"en":"Evidence now exists that many children can achieve high levels of success.","zh":"現已有證據顯示，許多兒童可以達到高水平成功。"},{"en":"Evidence now exists that means there is now information supporting a claim.","zh":"現已有證據顯示，是指現在有資料支持某個說法。"},{"en":"Evidence now exists that regular sleep improves students’ memory.","zh":"現已有證據顯示，規律睡眠能改善學生記憶。"},{"en":"When evidence exists, a claim becomes stronger than a personal opinion.","zh":"當有證據存在，某說法就比個人意見更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a supported statement.","zh":"這個短語引入有支持的陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"young children","meaning":"年幼兒童","examples":[{"en":"Most young children can achieve significant levels of ability with support.","zh":"大多年幼兒童在支援下可以達到顯著能力水平。"},{"en":"Young children are children in the early years of life or schooling.","zh":"年幼兒童是生命或學校教育早期階段的孩子。"},{"en":"Young children often learn quickly when activities are playful and encouraging.","zh":"年幼兒童在活動有趣且受鼓勵時，通常學得很快。"},{"en":"Support at a young age can help abilities develop before confidence is lost.","zh":"年幼時期的支援可以在信心流失前幫助能力發展。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to children who are still early in development.","zh":"這個短語指仍處於早期發展階段的孩子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"given enough opportunities and encouragement","meaning":"在獲得足夠機會和鼓勵下","examples":[{"en":"Children can succeed if given enough opportunities and encouragement.","zh":"兒童在獲得足夠機會和鼓勵下可以成功。"},{"en":"Given enough opportunities and encouragement means if they receive chances to try and support to keep going.","zh":"在獲得足夠機會和鼓勵下，是指如果他們得到嘗試機會和持續支持。"},{"en":"A shy student may improve speaking if given enough opportunities and encouragement.","zh":"害羞學生在獲得足夠機會和鼓勵下，可能改善說話能力。"},{"en":"Opportunities let children practise, while encouragement helps them continue after mistakes.","zh":"機會讓孩子練習，而鼓勵幫助他們在犯錯後繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how environment can help ability develop.","zh":"這個短語顯示環境如何幫助能力發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"opportunities and encouragement","meaning":"機會和鼓勵","examples":[{"en":"Children need opportunities and encouragement to develop talent.","zh":"兒童需要機會和鼓勵來發展才能。"},{"en":"Opportunities and encouragement mean chances to try and support from others.","zh":"機會和鼓勵，是指嘗試的機會和來自他人的支持。"},{"en":"A child who loves drawing needs paper, time, praise, and useful feedback.","zh":"喜歡畫畫的孩子需要紙張、時間、讚賞和有用回饋。"},{"en":"Without opportunities and encouragement, talent may remain hidden.","zh":"沒有機會和鼓勵，才能可能一直被隱藏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two important forms of support.","zh":"這個短語描述兩種重要支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"achieve significant and sustainable levels of","meaning":"達到顯著而可持續的……水平","examples":[{"en":"Many children can achieve significant and sustainable levels of achievement.","zh":"許多兒童可以達到顯著而可持續的成就水平。"},{"en":"To achieve significant and sustainable levels of something means to reach an important level that can last over time.","zh":"達到顯著而可持續的某種水平，是指達到重要且能長期保持的程度。"},{"en":"A student may achieve significant and sustainable levels of progress after regular practice for a year.","zh":"學生經過一年定期練習後，可能達到顯著而可持續的進步水平。"},{"en":"Sustainable achievement is stronger than a short lucky improvement.","zh":"可持續成就比短暫幸運改善更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaningful success that can continue.","zh":"這個短語描述可以延續的有意義成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sustainable levels","meaning":"可持續的水平","examples":[{"en":"Children can achieve sustainable levels of academic or sporting success.","zh":"兒童可以達到學業或運動成功的可持續水平。"},{"en":"Sustainable levels are levels that can be maintained over time.","zh":"可持續的水平，是可以隨時間維持的水平。"},{"en":"A runner reaches a sustainable level when they can train regularly without injury.","zh":"跑手如果能定期訓練而不受傷，就達到可持續水平。"},{"en":"Sustainable success depends on habits, support, and balance.","zh":"可持續成功取決於習慣、支援和平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts lasting achievement with short-term performance.","zh":"這個短語把持久成就與短期表現作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"academic prowess","meaning":"學業上的卓越能力","examples":[{"en":"Some children can achieve high levels of academic prowess.","zh":"有些兒童可以達到高水平的學業卓越能力。"},{"en":"Academic prowess means outstanding ability in school subjects or study.","zh":"學業上的卓越能力，是在學校科目或學習上的出色能力。"},{"en":"A student with academic prowess may solve difficult maths problems quickly.","zh":"具有學業卓越能力的學生可能很快解決困難數學題。"},{"en":"Academic prowess can grow through teaching, effort, and intellectual curiosity.","zh":"學業卓越能力可以透過教學、努力和求知心成長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong educational ability.","zh":"這個短語描述強大的教育能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sporting prowess","meaning":"運動方面的卓越能力","examples":[{"en":"Some children can achieve high levels of sporting prowess.","zh":"有些兒童可以達到高水平的運動卓越能力。"},{"en":"Sporting prowess means outstanding skill or ability in sport.","zh":"運動方面的卓越能力，是在運動上的出色技巧或能力。"},{"en":"A child with sporting prowess may run faster, jump higher, or learn techniques quickly.","zh":"具有運動卓越能力的孩子可能跑得更快、跳得更高，或很快學會技巧。"},{"en":"Sporting prowess still needs coaching, practice, and physical health to develop.","zh":"運動卓越能力仍需要教練、練習和身體健康來發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong athletic ability.","zh":"這個短語描述強大的運動能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"physically very active","meaning":"身體活動量很高","examples":[{"en":"Bright or creative children are often physically very active.","zh":"聰明或有創造力的兒童通常身體活動量很高。"},{"en":"Physically very active means moving a lot and having high bodily energy.","zh":"身體活動量很高，是指經常移動並有很高身體能量。"},{"en":"A physically very active child may run, climb, dance, or play games all afternoon.","zh":"身體活動量很高的孩子可能整個下午跑步、攀爬、跳舞或玩遊戲。"},{"en":"Active children may receive more attention because adults need to keep them safe.","zh":"活躍兒童可能得到更多關注，因為成人需要確保他們安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes high physical movement, not mental ability directly.","zh":"這個短語描述高度身體活動，而不是直接描述心智能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"同時","examples":[{"en":"Creative children may also be physically active at the same time.","zh":"有創造力的兒童同時也可能身體活躍。"},{"en":"At the same time means simultaneously, or while another thing is also true.","zh":"同時，是指同一時間，或另一件事也成立。"},{"en":"A student can enjoy sport and be good at music at the same time.","zh":"學生可以同時喜歡運動並擅長音樂。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show that two qualities can coexist.","zh":"這個短語有助顯示兩種特質可以共存。"},{"en":"It is useful when avoiding a false choice between two ideas.","zh":"它適合用於避免把兩種想法錯誤地二選一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"receive more parental attention","meaning":"得到更多父母關注","examples":[{"en":"Active children may receive more parental attention.","zh":"活躍兒童可能得到更多父母關注。"},{"en":"To receive more parental attention means to get more notice, time, or care from parents.","zh":"得到更多父母關注，是指得到父母更多注意、時間或照顧。"},{"en":"A child learning to cycle may receive more parental attention because they might fall.","zh":"正在學踩單車的孩子可能因可能跌倒而得到更多父母關注。"},{"en":"More parental attention can encourage development, but it may also affect siblings.","zh":"更多父母關注可以鼓勵發展，但也可能影響兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extra focus from parents.","zh":"這個短語描述來自父母的額外注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"Physically active children may receive more attention as a result.","zh":"身體活躍的兒童可能因此得到更多關注。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what was just mentioned.","zh":"因此，是指由於剛才提到的事情。"},{"en":"The bus was late; as a result, several students missed the first lesson.","zh":"巴士遲到；因此，幾名學生錯過第一節課。"},{"en":"This phrase connects cause and consequence clearly.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接原因和結果。"},{"en":"It is useful for explaining why something happens next.","zh":"它適合解釋為何某事接着發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"almost by default","meaning":"幾乎自然而然地","examples":[{"en":"They may receive more parental attention almost by default.","zh":"他們可能幾乎自然而然地得到更多父母關注。"},{"en":"Almost by default means almost automatically, without anyone deliberately planning it.","zh":"幾乎自然而然地，是指幾乎自動發生，而不是有人刻意計劃。"},{"en":"The oldest child may become the family helper almost by default when parents are busy.","zh":"父母忙碌時，長子女可能幾乎自然而然地成為家庭小幫手。"},{"en":"Active children may get attention almost by default because adults must watch them closely.","zh":"活躍兒童可能幾乎自然而然地得到關注，因為成人必須密切看顧。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something happening naturally because of the situation.","zh":"這個短語描述某事因情況而自然發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in order to ensure","meaning":"為了確保","examples":[{"en":"Parents pay attention in order to ensure their children’s safety.","zh":"父母給予關注，是為了確保孩子安全。"},{"en":"In order to ensure means for the purpose of making certain that something happens.","zh":"為了確保，是指以保證某事發生為目的。"},{"en":"A teacher checks the door in order to ensure that the classroom is safe.","zh":"老師檢查門，是為了確保課室安全。"},{"en":"Parents may watch active children closely in order to ensure they do not hurt themselves.","zh":"父母可能密切看顧活躍兒童，為了確保他們不會弄傷自己。"},{"en":"This phrase explains purpose.","zh":"這個短語解釋目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ensure their safety","meaning":"確保他們的安全","examples":[{"en":"Parents may give more attention to ensure their safety.","zh":"父母可能給予更多關注以確保他們的安全。"},{"en":"To ensure their safety means to make sure they are protected from danger.","zh":"確保他們的安全，是指確保他們受到保護，不受危險傷害。"},{"en":"Coaches check equipment before training to ensure players’ safety.","zh":"教練在訓練前檢查設備，以確保球員安全。"},{"en":"Extra attention may be needed when children climb, run, or explore new places.","zh":"當孩子攀爬、奔跑或探索新地方，可能需要額外關注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preventing harm.","zh":"這個短語描述防止傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"talk earlier","meaning":"較早開始說話","examples":[{"en":"Some bright children may talk earlier.","zh":"有些聰明兒童可能較早開始說話。"},{"en":"To talk earlier means to begin speaking at a younger age than usual.","zh":"較早開始說話，是指比一般年齡更早開始說話。"},{"en":"A child who talks earlier may start using short sentences before other children of the same age.","zh":"較早開始說話的孩子，可能比同齡孩子更早使用短句。"},{"en":"Early speech may attract more attention from parents and adults.","zh":"早期說話可能吸引父母和成人更多注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes early language development.","zh":"這個短語描述早期語言發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in turn","meaning":"轉而；繼而","examples":[{"en":"Early talking, in turn, breeds parental interest.","zh":"早期說話繼而引起父母興趣。"},{"en":"In turn means as the next result in a chain of events.","zh":"轉而或繼而，是指作為一連串事件中的下一個結果。"},{"en":"Better sleep improves attention; this, in turn, can improve learning.","zh":"更好睡眠改善注意力；這繼而可以改善學習。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how one effect becomes the cause of another effect.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個結果如何成為另一結果的原因。"},{"en":"It is useful for explaining linked consequences.","zh":"它適合解釋相連後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"breeds parental interest","meaning":"引起父母興趣","examples":[{"en":"Early speech breeds parental interest.","zh":"早期說話會引起父母興趣。"},{"en":"To breed parental interest means to create or increase parents’ attention and curiosity.","zh":"引起父母興趣，是指創造或增加父母的注意和好奇。"},{"en":"A child who asks unusual questions may breed parental interest in their learning.","zh":"會問不尋常問題的孩子，可能引起父母對其學習的興趣。"},{"en":"More parental interest can lead to more conversation, books, and learning opportunities.","zh":"更多父母興趣可以帶來更多對話、書本和學習機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a child’s behaviour can draw parents in.","zh":"這個短語描述孩子行為如何吸引父母投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cause problems with","meaning":"對……造成問題","examples":[{"en":"Extra attention can cause problems with other siblings.","zh":"額外關注可能對其他兄弟姊妹造成問題。"},{"en":"To cause problems with someone means to create difficulty or tension involving them.","zh":"對某人造成問題，是指製造涉及他們的困難或緊張。"},{"en":"Giving one employee all the praise may cause problems with other team members.","zh":"只表揚一名員工，可能對其他團隊成員造成問題。"},{"en":"Extra attention to one child can cause jealousy among brothers and sisters.","zh":"對一名孩子的額外關注可能在兄弟姊妹之間造成嫉妒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a negative effect on a relationship.","zh":"這個短語描述對關係的負面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"siblings","meaning":"兄弟姊妹","examples":[{"en":"Other siblings may feel jealous.","zh":"其他兄弟姊妹可能感到嫉妒。"},{"en":"Siblings are brothers and sisters.","zh":"兄弟姊妹是 brothers and sisters。"},{"en":"A child may argue with siblings when they feel attention is unfair.","zh":"當孩子覺得關注不公平，可能會與兄弟姊妹爭吵。"},{"en":"Sibling relationships can affect confidence and family atmosphere.","zh":"手足關係可以影響信心和家庭氣氛。"},{"en":"This word refers to children who share one or both parents.","zh":"這個詞指共享一位或兩位父母的孩子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"feel jealous","meaning":"感到嫉妒","examples":[{"en":"Siblings may feel jealous even if they are bright themselves.","zh":"兄弟姊妹即使自己也聰明，仍可能感到嫉妒。"},{"en":"To feel jealous means to feel unhappy because someone else receives attention, success, or advantages.","zh":"感到嫉妒，是指因別人得到關注、成功或優勢而感到不快。"},{"en":"A student may feel jealous when a friend wins an award they also wanted.","zh":"當朋友贏得自己也想得到的獎項，學生可能感到嫉妒。"},{"en":"Jealousy can occur when children think praise or love is not shared fairly.","zh":"當孩子覺得讚賞或愛沒有被公平分享，嫉妒可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an emotional response to comparison.","zh":"這個短語描述比較下的情緒反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"even though","meaning":"即使","examples":[{"en":"Siblings may feel jealous even though they themselves may be bright.","zh":"兄弟姊妹即使自己也可能聰明，仍可能感到嫉妒。"},{"en":"Even though introduces a contrast and means although.","zh":"即使引入對比，意思是 although。"},{"en":"A student may feel nervous even though they studied hard.","zh":"學生即使很努力溫習，仍可能感到緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one fact does not prevent another from being true.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個事實不會阻止另一事實成立。"},{"en":"It is useful for expressing unexpected contrast.","zh":"它適合表達意想不到的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"undervalued","meaning":"被低估","examples":[{"en":"Their creative talents may be undervalued.","zh":"他們的創造才能可能被低估。"},{"en":"If something is undervalued, people do not recognise its true worth or importance.","zh":"如果某事被低估，人們沒有認清其真正價值或重要性。"},{"en":"A quiet student’s ideas may be undervalued if teachers notice only loud speakers.","zh":"如果老師只留意說話大聲的人，安靜學生的想法可能被低估。"},{"en":"When talent is undervalued, the person may receive fewer chances to develop it.","zh":"當才能被低估，當事人可能得到較少發展機會。"},{"en":"This word describes ability being treated as less valuable than it really is.","zh":"這個詞描述能力被視為低於其真正價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"come to fruition","meaning":"開花結果；得以實現","examples":[{"en":"Creative talents may never come to fruition.","zh":"創造才能可能永遠無法開花結果。"},{"en":"To come to fruition means to develop successfully and produce results.","zh":"開花結果，是指成功發展並產生成果。"},{"en":"A student’s writing talent may come to fruition after years of reading and practice.","zh":"學生的寫作才能可能在多年閱讀和練習後開花結果。"},{"en":"Without support, a promising ability may never fully develop.","zh":"沒有支援，有前途的能力可能永遠無法充分發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes potential becoming real achievement.","zh":"這個短語描述潛力變成真正成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"themes seem to run through","meaning":"主題似乎貫穿……","examples":[{"en":"Two themes seem to run through famously creative families.","zh":"兩個主題似乎貫穿著名的創意家庭。"},{"en":"If themes run through something, they appear repeatedly in different parts of it.","zh":"如果主題貫穿某事，表示它們在不同部分反覆出現。"},{"en":"A theme of hard work may run through many success stories.","zh":"努力這個主題可能貫穿許多成功故事。"},{"en":"Repeated themes help readers see patterns across different families or examples.","zh":"反覆出現的主題幫助讀者看見不同家庭或例子之間的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ideas that appear again and again.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆出現的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"famously creative families","meaning":"著名的創意家庭","examples":[{"en":"The writer discusses famously creative families.","zh":"作者討論著名的創意家庭。"},{"en":"Famously creative families are families known for producing creative or talented members.","zh":"著名的創意家庭，是以培養出有創造力或有才華成員而聞名的家庭。"},{"en":"A family of actors, musicians, or writers may be described as famously creative.","zh":"演員、音樂家或作家世家可能被描述為著名的創意家庭。"},{"en":"Studying such families may reveal how environment and support help talent develop.","zh":"研究這類家庭可能揭示環境和支援如何幫助才能發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes well-known families linked with creativity.","zh":"這個短語描述與創造力相關的知名家庭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"Two themes emerge as a result of these family patterns.","zh":"因此，這些家庭模式中出現兩個主題。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what has just been described.","zh":"因此，是指由剛剛描述的事情造成。"},{"en":"The school added more reading time; as a result, students borrowed more books.","zh":"學校增加閱讀時間；因此，學生借了更多書。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links a cause with a consequence.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接原因與後果。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining what follows from evidence.","zh":"它適合解釋證據帶來甚麼結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"identify the talents of","meaning":"辨認……的才能","examples":[{"en":"Parents should identify the talents of each child.","zh":"父母應辨認每個孩子的才能。"},{"en":"To identify the talents of someone means to notice and recognise what they are good at.","zh":"辨認某人的才能，是指注意並認出他們擅長甚麼。"},{"en":"A teacher may identify the talents of a student who writes unusually imaginative stories.","zh":"老師可能辨認出寫故事特別有想像力的學生的才能。"},{"en":"Identifying talent early can help adults provide suitable support.","zh":"早期辨認才能可以幫助成人提供合適支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognising individual strengths.","zh":"這個短語描述認出個人強項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"nurture and encourage","meaning":"培育和鼓勵","examples":[{"en":"Parents can nurture and encourage each child’s talents.","zh":"父母可以培育和鼓勵每個孩子的才能。"},{"en":"To nurture and encourage something means to help it grow and give support for it.","zh":"培育和鼓勵某事，是指幫助它成長並給予支持。"},{"en":"A parent can nurture and encourage a child’s love of music by providing lessons and praise.","zh":"父母可以透過提供課堂和讚賞來培育和鼓勵孩子對音樂的熱愛。"},{"en":"Talent may weaken if it is not nurtured and encouraged.","zh":"如果才能沒有被培育和鼓勵，它可能變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active support for development.","zh":"這個短語描述對發展的主動支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"accordingly","meaning":"相應地","examples":[{"en":"Parents nurture each child’s talents accordingly.","zh":"父母相應地培育每個孩子的才能。"},{"en":"Accordingly means in a way that matches the situation or information just mentioned.","zh":"相應地，是指以符合剛提到情況或資訊的方式。"},{"en":"If a student is weak in grammar, the teacher should plan exercises accordingly.","zh":"如果學生文法較弱，老師應相應地設計練習。"},{"en":"Parents who understand each child’s talent can support them accordingly.","zh":"了解每個孩子才能的父母，可以相應地支援他們。"},{"en":"This word shows that action should fit the need.","zh":"這個詞顯示行動應配合需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in an even-handed manner","meaning":"以公平的方式","examples":[{"en":"Talents should be encouraged in an even-handed manner.","zh":"才能應以公平的方式被鼓勵。"},{"en":"In an even-handed manner means fairly, without favouring one person unfairly over another.","zh":"以公平的方式，是指公平地，不偏袒某人而不公平對待另一人。"},{"en":"A teacher should give feedback in an even-handed manner to both strong and weak students.","zh":"老師應以公平方式給予強弱學生回饋。"},{"en":"Even-handed encouragement can reduce jealousy between siblings.","zh":"公平鼓勵可以減少兄弟姊妹之間的嫉妒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fair and balanced treatment.","zh":"這個短語描述公平而平衡的對待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"individual differences","meaning":"個體差異","examples":[{"en":"Individual differences were encouraged in creative families.","zh":"創意家庭鼓勵個體差異。"},{"en":"Individual differences are the ways people differ in interests, abilities, personality, or needs.","zh":"個體差異是人們在興趣、能力、性格或需要上的不同。"},{"en":"In a classroom, individual differences may appear in reading speed, confidence, and learning style.","zh":"在課室中，個體差異可能出現在閱讀速度、信心和學習方式上。"},{"en":"Encouraging individual differences helps children develop their own strengths.","zh":"鼓勵個體差異有助孩子發展自己的強項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes variation between people.","zh":"這個短語描述人與人之間的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"friendly sibling rivalry","meaning":"友善的手足競爭","examples":[{"en":"Friendly sibling rivalry was not seen as a major problem.","zh":"友善的手足競爭不被視為重大問題。"},{"en":"Friendly sibling rivalry is mild competition between brothers and sisters that is not harmful.","zh":"友善的手足競爭，是兄弟姊妹之間不具傷害性的輕微競爭。"},{"en":"Two siblings may compete to finish homework first in a friendly way.","zh":"兩名兄弟姊妹可能友善地比賽誰先完成功課。"},{"en":"Friendly rivalry can motivate children if parents keep it fair and supportive.","zh":"如果父母保持公平和支持，友善競爭可以激勵孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes competition that remains positive.","zh":"這個短語描述仍然正面的競爭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not seen as","meaning":"不被視為……","examples":[{"en":"Sibling rivalry was not seen as a particular problem.","zh":"手足競爭不被視為特別問題。"},{"en":"Not seen as something means not regarded or considered in that way.","zh":"不被視為某事，是指不被認為或看作那樣。"},{"en":"Asking questions is not seen as rude in a good classroom.","zh":"在好的課室中，提問不被視為無禮。"},{"en":"If friendly rivalry is not seen as a problem, parents may allow it to continue.","zh":"如果友善競爭不被視為問題，父母可能容許它繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how people judge or interpret something.","zh":"這個短語描述人們如何判斷或理解某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"particular problem","meaning":"特別的問題","examples":[{"en":"Friendly sibling rivalry was not seen as a particular problem.","zh":"友善的手足競爭不被視為特別的問題。"},{"en":"A particular problem is a specific difficulty that needs attention.","zh":"特別的問題，是需要注意的具體困難。"},{"en":"Noise may be a particular problem for students trying to study in a small flat.","zh":"對在細小單位中溫習的學生而言，噪音可能是特別的問題。"},{"en":"If rivalry remains friendly, it may not become a particular problem.","zh":"如果競爭保持友善，它可能不會成為特別問題。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific source of difficulty.","zh":"這個短語指出具體困難來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"say","meaning":"比方說","examples":[{"en":"If the father is, say, a famous actor, his children need not follow him.","zh":"如果父親比方說是一位著名演員，他的孩子不必跟隨他。"},{"en":"Say can introduce an example and means for example.","zh":"say 可以引入例子，意思是「比方說」。"},{"en":"If a student needs help, say with grammar, they can ask the teacher after class.","zh":"如果學生需要幫助，比方說文法方面，他們可以課後問老師。"},{"en":"This word makes examples sound natural and conversational.","zh":"這個詞令例子聽起來自然且口語化。"},{"en":"It is used to suggest one possible case among many.","zh":"它用來提出眾多可能情況中的一個例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"famous actor","meaning":"著名演員","examples":[{"en":"A famous actor should not pressure his children to follow him.","zh":"著名演員不應迫使孩子跟隨自己。"},{"en":"A famous actor is a well-known person who performs in films, television, or theatre.","zh":"著名演員是在電影、電視或劇場中表演的知名人士。"},{"en":"The child of a famous actor may feel public pressure to enter acting too.","zh":"著名演員的孩子可能感到公眾壓力，也要投身演藝。"},{"en":"Fame in one generation can create expectations for the next generation.","zh":"一代人的名氣可能為下一代造成期望。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a public figure in the acting profession.","zh":"這個短語指出演藝行業中的公眾人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"undue pressure","meaning":"不適當的壓力","examples":[{"en":"There is no undue pressure for the children to follow their father.","zh":"孩子沒有受到不適當壓力，要跟隨父親。"},{"en":"Undue pressure means unfair, excessive, or inappropriate pressure.","zh":"不適當的壓力，是不公平、過度或不合適的壓力。"},{"en":"Parents put undue pressure on a child if they demand perfect grades every time.","zh":"如果父母每次都要求孩子考滿分，就是給孩子不適當壓力。"},{"en":"Undue pressure can reduce confidence and make talent feel like a burden.","zh":"不適當壓力會削弱信心，令才能變成負擔。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pressure that goes too far.","zh":"這個短語描述過了火的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"follow him onto the boards","meaning":"跟隨他登上舞台","examples":[{"en":"The children are not pressured to follow him onto the boards.","zh":"孩子沒有被迫跟隨他登上舞台。"},{"en":"To follow someone onto the boards means to enter the theatre profession like that person.","zh":"跟隨某人登上舞台，是指像那人一樣進入劇場表演行業。"},{"en":"An actor’s daughter may follow him onto the boards if she also loves acting.","zh":"如果演員的女兒也熱愛演戲，她可能跟隨他登上舞台。"},{"en":"The phrase is theatrical because “the boards” refers to the stage.","zh":"這個短語具劇場色彩，因為 “the boards” 指舞台。"},{"en":"This expression means following someone into stage acting.","zh":"這個表達意思是跟隨某人投身舞台表演。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"chosen interests","meaning":"自己選擇的興趣","examples":[{"en":"The children’s chosen interests are encouraged.","zh":"孩子自己選擇的興趣得到鼓勵。"},{"en":"Chosen interests are activities or subjects a person personally selects and enjoys.","zh":"自己選擇的興趣，是一個人親自選擇並喜歡的活動或科目。"},{"en":"A child’s chosen interests may include painting, football, coding, or cooking.","zh":"孩子自己選擇的興趣可能包括畫畫、足球、編程或烹飪。"},{"en":"Encouraging chosen interests helps children develop identity and motivation.","zh":"鼓勵自己選擇的興趣有助孩子發展身份和動力。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises personal choice rather than parental pressure.","zh":"這個短語強調個人選擇，而不是父母壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"there need not even be","meaning":"甚至不一定要有……","examples":[{"en":"There need not even be any obvious talent in such a family.","zh":"在這樣的家庭中甚至不一定要有任何明顯才能。"},{"en":"There need not even be means it is not necessary for something to exist.","zh":"甚至不一定要有，是指某物並非必須存在。"},{"en":"There need not even be a large budget for a school project if students are creative.","zh":"如果學生有創意，學校專題甚至不一定要有大筆預算。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that something expected may not be required.","zh":"這個短語強調某個被預期的東西未必需要。"},{"en":"It is useful when correcting an assumption.","zh":"它適合用於修正假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"obvious talent","meaning":"明顯才能","examples":[{"en":"There need not be any obvious talent at first in a creative family.","zh":"在創意家庭中，起初不一定有任何明顯才能。"},{"en":"Obvious talent is ability that is easy to notice.","zh":"明顯才能是容易被注意到的能力。"},{"en":"A child who sings beautifully in public may show obvious talent.","zh":"在公開場合唱歌很好聽的孩子可能顯示明顯才能。"},{"en":"Some talents are not obvious at first because they need time and opportunity to appear.","zh":"有些才能起初並不明顯，因為需要時間和機會才會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible ability.","zh":"這個短語描述可見能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sets the family career in motion","meaning":"開創家族事業","examples":[{"en":"Someone must set the family career in motion.","zh":"必須有人開創家族事業。"},{"en":"To set something in motion means to start a process that continues afterward.","zh":"使某事開始運作，是指啟動一個之後持續的過程。"},{"en":"One successful shop owner may set a family business career in motion.","zh":"一位成功店主可能開創家族營商事業。"},{"en":"The first creative person in a family can inspire later generations to follow a similar path.","zh":"家庭中第一位有創意的人可以啟發後代走類似道路。"},{"en":"This phrase describes starting a chain of events.","zh":"這個短語描述啟動一連串事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in the case of","meaning":"在……的例子中","examples":[{"en":"This can be seen in the case of the Sheen acting dynasty.","zh":"這可在 Sheen 演藝世家的例子中看見。"},{"en":"In the case of something means when looking at a particular example.","zh":"在某事的例子中，是指觀察某個特定例子時。"},{"en":"In the case of a shy student, oral presentations may require extra support.","zh":"在害羞學生的例子中，口頭報告可能需要額外支援。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a specific example to support a general point.","zh":"這個短語引入具體例子，以支持一般觀點。"},{"en":"It is common in academic explanation.","zh":"它常見於學術解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"acting dynasty","meaning":"演藝世家","examples":[{"en":"The Sheen family became an acting dynasty.","zh":"Sheen 家族成為演藝世家。"},{"en":"An acting dynasty is a family with several generations or members involved in acting.","zh":"演藝世家是有幾代人或多名成員參與演藝的家庭。"},{"en":"A family with a famous parent and several actor children may be called an acting dynasty.","zh":"有著名父母和幾名演員子女的家庭，可以被稱為演藝世家。"},{"en":"Such dynasties often form when children are inspired by a parent’s profession.","zh":"這類世家常在孩子受到父母職業啟發時形成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a family strongly linked with acting.","zh":"這個短語描述與演藝緊密相關的家庭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"born to","meaning":"出生於……家庭","examples":[{"en":"Martin Sheen was born to a Spanish immigrant father and an Irish mother.","zh":"Martin Sheen 出生於西班牙移民父親和愛爾蘭裔母親的家庭。"},{"en":"Born to someone means born as the child of those parents.","zh":"born to 某人，是指作為那些父母的孩子出生。"},{"en":"A child born to musician parents may grow up hearing music every day.","zh":"出生於音樂家父母家庭的孩子，可能每天聽到音樂。"},{"en":"Family background can shape early experiences, even if it does not decide everything.","zh":"家庭背景可以塑造早期經驗，即使它不能決定一切。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies parentage.","zh":"這個短語指出父母背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Spanish immigrant father","meaning":"西班牙移民父親","examples":[{"en":"Martin Sheen had a Spanish immigrant father.","zh":"Martin Sheen 有一位西班牙移民父親。"},{"en":"A Spanish immigrant father is a father who came from Spain to live in another country.","zh":"西班牙移民父親，是從西班牙移居到另一個國家生活的父親。"},{"en":"A child with an immigrant father may grow up with more than one cultural influence.","zh":"有移民父親的孩子可能在多於一種文化影響下成長。"},{"en":"Immigrant family backgrounds can shape identity, language, and opportunity.","zh":"移民家庭背景可以塑造身份、語言和機會。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies national origin and migration background.","zh":"這個短語指出國籍來源和移民背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Irish mother","meaning":"愛爾蘭裔母親","examples":[{"en":"Martin Sheen had an Irish mother.","zh":"Martin Sheen 有一位愛爾蘭裔母親。"},{"en":"An Irish mother is a mother from Ireland or of Irish background.","zh":"愛爾蘭裔母親，是來自愛爾蘭或有愛爾蘭背景的母親。"},{"en":"A child with an Irish mother may grow up hearing stories about Irish family history.","zh":"有愛爾蘭裔母親的孩子可能聽着愛爾蘭家族故事長大。"},{"en":"Family heritage can influence a person’s identity even if their career later goes in another direction.","zh":"家族傳承可以影響一個人的身份，即使其事業後來走向另一方向。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies maternal background.","zh":"這個短語指出母系背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"despite intense parental disapproval","meaning":"儘管父母強烈反對","examples":[{"en":"Despite intense parental disapproval, he pursued acting.","zh":"儘管父母強烈反對，他仍追求演藝。"},{"en":"Despite intense parental disapproval means even though his parents strongly objected.","zh":"儘管父母強烈反對，是指即使父母非常反對。"},{"en":"A student may choose art school despite intense parental disapproval.","zh":"學生可能儘管父母強烈反對，仍選擇藝術學校。"},{"en":"Strong disapproval can make a career choice harder, but it does not always stop it.","zh":"強烈反對會令職業選擇更困難，但不一定能阻止它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows contrast between family opposition and personal determination.","zh":"這個短語顯示家庭反對與個人決心之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"intense parental disapproval","meaning":"父母強烈反對","examples":[{"en":"Martin Sheen faced intense parental disapproval.","zh":"Martin Sheen 面對父母強烈反對。"},{"en":"Intense parental disapproval is strong objection from parents.","zh":"父母強烈反對，是來自父母的強烈異議。"},{"en":"A teenager may face intense parental disapproval if they reject a safe career path.","zh":"如果青少年拒絕安全的職業道路，可能面對父母強烈反對。"},{"en":"Such disapproval can create conflict between personal ambition and family expectations.","zh":"這種反對會在個人志向和家庭期望之間造成衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong negative reaction from parents.","zh":"這個短語描述父母強烈負面反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"turn his back on","meaning":"背棄；放棄","examples":[{"en":"Martin Sheen turned his back on entrance exams to university.","zh":"Martin Sheen 放棄了大學入學試。"},{"en":"To turn one’s back on something means to reject or leave it behind.","zh":"背棄或放棄某事，是指拒絕它或把它拋在身後。"},{"en":"A worker may turn his back on a stable job to start a small business.","zh":"工人可能放棄穩定工作，去開創小生意。"},{"en":"Turning one’s back on a safe path can be risky but may follow personal passion.","zh":"放棄安全道路可能有風險，但也可能是追隨個人熱情。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a deliberate rejection.","zh":"這個短語描述有意識的拒絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"entrance exams to university","meaning":"大學入學試","examples":[{"en":"He turned his back on entrance exams to university.","zh":"他放棄了大學入學試。"},{"en":"Entrance exams to university are tests taken to gain admission to university.","zh":"大學入學試是為獲得大學錄取而參加的考試。"},{"en":"Students often prepare for entrance exams to university months in advance.","zh":"學生通常提前數月準備大學入學試。"},{"en":"Choosing not to take these exams may close one educational route.","zh":"選擇不參加這些考試，可能關閉一條教育路線。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal tests for university admission.","zh":"這個短語指大學入學的正式考試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"borrowed cash from","meaning":"向……借錢","examples":[{"en":"He borrowed cash from a local priest.","zh":"他向本地神父借錢。"},{"en":"To borrow cash from someone means to receive money from them with the expectation of repayment.","zh":"向某人借錢，是指從對方取得金錢，並預期日後歸還。"},{"en":"A student may borrow cash from a parent to pay for a school trip.","zh":"學生可能向父母借錢支付學校旅行費用。"},{"en":"Borrowing money can help someone start a plan when they lack savings.","zh":"借錢可以幫助缺乏積蓄的人開始一個計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes getting money temporarily from another person.","zh":"這個短語描述暫時從他人取得金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"local priest","meaning":"本地神父","examples":[{"en":"A local priest lent Martin Sheen money to start acting.","zh":"一位本地神父借錢給 Martin Sheen 開始演藝事業。"},{"en":"A local priest is a religious leader serving a nearby community.","zh":"本地神父是在附近社區服務的宗教領袖。"},{"en":"A local priest may know many families in the neighbourhood.","zh":"本地神父可能認識社區內許多家庭。"},{"en":"Help from a local priest can show community support outside the family.","zh":"來自本地神父的幫助可以顯示家庭以外的社區支持。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a religious figure in a local area.","zh":"這個短語指出本地區域中的宗教人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"fledgling acting career","meaning":"剛起步的演藝事業","examples":[{"en":"Martin Sheen used the money to start a fledgling acting career.","zh":"Martin Sheen 用這筆錢開始剛起步的演藝事業。"},{"en":"A fledgling acting career is an acting career that is just beginning and still fragile.","zh":"剛起步的演藝事業，是剛開始且仍不穩定的演藝職業。"},{"en":"A young performer may take small theatre roles to build a fledgling acting career.","zh":"年輕表演者可能接小型劇場角色，建立剛起步的演藝事業。"},{"en":"Early support can help a fledgling career survive its uncertain first stage.","zh":"早期支援可以幫助剛起步的事業度過不確定的初期。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a new and undeveloped acting career.","zh":"這個短語描述新的、尚未成熟的演藝事業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"acting successes","meaning":"演藝成就","examples":[{"en":"His acting successes made him highly regarded.","zh":"他的演藝成就令他備受推崇。"},{"en":"Acting successes are achievements in acting, such as strong performances, awards, or respected roles.","zh":"演藝成就是在演戲方面的成就，例如出色表演、獎項或受尊重角色。"},{"en":"A young actor’s acting successes may include a popular school play and a local theatre prize.","zh":"年輕演員的演藝成就可能包括受歡迎的學校劇和本地劇場獎。"},{"en":"Acting successes can build reputation and inspire family members.","zh":"演藝成就可以建立聲譽並啟發家庭成員。"},{"en":"This phrase describes successful outcomes in an acting career.","zh":"這個短語描述演藝事業中的成功成果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"highly regarded actors","meaning":"備受推崇的演員","examples":[{"en":"Martin Sheen became one of the most highly regarded actors of the 1970s.","zh":"Martin Sheen 成為二十世紀七十年代最備受推崇的演員之一。"},{"en":"Highly regarded actors are actors who are respected and admired for their work.","zh":"備受推崇的演員，是因作品而受到尊重和欣賞的演員。"},{"en":"A highly regarded actor may be praised by critics, audiences, and other performers.","zh":"備受推崇的演員可能受到評論家、觀眾和其他表演者讚賞。"},{"en":"Becoming highly regarded usually requires talent, dedication, and memorable performances.","zh":"成為備受推崇的人通常需要才能、投入和令人難忘的表演。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong professional respect.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈專業尊重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"followed him into the profession","meaning":"跟隨他投身該行業","examples":[{"en":"Three of his sons followed him into the acting profession.","zh":"他的三個兒子跟隨他投身演藝行業。"},{"en":"To follow someone into the profession means to enter the same career as that person.","zh":"跟隨某人投身該行業，是指進入與那人相同的職業。"},{"en":"A doctor’s child may follow her into the profession after seeing her work.","zh":"醫生的孩子看見母親工作後，可能跟隨她投身該行業。"},{"en":"Children may follow a parent into a profession because they are inspired by their example.","zh":"子女可能因受父母榜樣啟發而跟隨他們投身某專業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing the same career path.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇相同職業道路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the profession","meaning":"該專業；該行業","examples":[{"en":"His sons followed him into the profession.","zh":"他的兒子跟隨他投身該行業。"},{"en":"The profession means the particular career or field already being discussed.","zh":"該專業或該行業，是指前面已討論的特定職業或領域。"},{"en":"If a teacher’s daughter becomes a teacher, she has entered the profession too.","zh":"如果老師的女兒成為老師，她也進入了該行業。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating the name of the job again.","zh":"這個短語避免再次重複職業名稱。"},{"en":"It refers to a recognised line of work.","zh":"它指一個被認可的工作領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as a consequence of","meaning":"作為……的結果","examples":[{"en":"His sons became actors as a consequence of his motivation and enthusiasm.","zh":"他的兒子因他的動力和熱情而成為演員。"},{"en":"As a consequence of means as a result of.","zh":"作為某事的結果，是指由某事造成。"},{"en":"As a consequence of regular practice, the student’s pronunciation improved.","zh":"作為定期練習的結果，學生的發音改善了。"},{"en":"This phrase links an outcome to its cause.","zh":"這個短語把結果與原因連接起來。"},{"en":"It is more formal than saying because of.","zh":"它比 because of 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"inspired by","meaning":"受到……啟發","examples":[{"en":"His sons were inspired by his motivation and enthusiasm.","zh":"他的兒子受到他的動力和熱情啟發。"},{"en":"Inspired by someone means encouraged or influenced by them to do something.","zh":"受到某人啟發，是指被他們鼓勵或影響去做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be inspired by a teacher who loves science.","zh":"學生可能受到熱愛科學的老師啟發。"},{"en":"Inspiration can lead people to choose a similar path or work harder.","zh":"啟發可以令人選擇相似道路或更努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes positive influence.","zh":"這個短語描述正面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"motivation and enthusiasm","meaning":"動力和熱情","examples":[{"en":"Martin Sheen’s motivation and enthusiasm inspired his sons.","zh":"Martin Sheen 的動力和熱情啟發了他的兒子。"},{"en":"Motivation and enthusiasm mean the drive to act and the excitement to continue.","zh":"動力和熱情，是行動的推動力和繼續下去的興奮感。"},{"en":"A coach with motivation and enthusiasm can make training feel meaningful.","zh":"有動力和熱情的教練可以令訓練感覺有意義。"},{"en":"Children may copy a parent’s motivation and enthusiasm more than their exact career.","zh":"孩子模仿父母的，可能更多是動力和熱情，而不是完全相同的職業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes energy, passion, and commitment.","zh":"這個短語描述能量、熱愛和投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a stream seems to run through","meaning":"一種傾向似乎貫穿……","examples":[{"en":"A stream seems to run through creative families.","zh":"一種傾向似乎貫穿創意家庭。"},{"en":"If a stream runs through something, a common pattern or quality appears repeatedly in it.","zh":"如果某種傾向貫穿某事，表示一種共同模式或特質反覆出現。"},{"en":"A stream of discipline may run through many successful sports families.","zh":"自律這種傾向可能貫穿許多成功運動家庭。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a continuing influence across people or generations.","zh":"這個短語暗示一種跨越人物或世代的持續影響。"},{"en":"It is a figurative way to describe a repeated pattern.","zh":"它是描述重複模式的比喻說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"necessarily","meaning":"必然；一定","examples":[{"en":"Creative children are not necessarily smothered with love.","zh":"有創造力的兒童不一定被父母過度關愛。"},{"en":"Necessarily means always or as an unavoidable result, often used in negatives.","zh":"necessarily 指總是或必然如此，常用於否定句。"},{"en":"A quiet student is not necessarily unhappy.","zh":"安靜的學生不一定不開心。"},{"en":"The word helps prevent overgeneralisation.","zh":"這個詞有助避免過度概括。"},{"en":"In “not necessarily,” it means something may be true, but is not always true.","zh":"在 “not necessarily” 中，它表示某事可能是真的，但不總是真的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"smothered with love","meaning":"被過度關愛","examples":[{"en":"Creative children are not necessarily smothered with love by their parents.","zh":"有創造力的兒童不一定被父母過度關愛。"},{"en":"To be smothered with love means to receive so much affection or attention that it may feel excessive.","zh":"被過度關愛，是指得到太多愛或關注，以致可能感覺過度。"},{"en":"A child may feel smothered with love if parents never allow them to make choices alone.","zh":"如果父母從不讓孩子獨自作選擇，孩子可能覺得被過度關愛。"},{"en":"Too much protective love can sometimes limit independence.","zh":"過多保護性愛護有時會限制獨立性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes excessive affection, not ordinary care.","zh":"這個短語描述過度關愛，而不是普通照顧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"feel loved and wanted","meaning":"感到被愛和被需要","examples":[{"en":"Creative children usually feel loved and wanted.","zh":"有創造力的兒童通常感到被愛和被需要。"},{"en":"To feel loved and wanted means to feel cared for and valued by others.","zh":"感到被愛和被需要，是指感到被他人關心和重視。"},{"en":"A child feels loved and wanted when parents listen, spend time, and show affection.","zh":"當父母聆聽、陪伴並表達愛意，孩子會感到被愛和被需要。"},{"en":"Feeling loved and wanted can give children confidence to explore their interests.","zh":"感到被愛和被需要可以給孩子信心去探索興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional security.","zh":"這個短語描述情感安全感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"secure in their home","meaning":"在家中有安全感","examples":[{"en":"Creative children often feel secure in their home.","zh":"有創造力的兒童通常在家中有安全感。"},{"en":"To feel secure in one’s home means to feel safe, accepted, and emotionally supported there.","zh":"在家中有安全感，是指在家裡感到安全、被接納和得到情感支持。"},{"en":"A child who feels secure at home is more likely to try difficult tasks without fear.","zh":"在家中有安全感的孩子較可能不怕失敗地嘗試困難任務。"},{"en":"Home security can support creativity because children are less afraid of failure.","zh":"家庭安全感可以支持創造力，因為孩子較少害怕失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional safety within the family.","zh":"這個短語描述家庭中的情感安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"surrounded by","meaning":"被……包圍","examples":[{"en":"They are often surrounded by an atmosphere of work.","zh":"他們通常被勤奮工作的氣氛包圍。"},{"en":"To be surrounded by something means to have it all around you.","zh":"被某物包圍，是指周圍都有它。"},{"en":"A student surrounded by books and discussion may become more curious.","zh":"被書本和討論包圍的學生可能變得更好奇。"},{"en":"Being surrounded by hardworking adults can shape a child’s habits.","zh":"被勤奮工作的成人包圍，可以塑造孩子的習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the environment around a person.","zh":"這個短語描述人周圍的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"atmosphere of work","meaning":"勤奮工作的氣氛","examples":[{"en":"Creative families often have an atmosphere of work.","zh":"創意家庭通常有勤奮工作的氣氛。"},{"en":"An atmosphere of work is a home or environment where effort, practice, and serious activity are normal.","zh":"勤奮工作的氣氛，是努力、練習和認真活動被視為正常的家庭或環境。"},{"en":"A music family may have an atmosphere of work if everyone practises daily.","zh":"如果每個人每天練習，音樂家庭可能有勤奮工作的氣氛。"},{"en":"Such an atmosphere teaches children that skill takes time and discipline.","zh":"這種氣氛教導孩子技能需要時間和紀律。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a culture of steady effort.","zh":"這個短語描述穩定努力的文化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"following a calling","meaning":"追隨志業","examples":[{"en":"Following a calling appears to be important in creative families.","zh":"追隨志業在創意家庭中似乎很重要。"},{"en":"Following a calling means pursuing work or activity that feels deeply meaningful.","zh":"追隨志業，是指追求感到深具意義的工作或活動。"},{"en":"A nurse may feel she is following a calling rather than simply doing a job.","zh":"護士可能覺得自己是在追隨志業，而不只是做一份工作。"},{"en":"When parents follow a calling, children may learn dedication from watching them.","zh":"當父母追隨志業，孩子可能透過觀察學到投入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes commitment to a meaningful vocation.","zh":"這個短語描述對有意義職志的承諾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"appears to be","meaning":"似乎是……","examples":[{"en":"Following a calling appears to be important.","zh":"追隨志業似乎很重要。"},{"en":"Appears to be means seems to be, based on available evidence or impression.","zh":"似乎是，是指根據現有證據或印象看起來是。"},{"en":"The new student appears to be nervous on the first day.","zh":"新學生第一天似乎很緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase is cautious because it does not claim complete certainty.","zh":"這個短語較謹慎，因為它不聲稱完全確定。"},{"en":"It is useful in academic writing when evidence suggests, but does not prove, a point.","zh":"當證據暗示但未完全證明某點時，它適合用於學術寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"dedication","meaning":"投入；奉獻","examples":[{"en":"Children may learn that mastery takes time and dedication.","zh":"兒童可能學到，精通需要時間和投入。"},{"en":"Dedication means serious commitment and steady effort over time.","zh":"投入是長時間認真承諾和穩定努力。"},{"en":"Learning the violin well requires dedication because practice must continue for years.","zh":"學好小提琴需要投入，因為練習必須持續多年。"},{"en":"Dedication helps talent develop into real skill.","zh":"投入幫助才能發展成真正技能。"},{"en":"This word describes long-term commitment.","zh":"這個詞描述長期承諾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"master of a craft","meaning":"工藝大師；精通一門技藝的人","examples":[{"en":"It takes time and dedication to be a master of a craft.","zh":"成為精通一門技藝的人需要時間和投入。"},{"en":"A master of a craft is someone highly skilled in a particular art, trade, or activity.","zh":"工藝大師或精通一門技藝的人，是在某種藝術、行業或活動中技術高超的人。"},{"en":"A baker becomes a master of a craft after years of learning recipes, timing, and technique.","zh":"麵包師經過多年學習食譜、時間控制和技巧後，成為精通一門技藝的人。"},{"en":"Mastery requires repeated practice, not just natural talent.","zh":"精通需要反覆練習，而不只是天生才能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes expert skill in a specific field.","zh":"這個短語描述某特定領域中的專家技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"in less of a hurry to","meaning":"不那麼急於……","examples":[{"en":"Creative children may be in less of a hurry to achieve success.","zh":"有創造力的兒童可能不那麼急於取得成功。"},{"en":"To be in less of a hurry to do something means to feel less rushed or impatient about doing it.","zh":"不那麼急於做某事，是指較不感到匆忙或不耐煩。"},{"en":"A patient student may be in less of a hurry to finish a difficult book.","zh":"有耐性的學生可能不那麼急於讀完一本困難的書。"},{"en":"Being less hurried can help people focus on quality rather than quick results.","zh":"不那麼急躁可以幫助人們專注於質素，而不是快速結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a more patient attitude.","zh":"這個短語描述較有耐性的態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"achieve for themselves","meaning":"為自己取得成就","examples":[{"en":"They may be less hurried to achieve for themselves.","zh":"他們可能不那麼急於為自己取得成就。"},{"en":"To achieve for themselves means to succeed through their own efforts and in their own way.","zh":"為自己取得成就，是指透過自己的努力和方式成功。"},{"en":"A young artist may need time to achieve for herself rather than copy a famous parent.","zh":"年輕藝術家可能需要時間為自己取得成就，而不是模仿著名父母。"},{"en":"Personal achievement feels stronger when it matches one’s own interests.","zh":"當成就符合自己的興趣，個人成就感會更強。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises individual success.","zh":"這個短語強調個人成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"once they start to work","meaning":"一旦開始工作","examples":[{"en":"They may be more patient once they start to work.","zh":"一旦開始工作，他們可能更有耐性。"},{"en":"Once they start to work means after they begin working seriously.","zh":"一旦開始工作，是指他們開始認真工作之後。"},{"en":"A student may feel confused at first, but once they start to work, the task becomes clearer.","zh":"學生起初可能感到困惑，但一旦開始工作，任務會變得更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the point when action begins.","zh":"這個短語標示行動開始的時間點。"},{"en":"It is useful for showing how behaviour changes after starting.","zh":"它適合顯示開始後行為如何改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the generation of creativity","meaning":"創造力的產生","examples":[{"en":"The generation of creativity is complex.","zh":"創造力的產生很複雜。"},{"en":"The generation of creativity means how creativity is produced or developed.","zh":"創造力的產生，是指創造力如何被產生或發展。"},{"en":"In a classroom, the generation of creativity may depend on freedom, examples, and feedback.","zh":"在課室中，創造力的產生可能取決於自由、例子和回饋。"},{"en":"Creativity is complex because it may involve family, environment, teaching, and luck.","zh":"創造力很複雜，因為它可能涉及家庭、環境、教學和運氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process by which creativity comes into being.","zh":"這個短語描述創造力如何出現的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a mixture of","meaning":"……的混合","examples":[{"en":"Creativity is a mixture of genetics, environment, teaching and luck.","zh":"創造力是遺傳、環境、教學和運氣的混合。"},{"en":"A mixture of things means several different elements combined together.","zh":"某幾事物的混合，是指幾種不同元素結合在一起。"},{"en":"A good lesson may be a mixture of explanation, practice, and discussion.","zh":"好課堂可能是講解、練習和討論的混合。"},{"en":"If talent is a mixture of several factors, no single factor explains everything.","zh":"如果才能是幾個因素的混合，單一因素就不能解釋一切。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a combined explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述綜合式解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"parental teaching","meaning":"父母教導","examples":[{"en":"Parental teaching can affect how talent develops.","zh":"父母教導可以影響才能如何發展。"},{"en":"Parental teaching means the instruction, guidance, and habits parents give their children.","zh":"父母教導是父母給予子女的指導、引導和習慣。"},{"en":"Parents provide parental teaching when they read with a child or show how to practise piano.","zh":"父母與孩子一起閱讀或示範如何練琴時，就是提供父母教導。"},{"en":"Good parental teaching can turn early interest into lasting skill.","zh":"良好父母教導可以把早期興趣變成持久技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning support from parents.","zh":"這個短語描述來自父母的學習支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"determines how","meaning":"決定……如何","examples":[{"en":"Several factors determine how successful family members become.","zh":"幾個因素決定家庭成員會變得多成功。"},{"en":"Determine how means influence or decide the way something happens.","zh":"決定某事如何發生，是指影響或決定它發生的方式。"},{"en":"Sleep, practice, and confidence determine how well a student performs in an exam.","zh":"睡眠、練習和信心決定學生在考試中表現如何。"},{"en":"In talent development, many factors determine how far ability grows.","zh":"在才能發展中，許多因素決定能力能成長到甚麼程度。"},{"en":"This phrase connects causes with outcomes.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"family members","meaning":"家庭成員","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses how talented family members become successful.","zh":"篇章討論有才華的家庭成員如何變得成功。"},{"en":"Family members are people who belong to the same family.","zh":"家庭成員是屬於同一家庭的人。"},{"en":"Parents, children, brothers, sisters, and grandparents are family members.","zh":"父母、子女、兄弟姊妹和祖父母都是家庭成員。"},{"en":"Family members can influence one another through support, example, and expectations.","zh":"家庭成員可以透過支持、榜樣和期望互相影響。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people connected by family relationships.","zh":"這個短語指因家庭關係相連的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"where talent is concerned","meaning":"就才能而言","examples":[{"en":"Luck is often not mentioned where talent is concerned.","zh":"就才能而言，運氣常常沒有被提及。"},{"en":"Where talent is concerned means when discussing talent.","zh":"就才能而言，是指在討論才能時。"},{"en":"Where health is concerned, sleep and diet are both important.","zh":"就健康而言，睡眠和飲食都很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows the topic to one area of discussion.","zh":"這個短語把主題收窄到某個討論範疇。"},{"en":"It is useful for saying what matters in a specific context.","zh":"它適合說明在特定語境中甚麼重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"plays an undoubted part","meaning":"起着無可置疑的作用","examples":[{"en":"Luck plays an undoubted part in talent.","zh":"運氣在才能中起着無可置疑的作用。"},{"en":"To play an undoubted part means to have a role that cannot reasonably be denied.","zh":"起着無可置疑的作用，是指有一個難以否認的角色。"},{"en":"Good timing can play an undoubted part in business success.","zh":"良好時機可以在商業成功中起着無可置疑的作用。"},{"en":"Even talented people may need luck to meet the right teacher or opportunity.","zh":"即使有才華的人，也可能需要運氣遇到合適老師或機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an influence that is clearly important.","zh":"這個短語描述明顯重要的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"considered by many to be","meaning":"被許多人認為是……","examples":[{"en":"Mozart is considered by many to be the finest composer of all time.","zh":"莫扎特被許多人認為是有史以來最出色的作曲家。"},{"en":"Considered by many to be means many people regard someone or something in that way.","zh":"被許多人認為是，是指很多人以那種方式看待某人或某事。"},{"en":"The novel is considered by many to be a classic of modern literature.","zh":"這本小說被許多人認為是現代文學經典。"},{"en":"This phrase reports a widely held opinion, not an absolute fact.","zh":"這個短語報告一種廣泛持有的看法，而不是絕對事實。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing reputation.","zh":"它適合描述聲譽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the finest composer of all time","meaning":"有史以來最出色的作曲家","examples":[{"en":"Mozart is considered by many to be the finest composer of all time.","zh":"莫扎特被許多人認為是有史以來最出色的作曲家。"},{"en":"The finest composer of all time means the greatest music writer in history.","zh":"有史以來最出色的作曲家，是歷史上最偉大的音樂創作者。"},{"en":"A critic may call Mozart the finest composer of all time because of the beauty and complexity of his music.","zh":"評論家可能因莫扎特音樂的美感和複雜性，稱他為有史以來最出色的作曲家。"},{"en":"Such a title shows exceptional reputation across generations.","zh":"這種稱號顯示跨越世代的非凡聲譽。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses extremely high artistic praise.","zh":"這個短語表達極高藝術讚賞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"living in an age that","meaning":"生活在一個……的時代","examples":[{"en":"Mozart was lucky to be living in an age that encouraged music.","zh":"莫扎特很幸運，生活在一個鼓勵音樂的時代。"},{"en":"Living in an age that means being alive during a historical period with certain conditions.","zh":"生活在一個怎樣的時代，是指身處具有某些條件的歷史時期。"},{"en":"A programmer today is living in an age that values digital skills.","zh":"今天的程式員生活在一個重視數碼技能的時代。"},{"en":"The age someone lives in can create or limit opportunities.","zh":"一個人所處的時代可以創造或限制機會。"},{"en":"This phrase connects personal success with historical timing.","zh":"這個短語把個人成功與歷史時機連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"encouraged the writing of music","meaning":"鼓勵音樂創作","examples":[{"en":"Mozart lived in an age that encouraged the writing of music.","zh":"莫扎特生活在一個鼓勵音樂創作的時代。"},{"en":"Encouraged the writing of music means supported or valued musical composition.","zh":"鼓勵音樂創作，是指支持或重視作曲。"},{"en":"A school encourages the writing of music when it gives students time to compose songs.","zh":"學校如果給學生時間創作歌曲，就是鼓勵音樂創作。"},{"en":"When society values music, talented composers may receive more chances to develop.","zh":"當社會重視音樂，有才華的作曲家可能得到更多發展機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cultural support for musical creation.","zh":"這個短語描述對音樂創作的文化支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"brought up surrounded by","meaning":"在……環境中長大","examples":[{"en":"Mozart was brought up surrounded by music.","zh":"莫扎特在音樂環境中長大。"},{"en":"Brought up surrounded by something means raised in an environment full of it.","zh":"在某種環境中長大，是指在充滿該事物的環境中被養育。"},{"en":"A child brought up surrounded by books may become comfortable with reading early.","zh":"在書本環境中長大的孩子可能很早就對閱讀感到自在。"},{"en":"Being surrounded by music can make musical learning feel natural.","zh":"被音樂包圍可以令音樂學習感覺自然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an upbringing shaped by the surrounding environment.","zh":"這個短語描述由周遭環境塑造的成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"to the point of","meaning":"到了……的程度","examples":[{"en":"His father encouraged him to the point of giving up his job.","zh":"他的父親鼓勵他，到了放棄自己工作的程度。"},{"en":"To the point of means reaching the extreme level of doing something.","zh":"到了某種程度，是指達到做某事的極端程度。"},{"en":"A parent may support a child’s sport to the point of moving closer to a training centre.","zh":"父母可能支持孩子運動，到了搬近訓練中心的程度。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that support went very far.","zh":"這個短語顯示支持走得很遠。"},{"en":"It describes the degree or extent of an action.","zh":"它描述行動的程度或幅度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"giving up his job","meaning":"放棄他的工作","examples":[{"en":"Mozart’s father gave up his job to promote his son.","zh":"莫扎特的父親放棄他的工作，以推動兒子發展。"},{"en":"Giving up his job means leaving or quitting his work.","zh":"放棄他的工作，是指離開或辭去工作。"},{"en":"A parent may consider giving up a job to care for a seriously ill child.","zh":"父母可能考慮放棄工作，以照顧重病孩子。"},{"en":"Giving up a job is a major sacrifice because it affects income and security.","zh":"放棄工作是重大犧牲，因為會影響收入和安全感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes leaving employment for another priority.","zh":"這個短語描述為另一優先事項而離開職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"promote his child genius","meaning":"推動他的神童兒子發展","examples":[{"en":"Mozart’s father gave up his job to promote his child genius.","zh":"莫扎特的父親放棄工作，以推動他的神童兒子發展。"},{"en":"To promote his child genius means to help his exceptionally talented child become known and successful.","zh":"推動他的神童兒子發展，是指幫助他極有天賦的孩子成名和成功。"},{"en":"A parent may promote a child musician by arranging concerts and lessons.","zh":"父母可能透過安排音樂會和課堂來推動孩子音樂家發展。"},{"en":"Promotion can create opportunities, but it may also put pressure on the child.","zh":"推動發展可以創造機會，但也可能給孩子壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active support for a gifted child’s public development.","zh":"這個短語描述對有天賦孩子公開發展的主動支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"child genius","meaning":"神童","examples":[{"en":"Mozart was treated as a child genius.","zh":"莫扎特被視為神童。"},{"en":"A child genius is a child with extraordinary ability far beyond their age.","zh":"神童是能力遠超同齡人的孩子。"},{"en":"A child genius in maths may solve problems normally taught to university students.","zh":"數學神童可能能解決通常教給大學生的題目。"},{"en":"Being seen as a child genius can bring attention, training, and pressure.","zh":"被視為神童可以帶來關注、訓練和壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exceptional ability at a very young age.","zh":"這個短語描述很小年紀已有非凡能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"musical composition","meaning":"音樂創作","examples":[{"en":"Mozart learnt musical composition with frightening speed.","zh":"莫扎特以驚人的速度學會音樂創作。"},{"en":"Musical composition is the art or process of creating music.","zh":"音樂創作是創造音樂的藝術或過程。"},{"en":"A student studies musical composition when they learn how to write melodies and harmonies.","zh":"學生學習如何寫旋律和和聲時，就是學習音樂創作。"},{"en":"Strong training in composition can help a musician create original works.","zh":"強大的作曲訓練可以幫助音樂家創作原創作品。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to writing music, not just performing it.","zh":"這個短語指創作音樂，而不只是表演音樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"with frightening speed","meaning":"以驚人的速度","examples":[{"en":"Mozart learnt musical composition with frightening speed.","zh":"莫扎特以驚人的速度學會音樂創作。"},{"en":"With frightening speed means extremely quickly, almost unbelievably quickly.","zh":"以驚人的速度，是指極快，快到幾乎令人難以置信。"},{"en":"A talented coder may learn a new programming language with frightening speed.","zh":"有才華的程式員可能以驚人的速度學會新的編程語言。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that the speed is impressive and almost shocking.","zh":"這個短語暗示速度令人佩服且幾乎令人震驚。"},{"en":"It is used to emphasise unusually rapid progress.","zh":"它用來強調異常快速的進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the speed of a genius","meaning":"天才般的速度","examples":[{"en":"Mozart learnt with the speed of a genius.","zh":"莫扎特以天才般的速度學習。"},{"en":"The speed of a genius means an extremely fast learning or creating pace associated with exceptional ability.","zh":"天才般的速度，是與非凡能力相關的極快學習或創作速度。"},{"en":"A child who masters chess strategies in weeks may seem to learn with the speed of a genius.","zh":"幾星期內掌握國際象棋策略的孩子，可能看似以天才般的速度學習。"},{"en":"Such speed suggests unusual talent, though support and practice still matter.","zh":"這種速度暗示不尋常才能，但支援和練習仍然重要。"},{"en":"This phrase praises extraordinary quickness in learning.","zh":"這個短語讚揚非凡的學習速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"simply wanted to","meaning":"只是想要……","examples":[{"en":"Mozart simply wanted to create the finest music ever written.","zh":"莫扎特只是想創作有史以來最出色的音樂。"},{"en":"Simply wanted to means only wanted to, without a more complicated motive.","zh":"只是想要，是指單純想要，而沒有更複雜動機。"},{"en":"A child may simply want to draw because it feels enjoyable, not because of prizes.","zh":"孩子可能只是想畫畫，因為覺得有趣，而不是為了獎項。"},{"en":"This phrase reduces an action to its basic motivation.","zh":"這個短語把行動簡化至基本動機。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining someone’s main desire.","zh":"它適合解釋某人的主要願望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the finest music ever written","meaning":"有史以來最出色的音樂","examples":[{"en":"Mozart wanted to create the finest music ever written.","zh":"莫扎特想創作有史以來最出色的音樂。"},{"en":"The finest music ever written means the best music created in all history.","zh":"有史以來最出色的音樂，是歷史上被創作出的最佳音樂。"},{"en":"A composer aiming for the finest music ever written is seeking an extremely high standard.","zh":"以有史以來最出色的音樂為目標的作曲家，是追求極高標準。"},{"en":"Such ambition can drive long hours of practice and revision.","zh":"這種抱負可以推動長時間練習和修改。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses the highest possible artistic goal.","zh":"這個短語表達最高可能的藝術目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"not necessarily view himself as","meaning":"不一定視自己為……","examples":[{"en":"Mozart did not necessarily view himself as a genius.","zh":"莫扎特不一定視自己為天才。"},{"en":"To not necessarily view oneself as something means not always or not clearly see oneself in that way.","zh":"不一定視自己為某種人，是指不總是或不明確以那種方式看待自己。"},{"en":"A talented student may not necessarily view herself as clever if she compares herself with others.","zh":"有才華的學生如果常與別人比較，未必視自己為聰明。"},{"en":"People may have great ability without strongly identifying with the label of genius.","zh":"人們可以有很強能力，卻不一定強烈認同天才這個標籤。"},{"en":"This phrase shows uncertainty about self-perception.","zh":"這個短語顯示自我認知上的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"sublime music","meaning":"崇高美妙的音樂","examples":[{"en":"Mozart could write sublime music at will.","zh":"莫扎特可以隨心所欲地寫出崇高美妙的音樂。"},{"en":"Sublime music is music of extraordinary beauty, power, or emotional depth.","zh":"崇高美妙的音樂，是具有非凡美感、力量或情感深度的音樂。"},{"en":"A listener may feel moved to tears by sublime music in a concert hall.","zh":"聽眾可能在音樂廳中被崇高美妙的音樂感動落淚。"},{"en":"Writing sublime music requires rare skill and imagination.","zh":"寫出崇高美妙的音樂需要罕見技巧和想像力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes music of very high artistic quality.","zh":"這個短語描述極高藝術質素的音樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"at will","meaning":"隨心所欲地","examples":[{"en":"Mozart could write sublime music at will.","zh":"莫扎特可以隨心所欲地寫出崇高美妙的音樂。"},{"en":"At will means whenever someone chooses or wants to do it.","zh":"隨心所欲地，是指只要某人選擇或想做就能做到。"},{"en":"A skilled speaker can switch between English and Cantonese at will.","zh":"熟練講者可以隨心所欲地在英語和廣東話之間轉換。"},{"en":"Doing something at will suggests great control and confidence.","zh":"能隨心所欲地做某事，暗示高度控制和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ability that can be used freely.","zh":"這個短語描述可自由運用的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"preferred to lead","meaning":"較喜歡過……生活","examples":[{"en":"Mozart often preferred to lead a hedonistic lifestyle.","zh":"莫扎特常較喜歡過享樂主義的生活。"},{"en":"Preferred to lead a lifestyle means chose or liked living in that particular way.","zh":"較喜歡過某種生活，是指選擇或喜歡以某種方式生活。"},{"en":"Some people prefer to lead a quiet lifestyle away from social media.","zh":"有些人較喜歡過遠離社交媒體的安靜生活。"},{"en":"Lifestyle preference can affect how someone uses time, money, and energy.","zh":"生活方式偏好會影響一個人如何使用時間、金錢和精力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a chosen way of life.","zh":"這個短語描述被選擇的生活方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"hedonistic lifestyle","meaning":"享樂主義的生活方式","examples":[{"en":"Mozart often preferred to lead a hedonistic lifestyle.","zh":"莫扎特常較喜歡過享樂主義的生活方式。"},{"en":"A hedonistic lifestyle focuses on pleasure, enjoyment, and personal satisfaction.","zh":"享樂主義的生活方式聚焦快樂、享受和個人滿足。"},{"en":"Someone with a hedonistic lifestyle may spend freely on food, parties, and entertainment.","zh":"過享樂主義生活的人可能在食物、派對和娛樂上大量花費。"},{"en":"Such a lifestyle may feel exciting, but it can conflict with discipline and long-term work.","zh":"這種生活方式可能感覺刺激，但可能與紀律和長期工作衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a pleasure-seeking way of life.","zh":"這個短語描述追求享樂的生活方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"more exciting than","meaning":"比……更刺激","examples":[{"en":"Mozart found his lifestyle more exciting than writing music to order.","zh":"莫扎特覺得他的生活方式比按要求創作音樂更刺激。"},{"en":"More exciting than means giving more pleasure, interest, or stimulation than something else.","zh":"比某事更刺激，是指比另一事物帶來更多快樂、興趣或刺激。"},{"en":"Some students find group projects more exciting than silent worksheets.","zh":"有些學生覺得小組專題比安靜工作紙更刺激。"},{"en":"Comparing what is more exciting can explain why someone chooses one activity over another.","zh":"比較甚麼更刺激，可以解釋某人為何選擇某活動而不是另一活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a comparison of interest or enjoyment.","zh":"這個短語描述興趣或享受上的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"writing music to order","meaning":"按要求創作音樂","examples":[{"en":"Mozart sometimes had to write music to order.","zh":"莫扎特有時必須按要求創作音樂。"},{"en":"Writing music to order means composing music because someone has requested or commissioned it.","zh":"按要求創作音樂，是因有人要求或委託而作曲。"},{"en":"A composer may write music to order for a wedding, film, or ceremony.","zh":"作曲家可能為婚禮、電影或典禮按要求創作音樂。"},{"en":"Writing to order can provide income, but it may feel less free than creating for oneself.","zh":"按要求創作可以帶來收入，但可能比為自己創作較不自由。"},{"en":"This phrase describes commissioned musical work.","zh":"這個短語描述受委託的音樂創作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"talents have blossomed","meaning":"才能得以綻放","examples":[{"en":"Einstein’s and Gates’s talents blossomed because of their times.","zh":"愛因斯坦和 Gates 的才能因他們所處的時代而得以綻放。"},{"en":"Talents have blossomed means abilities have developed fully and successfully.","zh":"才能得以綻放，是指能力充分而成功地發展。"},{"en":"A student’s writing talent may blossom after joining a supportive writing club.","zh":"學生加入支持性寫作學會後，寫作才能可能得以綻放。"},{"en":"Talent can blossom when the right environment meets the right opportunity.","zh":"當合適環境遇上合適機會，才能可以綻放。"},{"en":"This phrase compares talent development to a flower opening.","zh":"這個短語把才能發展比作花朵盛開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"by virtue of","meaning":"憑藉；由於","examples":[{"en":"Their talents blossomed by virtue of the times they were living in.","zh":"他們的才能憑藉所處時代而得以綻放。"},{"en":"By virtue of means because of or as a result of a particular factor.","zh":"憑藉或由於，是指因某個特定因素而發生。"},{"en":"A student may win a prize by virtue of hard work and steady practice.","zh":"學生可能憑藉努力和穩定練習而得獎。"},{"en":"Einstein and Gates succeeded partly by virtue of the historical opportunities around them.","zh":"愛因斯坦和 Gates 部分憑藉身邊的歷史機會而成功。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the reason for an outcome.","zh":"這個短語給出結果的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the times they were living in","meaning":"他們所處的時代","examples":[{"en":"Their success was partly due to the times they were living in.","zh":"他們的成功部分由於他們所處的時代。"},{"en":"The times they were living in means the historical period and conditions around them.","zh":"他們所處的時代，是指他們身處的歷史時期和周遭條件。"},{"en":"A young app developer today benefits from the times they are living in because smartphones are everywhere.","zh":"今天的年輕應用程式開發者受惠於所處時代，因為智能手機無處不在。"},{"en":"Historical timing can create opportunities that earlier generations did not have.","zh":"歷史時機可以創造較早世代沒有的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase connects success with the wider era.","zh":"這個短語把成功與更廣闊時代連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"solitary","meaning":"孤僻的；獨處的","examples":[{"en":"Einstein was a solitary, somewhat slow child.","zh":"愛因斯坦是一個孤僻、有點遲鈍的孩子。"},{"en":"Solitary means spending much time alone or preferring to be alone.","zh":"孤僻或獨處的，是指花很多時間獨自一人，或較喜歡獨處。"},{"en":"A solitary student may read quietly during lunch instead of joining a large group.","zh":"孤僻的學生可能午飯時安靜閱讀，而不是加入大群人。"},{"en":"Being solitary does not mean a child lacks ability or imagination.","zh":"孤僻不代表孩子缺乏能力或想像力。"},{"en":"This word describes social style or behaviour.","zh":"這個詞描述社交風格或行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"somewhat slow child","meaning":"有點遲鈍的孩子","examples":[{"en":"Einstein was described as a somewhat slow child.","zh":"愛因斯坦被描述為一個有點遲鈍的孩子。"},{"en":"A somewhat slow child is a child who appears a little slow in development, speech, or response.","zh":"有點遲鈍的孩子，是在發展、說話或反應上看起來稍慢的孩子。"},{"en":"A somewhat slow child may still become strong later if given time and support.","zh":"有點遲鈍的孩子如果得到時間和支援，日後仍可能變得很強。"},{"en":"Early slowness does not necessarily predict adult ability.","zh":"早期遲緩不一定預測成年能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an early impression, not a final judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述早期印象，而不是最終判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"affection at home","meaning":"家中的關愛","examples":[{"en":"Einstein had affection at home.","zh":"愛因斯坦在家中有關愛。"},{"en":"Affection at home means warmth, care, and love within the family.","zh":"家中的關愛，是家庭中的溫暖、照顧和愛。"},{"en":"A child who receives affection at home may feel safer trying difficult tasks.","zh":"在家中得到關愛的孩子，可能更有安全感去嘗試困難任務。"},{"en":"Affection can support confidence even when a child seems unusual or slow.","zh":"即使孩子看起來不尋常或較慢，關愛也可以支持信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional support in family life.","zh":"這個短語描述家庭生活中的情感支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"phenomenal intelligence","meaning":"驚人的智力","examples":[{"en":"Einstein’s phenomenal intelligence emerged without obvious parental input.","zh":"愛因斯坦驚人的智力在沒有明顯父母投入下顯現出來。"},{"en":"Phenomenal intelligence means extremely impressive and unusual mental ability.","zh":"驚人的智力，是極其令人印象深刻且不尋常的心智能力。"},{"en":"A child with phenomenal intelligence may understand complex ideas much earlier than expected.","zh":"具有驚人智力的孩子可能比預期更早理解複雜概念。"},{"en":"Such intelligence can surprise others because it seems far beyond ordinary ability.","zh":"這種智力會令人驚訝，因為它似乎遠超普通能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exceptional intellectual power.","zh":"這個短語描述非凡的智力力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"emerged","meaning":"顯現出來","examples":[{"en":"Einstein’s intelligence emerged without obvious parental input.","zh":"愛因斯坦的智力在沒有明顯父母投入下顯現出來。"},{"en":"Emerged means appeared, became clear, or began to be noticed.","zh":"顯現出來，是指出現、變得清楚或開始被注意。"},{"en":"A student’s leadership ability may emerge during a group project.","zh":"學生的領導能力可能在小組專題中顯現出來。"},{"en":"Talent may emerge slowly when the right challenge appears.","zh":"當合適挑戰出現，才能可能慢慢顯現出來。"},{"en":"This word describes something becoming visible or recognised.","zh":"這個詞描述某事變得可見或被認出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"obvious parental input","meaning":"明顯的父母投入","examples":[{"en":"Einstein’s intelligence emerged without obvious parental input.","zh":"愛因斯坦的智力在沒有明顯父母投入下顯現出來。"},{"en":"Obvious parental input means clear effort, teaching, or involvement from parents.","zh":"明顯的父母投入，是指父母清楚可見的努力、教導或參與。"},{"en":"A child’s piano skill may show obvious parental input if parents arrange lessons and daily practice.","zh":"如果父母安排課堂和每日練習，孩子的鋼琴能力可能顯示明顯父母投入。"},{"en":"Lack of obvious parental input does not mean parents had no influence at all.","zh":"沒有明顯父母投入不代表父母完全沒有影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible parent involvement.","zh":"這個短語描述可見的父母參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"partly due to","meaning":"部分由於","examples":[{"en":"His success may have been partly due to changes in physics at the time.","zh":"他的成功可能部分由於當時物理學的變化。"},{"en":"Partly due to means caused in part by something, but not entirely.","zh":"部分由於，是指某事部分由另一因素造成，但不完全是。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be partly due to better sleep and partly due to more practice.","zh":"學生進步可能部分由於睡眠改善，也部分由於更多練習。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids saying there is only one cause.","zh":"這個短語避免說只有一個原因。"},{"en":"It is useful for balanced explanations.","zh":"它適合用於平衡解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"Newtonian laws of physics","meaning":"牛頓物理定律","examples":[{"en":"The Newtonian laws of physics were being questioned.","zh":"牛頓物理定律正受到質疑。"},{"en":"Newtonian laws of physics are the classical laws of motion and gravity associated with Isaac Newton.","zh":"牛頓物理定律是與 Isaac Newton 相關的經典運動和重力定律。"},{"en":"Students learn Newtonian laws of physics when studying force, motion, and acceleration.","zh":"學生學習力、運動和加速度時，會學到牛頓物理定律。"},{"en":"When these laws were questioned, new ideas in physics became possible.","zh":"當這些定律受到質疑，物理學的新想法變得可能。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to traditional classical physics.","zh":"這個短語指傳統經典物理學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"being questioned","meaning":"正受到質疑","examples":[{"en":"At the start of the 20th century, Newtonian laws were being questioned.","zh":"二十世紀初，牛頓物理定律正受到質疑。"},{"en":"Being questioned means being doubted, challenged, or examined critically.","zh":"正受到質疑，是指被懷疑、挑戰或批判性檢視。"},{"en":"A school rule may be questioned if students think it is unfair.","zh":"如果學生認為校規不公平，該規則可能正受到質疑。"},{"en":"When old ideas are questioned, new explanations may emerge.","zh":"當舊想法受到質疑，新解釋可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active doubt or challenge.","zh":"這個短語描述正在發生的懷疑或挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"fertile ground for","meaning":"……的肥沃土壤；有利條件","examples":[{"en":"The questioning of physics left fertile ground for Einstein’s ideas.","zh":"對物理學的質疑為愛因斯坦的想法留下肥沃土壤。"},{"en":"Fertile ground for something means favourable conditions that help it grow or succeed.","zh":"某事的肥沃土壤或有利條件，是幫助它成長或成功的良好條件。"},{"en":"A supportive classroom can provide fertile ground for creative writing.","zh":"支持性的課室可以為創意寫作提供肥沃土壤。"},{"en":"When old theories are uncertain, new ideas may find fertile ground.","zh":"當舊理論不確定，新想法可能找到有利條件。"},{"en":"This phrase uses farming imagery to describe opportunity.","zh":"這個短語用農業意象描述機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"ideas such as his","meaning":"像他那樣的想法","examples":[{"en":"The period created fertile ground for ideas such as his.","zh":"這個時期為像他那樣的想法創造了肥沃土壤。"},{"en":"Ideas such as his means ideas like the ones he developed or proposed.","zh":"像他那樣的想法，是指與他發展或提出的想法相似的想法。"},{"en":"A new computer age created opportunities for ideas such as Gates’s.","zh":"新電腦時代為像 Gates 那樣的想法創造機會。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a type of idea without repeating the full description.","zh":"這個短語指出某類想法，而不重複完整描述。"},{"en":"It connects a person’s thinking with a broader group of similar ideas.","zh":"它把一個人的思想與更廣泛的相似想法連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"creative vision","meaning":"創意眼光","examples":[{"en":"Bill Gates had the creative vision to develop Microsoft.","zh":"Bill Gates 有創意眼光去發展 Microsoft。"},{"en":"Creative vision means the ability to imagine a new possibility and see how it could become real.","zh":"創意眼光是想像新可能性並看見它如何成真的能力。"},{"en":"An entrepreneur with creative vision may see how a simple app can solve a common problem.","zh":"有創意眼光的創業者可能看見一個簡單應用程式如何解決常見問題。"},{"en":"Creative vision can turn technical knowledge into a new business or product.","zh":"創意眼光可以把技術知識變成新企業或產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes imaginative foresight.","zh":"這個短語描述富想像力的遠見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"computer age","meaning":"電腦時代","examples":[{"en":"The new computer age helped Gates achieve success.","zh":"新電腦時代幫助 Gates 取得成功。"},{"en":"The computer age is the period when computers became central to work, business, and daily life.","zh":"電腦時代是電腦成為工作、商業和日常生活核心的時期。"},{"en":"Students in the computer age need digital skills for many careers.","zh":"電腦時代的學生在許多職業中需要數碼技能。"},{"en":"Gates’s talent became powerful because the computer age created huge demand for software.","zh":"Gates 的才能變得有影響力，因為電腦時代創造了巨大軟件需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a historical period shaped by computers.","zh":"這個短語描述由電腦塑造的歷史時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"dawning","meaning":"正開始出現","examples":[{"en":"The new computer age was dawning at the same time.","zh":"新電腦時代同時正開始出現。"},{"en":"Dawning means beginning to appear or develop.","zh":"正開始出現，是指開始顯現或發展。"},{"en":"A new era of online learning was dawning when schools started using video lessons.","zh":"當學校開始使用視像課堂，網上學習的新時代正開始出現。"},{"en":"When an age is dawning, early opportunities may appear for people who recognise them.","zh":"當一個時代正開始出現，能看見機會的人可能得到早期優勢。"},{"en":"This word describes the beginning of a new period.","zh":"這個詞描述新時期的開端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"同時","examples":[{"en":"The computer age was dawning at the same time as Gates’s career.","zh":"電腦時代與 Gates 的事業同時開始出現。"},{"en":"At the same time means during the same period or simultaneously.","zh":"同時，是指在同一時期或同一時間。"},{"en":"A student may study and work part-time at the same time.","zh":"學生可能同時學習和兼職工作。"},{"en":"Gates’s rise mattered because his career and the computer age developed together.","zh":"Gates 的崛起重要，是因為他的事業和電腦時代一起發展。"},{"en":"This phrase links two events happening together.","zh":"這個短語連接兩件同時發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"achieved the position","meaning":"取得地位","examples":[{"en":"Without the computer age, Gates may not have achieved his position.","zh":"沒有電腦時代，Gates 可能不會取得他的地位。"},{"en":"To achieve a position means to reach a particular status, role, or level of success.","zh":"取得某個地位，是指達到某種身份、角色或成功水平。"},{"en":"A teacher may achieve the position of principal after years of leadership.","zh":"老師經過多年領導工作後，可能取得校長地位。"},{"en":"Achieving a major position often requires ability and the right timing.","zh":"取得重要地位通常需要能力和合適時機。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching a recognised place in society or a profession.","zh":"這個短語描述在社會或專業中達到被認可的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"on the world stage","meaning":"在世界舞台上","examples":[{"en":"Bill Gates occupies a major position on the world stage.","zh":"Bill Gates 在世界舞台上佔據重要地位。"},{"en":"On the world stage means in international public life or global influence.","zh":"在世界舞台上，是指在國際公共生活或全球影響力中。"},{"en":"A young activist may speak on the world stage if their campaign becomes global.","zh":"如果年輕倡議者的運動變成全球性，他們可能在世界舞台上發言。"},{"en":"People on the world stage can influence ideas, business, or policy across countries.","zh":"在世界舞台上的人物可以影響跨國思想、商業或政策。"},{"en":"This phrase describes global visibility and importance.","zh":"這個短語描述全球可見度和重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"now occupies","meaning":"現在佔據的","examples":[{"en":"Gates may never have achieved the position he now occupies.","zh":"Gates 可能永遠無法取得他現在佔據的地位。"},{"en":"Now occupies means currently holds or has a particular position.","zh":"現在佔據的，是指目前擁有或處於某個位置。"},{"en":"A former student may now occupy a senior role in a technology company.","zh":"一名前學生現在可能在科技公司佔據高級職位。"},{"en":"The phrase compares a person’s present status with what might have happened otherwise.","zh":"這個短語把一個人的現時地位與另一種可能情況作比較。"},{"en":"It describes someone’s current place or role.","zh":"它描述某人目前的位置或角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"complete the notes","meaning":"完成筆記","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the notes about changing definitions of talent.","zh":"學生完成關於才能定義變化的筆記。"},{"en":"To complete the notes means to fill in missing information in a note-taking task.","zh":"完成筆記，是指在筆記題中填上缺失資料。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may complete the notes using words from the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能用篇章中的字詞完成筆記。"},{"en":"This task checks whether students can locate and understand key details.","zh":"這類題目檢查學生能否定位並理解關鍵細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"approaches to defining","meaning":"定義……的方法","examples":[{"en":"The notes show different approaches to defining talent.","zh":"筆記顯示定義才能的不同方法。"},{"en":"Approaches to defining something are different ways of explaining or setting its meaning.","zh":"定義某事的方法，是解釋或設定其意思的不同方式。"},{"en":"Teachers may use several approaches to defining success in a course.","zh":"老師可能使用幾種方法定義一門課程中的成功。"},{"en":"Different definitions can lead to different ways of selecting or supporting students.","zh":"不同定義可以帶來不同選拔或支援學生的方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes methods for deciding meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述決定意思的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"have changed","meaning":"已經改變","examples":[{"en":"The approaches to defining talent have changed over time.","zh":"定義才能的方法已經隨時間改變。"},{"en":"Have changed means are different now from before.","zh":"已經改變，是指現在與以前不同。"},{"en":"School rules have changed since students started using tablets.","zh":"自從學生開始使用平板電腦後，校規已經改變。"},{"en":"Ideas about talent have changed as researchers considered creativity and environment.","zh":"隨着研究人員考慮創造力和環境，對才能的看法已經改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes development across time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"choose one or two words","meaning":"選擇一至兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Students choose one or two words from the passage.","zh":"學生從文章中選擇一至兩個字。"},{"en":"To choose one or two words means to select a short answer with only one or two words.","zh":"選擇一至兩個字，是指選取只包含一個或兩個詞的短答案。"},{"en":"In IELTS reading, students must follow the word limit carefully.","zh":"在 IELTS 閱讀中，學生必須小心遵守字數限制。"},{"en":"Choosing too many words can make an answer wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，選太多字也可能令答案錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"from the passage","meaning":"來自文章","examples":[{"en":"The answers must come from the passage.","zh":"答案必須來自文章。"},{"en":"From the passage means taken directly from the reading text.","zh":"來自文章，是指直接取自閱讀文本。"},{"en":"Students should not use their own words if the instruction says answers must come from the passage.","zh":"如果指示說答案必須來自文章，學生不應使用自己的字眼。"},{"en":"This requirement tests careful reading rather than outside knowledge.","zh":"這項要求測試仔細閱讀，而不是外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading-completion tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀填空題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"answer sheet","meaning":"答題紙","examples":[{"en":"Students write their answers on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生把答案寫在答題紙上。"},{"en":"An answer sheet is the paper or form where candidates record final answers.","zh":"答題紙是考生記錄最終答案的紙張或表格。"},{"en":"In an exam, writing on the question paper may not count if the answer sheet is required.","zh":"在考試中，如果要求使用答題紙，寫在試題紙上可能不會被計分。"},{"en":"Careful transfer to the answer sheet helps avoid losing marks.","zh":"小心把答案轉到答題紙上，有助避免失分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the official place for exam answers.","zh":"這個短語指考試答案的正式位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"regard as","meaning":"視為……","examples":[{"en":"The writer regards several features as common in creative families.","zh":"作者視幾個特徵為創意家庭中的常見特徵。"},{"en":"To regard something as something means to consider or see it in that way.","zh":"視某事為某物，是指以那種方式考慮或看待它。"},{"en":"A teacher may regard punctuality as an important study habit.","zh":"老師可能視準時為重要學習習慣。"},{"en":"What people regard as talent can change across cultures and time.","zh":"人們視為才能的東西，會隨文化和時代改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes judgement or interpretation.","zh":"這個短語描述判斷或理解方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"a feature of","meaning":"……的一項特徵","examples":[{"en":"Parental commitment may be a feature of creative families.","zh":"父母投入可能是創意家庭的一項特徵。"},{"en":"A feature of something is a characteristic or quality it has.","zh":"某事的一項特徵，是它所具有的特點或性質。"},{"en":"Small class size may be a feature of a private language school.","zh":"小班教學可能是私立語言學校的一項特徵。"},{"en":"Identifying features helps compare one group with another.","zh":"識別特徵有助比較一個群體與另一群體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a typical characteristic.","zh":"這個短語描述典型特點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"creative families","meaning":"創意家庭","examples":[{"en":"The questions ask about features of creative families.","zh":"題目問關於創意家庭的特徵。"},{"en":"Creative families are families in which creativity is valued, supported, or repeatedly shown.","zh":"創意家庭是重視、支持或反覆展現創造力的家庭。"},{"en":"Creative families may encourage children to explore music, acting, writing, or design.","zh":"創意家庭可能鼓勵孩子探索音樂、演戲、寫作或設計。"},{"en":"Such families can create an environment where talent is noticed and nurtured.","zh":"這類家庭可以創造一種才能被注意和培育的環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes families connected with creative development.","zh":"這個短語描述與創意發展相關的家庭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"higher than average level of","meaning":"高於平均水平的……","examples":[{"en":"One option mentions a higher than average level of parental affection.","zh":"一個選項提到高於平均水平的父母關愛。"},{"en":"A higher than average level of something means more of it than is usual.","zh":"高於平均水平的某事，是指比平常更多。"},{"en":"A class may have a higher than average level of reading ability if most students read daily.","zh":"如果大多數學生每天閱讀，一班學生可能有高於平均水平的閱讀能力。"},{"en":"Higher than average affection does not necessarily mean better talent development.","zh":"高於平均水平的關愛不一定代表更好的才能發展。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one level with the normal level.","zh":"這個短語把某水平與正常水平比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"parental affection","meaning":"父母關愛","examples":[{"en":"Creative families are not necessarily marked by unusually high parental affection.","zh":"創意家庭不一定以異常高水平的父母關愛為特徵。"},{"en":"Parental affection means love, warmth, and emotional care from parents.","zh":"父母關愛是來自父母的愛、溫暖和情感照顧。"},{"en":"A parent shows affection by listening, hugging, praising, or spending time with a child.","zh":"父母透過聆聽、擁抱、讚賞或陪伴孩子來表達關愛。"},{"en":"Parental affection can help children feel secure, but creativity also needs challenge and work.","zh":"父母關愛可以幫助孩子有安全感，但創造力也需要挑戰和努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional warmth from parents.","zh":"這個短語描述來自父母的情感溫暖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"competition between","meaning":"……之間的競爭","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions competition between brothers and sisters.","zh":"題目提到兄弟姊妹之間的競爭。"},{"en":"Competition between people means they try to do better than each other.","zh":"人與人之間的競爭，是指他們嘗試比對方做得更好。"},{"en":"Competition between classmates can be healthy if it encourages effort without cruelty.","zh":"同學之間的競爭如果鼓勵努力而不殘酷，可以是健康的。"},{"en":"Competition between siblings may create motivation, jealousy, or both.","zh":"兄弟姊妹之間的競爭可能帶來動力、嫉妒，或兩者都有。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rivalry involving two or more people.","zh":"這個短語描述兩人或多人之間的 rivalry。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"brothers and sisters","meaning":"兄弟姊妹","examples":[{"en":"Competition between brothers and sisters can exist in creative families.","zh":"創意家庭中可能存在兄弟姊妹之間的競爭。"},{"en":"Brothers and sisters are children in the same family who share one or both parents.","zh":"兄弟姊妹是同一家庭中共享一位或兩位父母的孩子。"},{"en":"Brothers and sisters may compete for attention, praise, or opportunities.","zh":"兄弟姊妹可能為關注、讚賞或機會而競爭。"},{"en":"Family competition can be positive if parents treat each child fairly.","zh":"如果父母公平對待每個孩子，家庭競爭可以是正面的。"},{"en":"This phrase is a simple way to refer to siblings.","zh":"這個短語是 siblings 的簡單說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"demonstrate vocational commitment","meaning":"展示對職業的投入","examples":[{"en":"Parents may demonstrate vocational commitment through their work.","zh":"父母可能透過工作展示對職業的投入。"},{"en":"To demonstrate vocational commitment means to show serious dedication to one’s profession or calling.","zh":"展示對職業的投入，是指顯示對專業或志業的認真奉獻。"},{"en":"A chef demonstrates vocational commitment by practising recipes and improving skills every day.","zh":"廚師每天練習食譜和改善技巧，就是展示對職業的投入。"},{"en":"Children may learn dedication when they see parents committed to their work.","zh":"當孩子看見父母投入工作，可能學到奉獻精神。"},{"en":"This phrase describes showing commitment through professional behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述透過專業行為顯示投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"vocational commitment","meaning":"對職業／志業的投入","examples":[{"en":"Creative families often show vocational commitment.","zh":"創意家庭通常展示對職業或志業的投入。"},{"en":"Vocational commitment means dedication to a chosen career, craft, or calling.","zh":"對職業或志業的投入，是對所選職業、技藝或志業的奉獻。"},{"en":"A musician practising every morning shows vocational commitment.","zh":"每天早上練習的音樂家展示對志業的投入。"},{"en":"Vocational commitment can teach children that mastery requires time and effort.","zh":"對職業的投入可以教導孩子，精通需要時間和努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious devotion to work or craft.","zh":"這個短語描述對工作或技藝的認真奉獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"strong motivation to","meaning":"做……的強烈動力","examples":[{"en":"One option refers to strong motivation to take exams and attend university.","zh":"一個選項提到參加考試和入讀大學的強烈動力。"},{"en":"Strong motivation to do something means a powerful desire or drive to do it.","zh":"做某事的強烈動力，是指做該事的強烈願望或推動力。"},{"en":"A student with strong motivation to improve English may practise speaking every day.","zh":"有強烈動力改善英語的學生可能每天練習說話。"},{"en":"Strong motivation can help people continue even when tasks are difficult.","zh":"強烈動力可以幫助人們即使任務困難仍繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intense inner drive.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈內在推動力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"take exams","meaning":"參加考試","examples":[{"en":"Martin Sheen turned his back on taking entrance exams.","zh":"Martin Sheen 放棄參加入學考試。"},{"en":"To take exams means to sit formal tests.","zh":"參加考試，是指應考正式測驗。"},{"en":"Students take exams at the end of a school term to show what they have learned.","zh":"學生在學期末參加考試，以顯示自己學到了甚麼。"},{"en":"Choosing not to take exams may close some academic routes.","zh":"選擇不參加考試可能關閉某些學術路線。"},{"en":"This phrase describes participating in formal assessment.","zh":"這個短語描述參與正式評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"attend university","meaning":"入讀大學","examples":[{"en":"Some parents may expect their children to attend university.","zh":"有些父母可能期望孩子入讀大學。"},{"en":"To attend university means to study at a university as a student.","zh":"入讀大學，是指以學生身份在大學學習。"},{"en":"A student may attend university to study medicine, engineering, or literature.","zh":"學生可能入讀大學修讀醫學、工程或文學。"},{"en":"Attending university can open career paths, but it is not the only route to success.","zh":"入讀大學可以打開職業道路，但不是成功唯一途徑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes going into higher education.","zh":"這個短語描述進入高等教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"patient approach to","meaning":"對……採取耐心的方法","examples":[{"en":"Creative families may encourage a patient approach to achieving success.","zh":"創意家庭可能鼓勵對取得成功採取耐心的方法。"},{"en":"A patient approach to something means dealing with it calmly and over time, without rushing.","zh":"對某事採取耐心的方法，是指冷靜且長期處理它，不急於求成。"},{"en":"Learning a language requires a patient approach to grammar, vocabulary, and speaking practice.","zh":"學習語言需要對文法、詞彙和口語練習採取耐心的方法。"},{"en":"A patient approach can reduce pressure and support long-term growth.","zh":"耐心方法可以減少壓力並支持長期成長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow, steady effort.","zh":"這個短語描述緩慢而穩定的努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"achieving success","meaning":"取得成功","examples":[{"en":"Talent often requires patience in achieving success.","zh":"才能在取得成功時通常需要耐性。"},{"en":"Achieving success means reaching a desired goal or strong result.","zh":"取得成功，是指達到想要的目標或強而有力的結果。"},{"en":"A student may achieve success in writing after many drafts and feedback sessions.","zh":"學生可能經過多次草稿和回饋後，在寫作上取得成功。"},{"en":"Success usually requires more than talent; it also needs time, effort, and opportunity.","zh":"成功通常需要的不只是才能，也需要時間、努力和機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of reaching a goal.","zh":"這個短語描述達成目標的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"identification of","meaning":"對……的識別","examples":[{"en":"The identification of each child’s talent is important.","zh":"對每個孩子才能的識別很重要。"},{"en":"Identification of something means recognising and naming it clearly.","zh":"對某事的識別，是指清楚認出並說明它。"},{"en":"Early identification of reading problems can help students receive support sooner.","zh":"早期識別閱讀問題可以幫助學生更快得到支援。"},{"en":"Identifying talent allows parents and teachers to provide suitable opportunities.","zh":"識別才能讓父母和老師提供合適機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the act of recognising something.","zh":"這個短語描述認出某事的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"most talented child","meaning":"家中最有才華的孩子","examples":[{"en":"The question option refers to the most talented child in the family.","zh":"題目選項指家中最有才華的孩子。"},{"en":"The most talented child is the child who appears to have the strongest ability in a particular area or overall.","zh":"家中最有才華的孩子，是在某方面或整體上看似能力最強的孩子。"},{"en":"A family may wrongly focus only on the most talented child and ignore others.","zh":"家庭可能錯誤地只關注最有才華的孩子，而忽略其他孩子。"},{"en":"Labelling one child as the most talented can create jealousy or pressure.","zh":"把一名孩子標籤為最有才華，可能造成嫉妒或壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a comparison within a family or group.","zh":"這個短語描述家庭或群體內的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"choose the appropriate letters","meaning":"選出合適字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the appropriate letters for the questions.","zh":"學生為題目選出合適字母。"},{"en":"To choose the appropriate letters means to select the option letters that correctly answer the questions.","zh":"選出合適字母，是指選擇正確回答題目的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a matching task, students may choose letters A to F from a list.","zh":"在配對題中，學生可能從 A 至 F 的列表中選字母。"},{"en":"Choosing the appropriate letters requires understanding the passage, not just guessing.","zh":"選出合適字母需要理解篇章，而不只是猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction about answer format.","zh":"這個短語是關於答案格式的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"rat experiment","meaning":"老鼠實驗","examples":[{"en":"The rat experiment shows that surroundings can influence behaviour.","zh":"老鼠實驗顯示周遭環境可以影響行為。"},{"en":"A rat experiment is a scientific study using rats to test behaviour, learning, or biology.","zh":"老鼠實驗是使用老鼠測試行為、學習或生物學的科學研究。"},{"en":"In a rat experiment, researchers may count how many mistakes rats make in a maze.","zh":"在老鼠實驗中，研究人員可能計算老鼠在迷宮中犯多少錯。"},{"en":"Such experiments can help scientists think about genetics and environment.","zh":"這類實驗可以幫助科學家思考遺傳和環境。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an animal study involving rats.","zh":"這個短語指涉及老鼠的動物研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"was conducted to show that","meaning":"被進行以顯示……","examples":[{"en":"The rat experiment was conducted to show that environment matters.","zh":"老鼠實驗被進行以顯示環境很重要。"},{"en":"Was conducted to show that means was carried out in order to demonstrate a point.","zh":"被進行以顯示某事，是指被執行來證明某個重點。"},{"en":"A survey was conducted to show that students wanted more library time.","zh":"一項問卷被進行以顯示學生想要更多圖書館時間。"},{"en":"Experiments are conducted to test ideas, not just to collect random information.","zh":"實驗被進行是為了測試想法，而不只是收集隨機資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose of a study.","zh":"這個短語解釋研究目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"certain species of","meaning":"某些物種的……","examples":[{"en":"One option suggests that certain species of rat are more intelligent.","zh":"一個選項提出某些物種的老鼠較聰明。"},{"en":"Certain species of something means particular types within a larger biological group.","zh":"某些物種的某物，是指較大生物群體中的特定類型。"},{"en":"Certain species of birds can remember long migration routes.","zh":"某些物種的鳥能記住長途遷徙路線。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies selected kinds, not all members of a group.","zh":"這個短語指出被選定的種類，而不是整個群體。"},{"en":"It is often used in scientific comparison.","zh":"它常用於科學比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"more intelligent than","meaning":"比……更聰明","examples":[{"en":"Some rats appeared more intelligent than others.","zh":"有些老鼠看起來比其他老鼠更聰明。"},{"en":"More intelligent than means showing stronger thinking, learning, or problem-solving ability than another person or animal.","zh":"比某人更聰明，是指顯示比另一人或動物更強的思考、學習或解難能力。"},{"en":"A student may seem more intelligent than others in one subject but not in every area.","zh":"學生可能在某一科看起來比其他人更聰明，但不一定在每方面都是。"},{"en":"In the maze, fewer wrong turns made some rats appear more intelligent.","zh":"在迷宮中，較少錯誤轉向令有些老鼠看起來更聰明。"},{"en":"This phrase compares mental performance.","zh":"這個短語比較心智表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"more motivated than","meaning":"比……更有動力","examples":[{"en":"One option says intelligent rats are more motivated than dull rats.","zh":"一個選項說聰明老鼠比遲鈍老鼠更有動力。"},{"en":"More motivated than means having a stronger desire or drive to act than another person or group.","zh":"比某人更有動力，是指比另一人或群體有更強行動願望或推動力。"},{"en":"A student who wants a scholarship may be more motivated than someone with no clear goal.","zh":"想拿獎學金的學生可能比沒有明確目標的人更有動力。"},{"en":"Motivation can affect performance, so researchers must distinguish it from intelligence.","zh":"動力可以影響表現，所以研究人員必須把它與智力區分開。"},{"en":"This phrase compares levels of drive.","zh":"這個短語比較推動力水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"surroundings","meaning":"周遭環境","examples":[{"en":"A rat’s surroundings can influence its behaviour.","zh":"老鼠的周遭環境可以影響其行為。"},{"en":"Surroundings are the environment or conditions around a person or animal.","zh":"周遭環境是一個人或動物周圍的環境或條件。"},{"en":"A quiet library gives students different surroundings from a noisy café.","zh":"安靜圖書館給學生的周遭環境不同於嘈雜咖啡店。"},{"en":"Surroundings can change how well someone concentrates, learns, or behaves.","zh":"周遭環境可以改變某人集中、學習或行為的表現。"},{"en":"This word refers to what is around someone.","zh":"這個詞指某人周圍的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"influence its behaviour","meaning":"影響其行為","examples":[{"en":"The rat’s surroundings can influence its behaviour.","zh":"老鼠的周遭環境可以影響其行為。"},{"en":"To influence its behaviour means to affect how it acts.","zh":"影響其行為，是指影響它如何行動。"},{"en":"Noise can influence a child’s behaviour by making them restless.","zh":"噪音可以令孩子坐立不安，從而影響其行為。"},{"en":"In the experiment, a stimulating maze influenced how well rats performed.","zh":"在實驗中，有刺激性的迷宮影響老鼠表現如何。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an effect on actions.","zh":"這個短語描述對行動的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"boring environment","meaning":"沉悶的環境","examples":[{"en":"A boring environment affected both bright and dull rats.","zh":"沉悶的環境影響了聰明和遲鈍老鼠。"},{"en":"A boring environment is a place with little stimulation, interest, or challenge.","zh":"沉悶的環境是缺乏刺激、興趣或挑戰的地方。"},{"en":"A classroom with no discussion, colour, or activity may feel like a boring environment.","zh":"沒有討論、色彩或活動的課室可能像沉悶的環境。"},{"en":"A boring environment can reduce motivation and hide differences in ability.","zh":"沉悶的環境可以降低動力並掩蓋能力差異。"},{"en":"This phrase describes surroundings that do not encourage engagement.","zh":"這個短語描述不鼓勵投入的周遭環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"have little impact on","meaning":"對……影響很小","examples":[{"en":"One option says a boring environment has little impact on a bright rat.","zh":"一個選項說沉悶環境對聰明老鼠影響很小。"},{"en":"To have little impact on something means to affect it only slightly.","zh":"對某事影響很小，是指只輕微影響它。"},{"en":"A short power cut may have little impact on a school if lessons continue normally.","zh":"如果課堂正常繼續，短暫停電可能對學校影響很小。"},{"en":"If a boring environment has little impact, performance should remain similar.","zh":"如果沉悶環境影響很小，表現應保持相似。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weak effect.","zh":"這個短語描述微弱影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"cites the story of","meaning":"引用……的故事","examples":[{"en":"The writer cites the story of Martin Sheen as an example.","zh":"作者引用 Martin Sheen 的故事作為例子。"},{"en":"To cite the story of someone means to mention their experience as evidence or illustration.","zh":"引用某人的故事，是指提及其經歷作為證據或說明。"},{"en":"A teacher may cite the story of a successful student to encourage a class.","zh":"老師可能引用成功學生的故事來鼓勵全班。"},{"en":"Citing a story can make an abstract argument easier to understand.","zh":"引用故事可以令抽象論點更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using a real example.","zh":"這個短語描述使用真實例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"creative line","meaning":"創意家族傳承","examples":[{"en":"Martin Sheen was the first in a creative line.","zh":"Martin Sheen 是創意家族傳承中的第一人。"},{"en":"A creative line is a family line or sequence of people connected by creative work.","zh":"創意家族傳承，是由創意工作連接起來的家庭脈絡或人物序列。"},{"en":"If a painter’s children become designers and musicians, the family may form a creative line.","zh":"如果畫家的孩子成為設計師和音樂家，該家庭可能形成創意傳承。"},{"en":"One person’s success can begin a creative line that later generations follow.","zh":"一個人的成功可以開創後代跟隨的創意傳承。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creative talent continuing through a family.","zh":"這個短語描述創意才能在家庭中延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"creative flair","meaning":"創意才華","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to whether his parents had creative flair.","zh":"該選項提到他的父母是否有創意才華。"},{"en":"Creative flair is a natural talent for imaginative, artistic, or original work.","zh":"創意才華是在富想像力、藝術或原創工作上的自然才能。"},{"en":"A student with creative flair may turn a simple poster into something memorable.","zh":"有創意才華的學生可能把簡單海報變成令人難忘的作品。"},{"en":"Creative flair can appear in design, acting, writing, or problem-solving.","zh":"創意才華可以出現在設計、演戲、寫作或解難中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes natural creative style and ability.","zh":"這個短語描述自然創意風格和能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"proper training","meaning":"正規訓練","examples":[{"en":"The question option mentions becoming an actor without proper training.","zh":"題目選項提到在沒有正規訓練下成為演員。"},{"en":"Proper training is suitable and serious instruction for developing a skill.","zh":"正規訓練是發展技能所需的合適而認真的指導。"},{"en":"A swimmer needs proper training to improve technique and avoid injury.","zh":"游泳選手需要正規訓練來改善技巧並避免受傷。"},{"en":"Talent without proper training may develop slowly or unevenly.","zh":"沒有正規訓練，才能可能發展緩慢或不均衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal or adequate preparation.","zh":"這個短語描述正式或足夠的準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"benefit from","meaning":"從……得益","examples":[{"en":"His sons were able to benefit from his talents and example.","zh":"他的兒子能夠從他的才能和榜樣中得益。"},{"en":"To benefit from something means to gain help, advantage, or improvement from it.","zh":"從某事得益，是指從中得到幫助、優勢或改善。"},{"en":"Students benefit from clear feedback because they know how to improve.","zh":"學生從清楚回饋中得益，因為他們知道如何改善。"},{"en":"Children may benefit from seeing a parent work with passion and discipline.","zh":"孩子可能從看見父母熱情而有紀律地工作中得益。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving a positive effect.","zh":"這個短語描述得到正面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"agree with the claims of","meaning":"與……的主張一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether statements agree with the claims of the writer.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與作者的主張一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the claims of the writer means to match what the writer argues or believes.","zh":"與作者的主張一致，是指符合作者論證或相信的內容。"},{"en":"A statement agrees with the writer if it says the same idea as the passage.","zh":"如果陳述說出與篇章相同的想法，它就與作者一致。"},{"en":"Students must read carefully because claims are not always stated in simple words.","zh":"學生必須仔細閱讀，因為主張不一定用簡單字眼直接說出。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in YES/NO/NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 YES/NO/NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"claims of the writer","meaning":"作者的主張","examples":[{"en":"The questions test the claims of the writer.","zh":"題目測試作者的主張。"},{"en":"Claims of the writer are the views, arguments, or conclusions the writer presents.","zh":"作者的主張，是作者提出的觀點、論點或結論。"},{"en":"A writer’s claim may be that environment matters more than natural ability.","zh":"作者的主張可能是環境比天生能力更重要。"},{"en":"Reading questions may ask whether a statement matches the writer’s claims.","zh":"閱讀題可能問某陳述是否符合作者主張。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to what the writer argues, not what the reader thinks.","zh":"這個短語指作者所論證的內容，而不是讀者想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"agrees with the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點一致","examples":[{"en":"A “YES” answer agrees with the views of the writer.","zh":"YES 答案與作者的觀點一致。"},{"en":"Agrees with the views of someone means matches that person’s opinion or argument.","zh":"與某人的觀點一致，是指符合該人的意見或論點。"},{"en":"If the writer says luck matters, a statement saying luck matters agrees with the writer’s view.","zh":"如果作者說運氣重要，而陳述也說運氣重要，它就與作者觀點一致。"},{"en":"Students must separate the writer’s view from general knowledge.","zh":"學生必須把作者觀點與常識分開。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in opinion-based reading questions.","zh":"這個短語用於觀點型閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"contradicts the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A “NO” answer contradicts the views of the writer.","zh":"NO 答案與作者的觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradicts the views of someone means says the opposite of what that person believes or argues.","zh":"與某人的觀點相矛盾，是指說出與該人相信或論證內容相反的東西。"},{"en":"If the writer says environment matters, a statement saying environment has no role contradicts the writer.","zh":"如果作者說環境重要，而陳述說環境沒有作用，就是與作者相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be based on the passage, not the student’s opinion.","zh":"矛盾必須基於篇章，而不是學生意見。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a NO answer in YES/NO/NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個短語在 YES/NO/NOT GIVEN 題中指向 NO 答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"“NOT GIVEN” means it is impossible to say from the passage.","zh":"NOT GIVEN 意味着無法從篇章判斷。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"無法判斷，是指沒有足夠資料作決定。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions a child’s age, it is impossible to say how old they are.","zh":"如果篇章從未提及孩子年齡，就無法判斷他們幾歲。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when the text gives no clear evidence.","zh":"當文本沒有清楚證據，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase corresponds to NOT GIVEN.","zh":"這個短語對應 NOT GIVEN。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"intelligence tests","meaning":"智力測驗","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to whether intelligence tests are unreliable.","zh":"該陳述提到智力測驗是否不可靠。"},{"en":"Intelligence tests are formal tests designed to measure mental ability or reasoning.","zh":"智力測驗是用來量度心智能力或推理能力的正式測驗。"},{"en":"A psychologist may use intelligence tests together with interviews and school records.","zh":"心理學家可能把智力測驗與訪談和學校紀錄一起使用。"},{"en":"Intelligence tests can be useful, but they may not measure creativity or practical talent fully.","zh":"智力測驗可以有用，但未必能完整量度創造力或實際才能。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to tests of intellectual ability.","zh":"這個短語指智力能力測驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"proved to be unreliable","meaning":"被證明不可靠","examples":[{"en":"The statement says intelligence tests have been proved to be unreliable.","zh":"該陳述說智力測驗已被證明不可靠。"},{"en":"Proved to be unreliable means shown by evidence not to be dependable or trustworthy.","zh":"被證明不可靠，是指證據顯示不能依賴或信任。"},{"en":"A bus timetable may prove to be unreliable if buses are late every day.","zh":"如果巴士每天遲到，時間表可能被證明不可靠。"},{"en":"If a test is proved unreliable, its results should not be trusted alone.","zh":"如果測驗被證明不可靠，就不應單獨信任其結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence showing that something cannot be depended on.","zh":"這個短語描述證據顯示某事不能依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"fulfil their own potential","meaning":"發揮自己的潛能","examples":[{"en":"A gifted child’s sibling may fail to fulfil their own potential.","zh":"有天賦孩子的兄弟姊妹可能未能發揮自己的潛能。"},{"en":"To fulfil one’s own potential means to develop one’s abilities as fully as possible.","zh":"發揮自己的潛能，是指盡可能充分發展自己的能力。"},{"en":"A quiet student may fulfil their potential when given confidence and suitable challenges.","zh":"安靜學生在得到信心和合適挑戰時，可能發揮自己的潛能。"},{"en":"If a sibling is ignored, their talent may not develop fully.","zh":"如果兄弟姊妹被忽略，他們的才能可能無法充分發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes turning ability into real achievement.","zh":"這個短語描述把能力變成真正成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"importance of luck","meaning":"運氣的重要性","examples":[{"en":"The importance of luck in talent is often ignored.","zh":"運氣在才能中的重要性常被忽略。"},{"en":"The importance of luck means the role chance or timing plays in success.","zh":"運氣的重要性，是機會或時機在成功中所扮演的角色。"},{"en":"Meeting the right teacher at the right time can show the importance of luck.","zh":"在合適時間遇到合適老師，可以顯示運氣的重要性。"},{"en":"Talent may not blossom if opportunity never appears.","zh":"如果機會從未出現，才能可能無法綻放。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that success is not always earned by ability alone.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者，成功不一定只靠能力得來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"genius equation","meaning":"天才形成因素","examples":[{"en":"Luck is part of the genius equation.","zh":"運氣是天才形成因素的一部分。"},{"en":"The genius equation means the combination of factors that help create genius.","zh":"天才形成因素，是幫助造就天才的因素組合。"},{"en":"Natural ability, training, family support, historical timing, and luck may all be part of the genius equation.","zh":"天生能力、訓練、家庭支持、歷史時機和運氣都可能是天才形成因素的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests genius is not caused by one simple factor.","zh":"這個短語暗示天才不是由單一簡單因素造成。"},{"en":"It describes a formula-like way of thinking about exceptional talent.","zh":"它描述一種像公式般思考非凡才能的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"tends to be ignored","meaning":"往往被忽略","examples":[{"en":"The role of luck tends to be ignored.","zh":"運氣的作用往往被忽略。"},{"en":"Tends to be ignored means is often not noticed or not considered enough.","zh":"往往被忽略，是指經常不被注意或沒有被充分考慮。"},{"en":"In group projects, quiet students’ work tends to be ignored if only loud students present.","zh":"在小組專題中，如果只有說話大聲的學生匯報，安靜學生的工作往往被忽略。"},{"en":"Luck tends to be ignored because people prefer to credit talent and effort.","zh":"運氣往往被忽略，因為人們較喜歡把功勞歸於才能和努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated pattern of being overlooked.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆被忽視的模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"acutely aware of","meaning":"強烈意識到……","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Mozart was acutely aware of his talent.","zh":"該陳述問莫扎特是否強烈意識到自己的才能。"},{"en":"Acutely aware of something means very strongly and clearly conscious of it.","zh":"強烈意識到某事，是指非常清楚且強烈地察覺它。"},{"en":"A student may be acutely aware of their accent when speaking in front of classmates.","zh":"學生在同學面前說話時，可能強烈意識到自己的口音。"},{"en":"Being acutely aware of talent may affect confidence, pressure, or self-image.","zh":"強烈意識到才能可能影響信心、壓力或自我形象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intense awareness.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈覺察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"remarkable talent","meaning":"非凡才能","examples":[{"en":"Mozart had remarkable talent in music.","zh":"莫扎特在音樂方面有非凡才能。"},{"en":"Remarkable talent means ability that is unusual, impressive, and worth noticing.","zh":"非凡才能，是不尋常、令人印象深刻且值得注意的能力。"},{"en":"A child who writes beautiful music at age six shows remarkable talent.","zh":"六歲就能寫出美妙音樂的孩子顯示非凡才能。"},{"en":"Remarkable talent often attracts attention from teachers, parents, and the public.","zh":"非凡才能通常會吸引老師、父母和公眾注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exceptional ability.","zh":"這個短語描述卓越能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"in any era","meaning":"在任何時代","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Einstein and Gates would have succeeded in any era.","zh":"該陳述問愛因斯坦和 Gates 是否會在任何時代成功。"},{"en":"In any era means in every historical period, regardless of time or conditions.","zh":"在任何時代，是指在每個歷史時期，不論時間或條件。"},{"en":"A skill useful today may not be useful in any era.","zh":"今天有用的技能未必在任何時代都有用。"},{"en":"The phrase questions whether talent alone is enough without the right historical moment.","zh":"這個短語質疑沒有合適歷史時機時，單靠才能是否足夠。"},{"en":"It describes success across all possible time periods.","zh":"它描述跨越所有可能時代的成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"most suitable title","meaning":"最合適的標題","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the most suitable title for the whole passage.","zh":"學生為整篇文章選擇最合適的標題。"},{"en":"The most suitable title is the title that best matches the main idea of a text.","zh":"最合適的標題，是最能配合文本主旨的標題。"},{"en":"A passage about talent, family, environment, and luck needs a title that covers all these ideas.","zh":"一篇關於才能、家庭、環境和運氣的文章，需要涵蓋所有這些想法的標題。"},{"en":"A title that focuses on only one paragraph may not be the most suitable title.","zh":"只聚焦一段的標題未必是最合適的標題。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in main-idea reading questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於主旨閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"whole of the passage","meaning":"整篇文章","examples":[{"en":"The title should fit the whole of the passage.","zh":"標題應適合整篇文章。"},{"en":"The whole of the passage means the entire reading text, not just one part.","zh":"整篇文章，是指整個閱讀文本，而不是其中一部分。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole of the passage before choosing a title.","zh":"學生應在選標題前閱讀整篇文章。"},{"en":"A good title must cover the overall message, not only one example like Mozart.","zh":"好標題必須涵蓋整體訊息，而不只是莫扎特這類例子。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses complete coverage.","zh":"這個短語強調完整涵蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"geniuses in their time","meaning":"時代中的天才","examples":[{"en":"The title “Geniuses in their time” focuses on timing and talent.","zh":"「時代中的天才」這個標題聚焦時機和才能。"},{"en":"Geniuses in their time means highly gifted people whose success is connected to the historical period they lived in.","zh":"時代中的天才，是成功與所處歷史時期相關的高度天賦人物。"},{"en":"Einstein and Gates can be seen as geniuses in their time because their eras created special opportunities.","zh":"愛因斯坦和 Gates 可以被視為時代中的天才，因為他們的時代創造了特殊機會。"},{"en":"This title suggests that genius depends partly on timing, not only ability.","zh":"這個標題暗示天才部分取決於時機，而不只是能力。"},{"en":"This phrase links exceptional talent with historical context.","zh":"這個短語把非凡才能與歷史背景連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"education for the gifted","meaning":"資優教育","examples":[{"en":"One possible title is “Education for the gifted”.","zh":"其中一個可能標題是「資優教育」。"},{"en":"Education for the gifted means teaching and support designed for students with exceptional ability.","zh":"資優教育是為具有非凡能力的學生設計的教學和支援。"},{"en":"A gifted programme may provide harder tasks, creative projects, or specialist coaching.","zh":"資優課程可能提供更難任務、創意專題或專門指導。"},{"en":"Education for the gifted should develop talent without creating unfair pressure.","zh":"資優教育應發展才能，而不造成不公平壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to schooling for highly able learners.","zh":"這個短語指為高能力學習者而設的教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"revising the definition of intelligence","meaning":"修訂智力的定義","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses revising the definition of intelligence.","zh":"篇章討論修訂智力的定義。"},{"en":"Revising the definition of intelligence means changing or updating what intelligence is understood to include.","zh":"修訂智力的定義，是改變或更新對智力所包含內容的理解。"},{"en":"A school may revise its definition of intelligence to include creativity and problem-solving.","zh":"學校可能修訂智力定義，以包括創造力和解難能力。"},{"en":"Revising a definition can change how students are assessed and supported.","zh":"修訂定義可以改變學生如何被評估和支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rethinking what intelligence means.","zh":"這個短語描述重新思考智力的意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"nurturing talent within the family","meaning":"在家庭中培育才能","examples":[{"en":"The passage also discusses nurturing talent within the family.","zh":"篇章也討論在家庭中培育才能。"},{"en":"Nurturing talent within the family means helping ability grow through family support, example, and encouragement.","zh":"在家庭中培育才能，是透過家庭支持、榜樣和鼓勵幫助能力成長。"},{"en":"Parents nurture talent within the family when they notice each child’s interests and provide suitable chances.","zh":"父母注意每個孩子的興趣並提供合適機會時，就是在家庭中培育才能。"},{"en":"Family support can help talent develop, but favouring one child may harm siblings.","zh":"家庭支持可以幫助才能發展，但偏袒一名孩子可能傷害兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"This phrase describes talent development inside family life.","zh":"這個短語描述家庭生活中的才能發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 105 - ‘talented’ or ‘gifted’?.pdf","sourcePage":26}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 106":[{"front":"saving language","meaning":"拯救語言","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the cost and importance of saving language.","zh":"文章討論拯救語言的成本和重要性。"},{"en":"Saving language means protecting a language so that people continue to speak, read, write, and pass it on.","zh":"saving language 指保護一種語言，使人們繼續說、讀、寫並傳承它。"},{"en":"A school can help with saving language by teaching children songs, stories, and daily phrases in their mother tongue.","zh":"學校可以透過教孩子用母語唱歌、說故事和使用日常短語來協助拯救語言。"},{"en":"Saving language becomes urgent when young people stop using it at home or in public.","zh":"當年輕人停止在家中或公共場合使用某語言，拯救語言就變得迫切。"},{"en":"This phrase is about preserving living culture, not just collecting old words in a book.","zh":"這個短語關乎保存活的文化，而不只是把舊詞收集在書中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for the first time","meaning":"首次；第一次","examples":[{"en":"For the first time, linguists have put a price on language.","zh":"語言學家首次為語言定價。"},{"en":"For the first time means something has never happened before this moment.","zh":"for the first time 指某事在此刻以前從未發生過。"},{"en":"For the first time, the quiet student raised her hand and answered in English.","zh":"那名安靜學生第一次舉手並用英文回答。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when an event is new, unusual, or historically important.","zh":"當事件是新的、不尋常的或具歷史意義時，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It highlights a beginning rather than a repeated action.","zh":"它強調開始，而不是重複發生的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"put a price on","meaning":"為……定價","examples":[{"en":"Linguists have put a price on language preservation.","zh":"語言學家已為語言保存定價。"},{"en":"To put a price on something means to estimate how much money it would cost or be worth.","zh":"put a price on something 指估計某事需要多少金錢或值多少錢。"},{"en":"A school may put a price on a new library project before asking for funding.","zh":"學校在申請資金前，可能先為新圖書館項目定價。"},{"en":"Putting a price on language preservation helps governments understand the resources needed.","zh":"為語言保存定價有助政府了解所需資源。"},{"en":"This phrase can feel uncomfortable when the thing being valued is cultural or emotional.","zh":"當被估價的是文化或情感事物時，這個短語可能令人感到不太舒服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"save a language from extinction","meaning":"拯救一種語言免於滅絕","examples":[{"en":"It is expensive to save a language from extinction.","zh":"拯救一種語言免於滅絕成本很高。"},{"en":"To save a language from extinction means to stop it from disappearing completely.","zh":"save a language from extinction 指阻止一種語言完全消失。"},{"en":"A community may save a language from extinction by teaching it to children every weekend.","zh":"社群可以透過每個週末教孩子該語言，拯救一種語言免於滅絕。"},{"en":"A language can move closer to extinction when its last fluent speakers become elderly.","zh":"當最後一批流利使用者變老，一種語言可能更接近滅絕。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active protection before it is too late.","zh":"這個短語描述在太遲之前主動保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"language extinction","meaning":"語言滅絕","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses language extinction on a massive scale.","zh":"文章討論大規模的語言滅絕。"},{"en":"Language extinction is the disappearance of a language when no one uses it anymore.","zh":"language extinction 指當沒有人再使用一種語言時，該語言便消失。"},{"en":"Language extinction may happen when children grow up speaking only a dominant national language.","zh":"當孩子成長時只說主流國家語言，語言滅絕可能發生。"},{"en":"When language extinction occurs, songs, jokes, stories, and local knowledge may disappear too.","zh":"當語言滅絕發生，歌曲、笑話、故事和本地知識也可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase treats a language like a living system that can die if not passed on.","zh":"這個短語把語言視為活的系統；如果沒有傳承，它就會死亡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"more and more people are arguing that","meaning":"越來越多人主張","examples":[{"en":"More and more people are arguing that language loss harms communities.","zh":"越來越多人主張語言流失會傷害社群。"},{"en":"More and more people are arguing that means an increasing number of people are publicly supporting an idea.","zh":"more and more people are arguing that 指越來越多人公開支持某個想法。"},{"en":"More and more people are arguing that schools should protect students’ mental health, not only exam results.","zh":"越來越多人主張學校應保護學生心理健康，而不只是考試成績。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an opinion is becoming more common over time.","zh":"這個短語顯示某種意見隨時間變得更普遍。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing a growing debate or social movement.","zh":"描述日益擴大的辯論或社會運動時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the alternative is","meaning":"另一種選擇是；否則就是","examples":[{"en":"The alternative is the death of communities.","zh":"否則就是社群的消亡。"},{"en":"The alternative is introduces what may happen if the first option is not chosen.","zh":"the alternative is 用來引出如果不選第一個選項，可能會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"We must repair the roof now; the alternative is water damage during the next storm.","zh":"我們現在必須修理屋頂；否則下一場暴風雨時就會出現水浸損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase often makes the second option sound serious or undesirable.","zh":"這個短語常令第二個選項聽起來嚴重或不可取。"},{"en":"It is used to warn people what may happen if they do nothing.","zh":"它用來警告人們如果甚麼都不做會發生甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"death of communities","meaning":"社群的消亡","examples":[{"en":"Language extinction can lead to the death of communities.","zh":"語言滅絕可以導致社群的消亡。"},{"en":"Death of communities means the collapse or disappearance of a group’s shared life, identity, and traditions.","zh":"death of communities 指一個群體共同生活、身份和傳統的崩解或消失。"},{"en":"A village may face the death of its community if all young families move away.","zh":"如果所有年輕家庭都搬走，村落可能面臨社群消亡。"},{"en":"When a language disappears, people may lose the stories and customs that hold the community together.","zh":"當語言消失，人們可能失去維繫社群的故事和習俗。"},{"en":"This phrase is usually figurative, not about every person physically dying.","zh":"這個短語通常是比喻，不是指每個人身體死亡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"nothing unusual about","meaning":"……並不罕見","examples":[{"en":"There is nothing unusual about a single language dying.","zh":"一種語言消亡並不罕見。"},{"en":"Nothing unusual about something means it is normal, expected, or not surprising.","zh":"nothing unusual about something 指某事正常、可預期或不令人驚訝。"},{"en":"There is nothing unusual about students feeling nervous before an oral exam.","zh":"學生在口試前緊張並不罕見。"},{"en":"This phrase reduces surprise by showing that something has happened before.","zh":"這個短語透過指出某事曾經發生，減低驚訝感。"},{"en":"It often prepares the reader for a contrast with something truly unusual.","zh":"它常為後面真正不尋常的事情鋪墊對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a single language dying","meaning":"一種語言消亡","examples":[{"en":"A single language dying is not unusual in human history.","zh":"一種語言消亡在人類歷史中並不罕見。"},{"en":"A single language dying means one language gradually stops being used by any speakers.","zh":"a single language dying 指一種語言逐漸停止被任何使用者使用。"},{"en":"A local dialect may begin dying when families stop using it with children.","zh":"當家庭停止與孩子使用本地方言，該方言可能開始消亡。"},{"en":"One language dying is sad, but mass language loss is much more alarming.","zh":"一種語言消亡令人傷感，但大規模語言流失更令人憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on one language, not the global pattern of language loss.","zh":"這個短語集中於一種語言，而不是全球語言流失模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"come and go","meaning":"興衰更替；來去變遷","examples":[{"en":"Communities have come and gone throughout history.","zh":"社群縱觀歷史一直興衰更替。"},{"en":"To come and go means to appear, exist for a time, and then disappear or change.","zh":"come and go 指出現、存在一段時間，然後消失或改變。"},{"en":"Shops in a busy street may come and go as rents and customers change.","zh":"隨着租金和顧客改變，繁忙街道上的店舖可能不斷更替。"},{"en":"Communities come and go when people migrate, merge, or lose their shared identity.","zh":"當人們遷移、融合或失去共同身份，社群就會興衰變遷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes natural change over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間出現的自然變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"throughout history","meaning":"縱觀歷史","examples":[{"en":"Communities and languages have disappeared throughout history.","zh":"縱觀歷史，社群和語言一直有消失。"},{"en":"Throughout history means during all periods of the past.","zh":"throughout history 指在整個過去的各個時期。"},{"en":"Throughout history, people have moved to new places in search of safety, food, and work.","zh":"縱觀歷史，人們一直為了安全、食物和工作遷往新地方。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a statement broad by connecting it to many times and places.","zh":"這個短語透過連接許多時期和地方，使說法變得廣泛。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing that something is not only a modern issue.","zh":"當要顯示某事不只是現代問題時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what is happening today","meaning":"現今正在發生的事","examples":[{"en":"What is happening today is extraordinary by past standards.","zh":"按過去標準來看，現今正在發生的事非比尋常。"},{"en":"What is happening today means the current situation or present trend.","zh":"what is happening today 指目前情況或現時趨勢。"},{"en":"What is happening today in online learning may change how schools design lessons.","zh":"現今網上學習正在發生的事，可能改變學校設計課堂的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase draws attention to the present moment before explaining why it matters.","zh":"這個短語先把注意力引到當下，再解釋其重要性。"},{"en":"It often contrasts today’s situation with the past.","zh":"它常把今日情況與過去作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be judged by the standards of","meaning":"按……的標準來判斷","examples":[{"en":"Today’s language extinction is extraordinary, judged by the standards of the past.","zh":"按過去的標準來判斷，今日的語言滅絕非比尋常。"},{"en":"To be judged by the standards of something means to be evaluated according to that set of expectations or norms.","zh":"be judged by the standards of something 指按照某套期望或規範來評價。"},{"en":"A student’s handwriting may look poor today but excellent when judged by the standards of a quick classroom note.","zh":"學生字跡今日看似差，但若按快速課堂筆記的標準來判斷，可能已很好。"},{"en":"Standards affect judgement because they decide what counts as normal or unusual.","zh":"標準會影響判斷，因為它決定甚麼算正常或不尋常。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain why the same situation may look different under different criteria.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋同一情況在不同準則下為何看起來不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the standards of the past","meaning":"過去的標準","examples":[{"en":"Today’s rate of language loss is unusual by the standards of the past.","zh":"以過去的標準來看，今日語言流失速度很不尋常。"},{"en":"The standards of the past are the expectations or normal patterns from earlier times.","zh":"standards of the past 指早期時代的期望或正常模式。"},{"en":"By the standards of the past, sending instant messages across the world would seem astonishing.","zh":"以過去的標準來看，即時向世界另一端發訊息會令人驚訝。"},{"en":"Comparing with past standards helps show whether a modern trend is really exceptional.","zh":"與過去標準比較，有助顯示現代趨勢是否真的異常。"},{"en":"This phrase uses history as a measuring point.","zh":"這個短語把歷史用作衡量點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on a massive scale","meaning":"大規模地","examples":[{"en":"Language extinction is now happening on a massive scale.","zh":"語言滅絕現正大規模發生。"},{"en":"On a massive scale means happening in very large numbers or across a very wide area.","zh":"on a massive scale 指以非常大的數量或在非常廣泛的範圍發生。"},{"en":"A city may provide free testing on a massive scale during a public health emergency.","zh":"在公共衛生緊急情況中，城市可能大規模提供免費檢測。"},{"en":"When a problem happens on a massive scale, small local solutions may not be enough.","zh":"當問題大規模發生，小型本地解決方法可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses size, seriousness, and wide impact.","zh":"這個短語強調規模、嚴重性和廣泛影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"according to the best estimates","meaning":"根據最可靠的估計","examples":[{"en":"According to the best estimates, there are about 6,000 languages in the world.","zh":"根據最可靠的估計，世界上大約有六千種語言。"},{"en":"According to the best estimates means based on the most reliable available calculations or expert guesses.","zh":"according to the best estimates 指根據目前最可靠的計算或專家估算。"},{"en":"According to the best estimates, the school needs three more classrooms next year.","zh":"根據最可靠的估計，學校明年需要多三間課室。"},{"en":"Estimates are used when exact counting is difficult or impossible.","zh":"當精確計算困難或不可能時，就會使用估計。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the number is informed but not perfectly exact.","zh":"這個短語表示數字有根據，但並非完全精確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"some 6,000 languages","meaning":"約六千種語言","examples":[{"en":"There are some 6,000 languages in the world.","zh":"世界上約有六千種語言。"},{"en":"Some 6,000 languages means approximately 6,000 languages.","zh":"some 6,000 languages 指大約六千種語言。"},{"en":"A report may say a festival attracted some 6,000 visitors if the exact number is not known.","zh":"如果確切人數未知，報告可能說節日吸引了約六千名訪客。"},{"en":"The word “some” here means “about”, not “a few.”","zh":"這裡的 some 意思是「約」，不是「一些」。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a large approximate number.","zh":"這個短語給出一個大型近似數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"die out","meaning":"消亡；滅絕","examples":[{"en":"About half of the world’s languages may die out this century.","zh":"世界上約一半語言可能在本世紀消亡。"},{"en":"To die out means to disappear completely because no one continues to use or practise it.","zh":"die out 指因沒有人繼續使用或實踐而完全消失。"},{"en":"A family custom may die out if children no longer learn it from older relatives.","zh":"如果孩子不再向年長親人學習，家庭習俗可能消亡。"},{"en":"Languages die out when speakers shift to another language and stop passing the old one on.","zh":"當使用者轉用另一種語言並停止傳承舊語言，語言便會消亡。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe languages, traditions, species, or practices disappearing.","zh":"這個短語可以描述語言、傳統、物種或做法消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in the course of","meaning":"在……期間","examples":[{"en":"Many languages may disappear in the course of the next century.","zh":"許多語言可能在下一個世紀期間消失。"},{"en":"In the course of a period means during that period of time.","zh":"in the course of a period 指在某段時間之內。"},{"en":"A student may improve greatly in the course of one school year.","zh":"學生可能在一個學年期間大幅進步。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a change happens gradually over a period, not at one exact moment.","zh":"當變化在一段時間內逐漸發生，而不是在某一刻發生時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It gives a time frame for a process.","zh":"它為一個過程提供時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the next century","meaning":"下一個世紀","examples":[{"en":"About 3,000 languages may die out in the next century.","zh":"約三千種語言可能在下一個世紀消亡。"},{"en":"The next century means the coming period of one hundred years.","zh":"the next century 指接下來的一百年。"},{"en":"The next century may bring major changes in climate, technology, and education.","zh":"下一個世紀可能帶來氣候、科技和教育上的重大變化。"},{"en":"When writers use this phrase, they are thinking on a long historical scale.","zh":"作者使用這個短語時，是以長期歷史尺度思考。"},{"en":"It suggests that action now may affect many future generations.","zh":"它暗示現在的行動可能影響許多未來世代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on average","meaning":"平均而言","examples":[{"en":"On average, a language dies out every two weeks or so.","zh":"平均而言，大約每兩星期就有一種語言消亡。"},{"en":"On average means when the total pattern is divided into a typical rate or amount.","zh":"on average 指把整體模式換算成典型速度或數量。"},{"en":"On average, students in the class read two books a month.","zh":"平均而言，班中學生每月讀兩本書。"},{"en":"An average does not mean the event happens at exactly the same time every period.","zh":"平均數不代表事件在每個時段都準時發生。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe a general rate.","zh":"這個短語有助描述一般速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"every two weeks or so","meaning":"大約每兩星期","examples":[{"en":"A language is dying out somewhere every two weeks or so.","zh":"世界某處大約每兩星期就有一種語言正在消亡。"},{"en":"Every two weeks or so means approximately once every two weeks.","zh":"every two weeks or so 指大約每兩星期一次。"},{"en":"The school newsletter is sent out every two weeks or so.","zh":"學校通訊大約每兩星期發出一次。"},{"en":"“Or so” shows that the timing is approximate, not exact.","zh":"“or so” 顯示時間是近似，而不是精確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated pattern with a rough interval.","zh":"這個短語描述有大約間隔的重複模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the course of the past two or three decades","meaning":"在過去二三十年間","examples":[{"en":"Linguists have been gathering data in the course of the past two or three decades.","zh":"語言學家在過去二三十年間一直收集資料。"},{"en":"In the course of the past two or three decades means during the last twenty or thirty years.","zh":"in the course of the past two or three decades 指在過去二十或三十年間。"},{"en":"In the course of the past two or three decades, many classrooms have started using computers.","zh":"在過去二三十年間，許多課室開始使用電腦。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a broad recent time frame rather than an exact date.","zh":"這個短語給出一個較廣泛的近代時間範圍，而不是精確日期。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing gradual research, change, or development.","zh":"描述逐步研究、變化或發展時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"linguists all over the world","meaning":"世界各地的語言學家","examples":[{"en":"Linguists all over the world have collected comparative data.","zh":"世界各地的語言學家已收集比較資料。"},{"en":"Linguists all over the world means language experts in many different countries and regions.","zh":"linguists all over the world 指許多不同國家和地區的語言專家。"},{"en":"Linguists all over the world may study how children learn sounds, grammar, and vocabulary.","zh":"世界各地的語言學家可能研究孩子如何學習語音、文法和詞彙。"},{"en":"Global cooperation helps researchers compare languages from many communities.","zh":"全球合作幫助研究者比較來自許多社群的語言。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the work is international, not limited to one country.","zh":"這個短語強調工作具有國際性，而不限於一個國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"gather comparative data","meaning":"收集比較資料","examples":[{"en":"Linguists have been gathering comparative data on endangered languages.","zh":"語言學家一直在收集關於瀕危語言的比較資料。"},{"en":"To gather comparative data means to collect information that allows different cases to be compared.","zh":"gather comparative data 指收集可讓不同個案作比較的資料。"},{"en":"A teacher may gather comparative data by checking exam results from several classes.","zh":"老師可能透過檢查幾個班的考試成績來收集比較資料。"},{"en":"Comparative data helps researchers see which languages are most at risk.","zh":"比較資料幫助研究者看出哪些語言風險最高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collecting evidence for comparison, not just storing random facts.","zh":"這個短語描述為比較而收集證據，而不是隨意儲存資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"comparative data","meaning":"比較資料","examples":[{"en":"Comparative data helps linguists judge whether a language is endangered.","zh":"比較資料幫助語言學家判斷一種語言是否瀕危。"},{"en":"Comparative data is information collected so that different groups, times, or situations can be compared.","zh":"comparative data 指為比較不同群體、時期或情況而收集的資料。"},{"en":"A school uses comparative data when it compares this year’s results with last year’s results.","zh":"學校把今年成績與去年成績比較時，就是使用比較資料。"},{"en":"Without comparative data, it is harder to know whether a problem is unusual or normal.","zh":"沒有比較資料，就較難知道一個問題是不尋常還是正常。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to evidence useful for comparison.","zh":"這個短語指有助比較的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"just a few speakers left","meaning":"只剩下少數使用者","examples":[{"en":"A language with just a few speakers left is likely to disappear.","zh":"只剩下少數使用者的語言很可能消失。"},{"en":"Just a few speakers left means only a very small number of people can still use the language.","zh":"just a few speakers left 指只有極少數人仍能使用該語言。"},{"en":"If only three grandparents in a village still speak a dialect, it has just a few speakers left.","zh":"如果村中只有三位祖父母仍會說某方言，它就只剩下少數使用者。"},{"en":"A language becomes fragile when there are too few speakers to teach children regularly.","zh":"當使用者太少，無法定期教孩子，語言就變得脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a language is close to extinction.","zh":"這個短語顯示一種語言接近滅絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"bother to","meaning":"費心去；特意去","examples":[{"en":"Nobody is bothering to pass the language on to the children.","zh":"沒有人費心把這種語言傳給孩子。"},{"en":"To bother to do something means to make the effort to do it, often when it is inconvenient.","zh":"bother to do something 指花力氣去做某事，尤其在不方便時。"},{"en":"Some students do not bother to check spelling before handing in homework.","zh":"有些學生交功課前不費心檢查拼字。"},{"en":"If adults do not bother to teach a language, children may never learn it.","zh":"如果成人不費心教一種語言，孩子可能永遠學不到它。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound critical because it suggests people are not making enough effort.","zh":"這個短語可以帶批評意味，因為它暗示人們沒有付出足夠努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pass the language on to","meaning":"把語言傳給……","examples":[{"en":"Parents may fail to pass the language on to their children.","zh":"父母可能未能把語言傳給孩子。"},{"en":"To pass the language on to someone means to teach it to the next person or generation.","zh":"pass the language on to someone 指把語言教給下一個人或下一代。"},{"en":"Grandparents can pass the language on to children by telling stories in it every night.","zh":"祖父母可以透過每晚用該語言說故事，把語言傳給孩子。"},{"en":"If a language is not passed on at home or school, it may stop being used.","zh":"如果語言沒有在家中或學校傳承，它可能停止被使用。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on transmission between generations.","zh":"這個短語集中於世代之間的傳承。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"conclude that","meaning":"得出……結論","examples":[{"en":"Linguists may conclude that the language is bound to die out.","zh":"語言學家可能得出結論，認為該語言必定會消亡。"},{"en":"To conclude that means to reach a judgement after considering evidence.","zh":"conclude that 指考慮證據後得出判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher may conclude that students need more practice after reading their essays.","zh":"老師閱讀學生作文後，可能得出學生需要更多練習的結論。"},{"en":"Researchers conclude something when the available facts point strongly in one direction.","zh":"當現有事實明顯指向某方向，研究者就會得出結論。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a reasoned decision, not a random guess.","zh":"這個短語引出有根據的判斷，而不是隨機猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be bound to","meaning":"必定會；注定會","examples":[{"en":"A language with too few speakers is bound to die out soon.","zh":"使用者太少的語言必定很快消亡。"},{"en":"To be bound to do something means to be almost certain to do it or have it happen.","zh":"be bound to do something 指幾乎肯定會做某事或某事會發生。"},{"en":"A student who never sleeps before exams is bound to feel tired.","zh":"考試前從不睡覺的學生必定會感到疲倦。"},{"en":"If no children learn a language, it is bound to weaken over time.","zh":"如果沒有孩子學習一種語言，它必定會隨時間變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses strong likelihood or inevitability.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈可能性或不可避免性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"draw the same conclusion","meaning":"得出同樣結論","examples":[{"en":"Researchers draw the same conclusion if a language has fewer than 100 speakers.","zh":"如果一種語言少於一百名使用者，研究者會得出同樣結論。"},{"en":"To draw the same conclusion means to reach the same judgement from similar evidence.","zh":"draw the same conclusion 指從相似證據得出相同判斷。"},{"en":"Two teachers may draw the same conclusion if both see that students struggle with articles.","zh":"如果兩名老師都看見學生在冠詞上有困難，他們可能得出同樣結論。"},{"en":"When different cases show the same pattern, researchers often reach the same result.","zh":"當不同個案顯示相同模式，研究者常會得出相同結果。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses agreement in reasoning.","zh":"這個短語強調推理上的一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fewer than 100 speakers","meaning":"少於一百名使用者","examples":[{"en":"A language with fewer than 100 speakers is unlikely to last long.","zh":"少於一百名使用者的語言不大可能長久維持。"},{"en":"Fewer than 100 speakers means less than one hundred people can still use the language.","zh":"fewer than 100 speakers 指少於一百人仍能使用該語言。"},{"en":"If a dialect has fewer than 100 speakers, every fluent speaker becomes very important.","zh":"如果一種方言少於一百名使用者，每位流利使用者都變得非常重要。"},{"en":"Small speaker numbers make teaching, daily use, and community support harder.","zh":"使用者人數少，會令教學、日常使用和社群支持更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a warning sign of severe language endangerment.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴重語言瀕危的警號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not likely to last","meaning":"不大可能持續","examples":[{"en":"A language with too few speakers is not likely to last very long.","zh":"使用者太少的語言不大可能持續很久。"},{"en":"Not likely to last means unlikely to continue or survive for much more time.","zh":"not likely to last 指不大可能繼續或存活很長時間。"},{"en":"A school club with only one active member is not likely to last.","zh":"只有一名活躍成員的學會不大可能持續。"},{"en":"A language needs enough speakers and learners to continue across generations.","zh":"一種語言需要足夠使用者和學習者，才能跨代延續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weak chances of survival.","zh":"這個短語描述存續機會薄弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a 1999 survey","meaning":"一項1999年的調查","examples":[{"en":"A 1999 survey showed how unevenly languages are distributed.","zh":"一項1999年的調查顯示語言分布多麼不均。"},{"en":"A 1999 survey is a study or investigation carried out in the year 1999.","zh":"a 1999 survey 指在1999年進行的一項研究或調查。"},{"en":"A school may use a 1999 survey as historical data to compare with current results.","zh":"學校可能使用一項1999年的調查作歷史數據，與現時結果比較。"},{"en":"Surveys help researchers collect information from many cases in a structured way.","zh":"調查幫助研究者以有結構方式從許多個案收集資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both the type of evidence and the year it came from.","zh":"這個短語同時指出證據類型和年份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be spoken by","meaning":"被……使用","examples":[{"en":"Most of the world’s languages are spoken by a small proportion of people.","zh":"世界上大部分語言只被少數人使用。"},{"en":"To be spoken by a group means that group uses the language for communication.","zh":"be spoken by a group 指某群體使用該語言溝通。"},{"en":"Cantonese is spoken by many people in Hong Kong.","zh":"粵語被許多香港人使用。"},{"en":"A language may be spoken by only a few elders if younger people shift to another language.","zh":"如果年輕人轉用另一種語言，一種語言可能只被少數長者使用。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the people who use a language.","zh":"這個短語指出使用某語言的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"just four per cent of the people","meaning":"僅百分之四的人口","examples":[{"en":"Ninety-seven per cent of languages are spoken by just four per cent of people.","zh":"百分之九十七的語言由僅百分之四的人口使用。"},{"en":"Just four per cent of the people means only a very small share of the population.","zh":"just four per cent of the people 指只有非常小比例的人口。"},{"en":"If just four per cent of students join a club, the club may struggle to survive.","zh":"如果只有百分之四的學生加入學會，該學會可能難以維持。"},{"en":"A small percentage of speakers can still represent a huge number of languages.","zh":"一小比例使用者仍可能代表大量語言。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights imbalance between language numbers and speaker numbers.","zh":"這個短語突出語言數量與使用者數量之間的不平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"too late to do anything","meaning":"已太遲，無法做任何事","examples":[{"en":"It is too late to do anything to help many languages.","zh":"要幫助許多語言已太遲，無法做任何事。"},{"en":"Too late to do anything means the chance to act effectively has already passed.","zh":"too late to do anything 指有效行動的機會已經過去。"},{"en":"If a deadline passed last month, it may be too late to do anything about the application.","zh":"如果截止日期上月已過，申請可能已太遲而無法補救。"},{"en":"For some languages, the remaining speakers may be too few for full revival.","zh":"對某些語言來說，剩餘使用者可能太少，難以全面復興。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses regret and urgency.","zh":"這個短語表達遺憾和迫切感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"too few or too old","meaning":"人數太少或年紀太大","examples":[{"en":"Some languages have speakers who are too few or too old.","zh":"有些語言的使用者人數太少或年紀太大。"},{"en":"Too few or too old means there are not enough speakers, or the remaining speakers are mostly elderly.","zh":"too few or too old 指使用者不足，或剩餘使用者大多是長者。"},{"en":"A village festival may be at risk if its performers are too few or too old.","zh":"如果村莊節日的表演者人數太少或年紀太大，節日可能有風險。"},{"en":"A language becomes harder to revive when few young people can learn directly from fluent speakers.","zh":"當很少年輕人能直接向流利使用者學習，語言復興會更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why some rescue efforts may be difficult.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何某些拯救工作可能很困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"just trying to survive","meaning":"只是忙於求生","examples":[{"en":"Some communities are too busy just trying to survive to protect their language.","zh":"有些社群只是忙於求生，無暇保護自己的語言。"},{"en":"Just trying to survive means focusing only on basic needs such as food, safety, income, or shelter.","zh":"just trying to survive 指只集中於食物、安全、收入或住所等基本需要。"},{"en":"A family in crisis may be just trying to survive and unable to think about long-term plans.","zh":"陷入危機的家庭可能只是忙於求生，無法思考長遠計劃。"},{"en":"When daily life is insecure, cultural work may feel impossible even if people value it.","zh":"當日常生活不穩，文化工作即使重要，也可能令人覺得難以實行。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that survival pressure can push other priorities aside.","zh":"這個短語顯示生存壓力可以把其他優先事項擠到一旁。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"care about their language","meaning":"關心自己的語言","examples":[{"en":"Some communities have little time to care about their language.","zh":"有些社群幾乎沒有時間關心自己的語言。"},{"en":"To care about their language means to value it and want it to survive.","zh":"care about their language 指重視自己的語言並希望它存續。"},{"en":"Parents show they care about their language when they speak it with children at home.","zh":"父母在家中與孩子說自己的語言，就是表現出關心自己的語言。"},{"en":"A community may stop caring publicly about a language if poverty and danger dominate daily life.","zh":"如果貧窮和危險主導日常生活，社群可能停止公開關心該語言。"},{"en":"This phrase connects emotional value with practical action.","zh":"這個短語把情感價值與實際行動連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not in such a serious position","meaning":"情況並非如此嚴重","examples":[{"en":"Many endangered languages are not in such a serious position.","zh":"許多瀕危語言的情況並非如此嚴重。"},{"en":"Not in such a serious position means the situation is worrying but not yet hopeless.","zh":"not in such a serious position 指情況令人擔心，但尚未絕望。"},{"en":"A student who has failed one quiz is not in such a serious position if there is time to improve.","zh":"如果仍有時間改善，只測驗不合格一次的學生情況並非如此嚴重。"},{"en":"Some languages still have enough speakers, young learners, or community support to be helped.","zh":"有些語言仍有足夠使用者、年輕學習者或社群支持，因此仍可被幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase offers a more hopeful contrast.","zh":"這個短語提供較有希望的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"seriously endangered","meaning":"嚴重瀕危","examples":[{"en":"Some languages are seriously endangered but can still be helped.","zh":"有些語言嚴重瀕危，但仍可被幫助。"},{"en":"Seriously endangered means at high risk of disappearing but not necessarily beyond rescue.","zh":"seriously endangered 指消失風險很高，但不一定已無法拯救。"},{"en":"A seriously endangered tradition may survive if schools and families practise it again.","zh":"如果學校和家庭重新實踐，一項嚴重瀕危的傳統可能存續。"},{"en":"A language becomes seriously endangered when few children learn it naturally.","zh":"當很少孩子自然學習一種語言，該語言便變得嚴重瀕危。"},{"en":"This phrase signals danger while leaving room for action.","zh":"這個短語顯示危險，同時仍留下行動空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"give new life to","meaning":"為……注入新生命","examples":[{"en":"Revitalisation can give new life to an endangered language.","zh":"復興可以為瀕危語言注入新生命。"},{"en":"To give new life to something means to make it active, useful, or energetic again.","zh":"give new life to something 指使某事再次活躍、有用或有活力。"},{"en":"A community festival can give new life to an old market street.","zh":"社區節日可以為一條舊市場街注入新生命。"},{"en":"Language classes, songs, and public signs can give new life to a language people had stopped using.","zh":"語言課程、歌曲和公共標示可以為一種人們曾停止使用的語言注入新生命。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests renewal rather than simple preservation.","zh":"這個短語暗示更新，而不只是保存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"revitalisation","meaning":"復興；重振","examples":[{"en":"Revitalisation can help a language recover.","zh":"復興可以幫助一種語言恢復。"},{"en":"Revitalisation is the process of making something active, strong, or widely used again.","zh":"revitalisation 指令某事再次活躍、強大或被廣泛使用的過程。"},{"en":"A town may plan revitalisation by reopening shops and improving public spaces.","zh":"城鎮可能透過重開商店和改善公共空間來規劃復興。"},{"en":"Language revitalisation needs speakers, teaching materials, community support, and time.","zh":"語言復興需要使用者、教材、社群支持和時間。"},{"en":"This word describes bringing life back to something weakened.","zh":"這個字描述把生命重新帶回已變弱的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"once a community realises that","meaning":"一旦一個社群意識到","examples":[{"en":"Once a community realises that its language is in danger, it can act.","zh":"一旦一個社群意識到自己的語言處於危險之中，就可以採取行動。"},{"en":"Once a community realises that something is true means after the community becomes aware of it.","zh":"once a community realises that something is true 指當社群意識到某事屬實之後。"},{"en":"Once a school realises that students are stressed, it can reduce unnecessary homework.","zh":"一旦學校意識到學生有壓力，就可以減少不必要功課。"},{"en":"Awareness is often the first step before planning and action.","zh":"意識到問題通常是規劃和行動前的第一步。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the moment understanding leads to possible change.","zh":"這個短語顯示理解帶來可能改變的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be in danger","meaning":"處於危險之中","examples":[{"en":"A community may realise that its language is in danger.","zh":"一個社群可能意識到自己的語言處於危險之中。"},{"en":"To be in danger means to face a real risk of harm, loss, or disappearance.","zh":"be in danger 指面對真正的傷害、失去或消失風險。"},{"en":"A child is in danger if they cross a busy road without looking.","zh":"如果孩子過繁忙馬路時不看路，就處於危險之中。"},{"en":"A language is in danger when fewer children learn it and public use declines.","zh":"當學習某語言的孩子變少，公共使用也下降，該語言就處於危險之中。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that action may be needed soon.","zh":"這個短語警告可能需要盡快行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"introduce measures","meaning":"推出措施","examples":[{"en":"A community can introduce measures to revitalise its language.","zh":"社群可以推出措施來重振自己的語言。"},{"en":"To introduce measures means to start using practical actions or policies to solve a problem.","zh":"introduce measures 指開始採用實際行動或政策來解決問題。"},{"en":"A school may introduce measures such as quiet study rooms and counselling to reduce stress.","zh":"學校可能推出安靜自修室和輔導等措施來減低壓力。"},{"en":"Language measures may include classes, signs, media programmes, and teacher training.","zh":"語言措施可包括課程、標示、媒體節目和教師培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on concrete action, not just concern.","zh":"這個短語集中於具體行動，而不只是關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"genuinely revitalise","meaning":"真正重振","examples":[{"en":"Some measures can genuinely revitalise an endangered language.","zh":"有些措施可以真正重振一種瀕危語言。"},{"en":"To genuinely revitalise something means to truly make it stronger and more active again.","zh":"genuinely revitalise something 指真正令某事再次更強和更活躍。"},{"en":"A reading club can genuinely revitalise a school library if students start borrowing books regularly.","zh":"如果學生開始定期借書，閱讀會可以真正重振學校圖書館。"},{"en":"A language is genuinely revitalised when people use it in real life, not only in ceremonies.","zh":"當人們在真實生活中使用語言，而不只在儀式中使用，它才算真正被重振。"},{"en":"This phrase separates real recovery from symbolic support.","zh":"這個短語把真正恢復與象徵性支持分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the community itself","meaning":"社群本身","examples":[{"en":"The community itself must want to save its language.","zh":"社群本身必須想拯救自己的語言。"},{"en":"The community itself means the people directly connected to the language or issue, not only outside experts.","zh":"community itself 指與語言或議題直接相關的人，而不只是外來專家。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood itself must support a clean-up project, or the rubbish will return quickly.","zh":"社區本身必須支持清潔計劃，否則垃圾很快會再次出現。"},{"en":"Language revival is stronger when local people choose it for themselves.","zh":"當本地人自己選擇語言復興，復興會更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses local ownership and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語強調本地擁有感和責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be a part of","meaning":"是……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"The language belongs to the culture of which it is a part.","zh":"語言屬於它本身作為一部分的文化。"},{"en":"To be a part of something means to belong within a larger whole.","zh":"be a part of something 指屬於一個更大整體之內。"},{"en":"School songs are a part of school culture because students sing them at important events.","zh":"校歌是學校文化的一部分，因為學生在重要活動中唱它。"},{"en":"A language is part of culture because it carries stories, jokes, names, and values.","zh":"語言是文化的一部分，因為它承載故事、笑話、名字和價值觀。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one thing is connected to a wider system.","zh":"這個短語顯示一件事與更廣泛制度相連。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have respect for","meaning":"尊重……","examples":[{"en":"The wider culture must have respect for minority languages.","zh":"較大的文化必須尊重少數語言。"},{"en":"To have respect for something means to value it and treat it seriously.","zh":"have respect for something 指重視某物並認真對待它。"},{"en":"Students show respect for classmates’ names by pronouncing them carefully.","zh":"學生仔細讀同學名字，就是尊重同學名字。"},{"en":"A language is more likely to survive when outsiders respect it rather than mock it.","zh":"當外人尊重一種語言而不是嘲笑它，它更有可能存續。"},{"en":"This phrase combines attitude with behaviour.","zh":"這個短語結合態度與行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"minority languages","meaning":"少數族裔語言；少數語言","examples":[{"en":"Minority languages need respect and support.","zh":"少數語言需要尊重和支持。"},{"en":"Minority languages are languages spoken by smaller groups within a larger society.","zh":"minority languages 指在較大社會中由較小群體使用的語言。"},{"en":"A school may support minority languages by allowing students to use them in cultural activities.","zh":"學校可以透過容許學生在文化活動中使用少數語言來支持它們。"},{"en":"Minority languages can weaken when public life, work, and education use only a dominant language.","zh":"當公共生活、工作和教育只使用主流語言，少數語言可能變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to speaker numbers and social position, not language quality.","zh":"這個短語指使用者數量和社會位置，而不是語言質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"funding to support","meaning":"支持……的資金","examples":[{"en":"There needs to be funding to support courses, materials and teachers.","zh":"需要有資金支持課程、教材及教師。"},{"en":"Funding to support something is money provided to help it operate or develop.","zh":"funding to support something 指用來幫助某事運作或發展的金錢。"},{"en":"A community centre needs funding to support free homework classes.","zh":"社區中心需要資金支持免費功課班。"},{"en":"Without funding, language programmes may lack books, classrooms, and trained staff.","zh":"沒有資金，語言計劃可能缺乏書本、課室和受訓人員。"},{"en":"This phrase connects financial resources with practical help.","zh":"這個短語把財政資源與實際幫助連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"courses, materials and teachers","meaning":"課程、教材及教師","examples":[{"en":"Revitalisation requires courses, materials and teachers.","zh":"復興需要課程、教材及教師。"},{"en":"Courses, materials and teachers are the organised lessons, learning resources, and people needed for education.","zh":"courses, materials and teachers 指教育所需的有組織課堂、學習資源和人員。"},{"en":"A new English programme cannot work without courses, materials and teachers.","zh":"新英文課程沒有課程、教材及教師就無法運作。"},{"en":"Language learning becomes more sustainable when learners have lessons, books, recordings, and trained instructors.","zh":"當學習者有課堂、書本、錄音和受訓教師，語言學習會更可持續。"},{"en":"This phrase lists the basic educational support needed for revival.","zh":"這個短語列出復興所需的基本教育支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get on with","meaning":"開始／繼續處理","examples":[{"en":"Linguists need to get on with the basic task of documentation.","zh":"語言學家需要開始／繼續處理記錄工作的基本任務。"},{"en":"To get on with something means to start or continue doing it without delay.","zh":"get on with something 指不再拖延，開始或繼續做某事。"},{"en":"Students should get on with homework instead of waiting until midnight.","zh":"學生應開始做功課，而不是等到午夜。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when action is needed and further delay is unhelpful.","zh":"當需要行動而繼續拖延沒有幫助時，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound practical, direct, and urgent.","zh":"這個短語聽起來實際、直接且有迫切感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the basic task of","meaning":"……的基本任務","examples":[{"en":"The basic task of linguists is to put the language down on paper.","zh":"語言學家的基本任務是把語言記錄成文字。"},{"en":"The basic task of someone is their most fundamental duty or job.","zh":"basic task of someone 指某人最根本的職責或工作。"},{"en":"The basic task of a teacher is to help students understand and improve.","zh":"老師的基本任務是幫助學生理解和進步。"},{"en":"Basic tasks must be done before more advanced work can succeed.","zh":"基本任務必須先完成，更進階工作才可能成功。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the first essential responsibility.","zh":"這個短語指出第一項必要責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put the language down on paper","meaning":"把語言記錄成文字","examples":[{"en":"Linguists help by putting the language down on paper.","zh":"語言學家透過把語言記錄成文字來提供幫助。"},{"en":"To put the language down on paper means to record its words, grammar, sounds, and rules in written form.","zh":"put the language down on paper 指把語言的詞語、文法、語音和規則以書面形式記錄下來。"},{"en":"A grandparent can help put a dialect down on paper by listing old sayings and their meanings.","zh":"祖父母可以透過列出舊俗語及其意思，幫助把方言記錄成文字。"},{"en":"Writing a language down makes it easier to teach, study, and preserve.","zh":"把語言寫下來會令教學、研究和保存更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase turns spoken knowledge into a lasting record.","zh":"這個短語把口頭知識轉化為持久記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the bottom line","meaning":"最基本的一點；關鍵","examples":[{"en":"The bottom line is that the language must be documented.","zh":"最基本的一點是，該語言必須被記錄下來。"},{"en":"The bottom line means the most important point after everything else has been considered.","zh":"bottom line 指考慮所有事情後最重要的一點。"},{"en":"The bottom line is that students need enough sleep before an exam.","zh":"最基本的一點是，學生考試前需要足夠睡眠。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to cut through details and state the key message.","zh":"人們使用這個短語來越過細節，說出核心訊息。"},{"en":"It often introduces a practical conclusion.","zh":"它常引出實際結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get the language documented","meaning":"把語言記錄下來","examples":[{"en":"Getting the language documented is essential for survival.","zh":"把語言記錄下來對存續至關重要。"},{"en":"To get the language documented means to have it recorded, analysed, and written down properly.","zh":"get the language documented 指讓語言被妥善記錄、分析和寫下來。"},{"en":"A community may get the language documented by working with elders and linguists.","zh":"社群可以透過與長者和語言學家合作，把語言記錄下來。"},{"en":"Documentation creates materials that future teachers and learners can use.","zh":"記錄工作會建立未來教師和學習者可用的教材。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on turning speech into a usable record.","zh":"這個短語集中於把口語轉化為可用記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"recorded, analysed and written down","meaning":"被記錄、分析及寫下來","examples":[{"en":"The language needs to be recorded, analysed and written down.","zh":"這種語言需要被記錄、分析及寫下來。"},{"en":"Recorded, analysed and written down means the language is collected, studied carefully, and put into written form.","zh":"recorded, analysed and written down 指語言被收集、仔細研究並轉成書面形式。"},{"en":"A researcher may record conversations, analyse grammar patterns, and write down common expressions.","zh":"研究者可能錄下對話、分析文法模式，並寫下常用表達。"},{"en":"These steps help turn a spoken language into teachable materials.","zh":"這些步驟有助把口頭語言變成可教教材。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main stages of language documentation.","zh":"這個短語描述語言記錄工作的主要階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"read and write","meaning":"讀寫","examples":[{"en":"People must be able to read and write their language.","zh":"人們必須能夠讀寫自己的語言。"},{"en":"To read and write a language means to understand its written form and produce it in writing.","zh":"read and write a language 指理解其書面形式並能用文字寫出。"},{"en":"Children read and write more confidently when they have books in their home language.","zh":"當孩子有母語書本，他們讀寫會更有信心。"},{"en":"Literacy helps a language appear in schools, messages, signs, and online spaces.","zh":"讀寫能力幫助語言出現在學校、訊息、標示和網上空間。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to written language skills, not only speaking.","zh":"這個短語指書面語能力，而不只是說話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have a future","meaning":"有未來","examples":[{"en":"A language needs literacy if it is to have a future.","zh":"一種語言如果要有未來，就需要讀寫能力。"},{"en":"To have a future means to be likely to continue, grow, or remain useful later.","zh":"have a future 指將來有可能繼續、成長或保持有用。"},{"en":"A small business has a future if it can attract young customers and control costs.","zh":"如果小企業能吸引年輕顧客並控制成本，它就有未來。"},{"en":"A language has a future when children learn it and adults use it in real situations.","zh":"當孩子學習語言，成人也在真實情境中使用它，該語言就有未來。"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether something can survive beyond the present.","zh":"這個短語問某事是否能超越現在而存續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"increasingly computer-literate civilisation","meaning":"電腦讀寫能力日益普及的文明","examples":[{"en":"Languages need written forms in an increasingly computer-literate civilisation.","zh":"在電腦讀寫能力日益普及的文明中，語言需要書面形式。"},{"en":"An increasingly computer-literate civilisation is a society where more and more people use computers and digital text confidently.","zh":"increasingly computer-literate civilisation 指越來越多人能自信使用電腦和數碼文字的社會。"},{"en":"Schools become more computer-literate when students submit homework online and use digital libraries.","zh":"當學生網上交功課並使用數碼圖書館，學校就變得更具電腦讀寫能力。"},{"en":"Languages without writing systems may struggle to appear in websites, apps, and online education.","zh":"沒有書寫系統的語言可能難以出現在網站、應用程式和網上教育中。"},{"en":"This phrase connects language survival with modern digital life.","zh":"這個短語把語言存續與現代數碼生活連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"just like that","meaning":"就這樣；輕易地","examples":[{"en":"Saving thousands of languages cannot happen just like that.","zh":"拯救數千種語言不可能就這樣發生。"},{"en":"Just like that means easily, suddenly, or without serious effort.","zh":"just like that 指輕易、突然或不需認真努力。"},{"en":"A student cannot become fluent in English just like that after watching one video.","zh":"學生不可能只看一段影片就這樣變得英文流利。"},{"en":"Big changes need planning, time, and resources, not instant hope.","zh":"重大改變需要計劃、時間和資源，而不是即時希望。"},{"en":"This phrase often reminds people that a difficult task is not automatic.","zh":"這個短語常提醒人們困難任務不會自動完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the will and funding","meaning":"意願和資金","examples":[{"en":"Languages can be saved if the will and funding are available.","zh":"如果有意願和資金，語言可以被拯救。"},{"en":"The will and funding means both the determination to act and the money needed to act.","zh":"will and funding 指行動決心以及行動所需金錢。"},{"en":"A community project can succeed when the will and funding are both present.","zh":"當意願和資金同時存在，社區項目可以成功。"},{"en":"Good intentions alone are not enough if there is no money for teachers, books, and programmes.","zh":"如果沒有錢聘請教師、製作書本和開設計劃，光有好意並不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase combines motivation with practical resources.","zh":"這個短語結合動機與實際資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be available","meaning":"可得到；可用","examples":[{"en":"Revitalisation is possible if funding is available.","zh":"如果資金可得到，復興是可能的。"},{"en":"To be available means to be ready, obtainable, or able to be used.","zh":"be available 指已準備好、可取得或可使用。"},{"en":"Extra classrooms are available after lunch, so clubs can meet there.","zh":"午飯後有額外課室可用，所以學會可以在那裡開會。"},{"en":"If funding is available, communities can hire teachers and create learning materials.","zh":"如果資金可用，社群可以聘請教師和製作學習教材。"},{"en":"This phrase describes whether a resource can actually be used.","zh":"這個短語描述資源是否真的能被使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get linguists into the field","meaning":"讓語言學家到實地工作","examples":[{"en":"Saving languages requires getting linguists into the field.","zh":"拯救語言需要讓語言學家到實地工作。"},{"en":"To get linguists into the field means to send language experts to work directly with communities in real locations.","zh":"get linguists into the field 指派語言專家到真實地點直接與社群合作。"},{"en":"A university may get researchers into the field to record how a local dialect is spoken at home.","zh":"大學可能讓研究者到實地記錄本地方言在家中如何被使用。"},{"en":"Fieldwork lets linguists hear real speech, not only study books in an office.","zh":"實地工作讓語言學家聽到真實說話，而不只是坐在辦公室研究書本。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses direct contact with speakers.","zh":"這個短語強調與使用者直接接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in the field","meaning":"在實地；在現場","examples":[{"en":"Linguists need to work in the field with communities.","zh":"語言學家需要在實地與社群合作。"},{"en":"In the field means in the real place where the subject is being studied, not only in an office or classroom.","zh":"in the field 指在研究對象所在的真實地方，而不只是在辦公室或課室。"},{"en":"Biology students learn more about plants when they work in the field rather than only reading diagrams.","zh":"生物學生在實地工作時，會比只讀圖表更了解植物。"},{"en":"Fieldwork can reveal details that formal reports miss.","zh":"實地工作可以揭示正式報告忽略的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical, on-site research.","zh":"這個短語描述實際的現場研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"train local analysts","meaning":"培訓本地分析員","examples":[{"en":"Revitalisation involves training local analysts.","zh":"復興涉及培訓本地分析員。"},{"en":"To train local analysts means to teach community members how to study, record, and support their language.","zh":"train local analysts 指教社群成員如何研究、記錄和支援自己的語言。"},{"en":"A village project may train local analysts to interview elders and organise recordings.","zh":"村落項目可能培訓本地分析員訪問長者並整理錄音。"},{"en":"Local analysts help because they understand the culture, people, and daily language use.","zh":"本地分析員有幫助，因為他們理解文化、人群和日常語言使用。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that communities should build their own expertise.","zh":"這個短語顯示社群應建立自己的專業能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"local analysts","meaning":"本地分析員","examples":[{"en":"Local analysts can help document and support endangered languages.","zh":"本地分析員可以幫助記錄和支援瀕危語言。"},{"en":"Local analysts are trained people from the community who help study and record local language use.","zh":"local analysts 指來自社群並受訓協助研究和記錄本地語言使用的人。"},{"en":"Local analysts may collect stories, word lists, songs, and conversations from older speakers.","zh":"本地分析員可能向年長使用者收集故事、詞表、歌曲和對話。"},{"en":"They make language projects more sustainable because the work does not depend only on outside experts.","zh":"他們令語言項目更可持續，因為工作不只依賴外來專家。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to community-based language workers.","zh":"這個短語指以社群為基礎的語言工作者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"support the community with","meaning":"以……支援社群","examples":[{"en":"Experts support the community with language resources and teachers.","zh":"專家以語言資源和教師支援社群。"},{"en":"To support the community with something means to help local people by providing that resource.","zh":"support the community with something 指透過提供某資源來幫助本地人。"},{"en":"A hospital can support the community with free health talks and basic check-ups.","zh":"醫院可以透過免費健康講座和基本檢查支援社群。"},{"en":"Language experts support communities by giving tools they can continue using themselves.","zh":"語言專家透過提供社群能繼續自行使用的工具來支援他們。"},{"en":"This phrase connects outside help with local needs.","zh":"這個短語把外來幫助與本地需要連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"language resources","meaning":"語言資源","examples":[{"en":"Communities need language resources to revive a language.","zh":"社群需要語言資源來復興一種語言。"},{"en":"Language resources are materials and tools that help people learn, teach, record, or use a language.","zh":"language resources 指幫助人們學習、教導、記錄或使用語言的材料和工具。"},{"en":"Language resources may include dictionaries, recordings, storybooks, apps, and classroom worksheets.","zh":"語言資源可包括字典、錄音、故事書、應用程式和課堂工作紙。"},{"en":"Without resources, teachers may want to teach a language but have nothing to use.","zh":"沒有資源，教師即使想教一種語言，也可能沒有東西可用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical support for language learning and use.","zh":"這個短語指支援語言學習和使用的實際材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"compile grammars and dictionaries","meaning":"編寫語法書和字典","examples":[{"en":"Linguists may compile grammars and dictionaries for endangered languages.","zh":"語言學家可能為瀕危語言編寫語法書和字典。"},{"en":"To compile grammars and dictionaries means to collect and organise the rules and words of a language into reference books.","zh":"compile grammars and dictionaries 指把一種語言的規則和詞語收集並整理成參考書。"},{"en":"A local team may compile a small dictionary by asking elders for words and example sentences.","zh":"本地團隊可以透過向長者詢問詞語和例句來編寫小型字典。"},{"en":"Grammars and dictionaries help teachers create lessons and learners check correct usage.","zh":"語法書和字典幫助教師建立課程，也幫助學習者查核正確用法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes building core reference tools for a language.","zh":"這個短語描述為語言建立核心參考工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"grammars and dictionaries","meaning":"語法書和字典","examples":[{"en":"Grammars and dictionaries are important tools for language revitalisation.","zh":"語法書和字典是語言復興的重要工具。"},{"en":"Grammars and dictionaries record how a language works and what its words mean.","zh":"grammars and dictionaries 記錄語言如何運作以及詞語意思。"},{"en":"Students use dictionaries to check meanings and grammars to understand sentence patterns.","zh":"學生使用字典查意思，使用語法書理解句式模式。"},{"en":"For endangered languages, these books can preserve knowledge after fluent speakers pass away.","zh":"對瀕危語言而言，這些書可在流利使用者離世後保存知識。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to reference materials that support learning and teaching.","zh":"這個短語指支援學習和教學的參考材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"materials for use in schools","meaning":"供學校使用的教材","examples":[{"en":"Communities need materials for use in schools.","zh":"社群需要供學校使用的教材。"},{"en":"Materials for use in schools are teaching resources designed for classroom learning.","zh":"materials for use in schools 指為課堂學習而設計的教學資源。"},{"en":"A language programme may create storybooks, posters, songs, and exercises for use in schools.","zh":"語言計劃可能製作故事書、海報、歌曲和練習，供學校使用。"},{"en":"School materials help children learn a language regularly rather than only hearing it at ceremonies.","zh":"學校教材幫助孩子定期學習語言，而不只是在儀式中聽到它。"},{"en":"This phrase connects language revival with formal education.","zh":"這個短語把語言復興與正規教育連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"it takes time","meaning":"需要時間","examples":[{"en":"It takes time to revitalise an endangered language.","zh":"重振一種瀕危語言需要時間。"},{"en":"It takes time means the process cannot be completed quickly.","zh":"it takes time 指某過程不能很快完成。"},{"en":"It takes time for students to become confident speakers of a new language.","zh":"學生成為有信心的新語言使用者需要時間。"},{"en":"Language revival requires years of teaching, practice, community use, and patience.","zh":"語言復興需要多年教學、練習、社群使用和耐性。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds people not to expect instant results.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們不要期待即時成果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"conditions vary","meaning":"情況各有不同","examples":[{"en":"Conditions vary greatly from one language community to another.","zh":"不同語言社群之間的情況差異很大。"},{"en":"Conditions vary means situations are different in different places or cases.","zh":"conditions vary 指不同地方或個案的情況不一樣。"},{"en":"Study conditions vary because some students have quiet rooms while others share crowded homes.","zh":"學習情況各有不同，因為有些學生有安靜房間，另一些則住在擠迫家庭中。"},{"en":"Language revival costs vary because communities have different numbers of speakers, teachers, and materials.","zh":"語言復興成本各有不同，因為社群有不同數量的使用者、教師和教材。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against using one answer for every situation.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們不應用同一答案套用所有情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"difficult to generalise","meaning":"難以一概而論","examples":[{"en":"It is difficult to generalise about the cost of language revitalisation.","zh":"語言復興的成本難以一概而論。"},{"en":"Difficult to generalise means hard to make one statement that is true for all cases.","zh":"difficult to generalise 指難以作出一個適用於所有個案的說法。"},{"en":"It is difficult to generalise about students because each learner has different habits and needs.","zh":"學生情況難以一概而論，因為每個學習者都有不同習慣和需要。"},{"en":"When conditions vary widely, broad claims may become misleading.","zh":"當情況差異很大，籠統說法可能令人誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages careful, case-by-case thinking.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵逐個個案仔細思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cannot be far from the truth","meaning":"應該與事實相差不遠","examples":[{"en":"The estimated cost cannot be far from the truth.","zh":"估計成本應該與事實相差不遠。"},{"en":"Cannot be far from the truth means the estimate is probably close to reality.","zh":"cannot be far from the truth 指估計很可能接近現實。"},{"en":"If several teachers give similar marks, their estimate cannot be far from the truth.","zh":"如果幾名老師給出相似分數，他們的估計應該與事實相差不遠。"},{"en":"This phrase accepts that a number may not be exact but is still reasonable.","zh":"這個短語承認數字未必精確，但仍合理。"},{"en":"It is useful when defending an informed approximation.","zh":"當要支持有根據的近似估計時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"devote effort over","meaning":"在……期間投入努力","examples":[{"en":"If we devoted enough effort over three years, many languages could be helped.","zh":"如果我們在三年間投入足夠努力，許多語言都能得到幫助。"},{"en":"To devote effort over a period means to spend serious energy and work during that time.","zh":"devote effort over a period 指在某段時間內投入認真精力和工作。"},{"en":"A student who devotes effort over six months can make real progress in writing.","zh":"在六個月內持續投入努力的學生，可以在寫作上取得真正進步。"},{"en":"Long-term effort matters because difficult goals rarely improve after one short attempt.","zh":"長期努力很重要，因為困難目標很少靠一次短暫嘗試就改善。"},{"en":"This phrase connects sustained work with possible success.","zh":"這個短語把持續工作與可能成功連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"we would be talking about","meaning":"我們所說的將會是","examples":[{"en":"We would be talking about some $900 million.","zh":"我們所說的將會是大約九億美元。"},{"en":"We would be talking about means the amount, scale, or situation would be approximately this.","zh":"we would be talking about 指金額、規模或情況大約會是這樣。"},{"en":"If every student bought a new laptop, we would be talking about a very large school expense.","zh":"如果每名學生都買新手提電腦，我們所說的將會是一筆很大的學校開支。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used before giving a rough but impressive figure.","zh":"這個短語常在給出粗略但驚人的數字前使用。"},{"en":"It helps the reader understand the size of a proposal.","zh":"它幫助讀者理解一項提議的規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"famous cases","meaning":"著名案例","examples":[{"en":"There are famous cases which illustrate what can be done.","zh":"有些著名案例說明可以做到甚麼。"},{"en":"Famous cases are well-known examples that many people recognise or discuss.","zh":"famous cases 指許多人認識或討論的知名例子。"},{"en":"A teacher may use famous cases of successful students to show how practice works.","zh":"老師可能使用成功學生的著名案例來展示練習如何有效。"},{"en":"Famous cases help readers understand abstract ideas through real examples.","zh":"著名案例幫助讀者透過真實例子理解抽象想法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples that carry persuasive value.","zh":"這個短語引出具有說服力的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"illustrate what can be done","meaning":"說明可以做到甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The case of Welsh illustrates what can be done.","zh":"威爾斯語的案例說明可以做到甚麼。"},{"en":"To illustrate what can be done means to show, through an example, what action is possible.","zh":"illustrate what can be done 指透過例子顯示可以採取甚麼行動。"},{"en":"A successful school recycling project can illustrate what can be done with student leadership.","zh":"成功的學校回收計劃可以說明學生領導下可以做到甚麼。"},{"en":"Good examples make a difficult goal feel more practical.","zh":"好例子會令困難目標感覺更實際。"},{"en":"This phrase uses evidence to inspire or guide action.","zh":"這個短語用證據來鼓勵或引導行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Welsh","meaning":"威爾斯語","examples":[{"en":"Welsh is one of the Celtic languages discussed in the passage.","zh":"威爾斯語是文章討論的凱爾特語族語言之一。"},{"en":"Welsh is a language spoken in Wales and connected with Welsh cultural identity.","zh":"Welsh 指在威爾斯使用、與威爾斯文化身份相關的語言。"},{"en":"Welsh may appear on road signs, school materials, and public services in Wales.","zh":"威爾斯語可能出現在威爾斯的路牌、學校教材和公共服務中。"},{"en":"Public support can help Welsh remain visible and useful in daily life.","zh":"公眾支持可以幫助威爾斯語在日常生活中保持可見和有用。"},{"en":"This word names a specific minority language with a strong revival story.","zh":"這個字指出一種有強烈復興故事的特定少數語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"alone among","meaning":"在……之中唯一","examples":[{"en":"Welsh, alone among the Celtic languages, is showing signs of growth.","zh":"威爾斯語在凱爾特語族語言中唯一顯示增長跡象。"},{"en":"Alone among a group means the only one in that group with a particular quality.","zh":"alone among a group 指在某群體中唯一具有某特質。"},{"en":"This school, alone among the district schools, offers three language immersion programmes.","zh":"這間學校在該區學校中唯一提供三個語言沉浸課程。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights uniqueness within a wider category.","zh":"這個短語突出某物在更大類別中的獨特性。"},{"en":"It often makes the example sound especially notable.","zh":"它常令例子聽起來特別值得注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Celtic languages","meaning":"凱爾特語族語言","examples":[{"en":"Welsh is alone among the Celtic languages in showing signs of real growth.","zh":"威爾斯語在凱爾特語族語言中唯一顯示真正增長跡象。"},{"en":"Celtic languages are a family of languages including Welsh, Irish, Scottish Gaelic, and others.","zh":"Celtic languages 指包括威爾斯語、愛爾蘭語、蘇格蘭蓋爾語等在內的一個語族。"},{"en":"A language class may introduce Celtic languages when teaching European linguistic diversity.","zh":"語言課教授歐洲語言多樣性時，可能介紹凱爾特語族語言。"},{"en":"Some Celtic languages have struggled because dominant national languages became more powerful.","zh":"有些凱爾特語族語言曾因主流國家語言變得更強勢而面臨困難。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a language family, not one single language.","zh":"這個短語指一個語族，而不是單一語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"steady decline towards extinction","meaning":"走向滅絕的持續衰落","examples":[{"en":"Welsh is stopping its steady decline towards extinction.","zh":"威爾斯語正在停止其走向滅絕的持續衰落。"},{"en":"Steady decline towards extinction means a gradual, continuing fall that may end in disappearance.","zh":"steady decline towards extinction 指逐步而持續下降，最終可能消失。"},{"en":"A school club may face steady decline towards closure if fewer students join each year.","zh":"如果每年加入學生都減少，學會可能面臨走向結束的持續衰落。"},{"en":"Reversing steady decline requires long-term support, not one short event.","zh":"扭轉持續衰落需要長期支持，而不是一次短暫活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a slow but serious movement toward disappearance.","zh":"這個短語描述緩慢但嚴重地走向消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"show signs of","meaning":"顯示……跡象","examples":[{"en":"Welsh is showing signs of real growth.","zh":"威爾斯語正顯示真正增長的跡象。"},{"en":"To show signs of something means to give early evidence that it is happening.","zh":"show signs of something 指給出某事正在發生的早期證據。"},{"en":"A student may show signs of improvement when mistakes become fewer each week.","zh":"當錯誤每週變少，學生可能顯示進步跡象。"},{"en":"Signs of growth can encourage people because they suggest effort is working.","zh":"增長跡象可以鼓舞人，因為它暗示努力正在奏效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible clues of a developing change.","zh":"這個短語描述發展中變化的可見線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"real growth","meaning":"真正增長","examples":[{"en":"Welsh is now showing signs of real growth.","zh":"威爾斯語現在正顯示真正增長的跡象。"},{"en":"Real growth means genuine increase, not just temporary attention or symbolic support.","zh":"real growth 指真正增加，而不只是短暫關注或象徵性支持。"},{"en":"A tutoring centre shows real growth when more students stay, improve, and recommend it to friends.","zh":"當更多學生留下來、進步並推薦給朋友，補習中心就顯示真正增長。"},{"en":"In language revival, real growth may mean more speakers, more learners, and more public use.","zh":"在語言復興中，真正增長可能指更多使用者、更多學習者和更多公共使用。"},{"en":"This phrase separates actual progress from appearance only.","zh":"這個短語把實際進展與表面現象分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Language Acts","meaning":"語言法案","examples":[{"en":"Two Language Acts now protect the status of Welsh.","zh":"兩項語言法案現在保護威爾斯語的地位。"},{"en":"Language Acts are laws that give legal recognition or protection to a language.","zh":"Language Acts 指給予某語言法律承認或保護的法例。"},{"en":"A government may pass Language Acts to allow a minority language in schools and public services.","zh":"政府可能通過語言法案，容許少數語言在學校和公共服務中使用。"},{"en":"Legal protection can make a language more visible in daily life.","zh":"法律保護可以令一種語言在日常生活中更明顯可見。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to official laws, not classroom language rules only.","zh":"這個短語指官方法律，而不只是課堂語言規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"protect the status of","meaning":"保護……的地位","examples":[{"en":"Two Language Acts protect the status of Welsh.","zh":"兩項語言法案保護威爾斯語的地位。"},{"en":"To protect the status of something means to defend its official position, value, or rights.","zh":"protect the status of something 指維護某物的官方位置、價值或權利。"},{"en":"School rules can protect the status of student representatives by giving them meeting time.","zh":"校規可以透過給學生代表開會時間來保護其地位。"},{"en":"A language’s status is protected when people have the right to use it in public life.","zh":"當人們有權在公共生活中使用某語言，該語言的地位就受到保護。"},{"en":"This phrase connects legal or social support with recognition.","zh":"這個短語把法律或社會支持與承認連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"its presence is increasingly in evidence","meaning":"……越來越明顯可見","examples":[{"en":"The presence of Welsh is increasingly in evidence in Wales.","zh":"威爾斯語在威爾斯越來越明顯可見。"},{"en":"Its presence is increasingly in evidence means it is becoming more visible or noticeable.","zh":"its presence is increasingly in evidence 指某物變得更可見或更令人注意。"},{"en":"The school’s focus on mental health is increasingly in evidence through posters, talks, and counselling rooms.","zh":"學校對心理健康的重視透過海報、講座和輔導室變得越來越明顯。"},{"en":"A language becomes more visible when it appears on signs, media, forms, and lessons.","zh":"當語言出現在標示、媒體、表格和課堂中，它就變得更可見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growing public visibility.","zh":"這個短語描述公共可見度日益提高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"wherever you travel","meaning":"無論你到哪裏","examples":[{"en":"You can see evidence of Welsh wherever you travel in Wales.","zh":"無論你到威爾斯哪裏，都可以看見威爾斯語的證據。"},{"en":"Wherever you travel means in any place you go within an area.","zh":"wherever you travel 指在某範圍內你去到任何地方。"},{"en":"Wherever you travel in a city, you may notice public signs in more than one language.","zh":"無論你到城市哪裏，都可能注意到多於一種語言的公共標示。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that something is widespread, not limited to one location.","zh":"這個短語強調某物分布廣泛，而不限於一個地點。"},{"en":"It helps describe visible presence across a whole region.","zh":"它有助描述整個地區中的可見存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"on the other side of the world","meaning":"在世界另一邊","examples":[{"en":"On the other side of the world, Maori has been maintained in New Zealand.","zh":"在世界另一邊，毛利語在新西蘭得以維持。"},{"en":"On the other side of the world means in a very distant place.","zh":"on the other side of the world 指在非常遙遠的地方。"},{"en":"A student in Hong Kong can speak online with a friend on the other side of the world.","zh":"香港學生可以在線上與世界另一邊的朋友交談。"},{"en":"This phrase shifts attention to a faraway example.","zh":"這個短語把注意力轉向一個遠方例子。"},{"en":"It often introduces comparison across countries or continents.","zh":"它常引出跨國或跨洲比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Maori","meaning":"毛利語","examples":[{"en":"Maori has been maintained by a system of language nests.","zh":"毛利語透過一套語言巢制度得以維持。"},{"en":"Maori is the language of the Indigenous Maori people of New Zealand.","zh":"Maori 指新西蘭原住民毛利人的語言。"},{"en":"Maori may be taught through songs, stories, greetings, and early-childhood programmes.","zh":"毛利語可以透過歌曲、故事、問候語和幼兒教育計劃教授。"},{"en":"When children hear Maori regularly, they are more likely to keep using it as they grow.","zh":"當孩子定期聽到毛利語，他們長大後更可能繼續使用它。"},{"en":"This word names a specific Indigenous language linked to cultural identity.","zh":"這個字指出一種與文化身份相關的特定原住民語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be maintained by","meaning":"透過……得以維持","examples":[{"en":"Maori has been maintained by a system of language nests.","zh":"毛利語透過一套語言巢制度得以維持。"},{"en":"To be maintained by something means to be kept alive, active, or in good condition through that support.","zh":"be maintained by something 指透過某種支持而保持存活、活躍或良好狀態。"},{"en":"A school garden is maintained by students who water plants every week.","zh":"學校花園透過學生每週澆水得以維持。"},{"en":"A language can be maintained by families, schools, media, and community programmes.","zh":"語言可以透過家庭、學校、媒體和社群計劃得以維持。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what keeps something going.","zh":"這個短語解釋甚麼令某事持續下去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"so-called","meaning":"所謂的","examples":[{"en":"The programme uses so-called language nests.","zh":"該計劃使用所謂的語言巢。"},{"en":"So-called introduces a name or term that people use for something.","zh":"so-called 用來引出人們用於某事物的名稱或術語。"},{"en":"The school created a so-called quiet zone where students can study without talking.","zh":"學校設立了一個所謂的安靜區，讓學生不用說話也能自修。"},{"en":"This phrase can be neutral, but sometimes it suggests the term is unusual or unofficial.","zh":"這個短語可以是中性，但有時暗示該名稱不尋常或非正式。"},{"en":"It helps introduce a special label.","zh":"它幫助引入一個特殊標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"language nests","meaning":"語言巢","examples":[{"en":"Language nests expose young children to Maori in a domestic setting.","zh":"語言巢讓幼兒在家庭式環境中接觸毛利語。"},{"en":"Language nests are early-childhood programmes where children are surrounded by an endangered language.","zh":"language nests 指讓孩子置身於瀕危語言中的幼兒教育計劃。"},{"en":"A language nest may use games, meals, songs, and stories entirely in the target language.","zh":"語言巢可能完全用目標語言進行遊戲、用餐、唱歌和講故事。"},{"en":"Young children learn naturally when the language is part of daily care, not just a lesson.","zh":"當語言成為日常照顧的一部分，而不只是課堂，幼兒會自然學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes immersion for very young learners.","zh":"這個短語描述為幼兒而設的沉浸式學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"first introduced in","meaning":"最早於……引入","examples":[{"en":"Language nests were first introduced in 1982.","zh":"語言巢最早於1982年引入。"},{"en":"First introduced in a year means started or brought into use for the first time in that year.","zh":"first introduced in a year 指某事在該年份首次開始或被使用。"},{"en":"The school’s online homework system was first introduced in 2020.","zh":"學校網上功課系統最早於2020年引入。"},{"en":"Giving the year helps readers place an innovation in historical order.","zh":"給出年份有助讀者把創新放入歷史次序中。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the beginning of a practice or programme.","zh":"這個短語標示某做法或計劃的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"provide children under five with","meaning":"為五歲以下兒童提供……","examples":[{"en":"Language nests provide children under five with a Maori-speaking environment.","zh":"語言巢為五歲以下兒童提供毛利語環境。"},{"en":"To provide children under five with something means to give very young children that support or experience.","zh":"provide children under five with something 指為幼兒提供某種支援或經驗。"},{"en":"A nursery may provide children under five with safe play areas and story time.","zh":"幼兒園可能為五歲以下兒童提供安全遊戲區和故事時間。"},{"en":"Early support matters because young children absorb language through daily interaction.","zh":"早期支援很重要，因為幼兒透過日常互動吸收語言。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on resources given to preschool children.","zh":"這個短語集中於提供給學前兒童的資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"domestic setting","meaning":"家庭式環境","examples":[{"en":"The children learn Maori in a domestic setting.","zh":"孩子在家庭式環境中學習毛利語。"},{"en":"A domestic setting is a home-like environment rather than a formal classroom.","zh":"domestic setting 指像家一樣的環境，而不是正式課室。"},{"en":"Children may feel more relaxed in a domestic setting with toys, meals, and familiar routines.","zh":"有玩具、膳食和熟悉常規的家庭式環境，可以令孩子較放鬆。"},{"en":"A home-like setting can make language learning feel natural and safe.","zh":"家庭式環境可以令語言學習感覺自然和安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the atmosphere and place where learning happens.","zh":"這個短語描述學習發生的氣氛和地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be intensively exposed to","meaning":"密集接觸……","examples":[{"en":"Children are intensively exposed to the language.","zh":"孩子密集接觸該語言。"},{"en":"To be intensively exposed to something means to experience it often and deeply over a period of time.","zh":"be intensively exposed to something 指在一段時間內頻繁而深入地接觸某物。"},{"en":"Students are intensively exposed to English during a full-day language camp.","zh":"學生在全日語言營中密集接觸英文。"},{"en":"Intensive exposure helps learners hear patterns repeatedly and use them naturally.","zh":"密集接觸幫助學習者反覆聽到模式並自然使用。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests frequent contact, not occasional practice.","zh":"這個短語暗示頻繁接觸，而不是偶爾練習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"local community","meaning":"本地社群","examples":[{"en":"The staff are Maori speakers from the local community.","zh":"工作人員是來自本地社群的毛利語使用者。"},{"en":"Local community means the people who live in or belong to a particular area.","zh":"local community 指生活在或屬於某特定地區的人。"},{"en":"A local community may organise weekend classes to teach children traditional songs.","zh":"本地社群可能組織週末課程，教孩子傳統歌曲。"},{"en":"Language projects work better when the local community takes part directly.","zh":"當本地社群直接參與，語言項目會運作得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the people closest to the language or issue.","zh":"這個短語強調最接近該語言或議題的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the hope is that","meaning":"希望是","examples":[{"en":"The hope is that the children will keep their Maori skills alive.","zh":"希望是孩子會保持毛利語技能不失傳。"},{"en":"The hope is that introduces the desired result of an action or plan.","zh":"the hope is that 用來引出某行動或計劃想達到的結果。"},{"en":"The hope is that after-school reading will help students enjoy books again.","zh":"希望是課後閱讀能幫助學生重新享受書本。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what people want to happen, even if success is not guaranteed.","zh":"這個短語顯示人們希望發生甚麼，即使成功未必保證。"},{"en":"It is often used when discussing programmes, policies, or future outcomes.","zh":"它常用於討論計劃、政策或未來結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"keep their skills alive","meaning":"保持技能不失傳","examples":[{"en":"Children are expected to keep their Maori skills alive.","zh":"人們期望孩子保持毛利語技能不失傳。"},{"en":"To keep skills alive means to continue practising them so they are not lost.","zh":"keep skills alive 指繼續練習某技能，使它不會消失。"},{"en":"A musician keeps piano skills alive by playing a little every day.","zh":"音樂家透過每天彈一點鋼琴來保持鋼琴技能。"},{"en":"Language skills fade when children stop using the language after leaving a programme.","zh":"如果孩子離開計劃後停止使用語言，語言技能會逐漸減弱。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that ability survives through regular use.","zh":"這個短語顯示能力透過定期使用而存續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"after leaving","meaning":"離開之後","examples":[{"en":"The children may keep using Maori after leaving the language nests.","zh":"孩子離開語言巢之後，可能繼續使用毛利語。"},{"en":"After leaving means once someone has finished or departed from a place, programme, or stage.","zh":"after leaving 指某人完成或離開某地方、計劃或階段之後。"},{"en":"Students should keep reading English after leaving the exam course.","zh":"學生離開考試課程之後，仍應繼續閱讀英文。"},{"en":"A programme succeeds more fully when learners continue the habit after leaving it.","zh":"當學習者離開計劃後仍維持習慣，計劃就更完整地成功。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what happens beyond the original setting.","zh":"這個短語集中於原本環境之外發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as they grow older","meaning":"隨着他們長大","examples":[{"en":"As they grow older, the children may become role models.","zh":"隨着他們長大，孩子可能成為榜樣。"},{"en":"As they grow older means while they become older over time.","zh":"as they grow older 指隨着他們年齡逐漸增長。"},{"en":"As children grow older, they often become more confident in explaining their opinions.","zh":"隨着孩子長大，他們常會更有信心解釋自己的意見。"},{"en":"Skills learned early can become stronger if children keep using them as they grow.","zh":"如果孩子隨着成長繼續使用早期學到的技能，這些技能可以變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase links development with the passage of time.","zh":"這個短語把發展與時間流逝連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in turn","meaning":"繼而；反過來","examples":[{"en":"The children may in turn become role models for the next generation.","zh":"這些孩子繼而可能成為下一代的榜樣。"},{"en":"In turn means as the next step in a chain of effects.","zh":"in turn 指作為一連串影響中的下一步。"},{"en":"A teacher inspires students, and those students may in turn help younger classmates.","zh":"老師啟發學生，而那些學生繼而可能幫助年幼同學。"},{"en":"One generation’s learning can influence the next generation.","zh":"一代人的學習可以影響下一代。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a sequence where one result leads to another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個結果帶來另一個結果的次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"become role models to","meaning":"成為……的榜樣","examples":[{"en":"Young Maori speakers may become role models to a new generation.","zh":"年輕毛利語使用者可能成為新一代的榜樣。"},{"en":"To become role models to someone means to become examples that others want to follow.","zh":"become role models to someone 指成為他人想效法的例子。"},{"en":"Senior students can become role models to younger students by speaking kindly and working hard.","zh":"高年級學生可以透過友善說話和努力學習成為低年級學生的榜樣。"},{"en":"Young speakers help language revival when children see people like them using the language proudly.","zh":"當孩子看見與自己相似的人自豪地使用語言，年輕使用者就有助語言復興。"},{"en":"This phrase connects personal example with influence.","zh":"這個短語把個人榜樣與影響力連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a new generation of","meaning":"新一代的……","examples":[{"en":"The children may become role models to a new generation of young children.","zh":"這些孩子可能成為新一代幼兒的榜樣。"},{"en":"A new generation of people means the younger group growing up after an older group.","zh":"a new generation of people 指在較年長群體之後成長的年輕一代。"},{"en":"A new generation of students may learn coding earlier than their parents did.","zh":"新一代學生可能比父母更早學習編程。"},{"en":"Languages survive when a new generation of children learns and uses them naturally.","zh":"當新一代孩子自然學習和使用語言，語言便能存續。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on continuity across age groups.","zh":"這個短語集中於不同年齡群體之間的延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the reviving language","meaning":"正在復興的語言","examples":[{"en":"The reviving language may gain strength through political autonomy.","zh":"正在復興的語言可能透過政治自治獲得力量。"},{"en":"The reviving language means a language that is becoming stronger again after decline.","zh":"reviving language 指經歷衰落後正在重新變強的語言。"},{"en":"A reviving language may appear again in schools, songs, public signs, and local media.","zh":"正在復興的語言可能再次出現在學校、歌曲、公共標示和本地媒體中。"},{"en":"Revival becomes more real when people use the language in everyday situations.","zh":"當人們在日常情況中使用該語言，復興就更真實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a language in the process of recovery.","zh":"這個短語描述正在恢復中的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be associated with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"A reviving language may be associated with political autonomy.","zh":"正在復興的語言可能與政治自治有關。"},{"en":"To be associated with something means to be connected with it in people’s minds or in reality.","zh":"be associated with something 指在現實中或在人們心目中與某事相連。"},{"en":"A school uniform may be associated with discipline and belonging.","zh":"校服可能與紀律和歸屬感有關。"},{"en":"Language revival can be associated with political power when communities gain more control over education and public life.","zh":"當社群對教育和公共生活有更多控制權，語言復興可能與政治權力有關。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a connection, not always direct causation.","zh":"這個短語顯示關聯，不一定是直接因果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a degree of political autonomy","meaning":"某程度的政治自治","examples":[{"en":"Language growth can be striking when linked to a degree of political autonomy.","zh":"當語言增長與某程度的政治自治相連時，可能特別顯著。"},{"en":"A degree of political autonomy means some level of self-government or local control.","zh":"degree of political autonomy 指某程度的自治或本地控制權。"},{"en":"A region with a degree of political autonomy may decide more of its own education policy.","zh":"具有某程度政治自治的地區，可能可自行決定更多教育政策。"},{"en":"Local control can help a community support its language in schools and public services.","zh":"本地控制權可以幫助社群在學校和公共服務中支持自己的語言。"},{"en":"This phrase describes partial autonomy, not complete independence.","zh":"這個短語描述部分自治，而不是完全獨立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"especially striking","meaning":"特別顯著","examples":[{"en":"The growth of a language can be especially striking under political autonomy.","zh":"在政治自治下，語言增長可能特別顯著。"},{"en":"Especially striking means particularly noticeable, impressive, or surprising.","zh":"especially striking 指特別明顯、令人印象深刻或令人驚訝。"},{"en":"A shy student’s improvement is especially striking when she begins speaking confidently in front of the class.","zh":"當害羞學生開始在全班面前自信說話，她的進步特別顯著。"},{"en":"Something becomes striking when the change is clear and unexpected.","zh":"當變化清楚且出乎意料，某事就會顯得突出。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a result that stands out strongly.","zh":"這個短語突出非常明顯的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as shown by","meaning":"正如……所顯示","examples":[{"en":"This is shown by Faroese in the Faroe Islands.","zh":"正如法羅群島的法羅語所顯示，情況正是如此。"},{"en":"As shown by means as demonstrated by this example or evidence.","zh":"as shown by 指正如某例子或證據所證明。"},{"en":"Good sleep improves concentration, as shown by students who perform better after resting well.","zh":"充足睡眠改善專注力，正如休息良好後表現更好的學生所顯示。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to support a claim with an example.","zh":"作者使用這個短語以例子支持論點。"},{"en":"It links an argument to evidence.","zh":"它把論點與證據連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Faroese","meaning":"法羅語","examples":[{"en":"Faroese grew after the Faroe Islands gained a measure of autonomy.","zh":"法羅群島取得某程度自治後，法羅語有所增長。"},{"en":"Faroese is a language spoken in the Faroe Islands.","zh":"Faroese 指在法羅群島使用的語言。"},{"en":"Faroese may be used in schools, local media, and everyday communication in the islands.","zh":"法羅語可能用於群島內的學校、本地媒體和日常溝通。"},{"en":"A language can grow stronger when institutions support it officially and socially.","zh":"當制度在官方和社會層面支持語言，它可以變得更強。"},{"en":"This word names a specific language connected with regional identity.","zh":"這個字指出一種與地區身份相關的特定語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Faroe Islands","meaning":"法羅群島","examples":[{"en":"Faroese is spoken in the Faroe Islands.","zh":"法羅語在法羅群島使用。"},{"en":"The Faroe Islands are a group of islands in the North Atlantic with their own language and culture.","zh":"Faroe Islands 指北大西洋的一組島嶼，擁有自己的語言和文化。"},{"en":"A geography class may locate the Faroe Islands between Iceland, Norway, and Scotland.","zh":"地理課可能把法羅群島定位在冰島、挪威和蘇格蘭之間。"},{"en":"Island communities often preserve distinctive languages because they develop in relative isolation.","zh":"島嶼社群常保存獨特語言，因為它們在相對孤立中發展。"},{"en":"This phrase names the place connected with Faroese.","zh":"這個短語指出與法羅語相關的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a measure of autonomy","meaning":"某程度的自治","examples":[{"en":"The islanders received a measure of autonomy from Denmark.","zh":"島民從丹麥取得某程度的自治。"},{"en":"A measure of autonomy means some degree of self-rule or decision-making power.","zh":"a measure of autonomy 指某程度的自治或決策權。"},{"en":"A school club has a measure of autonomy if students can choose its activities themselves.","zh":"如果學生可自行選擇活動，學會就有某程度自治。"},{"en":"Autonomy can help communities protect their language through local policies.","zh":"自治可以幫助社群透過本地政策保護自己的語言。"},{"en":"This phrase means partial control, not total independence.","zh":"這個短語指部分控制權，而不是完全獨立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"receive autonomy from","meaning":"從……取得自治","examples":[{"en":"The islanders received autonomy from Denmark.","zh":"島民從丹麥取得自治。"},{"en":"To receive autonomy from a government means to be given more power to govern oneself.","zh":"receive autonomy from a government 指獲得更多自我管治權力。"},{"en":"A local council may receive more autonomy from the central office to manage community services.","zh":"本地議會可能從中央辦公室取得更多自治權，以管理社區服務。"},{"en":"More autonomy can allow a region to support local language and culture more directly.","zh":"更多自治可以讓地區更直接支持本地語言和文化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes political power being granted by a higher authority.","zh":"這個短語描述較高權力機構授予政治權力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Romansch","meaning":"羅曼什語","examples":[{"en":"Romansch was facing a difficult situation in Switzerland.","zh":"羅曼什語在瑞士面對困難局面。"},{"en":"Romansch is a minority language spoken in parts of Switzerland.","zh":"Romansch 指在瑞士部分地區使用的一種少數語言。"},{"en":"Romansch may be used by small communities whose speakers also know larger national languages.","zh":"羅曼什語可能由一些同時懂較大國家語言的小社群使用。"},{"en":"A language like Romansch can face pressure when young people move to cities using another language.","zh":"當年輕人搬到使用另一語言的城市，像羅曼什語這樣的語言可能面對壓力。"},{"en":"This word names a specific language with several dialects.","zh":"這個字指出一種有多種方言的特定語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"face a difficult situation","meaning":"面對困難局面","examples":[{"en":"Romansch was facing a difficult situation.","zh":"羅曼什語正面對困難局面。"},{"en":"To face a difficult situation means to deal with a serious problem or challenge.","zh":"face a difficult situation 指處理嚴重問題或挑戰。"},{"en":"A school may face a difficult situation if many teachers leave at the same time.","zh":"如果許多老師同時離職，學校可能面對困難局面。"},{"en":"A language faces difficulty when speaker numbers fall and dialects become divided.","zh":"當使用者人數下降且方言分裂，一種語言就會面對困難。"},{"en":"This phrase shows pressure, uncertainty, and the need for action.","zh":"這個短語顯示壓力、不確定性和行動需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"very different dialects","meaning":"非常不同的方言","examples":[{"en":"Romansch was spoken in five very different dialects.","zh":"羅曼什語有五種非常不同的方言。"},{"en":"Very different dialects are regional forms of a language that differ strongly in speech or vocabulary.","zh":"very different dialects 指一種語言中在說法或詞彙上差異很大的地區形式。"},{"en":"Students from different districts may use very different dialects at home.","zh":"來自不同地區的學生可能在家使用非常不同的方言。"},{"en":"Strong dialect differences can make a unified writing system harder to create.","zh":"強烈方言差異會令建立統一書寫系統更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes internal variety within one language.","zh":"這個短語描述一種語言內部的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"small and diminishing numbers","meaning":"人數少且不斷減少","examples":[{"en":"Romansch had small and diminishing numbers of speakers.","zh":"羅曼什語使用者人數少且不斷減少。"},{"en":"Small and diminishing numbers means the number is already low and still decreasing.","zh":"small and diminishing numbers 指數量已經很少，而且仍在下降。"},{"en":"A school club with small and diminishing numbers may close if no new students join.","zh":"如果沒有新學生加入，人數少且不斷減少的學會可能關閉。"},{"en":"Falling speaker numbers make a language harder to teach and use publicly.","zh":"使用者人數下降會令語言更難教學和公開使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both weakness and continuing decline.","zh":"這個短語同時描述薄弱和持續衰落。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"German-speaking cities","meaning":"德語城市","examples":[{"en":"Young people left their communities for work in German-speaking cities.","zh":"年輕人離開自己的社群，到德語城市工作。"},{"en":"German-speaking cities are cities where German is the main language of public life, work, or education.","zh":"German-speaking cities 指公共生活、工作或教育主要使用德語的城市。"},{"en":"A young worker moving to a German-speaking city may use German more often than their home language.","zh":"搬到德語城市的年輕工人可能比使用家鄉語言更常使用德語。"},{"en":"Migration to larger-language cities can weaken smaller community languages.","zh":"遷往使用較大語言的城市，可能削弱較小社群語言。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies cities by the dominant language used there.","zh":"這個短語按主導語言辨認城市。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the solution here was","meaning":"這裏的解決方法是","examples":[{"en":"The solution here was the creation of a unified written language.","zh":"這裏的解決方法是創立一種統一書面語。"},{"en":"The solution here was introduces the answer used in this particular case.","zh":"the solution here was 用來引出此特定個案所採用的答案。"},{"en":"When students kept losing notices, the solution here was a shared online calendar.","zh":"當學生經常遺失通告，這裡的解決方法是共享網上日曆。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that different problems may need different solutions.","zh":"這個短語顯示不同問題可能需要不同解決方法。"},{"en":"It points to a specific strategy in a specific situation.","zh":"它指出特定情況中的具體策略。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"creation of","meaning":"……的創立","examples":[{"en":"The creation of a unified written language helped Romansch.","zh":"統一書面語的創立幫助了羅曼什語。"},{"en":"Creation of something means the act or process of making it exist.","zh":"creation of something 指使某物存在的行動或過程。"},{"en":"The creation of a school reading corner can encourage students to borrow more books.","zh":"學校閱讀角的創立可以鼓勵學生借更多書。"},{"en":"Creating a shared written form can make teaching and publishing easier.","zh":"創立共同書面形式可以令教學和出版更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on bringing something new into existence.","zh":"這個短語集中於把新事物創造出來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"unified written language","meaning":"統一書面語","examples":[{"en":"Romansch Grischun is a unified written language for several dialects.","zh":"Romansch Grischun 是適用於幾種方言的統一書面語。"},{"en":"A unified written language is one shared writing form used across different dialects or varieties.","zh":"unified written language 指跨不同方言或變體使用的一種共同書寫形式。"},{"en":"A school may use a unified written language so students from different villages can read the same textbook.","zh":"學校可能使用統一書面語，讓來自不同村落的學生能讀同一本教科書。"},{"en":"A shared written form can reduce confusion and support publishing, education, and official use.","zh":"共同書面形式可以減少混亂，並支援出版、教育和官方使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unity in writing, even if spoken dialects remain different.","zh":"這個短語描述書寫上的統一，即使口語方言仍不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"for all these dialects","meaning":"適用於所有這些方言","examples":[{"en":"A single written language was created for all these dialects.","zh":"一種單一書面語被創立，適用於所有這些方言。"},{"en":"For all these dialects means intended to serve every dialect being discussed.","zh":"for all these dialects 指為正在討論的每種方言服務。"},{"en":"A school may create one pronunciation guide for all these dialects if students come from many villages.","zh":"如果學生來自許多村落，學校可能為所有這些方言制定一份發音指南。"},{"en":"A shared written form can help different dialect speakers communicate in writing.","zh":"共同書面形式可以幫助不同方言使用者以文字溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses inclusion across several language varieties.","zh":"這個短語強調涵蓋多種語言變體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Romansch Grischun","meaning":"羅曼什格里順語","examples":[{"en":"Romansch Grischun has official status in parts of Switzerland.","zh":"羅曼什格里順語在瑞士部分地區具有官方地位。"},{"en":"Romansch Grischun is a standard written form created for Romansch dialects.","zh":"Romansch Grischun 是為羅曼什語各方言創立的標準書面形式。"},{"en":"A language textbook may use Romansch Grischun so learners can study one shared form.","zh":"語言教科書可能使用羅曼什格里順語，讓學習者學習一種共同形式。"},{"en":"Standard written forms can help small languages appear in schools, media, and government documents.","zh":"標準書面形式可以幫助小語言出現在學校、媒體和政府文件中。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific planned written variety.","zh":"這個短語指出一種特定規劃書面變體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"official status","meaning":"官方地位","examples":[{"en":"Romansch Grischun has official status in parts of Switzerland.","zh":"羅曼什格里順語在瑞士部分地區具有官方地位。"},{"en":"Official status means legal or formal recognition by a government or institution.","zh":"official status 指得到政府或機構的法律或正式承認。"},{"en":"A language with official status may be used on public signs and government forms.","zh":"具有官方地位的語言可用於公共標示和政府表格。"},{"en":"Official recognition can increase respect, funding, and public use.","zh":"官方承認可以增加尊重、資金和公共使用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal recognition, not only popularity among speakers.","zh":"這個短語指正式承認，而不只是使用者之間流行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be increasingly used in spoken form","meaning":"越來越多以口語形式使用","examples":[{"en":"Romansch Grischun is increasingly used in spoken form.","zh":"羅曼什格里順語越來越多以口語形式使用。"},{"en":"To be increasingly used in spoken form means more people are beginning to speak it, not only write it.","zh":"be increasingly used in spoken form 指越來越多人開始說它，而不只是寫它。"},{"en":"A school motto may become increasingly used in spoken form if teachers and students repeat it daily.","zh":"如果老師和學生每天重複，校訓可能越來越多以口語形式使用。"},{"en":"Spoken use makes a language feel more alive than written documents alone.","zh":"口語使用令語言比只存在於書面文件中更有生命力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth in everyday oral communication.","zh":"這個短語描述日常口頭溝通中的增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"on radio and television","meaning":"在電台和電視上","examples":[{"en":"Romansch Grischun is used on radio and television.","zh":"羅曼什格里順語在電台和電視上使用。"},{"en":"On radio and television means broadcast through audio and visual media.","zh":"on radio and television 指透過聲音和影像媒體廣播。"},{"en":"A public message on radio and television can reach people who do not read newspapers.","zh":"在電台和電視上的公共訊息可以接觸不讀報紙的人。"},{"en":"Media use helps a language become familiar beyond private homes.","zh":"媒體使用幫助語言超越私人家庭，變得更熟悉。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to public broadcasting platforms.","zh":"這個短語指公共廣播平台。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be brought back from","meaning":"從……中恢復過來","examples":[{"en":"A language can be brought back from the brink of extinction.","zh":"一種語言可以從滅絕邊緣恢復過來。"},{"en":"To be brought back from something means to be rescued from a dangerous or failing state.","zh":"be brought back from something 指從危險或失敗狀態中被拯救回來。"},{"en":"A failing school club can be brought back from closure if new students join and teachers help.","zh":"如果新學生加入並有老師幫助，瀕臨關閉的學會可以恢復過來。"},{"en":"Languages can be brought back when people document them, teach them, and value them again.","zh":"當人們記錄、教導並重新重視語言，語言可以被拯救回來。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests recovery from a very serious situation.","zh":"這個短語暗示從非常嚴重的情況中恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the very brink of extinction","meaning":"滅絕邊緣","examples":[{"en":"Ainu was brought back from the very brink of extinction.","zh":"阿伊努語從滅絕邊緣被拯救回來。"},{"en":"The very brink of extinction means the point just before complete disappearance.","zh":"very brink of extinction 指完全消失前的最後邊緣。"},{"en":"A local festival with only one remaining organiser may be on the very brink of ending.","zh":"如果本地節日只剩一名組織者，它可能已在消失邊緣。"},{"en":"At this stage, urgent action is needed because there is almost no time left.","zh":"到了這個階段，需要緊急行動，因為時間幾乎耗盡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an extremely dangerous final edge.","zh":"這個短語描述極度危險的最後邊緣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Ainu language","meaning":"阿伊努語","examples":[{"en":"The Ainu language of Japan had only eight fluent speakers left.","zh":"日本的阿伊努語只剩八名流利使用者。"},{"en":"The Ainu language is the language of the Ainu people, an Indigenous people of Japan.","zh":"Ainu language 指日本原住民族阿伊努人的語言。"},{"en":"Ainu language classes can help younger people reconnect with cultural songs and stories.","zh":"阿伊努語課程可以幫助年輕人重新連接文化歌曲和故事。"},{"en":"When a language has very few fluent speakers, documentation and teaching become urgent.","zh":"當一種語言只剩很少流利使用者，記錄和教學就變得迫切。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific Indigenous language at risk.","zh":"這個短語指出一種處於風險中的特定原住民語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"years of neglect and repression","meaning":"多年的忽視和壓制","examples":[{"en":"Ainu suffered many years of neglect and repression.","zh":"阿伊努語經歷多年的忽視和壓制。"},{"en":"Years of neglect and repression means a long period of being ignored and actively suppressed.","zh":"years of neglect and repression 指長時間被忽略並被積極壓制。"},{"en":"A local tradition may weaken after years of neglect if no one teaches it to children.","zh":"如果沒有人教孩子，本地傳統經過多年忽視後可能變弱。"},{"en":"Repression makes language loss worse when people feel ashamed or afraid to speak.","zh":"當人們因說某語言感到羞恥或害怕，壓制會令語言流失更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both passive ignoring and active pressure.","zh":"這個短語同時描述被動忽視和主動壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"reach a stage where","meaning":"發展到……的階段","examples":[{"en":"Ainu reached a stage where only eight fluent speakers remained.","zh":"阿伊努語發展到只剩八名流利使用者的階段。"},{"en":"To reach a stage where something happens means to arrive at a particular point in a process.","zh":"reach a stage where something happens 指到達某過程中的特定階段。"},{"en":"A student may reach a stage where basic grammar is no longer the main problem.","zh":"學生可能發展到基本文法不再是主要問題的階段。"},{"en":"When a language reaches a stage with very few speakers, recovery becomes much harder.","zh":"當語言發展到使用者極少的階段，復興會困難得多。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a point in development, decline, or change.","zh":"這個短語標示發展、衰落或變化中的某一點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"fluent speakers","meaning":"流利使用者","examples":[{"en":"Only eight fluent speakers of Ainu were left.","zh":"阿伊努語只剩八名流利使用者。"},{"en":"Fluent speakers are people who can use a language smoothly, naturally, and accurately.","zh":"fluent speakers 指能流暢、自然和準確使用某語言的人。"},{"en":"A fluent speaker can usually tell stories, explain problems, and hold daily conversations without much struggle.","zh":"流利使用者通常能說故事、解釋問題並輕鬆進行日常對話。"},{"en":"A language revival depends heavily on fluent speakers because they carry living knowledge.","zh":"語言復興高度依賴流利使用者，因為他們承載活的知識。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to strong ability, not just knowing a few words.","zh":"這個短語指強能力，而不只是知道幾個詞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"all elderly","meaning":"全都是長者","examples":[{"en":"The remaining fluent speakers were all elderly.","zh":"剩餘流利使用者全都是長者。"},{"en":"All elderly means every person in the group was old.","zh":"all elderly 指群體中每個人都是老人。"},{"en":"If all remaining craft masters are elderly, young apprentices must learn quickly.","zh":"如果剩下的工藝大師全都是長者，年輕學徒就必須盡快學習。"},{"en":"A language becomes more vulnerable when its fluent speakers are all elderly.","zh":"當流利使用者全都是長者，一種語言會變得更脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses age-related urgency.","zh":"這個短語強調與年齡相關的迫切性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"government policies","meaning":"政府政策","examples":[{"en":"New government policies brought fresh attitudes towards Ainu.","zh":"新政府政策為阿伊努語帶來新的態度。"},{"en":"Government policies are official plans, rules, or actions made by the government.","zh":"government policies 指政府制定的官方計劃、規則或行動。"},{"en":"Government policies can support minority languages through funding, schools, and public recognition.","zh":"政府政策可以透過資金、學校和公共承認支援少數語言。"},{"en":"Policy changes can influence how people feel about a language in public life.","zh":"政策改變可以影響人們在公共生活中如何看待一種語言。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to official decisions, not private opinions.","zh":"這個短語指官方決定，而不是私人意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"bring fresh attitudes","meaning":"帶來新的態度","examples":[{"en":"New policies brought fresh attitudes and interest in survival.","zh":"新政策帶來新的態度和對存續的關注。"},{"en":"To bring fresh attitudes means to create newer, more positive, or more open ways of thinking.","zh":"bring fresh attitudes 指創造更新、更正面或更開放的思考方式。"},{"en":"A new principal may bring fresh attitudes toward student mental health.","zh":"新校長可能為學生心理健康帶來新的態度。"},{"en":"Fresh attitudes can encourage people to value something they once ignored.","zh":"新態度可以鼓勵人們重視曾被忽略的事物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change in mindset.","zh":"這個短語描述心態上的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"positive interest in survival","meaning":"對存續的正面關注","examples":[{"en":"The new policies encouraged a positive interest in survival.","zh":"新政策鼓勵了對存續的正面關注。"},{"en":"Positive interest in survival means supportive concern about keeping something alive or continuing.","zh":"positive interest in survival 指支持某事繼續存在的正面關心。"},{"en":"A school may show positive interest in a club’s survival by giving it a room and budget.","zh":"學校給學會課室和預算，就是對該學會存續表示正面關注。"},{"en":"When people care positively about a language’s survival, they are more likely to learn and teach it.","zh":"當人們正面關心一種語言的存續，他們更可能學習和教授它。"},{"en":"This phrase combines hope, support, and practical concern.","zh":"這個短語結合希望、支持和實際關心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"semi-speakers","meaning":"半使用者；半流利者","examples":[{"en":"Semi-speakers were encouraged to speak Ainu again.","zh":"半使用者被鼓勵再次說阿伊努語。"},{"en":"Semi-speakers are people who understand or partly speak a language but are not fully fluent.","zh":"semi-speakers 指能理解或部分說某語言，但並非完全流利的人。"},{"en":"A semi-speaker may understand grandparents’ conversations but struggle to answer smoothly.","zh":"半使用者可能聽得懂祖父母對話，但難以流暢回答。"},{"en":"Encouraging semi-speakers matters because they can become stronger speakers with practice.","zh":"鼓勵半使用者很重要，因為他們可以透過練習成為更強使用者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes partial language ability.","zh":"這個短語描述部分語言能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"become unwilling to","meaning":"變得不願意","examples":[{"en":"Some people had become unwilling to speak Ainu.","zh":"有些人已變得不願意說阿伊努語。"},{"en":"To become unwilling to do something means to stop wanting to do it or feel reluctant to do it.","zh":"become unwilling to do something 指不再想做某事或對做某事感到抗拒。"},{"en":"A student may become unwilling to speak in class after being laughed at.","zh":"學生被嘲笑後，可能變得不願意在課堂發言。"},{"en":"Negative attitudes can make people avoid using a language even if they know it.","zh":"負面態度可以令人即使懂某語言，也避免使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how social pressure can change behaviour.","zh":"這個短語顯示社會壓力如何改變行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"negative attitudes of","meaning":"……的負面態度","examples":[{"en":"They avoided Ainu because of the negative attitudes of Japanese speakers.","zh":"他們因日語使用者的負面態度而避免使用阿伊努語。"},{"en":"Negative attitudes of a group are unfavourable beliefs, judgements, or reactions held by that group.","zh":"negative attitudes of a group 指某群體持有的不友善信念、判斷或反應。"},{"en":"The negative attitudes of classmates can make a shy student stop asking questions.","zh":"同學的負面態度可以令害羞學生停止提問。"},{"en":"If dominant speakers mock a minority language, its users may feel ashamed.","zh":"如果主流語言使用者嘲笑少數語言，其使用者可能感到羞恥。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how social judgement can discourage language use.","zh":"這個短語解釋社會評價如何阻礙語言使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be prompted to","meaning":"被促使去","examples":[{"en":"Semi-speakers were prompted to become active speakers again.","zh":"半使用者被促使再次成為活躍使用者。"},{"en":"To be prompted to do something means to be encouraged or moved to take action.","zh":"be prompted to do something 指受到鼓勵或推動而採取行動。"},{"en":"A student may be prompted to revise harder after receiving honest feedback.","zh":"學生收到坦誠回饋後，可能被促使更努力溫習。"},{"en":"Supportive policies can prompt people to use a language they once avoided.","zh":"支持性政策可以促使人們使用曾經避免使用的語言。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what pushes someone toward action.","zh":"這個短語顯示甚麼推動某人行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"active speakers","meaning":"活躍使用者","examples":[{"en":"Some semi-speakers became active speakers again.","zh":"有些半使用者再次成為活躍使用者。"},{"en":"Active speakers are people who use a language regularly, not only understand it passively.","zh":"active speakers 指定期使用某語言，而不只是被動理解的人。"},{"en":"A student becomes an active speaker of English when she uses it in discussions, messages, and presentations.","zh":"當學生在討論、訊息和簡報中使用英文，她就成為英文活躍使用者。"},{"en":"Languages grow stronger when more people become active speakers in daily life.","zh":"當更多人在日常生活中成為活躍使用者，語言會變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts regular use with passive knowledge.","zh":"這個短語把定期使用與被動知識作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"fresh interest","meaning":"新的興趣；重新關注","examples":[{"en":"There is fresh interest in the Ainu language now.","zh":"現在對阿伊努語有新的興趣。"},{"en":"Fresh interest means new or renewed attention, curiosity, and support.","zh":"fresh interest 指新的或重新出現的注意、好奇和支持。"},{"en":"A local museum may create fresh interest in old photographs by sharing them online.","zh":"本地博物館可以透過網上分享舊照片，帶來新的興趣。"},{"en":"Fresh interest can bring new learners, funding, and public discussion.","zh":"新的關注可以帶來新學習者、資金和公共討論。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that people are paying attention again.","zh":"這個短語暗示人們再次注意某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"publicly available","meaning":"更公開可接觸","examples":[{"en":"The language is more publicly available than it has been for years.","zh":"這種語言比多年來任何時候都更公開可接觸。"},{"en":"Publicly available means accessible to people in public spaces, media, schools, or official settings.","zh":"publicly available 指人們可在公共空間、媒體、學校或官方環境中接觸到。"},{"en":"A school report becomes publicly available when parents can read it online.","zh":"當家長能在網上閱讀學校報告，報告就變得公開可得。"},{"en":"A language becomes more publicly available when lessons, recordings, and signs are easy to find.","zh":"當課程、錄音和標示容易找到，語言就更公開可接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes access beyond private homes or small groups.","zh":"這個短語描述超越私人家庭或小群體的可接觸性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"good descriptions and materials","meaning":"良好的描述資料和教材","examples":[{"en":"Extinct languages can be revived if good descriptions and materials are available.","zh":"如果有良好的描述資料和教材，已滅絕語言可以被復興。"},{"en":"Good descriptions and materials are clear records, explanations, and resources that help people learn a language.","zh":"good descriptions and materials 指幫助人學習語言的清楚記錄、解釋和資源。"},{"en":"A teacher can rebuild a lost lesson plan if good descriptions and materials were saved.","zh":"如果保存了良好描述和教材，老師可以重建遺失的教案。"},{"en":"Detailed notes, recordings, word lists, and grammar explanations make revival more possible.","zh":"詳細筆記、錄音、詞表和文法解釋令復興更有可能。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the importance of high-quality documentation.","zh":"這個短語強調高質素記錄的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"extinct languages","meaning":"已滅絕語言","examples":[{"en":"Even extinct languages can sometimes be resurrected.","zh":"即使已滅絕語言有時也可以被復活。"},{"en":"Extinct languages are languages that no longer have living native or fluent speakers.","zh":"extinct languages 指不再有在世母語者或流利使用者的語言。"},{"en":"A language may become extinct if the last speakers die without passing it on.","zh":"如果最後使用者去世前沒有傳承，一種語言可能變成已滅絕語言。"},{"en":"Extinct languages can sometimes be studied through old documents, recordings, and word lists.","zh":"已滅絕語言有時可以透過舊文件、錄音和詞表研究。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to languages no longer used as living community languages.","zh":"這個短語指不再作為活社群語言使用的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be resurrected","meaning":"被復活；被重現","examples":[{"en":"Extinct languages can be resurrected if they are well documented.","zh":"如果記錄完整，已滅絕語言可以被復活。"},{"en":"To be resurrected means to be brought back to life, use, or activity after seeming dead or lost.","zh":"be resurrected 指看似死亡或失去後，被重新帶回生命、使用或活動中。"},{"en":"An old school tradition can be resurrected if students decide to practise it again.","zh":"如果學生決定再次實踐，舊學校傳統可以被復活。"},{"en":"A language is easier to resurrect when records show its sounds, grammar, and vocabulary.","zh":"當記錄顯示語音、文法和詞彙，語言更容易被復活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes revival after disappearance.","zh":"這個短語描述消失後的復興。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"Kaurna","meaning":"卡烏爾納語","examples":[{"en":"Kaurna is an example of a resurrected language from South Australia.","zh":"卡烏爾納語是來自南澳洲的一種被復活語言例子。"},{"en":"Kaurna is an Indigenous Australian language associated with the Adelaide region of South Australia.","zh":"Kaurna 指與南澳洲阿德萊德地區相關的澳洲原住民語言。"},{"en":"Kaurna may be taught through reconstructed words, songs, names, and classroom materials.","zh":"卡烏爾納語可透過重建詞語、歌曲、名字和課堂教材教授。"},{"en":"A documented extinct language can sometimes regain community use.","zh":"有記錄的已滅絕語言有時可以重新獲得社群使用。"},{"en":"This word names a specific language used as an example of revival.","zh":"這個字指出一種作為復興例子的特定語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"South Australia","meaning":"南澳洲","examples":[{"en":"Kaurna comes from South Australia.","zh":"卡烏爾納語來自南澳洲。"},{"en":"South Australia is a state in Australia where the Kaurna language is historically connected to local Indigenous people.","zh":"South Australia 指澳洲的一個州，卡烏爾納語在歷史上與當地原住民相關。"},{"en":"A geography lesson may locate South Australia on the southern coast of the continent.","zh":"地理課可能把南澳洲定位在澳洲大陸南岸。"},{"en":"Place matters because languages are often tied to land, stories, and community identity.","zh":"地方很重要，因為語言常與土地、故事和社群身份相連。"},{"en":"This phrase names the region connected with Kaurna.","zh":"這個短語指出與卡烏爾納語相關的地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"extinct for about a century","meaning":"滅絕了約一個世紀","examples":[{"en":"Kaurna had been extinct for about a century.","zh":"卡烏爾納語已滅絕了約一個世紀。"},{"en":"Extinct for about a century means no longer used as a living language for roughly one hundred years.","zh":"extinct for about a century 指約一百年來不再作為活語言使用。"},{"en":"A tradition extinct for about a century may still be revived if records and community interest remain.","zh":"如果記錄和社群興趣仍在，滅絕了約一個世紀的傳統仍可能被復興。"},{"en":"Long extinction makes revival harder because there are no fluent speakers to ask directly.","zh":"長時間滅絕令復興更困難，因為沒有流利使用者可直接詢問。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the length of disappearance.","zh":"這個短語描述消失的時間長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"quite well documented","meaning":"記錄相當完整","examples":[{"en":"Kaurna had been quite well documented before revival efforts began.","zh":"在復興工作開始前，卡烏爾納語已有相當完整記錄。"},{"en":"Quite well documented means recorded in enough detail to be useful, though perhaps not perfectly complete.","zh":"quite well documented 指記錄細節足夠有用，雖然未必完全完整。"},{"en":"A school project is quite well documented if notes, photos, and meeting records are saved.","zh":"如果筆記、照片和會議記錄都有保存，學校項目就算記錄相當完整。"},{"en":"Good documentation gives later learners a foundation for reconstruction.","zh":"良好記錄為後來學習者提供重建基礎。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that records are helpful but may still have gaps.","zh":"這個短語表示記錄有幫助，但可能仍有缺口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a strong movement grew for","meaning":"出現一股強大的……運動","examples":[{"en":"A strong movement grew for the revival of Kaurna.","zh":"出現一股強大的卡烏爾納語復興運動。"},{"en":"A strong movement grew for something means many people gradually joined efforts to support it.","zh":"a strong movement grew for something 指越來越多人逐漸加入支持某事的努力。"},{"en":"A strong movement grew for safer school crossings after several accidents.","zh":"幾宗意外後，出現一股強大的學校路口安全運動。"},{"en":"Movements grow when people share concern and organise action together.","zh":"當人們有共同關注並一起組織行動，運動就會成長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes expanding collective support.","zh":"這個短語描述不斷擴大的集體支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"revival","meaning":"復興","examples":[{"en":"The revival of Kaurna was possible because written records existed.","zh":"卡烏爾納語的復興之所以可能，是因為有文字記錄存在。"},{"en":"Revival means bringing something back into use, life, popularity, or strength.","zh":"revival 指把某事重新帶回使用、生命、流行或力量中。"},{"en":"A town may see the revival of its night market after new stalls open.","zh":"新攤檔開張後，城鎮可能見證夜市復興。"},{"en":"Language revival depends on records, speakers, learners, and community commitment.","zh":"語言復興取決於記錄、使用者、學習者和社群承諾。"},{"en":"This word describes recovery after decline or disappearance.","zh":"這個字描述衰落或消失後的恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reconstruct it","meaning":"重建它","examples":[{"en":"Researchers were able to reconstruct the language.","zh":"研究者能夠重建該語言。"},{"en":"To reconstruct it means to rebuild it from surviving records, evidence, or fragments.","zh":"reconstruct it 指從保存下來的記錄、證據或碎片中重建它。"},{"en":"A teacher may reconstruct a lost lesson plan from old notes and student worksheets.","zh":"老師可能從舊筆記和學生工作紙中重建遺失的教案。"},{"en":"Language reconstruction is possible when enough grammar, vocabulary, and pronunciation clues survive.","zh":"當足夠文法、詞彙和發音線索保存下來，語言重建就可能做到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rebuilding something incomplete.","zh":"這個短語描述重建不完整的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"revised language","meaning":"修訂後的語言","examples":[{"en":"The revised language is not the same as the original.","zh":"修訂後的語言與原本的語言並不相同。"},{"en":"A revised language is a changed or reconstructed form of a language after editing or rebuilding.","zh":"revised language 指經修改、重建或整理後的語言形式。"},{"en":"A revised textbook is useful, but it may differ from the first edition.","zh":"修訂後的教科書很有用，但可能與第一版不同。"},{"en":"A revived language may be revised because some old vocabulary or pronunciation details are missing.","zh":"被復興語言可能經過修訂，因為部分舊詞彙或發音細節已缺失。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that recovery may involve change.","zh":"這個短語強調恢復可能涉及改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the original","meaning":"原本的語言","examples":[{"en":"The revised language lacks some features of the original.","zh":"修訂後的語言缺少原本語言的一些特徵。"},{"en":"The original means the first or earlier form of something before change or revision.","zh":"the original 指某物在改變或修訂前的最初或早期形式。"},{"en":"A copied painting may look similar, but the original has historical value.","zh":"複製畫可能看似相似，但原作具有歷史價值。"},{"en":"When records are incomplete, a revived language may not fully match the original.","zh":"當記錄不完整，被復興語言可能無法完全符合原本形式。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the source form with a later version.","zh":"這個短語把來源形式與後來版本作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"lack the range","meaning":"缺乏原有的廣度","examples":[{"en":"The revived language lacks the range that the original had.","zh":"復興後的語言缺乏原本語言曾有的廣度。"},{"en":"To lack the range means to not have the full variety, depth, or breadth that something once had.","zh":"lack the range 指沒有某物曾經擁有的完整多樣性、深度或廣度。"},{"en":"A beginner’s English may lack the range needed for formal debate.","zh":"初學者英文可能缺乏正式辯論所需的廣度。"},{"en":"A reconstructed language may lack range if many old words and expressions were never recorded.","zh":"如果許多舊詞和表達從未被記錄，重建語言可能缺乏廣度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited variety or coverage.","zh":"這個短語描述多樣性或涵蓋範圍有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"old vocabulary","meaning":"舊有詞彙","examples":[{"en":"The revived language lacks much of the old vocabulary.","zh":"復興後的語言缺乏大量舊有詞彙。"},{"en":"Old vocabulary means words that belonged to an earlier form of a language.","zh":"old vocabulary 指屬於某語言早期形式的詞語。"},{"en":"Grandparents may know old vocabulary that younger speakers no longer use.","zh":"祖父母可能知道年輕使用者不再使用的舊有詞彙。"},{"en":"When old vocabulary is lost, it becomes harder to talk about traditional tools, customs, and places.","zh":"當舊有詞彙流失，就更難談論傳統工具、習俗和地方。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to words from the past.","zh":"這個短語指來自過去的詞語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"nonetheless","meaning":"儘管如此","examples":[{"en":"The revived language can nonetheless act as a badge of identity.","zh":"儘管如此，復興後的語言仍可作為身份標誌。"},{"en":"Nonetheless means despite what was just said.","zh":"nonetheless 指儘管剛才所說的情況如此。"},{"en":"The course is difficult; nonetheless, many students continue because it is useful.","zh":"課程很困難；儘管如此，許多學生因它有用而繼續學習。"},{"en":"This word introduces a positive or contrasting point after a limitation.","zh":"這個字在限制之後引出正面或對比觀點。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing that something still has value despite problems.","zh":"當要顯示某事即使有問題仍有價值時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"act as a badge of","meaning":"作為……的標誌","examples":[{"en":"A revived language can act as a badge of present-day identity.","zh":"被復興的語言可以作為當代身份認同的標誌。"},{"en":"To act as a badge of something means to serve as a visible sign of it.","zh":"act as a badge of something 指作為某事的可見象徵。"},{"en":"A school pin can act as a badge of belonging during a graduation ceremony.","zh":"畢業禮上的校章可以作為歸屬感的標誌。"},{"en":"A language can show who people are and where they feel they belong.","zh":"語言可以顯示人們是誰，以及他們覺得自己屬於哪裡。"},{"en":"This phrase connects symbols with identity.","zh":"這個短語把象徵與身份連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"present-day identity","meaning":"當代身份認同","examples":[{"en":"Kaurna can act as a badge of present-day identity.","zh":"卡烏爾納語可以作為當代身份認同的標誌。"},{"en":"Present-day identity means the way people understand who they are today.","zh":"present-day identity 指人們今日如何理解自己是誰。"},{"en":"A city’s present-day identity may include both old traditions and modern creativity.","zh":"城市的當代身份認同可能同時包括舊傳統和現代創意。"},{"en":"Revived languages can help communities express identity in the present, not only remember the past.","zh":"被復興語言可以幫助社群在當下表達身份，而不只是記住過去。"},{"en":"This phrase connects heritage with current life.","zh":"這個短語把文化遺產與現今生活連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"as long as","meaning":"只要","examples":[{"en":"As long as people value the language, it can continue to develop.","zh":"只要人們重視該語言，它就可以繼續發展。"},{"en":"As long as means provided that or if this condition remains true.","zh":"as long as 指只要某條件仍然成立。"},{"en":"A student can improve as long as they practise regularly and accept feedback.","zh":"只要學生定期練習並接受回饋，就可以進步。"},{"en":"A language can grow as long as people keep using it in real situations.","zh":"只要人們在真實情況中繼續使用語言，它就可以成長。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the condition needed for something to happen.","zh":"這個短語引出某事發生所需的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"value it as","meaning":"把它重視為","examples":[{"en":"People value the language as a marker of identity.","zh":"人們把該語言重視為身份認同標誌。"},{"en":"To value it as something means to treat it as important because it serves that role.","zh":"value it as something 指因某物具有某角色而重視它。"},{"en":"A family may value an old photograph as a memory of grandparents.","zh":"家庭可能把舊照片重視為祖父母記憶。"},{"en":"When people value a language as identity, they are more likely to teach it to children.","zh":"當人們把語言重視為身份，他們更可能把它教給孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why something matters to people.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物為何對人重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"true marker of identity","meaning":"身份認同的真正標誌","examples":[{"en":"A language can be a true marker of identity.","zh":"語言可以是身份認同的真正標誌。"},{"en":"A true marker of identity is something that genuinely shows who people are or where they belong.","zh":"true marker of identity 指真正顯示人們是誰或屬於哪裡的事物。"},{"en":"A family name can be a marker of identity because it connects people with relatives and history.","zh":"姓氏可以是身份標誌，因為它把人與親人和歷史連起來。"},{"en":"Language marks identity when people use it to tell stories, greet elders, and name places.","zh":"當人們用語言說故事、問候長者和命名地方，語言就標示身份。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses real symbolic meaning.","zh":"這個短語強調真正的象徵意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be prepared to","meaning":"願意；準備好","examples":[{"en":"People must be prepared to keep using the language.","zh":"人們必須願意繼續使用該語言。"},{"en":"To be prepared to do something means to be willing and ready to do it.","zh":"be prepared to do something 指願意並準備好做某事。"},{"en":"A student must be prepared to make mistakes when learning to speak English.","zh":"學生學習說英文時，必須準備好犯錯。"},{"en":"Language revival needs people who are prepared to use the language even when it feels difficult.","zh":"語言復興需要人們願意在感覺困難時仍使用該語言。"},{"en":"This phrase combines readiness with willingness.","zh":"這個短語結合準備好和願意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"keep using it","meaning":"繼續使用它","examples":[{"en":"A revived language can develop if people keep using it.","zh":"如果人們繼續使用它，被復興語言可以發展。"},{"en":"To keep using it means to continue using it regularly after revival or learning begins.","zh":"keep using it 指在復興或學習開始後持續定期使用它。"},{"en":"A student keeps using new vocabulary by writing sentences and speaking with classmates.","zh":"學生透過寫句子和與同學交談來繼續使用新詞彙。"},{"en":"A language grows when people use it at home, online, in school, and in public.","zh":"當人們在家、網上、學校和公共場合使用語言，語言就會成長。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that survival depends on continued practice.","zh":"這個短語顯示存續取決於持續練習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"develop new functions","meaning":"發展出新功能","examples":[{"en":"A living language can develop new functions.","zh":"活語言可以發展出新功能。"},{"en":"To develop new functions means to gain new uses or roles over time.","zh":"develop new functions 指隨時間獲得新用途或新角色。"},{"en":"A school hall may develop new functions if it becomes a theatre, meeting room, and exam centre.","zh":"如果學校禮堂變成劇場、會議室和考試中心，它就發展出新功能。"},{"en":"A revived language develops new functions when people use it for texting, science lessons, or public signs.","zh":"當人們用被復興語言發訊息、上科學課或寫公共標示，它就發展出新功能。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a language can adapt to modern needs.","zh":"這個短語顯示語言可以適應現代需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"living language","meaning":"活語言；仍被使用的語言","examples":[{"en":"A revived language can grow like any other living language.","zh":"被復興語言可以像任何其他活語言一樣成長。"},{"en":"A living language is a language that people actively use and change through daily life.","zh":"living language 指人們在日常生活中積極使用並不斷改變的語言。"},{"en":"English is a living language because speakers constantly create new expressions.","zh":"英文是一種活語言，因為使用者不斷創造新表達。"},{"en":"A language becomes living when it is used in homes, schools, media, and ordinary conversation.","zh":"當語言在家庭、學校、媒體和日常對話中被使用，它就成為活語言。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts active use with a language preserved only in records.","zh":"這個短語把活躍使用與只保存在記錄中的語言作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"too soon to predict","meaning":"現在預測仍為時過早","examples":[{"en":"It is too soon to predict the future of these revived languages.","zh":"現在預測這些被復興語言的未來仍為時過早。"},{"en":"Too soon to predict means not enough time has passed to make a reliable judgement.","zh":"too soon to predict 指經過的時間不足以作出可靠判斷。"},{"en":"After one lesson, it is too soon to predict whether a student will become fluent.","zh":"只上一堂課後，現在預測學生是否會變流利仍為時過早。"},{"en":"Predictions are weak when evidence is still early and outcomes are uncertain.","zh":"當證據仍處早期且結果不確定，預測就很薄弱。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses caution about the future.","zh":"這個短語表達對未來的謹慎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the future of","meaning":"……的未來","examples":[{"en":"It is too soon to predict the future of revived languages.","zh":"現在預測被復興語言的未來仍為時過早。"},{"en":"The future of something means what may happen to it later.","zh":"future of something 指某事後來可能會怎樣。"},{"en":"A teacher may discuss the future of a student’s study plan after seeing several months of progress.","zh":"老師可能在看見幾個月進展後，討論學生學習計劃的未來。"},{"en":"The future of a language depends on speakers, schools, media, and community pride.","zh":"一種語言的未來取決於使用者、學校、媒體和社群自豪感。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on later development or survival.","zh":"這個短語集中於後來的發展或存續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"revived languages","meaning":"被復興的語言","examples":[{"en":"Revived languages need support to survive.","zh":"被復興的語言需要支持才能存續。"},{"en":"Revived languages are languages that have been brought back into use after serious decline or extinction.","zh":"revived languages 指在嚴重衰落或滅絕後被重新帶回使用的語言。"},{"en":"Revived languages may appear first in classes, ceremonies, songs, and community events.","zh":"被復興的語言起初可能出現在課程、儀式、歌曲和社群活動中。"},{"en":"They need regular speakers to become living languages again.","zh":"它們需要定期使用者才能重新成為活語言。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to languages in recovery, not languages that have always remained strong.","zh":"這個短語指正在恢復中的語言，而不是一直強勢的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"attract positive attitudes","meaning":"吸引正面態度","examples":[{"en":"Some revived languages are attracting positive attitudes.","zh":"有些被復興的語言正在吸引正面態度。"},{"en":"To attract positive attitudes means to receive supportive, respectful, or hopeful reactions from people.","zh":"attract positive attitudes 指獲得人們支持、尊重或抱有希望的反應。"},{"en":"A new school reading programme may attract positive attitudes if students enjoy the books.","zh":"如果學生喜歡那些書，新學校閱讀計劃可能吸引正面態度。"},{"en":"Positive attitudes make people more willing to learn, speak, and fund a language.","zh":"正面態度令人更願意學習、使用和資助一種語言。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growing goodwill.","zh":"這個短語描述不斷增長的善意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"precisely the range of","meaning":"正正是那一系列的……","examples":[{"en":"Some languages are attracting precisely the range of support they need.","zh":"有些語言正在吸引正正是它們所需的一系列支持。"},{"en":"Precisely the range of something means exactly the variety or set that is required.","zh":"precisely the range of something 指正是所需的多種項目或整套內容。"},{"en":"A student preparing for IELTS needs precisely the range of practice that covers reading, writing, listening, and speaking.","zh":"準備 IELTS 的學生需要正正是涵蓋讀、寫、聽、說的一系列練習。"},{"en":"Language revival may need support from families, schools, media, and government together.","zh":"語言復興可能需要家庭、學校、媒體和政府共同支持。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the mix of support is exactly appropriate.","zh":"這個短語強調支持組合正好合適。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"grass-roots support","meaning":"基層支持；民間支持","examples":[{"en":"Grass-roots support is essential for language survival.","zh":"基層支持對語言存續至關重要。"},{"en":"Grass-roots support is support from ordinary people in the community, not only leaders or officials.","zh":"grass-roots support 指來自社群普通人的支持，而不只是領袖或官員的支持。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood recycling scheme works better when it has grass-roots support from residents.","zh":"當社區居民提供基層支持，鄰里回收計劃會運作得更好。"},{"en":"A language survives more strongly when ordinary families choose to speak it every day.","zh":"當普通家庭每天選擇使用某語言，它會更有力地存續。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses bottom-up community involvement.","zh":"這個短語強調由下而上的社群參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"preconditions for","meaning":"……的先決條件","examples":[{"en":"Positive attitudes are preconditions for language survival.","zh":"正面態度是語言存續的先決條件。"},{"en":"Preconditions for something are things that must exist before it can happen successfully.","zh":"preconditions for something 指某事成功發生前必須存在的條件。"},{"en":"Enough sleep and regular practice are preconditions for steady exam improvement.","zh":"充足睡眠和定期練習是考試穩定進步的先決條件。"},{"en":"Without respect and community desire, language revival is unlikely to succeed.","zh":"沒有尊重和社群意願，語言復興不大可能成功。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies necessary starting conditions.","zh":"這個短語指出必要的起始條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"language survival","meaning":"語言存續","examples":[{"en":"Grass-roots support is important for language survival.","zh":"基層支持對語言存續很重要。"},{"en":"Language survival means a language continues to be used by speakers across generations.","zh":"language survival 指一種語言能夠跨世代繼續被使用。"},{"en":"Language survival is stronger when children hear the language at home and at school.","zh":"當孩子在家中和學校都聽到該語言，語言存續會更穩固。"},{"en":"A language may fail to survive if it is only remembered but not spoken.","zh":"如果語言只被記住而不被使用，它可能無法存續。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on long-term continuation.","zh":"這個短語集中於長期延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"unexpected but heart-warming ways","meaning":"出人意料但令人暖心的方式","examples":[{"en":"Languages may survive in unexpected but heart-warming ways.","zh":"語言可能以出人意料但令人暖心的方式存續。"},{"en":"Unexpected but heart-warming ways are surprising methods or events that create warm, hopeful feelings.","zh":"unexpected but heart-warming ways 指令人意外但帶來溫暖和希望的方法或事件。"},{"en":"A child learning a grandparent’s old song online is an unexpected but heart-warming way to keep tradition alive.","zh":"孩子在網上學習祖父母的舊歌，是延續傳統的出人意料但暖心方式。"},{"en":"Language survival can happen through small community actions, not only official programmes.","zh":"語言存續可以透過小型社群行動發生，而不只是官方計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase combines surprise with emotional encouragement.","zh":"這個短語結合驚喜和情感鼓舞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"grand total of","meaning":"總數","examples":[{"en":"The grand total of languages in the world might increase slightly.","zh":"世界語言的總數可能略為增加。"},{"en":"The grand total of something means the final complete number after everything is counted.","zh":"grand total of something 指把所有東西計算後得到的最終完整數目。"},{"en":"After counting books from every classroom, the grand total was 850.","zh":"點算每間課室的書本後，總數是850本。"},{"en":"A grand total can change if revived languages are counted as living languages again.","zh":"如果被復興語言再次被計作活語言，總數可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the overall final count.","zh":"這個短語指整體最終數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be minimally increased","meaning":"略為增加","examples":[{"en":"The number of languages may be minimally increased.","zh":"語言數量可能略為增加。"},{"en":"To be minimally increased means to rise by a very small amount.","zh":"be minimally increased 指只增加非常少的數量。"},{"en":"A student’s score may be minimally increased after correcting only one spelling mistake.","zh":"學生只改正一個串字錯誤後，分數可能略為增加。"},{"en":"Even a small increase can matter when it represents a language being revived.","zh":"即使增幅很小，如果代表一種語言被復興，也可能很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slight growth, not dramatic change.","zh":"這個短語描述輕微增長，而不是巨大改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"agree with the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements agree with the views of the writer.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與作者的觀點一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the views of someone means to match what that person thinks or argues.","zh":"agree with the views of someone 指與某人的想法或論點相符。"},{"en":"A reading answer agrees with the writer only if the passage clearly supports it.","zh":"只有文章清楚支持某答案時，它才與作者觀點一致。"},{"en":"Students should not choose “Yes” just because the statement sounds true in real life.","zh":"學生不應只因陳述在現實中聽起來正確就選 “Yes”。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in Yes, No, Not Given questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 Yes, No, Not Given 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相反","examples":[{"en":"A “No” answer contradicts the views of the writer.","zh":"“No” 答案與作者的觀點相反。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what that person thinks or argues.","zh":"contradict the views of someone 指說出與某人的想法或論點相反的意思。"},{"en":"If the writer says language revival is possible, a statement saying it is impossible may contradict the writer’s views.","zh":"如果作者說語言復興是可能的，而陳述說它不可能，就可能與作者觀點相反。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be based on the text, not personal belief.","zh":"矛盾必須基於文本，而不是個人信念。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear conflict with an opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述與觀點的清楚衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Students choose “Not Given” when it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"當無法判斷作者想法時，學生選擇 “Not Given”。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資料作出判斷。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions the writer’s view on a specific language, it is impossible to say what they think.","zh":"如果文章從未提到作者對某特定語言的看法，就無法判斷其想法。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students should not guess beyond the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生不應超出文章猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase signals missing evidence.","zh":"這個短語表示缺乏證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"rate at which","meaning":"……的速度","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the rate at which languages are becoming extinct.","zh":"題目問語言變得滅絕的速度。"},{"en":"The rate at which something happens means how fast it happens.","zh":"rate at which something happens 指某事發生得有多快。"},{"en":"The rate at which students learn vocabulary depends on practice, review, and use.","zh":"學生學習詞彙的速度取決於練習、複習和使用。"},{"en":"If languages disappear faster than communities can document them, action becomes urgent.","zh":"如果語言消失速度快過社群能記錄的速度，行動就變得迫切。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on speed of change.","zh":"這個短語集中於變化速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"become extinct","meaning":"變得滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Many languages are becoming extinct at an increasing rate.","zh":"許多語言正以越來越快的速度變得滅絕。"},{"en":"To become extinct means to disappear completely because no living users remain.","zh":"become extinct 指因沒有在世使用者而完全消失。"},{"en":"A tradition may become extinct if no young people learn how to practise it.","zh":"如果沒有年輕人學習如何實踐，一項傳統可能變得滅絕。"},{"en":"Languages become extinct when the final speakers die or stop using them.","zh":"當最後使用者去世或停止使用，語言就會變得滅絕。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of moving toward complete disappearance.","zh":"這個短語描述走向完全消失的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"research on the subject of","meaning":"關於……的研究","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to research on the subject of language extinction.","zh":"該陳述提到關於語言滅絕的研究。"},{"en":"Research on the subject of something means careful study about that topic.","zh":"research on the subject of something 指對某主題進行仔細研究。"},{"en":"A student may do research on the subject of teenage sleep habits for a school project.","zh":"學生可能為學校專題進行關於青少年睡眠習慣的研究。"},{"en":"Research helps people move beyond opinion by collecting evidence.","zh":"研究透過收集證據幫助人超越個人意見。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the topic being studied.","zh":"這個短語指出正在被研究的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"in order to survive","meaning":"為了生存","examples":[{"en":"In order to survive, a language needs active users.","zh":"為了生存，一種語言需要活躍使用者。"},{"en":"In order to survive means for the purpose of continuing to exist.","zh":"in order to survive 指為了繼續存在。"},{"en":"In order to survive, a small shop must keep enough regular customers.","zh":"為了生存，小店必須保住足夠固定顧客。"},{"en":"A language survives when people use it in homes, schools, work, and public life.","zh":"當人們在家庭、學校、工作和公共生活中使用語言，它就能存續。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what is necessary for continued existence.","zh":"這個短語引出繼續存在所必需的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be vulnerable to","meaning":"容易受到……影響","examples":[{"en":"Some parts of the world may be vulnerable to language extinction.","zh":"世界某些地區可能容易受到語言滅絕影響。"},{"en":"To be vulnerable to something means to be easily harmed or affected by it.","zh":"be vulnerable to something 指容易被某事傷害或影響。"},{"en":"Elderly people may be vulnerable to heat during extremely hot weather.","zh":"在極端炎熱天氣中，長者可能容易受到高溫影響。"},{"en":"Small language communities are vulnerable when young people shift to dominant languages.","zh":"當年輕人轉用主流語言，小語言社群就變得脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exposure to risk.","zh":"這個短語描述暴露於風險之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"under threat","meaning":"受到威脅","examples":[{"en":"A small community may have a language under threat.","zh":"小社群可能有一種受到威脅的語言。"},{"en":"Under threat means facing danger, pressure, or possible loss.","zh":"under threat 指面對危險、壓力或可能失去。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood park is under threat if developers plan to replace it with buildings.","zh":"如果發展商計劃把社區公園改建成樓宇，該公園就受到威脅。"},{"en":"A language is under threat when speakers are decreasing and children are not learning it.","zh":"當使用者減少且孩子沒有學習，一種語言就受到威脅。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that protection may be needed.","zh":"這個短語表示可能需要保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"major concern","meaning":"主要關注","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether saving language should be the major concern.","zh":"該陳述問拯救語言是否應成為主要關注。"},{"en":"A major concern is an important worry or priority.","zh":"major concern 指重要憂慮或優先事項。"},{"en":"For many parents, school safety is a major concern.","zh":"對許多家長而言，學校安全是主要關注。"},{"en":"Something becomes a major concern when ignoring it could cause serious damage.","zh":"當忽視某事可能造成嚴重損害，它就成為主要關注。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what people should care about most.","zh":"這個短語指出人們最應關心的是甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the list below gives","meaning":"以下列表列出","examples":[{"en":"The list below gives factors that assist language revitalisation.","zh":"以下列表列出協助語言復興的因素。"},{"en":"The list below gives means the following list provides certain information.","zh":"the list below gives 指接下來的列表提供某些資訊。"},{"en":"The list below gives the homework tasks students must complete this week.","zh":"以下列表列出學生本週必須完成的功課任務。"},{"en":"This phrase directs readers to information that follows.","zh":"這個短語指引讀者查看後面的資訊。"},{"en":"It is common in exam and textbook instructions.","zh":"它常見於考試和教科書指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"factors that are necessary to","meaning":"……所必需的因素","examples":[{"en":"The task asks for factors that are necessary to assist revitalisation.","zh":"題目要求找出協助復興所必需的因素。"},{"en":"Factors that are necessary to do something are conditions or elements required for success.","zh":"factors that are necessary to do something 指成功所需的條件或元素。"},{"en":"Sleep, practice, and feedback are factors that are necessary to improve exam writing.","zh":"睡眠、練習和回饋是改善考試寫作所必需的因素。"},{"en":"Language revival needs several necessary factors working together.","zh":"語言復興需要幾個必要因素共同發揮作用。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies essential requirements.","zh":"這個短語指出不可或缺的要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"assist the revitalisation of","meaning":"協助……的復興","examples":[{"en":"Several factors can assist the revitalisation of a language.","zh":"幾個因素可以協助一種語言的復興。"},{"en":"To assist the revitalisation of something means to help bring it back to life or stronger use.","zh":"assist the revitalisation of something 指幫助某事重新恢復生命力或更強使用。"},{"en":"Volunteers can assist the revitalisation of a community centre by organising classes and events.","zh":"義工可以透過組織課程和活動協助社區中心復興。"},{"en":"In language work, teachers, recordings, and community support can assist revival.","zh":"在語言工作中，教師、錄音和社群支持都可以協助復興。"},{"en":"This phrase describes support that helps recovery.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助恢復的支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"within a community","meaning":"在一個社群內","examples":[{"en":"Language revitalisation must happen within a community.","zh":"語言復興必須在一個社群內發生。"},{"en":"Within a community means among the people who belong to that social or local group.","zh":"within a community 指在屬於某社會或本地群體的人之間。"},{"en":"A reading habit grows within a community when parents, teachers, and students all take part.","zh":"當家長、老師和學生都參與，閱讀習慣就在社群內成長。"},{"en":"Language revival cannot depend only on outside experts because daily use happens within the community.","zh":"語言復興不能只依賴外來專家，因為日常使用發生在社群內。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the local social setting.","zh":"這個短語強調本地社會環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be mentioned by","meaning":"被……提及","examples":[{"en":"The correct factors are mentioned by the writer of the text.","zh":"正確因素由文章作者提及。"},{"en":"To be mentioned by someone means to be stated or referred to by that person.","zh":"be mentioned by someone 指被某人說出或提到。"},{"en":"An answer is correct only if the idea is mentioned by the passage, not just guessed.","zh":"只有某想法被文章提及，而不只是猜測，答案才正確。"},{"en":"Exam questions often require students to find what is actually mentioned.","zh":"考試題目常要求學生找出實際被提及的內容。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an answer with its source.","zh":"這個短語把答案與其來源連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"appropriate letters","meaning":"適當字母","examples":[{"en":"Students write the appropriate letters on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生在答題紙上寫上適當字母。"},{"en":"Appropriate letters are the correct option letters that match the answer choices.","zh":"appropriate letters 指與答案選項相符的正確字母。"},{"en":"In a matching task, students may write the appropriate letters beside each question number.","zh":"在配對題中，學生可能在每條題號旁寫上適當字母。"},{"en":"Choosing appropriate letters requires reading both the statement and the passage carefully.","zh":"選擇適當字母需要仔細閱讀陳述和文章。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"existence of related languages","meaning":"相關語言的存在","examples":[{"en":"The existence of related languages may help some language studies.","zh":"相關語言的存在可能有助某些語言研究。"},{"en":"Existence of related languages means that similar languages from the same family still exist.","zh":"existence of related languages 指同一語族中仍存在相似語言。"},{"en":"If one dialect is poorly recorded, a related dialect may help researchers understand missing patterns.","zh":"如果一種方言記錄不足，相關方言可能幫助研究者理解缺失模式。"},{"en":"Related languages can provide clues about old words, grammar, and sound changes.","zh":"相關語言可以提供舊詞、文法和語音變化的線索。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to linguistic relatives, not political allies.","zh":"這個短語指語言上的親屬，而不是政治盟友。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"indigenous population","meaning":"原住民人口","examples":[{"en":"Support from the indigenous population can help revitalisation.","zh":"原住民人口的支持可以幫助復興。"},{"en":"Indigenous population means the original or native people of a region.","zh":"indigenous population 指某地區的原有或本土民族。"},{"en":"An indigenous population may preserve place names, stories, and traditional knowledge through language.","zh":"原住民人口可能透過語言保存地名、故事和傳統知識。"},{"en":"Language revival is stronger when Indigenous people themselves support and guide it.","zh":"當原住民自己支持並引導語言復興，復興會更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a people’s historical connection with land and culture.","zh":"這個短語指一個民族與土地和文化的歷史聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"books tracing the historical development of","meaning":"追溯……歷史發展的書籍","examples":[{"en":"Books may trace the historical development of a language.","zh":"書籍可能追溯一種語言的歷史發展。"},{"en":"Books tracing the historical development of something explain how it changed over time.","zh":"books tracing the historical development of something 指解釋某事如何隨時間改變的書。"},{"en":"A book tracing the development of English may show how words entered from French and Latin.","zh":"追溯英文發展的書可能顯示詞語如何從法文和拉丁文進入英文。"},{"en":"Historical books help learners understand why a language has certain forms today.","zh":"歷史書籍幫助學習者理解語言今日為何有某些形式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes written studies of change through time.","zh":"這個短語描述研究隨時間變化的書面著作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"on-the-spot help","meaning":"現場協助","examples":[{"en":"Revitalisation may require on-the-spot help from language experts.","zh":"復興可能需要語言專家的現場協助。"},{"en":"On-the-spot help means help given directly at the place where the problem or work is happening.","zh":"on-the-spot help 指在問題或工作發生的實際地方直接提供幫助。"},{"en":"A technician gives on-the-spot help when she repairs classroom computers during a lesson.","zh":"技術員在課堂中維修課室電腦時，就是提供現場協助。"},{"en":"Language experts can provide on-site help by recording speakers and training local workers.","zh":"語言專家可以透過記錄使用者和培訓本地工作者提供現場協助。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses immediate practical help in the real location.","zh":"這個短語強調在真實地點即時提供實際幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"language experts","meaning":"語言專家","examples":[{"en":"Language experts can help communities document endangered languages.","zh":"語言專家可以幫助社群記錄瀕危語言。"},{"en":"Language experts are people with specialist knowledge of how languages work, change, and are recorded.","zh":"language experts 指對語言如何運作、變化和被記錄有專門知識的人。"},{"en":"A language expert may help create a spelling system for a language that was mostly spoken.","zh":"語言專家可能協助為主要以口語存在的語言建立拼寫系統。"},{"en":"Experts can support communities, but the community still needs to value and use the language.","zh":"專家可以支援社群，但社群仍需要重視和使用該語言。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to specialists such as linguists, teachers, or trained researchers.","zh":"這個短語指語言學家、教師或受訓研究者等專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"a range of speakers of different ages","meaning":"不同年齡層的使用者","examples":[{"en":"A range of speakers of different ages can help a language survive.","zh":"不同年齡層的使用者可以幫助語言存續。"},{"en":"A range of speakers of different ages means speakers from children to elders, not only one age group.","zh":"range of speakers of different ages 指從孩子到長者都有使用者，而不只是一個年齡層。"},{"en":"A festival feels healthier when it has helpers of different ages, from teenagers to grandparents.","zh":"當節日有從青少年到祖父母的不同年齡幫手，它會顯得更健康。"},{"en":"Languages survive better when children, parents, and elders all use them.","zh":"當孩子、父母和長者都使用語言，語言更能存續。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses intergenerational support.","zh":"這個短語強調跨世代支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"formal education procedures","meaning":"正規教育程序","examples":[{"en":"Formal education procedures may support language learning.","zh":"正規教育程序可能支援語言學習。"},{"en":"Formal education procedures are organised school-based methods, rules, and programmes for teaching.","zh":"formal education procedures 指以學校為基礎、有組織的教學方法、規則和計劃。"},{"en":"Exams, textbooks, timetables, and trained teachers are part of formal education procedures.","zh":"考試、教科書、時間表和受訓教師都是正規教育程序的一部分。"},{"en":"Formal education can help a language reach children regularly and systematically.","zh":"正規教育可以幫助語言定期而有系統地接觸孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to structured schooling, not casual home learning only.","zh":"這個短語指結構化學校教育，而不只是非正式家庭學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"common purpose","meaning":"共同目的","examples":[{"en":"A common purpose can strengthen community language use.","zh":"共同目的可以加強社群語言使用。"},{"en":"Common purpose means a shared goal that brings people together.","zh":"common purpose 指把人凝聚起來的共同目標。"},{"en":"A class works better when students have the common purpose of improving before the exam.","zh":"當學生有考試前進步這個共同目的，班級會運作得更好。"},{"en":"A language community becomes stronger when people agree that saving the language matters.","zh":"當語言社群認同拯救語言重要，它會變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unity around a goal.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞目標形成的團結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"match the languages with","meaning":"將語言與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match the languages with statements about how they were saved.","zh":"學生將語言與關於它們如何被拯救的陳述配對。"},{"en":"To match the languages with statements means to connect each language to the correct description.","zh":"match the languages with statements 指把每種語言連接到正確描述。"},{"en":"In a reading task, students may match countries with the policies described in the passage.","zh":"在閱讀題中，學生可能把國家與文章描述的政策配對。"},{"en":"Matching requires careful reading because several options may sound similar.","zh":"配對需要仔細閱讀，因為幾個選項可能聽起來相似。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common exam task.","zh":"這個短語描述常見考試任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"describe how","meaning":"描述……如何","examples":[{"en":"The statements describe how a language was saved.","zh":"這些陳述描述一種語言如何被拯救。"},{"en":"To describe how something happened means to explain the method, process, or way it happened.","zh":"describe how something happened 指解釋某事發生的方法、過程或方式。"},{"en":"A student may describe how she improved her writing by reading model essays and correcting mistakes.","zh":"學生可能描述她如何透過閱讀範文和改正錯誤改善寫作。"},{"en":"“How” questions usually ask for process, not just result.","zh":"“How” 題通常問過程，而不只是結果。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the way something was done.","zh":"這個短語集中於某事是以甚麼方式完成的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"gain increased independence","meaning":"獲得更大獨立性","examples":[{"en":"The region gained increased independence.","zh":"該地區獲得更大獨立性。"},{"en":"To gain increased independence means to obtain more control over one’s own decisions.","zh":"gain increased independence 指取得更多自行決定的控制權。"},{"en":"A teenager gains increased independence when parents allow them to travel to school alone.","zh":"當父母容許青少年獨自上學，他們就獲得更大獨立性。"},{"en":"A region with more independence can often make stronger choices about language and education.","zh":"擁有更多獨立性的地區，往往能在語言和教育上作出更有力選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rise in self-control or autonomy.","zh":"這個短語描述自我控制或自治程度上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"view the language with less prejudice","meaning":"以較少偏見看待該語言","examples":[{"en":"People were encouraged to view the language with less prejudice.","zh":"人們被鼓勵以較少偏見看待該語言。"},{"en":"To view the language with less prejudice means to see it more fairly and with fewer negative assumptions.","zh":"view the language with less prejudice 指更公平地看待某語言，減少負面假設。"},{"en":"Students may view a classmate’s accent with less prejudice after learning about their background.","zh":"學生了解同學背景後，可能以較少偏見看待其口音。"},{"en":"Less prejudice can make speakers feel safer and prouder to use their language.","zh":"較少偏見可以令使用者更安全、更自豪地使用自己的語言。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change toward fairer attitudes.","zh":"這個短語描述態度變得更公平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"language immersion programmes","meaning":"語言沉浸課程","examples":[{"en":"Language immersion programmes were set up for young children.","zh":"語言沉浸課程為幼兒設立。"},{"en":"Language immersion programmes are courses where learners are surrounded by the target language during daily activities.","zh":"language immersion programmes 指讓學習者在日常活動中置身於目標語言的課程。"},{"en":"A kindergarten immersion programme may use only the target language for songs, games, and meals.","zh":"幼稚園沉浸課程可能在歌曲、遊戲和用餐時只使用目標語言。"},{"en":"Immersion helps learners absorb a language naturally because they hear it often.","zh":"沉浸式學習幫助學習者自然吸收語言，因為他們經常聽到它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to intensive language exposure, not ordinary weekly lessons only.","zh":"這個短語指密集語言接觸，而不只是普通每週課堂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be set up for","meaning":"為……設立","examples":[{"en":"Language programmes were set up for sectors of the population.","zh":"語言計劃為人口中的某些群體設立。"},{"en":"To be set up for someone means to be created or organised for that group’s use.","zh":"be set up for someone 指為某群體使用而創立或組織。"},{"en":"A homework club may be set up for junior students who need quiet study time.","zh":"功課班可能為需要安靜自修時間的初中學生設立。"},{"en":"Programmes work better when they are designed for the needs of a specific group.","zh":"當計劃按特定群體需要設計，效果會更好。"},{"en":"This phrase links a service with its target users.","zh":"這個短語把服務與目標使用者連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"sectors of the population","meaning":"人口中的某些群體","examples":[{"en":"The programme targeted particular sectors of the population.","zh":"該計劃針對人口中的某些群體。"},{"en":"Sectors of the population are particular groups within society, such as children, parents, elders, or workers.","zh":"sectors of the population 指社會中的特定群體，例如兒童、家長、長者或工人。"},{"en":"A health campaign may target different sectors of the population with different messages.","zh":"健康宣傳可能以不同訊息針對人口中的不同群體。"},{"en":"Language programmes may focus on young children because they can become future speakers.","zh":"語言計劃可能集中於幼兒，因為他們可以成為未來使用者。"},{"en":"This phrase divides society into meaningful groups.","zh":"這個短語把社會劃分成有意義的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"merger of different varieties","meaning":"不同語言變體的合併","examples":[{"en":"A merger of different varieties of the language took place.","zh":"該語言的不同變體發生了合併。"},{"en":"A merger of different varieties means several forms or dialects were combined into one shared form.","zh":"merger of different varieties 指把幾種形式或方言合併成一種共同形式。"},{"en":"A school may create one shared handbook through a merger of different teachers’ notes.","zh":"學校可能透過合併不同老師筆記來製作一本共同手冊。"},{"en":"Merging varieties can help publishing and education, but it may also reduce local differences.","zh":"合併變體可以幫助出版和教育，但也可能減少地方差異。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unifying separate forms.","zh":"這個短語描述把分開形式統一起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"varieties of the language","meaning":"該語言的不同變體","examples":[{"en":"Different varieties of the language were merged into one written form.","zh":"該語言的不同變體被合併成一種書面形式。"},{"en":"Varieties of the language are different forms, dialects, or styles of the same language.","zh":"varieties of the language 指同一語言的不同形式、方言或風格。"},{"en":"English has varieties such as British English, American English, and Singapore English.","zh":"英文有英式英文、美式英文和新加坡英文等變體。"},{"en":"Different varieties may share a base but differ in words, sounds, or grammar.","zh":"不同變體可能共享基礎，但在詞語、語音或文法上不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes internal diversity within a language.","zh":"這個短語描述一種語言內部的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"take place","meaning":"發生；進行","examples":[{"en":"A merger of different dialects took place.","zh":"不同方言的合併發生了。"},{"en":"To take place means to happen or occur.","zh":"take place 指發生或進行。"},{"en":"The school concert will take place in the hall on Friday.","zh":"學校音樂會將於星期五在禮堂舉行。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than “happen” and is often used for events or processes.","zh":"這個短語比 “happen” 更正式，常用於事件或過程。"},{"en":"It tells readers that a specific event occurred.","zh":"它告訴讀者某個特定事件發生了。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"written samples","meaning":"書面樣本","examples":[{"en":"Written samples permitted the revitalisation of the language.","zh":"書面樣本使該語言的復興成為可能。"},{"en":"Written samples are examples of a language recorded in written form.","zh":"written samples 指以書面形式記錄下來的語言例子。"},{"en":"Old letters, word lists, and prayer books can be written samples of a language.","zh":"舊信件、詞表和祈禱書都可以是某語言的書面樣本。"},{"en":"Written samples help researchers reconstruct spelling, vocabulary, and sentence patterns.","zh":"書面樣本幫助研究者重建拼寫、詞彙和句式模式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to surviving written evidence.","zh":"這個短語指保存下來的書面證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"permit revitalisation","meaning":"使復興成為可能","examples":[{"en":"Written records can permit the revitalisation of an extinct language.","zh":"文字記錄可以使已滅絕語言的復興成為可能。"},{"en":"To permit revitalisation means to make revival possible.","zh":"permit revitalisation 指令復興成為可能。"},{"en":"Old recordings may permit revitalisation by showing how words were pronounced.","zh":"舊錄音可以透過顯示詞語如何發音，使復興成為可能。"},{"en":"Without records, people may not have enough information to rebuild a language.","zh":"沒有記錄，人們可能沒有足夠資訊重建一種語言。"},{"en":"This phrase connects available evidence with the possibility of recovery.","zh":"這個短語把現有證據與恢復的可能性連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 106 - SAVING LANGUAGE.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 107":[{"front":"strike the right note","meaning":"做得恰到好處；拿捏準確","examples":[{"en":"The title asks whether perfect pitch helps musicians strike the right note.","zh":"標題問絕對音感是否幫助音樂家做到恰到好處。"},{"en":"To strike the right note means to do or say something in a suitable, effective and well-judged way.","zh":"strike the right note 指以合適、有效和判斷得宜的方式做事或說話。"},{"en":"A teacher strikes the right note when she corrects a student firmly but kindly.","zh":"老師堅定但友善地糾正學生時，就是拿捏準確。"},{"en":"If a company apologises quickly and sincerely, it may strike the right note with angry customers.","zh":"如果公司迅速而真誠地道歉，可能會對憤怒顧客做到恰到好處。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when tone, timing and judgement are all important.","zh":"當語氣、時機和判斷都很重要時，常會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"perfect pitch","meaning":"絕對音感","examples":[{"en":"Perfect pitch is a rare musical ability.","zh":"絕對音感是一種罕見的音樂能力。"},{"en":"Perfect pitch is the ability to recognise or name a musical note without hearing another note first.","zh":"perfect pitch 指不用先聽另一個音作參照，也能認出或說出某個音符名稱的能力。"},{"en":"A child with perfect pitch may hear a doorbell and say exactly what note it sounds like.","zh":"有絕對音感的孩子可能聽到門鈴，便準確說出它像哪個音。"},{"en":"Perfect pitch can help musicians learn music quickly, but it may also make wrong notes more distracting.","zh":"絕對音感可以幫助音樂家快速學習音樂，但也可能令錯音更令人分心。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific listening ability, not simply being a good singer.","zh":"這個短語指一種特定聆聽能力，而不只是唱歌好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rare talent","meaning":"罕有天賦","examples":[{"en":"Perfect pitch is often seen as a rare talent.","zh":"絕對音感常被視為罕有天賦。"},{"en":"A rare talent is an unusual ability that only a small number of people have.","zh":"rare talent 指只有少數人擁有的不尋常能力。"},{"en":"A student who can draw realistic portraits at a young age may be seen as having a rare talent.","zh":"年紀很小就能畫出逼真人像的學生，可能被視為有罕有天賦。"},{"en":"Rare talent can attract attention, but it still needs practice to develop fully.","zh":"罕有天賦可以吸引注意，但仍需要練習才能充分發展。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests special ability, not an ordinary skill everyone has.","zh":"這個短語暗示特殊能力，而不是人人都有的普通技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be possessed solely by","meaning":"只由……擁有","examples":[{"en":"Some people wonder whether perfect pitch is possessed solely by great musicians.","zh":"有些人想知道絕對音感是否只由偉大音樂家擁有。"},{"en":"To be possessed solely by a group means to be owned or held only by that group.","zh":"be possessed solely by a group 指只由某個群體擁有。"},{"en":"Leadership ability is not possessed solely by managers; junior staff can show it too.","zh":"領導能力並非只由經理擁有；初級職員也可以展現。"},{"en":"If a skill is not possessed solely by experts, ordinary learners may also develop it.","zh":"如果某技能不是只由專家擁有，普通學習者也可能培養出來。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses exclusiveness and asks who truly has the ability.","zh":"這個短語強調排他性，並詢問誰真正擁有該能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the likes of","meaning":"像……這類人物","examples":[{"en":"The article mentions great musicians the likes of Beethoven.","zh":"文章提到像 Beethoven 這類偉大音樂家。"},{"en":"The likes of means people or things similar to the example mentioned.","zh":"the likes of 指與所提例子相似的人或事物。"},{"en":"Young footballers often admire players the likes of Messi or Mbappé.","zh":"年輕足球員常崇拜像 Messi 或 Mbappé 這類球員。"},{"en":"Mentioning the likes of famous figures can make an ability seem more impressive.","zh":"提到名人這類例子，可以令某種能力顯得更令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples from a respected or well-known group.","zh":"這個短語引入受尊敬或知名群體中的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"much sought-after","meaning":"備受追求的","examples":[{"en":"Perfect pitch is a much sought-after musical ability.","zh":"絕對音感是一種備受追求的音樂能力。"},{"en":"Much sought-after means strongly wanted by many people.","zh":"much sought-after 指受到許多人強烈追求。"},{"en":"A place in a top university programme is often much sought-after.","zh":"頂尖大學課程的學位通常備受追求。"},{"en":"When something is much sought-after, people may spend years trying to obtain it.","zh":"當某物備受追求，人們可能花多年時間努力取得。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests high demand and strong desire.","zh":"這個短語暗示高需求和強烈渴望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"musical ability","meaning":"音樂能力","examples":[{"en":"Kathryn Brown discusses this much sought-after musical ability.","zh":"Kathryn Brown 討論這種備受追求的音樂能力。"},{"en":"Musical ability is the skill to understand, perform, recognise or create music.","zh":"musical ability 指理解、演奏、辨認或創作音樂的能力。"},{"en":"A student shows musical ability when she can keep rhythm and learn melodies quickly.","zh":"學生能保持節奏並快速學會旋律時，就展現音樂能力。"},{"en":"Musical ability can develop through practice, listening and good teaching.","zh":"音樂能力可以透過練習、聆聽和良好教學發展。"},{"en":"This phrase covers many skills, not only singing or playing an instrument.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋多種技能，而不只是唱歌或演奏樂器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"uncanny ability","meaning":"不可思議的能力","examples":[{"en":"The ability to name a note without reference is uncanny.","zh":"不需參照便能說出音符名稱，是一種不可思議的能力。"},{"en":"An uncanny ability is a skill that seems strange, surprising or almost impossible to explain.","zh":"uncanny ability 指看似奇特、令人驚訝或幾乎難以解釋的技能。"},{"en":"A student may have an uncanny ability to remember every bus route in the city.","zh":"學生可能有不可思議的能力，能記住城市中每條巴士路線。"},{"en":"Such ability feels uncanny because it goes beyond what most people can do.","zh":"這種能力令人覺得不可思議，因為它超出大多數人能做到的範圍。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses admiration mixed with surprise.","zh":"這個短語表達帶有驚訝的欣賞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"if sometimes distracting","meaning":"雖然有時令人分心","examples":[{"en":"The ability is uncanny, if sometimes distracting.","zh":"這種能力不可思議，雖然有時令人分心。"},{"en":"If sometimes distracting means although it can sometimes take attention away from what matters.","zh":"if sometimes distracting 指雖然它有時會把注意力從重要事情上帶走。"},{"en":"A very sharp memory is useful, if sometimes distracting during a busy lesson.","zh":"很強的記憶力很有用，雖然在繁忙課堂中有時令人分心。"},{"en":"Perfect pitch may distract musicians when they notice every note that sounds slightly wrong.","zh":"當音樂家注意到每個略微不準的音時，絕對音感可能令人分心。"},{"en":"This phrase adds a small limitation to a generally positive idea.","zh":"這個短語為整體正面的想法加上一個小限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"name a solitary note","meaning":"說出單一音符的名稱","examples":[{"en":"Some musicians can name a solitary note without hearing any other notes.","zh":"有些音樂家不用聽任何其他音符，也能說出單一音符的名稱。"},{"en":"To name a solitary note means to identify one note by itself.","zh":"name a solitary note 指辨認單獨一個音符。"},{"en":"A pianist with perfect pitch may name a solitary note played in another room.","zh":"有絕對音感的鋼琴家可能說出另一個房間中彈出的單一音符名稱。"},{"en":"This ability is impressive because most people need another note for comparison.","zh":"這種能力令人印象深刻，因為大多數人需要另一個音作比較。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on identifying one isolated sound.","zh":"這個短語著重辨認一個孤立聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"solitary note","meaning":"單一音符","examples":[{"en":"A person with perfect pitch can identify a solitary note.","zh":"有絕對音感的人可以辨認單一音符。"},{"en":"A solitary note is one musical note heard alone, without other notes around it.","zh":"solitary note 指單獨聽到、周圍沒有其他音符的一個音符。"},{"en":"A teacher may play a solitary note on the piano and ask students to identify it.","zh":"老師可能在鋼琴上彈出一個單一音符，要求學生辨認。"},{"en":"Identifying a solitary note is harder when there is no musical context.","zh":"沒有音樂背景時，辨認單一音符較困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one isolated note, not a melody.","zh":"這個短語描述一個孤立音符，而不是旋律。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"out of the blue","meaning":"突然地；毫無提示地","examples":[{"en":"They can name a note out of the blue.","zh":"他們可以毫無提示地說出某個音符名稱。"},{"en":"Out of the blue means suddenly and without warning or preparation.","zh":"out of the blue 指突然且沒有預警或準備。"},{"en":"A friend may call you out of the blue after years of no contact.","zh":"多年沒有聯絡的朋友可能突然打電話給你。"},{"en":"If someone can name a note out of the blue, they do not need a warm-up or clue.","zh":"如果某人能毫無提示地說出音符名稱，就不需要熱身或線索。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses surprise and lack of preparation.","zh":"這個短語強調出乎意料和沒有準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"without any other notes for reference","meaning":"沒有其他音符作參照","examples":[{"en":"They can identify a note without any other notes for reference.","zh":"他們可以在沒有其他音符作參照的情況下辨認一個音。"},{"en":"Without any other notes for reference means without using another note as a comparison point.","zh":"without any other notes for reference 指不用另一個音作比較點。"},{"en":"Most singers need a starting note for reference before they can sing accurately.","zh":"大多數歌手需要一個起始音作參照，才能準確唱出音高。"},{"en":"Perfect pitch is unusual because the listener does not need another sound to compare with.","zh":"絕對音感不尋常，因為聆聽者不需要另一個聲音作比較。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why absolute pitch is different from relative pitch.","zh":"這個短語解釋絕對音感與相對音感有何不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"for reference","meaning":"作參照","examples":[{"en":"Most musicians need another note for reference.","zh":"大多數音樂家需要另一個音符作參照。"},{"en":"For reference means as a guide or comparison point.","zh":"for reference 指作為指引或比較點。"},{"en":"A student may keep a model essay for reference when learning structure.","zh":"學生學習結構時，可能保留一篇範文作參照。"},{"en":"Having something for reference helps people judge accuracy more easily.","zh":"有東西作參照可以幫助人更容易判斷準確性。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when one thing helps you understand or compare another.","zh":"當一件事幫助你理解或比較另一件事時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"prized musical talent","meaning":"珍貴的音樂天賦","examples":[{"en":"Perfect pitch is a prized musical talent.","zh":"絕對音感是一種珍貴的音樂天賦。"},{"en":"A prized musical talent is a musical ability that is highly valued.","zh":"prized musical talent 指受到高度重視的音樂能力。"},{"en":"A choir may value a singer with a prized musical talent for hearing wrong notes quickly.","zh":"合唱團可能重視一名有珍貴音樂天賦、能快速聽出錯音的歌手。"},{"en":"Talents become prized when they help people perform difficult tasks more accurately.","zh":"當天賦幫助人更準確完成困難任務，它就會變得珍貴。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests both rarity and usefulness.","zh":"這個短語暗示罕有和有用兩方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"scientific mystery","meaning":"科學謎團","examples":[{"en":"Perfect pitch remains a scientific mystery.","zh":"絕對音感仍然是一個科學謎團。"},{"en":"A scientific mystery is a question that researchers cannot yet fully explain.","zh":"scientific mystery 指研究人員尚未能完全解釋的問題。"},{"en":"Why some children learn languages unusually fast can be a scientific mystery.","zh":"為何有些孩子學語言異常快速，可以是一個科學謎團。"},{"en":"A scientific mystery encourages experiments because evidence is still incomplete.","zh":"科學謎團會推動實驗，因為證據仍不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unexplained issue in science.","zh":"這個短語描述科學中尚未解釋的議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as researchers prefer to call it","meaning":"正如研究人員較喜歡稱之為","examples":[{"en":"Many researchers prefer to call perfect pitch absolute pitch.","zh":"許多研究人員較喜歡把 perfect pitch 稱為 absolute pitch。"},{"en":"As researchers prefer to call it introduces the technical name experts choose to use.","zh":"as researchers prefer to call it 用來引入專家較喜歡使用的技術名稱。"},{"en":"Some doctors call a heart attack myocardial infarction, as specialists prefer to call it.","zh":"有些醫生把 heart attack 稱為 myocardial infarction，正如專家較喜歡稱之為的名稱。"},{"en":"Using the expert term can make discussion more precise.","zh":"使用專家術語可以令討論更精確。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that a more formal term is being introduced.","zh":"這個短語表示正在引入較正式的名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"absolute pitch","meaning":"絕對音感","examples":[{"en":"Absolute pitch allows musicians to identify notes without reference.","zh":"絕對音感讓音樂家無需參照便能辨認音符。"},{"en":"Absolute pitch is the ability to recognise a note’s exact pitch without comparing it with another note.","zh":"absolute pitch 指不用與另一個音比較，也能認出某音符確切音高的能力。"},{"en":"A musician with absolute pitch may know that a phone ringtone begins on F-sharp.","zh":"有絕對音感的音樂家可能知道手機鈴聲以 F-sharp 開始。"},{"en":"Absolute pitch can make music dictation easier because notes are heard as named sounds.","zh":"絕對音感可以令聽寫音樂較容易，因為音符會被聽成有名稱的聲音。"},{"en":"This is the more technical term for perfect pitch.","zh":"這是 perfect pitch 較技術性的說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"play pieces by ear","meaning":"憑聽覺彈奏樂曲","examples":[{"en":"Musicians with perfect pitch can often play pieces by ear.","zh":"有絕對音感的音樂家通常可以憑聽覺彈奏樂曲。"},{"en":"To play pieces by ear means to perform music after hearing it, without reading the score first.","zh":"play pieces by ear 指先聽到音樂後，不先讀樂譜也能演奏。"},{"en":"A child may hear a cartoon theme song once and then play it by ear on the piano.","zh":"孩子可能聽一次卡通主題曲後，就能在鋼琴上憑聽覺彈奏。"},{"en":"Playing by ear is easier when a musician can remember melody, rhythm and pitch accurately.","zh":"當音樂家能準確記住旋律、節奏和音高，憑聽覺彈奏就更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning music through listening rather than notation.","zh":"這個短語描述透過聆聽而不是樂譜學音樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"by ear","meaning":"憑聽覺","examples":[{"en":"Some musicians can learn music by ear.","zh":"有些音樂家可以憑聽覺學習音樂。"},{"en":"By ear means by listening rather than by reading written music or instructions.","zh":"by ear 指透過聆聽，而不是讀樂譜或書面指示。"},{"en":"A guitarist may learn a pop song by ear after replaying the chorus several times.","zh":"結他手可能重播副歌幾次後，憑聽覺學會一首流行歌。"},{"en":"Learning by ear develops listening skills because the player must notice small sound differences.","zh":"憑聽覺學習會培養聆聽能力，因為演奏者必須注意細微聲音差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in music, but it can also mean judging sound without formal notes.","zh":"這個短語常用於音樂，但也可表示不用正式記譜而靠聽覺判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"transcribe music","meaning":"記錄樂譜；聽寫音樂","examples":[{"en":"Many musicians with perfect pitch can transcribe music brilliantly.","zh":"許多有絕對音感的音樂家能出色地聽寫音樂。"},{"en":"To transcribe music means to write down music after hearing it.","zh":"transcribe music 指聽到音樂後把它寫成樂譜。"},{"en":"A music student may transcribe a short melody from a recording as homework.","zh":"音樂學生可能把錄音中的短旋律聽寫成樂譜作功課。"},{"en":"Transcribing music is easier when the listener can identify pitch, rhythm and harmony accurately.","zh":"當聆聽者能準確辨認音高、節奏和和聲，聽寫音樂會更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to turning sound into written notation.","zh":"這個短語指把聲音轉化為書面記譜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"brilliantly","meaning":"出色地","examples":[{"en":"Some musicians can transcribe music brilliantly.","zh":"有些音樂家可以出色地聽寫音樂。"},{"en":"Brilliantly means extremely well or with great skill.","zh":"brilliantly 指非常好或以高超技巧完成。"},{"en":"A student may explain a difficult grammar point brilliantly with one simple example.","zh":"學生可能用一個簡單例子出色地解釋困難文法點。"},{"en":"When something is done brilliantly, people notice both accuracy and skill.","zh":"當某事被出色地完成，人們會注意到準確性和技巧。"},{"en":"This word gives strong praise for performance.","zh":"這個詞對表現給予高度讚賞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"perceive the position of","meaning":"感知……的位置","examples":[{"en":"They perceive the position of a note very clearly.","zh":"他們非常清楚地感知一個音符的位置。"},{"en":"To perceive the position of something means to sense or understand where it belongs.","zh":"perceive the position of something 指感覺或理解某物屬於哪個位置。"},{"en":"A good driver can perceive the position of nearby cars before changing lanes.","zh":"好司機在轉線前能感知附近車輛的位置。"},{"en":"Musicians with absolute pitch perceive where a note sits in the musical system without comparison.","zh":"有絕對音感的音樂家不用比較，也能感知音符在音樂系統中的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental recognition, not only physical seeing.","zh":"這個短語描述心理辨認，而不只是實際看見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"musical stave","meaning":"五線譜","examples":[{"en":"They perceive the position of a note in the musical stave.","zh":"他們感知音符在五線譜中的位置。"},{"en":"A musical stave is the set of five lines on which musical notes are written.","zh":"musical stave 指書寫音符的五條線。"},{"en":"Beginners learn to read the musical stave before playing simple songs from sheet music.","zh":"初學者在按樂譜演奏簡單歌曲前，會學習閱讀五線譜。"},{"en":"Knowing the stave helps musicians connect written notes with sounds.","zh":"認識五線譜幫助音樂家把書面音符與聲音連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the visual system used in written music.","zh":"這個短語指書面音樂中使用的視覺系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pitch","meaning":"音高","examples":[{"en":"The pitch of a note is its position in the musical stave.","zh":"一個音符的音高就是它在五線譜中的位置。"},{"en":"Pitch is how high or low a sound is.","zh":"pitch 指聲音有多高或多低。"},{"en":"A whistle usually has a higher pitch than a large drum.","zh":"哨子通常比大鼓有更高音高。"},{"en":"Changing pitch can change the melody and sometimes the meaning of spoken words.","zh":"改變音高可以改變旋律，有時也會改變說話詞語的意思。"},{"en":"This word is central to music and speech because it describes sound height.","zh":"這個詞對音樂和語音都很重要，因為它描述聲音高度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as clearly as","meaning":"像……一樣清楚","examples":[{"en":"They perceive pitch as clearly as the fact that they heard it.","zh":"他們感知音高，就像知道自己聽到它一樣清楚。"},{"en":"As clearly as means with the same level of certainty or obviousness.","zh":"as clearly as 指具有同樣程度的確定性或明顯性。"},{"en":"A student may remember a teacher’s warning as clearly as the test date itself.","zh":"學生可能記得老師的提醒，就像記得測驗日期本身一樣清楚。"},{"en":"If something is perceived as clearly as a sound, it feels immediate and unmistakable.","zh":"如果某事被感知得像聲音一樣清楚，它會感覺即時且不容誤認。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two levels of clarity.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種清晰程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"go hand in hand","meaning":"密切相關；相輔相成","examples":[{"en":"Hearing and naming the pitch go hand in hand.","zh":"聽到音高和說出其名稱密切相關。"},{"en":"If two things go hand in hand, they are closely connected and often happen together.","zh":"如果兩件事 go hand in hand，它們密切相關並常同時發生。"},{"en":"Good sleep and better concentration often go hand in hand for students.","zh":"對學生來說，良好睡眠和更好專注力常相輔相成。"},{"en":"In perfect pitch, hearing a note and naming it may happen almost at the same time.","zh":"在絕對音感中，聽到音符和說出名稱可能幾乎同時發生。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a close relationship between two things.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩件事之間的密切關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"by contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"By contrast, most musicians follow the relationship between notes.","zh":"相比之下，大多數音樂家追蹤音符之間的關係。"},{"en":"By contrast introduces a difference from what has just been described.","zh":"by contrast 用來引入與剛描述內容不同的情況。"},{"en":"Some students learn best through reading; by contrast, others need diagrams and examples.","zh":"有些學生最適合透過閱讀學習；相比之下，另一些學生需要圖表和例子。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers see two ideas side by side.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者並列看見兩個想法。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing absolute pitch with relative pitch.","zh":"比較絕對音感和相對音感時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the relationship between","meaning":"……之間的關係","examples":[{"en":"Most musicians follow the relationship between notes.","zh":"大多數音樂家追蹤音符之間的關係。"},{"en":"The relationship between two things is how they are connected or compared.","zh":"the relationship between two things 指兩者如何連接或比較。"},{"en":"Students study the relationship between sleep and exam performance.","zh":"學生研究睡眠與考試表現之間的關係。"},{"en":"In music, the relationship between notes helps listeners recognise melodies.","zh":"在音樂中，音符之間的關係幫助聆聽者辨認旋律。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on connection, not isolated items.","zh":"這個短語著重連繫，而不是孤立事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a certain number of tones apart","meaning":"相隔某個音程","examples":[{"en":"They may recognise two notes as being a certain number of tones apart.","zh":"他們可能辨認出兩個音相隔某個音程。"},{"en":"A certain number of tones apart means separated by a particular musical distance.","zh":"a certain number of tones apart 指相隔某個特定音樂距離。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students whether two notes are one tone or two tones apart.","zh":"老師可能問學生兩個音是相隔一個全音還是兩個全音。"},{"en":"Recognising distance between notes helps musicians sing or play melodies accurately.","zh":"辨認音符之間的距離幫助音樂家準確唱出或演奏旋律。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relative distance in pitch.","zh":"這個短語描述音高上的相對距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"tones apart","meaning":"相隔若干音","examples":[{"en":"Two notes may be several tones apart.","zh":"兩個音符可能相隔若干音。"},{"en":"Tones apart means separated by a number of steps in pitch.","zh":"tones apart 指在音高上相隔若干步。"},{"en":"In singing class, students practise hearing whether two notes are close together or several tones apart.","zh":"在歌唱課中，學生練習聽出兩個音是接近還是相隔若干音。"},{"en":"Notes that are many tones apart can sound very different in height.","zh":"相隔很多音的音符在高低上可以聽起來很不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to describe musical distance.","zh":"這個短語用來描述音樂距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"relative pitch","meaning":"相對音感","examples":[{"en":"Most musicians rely on relative pitch.","zh":"大多數音樂家依靠相對音感。"},{"en":"Relative pitch is the ability to understand notes by comparing them with other notes.","zh":"relative pitch 指透過與其他音比較來理解音符的能力。"},{"en":"A singer uses relative pitch when she hears one starting note and then finds the rest of the melody.","zh":"歌手聽到一個起始音後，再找出旋律其他部分，就是使用相對音感。"},{"en":"Relative pitch is useful because music often depends on relationships between sounds.","zh":"相對音感很有用，因為音樂常取決於聲音之間的關係。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with absolute pitch, which does not need comparison.","zh":"這個短語與不需要比較的絕對音感形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"useful, but much less mysterious","meaning":"有用，但神秘感低得多","examples":[{"en":"Relative pitch is useful, but much less mysterious.","zh":"相對音感有用，但神秘感低得多。"},{"en":"Useful, but much less mysterious means helpful, though easier to understand and explain.","zh":"useful, but much less mysterious 指有幫助，但較容易理解和解釋。"},{"en":"A calculator is useful, but much less mysterious than a human brain.","zh":"計算機有用，但比人腦神秘感低得多。"},{"en":"Relative pitch seems less mysterious because it depends on comparison, which many musicians can learn.","zh":"相對音感看起來較不神秘，因為它依賴比較，而許多音樂家都能學會。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts practical value with scientific mystery.","zh":"這個短語把實用價值與科學神秘感作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"for centuries","meaning":"數百年來","examples":[{"en":"For centuries, absolute pitch has been associated with musical elites.","zh":"數百年來，絕對音感一直與音樂精英相關。"},{"en":"For centuries means for hundreds of years.","zh":"for centuries 指長達數百年。"},{"en":"For centuries, families have passed down local recipes through daily cooking.","zh":"數百年來，家庭透過日常烹飪傳承本地食譜。"},{"en":"If an idea lasts for centuries, it can become deeply rooted in culture.","zh":"如果一個想法延續數百年，它可能深深植根於文化。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a long historical time frame.","zh":"這個短語給出長歷史時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be thought of as","meaning":"被視為","examples":[{"en":"Absolute pitch has long been thought of as a rare gift.","zh":"絕對音感長久以來被視為罕有天賦。"},{"en":"To be thought of as something means to be regarded or understood in that way.","zh":"be thought of as something 指被看作或理解為某事物。"},{"en":"Good handwriting was once thought of as an important sign of education.","zh":"良好書寫字體曾被視為教育程度的重要象徵。"},{"en":"How something is thought of may change when new evidence appears.","zh":"當新證據出現，人們如何看待某事可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes common belief or perception.","zh":"這個短語描述常見信念或看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the preserve of","meaning":"……的專屬領域","examples":[{"en":"Absolute pitch has been thought of as the preserve of the musical elite.","zh":"絕對音感一直被視為音樂精英的專屬領域。"},{"en":"The preserve of a group means something believed to belong mainly or only to that group.","zh":"the preserve of a group 指被認為主要或只屬於某群體的事物。"},{"en":"Higher education was once seen as the preserve of wealthy families.","zh":"高等教育曾被視為富裕家庭的專屬領域。"},{"en":"If a skill is seen as the preserve of experts, ordinary learners may not try to develop it.","zh":"如果某技能被視為專家的專屬領域，普通學習者可能不會嘗試培養。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests exclusiveness or restricted access.","zh":"這個短語暗示排他性或受限制的接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"musical elite","meaning":"音樂精英","examples":[{"en":"Perfect pitch was once considered the preserve of the musical elite.","zh":"絕對音感曾被視為音樂精英的專屬領域。"},{"en":"The musical elite are highly skilled or highly respected people in the music world.","zh":"musical elite 指音樂界中技術高超或備受尊敬的人。"},{"en":"Young performers may dream of joining the musical elite by entering a famous conservatory.","zh":"年輕表演者可能夢想進入著名音樂學院，加入音樂精英。"},{"en":"A talent associated with the musical elite may seem unreachable to ordinary learners.","zh":"與音樂精英相關的天賦，對普通學習者來說可能顯得遙不可及。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to top-level musicians or music professionals.","zh":"這個短語指頂尖音樂家或音樂專業人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"estimates suggest that","meaning":"估計顯示","examples":[{"en":"Some estimates suggest that fewer than 1 in 2,000 people possess perfect pitch.","zh":"有些估計顯示，少於每 2,000 人中 1 人擁有絕對音感。"},{"en":"Estimates suggest that means approximate calculations or informed guesses point to a conclusion.","zh":"estimates suggest that 指約略計算或有根據推測指向某結論。"},{"en":"Estimates suggest that many students spend more time online than reading printed books.","zh":"估計顯示，許多學生花在網上的時間比閱讀紙本書多。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when exact numbers are uncertain but evidence gives a likely picture.","zh":"當確切數字不確定但證據提供可能圖像時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It introduces cautious numerical information.","zh":"它引入謹慎的數字資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fewer than","meaning":"少於","examples":[{"en":"Fewer than 1 in 2,000 people may possess absolute pitch.","zh":"少於每 2,000 人中 1 人可能擁有絕對音感。"},{"en":"Fewer than means a smaller number than the amount mentioned.","zh":"fewer than 指數量少於所提及的數字。"},{"en":"Fewer than ten students joined the music club this year.","zh":"今年少於十名學生加入音樂學會。"},{"en":"This phrase is used with countable things, such as people, notes or lessons.","zh":"這個短語用於可數事物，例如人、音符或課堂。"},{"en":"It shows that the real number is below a stated limit.","zh":"它顯示真實數量低於某個限度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"possess it","meaning":"擁有它","examples":[{"en":"Only a small number of people are thought to possess it.","zh":"人們認為只有少數人擁有它。"},{"en":"To possess it means to have that ability, quality or object.","zh":"possess it 指擁有那種能力、特質或物件。"},{"en":"A student may possess a strong memory but still need good study habits.","zh":"學生可能擁有很強記憶力，但仍需要良好學習習慣。"},{"en":"Possessing a talent does not remove the need for practice.","zh":"擁有天賦不代表不需要練習。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than simply saying “have it”.","zh":"這個短語比單純說 “have it” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a growing number of","meaning":"越來越多的……","examples":[{"en":"A growing number of studies suggest that absolute pitch may be more common.","zh":"越來越多研究顯示，絕對音感可能更普遍。"},{"en":"A growing number of means more and more over time.","zh":"a growing number of 指隨時間變得越來越多。"},{"en":"A growing number of students use online dictionaries when writing essays.","zh":"越來越多學生寫作文時使用網上字典。"},{"en":"When a growing number of studies support an idea, researchers take it more seriously.","zh":"當越來越多研究支持某想法，研究人員會更認真看待它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an increasing trend.","zh":"這個短語顯示增長趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"speech experiments","meaning":"語音實驗","examples":[{"en":"Speech experiments have provided evidence about absolute pitch.","zh":"語音實驗提供了關於絕對音感的證據。"},{"en":"Speech experiments are studies that test how people produce, hear or use spoken sounds.","zh":"speech experiments 指測試人們如何發出、聽到或使用語音的研究。"},{"en":"A researcher may use speech experiments to see how children hear tones in Mandarin.","zh":"研究人員可能用語音實驗看看孩子如何聽普通話聲調。"},{"en":"Speech experiments can reveal sound abilities that ordinary conversation hides.","zh":"語音實驗可以揭示普通對話中隱藏的聲音能力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to controlled studies of spoken language.","zh":"這個短語指對口語聲音的受控研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"brain scans","meaning":"腦部掃描","examples":[{"en":"Brain scans have also contributed to research on absolute pitch.","zh":"腦部掃描也對絕對音感研究有所貢獻。"},{"en":"Brain scans are medical images that show the structure or activity of the brain.","zh":"brain scans 指顯示大腦結構或活動的醫學影像。"},{"en":"Doctors may use brain scans to check whether an injury has affected memory or movement.","zh":"醫生可能使用腦部掃描檢查受傷是否影響記憶或活動。"},{"en":"Brain scans help researchers connect musical ability with brain patterns.","zh":"腦部掃描幫助研究人員把音樂能力與大腦模式連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to imaging methods used to study the brain.","zh":"這個短語指用於研究大腦的影像方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"suggest that","meaning":"顯示；指出","examples":[{"en":"Recent studies suggest that absolute pitch may be more common than previously thought.","zh":"近期研究顯示，絕對音感可能比以往所想更普遍。"},{"en":"Suggest that means show or indicate something may be true.","zh":"suggest that 指顯示或指出某事可能是真的。"},{"en":"Several late assignments suggest that a student may be struggling with time management.","zh":"多份遲交功課顯示學生可能在時間管理上遇到困難。"},{"en":"Research can suggest a conclusion before it proves it completely.","zh":"研究可以在完全證明前指出一個結論。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence points toward an idea cautiously.","zh":"當證據謹慎地指向某想法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a knack for","meaning":"……的本領；……的天賦","examples":[{"en":"A knack for absolute pitch may be more common than expected.","zh":"絕對音感的本領可能比預期更普遍。"},{"en":"A knack for something is a natural or easily developed ability to do it well.","zh":"a knack for something 指自然擁有或容易發展出做好某事的能力。"},{"en":"A student with a knack for languages may remember new phrases after hearing them once.","zh":"有語言天賦的學生可能聽一次就記住新短語。"},{"en":"A knack can become stronger when it is noticed early and practised regularly.","zh":"如果天賦被早早注意並定期練習，它可以變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an ability that feels natural rather than forced.","zh":"這個短語暗示一種感覺自然、不勉強的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"far more common","meaning":"普遍得多","examples":[{"en":"Absolute pitch may be far more common than previously thought.","zh":"絕對音感可能比以往所想普遍得多。"},{"en":"Far more common means much more frequent than people believed before.","zh":"far more common 指比人們以前相信的出現頻率高得多。"},{"en":"Food allergies are far more common in some schools than teachers expected.","zh":"在某些學校，食物過敏比老師預期普遍得多。"},{"en":"If an ability is far more common, researchers may need to change old assumptions.","zh":"如果某能力普遍得多，研究人員可能需要改變舊假設。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a large difference in frequency.","zh":"這個短語強調頻率上的巨大差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"more varied than previously thought","meaning":"比以往所想更多樣化","examples":[{"en":"The ability may be more varied than previously thought.","zh":"這種能力可能比以往所想更多樣化。"},{"en":"More varied than previously thought means it appears in more forms or levels than people once believed.","zh":"more varied than previously thought 指它以比人們以前相信更多的形式或程度出現。"},{"en":"Student learning styles may be more varied than previously thought, so one method cannot help everyone.","zh":"學生學習方式可能比以往所想更多樣化，因此一種方法不能幫助所有人。"},{"en":"If perfect pitch is more varied, researchers should not treat it as one simple ability.","zh":"如果絕對音感更多樣化，研究人員就不應把它視為一種簡單能力。"},{"en":"This phrase challenges an older, narrower view.","zh":"這個短語挑戰較舊、較狹窄的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"previously thought","meaning":"以往所想","examples":[{"en":"The skill may be more common than previously thought.","zh":"這項技能可能比以往所想更普遍。"},{"en":"Previously thought means believed before new evidence or a new understanding appeared.","zh":"previously thought 指在新證據或新理解出現之前所相信的。"},{"en":"The exam was easier than previously thought after students saw the sample questions.","zh":"學生看到樣本題後，發現考試比以往所想容易。"},{"en":"New research can change what people previously thought about learning and talent.","zh":"新研究可以改變人們以往對學習和天賦的看法。"},{"en":"This phrase compares old belief with newer information.","zh":"這個短語比較舊信念與新資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"music theorist","meaning":"音樂理論家","examples":[{"en":"Marvin is a music theorist at the University of Rochester.","zh":"Marvin 是羅徹斯特大學的音樂理論家。"},{"en":"A music theorist studies how music is structured, including harmony, melody, rhythm and form.","zh":"music theorist 指研究音樂結構的人，包括和聲、旋律、節奏和形式。"},{"en":"A music theorist may explain why a song sounds sad even when the lyrics are simple.","zh":"音樂理論家可能解釋為何一首歌即使歌詞簡單，也聽起來悲傷。"},{"en":"Music theorists help performers understand patterns behind what they play or hear.","zh":"音樂理論家幫助演奏者理解他們演奏或聽到內容背後的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specialist who studies the logic of music.","zh":"這個短語命名研究音樂邏輯的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"all-or-nothing feature","meaning":"非有即無的特徵","examples":[{"en":"Absolute pitch is not an all-or-nothing feature.","zh":"絕對音感不是非有即無的特徵。"},{"en":"An all-or-nothing feature is something people either completely have or completely lack.","zh":"all-or-nothing feature 指某物要麼完全擁有，要麼完全沒有。"},{"en":"Confidence is not an all-or-nothing feature; a student may feel confident in speaking but not writing.","zh":"自信不是非有即無的特徵；學生可能對說話有信心，但對寫作沒有信心。"},{"en":"If absolute pitch is not all-or-nothing, people may have it in different degrees.","zh":"如果絕對音感不是非有即無，人們可能以不同程度擁有它。"},{"en":"This phrase challenges the idea of a simple yes-or-no ability.","zh":"這個短語挑戰能力只有有或沒有的簡單想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"claim that","meaning":"聲稱","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers claim that everyone could develop the skill.","zh":"有些研究人員聲稱人人都可以培養這項技能。"},{"en":"To claim that means to state that something is true, especially when others may question it.","zh":"claim that 指表示某事是真，尤其是在他人可能質疑時。"},{"en":"A student may claim that online lessons help him focus better than classroom lessons.","zh":"學生可能聲稱網課比實體課更能幫助他集中。"},{"en":"A claim becomes stronger when it is supported by evidence.","zh":"當聲稱有證據支持，就會變得更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a stated position, not always a proven fact.","zh":"這個短語引入一個被提出的立場，不一定是已證明的事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"develop the skill","meaning":"培養這項技能","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers believe that we could all develop the skill.","zh":"有些研究人員相信我們都可以培養這項技能。"},{"en":"To develop the skill means to improve an ability through time, practice or training.","zh":"develop the skill 指透過時間、練習或訓練提升某種能力。"},{"en":"A student can develop the skill of summarising by reading short articles every day.","zh":"學生可以透過每天閱讀短文來培養摘要技能。"},{"en":"Early practice may help children develop musical skills before habits become fixed.","zh":"早期練習可能幫助孩子在習慣固定前培養音樂技能。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that ability can grow rather than remain unchanged.","zh":"這個短語顯示能力可以成長，而不是維持不變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"regardless of","meaning":"不論；不管","examples":[{"en":"People may develop absolute pitch regardless of musical talent.","zh":"人們可能不論音樂天賦如何，都能培養絕對音感。"},{"en":"Regardless of means without being affected by a particular factor.","zh":"regardless of 指不受某特定因素影響。"},{"en":"Students should receive respect regardless of their exam results.","zh":"學生不論考試成績如何，都應受到尊重。"},{"en":"If a rule applies regardless of age, it applies to children and adults alike.","zh":"如果規則不論年齡都適用，它就同時適用於兒童和成人。"},{"en":"This phrase means one condition does not change the outcome.","zh":"這個短語表示某條件不改變結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"musical talent","meaning":"音樂天賦","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers say absolute pitch may not depend entirely on musical talent.","zh":"有些研究人員說，絕對音感可能不完全取決於音樂天賦。"},{"en":"Musical talent is a natural or developed ability in music.","zh":"musical talent 指音樂方面的天生或後天發展能力。"},{"en":"A child with musical talent may remember melodies easily and enjoy rhythm games.","zh":"有音樂天賦的孩子可能容易記住旋律並喜歡節奏遊戲。"},{"en":"Musical talent can help, but training and environment may also shape ability.","zh":"音樂天賦可以有幫助，但訓練和環境也可能塑造能力。"},{"en":"This phrase should not be confused with general intelligence.","zh":"這個短語不應與一般智力混淆。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"finally settle","meaning":"最終解決","examples":[{"en":"The research may finally settle a long debate.","zh":"這項研究可能最終解決一場長期爭論。"},{"en":"To finally settle a debate means to provide enough evidence to end disagreement.","zh":"finally settle a debate 指提供足夠證據來結束分歧。"},{"en":"A clear video replay may finally settle an argument about whether a goal was scored.","zh":"清晰的重播影片可能最終解決是否入球的爭論。"},{"en":"Research can settle a debate when it answers the key question directly.","zh":"當研究直接回答關鍵問題，它就可以解決爭論。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an issue may at last be resolved.","zh":"這個短語暗示議題可能終於得到解決。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"decades-old debate","meaning":"數十年來的爭論","examples":[{"en":"The research may settle a decades-old debate about absolute pitch.","zh":"這項研究可能解決關於絕對音感的數十年來的爭論。"},{"en":"A decades-old debate is an argument or disagreement that has lasted for many decades.","zh":"decades-old debate 指持續了數十年的爭論或分歧。"},{"en":"Education experts may revisit a decades-old debate about exams and creativity.","zh":"教育專家可能重新討論關於考試和創意的數十年來爭論。"},{"en":"A debate can last for decades when evidence is difficult to collect.","zh":"當證據難以收集，爭論可以持續數十年。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the disagreement is long-standing.","zh":"這個短語強調分歧存在已久。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"depend on","meaning":"取決於","examples":[{"en":"Researchers debate whether absolute pitch depends on genes or lessons.","zh":"研究人員爭論絕對音感取決於基因還是課堂。"},{"en":"To depend on something means to be affected or determined by it.","zh":"depend on something 指受某事影響或由某事決定。"},{"en":"A student’s progress may depend on regular practice and clear feedback.","zh":"學生進步可能取決於定期練習和清楚回饋。"},{"en":"If an ability depends on early lessons, children who start earlier may have an advantage.","zh":"如果某能力取決於早期課堂，較早開始的孩子可能有優勢。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what factor controls or influences an outcome.","zh":"這個短語顯示哪個因素控制或影響結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"melodious genes","meaning":"音樂基因","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe absolute pitch may depend on melodious genes.","zh":"有些人相信絕對音感可能取決於音樂基因。"},{"en":"Melodious genes is a playful phrase meaning genes that may support musical ability.","zh":"melodious genes 是較生動的說法，指可能支持音樂能力的基因。"},{"en":"A family with many singers may jokingly say their children have melodious genes.","zh":"一個有很多歌手的家庭可能開玩笑說孩子有音樂基因。"},{"en":"If genes play a role, some children may be naturally more ready to develop pitch skills.","zh":"如果基因有作用，有些孩子可能天生更容易發展音高技能。"},{"en":"This phrase is not a formal scientific term; it is a vivid way to discuss inheritance.","zh":"這個短語不是正式科學術語；它是討論遺傳的生動說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"early music lessons","meaning":"早期音樂課","examples":[{"en":"Others believe early music lessons are crucial.","zh":"另一些人相信早期音樂課至關重要。"},{"en":"Early music lessons are music classes taken in childhood, especially before habits and hearing patterns are fixed.","zh":"early music lessons 指童年時上的音樂課，尤其是在習慣和聽覺模式固定前。"},{"en":"Parents may enrol a child in early music lessons to build listening and rhythm skills.","zh":"家長可能為孩子報讀早期音樂課，以建立聆聽和節奏能力。"},{"en":"Early lessons may matter because young brains can learn sound categories quickly.","zh":"早期課堂可能重要，因為年幼大腦能快速學習聲音類別。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on training received at a young age.","zh":"這個短語著重年幼時接受的訓練。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"music psychologist","meaning":"音樂心理學家","examples":[{"en":"Diana Deutsch is a music psychologist at the University of California.","zh":"Diana Deutsch 是加州大學的音樂心理學家。"},{"en":"A music psychologist studies how people hear, understand, remember and respond to music.","zh":"music psychologist 指研究人們如何聽、理解、記住和回應音樂的心理學家。"},{"en":"A music psychologist may test whether songs affect memory or mood.","zh":"音樂心理學家可能測試歌曲是否影響記憶或情緒。"},{"en":"Music psychology connects musical behaviour with the mind and brain.","zh":"音樂心理學把音樂行為與心理和大腦連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specialist in the psychology of music.","zh":"這個短語命名音樂心理學方面的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"leading voice","meaning":"主要代表人物；權威聲音","examples":[{"en":"Diana Deutsch is a leading voice in the debate on absolute pitch.","zh":"Diana Deutsch 是絕對音感爭論中的主要代表人物。"},{"en":"A leading voice is an influential person whose opinions are respected in a discussion.","zh":"leading voice 指在討論中具影響力、其意見受尊重的人。"},{"en":"A doctor may become a leading voice in public health after years of clear research.","zh":"醫生經多年清晰研究後，可能成為公共健康中的權威聲音。"},{"en":"Leading voices can shape debates because other people listen to their evidence and arguments.","zh":"主要代表人物可以塑造辯論，因為其他人會聽取其證據和論點。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to influence, not literal loudness.","zh":"這個短語指影響力，而不是字面上的聲音大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at the Acoustical Society of America meeting","meaning":"在美國聲學學會會議上","examples":[{"en":"Deutsch reported her study at the Acoustical Society of America meeting.","zh":"Deutsch 在美國聲學學會會議上發表她的研究。"},{"en":"At the Acoustical Society of America meeting means during a formal conference about sound research.","zh":"at the Acoustical Society of America meeting 指在關於聲音研究的正式會議期間。"},{"en":"A scientist may present new findings at an academic meeting before publishing a full paper.","zh":"科學家可能在學術會議上發表新發現，之後才出版完整論文。"},{"en":"Presenting at a specialist meeting allows other experts to question the research.","zh":"在專業會議上發表，讓其他專家可以質疑研究。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the professional setting where the study was reported.","zh":"這個短語指出該研究發表的專業場合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reported a study","meaning":"發表一項研究","examples":[{"en":"Deutsch reported a study about tone-language speakers.","zh":"Deutsch 發表一項關於聲調語言說話者的研究。"},{"en":"To report a study means to present or describe research findings.","zh":"report a study 指提出或描述研究發現。"},{"en":"A teacher may report a study showing that sleep affects memory.","zh":"老師可能發表一項顯示睡眠影響記憶的研究。"},{"en":"Reporting a study allows others to examine its method, data and conclusions.","zh":"發表研究讓其他人審視其方法、數據和結論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes communicating research results.","zh":"這個短語描述傳達研究結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have the potential to","meaning":"有潛力去……","examples":[{"en":"Deutsch suggests that we all have the potential to acquire absolute pitch.","zh":"Deutsch 指出，我們都有潛力獲得絕對音感。"},{"en":"To have the potential to do something means to be able to develop that ability in the right conditions.","zh":"have the potential to do something 指在合適條件下能發展出某能力。"},{"en":"A quiet student may have the potential to become a strong speaker with practice.","zh":"安靜的學生透過練習，可能有潛力成為出色演說者。"},{"en":"Potential does not guarantee success; it needs opportunity, training and effort.","zh":"潛力不保證成功；它需要機會、訓練和努力。"},{"en":"This phrase points to possible future ability.","zh":"這個短語指向未來可能的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"acquire absolute pitch","meaning":"獲得絕對音感","examples":[{"en":"Speakers of tone languages may acquire absolute pitch naturally.","zh":"聲調語言說話者可能自然獲得絕對音感。"},{"en":"To acquire absolute pitch means to gain the ability to recognise exact notes without comparison.","zh":"acquire absolute pitch 指獲得不用比較也能認出確切音符的能力。"},{"en":"A child may acquire pitch sensitivity through early music lessons and careful listening.","zh":"孩子可能透過早期音樂課和仔細聆聽獲得音高敏感度。"},{"en":"If absolute pitch can be acquired, it may not be only an inborn gift.","zh":"如果絕對音感可以被獲得，它可能不只是天生禮物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gaining the ability over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間取得這種能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tone languages","meaning":"聲調語言","examples":[{"en":"Speakers of tone languages use pitch to distinguish meaning.","zh":"聲調語言說話者使用音高來區分意思。"},{"en":"Tone languages are languages in which changes in pitch can change the meaning of words.","zh":"tone languages 指音高改變可以改變詞義的語言。"},{"en":"Mandarin and Vietnamese are examples of tone languages.","zh":"普通話和越南語都是聲調語言的例子。"},{"en":"Children who grow up with tone languages practise hearing pitch differences every day.","zh":"在聲調語言環境中成長的孩子每天都練習聽音高差異。"},{"en":"This phrase connects language meaning with voice pitch.","zh":"這個短語把語言意思與聲線音高連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a third of","meaning":"三分之一","examples":[{"en":"A third of the world’s population speaks tone languages.","zh":"世界人口三分之一說聲調語言。"},{"en":"A third of means one out of three equal parts.","zh":"a third of 指三等份中的一份。"},{"en":"A third of the class chose music as their favourite subject.","zh":"班中三分之一學生選音樂為最喜歡的科目。"},{"en":"Saying a third of a group shows a large minority, not just a few people.","zh":"說某群體的三分之一表示相當大的少數，而不是只有少數人。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to express proportion.","zh":"這個短語用來表達比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"chiefly","meaning":"主要","examples":[{"en":"Tone languages are spoken chiefly by people in Asia and Africa.","zh":"聲調語言主要由亞洲和非洲的人使用。"},{"en":"Chiefly means mainly or mostly.","zh":"chiefly 指主要地或大多數地。"},{"en":"This library is used chiefly by students who need a quiet place to revise.","zh":"這間圖書館主要由需要安靜地方溫習的學生使用。"},{"en":"If something happens chiefly in one region, that region is the main focus.","zh":"如果某事主要發生在一個地區，那個地區就是主要焦點。"},{"en":"This word points to the most important or common part.","zh":"這個詞指向最重要或最常見的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"depending on","meaning":"視乎……而定","examples":[{"en":"A word’s meaning can vary depending on pitch.","zh":"一個詞的意思可以視乎音高而變化。"},{"en":"Depending on means changing according to a particular condition or factor.","zh":"depending on 指根據某條件或因素而改變。"},{"en":"A bus journey may take 20 or 40 minutes depending on traffic.","zh":"巴士旅程可能需 20 或 40 分鐘，視乎交通而定。"},{"en":"In tone languages, meaning changes depending on how the speaker’s voice rises or falls.","zh":"在聲調語言中，意思會視乎說話者聲線如何升降而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one thing is controlled by another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一件事受另一件事控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a speaker uses","meaning":"說話者使用的……","examples":[{"en":"In tone languages, meaning can depend on the pitch a speaker uses.","zh":"在聲調語言中，意思可以取決於說話者使用的音高。"},{"en":"The pitch a speaker uses is the high or low level of the person’s voice when saying a word.","zh":"the pitch a speaker uses 指某人說詞語時聲音的高低。"},{"en":"In Mandarin, the tone a speaker uses can change which word listeners understand.","zh":"在普通話中，說話者使用的聲調可以改變聆聽者理解到的詞。"},{"en":"If a speaker uses the wrong pitch, the meaning may become unclear.","zh":"如果說話者使用錯誤音高，意思可能變得不清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the sound choices made by the person speaking.","zh":"這個短語著重說話者作出的聲音選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"native Vietnamese speakers","meaning":"越南語母語者","examples":[{"en":"The researchers asked seven native Vietnamese speakers to read word lists.","zh":"研究人員要求七名越南語母語者朗讀詞表。"},{"en":"Native Vietnamese speakers are people who learned Vietnamese as their first language.","zh":"native Vietnamese speakers 指把越南語作為第一語言學會的人。"},{"en":"A language study may compare native Vietnamese speakers with learners of Vietnamese.","zh":"語言研究可能比較越南語母語者和越南語學習者。"},{"en":"Native speakers are useful in research because they use the language naturally.","zh":"母語者對研究有用，因為他們自然地使用該語言。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies participants by their first language.","zh":"這個短語以第一語言識別參與者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"native Mandarin speakers","meaning":"普通話母語者","examples":[{"en":"The study also involved native Mandarin speakers.","zh":"這項研究也涉及普通話母語者。"},{"en":"Native Mandarin speakers are people who learned Mandarin as their first language.","zh":"native Mandarin speakers 指把普通話作為第一語言學會的人。"},{"en":"A speech experiment may ask native Mandarin speakers to pronounce words with different tones.","zh":"語音實驗可能要求普通話母語者讀出不同聲調的詞語。"},{"en":"Their pronunciation helps researchers study how pitch is used in daily language.","zh":"他們的發音幫助研究人員研究日常語言如何使用音高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people whose natural first language is Mandarin.","zh":"這個短語描述第一語言自然是普通話的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"read out lists of words","meaning":"朗讀詞表","examples":[{"en":"The speakers were asked to read out lists of words.","zh":"說話者被要求朗讀詞表。"},{"en":"To read out lists of words means to say written word lists aloud.","zh":"read out lists of words 指把書面詞表讀出聲。"},{"en":"In a pronunciation class, students may read out lists of words so the teacher can check their sounds.","zh":"在發音課中，學生可能朗讀詞表，讓老師檢查其發音。"},{"en":"Reading words aloud lets researchers record pitch, rhythm and pronunciation.","zh":"朗讀詞語讓研究人員記錄音高、節奏和發音。"},{"en":"This phrase describes spoken production from written prompts.","zh":"這個短語描述根據書面提示發聲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on different days","meaning":"在不同日子","examples":[{"en":"The speakers read the word lists on different days.","zh":"說話者在不同日子朗讀詞表。"},{"en":"On different days means at separate times, not during one single session.","zh":"on different days 指在分開的時間，而不是同一次進行。"},{"en":"A teacher may test spelling on different days to see whether students remember words long-term.","zh":"老師可能在不同日子測驗串字，以看看學生是否長期記得詞語。"},{"en":"Repeating a task on different days helps researchers check consistency.","zh":"在不同日子重複任務，幫助研究人員檢查一致性。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights that results are compared across time.","zh":"這個短語強調結果是跨時間比較的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"chosen words","meaning":"被選出的詞語","examples":[{"en":"The chosen words spanned a range of pitches.","zh":"被選出的詞語涵蓋一系列音高。"},{"en":"Chosen words are the words selected for a task, test or study.","zh":"chosen words 指為某項任務、測驗或研究選出的詞語。"},{"en":"A teacher’s chosen words in a grammar exercise should match the students’ level.","zh":"老師在文法練習中選出的詞語應符合學生程度。"},{"en":"In research, chosen words affect what kind of evidence the experiment can produce.","zh":"在研究中，被選出的詞語會影響實驗能產生哪類證據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to words deliberately selected, not random speech.","zh":"這個短語指刻意選出的詞語，而不是隨意說話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"span a range of","meaning":"涵蓋一系列……","examples":[{"en":"The chosen words spanned a range of pitches.","zh":"被選出的詞語涵蓋一系列音高。"},{"en":"To span a range of something means to cover several different types, levels or points.","zh":"span a range of something 指涵蓋幾種不同類型、水平或點。"},{"en":"A reading course may span a range of topics from health to technology.","zh":"閱讀課程可能涵蓋從健康到科技的一系列主題。"},{"en":"Words spanning a range of pitches force speakers to use high and low sounds.","zh":"涵蓋一系列音高的詞語會迫使說話者使用高低不同的聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase shows breadth or coverage.","zh":"這個短語顯示廣度或覆蓋範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a range of pitches","meaning":"一系列音高","examples":[{"en":"The words covered a range of pitches.","zh":"這些詞語涵蓋一系列音高。"},{"en":"A range of pitches is a set of different high and low sound levels.","zh":"a range of pitches 指一組不同高低的聲音水平。"},{"en":"A song for beginners may use a narrow range of pitches so it is easier to sing.","zh":"初學者歌曲可能使用較窄的一系列音高，令它較容易唱。"},{"en":"A wider range of pitches gives researchers more information about voice control.","zh":"較廣的一系列音高為研究人員提供更多關於聲線控制的資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes variety in sound height.","zh":"這個短語描述聲音高度的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"force someone to","meaning":"迫使某人去……","examples":[{"en":"The word lists forced speakers to change their pitch.","zh":"詞表迫使說話者改變音高。"},{"en":"To force someone to do something means to make them do it because the situation requires it.","zh":"force someone to do something 指因情況要求而令某人做某事。"},{"en":"A fire drill forces students to leave the classroom quickly.","zh":"消防演習迫使學生快速離開課室。"},{"en":"In experiments, tasks can force participants to reveal abilities they normally use automatically.","zh":"在實驗中，任務可以迫使參與者展示他們平時自動使用的能力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows pressure or necessity, not free choice.","zh":"這個短語顯示壓力或必要性，而不是自由選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"raise and lower their voices","meaning":"升高和降低聲線","examples":[{"en":"The speakers had to raise and lower their voices considerably.","zh":"說話者必須大幅升高和降低聲線。"},{"en":"To raise and lower their voices means to make their voices higher and lower in pitch.","zh":"raise and lower their voices 指把聲線音高變高和變低。"},{"en":"A drama teacher may ask students to raise and lower their voices to show different emotions.","zh":"戲劇老師可能要求學生升高和降低聲線，以表現不同情緒。"},{"en":"Tone-language speakers raise and lower their voices to distinguish word meanings.","zh":"聲調語言說話者升高和降低聲線，以區分詞義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pitch movement in speech.","zh":"這個短語描述說話中的音高變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"considerably","meaning":"大幅地","examples":[{"en":"The speakers raised and lowered their voices considerably.","zh":"說話者大幅升高和降低聲線。"},{"en":"Considerably means by a large or noticeable amount.","zh":"considerably 指以很大或明顯的程度。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may improve considerably after several months of speaking practice.","zh":"經過幾個月口語練習，學生信心可能大幅提升。"},{"en":"If a voice changes considerably, listeners can clearly hear the difference.","zh":"如果聲線大幅改變，聆聽者可以清楚聽到差異。"},{"en":"This word suggests more than a small change.","zh":"這個詞暗示不只是小改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"recited lists","meaning":"朗讀出的詞表","examples":[{"en":"The researchers recorded the recited lists.","zh":"研究人員錄下朗讀出的詞表。"},{"en":"Recited lists are lists that have been read or spoken aloud.","zh":"recited lists 指已被朗讀或說出的列表。"},{"en":"A teacher may record recited lists of vocabulary to check students’ pronunciation.","zh":"老師可能錄下學生朗讀出的詞彙表，以檢查發音。"},{"en":"Recording recited lists lets researchers compare how the same words sound on different days.","zh":"錄下朗讀出的詞表，讓研究人員比較同一詞語在不同日子聽起來如何。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to word lists after they have been spoken aloud.","zh":"這個短語指已被讀出聲的詞表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take the average pitch","meaning":"計算平均音高","examples":[{"en":"The researchers took the average pitch for each word.","zh":"研究人員計算每個詞的平均音高。"},{"en":"To take the average pitch means to calculate the typical pitch level across the word.","zh":"take the average pitch 指計算整個詞語的典型音高水平。"},{"en":"A music app may take the average pitch of a singer’s voice during practice.","zh":"音樂應用程式可能在練習期間計算歌手聲音的平均音高。"},{"en":"Taking an average helps reduce the effect of small moment-to-moment changes.","zh":"計算平均值有助減少瞬間細小變化的影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes measuring a representative pitch value.","zh":"這個短語描述量度具代表性的音高數值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"average pitch","meaning":"平均音高","examples":[{"en":"The researchers compared the average pitch used for each word.","zh":"研究人員比較每個詞所使用的平均音高。"},{"en":"Average pitch is the typical high or low sound level across a word or sound.","zh":"average pitch 指一個詞或聲音整體上的典型高低水平。"},{"en":"A speech coach may measure average pitch to see whether someone speaks too high or too low.","zh":"語音教練可能量度平均音高，以看看某人說話是否太高或太低。"},{"en":"Comparing average pitch helps researchers check whether a speaker is consistent.","zh":"比較平均音高幫助研究人員檢查說話者是否一致。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a calculated sound level, not one instant of sound.","zh":"這個短語指計算出的聲音水平，而不是某一瞬間的聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"whole word","meaning":"整個詞語","examples":[{"en":"The average pitch was calculated for each whole word.","zh":"平均音高是為每個整個詞語計算出來的。"},{"en":"A whole word means the complete word, not just one sound or syllable inside it.","zh":"whole word 指完整詞語，而不是其中一個聲音或音節。"},{"en":"In spelling practice, students should read the whole word before guessing its meaning.","zh":"在串字練習中，學生應先讀整個詞語，再猜意思。"},{"en":"Calculating pitch across a whole word gives a more stable measure than using one tiny sound.","zh":"計算整個詞語的音高，比使用一個微小聲音給出更穩定量度。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses completeness.","zh":"這個短語強調完整性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"compare the pitches used","meaning":"比較所使用的音高","examples":[{"en":"The researchers compared the pitches used by each person.","zh":"研究人員比較每個人所使用的音高。"},{"en":"To compare the pitches used means to examine whether the sound heights are similar or different.","zh":"compare the pitches used 指檢查所用聲音高度是否相似或不同。"},{"en":"A singing teacher may compare the pitches used by two students singing the same line.","zh":"歌唱老師可能比較兩名學生唱同一句時所使用的音高。"},{"en":"Comparing pitches helps show whether speakers repeat words at stable sound levels.","zh":"比較音高有助顯示說話者是否以穩定聲音水平重複詞語。"},{"en":"This phrase describes checking differences in voice height.","zh":"這個短語描述檢查聲線高度差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"strikingly consistent pitch","meaning":"驚人一致的音高","examples":[{"en":"Both groups showed strikingly consistent pitch for each word.","zh":"兩組人對每個詞都顯示驚人一致的音高。"},{"en":"Strikingly consistent pitch means the pitch stayed surprisingly similar each time.","zh":"strikingly consistent pitch 指音高每次都保持出乎意料地相似。"},{"en":"A student with strikingly consistent pronunciation says the same word almost the same way every time.","zh":"發音驚人一致的學生每次說同一個詞幾乎都一樣。"},{"en":"Consistent pitch across different days suggests speakers may remember pitch more precisely than expected.","zh":"不同日子音高一致，顯示說話者可能比預期更精確地記住音高。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights surprising stability in sound.","zh":"這個短語突出聲音上的驚人穩定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for any given word","meaning":"對任何指定詞語而言","examples":[{"en":"The pitch was consistent for any given word.","zh":"對任何指定詞語而言，音高都一致。"},{"en":"For any given word means for each particular word being considered.","zh":"for any given word 指對正在考慮的每一個特定詞語而言。"},{"en":"A dictionary gives one spelling for any given word, even if pronunciation varies.","zh":"字典對任何指定詞語都給出一種拼法，即使發音有所不同。"},{"en":"If pitch is stable for any given word, the same word is spoken at a similar pitch repeatedly.","zh":"如果對任何指定詞語音高都穩定，同一詞語就會反覆以相似音高說出。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on one specific item at a time.","zh":"這個短語一次聚焦於一個特定項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"quarter-tone difference","meaning":"四分之一音差","examples":[{"en":"The difference between days was often less than a quarter-tone.","zh":"不同日子之間的差異通常少於四分之一音。"},{"en":"A quarter-tone difference is a very small difference in pitch.","zh":"quarter-tone difference 指非常細小的音高差異。"},{"en":"Most ordinary listeners would find a quarter-tone difference difficult to notice.","zh":"大多數普通聆聽者會覺得四分之一音差很難察覺。"},{"en":"If speakers differ by less than a quarter-tone, their pitch control is surprisingly precise.","zh":"如果說話者差異少於四分之一音，他們的音高控制就驚人地精確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a tiny musical distance.","zh":"這個短語描述極細小的音樂距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"between days","meaning":"不同日子之間","examples":[{"en":"The pitch difference between days was very small.","zh":"不同日子之間的音高差異很小。"},{"en":"Between days means comparing what happened on one day with what happened on another day.","zh":"between days 指比較某一天與另一日發生的情況。"},{"en":"A teacher may compare a student’s reading speed between days to see improvement.","zh":"老師可能比較學生不同日子之間的閱讀速度，以觀察進步。"},{"en":"Small differences between days suggest that a result is stable over time.","zh":"不同日子之間差異小，表示結果隨時間穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when repeated measurements are taken on separate days.","zh":"當分開日子進行重複量度時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"mind-boggling","meaning":"令人難以置信的","examples":[{"en":"Deutsch says the similarity is mind-boggling.","zh":"Deutsch 說這種相似程度令人難以置信。"},{"en":"Mind-boggling means extremely surprising, difficult to imagine or hard to understand.","zh":"mind-boggling 指極令人驚訝、難以想像或難以理解。"},{"en":"The number of messages people send every day is mind-boggling.","zh":"人們每天發送的訊息數量令人難以置信。"},{"en":"A result feels mind-boggling when it is much more precise than expected.","zh":"當結果比預期精確得多，就會令人難以置信。"},{"en":"This word expresses strong surprise.","zh":"這個詞表達強烈驚訝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a real example of","meaning":"……的真實例子","examples":[{"en":"Deutsch considers this a real example of absolute pitch.","zh":"Deutsch 認為這是絕對音感的真實例子。"},{"en":"A real example of something is a genuine case that shows the idea clearly.","zh":"a real example of something 指真正顯示該概念的個案。"},{"en":"A student helping a classmate without being asked is a real example of kindness.","zh":"學生在沒被要求下幫助同學，是真正善良的例子。"},{"en":"Real examples help people understand abstract claims more clearly.","zh":"真實例子幫助人更清楚理解抽象說法。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the evidence directly demonstrates the concept.","zh":"這個短語表示證據直接展示該概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as babies","meaning":"在嬰兒時期","examples":[{"en":"As babies, the speakers learnt to connect pitches with words.","zh":"在嬰兒時期，這些說話者學會把音高與詞語連繫起來。"},{"en":"As babies means when they were infants or very young children.","zh":"as babies 指在嬰兒或非常年幼時。"},{"en":"As babies, children begin learning the sounds of their home language.","zh":"在嬰兒時期，孩子開始學習家庭語言的聲音。"},{"en":"Experiences as babies can shape later listening and speaking habits.","zh":"嬰兒時期的經驗可以塑造後來的聆聽和說話習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the earliest stage of life.","zh":"這個短語指人生最早階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"associate certain pitches with","meaning":"將某些音高與……聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"The speakers learnt to associate certain pitches with meaningful words.","zh":"說話者學會將某些音高與有意義的詞語聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To associate certain pitches with something means to connect particular sound heights with it in the mind.","zh":"associate certain pitches with something 指在心中把特定聲音高度與某事連接。"},{"en":"A child may associate a high alarm sound with danger.","zh":"孩子可能把尖銳警報聲與危險聯繫起來。"},{"en":"In tone languages, children associate pitch patterns with word meanings from early life.","zh":"在聲調語言中，孩子從早年起就把音高模式與詞義聯繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental linking between sound and meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述聲音與意思之間的心理連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"meaningful words","meaning":"有意義的詞語","examples":[{"en":"Babies associate certain pitches with meaningful words.","zh":"嬰兒將某些音高與有意義的詞語聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Meaningful words are words that carry clear meaning for the speaker or listener.","zh":"meaningful words 指對說話者或聆聽者有清楚意思的詞語。"},{"en":"A child first learns meaningful words such as “mum”, “milk” and “no”.","zh":"孩子最初學會 “mum”、“milk” 和 “no” 等有意義的詞語。"},{"en":"Words become meaningful when children connect sounds with people, objects or actions.","zh":"當孩子把聲音與人物、物件或行動連繫起來，詞語就變得有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts real language meaning with meaningless sounds.","zh":"這個短語把真正語言意思與無意義聲音作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"just as","meaning":"正如；就像","examples":[{"en":"Speakers label pitches just as musicians label musical tones.","zh":"說話者標記音高，正如音樂家標記音樂音一樣。"},{"en":"Just as means in the same way that.","zh":"just as 指以同樣方式。"},{"en":"Students organise vocabulary by topic just as librarians organise books by subject.","zh":"學生按主題整理詞彙，正如圖書館員按科目整理書籍。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a comparison that helps explain an unfamiliar idea.","zh":"這個短語建立比較，幫助解釋陌生概念。"},{"en":"It shows that two actions follow a similar pattern.","zh":"它顯示兩個行動遵循相似模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"label one tone A and another B","meaning":"將一個音標為 A、另一個標為 B","examples":[{"en":"A musician labels one tone A and another B.","zh":"音樂家將一個音標為 A、另一個標為 B。"},{"en":"To label one tone A and another B means to give different names to different pitches.","zh":"label one tone A and another B 指給不同音高不同名稱。"},{"en":"A teacher may label one box “verbs” and another “nouns” to help students sort words.","zh":"老師可能把一個盒子標為「動詞」，另一個標為「名詞」，幫助學生分類詞語。"},{"en":"Labelling tones helps musicians talk about sound accurately.","zh":"標記音有助音樂家準確談論聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase describes naming and categorising sounds.","zh":"這個短語描述命名和分類聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"demonstrate this precise use of","meaning":"展示對……的精確使用","examples":[{"en":"Speakers demonstrate this precise use of pitch.","zh":"說話者展示對音高的精確使用。"},{"en":"To demonstrate this precise use of something means to show clearly that it is being used accurately.","zh":"demonstrate this precise use of something 指清楚顯示某物正被準確使用。"},{"en":"A student can demonstrate precise use of grammar by choosing the correct tense in context.","zh":"學生可以透過在語境中選擇正確時態，展示對文法的精確使用。"},{"en":"Precise use of pitch matters in tone languages because small changes can change meaning.","zh":"在聲調語言中，精確使用音高很重要，因為細小變化可以改變意思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes showing accurate control of a skill.","zh":"這個短語描述展示對某技能的準確控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"regardless of whether or not","meaning":"不論是否","examples":[{"en":"They use pitch precisely regardless of whether or not they have musical training.","zh":"他們精確使用音高，不論是否接受過音樂訓練。"},{"en":"Regardless of whether or not means no matter if something is true or false.","zh":"regardless of whether or not 指不管某事是真是假。"},{"en":"Students should be treated respectfully regardless of whether or not they get high marks.","zh":"學生不論是否取得高分，都應受到尊重。"},{"en":"If speakers show pitch control regardless of musical training, language may be the key factor.","zh":"如果說話者不論是否受過音樂訓練都展現音高控制，語言可能是關鍵因素。"},{"en":"This phrase removes one condition from the explanation.","zh":"這個短語把某條件從解釋中移除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"musical training","meaning":"音樂訓練","examples":[{"en":"The speakers showed pitch consistency even without musical training.","zh":"說話者即使沒有音樂訓練，也顯示音高一致性。"},{"en":"Musical training is formal or regular practice in singing, playing instruments or understanding music.","zh":"musical training 指在歌唱、演奏樂器或理解音樂方面的正式或定期練習。"},{"en":"A child may receive musical training through piano lessons and choir practice.","zh":"孩子可能透過鋼琴課和合唱團練習接受音樂訓練。"},{"en":"Musical training can improve listening because students practise noticing sound differences.","zh":"音樂訓練可以提升聆聽能力，因為學生練習注意聲音差異。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to learned instruction, not natural talent alone.","zh":"這個短語指後天教學，而不只是天生才能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"turn up evidence of","meaning":"發現……的證據","examples":[{"en":"Other researchers are turning up evidence of everyday absolute pitch.","zh":"其他研究人員正在發現日常絕對音感的證據。"},{"en":"To turn up evidence of something means to discover information that supports its existence.","zh":"turn up evidence of something 指發現支持某事存在的資料。"},{"en":"A school survey may turn up evidence of bullying that teachers had not noticed.","zh":"學校調查可能發現老師未注意到的欺凌證據。"},{"en":"New evidence can change how researchers understand an ability.","zh":"新證據可以改變研究人員對某能力的理解。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests discovery through investigation.","zh":"這個短語暗示透過調查得到發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"everyday evidence","meaning":"日常生活中的證據","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are finding everyday evidence of absolute pitch.","zh":"研究人員正在發現絕對音感在日常生活中的證據。"},{"en":"Everyday evidence is evidence found in ordinary life rather than in rare or special situations.","zh":"everyday evidence 指在普通生活中，而不是罕見或特殊情況中找到的證據。"},{"en":"A teacher may find everyday evidence of stress when students often forget homework and look tired.","zh":"當學生經常忘記功課並看起來疲倦，老師可能找到壓力的日常證據。"},{"en":"Everyday evidence is useful because it shows how an ability appears outside the laboratory.","zh":"日常證據很有用，因為它顯示能力如何在實驗室以外出現。"},{"en":"This phrase connects research with normal daily behaviour.","zh":"這個短語把研究與正常日常行為連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at least three other experiments","meaning":"至少另外三項實驗","examples":[{"en":"At least three other experiments have found similar evidence.","zh":"至少另外三項實驗發現了相似證據。"},{"en":"At least three other experiments means three or more separate studies besides the one already mentioned.","zh":"at least three other experiments 指除了已提及的一項外，還有三項或以上分開研究。"},{"en":"At least three other teachers noticed the same problem in students’ writing.","zh":"至少另外三位老師注意到學生寫作中的同一問題。"},{"en":"Similar results from several experiments make an argument stronger.","zh":"幾項實驗得出相似結果，會令論點更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the evidence does not come from only one study.","zh":"這個短語顯示證據不是只來自一項研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"launch into","meaning":"突然開始唱","examples":[{"en":"People can launch into familiar songs at nearly the correct pitch.","zh":"人們可以幾乎以正確音高突然開始唱熟悉歌曲。"},{"en":"To launch into something means to begin doing it suddenly and energetically.","zh":"launch into something 指突然且有活力地開始做某事。"},{"en":"A child may launch into a favourite song as soon as the music starts.","zh":"音樂一開始，孩子可能突然開始唱最喜歡的歌曲。"},{"en":"If people launch into songs at the right pitch, they may remember pitch more accurately than expected.","zh":"如果人們能以正確音高突然開始唱歌，他們可能比預期更準確記住音高。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a quick, confident beginning.","zh":"這個短語暗示快速而有信心的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"familiar songs","meaning":"熟悉的歌曲","examples":[{"en":"People often begin familiar songs near the correct pitch.","zh":"人們常以接近正確音高開始唱熟悉的歌曲。"},{"en":"Familiar songs are songs people know well from repeated listening.","zh":"familiar songs 指人們因反覆聆聽而很熟悉的歌曲。"},{"en":"Students may remember familiar songs from childhood even after many years.","zh":"學生可能多年後仍記得童年時熟悉的歌曲。"},{"en":"Familiar songs are easier to sing because the melody is already stored in memory.","zh":"熟悉的歌曲較容易唱，因為旋律已儲存在記憶中。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to music that listeners already recognise.","zh":"這個短語指聆聽者已經認得的音樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at or very near","meaning":"在……或非常接近……","examples":[{"en":"People can sing familiar songs at or very near the correct pitch.","zh":"人們可以在正確音高或非常接近正確音高的位置唱熟悉歌曲。"},{"en":"At or very near means exactly at a point or extremely close to it.","zh":"at or very near 指正正在某點或極接近某點。"},{"en":"A bus may stop at or very near the school gate in the morning.","zh":"早上巴士可能停在學校門口或非常接近校門的位置。"},{"en":"Singing at or very near the correct pitch suggests strong pitch memory.","zh":"以正確音高或非常接近的音高唱歌，顯示很強的音高記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase allows for exactness or a very small difference.","zh":"這個短語容許完全準確或只有極小差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"correct pitches","meaning":"正確音高","examples":[{"en":"Some people start familiar songs at the correct pitches.","zh":"有些人以正確音高開始唱熟悉歌曲。"},{"en":"Correct pitches are the accurate high or low notes required by a piece of music.","zh":"correct pitches 指樂曲所需的準確高低音。"},{"en":"A choir sounds better when singers enter at the correct pitches.","zh":"當歌手以正確音高進入，合唱團聽起來會更好。"},{"en":"Wrong pitches can make a melody sound uncomfortable or out of tune.","zh":"錯誤音高可以令旋律聽起來不舒服或走音。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on accurate sound height.","zh":"這個短語著重準確聲音高度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"nickname this ability","meaning":"將這種能力稱為","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers have nicknamed this ability absolute memory.","zh":"有些研究人員將這種能力稱為絕對記憶。"},{"en":"To nickname this ability means to give it an informal or shorter name.","zh":"nickname this ability 指給這種能力一個非正式或較短的名稱。"},{"en":"Students may nickname a difficult grammar rule “the danger rule” to remember it more easily.","zh":"學生可能把一條困難文法規則稱為「危險規則」，以便更易記住。"},{"en":"A nickname can make a complex idea easier to discuss.","zh":"暱稱可以令複雜概念更容易討論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving an ability a memorable label.","zh":"這個短語描述給能力一個容易記住的標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"absolute memory","meaning":"絕對記憶","examples":[{"en":"Absolute memory may appear in senses other than hearing.","zh":"絕對記憶可能出現在聽覺以外的感官中。"},{"en":"Absolute memory is the ability to remember exact sensory details, such as pitch or colour, without comparison.","zh":"absolute memory 指不用比較也能記住確切感官細節，例如音高或顏色的能力。"},{"en":"A person with strong colour memory may recognise a shade without seeing a sample beside it.","zh":"有強烈顏色記憶的人，可能不用把樣本放在旁邊也能認出某種色調。"},{"en":"Absolute memory suggests the mind can store precise information from past experience.","zh":"絕對記憶顯示心智可以儲存來自過去經驗的精確資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase extends the idea of absolute pitch beyond music.","zh":"這個短語把絕對音感的概念擴展到音樂以外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pop up","meaning":"出現","examples":[{"en":"The ability pops up in other senses too.","zh":"這種能力也出現在其他感官中。"},{"en":"To pop up means to appear suddenly or unexpectedly.","zh":"pop up 指突然或意外出現。"},{"en":"A spelling mistake may pop up again if a student has not fully learned the pattern.","zh":"如果學生未完全掌握模式，拼字錯誤可能再次出現。"},{"en":"If an ability pops up in different senses, it may be more general than researchers thought.","zh":"如果某能力出現在不同感官中，它可能比研究人員所想更普遍。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests surprising appearance.","zh":"這個短語暗示令人意外的出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"other senses","meaning":"其他感官","examples":[{"en":"Absolute memory may pop up in other senses.","zh":"絕對記憶可能出現在其他感官中。"},{"en":"Other senses are ways of perceiving beyond the one already mentioned, such as sight, smell, touch or taste.","zh":"other senses 指已提及感官以外的感知方式，例如視覺、嗅覺、觸覺或味覺。"},{"en":"A cooking class may train other senses, not only taste, because smell and texture matter too.","zh":"烹飪課可能訓練味覺以外的其他感官，因為氣味和質感也重要。"},{"en":"If memory appears in other senses, researchers may study colour, smell or touch as well as sound.","zh":"如果記憶出現在其他感官中，研究人員可能研究顏色、氣味或觸覺以及聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase broadens the discussion beyond hearing.","zh":"這個短語把討論擴展至聽覺以外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"given studies like these","meaning":"鑑於這類研究","examples":[{"en":"Given studies like these, the real mystery is why we do not all have absolute pitch.","zh":"鑑於這類研究，真正的謎團是為何我們不是人人都有絕對音感。"},{"en":"Given studies like these means considering this kind of research evidence.","zh":"given studies like these 指考慮到這類研究證據。"},{"en":"Given results like these, a teacher may decide to give students more speaking practice.","zh":"鑑於這類結果，老師可能決定給學生更多口語練習。"},{"en":"This phrase uses evidence as the reason for the next conclusion.","zh":"這個短語把證據作為下一個結論的理由。"},{"en":"It signals that the following idea is based on the studies just mentioned.","zh":"它表示接下來的想法基於剛提到的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cognitive psychologist","meaning":"認知心理學家","examples":[{"en":"Daniel Levitin is a cognitive psychologist at McGill University.","zh":"Daniel Levitin 是麥基爾大學的認知心理學家。"},{"en":"A cognitive psychologist studies mental processes such as memory, attention, perception and learning.","zh":"cognitive psychologist 指研究記憶、注意力、感知和學習等心理過程的心理學家。"},{"en":"A cognitive psychologist may test how students remember vocabulary after different types of practice.","zh":"認知心理學家可能測試學生在不同練習方式後如何記住詞彙。"},{"en":"Cognitive psychology helps explain how people process music, language and information.","zh":"認知心理學幫助解釋人們如何處理音樂、語言和資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specialist who studies the mind.","zh":"這個短語命名研究心智的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the real mystery is why","meaning":"真正的謎團是為何……","examples":[{"en":"The real mystery is why we do not all have absolute pitch.","zh":"真正的謎團是為何我們不是人人都有絕對音感。"},{"en":"The real mystery is why means the most puzzling question is the reason behind something.","zh":"the real mystery is why 指最令人困惑的問題是某事背後的原因。"},{"en":"The real mystery is why some students lose confidence even after improving.","zh":"真正的謎團是為何有些學生即使進步了仍失去信心。"},{"en":"This phrase shifts attention from an obvious question to a deeper puzzle.","zh":"這個短語把注意力從明顯問題轉向更深層謎題。"},{"en":"It is useful when evidence changes what seems surprising.","zh":"當證據改變何者令人驚訝時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"over the past decade","meaning":"在過去十年","examples":[{"en":"Over the past decade, researchers have studied the family patterns of absolute pitch.","zh":"在過去十年，研究人員研究了絕對音感的家族模式。"},{"en":"Over the past decade means during the last ten years.","zh":"over the past decade 指在過去十年期間。"},{"en":"Over the past decade, many schools have introduced more online learning tools.","zh":"在過去十年，許多學校引入更多網上學習工具。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that change or research has happened across a recent ten-year period.","zh":"這個短語顯示變化或研究發生於最近十年間。"},{"en":"It is commonly used in reports about trends.","zh":"它常用於關於趨勢的報告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"confirm that","meaning":"確認","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have confirmed that absolute pitch often runs in families.","zh":"研究人員已確認絕對音感常在家族中遺傳。"},{"en":"To confirm that means to show that something is true or very likely true.","zh":"confirm that 指顯示某事是真的或很可能是真的。"},{"en":"A doctor may confirm that a patient has recovered after checking test results.","zh":"醫生可能在檢查測試結果後，確認病人已康復。"},{"en":"Confirmation is stronger than a guess because it is based on evidence.","zh":"確認比猜測更有力，因為它基於證據。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces information that has been supported by research or checking.","zh":"這個短語引入已由研究或檢查支持的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"run in families","meaning":"在家族中遺傳","examples":[{"en":"Absolute pitch often runs in families.","zh":"絕對音感常在家族中遺傳。"},{"en":"If a trait runs in families, it appears in several relatives and may have a genetic connection.","zh":"如果某特徵 runs in families，它會出現在幾名親屬身上，並可能有基因關聯。"},{"en":"Poor eyesight can run in families, so parents may take children for eye checks early.","zh":"視力差可以在家族中遺傳，所以父母可能早早帶孩子驗眼。"},{"en":"A skill that runs in families may still need training before it fully develops.","zh":"在家族中遺傳的技能仍可能需要訓練才能完全發展。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests inheritance or family pattern.","zh":"這個短語暗示遺傳或家族模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"strongly suggest","meaning":"強烈顯示","examples":[{"en":"Freimer’s study strongly suggests that genes help create absolute pitch.","zh":"Freimer 的研究強烈顯示基因有助形成絕對音感。"},{"en":"Strongly suggest means give powerful evidence that something is likely true.","zh":"strongly suggest 指提供有力證據，顯示某事很可能是真的。"},{"en":"Repeated late arrivals strongly suggest that the bus schedule is causing problems.","zh":"反覆遲到強烈顯示巴士時間表正在造成問題。"},{"en":"Strong evidence can suggest a conclusion even before every detail is known.","zh":"即使不是每個細節都已知道，有力證據也可以顯示一個結論。"},{"en":"This phrase is cautious but confident.","zh":"這個短語語氣謹慎但有信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the right genes","meaning":"合適的基因","examples":[{"en":"The right genes may help create this musical ability.","zh":"合適的基因可能有助形成這種音樂能力。"},{"en":"The right genes means genetic factors that make a certain ability more likely to develop.","zh":"the right genes 指令某種能力更可能發展的基因因素。"},{"en":"A child may have the right genes for height, but nutrition still matters.","zh":"孩子可能有長高的合適基因，但營養仍然重要。"},{"en":"Genes may create potential, while environment helps decide whether that potential grows.","zh":"基因可能創造潛力，而環境幫助決定該潛力是否成長。"},{"en":"This phrase links inherited biology with later ability.","zh":"這個短語把遺傳生物因素與後來能力連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"this brand of musical genius","meaning":"這種音樂天才","examples":[{"en":"The right genes may help create this brand of musical genius.","zh":"合適的基因可能有助形成這種音樂天才。"},{"en":"This brand of musical genius means this particular type of exceptional musical ability.","zh":"this brand of musical genius 指這種特定類型的卓越音樂能力。"},{"en":"A composer’s gift for melody is one brand of musical genius, while a performer’s memory is another.","zh":"作曲家的旋律天賦是一種音樂天才，而演奏者的記憶力是另一種。"},{"en":"Calling something a brand of genius suggests it is special but also one type among several.","zh":"把某事稱為一種天才，暗示它特殊但也是多種類型之一。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a distinctive form of musical talent.","zh":"這個短語描述一種獨特形式的音樂天賦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tone tests","meaning":"音高測試","examples":[{"en":"Freimer gave tone tests to people with absolute pitch.","zh":"Freimer 向有絕對音感的人進行音高測試。"},{"en":"Tone tests are tests that check how well people recognise or compare musical pitches.","zh":"tone tests 指檢查人們辨認或比較音高能力的測試。"},{"en":"A music teacher may use tone tests to see whether students can hear high and low notes accurately.","zh":"音樂老師可能使用音高測試，看學生能否準確聽出高低音。"},{"en":"Tone tests help researchers measure listening ability rather than relying only on self-reports.","zh":"音高測試幫助研究人員量度聆聽能力，而不是只依賴自我報告。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to tests of pitch perception.","zh":"這個短語指音高感知測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"relatives of","meaning":"……的親屬","examples":[{"en":"Freimer tested relatives of people with absolute pitch.","zh":"Freimer 測試了有絕對音感者的親屬。"},{"en":"Relatives of someone are people connected to that person by family relationship.","zh":"relatives of someone 指與某人有家庭關係的人。"},{"en":"Doctors may ask relatives of a patient whether a disease runs in the family.","zh":"醫生可能詢問病人的親屬某疾病是否在家族中出現。"},{"en":"Testing relatives helps researchers see whether a trait may be inherited.","zh":"測試親屬幫助研究人員了解某特徵是否可能遺傳。"},{"en":"This phrase points to family members.","zh":"這個短語指家庭成員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"early music lessons","meaning":"早期音樂課","examples":[{"en":"He also tested people who had taken early music lessons.","zh":"他也測試了上過早期音樂課的人。"},{"en":"Early music lessons are music classes or training received at a young age.","zh":"early music lessons 指年幼時接受的音樂課或訓練。"},{"en":"Children who take early music lessons may learn to hear rhythm and pitch more carefully.","zh":"上早期音樂課的孩子可能學會更仔細地聽節奏和音高。"},{"en":"Early training may matter because young learners can form sound categories quickly.","zh":"早期訓練可能重要，因為年幼學習者能快速形成聲音類別。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights when musical instruction begins.","zh":"這個短語突出音樂教學開始的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"far more likely to","meaning":"更有可能","examples":[{"en":"Relatives of people with absolute pitch were far more likely to develop the skill.","zh":"有絕對音感者的親屬更有可能培養出這項技能。"},{"en":"Far more likely to means having a much greater chance of doing or becoming something.","zh":"far more likely to 指做某事或變成某狀態的機會大得多。"},{"en":"Students who revise regularly are far more likely to remember vocabulary in the exam.","zh":"定期溫習的學生更有可能在考試中記住詞彙。"},{"en":"A much higher likelihood suggests that an important factor may be involved.","zh":"機會高得多，顯示可能有重要因素參與其中。"},{"en":"This phrase compares probability strongly.","zh":"這個短語強烈比較可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"simply had the music lessons","meaning":"只是上過音樂課","examples":[{"en":"Some people had simply had the music lessons without developing absolute pitch.","zh":"有些人只是上過音樂課，卻沒有發展出絕對音感。"},{"en":"Simply had the music lessons means only received the lessons, without the other result happening.","zh":"simply had the music lessons 指只是接受了課堂，而沒有產生另一結果。"},{"en":"Some students simply had extra tutoring but did not improve because they never practised alone.","zh":"有些學生只是上過補習，但因從不自行練習而沒有進步。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor by itself may not be enough.","zh":"這個短語顯示單一因素本身可能不足夠。"},{"en":"It helps separate taking lessons from actually developing the ability.","zh":"它幫助區分上課與真正培養出能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"familial aggregation","meaning":"家族聚集現象","examples":[{"en":"Freimer says there is familial aggregation of absolute pitch.","zh":"Freimer 說絕對音感有家族聚集現象。"},{"en":"Familial aggregation means a trait appears more often among family members than in the general population.","zh":"familial aggregation 指某特徵在家庭成員中比在一般人口中更常出現。"},{"en":"Doctors may notice familial aggregation when several relatives have the same allergy.","zh":"當幾名親屬有同一過敏，醫生可能注意到家族聚集現象。"},{"en":"Familial aggregation suggests genes may be involved, though environment can also matter.","zh":"家族聚集現象顯示基因可能有關，但環境也可能重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is a scientific way to describe family clustering.","zh":"這個短語是描述家族集中出現的科學說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"genetically predisposed toward","meaning":"在基因上傾向於……","examples":[{"en":"Some children are genetically predisposed toward absolute pitch.","zh":"有些孩子在基因上傾向於擁有絕對音感。"},{"en":"To be genetically predisposed toward something means to have inherited traits that make it more likely.","zh":"genetically predisposed toward something 指擁有遺傳特徵，令某事更可能發生。"},{"en":"A child may be genetically predisposed toward tall height if both parents are tall.","zh":"如果父母都高，孩子可能在基因上傾向於長得高。"},{"en":"Genetic predisposition does not guarantee the result, but it can create a strong tendency.","zh":"基因傾向不保證結果，但可以創造強烈傾向。"},{"en":"This phrase links inherited biology with future possibility.","zh":"這個短語把遺傳生物因素與未來可能性連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"innate inclination","meaning":"天生傾向","examples":[{"en":"This innate inclination may develop during childhood lessons.","zh":"這種天生傾向可能在童年課堂期間發展起來。"},{"en":"An innate inclination is a natural tendency someone is born with.","zh":"innate inclination 指某人天生具有的自然傾向。"},{"en":"A child may have an innate inclination to move rhythmically when music plays.","zh":"孩子可能有天生傾向，音樂一響就有節奏地移動。"},{"en":"An innate inclination can remain hidden if it is never trained or encouraged.","zh":"如果從未受訓練或鼓勵，天生傾向可能一直隱藏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a natural starting tendency, not a finished skill.","zh":"這個短語描述自然起點，而不是完成了的技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"blossom during","meaning":"在……期間發展起來","examples":[{"en":"A genetic inclination may blossom during childhood music lessons.","zh":"基因傾向可能在童年音樂課期間發展起來。"},{"en":"To blossom during a period means to develop strongly and successfully during that time.","zh":"blossom during a period 指在某段時間中強而成功地發展。"},{"en":"A shy student may blossom during drama lessons when she feels safe to perform.","zh":"害羞學生在感到安全地表演時，可能在戲劇課期間發展起來。"},{"en":"Talent can blossom when the right environment gives it practice and confidence.","zh":"當合適環境給予練習和信心，天賦可以發展起來。"},{"en":"This phrase compares development to a flower opening.","zh":"這個短語把發展比作花朵盛開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"childhood music lessons","meaning":"童年音樂課","examples":[{"en":"Childhood music lessons may help absolute pitch develop.","zh":"童年音樂課可能幫助絕對音感發展。"},{"en":"Childhood music lessons are music classes taken when someone is young.","zh":"childhood music lessons 指年幼時上的音樂課。"},{"en":"A child who attends childhood music lessons may learn rhythm, melody and note names early.","zh":"參加童年音樂課的孩子可能早早學會節奏、旋律和音符名稱。"},{"en":"These lessons may matter because early experience can shape listening habits.","zh":"這些課可能重要，因為早期經驗可以塑造聆聽習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights musical training during childhood.","zh":"這個短語突出童年期間的音樂訓練。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"point to","meaning":"指向；指出","examples":[{"en":"Many researchers point to the harmony of nature and nurture.","zh":"許多研究人員指出先天與後天的配合。"},{"en":"To point to something means to suggest it as an explanation or important factor.","zh":"point to something 指把某事指出為解釋或重要因素。"},{"en":"Falling grades may point to sleep problems rather than laziness.","zh":"成績下降可能指向睡眠問題，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"Evidence pointing to both genes and training suggests a mixed explanation.","zh":"指向基因和訓練兩者的證據，顯示解釋可能是混合的。"},{"en":"This phrase shows where evidence or reasoning leads.","zh":"這個短語顯示證據或推理導向何處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"nature and nurture","meaning":"先天與後天","examples":[{"en":"Absolute pitch may depend on both nature and nurture.","zh":"絕對音感可能同時取決於先天與後天。"},{"en":"Nature and nurture means inherited traits and environmental experience working together.","zh":"nature and nurture 指遺傳特質與環境經驗共同作用。"},{"en":"A student’s language ability may reflect both nature and nurture: memory, home language and practice all matter.","zh":"學生的語言能力可能反映先天與後天：記憶力、家庭語言和練習都重要。"},{"en":"If both nature and nurture are important, genes and lessons should both be studied.","zh":"如果先天與後天都重要，基因和課堂都應研究。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts inborn factors with training and environment.","zh":"這個短語對比天生因素與訓練和環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"explain why","meaning":"解釋為何","examples":[{"en":"This combination may explain why musicians show different levels of the talent.","zh":"這種結合可能解釋為何音樂家展現不同程度的天賦。"},{"en":"To explain why means to give the reason for something.","zh":"explain why 指給出某事的原因。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain why an answer is wrong by pointing to the grammar before the blank.","zh":"老師可能透過指出空格前的文法來解釋為何答案錯。"},{"en":"Good explanations help students understand causes rather than memorise results.","zh":"好解釋幫助學生理解原因，而不是死記結果。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the reason behind a situation.","zh":"這個短語引入某情況背後的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"different levels of","meaning":"不同程度的……","examples":[{"en":"Musicians with absolute pitch show different levels of the talent.","zh":"有絕對音感的音樂家展現不同程度的天賦。"},{"en":"Different levels of something means varying degrees of strength, skill or amount.","zh":"different levels of something 指強度、技能或數量上的不同程度。"},{"en":"Students in one class may have different levels of confidence in speaking English.","zh":"同一班學生可能有不同程度的英語口語信心。"},{"en":"Different levels suggest that an ability may develop gradually rather than appear fully formed.","zh":"不同程度顯示某能力可能逐步發展，而不是完整地突然出現。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe variation within a group.","zh":"這個短語幫助描述群體內差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"more and more evidence","meaning":"越來越多證據","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are finding more and more evidence for the importance of music lessons.","zh":"研究人員找到越來越多證據，支持音樂課的重要性。"},{"en":"More and more evidence means an increasing amount of information supporting an idea.","zh":"more and more evidence 指支持某想法的資料越來越多。"},{"en":"Teachers are finding more and more evidence that sleep affects student performance.","zh":"老師找到越來越多證據，顯示睡眠影響學生表現。"},{"en":"As evidence grows, a claim becomes harder to ignore.","zh":"隨着證據增加，某說法變得更難被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that support for an idea is increasing.","zh":"這個短語顯示對某想法的支持正在增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"evidence suggesting","meaning":"顯示……的證據","examples":[{"en":"There is evidence suggesting that music lessons are critical.","zh":"有證據顯示音樂課至關重要。"},{"en":"Evidence suggesting something is information that points toward a possible conclusion.","zh":"evidence suggesting something 指指向某個可能結論的資料。"},{"en":"There is evidence suggesting that regular reading improves vocabulary.","zh":"有證據顯示定期閱讀能改善詞彙。"},{"en":"Suggestive evidence may support an idea even before all details are fully proven.","zh":"顯示性的證據即使在所有細節完全證明前，也可能支持某想法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces cautious support from research or observation.","zh":"這個短語引入來自研究或觀察的謹慎支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be critical to","meaning":"對……至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Music lessons are critical to the development of absolute pitch.","zh":"音樂課對絕對音感的發展至關重要。"},{"en":"To be critical to something means to be extremely important for it.","zh":"be critical to something 指對某事極其重要。"},{"en":"Clear feedback is critical to improving academic writing.","zh":"清楚回饋對改善學術寫作至關重要。"},{"en":"If early music lessons are critical, missing them may reduce the chance of developing the skill.","zh":"如果早期音樂課至關重要，錯過它們可能降低發展技能的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor is central, not merely helpful.","zh":"這個短語顯示某因素是核心，而不只是有幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the development of","meaning":"……的發展","examples":[{"en":"Music lessons may be critical to the development of absolute pitch.","zh":"音樂課可能對絕對音感的發展至關重要。"},{"en":"The development of something is the process by which it grows, forms or improves.","zh":"the development of something 指某物成長、形成或改善的過程。"},{"en":"Reading aloud can support the development of pronunciation in young learners.","zh":"朗讀可以支持年幼學習者發音的發展。"},{"en":"Development takes time because skills usually grow through repeated experience.","zh":"發展需要時間，因為技能通常透過反覆經驗成長。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how something becomes stronger or more complete.","zh":"這個短語著重某物如何變得更強或更完整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in a survey of","meaning":"在一項關於……的調查中","examples":[{"en":"Researchers collected data in a survey of music students.","zh":"研究人員在一項關於音樂學生的調查中收集數據。"},{"en":"In a survey of a group means through a study that asks that group questions or collects data from them.","zh":"in a survey of a group 指透過向該群體提問或收集其數據的研究。"},{"en":"In a survey of parents, the school found that many wanted earlier notices.","zh":"在一項關於家長的調查中，學校發現許多人想要更早通知。"},{"en":"Surveys help researchers compare patterns across many people.","zh":"調查幫助研究人員比較許多人之間的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the group studied.","zh":"這個短語指出被研究的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"music conservatories","meaning":"音樂學院","examples":[{"en":"The survey included students in American music conservatories.","zh":"這項調查包括美國音樂學院的學生。"},{"en":"Music conservatories are specialised schools or colleges for advanced music training.","zh":"music conservatories 指提供高階音樂訓練的專門學校或學院。"},{"en":"A talented violinist may apply to music conservatories to study performance seriously.","zh":"有天賦的小提琴手可能申請音樂學院，認真學習演奏。"},{"en":"Conservatories attract students who practise music more intensively than ordinary learners.","zh":"音樂學院吸引比普通學習者更密集練習音樂的學生。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to institutions focused on professional music education.","zh":"這個短語指專注專業音樂教育的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"college programmes","meaning":"大學課程","examples":[{"en":"The survey also included students in college programmes.","zh":"這項調查也包括大學課程中的學生。"},{"en":"College programmes are organised courses of study offered by colleges or universities.","zh":"college programmes 指由學院或大學提供的有組織學習課程。"},{"en":"A student may join a college programme in music, business or engineering.","zh":"學生可能參加音樂、商科或工程的大學課程。"},{"en":"Including different college programmes can make a survey sample more varied.","zh":"包括不同大學課程，可以令調查樣本更多樣化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal courses at tertiary level.","zh":"這個短語指高等教育層面的正式課程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a whopping 32 per cent","meaning":"高達 32%","examples":[{"en":"A whopping 32 per cent of Asian students reported having absolute pitch.","zh":"高達 32% 的亞洲學生報稱有絕對音感。"},{"en":"A whopping 32 per cent means a surprisingly large 32 per cent.","zh":"a whopping 32 per cent 指令人驚訝地高的 32%。"},{"en":"A whopping 60 per cent of students chose online revision over printed notes.","zh":"高達 60% 的學生選擇網上溫習，而不是紙本筆記。"},{"en":"The word “whopping” emphasises that the number is bigger than expected.","zh":"“whopping” 這個詞強調數字比預期大。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and highlights a striking statistic.","zh":"這個短語較口語，突出驚人的統計數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Thirty-two per cent of Asian students reported absolute pitch, compared with 7 per cent of non-Asian students.","zh":"32% 的亞洲學生報稱有絕對音感，與 7% 的非亞洲學生相比。"},{"en":"Compared with introduces a contrast between two numbers, groups or situations.","zh":"compared with 用來引入兩個數字、群體或情況之間的對比。"},{"en":"The school library had 500 visitors this week, compared with 300 last week.","zh":"學校圖書館本週有 500 名訪客，與上週 300 名相比。"},{"en":"Comparing figures helps readers see the size of a difference clearly.","zh":"比較數字幫助讀者清楚看見差異大小。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in data description.","zh":"這個短語常用於數據描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"non-Asian students","meaning":"非亞洲學生","examples":[{"en":"Only 7 per cent of non-Asian students reported having absolute pitch.","zh":"只有 7% 的非亞洲學生報稱有絕對音感。"},{"en":"Non-Asian students are students who are not from Asian backgrounds.","zh":"non-Asian students 指並非亞洲背景的學生。"},{"en":"A survey may compare Asian and non-Asian students to look for cultural or educational patterns.","zh":"調查可能比較亞洲和非亞洲學生，以尋找文化或教育模式。"},{"en":"Such categories should be interpreted carefully because many factors can affect results.","zh":"這類分類應謹慎解讀，因為許多因素可以影響結果。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a comparison group in the study.","zh":"這個短語指出研究中的比較組別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"genetic tendency towards","meaning":"對……的基因傾向","examples":[{"en":"The result might suggest a genetic tendency towards absolute pitch.","zh":"這個結果可能顯示對絕對音感的基因傾向。"},{"en":"A genetic tendency towards something is an inherited leaning that makes it more likely.","zh":"genetic tendency towards something 指令某事更可能發生的遺傳傾向。"},{"en":"A family history of poor eyesight may suggest a genetic tendency towards vision problems.","zh":"視力差的家族史可能顯示對視力問題的基因傾向。"},{"en":"A genetic tendency can increase probability, but it does not guarantee the outcome.","zh":"基因傾向可以增加可能性，但不保證結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inherited likelihood.","zh":"這個短語描述遺傳上的可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"much of the difference","meaning":"大部分差異","examples":[{"en":"Gregersen believes music lessons probably explain much of the difference.","zh":"Gregersen 認為音樂課很可能解釋大部分差異。"},{"en":"Much of the difference means a large part of the gap between two groups or results.","zh":"much of the difference 指兩組或兩個結果之間差距的大部分。"},{"en":"Better sleep may explain much of the difference between two students’ concentration levels.","zh":"較好睡眠可能解釋兩名學生專注程度的大部分差異。"},{"en":"Explaining much of the difference helps identify which factor matters most.","zh":"解釋大部分差異有助找出哪個因素最重要。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean every part of the difference is explained.","zh":"這個短語不表示差異的每一部分都被解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"for one thing","meaning":"首先；其中一點是","examples":[{"en":"For one thing, students with absolute pitch started lessons earlier.","zh":"其中一點是，有絕對音感的學生較早開始上課。"},{"en":"For one thing introduces one reason or example among several.","zh":"for one thing 用來引入幾個理由或例子中的其中一個。"},{"en":"This study plan works well; for one thing, it gives students time to review mistakes.","zh":"這個學習計劃有效；首先，它給學生時間檢討錯誤。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when they are beginning to explain why they believe something.","zh":"作者開始解釋自己為何相信某事時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It suggests more reasons may follow.","zh":"它暗示後面可能還有更多理由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"on average","meaning":"平均而言","examples":[{"en":"Students with absolute pitch started lessons, on average, at age five.","zh":"有絕對音感的學生平均而言五歲開始上課。"},{"en":"On average means considering the typical value across a group.","zh":"on average 指考慮整個群體的典型數值。"},{"en":"Students in the class read for 20 minutes a day on average.","zh":"班中學生平均而言每天閱讀 20 分鐘。"},{"en":"Averages help describe a group, even though individuals may differ.","zh":"平均數幫助描述群體，即使個別人士可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting survey or research results.","zh":"這個短語適合報告調查或研究結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"around the age of","meaning":"大約在……歲時","examples":[{"en":"Students without absolute pitch started around the age of eight.","zh":"沒有絕對音感的學生大約在八歲時開始。"},{"en":"Around the age of means approximately at that age.","zh":"around the age of 指大約在某個年齡。"},{"en":"Many children begin formal piano lessons around the age of six.","zh":"許多孩子大約在六歲時開始正式鋼琴課。"},{"en":"Starting around a certain age can matter if early development is important.","zh":"如果早期發展重要，大約在某年齡開始就可能有影響。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate age, not an exact birthday.","zh":"這個短語給出約略年齡，而不是確切生日。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the type of music lessons","meaning":"音樂課的類型","examples":[{"en":"The type of music lessons may affect the development of absolute pitch.","zh":"音樂課的類型可能影響絕對音感的發展。"},{"en":"The type of music lessons means the teaching method, content or style used in music training.","zh":"the type of music lessons 指音樂訓練所用的教學方法、內容或風格。"},{"en":"Some music lessons focus on listening, while others focus on reading notes.","zh":"有些音樂課專注於聆聽，另一些則專注於讀譜。"},{"en":"Different lesson types can train different musical habits.","zh":"不同課堂類型可以訓練不同音樂習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that how lessons are taught may matter as much as when they begin.","zh":"這個短語暗示課堂如何教，可能和何時開始一樣重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be favoured in","meaning":"在……受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Certain teaching methods are favoured in Asia.","zh":"某些教學方法在亞洲受歡迎。"},{"en":"To be favoured in a place means to be preferred or commonly chosen there.","zh":"be favoured in a place 指在某地較受偏好或常被選擇。"},{"en":"Group practice may be favoured in some schools because it encourages teamwork.","zh":"小組練習可能在某些學校受歡迎，因為它鼓勵團隊合作。"},{"en":"A method favoured in one culture may train skills differently from methods used elsewhere.","zh":"在某文化中受歡迎的方法，可能與其他地方的方法訓練出不同技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes local preference or popularity.","zh":"這個短語描述本地偏好或普及程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the Suzuki method","meaning":"鈴木教學法","examples":[{"en":"The Suzuki method often focuses on playing by ear.","zh":"鈴木教學法常專注於憑聽覺演奏。"},{"en":"The Suzuki method is a music-teaching approach that emphasises early listening, imitation and repeated practice.","zh":"Suzuki method 指強調早期聆聽、模仿和反覆練習的音樂教學方法。"},{"en":"A child learning violin through the Suzuki method may hear pieces many times before reading the score.","zh":"透過鈴木教學法學小提琴的孩子，可能在讀譜前已多次聽過樂曲。"},{"en":"This method may support pitch memory because children listen closely from a young age.","zh":"這種方法可能支持音高記憶，因為孩子從年幼起仔細聆聽。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific approach to music education.","zh":"這個短語命名一種特定音樂教育方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"專注於","examples":[{"en":"Some music lessons focus on playing by ear.","zh":"有些音樂課專注於憑聽覺演奏。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give most attention to it.","zh":"focus on something 指把大部分注意力放在某事上。"},{"en":"A grammar lesson may focus on articles before moving to complex sentences.","zh":"文法課可能先專注於冠詞，再進入複雜句。"},{"en":"What a lesson focuses on affects what students practise most.","zh":"課堂專注於甚麼，會影響學生最多練習甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the main area of attention.","zh":"這個短語顯示主要注意範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"learning the names of musical notes","meaning":"學習音符名稱","examples":[{"en":"Some lessons focus on learning the names of musical notes.","zh":"有些課堂專注於學習音符名稱。"},{"en":"Learning the names of musical notes means studying labels such as A, B, C or do, re, mi.","zh":"learning the names of musical notes 指學習 A、B、C 或 do、re、mi 等標籤。"},{"en":"Beginners may learn the names of musical notes before reading simple sheet music.","zh":"初學者可能在閱讀簡單樂譜前先學習音符名稱。"},{"en":"Naming notes helps students connect sounds with written symbols.","zh":"命名音符幫助學生把聲音與書面符號連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a basic part of music education.","zh":"這個短語描述音樂教育的基本部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be commonly used in","meaning":"在……更常用","examples":[{"en":"Other methods are more commonly used in the United States.","zh":"其他方法在美國更常用。"},{"en":"To be commonly used in a place means to be used often there.","zh":"be commonly used in a place 指在某地經常被使用。"},{"en":"Online homework platforms are commonly used in many schools today.","zh":"網上功課平台現今在許多學校常用。"},{"en":"A method commonly used in one country may reflect that country’s teaching culture.","zh":"在某國常用的方法，可能反映該國教學文化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regular or widespread use.","zh":"這個短語描述經常或廣泛使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"tend to emphasise","meaning":"往往強調","examples":[{"en":"Music lessons in the United States tend to emphasise relative pitch.","zh":"美國的音樂課往往強調相對音感。"},{"en":"Tend to emphasise means usually give more attention or importance to something.","zh":"tend to emphasise 指通常較重視或給予更多注意。"},{"en":"Some schools tend to emphasise exam skills more than creative thinking.","zh":"有些學校往往強調考試技巧多於創意思考。"},{"en":"If lessons emphasise relative pitch, students may practise comparison more than exact note naming.","zh":"如果課堂強調相對音感，學生可能較多練習比較，而不是準確命名音符。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a general teaching tendency.","zh":"這個短語描述一般教學傾向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"learning scales","meaning":"學習音階","examples":[{"en":"Many US methods emphasise learning scales.","zh":"許多美國方法強調學習音階。"},{"en":"Learning scales means practising ordered sets of musical notes that move step by step.","zh":"learning scales 指練習按順序逐步移動的一組音符。"},{"en":"Piano students often begin lessons by learning scales to build finger control and pitch awareness.","zh":"鋼琴學生常透過學習音階開始課堂，以建立手指控制和音高意識。"},{"en":"Scales help musicians understand relationships between notes.","zh":"音階幫助音樂家理解音符之間的關係。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a common foundation of music training.","zh":"這個短語指音樂訓練的常見基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"in a relative pitch way","meaning":"以相對音感方式","examples":[{"en":"Some methods teach scales in a relative pitch way.","zh":"有些方法以相對音感方式教授音階。"},{"en":"In a relative pitch way means by focusing on the distance between notes rather than their absolute names.","zh":"in a relative pitch way 指著重音符之間的距離，而不是其絕對名稱。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to hear how far one note moves from another in a relative pitch way.","zh":"老師可能要求學生以相對音感方式聽出一個音離另一個音有多遠。"},{"en":"Teaching in this way trains comparison more than isolated note recognition.","zh":"這種教法訓練比較能力多於孤立音符辨認。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a method based on relationships between sounds.","zh":"這個短語描述基於聲音關係的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"pre-school music programmes","meaning":"學前音樂課程","examples":[{"en":"Japanese pre-school music programmes train children to recognise pitch.","zh":"日本學前音樂課程訓練孩子辨認音高。"},{"en":"Pre-school music programmes are music classes designed for children before primary school.","zh":"pre-school music programmes 指為小學前兒童設計的音樂課。"},{"en":"A pre-school music programme may use songs, clapping games and simple instruments.","zh":"學前音樂課程可能使用歌曲、拍手遊戲和簡單樂器。"},{"en":"Early programmes can shape listening habits before formal school begins.","zh":"早期課程可以在正式上學前塑造聆聽習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to structured music learning for very young children.","zh":"這個短語指為非常年幼孩子而設的有結構音樂學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"listen to notes played on a piano","meaning":"聆聽鋼琴彈出的音符","examples":[{"en":"Children listen to notes played on a piano.","zh":"孩子聆聽鋼琴彈出的音符。"},{"en":"To listen to notes played on a piano means to hear individual piano sounds for training or recognition.","zh":"listen to notes played on a piano 指聽單個鋼琴聲音以作訓練或辨認。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask children to listen to notes played on a piano and then point to matching cards.","zh":"老師可能要求孩子聆聽鋼琴彈出的音符，然後指出相應卡片。"},{"en":"Repeated listening helps children connect sounds with names or colours.","zh":"反覆聆聽幫助孩子把聲音與名稱或顏色連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple ear-training activity.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單的聽覺訓練活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"hold up","meaning":"舉起","examples":[{"en":"Children hold up a coloured flag to signal the pitch.","zh":"孩子舉起彩色旗來表示音高。"},{"en":"To hold up something means to raise it so others can see it.","zh":"hold up something 指把某物舉起，讓其他人看見。"},{"en":"In class, students may hold up answer cards after hearing a question.","zh":"在課堂上，學生聽到問題後可能舉起答案卡。"},{"en":"Holding up a flag lets the teacher see each child’s response quickly.","zh":"舉起旗幟讓老師快速看到每個孩子的回應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visible response action.","zh":"這個短語描述可見的回應動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"coloured flag","meaning":"彩色旗","examples":[{"en":"Children use a coloured flag to signal pitch.","zh":"孩子使用彩色旗來表示音高。"},{"en":"A coloured flag is a small flag with a particular colour used as a sign or answer.","zh":"coloured flag 指帶有特定顏色、用作信號或答案的小旗。"},{"en":"A teacher may give each group a coloured flag to show when they are ready.","zh":"老師可能給每組一面彩色旗，用來表示他們已準備好。"},{"en":"Colours can help young learners connect abstract sounds with visible symbols.","zh":"顏色可以幫助年幼學習者把抽象聲音與可見符號連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple classroom tool.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單課堂工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"signal the pitch","meaning":"表示音高","examples":[{"en":"The coloured flag is used to signal the pitch.","zh":"彩色旗被用來表示音高。"},{"en":"To signal the pitch means to show which pitch has been heard or recognised.","zh":"signal the pitch 指顯示聽到或辨認的是哪個音高。"},{"en":"A student may signal the pitch by pointing to the correct note name on a chart.","zh":"學生可能透過指向圖表上正確音符名稱來表示音高。"},{"en":"Signalling pitch lets teachers check whether children can identify sounds accurately.","zh":"表示音高讓老師檢查孩子能否準確辨認聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase describes showing a listening answer.","zh":"這個短語描述展示聆聽答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"distinct cultural difference","meaning":"明顯的文化差異","examples":[{"en":"Gregersen says there is a distinct cultural difference.","zh":"Gregersen 說存在明顯的文化差異。"},{"en":"A distinct cultural difference is a clear difference between the habits, values or practices of cultures.","zh":"distinct cultural difference 指文化在習慣、價值或做法上的清楚差異。"},{"en":"There may be a distinct cultural difference in how schools teach children to speak in class.","zh":"不同文化在學校如何教孩子課堂發言方面，可能有明顯文化差異。"},{"en":"Cultural differences can affect learning because children practise different skills early.","zh":"文化差異可以影響學習，因為孩子早期練習不同技能。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a clear contrast between cultures.","zh":"這個短語突出文化之間的清楚對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"predict that","meaning":"預測","examples":[{"en":"Deutsch predicts that further studies will reveal hidden absolute pitch.","zh":"Deutsch 預測進一步研究會揭示隱藏的絕對音感。"},{"en":"To predict that means to say what is likely to happen in the future.","zh":"predict that 指說明未來很可能發生甚麼。"},{"en":"A teacher may predict that students will improve if they practise speaking weekly.","zh":"老師可能預測，如果學生每週練習口語，他們會進步。"},{"en":"Predictions are stronger when they are based on evidence rather than hope.","zh":"當預測基於證據而不是希望，它會更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an expected future result.","zh":"這個短語引入預期的未來結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"further studies","meaning":"進一步研究","examples":[{"en":"Further studies may reveal absolute pitch in more people.","zh":"進一步研究可能在更多人身上揭示絕對音感。"},{"en":"Further studies are additional research carried out after earlier work.","zh":"further studies 指在早前研究之後進行的額外研究。"},{"en":"Further studies may test whether younger children respond differently from adults.","zh":"進一步研究可能測試年幼孩子是否與成人反應不同。"},{"en":"More research can confirm, challenge or refine earlier findings.","zh":"更多研究可以確認、挑戰或修正早前發現。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the topic is not yet fully settled.","zh":"這個短語顯示議題尚未完全解決。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"latent form","meaning":"潛在形式","examples":[{"en":"Absolute pitch may exist inside all of us in a latent form.","zh":"絕對音感可能以潛在形式存在於我們所有人心中。"},{"en":"A latent form is a hidden or undeveloped state that may appear under the right conditions.","zh":"latent form 指隱藏或未發展的狀態，可能在合適條件下出現。"},{"en":"A student may have leadership in a latent form until a group project gives him a chance.","zh":"學生可能有潛在形式的領導能力，直到小組項目給他機會。"},{"en":"If ability is latent, training may be needed to bring it out.","zh":"如果能力是潛在的，就可能需要訓練把它引發出來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes potential that exists but is not yet obvious.","zh":"這個短語描述存在但尚不明顯的潛力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"inside all of us","meaning":"在我們所有人心中","examples":[{"en":"Deutsch believes absolute pitch may exist inside all of us.","zh":"Deutsch 相信絕對音感可能存在於我們所有人心中。"},{"en":"Inside all of us means present in every person, at least as a possibility.","zh":"inside all of us 指存在於每個人之中，至少作為一種可能性。"},{"en":"Curiosity exists inside all of us, but school can either encourage or weaken it.","zh":"好奇心存在於我們所有人心中，但學校可以鼓勵或削弱它。"},{"en":"If a skill exists inside all of us, the main question becomes how to develop it.","zh":"如果某技能存在於我們所有人心中，主要問題就變成如何發展它。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a shared human potential.","zh":"這個短語暗示共同的人類潛能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"Western emphasis on","meaning":"西方對……的重視","examples":[{"en":"The Western emphasis on relative pitch may obscure absolute pitch.","zh":"西方對相對音感的重視可能掩蓋絕對音感。"},{"en":"Western emphasis on something means the importance given to it in Western teaching or culture.","zh":"Western emphasis on something 指西方教學或文化中給予某事的重要性。"},{"en":"The Western emphasis on individual expression may differ from cultures that stress group harmony.","zh":"西方對個人表達的重視，可能不同於強調群體和諧的文化。"},{"en":"If teaching emphasises one skill, other possible abilities may receive less attention.","zh":"如果教學強調一項技能，其他可能能力可能較少受到注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a cultural or educational focus.","zh":"這個短語描述文化或教育上的焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"obscure it","meaning":"掩蓋它","examples":[{"en":"The emphasis on relative pitch may obscure absolute pitch.","zh":"對相對音感的重視可能掩蓋絕對音感。"},{"en":"To obscure something means to hide it, make it unclear or prevent people from noticing it.","zh":"obscure something 指隱藏、使不清楚或阻止人注意到某事。"},{"en":"Too many difficult words can obscure the main idea of an essay.","zh":"太多困難詞語可以掩蓋文章主旨。"},{"en":"If one teaching method dominates, it may obscure other abilities students have.","zh":"如果一種教學方法佔主導，它可能掩蓋學生擁有的其他能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making something less visible or less understood.","zh":"這個短語描述令某事較不明顯或較難理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contend","meaning":"主張；認為","examples":[{"en":"Deutsch contends that we may all have the potential for absolute pitch.","zh":"Deutsch 主張我們可能都有絕對音感的潛力。"},{"en":"To contend means to argue or state a position strongly.","zh":"contend 指有力地提出或主張某立場。"},{"en":"A teacher may contend that daily reading is more useful than last-minute revision.","zh":"老師可能主張每日閱讀比臨急溫習更有用。"},{"en":"People usually contend something when they want others to take their argument seriously.","zh":"人們通常在希望他人認真看待其論點時使用 contend。"},{"en":"This word is formal and often used in academic discussion.","zh":"這個詞較正式，常用於學術討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"end up concluding that","meaning":"最終得出結論認為","examples":[{"en":"Scientists may end up concluding that we are all born with this potential.","zh":"科學家可能最終得出結論認為，我們天生都有這種潛力。"},{"en":"To end up concluding that means to finally reach a judgement after thinking or researching.","zh":"end up concluding that 指經思考或研究後，最終得出判斷。"},{"en":"After comparing many essays, a teacher may end up concluding that students need clearer examples.","zh":"比較多篇文章後，老師可能最終得出結論認為學生需要更清楚例子。"},{"en":"Research can begin with one question and end up reaching a surprising conclusion.","zh":"研究可以從一個問題開始，最終得出令人驚訝的結論。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the final result of a reasoning process.","zh":"這個短語強調推理過程的最終結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be born with","meaning":"天生具有","examples":[{"en":"We may all be born with the potential to acquire absolute pitch.","zh":"我們可能天生具有獲得絕對音感的潛力。"},{"en":"To be born with something means to have it naturally from birth.","zh":"be born with something 指從出生起自然擁有某物。"},{"en":"Some children are born with a strong sense of rhythm.","zh":"有些孩子天生具有很強節奏感。"},{"en":"Being born with potential does not mean the skill will develop without practice.","zh":"天生具有潛力不代表技能會在沒有練習下發展。"},{"en":"This phrase points to natural ability or inherited tendency.","zh":"這個短語指自然能力或遺傳傾向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the potential to acquire","meaning":"獲得……的潛力","examples":[{"en":"People may be born with the potential to acquire very fine-grained absolute pitch.","zh":"人們可能天生具有獲得非常精細絕對音感的潛力。"},{"en":"The potential to acquire something is the possibility of gaining it under the right conditions.","zh":"the potential to acquire something 指在合適條件下取得某物的可能性。"},{"en":"A student may have the potential to acquire fluent English through regular speaking practice.","zh":"學生可能透過定期口語練習，擁有獲得流利英語的潛力。"},{"en":"Potential becomes real ability only when experience, effort and opportunity support it.","zh":"只有當經驗、努力和機會支持時，潛力才會變成真正能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes possible development, not guaranteed success.","zh":"這個短語描述可能發展，而不是保證成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"fine-grained absolute pitch","meaning":"非常精細的絕對音感","examples":[{"en":"Deutsch believes people may develop very fine-grained absolute pitch.","zh":"Deutsch 相信人們可能發展出非常精細的絕對音感。"},{"en":"Fine-grained absolute pitch is a very precise form of pitch recognition.","zh":"fine-grained absolute pitch 指非常精準的音高辨認能力。"},{"en":"A musician with fine-grained pitch awareness may notice tiny differences that others miss.","zh":"有精細音高意識的音樂家可能注意到其他人錯過的微小差異。"},{"en":"Fine-grained ability matters when small sound changes affect meaning or musical accuracy.","zh":"當細小聲音變化影響意思或音樂準確度時，精細能力很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a detailed and highly sensitive version of absolute pitch.","zh":"這個短語描述細緻且高度敏感的絕對音感版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a matter of","meaning":"……的問題","examples":[{"en":"The problem may be a matter of life getting in the way.","zh":"問題可能是生活阻礙了發展。"},{"en":"A matter of something means the issue is mainly about that thing.","zh":"a matter of something 指問題主要關乎某事。"},{"en":"Improving writing is often a matter of practice, feedback and careful revision.","zh":"改善寫作常是練習、回饋和仔細修改的問題。"},{"en":"If a problem is a matter of timing, changing when students learn may solve it.","zh":"如果問題是時間安排的問題，改變學生何時學習可能解決它。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main nature of a problem.","zh":"這個短語指出問題的主要性質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"life getting in the way","meaning":"生活阻礙了發展","examples":[{"en":"Deutsch suggests that life simply gets in the way of developing absolute pitch.","zh":"Deutsch 指出，生活只是阻礙了絕對音感的發展。"},{"en":"Life getting in the way means ordinary experiences, habits or pressures prevent something from developing.","zh":"life getting in the way 指日常經驗、習慣或壓力阻止某事發展。"},{"en":"A student may plan to practise piano daily, but homework and travel get in the way.","zh":"學生可能計劃每天練琴，但功課和交通阻礙了練習。"},{"en":"If life gets in the way, potential may remain hidden instead of becoming a skill.","zh":"如果生活造成阻礙，潛力可能一直隱藏，而不是變成技能。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a simple explanation for why development does not happen.","zh":"這個短語簡單解釋為何發展沒有發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete the notes below","meaning":"完成以下筆記","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to complete the notes below using words from the box.","zh":"考生需要使用方框中的詞語完成以下筆記。"},{"en":"To complete the notes below means to fill in missing information in the notes that follow.","zh":"complete the notes below 指填寫下方筆記中的缺失資料。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should read the full notes before choosing answers.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先閱讀完整筆記，再選答案。"},{"en":"Completing notes accurately requires matching grammar, meaning and word limits.","zh":"準確完成筆記需要配合文法、意思和字數限制。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"using words from the box","meaning":"使用方框中的詞語","examples":[{"en":"The notes should be completed using words from the box.","zh":"筆記應使用方框中的詞語完成。"},{"en":"Using words from the box means choosing answers only from the given set of words.","zh":"using words from the box 指只從所給詞語組中選擇答案。"},{"en":"Students lose marks if they write their own words instead of using words from the box.","zh":"如果學生寫自己的字，而不是使用方框中的詞語，可能會失分。"},{"en":"The word box limits possible answers and helps guide the choice.","zh":"詞語方框限制可能答案，並幫助引導選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase tells candidates where the answers must come from.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生答案必須來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"write your answers in boxes","meaning":"在方格內寫上答案","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write their answers in boxes on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生在答題紙上的方格內寫上答案。"},{"en":"To write your answers in boxes means to put each answer in the numbered space provided.","zh":"write your answers in boxes 指把每個答案寫在所提供的編號空格內。"},{"en":"In an exam, students should write clearly in boxes so markers can read their answers.","zh":"在考試中，學生應清楚地在方格內寫答案，讓評卷員能閱讀。"},{"en":"Writing outside the boxes may cause confusion or marking problems.","zh":"寫在方格外可能造成混亂或評分問題。"},{"en":"This phrase gives practical instructions for answer placement.","zh":"這個短語提供答案位置的實用指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"on your answer sheet","meaning":"在答題紙上","examples":[{"en":"Answers should be written on your answer sheet.","zh":"答案應寫在答題紙上。"},{"en":"On your answer sheet means in the official paper or form where answers are recorded.","zh":"on your answer sheet 指在記錄答案的正式紙張或表格上。"},{"en":"A candidate may know the answer but lose marks if it is not written on the answer sheet.","zh":"考生可能知道答案，但如果沒有寫在答題紙上，可能會失分。"},{"en":"Exam instructions often repeat this phrase to prevent students from writing only on the question paper.","zh":"考試指示常重複這個短語，以免學生只寫在題目紙上。"},{"en":"This phrase tells students where their final answers must appear.","zh":"這個短語告訴學生最終答案必須出現在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"research is being conducted into","meaning":"正在就……進行研究","examples":[{"en":"Research is being conducted into the mysterious musical ability known as perfect pitch.","zh":"正在就被稱為絕對音感的神秘音樂能力進行研究。"},{"en":"Research is being conducted into something means experts are actively studying it.","zh":"research is being conducted into something 指專家正在積極研究某事。"},{"en":"Research is being conducted into how screen time affects teenagers’ sleep.","zh":"正在就螢幕時間如何影響青少年睡眠進行研究。"},{"en":"When research is being conducted, the final answer may not yet be settled.","zh":"當研究正在進行，最終答案可能尚未確定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an ongoing investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述正在進行的調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"mysterious musical ability","meaning":"神秘的音樂能力","examples":[{"en":"Perfect pitch is a mysterious musical ability.","zh":"絕對音感是一種神秘的音樂能力。"},{"en":"A mysterious musical ability is a music-related skill that researchers cannot fully explain.","zh":"mysterious musical ability 指研究人員未能完全解釋的音樂相關技能。"},{"en":"A child who can remember songs after one hearing may seem to have a mysterious musical ability.","zh":"聽一次就能記住歌曲的孩子，可能看似有神秘的音樂能力。"},{"en":"Such abilities attract research because they raise questions about talent and training.","zh":"這類能力會吸引研究，因為它們引出關於天賦和訓練的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase combines musical skill with scientific uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語結合音樂技能和科學不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"known as","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"The ability is known as perfect pitch.","zh":"這種能力被稱為絕對音感。"},{"en":"Known as means called by a particular name.","zh":"known as 指以某個特定名稱稱呼。"},{"en":"Hong Kong’s old airport was known as Kai Tak.","zh":"香港舊機場被稱為啟德。"},{"en":"When a term is known as something, that name helps readers identify it.","zh":"當一個術語被稱為某名，該名稱幫助讀者識別它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a name or label.","zh":"這個短語引入名稱或標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"name and sing","meaning":"說出並唱出","examples":[{"en":"Musicians with this talent can name and sing a note without reference.","zh":"有這種天賦的音樂家可以無需參照便說出並唱出一個音。"},{"en":"To name and sing a note means to identify its name and then produce that pitch with the voice.","zh":"name and sing a note 指辨認音符名稱，然後用聲音唱出該音高。"},{"en":"A music teacher may ask students to name and sing C before playing it on the piano.","zh":"音樂老師可能要求學生在彈鋼琴前先說出並唱出 C 音。"},{"en":"Naming and singing a note shows both recognition and vocal control.","zh":"說出並唱出一個音，顯示辨認能力和聲音控制。"},{"en":"This phrase combines hearing, naming and producing sound.","zh":"這個短語結合聆聽、命名和發聲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"without reference to","meaning":"無需參照……","examples":[{"en":"They can identify a note without reference to another note.","zh":"他們可以無需參照另一個音符便辨認一個音。"},{"en":"Without reference to something means without using it as a guide or comparison.","zh":"without reference to something 指不用某事作指引或比較。"},{"en":"A student may answer a question without reference to notes if she remembers the concept well.","zh":"如果學生很熟悉概念，可能無需參照筆記就回答問題。"},{"en":"Perfect pitch works without reference to another note, unlike relative pitch.","zh":"絕對音感無需參照另一音符也能運作，不同於相對音感。"},{"en":"This phrase shows independence from outside comparison.","zh":"這個短語顯示不依賴外部比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"separate someone from","meaning":"將某人與……區分開","examples":[{"en":"This ability separates them from the majority.","zh":"這種能力將他們與大多數人區分開。"},{"en":"To separate someone from a group means to make them different from that group.","zh":"separate someone from a group 指令某人不同於該群體。"},{"en":"Strong listening skills can separate a good language learner from the majority.","zh":"強聆聽能力可以將好的語言學習者與大多數人區分開。"},{"en":"A rare ability separates people from others because it allows them to do something unusual.","zh":"罕有能力會把人與其他人區分開，因為它讓人做到不尋常的事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distinction or difference.","zh":"這個短語描述區別或差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the majority","meaning":"大多數人","examples":[{"en":"Most musicians have only relative pitch.","zh":"大多數音樂家只有相對音感。"},{"en":"The majority means most people or the larger part of a group.","zh":"the majority 指大多數人或群體中的較大部分。"},{"en":"The majority of students in the class prefer examples before rules.","zh":"班中大多數學生較喜歡先看例子再學規則。"},{"en":"If a skill separates someone from the majority, only a smaller group has it.","zh":"如果某技能將某人與大多數人區分開，就只有較小群體擁有它。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when comparing most people with a smaller group.","zh":"這個短語用於比較大多數人和較小群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the product of","meaning":"……的產物","examples":[{"en":"Researchers ask whether the skill is the product of genes or early lessons.","zh":"研究人員問這項技能是基因還是早期課堂的產物。"},{"en":"The product of something means the result produced by it.","zh":"the product of something 指由某事產生的結果。"},{"en":"A student’s strong writing may be the product of reading, practice and feedback.","zh":"學生強大的寫作能力可能是閱讀、練習和回饋的產物。"},{"en":"If absolute pitch is the product of both genes and lessons, neither factor alone explains it fully.","zh":"如果絕對音感是基因和課堂兩者的產物，單一因素就不能完全解釋它。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a result with its causes.","zh":"這個短語把結果與原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"genetic inheritance","meaning":"基因遺傳","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers believe perfect pitch may depend on genetic inheritance.","zh":"有些研究人員相信絕對音感可能取決於基因遺傳。"},{"en":"Genetic inheritance is the passing of traits from parents to children through genes.","zh":"genetic inheritance 指透過基因把特徵由父母傳給孩子。"},{"en":"Eye colour is influenced by genetic inheritance.","zh":"眼睛顏色受基因遺傳影響。"},{"en":"If perfect pitch involves genetic inheritance, relatives may show the ability more often.","zh":"如果絕對音感涉及基因遺傳，親屬可能較常展現這種能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes biological transmission across generations.","zh":"這個短語描述跨代的生物傳遞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"early exposure to","meaning":"早期接觸……","examples":[{"en":"The skill may result from early exposure to music lessons.","zh":"這項技能可能來自早期接觸音樂課。"},{"en":"Early exposure to something means contact with it at a young age.","zh":"early exposure to something 指在年幼時接觸某事。"},{"en":"Early exposure to English stories can help children feel comfortable with the language.","zh":"早期接觸英語故事可以幫助孩子對該語言感到自在。"},{"en":"Early exposure matters because young learners may absorb patterns quickly.","zh":"早期接觸很重要，因為年幼學習者可能快速吸收模式。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the importance of first contact during childhood.","zh":"這個短語突出童年第一次接觸的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a combination of both","meaning":"兩者的結合","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers believe absolute pitch comes from a combination of both.","zh":"有些研究人員相信絕對音感來自兩者的結合。"},{"en":"A combination of both means two factors working together rather than one alone.","zh":"a combination of both 指兩個因素共同作用，而不是只有其中一個。"},{"en":"Good exam results often come from a combination of both ability and consistent revision.","zh":"好考試成績常來自能力和持續溫習兩者的結合。"},{"en":"If two factors combine, removing either one may weaken the final result.","zh":"如果兩個因素結合，移除其中一個可能削弱最終結果。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids choosing only one explanation.","zh":"這個短語避免只選擇一個解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"seek a link between","meaning":"尋找……之間的關聯","examples":[{"en":"One research team sought a link between perfect pitch and tone languages.","zh":"一個研究團隊尋找絕對音感與聲調語言之間的關聯。"},{"en":"To seek a link between two things means to look for a connection between them.","zh":"seek a link between two things 指尋找兩件事之間的連繫。"},{"en":"Doctors may seek a link between poor sleep and headaches in teenagers.","zh":"醫生可能尋找青少年睡眠不足與頭痛之間的關聯。"},{"en":"Finding a link can suggest that one factor helps explain another.","zh":"找到關聯可以顯示一個因素有助解釋另一個因素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes searching for a relationship.","zh":"這個短語描述尋找關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"high number of","meaning":"大量的……","examples":[{"en":"Researchers tried to explain the high number of Asian speakers with perfect pitch.","zh":"研究人員試圖解釋大量有絕對音感的亞洲說話者。"},{"en":"A high number of means many people or cases compared with what is expected.","zh":"high number of 指人數或個案數量相比預期多。"},{"en":"A school may investigate a high number of late arrivals on rainy days.","zh":"學校可能調查雨天大量學生遲到的情況。"},{"en":"A high number of cases can suggest that a shared factor is involved.","zh":"大量個案可以顯示可能有共同因素參與。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on a large count.","zh":"這個短語著重大數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"on different occasions","meaning":"在不同場合；在不同時間","examples":[{"en":"Speakers recited words on different occasions.","zh":"說話者在不同時間朗讀詞語。"},{"en":"On different occasions means at separate times or in separate instances.","zh":"on different occasions 指在分開的時間或不同次數中。"},{"en":"A teacher may test the same vocabulary on different occasions to check long-term memory.","zh":"老師可能在不同時間測試同一組詞彙，以檢查長期記憶。"},{"en":"Repeating a task on different occasions helps show whether results are stable.","zh":"在不同場合重複任務，幫助顯示結果是否穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase is similar to “on different days” but can refer to any separate events.","zh":"這個短語接近 “on different days”，但可指任何分開事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"in terms of","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"The results were compared in terms of pitch.","zh":"結果就音高而言被比較。"},{"en":"In terms of means considering one particular aspect of something.","zh":"in terms of 指從某一特定方面考慮某事。"},{"en":"Two schools may be compared in terms of class size, exam results and facilities.","zh":"兩間學校可以就班級人數、考試成績和設施而言作比較。"},{"en":"Comparing results in terms of pitch focuses on sound height rather than meaning or speed.","zh":"就音高比較結果，焦點在聲音高低，而不是意思或速度。"},{"en":"This phrase tells readers the basis of comparison.","zh":"這個短語告訴讀者比較的基準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a separate study","meaning":"另一項研究","examples":[{"en":"A separate study examined music-teaching approaches.","zh":"另一項研究審視了音樂教學方法。"},{"en":"A separate study is another piece of research carried out apart from the first one.","zh":"a separate study 指與第一項研究分開進行的另一項研究。"},{"en":"A separate study may examine whether students learn better online or in person.","zh":"另一項研究可能審視學生網上學習還是面授學習較好。"},{"en":"Separate studies can support each other if they point to similar conclusions.","zh":"如果分開研究指向相似結論，它們可以互相支持。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces additional research.","zh":"這個短語引入額外研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"approach to teaching music","meaning":"音樂教學方法","examples":[{"en":"The approach to teaching music may affect absolute pitch.","zh":"音樂教學方法可能影響絕對音感。"},{"en":"An approach to teaching music is the method or style used to help students learn music.","zh":"approach to teaching music 指幫助學生學習音樂所用的方法或風格。"},{"en":"One approach may begin with listening, while another begins with reading notes.","zh":"一種方法可能從聆聽開始，另一種可能從讀譜開始。"},{"en":"Teaching approach matters because students practise what the method values most.","zh":"教學方法很重要，因為學生會練習該方法最重視的技能。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how music is taught.","zh":"這個短語著重音樂如何被教授。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"emphasise playing by ear","meaning":"強調憑聽覺演奏","examples":[{"en":"Many Asian cultures emphasise playing by ear.","zh":"許多亞洲文化強調憑聽覺演奏。"},{"en":"To emphasise playing by ear means to give special importance to learning music through listening.","zh":"emphasise playing by ear 指特別重視透過聆聽學習音樂。"},{"en":"A violin teacher may emphasise playing by ear before introducing written scores.","zh":"小提琴老師可能在引入書面樂譜前，強調憑聽覺演奏。"},{"en":"This emphasis can train children to connect sounds directly with actions.","zh":"這種重視可以訓練孩子把聲音直接與動作連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts listening-based teaching with note-reading-based teaching.","zh":"這個短語把聆聽式教學與讀譜式教學作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"基於……","examples":[{"en":"The US method was based on the relative pitch approach.","zh":"美國方法基於相對音感方法。"},{"en":"To be based on something means to use it as the foundation or main idea.","zh":"be based on something 指以某事作為基礎或主要想法。"},{"en":"A grammar lesson may be based on common mistakes from students’ essays.","zh":"文法課可能基於學生作文中的常見錯誤。"},{"en":"If a method is based on relative pitch, comparison between notes becomes central.","zh":"如果方法基於相對音感，音符之間的比較就變得核心。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the foundation of a system or method.","zh":"這個短語解釋系統或方法的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"relative pitch approach","meaning":"相對音感方法","examples":[{"en":"The US method often uses the relative pitch approach.","zh":"美國方法常使用相對音感方法。"},{"en":"The relative pitch approach teaches students to understand notes by comparing them with other notes.","zh":"relative pitch approach 指教學生透過與其他音符比較來理解音符。"},{"en":"A singing teacher using this approach may first give a starting note, then ask students to find the next one.","zh":"使用這種方法的歌唱老師可能先給一個起始音，再要求學生找下一個音。"},{"en":"This approach strengthens musical relationships but may not train isolated note naming.","zh":"這種方法強化音樂關係，但未必訓練孤立音符命名。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a comparison-based teaching method.","zh":"這個短語描述基於比較的教學方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"list of words","meaning":"詞語列表","examples":[{"en":"The question provides a list of words for completing the notes.","zh":"題目提供一個詞語列表，用來完成筆記。"},{"en":"A list of words is a set of words given as possible answers or reference items.","zh":"list of words 指作為可能答案或參考項目的一組詞語。"},{"en":"A vocabulary worksheet may include a list of words for students to match with meanings.","zh":"詞彙工作紙可能包括詞語列表，讓學生配對意思。"},{"en":"A word list limits choices and helps students focus on grammar and meaning.","zh":"詞語列表限制選擇，並幫助學生專注於文法和意思。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the supplied group of words.","zh":"這個短語指所提供的一組詞語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"match each opinion with","meaning":"將每項意見與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match each opinion with one of the scientists.","zh":"考生將每項意見與其中一位科學家配對。"},{"en":"To match each opinion with someone means to connect each view to the person who expressed it.","zh":"match each opinion with someone 指把每個觀點連接到表達該觀點的人。"},{"en":"In a reading task, students may match each opinion with the correct speaker.","zh":"在閱讀題中，學生可能要把每項意見與正確說話者配對。"},{"en":"This requires careful reading because two people may discuss similar topics differently.","zh":"這需要仔細閱讀，因為兩個人可能以不同方式討論相似主題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a matching question based on viewpoints.","zh":"這個短語描述基於觀點的配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"one of the scientists","meaning":"其中一位科學家","examples":[{"en":"Each opinion should be matched with one of the scientists.","zh":"每項意見應與其中一位科學家配對。"},{"en":"One of the scientists means a single person chosen from the group of scientists mentioned.","zh":"one of the scientists 指從提到的一組科學家中選出的一人。"},{"en":"A reading question may ask which claim belongs to one of the scientists in the passage.","zh":"閱讀題可能問某個說法屬於文章中其中一位科學家。"},{"en":"Students must use evidence from the text to choose the correct scientist.","zh":"學生必須用文本證據選出正確科學家。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies one member of a named group.","zh":"這個短語指出某個已命名群體中的一員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"you may use","meaning":"你可以使用","examples":[{"en":"Candidates may use any of the people more than once.","zh":"考生可以使用任何人物多於一次。"},{"en":"You may use means you are allowed to choose or apply something.","zh":"you may use 指你被允許選擇或使用某物。"},{"en":"In a vocabulary exercise, you may use a dictionary after the first attempt.","zh":"在詞彙練習中，你可以在第一次嘗試後使用字典。"},{"en":"When instructions say you may use an option more than once, repeated answers are allowed.","zh":"當指示說你可以多於一次使用某選項，重複答案就是被容許的。"},{"en":"This phrase gives permission.","zh":"這個短語表示許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"more than once","meaning":"多於一次","examples":[{"en":"Some names may be used more than once.","zh":"有些名字可以使用多於一次。"},{"en":"More than once means two or more times.","zh":"more than once 指兩次或以上。"},{"en":"A student may need to read a difficult paragraph more than once.","zh":"學生可能需要閱讀困難段落多於一次。"},{"en":"In matching tasks, using an answer more than once means the same option can fit several questions.","zh":"在配對題中，多於一次使用某答案，表示同一選項可以符合幾題。"},{"en":"This phrase removes the assumption that each answer is used only one time.","zh":"這個短語消除每個答案只能用一次的假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"clear-cut issue","meaning":"清楚分明的問題","examples":[{"en":"Absolute pitch is not a clear-cut issue.","zh":"絕對音感不是一個清楚分明的問題。"},{"en":"A clear-cut issue is simple, obvious and easy to decide.","zh":"clear-cut issue 指簡單、明顯且容易判斷的問題。"},{"en":"Whether a student copied homework may not be a clear-cut issue if both students studied together.","zh":"如果兩名學生一起溫習，某學生是否抄功課可能不是清楚分明的問題。"},{"en":"When an issue is not clear-cut, several explanations may be partly true.","zh":"當問題不是清楚分明，幾種解釋可能都有部分真確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that is not simply yes or no.","zh":"這個短語描述並非簡單是或否的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"anyone can acquire","meaning":"任何人都可以獲得","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers believe anyone can acquire perfect pitch.","zh":"有些研究人員相信任何人都可以獲得絕對音感。"},{"en":"Anyone can acquire means every person has the possibility of gaining the ability.","zh":"anyone can acquire 指每個人都有可能取得該能力。"},{"en":"With patient practice, anyone can acquire basic public-speaking confidence.","zh":"透過耐心練習，任何人都可以獲得基本公開演說信心。"},{"en":"Saying anyone can acquire a skill suggests it is not reserved for a tiny elite.","zh":"說任何人都可以獲得某技能，表示它不是只留給極少數精英。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses broad possibility.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"actually surprising","meaning":"其實令人驚訝","examples":[{"en":"It is actually surprising that not everyone has absolute pitch.","zh":"不是人人都有絕對音感，其實令人驚訝。"},{"en":"Actually surprising means genuinely unexpected after considering the evidence.","zh":"actually surprising 指在考慮證據後真的出乎意料。"},{"en":"It is actually surprising that some students avoid revision even when they know it helps.","zh":"有些學生明知溫習有幫助仍避免溫習，這其實令人驚訝。"},{"en":"Something becomes surprising when new evidence changes what we expect.","zh":"當新證據改變我們的預期，某事就會變得令人驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a shift in perspective.","zh":"這個短語表示觀點上的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"absolute pitch is genetic","meaning":"絕對音感是遺傳的","examples":[{"en":"One opinion suggests that absolute pitch is genetic.","zh":"一項意見指出絕對音感是遺傳的。"},{"en":"Absolute pitch is genetic means inherited genes play a major role in creating the ability.","zh":"absolute pitch is genetic 指遺傳基因在形成這種能力中扮演主要角色。"},{"en":"If a musical ability is genetic, it may appear more often among relatives.","zh":"如果某音樂能力是遺傳的，它可能較常出現在親屬之間。"},{"en":"A genetic explanation does not always exclude training, but it gives biology an important role.","zh":"基因解釋不一定排除訓練，但它賦予生物因素重要角色。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses the view that inheritance is central.","zh":"這個短語表達遺傳是核心的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the important thing is","meaning":"重要的是","examples":[{"en":"The important thing may be the age at which music lessons are started.","zh":"重要的可能是開始上音樂課的年齡。"},{"en":"The important thing is introduces the key factor in a situation.","zh":"the important thing is 用來引入情況中的關鍵因素。"},{"en":"The important thing is not how many notes students copy, but whether they understand them.","zh":"重要的不是學生抄了多少音符，而是他們是否理解。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers focus on the factor that matters most.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者聚焦於最重要的因素。"},{"en":"It is useful when several possible explanations exist.","zh":"當存在幾種可能解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the age at which","meaning":"……的年齡","examples":[{"en":"The age at which music lessons are started may matter.","zh":"開始上音樂課的年齡可能很重要。"},{"en":"The age at which something happens means how old someone is when it happens.","zh":"the age at which something happens 指某事發生時某人幾歲。"},{"en":"The age at which children start reading can affect early confidence.","zh":"孩子開始閱讀的年齡可以影響早期信心。"},{"en":"If a skill develops best early, the age at which training begins may be important.","zh":"如果某技能在早期最容易發展，訓練開始的年齡可能很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase connects timing with development.","zh":"這個短語把時間與發展連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"music lessons are started","meaning":"開始上音樂課的時間","examples":[{"en":"The timing of when music lessons are started may be important.","zh":"開始上音樂課的時間可能很重要。"},{"en":"Music lessons are started means a person begins formal or regular music instruction.","zh":"music lessons are started 指一個人開始接受正式或定期音樂教學。"},{"en":"Parents may choose when music lessons are started based on a child’s interest and attention span.","zh":"家長可能根據孩子的興趣和專注時間，選擇開始上音樂課的時間。"},{"en":"If lessons are started very early, children may develop listening habits sooner.","zh":"如果很早開始上課，孩子可能更早發展聆聽習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the beginning point of music education.","zh":"這個短語著重音樂教育的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 107 - Striking the right note.pdf","sourcePage":22}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 108":[{"front":"the art of healing","meaning":"治療之道；醫術","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the art of healing in the Tang dynasty.","zh":"文章討論唐代的治療之道。"},{"en":"The art of healing means the knowledge, skill, and judgement used to treat illness and restore health.","zh":"the art of healing 指用來治療疾病和恢復健康的知識、技巧和判斷。"},{"en":"A good nurse practises the art of healing not only by giving medicine, but also by comforting anxious patients.","zh":"好護士不只透過給藥實踐醫術，也透過安慰焦慮病人實踐醫術。"},{"en":"The art of healing improves when medical knowledge is combined with care, experience, and ethical judgement.","zh":"當醫學知識結合關懷、經驗和倫理判斷，治療之道就會進步。"},{"en":"This phrase presents medicine as a skilled human practice, not just a set of technical procedures.","zh":"這個短語把醫學呈現為一種熟練的人類實踐，而不只是技術程序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as with so much","meaning":"與許多事情一樣","examples":[{"en":"As with so much, Tang medicine was far ahead of its European counterpart.","zh":"與許多事情一樣，唐代醫學遠遠領先於其歐洲同類事物。"},{"en":"As with so much means “as was true in many other cases too”.","zh":"as with so much 指「正如許多其他情況一樣」。"},{"en":"As with so much in school life, good exam results depend on steady habits more than last-minute effort.","zh":"與學校生活中許多事情一樣，好考試成績取決於穩定習慣，多於臨急努力。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that the example being discussed fits a wider pattern.","zh":"這個短語暗示正在討論的例子符合一個更廣泛模式。"},{"en":"It is often used when one case reflects many similar examples.","zh":"當某個個案反映許多相似例子時，常使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the medicine of the Tang dynasty","meaning":"唐代醫學","examples":[{"en":"The medicine of the Tang dynasty was highly organised and sophisticated.","zh":"唐代醫學組織嚴密且高度精深。"},{"en":"The medicine of the Tang dynasty refers to the medical knowledge, institutions, doctors, texts, and treatments used during the Tang period.","zh":"the medicine of the Tang dynasty 指唐代使用的醫學知識、機構、醫生、文本和治療方法。"},{"en":"A history teacher may discuss the medicine of the Tang dynasty when explaining how ancient governments organised public services.","zh":"歷史老師解釋古代政府如何組織公共服務時，可能會討論唐代醫學。"},{"en":"Studying Tang medicine helps students see that medical systems can be shaped by politics, education, and law.","zh":"研究唐代醫學幫助學生看見醫療制度可以受政治、教育和法律塑造。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a whole medical system, not one single cure.","zh":"這個短語指整個醫療系統，而不是單一療法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"leave someone in the shade","meaning":"令……相形見絀","examples":[{"en":"The medicine of the Tang dynasty left its European counterpart in the shade.","zh":"唐代醫學令其歐洲同類事物相形見絀。"},{"en":"To leave someone in the shade means to be much better or more impressive than them.","zh":"leave someone in the shade 指比某人或某事好得多、出色得多。"},{"en":"Her carefully prepared presentation left the other group’s rushed report in the shade.","zh":"她準備充分的匯報令另一組倉促完成的報告相形見絀。"},{"en":"When one system is better organised, more advanced, and more effective, it can leave another in the shade.","zh":"當一個制度組織更好、更先進、更有效，它就可以令另一個制度相形見絀。"},{"en":"The phrase is a strong comparison showing that one side clearly outperforms the other.","zh":"這個短語是強烈比較，表示一方明顯勝過另一方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"European counterpart","meaning":"歐洲對應事物；歐洲同類事物","examples":[{"en":"Chinese medicine was far ahead of its European counterpart.","zh":"中國醫學遠遠領先於其歐洲同類事物。"},{"en":"A European counterpart is the European version or equivalent of something found elsewhere.","zh":"European counterpart 指某事物在歐洲的版本或對應例子。"},{"en":"A Hong Kong exam system may be compared with its European counterpart to show different educational priorities.","zh":"香港考試制度可以與其歐洲對應制度比較，以顯示不同教育優先次序。"},{"en":"Comparing something with its counterpart helps readers see similarities and differences clearly.","zh":"把某事物與其對應事物比較，幫助讀者清楚看見相似和差異。"},{"en":"The phrase does not mean an opponent; it means a corresponding example from Europe.","zh":"這個短語不是指敵手，而是指來自歐洲的相應例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"boast its own","meaning":"擁有自己的……","examples":[{"en":"The Tang dynasty boasted its own national health service.","zh":"唐代擁有自己的國民醫療服務。"},{"en":"To boast its own something means to possess something impressive or special.","zh":"boast its own something 指擁有某種令人印象深刻或特別的東西。"},{"en":"The school boasts its own theatre, so students can perform plays without renting a hall.","zh":"這所學校擁有自己的劇場，所以學生不用租禮堂也能演出。"},{"en":"When a city boasts its own medical university, it can train local healthcare workers more easily.","zh":"當城市擁有自己的醫科大學，它可以更容易培訓本地醫護人員。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests pride in having a valuable feature.","zh":"這個短語常暗示對擁有某種有價值特徵感到自豪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"national health service","meaning":"國民醫療服務","examples":[{"en":"The Tang dynasty had something like a national health service.","zh":"唐代有類似國民醫療服務的制度。"},{"en":"A national health service is an organised system that provides medical care to people across a country.","zh":"national health service 指在全國範圍為人民提供醫療照顧的有組織制度。"},{"en":"A modern national health service may include hospitals, clinics, doctors, medicines, and public health rules.","zh":"現代國民醫療服務可能包括醫院、診所、醫生、藥物和公共衛生規則。"},{"en":"If a country has a strong national health service, ordinary people may receive care more reliably.","zh":"如果一個國家有強大的國民醫療服務，普通人可能更可靠地獲得照顧。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a public medical system, not one private hospital.","zh":"這個短語指公共醫療制度，而不是一間私人醫院。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"leave behind","meaning":"留下","examples":[{"en":"Tang medicine left behind the teachings of Sun Simiao.","zh":"唐代醫學留下了孫思邈的學說。"},{"en":"To leave behind something means to pass it on to later people or future generations.","zh":"leave behind something 指把某事物傳給後人或後代。"},{"en":"A good teacher may leave behind clear notes that help students for many years.","zh":"好老師可能留下清楚筆記，幫助學生多年。"},{"en":"When a civilisation leaves behind books and institutions, later societies can learn from them.","zh":"當文明留下書籍和制度，後來社會就可以向它學習。"},{"en":"The phrase can mean physical remains or lasting influence.","zh":"這個短語可以指實物遺留，也可以指持久影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"teachings of","meaning":"……的教導；學說","examples":[{"en":"The dynasty left behind the teachings of the incomparable Sun Simiao.","zh":"這個朝代留下了無與倫比的孫思邈的學說。"},{"en":"The teachings of someone are the ideas, principles, or lessons that person passed on.","zh":"teachings of someone 指某人傳下來的思想、原則或教訓。"},{"en":"Students may still follow the teachings of an old headmaster about honesty and service.","zh":"學生可能仍遵循一位舊校長關於誠實和服務的教導。"},{"en":"Teachings survive when later people copy, explain, and practise them.","zh":"當後人抄錄、解釋和實踐教導，它們就能延續。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to intellectual or moral inheritance from a person.","zh":"這個短語指來自某人的思想或道德遺產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"incomparable","meaning":"無與倫比的","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao was described as an incomparable physician.","zh":"孫思邈被形容為一位無與倫比的醫師。"},{"en":"Incomparable means so excellent or unusual that it is difficult to compare with others.","zh":"incomparable 指非常出色或獨特，以致難以與他人相比。"},{"en":"A school coach may be called incomparable if generations of students remember his guidance.","zh":"如果幾代學生都記得一位學校教練的指導，他可能被稱為無與倫比。"},{"en":"Someone becomes incomparable when their skill, influence, and character stand far above normal standards.","zh":"當一個人的技能、影響和品格遠高於一般標準，他就變得無與倫比。"},{"en":"The word gives very strong praise.","zh":"這個詞表示非常強烈的讚美。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"if no further evidence were available of","meaning":"如果沒有更多關於……的證據","examples":[{"en":"If no further evidence were available of Tang sophistication, Chinese medicine would be sufficient proof.","zh":"如果沒有更多關於唐代精深程度的證據，中國醫學也足以證明。"},{"en":"If no further evidence were available of something means even if there were no more proof of it.","zh":"if no further evidence were available of something 指即使沒有更多證據證明某事。"},{"en":"If no further evidence were available of the school’s improvement, the students’ confident writing would still prove it.","zh":"如果沒有更多關於學校進步的證據，學生自信的寫作仍足以證明。"},{"en":"This structure emphasises that one example alone is strong enough to support the point.","zh":"這個結構強調單一例子已足夠支持觀點。"},{"en":"It is useful when arguing that one piece of evidence is already convincing.","zh":"當要論證某一項證據已很有說服力時，這個結構很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sophistication of China","meaning":"中國的精深程度；高度文明","examples":[{"en":"Chinese medicine shows the sophistication of China in the Tang era.","zh":"中國醫學顯示唐代中國的高度文明。"},{"en":"The sophistication of China means China’s high level of organisation, knowledge, culture, and technical development.","zh":"sophistication of China 指中國在組織、知識、文化和技術發展上的高水平。"},{"en":"The design of ancient canals can show the sophistication of a society’s engineering.","zh":"古代運河設計可以顯示一個社會工程技術的精深程度。"},{"en":"A civilisation’s sophistication becomes visible when its laws, education, and public services are well developed.","zh":"當文明的法律、教育和公共服務發展良好，其精深程度就會顯現。"},{"en":"The phrase praises depth and refinement, not just wealth.","zh":"這個短語讚揚深度和精緻程度，而不只是財富。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Tang era","meaning":"唐代","examples":[{"en":"Chinese medicine was highly developed in the Tang era.","zh":"中國醫學在唐代高度發展。"},{"en":"The Tang era refers to the historical period when the Tang dynasty ruled China.","zh":"Tang era 指唐朝統治中國的歷史時期。"},{"en":"A history lesson on poetry, trade, and medicine may focus on the Tang era.","zh":"關於詩歌、貿易和醫學的歷史課可能集中於唐代。"},{"en":"Naming the era helps readers place people, institutions, and ideas in the correct historical setting.","zh":"指明年代幫助讀者把人物、制度和思想放在正確歷史背景中。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a time period, not only the ruling family.","zh":"這個短語指一段時期，而不只是統治家族。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a look at","meaning":"看一看……","examples":[{"en":"A look at Chinese medicine would be sufficient evidence of Tang sophistication.","zh":"看一看中國醫學，就足以證明唐代的高度文明。"},{"en":"A look at something means a brief examination or consideration of it.","zh":"a look at something 指對某事作簡短檢視或考慮。"},{"en":"A look at a student’s draft can quickly show whether the main idea is clear.","zh":"看一看學生草稿，就可以快速看出主旨是否清楚。"},{"en":"Sometimes even a short examination can reveal the quality of a system.","zh":"有時即使只是簡短檢視，也能揭示一個制度的質素。"},{"en":"The phrase means examining something, not literally staring at it only.","zh":"這個短語指檢視某事，而不只是字面上看着它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be sufficient","meaning":"足夠","examples":[{"en":"A look at Chinese medicine would be sufficient to show Tang sophistication.","zh":"看一看中國醫學就足以顯示唐代的高度文明。"},{"en":"To be sufficient means to be enough for a particular purpose.","zh":"be sufficient 指對某個目的而言足夠。"},{"en":"Thirty minutes may be sufficient for checking a short essay, but not for rewriting it completely.","zh":"三十分鐘可能足夠檢查一篇短作文，但不足以完全重寫。"},{"en":"If one example is strong enough, no extra proof may be necessary.","zh":"如果一個例子已足夠有力，就未必需要額外證據。"},{"en":"The phrase means enough, not excessive.","zh":"這個短語意思是足夠，而不是過量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at the western end of","meaning":"在……的西端","examples":[{"en":"The Roman Empire had vanished at the western end of the Eurasian continent.","zh":"羅馬帝國已在歐亞大陸西端消失。"},{"en":"At the western end of a place means at the far west side of that area.","zh":"at the western end of a place 指在某地最西邊的位置。"},{"en":"A small fishing village sits at the western end of the island.","zh":"一個小漁村坐落於島嶼西端。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers locate something geographically within a larger landmass or region.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者在較大陸地或地區中定位某事物。"},{"en":"It describes position, not political importance.","zh":"它描述位置，而不是政治重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Eurasian continent","meaning":"歐亞大陸","examples":[{"en":"The Roman Empire was located at the western end of the Eurasian continent.","zh":"羅馬帝國位於歐亞大陸西端。"},{"en":"The Eurasian continent is the large landmass that includes Europe and Asia.","zh":"Eurasian continent 指包括歐洲和亞洲的大型陸地。"},{"en":"Trade routes across the Eurasian continent connected merchants, religions, and medical ideas.","zh":"橫跨歐亞大陸的貿易路線連接商人、宗教和醫學思想。"},{"en":"Because the continent is so large, ideas could develop very differently at its eastern and western ends.","zh":"因為這片大陸非常廣闊，思想可以在東西兩端發展得很不同。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a huge geographical area joining Europe and Asia.","zh":"這個短語描述連接歐洲和亞洲的巨大地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"vanish","meaning":"消失","examples":[{"en":"By the Tang era, the Roman Empire had vanished.","zh":"到唐代時，羅馬帝國已經消失。"},{"en":"To vanish means to disappear completely or no longer exist in the same form.","zh":"vanish 指完全消失或不再以同一形式存在。"},{"en":"A student’s nervousness may vanish after several successful speaking practices.","zh":"學生經過幾次成功口語練習後，緊張感可能消失。"},{"en":"Empires can vanish when political control, military power, and institutions collapse.","zh":"當政治控制、軍事力量和制度崩潰，帝國可能消失。"},{"en":"The word suggests disappearance, not simply becoming weaker.","zh":"這個詞暗示消失，而不只是變弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"claim the status of","meaning":"聲稱擁有……地位","examples":[{"en":"No new power could claim the status of the world’s cultural and political centre.","zh":"沒有新勢力能聲稱擁有世界文化和政治中心的地位。"},{"en":"To claim the status of something means to present oneself as having that recognised position.","zh":"claim the status of something 指把自己呈現為具有某種公認地位。"},{"en":"A university may claim the status of a leading research centre if it produces major discoveries.","zh":"如果一所大學產生重大發現，它可能聲稱擁有領先研究中心的地位。"},{"en":"A place can claim such status only when others recognise its influence and importance.","zh":"一個地方只有在他人承認其影響力和重要性時，才能聲稱擁有這種地位。"},{"en":"The phrase is about asserting or holding a prestigious position.","zh":"這個短語關於宣稱或擁有崇高地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cultural and political centre","meaning":"文化和政治中心","examples":[{"en":"The Tang capital became the cultural and political centre of the world.","zh":"唐都成為世界的文化和政治中心。"},{"en":"A cultural and political centre is a place where art, learning, government, and power are concentrated.","zh":"cultural and political centre 指藝術、學術、政府和權力集中之地。"},{"en":"A capital city often becomes a cultural and political centre because leaders, museums, schools, and officials gather there.","zh":"首都常成為文化和政治中心，因為領袖、博物館、學校和官員聚集在那裏。"},{"en":"When a city becomes such a centre, people and ideas from many regions may flow into it.","zh":"當城市成為這種中心，來自許多地區的人和思想可能流入其中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both intellectual influence and governing power.","zh":"這個短語同時描述思想文化影響和治理權力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, the centre of the world was the Tang capital for several centuries.","zh":"事實上，數個世紀以來，世界中心是唐帝國的首都。"},{"en":"In fact introduces a point that strengthens, corrects, or clarifies what has just been said.","zh":"in fact 用來引入一個加強、修正或澄清前文的重點。"},{"en":"The course seemed difficult at first; in fact, most students improved after two weeks.","zh":"這個課程起初看似困難；事實上，大多數學生兩星期後都有進步。"},{"en":"The phrase often gives a stronger or more precise version of the previous idea.","zh":"這個短語常給出前一想法的更強或更準確版本。"},{"en":"It signals that the writer is adding factual emphasis.","zh":"它表示作者正在加入事實上的強調。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"happen to be","meaning":"碰巧是；剛好是","examples":[{"en":"For a few centuries, this centre happened to be the capital of the Tang empire.","zh":"數個世紀裏，這個中心剛好是唐帝國的首都。"},{"en":"To happen to be means to be something by circumstance or fact, sometimes unexpectedly.","zh":"happen to be 指因情況或事實而是某事，有時帶有意外感。"},{"en":"The quiet student happened to be the best speaker in the competition.","zh":"那位安靜學生剛好是比賽中最好的演講者。"},{"en":"This phrase can make a statement sound slightly surprising or casual.","zh":"這個短語可以令陳述聽起來略帶意外或自然。"},{"en":"It does not mean an accident happened; it means the situation turned out that way.","zh":"它不是指意外事件發生，而是指情況結果如此。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"capital of the Tang empire","meaning":"唐帝國的首都","examples":[{"en":"The capital of the Tang empire became a major cultural centre.","zh":"唐帝國的首都成為主要文化中心。"},{"en":"The capital of the Tang empire was the main city from which the Tang rulers governed.","zh":"capital of the Tang empire 指唐朝統治者治理國家的主要城市。"},{"en":"A capital city often attracts officials, scholars, traders, and artists.","zh":"首都通常吸引官員、學者、商人和藝術家。"},{"en":"When a capital grows wealthy and powerful, it can influence medicine, education, and culture.","zh":"當首都變得富裕而強大，它可以影響醫學、教育和文化。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the political centre of Tang rule.","zh":"這個短語指唐朝統治的政治中心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"far ahead of","meaning":"遠遠領先於……","examples":[{"en":"Chinese medicine was far ahead of its European counterpart.","zh":"中國醫學遠遠領先於其歐洲同類事物。"},{"en":"To be far ahead of something means to be much more advanced or developed than it.","zh":"far ahead of something 指比某事物先進或發達得多。"},{"en":"A school with strong digital teaching may be far ahead of others that still use only paper notes.","zh":"一所擁有強大數碼教學的學校，可能遠遠領先於仍只用紙本筆記的學校。"},{"en":"A system becomes far ahead when it has better organisation, training, tools, and results.","zh":"當一個制度有更好的組織、培訓、工具和成果，它就會遠遠領先。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a large gap, not a small advantage.","zh":"這個短語表示很大差距，而不是小優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"organisational context","meaning":"組織背景；制度環境","examples":[{"en":"The organisational context of health and healing was highly structured.","zh":"健康與治療的制度環境高度有結構。"},{"en":"Organisational context means the system, rules, offices, roles, and procedures surrounding an activity.","zh":"organisational context 指圍繞某活動的制度、規則、機構、角色和程序。"},{"en":"In a school, the organisational context of exams includes timetables, invigilators, marking rules, and classrooms.","zh":"在學校，考試的組織背景包括時間表、監考員、評分規則和課室。"},{"en":"A strong organisational context helps people know who is responsible and how work should be done.","zh":"強大的制度環境幫助人知道誰負責以及工作應如何進行。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the institutional setting, not the medical treatment itself.","zh":"這個短語重點是制度環境，而不是醫療本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"health and healing","meaning":"健康與治療","examples":[{"en":"The Tang state created a strong system for health and healing.","zh":"唐朝國家為健康與治療建立了強大制度。"},{"en":"Health and healing refers to both keeping people well and treating them when they are ill.","zh":"health and healing 指保持人們健康，以及在患病時治療他們。"},{"en":"A community clinic supports health and healing by giving vaccines, advice, and treatment.","zh":"社區診所透過提供疫苗、建議和治療來支持健康與治療。"},{"en":"A good medical system must prevent illness as well as cure it.","zh":"良好醫療制度必須預防疾病，也要治療疾病。"},{"en":"The phrase combines public wellbeing with medical care.","zh":"這個短語結合公共福祉與醫療照顧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be structured to a degree that","meaning":"被組織到……的程度","examples":[{"en":"The system was structured to a degree that had no precedent in Chinese history.","zh":"這個制度被組織到在中國歷史上沒有先例的程度。"},{"en":"To be structured to a degree that means to be organised so strongly or extensively that a particular result follows.","zh":"be structured to a degree that 指被組織得非常強或非常廣，以致產生某種結果。"},{"en":"The school timetable was structured to a degree that every student knew exactly where to go.","zh":"學校時間表被安排到每位學生都清楚知道去哪裏的程度。"},{"en":"When a system is highly structured, confusion is reduced because roles and rules are clear.","zh":"當制度高度有結構，角色和規則清楚，混亂就會減少。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises an unusually high level of organisation.","zh":"這個短語強調異常高的組織程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have no precedent in","meaning":"在……中沒有先例","examples":[{"en":"The Tang medical system had no precedent in Chinese history.","zh":"唐代醫療制度在中國歷史上沒有先例。"},{"en":"To have no precedent in something means nothing similar had happened or existed before in that field or history.","zh":"have no precedent in something 指在某領域或歷史中以前沒有類似事情發生或存在。"},{"en":"The school’s decision to open all classrooms at night had no precedent in its history.","zh":"學校晚上開放所有課室的決定，在其歷史中沒有先例。"},{"en":"When something has no precedent, people may see it as innovative or extraordinary.","zh":"當某事沒有先例，人們可能視之為創新或非凡。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the case was new and unmatched in earlier experience.","zh":"這個短語強調該案例在過往經驗中全新且無可比擬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"find no parallel elsewhere","meaning":"在其他地方找不到同類例子","examples":[{"en":"The Tang medical system found no parallel elsewhere.","zh":"唐代醫療制度在其他地方找不到同類例子。"},{"en":"To find no parallel elsewhere means there was no similar example in other places.","zh":"find no parallel elsewhere 指在其他地方沒有相似例子。"},{"en":"The school’s student-support system found no parallel elsewhere in the district.","zh":"這所學校的學生支援制度在區內其他地方找不到同類例子。"},{"en":"If a system has no parallel elsewhere, it may be unusually advanced or unique.","zh":"如果一個制度在其他地方沒有同類例子，它可能異常先進或獨特。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights uniqueness through comparison with other places.","zh":"這個短語透過與其他地方比較來突出獨特性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Imperial Medical Office","meaning":"太醫署；宮廷醫療機構","examples":[{"en":"An Imperial Medical Office had been inherited from previous dynasties.","zh":"太醫署是從前朝繼承下來的。"},{"en":"The Imperial Medical Office was a government medical institution serving the court and helping organise official medicine.","zh":"Imperial Medical Office 指服務宮廷並協助組織官方醫學的政府醫療機構。"},{"en":"A modern health department is similar in that it manages medical rules, staff, and public services.","zh":"現代衛生部門在管理醫療規則、人員和公共服務方面有相似之處。"},{"en":"Such an office allows a government to supervise doctors, medicines, and medical education.","zh":"這類機構讓政府監督醫生、藥物和醫學教育。"},{"en":"The phrase names an official medical body, not a private clinic.","zh":"這個短語命名官方醫療機構，而不是私人診所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be inherited from","meaning":"從……繼承","examples":[{"en":"The Imperial Medical Office was inherited from previous dynasties.","zh":"太醫署是從前朝繼承而來的。"},{"en":"To be inherited from something means to be received or continued from an earlier person, group, or period.","zh":"be inherited from something 指從較早的人、群體或時期接收或延續下來。"},{"en":"A school tradition may be inherited from teachers who worked there decades ago.","zh":"學校傳統可能從數十年前在那裏工作的老師繼承而來。"},{"en":"Inherited institutions can be reformed by later governments instead of being created from nothing.","zh":"繼承下來的制度可以由後來政府改革，而不是從零創造。"},{"en":"The phrase shows continuity from the past.","zh":"這個短語顯示與過去的延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"previous dynasties","meaning":"前朝","examples":[{"en":"The office had existed under previous dynasties.","zh":"這個機構在前朝已經存在。"},{"en":"Previous dynasties are ruling families or regimes that governed before the current dynasty.","zh":"previous dynasties 指在現有朝代之前統治的王朝或政權。"},{"en":"A historian may compare laws from previous dynasties to see how government changed.","zh":"歷史學家可能比較前朝法律，以了解政府如何改變。"},{"en":"Institutions from previous dynasties may survive if later rulers find them useful.","zh":"如果後來統治者認為有用，前朝制度可能延續下來。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to earlier periods of rule.","zh":"這個短語指較早的統治時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be immediately restructured","meaning":"立即被重組","examples":[{"en":"The Imperial Medical Office was immediately restructured.","zh":"太醫署立即被重組。"},{"en":"To be immediately restructured means to be reorganised without delay.","zh":"be immediately restructured 指毫不延誤地被重新組織。"},{"en":"After the new principal arrived, the school timetable was immediately restructured to reduce clashes.","zh":"新校長到任後，學校時間表立即被重組，以減少衝突。"},{"en":"Immediate restructuring can show that leaders see the system as important or problematic.","zh":"立即重組可以顯示領導者認為該制度重要或有問題。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses quick organisational change.","zh":"這個短語強調快速的組織變革。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be staffed with","meaning":"配備……人員","examples":[{"en":"The office was staffed with directors, pharmacists and other personnel.","zh":"這個機構配備主管、藥劑師和其他人員。"},{"en":"To be staffed with people means to have those people working there in official roles.","zh":"be staffed with people 指有這些人在該處擔任正式職務。"},{"en":"A hospital ward must be staffed with nurses, doctors, cleaners, and support workers.","zh":"醫院病房必須配備護士、醫生、清潔員和支援人員。"},{"en":"Good staffing allows an organisation to divide work clearly and operate reliably.","zh":"良好人手配置讓機構清楚分工並可靠運作。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the people assigned to run a place or service.","zh":"這個短語重點是被安排去運作某地方或服務的人員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"directors and deputy directors","meaning":"主管和副主管","examples":[{"en":"The office had directors and deputy directors.","zh":"這個機構有主管和副主管。"},{"en":"Directors and deputy directors are senior managers and their assistants or second-in-command officers.","zh":"directors and deputy directors 指高級管理者及其助手或副手。"},{"en":"A school project may have a director and deputy director to share leadership duties.","zh":"學校項目可能有主管和副主管，共同分擔領導職責。"},{"en":"Having deputy directors helps an office keep running when the main director is absent or busy.","zh":"有副主管可以在主管缺席或忙碌時幫助機構繼續運作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a hierarchy of leadership.","zh":"這個短語描述領導層級。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"chief and assistant medical directors","meaning":"首席和助理醫務主管","examples":[{"en":"The office included chief and assistant medical directors.","zh":"這個機構包括首席和助理醫務主管。"},{"en":"Chief and assistant medical directors are senior doctors or officials responsible for leading medical work and supporting that leadership.","zh":"chief and assistant medical directors 指負責領導醫療工作及支援該領導工作的高級醫生或官員。"},{"en":"A large hospital may have a chief medical director and assistant directors for different departments.","zh":"大型醫院可能有首席醫務主管，以及負責不同部門的助理主管。"},{"en":"Clear leadership roles help medical staff know who sets standards and who handles daily decisions.","zh":"清楚的領導角色幫助醫療人員知道誰設定標準、誰處理日常決定。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to official medical leadership positions.","zh":"這個短語指正式醫療領導職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pharmacists","meaning":"藥劑師","examples":[{"en":"Pharmacists worked within the Imperial Medical Office.","zh":"藥劑師在太醫署內工作。"},{"en":"Pharmacists are trained professionals who prepare, check, and advise on medicines.","zh":"pharmacists 指受過訓練、負責配製、檢查和提供藥物建議的專業人士。"},{"en":"A pharmacist may explain how often a patient should take antibiotics.","zh":"藥劑師可能解釋病人應多久服用一次抗生素。"},{"en":"Pharmacists reduce medical risk by checking doses, ingredients, and possible drug problems.","zh":"藥劑師透過檢查劑量、成分和可能的藥物問題來降低醫療風險。"},{"en":"The word refers to medicine specialists, not general shopkeepers.","zh":"這個詞指藥物專家，而不是一般店員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"curators of medicinal herb gardens","meaning":"藥草園管理員","examples":[{"en":"The office employed curators of medicinal herb gardens.","zh":"這個機構僱用藥草園管理員。"},{"en":"Curators of medicinal herb gardens are people responsible for managing gardens where healing plants are grown.","zh":"curators of medicinal herb gardens 指負責管理種植治療用植物園圃的人。"},{"en":"A hospital garden may need curators to label herbs, care for plants, and record their uses.","zh":"醫院花園可能需要管理員為草藥標籤、照顧植物並記錄用途。"},{"en":"Good curators help ensure that useful plants are grown correctly and not confused with harmful ones.","zh":"好管理員幫助確保有用植物被正確種植，且不會與有害植物混淆。"},{"en":"The phrase combines plant management with medical knowledge.","zh":"這個短語結合植物管理和醫學知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"medicinal herb gardens","meaning":"藥草園","examples":[{"en":"Medicinal herb gardens supplied plants for medical use.","zh":"藥草園供應醫療用途的植物。"},{"en":"Medicinal herb gardens are gardens where plants used for medicine are grown and studied.","zh":"medicinal herb gardens 指種植和研究藥用植物的園圃。"},{"en":"A university may keep medicinal herb gardens so pharmacy students can learn to identify plants.","zh":"大學可能保留藥草園，讓藥劑學學生學習辨認植物。"},{"en":"Such gardens help doctors and pharmacists obtain ingredients more reliably.","zh":"這類園圃幫助醫生和藥劑師更可靠地取得成分。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to plant-growing spaces connected with healthcare.","zh":"這個短語指與醫療相關的植物種植空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"further personnel","meaning":"其他人員","examples":[{"en":"The office was staffed with pharmacists, curators and further personnel.","zh":"這個機構配備藥劑師、管理員和其他人員。"},{"en":"Further personnel means additional staff members beyond those already named.","zh":"further personnel 指除已提及人員以外的額外員工。"},{"en":"A school camp needs teachers, nurses, drivers, and further personnel to run safely.","zh":"學校營需要老師、護士、司機和其他人員才能安全運作。"},{"en":"Extra personnel allow an organisation to handle specialised or routine tasks.","zh":"額外人員讓機構處理專門或日常任務。"},{"en":"The phrase indicates more staff without listing every role.","zh":"這個短語表示還有更多職員，但不逐一列出所有職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"within the first two decades","meaning":"在最初二十年內","examples":[{"en":"Within the first two decades, the Tang administration set up medical colleges.","zh":"在最初二十年內，唐代政府設立了醫學院。"},{"en":"Within the first two decades means during the first twenty years of a period.","zh":"within the first two decades 指在某一時期的首二十年內。"},{"en":"Within the first two decades of a school’s founding, it may build a library and science labs.","zh":"一所學校創立後最初二十年內，可能建成圖書館和科學實驗室。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a development happened relatively early.","zh":"這個短語顯示某發展相對早期發生。"},{"en":"It helps readers understand timing in a historical process.","zh":"它幫助讀者理解歷史過程中的時間點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"consolidate its rule","meaning":"鞏固其統治","examples":[{"en":"The Tang administration created medical colleges after consolidating its rule.","zh":"唐代政府在鞏固其統治後建立醫學院。"},{"en":"To consolidate its rule means to make political control stable, secure, and widely accepted.","zh":"consolidate its rule 指令政治控制穩定、安全並被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"A new school principal may consolidate her leadership by setting clear rules and building trust.","zh":"新校長可能透過制定清楚規則和建立信任來鞏固其領導。"},{"en":"Once a government consolidates its rule, it can focus on building institutions and services.","zh":"一旦政府鞏固其統治，就可以集中建立制度和服務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strengthening authority after gaining power.","zh":"這個短語描述取得權力後加強權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Tang administration","meaning":"唐代政府；唐朝行政當局","examples":[{"en":"The Tang administration set up central and provincial medical colleges.","zh":"唐代政府設立中央及地方醫學院。"},{"en":"The Tang administration means the government and officials who managed the Tang dynasty.","zh":"Tang administration 指管理唐朝的政府和官員。"},{"en":"A history student may study the Tang administration to understand how education and law were organised.","zh":"歷史學生可能研究唐代政府，以理解教育和法律如何組織。"},{"en":"A strong administration can create offices, exams, schools, and public rules.","zh":"強大的行政當局可以建立機構、考試、學校和公共規則。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the governing system, not only the emperor personally.","zh":"這個短語指治理系統，而不只是皇帝本人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"set up","meaning":"設立","examples":[{"en":"The Tang administration set up medical colleges.","zh":"唐代政府設立醫學院。"},{"en":"To set up something means to establish, create, or organise it.","zh":"set up something 指建立、創立或組織某事物。"},{"en":"A teacher may set up a reading club for students who want extra practice.","zh":"老師可能為想額外練習的學生設立閱讀學會。"},{"en":"When an institution is set up, people, rules, resources, and purposes must be arranged.","zh":"當一個機構被設立，人員、規則、資源和目的都必須安排好。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on starting something organised.","zh":"這個短語重點是開始有組織的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"central and provincial medical colleges","meaning":"中央及地方醫學院","examples":[{"en":"The Tang administration set up one central and several provincial medical colleges.","zh":"唐代政府設立一所中央醫學院和幾所地方醫學院。"},{"en":"Central and provincial medical colleges are medical schools at the national centre and in regional areas.","zh":"central and provincial medical colleges 指位於國家中心和地方地區的醫學校。"},{"en":"A country may build one central training college and several provincial colleges to reach more students.","zh":"一個國家可能建立一所中央培訓學院和幾所地方學院，以接觸更多學生。"},{"en":"Regional colleges help spread professional knowledge beyond the capital.","zh":"地方學院幫助把專業知識傳播到首都以外。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that medical education was organised at more than one level.","zh":"這個短語顯示醫學教育在多於一個層面被組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"professors and lecturers","meaning":"教授和講師","examples":[{"en":"Professors and lecturers trained students in medicine and acupuncture.","zh":"教授和講師訓練學生學習醫學和針灸。"},{"en":"Professors and lecturers are academic teachers who teach and guide students in specialised subjects.","zh":"professors and lecturers 指教授和指導學生學習專門科目的學術教師。"},{"en":"University professors and lecturers may teach through lectures, demonstrations, and supervised practice.","zh":"大學教授和講師可能透過講課、示範和督導練習教學。"},{"en":"Skilled teaching staff help students turn written knowledge into professional ability.","zh":"熟練教學人員幫助學生把書面知識轉化為專業能力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people responsible for formal education.","zh":"這個短語指負責正式教育的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"clinical practitioners","meaning":"臨床醫師","examples":[{"en":"Clinical practitioners helped train medical students.","zh":"臨床醫師協助訓練醫學生。"},{"en":"Clinical practitioners are medical professionals who treat real patients in practice.","zh":"clinical practitioners 指在實際工作中治療真實病人的醫療專業人員。"},{"en":"A nursing student learns more safely when clinical practitioners supervise work in a hospital ward.","zh":"當臨床醫師在病房監督工作，護理學生會學得更安全。"},{"en":"Practitioners connect classroom learning with real patient care.","zh":"臨床工作者把課堂學習與真實病人照顧連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to experienced people working in actual medical settings.","zh":"這個短語指在實際醫療環境中工作的有經驗人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"train students in","meaning":"訓練學生學習……","examples":[{"en":"The colleges trained students in medicine, acupuncture and physical therapy.","zh":"這些學院訓練學生學習醫學、針灸和物理治療。"},{"en":"To train students in a subject means to teach them knowledge and practical skills in that area.","zh":"train students in a subject 指教授學生該範疇的知識和實用技能。"},{"en":"A school may train students in public speaking by giving them weekly practice and feedback.","zh":"學校可能透過每星期練習和回饋，訓練學生學習公開演說。"},{"en":"Training helps students become able to perform tasks, not merely remember facts.","zh":"訓練幫助學生能夠執行任務，而不只是記住事實。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when teaching includes skill-building.","zh":"當教學包括技能建立時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"departments of medicine","meaning":"醫學部門","examples":[{"en":"Students could study in different departments of medicine.","zh":"學生可以在不同醫學部門學習。"},{"en":"Departments of medicine are separate branches or sections of medical study and practice.","zh":"departments of medicine 指醫學學習和實踐中的不同分支或部門。"},{"en":"A modern hospital may have departments of medicine, surgery, paediatrics, and emergency care.","zh":"現代醫院可能有內科、外科、兒科和急症等醫學部門。"},{"en":"Dividing medicine into departments helps teachers specialise and students follow clearer training paths.","zh":"把醫學分成部門，幫助老師專門化，也讓學生有更清楚培訓路徑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised fields within medical education or service.","zh":"這個短語描述醫學教育或服務中的有組織領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"acupuncture","meaning":"針灸","examples":[{"en":"Acupuncture was one of the four departments of medical training.","zh":"針灸是醫學訓練四個部門之一。"},{"en":"Acupuncture is a treatment method that involves inserting fine needles into specific points of the body.","zh":"acupuncture 指把幼針插入身體特定穴位的治療方法。"},{"en":"Some patients use acupuncture to manage pain or support recovery.","zh":"有些病人使用針灸來處理痛楚或輔助康復。"},{"en":"Because acupuncture requires precision, students need careful training before practising it.","zh":"因為針灸需要精準，學生行醫前需要仔細訓練。"},{"en":"The word refers to a specific medical technique, not all Chinese medicine.","zh":"這個詞指一種特定醫療技術，而不是全部中醫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"physical therapy","meaning":"物理治療","examples":[{"en":"Physical therapy was included in Tang medical training.","zh":"物理治療包括在唐代醫學訓練之中。"},{"en":"Physical therapy is treatment that uses movement, exercise, touch, or physical methods to improve the body’s function.","zh":"physical therapy 指使用動作、運動、觸摸或物理方法改善身體功能的治療。"},{"en":"A patient may receive physical therapy after a knee injury to walk normally again.","zh":"病人膝部受傷後可能接受物理治療，以重新正常走路。"},{"en":"Physical therapy helps when recovery depends on strength, movement, and repeated practice.","zh":"當康復取決於力量、動作和反覆練習時，物理治療很有幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to body-based treatment, not medicine taken by mouth.","zh":"這個短語指以身體為基礎的治療，而不是口服藥物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"exorcism","meaning":"驅邪療法","examples":[{"en":"Exorcism was listed as one department of medicine in Tang colleges.","zh":"驅邪療法在唐代醫學院被列為醫學部門之一。"},{"en":"Exorcism is a ritual practice intended to drive away harmful spirits or evil influences.","zh":"exorcism 指旨在驅走有害靈體或邪惡影響的儀式做法。"},{"en":"In some traditional communities, illness may be treated through prayer, ritual, or exorcism.","zh":"在一些傳統社區，疾病可能透過祈禱、儀式或驅邪療法處理。"},{"en":"Including exorcism shows that historical medicine could mix healing, religion, and belief.","zh":"把驅邪列入其中，顯示歷史醫學可以混合治療、宗教和信念。"},{"en":"The word refers to a spiritual practice, not modern scientific treatment.","zh":"這個詞指精神或宗教做法，而不是現代科學治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"physicians","meaning":"醫師","examples":[{"en":"Physicians had to pass qualifying examinations.","zh":"醫師必須通過資格考試。"},{"en":"Physicians are doctors who diagnose and treat illness.","zh":"physicians 指診斷和治療疾病的醫生。"},{"en":"A physician may examine a patient, ask about symptoms, and prescribe medicine.","zh":"醫師可能檢查病人、詢問症狀並開藥。"},{"en":"When physicians are properly trained and examined, patients receive safer care.","zh":"當醫師接受適當訓練和考核，病人會得到較安全照顧。"},{"en":"The word refers to medical doctors, especially those practising medicine rather than surgery.","zh":"這個詞指醫生，尤其是行醫而非外科手術的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"governmental medical service","meaning":"政府醫療服務","examples":[{"en":"Physicians could enter governmental medical service after passing exams.","zh":"醫師通過考試後可以進入政府醫療服務。"},{"en":"Governmental medical service is medical work organised and paid for by the state.","zh":"governmental medical service 指由國家組織和支付的醫療工作。"},{"en":"A doctor in a public hospital may be part of governmental medical service.","zh":"公立醫院醫生可能屬於政府醫療服務的一部分。"},{"en":"Exams can help a government choose qualified people for official medical posts.","zh":"考試可以幫助政府選擇合資格人士擔任官方醫療職位。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to medicine within government service, not private practice.","zh":"這個短語指政府服務中的醫療，而不是私人執業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"only after passing","meaning":"只有通過……之後","examples":[{"en":"Physicians received official positions only after passing qualifying examinations.","zh":"醫師只有通過資格考試後才獲得官方職位。"},{"en":"Only after passing means not before someone has successfully passed a test or requirement.","zh":"only after passing 指必須成功通過測試或要求之後才可以。"},{"en":"Students may join the advanced class only after passing the foundation course.","zh":"學生只有通過基礎課程後，才可以加入進階班。"},{"en":"This structure emphasises that passing is a necessary condition.","zh":"這個結構強調通過是必要條件。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show a strict order: first pass, then receive permission or status.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示嚴格次序：先通過，然後才獲得許可或地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"qualifying examinations","meaning":"資格考試","examples":[{"en":"Tang physicians had to pass qualifying examinations.","zh":"唐代醫師必須通過資格考試。"},{"en":"Qualifying examinations are tests that people must pass to prove they are suitable for a profession or role.","zh":"qualifying examinations 指人們必須通過以證明自己適合某職業或角色的考試。"},{"en":"Teachers may need to pass qualifying examinations before working in public schools.","zh":"老師在公立學校工作前可能需要通過資格考試。"},{"en":"Such exams protect the public by checking whether candidates have enough knowledge and skill.","zh":"這類考試透過檢查考生是否有足夠知識和技能來保護公眾。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to exams that grant eligibility, not ordinary classroom tests.","zh":"這個短語指授予資格的考試，而不是普通課堂測驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be remunerated in accordance with","meaning":"按照……獲得報酬","examples":[{"en":"Physicians were remunerated in accordance with the number of cures they had effected.","zh":"醫師按照他們促成治癒的個案數目獲得報酬。"},{"en":"To be remunerated in accordance with something means to be paid according to that factor.","zh":"be remunerated in accordance with something 指根據某因素獲得薪酬。"},{"en":"A salesperson may be remunerated in accordance with the number of successful orders.","zh":"銷售員可能按照成功訂單數目獲得報酬。"},{"en":"When pay is linked to results, workers may be encouraged to improve performance.","zh":"當薪酬與成果掛鈎，工作者可能被鼓勵改善表現。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and refers to salary or payment rules.","zh":"這個短語較正式，指薪金或付款規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the number of cures","meaning":"治癒個案數目","examples":[{"en":"A doctor’s salary depended on the number of cures he had achieved.","zh":"醫生薪酬取決於他所達成的治癒個案數目。"},{"en":"The number of cures means how many patients were successfully healed or treated.","zh":"number of cures 指有多少病人被成功治好或治療成功。"},{"en":"A clinic might record the number of cures to evaluate how effective a treatment is.","zh":"診所可能記錄治癒個案數目，以評估某治療有多有效。"},{"en":"If payment depends on cures, doctors may be judged by patient outcomes.","zh":"如果薪酬取決於治癒個案，醫生可能按病人結果被評估。"},{"en":"The phrase measures successful treatment cases.","zh":"這個短語量度成功治療個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"effect a cure","meaning":"促成治癒；成功治好","examples":[{"en":"Physicians were rewarded for the cures they had effected.","zh":"醫師因他們成功促成的治癒而獲得獎勵。"},{"en":"To effect a cure means to successfully bring about a recovery from illness.","zh":"effect a cure 指成功使病人從疾病中康復。"},{"en":"A doctor may effect a cure by diagnosing the illness correctly and giving the right treatment.","zh":"醫生可能透過正確診斷疾病並給予適當治療來促成治癒。"},{"en":"If the treatment does not remove the illness, it has not effected a cure.","zh":"如果治療未能消除疾病，它就沒有促成治癒。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and means to make healing happen.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是使治療成功發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"during the past year","meaning":"在過去一年","examples":[{"en":"The number of cures was counted during the past year.","zh":"治癒個案數目是在過去一年計算的。"},{"en":"During the past year means within the previous twelve months.","zh":"during the past year 指在之前十二個月內。"},{"en":"A school may count absences during the past year to identify attendance problems.","zh":"學校可能計算過去一年缺席次數，以找出出席問題。"},{"en":"Measuring performance over a year gives a broader picture than looking at one week.","zh":"以一年量度表現比只看一星期能提供更廣闊圖像。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a recent time period for counting or evaluation.","zh":"這個短語為計算或評估設定近期時間範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"personally composed","meaning":"親自編寫","examples":[{"en":"Emperor Xuanzong personally composed a general formulary of prescriptions.","zh":"玄宗皇帝親自編寫了一本通用處方集。"},{"en":"Personally composed means written or created by the person himself or herself, not only by assistants.","zh":"personally composed 指由某人本人親自書寫或創作，而不只是由助手完成。"},{"en":"The principal personally composed a letter to thank students after the charity event.","zh":"校長在慈善活動後親自寫信感謝學生。"},{"en":"When a ruler personally composes a text, it shows direct interest and authority.","zh":"當統治者親自編寫文本，顯示直接關注和權威。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises personal involvement in writing or creation.","zh":"這個短語強調在寫作或創作中的親身參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"general formulary of prescriptions","meaning":"通用處方集","examples":[{"en":"The emperor composed a general formulary of prescriptions.","zh":"皇帝編寫了一本通用處方集。"},{"en":"A general formulary of prescriptions is a collection of standard medical recipes or treatments for common use.","zh":"general formulary of prescriptions 指供一般使用的標準醫療方劑或治療方法集合。"},{"en":"A hospital may keep a formulary so doctors know which medicines are officially approved.","zh":"醫院可能保存處方集，讓醫生知道哪些藥物獲正式批准。"},{"en":"A shared formulary can standardise treatment and reduce dangerous guesswork.","zh":"共同處方集可以標準化治療並減少危險猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an organised list of medical prescriptions.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的醫療處方列表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be recommended to","meaning":"被推薦給……","examples":[{"en":"The prescriptions were recommended to the emperor by an imperial pharmacist.","zh":"這些處方由御用藥劑師推薦給皇帝。"},{"en":"To be recommended to someone means to be suggested to that person as useful or suitable.","zh":"be recommended to someone 指被建議給某人作為有用或合適選擇。"},{"en":"A book may be recommended to a student who wants to improve vocabulary.","zh":"一本書可能被推薦給想改善詞彙的學生。"},{"en":"Recommendations help decision-makers choose from many possible options.","zh":"推薦幫助決策者從許多可能選項中選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase shows who received the advice or suggestion.","zh":"這個短語顯示誰收到建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"imperial pharmacist","meaning":"御用藥劑師","examples":[{"en":"An imperial pharmacist recommended prescriptions to Emperor Xuanzong.","zh":"一位御用藥劑師向玄宗皇帝推薦處方。"},{"en":"An imperial pharmacist was a medicine specialist serving the emperor or imperial court.","zh":"imperial pharmacist 指服務皇帝或宮廷的藥物專家。"},{"en":"A royal household might rely on an imperial pharmacist to prepare safe and trusted medicines.","zh":"王室家庭可能依賴御用藥劑師配製安全可靠藥物。"},{"en":"Such a role required medical knowledge because mistakes could affect powerful patients.","zh":"這種職位需要醫學知識，因為錯誤可能影響權貴病人。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a court-based medicine expert.","zh":"這個短語指宮廷中的藥物專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"provincial medical schools","meaning":"地方醫學校","examples":[{"en":"The formulary was sent to all the provincial medical schools.","zh":"這本處方集被送到所有地方醫學校。"},{"en":"Provincial medical schools are medical training institutions located in regional areas outside the central capital.","zh":"provincial medical schools 指位於中央首都以外地方地區的醫學培訓機構。"},{"en":"A country may build provincial medical schools so students outside major cities can study medicine.","zh":"一個國家可能建立地方醫學校，讓大城市以外的學生也能學醫。"},{"en":"Sending texts to provincial schools helps spread standard knowledge across the country.","zh":"把文本送到地方學校，有助在全國傳播標準知識。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to regional centres of medical education.","zh":"這個短語指地方醫學教育中心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Arabic traveller","meaning":"阿拉伯旅行者","examples":[{"en":"An Arabic traveller visited China in 851.","zh":"一位阿拉伯旅行者在851年到訪中國。"},{"en":"An Arabic traveller is a traveller from the Arab world or one who writes in Arabic cultural contexts.","zh":"Arabic traveller 指來自阿拉伯世界，或在阿拉伯文化語境中寫作的旅行者。"},{"en":"An Arabic traveller might record what he saw in markets, ports, schools, and hospitals.","zh":"阿拉伯旅行者可能記錄他在市場、港口、學校和醫院所見。"},{"en":"Travellers’ accounts can preserve outside observations of another civilisation.","zh":"旅行者記述可以保存外人對另一文明的觀察。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the visitor’s cultural or linguistic background.","zh":"這個短語指出訪客的文化或語言背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"note with surprise that","meaning":"驚訝地指出","examples":[{"en":"The traveller noted with surprise that prescriptions were displayed publicly.","zh":"那位旅行者驚訝地指出，處方被公開展示。"},{"en":"To note with surprise that means to observe something and feel it is unexpected.","zh":"note with surprise that 指觀察到某事並覺得出乎意料。"},{"en":"A visitor may note with surprise that students clean their own classrooms after lessons.","zh":"訪客可能驚訝地指出學生課後自己清潔課室。"},{"en":"This phrase shows both observation and the observer’s reaction.","zh":"這個短語同時顯示觀察內容和觀察者反應。"},{"en":"It is useful when a fact seems unusual to an outsider.","zh":"當某事實對外人來說不尋常時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be publicised on notice boards","meaning":"在告示板上公布","examples":[{"en":"The prescriptions were publicised on notice boards at crossroads.","zh":"這些處方在十字路口的告示板上公布。"},{"en":"To be publicised on notice boards means to be displayed publicly on boards where people can read the information.","zh":"be publicised on notice boards 指在公眾可閱讀資訊的告示板上公開展示。"},{"en":"School exam rules may be publicised on notice boards before the test week.","zh":"學校考試規則可能在考試周前在告示板上公布。"},{"en":"Publicising information in visible places helps many people receive the same message.","zh":"在顯眼地方公布資訊幫助許多人收到同一訊息。"},{"en":"The phrase describes official public display of information.","zh":"這個短語描述資訊的官方公開展示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"notice boards","meaning":"告示板","examples":[{"en":"The prescriptions appeared on notice boards.","zh":"這些處方出現在告示板上。"},{"en":"Notice boards are boards used to display public information, announcements, or instructions.","zh":"notice boards 指用來展示公共資訊、公告或指示的板。"},{"en":"A school notice board may show club times, exam dates, and lost items.","zh":"學校告示板可能顯示學會時間、考試日期和失物。"},{"en":"Notice boards help communities share information without speaking to each person individually.","zh":"告示板幫助社區分享資訊，而不用逐一告訴每個人。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a public display space for written notices.","zh":"這個短語指用於書面告示的公共展示空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"crossroads","meaning":"十字路口","examples":[{"en":"The notice boards were placed at crossroads.","zh":"告示板被放在十字路口。"},{"en":"Crossroads are places where two or more roads meet and cross.","zh":"crossroads 指兩條或多條道路相交的地方。"},{"en":"A shop at busy crossroads may attract many customers because people pass from several directions.","zh":"位於繁忙十字路口的商店可能吸引許多顧客，因為人們從多個方向經過。"},{"en":"Posting notices at crossroads helps more travellers and residents see them.","zh":"在十字路口張貼告示，幫助更多旅人和居民看到。"},{"en":"The word refers to road intersections, not a difficult life decision in this context.","zh":"在這個語境中，這個詞指道路交匯處，不是人生難關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"enhance the welfare of","meaning":"增進……的福祉","examples":[{"en":"The prescriptions were publicised to enhance the welfare of the population.","zh":"這些處方被公開公布，以增進民眾福祉。"},{"en":"To enhance the welfare of people means to improve their health, safety, comfort, or general wellbeing.","zh":"enhance the welfare of people 指改善人們的健康、安全、舒適或整體福祉。"},{"en":"Free school lunches can enhance the welfare of children from low-income families.","zh":"免費學校午餐可以增進低收入家庭兒童的福祉。"},{"en":"Public medical information can enhance welfare by helping people treat illness more safely.","zh":"公共醫療資訊可以透過幫助人更安全治療疾病來增進福祉。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improving people’s quality of life.","zh":"這個短語描述改善人們的生活質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the welfare of the population","meaning":"民眾福祉","examples":[{"en":"The government aimed to enhance the welfare of the population.","zh":"政府旨在增進民眾福祉。"},{"en":"The welfare of the population means the health, safety, and wellbeing of ordinary people in society.","zh":"welfare of the population 指社會中普通人的健康、安全和福祉。"},{"en":"Clean water, basic clinics, and safe housing all support the welfare of the population.","zh":"清潔食水、基本診所和安全住屋都支持民眾福祉。"},{"en":"Governments protect welfare when they reduce avoidable disease and danger.","zh":"當政府減少可避免疾病和危險，就是在保護福祉。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to public wellbeing, not only wealth.","zh":"這個短語指公共福祉，而不只是財富。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take care to","meaning":"小心地；特意去","examples":[{"en":"The government took care to protect the general populace.","zh":"政府特意保護一般民眾。"},{"en":"To take care to do something means to make a deliberate effort to do it carefully.","zh":"take care to do something 指刻意小心地做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher takes care to explain exam rules slowly so no student misunderstands them.","zh":"老師特意慢慢解釋考試規則，讓沒有學生誤解。"},{"en":"Taking care reduces mistakes, harm, and unfairness.","zh":"小心處理可以減少錯誤、傷害和不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase shows careful intention, not casual action.","zh":"這個短語顯示仔細意圖，而不是隨便行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"protect someone from","meaning":"保護某人免受……","examples":[{"en":"The government protected the general populace from harmful medical practice.","zh":"政府保護一般民眾免受有害醫療做法影響。"},{"en":"To protect someone from something means to prevent that person from being harmed by it.","zh":"protect someone from something 指防止某人受到某事傷害。"},{"en":"Schools protect students from accidents by setting laboratory safety rules.","zh":"學校透過制定實驗室安全規則，保護學生免受意外傷害。"},{"en":"Protection works best when risks are recognised before damage happens.","zh":"當風險在造成傷害前被識別，保護最有效。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on preventing harm.","zh":"這個短語重點是防止傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the general populace","meaning":"一般民眾","examples":[{"en":"The Tang government tried to protect the general populace.","zh":"唐代政府試圖保護一般民眾。"},{"en":"The general populace means ordinary people in society, not only officials, experts, or elites.","zh":"general populace 指社會中的普通人，而不只是官員、專家或精英。"},{"en":"Public transport policy affects the general populace because many people use buses and trains daily.","zh":"公共交通政策影響一般民眾，因為許多人每天使用巴士和鐵路。"},{"en":"Medical information helps the general populace when it is written clearly and displayed publicly.","zh":"當醫療資訊寫得清楚並公開展示，它就能幫助一般民眾。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the wider population.","zh":"這個短語指較廣泛的人口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"potentially harmful medical practice","meaning":"可能有害的醫療做法","examples":[{"en":"The legal code targeted potentially harmful medical practice.","zh":"法律針對可能有害的醫療做法。"},{"en":"Potentially harmful medical practice means treatment that may injure patients or make their condition worse.","zh":"potentially harmful medical practice 指可能傷害病人或令病情惡化的治療。"},{"en":"Giving strong medicine without checking allergies can be a potentially harmful medical practice.","zh":"未檢查過敏就給強效藥物，可以是可能有害的醫療做法。"},{"en":"Laws can reduce harm by stopping unqualified people from treating patients dangerously.","zh":"法律可以透過阻止無資格人士危險地治療病人來減少傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes medical actions that carry risk, even before harm occurs.","zh":"這個短語描述帶有風險的醫療行為，即使傷害尚未發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Tang legal code","meaning":"唐律","examples":[{"en":"The Tang legal code included laws on harmful medical practices.","zh":"唐律包括關於有害醫療做法的法律。"},{"en":"The Tang legal code was the organised body of laws used in the Tang dynasty.","zh":"Tang legal code 指唐代使用的有系統法律體系。"},{"en":"A legal code tells officials what actions are crimes and what punishments apply.","zh":"法典告訴官員哪些行為屬犯罪，以及適用甚麼懲罰。"},{"en":"Including medical rules in the legal code shows that healthcare was treated as a public responsibility.","zh":"把醫療規則納入法典，顯示醫療被視為公共責任。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to formal law, not informal custom.","zh":"這個短語指正式法律，而不是非正式習俗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be concerned with","meaning":"關乎……","examples":[{"en":"The laws were concerned with harmful and heterodox medical practices.","zh":"這些法律關乎有害和非正統醫療做法。"},{"en":"To be concerned with something means to deal with or focus on that topic.","zh":"be concerned with something 指處理或集中於某主題。"},{"en":"A school rule may be concerned with student safety during laboratory lessons.","zh":"校規可能關乎學生在實驗課中的安全。"},{"en":"Laws concerned with medicine try to prevent unsafe treatment and protect patients.","zh":"關乎醫學的法律嘗試防止不安全治療並保護病人。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the subject or purpose of a rule, text, or discussion.","zh":"這個短語指出規則、文本或討論的主題或目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"heterodox medical practices","meaning":"非正統醫療做法","examples":[{"en":"The Tang legal code regulated heterodox medical practices.","zh":"唐律規管非正統醫療做法。"},{"en":"Heterodox medical practices are treatments that do not follow accepted or official medical standards.","zh":"heterodox medical practices 指不遵循公認或官方醫學標準的治療。"},{"en":"A healer using secret remedies without training may be accused of heterodox practice.","zh":"使用秘密偏方而沒有訓練的治療者，可能被指進行非正統醫療做法。"},{"en":"Governments may regulate such practices because they can confuse or harm patients.","zh":"政府可能規管這類做法，因為它們可以令病人困惑或受傷。"},{"en":"The phrase means non-standard or unorthodox medicine.","zh":"這個短語意思是非標準或非正統醫學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"treat patients for money","meaning":"收費為病人治療","examples":[{"en":"It was illegal to treat patients for money without following standard procedures.","zh":"不遵循標準程序而收費為病人治療是違法的。"},{"en":"To treat patients for money means to provide medical care in exchange for payment.","zh":"treat patients for money 指收取費用來提供醫療照顧。"},{"en":"A person should not treat patients for money unless properly trained and licensed.","zh":"一個人除非受過適當訓練並獲發牌照，否則不應收費為病人治療。"},{"en":"Charging money for unsafe treatment can be treated as fraud because patients trust the healer.","zh":"為不安全治療收費可以被視為欺詐，因為病人信任治療者。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on paid medical practice.","zh":"這個短語重點是收費醫療行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"adhere to standard procedures","meaning":"遵守標準程序","examples":[{"en":"Doctors had to adhere to standard procedures.","zh":"醫生必須遵守標準程序。"},{"en":"To adhere to standard procedures means to follow accepted rules and steps carefully.","zh":"adhere to standard procedures 指仔細遵循公認規則和步驟。"},{"en":"Laboratory students must adhere to standard procedures when handling chemicals.","zh":"實驗室學生處理化學品時必須遵守標準程序。"},{"en":"Standard procedures reduce danger because everyone follows tested methods.","zh":"標準程序可以減少危險，因為每個人都遵循經測試的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses disciplined compliance with established rules.","zh":"這個短語強調有紀律地遵守既定規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be defined as","meaning":"被定義為","examples":[{"en":"Such behaviour was defined as fraud combined with theft.","zh":"這種行為被定義為欺詐加盜竊。"},{"en":"To be defined as something means to be officially explained or classified in that way.","zh":"be defined as something 指被正式解釋或分類為某事。"},{"en":"In school rules, plagiarism may be defined as using another person’s work as your own.","zh":"在校規中，抄襲可能被定義為把他人作品當作自己的作品。"},{"en":"Definitions matter because they decide how an action is judged and punished.","zh":"定義很重要，因為它們決定行為如何被判斷和懲罰。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an official meaning or classification.","zh":"這個短語引入正式意思或分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fraud combined with theft","meaning":"欺詐加盜竊","examples":[{"en":"Treating patients improperly for money was treated as fraud combined with theft.","zh":"不當收費治療病人被視為欺詐加盜竊。"},{"en":"Fraud combined with theft means cheating someone and wrongly taking their money or property.","zh":"fraud combined with theft 指欺騙某人並不當取得其金錢或財物。"},{"en":"Selling fake medicine to sick people can be fraud combined with theft because the seller lies and takes payment.","zh":"向病人出售假藥可以是欺詐加盜竊，因為賣方說謊並收錢。"},{"en":"When trust is abused for money, the offence may be seen as more serious.","zh":"當信任被用來牟利，罪行可能被視為更嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase joins deception with unlawful gain.","zh":"這個短語把欺騙與非法得益結合起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be tried in accordance with","meaning":"按照……受審","examples":[{"en":"Offenders were tried in accordance with the legal statutes on theft.","zh":"犯法者按照盜竊相關法規受審。"},{"en":"To be tried in accordance with a law means to be judged in court according to that law.","zh":"be tried in accordance with a law 指在法庭上根據該法律接受審判。"},{"en":"A student accused of cheating may be dealt with in accordance with school regulations.","zh":"被指作弊的學生可能按照校規處理。"},{"en":"Clear rules ensure that similar offences are judged in a similar way.","zh":"清楚規則確保相似違規行為以相似方式判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and legal, showing which rules guide the judgement.","zh":"這個短語正式且帶法律意味，顯示哪套規則指導判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"legal statutes on theft","meaning":"盜竊相關法規","examples":[{"en":"The healer was tried under the legal statutes on theft.","zh":"該治療者根據盜竊相關法規受審。"},{"en":"Legal statutes on theft are written laws dealing with stealing or unlawful taking of property.","zh":"legal statutes on theft 指處理偷竊或非法取得財物的成文法律。"},{"en":"A shoplifter may be punished under legal statutes on theft.","zh":"商店扒手可能根據盜竊相關法規受罰。"},{"en":"Applying theft laws to medical fraud shows that money taken through false treatment was treated seriously.","zh":"把盜竊法應用於醫療欺詐，顯示透過虛假治療取得金錢被嚴肅看待。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to formal written laws about stealing.","zh":"這個短語指關於偷竊的正式成文法律。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"result in the death of","meaning":"導致……死亡","examples":[{"en":"Some improper therapies resulted in the death of a patient.","zh":"一些不當療法導致病人死亡。"},{"en":"To result in the death of someone means to cause that person to die.","zh":"result in the death of someone 指造成某人死亡。"},{"en":"A serious medical mistake can result in the death of a patient if no one corrects it quickly.","zh":"嚴重醫療錯誤若沒有人迅速糾正，可能導致病人死亡。"},{"en":"Because the result is so severe, laws often punish dangerous treatment harshly.","zh":"因為結果非常嚴重，法律常嚴厲懲罰危險治療。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a fatal consequence.","zh":"這個短語描述致命後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be banished for","meaning":"被流放……","examples":[{"en":"A healer could be banished for two and a half years.","zh":"治療者可能被流放兩年半。"},{"en":"To be banished for a period means to be forced to leave a place as punishment for that length of time.","zh":"be banished for a period 指作為懲罰被迫離開某地一段時間。"},{"en":"In an old kingdom, a criminal might be banished for several years instead of being imprisoned.","zh":"在古代王國，罪犯可能被流放數年，而不是被囚禁。"},{"en":"Banishment separates the offender from home, work, family, and community.","zh":"流放會把犯事者與家、工作、家庭和社區分開。"},{"en":"The phrase describes punishment by forced exile.","zh":"這個短語描述以強制放逐作為懲罰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in case","meaning":"如果；倘若","examples":[{"en":"In case a physician purposely failed to follow the standards, he faced severe punishment.","zh":"如果醫師故意沒有遵循標準，他會面對嚴厲懲罰。"},{"en":"In case means if a particular situation happens.","zh":"in case 指如果某特定情況發生。"},{"en":"In case a student loses the worksheet, the teacher keeps extra copies in the classroom.","zh":"如果學生遺失工作紙，老師會在課室保留額外副本。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a possible situation that requires preparation or response.","zh":"這個短語引入需要準備或回應的可能情況。"},{"en":"In legal contexts, it can mean “if this condition occurs”.","zh":"在法律語境中，它可以表示「如果這條件出現」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"purposely fail to","meaning":"故意沒有……","examples":[{"en":"A physician might purposely fail to practise according to the standards.","zh":"醫師可能故意沒有按標準行醫。"},{"en":"To purposely fail to do something means to deliberately not do what one should do.","zh":"purposely fail to do something 指故意不做自己應該做的事。"},{"en":"A student who purposely fails to cite sources may be accused of plagiarism.","zh":"故意不引用資料來源的學生可能被指抄襲。"},{"en":"Deliberate failure is judged more seriously than an honest mistake.","zh":"故意不做通常比誠實錯誤被判斷得更嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses intention, not accident.","zh":"這個短語強調意圖，而不是意外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"practise according to the standards","meaning":"按標準行醫","examples":[{"en":"Physicians were required to practise according to the standards.","zh":"醫師被要求按標準行醫。"},{"en":"To practise according to the standards means to work in line with accepted professional rules.","zh":"practise according to the standards 指按照公認專業規則工作。"},{"en":"A nurse must practise according to hospital standards when giving injections.","zh":"護士打針時必須按照醫院標準執業。"},{"en":"Standards protect patients because they reduce unsafe personal improvisation.","zh":"標準保護病人，因為它們減少不安全的個人即興做法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes professional behaviour controlled by rules.","zh":"這個短語描述受規則控制的專業行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"premeditated homicide","meaning":"預謀殺人","examples":[{"en":"A physician could be tried under the statutes on premeditated homicide.","zh":"醫師可能根據預謀殺人相關法規受審。"},{"en":"Premeditated homicide means killing someone after planning or intending it beforehand.","zh":"premeditated homicide 指事先計劃或有意圖地殺害某人。"},{"en":"A legal system treats premeditated homicide more seriously than an accidental death.","zh":"法律制度把預謀殺人視為比意外死亡更嚴重。"},{"en":"If a doctor knowingly gives dangerous treatment with harmful intent, the law may treat it as deliberate killing.","zh":"如果醫生明知治療危險並帶有傷害意圖，法律可能把它視為故意殺人。"},{"en":"The phrase is a serious legal term involving planned death.","zh":"這個短語是嚴重法律術語，涉及有計劃的死亡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"even if no harm resulted","meaning":"即使沒有造成傷害","examples":[{"en":"Even if no harm resulted, the physician could still be punished.","zh":"即使沒有造成傷害，醫師仍可能受罰。"},{"en":"Even if no harm resulted means punishment or concern may apply although no actual damage happened.","zh":"even if no harm resulted 指即使沒有實際損害發生，仍可能需要處罰或關注。"},{"en":"A student may be punished for bringing a knife to school even if no harm resulted.","zh":"學生帶刀回校，即使沒有造成傷害，也可能被處罰。"},{"en":"Rules may punish dangerous behaviour because it could have caused serious damage.","zh":"規則可能懲罰危險行為，因為它本來可能造成嚴重損害。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that risk and intention can matter even without injury.","zh":"這個短語顯示即使沒有受傷，風險和意圖仍可能重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be sentenced to","meaning":"被判處","examples":[{"en":"A physician could be sentenced to sixty strokes with a heavy cane.","zh":"醫師可能被判處以重杖擊打六十下。"},{"en":"To be sentenced to a punishment means to be officially ordered by a court or authority to receive it.","zh":"be sentenced to a punishment 指由法院或權威正式命令接受某懲罰。"},{"en":"A driver may be sentenced to community service after repeated dangerous driving.","zh":"司機多次危險駕駛後，可能被判處社會服務令。"},{"en":"Sentencing shows the official consequence of breaking a law.","zh":"判刑顯示違法的正式後果。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in legal or disciplinary contexts.","zh":"這個短語用於法律或紀律語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"strokes with a heavy cane","meaning":"以重杖擊打","examples":[{"en":"The punishment could be sixty strokes with a heavy cane.","zh":"懲罰可以是以重杖擊打六十下。"},{"en":"Strokes with a heavy cane are blows delivered with a thick stick as corporal punishment.","zh":"strokes with a heavy cane 指用厚重棍杖擊打作為體罰。"},{"en":"In some historical legal systems, offenders were punished by strokes with a cane instead of prison.","zh":"在一些歷史法律制度中，犯法者以杖擊而不是監禁受罰。"},{"en":"Such punishment was meant to cause pain and publicly show legal authority.","zh":"這種懲罰旨在造成痛楚並公開顯示法律權威。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a physical punishment from a historical context.","zh":"這個短語描述歷史語境中的身體懲罰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"practising during the Tang era","meaning":"在唐代行醫的","examples":[{"en":"Physicians practising during the Tang era had access to many texts.","zh":"在唐代行醫的醫師可以接觸大量文本。"},{"en":"Practising during the Tang era means working professionally in that historical period.","zh":"practising during the Tang era 指在唐代這個歷史時期專業工作。"},{"en":"A teacher practising during the early internet era had to adjust as online resources appeared.","zh":"在早期互聯網時代教書的老師，必須隨着網上資源出現而調整。"},{"en":"The time when someone practises affects the tools, rules, and knowledge available to them.","zh":"一個人執業的時代會影響其可用工具、規則和知識。"},{"en":"The phrase links professional work to a specific historical period.","zh":"這個短語把專業工作與特定歷史時期連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have access to","meaning":"可以使用；接觸到","examples":[{"en":"Tang physicians had access to a wealth of medical texts.","zh":"唐代醫師可以接觸大量醫學文本。"},{"en":"To have access to something means to be able to use, read, enter, or obtain it.","zh":"have access to something 指可以使用、閱讀、進入或取得某物。"},{"en":"Students with library cards have access to books, databases, and quiet study areas.","zh":"有圖書證的學生可以使用書籍、資料庫和安靜自修區。"},{"en":"Access to reliable information can improve learning and decision-making.","zh":"接觸可靠資訊可以改善學習和決策。"},{"en":"The phrase describes availability, not ownership.","zh":"這個短語描述可取得性，而不是擁有權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a wealth of","meaning":"大量；豐富的……","examples":[{"en":"Physicians had access to a wealth of pharmaceutical and medical texts.","zh":"醫師可以接觸大量藥物學和醫學文本。"},{"en":"A wealth of something means a large and valuable supply of it.","zh":"a wealth of something 指大量而有價值的某物。"},{"en":"A good school library provides a wealth of reading materials for students.","zh":"好學校圖書館為學生提供豐富閱讀材料。"},{"en":"A wealth of sources can help researchers compare ideas and avoid relying on one text only.","zh":"大量資料來源可以幫助研究人員比較想法，避免只依賴一份文本。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests richness and abundance.","zh":"這個短語暗示豐富和充足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pharmaceutical and medical texts","meaning":"藥物學和醫學文本","examples":[{"en":"Tang libraries contained pharmaceutical and medical texts.","zh":"唐代圖書館藏有藥物學和醫學文本。"},{"en":"Pharmaceutical and medical texts are writings about medicines, treatments, diseases, and healthcare knowledge.","zh":"pharmaceutical and medical texts 指關於藥物、治療、疾病和醫療知識的文字著作。"},{"en":"Pharmacy students read pharmaceutical texts to learn how medicines are prepared and used.","zh":"藥劑學學生閱讀藥物學文本，以學習藥物如何配製和使用。"},{"en":"Medical texts preserve knowledge so later doctors can study and apply it.","zh":"醫學文本保存知識，讓後來醫生可以學習和應用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to written professional knowledge about drugs and medicine.","zh":"這個短語指關於藥物和醫學的書面專業知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"range from…to…","meaning":"由……到……不等","examples":[{"en":"The contents ranged from pragmatic advice to theoretical considerations.","zh":"內容由實用建議到理論思考不等。"},{"en":"Range from A to B means include many things between two different types or extremes.","zh":"range from A to B 指包括由一類事物到另一類事物之間的多種內容。"},{"en":"The school library’s books range from simple picture books to advanced science texts.","zh":"學校圖書館的書由簡單圖畫書到進階科學文本不等。"},{"en":"A wide range shows that a collection covers both practical and complex needs.","zh":"廣泛範圍顯示收藏涵蓋實用和複雜需要。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show variety.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"purely pragmatic advice","meaning":"純粹實用的建議","examples":[{"en":"Some medical texts offered purely pragmatic advice.","zh":"一些醫學文本提供純粹實用的建議。"},{"en":"Purely pragmatic advice is advice focused only on practical use rather than theory.","zh":"purely pragmatic advice 指只集中於實際用途而不是理論的建議。"},{"en":"A teacher gives purely pragmatic advice when she says, “Check verbs first because that is where you lose marks.”","zh":"當老師說「先檢查動詞，因為你常在那裏失分」，她就是給純粹實用的建議。"},{"en":"Practical advice helps people act immediately, even if it does not explain every theory behind the action.","zh":"實用建議幫助人立即行動，即使它不解釋行動背後每一項理論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes usefulness in real situations.","zh":"這個短語描述在真實情況中的有用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"highly sophisticated theoretical considerations","meaning":"高度精深的理論思考","examples":[{"en":"Other texts contained highly sophisticated theoretical considerations.","zh":"其他文本包含高度精深的理論思考。"},{"en":"Highly sophisticated theoretical considerations are complex and advanced ideas used to explain a subject deeply.","zh":"highly sophisticated theoretical considerations 指用來深入解釋某主題的複雜而高階想法。"},{"en":"A university lecture may include sophisticated theoretical considerations about how language changes over time.","zh":"大學講座可能包括關於語言如何隨時間變化的精深理論思考。"},{"en":"Such ideas can help experts understand causes, patterns, and hidden relationships.","zh":"這類想法可以幫助專家理解原因、模式和隱藏關係。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts deep theory with simple practical advice.","zh":"這個短語把深層理論與簡單實用建議作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"concise descriptions of","meaning":"對……的簡明描述","examples":[{"en":"The books included concise descriptions of the human body.","zh":"這些書包括對人體的簡明描述。"},{"en":"Concise descriptions of something are short but clear explanations of its main features.","zh":"concise descriptions of something 指對某物主要特徵作簡短但清楚的解釋。"},{"en":"A good revision note gives concise descriptions of each grammar rule before examples.","zh":"好溫習筆記會先簡明描述每條文法規則，再給例子。"},{"en":"Concise descriptions help readers understand quickly without being overloaded.","zh":"簡明描述幫助讀者快速理解，而不會負擔過重。"},{"en":"The phrase praises clear brevity.","zh":"這個短語讚揚清楚而簡潔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"morphology","meaning":"形態學；形態結構","examples":[{"en":"The texts described the morphology of the organs.","zh":"這些文本描述器官的形態結構。"},{"en":"Morphology means the form, shape, and structure of something, especially in biology.","zh":"morphology 指某物的形式、形狀和結構，尤其用於生物學。"},{"en":"A biology student studies plant morphology by comparing roots, stems, leaves, and flowers.","zh":"生物學生透過比較根、莖、葉和花來研究植物形態學。"},{"en":"Understanding morphology helps doctors and scientists know how body parts are built.","zh":"理解形態結構幫助醫生和科學家知道身體部位如何構成。"},{"en":"The word focuses on structure and form, not function alone.","zh":"這個詞重點是結構和形態，而不只是功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"organs of the human body","meaning":"人體器官","examples":[{"en":"The medical texts described the organs of the human body.","zh":"這些醫學文本描述人體器官。"},{"en":"Organs of the human body are parts such as the heart, lungs, liver, stomach, and kidneys that perform important functions.","zh":"organs of the human body 指心臟、肺、肝、胃和腎等執行重要功能的身體部分。"},{"en":"A health lesson may teach students how the organs of the human body work together.","zh":"健康課可能教學生人體器官如何互相配合。"},{"en":"If an organ fails, the whole body can be affected because organs depend on one another.","zh":"如果一個器官衰竭，整個身體可能受影響，因為器官彼此依賴。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to major internal body parts.","zh":"這個短語指主要內部身體部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stand side by side with","meaning":"與……並存","examples":[{"en":"Practical medical texts stood side by side with theoretical works.","zh":"實用醫學文本與理論著作並存。"},{"en":"To stand side by side with something means to exist together with it as an equally present part.","zh":"stand side by side with something 指與某物共同存在，並作為同樣存在的一部分。"},{"en":"In a good English course, grammar practice stands side by side with real speaking tasks.","zh":"在好的英文課程中，文法練習與真實口語任務並存。"},{"en":"When practical and theoretical materials stand together, learners gain both action and understanding.","zh":"當實用和理論材料並存，學習者既獲得行動方法，也獲得理解。"},{"en":"The phrase shows coexistence, not physical standing only.","zh":"這個短語顯示共存，而不只是字面並排站立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"enable readers to","meaning":"使讀者能夠……","examples":[{"en":"Some books enabled readers to calculate climatic conditions.","zh":"一些書使讀者能夠計算氣候狀況。"},{"en":"To enable readers to do something means to make it possible for them to do it.","zh":"enable readers to do something 指使讀者可以做某事。"},{"en":"Clear diagrams enable students to understand how the heart pumps blood.","zh":"清楚圖表使學生能夠理解心臟如何泵血。"},{"en":"Good explanations give readers tools, not just facts.","zh":"好解釋給讀者工具，而不只是事實。"},{"en":"The phrase links a text or tool with the ability it gives people.","zh":"這個短語把文本或工具與它給人的能力連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"calculate climatic conditions","meaning":"計算氣候狀況","examples":[{"en":"Readers could calculate daily, seasonal and annual climatic conditions.","zh":"讀者可以計算每日、季節性和年度氣候狀況。"},{"en":"To calculate climatic conditions means to work out weather or climate patterns using rules, numbers, or observations.","zh":"calculate climatic conditions 指使用規則、數字或觀察來推算天氣或氣候模式。"},{"en":"Farmers may calculate rainfall patterns before deciding when to plant crops.","zh":"農夫可能在決定何時種植作物前計算降雨模式。"},{"en":"Calculating climate conditions can help people predict health risks, harvests, or seasonal changes.","zh":"計算氣候狀況可以幫助人預測健康風險、收成或季節變化。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to systematic estimation, not casual weather guessing.","zh":"這個短語指有系統估算，而不是隨意猜天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"daily, seasonal and annual","meaning":"每日、季節性和年度的","examples":[{"en":"The texts discussed daily, seasonal and annual climatic conditions.","zh":"這些文本討論每日、季節性和年度氣候狀況。"},{"en":"Daily, seasonal and annual means happening by day, by season, and by year.","zh":"daily, seasonal and annual 指按日、按季節和按年發生。"},{"en":"A school may track daily attendance, seasonal illness, and annual exam results.","zh":"學校可能追蹤每日出席率、季節性疾病和年度考試結果。"},{"en":"Looking at different time scales helps people see short-term and long-term patterns.","zh":"觀察不同時間尺度，幫助人看見短期和長期模式。"},{"en":"The phrase organises information by time period.","zh":"這個短語按時間段組織資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cycles of sixty years","meaning":"六十年周期","examples":[{"en":"Some works analysed climatic conditions in cycles of sixty years.","zh":"一些著作以六十年周期分析氣候狀況。"},{"en":"Cycles of sixty years are repeating periods or patterns measured in sixty-year units.","zh":"cycles of sixty years 指以六十年為單位量度的重複時期或模式。"},{"en":"A historian may study economic cycles of ten years to see repeated rises and falls.","zh":"歷史學家可能研究十年經濟周期，以看見反覆升跌。"},{"en":"Thinking in cycles helps people look for patterns that return over time.","zh":"以周期思考幫助人尋找隨時間重現的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long repeated time patterns.","zh":"這個短語描述長期重複時間模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"predict their effects on","meaning":"預測……對……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Readers tried to predict the effects of climate on health.","zh":"讀者嘗試預測氣候對健康的影響。"},{"en":"To predict their effects on something means to estimate how they will influence it.","zh":"predict their effects on something 指估計它們會如何影響某事。"},{"en":"Doctors may predict the effects of heatwaves on elderly patients.","zh":"醫生可能預測熱浪對長者病人的影響。"},{"en":"Predicting effects helps people prepare before problems appear.","zh":"預測影響幫助人在問題出現前作準備。"},{"en":"The phrase connects future forecasting with impact.","zh":"這個短語把未來預測與影響連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"several Tang authors","meaning":"幾位唐代作者","examples":[{"en":"Several Tang authors wrote large collections of prescriptions.","zh":"幾位唐代作者寫了大型處方集。"},{"en":"Several Tang authors means a number of writers from the Tang period.","zh":"several Tang authors 指幾位來自唐代的作者。"},{"en":"Several school writers may contribute essays to one graduation booklet.","zh":"幾位校內作者可能為一本畢業文集撰寫文章。"},{"en":"When several authors work in one tradition, it suggests the subject was active and important.","zh":"當幾位作者在同一傳統中寫作，表示該主題活躍且重要。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies multiple writers from the same historical era.","zh":"這個短語指出同一歷史時代的多位作者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"large collections of prescriptions","meaning":"大型處方集","examples":[{"en":"Tang authors wrote large collections of prescriptions.","zh":"唐代作者撰寫大型處方集。"},{"en":"Large collections of prescriptions are big organised sets of medical formulas or treatment instructions.","zh":"large collections of prescriptions 指大型、有組織的醫療方劑或治療指示集合。"},{"en":"A clinic may keep a collection of standard prescriptions for common illnesses.","zh":"診所可能保存一套常見疾病的標準處方集。"},{"en":"Large collections help doctors find treatments more quickly and compare different options.","zh":"大型處方集幫助醫生更快找到療法並比較不同選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to many medical recipes gathered together.","zh":"這個短語指大量醫療方劑被集合在一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"continue a literary tradition","meaning":"延續一個文學傳統","examples":[{"en":"These authors continued a literary tradition documented since the second century BC.","zh":"這些作者延續了一個自公元前二世紀以來有記載的文學傳統。"},{"en":"To continue a literary tradition means to keep writing in a form or style that earlier writers had already developed.","zh":"continue a literary tradition 指繼續使用早期作者已發展出的形式或風格寫作。"},{"en":"Modern poets may continue a literary tradition by writing in classical forms with new themes.","zh":"現代詩人可能透過用古典形式寫新主題來延續文學傳統。"},{"en":"Traditions continue when later writers copy, adapt, and expand earlier works.","zh":"當後來作者抄錄、改編和擴展早期作品，傳統就會延續。"},{"en":"The phrase shows continuity in written culture.","zh":"這個短語顯示書面文化的延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be documented since","meaning":"自……以來有記載","examples":[{"en":"The tradition had been documented since the second century BC.","zh":"這個傳統自公元前二世紀以來有記載。"},{"en":"To be documented since a time means written evidence of it has existed from that period onward.","zh":"be documented since a time 指從某時期開始已有關於它的書面證據。"},{"en":"The school’s debating tradition has been documented since 1965 in old yearbooks.","zh":"學校辯論傳統自1965年起已在舊年刊中有記載。"},{"en":"Documentation helps historians prove that a practice existed in the past.","zh":"文獻記載幫助歷史學家證明某做法過去已存在。"},{"en":"The phrase links evidence with a starting point in time.","zh":"這個短語把證據與時間起點連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the second century BC","meaning":"公元前二世紀","examples":[{"en":"The prescription-writing tradition dated back to the second century BC.","zh":"處方寫作傳統可追溯至公元前二世紀。"},{"en":"The second century BC means the years from 200 BC to 101 BC.","zh":"the second century BC 指公元前200年至公元前101年。"},{"en":"A museum object from the second century BC is over two thousand years old.","zh":"來自公元前二世紀的博物館物件已有二千多年歷史。"},{"en":"Dates like this help readers understand how ancient a tradition is.","zh":"這類日期幫助讀者理解一個傳統有多古老。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a specific historical century before the common era.","zh":"這個短語指出公元紀年前的一個特定歷史世紀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"outstanding works","meaning":"傑出著作","examples":[{"en":"Two outstanding works were written by Sun Simiao and Wang Tao.","zh":"兩部傑出著作由孫思邈和王燾寫成。"},{"en":"Outstanding works are excellent and important pieces of writing or creation.","zh":"outstanding works 指優秀而重要的文字或創作作品。"},{"en":"A student’s outstanding work may be shown to the class as a model answer.","zh":"學生的傑出作品可能被展示給全班作為範文。"},{"en":"Works become outstanding when they are useful, influential, and remembered by later readers.","zh":"當作品有用、有影響力並被後來讀者記住，它就成為傑出著作。"},{"en":"The phrase gives strong praise to important writings.","zh":"這個短語對重要作品給予強烈讚揚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the latter","meaning":"後者","examples":[{"en":"The latter was a librarian who copied thousands of formulas.","zh":"後者是一位抄錄數千條方劑的圖書館員。"},{"en":"The latter means the second of two people or things just mentioned.","zh":"the latter 指剛提到兩個人或事物中的第二個。"},{"en":"Tom and Amy both joined the debate team; the latter became captain the next year.","zh":"Tom 和 Amy 都加入了辯論隊；後者翌年成為隊長。"},{"en":"The phrase avoids repeating the second name, but readers must know the order clearly.","zh":"這個短語避免重複第二個名稱，但讀者必須清楚次序。"},{"en":"It contrasts with “the former”, which means the first one.","zh":"它與 the former 相對，後者指第一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"copy formulas","meaning":"抄錄方劑","examples":[{"en":"Wang Tao copied more than six thousand formulas.","zh":"王燾抄錄了六千多條方劑。"},{"en":"To copy formulas means to write down or reproduce medical recipes or treatment instructions from other sources.","zh":"copy formulas 指從其他來源寫下或複製醫療方劑或治療指示。"},{"en":"A student may copy important grammar formulas into a notebook for revision.","zh":"學生可能把重要文法公式抄錄到筆記簿中溫習。"},{"en":"Copying formulas preserves them so later people can study and use them.","zh":"抄錄方劑能保存它們，讓後來的人研究和使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reproduction of written instructions, not mathematical calculation only.","zh":"這個短語描述複製書面指示，而不只是數學計算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be categorised in","meaning":"被分類為……","examples":[{"en":"The formulas were categorised in 1,104 sections.","zh":"這些方劑被分類為1,104個部分。"},{"en":"To be categorised in sections means to be organised into groups according to type or topic.","zh":"be categorised in sections 指按類型或主題被整理成不同組別。"},{"en":"A school library’s books may be categorised in fiction, history, science, and language sections.","zh":"學校圖書館的書可能被分類為小說、歷史、科學和語言區。"},{"en":"Categorising information helps readers find what they need more quickly.","zh":"分類資訊幫助讀者更快找到所需內容。"},{"en":"The phrase describes systematic organisation.","zh":"這個短語描述有系統的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"publish under the title","meaning":"以……為題出版","examples":[{"en":"Wang Tao published the formulas under the title Waitai miyao.","zh":"王燾以《外台秘要》為題出版這些方劑。"},{"en":"To publish something under the title means to release it with that name.","zh":"publish something under the title 指以某名稱發表或出版某作品。"},{"en":"A teacher may publish a booklet under the title Common Grammar Mistakes.","zh":"老師可能以《常見文法錯誤》為題出版小冊子。"},{"en":"A title helps readers identify the work and remember its topic.","zh":"標題幫助讀者辨認作品並記住主題。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a work with its published name.","zh":"這個短語把作品與其出版名稱連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be devoted to","meaning":"專門論述……","examples":[{"en":"Twenty-four sections were devoted to ophthalmology.","zh":"二十四個部分專門論述眼科。"},{"en":"To be devoted to a topic means to be used mainly for that topic.","zh":"be devoted to a topic 指主要用於某一主題。"},{"en":"Three lessons were devoted to essay planning before students began writing.","zh":"學生開始寫作前，有三節課專門用於作文構思。"},{"en":"Devoting space to a subject shows that the writer considers it important.","zh":"把篇幅專門給予某主題，顯示作者認為它重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes focused attention or allocation.","zh":"這個短語描述集中關注或分配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ophthalmology","meaning":"眼科","examples":[{"en":"Twenty-four sections of Waitai miyao were devoted to ophthalmology.","zh":"《外台秘要》中二十四個部分專門論述眼科。"},{"en":"Ophthalmology is the branch of medicine concerned with the eyes and eye diseases.","zh":"ophthalmology 指關於眼睛和眼疾的醫學分支。"},{"en":"A patient with serious vision problems may be referred to ophthalmology.","zh":"有嚴重視力問題的病人可能被轉介到眼科。"},{"en":"Eye medicine needs specialised knowledge because vision is delicate and complex.","zh":"眼科醫學需要專門知識，因為視力精細而複雜。"},{"en":"The word refers to medical study and treatment of the eyes.","zh":"這個詞指眼睛的醫學研究和治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reflect the Indian origin of","meaning":"反映……的印度源流","examples":[{"en":"The sections reflect the Indian origin of much Chinese knowledge on eye diseases.","zh":"這些部分反映許多中國眼疾知識的印度源流。"},{"en":"To reflect the Indian origin of something means to show that it came partly or mainly from India.","zh":"reflect the Indian origin of something 指顯示某事部分或主要來自印度。"},{"en":"A recipe using curry spices may reflect the Indian origin of part of a family’s cooking tradition.","zh":"使用咖喱香料的食譜可能反映家庭烹飪傳統中部分印度源流。"},{"en":"Cultural exchange can leave traces in medical texts, food, language, and art.","zh":"文化交流可以在醫學文本、食物、語言和藝術中留下痕跡。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies historical influence from India.","zh":"這個短語指出來自印度的歷史影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ailments of the eye","meaning":"眼疾","examples":[{"en":"The book contains knowledge about ailments of the eye.","zh":"這本書包含關於眼疾的知識。"},{"en":"Ailments of the eye are illnesses, disorders, or problems affecting vision or the eye itself.","zh":"ailments of the eye 指影響視力或眼睛本身的疾病、障礙或問題。"},{"en":"Redness, pain, blurred vision, and cataracts can be ailments of the eye.","zh":"眼紅、疼痛、視力模糊和白內障都可以是眼疾。"},{"en":"Eye ailments need careful treatment because poor care may damage sight.","zh":"眼疾需要仔細治療，因為護理不當可能損害視力。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to refer to eye diseases or problems.","zh":"這個短語是指眼部疾病或問題的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in particular","meaning":"尤其是","examples":[{"en":"The text discusses ailments of the eye and, in particular, cataract surgery.","zh":"該文本討論眼疾，尤其是白內障手術。"},{"en":"In particular means especially one specific thing within a larger group.","zh":"in particular 指在較大群體中特別指某一具體事物。"},{"en":"Many students need grammar help, in particular with articles and verb forms.","zh":"許多學生需要文法幫助，尤其是在冠詞和動詞形式方面。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows attention from a general topic to one important example.","zh":"這個短語把注意力從一般主題收窄到一個重要例子。"},{"en":"It tells readers which detail deserves special focus.","zh":"它告訴讀者哪個細節值得特別關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cataract surgery","meaning":"白內障手術","examples":[{"en":"Some Chinese knowledge of cataract surgery had Indian origins.","zh":"一些中國白內障手術知識具有印度源流。"},{"en":"Cataract surgery is an operation to treat cloudy vision caused by a cataract in the eye.","zh":"cataract surgery 指治療眼睛白內障造成視力混濁的手術。"},{"en":"An elderly patient may need cataract surgery when reading and walking become difficult because of blurred sight.","zh":"當長者因視力模糊而閱讀和走路變得困難，他可能需要白內障手術。"},{"en":"Successful cataract surgery can restore clearer vision and improve daily independence.","zh":"成功的白內障手術可以恢復較清晰視力並改善日常獨立能力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a specific eye operation.","zh":"這個短語指一種特定眼科手術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"eminent physician","meaning":"著名醫師；卓越醫師","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao was the most eminent physician of the Tang dynasty.","zh":"孫思邈是唐代最卓越的醫師。"},{"en":"An eminent physician is a highly respected and important doctor.","zh":"eminent physician 指備受尊敬且重要的醫生。"},{"en":"An eminent physician may be invited to advise hospitals, teach students, and write medical texts.","zh":"卓越醫師可能被邀請為醫院提供建議、教導學生和撰寫醫學文本。"},{"en":"A doctor becomes eminent through skill, integrity, learning, and lasting influence.","zh":"醫生透過技能、誠信、學識和持久影響成為卓越人物。"},{"en":"The phrase gives formal praise to a leading medical figure.","zh":"這個短語正式讚揚一位領先醫學人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the entire first millennium AD","meaning":"整個公元第一個千年","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao was one of the greatest physicians of the entire first millennium AD.","zh":"孫思邈是整個公元第一個千年最偉大的醫師之一。"},{"en":"The entire first millennium AD means the whole period from AD 1 to AD 1000.","zh":"the entire first millennium AD 指公元1年至公元1000年的整個時期。"},{"en":"A historian might compare inventions across the entire first millennium AD to see long-term change.","zh":"歷史學家可能比較整個公元第一個千年的發明，以觀察長期變化。"},{"en":"Calling someone great across a whole millennium gives very strong praise.","zh":"稱某人偉大到跨越整個千年，是非常強烈的讚美。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a thousand-year period after the birth of Christ.","zh":"這個短語指基督誕生後的一千年時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"broadly educated intellectual","meaning":"學識廣博的知識分子","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao was a broadly educated intellectual and physician.","zh":"孫思邈是一位學識廣博的知識分子和醫師。"},{"en":"A broadly educated intellectual is a learned person with knowledge across many fields.","zh":"broadly educated intellectual 指在多個領域都有知識的博學人士。"},{"en":"A broadly educated teacher may connect literature, history, science, and ethics in one lesson.","zh":"學識廣博的老師可能在一課中連結文學、歷史、科學和倫理。"},{"en":"Broad education helps people understand problems from several angles.","zh":"廣泛教育幫助人從多個角度理解問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes wide learning, not narrow technical training only.","zh":"這個短語描述廣博學識，而不只是狹窄技術訓練。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"world view","meaning":"世界觀","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao’s world view integrated several major traditions.","zh":"孫思邈的世界觀融合了幾個主要傳統。"},{"en":"A world view is the way a person understands life, values, society, and the universe.","zh":"world view 指一個人理解人生、價值、社會和宇宙的方式。"},{"en":"A student’s world view may change after volunteering in a poor community.","zh":"學生在貧困社區做義工後，世界觀可能改變。"},{"en":"World views influence how people judge right and wrong, health and illness, or duty and compassion.","zh":"世界觀影響人如何判斷對錯、健康與疾病，或責任與慈悲。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a person’s broad outlook on life.","zh":"這個短語指一個人對人生的廣闊看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"integrate notions of","meaning":"融合……的觀念","examples":[{"en":"His world view integrated notions of Confucianism, Daoism and Buddhism.","zh":"他的世界觀融合了儒家、道家和佛教的觀念。"},{"en":"To integrate notions of different traditions means to combine ideas from them into one connected view.","zh":"integrate notions of different traditions 指把來自不同傳統的思想結合成一個連貫看法。"},{"en":"A teacher may integrate notions of psychology and language learning when designing speaking lessons.","zh":"老師設計口語課時，可能融合心理學和語言學習的觀念。"},{"en":"Integration allows people to use ideas from several sources rather than choosing only one.","zh":"融合讓人使用多個來源的思想，而不是只選一個。"},{"en":"The phrase describes combining concepts into a wider framework.","zh":"這個短語描述把概念結合成更廣闊框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"major currents","meaning":"主要思潮","examples":[{"en":"Confucianism, Daoism and Buddhism were major currents of thought.","zh":"儒家、道家和佛教是主要思潮。"},{"en":"Major currents are important streams or movements of ideas in a culture or period.","zh":"major currents 指一個文化或時代中重要的思想潮流或運動。"},{"en":"In education, major currents today include technology use, wellbeing, and personalised learning.","zh":"在教育中，今日主要思潮包括科技使用、身心健康和個人化學習。"},{"en":"When several currents compete, thinkers may combine, reject, or revise their ideas.","zh":"當幾種思潮競爭，思想家可能融合、拒絕或修正它們。"},{"en":"The phrase uses the image of flowing water to describe influential ideas.","zh":"這個短語用流水意象描述有影響力的思想。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"compete at his time","meaning":"在他那個時代相互競爭","examples":[{"en":"Several intellectual currents were competing at his time.","zh":"幾種思想潮流在他那個時代相互競爭。"},{"en":"To compete at his time means to exist together and struggle for influence during his lifetime.","zh":"compete at his time 指在他有生之年共同存在並爭奪影響力。"},{"en":"Different teaching methods may compete at one school when teachers disagree about what works best.","zh":"當老師對甚麼方法最有效有不同意見，不同教學方法可能在一所學校內競爭。"},{"en":"Competing ideas can push thinkers to explain their own beliefs more clearly.","zh":"互相競爭的思想可以迫使思想家更清楚解釋自己的信念。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rivalry between ideas in a particular period.","zh":"這個短語描述某時期中思想之間的競爭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Confucianism","meaning":"儒家思想","examples":[{"en":"Confucianism influenced Sun Simiao’s medical ethics.","zh":"儒家思想影響了孫思邈的醫學倫理。"},{"en":"Confucianism is a Chinese tradition of thought that emphasises moral conduct, social duties, family relationships, and proper behaviour.","zh":"Confucianism 指強調道德行為、社會責任、家庭關係和合宜行為的中國思想傳統。"},{"en":"A school lesson on respect for parents may discuss Confucianism.","zh":"關於孝敬父母的學校課堂可能討論儒家思想。"},{"en":"Confucian ideas can shape medical ethics by stressing responsibility and moral duty.","zh":"儒家思想可以透過強調責任和道德義務來塑造醫學倫理。"},{"en":"The word refers to a major Chinese intellectual tradition.","zh":"這個詞指中國主要思想傳統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Daoism","meaning":"道家思想","examples":[{"en":"Daoism formed part of Sun Simiao’s world view.","zh":"道家思想構成孫思邈世界觀的一部分。"},{"en":"Daoism is a Chinese tradition that values harmony with the Dao, naturalness, balance, and simplicity.","zh":"Daoism 指重視與道和諧、自然、平衡和簡樸的中國傳統。"},{"en":"A discussion of ancient Chinese ideas about health may include Daoism and its concern with balance.","zh":"關於中國古代健康觀的討論可能包括道家思想及其對平衡的關注。"},{"en":"Daoist thought can influence medicine by linking health with nature and the body’s internal harmony.","zh":"道家思想可以透過把健康與自然和身體內在和諧連結起來影響醫學。"},{"en":"The word refers to a major Chinese philosophical and religious tradition.","zh":"這個詞指中國主要哲學和宗教傳統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Buddhism","meaning":"佛教","examples":[{"en":"Buddhism influenced Sun Simiao’s ethical concerns.","zh":"佛教影響了孫思邈的倫理關注。"},{"en":"Buddhism is a religious and philosophical tradition that teaches compassion, suffering, moral conduct, and liberation.","zh":"Buddhism 指教導慈悲、苦、道德行為和解脫的宗教及哲學傳統。"},{"en":"A charity hospital may reflect Buddhist values if it treats poor patients with compassion.","zh":"如果慈善醫院以慈悲對待貧困病人，它可能反映佛教價值。"},{"en":"Buddhist ideas can influence medical ethics by emphasising kindness toward all living beings.","zh":"佛教思想可以透過強調對所有生命的仁慈來影響醫學倫理。"},{"en":"The word refers to a major Asian religious and intellectual tradition.","zh":"這個詞指亞洲主要宗教和思想傳統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"gain fame during his lifetime","meaning":"在有生之年成名","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao gained fame during his lifetime as a clinician and author.","zh":"孫思邈在有生之年以臨床醫師和作者身份成名。"},{"en":"To gain fame during one’s lifetime means to become well known while still alive.","zh":"gain fame during one’s lifetime 指在仍然在世時變得有名。"},{"en":"A writer may gain fame during her lifetime if her books are read widely before she dies.","zh":"如果作家的書在她去世前已被廣泛閱讀，她可能在有生之年成名。"},{"en":"Fame during life allows a person to influence students, rulers, and readers directly.","zh":"生前成名讓一個人可以直接影響學生、統治者和讀者。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts living recognition with fame after death.","zh":"這個短語把生前認可與死後名聲作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"clinician","meaning":"臨床醫師","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao was famous as a clinician.","zh":"孫思邈以臨床醫師身份聞名。"},{"en":"A clinician is a medical professional who works directly with patients.","zh":"clinician 指直接與病人工作的醫療專業人員。"},{"en":"A clinician listens to symptoms, examines patients, and decides on treatment.","zh":"臨床醫師聆聽症狀、檢查病人並決定治療。"},{"en":"Clinical experience helps doctors understand illness beyond what books describe.","zh":"臨床經驗幫助醫生理解書本描述以外的疾病。"},{"en":"The word focuses on patient care, not research alone.","zh":"這個詞重點是病人照顧，而不只是研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be summoned to","meaning":"被召往……","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao was summoned to the imperial court at least once.","zh":"孫思邈至少一次被召往朝廷。"},{"en":"To be summoned to a place means to be officially called or ordered to go there.","zh":"be summoned to a place 指被正式召喚或命令前往某地。"},{"en":"A student may be summoned to the principal’s office after a serious incident.","zh":"嚴重事件後，學生可能被召往校長室。"},{"en":"Being summoned by a ruler shows that the person was considered important or needed.","zh":"被統治者召見顯示該人被視為重要或有需要。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests an official call, not a casual invitation.","zh":"這個短語暗示正式召喚，而不是普通邀請。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"imperial court","meaning":"宮廷；朝廷","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao was once summoned to the imperial court.","zh":"孫思邈曾被召往朝廷。"},{"en":"The imperial court was the emperor’s official centre of government, ceremony, and elite life.","zh":"imperial court 指皇帝的官方政府、禮儀和上層生活中心。"},{"en":"A talented doctor invited to the imperial court might treat royal family members or advise officials.","zh":"被邀到朝廷的有才醫生可能治療皇室成員或為官員提供建議。"},{"en":"Court recognition could raise a scholar’s status and spread his ideas more widely.","zh":"朝廷認可可以提升學者地位並更廣泛傳播其思想。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the political and ceremonial world around the emperor.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞皇帝的政治和禮儀世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"at least once","meaning":"至少一次","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao was summoned to the imperial court at least once.","zh":"孫思邈至少一次被召往朝廷。"},{"en":"At least once means one time or more, though the exact number may be unknown.","zh":"at least once 指一次或以上，雖然確實次數可能未知。"},{"en":"Every student should practise the speech at least once before presenting it.","zh":"每位學生演講前應至少練習一次。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a minimum number without claiming the maximum.","zh":"這個短語設定最低次數，而不聲稱最高次數。"},{"en":"It is useful when evidence confirms one occurrence but not the total count.","zh":"當證據能確認一次發生但不能確認總數時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sequel","meaning":"續篇","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao wrote Prescriptions Worth Thousands in Gold and its sequel.","zh":"孫思邈寫了《千金方》及其續篇。"},{"en":"A sequel is a later work that continues or follows an earlier work.","zh":"sequel 指延續或接續早期作品的後續作品。"},{"en":"A popular children’s book may have a sequel that follows the same characters into a new adventure.","zh":"受歡迎兒童書可能有續篇，讓同一角色展開新冒險。"},{"en":"Sequels allow authors to expand ideas, add cases, or correct earlier gaps.","zh":"續篇讓作者擴展想法、加入案例或補足早期不足。"},{"en":"The word refers to a follow-up work.","zh":"這個詞指後續作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in contrast to","meaning":"與……形成對比","examples":[{"en":"In contrast to later developments, Tang physicians relied mainly on prescriptions.","zh":"與後來發展形成對比，唐代醫師主要依賴處方。"},{"en":"In contrast to means compared with something different or opposite.","zh":"in contrast to 指與不同或相反的事物相比。"},{"en":"In contrast to online lessons, face-to-face classes allow teachers to notice body language more easily.","zh":"與網課形成對比，面授課讓老師更容易注意到身體語言。"},{"en":"The phrase helps writers show difference between two periods, ideas, or systems.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者顯示兩個時期、思想或制度之間的差異。"},{"en":"It makes comparison clear by highlighting opposition.","zh":"它透過突出相反之處令比較清楚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rely on","meaning":"依賴","examples":[{"en":"Tang physicians relied on prescriptions and single substances.","zh":"唐代醫師依賴處方和單一藥物。"},{"en":"To rely on something means to depend on it for support, help, or results.","zh":"rely on something 指依靠某物提供支援、幫助或結果。"},{"en":"Many students rely on examples to understand difficult grammar.","zh":"許多學生依賴例句來理解困難文法。"},{"en":"If doctors rely on prescriptions, written formulas become central to treatment.","zh":"如果醫生依賴處方，書面方劑就成為治療核心。"},{"en":"The phrase shows dependence, not casual use.","zh":"這個短語顯示依賴，而不是隨便使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"prescriptions and single substances","meaning":"處方和單一藥物","examples":[{"en":"Physicians relied on prescriptions and single substances to treat illnesses.","zh":"醫師依賴處方和單一藥物來治療疾病。"},{"en":"Prescriptions and single substances are prepared formulas and individual medicinal ingredients used for treatment.","zh":"prescriptions and single substances 指用於治療的配製方劑和個別藥物成分。"},{"en":"A doctor may use a mixed prescription for a complex illness and a single substance for a simple symptom.","zh":"醫生可能用複方處理複雜疾病，用單一藥物處理簡單症狀。"},{"en":"Depending on these treatments shows that pharmacological practice was central to Tang medicine.","zh":"依賴這些治療顯示藥物實踐是唐代醫學核心。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts combined formulas with individual medicines.","zh":"這個短語把組合方劑與個別藥物作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"treat patients’ illnesses","meaning":"治療病人的疾病","examples":[{"en":"Tang physicians used prescriptions to treat patients’ illnesses.","zh":"唐代醫師使用處方來治療病人的疾病。"},{"en":"To treat patients’ illnesses means to use medical methods to reduce or cure disease in patients.","zh":"treat patients’ illnesses 指使用醫療方法減輕或治癒病人的疾病。"},{"en":"A family doctor treats patients’ illnesses by diagnosing symptoms and choosing suitable medicine.","zh":"家庭醫生透過診斷症狀和選擇合適藥物來治療病人的疾病。"},{"en":"Effective treatment depends on understanding the illness and applying the right method safely.","zh":"有效治療取決於理解疾病並安全地應用正確方法。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on medical care for sick people.","zh":"這個短語重點是對病人的醫療照顧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"theories of systematic correspondences","meaning":"系統對應理論","examples":[{"en":"Theories of systematic correspondences were linked to acupuncture.","zh":"系統對應理論與針灸有關。"},{"en":"Theories of systematic correspondences are ideas that explain how different parts of the body, nature, or time are connected in ordered patterns.","zh":"theories of systematic correspondences 指解釋身體、自然或時間的不同部分如何以有序模式互相關聯的思想。"},{"en":"A traditional medical system may link seasons, organs, and symptoms through systematic correspondences.","zh":"傳統醫學系統可能透過系統對應把季節、器官和症狀連起來。"},{"en":"Such theories help practitioners interpret illness through relationships rather than isolated symptoms.","zh":"這類理論幫助從關係而不是孤立症狀來理解疾病。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an organised theory of connections.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的關聯理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"characteristic of","meaning":"……的特徵","examples":[{"en":"Systematic correspondences were characteristic of the acupuncture tradition.","zh":"系統對應是針灸傳統的特徵。"},{"en":"Characteristic of something means typical of it or commonly found in it.","zh":"characteristic of something 指某事物的典型特質或常見特徵。"},{"en":"Short, clear examples are characteristic of good teaching materials for beginners.","zh":"短而清楚的例句是初學者良好教材的特徵。"},{"en":"A feature that is characteristic of a tradition helps people recognise that tradition.","zh":"某項特徵若是某傳統的典型特質，就能幫助人辨認該傳統。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a typical quality.","zh":"這個短語指出典型特質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"acupuncture tradition","meaning":"針灸傳統","examples":[{"en":"The acupuncture tradition developed theories of systematic correspondences.","zh":"針灸傳統發展出系統對應理論。"},{"en":"The acupuncture tradition is the body of practices, ideas, and teachings connected with acupuncture over time.","zh":"acupuncture tradition 指隨時間與針灸相關的做法、思想和教導整體。"},{"en":"A medical historian may study the acupuncture tradition through old manuals and training methods.","zh":"醫學史學家可能透過舊手冊和訓練方法研究針灸傳統。"},{"en":"Traditions develop when knowledge is taught, practised, revised, and passed on.","zh":"當知識被教授、實踐、修訂和傳承，傳統就會發展。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to more than the act of inserting needles; it includes theory and training.","zh":"這個短語不只是指插針動作，也包括理論和訓練。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be extended to cover","meaning":"被擴展至涵蓋……","examples":[{"en":"These theories had not yet been extended to cover pharmacology.","zh":"這些理論尚未被擴展至涵蓋藥理學。"},{"en":"To be extended to cover something means to be expanded so that it includes that area too.","zh":"be extended to cover something 指被擴大到也包括該範疇。"},{"en":"A school rule about phones may be extended to cover smartwatches.","zh":"關於手機的校規可能被擴展至涵蓋智能手錶。"},{"en":"When a theory is extended, it can explain more subjects than before.","zh":"當理論被擴展，它可以解釋比以前更多主題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes widening the scope of an idea or rule.","zh":"這個短語描述擴大思想或規則的範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"pharmacology","meaning":"藥理學","examples":[{"en":"Systematic theories had not yet been extended to pharmacology.","zh":"系統理論尚未被擴展至藥理學。"},{"en":"Pharmacology is the study of medicines, their effects, and how they work in the body.","zh":"pharmacology 指研究藥物、其作用，以及它們如何在身體內運作的學科。"},{"en":"Medical students study pharmacology to learn correct doses and possible side effects.","zh":"醫學生學習藥理學，以了解正確劑量和可能副作用。"},{"en":"Understanding pharmacology helps doctors use medicines safely and effectively.","zh":"理解藥理學幫助醫生安全有效地使用藥物。"},{"en":"The word refers to the science of drugs and medicinal substances.","zh":"這個詞指藥物和藥用物質的科學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rise to the pantheon of","meaning":"躋身……神祇行列","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao rose to the pantheon of Chinese popular Buddhism.","zh":"孫思邈躋身中國民間佛教神祇行列。"},{"en":"To rise to the pantheon of a tradition means to become honoured among its most revered figures.","zh":"rise to the pantheon of a tradition 指成為某傳統中最受尊崇人物之一。"},{"en":"A national hero may rise to the pantheon of public memory after generations continue to honour him.","zh":"如果幾代人持續紀念某位民族英雄，他可能躋身公共記憶中的偉人行列。"},{"en":"This happens when admiration becomes deep, lasting, and almost sacred.","zh":"當敬仰變得深厚、持久並近乎神聖，這種情況就會發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes elevation to a very high symbolic status.","zh":"這個短語描述被提升至非常高的象徵地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Chinese popular Buddhism","meaning":"中國民間佛教","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao became important in Chinese popular Buddhism.","zh":"孫思邈在中國民間佛教中變得重要。"},{"en":"Chinese popular Buddhism refers to Buddhist belief and practice as lived by ordinary Chinese communities.","zh":"Chinese popular Buddhism 指普通中國社群日常實踐中的佛教信仰和做法。"},{"en":"Popular Buddhism may include temple worship, protective deities, healing rituals, and local festivals.","zh":"民間佛教可能包括寺廟敬拜、護法神、治療儀式和地方節日。"},{"en":"A historical doctor could become important in popular Buddhism if people associated him with healing and protection.","zh":"如果人們把一位歷史醫生與治療和保護聯繫起來，他可能在民間佛教中變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on Buddhism in everyday religious life.","zh":"這個短語重點是日常宗教生活中的佛教。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be revered as","meaning":"被尊為","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao was revered as the paramount Medicine God.","zh":"孫思邈被尊為最高醫藥之神。"},{"en":"To be revered as something means to be deeply respected and honoured in that role.","zh":"be revered as something 指在某角色中被深深尊敬和敬奉。"},{"en":"A teacher may be revered as the founder of a school’s strongest writing programme.","zh":"一位老師可能被尊為學校最強寫作課程的創立者。"},{"en":"People are revered when later generations continue to honour their wisdom or service.","zh":"當後代繼續敬重某人的智慧或服務，他就會受尊崇。"},{"en":"The phrase is stronger than “respected”; it suggests deep admiration.","zh":"這個短語比 respected 更強，暗示深厚敬仰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"paramount Medicine God","meaning":"最高醫藥之神","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao was revered as the paramount Medicine God.","zh":"孫思邈被尊為最高醫藥之神。"},{"en":"The paramount Medicine God means the highest or most important deity associated with medicine and healing.","zh":"paramount Medicine God 指與醫藥和治療相關的最高或最重要神祇。"},{"en":"In a temple, worshippers may pray to a Medicine God for recovery from illness.","zh":"在寺廟中，信眾可能向醫藥之神祈求疾病康復。"},{"en":"Calling someone paramount shows that he stands above other figures in status.","zh":"稱某人為 paramount 顯示他在地位上高於其他人物。"},{"en":"The phrase combines religious honour with medical memory.","zh":"這個短語結合宗教尊崇和醫學記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"extraordinary position","meaning":"非凡地位","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao gained an extraordinary position in Chinese collective memory.","zh":"孫思邈在中國集體記憶中獲得非凡地位。"},{"en":"An extraordinary position is a very unusual, important, or respected place in people’s memory or society.","zh":"extraordinary position 指在人們記憶或社會中非常不尋常、重要或受尊敬的位置。"},{"en":"A school founder may hold an extraordinary position in alumni memory if generations still quote her words.","zh":"如果幾代校友仍引用一位學校創辦人的話，她可能在校友記憶中有非凡地位。"},{"en":"Such a position develops when influence continues long after a person’s lifetime.","zh":"當影響在一個人死後很久仍延續，這種地位就會形成。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses exceptional status.","zh":"這個短語強調特殊地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Chinese collective memory","meaning":"中國集體記憶","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao held a special place in Chinese collective memory.","zh":"孫思邈在中國集體記憶中佔有特殊位置。"},{"en":"Chinese collective memory means the shared memory of Chinese society about important people, events, and values.","zh":"Chinese collective memory 指中國社會對重要人物、事件和價值的共同記憶。"},{"en":"Historical festivals help keep collective memory alive by repeating stories every year.","zh":"歷史節日透過每年重述故事，幫助集體記憶延續。"},{"en":"When a figure enters collective memory, people remember him beyond academic history.","zh":"當一個人物進入集體記憶，人們對他的記得就超越學術歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what a culture remembers together.","zh":"這個短語指一種文化共同記住的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"outstanding clinician and writer","meaning":"傑出的臨床醫師和作家","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao was an outstanding clinician and writer.","zh":"孫思邈是一位傑出的臨床醫師和作家。"},{"en":"An outstanding clinician and writer is someone excellent both in treating patients and producing important medical writings.","zh":"outstanding clinician and writer 指在治療病人和撰寫重要醫學作品方面都很出色的人。"},{"en":"A doctor who heals patients well and writes clear textbooks can be an outstanding clinician and writer.","zh":"能好好治療病人並寫出清楚教科書的醫生，可以是傑出的臨床醫師和作家。"},{"en":"Combining practice and writing allows medical knowledge to help both present patients and future readers.","zh":"結合實踐和寫作，讓醫學知識既幫助當下病人，也幫助未來讀者。"},{"en":"The phrase praises excellence in both care and scholarship.","zh":"這個短語讚揚照顧病人和學術寫作兩方面的卓越。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ethical concerns","meaning":"倫理關注","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao was remembered partly for his ethical concerns.","zh":"孫思邈被記住，部分原因是他的倫理關注。"},{"en":"Ethical concerns are worries or principles about what is morally right and wrong.","zh":"ethical concerns 指關於道德上對與錯的擔憂或原則。"},{"en":"A teacher has ethical concerns when deciding how to grade a student who was seriously ill.","zh":"老師在決定如何評分一位重病學生時，會有倫理關注。"},{"en":"In medicine, ethical concerns protect patients from selfish, careless, or harmful treatment.","zh":"在醫學中，倫理關注保護病人免受自私、粗心或有害治療。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on moral responsibility.","zh":"這個短語重點是道德責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"first Chinese author known to","meaning":"已知第一位……的中國作者","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao was the first Chinese author known to write a medical ethical code.","zh":"孫思邈是已知第一位撰寫醫學倫理守則的中國作者。"},{"en":"The first Chinese author known to do something means the earliest Chinese writer for whom evidence shows that action.","zh":"first Chinese author known to do something 指根據證據可知最早做某事的中國作者。"},{"en":"A scholar may be the first local author known to write a textbook on modern astronomy.","zh":"一位學者可能是已知第一位撰寫現代天文學教科書的本地作者。"},{"en":"The phrase depends on available evidence, not absolute certainty that no one earlier did it.","zh":"這個短語取決於現有證據，不代表絕對確定以前沒有人做過。"},{"en":"It identifies historical priority based on records.","zh":"它根據紀錄指出歷史上的優先地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"compose an elaborate medical ethical code","meaning":"編寫詳盡的醫學倫理守則","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao composed an elaborate medical ethical code.","zh":"孫思邈編寫了一套詳盡的醫學倫理守則。"},{"en":"To compose an elaborate medical ethical code means to write a detailed set of moral rules for medical practice.","zh":"compose an elaborate medical ethical code 指撰寫一套詳細規範醫療實踐的道德規則。"},{"en":"A hospital committee may compose an ethical code explaining how doctors should treat vulnerable patients.","zh":"醫院委員會可能編寫倫理守則，解釋醫生應如何對待弱勢病人。"},{"en":"A detailed code guides behaviour when doctors face difficult choices.","zh":"詳細守則在醫生面對困難選擇時指導行為。"},{"en":"The phrase combines writing, detail, medicine, and moral duty.","zh":"這個短語結合寫作、細節、醫學和道德責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"medical ethical code","meaning":"醫學倫理守則","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao wrote a medical ethical code for physicians.","zh":"孫思邈為醫師撰寫醫學倫理守則。"},{"en":"A medical ethical code is a set of moral rules guiding how medical professionals should behave.","zh":"medical ethical code 指指導醫療專業人員應如何行事的一套道德規則。"},{"en":"A medical ethical code may tell doctors to avoid greed, protect patients, and treat people fairly.","zh":"醫學倫理守則可能要求醫生避免貪婪、保護病人並公平待人。"},{"en":"Ethical codes are important because patients are vulnerable and must trust medical workers.","zh":"倫理守則很重要，因為病人處於脆弱位置並必須信任醫護人員。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to moral standards in healthcare.","zh":"這個短語指醫療中的道德標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"based on","meaning":"基於","examples":[{"en":"His ethical code was based on Buddhist and Confucian values.","zh":"他的倫理守則基於佛教和儒家價值觀。"},{"en":"Based on means built from, supported by, or developed from a particular source.","zh":"based on 指建基於、受支持於或由某來源發展而來。"},{"en":"A school rule based on student safety may ban running in crowded corridors.","zh":"基於學生安全的校規可能禁止在擁擠走廊奔跑。"},{"en":"When an idea is based on clear values, people can understand why it exists.","zh":"當一個想法基於清楚價值，人們就能理解它為何存在。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the foundation behind something.","zh":"這個短語指出某事背後的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Buddhist and Confucian values","meaning":"佛教和儒家價值觀","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao’s deontology was based on Buddhist and Confucian values.","zh":"孫思邈的義務倫理基於佛教和儒家價值觀。"},{"en":"Buddhist and Confucian values are moral ideas drawn from Buddhism and Confucianism.","zh":"Buddhist and Confucian values 指來自佛教和儒家思想的道德觀念。"},{"en":"Compassion from Buddhism and duty from Confucianism can both shape how a doctor treats patients.","zh":"佛教的慈悲和儒家的責任都可以塑造醫生如何對待病人。"},{"en":"Combining values from different traditions can create a broad ethical framework.","zh":"結合不同傳統的價值，可以創造廣闊倫理框架。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to moral principles, not medical techniques.","zh":"這個短語指道德原則，而不是醫療技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"deontology","meaning":"義務倫理；職業倫理","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao’s deontology can be compared with the Hippocratic Oath.","zh":"孫思邈的義務倫理可與希波克拉底誓詞相比。"},{"en":"Deontology is an ethical approach focused on duties, rules, and obligations.","zh":"deontology 指集中於責任、規則和義務的倫理取向。"},{"en":"A teacher follows deontology when she refuses to change marks unfairly, even under pressure.","zh":"老師即使受壓也拒絕不公平改分，就是遵循義務倫理。"},{"en":"In medicine, deontology asks what doctors must do because of their professional duty.","zh":"在醫學中，義務倫理會問醫生因專業責任必須做甚麼。"},{"en":"The word refers to duty-based ethics.","zh":"這個詞指以義務為本的倫理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be comparable to","meaning":"可與……相比","examples":[{"en":"His medical ethics are comparable to the Hippocratic Oath.","zh":"他的醫學倫理可與希波克拉底誓詞相比。"},{"en":"To be comparable to something means to be similar enough in importance, nature, or quality to be compared with it.","zh":"be comparable to something 指在重要性、性質或質素上相似到可以比較。"},{"en":"A local student’s essay may be comparable to a published model if it is clearly argued and well organised.","zh":"如果本地學生的作文論證清楚且組織良好，它可能可與範文相比。"},{"en":"Comparing two things helps readers see shared functions or standards.","zh":"比較兩件事幫助讀者看見共同功能或標準。"},{"en":"The phrase does not mean identical; it means meaningfully similar.","zh":"這個短語不表示完全相同，而是有意義地相似。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"Hippocratic Oath","meaning":"希波克拉底誓詞","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao’s ethical code is comparable to the Hippocratic Oath.","zh":"孫思邈的倫理守則可與希波克拉底誓詞相比。"},{"en":"The Hippocratic Oath is a famous ethical statement traditionally associated with doctors’ professional duties.","zh":"Hippocratic Oath 指一份著名倫理誓詞，傳統上與醫生專業義務相關。"},{"en":"Medical students may discuss the Hippocratic Oath when learning about patient trust and responsibility.","zh":"醫學生學習病人信任和責任時，可能討論希波克拉底誓詞。"},{"en":"Such an oath reminds doctors that skill must be guided by moral duty.","zh":"這類誓詞提醒醫生，技能必須受道德責任引導。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a classic symbol of medical ethics.","zh":"這個短語指醫學倫理的經典象徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"initiate a debate on","meaning":"開啟關於……的討論","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao’s code initiated a debate on the task of medicine.","zh":"孫思邈的守則開啟了關於醫學任務的討論。"},{"en":"To initiate a debate on something means to start a serious discussion about it.","zh":"initiate a debate on something 指開始對某事進行認真討論。"},{"en":"A new school policy may initiate a debate on how much homework is healthy.","zh":"新校政可能開啟關於多少功課才健康的討論。"},{"en":"Important texts can start debates because they raise questions others continue to discuss.","zh":"重要文本可以開啟討論，因為它們提出別人會繼續討論的問題。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on beginning a wider argument or discussion.","zh":"這個短語重點是開始更廣泛爭論或討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the task of medicine","meaning":"醫學的任務","examples":[{"en":"The debate considered the task of medicine.","zh":"該討論思考醫學的任務。"},{"en":"The task of medicine means what medicine is supposed to do and what responsibilities it has.","zh":"task of medicine 指醫學應該做甚麼，以及它有甚麼責任。"},{"en":"A medical ethics class may ask whether the task of medicine is only to cure illness or also to comfort patients.","zh":"醫學倫理課可能問，醫學的任務是否只為治病，還是也要安慰病人。"},{"en":"Defining medicine’s task affects how doctors treat the poor, the dying, and the vulnerable.","zh":"定義醫學任務會影響醫生如何對待貧困者、臨終者和弱勢者。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to medicine’s purpose and duty.","zh":"這個短語指醫學的目的和責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"professional obligations","meaning":"專業義務","examples":[{"en":"The debate covered physicians’ professional obligations.","zh":"該討論涵蓋醫師的專業義務。"},{"en":"Professional obligations are duties that come with a particular job or profession.","zh":"professional obligations 指某職業或專業所附帶的責任。"},{"en":"Teachers have professional obligations to prepare lessons, mark fairly, and protect students.","zh":"老師有備課、公平評分和保護學生的專業義務。"},{"en":"In medicine, professional obligations help ensure that doctors act for patients, not only for money.","zh":"在醫學中，專業義務幫助確保醫生為病人行事，而不只是為金錢。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to responsibilities required by a profession.","zh":"這個短語指由專業要求的責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"social position","meaning":"社會地位","examples":[{"en":"The debate considered the social position of medicine.","zh":"該討論思考醫學的社會地位。"},{"en":"Social position means the status, role, or respect something or someone has in society.","zh":"social position 指某人或某事在社會中的地位、角色或受尊重程度。"},{"en":"A teacher’s social position may be high in a community that values education deeply.","zh":"在重視教育的社區中，老師的社會地位可能很高。"},{"en":"The social position of medicine affects how doctors are trusted, paid, and regulated.","zh":"醫學的社會地位影響醫生如何被信任、獲薪酬和受規管。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to place within society’s hierarchy and values.","zh":"這個短語指在社會階層和價值中的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"moral justification","meaning":"道德正當性","examples":[{"en":"The debate addressed the moral justification of medicine.","zh":"該討論處理醫學的道德正當性。"},{"en":"Moral justification means the ethical reason that makes an action or profession right and acceptable.","zh":"moral justification 指令某行動或職業在倫理上正確和可接受的理由。"},{"en":"A school punishment needs moral justification, such as protecting students from harm.","zh":"學校懲罰需要道德正當性，例如保護學生免受傷害。"},{"en":"Medicine needs moral justification because doctors hold power over vulnerable patients.","zh":"醫學需要道德正當性，因為醫生對脆弱病人擁有權力。"},{"en":"The phrase asks why something is ethically acceptable.","zh":"這個短語是在問某事為何在倫理上可接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the arrival of Western medicine","meaning":"西方醫學的傳入","examples":[{"en":"The debate continued until the arrival of Western medicine.","zh":"這場討論一直延續至西方醫學傳入。"},{"en":"The arrival of Western medicine means the introduction or spread of Western medical ideas and practices into a place.","zh":"arrival of Western medicine 指西方醫學思想和做法被引入或傳播到某地。"},{"en":"The arrival of modern computers changed how schools stored student records.","zh":"現代電腦的引入改變了學校儲存學生紀錄的方式。"},{"en":"When a new system arrives, older debates may change because people compare different methods.","zh":"當新制度傳入，舊討論可能改變，因為人們會比較不同方法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a historical introduction, not a person physically arriving.","zh":"這個短語指歷史上的傳入，而不是某人實際到達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"despite or more likely because of","meaning":"儘管，或更可能是因為……","examples":[{"en":"Despite or more likely because of its stability, Tang medicine added few new ideas.","zh":"儘管，或更可能是因為其穩定性，唐代醫學加入的新思想很少。"},{"en":"Despite or more likely because of means although one explanation is possible, the opposite explanation is probably more accurate.","zh":"despite or more likely because of 指雖然一種解釋可能成立，但相反解釋可能更準確。"},{"en":"Despite or more likely because of his confidence, the student stopped asking for feedback and improved slowly.","zh":"儘管，或更可能是因為他的自信，那位學生停止尋求回饋，進步很慢。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a careful correction in reasoning.","zh":"這個短語顯示推理中的謹慎修正。"},{"en":"It means the stated factor may not be a problem to overcome, but the real cause.","zh":"它表示所述因素可能不是需要克服的問題，而是真正原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"long-lasting affluence","meaning":"長期富裕","examples":[{"en":"The Tang dynasty enjoyed long-lasting affluence and political stability.","zh":"唐代享有長期富裕和政治穩定。"},{"en":"Long-lasting affluence means wealth and prosperity that continue for a long time.","zh":"long-lasting affluence 指持續很長時間的財富和繁榮。"},{"en":"A city with long-lasting affluence can build schools, hospitals, parks, and libraries.","zh":"有長期富裕的城市可以興建學校、醫院、公園和圖書館。"},{"en":"Wealth that lasts may reduce pressure for urgent reform because life already feels stable.","zh":"持久財富可能減少迫切改革壓力，因為生活已感到穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase combines money, comfort, and duration.","zh":"這個短語結合金錢、舒適和持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"political stability","meaning":"政治穩定","examples":[{"en":"Political stability may have reduced the need for new medical ideas.","zh":"政治穩定可能降低了對新醫學思想的需要。"},{"en":"Political stability means a situation in which government and society remain orderly and secure.","zh":"political stability 指政府和社會保持有序和安全的情況。"},{"en":"Businesses often prefer political stability because rules and plans become more predictable.","zh":"企業通常喜歡政治穩定，因為規則和計劃變得更可預測。"},{"en":"Stability can support education and public services, but it may also reduce pressure for change.","zh":"穩定可以支持教育和公共服務，但也可能減少改變壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to steadiness in government and public life.","zh":"這個短語指政府和公共生活中的穩定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"add significantly new ideas to","meaning":"為……加入重大新意","examples":[{"en":"The Tang dynasty did not add significantly new ideas to medical theory.","zh":"唐代沒有為醫學理論加入重大新意。"},{"en":"To add significantly new ideas to a field means to introduce important fresh thinking into it.","zh":"add significantly new ideas to a field 指為某領域引入重要的新思想。"},{"en":"A student adds significantly new ideas to a group project when she gives a solution no one else considered.","zh":"當學生提出其他人沒有考慮過的解決方法，她就為小組項目加入重大新意。"},{"en":"If a field is stable and respected, people may preserve old ideas rather than create new ones.","zh":"如果某領域穩定且受尊重，人們可能保存舊思想而不是創造新思想。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses major intellectual innovation.","zh":"這個短語強調重大思想創新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"interpretation of illness","meaning":"對疾病的解釋","examples":[{"en":"Tang medicine did not greatly change the interpretation of illness.","zh":"唐代醫學沒有大幅改變對疾病的解釋。"},{"en":"The interpretation of illness means the way people explain what causes disease and what it means.","zh":"interpretation of illness 指人們如何解釋疾病成因及其意義。"},{"en":"Some people interpret a headache as stress, while others see it as a sign of poor sleep or illness.","zh":"有些人把頭痛解釋為壓力，另一些人則視為睡眠不足或疾病跡象。"},{"en":"How people interpret illness affects the treatment they choose.","zh":"人們如何解釋疾病會影響他們選擇的治療。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to explanation and meaning, not the illness itself.","zh":"這個短語指解釋和意義，而不是疾病本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"illness, health and healing","meaning":"疾病、健康與治療","examples":[{"en":"Medical ideas about illness, health and healing changed little.","zh":"關於疾病、健康與治療的醫學思想變化不大。"},{"en":"Illness, health and healing refers to disease, wellbeing, and the process of becoming well again.","zh":"illness, health and healing 指疾病、福祉，以及重新變得健康的過程。"},{"en":"A health class may discuss illness, health and healing through examples of flu, exercise, and recovery.","zh":"健康課可能透過流感、運動和康復例子討論疾病、健康與治療。"},{"en":"A medical system must explain all three: what goes wrong, what good health is, and how recovery happens.","zh":"醫療制度必須解釋三者：甚麼出了問題、甚麼是良好健康，以及如何康復。"},{"en":"The phrase covers the main concerns of medicine.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋醫學的主要關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"medical thought","meaning":"醫學思想","examples":[{"en":"Medical thought reflects human anxieties.","zh":"醫學思想反映人類焦慮。"},{"en":"Medical thought means the ideas and theories people use to understand health, illness, and treatment.","zh":"medical thought 指人們用來理解健康、疾病和治療的思想和理論。"},{"en":"Medical thought changes when new diseases, technologies, or social fears appear.","zh":"當新疾病、新技術或社會恐懼出現，醫學思想會改變。"},{"en":"A society’s medical thought may reveal what people fear most about the body and death.","zh":"一個社會的醫學思想可能揭示人們最害怕身體和死亡的甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to ideas about medicine, not medical equipment.","zh":"這個短語指關於醫學的思想，而不是醫療設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reflect human anxieties","meaning":"反映人類焦慮","examples":[{"en":"Medical thought often reflects human anxieties.","zh":"醫學思想常反映人類焦慮。"},{"en":"To reflect human anxieties means to show the fears and worries people have.","zh":"reflect human anxieties 指顯示人們的恐懼和擔憂。"},{"en":"Stories about exams often reflect students’ anxieties about failure and future choices.","zh":"關於考試的故事常反映學生對失敗和未來選擇的焦慮。"},{"en":"Medical theories may change when people become anxious about epidemics, aging, or sudden death.","zh":"當人們對疫症、衰老或突然死亡感到焦慮，醫學理論可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase links ideas with deeper social fears.","zh":"這個短語把思想與更深層社會恐懼連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"occur in the context of","meaning":"在……背景下發生","examples":[{"en":"Changes in medical thought occur in the context of new fears.","zh":"醫學思想變化在新恐懼的背景下發生。"},{"en":"To occur in the context of something means to happen within a particular situation or background.","zh":"occur in the context of something 指在某特定情況或背景中發生。"},{"en":"Changes in school rules often occur in the context of new safety concerns.","zh":"校規變化常在新安全關注的背景下發生。"},{"en":"Context matters because it helps explain why a change happened then, not earlier.","zh":"背景很重要，因為它幫助解釋為何變化在那時發生，而不是更早。"},{"en":"The phrase links an event with its surrounding conditions.","zh":"這個短語把事件與其周圍條件連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"existential fears","meaning":"生存焦慮","examples":[{"en":"New existential fears can reshape medical thought.","zh":"新的生存焦慮可以重塑醫學思想。"},{"en":"Existential fears are deep worries about survival, death, meaning, or the basic security of life.","zh":"existential fears 指關於生存、死亡、意義或生命基本安全的深層恐懼。"},{"en":"A pandemic can create existential fears because people suddenly feel life is fragile.","zh":"疫情可以造成生存焦慮，因為人們突然感到生命脆弱。"},{"en":"Such fears can make societies rethink medicine, religion, law, and daily behaviour.","zh":"這類恐懼可以令社會重新思考醫學、宗教、法律和日常行為。"},{"en":"The phrase describes very deep fears, not small everyday worries.","zh":"這個短語描述非常深層的恐懼，而不是小日常擔憂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"fundamentally changed social circumstances","meaning":"根本改變的社會環境","examples":[{"en":"Medical thought changes when social circumstances are fundamentally changed.","zh":"當社會環境根本改變時，醫學思想會改變。"},{"en":"Fundamentally changed social circumstances are basic conditions of society that have changed deeply and seriously.","zh":"fundamentally changed social circumstances 指社會基本條件出現深刻而重大的改變。"},{"en":"Online learning created fundamentally changed social circumstances for teachers, students, and parents.","zh":"網上學習為老師、學生和家長創造了根本改變的社會環境。"},{"en":"When society changes at a basic level, older ideas may no longer feel sufficient.","zh":"當社會在基本層面改變，舊思想可能不再顯得足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep structural change in society.","zh":"這個短語描述社會中的深層結構變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"nevertheless","meaning":"然而","examples":[{"en":"Nevertheless, medicine was a fascinating part of Tang civilisation.","zh":"然而，醫學是唐代文明中迷人的一部分。"},{"en":"Nevertheless means however, despite what has just been said.","zh":"nevertheless 指然而，即使剛才所說成立。"},{"en":"The essay had several grammar mistakes; nevertheless, its main argument was clear.","zh":"這篇作文有幾個文法錯誤；然而，主要論點清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a contrast that keeps the previous point but adds a different judgement.","zh":"這個短語引入對比，保留前一點同時加入不同判斷。"},{"en":"It is useful when something remains true despite a limitation.","zh":"當某事儘管有局限仍然成立時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"fascinating ingredient of","meaning":"……中迷人的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Medicine was a fascinating ingredient of Tang civilisation.","zh":"醫學是唐代文明中迷人的一部分。"},{"en":"A fascinating ingredient of something is an interesting and important part of a larger whole.","zh":"fascinating ingredient of something 指較大整體中有趣而重要的一部分。"},{"en":"School festivals are a fascinating ingredient of campus life because they show students’ creativity.","zh":"學校節慶是校園生活中迷人的一部分，因為它們展示學生創意。"},{"en":"One part can reveal much about the values and organisation of a whole society.","zh":"一個部分可以揭示整個社會的價值和組織。"},{"en":"The phrase presents a component as especially interesting.","zh":"這個短語把某個組成部分呈現為特別有趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"Tang civilisation","meaning":"唐代文明","examples":[{"en":"Medicine was an important part of Tang civilisation.","zh":"醫學是唐代文明的重要部分。"},{"en":"Tang civilisation means the culture, institutions, knowledge, art, and social life of the Tang dynasty.","zh":"Tang civilisation 指唐代的文化、制度、知識、藝術和社會生活。"},{"en":"Poetry, trade, religion, law, and medicine all help students understand Tang civilisation.","zh":"詩歌、貿易、宗教、法律和醫學都幫助學生理解唐代文明。"},{"en":"A civilisation is easier to understand when we study both elite achievements and ordinary public systems.","zh":"當我們同時研究精英成就和普通公共制度，文明會更容易理解。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the wider cultural world of Tang China.","zh":"這個短語指唐代中國更廣闊的文化世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"leave a rich legacy to","meaning":"為……留下豐富遺產","examples":[{"en":"Tang medicine left a rich legacy to subsequent centuries.","zh":"唐代醫學為後來數個世紀留下豐富遺產。"},{"en":"To leave a rich legacy to later times means to pass on many valuable ideas, practices, or achievements.","zh":"leave a rich legacy to later times 指把許多有價值的思想、做法或成就傳給後世。"},{"en":"A great teacher can leave a rich legacy to future students through notes, methods, and example essays.","zh":"偉大老師可以透過筆記、方法和範文，為未來學生留下豐富遺產。"},{"en":"A rich legacy continues to influence people long after its original period ends.","zh":"豐富遺產在原本時期結束很久後仍繼續影響人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lasting inheritance with depth and value.","zh":"這個短語描述具有深度和價值的持久傳承。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"subsequent centuries","meaning":"後來數個世紀","examples":[{"en":"Tang medicine influenced subsequent centuries.","zh":"唐代醫學影響後來數個世紀。"},{"en":"Subsequent centuries are the centuries that came after the period being discussed.","zh":"subsequent centuries 指所討論時期之後的幾個世紀。"},{"en":"A scientific discovery may influence subsequent centuries if later researchers build on it.","zh":"如果後來研究人員在某科學發現上繼續發展，它可能影響後來數個世紀。"},{"en":"Historical influence is strong when ideas continue to shape later generations.","zh":"當思想繼續塑造後代，歷史影響就很強。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to later time periods.","zh":"這個短語指較後的時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"choose the appropriate letters","meaning":"選出適當字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the appropriate letters for the questions.","zh":"考生為題目選出適當字母。"},{"en":"To choose the appropriate letters means to select the answer options that correctly match the questions.","zh":"choose the appropriate letters 指選擇正確配合題目的答案選項字母。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice exercise, students must choose the appropriate letters, not copy the whole answer.","zh":"在選擇題練習中，學生必須選出適當字母，而不是抄寫整個答案。"},{"en":"Choosing carefully matters because one wrong letter can change the score.","zh":"小心選擇很重要，因為一個錯字母就可以改變分數。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"draw particular attention to","meaning":"特別令人注意……","examples":[{"en":"The writer draws particular attention to the organisation of Tang medicine.","zh":"作者特別令人注意唐代醫學的組織。"},{"en":"To draw particular attention to something means to make readers notice it especially.","zh":"draw particular attention to something 指令讀者特別注意某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may draw particular attention to common article mistakes before an exam.","zh":"老師可能在考試前特別提醒學生注意常見冠詞錯誤。"},{"en":"Writers highlight a point when it is central to their argument.","zh":"當某重點是論點核心，作者就會突出它。"},{"en":"The phrase means to emphasise one detail more than others.","zh":"這個短語意思是比其他細節更強調某一點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"lack of medical knowledge","meaning":"醫學知識不足","examples":[{"en":"The answer option mentions a lack of medical knowledge before the Tang era.","zh":"該答案選項提到唐代以前醫學知識不足。"},{"en":"Lack of medical knowledge means not having enough understanding about illness, treatment, or healthcare.","zh":"lack of medical knowledge 指對疾病、治療或醫療保健沒有足夠理解。"},{"en":"A lack of medical knowledge can make people misuse antibiotics or ignore serious symptoms.","zh":"醫學知識不足可能令人誤用抗生素或忽視嚴重症狀。"},{"en":"When knowledge is lacking, harmful rumours and unsafe treatments may spread.","zh":"當知識不足，有害謠言和不安全療法可能傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase describes absence or shortage of medical understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述醫學理解的缺乏或不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"prior to","meaning":"在……之前","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to medical knowledge prior to the Tang era.","zh":"題目提到唐代之前的醫學知識。"},{"en":"Prior to means before a particular time or event.","zh":"prior to 指在某個時間或事件之前。"},{"en":"Students should check the word limit prior to writing their answers.","zh":"學生寫答案之前應先檢查字數限制。"},{"en":"The phrase helps place one thing earlier than another in time.","zh":"這個短語幫助把一件事放在另一件事之前。"},{"en":"It is more formal than “before”.","zh":"它比 before 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"Western interest in","meaning":"西方對……的興趣","examples":[{"en":"The answer option refers to Western interest in Chinese medicine.","zh":"該答案選項提到西方對中國醫學的興趣。"},{"en":"Western interest in something means attention or curiosity from people or institutions in Western countries.","zh":"Western interest in something 指西方國家的人或機構對某事的關注或好奇。"},{"en":"Western interest in Japanese animation grew as streaming platforms made it easier to watch.","zh":"隨着串流平台令觀看更容易，西方對日本動畫的興趣增加。"},{"en":"Interest from another region can lead to translation, research, trade, or cultural exchange.","zh":"來自另一地區的興趣可以帶來翻譯、研究、貿易或文化交流。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who is interested and what they are interested in.","zh":"這個短語指出誰感興趣，以及對甚麼感興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"systematic approach to","meaning":"對……的系統化處理方式","examples":[{"en":"The Tang government took a systematic approach to medical issues.","zh":"唐代政府對醫療問題採取系統化處理方式。"},{"en":"A systematic approach to something is an organised method with clear steps, rules, and structure.","zh":"systematic approach to something 指有清楚步驟、規則和結構的有組織方法。"},{"en":"A school takes a systematic approach to writing by teaching planning, drafting, feedback, and revision.","zh":"學校透過教授構思、起稿、回饋和修改，對寫作採取系統化方法。"},{"en":"Systematic approaches reduce confusion because people know what procedure to follow.","zh":"系統化方法減少混亂，因為人們知道要遵循甚麼程序。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts organised handling with random action.","zh":"這個短語把有組織處理與隨機行動作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"medical issues","meaning":"醫療問題","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses medical issues in the Tang dynasty.","zh":"文章討論唐代的醫療問題。"},{"en":"Medical issues are problems or topics related to health, illness, treatment, and healthcare systems.","zh":"medical issues 指與健康、疾病、治療和醫療制度相關的問題或主題。"},{"en":"Vaccination, hospital access, medicine safety, and doctor training are medical issues.","zh":"疫苗接種、醫院可及性、藥物安全和醫生培訓都是醫療問題。"},{"en":"Governments deal with medical issues because poor health can affect the whole population.","zh":"政府處理醫療問題，因為健康不佳可以影響整體人口。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both individual illness and public health matters.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋個人疾病和公共衛生事項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"rivalry between","meaning":"……之間的競爭","examples":[{"en":"The answer option mentions rivalry between Chinese and Western cultures.","zh":"該答案選項提到中西文化之間的競爭。"},{"en":"Rivalry between two groups means competition or tension between them.","zh":"rivalry between two groups 指兩個群體之間的競爭或緊張關係。"},{"en":"Rivalry between two schools can be healthy if it encourages better teaching and sportsmanship.","zh":"如果兩所學校之間的競爭能鼓勵更好教學和體育精神，它可以是健康的。"},{"en":"Rivalry can become harmful when comparison turns into hostility or unfair judgement.","zh":"當比較變成敵意或不公平判斷，競爭可能有害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes competitive relationship between two sides.","zh":"這個短語描述兩方之間的競爭關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"annual salary","meaning":"年薪","examples":[{"en":"A government doctor’s annual salary depended on successful cures.","zh":"政府醫生的年薪取決於成功治癒個案。"},{"en":"Annual salary is the amount of money a person earns in one year from a job.","zh":"annual salary 指一個人一年從工作中賺取的金額。"},{"en":"A teacher’s annual salary may depend on experience, qualifications, and school type.","zh":"老師年薪可能取決於經驗、資歷和學校類型。"},{"en":"Linking salary to performance can encourage effort, but it can also create pressure.","zh":"把薪金與表現掛鈎可以鼓勵努力，但也可能製造壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to yearly pay.","zh":"這個短語指每年薪酬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"depend upon","meaning":"取決於","examples":[{"en":"The salary depended upon the effectiveness of treatment.","zh":"薪酬取決於治療成效。"},{"en":"To depend upon something means to be decided or influenced by it.","zh":"depend upon something 指由某事決定或受其影響。"},{"en":"A student’s final grade may depend upon coursework, exams, and attendance.","zh":"學生最終成績可能取決於課業、考試和出席率。"},{"en":"If income depends upon results, people may pay more attention to measurable outcomes.","zh":"如果收入取決於結果，人們可能更重視可量度成果。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one thing is controlled by another factor.","zh":"這個短語顯示一件事受另一因素控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"effectiveness of treatment","meaning":"治療成效","examples":[{"en":"The doctor’s salary reflected the effectiveness of his treatment.","zh":"醫生薪酬反映其治療成效。"},{"en":"Effectiveness of treatment means how well a treatment works in improving or curing a condition.","zh":"effectiveness of treatment 指治療在改善或治癒病情方面有多有效。"},{"en":"Doctors may compare the effectiveness of treatment by checking recovery rates and side effects.","zh":"醫生可能透過檢查康復率和副作用來比較治療成效。"},{"en":"If treatment is effective, patients should become healthier or suffer less.","zh":"如果治療有效，病人應變得更健康或痛苦減少。"},{"en":"The phrase measures medical success.","zh":"這個短語量度醫療成功程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"extent of medical experience","meaning":"醫療經驗的程度","examples":[{"en":"The answer option refers to the extent of a doctor’s medical experience.","zh":"該答案選項提到醫生醫療經驗的程度。"},{"en":"Extent of medical experience means how much practical medical work or exposure a doctor has had.","zh":"extent of medical experience 指醫生有多少實際醫療工作或接觸經驗。"},{"en":"A young doctor may have less medical experience than a senior physician who has treated thousands of patients.","zh":"年輕醫生的醫療經驗可能少於治療過數千名病人的資深醫師。"},{"en":"Experience can improve judgement, but it is different from measured treatment success.","zh":"經驗可以改善判斷，但它不同於可量度的治療成功。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to amount or breadth of past medical practice.","zh":"這個短語指過往醫療實踐的數量或廣度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"breadth of medical expertise","meaning":"醫學專業知識的廣度","examples":[{"en":"The question contrasts salary with the breadth of medical expertise.","zh":"題目把薪酬與醫學專業知識的廣度作對比。"},{"en":"Breadth of medical expertise means the wide range of medical knowledge and skills a doctor has.","zh":"breadth of medical expertise 指醫生所具備的廣泛醫學知識和技能。"},{"en":"A doctor with breadth of expertise may understand internal medicine, emergency care, and public health.","zh":"具有廣泛專業知識的醫生可能理解內科、急症護理和公共衛生。"},{"en":"Broad expertise is useful, but a salary system may reward cure numbers instead.","zh":"廣泛專業知識很有用，但薪酬制度可能反而獎勵治癒數目。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on range of knowledge, not one narrow skill.","zh":"這個短語重點是知識範圍，而不是一項狹窄技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"contravene the law","meaning":"違反法律","examples":[{"en":"Certain medical practices contravened the law during the Tang era.","zh":"某些醫療做法在唐代違反法律。"},{"en":"To contravene the law means to break or go against legal rules.","zh":"contravene the law 指違反或抵觸法律規則。"},{"en":"A shop contravenes the law if it sells medicine without a licence.","zh":"如果商店無牌售賣藥物，它就違反法律。"},{"en":"When an action contravenes the law, the person responsible may be punished.","zh":"當行為違反法律，負責人可能被懲罰。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and means “violate the law”.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是「違法」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"qualified doctor","meaning":"合資格醫生","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to the actions of a qualified doctor.","zh":"題目提到合資格醫生的行為。"},{"en":"A qualified doctor is a doctor who has completed the required training and examinations.","zh":"qualified doctor 指已完成所需訓練和考試的醫生。"},{"en":"Patients usually trust a qualified doctor more than an untrained healer.","zh":"病人通常比起未受訓治療者更信任合資格醫生。"},{"en":"Qualification matters because medical mistakes can seriously harm people.","zh":"資格很重要，因為醫療錯誤可以嚴重傷害人。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to someone officially recognised as fit to practise medicine.","zh":"這個短語指被正式承認適合行醫的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"refusal to practise","meaning":"拒絕行醫","examples":[{"en":"The answer option mentions a qualified doctor’s refusal to practise.","zh":"該答案選項提到合資格醫生拒絕行醫。"},{"en":"Refusal to practise means deliberately choosing not to perform professional medical work.","zh":"refusal to practise 指故意選擇不進行專業醫療工作。"},{"en":"A doctor’s refusal to practise during an emergency may raise serious ethical questions.","zh":"醫生在緊急情況拒絕行醫，可能引起嚴重倫理問題。"},{"en":"Refusing to work can affect patients if no other medical help is available.","zh":"如果沒有其他醫療協助可用，拒絕工作可能影響病人。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on choosing not to carry out medical duties.","zh":"這個短語重點是選擇不履行醫療職責。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"unorthodox medical practices","meaning":"非正統醫療做法","examples":[{"en":"Unorthodox medical practices could be illegal in the Tang era.","zh":"非正統醫療做法在唐代可能屬違法。"},{"en":"Unorthodox medical practices are treatments that differ from accepted or standard medical methods.","zh":"unorthodox medical practices 指不同於公認或標準醫療方法的治療。"},{"en":"A healer using unknown powders without explanation may be using unorthodox medical practices.","zh":"使用來歷不明粉末而不作解釋的治療者，可能正在使用非正統醫療做法。"},{"en":"Such practices may be regulated if they put patients at risk.","zh":"如果這類做法使病人面臨風險，它們可能被規管。"},{"en":"The phrase means non-standard medical methods, not necessarily always ineffective.","zh":"這個短語意思是非標準醫療方法，不一定總是無效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"receipt of money","meaning":"收取金錢","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to the receipt of money for medical treatment.","zh":"題目提到為醫療治療收取金錢。"},{"en":"Receipt of money means the act of receiving payment.","zh":"receipt of money 指收款這一行為。"},{"en":"A tutor should keep records of the receipt of money for each lesson.","zh":"補習老師應記錄每堂課的收款情況。"},{"en":"Receiving money can make an action legally serious if the service is dishonest or unsafe.","zh":"如果服務不誠實或不安全，收取金錢可以令行為在法律上更嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and focuses on payment being taken.","zh":"這個短語較正式，重點是收取付款。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所提供資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether statements agree with the information given.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與所提供資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the text says physicians had to pass exams, a statement saying this is true agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文本說醫師必須通過考試，陳述這一點就與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should check the exact wording before choosing TRUE.","zh":"學生選 TRUE 前應檢查確切措辭。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE、FALSE、NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement is false if it contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"如果陳述與文章資料相矛盾，它就是錯誤。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage states.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章所述相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says prescriptions were publicised, saying they were kept secret contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說處方被公開公布，說它們被保密就是與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"A contradiction must be based on clear evidence, not outside knowledge.","zh":"判斷矛盾必須基於清楚證據，而不是外部知識。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct conflict with the text.","zh":"這個短語描述與文本直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文章沒有這方面的資料，考生寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not give enough evidence to decide.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有提供足夠證據作判斷。"},{"en":"If a passage names a doctor but never mentions his family, there is no information on his children.","zh":"如果文章提到一位醫生但從未提及其家庭，就沒有關於其子女的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from general knowledge when the text gives no evidence.","zh":"當文本沒有證據，學生不應憑常識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the answer cannot be proven from the passage.","zh":"這個短語表示答案不能從文章證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"academic staff","meaning":"教學人員","examples":[{"en":"Academic staff taught medical subjects in Tang colleges.","zh":"教學人員在唐代學院教授醫學科目。"},{"en":"Academic staff are teachers, lecturers, professors, and researchers working in educational institutions.","zh":"academic staff 指在教育機構工作的教師、講師、教授和研究人員。"},{"en":"Academic staff in a university may teach classes, supervise students, and publish research.","zh":"大學教學人員可能授課、指導學生和發表研究。"},{"en":"Strong academic staff improve education because students learn from trained specialists.","zh":"強大的教學人員能改善教育，因為學生向受訓專家學習。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to teaching and research personnel.","zh":"這個短語指教學和研究人員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a range of medical subjects","meaning":"一系列醫學科目","examples":[{"en":"Academic staff sometimes taught a range of medical subjects.","zh":"教學人員有時教授一系列醫學科目。"},{"en":"A range of medical subjects means several different areas of medical knowledge or training.","zh":"a range of medical subjects 指幾個不同醫學知識或訓練範疇。"},{"en":"A medical school may teach a range of subjects, including anatomy, pharmacy, ethics, and diagnosis.","zh":"醫學院可能教授一系列科目，包括解剖、藥劑、倫理和診斷。"},{"en":"A broad range helps students prepare for different patient needs.","zh":"廣泛科目幫助學生準備應對不同病人需要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses variety within medical education.","zh":"這個短語強調醫學教育中的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"benefit the wealthy","meaning":"令富人受惠","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether medical knowledge only benefited the wealthy.","zh":"該陳述問醫學知識是否只令富人受惠。"},{"en":"To benefit the wealthy means to help rich people in particular.","zh":"benefit the wealthy 指特別幫助富人。"},{"en":"Expensive private tutoring may benefit the wealthy more than low-income students.","zh":"昂貴私人補習可能令富裕學生比低收入學生更受惠。"},{"en":"Publicly shared medical knowledge can prevent benefits from being limited to rich families.","zh":"公開分享醫學知識可以防止好處只限於富裕家庭。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on who gains from a system or policy.","zh":"這個短語重點是誰從制度或政策中得益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be encouraged to","meaning":"被鼓勵去……","examples":[{"en":"Tang citizens may have been encouraged to use official prescriptions.","zh":"唐代百姓可能被鼓勵使用官方處方。"},{"en":"To be encouraged to do something means to be advised or motivated to do it.","zh":"be encouraged to do something 指被建議或推動去做某事。"},{"en":"Students are encouraged to read the question twice before answering.","zh":"學生被鼓勵在回答前讀兩次題目。"},{"en":"Encouragement can guide behaviour without forcing people directly.","zh":"鼓勵可以引導行為，而不一定直接強迫。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests support or recommendation.","zh":"這個短語暗示支持或建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"lead a healthy lifestyle","meaning":"過健康生活","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether citizens were encouraged to lead a healthy lifestyle.","zh":"該陳述問百姓是否被鼓勵過健康生活。"},{"en":"To lead a healthy lifestyle means to live in a way that supports physical and mental health.","zh":"lead a healthy lifestyle 指以支持身心健康的方式生活。"},{"en":"Sleeping enough, eating balanced meals, and exercising regularly help people lead a healthy lifestyle.","zh":"充足睡眠、均衡飲食和定期運動幫助人過健康生活。"},{"en":"A healthy lifestyle can reduce illness risk, but it does not replace medical treatment when needed.","zh":"健康生活可以降低患病風險，但在需要時不能取代醫療治療。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to everyday habits that support health.","zh":"這個短語指支持健康的日常習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"fraudulent manner","meaning":"欺詐方式","examples":[{"en":"Doctors who behaved in a fraudulent manner were punished by law.","zh":"以欺詐方式行事的醫生會被法律懲罰。"},{"en":"In a fraudulent manner means in a dishonest way intended to deceive people for gain.","zh":"in a fraudulent manner 指以不誠實方式欺騙他人以獲取利益。"},{"en":"A shop acts in a fraudulent manner if it sells fake medicine as real medicine.","zh":"如果商店把假藥當真藥出售，就是以欺詐方式行事。"},{"en":"Fraudulent behaviour harms trust because people pay for something they are falsely promised.","zh":"欺詐行為傷害信任，因為人們為虛假承諾付款。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dishonest conduct, especially involving money or false claims.","zh":"這個短語描述不誠實行為，尤其涉及金錢或虛假聲稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"ordinary criminals","meaning":"普通罪犯","examples":[{"en":"Fraudulent healers could be treated like ordinary criminals.","zh":"欺詐治療者可被當作普通罪犯處理。"},{"en":"Ordinary criminals are people who commit crimes and are punished under normal criminal law.","zh":"ordinary criminals 指犯罪並根據一般刑法受罰的人。"},{"en":"A person who steals from a shop is treated as an ordinary criminal, not a professional offender.","zh":"在商店偷竊的人被視為普通罪犯，而不是專業違規者。"},{"en":"Treating dishonest healers this way shows that medical fraud was not excused as a special case.","zh":"以這種方式處理不誠實治療者，顯示醫療欺詐沒有被視為特例而獲寬免。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts normal criminal punishment with professional discipline only.","zh":"這個短語把一般刑事懲罰與單純專業紀律作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"medical reference books","meaning":"醫學參考書","examples":[{"en":"Medical reference books covered practical and theoretical issues.","zh":"醫學參考書涵蓋實用和理論問題。"},{"en":"Medical reference books are books doctors or students consult for medical facts, treatments, and explanations.","zh":"medical reference books 指醫生或學生查閱醫學事實、治療和解釋的書。"},{"en":"A nurse may check a medical reference book before learning about an unfamiliar condition.","zh":"護士學習陌生病症前，可能查閱醫學參考書。"},{"en":"Reference books help standardise knowledge because many readers consult the same information.","zh":"參考書幫助標準化知識，因為許多讀者查閱同一資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to books used for checking and learning medical knowledge.","zh":"這個短語指用於查核和學習醫學知識的書。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"practical and academic issues","meaning":"實用和學術問題","examples":[{"en":"Tang medical texts covered both practical and academic issues.","zh":"唐代醫學文本同時涵蓋實用和學術問題。"},{"en":"Practical and academic issues are real-use problems and theoretical or scholarly questions.","zh":"practical and academic issues 指實際使用問題，以及理論或學術問題。"},{"en":"A teacher-training course may cover practical classroom skills and academic theories of learning.","zh":"教師培訓課程可能涵蓋實用課堂技巧和學習理論。"},{"en":"A strong field needs both practical solutions and deeper explanation.","zh":"強大領域既需要實際解決方法，也需要更深層解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts applied concerns with intellectual study.","zh":"這個短語把應用關注與學術研究作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"medical data","meaning":"醫學資料","examples":[{"en":"Waitai miyao contained medical data from older works.","zh":"《外台秘要》包含來自舊著作的醫學資料。"},{"en":"Medical data means information about diseases, treatments, prescriptions, bodies, or patient outcomes.","zh":"medical data 指關於疾病、治療、處方、身體或病人結果的資訊。"},{"en":"A hospital collects medical data to understand which treatments help patients recover fastest.","zh":"醫院收集醫學資料，以了解哪些治療能幫助病人最快康復。"},{"en":"Old medical data can preserve earlier experience even when original books are lost.","zh":"舊醫學資料可以保存早期經驗，即使原書已失傳。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to health-related information used for study or practice.","zh":"這個短語指用於研究或實踐的健康相關資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"influence Indian writing","meaning":"影響印度著作","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Chinese medical authors influenced Indian writing.","zh":"該陳述問中國醫學作者是否影響印度著作。"},{"en":"To influence Indian writing means to affect texts, ideas, or authors in the Indian tradition.","zh":"influence Indian writing 指影響印度傳統中的文本、思想或作者。"},{"en":"A popular teaching method from one country may influence education writing in another country.","zh":"一個國家的受歡迎教學方法可能影響另一國的教育著作。"},{"en":"Influence can be shown when later writers borrow, translate, or respond to earlier ideas.","zh":"當後來作者借用、翻譯或回應早期思想，就可以顯示影響。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on cross-cultural impact on written work.","zh":"這個短語重點是對書面作品的跨文化影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"complete the sentences below","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the sentences below with words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成以下句子。"},{"en":"To complete the sentences below means to fill the blanks in the following sentences.","zh":"complete the sentences below 指填補下方句子中的空格。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole sentence before choosing the answer.","zh":"學生選答案前應讀完整句子。"},{"en":"Completing sentences correctly requires understanding both meaning and grammar.","zh":"正確完成句子需要理解意思和文法。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"words taken from","meaning":"取自……的字詞","examples":[{"en":"The answers should use words taken from Reading Passage 3.","zh":"答案應使用取自閱讀篇章三的字詞。"},{"en":"Words taken from a passage are exact words copied from that text.","zh":"words taken from a passage 指從該文本中原文抄出的字詞。"},{"en":"In IELTS reading, an answer may be wrong if students use their own words instead of words taken from the passage.","zh":"在 IELTS 閱讀中，如果學生用自己的字而不是取自文章的字詞，答案可能錯。"},{"en":"This rule forces candidates to locate the exact phrase in the text.","zh":"這條規則迫使考生在文本中找到準確短語。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses source-based wording.","zh":"這個短語強調以來源文字作答。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should use no more than three words.","zh":"每個答案應使用不多於三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must contain one, two, or three words only.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案只能包含一個、兩個或三個詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “medical ethical code”, it fits because it has three words.","zh":"如果答案是 “medical ethical code”，它符合要求，因為有三個詞。"},{"en":"Writing four words may lose marks even if the meaning is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫四個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict exam word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格考試字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"dates back to","meaning":"追溯至","examples":[{"en":"The first known medical writing in China dates back to the second century BC.","zh":"中國已知最早醫學著作可追溯至公元前二世紀。"},{"en":"To date back to a time means to have existed since that earlier period.","zh":"date back to a time 指自較早時期起已存在。"},{"en":"The school’s speech day tradition dates back to the 1950s.","zh":"學校演講日傳統可追溯至1950年代。"},{"en":"If a practice dates back many centuries, it has a long recorded history.","zh":"如果某做法可追溯至多個世紀前，它就有悠長記錄歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase traces something to an earlier origin.","zh":"這個短語把某事追溯到較早起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"depend most on","meaning":"最依賴","examples":[{"en":"Tang doctors depended most on prescriptions and single substances.","zh":"唐代醫生最依賴處方和單一藥物。"},{"en":"To depend most on something means to rely on it more than on other methods or resources.","zh":"depend most on something 指比起其他方法或資源更依賴某事。"},{"en":"Some students depend most on examples when learning grammar.","zh":"有些學生學文法時最依賴例句。"},{"en":"What people depend most on reveals what they consider central or reliable.","zh":"人們最依賴甚麼，揭示他們認為甚麼最核心或可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the main source of support or method used.","zh":"這個短語顯示主要支援來源或使用方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"single substances","meaning":"單一藥物","examples":[{"en":"Doctors used prescriptions and single substances to treat patients.","zh":"醫生使用處方和單一藥物治療病人。"},{"en":"Single substances are individual medicinal ingredients used alone rather than as part of a mixture.","zh":"single substances 指單獨使用、而非作為混合方劑一部分的個別藥物成分。"},{"en":"A doctor may use one single substance for a simple symptom but a formula for a complex illness.","zh":"醫生可能用單一藥物處理簡單症狀，但用方劑處理複雜疾病。"},{"en":"Using single substances requires knowing the effect and risk of each ingredient clearly.","zh":"使用單一藥物需要清楚知道每種成分的作用和風險。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts one ingredient with combined prescriptions.","zh":"這個短語把一種成分與組合處方作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"set of medical rules","meaning":"一套醫學規則","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao produced a set of medical rules for Chinese physicians.","zh":"孫思邈為中國醫師制定了一套醫學規則。"},{"en":"A set of medical rules is a group of guidelines that tells doctors how to practise properly.","zh":"set of medical rules 指一組告訴醫生如何正確行醫的指引。"},{"en":"A hospital may create a set of medical rules about hygiene, patient privacy, and emergency care.","zh":"醫院可能制定一套關於衛生、病人私隱和急症護理的醫學規則。"},{"en":"Clear rules reduce unsafe behaviour because doctors know what is expected.","zh":"清楚規則可以減少不安全行為，因為醫生知道被期望做甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised professional guidance.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的專業指引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"Chinese physicians","meaning":"中國醫師","examples":[{"en":"Sun Simiao wrote ethical rules for Chinese physicians.","zh":"孫思邈為中國醫師撰寫倫理規則。"},{"en":"Chinese physicians are doctors practising within Chinese medical traditions or in China.","zh":"Chinese physicians 指在中國或中國醫學傳統中行醫的醫生。"},{"en":"Chinese physicians in history often studied prescriptions, herbs, acupuncture, and medical ethics.","zh":"歷史上的中國醫師通常學習處方、草藥、針灸和醫學倫理。"},{"en":"Ethical rules guide physicians because patients depend on their knowledge and honesty.","zh":"倫理規則指導醫師，因為病人依賴他們的知識和誠信。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the doctors addressed by the medical code.","zh":"這個短語指出醫學守則所針對的醫生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 108 - THE ART OF HEALING.pdf","sourcePage":21}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 109":[{"front":"keep taking the tablets","meaning":"繼續服藥","examples":[{"en":"The title “Keep taking the tablets” introduces a passage about aspirin.","zh":"標題 “Keep taking the tablets” 引入一篇關於阿士匹靈的文章。"},{"en":"Keep taking the tablets means continue taking medicine as instructed.","zh":"keep taking the tablets 指按照指示繼續服藥。"},{"en":"A doctor may tell a patient to keep taking the tablets even after the fever improves.","zh":"即使退燒後，醫生也可能叫病人繼續服藥。"},{"en":"If patients stop too early, the illness may return or the treatment may fail.","zh":"如果病人太早停藥，疾病可能復發或治療可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing regular medicine use.","zh":"討論定期用藥時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the history of aspirin","meaning":"阿士匹靈的歷史","examples":[{"en":"The history of aspirin is full of surprising developments.","zh":"阿士匹靈的歷史充滿令人驚訝的發展。"},{"en":"The history of aspirin refers to how aspirin was discovered, developed, marketed, and reused over time.","zh":"the history of aspirin 指阿士匹靈如何被發現、發展、推廣並隨時間有新用途。"},{"en":"A science lesson may use the history of aspirin to show how old remedies become modern drugs.","zh":"科學課可能用阿士匹靈的歷史展示古老療法如何變成現代藥物。"},{"en":"Its history includes ancient medicine, chemical research, business competition, and new medical findings.","zh":"它的歷史包括古代醫學、化學研究、商業競爭和新醫學發現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the development of a famous medicine.","zh":"討論著名藥物的發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a product of","meaning":"……的產物","examples":[{"en":"The history of aspirin is a product of accidental discoveries and corporate rivalry.","zh":"阿士匹靈的歷史是偶然發現和企業競爭的產物。"},{"en":"A product of something means the result of particular causes, influences, or conditions.","zh":"a product of something 指由特定原因、影響或條件造成的結果。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may be a product of regular practice and patient teaching.","zh":"學生的信心可能是定期練習和耐心教導的產物。"},{"en":"When many forces shape one result, we can say it is a product of those forces.","zh":"當許多力量塑造一個結果，我們可以說它是那些力量的產物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining what created an outcome.","zh":"解釋某結果由甚麼造成時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a rollercoaster ride through time","meaning":"一段跌宕起伏的歷史旅程","examples":[{"en":"The history of aspirin is a rollercoaster ride through time.","zh":"阿士匹靈的歷史是一段跌宕起伏的歷史旅程。"},{"en":"A rollercoaster ride through time means a history full of ups, downs, surprises, and sudden changes.","zh":"rollercoaster ride through time 指一段充滿高低起伏、驚喜和突然轉變的歷史。"},{"en":"A company’s story can be a rollercoaster ride through time if it rises, nearly fails, and then succeeds again.","zh":"如果一間公司興起、幾乎失敗、然後再次成功，它的故事就是跌宕起伏的歷史旅程。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the story is not simple or smooth.","zh":"這個短語暗示故事並不簡單或平順。"},{"en":"It is useful when history feels dramatic and unpredictable.","zh":"當歷史感覺戲劇化和難以預測時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"accidental discoveries","meaning":"偶然發現","examples":[{"en":"Accidental discoveries played an important role in the history of aspirin.","zh":"偶然發現在阿士匹靈的歷史中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"Accidental discoveries are findings made by chance rather than through a planned result.","zh":"accidental discoveries 指偶然作出的發現，而不是按計劃得到的結果。"},{"en":"A student may make an accidental discovery when a wrong experiment still reveals something useful.","zh":"當錯誤實驗仍揭示有用東西時，學生可能作出偶然發現。"},{"en":"Scientific progress can happen when researchers notice unexpected results instead of ignoring them.","zh":"當研究人員注意意外結果而不是忽視它們，科學進步就可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when luck contributes to knowledge.","zh":"當運氣促成知識時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"intuitive reasoning","meaning":"直覺推理","examples":[{"en":"Intuitive reasoning helped scientists make progress.","zh":"直覺推理幫助科學家取得進展。"},{"en":"Intuitive reasoning is thinking based on instinct, experience, or a strong sense of what may be true.","zh":"intuitive reasoning 指基於本能、經驗或對真相的強烈感覺而作出的思考。"},{"en":"A teacher may use intuitive reasoning to guess why a student is suddenly quiet.","zh":"老師可能用直覺推理猜測為何學生突然變得安靜。"},{"en":"Intuition can guide investigation, but evidence is still needed to confirm it.","zh":"直覺可以引導調查，但仍需要證據確認。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when ideas begin from educated instinct rather than full proof.","zh":"當想法源自有經驗的直覺而非完整證明時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"intense corporate rivalry","meaning":"激烈的企業競爭","examples":[{"en":"Intense corporate rivalry shaped the development of aspirin.","zh":"激烈的企業競爭塑造了阿士匹靈的發展。"},{"en":"Intense corporate rivalry means strong competition between companies.","zh":"intense corporate rivalry 指公司之間強烈競爭。"},{"en":"Phone companies may enter intense corporate rivalry when each tries to release a better model first.","zh":"當手機公司都想率先推出更好型號，就可能進入激烈企業競爭。"},{"en":"Rivalry can speed up innovation, but it can also push companies to focus on profit.","zh":"競爭可以加快創新，但也可能推動公司只專注利潤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when business competition affects development.","zh":"當商業競爭影響發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the opening pages of","meaning":"……的開首幾頁","examples":[{"en":"In the opening pages of the book, Jeffreys describes aspirin as a wonder drug.","zh":"在書的開首幾頁，Jeffreys 把阿士匹靈描述為神奇藥物。"},{"en":"The opening pages of a book are its first few pages.","zh":"opening pages of a book 指一本書最初的幾頁。"},{"en":"In the opening pages of a novel, the writer may introduce the main character and setting.","zh":"在小說開首幾頁，作者可能介紹主角和背景。"},{"en":"Strong opening pages can shape how readers understand the whole book.","zh":"有力的開首幾頁可以塑造讀者如何理解整本書。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when referring to the beginning of a text.","zh":"指文本開端時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a remarkable story","meaning":"非凡的故事","examples":[{"en":"The book tells the remarkable story of a wonder drug.","zh":"這本書講述一種神奇藥物的非凡故事。"},{"en":"A remarkable story is a story that is unusual, impressive, and worth noticing.","zh":"remarkable story 指不尋常、令人印象深刻且值得注意的故事。"},{"en":"A student’s journey from failing English to winning a speech contest can be a remarkable story.","zh":"學生由英文不合格到贏得演講比賽，可以是一個非凡故事。"},{"en":"A story becomes remarkable when it contains struggle, surprise, and lasting impact.","zh":"當故事包含掙扎、驚喜和長遠影響，它就變得非凡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a story is more than ordinary.","zh":"當故事不只是普通事件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a wonder drug","meaning":"神奇藥物","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin is described as a wonder drug.","zh":"阿士匹靈被描述為神奇藥物。"},{"en":"A wonder drug is a medicine seen as unusually effective or useful for many conditions.","zh":"wonder drug 指被視為異常有效或可用於多種情況的藥物。"},{"en":"A new antibiotic may be called a wonder drug if it saves patients whom older medicines cannot help.","zh":"如果新抗生素能救回舊藥無法幫助的病人，它可能被稱為神奇藥物。"},{"en":"The label suggests admiration, but doctors still need evidence about risks and benefits.","zh":"這個稱呼帶有讚賞，但醫生仍需要有關風險和好處的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a medicine has an unusually strong reputation.","zh":"當一種藥物有異常強烈聲譽時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"little white pill","meaning":"白色小藥丸","examples":[{"en":"This little white pill has had a major impact on medicine.","zh":"這粒白色小藥丸對醫學產生了重大影響。"},{"en":"Little white pill refers to a small white tablet, here meaning aspirin in a simple physical form.","zh":"little white pill 指一粒小小的白色藥片，這裏指阿士匹靈的簡單外形。"},{"en":"A patient may not realise that a little white pill can contain powerful active ingredients.","zh":"病人可能沒有意識到一粒白色小藥丸可以含有強大有效成分。"},{"en":"Its small appearance contrasts with its large medical influence.","zh":"它細小的外觀與巨大的醫學影響形成對比。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a simple object has a big effect.","zh":"當簡單物件有巨大影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one of the most amazing creations in","meaning":"……中最驚人的創造之一","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin is one of the most amazing creations in medical history.","zh":"阿士匹靈是醫學史中最驚人的創造之一。"},{"en":"One of the most amazing creations in a field means one of the most impressive things ever made in that area.","zh":"one of the most amazing creations in a field 指某領域中最令人驚嘆的創造之一。"},{"en":"The internet is one of the most amazing creations in communication history.","zh":"互聯網是通訊史中最驚人的創造之一。"},{"en":"Such a phrase highlights importance, influence, and admiration.","zh":"這個短語突出重要性、影響力和讚賞。"},{"en":"It is useful when ranking something among major achievements.","zh":"把某物列為重大成就之一時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"medical history","meaning":"醫學史","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin is an important drug in medical history.","zh":"阿士匹靈是醫學史上的重要藥物。"},{"en":"Medical history is the history of medicine, diseases, treatments, doctors, and health systems.","zh":"medical history 指醫學、疾病、治療、醫生和醫療制度的歷史。"},{"en":"Students studying medical history may learn how vaccines changed public health.","zh":"學習醫學史的學生可能了解疫苗如何改變公共健康。"},{"en":"Medical history helps people understand how modern healthcare developed.","zh":"醫學史幫助人們理解現代醫療如何發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing medicine across time.","zh":"討論跨時代的醫學時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"astonishingly versatile","meaning":"用途驚人地廣泛","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin is astonishingly versatile in its medical uses.","zh":"阿士匹靈在醫學用途上驚人地廣泛。"},{"en":"Astonishingly versatile means surprisingly able to be used in many different ways.","zh":"astonishingly versatile 指令人驚訝地能以許多不同方式使用。"},{"en":"A smartphone is astonishingly versatile because it can be a camera, map, notebook, and payment tool.","zh":"智能手機用途驚人地廣泛，因為它可以是相機、地圖、筆記本和付款工具。"},{"en":"Versatility makes something valuable because it can solve several different problems.","zh":"多用途令某物有價值，因為它能解決幾種不同問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one thing has many uses.","zh":"當一件事物有很多用途時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"relieve headache","meaning":"紓緩頭痛","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin can relieve headache.","zh":"阿士匹靈可以紓緩頭痛。"},{"en":"To relieve headache means to reduce or ease pain in the head.","zh":"relieve headache 指減輕或紓緩頭部疼痛。"},{"en":"A student with a headache may rest, drink water, or take medicine after advice from an adult.","zh":"頭痛的學生可能休息、喝水，或在成人建議後服藥。"},{"en":"Pain relief can help people return to work or study more comfortably.","zh":"止痛可以幫助人更舒服地回到工作或學習。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing common symptoms and treatment.","zh":"討論常見症狀和治療時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ease your aching limbs","meaning":"紓緩四肢痠痛","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin can ease aching limbs.","zh":"阿士匹靈可以紓緩四肢痠痛。"},{"en":"To ease aching limbs means to reduce pain or soreness in the arms and legs.","zh":"ease aching limbs 指減輕手臂和腿部的疼痛或痠痛。"},{"en":"After a long hike, a person may want to ease aching limbs with rest and gentle stretching.","zh":"長途行山後，人可能想透過休息和輕柔伸展來紓緩四肢痠痛。"},{"en":"When limb pain improves, movement becomes easier and daily tasks feel less difficult.","zh":"當四肢疼痛改善，活動會較容易，日常工作也較不困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing relief from body aches.","zh":"描述身體痠痛得到紓緩時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lower your temperature","meaning":"降低體溫","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin can lower a person’s temperature.","zh":"阿士匹靈可以降低一個人的體溫。"},{"en":"To lower your temperature means to reduce fever or bring body temperature down.","zh":"lower your temperature 指退燒或降低身體溫度。"},{"en":"A child with a fever may need medicine, rest, and fluids to lower their temperature safely.","zh":"發燒的孩子可能需要藥物、休息和補充水分，安全地降低體溫。"},{"en":"Lowering a high temperature can make the patient feel less weak and uncomfortable.","zh":"降低高體溫可以令病人減少虛弱和不適。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing fever treatment.","zh":"討論退燒治療時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"treat some of the deadliest human diseases","meaning":"治療一些最致命的人類疾病","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin can treat some of the deadliest human diseases.","zh":"阿士匹靈可以治療一些最致命的人類疾病。"},{"en":"To treat some of the deadliest human diseases means to help manage or reduce risks from illnesses that kill many people.","zh":"treat some of the deadliest human diseases 指幫助處理或減低會殺死許多人的疾病風險。"},{"en":"Doctors use different medicines to treat serious diseases such as heart disease, infections, and cancer.","zh":"醫生使用不同藥物治療心臟病、感染和癌症等嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"A drug becomes especially important if it helps with conditions that threaten many lives.","zh":"如果一種藥物有助處理威脅許多生命的疾病，它就特別重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when medicine affects major causes of death.","zh":"當藥物影響主要死因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"its properties","meaning":"其特性","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin’s properties have been known for thousands of years.","zh":"阿士匹靈的特性已為人所知數千年。"},{"en":"Its properties means the qualities or effects that a thing naturally has.","zh":"its properties 指某物自然具有的特質或效果。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain the properties of water, such as freezing, boiling, and dissolving substances.","zh":"老師可能解釋水的特性，例如結冰、沸騰和溶解物質。"},{"en":"Knowing a substance’s properties helps people decide how it can be used safely.","zh":"了解物質特性有助人們決定如何安全使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing features of a material or medicine.","zh":"討論材料或藥物特徵時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be known for thousands of years","meaning":"已為人所知數千年","examples":[{"en":"The medicinal properties of willow extracts have been known for thousands of years.","zh":"柳樹提取物的藥用特性已為人所知數千年。"},{"en":"Be known for thousands of years means people have understood or used something since very ancient times.","zh":"be known for thousands of years 指人們自古代已理解或使用某物。"},{"en":"The healing value of certain herbs has been known for thousands of years in some communities.","zh":"某些草藥的療效在一些社群中已為人所知數千年。"},{"en":"Long use may suggest value, but modern testing is still needed for safety and dosage.","zh":"長期使用可能暗示價值，但仍需要現代測試確認安全和劑量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when knowledge has very old roots.","zh":"當知識有非常古老根源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Ancient Egyptian physicians","meaning":"古埃及醫師","examples":[{"en":"Ancient Egyptian physicians used extracts from the willow tree.","zh":"古埃及醫師使用柳樹提取物。"},{"en":"Ancient Egyptian physicians were doctors or healers in ancient Egypt.","zh":"Ancient Egyptian physicians 指古埃及的醫生或治療者。"},{"en":"Ancient Egyptian physicians used plants, minerals, and practical observation to treat illness.","zh":"古埃及醫師使用植物、礦物和實際觀察來治療疾病。"},{"en":"Their use of willow shows that some medical ideas existed long before modern chemistry.","zh":"他們使用柳樹，顯示一些醫學想法早於現代化學已存在。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing early medicine.","zh":"討論早期醫學時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"extracts from","meaning":"……的提取物","examples":[{"en":"Ancient physicians used extracts from the willow tree.","zh":"古代醫師使用柳樹的提取物。"},{"en":"Extracts from something are substances taken out of a plant, material, or source.","zh":"extracts from something 指從植物、材料或來源中取出的物質。"},{"en":"Tea is made using extracts from leaves when hot water draws out flavour and colour.","zh":"熱水把味道和顏色帶出茶葉時，茶就是用葉子的提取物製成。"},{"en":"Extracts can contain useful chemicals, but they may also need careful preparation.","zh":"提取物可以含有有用化學物質，但也可能需要小心製備。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing natural ingredients.","zh":"討論天然成分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the willow tree","meaning":"柳樹","examples":[{"en":"The willow tree contains chemicals related to aspirin.","zh":"柳樹含有與阿士匹靈有關的化學物質。"},{"en":"The willow tree is a tree whose bark and leaves have long been linked with pain relief.","zh":"willow tree 指一種樹，其樹皮和葉長久以來與止痛有關。"},{"en":"A traditional healer may use part of the willow tree to prepare a simple remedy.","zh":"傳統治療者可能使用柳樹的一部分來製備簡單療法。"},{"en":"Studying the willow tree helped scientists understand the chemical basis of an old medicine.","zh":"研究柳樹幫助科學家理解古老藥物的化學基礎。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing aspirin’s natural origins.","zh":"討論阿士匹靈的天然起源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"analgesic","meaning":"止痛藥","examples":[{"en":"Willow-tree extracts were used as an analgesic.","zh":"柳樹提取物被用作止痛藥。"},{"en":"An analgesic is a medicine that reduces pain.","zh":"analgesic 指能減輕疼痛的藥物。"},{"en":"A dentist may give a patient an analgesic after removing a tooth.","zh":"牙醫拔牙後可能給病人止痛藥。"},{"en":"Analgesics help people function when pain would otherwise stop normal activity.","zh":"止痛藥幫助人在疼痛本會阻礙正常活動時仍能運作。"},{"en":"This word is useful in medical contexts about pain relief.","zh":"這個詞適用於關於止痛的醫學語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"painkiller","meaning":"止痛藥","examples":[{"en":"An analgesic is a painkiller.","zh":"analgesic 是止痛藥。"},{"en":"A painkiller is a medicine used to reduce or remove pain.","zh":"painkiller 指用來減輕或消除疼痛的藥物。"},{"en":"Someone with a bad headache may take a painkiller after checking the correct dose.","zh":"嚴重頭痛的人可能在確認正確劑量後服用止痛藥。"},{"en":"Painkillers can make people feel better, but misuse can create health risks.","zh":"止痛藥可以令人感覺較好，但誤用可能造成健康風險。"},{"en":"This word is useful in everyday discussions of medicine.","zh":"這個詞適用於日常藥物討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"centuries later","meaning":"數百年後","examples":[{"en":"Centuries later, Hippocrates recommended willow bark as medicine.","zh":"數百年後，希波克拉底推薦柳樹皮作為藥物。"},{"en":"Centuries later means many hundreds of years after an earlier event.","zh":"centuries later 指在較早事件之後許多百年。"},{"en":"Centuries later, old city walls may still shape where modern roads are built.","zh":"數百年後，舊城牆仍可能影響現代道路建在哪裏。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a long gap between two historical moments.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個歷史時刻之間有長時間間隔。"},{"en":"It is useful when tracing slow development over time.","zh":"追蹤緩慢歷史發展時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Greek physician","meaning":"希臘醫師","examples":[{"en":"Hippocrates was a Greek physician.","zh":"希波克拉底是一位希臘醫師。"},{"en":"A Greek physician was a doctor or medical thinker from ancient Greece.","zh":"Greek physician 指古希臘的醫生或醫學思想家。"},{"en":"A Greek physician might observe symptoms carefully before recommending a treatment.","zh":"希臘醫師可能在建議治療前仔細觀察症狀。"},{"en":"Ancient Greek medicine influenced later European medical traditions.","zh":"古希臘醫學影響了後來歐洲醫學傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing early medical history.","zh":"討論早期醫學史時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"recommend something as","meaning":"推薦……作為","examples":[{"en":"Hippocrates recommended willow bark as a remedy.","zh":"希波克拉底推薦柳樹皮作為療法。"},{"en":"To recommend something as something means to suggest it should be used for a particular purpose.","zh":"recommend something as something 指建議把某物用作特定用途。"},{"en":"A teacher may recommend a diary as a way to practise daily writing.","zh":"老師可能推薦日記作為每日練習寫作的方法。"},{"en":"Recommendations are stronger when they are based on experience or evidence.","zh":"當建議基於經驗或證據，它就更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone suggests a use for something.","zh":"當某人建議某物的用途時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the bark of the willow tree","meaning":"柳樹樹皮","examples":[{"en":"The bark of the willow tree was used as a remedy.","zh":"柳樹樹皮被用作療法。"},{"en":"The bark of the willow tree is the outer layer of the willow trunk and branches.","zh":"bark of the willow tree 指柳樹樹幹和樹枝的外層。"},{"en":"Traditional medicine may use tree bark when it contains useful natural chemicals.","zh":"當樹皮含有有用天然化學物質，傳統醫學可能會使用它。"},{"en":"Willow bark mattered because it contained substances connected with pain relief.","zh":"柳樹皮重要，因為它含有與止痛有關的物質。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing plant-based medicine.","zh":"討論植物藥物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a remedy for","meaning":"……的療法","examples":[{"en":"Willow bark was used as a remedy for pain.","zh":"柳樹皮被用作止痛療法。"},{"en":"A remedy for something is a treatment or solution used to reduce a problem.","zh":"remedy for something 指用來減輕問題的治療或解決方法。"},{"en":"Warm tea may be a simple remedy for a sore throat.","zh":"熱茶可能是喉嚨痛的簡單療法。"},{"en":"A remedy is useful only if it actually addresses the problem safely.","zh":"只有在安全地處理問題時，療法才有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing treatment or solutions.","zh":"討論治療或解決方法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the pains of childbirth","meaning":"分娩痛楚","examples":[{"en":"Willow bark was used for the pains of childbirth.","zh":"柳樹皮被用於分娩痛楚。"},{"en":"The pains of childbirth are the strong pains experienced during labour and delivery.","zh":"pains of childbirth 指生產和分娩期間經歷的強烈痛楚。"},{"en":"Nurses help mothers manage the pains of childbirth through support, breathing, and medical care.","zh":"護士透過支援、呼吸方法和醫療照顧幫助母親應對分娩痛楚。"},{"en":"Because childbirth pain can be severe, people have long searched for safe relief.","zh":"因為分娩痛楚可以很嚴重，人們長久以來尋找安全紓緩方法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing pregnancy, labour, and pain relief.","zh":"討論懷孕、分娩和止痛時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fever reducer","meaning":"退燒藥","examples":[{"en":"Willow bark was used as a fever reducer.","zh":"柳樹皮被用作退燒藥。"},{"en":"A fever reducer is a medicine or treatment that lowers a high body temperature.","zh":"fever reducer 指降低高體溫的藥物或治療方法。"},{"en":"Parents may use a fever reducer only after checking the child’s age and correct dose.","zh":"家長可能在確認孩子年齡和正確劑量後才使用退燒藥。"},{"en":"Reducing fever can make patients more comfortable while the body fights illness.","zh":"退燒可以令病人在身體對抗疾病時感覺較舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing treatment for fever.","zh":"討論發燒治療時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it wasn’t until...that","meaning":"直到……才……","examples":[{"en":"It wasn’t until later centuries that salicylates became a subject of serious study.","zh":"直到後來幾個世紀，水楊酸鹽才成為嚴肅研究的對象。"},{"en":"It wasn’t until A that B means B happened only after A, not before.","zh":"it wasn’t until A that B 指 B 直到 A 之後才發生，而不是之前。"},{"en":"It wasn’t until the teacher explained the example that the student understood the rule.","zh":"直到老師解釋例子，學生才理解規則。"},{"en":"This structure emphasises delay or late realisation.","zh":"這個結構強調延遲或較晚的認識。"},{"en":"It is useful when something important happened much later than expected.","zh":"當重要事情比預期更晚發生時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries","meaning":"十八及十九世紀","examples":[{"en":"Salicylates became a subject of scientific investigation in the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries.","zh":"水楊酸鹽在十八及十九世紀成為科學研究對象。"},{"en":"The eighteenth and nineteenth centuries refer to the 1700s and 1800s.","zh":"eighteenth and nineteenth centuries 指1700年代和1800年代。"},{"en":"Many scientific and industrial changes happened in the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries.","zh":"十八及十九世紀發生了許多科學和工業變化。"},{"en":"This period matters because older remedies began to be studied with more systematic methods.","zh":"這段時期重要，因為古老療法開始以更有系統的方法被研究。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when placing developments in historical time.","zh":"把發展放入歷史時間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"salicylates","meaning":"水楊酸鹽","examples":[{"en":"Salicylates are chemicals found in the willow tree.","zh":"水楊酸鹽是在柳樹中發現的化學物質。"},{"en":"Salicylates are a group of chemicals related to salicylic acid and aspirin-like effects.","zh":"salicylates 指一組與水楊酸及類似阿士匹靈效果有關的化學物質。"},{"en":"A chemistry student may study salicylates to understand how some pain-relieving drugs work.","zh":"化學學生可能研究水楊酸鹽，以理解某些止痛藥如何運作。"},{"en":"These chemicals became important because they helped connect traditional willow remedies with modern medicine.","zh":"這些化學物質很重要，因為它們把傳統柳樹療法與現代醫學連接起來。"},{"en":"This word is useful in discussions of aspirin chemistry.","zh":"討論阿士匹靈化學時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the chemical found in","meaning":"在……中發現的化學物質","examples":[{"en":"Salicylates are the chemical found in the willow tree.","zh":"水楊酸鹽是在柳樹中發現的化學物質。"},{"en":"The chemical found in something means the substance naturally present inside that material or organism.","zh":"chemical found in something 指自然存在於某材料或生物中的物質。"},{"en":"Caffeine is the chemical found in coffee that helps many people feel more awake.","zh":"咖啡因是在咖啡中發現、幫助許多人更清醒的化學物質。"},{"en":"Identifying a chemical in a plant helps scientists understand why the plant has an effect.","zh":"找出植物中的化學物質有助科學家理解該植物為何有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when linking a natural source with its active substance.","zh":"把天然來源與有效物質連接起來時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"become the subject of","meaning":"成為……的研究對象","examples":[{"en":"Salicylates became the subject of serious scientific investigation.","zh":"水楊酸鹽成為嚴肅科學研究的對象。"},{"en":"Become the subject of something means become the main thing being studied, discussed, or examined.","zh":"become the subject of something 指成為被研究、討論或檢視的主要事物。"},{"en":"A student’s unusual improvement may become the subject of a teacher’s research project.","zh":"學生異常進步可能成為老師研究項目的對象。"},{"en":"When something becomes the subject of investigation, people start asking detailed questions about it.","zh":"當某事成為調查對象，人們開始對它提出詳細問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when attention shifts toward a topic.","zh":"當注意力轉向某主題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"serious scientific investigation","meaning":"嚴肅的科學研究","examples":[{"en":"Salicylates became the subject of serious scientific investigation.","zh":"水楊酸鹽成為嚴肅科學研究的對象。"},{"en":"Serious scientific investigation means careful, systematic research using evidence and testing.","zh":"serious scientific investigation 指使用證據和測試進行仔細、有系統的研究。"},{"en":"A claim about a new diet needs serious scientific investigation before doctors recommend it.","zh":"關於新飲食法的說法，需要嚴肅科學研究後，醫生才會推薦。"},{"en":"Investigation can turn traditional knowledge into clearer medical understanding.","zh":"研究可以把傳統知識轉化為更清晰的醫學理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research is formal and evidence-based.","zh":"當研究是正式且以證據為本時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the race was on to","meaning":"競賽已經開始去……","examples":[{"en":"The race was on to identify the active ingredient.","zh":"找出有效成分的競賽已經開始。"},{"en":"The race was on to do something means people or groups had begun competing urgently to achieve it first.","zh":"the race was on to do something 指人們或群體已開始急切競爭，想率先完成某事。"},{"en":"After a new exam format was announced, the race was on to produce useful study guides.","zh":"新考試形式公布後，製作有用溫習指南的競賽已經開始。"},{"en":"Competition can speed up discovery because each group wants to be first.","zh":"競爭可以加快發現，因為每個團隊都想成為第一。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when urgency and competition begin.","zh":"當緊迫感和競爭開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"identify the active ingredient","meaning":"找出有效成分","examples":[{"en":"Scientists tried to identify the active ingredient in willow bark.","zh":"科學家嘗試找出柳樹皮中的有效成分。"},{"en":"To identify the active ingredient means to find the substance that actually produces the effect.","zh":"identify the active ingredient 指找出真正產生效果的物質。"},{"en":"Food scientists may identify the active ingredient in a herb that reduces inflammation.","zh":"食品科學家可能找出某種減少發炎草藥中的有效成分。"},{"en":"Finding the active ingredient allows researchers to control dose and test safety.","zh":"找出有效成分讓研究人員控制劑量並測試安全性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when separating the useful substance from the whole material.","zh":"從整體材料中分離有用物質時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"replicate it synthetically","meaning":"以人工方式合成複製","examples":[{"en":"Scientists wanted to replicate the active ingredient synthetically.","zh":"科學家希望以人工方式合成複製有效成分。"},{"en":"To replicate it synthetically means to create the same substance artificially through chemistry.","zh":"replicate it synthetically 指透過化學方式人工製造相同物質。"},{"en":"A lab may replicate a natural fragrance synthetically instead of collecting it from rare flowers.","zh":"實驗室可能以人工方式合成複製天然香氣，而不是從稀有花朵中採集。"},{"en":"Synthetic replication can make a substance cheaper, safer, and easier to produce consistently.","zh":"合成複製可以令物質更便宜、更安全，並更容易穩定生產。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when natural materials are copied in a laboratory.","zh":"當天然材料在實驗室被複製時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at the end of","meaning":"在……末期","examples":[{"en":"At the end of the nineteenth century, a German company created acetylsalicylic acid.","zh":"在十九世紀末期，一間德國公司創造了乙酰水楊酸。"},{"en":"At the end of a period means near its final part.","zh":"at the end of a period 指接近某段時間的最後部分。"},{"en":"At the end of the school year, students often review what they have learned.","zh":"在學年末，學生常回顧自己學到了甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase helps locate an event within a clear time frame.","zh":"這個短語幫助把事件放在清楚時間框架內。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing when something happened.","zh":"描述某事何時發生時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"succeed in creating","meaning":"成功創造","examples":[{"en":"Friedrich Bayer & Co. succeeded in creating a safe chemical compound.","zh":"Friedrich Bayer & Co. 成功創造一種安全的化合物。"},{"en":"To succeed in creating something means to manage to produce or develop it successfully.","zh":"succeed in creating something 指成功製造或發展某物。"},{"en":"A student may succeed in creating a clear essay after several drafts.","zh":"學生可能在幾次草稿後成功創作一篇清晰文章。"},{"en":"Success often follows repeated testing, correction, and persistence.","zh":"成功常來自反覆測試、修正和堅持。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when effort leads to a successful product.","zh":"當努力帶來成功產品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"relatively safe","meaning":"相對安全","examples":[{"en":"The chemical compound was relatively safe.","zh":"這種化合物相對安全。"},{"en":"Relatively safe means safe compared with other options, though not necessarily risk-free.","zh":"relatively safe 指與其他選項相比安全，但不一定完全沒有風險。"},{"en":"Cycling on a protected bike lane is relatively safe compared with cycling beside fast traffic.","zh":"與在快速車流旁踩單車相比，在受保護單車徑踩車相對安全。"},{"en":"In medicine, a treatment may be relatively safe if side effects are limited and manageable.","zh":"在醫學中，如果副作用有限且可處理，一種治療可能相對安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when safety is judged by comparison.","zh":"當安全性透過比較來判斷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"very effective","meaning":"非常有效","examples":[{"en":"The chemical compound was very effective.","zh":"這種化合物非常有效。"},{"en":"Very effective means able to produce the desired result well.","zh":"very effective 指能很好地產生想要的結果。"},{"en":"A clear revision timetable can be very effective if students actually follow it.","zh":"如果學生真正跟從，清晰溫習時間表可以非常有效。"},{"en":"A medicine is effective when it improves symptoms or reduces risk.","zh":"當藥物改善症狀或降低風險，它就是有效的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something works well.","zh":"當某事很有作用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"chemical compound","meaning":"化合物","examples":[{"en":"Acetylsalicylic acid is a chemical compound.","zh":"乙酰水楊酸是一種化合物。"},{"en":"A chemical compound is a substance made from two or more elements chemically joined together.","zh":"chemical compound 指由兩種或以上元素以化學方式結合而成的物質。"},{"en":"Water is a simple chemical compound made from hydrogen and oxygen.","zh":"水是一種由氫和氧組成的簡單化合物。"},{"en":"Understanding a compound’s structure helps scientists predict how it behaves.","zh":"理解化合物結構有助科學家預測它如何表現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in chemistry and medicine.","zh":"這個短語適用於化學和醫學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"acetylsalicylic acid","meaning":"乙酰水楊酸","examples":[{"en":"Acetylsalicylic acid was renamed aspirin.","zh":"乙酰水楊酸被重新命名為阿士匹靈。"},{"en":"Acetylsalicylic acid is the chemical name of aspirin.","zh":"acetylsalicylic acid 是阿士匹靈的化學名稱。"},{"en":"A medicine may have a scientific name such as acetylsalicylic acid and a shorter brand name for consumers.","zh":"藥物可能有乙酰水楊酸這類科學名稱，也有較短的消費者品牌名稱。"},{"en":"Chemical names help scientists identify the exact substance being discussed.","zh":"化學名稱幫助科學家識別正在討論的準確物質。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about aspirin scientifically.","zh":"以科學方式談論阿士匹靈時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be renamed","meaning":"被重新命名為","examples":[{"en":"Acetylsalicylic acid was renamed aspirin.","zh":"乙酰水楊酸被重新命名為阿士匹靈。"},{"en":"Be renamed means be given a new name.","zh":"be renamed 指被給予一個新名稱。"},{"en":"A school building may be renamed after a respected former principal.","zh":"學校建築可能以一位受尊敬的前校長重新命名。"},{"en":"Renaming can make something easier to remember, market, or identify.","zh":"重新命名可以令某物更容易被記住、推廣或識別。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a name changes.","zh":"當名稱改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a fertile period for experimentation","meaning":"適合實驗蓬勃發展的時期","examples":[{"en":"The late nineteenth century was a fertile period for experimentation.","zh":"十九世紀末是一個適合實驗蓬勃發展的時期。"},{"en":"A fertile period for experimentation is a time when conditions strongly support testing, discovery, and new ideas.","zh":"fertile period for experimentation 指條件非常有利於測試、發現和新想法的時期。"},{"en":"A new school laboratory can create a fertile period for experimentation in science lessons.","zh":"新學校實驗室可以為科學課創造一個適合實驗蓬勃發展的時期。"},{"en":"When tools, questions, and motivation come together, experimentation can increase quickly.","zh":"當工具、問題和動機結合，實驗可以迅速增加。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a period produces many trials and discoveries.","zh":"當某時期產生許多試驗和發現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"partly because of","meaning":"部分原因是","examples":[{"en":"This was possible partly because of scientists’ hunger for answers.","zh":"這之所以可能，部分原因是科學家渴望尋找答案。"},{"en":"Partly because of means one cause was involved, but it was not the only cause.","zh":"partly because of 指某原因有份造成結果，但不是唯一原因。"},{"en":"A student improved partly because of extra practice and partly because of better sleep.","zh":"學生進步部分原因是額外練習，部分原因是睡眠改善。"},{"en":"This phrase helps avoid overexplaining a result with only one reason.","zh":"這個短語幫助避免只用一個原因過度解釋結果。"},{"en":"It is useful when several causes work together.","zh":"當幾個原因共同作用時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the hunger among scientists to","meaning":"科學家渴望……","examples":[{"en":"There was a hunger among scientists to answer major questions.","zh":"科學家渴望解答重大問題。"},{"en":"The hunger among scientists to do something means scientists had a strong desire to achieve it.","zh":"hunger among scientists to do something 指科學家強烈渴望完成某事。"},{"en":"There may be a hunger among students to understand AI because it affects their future careers.","zh":"學生可能渴望理解人工智能，因為它影響未來職業。"},{"en":"Strong curiosity can push people to work through difficulty and uncertainty.","zh":"強烈好奇心可以推動人克服困難和不確定性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when intellectual desire drives action.","zh":"當知識渴望推動行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"great scientific questions","meaning":"重大科學問題","examples":[{"en":"Scientists wanted to answer some of the great scientific questions.","zh":"科學家希望解答一些重大科學問題。"},{"en":"Great scientific questions are major questions about nature, life, matter, health, or the universe.","zh":"great scientific questions 指關於自然、生命、物質、健康或宇宙的重大問題。"},{"en":"A great scientific question might ask how diseases spread or how the brain stores memory.","zh":"重大科學問題可能會問疾病如何傳播，或大腦如何儲存記憶。"},{"en":"Such questions inspire research because answering them can change human understanding.","zh":"這類問題激發研究，因為解答它們可以改變人類理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a question has broad scientific importance.","zh":"當問題有廣泛科學重要性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"within their means to answer","meaning":"在其能力範圍內可以解答","examples":[{"en":"Some scientific questions were within their means to answer.","zh":"有些科學問題在他們能力範圍內可以解答。"},{"en":"Within their means to answer means possible for them to answer with the tools, money, and knowledge they had.","zh":"within their means to answer 指以他們擁有的工具、金錢和知識可以解答。"},{"en":"A simple survey may be within students’ means to answer a question about lunch habits.","zh":"簡單問卷可能在學生能力範圍內解答關於午餐習慣的問題。"},{"en":"Research becomes more realistic when the question matches available resources.","zh":"當研究問題配合可用資源，研究就更現實。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when ability and resources limit what can be done.","zh":"當能力和資源限制可做事情時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"significant breakthroughs","meaning":"重大突破","examples":[{"en":"A scientist with simple equipment could make significant breakthroughs.","zh":"一位擁有簡單設備的科學家也可以作出重大突破。"},{"en":"Significant breakthroughs are important discoveries or advances that change understanding or practice.","zh":"significant breakthroughs 指改變理解或做法的重要發現或進展。"},{"en":"A teacher may make a breakthrough when a struggling student finally understands sentence structure.","zh":"當學習困難的學生終於理解句子結構，老師可能取得突破。"},{"en":"Breakthroughs often happen after many smaller failed attempts.","zh":"突破常發生在許多較小失敗嘗試之後。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when progress is large and meaningful.","zh":"當進展巨大且有意義時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"whereas","meaning":"然而","examples":[{"en":"One scientist could once make breakthroughs, whereas modern research often needs large teams.","zh":"從前一位科學家可以作出突破，然而現代研究常需要大型團隊。"},{"en":"Whereas means while, and it shows contrast between two facts.","zh":"whereas 指然而或而，用來顯示兩個事實之間的對比。"},{"en":"Some students learn best by reading, whereas others need discussion and examples.","zh":"有些學生透過閱讀學得最好，而另一些需要討論和例子。"},{"en":"This word helps compare two different situations in one sentence.","zh":"這個詞幫助在一句中比較兩種不同情況。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing a clear difference.","zh":"顯示清楚差異時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in order to","meaning":"為了","examples":[{"en":"Today, in order to map the human genome, researchers need large resources.","zh":"今天，為了繪製人類基因組圖譜，研究人員需要大量資源。"},{"en":"In order to means for the purpose of doing something.","zh":"in order to 指為了做某事。"},{"en":"Students practise speaking in order to become more confident in interviews.","zh":"學生練習口語，是為了在面試中更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly connects an action with its goal.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接行動和目標。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining purpose.","zh":"解釋目的時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"map the human genome","meaning":"繪製人類基因組圖譜","examples":[{"en":"Modern scientists need many resources to map the human genome.","zh":"現代科學家需要許多資源來繪製人類基因組圖譜。"},{"en":"To map the human genome means to identify and record the structure and sequence of human genetic information.","zh":"map the human genome 指識別並記錄人類遺傳資訊的結構和序列。"},{"en":"A biology class may discuss how mapping the human genome helped scientists understand inherited diseases.","zh":"生物課可能討論繪製人類基因組圖譜如何幫助科學家理解遺傳病。"},{"en":"Such work requires advanced technology because human DNA contains huge amounts of information.","zh":"這項工作需要先進科技，因為人類 DNA 含有龐大資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing modern genetics.","zh":"討論現代遺傳學時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"Mapping the human genome, for instance, requires many researchers.","zh":"例如，繪製人類基因組圖譜需要許多研究人員。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance 指例如。"},{"en":"Healthy habits, for instance, regular sleep and exercise, can improve concentration.","zh":"健康習慣，例如定時睡眠和運動，可以改善專注力。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a concrete example to support a general point.","zh":"這個短語引入具體例子來支持一般觀點。"},{"en":"It is useful when making an idea clearer.","zh":"令想法更清楚時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"an army of researchers","meaning":"一大批研究人員","examples":[{"en":"Modern scientific projects may require an army of researchers.","zh":"現代科學項目可能需要一大批研究人員。"},{"en":"An army of researchers means a very large group of researchers working together.","zh":"army of researchers 指一大群一起工作的研究人員。"},{"en":"A national health survey may need an army of researchers to collect and analyse data.","zh":"全國健康調查可能需要一大批研究人員收集和分析數據。"},{"en":"Some modern problems are too large for one person to solve alone.","zh":"有些現代問題太大，不是一個人能獨自解決。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when emphasising the scale of teamwork.","zh":"強調團隊合作規模時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a bank of computers","meaning":"大量電腦","examples":[{"en":"Mapping the human genome requires a bank of computers.","zh":"繪製人類基因組圖譜需要大量電腦。"},{"en":"A bank of computers means many computers connected or used together for a task.","zh":"bank of computers 指許多電腦連接起來或一起用於某任務。"},{"en":"A weather centre may use a bank of computers to process storm data.","zh":"天氣中心可能使用大量電腦處理風暴數據。"},{"en":"Large scientific projects need computing power because the data are too huge for manual work.","zh":"大型科學項目需要運算能力，因為數據太龐大，不能靠人手處理。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing heavy computing resources.","zh":"描述大量運算資源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"millions and millions of dollars","meaning":"數以百萬計的金錢","examples":[{"en":"Modern research can require millions and millions of dollars.","zh":"現代研究可能需要數以百萬計的金錢。"},{"en":"Millions and millions of dollars means a very large amount of money.","zh":"millions and millions of dollars 指非常大量的金錢。"},{"en":"Building a new hospital can cost millions and millions of dollars.","zh":"興建新醫院可能花費數以百萬計的金錢。"},{"en":"When research is expensive, governments, universities, and companies often need to cooperate.","zh":"當研究昂貴時，政府、大學和公司常需要合作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing huge financial cost.","zh":"強調巨大財政成本時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"an understanding of","meaning":"對……的理解","examples":[{"en":"An understanding of science is not enough to explain innovation.","zh":"對科學的理解不足以解釋創新。"},{"en":"An understanding of something means knowledge of how it works or why it matters.","zh":"understanding of something 指知道某事如何運作或為何重要。"},{"en":"An understanding of grammar helps students write clearer sentences.","zh":"對文法的理解幫助學生寫出更清晰句子。"},{"en":"Understanding one area may not be enough if money, society, and institutions also affect the result.","zh":"如果金錢、社會和制度也影響結果，只理解一個領域可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when knowledge is part of a larger explanation.","zh":"當知識只是較大解釋的一部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the nature of science","meaning":"科學的本質","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the nature of science and innovation.","zh":"文章討論科學和創新的本質。"},{"en":"The nature of science means what science is like, how it works, and how knowledge is built.","zh":"nature of science 指科學是甚麼、如何運作，以及知識如何被建立。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain the nature of science by showing that experiments can fail and still teach us something.","zh":"老師可能透過展示實驗失敗仍能教人東西，來解釋科學的本質。"},{"en":"Science involves evidence, testing, revision, creativity, and sometimes uncertainty.","zh":"科學涉及證據、測試、修正、創意，有時也涉及不確定性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing science as a process.","zh":"把科學作為一個過程來討論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"scientific inquiry","meaning":"科學探究","examples":[{"en":"Scientific inquiry alone does not fully explain innovation.","zh":"單靠科學探究不能完全解釋創新。"},{"en":"Scientific inquiry is the process of asking questions, testing ideas, collecting evidence, and drawing conclusions.","zh":"scientific inquiry 指提出問題、測試想法、收集證據並得出結論的過程。"},{"en":"Students practise scientific inquiry when they test which material keeps water warm longest.","zh":"學生測試哪種材料最能保溫時，就是在進行科學探究。"},{"en":"Inquiry produces knowledge, but society and business may decide how that knowledge is used.","zh":"探究產生知識，但社會和商業可能決定知識如何被使用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how science investigates questions.","zh":"討論科學如何研究問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not enough on its own","meaning":"單靠本身並不足夠","examples":[{"en":"Scientific knowledge is not enough on its own to explain innovation.","zh":"科學知識單靠本身並不足以解釋創新。"},{"en":"Not enough on its own means insufficient by itself without other support or factors.","zh":"not enough on its own 指單獨存在時不足夠，需要其他支持或因素。"},{"en":"Talent is not enough on its own if a student never practises.","zh":"如果學生從不練習，天分單靠本身並不足夠。"},{"en":"Many goals require a combination of knowledge, resources, motivation, and timing.","zh":"許多目標需要知識、資源、動機和時機結合。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one factor cannot explain everything.","zh":"當單一因素不能解釋全部時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"explain how society innovates","meaning":"解釋社會如何創新","examples":[{"en":"The passage tries to explain how society innovates.","zh":"文章試圖解釋社會如何創新。"},{"en":"To explain how society innovates means to show how new ideas become useful products, systems, or practices.","zh":"explain how society innovates 指展示新想法如何變成有用產品、系統或做法。"},{"en":"A business class may explain how society innovates by studying smartphones, vaccines, or online banking.","zh":"商科課可能透過研究智能手機、疫苗或網上銀行，解釋社會如何創新。"},{"en":"Innovation happens when ideas meet resources, demand, institutions, and practical needs.","zh":"當想法遇上資源、需求、制度和實際需要，創新就會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing creativity at a social level.","zh":"討論社會層面的創造力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"scientific advance","meaning":"科學進步","examples":[{"en":"Scientific advance was closely linked to the industrial revolution.","zh":"科學進步與工業革命密切相關。"},{"en":"Scientific advance means progress in scientific knowledge, methods, or technology.","zh":"scientific advance 指科學知識、方法或技術上的進展。"},{"en":"Scientific advance in medicine can lead to better tests and safer treatments.","zh":"醫學上的科學進步可以帶來更好的檢測和更安全的治療。"},{"en":"Advances often create new possibilities for industry, healthcare, and daily life.","zh":"進步常為工業、醫療和日常生活創造新可能性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when knowledge moves forward.","zh":"當知識向前發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be closely linked to","meaning":"與……密切相關","examples":[{"en":"Scientific advance was closely linked to industrial development.","zh":"科學進步與工業發展密切相關。"},{"en":"Be closely linked to means have a strong connection with something.","zh":"be closely linked to 指與某事有強烈連繫。"},{"en":"Student confidence is closely linked to preparation and feedback.","zh":"學生信心與準備和回饋密切相關。"},{"en":"When two things are closely linked, changes in one may affect the other.","zh":"當兩件事密切相關，其中一方改變可能影響另一方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining strong relationships.","zh":"解釋強關係時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the industrial revolution","meaning":"工業革命","examples":[{"en":"The industrial revolution helped create conditions for innovation.","zh":"工業革命幫助創造創新的條件。"},{"en":"The industrial revolution was a period of major change when machine production, factories, and industry expanded.","zh":"industrial revolution 指機器生產、工廠和工業擴張的重大變革時期。"},{"en":"In history lessons, students learn how the industrial revolution changed work, cities, and transport.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生學習工業革命如何改變工作、城市和交通。"},{"en":"Industrial growth gave people new tools, markets, and reasons to turn inventions into products.","zh":"工業增長給人新工具、市場和理由，把發明變成產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing modern economic and technological change.","zh":"討論現代經濟和科技變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the means, motive and determination to","meaning":"做……的手段、動機和決心","examples":[{"en":"People had the means, motive and determination to turn ideas into reality.","zh":"人們有把想法變成現實的手段、動機和決心。"},{"en":"The means, motive and determination to do something are the resources, reason, and willpower needed to do it.","zh":"means, motive and determination to do something 指做某事所需的資源、原因和意志力。"},{"en":"A student with time, a clear goal, and discipline has the means, motive and determination to improve.","zh":"有時間、清晰目標和紀律的學生，有進步的手段、動機和決心。"},{"en":"Ideas become real only when people can act, want to act, and keep going.","zh":"只有當人們能行動、想行動並堅持下去，想法才會成真。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why action becomes possible.","zh":"解釋行動為何變得可能時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"turn an idea into reality","meaning":"把想法變成現實","examples":[{"en":"Nineteenth-century innovators could turn an idea into reality.","zh":"十九世紀的創新者能把想法變成現實。"},{"en":"To turn an idea into reality means to make a plan, invention, or dream actually happen.","zh":"turn an idea into reality 指令計劃、發明或夢想真正發生。"},{"en":"Students turn an idea into reality when they plan a charity sale and actually run it.","zh":"學生計劃慈善義賣並實際舉行時，就是把想法變成現實。"},{"en":"Turning ideas into reality usually requires planning, resources, teamwork, and persistence.","zh":"把想法變成現實通常需要規劃、資源、團隊合作和堅持。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when imagination becomes practical action.","zh":"當想像變成實際行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in the case of","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"In the case of aspirin, progress happened gradually.","zh":"就阿士匹靈而言，進展是逐步發生的。"},{"en":"In the case of means when we are talking about this particular example.","zh":"in the case of 指當我們談論這個特定例子時。"},{"en":"In the case of online learning, good internet access is essential.","zh":"就網上學習而言，良好網絡連接是必要的。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows a general discussion to one specific example.","zh":"這個短語把一般討論收窄到一個具體例子。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing different cases.","zh":"比較不同個案時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"happen piecemeal","meaning":"零碎地發生；逐步發生","examples":[{"en":"The development of aspirin happened piecemeal.","zh":"阿士匹靈的發展是零碎地發生的。"},{"en":"Happen piecemeal means happen gradually in separate small parts rather than all at once.","zh":"happen piecemeal 指以分散的小部分逐步發生，而不是一次完成。"},{"en":"A school renovation may happen piecemeal, with one classroom repaired each month.","zh":"學校翻新可能逐步發生，每月修理一間課室。"},{"en":"Piecemeal development can look messy because progress comes from many small steps.","zh":"零碎發展可能看似混亂，因為進展來自許多小步驟。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when change is gradual and fragmented.","zh":"當變化逐步而分散時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a series of minor advances","meaning":"一連串小進展","examples":[{"en":"A series of minor advances led to the final breakthrough.","zh":"一連串小進展促成最終突破。"},{"en":"A series of minor advances means several small improvements or discoveries happening one after another.","zh":"series of minor advances 指幾個小改進或發現一個接一個發生。"},{"en":"A student’s writing improves through a series of minor advances in grammar, planning, and vocabulary.","zh":"學生寫作透過文法、規劃和詞彙上的一連串小進展而改善。"},{"en":"Small advances can accumulate until they create a major result.","zh":"小進展可以累積，直到產生重大結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when big progress comes from many little steps.","zh":"當大進步來自許多小步驟時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"often unrelated advances","meaning":"往往互不相關的進展","examples":[{"en":"Several often unrelated advances contributed to aspirin’s development.","zh":"幾個往往互不相關的進展促成阿士匹靈的發展。"},{"en":"Often unrelated advances are improvements that do not seem directly connected at first.","zh":"often unrelated advances 指起初看似沒有直接關係的改進。"},{"en":"Better transport, new computers, and improved teaching methods may be unrelated advances that together help a school.","zh":"更好交通、新電腦和改善教學方法，可能是互不相關但共同幫助學校的進展。"},{"en":"Innovation can happen when separate developments unexpectedly support one another.","zh":"當分散發展意外互相支持，創新就可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when progress comes from different directions.","zh":"當進步來自不同方向時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be fertilised by","meaning":"受到……滋養；受……促進","examples":[{"en":"The advances were fertilised by broader developments in society.","zh":"這些進展受到社會更廣泛發展的滋養。"},{"en":"Be fertilised by means be encouraged, nourished, or made stronger by something else.","zh":"be fertilised by 指受到其他事物鼓勵、滋養或加強。"},{"en":"A student’s interest in science may be fertilised by good teachers and exciting experiments.","zh":"學生對科學的興趣可能受到好老師和有趣實驗滋養。"},{"en":"New ideas grow faster when the surrounding environment supports them.","zh":"當周圍環境支持新想法，它們會更快成長。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when outside conditions help development.","zh":"當外部條件幫助發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"broader economic, medical and scientific developments","meaning":"更廣泛的經濟、醫學和科學發展","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin’s development was helped by broader economic, medical and scientific developments.","zh":"阿士匹靈的發展受到更廣泛的經濟、醫學和科學發展幫助。"},{"en":"Broader economic, medical and scientific developments are wider changes in business, healthcare, and scientific knowledge.","zh":"broader economic, medical and scientific developments 指商業、醫療和科學知識方面更大範圍的變化。"},{"en":"A new hospital project may depend on broader economic, medical and scientific developments.","zh":"新醫院項目可能依賴更廣泛的經濟、醫學和科學發展。"},{"en":"Inventions rarely grow in isolation; they are shaped by the wider world around them.","zh":"發明很少孤立成長；它們受周圍更廣闊世界塑造。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when several social forces support innovation.","zh":"當幾種社會力量支持創新時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"導致；促成","examples":[{"en":"Many minor advances led to one final breakthrough.","zh":"許多小進展促成一個最終突破。"},{"en":"Lead to means cause or result in something.","zh":"lead to 指導致或產生某結果。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can lead to weak concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致課堂專注力弱。"},{"en":"Small decisions can lead to large consequences over time.","zh":"小決定隨時間可以導致重大後果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing cause and effect.","zh":"顯示因果關係時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"one big final breakthrough","meaning":"一個重大的最終突破","examples":[{"en":"A series of advances led to one big final breakthrough.","zh":"一連串進展促成一個重大的最終突破。"},{"en":"One big final breakthrough is the major successful discovery or result that comes after many earlier steps.","zh":"one big final breakthrough 指經過許多早期步驟後出現的重大成功發現或結果。"},{"en":"A student may have one big final breakthrough after weeks of struggling with essay structure.","zh":"學生在掙扎幾星期後，可能在文章結構上取得一個重大的最終突破。"},{"en":"The breakthrough looks sudden, but it often depends on earlier small improvements.","zh":"突破看似突然，但常依賴早前的小改進。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the final success follows gradual progress.","zh":"當最終成功源自逐步進展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the link between","meaning":"……之間的關係","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the link between big money and pharmaceutical innovation.","zh":"文章討論大量資金與製藥創新之間的關係。"},{"en":"The link between two things is the relationship or connection between them.","zh":"link between two things 指兩件事之間的關係或連繫。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain the link between reading more and writing better.","zh":"老師可能解釋多閱讀與寫作更好之間的關係。"},{"en":"Understanding a link helps people see why two issues influence each other.","zh":"理解關係有助人看見兩個議題為何互相影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing relationships between ideas.","zh":"討論想法之間的關係時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"big money","meaning":"大量資金","examples":[{"en":"Big money can influence pharmaceutical innovation.","zh":"大量資金可以影響製藥創新。"},{"en":"Big money means large amounts of money, especially money used by companies or investors.","zh":"big money 指大量金錢，尤其是公司或投資者使用的資金。"},{"en":"Big money can shape sport when sponsors pay for stadiums, players, and media rights.","zh":"當贊助商支付運動場、球員和媒體權利費用，大量資金可以塑造體育。"},{"en":"Money can support research, but it can also push attention toward profitable products.","zh":"金錢可以支持研究，但也可能把注意力推向有利可圖的產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when finance has strong influence.","zh":"當財務有強大影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pharmaceutical innovation","meaning":"製藥創新","examples":[{"en":"The link between money and pharmaceutical innovation is significant.","zh":"金錢與製藥創新之間的關係很重要。"},{"en":"Pharmaceutical innovation means the development of new medicines, treatments, or drug uses.","zh":"pharmaceutical innovation 指新藥、治療方法或藥物用途的開發。"},{"en":"A company may invest in pharmaceutical innovation to create a safer cancer drug.","zh":"公司可能投資製藥創新，以創造更安全的癌症藥物。"},{"en":"Innovation in medicine can save lives, but it often needs research funding and regulation.","zh":"醫學創新可以拯救生命，但常需要研究資金和規管。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing new drug development.","zh":"討論新藥開發時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a significant one","meaning":"重要的一項","examples":[{"en":"The link between money and drug development is a significant one.","zh":"金錢與藥物開發之間的關係是重要的一項。"},{"en":"A significant one means an important example, relationship, or factor.","zh":"significant one 指一個重要例子、關係或因素。"},{"en":"The link between sleep and exam performance is a significant one for students.","zh":"睡眠與考試表現之間的關係對學生來說是重要的一項。"},{"en":"Calling something significant shows it should not be ignored.","zh":"說某事 significant 顯示它不應被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing importance.","zh":"強調重要性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"continued shelf life","meaning":"持續存在於市場的時間","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin’s continued shelf life was helped by heavy promotion.","zh":"阿士匹靈持續存在於市場的時間受到大量宣傳幫助。"},{"en":"Continued shelf life means a product keeps staying available, known, and saleable over time.","zh":"continued shelf life 指產品長時間保持可供應、為人所知並可銷售。"},{"en":"A classic snack may have continued shelf life because shops keep advertising it to new customers.","zh":"經典零食可能因商店持續向新顧客宣傳而繼續存在於市場。"},{"en":"Promotion can keep an old product alive in the market even when newer products appear.","zh":"即使新產品出現，宣傳也可以讓舊產品在市場中保持生命力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how long a product remains commercially active.","zh":"討論產品商業生命有多長時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be ensured because","meaning":"因……而得到保證","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin’s survival was ensured because it was heavily promoted.","zh":"阿士匹靈的存續因它被大力宣傳而得到保證。"},{"en":"Be ensured because means be made certain or protected as a result of a cause.","zh":"be ensured because 指因某原因而變得確定或受到保障。"},{"en":"A school trip’s safety is ensured because teachers check transport, food, and emergency contacts.","zh":"學校旅行的安全因老師檢查交通、食物和緊急聯絡而得到保證。"},{"en":"Strong support can make an outcome more likely to continue.","zh":"強大支持可以令某結果更可能持續。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why something was secured.","zh":"解釋某事為何得到保障時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"huge amounts of money","meaning":"大量金錢","examples":[{"en":"Huge amounts of money were put into promoting aspirin.","zh":"大量金錢被投入於宣傳阿士匹靈。"},{"en":"Huge amounts of money means very large sums of money.","zh":"huge amounts of money 指非常龐大的金錢數額。"},{"en":"Huge amounts of money may be spent on advertising during a major sports event.","zh":"大型體育賽事期間，可能有大量金錢花在廣告上。"},{"en":"Large spending can make a product familiar to millions of people.","zh":"巨額開支可以令產品為數以百萬計的人熟悉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when financial scale is very large.","zh":"當財務規模很大時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be put into","meaning":"被投入於……","examples":[{"en":"Money was put into promoting aspirin as an everyday painkiller.","zh":"金錢被投入於把阿士匹靈宣傳為日常止痛藥。"},{"en":"Be put into means be invested, used, or directed toward a purpose.","zh":"be put into 指被投資、使用或導向某目的。"},{"en":"More time can be put into reading practice before an English exam.","zh":"英文考試前，可以把更多時間投入閱讀練習。"},{"en":"Resources put into a goal can increase its chance of success.","zh":"投入目標的資源可以增加成功機會。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when effort, time, or money is directed somewhere.","zh":"當努力、時間或金錢被投放到某處時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"promote something as","meaning":"將……宣傳為","examples":[{"en":"Companies promoted aspirin as an ordinary everyday analgesic.","zh":"公司將阿士匹靈宣傳為日常普通止痛藥。"},{"en":"To promote something as something means to advertise or present it in a particular way.","zh":"promote something as something 指以某種方式宣傳或呈現某物。"},{"en":"A school may promote reading as a way to reduce stress, not only improve marks.","zh":"學校可能將閱讀宣傳為減壓方法，而不只是提高分數的方法。"},{"en":"Promotion shapes how people understand and use a product.","zh":"宣傳會塑造人們如何理解和使用產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when marketing creates an image.","zh":"當行銷創造形象時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ordinary everyday analgesic","meaning":"日常普通止痛藥","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin was promoted as an ordinary everyday analgesic.","zh":"阿士匹靈被宣傳為日常普通止痛藥。"},{"en":"An ordinary everyday analgesic is a common painkiller used for normal minor pain.","zh":"ordinary everyday analgesic 指用於普通輕微疼痛的常見止痛藥。"},{"en":"A person may keep an ordinary everyday analgesic at home for headaches or muscle pain.","zh":"一個人可能在家中備有日常普通止痛藥，用於頭痛或肌肉痛。"},{"en":"Presenting aspirin this way made it seem familiar, safe, and useful in daily life.","zh":"以這種方式呈現阿士匹靈，令它看似熟悉、安全並適合日常使用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a medicine is marketed for common use.","zh":"當藥物被推廣作常見用途時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"enter the market","meaning":"進入市場","examples":[{"en":"Other analgesics began to enter the market in the 1970s.","zh":"其他止痛藥在1970年代開始進入市場。"},{"en":"To enter the market means to become available for sale to customers.","zh":"enter the market 指開始可供顧客購買。"},{"en":"A new phone brand may enter the market with a cheaper model.","zh":"新手機品牌可能以較便宜型號進入市場。"},{"en":"When new products enter the market, older products may face stronger competition.","zh":"當新產品進入市場，舊產品可能面對更強競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing business and product competition.","zh":"討論商業和產品競爭時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"集中於；專注於","examples":[{"en":"Pharmaceutical companies focused on publicising new drugs.","zh":"製藥公司專注於宣傳新藥。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give main attention to it.","zh":"focus on something 指把主要注意力放在某事上。"},{"en":"A student should focus on weak grammar points before the exam.","zh":"學生考試前應專注於薄弱文法點。"},{"en":"Focusing on one goal can improve results, but it may also make people ignore other possibilities.","zh":"專注於一個目標可以改善結果，但也可能令人忽視其他可能性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when attention is directed toward one area.","zh":"當注意力被導向某一範疇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"publicise new drugs","meaning":"宣傳新藥","examples":[{"en":"Companies focused on publicising new drugs such as ibuprofen.","zh":"公司專注於宣傳布洛芬等新藥。"},{"en":"To publicise new drugs means to advertise or spread information about new medicines.","zh":"publicise new drugs 指為新藥做廣告或傳播資訊。"},{"en":"A pharmaceutical company may publicise a new allergy drug through doctors, posters, and websites.","zh":"製藥公司可能透過醫生、海報和網站宣傳新過敏藥。"},{"en":"Publicity can increase demand, especially when patients recognise a drug’s name.","zh":"宣傳可以增加需求，尤其當病人認得藥名時。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing drug marketing.","zh":"討論藥物行銷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"與此同時","examples":[{"en":"At the same time, new discoveries were made about aspirin.","zh":"與此同時，關於阿士匹靈的新發現出現了。"},{"en":"At the same time means while another thing is happening.","zh":"at the same time 指在另一件事發生的同時。"},{"en":"A student may work part-time and, at the same time, prepare for exams.","zh":"學生可能一邊兼職，與此同時準備考試。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two developments happened together.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩項發展同時發生。"},{"en":"It is useful when events overlap.","zh":"當事件重疊時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"discoveries were made regarding","meaning":"有關……的發現被作出","examples":[{"en":"Discoveries were made regarding aspirin’s role in preventing illness.","zh":"有關阿士匹靈在預防疾病方面作用的發現被作出。"},{"en":"Discoveries were made regarding something means new findings were produced about that topic.","zh":"discoveries were made regarding something 指關於某主題出現了新發現。"},{"en":"Discoveries were made regarding sleep and memory after researchers studied students overnight.","zh":"研究人員整晚研究學生後，有關睡眠和記憶的發現被作出。"},{"en":"New discoveries can change how an old product or idea is understood.","zh":"新發現可以改變人們如何理解舊產品或想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research reveals new information.","zh":"當研究揭示新資訊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"beneficial role","meaning":"有益作用","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin has a beneficial role in preventing some diseases.","zh":"阿士匹靈在預防某些疾病方面有有益作用。"},{"en":"A beneficial role is a helpful function or positive part something plays.","zh":"beneficial role 指某事物發揮的有幫助功能或正面作用。"},{"en":"Exercise has a beneficial role in improving mood and heart health.","zh":"運動在改善情緒和心臟健康方面有有益作用。"},{"en":"If something plays a beneficial role, it helps produce a better outcome.","zh":"如果某物發揮有益作用，它就有助產生較好結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining positive effects.","zh":"解釋正面效果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"preventing heart attacks","meaning":"預防心臟病發","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin may help in preventing heart attacks.","zh":"阿士匹靈可能有助預防心臟病發。"},{"en":"Preventing heart attacks means reducing the chance that blood flow to the heart becomes blocked.","zh":"preventing heart attacks 指降低通往心臟的血流受阻的機會。"},{"en":"Doctors may discuss preventing heart attacks through diet, exercise, medicine, and not smoking.","zh":"醫生可能討論透過飲食、運動、藥物和不吸煙來預防心臟病發。"},{"en":"Prevention is important because heart attacks can be sudden and life-threatening.","zh":"預防很重要，因為心臟病發可以突然且危及生命。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing cardiovascular health.","zh":"討論心血管健康時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"strokes and other afflictions","meaning":"中風及其他疾病","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin may help prevent strokes and other afflictions.","zh":"阿士匹靈可能有助預防中風及其他疾病。"},{"en":"Strokes and other afflictions means strokes and other serious illnesses or health problems.","zh":"strokes and other afflictions 指中風和其他嚴重疾病或健康問題。"},{"en":"A public health campaign may teach people how to reduce strokes and other afflictions through lifestyle changes.","zh":"公共健康宣傳可能教人如何透過生活方式改變減少中風及其他疾病。"},{"en":"Preventing serious conditions can reduce suffering, disability, and medical costs.","zh":"預防嚴重狀況可以減少痛苦、殘疾和醫療成本。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing major health risks.","zh":"討論重大健康風險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"had it not been for","meaning":"要不是因為……","examples":[{"en":"Had it not been for these findings, aspirin might have disappeared.","zh":"要不是因為這些發現，阿士匹靈可能已經消失。"},{"en":"Had it not been for means if something had not happened or existed.","zh":"had it not been for 指如果某事沒有發生或不存在。"},{"en":"Had it not been for a helpful teacher, the student might have given up English.","zh":"要不是因為一位有幫助的老師，學生可能已放棄英文。"},{"en":"This structure shows that one factor prevented a different outcome.","zh":"這個結構顯示某因素阻止了另一種結果。"},{"en":"It is useful when imagining what would have happened without an important cause.","zh":"想像沒有重要原因會發生甚麼時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pharmaceutical marvel","meaning":"製藥奇蹟","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin is described as a pharmaceutical marvel.","zh":"阿士匹靈被描述為製藥奇蹟。"},{"en":"A pharmaceutical marvel is a medicine considered unusually impressive or successful.","zh":"pharmaceutical marvel 指被視為異常令人驚嘆或成功的藥物。"},{"en":"A cheap drug that saves many lives may be called a pharmaceutical marvel.","zh":"如果一種便宜藥物拯救許多生命，它可能被稱為製藥奇蹟。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests wonder at both the science and the practical effect of a drug.","zh":"這個短語暗示人們對藥物的科學和實際效果都感到驚嘆。"},{"en":"It is useful when a medicine has exceptional importance.","zh":"當藥物有非凡重要性時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"might well have disappeared","meaning":"很可能已經消失","examples":[{"en":"Without new findings, aspirin might well have disappeared.","zh":"如果沒有新發現，阿士匹靈很可能已經消失。"},{"en":"Might well have disappeared means it was quite possible that something would have vanished.","zh":"might well have disappeared 指某物相當可能已經消失。"},{"en":"Without community support, the small library might well have disappeared.","zh":"如果沒有社區支持，小圖書館很可能已經消失。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a serious possibility, not a weak or unlikely one.","zh":"這個短語暗示一個相當真實的可能性，而不是很微弱的可能性。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing how close something came to being lost.","zh":"顯示某事物差點消失時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the relationship between","meaning":"……之間的關係","examples":[{"en":"The relationship between big money and drugs is an odd one.","zh":"大量資金與藥物之間的關係是一種奇怪的關係。"},{"en":"The relationship between two things means the way they are connected or affect each other.","zh":"relationship between two things 指兩者如何連接或互相影響。"},{"en":"The relationship between sleep and learning is important for students.","zh":"睡眠與學習之間的關係對學生很重要。"},{"en":"Understanding a relationship helps explain why one factor changes another.","zh":"理解關係有助解釋為何一個因素會改變另一個因素。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when analysing connections.","zh":"分析連繫時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an odd one","meaning":"奇怪的一種關係","examples":[{"en":"The relationship between money and drugs is an odd one.","zh":"金錢與藥物之間的關係是一種奇怪的關係。"},{"en":"An odd one means a strange, unusual, or surprising case or relationship.","zh":"odd one 指奇怪、不尋常或令人意外的個案或關係。"},{"en":"The friendship between two students who always argue may seem an odd one.","zh":"兩名總是爭論的學生之間的友誼，可能看似奇怪。"},{"en":"Something can be odd because it contains both helpful and harmful effects.","zh":"某事可能奇怪，是因為它同時包含有益和有害效果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a situation does not fit simple expectations.","zh":"當情況不符合簡單預期時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"commercial markets","meaning":"商業市場","examples":[{"en":"Commercial markets are necessary for developing new products.","zh":"商業市場對開發新產品是必要的。"},{"en":"Commercial markets are systems where products are bought and sold for profit.","zh":"commercial markets 指產品以盈利為目的被買賣的系統。"},{"en":"A new app enters commercial markets when customers can pay to download or use it.","zh":"當顧客可以付費下載或使用新應用程式，它就進入商業市場。"},{"en":"Markets can reward useful products but may ignore products with little profit.","zh":"市場可以獎勵有用產品，但可能忽視利潤低的產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing business forces.","zh":"討論商業力量時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be necessary for","meaning":"對……是必要的","examples":[{"en":"Commercial markets are necessary for drug development.","zh":"商業市場對藥物開發是必要的。"},{"en":"Be necessary for means be needed in order for something to happen or succeed.","zh":"be necessary for 指某事發生或成功所需要的條件。"},{"en":"Regular practice is necessary for improving pronunciation.","zh":"定期練習對改善發音是必要的。"},{"en":"If something is necessary, removing it may stop the process from working.","zh":"如果某事是必要的，移除它可能令過程無法運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining essential conditions.","zh":"解釋必要條件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"developing new products","meaning":"開發新產品","examples":[{"en":"Commercial markets support the development of new products.","zh":"商業市場支持新產品開發。"},{"en":"Developing new products means designing, testing, producing, and improving things for customers to use.","zh":"developing new products 指為顧客設計、測試、生產和改良物品。"},{"en":"A company developing new products may test samples with customers before launching them.","zh":"開發新產品的公司可能在推出前讓顧客測試樣本。"},{"en":"Product development needs ideas, money, research, and a market.","zh":"產品開發需要想法、金錢、研究和市場。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing innovation in business.","zh":"討論商業創新時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ensure that","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Markets help ensure that products remain available.","zh":"市場幫助確保產品仍然可取得。"},{"en":"Ensure that means make certain that something happens.","zh":"ensure that 指確保某事發生。"},{"en":"Teachers check attendance to ensure that every student is safe at school.","zh":"老師點名以確保每名學生在校安全。"},{"en":"Systems are needed to ensure that important products do not disappear.","zh":"需要制度確保重要產品不會消失。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing guarantees or protection.","zh":"討論保證或保護時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"remain around long enough","meaning":"留存足夠長時間","examples":[{"en":"Products must remain around long enough for research to be carried out.","zh":"產品必須留存足夠長時間，研究才能進行。"},{"en":"Remain around long enough means continue existing for enough time for something else to happen.","zh":"remain around long enough 指持續存在足夠時間，讓另一件事發生。"},{"en":"A community garden must remain around long enough for children to learn how plants grow.","zh":"社區花園必須留存足夠長時間，孩子才能學會植物如何生長。"},{"en":"If a product disappears too quickly, researchers may never discover its further value.","zh":"如果產品太快消失，研究人員可能永遠無法發現其進一步價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when time allows later investigation.","zh":"當時間容許後續研究時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"carry out research on","meaning":"對……進行研究","examples":[{"en":"Scientists carry out research on drugs that remain available.","zh":"科學家對仍可取得的藥物進行研究。"},{"en":"To carry out research on something means to study it carefully and systematically.","zh":"carry out research on something 指仔細而有系統地研究某事。"},{"en":"A school may carry out research on whether later start times improve student focus.","zh":"學校可能研究較遲上課是否改善學生專注力。"},{"en":"Research can reveal benefits, risks, or uses that were not obvious at first.","zh":"研究可以揭示起初不明顯的好處、風險或用途。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing formal investigation.","zh":"討論正式調查時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"just as likely to","meaning":"同樣有可能……","examples":[{"en":"Commercial markets are just as likely to kill off some products.","zh":"商業市場同樣有可能淘汰某些產品。"},{"en":"Just as likely to means equally likely to do something, often something opposite or surprising.","zh":"just as likely to 指同樣可能做某事，常是相反或令人意外的事。"},{"en":"Competition is just as likely to stress students as to motivate them if it is too harsh.","zh":"如果競爭太激烈，它同樣有可能令學生受壓，而不是激勵他們。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that one system can produce both good and bad outcomes.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，一個系統可以產生正反結果。"},{"en":"It is useful when balancing two possibilities.","zh":"平衡兩種可能性時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"kill off certain products","meaning":"淘汰某些產品","examples":[{"en":"Markets can kill off certain products when better options appear.","zh":"當更好的選擇出現，市場可以淘汰某些產品。"},{"en":"To kill off certain products means to make them disappear from the market.","zh":"kill off certain products 指令某些產品從市場消失。"},{"en":"Streaming services killed off some video-rental shops when customers changed habits.","zh":"當顧客習慣改變，串流服務淘汰了一些影碟出租店。"},{"en":"A product may disappear if it becomes less profitable or less attractive than newer alternatives.","zh":"如果產品利潤降低或不及新選擇吸引，它可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when competition removes old products.","zh":"當競爭令舊產品被移除時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"come along","meaning":"出現","examples":[{"en":"A more attractive product may come along.","zh":"更吸引的產品可能會出現。"},{"en":"Come along means appear, arrive, or become available.","zh":"come along 指出現、到來或變得可取得。"},{"en":"A better job opportunity may come along after months of searching.","zh":"經過幾個月求職後，更好的工作機會可能出現。"},{"en":"When a stronger competitor comes along, older products may lose attention.","zh":"當更強競爭者出現，舊產品可能失去關注。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something new appears unexpectedly or naturally.","zh":"當新事物意外或自然出現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"potential wonder drug","meaning":"潛在神奇藥物","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin was a potential wonder drug.","zh":"阿士匹靈是一種潛在神奇藥物。"},{"en":"A potential wonder drug is a medicine that may become unusually valuable or effective if its benefits are fully discovered.","zh":"potential wonder drug 指如果其好處被充分發現，可能變得異常有價值或有效的藥物。"},{"en":"A cheap old drug may be a potential wonder drug if researchers find it treats another disease.","zh":"如果研究人員發現一種便宜舊藥能治療另一種疾病，它可能是潛在神奇藥物。"},{"en":"Potential matters because value may be hidden until later studies reveal it.","zh":"潛力重要，因為價值可能被隱藏，直到後來研究揭示它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a medicine may have great future importance.","zh":"當藥物未來可能非常重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be around for","meaning":"存在了……","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin was around for over 70 years.","zh":"阿士匹靈已存在超過70年。"},{"en":"Be around for a period means exist or remain available for that length of time.","zh":"be around for a period 指存在或持續可取得某段時間。"},{"en":"A family restaurant may be around for fifty years if customers keep returning.","zh":"如果顧客持續光顧，家庭餐廳可能存在五十年。"},{"en":"The longer something remains available, the more chances people have to study or reuse it.","zh":"某物存在越久，人們研究或重新使用它的機會越多。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing duration of existence.","zh":"討論存在時間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"investigate the way in which","meaning":"研究……的方式","examples":[{"en":"Few people investigated the way in which aspirin achieved its effects.","zh":"很少人研究阿士匹靈產生效果的方式。"},{"en":"To investigate the way in which something happens means to study the process or mechanism behind it.","zh":"investigate the way in which something happens 指研究某事背後的過程或機制。"},{"en":"A teacher may investigate the way in which students remember vocabulary best.","zh":"老師可能研究學生最好記住詞彙的方式。"},{"en":"Knowing that something works is different from knowing how it works.","zh":"知道某物有效不同於知道它如何有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when focusing on mechanism, not just result.","zh":"當焦點在機制而不只是結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"achieve its effects","meaning":"產生其效果","examples":[{"en":"Scientists later studied how aspirin achieved its effects.","zh":"科學家後來研究阿士匹靈如何產生其效果。"},{"en":"To achieve its effects means to produce the results or changes it is known for.","zh":"achieve its effects 指產生它為人所知的結果或變化。"},{"en":"A teaching method achieves its effects when students understand faster and remember longer.","zh":"當學生理解更快並記得更久，教學方法就產生其效果。"},{"en":"Studying how a drug achieves its effects helps doctors use it more safely.","zh":"研究藥物如何產生其效果，有助醫生更安全使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when asking how something works.","zh":"詢問某物如何運作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make more than enough money out of","meaning":"從……賺取大量金錢","examples":[{"en":"Companies made more than enough money out of aspirin.","zh":"公司從阿士匹靈賺取了大量金錢。"},{"en":"To make more than enough money out of something means to earn a large profit from it.","zh":"make more than enough money out of something 指從某物賺取大量利潤。"},{"en":"A tutoring centre may make more than enough money out of a popular exam course.","zh":"補習中心可能從熱門考試課程賺取大量金錢。"},{"en":"When a product already earns well, companies may feel less need to research it deeply.","zh":"當產品已經賺很多，公司可能覺得不需要深入研究它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when profit is already high.","zh":"當利潤已經很高時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as it was","meaning":"就其原有狀態而言","examples":[{"en":"Companies profited from aspirin as it was.","zh":"公司就阿士匹靈原有狀態而言已能獲利。"},{"en":"As it was means in its existing form or situation, without needing change.","zh":"as it was 指以現有形式或情況而言，不需要改變。"},{"en":"The essay was already clear as it was, so the teacher only corrected a few small errors.","zh":"文章原本已清楚，所以老師只改了幾個小錯。"},{"en":"If a product sells well as it is, companies may avoid risky changes.","zh":"如果產品以原有狀態已賣得好，公司可能避免冒險改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something already works in its current state.","zh":"當某物以目前狀態已有效時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a decade earlier","meaning":"早十年","examples":[{"en":"If newer drugs had arrived a decade earlier, aspirin might have disappeared.","zh":"如果較新藥物早十年出現，阿士匹靈可能已消失。"},{"en":"A decade earlier means ten years before the time being discussed.","zh":"a decade earlier 指比正在討論的時間早十年。"},{"en":"If the railway had opened a decade earlier, the town might have grown faster.","zh":"如果鐵路早十年開通，城鎮可能發展得更快。"},{"en":"A ten-year difference can change whether a product survives or disappears.","zh":"十年差異可以改變產品是存活還是消失。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when timing affects outcomes.","zh":"當時機影響結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not be here today","meaning":"今天可能已不存在","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin might not be here today if other drugs had arrived earlier.","zh":"如果其他藥物較早出現，阿士匹靈今天可能已不存在。"},{"en":"Not be here today means no longer exist or no longer be available now.","zh":"not be here today 指現在不再存在或不再可取得。"},{"en":"A small school might not be here today without support from parents and graduates.","zh":"如果沒有家長和校友支持，小學校今天可能已不存在。"},{"en":"Survival can depend on timing, demand, funding, and public attention.","zh":"存續可以取決於時機、需求、資金和公眾關注。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something almost disappeared but survived.","zh":"當某物差點消失但仍存活時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"just another forgotten drug","meaning":"又一種被遺忘的藥物","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin might have become just another forgotten drug.","zh":"阿士匹靈可能已變成又一種被遺忘的藥物。"},{"en":"Just another forgotten drug means one more medicine that people no longer remember or use.","zh":"just another forgotten drug 指又一種人們不再記得或使用的藥物。"},{"en":"A once-popular app can become just another forgotten product if users move to better alternatives.","zh":"如果用戶轉向更好選擇，曾經流行的應用程式也可能變成又一個被遺忘的產品。"},{"en":"Without new uses or continued demand, even important products can fade from memory.","zh":"沒有新用途或持續需求，即使重要產品也可能被淡忘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something risks becoming ordinary and ignored.","zh":"當某物有風險變得普通且被忽視時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"bother to explore","meaning":"費心探索","examples":[{"en":"People might not have bothered to explore aspirin’s further uses.","zh":"人們可能不會費心探索阿士匹靈的進一步用途。"},{"en":"To bother to explore something means to make the effort to investigate it.","zh":"bother to explore something 指花力氣去調查或研究某事。"},{"en":"A student may not bother to explore a difficult topic if they think it will not appear in the exam.","zh":"如果學生認為難題不會出現在考試中，可能不會費心探索它。"},{"en":"If no one makes the effort, hidden value may remain undiscovered.","zh":"如果沒有人付出努力，隱藏價值可能仍未被發現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when effort is required but may be neglected.","zh":"當需要努力但可能被忽視時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"recent discoveries","meaning":"近期發現","examples":[{"en":"Recent discoveries revealed new benefits of aspirin.","zh":"近期發現揭示了阿士匹靈的新好處。"},{"en":"Recent discoveries are new findings made not long ago.","zh":"recent discoveries 指不久前作出的新發現。"},{"en":"Recent discoveries about sleep may change how schools think about early classes.","zh":"關於睡眠的近期發現可能改變學校如何看待早課。"},{"en":"New discoveries can change old beliefs or create new uses for familiar things.","zh":"新發現可以改變舊信念，或為熟悉事物創造新用途。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research has updated knowledge.","zh":"當研究更新知識時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"aspirin’s benefits","meaning":"阿士匹靈的好處","examples":[{"en":"Recent discoveries focused on aspirin’s benefits.","zh":"近期發現集中於阿士匹靈的好處。"},{"en":"Aspirin’s benefits are the helpful effects or medical advantages of aspirin.","zh":"aspirin’s benefits 指阿士匹靈的有益效果或醫學優點。"},{"en":"Doctors may weigh aspirin’s benefits against its possible side effects before recommending it.","zh":"醫生在推薦阿士匹靈前，可能權衡其好處和可能副作用。"},{"en":"A drug’s benefits matter only when they are supported by evidence and balanced with risk.","zh":"藥物好處只有在有證據支持並與風險平衡時才重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing what aspirin can usefully do.","zh":"討論阿士匹靈有甚麼有用作用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"big pharmaceutical companies","meaning":"大型製藥公司","examples":[{"en":"The discoveries were not made by big pharmaceutical companies.","zh":"這些發現不是由大型製藥公司作出的。"},{"en":"Big pharmaceutical companies are large businesses that develop, manufacture, and sell medicines.","zh":"big pharmaceutical companies 指開發、生產和銷售藥物的大型企業。"},{"en":"Big pharmaceutical companies may fund expensive clinical trials for profitable new drugs.","zh":"大型製藥公司可能為有利可圖的新藥資助昂貴臨床試驗。"},{"en":"Large companies can support research, but profit may affect which questions they pursue.","zh":"大公司可以支持研究，但利潤可能影響它們追求哪些問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the drug industry.","zh":"討論製藥業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"public sector","meaning":"公營部門","examples":[{"en":"The discoveries were made by scientists working in the public sector.","zh":"這些發現由在公營部門工作的科學家作出。"},{"en":"The public sector includes government-funded organisations, public hospitals, universities, and public research bodies.","zh":"public sector 包括由政府資助的組織、公立醫院、大學和公共研究機構。"},{"en":"A public hospital belongs to the public sector because it serves the community with public support.","zh":"公立醫院屬於公營部門，因為它以公共支持服務社區。"},{"en":"Public-sector research may investigate important questions even when profits are low.","zh":"公營部門研究即使利潤低，也可能調查重要問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing public and private work.","zh":"比較公共和私人工作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"simple and straightforward","meaning":"簡單直接","examples":[{"en":"The reason is simple and straightforward.","zh":"原因簡單直接。"},{"en":"Simple and straightforward means easy to understand and not complicated.","zh":"simple and straightforward 指容易理解且不複雜。"},{"en":"A good classroom rule should be simple and straightforward so every student understands it.","zh":"好的課室規則應簡單直接，讓每名學生都明白。"},{"en":"Clear explanations reduce confusion and help people see the main point quickly.","zh":"清楚解釋可以減少困惑，幫助人很快看見重點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an answer is direct.","zh":"當答案直接時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"pursue research","meaning":"進行研究","examples":[{"en":"Drug companies pursue research that brings financial benefits.","zh":"藥廠進行能帶來經濟利益的研究。"},{"en":"To pursue research means to continue studying or investigating a topic seriously.","zh":"pursue research 指持續認真研究或調查某主題。"},{"en":"A university may pursue research into cleaner energy if society needs better fuel sources.","zh":"如果社會需要更好的燃料來源，大學可能進行清潔能源研究。"},{"en":"Researchers choose topics based on curiosity, need, funding, or possible impact.","zh":"研究人員根據好奇心、需要、資金或可能影響選擇主題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing ongoing investigation.","zh":"描述持續調查時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"deliver financial benefits","meaning":"帶來經濟利益","examples":[{"en":"Companies pursue research that will deliver financial benefits.","zh":"公司進行會帶來經濟利益的研究。"},{"en":"To deliver financial benefits means to bring money, profit, savings, or economic advantage.","zh":"deliver financial benefits 指帶來金錢、利潤、節省或經濟優勢。"},{"en":"A new booking system may deliver financial benefits by reducing staff workload and errors.","zh":"新預約系統可以透過減少員工工作量和錯誤帶來經濟利益。"},{"en":"Companies usually prefer projects that are likely to earn or save money.","zh":"公司通常偏好可能賺錢或省錢的項目。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when money is the expected result.","zh":"當金錢是預期結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"there’s no profit in","meaning":"……已沒有利潤","examples":[{"en":"There’s no profit in aspirin any more.","zh":"阿士匹靈已沒有利潤。"},{"en":"There’s no profit in something means it no longer makes enough money to attract business interest.","zh":"there’s no profit in something 指某事不再賺到足夠金錢來吸引商業興趣。"},{"en":"A shop may stop selling a product if there is no profit in it after rent and staff costs.","zh":"如果扣除租金和員工成本後沒有利潤，商店可能停止售賣某產品。"},{"en":"When profit disappears, companies may stop promoting or researching a product.","zh":"當利潤消失，公司可能停止宣傳或研究某產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when business interest depends on money.","zh":"當商業興趣取決於金錢時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"incredibly inexpensive","meaning":"非常便宜","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin is incredibly inexpensive.","zh":"阿士匹靈非常便宜。"},{"en":"Incredibly inexpensive means surprisingly cheap.","zh":"incredibly inexpensive 指便宜得令人驚訝。"},{"en":"A notebook may be incredibly inexpensive if it costs less than a bottle of water.","zh":"如果一本筆記簿比一瓶水還便宜，它就非常便宜。"},{"en":"A very cheap product may help patients but offer little profit to companies.","zh":"非常便宜的產品可能幫助病人，但給公司的利潤很少。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when low cost is surprising or important.","zh":"當低成本令人驚訝或很重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tiny profit margins","meaning":"微薄利潤率","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin has tiny profit margins.","zh":"阿士匹靈的利潤率微薄。"},{"en":"Tiny profit margins mean the difference between selling price and cost is very small.","zh":"tiny profit margins 指售價和成本之間的差距很小。"},{"en":"A small café may have tiny profit margins if food costs and rent are high.","zh":"如果食材成本和租金很高，小咖啡店可能利潤率微薄。"},{"en":"When profit margins are tiny, companies may prefer selling more expensive products.","zh":"當利潤率微薄，公司可能偏好銷售更昂貴產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a product earns little money per sale.","zh":"當產品每次銷售賺很少錢時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have no patent","meaning":"沒有專利","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin has no patent any more.","zh":"阿士匹靈已沒有專利。"},{"en":"Have no patent means no company has exclusive legal rights to make or sell the product.","zh":"have no patent 指沒有公司擁有製造或銷售該產品的獨家法律權利。"},{"en":"A medicine with no patent can often be produced by many manufacturers.","zh":"沒有專利的藥物通常可由許多製造商生產。"},{"en":"Without patent protection, prices may fall and profits may shrink.","zh":"沒有專利保護，價格可能下降，利潤可能縮小。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing drug ownership and competition.","zh":"討論藥物擁有權和競爭時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"anyone can produce it","meaning":"任何人都可以生產它","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin has no patent, so anyone can produce it.","zh":"阿士匹靈沒有專利，所以任何人都可以生產它。"},{"en":"Anyone can produce it means no single company controls production rights.","zh":"anyone can produce it 指沒有單一公司控制生產權。"},{"en":"If a recipe is public, anyone can produce the dish and sell their own version.","zh":"如果食譜是公開的，任何人都可以製作並售賣自己的版本。"},{"en":"Open production can lower prices because many suppliers compete.","zh":"開放生產可以降低價格，因為許多供應商競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a product is no longer legally restricted.","zh":"當產品不再受法律限制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, companies may have a disincentive to promote aspirin.","zh":"事實上，公司可能有阻礙推廣阿士匹靈的因素。"},{"en":"In fact introduces a statement that strengthens, corrects, or surprises after the previous point.","zh":"in fact 引入一個加強、修正或令人意外的說法。"},{"en":"The lesson seemed easy; in fact, many students failed the quiz.","zh":"課堂看似容易；事實上，很多學生測驗不合格。"},{"en":"This phrase often prepares readers for a clearer or unexpected truth.","zh":"這個短語常讓讀者準備接受更清楚或意外的真相。"},{"en":"It is useful when adding emphasis or correction.","zh":"加強語氣或修正說法時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"disincentive for","meaning":"阻礙……的因素","examples":[{"en":"There may be a disincentive for companies to boost aspirin.","zh":"公司可能有阻礙推廣阿士匹靈的因素。"},{"en":"A disincentive for something is a reason that discourages people from doing it.","zh":"disincentive for something 指令人不想做某事的原因。"},{"en":"High transport costs can be a disincentive for students to attend after-school classes.","zh":"高交通成本可能成為學生參加課後課程的阻礙因素。"},{"en":"If an action brings little profit or even harms business, companies may avoid it.","zh":"如果某行動利潤很低甚至傷害生意，公司可能避免它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why people do not act.","zh":"解釋人們為何不行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"further boost the drug","meaning":"進一步推動該藥物","examples":[{"en":"Companies may not want to further boost the drug.","zh":"公司可能不想進一步推動該藥物。"},{"en":"To further boost the drug means to increase its use, reputation, or sales even more.","zh":"further boost the drug 指進一步增加該藥物的使用、聲譽或銷量。"},{"en":"A hospital campaign may further boost a vaccine if doctors explain its benefits clearly.","zh":"如果醫生清楚解釋疫苗好處，醫院宣傳可以進一步推動疫苗接種。"},{"en":"A company may avoid boosting a cheap drug if it reduces sales of expensive alternatives.","zh":"如果便宜藥物會減少昂貴替代品銷售，公司可能避免推動它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when promotion would increase a medicine’s success.","zh":"當宣傳會增加藥物成功時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"put them out of business","meaning":"令……倒閉","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin could put some companies out of business.","zh":"阿士匹靈可能令一些公司倒閉。"},{"en":"To put a company out of business means to make it fail or close.","zh":"put a company out of business 指令公司失敗或關閉。"},{"en":"A large supermarket may put a small shop out of business if customers stop going there.","zh":"如果顧客不再去小店，大型超市可能令它倒閉。"},{"en":"Cheap effective products can threaten companies that depend on expensive alternatives.","zh":"便宜有效的產品可以威脅依賴昂貴替代品的公司。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when competition destroys a business.","zh":"當競爭摧毀生意時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stop someone from doing","meaning":"阻止某人做……","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin might stop companies from selling expensive brands.","zh":"阿士匹靈可能阻止公司銷售昂貴品牌。"},{"en":"To stop someone from doing something means to prevent them from taking that action.","zh":"stop someone from doing something 指阻止某人採取某行動。"},{"en":"Heavy rain may stop students from playing football outside.","zh":"大雨可能阻止學生在戶外踢足球。"},{"en":"If a cheaper product meets the same need, it can stop customers from buying expensive versions.","zh":"如果較便宜產品滿足同樣需要，它可以阻止顧客購買昂貴版本。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one factor prevents an action.","zh":"當一個因素阻止行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"expensive brands","meaning":"昂貴品牌","examples":[{"en":"Drug companies prefer selling their more expensive brands.","zh":"藥廠較喜歡銷售它們較昂貴的品牌。"},{"en":"Expensive brands are products sold under a brand name at a high price.","zh":"expensive brands 指以品牌名稱高價出售的產品。"},{"en":"Some shoppers buy expensive brands because they trust the name or packaging.","zh":"有些消費者購買昂貴品牌，因為信任其名稱或包裝。"},{"en":"Companies often earn more profit from expensive brands than from cheap generic products.","zh":"公司通常從昂貴品牌賺取比廉價非專利產品更多利潤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing price and marketing.","zh":"討論價格和行銷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the solution to","meaning":"……的解決方法","examples":[{"en":"The passage asks about the solution to a lack of commercial interest.","zh":"文章詢問缺乏商業興趣的解決方法。"},{"en":"The solution to a problem is the answer or method that deals with it.","zh":"solution to a problem 指處理某問題的答案或方法。"},{"en":"The solution to poor spelling may be regular reading and correction practice.","zh":"拼字差的解決方法可能是定期閱讀和改錯練習。"},{"en":"A good solution addresses the cause, not only the surface symptom.","zh":"好的解決方法會處理原因，而不只是表面症狀。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing problem-solving.","zh":"討論解難時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a lack of commercial interest","meaning":"缺乏商業興趣","examples":[{"en":"There is a lack of commercial interest in further aspirin research.","zh":"對進一步阿士匹靈研究缺乏商業興趣。"},{"en":"A lack of commercial interest means businesses are not strongly motivated because profit is low.","zh":"lack of commercial interest 指因利潤低，企業沒有強烈動機。"},{"en":"A village bus route may suffer from a lack of commercial interest if few passengers use it.","zh":"如果乘客很少，鄉村巴士線可能因缺乏商業興趣而受影響。"},{"en":"When businesses are not interested, public funding may be needed to support important work.","zh":"當企業不感興趣，可能需要公共資金支持重要工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when social value exists but profit does not.","zh":"當有社會價值但沒有利潤時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"further exploring","meaning":"進一步探索","examples":[{"en":"Scientists want to further explore the therapeutic benefits of aspirin.","zh":"科學家希望進一步探索阿士匹靈的治療益處。"},{"en":"Further exploring means studying something more deeply or continuing investigation.","zh":"further exploring 指更深入研究或繼續調查某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may further explore a grammar problem if many students keep making the same mistake.","zh":"如果許多學生持續犯同一文法錯誤，老師可能進一步探索該問題。"},{"en":"Further exploration can reveal uses, risks, or explanations that were missed before.","zh":"進一步探索可以揭示以前被忽略的用途、風險或解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research should continue.","zh":"當研究應該繼續時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"therapeutic benefits","meaning":"治療益處","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin may have additional therapeutic benefits.","zh":"阿士匹靈可能有額外治療益處。"},{"en":"Therapeutic benefits are health improvements or treatment advantages brought by a medicine or therapy.","zh":"therapeutic benefits 指藥物或療法帶來的健康改善或治療優點。"},{"en":"Gentle exercise can have therapeutic benefits for stress and sleep.","zh":"溫和運動對壓力和睡眠可以有治療益處。"},{"en":"A drug’s therapeutic benefits must be tested before doctors recommend new uses.","zh":"藥物的新治療益處必須經測試，醫生才會推薦新用途。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing medical value.","zh":"討論醫學價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"public money","meaning":"公帑；公共資金","examples":[{"en":"Jeffreys argues for more public money for clinical trials.","zh":"Jeffreys 主張為臨床試驗投入更多公共資金。"},{"en":"Public money is money from the government or taxpayers used for public purposes.","zh":"public money 指來自政府或納稅人、用於公共目的的金錢。"},{"en":"Public money may fund schools, hospitals, roads, and scientific research.","zh":"公共資金可能資助學校、醫院、道路和科學研究。"},{"en":"When private companies see little profit, public money can support socially useful work.","zh":"當私人公司看不到多少利潤，公共資金可以支持有社會價值的工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing government-funded projects.","zh":"討論政府資助項目時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"go into","meaning":"投入於……","examples":[{"en":"More public money should go into clinical trials.","zh":"更多公共資金應投入臨床試驗。"},{"en":"Go into means be spent on, invested in, or directed toward something.","zh":"go into 指被花在、投資於或導向某事。"},{"en":"More school funding should go into teacher training if lessons need improvement.","zh":"如果課堂需要改善，更多學校資金應投入教師培訓。"},{"en":"Where money goes affects what society is able to develop or protect.","zh":"金錢投向哪裏，會影響社會能發展或保護甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing funding priorities.","zh":"討論資金優先次序時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"clinical trials","meaning":"臨床試驗","examples":[{"en":"Clinical trials are needed to explore aspirin’s benefits.","zh":"需要臨床試驗來探索阿士匹靈的好處。"},{"en":"Clinical trials are research studies that test medicines or treatments in people.","zh":"clinical trials 指在人身上測試藥物或治療方法的研究。"},{"en":"A new vaccine must pass clinical trials before it can be widely used.","zh":"新疫苗必須通過臨床試驗，才可廣泛使用。"},{"en":"Trials help show whether a treatment is safe, effective, and better than alternatives.","zh":"試驗幫助顯示治療是否安全、有效，並優於替代方案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing medical research.","zh":"討論醫學研究時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a very inexpensive drug","meaning":"非常便宜的藥物","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin is a very inexpensive drug.","zh":"阿士匹靈是一種非常便宜的藥物。"},{"en":"A very inexpensive drug is a medicine that costs very little to buy or produce.","zh":"very inexpensive drug 指購買或生產成本很低的藥物。"},{"en":"A very inexpensive drug can be valuable in poorer communities if it treats common conditions safely.","zh":"如果非常便宜的藥物能安全治療常見疾病，它在較貧困社區會很有價值。"},{"en":"Low price helps patients, but it may reduce companies’ motivation to invest in research.","zh":"低價格有助病人，但可能減少公司投資研究的動機。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when cost affects access and profit.","zh":"當成本影響可及性和利潤時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"there may be","meaning":"可能有……","examples":[{"en":"There may be many other things we could do with aspirin.","zh":"我們可能還有許多其他方式可以使用阿士匹靈。"},{"en":"There may be means it is possible that something exists or is true.","zh":"there may be 指某事可能存在或可能是真。"},{"en":"There may be a simpler way to solve the maths problem.","zh":"可能有更簡單的方法解決數學題。"},{"en":"This phrase allows cautious possibility without claiming certainty.","zh":"這個短語表達謹慎可能性，而不是聲稱確定。"},{"en":"It is useful when more investigation is needed.","zh":"當需要更多調查時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"find out","meaning":"查明；找出","examples":[{"en":"Researchers should try to find out more about aspirin.","zh":"研究人員應嘗試查明更多關於阿士匹靈的資料。"},{"en":"To find out means to discover information by asking, checking, studying, or investigating.","zh":"find out 指透過詢問、查閱、研究或調查來發現資訊。"},{"en":"A student can find out the meaning of a word by checking context and examples.","zh":"學生可以透過查看語境和例子找出詞語意思。"},{"en":"Finding out requires active effort, not just guessing.","zh":"查明需要主動努力，而不只是猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when information is unknown.","zh":"當資訊未知時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"tell the tale of","meaning":"講述……的故事","examples":[{"en":"Jeffreys’ book tells the tale of a wonder drug.","zh":"Jeffreys 的書講述一種神奇藥物的故事。"},{"en":"To tell the tale of something means to narrate its story or history.","zh":"tell the tale of something 指敘述某事物的故事或歷史。"},{"en":"A museum exhibition may tell the tale of a city’s old fishing community.","zh":"博物館展覽可能講述城市舊漁業社群的故事。"},{"en":"Telling a tale helps readers see events as a connected story rather than isolated facts.","zh":"講述故事幫助讀者把事件看成相連敘事，而不是孤立事實。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when presenting history in narrative form.","zh":"以敘事方式呈現歷史時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"explore the nature of","meaning":"探討……的本質","examples":[{"en":"The book explores the nature of innovation.","zh":"這本書探討創新的本質。"},{"en":"To explore the nature of something means to examine what it really is and how it works.","zh":"explore the nature of something 指檢視某事真正是甚麼以及如何運作。"},{"en":"A philosophy class may explore the nature of happiness by comparing money, friendship, and purpose.","zh":"哲學課可能透過比較金錢、友誼和人生目的來探討幸福的本質。"},{"en":"Exploring the nature of a topic goes deeper than listing examples.","zh":"探討主題本質比列舉例子更深入。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when analysing an idea seriously.","zh":"認真分析一個想法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the role of","meaning":"……的作用","examples":[{"en":"The book explores the role of big business, public money and regulation.","zh":"這本書探討大企業、公共資金和規管的作用。"},{"en":"The role of something means the part it plays in a process or situation.","zh":"role of something 指某事在過程或情況中扮演的部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may discuss the role of parents in supporting students’ reading habits.","zh":"老師可能討論家長在支持學生閱讀習慣方面的作用。"},{"en":"Understanding roles helps explain who or what influences the final result.","zh":"理解作用有助解釋誰或甚麼影響最終結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when analysing how different factors contribute.","zh":"分析不同因素如何貢獻時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"big business","meaning":"大企業","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses the role of big business in innovation.","zh":"這本書討論大企業在創新中的作用。"},{"en":"Big business means large companies or powerful commercial organisations.","zh":"big business 指大型公司或有權勢的商業組織。"},{"en":"Big business can influence what products are developed, advertised, and sold.","zh":"大企業可以影響哪些產品被開發、宣傳和銷售。"},{"en":"Large companies can fund research, but they may also prioritise profit.","zh":"大公司可以資助研究，但也可能優先考慮利潤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing corporate power.","zh":"討論企業權力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"regulation","meaning":"規管","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses the role of regulation in drug development.","zh":"這本書討論規管在藥物開發中的作用。"},{"en":"Regulation means official rules that control how something is made, sold, tested, or used.","zh":"regulation 指控制某物如何製造、銷售、測試或使用的官方規則。"},{"en":"Food regulation helps make sure restaurants store ingredients safely.","zh":"食物規管幫助確保餐廳安全儲存食材。"},{"en":"In medicine, regulation protects patients by requiring evidence of safety and effectiveness.","zh":"在醫學中，規管透過要求安全和有效證據來保護病人。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing laws and safety standards.","zh":"討論法律和安全標準時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"remind us why","meaning":"提醒我們為何……","examples":[{"en":"The book reminds us why such research is important.","zh":"這本書提醒我們為何這類研究重要。"},{"en":"Remind us why means make us remember or understand the reason something matters.","zh":"remind us why 指令我們記得或明白某事重要的原因。"},{"en":"A traffic accident may remind us why seat belts are necessary.","zh":"交通意外可能提醒我們為何安全帶是必要的。"},{"en":"Good examples can remind people why a familiar issue still deserves attention.","zh":"好例子可以提醒人們為何熟悉議題仍值得關注。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when restating importance.","zh":"重新說明重要性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"such research","meaning":"這類研究","examples":[{"en":"Such research may reveal new uses for old drugs.","zh":"這類研究可能揭示舊藥的新用途。"},{"en":"Such research means research of the type just mentioned.","zh":"such research 指剛才提到的那一類研究。"},{"en":"Such research into student stress can help schools design better support systems.","zh":"這類關於學生壓力的研究可以幫助學校設計更好的支援系統。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating a long description while still referring clearly to it.","zh":"這個短語避免重複長描述，同時仍清楚回指它。"},{"en":"It is useful when continuing a discussion about a specific type of study.","zh":"繼續討論某類研究時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete each sentence with","meaning":"用……完成每句","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete each sentence with the correct ending.","zh":"考生用正確句末完成每句。"},{"en":"Complete each sentence with something means finish the sentence by adding the required ending, word, or phrase.","zh":"complete each sentence with something 指加入所需句末、詞語或短語來完成句子。"},{"en":"Students may complete each sentence with a phrase from the box.","zh":"學生可能用方框中的短語完成每句。"},{"en":"The answer must fit both the grammar and the meaning of the passage.","zh":"答案必須同時符合文法和文章意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading and grammar instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於閱讀和文法指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the correct ending","meaning":"正確句末","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct ending from the box.","zh":"考生從方框中選出正確句末。"},{"en":"The correct ending is the sentence ending that matches both meaning and grammar.","zh":"correct ending 指同時符合意思和文法的句子結尾。"},{"en":"In a matching task, one correct ending may complete the sentence better than all other options.","zh":"在配對題中，一個正確句末可能比所有其他選項更好地完成句子。"},{"en":"A wrong ending may contain familiar words but still distort the passage’s meaning.","zh":"錯誤句末可能包含熟悉字眼，但仍扭曲文章意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in sentence-completion questions.","zh":"這個短語適用於句子完成題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"from the box below","meaning":"從下面方框中","examples":[{"en":"The correct ending is selected from the box below.","zh":"正確句末從下面方框中選出。"},{"en":"From the box below means the answer must be chosen from the listed options underneath the question.","zh":"from the box below 指答案必須從題目下方列出的選項中選出。"},{"en":"Students should choose a verb from the box below, not invent their own answer.","zh":"學生應從下面方框中選擇動詞，而不是自己創作答案。"},{"en":"This instruction limits the possible answers and helps students focus on matching.","zh":"這個指示限制可能答案，幫助學生專注配對。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be aware of","meaning":"知道；意識到","examples":[{"en":"Ancient doctors were aware of the medical uses of willow.","zh":"古代醫生知道柳樹的醫學用途。"},{"en":"Be aware of something means know about it or realise that it exists.","zh":"be aware of something 指知道某事或意識到它存在。"},{"en":"Students should be aware of the deadline before starting a project.","zh":"學生開始專題前應知道截止日期。"},{"en":"Awareness can guide action, even if people do not yet understand all the details.","zh":"意識可以引導行動，即使人們尚未理解所有細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone knows or notices something important.","zh":"當某人知道或注意到重要事情時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"medical applications","meaning":"醫學應用","examples":[{"en":"New medical applications of aspirin were discovered later.","zh":"阿士匹靈的新醫學應用後來被發現。"},{"en":"Medical applications are ways a medicine, method, or discovery can be used in healthcare.","zh":"medical applications 指藥物、方法或發現在醫療中的使用方式。"},{"en":"A new imaging tool may have medical applications in cancer diagnosis.","zh":"新成像工具可能在癌症診斷中有醫學應用。"},{"en":"Discovering new applications can make an old treatment useful again.","zh":"發現新應用可以令舊治療再次有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing practical medical uses.","zh":"討論實際醫學用途時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"negative effects of publicity","meaning":"宣傳的負面影響","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions the negative effects of publicity.","zh":"題目提到宣傳的負面影響。"},{"en":"Negative effects of publicity are harmful results caused by advertising or public attention.","zh":"negative effects of publicity 指廣告或公眾關注造成的有害結果。"},{"en":"Too much publicity may create panic if people misunderstand a health warning.","zh":"如果人們誤解健康警告，過多宣傳可能造成恐慌。"},{"en":"Publicity can help a product, but it can also exaggerate claims or mislead consumers.","zh":"宣傳可以幫助產品，但也可能誇大說法或誤導消費者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when promotion has harmful consequences.","zh":"當推廣帶來有害後果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"large pharmaceutical companies","meaning":"大型製藥公司","examples":[{"en":"Large pharmaceutical companies did not make the recent discoveries.","zh":"大型製藥公司並沒有作出近期發現。"},{"en":"Large pharmaceutical companies are major businesses that research, manufacture, and sell medicines.","zh":"large pharmaceutical companies 指研究、生產和銷售藥物的大型企業。"},{"en":"Large pharmaceutical companies may spend heavily on marketing and clinical trials.","zh":"大型製藥公司可能在行銷和臨床試驗上花費大量金錢。"},{"en":"Their size gives them resources, but profit can influence their research priorities.","zh":"它們的規模給予資源，但利潤可以影響研究優先次序。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the medicine industry.","zh":"討論醫藥業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"medical uses of a particular tree","meaning":"某種樹的醫學用途","examples":[{"en":"Ancient doctors knew about the medical uses of a particular tree.","zh":"古代醫生知道某種樹的醫學用途。"},{"en":"Medical uses of a particular tree are health-related ways parts of that tree can be used.","zh":"medical uses of a particular tree 指該樹某些部分與健康相關的使用方式。"},{"en":"A healer may know the medical uses of a tree whose bark reduces pain.","zh":"治療者可能知道一種樹的醫學用途，因其樹皮可減痛。"},{"en":"Plant-based medical knowledge often begins with observation of repeated effects.","zh":"植物醫學知識常始於對重複效果的觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a specific plant has healing value.","zh":"當特定植物有治療價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"limited availability of","meaning":"……供應有限","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to the limited availability of new drugs.","zh":"題目提到新藥供應有限。"},{"en":"Limited availability of something means it is not easy to get or not widely supplied.","zh":"limited availability of something 指某物不容易取得或供應不廣泛。"},{"en":"A shortage of textbooks can create limited availability of study materials.","zh":"課本短缺可以造成學習材料供應有限。"},{"en":"When availability is limited, prices may rise and access may become unfair.","zh":"當供應有限，價格可能上升，取得機會也可能變得不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when supply is restricted.","zh":"當供應受限制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"commercial advertising campaigns","meaning":"商業廣告宣傳活動","examples":[{"en":"Commercial advertising campaigns helped create a market for aspirin.","zh":"商業廣告宣傳活動幫助為阿士匹靈創造市場。"},{"en":"Commercial advertising campaigns are organised business efforts to promote a product to customers.","zh":"commercial advertising campaigns 指企業有組織地向顧客推廣產品的活動。"},{"en":"A company may run commercial advertising campaigns on television, buses, and social media.","zh":"公司可能在電視、巴士和社交媒體上進行商業廣告宣傳活動。"},{"en":"Strong advertising can teach consumers what a product is for and why they should buy it.","zh":"強力廣告可以教消費者產品用途和為何應購買。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when marketing shapes demand.","zh":"當行銷塑造需求時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be able to reproduce","meaning":"能夠複製","examples":[{"en":"Friedrich Bayer & Co. were able to reproduce the chemical synthetically.","zh":"Friedrich Bayer & Co. 能夠以合成方式複製該化學物質。"},{"en":"Be able to reproduce something means have the ability to make or copy it again.","zh":"be able to reproduce something 指有能力再次製造或複製某物。"},{"en":"A student is able to reproduce a science result when the same experiment gives the same outcome.","zh":"當同一實驗得到同一結果，學生就能夠複製科學結果。"},{"en":"Reproducibility matters because it allows reliable production and testing.","zh":"可複製性很重要，因為它容許可靠生產和測試。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a result can be repeated.","zh":"當結果可以重複時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the development of aspirin","meaning":"阿士匹靈的發展","examples":[{"en":"The development of aspirin was influenced by the industrial revolution.","zh":"阿士匹靈的發展受到工業革命影響。"},{"en":"The development of aspirin means the process by which aspirin was discovered, produced, named, marketed, and studied.","zh":"development of aspirin 指阿士匹靈被發現、生產、命名、推廣和研究的過程。"},{"en":"A timeline can help students understand the development of aspirin from willow bark to modern tablets.","zh":"時間線可以幫助學生理解阿士匹靈由柳樹皮到現代藥片的發展。"},{"en":"Development involved science, business, technology, and later public research.","zh":"其發展涉及科學、商業、科技和後來的公共研究。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when tracing how a medicine came into being.","zh":"追蹤藥物如何形成時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be partly due to","meaning":"部分歸因於","examples":[{"en":"The development of aspirin was partly due to broader social changes.","zh":"阿士匹靈的發展部分歸因於更廣泛的社會變化。"},{"en":"Be partly due to means be caused in part by something, though not entirely.","zh":"be partly due to 指部分由某事造成，但不完全是。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be partly due to more sleep and partly due to better teaching.","zh":"學生進步可能部分歸因於更多睡眠，部分歸因於更好教學。"},{"en":"This phrase allows a balanced explanation with more than one cause.","zh":"這個短語容許包含多於一個原因的平衡解釋。"},{"en":"It is useful when a result has mixed causes.","zh":"當結果有混合原因時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the creation of a market for","meaning":"為……創造市場","examples":[{"en":"The creation of a market for aspirin required advertising.","zh":"為阿士匹靈創造市場需要廣告。"},{"en":"The creation of a market for something means building demand so people want to buy it.","zh":"creation of a market for something 指建立需求，使人想購買某物。"},{"en":"A company may need demonstrations to create a market for a new kitchen tool.","zh":"公司可能需要示範來為新廚具創造市場。"},{"en":"Consumers often need to understand a product before a market can grow.","zh":"市場能夠增長前，消費者通常需要理解產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when demand must be developed.","zh":"當需求需要被建立時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"become unavailable","meaning":"變得無法取得","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin might have become unavailable without later discoveries.","zh":"如果沒有後來的發現，阿士匹靈可能變得無法取得。"},{"en":"Become unavailable means no longer be possible to buy, use, or access.","zh":"become unavailable 指不再能購買、使用或取得。"},{"en":"A bus route may become unavailable if the company stops operating it.","zh":"如果巴士公司停止營運，某條巴士路線可能變得無法使用。"},{"en":"If a product disappears from shops, people may lose access even if it is useful.","zh":"如果產品從商店消失，即使有用，人們也可能失去取得它的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when access to something is lost.","zh":"當某物失去可及性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"actually worked","meaning":"實際上發揮作用","examples":[{"en":"The way aspirin actually worked was not investigated for decades.","zh":"阿士匹靈實際上如何發揮作用，數十年來都未被研究。"},{"en":"Actually worked means truly produced its effect in real terms, not just seemed to work.","zh":"actually worked 指真正實際產生效果，而不只是看似有效。"},{"en":"A study may ask whether a new study app actually worked or only made students feel organised.","zh":"研究可能詢問新學習應用程式實際上是否有效，還是只令人感覺有組織。"},{"en":"Knowing that something works is useful, but knowing how it works can improve safety and design.","zh":"知道某物有效很有用，但知道它如何有效可以改善安全和設計。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when focusing on real mechanism or effectiveness.","zh":"聚焦真實機制或成效時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agree with the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether the statements agree with the views of the writer.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與作者觀點一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the views of someone means match that person’s opinion or argument.","zh":"agree with the views of someone 指符合某人的意見或論點。"},{"en":"A statement agrees with the writer only if the passage clearly supports it.","zh":"只有文章清楚支持某陳述，它才與作者觀點一致。"},{"en":"Students should not answer from personal opinion when judging the writer’s view.","zh":"判斷作者觀點時，學生不應根據個人意見作答。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in YES, NO, NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 YES, NO, NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the views of the writer.","zh":"一個陳述可能與作者觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradict the views of someone means say the opposite of that person’s opinion or argument.","zh":"contradict the views of someone 指說出與某人意見或論點相反的意思。"},{"en":"If a writer says public money is needed, a statement saying only companies should pay may contradict the view.","zh":"如果作者說需要公共資金，而陳述說只應由公司付款，就可能與觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be based on the passage, not on outside knowledge.","zh":"矛盾必須基於文章，而不是外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying NO answers.","zh":"辨認 NO 答案時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Write NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"如果無法判斷作者想法，寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資料作出判斷。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions the writer’s view on price controls, it is impossible to say what they think.","zh":"如果文章從未提到作者對價格管制的看法，就無法判斷他怎樣想。"},{"en":"Students should choose NOT GIVEN when evidence is missing.","zh":"當證據缺失時，學生應選 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a text does not support either true or false.","zh":"當文本不支持真或假任何一方時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"small-scale research","meaning":"小規模研究","examples":[{"en":"Small-scale research was once enough to make discoveries.","zh":"小規模研究曾經足以作出發現。"},{"en":"Small-scale research is research done with limited equipment, money, or number of people.","zh":"small-scale research 指使用有限設備、金錢或人手進行的研究。"},{"en":"A teacher can run small-scale research by testing one new activity with one class.","zh":"老師可以用一班學生測試一項新活動來進行小規模研究。"},{"en":"Small studies can be useful when the question is focused and the method is clear.","zh":"當問題集中且方法清楚，小型研究也可以有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research does not require huge resources.","zh":"當研究不需要龐大資源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"make important discoveries","meaning":"作出重要發現","examples":[{"en":"Nineteenth-century scientists could make important discoveries with simple tools.","zh":"十九世紀科學家能用簡單工具作出重要發現。"},{"en":"To make important discoveries means to find new knowledge that matters.","zh":"make important discoveries 指找到有意義的新知識。"},{"en":"A student may make an important discovery when they realise why they keep making the same grammar error.","zh":"當學生意識到自己為何不斷犯同一文法錯誤，他可能作出重要發現。"},{"en":"Discoveries matter when they change understanding, decisions, or future research.","zh":"當發現改變理解、決策或未來研究，它就重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when new findings have real value.","zh":"當新發現有真實價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"cause a change in","meaning":"導致……的改變","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether the industrial revolution caused a change in research focus.","zh":"題目問工業革命是否導致科學研究重點改變。"},{"en":"Cause a change in something means make it become different.","zh":"cause a change in something 指令某事變得不同。"},{"en":"A new exam format may cause a change in how students revise.","zh":"新考試形式可能導致學生溫習方式改變。"},{"en":"When conditions change, people often change their priorities and methods.","zh":"當條件改變，人們常會改變優先次序和方法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one factor leads to a shift.","zh":"當一個因素導致轉變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the focus of scientific research","meaning":"科學研究重點","examples":[{"en":"The focus of scientific research may change over time.","zh":"科學研究重點可能隨時間改變。"},{"en":"The focus of scientific research means the main questions or topics scientists are studying.","zh":"focus of scientific research 指科學家正在研究的主要問題或主題。"},{"en":"During a disease outbreak, the focus of scientific research may shift to vaccines and treatments.","zh":"疾病爆發期間，科學研究重點可能轉向疫苗和治療。"},{"en":"Research focus changes when society faces new problems or gains new tools.","zh":"當社會面對新問題或獲得新工具，研究重點會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing what scientists pay attention to.","zh":"討論科學家關注甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"follow a structured pattern of development","meaning":"遵循有系統的發展模式","examples":[{"en":"The development of aspirin did not follow a structured pattern of development.","zh":"阿士匹靈的發展並沒有遵循有系統的發展模式。"},{"en":"Follow a structured pattern of development means progress in an organised, planned, step-by-step way.","zh":"follow a structured pattern of development 指以有組織、有計劃、逐步方式進展。"},{"en":"A school curriculum follows a structured pattern of development when students learn basics before advanced topics.","zh":"如果學生先學基礎再學高階主題，學校課程就是遵循有系統的發展模式。"},{"en":"Some innovations do not follow a neat plan; they grow through accidents and separate discoveries.","zh":"有些創新並不按整齊計劃發展，而是透過意外和分散發現成長。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing planned progress with messy progress.","zh":"比較有計劃進展和混亂進展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"sales of new analgesic drugs","meaning":"新止痛藥的銷量","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions sales of new analgesic drugs.","zh":"題目提到新止痛藥的銷量。"},{"en":"Sales of new analgesic drugs are the number or value of newly introduced painkillers sold.","zh":"sales of new analgesic drugs 指新推出止痛藥售出的數量或金額。"},{"en":"Sales of new painkillers may rise if doctors and advertisements promote them heavily.","zh":"如果醫生和廣告大力推廣，新止痛藥銷量可能上升。"},{"en":"High sales can encourage companies to focus on new products rather than old medicines.","zh":"高銷量可以鼓勵公司專注新產品，而不是舊藥。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when business data are linked to medicine.","zh":"當商業數據與藥物有關時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"overtake sales of","meaning":"超越……的銷量","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether new drugs overtook sales of aspirin.","zh":"題目問新藥銷量是否超越阿士匹靈。"},{"en":"Overtake sales of something means sell more than that product.","zh":"overtake sales of something 指銷量超過某產品。"},{"en":"A new phone model may overtake sales of an older model if it is cheaper and faster.","zh":"如果新手機型號更便宜、更快速，它可能超越舊型號銷量。"},{"en":"When one product overtakes another, companies may shift advertising and investment.","zh":"當一個產品超越另一個，公司可能轉移廣告和投資。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing market performance.","zh":"比較市場表現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"both good and bad effects","meaning":"正反兩方面的影響","examples":[{"en":"Commercial companies may have both good and bad effects.","zh":"商業公司可能有正反兩方面的影響。"},{"en":"Both good and bad effects means positive and negative results happen together or are both possible.","zh":"both good and bad effects 指正面和負面結果同時出現或都可能出現。"},{"en":"Homework can have both good and bad effects: it gives practice but may reduce sleep if excessive.","zh":"功課可以有正反兩方面影響：它提供練習，但過多時可能減少睡眠。"},{"en":"A balanced argument should recognise benefits and risks at the same time.","zh":"平衡論點應同時承認好處和風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an issue is mixed rather than simple.","zh":"當議題混合而不簡單時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"availability of pharmaceutical products","meaning":"藥品的供應情況","examples":[{"en":"Commercial markets affect the availability of pharmaceutical products.","zh":"商業市場影響藥品的供應情況。"},{"en":"Availability of pharmaceutical products means whether medicines can be obtained by patients, hospitals, or pharmacies.","zh":"availability of pharmaceutical products 指病人、醫院或藥房是否能取得藥物。"},{"en":"A medicine’s availability may improve when more factories produce it.","zh":"當更多工廠生產某藥物，它的供應情況可能改善。"},{"en":"If availability falls, patients may face delays, higher prices, or fewer treatment choices.","zh":"如果供應下降，病人可能面對延誤、更高價格或較少治療選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing access to medicines.","zh":"討論藥物可及性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the summary below","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the summary below using the list of words.","zh":"考生使用詞語列表完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"Complete the summary below means fill in the missing parts of the summary that appears under the instructions.","zh":"complete the summary below 指填寫指示下方摘要中的缺漏部分。"},{"en":"Students should complete the summary below by matching each gap with the passage meaning.","zh":"學生應透過把每個空格與文章意思配對來完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"Summary completion tests understanding, grammar, and careful word choice.","zh":"摘要填空測試理解、文法和謹慎選詞。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"using the list of words","meaning":"使用詞語列表","examples":[{"en":"The summary must be completed using the list of words.","zh":"摘要必須使用詞語列表完成。"},{"en":"Using the list of words means answers must come from the given word choices.","zh":"using the list of words 指答案必須來自提供的詞語選項。"},{"en":"In a vocabulary exercise, students may complete sentences using the list of words at the top.","zh":"在詞彙練習中，學生可能使用頁頂詞語列表完成句子。"},{"en":"This instruction prevents students from inventing answers outside the options.","zh":"這個指示防止學生自行創作選項以外的答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when answer choices are restricted.","zh":"當答案選擇受限制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"research into aspirin","meaning":"對阿士匹靈的研究","examples":[{"en":"The summary focuses on research into aspirin.","zh":"摘要聚焦對阿士匹靈的研究。"},{"en":"Research into aspirin means scientific study of aspirin’s effects, uses, risks, or mechanisms.","zh":"research into aspirin 指對阿士匹靈效果、用途、風險或機制的科學研究。"},{"en":"A university may conduct research into aspirin to test whether it helps prevent another disease.","zh":"大學可能進行阿士匹靈研究，以測試它是否有助預防另一種疾病。"},{"en":"Research into old medicines can reveal uses that earlier doctors did not know.","zh":"對舊藥的研究可以揭示早期醫生不知道的用途。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when aspirin is the subject of investigation.","zh":"當阿士匹靈是調查對象時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"new uses of aspirin","meaning":"阿士匹靈的新用途","examples":[{"en":"Scientists discovered new uses of aspirin.","zh":"科學家發現阿士匹靈的新用途。"},{"en":"New uses of aspirin are medical purposes for aspirin that were not originally known or emphasised.","zh":"new uses of aspirin 指阿士匹靈原本不為人知或不被強調的醫學用途。"},{"en":"Researchers may find new uses of an old drug by testing it in different patient groups.","zh":"研究人員可能透過在不同病人群體中測試舊藥，找出其新用途。"},{"en":"New uses can keep a cheap medicine important long after it first enters the market.","zh":"新用途可以令便宜藥物在首次進入市場很久後仍然重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when old drugs gain fresh medical value.","zh":"當舊藥獲得新的醫學價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no longer","meaning":"不再","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin is no longer a highly profitable drug.","zh":"阿士匹靈不再是一種高度有利可圖的藥物。"},{"en":"No longer means not now, although it was true before.","zh":"no longer 指現在不再如此，雖然以前是如此。"},{"en":"A student who practises daily may no longer be afraid of speaking English.","zh":"每天練習的學生可能不再害怕說英文。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a change between the past and present.","zh":"這個短語突出過去與現在之間的改變。"},{"en":"It is useful when something has stopped being true.","zh":"當某事已不再真實時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"profitable drug","meaning":"有利可圖的藥物","examples":[{"en":"Aspirin is no longer a profitable drug for large companies.","zh":"對大型公司來說，阿士匹靈不再是有利可圖的藥物。"},{"en":"A profitable drug is a medicine that earns enough money for the company selling it.","zh":"profitable drug 指能為銷售公司賺取足夠金錢的藥物。"},{"en":"A patented cancer drug may be profitable because few companies can sell the same product.","zh":"有專利的癌症藥物可能有利可圖，因為很少公司能售賣相同產品。"},{"en":"When a drug is not profitable, companies may stop investing in promotion or research.","zh":"當藥物不再有利可圖，公司可能停止投資宣傳或研究。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when money affects medicine.","zh":"當金錢影響藥物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"support for further research","meaning":"對進一步研究的支持","examples":[{"en":"Jeffreys suggests support for further research into aspirin.","zh":"Jeffreys 建議支持對阿士匹靈的進一步研究。"},{"en":"Support for further research means help, funding, or encouragement for continued study.","zh":"support for further research 指為繼續研究提供幫助、資金或鼓勵。"},{"en":"A school may offer support for further research by giving students library access and teacher guidance.","zh":"學校可能透過提供圖書館使用權和老師指導，支持學生進一步研究。"},{"en":"Without support, useful questions may remain unanswered.","zh":"沒有支持，有用問題可能仍然得不到解答。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when more study is needed.","zh":"當需要更多研究時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"possible applications of the drug","meaning":"該藥物的可能用途","examples":[{"en":"Researchers may investigate possible applications of the drug.","zh":"研究人員可能調查該藥物的可能用途。"},{"en":"Possible applications of the drug are the potential ways the medicine could be used.","zh":"possible applications of the drug 指該藥物可能被使用的潛在方式。"},{"en":"Doctors may study possible applications of a painkiller in preventing other conditions.","zh":"醫生可能研究止痛藥在預防其他疾病方面的可能用途。"},{"en":"Investigating possible applications can reveal whether a drug has value beyond its original purpose.","zh":"調查可能用途可以揭示藥物是否有超出原本目的的價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a medicine may have more uses than expected.","zh":"當藥物可能有比預期更多用途時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 109 - Keep taking the tablets.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 110":[{"front":"Quiet roads ahead","meaning":"前方將有更寧靜的道路","examples":[{"en":"New road-building techniques may create quieter roads in the future.","zh":"新道路建設技術可能在未來創造更寧靜的道路。"},{"en":"Quiet roads ahead means roads may become less noisy because of new design or technology.","zh":"「Quiet roads ahead」意思是由於新設計或科技，道路可能變得較少噪音。"},{"en":"A family living near a highway may hope for quiet roads ahead if the government uses better surfaces.","zh":"住在高速公路附近的家庭，如果政府使用更好路面，可能期望前方將有更寧靜的道路。"},{"en":"If tyre noise can be reduced, people near busy roads may sleep and work more comfortably.","zh":"如果車胎噪音可以減少，住在繁忙道路附近的人可能睡得更好，工作也更舒服。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a future with less traffic noise, not fewer cars.","zh":"這個短語暗示未來交通噪音較少，而不是車輛較少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the roar of passing vehicles","meaning":"駛過車輛的轟鳴聲","examples":[{"en":"The roar of passing vehicles can disturb people living near busy roads.","zh":"駛過車輛的轟鳴聲會打擾住在繁忙道路附近的人。"},{"en":"The roar of passing vehicles means the loud, continuous noise made by cars, buses, and trucks as they go by.","zh":"「the roar of passing vehicles」意思是汽車、巴士和貨車駛過時發出的巨大連續噪音。"},{"en":"Students may find it hard to study if the roar of passing vehicles comes through the classroom windows.","zh":"如果駛過車輛的轟鳴聲從課室窗戶傳入，學生可能難以溫習。"},{"en":"If traffic is heavy all day, this constant roar can cause stress and tiredness.","zh":"如果交通整天繁忙，這種持續轟鳴聲會造成壓力和疲倦。"},{"en":"The phrase describes traffic noise as powerful and unpleasant.","zh":"這個短語把交通噪音描述成強烈而令人不快。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a thing of the past","meaning":"成為過去；不復存在","examples":[{"en":"Excessive road noise could soon become a thing of the past.","zh":"過量道路噪音可能很快成為過去。"},{"en":"A thing of the past is something that no longer exists or is no longer common.","zh":"「a thing of the past」是指不再存在或不再常見的事物。"},{"en":"Paper bus tickets may become a thing of the past when everyone uses electronic payment.","zh":"當人人使用電子支付，紙本巴士票可能成為過去。"},{"en":"If quieter road surfaces become common, loud traffic noise may gradually disappear.","zh":"如果較寧靜的路面變得普遍，嘈吵交通噪音可能逐漸消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something old that has been replaced by something better.","zh":"這個短語描述被更好事物取代的舊事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"noise produced by","meaning":"由……產生的噪音","examples":[{"en":"The noise produced by busy roads is a growing environmental problem.","zh":"由繁忙道路產生的噪音是日益嚴重的環境問題。"},{"en":"Noise produced by something is the sound that something creates.","zh":"「noise produced by」某物，是某物製造出來的聲音。"},{"en":"The noise produced by a construction site can disturb office workers nearby.","zh":"由建築地盤產生的噪音會打擾附近辦公室員工。"},{"en":"If the noise produced by traffic is constant, residents may suffer stress and poor sleep.","zh":"如果由交通產生的噪音持續不斷，居民可能承受壓力和睡眠欠佳。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of a sound.","zh":"這個短語指出聲音來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"busy roads","meaning":"繁忙道路","examples":[{"en":"People living near busy roads are regularly exposed to traffic noise.","zh":"住在繁忙道路附近的人經常接觸交通噪音。"},{"en":"Busy roads are roads with many vehicles using them throughout the day.","zh":"「busy roads」是整天有很多車輛使用的道路。"},{"en":"A school beside busy roads may need better windows to keep classrooms quiet.","zh":"位於繁忙道路旁的學校可能需要更好的窗戶，以保持課室安靜。"},{"en":"If traffic increases, busy roads can become noisier and more dangerous for pedestrians.","zh":"如果交通量增加，繁忙道路會變得更嘈吵，對行人也更危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes roads with heavy traffic.","zh":"這個短語描述交通繁重的道路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a growing problem","meaning":"日益嚴重的問題","examples":[{"en":"Road noise is becoming a growing problem around the world.","zh":"道路噪音正在世界各地成為日益嚴重的問題。"},{"en":"A growing problem is an issue that is becoming more serious or more common.","zh":"「a growing problem」是變得更嚴重或更常見的問題。"},{"en":"Screen addiction is a growing problem among students who sleep with their phones nearby.","zh":"對睡覺時把電話放在身邊的學生而言，屏幕成癮是日益嚴重的問題。"},{"en":"If more cars use the roads, traffic noise may grow into a larger public health issue.","zh":"如果更多汽車使用道路，交通噪音可能演變成更大的公共健康問題。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that a problem is getting worse, not staying the same.","zh":"這個短語警告問題正在惡化，而不是維持不變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"vehicle designers","meaning":"車輛設計師","examples":[{"en":"Vehicle designers have worked hard to reduce engine noise.","zh":"車輛設計師一直努力降低引擎噪音。"},{"en":"Vehicle designers are people who design cars, buses, trucks, or other forms of transport.","zh":"「vehicle designers」是設計汽車、巴士、貨車或其他交通工具的人。"},{"en":"Vehicle designers may improve seats, engines, safety systems, and fuel efficiency.","zh":"車輛設計師可能改善座椅、引擎、安全系統和燃油效率。"},{"en":"If designers make engines quieter, tyre noise becomes a more noticeable problem.","zh":"如果設計師令引擎更安靜，車胎噪音就變得更明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to specialists who shape how vehicles work and feel.","zh":"這個短語指塑造車輛運作和感覺的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"work hard to","meaning":"努力去……","examples":[{"en":"Engineers have worked hard to make vehicles quieter.","zh":"工程師一直努力去令車輛更安靜。"},{"en":"To work hard to do something means to put serious effort into achieving it.","zh":"「work hard to」做某事，意思是投入認真努力去達成它。"},{"en":"Students work hard to improve grammar when they practise corrections every week.","zh":"學生每星期練習改錯時，就是努力改善文法。"},{"en":"If engineers work hard on noise reduction, road users and residents may benefit.","zh":"如果工程師努力研究降噪，道路使用者和居民都可能受惠。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises effort and persistence.","zh":"這個短語強調努力和堅持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"quieten engines","meaning":"降低引擎噪音","examples":[{"en":"Vehicle manufacturers have developed technology to quieten engines.","zh":"車輛製造商已研發科技來降低引擎噪音。"},{"en":"To quieten engines means to reduce the noise made by engines.","zh":"「quieten engines」意思是減少引擎發出的噪音。"},{"en":"A bus company may quieten engines to make early morning routes less disturbing.","zh":"巴士公司可能降低引擎噪音，使清晨路線較少打擾居民。"},{"en":"If engines become quieter, other sources of vehicle noise become easier to hear.","zh":"如果引擎變得更安靜，其他車輛噪音來源就更容易聽見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making engines less loud.","zh":"這個短語描述令引擎不那麼嘈吵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be less successful elsewhere","meaning":"在其他方面較不成功","examples":[{"en":"Designers have been less successful elsewhere in controlling vehicle noise.","zh":"設計師在控制車輛噪音的其他方面較不成功。"},{"en":"To be less successful elsewhere means to achieve poorer results in another area or aspect.","zh":"「be less successful elsewhere」意思是在另一範疇或方面取得較差成果。"},{"en":"A student may be strong in reading but less successful elsewhere, such as speaking.","zh":"學生可能閱讀很強，但在說話等其他方面較不成功。"},{"en":"If engine noise is reduced but tyre noise remains high, progress is uneven.","zh":"如果引擎噪音減少但車胎噪音仍高，進展就不平均。"},{"en":"The phrase compares success in one area with weaker success in another.","zh":"這個短語比較某方面成功與另一方面較弱的成果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sound created by tyres","meaning":"車胎產生的聲音","examples":[{"en":"The sound created by tyres is now a major source of road noise.","zh":"車胎產生的聲音現在是道路噪音的主要來源。"},{"en":"Sound created by tyres means noise produced when tyres roll, press, and vibrate against the road surface.","zh":"「sound created by tyres」是車胎在路面上滾動、受壓和震動時產生的噪音。"},{"en":"Drivers may notice the sound created by tyres more clearly on rough concrete roads.","zh":"司機在粗糙混凝土路上可能更清楚注意到車胎產生的聲音。"},{"en":"If engines are quiet, tyre sound can become the main noise heard by residents.","zh":"如果引擎安靜，車胎聲就可能成為居民聽到的主要噪音。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies tyre-road contact as the noise source.","zh":"這個短語指出車胎與路面接觸是噪音來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the road surface","meaning":"路面","examples":[{"en":"Tyres create noise when they make contact with the road surface.","zh":"車胎與路面接觸時會產生噪音。"},{"en":"The road surface is the top layer of a road that vehicles drive on.","zh":"「the road surface」是車輛行駛其上的道路最上層。"},{"en":"A smooth road surface makes cycling more comfortable than a cracked one.","zh":"平滑路面比裂開路面令踩單車更舒服。"},{"en":"If the road surface is rough, tyres may vibrate and produce more noise.","zh":"如果路面粗糙，車胎可能震動並產生更多噪音。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the part of the road that directly touches tyres.","zh":"這個短語指道路中直接接觸車胎的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"account for more than half","meaning":"佔超過一半","examples":[{"en":"Tyre noise accounts for more than half of the noise produced by vehicles.","zh":"車胎噪音佔車輛產生噪音超過一半。"},{"en":"To account for more than half means to make up over 50 percent of the total.","zh":"「account for more than half」意思是構成總數的百分之五十以上。"},{"en":"Rent may account for more than half of a student’s monthly spending.","zh":"租金可能佔學生每月開支超過一半。"},{"en":"If tyre noise forms most vehicle noise, road surfaces become an important target for improvement.","zh":"如果車胎噪音構成大部分車輛噪音，路面就成為重要改善目標。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large share of a whole.","zh":"這個短語描述整體中的大比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"road building","meaning":"道路建設","examples":[{"en":"Road building is continuing rapidly in many parts of the world.","zh":"道路建設在世界許多地方繼續快速進行。"},{"en":"Road building is the construction of new roads or the improvement of existing ones.","zh":"「road building」是興建新道路或改善現有道路。"},{"en":"A growing town may need road building to connect new housing estates with schools and shops.","zh":"發展中的城鎮可能需要道路建設，把新屋苑與學校和商店連接起來。"},{"en":"If road building increases without noise control, more communities may suffer traffic noise.","zh":"如果道路建設增加而沒有噪音控制，更多社區可能受交通噪音困擾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes infrastructure development for transport.","zh":"這個短語描述交通基礎設施發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"car sales","meaning":"汽車銷售量","examples":[{"en":"Increasing car sales contribute to the global problem of traffic noise.","zh":"不斷增加的汽車銷售量促成全球交通噪音問題。"},{"en":"Car sales are the number of cars sold to customers in a period or market.","zh":"「car sales」是某時期或市場中售予顧客的汽車數量。"},{"en":"Car sales often rise when incomes increase and public transport is inconvenient.","zh":"當收入上升而公共交通不方便時，汽車銷售量常會增加。"},{"en":"If car sales grow quickly, roads may become busier and noisier.","zh":"如果汽車銷售量快速增長，道路可能變得更繁忙和更嘈吵。"},{"en":"The phrase connects consumer demand with transport pressure.","zh":"這個短語把消費需求與交通壓力連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"continue to boom","meaning":"持續蓬勃增長","examples":[{"en":"Road construction and car sales continue to boom in several regions.","zh":"道路建設和汽車銷售在幾個地區持續蓬勃增長。"},{"en":"To continue to boom means to keep growing very quickly and strongly.","zh":"「continue to boom」意思是繼續非常快速而強勁地增長。"},{"en":"Online shopping may continue to boom if delivery remains fast and cheap.","zh":"如果送貨仍然快速便宜，網上購物可能持續蓬勃增長。"},{"en":"If car sales continue to boom, traffic noise may become harder to control.","zh":"如果汽車銷售持續蓬勃增長，交通噪音可能更難控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rapid ongoing growth.","zh":"這個短語描述持續快速增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"particularly in","meaning":"尤其在……","examples":[{"en":"The problem is growing particularly quickly in Asia and the US.","zh":"這個問題尤其在亞洲和美國增長得很快。"},{"en":"Particularly in means especially in a certain place, group, or situation.","zh":"「particularly in」意思是尤其在某地方、群體或情況中。"},{"en":"Housing costs are high in many cities, particularly in areas near railway stations.","zh":"許多城市住屋成本高，尤其在靠近鐵路站的地區。"},{"en":"If road building grows especially fast in some regions, noise problems may appear there first.","zh":"如果道路建設在某些地區特別快速增長，噪音問題可能先在那裡出現。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a specific area more strongly than others.","zh":"這個短語比其他地方更強調某一特定範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"turn into a global issue","meaning":"演變成全球問題","examples":[{"en":"Road noise is turning into a global issue.","zh":"道路噪音正演變成全球問題。"},{"en":"To turn into a global issue means to become a problem affecting many countries or regions.","zh":"「turn into a global issue」意思是變成影響許多國家或地區的問題。"},{"en":"Plastic waste turned into a global issue when it began appearing in oceans worldwide.","zh":"當塑膠廢物開始出現在全球海洋中，它演變成全球問題。"},{"en":"If many countries build more roads and buy more cars, traffic noise can spread internationally.","zh":"如果許多國家興建更多道路並購買更多汽車，交通噪音可以在國際間擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a local problem becoming worldwide.","zh":"這個短語描述本地問題變成全球問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"According to the World Health Organization, prolonged traffic noise can damage health.","zh":"根據世界衞生組織，長時間交通噪音會損害健康。"},{"en":"According to means based on what a person, organisation, report, or source says.","zh":"「according to」意思是根據某人、機構、報告或來源所說。"},{"en":"According to the timetable, the last train leaves at midnight.","zh":"根據時間表，尾班火車午夜開出。"},{"en":"If an international health body gives a warning, governments may take the issue more seriously.","zh":"如果國際健康機構發出警告，政府可能更認真看待問題。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the source of information.","zh":"這個短語引入資料來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"World Health Organization","meaning":"世界衞生組織","examples":[{"en":"The World Health Organization has warned about the effects of traffic noise.","zh":"世界衞生組織曾警告交通噪音的影響。"},{"en":"The World Health Organization is an international public health organisation that advises countries on health issues.","zh":"「World Health Organization」是就健康議題向各國提供建議的國際公共衞生組織。"},{"en":"Governments may refer to the World Health Organization during disease outbreaks.","zh":"政府在疾病爆發期間可能參考世界衞生組織。"},{"en":"If the organisation warns about noise, the issue is not just an inconvenience but a health concern.","zh":"如果該組織警告噪音問題，這問題就不只是令人不便，而是健康關注。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major global health authority.","zh":"這個短語指出主要全球健康權威機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"exposure to noise","meaning":"接觸噪音","examples":[{"en":"Long-term exposure to noise can cause stress-related health problems.","zh":"長期接觸噪音會造成與壓力有關的健康問題。"},{"en":"Exposure to noise means being in contact with sound, especially loud or repeated sound.","zh":"「exposure to noise」意思是接觸聲音，尤其是巨大或反覆出現的聲音。"},{"en":"Factory workers may wear ear protection because of daily exposure to noise.","zh":"工廠工人可能因每日接觸噪音而佩戴耳罩。"},{"en":"If exposure to noise continues for years, sleep and concentration may suffer.","zh":"如果接觸噪音持續多年，睡眠和專注力可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes contact with noise over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間接觸噪音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"road traffic","meaning":"道路交通","examples":[{"en":"Noise from road traffic affects many people living in cities.","zh":"來自道路交通的噪音影響許多住在城市的人。"},{"en":"Road traffic means cars, buses, trucks, motorcycles, and other vehicles moving on roads.","zh":"「road traffic」是道路上行駛的汽車、巴士、貨車、電單車和其他車輛。"},{"en":"Road traffic is usually heavier near schools during morning drop-off times.","zh":"早上送學生上學時，學校附近道路交通通常較繁忙。"},{"en":"If road traffic increases, air pollution and noise may rise together.","zh":"如果道路交通增加，空氣污染和噪音可能一起上升。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to vehicles using roads, not pedestrians.","zh":"這個短語指使用道路的車輛，而不是行人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"over long periods","meaning":"長時間","examples":[{"en":"Exposure to loud traffic over long periods may damage people’s health.","zh":"長時間接觸嘈吵交通可能損害人們健康。"},{"en":"Over long periods means during a long time, often months or years.","zh":"「over long periods」意思是在很長時間內，通常是數月或數年。"},{"en":"Poor posture over long periods can cause back pain.","zh":"長時間姿勢不良可以造成背痛。"},{"en":"If residents hear loud road noise for years, their stress levels may rise.","zh":"如果居民多年聽到巨大道路噪音，其壓力水平可能上升。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises long-term exposure rather than one short event.","zh":"這個短語強調長期接觸，而不是一次短暫事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"Persistent traffic noise can lead to serious health problems.","zh":"持續交通噪音會導致嚴重健康問題。"},{"en":"To lead to something means to cause it or make it happen.","zh":"「lead to」某事，意思是造成它或令它發生。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can lead to poor concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致上課專注力差。"},{"en":"If noise causes stress every day, it may lead to illness over time.","zh":"如果噪音每天造成壓力，長遠可能導致疾病。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a cause with a result.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stress-related health problems","meaning":"與壓力有關的健康問題","examples":[{"en":"Road traffic noise may cause stress-related health problems.","zh":"道路交通噪音可能造成與壓力有關的健康問題。"},{"en":"Stress-related health problems are illnesses or symptoms caused or worsened by long-term stress.","zh":"「stress-related health problems」是由長期壓力造成或惡化的疾病或症狀。"},{"en":"Headaches, poor sleep, and high blood pressure can be stress-related health problems.","zh":"頭痛、睡眠欠佳和高血壓都可以是與壓力有關的健康問題。"},{"en":"If noise prevents people from resting, stress may build up and affect the body.","zh":"如果噪音阻止人們休息，壓力可能累積並影響身體。"},{"en":"The phrase links mental pressure with physical health.","zh":"這個短語把精神壓力與身體健康連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"exceed a certain threshold","meaning":"超過某個臨界水平","examples":[{"en":"Protective measures may be required when traffic noise exceeds a certain threshold.","zh":"當交通噪音超過某個臨界水平時，可能需要保護措施。"},{"en":"To exceed a certain threshold means to go beyond a fixed limit or level.","zh":"「exceed a certain threshold」意思是超過固定限制或水平。"},{"en":"If a student’s temperature exceeds a certain threshold, the school may ask them to go home.","zh":"如果學生體溫超過某個臨界水平，學校可能要求他回家。"},{"en":"If noise passes a safe limit, authorities may have to take action.","zh":"如果噪音超過安全限度，當局可能必須採取行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes crossing a boundary where something becomes serious.","zh":"這個短語描述跨過某界線後事情變得嚴重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"road builders","meaning":"道路建造商","examples":[{"en":"Road builders sometimes have to install costly noise-control measures.","zh":"道路建造商有時必須安裝昂貴的噪音控制措施。"},{"en":"Road builders are companies, engineers, or workers who construct and repair roads.","zh":"「road builders」是建造和維修道路的公司、工程師或工人。"},{"en":"Road builders may close lanes at night to resurface a highway safely.","zh":"道路建造商可能在夜間封閉行車線，以安全重鋪高速公路。"},{"en":"If roads create too much noise, builders may need extra designs to protect residents.","zh":"如果道路製造太多噪音，建造商可能需要額外設計來保護居民。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people or organisations involved in road construction.","zh":"這個短語指參與道路建設的人或機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"spend money doing something","meaning":"花費金錢做某事","examples":[{"en":"Authorities may have to spend money erecting sound barriers.","zh":"當局可能必須花錢興建隔音屏障。"},{"en":"To spend money doing something means to use money for that activity.","zh":"「spend money doing something」意思是把金錢用於該活動。"},{"en":"Parents may spend money buying extra books if a child enjoys reading.","zh":"如果孩子喜歡閱讀，父母可能花錢買額外書本。"},{"en":"If road noise is high, governments may need to spend money on protection rather than other projects.","zh":"如果道路噪音很高，政府可能需要花錢做保護措施，而不是其他項目。"},{"en":"The phrase connects cost with an action.","zh":"這個短語把成本與行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"erect sound barriers","meaning":"興建隔音屏障","examples":[{"en":"Road builders erect sound barriers beside particularly noisy roads.","zh":"道路建造商在特別嘈吵的道路旁興建隔音屏障。"},{"en":"To erect sound barriers means to build walls or structures that block or reduce noise.","zh":"「erect sound barriers」意思是建造阻隔或減少噪音的牆或結構。"},{"en":"A railway company may erect sound barriers near homes beside train tracks.","zh":"鐵路公司可能在靠近鐵路的住宅旁興建隔音屏障。"},{"en":"If a road is too noisy, barriers can reduce the sound reaching nearby residents.","zh":"如果道路太嘈吵，屏障可以減少傳到附近居民的聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes building physical noise protection.","zh":"這個短語描述建造實體噪音保護設施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sound barriers","meaning":"隔音屏障","examples":[{"en":"Sound barriers can reduce the amount of traffic noise reaching nearby homes.","zh":"隔音屏障可以減少到達附近住宅的交通噪音量。"},{"en":"Sound barriers are walls, screens, or structures built to block noise.","zh":"「sound barriers」是為阻隔噪音而建的牆、屏風或結構。"},{"en":"A school next to a highway may need sound barriers to keep classrooms quieter.","zh":"高速公路旁的學校可能需要隔音屏障，以保持課室較安靜。"},{"en":"If sound barriers are high and well placed, they can reduce noise for nearby residents.","zh":"如果隔音屏障夠高且位置合適，可以為附近居民減少噪音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes structures designed for noise control.","zh":"這個短語描述用於噪音控制的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"install double glazing","meaning":"安裝雙層玻璃窗","examples":[{"en":"Residents may install double glazing to reduce noise inside their homes.","zh":"居民可能安裝雙層玻璃窗，以減少家中噪音。"},{"en":"To install double glazing means to fit windows with two layers of glass.","zh":"「install double glazing」意思是安裝有兩層玻璃的窗戶。"},{"en":"A family near an airport may install double glazing to sleep better at night.","zh":"機場附近的家庭可能安裝雙層玻璃窗，以在晚上睡得更好。"},{"en":"If outside noise cannot be stopped, better windows can reduce noise indoors.","zh":"如果外面噪音不能停止，更好的窗戶可以減少室內噪音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adding special windows for insulation or noise control.","zh":"這個短語描述加裝特殊窗戶來隔熱或隔音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"double glazing","meaning":"雙層玻璃窗","examples":[{"en":"Double glazing can help protect residents from environmental noise.","zh":"雙層玻璃窗有助保護居民免受環境噪音影響。"},{"en":"Double glazing is a type of window with two panes of glass and a space between them.","zh":"「double glazing」是一種有兩片玻璃且中間有空隙的窗戶。"},{"en":"Homes in cold countries often use double glazing to keep heat indoors.","zh":"寒冷國家的住宅常使用雙層玻璃窗來保暖。"},{"en":"If a window has two layers, sound and heat pass through less easily.","zh":"如果窗戶有兩層，聲音和熱力較不容易通過。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a window design that improves insulation and quietness.","zh":"這個短語描述改善隔熱和安靜程度的窗戶設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"blighted homes","meaning":"受噪音嚴重困擾的住宅","examples":[{"en":"Some blighted homes require additional protection from road noise.","zh":"一些受噪音嚴重困擾的住宅需要額外保護。"},{"en":"Blighted homes are homes badly affected by an unpleasant problem such as noise, pollution, or poor surroundings.","zh":"「blighted homes」是被噪音、污染或惡劣環境等問題嚴重影響的住宅。"},{"en":"Houses beside a busy flyover may become blighted homes if traffic noise is constant.","zh":"如果交通噪音持續，高架橋旁的房屋可能成為受困擾住宅。"},{"en":"If a home is blighted by noise, its residents may suffer and its value may fall.","zh":"如果住宅受噪音困擾，居民可能受苦，物業價值也可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes homes damaged in quality by their environment.","zh":"這個短語描述因環境而質素受損的住宅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"become harder to sell","meaning":"變得較難出售","examples":[{"en":"Houses become harder to sell when environmental noise is high.","zh":"當環境噪音高，房屋會變得較難出售。"},{"en":"To become harder to sell means to become less attractive to buyers.","zh":"「become harder to sell」意思是對買家變得較不吸引。"},{"en":"A flat without natural light may become harder to sell than one with open views.","zh":"沒有自然光的單位可能比有開揚景觀的單位較難出售。"},{"en":"If road noise is constant, buyers may offer lower prices or avoid the property.","zh":"如果道路噪音持續，買家可能出價較低或避開該物業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reduced market appeal.","zh":"這個短語描述市場吸引力下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"environmental noise","meaning":"環境噪音","examples":[{"en":"High levels of environmental noise can reduce property values.","zh":"高水平環境噪音可以降低物業價值。"},{"en":"Environmental noise is unwanted sound from surroundings such as traffic, aircraft, factories, or construction.","zh":"「environmental noise」是來自周遭環境的不想要聲音，例如交通、飛機、工廠或建築工程。"},{"en":"A hospital near a construction site may suffer from environmental noise.","zh":"建築地盤附近的醫院可能受到環境噪音影響。"},{"en":"If environmental noise is constant, people may feel stressed even inside their homes.","zh":"如果環境噪音持續不斷，人們即使在家中也可能感到壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes noise pollution in daily surroundings.","zh":"這個短語描述日常周遭環境中的噪音污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"efficient or productive at work","meaning":"工作效率高或有生產力","examples":[{"en":"People may become less efficient or productive at work because of noise.","zh":"人們可能因噪音而在工作上變得較低效率或較少產出。"},{"en":"Efficient or productive at work means able to finish tasks well, quickly, and with useful results.","zh":"「efficient or productive at work」意思是能夠良好、快速並有成果地完成工作。"},{"en":"An employee is more productive at work when the office is quiet and organised.","zh":"當辦公室安靜有序，員工工作效率會更高。"},{"en":"If traffic noise interrupts concentration, workers may complete less and make more mistakes.","zh":"如果交通噪音打斷專注，工人可能完成較少工作並犯更多錯。"},{"en":"The phrase connects working conditions with performance.","zh":"這個短語把工作環境與表現連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"densely populated countries","meaning":"人口最稠密的國家","examples":[{"en":"The Netherlands is one of the most densely populated countries in the world.","zh":"荷蘭是世界上人口最稠密的國家之一。"},{"en":"Densely populated countries are countries with many people living in a relatively small area.","zh":"「densely populated countries」是許多人生活在相對細小面積內的國家。"},{"en":"In densely populated countries, roads, homes, schools, and businesses are often close together.","zh":"在人口稠密國家，道路、住宅、學校和商業區通常很接近。"},{"en":"If a country is densely populated, traffic noise can affect many residents at once.","zh":"如果一個國家人口稠密，交通噪音可以同時影響許多居民。"},{"en":"The phrase describes high population concentration.","zh":"這個短語描述高度人口集中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"work to develop","meaning":"致力研發","examples":[{"en":"Dutch researchers are working to develop quieter road surfaces.","zh":"荷蘭研究人員正致力研發較寧靜的路面。"},{"en":"To work to develop something means to make continued efforts to design or improve it.","zh":"「work to develop」某物，意思是持續努力設計或改善它。"},{"en":"Teachers may work to develop better reading materials for weaker students.","zh":"老師可能致力研發更適合較弱學生的閱讀材料。"},{"en":"If researchers keep testing new surfaces, they may find ways to lower tyre noise.","zh":"如果研究人員持續測試新路面，他們可能找到降低車胎噪音的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active research and improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述積極研究和改進。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"techniques for silencing roads","meaning":"降低道路噪音的技術","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are developing techniques for silencing roads.","zh":"研究人員正在研發降低道路噪音的技術。"},{"en":"Techniques for silencing roads are methods used to reduce noise from road surfaces and traffic.","zh":"「techniques for silencing roads」是用來減少路面和交通噪音的方法。"},{"en":"A city may test techniques for silencing roads near hospitals and schools first.","zh":"城市可能先在醫院和學校附近測試降低道路噪音的技術。"},{"en":"If these techniques work, residents may hear less tyre vibration and traffic roar.","zh":"如果這些技術有效，居民可能聽到較少車胎震動和交通轟鳴。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical methods for making roads quieter.","zh":"這個短語描述令道路更安靜的實用方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the next five years","meaning":"在未來五年間","examples":[{"en":"The government hopes to achieve its target in the next five years.","zh":"政府希望在未來五年間達成目標。"},{"en":"In the next five years means during the five-year period starting from now or from the time mentioned.","zh":"「in the next five years」意思是在由現在或所提時間開始的五年期間。"},{"en":"A school may plan to renovate all classrooms in the next five years.","zh":"學校可能計劃在未來五年間翻新所有課室。"},{"en":"If the government has a five-year target, researchers must test and apply the technology quickly.","zh":"如果政府有五年目標，研究人員必須快速測試和應用技術。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a medium-term future time frame.","zh":"這個短語提供中期未來時間範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"aim to have reduced","meaning":"目標是屆時已降低……","examples":[{"en":"The Dutch government aims to have reduced road noise significantly.","zh":"荷蘭政府的目標是屆時已大幅降低道路噪音。"},{"en":"To aim to have reduced something means to set a target that the reduction will already be achieved by a future time.","zh":"「aim to have reduced」某物，意思是設定目標，希望到未來某時已完成減少。"},{"en":"A school may aim to have reduced paper use by half before the next academic year.","zh":"學校可能目標是在下一學年前已把用紙量減半。"},{"en":"If the target is clear, engineers can measure whether noise has fallen enough.","zh":"如果目標清楚，工程師就能量度噪音是否已足夠下降。"},{"en":"The phrase combines a goal with a completed future result.","zh":"這個短語結合目標和未來完成的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"noise levels","meaning":"噪音水平","examples":[{"en":"The project aims to reduce noise levels from road surfaces.","zh":"該項目旨在降低路面造成的噪音水平。"},{"en":"Noise levels are measured amounts of sound, usually showing how loud something is.","zh":"「noise levels」是量度出來的聲音大小，通常顯示某物有多嘈吵。"},{"en":"A library may monitor noise levels to keep study areas quiet.","zh":"圖書館可能監察噪音水平，以保持自修區安靜。"},{"en":"If road noise levels fall, nearby homes and workplaces may become more comfortable.","zh":"如果道路噪音水平下降，附近住宅和工作場所可能更舒適。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the degree or amount of noise.","zh":"這個短語描述噪音的程度或數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reduce something by six decibels","meaning":"將……降低六分貝","examples":[{"en":"The government aims to reduce road noise by six decibels overall.","zh":"政府目標是整體將道路噪音降低六分貝。"},{"en":"To reduce something by six decibels means to lower measured sound by six units on the decibel scale.","zh":"「reduce something by six decibels」意思是在分貝尺度上把量度聲音降低六個單位。"},{"en":"A factory may reduce machine noise by six decibels after installing better covers.","zh":"工廠安裝更好外罩後，可能將機器噪音降低六分貝。"},{"en":"If road noise falls by six decibels, residents may notice a real improvement.","zh":"如果道路噪音下降六分貝，居民可能感到實質改善。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a precise noise-reduction target.","zh":"這個短語提供精確降噪目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"decibels","meaning":"分貝","examples":[{"en":"Road noise is measured in decibels.","zh":"道路噪音以分貝量度。"},{"en":"Decibels are units used to measure how loud a sound is.","zh":"「decibels」是用來量度聲音有多大的單位。"},{"en":"A phone app may show classroom noise in decibels during a science activity.","zh":"在科學活動中，手機應用程式可能顯示課室噪音分貝。"},{"en":"If decibel levels rise, people may feel more disturbed by the sound.","zh":"如果分貝水平上升，人們可能更受聲音打擾。"},{"en":"The word is used when discussing measured sound intensity.","zh":"這個詞用於討論量度出來的聲音強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mechanical engineer","meaning":"機械工程師","examples":[{"en":"Ard Kuijpers is a Dutch mechanical engineer.","zh":"Ard Kuijpers 是一位荷蘭機械工程師。"},{"en":"A mechanical engineer designs, tests, or improves machines, mechanical systems, and moving parts.","zh":"「mechanical engineer」是設計、測試或改良機器、機械系統和活動部件的工程師。"},{"en":"A mechanical engineer may design lifts, engines, factory machines, or vehicle parts.","zh":"機械工程師可能設計升降機、引擎、工廠機器或車輛零件。"},{"en":"If road noise depends on vibration and movement, mechanical engineering can help solve it.","zh":"如果道路噪音取決於震動和移動，機械工程可以幫助解決。"},{"en":"The phrase names an engineering specialist.","zh":"這個短語指出一種工程專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"come up with","meaning":"想出；提出","examples":[{"en":"Kuijpers has come up with a radical road-building idea.","zh":"Kuijpers 想出了一個突破常規的道路建設構思。"},{"en":"To come up with an idea means to think of it or invent it.","zh":"「come up with」一個想法，意思是想到或發明它。"},{"en":"A student may come up with a new way to remember difficult vocabulary.","zh":"學生可能想出記住困難詞彙的新方法。"},{"en":"If engineers come up with better designs, old traffic problems may become easier to solve.","zh":"如果工程師提出更好設計，舊有交通問題可能變得較容易解決。"},{"en":"The phrase describes producing an idea or solution.","zh":"這個短語描述產生想法或解決方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"promising and radical ideas","meaning":"有前景而突破常規的構思","examples":[{"en":"His design is considered one of the most promising and radical ideas.","zh":"他的設計被視為最有前景而突破常規的構思之一。"},{"en":"Promising and radical ideas are ideas that seem likely to succeed and are very different from usual methods.","zh":"「promising and radical ideas」是看似有成功可能，並且與常規方法非常不同的想法。"},{"en":"A school’s plan to replace long lectures with project learning may be promising and radical.","zh":"學校用專題學習取代長篇講課的計劃，可能是有前景而突破常規的構思。"},{"en":"If an idea is both promising and radical, it may attract attention but also need testing.","zh":"如果一個想法既有前景又突破常規，它可能吸引注意，但也需要測試。"},{"en":"The phrase combines hope for success with bold change.","zh":"這個短語結合成功希望與大膽改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"set out to tackle","meaning":"着手處理","examples":[{"en":"Kuijpers set out to tackle the main causes of tyre noise.","zh":"Kuijpers 着手處理車胎噪音的主要成因。"},{"en":"To set out to tackle something means to begin trying seriously to solve a problem.","zh":"「set out to tackle」某事，意思是開始認真嘗試解決某問題。"},{"en":"A teacher may set out to tackle weak grammar by giving short daily exercises.","zh":"老師可能透過每日短練習着手處理薄弱文法。"},{"en":"If an engineer identifies the main cause of noise, they can begin solving it directly.","zh":"如果工程師找出噪音主因，就可以開始直接解決它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes starting a focused attempt to deal with a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述開始專注處理問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"surface texture","meaning":"表面質感","examples":[{"en":"Surface texture is one of the factors affecting road noise.","zh":"表面質感是影響道路噪音的因素之一。"},{"en":"Surface texture means how smooth, rough, bumpy, or patterned the top of a surface feels or looks.","zh":"「surface texture」意思是表面最上層感覺或看起來有多平滑、粗糙、凹凸或有紋理。"},{"en":"A desk with rough surface texture may make handwriting less neat.","zh":"表面質感粗糙的書桌可能令書寫較不整齊。"},{"en":"If road surface texture is rough, tyres may vibrate and create more sound.","zh":"如果路面質感粗糙，車胎可能震動並產生更多聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the feel and pattern of a surface.","zh":"這個短語描述表面的觸感和紋理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"surface hardness","meaning":"表面硬度","examples":[{"en":"The hardness of a road surface influences tyre vibration.","zh":"路面的硬度影響車胎震動。"},{"en":"Surface hardness means how firm or resistant a surface is when pressure is applied.","zh":"「surface hardness」意思是表面受壓時有多堅硬或抗壓。"},{"en":"A soft running track has lower surface hardness than a concrete pavement.","zh":"軟身跑道的表面硬度低於混凝土行人路。"},{"en":"If a road is too hard, tyres may vibrate more strongly when passing over it.","zh":"如果道路太硬，車胎駛過時可能震動得更強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how hard the top layer of a material is.","zh":"這個短語描述材料最上層有多硬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ability to absorb sound","meaning":"吸收聲音的能力","examples":[{"en":"The road’s ability to absorb sound is central to the new design.","zh":"道路吸收聲音的能力是新設計的核心。"},{"en":"Ability to absorb sound means the capacity to take in sound energy instead of reflecting it back loudly.","zh":"「ability to absorb sound」意思是吸收聲能而不是大聲反射回去的能力。"},{"en":"Thick curtains improve a room’s ability to absorb sound during music practice.","zh":"厚窗簾提高房間在音樂練習期間吸收聲音的能力。"},{"en":"If a road absorbs sound well, less noise travels to nearby homes.","zh":"如果道路能有效吸收聲音，較少噪音會傳到附近住宅。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how effectively a material reduces noise.","zh":"這個短語描述材料減少噪音的效能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the rougher…, the more likely…","meaning":"越……，就越可能……","examples":[{"en":"The rougher the road surface is, the more likely a tyre is to vibrate.","zh":"路面越粗糙，車胎就越可能震動。"},{"en":"The rougher…, the more likely… means that as one condition increases, another result becomes more probable.","zh":"「the rougher…, the more likely…」意思是一個條件越強，另一結果就越可能發生。"},{"en":"The harder a test is, the more likely students are to need extra practice.","zh":"測驗越困難，學生就越可能需要額外練習。"},{"en":"If a surface becomes rougher, tyres hit more tiny bumps and vibrate more.","zh":"如果表面變得越粗糙，車胎撞上更多細小凹凸，震動就更多。"},{"en":"This structure clearly shows a cause-and-result relationship.","zh":"這個結構清楚顯示因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"tyre vibration","meaning":"車胎震動","examples":[{"en":"Tyre vibration creates a considerable amount of road noise.","zh":"車胎震動產生相當大量道路噪音。"},{"en":"Tyre vibration is the shaking movement of a tyre as it rolls over a surface.","zh":"「tyre vibration」是車胎在表面上滾動時的搖動。"},{"en":"Drivers may feel tyre vibration through the steering wheel on a rough road.","zh":"司機在粗糙路面上可能透過軚盤感到車胎震動。"},{"en":"If tyres vibrate more, they can produce more noise and reduce comfort.","zh":"如果車胎震動更多，它們會產生更多噪音並降低舒適度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a physical movement that creates sound.","zh":"這個短語描述產生聲音的物理移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"eliminate bumps","meaning":"消除凹凸不平","examples":[{"en":"Road builders use heavy rollers to eliminate bumps in fresh asphalt.","zh":"道路建造商使用重型壓路機來消除新瀝青中的凹凸不平。"},{"en":"To eliminate bumps means to remove raised or uneven parts from a surface.","zh":"「eliminate bumps」意思是移除表面凸起或不平部分。"},{"en":"A carpenter may sand a wooden desk to eliminate bumps before painting it.","zh":"木匠可能在髹漆前打磨木桌，以消除凹凸不平。"},{"en":"If bumps remain in a road, tyres may vibrate and create extra noise.","zh":"如果道路上仍有凹凸，車胎可能震動並產生額外噪音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a surface smoother.","zh":"這個短語描述令表面更平滑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"freshly laid asphalt","meaning":"剛鋪設的瀝青","examples":[{"en":"Heavy rollers are normally used on freshly laid asphalt.","zh":"重型壓路機通常用於剛鋪設的瀝青上。"},{"en":"Freshly laid asphalt is asphalt that has just been placed on a road surface and has not fully cooled or hardened.","zh":"「freshly laid asphalt」是剛放在路面上，尚未完全冷卻或硬化的瀝青。"},{"en":"Drivers may be asked to avoid freshly laid asphalt until road workers finish the job.","zh":"司機可能被要求避開剛鋪設的瀝青，直到道路工人完成工程。"},{"en":"If fresh asphalt is not flattened properly, the road may become uneven.","zh":"如果新瀝青沒有正確壓平，道路可能變得不平。"},{"en":"The phrase describes new road material immediately after placement.","zh":"這個短語描述鋪放後不久的新道路材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"heavy rollers","meaning":"重型壓路機","examples":[{"en":"Heavy rollers flatten the asphalt after it has been laid.","zh":"重型壓路機在瀝青鋪好後把它壓平。"},{"en":"Heavy rollers are large road machines that press down surfaces to make them flat and firm.","zh":"「heavy rollers」是大型道路機器，用來壓實表面，使其平坦堅固。"},{"en":"People often see heavy rollers at roadworks after hot asphalt has been spread.","zh":"人們常在熱瀝青鋪開後的道路工程中看見重型壓路機。"},{"en":"If heavy rollers are used well, the road surface becomes smoother and stronger.","zh":"如果重型壓路機使用得好，路面會更平滑、更堅固。"},{"en":"The phrase names a machine used in road construction.","zh":"這個短語指出道路建設中使用的機器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"develop a method of","meaning":"研發……的方法","examples":[{"en":"Kuijpers developed a new method of road construction.","zh":"Kuijpers 研發了一種新的道路建設方法。"},{"en":"To develop a method of doing something means to create or improve a systematic way to do it.","zh":"「develop a method of」做某事，意思是創造或改善一套有系統的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may develop a method of teaching vocabulary through pictures and examples.","zh":"老師可能研發透過圖片和例子教授詞彙的方法。"},{"en":"If an old method cannot reduce noise enough, engineers may develop a new one.","zh":"如果舊方法不能足夠降低噪音，工程師可能研發新方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating a practical procedure.","zh":"這個短語描述創造實際程序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the ultimate quiet road","meaning":"極致寧靜的道路","examples":[{"en":"The engineer hopes his design will create the ultimate quiet road.","zh":"這位工程師希望其設計能創造極致寧靜的道路。"},{"en":"The ultimate quiet road means the best possible road design for reducing traffic noise.","zh":"「the ultimate quiet road」意思是在減少交通噪音方面最理想的道路設計。"},{"en":"A city planner may dream of the ultimate quiet road outside hospitals and schools.","zh":"城市規劃師可能夢想在醫院和學校外有極致寧靜的道路。"},{"en":"If a surface reduces vibration, absorbs sound, and drains water, it may come close to this ideal.","zh":"如果路面能減少震動、吸收聲音並排水，它可能接近這個理想。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an ideal version of a quiet road.","zh":"這個短語描述寧靜道路的理想版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a special mould","meaning":"特製模具","examples":[{"en":"The road surface is formed inside a special mould.","zh":"路面在特製模具內形成。"},{"en":"A special mould is a shaped container or frame used to give material a particular form.","zh":"「a special mould」是用來令材料形成特定形狀的容器或框架。"},{"en":"A bakery may use a special mould to make cakes in the shape of animals.","zh":"麵包店可能用特製模具製作動物形狀蛋糕。"},{"en":"If asphalt is shaped in a mould, the surface can become smoother than ordinary roadwork allows.","zh":"如果瀝青在模具中成形，表面可比普通道路工程做到的更平滑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a tool for controlling shape.","zh":"這個短語描述控制形狀的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hot asphalt","meaning":"熱瀝青","examples":[{"en":"Hot asphalt is mixed with small stones before it is placed in the mould.","zh":"熱瀝青在放入模具前與小石塊混合。"},{"en":"Hot asphalt is heated road material made from bitumen and aggregate before it cools and hardens.","zh":"「hot asphalt」是由瀝青黏合料和骨料製成、在冷卻硬化前加熱的道路材料。"},{"en":"Workers must handle hot asphalt carefully because it can burn skin.","zh":"工人必須小心處理熱瀝青，因為它可以灼傷皮膚。"},{"en":"If hot asphalt is spread evenly, it can set into a smoother road surface.","zh":"如果熱瀝青鋪得均勻，它可以凝固成更平滑的路面。"},{"en":"The phrase describes asphalt while it is still warm and workable.","zh":"這個短語描述仍然溫熱且可加工的瀝青。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be mixed with","meaning":"與……混合","examples":[{"en":"The asphalt is mixed with stones of a carefully selected size.","zh":"瀝青與精心選定大小的石塊混合。"},{"en":"To be mixed with something means to be combined with it to form one material or mixture.","zh":"「be mixed with」某物，意思是與它結合形成一種材料或混合物。"},{"en":"Flour is mixed with water to make dough for bread.","zh":"麵粉與水混合來製作麵包麵糰。"},{"en":"If asphalt is mixed with stones of the right size, the road can gain useful pores and strength.","zh":"如果瀝青與合適大小的石塊混合，道路就能有有用小孔和強度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes combining materials.","zh":"這個短語描述材料結合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"spread into the mould","meaning":"鋪進模具","examples":[{"en":"A machine spreads the hot asphalt mixture into the mould.","zh":"機器把熱瀝青混合物鋪進模具。"},{"en":"To spread something into the mould means to place and distribute it evenly inside the mould.","zh":"「spread something into the mould」意思是把某物放入模具並均勻鋪開。"},{"en":"A baker spreads cake mixture into a mould before putting it in the oven.","zh":"麵包師把蛋糕混合物鋪進模具，然後放入焗爐。"},{"en":"If asphalt is spread evenly in the mould, the finished sheet can be smooth and regular.","zh":"如果瀝青在模具中鋪得均勻，完成的薄層就可以平滑規則。"},{"en":"The phrase describes filling a shaped container with material.","zh":"這個短語描述把材料填入成形容器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rail-mounted machine","meaning":"安裝在軌道上的機器","examples":[{"en":"A rail-mounted machine spreads and flattens the asphalt.","zh":"安裝在軌道上的機器會鋪開並壓平瀝青。"},{"en":"A rail-mounted machine is a machine that moves along rails while performing a task.","zh":"「rail-mounted machine」是在軌道上移動並執行工作的機器。"},{"en":"A warehouse may use a rail-mounted machine to move heavy goods in a straight line.","zh":"倉庫可能使用安裝在軌道上的機器，以直線移動重貨。"},{"en":"If the machine follows rails, it can spread material more accurately and evenly.","zh":"如果機器沿軌道移動，它可以更準確、更均勻地鋪開材料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes equipment guided by tracks.","zh":"這個短語描述由軌道引導的設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"flatten the asphalt mix","meaning":"壓平瀝青混合物","examples":[{"en":"The machine uses a roller to flatten the asphalt mix.","zh":"機器使用滾筒壓平瀝青混合物。"},{"en":"To flatten the asphalt mix means to press the asphalt mixture into a smooth, even layer.","zh":"「flatten the asphalt mix」意思是把瀝青混合物壓成平滑均勻的一層。"},{"en":"A cook may flatten dough before cutting it into biscuits.","zh":"廚師可能先壓平麵糰，再切成餅乾。"},{"en":"If the asphalt mix is not flattened evenly, the final road surface may be rough.","zh":"如果瀝青混合物沒有均勻壓平，最終路面可能粗糙。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pressing material into a flat shape.","zh":"這個短語描述把材料壓成平面形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"when it sets","meaning":"當……凝固時","examples":[{"en":"When the asphalt sets, it forms a thin, smooth sheet.","zh":"當瀝青凝固時，它形成一片薄而平滑的薄層。"},{"en":"When a material sets, it becomes firm or hard after cooling, drying, or reacting.","zh":"當材料「sets」，意思是它在冷卻、乾燥或反應後變堅固或變硬。"},{"en":"Jelly must be left in the fridge until it sets.","zh":"啫喱必須放在雪櫃中，直到它凝固。"},{"en":"If asphalt sets in a smooth mould, it keeps that smooth shape.","zh":"如果瀝青在平滑模具中凝固，它會保持那種平滑形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the moment a soft material becomes solid.","zh":"這個短語描述柔軟材料變成固體的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a ten-millimetre-thick sheet","meaning":"十毫米厚的薄層","examples":[{"en":"The process produces a ten-millimetre-thick sheet of asphalt.","zh":"這個過程製成一片十毫米厚的瀝青薄層。"},{"en":"A ten-millimetre-thick sheet is a flat layer that is ten millimetres from top to bottom.","zh":"「a ten-millimetre-thick sheet」是由上至下厚度為十毫米的平面薄層。"},{"en":"A craft board may be a ten-millimetre-thick sheet if it is about one centimetre thick.","zh":"如果手工板約一厘米厚，它就可以說是十毫米厚的薄板。"},{"en":"If the asphalt sheet has controlled thickness, workers can handle and lay it more predictably.","zh":"如果瀝青薄層厚度受控，工人就能更可預測地處理和鋪設。"},{"en":"The phrase gives both shape and precise thickness.","zh":"這個短語同時提供形狀和精確厚度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"smoother than anything","meaning":"比任何……都更平滑","examples":[{"en":"The resulting surface is smoother than anything produced conventionally.","zh":"所得表面比任何傳統方法製成的表面都更平滑。"},{"en":"Smoother than anything means smoother than all other things being compared.","zh":"「smoother than anything」意思是比所有被比較事物都更平滑。"},{"en":"A new screen protector may feel smoother than anything the student has used before.","zh":"新手機保護貼可能比學生以前用過的任何保護貼都更平滑。"},{"en":"If the road surface is extremely smooth, tyres may vibrate less.","zh":"如果路面極其平滑，車胎可能較少震動。"},{"en":"The phrase makes a strong comparison about smoothness.","zh":"這個短語對平滑程度作強烈比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be achieved by conventional methods","meaning":"可用傳統方法做到","examples":[{"en":"Such a smooth surface cannot be achieved by conventional methods.","zh":"如此平滑的表面不能用傳統方法做到。"},{"en":"To be achieved by conventional methods means to be done using the usual or traditional ways.","zh":"「be achieved by conventional methods」意思是用通常或傳統方式完成。"},{"en":"Some digital effects in films cannot be achieved by conventional camera work alone.","zh":"電影中的某些數碼效果不能單靠傳統攝影方法做到。"},{"en":"If normal road-building methods cannot make the surface smooth enough, a new process is needed.","zh":"如果普通道路建設方法不能把表面做得足夠平滑，就需要新過程。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts ordinary methods with a new technique.","zh":"這個短語把普通方法與新技術作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"optimise the performance of","meaning":"充分改善……的效能","examples":[{"en":"Kuijpers adds another layer to optimise the performance of the road surface.","zh":"Kuijpers 加入另一層，以充分改善路面的效能。"},{"en":"To optimise the performance of something means to make it work as well as possible.","zh":"「optimise the performance of」某物，意思是令它盡可能有效運作。"},{"en":"A student can optimise the performance of a laptop by closing unnecessary apps.","zh":"學生可以透過關閉不必要應用程式，充分改善手提電腦效能。"},{"en":"If the road has both a smooth top and a soft lower layer, it may reduce noise more effectively.","zh":"如果道路同時有平滑上層和柔軟下層，它可能更有效降低噪音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improving efficiency or effectiveness to the highest practical level.","zh":"這個短語描述把效率或效能提升至實際上最高水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hard-wearing","meaning":"耐磨的","examples":[{"en":"The surface must be hard-wearing enough to withstand traffic.","zh":"表面必須足夠耐磨，以承受交通。"},{"en":"Hard-wearing means strong enough to last despite heavy use.","zh":"「hard-wearing」意思是足夠堅固，即使頻繁使用也能持久。"},{"en":"School shoes need to be hard-wearing because students walk and run in them every day.","zh":"校鞋需要耐磨，因為學生每天穿着它們行走和跑動。"},{"en":"If a road surface is not hard-wearing, heavy vehicles will damage it quickly.","zh":"如果路面不耐磨，重型車輛會很快損壞它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes durability under regular pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述在經常受壓下的耐用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"soft enough to","meaning":"足夠柔軟以……","examples":[{"en":"The lower layer must be soft enough to reduce vibration.","zh":"下層必須足夠柔軟，以減少震動。"},{"en":"Soft enough to do something means having enough softness for a particular purpose.","zh":"「soft enough to」做某事，意思是柔軟程度足以達到某目的。"},{"en":"A pillow should be soft enough to support the neck comfortably.","zh":"枕頭應足夠柔軟，以舒適地支撐頸部。"},{"en":"If the road layer is slightly soft, it can absorb movement from tyres.","zh":"如果道路層稍為柔軟，它可以吸收車胎的移動。"},{"en":"The phrase links degree of softness with function.","zh":"這個短語把柔軟程度與功能連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"snuff out vibrations","meaning":"消除震動","examples":[{"en":"The rubber layer helps snuff out vibrations from moving tyres.","zh":"橡膠層有助消除移動車胎造成的震動。"},{"en":"To snuff out vibrations means to stop or greatly reduce shaking movements.","zh":"「snuff out vibrations」意思是停止或大幅減少震動。"},{"en":"Soft mats can snuff out vibrations from a washing machine on a hard floor.","zh":"軟墊可以消除洗衣機在硬地板上造成的震動。"},{"en":"If vibrations are reduced, less noise is produced by the tyres.","zh":"如果震動減少，車胎產生的噪音就較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes damping movement until it becomes much weaker.","zh":"這個短語描述把移動減弱至很低程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"add another layer below","meaning":"在下方加入另一層","examples":[{"en":"The engineer adds another layer below the asphalt surface.","zh":"工程師在瀝青表面下方加入另一層。"},{"en":"To add another layer below means to place an extra layer underneath an existing one.","zh":"「add another layer below」意思是在現有層下面放入額外一層。"},{"en":"A student may add another layer below a drawing by placing cardboard under the paper.","zh":"學生可能把卡紙放在紙張下方，為圖畫加入另一層。"},{"en":"If a soft layer is added below the road surface, it can absorb some vibration.","zh":"如果路面下方加入柔軟層，它可以吸收部分震動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes building a multi-layer structure.","zh":"這個短語描述建造多層結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"consist of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"The lower layer consists of rubber mixed with stones.","zh":"下層由混有石塊的橡膠組成。"},{"en":"To consist of something means to be made up of particular parts or materials.","zh":"「consist of」某物，意思是由特定部分或材料組成。"},{"en":"A simple lunch may consist of rice, vegetables, and fish.","zh":"一頓簡單午餐可能由飯、蔬菜和魚組成。"},{"en":"If a road layer consists of rubber and stones, it can combine softness with strength.","zh":"如果道路層由橡膠和石塊組成，它可以結合柔軟度和強度。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what something is made from.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物由甚麼製成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rubber mixed with stones","meaning":"混有石塊的橡膠","examples":[{"en":"The lower layer contains rubber mixed with larger stones.","zh":"下層含有混有較大石塊的橡膠。"},{"en":"Rubber mixed with stones is a material combining flexible rubber with solid pieces of stone.","zh":"「rubber mixed with stones」是把有彈性的橡膠與堅硬石塊結合的材料。"},{"en":"A playground surface may use rubber mixed with small particles to reduce injury from falls.","zh":"遊樂場地面可能使用混有細小顆粒的橡膠，以減少跌倒受傷。"},{"en":"If rubber is mixed with stones, the road can be softer while still staying stable.","zh":"如果橡膠混有石塊，道路可以較柔軟，同時仍保持穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a composite road material.","zh":"這個短語描述複合道路材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a giant mouse mat","meaning":"巨型滑鼠墊","examples":[{"en":"Kuijpers compares the soft layer to a giant mouse mat.","zh":"Kuijpers 把柔軟層比作巨型滑鼠墊。"},{"en":"A giant mouse mat is a large soft pad used as a comparison for the rubber road layer.","zh":"「a giant mouse mat」是用來比喻橡膠道路層的大型軟墊。"},{"en":"A desk mouse mat softens movement and gives the hand a smoother surface.","zh":"書桌上的滑鼠墊令移動更柔和，並給手部較平滑表面。"},{"en":"If the road layer behaves like a huge soft pad, it can reduce tyre vibration.","zh":"如果道路層像巨型軟墊一樣運作，就可以減少車胎震動。"},{"en":"The phrase uses a familiar object to explain softness and cushioning.","zh":"這個短語用熟悉物件解釋柔軟和緩衝作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"make the road softer","meaning":"令路面更柔軟","examples":[{"en":"The rubber layer makes the road softer and reduces vibration.","zh":"橡膠層令路面更柔軟並減少震動。"},{"en":"To make the road softer means to make the surface or layers less hard and more able to absorb pressure.","zh":"「make the road softer」意思是令路面或道路層較不堅硬，更能吸收壓力。"},{"en":"A rubber playground floor makes the ground softer for children who fall.","zh":"橡膠遊樂場地面令地面更柔軟，保護跌倒的孩子。"},{"en":"If the road is softer under the asphalt, tyre vibration may be reduced.","zh":"如果瀝青下方道路較柔軟，車胎震動可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing road material to absorb movement.","zh":"這個短語描述改變道路材料以吸收移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the size of the stones","meaning":"石塊的大小","examples":[{"en":"The size of the stones affects the pores created in the surface.","zh":"石塊的大小影響路面中形成的小孔。"},{"en":"The size of the stones means how large or small the pieces of stone are.","zh":"「the size of the stones」意思是石塊有多大或多小。"},{"en":"Garden paths use different stone sizes depending on whether people walk or drive over them.","zh":"花園小路會按人步行或車輛通過而使用不同大小的石塊。"},{"en":"If stones are chosen carefully, the road can form pores of the right size.","zh":"如果石塊經小心選擇，道路可以形成合適大小的小孔。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a material detail that affects road performance.","zh":"這個短語描述影響道路效能的材料細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"create pores","meaning":"形成小孔","examples":[{"en":"Stones of different sizes create pores within the road surface.","zh":"不同大小的石塊在路面中形成小孔。"},{"en":"To create pores means to form tiny holes or spaces in a material.","zh":"「create pores」意思是在材料中形成細小孔洞或空隙。"},{"en":"Baking bread with yeast creates pores in the dough as gas expands.","zh":"用酵母烘焙麵包時，氣體膨脹會在麵糰中形成小孔。"},{"en":"If pores form in road material, air and water can move through it.","zh":"如果道路材料形成小孔，空氣和水就能穿過它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making small openings inside a structure.","zh":"這個短語描述在結構內製造小開口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pores of a specific size","meaning":"特定大小的小孔","examples":[{"en":"The two layers create pores of a specific size.","zh":"這兩層形成特定大小的小孔。"},{"en":"Pores of a specific size are tiny openings made to a controlled or planned width.","zh":"「pores of a specific size」是被控制或計劃為某種闊度的細小開口。"},{"en":"A water filter needs pores of a specific size to let water pass but block dirt.","zh":"濾水器需要特定大小的小孔，以讓水通過但阻隔污垢。"},{"en":"If road pores are too large or too small, they may not absorb sound effectively.","zh":"如果道路小孔太大或太小，可能不能有效吸收聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes carefully controlled openings.","zh":"這個短語描述被仔細控制的開口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the top layer","meaning":"上層","examples":[{"en":"The stones used in the top layer are only a few millimetres across.","zh":"上層所用的石塊直徑只有幾毫米。"},{"en":"The top layer is the uppermost layer of a material or structure.","zh":"「the top layer」是材料或結構中最上面的一層。"},{"en":"The top layer of a cake may be covered with cream and fruit.","zh":"蛋糕的上層可能鋪有忌廉和水果。"},{"en":"If the top layer of a road is smooth, tyres may roll more quietly over it.","zh":"如果道路上層平滑，車胎在其上滾動時可能更安靜。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the part closest to the surface.","zh":"這個短語指最接近表面的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"approximately twice that size","meaning":"大約是該大小的兩倍","examples":[{"en":"The stones in the lower layer are approximately twice that size.","zh":"下層的石塊大約是該大小的兩倍。"},{"en":"Approximately twice that size means about two times as large as the size just mentioned.","zh":"「approximately twice that size」意思是約為剛提及大小的兩倍。"},{"en":"If one notebook is 10 millimetres thick, another approximately twice that size is about 20 millimetres thick.","zh":"如果一本筆記簿厚10毫米，另一本大約是該大小的兩倍，就是約20毫米厚。"},{"en":"If lower stones are larger, they may create larger pores for drainage and sound absorption.","zh":"如果下層石塊較大，它們可能形成較大孔洞，以便排水和吸音。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate comparison in size.","zh":"這個短語提供大小上的近似比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"passing through a tyre’s tread","meaning":"穿過車胎胎紋","examples":[{"en":"The pores absorb air passing through a tyre’s tread.","zh":"小孔吸收穿過車胎胎紋的空氣。"},{"en":"Air passing through a tyre’s tread is air moving through the patterned grooves on a tyre as it rolls.","zh":"「air passing through a tyre’s tread」是車胎滾動時穿過胎紋凹槽的空氣。"},{"en":"A cyclist may hear air moving through tyre grooves on a rough path.","zh":"單車手在粗糙小路上可能聽到空氣穿過車胎凹紋的聲音。"},{"en":"If this air movement is absorbed, less tyre noise may be produced.","zh":"如果這種空氣流動被吸收，產生的車胎噪音可能較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small movement of air that can create sound.","zh":"這個短語描述可能產生聲音的細小空氣移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tyre tread","meaning":"車胎胎紋","examples":[{"en":"The tread is the patterned outer surface of a tyre.","zh":"胎紋是車胎有圖案的外層表面。"},{"en":"Tyre tread is the grooved part of a tyre that touches the road and helps grip the surface.","zh":"「tyre tread」是車胎接觸道路並幫助抓地的凹紋部分。"},{"en":"Drivers check tyre tread before long journeys because worn tyres can be dangerous.","zh":"司機在長途旅程前檢查車胎胎紋，因為磨蝕車胎可能危險。"},{"en":"If tyre tread traps and releases air quickly, it can create noise.","zh":"如果車胎胎紋快速困住並釋放空氣，就會產生噪音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the patterned contact surface of a tyre.","zh":"這個短語描述車胎有圖案的接觸面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"indentations or ridges","meaning":"凹紋或凸紋","examples":[{"en":"A tyre’s tread consists of indentations or ridges on its surface.","zh":"車胎胎紋由表面的凹紋或凸紋組成。"},{"en":"Indentations or ridges are sunken grooves or raised lines on a surface.","zh":"「indentations or ridges」是表面上的凹下溝槽或凸起線條。"},{"en":"The indentations on a coin help people feel its edge without looking.","zh":"硬幣邊緣的凹紋幫助人不用看也能摸出邊位。"},{"en":"If tyre ridges press against the road, air can be squeezed and released noisily.","zh":"如果車胎凸紋壓在路面上，空氣會被擠壓並嘈吵地釋放。"},{"en":"The phrase describes uneven surface patterns.","zh":"這個短語描述不平表面圖案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"damp oscillations","meaning":"減弱振盪","examples":[{"en":"The pores damp oscillations that would otherwise produce noise.","zh":"小孔減弱本來會產生噪音的振盪。"},{"en":"To damp oscillations means to reduce repeated back-and-forth movement or vibration.","zh":"「damp oscillations」意思是減少反覆來回移動或震動。"},{"en":"Shock absorbers in a car damp oscillations after the wheels hit a bump.","zh":"汽車避震器在車輪撞上凹凸後減弱振盪。"},{"en":"If oscillations are damped, the road and tyres produce less sound.","zh":"如果振盪被減弱，道路和車胎產生的聲音就較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weakening repeated movement.","zh":"這個短語描述削弱重複移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"would otherwise create noise","meaning":"否則會產生噪音","examples":[{"en":"The air movements would otherwise create additional tyre noise.","zh":"這些空氣移動否則會產生額外車胎噪音。"},{"en":"Would otherwise create noise means would create noise if the preventing action did not happen.","zh":"「would otherwise create noise」意思是如果沒有預防行動，就會產生噪音。"},{"en":"A carpet absorbs footsteps that would otherwise create noise on a wooden floor.","zh":"地氈吸收腳步聲，否則木地板上會產生噪音。"},{"en":"If road pores absorb air movement, they prevent noise that would normally be produced.","zh":"如果道路小孔吸收空氣移動，它們就防止通常會產生的噪音。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what would happen without the solution.","zh":"這個短語解釋如果沒有解決方法會發生甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in addition","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"In addition, the pores allow rainwater to leave the surface.","zh":"此外，小孔讓雨水離開表面。"},{"en":"In addition means also or as another point.","zh":"「in addition」意思是另外或作為另一點。"},{"en":"The new library has more books; in addition, it provides quiet study rooms.","zh":"新圖書館有更多書；此外，它提供安靜自修室。"},{"en":"If a road surface reduces noise and also drains water, it has more than one benefit.","zh":"如果路面既減少噪音又排水，它就有不只一個好處。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an extra advantage or idea.","zh":"這個短語引入額外優點或想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make it easier for","meaning":"令……更容易","examples":[{"en":"The open pores make it easier for water to drain away.","zh":"開放小孔令水更容易排走。"},{"en":"To make it easier for something to happen means to help it happen with less difficulty.","zh":"「make it easier for」某事發生，意思是幫助它較少困難地發生。"},{"en":"Clear notes make it easier for students to revise before exams.","zh":"清晰筆記令學生考試前更容易溫習。"},{"en":"If pores give water an escape route, drainage becomes faster.","zh":"如果小孔給水一條離開路徑，排水就變得更快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reducing difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述降低難度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"drain away","meaning":"排走","examples":[{"en":"Water can drain away quickly through the porous surface.","zh":"水可以透過多孔表面快速排走。"},{"en":"To drain away means to flow away from a surface or place.","zh":"「drain away」意思是從表面或地方流走。"},{"en":"After heavy rain, water should drain away from a school playground to prevent puddles.","zh":"大雨後，學校操場的水應排走，以防積水。"},{"en":"If rainwater drains away quickly, tyres have better contact with the road.","zh":"如果雨水快速排走，車胎與道路接觸會更好。"},{"en":"The phrase describes water leaving an area.","zh":"這個短語描述水離開某地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"safer in wet weather","meaning":"在雨天更加安全","examples":[{"en":"Efficient drainage can make the road safer in wet weather.","zh":"有效排水可以令道路在雨天更加安全。"},{"en":"Safer in wet weather means less dangerous when it rains or the surface is wet.","zh":"「safer in wet weather」意思是在下雨或表面濕滑時較少危險。"},{"en":"Shoes with good grip make walking safer in wet weather.","zh":"抓地力好的鞋令人在雨天行走更安全。"},{"en":"If water leaves the road quickly, vehicles are less likely to skid.","zh":"如果水快速離開道路，車輛較不容易打滑。"},{"en":"The phrase connects drainage with safety during rain.","zh":"這個短語把排水與雨天安全連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Compared with the manufacturing process, laying the surface is relatively simple.","zh":"與生產程序相比，鋪設路面相對簡單。"},{"en":"Compared with means when one thing is considered in relation to another.","zh":"「compared with」意思是把一件事與另一件事放在一起考慮。"},{"en":"Compared with writing an essay, correcting a short paragraph is easier.","zh":"與寫一篇文章相比，修改一段短文較容易。"},{"en":"If manufacturing is complex but laying is simple, most difficulty happens before the road reaches the site.","zh":"如果生產複雜但鋪設簡單，大部分困難就在路面到達工地前發生。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a direct comparison.","zh":"這個短語引出直接比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"complex manufacturing process","meaning":"複雜的生產程序","examples":[{"en":"The road surface requires a complex manufacturing process.","zh":"這種路面需要複雜的生產程序。"},{"en":"A complex manufacturing process is a difficult series of steps used to make a product.","zh":"「complex manufacturing process」是用來製作產品的一系列困難步驟。"},{"en":"Making a smartphone requires a complex manufacturing process with many specialised parts.","zh":"製造智能手機需要複雜的生產程序，涉及許多專門零件。"},{"en":"If the road surface needs precise layers and pores, it must be produced carefully.","zh":"如果路面需要精確層次和小孔，就必須仔細生產。"},{"en":"The phrase describes complicated factory production.","zh":"這個短語描述複雜工廠生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lay the surface","meaning":"鋪設路面","examples":[{"en":"Workers can lay the prefabricated surface relatively quickly.","zh":"工人可以相對快速地鋪設預製路面。"},{"en":"To lay the surface means to place the road surface in position on the road foundation.","zh":"「lay the surface」意思是把路面放置在道路基層上的正確位置。"},{"en":"Workers lay tiles carefully so the floor becomes even and safe.","zh":"工人小心鋪設瓷磚，使地板平整安全。"},{"en":"If the surface arrives ready-made, workers can lay it faster on site.","zh":"如果路面以預製形式到達，工人可以在現場更快鋪設。"},{"en":"The phrase describes installing a surface layer.","zh":"這個短語描述安裝表面層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"emerge from the factory","meaning":"從工廠製成運出","examples":[{"en":"The finished road material emerges from the factory in a roll.","zh":"完成的道路材料從工廠以卷狀製成運出。"},{"en":"To emerge from the factory means to come out after being made or completed there.","zh":"「emerge from the factory」意思是在工廠製成或完成後出來。"},{"en":"New phones emerge from the factory after assembly and quality checks.","zh":"新電話在組裝和品質檢查後從工廠製成運出。"},{"en":"If road material emerges already prepared, on-site construction can be faster.","zh":"如果道路材料出廠時已準備好，現場施工可以更快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a product leaving the place where it is manufactured.","zh":"這個短語描述產品離開製造地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rolled like a carpet","meaning":"像地氈般捲起","examples":[{"en":"The road surface is transported rolled like a carpet.","zh":"路面像地氈般捲起來運送。"},{"en":"Rolled like a carpet means wound into a roll, similar to how a carpet is stored or carried.","zh":"「rolled like a carpet」意思是捲成一卷，像地氈儲存或搬運一樣。"},{"en":"A poster can be rolled like a carpet so it does not fold or crease.","zh":"海報可以像地氈般捲起，以免摺疊或起摺痕。"},{"en":"If road material can be rolled, it becomes easier to transport to the site.","zh":"如果道路材料可以捲起，就更容易運到工地。"},{"en":"The phrase uses a familiar object to describe the form of transport.","zh":"這個短語用熟悉物件描述運輸形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"onto a drum","meaning":"捲在圓筒上","examples":[{"en":"The finished surface is rolled onto a large drum.","zh":"完成的路面被捲在大型圓筒上。"},{"en":"Onto a drum means onto a large round cylinder used for winding or carrying material.","zh":"「onto a drum」意思是捲到用來收卷或運送材料的大型圓柱上。"},{"en":"Long electrical cable may be wound onto a drum before being moved to a building site.","zh":"長電線可能在運到建築地盤前捲在圓筒上。"},{"en":"If the road surface is rolled onto a drum, workers can unroll it later like a carpet.","zh":"如果路面捲在圓筒上，工人之後可以像地氈般把它攤開。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how a long flexible material is stored for transport.","zh":"這個短語描述長而柔韌材料如何儲存以便運輸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on site","meaning":"在施工現場","examples":[{"en":"On site, workers unroll and attach the road surface.","zh":"在施工現場，工人攤開並固定路面。"},{"en":"On site means at the actual place where work, construction, or installation happens.","zh":"「on site」意思是在工作、建築或安裝實際發生的地方。"},{"en":"Engineers may solve problems on site when a building project does not match the plan.","zh":"當建築項目與計劃不符，工程師可能在現場解決問題。"},{"en":"If most production happens in the factory, less work is needed on site.","zh":"如果大部分生產在工廠完成，現場需要的工作就較少。"},{"en":"The phrase distinguishes the workplace from the factory or office.","zh":"這個短語把工作地點與工廠或辦公室區分開來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be unrolled and stuck onto","meaning":"被攤開並黏在……上","examples":[{"en":"The surface is unrolled and stuck onto its foundation.","zh":"路面被攤開並黏在其基層上。"},{"en":"To be unrolled and stuck onto something means to be opened from a roll and attached to a base.","zh":"「be unrolled and stuck onto」某物，意思是從卷中攤開並固定在基底上。"},{"en":"Wallpaper is unrolled and stuck onto a wall during home decoration.","zh":"家居裝修時，牆紙被攤開並黏在牆上。"},{"en":"If the road surface can be attached this way, installation becomes faster and more controlled.","zh":"如果路面可以用這種方式安裝，施工就變得更快速且更受控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a roll-out installation method.","zh":"這個短語描述卷材式安裝方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"road foundation","meaning":"道路基層","examples":[{"en":"The prefabricated surface is attached to a specially designed road foundation.","zh":"預製路面被固定在特別設計的道路基層上。"},{"en":"A road foundation is the supporting base underneath the visible road surface.","zh":"「road foundation」是可見路面下方的支撐基底。"},{"en":"A house needs a strong foundation, and a road also needs a stable base.","zh":"房屋需要堅固地基，道路也需要穩定基層。"},{"en":"If the foundation is weak, the road surface may crack or move.","zh":"如果基層薄弱，路面可能裂開或移動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the hidden support layer below the road.","zh":"這個短語指道路下方隱藏的支撐層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"bitumen","meaning":"瀝青黏合料","examples":[{"en":"Bitumen is used to stick the surface onto its foundation.","zh":"瀝青黏合料用來把路面黏在基層上。"},{"en":"Bitumen is a thick, black, sticky material used in asphalt and road construction.","zh":"「bitumen」是用於瀝青和道路建設中的濃稠、黑色、黏性材料。"},{"en":"Road workers may use bitumen to bind stones together in a road surface.","zh":"道路工人可能使用瀝青黏合料把石塊黏合成路面。"},{"en":"If bitumen holds the layers firmly, the surface is less likely to move under traffic.","zh":"如果瀝青黏合料牢固固定各層，路面在交通下較不容易移動。"},{"en":"The word names a sticky road-building material.","zh":"這個詞指出一種黏性道路建材。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be applied in the factory","meaning":"在工廠預先髹上","examples":[{"en":"Even the white road markings are applied in the factory.","zh":"連白色道路標線也在工廠預先髹上。"},{"en":"To be applied in the factory means to be added or painted during production before delivery.","zh":"「be applied in the factory」意思是在運送前的生產期間加入或髹上。"},{"en":"A logo may be applied in the factory before a school bag reaches the shop.","zh":"書包到達商店前，標誌可能已在工廠預先印上。"},{"en":"If road markings are added before installation, on-site work becomes quicker.","zh":"如果道路標線在安裝前已加上，現場工作會更快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes completing a step during manufacturing.","zh":"這個短語描述在製造期間完成某步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a more sophisticated technique","meaning":"更精密的技術","examples":[{"en":"The foundation uses a more sophisticated technique to absorb sound.","zh":"基層使用更精密的技術來吸收聲音。"},{"en":"A more sophisticated technique is a more advanced, complex, or carefully designed method.","zh":"「a more sophisticated technique」是更先進、更複雜或更仔細設計的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a more sophisticated technique to help advanced students analyse essays.","zh":"老師可能使用更精密的技巧，幫助高階學生分析文章。"},{"en":"If ordinary surfaces cannot absorb enough sound, engineers may need a more complex design.","zh":"如果普通表面不能吸收足夠聲音，工程師可能需要更複雜設計。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a method that is more technically advanced.","zh":"這個短語描述技術上更先進的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reduce noise further","meaning":"進一步降低噪音","examples":[{"en":"The concrete foundation is designed to reduce noise further.","zh":"混凝土基層設計用來進一步降低噪音。"},{"en":"To reduce noise further means to lower noise even more after some reduction has already been achieved.","zh":"「reduce noise further」意思是在已經減少一些噪音後，再進一步降低。"},{"en":"A library may add carpets after closing windows to reduce noise further.","zh":"圖書館關窗後可能加上地氈，以進一步降低噪音。"},{"en":"If the upper layer already lowers tyre vibration, the foundation can provide extra sound reduction.","zh":"如果上層已降低車胎震動，基層可以提供額外降噪。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an additional improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述額外改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sound-absorbing concrete base","meaning":"吸音混凝土基層","examples":[{"en":"The foundation consists of a sound-absorbing concrete base.","zh":"基層由吸音混凝土基層組成。"},{"en":"A sound-absorbing concrete base is a concrete foundation designed to take in sound energy and reduce noise.","zh":"「sound-absorbing concrete base」是設計用來吸收聲能和降低噪音的混凝土基層。"},{"en":"A music room may use sound-absorbing panels to make practice less disturbing.","zh":"音樂室可能使用吸音板，使練習較少打擾別人。"},{"en":"If the concrete base absorbs sound, less road noise is reflected back into the air.","zh":"如果混凝土基層吸收聲音，較少道路噪音會反射回空氣中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a foundation that supports the road and reduces noise.","zh":"這個短語描述既支撐道路又減少噪音的基層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"flask-shaped slots","meaning":"燒瓶形凹槽","examples":[{"en":"The concrete base contains numerous flask-shaped slots.","zh":"混凝土基層含有大量燒瓶形凹槽。"},{"en":"Flask-shaped slots are openings shaped like laboratory flasks, narrow at one part and wider inside.","zh":"「flask-shaped slots」是形狀像實驗室燒瓶的開口，某部分較窄，內部較闊。"},{"en":"A science worksheet may ask students to draw a flask-shaped container with a narrow neck.","zh":"科學工作紙可能要求學生畫一個窄頸燒瓶形容器。"},{"en":"If slots have this shape, they can trap and absorb certain sound waves.","zh":"如果凹槽有這種形狀，它們可以困住並吸收某些聲波。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the special shape of cavities inside the concrete.","zh":"這個短語描述混凝土內空腔的特殊形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"open at the top","meaning":"頂部開口","examples":[{"en":"Each slot is open at the top.","zh":"每個凹槽頂部開口。"},{"en":"Open at the top means not covered or sealed on the upper side.","zh":"「open at the top」意思是上方沒有被覆蓋或密封。"},{"en":"A cup is open at the top so people can pour water into it.","zh":"杯子頂部開口，所以人們可以把水倒入。"},{"en":"If a cavity is open at the top, sound waves and water can enter it.","zh":"如果空腔頂部開口，聲波和水可以進入其中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where an opening is located.","zh":"這個短語描述開口所在位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sealed at the lower end","meaning":"底部密封","examples":[{"en":"The slots are sealed at the lower end.","zh":"這些凹槽底部密封。"},{"en":"Sealed at the lower end means closed at the bottom so material cannot pass through that end.","zh":"「sealed at the lower end」意思是底部封閉，使材料不能從該端通過。"},{"en":"A test tube is sealed at the lower end and open at the top.","zh":"試管底部密封，頂部開口。"},{"en":"If a cavity is closed below, sound waves may resonate inside it instead of passing straight through.","zh":"如果空腔下方封閉，聲波可能在其中共振，而不是直接穿過。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a bottom closure.","zh":"這個短語描述底部封口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cavities","meaning":"空腔","examples":[{"en":"The cavities inside the concrete absorb sound energy.","zh":"混凝土內的空腔吸收聲能。"},{"en":"Cavities are hollow spaces inside a solid material.","zh":"「cavities」是固體材料內部的中空空間。"},{"en":"A sponge has many small cavities that can hold water.","zh":"海綿有許多可以盛水的小空腔。"},{"en":"If concrete contains cavities of the right shape, it can absorb certain sounds.","zh":"如果混凝土含有合適形狀的空腔，它可以吸收某些聲音。"},{"en":"The word describes empty spaces within a structure.","zh":"這個詞描述結構內部的空位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"act like","meaning":"發揮像……一樣的作用","examples":[{"en":"The cavities act like specialised sound resonators.","zh":"這些空腔發揮像專門聲音共鳴器一樣的作用。"},{"en":"To act like something means to function in a similar way to it.","zh":"「act like」某物，意思是以與它相似的方式運作。"},{"en":"A blanket can act like a curtain if it is hung over a window.","zh":"如果把毛氈掛在窗戶上，它可以像窗簾一樣發揮作用。"},{"en":"If cavities act like resonators, they can absorb sound at certain frequencies.","zh":"如果空腔像共鳴器一樣運作，它們可以吸收某些頻率的聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase compares function, not identity.","zh":"這個短語比較功能，而不是身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Helmholtz resonators","meaning":"亥姆霍茲共鳴器","examples":[{"en":"The flask-shaped cavities act like Helmholtz resonators.","zh":"燒瓶形空腔像亥姆霍茲共鳴器一樣運作。"},{"en":"Helmholtz resonators are shaped spaces that can absorb or resonate with sound at particular frequencies.","zh":"「Helmholtz resonators」是能吸收或與特定頻率聲音共鳴的成形空間。"},{"en":"A bottle can behave like a simple resonator when air vibrates inside it after you blow across the top.","zh":"當你吹過瓶口，瓶內空氣震動時，瓶子可以像簡單共鳴器一樣運作。"},{"en":"If road cavities work like resonators, they can target specific vehicle noises.","zh":"如果道路空腔像共鳴器一樣運作，它們就能針對特定車輛噪音。"},{"en":"The phrase names a sound-control principle used in the road design.","zh":"這個短語指出道路設計中使用的聲音控制原理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sound waves","meaning":"聲波","examples":[{"en":"Sound waves enter the cavities through their open tops.","zh":"聲波透過空腔的頂部開口進入。"},{"en":"Sound waves are vibrations that travel through air, water, or solid materials and are heard as sound.","zh":"「sound waves」是在空氣、水或固體材料中傳播，並被聽成聲音的震動。"},{"en":"A loudspeaker sends sound waves through the air to listeners.","zh":"揚聲器把聲波透過空氣傳到聽眾。"},{"en":"If sound waves enter a cavity, their energy may be absorbed or changed.","zh":"如果聲波進入空腔，其能量可能被吸收或改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how sound travels physically.","zh":"這個短語描述聲音如何以物理方式傳播。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"specific frequencies","meaning":"特定頻率","examples":[{"en":"The resonators absorb sound waves of specific frequencies.","zh":"共鳴器吸收特定頻率的聲波。"},{"en":"Specific frequencies are particular rates of vibration in sound, often linked to pitch.","zh":"「specific frequencies」是聲音中特定的震動速率，通常與音高有關。"},{"en":"A music teacher may explain that different notes have different frequencies.","zh":"音樂老師可能解釋不同音符有不同頻率。"},{"en":"If a road absorbs the frequencies made by tyres, traffic may sound quieter.","zh":"如果道路吸收車胎產生的頻率，交通聲可能聽起來更安靜。"},{"en":"The phrase describes exact sound ranges rather than all sounds.","zh":"這個短語描述精確聲音範圍，而不是所有聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"set up resonances","meaning":"產生共振","examples":[{"en":"Sound waves set up resonances inside the flask-shaped cavities.","zh":"聲波在燒瓶形空腔內產生共振。"},{"en":"To set up resonances means to create vibrations that match and reinforce a particular frequency.","zh":"「set up resonances」意思是產生配合並加強某特定頻率的震動。"},{"en":"A singer may set up resonance in a glass if the note matches the glass’s natural frequency.","zh":"如果歌手唱出的音符配合玻璃杯的自然頻率，可能在杯中產生共振。"},{"en":"If resonance occurs in the cavities, sound energy can be trapped and reduced.","zh":"如果空腔中出現共振，聲能可以被困住並減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sound causing controlled vibration.","zh":"這個短語描述聲音造成受控制的震動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sound energy","meaning":"聲能","examples":[{"en":"The resonators convert sound energy into heat.","zh":"共鳴器將聲能轉化為熱能。"},{"en":"Sound energy is energy carried by vibrating sound waves.","zh":"「sound energy」是由震動聲波攜帶的能量。"},{"en":"Loud music carries more sound energy than a quiet whisper.","zh":"巨大音樂比輕聲耳語帶有更多聲能。"},{"en":"If sound energy is absorbed by a material, less noise reaches listeners.","zh":"如果聲能被材料吸收，較少噪音會到達聽者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sound as a form of energy.","zh":"這個短語把聲音描述為一種能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"dissipate into","meaning":"消散至……","examples":[{"en":"The energy of the sound dissipates into the concrete as heat.","zh":"聲音的能量以熱的形式消散至混凝土中。"},{"en":"To dissipate into something means to spread out and disappear into it gradually.","zh":"「dissipate into」某物，意思是逐漸擴散並消失於其中。"},{"en":"Heat from a hot cup may dissipate into the surrounding air.","zh":"熱杯中的熱力可能消散至周圍空氣中。"},{"en":"If sound energy dissipates into concrete, the sound becomes weaker.","zh":"如果聲能消散至混凝土中，聲音就變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes energy spreading away and losing intensity.","zh":"這個短語描述能量散開並失去強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"convert sound into heat","meaning":"將聲音轉化成熱能","examples":[{"en":"The foundation helps convert sound into heat.","zh":"基層有助將聲音轉化成熱能。"},{"en":"To convert sound into heat means to change sound energy into a small amount of thermal energy.","zh":"「convert sound into heat」意思是把聲能轉化成少量熱能。"},{"en":"Some sound-absorbing materials convert vibration into tiny amounts of heat.","zh":"有些吸音材料會把震動轉化成微量熱能。"},{"en":"If road noise is converted into heat, less of it remains as audible sound.","zh":"如果道路噪音被轉化成熱能，剩下可聽見的聲音就較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes energy transformation.","zh":"這個短語描述能量轉化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"play another important role","meaning":"發揮另一項重要作用","examples":[{"en":"The cavities play another important role in road drainage.","zh":"這些空腔在道路排水中發揮另一項重要作用。"},{"en":"To play another important role means to have an additional significant function.","zh":"「play another important role」意思是具有另一項重要功能。"},{"en":"A school library supports reading and plays another important role as a quiet study space.","zh":"學校圖書館支持閱讀，也發揮另一項重要作用，作為安靜自修空間。"},{"en":"If cavities absorb sound and drain water, the design has two major benefits.","zh":"如果空腔既吸音又排水，設計就有兩大好處。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an extra function.","zh":"這個短語引入額外功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"drain water","meaning":"排走水分","examples":[{"en":"The slots help drain water from the upper surface.","zh":"這些凹槽有助從上層表面排走水分。"},{"en":"To drain water means to remove water by letting it flow away.","zh":"「drain water」意思是讓水流走以移除水分。"},{"en":"A bathroom floor needs a slope to drain water after a shower.","zh":"浴室地面需要斜度，以便洗澡後排走水分。"},{"en":"If road water drains quickly, cars are less likely to skid.","zh":"如果道路水分快速排走，汽車較不容易打滑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving unwanted water away.","zh":"這個短語描述移走不需要的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"seep through","meaning":"滲過","examples":[{"en":"Rainwater seeps through the porous upper layers.","zh":"雨水滲過多孔上層。"},{"en":"To seep through means to pass slowly through small spaces or holes.","zh":"「seep through」意思是慢慢穿過小空隙或孔洞。"},{"en":"Water may seep through a cracked wall during heavy rain.","zh":"大雨期間，水可能滲過裂開的牆。"},{"en":"If rainwater seeps through the road surface, it can be carried away below.","zh":"如果雨水滲過路面，就可以在下方被帶走。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow movement through a material.","zh":"這個短語描述穿過材料的緩慢移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"upper surface","meaning":"上層表面","examples":[{"en":"Water passes from the upper surface into the concrete foundation.","zh":"水從上層表面進入混凝土基層。"},{"en":"The upper surface is the top side of a material or object.","zh":"「upper surface」是材料或物件的最上方表面。"},{"en":"The upper surface of a desk should be smooth enough for writing.","zh":"書桌上層表面應足夠平滑，方便書寫。"},{"en":"If water leaves the upper surface quickly, the road becomes less slippery.","zh":"如果水快速離開上層表面，道路就較不濕滑。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the visible top part.","zh":"這個短語指可見的頂部部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"flush out waste material","meaning":"沖走廢物","examples":[{"en":"The flow of water helps flush out waste material.","zh":"水流有助沖走廢物。"},{"en":"To flush out waste material means to wash unwanted dirt or particles away with moving water.","zh":"「flush out waste material」意思是用流動的水洗走不需要的污垢或微粒。"},{"en":"Cleaning staff flush out waste material from drains after a storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，清潔工人從排水渠沖走廢物。"},{"en":"If water flows through road pores, it can remove dirt that might block them.","zh":"如果水流過道路小孔，就可以移走可能堵塞小孔的污垢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cleaning by water movement.","zh":"這個短語描述透過水流清潔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"keep the pores clear","meaning":"保持小孔暢通","examples":[{"en":"Regular water flow helps keep the pores clear.","zh":"定期水流有助保持小孔暢通。"},{"en":"To keep the pores clear means to prevent tiny openings from being blocked.","zh":"「keep the pores clear」意思是防止細小開口被堵塞。"},{"en":"Washing a sink filter regularly helps keep its holes clear.","zh":"定期清洗水槽濾網有助保持孔洞暢通。"},{"en":"If road pores stay clear, they can continue draining water and absorbing sound.","zh":"如果道路小孔保持暢通，它們就能繼續排水和吸音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes maintaining open passages.","zh":"這個短語描述維持通道開放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"control the sounds absorbed","meaning":"控制所吸收的聲音","examples":[{"en":"Kuijpers can control the sounds absorbed by the resonators.","zh":"Kuijpers 可以控制共鳴器所吸收的聲音。"},{"en":"To control the sounds absorbed means to decide which sounds or frequencies a material takes in.","zh":"「control the sounds absorbed」意思是決定材料吸收哪些聲音或頻率。"},{"en":"A music studio uses panels to control the sounds absorbed in different parts of the room.","zh":"音樂錄音室使用吸音板來控制房間不同部分所吸收的聲音。"},{"en":"If engineers control absorbed sounds, they can target the noises made by different vehicles.","zh":"如果工程師控制被吸收的聲音，就能針對不同車輛產生的噪音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adjusting sound absorption deliberately.","zh":"這個短語描述有意調整吸音效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"alter the dimensions","meaning":"改變尺寸","examples":[{"en":"He changes the absorbed frequencies by altering the dimensions of the cavities.","zh":"他透過改變空腔尺寸來改變被吸收的頻率。"},{"en":"To alter the dimensions means to change the size, length, width, height, or shape of something.","zh":"「alter the dimensions」意思是改變某物的大小、長度、闊度、高度或形狀。"},{"en":"A carpenter may alter the dimensions of a shelf so it fits a small room.","zh":"木匠可能改變書架尺寸，使它適合小房間。"},{"en":"If cavity dimensions change, the sounds they absorb may change too.","zh":"如果空腔尺寸改變，它們吸收的聲音也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing physical measurements.","zh":"這個短語描述改變物理量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"prove especially useful","meaning":"證明特別有用","examples":[{"en":"This ability could prove especially useful on major roads.","zh":"這種能力在主要道路上可能證明特別有用。"},{"en":"To prove especially useful means to turn out to be particularly helpful.","zh":"「prove especially useful」意思是結果顯示特別有幫助。"},{"en":"A spare charger may prove especially useful during a long school trip.","zh":"在長途學校旅行中，備用充電器可能證明特別有用。"},{"en":"If different lanes have different vehicle noise, adjustable resonators may be very helpful.","zh":"如果不同行車線有不同車輛噪音，可調整共鳴器可能非常有幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase describes usefulness that becomes clear in practice.","zh":"這個短語描述在實際使用中變得明顯的用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"produce noise at different frequencies","meaning":"產生不同頻率的噪音","examples":[{"en":"Different types of vehicle produce noise at different frequencies.","zh":"不同類型車輛產生不同頻率的噪音。"},{"en":"To produce noise at different frequencies means to create sounds with different vibration rates or pitches.","zh":"「produce noise at different frequencies」意思是產生有不同震動速率或音高的聲音。"},{"en":"A small fan and a large generator produce noise at different frequencies.","zh":"小風扇和大型發電機會產生不同頻率的噪音。"},{"en":"If trucks and cars sound different, the road may need to absorb more than one frequency range.","zh":"如果貨車和私家車聲音不同，道路可能需要吸收不只一個頻率範圍。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why one design may need adjustable sound control.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何一種設計可能需要可調式聲音控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"peak at","meaning":"在……達到峰值","examples":[{"en":"Noise from car tyres peaks at around 1,000 hertz.","zh":"汽車車胎噪音在約1,000赫茲達到峰值。"},{"en":"To peak at a level means to reach the highest point at that level.","zh":"「peak at」某水平，意思是在該水平達到最高點。"},{"en":"Train crowding may peak at 8 a.m. when most people go to work.","zh":"火車擠迫程度可能在早上八點大多數人上班時達到峰值。"},{"en":"If tyre noise peaks at a certain frequency, engineers can design resonators for that frequency.","zh":"如果車胎噪音在某頻率達到峰值，工程師可以為該頻率設計共鳴器。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where something reaches its maximum.","zh":"這個短語指出某事在哪裡達到最大值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"generate lower-frequency noise","meaning":"產生較低頻率的噪音","examples":[{"en":"Trucks generate lower-frequency noise than cars.","zh":"貨車比汽車產生較低頻率的噪音。"},{"en":"To generate lower-frequency noise means to produce deeper sounds with slower vibrations.","zh":"「generate lower-frequency noise」意思是產生震動較慢、聲音較低沉的噪音。"},{"en":"A large air-conditioner may generate lower-frequency noise than a small phone alarm.","zh":"大型冷氣機可能比小型電話鬧鐘產生較低頻率的噪音。"},{"en":"If trucks create deeper noise, the road design may need larger resonators to absorb it.","zh":"如果貨車產生較低沉噪音，道路設計可能需要較大共鳴器來吸收。"},{"en":"The phrase describes producing low-pitched sound.","zh":"這個短語描述產生低音調聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"by varying the size of","meaning":"藉着改變……的大小","examples":[{"en":"Engineers can alter performance by varying the size of the resonators.","zh":"工程師可以藉着改變共鳴器大小來改變效能。"},{"en":"By varying the size of something means by changing how large or small it is.","zh":"「by varying the size of」某物，意思是透過改變它有多大或多小。"},{"en":"A teacher can change task difficulty by varying the size of the vocabulary list.","zh":"老師可以藉着改變詞彙表大小來調整任務難度。"},{"en":"If resonators are made larger or smaller, they may absorb different frequencies.","zh":"如果共鳴器被做得較大或較小，它們可能吸收不同頻率。"},{"en":"The phrase explains a method of adjustment.","zh":"這個短語解釋調整方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"control which frequencies","meaning":"控制吸收哪些頻率","examples":[{"en":"The design allows engineers to control which frequencies the concrete absorbs.","zh":"這個設計讓工程師控制混凝土吸收哪些頻率。"},{"en":"To control which frequencies are absorbed means to choose the sound ranges that a material reduces.","zh":"「control which frequencies are absorbed」意思是選擇材料減少哪些聲音範圍。"},{"en":"A recording studio controls which frequencies are absorbed to make speech clearer.","zh":"錄音室控制吸收哪些頻率，以令說話更清楚。"},{"en":"If road concrete absorbs the noisiest frequencies, traffic sounds less harsh.","zh":"如果道路混凝土吸收最嘈吵的頻率，交通聲聽起來較不刺耳。"},{"en":"The phrase describes targeted sound control.","zh":"這個短語描述針對式聲音控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"large highways","meaning":"大型公路","examples":[{"en":"The system could be adapted for different lanes on large highways.","zh":"這個系統可調整以適用於大型公路的不同行車線。"},{"en":"Large highways are major wide roads that carry heavy traffic over long distances.","zh":"「large highways」是承載大量長距離交通的主要寬闊道路。"},{"en":"Large highways often have several lanes for cars, buses, and trucks.","zh":"大型公路通常有幾條行車線，供汽車、巴士和貨車使用。"},{"en":"If highway lanes carry different vehicle types, each lane may need different noise control.","zh":"如果公路行車線承載不同車輛類型，每條線可能需要不同噪音控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes big main roads built for fast traffic.","zh":"這個短語描述為快速交通而建的大型主要道路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tend to use","meaning":"通常使用……","examples":[{"en":"Trucks tend to use the inside lane on major roads.","zh":"貨車通常使用主要道路的內線行車線。"},{"en":"To tend to use something means to usually or often use it.","zh":"「tend to use」某物，意思是通常或經常使用它。"},{"en":"Students tend to use phones for quick dictionary checks during homework.","zh":"學生做功課時通常使用電話快速查字典。"},{"en":"If trucks usually use one lane, that lane can be designed to absorb truck noise better.","zh":"如果貨車通常使用某一行車線，該線可以設計成更好吸收貨車噪音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common habit or pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述常見習慣或模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the inside lane","meaning":"內線行車線","examples":[{"en":"Resonators in the inside lane could be designed for truck noise.","zh":"內線行車線的共鳴器可設計用來處理貨車噪音。"},{"en":"The inside lane is a lane on a multi-lane road, often used by slower or heavier vehicles depending on the road system.","zh":"「the inside lane」是多線道路上的一條行車線，按道路系統常由較慢或較重車輛使用。"},{"en":"Driving instructors teach learners when to stay in the inside lane and when to change lanes.","zh":"駕駛導師會教學員何時留在內線行車線，何時轉線。"},{"en":"If trucks mainly use the inside lane, noise control there can target lower frequencies.","zh":"如果貨車主要使用內線行車線，那裡的噪音控制可以針對較低頻率。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a specific lane on a major road.","zh":"這個短語指出主要道路上的特定行車線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be tuned to absorb","meaning":"被調校以吸收……","examples":[{"en":"The resonators can be tuned to absorb particular frequencies.","zh":"共鳴器可以被調校以吸收特定頻率。"},{"en":"To be tuned to absorb something means to be adjusted so it takes in a specific kind of sound or vibration.","zh":"「be tuned to absorb」某物，意思是被調整到能吸收特定聲音或震動。"},{"en":"A radio is tuned to receive a particular station.","zh":"收音機被調校以接收某個特定電台。"},{"en":"If resonators are tuned correctly, they can reduce the loudest vehicle sounds.","zh":"如果共鳴器調校正確，它們可以減少最嘈吵的車輛聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes precise adjustment for a target frequency.","zh":"這個短語描述為目標頻率作精確調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"deal with higher-frequency noise","meaning":"處理較高頻率的噪音","examples":[{"en":"Resonators in other lanes could deal with higher-frequency noise from cars.","zh":"其他行車線的共鳴器可以處理來自汽車的較高頻率噪音。"},{"en":"To deal with higher-frequency noise means to reduce or manage sounds with faster vibrations and higher pitch.","zh":"「deal with higher-frequency noise」意思是減少或管理震動較快、音調較高的聲音。"},{"en":"A sound engineer may deal with higher-frequency noise by adjusting microphone settings.","zh":"音響工程師可能透過調整咪高峰設定來處理較高頻率噪音。"},{"en":"If cars create higher-pitched tyre noise, different resonators may be needed.","zh":"如果汽車產生較高音調車胎噪音，就可能需要不同共鳴器。"},{"en":"The phrase describes handling a particular type of sound.","zh":"這個短語描述處理特定類型聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cut noise by five decibels","meaning":"將噪音降低五分貝","examples":[{"en":"Kuijpers believes his surface can cut noise by five decibels.","zh":"Kuijpers 相信他的路面可以將噪音降低五分貝。"},{"en":"To cut noise by five decibels means to reduce measured sound by five decibel units.","zh":"「cut noise by five decibels」意思是把量度聲音降低五個分貝單位。"},{"en":"A new window design may cut street noise by five decibels in a flat.","zh":"新窗戶設計可能在單位內將街道噪音降低五分貝。"},{"en":"If a road surface cuts noise noticeably, residents may experience less daily disturbance.","zh":"如果路面明顯降低噪音，居民日常受干擾程度可能較低。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a precise claimed reduction.","zh":"這個短語提供精確聲稱的減幅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"compared with the quietest roads","meaning":"與現時最寧靜的道路相比","examples":[{"en":"The new design may be quieter than the quietest roads currently available.","zh":"新設計可能比現時可用的最寧靜道路更安靜。"},{"en":"Compared with the quietest roads means measured against roads that already produce the least noise.","zh":"「compared with the quietest roads」意思是與已經產生最少噪音的道路比較。"},{"en":"A new library room may be judged compared with the quietest study areas in the school.","zh":"新圖書館房間可能與學校最安靜的自修區相比來判斷。"},{"en":"If the design beats even today’s quietest roads, it would represent real progress.","zh":"如果設計連今天最寧靜的道路也勝過，就代表真正進步。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a high standard for comparison.","zh":"這個短語設定很高的比較標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"test a section of road","meaning":"測試一段道路","examples":[{"en":"The engineer has already tested a 100-metre section of road.","zh":"這位工程師已經測試了一段100米道路。"},{"en":"To test a section of road means to try a road design on a limited length before wider use.","zh":"「test a section of road」意思是在更廣泛使用前，先在有限長度道路上試用設計。"},{"en":"A city may test a section of cycle path before building the full route.","zh":"城市可能先測試一段單車徑，再建造完整路線。"},{"en":"If a short road test performs well, engineers may expand the project.","zh":"如果短道路測試表現良好，工程師可能擴大項目。"},{"en":"The phrase describes small-scale practical testing.","zh":"這個短語描述小規模實際測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a motorway near Apeldoorn","meaning":"Apeldoorn 附近的一條高速公路","examples":[{"en":"The trial surface was installed on a motorway near Apeldoorn.","zh":"試驗路面安裝在 Apeldoorn 附近的一條高速公路上。"},{"en":"A motorway near Apeldoorn means a high-speed main road located close to the Dutch city of Apeldoorn.","zh":"「a motorway near Apeldoorn」意思是位於荷蘭城市 Apeldoorn 附近的高速主要道路。"},{"en":"Engineers may choose a motorway near a city because it carries enough traffic for a realistic test.","zh":"工程師可能選擇城市附近高速公路，因為它有足夠交通量作真實測試。"},{"en":"If a trial works on a busy motorway, it may be suitable for other major roads.","zh":"如果試驗在繁忙高速公路上成功，它可能適用於其他主要道路。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the test location.","zh":"這個短語指出測試地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"construction company","meaning":"建築公司","examples":[{"en":"A Dutch construction company is involved in the project.","zh":"一間荷蘭建築公司參與該項目。"},{"en":"A construction company is a business that builds roads, buildings, bridges, or other structures.","zh":"「construction company」是建造道路、建築物、橋樑或其他結構的企業。"},{"en":"A school may hire a construction company to build a new sports hall.","zh":"學校可能聘請建築公司興建新體育館。"},{"en":"If a construction company joins the project, the idea can move from laboratory testing to real roads.","zh":"如果建築公司加入項目，想法就可以從實驗室測試走向真實道路。"},{"en":"The phrase names a company that carries out building work.","zh":"這個短語指出執行建造工程的公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"discuss the location of","meaning":"討論……的地點","examples":[{"en":"The company is discussing the location of the next road installation.","zh":"該公司正在討論下一次道路安裝的地點。"},{"en":"To discuss the location of something means to talk about where it should be placed or built.","zh":"「discuss the location of」某物，意思是討論它應放置或建於哪裡。"},{"en":"Teachers may discuss the location of a new reading corner before moving furniture.","zh":"老師搬家具前可能討論新閱讀角的地點。"},{"en":"If a trial site is chosen carefully, the results may be more useful.","zh":"如果試驗地點被仔細選擇，結果可能更有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deciding where something should happen.","zh":"這個短語描述決定某事應在哪裡發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the next roll-out","meaning":"下一次正式推行","examples":[{"en":"The government is considering where the next roll-out should take place.","zh":"政府正考慮下一次正式推行應在哪裡進行。"},{"en":"The next roll-out means the next stage when a new product, service, or system is introduced more widely.","zh":"「the next roll-out」意思是新產品、服務或系統更廣泛推出的下一階段。"},{"en":"A school may plan the next roll-out of a new learning app after testing it with one class.","zh":"學校在一班試用新學習應用程式後，可能計劃下一次正式推行。"},{"en":"If the first road trial succeeds, the next roll-out may involve a longer road section.","zh":"如果首次道路試驗成功，下一次正式推行可能涉及更長路段。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a planned wider introduction.","zh":"這個短語描述有計劃的更廣泛引入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"depend on how much it costs","meaning":"取決於成本多少","examples":[{"en":"The success of the proposal will depend on how much it costs.","zh":"這項提議的成功將取決於成本多少。"},{"en":"To depend on how much it costs means to be influenced by whether the price is affordable.","zh":"「depend on how much it costs」意思是受價格是否可負擔影響。"},{"en":"A family’s decision to buy a new laptop may depend on how much it costs.","zh":"家庭是否購買新手提電腦，可能取決於成本多少。"},{"en":"If the road surface is too expensive, governments may hesitate to use it widely.","zh":"如果路面太昂貴，政府可能猶豫是否廣泛使用。"},{"en":"The phrase connects success or adoption with cost.","zh":"這個短語把成功或採用與成本連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"those affected by","meaning":"受……影響的人","examples":[{"en":"The new design offers hope to those affected by traffic noise.","zh":"新設計為受交通噪音影響的人帶來希望。"},{"en":"Those affected by something are the people who experience its impact or suffer because of it.","zh":"「those affected by」某事，是經歷其影響或因它受苦的人。"},{"en":"Schools may provide support to those affected by a sudden flood.","zh":"學校可能向受突發水災影響的人提供支援。"},{"en":"If residents are affected by traffic noise, quieter roads may improve daily life.","zh":"如果居民受交通噪音影響，較寧靜道路可能改善日常生活。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the people harmed or influenced by a problem.","zh":"這個短語指出受問題傷害或影響的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"quieter times ahead","meaning":"未來將會更加寧靜","examples":[{"en":"Residents near major roads may have quieter times ahead.","zh":"住在主要道路附近的居民未來可能會更加寧靜。"},{"en":"Quieter times ahead means the future may be less noisy or less disturbed.","zh":"「quieter times ahead」意思是未來可能較少噪音或較少受打擾。"},{"en":"A school beside a construction site may hope for quieter times ahead after the work finishes.","zh":"位於建築地盤旁的學校可能期望工程完成後未來更加寧靜。"},{"en":"If new road surfaces reduce noise, neighbourhoods may become calmer.","zh":"如果新路面減少噪音，社區可能變得更平靜。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a more peaceful future.","zh":"這個短語暗示更安寧的未來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"which paragraph contains","meaning":"哪一段包含……","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which paragraph contains each piece of information.","zh":"學生辨認哪一段包含每項資料。"},{"en":"Which paragraph contains asks students to find the paragraph where specific information appears.","zh":"「which paragraph contains」要求學生找出特定資料出現在哪一段。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may decide which paragraph contains a description of a problem.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能要判斷哪一段包含問題描述。"},{"en":"If students scan for key words carefully, they can locate the right paragraph faster.","zh":"如果學生仔細掃讀關鍵詞，就能更快找到正確段落。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common paragraph-matching instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見段落配對指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the following information","meaning":"以下資料","examples":[{"en":"The task asks students to locate the following information in the passage.","zh":"題目要求學生在文章中找出以下資料。"},{"en":"The following information means the details listed after the instruction.","zh":"「the following information」意思是指示後列出的細節。"},{"en":"A worksheet may ask students to find the following information: date, place, reason, and result.","zh":"工作紙可能要求學生找出以下資料：日期、地點、原因和結果。"},{"en":"If students understand what information is required, they can scan the passage more efficiently.","zh":"如果學生理解需要甚麼資料，就能更有效地掃讀文章。"},{"en":"The phrase points forward to a list of details.","zh":"這個短語指向後面的細節列表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a description of the form","meaning":"對形態的描述","examples":[{"en":"One paragraph contains a description of the form in which the surface is transported.","zh":"其中一段包含對路面運輸形態的描述。"},{"en":"A description of the form means an explanation of the shape or physical condition of something.","zh":"「a description of the form」意思是解釋某物的形狀或物理狀態。"},{"en":"A product manual may give a description of the form in which a table arrives, such as flat-packed pieces.","zh":"產品說明書可能描述桌子送達時的形態，例如平板包裝零件。"},{"en":"If the road surface is transported in a roll, its form affects how it is delivered and installed.","zh":"如果路面以卷狀運輸，其形態會影響運送和安裝方式。"},{"en":"The phrase asks what something looks like or how it is physically arranged.","zh":"這個短語問某物看起來如何或物理上如何安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be taken to its destination","meaning":"被運送到目的地","examples":[{"en":"The rolled surface is taken to its destination on a large drum.","zh":"捲起的路面被放在大型圓筒上運送到目的地。"},{"en":"To be taken to its destination means to be transported to the place where it is needed.","zh":"「be taken to its destination」意思是被運送到需要它的地方。"},{"en":"School lunch boxes are taken to their destination before students arrive.","zh":"學校飯盒在學生到達前被運送到目的地。"},{"en":"If road material can be carried on a drum, it can reach the work site ready for installation.","zh":"如果道路材料可以用圓筒運送，它到達工地時就已準備好安裝。"},{"en":"The phrase describes delivery to a final place.","zh":"這個短語描述送達最終地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"an explanation of how","meaning":"對……如何進行的解釋","examples":[{"en":"The passage provides an explanation of how the smooth surface is made.","zh":"文章提供對平滑路面如何製成的解釋。"},{"en":"An explanation of how something happens describes the steps or process behind it.","zh":"「an explanation of how」某事發生，是描述其背後步驟或過程。"},{"en":"A teacher may give an explanation of how rain forms before asking students to draw the water cycle.","zh":"老師可能先解釋雨如何形成，再要求學生畫水循環。"},{"en":"If students understand the process, they can answer diagram and flow-chart questions more easily.","zh":"如果學生理解過程，就能更容易回答圖表和流程圖題。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces process information.","zh":"這個短語引入過程資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"smooth road surface","meaning":"平滑路面","examples":[{"en":"Kuijpers uses a mould to produce a smooth road surface.","zh":"Kuijpers 使用模具製作平滑路面。"},{"en":"A smooth road surface is a road top layer that is even and has few bumps or rough points.","zh":"「smooth road surface」是平整且少凹凸或粗糙點的道路表層。"},{"en":"Cyclists prefer a smooth road surface because it makes riding safer and more comfortable.","zh":"單車手較喜歡平滑路面，因為它令騎行更安全舒服。"},{"en":"If the road surface is smooth, tyres vibrate less and create less noise.","zh":"如果路面平滑，車胎震動較少，產生的噪音也較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a flat, even driving surface.","zh":"這個短語描述平坦均勻的行車表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"something to be considered","meaning":"需要考慮的因素","examples":[{"en":"Cost is something to be considered when evaluating the proposal.","zh":"成本是評估該提議時需要考慮的因素。"},{"en":"Something to be considered is a factor that should be thought about before making a decision.","zh":"「something to be considered」是在作決定前應該思考的因素。"},{"en":"Travel time is something to be considered before choosing a new school.","zh":"選擇新學校前，交通時間是需要考慮的因素。"},{"en":"If a design is effective but too expensive, decision-makers may hesitate to adopt it.","zh":"如果設計有效但太昂貴，決策者可能猶豫是否採用。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies an important factor in judgment.","zh":"這個短語指出判斷中的重要因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"evaluate a proposal","meaning":"評估提議","examples":[{"en":"Researchers must evaluate the proposal’s effectiveness and cost.","zh":"研究人員必須評估該提議的效能和成本。"},{"en":"To evaluate a proposal means to judge its value, usefulness, risks, and practicality.","zh":"「evaluate a proposal」意思是判斷一項提議的價值、用途、風險和可行性。"},{"en":"A school committee may evaluate a proposal for longer lunch breaks before approving it.","zh":"學校委員會可能在批准前評估延長午膳時間的提議。"},{"en":"If a road design is costly, officials need evidence before supporting it.","zh":"如果道路設計昂貴，官員在支持前需要證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful assessment before action.","zh":"這個短語描述行動前的仔細評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"economic reasons for","meaning":"減低道路噪音的經濟原因","examples":[{"en":"There are several economic reasons for reducing road noise.","zh":"減低道路噪音有幾個經濟原因。"},{"en":"Economic reasons for something are financial or business-related reasons that support it.","zh":"「economic reasons for」某事，是支持它的財政或商業相關原因。"},{"en":"There are economic reasons for improving public transport, such as saving time and attracting workers.","zh":"改善公共交通有經濟原因，例如節省時間和吸引工人。"},{"en":"If noise lowers property values and productivity, reducing it has financial benefits.","zh":"如果噪音降低物業價值和生產力，減少噪音就有財政好處。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an action with money-related benefits.","zh":"這個短語把行動與金錢相關好處連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a generalisation about","meaning":"對……的概括說法","examples":[{"en":"The passage makes a generalisation about how vehicles use motorway lanes.","zh":"文章對車輛如何使用高速公路行車線作出概括說法。"},{"en":"A generalisation about something is a broad statement that describes what is usually true.","zh":"「a generalisation about」某事，是描述通常情況的廣泛說法。"},{"en":"Saying that teenagers use phones often is a generalisation about young people.","zh":"說青少年常用電話，是對年輕人的概括說法。"},{"en":"If trucks usually use one lane, engineers can design that lane for truck noise.","zh":"如果貨車通常使用某條行車線，工程師可以為該線設計處理貨車噪音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broad pattern, not an absolute rule.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛模式，而不是絕對規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"patterns of vehicle use","meaning":"車輛使用模式","examples":[{"en":"Different vehicles follow different patterns of use on major roads.","zh":"不同車輛在主要道路上有不同使用模式。"},{"en":"Patterns of vehicle use are regular ways in which vehicles move, choose lanes, or use roads.","zh":"「patterns of vehicle use」是車輛移動、選擇行車線或使用道路的規律方式。"},{"en":"Delivery vans may show different patterns of use during morning and evening hours.","zh":"送貨車在早上和晚上可能呈現不同使用模式。"},{"en":"If trucks use one lane more often, noise-control design can be adjusted for that lane.","zh":"如果貨車較常使用某條行車線，降噪設計可以針對該線調整。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated transport behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述重複出現的交通行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"major roads","meaning":"主要道路","examples":[{"en":"Heavy vehicles often use particular lanes on major roads.","zh":"重型車輛常在主要道路上使用特定行車線。"},{"en":"Major roads are important roads that carry large amounts of traffic between places.","zh":"「major roads」是承載大量交通並連接各地的重要道路。"},{"en":"A bus route may follow major roads because they connect many neighbourhoods.","zh":"巴士路線可能沿主要道路行駛，因為它們連接許多社區。"},{"en":"If major roads are noisy, many homes and workplaces may be affected.","zh":"如果主要道路嘈吵，許多住宅和工作場所可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes important, heavily used roads.","zh":"這個短語描述重要且使用量大的道路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a summary of","meaning":"對……的概述","examples":[{"en":"One paragraph gives a summary of the factors affecting road noise.","zh":"其中一段對影響道路噪音的因素作出概述。"},{"en":"A summary of something is a short account of its main points.","zh":"「a summary of」某事，是對其要點的簡短說明。"},{"en":"A teacher may give a summary of a chapter before students answer questions.","zh":"老師可能在學生回答問題前概述一章內容。"},{"en":"If students read the summary first, they may understand the main causes more quickly.","zh":"如果學生先讀概述，可能更快理解主要原因。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a brief overview.","zh":"這個短語描述簡短總覽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"affect noise levels","meaning":"影響噪音水平","examples":[{"en":"Surface texture and hardness affect noise levels on roads.","zh":"表面質感和硬度影響道路噪音水平。"},{"en":"To affect noise levels means to change how loud or quiet a place or object is.","zh":"「affect noise levels」意思是改變某地方或物件有多嘈吵或安靜。"},{"en":"Closing classroom doors can affect noise levels in a school corridor.","zh":"關上課室門可以影響學校走廊噪音水平。"},{"en":"If road texture makes tyres vibrate, it directly affects traffic noise.","zh":"如果路面質感令車胎震動，它就直接影響交通噪音。"},{"en":"The phrase links a factor with changes in loudness.","zh":"這個短語把某因素與聲音大小變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"label the diagram","meaning":"為圖表加上標示","examples":[{"en":"Students label the diagram using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的詞語為圖表加上標示。"},{"en":"To label the diagram means to write the correct names beside parts of a picture or drawing.","zh":"「label the diagram」意思是在圖片或圖畫各部分旁寫上正確名稱。"},{"en":"In science class, students label the diagram of a flower with words such as petal and stem.","zh":"在科學課中，學生為花的圖表加上 petal 和 stem 等標示。"},{"en":"If students understand the road structure, they can label its layers correctly.","zh":"如果學生理解道路結構，就能正確標示其各層。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction in diagram-completion questions.","zh":"這個短語是圖表填充題的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no more than one word and/or a number","meaning":"不多於一個詞及／或一個數字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer must contain no more than one word and/or a number.","zh":"每個答案必須包含不多於一個詞及／或一個數字。"},{"en":"No more than one word and/or a number means the answer may include only one word, one number, or one word plus one number.","zh":"「no more than one word and/or a number」意思是答案只可包含一個詞、一個數字，或一個詞加一個數字。"},{"en":"If the answer is “10 millimetres”, it fits because it contains a number and one word.","zh":"如果答案是 “10 millimetres”，它符合要求，因為包含一個數字和一個詞。"},{"en":"If students write extra words, the answer may be marked wrong even if the idea is right.","zh":"如果學生寫多餘詞語，即使意思正確，答案也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict answer-length rule.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格答案長度規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"cross section","meaning":"橫切面","examples":[{"en":"The diagram shows a cross section of the proposed road.","zh":"圖表顯示建議道路的橫切面。"},{"en":"A cross section is a view of something as if it has been cut through to show the inside.","zh":"「cross section」是像把某物切開後顯示內部的視圖。"},{"en":"A biology textbook may show a cross section of a leaf to reveal its layers.","zh":"生物課本可能顯示葉子的橫切面，以展示其層次。"},{"en":"If students see a road cross section, they can understand its upper and lower layers.","zh":"如果學生看見道路橫切面，就能理解其上下兩層。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an internal side view of a structure.","zh":"這個短語描述結構內部的側面視圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"proposed noise-reducing road","meaning":"建議中的降噪道路","examples":[{"en":"The diagram illustrates Kuijpers’ proposed noise-reducing road.","zh":"圖表展示 Kuijpers 建議中的降噪道路。"},{"en":"A proposed noise-reducing road is a suggested road design intended to make traffic quieter.","zh":"「proposed noise-reducing road」是建議用來令交通更安靜的道路設計。"},{"en":"A city council may review a proposed noise-reducing road before approving construction.","zh":"市議會可能在批准工程前審視建議中的降噪道路。"},{"en":"If the proposal works, residents near highways may hear less traffic noise.","zh":"如果該提議有效，高速公路附近居民可能聽到較少交通噪音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a road design not yet widely adopted.","zh":"這個短語描述尚未被廣泛採用的道路設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete the table","meaning":"完成表格","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the table using words from the box.","zh":"學生使用方框中的詞語完成表格。"},{"en":"To complete the table means to fill in missing information in a table.","zh":"「complete the table」意思是在表格中填入缺失資料。"},{"en":"In a reading lesson, students complete the table by matching headings with details from the text.","zh":"在閱讀課中，學生透過把標題與文本細節配對來完成表格。"},{"en":"If students understand the passage structure, they can fill the table more accurately.","zh":"如果學生理解文章結構，就能更準確地填表。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"list of words","meaning":"詞語列表","examples":[{"en":"The list of words contains both correct answers and distractors.","zh":"詞語列表包含正確答案和干擾選項。"},{"en":"A list of words is a group of possible words given for students to choose from.","zh":"「list of words」是一組給學生選擇的可能詞語。"},{"en":"A vocabulary exercise may provide a list of words at the top of the page.","zh":"詞彙練習可能在頁面頂部提供詞語列表。"},{"en":"If the list contains distractors, students must check meaning carefully before choosing.","zh":"如果列表包含干擾選項，學生選擇前必須仔細核對意思。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the answer options in some reading tasks.","zh":"這個短語描述某些閱讀題中的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"components and functions","meaning":"組件與功能","examples":[{"en":"The table summarises the road’s components and functions.","zh":"表格概述道路的組件與功能。"},{"en":"Components and functions means the parts of something and what each part does.","zh":"「components and functions」意思是某物的各部分以及每部分做甚麼。"},{"en":"A science diagram may show the components and functions of the human eye.","zh":"科學圖表可能展示人眼的組件與功能。"},{"en":"If students know each road layer’s function, they can understand the whole design.","zh":"如果學生知道每個道路層的功能，就能理解整個設計。"},{"en":"The phrase links structure with purpose.","zh":"這個短語把結構與用途連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"upper and lower layers","meaning":"上下兩層","examples":[{"en":"Stones are used in both the upper and lower layers.","zh":"上下兩層都使用石塊。"},{"en":"Upper and lower layers are the top and bottom parts of a layered structure.","zh":"「upper and lower layers」是分層結構中的上面和下面部分。"},{"en":"A sandwich has upper and lower layers of bread with filling between them.","zh":"三文治有上下兩層麵包，中間有餡料。"},{"en":"If the two road layers use different stone sizes, they can perform different functions.","zh":"如果兩個道路層使用不同大小的石塊，它們可以發揮不同功能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a structure built in levels.","zh":"這個短語描述以層次建成的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reduce oscillations","meaning":"減低振盪","examples":[{"en":"The pores reduce oscillations caused by moving air.","zh":"小孔減低由移動空氣造成的振盪。"},{"en":"To reduce oscillations means to make repeated vibrations or movements weaker.","zh":"「reduce oscillations」意思是令反覆震動或移動變弱。"},{"en":"A shock absorber reduces oscillations after a bicycle hits a bump.","zh":"單車撞上凹凸後，避震器會減低振盪。"},{"en":"If air movement oscillations are reduced, tyre noise may fall.","zh":"如果空氣移動造成的振盪被減少，車胎噪音可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes damping repeated motion.","zh":"這個短語描述減弱重複動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"air flow","meaning":"氣流","examples":[{"en":"Air flow through a tyre’s tread can create noise.","zh":"穿過車胎胎紋的氣流可以產生噪音。"},{"en":"Air flow is the movement of air through or around something.","zh":"「air flow」是空氣穿過或圍繞某物移動。"},{"en":"Opening a window improves air flow in a warm classroom.","zh":"打開窗戶可以改善悶熱課室中的氣流。"},{"en":"If air moves quickly through tyre grooves, it may vibrate and produce sound.","zh":"如果空氣快速穿過車胎凹槽，它可能震動並產生聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving air.","zh":"這個短語描述移動中的空氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"aid drainage","meaning":"有助排水","examples":[{"en":"The pores aid drainage by allowing water to escape.","zh":"小孔透過讓水離開而有助排水。"},{"en":"To aid drainage means to help water flow away from a surface or area.","zh":"「aid drainage」意思是幫助水從表面或地方流走。"},{"en":"Small holes in a plant pot aid drainage after watering.","zh":"花盆中的小孔在澆水後有助排水。"},{"en":"If road pores aid drainage, fewer puddles form during rain.","zh":"如果道路小孔有助排水，下雨時就較少形成水窪。"},{"en":"The phrase describes helping water leave a place.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助水離開某地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"drainage","meaning":"排水","examples":[{"en":"Efficient drainage makes the road safer in wet conditions.","zh":"有效排水令道路在潮濕情況下更安全。"},{"en":"Drainage is the process or system by which water is removed from an area.","zh":"「drainage」是從某區移除水分的過程或系統。"},{"en":"Good drainage prevents a school playground from flooding after heavy rain.","zh":"良好排水防止學校操場在大雨後水浸。"},{"en":"If drainage is poor, water stays on the road and increases accident risk.","zh":"如果排水差，水會留在路面並增加意外風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes water removal.","zh":"這個短語描述移除水分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"convert sound energy to heat","meaning":"將聲能轉化成熱能","examples":[{"en":"The resonators convert sound energy to heat.","zh":"共鳴器將聲能轉化成熱能。"},{"en":"To convert sound energy to heat means to change vibration energy into thermal energy.","zh":"「convert sound energy to heat」意思是把震動能量轉變成熱能。"},{"en":"Some acoustic panels convert sound energy to heat inside their fibres.","zh":"有些吸音板會在纖維內將聲能轉化成熱能。"},{"en":"If sound energy becomes heat, less sound remains to disturb nearby people.","zh":"如果聲能變成熱能，剩下打擾附近人們的聲音就較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one way sound is absorbed.","zh":"這個短語描述聲音被吸收的一種方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"remove waste material","meaning":"清除廢料","examples":[{"en":"Water flowing through the road helps remove waste material.","zh":"流經道路的水有助清除廢料。"},{"en":"To remove waste material means to take away dirt, particles, or unwanted matter.","zh":"「remove waste material」意思是移走污垢、微粒或不需要的物質。"},{"en":"A classroom cleaner removes waste material from bins and desks after school.","zh":"放學後，課室清潔工會從垃圾桶和書桌清除廢料。"},{"en":"If waste material blocks road pores, drainage and sound absorption may become weaker.","zh":"如果廢料堵塞道路小孔，排水和吸音可能變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes clearing unwanted material away.","zh":"這個短語描述移走不需要的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be adapted to absorb","meaning":"可調整以吸收……","examples":[{"en":"The resonators can be adapted to absorb different sound frequencies.","zh":"共鳴器可調整以吸收不同聲音頻率。"},{"en":"To be adapted to absorb something means to be changed so it can take in a particular kind of sound or energy.","zh":"「be adapted to absorb」某物，意思是被改動以吸收某特定聲音或能量。"},{"en":"A classroom can be adapted to absorb noise by adding carpets and wall panels.","zh":"課室可以透過加入地氈和牆板調整成能吸收噪音。"},{"en":"If road resonators are adapted for truck noise, they may reduce low-frequency sounds better.","zh":"如果道路共鳴器為貨車噪音作調整，它們可能更好地減少低頻聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes modifying a design for a specific purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述為特定目的修改設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"different frequencies","meaning":"不同頻率","examples":[{"en":"Different vehicles produce sound at different frequencies.","zh":"不同車輛產生不同頻率的聲音。"},{"en":"Different frequencies are different rates of vibration in sound waves.","zh":"「different frequencies」是聲波中不同的震動速率。"},{"en":"A deep drum and a high whistle produce sounds at different frequencies.","zh":"低沉鼓聲和高音哨聲產生不同頻率的聲音。"},{"en":"If cars and trucks make different frequencies, one road design may need several sound-control settings.","zh":"如果汽車和貨車發出不同頻率，一種道路設計可能需要幾種聲音控制設定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes variation in pitch or vibration rate.","zh":"這個短語描述音高或震動速率上的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"dissipation of sound energy","meaning":"聲能的消散","examples":[{"en":"The cavities allow the dissipation of sound energy into the concrete.","zh":"空腔讓聲能消散至混凝土中。"},{"en":"Dissipation of sound energy means sound energy spreads out and becomes weaker, often as heat.","zh":"「dissipation of sound energy」意思是聲能擴散並變弱，通常轉成熱能。"},{"en":"Thick curtains help the dissipation of sound energy in a noisy room.","zh":"厚窗簾有助嘈吵房間中聲能的消散。"},{"en":"If sound energy dissipates inside concrete, less noise reflects back to the road.","zh":"如果聲能在混凝土內消散，反射回道路的噪音就較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the weakening and spreading of sound energy.","zh":"這個短語描述聲能變弱和散開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"noise sources","meaning":"噪音來源","examples":[{"en":"Tyres and engines are different noise sources associated with vehicles.","zh":"車胎和引擎是與車輛相關的不同噪音來源。"},{"en":"Noise sources are the people, machines, objects, or activities that produce sound.","zh":"「noise sources」是產生聲音的人、機器、物件或活動。"},{"en":"In a classroom, noise sources may include fans, corridors, phones, and talking students.","zh":"在課室中，噪音來源可能包括風扇、走廊、電話和說話的學生。"},{"en":"If engineers identify the main noise sources, they can design better solutions.","zh":"如果工程師找出主要噪音來源，就能設計更好解決方案。"},{"en":"The phrase names where noise comes from.","zh":"這個短語指出噪音來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 110 - Quiet roads ahead.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 111":[{"front":"the final archaeological frontier","meaning":"最後的考古前沿","examples":[{"en":"Space may become the final archaeological frontier.","zh":"太空可能成為最後的考古前沿。"},{"en":"The final archaeological frontier means the last major unexplored area where archaeologists may study human remains and artefacts.","zh":"最後的考古前沿，指考古學家可能研究人類遺跡和文物的最後大型未探索領域。"},{"en":"Just as ancient cities became archaeological sites, old spacecraft and landing places may one day be studied as evidence of human history.","zh":"正如古代城市成為考古遺址，舊太空船和着陸地點有一天也可能被研究為人類歷史證據。"},{"en":"If humans leave objects on the Moon and Mars, those places can become new archaeological frontiers.","zh":"如果人類在月球和火星留下物件，那些地方就可以成為新的考古前沿。"},{"en":"The phrase presents space as the next great field for archaeology, not only for science fiction.","zh":"這個短語把太空呈現為考古學下一個重大領域，而不只是科幻題材。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have a long way to go","meaning":"還有很長的路要走","examples":[{"en":"Space travel may still have a long way to go.","zh":"太空旅行可能仍然還有很長的路要走。"},{"en":"To have a long way to go means to need much more progress before something is fully developed or successful.","zh":"還有很長的路要走，指某事在完全發展或成功前仍需要很多進步。"},{"en":"A student who knows basic grammar but cannot speak fluently still has a long way to go.","zh":"一個懂基本文法但不能流利說話的學生，仍然還有很長的路要走。"},{"en":"If space travel is expensive, risky and rare, it clearly still needs major development.","zh":"如果太空旅行昂貴、危險又罕見，它明顯仍需要重大發展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes incomplete progress, not total failure.","zh":"這個短語描述進展尚未完成，而不是完全失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the notion of","meaning":"……的概念","examples":[{"en":"The notion of archaeology in space is already attracting attention.","zh":"太空考古的概念已經引起關注。"},{"en":"The notion of something means the idea or concept of it.","zh":"某事的概念，指關於它的想法或觀念。"},{"en":"The notion of online exams became more familiar when schools moved lessons onto digital platforms.","zh":"當學校把課堂轉到電子平台，網上考試的概念變得更熟悉。"},{"en":"If the notion of space archaeology sounds strange at first, examples of lunar landing sites make it easier to understand.","zh":"如果太空考古的概念起初聽起來奇怪，月球着陸地點的例子會令它更容易理解。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an idea, often one that needs explanation.","zh":"這個短語引入一個想法，通常是需要解釋的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"archaeological research","meaning":"考古研究","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are beginning to consider archaeological research in space.","zh":"科學家開始考慮在太空進行考古研究。"},{"en":"Archaeological research is the study of past human activity through objects, sites and physical remains.","zh":"考古研究是透過物件、遺址和實物遺存研究過去人類活動。"},{"en":"Archaeological research can reveal how people lived, worked, travelled and used tools in the past.","zh":"考古研究可以揭示過去人們如何生活、工作、旅行和使用工具。"},{"en":"If astronauts leave equipment on the Moon, future research may study those objects like artefacts.","zh":"如果太空人在月球留下設備，未來研究可能像研究文物一樣研究那些物件。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to systematic study of material evidence from the past.","zh":"這個短語指對過去物質證據的有系統研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"heritage management","meaning":"文化遺產管理","examples":[{"en":"Heritage management may eventually be necessary on the Moon and Mars.","zh":"文化遺產管理最終可能在月球和火星上變得必要。"},{"en":"Heritage management means protecting, organising and deciding how to treat historically important sites or objects.","zh":"文化遺產管理指保護、組織和決定如何處理具有歷史重要性的遺址或物件。"},{"en":"A city uses heritage management when it protects old buildings from careless redevelopment.","zh":"城市保護舊建築免受草率重建破壞時，就是在進行文化遺產管理。"},{"en":"If tourists visit lunar landing sites, heritage management may prevent damage to footprints and equipment.","zh":"如果遊客參觀月球着陸遺址，文化遺產管理可能防止腳印和設備受損。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on preserving cultural value for the future.","zh":"這個短語強調為未來保存文化價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be of concern to","meaning":"引起……關注","examples":[{"en":"Archaeology in space is already of concern to scientists and environmentalists.","zh":"太空考古已經引起科學家和環保人士關注。"},{"en":"To be of concern to someone means to matter to them because it may involve a problem, risk or responsibility.","zh":"引起某人關注，指因可能涉及問題、風險或責任而對他們重要。"},{"en":"Air pollution is of concern to parents because it may affect children’s health.","zh":"空氣污染引起家長關注，因為它可能影響孩子健康。"},{"en":"If space tourists could damage historic sites, the issue becomes important to archaeologists.","zh":"如果太空旅客可能破壞歷史遺址，這問題就對考古學家重要。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a topic deserves attention from a particular group.","zh":"這個短語顯示某題目值得特定群體注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for much of his career","meaning":"在其大部分職業生涯中","examples":[{"en":"For much of his career, Ben Finney studied Polynesian technology.","zh":"在其大部分職業生涯中，Ben Finney 研究波利尼西亞技術。"},{"en":"For much of his career means during a large part of a person’s working life.","zh":"在其大部分職業生涯中，指在某人工作生涯很大部分時間內。"},{"en":"For much of her career, a teacher may focus on helping weaker students build confidence.","zh":"在一位老師大部分職業生涯中，她可能專注幫助較弱學生建立信心。"},{"en":"If someone studies one topic for decades, that topic becomes central to their professional identity.","zh":"如果某人數十年研究一個題目，該題目就成為其專業身份核心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a long period within someone’s career.","zh":"這個短語描述某人職業生涯中的長時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"technology once used by","meaning":"曾由……使用的技術","examples":[{"en":"Finney studied technology once used by Polynesians.","zh":"Finney 研究曾由波利尼西亞人使用的技術。"},{"en":"Technology once used by a group means tools, methods or skills that people in that group used in the past.","zh":"曾由某群體使用的技術，指該群體過去使用的工具、方法或技能。"},{"en":"Museums may display farming technology once used by villagers before modern machines arrived.","zh":"博物館可能展示現代機器出現前曾由村民使用的農業技術。"},{"en":"If researchers study old navigation tools, they can understand how people travelled before GPS.","zh":"如果研究者研究舊導航工具，就能理解人們在 GPS 出現前如何旅行。"},{"en":"The phrase connects past communities with the practical tools they used.","zh":"這個短語把過去社群與其使用的實用工具連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"colonize islands","meaning":"移居並開拓島嶼","examples":[{"en":"Polynesians used advanced technology to colonize islands in the Pacific.","zh":"波利尼西亞人使用先進技術移居並開拓太平洋島嶼。"},{"en":"To colonize islands means to travel to islands, settle there and establish communities.","zh":"移居並開拓島嶼，指前往島嶼、定居並建立社群。"},{"en":"Early settlers needed boats, navigation skills and food supplies to colonize distant islands.","zh":"早期定居者需要船隻、導航技巧和食物供應，才能移居並開拓遙遠島嶼。"},{"en":"If people colonize new islands, their culture may change as they adapt to new environments.","zh":"如果人們開拓新島嶼，其文化可能因適應新環境而改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes settlement and expansion into island territories.","zh":"這個短語描述向島嶼地區定居和擴展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"it would not be premature to","meaning":"現在開始……並不算過早","examples":[{"en":"Finney suggested that it would not be premature to consider space archaeology.","zh":"Finney 認為現在開始考慮太空考古並不算過早。"},{"en":"It would not be premature to do something means it is not too early to begin thinking about or doing it.","zh":"現在開始做某事並不算過早，指開始思考或做該事並非太早。"},{"en":"It would not be premature to teach students exam strategy before they start full practice papers.","zh":"在學生開始完整練習卷前教考試策略，並不算過早。"},{"en":"If future tourists may damage lunar sites, planning protection now is not too early.","zh":"如果未來遊客可能破壞月球遺址，現在規劃保護並不太早。"},{"en":"The phrase justifies early preparation.","zh":"這個短語為提早準備提供理由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"begin thinking about","meaning":"開始思考","examples":[{"en":"Researchers should begin thinking about the archaeology of space sites.","zh":"研究者應開始思考太空遺址的考古問題。"},{"en":"To begin thinking about something means to start considering it seriously.","zh":"開始思考某事，指開始認真考慮它。"},{"en":"A family may begin thinking about university costs before a child reaches senior secondary school.","zh":"家庭可能在孩子升上高中前開始思考大學費用。"},{"en":"If a problem may appear in the future, early thinking can prevent rushed decisions later.","zh":"如果問題可能在未來出現，早期思考可以避免日後倉促決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the first stage of planning or reflection.","zh":"這個短語描述規劃或反思的第一階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"aerospace sites","meaning":"航天遺址","examples":[{"en":"Future archaeologists may study Russian and American aerospace sites.","zh":"未來考古學家可能研究俄羅斯和美國的航天遺址。"},{"en":"Aerospace sites are places connected with aircraft, rockets, satellites or space missions.","zh":"航天遺址是與飛機、火箭、衛星或太空任務相關的地點。"},{"en":"A launch pad, a mission-control centre or an abandoned probe can become an aerospace site.","zh":"發射台、任務控制中心或廢棄探測器都可以成為航天遺址。"},{"en":"If a site records an important step in flight or space exploration, it may have historical value.","zh":"如果某地點記錄飛行或太空探索的重要一步，它可能具有歷史價值。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to locations linked to air and space technology.","zh":"這個短語指與航空和太空技術相關的地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"point out that","meaning":"指出","examples":[{"en":"Finney pointed out that future archaeologists would study off-Earth sites.","zh":"Finney 指出未來考古學家會研究地球以外的遺址。"},{"en":"To point out that something is true means to draw attention to it clearly.","zh":"指出某事為真，指清楚把注意力引向它。"},{"en":"A teacher may point out that a wrong answer still uses the correct grammar pattern.","zh":"老師可能指出錯誤答案仍使用了正確文法結構。"},{"en":"If a scholar points out a future risk, readers may start taking the issue seriously.","zh":"如果學者指出未來風險，讀者可能開始認真看待該問題。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an observation or important reminder.","zh":"這個短語引入觀察或重要提醒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"just as…, … will…","meaning":"正如……，……也將會……","examples":[{"en":"Just as scholars study Polynesian sites, future archaeologists will study sites in space.","zh":"正如學者研究波利尼西亞遺址，未來考古學家也將會研究太空遺址。"},{"en":"Just as A, B will means B is expected to happen in a similar way to A.","zh":"“Just as A, B will” 指 B 預計會以類似 A 的方式發生。"},{"en":"Just as students practise grammar before writing, they will need examples before speaking confidently.","zh":"正如學生寫作前練習文法，他們自信說話前也將會需要例子。"},{"en":"If one kind of exploration leaves archaeological traces, space exploration may do the same.","zh":"如果一種探索會留下考古痕跡，太空探索也可能如此。"},{"en":"The structure creates a clear comparison between present knowledge and future expectation.","zh":"這個結構在現有知識和未來預期之間建立清楚比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"archaeological records","meaning":"考古記錄","examples":[{"en":"Scholars use archaeological records to study cultural development.","zh":"學者使用考古記錄研究文化發展。"},{"en":"Archaeological records are physical evidence from the past, such as tools, buildings, footprints and objects.","zh":"考古記錄是來自過去的實物證據，例如工具、建築、腳印和物件。"},{"en":"Old pottery and stone tools can form archaeological records of how a community lived.","zh":"舊陶器和石器可以構成一個社群如何生活的考古記錄。"},{"en":"If written history is missing, archaeological records may provide the strongest evidence.","zh":"如果缺乏文字歷史，考古記錄可能提供最有力證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to material traces that help reconstruct the past.","zh":"這個短語指幫助重建過去的物質痕跡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"investigate how","meaning":"研究……如何","examples":[{"en":"Researchers investigate how communities changed as they explored new regions.","zh":"研究者研究社群在探索新地區時如何改變。"},{"en":"To investigate how something happens means to study the process or method behind it.","zh":"研究某事如何發生，指探討其背後的過程或方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may investigate how students revise before designing better study advice.","zh":"老師可能先研究學生如何溫習，再設計更好的學習建議。"},{"en":"If researchers investigate how settlers adapted, they look for evidence of changes in tools, food and social life.","zh":"如果研究者研究定居者如何適應，他們會尋找工具、食物和社會生活改變的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on understanding process, not only final results.","zh":"這個短語強調理解過程，而不只是最終結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"diverge culturally","meaning":"在文化上逐漸分化","examples":[{"en":"Polynesian communities diverged culturally as they spread across the Pacific.","zh":"波利尼西亞社群在散布至太平洋各地時，在文化上逐漸分化。"},{"en":"To diverge culturally means to become different in customs, language, beliefs or social practices over time.","zh":"在文化上逐漸分化，指習俗、語言、信念或社會做法隨時間變得不同。"},{"en":"Two branches of a family may diverge culturally after living in different countries for generations.","zh":"一個家庭的兩個分支在不同國家生活幾代後，可能在文化上逐漸分化。"},{"en":"If communities settle on distant islands, local environments can push their cultures in different directions.","zh":"如果社群定居在遙遠島嶼，本地環境可以把其文化推向不同方向。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cultural separation and difference developing gradually.","zh":"這個短語描述文化分離和差異逐步形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"explore the Pacific","meaning":"探索太平洋","examples":[{"en":"Polynesians explored the Pacific and settled on distant islands.","zh":"波利尼西亞人探索太平洋，並在遙遠島嶼定居。"},{"en":"To explore the Pacific means to travel through the Pacific Ocean to discover, navigate or settle places.","zh":"探索太平洋，指穿越太平洋以發現、航行或定居某些地方。"},{"en":"Ancient sailors needed stars, winds and ocean knowledge to explore the Pacific safely.","zh":"古代航海者需要星象、風向和海洋知識，才能安全探索太平洋。"},{"en":"If people explore a wide ocean, their journeys may leave evidence in tools, stories and settlements.","zh":"如果人們探索廣闊海洋，其旅程可能在工具、故事和定居點中留下證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long-distance movement across a vast ocean region.","zh":"這個短語描述跨越巨大海洋區域的長距離移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"off-Earth sites","meaning":"地球以外的遺址","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists may one day study off-Earth sites.","zh":"考古學家有一天可能研究地球以外的遺址。"},{"en":"Off-Earth sites are places beyond Earth, such as sites on the Moon, Mars or other bodies in space.","zh":"地球以外的遺址，是地球之外的地方，例如月球、火星或其他太空天體上的遺址。"},{"en":"A lunar landing area could become an off-Earth site with historical and scientific value.","zh":"月球着陸區可以成為具有歷史和科學價值的地球以外遺址。"},{"en":"If humans build bases on Mars, those bases may later be studied as off-Earth heritage.","zh":"如果人類在火星建立基地，那些基地日後可能被研究為地球以外文化遺產。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies locations outside our planet.","zh":"這個短語指出我們星球以外的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"trace the development of","meaning":"追溯……的發展","examples":[{"en":"Space sites could help archaeologists trace the development of humans in space.","zh":"太空遺址可以幫助考古學家追溯人類在太空中的發展。"},{"en":"To trace the development of something means to follow and explain how it changed over time.","zh":"追溯某事的發展，指跟隨並解釋它如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"A historian may trace the development of public transport from horse carts to electric trains.","zh":"歷史學家可能追溯公共交通由馬車到電動列車的發展。"},{"en":"If researchers study early spacecraft and later bases, they can see how human space activity evolved.","zh":"如果研究者研究早期太空船和後來基地，就能看見人類太空活動如何演變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reconstructing a history of change.","zh":"這個短語描述重建變化歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"conduct fieldwork","meaning":"進行田野考察","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are unlikely to conduct archaeological fieldwork in space soon.","zh":"研究者不太可能很快在太空進行考古田野考察。"},{"en":"To conduct fieldwork means to do research directly at the site being studied.","zh":"進行田野考察，指直接在研究地點進行研究。"},{"en":"Geography students may conduct fieldwork by measuring traffic and interviewing residents.","zh":"地理學生可能透過量度交通和訪問居民進行田野考察。"},{"en":"If archaeologists conduct fieldwork on the Moon, they would examine objects and locations in person or by robots.","zh":"如果考古學家在月球進行田野考察，他們會親自或透過機械人檢查物件和地點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research outside the office or laboratory.","zh":"這個短語描述在辦公室或實驗室以外進行研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in the near future","meaning":"在不久的將來","examples":[{"en":"Fieldwork on the Moon is unlikely to take place in the near future.","zh":"在不久的將來，月球田野考察不太可能發生。"},{"en":"In the near future means soon, within a relatively short time from now.","zh":"在不久的將來，指從現在起相對短時間內。"},{"en":"A school may introduce a new timetable in the near future if the trial is successful.","zh":"如果試行成功，學校可能在不久的將來推出新時間表。"},{"en":"If a project is unlikely in the near future, it may still happen later but not soon.","zh":"如果某項目在不久將來不太可能發生，它仍可能日後發生，但不是很快。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a short-term future time frame.","zh":"這個短語給出短期未來時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be convinced that","meaning":"深信","examples":[{"en":"Finney was convinced that space archaeology would eventually become possible.","zh":"Finney 深信太空考古最終會成為可能。"},{"en":"To be convinced that something is true means to strongly believe it because of evidence or reasoning.","zh":"深信某事為真，指因證據或推理而強烈相信它。"},{"en":"A doctor may be convinced that a patient is improving after several test results become normal.","zh":"幾項檢查結果恢復正常後，醫生可能深信病人正在改善。"},{"en":"If a scholar is convinced, they are not merely guessing; they think the idea is strongly supported.","zh":"如果學者深信某事，他不是純粹猜測，而是認為該想法有力支持。"},{"en":"The phrase shows firm belief.","zh":"這個短語顯示堅定信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a growing awareness","meaning":"日益增加的認知","examples":[{"en":"There is a growing awareness that commercial travel to space is approaching.","zh":"人們日益意識到商業太空旅行正在接近。"},{"en":"A growing awareness means more and more people are beginning to understand or notice something.","zh":"日益增加的認知，指越來越多人開始理解或注意到某事。"},{"en":"There is a growing awareness among students that sleep affects exam performance.","zh":"學生越來越意識到睡眠會影響考試表現。"},{"en":"If people become more aware of future space tourism, they may start asking how historic sites will be protected.","zh":"如果人們更意識到未來太空旅遊，就可能開始詢問歷史遺址如何被保護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes increasing public or professional recognition.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾或專業界認知增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it will not be long before","meaning":"不久之後便會","examples":[{"en":"It may not be long before tourists reach the Moon.","zh":"可能不久之後遊客便會到達月球。"},{"en":"It will not be long before something happens means it is expected to happen soon.","zh":"不久之後某事便會發生，指預計它很快會發生。"},{"en":"It will not be long before students receive their exam results after marking is finished.","zh":"評卷完成後，不久學生便會收到考試成績。"},{"en":"If technology and funding improve quickly, lunar tourism may become a near-term reality.","zh":"如果技術和資金迅速改善，月球旅遊可能成為近期現實。"},{"en":"The phrase predicts that an event is approaching.","zh":"這個短語預測某事件正在接近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"corporate adventurers","meaning":"企業探險者","examples":[{"en":"Corporate adventurers may soon travel to the Moon and Mars.","zh":"企業探險者可能很快前往月球和火星。"},{"en":"Corporate adventurers are private companies or business-backed travellers who take risks in new commercial frontiers.","zh":"企業探險者是私人公司或由商業支持、在新商業前沿冒險的人。"},{"en":"A company funding deep-sea tourism could be called a corporate adventurer.","zh":"資助深海旅遊的公司可以被稱為企業探險者。"},{"en":"If corporate adventurers enter space, profit may become a major force in exploration.","zh":"如果企業探險者進入太空，利潤可能成為探索中的主要力量。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests business-driven exploration with risk and ambition.","zh":"這個短語暗示由商業推動、帶風險和野心的探索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"space tourists","meaning":"太空旅客","examples":[{"en":"Space tourists could pose a threat to historic sites.","zh":"太空旅客可能對歷史遺址構成威脅。"},{"en":"Space tourists are people who travel into space for leisure rather than professional science or government missions.","zh":"太空旅客是為休閒而非專業科學或政府任務前往太空的人。"},{"en":"A wealthy traveller taking a paid trip around the Moon would be a space tourist.","zh":"付費繞月旅行的富裕旅客就是太空旅客。"},{"en":"If space tourists walk near fragile footprints, they could accidentally damage them.","zh":"如果太空旅客走近脆弱腳印，他們可能意外破壞它們。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to leisure travellers beyond Earth.","zh":"這個短語指地球以外的休閒旅客。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a wealth of","meaning":"大量；豐富的","examples":[{"en":"The Moon contains a wealth of important archaeological sites.","zh":"月球包含大量重要考古遺址。"},{"en":"A wealth of something means a large amount or rich supply of it.","zh":"大量或豐富的某物，指有很多或充足供應。"},{"en":"A library with many books, recordings and archives contains a wealth of learning materials.","zh":"一間有許多書籍、錄音和檔案的圖書館，擁有豐富學習材料。"},{"en":"If the Moon has many historic landing sites and objects, it offers rich evidence for future study.","zh":"如果月球有許多歷史着陸點和物件，它就為未來研究提供豐富證據。"},{"en":"The phrase means abundance, not money only.","zh":"這個短語指豐富，不只指金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the history of space exploration","meaning":"太空探索史","examples":[{"en":"Many lunar sites are important to the history of space exploration.","zh":"許多月球遺址對太空探索史很重要。"},{"en":"The history of space exploration is the record of how humans and machines have travelled beyond Earth.","zh":"太空探索史是人類和機器如何離開地球旅行的記錄。"},{"en":"Old satellites, probes and landing sites can show the history of space exploration.","zh":"舊衛星、探測器和着陸地點可以展示太空探索史。"},{"en":"If a site marks the first human step on the Moon, it becomes historically important.","zh":"如果某地點標誌人類在月球上的第一步，它就具有歷史重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the development of human activity in space.","zh":"這個短語指人類太空活動的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"measures need to be taken","meaning":"必須採取措施","examples":[{"en":"Measures need to be taken to protect historic sites in space.","zh":"必須採取措施保護太空中的歷史遺址。"},{"en":"Measures need to be taken means actions must be planned and carried out to solve a problem.","zh":"必須採取措施，指必須計劃並執行行動來解決問題。"},{"en":"If students keep arriving late, measures need to be taken to improve punctuality.","zh":"如果學生持續遲到，必須採取措施改善準時情況。"},{"en":"If lunar sites are fragile, rules, signs or barriers may be needed before tourists arrive.","zh":"如果月球遺址脆弱，在遊客到達前可能需要規則、標示或屏障。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that action is necessary.","zh":"這個短語表示行動是必要的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in addition to","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"In addition to corporations, careless visitors could damage the sites.","zh":"除了企業之外，粗心訪客也可能破壞遺址。"},{"en":"In addition to means besides or as well as something already mentioned.","zh":"除了某事之外，指除了已提到的事物，也包括另一事物。"},{"en":"In addition to homework, students may need time for rest and exercise.","zh":"除了功課之外，學生可能需要休息和運動時間。"},{"en":"If both companies and tourists can cause damage, protection must consider more than one risk.","zh":"如果公司和遊客都可能造成破壞，保護工作就必須考慮多於一種風險。"},{"en":"The phrase adds another item or factor.","zh":"這個短語加入另一項事物或因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"profit-seeking corporations","meaning":"牟利企業","examples":[{"en":"Profit-seeking corporations may threaten archaeological remains.","zh":"牟利企業可能威脅考古遺存。"},{"en":"Profit-seeking corporations are companies mainly aiming to make money.","zh":"牟利企業是主要目標為賺錢的公司。"},{"en":"A tourism company that sells expensive lunar trips is a profit-seeking corporation.","zh":"銷售昂貴月球旅行的旅遊公司就是牟利企業。"},{"en":"If profit becomes more important than preservation, historic objects may be put at risk.","zh":"如果利潤比保存更重要，歷史物件可能陷入風險。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the commercial motive behind corporate action.","zh":"這個短語突出企業行動背後的商業動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"potentially destructive forces","meaning":"潛在破壞力量","examples":[{"en":"Scholars have identified several potentially destructive forces.","zh":"學者已識別幾種潛在破壞力量。"},{"en":"Potentially destructive forces are people, actions or pressures that could cause damage.","zh":"潛在破壞力量是可能造成損害的人、行動或壓力。"},{"en":"Heavy tourism, careless construction and pollution can be potentially destructive forces for an old village.","zh":"大量旅遊、草率建設和污染可以成為舊村落的潛在破壞力量。"},{"en":"If such forces are not controlled, fragile heritage may disappear.","zh":"如果這些力量不受控制，脆弱文化遺產可能消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes risks that may become harmful.","zh":"這個短語描述可能變得有害的風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"souvenir hunting","meaning":"搜集紀念品的行為","examples":[{"en":"Souvenir hunting could result in objects being removed from historic sites.","zh":"搜集紀念品的行為可能導致物件從歷史遺址被移走。"},{"en":"Souvenir hunting means searching for and taking objects as keepsakes, often without permission.","zh":"搜集紀念品的行為指尋找並拿走物件作紀念，通常未經批准。"},{"en":"Tourists who take stones from an ancient ruin are engaging in souvenir hunting.","zh":"從古代遺址拿走石頭的遊客，就是在搜集紀念品。"},{"en":"If many visitors remove small objects, a historic site can lose important evidence.","zh":"如果許多訪客移走小物件，歷史遺址可能失去重要證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a harmful collecting behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述有害的收藏行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"unmonitored scientific sampling","meaning":"不受監察的科學採樣","examples":[{"en":"Unmonitored scientific sampling may damage sensitive sites.","zh":"不受監察的科學採樣可能破壞敏感遺址。"},{"en":"Unmonitored scientific sampling means taking research samples without proper supervision or control.","zh":"不受監察的科學採樣，指在沒有適當監督或管制下取研究樣本。"},{"en":"Scientists collecting soil from a protected wetland without permission would be doing unmonitored sampling.","zh":"科學家未經批准從受保護濕地採集泥土，就是進行不受監察的採樣。"},{"en":"If sampling is not monitored, researchers may accidentally remove too much material or disturb fragile evidence.","zh":"如果採樣不受監察，研究者可能意外移走太多材料或擾亂脆弱證據。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that even scientific work can be harmful without control.","zh":"這個短語提醒，即使科學工作沒有管制也可能有害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"remote polar regions","meaning":"偏遠極地地區","examples":[{"en":"Similar damage has already occurred in remote polar regions.","zh":"類似破壞已經在偏遠極地地區發生。"},{"en":"Remote polar regions are faraway areas near the North or South Pole where few people live.","zh":"偏遠極地地區是接近北極或南極、少有人居住的遙遠地區。"},{"en":"Researchers visiting remote polar regions must avoid damaging fragile ice, wildlife and historic huts.","zh":"到訪偏遠極地地區的研究者必須避免破壞脆弱冰層、野生動物和歷史小屋。"},{"en":"If damage can happen in isolated polar areas, similar risks may exist on the Moon.","zh":"如果破壞能在孤立極地地區發生，月球上也可能有類似風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes distant, difficult-to-reach cold regions.","zh":"這個短語描述遙遠、難以到達的寒冷地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"propose a mission","meaning":"提議一項任務","examples":[{"en":"One company proposed a robotic mission across the Moon.","zh":"一間公司提議一項橫越月球的機械任務。"},{"en":"To propose a mission means to suggest a planned journey or operation for approval.","zh":"提議一項任務，指提出一個旅程或行動計劃以供批准。"},{"en":"A science club may propose a mission to clean a beach and record the types of waste found there.","zh":"科學學會可能提議一項清潔海灘並記錄垃圾種類的任務。"},{"en":"If a company proposes a lunar mission, experts may ask whether it is safe for historic sites.","zh":"如果公司提議月球任務，專家可能詢問它對歷史遺址是否安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes putting forward a planned operation.","zh":"這個短語描述提出一項計劃中的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"robotic lunar rover","meaning":"機械月球車","examples":[{"en":"The proposed mission would use a robotic lunar rover.","zh":"擬議任務會使用一部機械月球車。"},{"en":"A robotic lunar rover is a remote-controlled or autonomous vehicle designed to travel on the Moon.","zh":"機械月球車是設計在月球上行駛的遙控或自動車輛。"},{"en":"A rover can take photos, collect data and move across rough ground without carrying humans.","zh":"月球車可以拍照、收集數據，並在崎嶇地面行駛而不用載人。"},{"en":"If a lunar rover drives too close to historic footprints, its wheels may damage them.","zh":"如果月球車駛得太近歷史腳印，其車輪可能破壞它們。"},{"en":"The phrase names a machine vehicle used for Moon exploration.","zh":"這個短語指出用於月球探索的機械車輛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Tranquility Base","meaning":"Tranquility Base 月球遺址","examples":[{"en":"Tranquility Base is one of the Moon’s most famous historic sites.","zh":"Tranquility Base 是月球上最著名的歷史遺址之一。"},{"en":"Tranquility Base is the lunar site where Apollo 11 astronauts first landed on the Moon.","zh":"Tranquility Base 是 Apollo 11 太空人首次登月的月球地點。"},{"en":"A school lesson about space history may mention Tranquility Base as a turning point in human exploration.","zh":"關於太空史的學校課堂可能提到 Tranquility Base 是人類探索的轉捩點。"},{"en":"If tourists visit Tranquility Base without controls, historic footprints and equipment could be damaged.","zh":"如果遊客在沒有管制下參觀 Tranquility Base，歷史腳印和設備可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a specific Moon landing site of major heritage value.","zh":"這個短語指具有重大文化遺產價值的特定月球着陸點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rumble across","meaning":"隆隆地駛過","examples":[{"en":"The rover would rumble across the Moon from site to site.","zh":"月球車會從一個地點到另一個地點，隆隆地駛過月球。"},{"en":"To rumble across a place means to move across it with a low, heavy rolling sound or rough movement.","zh":"隆隆地駛過某處，指以低沉、沉重的滾動聲或粗糙動作穿越該地。"},{"en":"A truck may rumble across a bridge early in the morning.","zh":"貨車清晨可能隆隆地駛過橋樑。"},{"en":"If a rover rumbles across fragile ground, its movement may leave visible tracks.","zh":"如果月球車隆隆地駛過脆弱地面，其動作可能留下可見車痕。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests heavy movement over a surface.","zh":"這個短語暗示在表面上的沉重移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"from one site to another","meaning":"從一個遺址到另一個遺址","examples":[{"en":"The vehicle would travel from one archaeological site to another.","zh":"車輛會從一個考古遺址前往另一個考古遺址。"},{"en":"From one site to another means moving between different locations.","zh":"從一個地點到另一個地點，指在不同位置之間移動。"},{"en":"A museum guide may take students from one display site to another during a tour.","zh":"博物館導賞員可能在參觀中帶學生從一個展點到另一個展點。"},{"en":"If a rover travels between lunar sites, each stop may create a new risk of damage.","zh":"如果月球車在月球遺址之間行駛，每一站都可能造成新的破壞風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement across several places.","zh":"這個短語描述跨越多個地方的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the wreck of","meaning":"……的殘骸","examples":[{"en":"The route would pass the wreck of the Ranger 8 probe.","zh":"路線會經過 Ranger 8 探測器的殘骸。"},{"en":"The wreck of something is the damaged remains of a vehicle, ship, aircraft or machine.","zh":"某物的殘骸，是車輛、船隻、飛機或機器受損後留下的部分。"},{"en":"Divers may study the wreck of an old ship to learn about trade routes.","zh":"潛水員可能研究舊船殘骸，以了解貿易路線。"},{"en":"If a space probe crashes, its wreck can still become historically important evidence.","zh":"如果太空探測器墜毀，其殘骸仍可成為具有歷史重要性的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to broken remains after damage or destruction.","zh":"這個短語指受損或毀壞後的破碎遺留物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"landing site","meaning":"着陸地點","examples":[{"en":"Apollo 17’s landing site has great historical significance.","zh":"Apollo 17 的着陸地點具有重大歷史意義。"},{"en":"A landing site is the place where a spacecraft, aircraft or vehicle lands.","zh":"着陸地點是太空船、飛機或車輛降落的地方。"},{"en":"Rescue teams may mark a helicopter landing site before an emergency flight arrives.","zh":"救援隊可能在緊急直升機抵達前標示着陸地點。"},{"en":"If humans first reached a place at a landing site, that location may become historically important.","zh":"如果人類首次在某個着陸地點到達某地，該位置可能變得具有歷史重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the exact place of arrival.","zh":"這個短語指出抵達的準確地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"leave tyre marks","meaning":"留下輪胎痕跡","examples":[{"en":"The rover would leave tyre marks across famous lunar sites.","zh":"月球車會在著名月球遺址上留下輪胎痕跡。"},{"en":"To leave tyre marks means to create visible tracks on the ground with vehicle wheels.","zh":"留下輪胎痕跡，指車輪在地面造成可見軌跡。"},{"en":"A bicycle may leave tyre marks in wet mud after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，單車可能在濕泥上留下輪胎痕跡。"},{"en":"If a rover leaves tyre marks on lunar dust, the marks may disturb older historic traces.","zh":"如果月球車在月塵上留下輪胎痕跡，可能擾亂較舊的歷史痕跡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical evidence left by wheels.","zh":"這個短語描述車輪留下的物理證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"all over","meaning":"遍佈","examples":[{"en":"The vehicle could leave marks all over the historic area.","zh":"車輛可能在整個歷史區域遍佈留下痕跡。"},{"en":"All over a place means across many parts of that place.","zh":"遍佈某地，指分佈在該地方許多部分。"},{"en":"Children may leave toys all over the living room after playing.","zh":"孩子玩耍後，可能把玩具放得到處都是。"},{"en":"If tracks appear all over a heritage site, the original surface evidence may be difficult to study.","zh":"如果車痕遍佈文化遺產地點，原本地面證據可能難以研究。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests widespread coverage, not one small spot.","zh":"這個短語暗示廣泛覆蓋，而不是一小處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be promoted as","meaning":"被宣傳為","examples":[{"en":"The mission was promoted as a form of entertainment.","zh":"這項任務被宣傳為一種娛樂。"},{"en":"To be promoted as something means to be advertised or presented to the public in that way.","zh":"被宣傳為某物，指被廣告或向公眾呈現為該樣東西。"},{"en":"A museum exhibition may be promoted as a family-friendly weekend activity.","zh":"博物館展覽可能被宣傳為適合家庭的週末活動。"},{"en":"If a serious lunar mission is promoted as entertainment, scholars may worry that heritage is being treated lightly.","zh":"如果嚴肅月球任務被宣傳為娛樂，學者可能擔心文化遺產被輕率對待。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how something is marketed or described.","zh":"這個短語強調某事如何被市場推廣或描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"theme-park entertainment","meaning":"主題公園式娛樂","examples":[{"en":"The lunar mission was presented as theme-park entertainment.","zh":"這項月球任務被呈現為主題公園式娛樂。"},{"en":"Theme-park entertainment is amusement designed to excite visitors, like rides, shows or attractions.","zh":"主題公園式娛樂，是像機動遊戲、表演或景點一樣設計來刺激遊客的娛樂。"},{"en":"A historical village can become theme-park entertainment if it focuses only on fun and ignores accuracy.","zh":"如果歷史村落只重視趣味而忽視準確性，它就可能變成主題公園式娛樂。"},{"en":"If a lunar heritage site is treated like a theme park, visitors may forget its historical seriousness.","zh":"如果月球文化遺產地點被當成主題公園，訪客可能忘記其歷史嚴肅性。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests entertainment that may simplify or commercialise history.","zh":"這個短語暗示可能簡化或商業化歷史的娛樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"vaguely worded","meaning":"措辭含糊的","examples":[{"en":"The United Nations treaty is vaguely worded in several important areas.","zh":"聯合國條約在幾個重要範疇措辭含糊。"},{"en":"Vaguely worded means written in a way that is not clear, exact or specific enough.","zh":"措辭含糊的，指文字不夠清楚、精確或具體。"},{"en":"A school rule is vaguely worded if students cannot tell what is allowed and what is banned.","zh":"如果學生無法判斷甚麼允許、甚麼禁止，校規就是措辭含糊。"},{"en":"If a treaty is vague, countries may disagree about how to apply it.","zh":"如果條約含糊，各國可能不同意如何應用它。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises unclear language in a document.","zh":"這個短語批評文件語言不清楚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Outer Space Treaty","meaning":"《外太空條約》","examples":[{"en":"The Outer Space Treaty was adopted in 1967.","zh":"《外太空條約》於1967年獲採納。"},{"en":"The Outer Space Treaty is an international agreement setting basic legal rules for human activity in outer space.","zh":"《外太空條約》是一項國際協議，為人類在外太空活動設定基本法律規則。"},{"en":"A law student may study the Outer Space Treaty when learning about ownership and responsibility beyond Earth.","zh":"法律學生學習地球以外的擁有權和責任時，可能研究《外太空條約》。"},{"en":"If space tourism grows, older treaties may be tested by new commercial activities.","zh":"如果太空旅遊增長，舊條約可能受到新商業活動考驗。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major legal document about space.","zh":"這個短語指出一份關於太空的重要法律文件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"what it terms","meaning":"它所稱的……","examples":[{"en":"What the treaty terms “space junk” may include historically important objects.","zh":"條約所稱的「太空垃圾」可能包括具有歷史重要性的物件。"},{"en":"What it terms something means what it calls or labels something.","zh":"它所稱的某物，指它把某事稱為或標籤為甚麼。"},{"en":"What a school terms “misbehaviour” may include talking, lateness or using a phone in class.","zh":"學校所稱的「不當行為」可能包括說話、遲到或在課堂使用手機。"},{"en":"If a treaty terms old spacecraft “junk,” it may overlook their heritage value.","zh":"如果條約把舊太空船稱為「垃圾」，可能忽略其文化遺產價值。"},{"en":"The phrase draws attention to the language used to classify something.","zh":"這個短語把注意力引向分類某事時使用的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"space junk","meaning":"太空垃圾","examples":[{"en":"The treaty treats some human-made objects as space junk.","zh":"條約把一些人造物件視為太空垃圾。"},{"en":"Space junk is unwanted human-made material left in orbit or space, such as broken satellites or rocket parts.","zh":"太空垃圾是留在軌道或太空中的不需要人造物料，例如壞衛星或火箭零件。"},{"en":"Engineers worry about space junk because it can collide with working spacecraft.","zh":"工程師擔心太空垃圾，因為它可能撞上正在運作的太空船。"},{"en":"If historic probes are treated only as space junk, their cultural value may be ignored.","zh":"如果歷史探測器只被視為太空垃圾，其文化價值可能被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase usually suggests waste, but some objects may also be heritage.","zh":"這個短語通常暗示廢物，但有些物件也可能是文化遺產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"remain the property of","meaning":"仍屬於……的財產","examples":[{"en":"A space probe remains the property of the country that launched it.","zh":"太空探測器仍屬於發射它的國家的財產。"},{"en":"To remain the property of someone means to continue legally belonging to that person, group or country.","zh":"仍屬於某人的財產，指在法律上繼續屬於該人、群體或國家。"},{"en":"A borrowed library book remains the property of the library even when a student takes it home.","zh":"借出的圖書館書籍即使被學生帶回家，仍屬於圖書館的財產。"},{"en":"If a probe remains a country’s property, other visitors may not have the right to remove it.","zh":"如果探測器仍屬於某國財產，其他訪客可能沒有權移走它。"},{"en":"The phrase concerns legal ownership.","zh":"這個短語涉及法律擁有權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"send a craft into space","meaning":"將太空船送入太空","examples":[{"en":"Countries that send a craft into space retain ownership of it.","zh":"將太空船送入太空的國家保留其擁有權。"},{"en":"To send a craft into space means to launch a spacecraft, probe or vehicle beyond Earth.","zh":"將太空船送入太空，指把太空船、探測器或車輛發射到地球以外。"},{"en":"A space agency may send a craft into space to study Mars or repair a satellite.","zh":"太空機構可能將太空船送入太空，以研究火星或修理衛星。"},{"en":"If a country sends a craft into space, international law may still recognise its ownership.","zh":"如果某國將太空船送入太空，國際法仍可能承認其擁有權。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the act of launching a space vehicle.","zh":"這個短語描述發射太空交通工具的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"explicitly address","meaning":"明確處理","examples":[{"en":"The treaty does not explicitly address the protection of historic sites.","zh":"條約沒有明確處理歷史遺址保護問題。"},{"en":"To explicitly address an issue means to deal with it directly and clearly in words.","zh":"明確處理某議題，指用文字直接而清楚地處理它。"},{"en":"A school policy should explicitly address bullying so students know what behaviour is banned.","zh":"學校政策應明確處理欺凌，讓學生知道哪些行為被禁止。"},{"en":"If a treaty does not explicitly address heritage sites, legal protection may be uncertain.","zh":"如果條約沒有明確處理文化遺產地點，法律保護可能不確定。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses direct and clear treatment of a topic.","zh":"這個短語強調直接而清晰處理某題目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"equate something with","meaning":"將……等同於……","examples":[{"en":"It is problematic to equate historic remains with space junk.","zh":"將歷史遺存等同於太空垃圾是有問題的。"},{"en":"To equate something with another thing means to treat them as if they are the same.","zh":"將某物等同於另一物，指把它們當成相同。"},{"en":"It is unfair to equate shyness with laziness because quiet students may still work hard.","zh":"將害羞等同於懶惰並不公平，因為安靜學生仍可能很努力。"},{"en":"If old lunar equipment is equated with rubbish, its historical meaning may be lost.","zh":"如果舊月球設備被等同於垃圾，其歷史意義可能消失。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used to challenge an oversimplified comparison.","zh":"這個短語常用來挑戰過分簡化的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"human exploration of the heavens","meaning":"人類探索太空","examples":[{"en":"The remains record the history of human exploration of the heavens.","zh":"這些遺存記錄人類探索太空的歷史。"},{"en":"Human exploration of the heavens means people’s attempts to study and travel through space.","zh":"人類探索太空，指人們嘗試研究並穿越太空。"},{"en":"Early telescopes, rockets and lunar probes all belong to the story of human exploration beyond Earth.","zh":"早期望遠鏡、火箭和月球探測器都屬於人類探索地球以外空間的故事。"},{"en":"If objects record this history, they deserve protection as more than technical waste.","zh":"如果物件記錄這段歷史，它們就不只是技術廢物，而值得保護。"},{"en":"The phrase uses “the heavens” poetically to mean outer space.","zh":"這個短語以 “the heavens” 詩意地指外太空。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"leave something vulnerable to","meaning":"令……容易受到……傷害","examples":[{"en":"Weak legal protection leaves historic objects vulnerable to scavengers.","zh":"薄弱法律保護令歷史物件容易受到搜掠者傷害。"},{"en":"To leave something vulnerable to a danger means to make it easy for that danger to harm it.","zh":"令某物容易受到某危險傷害，指使該危險很容易傷害它。"},{"en":"Leaving a phone on a café table makes it vulnerable to theft.","zh":"把手機留在咖啡店桌上，會令它容易被偷。"},{"en":"If lunar objects are not protected by clear law, collectors may remove them.","zh":"如果月球物件沒有清楚法律保護，收藏者可能移走它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes exposure to risk.","zh":"這個短語描述暴露於風險之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"scavengers","meaning":"搜掠者","examples":[{"en":"Scavengers could remove valuable objects from lunar sites.","zh":"搜掠者可能從月球遺址移走有價值物件。"},{"en":"Scavengers are people who search through places to take useful, valuable or leftover items.","zh":"搜掠者是在某些地方搜尋並拿走有用、有價值或剩餘物品的人。"},{"en":"Scavengers may enter an abandoned building to collect metal parts or old furniture.","zh":"搜掠者可能進入廢棄建築收集金屬零件或舊家具。"},{"en":"If scavengers take objects from a historic site, they destroy context and evidence.","zh":"如果搜掠者從歷史遺址拿走物件，他們會破壞背景和證據。"},{"en":"The word suggests uncontrolled collecting, often harmful to preservation.","zh":"這個詞暗示不受控制的搜集，通常對保存有害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"another problem arises","meaning":"另一個問題出現","examples":[{"en":"Another problem arises from international rules on land ownership.","zh":"另一個問題源於關於土地擁有權的國際規則。"},{"en":"Another problem arises means a further difficulty appears or becomes important.","zh":"另一個問題出現，指進一步困難出現或變得重要。"},{"en":"If a school changes the timetable, another problem may arise when buses no longer match dismissal time.","zh":"如果學校更改時間表，另一個問題可能出現：巴士時間不再配合放學時間。"},{"en":"If ownership rules are unclear, heritage managers face legal uncertainty.","zh":"如果擁有權規則不清楚，文化遺產管理者會面對法律不確定性。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an additional complication.","zh":"這個短語引入額外複雜問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"international treaties","meaning":"國際條約","examples":[{"en":"International treaties state that no country may own land in space.","zh":"國際條約規定沒有國家可以擁有太空土地。"},{"en":"International treaties are formal agreements between countries.","zh":"國際條約是國家之間的正式協議。"},{"en":"Countries may sign international treaties to control trade, protect wildlife or reduce pollution.","zh":"各國可能簽署國際條約來管制貿易、保護野生動物或減少污染。"},{"en":"If space is governed by treaties, individual countries cannot simply make their own rules alone.","zh":"如果太空由條約規管，個別國家就不能單方面制定自己的規則。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to legally important agreements across nations.","zh":"這個短語指跨國之間具有法律重要性的協議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"proclaim that","meaning":"宣稱","examples":[{"en":"Several agreements proclaim that space land cannot be privately owned.","zh":"幾項協議宣稱太空土地不能由私人擁有。"},{"en":"To proclaim that something is true means to state it publicly and formally.","zh":"宣稱某事為真，指公開而正式地陳述它。"},{"en":"A school may proclaim that all students have the right to learn safely.","zh":"學校可能宣稱所有學生都有安全學習的權利。"},{"en":"If a treaty proclaims a rule, it presents the rule as official and important.","zh":"如果條約宣稱一項規則，就是把該規則呈現為正式且重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong formal announcement.","zh":"這個短語描述強而正式的宣布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cannot be owned by","meaning":"不能由……擁有","examples":[{"en":"Land on the Moon cannot be owned by a country or individual.","zh":"月球上的土地不能由國家或個人擁有。"},{"en":"Cannot be owned by someone means no person, group or country has legal ownership of it.","zh":"不能由某人擁有，指沒有個人、群體或國家在法律上擁有它。"},{"en":"A public park cannot be owned by one student simply because they use it every day.","zh":"公園不能只因一名學生每天使用，就由該學生擁有。"},{"en":"If Moon land cannot be owned, responsibility for protecting sites becomes harder to assign.","zh":"如果月球土地不能被擁有，分配保護遺址的責任就更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a legal limit on ownership.","zh":"這個短語描述法律上的擁有權限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"present a dilemma for","meaning":"為……帶來兩難局面","examples":[{"en":"These legal rules present a dilemma for heritage managers.","zh":"這些法律規則為文化遺產管理者帶來兩難局面。"},{"en":"To present a dilemma for someone means to create a difficult choice or problem for them.","zh":"為某人帶來兩難局面，指為他們造成困難選擇或問題。"},{"en":"A cheap but unhealthy lunch menu presents a dilemma for school administrators.","zh":"便宜但不健康的午餐餐單，會為學校管理者帶來兩難局面。"},{"en":"If no one owns lunar land, managers may not know who can enforce protection.","zh":"如果沒有人擁有月球土地，管理者可能不知道誰能執行保護。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a situation creates conflicting pressures.","zh":"這個短語顯示某情況造成互相衝突的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"aspiring manager","meaning":"有志成為……的管理者","examples":[{"en":"An aspiring manager of lunar heritage would face difficult legal questions.","zh":"有志成為月球文化遺產管理者的人，會面對困難法律問題。"},{"en":"An aspiring manager is someone who hopes or aims to become a manager.","zh":"有志成為管理者的人，是希望或目標是成為管理者的人。"},{"en":"An aspiring manager in a hotel may study customer service and team leadership.","zh":"酒店中有志成為經理的人，可能學習客戶服務和團隊領導。"},{"en":"If someone wants to manage lunar heritage, they must understand law, archaeology and space travel.","zh":"如果某人想管理月球文化遺產，就必須理解法律、考古和太空旅行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ambition toward a future role.","zh":"這個短語描述對未來角色的志向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"extraterrestrial cultural resources","meaning":"地球以外的文化資源","examples":[{"en":"Historic objects on the Moon are extraterrestrial cultural resources.","zh":"月球上的歷史物件是地球以外的文化資源。"},{"en":"Extraterrestrial cultural resources are culturally important objects or sites located beyond Earth.","zh":"地球以外的文化資源，是位於地球以外且在文化上重要的物件或遺址。"},{"en":"A spacecraft part left on Mars could become an extraterrestrial cultural resource.","zh":"留在火星上的太空船零件可以成為地球以外的文化資源。"},{"en":"If an object records human achievement in space, it may deserve heritage protection.","zh":"如果某物記錄人類在太空中的成就，它可能值得文化遺產保護。"},{"en":"The phrase combines space location with cultural value.","zh":"這個短語結合太空位置與文化價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"famous first footprints","meaning":"著名的第一組腳印","examples":[{"en":"Neil Armstrong’s famous first footprints have enormous historical value.","zh":"Neil Armstrong 著名的第一組腳印具有巨大歷史價值。"},{"en":"Famous first footprints are the well-known marks made by the first human steps in a historic place.","zh":"著名的第一組腳印，是人在歷史地點踏出第一步所留下的知名痕跡。"},{"en":"A museum photograph of first footprints can help students imagine a major moment in exploration.","zh":"博物館中第一組腳印的照片，可以幫助學生想像探索史上的重大時刻。"},{"en":"If footprints mark a first human achievement, even dust marks can become priceless evidence.","zh":"如果腳印標誌人類首次成就，即使塵埃痕跡也可以成為無價證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to physical traces of a historic first step.","zh":"這個短語指歷史性第一步的實物痕跡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lunar dust","meaning":"月塵","examples":[{"en":"The footprints were recorded in lunar dust.","zh":"這些腳印被記錄在月塵中。"},{"en":"Lunar dust is the fine powdery material covering the surface of the Moon.","zh":"月塵是覆蓋月球表面的幼細粉狀物質。"},{"en":"A bootprint in lunar dust may remain visible because there is no wind or rain like on Earth.","zh":"月塵中的靴印可能仍然清晰，因為月球不像地球有風雨。"},{"en":"If lunar dust is disturbed by a rover or tourist, old marks may disappear.","zh":"如果月塵被月球車或遊客擾亂，舊痕跡可能消失。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the Moon’s surface dust.","zh":"這個短語指月球表面的塵埃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as important as","meaning":"與……同樣重要","examples":[{"en":"The lunar footprints may be as important as ancient hominid prints.","zh":"月球腳印可能與古代人科動物腳印同樣重要。"},{"en":"As important as means having the same level of importance as something else.","zh":"與某物同樣重要，指具有與另一事物相同程度的重要性。"},{"en":"For a student, sleep may be as important as revision before an exam.","zh":"對學生來說，睡眠在考試前可能與溫習同樣重要。"},{"en":"If lunar footprints mark a turning point in human development, they may equal ancient footprints in value.","zh":"如果月球腳印標誌人類發展的轉折，它們在價值上可能等同古代腳印。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a comparison of equal significance.","zh":"這個短語建立同等重要性的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"human development","meaning":"人類發展","examples":[{"en":"The footprints form an important part of the story of human development.","zh":"這些腳印構成人類發展故事的重要部分。"},{"en":"Human development means the long process by which humans physically, socially, culturally and technologically change.","zh":"人類發展指人類在身體、社會、文化和科技上變化的漫長過程。"},{"en":"The invention of writing was a major step in human development.","zh":"文字發明是人類發展中的重要一步。"},{"en":"If humans learn to live beyond Earth, space activity becomes part of human development.","zh":"如果人類學會在地球以外生活，太空活動就成為人類發展的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the broad story of human progress and change.","zh":"這個短語指人類進步和變化的廣闊故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hominids","meaning":"早期人科動物","examples":[{"en":"The Laetoli footprints were left by early hominids.","zh":"Laetoli 腳印由早期人科動物留下。"},{"en":"Hominids are humans and their close extinct relatives in the human evolutionary family.","zh":"人科動物是人類及其在人類演化家族中的已滅絕近親。"},{"en":"Archaeologists study hominid bones and footprints to understand early walking and tool use.","zh":"考古學家研究人科動物骨骼和腳印，以理解早期行走和工具使用。"},{"en":"If ancient hominid footprints survive, they can reveal how early human relatives moved.","zh":"如果古代人科動物腳印保存下來，就能揭示早期人類近親如何移動。"},{"en":"The word refers to early members of the human family, not modern apes only.","zh":"這個詞指人類家族的早期成員，而不只是現代猿類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"encased in","meaning":"被包裹於……之中","examples":[{"en":"The Laetoli prints survived because they were encased in hardened ash.","zh":"Laetoli 腳印能保存下來，是因為它們被包裹於硬化火山灰之中。"},{"en":"To be encased in something means to be completely surrounded or covered by it.","zh":"被包裹於某物之中，指被它完全圍住或覆蓋。"},{"en":"A fragile phone may be encased in a protective cover to prevent damage.","zh":"易碎手機可能被包裹在保護殼中，以防損壞。"},{"en":"If footprints are encased in ash, the covering can protect their shape for thousands of years.","zh":"如果腳印被包裹在火山灰中，覆蓋物可以保護其形狀數千年。"},{"en":"The phrase describes protective enclosure.","zh":"這個短語描述保護性包圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cement-like ash","meaning":"水泥狀火山灰","examples":[{"en":"The ancient footprints were preserved in cement-like ash.","zh":"古代腳印保存在水泥狀火山灰中。"},{"en":"Cement-like ash is ash that hardens and behaves like cement.","zh":"水泥狀火山灰，是硬化後表現得像水泥的火山灰。"},{"en":"Wet volcanic ash can become cement-like when it dries and solidifies.","zh":"濕火山灰乾燥並凝固後，可以變成水泥狀。"},{"en":"If footprints sink into soft ash before it hardens, their shapes may be preserved.","zh":"如果腳印在火山灰硬化前陷入其中，其形狀可能被保存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ash that becomes firm enough to protect impressions.","zh":"這個短語描述變得足夠堅硬以保護壓痕的火山灰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sweep something away","meaning":"掃走；破壞","examples":[{"en":"A careless tourist could sweep the lunar footprints away.","zh":"粗心遊客可能把月球腳印掃走。"},{"en":"To sweep something away means to remove or destroy it with a sweeping movement.","zh":"掃走某物，指用掃動動作移除或破壞它。"},{"en":"A cleaner may accidentally sweep away tiny pieces of evidence from a classroom floor.","zh":"清潔工可能意外掃走課室地板上的細小證據。"},{"en":"If a hand brushes lunar dust, fragile footprints could disappear permanently.","zh":"如果手掃過月塵，脆弱腳印可能永久消失。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how easily delicate traces can be lost.","zh":"這個短語顯示精細痕跡多麼容易失去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a casual brush of","meaning":"隨手輕輕一掃","examples":[{"en":"The marks could disappear with a casual brush of a tourist’s hand.","zh":"這些痕跡可能因遊客隨手輕輕一掃而消失。"},{"en":"A casual brush of something is a light, careless touching or sweeping movement.","zh":"隨手輕輕一掃，是輕微、漫不經心的觸碰或掃動。"},{"en":"A casual brush of an elbow can knock a pencil off a desk.","zh":"手肘隨便輕輕一碰，就可能把鉛筆撞下書桌。"},{"en":"If a site is extremely fragile, even a small careless movement can cause damage.","zh":"如果遺址極其脆弱，即使小小粗心動作也可造成破壞。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that only slight contact may be enough.","zh":"這個短語強調只有輕微接觸也可能足夠造成影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"deal with problems","meaning":"處理問題","examples":[{"en":"International cooperation may be needed to deal with these problems.","zh":"可能需要國際合作來處理這些問題。"},{"en":"To deal with problems means to take action to manage, solve or reduce them.","zh":"處理問題，指採取行動去管理、解決或減少問題。"},{"en":"A school may deal with bullying problems by creating clear reporting rules and support systems.","zh":"學校可能透過建立清楚舉報規則和支援系統來處理欺凌問題。"},{"en":"If lunar heritage faces legal and tourist risks, one country alone may not be able to manage them.","zh":"如果月球文化遺產面對法律和旅遊風險，單一國家可能無法管理。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on practical response to difficulties.","zh":"這個短語強調對困難作出實際回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"look to","meaning":"求助於；寄望於","examples":[{"en":"Researchers may need to look to new international organisations for protection.","zh":"研究者可能需要求助於新的國際組織來取得保護。"},{"en":"To look to someone or something means to depend on them or seek help from them.","zh":"求助於或寄望於某人或某物，指依賴他們或向他們尋求幫助。"},{"en":"Students may look to a teacher for advice when they do not understand an exam question.","zh":"學生不明白考試題目時，可能求助於老師。"},{"en":"If existing treaties are unclear, archaeologists may look to new organisations for stronger rules.","zh":"如果現有條約不清楚，考古學家可能寄望新組織制定更強規則。"},{"en":"The phrase shows where people place hope or seek support.","zh":"這個短語顯示人們把希望放在哪裡或向誰尋求支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"innovative administrative structures","meaning":"創新的行政架構","examples":[{"en":"Innovative administrative structures may be required to protect lunar heritage.","zh":"可能需要創新的行政架構來保護月球文化遺產。"},{"en":"Innovative administrative structures are new ways of organising rules, responsibilities and management.","zh":"創新的行政架構，是組織規則、責任和管理的新方式。"},{"en":"A school may create an innovative administrative structure by letting teachers, students and parents share decisions.","zh":"學校讓老師、學生和家長共同決策，就是建立創新的行政架構。"},{"en":"If space heritage does not fit old laws, new management systems may be needed.","zh":"如果太空文化遺產不適合舊法律，就可能需要新管理系統。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creative organisation for difficult governance problems.","zh":"這個短語描述用於困難治理問題的創意組織方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"preservation of historic remains","meaning":"保存歷史遺蹟","examples":[{"en":"International controls could support the preservation of historic remains.","zh":"國際管制可以支持保存歷史遺蹟。"},{"en":"Preservation of historic remains means protecting old objects, structures or traces so they survive.","zh":"保存歷史遺蹟，指保護舊物件、結構或痕跡，使它們能保留下來。"},{"en":"A museum supports preservation by storing fragile documents away from heat and moisture.","zh":"博物館透過把脆弱文件存放在遠離高溫和濕氣的地方來支持保存。"},{"en":"If historic remains are not preserved, future researchers lose evidence permanently.","zh":"如果歷史遺蹟沒有被保存，未來研究者會永久失去證據。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on keeping material history safe.","zh":"這個短語強調保護物質歷史安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the new frontier","meaning":"新前沿","examples":[{"en":"Space is becoming a new frontier for heritage protection.","zh":"太空正在成為文化遺產保護的新前沿。"},{"en":"A new frontier is a new area of activity, study or challenge that has not yet been fully explored.","zh":"新前沿是尚未被充分探索的活動、研究或挑戰新領域。"},{"en":"Online learning became a new frontier for many teachers during school closures.","zh":"在學校停課期間，網上學習成為許多老師的新前沿。"},{"en":"If heritage protection moves into space, old methods may need to be changed.","zh":"如果文化遺產保護進入太空，舊方法可能需要改變。"},{"en":"The phrase presents a field as fresh, challenging and not yet settled.","zh":"這個短語把某領域呈現為新鮮、有挑戰且未定型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"with its wealth of sites","meaning":"因擁有大量遺址","examples":[{"en":"The Moon, with its wealth of sites, will attract future archaeologists.","zh":"月球因擁有大量遺址，將吸引未來考古學家。"},{"en":"With its wealth of sites means because it has many valuable or interesting locations.","zh":"因擁有大量遺址，指因它有許多有價值或有趣的位置。"},{"en":"A city, with its wealth of museums and old streets, can attract history students.","zh":"一座城市因擁有大量博物館和舊街道，可以吸引歷史學生。"},{"en":"If the Moon contains many spacecraft, footprints and landing areas, it becomes rich in archaeological evidence.","zh":"如果月球包含許多太空船、腳印和着陸區，它就擁有豐富考古證據。"},{"en":"The phrase explains attraction through abundance.","zh":"這個短語透過豐富性解釋吸引力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"first destination","meaning":"首個目的地","examples":[{"en":"The Moon will probably be the first destination for space archaeologists.","zh":"月球很可能是太空考古學家的首個目的地。"},{"en":"A first destination is the first place someone chooses or plans to visit.","zh":"首個目的地，是某人選擇或計劃前往的第一個地方。"},{"en":"For a school trip, the museum may be the first destination before students go to the park.","zh":"在學校旅行中，博物館可能是學生去公園前的首個目的地。"},{"en":"If the Moon has many accessible historic sites, researchers may go there before Mars.","zh":"如果月球有許多較易到達的歷史遺址，研究者可能先去那裡而不是火星。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the starting place in a journey or plan.","zh":"這個短語標示旅程或計劃中的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be trained to","meaning":"接受訓練去","examples":[{"en":"Future archaeologists may be trained to work in space.","zh":"未來考古學家可能接受訓練去在太空工作。"},{"en":"To be trained to do something means to be taught the skills needed to do it safely or well.","zh":"接受訓練去做某事，指被教授安全或有效完成該事所需技能。"},{"en":"Nurses are trained to check patients’ conditions and respond to emergencies.","zh":"護士接受訓練去檢查病人情況並應對緊急事件。"},{"en":"If archaeologists work on the Moon, they need training in archaeology, space suits and fragile-site protection.","zh":"如果考古學家在月球工作，他們需要考古、太空衣和脆弱遺址保護訓練。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preparation for a specific task.","zh":"這個短語描述為特定任務作準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"claim the mantle of","meaning":"取得……的名銜","examples":[{"en":"Young scholars may hope to claim the mantle of the first lunar archaeologist.","zh":"年輕學者可能希望取得首位月球考古學家的名銜。"},{"en":"To claim the mantle of a role means to take or be recognised for an important title, position or legacy.","zh":"取得某角色的名銜，指取得或被承認擁有重要頭銜、位置或傳承。"},{"en":"A young athlete may hope to claim the mantle of the team’s next captain.","zh":"年輕運動員可能希望取得球隊下一任隊長的名銜。"},{"en":"If someone becomes the first recognised lunar archaeologist, they gain a symbolic honour.","zh":"如果某人成為首位被承認的月球考古學家，他就獲得象徵性榮譽。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests receiving a prestigious role or distinction.","zh":"這個短語暗示獲得有聲望的角色或殊榮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be disappointed","meaning":"感到失望","examples":[{"en":"Anyone hoping to be the first lunar archaeologist will be disappointed.","zh":"任何希望成為首位月球考古學家的人都會感到失望。"},{"en":"To be disappointed means to feel unhappy because what one hoped for did not happen.","zh":"感到失望，指因所希望的事情沒有發生而不開心。"},{"en":"A student may be disappointed if they studied hard but missed the top grade.","zh":"如果學生努力溫習但未取得最高等級，可能感到失望。"},{"en":"If someone discovers the honour already belongs to others, their hope may collapse.","zh":"如果某人發現該榮譽已屬於別人，他的希望可能落空。"},{"en":"The phrase describes emotional reaction to unmet expectation.","zh":"這個短語描述期望落空時的情緒反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"that distinction","meaning":"那項殊榮","examples":[{"en":"That distinction already belongs to the Apollo 12 astronauts.","zh":"那項殊榮已經屬於 Apollo 12 太空人。"},{"en":"That distinction means that special honour, title or difference just mentioned.","zh":"那項殊榮，指剛提到的特別榮譽、名銜或區別。"},{"en":"If a student wins the school’s first national prize, that distinction belongs to them.","zh":"如果學生贏得學校首個全國獎項，那項殊榮就屬於他。"},{"en":"When a title has already been earned, later people cannot claim to be first.","zh":"當某名銜已被取得，後來者就不能聲稱自己是第一。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to a special recognised status.","zh":"這個短語回指一種特別被承認的地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make a difficult manual landing","meaning":"進行高難度人手着陸","examples":[{"en":"The astronauts made a difficult manual landing on the Moon.","zh":"太空人在月球進行高難度人手着陸。"},{"en":"To make a difficult manual landing means to land a craft by human control under challenging conditions.","zh":"進行高難度人手着陸，指在具挑戰條件下由人手控制太空船降落。"},{"en":"A pilot may make a manual landing when automatic systems fail.","zh":"當自動系統失靈，機師可能進行人手着陸。"},{"en":"If landing is difficult and manual, the astronauts must rely on skill, judgement and calm control.","zh":"如果着陸困難又需人手操作，太空人必須依靠技巧、判斷和冷靜控制。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights both technical difficulty and human control.","zh":"這個短語同時突出技術困難和人為控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lunar module","meaning":"登月艙","examples":[{"en":"Apollo 12’s lunar module landed in the Ocean of Storms.","zh":"Apollo 12 的登月艙降落在月球風暴洋。"},{"en":"A lunar module is the spacecraft section designed to land on the Moon and lift off again.","zh":"登月艙是設計用來降落月球並再次升空的太空船部分。"},{"en":"In a space museum, students may see a model of a lunar module and learn how astronauts reached the surface.","zh":"在太空博物館中，學生可能看見登月艙模型，了解太空人如何到達月面。"},{"en":"If the lunar module lands close to an older probe, astronauts can inspect previous equipment.","zh":"如果登月艙降落在舊探測器附近，太空人就能檢查先前設備。"},{"en":"The phrase names the Moon-landing part of an Apollo spacecraft.","zh":"這個短語指出 Apollo 太空船中用於登月的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the Ocean of Storms","meaning":"月球風暴洋","examples":[{"en":"The astronauts landed in the Moon’s Ocean of Storms.","zh":"太空人降落在月球風暴洋。"},{"en":"The Ocean of Storms is a large dark plain on the Moon, not an actual ocean of water.","zh":"月球風暴洋是月球上一大片深色平原，而不是真正有水的海洋。"},{"en":"A student may be surprised that lunar “seas” and “oceans” are names for flat volcanic plains.","zh":"學生可能驚訝於月球「海」和「洋」其實是平坦火山平原的名稱。"},{"en":"If a mission lands in the Ocean of Storms, the name identifies a specific lunar region.","zh":"如果任務降落在風暴洋，該名稱就指出特定月球區域。"},{"en":"The phrase is a traditional name for a place on the Moon.","zh":"這個短語是月球上一個地方的傳統名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a few hundred feet from","meaning":"距離……數百英尺","examples":[{"en":"The lunar module landed a few hundred feet from Surveyor 3.","zh":"登月艙在距離 Surveyor 3 數百英尺處着陸。"},{"en":"A few hundred feet from something means several hundred feet away from it.","zh":"距離某物數百英尺，指離它幾百英尺。"},{"en":"A school bus stop may be a few hundred feet from the main gate.","zh":"校巴站可能距離正門數百英尺。"},{"en":"If astronauts land a few hundred feet from a probe, they can walk to it for inspection.","zh":"如果太空人在距離探測器數百英尺處降落，就能步行到它旁邊檢查。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate short distance.","zh":"這個短語給出大約的短距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"unmanned probe","meaning":"無人探測器","examples":[{"en":"Surveyor 3 was an unmanned probe.","zh":"Surveyor 3 是一部無人探測器。"},{"en":"An unmanned probe is a spacecraft or machine sent to explore without people on board.","zh":"無人探測器是沒有載人、被送去探索的太空船或機器。"},{"en":"Scientists use unmanned probes to study planets that humans cannot safely visit yet.","zh":"科學家使用無人探測器研究人類尚不能安全到訪的行星。"},{"en":"If a probe is unmanned, it can collect information while avoiding human risk.","zh":"如果探測器無人，它可以收集資料，同時避免人類風險。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to robotic exploration equipment.","zh":"這個短語指機械探索設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"land in a crater","meaning":"降落在隕石坑內","examples":[{"en":"The probe had landed in a crater two years earlier.","zh":"該探測器兩年前降落在隕石坑內。"},{"en":"To land in a crater means to come down inside a bowl-shaped hollow on a planet or Moon.","zh":"降落在隕石坑內，指降落在行星或月球表面碗狀凹地中。"},{"en":"A rover landing in a crater may study rocks protected inside the hollow.","zh":"降落在隕石坑內的月球車，可能研究凹地中受保護的岩石。"},{"en":"If a probe lands in a crater, later astronauts may need to walk carefully on uneven ground.","zh":"如果探測器降落在隕石坑內，後來太空人可能需要在不平地面小心行走。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the landing location in a surface depression.","zh":"這個短語給出位於表面凹陷中的着陸位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"unrecognised at the time","meaning":"當時未被察覺的","examples":[{"en":"The importance of the event was unrecognised at the time.","zh":"該事件的重要性當時未被察覺。"},{"en":"Unrecognised at the time means not understood or appreciated when it happened.","zh":"當時未被察覺，指事情發生時沒有被理解或重視。"},{"en":"A student’s small idea may be unrecognised at the time but later become the basis of a successful project.","zh":"學生的小想法當時可能未被察覺，但後來成為成功項目的基礎。"},{"en":"If an event seems ordinary during the mission, historians may only later realise its importance.","zh":"如果某事件在任務期間看似普通，歷史學家可能後來才意識到其重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes value noticed only afterwards.","zh":"這個短語描述事後才被注意到的價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"an important moment in","meaning":"……中的重要時刻","examples":[{"en":"The landing was an important moment in the history of science.","zh":"這次着陸是科學史中的重要時刻。"},{"en":"An important moment in something is a point in time that significantly affects its development.","zh":"某事中的重要時刻，是對其發展有重大影響的時間點。"},{"en":"The first successful school debate may be an important moment in a shy student’s confidence.","zh":"第一次成功校內辯論，可能是害羞學生信心發展中的重要時刻。"},{"en":"If astronauts study an old probe on the Moon, it becomes important for both science and archaeology.","zh":"如果太空人在月球研究舊探測器，它對科學和考古都變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a turning point or meaningful event.","zh":"這個短語標示轉捩點或有意義事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be about to","meaning":"即將","examples":[{"en":"Conrad and Bean were about to conduct the first lunar archaeological study.","zh":"Conrad 和 Bean 即將進行首次月球考古研究。"},{"en":"To be about to do something means to be going to do it very soon.","zh":"即將做某事，指很快就會做該事。"},{"en":"A student is about to speak when the teacher calls their name.","zh":"當老師叫到學生名字時，學生即將發言。"},{"en":"If astronauts are about to inspect a probe, the important action is just moments away.","zh":"如果太空人即將檢查探測器，重要行動就近在眼前。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an event that is immediately upcoming.","zh":"這個短語描述即將發生的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"conduct a study","meaning":"進行研究","examples":[{"en":"The astronauts conducted an archaeological study of Surveyor 3.","zh":"太空人對 Surveyor 3 進行考古研究。"},{"en":"To conduct a study means to carry out organised research into a question or object.","zh":"進行研究，指對某問題或物件進行有組織的研究。"},{"en":"A school may conduct a study on how homework affects students’ sleep.","zh":"學校可能研究功課如何影響學生睡眠。"},{"en":"If astronauts photograph, collect and label objects, they are carrying out a structured investigation.","zh":"如果太空人拍照、收集和標記物件，他們就是在進行有結構的調查。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research done with a clear purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述有清楚目的的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"obligatory planting of the flag","meaning":"例行插旗儀式","examples":[{"en":"The astronauts completed the obligatory planting of the American flag.","zh":"太空人完成例行插上美國國旗儀式。"},{"en":"Obligatory planting of the flag means the expected or required act of placing a national flag at a mission site.","zh":"例行插旗儀式，指在任務地點放置國旗這一預期或必要行動。"},{"en":"At a school ceremony, an obligatory group photo may happen before the main event begins.","zh":"在學校典禮中，主活動開始前可能有例行大合照。"},{"en":"If flag planting is obligatory, it is treated as a standard symbolic duty.","zh":"如果插旗是例行的，它就被視為標準象徵性職責。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a ritual action that people expect to be done.","zh":"這個短語暗示人們預期要完成的儀式性行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"geological sampling","meaning":"地質採樣","examples":[{"en":"They carried out geological sampling before visiting the probe.","zh":"他們在探訪探測器前進行地質採樣。"},{"en":"Geological sampling means collecting rock, soil or mineral samples to study the ground’s history and composition.","zh":"地質採樣指收集岩石、泥土或礦物樣本，以研究地面的歷史和成分。"},{"en":"Geography students may practise simple sampling by collecting soil from different parts of a park.","zh":"地理學生可能透過從公園不同部分收集泥土來練習簡單採樣。"},{"en":"If astronauts collect Moon rocks, scientists can learn how the lunar surface formed.","zh":"如果太空人收集月岩，科學家就能了解月球表面如何形成。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to taking physical samples for Earth or planetary science.","zh":"這個短語指為地球或行星科學採集實物樣本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make their way to","meaning":"前往","examples":[{"en":"The astronauts made their way to Surveyor 3.","zh":"太空人前往 Surveyor 3。"},{"en":"To make one’s way to a place means to move or travel toward it, often with some effort.","zh":"前往某地，指向該地移動或行進，通常帶有一定努力。"},{"en":"Students may make their way to the assembly hall after the bell rings.","zh":"鐘聲響起後，學生可能前往禮堂。"},{"en":"If astronauts cross uneven lunar ground, reaching the probe takes careful movement.","zh":"如果太空人穿越不平月面，到達探測器需要小心移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes purposeful movement toward a destination.","zh":"這個短語描述朝目的地有目的地移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"observe that","meaning":"觀察到","examples":[{"en":"They observed that the probe had bounced after landing.","zh":"他們觀察到探測器着陸後曾彈起。"},{"en":"To observe that something happened means to notice and report it carefully.","zh":"觀察到某事發生，指仔細注意並報告它。"},{"en":"A teacher may observe that students participate more when examples are familiar.","zh":"老師可能觀察到例子熟悉時，學生更願意參與。"},{"en":"If astronauts observe marks in the soil, they can infer what happened during landing.","zh":"如果太空人觀察到土壤中的痕跡，就能推斷着陸時發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces careful observation, not casual guessing.","zh":"這個短語引出仔細觀察，而不是隨意猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bounce after touchdown","meaning":"着陸後彈起","examples":[{"en":"The probe appeared to have bounced after touchdown.","zh":"該探測器看似着陸後曾彈起。"},{"en":"To bounce after touchdown means to hit the surface when landing and then spring up or move again.","zh":"着陸後彈起，指降落時撞到表面後再彈起或再次移動。"},{"en":"A ball dropped onto a hard floor will bounce after touchdown.","zh":"球掉到硬地板上，着地後會彈起。"},{"en":"If a probe bounces after landing, its footpad marks may show several contact points.","zh":"如果探測器着陸後彈起，其着陸腳墊痕跡可能顯示多個接觸點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement immediately after landing.","zh":"這個短語描述着陸後立即發生的動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"carefully photograph","meaning":"仔細拍攝","examples":[{"en":"The astronauts carefully photographed the marks around the probe.","zh":"太空人仔細拍攝探測器周圍的痕跡。"},{"en":"To carefully photograph something means to take pictures of it with attention to detail and evidence.","zh":"仔細拍攝某物，指重視細節和證據地為它拍照。"},{"en":"Police may carefully photograph a damaged car after an accident.","zh":"意外後，警方可能仔細拍攝受損汽車。"},{"en":"If a site cannot be moved, careful photographs preserve information for later study.","zh":"如果遺址不能移動，仔細照片可以為日後研究保存資料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes photography used as serious documentation.","zh":"這個短語描述用作嚴肅記錄的攝影。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"impressions made by","meaning":"由……留下的壓痕","examples":[{"en":"They photographed the impressions made by the probe’s footpads.","zh":"他們拍攝探測器着陸腳墊留下的壓痕。"},{"en":"Impressions made by something are marks pressed into a soft surface by that object.","zh":"由某物留下的壓痕，是該物壓入柔軟表面形成的痕跡。"},{"en":"A shoe can leave impressions made by its sole in wet sand.","zh":"鞋底可以在濕沙中留下壓痕。"},{"en":"If probe footpads press into lunar soil, the resulting marks can reveal how the landing happened.","zh":"如果探測器腳墊壓入月壤，所得痕跡可以揭示着陸如何發生。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to physical pressed marks.","zh":"這個短語指實物壓出的痕跡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"footpads","meaning":"着陸腳墊","examples":[{"en":"The probe’s footpads left clear impressions in the lunar soil.","zh":"探測器的着陸腳墊在月壤中留下清晰壓痕。"},{"en":"Footpads are flat supporting parts at the bottom of a landing vehicle’s legs.","zh":"着陸腳墊是着陸車輛腳部底端的平坦支撐部分。"},{"en":"A table has feet to spread weight; a lunar probe has footpads to rest on the surface.","zh":"桌子有腳來分散重量；月球探測器有着陸腳墊來停在表面。"},{"en":"If footpads sink into soft soil, they can leave marks that show the landing position.","zh":"如果腳墊陷入柔軟泥土，就能留下顯示着陸位置的痕跡。"},{"en":"The word names the parts that touch the ground during landing.","zh":"這個詞指出着陸時接觸地面的部件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be covered in dust","meaning":"被塵埃覆蓋","examples":[{"en":"The entire spacecraft was covered in dust.","zh":"整艘太空船被塵埃覆蓋。"},{"en":"To be covered in dust means to have dust spread over the surface.","zh":"被塵埃覆蓋，指表面布滿塵埃。"},{"en":"A desk may be covered in dust after a classroom is unused for months.","zh":"課室數月未使用後，書桌可能被塵埃覆蓋。"},{"en":"If a spacecraft is covered in lunar dust, researchers can study how landing disturbed the surface.","zh":"如果太空船被月塵覆蓋，研究者可以研究着陸如何擾動表面。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a surface condition.","zh":"這個短語描述表面狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"kick up dust","meaning":"揚起塵埃","examples":[{"en":"The landing may have kicked up a large amount of dust.","zh":"這次着陸可能揚起大量塵埃。"},{"en":"To kick up dust means to disturb dust so that it rises into the air or spreads around.","zh":"揚起塵埃，指擾動塵埃，使它升起或四散。"},{"en":"A running child may kick up dust on a dry sports field.","zh":"孩子在乾燥運動場奔跑時，可能揚起塵埃。"},{"en":"If a spacecraft lands with force, it can blow or lift dust onto nearby objects.","zh":"如果太空船大力着陸，它可以吹起或揚起塵埃到附近物件上。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dust being stirred up by movement.","zh":"這個短語描述塵埃因動作而被攪起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"astronaut-archaeologists","meaning":"太空人考古學家","examples":[{"en":"Conrad and Bean acted as the first astronaut-archaeologists.","zh":"Conrad 和 Bean 充當首批太空人考古學家。"},{"en":"Astronaut-archaeologists are astronauts who carry out archaeological observation or collection in space.","zh":"太空人考古學家是在太空進行考古觀察或收集的太空人。"},{"en":"A future astronaut-archaeologist may photograph old landing sites before tourists arrive.","zh":"未來太空人考古學家可能在遊客到達前拍攝舊着陸遺址。"},{"en":"If astronauts document artefacts carefully, they combine space work with archaeological method.","zh":"如果太空人仔細記錄文物，他們就是把太空工作與考古方法結合。"},{"en":"The phrase blends two roles: space traveller and archaeological researcher.","zh":"這個短語融合兩種角色：太空旅人和考古研究者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"carefully remove","meaning":"小心拆除","examples":[{"en":"The astronauts carefully removed several parts of the probe.","zh":"太空人小心拆除探測器的幾個部分。"},{"en":"To carefully remove something means to take it away slowly and gently to avoid damage.","zh":"小心拆除某物，指慢慢而輕柔地取走它，以避免損壞。"},{"en":"A dentist carefully removes a damaged tooth so nearby teeth are not harmed.","zh":"牙醫小心移除受損牙齒，以免傷害附近牙齒。"},{"en":"If artefacts are removed too roughly, evidence may be destroyed.","zh":"如果文物被太粗暴地拆除，證據可能被破壞。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses controlled and delicate handling.","zh":"這個短語強調受控而細緻的處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"remote sampling arm","meaning":"遙距採樣臂","examples":[{"en":"They removed the probe’s remote sampling arm.","zh":"他們拆除了探測器的遙距採樣臂。"},{"en":"A remote sampling arm is a mechanical arm used to collect samples from a distance.","zh":"遙距採樣臂是用來從遠處收集樣本的機械臂。"},{"en":"A robot in a dangerous factory may use a remote arm to pick up hot or toxic materials.","zh":"危險工廠中的機械人可能使用遙距機械臂拿起高溫或有毒物料。"},{"en":"If a probe has a sampling arm, it can collect soil without moving its whole body.","zh":"如果探測器有採樣臂，它不用移動整個機身也能收集土壤。"},{"en":"The phrase names a tool for robotic scientific sampling.","zh":"這個短語指出用於機械科學採樣的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pieces of tubing","meaning":"管道組件","examples":[{"en":"Pieces of tubing were also collected as artefacts.","zh":"管道組件也被收集作為文物。"},{"en":"Pieces of tubing are short sections of pipe-like material.","zh":"管道組件是短小的管狀材料部分。"},{"en":"A mechanic may replace small pieces of tubing in a car engine if they crack.","zh":"如果汽車引擎中的小管道破裂，技工可能更換它們。"},{"en":"If tubing has spent years on the Moon, scientists can study how space conditions changed it.","zh":"如果管道在月球上停留多年，科學家可以研究太空環境如何改變它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to simple pipe sections that may still have research value.","zh":"這個短語指簡單管道部分，但仍可能具有研究價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"bag and label","meaning":"裝袋並加上標籤","examples":[{"en":"The astronauts bagged and labelled every artefact.","zh":"太空人把每件文物裝袋並加上標籤。"},{"en":"To bag and label an object means to place it in a bag and mark it with identifying information.","zh":"把物件裝袋並加上標籤，指把它放入袋中並標上識別資料。"},{"en":"In a science lab, students bag and label samples so they do not mix them up.","zh":"在科學實驗室中，學生把樣本裝袋並貼上標籤，以免混淆。"},{"en":"If artefacts are not labelled, researchers may lose information about where they came from.","zh":"如果文物沒有標籤，研究者可能失去它們來自何處的資料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful evidence handling.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細處理證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stow something on board","meaning":"將……存放在太空船上","examples":[{"en":"They stowed the collected objects on board the lunar module.","zh":"他們把收集到的物件存放在登月艙上。"},{"en":"To stow something on board means to store it safely inside a vehicle, ship or spacecraft.","zh":"將某物存放在交通工具、船隻或太空船上，指把它安全放在其中。"},{"en":"Passengers stow bags on board a plane before take-off.","zh":"乘客在飛機起飛前把行李存放在機上。"},{"en":"If astronauts collect artefacts, they must stow them securely so they survive the return journey.","zh":"如果太空人收集文物，就必須安全存放，使它們能經受返回旅程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes safe storage during travel.","zh":"這個短語描述旅行期間的安全儲存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"on their return to Earth","meaning":"返回地球後","examples":[{"en":"On their return to Earth, the astronauts delivered the artefacts to scientists.","zh":"返回地球後，太空人把文物交給科學家。"},{"en":"On their return to Earth means when they came back to Earth after being in space.","zh":"返回地球後，指他們在太空後回到地球時。"},{"en":"On returning from a field trip, students may give their samples to the laboratory teacher.","zh":"學生從田野考察回來後，可能把樣本交給實驗室老師。"},{"en":"If astronauts bring objects back, scientists can analyse them under controlled conditions.","zh":"如果太空人把物件帶回來，科學家就能在受控條件下分析它們。"},{"en":"The phrase marks what happened after the space mission ended.","zh":"這個短語標示太空任務結束後發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pass something on to","meaning":"將……交給","examples":[{"en":"The astronauts passed the objects on to research organisations.","zh":"太空人把這些物件交給研究組織。"},{"en":"To pass something on to someone means to give or transfer it to them.","zh":"將某物交給某人，指把它給予或轉交給他們。"},{"en":"A teacher may pass exam feedback on to students after marking.","zh":"老師評改後可能把考試回饋交給學生。"},{"en":"If astronauts pass artefacts on to scientists, specialists can study them in detail.","zh":"如果太空人把文物交給科學家，專家就能詳細研究它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes transfer from one person or group to another.","zh":"這個短語描述由一人或一群體轉交給另一方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"aerospace artefacts","meaning":"航天文物","examples":[{"en":"Scientists analysed changes in the aerospace artefacts.","zh":"科學家分析航天文物中的變化。"},{"en":"Aerospace artefacts are human-made objects connected with aircraft, rockets or space missions.","zh":"航天文物是與飛機、火箭或太空任務相關的人造物件。"},{"en":"A museum may display aerospace artefacts such as spacesuit parts, tools and old satellite equipment.","zh":"博物館可能展出太空衣部件、工具和舊衛星設備等航天文物。"},{"en":"If artefacts have been exposed to space, scientists can study how materials changed over time.","zh":"如果文物曾暴露於太空，科學家可以研究材料如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"The phrase treats space technology objects as historical evidence.","zh":"這個短語把太空科技物件視為歷史證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"one result of the analysis","meaning":"分析的一項結果","examples":[{"en":"One result of the analysis astonished the researchers.","zh":"分析的一項結果令研究人員震驚。"},{"en":"One result of the analysis means one finding produced after studying the evidence.","zh":"分析的一項結果，指研究證據後產生的一項發現。"},{"en":"One result of a school survey may show that students sleep less before exams.","zh":"學校調查的一項結果可能顯示學生考試前睡得較少。"},{"en":"If analysis produces an unexpected result, researchers may need further tests.","zh":"如果分析產生意料之外的結果，研究者可能需要進一步測試。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a specific finding from research.","zh":"這個短語引入研究中的一項具體發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"astonish someone","meaning":"令某人震驚","examples":[{"en":"The discovery of bacteria astonished the scientists.","zh":"發現細菌令科學家震驚。"},{"en":"To astonish someone means to surprise them greatly.","zh":"令某人震驚，指令他們非常驚訝。"},{"en":"A student’s sudden improvement may astonish a teacher who expected slow progress.","zh":"學生突然進步可能令原本預期進展緩慢的老師震驚。"},{"en":"If bacteria survive harsh space conditions, scientists may be deeply surprised.","zh":"如果細菌能在嚴酷太空環境中生存，科學家可能非常驚訝。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a very strong reaction of surprise.","zh":"這個短語描述非常強烈的驚訝反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a fragment of","meaning":"……的一塊碎片","examples":[{"en":"A fragment of the television camera contained unexpected evidence.","zh":"電視攝影機的一塊碎片含有意外證據。"},{"en":"A fragment of something is a small broken piece or part of it.","zh":"某物的一塊碎片，是它破裂後的小片或部分。"},{"en":"A fragment of glass on the floor may show where a window broke.","zh":"地板上的一塊玻璃碎片可能顯示窗戶在哪裡破裂。"},{"en":"If a camera fragment contains bacteria, even a tiny piece can become scientifically important.","zh":"如果攝影機碎片含有細菌，即使小碎片也可以具有科學重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a small part separated from a larger object.","zh":"這個短語指從較大物件分離出來的小部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"reveal evidence of","meaning":"顯示……的證據","examples":[{"en":"The camera fragment revealed evidence of bacteria.","zh":"攝影機碎片顯示細菌存在的證據。"},{"en":"To reveal evidence of something means to show signs that it exists or happened.","zh":"顯示某事的證據，指展示它存在或發生過的跡象。"},{"en":"A medical test may reveal evidence of infection before symptoms become serious.","zh":"醫學檢查可能在症狀變嚴重前顯示感染證據。"},{"en":"If an artefact reveals bacteria, scientists must ask whether the bacteria came from space or Earth.","zh":"如果文物顯示細菌，科學家必須問細菌來自太空還是地球。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces proof or signs discovered through investigation.","zh":"這個短語引出透過調查發現的證明或跡象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Streptococcus mitis","meaning":"緩症鏈球菌","examples":[{"en":"Scientists found evidence of the bacterium Streptococcus mitis.","zh":"科學家發現緩症鏈球菌這種細菌的證據。"},{"en":"Streptococcus mitis is a type of bacterium commonly associated with the human mouth and throat.","zh":"緩症鏈球菌是一種常與人類口腔和喉嚨相關的細菌。"},{"en":"A biology student may learn that some bacteria live harmlessly in the body but can still contaminate objects.","zh":"生物學生可能學到一些細菌無害地生活在人體內，但仍可污染物件。"},{"en":"If Streptococcus mitis is found on space equipment, researchers may suspect human contamination.","zh":"如果在太空設備上發現緩症鏈球菌，研究者可能懷疑人類污染。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific bacterial species.","zh":"這個短語指出一種特定細菌物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"for a moment","meaning":"一度；有一刻","examples":[{"en":"For a moment, researchers thought they had found life on the Moon.","zh":"有一刻，研究者以為他們在月球上發現了生命。"},{"en":"For a moment means for a very short time.","zh":"有一刻，指非常短的時間。"},{"en":"For a moment, a student may think they have lost their phone before finding it in their bag.","zh":"有一刻，學生可能以為自己遺失了手機，然後在書包中找到它。"},{"en":"If evidence looks surprising at first, people may briefly believe an exciting explanation.","zh":"如果證據起初看起來驚人，人們可能短暫相信令人興奮的解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a temporary thought or feeling.","zh":"這個短語標示暫時的想法或感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"evidence for life","meaning":"生命存在的證據","examples":[{"en":"The bacteria initially appeared to be evidence for life on the Moon.","zh":"這些細菌最初看似月球上有生命存在的證據。"},{"en":"Evidence for life means signs or proof suggesting that living organisms exist or existed.","zh":"生命存在的證據，指暗示生物存在或曾存在的跡象或證明。"},{"en":"Scientists may search for evidence for life on Mars by studying soil, ice and chemical traces.","zh":"科學家可能透過研究泥土、冰和化學痕跡，在火星尋找生命證據。"},{"en":"If bacteria are found in a sample, researchers must check whether they truly came from that environment.","zh":"如果樣本中發現細菌，研究者必須檢查它們是否真正來自該環境。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to possible proof of living things.","zh":"這個短語指生物存在的可能證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"after further research","meaning":"經進一步研究後","examples":[{"en":"After further research, scientists discovered a simpler explanation.","zh":"經進一步研究後，科學家發現一個較簡單的解釋。"},{"en":"After further research means after more investigation, testing or study has been done.","zh":"經進一步研究後，指在進行更多調查、測試或研究之後。"},{"en":"After further research, a student may realise that their first answer was wrong.","zh":"經進一步研究後，學生可能意識到自己最初答案錯了。"},{"en":"If an exciting discovery has a simple explanation, additional study is needed before conclusions are made.","zh":"如果令人興奮的發現有簡單解釋，在下結論前就需要額外研究。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that later evidence changed understanding.","zh":"這個短語顯示後來證據改變了理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the explanation became apparent","meaning":"解釋逐漸明朗","examples":[{"en":"The real explanation became apparent after further investigation.","zh":"經進一步調查後，真正解釋逐漸明朗。"},{"en":"If an explanation becomes apparent, it becomes clear or easy to understand.","zh":"如果解釋逐漸明朗，它就變得清楚或容易理解。"},{"en":"The reason for a student’s absence became apparent when the teacher received a medical note.","zh":"當老師收到醫生紙，學生缺席的原因就變得明朗。"},{"en":"If more evidence shows contamination before launch, the mystery of lunar bacteria becomes clearer.","zh":"如果更多證據顯示發射前已有污染，月球細菌之謎就更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a hidden answer becoming visible.","zh":"這個短語描述隱藏答案變得可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"prior to the launch","meaning":"在發射之前","examples":[{"en":"The camera had been contaminated prior to the launch.","zh":"攝影機在發射之前已被污染。"},{"en":"Prior to the launch means before the spacecraft was sent into space.","zh":"在發射之前，指太空船被送入太空之前。"},{"en":"Prior to an exam, students should check the time, room and required materials.","zh":"在考試之前，學生應檢查時間、課室和所需物品。"},{"en":"If contamination happened before launch, the bacteria came from Earth rather than the Moon.","zh":"如果污染發生在發射之前，細菌就來自地球而不是月球。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a time before an important event.","zh":"這個短語標示重要事件之前的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"install something in","meaning":"將……安裝於……","examples":[{"en":"A technician installed the camera in the probe.","zh":"技術員將攝影機安裝於探測器中。"},{"en":"To install something in a machine means to fit or place it there so it can work.","zh":"將某物安裝於機器中，指把它裝配或放置在那裡，使其能運作。"},{"en":"A technician may install a new projector in a classroom ceiling.","zh":"技術員可能把新投影機安裝於課室天花板。"},{"en":"If an object is contaminated during installation, the contamination can travel with the machine.","zh":"如果物件在安裝期間受污染，污染物就可以隨機器同行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes putting equipment into position for use.","zh":"這個短語描述把設備放到使用位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sneeze on","meaning":"對着……打噴嚏","examples":[{"en":"Someone had apparently sneezed on the camera.","zh":"顯然有人曾對着攝影機打噴嚏。"},{"en":"To sneeze on something means to release droplets from the nose or mouth onto it while sneezing.","zh":"對着某物打噴嚏，指打噴嚏時把鼻或口中的飛沫噴到它上面。"},{"en":"A student should not sneeze on shared books because germs may spread.","zh":"學生不應對着共用書本打噴嚏，因為細菌可能傳播。"},{"en":"If a technician sneezes on equipment, bacteria from the body may contaminate it.","zh":"如果技術員對着設備打噴嚏，人體細菌可能污染它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a simple action that can transfer germs.","zh":"這個短語描述一個可轉移病菌的簡單動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the resulting bacteria","meaning":"因而產生的細菌","examples":[{"en":"The resulting bacteria travelled to the Moon on the probe.","zh":"因而產生的細菌隨探測器前往月球。"},{"en":"The resulting bacteria means the bacteria that appeared or were left because of the earlier action.","zh":"因而產生的細菌，指因早前行動而出現或留下的細菌。"},{"en":"If someone coughs on a desk, the resulting germs may remain on the surface.","zh":"如果有人對着書桌咳嗽，因而留下的病菌可能停留在表面。"},{"en":"If bacteria from a sneeze stay on a camera, they can be carried wherever the camera goes.","zh":"如果噴嚏中的細菌留在攝影機上，它們就可以隨攝影機到任何地方。"},{"en":"The phrase links bacteria to the action that produced or left them.","zh":"這個短語把細菌與產生或留下它們的行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"alternating freezing and boiling","meaning":"冷熱交替","examples":[{"en":"The bacteria survived alternating freezing and boiling conditions.","zh":"這些細菌在冷熱交替的環境中存活下來。"},{"en":"Alternating freezing and boiling means repeated changes between extremely cold and extremely hot conditions.","zh":"冷熱交替，指在極冷和極熱條件之間反覆變化。"},{"en":"A material tested by moving it from ice to boiling water faces alternating temperature extremes.","zh":"材料從冰中移到沸水中測試，就是面對交替溫度極端。"},{"en":"If bacteria survive such changes, they are tougher than scientists expected.","zh":"如果細菌能在這些變化中存活，它們就比科學家預期更頑強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes harsh repeated temperature shifts.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴酷而反覆的溫度轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in a vacuum","meaning":"在真空中","examples":[{"en":"The bacteria remained in a vacuum for more than two years.","zh":"這些細菌在真空中停留了超過兩年。"},{"en":"In a vacuum means in a space with little or no air.","zh":"在真空中，指處於幾乎沒有或完全沒有空氣的空間。"},{"en":"Food can be sealed in a vacuum bag so air does not spoil it quickly.","zh":"食物可以密封在真空袋中，使空氣不會很快令它變壞。"},{"en":"If bacteria survive in a vacuum, they can live through conditions that seem deadly.","zh":"如果細菌能在真空中存活，它們就能經受看似致命的環境。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an airless environment.","zh":"這個短語描述無空氣環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"return promptly to life","meaning":"迅速恢復活性","examples":[{"en":"The bacteria returned promptly to life in the laboratory.","zh":"這些細菌在實驗室中迅速恢復活性。"},{"en":"To return promptly to life means to become active again quickly after appearing inactive or dead.","zh":"迅速恢復活性，指在看似不活躍或死亡後很快再次變得活躍。"},{"en":"A dried plant may return promptly to life after being watered, if its roots are still healthy.","zh":"如果根部仍健康，乾枯植物澆水後可能迅速恢復生機。"},{"en":"If bacteria revive quickly in a lab, harsh space conditions did not destroy them completely.","zh":"如果細菌在實驗室迅速復活，嚴酷太空環境就沒有完全摧毀它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rapid revival.","zh":"這個短語描述快速復活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"upon reaching","meaning":"一到達……便","examples":[{"en":"The bacteria revived upon reaching the safety of a laboratory.","zh":"細菌一到達實驗室的安全環境便復活。"},{"en":"Upon reaching a place means as soon as something arrives there.","zh":"一到達某地便，指某事一抵達該處就立即發生。"},{"en":"Upon reaching the classroom, students should put their homework on the teacher’s desk.","zh":"學生一到達課室，便應把功課放在老師桌上。"},{"en":"If bacteria became active upon reaching the laboratory, the new environment allowed them to recover.","zh":"如果細菌一到達實驗室便變活躍，新環境就讓它們恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase marks immediate action after arrival.","zh":"這個短語標示到達後立即發生的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the safety of a laboratory","meaning":"實驗室的安全環境","examples":[{"en":"The organisms became active again in the safety of a laboratory.","zh":"這些生物在實驗室的安全環境中再次變得活躍。"},{"en":"The safety of a laboratory means the controlled and protected conditions inside a scientific lab.","zh":"實驗室的安全環境，指科學實驗室內受控制和受保護的條件。"},{"en":"A dangerous chemical is easier to study in the safety of a laboratory than in a public space.","zh":"危險化學品在實驗室安全環境中，比在公共空間中更容易研究。"},{"en":"If organisms revive in a lab, the safe temperature, air and nutrients may support them.","zh":"如果生物在實驗室復活，安全溫度、空氣和營養可能支援它們。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts controlled research conditions with harsh outside environments.","zh":"這個短語把受控研究條件與嚴酷外部環境作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the vastness of space","meaning":"浩瀚太空","examples":[{"en":"Even the vastness of space could not destroy the bacteria.","zh":"即使浩瀚太空也不能摧毀這些細菌。"},{"en":"The vastness of space means the enormous size, emptiness and distance of outer space.","zh":"浩瀚太空指外太空巨大的尺度、空曠和距離。"},{"en":"Looking at the night sky can make people feel the vastness of space.","zh":"望着夜空可以令人感受到浩瀚太空。"},{"en":"If bacteria survive such emptiness and distance, the discovery feels surprising.","zh":"如果細菌能在這種空曠和距離中存活，發現就令人驚訝。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises the huge and harsh scale of space.","zh":"這個短語強調太空巨大而嚴酷的尺度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stop someone from doing something","meaning":"阻止某人做某事","examples":[{"en":"Space could not stop humans from spreading bacteria.","zh":"太空不能阻止人類傳播細菌。"},{"en":"To stop someone from doing something means to prevent them from doing it.","zh":"阻止某人做某事，指防止他們做該事。"},{"en":"Clear rules can stop students from entering a laboratory without safety goggles.","zh":"清楚規則可以阻止學生不戴護目鏡進入實驗室。"},{"en":"If even space cannot stop bacteria from travelling with humans, contamination control is important.","zh":"如果連太空也不能阻止細菌隨人類旅行，污染管制就很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes prevention of an action.","zh":"這個短語描述防止某行動發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"spread a sore throat","meaning":"傳播引致喉嚨痛的病菌","examples":[{"en":"The finding humorously suggested that humans could spread a sore throat into space.","zh":"這項發現幽默地暗示人類可以把引致喉嚨痛的病菌傳到太空。"},{"en":"To spread a sore throat means to pass throat-related germs from one person or place to another.","zh":"傳播喉嚨痛病菌，指把與喉嚨相關的病菌從一個人或地方傳到另一處。"},{"en":"A student with a sore throat may spread germs by coughing on shared desks.","zh":"喉嚨痛的學生可能透過對共用書桌咳嗽來傳播病菌。"},{"en":"If bacteria from the mouth travel on space equipment, human illness can symbolically reach space.","zh":"如果口腔細菌隨太空設備旅行，人類疾病就象徵性地到達太空。"},{"en":"The phrase is humorous here because a minor human infection appears in a space context.","zh":"這個短語在此帶幽默意味，因為小小人類感染出現在太空語境中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"unexpected spin-off","meaning":"意料之外的附帶發現","examples":[{"en":"The bacterial discovery was an unexpected spin-off of the mission.","zh":"細菌發現是這次任務意料之外的附帶發現。"},{"en":"An unexpected spin-off is an unplanned result or benefit that comes from another activity.","zh":"意料之外的附帶發現，是由另一活動帶來的非計劃結果或好處。"},{"en":"A school project about recycling may have an unexpected spin-off when students start saving energy at home.","zh":"關於回收的學校項目，可能產生學生在家開始節能這一意料之外的附帶效果。"},{"en":"If scientists study a spacecraft and accidentally learn about bacteria survival, the extra discovery is a spin-off.","zh":"如果科學家研究太空船時意外了解細菌生存，額外發現就是附帶成果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a surprising secondary outcome.","zh":"這個短語描述令人驚訝的次要結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"broader significance","meaning":"更廣泛的意義","examples":[{"en":"The recovered artefacts have a broader significance for archaeology.","zh":"被帶回的文物對考古學有更廣泛的意義。"},{"en":"Broader significance means importance beyond the immediate case or simple example.","zh":"更廣泛的意義，指重要性超出眼前個案或簡單例子。"},{"en":"A student’s grammar mistake may have broader significance if many classmates make the same error.","zh":"如果許多同學犯同一文法錯誤，某學生的錯誤可能有更廣泛意義。"},{"en":"If lunar artefacts change how archaeologists think about evidence, their meaning extends beyond one mission.","zh":"如果月球文物改變考古學家對證據的看法，其意義就超出單一任務。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something matters in a wider context.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事在更大語境中重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"simple as they may seem","meaning":"儘管它們看似簡單","examples":[{"en":"Simple as they may seem, the objects are historically important.","zh":"儘管它們看似簡單，這些物件在歷史上很重要。"},{"en":"Simple as they may seem means although they appear ordinary or plain.","zh":"儘管它們看似簡單，指雖然它們看起來普通或樸素。"},{"en":"Simple as they may seem, old family letters can reveal personal history.","zh":"儘管舊家書看似簡單，它們可以揭示個人歷史。"},{"en":"If an object looks basic but records a first achievement, it can still have great value.","zh":"如果物件看似基本但記錄首次成就，它仍可以有巨大價值。"},{"en":"The phrase creates contrast between appearance and importance.","zh":"這個短語在外觀和重要性之間建立對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"provide the first example of","meaning":"提供……的首個例子","examples":[{"en":"The artefacts provide the first example of extraterrestrial archaeology.","zh":"這些文物提供地球以外考古學的首個例子。"},{"en":"To provide the first example of something means to be the earliest case showing that thing.","zh":"提供某事的首個例子，指成為展示該事的最早個案。"},{"en":"A school’s first online debate may provide the first example of a new teaching method in action.","zh":"學校首次網上辯論可能提供新教學方法實行的首個例子。"},{"en":"If astronauts studied a human-made object on the Moon, that event can count as an early case of space archaeology.","zh":"如果太空人在月球研究人造物件，該事件可算作太空考古的早期案例。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a pioneering instance.","zh":"這個短語突出開創性個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"extraterrestrial archaeology","meaning":"地球以外的考古學","examples":[{"en":"The study of Surveyor 3 was an early example of extraterrestrial archaeology.","zh":"對 Surveyor 3 的研究是地球以外考古學的早期例子。"},{"en":"Extraterrestrial archaeology is archaeology carried out beyond Earth or on objects from space missions.","zh":"地球以外的考古學，是在地球以外或針對太空任務物件進行的考古。"},{"en":"Future researchers may practise extraterrestrial archaeology by studying old equipment on the Moon.","zh":"未來研究者可能透過研究月球上的舊設備來實踐地球以外考古學。"},{"en":"If human artefacts exist on another planet, archaeology can extend beyond Earth.","zh":"如果另一行星上有人造文物，考古學就能延伸至地球以外。"},{"en":"The phrase names a new field linking archaeology with space exploration.","zh":"這個短語指出連結考古學與太空探索的新領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"more significant for","meaning":"對……更具重要性","examples":[{"en":"The artefacts may be even more significant for the history of archaeology.","zh":"這些文物對考古學史可能更具重要性。"},{"en":"More significant for something means more important in relation to that field, question or purpose.","zh":"對某事更具重要性，指在該範疇、問題或目的上更重要。"},{"en":"A student’s first failure may be more significant for their growth than an easy success.","zh":"學生第一次失敗對其成長可能比輕易成功更具重要性。"},{"en":"If lunar objects change how archaeology is defined, they become highly important to the discipline.","zh":"如果月球物件改變考古學的定義，它們對該學科就非常重要。"},{"en":"The phrase compares importance for a particular area.","zh":"這個短語比較某範疇中的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the history of the discipline","meaning":"該學科的歷史","examples":[{"en":"The discovery has importance for the history of the archaeological discipline.","zh":"這項發現對考古學這門學科的歷史很重要。"},{"en":"The history of the discipline means the development of an academic field over time.","zh":"該學科的歷史，指某學術領域隨時間發展的過程。"},{"en":"A new teaching theory may become part of the history of education as a discipline.","zh":"新教學理論可能成為教育學作為一門學科的歷史一部分。"},{"en":"If archaeology expands into space, that change becomes a landmark in the field’s history.","zh":"如果考古學擴展到太空，這種改變就成為該領域歷史中的里程碑。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how a subject itself has evolved.","zh":"這個短語強調某學科本身如何演變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"formational archaeology","meaning":"形成過程考古學","examples":[{"en":"Formational archaeology studies how artefacts change over time.","zh":"形成過程考古學研究文物如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"Formational archaeology examines the processes that affect objects after they are made, used, abandoned or buried.","zh":"形成過程考古學檢視物件被製造、使用、棄置或埋藏後受到哪些過程影響。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may study how rain, soil, animals and people change a site after it is left behind.","zh":"考古學家可能研究雨水、泥土、動物和人如何在遺址被留下後改變它。"},{"en":"If a spacecraft part changes after years on the Moon, formational archaeology asks what forces caused those changes.","zh":"如果太空船零件在月球多年後改變，形成過程考古學會問哪些力量造成這些變化。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how archaeological evidence is formed and altered.","zh":"這個短語強調考古證據如何形成和被改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"environmental and cultural forces","meaning":"環境及文化力量","examples":[{"en":"Artefacts are affected by environmental and cultural forces.","zh":"文物受到環境及文化力量影響。"},{"en":"Environmental and cultural forces are natural conditions and human behaviours that shape or change objects.","zh":"環境及文化力量，是塑造或改變物件的自然條件和人類行為。"},{"en":"Rain, sunlight, cleaning habits and tourism can all affect a historic building.","zh":"雨水、陽光、清潔習慣和旅遊都可以影響歷史建築。"},{"en":"If an artefact sits in space, radiation is an environmental force, while human removal is a cultural force.","zh":"如果文物位於太空，輻射是環境力量，而人類移走物件是文化力量。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why objects do not remain unchanged after use.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何物件使用後不會保持不變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the life history of","meaning":"……的生命歷程","examples":[{"en":"Researchers study the life history of human artefacts in space.","zh":"研究者研究太空中人造文物的生命歷程。"},{"en":"The life history of an artefact is the full story of its creation, use, abandonment, change and discovery.","zh":"文物的生命歷程，是其製造、使用、棄置、變化和被發現的完整故事。"},{"en":"A museum may explain the life history of a clay pot from its making to its excavation.","zh":"博物館可能解釋陶罐由製作到出土的生命歷程。"},{"en":"If a probe was built on Earth, landed on the Moon and later sampled, its life history crosses worlds.","zh":"如果探測器在地球製造、降落月球並後來被採樣，其生命歷程就跨越兩個世界。"},{"en":"The phrase treats objects as having a history of stages.","zh":"這個短語把物件視為擁有不同階段的歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"human artefacts","meaning":"人造文物","examples":[{"en":"Human artefacts in space may preserve evidence of exploration.","zh":"太空中的人造文物可能保存探索證據。"},{"en":"Human artefacts are objects made, used or modified by people.","zh":"人造文物是由人製造、使用或改造的物件。"},{"en":"A stone tool, a cooking pot or a spacecraft camera can all be human artefacts.","zh":"石器、煮食陶罐或太空船攝影機都可以是人造文物。"},{"en":"If an artefact is left behind, later researchers can study what people valued and how they worked.","zh":"如果文物被留下，後來研究者可以研究人們重視甚麼以及如何工作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to human-made evidence, not natural objects.","zh":"這個短語指人造證據，而不是自然物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"complete each sentence with","meaning":"用……完成每個句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete each sentence with the correct ending.","zh":"考生用正確句尾完成每個句子。"},{"en":"To complete each sentence with something means to finish every sentence using the required word, phrase or option.","zh":"用某物完成每個句子，指使用所需詞語、短語或選項完成每句。"},{"en":"In a reading exercise, students complete each sentence with information from the passage.","zh":"在閱讀練習中，學生用文章資料完成每個句子。"},{"en":"If the ending does not match the grammar or meaning, the answer will not fit.","zh":"如果句尾不符合文法或意思，答案就不合適。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction for sentence-completion questions.","zh":"這個短語是句子完成題的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the correct ending","meaning":"正確句尾","examples":[{"en":"Students select the correct ending from the box.","zh":"學生從方框中選出正確句尾。"},{"en":"The correct ending is the option that accurately completes the sentence according to the passage.","zh":"正確句尾是根據文章準確完成句子的選項。"},{"en":"A student should read the sentence before and after the gap to find the correct ending.","zh":"學生應閱讀空格前後句子，以找出正確句尾。"},{"en":"If two endings seem possible, the passage evidence should decide the answer.","zh":"如果兩個句尾看似可能，文章證據應決定答案。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the exact final part needed in a matching task.","zh":"這個短語指配對題中所需的準確結尾部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"main academic work","meaning":"主要學術研究","examples":[{"en":"Ben Finney’s main academic work concerns Polynesian exploration.","zh":"Ben Finney 的主要學術研究關於波利尼西亞探索。"},{"en":"Main academic work means the central research area or scholarly focus of a person’s career.","zh":"主要學術研究，指某人職業生涯中的核心研究範圍或學術焦點。"},{"en":"A professor’s main academic work may be child language development rather than classroom testing.","zh":"教授的主要學術研究可能是兒童語言發展，而不是課堂測驗。"},{"en":"If a scholar spends many years on one topic, that topic becomes their main academic work.","zh":"如果學者多年研究同一題目，該題目就成為其主要學術研究。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a researcher’s primary field of study.","zh":"這個短語指出研究者的主要研究領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"investigate the way that","meaning":"研究……的方式","examples":[{"en":"His research investigates the way that early explorers used technology.","zh":"他的研究探討早期探險者使用技術的方式。"},{"en":"To investigate the way that something happens means to study how it happens or is done.","zh":"研究某事發生的方式，指研究它如何發生或如何完成。"},{"en":"A school may investigate the way that students use phones during revision.","zh":"學校可能研究學生溫習時使用手機的方式。"},{"en":"If researchers study how explorers navigated, they can understand the technology behind migration.","zh":"如果研究者研究探險者如何導航，就能理解遷徙背後的技術。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on method and process.","zh":"這個短語強調方法和過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"past explorers","meaning":"過去的探險者","examples":[{"en":"Past explorers used technology to settle new regions.","zh":"過去的探險者使用技術定居新地區。"},{"en":"Past explorers are people from earlier times who travelled into unfamiliar places.","zh":"過去的探險者，是早期前往陌生地方的人。"},{"en":"Past explorers may have used maps, boats, stars or local guides to move through unknown areas.","zh":"過去的探險者可能使用地圖、船隻、星象或本地嚮導穿越未知地區。"},{"en":"If past explorers left tools behind, archaeologists can study how they travelled.","zh":"如果過去探險者留下工具，考古學家就能研究他們如何旅行。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to historical travellers who expanded known worlds.","zh":"這個短語指擴展已知世界的歷史旅行者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"find new places to live","meaning":"尋找新的居住地","examples":[{"en":"Polynesians used technology to find new places to live.","zh":"波利尼西亞人使用技術尋找新的居住地。"},{"en":"To find new places to live means to discover and settle in new homes or territories.","zh":"尋找新的居住地，指發現並定居於新的家園或地區。"},{"en":"A family may find a new place to live when rent becomes too high in their old district.","zh":"當舊區租金太高，家庭可能尋找新的居住地。"},{"en":"If explorers find suitable islands, their communities can grow in new environments.","zh":"如果探險者找到合適島嶼，其社群就能在新環境中成長。"},{"en":"The phrase connects searching with settlement.","zh":"這個短語把尋找與定居連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in the long term","meaning":"長遠而言","examples":[{"en":"Finney believed that space sites would be studied in the long term.","zh":"Finney 相信太空遺址長遠而言會被研究。"},{"en":"In the long term means over a long future period, not immediately.","zh":"長遠而言，指在很長的未來時期內，而不是立即。"},{"en":"In the long term, regular reading improves writing more than last-minute memorisation.","zh":"長遠而言，定期閱讀比臨急背誦更能改善寫作。"},{"en":"If space archaeology is not possible now, it may still become important decades later.","zh":"如果太空考古現在不可行，它仍可能在數十年後變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase shifts attention from immediate results to future development.","zh":"這個短語把注意力由即時結果轉向未來發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"commercial pressures","meaning":"商業壓力","examples":[{"en":"Commercial pressures may place lunar sites under threat.","zh":"商業壓力可能令月球遺址面臨威脅。"},{"en":"Commercial pressures are business forces or demands connected with making money.","zh":"商業壓力是與賺錢相關的商業力量或要求。"},{"en":"A small shop may face commercial pressures when rent rises and chain stores compete nearby.","zh":"當租金上升且連鎖店在附近競爭，小店可能面對商業壓力。"},{"en":"If companies want profit from space tourism, historic sites may be treated as attractions rather than heritage.","zh":"如果公司想從太空旅遊獲利，歷史遺址可能被當成景點而不是文化遺產。"},{"en":"The phrase describes money-driven pressure on decisions.","zh":"這個短語描述由金錢推動的決策壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in the immediate future","meaning":"在不久的將來","examples":[{"en":"Important lunar sites may face danger in the immediate future.","zh":"重要月球遺址可能在不久的將來面臨危險。"},{"en":"In the immediate future means very soon or in the near short term.","zh":"在不久的將來，指很快或近期短時間內。"},{"en":"A school may not build a new library in the immediate future if funding is not ready.","zh":"如果資金未準備好，學校可能在不久將來不會興建新圖書館。"},{"en":"If space tourism develops quickly, heritage risks may appear sooner than expected.","zh":"如果太空旅遊迅速發展，文化遺產風險可能比預期更早出現。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the next short period of time.","zh":"這個短語指接下來短時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be under threat","meaning":"面臨威脅","examples":[{"en":"Historic sites on the Moon may be under threat from tourism.","zh":"月球上的歷史遺址可能因旅遊而面臨威脅。"},{"en":"To be under threat means to be in danger of being harmed, damaged or lost.","zh":"面臨威脅，指處於可能受害、受損或消失的危險中。"},{"en":"A local market may be under threat if a new development plan replaces old shops.","zh":"如果新發展計劃取代舊商店，本地市場可能面臨威脅。"},{"en":"If tourists enter fragile lunar areas, footprints and equipment may be damaged.","zh":"如果遊客進入脆弱月球區域，腳印和設備可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a serious risk to survival or safety.","zh":"這個短語描述對生存或安全的嚴重風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be concerned by","meaning":"對……感到憂慮","examples":[{"en":"Academics are concerned by damage caused in isolated regions.","zh":"學者對偏遠地區造成的破壞感到憂慮。"},{"en":"To be concerned by something means to feel worried about it.","zh":"對某事感到憂慮，指因它而擔心。"},{"en":"Parents may be concerned by a sudden fall in a child’s school results.","zh":"家長可能因孩子成績突然下跌而感到憂慮。"},{"en":"If damage already happened in remote places on Earth, scholars may worry about similar damage in space.","zh":"如果地球偏遠地區已發生破壞，學者可能擔心太空出現類似破壞。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses worry caused by evidence or events.","zh":"這個短語表達由證據或事件引起的擔心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"isolated regions","meaning":"偏遠地區","examples":[{"en":"Tourists and scientists have already damaged some isolated regions.","zh":"遊客和科學家已經破壞了一些偏遠地區。"},{"en":"Isolated regions are areas far from major towns, roads or regular human activity.","zh":"偏遠地區是遠離主要城鎮、道路或日常人類活動的地方。"},{"en":"A small mountain village may be an isolated region if it is difficult to reach.","zh":"如果小山村難以到達，它可能是偏遠地區。"},{"en":"If isolated regions are damaged despite being remote, fragile lunar sites may also be vulnerable.","zh":"如果偏遠地區即使遙遠也被破壞，脆弱月球遺址也可能容易受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes places separated from ordinary centres of activity.","zh":"這個短語描述與普通活動中心分隔的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"harm the environment","meaning":"破壞環境","examples":[{"en":"Uncontrolled activities can harm the environment.","zh":"不受控制的活動可以破壞環境。"},{"en":"To harm the environment means to damage air, water, land, wildlife or natural systems.","zh":"破壞環境，指損害空氣、水、土地、野生動物或自然系統。"},{"en":"Dumping rubbish into a river can harm the environment and the people who depend on it.","zh":"把垃圾倒入河流可以破壞環境，也傷害依賴河流的人。"},{"en":"If visitors leave waste in a fragile region, the local ecosystem may suffer.","zh":"如果訪客在脆弱地區留下廢物，本地生態系統可能受害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes negative effects on nature.","zh":"這個短語描述對自然的負面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"one problem with","meaning":"……的一個問題","examples":[{"en":"One problem with the treaty is its treatment of human-made objects.","zh":"該條約的一個問題是它對人造物件的處理。"},{"en":"One problem with something means one weakness, difficulty or fault in it.","zh":"某事的一個問題，指其中一個弱點、困難或缺陷。"},{"en":"One problem with online lessons is that some students have poor internet access.","zh":"網課的一個問題是一些學生網絡不穩。"},{"en":"If a treaty treats historic objects as junk, that weakness can affect heritage protection.","zh":"如果條約把歷史物件視為垃圾，這弱點會影響文化遺產保護。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a specific criticism.","zh":"這個短語引入具體批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"man-made objects","meaning":"人造物件","examples":[{"en":"Man-made objects left in space may be historically valuable.","zh":"留在太空中的人造物件可能具有歷史價值。"},{"en":"Man-made objects are things created by humans rather than by nature.","zh":"人造物件是由人類而非自然創造的東西。"},{"en":"A bridge, a pencil and a spacecraft are all man-made objects.","zh":"橋樑、鉛筆和太空船都是人造物件。"},{"en":"If man-made objects record exploration, they may become artefacts instead of rubbish.","zh":"如果人造物件記錄探索，它們可能成為文物，而不是垃圾。"},{"en":"The phrase distinguishes human creations from natural materials.","zh":"這個短語把人類創造物與自然材料區分開來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be regarded as rubbish","meaning":"被視為垃圾","examples":[{"en":"Historically important objects may be regarded as rubbish under the treaty.","zh":"具有歷史重要性的物件在條約下可能被視為垃圾。"},{"en":"To be regarded as rubbish means to be seen as waste with little or no value.","zh":"被視為垃圾，指被看成沒有或幾乎沒有價值的廢物。"},{"en":"Old letters may be regarded as rubbish by one person but as family history by another.","zh":"舊信件可能被一個人視為垃圾，卻被另一個人視為家族歷史。"},{"en":"If space artefacts are treated as rubbish, people may remove or destroy them too easily.","zh":"如果太空文物被當作垃圾，人們可能太容易移走或毀壞它們。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how classification can reduce perceived value.","zh":"這個短語顯示分類如何降低被感知的價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"legal agreements","meaning":"法律協議","examples":[{"en":"Legal agreements do not clearly assign responsibility for lunar sites.","zh":"法律協議沒有清楚分配月球遺址的責任。"},{"en":"Legal agreements are formal documents or arrangements that create rights, duties or rules.","zh":"法律協議是建立權利、義務或規則的正式文件或安排。"},{"en":"A rental contract is a legal agreement between a landlord and a tenant.","zh":"租約是業主與租客之間的法律協議。"},{"en":"If legal agreements are unclear, people may argue about who must protect a site.","zh":"如果法律協議不清楚，人們可能爭論誰必須保護遺址。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to rules with legal force.","zh":"這個短語指具有法律效力的規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ownership of land","meaning":"土地擁有權","examples":[{"en":"International rules restrict the ownership of land in space.","zh":"國際規則限制太空中的土地擁有權。"},{"en":"Ownership of land means the legal right to possess or control land.","zh":"土地擁有權指擁有或控制土地的法律權利。"},{"en":"A family buying a house must also understand ownership of the land under it.","zh":"家庭購買房屋時，也必須理解其下土地的擁有權。"},{"en":"If ownership of lunar land is forbidden, heritage managers cannot use ordinary property law easily.","zh":"如果月球土地擁有權被禁止，文化遺產管理者就難以使用普通物業法。"},{"en":"The phrase concerns who legally controls land.","zh":"這個短語涉及誰在法律上控制土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"responsibility for","meaning":"對……的責任","examples":[{"en":"It may be unclear who has responsibility for historic footprints.","zh":"誰對歷史腳印負有責任可能並不清楚。"},{"en":"Responsibility for something means the duty to look after it, protect it or deal with it.","zh":"對某事的責任，指照顧、保護或處理它的義務。"},{"en":"In a classroom, students may share responsibility for keeping the room clean.","zh":"在課室中，學生可能共同負責保持房間清潔。"},{"en":"If no one has responsibility for lunar footprints, no one may prevent tourists from damaging them.","zh":"如果沒有人對月球腳印負責，就可能沒有人阻止遊客破壞它們。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who must take care of an issue.","zh":"這個短語指出誰必須照顧某問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete the flow chart","meaning":"完成流程圖","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the flow chart with words from the passage.","zh":"考生用文章中的詞語完成流程圖。"},{"en":"To complete the flow chart means to fill in missing steps or labels in a process diagram.","zh":"完成流程圖，指填寫過程圖中的缺漏步驟或標籤。"},{"en":"Students may complete a flow chart showing how rainwater becomes drinking water.","zh":"學生可能完成展示雨水如何變成飲用水的流程圖。"},{"en":"If the chart shows a sequence, each answer must fit the next stage logically.","zh":"如果圖表顯示次序，每個答案都必須在邏輯上符合下一階段。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction for process-based reading questions.","zh":"這個短語是過程類閱讀題的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"no more than one word","meaning":"不超過一個字","examples":[{"en":"Each flow-chart answer must contain no more than one word.","zh":"每個流程圖答案必須不超過一個字。"},{"en":"No more than one word means the answer must be one word only, not a phrase.","zh":"不超過一個字，指答案必須只是一個詞，而不是短語。"},{"en":"If the answer is “dust,” it fits; if the answer is “lunar dust,” it may break the rule.","zh":"如果答案是 “dust”，就符合要求；如果答案是 “lunar dust”，可能違反規則。"},{"en":"If students write two words when only one is allowed, the answer may be marked wrong.","zh":"如果只准一個詞而學生寫兩個詞，答案可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict exam word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格考試字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"choose two letters","meaning":"選出兩個字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose two letters from the answer options.","zh":"考生從答案選項中選出兩個字母。"},{"en":"To choose two letters means to select two answer choices, usually from options such as A, B, C and D.","zh":"選出兩個字母，指從 A、B、C、D 等選項中選擇兩個答案。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should choose two letters only if the question asks for two answers.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，只有題目要求兩個答案時，學生才應選兩個字母。"},{"en":"If students choose three letters, even one correct answer may not save the response.","zh":"如果學生選三個字母，即使其中一個正確，也未必能保住答案。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the required number of multiple-choice answers.","zh":"這個短語給出選擇題所需答案數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"main purposes of the writer","meaning":"作者的主要目的","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the main purposes of the writer.","zh":"題目詢問作者的主要目的。"},{"en":"The main purposes of the writer are the central reasons why the writer wrote the passage or section.","zh":"作者的主要目的，是作者寫該文章或段落的核心原因。"},{"en":"A writer’s main purposes may be to explain a problem and persuade readers to care about it.","zh":"作者的主要目的可能是解釋問題並說服讀者關心它。"},{"en":"If a passage both warns about damage and introduces a new field, the writer may have more than one purpose.","zh":"如果文章既警告破壞，又介紹新領域，作者可能有多於一個目的。"},{"en":"The phrase asks about intention, not just topic.","zh":"這個短語問的是意圖，而不只是題目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the reasons why","meaning":"……的原因","examples":[{"en":"One option concerns the reasons why space archaeology might be impossible.","zh":"一個選項涉及太空考古可能不可能的原因。"},{"en":"The reasons why means the causes or explanations for something.","zh":"某事的原因，指造成或解釋該事的因素。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to explain the reasons why a character made a poor decision.","zh":"老師可能要求學生解釋角色作出差劣決定的原因。"},{"en":"If people claim space archaeology is impossible, they should provide practical or legal reasons.","zh":"如果有人聲稱太空考古不可能，他們應提供實際或法律原因。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces explanation of causes.","zh":"這個短語引入成因解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"dangers that could follow from","meaning":"可能由……引起的危險","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions dangers that could follow from contamination.","zh":"題目提到可能由污染引起的危險。"},{"en":"Dangers that could follow from something are risks or harmful results that may happen because of it.","zh":"可能由某事引起的危險，是因它而可能發生的風險或有害結果。"},{"en":"Dangers that could follow from poor food storage include illness and waste.","zh":"可能由食物儲存不當引起的危險包括疾病和浪費。"},{"en":"If space objects are contaminated, scientists may draw false conclusions about life beyond Earth.","zh":"如果太空物件受到污染，科學家可能對地球以外生命作出錯誤結論。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a cause with possible negative consequences.","zh":"這個短語把原因與可能負面後果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contamination of objects","meaning":"物件受到污染","examples":[{"en":"Contamination of objects can produce misleading scientific evidence.","zh":"物件受到污染可以產生誤導性的科學證據。"},{"en":"Contamination of objects means unwanted material, germs or chemicals get onto objects and affect them.","zh":"物件受到污染，指不需要的物質、細菌或化學品沾上物件並影響它們。"},{"en":"A lab sample may be ruined by contamination if someone touches it with dirty hands.","zh":"如果有人用髒手觸摸實驗室樣本，樣本可能因污染而毀掉。"},{"en":"If space equipment is contaminated before launch, later discoveries may be wrongly interpreted.","zh":"如果太空設備在發射前受污染，後來發現可能被錯誤解讀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pollution or impurity affecting physical evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述污染或雜質影響實物證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"set up careful controls","meaning":"設立嚴格管制","examples":[{"en":"Authorities may need to set up careful controls over space tourism.","zh":"當局可能需要對太空旅遊設立嚴格管制。"},{"en":"To set up careful controls means to create detailed rules and systems to manage risk.","zh":"設立嚴格管制，指建立詳細規則和系統來管理風險。"},{"en":"A school may set up careful controls for laboratory experiments involving chemicals.","zh":"學校可能為涉及化學品的實驗設立嚴格管制。"},{"en":"If tourists visit fragile sites, careful controls can limit where they walk and what they touch.","zh":"如果遊客參觀脆弱遺址，嚴格管制可以限制他們走到哪裡和觸摸甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised prevention before damage happens.","zh":"這個短語描述在破壞發生前有組織地預防。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"controls over space tourism","meaning":"對太空旅遊的管制","examples":[{"en":"Controls over space tourism could protect historic lunar sites.","zh":"對太空旅遊的管制可以保護歷史月球遺址。"},{"en":"Controls over space tourism are rules that limit and manage tourist activity beyond Earth.","zh":"對太空旅遊的管制，是限制和管理地球以外旅遊活動的規則。"},{"en":"Controls over a school trip may include fixed routes, group leaders and no-touch rules.","zh":"對學校旅行的管制可能包括固定路線、小組領袖和禁止觸摸規則。"},{"en":"If space tourists must follow strict controls, fragile footprints and artefacts are less likely to be damaged.","zh":"如果太空旅客必須遵守嚴格管制，脆弱腳印和文物就較不容易受損。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to regulation of leisure travel in space.","zh":"這個短語指對太空休閒旅遊的規管。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"preserve historic sites and objects","meaning":"保存歷史遺址及文物","examples":[{"en":"International action is needed to preserve historic sites and objects in space.","zh":"需要國際行動來保存太空中的歷史遺址及文物。"},{"en":"To preserve historic sites and objects means to protect important places and artefacts from damage or loss.","zh":"保存歷史遺址及文物，指保護重要地點和文物免受損害或消失。"},{"en":"Museums preserve old objects by controlling light, temperature and handling.","zh":"博物館透過控制光線、溫度和處理方式來保存舊物件。"},{"en":"If lunar landing sites are preserved, future generations can study the beginning of space exploration.","zh":"如果月球着陸遺址得到保存，未來世代就能研究太空探索的開端。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on keeping physical heritage safe.","zh":"這個短語強調保護實體文化遺產安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"cultural effects of space travel","meaning":"太空旅行的文化影響","examples":[{"en":"Space travel may eventually produce important cultural effects.","zh":"太空旅行最終可能產生重要文化影響。"},{"en":"Cultural effects of space travel are changes in human values, identity, memory, heritage or social behaviour caused by going into space.","zh":"太空旅行的文化影響，是進入太空所造成的人類價值觀、身份、記憶、文化遺產或社會行為改變。"},{"en":"A successful Moon base could affect culture by changing how people imagine home, nation and humanity.","zh":"成功的月球基地可以透過改變人們對家園、國家和人類的想像而影響文化。"},{"en":"If space travel leaves objects, stories and rituals behind, it becomes part of cultural history.","zh":"如果太空旅行留下物件、故事和儀式，它就成為文化史的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase looks beyond technology to the human meaning of space exploration.","zh":"這個短語超越科技，關注太空探索的人類意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 111 - Space - The Final Archaeological Frontier.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 112":[{"front":"Aboriginal artists","meaning":"澳洲原住民藝術家","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal artists are now internationally recognised for their distinctive work.","zh":"澳洲原住民藝術家現在因其獨特作品而獲國際認可。"},{"en":"Aboriginal artists are artists from Australia’s Indigenous communities who create works connected with culture, land, memory and identity.","zh":"Aboriginal artists 是來自澳洲原住民社群、創作與文化、土地、記憶和身份相關作品的藝術家。"},{"en":"A museum may invite Aboriginal artists to explain the stories behind their paintings.","zh":"博物館可能邀請澳洲原住民藝術家解釋畫作背後的故事。"},{"en":"When Aboriginal artists gain international attention, their communities may receive wider cultural recognition.","zh":"當澳洲原住民藝術家獲得國際關注，其社群也可能得到更廣泛文化認可。"},{"en":"This phrase refers not only to individual painters but also to a living cultural tradition.","zh":"這個片語不只指個別畫家，也指一種活生生的文化傳統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be much in demand","meaning":"需求很高；大受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The works of Aboriginal artists are now much in demand throughout the world.","zh":"澳洲原住民藝術家的作品現在在世界各地需求很高。"},{"en":"To be much in demand means many people want to buy, see or use something.","zh":"be much in demand 指許多人想購買、觀看或使用某物。"},{"en":"Good English tutors are much in demand before public examinations.","zh":"公開考試前，優秀英文導師需求很高。"},{"en":"If an artist’s work is much in demand, galleries may compete to display it.","zh":"如果藝術家的作品大受歡迎，畫廊可能爭相展出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong popularity or market interest.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈受歡迎程度或市場興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"throughout the world","meaning":"世界各地","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal art is exhibited throughout the world.","zh":"澳洲原住民藝術在世界各地展出。"},{"en":"Throughout the world means in many countries or across the whole world.","zh":"throughout the world 指在許多國家或遍及全球。"},{"en":"Popular films can be watched throughout the world through streaming platforms.","zh":"受歡迎電影可以透過串流平台在世界各地觀看。"},{"en":"If an art form is shown throughout the world, people from very different cultures may encounter it.","zh":"如果一種藝術形式在世界各地展出，來自非常不同文化的人都可能接觸到它。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses wide international reach.","zh":"這個片語強調廣泛國際範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"not just in","meaning":"不只在……","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal art is recognised not just in Australia but also overseas.","zh":"澳洲原住民藝術不只在澳洲得到認可，也在海外得到認可。"},{"en":"Not just in means something is true in one place, and also in other places.","zh":"not just in 指某事不只在一個地方成立，也在其他地方成立。"},{"en":"A student’s writing may improve not just in grammar but also in organisation.","zh":"學生寫作不只在文法上進步，也在組織上進步。"},{"en":"If a problem appears not just in one school but across the city, officials may need a wider policy.","zh":"如果問題不只在一所學校出現，而是在全城出現，官員可能需要更廣泛政策。"},{"en":"This phrase expands the range beyond the first place or area mentioned.","zh":"這個片語把範圍擴展到最初提到的地方或範疇以外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be fully recognised","meaning":"得到充分認可","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal art is now fully recognised in Australia.","zh":"澳洲原住民藝術現在在澳洲得到充分認可。"},{"en":"To be fully recognised means to be properly accepted, valued and respected.","zh":"be fully recognised 指被恰當接受、重視和尊重。"},{"en":"A student’s effort may not be fully recognised if teachers only look at exam marks.","zh":"如果老師只看考試分數，學生的努力可能未得到充分認可。"},{"en":"When a culture is fully recognised, its history and artistic achievements are taken seriously.","zh":"當一種文化得到充分認可，其歷史和藝術成就會被認真看待。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete acceptance rather than partial attention.","zh":"這個片語描述完整接納，而不是部分關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"designate space to","meaning":"撥出空間予……","examples":[{"en":"The museum designated a large amount of exhibition space to Aboriginal art.","zh":"博物館撥出大量展覽空間予澳洲原住民藝術。"},{"en":"To designate space to something means to set aside an area for that purpose.","zh":"designate space to something 指為某目的預留一個區域。"},{"en":"A school may designate space to quiet reading so students have a calm place to study.","zh":"學校可能撥出空間予安靜閱讀，讓學生有平靜地方學習。"},{"en":"If a museum designates more space to one culture, it shows that the culture is considered important.","zh":"如果博物館為某文化撥出更多空間，顯示該文化被視為重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving physical room and institutional attention to something.","zh":"這個片語描述給予某事實體空間和制度上的重視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"exhibition space","meaning":"展覽空間","examples":[{"en":"The National Museum of Australia devoted substantial exhibition space to Aboriginal works.","zh":"澳洲國家博物館撥出大量展覽空間予原住民作品。"},{"en":"Exhibition space is the area in a museum or gallery used to display objects or artworks.","zh":"exhibition space 是博物館或畫廊中用來展示物件或藝術品的地方。"},{"en":"A small gallery may need more exhibition space if it receives many new paintings.","zh":"如果小畫廊收到許多新畫作，它可能需要更多展覽空間。"},{"en":"If exhibition space is limited, curators must decide which works deserve display.","zh":"如果展覽空間有限，策展人必須決定哪些作品值得展出。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the physical area used for public display.","zh":"這個片語指用作公開展示的實體空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"works by Aboriginal artists","meaning":"澳洲原住民藝術家的作品","examples":[{"en":"The museum displays many works by Aboriginal artists.","zh":"博物館展示許多澳洲原住民藝術家的作品。"},{"en":"Works by Aboriginal artists are paintings, sculptures or other artworks created by Indigenous Australian artists.","zh":"works by Aboriginal artists 是由澳洲原住民藝術家創作的畫作、雕塑或其他藝術品。"},{"en":"A teacher may show students works by Aboriginal artists to discuss culture and storytelling.","zh":"老師可能向學生展示澳洲原住民藝術家的作品，以討論文化和敘事。"},{"en":"If these works are displayed respectfully, viewers may learn about history as well as beauty.","zh":"如果這些作品得到尊重地展示，觀眾不只學到美感，也能了解歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the creators of the artworks.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於藝術品的創作者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be exhibited at","meaning":"在……展出","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal art is being exhibited at museums in Europe.","zh":"澳洲原住民藝術正在歐洲博物館展出。"},{"en":"To be exhibited at a place means to be shown publicly there.","zh":"be exhibited at a place 指在某地公開展示。"},{"en":"A student’s painting may be exhibited at the school open day.","zh":"學生畫作可能在學校開放日展出。"},{"en":"If artwork is exhibited at a major museum, it can reach a much wider audience.","zh":"如果藝術品在大型博物館展出，它可以接觸更廣泛觀眾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public display in a particular venue.","zh":"這個片語描述在特定場地公開展示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be devoted to","meaning":"專門展示；致力於","examples":[{"en":"The museum is devoted to the arts and civilisations of several regions.","zh":"該博物館專門展示幾個地區的藝術與文明。"},{"en":"To be devoted to something means to be mainly focused on it or dedicated to it.","zh":"be devoted to something 指主要聚焦於某事或致力於某事。"},{"en":"A library corner may be devoted to children’s books.","zh":"圖書館角落可能專門放置兒童書籍。"},{"en":"If an institution is devoted to a culture, it collects, studies and displays that culture seriously.","zh":"如果機構致力於某文化，它會認真收藏、研究和展示該文化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear main purpose or focus.","zh":"這個片語描述清楚的主要目的或焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"arts and civilisations","meaning":"藝術與文明","examples":[{"en":"The museum presents the arts and civilisations of Africa, Asia, Oceania and the Americas.","zh":"該博物館呈現非洲、亞洲、大洋洲和美洲的藝術與文明。"},{"en":"Arts and civilisations means creative works together with the societies, histories and cultures that produced them.","zh":"arts and civilisations 指創作作品，以及產生這些作品的社會、歷史和文化。"},{"en":"A world history course may compare the arts and civilisations of ancient Egypt and China.","zh":"世界歷史課可能比較古埃及和中國的藝術與文明。"},{"en":"If students study art without civilisation, they may miss the beliefs and social life behind it.","zh":"如果學生只學藝術而不學文明，可能忽略背後信仰和社會生活。"},{"en":"This phrase connects artistic objects with wider human cultures.","zh":"這個片語把藝術物件與更廣泛的人類文化連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"commission frescoes","meaning":"委託創作濕壁畫","examples":[{"en":"The museum planned to commission frescoes from Australian artists.","zh":"該博物館計劃委託澳洲藝術家創作濕壁畫。"},{"en":"To commission frescoes means to officially ask and pay artists to create wall paintings on wet plaster.","zh":"commission frescoes 指正式邀請並付費請藝術家在濕灰泥上創作壁畫。"},{"en":"A hotel may commission murals from local artists to decorate its lobby.","zh":"酒店可能委託本地藝術家創作壁畫來裝飾大堂。"},{"en":"If a museum commissions new works, it helps artists create pieces for a specific space.","zh":"如果博物館委託新作品，它能幫助藝術家為特定空間創作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordering original artwork for an institution or building.","zh":"這個片語描述為機構或建築訂製原創藝術品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"artistic movement","meaning":"藝術運動","examples":[{"en":"The Aboriginal artistic movement began about thirty years before the article was written.","zh":"澳洲原住民藝術運動大約在文章寫成前三十年開始。"},{"en":"An artistic movement is a period when artists share new styles, ideas or purposes.","zh":"artistic movement 是藝術家共享新風格、想法或目的的一段時期。"},{"en":"A group of young painters may create an artistic movement if their work changes how people see art.","zh":"如果一群年輕畫家改變人們看待藝術的方式，他們可能創造一場藝術運動。"},{"en":"When an artistic movement grows, museums, collectors and critics may begin to pay attention.","zh":"當藝術運動發展，博物館、收藏家和評論家可能開始關注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a wider cultural development, not just one artist.","zh":"這個片語描述更廣泛的文化發展，而不只是單一藝術家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have roots in","meaning":"源於……","examples":[{"en":"The movement has roots in ancient cultural traditions.","zh":"這場運動源於古老文化傳統。"},{"en":"To have roots in something means to come from it or be deeply connected with it.","zh":"have roots in something 指源自某事或與某事有深層連繫。"},{"en":"A family recipe may have roots in a grandmother’s village cooking.","zh":"家庭食譜可能源於祖母村莊的烹調方式。"},{"en":"If an art form has roots in ritual, its symbols may carry spiritual meaning.","zh":"如果藝術形式源於儀式，其符號可能帶有精神意義。"},{"en":"This phrase explains deep origin and connection.","zh":"這個片語解釋深層起源和連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"time immemorial","meaning":"遠古時代；遠古以來","examples":[{"en":"The cultural roots of Aboriginal painting go back to time immemorial.","zh":"澳洲原住民繪畫的文化根源可追溯至遠古時代。"},{"en":"Time immemorial means a time so ancient that no one can remember its beginning.","zh":"time immemorial 指古老到沒有人記得其開始的時代。"},{"en":"Some village customs have been practised since time immemorial.","zh":"一些村莊習俗自遠古以來便一直實踐。"},{"en":"If a tradition goes back to time immemorial, it feels older than written records.","zh":"如果傳統可追溯至遠古，它會感覺比文字記錄更古老。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses extreme antiquity.","zh":"這個片語強調極度古老。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"涉及；指向","examples":[{"en":"Many Aboriginal works refer to the Dreaming.","zh":"許多澳洲原住民作品涉及「夢創時代」。"},{"en":"To refer to something means to mention it, point to it or connect with it indirectly.","zh":"refer to something 指提及、指向或間接連接某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may refer to a previous lesson when explaining a new grammar point.","zh":"老師解釋新文法點時，可能提到上一課。"},{"en":"If a painting refers to a sacred story, viewers may need cultural knowledge to understand it.","zh":"如果畫作指向神聖故事，觀眾可能需要文化知識才能理解。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe direct mention or symbolic connection.","zh":"這個片語可以描述直接提及或象徵性連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"founding myth","meaning":"文化起源神話","examples":[{"en":"The Dreaming is the founding myth of Aboriginal culture.","zh":"「夢創時代」是澳洲原住民文化的起源神話。"},{"en":"A founding myth is a traditional story that explains the origin and meaning of a people, place or culture.","zh":"founding myth 是解釋一個民族、地方或文化起源與意義的傳統故事。"},{"en":"Many cultures have founding myths about ancestors, gods or the beginning of the world.","zh":"許多文化都有關於祖先、神明或世界開始的起源神話。"},{"en":"If a community shares a founding myth, it can strengthen identity and belonging.","zh":"如果社群共享起源神話，它可以強化身份和歸屬感。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an origin story with cultural power.","zh":"這個片語指具有文化力量的起源故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Aboriginal culture","meaning":"澳洲原住民文化","examples":[{"en":"The Dreaming is central to Aboriginal culture.","zh":"「夢創時代」是澳洲原住民文化的核心。"},{"en":"Aboriginal culture includes the beliefs, stories, art, languages, laws and relationships to land of Indigenous Australians.","zh":"Aboriginal culture 包括澳洲原住民的信仰、故事、藝術、語言、法律和與土地的關係。"},{"en":"Schools may teach Aboriginal culture through art, oral history and respectful community visits.","zh":"學校可能透過藝術、口述歷史和尊重社群的探訪教授澳洲原住民文化。"},{"en":"If Aboriginal culture is separated from land, much of its meaning may be lost.","zh":"如果澳洲原住民文化與土地分離，其許多意義可能會流失。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a deep and diverse cultural tradition.","zh":"這個片語指深厚而多元的文化傳統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the Dreaming","meaning":"「夢創時代」；原住民創世信仰","examples":[{"en":"The Dreaming connects Aboriginal history, belief, land and identity.","zh":"「夢創時代」連接澳洲原住民的歷史、信仰、土地和身份。"},{"en":"The Dreaming is a central Aboriginal belief system about creation, ancestors, law, land and continuing spiritual reality.","zh":"the Dreaming 是澳洲原住民關於創世、祖先、法律、土地和持續精神現實的核心信仰系統。"},{"en":"An Aboriginal painting may depict a Dreaming story that belongs to a particular community.","zh":"澳洲原住民畫作可能描繪屬於某個特定社群的「夢創時代」故事。"},{"en":"If people do not understand the Dreaming, they may see only patterns and miss the sacred meaning.","zh":"如果人們不理解「夢創時代」，可能只看見圖案，而錯過神聖意義。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a living spiritual framework, not simply a dream.","zh":"這個片語指活生生的精神框架，而不只是夢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"internal geography","meaning":"內在地理景觀","examples":[{"en":"The paintings express an internal geography connected with memory and land.","zh":"這些畫作表達與記憶和土地相連的內在地理景觀。"},{"en":"Internal geography means a mental or spiritual map shaped by memory, identity and place.","zh":"internal geography 指由記憶、身份和地方塑造的心理或精神地圖。"},{"en":"A migrant may carry an internal geography of streets, smells and voices from home.","zh":"移民可能帶着由家鄉街道、氣味和聲音組成的內在地理景觀。"},{"en":"If art shows internal geography, it may represent feelings about land rather than a simple map.","zh":"如果藝術展示內在地理，它可能代表對土地的感受，而不是簡單地圖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes geography experienced inwardly.","zh":"這個片語描述被內在經驗到的地理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be rendered with","meaning":"以……呈現","examples":[{"en":"This spiritual geography is rendered with brushes and colours.","zh":"這種精神地理以畫筆和色彩呈現。"},{"en":"To be rendered with something means to be represented or expressed using that material or method.","zh":"be rendered with something 指用某材料或方法代表或表達某事。"},{"en":"A child’s memory of home may be rendered with simple drawings and bright colours.","zh":"孩子對家的記憶可能以簡單圖畫和鮮艷色彩呈現。"},{"en":"If a story is rendered with music, listeners feel it through sound rather than words alone.","zh":"如果故事以音樂呈現，聽眾會透過聲音而不只是文字感受它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the medium used to express an idea.","zh":"這個片語描述用來表達想法的媒介。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an expression of","meaning":"……的表達","examples":[{"en":"The artwork is also an expression of Aboriginal people’s connection to their land.","zh":"這件藝術品也是澳洲原住民與其土地連繫的表達。"},{"en":"An expression of something is a way of showing a feeling, belief or relationship.","zh":"expression of something 是展示感受、信念或關係的方式。"},{"en":"A thank-you card can be an expression of gratitude.","zh":"感謝卡可以是感激之情的表達。"},{"en":"If a painting is an expression of identity, it may carry personal and communal meaning.","zh":"如果畫作是身份的表達，它可能帶有個人和社群意義。"},{"en":"This phrase links an object or action with what it reveals.","zh":"這個片語把物件或行動與其揭示的內容連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a long quest to regain","meaning":"尋回……的漫長努力","examples":[{"en":"The paintings reflect a long quest to regain land taken from Aboriginal communities.","zh":"這些畫作反映尋回被奪去原住民社群土地的漫長努力。"},{"en":"A long quest to regain something is a prolonged effort to recover what was lost or taken.","zh":"long quest to regain something 指長期努力取回失去或被奪去的東西。"},{"en":"A family may begin a long quest to regain property after an unfair legal decision.","zh":"家庭在不公平法律裁決後，可能開始尋回財產的漫長努力。"},{"en":"If land has been taken for generations, regaining it may require law, activism and cultural memory.","zh":"如果土地被奪去幾代人，尋回它可能需要法律、行動和文化記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests difficulty, persistence and historical loss.","zh":"這個片語暗示困難、堅持和歷史失落。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stolen from","meaning":"從……奪去","examples":[{"en":"The land was stolen from Aboriginal people after European settlement began.","zh":"歐洲人開始定居後，土地從澳洲原住民手中被奪去。"},{"en":"To be stolen from someone means to be taken away from them unfairly or unlawfully.","zh":"be stolen from someone 指某物被不公平或非法地從某人手中拿走。"},{"en":"A phone stolen from a student may contain photos, contacts and schoolwork.","zh":"從學生手中偷去的電話可能含有照片、聯絡人和功課。"},{"en":"If land is stolen from a community, the loss affects homes, identity and future generations.","zh":"如果土地從社群手中被奪去，損失會影響家園、身份和後代。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights injustice and loss.","zh":"這個片語突出不公和失去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"when Europeans arrived","meaning":"當歐洲人到來時","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal communities suffered severe disruption when Europeans arrived.","zh":"當歐洲人到來時，澳洲原住民社群遭受嚴重破壞。"},{"en":"When Europeans arrived refers to the period when European settlers first came and began changing Aboriginal life.","zh":"when Europeans arrived 指歐洲殖民者最初到來並開始改變原住民生活的時期。"},{"en":"When new settlers arrive in a place, they may bring new laws, diseases and land claims.","zh":"當新定居者到達某地時，他們可能帶來新法律、疾病和土地主張。"},{"en":"If arrival leads to colonisation, local communities may lose land and control.","zh":"如果到來導致殖民，本地社群可能失去土地和控制權。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a historical turning point.","zh":"這個片語標示歷史轉折點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"painting is nothing without history","meaning":"繪畫離不開歷史","examples":[{"en":"Michael Nelson Tjakamarra said that painting is nothing without history.","zh":"Michael Nelson Tjakamarra 說，繪畫離不開歷史。"},{"en":"Painting is nothing without history means art loses meaning if its cultural and historical background is ignored.","zh":"painting is nothing without history 指如果忽視文化和歷史背景，藝術就會失去意義。"},{"en":"A family photograph means more when people know the story behind it.","zh":"當人們知道家庭照片背後的故事，它就更有意義。"},{"en":"If viewers ignore history, they may treat sacred paintings as decoration only.","zh":"如果觀眾忽視歷史，可能只把神聖畫作當作裝飾。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that art and memory belong together.","zh":"這個片語強調藝術與記憶不可分割。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fewer than","meaning":"少於","examples":[{"en":"There are fewer than 400,000 Aboriginal people mentioned in the passage.","zh":"文章提到澳洲原住民人數少於四十萬。"},{"en":"Fewer than means less than a particular number, and it is used with countable things.","zh":"fewer than 指少於某個數字，並用於可數事物。"},{"en":"Fewer than ten students joined the optional writing workshop.","zh":"少於十名學生參加選修寫作工作坊。"},{"en":"If fewer than half the group agree, the proposal may not pass.","zh":"如果少於一半小組成員同意，建議可能不會通過。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a number below a stated limit.","zh":"這個片語表示低於某個界限的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be vastly outnumbered by","meaning":"人數遠少於……","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal people were vastly outnumbered by Australia’s immigrant population.","zh":"澳洲原住民人數遠少於澳洲移民人口。"},{"en":"To be vastly outnumbered by a group means to be far fewer in number than that group.","zh":"be vastly outnumbered by a group 指數量遠少於另一群體。"},{"en":"In a debate, one speaker may feel outnumbered if everyone else supports the opposite view.","zh":"在辯論中，如果其他人都支持相反觀點，一名發言者可能感到寡不敵眾。"},{"en":"If a minority is vastly outnumbered, its voice may be ignored unless protected.","zh":"如果少數群體人數遠少於他人，其聲音可能被忽視，除非受到保護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very large difference in numbers.","zh":"這個片語描述數量上的巨大差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"original inhabitants","meaning":"原住民；最早居民","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal Australians are the original inhabitants of the continent.","zh":"澳洲原住民是該大陸的原住民。"},{"en":"Original inhabitants are the first known people who lived in a place.","zh":"original inhabitants 是已知最早居住在某地的人。"},{"en":"A history lesson may discuss the original inhabitants before later settlers arrived.","zh":"歷史課可能討論後來定居者到來前的最早居民。"},{"en":"If original inhabitants lose land, the damage can affect culture for generations.","zh":"如果原住民失去土地，傷害可以影響文化幾代人。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the earliest resident people of a place.","zh":"這個片語指某地最早居住的人群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"for tens of thousands of years","meaning":"數以萬年來","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal people have lived in Australia for tens of thousands of years.","zh":"澳洲原住民數以萬年來一直生活在澳洲。"},{"en":"For tens of thousands of years means for an extremely long period, at least many ten-thousand-year spans.","zh":"for tens of thousands of years 指極長時間，至少許多個一萬年。"},{"en":"Some landscapes have been shaped by human use for tens of thousands of years.","zh":"一些景觀數以萬年來一直受人類使用塑造。"},{"en":"If a people have lived somewhere for so long, their connection to land may be very deep.","zh":"如果一個民族在某地生活如此之久，他們與土地的連繫可能非常深。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises ancient and continuous presence.","zh":"這個片語強調古老而持續的存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be badly mistreated by","meaning":"受到……嚴重虐待","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal communities were badly mistreated by European settlers.","zh":"澳洲原住民社群受到歐洲殖民者嚴重虐待。"},{"en":"To be badly mistreated by someone means to be treated with serious cruelty, unfairness or neglect.","zh":"be badly mistreated by someone 指受到某人嚴重殘酷、不公平或忽視的對待。"},{"en":"Workers may be badly mistreated if they are underpaid and forced to live in unsafe housing.","zh":"如果工人被低薪並被迫住在不安全住處，他們可能受到嚴重虐待。"},{"en":"If a group is badly mistreated for generations, trust in authorities may be damaged.","zh":"如果一個群體幾代人受到嚴重虐待，對當局的信任可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severe injustice in treatment.","zh":"這個片語描述待遇上的嚴重不公。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"European settlers","meaning":"歐洲殖民者","examples":[{"en":"European settlers imposed damaging policies on Aboriginal communities.","zh":"歐洲殖民者對澳洲原住民社群施加破壞性政策。"},{"en":"European settlers were people from Europe who moved to another land and established homes, farms or colonies there.","zh":"European settlers 是從歐洲遷往另一片土地，並在那裡建立家園、農場或殖民地的人。"},{"en":"Settlers may bring new laws and ownership systems that affect existing communities.","zh":"殖民者可能帶來影響既有社群的新法律和所有權制度。"},{"en":"If settlers take land without consent, conflict and displacement may follow.","zh":"如果殖民者未經同意奪取土地，衝突和遷離可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to Europeans who settled in colonised regions.","zh":"這個片語指在被殖民地區定居的歐洲人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be driven onto","meaning":"被迫遷到……","examples":[{"en":"Many Aboriginal communities were driven onto barren land.","zh":"許多澳洲原住民社群被迫遷到貧瘠土地。"},{"en":"To be driven onto land means to be forced to move there, usually against one’s will.","zh":"be driven onto land 指通常違反意願地被迫遷往某土地。"},{"en":"Poor families may be driven onto cheaper land when city rents rise too quickly.","zh":"當城市租金上升太快，貧困家庭可能被迫遷到較便宜地區。"},{"en":"If people are driven onto poor land, survival becomes harder and traditional life may be disrupted.","zh":"如果人們被迫遷到貧瘠土地，生存會更困難，傳統生活也可能被打亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes forced relocation.","zh":"這個片語描述強迫遷移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"barren land","meaning":"貧瘠土地","examples":[{"en":"Some communities were forced to survive on barren land.","zh":"一些社群被迫在貧瘠土地上生存。"},{"en":"Barren land is land where little grows and farming or living is difficult.","zh":"barren land 是幾乎沒有植物生長、耕作或生活困難的土地。"},{"en":"A village on barren land may struggle to find enough water and food.","zh":"位於貧瘠土地上的村莊可能難以找到足夠水和食物。"},{"en":"If people are moved to barren land, their health and livelihood may suffer.","zh":"如果人們被遷到貧瘠土地，其健康和生計可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes poor, unproductive land.","zh":"這個片語描述貧乏、缺乏生產力的土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be crammed into","meaning":"被擠進……","examples":[{"en":"Many Aboriginal people were crammed into overcrowded urban slums.","zh":"許多澳洲原住民被擠進擁擠的城市貧民區。"},{"en":"To be crammed into a place means to be forced into a space that is too small or crowded.","zh":"be crammed into a place 指被迫進入過小或過度擁擠的空間。"},{"en":"Students may feel uncomfortable if too many chairs are crammed into one classroom.","zh":"如果太多椅子被擠進一間課室，學生可能感到不舒服。"},{"en":"If families are crammed into poor housing, disease and stress may spread more easily.","zh":"如果家庭被擠進惡劣住房，疾病和壓力可能更易蔓延。"},{"en":"This phrase describes overcrowded and uncomfortable living conditions.","zh":"這個片語描述擁擠而不舒適的生活條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"urban slums","meaning":"城市貧民區","examples":[{"en":"Some displaced Aboriginal people lived in urban slums.","zh":"一些被迫離開家園的澳洲原住民住在城市貧民區。"},{"en":"Urban slums are poor, overcrowded areas in cities with bad housing and limited services.","zh":"urban slums 是城市中貧困、擁擠、住房惡劣且服務有限的地區。"},{"en":"Families in urban slums may lack clean water, safe buildings and public facilities.","zh":"城市貧民區的家庭可能缺乏潔淨食水、安全建築和公共設施。"},{"en":"If people are pushed into urban slums, poverty can become harder to escape.","zh":"如果人們被推入城市貧民區，貧窮可能更難逃離。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severely disadvantaged city neighbourhoods.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重弱勢的城市社區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on the outskirts of","meaning":"在……的外圍","examples":[{"en":"Many disadvantaged communities were located on the outskirts of cities.","zh":"許多弱勢社群位於城市外圍。"},{"en":"On the outskirts of a place means near the outer edge of a town or city.","zh":"on the outskirts of a place 指位於城鎮或城市外邊緣附近。"},{"en":"A new housing estate may be built on the outskirts of the city where land is cheaper.","zh":"新屋苑可能建在城市外圍，因為土地較便宜。"},{"en":"If people live on the outskirts, they may have longer journeys to schools, hospitals and jobs.","zh":"如果人們住在外圍地區，前往學校、醫院和工作地點可能需時更長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a location away from the city centre.","zh":"這個片語描述遠離市中心的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be subjected to","meaning":"遭受；被迫接受","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal people were subjected to a policy of forced assimilation.","zh":"澳洲原住民遭受強制同化政策。"},{"en":"To be subjected to something means to be made to experience something unpleasant, unfair or controlling.","zh":"be subjected to something 指被迫經歷令人不快、不公平或控制性的事。"},{"en":"Workers should not be subjected to unsafe conditions or abusive managers.","zh":"工人不應遭受不安全環境或辱罵式管理。"},{"en":"If children are subjected to harsh policies, the effects can last into adulthood.","zh":"如果兒童被迫接受嚴苛政策，影響可能延續至成年。"},{"en":"This phrase usually describes suffering under a system or treatment.","zh":"這個片語通常描述在制度或待遇下受苦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a policy of assimilation","meaning":"同化政策","examples":[{"en":"The government imposed a policy of assimilation on Aboriginal communities.","zh":"政府對澳洲原住民社群施加同化政策。"},{"en":"A policy of assimilation is an official attempt to make a minority group adopt the culture of the dominant group.","zh":"policy of assimilation 是官方嘗試令少數群體採納主流群體文化的政策。"},{"en":"A school may follow assimilation if it punishes children for speaking their home language.","zh":"如果學校懲罰孩子說家庭語言，它可能是在實行同化。"},{"en":"If assimilation is forced, people may lose language, family links and cultural confidence.","zh":"如果同化是強制的，人們可能失去語言、家庭連繫和文化信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cultural absorption imposed by authority.","zh":"這個片語描述由權力施加的文化吸收。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"remove children from their families","meaning":"把兒童帶離其家庭","examples":[{"en":"Children were removed from their families under assimilation policies.","zh":"在同化政策下，兒童被帶離其家庭。"},{"en":"To remove children from their families means to take them away from parents or relatives, often by official force.","zh":"remove children from their families 指把孩子從父母或親人身邊帶走，常由官方強制執行。"},{"en":"Social workers may remove children from families only when there is serious danger.","zh":"社工通常只在有嚴重危險時才會把兒童帶離家庭。"},{"en":"If children are removed from families for cultural reasons, the trauma can affect generations.","zh":"如果兒童因文化原因被帶離家庭，創傷可以影響幾代人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a severe break in family life.","zh":"這個片語描述家庭生活中的嚴重斷裂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"assimilate someone into","meaning":"把某人同化融入……","examples":[{"en":"Officials attempted to assimilate Aboriginal children into European society.","zh":"官員試圖把澳洲原住民兒童同化融入歐洲社會。"},{"en":"To assimilate someone into a society means to make them adopt that society’s language, customs and values.","zh":"assimilate someone into a society 指令某人採納該社會的語言、習俗和價值觀。"},{"en":"New students may be gently helped to adapt, but they should not be forced to abandon their identity.","zh":"新學生可以被溫和地幫助適應，但不應被迫放棄身份。"},{"en":"If assimilation is forced, cultural loss and emotional harm may result.","zh":"如果同化是強制的，可能造成文化流失和情感傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pushing someone into another cultural system.","zh":"這個片語描述把某人推入另一文化系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"European society","meaning":"歐洲社會","examples":[{"en":"The policy was intended to absorb Aboriginal children into European society.","zh":"該政策旨在把澳洲原住民兒童吸收進歐洲社會。"},{"en":"European society means the social world shaped by European culture, law, language and institutions.","zh":"European society 指由歐洲文化、法律、語言和制度塑造的社會世界。"},{"en":"Colonial schools often tried to teach Indigenous children European social rules.","zh":"殖民學校常試圖教原住民兒童歐洲社會規則。"},{"en":"If one society dominates another, minority children may be pressured to copy it.","zh":"如果一個社會支配另一個社會，少數族裔兒童可能被迫模仿它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to European cultural and social structures.","zh":"這個片語指歐洲文化和社會結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"forcibly relocate","meaning":"強行遷移","examples":[{"en":"Authorities forcibly relocated nomadic Aboriginal people into permanent settlements.","zh":"當局強行把遊牧澳洲原住民遷移到永久定居點。"},{"en":"To forcibly relocate people means to move them to another place against their will.","zh":"forcibly relocate people 指違反人們意願把他們遷往另一地方。"},{"en":"Families may be forcibly relocated when land is taken for a large project without fair consent.","zh":"當土地在沒有公平同意下被大型項目徵用，家庭可能被強行遷移。"},{"en":"If people are forcibly relocated, they may lose jobs, community ties and access to sacred places.","zh":"如果人們被強行遷移，他們可能失去工作、社群連繫和進入聖地的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement imposed by power.","zh":"這個片語描述由權力施加的遷移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"nomadic communities","meaning":"遊牧社群","examples":[{"en":"Some Aboriginal communities traditionally followed a nomadic way of life.","zh":"一些澳洲原住民社群傳統上遵循遊牧生活方式。"},{"en":"Nomadic communities are groups that move from place to place rather than living permanently in one location.","zh":"nomadic communities 是從一地移到另一地，而不是永久居於一處的群體。"},{"en":"Nomadic herders may move with their animals to find water and grass.","zh":"遊牧牧民可能與牲畜一起遷移，以尋找水和草。"},{"en":"If nomadic communities are forced to settle, their traditional skills and routes may be disrupted.","zh":"如果遊牧社群被迫定居，其傳統技能和路線可能被打亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mobile communities connected to changing landscapes.","zh":"這個片語描述與變動景觀相連的流動社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"permanent settlements","meaning":"永久定居點","examples":[{"en":"Nomadic people were forced into permanent settlements.","zh":"遊牧民族被迫進入永久定居點。"},{"en":"Permanent settlements are fixed places where people are expected to live continuously.","zh":"permanent settlements 是人們被預期持續居住的固定地方。"},{"en":"A government may build permanent settlements after a natural disaster destroys villages.","zh":"天災摧毀村莊後，政府可能建造永久定居點。"},{"en":"If mobile communities are placed in permanent settlements, their relationship with land may change.","zh":"如果流動社群被安置在永久定居點，他們與土地的關係可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts fixed residence with nomadic movement.","zh":"這個片語把固定居住與遊牧流動作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in one such community","meaning":"在其中一個這類社區","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal painting developed significantly in one such community.","zh":"澳洲原住民繪畫在其中一個這類社區中有重大發展。"},{"en":"In one such community means in one community of the type just described.","zh":"in one such community 指在剛剛描述的那類社群中的其中一個。"},{"en":"Several schools tried a new reading scheme, and in one such school, results improved quickly.","zh":"幾所學校嘗試新閱讀計劃，而在其中一所這類學校，成績很快改善。"},{"en":"If a practice begins in one such community, it may later spread to others.","zh":"如果做法始於其中一個這類社群，它日後可能傳到其他社群。"},{"en":"This phrase links a specific example to a previously mentioned category.","zh":"這個片語把具體例子與先前提到的類別連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the central desert","meaning":"中部沙漠地區","examples":[{"en":"Papunya is situated in Australia’s central desert.","zh":"Papunya 位於澳洲中部沙漠地區。"},{"en":"The central desert is the dry inland desert region near the centre of Australia.","zh":"central desert 是澳洲中部附近乾旱的內陸沙漠區域。"},{"en":"Communities in the central desert may face long distances, heat and limited water.","zh":"中部沙漠地區的社群可能面對長距離、高溫和有限水源。"},{"en":"If an art movement begins in the central desert, its imagery may be closely tied to land and survival.","zh":"如果藝術運動始於中部沙漠，其圖像可能與土地和生存密切相關。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a particular harsh inland landscape.","zh":"這個片語指特定的嚴酷內陸景觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"come into its own","meaning":"開始充分展現價值；逐漸成熟","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal painting first came into its own at Papunya.","zh":"澳洲原住民繪畫最早在 Papunya 開始充分展現價值。"},{"en":"To come into its own means to begin showing its full value, strength or importance.","zh":"come into its own 指開始展現完整價值、力量或重要性。"},{"en":"A quiet student may come into their own during a drama performance.","zh":"安靜學生可能在戲劇表演中開始展現實力。"},{"en":"When artists receive proper materials and support, their tradition may come into its own.","zh":"當藝術家獲得合適材料和支持，其傳統可能逐漸成熟。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a moment of maturity or full expression.","zh":"這個片語描述成熟或充分表達的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"schoolteacher","meaning":"學校教師","examples":[{"en":"Geoffrey Bardon was a schoolteacher working in Papunya.","zh":"Geoffrey Bardon 是在 Papunya 工作的學校教師。"},{"en":"A schoolteacher is a person whose job is to teach students in a school.","zh":"schoolteacher 是在學校教學生的人。"},{"en":"A schoolteacher may notice talent in children or community members that others overlook.","zh":"學校教師可能注意到兒童或社區成員被他人忽略的才能。"},{"en":"If a teacher supports local culture, school projects can become more meaningful.","zh":"如果老師支持本地文化，學校項目可以變得更有意義。"},{"en":"This word refers to a teacher working in a school setting.","zh":"這個詞指在學校環境工作的教師。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"suggest that someone should","meaning":"建議某人應該……","examples":[{"en":"Bardon suggested that the artists should decorate the school walls.","zh":"Bardon 建議藝術家應該裝飾學校牆壁。"},{"en":"To suggest that someone should do something means to propose an action as a good idea.","zh":"suggest that someone should do something 指提出某行動是好主意。"},{"en":"A teacher may suggest that students should read the question twice before answering.","zh":"老師可能建議學生回答前應該讀題兩次。"},{"en":"If someone suggests a project, others can decide whether to accept the idea.","zh":"如果有人建議一個項目，其他人可以決定是否接受該想法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces advice or a proposal.","zh":"這個片語引入建議或提議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"decorate the school walls","meaning":"裝飾學校牆壁","examples":[{"en":"The artists were invited to decorate the school walls with traditional designs.","zh":"藝術家獲邀以傳統設計裝飾學校牆壁。"},{"en":"To decorate the school walls means to add images, colours or patterns to make the walls meaningful or attractive.","zh":"decorate the school walls 指在牆上加入圖像、顏色或圖案，使牆壁有意義或更吸引。"},{"en":"Students may decorate classroom walls with posters about books they have read.","zh":"學生可能用關於讀過書本的海報裝飾課室牆壁。"},{"en":"If walls are decorated with cultural designs, they can teach history as well as brighten the room.","zh":"如果牆壁以文化圖案裝飾，它們既能教授歷史，也能令房間更明亮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes turning a plain school space into a visual learning space.","zh":"這個片語描述把普通學校空間變成視覺學習空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ritual motifs","meaning":"儀式圖案","examples":[{"en":"The artists painted ritual motifs on the walls.","zh":"藝術家在牆上畫上儀式圖案。"},{"en":"Ritual motifs are repeated patterns or symbols connected with ceremonies or sacred practices.","zh":"ritual motifs 是與儀式或神聖做法相關的重複圖案或符號。"},{"en":"A temple cloth may contain ritual motifs that worshippers recognise.","zh":"廟宇布料可能含有信眾認得的儀式圖案。"},{"en":"If an artist uses ritual motifs, the design may carry meanings beyond decoration.","zh":"如果藝術家使用儀式圖案，設計可能帶有超越裝飾的意義。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to symbolic patterns used in religious or ceremonial contexts.","zh":"這個片語指用於宗教或儀式背景的象徵圖案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pass something on to","meaning":"把……傳承給","examples":[{"en":"The project helped pass traditional stories on to younger people.","zh":"該項目幫助把傳統故事傳承給年輕人。"},{"en":"To pass something on to someone means to give knowledge, stories, skills or objects to another person or generation.","zh":"pass something on to someone 指把知識、故事、技能或物件交給另一人或下一代。"},{"en":"Grandparents may pass family recipes on to their grandchildren.","zh":"祖父母可能把家庭食譜傳承給孫兒女。"},{"en":"If elders pass stories on to young people, cultural memory can survive.","zh":"如果長者把故事傳給年輕人，文化記憶就能延續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transmission across people or generations.","zh":"這個片語描述人與人或世代之間的傳遞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the younger generation","meaning":"年輕一代","examples":[{"en":"The paintings introduced traditional myths to the younger generation.","zh":"這些畫作把傳統神話介紹給年輕一代。"},{"en":"The younger generation means young people in a community compared with older adults.","zh":"younger generation 指社群中相對於成年人和長者的年輕人。"},{"en":"Schools help the younger generation understand local history and values.","zh":"學校幫助年輕一代理解本地歷史和價值。"},{"en":"If the younger generation does not learn traditional stories, those stories may fade.","zh":"如果年輕一代沒有學習傳統故事，那些故事可能淡忘。"},{"en":"This phrase describes those who will inherit the future of a culture.","zh":"這個片語描述將承繼文化未來的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"start to fade from","meaning":"開始從……淡忘","examples":[{"en":"Some traditional myths were starting to fade from collective memory.","zh":"一些傳統神話開始從集體記憶中淡忘。"},{"en":"To start to fade from memory means to begin being forgotten gradually.","zh":"start to fade from memory 指開始逐漸被遺忘。"},{"en":"Old playground games may start to fade from children’s lives when everyone uses phones.","zh":"當每個人都使用手機，舊式操場遊戲可能開始從孩子生活中淡出。"},{"en":"If stories are not told regularly, they may fade from a community’s memory.","zh":"如果故事不被定期講述，它們可能從社群記憶中淡忘。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow disappearance from remembrance.","zh":"這個片語描述從記憶中慢慢消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"collective memory","meaning":"集體記憶","examples":[{"en":"The artists sought to preserve stories in their community’s collective memory.","zh":"藝術家試圖保存其社群集體記憶中的故事。"},{"en":"Collective memory is the shared memory of a group, including stories, events and traditions remembered together.","zh":"collective memory 是一個群體共同記住的記憶，包括故事、事件和傳統。"},{"en":"A city’s collective memory may include old disasters, festivals and local heroes.","zh":"城市的集體記憶可能包括舊災難、節日和本地英雄。"},{"en":"If collective memory is weakened, a community may lose part of its identity.","zh":"如果集體記憶被削弱，社群可能失去部分身份。"},{"en":"This phrase describes memory held by a group rather than one person.","zh":"這個片語描述由群體而非個人持有的記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"surfaces to paint on","meaning":"作畫表面","examples":[{"en":"Bardon provided brushes, colours and surfaces to paint on.","zh":"Bardon 提供畫筆、顏料和作畫表面。"},{"en":"Surfaces to paint on are materials or places where artists can apply paint.","zh":"surfaces to paint on 是藝術家可以上色的材料或地方。"},{"en":"Students need paper, canvas or boards as surfaces to paint on during art class.","zh":"學生在美術課需要紙張、畫布或木板作為作畫表面。"},{"en":"If artists receive suitable surfaces, their work can last longer and be displayed more easily.","zh":"如果藝術家得到合適作畫表面，作品可以保存更久並更容易展示。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the physical base for painting.","zh":"這個片語指繪畫的實體基底。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cardboard and canvas","meaning":"硬卡紙與畫布","examples":[{"en":"The artists were given cardboard and canvas to work on.","zh":"藝術家獲得硬卡紙和畫布作畫。"},{"en":"Cardboard and canvas are materials that can be used as surfaces for painting.","zh":"cardboard and canvas 是可用作繪畫表面的材料。"},{"en":"Children may practise on cardboard before using more expensive canvas.","zh":"孩子可能先在硬卡紙上練習，再使用較昂貴畫布。"},{"en":"If traditional designs move onto canvas, they can be transported, sold and displayed more easily.","zh":"如果傳統設計轉移到畫布上，就更容易運送、出售和展示。"},{"en":"This phrase names simple materials used for creating portable artworks.","zh":"這個片語指出創作可移動畫作的簡單材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be astounded by","meaning":"對……感到非常驚訝","examples":[{"en":"Bardon was astounded by the quality of the results.","zh":"Bardon 對成果的質素感到非常驚訝。"},{"en":"To be astounded by something means to be extremely surprised or impressed by it.","zh":"be astounded by something 指對某事極度驚訝或留下深刻印象。"},{"en":"A teacher may be astounded by a quiet student’s powerful speech.","zh":"老師可能對安靜學生有力的演講感到非常驚訝。"},{"en":"If a simple school project produces outstanding art, people may be shocked by its quality.","zh":"如果簡單學校項目產生出色藝術，人們可能對其質素感到震驚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong surprise, often positive.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈驚訝，通常帶正面意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"come like a bolt from the blue","meaning":"突如其來","examples":[{"en":"The artistic development did not come like a bolt from the blue.","zh":"這種藝術發展並非突如其來。"},{"en":"To come like a bolt from the blue means to happen suddenly and unexpectedly.","zh":"come like a bolt from the blue 指突然且出乎意料地發生。"},{"en":"A surprise scholarship offer may come like a bolt from the blue to a hardworking student.","zh":"意外獲得獎學金對勤奮學生而言可能像突如其來的驚喜。"},{"en":"If an achievement has deep historical roots, it did not appear suddenly from nowhere.","zh":"如果成就有深厚歷史根源，它就不是憑空突然出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shocking sudden event, often contrasted with gradual development.","zh":"這個片語描述令人震驚的突發事件，常與漸進發展作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for thousands of years","meaning":"數千年來","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal people had created ground and rock paintings for thousands of years.","zh":"澳洲原住民數千年來一直創作地面畫和岩畫。"},{"en":"For thousands of years means for a very long period across many centuries.","zh":"for thousands of years 指跨越許多世紀的極長時間。"},{"en":"People have used stories to teach children for thousands of years.","zh":"人類數千年來一直用故事教導孩子。"},{"en":"If a practice lasts for thousands of years, it likely carries deep cultural value.","zh":"如果某做法持續數千年，它很可能帶有深厚文化價值。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long historical continuity.","zh":"這個片語強調長久歷史延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"paint on the ground","meaning":"在地面作畫","examples":[{"en":"Artists traditionally painted on the ground with coloured sand.","zh":"藝術家傳統上以彩色沙粒在地面作畫。"},{"en":"To paint on the ground means to create images or patterns directly on the earth’s surface.","zh":"paint on the ground 指直接在土地表面創作圖像或圖案。"},{"en":"Children may paint on the ground with chalk during a school festival.","zh":"孩子可能在學校節日用粉筆在地面作畫。"},{"en":"If ground paintings are made from sand, wind and weather may remove them quickly.","zh":"如果地面畫由沙製成，風和天氣可能很快把它們抹去。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a temporary or place-based art practice.","zh":"這個片語描述臨時或與地方相連的藝術實踐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"coloured sand","meaning":"彩色沙粒","examples":[{"en":"Different shades of coloured sand were used to create traditional designs.","zh":"不同深淺的彩色沙粒被用來創作傳統設計。"},{"en":"Coloured sand is sand with natural or added colours used for decoration or artwork.","zh":"coloured sand 是具有天然或加入顏色、用於裝飾或藝術品的沙。"},{"en":"Students may use coloured sand to make festival patterns on the floor.","zh":"學生可能用彩色沙粒在地板上製作節日圖案。"},{"en":"If artists use coloured sand, the artwork may be beautiful but temporary.","zh":"如果藝術家使用彩色沙粒，作品可能美麗但短暫。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a simple material used in visual design.","zh":"這個片語指視覺設計中使用的簡單材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rock faces","meaning":"岩壁","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal artists also created paintings on rock faces.","zh":"澳洲原住民藝術家也在岩壁上創作畫作。"},{"en":"Rock faces are exposed vertical or sloping surfaces of natural rock.","zh":"rock faces 是自然岩石外露的垂直或傾斜表面。"},{"en":"Climbers look for safe rock faces before climbing a cliff.","zh":"攀石者在攀爬懸崖前會尋找安全岩壁。"},{"en":"If ancient paintings appear on rock faces, they may survive longer than paintings on sand.","zh":"如果古代畫作出現在岩壁上，它們可能比沙畫保存更久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes natural stone surfaces.","zh":"這個片語描述天然石面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"decorate their bodies","meaning":"裝飾身體","examples":[{"en":"People decorated their bodies for ceremonial purposes.","zh":"人們為儀式用途裝飾身體。"},{"en":"To decorate their bodies means to paint, mark or adorn the body with colours, patterns or objects.","zh":"decorate their bodies 指用顏色、圖案或物件在身體上繪畫、標記或裝飾。"},{"en":"Performers may decorate their bodies before a traditional dance.","zh":"表演者可能在傳統舞蹈前裝飾身體。"},{"en":"If body decoration is used in ceremony, it may show identity, role or sacred meaning.","zh":"如果身體裝飾用於儀式，它可能顯示身份、角色或神聖意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the body as a surface for cultural expression.","zh":"這個片語描述身體作為文化表達的表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ceremonial purposes","meaning":"儀式用途","examples":[{"en":"Body painting was used for ceremonial purposes.","zh":"身體彩繪被用於儀式用途。"},{"en":"Ceremonial purposes are reasons connected with formal rituals, traditions or sacred events.","zh":"ceremonial purposes 是與正式儀式、傳統或神聖事件相關的用途。"},{"en":"A special robe may be worn for ceremonial purposes at graduation.","zh":"畢業典禮上可能為儀式用途穿着特別長袍。"},{"en":"If an object is used for ceremonial purposes, its meaning is more than practical.","zh":"如果物件用於儀式用途，其意義不只是實用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes use in rituals or formal occasions.","zh":"這個片語描述在儀式或正式場合中的用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"formal vocabulary","meaning":"正式的視覺語彙","examples":[{"en":"Traditional Aboriginal art already possessed a formal visual vocabulary.","zh":"傳統澳洲原住民藝術已經擁有正式的視覺語彙。"},{"en":"A formal vocabulary is an organised set of signs, patterns or methods used to express meaning.","zh":"formal vocabulary 是一套有組織的符號、圖案或方法，用來表達意義。"},{"en":"Music has a formal vocabulary of notes, rhythm and structure.","zh":"音樂有由音符、節奏和結構組成的正式語彙。"},{"en":"If art has a formal visual vocabulary, viewers can learn to read its symbols.","zh":"如果藝術有正式視覺語彙，觀眾就可以學習讀懂其符號。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a structured language of artistic expression.","zh":"這個片語描述藝術表達中的結構化語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be noted by","meaning":"被……注意到","examples":[{"en":"The existence of this artistic vocabulary had already been noted by Europeans.","zh":"這種藝術語彙的存在早已被歐洲人注意到。"},{"en":"To be noted by someone means to be noticed, recorded or mentioned by them.","zh":"be noted by someone 指被某人注意、記錄或提及。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be noted by several teachers after weeks of effort.","zh":"經過數星期努力後，學生的進步可能被幾位老師注意到。"},{"en":"If a cultural practice is noted by outsiders, it may enter written records.","zh":"如果文化做法被外來者注意到，它可能進入文字記錄。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something being observed or documented.","zh":"這個片語描述某事被觀察或記錄下來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in the early twentieth century","meaning":"在二十世紀初","examples":[{"en":"New forms of Aboriginal painting appeared in the early twentieth century.","zh":"新形式的澳洲原住民繪畫出現在二十世紀初。"},{"en":"In the early twentieth century means during the first decades of the 1900s.","zh":"in the early twentieth century 指在1900年代最初幾十年。"},{"en":"Many cities introduced electric trams in the early twentieth century.","zh":"許多城市在二十世紀初引入電車。"},{"en":"If an art form changed in this period, colonial contact may have shaped its materials or audience.","zh":"如果藝術形式在這時期改變，殖民接觸可能塑造其材料或觀眾。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a historical time frame.","zh":"這個片語給出歷史時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be brought together by","meaning":"由……聚集起來","examples":[{"en":"Some Aboriginal communities were brought together by missionaries.","zh":"一些澳洲原住民社群由傳教士聚集起來。"},{"en":"To be brought together by someone means to be gathered into one place or group by that person or organisation.","zh":"be brought together by someone 指由某人或組織把人聚集到一個地方或群體中。"},{"en":"Students from different classes may be brought together by a school debate competition.","zh":"來自不同班級的學生可能由學校辯論比賽聚集起來。"},{"en":"If communities are brought together by outsiders, traditional patterns of life may change.","zh":"如果社群由外來者聚集起來，傳統生活模式可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gathering caused by an external force.","zh":"這個片語描述由外部力量造成的聚集。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"missionaries","meaning":"傳教士","examples":[{"en":"Missionaries encouraged Aboriginal communities to paint on tree bark.","zh":"傳教士鼓勵澳洲原住民社群在樹皮上作畫。"},{"en":"Missionaries are religious workers who travel to spread their faith and often set up schools or churches.","zh":"missionaries 是前往不同地方傳播信仰，並常建立學校或教會的宗教工作者。"},{"en":"Missionaries in colonial areas sometimes influenced education, language and local customs.","zh":"殖民地區的傳教士有時影響教育、語言和本地習俗。"},{"en":"If missionaries support local art, they may also affect how and where it is produced.","zh":"如果傳教士支持本地藝術，他們也可能影響藝術如何以及在哪裡製作。"},{"en":"This word refers to religious agents, often in historical colonial contexts.","zh":"這個詞指宗教代理人，常出現在歷史殖民背景中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"northern Australia","meaning":"澳洲北部","examples":[{"en":"Bark painting developed in communities in northern Australia.","zh":"樹皮畫在澳洲北部社群中發展。"},{"en":"Northern Australia refers to the northern region of the Australian continent.","zh":"northern Australia 指澳洲大陸北部地區。"},{"en":"Northern Australia includes tropical areas where climate, plants and communities differ from the central desert.","zh":"澳洲北部包括熱帶地區，其氣候、植物和社群與中部沙漠不同。"},{"en":"If bark painting developed there, available trees and local traditions helped shape the art.","zh":"如果樹皮畫在那裡發展，可用樹木和本地傳統幫助塑造藝術。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a regional location within Australia.","zh":"這個片語給出澳洲內部的地區位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be encouraged to","meaning":"獲鼓勵去……","examples":[{"en":"Artists were encouraged to reproduce traditional motifs on bark.","zh":"藝術家獲鼓勵在樹皮上重現傳統圖案。"},{"en":"To be encouraged to do something means to be supported or advised to do it.","zh":"be encouraged to do something 指獲得支持或建議去做某事。"},{"en":"Students are encouraged to ask questions when they do not understand a lesson.","zh":"學生不明白課堂時，獲鼓勵去提問。"},{"en":"If artists are encouraged to try new materials, an old tradition may take a new form.","zh":"如果藝術家獲鼓勵嘗試新材料，古老傳統可能呈現新形式。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests support rather than force.","zh":"這個片語暗示支持，而不是強迫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reproduce motifs","meaning":"重現圖案","examples":[{"en":"The artists reproduced motifs that had previously appeared on rock faces.","zh":"藝術家重現了先前出現在岩壁上的圖案。"},{"en":"To reproduce motifs means to copy or recreate repeated traditional patterns or symbols.","zh":"reproduce motifs 指複製或重新創作重複出現的傳統圖案或符號。"},{"en":"A designer may reproduce old flower motifs on modern fabric.","zh":"設計師可能在現代布料上重現舊花卉圖案。"},{"en":"If motifs are reproduced on new materials, they can reach new audiences while keeping old meanings.","zh":"如果圖案在新材料上重現，它們可以接觸新觀眾，同時保留舊意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes carrying visual patterns from one medium to another.","zh":"這個片語描述把視覺圖案從一種媒介帶到另一種媒介。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tree bark","meaning":"樹皮","examples":[{"en":"Artists in northern Australia painted on tree bark.","zh":"澳洲北部藝術家在樹皮上作畫。"},{"en":"Tree bark is the outer covering of a tree trunk or branch.","zh":"tree bark 是樹幹或樹枝的外層覆蓋物。"},{"en":"Children can feel tree bark to notice whether it is rough, smooth, thick or thin.","zh":"孩子可以觸摸樹皮，留意它是粗糙、光滑、厚還是薄。"},{"en":"If artists paint on bark, natural material becomes part of the artwork’s meaning.","zh":"如果藝術家在樹皮上作畫，天然材料會成為藝術品意義的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a traditional painting surface taken from trees.","zh":"這個片語指取自樹木的傳統繪畫表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"turn out a steady stream of","meaning":"持續創作大量……","examples":[{"en":"The artists turned out a steady stream of paintings.","zh":"藝術家持續創作大量畫作。"},{"en":"To turn out a steady stream of something means to produce many examples regularly over time.","zh":"turn out a steady stream of something 指長期定期生產許多作品或物品。"},{"en":"A small bakery may turn out a steady stream of fresh bread every morning.","zh":"小麵包店可能每天早上持續製作大量新鮮麵包。"},{"en":"If artists produce a steady stream of works, galleries have enough pieces to sell or display.","zh":"如果藝術家穩定創作作品，畫廊就有足夠作品出售或展示。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continuous production.","zh":"這個片語描述持續生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be supported by","meaning":"得到……支持","examples":[{"en":"The artists were supported by local churches.","zh":"藝術家得到本地教會支持。"},{"en":"To be supported by someone means to receive help, resources or encouragement from them.","zh":"be supported by someone 指從某人或某組織獲得幫助、資源或鼓勵。"},{"en":"A student may be supported by teachers, family and classmates during exams.","zh":"學生在考試期間可能得到老師、家人和同學支持。"},{"en":"If artists are supported by institutions, they may gain materials, buyers and wider attention.","zh":"如果藝術家得到機構支持，他們可能獲得材料、買家和更廣泛關注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes help that makes work possible.","zh":"這個片語描述令工作得以進行的幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sell something to the public","meaning":"向公眾出售某物","examples":[{"en":"The churches helped sell the paintings to the public.","zh":"教會幫助向公眾出售畫作。"},{"en":"To sell something to the public means to offer it for ordinary people to buy.","zh":"sell something to the public 指把某物提供給普通人購買。"},{"en":"A school charity fair may sell handmade cards to the public.","zh":"學校慈善市集可能向公眾出售手製卡。"},{"en":"If artworks are sold to the public, artists can earn income and reach new audiences.","zh":"如果藝術品向公眾出售，藝術家可以賺取收入並接觸新觀眾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving a product from creators to buyers.","zh":"這個片語描述把產品從創作者帶到買家手中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reach overseas museums","meaning":"進入海外博物館","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal paintings began to reach overseas museums during the mid-twentieth century.","zh":"澳洲原住民畫作在二十世紀中期開始進入海外博物館。"},{"en":"To reach overseas museums means to be collected, shown or stored by museums in other countries.","zh":"reach overseas museums 指被其他國家的博物館收藏、展示或保存。"},{"en":"A local artist’s work may reach overseas museums after an international exhibition.","zh":"本地藝術家的作品可能在國際展覽後進入海外博物館。"},{"en":"If artworks reach foreign museums, they can influence how other countries understand the culture.","zh":"如果藝術品進入外國博物館，它們可以影響其他國家如何理解該文化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes international movement of art into institutions.","zh":"這個片語描述藝術品進入國際機構的流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"persist in","meaning":"在……持續","examples":[{"en":"Painting on bark persisted in northern Australia.","zh":"樹皮繪畫在澳洲北部持續存在。"},{"en":"To persist in a place means to continue existing or being practised there.","zh":"persist in a place 指在某地繼續存在或被實踐。"},{"en":"Handwriting lessons may persist in some schools even when laptops are common.","zh":"即使手提電腦普及，手寫課在一些學校仍可能持續。"},{"en":"If a tradition persists, it survives despite social or material change.","zh":"如果傳統持續存在，它就在社會或材料變化中存活下來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continued existence over time.","zh":"這個片語描述隨時間繼續存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"whereas","meaning":"然而；而","examples":[{"en":"Bark remained common in the north, whereas central communities increasingly used acrylics.","zh":"樹皮在北部仍然常見，而中部社群越來越多使用塑膠彩。"},{"en":"Whereas introduces a contrast between two facts or situations.","zh":"whereas 用來引入兩個事實或情況之間的對比。"},{"en":"Some students prefer quiet study, whereas others learn better through discussion.","zh":"有些學生喜歡安靜溫習，而另一些則透過討論學得更好。"},{"en":"If one region uses bark whereas another uses acrylic paint, local materials and history may differ.","zh":"如果一個地區使用樹皮，而另一地區使用塑膠彩，本地材料和歷史可能不同。"},{"en":"This word helps compare differences clearly.","zh":"這個詞幫助清楚比較差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"central desert communities","meaning":"中部沙漠社區","examples":[{"en":"Central desert communities increasingly used acrylic paint.","zh":"中部沙漠社區越來越多使用塑膠彩。"},{"en":"Central desert communities are groups living in Australia’s inland desert regions.","zh":"central desert communities 是生活在澳洲內陸沙漠地區的群體。"},{"en":"These communities may be far from large cities but strongly connected to land and tradition.","zh":"這些社區可能遠離大城市，但與土地和傳統有強烈連繫。"},{"en":"If central desert communities adopt new materials, ancient stories can take portable modern forms.","zh":"如果中部沙漠社區採用新材料，古老故事可以呈現可移動的現代形式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to Indigenous communities in the Australian desert interior.","zh":"這個片語指澳洲沙漠內陸的原住民社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"acrylic paint","meaning":"塑膠彩；丙烯顏料","examples":[{"en":"Artists in the central desert adopted acrylic paint.","zh":"中部沙漠藝術家採用了塑膠彩。"},{"en":"Acrylic paint is a fast-drying modern paint made with synthetic materials.","zh":"acrylic paint 是由合成材料製成、乾得快的現代顏料。"},{"en":"Students often use acrylic paint because it is bright, flexible and easier to clean than oil paint.","zh":"學生常使用塑膠彩，因為它顏色鮮明、有彈性，而且比油畫顏料較易清理。"},{"en":"If traditional designs are made with acrylic paint, the works can be sold and transported more easily.","zh":"如果傳統設計用塑膠彩創作，作品更容易出售和運輸。"},{"en":"This phrase names a modern painting material.","zh":"這個片語指出一種現代繪畫材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"explore the possibilities of","meaning":"探索……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"Women artists explored the possibilities of wax painting and dyeing.","zh":"女性藝術家探索蠟染畫和染色工藝的可能性。"},{"en":"To explore the possibilities of something means to try different ways it can be used or developed.","zh":"explore the possibilities of something 指嘗試某物可以如何使用或發展。"},{"en":"A teacher may explore the possibilities of games in grammar lessons.","zh":"老師可能探索遊戲在文法課中的可能性。"},{"en":"If artists explore new materials, they may discover fresh forms of expression.","zh":"如果藝術家探索新材料，他們可能發現新的表達形式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creative experimentation.","zh":"這個片語描述創意實驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"wax painting","meaning":"蠟染畫","examples":[{"en":"Some Aboriginal women developed works using wax painting.","zh":"一些澳洲原住民女性使用蠟染畫發展作品。"},{"en":"Wax painting is a technique that uses wax to create or protect patterns before colour is added.","zh":"wax painting 是使用蠟來創作或保護圖案，再加入顏色的技巧。"},{"en":"Students may use wax painting to make patterns that resist watercolour.","zh":"學生可能使用蠟染畫製作不吸水彩的圖案。"},{"en":"If wax blocks dye, artists can create sharp designs on cloth or paper.","zh":"如果蠟阻擋染料，藝術家可以在布或紙上創造清晰設計。"},{"en":"This phrase names an art technique based on wax and colour.","zh":"這個片語指出一種以蠟和顏色為基礎的藝術技巧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dyeing processes","meaning":"染色工藝","examples":[{"en":"The artists experimented with different dyeing processes.","zh":"藝術家嘗試不同染色工藝。"},{"en":"Dyeing processes are methods of adding colour to cloth, fibre or other materials.","zh":"dyeing processes 是把顏色加入布料、纖維或其他材料的方法。"},{"en":"A fashion class may teach dyeing processes using natural colours from plants.","zh":"時裝課可能教授使用植物天然顏色的染色工藝。"},{"en":"If artists change the dyeing process, the final colour and pattern may change.","zh":"如果藝術家改變染色工藝，最終顏色和圖案可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes techniques for colouring materials.","zh":"這個片語描述為材料上色的技巧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"batik","meaning":"蠟染","examples":[{"en":"Batik involves applying wax and dye to create patterned cloth.","zh":"蠟染涉及使用蠟和染料創造有圖案布料。"},{"en":"Batik is a fabric-decorating technique using wax to resist dye and form designs.","zh":"batik 是一種布料裝飾技巧，用蠟防染以形成設計。"},{"en":"Students may make batik scarves in an art workshop.","zh":"學生可能在藝術工作坊製作蠟染圍巾。"},{"en":"If wax is applied before dyeing, the covered areas stay lighter and create patterns.","zh":"如果染色前先上蠟，被覆蓋部分會保持較淺並形成圖案。"},{"en":"This word refers to a traditional textile art technique.","zh":"這個詞指一種傳統紡織藝術技巧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"depict elements of","meaning":"描繪……的元素","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal paintings depict elements of the Dreaming.","zh":"澳洲原住民畫作描繪「夢創時代」的元素。"},{"en":"To depict elements of something means to show parts of it in a picture, story or artwork.","zh":"depict elements of something 指在圖像、故事或藝術品中展示某事的部分內容。"},{"en":"A poster may depict elements of school life such as lessons, sports and friendships.","zh":"海報可能描繪學校生活元素，例如課堂、運動和友誼。"},{"en":"If a painting depicts sacred elements, it may need permission from the community that owns the story.","zh":"如果畫作描繪神聖元素，可能需要擁有該故事的社群批准。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual representation of selected parts.","zh":"這個片語描述對特定部分的視覺呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"collective history","meaning":"集體歷史","examples":[{"en":"The Dreaming represents the collective history of each community.","zh":"「夢創時代」代表每個社群的集體歷史。"},{"en":"Collective history is the shared past remembered and understood by a group.","zh":"collective history 是一個群體共同記住和理解的過去。"},{"en":"A village’s collective history may include migration, hardship, festivals and local heroes.","zh":"村莊的集體歷史可能包括遷徙、苦難、節日和本地英雄。"},{"en":"If collective history is passed on through art, younger people can learn who they are.","zh":"如果集體歷史透過藝術傳承，年輕人可以了解自己是誰。"},{"en":"This phrase connects group memory with identity.","zh":"這個片語把群體記憶與身份連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be part of and guardian of","meaning":"既是……的一部分，也是其守護者","examples":[{"en":"Each community is both part of and guardian of its Dreaming stories.","zh":"每個社群既是其「夢創時代」故事的一部分，也是其守護者。"},{"en":"To be part of and guardian of something means to belong to it while also protecting it.","zh":"be part of and guardian of something 指屬於某事，同時也保護它。"},{"en":"A family member can be part of a tradition and guardian of it by teaching younger relatives.","zh":"家庭成員可以透過教導年輕親人，既成為傳統的一部分，也成為其守護者。"},{"en":"If a community guards a story, outsiders cannot freely use it without respect or permission.","zh":"如果社群守護某故事，外人不能在缺乏尊重或批准下自由使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase combines belonging with responsibility.","zh":"這個片語結合歸屬與責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the story of their origins","meaning":"他們的起源故事","examples":[{"en":"The Dreaming tells the story of Aboriginal people’s origins.","zh":"「夢創時代」講述澳洲原住民的起源故事。"},{"en":"The story of their origins is the account explaining where a people came from and how their world began.","zh":"story of their origins 是解釋一個民族從何而來，以及其世界如何開始的敘述。"},{"en":"Families sometimes tell children the story of their origins through old photographs and migration memories.","zh":"家庭有時透過舊照片和移民記憶向孩子講述起源故事。"},{"en":"If people lose their origin stories, they may feel less connected to place and ancestry.","zh":"如果人們失去起源故事，他們可能與地方和祖先的連繫較弱。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a group’s beginning and identity.","zh":"這個片語指一個群體的開始和身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Great Ancestors","meaning":"偉大祖先","examples":[{"en":"The Great Ancestors passed knowledge and skills on to later generations.","zh":"偉大祖先把知識和技能傳給後世。"},{"en":"Great Ancestors are sacred ancestral figures who shaped the world and gave people laws, stories and skills.","zh":"Great Ancestors 是塑造世界並給予人們法律、故事和技能的神聖祖先人物。"},{"en":"In many cultures, ancestors are honoured because they connect the living with the past.","zh":"在許多文化中，祖先受到尊敬，因為他們連接活着的人與過去。"},{"en":"If ancestors are central to belief, art may show their journeys and actions.","zh":"如果祖先是信仰核心，藝術可能展示他們的旅程和行動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to powerful ancestral beings in Aboriginal tradition.","zh":"這個片語指澳洲原住民傳統中的強大神聖祖先。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pass on knowledge","meaning":"傳授知識","examples":[{"en":"The ancestors passed on their knowledge, art and skills.","zh":"祖先傳授他們的知識、藝術和技能。"},{"en":"To pass on knowledge means to teach or transmit what someone knows to others.","zh":"pass on knowledge 指把某人知道的東西教給或傳給他人。"},{"en":"A chef may pass on knowledge by teaching apprentices how to prepare traditional dishes.","zh":"廚師可能透過教學徒準備傳統菜式來傳授知識。"},{"en":"If elders pass on knowledge, young people can continue important practices.","zh":"如果長者傳授知識，年輕人就能延續重要做法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cultural and practical teaching across generations.","zh":"這個片語描述跨世代的文化和實用教學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"traditional skills","meaning":"傳統技能","examples":[{"en":"Hunting, medicine, painting, music and dance are traditional skills.","zh":"狩獵、醫藥、繪畫、音樂和舞蹈都是傳統技能。"},{"en":"Traditional skills are abilities passed down through a community over time.","zh":"traditional skills 是社群隨時間傳承下來的能力。"},{"en":"Sewing festival clothes or preparing herbal medicine can be traditional skills.","zh":"縫製節日服裝或準備草藥可以是傳統技能。"},{"en":"If traditional skills are not taught, they may disappear within a few generations.","zh":"如果傳統技能沒有被教授，它們可能在幾代內消失。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical cultural knowledge.","zh":"這個片語指實用的文化知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be synonymous with","meaning":"與……同義；等同於","examples":[{"en":"The Dreaming is not synonymous with a single moment of creation.","zh":"「夢創時代」並不等同於單一創世時刻。"},{"en":"To be synonymous with something means to have the same meaning as it.","zh":"be synonymous with something 指與某事有相同意思。"},{"en":"Good grades are not synonymous with true understanding.","zh":"好成績並不等同於真正理解。"},{"en":"If a belief system is not synonymous with one event, it may include continuing laws and practices.","zh":"如果一套信仰系統不等同於單一事件，它可能包括持續的法律和做法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when clarifying what two ideas are not exactly the same.","zh":"這個片語適合用於澄清兩個概念並不完全相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the creation of the world","meaning":"世界的創造","examples":[{"en":"The Dreaming is not limited to the creation of the world.","zh":"「夢創時代」並不限於世界的創造。"},{"en":"The creation of the world means the beginning or formation of the world in a religious or mythological story.","zh":"creation of the world 指宗教或神話故事中世界的開始或形成。"},{"en":"Many ancient cultures have stories about the creation of the world.","zh":"許多古代文化都有關於世界創造的故事。"},{"en":"If a belief goes beyond creation, it may also guide present-day behaviour and ceremonies.","zh":"如果信仰超越創世，它也可能指導今天的行為和儀式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to origin stories about how the world began.","zh":"這個片語指關於世界如何開始的起源故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cease to exist","meaning":"不復存在；停止存在","examples":[{"en":"For Aboriginal people, the Dreaming has never ceased to exist.","zh":"對澳洲原住民而言，「夢創時代」從未不復存在。"},{"en":"To cease to exist means to stop existing completely.","zh":"cease to exist 指完全停止存在。"},{"en":"A shop may cease to exist after it closes and its building is replaced.","zh":"商店關閉並被新建築取代後，可能不復存在。"},{"en":"If a belief is practised through ceremonies, it does not cease to exist simply because it is ancient.","zh":"如果信仰透過儀式實踐，它不會只因古老而停止存在。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete disappearance or ending.","zh":"這個片語描述完全消失或終結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be perpetuated by","meaning":"透過……延續","examples":[{"en":"The Dreaming is perpetuated by seasonal cycles and religious ceremonies.","zh":"「夢創時代」透過季節循環和宗教儀式延續。"},{"en":"To be perpetuated by something means to be kept alive or continued through it.","zh":"be perpetuated by something 指透過某事保持存在或延續。"},{"en":"A family tradition may be perpetuated by yearly gatherings.","zh":"家庭傳統可能透過每年聚會延續。"},{"en":"If stories are repeated in ceremonies, they can be passed on for generations.","zh":"如果故事在儀式中重複，它們可以傳承幾代。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how something continues over time.","zh":"這個片語描述某事如何隨時間持續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the cycle of the seasons","meaning":"季節循環","examples":[{"en":"The cycle of the seasons helps sustain the Dreaming.","zh":"季節循環有助維持「夢創時代」。"},{"en":"The cycle of the seasons is the repeated pattern of seasonal change through the year.","zh":"cycle of the seasons 是一年中季節變化的重複模式。"},{"en":"Farmers follow the cycle of the seasons when planting and harvesting crops.","zh":"農民在種植和收割作物時遵循季節循環。"},{"en":"If ceremonies follow seasonal cycles, culture stays connected to land and time.","zh":"如果儀式跟隨季節循環，文化就會與土地和時間保持連接。"},{"en":"This phrase describes nature’s repeating yearly rhythm.","zh":"這個片語描述自然界每年重複的節奏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"religious ceremonies","meaning":"宗教儀式","examples":[{"en":"Religious ceremonies help preserve Aboriginal cultural beliefs.","zh":"宗教儀式有助保存澳洲原住民文化信仰。"},{"en":"Religious ceremonies are formal acts of worship, remembrance or ritual connected with belief.","zh":"religious ceremonies 是與信仰相關的正式崇拜、紀念或儀式行為。"},{"en":"Weddings, funerals and temple festivals can be religious ceremonies.","zh":"婚禮、葬禮和廟會都可以是宗教儀式。"},{"en":"If ceremonies are repeated, beliefs can remain active in community life.","zh":"如果儀式被重複實踐，信仰可以在社群生活中保持活力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to structured sacred practices.","zh":"這個片語指有結構的神聖做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ensure the permanence of","meaning":"確保……長存","examples":[{"en":"The ceremonies aim to ensure the permanence of the Dreaming.","zh":"這些儀式旨在確保「夢創時代」長存。"},{"en":"To ensure the permanence of something means to make sure it continues to exist for a long time.","zh":"ensure the permanence of something 指確保某事長期持續存在。"},{"en":"Schools archive old photos to ensure the permanence of community memory.","zh":"學校保存舊照片，以確保社群記憶長存。"},{"en":"If traditions are taught to children, their permanence becomes more likely.","zh":"如果傳統被教給孩子，它們長存的可能性就更高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protecting something from disappearing.","zh":"這個片語描述保護某事免於消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"golden age","meaning":"黃金時代","examples":[{"en":"The ceremonies help preserve a sacred golden age.","zh":"這些儀式有助保存一個神聖黃金時代。"},{"en":"A golden age is a special period remembered as highly valuable, successful or sacred.","zh":"golden age 是被記住為極有價值、成功或神聖的特殊時期。"},{"en":"Some people see childhood as a golden age because it feels innocent and free.","zh":"有些人把童年視為黃金時代，因為它感覺天真自由。"},{"en":"If a culture preserves stories of a golden age, it keeps a model of order and meaning.","zh":"如果文化保存黃金時代的故事，它就保留了秩序和意義的典範。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an idealised important time.","zh":"這個片語描述被理想化的重要時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"central function","meaning":"核心功能","examples":[{"en":"The central function of Aboriginal painting is cultural preservation.","zh":"澳洲原住民繪畫的核心功能是文化保存。"},{"en":"A central function is the main role or purpose of something.","zh":"central function 是某事物的主要角色或目的。"},{"en":"The central function of a dictionary is to explain word meanings clearly.","zh":"字典的核心功能是清楚解釋詞義。"},{"en":"If the central function of art is preservation, beauty is connected with memory and survival.","zh":"如果藝術的核心功能是保存，美感就與記憶和延續相連。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the most important purpose.","zh":"這個片語指出最重要的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"contemporary manifestations","meaning":"當代表現形式","examples":[{"en":"The tradition survives through its contemporary manifestations.","zh":"這種傳統透過其當代表現形式延續。"},{"en":"Contemporary manifestations are modern forms or examples of an older idea, tradition or belief.","zh":"contemporary manifestations 是較古老想法、傳統或信仰的現代形式或例子。"},{"en":"Online festivals can be contemporary manifestations of traditional community celebrations.","zh":"網上節日可以是傳統社區慶典的當代表現形式。"},{"en":"If ancient stories appear in modern paintings, they become visible in contemporary form.","zh":"如果古老故事出現在現代畫作中，它們就以當代形式可見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how old traditions appear today.","zh":"這個片語描述舊傳統今天如何呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"guarantee the survival of","meaning":"確保……得以延續","examples":[{"en":"The paintings help guarantee the survival of the spiritual world they represent.","zh":"這些畫作有助確保它們所代表的精神世界得以延續。"},{"en":"To guarantee the survival of something means to help make sure it continues to exist.","zh":"guarantee the survival of something 指幫助確保某事繼續存在。"},{"en":"Recording elders’ stories can help guarantee the survival of local history.","zh":"記錄長者故事可以幫助確保本地歷史得以延續。"},{"en":"If a culture is taught through art, its beliefs may survive even under pressure.","zh":"如果文化透過藝術被教授，其信仰即使在壓力下也可能存續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protecting something from disappearance.","zh":"這個片語描述保護某事免於消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"past, present and future","meaning":"過去、現在與未來","examples":[{"en":"The Dreaming connects the past, present and future.","zh":"「夢創時代」連接過去、現在與未來。"},{"en":"Past, present and future means earlier time, the current moment and the time still to come.","zh":"past, present and future 指較早時間、當下和仍未到來的時間。"},{"en":"A family tree connects past, present and future by linking ancestors, living relatives and children.","zh":"族譜透過連接祖先、在世親人和孩子，把過去、現在與未來連起來。"},{"en":"If a belief links all three, it is not only about history but also about present duties and future survival.","zh":"如果信仰連接三者，它就不只是關於歷史，也關於當下責任和未來延續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continuity across time.","zh":"這個片語描述跨越時間的連續性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be created individually","meaning":"由個別藝術家創作","examples":[{"en":"Each work is created individually by an artist.","zh":"每件作品由個別藝術家創作。"},{"en":"To be created individually means to be made by one particular person rather than by an anonymous group.","zh":"be created individually 指由某一個特定人物製作，而不是由匿名群體製作。"},{"en":"A student’s portfolio should be created individually so teachers can judge personal progress.","zh":"學生作品集應由個別學生創作，讓老師評估個人進步。"},{"en":"If works are created individually, each artist’s style and choices matter.","zh":"如果作品由個別創作者製作，每位藝術家的風格和選擇都重要。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights personal authorship.","zh":"這個片語突出個人作者身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a form peculiar to","meaning":"……獨有的形式","examples":[{"en":"Each painting has a form peculiar to its artist.","zh":"每幅畫都有其藝術家獨有的形式。"},{"en":"A form peculiar to someone means a style or shape that is especially characteristic of that person.","zh":"form peculiar to someone 指特別屬於某人的風格或形態。"},{"en":"A singer may have a voice peculiar to them, so listeners recognise it immediately.","zh":"歌手可能有獨有聲音，令聽眾立即認出。"},{"en":"If an artwork has a form peculiar to its artist, it shows personal creativity within tradition.","zh":"如果藝術品有藝術家獨有形式，它顯示傳統內的個人創意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a distinctive individual style.","zh":"這個片語描述獨特個人風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"within a community","meaning":"在社群之內","examples":[{"en":"The work is created within a particular community.","zh":"作品是在某個特定社群之內創作的。"},{"en":"Within a community means inside a specific social or cultural group.","zh":"within a community 指在特定社會或文化群體之內。"},{"en":"A charity project may begin within a community before spreading to nearby districts.","zh":"慈善項目可能先在社群之內開始，再傳到附近地區。"},{"en":"If art is made within a community, its meaning may depend on shared stories and rules.","zh":"如果藝術在社群之內製作，其意義可能取決於共同故事和規則。"},{"en":"This phrase places an action inside a social group.","zh":"這個片語把行動放在社會群體內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"on behalf of","meaning":"代表……","examples":[{"en":"An artist creates a work on behalf of the wider community.","zh":"藝術家代表更廣泛社群創作作品。"},{"en":"On behalf of someone means representing them or acting for them.","zh":"on behalf of someone 指代表某人或為某人行事。"},{"en":"A class monitor may speak on behalf of classmates in a meeting.","zh":"班長可能在會議中代表同學發言。"},{"en":"If an artist works on behalf of a community, the work carries communal responsibility.","zh":"如果藝術家代表社群創作，作品就承載社群責任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes representation, not just personal action.","zh":"這個片語描述代表性，而不只是個人行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"approve a work","meaning":"批准作品","examples":[{"en":"The community must approve the completed work.","zh":"社群必須批准已完成作品。"},{"en":"To approve a work means to formally accept it as suitable or correct.","zh":"approve a work 指正式接受某作品合適或正確。"},{"en":"A teacher may approve a project topic before students begin research.","zh":"老師可能在學生開始研究前批准專題題目。"},{"en":"If a painting contains community-owned stories, community approval protects cultural rules.","zh":"如果畫作包含社群擁有的故事，社群批准可以保護文化規則。"},{"en":"This phrase describes permission or acceptance after checking.","zh":"這個片語描述檢查後的許可或接納。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"belong to","meaning":"屬於……","examples":[{"en":"An artist cannot use a Dreaming story that does not belong to their community.","zh":"藝術家不能使用不屬於其社群的「夢創時代」故事。"},{"en":"To belong to someone or a group means to be owned by them or properly connected with them.","zh":"belong to someone or a group 指由某人或群體擁有，或與其有正當連繫。"},{"en":"A school uniform belongs to the student who bought it, not to the classroom.","zh":"校服屬於購買它的學生，而不是課室。"},{"en":"If a sacred story belongs to one community, others should not use it freely.","zh":"如果神聖故事屬於某一社群，其他人不應自由使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ownership, connection or rightful association.","zh":"這個片語描述擁有權、連繫或正當歸屬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be the owner of","meaning":"是……的擁有者","examples":[{"en":"Each community is regarded as the owner of its Dreaming stories.","zh":"每個社群被視為其「夢創時代」故事的擁有者。"},{"en":"To be the owner of something means to have the right to control, protect or use it.","zh":"be the owner of something 指擁有控制、保護或使用某物的權利。"},{"en":"A shop is the owner of its logo and can stop others copying it.","zh":"店舖是其標誌的擁有者，可以阻止他人抄襲。"},{"en":"If a community owns a story, permission may be needed before it is painted or sold.","zh":"如果社群擁有某故事，在它被繪畫或出售前可能需要許可。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognised rights over something.","zh":"這個片語描述對某物被承認的權利。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be anchored to","meaning":"扎根於……","examples":[{"en":"Each Aboriginal community is anchored to a particular territory.","zh":"每個澳洲原住民社群都扎根於特定領土。"},{"en":"To be anchored to something means to be strongly fixed or connected to it.","zh":"be anchored to something 指牢牢固定於或連接於某物。"},{"en":"A family business may be anchored to one neighbourhood through long relationships with customers.","zh":"家族企業可能透過與顧客的長期關係扎根於某個社區。"},{"en":"If identity is anchored to land, losing land can damage culture deeply.","zh":"如果身份扎根於土地，失去土地可以深深破壞文化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong foundation or attachment.","zh":"這個片語描述強大基礎或依附。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mark out a territory","meaning":"劃定領土","examples":[{"en":"The ancestors marked out the community’s territory.","zh":"祖先劃定了社群的領土。"},{"en":"To mark out a territory means to define or show the boundaries of an area.","zh":"mark out a territory 指界定或顯示某區域的邊界。"},{"en":"A school may mark out a football pitch with white lines before a match.","zh":"學校可能在比賽前用白線劃定足球場。"},{"en":"If ancestors mark out territory in stories, land becomes tied to memory and law.","zh":"如果祖先在故事中劃定領土，土地就與記憶和法律相連。"},{"en":"This phrase describes setting or showing boundaries.","zh":"這個片語描述設定或顯示邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be interpreted as","meaning":"被理解為；被詮釋為","examples":[{"en":"Each painting can be interpreted as a spiritual road map.","zh":"每幅畫都可以被詮釋為一幅精神地圖。"},{"en":"To be interpreted as something means to be understood or explained in that way.","zh":"be interpreted as something 指被以某種方式理解或解釋。"},{"en":"A student’s silence may be interpreted as shyness, not rudeness.","zh":"學生沉默可能被理解為害羞，而不是無禮。"},{"en":"If a painting is interpreted as a map, viewers look for paths, places and relationships.","zh":"如果畫作被詮釋為地圖，觀眾會尋找路徑、地方和關係。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how meaning is read from something.","zh":"這個片語描述如何從某物讀出意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"spiritual road map","meaning":"精神地圖","examples":[{"en":"A painting may function as a spiritual road map for its community.","zh":"畫作可能為其社群發揮精神地圖的作用。"},{"en":"A spiritual road map is a symbolic guide to sacred places, stories, journeys or relationships.","zh":"spiritual road map 是通往神聖地方、故事、旅程或關係的象徵指南。"},{"en":"A family tree can act like a road map of relationships across generations.","zh":"族譜可以像一幅跨世代關係地圖。"},{"en":"If a painting is a spiritual road map, it guides memory rather than only physical travel.","zh":"如果畫作是精神地圖，它引導記憶，而不只是實際旅行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a map of belief and identity.","zh":"這個片語描述信仰和身份的地圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be organised as a cooperative","meaning":"以合作社形式運作","examples":[{"en":"Many Aboriginal art communities are organised as cooperatives.","zh":"許多澳洲原住民藝術社群以合作社形式運作。"},{"en":"To be organised as a cooperative means to operate as a group whose members share control and benefits.","zh":"be organised as a cooperative 指以成員共享控制權和利益的群體形式運作。"},{"en":"Farmers may be organised as a cooperative so they can sell crops together.","zh":"農民可能以合作社形式運作，方便一起出售作物。"},{"en":"If artists work through a cooperative, sales income can be managed more fairly.","zh":"如果藝術家透過合作社工作，銷售收入可以更公平管理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shared business or community structure.","zh":"這個片語描述共享式商業或社群結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"draw on the services of","meaning":"使用……提供的服務","examples":[{"en":"Each cooperative draws on the services of an art adviser.","zh":"每個合作社都使用藝術顧問提供的服務。"},{"en":"To draw on the services of someone means to use their help, skills or professional support.","zh":"draw on the services of someone 指使用某人的幫助、技能或專業支援。"},{"en":"A school may draw on the services of a counsellor during exam season.","zh":"學校可能在考試季使用輔導員提供的服務。"},{"en":"If artists draw on an adviser’s services, they can handle contracts and galleries more easily.","zh":"如果藝術家使用顧問服務，他們可以更容易處理合約和畫廊事務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using available expert support.","zh":"這個片語描述使用可用的專家支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"art adviser","meaning":"藝術顧問","examples":[{"en":"An art adviser helps artists deal with galleries and museums.","zh":"藝術顧問幫助藝術家與畫廊和博物館接洽。"},{"en":"An art adviser is a professional who supports artists with materials, sales, exhibitions and negotiations.","zh":"art adviser 是在材料、銷售、展覽和談判方面支援藝術家的專業人士。"},{"en":"A young painter may ask an art adviser how to price a first exhibition.","zh":"年輕畫家可能詢問藝術顧問如何為首次展覽定價。"},{"en":"If artists live far from art markets, advisers can connect them with buyers.","zh":"如果藝術家住得遠離藝術市場，顧問可以把他們與買家連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a practical helper in the art world.","zh":"這個片語指藝術世界中的實務協助者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"government-employed agent","meaning":"政府聘用的代理人","examples":[{"en":"The art adviser is a government-employed agent.","zh":"藝術顧問是政府聘用的代理人。"},{"en":"A government-employed agent is someone hired by the government to act on behalf of a programme or community.","zh":"government-employed agent 是由政府聘請，代表某計劃或社群行事的人。"},{"en":"A government-employed agent may help farmers apply for rural support funding.","zh":"政府聘用的代理人可能幫助農民申請鄉郊支援資金。"},{"en":"If an agent is paid by the government, they may have official duties and reporting responsibilities.","zh":"如果代理人由政府支付薪酬，他可能有官方職責和匯報責任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a representative employed by public authorities.","zh":"這個片語描述由公共當局聘用的代表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"provide someone with materials","meaning":"為某人提供材料","examples":[{"en":"The adviser provides the artists with materials.","zh":"顧問為藝術家提供材料。"},{"en":"To provide someone with materials means to give them the tools or supplies they need to work.","zh":"provide someone with materials 指給某人工具或物資，使其能工作。"},{"en":"A school provides students with paper, books and laboratory equipment.","zh":"學校為學生提供紙張、書本和實驗室設備。"},{"en":"If artists receive good materials, they can create works that last and can be displayed.","zh":"如果藝術家得到優良材料，他們可以創作能保存和展示的作品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes supplying practical resources.","zh":"這個片語描述供應實用資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"deal with galleries and museums","meaning":"與畫廊及博物館接洽","examples":[{"en":"The adviser deals with galleries and museums on the artists’ behalf.","zh":"顧問代表藝術家與畫廊及博物館接洽。"},{"en":"To deal with galleries and museums means to communicate, negotiate or make arrangements with them.","zh":"deal with galleries and museums 指與它們溝通、談判或作安排。"},{"en":"A musician’s manager may deal with concert halls so the performer can focus on practice.","zh":"音樂人的經理可能與音樂廳接洽，讓表演者專注練習。"},{"en":"If advisers handle galleries, artists may avoid unfair contracts or confusing paperwork.","zh":"如果顧問處理畫廊事務，藝術家可能避免不公平合約或混亂文件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes managing professional relationships with art institutions.","zh":"這個片語描述管理與藝術機構的專業關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"redistribute the proceeds","meaning":"重新分配收益","examples":[{"en":"The cooperative redistributes the proceeds from sales among the artists.","zh":"合作社把銷售收益重新分配給藝術家。"},{"en":"To redistribute the proceeds means to share out the money received from sales again according to a system.","zh":"redistribute the proceeds 指按照某制度重新分享銷售所得金錢。"},{"en":"A class charity stall may redistribute the proceeds to several community groups.","zh":"班級慈善攤位可能把收益重新分配給幾個社區團體。"},{"en":"If sales income is redistributed fairly, more members benefit from the project.","zh":"如果銷售收入被公平重新分配，更多成員可從項目受益。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sharing money after it has been collected.","zh":"這個片語描述收集金錢後再作分配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"proceeds from sales","meaning":"銷售收益","examples":[{"en":"The proceeds from sales are shared among the artists.","zh":"銷售收益由藝術家共同分享。"},{"en":"Proceeds from sales are the money received after selling products or artworks.","zh":"proceeds from sales 是出售產品或藝術品後收到的金錢。"},{"en":"A school fair may donate the proceeds from sales to a children’s charity.","zh":"學校市集可能把銷售收益捐給兒童慈善機構。"},{"en":"If proceeds are shared transparently, trust among members can increase.","zh":"如果收益分配透明，成員之間的信任可以增加。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to income gained through selling.","zh":"這個片語指透過銷售獲得的收入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"become a great success","meaning":"取得巨大成功","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal painting has become a great international success.","zh":"澳洲原住民繪畫已取得巨大國際成功。"},{"en":"To become a great success means to achieve strong recognition, popularity or results.","zh":"become a great success 指獲得強烈認可、受歡迎程度或成果。"},{"en":"A small student performance can become a great success if the audience responds warmly.","zh":"如果觀眾反應熱烈，小型學生表演也可以取得巨大成功。"},{"en":"If an art form becomes successful internationally, it may attract collectors and museums.","zh":"如果藝術形式在國際上成功，它可能吸引收藏家和博物館。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major positive achievement.","zh":"這個片語描述重大正面成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sell for more than","meaning":"售價超過……","examples":[{"en":"Some Aboriginal artworks sell for more than $25,000.","zh":"一些澳洲原住民藝術品售價超過25,000美元。"},{"en":"To sell for more than an amount means to be bought at a price higher than that amount.","zh":"sell for more than an amount 指以高於某金額的價格售出。"},{"en":"A rare comic book may sell for more than a new laptop.","zh":"一本稀有漫畫書售價可能超過一部新手提電腦。"},{"en":"If artworks sell for high prices, artists may gain income but market pressure may also rise.","zh":"如果藝術品以高價售出，藝術家可能獲得收入，但市場壓力也可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a selling price above a stated level.","zh":"這個片語給出高於某水平的售價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"exceptional items","meaning":"特別出色的作品","examples":[{"en":"Exceptional items may command extremely high prices.","zh":"特別出色的作品可能叫價極高。"},{"en":"Exceptional items are unusually good, rare or valuable pieces.","zh":"exceptional items 是異常優秀、稀有或有價值的作品或物品。"},{"en":"A museum may protect exceptional items in special cases with controlled lighting.","zh":"博物館可能把特別出色的作品放在有控光的專櫃中保護。"},{"en":"If an item is exceptional, collectors may pay far more for it than for ordinary works.","zh":"如果作品非常出色，收藏家可能付出遠高於普通作品的價錢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes outstanding examples within a group.","zh":"這個片語描述同類中的傑出例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fetch as much as","meaning":"售得高達……","examples":[{"en":"Exceptional paintings may fetch as much as $180,000.","zh":"特別出色的畫作可能售得高達180,000美元。"},{"en":"To fetch as much as an amount means to sell for a price up to that amount.","zh":"fetch as much as an amount 指售價可高達某金額。"},{"en":"A signed first edition may fetch as much as several thousand dollars at auction.","zh":"簽名初版書在拍賣中可能售得高達數千美元。"},{"en":"If a painting fetches a very high price, demand and reputation are probably strong.","zh":"如果畫作售得非常高價，需求和聲譽很可能強勁。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for auction or art-market prices.","zh":"這個片語常用於拍賣或藝術市場價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"export paintings","meaning":"出口畫作","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal communities export paintings to Western museums.","zh":"澳洲原住民社群把畫作出口到西方博物館。"},{"en":"To export paintings means to send or sell artworks to other countries.","zh":"export paintings 指把藝術品送往或售往其他國家。"},{"en":"A local gallery may export paintings to an overseas art fair.","zh":"本地畫廊可能把畫作出口到海外藝術博覽會。"},{"en":"If communities export paintings, their art can travel while their cultural stories remain rooted in land.","zh":"如果社群出口畫作，其藝術可以遠行，而文化故事仍扎根土地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes international movement of artworks.","zh":"這個片語描述藝術品的國際流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as though","meaning":"彷彿；好像","examples":[{"en":"The paintings are exported as though they were surfaces of Aboriginal territory.","zh":"這些畫作被出口，彷彿它們是澳洲原住民領土的表面。"},{"en":"As though means as if something were true or seemed true.","zh":"as though 指好像某事是真的或看似如此。"},{"en":"A student looked at the old letter as though it were a treasure.","zh":"學生看着那封舊信，彷彿它是一件寶物。"},{"en":"If paintings are treated as territory, they carry symbolic land meaning beyond the canvas.","zh":"如果畫作被視為領土，它們就承載超越畫布的象徵土地意義。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an imaginative comparison.","zh":"這個片語引入想像式比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"accompany something to","meaning":"陪同……前往","examples":[{"en":"The artists accompany their works to major Western art institutions.","zh":"藝術家陪同其作品前往主要西方藝術機構。"},{"en":"To accompany something to a place means to go with it there.","zh":"accompany something to a place 指與某物一起前往某地。"},{"en":"A teacher may accompany students to a museum during a school trip.","zh":"老師可能在學校旅行中陪同學生前往博物館。"},{"en":"If artists accompany their works, they can explain the cultural meaning directly.","zh":"如果藝術家陪同作品前往，他們可以直接解釋文化意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes travelling together with someone or something.","zh":"這個片語描述與某人或某物一同前往。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"temples of Western art","meaning":"西方藝術殿堂","examples":[{"en":"The phrase “temples of Western art” refers to prestigious Western museums.","zh":"“temples of Western art” 這個片語指享有盛名的西方博物館。"},{"en":"Temples of Western art is a metaphor for highly respected museums and galleries in Western countries.","zh":"temples of Western art 是比喻，指西方國家中備受尊敬的博物館和畫廊。"},{"en":"A famous museum may feel like a temple of art because visitors treat it with great respect.","zh":"著名博物館可能像藝術殿堂，因為訪客以極大尊重對待它。"},{"en":"If Aboriginal works enter these institutions, they gain visibility within powerful art systems.","zh":"如果澳洲原住民作品進入這些機構，它們就在強大藝術體系中獲得能見度。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests cultural authority and prestige.","zh":"這個片語暗示文化權威和聲望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"redraw the map of","meaning":"重新繪畫……的地圖","examples":[{"en":"Through their paintings, Aboriginal artists have symbolically redrawn the map of their country.","zh":"澳洲原住民藝術家透過畫作象徵性地重新繪畫其國家的地圖。"},{"en":"To redraw the map of something means to change how people understand its spaces, boundaries or meanings.","zh":"redraw the map of something 指改變人們理解其空間、邊界或意義的方式。"},{"en":"A new railway line can redraw the map of a city by changing where people live and work.","zh":"新鐵路線可以透過改變人們居住和工作的地方，重新繪畫城市地圖。"},{"en":"If artists redraw a map symbolically, they challenge older ways of seeing land.","zh":"如果藝術家象徵性地重繪地圖，他們就是挑戰舊有觀看土地的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal or metaphorical.","zh":"這個片語可作字面或比喻使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be exiled into","meaning":"被放逐到……","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal communities were exiled into remote parts of their own country.","zh":"澳洲原住民社群被放逐到自己國家的偏遠地區。"},{"en":"To be exiled into a place means to be forced to live away from one’s rightful home or centre of life.","zh":"be exiled into a place 指被迫遠離自己正當家園或生活中心而居住。"},{"en":"A political prisoner may be exiled into a distant region to silence their influence.","zh":"政治犯可能被放逐到偏遠地區，以壓制其影響力。"},{"en":"If people are exiled within their own country, the injustice can feel especially bitter.","zh":"如果人們在自己國家內被放逐，這種不公會尤其令人痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes forced displacement and exclusion.","zh":"這個片語描述強迫遷離和排斥。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"masterpieces","meaning":"傑作","examples":[{"en":"Many outstanding Aboriginal paintings are regarded as masterpieces.","zh":"許多出色的澳洲原住民畫作被視為傑作。"},{"en":"Masterpieces are works of art that are considered extremely skilful, beautiful or important.","zh":"masterpieces 是被認為技巧極高、美麗或重要的藝術作品。"},{"en":"A composer’s best symphony may be called a masterpiece.","zh":"作曲家最好的交響曲可能被稱為傑作。"},{"en":"If a painting becomes a masterpiece, it may influence artists and museums for many years.","zh":"如果畫作成為傑作，它可能多年來影響藝術家和博物館。"},{"en":"This word describes works of exceptional artistic value.","zh":"這個詞描述具有非凡藝術價值的作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"undeniable power","meaning":"無可否認的力量","examples":[{"en":"The paintings possess undeniable emotional and cultural power.","zh":"這些畫作具有無可否認的情感和文化力量。"},{"en":"Undeniable power means a force or impact so strong that people cannot reasonably ignore it.","zh":"undeniable power 指強烈到人們不能合理忽視的力量或影響。"},{"en":"A personal speech about hardship may have undeniable power because it feels honest.","zh":"關於困境的個人演講可能因真誠而具有無可否認的力量。"},{"en":"If a painting has undeniable power, viewers may feel moved even before understanding all the symbols.","zh":"如果畫作有無可否認的力量，觀眾即使未完全理解符號，也可能受到感動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very strong effect or influence.","zh":"這個片語描述非常強大的效果或影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"prompt a dialogue","meaning":"促成對話","examples":[{"en":"The power of the paintings prompts a dialogue between cultures.","zh":"這些畫作的力量促成文化之間的對話。"},{"en":"To prompt a dialogue means to encourage people to begin a serious exchange of ideas.","zh":"prompt a dialogue 指鼓勵人們開始認真的思想交流。"},{"en":"A film about poverty can prompt a dialogue between students, teachers and social workers.","zh":"關於貧窮的電影可以促成學生、老師和社工之間的對話。"},{"en":"If art prompts dialogue, viewers may ask questions rather than simply consume it.","zh":"如果藝術促成對話，觀眾可能會提問，而不只是消費它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that opens discussion.","zh":"這個片語描述某事開啟討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"prove all too rare","meaning":"一直極為罕見","examples":[{"en":"Meaningful dialogue between the two cultures has proved all too rare.","zh":"兩種文化之間有意義的對話一直極為罕見。"},{"en":"To prove all too rare means to turn out to be sadly uncommon.","zh":"prove all too rare 指結果是令人遺憾地很少見。"},{"en":"Honest feedback can prove all too rare in workplaces where everyone fears conflict.","zh":"在人人害怕衝突的工作場所，真誠回饋可能一直極為罕見。"},{"en":"If dialogue is too rare, misunderstanding may continue for generations.","zh":"如果對話太罕見，誤解可能延續幾代。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses regret that something important happens too little.","zh":"這個片語表達對重要事情太少發生的遺憾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the history of contact between","meaning":"……之間的接觸歷史","examples":[{"en":"The history of contact between Aboriginal and European cultures was often destructive.","zh":"澳洲原住民文化與歐洲文化之間的接觸歷史常常具破壞性。"},{"en":"The history of contact between two groups is the record of how they met, interacted and affected each other over time.","zh":"history of contact between two groups 是兩個群體如何相遇、互動並隨時間互相影響的記錄。"},{"en":"A textbook may examine the history of contact between traders and local communities.","zh":"教科書可能研究商人與本地社群之間的接觸歷史。"},{"en":"If contact involves violence and unequal power, its history may be painful.","zh":"如果接觸涉及暴力和不平等權力，其歷史可能令人痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on long-term relationships between cultures or peoples.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於文化或民族之間的長期關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"choose the most suitable heading","meaning":"選出最合適的標題","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the most suitable heading for each paragraph.","zh":"考生為每一段選出最合適的標題。"},{"en":"To choose the most suitable heading means to select the title that best matches a paragraph’s main idea.","zh":"choose the most suitable heading 指選擇最符合段落主旨的標題。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should read the whole paragraph before choosing a heading.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先讀完整段再選標題。"},{"en":"If a heading matches only one small detail, it may not be the most suitable one.","zh":"如果標題只符合一個小細節，它未必是最合適的。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in paragraph-matching tasks.","zh":"這個片語常見於段落配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The list of headings contains possible summaries of the paragraphs.","zh":"標題列表包含段落的可能摘要。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a set of title options for matching with paragraphs.","zh":"list of headings 是一組用來與段落配對的標題選項。"},{"en":"Students may cross out headings that clearly do not match the passage.","zh":"學生可能刪去明顯不符合文章的標題。"},{"en":"If there are more headings than paragraphs, some options will not be used.","zh":"如果標題多於段落，有些選項不會被使用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the answer choices in a reading task.","zh":"這個片語指閱讀題中的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"amazing results from a project","meaning":"一個項目的驚人成果","examples":[{"en":"Bardon was astounded by the amazing results from the school art project.","zh":"Bardon 對學校藝術項目的驚人成果感到非常驚訝。"},{"en":"Amazing results from a project are unexpectedly impressive outcomes produced by an organised activity.","zh":"amazing results from a project 是有組織活動產生的出乎意料而令人印象深刻的成果。"},{"en":"A simple reading club may produce amazing results if shy students begin speaking confidently.","zh":"如果害羞學生開始自信發言，一個簡單閱讀會可能產生驚人成果。"},{"en":"If a project gives people the right tools, hidden talent may become visible.","zh":"如果項目給人們合適工具，隱藏才能可能變得可見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes surprising success from a planned activity.","zh":"這個片語描述計劃活動帶來的意外成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"religious ceremonies","meaning":"宗教儀式","examples":[{"en":"Religious ceremonies help perpetuate the Dreaming.","zh":"宗教儀式有助延續「夢創時代」。"},{"en":"Religious ceremonies are formal sacred practices carried out according to belief or tradition.","zh":"religious ceremonies 是根據信仰或傳統進行的正式神聖做法。"},{"en":"A community may hold religious ceremonies to mark birth, marriage, death or seasonal change.","zh":"社群可能舉行宗教儀式，以標示出生、婚姻、死亡或季節變化。"},{"en":"If ceremonies are repeated, stories and laws can remain alive in people’s lives.","zh":"如果儀式被重複進行，故事和法律可以在人們生活中保持活力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ritual practices that preserve belief.","zh":"這個片語描述保存信仰的儀式做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"community art centres","meaning":"社區藝術中心","examples":[{"en":"Community art centres help artists produce and market their work.","zh":"社區藝術中心幫助藝術家創作和推廣作品。"},{"en":"Community art centres are local organisations that support artists with materials, advice, space and sales.","zh":"community art centres 是以材料、建議、空間和銷售支援藝術家的本地組織。"},{"en":"A community art centre may run workshops for young people after school.","zh":"社區藝術中心可能為年輕人開辦課後工作坊。"},{"en":"If artists have access to art centres, they can create work and reach buyers more easily.","zh":"如果藝術家能使用藝術中心，他們可以更容易創作作品並接觸買家。"},{"en":"This phrase describes local support structures for creative work.","zh":"這個片語描述支持創意工作的本地結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"early painting techniques","meaning":"早期繪畫技巧","examples":[{"en":"Early painting techniques included ground, rock and bark painting.","zh":"早期繪畫技巧包括地面畫、岩畫和樹皮畫。"},{"en":"Early painting techniques are older methods people used to create images before later materials became common.","zh":"early painting techniques 是後來材料普及前，人們用來創作圖像的較古老方法。"},{"en":"Children may learn early painting techniques by using natural pigments and simple brushes.","zh":"孩子可能透過使用天然顏料和簡單畫筆學習早期繪畫技巧。"},{"en":"If early techniques used temporary surfaces, many works may not survive physically.","zh":"如果早期技巧使用臨時表面，許多作品可能不能實體保存。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to older methods of making art.","zh":"這個片語指較古老的藝術創作方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"marketing systems","meaning":"市場推廣制度","examples":[{"en":"Churches helped develop early marketing systems for Aboriginal art.","zh":"教會幫助發展澳洲原住民藝術的早期市場推廣制度。"},{"en":"Marketing systems are organised ways of promoting, selling and distributing products or artworks.","zh":"marketing systems 是推廣、銷售和分發產品或藝術品的有組織方法。"},{"en":"A small farm may use a farmers’ market as part of its marketing system.","zh":"小農場可能把農墟作為市場推廣制度的一部分。"},{"en":"If artists lack marketing systems, their work may not reach buyers even if it is excellent.","zh":"如果藝術家缺乏市場推廣制度，即使作品出色也可能接觸不到買家。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the structure behind selling and promotion.","zh":"這個片語描述銷售和推廣背後的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"mythology and history combined","meaning":"神話與歷史的結合","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal art combines mythology and history.","zh":"澳洲原住民藝術結合神話與歷史。"},{"en":"Mythology and history combined means traditional sacred stories and real historical experience are joined together.","zh":"mythology and history combined 指傳統神聖故事與真實歷史經驗結合在一起。"},{"en":"A festival may combine mythology and history when it celebrates both a legend and a real migration.","zh":"當節日同時慶祝傳說和真實遷徙時，它可能結合神話與歷史。"},{"en":"If art combines both, viewers must understand story, belief and historical suffering together.","zh":"如果藝術結合兩者，觀眾就必須一起理解故事、信仰和歷史苦難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mix of sacred narrative and lived past.","zh":"這個片語描述神聖敘事與實際過去的混合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"increasing acclaim","meaning":"日益提高的讚譽","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes the increasing acclaim for Aboriginal art.","zh":"文章描述澳洲原住民藝術日益提高的讚譽。"},{"en":"Increasing acclaim means growing praise, recognition or respect.","zh":"increasing acclaim 指不斷增加的稱讚、認可或尊重。"},{"en":"A young writer may receive increasing acclaim after winning several prizes.","zh":"年輕作家在贏得幾個獎項後，可能獲得日益提高的讚譽。"},{"en":"If an art form gains increasing acclaim, museums may collect it more actively.","zh":"如果藝術形式獲得越來越多讚譽，博物館可能更積極收藏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rising public or critical approval.","zh":"這個片語描述公眾或評論界認可上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"belief in continuity","meaning":"對延續性的信念","examples":[{"en":"The Dreaming reflects a belief in continuity across time.","zh":"「夢創時代」反映跨越時間的延續性信念。"},{"en":"Belief in continuity means the idea that something continues across past, present and future.","zh":"belief in continuity 指相信某事跨越過去、現在與未來而延續。"},{"en":"A family that keeps old recipes alive shows a belief in continuity between generations.","zh":"保留舊食譜的家庭展示了世代之間延續性的信念。"},{"en":"If a culture believes in continuity, old stories can guide present action.","zh":"如果文化相信延續性，古老故事可以指導當下行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes faith in lasting connection.","zh":"這個片語描述對持久連繫的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"oppression of a minority people","meaning":"對少數族群的壓迫","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes the oppression of a minority people.","zh":"文章描述對少數族群的壓迫。"},{"en":"Oppression of a minority people means unfair and harmful control over a smaller or less powerful group.","zh":"oppression of a minority people 指對人數較少或權力較弱群體的不公平、有害控制。"},{"en":"A minority group may face oppression if its language is banned and its land is taken.","zh":"如果少數族群的語言被禁止且土地被奪走，它可能面對壓迫。"},{"en":"If oppression continues for generations, education, health and identity may suffer.","zh":"如果壓迫持續幾代，教育、健康和身份都可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes systematic injustice against a vulnerable group.","zh":"這個片語描述對弱勢群體的系統性不公。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"complete the flow chart","meaning":"完成流程圖","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the flow chart with words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用篇章中的字詞完成流程圖。"},{"en":"To complete the flow chart means to fill missing information into a diagram showing steps or development.","zh":"complete the flow chart 指把缺失資訊填入展示步驟或發展的圖表中。"},{"en":"In science class, students may complete a flow chart showing how rain forms.","zh":"在科學課中，學生可能完成展示雨水如何形成的流程圖。"},{"en":"If the flow chart follows time order, students should look for sequence words in the text.","zh":"如果流程圖按時間順序排列，學生應在文本中尋找表示先後的字詞。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction for process or history tasks.","zh":"這個片語是過程或歷史題常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than three words.","zh":"每個答案應不多於三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must use one, two or three words only.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案只可使用一個、兩個或三個英文詞。"},{"en":"If the correct phrase is “tree bark”, students should not add extra words.","zh":"如果正確片語是 “tree bark”，學生不應加入額外字詞。"},{"en":"If a student writes four words, the answer may be marked wrong even if the idea is close.","zh":"如果學生寫四個詞，即使意思接近，也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit in an exam.","zh":"這個片語給出考試中的嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"ground and rock paintings","meaning":"地面畫與岩畫","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal people produced ground and rock paintings for thousands of years.","zh":"澳洲原住民數千年來創作地面畫與岩畫。"},{"en":"Ground and rock paintings are artworks made on earth surfaces and natural rock surfaces.","zh":"ground and rock paintings 是在土地表面和天然岩石表面創作的藝術品。"},{"en":"Students may compare ground paintings with murals to understand different painting surfaces.","zh":"學生可能把地面畫與壁畫比較，以理解不同繪畫表面。"},{"en":"If paintings are made on the ground, they may disappear faster than those on rock.","zh":"如果畫作在地面創作，它們可能比岩畫更快消失。"},{"en":"This phrase names two early forms of visual art.","zh":"這個片語指出兩種早期視覺藝術形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"promote the use of","meaning":"推廣使用……","examples":[{"en":"Churches promoted the use of tree bark for paintings.","zh":"教會推廣使用樹皮作畫。"},{"en":"To promote the use of something means to encourage people to use it more.","zh":"promote the use of something 指鼓勵人們更多使用某物。"},{"en":"Schools may promote the use of reusable bottles to reduce plastic waste.","zh":"學校可能推廣使用可重用水樽，以減少塑膠廢物。"},{"en":"If an organisation promotes a material, artists may adopt it more widely.","zh":"如果組織推廣某材料，藝術家可能更廣泛採用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes encouraging wider adoption.","zh":"這個片語描述鼓勵更廣泛採用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in overseas museums","meaning":"在海外博物館","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal paintings appeared in overseas museums during the mid-twentieth century.","zh":"澳洲原住民畫作在二十世紀中期出現在海外博物館。"},{"en":"In overseas museums means in museums located in foreign countries.","zh":"in overseas museums 指在位於外國的博物館中。"},{"en":"A local artist may feel proud when their work appears in overseas museums.","zh":"當本地藝術家的作品出現在海外博物館時，他可能感到自豪。"},{"en":"If artworks enter overseas museums, they become part of international cultural discussion.","zh":"如果藝術品進入海外博物館，它們就成為國際文化討論的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes display or collection outside the home country.","zh":"這個片語描述在本國以外展示或收藏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"traditional patterns","meaning":"傳統圖案","examples":[{"en":"The artists painted traditional patterns on the school walls.","zh":"藝術家在學校牆壁上畫上傳統圖案。"},{"en":"Traditional patterns are designs passed down through culture, ceremony or community memory.","zh":"traditional patterns 是透過文化、儀式或社群記憶傳承下來的設計。"},{"en":"A grandmother may sew traditional patterns onto festival clothing.","zh":"祖母可能把傳統圖案縫在節日服裝上。"},{"en":"If traditional patterns are painted in schools, young people can learn their meanings visually.","zh":"如果傳統圖案被畫在學校中，年輕人可以透過視覺學習其意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated cultural designs.","zh":"這個片語描述重複出現的文化設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"an important feature of","meaning":"……的一個重要特點","examples":[{"en":"Community significance is an important feature of Aboriginal art.","zh":"社群意義是澳洲原住民藝術的一個重要特點。"},{"en":"An important feature of something is a key characteristic that helps define it.","zh":"important feature of something 是幫助定義某事的關鍵特徵。"},{"en":"Clear organisation is an important feature of a strong essay.","zh":"清晰組織是優秀文章的一個重要特點。"},{"en":"If community meaning is an important feature, art cannot be judged only as personal decoration.","zh":"如果社群意義是重要特點，藝術就不能只被視為個人裝飾。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a major characteristic.","zh":"這個片語指出主要特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"historical context","meaning":"歷史背景","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal paintings cannot be fully understood without their historical context.","zh":"沒有歷史背景，就不能充分理解澳洲原住民畫作。"},{"en":"Historical context is the background of past events, social conditions and power relations surrounding something.","zh":"historical context 是圍繞某事的過去事件、社會狀況和權力關係背景。"},{"en":"A speech may sound very different once students learn its historical context.","zh":"當學生了解演講的歷史背景後，它聽起來可能很不同。"},{"en":"If viewers ignore historical context, they may misunderstand why an artwork matters.","zh":"如果觀眾忽略歷史背景，可能誤解藝術品為何重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the past circumstances needed for interpretation.","zh":"這個片語描述詮釋所需的過去情境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"significance to the group","meaning":"對所屬群體的重要性","examples":[{"en":"Each work has deep significance to the community that owns its Dreaming story.","zh":"每件作品對擁有其「夢創時代」故事的社群都有深厚重要性。"},{"en":"Significance to the group means importance for the people who share or protect it.","zh":"significance to the group 指對共同擁有或守護某事的人具有重要意義。"},{"en":"A school song may have significance to alumni because it reminds them of shared memories.","zh":"校歌可能對校友有重要性，因為它喚起共同記憶。"},{"en":"If an artwork has group significance, outsiders should treat it with care and respect.","zh":"如果藝術品對群體有重要意義，外人應謹慎和尊重地對待它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaning held by a community.","zh":"這個片語描述由社群持有的意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"religious content","meaning":"宗教內容","examples":[{"en":"Many Aboriginal paintings contain religious content.","zh":"許多澳洲原住民畫作含有宗教內容。"},{"en":"Religious content means ideas, symbols or stories connected with belief, worship or sacred tradition.","zh":"religious content 指與信仰、崇拜或神聖傳統有關的想法、符號或故事。"},{"en":"A temple painting may contain religious content that explains a festival.","zh":"廟宇畫作可能含有解釋節日的宗教內容。"},{"en":"If art contains religious content, viewers may need cultural guidance to understand it properly.","zh":"如果藝術含有宗教內容，觀眾可能需要文化指引才能正確理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sacred meaning within a work.","zh":"這個片語描述作品中的神聖意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"message about the environment","meaning":"關於環境的信息","examples":[{"en":"Some artworks communicate a message about the environment and territory.","zh":"一些藝術品傳達關於環境和領土的信息。"},{"en":"A message about the environment is an idea or warning concerning land, nature or ecological relationships.","zh":"message about the environment 是關於土地、自然或生態關係的想法或警示。"},{"en":"A poster showing polluted rivers may carry a message about the environment.","zh":"展示受污染河流的海報可能帶有關於環境的信息。"},{"en":"If an artwork links land with identity, its environmental message may also be cultural.","zh":"如果藝術品把土地與身份連繫起來，其環境信息也可能是文化信息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaning related to nature and place.","zh":"這個片語描述與自然和地方相關的意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Aboriginal beliefs","meaning":"澳洲原住民信仰","examples":[{"en":"The question examines relationships within Aboriginal beliefs.","zh":"題目考查澳洲原住民信仰中的關係。"},{"en":"Aboriginal beliefs are Indigenous Australian understandings of ancestors, land, law, creation and spiritual life.","zh":"Aboriginal beliefs 是澳洲原住民對祖先、土地、法律、創世和精神生活的理解。"},{"en":"A classroom discussion of Aboriginal beliefs should be respectful and culturally careful.","zh":"課堂討論澳洲原住民信仰時應尊重且具文化敏感度。"},{"en":"If beliefs are tied to land, losing land can also threaten spiritual identity.","zh":"如果信仰與土地相連，失去土地也會威脅精神身份。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a complex system of Indigenous knowledge and faith.","zh":"這個片語指複雜的原住民知識和信仰系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a significant relationship between","meaning":"……之間的重要關係","examples":[{"en":"There is a significant relationship between Aboriginal ancestors and territory.","zh":"澳洲原住民祖先與領土之間有重要關係。"},{"en":"A significant relationship between two things is an important connection between them.","zh":"significant relationship between two things 指兩者之間有重要連繫。"},{"en":"Researchers may find a significant relationship between sleep and exam performance.","zh":"研究人員可能發現睡眠與考試表現之間有重要關係。"},{"en":"If ancestors and territory are strongly connected, land is not merely property.","zh":"如果祖先與領土有強烈連繫，土地就不只是財產。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a meaningful link.","zh":"這個片語描述有意義的關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"communities and lifestyles","meaning":"社群與生活方式","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to a relationship between communities and lifestyles.","zh":"該選項指社群與生活方式之間的關係。"},{"en":"Communities and lifestyles means social groups and the ways they live day to day.","zh":"communities and lifestyles 指社會群體及其日常生活方式。"},{"en":"Coastal communities and farming communities often have different lifestyles.","zh":"沿海社群和農業社群通常有不同生活方式。"},{"en":"If a community is moved, its lifestyle may change because work, food and social habits change.","zh":"如果社群被遷移，其生活方式可能因工作、食物和社交習慣改變而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase links people with their patterns of living.","zh":"這個片語把人群與生活模式連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"images and techniques","meaning":"圖像與技巧","examples":[{"en":"The option compares artistic images and techniques.","zh":"該選項比較藝術圖像與技巧。"},{"en":"Images and techniques means what artists show and the methods they use to create it.","zh":"images and techniques 指藝術家展示的內容，以及他們用來創作的方法。"},{"en":"A film class may compare images and techniques in old and modern movies.","zh":"電影課可能比較舊電影和現代電影的圖像與技巧。"},{"en":"If techniques change from sand to acrylic paint, images may travel more easily to galleries.","zh":"如果技巧從沙畫改為塑膠彩，圖像可能更容易進入畫廊。"},{"en":"This phrase connects visual content with artistic method.","zh":"這個片語把視覺內容與藝術方法連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"culture and form","meaning":"文化與形式","examples":[{"en":"The style of each painting connects culture and artistic form.","zh":"每幅畫的風格連接文化與藝術形式。"},{"en":"Culture and form means the relationship between cultural meaning and the visible shape or style of a work.","zh":"culture and form 指文化意義與作品可見形狀或風格之間的關係。"},{"en":"A poem’s culture and form may both appear in its language, rhythm and imagery.","zh":"詩歌的文化與形式可能同時出現在其語言、節奏和意象中。"},{"en":"If a painting’s form is rooted in culture, changing the form may also affect meaning.","zh":"如果畫作形式根源於文化，改變形式也可能影響意義。"},{"en":"This phrase links what a work means with how it is made.","zh":"這個片語把作品的意義與製作方式連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"ancestors and territory","meaning":"祖先與領土","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal beliefs closely connect ancestors and territory.","zh":"澳洲原住民信仰密切連接祖先與領土。"},{"en":"Ancestors and territory means forebears and the land connected with them.","zh":"ancestors and territory 指祖先以及與他們相連的土地。"},{"en":"A family graveyard can connect ancestors and territory in a village.","zh":"家族墓地可以在村莊中連接祖先與領土。"},{"en":"If ancestors marked out land in sacred stories, territory becomes part of identity.","zh":"如果祖先在神聖故事中劃定土地，領土就成為身份的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a relationship between people, memory and land.","zh":"這個片語描述人、記憶和土地之間的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"invite someone to engage with","meaning":"邀請某人認識並接觸……","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal art invites Western audiences to engage with Aboriginal culture.","zh":"澳洲原住民藝術邀請西方觀眾認識並接觸澳洲原住民文化。"},{"en":"To invite someone to engage with something means to encourage them to think about it, respond to it and understand it more deeply.","zh":"invite someone to engage with something 指鼓勵某人思考、回應並更深入理解某事。"},{"en":"A museum display can invite visitors to engage with history through objects and personal stories.","zh":"博物館展覽可以透過物件和個人故事邀請訪客接觸歷史。"},{"en":"If art invites engagement, viewers should not remain passive or superficial.","zh":"如果藝術邀請觀眾投入，觀眾就不應保持被動或表面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes encouraging serious contact and reflection.","zh":"這個片語描述鼓勵認真接觸和反思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"Western audiences","meaning":"西方觀眾","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal paintings have introduced Western audiences to Aboriginal culture.","zh":"澳洲原住民畫作向西方觀眾介紹澳洲原住民文化。"},{"en":"Western audiences are viewers or readers from Western countries or cultural backgrounds.","zh":"Western audiences 是來自西方國家或文化背景的觀眾或讀者。"},{"en":"A film festival may introduce Western audiences to stories from Asia, Africa or Oceania.","zh":"電影節可能向西方觀眾介紹來自亞洲、非洲或大洋洲的故事。"},{"en":"If Western audiences see Aboriginal works only as decoration, they may miss the historical meaning.","zh":"如果西方觀眾只把澳洲原住民作品視為裝飾，可能錯過歷史意義。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people receiving art from a Western cultural context.","zh":"這個片語指從西方文化背景接收藝術的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the Australian land","meaning":"澳洲土地","examples":[{"en":"Many paintings express a profound connection with the Australian land.","zh":"許多畫作表達與澳洲土地的深厚連繫。"},{"en":"The Australian land means the physical country, territory and landscapes of Australia.","zh":"Australian land 指澳洲的實體國土、領土和景觀。"},{"en":"Aboriginal stories often connect people with rivers, deserts, rocks and pathways in the Australian land.","zh":"澳洲原住民故事常把人與澳洲土地中的河流、沙漠、岩石和路徑連接起來。"},{"en":"If land is central to identity, painting it can become an act of cultural memory.","zh":"如果土地是身份核心，描繪它可以成為文化記憶的行動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to land as geography, home and cultural meaning.","zh":"這個片語指作為地理、家園和文化意義的土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"one’s own art","meaning":"自己的藝術","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that Westerners are encouraged to reconsider their own art.","zh":"該選項指出西方人被鼓勵重新思考自己的藝術。"},{"en":"One’s own art means the art belonging to one’s own culture, tradition or personal practice.","zh":"one’s own art 指屬於自己文化、傳統或個人實踐的藝術。"},{"en":"A painter may understand their own art better after seeing work from another culture.","zh":"畫家在觀看另一文化作品後，可能更理解自己的藝術。"},{"en":"If people compare traditions, they may notice limits in their own artistic assumptions.","zh":"如果人們比較傳統，可能注意到自己藝術假設中的限制。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to art connected with oneself or one’s society.","zh":"這個片語指與自己或自己社會相連的藝術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"Aboriginal culture","meaning":"澳洲原住民文化","examples":[{"en":"The paintings encourage a deeper engagement with Aboriginal culture.","zh":"這些畫作鼓勵人們更深入接觸澳洲原住民文化。"},{"en":"Aboriginal culture includes Indigenous Australian stories, land relationships, ceremonies, laws and artistic traditions.","zh":"Aboriginal culture 包括澳洲原住民故事、土地關係、儀式、法律和藝術傳統。"},{"en":"Students can engage with Aboriginal culture by learning from respectful sources and community voices.","zh":"學生可以透過尊重的資料來源和社群聲音認識澳洲原住民文化。"},{"en":"If people understand Aboriginal culture more deeply, they may see paintings as history and belief, not only design.","zh":"如果人們更深入理解澳洲原住民文化，他們可能把畫作視為歷史和信仰，而不只是設計。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a living culture with strong ties to land and memory.","zh":"這個片語指一種與土地和記憶有強烈連繫的活文化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"one’s own history","meaning":"自己的歷史","examples":[{"en":"Art can sometimes encourage viewers to reconsider their own history.","zh":"藝術有時可以鼓勵觀眾重新思考自己的歷史。"},{"en":"One’s own history means the past of oneself, one’s family, community or culture.","zh":"one’s own history 指自己、家庭、社群或文化的過去。"},{"en":"A family interview project can help students understand their own history.","zh":"家庭訪問項目可以幫助學生理解自己的歷史。"},{"en":"If viewers learn another people’s painful history, they may question what their own society remembers or forgets.","zh":"如果觀眾了解另一民族痛苦的歷史，他們可能質疑自己社會記住或遺忘了甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the past that shapes a person or group.","zh":"這個片語指塑造個人或群體的過去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 112 - Painters of time.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 113":[{"front":"the accidental rainforest","meaning":"意外形成的熱帶雨林","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains how an accidental rainforest developed on Ascension.","zh":"文章解釋阿森松島上一片意外形成的熱帶雨林如何發展。"},{"en":"The accidental rainforest is a forest that formed unintentionally, not through a planned natural process.","zh":"the accidental rainforest 指非有意形成、不是經由計劃中的自然過程形成的森林。"},{"en":"A park may become an accidental woodland if abandoned land is left untouched for many years.","zh":"如果棄置土地多年無人打理，公園可能變成意外形成的林地。"},{"en":"If many introduced plants grow together successfully, they may create an unexpected ecosystem.","zh":"如果許多引入植物成功一起生長，它們可能創造出意想不到的生態系統。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the forest was surprising and unplanned.","zh":"這個片語強調該森林令人意外，而且不是原本計劃好的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"according to ecological theory","meaning":"根據生態學理論","examples":[{"en":"According to ecological theory, rainforests develop over very long periods.","zh":"根據生態學理論，熱帶雨林會經歷非常漫長的時期發展。"},{"en":"According to ecological theory means based on accepted ideas about how ecosystems work.","zh":"according to ecological theory 指根據關於生態系統如何運作的公認觀點。"},{"en":"According to learning theory, students remember better when they use new words in real contexts.","zh":"根據學習理論，學生在真實語境中使用新詞時會記得更好。"},{"en":"If a real forest develops faster than theory predicts, scientists may need to rethink the theory.","zh":"如果真實森林的發展比理論預測快，科學家可能需要重新思考該理論。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an explanation from ecology.","zh":"這個片語引出生態學上的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be supposed to","meaning":"理應；被認為會……","examples":[{"en":"Rainforests are supposed to develop slowly over millions of years.","zh":"熱帶雨林被認為會經歷數百萬年緩慢發展。"},{"en":"Be supposed to means be expected or believed to do something.","zh":"be supposed to 指被期望或被認為會做某事。"},{"en":"Students are supposed to read the instructions before answering exam questions.","zh":"學生理應在回答考試題目前閱讀指示。"},{"en":"If something does not happen as it is supposed to, people may become surprised or doubtful.","zh":"如果某事沒有按理應的方式發生，人們可能會感到驚訝或懷疑。"},{"en":"The phrase often shows a contrast between expectation and reality.","zh":"這個片語常顯示期望與現實之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"develop slowly","meaning":"緩慢發展","examples":[{"en":"Complex rainforests are believed to develop slowly.","zh":"複雜的熱帶雨林被認為會緩慢發展。"},{"en":"Develop slowly means grow or change gradually over a long period.","zh":"develop slowly 指在很長時間內逐漸生長或改變。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may develop slowly through regular practice and encouragement.","zh":"學生的信心可能透過定期練習和鼓勵而緩慢發展。"},{"en":"If an ecosystem develops slowly, many relationships between species form over time.","zh":"如果生態系統緩慢發展，物種之間許多關係會隨時間形成。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts with sudden or rapid formation.","zh":"這個片語與突然或快速形成形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"over millions of years","meaning":"經歷數百萬年","examples":[{"en":"Ecologists once believed that rainforests formed over millions of years.","zh":"生態學家曾相信熱帶雨林經歷數百萬年形成。"},{"en":"Over millions of years means across an extremely long period of time.","zh":"over millions of years 指跨越極其漫長的時間。"},{"en":"Mountains can change shape over millions of years through erosion and movement.","zh":"山脈可以經歷數百萬年的侵蝕和移動而改變形狀。"},{"en":"If a forest is thought to form over millions of years, a fast-forming forest becomes surprising.","zh":"如果森林被認為要經歷數百萬年才形成，快速形成的森林就令人驚訝。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses very long geological or evolutionary time.","zh":"這個片語強調非常漫長的地質或演化時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be forced to reconsider","meaning":"被迫重新考慮","examples":[{"en":"Ecologists are being forced to reconsider their ideas.","zh":"生態學家正被迫重新考慮他們的觀點。"},{"en":"Be forced to reconsider means have to think again because new evidence challenges old beliefs.","zh":"be forced to reconsider 指因新證據挑戰舊信念而必須重新思考。"},{"en":"A teacher may be forced to reconsider a method if students still do not understand.","zh":"如果學生仍然不明白，老師可能被迫重新考慮某種教學方法。"},{"en":"If facts do not fit a theory, researchers must reconsider that theory.","zh":"如果事實不符合某理論，研究人員就必須重新考慮該理論。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests pressure from evidence or events.","zh":"這個片語暗示來自證據或事件的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"reconsider their ideas","meaning":"重新考慮他們的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The unusual forest has made scientists reconsider their ideas.","zh":"這片不尋常的森林令科學家重新考慮他們的觀點。"},{"en":"Reconsider their ideas means think again about whether their beliefs are correct.","zh":"reconsider their ideas 指重新思考自己的看法是否正確。"},{"en":"Students may reconsider their ideas after hearing a strong counterargument.","zh":"學生聽到有力反方論點後，可能會重新考慮自己的觀點。"},{"en":"If a small island creates a functioning forest quickly, ecologists may question older assumptions.","zh":"如果一個小島能快速形成有功能的森林，生態學家可能會質疑舊假設。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing one’s thinking after new information appears.","zh":"這個片語描述在新資訊出現後改變想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"stop off at","meaning":"途中短暫停留於……","examples":[{"en":"Peter Osbeck stopped off at Ascension on his journey home.","zh":"Peter Osbeck 在回家途中短暫停留於阿森松島。"},{"en":"Stop off at means make a short visit somewhere during a longer journey.","zh":"stop off at 指在較長旅程途中短暫到訪某地。"},{"en":"A family may stop off at a supermarket on the way home from school.","zh":"一家人可能在放學回家途中短暫停留於超級市場。"},{"en":"If a traveller stops off at an island, the visit may be brief but important.","zh":"如果旅客短暫停留於一個島嶼，訪問可能短暫但重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a short break in a journey.","zh":"這個片語描述旅程中的短暫停留。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mid-Atlantic island","meaning":"大西洋中部島嶼","examples":[{"en":"Ascension is a mid-Atlantic island.","zh":"阿森松島是一個大西洋中部島嶼。"},{"en":"A mid-Atlantic island is an island located in the central part of the Atlantic Ocean.","zh":"mid-Atlantic island 指位於大西洋中央部分的島嶼。"},{"en":"A remote mid-Atlantic island may be difficult to reach without ships or aircraft.","zh":"偏遠的大西洋中部島嶼若沒有船或飛機，可能難以到達。"},{"en":"If an island is isolated in the ocean, its plants and animals may develop unusual features.","zh":"如果島嶼在海洋中孤立，島上的動植物可能發展出不尋常特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase describes location in the middle Atlantic region.","zh":"這個片語描述位於大西洋中部的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on his way home from","meaning":"從……回家途中","examples":[{"en":"Osbeck visited Ascension on his way home from China.","zh":"Osbeck 從中國回家途中到訪阿森松島。"},{"en":"On his way home from means during the journey back from a place.","zh":"on his way home from 指從某地回家或回程途中。"},{"en":"A student may buy dinner on his way home from tutorial class.","zh":"學生可能從補習班回家途中買晚餐。"},{"en":"If a scientist visits a place on the way home, the stop may still produce useful observations.","zh":"如果科學家在回程途中到訪某地，該短暫停留仍可能產生有用觀察。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an action with a return journey.","zh":"這個片語把某行動與回程連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a heap of ruinous rocks","meaning":"一堆破敗的岩石","examples":[{"en":"Osbeck described the island as a heap of ruinous rocks.","zh":"Osbeck 把該島描述為一堆破敗的岩石。"},{"en":"A heap of ruinous rocks means a rough pile or mass of broken, barren rocks.","zh":"a heap of ruinous rocks 指一堆粗糙、破碎而荒涼的岩石。"},{"en":"An abandoned building site may look like a heap of ruinous rocks after demolition.","zh":"建築物拆卸後，廢棄工地可能看似一堆破敗的岩石。"},{"en":"If an island looks rocky and lifeless, early visitors may assume little can grow there.","zh":"如果島嶼看起來岩石遍布且毫無生氣，早期訪客可能以為那裡很少東西能生長。"},{"en":"The phrase creates an image of barrenness and decay.","zh":"這個片語營造荒涼和破敗的畫面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"bare, white mountain","meaning":"光禿禿的白色山峰","examples":[{"en":"A bare, white mountain stood in the middle of the island.","zh":"一座光禿禿的白色山峰矗立在島中央。"},{"en":"A bare, white mountain is a pale mountain with little or no vegetation.","zh":"bare, white mountain 指顏色偏白且幾乎沒有植被的山。"},{"en":"A hillside after a fire may look bare because plants have been burned away.","zh":"山坡經火災後可能變得光禿，因為植物被燒走。"},{"en":"If a mountain has no trees or soil cover, rain and wind can make it even more exposed.","zh":"如果山上沒有樹木或泥土覆蓋，雨和風會令它更加暴露。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a dry, empty-looking landscape.","zh":"這個片語描述乾燥、空蕩的景觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"all it boasted was","meaning":"它所擁有的只有……","examples":[{"en":"All the island boasted was a small number of plant species.","zh":"該島所擁有的只有少量植物物種。"},{"en":"All it boasted was means the only notable thing it had was something limited or unimpressive.","zh":"all it boasted was 指它唯一值得一提的只有某些有限或不太出色的東西。"},{"en":"The old classroom boasted only a broken fan and a few desks.","zh":"舊課室所擁有的只有一把壞風扇和幾張書桌。"},{"en":"If a place boasts only a few plants, it seems poor in natural resources.","zh":"如果一個地方只有少數植物，它看起來自然資源貧乏。"},{"en":"The phrase often carries a slightly ironic tone.","zh":"這個片語常帶有輕微諷刺語氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a couple of dozen species","meaning":"約二十多個物種","examples":[{"en":"The island contained only a couple of dozen species of plant.","zh":"該島只有約二十多種植物。"},{"en":"A couple of dozen species means about twenty to thirty different species.","zh":"a couple of dozen species 指約二十至三十個不同物種。"},{"en":"A small garden may contain a couple of dozen plant species if flowers, herbs, and shrubs are counted.","zh":"如果把花、香草和灌木都計算在內，小花園可能有二十多種植物。"},{"en":"If an island has only a couple of dozen species, its biodiversity is limited.","zh":"如果島上只有二十多個物種，其生物多樣性就有限。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate small number.","zh":"這個片語給出大約而偏少的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"species of plant","meaning":"植物物種","examples":[{"en":"Only a small number of plant species grew on the island.","zh":"島上只生長少量植物物種。"},{"en":"Species of plant are different kinds of plants with their own biological identity.","zh":"species of plant 指具有自己生物身份的不同植物種類。"},{"en":"A school garden may grow several species of plant, such as herbs, flowers, and vegetables.","zh":"學校花園可能種植幾種植物物種，例如香草、花和蔬菜。"},{"en":"If a place has few plant species, its ecosystem may be simple and fragile.","zh":"如果一個地方植物物種很少，其生態系統可能簡單而脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to types of plants, not individual plants.","zh":"這個片語指植物種類，而不是單一植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"unique to the island","meaning":"該島獨有的","examples":[{"en":"Some of the ferns were unique to the island.","zh":"有些蕨類植物是該島獨有的。"},{"en":"Unique to the island means found naturally only on that island and nowhere else.","zh":"unique to the island 指自然只在該島找到，而其他地方沒有。"},{"en":"A local festival may be unique to one village because no other community celebrates it.","zh":"某本地節日可能是某村獨有的，因為沒有其他社區慶祝它。"},{"en":"If a plant is unique to an island, losing it means losing a species from the whole world.","zh":"如果植物是某島獨有的，失去它就等於全世界失去該物種。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses special local existence.","zh":"這個片語強調特殊的本地存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"might have remained","meaning":"本來可能一直維持……","examples":[{"en":"The island might have remained bare without human intervention.","zh":"如果沒有人類干預，該島本來可能一直維持光禿狀態。"},{"en":"Might have remained means could have continued in the same condition if events had been different.","zh":"might have remained 指如果事情不同，某狀態本可能繼續存在。"},{"en":"A student might have remained confused if the teacher had not given examples.","zh":"如果老師沒有給例子，學生本來可能一直感到困惑。"},{"en":"If no one planted trees, the island may have stayed dry and rocky.","zh":"如果沒有人植樹，該島可能一直保持乾燥多石。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an unreal or possible past outcome.","zh":"這個片語描述與現實不同或可能發生的過去結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"plant collector","meaning":"植物採集家","examples":[{"en":"Joseph Hooker was a British plant collector.","zh":"Joseph Hooker 是一位英國植物採集家。"},{"en":"A plant collector is someone who gathers plant specimens for study, classification, or cultivation.","zh":"plant collector 指為研究、分類或栽培而收集植物標本的人。"},{"en":"A plant collector may travel to remote forests to find unusual flowers or seeds.","zh":"植物採集家可能前往偏遠森林尋找不尋常花卉或種子。"},{"en":"If collectors bring plants to new places, they can change local ecosystems.","zh":"如果採集者把植物帶到新地方，就可能改變本地生態系統。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a person involved in botanical exploration.","zh":"這個片語描述參與植物探索的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"made a brief call on","meaning":"短暫到訪……","examples":[{"en":"Joseph Hooker made a brief call on the island.","zh":"Joseph Hooker 短暫到訪該島。"},{"en":"Made a brief call on means paid a short visit to a place or person.","zh":"made a brief call on 指短暫拜訪某地方或某人。"},{"en":"A teacher may make a brief call on a student’s parents after class.","zh":"老師可能在課後短暫拜訪學生家長。"},{"en":"If a scientist makes a brief call on an island, even a short visit may lead to important ideas.","zh":"如果科學家短暫到訪一個島嶼，即使短暫訪問也可能帶來重要想法。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds formal and means visited briefly.","zh":"這個片語較正式，意思是短暫探訪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on his return from","meaning":"從……回程時","examples":[{"en":"Hooker visited Ascension on his return from Antarctica.","zh":"Hooker 從南極洲回程時到訪阿森松島。"},{"en":"On his return from means while travelling back after leaving a place.","zh":"on his return from 指離開某地後回程途中。"},{"en":"A student may buy stationery on his return from school.","zh":"學生可能從學校回程時買文具。"},{"en":"If a traveller stops somewhere on his return, the visit happens during the journey back.","zh":"如果旅客在回程中停留某地，該訪問就是在返回途中發生。"},{"en":"The phrase places an event in a return journey.","zh":"這個片語把事件放在回程旅程中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"surveying the bare earth","meaning":"察看光禿土地","examples":[{"en":"Surveying the bare earth, Hooker considered what had happened to the island.","zh":"Hooker 察看光禿土地時，思考該島曾經發生甚麼事。"},{"en":"Surveying the bare earth means looking carefully over land with little or no vegetation.","zh":"surveying the bare earth 指仔細察看幾乎沒有植被的土地。"},{"en":"A farmer may survey bare earth before deciding where to plant new crops.","zh":"農民可能先察看光禿土地，再決定在哪裡種植新作物。"},{"en":"If scientists survey damaged land, they may infer what caused the loss of vegetation.","zh":"如果科學家察看受損土地，可能推斷植被流失的原因。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful visual examination of exposed land.","zh":"這個片語描述對裸露土地的仔細視察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"concluded that","meaning":"得出結論認為","examples":[{"en":"Hooker concluded that the island had suffered a natural calamity.","zh":"Hooker 得出結論認為該島曾遭受自然災害。"},{"en":"Concluded that means decided something after thinking about evidence.","zh":"concluded that 指思考證據後判斷某事。"},{"en":"A doctor concluded that the patient needed rest after checking the symptoms.","zh":"醫生檢查症狀後得出結論認為病人需要休息。"},{"en":"If a researcher sees bare land and low rainfall, they may conclude that the environment has changed.","zh":"如果研究人員看見光禿土地和低降雨，可能得出結論認為環境已改變。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a judgement based on evidence.","zh":"這個片語引出基於證據的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"natural calamity","meaning":"自然災害","examples":[{"en":"Hooker believed that a natural calamity had damaged the island.","zh":"Hooker 相信一場自然災害破壞了該島。"},{"en":"A natural calamity is a serious disaster caused by nature, such as drought, storm, or volcanic activity.","zh":"natural calamity 指由自然造成的嚴重災難，例如乾旱、風暴或火山活動。"},{"en":"A village may need help after a natural calamity destroys homes and farmland.","zh":"如果自然災害摧毀房屋和農地，村莊可能需要援助。"},{"en":"If a calamity removes vegetation, soil and rainfall patterns may also change.","zh":"如果災害移除植被，土壤和降雨模式也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a destructive natural event.","zh":"這個片語描述具破壞性的自然事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"denude something of vegetation","meaning":"使……失去植被","examples":[{"en":"The calamity had denuded the island of vegetation.","zh":"該災害使島嶼失去植被。"},{"en":"Denude something of vegetation means strip plants away from a place until it becomes bare.","zh":"denude something of vegetation 指把某地植物剝除，使其變得光禿。"},{"en":"Construction work can denude a hillside of vegetation if trees and shrubs are removed.","zh":"如果樹木和灌木被移除，建築工程可以使山坡失去植被。"},{"en":"If land is denuded of vegetation, soil may dry out or wash away more easily.","zh":"如果土地失去植被，泥土可能更容易乾涸或被沖走。"},{"en":"The phrase describes severe loss of plant cover.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重植被流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"trigger a decline in","meaning":"引發……下降","examples":[{"en":"The loss of vegetation triggered a decline in rainfall.","zh":"植被流失引發降雨量下降。"},{"en":"Trigger a decline in means cause something to start decreasing.","zh":"trigger a decline in 指導致某事開始下降。"},{"en":"Poor service can trigger a decline in customer numbers.","zh":"差劣服務可以引發顧客人數下降。"},{"en":"If plants disappear, less moisture may return to the air, reducing rainfall.","zh":"如果植物消失，較少水分回到空氣中，降雨可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase connects one change with a downward trend.","zh":"這個片語把一項變化與下降趨勢連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a decline in rainfall","meaning":"降雨量下降","examples":[{"en":"Hooker believed that the island had experienced a decline in rainfall.","zh":"Hooker 相信該島曾經歷降雨量下降。"},{"en":"A decline in rainfall means less rain falling over time.","zh":"a decline in rainfall 指隨時間降雨減少。"},{"en":"Farmers may struggle when a decline in rainfall leaves fields dry.","zh":"當降雨量下降令田地乾涸，農民可能會陷入困境。"},{"en":"If rainfall declines, plants may die and the land may become more desert-like.","zh":"如果降雨減少，植物可能死亡，土地可能變得更像沙漠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a reduction in rain.","zh":"這個片語描述雨量減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"turn the place into a desert","meaning":"把該地變成沙漠","examples":[{"en":"Reduced rainfall was turning the place into a desert.","zh":"降雨減少正把該地變成沙漠。"},{"en":"Turn the place into a desert means make an area dry, barren, and unable to support much life.","zh":"turn the place into a desert 指使某地變得乾旱、荒蕪，難以支持大量生命。"},{"en":"Poor land management can turn farmland into a desert over many years.","zh":"不善土地管理可以在多年後把農田變成沙漠。"},{"en":"If rainfall falls and plants disappear, the land may become increasingly dry.","zh":"如果降雨下降而植物消失，土地可能變得越來越乾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious environmental degradation.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重環境退化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"maintain a garrison","meaning":"駐守一支部隊","examples":[{"en":"The British Navy maintained a garrison on the island.","zh":"英國海軍在島上駐守一支部隊。"},{"en":"Maintain a garrison means keep a military force stationed in a place.","zh":"maintain a garrison 指讓一支軍隊長期駐紮在某地。"},{"en":"A government may maintain a garrison at a remote border for security.","zh":"政府可能在偏遠邊境駐守部隊，以保障安全。"},{"en":"If soldiers live on an isolated island, they need water, food, and a stable environment.","zh":"如果士兵生活在孤島上，他們需要水、食物和穩定環境。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continuing military presence.","zh":"這個片語描述持續的軍事駐紮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be keen to improve","meaning":"渴望改善……","examples":[{"en":"The British Navy was keen to improve the island.","zh":"英國海軍渴望改善該島。"},{"en":"Be keen to improve means strongly want to make something better.","zh":"be keen to improve 指強烈希望令某事變得更好。"},{"en":"A school may be keen to improve reading results after weak exam performance.","zh":"學校在考試表現欠佳後，可能渴望改善閱讀成績。"},{"en":"If a place is dry and difficult to live on, officials may want to improve its environment.","zh":"如果某地乾旱且難以居住，官員可能想改善其環境。"},{"en":"The phrase shows active interest in making progress.","zh":"這個片語顯示對進步的積極興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ask someone’s advice","meaning":"徵詢某人的意見","examples":[{"en":"The Navy asked Hooker’s advice about restoring the island.","zh":"海軍就恢復該島徵詢 Hooker 的意見。"},{"en":"Ask someone’s advice means request someone’s opinion or guidance.","zh":"ask someone’s advice 指請求某人的意見或指導。"},{"en":"A student may ask a teacher’s advice before choosing subjects.","zh":"學生在選科前可能徵詢老師意見。"},{"en":"If officials lack scientific knowledge, they may ask an expert for advice.","zh":"如果官員缺乏科學知識，他們可能徵詢專家意見。"},{"en":"The phrase shows dependence on another person’s judgement.","zh":"這個片語顯示依靠他人的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ambitious scheme","meaning":"雄心勃勃的計劃","examples":[{"en":"Hooker proposed an ambitious scheme for planting trees.","zh":"Hooker 提出一項植樹的雄心勃勃計劃。"},{"en":"An ambitious scheme is a large and difficult plan that aims to achieve something important.","zh":"ambitious scheme 指一項大型而困難、旨在達成重要目標的計劃。"},{"en":"A city may launch an ambitious scheme to reduce traffic and air pollution.","zh":"城市可能推出一項雄心勃勃的計劃，以減少交通和空氣污染。"},{"en":"If a plan tries to change an island’s climate and vegetation, it is clearly ambitious.","zh":"如果計劃試圖改變島嶼氣候和植被，它顯然很有雄心。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests both scale and difficulty.","zh":"這個片語暗示規模和難度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"planting trees and shrubs","meaning":"種植樹木和灌木","examples":[{"en":"His scheme involved planting trees and shrubs across the island.","zh":"他的計劃涉及在全島種植樹木和灌木。"},{"en":"Planting trees and shrubs means putting young woody plants into the ground so they can grow.","zh":"planting trees and shrubs 指把年幼木本植物種進泥土中，使其生長。"},{"en":"A school may improve its playground by planting trees and shrubs for shade.","zh":"學校可能透過種植樹木和灌木為操場增加樹蔭。"},{"en":"If trees and shrubs spread, they can protect soil and provide habitat.","zh":"如果樹木和灌木擴散，就能保護土壤並提供棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical re-greening work.","zh":"這個片語描述實際的綠化工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"revive rainfall","meaning":"恢復降雨","examples":[{"en":"Hooker hoped that the trees would revive rainfall.","zh":"Hooker 希望樹木能恢復降雨。"},{"en":"Revive rainfall means help bring back more regular or higher levels of rain.","zh":"revive rainfall 指幫助恢復較規律或較高水平的降雨。"},{"en":"Farmers may hope that forest restoration will revive rainfall in dry areas.","zh":"農民可能希望森林恢復能令乾旱地區恢復降雨。"},{"en":"If vegetation increases moisture in the air, it may support local rainfall patterns.","zh":"如果植被增加空氣中的水分，就可能支持本地降雨模式。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests restoring rain that has declined.","zh":"這個片語暗示恢復已下降的雨量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"stimulate ecological recovery","meaning":"促進生態復原","examples":[{"en":"The new vegetation was intended to stimulate ecological recovery.","zh":"新植被旨在促進生態復原。"},{"en":"Stimulate ecological recovery means encourage a damaged ecosystem to become healthier again.","zh":"stimulate ecological recovery 指鼓勵受損生態系統重新變得健康。"},{"en":"Planting native trees can stimulate ecological recovery in a polluted park.","zh":"種植本土樹木可以促進受污染公園的生態復原。"},{"en":"If soil improves and insects return, wider recovery may follow.","zh":"如果土壤改善、昆蟲回來，更廣泛的復原可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes helping nature repair itself.","zh":"這個片語描述幫助大自然自我修復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"wider ecological recovery","meaning":"更廣泛的生態復原","examples":[{"en":"The planting scheme aimed to encourage a wider ecological recovery.","zh":"植樹計劃旨在鼓勵更廣泛的生態復原。"},{"en":"Wider ecological recovery means improvement across many parts of an ecosystem, not just one species.","zh":"wider ecological recovery 指生態系統許多部分改善，而不只是單一物種。"},{"en":"Cleaning a river can lead to wider ecological recovery if fish, insects, and plants return.","zh":"如果魚類、昆蟲和植物回歸，清理河流可以帶來更廣泛的生態復原。"},{"en":"If trees grow successfully, they may support birds, soil organisms, and rainfall patterns.","zh":"如果樹木成功生長，它們可能支持鳥類、土壤生物和降雨模式。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses broad ecosystem improvement.","zh":"這個片語強調廣泛的生態系統改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lacking anything else to do","meaning":"因為沒有其他事情可做","examples":[{"en":"The sailors may have joined the project because they lacked anything else to do.","zh":"水手可能因為沒有其他事情可做而參與該項目。"},{"en":"Lacking anything else to do means having no other useful or interesting activity available.","zh":"lacking anything else to do 指沒有其他有用或有趣的活動可做。"},{"en":"Students may clean the classroom after exams, lacking anything else to do before dismissal.","zh":"考試後、放學前沒有其他事情可做，學生可能清潔課室。"},{"en":"If people have free time and clear instructions, they may join a practical project.","zh":"如果人們有空閒時間和清楚指示，就可能加入實際項目。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests boredom or lack of alternatives.","zh":"這個片語暗示無聊或缺乏其他選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"set out with a will","meaning":"積極投入地開始工作","examples":[{"en":"The sailors set out with a will to plant the island.","zh":"水手積極投入地開始在島上植樹。"},{"en":"Set out with a will means begin a task energetically and with determination.","zh":"set out with a will 指充滿幹勁和決心地開始一項任務。"},{"en":"A class may set out with a will to clean the beach after seeing plastic waste.","zh":"一班學生看見塑膠垃圾後，可能積極投入地開始清潔海灘。"},{"en":"If people work with energy from the start, a difficult project can progress quickly.","zh":"如果人們一開始就充滿幹勁，困難項目也能快速推進。"},{"en":"The phrase describes enthusiastic effort.","zh":"這個片語描述熱心努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"naval transport ship","meaning":"海軍運輸船","examples":[{"en":"A naval transport ship carried seedlings from Argentina.","zh":"一艘海軍運輸船從阿根廷運送幼苗。"},{"en":"A naval transport ship is a military ship used to carry people, goods, or supplies.","zh":"naval transport ship 指用來運送人員、貨物或補給的軍用船隻。"},{"en":"During an emergency, a naval transport ship may deliver food and medicine to an island.","zh":"緊急情況下，海軍運輸船可能向島嶼運送食物和藥物。"},{"en":"If seedlings are moved by ship, they can reach remote places far from their origin.","zh":"如果幼苗由船運送，就能到達遠離原產地的偏遠地方。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a supply-carrying ship connected with the navy.","zh":"這個片語指與海軍有關的補給運輸船。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"deliver a batch of","meaning":"運送一批……","examples":[{"en":"The ship delivered a batch of seedlings in 1845.","zh":"該船在1845年運送一批幼苗。"},{"en":"Deliver a batch of means bring a group or quantity of items at one time.","zh":"deliver a batch of 指一次運送一組或一批物品。"},{"en":"A bakery may deliver a batch of bread to a school canteen every morning.","zh":"麵包店可能每天早上向學校飯堂運送一批麵包。"},{"en":"If a batch of seedlings survives, a planting project can begin on a larger scale.","zh":"如果一批幼苗能存活，植樹計劃就能更大規模地開始。"},{"en":"The phrase describes transporting a set of things together.","zh":"這個片語描述把一組東西一起運送。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"seedlings","meaning":"幼苗","examples":[{"en":"The first batch of seedlings arrived from Argentina.","zh":"第一批幼苗來自阿根廷。"},{"en":"Seedlings are young plants that have recently grown from seeds.","zh":"seedlings 指剛從種子長出的年幼植物。"},{"en":"Students may plant seedlings in small pots before moving them to a garden.","zh":"學生可能先把幼苗種在小盆中，再移到花園。"},{"en":"If seedlings receive enough water and sunlight, they can grow into strong plants.","zh":"如果幼苗得到足夠水和陽光，就能長成強壯植物。"},{"en":"The word refers to young plants, not seeds themselves.","zh":"這個詞指幼小植物，而不是種子本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the following years","meaning":"在其後數年","examples":[{"en":"More plant species arrived in the following years.","zh":"在其後數年，更多植物物種到達。"},{"en":"In the following years means during the years after the time just mentioned.","zh":"in the following years 指在剛才提及時間之後的幾年中。"},{"en":"A school may start one new programme, and in the following years add more clubs.","zh":"學校可能先開始一個新計劃，然後在其後數年增加更多學會。"},{"en":"If more plants arrive over several years, the ecosystem changes gradually.","zh":"如果更多植物在幾年間到達，生態系統就會逐漸改變。"},{"en":"The phrase shows events continuing after an initial stage.","zh":"這個片語顯示事件在初始階段後持續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"packets of seeds","meaning":"一包包種子","examples":[{"en":"England sent 700 packets of seeds to Ascension.","zh":"英格蘭向阿森松島寄出700包種子。"},{"en":"Packets of seeds are small packages containing seeds for planting.","zh":"packets of seeds 指裝有種子、供種植用的小包裝。"},{"en":"A family may buy packets of seeds to grow herbs on a balcony.","zh":"家庭可能購買一包包種子，在露台種植香草。"},{"en":"If many seed packets are planted, a bare area can quickly gain new vegetation.","zh":"如果大量種子包被種下，光禿地區可以很快出現新植被。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to packaged seeds ready for planting.","zh":"這個片語指已包裝好、可供種植的種子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"especially liked the place","meaning":"特別適應該地環境","examples":[{"en":"Bamboo and prickly pear especially liked the island’s conditions.","zh":"竹和梨果仙人掌特別適應該島環境。"},{"en":"Especially liked the place means grew particularly well in that environment.","zh":"especially liked the place 指在該環境中特別生長良好。"},{"en":"Some herbs especially like a sunny balcony with well-drained soil.","zh":"有些香草特別喜歡陽光充足、排水良好的露台。"},{"en":"If a plant likes a place, it may spread quickly and outcompete weaker plants.","zh":"如果植物適應某地，它可能快速擴散並勝過較弱植物。"},{"en":"The phrase personifies plants to show that conditions suit them.","zh":"這個片語把植物擬人化，以顯示環境適合牠們。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bamboo","meaning":"竹","examples":[{"en":"Bamboo was one of the species that grew successfully on Ascension.","zh":"竹是在阿森松島成功生長的物種之一。"},{"en":"Bamboo is a fast-growing woody grass often used for building, furniture, and food shoots.","zh":"bamboo 指生長快速的木質草本植物，常用於建築、家具和食用竹筍。"},{"en":"A school may plant bamboo as a screen because it grows tall and dense.","zh":"學校可能種植竹作為屏障，因為它長得高而密。"},{"en":"If bamboo spreads unchecked, it can dominate a garden or hillside.","zh":"如果竹不受控制地擴散，它可以主導花園或山坡。"},{"en":"The word names a plant that can grow quickly in suitable conditions.","zh":"這個詞指在合適條件下可以快速生長的植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"prickly pear","meaning":"仙人掌果；梨果仙人掌","examples":[{"en":"Prickly pear grew particularly well on the island.","zh":"梨果仙人掌在島上生長得特別好。"},{"en":"Prickly pear is a cactus plant that can survive dry conditions and produce edible fruit.","zh":"prickly pear 指一種能在乾旱環境生存並結出可食果實的仙人掌植物。"},{"en":"A garden in a dry area may use prickly pear because it needs little water.","zh":"乾旱地區的花園可能使用梨果仙人掌，因為它需要很少水。"},{"en":"If prickly pear grows too well, it may spread and crowd out other plants.","zh":"如果梨果仙人掌生長過於良好，可能擴散並排擠其他植物。"},{"en":"The phrase names a hardy cactus-like plant.","zh":"這個片語指出一種耐旱的仙人掌類植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"several thousand trees a year","meaning":"每年數千棵樹","examples":[{"en":"The sailors planted several thousand trees a year.","zh":"水手每年種植數千棵樹。"},{"en":"Several thousand trees a year means many thousands of trees planted annually.","zh":"several thousand trees a year 指每年種植好幾千棵樹。"},{"en":"A city may plant several thousand trees a year to reduce heat and improve air quality.","zh":"城市可能每年種植數千棵樹，以減低熱力並改善空氣質素。"},{"en":"If planting continues at this scale, a landscape can change quickly.","zh":"如果植樹以這種規模持續，景觀可以迅速改變。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses repeated large-scale planting.","zh":"這個片語強調重複而大規模的植樹。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be cloaked in green","meaning":"被綠色植物覆蓋","examples":[{"en":"The formerly bare mountain was soon cloaked in green.","zh":"原本光禿的山很快被綠色植物覆蓋。"},{"en":"Be cloaked in green means become covered with green plants.","zh":"be cloaked in green 指被綠色植物覆蓋。"},{"en":"After months of rain, a dry hillside may be cloaked in green grass.","zh":"幾個月雨水後，乾旱山坡可能被綠草覆蓋。"},{"en":"If trees and shrubs spread across slopes, the land can look transformed.","zh":"如果樹木和灌木蔓延到山坡上，土地看起來可以完全改變。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a visual image of vegetation covering a place.","zh":"這個片語營造植物覆蓋某地的視覺畫面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be renamed","meaning":"被重新命名","examples":[{"en":"The mountain was renamed Green Mountain.","zh":"該山被重新命名為 Green Mountain。"},{"en":"Be renamed means be given a new name.","zh":"be renamed 指被賦予一個新名稱。"},{"en":"A school hall may be renamed after a respected former principal.","zh":"學校禮堂可能以受尊敬的前校長重新命名。"},{"en":"If a place changes greatly, people may rename it to reflect its new appearance.","zh":"如果一個地方大幅改變，人們可能重新命名它，以反映其新面貌。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change in name.","zh":"這個片語描述名稱改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mountain slopes","meaning":"山坡","examples":[{"en":"The mountain’s slopes became covered with trees and shrubs.","zh":"山坡被樹木和灌木覆蓋。"},{"en":"Mountain slopes are the sides of a mountain between the base and the top.","zh":"mountain slopes 指山腳與山頂之間的山側斜面。"},{"en":"Farmers sometimes grow tea or grapes on mountain slopes.","zh":"農民有時在山坡種茶或葡萄。"},{"en":"If slopes are planted with trees, soil erosion may be reduced.","zh":"如果山坡種上樹木，水土流失可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the inclined sides of a mountain.","zh":"這個片語指山的傾斜側面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a variety of trees and shrubs","meaning":"各式各樣的樹木和灌木","examples":[{"en":"The slopes supported a variety of trees and shrubs.","zh":"山坡支持各式各樣的樹木和灌木生長。"},{"en":"A variety of trees and shrubs means many different kinds of woody plants.","zh":"a variety of trees and shrubs 指許多不同種類的木本植物。"},{"en":"A park with a variety of trees and shrubs can attract birds and insects.","zh":"有各式各樣樹木和灌木的公園可以吸引鳥類和昆蟲。"},{"en":"If many plant types grow together, the habitat becomes more complex.","zh":"如果許多植物類型一起生長，棲息地就變得更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses diversity in vegetation.","zh":"這個片語強調植被多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"from all over the world","meaning":"來自世界各地","examples":[{"en":"The plants had been brought from all over the world.","zh":"這些植物來自世界各地。"},{"en":"From all over the world means from many different countries or regions.","zh":"from all over the world 指來自許多不同國家或地區。"},{"en":"A university may welcome students from all over the world.","zh":"大學可能歡迎來自世界各地的學生。"},{"en":"If species come from many regions, they may not have evolved together naturally.","zh":"如果物種來自許多地區，它們可能不是自然共同演化出來。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses global variety of origin.","zh":"這個片語強調來源的全球多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"throw up their hands in horror","meaning":"驚恐得舉手投降；大為震驚","examples":[{"en":"Modern ecologists throw up their hands in horror at Hooker’s actions.","zh":"現代生態學家對 Hooker 的行動大為震驚。"},{"en":"Throw up their hands in horror means react with shock, alarm, or helpless disapproval.","zh":"throw up their hands in horror 指因震驚、恐慌或無奈反對而作出反應。"},{"en":"A teacher may throw up her hands in horror if students delete a project the night before submission.","zh":"如果學生在提交前一晚刪掉項目，老師可能會驚恐得舉手投降。"},{"en":"If experts see many foreign species introduced carelessly, they may respond with alarm.","zh":"如果專家看見許多外來物種被草率引入，可能會驚恐回應。"},{"en":"The phrase is vivid and slightly dramatic.","zh":"這個片語生動且略帶戲劇性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"environmental anarchy","meaning":"生態環境上的無政府狀態","examples":[{"en":"Some ecologists regard the planting programme as environmental anarchy.","zh":"有些生態學家把該植樹計劃視為生態環境上的無政府狀態。"},{"en":"Environmental anarchy means uncontrolled interference with nature without clear ecological order or caution.","zh":"environmental anarchy 指在缺乏清楚生態秩序或謹慎考慮下，不受控制地干預自然。"},{"en":"Dumping random fish into a lake can look like environmental anarchy if no one studies the effects.","zh":"如果沒有人研究影響，就隨意把魚倒入湖中，可能像生態環境上的無政府狀態。"},{"en":"If many species are introduced without planning, native ecosystems may be damaged.","zh":"如果許多物種在無計劃下被引入，本土生態系統可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly criticises disorderly environmental action.","zh":"這個片語強烈批評混亂的環境行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"exotic species","meaning":"外來物種","examples":[{"en":"Many exotic species were introduced to Ascension.","zh":"許多外來物種被引入阿森松島。"},{"en":"Exotic species are plants or animals brought from another region, rather than native to the place.","zh":"exotic species 指從其他地區帶來，而非本地原生的植物或動物。"},{"en":"A pet shop may sell exotic species that do not naturally live in the local environment.","zh":"寵物店可能售賣本地環境中自然沒有的外來物種。"},{"en":"If exotic species spread quickly, they may compete with native species.","zh":"如果外來物種快速擴散，可能與本土物種競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase describes origin, not beauty or value.","zh":"這個片語描述來源，而不是美感或價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"wreck the indigenous ecosystem","meaning":"破壞原生生態系統","examples":[{"en":"The exotic species wrecked the indigenous ecosystem.","zh":"外來物種破壞了原生生態系統。"},{"en":"Wreck the indigenous ecosystem means seriously damage the original native ecosystem.","zh":"wreck the indigenous ecosystem 指嚴重破壞原本的本土生態系統。"},{"en":"Introducing a predator to an island can wreck the indigenous ecosystem if native animals cannot defend themselves.","zh":"如果本土動物無法自我防禦，把捕食者引入島嶼可以破壞原生生態系統。"},{"en":"If native plants are crowded out, insects and birds that depend on them may also suffer.","zh":"如果本土植物被排擠，依賴它們的昆蟲和鳥類也可能受害。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests severe ecological harm.","zh":"這個片語暗示嚴重生態傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"indigenous ecosystem","meaning":"原生生態系統","examples":[{"en":"Ascension’s indigenous ecosystem was changed by imported plants.","zh":"阿森松島的原生生態系統被引入植物改變。"},{"en":"An indigenous ecosystem is the original community of native plants, animals, and organisms in a place.","zh":"indigenous ecosystem 指某地原本的本土植物、動物和生物群落。"},{"en":"A wetland’s indigenous ecosystem may include local reeds, fish, insects, and birds.","zh":"濕地的原生生態系統可能包括本地蘆葦、魚、昆蟲和鳥。"},{"en":"If foreign species dominate, the indigenous ecosystem may lose its original balance.","zh":"如果外來物種佔主導，原生生態系統可能失去原本平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the ecosystem native to a location.","zh":"這個片語集中於某地本土的生態系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"squeeze out","meaning":"排擠；令……無法生存","examples":[{"en":"The imported species squeezed out some native plants.","zh":"引入物種排擠了一些本土植物。"},{"en":"Squeeze out means push others aside until they cannot survive or compete.","zh":"squeeze out 指把其他對象擠走，直到它們無法生存或競爭。"},{"en":"Large chain stores may squeeze out small shops if rents rise and customers move away.","zh":"如果租金上升而顧客流失，大型連鎖店可能排擠小店。"},{"en":"If fast-growing plants take light, water, and space, slower native plants may disappear.","zh":"如果快速生長植物奪取陽光、水和空間，較慢的本土植物可能消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual displacement.","zh":"這個片語描述逐漸取代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"endemic plants","meaning":"特有植物","examples":[{"en":"Some of the island’s endemic plants were threatened.","zh":"該島一些特有植物受到威脅。"},{"en":"Endemic plants are plants found naturally only in one particular place.","zh":"endemic plants 指自然只在某一特定地方出現的植物。"},{"en":"A small island may have endemic plants that exist nowhere else on Earth.","zh":"小島可能有地球其他地方都沒有的特有植物。"},{"en":"If endemic plants disappear from their only habitat, the species becomes extinct.","zh":"如果特有植物從其唯一棲息地消失，該物種就會滅絕。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses local uniqueness and conservation importance.","zh":"這個片語強調本地獨特性和保育重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"know well enough what might happen","meaning":"十分清楚可能會發生甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Hooker knew well enough what might happen after introducing new species.","zh":"Hooker 十分清楚引入新物種後可能會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Know well enough what might happen means understand clearly the possible consequences.","zh":"know well enough what might happen 指清楚明白可能後果。"},{"en":"A student knows well enough what might happen if they submit copied homework.","zh":"學生十分清楚提交抄襲功課可能會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"If experts introduce foreign species, they should understand the risks before acting.","zh":"如果專家引入外來物種，行動前應了解風險。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests awareness of danger or consequence.","zh":"這個片語暗示對危險或後果有認知。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"see greater benefit in","meaning":"認為……有更大好處","examples":[{"en":"Hooker saw greater benefit in increasing rainfall and vegetation.","zh":"Hooker 認為增加降雨和植被有更大好處。"},{"en":"See greater benefit in means believe one option is more useful or valuable than another.","zh":"see greater benefit in 指相信某選項比另一選項更有用或更有價值。"},{"en":"A school may see greater benefit in extra reading time than in more tests.","zh":"學校可能認為增加閱讀時間比增加測驗有更大好處。"},{"en":"If restoring rainfall seems more urgent, officials may accept ecological risks.","zh":"如果恢復降雨看似更迫切，官員可能接受生態風險。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a judgement about relative value.","zh":"這個片語顯示對相對價值的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"improve rainfall","meaning":"增加降雨；改善降雨情況","examples":[{"en":"Hooker hoped that vegetation would improve rainfall.","zh":"Hooker 希望植被能改善降雨情況。"},{"en":"Improve rainfall means increase the amount or regularity of rain.","zh":"improve rainfall 指增加降雨量或令降雨更規律。"},{"en":"Planting trees may improve rainfall patterns by increasing moisture in the local environment.","zh":"種植樹木可能透過增加本地環境濕度來改善降雨模式。"},{"en":"If rainfall improves, plants, soil, and water supplies may also recover.","zh":"如果降雨改善，植物、土壤和水源也可能恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making rain conditions better.","zh":"這個片語描述令降雨情況變好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prolific vegetation","meaning":"茂盛的植被","examples":[{"en":"Hooker wanted to encourage more prolific vegetation.","zh":"Hooker 想鼓勵更茂盛的植被。"},{"en":"Prolific vegetation is thick, abundant plant growth.","zh":"prolific vegetation 指濃密而豐富的植物生長。"},{"en":"After heavy rain, a neglected garden may develop prolific vegetation.","zh":"大雨過後，被忽略的花園可能長出茂盛植被。"},{"en":"If vegetation becomes prolific, it can shade soil, support insects, and change the landscape.","zh":"如果植被變得茂盛，就能遮蔽土壤、支持昆蟲並改變景觀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rich and vigorous plant growth.","zh":"這個片語描述豐富而旺盛的植物生長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a much deeper issue","meaning":"更深層次的問題","examples":[{"en":"The forest raises a much deeper ecological issue.","zh":"這片森林提出了一個更深層次的生態問題。"},{"en":"A much deeper issue is a more important underlying question behind a surface problem.","zh":"a much deeper issue 指表面問題背後更重要的根本問題。"},{"en":"A student’s bad marks may reveal a deeper issue, such as anxiety or lack of sleep.","zh":"學生成績差可能揭示更深層次問題，例如焦慮或睡眠不足。"},{"en":"If a forest challenges ecological theory, the debate is not only about one island.","zh":"如果一片森林挑戰生態學理論，爭論就不只關於一個島。"},{"en":"The phrase points beyond immediate facts to bigger questions.","zh":"這個片語指向即時事實背後更大的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"relative benefits of","meaning":"……的相對好處","examples":[{"en":"The debate concerns the relative benefits of native and imported species.","zh":"這場爭論涉及本土物種與引入物種的相對好處。"},{"en":"Relative benefits of means the advantages of different things when they are compared with each other.","zh":"relative benefits of 指不同事物互相比較時各自的好處。"},{"en":"A family may compare the relative benefits of taking a bus and driving.","zh":"家庭可能比較乘巴士和駕車的相對好處。"},{"en":"If imported plants create forest but harm native species, their benefits must be weighed carefully.","zh":"如果引入植物創造森林但傷害本土物種，其好處就必須仔細衡量。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on comparison, not absolute value.","zh":"這個片語集中於比較，而不是絕對價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sparse endemic species","meaning":"稀少的特有物種","examples":[{"en":"The island originally supported only sparse endemic species.","zh":"該島原本只支持稀少的特有物種。"},{"en":"Sparse endemic species are a small number of native species found only in that place.","zh":"sparse endemic species 指數量少、只在該地出現的本土物種。"},{"en":"A rocky island may support only sparse plant life because soil and water are limited.","zh":"多石島嶼可能因土壤和水分有限，只支持稀少植物生命。"},{"en":"If endemic species are sparse, each one may become especially important for conservation.","zh":"如果特有物種稀少，每一種都可能對保育特別重要。"},{"en":"The phrase combines rarity in number with local uniqueness.","zh":"這個片語結合數量稀少和本地獨特性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"luxuriant imported species","meaning":"茂盛的外來物種","examples":[{"en":"The mountain now contains luxuriant imported species.","zh":"該山現在有茂盛的外來物種。"},{"en":"Luxuriant imported species are foreign plants growing thickly and vigorously.","zh":"luxuriant imported species 指生長濃密而旺盛的外來植物。"},{"en":"A garden may look green because luxuriant imported plants have spread quickly.","zh":"花園可能因茂盛的外來植物快速擴散而看起來翠綠。"},{"en":"If imported species grow luxuriantly, they can transform a bare landscape.","zh":"如果外來物種生長茂盛，就能改變光禿景觀。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses rich growth by plants from elsewhere.","zh":"這個片語強調來自其他地方的植物旺盛生長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"point out","meaning":"指出","examples":[{"en":"David Wilkinson pointed out the wider importance of the forest.","zh":"David Wilkinson 指出這片森林更廣泛的重要性。"},{"en":"Point out means mention something clearly so others notice it.","zh":"point out 指清楚提及某事，使他人注意到。"},{"en":"A teacher may point out a common grammar mistake before students write essays.","zh":"老師可能在學生寫作文前指出常見文法錯誤。"},{"en":"If someone points out a hidden issue, the discussion may change direction.","zh":"如果有人指出隱藏問題，討論方向可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes drawing attention to something.","zh":"這個片語描述把注意力引向某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"go to the heart of","meaning":"觸及……的核心","examples":[{"en":"The case goes to the heart of fundamental ecological theories.","zh":"這個案例觸及基本生態學理論的核心。"},{"en":"Go to the heart of means touch the most important part of an issue.","zh":"go to the heart of 指觸及一個問題最重要的部分。"},{"en":"A question about fairness goes to the heart of school discipline.","zh":"關於公平的問題觸及學校紀律的核心。"},{"en":"If one forest challenges how ecosystems are believed to form, it affects a central theory.","zh":"如果一片森林挑戰生態系統被認為如何形成，就影響核心理論。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the core of a debate.","zh":"這個片語指出爭論的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"dearly held tenets","meaning":"備受珍視的信條","examples":[{"en":"The forest challenges some of ecology’s most dearly held tenets.","zh":"這片森林挑戰了生態學一些最備受珍視的信條。"},{"en":"Dearly held tenets are beliefs or principles that people strongly value and defend.","zh":"dearly held tenets 指人們高度重視並維護的信念或原則。"},{"en":"A school’s dearly held tenet may be that every student can improve with support.","zh":"學校備受珍視的信條可能是每位學生都能在支援下進步。"},{"en":"If evidence challenges a dearly held belief, experts may resist changing their views.","zh":"如果證據挑戰備受珍視的信念，專家可能抗拒改變看法。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests ideas that are emotionally and intellectually important.","zh":"這個片語暗示思想在情感和智識上都很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"conservationists’ concern for","meaning":"保育人士對……的關注","examples":[{"en":"Conservationists have understandable concern for Ascension’s unique species.","zh":"保育人士對阿森松島獨有物種的關注可以理解。"},{"en":"Conservationists’ concern for something is their worry about protecting it from harm or extinction.","zh":"conservationists’ concern for something 指保育人士擔心保護某物免受傷害或滅絕。"},{"en":"Conservationists’ concern for old trees may grow when developers plan new roads.","zh":"當發展商計劃新道路時，保育人士對老樹的關注可能增加。"},{"en":"If species exist nowhere else, concern for them is easy to understand.","zh":"如果物種在其他地方都不存在，人們關注它們是容易理解的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes protective worry by people who care about nature.","zh":"這個片語描述關心自然的人所產生的保護性憂慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the fate of","meaning":"……的命運","examples":[{"en":"Conservationists worry about the fate of the island’s endemic plants.","zh":"保育人士擔心該島特有植物的命運。"},{"en":"The fate of something is what finally happens to it.","zh":"the fate of something 指某物最後會發生甚麼事。"},{"en":"Parents may worry about the fate of a small school if student numbers keep falling.","zh":"如果學生人數持續下降，家長可能擔心小學校的命運。"},{"en":"If endemic plants are squeezed out, their fate may be extinction.","zh":"如果特有植物被排擠，它們的命運可能是滅絕。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests uncertainty or danger about the future.","zh":"這個片語常暗示未來的不確定或危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a handful of","meaning":"少數；寥寥可數的","examples":[{"en":"Only a handful of unique species originally grew on the island.","zh":"原本只有寥寥可數的獨有物種生長在該島。"},{"en":"A handful of means a very small number of something.","zh":"a handful of 指數量非常少的某物。"},{"en":"Only a handful of students stayed after class to ask questions.","zh":"只有少數學生課後留下來問問題。"},{"en":"If only a handful of species are native, losing even one matters greatly.","zh":"如果只有寥寥可數的物種是本土的，即使失去一種也非常重要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses scarcity.","zh":"這個片語強調稀少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"blind someone to","meaning":"令某人看不到……","examples":[{"en":"Concern for native species may blind scientists to the forest’s success.","zh":"對本土物種的關注可能令科學家看不到這片森林的成功。"},{"en":"Blind someone to means prevent someone from noticing or understanding something.","zh":"blind someone to 指阻止某人注意或理解某事。"},{"en":"Fear of mistakes can blind students to the progress they have already made.","zh":"對錯誤的恐懼可以令學生看不到自己已取得的進步。"},{"en":"If people focus only on native species, they may miss how well the new forest functions.","zh":"如果人們只集中於本土物種，可能錯過新森林運作良好的事實。"},{"en":"The phrase describes attention being narrowed by one strong concern.","zh":"這個片語描述注意力被某強烈關注收窄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"something quite astonishing","meaning":"相當令人驚訝的事情","examples":[{"en":"The introduced species achieved something quite astonishing.","zh":"引入物種達成了相當令人驚訝的事情。"},{"en":"Something quite astonishing is something very surprising and impressive.","zh":"something quite astonishing 指非常令人驚訝且令人印象深刻的事情。"},{"en":"A shy student giving a confident speech can be something quite astonishing.","zh":"害羞學生作出自信演講，可以是相當令人驚訝的事情。"},{"en":"If unrelated plants form a working forest, the result is scientifically surprising.","zh":"如果互不相關的植物形成運作中的森林，結果在科學上令人驚訝。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses strong surprise.","zh":"這個片語表達強烈驚訝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"introduced species","meaning":"引入物種","examples":[{"en":"The introduced species have developed into a functioning ecosystem.","zh":"引入物種已發展成一個運作中的生態系統。"},{"en":"Introduced species are plants or animals brought into a place by humans.","zh":"introduced species 指由人類帶到某地的植物或動物。"},{"en":"Garden plants introduced from another country may grow well in a new climate.","zh":"從另一國家引入的園藝植物可能在新氣候中生長良好。"},{"en":"If introduced species spread quickly, they can either create new habitats or harm native species.","zh":"如果引入物種快速擴散，它們既可能創造新棲息地，也可能傷害本土物種。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how the species arrived.","zh":"這個片語集中於物種如何到達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a roaring success","meaning":"巨大成功","examples":[{"en":"Wilkinson considers the introduced species a roaring success.","zh":"Wilkinson 認為引入物種是一個巨大成功。"},{"en":"A roaring success is a very great and obvious success.","zh":"a roaring success 指非常巨大而明顯的成功。"},{"en":"A school concert can be a roaring success if the hall is full and students perform confidently.","zh":"如果禮堂坐滿、學生自信表演，學校音樂會可以是巨大成功。"},{"en":"If a bare mountain becomes a functioning forest, some people may call it a roaring success.","zh":"如果光禿山峰變成運作中的森林，有些人可能稱之為巨大成功。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and highly positive.","zh":"這個片語較口語，而且非常正面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fully functioning","meaning":"功能完整的","examples":[{"en":"Green Mountain is now a fully functioning tropical forest.","zh":"Green Mountain 現在是一片功能完整的熱帶森林。"},{"en":"Fully functioning means working properly as a complete system.","zh":"fully functioning 指作為完整系統正常運作。"},{"en":"A fully functioning school library has books, staff, quiet space, and borrowing rules.","zh":"功能完整的學校圖書館有書籍、職員、安靜空間和借書規則。"},{"en":"If a forest supports plants, insects, soil life, and water cycles, it may be fully functioning.","zh":"如果森林支持植物、昆蟲、土壤生命和水循環，它可能是功能完整的。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that something is not just present but working.","zh":"這個片語強調某物不只是存在，而是正在運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"man-made tropical cloud forest","meaning":"人造熱帶雲霧林","examples":[{"en":"Green Mountain is a man-made tropical cloud forest.","zh":"Green Mountain 是一片人造熱帶雲霧林。"},{"en":"A man-made tropical cloud forest is a humid mountain forest created largely by human action.","zh":"man-made tropical cloud forest 指主要由人類行動創造的潮濕山地森林。"},{"en":"A city park is man-made because people design and plant it.","zh":"城市公園是人造的，因為人們設計並種植它。"},{"en":"If humans introduce plants that create misty forest conditions, the result may be man-made but ecologically active.","zh":"如果人類引入植物並創造霧氣森林環境，結果可能是人造但有生態功能。"},{"en":"The phrase combines artificial origin with forest function.","zh":"這個片語結合人工起源與森林功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"grow from scratch","meaning":"從零開始形成","examples":[{"en":"The forest grew from scratch on a previously bare mountain.","zh":"這片森林在原本光禿的山上從零開始形成。"},{"en":"Grow from scratch means develop from nothing or from a very basic starting point.","zh":"grow from scratch 指從沒有東西或非常基本的起點發展。"},{"en":"A student can build an essay from scratch by starting with a blank page and outline.","zh":"學生可以從空白頁和大綱開始，從零建立一篇文章。"},{"en":"If a forest grows from scratch, there was no mature forest there before.","zh":"如果森林從零開始形成，表示那裡以前沒有成熟森林。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses creation from an empty beginning.","zh":"這個片語強調從空白起點創造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a ragbag of species","meaning":"胡亂拼湊的一批物種","examples":[{"en":"The forest developed from a ragbag of unrelated species.","zh":"這片森林由一批互不相關、胡亂拼湊的物種發展而成。"},{"en":"A ragbag of species means a mixed and disorderly collection of different species.","zh":"a ragbag of species 指不同物種混雜而無序地聚在一起。"},{"en":"A classroom shelf may become a ragbag of old books, broken pens, and random worksheets.","zh":"課室書架可能變成舊書、壞筆和零散工作紙胡亂堆成的一堆。"},{"en":"If species are collected without a plan, the resulting ecosystem seems accidental.","zh":"如果物種在沒有計劃下被收集，形成的生態系統就顯得偶然。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a messy mixture rather than careful selection.","zh":"這個片語暗示雜亂混合，而不是仔細挑選。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"more or less at random","meaning":"差不多隨機地","examples":[{"en":"The plants were collected more or less at random.","zh":"這些植物差不多是隨機收集的。"},{"en":"More or less at random means without a clear plan or strict selection method.","zh":"more or less at random 指沒有清楚計劃或嚴格挑選方法。"},{"en":"A student choosing essay examples more or less at random may produce a weak argument.","zh":"如果學生差不多隨機地選作文例子，論證可能薄弱。"},{"en":"If plants are introduced randomly, no one can predict exactly how they will interact.","zh":"如果植物被隨機引入，沒有人能準確預測牠們如何互動。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests limited organisation or planning.","zh":"這個片語暗示組織或計劃有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"all over the planet","meaning":"遍及全球","examples":[{"en":"The species came from locations all over the planet.","zh":"這些物種來自遍及全球的地點。"},{"en":"All over the planet means from many places across the whole world.","zh":"all over the planet 指來自整個世界許多地方。"},{"en":"A popular song may be heard by listeners all over the planet.","zh":"一首受歡迎的歌曲可能被全球各地聽眾聽到。"},{"en":"If species come from all over the planet, they have very different evolutionary histories.","zh":"如果物種來自全球各地，牠們就有非常不同的演化歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses global spread or origin.","zh":"這個片語強調全球分布或來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"conventional ecological theory","meaning":"傳統生態學理論","examples":[{"en":"Conventional ecological theory says that complex ecosystems develop gradually.","zh":"傳統生態學理論認為複雜生態系統會逐漸發展。"},{"en":"Conventional ecological theory means the traditional accepted explanation used by ecologists.","zh":"conventional ecological theory 指生態學家使用的傳統公認解釋。"},{"en":"Conventional teaching theory may say students learn best step by step.","zh":"傳統教學理論可能認為學生最好一步步學習。"},{"en":"If a real case contradicts conventional theory, scientists may need to revise it.","zh":"如果真實案例與傳統理論矛盾，科學家可能需要修訂它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to established ecological thinking.","zh":"這個片語指既有生態學思想。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"complex ecosystems","meaning":"複雜的生態系統","examples":[{"en":"Cloud forests are highly complex ecosystems.","zh":"雲霧林是高度複雜的生態系統。"},{"en":"Complex ecosystems are natural systems with many species interacting in many ways.","zh":"complex ecosystems 指有許多物種以多種方式互動的自然系統。"},{"en":"A coral reef is a complex ecosystem because fish, corals, algae, and microbes depend on one another.","zh":"珊瑚礁是複雜生態系統，因為魚類、珊瑚、藻類和微生物互相依賴。"},{"en":"If one part of a complex ecosystem changes, many other parts may be affected.","zh":"如果複雜生態系統其中一部分改變，許多其他部分也可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses many connected living relationships.","zh":"這個片語強調許多相連的生命關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"emerge only through","meaning":"只能透過……形成","examples":[{"en":"Such forests were believed to emerge only through evolutionary processes.","zh":"這類森林被認為只能透過演化過程形成。"},{"en":"Emerge only through means develop only by means of one particular process.","zh":"emerge only through 指只能經由某一特定過程發展出來。"},{"en":"Some skills emerge only through repeated practice, not through reading notes once.","zh":"有些技能只能透過反覆練習形成，而不是讀一次筆記。"},{"en":"If forests can form without long co-evolution, the old belief becomes questionable.","zh":"如果森林不經長期共同演化也能形成，舊信念就變得可疑。"},{"en":"The phrase limits the possible route of development.","zh":"這個片語限制發展的可能途徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"evolutionary processes","meaning":"演化過程","examples":[{"en":"Ecologists traditionally explain rainforests through evolutionary processes.","zh":"生態學家傳統上透過演化過程解釋熱帶雨林。"},{"en":"Evolutionary processes are long-term changes in living things across generations.","zh":"evolutionary processes 指生命體跨世代的長期變化。"},{"en":"The shape of a bird’s beak can change through evolutionary processes over many generations.","zh":"鳥喙形狀可以經過許多世代的演化過程而改變。"},{"en":"If species evolve together, their relationships may become highly specialised.","zh":"如果物種共同演化，牠們的關係可能變得高度專門化。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to biological change over long periods.","zh":"這個片語指長時間中的生物變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"develop in concert with","meaning":"與……協調演化","examples":[{"en":"Each organism is thought to develop in concert with other species.","zh":"每種生物被認為會與其他物種協調演化。"},{"en":"Develop in concert with means grow or change together in coordination with something else.","zh":"develop in concert with 指與其他事物一起協調地成長或改變。"},{"en":"A school timetable should develop in concert with students’ transport needs.","zh":"學校時間表應與學生交通需要協調發展。"},{"en":"If a flower and its pollinator develop together, each may adapt to the other.","zh":"如果花和其傳粉者一起發展，雙方可能互相適應。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses coordinated development.","zh":"這個片語強調協調發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fill particular niches","meaning":"填補特定生態位","examples":[{"en":"Organisms develop specialised features to fill particular niches.","zh":"生物發展出專門特徵以填補特定生態位。"},{"en":"Fill particular niches means occupy specific roles in an ecosystem.","zh":"fill particular niches 指在生態系統中佔據特定角色。"},{"en":"In a school club, one student may fill the role of organiser while another handles design.","zh":"在學會中，一名學生可能擔任組織者角色，另一名負責設計。"},{"en":"If a bird eats insects that others ignore, it fills a particular ecological niche.","zh":"如果鳥類吃其他動物忽略的昆蟲，它就填補了特定生態位。"},{"en":"The phrase connects adaptation with a specific function.","zh":"這個片語把適應與特定功能連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ecological niches","meaning":"生態位","examples":[{"en":"Different species occupy different ecological niches.","zh":"不同物種佔據不同生態位。"},{"en":"Ecological niches are the roles species play in an ecosystem, including what they eat and how they live.","zh":"ecological niches 指物種在生態系統中的角色，包括吃甚麼和如何生活。"},{"en":"Bees and earthworms occupy different ecological niches in a garden.","zh":"蜜蜂和蚯蚓在花園中佔據不同生態位。"},{"en":"If two species use the same niche, they may compete strongly.","zh":"如果兩個物種使用同一生態位，牠們可能激烈競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ecological roles, not physical holes.","zh":"這個片語描述生態角色，而不是實體洞穴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"co-evolve with","meaning":"與……共同演化","examples":[{"en":"Plants often co-evolve with their pollinators.","zh":"植物常與其傳粉者共同演化。"},{"en":"Co-evolve with means evolve together so that two species influence each other’s development.","zh":"co-evolve with 指兩個物種一起演化，並互相影響對方的發展。"},{"en":"A flower and a bee may co-evolve if each depends on the other for food or reproduction.","zh":"如果花和蜜蜂在食物或繁殖上互相依賴，就可能共同演化。"},{"en":"If species co-evolve, their relationship can become very specialised.","zh":"如果物種共同演化，牠們的關係可能變得非常專門化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes linked evolution between species.","zh":"這個片語描述物種之間相連的演化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pollinators","meaning":"傳粉者","examples":[{"en":"Many plants depend on pollinators for reproduction.","zh":"許多植物依賴傳粉者繁殖。"},{"en":"Pollinators are animals or insects that carry pollen from one flower to another.","zh":"pollinators 指把花粉從一朵花帶到另一朵花的動物或昆蟲。"},{"en":"Bees are common pollinators in gardens and farms.","zh":"蜜蜂是花園和農場中常見的傳粉者。"},{"en":"If pollinators disappear, many fruit and seed-producing plants may decline.","zh":"如果傳粉者消失，許多結果和結子的植物可能衰退。"},{"en":"The word names organisms that help plants reproduce.","zh":"這個詞指幫助植物繁殖的生物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"seed dispersers","meaning":"種子傳播者","examples":[{"en":"Seed dispersers carry seeds away from parent plants.","zh":"種子傳播者把種子帶離母株。"},{"en":"Seed dispersers are animals, wind, water, or other agents that move seeds to new places.","zh":"seed dispersers 指把種子移到新地方的動物、風、水或其他媒介。"},{"en":"Birds can be seed dispersers when they eat fruit and later drop the seeds elsewhere.","zh":"鳥類吃果實後在其他地方排出種子時，就可以是種子傳播者。"},{"en":"If seeds are dispersed widely, young plants face less competition from the parent plant.","zh":"如果種子被廣泛傳播，幼苗就較少與母株競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how plants spread to new locations.","zh":"這個片語描述植物如何擴散到新地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"microbes in the soil","meaning":"土壤中的微生物","examples":[{"en":"Microbes in the soil help break down plant material.","zh":"土壤中的微生物幫助分解植物物質。"},{"en":"Microbes in the soil are tiny living organisms that live underground and affect nutrients.","zh":"microbes in the soil 指生活在地下、影響養分的微小生物。"},{"en":"Healthy garden soil contains microbes that help plants grow.","zh":"健康花園土壤含有幫助植物生長的微生物。"},{"en":"If soil microbes are damaged, dead leaves may decompose more slowly.","zh":"如果土壤微生物受損，枯葉可能分解得更慢。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to microscopic life beneath the ground.","zh":"這個片語指地下的微觀生命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deal with","meaning":"處理；應付","examples":[{"en":"Soil microbes evolve to deal with leaf litter.","zh":"土壤微生物演化出能力來處理落葉層。"},{"en":"Deal with means handle, process, or manage something.","zh":"deal with 指處理、加工或應付某事。"},{"en":"A school counsellor helps students deal with stress before exams.","zh":"學校輔導員幫助學生應付考試前壓力。"},{"en":"If microbes deal with leaf litter, they break it down into useful nutrients.","zh":"如果微生物處理落葉層，它們會把它分解成有用養分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical handling of a problem or material.","zh":"這個片語描述對問題或物質的實際處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"leaf litter","meaning":"落葉層","examples":[{"en":"Microbes help decompose leaf litter on the forest floor.","zh":"微生物幫助分解森林地面的落葉層。"},{"en":"Leaf litter is the layer of fallen leaves and plant material on the ground.","zh":"leaf litter 指地面上的落葉和植物物質層。"},{"en":"In autumn, parks often have thick leaf litter under trees.","zh":"秋天時，公園樹下常有厚厚落葉層。"},{"en":"If leaf litter decomposes, nutrients return to the soil.","zh":"如果落葉層分解，養分會回到土壤中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dead plant material covering the ground.","zh":"這個片語描述覆蓋地面的枯死植物物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"that is not what happened","meaning":"事情並非如此發生","examples":[{"en":"Evolutionary co-development is not what happened on Green Mountain.","zh":"共同演化並不是 Green Mountain 上發生的事情。"},{"en":"That is not what happened means the real events were different from the expected explanation.","zh":"that is not what happened 指真實事件與預期解釋不同。"},{"en":"A student may think the answer was guessed, but that is not what happened if it was carefully calculated.","zh":"學生可能以為答案是猜出來的，但如果是仔細計算得出，事情就並非如此。"},{"en":"If species did not evolve together, the forest challenges the usual theory.","zh":"如果物種沒有共同演化，這片森林就挑戰通常理論。"},{"en":"The phrase corrects a wrong assumption.","zh":"這個片語糾正錯誤假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the experience suggests that","meaning":"這個經驗顯示","examples":[{"en":"The experience suggests that forests may form partly by chance.","zh":"這個經驗顯示森林可能部分由偶然形成。"},{"en":"The experience suggests that means what happened seems to show or imply something.","zh":"the experience suggests that 指發生的事情似乎顯示或暗示某事。"},{"en":"A successful online lesson may suggest that some students learn well from home.","zh":"一堂成功的網課可能顯示有些學生在家學習效果良好。"},{"en":"If one accidental forest works, it may suggest that ecosystem formation is more flexible than expected.","zh":"如果一片偶然森林能運作，可能顯示生態系統形成比預期更有彈性。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a cautious conclusion from an example.","zh":"這個片語從例子引出謹慎結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be constructed by chance","meaning":"偶然形成","examples":[{"en":"Some rainforests may be constructed more by chance than by evolution.","zh":"有些熱帶雨林可能更多是偶然形成，而不是由演化造成。"},{"en":"Be constructed by chance means form accidentally rather than through a planned or predictable process.","zh":"be constructed by chance 指偶然形成，而不是透過計劃或可預測過程形成。"},{"en":"A friendship may be constructed by chance when two students sit together randomly.","zh":"兩名學生隨機坐在一起時，友誼可能偶然形成。"},{"en":"If species meet accidentally but survive together, a new ecosystem may form.","zh":"如果物種偶然相遇但能共同生存，新生態系統可能形成。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses accident rather than design.","zh":"這個片語強調偶然而不是設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"far more by chance than by evolution","meaning":"偶然因素遠多於演化因素","examples":[{"en":"The forest may have developed far more by chance than by evolution.","zh":"這片森林的發展可能偶然因素遠多於演化因素。"},{"en":"Far more by chance than by evolution means accident played a larger role than long-term co-evolution.","zh":"far more by chance than by evolution 指偶然比長期共同演化發揮更大作用。"},{"en":"A group project may succeed more by luck than planning if the members happen to work well together.","zh":"如果組員剛好合作良好，小組項目成功可能更多靠運氣而不是計劃。"},{"en":"If unrelated species form a forest quickly, chance may be more important than expected.","zh":"如果互不相關的物種快速形成森林，偶然可能比預期更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly contrasts accident with evolutionary planning.","zh":"這個片語強烈對比偶然與演化安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"do not so much … as …","meaning":"與其說……不如說……","examples":[{"en":"Species do not so much create ecosystems as adapt to available conditions.","zh":"與其說物種創造生態系統，不如說牠們適應現有條件。"},{"en":"Do not so much A as B means B is a better description than A.","zh":"do not so much A as B 指 B 比 A 更能描述情況。"},{"en":"Good teachers do not so much give answers as guide students to think clearly.","zh":"與其說好老師給答案，不如說他們引導學生清楚思考。"},{"en":"If species mainly adapt to what exists, ecosystems may arise from practical adjustment.","zh":"如果物種主要適應現有條件，生態系統可能來自實際調整。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a refined contrast between two interpretations.","zh":"這個片語在兩種解釋之間作出細緻對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make the best of","meaning":"充分利用現有條件","examples":[{"en":"Species may simply make the best of what they have.","zh":"物種可能只是充分利用現有條件。"},{"en":"Make the best of means use a difficult or imperfect situation as well as possible.","zh":"make the best of 指盡量善用困難或不完美的情況。"},{"en":"A student may make the best of a short revision period by focusing on the weakest topics.","zh":"學生可能透過集中最弱課題，充分利用短暫溫習時間。"},{"en":"If organisms arrive in a new place, they survive by using available food, soil, and shelter.","zh":"如果生物到達新地方，牠們會透過利用現有食物、土壤和庇護來生存。"},{"en":"The phrase shows practical adaptation rather than perfect conditions.","zh":"這個片語顯示實際適應，而不是完美條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"constituent species","meaning":"組成物種","examples":[{"en":"The forest developed without co-evolution among its constituent species.","zh":"這片森林在其組成物種之間沒有共同演化的情況下發展。"},{"en":"Constituent species are the different species that make up an ecosystem or group.","zh":"constituent species 指組成一個生態系統或群體的不同物種。"},{"en":"The constituent species of a pond may include fish, insects, algae, and frogs.","zh":"池塘的組成物種可能包括魚、昆蟲、藻類和青蛙。"},{"en":"If the constituent species come from different continents, they may not share evolutionary history.","zh":"如果組成物種來自不同大陸，牠們可能沒有共同演化歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the member species of a larger system.","zh":"這個片語指較大系統中的成員物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not everyone agrees","meaning":"並非人人都同意","examples":[{"en":"Not everyone agrees with Wilkinson’s interpretation.","zh":"並非人人都同意 Wilkinson 的解釋。"},{"en":"Not everyone agrees means some people accept the idea, but others do not.","zh":"not everyone agrees 指有些人接受某想法，但其他人不同意。"},{"en":"Not everyone agrees that homework should be completely removed from schools.","zh":"並非人人都同意學校應完全取消功課。"},{"en":"If evidence is open to interpretation, experts may disagree.","zh":"如果證據可有不同解讀，專家可能意見不一。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces disagreement without saying everyone is opposed.","zh":"這個片語引出分歧，但不是說所有人都反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"surviving endemic species","meaning":"存活下來的特有物種","examples":[{"en":"The surviving endemic species may still support the ecosystem.","zh":"存活下來的特有物種可能仍然支持該生態系統。"},{"en":"Surviving endemic species are native species found only in one place that have not died out.","zh":"surviving endemic species 指只在某地出現且尚未滅絕的本土物種。"},{"en":"A few surviving endemic plants may be protected in a fenced garden.","zh":"少數存活下來的特有植物可能在圍欄花園中受到保護。"},{"en":"If these species form the base of an ecosystem, they remain important even in small numbers.","zh":"如果這些物種構成生態系統基礎，即使數量少仍然重要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both survival and local uniqueness.","zh":"這個片語同時強調存活和本地獨特性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"though small in number","meaning":"雖然數目很少","examples":[{"en":"The endemic species, though small in number, may remain important.","zh":"這些特有物種雖然數目很少，可能仍然重要。"},{"en":"Though small in number means although there are only a few of them.","zh":"though small in number 指雖然數量只有少數。"},{"en":"A few student volunteers, though small in number, can organise a successful charity sale.","zh":"少數學生義工雖然數目很少，也可以組織成功的慈善義賣。"},{"en":"If rare native plants support soil or insects, their small number does not make them unimportant.","zh":"如果稀有本土植物支持土壤或昆蟲，數量少不代表不重要。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts quantity with significance.","zh":"這個片語對比數量和重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"form the framework of","meaning":"構成……的骨架","examples":[{"en":"Alan Gray argues that native species form the framework of the ecosystem.","zh":"Alan Gray 主張本土物種構成該生態系統的骨架。"},{"en":"Form the framework of means provide the basic structure that supports something.","zh":"form the framework of 指提供支撐某事的基本結構。"},{"en":"Clear rules form the framework of a fair classroom.","zh":"清楚規則構成公平課室的骨架。"},{"en":"If native species hold the ecosystem together, imported species may simply grow around them.","zh":"如果本土物種支撐整個生態系統，外來物種可能只是圍繞它們生長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a supporting structure.","zh":"這個片語描述支撐性結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"new arrivals","meaning":"新引入的物種","examples":[{"en":"The new arrivals may play only a limited ecological role.","zh":"新引入的物種可能只扮演有限的生態角色。"},{"en":"New arrivals are people, animals, or plants that have recently come to a place.","zh":"new arrivals 指最近來到某地的人、動物或植物。"},{"en":"New arrivals at a school may need time to understand routines and friendships.","zh":"新來學校的學生可能需要時間理解日常程序和人際關係。"},{"en":"If new plant arrivals do not support many insects or soil processes, their role may be limited.","zh":"如果新引入植物沒有支持很多昆蟲或土壤過程，其角色可能有限。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to recently introduced members of a place or system.","zh":"這個片語指某地或系統中最近加入的成員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"an adornment","meaning":"裝飾物；點綴","examples":[{"en":"Gray suggests that the imported plants may be merely an adornment.","zh":"Gray 認為引入植物可能只是裝飾物。"},{"en":"An adornment is something that decorates or adds appearance but is not structurally essential.","zh":"an adornment 指用作裝飾或增加外觀，但不是結構上必要的東西。"},{"en":"A ribbon on a gift box is an adornment, not the gift itself.","zh":"禮物盒上的絲帶是點綴，而不是禮物本身。"},{"en":"If imported plants only make the forest look lush, they may not support its basic structure.","zh":"如果引入植物只是令森林看起來茂盛，它們可能沒有支撐其基本結構。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts decoration with real importance.","zh":"這個片語對比裝飾與真正重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"structural importance","meaning":"結構上的重要性","examples":[{"en":"The new plants may have little structural importance.","zh":"新植物可能沒有多少結構上的重要性。"},{"en":"Structural importance means importance in supporting the basic organisation or function of a system.","zh":"structural importance 指在支撐系統基本組織或功能方面的重要性。"},{"en":"A timetable has structural importance because it shapes the whole school day.","zh":"時間表有結構上的重要性，因為它塑造整個上課日。"},{"en":"If a species provides food, shade, or soil stability, it may have structural importance.","zh":"如果某物種提供食物、樹蔭或土壤穩定，它可能具有結構上的重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a role that holds a system together.","zh":"這個片語指維持系統整體的角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sound like clutching at straws","meaning":"聽起來像在勉強找藉口","examples":[{"en":"To Wilkinson, Gray’s argument sounds like clutching at straws.","zh":"在 Wilkinson 看來，Gray 的論點聽起來像在勉強找藉口。"},{"en":"Sound like clutching at straws means seem like a desperate attempt to defend a weak argument.","zh":"sound like clutching at straws 指看似絕望地嘗試維護一個薄弱論點。"},{"en":"Blaming a late bus for homework not done for a week sounds like clutching at straws.","zh":"一星期沒做功課卻怪巴士遲到，聽起來像在勉強找藉口。"},{"en":"If evidence strongly challenges a theory, weak excuses may look desperate.","zh":"如果證據強烈挑戰某理論，薄弱藉口可能顯得很勉強。"},{"en":"The phrase is critical and suggests the argument is not convincing.","zh":"這個片語帶批判語氣，暗示論點不具說服力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"clutch at straws","meaning":"抓住救命稻草；勉強找理由","examples":[{"en":"Scientists may clutch at straws when evidence challenges established beliefs.","zh":"當證據挑戰既有信念時，科學家可能會抓住救命稻草。"},{"en":"Clutch at straws means desperately use weak arguments or unlikely hopes because better options are gone.","zh":"clutch at straws 指因沒有更好選擇而絕望地使用薄弱論點或渺茫希望。"},{"en":"A student who has not revised may clutch at straws by guessing every answer.","zh":"沒有溫習的學生可能靠亂猜所有答案來抓救命稻草。"},{"en":"If a theory is failing, supporters may search for tiny details to protect it.","zh":"如果理論正在失敗，其支持者可能尋找微小細節來保護它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes desperate reasoning.","zh":"這個片語描述絕望式推理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"instant formation","meaning":"瞬間形成","examples":[{"en":"The instant formation of a rainforest seems increasingly possible.","zh":"熱帶雨林的瞬間形成似乎越來越可能。"},{"en":"Instant formation means very rapid creation, far faster than expected.","zh":"instant formation 指非常快速地形成，遠比預期快。"},{"en":"A classroom group may show instant formation if students quickly organise roles without being told.","zh":"如果學生未經指示就快速分配角色，課室小組可能出現即時形成。"},{"en":"If a rainforest forms quickly from introduced plants, ecological development may be more flexible than theory suggests.","zh":"如果雨林由引入植物快速形成，生態發展可能比理論所說更有彈性。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts rapid formation with slow natural development.","zh":"這個片語把快速形成與緩慢自然發展作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"increasingly plausible","meaning":"越來越可信","examples":[{"en":"The theory of rapid rainforest formation sounds increasingly plausible.","zh":"熱帶雨林快速形成的理論聽起來越來越可信。"},{"en":"Increasingly plausible means becoming more believable as more evidence appears.","zh":"increasingly plausible 指隨着更多證據出現而變得更可信。"},{"en":"A student’s explanation becomes increasingly plausible when several examples support it.","zh":"當幾個例子支持學生的解釋時，該解釋會變得越來越可信。"},{"en":"If research elsewhere finds similar human-made forests, Wilkinson’s idea gains credibility.","zh":"如果其他地方的研究發現相似的人造森林，Wilkinson 的想法就更有可信度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a theory becoming easier to accept.","zh":"這個片語描述理論變得更容易被接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"research reveals that","meaning":"研究顯示","examples":[{"en":"Recent research reveals that some forests have human origins.","zh":"最新研究顯示有些森林源自人類活動。"},{"en":"Research reveals that means studies show something previously unknown or unclear.","zh":"research reveals that 指研究顯示以前未知或不清楚的事情。"},{"en":"Research may reveal that students learn vocabulary better with repeated examples.","zh":"研究可能顯示學生透過重複例子更好地學習詞彙。"},{"en":"If research reveals human influence in forests, ideas about pristine nature may change.","zh":"如果研究顯示森林有人類影響，關於原始自然的想法可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a finding from study.","zh":"這個片語引出研究結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"supposedly pristine","meaning":"據稱原始未受破壞的","examples":[{"en":"Some supposedly pristine rainforests may have been altered by people.","zh":"有些據稱原始未受破壞的熱帶雨林可能曾被人類改變。"},{"en":"Supposedly pristine means believed to be untouched and pure, although that may not be true.","zh":"supposedly pristine 指被認為未受觸碰而純淨，但這未必真實。"},{"en":"A supposedly quiet study room may actually be noisy during lunch.","zh":"據稱安靜的自修室在午飯時間其實可能很嘈吵。"},{"en":"If a forest thought to be untouched was planted by humans, the label “pristine” becomes doubtful.","zh":"如果被認為未受破壞的森林其實由人類種植，「原始」這個標籤就變得可疑。"},{"en":"The phrase signals scepticism about an accepted description.","zh":"這個片語表示對既有描述的懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tropical rainforests","meaning":"熱帶雨林","examples":[{"en":"The research covers tropical rainforests from the Amazon to Asia.","zh":"該研究涵蓋從亞馬遜到亞洲的熱帶雨林。"},{"en":"Tropical rainforests are warm, wet forests with dense vegetation and high biodiversity.","zh":"tropical rainforests 指溫暖潮濕、植被濃密且生物多樣性高的森林。"},{"en":"Students often learn that tropical rainforests contain many plant and animal species.","zh":"學生常學到熱帶雨林包含許多植物和動物物種。"},{"en":"If rainfall and heat remain high, forests can support thick plant growth all year.","zh":"如果降雨和熱量維持高水平，森林可全年支持茂密植物生長。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to humid forests in tropical regions.","zh":"這個片語指熱帶地區的潮濕森林。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"little more than","meaning":"只不過是……","examples":[{"en":"Some forests may be little more than overgrown ancient gardens.","zh":"有些森林可能只不過是植物過度生長的古代花園。"},{"en":"Little more than means almost only, often reducing the importance or status of something.","zh":"little more than 指幾乎只是某事，常降低某物的重要性或地位。"},{"en":"A messy notebook may be little more than a pile of loose pages without organisation.","zh":"如果筆記本毫無組織，它可能只不過是一堆散紙。"},{"en":"If a rainforest is actually an abandoned garden, its “wild” origin becomes questionable.","zh":"如果熱帶雨林其實是被棄置的花園，其「野生」起源就變得可疑。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests something is less impressive than it appears.","zh":"這個片語暗示某事不如表面看來那麼了不起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"overgrown gardens","meaning":"植物過度生長的花園","examples":[{"en":"Some rainforests may be the overgrown gardens of earlier societies.","zh":"有些熱帶雨林可能是早期社會中植物過度生長的花園。"},{"en":"Overgrown gardens are gardens where plants have grown thickly after people stopped managing them.","zh":"overgrown gardens 指在人們停止管理後，植物濃密生長的花園。"},{"en":"An empty house may have an overgrown garden full of vines and weeds.","zh":"空置房屋可能有一個長滿藤蔓和雜草的過度生長花園。"},{"en":"If abandoned gardens continue growing for centuries, they may look like natural forest.","zh":"如果被棄置花園持續生長幾百年，它們可能看起來像天然森林。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests human origin hidden by wild growth.","zh":"這個片語暗示被野生生長掩蓋的人類起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"past rainforest civilisations","meaning":"過往的雨林文明","examples":[{"en":"Past rainforest civilisations may have planted parts of today’s forests.","zh":"過往的雨林文明可能種植了今天森林的某些部分。"},{"en":"Past rainforest civilisations were earlier human societies that lived in rainforest regions.","zh":"past rainforest civilisations 指早期生活在雨林地區的人類社會。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may study old paths, pottery, and tree patterns to understand past rainforest civilisations.","zh":"考古學家可能研究舊道路、陶器和樹木模式，以了解過往雨林文明。"},{"en":"If ancient people planted useful trees, modern forests may preserve traces of their work.","zh":"如果古人種植有用樹木，現代森林可能保存其活動痕跡。"},{"en":"The phrase connects human history with forest ecology.","zh":"這個片語把人類歷史與森林生態連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the most surprising thing of all","meaning":"最令人驚訝的是","examples":[{"en":"The most surprising thing of all is the lack of proper research.","zh":"最令人驚訝的是缺乏正式研究。"},{"en":"The most surprising thing of all means the fact that is most unexpected among all the facts mentioned.","zh":"the most surprising thing of all 指在所有提到的事實中最出乎意料的一點。"},{"en":"After a successful exam, the most surprising thing of all may be that the student studied calmly.","zh":"考試成功後，最令人驚訝的可能是學生平靜地溫習。"},{"en":"If a forest challenges major theory but few people study it, that lack is surprising.","zh":"如果一片森林挑戰重大理論，但很少人研究它，這種缺乏就令人驚訝。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the strongest surprise.","zh":"這個片語引出最強烈的驚訝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"conduct proper research into","meaning":"對……進行正式研究","examples":[{"en":"Few ecologists have conducted proper research into the forest.","zh":"很少生態學家對這片森林進行正式研究。"},{"en":"Conduct proper research into means study something carefully using suitable methods.","zh":"conduct proper research into 指使用合適方法仔細研究某事。"},{"en":"A school should conduct proper research into bullying before changing its rules.","zh":"學校在改變規則前應對欺凌進行正式研究。"},{"en":"If scientists do not study a mystery properly, important evidence may be missed.","zh":"如果科學家沒有正式研究一個謎團，重要證據可能被錯過。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses serious and systematic investigation.","zh":"這個片語強調認真而有系統的調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"human-made rainforest ecosystem","meaning":"人造雨林生態系統","examples":[{"en":"Green Mountain is a human-made rainforest ecosystem.","zh":"Green Mountain 是一個人造雨林生態系統。"},{"en":"A human-made rainforest ecosystem is a forest system created mainly through human planting or intervention.","zh":"human-made rainforest ecosystem 指主要透過人類種植或干預創造的森林系統。"},{"en":"A greenhouse full of tropical plants is human-made, even if it contains living ecological relationships.","zh":"溫室中滿是熱帶植物，即使有生命之間的生態關係，它仍是人造的。"},{"en":"If humans create a forest that functions like a natural one, it raises difficult ecological questions.","zh":"如果人類創造出像天然森林般運作的森林，就會提出困難的生態問題。"},{"en":"The phrase combines artificial origin with ecosystem function.","zh":"這個片語結合人工起源與生態系統功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a survey of the island’s flora","meaning":"對島上植物群的調查","examples":[{"en":"A survey of the island’s flora focused on native plants.","zh":"對島上植物群的調查集中於本土植物。"},{"en":"A survey of the island’s flora is a study of the plant life found on the island.","zh":"a survey of the island’s flora 指研究島上發現的植物生命。"},{"en":"Students may conduct a survey of schoolyard plants to learn local biodiversity.","zh":"學生可能進行校園植物調查，以認識本地生物多樣性。"},{"en":"If a survey focuses only on native plants, it may miss how introduced plants function.","zh":"如果調查只集中於本土植物，可能錯過引入植物如何運作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a systematic study of plants.","zh":"這個片語指對植物的系統研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"flora","meaning":"植物群","examples":[{"en":"The survey examined the flora of Ascension.","zh":"該調查檢視阿森松島的植物群。"},{"en":"Flora means all the plant life in a particular area.","zh":"flora 指某特定地區的全部植物生命。"},{"en":"A nature guide may describe the flora of a country park.","zh":"自然導賞手冊可能描述郊野公園的植物群。"},{"en":"If the flora changes, animals that depend on those plants may also change.","zh":"如果植物群改變，依賴那些植物的動物也可能改變。"},{"en":"The word refers to plants, while fauna refers to animals.","zh":"這個詞指植物，而 fauna 則指動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be concerned only with","meaning":"只關注……","examples":[{"en":"The researchers were concerned only with endemic species.","zh":"研究人員只關注特有物種。"},{"en":"Be concerned only with means focus on just one issue and ignore others.","zh":"be concerned only with 指只集中於一個問題而忽略其他問題。"},{"en":"A teacher concerned only with grammar may miss problems with ideas and organisation.","zh":"只關注文法的老師可能錯過思想和組織方面的問題。"},{"en":"If researchers study only endemic plants, they may overlook the wider forest system.","zh":"如果研究人員只研究特有植物，可能忽略更廣泛的森林系統。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a narrow focus.","zh":"這個片語暗示焦點狹窄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"characterise something as a threat","meaning":"將……形容為威脅","examples":[{"en":"The researchers characterised every introduced species as a threat.","zh":"研究人員將每個引入物種都形容為威脅。"},{"en":"Characterise something as a threat means describe it as dangerous or harmful.","zh":"characterise something as a threat 指把某事描述為危險或有害。"},{"en":"A school may characterise cyberbullying as a serious threat to student wellbeing.","zh":"學校可能把網絡欺凌形容為對學生福祉的嚴重威脅。"},{"en":"If all foreign plants are labelled threats, their possible benefits may be ignored.","zh":"如果所有外來植物都被標籤為威脅，其可能好處就可能被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how something is framed or presented.","zh":"這個片語描述某事如何被框定或呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Ascension authorities","meaning":"阿森松島當局","examples":[{"en":"The Ascension authorities are creating a national park.","zh":"阿森松島當局正在建立一個國家公園。"},{"en":"Ascension authorities are the officials or governing bodies responsible for managing Ascension.","zh":"Ascension authorities 指負責管理阿森松島的官員或管治機構。"},{"en":"Local authorities may decide how parks, roads, and public services are managed.","zh":"地方當局可能決定公園、道路和公共服務如何管理。"},{"en":"If authorities control land use, they can decide which plants to protect or remove.","zh":"如果當局控制土地使用，就能決定保護或移除哪些植物。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the island’s governing decision-makers.","zh":"這個片語指該島的管治決策者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"turn something into a national park","meaning":"將……改建為國家公園","examples":[{"en":"The authorities are turning Green Mountain into a national park.","zh":"當局正將 Green Mountain 改建為國家公園。"},{"en":"Turn something into a national park means officially manage an area for protection, recreation, or conservation.","zh":"turn something into a national park 指正式管理某地，以作保護、康樂或保育用途。"},{"en":"A government may turn a wetland into a national park to protect birds.","zh":"政府可能把濕地改建為國家公園，以保護鳥類。"},{"en":"If an area becomes a national park, rules may limit building, hunting, or plant removal.","zh":"如果某地成為國家公園，規則可能限制建築、狩獵或移除植物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes official land-use change.","zh":"這個片語描述官方土地用途改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"invasive species","meaning":"入侵物種","examples":[{"en":"Some introduced plants are classified as invasive species.","zh":"有些引入植物被分類為入侵物種。"},{"en":"Invasive species are non-native organisms that spread and harm local ecosystems.","zh":"invasive species 指非本土、會擴散並傷害本地生態系統的生物。"},{"en":"An invasive plant may cover a riverbank and block native plants from growing.","zh":"入侵植物可能覆蓋河岸，阻止本土植物生長。"},{"en":"If invasive species spread unchecked, they can reduce biodiversity.","zh":"如果入侵物種不受控制地擴散，就會降低生物多樣性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes foreign species that cause ecological damage.","zh":"這個片語描述造成生態破壞的外來物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be earmarked for","meaning":"被指定作……用途","examples":[{"en":"Invasive species are earmarked for culling.","zh":"入侵物種被指定作選擇性移除。"},{"en":"Be earmarked for means be officially chosen or planned for a particular purpose.","zh":"be earmarked for 指被官方選定或計劃作某用途。"},{"en":"Money may be earmarked for repairing school roofs after a storm.","zh":"風暴後，資金可能被指定用於修理學校屋頂。"},{"en":"If plants are earmarked for removal, authorities have already decided their future use or treatment.","zh":"如果植物被指定移除，當局已決定其未來處理方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes planned allocation or selection.","zh":"這個片語描述有計劃的分配或選定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"culling","meaning":"選擇性移除；撲殺","examples":[{"en":"Some introduced species are earmarked for culling.","zh":"有些引入物種被指定作選擇性移除。"},{"en":"Culling is the controlled removal or killing of selected plants or animals.","zh":"culling 指有控制地移除或殺死被選定的植物或動物。"},{"en":"A park may use culling to control an animal population that is damaging habitat.","zh":"公園可能使用撲殺來控制破壞棲息地的動物種群。"},{"en":"If a plant is culled, managers hope to protect other species or restore balance.","zh":"如果植物被選擇性移除，管理者希望保護其他物種或恢復平衡。"},{"en":"The word often appears in wildlife and conservation management.","zh":"這個詞常出現在野生動物和保育管理中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rather than conservation","meaning":"而不是保育","examples":[{"en":"The invasive plants are marked for removal rather than conservation.","zh":"入侵植物被標記為移除，而不是保育。"},{"en":"Rather than conservation means instead of being protected and preserved.","zh":"rather than conservation 指不是被保護和保存，而是作其他處理。"},{"en":"A dangerous old building may be marked for demolition rather than restoration.","zh":"危險舊建築可能被標記為拆卸，而不是修復。"},{"en":"If authorities see a plant as invasive, they may remove it instead of protecting it.","zh":"如果當局把植物視為入侵物種，可能會移除它而不是保護它。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a clear contrast between two policies.","zh":"這個片語清楚對比兩種政策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"understandable concerns","meaning":"可以理解的憂慮","examples":[{"en":"Conservationists have understandable concerns about endemic species.","zh":"保育人士對特有物種有可以理解的憂慮。"},{"en":"Understandable concerns are worries that are reasonable and easy to sympathise with.","zh":"understandable concerns 指合理且容易令人同情的擔憂。"},{"en":"Parents have understandable concerns when a school bus route changes suddenly.","zh":"當校巴路線突然改變，家長有可以理解的憂慮。"},{"en":"If unique species may disappear, concern about their survival is reasonable.","zh":"如果獨有物種可能消失，對其生存感到憂慮是合理的。"},{"en":"The phrase respects the worry even if the writer questions the response.","zh":"這個片語尊重該擔憂，即使作者質疑其反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"go extinct","meaning":"滅絕","examples":[{"en":"At least four endemic species have gone extinct on Ascension.","zh":"至少四種特有物種已在阿森松島滅絕。"},{"en":"Go extinct means disappear completely as a species.","zh":"go extinct 指作為物種完全消失。"},{"en":"A language may go extinct if no children learn to speak it.","zh":"如果沒有孩子學會說某語言，該語言可能消失。"},{"en":"If a plant exists only on one island, it can go extinct when its last population dies.","zh":"如果植物只存在於一個島，當最後一個種群死亡時就會滅絕。"},{"en":"The phrase is commonly used for species loss.","zh":"這個片語常用於物種消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"since the exotics started arriving","meaning":"自外來物種開始到來以來","examples":[{"en":"Several native plants disappeared after the exotic species arrived.","zh":"自外來物種開始到來以來，幾種本土植物消失了。"},{"en":"Since the exotics started arriving means from the time foreign species began to come in.","zh":"since the exotics started arriving 指從外來物種開始進入某地的時候起。"},{"en":"Since new shops started arriving, the old market has become busier.","zh":"自新商店開始進駐以來，舊街市變得更繁忙。"},{"en":"If native plants disappeared after exotics arrived, ecologists may suspect competition.","zh":"如果本土植物在外來物種到來後消失，生態學家可能懷疑競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase links a period of change with the arrival of outside species.","zh":"這個片語把變化時期與外來物種到達連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in their urgency to","meaning":"在急於……的情況下","examples":[{"en":"In their urgency to protect native plants, scientists may overlook other issues.","zh":"在急於保護本土植物的情況下，科學家可能忽略其他問題。"},{"en":"In their urgency to means because they are acting quickly and anxiously to do something.","zh":"in their urgency to 指因急切而焦慮地想做某事。"},{"en":"In their urgency to finish homework, students may forget to check grammar.","zh":"學生在急於完成功課的情況下，可能忘記檢查文法。"},{"en":"If people rush to protect one thing, they may miss another important question.","zh":"如果人們急於保護一件事，可能錯過另一個重要問題。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests haste caused by strong concern.","zh":"這個片語暗示由強烈關注造成的匆忙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"protect endemics","meaning":"保護特有物種","examples":[{"en":"Conservationists are trying to protect endemics from extinction.","zh":"保育人士正嘗試保護特有物種免於滅絕。"},{"en":"Protect endemics means safeguard species found only in one particular place.","zh":"protect endemics 指保護只在某一特定地方出現的物種。"},{"en":"A nature reserve may protect endemic birds by limiting visitors during breeding season.","zh":"自然保護區可能在繁殖季節限制訪客，以保護特有鳥類。"},{"en":"If endemics disappear, the world loses species that cannot be replaced elsewhere.","zh":"如果特有物種消失，世界就失去無法在其他地方取代的物種。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on protecting locally unique life.","zh":"這個片語集中於保護本地獨有生命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"miss out on","meaning":"錯過……","examples":[{"en":"Ecologists may be missing out on the study of an important mystery.","zh":"生態學家可能正在錯過研究一個重要謎團的機會。"},{"en":"Miss out on means fail to get, experience, or notice something valuable.","zh":"miss out on 指未能得到、經歷或注意到有價值的東西。"},{"en":"A student may miss out on marks if they forget to answer the final question.","zh":"如果學生忘記回答最後一題，可能錯過分數。"},{"en":"If researchers focus too narrowly, they may miss out on a larger scientific opportunity.","zh":"如果研究人員焦點太狹窄，可能錯過更大的科學機會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes losing a chance.","zh":"這個片語描述失去機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a great enigma","meaning":"巨大謎團","examples":[{"en":"The origins of the new ecosystem remain a great enigma.","zh":"新生態系統的起源仍是一個巨大謎團。"},{"en":"A great enigma is a major mystery that is difficult to explain.","zh":"a great enigma 指難以解釋的重大謎團。"},{"en":"Why one student suddenly improves after months of struggle can be a great enigma until the teacher learns what changed.","zh":"一名學生在掙扎數月後突然進步，在老師了解改變之前可能是巨大謎團。"},{"en":"If a forest forms in an unexpected way, its origin becomes a scientific puzzle.","zh":"如果森林以意想不到的方式形成，其起源就成為科學謎題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a deep and fascinating mystery.","zh":"這個片語描述深刻而引人入勝的謎團。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"chunks taken out of","meaning":"被咬去一大塊","examples":[{"en":"Many leaves have chunks taken out of them by insects.","zh":"許多葉子被昆蟲咬去一大塊。"},{"en":"Chunks taken out of means large pieces have been bitten, cut, or removed.","zh":"chunks taken out of 指大塊部分被咬走、切走或移除。"},{"en":"A sandwich may have chunks taken out of it if a hungry child keeps taking bites.","zh":"如果飢餓孩子一直咬，三文治可能被咬去一大塊。"},{"en":"If insects feed heavily on leaves, missing pieces can show their activity.","zh":"如果昆蟲大量吃葉，缺失部分可以顯示牠們的活動。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a visible sign of damage or feeding.","zh":"這個片語給出受損或被進食的可見跡象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"various insects","meaning":"各種昆蟲","examples":[{"en":"Various insects feed on plants in the forest.","zh":"各種昆蟲以森林中的植物為食。"},{"en":"Various insects means several different kinds of insects.","zh":"various insects 指幾種不同昆蟲。"},{"en":"A school garden may attract various insects, including bees, butterflies, and beetles.","zh":"學校花園可能吸引各種昆蟲，包括蜜蜂、蝴蝶和甲蟲。"},{"en":"If many insects use the plants, the forest may already have complex food relationships.","zh":"如果許多昆蟲使用這些植物，森林可能已有複雜食物關係。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses variety among insects.","zh":"這個片語強調昆蟲種類多樣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"caterpillars and beetles","meaning":"毛蟲和甲蟲","examples":[{"en":"Caterpillars and beetles can be found throughout the forest.","zh":"毛蟲和甲蟲可在整片森林中找到。"},{"en":"Caterpillars and beetles are common insects, often feeding on leaves, wood, or plant material.","zh":"caterpillars and beetles 指常見昆蟲，通常以葉、木或植物物質為食。"},{"en":"Children may find caterpillars and beetles in a garden after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，孩子可能在花園中找到毛蟲和甲蟲。"},{"en":"If these insects feed on introduced plants, new food links may be forming.","zh":"如果這些昆蟲以引入植物為食，新的食物連結可能正在形成。"},{"en":"The phrase names two visible groups of insects.","zh":"這個片語指出兩類可見昆蟲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"endemic or alien","meaning":"本地特有還是外來的","examples":[{"en":"Scientists do not know whether some insects are endemic or alien.","zh":"科學家不知道某些昆蟲是本地特有還是外來的。"},{"en":"Endemic or alien means native and unique to the place, or introduced from elsewhere.","zh":"endemic or alien 指本地獨有，或從其他地方引入。"},{"en":"A plant in a city park may be endemic or alien, depending on where it originally came from.","zh":"城市公園中的植物可能是本地特有或外來，視乎其原產地。"},{"en":"If insects are alien, they may have arrived with imported plants.","zh":"如果昆蟲是外來的，牠們可能隨引入植物到達。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts local origin with foreign origin.","zh":"這個片語對比本地來源和外來來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"alien species","meaning":"外來物種","examples":[{"en":"Some of the insects may be alien species.","zh":"有些昆蟲可能是外來物種。"},{"en":"Alien species are organisms that come from outside the local ecosystem.","zh":"alien species 指來自本地生態系統以外的生物。"},{"en":"A fish released from an aquarium may become an alien species in a local pond.","zh":"從水族箱放生的魚可能成為本地池塘中的外來物種。"},{"en":"If alien species spread quickly, they may change food webs and habitats.","zh":"如果外來物種快速擴散，就可能改變食物網和棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase means foreign to the ecosystem, not from outer space.","zh":"這個片語指對生態系統而言是外來的，不是來自太空。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"come with the plant","meaning":"隨植物一同到來","examples":[{"en":"An insect may have come with the plant on which it feeds.","zh":"昆蟲可能隨牠所吃的植物一同到來。"},{"en":"Come with the plant means arrive accidentally together with the imported plant.","zh":"come with the plant 指與引入植物一起意外到達。"},{"en":"Small insects may come with vegetables if they hide under leaves.","zh":"如果小昆蟲藏在葉底，牠們可能隨蔬菜一起到來。"},{"en":"If a plant is transported across oceans, insects or eggs may travel with it unnoticed.","zh":"如果植物被運過海洋，昆蟲或蟲卵可能在不被察覺下同行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes accidental introduction through transport.","zh":"這個片語描述透過運輸意外引入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"feed on","meaning":"以……為食","examples":[{"en":"Some insects feed on the introduced plants.","zh":"有些昆蟲以引入植物為食。"},{"en":"Feed on means eat a particular thing as food.","zh":"feed on 指把某物作為食物來吃。"},{"en":"Caterpillars feed on leaves in many gardens.","zh":"許多花園中的毛蟲以葉子為食。"},{"en":"If insects feed on a plant, they may leave holes or missing pieces in its leaves.","zh":"如果昆蟲以植物為食，可能在葉子上留下洞或缺口。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what an organism eats.","zh":"這個片語描述生物吃甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"discover it on arrival","meaning":"到達後才發現它","examples":[{"en":"The insects may have discovered a new food source on arrival.","zh":"昆蟲可能到達後才發現新的食物來源。"},{"en":"Discover it on arrival means find something only after reaching a new place.","zh":"discover it on arrival 指到達新地方後才找到某物。"},{"en":"A student may discover a quiet study room on arrival at a new school.","zh":"學生到達新學校後才可能發現一間安靜自修室。"},{"en":"If insects did not travel with the plant, they may have found it after arriving separately.","zh":"如果昆蟲不是隨植物而來，牠們可能是分開到達後才找到它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes finding something after entering a place.","zh":"這個片語描述進入某地後找到某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"go to the heart of how","meaning":"觸及……如何形成的核心","examples":[{"en":"These questions go to the heart of how rainforests develop.","zh":"這些問題觸及熱帶雨林如何形成的核心。"},{"en":"Go to the heart of how means address the central question about the way something happens.","zh":"go to the heart of how 指處理關於某事如何發生的核心問題。"},{"en":"Asking why students fear speaking goes to the heart of how confidence develops.","zh":"詢問學生為何害怕說話，觸及自信如何形成的核心。"},{"en":"If insect relationships show how a new forest works, they address the core ecological issue.","zh":"如果昆蟲關係顯示新森林如何運作，它們就觸及核心生態問題。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the deepest part of an explanation.","zh":"這個片語指向解釋最深層部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"hold many secrets","meaning":"蘊藏很多秘密","examples":[{"en":"The Green Mountain forest holds many secrets.","zh":"Green Mountain 森林蘊藏很多秘密。"},{"en":"Hold many secrets means contain many unknown facts or mysteries.","zh":"hold many secrets 指包含許多未知事實或謎團。"},{"en":"An old family photo album may hold many secrets about past generations.","zh":"一本舊家庭相簿可能蘊藏許多關於前幾代人的秘密。"},{"en":"If a forest has not been studied properly, it may contain hidden ecological relationships.","zh":"如果一片森林未被正式研究，它可能包含隱藏的生態關係。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that much remains to be discovered.","zh":"這個片語暗示仍有許多東西有待發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the irony is that","meaning":"諷刺的是","examples":[{"en":"The irony is that an artificial forest may teach us about natural forests.","zh":"諷刺的是，一片人工森林可能教會我們關於天然森林的知識。"},{"en":"The irony is that introduces a surprising contrast between what we expect and what is true.","zh":"the irony is that 引出期望與事實之間令人意外的對比。"},{"en":"The irony is that the quietest student may give the strongest speech.","zh":"諷刺的是，最安靜的學生可能作出最有力的演講。"},{"en":"If an artificial forest explains natural forests better than wild forests do, the result is ironic.","zh":"如果人工森林比野生森林更能解釋天然森林，結果就很諷刺。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights an unexpected reversal.","zh":"這個片語突出意想不到的反轉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"artificial rainforest","meaning":"人工形成的雨林","examples":[{"en":"Green Mountain may be the most artificial rainforest in the world.","zh":"Green Mountain 可能是世界上最人工形成的雨林。"},{"en":"An artificial rainforest is a rainforest-like ecosystem created or heavily shaped by humans.","zh":"artificial rainforest 指由人類創造或深度塑造、類似雨林的生態系統。"},{"en":"A greenhouse can contain an artificial rainforest for education or conservation.","zh":"溫室可以設有人造雨林，用於教育或保育。"},{"en":"If people plant the species and shape the environment, the forest is not purely natural.","zh":"如果人們種植物種並塑造環境，該森林就不是純天然的。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts human origin with rainforest appearance.","zh":"這個片語把人類起源與雨林外觀作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"tell us more about","meaning":"令我們更了解……","examples":[{"en":"The forest could tell us more about rainforest ecology.","zh":"這片森林可以令我們更了解雨林生態學。"},{"en":"Tell us more about means help us understand something more deeply.","zh":"tell us more about 指幫助我們更深入理解某事。"},{"en":"Student mistakes can tell teachers more about what learners do not yet understand.","zh":"學生錯誤可以令老師更了解學習者尚未明白的地方。"},{"en":"If Green Mountain formed quickly, it may reveal how ecosystems assemble.","zh":"如果 Green Mountain 快速形成，它可能揭示生態系統如何組合。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something acting as evidence or a lesson.","zh":"這個片語描述某物作為證據或教訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"rainforest ecology","meaning":"雨林生態學","examples":[{"en":"Green Mountain may offer valuable lessons about rainforest ecology.","zh":"Green Mountain 可能提供關於雨林生態學的寶貴教訓。"},{"en":"Rainforest ecology is the study of how rainforest organisms and environments interact.","zh":"rainforest ecology 指研究雨林生物和環境如何互動的學科。"},{"en":"Students studying rainforest ecology learn about trees, insects, soil, rainfall, and food webs.","zh":"學生研究雨林生態學時，會學到樹木、昆蟲、土壤、降雨和食物網。"},{"en":"If an artificial rainforest works, it may challenge ideas about natural rainforest ecology.","zh":"如果人工雨林能運作，它可能挑戰關於天然雨林生態學的觀點。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the science of rainforest systems.","zh":"這個片語指雨林系統的科學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"any number of","meaning":"許多；任意數量的","examples":[{"en":"One artificial forest may be more informative than any number of natural forests.","zh":"一片人工森林可能比許多天然森林更有啟發性。"},{"en":"Any number of means many, or even a very large number of something.","zh":"any number of 指許多，甚至非常大量的某物。"},{"en":"A clear example can teach more than any number of vague explanations.","zh":"一個清楚例子可能比許多含糊解釋更有教學作用。"},{"en":"If one unusual case reveals a hidden rule, it may be more useful than many ordinary cases.","zh":"如果一個不尋常案例揭示隱藏規律，它可能比許多普通案例更有用。"},{"en":"The phrase exaggerates to stress quantity.","zh":"這個片語用誇張方式強調數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與文章資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷每句陳述是否與文章一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the information means match what the text says.","zh":"agree with the information 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"In a reading test, a statement agrees with the information if it repeats the same meaning accurately.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，如果陳述準確重述同一意思，就與資料一致。"},{"en":"If a statement changes one important detail, it may no longer agree with the passage.","zh":"如果陳述改變一個重要細節，就可能不再與文章一致。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in True, False, Not Given questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於 True, False, Not Given 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文章資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradict the information means say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章內容相反的意思。"},{"en":"If a passage says the island was bare, a statement saying it was thickly forested would contradict it.","zh":"如果文章說該島光禿，而陳述說它森林茂密，就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should choose False only when there is a clear conflict with the passage.","zh":"學生只有在與文章有清楚衝突時才應選 False。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct disagreement with the text.","zh":"這個片語描述與文本直接不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有關於此事的資料","examples":[{"en":"Not Given means that there is no information on the point.","zh":"Not Given 指文章沒有關於該點的資料。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有說明該陳述是真是假。"},{"en":"If the passage mentions plants but not the sailors’ ages, there is no information on that detail.","zh":"如果文章提到植物但沒有提到水手年齡，就沒有關於該細節的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from outside knowledge when the passage gives no information.","zh":"當文章沒有資料時，學生不應用外部知識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase explains when to choose Not Given.","zh":"這個片語解釋何時選 Not Given。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"inhabitants on the island","meaning":"島上的居民","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Osbeck found inhabitants on the island.","zh":"題目問 Osbeck 是否在島上發現居民。"},{"en":"Inhabitants on the island are people or animals living there.","zh":"inhabitants on the island 指生活在島上的人或動物。"},{"en":"A census counts the inhabitants on an island to plan schools and services.","zh":"人口普查會點算島上居民，以規劃學校和服務。"},{"en":"If early visitors mention no inhabitants, students should not assume people lived there.","zh":"如果早期訪客沒有提到居民，學生不應假定那裡有人居住。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to living residents of the island.","zh":"這個片語指島上的居住者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"natural vegetation","meaning":"天然植被","examples":[{"en":"The island’s natural vegetation included several unusual ferns.","zh":"該島的天然植被包括幾種不尋常的蕨類植物。"},{"en":"Natural vegetation is the plant life that grows in a place without being planted by people.","zh":"natural vegetation 指在某地自然生長、不是由人種植的植物生命。"},{"en":"A hillside’s natural vegetation may include grasses, shrubs, and native trees.","zh":"山坡的天然植被可能包括草、灌木和本土樹木。"},{"en":"If natural vegetation is removed, soil and animal habitat may be damaged.","zh":"如果天然植被被移除，土壤和動物棲息地可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts native plant cover with planted vegetation.","zh":"這個片語把原生植物覆蓋與人工種植植被作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"found nowhere else","meaning":"在其他地方找不到","examples":[{"en":"Some plants on Ascension were found nowhere else.","zh":"阿森松島上的有些植物在其他地方找不到。"},{"en":"Found nowhere else means existing only in that one place.","zh":"found nowhere else 指只存在於那一個地方。"},{"en":"A local snack recipe may be found nowhere else if only one village still makes it.","zh":"如果只有一條村仍製作某本地小食食譜，它可能在其他地方找不到。"},{"en":"If a species is found nowhere else, losing it from one island means global extinction.","zh":"如果物種在其他地方找不到，從一個島消失就等於全球滅絕。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses complete uniqueness of location.","zh":"這個片語強調地點上的完全獨特性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"assume that","meaning":"假定；認為","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Hooker assumed that people had caused the damage.","zh":"題目問 Hooker 是否假定人類造成了破壞。"},{"en":"Assume that means believe something is true without full proof.","zh":"assume that 指在沒有完整證據下相信某事是真的。"},{"en":"A teacher should not assume that quiet students understand everything.","zh":"老師不應假定安靜學生甚麼都明白。"},{"en":"If evidence is limited, assuming a cause can lead to mistakes.","zh":"如果證據有限，假定某原因可能導致錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an unproven belief.","zh":"這個片語描述未經證明的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"human activity","meaning":"人類活動","examples":[{"en":"The decline in vegetation was not originally blamed on human activity.","zh":"植被下降最初並沒有被歸咎於人類活動。"},{"en":"Human activity means actions done by people, such as farming, building, hunting, or planting.","zh":"human activity 指人類所做的行動，例如耕作、建築、狩獵或種植。"},{"en":"Cutting trees for roads is a form of human activity that changes habitats.","zh":"為道路砍伐樹木是改變棲息地的人類活動。"},{"en":"If human activity damages vegetation, rainfall and soil conditions may also change.","zh":"如果人類活動破壞植被，降雨和土壤條件也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies people as the source of change.","zh":"這個片語指出人類是變化來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"cause a decline in","meaning":"導致……下降","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to activity that may cause a decline in plant life.","zh":"題目提到可能導致植物生命下降的活動。"},{"en":"Cause a decline in means make something decrease.","zh":"cause a decline in 指令某事減少。"},{"en":"Poor teaching may cause a decline in students’ interest in reading.","zh":"差劣教學可能導致學生閱讀興趣下降。"},{"en":"If too many trees are cut, plant life in the area may decline.","zh":"如果砍伐太多樹，該區植物生命可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a cause with reduction.","zh":"這個片語把原因與減少連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"take part in","meaning":"參與……","examples":[{"en":"British sailors took part in the tree-planting project.","zh":"英國水手參與了植樹項目。"},{"en":"Take part in means participate in an activity.","zh":"take part in 指參與某活動。"},{"en":"Students may take part in a beach clean-up after school.","zh":"學生可能在放學後參與海灘清潔活動。"},{"en":"If many people take part in a project, the work can be completed more quickly.","zh":"如果許多人參與項目，工作可以更快完成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active involvement.","zh":"這個片語描述主動投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"major tree-planting project","meaning":"大型植樹計劃","examples":[{"en":"The sailors participated in a major tree-planting project.","zh":"水手參與了一項大型植樹計劃。"},{"en":"A major tree-planting project is a large organised effort to plant many trees.","zh":"major tree-planting project 指有組織地種植大量樹木的大型工作。"},{"en":"A city may run a major tree-planting project to cool streets and improve air quality.","zh":"城市可能推行大型植樹計劃，以為街道降溫並改善空氣質素。"},{"en":"If thousands of trees are planted each year, the landscape can change dramatically.","zh":"如果每年種植數千棵樹，景觀可以大幅改變。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both scale and organisation.","zh":"這個片語強調規模和組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"details of a planting scheme","meaning":"植樹計劃的細節","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to details of Hooker’s planting scheme.","zh":"題目提到 Hooker 植樹計劃的細節。"},{"en":"Details of a planting scheme are specific facts about what was planted, where, and how.","zh":"details of a planting scheme 指關於種植了甚麼、在哪裡種植和如何種植的具體資料。"},{"en":"A school garden plan should include details of a planting scheme, such as seed types and watering times.","zh":"學校花園計劃應包括植樹計劃的細節，例如種子種類和澆水時間。"},{"en":"If details are missing, students cannot know exactly how the project was carried out.","zh":"如果缺少細節，學生就不能確切知道該項目如何進行。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical information about a planting plan.","zh":"這個片語指關於種植計劃的實際資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be unsuitable for","meaning":"不適合……","examples":[{"en":"Some plants may be unsuitable for a particular climate.","zh":"有些植物可能不適合特定氣候。"},{"en":"Be unsuitable for means not fit or not appropriate for a particular use, place, or condition.","zh":"be unsuitable for 指不適合某用途、地方或條件。"},{"en":"Thin shoes are unsuitable for hiking on wet mountain paths.","zh":"薄鞋不適合在濕滑山路遠足。"},{"en":"If a plant is unsuitable for dry soil, it may die soon after planting.","zh":"如果植物不適合乾燥土壤，種下後可能很快死亡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes poor fit between something and its environment.","zh":"這個片語描述某物與其環境不匹配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete each sentence","meaning":"完成每個句子","examples":[{"en":"Students complete each sentence with the correct ending.","zh":"學生用正確結尾完成每個句子。"},{"en":"Complete each sentence means finish every sentence by adding the missing part.","zh":"complete each sentence 指加入缺失部分，使每句句子完整。"},{"en":"In grammar practice, students complete each sentence by choosing the correct verb form.","zh":"在文法練習中，學生透過選擇正確動詞形式完成每個句子。"},{"en":"If the ending does not match the meaning, the sentence becomes incorrect.","zh":"如果結尾與意思不配合，句子就會錯。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction in matching exercises.","zh":"這個片語是配對練習中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the correct ending","meaning":"正確結尾","examples":[{"en":"Each sentence must be matched with the correct ending.","zh":"每句句子必須與正確結尾配對。"},{"en":"The correct ending is the sentence part that completes both meaning and grammar properly.","zh":"the correct ending 指在意思和文法上都能正確完成句子的部分。"},{"en":"A student should check whether the correct ending fits the subject and verb.","zh":"學生應檢查正確結尾是否配合主語和動詞。"},{"en":"If two endings seem possible, the passage meaning decides which one is correct.","zh":"如果兩個結尾看似可行，文章意思決定哪一個正確。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the right final part of a sentence.","zh":"這個片語指句子的正確最後部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"concern over","meaning":"對……的關注","examples":[{"en":"Conservationists expressed concern over Hooker’s planting programme.","zh":"保育人士對 Hooker 的植樹計劃表示關注。"},{"en":"Concern over means worry about a problem or possible danger.","zh":"concern over 指對問題或可能危險的擔憂。"},{"en":"Parents may express concern over traffic outside a school.","zh":"家長可能對學校外交通表示關注。"},{"en":"If introduced plants threaten native species, conservationists naturally become worried.","zh":"如果引入植物威脅本土物種，保育人士自然會擔心。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces anxiety about an issue.","zh":"這個片語引出對某議題的憂慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be threatened with destruction","meaning":"面臨被破壞的威脅","examples":[{"en":"Many original species were threatened with destruction.","zh":"許多原有物種面臨被破壞的威脅。"},{"en":"Be threatened with destruction means face the danger of being damaged or wiped out.","zh":"be threatened with destruction 指面臨被破壞或消滅的危險。"},{"en":"An old market may be threatened with destruction if a new road is planned through it.","zh":"如果新道路計劃穿過舊街市，舊街市可能面臨被拆毀的威脅。"},{"en":"If native plants are outcompeted, their survival may become uncertain.","zh":"如果本土植物被競爭勝過，其生存可能變得不確定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious danger to continued existence.","zh":"這個片語描述對持續存在的嚴重危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"randomly introduced species","meaning":"隨機引入的物種","examples":[{"en":"Randomly introduced species created the Green Mountain forest.","zh":"隨機引入的物種創造了 Green Mountain 森林。"},{"en":"Randomly introduced species are species brought into a place without careful ecological planning.","zh":"randomly introduced species 指未經仔細生態規劃而被帶入某地的物種。"},{"en":"A garden planted with random seeds may contain a surprising mix of flowers and weeds.","zh":"用隨機種子種出的花園可能含有令人意外的花和雜草混合。"},{"en":"If introduced species are random, their relationships may form by chance.","zh":"如果引入物種是隨機的，牠們之間的關係可能偶然形成。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses unplanned introduction.","zh":"這個片語強調沒有計劃的引入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"coexist","meaning":"共存","examples":[{"en":"Very different species can coexist within one ecosystem.","zh":"非常不同的物種可以在同一生態系統中共存。"},{"en":"Coexist means live or exist together in the same place.","zh":"coexist 指在同一地方一起生活或存在。"},{"en":"Students with different personalities can coexist peacefully in one class if rules are fair.","zh":"如果規則公平，性格不同的學生可以在同一班和平共存。"},{"en":"If species use different resources, they may coexist without strong competition.","zh":"如果物種使用不同資源，牠們可能共存而沒有強烈競爭。"},{"en":"The word stresses shared existence.","zh":"這個詞強調共同存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"ecological significance","meaning":"生態重要性","examples":[{"en":"The imported plants may have less ecological significance than native species.","zh":"引入植物的生態重要性可能低於本土物種。"},{"en":"Ecological significance means importance within an ecosystem’s structure or function.","zh":"ecological significance 指在生態系統結構或功能中的重要性。"},{"en":"Bees have ecological significance because they help many plants reproduce.","zh":"蜜蜂具有生態重要性，因為牠們幫助許多植物繁殖。"},{"en":"If a species supports food webs or soil health, its ecological significance is high.","zh":"如果某物種支持食物網或土壤健康，其生態重要性就高。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ecological importance, not beauty.","zh":"這個片語描述生態上的重要性，而不是美感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"challenge the theory that","meaning":"挑戰……的理論","examples":[{"en":"The forest challenges the theory that ecosystems must evolve slowly.","zh":"這片森林挑戰生態系統必須緩慢演化的理論。"},{"en":"Challenge the theory that means question whether a theory is correct.","zh":"challenge the theory that 指質疑某理論是否正確。"},{"en":"New exam results may challenge the theory that more homework always improves learning.","zh":"新考試結果可能挑戰功課越多學習越好的理論。"},{"en":"If an ecosystem forms quickly, it questions the idea that slow evolution is always necessary.","zh":"如果生態系統快速形成，就質疑緩慢演化永遠必要的想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence putting pressure on a belief.","zh":"這個片語描述證據對某信念造成壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"additional support for","meaning":"對……的額外支持","examples":[{"en":"Research elsewhere provides additional support for Wilkinson’s theory.","zh":"其他地方的研究為 Wilkinson 的理論提供額外支持。"},{"en":"Additional support for means extra evidence or reasons that make an idea stronger.","zh":"additional support for 指令某想法更有力的額外證據或理由。"},{"en":"A second experiment can provide additional support for a student’s science project.","zh":"第二個實驗可以為學生科學項目提供額外支持。"},{"en":"If other forests show human origins, Wilkinson’s argument becomes more convincing.","zh":"如果其他森林顯示人類起源，Wilkinson 的論點就更有說服力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence added to an existing claim.","zh":"這個片語描述加入既有主張的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"come from findings that","meaning":"來自……的研究結果","examples":[{"en":"Additional support comes from findings that some rainforests were planted.","zh":"額外支持來自一些雨林曾被種植的研究結果。"},{"en":"Come from findings that means be based on research results showing something.","zh":"come from findings that 指基於顯示某事的研究結果。"},{"en":"A school policy may come from findings that students learn better after breaks.","zh":"學校政策可能來自學生休息後學得更好的研究結果。"},{"en":"If research findings show planted origins, they can support the theory of rapid formation.","zh":"如果研究結果顯示種植起源，就能支持快速形成理論。"},{"en":"The phrase links support to evidence.","zh":"這個片語把支持與證據連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be misguided","meaning":"受到誤導；方向錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Wilkinson suggests that the conservationists’ priorities may be misguided.","zh":"Wilkinson 暗示保育人士的優先事項可能方向錯誤。"},{"en":"Be misguided means be based on wrong judgement or a mistaken understanding.","zh":"be misguided 指基於錯誤判斷或誤解。"},{"en":"A student’s revision plan may be misguided if it ignores the weakest topics.","zh":"如果學生的溫習計劃忽略最弱課題，它可能方向錯誤。"},{"en":"If conservation focuses only on removing exotics, it may miss the larger ecological mystery.","zh":"如果保育只集中於移除外來物種，可能錯過更大的生態謎團。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises the direction of thinking or action.","zh":"這個片語批評思考或行動方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"以……為基礎","examples":[{"en":"Environmental policies should be based on reliable scientific evidence.","zh":"環境政策應以可靠科學證據為基礎。"},{"en":"Be based on means be built from or supported by something.","zh":"be based on 指以某事建立或受某事支持。"},{"en":"A good essay should be based on clear arguments and relevant examples.","zh":"好文章應以清楚論點和相關例子為基礎。"},{"en":"If policy is based on weak evidence, it may solve the wrong problem.","zh":"如果政策以薄弱證據為基礎，可能解決錯誤問題。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a decision with its foundation.","zh":"這個片語把決定與其基礎連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"focus on the most important question","meaning":"集中於最重要的問題","examples":[{"en":"Researchers should focus on the most important ecological question.","zh":"研究人員應集中於最重要的生態問題。"},{"en":"Focus on the most important question means give attention to the central issue rather than side details.","zh":"focus on the most important question 指注意核心問題，而不是旁枝細節。"},{"en":"In an exam, students should focus on the main question instead of copying every detail.","zh":"在考試中，學生應集中於主要問題，而不是抄下每個細節。"},{"en":"If researchers ask the wrong question, they may miss the real value of the forest.","zh":"如果研究人員問錯問題，可能錯過森林的真正價值。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses choosing the right priority.","zh":"這個片語強調選擇正確優先事項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be supported by","meaning":"得到……支持","examples":[{"en":"A scientific claim should be supported by evidence.","zh":"科學主張應得到證據支持。"},{"en":"Be supported by means be backed up or made stronger by something.","zh":"be supported by 指由某事支撐或令其更有力。"},{"en":"An essay point should be supported by examples from the text.","zh":"文章論點應由文本例子支持。"},{"en":"If a theory is supported by several studies, it becomes more credible.","zh":"如果理論得到幾項研究支持，它就變得更可信。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a claim with proof.","zh":"這個片語把主張與證明連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"local authorities","meaning":"地方當局","examples":[{"en":"The local authorities are responsible for managing Green Mountain.","zh":"地方當局負責管理 Green Mountain。"},{"en":"Local authorities are officials or organisations that govern a particular area.","zh":"local authorities 指管治某特定地區的官員或組織。"},{"en":"Local authorities may manage parks, roads, schools, and waste collection.","zh":"地方當局可能管理公園、道路、學校和垃圾收集。"},{"en":"If local authorities set conservation rules, they decide what can be removed or protected.","zh":"如果地方當局制定保育規則，它們就決定甚麼可以移除或保護。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to government bodies at a local level.","zh":"這個片語指地方層面的政府機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"studies of insects","meaning":"對昆蟲的研究","examples":[{"en":"Studies of insects could reveal how new ecosystems form.","zh":"對昆蟲的研究可以揭示新生態系統如何形成。"},{"en":"Studies of insects are investigations into insect species, behaviour, feeding, and relationships.","zh":"studies of insects 指研究昆蟲物種、行為、覓食和關係。"},{"en":"Students may do studies of insects by observing ants in a school garden.","zh":"學生可能透過觀察學校花園中的螞蟻來進行昆蟲研究。"},{"en":"If insects feed on introduced plants, they may show how food webs are forming.","zh":"如果昆蟲以引入植物為食，就可能顯示食物網如何形成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research into small but important animals.","zh":"這個片語描述對細小但重要動物的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"demonstrate the possibility of","meaning":"證明……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"The insects may demonstrate the possibility of new ecological relationships.","zh":"這些昆蟲可能證明新生態關係形成的可能性。"},{"en":"Demonstrate the possibility of means show that something can happen or exist.","zh":"demonstrate the possibility of 指顯示某事可以發生或存在。"},{"en":"A successful trial lesson can demonstrate the possibility of teaching grammar through games.","zh":"一堂成功試驗課可以證明透過遊戲教文法的可能性。"},{"en":"If insects adapt to new plants, they show that fresh ecological links can form.","zh":"如果昆蟲適應新植物，就顯示新生態連結可以形成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence that something is possible.","zh":"這個片語描述某事可行的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"ecological relationships","meaning":"生態關係","examples":[{"en":"New ecological relationships may form between unrelated species.","zh":"互不相關的物種之間可能形成新的生態關係。"},{"en":"Ecological relationships are connections between organisms, such as feeding, pollination, competition, or dependence.","zh":"ecological relationships 指生物之間的連繫，例如覓食、傳粉、競爭或依賴。"},{"en":"Bees and flowers have an ecological relationship because bees carry pollen.","zh":"蜜蜂和花有生態關係，因為蜜蜂傳播花粉。"},{"en":"If an insect begins eating a new plant, a new ecological relationship may appear.","zh":"如果昆蟲開始吃新植物，新的生態關係可能出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how living things interact.","zh":"這個片語描述生命體如何互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"previously unknown species","meaning":"以前未知的物種","examples":[{"en":"Researchers may discover previously unknown species on the island.","zh":"研究人員可能在島上發現以前未知的物種。"},{"en":"Previously unknown species are species that scientists had not identified before.","zh":"previously unknown species 指科學家以前未曾識別的物種。"},{"en":"A deep-sea expedition may find previously unknown species of fish or microbes.","zh":"深海考察可能發現以前未知的魚類或微生物物種。"},{"en":"If a forest has not been studied carefully, hidden species may remain unnoticed.","zh":"如果森林未被仔細研究，隱藏物種可能仍未被注意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes species new to science.","zh":"這個片語描述科學上的新物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"overall","meaning":"總括而言","examples":[{"en":"Overall, the writer stresses the rainforest’s unusual development.","zh":"總括而言，作者強調該雨林不尋常的發展。"},{"en":"Overall means considering the main situation as a whole.","zh":"overall 指從整體考慮主要情況。"},{"en":"Overall, the school trip was successful, although the bus was late.","zh":"總括而言，學校旅行是成功的，雖然巴士遲到。"},{"en":"If many details point to the same idea, an overview can summarise the whole message.","zh":"如果許多細節指向同一想法，總結可以概括整體信息。"},{"en":"The word introduces a general conclusion.","zh":"這個詞引出一般結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"unusual nature of","meaning":"……的不尋常特性","examples":[{"en":"The writer highlights the unusual nature of the forest’s structure.","zh":"作者突出該森林結構的不尋常特性。"},{"en":"Unusual nature of means the strange or unexpected quality of something.","zh":"unusual nature of 指某事物奇特或出乎意料的特質。"},{"en":"The unusual nature of a quiet student’s sudden anger may make a teacher ask what happened.","zh":"安靜學生突然發怒的不尋常特性，可能令老師詢問發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"If a forest forms from unrelated imported species, its structure is unusual.","zh":"如果森林由互不相關的引入物種形成，其結構就不尋常。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on what makes something different from normal.","zh":"這個片語集中於令某事不同於正常情況的特點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"ecological structure","meaning":"生態結構","examples":[{"en":"The rainforest has an unusual ecological structure.","zh":"該雨林有不尋常的生態結構。"},{"en":"Ecological structure is the way species and relationships are organised in an ecosystem.","zh":"ecological structure 指物種和關係在生態系統中的組織方式。"},{"en":"A pond’s ecological structure includes plants, insects, fish, and the links between them.","zh":"池塘的生態結構包括植物、昆蟲、魚和牠們之間的連繫。"},{"en":"If a forest is built from random species, its ecological structure may challenge normal theory.","zh":"如果森林由隨機物種組成，其生態結構可能挑戰一般理論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the organisation of living relationships.","zh":"這個片語描述生命關係的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"harm done by","meaning":"由……造成的傷害","examples":[{"en":"The passage considers the harm done by interfering with nature.","zh":"文章考慮干預大自然造成的傷害。"},{"en":"Harm done by means damage caused by a particular action or process.","zh":"harm done by 指由某行動或過程造成的損害。"},{"en":"The harm done by bullying can continue long after the incident ends.","zh":"欺凌造成的傷害可以在事件結束很久後仍持續。"},{"en":"If introduced species destroy native plants, the ecological harm may be serious.","zh":"如果引入物種摧毀本土植物，生態傷害可能很嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of damage.","zh":"這個片語指出傷害來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"interfere with nature","meaning":"干預大自然","examples":[{"en":"Introducing exotic plants can be seen as interfering with nature.","zh":"引入外來植物可被視為干預大自然。"},{"en":"Interfere with nature means disturb natural processes by human action.","zh":"interfere with nature 指透過人類行動擾亂自然過程。"},{"en":"Building on wetlands can interfere with nature by blocking water flow and animal movement.","zh":"在濕地上建築會阻塞水流和動物移動，從而干預大自然。"},{"en":"If people introduce species carelessly, they may change ecosystems in unpredictable ways.","zh":"如果人們草率引入物種，就可能以不可預測方式改變生態系統。"},{"en":"The phrase often carries a negative meaning.","zh":"這個片語通常帶有負面意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"speed and success of","meaning":"……的速度和成功程度","examples":[{"en":"The writer stresses the speed and success of the rainforest’s development.","zh":"作者強調該雨林發展的速度和成功程度。"},{"en":"Speed and success of means how quickly something happened and how well it worked.","zh":"speed and success of 指某事發生得多快以及運作得多好。"},{"en":"A school may judge a new reading programme by the speed and success of students’ improvement.","zh":"學校可能根據學生進步的速度和成功程度來評估新的閱讀計劃。"},{"en":"If a rainforest develops quickly and functions well, both its speed and success are remarkable.","zh":"如果雨林快速發展且運作良好，其速度和成功程度都很值得注意。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights both rapid progress and positive outcome.","zh":"這個片語同時突出快速進展和正面結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 113 - The accidental rainforest.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 114":[{"front":"running on empty","meaning":"耗盡能量地繼續；筋疲力盡","examples":[{"en":"The traditional theory portrays an exhausted athlete as running on empty.","zh":"傳統理論把筋疲力盡的運動員描繪成耗盡能量地繼續。"},{"en":"Running on empty means continuing to work or move when almost all energy is gone.","zh":"Running on empty 指幾乎耗盡所有能量後仍繼續工作或活動。"},{"en":"A student may feel like they are running on empty after sleeping only three hours before school.","zh":"學生如果上學前只睡了三小時，可能感覺自己筋疲力盡地硬撐。"},{"en":"If workers keep running on empty, their concentration, mood, and health may suffer.","zh":"如果員工一直耗盡能量地工作，他們的專注力、情緒和健康可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when someone keeps going despite extreme tiredness.","zh":"這個片語常用於形容某人極度疲倦仍繼續撐下去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a revolutionary new theory","meaning":"革命性的新理論","examples":[{"en":"The passage presents a revolutionary new theory about athletic fatigue.","zh":"文章提出一個關於運動疲勞的革命性新理論。"},{"en":"A revolutionary new theory is a very different idea that challenges older explanations.","zh":"Revolutionary new theory 是一種非常不同、挑戰舊有解釋的新想法。"},{"en":"A doctor may introduce a revolutionary new theory about why patients recover faster with better sleep.","zh":"醫生可能提出一個革命性新理論，解釋為何病人睡得更好便康復更快。"},{"en":"If a theory changes how experts understand a problem, it can influence future research.","zh":"如果理論改變專家理解問題的方式，它可以影響未來研究。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a major break from traditional thinking.","zh":"這個片語暗示與傳統思維出現重大分裂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sports physiology","meaning":"運動生理學","examples":[{"en":"The researchers are challenging a traditional theory in sports physiology.","zh":"研究人員正在挑戰運動生理學中的一個傳統理論。"},{"en":"Sports physiology is the study of how the body works during exercise and athletic performance.","zh":"Sports physiology 是研究身體在運動和體育表現中如何運作的學科。"},{"en":"A coach may use sports physiology to understand why runners need rest after hard training.","zh":"教練可能運用運動生理學理解為何跑手艱苦訓練後需要休息。"},{"en":"If sports physiology explains fatigue clearly, athletes can train more safely.","zh":"如果運動生理學能清楚解釋疲勞，運動員就可以更安全地訓練。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the science of the exercising body.","zh":"這個片語指研究運動中身體的科學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for almost a century","meaning":"近一個世紀以來","examples":[{"en":"Scientists accepted the limitations theory for almost a century.","zh":"科學家近一個世紀以來接受極限理論。"},{"en":"For almost a century means for nearly one hundred years.","zh":"For almost a century 指接近一百年的時間。"},{"en":"A school building may serve students for almost a century before it needs major repair.","zh":"一座校舍可能服務學生近一個世紀後才需要大修。"},{"en":"If an idea lasts for almost a century, people may treat it as common sense.","zh":"如果一個想法維持近一個世紀，人們可能把它視為常識。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a very long period of time.","zh":"這個片語強調非常長的一段時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"presume, not unreasonably, that","meaning":"不無道理地假定","examples":[{"en":"Scientists presumed, not unreasonably, that fatigue originated in the muscles.","zh":"科學家不無道理地假定疲勞源於肌肉。"},{"en":"To presume, not unreasonably, that something is true means to make a sensible assumption based on available evidence.","zh":"To presume, not unreasonably, that something is true 指根據已有證據作出合理假設。"},{"en":"A teacher may presume, not unreasonably, that tired students slept late before an exam.","zh":"老師可能不無道理地假定疲倦學生考試前睡得很晚。"},{"en":"If an assumption seems logical at first, later evidence may still prove it incomplete.","zh":"如果假設起初看似合邏輯，後來的證據仍可能證明它不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an assumption is understandable, even if it may be wrong.","zh":"這個片語顯示某假設可以理解，即使它可能是錯的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fatigue or exhaustion","meaning":"疲勞或筋疲力盡","examples":[{"en":"The researchers investigate the causes of fatigue or exhaustion in athletes.","zh":"研究人員調查運動員疲勞或筋疲力盡的成因。"},{"en":"Fatigue or exhaustion means strong tiredness that reduces a person’s ability to continue.","zh":"Fatigue or exhaustion 指強烈疲倦，令一個人繼續下去的能力下降。"},{"en":"Nurses may feel fatigue or exhaustion after several long night shifts.","zh":"護士連續上幾晚長夜班後，可能感到疲勞或筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"If fatigue becomes serious, mistakes and injuries become more likely.","zh":"如果疲勞變得嚴重，錯誤和受傷會更容易發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes tiredness that affects performance, not ordinary sleepiness only.","zh":"這個片語描述影響表現的疲倦，而不只是普通睏倦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"originate in","meaning":"源於……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists once believed that athletic fatigue originated in the muscles.","zh":"科學家曾經相信運動疲勞源於肌肉。"},{"en":"To originate in something means to begin or come from that source.","zh":"To originate in something 指從某來源開始或產生。"},{"en":"A misunderstanding may originate in one unclear message in a group chat.","zh":"誤會可能源於群組聊天中一條不清楚的訊息。"},{"en":"If a problem originates in poor planning, changing the final result alone will not fix it.","zh":"如果問題源於規劃差，只改變最終結果並不能解決它。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the starting point or source of something.","zh":"這個片語指出某事的起點或來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"precise explanations","meaning":"確切解釋","examples":[{"en":"Precise explanations of muscular fatigue have varied.","zh":"關於肌肉疲勞的確切解釋一直有所不同。"},{"en":"Precise explanations are exact accounts that describe clearly how or why something happens.","zh":"Precise explanations 是清楚描述某事如何或為何發生的準確說明。"},{"en":"A teacher gives precise explanations when she shows exactly why a grammar answer is wrong.","zh":"老師清楚指出文法答案為何錯誤時，就是給出確切解釋。"},{"en":"If explanations are precise, students can avoid guessing and understand the cause.","zh":"如果解釋確切，學生就可以避免猜測並理解原因。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on accuracy and detail.","zh":"這個片語著重準確和細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"vary considerably","meaning":"有相當大的差異","examples":[{"en":"Explanations of fatigue have varied considerably over time.","zh":"關於疲勞的解釋隨時間有相當大的差異。"},{"en":"To vary considerably means to differ greatly from one case, person, or period to another.","zh":"To vary considerably 指不同個案、人物或時期之間有很大差異。"},{"en":"Students’ revision habits can vary considerably, from daily practice to last-minute study.","zh":"學生的溫習習慣可以有相當大差異，由每日練習到臨急抱佛腳都有。"},{"en":"If results vary considerably, researchers need to look for the reasons behind the differences.","zh":"如果結果有相當大差異，研究人員需要尋找差異背後的原因。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large variation, not small differences.","zh":"這個片語描述大幅變化，而不是小差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"建基於……","examples":[{"en":"Traditional explanations have all been based on the limitations theory.","zh":"傳統解釋全部建基於極限理論。"},{"en":"To be based on something means to depend on it as the main idea, evidence, or foundation.","zh":"To be based on something 指以某事作為主要想法、證據或基礎。"},{"en":"A school rule should be based on student safety rather than convenience alone.","zh":"校規應建基於學生安全，而不只是方便。"},{"en":"If an argument is based on weak evidence, its conclusion may be unreliable.","zh":"如果論點建基於薄弱證據，其結論可能不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the foundation of an explanation or decision.","zh":"這個片語顯示解釋或決定的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the limitations theory","meaning":"極限理論","examples":[{"en":"The limitations theory holds that muscles stop working when they reach a physical limit.","zh":"極限理論認為肌肉到達生理極限時便停止運作。"},{"en":"The limitations theory is the idea that fatigue happens because the body reaches a direct physical limit.","zh":"Limitations theory 是認為疲勞因身體達到直接生理極限而出現的想法。"},{"en":"A coach using this theory may think a runner slows down because the muscles have no more fuel.","zh":"採用這理論的教練可能認為跑手慢下來，是因為肌肉沒有更多燃料。"},{"en":"If the limitations theory is wrong, fatigue may involve brain regulation rather than muscle failure alone.","zh":"如果極限理論錯誤，疲勞可能涉及大腦調節，而不只是肌肉失效。"},{"en":"This phrase names the traditional explanation of athletic fatigue.","zh":"這個片語命名運動疲勞的傳統解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in other words","meaning":"換句話說","examples":[{"en":"In other words, the theory claims that muscles eventually reach a physical limit.","zh":"換句話說，該理論聲稱肌肉最終會達到生理極限。"},{"en":"In other words introduces the same idea in a clearer or simpler way.","zh":"In other words 用較清楚或較簡單方式引出同一個意思。"},{"en":"The school is understaffed; in other words, there are not enough teachers for all classes.","zh":"學校人手不足；換句話說，教師不夠應付所有班級。"},{"en":"If an explanation is difficult, restating it in other words can help learners understand.","zh":"如果解釋很難，用其他話重新表達可以幫助學習者理解。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a rephrasing, not a new point.","zh":"這個片語表示換一種說法，而不是提出新觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hit a physical limit","meaning":"達到生理極限","examples":[{"en":"The traditional theory says that muscles tire when they hit a physical limit.","zh":"傳統理論認為肌肉達到生理極限時會疲倦。"},{"en":"To hit a physical limit means to reach the point where the body can no longer continue in the same way.","zh":"To hit a physical limit 指到達身體無法再以相同方式繼續的程度。"},{"en":"A beginner runner may hit a physical limit after climbing several steep streets.","zh":"初學跑手跑上幾條陡斜街道後，可能達到生理極限。"},{"en":"If someone hits a physical limit, pushing harder may increase the risk of injury.","zh":"如果某人達到生理極限，繼續硬撐可能增加受傷風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching a bodily boundary.","zh":"這個片語描述到達身體邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"run out of fuel","meaning":"耗盡能量","examples":[{"en":"Muscles were thought to tire when they ran out of fuel.","zh":"人們曾認為肌肉在耗盡能量時會疲倦。"},{"en":"To run out of fuel means to use up the energy supply needed to keep moving or working.","zh":"To run out of fuel 指用光維持活動或工作的能量供應。"},{"en":"A phone runs out of battery in the same way a machine can run out of fuel.","zh":"手機耗盡電量，就像機器耗盡燃料一樣。"},{"en":"If a runner truly runs out of fuel, their body may slow dramatically.","zh":"如果跑手真的耗盡能量，身體可能大幅慢下來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes having no remaining energy source.","zh":"這個片語描述沒有剩餘能源來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"run out of oxygen","meaning":"耗盡氧氣","examples":[{"en":"The old theory suggested that muscles could run out of oxygen.","zh":"舊理論提出肌肉可能耗盡氧氣。"},{"en":"To run out of oxygen means to no longer have enough oxygen for the body or muscles to work properly.","zh":"To run out of oxygen 指不再有足夠氧氣讓身體或肌肉正常運作。"},{"en":"A swimmer may panic if they feel they are running out of oxygen underwater.","zh":"游泳者在水底感到自己快耗盡氧氣時，可能會驚慌。"},{"en":"If muscles lack oxygen, movement can become painful, weak, or unsustainable.","zh":"如果肌肉缺氧，動作可能變得疼痛、無力或不能持續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an oxygen shortage.","zh":"這個片語描述氧氣不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"toxic by-products","meaning":"有毒副產品","examples":[{"en":"Some theories blamed toxic by-products produced during exercise.","zh":"有些理論把責任歸咎於運動期間產生的有毒副產品。"},{"en":"Toxic by-products are harmful substances created as a side effect of a process.","zh":"Toxic by-products 是某過程作為副作用產生的有害物質。"},{"en":"A factory may produce toxic by-products if waste chemicals are not controlled.","zh":"如果廢化學品未受控制，工廠可能產生有毒副產品。"},{"en":"If toxic by-products build up in the body, they may interfere with normal function.","zh":"如果有毒副產品在體內積聚，它們可能干擾正常功能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harmful secondary products, not the main intended result.","zh":"這個片語描述有害的次要產物，而不是主要目標產物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"drown in toxic by-products","meaning":"被有毒副產品淹沒","examples":[{"en":"The limitations theory suggests that muscles may drown in toxic by-products.","zh":"極限理論認為肌肉可能被有毒副產品淹沒。"},{"en":"To drown in toxic by-products means to be overwhelmed by harmful substances produced during activity.","zh":"To drown in toxic by-products 指被活動期間產生的有害物質壓倒。"},{"en":"A small river may seem to drown in waste if factories release chemicals every day.","zh":"如果工廠每天排放化學品，小河可能像被廢物淹沒一樣。"},{"en":"If muscles are flooded with harmful by-products, the old theory predicts they should stop working well.","zh":"如果肌肉充滿有害副產品，舊理論會預測它們不能好好運作。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a vivid image to describe being overwhelmed by waste substances.","zh":"這個片語用鮮明畫面描述被廢物物質壓倒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in the past few years","meaning":"在過去數年","examples":[{"en":"In the past few years, the researchers have examined the standard theory closely.","zh":"在過去數年，研究人員仔細審視傳統理論。"},{"en":"In the past few years means during the recent several years before now or before the time discussed.","zh":"In the past few years 指現在或所討論時間之前的最近幾年。"},{"en":"In the past few years, many students have used online lessons more often.","zh":"在過去數年，許多學生更常使用網上課堂。"},{"en":"If evidence has changed in the past few years, older explanations may need review.","zh":"如果證據在過去數年有所改變，舊解釋可能需要重新檢視。"},{"en":"This phrase points to recent developments.","zh":"這個片語指出近期發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"examine the standard theory","meaning":"審視傳統理論","examples":[{"en":"Noakes and St Clair Gibson examined the standard theory of fatigue.","zh":"Noakes 和 St Clair Gibson 審視疲勞的傳統理論。"},{"en":"To examine the standard theory means to study the accepted explanation carefully.","zh":"To examine the standard theory 指仔細研究被接受的解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may examine the standard theory about why students fail grammar tests.","zh":"老師可能審視關於學生為何文法測驗不合格的傳統理論。"},{"en":"If the standard theory is examined closely, hidden weaknesses may appear.","zh":"如果傳統理論被仔細審視，隱藏弱點可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful review of a widely accepted idea.","zh":"這個片語描述仔細檢查廣泛接受的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the deeper they dig, the more…","meaning":"越深入研究，就越……","examples":[{"en":"The deeper the researchers dig, the more convinced they become that the old theory is wrong.","zh":"研究人員越深入研究，就越深信舊理論是錯的。"},{"en":"The deeper they dig, the more something happens means that stronger investigation leads to a stronger result or belief.","zh":"The deeper they dig, the more something happens 指調查越深入，某結果或信念越強。"},{"en":"The deeper students dig into a poem, the more they notice hidden meanings.","zh":"學生越深入研究一首詩，就越注意到隱藏意思。"},{"en":"If researchers keep finding contradictions, deeper study may make them doubt the old view more.","zh":"如果研究人員不斷發現矛盾，更深入研究可能令他們更懷疑舊觀點。"},{"en":"This structure shows that one change increases together with another.","zh":"這個結構顯示一種變化與另一種變化同步增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"become convinced that","meaning":"開始深信","examples":[{"en":"The researchers became convinced that fatigue was not simply muscular failure.","zh":"研究人員開始深信疲勞不只是肌肉失效。"},{"en":"To become convinced that something is true means to gradually believe it strongly because of evidence or experience.","zh":"To become convinced that something is true 指因證據或經驗而逐漸強烈相信某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may become convinced that a student needs glasses after seeing repeated reading mistakes.","zh":"老師看見學生反覆閱讀錯誤後，可能開始深信他需要配眼鏡。"},{"en":"If evidence keeps pointing in one direction, people may become convinced of a new explanation.","zh":"如果證據不斷指向同一方向，人們可能開始深信新的解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a belief becoming firm.","zh":"這個片語描述信念變得堅定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"physical fatigue","meaning":"身體疲勞","examples":[{"en":"Physical fatigue is not necessarily the same as using up all available energy.","zh":"身體疲勞不一定等同於用盡所有可用能量。"},{"en":"Physical fatigue is tiredness in the body that reduces strength, speed, or endurance.","zh":"Physical fatigue 是身體上的疲倦，會降低力量、速度或耐力。"},{"en":"A nurse may feel physical fatigue after standing and walking through a long shift.","zh":"護士在長更中一直站立和走動後，可能感到身體疲勞。"},{"en":"If physical fatigue builds up, even simple tasks may feel heavier and slower.","zh":"如果身體疲勞累積，即使簡單任務也可能感覺更沉重和更慢。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to bodily tiredness, not only mental boredom.","zh":"這個片語指身體上的疲倦，而不只是心理上的沉悶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be the same as","meaning":"與……相同","examples":[{"en":"Physical fatigue is not the same as a car running out of petrol.","zh":"身體疲勞與汽車耗盡汽油並不相同。"},{"en":"To be the same as something means to be equal or identical in nature, meaning, or effect.","zh":"To be the same as something 指在性質、意思或效果上相等或一樣。"},{"en":"Being quiet is not the same as understanding the lesson.","zh":"安靜並不等同於明白課堂內容。"},{"en":"If two situations look similar but work differently, they should not be treated as the same.","zh":"如果兩種情況看起來相似但運作不同，就不應把它們視為相同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for correcting a false comparison.","zh":"這個片語適合用來糾正錯誤比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"run out of petrol","meaning":"耗盡汽油","examples":[{"en":"The researchers reject the comparison with a car running out of petrol.","zh":"研究人員否定把疲勞比作汽車耗盡汽油的說法。"},{"en":"To run out of petrol means to have no fuel left for a car or engine to keep moving.","zh":"To run out of petrol 指汽車或引擎沒有剩餘燃料繼續行駛。"},{"en":"A driver may be stuck on the road if the car runs out of petrol.","zh":"如果汽車耗盡汽油，司機可能被困在路上。"},{"en":"If a car runs out of petrol, it stops because there is no fuel left to burn.","zh":"如果汽車耗盡汽油，它會因沒有燃料燃燒而停下來。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used literally for cars and metaphorically for energy.","zh":"這個片語常按字面用於汽車，也可比喻能量耗盡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be caused not by…but by…","meaning":"並非由……引起，而是由……引起","examples":[{"en":"Fatigue may be caused not by exhausted muscles but by an emotional response in the brain.","zh":"疲勞可能並非由肌肉耗竭引起，而是由大腦中的情緒反應引起。"},{"en":"Be caused not by A but by B means the real cause is B, not the first explanation.","zh":"Be caused not by A but by B 指真正原因是B，而不是第一個解釋。"},{"en":"A student’s poor mark may be caused not by laziness but by misunderstanding the question.","zh":"學生成績差可能並非由懶惰引起，而是由誤解題目引起。"},{"en":"If the real cause is different, solving the wrong problem will not help.","zh":"如果真正原因不同，解決錯誤問題並沒有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly contrasts a rejected cause with the proposed cause.","zh":"這個片語清楚對比被否定的原因與提出的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"distress signals","meaning":"痛苦訊號；不適訊號","examples":[{"en":"The old theory assumes that distress signals come from overworked muscles.","zh":"舊理論假設痛苦訊號來自過度勞累的肌肉。"},{"en":"Distress signals are warning signs that something is under stress or in trouble.","zh":"Distress signals 是顯示某事物處於壓力或困境中的警告信號。"},{"en":"A child’s sudden silence may be a distress signal that they are upset or afraid.","zh":"孩子突然沉默可能是不適訊號，表示他不開心或害怕。"},{"en":"If the body sends distress signals, the brain may respond by reducing effort.","zh":"如果身體發出痛苦訊號，大腦可能透過降低努力程度作回應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes signs that alert us to danger or strain.","zh":"這個片語描述提醒我們危險或壓力的跡象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"spring from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"The sensations of fatigue may not spring directly from the muscles.","zh":"疲勞感可能並非直接源自肌肉。"},{"en":"To spring from something means to come from it or be caused by it.","zh":"To spring from something 指來自某事或由某事引起。"},{"en":"A classroom argument may spring from a small misunderstanding during group work.","zh":"課室爭執可能源自小組活動中的一個小誤會。"},{"en":"If a feeling does not spring from the obvious source, we need to look deeper.","zh":"如果某種感覺不是源自明顯來源，我們就需要更深入尋找。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where something begins.","zh":"這個片語指出某事從哪裡開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"overtaxed muscles","meaning":"過度勞累的肌肉","examples":[{"en":"The theory questions whether fatigue signals spring from overtaxed muscles.","zh":"該理論質疑疲勞訊號是否源自過度勞累的肌肉。"},{"en":"Overtaxed muscles are muscles that have been pushed too hard or used beyond a comfortable level.","zh":"Overtaxed muscles 是被過度使用或超出舒適水平的肌肉。"},{"en":"A beginner’s legs may become overtaxed after climbing many stairs too quickly.","zh":"初學者太快爬很多樓梯後，雙腿肌肉可能過度勞累。"},{"en":"If muscles are overtaxed, soreness and slower movement may follow.","zh":"如果肌肉過度勞累，之後可能出現酸痛和動作變慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes muscles under excessive strain.","zh":"這個片語描述承受過多壓力的肌肉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"an emotional response","meaning":"情緒反應","examples":[{"en":"Noakes argues that fatigue is partly an emotional response.","zh":"Noakes 認為疲勞部分是一種情緒反應。"},{"en":"An emotional response is a feeling-based reaction to information, danger, pressure, or experience.","zh":"Emotional response 是基於感受，對資訊、危險、壓力或經歷作出的反應。"},{"en":"A student may have an emotional response when exam results arrive and feel fear or relief.","zh":"學生收到考試成績時，可能產生恐懼或鬆一口氣的情緒反應。"},{"en":"If fatigue includes emotion, the brain may shape how tired the body feels.","zh":"如果疲勞包含情緒，大腦可能塑造身體感到多疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reaction involving feelings, not just physical processes.","zh":"這個片語描述涉及感受的反應，而不只是生理過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"begin in the brain","meaning":"始於大腦","examples":[{"en":"The sensations associated with exhaustion may begin in the brain.","zh":"與筋疲力盡相關的感覺可能始於大腦。"},{"en":"To begin in the brain means to start as a mental or neurological process.","zh":"To begin in the brain 指作為心理或神經過程開始。"},{"en":"A fear of public speaking may begin in the brain before any real danger appears.","zh":"對公開演說的恐懼可能在真正危險出現前已始於大腦。"},{"en":"If fatigue begins in the brain, changing thought or expectation may affect performance.","zh":"如果疲勞始於大腦，改變想法或預期可能影響表現。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the brain as the starting point.","zh":"這個片語指出大腦是起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the essence of","meaning":"……的核心","examples":[{"en":"The essence of the theory is that the brain protects the body from exhaustion.","zh":"該理論的核心是大腦保護身體免於耗竭。"},{"en":"The essence of something is its central meaning or most important idea.","zh":"Essence of something 是某事的中心意思或最重要想法。"},{"en":"The essence of good teaching is helping students understand, not just giving answers.","zh":"良好教學的核心是幫助學生理解，而不只是給答案。"},{"en":"If you understand the essence of a theory, the details become easier to organise.","zh":"如果你理解理論的核心，細節就更容易組織。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the core idea.","zh":"這個片語指出核心想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a mix of","meaning":"……的混合","examples":[{"en":"The brain uses a mix of physiological and psychological cues.","zh":"大腦使用生理和心理提示的混合。"},{"en":"A mix of things means a combination of different elements.","zh":"A mix of things 指不同元素的組合。"},{"en":"A good lesson may use a mix of explanation, examples, practice, and feedback.","zh":"一堂好課可能使用解釋、例子、練習和回饋的混合。"},{"en":"If a result depends on a mix of factors, one simple cause may not explain everything.","zh":"如果結果取決於多種因素的混合，一個簡單原因可能不能解釋全部。"},{"en":"This phrase describes several things working together.","zh":"這個片語描述幾種事物共同作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"physiological cues","meaning":"生理提示","examples":[{"en":"The brain monitors physiological cues from the body.","zh":"大腦監察來自身體的生理提示。"},{"en":"Physiological cues are physical signals from the body, such as heart rate, breathing, pain, or temperature.","zh":"Physiological cues 是來自身體的物理訊號，例如心跳、呼吸、疼痛或體溫。"},{"en":"A doctor may notice physiological cues that show a patient is under stress.","zh":"醫生可能注意到顯示病人受壓的生理提示。"},{"en":"If physiological cues warn of danger, the brain may slow the body down.","zh":"如果生理提示警告有危險，大腦可能令身體慢下來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes body-based information.","zh":"這個片語描述以身體為基礎的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"subconscious cues","meaning":"潛意識提示","examples":[{"en":"Subconscious cues may influence how tired an athlete feels.","zh":"潛意識提示可能影響運動員感到多疲倦。"},{"en":"Subconscious cues are signals that affect behaviour or feelings without full awareness.","zh":"Subconscious cues 是在沒有完全意識到的情況下影響行為或感受的訊號。"},{"en":"A student may feel nervous before a test because subconscious cues remind them of past failure.","zh":"學生測驗前可能感到緊張，因為潛意識提示令他想起過去失敗。"},{"en":"If subconscious cues shape effort, athletes may slow down before they consciously decide to stop.","zh":"如果潛意識提示塑造努力程度，運動員可能在有意識決定停止前已慢下來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hidden mental signals.","zh":"這個片語描述隱藏的心理訊號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"conscious cues","meaning":"意識層面的提示","examples":[{"en":"Conscious cues can also affect the sensation of fatigue.","zh":"意識層面的提示也可以影響疲勞感。"},{"en":"Conscious cues are signals or thoughts that a person is aware of and can notice directly.","zh":"Conscious cues 是人能意識到並直接注意到的訊號或想法。"},{"en":"Seeing the finish line is a conscious cue that may help a runner speed up.","zh":"看見終點線是一個意識層面的提示，可能幫助跑手加速。"},{"en":"If a student sees only five minutes left, that cue may change how quickly they write.","zh":"如果學生看見只剩五分鐘，該提示可能改變他寫作速度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information people actively notice.","zh":"這個片語描述人主動注意到的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pace the muscles","meaning":"調節肌肉運動節奏","examples":[{"en":"The brain may pace the muscles throughout a workout.","zh":"大腦可能在整個運動過程中調節肌肉運動節奏。"},{"en":"To pace the muscles means to control how hard and how fast the muscles work over time.","zh":"To pace the muscles 指控制肌肉在一段時間內用多大力和多快運作。"},{"en":"A runner must pace their legs carefully during a long race to avoid burning out too early.","zh":"跑手在長跑中必須小心調節腿部節奏，以免太早耗盡。"},{"en":"If the brain paces the muscles, effort is spread across the whole activity.","zh":"如果大腦調節肌肉節奏，努力程度就會分布在整個活動中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regulating muscle effort.","zh":"這個片語描述調節肌肉用力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"keep someone well back from","meaning":"令某人遠離……","examples":[{"en":"The brain keeps athletes well back from catastrophic exhaustion.","zh":"大腦令運動員遠離災難性耗竭。"},{"en":"To keep someone well back from something means to stop them from getting dangerously close to it.","zh":"To keep someone well back from something 指阻止某人危險地接近某事。"},{"en":"A teacher keeps children well back from a busy road during a school trip.","zh":"學校旅行期間，老師會令孩子遠離繁忙道路。"},{"en":"If the brain keeps the body away from collapse, fatigue may act as a safety warning.","zh":"如果大腦令身體遠離崩潰，疲勞可能是一種安全警告。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protective distance from danger.","zh":"這個片語描述與危險保持保護距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the brink of exhaustion","meaning":"筋疲力盡的邊緣","examples":[{"en":"The central governor prevents the body from reaching the brink of exhaustion.","zh":"中央調控系統防止身體到達筋疲力盡的邊緣。"},{"en":"The brink of exhaustion is the point just before complete physical collapse or extreme tiredness.","zh":"Brink of exhaustion 是完全身體崩潰或極度疲倦前的臨界點。"},{"en":"A nurse working double shifts may feel close to the brink of exhaustion by morning.","zh":"連續上雙更的護士，到早上可能感到接近筋疲力盡的邊緣。"},{"en":"If someone reaches the brink of exhaustion, rest becomes urgent rather than optional.","zh":"如果某人到達筋疲力盡的邊緣，休息就變得迫切，而不是可有可無。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the edge of total tiredness.","zh":"這個片語描述完全疲倦的邊緣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"decide it is time to quit","meaning":"決定是時候停止","examples":[{"en":"The brain may decide that it is time for the athlete to quit.","zh":"大腦可能決定運動員是時候停止。"},{"en":"To decide it is time to quit means to judge that continuing is no longer safe, useful, or possible.","zh":"To decide it is time to quit 指判斷繼續下去已不再安全、有用或可行。"},{"en":"A student may decide it is time to quit revising for the night when they can no longer focus.","zh":"當學生再也無法集中時，可能決定今晚是時候停止溫習。"},{"en":"If the body receives danger signals, the brain may push the person to stop.","zh":"如果身體收到危險訊號，大腦可能推動人停下來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the moment when stopping seems necessary.","zh":"這個片語描述停止變得必要的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"create distressing sensations","meaning":"產生令人難受的感覺","examples":[{"en":"The brain may create distressing sensations to slow the athlete down.","zh":"大腦可能產生令人難受的感覺，令運動員慢下來。"},{"en":"To create distressing sensations means to produce unpleasant feelings such as pain, heaviness, or discomfort.","zh":"To create distressing sensations 指產生疼痛、沉重或不適等不愉快感覺。"},{"en":"Anxiety can create distressing sensations, such as a tight chest before public speaking.","zh":"焦慮可以產生令人難受的感覺，例如公開演說前胸口繃緊。"},{"en":"If distressing sensations appear, a person may naturally reduce effort or stop.","zh":"如果令人難受的感覺出現，一個人可能自然降低努力程度或停止。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unpleasant feelings that influence behaviour.","zh":"這個片語描述影響行為的不愉快感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"interpret something as","meaning":"把……理解為","examples":[{"en":"Athletes interpret these sensations as unbearable muscle fatigue.","zh":"運動員把這些感覺理解為難以忍受的肌肉疲勞。"},{"en":"To interpret something as something else means to understand or explain it in that way.","zh":"To interpret something as something else 指以某種方式理解或解釋某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may interpret silence as confusion if students avoid eye contact.","zh":"如果學生避開眼神接觸，老師可能把沉默理解為困惑。"},{"en":"If people interpret a signal wrongly, they may respond to the wrong problem.","zh":"如果人們錯誤理解訊號，就可能回應錯誤問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how someone gives meaning to an experience.","zh":"這個片語描述某人如何賦予經驗意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"unbearable muscle fatigue","meaning":"難以忍受的肌肉疲勞","examples":[{"en":"The sensations may be interpreted as unbearable muscle fatigue.","zh":"這些感覺可能被理解為難以忍受的肌肉疲勞。"},{"en":"Unbearable muscle fatigue is extreme tiredness in the muscles that feels impossible to tolerate.","zh":"Unbearable muscle fatigue 是肌肉中極端疲倦，令人感覺無法忍受。"},{"en":"A runner climbing a steep hill may feel unbearable muscle fatigue in the final minutes.","zh":"跑手爬上陡斜山路的最後幾分鐘，可能感到難以忍受的肌肉疲勞。"},{"en":"If fatigue feels unbearable, athletes may slow down even if some energy remains.","zh":"如果疲勞感難以忍受，運動員即使仍有能量也可能慢下來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fatigue that feels beyond what a person can stand.","zh":"這個片語描述超出一個人承受範圍的疲勞感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the central governor theory","meaning":"中央調控理論","examples":[{"en":"The central governor theory proposes that the brain regulates athletic effort.","zh":"中央調控理論提出大腦調節運動努力程度。"},{"en":"The central governor theory is the idea that the brain controls fatigue to protect the body.","zh":"Central governor theory 是認為大腦控制疲勞以保護身體的想法。"},{"en":"A coach who accepts the central governor theory may train athletes to manage pace and expectation.","zh":"接受中央調控理論的教練，可能訓練運動員管理配速和預期。"},{"en":"If the brain governs effort, fatigue is not simply a sign that muscles have failed.","zh":"如果大腦控制努力程度，疲勞就不只是肌肉失效的跡象。"},{"en":"This phrase names a brain-centred theory of fatigue.","zh":"這個片語命名一種以大腦為中心的疲勞理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"remain controversial","meaning":"仍具爭議","examples":[{"en":"The central governor theory remains controversial.","zh":"中央調控理論仍具爭議。"},{"en":"To remain controversial means to continue causing disagreement or debate.","zh":"To remain controversial 指繼續引起分歧或辯論。"},{"en":"A school’s phone ban may remain controversial if students and parents disagree about it.","zh":"如果學生和家長對手機禁令有分歧，該政策可能仍具爭議。"},{"en":"If a theory remains controversial, researchers have not yet fully accepted it.","zh":"如果理論仍具爭議，研究人員尚未完全接受它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an issue that is still debated.","zh":"這個片語描述仍在被辯論的議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"explain puzzling aspects of","meaning":"解釋……令人困惑的方面","examples":[{"en":"The theory explains several puzzling aspects of athletic performance.","zh":"該理論解釋運動表現中幾個令人困惑的方面。"},{"en":"To explain puzzling aspects of something means to make confusing parts easier to understand.","zh":"To explain puzzling aspects of something 指令某事中令人困惑的部分更易理解。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain puzzling aspects of English articles by showing clear patterns.","zh":"老師可能透過展示清晰模式，解釋英文冠詞令人困惑的方面。"},{"en":"If a theory explains puzzling evidence, it becomes more useful to researchers.","zh":"如果理論能解釋令人困惑的證據，它對研究人員就更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes solving confusing parts of a topic.","zh":"這個片語描述解決某題目的困惑部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"athletic performance","meaning":"運動表現","examples":[{"en":"The researchers use the theory to explain athletic performance.","zh":"研究人員使用該理論解釋運動表現。"},{"en":"Athletic performance is how well an athlete runs, cycles, swims, lifts, or competes.","zh":"Athletic performance 是運動員在跑步、踩單車、游泳、舉重或比賽中的表現。"},{"en":"Sleep, training, food, and confidence can all affect athletic performance.","zh":"睡眠、訓練、飲食和信心都可以影響運動表現。"},{"en":"If athletic performance improves, the athlete may become faster, stronger, or more consistent.","zh":"如果運動表現改善，運動員可能變得更快、更強或更穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sports ability in action.","zh":"這個片語描述實際體育能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a recent discovery","meaning":"最近的一項發現","examples":[{"en":"A recent discovery encouraged Noakes to investigate fatigue more seriously.","zh":"最近的一項發現鼓勵 Noakes 更認真研究疲勞。"},{"en":"A recent discovery is something found or learned not long ago.","zh":"Recent discovery 是不久前發現或得知的事情。"},{"en":"A recent discovery in a classroom survey may show that many students are not sleeping enough.","zh":"課室調查中最近的一項發現，可能顯示許多學生睡眠不足。"},{"en":"If a discovery challenges old beliefs, it can start new research.","zh":"如果一項發現挑戰舊信念，它可以引發新研究。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces new evidence or information.","zh":"這個片語引出新證據或新資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the lactic acid paradox","meaning":"乳酸悖論","examples":[{"en":"Noakes calls the unexpected finding the lactic acid paradox.","zh":"Noakes 把這個意外發現稱為乳酸悖論。"},{"en":"The lactic acid paradox is a surprising situation where fatigue appears even when lactic acid levels are low.","zh":"Lactic acid paradox 是即使乳酸水平低，疲勞仍然出現的令人驚訝情況。"},{"en":"A science teacher may use the lactic acid paradox to show why simple explanations can fail.","zh":"科學老師可能使用乳酸悖論來顯示簡單解釋為何可能失敗。"},{"en":"If fatigue occurs without high lactic acid, researchers must look for another cause.","zh":"如果疲勞在乳酸不高時出現，研究人員就必須尋找另一原因。"},{"en":"This phrase names evidence that challenges the old fatigue theory.","zh":"這個片語命名挑戰舊疲勞理論的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"start researching seriously","meaning":"開始認真研究","examples":[{"en":"The paradox made Noakes start researching the issue seriously.","zh":"這個悖論令 Noakes 開始認真研究該問題。"},{"en":"To start researching seriously means to begin studying a question carefully and systematically.","zh":"To start researching seriously 指開始仔細而有系統地研究一個問題。"},{"en":"A student may start researching seriously after realising a topic is harder than expected.","zh":"學生發現題目比預期困難後，可能開始認真研究。"},{"en":"If a puzzling result appears, it can push researchers to investigate more deeply.","zh":"如果令人困惑的結果出現，它可以推動研究人員更深入調查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving from casual interest to focused study.","zh":"這個片語描述由普通興趣轉向專注研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a by-product of exercise","meaning":"運動產生的副產品","examples":[{"en":"Lactic acid is a by-product of exercise.","zh":"乳酸是運動產生的副產品。"},{"en":"A by-product of exercise is something produced as a secondary result of physical activity.","zh":"By-product of exercise 是身體活動作為次要結果產生的東西。"},{"en":"Sweat is a familiar by-product of exercise when the body tries to cool itself.","zh":"汗水是運動產生的常見副產品，因為身體嘗試降溫。"},{"en":"If a by-product builds up, scientists may ask whether it affects performance.","zh":"如果副產品積聚，科學家可能詢問它是否影響表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something produced during exercise, not the main goal of exercise.","zh":"這個片語描述運動期間產生的東西，而不是運動主要目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lactic acid","meaning":"乳酸","examples":[{"en":"Lactic acid has often been blamed for athletic fatigue.","zh":"乳酸常被歸咎為運動疲勞的原因。"},{"en":"Lactic acid is a substance produced in muscles during intense exercise.","zh":"Lactic acid 是肌肉在高強度運動期間產生的物質。"},{"en":"A runner may hear that lactic acid causes the burning feeling in tired legs.","zh":"跑手可能聽過乳酸造成疲倦雙腿的灼熱感。"},{"en":"If lactic acid levels are low but fatigue appears, the old explanation becomes questionable.","zh":"如果乳酸水平低但疲勞出現，舊解釋就變得可疑。"},{"en":"This phrase names a chemical often discussed in exercise science.","zh":"這個片語命名運動科學中常討論的一種化學物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the accumulation of","meaning":"……的積聚","examples":[{"en":"The accumulation of lactic acid is often cited as a cause of fatigue.","zh":"乳酸的積聚常被列為疲勞的成因。"},{"en":"The accumulation of something means its gradual build-up over time.","zh":"Accumulation of something 指某物隨時間逐漸累積。"},{"en":"The accumulation of homework can make students feel stressed before the weekend.","zh":"功課的積聚可能令學生在週末前感到壓力。"},{"en":"If waste accumulates in a river, water quality may decline.","zh":"如果廢物在河中積聚，水質可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something increasing and collecting.","zh":"這個片語描述某物增加並聚集。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be cited as a cause of","meaning":"被列為……的成因","examples":[{"en":"Lactic acid accumulation is often cited as a cause of fatigue.","zh":"乳酸積聚常被列為疲勞的成因。"},{"en":"To be cited as a cause of something means to be mentioned as a reason for it.","zh":"To be cited as a cause of something 指被提及為某事的原因。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep is often cited as a cause of poor concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足常被列為課堂專注力差的成因。"},{"en":"If one factor is repeatedly cited as a cause, people may overlook other explanations.","zh":"如果一個因素反覆被列為成因，人們可能忽視其他解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase reports what is commonly given as a reason.","zh":"這個片語報告常被提出的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"research subjects","meaning":"研究對象","examples":[{"en":"The research subjects exercised in simulated high-altitude conditions.","zh":"研究對象在模擬高海拔環境中運動。"},{"en":"Research subjects are people or animals taking part in a scientific study.","zh":"Research subjects 是參與科學研究的人或動物。"},{"en":"In a sleep study, research subjects may wear monitors while they rest.","zh":"在睡眠研究中，研究對象休息時可能佩戴監測器。"},{"en":"If research subjects are carefully selected, results become easier to interpret.","zh":"如果研究對象被仔細挑選，結果就更容易解讀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes participants in an experiment.","zh":"這個片語描述實驗參加者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"conditions simulating high altitude","meaning":"模擬高海拔的環境","examples":[{"en":"The subjects exercised in conditions simulating high altitude.","zh":"研究對象在模擬高海拔的環境中運動。"},{"en":"Conditions simulating high altitude are artificial settings that copy the low-oxygen environment of high mountains.","zh":"Conditions simulating high altitude 是人工設定，模仿高山低氧環境。"},{"en":"Athletes may train in rooms simulating high altitude to prepare for mountain races.","zh":"運動員可能在模擬高海拔的房間中訓練，以準備山地賽事。"},{"en":"If oxygen is reduced, the body may feel tired sooner during exercise.","zh":"如果氧氣減少，身體在運動時可能更早感到疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a controlled imitation of high-altitude conditions.","zh":"這個片語描述對高海拔環境的受控模擬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"become fatigued","meaning":"變得疲勞","examples":[{"en":"The research subjects became fatigued despite having low lactic acid levels.","zh":"研究對象雖然乳酸水平低，仍變得疲勞。"},{"en":"To become fatigued means to start feeling physically or mentally tired and less able to continue.","zh":"To become fatigued 指開始感到身體或精神疲倦，繼續下去的能力下降。"},{"en":"A student may become fatigued after writing essays for several hours.","zh":"學生連續寫作文數小時後，可能變得疲勞。"},{"en":"If people become fatigued early, their performance may fall even before resources are fully used.","zh":"如果人們很早變得疲勞，他們的表現可能在資源完全用盡前已下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of becoming tired.","zh":"這個片語描述變得疲倦的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"remain low","meaning":"維持在低水平","examples":[{"en":"Their lactic acid levels remained low during the test.","zh":"他們的乳酸水平在測試期間維持在低水平。"},{"en":"To remain low means to stay at a small or limited level.","zh":"To remain low 指保持在較小或有限水平。"},{"en":"A student’s stress may remain low if they revise steadily instead of waiting until the last night.","zh":"如果學生穩定溫習而不是等到最後一晚，壓力可能維持在低水平。"},{"en":"If a key measurement remains low, it may not explain a severe result.","zh":"如果關鍵量度維持在低水平，它可能不能解釋嚴重結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a level that does not rise much.","zh":"這個片語描述水平沒有大幅上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the oxygen content of","meaning":"……的含氧量","examples":[{"en":"The oxygen content of their blood had not fallen critically low.","zh":"他們血液的含氧量並沒有降至危急低水平。"},{"en":"The oxygen content of something is the amount of oxygen it contains.","zh":"Oxygen content of something 是某物所含氧氣的量。"},{"en":"Doctors may check the oxygen content of a patient’s blood with a small finger sensor.","zh":"醫生可能用細小手指感應器檢查病人血液的含氧量。"},{"en":"If oxygen content drops too low, the body may not work safely.","zh":"如果含氧量降得太低，身體可能不能安全運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how much oxygen is present.","zh":"這個片語描述有多少氧氣存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fall too low for someone to","meaning":"降至令某人無法……的水平","examples":[{"en":"The oxygen level had not fallen too low for the subjects to continue exercising.","zh":"氧氣水平並未降至令研究對象無法繼續運動的水平。"},{"en":"To fall too low for someone to do something means to drop below the level needed for that action.","zh":"To fall too low for someone to do something 指下降到低於進行該行動所需的水平。"},{"en":"A phone battery may fall too low for a student to finish an online lesson.","zh":"手機電量可能降至令學生無法完成網上課堂的水平。"},{"en":"If blood sugar falls too low for a runner to continue, they may need food or rest.","zh":"如果血糖降至令跑手無法繼續的水平，他可能需要食物或休息。"},{"en":"This phrase links a low level with inability to continue.","zh":"這個片語把低水平與無法繼續連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"deduce that","meaning":"推斷","examples":[{"en":"Noakes deduced that another factor was causing fatigue.","zh":"Noakes 推斷有另一個因素正在造成疲勞。"},{"en":"To deduce that something is true means to reach a conclusion by reasoning from evidence.","zh":"To deduce that something is true 指根據證據推理得出結論。"},{"en":"A teacher may deduce that students did not understand the topic after seeing the same mistake repeatedly.","zh":"老師看見同一錯誤反覆出現後，可能推斷學生沒有理解該題目。"},{"en":"If the expected cause is absent, researchers may deduce that another cause exists.","zh":"如果預期原因不存在，研究人員可能推斷存在另一原因。"},{"en":"This phrase describes logical conclusion from clues.","zh":"這個片語描述根據線索作出的邏輯結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"physiological limits","meaning":"生理極限","examples":[{"en":"The subjects became tired before reaching their physiological limits.","zh":"研究對象在達到生理極限前已變得疲倦。"},{"en":"Physiological limits are the body’s physical boundaries, such as maximum strength, fuel, oxygen, or endurance.","zh":"Physiological limits 是身體的實際邊界，例如最大力量、燃料、氧氣或耐力。"},{"en":"A climber may reach physiological limits when cold, hunger, and lack of oxygen combine.","zh":"當寒冷、飢餓和缺氧結合時，登山者可能達到生理極限。"},{"en":"If fatigue appears before these limits are reached, the brain may be holding the body back.","zh":"如果疲勞在這些極限達到前出現，大腦可能正在阻止身體繼續推進。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the body’s real physical boundaries.","zh":"這個片語描述身體真正的物理邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"probe further","meaning":"作進一步深入研究","examples":[{"en":"Noakes probed further by conducting an experiment with cyclists.","zh":"Noakes 透過與單車手進行實驗作進一步深入研究。"},{"en":"To probe further means to investigate more deeply after an earlier question or result.","zh":"To probe further 指在早前問題或結果之後更深入調查。"},{"en":"A teacher may probe further when a student gives an answer that sounds memorised but unclear.","zh":"當學生答案聽起來像背誦但不清楚時，老師可能進一步追問。"},{"en":"If early evidence is puzzling, probing further can reveal a better explanation.","zh":"如果早期證據令人困惑，進一步深入研究可以揭示更好解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deeper investigation.","zh":"這個片語描述更深入調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"conduct an experiment","meaning":"進行實驗","examples":[{"en":"Noakes conducted an experiment with seven cyclists.","zh":"Noakes 與七名單車手進行實驗。"},{"en":"To conduct an experiment means to carry out a planned scientific test.","zh":"To conduct an experiment 指進行一項有計劃的科學測試。"},{"en":"Students may conduct an experiment to see which material keeps water warm longest.","zh":"學生可能進行實驗，看看哪種材料最能保溫。"},{"en":"If an experiment is carefully controlled, its results are easier to trust.","zh":"如果實驗被仔細控制，其結果較容易令人信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised testing.","zh":"這個片語描述有組織的測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have sensors taped to","meaning":"把感應器貼在……上","examples":[{"en":"The cyclists had sensors taped to their legs.","zh":"單車手腿上貼有感應器。"},{"en":"To have sensors taped to a body part means to attach measuring devices there with tape.","zh":"To have sensors taped to a body part 指用膠帶把量度裝置貼在身體某部位。"},{"en":"A patient may have sensors taped to the chest during a heart test.","zh":"病人在心臟測試期間，胸口可能貼有感應器。"},{"en":"If sensors are attached securely, researchers can record movement or electrical activity accurately.","zh":"如果感應器貼得穩固，研究人員可以準確記錄動作或電活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using equipment to collect body data.","zh":"這個片語描述使用設備收集身體數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"measure nerve impulses","meaning":"測量神經脈衝","examples":[{"en":"The sensors measured nerve impulses travelling through the muscles.","zh":"感應器測量穿過肌肉傳遞的神經脈衝。"},{"en":"To measure nerve impulses means to record electrical signals sent through nerves.","zh":"To measure nerve impulses 指記錄透過神經傳送的電訊號。"},{"en":"Doctors may measure nerve impulses to check whether a damaged hand is recovering.","zh":"醫生可能測量神經脈衝，以檢查受傷的手是否正在康復。"},{"en":"If nerve impulses weaken, the muscle may receive less instruction to contract.","zh":"如果神經脈衝減弱，肌肉可能收到較少收縮指令。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recording nervous-system signals.","zh":"這個片語描述記錄神經系統訊號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"nerve impulses","meaning":"神經脈衝","examples":[{"en":"Nerve impulses control the activation of muscle fibres.","zh":"神經脈衝控制肌肉纖維的啟動。"},{"en":"Nerve impulses are electrical signals that travel through nerves to send instructions or information.","zh":"Nerve impulses 是透過神經傳遞指令或資訊的電訊號。"},{"en":"When you touch something hot, nerve impulses quickly carry the warning to your brain.","zh":"當你觸碰熱物時，神經脈衝迅速把警告傳到大腦。"},{"en":"If nerve impulses tell a muscle to contract, the muscle can move.","zh":"如果神經脈衝指示肌肉收縮，肌肉便能移動。"},{"en":"This phrase names the body’s electrical messages.","zh":"這個片語命名身體的電訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"travel through the muscles","meaning":"穿過肌肉傳遞","examples":[{"en":"The sensors recorded impulses travelling through the cyclists’ muscles.","zh":"感應器記錄穿過單車手肌肉傳遞的脈衝。"},{"en":"To travel through the muscles means to pass through muscle tissue or along nerves connected to it.","zh":"To travel through the muscles 指穿過肌肉組織或沿着連接肌肉的神經傳遞。"},{"en":"Electrical signals travel through the muscles when the body prepares to move.","zh":"當身體準備移動時，電訊號會穿過肌肉傳遞。"},{"en":"If signals travel less strongly through the muscles, movement may become weaker.","zh":"如果訊號穿過肌肉時變弱，動作可能變得較無力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes signals moving within the body.","zh":"這個片語描述訊號在身體內移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"available muscle fibres","meaning":"可使用的肌肉纖維","examples":[{"en":"The body does not use all its available muscle fibres in one contraction.","zh":"身體在一次收縮中不會使用所有可使用的肌肉纖維。"},{"en":"Available muscle fibres are muscle fibres that could potentially be used for movement.","zh":"Available muscle fibres 是可能被用於動作的肌肉纖維。"},{"en":"During a gentle walk, the body uses only some of its available muscle fibres.","zh":"在輕鬆步行時，身體只使用部分可使用的肌肉纖維。"},{"en":"If more force is needed, the nervous system may recruit additional available fibres.","zh":"如果需要更大力量，神經系統可能調動額外可用纖維。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unused but possible muscle resources.","zh":"這個片語描述尚未使用但可動用的肌肉資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in a single contraction","meaning":"在一次肌肉收縮中","examples":[{"en":"The body never uses every muscle fibre in a single contraction.","zh":"身體從不在一次肌肉收縮中使用每一條肌肉纖維。"},{"en":"In a single contraction means during one tightening movement of a muscle.","zh":"In a single contraction 指在肌肉一次收緊動作期間。"},{"en":"When you lift a light cup, your arm does not use all muscle fibres in a single contraction.","zh":"當你拿起輕杯子時，手臂不會在一次肌肉收縮中使用所有纖維。"},{"en":"If one contraction used everything, the body would have little reserve for later effort.","zh":"如果一次收縮用盡所有力量，身體之後就幾乎沒有儲備。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to one individual muscle action.","zh":"這個片語指一次個別肌肉動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the amount used varies","meaning":"使用量有所不同","examples":[{"en":"The amount of muscle used varies according to the activity.","zh":"使用的肌肉量會根據活動而有所不同。"},{"en":"The amount used varies means the quantity used changes depending on the situation.","zh":"The amount used varies 指使用的數量會因情況而改變。"},{"en":"The amount of water used varies between a quick shower and a full bath.","zh":"快速淋浴和浸浴之間，用水量有所不同。"},{"en":"If the activity is harder, the body may use a larger share of muscle fibres.","zh":"如果活動更困難，身體可能使用更大比例的肌肉纖維。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing levels of use.","zh":"這個片語描述使用程度的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"endurance tasks","meaning":"耐力活動","examples":[{"en":"Cycling over a long period is an endurance task.","zh":"長時間踩單車是一項耐力活動。"},{"en":"Endurance tasks are activities that require effort to be sustained for a long time.","zh":"Endurance tasks 是需要長時間維持努力的活動。"},{"en":"A long-distance swim is an endurance task because the swimmer must keep going steadily.","zh":"長途游泳是耐力活動，因為泳手必須穩定地繼續。"},{"en":"If a task demands endurance, pacing becomes more important than one burst of speed.","zh":"如果任務需要耐力，配速比一次爆發速度更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-lasting physical or mental effort.","zh":"這個片語描述長時間的身體或心理努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"call on","meaning":"動用","examples":[{"en":"The body calls on only part of its available muscle fibres.","zh":"身體只動用部分可使用的肌肉纖維。"},{"en":"To call on a resource means to use or draw upon it when needed.","zh":"To call on a resource 指在需要時使用或借助某資源。"},{"en":"A teacher may call on past examples to explain a difficult grammar point.","zh":"老師可能動用過往例子來解釋困難文法點。"},{"en":"If the body calls on more fibres, it can produce more force.","zh":"如果身體動用更多纖維，它可以產生更大力量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using a resource that is available.","zh":"這個片語描述使用可用資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"about thirty per cent","meaning":"約百分之三十","examples":[{"en":"During the cycling test, the body called on about thirty per cent of its muscle fibres.","zh":"在單車測試期間，身體動用了約百分之三十的肌肉纖維。"},{"en":"About thirty per cent means roughly three out of every ten parts.","zh":"About thirty per cent 指大約每十份中的三份。"},{"en":"About thirty per cent of a class may join a sports team if training is held after school.","zh":"如果訓練在放學後舉行，一班中約百分之三十學生可能加入運動隊。"},{"en":"If only thirty per cent is used, much of the total remains unused.","zh":"如果只使用百分之三十，大部分總量仍未被使用。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate proportion.","zh":"這個片語給出大約比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reason that","meaning":"推斷；推論","examples":[{"en":"Noakes reasoned that tired muscles should require additional fibres.","zh":"Noakes 推斷疲倦肌肉應該需要額外纖維。"},{"en":"To reason that something is true means to reach a conclusion through logical thinking.","zh":"To reason that something is true 指透過邏輯思考得出某結論。"},{"en":"A teacher may reason that homework was too hard if most students made the same mistake.","zh":"如果大多數學生犯同一錯誤，老師可能推斷功課太難。"},{"en":"If a theory predicts one result, researchers can reason what should happen in an experiment.","zh":"如果理論預測某結果，研究人員可以推論實驗中應該發生甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes logical thinking from evidence or assumptions.","zh":"這個片語描述根據證據或假設作出的邏輯思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"if the theory was correct","meaning":"如果該理論正確","examples":[{"en":"If the limitations theory was correct, muscle activity should have increased.","zh":"如果極限理論正確，肌肉活動應該增加。"},{"en":"If the theory was correct means if the explanation truly matched reality.","zh":"If the theory was correct 指如果該解釋真正符合現實。"},{"en":"If the teacher’s theory was correct, students who revised earlier should score higher.","zh":"如果老師的理論正確，較早溫習的學生應該得分較高。"},{"en":"If predicted results do not appear, the theory may need to be changed.","zh":"如果預測結果沒有出現，理論可能需要修改。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a testable prediction from an idea.","zh":"這個片語引出來自某想法的可測試預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be due to","meaning":"由……造成","examples":[{"en":"The old theory claims that fatigue is due to muscle fibres reaching a limit.","zh":"舊理論聲稱疲勞由肌肉纖維達到極限造成。"},{"en":"To be due to something means to be caused by it.","zh":"To be due to something 指由某事造成。"},{"en":"A student’s headache may be due to lack of sleep and too much screen time.","zh":"學生頭痛可能由睡眠不足和螢幕時間過多造成。"},{"en":"If fatigue is due to the brain, muscle chemistry alone cannot fully explain it.","zh":"如果疲勞由大腦造成，單靠肌肉化學作用不能完全解釋它。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the cause of a result.","zh":"這個片語指出結果的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pedal stroke","meaning":"踏單車時每一下踩踏","examples":[{"en":"The researchers measured muscle activity during each pedal stroke.","zh":"研究人員量度踏單車時每一下踩踏期間的肌肉活動。"},{"en":"A pedal stroke is one complete pushing movement on a bicycle pedal.","zh":"Pedal stroke 是踩單車踏板的一次完整推動動作。"},{"en":"A cycling coach may study each pedal stroke to improve a rider’s efficiency.","zh":"單車教練可能研究每一下踩踏，以改善騎手效率。"},{"en":"If pedal strokes become weaker, the cyclist’s speed may fall.","zh":"如果踩踏變弱，單車手速度可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one movement in cycling.","zh":"這個片語描述單車運動中的一次動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"attempt to compensate","meaning":"嘗試補償","examples":[{"en":"The cyclist’s body should attempt to compensate for tiring muscle fibres.","zh":"單車手的身體應嘗試補償疲倦的肌肉纖維。"},{"en":"To attempt to compensate means to try to make up for a weakness, loss, or problem.","zh":"To attempt to compensate 指嘗試彌補弱點、損失或問題。"},{"en":"A student may attempt to compensate for poor handwriting by organising answers very clearly.","zh":"學生可能透過非常清楚地組織答案，嘗試補償字跡差的問題。"},{"en":"If one muscle group tires, the body may try to use other fibres to maintain performance.","zh":"如果某組肌肉疲倦，身體可能嘗試使用其他纖維維持表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trying to balance or cover a deficit.","zh":"這個片語描述嘗試平衡或彌補不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"recruit muscle fibres","meaning":"調動肌肉纖維","examples":[{"en":"The body can recruit additional muscle fibres during exercise.","zh":"身體可以在運動期間調動額外肌肉纖維。"},{"en":"To recruit muscle fibres means to bring more muscle fibres into action.","zh":"To recruit muscle fibres 指把更多肌肉纖維投入運作。"},{"en":"When lifting a heavy box, the body recruits more muscle fibres than when lifting a pencil.","zh":"搬起重箱時，身體調動的肌肉纖維比拿起鉛筆時更多。"},{"en":"If more fibres are recruited, the muscle can produce more force for a short time.","zh":"如果更多纖維被調動，肌肉可以短時間內產生更大力量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes activating extra muscle resources.","zh":"這個片語描述啟動額外肌肉資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an ever-larger proportion of","meaning":"比例不斷增加的……","examples":[{"en":"The old theory predicted the use of an ever-larger proportion of muscle fibres.","zh":"舊理論預測會使用比例不斷增加的肌肉纖維。"},{"en":"An ever-larger proportion of something means a share that keeps increasing over time.","zh":"An ever-larger proportion of something 指某事物所佔比例隨時間不斷增加。"},{"en":"A growing company may need an ever-larger proportion of its budget for staff training.","zh":"成長中的公司可能需要把比例不斷增加的預算用於員工培訓。"},{"en":"If tired muscles need help, the old theory would expect more fibres to be used.","zh":"如果疲倦肌肉需要幫助，舊理論會預期更多纖維被使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a steadily increasing share.","zh":"這個片語描述持續增加的比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the total","meaning":"總數","examples":[{"en":"The researchers measured the proportion of the total muscle fibres being used.","zh":"研究人員量度正在使用的肌肉纖維佔總數的比例。"},{"en":"The total means the whole amount of something.","zh":"The total 指某事物的全部數量。"},{"en":"If ten students are absent from a class of forty, one quarter of the total is missing.","zh":"如果四十人的班有十名學生缺席，總數的四分之一缺席。"},{"en":"To understand a proportion, we need to know both the part and the total.","zh":"要理解比例，我們需要知道部分和總數。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the complete number or amount.","zh":"這個片語指完整數量或總量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"find exactly the opposite","meaning":"發現結果恰好相反","examples":[{"en":"The research team found exactly the opposite of what the old theory predicted.","zh":"研究團隊發現結果與舊理論預測恰好相反。"},{"en":"To find exactly the opposite means to discover a result that directly contradicts what was expected.","zh":"To find exactly the opposite 指發現與預期直接矛盾的結果。"},{"en":"A teacher may expect extra homework to help, but find exactly the opposite if students become exhausted.","zh":"老師可能預期額外功課有幫助，但如果學生變得疲憊，可能發現結果恰好相反。"},{"en":"If evidence shows the opposite result, the original theory becomes doubtful.","zh":"如果證據顯示相反結果，原本理論就變得可疑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a direct reversal of expectation.","zh":"這個片語描述預期的直接反轉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as fatigue sets in","meaning":"隨着疲勞開始出現","examples":[{"en":"Electrical activity declined as fatigue set in.","zh":"隨着疲勞開始出現，電流活動下降。"},{"en":"As fatigue sets in means when tiredness begins to appear and affect performance.","zh":"As fatigue sets in 指疲倦開始出現並影響表現時。"},{"en":"As fatigue sets in during revision, a student may read the same line several times.","zh":"溫習期間隨着疲勞開始出現，學生可能同一行讀好幾次。"},{"en":"If fatigue sets in early, speed and accuracy may decline.","zh":"如果疲勞很早出現，速度和準確度可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of tiredness.","zh":"這個片語描述疲倦開始形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"electrical activity","meaning":"電流活動","examples":[{"en":"The electrical activity in the cyclists’ legs declined.","zh":"單車手腿部的電流活動下降。"},{"en":"Electrical activity is the measurable electrical signalling in nerves or muscles.","zh":"Electrical activity 是神經或肌肉中可量度的電訊號活動。"},{"en":"Doctors may record electrical activity in the heart to check whether it beats normally.","zh":"醫生可能記錄心臟的電流活動，以檢查心跳是否正常。"},{"en":"If electrical activity in a muscle decreases, that muscle may be receiving fewer activation signals.","zh":"如果肌肉中的電流活動減少，該肌肉可能收到較少啟動訊號。"},{"en":"This phrase describes body signals that can be measured by equipment.","zh":"這個片語描述可由設備量度的身體訊號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"decline during exercise","meaning":"在運動期間下降","examples":[{"en":"Muscular electrical activity declined as the cyclists became tired.","zh":"隨着單車手變得疲倦，肌肉電流活動在運動期間下降。"},{"en":"To decline during exercise means to decrease while physical activity is taking place.","zh":"To decline during exercise 指在身體活動進行期間減少。"},{"en":"A runner’s speed may decline during exercise if the pace is too fast at the start.","zh":"如果一開始速度太快，跑手速度可能在運動期間下降。"},{"en":"If a measurement declines during exercise, researchers ask what is causing the drop.","zh":"如果某量度在運動期間下降，研究人員會問是甚麼造成下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reduction that happens while someone is exercising.","zh":"這個片語描述人在運動時發生的減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"even during sprinting","meaning":"即使在全速衝刺時","examples":[{"en":"Muscle activity declined even during sprinting.","zh":"肌肉活動即使在全速衝刺時也下降。"},{"en":"Even during sprinting means surprisingly, the result happened while the athlete was trying to go very fast.","zh":"Even during sprinting 指令人意外地，結果在運動員嘗試高速前進時仍發生。"},{"en":"A tired runner may lose form even during sprinting toward the finish line.","zh":"疲倦跑手即使在向終點線全速衝刺時，也可能姿勢變差。"},{"en":"If muscle activity falls during sprinting, it challenges the idea that effort is always increasing.","zh":"如果肌肉活動在全速衝刺時下降，它就挑戰努力程度總是在增加的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a surprising contrast.","zh":"這個片語突出令人意外的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"strive to","meaning":"努力去……","examples":[{"en":"The cyclists were striving to cycle as fast as they could.","zh":"單車手正努力盡可能踩得最快。"},{"en":"To strive to do something means to try very hard to achieve it.","zh":"To strive to do something 指非常努力去達成某事。"},{"en":"A student may strive to improve writing by practising one paragraph every day.","zh":"學生可能每天練習一段文章，努力改善寫作。"},{"en":"If someone strives to reach a goal, they usually invest effort and discipline.","zh":"如果某人努力達成目標，他通常會投入努力和紀律。"},{"en":"This phrase describes determined effort.","zh":"這個片語描述堅定努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"strong evidence that","meaning":"證明……的有力證據","examples":[{"en":"Noakes regarded the results as strong evidence that the old theory was wrong.","zh":"Noakes 認為結果是證明舊理論錯誤的有力證據。"},{"en":"Strong evidence that something is true is powerful support for a conclusion.","zh":"Strong evidence that something is true 是支持某結論的有力證據。"},{"en":"Repeated test improvement can be strong evidence that a study method works.","zh":"測驗成績反覆進步，可以成為證明學習方法有效的有力證據。"},{"en":"If evidence is strong, it becomes harder to defend the old explanation.","zh":"如果證據有力，維護舊解釋就變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes convincing proof.","zh":"這個片語描述令人信服的證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"feel completely exhausted","meaning":"感到筋疲力盡","examples":[{"en":"The cyclists may have felt completely exhausted.","zh":"單車手可能感到筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"To feel completely exhausted means to feel so tired that continuing seems almost impossible.","zh":"To feel completely exhausted 指疲倦到感覺幾乎不能繼續。"},{"en":"A parent may feel completely exhausted after caring for a sick child all night.","zh":"家長整晚照顧生病孩子後，可能感到筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"If someone feels completely exhausted, their body may still have reserves they cannot easily access.","zh":"如果某人感到筋疲力盡，身體可能仍有他不能輕易動用的儲備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extreme subjective tiredness.","zh":"這個片語描述極端主觀疲倦感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"considerable reserves","meaning":"相當多的儲備","examples":[{"en":"The cyclists still had considerable physical reserves.","zh":"單車手仍有相當多的身體儲備。"},{"en":"Considerable reserves are large remaining supplies of energy, strength, money, or resources.","zh":"Considerable reserves 是仍然剩下的大量能量、力量、金錢或資源。"},{"en":"A family with considerable savings can handle an unexpected repair more calmly.","zh":"有相當多儲蓄的家庭，可以更冷靜處理突如其來的維修。"},{"en":"If athletes still have reserves, fatigue may be a warning before total failure.","zh":"如果運動員仍有儲備，疲勞可能是在完全失效前的警告。"},{"en":"This phrase describes significant resources that are still available.","zh":"這個片語描述仍可使用的重要資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"theoretically tap","meaning":"理論上可動用","examples":[{"en":"The athletes could theoretically tap their unused reserves.","zh":"運動員理論上可動用未使用的儲備。"},{"en":"To theoretically tap a reserve means to be able in principle to use a stored resource.","zh":"To theoretically tap a reserve 指原則上能使用某種儲存資源。"},{"en":"A school could theoretically tap empty classrooms for after-school study groups.","zh":"學校理論上可動用空置課室作課後自修小組。"},{"en":"If a resource is available in theory, practical limits may still prevent its use.","zh":"如果資源理論上可用，實際限制仍可能阻止使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes possible access, not guaranteed real use.","zh":"這個片語描述可能動用，而不保證真正使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a greater proportion of","meaning":"更大比例的……","examples":[{"en":"The cyclists could have used a greater proportion of their resting fibres.","zh":"單車手本可以使用更大比例的休息中肌肉纖維。"},{"en":"A greater proportion of something means a larger share of the total amount.","zh":"A greater proportion of something 指總量中更大的份額。"},{"en":"A school may spend a greater proportion of its budget on counselling after student stress rises.","zh":"學生壓力上升後，學校可能把更大比例的預算用於輔導。"},{"en":"If athletes use a greater proportion of fibres, more muscle resources are being activated.","zh":"如果運動員使用更大比例的纖維，更多肌肉資源正在被啟動。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how large one share is.","zh":"這個片語比較某份額有多大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"resting fibres","meaning":"處於休息狀態的肌肉纖維","examples":[{"en":"Many resting muscle fibres remained available during the test.","zh":"測試期間，許多處於休息狀態的肌肉纖維仍可使用。"},{"en":"Resting fibres are muscle fibres that are not actively working at a particular moment.","zh":"Resting fibres 是在某一刻沒有積極工作的肌肉纖維。"},{"en":"During light walking, many leg muscle fibres remain resting because the effort is low.","zh":"輕鬆步行時，許多腿部肌肉纖維仍處於休息狀態，因為用力程度低。"},{"en":"If resting fibres are still available, the muscle is not using its full capacity.","zh":"如果仍有休息中的纖維可用，肌肉並未使用全部能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes muscle fibres kept in reserve.","zh":"這個片語描述被保留作儲備的肌肉纖維。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be proof that","meaning":"證明……","examples":[{"en":"Noakes believes the results are proof that the brain regulates effort.","zh":"Noakes 相信這些結果證明大腦會調節努力程度。"},{"en":"To be proof that something is true means to provide evidence strong enough to support that conclusion.","zh":"To be proof that something is true 指提供足夠強的證據支持該結論。"},{"en":"A student’s improved essays may be proof that regular feedback is helping.","zh":"學生作文進步可能證明定期回饋正在發揮作用。"},{"en":"If results repeatedly support one explanation, they may become proof for that theory.","zh":"如果結果反覆支持同一解釋，它們可能成為該理論的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence used to confirm a claim.","zh":"這個片語描述用來確認主張的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"regulate the pace of","meaning":"調節……的速度","examples":[{"en":"The brain regulates the pace of the workout.","zh":"大腦調節運動的速度。"},{"en":"To regulate the pace of something means to control how fast or intense it is over time.","zh":"To regulate the pace of something 指隨時間控制某事的速度或強度。"},{"en":"A teacher may regulate the pace of a lesson so weaker students can follow.","zh":"老師可能調節課堂速度，讓能力較弱的學生跟上。"},{"en":"If pace is regulated well, effort can be sustained longer.","zh":"如果速度調節得好，努力就可以維持更久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled adjustment of speed or intensity.","zh":"這個片語描述對速度或強度的受控調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the pace of the workout","meaning":"運動的節奏","examples":[{"en":"The central governor controls the pace of the workout.","zh":"中央調控系統控制運動的節奏。"},{"en":"The pace of the workout is how fast or intensely the exercise is performed.","zh":"Pace of the workout 是運動進行的速度或強度。"},{"en":"A beginner should keep the pace of the workout gentle during the first week.","zh":"初學者第一週應把運動節奏保持溫和。"},{"en":"If the pace is too high at the start, fatigue may arrive early.","zh":"如果一開始節奏太快，疲勞可能很早出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the speed and effort level of exercise.","zh":"這個片語描述運動的速度和努力程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hold someone back from","meaning":"阻止某人達到……","examples":[{"en":"The brain holds the athlete back from catastrophic exhaustion.","zh":"大腦阻止運動員達到災難性耗竭。"},{"en":"To hold someone back from something means to stop them from reaching or doing it.","zh":"To hold someone back from something 指阻止某人達到或做某事。"},{"en":"Fear may hold a student back from speaking English even when they know the answer.","zh":"恐懼可能阻止學生說英文，即使他知道答案。"},{"en":"If the brain holds an athlete back, it may be protecting the body from danger.","zh":"如果大腦阻止運動員繼續，它可能正在保護身體免受危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes restraint or prevention.","zh":"這個片語描述限制或阻止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the point of catastrophic exhaustion","meaning":"災難性衰竭的臨界點","examples":[{"en":"The body is kept away from the point of catastrophic exhaustion.","zh":"身體被保持在遠離災難性衰竭臨界點的位置。"},{"en":"The point of catastrophic exhaustion is the dangerous stage where the body may fail seriously.","zh":"Point of catastrophic exhaustion 是身體可能嚴重失效的危險階段。"},{"en":"A hiker without water may approach the point of catastrophic exhaustion in extreme heat.","zh":"在酷熱中沒有水的行山者，可能接近災難性衰竭的臨界點。"},{"en":"If the body reaches this point, stopping may no longer be a choice but a necessity.","zh":"如果身體到達這一點，停止可能不再是選擇，而是必須。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a severe physical danger point.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重身體危險點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"further evidence comes from","meaning":"進一步證據來自……","examples":[{"en":"Further evidence comes from measurements of muscle fuel.","zh":"進一步證據來自對肌肉燃料的量度。"},{"en":"Further evidence comes from something means additional support is provided by that source.","zh":"Further evidence comes from something 指額外支持由某來源提供。"},{"en":"Further evidence for poor sleep comes from students’ low energy in morning classes.","zh":"支持睡眠不足的進一步證據，來自學生早上課堂精力低。"},{"en":"If several sources provide evidence, a theory becomes more convincing.","zh":"如果幾個來源提供證據，理論就變得更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces another supporting fact.","zh":"這個片語引出另一項支持事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"run out of anything critical","meaning":"耗盡任何關鍵物質","examples":[{"en":"Fatigued muscles do not actually run out of anything critical.","zh":"疲倦肌肉其實沒有耗盡任何關鍵物質。"},{"en":"To run out of anything critical means to use up something essential for continuing.","zh":"To run out of anything critical 指用光繼續下去所必需的東西。"},{"en":"A phone cannot keep working if it runs out of battery, which is critical to its function.","zh":"如果手機耗盡電池這項關鍵資源，就不能繼續運作。"},{"en":"If muscles do not run out of critical fuel, fatigue may not be simple fuel failure.","zh":"如果肌肉沒有耗盡關鍵燃料，疲勞可能不是簡單燃料失效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes losing an essential resource.","zh":"這個片語描述失去必需資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"glycogen","meaning":"糖原","examples":[{"en":"Glycogen is the muscles’ primary fuel.","zh":"糖原是肌肉的主要燃料。"},{"en":"Glycogen is a stored form of carbohydrate that the body can use for energy.","zh":"Glycogen 是碳水化合物在體內儲存的形式，可被用作能量。"},{"en":"A runner may eat carbohydrates before a long race to help build glycogen stores.","zh":"跑手可能在長跑前進食碳水化合物，以幫助建立糖原儲備。"},{"en":"If glycogen levels fall, sustained exercise may feel harder.","zh":"如果糖原水平下降，持續運動可能感覺更困難。"},{"en":"This word names an important energy store in the body.","zh":"這個詞命名身體中重要的能量儲備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the muscles’ primary fuel","meaning":"肌肉的主要燃料","examples":[{"en":"Glycogen acts as the muscles’ primary fuel.","zh":"糖原作為肌肉的主要燃料。"},{"en":"The muscles’ primary fuel is the main energy source muscles use during activity.","zh":"Muscles’ primary fuel 是肌肉在活動期間使用的主要能量來源。"},{"en":"Carbohydrates help provide the muscles’ primary fuel for long runs and hard training.","zh":"碳水化合物幫助為長跑和艱苦訓練提供肌肉的主要燃料。"},{"en":"If the main fuel declines, athletes may need to reduce pace or refuel.","zh":"如果主要燃料下降，運動員可能需要降低速度或補充燃料。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the chief energy source for muscles.","zh":"這個片語指出肌肉的主要能量來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ATP","meaning":"三磷酸腺苷","examples":[{"en":"ATP is used for temporary energy storage in the muscles.","zh":"三磷酸腺苷用於肌肉中的暫時能量儲存。"},{"en":"ATP is a molecule that cells use to store and release energy quickly.","zh":"ATP 是細胞用來快速儲存和釋放能量的分子。"},{"en":"Science students may learn that ATP powers many small activities inside cells.","zh":"科學學生可能學到 ATP 為細胞內許多小活動供能。"},{"en":"If ATP supply were completely lost, muscles could not keep contracting normally.","zh":"如果 ATP 供應完全失去，肌肉不能維持正常收縮。"},{"en":"This term names a key energy molecule in biology.","zh":"這個術語命名生物學中的關鍵能量分子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"temporary energy storage","meaning":"暫時能量儲存","examples":[{"en":"ATP provides temporary energy storage in muscle cells.","zh":"ATP 在肌肉細胞中提供暫時能量儲存。"},{"en":"Temporary energy storage means holding energy for quick short-term use.","zh":"Temporary energy storage 指把能量保存起來，以供快速短期使用。"},{"en":"A phone power bank provides temporary energy storage when there is no socket nearby.","zh":"附近沒有插座時，手機充電寶提供暫時能量儲存。"},{"en":"If energy must be used instantly, temporary storage becomes important.","zh":"如果能量必須即時使用，暫時儲存就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes short-term energy holding, not long-term fuel reserves.","zh":"這個片語描述短期能量保存，而不是長期燃料儲備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"decline with exercise","meaning":"隨運動而下降","examples":[{"en":"Glycogen and ATP levels decline with exercise.","zh":"糖原和 ATP 水平隨運動而下降。"},{"en":"To decline with exercise means to decrease as physical activity continues.","zh":"To decline with exercise 指隨身體活動持續而減少。"},{"en":"A runner’s water level can decline with exercise if they do not drink enough.","zh":"如果跑手不喝足夠水，身體水分可隨運動而下降。"},{"en":"If fuel levels decline with exercise, the body may signal tiredness before they reach zero.","zh":"如果燃料水平隨運動下降，身體可能在它們降至零前已發出疲勞訊號。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a drop caused by ongoing activity.","zh":"這個片語描述持續活動造成的下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"bottom out","meaning":"降至最低點","examples":[{"en":"ATP and glycogen levels decline but never bottom out.","zh":"ATP 和糖原水平下降，但從未降至最低點。"},{"en":"To bottom out means to fall to the lowest possible level.","zh":"To bottom out 指跌至最低可能水平。"},{"en":"A shop’s sales may bottom out during a storm and then recover when customers return.","zh":"商店銷售可能在暴風雨期間降至最低點，之後顧客回來便恢復。"},{"en":"If fuel levels do not bottom out, some reserves remain even when the person feels tired.","zh":"如果燃料水平沒有降至最低點，即使人感到疲倦，仍有一些儲備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching the very bottom.","zh":"這個片語描述到達最低點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the resting norm","meaning":"休息時的正常水平","examples":[{"en":"ATP levels remain close to the resting norm even after a marathon.","zh":"即使在馬拉松後，ATP 水平仍接近休息時的正常水平。"},{"en":"The resting norm is the normal level measured when the body is at rest.","zh":"Resting norm 是身體休息時量度到的正常水平。"},{"en":"A doctor may compare a patient’s heart rate after exercise with the resting norm.","zh":"醫生可能把病人運動後的心率與休息時的正常水平比較。"},{"en":"If a value stays near the resting norm, it has not changed dramatically.","zh":"如果數值保持接近休息時正常水平，它就沒有大幅改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the normal baseline level.","zh":"這個片語描述正常基準水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"get to zero","meaning":"降至零","examples":[{"en":"Glycogen levels do not get to zero during a marathon.","zh":"糖原水平在馬拉松期間不會降至零。"},{"en":"To get to zero means to fall until nothing is left.","zh":"To get to zero 指下降至完全沒有剩餘。"},{"en":"A student should charge a laptop before the battery gets to zero.","zh":"學生應在手提電腦電量降至零前充電。"},{"en":"If a resource never gets to zero, complete depletion has not happened.","zh":"如果某資源從未降至零，完全耗盡就沒有發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching absolute emptiness.","zh":"這個片語描述到達完全空無。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"further support for","meaning":"對……的進一步支持","examples":[{"en":"The behaviour of top athletes provides further support for the theory.","zh":"頂尖運動員的行為為該理論提供進一步支持。"},{"en":"Further support for something is additional evidence that strengthens it.","zh":"Further support for something 是加強某事的額外證據。"},{"en":"Better attendance may provide further support for a school’s new morning routine.","zh":"更好的出席率可能為學校新的早晨安排提供進一步支持。"},{"en":"If several observations support the same idea, confidence in the idea increases.","zh":"如果幾項觀察都支持同一想法，人們對該想法的信心會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces extra backing for an argument.","zh":"這個片語引出對論點的額外支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"top athletes","meaning":"頂尖運動員","examples":[{"en":"Top athletes can often accelerate near the end of a race.","zh":"頂尖運動員常能在賽事接近尾聲時加速。"},{"en":"Top athletes are sportspeople who perform at a very high level.","zh":"Top athletes 是在體育上表現達很高水平的人。"},{"en":"Top athletes usually train carefully, rest strategically, and monitor their bodies.","zh":"頂尖運動員通常仔細訓練、有策略地休息並監察身體。"},{"en":"If top athletes can sprint when tired, fatigue may not mean total physical depletion.","zh":"如果頂尖運動員疲倦時仍能衝刺，疲勞可能不代表身體完全耗盡。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to elite sports performers.","zh":"這個片語指精英體育表現者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"manage to go their fastest","meaning":"成功以最快速度前進","examples":[{"en":"Top athletes usually manage to go their fastest at the end of a race.","zh":"頂尖運動員通常能在賽事尾段成功以最快速度前進。"},{"en":"To manage to go their fastest means to succeed in reaching their highest speed despite difficulty.","zh":"To manage to go their fastest 指儘管困難仍成功達到最高速度。"},{"en":"A tired student may still manage to write fastest in the final minutes of an exam.","zh":"疲倦學生可能仍在考試最後幾分鐘成功以最快速度書寫。"},{"en":"If athletes go fastest near the end, some reserve must still be available.","zh":"如果運動員在接近終點時速度最快，必然仍有一些儲備可用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes successful peak speed under pressure.","zh":"這個片語描述在壓力下成功達到最高速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at the end of a race","meaning":"在賽事尾段","examples":[{"en":"Many athletes produce their greatest speed at the end of a race.","zh":"許多運動員在賽事尾段跑出最高速度。"},{"en":"At the end of a race means during the final part before the finish line.","zh":"At the end of a race 指終點線前的最後部分。"},{"en":"Runners often hear the crowd more clearly at the end of a race.","zh":"跑手在賽事尾段通常更清楚聽到觀眾聲音。"},{"en":"If effort increases at the end, athletes may be responding to the knowledge that the finish is near.","zh":"如果努力在尾段增加，運動員可能正回應終點已近這一認知。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the closing stage of competition.","zh":"這個片語描述比賽的結尾階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be closest to exhaustion","meaning":"最接近筋疲力盡","examples":[{"en":"The muscles should theoretically be closest to exhaustion near the finish.","zh":"理論上，肌肉應在接近終點時最接近筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"To be closest to exhaustion means to be nearest to complete tiredness or failure.","zh":"To be closest to exhaustion 指最接近完全疲倦或失效。"},{"en":"A student may be closest to exhaustion after the final exam of a long week.","zh":"學生可能在漫長一週的最後一場考試後最接近筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"If someone is closest to exhaustion, we might expect them to slow down rather than speed up.","zh":"如果某人最接近筋疲力盡，我們可能預期他會慢下來，而不是加速。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the point where tiredness should be greatest.","zh":"這個片語描述疲倦理應最強的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the end spurt","meaning":"終點前衝刺","examples":[{"en":"The end spurt challenges traditional explanations of fatigue.","zh":"終點前衝刺挑戰疲勞的傳統解釋。"},{"en":"The end spurt is the sudden increase in speed near the end of a race.","zh":"End spurt 是比賽接近尾聲時突然加速。"},{"en":"A runner may save energy for an end spurt in the last hundred metres.","zh":"跑手可能為最後一百米的終點前衝刺保留能量。"},{"en":"If athletes can produce an end spurt, they must still have usable energy left.","zh":"如果運動員能作終點前衝刺，他們必然仍有可用能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a final burst of effort.","zh":"這個片語描述最後一段爆發努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make no sense","meaning":"說不通；不合理","examples":[{"en":"The end spurt makes no sense under the traditional theory.","zh":"在傳統理論下，終點前衝刺說不通。"},{"en":"To make no sense means to be illogical, confusing, or impossible to explain.","zh":"To make no sense 指不合邏輯、令人困惑或無法解釋。"},{"en":"It makes no sense to buy new books if the school library already has enough copies.","zh":"如果學校圖書館已有足夠副本，再買新書就說不通。"},{"en":"If evidence makes no sense under one theory, another explanation may be needed.","zh":"如果證據在某理論下說不通，可能需要另一個解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that does not fit logically.","zh":"這個片語描述邏輯上不配合的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"poison themselves with","meaning":"因……而令自身中毒","examples":[{"en":"The old theory suggests that muscles poison themselves with lactic acid.","zh":"舊理論認為肌肉因乳酸而令自身中毒。"},{"en":"To poison themselves with something means to harm themselves by accumulating a damaging substance.","zh":"To poison themselves with something 指因累積有害物質而傷害自身。"},{"en":"A river may poison itself with waste if dirty water keeps entering and cannot flow away.","zh":"如果污水不斷流入又不能排走，河流可能因廢物而令自身中毒。"},{"en":"If muscles poisoned themselves with lactic acid, more lactic acid should cause worse fatigue.","zh":"如果肌肉因乳酸而自身中毒，更多乳酸應造成更嚴重疲勞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes self-damage through harmful build-up.","zh":"這個片語描述因有害積聚而自我損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cause someone to slow down","meaning":"令某人減速","examples":[{"en":"Excess lactic acid should cause racers to slow down.","zh":"過量乳酸理應令賽跑者減速。"},{"en":"To cause someone to slow down means to make them reduce speed or effort.","zh":"To cause someone to slow down 指令某人降低速度或努力程度。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can cause drivers to slow down on a motorway.","zh":"大雨可以令司機在高速公路上減速。"},{"en":"If pain causes an athlete to slow down, it may be acting as a warning signal.","zh":"如果疼痛令運動員減速，它可能正在作為警告訊號。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a factor that reduces pace.","zh":"這個片語描述降低速度的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rather than enable someone to","meaning":"而不是使某人能夠……","examples":[{"en":"Lactic acid should slow racers down rather than enable them to sprint.","zh":"乳酸理應令賽跑者慢下來，而不是使他們能夠衝刺。"},{"en":"Rather than enable someone to do something means instead of helping them do it.","zh":"Rather than enable someone to do something 指不是幫助某人做到某事。"},{"en":"Poor feedback may confuse students rather than enable them to improve.","zh":"差劣回饋可能令學生困惑，而不是使他們能夠進步。"},{"en":"If a factor is harmful, it should reduce performance rather than enable better performance.","zh":"如果某因素有害，它理應降低表現，而不是使表現更好。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a clear contrast between expected harm and unexpected help.","zh":"這個片語在預期傷害與意外幫助之間建立清楚對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sprint for the finish line","meaning":"向終點線衝刺","examples":[{"en":"Athletes often sprint for the finish line despite feeling tired.","zh":"運動員即使感到疲倦，也常向終點線衝刺。"},{"en":"To sprint for the finish line means to run or move as fast as possible toward the end of a race.","zh":"To sprint for the finish line 指朝比賽終點盡可能快速奔跑或移動。"},{"en":"A runner may sprint for the finish line when they hear the crowd cheering.","zh":"跑手聽到觀眾歡呼時，可能向終點線衝刺。"},{"en":"If athletes sprint at the end, they show that some energy has been held back.","zh":"如果運動員在尾段衝刺，就顯示有些能量被保留下來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a final high-speed effort.","zh":"這個片語描述最後的高速努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the explanation is obvious","meaning":"解釋很明顯","examples":[{"en":"Under the new theory, the explanation is obvious.","zh":"在新理論下，解釋很明顯。"},{"en":"The explanation is obvious means the reason is clear and easy to see.","zh":"The explanation is obvious 指原因清楚而容易看出。"},{"en":"If a student studied every day and improved, the explanation is obvious.","zh":"如果學生每天溫習並進步，解釋很明顯。"},{"en":"When a theory fits the evidence well, the explanation may seem simple.","zh":"當理論很好地配合證據，解釋可能顯得簡單。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a reason that appears clear.","zh":"這個片語引出看似清楚的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"know the end is near","meaning":"知道終點已近","examples":[{"en":"The brain knows when the end of the race is near.","zh":"大腦知道賽事終點已近。"},{"en":"To know the end is near means to realise that a task or effort is almost finished.","zh":"To know the end is near 指意識到一項任務或努力快要完成。"},{"en":"A student may write faster when they know the end of the exam is near.","zh":"學生知道考試接近尾聲時，可能寫得更快。"},{"en":"If the brain knows the end is near, it may allow more effort for the final stage.","zh":"如果大腦知道終點已近，它可能容許最後階段投入更多努力。"},{"en":"This phrase links awareness of the finish with changed behaviour.","zh":"這個片語把對終點的意識與行為改變連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"relax its vigil","meaning":"稍為放鬆警戒","examples":[{"en":"The brain slightly relaxes its vigil near the end of a race.","zh":"大腦在賽事尾段稍為放鬆警戒。"},{"en":"To relax its vigil means to reduce its careful watch or protective control.","zh":"To relax its vigil 指減少仔細監視或保護性控制。"},{"en":"A teacher may relax her vigil once all students have safely crossed the road.","zh":"當所有學生安全過馬路後，老師可能稍為放鬆警戒。"},{"en":"If the brain relaxes its protective watch, the athlete may access more reserves.","zh":"如果大腦放鬆保護性監察，運動員可能能動用更多儲備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming less strict in monitoring danger.","zh":"這個片語描述在監察危險方面變得不那麼嚴格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"allow someone to tap","meaning":"讓某人動用……","examples":[{"en":"The brain allows the athlete to tap some of the body’s reserves.","zh":"大腦讓運動員動用身體部分儲備。"},{"en":"To allow someone to tap a reserve means to let them use stored resources.","zh":"To allow someone to tap a reserve 指讓某人使用儲存起來的資源。"},{"en":"A school may allow students to tap library computers when they do not have devices at home.","zh":"如果學生家中沒有設備，學校可能讓他們動用圖書館電腦。"},{"en":"If the brain allows more reserves to be used, the athlete may speed up near the finish.","zh":"如果大腦容許更多儲備被使用，運動員可能在接近終點時加速。"},{"en":"This phrase describes permitting access to something stored.","zh":"這個片語描述允許使用儲存的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"carefully hoarded reserves","meaning":"小心保留的儲備","examples":[{"en":"The body retains carefully hoarded reserves for emergencies.","zh":"身體為緊急情況保留小心儲存的儲備。"},{"en":"Carefully hoarded reserves are resources saved deliberately and protected for later use.","zh":"Carefully hoarded reserves 是刻意保存並保護以便日後使用的資源。"},{"en":"A family may keep carefully hoarded savings for medical emergencies.","zh":"家庭可能為醫療緊急情況保留小心儲存的儲蓄。"},{"en":"If reserves are hoarded, they are not used freely during ordinary effort.","zh":"如果儲備被小心保留，它們不會在普通努力中隨便使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protected supplies kept for serious need.","zh":"這個片語描述為嚴重需要而保護的供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"does not mean that","meaning":"並不表示","examples":[{"en":"The theory does not mean that muscular processes are irrelevant.","zh":"該理論並不表示肌肉過程無關重要。"},{"en":"Does not mean that introduces a correction, showing what should not be wrongly concluded.","zh":"Does not mean that 引出更正，顯示不應錯誤得出甚麼結論。"},{"en":"Asking for help does not mean that a student is weak.","zh":"求助並不表示學生軟弱。"},{"en":"If one explanation is incomplete, that does not mean every part of it is useless.","zh":"如果一個解釋不完整，並不表示它每一部分都沒有用。"},{"en":"This phrase prevents misunderstanding.","zh":"這個片語防止誤解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be irrelevant","meaning":"無關重要","examples":[{"en":"What happens in the muscles is not irrelevant to fatigue.","zh":"肌肉中發生的事情並非與疲勞無關。"},{"en":"To be irrelevant means to have no useful connection with the subject.","zh":"To be irrelevant 指與主題沒有有用關聯。"},{"en":"A student’s sleep is not irrelevant to exam performance because tiredness affects focus.","zh":"學生睡眠並非與考試表現無關，因為疲倦會影響專注。"},{"en":"If something is relevant, it should still be considered even if it is not the only cause.","zh":"如果某事相關，即使不是唯一原因，也仍應被考慮。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to reject the idea that something does not matter.","zh":"這個片語常用來否定某事不重要的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"constantly monitor","meaning":"持續監察","examples":[{"en":"The central governor constantly monitors signals from the muscles.","zh":"中央調控系統持續監察來自肌肉的訊號。"},{"en":"To constantly monitor something means to watch or check it continuously.","zh":"To constantly monitor something 指持續觀察或檢查某事。"},{"en":"Nurses constantly monitor a patient’s heart rate after surgery.","zh":"護士在手術後持續監察病人的心率。"},{"en":"If the brain constantly monitors body signals, it can adjust effort before danger arrives.","zh":"如果大腦持續監察身體訊號，它就可以在危險出現前調整努力程度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continuous checking.","zh":"這個片語描述連續檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"physiological signals","meaning":"生理訊號","examples":[{"en":"The brain receives physiological signals from working muscles.","zh":"大腦接收來自工作中肌肉的生理訊號。"},{"en":"Physiological signals are body-based messages about physical condition or function.","zh":"Physiological signals 是關於身體狀況或功能的身體訊息。"},{"en":"Pain, thirst, breathlessness, and heart rate can all be physiological signals.","zh":"疼痛、口渴、氣喘和心率都可以是生理訊號。"},{"en":"If the brain receives warning signals, it may change how hard the body works.","zh":"如果大腦收到警告訊號，它可能改變身體工作強度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information sent by the body.","zh":"這個片語描述身體發出的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"along with","meaning":"連同；以及","examples":[{"en":"The brain considers muscular signals along with other information.","zh":"大腦考慮肌肉訊號，連同其他資訊。"},{"en":"Along with means together with or in addition to.","zh":"Along with 指連同或加上。"},{"en":"A teacher may consider effort along with test scores when judging progress.","zh":"老師評估進步時，可能考慮測驗分數以及努力程度。"},{"en":"If one factor is considered along with others, the decision becomes more balanced.","zh":"如果一個因素連同其他因素一起考慮，決定會更平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase adds extra items to the same situation.","zh":"這個片語把額外項目加入同一情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"set the level of fatigue","meaning":"設定疲勞程度","examples":[{"en":"The brain uses incoming information to set the level of fatigue.","zh":"大腦使用傳入資訊來設定疲勞程度。"},{"en":"To set the level of fatigue means to determine how tired the body feels or is allowed to feel.","zh":"To set the level of fatigue 指決定身體感到多疲倦或被允許感到多疲倦。"},{"en":"A difficult timetable can set a high level of fatigue for students by the end of the day.","zh":"困難時間表可能令學生到一天結束時疲勞程度很高。"},{"en":"If the brain judges a task as long or risky, it may increase fatigue sensations earlier.","zh":"如果大腦判斷任務很長或有風險，它可能更早增加疲勞感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlling the perceived amount of tiredness.","zh":"這個片語描述控制感知到的疲倦程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a large number of","meaning":"大量","examples":[{"en":"A large number of physiological signals may be involved.","zh":"大量生理訊號可能牽涉其中。"},{"en":"A large number of something means many of them.","zh":"A large number of something 指很多某事物。"},{"en":"A large number of students may join a sports day if events are varied and fun.","zh":"如果項目多樣又有趣，大量學生可能參加陸運會。"},{"en":"If a large number of signals are involved, the process is complex.","zh":"如果大量訊號牽涉其中，該過程就很複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises quantity.","zh":"這個片語強調數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be involved","meaning":"牽涉其中","examples":[{"en":"Many different signals are probably involved in regulating fatigue.","zh":"許多不同訊號可能牽涉於調節疲勞之中。"},{"en":"To be involved means to take part in a process or be connected with it.","zh":"To be involved 指參與某過程或與它有關。"},{"en":"Parents may be involved in planning a school picnic by helping with food and transport.","zh":"家長可能參與策劃學校野餐，協助食物和交通安排。"},{"en":"If many factors are involved, one simple answer may not be enough.","zh":"如果許多因素牽涉其中，一個簡單答案可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes participation or connection.","zh":"這個片語描述參與或關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unlike the limitations theory","meaning":"與極限理論不同","examples":[{"en":"Unlike the limitations theory, the new theory gives the brain a controlling role.","zh":"與極限理論不同，新理論賦予大腦控制角色。"},{"en":"Unlike the limitations theory means different from that traditional explanation.","zh":"Unlike the limitations theory 指不同於那個傳統解釋。"},{"en":"Unlike a strict timetable, a flexible plan allows students to rest when needed.","zh":"與嚴格時間表不同，彈性計劃讓學生在需要時休息。"},{"en":"If a new theory differs from the old one, it may focus on a different cause.","zh":"如果新理論與舊理論不同，它可能集中於不同原因。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces contrast with the older theory.","zh":"這個片語引出與舊理論的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"physiological factors","meaning":"生理因素","examples":[{"en":"Physiological factors still influence the level of fatigue.","zh":"生理因素仍會影響疲勞程度。"},{"en":"Physiological factors are physical body conditions that affect how someone feels or performs.","zh":"Physiological factors 是影響人感受或表現的身體條件。"},{"en":"Sleep, hydration, oxygen levels, and muscle condition are physiological factors in sport.","zh":"睡眠、水分、氧氣水平和肌肉狀況都是運動中的生理因素。"},{"en":"If physiological factors worsen, athletes may feel tired sooner.","zh":"如果生理因素惡化，運動員可能更早感到疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to body-based causes or influences.","zh":"這個片語指以身體為基礎的原因或影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"direct determinants of","meaning":"……的直接決定因素","examples":[{"en":"These factors are not the direct determinants of fatigue.","zh":"這些因素並非疲勞的直接決定因素。"},{"en":"Direct determinants of something are the immediate factors that decide or control it.","zh":"Direct determinants of something 是即時決定或控制某事的因素。"},{"en":"Exam marks are not always direct determinants of future success.","zh":"考試分數不一定是未來成功的直接決定因素。"},{"en":"If muscle chemicals are not direct determinants of fatigue, the brain may decide how fatigue is felt.","zh":"如果肌肉化學物不是疲勞的直接決定因素，大腦可能決定疲勞如何被感受。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what directly sets an outcome.","zh":"這個片語指出直接設定結果的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take something into account","meaning":"把……納入考慮","examples":[{"en":"The brain takes physiological information into account.","zh":"大腦把生理資訊納入考慮。"},{"en":"To take something into account means to consider it when making a decision or judgment.","zh":"To take something into account 指在作決定或判斷時考慮某事。"},{"en":"A teacher should take a student’s illness into account when judging late homework.","zh":"老師評估遲交功課時，應把學生生病納入考慮。"},{"en":"If the brain takes body signals into account, effort can be adjusted according to risk.","zh":"如果大腦把身體訊號納入考慮，努力程度就可按風險調整。"},{"en":"This phrase describes including information in a decision.","zh":"這個片語描述在決定中包括資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"conscious factors","meaning":"意識層面的因素","examples":[{"en":"Conscious factors can also influence athletic fatigue.","zh":"意識層面的因素也可以影響運動疲勞。"},{"en":"Conscious factors are thoughts, expectations, and information that a person is aware of.","zh":"Conscious factors 是人能意識到的想法、預期和資訊。"},{"en":"A runner’s knowledge that only one kilometre remains is a conscious factor.","zh":"跑手知道只剩一公里，是一個意識層面的因素。"},{"en":"If conscious factors change, the same physical effort may feel easier or harder.","zh":"如果意識因素改變，同樣身體努力可能感覺更易或更難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental influences people can notice.","zh":"這個片語描述人能注意到的心理影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"intervene","meaning":"介入；干預","examples":[{"en":"Conscious thoughts can intervene in the regulation of effort.","zh":"意識想法可以介入努力程度的調節。"},{"en":"To intervene means to come into a situation and influence what happens.","zh":"To intervene 指進入某情況並影響其發展。"},{"en":"A teacher may intervene when two students begin arguing loudly.","zh":"當兩名學生開始大聲爭吵時，老師可能介入。"},{"en":"If conscious thoughts intervene, they can change how the brain controls effort.","zh":"如果意識想法介入，它們可以改變大腦如何控制努力。"},{"en":"This word describes active involvement that alters a process.","zh":"這個詞描述會改變過程的主動參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the central regulator","meaning":"中央調節系統","examples":[{"en":"The central regulator evaluates the athlete’s planned workout.","zh":"中央調節系統評估運動員預定的運動量。"},{"en":"The central regulator is the brain system that controls effort and fatigue according to this theory.","zh":"Central regulator 是根據這個理論控制努力程度和疲勞的大腦系統。"},{"en":"A thermostat is a simple regulator because it adjusts temperature when a room gets too hot or cold.","zh":"恆溫器是一種簡單調節器，因為房間太熱或太冷時它會調整溫度。"},{"en":"If the central regulator predicts danger, it may reduce muscle effort early.","zh":"如果中央調節系統預測有危險，它可能很早降低肌肉努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the brain’s controlling role.","zh":"這個片語描述大腦的控制角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"evaluate the planned workout","meaning":"評估預定的運動量","examples":[{"en":"The brain evaluates the planned workout before setting the pace.","zh":"大腦在設定速度前評估預定的運動量。"},{"en":"To evaluate the planned workout means to judge how long, hard, or risky the exercise will be.","zh":"To evaluate the planned workout 指判斷運動會有多長、多辛苦或多大風險。"},{"en":"A runner may evaluate a planned workout by checking distance, weather, and tiredness.","zh":"跑手可能透過檢查距離、天氣和疲倦程度來評估預定運動量。"},{"en":"If the workout seems long, the brain may encourage a slower starting pace.","zh":"如果運動看似很長，大腦可能鼓勵較慢起步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes assessing exercise before or during performance.","zh":"這個片語描述在表現前或期間評估運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a pacing strategy","meaning":"配速策略","examples":[{"en":"The central regulator sets a pacing strategy.","zh":"中央調節系統設定配速策略。"},{"en":"A pacing strategy is a plan for controlling speed and effort over a whole activity.","zh":"Pacing strategy 是在整個活動中控制速度和努力程度的計劃。"},{"en":"A student needs a pacing strategy in an exam so they do not spend too long on one question.","zh":"學生在考試中需要配速策略，才不會在一題上花太多時間。"},{"en":"If a pacing strategy is poor, the athlete may start too fast and tire early.","zh":"如果配速策略差，運動員可能起步太快並很早疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planning how to distribute effort.","zh":"這個片語描述規劃如何分配努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"accordingly","meaning":"相應地","examples":[{"en":"The brain adjusts fatigue symptoms accordingly.","zh":"大腦相應地調整疲勞症狀。"},{"en":"Accordingly means in a way that matches the situation or information just mentioned.","zh":"Accordingly 指以符合剛才提到的情況或資訊的方式。"},{"en":"If a lesson is too difficult, a teacher may slow down and adjust accordingly.","zh":"如果課堂太難，老師可能慢下來並相應調整。"},{"en":"If the brain expects a longer run, fatigue sensations may be adjusted accordingly.","zh":"如果大腦預期跑程較長，疲勞感可能相應地被調整。"},{"en":"This word links a response to the situation that caused it.","zh":"這個詞把反應與造成它的情況連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"experienced runners","meaning":"經驗豐富的跑手","examples":[{"en":"Experienced runners notice differences in effort between runs of different lengths.","zh":"經驗豐富的跑手會注意到不同長度跑程之間的努力差異。"},{"en":"Experienced runners are people who have trained and run often enough to understand pacing and fatigue.","zh":"Experienced runners 是訓練和跑步經驗足夠、理解配速和疲勞的人。"},{"en":"Experienced runners may start slowly because they know a long race becomes harder later.","zh":"經驗豐富的跑手可能慢慢起步，因為他們知道長跑後段會更困難。"},{"en":"If runners are experienced, they can judge effort more accurately.","zh":"如果跑手經驗豐富，他們可以更準確判斷努力程度。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to runners with practical training knowledge.","zh":"這個片語指有實際訓練知識的跑手。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"set out on","meaning":"開始進行","examples":[{"en":"A runner may set out on a five-kilometre or ten-kilometre run.","zh":"跑手可能開始進行五公里或十公里跑。"},{"en":"To set out on something means to begin a journey, task, or planned activity.","zh":"To set out on something 指開始一段旅程、任務或計劃活動。"},{"en":"A family may set out on a long drive early in the morning.","zh":"家庭可能清晨開始一段長途車程。"},{"en":"If a runner sets out on a long route, they may choose a slower pace.","zh":"如果跑手開始一條長路線，他可能選擇較慢配速。"},{"en":"This phrase describes starting something that will take time.","zh":"這個片語描述開始一件需要時間的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"feel easier than","meaning":"感覺比……容易","examples":[{"en":"The first kilometre of a long run may feel easier than that of a shorter run.","zh":"長跑的第一公里可能感覺比短跑的第一公里容易。"},{"en":"To feel easier than something means to seem less difficult or less tiring in comparison.","zh":"To feel easier than something 指相比之下似乎較不困難或較不疲倦。"},{"en":"A grammar exercise may feel easier than an essay because the task is more limited.","zh":"文法練習可能比作文感覺容易，因為任務較有限。"},{"en":"If the brain expects a long effort, the same first kilometre may feel easier because pace is reduced.","zh":"如果大腦預期長時間努力，同樣的第一公里可能因配速降低而感覺較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase compares subjective difficulty.","zh":"這個片語比較主觀難度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"farther to go","meaning":"還有更遠路程要完成","examples":[{"en":"The brain knows that the athlete has farther to go in a longer run.","zh":"大腦知道運動員在較長跑程中還有更遠路程要完成。"},{"en":"Farther to go means more distance, work, or time remains before the task is finished.","zh":"Farther to go 指任務完成前仍有更多距離、工作或時間。"},{"en":"A student with three essay paragraphs left has farther to go than one checking the conclusion.","zh":"還有三段作文要寫的學生，比正在檢查結論的學生有更遠路程要完成。"},{"en":"If there is farther to go, people may naturally save energy.","zh":"如果還有更遠路程，人們自然可能保存能量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes remaining distance or effort.","zh":"這個片語描述剩餘距離或努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"programme itself to","meaning":"自行設定去……","examples":[{"en":"The central governor programmes itself to control fatigue symptoms.","zh":"中央調控系統自行設定去控制疲勞症狀。"},{"en":"To programme itself to do something means to set itself to operate in a particular way.","zh":"To programme itself to do something 指自行設定以某種方式運作。"},{"en":"A phone can programme itself to save battery when power is low.","zh":"手機在電量低時，可以自行設定去節省電量。"},{"en":"If the brain programmes itself for a long run, it may release fatigue signals more gradually.","zh":"如果大腦為長跑自行設定，它可能更逐步釋放疲勞訊號。"},{"en":"This phrase describes automatic self-setting.","zh":"這個片語描述自動自我設定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"dole out","meaning":"逐步分配","examples":[{"en":"The brain may dole out sensations of fatigue gradually.","zh":"大腦可能逐步分配疲勞感。"},{"en":"To dole out something means to give or distribute it slowly, in small amounts.","zh":"To dole out something 指慢慢地、小量地給予或分發某物。"},{"en":"A parent may dole out pocket money weekly so a child learns to budget.","zh":"家長可能每週逐步分配零用錢，讓孩子學習預算。"},{"en":"If fatigue is doled out gradually, the athlete may not feel all the tiredness at once.","zh":"如果疲勞感被逐步分配，運動員可能不會一次過感到所有疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled distribution.","zh":"這個片語描述受控分發。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"fatigue symptoms","meaning":"疲勞症狀","examples":[{"en":"The brain may regulate when fatigue symptoms appear.","zh":"大腦可能調節疲勞症狀何時出現。"},{"en":"Fatigue symptoms are signs of tiredness, such as heaviness, pain, weakness, or loss of focus.","zh":"Fatigue symptoms 是疲倦的跡象，例如沉重、疼痛、無力或失去專注。"},{"en":"A student’s fatigue symptoms may include yawning, slow reading, and careless mistakes.","zh":"學生的疲勞症狀可能包括打呵欠、閱讀變慢和粗心錯誤。"},{"en":"If fatigue symptoms appear early, a person may reduce effort even before total exhaustion.","zh":"如果疲勞症狀很早出現，人可能在完全耗竭前已降低努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes signs that tiredness is being felt.","zh":"這個片語描述疲倦被感受到的跡象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"keep something back","meaning":"保留一些力量","examples":[{"en":"The body is designed to keep something back for emergencies.","zh":"身體被設計成為緊急情況保留一些力量。"},{"en":"To keep something back means to save or reserve it instead of using it all.","zh":"To keep something back 指保存或保留某物，而不是全部用掉。"},{"en":"A family may keep some money back for medical bills or sudden repairs.","zh":"家庭可能保留一些金錢，用於醫療費或突發維修。"},{"en":"If the body keeps energy back, it can respond to danger later.","zh":"如果身體保留能量，它之後就能回應危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes saving a reserve.","zh":"這個片語描述保存儲備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"something left in the tank","meaning":"仍留有一些體力","examples":[{"en":"The body ensures that there is always something left in the tank.","zh":"身體確保總是仍留有一些體力。"},{"en":"Something left in the tank means some energy, strength, or ability remains unused.","zh":"Something left in the tank 指仍有一些能量、力量或能力未被使用。"},{"en":"A student may still have something left in the tank after a short break and a snack.","zh":"學生短休和吃小食後，可能仍留有一些精力。"},{"en":"If athletes have something left in the tank, they may still sprint at the end.","zh":"如果運動員仍留有一些體力，他們可能在尾段仍能衝刺。"},{"en":"This phrase comes from the idea of fuel remaining in a vehicle.","zh":"這個片語來自車輛油箱仍有燃料的概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"in ancient times","meaning":"在古代","examples":[{"en":"In ancient times, keeping energy in reserve could be essential for survival.","zh":"在古代，保留能量可能對生存至關重要。"},{"en":"In ancient times means in the very distant past, before modern society.","zh":"In ancient times 指在非常久遠的過去，即現代社會以前。"},{"en":"In ancient times, people had to walk long distances to find food and shelter.","zh":"在古代，人們必須走很遠去尋找食物和庇護所。"},{"en":"If danger appeared suddenly, ancient humans needed spare energy to escape.","zh":"如果危險突然出現，古代人類需要額外能量逃走。"},{"en":"This phrase places an idea in a very old historical context.","zh":"這個片語把想法放在非常古老的歷史背景中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be designed to","meaning":"被設計成去……","examples":[{"en":"Our bodies may be designed to preserve emergency reserves.","zh":"我們的身體可能被設計成保存緊急儲備。"},{"en":"To be designed to do something means to be made or arranged for that purpose.","zh":"To be designed to do something 指被製造或安排來達成該目的。"},{"en":"A school timetable is designed to give students breaks between difficult lessons.","zh":"學校時間表被設計成讓學生在困難課堂之間有休息時間。"},{"en":"If the body is designed to save reserves, fatigue may appear before total depletion.","zh":"如果身體被設計成保存儲備，疲勞可能在完全耗盡前出現。"},{"en":"This phrase explains purpose or function.","zh":"這個片語解釋目的或功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be faced with","meaning":"面對","examples":[{"en":"A person may need to move quickly when faced with danger.","zh":"一個人在面對危險時可能需要快速移動。"},{"en":"To be faced with something means to have to deal with a situation or problem.","zh":"To be faced with something 指必須處理某情況或問題。"},{"en":"A student faced with a difficult question should first identify the key words.","zh":"學生面對困難題目時，應先找出關鍵詞。"},{"en":"If someone is faced with danger, quick action may be necessary.","zh":"如果某人面對危險，迅速行動可能是必要的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes encountering a challenge directly.","zh":"這個片語描述直接遇到挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"an unexpected need","meaning":"突如其來的需要","examples":[{"en":"The body keeps energy available for an unexpected need.","zh":"身體保留可用能量，以應付突如其來的需要。"},{"en":"An unexpected need is a demand or problem that appears suddenly without warning.","zh":"Unexpected need 是突然出現、沒有預警的需求或問題。"},{"en":"A family may keep emergency money for an unexpected need, such as a broken washing machine.","zh":"家庭可能保留應急金錢，以應付洗衣機壞掉等突如其來的需要。"},{"en":"If an unexpected need appears, reserves can prevent a small problem from becoming serious.","zh":"如果突如其來的需要出現，儲備可以防止小問題變嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sudden requirement.","zh":"這個片語描述突然出現的需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct heading for each paragraph.","zh":"學生為每一段選出正確標題。"},{"en":"To choose the correct heading means to select the title that best summarises a paragraph.","zh":"To choose the correct heading 指選擇最能概括段落的小標題。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should read the whole paragraph before choosing the heading.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先讀完整段，再選標題。"},{"en":"If a heading is too specific or too broad, it may not match the paragraph well.","zh":"如果標題太具體或太籠統，它可能不太符合段落。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in IELTS reading tasks.","zh":"這個片語是 IELTS 閱讀題常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"from the list of headings","meaning":"從標題列表中","examples":[{"en":"Each heading must be selected from the list of headings provided.","zh":"每個標題必須從所提供的標題列表中選出。"},{"en":"From the list of headings means using only the heading options given in the question.","zh":"From the list of headings 指只使用題目給出的標題選項。"},{"en":"Students should not invent their own title if the answer must come from the list of headings.","zh":"如果答案必須來自標題列表，學生不應自創標題。"},{"en":"If several headings look similar, checking the paragraph’s main idea helps narrow the choice.","zh":"如果幾個標題看起來相似，檢查段落主旨有助收窄選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase tells students where answer options come from.","zh":"這個片語告訴學生答案選項來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"avoiding tiredness in athletes","meaning":"避免運動員疲勞","examples":[{"en":"One heading concerns avoiding tiredness in athletes.","zh":"其中一個標題涉及避免運動員疲勞。"},{"en":"Avoiding tiredness in athletes means preventing or reducing fatigue during sport.","zh":"Avoiding tiredness in athletes 指在運動中預防或減少疲勞。"},{"en":"Coaches may focus on avoiding tiredness in athletes by planning rest, food, and pacing.","zh":"教練可能透過安排休息、飲食和配速來避免運動員疲勞。"},{"en":"If tiredness is avoided too aggressively, training may become too easy to improve performance.","zh":"如果過度避免疲勞，訓練可能變得太容易而無法改善表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes managing fatigue in sportspeople.","zh":"這個片語描述管理運動員疲勞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"puzzling evidence","meaning":"令人困惑的證據","examples":[{"en":"The lactic acid paradox provides puzzling evidence against the old theory.","zh":"乳酸悖論提供了反對舊理論的令人困惑的證據。"},{"en":"Puzzling evidence is information that is difficult to explain or does not fit expectations.","zh":"Puzzling evidence 是難以解釋或不符合預期的資訊。"},{"en":"A teacher may find puzzling evidence if a student understands classwork but fails every test.","zh":"如果學生理解課堂內容但每次測驗都不合格，老師可能發現令人困惑的證據。"},{"en":"If evidence is puzzling, it may lead researchers to question their assumptions.","zh":"如果證據令人困惑，它可能令研究人員質疑自己的假設。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence that creates a problem for existing ideas.","zh":"這個片語描述對既有想法造成問題的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"raise a question","meaning":"引起疑問","examples":[{"en":"The unexpected results raise a question about the cause of fatigue.","zh":"意外結果引起關於疲勞成因的疑問。"},{"en":"To raise a question means to create doubt or make people ask about something.","zh":"To raise a question 指造成疑慮或令人詢問某事。"},{"en":"A sudden drop in homework marks may raise a question about whether students understand the topic.","zh":"功課分數突然下降，可能引起學生是否理解題目的疑問。"},{"en":"If evidence contradicts a theory, it raises questions that need further research.","zh":"如果證據與理論矛盾，它會引起需要進一步研究的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating a new issue for discussion.","zh":"這個片語描述製造新的討論議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"traditional explanations","meaning":"傳統解釋","examples":[{"en":"The opening paragraph presents traditional explanations of fatigue.","zh":"開首段落提出疲勞的傳統解釋。"},{"en":"Traditional explanations are older accepted ways of explaining something.","zh":"Traditional explanations 是較舊且被接受的解釋方式。"},{"en":"Traditional explanations of poor grades often focus only on laziness, but the real causes may be deeper.","zh":"成績差的傳統解釋常只集中於懶惰，但真正原因可能更深。"},{"en":"If traditional explanations fail, new theories may appear.","zh":"如果傳統解釋失效，新理論可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-standing interpretations.","zh":"這個片語描述長期存在的解讀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"interpret the findings","meaning":"解讀研究結果","examples":[{"en":"The researchers interpret the findings as evidence of brain regulation.","zh":"研究人員把研究結果解讀為大腦調節的證據。"},{"en":"To interpret the findings means to explain what research results mean.","zh":"To interpret the findings 指解釋研究結果的意思。"},{"en":"A teacher may interpret test results as evidence that students need more reading practice.","zh":"老師可能把測驗結果解讀為學生需要更多閱讀練習的證據。"},{"en":"If findings are interpreted carefully, researchers avoid jumping to unsupported conclusions.","zh":"如果研究結果被謹慎解讀，研究人員就能避免跳到缺乏支持的結論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making sense of results.","zh":"這個片語描述理解結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"develop muscle fibres","meaning":"發展肌肉纖維","examples":[{"en":"One heading refers to the development of muscle fibres.","zh":"其中一個標題提到肌肉纖維的發展。"},{"en":"To develop muscle fibres means to make muscle fibres stronger, larger, or better trained.","zh":"To develop muscle fibres 指令肌肉纖維變得更強、更大或訓練得更好。"},{"en":"Regular strength training can help athletes develop muscle fibres over time.","zh":"定期力量訓練可以隨時間幫助運動員發展肌肉纖維。"},{"en":"If muscle fibres develop, the body may produce more force during demanding activities.","zh":"如果肌肉纖維發展，身體在高要求活動中可能產生更大力量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical improvement in muscle tissue.","zh":"這個片語描述肌肉組織的身體改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a new hypothesis","meaning":"新假說","examples":[{"en":"The central governor theory is a new hypothesis about fatigue.","zh":"中央調控理論是一個關於疲勞的新假說。"},{"en":"A new hypothesis is a fresh proposed explanation that can be tested.","zh":"New hypothesis 是一個可被測試的新提出解釋。"},{"en":"A science class may form a new hypothesis about why plants grow faster near a window.","zh":"科學課可能形成一個新假說，解釋植物為何在窗邊長得更快。"},{"en":"If a hypothesis makes clear predictions, researchers can design experiments to test it.","zh":"如果假說作出清晰預測，研究人員可以設計實驗測試它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible explanation, not a proven fact.","zh":"這個片語描述可能解釋，而不是已證實事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"description of a new test","meaning":"對新測試的描述","examples":[{"en":"One paragraph provides a description of a new cycling test.","zh":"其中一段提供對一項新單車測試的描述。"},{"en":"A description of a new test explains what the test involves and how it is carried out.","zh":"Description of a new test 解釋測試涉及甚麼以及如何進行。"},{"en":"A teacher may give a description of a new speaking test before students practise it.","zh":"老師可能在學生練習前，先給出對新口語測試的描述。"},{"en":"If the test is described clearly, readers can understand what was measured.","zh":"如果測試被清楚描述，讀者就能理解量度了甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an explanation of a testing method.","zh":"這個片語描述對測試方法的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"surprising results","meaning":"令人意外的結果","examples":[{"en":"The endurance test produced surprising results.","zh":"耐力測試產生令人意外的結果。"},{"en":"Surprising results are findings that are unexpected or different from what the theory predicted.","zh":"Surprising results 是出乎意料或不同於理論預測的發現。"},{"en":"A class survey may produce surprising results if students prefer paper books to tablets.","zh":"如果學生較喜歡紙本書而不是平板電腦，班級調查可能產生令人意外的結果。"},{"en":"If results are surprising, they may force people to question old assumptions.","zh":"如果結果令人意外，它們可能迫使人質疑舊假設。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unexpected findings.","zh":"這個片語描述意想不到的發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"an endurance test","meaning":"耐力測試","examples":[{"en":"The cyclists took part in an endurance test.","zh":"單車手參加了一項耐力測試。"},{"en":"An endurance test measures how long someone can sustain effort before becoming too tired.","zh":"Endurance test 量度某人能維持努力多久，才變得太疲倦。"},{"en":"A swimming coach may use an endurance test to see how far students can swim without stopping.","zh":"游泳教練可能使用耐力測試，看看學生不停下來能游多遠。"},{"en":"If an endurance test is long, pacing and mental control become important.","zh":"如果耐力測試很長，配速和心理控制就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a test of sustained effort.","zh":"這個片語描述對持續努力的測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"classify the following ideas","meaning":"把以下觀點分類","examples":[{"en":"Students classify the following ideas according to the relevant theory.","zh":"學生根據相關理論把以下觀點分類。"},{"en":"To classify the following ideas means to sort the listed points into categories.","zh":"To classify the following ideas 指把列出的重點分入類別。"},{"en":"In a reading task, students may classify ideas as supporting Theory A, Theory B, or both.","zh":"在閱讀任務中，學生可能把觀點分類為支持理論A、理論B或兩者。"},{"en":"If ideas are classified correctly, students show they understand the differences between theories.","zh":"如果觀點分類正確，學生就顯示自己理解理論之間的差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in matching and categorisation questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於配對和分類題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"relate to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Each idea relates to one or both theories.","zh":"每個觀點與其中一個或兩個理論有關。"},{"en":"To relate to something means to be connected with it.","zh":"To relate to something 指與某事有連繫。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may relate to sleep, diet, stress, or exercise.","zh":"學生疲倦可能與睡眠、飲食、壓力或運動有關。"},{"en":"If a statement relates to both theories, it should not be assigned to only one too quickly.","zh":"如果陳述與兩個理論都有關，就不應太快只分配給其中一個。"},{"en":"This phrase describes connection or relevance.","zh":"這個片語描述連繫或相關性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"use any letter more than once","meaning":"可多於一次使用任何字母","examples":[{"en":"Students may use any letter more than once.","zh":"學生可以多於一次使用任何字母。"},{"en":"To use any letter more than once means the same answer option can be repeated.","zh":"To use any letter more than once 指同一答案選項可以重複使用。"},{"en":"In a matching question, one paragraph may answer two items, so the same letter can appear twice.","zh":"在配對題中，同一段可能回答兩個項目，所以同一字母可以出現兩次。"},{"en":"If students assume each letter can be used only once, they may choose wrong answers.","zh":"如果學生假設每個字母只能用一次，他們可能選錯答案。"},{"en":"This phrase tells learners that repeated answers are allowed.","zh":"這個片語告訴學習者可以重複答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be produced in the muscles","meaning":"在肌肉中產生","examples":[{"en":"Lactic acid is produced in the muscles during exercise.","zh":"乳酸在運動期間於肌肉中產生。"},{"en":"To be produced in the muscles means to be created inside muscle tissue.","zh":"To be produced in the muscles 指在肌肉組織內被製造出來。"},{"en":"Heat is produced in the muscles when people exercise hard.","zh":"人們劇烈運動時，熱量會在肌肉中產生。"},{"en":"If a substance is produced in the muscles, it may affect how the body feels during movement.","zh":"如果某物質在肌肉中產生，它可能影響身體在活動時的感覺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where a body substance is made.","zh":"這個片語描述身體物質在哪裡製造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"use up all available resources","meaning":"耗盡所有可用資源","examples":[{"en":"The limitations theory suggests that athletes can use up all available resources.","zh":"極限理論認為運動員可以耗盡所有可用資源。"},{"en":"To use up all available resources means to consume everything that could be used.","zh":"To use up all available resources 指消耗所有可使用的東西。"},{"en":"A student may use up all available time if they spend too long on the first essay question.","zh":"如果學生在第一條作文題花太久，他可能耗盡所有可用時間。"},{"en":"If all resources are used up, continuing becomes very difficult or impossible.","zh":"如果所有資源被耗盡，繼續下去會變得非常困難或不可能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete consumption of what is available.","zh":"這個片語描述完全消耗可用之物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"mental processes","meaning":"心理過程","examples":[{"en":"The central governor theory gives mental processes a role in fatigue.","zh":"中央調控理論賦予心理過程在疲勞中的角色。"},{"en":"Mental processes are activities of the mind, such as thinking, judging, expecting, and deciding.","zh":"Mental processes 是心智活動，例如思考、判斷、預期和決定。"},{"en":"Planning an essay involves mental processes like organising ideas and choosing examples.","zh":"規劃作文涉及組織想法和選擇例子等心理過程。"},{"en":"If mental processes affect fatigue, thoughts and expectations may change performance.","zh":"如果心理過程影響疲勞，想法和預期可能改變表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what the mind does.","zh":"這個片語描述心智所做的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"control the symptoms of tiredness","meaning":"控制疲勞症狀","examples":[{"en":"Mental processes may control the symptoms of tiredness.","zh":"心理過程可能控制疲勞症狀。"},{"en":"To control the symptoms of tiredness means to regulate when and how strongly fatigue signs appear.","zh":"To control the symptoms of tiredness 指調節疲勞跡象何時及以多強程度出現。"},{"en":"Deep breathing may help a nervous student control symptoms of tiredness during a long exam.","zh":"深呼吸可能幫助緊張學生在長考試中控制疲勞症狀。"},{"en":"If the brain controls tiredness symptoms, the body may slow down before real danger occurs.","zh":"如果大腦控制疲勞症狀，身體可能在真正危險出現前慢下來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes managing signs of fatigue.","zh":"這個片語描述管理疲勞跡象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be linked to fatigue","meaning":"與疲勞有關","examples":[{"en":"Physiological signals from the muscles are linked to fatigue.","zh":"來自肌肉的生理訊號與疲勞有關。"},{"en":"To be linked to fatigue means to have a connection with tiredness or exhaustion.","zh":"To be linked to fatigue 指與疲倦或筋疲力盡有關。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is often linked to fatigue in students and office workers.","zh":"睡眠不足常與學生和辦公室員工的疲勞有關。"},{"en":"If a signal is linked to fatigue, it may help explain why tiredness appears.","zh":"如果某訊號與疲勞有關，它可能幫助解釋疲倦為何出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a relationship with tiredness.","zh":"這個片語描述與疲倦之間的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"plan and regulate","meaning":"計劃並調節","examples":[{"en":"The brain may plan and regulate muscle performance before a run.","zh":"大腦可能在跑步前計劃並調節肌肉表現。"},{"en":"To plan and regulate something means to prepare it and control how it happens.","zh":"To plan and regulate something 指準備某事並控制它如何發生。"},{"en":"A teacher may plan and regulate a debate so each student has time to speak.","zh":"老師可能計劃並調節辯論，讓每位學生都有時間發言。"},{"en":"If the brain plans and regulates effort, performance is managed before exhaustion appears.","zh":"如果大腦計劃並調節努力程度，表現就在耗竭出現前被管理。"},{"en":"This phrase combines preparation with control.","zh":"這個片語結合準備和控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in advance of","meaning":"在……之前","examples":[{"en":"The brain sets a pacing strategy in advance of a run.","zh":"大腦在跑步之前設定配速策略。"},{"en":"In advance of something means before it happens.","zh":"In advance of something 指在某事發生之前。"},{"en":"Students should read the question carefully in advance of writing an essay.","zh":"學生在寫作文之前應仔細閱讀題目。"},{"en":"If planning happens in advance of a task, mistakes and panic may be reduced.","zh":"如果規劃在任務之前完成，錯誤和慌亂可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparation before an event.","zh":"這個片語描述事件前的準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"muscle performance","meaning":"肌肉表現","examples":[{"en":"The central governor regulates muscle performance.","zh":"中央調控系統調節肌肉表現。"},{"en":"Muscle performance is how well muscles produce force, speed, endurance, or movement.","zh":"Muscle performance 是肌肉產生力量、速度、耐力或動作的表現。"},{"en":"Good sleep and training can improve muscle performance in athletes.","zh":"良好睡眠和訓練可以改善運動員的肌肉表現。"},{"en":"If muscle performance drops, the person may move more slowly or weakly.","zh":"如果肌肉表現下降，人可能移動得更慢或更無力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how effectively muscles work.","zh":"這個片語描述肌肉運作得有多有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"during a race","meaning":"在比賽期間","examples":[{"en":"Lactic acid levels may affect an athlete during a race.","zh":"乳酸水平可能在比賽期間影響運動員。"},{"en":"During a race means while the competition is happening.","zh":"During a race 指比賽正在進行時。"},{"en":"A runner may change pace during a race if the weather becomes too hot.","zh":"如果天氣變得太熱，跑手可能在比賽期間改變配速。"},{"en":"If a problem appears during a race, the athlete must respond immediately.","zh":"如果問題在比賽期間出現，運動員必須立即回應。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event inside the competition period.","zh":"這個片語把事件放在比賽進行期間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"lactic acid build-up","meaning":"乳酸積聚","examples":[{"en":"The limitations theory links fatigue to lactic acid build-up.","zh":"極限理論把疲勞與乳酸積聚聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Lactic acid build-up is the accumulation of lactic acid in muscles during intense exercise.","zh":"Lactic acid build-up 是高強度運動期間乳酸在肌肉中的累積。"},{"en":"A sprinter may feel burning in the legs and blame lactic acid build-up.","zh":"短跑手可能感到腿部灼熱，並把它歸咎於乳酸積聚。"},{"en":"If fatigue occurs without much build-up, the theory needs another explanation.","zh":"如果疲勞在乳酸積聚不多時仍發生，該理論就需要另一解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a chemical accumulation often connected with exercise fatigue.","zh":"這個片語描述常與運動疲勞連接的化學積累。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"genetically programmed","meaning":"由基因預設","examples":[{"en":"Humans may be genetically programmed to preserve energy.","zh":"人類可能由基因預設去保存能量。"},{"en":"Genetically programmed means shaped by inherited biological instructions.","zh":"Genetically programmed 指由遺傳生物指令塑造。"},{"en":"Some animals are genetically programmed to migrate when seasons change.","zh":"有些動物由基因預設在季節改變時遷徙。"},{"en":"If humans are programmed to save energy, fatigue may protect survival rather than simply signal failure.","zh":"如果人類被預設去保存能量，疲勞可能是在保護生存，而不只是表示失效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes behaviour influenced by genes.","zh":"這個片語描述受基因影響的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"energy reserves","meaning":"能量儲備","examples":[{"en":"The body keeps energy reserves available for emergencies.","zh":"身體保留可用能量儲備，以應付緊急情況。"},{"en":"Energy reserves are stored supplies of energy that can be used later.","zh":"Energy reserves 是儲存起來、可日後使用的能量供應。"},{"en":"A hiker carries snacks as energy reserves for a long walk.","zh":"行山者帶備小食作為長途步行的能量儲備。"},{"en":"If energy reserves are protected, the body can respond to sudden danger.","zh":"如果能量儲備受到保護，身體就能回應突如其來的危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes backup energy kept for future need.","zh":"這個片語描述為未來需要而保留的後備能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 114 - Running on empty.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 115":[{"front":"the creation of lasting memories","meaning":"長久記憶的形成","examples":[{"en":"Memory consolidation is the process involved in the creation of lasting memories.","zh":"記憶鞏固是參與長久記憶形成的過程。"},{"en":"The creation of lasting memories means the formation of memories that remain for a long time.","zh":"the creation of lasting memories 指能長時間保留下來的記憶的形成。"},{"en":"A student may experience the creation of lasting memories when she repeatedly practises a speech before a competition.","zh":"學生在比賽前反覆練習演講時，可能經歷長久記憶的形成。"},{"en":"Sleep, review and emotional importance can help new information become a lasting memory.","zh":"睡眠、複習和情感重要性可以幫助新資訊變成長久記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how temporary experience becomes something the brain can keep.","zh":"這個短語描述短暫經驗如何變成大腦可以保存的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"brain processes underlying","meaning":"……背後的大腦過程","examples":[{"en":"Researchers study the brain processes underlying memory consolidation.","zh":"研究人員研究記憶鞏固背後的大腦過程。"},{"en":"Brain processes underlying something are the hidden brain activities that make it possible.","zh":"brain processes underlying 某事，是使它成為可能的隱藏大腦活動。"},{"en":"Teachers may be interested in the brain processes underlying attention and learning.","zh":"老師可能會對注意力和學習背後的大腦過程感興趣。"},{"en":"If researchers understand these processes, they can explain why some memories last longer than others.","zh":"如果研究人員理解這些過程，就能解釋為何有些記憶較持久。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the biological mechanisms behind a mental ability.","zh":"這個短語指出心理能力背後的生物機制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"memory consolidation","meaning":"記憶鞏固","examples":[{"en":"Memory consolidation turns newly learned information into lasting memories.","zh":"記憶鞏固把新學會的資訊轉化為長久記憶。"},{"en":"Memory consolidation is the process by which the brain stabilises new memories after learning.","zh":"memory consolidation 是大腦在學習後穩定新記憶的過程。"},{"en":"A student’s memory consolidation may improve when she sleeps well after studying vocabulary.","zh":"學生學完詞彙後睡得好，記憶鞏固可能會改善。"},{"en":"If consolidation is disrupted, a person may remember something briefly but forget it later.","zh":"如果鞏固過程受干擾，一個人可能短暫記得某事，但之後忘記。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the strengthening of memory over time.","zh":"這個短語描述記憶隨時間變得更牢固。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"involve giving subjects treatment","meaning":"涉及向實驗對象施予處理","examples":[{"en":"Many experiments involve giving subjects treatment while they learn a task.","zh":"許多實驗涉及實驗對象學習任務時向他們施予處理。"},{"en":"To involve giving subjects treatment means the study includes applying a drug, method or condition to participants.","zh":"involve giving subjects treatment 指研究包括向參與者施加藥物、方法或條件。"},{"en":"A sleep study may involve giving subjects treatment such as light exposure before bedtime.","zh":"睡眠研究可能涉及向實驗對象施予睡前光線照射等處理。"},{"en":"Researchers use treatments to test whether they change learning, memory or behaviour.","zh":"研究人員使用處理方法來測試它們是否改變學習、記憶或行為。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an experimental design where subjects receive an intervention.","zh":"這個短語描述實驗對象接受干預的實驗設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"human and animal subjects","meaning":"人類和動物實驗對象","examples":[{"en":"The studies involved both human and animal subjects.","zh":"這些研究涉及人類和動物實驗對象。"},{"en":"Human and animal subjects are people and animals that take part in experiments or studies.","zh":"human and animal subjects 是參與實驗或研究的人和動物。"},{"en":"A medical study may begin with animal subjects before testing a treatment with human subjects.","zh":"醫學研究可能先使用動物實驗對象，再在人類實驗對象身上測試治療。"},{"en":"Researchers use different subjects to see whether a finding applies across species.","zh":"研究人員使用不同實驗對象，以了解發現是否適用於不同物種。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the living participants being studied.","zh":"這個短語指被研究的活體參與者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"perform a task","meaning":"執行一項任務","examples":[{"en":"The subjects were trained to perform a task.","zh":"實驗對象接受訓練去執行一項任務。"},{"en":"To perform a task means to carry out a specific action or activity.","zh":"perform a task 指進行一項特定行動或活動。"},{"en":"A student may perform a task such as solving ten grammar questions in five minutes.","zh":"學生可能執行一項任務，例如在五分鐘內完成十條文法題。"},{"en":"If someone performs a task repeatedly, the action may become faster and more accurate.","zh":"如果某人反覆執行一項任務，動作可能變得更快和更準確。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on doing something required or assigned.","zh":"這個短語重點在完成被要求或分配的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"contribute greatly to","meaning":"對……有重大貢獻","examples":[{"en":"These experiments have contributed greatly to our understanding of memory.","zh":"這些實驗對我們理解記憶有重大貢獻。"},{"en":"To contribute greatly to something means to help it develop or improve in an important way.","zh":"contribute greatly to 某事，指以重要方式幫助它發展或改善。"},{"en":"Clear feedback can contribute greatly to a student’s writing progress.","zh":"清楚回饋可以對學生寫作進步有重大貢獻。"},{"en":"Research contributes greatly when it answers questions that people could not explain before.","zh":"當研究回答了人們以前無法解釋的問題，它就有重大貢獻。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a strong and valuable contribution.","zh":"這個短語強調強大而有價值的貢獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pioneering studies","meaning":"開創性研究","examples":[{"en":"Bernard Agranoff conducted pioneering studies using goldfish.","zh":"Bernard Agranoff 使用金魚進行開創性研究。"},{"en":"Pioneering studies are early, original studies that open up a new area of research.","zh":"pioneering studies 是早期而原創、開拓新研究領域的研究。"},{"en":"A teacher may conduct a pioneering study on how students learn English through voice messages.","zh":"老師可能進行開創性研究，探討學生如何透過語音訊息學英文。"},{"en":"Such studies matter because later researchers can build on their methods and findings.","zh":"這類研究重要，因為後來研究人員可以建基於其方法和發現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research that is new, important and path-breaking.","zh":"這個短語描述新穎、重要並具開拓性的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"protein synthesis inhibitors","meaning":"蛋白質合成抑制劑","examples":[{"en":"Protein synthesis inhibitors prevented the formation of lasting memories.","zh":"蛋白質合成抑制劑阻止長久記憶的形成。"},{"en":"Protein synthesis inhibitors are substances that stop cells from making new proteins.","zh":"protein synthesis inhibitors 是阻止細胞製造新蛋白質的物質。"},{"en":"In a memory experiment, such inhibitors can show whether new protein production is needed after learning.","zh":"在記憶實驗中，這類抑制劑可以顯示學習後是否需要新蛋白質生成。"},{"en":"If blocking protein synthesis prevents long-term memory, researchers can infer that proteins are important for consolidation.","zh":"如果阻礙蛋白質合成會阻止長期記憶，研究人員可推斷蛋白質對鞏固很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to drugs or chemicals that interfere with protein production.","zh":"這個短語指干擾蛋白質製造的藥物或化學物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be injected after training","meaning":"在訓練後被注射","examples":[{"en":"The inhibitors were injected after the fish had completed their training.","zh":"抑制劑在魚完成訓練後被注射。"},{"en":"To be injected after training means to be put into the body by injection once learning practice is finished.","zh":"be injected after training 指在學習練習完成後，透過注射被送入體內。"},{"en":"In a medical study, a drug may be injected after exercise to test recovery effects.","zh":"在醫學研究中，藥物可能在運動後被注射，以測試恢復效果。"},{"en":"Changing the timing of injection helps researchers see which stage of learning is affected.","zh":"改變注射時間幫助研究人員了解學習哪一階段受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes treatment given after the training phase.","zh":"這個短語描述在訓練階段之後給予的處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cause someone to forget","meaning":"令某人忘記","examples":[{"en":"The treatment caused the goldfish to forget what they had learned.","zh":"這種處理令金魚忘記牠們所學的東西。"},{"en":"To cause someone to forget means to make a person or animal lose a memory.","zh":"cause someone to forget 指令一個人或動物失去記憶。"},{"en":"Stress before an exam may cause a student to forget facts she studied the night before.","zh":"考試前壓力可能令學生忘記前一晚溫習過的事實。"},{"en":"If a treatment disrupts memory formation, learned information may disappear quickly.","zh":"如果處理干擾記憶形成，已學資訊可能很快消失。"},{"en":"The phrase links a cause with memory loss.","zh":"這個短語把原因與記憶喪失連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"administer treatment","meaning":"施予治療；施用藥物","examples":[{"en":"Agranoff administered the treatment before training in later experiments.","zh":"Agranoff 在後來的實驗中於訓練前施予處理。"},{"en":"To administer treatment means to give a medicine, procedure or intervention to someone.","zh":"administer treatment 指向某人給予藥物、程序或干預。"},{"en":"A nurse may administer treatment to a patient before recording the patient’s response.","zh":"護士可能先向病人施予治療，再記錄病人反應。"},{"en":"The way treatment is administered can affect whether it works and what it changes.","zh":"治療施予方式可以影響它是否有效以及改變甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and often used in medical or experimental contexts.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於醫學或實驗語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"immediately before","meaning":"緊接在……之前","examples":[{"en":"The inhibitors were administered immediately before the fish were trained.","zh":"抑制劑緊接在魚接受訓練之前被施予。"},{"en":"Immediately before means just before something happens, with almost no delay.","zh":"immediately before 指就在某事發生之前，幾乎沒有時間間隔。"},{"en":"A student may check her notes immediately before entering the exam room.","zh":"學生可能在進入試場之前緊接着查看筆記。"},{"en":"Timing matters because an action taken immediately before a task may affect performance.","zh":"時間很重要，因為緊接任務前採取的行動可能影響表現。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a very close time relationship.","zh":"這個短語給出非常接近的時間關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"remarkable finding","meaning":"令人驚訝的發現","examples":[{"en":"The remarkable finding was that the fish initially learned normally.","zh":"令人驚訝的發現是魚最初正常學習。"},{"en":"A remarkable finding is a surprising or important result from research.","zh":"remarkable finding 是研究中令人驚訝或重要的結果。"},{"en":"A school survey may produce a remarkable finding that students learn better after short breaks.","zh":"學校調查可能得出令人驚訝的發現：學生在短休息後學得更好。"},{"en":"Remarkable findings often make researchers question old assumptions.","zh":"令人驚訝的發現常令研究人員質疑舊有假設。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a result worth special attention.","zh":"這個短語描述值得特別注意的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"learn the task normally","meaning":"正常學會任務","examples":[{"en":"The fish learned the task completely normally despite the treatment.","zh":"儘管接受了處理，魚仍完全正常地學會任務。"},{"en":"To learn the task normally means to acquire the required skill in the usual successful way.","zh":"learn the task normally 指以通常成功的方式掌握所需技能。"},{"en":"A student can learn a new grammar task normally even if she feels nervous at first.","zh":"即使學生起初緊張，她仍可以正常學會新的文法任務。"},{"en":"If subjects learn normally but later forget, the problem may be memory storage rather than initial learning.","zh":"如果實驗對象正常學會但之後忘記，問題可能在記憶儲存，而不是最初學習。"},{"en":"The phrase separates successful learning from later remembering.","zh":"這個短語把成功學習與之後記住分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"within a few hours","meaning":"在數小時內","examples":[{"en":"The fish forgot the task within a few hours.","zh":"魚在數小時內忘記了任務。"},{"en":"Within a few hours means before several hours have passed.","zh":"within a few hours 指在幾個小時過去之前。"},{"en":"A student may forget a new phone number within a few hours if she never uses it again.","zh":"如果學生之後從不使用新的電話號碼，可能在數小時內忘記。"},{"en":"Rapid forgetting suggests that the memory has not become stable.","zh":"快速遺忘顯示記憶尚未變得穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a short time frame for a change or result.","zh":"這個短語給出變化或結果發生的短時間範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"block memory consolidation","meaning":"阻礙記憶鞏固","examples":[{"en":"The inhibitors blocked memory consolidation.","zh":"抑制劑阻礙了記憶鞏固。"},{"en":"To block memory consolidation means to stop new memories from becoming stable and long-lasting.","zh":"block memory consolidation 指阻止新記憶變得穩定和持久。"},{"en":"Severe interruption after studying may block memory consolidation if the brain cannot process the material properly.","zh":"溫習後受到嚴重干擾，若大腦不能適當處理材料，可能阻礙記憶鞏固。"},{"en":"When consolidation is blocked, a person may learn something briefly but fail to retain it.","zh":"當鞏固受阻，一個人可能短暫學會某事，但未能保留。"},{"en":"The phrase describes interference with the strengthening stage of memory.","zh":"這個短語描述對記憶強化階段的干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"influence short-term memory","meaning":"影響短期記憶","examples":[{"en":"The treatment did not influence short-term memory.","zh":"這種處理沒有影響短期記憶。"},{"en":"To influence short-term memory means to affect the ability to hold information briefly.","zh":"influence short-term memory 指影響短暫保存資訊的能力。"},{"en":"A loud noise may influence short-term memory while a student is trying to remember a code.","zh":"學生嘗試記住密碼時，巨響可能影響短期記憶。"},{"en":"If short-term memory is not influenced, the person can still remember something for a short period.","zh":"如果短期記憶不受影響，該人仍能短時間記住某事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an effect on temporary memory.","zh":"這個短語描述對暫時記憶的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"extensive evidence","meaning":"大量證據","examples":[{"en":"There is now extensive evidence about the separation of memory processes.","zh":"現在有大量證據關於記憶過程的分離。"},{"en":"Extensive evidence means a large amount of proof or research support.","zh":"extensive evidence 指大量證明或研究支持。"},{"en":"There is extensive evidence that regular practice helps students improve pronunciation.","zh":"有大量證據顯示定期練習幫助學生改善發音。"},{"en":"When evidence is extensive, a claim becomes harder to dismiss.","zh":"當證據大量存在，一項主張就更難被否定。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that support comes from many observations or studies.","zh":"這個短語強調支持來自許多觀察或研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"short-term memory is spared","meaning":"短期記憶不受影響","examples":[{"en":"Short-term memory is spared by many treatments that disrupt consolidation.","zh":"許多破壞鞏固過程的處理不會影響短期記憶。"},{"en":"If short-term memory is spared, it remains unaffected while another process is damaged.","zh":"如果 short-term memory is spared，意思是另一過程受損時，短期記憶仍不受影響。"},{"en":"A patient may remember a nurse’s instruction for a few minutes even if long-term storage is weak.","zh":"即使長期儲存較弱，病人仍可能記住護士指示幾分鐘。"},{"en":"This separation helps researchers show that short-term and long-term memory are not identical.","zh":"這種分離幫助研究人員顯示短期和長期記憶並非相同。"},{"en":"The phrase means short-term memory is protected or left intact.","zh":"這個短語意思是短期記憶受到保護或保持完整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"many kinds of treatments","meaning":"多種治療方法","examples":[{"en":"Many kinds of treatments can interfere with memory formation.","zh":"多種處理方法可以干擾記憶形成。"},{"en":"Many kinds of treatments means several different medical, chemical or experimental interventions.","zh":"many kinds of treatments 指幾種不同醫學、化學或實驗干預。"},{"en":"In a sleep study, many kinds of treatments may include light, medicine or sound conditions.","zh":"在睡眠研究中，多種處理方法可能包括光線、藥物或聲音條件。"},{"en":"Comparing different treatments helps researchers find which memory process each one affects.","zh":"比較不同處理方法幫助研究人員找出每種方法影響哪個記憶過程。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses variety in the methods used.","zh":"這個短語強調所用方法的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"electro-convulsive therapy","meaning":"電痙攣治療","examples":[{"en":"Electro-convulsive therapy can block memory consolidation.","zh":"電痙攣治療可以阻礙記憶鞏固。"},{"en":"Electro-convulsive therapy is a medical treatment that uses controlled electric current to affect brain activity.","zh":"electro-convulsive therapy 是使用受控制電流影響大腦活動的醫學治療。"},{"en":"Doctors use electro-convulsive therapy only under medical supervision, not casually.","zh":"醫生只會在醫療監督下使用電痙攣治療，而不是隨便使用。"},{"en":"Because it affects the brain, it may also affect how some memories are formed or retained.","zh":"因為它影響大腦，也可能影響某些記憶如何形成或保留。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific medical treatment involving electrical stimulation.","zh":"這個短語指出一種涉及電刺激的特定醫學治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"On the other hand, some drugs affect short-term memory only.","zh":"另一方面，有些藥物只影響短期記憶。"},{"en":"On the other hand introduces a contrasting point or another side of the argument.","zh":"on the other hand 引出對比點或論點的另一面。"},{"en":"The library is quiet; on the other hand, it closes earlier than the study room.","zh":"圖書館很安靜；另一方面，它比自修室更早關門。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers compare two different facts fairly.","zh":"這個短語幫助寫作者公平比較兩個不同事實。"},{"en":"It signals that the next idea is different from the previous one.","zh":"它標誌下一個想法與前一個不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"equally importantly","meaning":"同樣重要的是","examples":[{"en":"Equally importantly, some treatments block short-term memory without affecting consolidation.","zh":"同樣重要的是，有些處理會阻礙短期記憶而不影響鞏固。"},{"en":"Equally importantly means the next point is just as important as the previous one.","zh":"equally importantly 指下一點與前一點同樣重要。"},{"en":"Students need grammar practice; equally importantly, they need chances to use English naturally.","zh":"學生需要文法練習；同樣重要的是，他們需要自然使用英語的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase prevents readers from treating the second idea as less important.","zh":"這個短語防止讀者把第二個想法看得較不重要。"},{"en":"It is useful when adding another major point.","zh":"它適合用於加入另一個主要重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"drug treatments","meaning":"藥物治療","examples":[{"en":"Some drug treatments can selectively affect short-term memory.","zh":"有些藥物治療可以選擇性地影響短期記憶。"},{"en":"Drug treatments are medical or experimental treatments that use drugs.","zh":"drug treatments 是使用藥物的醫學或實驗處理方法。"},{"en":"A doctor may prescribe drug treatments to control pain, infection or blood pressure.","zh":"醫生可能處方藥物治療，以控制痛楚、感染或血壓。"},{"en":"In research, drug treatments can help scientists test which brain functions are affected.","zh":"在研究中，藥物治療可以幫助科學家測試哪些大腦功能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to treatments based on medicine rather than surgery or training alone.","zh":"這個短語指以藥物為基礎的治療，而不只是手術或訓練。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"without blocking","meaning":"在不阻礙……的情況下","examples":[{"en":"Some treatments block short-term memory without blocking memory consolidation.","zh":"有些處理會阻礙短期記憶，但不阻礙記憶鞏固。"},{"en":"Without blocking means not stopping or preventing something.","zh":"without blocking 指沒有停止或防止某事。"},{"en":"A school can improve security without blocking students’ access to the library.","zh":"學校可以改善保安，而不阻礙學生使用圖書館。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one effect can happen while another process continues normally.","zh":"這個短語顯示一種效果可以發生，而另一過程仍正常繼續。"},{"en":"It is useful when separating two possible results.","zh":"它適合用於分開兩種可能結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"contrary to the hypothesis","meaning":"與該假說相反","examples":[{"en":"The findings were contrary to the hypothesis proposed by Donald Hebb.","zh":"這些發現與 Donald Hebb 提出的假說相反。"},{"en":"Contrary to the hypothesis means opposite to what the theory predicted.","zh":"contrary to the hypothesis 指與該理論所預測的相反。"},{"en":"Contrary to the teacher’s hypothesis, students performed better after shorter lessons.","zh":"與老師的假說相反，學生在較短課堂後表現更好。"},{"en":"When results are contrary to a hypothesis, researchers may need to revise the theory.","zh":"當結果與假說相反，研究人員可能需要修正理論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence that challenges an expected explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述挑戰預期解釋的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"put forward by","meaning":"由……提出","examples":[{"en":"The hypothesis was put forward by Donald Hebb in 1949.","zh":"該假說由 Donald Hebb 於1949年提出。"},{"en":"Put forward by someone means proposed or suggested by that person.","zh":"put forward by 某人，指由該人提出或建議。"},{"en":"A new school rule may be put forward by the student council.","zh":"新校規可能由學生會提出。"},{"en":"Ideas put forward by respected researchers can shape later debate.","zh":"由受尊敬研究人員提出的想法可以塑造後來討論。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the person who first proposed an idea.","zh":"這個短語指出最初提出想法的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"long-term memory","meaning":"長期記憶","examples":[{"en":"Long-term memory does not necessarily depend on short-term memory.","zh":"長期記憶不一定依賴短期記憶。"},{"en":"Long-term memory is memory that can last for hours, days, years or even a lifetime.","zh":"long-term memory 是可以持續數小時、數日、數年甚至一生的記憶。"},{"en":"A student’s memory of her first school day may remain in long-term memory for many years.","zh":"學生對第一天上學的記憶可能在長期記憶中保留多年。"},{"en":"Long-term memory allows people to use past learning in future situations.","zh":"長期記憶讓人們在未來情況中使用過去學到的東西。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts lasting memory with brief temporary memory.","zh":"這個短語把持久記憶與短暫暫時記憶作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"require short-term memory","meaning":"需要短期記憶","examples":[{"en":"Long-term memory does not require short-term memory.","zh":"長期記憶不需要短期記憶。"},{"en":"To require short-term memory means to need brief temporary memory in order to work.","zh":"require short-term memory 指需要短暫暫時記憶才能運作。"},{"en":"Remembering a phone code for ten seconds requires short-term memory.","zh":"記住電話驗證碼十秒需要短期記憶。"},{"en":"If long-term memory does not require short-term memory, the two systems may operate separately.","zh":"如果長期記憶不需要短期記憶，兩個系統可能分開運作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dependence on temporary memory.","zh":"這個短語描述對暫時記憶的依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"and vice versa","meaning":"反之亦然","examples":[{"en":"Long-term memory does not require short-term memory, and vice versa.","zh":"長期記憶不需要短期記憶，反之亦然。"},{"en":"And vice versa means the reverse is also true.","zh":"and vice versa 指反過來也成立。"},{"en":"Good teachers can learn from students, and vice versa.","zh":"好老師可以向學生學習，反之亦然。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when two things affect each other or when the opposite statement also applies.","zh":"當兩件事互相影響，或相反陳述也適用時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It avoids repeating the same idea in reverse.","zh":"它避免把同一想法反向重複一次。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"such findings suggest that","meaning":"這些發現顯示","examples":[{"en":"Such findings suggest that different forms of memory develop separately.","zh":"這些發現顯示不同形式的記憶分開發展。"},{"en":"Such findings suggest that means these results point to a likely conclusion.","zh":"such findings suggest that 指這些結果指向一個可能結論。"},{"en":"If students improve after more sleep, such findings suggest that rest supports learning.","zh":"如果學生睡多了後有進步，這些發現顯示休息支持學習。"},{"en":"Findings can suggest an explanation even before every detail is fully proven.","zh":"即使細節尚未完全證明，發現也可以暗示某解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase links evidence to an interpretation.","zh":"這個短語把證據與詮釋連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"create parallel stages","meaning":"形成平行的階段","examples":[{"en":"Our experiences may create parallel stages of memory.","zh":"我們的經歷可能形成平行的記憶階段。"},{"en":"To create parallel stages means to produce separate processes that develop at the same time.","zh":"create parallel stages 指產生同時發展的分開過程。"},{"en":"A school project may create parallel stages of planning, research and design that happen together.","zh":"學校項目可能形成規劃、研究和設計等同時進行的平行階段。"},{"en":"Parallel stages allow different parts of a process to progress independently.","zh":"平行階段讓過程的不同部分可以獨立推進。"},{"en":"The phrase describes processes running side by side rather than one after another.","zh":"這個短語描述並行過程，而不是一個接一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"possibly independent","meaning":"可能互相獨立","examples":[{"en":"The stages of memory may be parallel and possibly independent.","zh":"記憶階段可能是平行且可能互相獨立的。"},{"en":"Possibly independent means perhaps able to operate separately from one another.","zh":"possibly independent 指也許能夠彼此分開運作。"},{"en":"Two school clubs may be possibly independent if they share a room but make separate decisions.","zh":"如果兩個學會共用房間但分開決策，它們可能互相獨立。"},{"en":"If two processes are independent, damaging one may not damage the other.","zh":"如果兩個過程獨立，損害其中一個未必損害另一個。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses cautious uncertainty about separation.","zh":"這個短語謹慎表達對分離性的可能判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"stages of memory","meaning":"記憶階段","examples":[{"en":"Different stages of memory may have separate biological processes.","zh":"不同記憶階段可能有分開的生物過程。"},{"en":"Stages of memory are different phases through which information passes as it is learned, held and stored.","zh":"stages of memory 是資訊被學習、暫存和儲存時經過的不同階段。"},{"en":"A student may first hear a word, remember it briefly, and later store it through review.","zh":"學生可能先聽到一個字，短暫記住，然後透過複習把它儲存。"},{"en":"Understanding stages helps explain why learning something once may not be enough.","zh":"理解階段有助解釋為何只學一次可能不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes memory as a process with several phases.","zh":"這個短語把記憶描述為有幾個階段的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a different life span","meaning":"不同的持續時間","examples":[{"en":"Each form of memory has a different life span.","zh":"每種記憶形式都有不同的持續時間。"},{"en":"A different life span means a different length of time for which something lasts.","zh":"different life span 指某物能持續的時間長度不同。"},{"en":"A bus ticket may have a short life span, while a passport lasts for years.","zh":"巴士票的有效期可能很短，而護照可持續多年。"},{"en":"In memory, some information disappears quickly, while other memories remain for decades.","zh":"在記憶中，有些資訊很快消失，而其他記憶可保留數十年。"},{"en":"The phrase compares duration.","zh":"這個短語比較持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"clinical and experimental studies","meaning":"臨床及實驗研究","examples":[{"en":"Clinical and experimental studies provide evidence about memory formation.","zh":"臨床及實驗研究提供關於記憶形成的證據。"},{"en":"Clinical and experimental studies are studies based on medical cases and controlled experiments.","zh":"clinical and experimental studies 是基於醫療個案和受控實驗的研究。"},{"en":"A hospital may provide clinical data, while a laboratory provides experimental data.","zh":"醫院可能提供臨床數據，而實驗室提供實驗數據。"},{"en":"Using both types of study can make scientific conclusions stronger.","zh":"使用兩類研究可以令科學結論更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase combines evidence from real patients and planned experiments.","zh":"這個短語結合來自真實病人和計劃實驗的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"strongly indicate that","meaning":"強烈顯示","examples":[{"en":"The findings strongly indicate that the brain treats memories differently.","zh":"這些發現強烈顯示大腦以不同方式處理記憶。"},{"en":"Strongly indicate that means provide clear evidence suggesting something is true.","zh":"strongly indicate that 指提供清楚證據顯示某事可能是真的。"},{"en":"Repeated absences may strongly indicate that a student is facing a serious problem.","zh":"反覆缺席可能強烈顯示學生正面對嚴重問題。"},{"en":"Strong evidence does not always prove everything, but it points clearly in one direction.","zh":"有力證據未必證明一切，但它清楚指向一個方向。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses a firm evidence-based conclusion.","zh":"這個短語表達基於證據的堅定結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"handle recent and remote memory","meaning":"以不同方式處理近期及久遠記憶","examples":[{"en":"The brain handles recent and remote memory in different ways.","zh":"大腦以不同方式處理近期及久遠記憶。"},{"en":"To handle recent and remote memory means to process new memories and old memories.","zh":"handle recent and remote memory 指處理新近記憶和久遠記憶。"},{"en":"A person may remember yesterday’s lesson differently from a childhood holiday.","zh":"一個人記住昨天課堂的方式，可能不同於記住童年假期。"},{"en":"If the brain treats these memories differently, damage may affect one type more than another.","zh":"如果大腦不同地處理這些記憶，損傷可能對某一類影響較大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how the brain manages memories from different times.","zh":"這個短語描述大腦如何管理不同時間的記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"recent memory","meaning":"近期記憶","examples":[{"en":"Recent memory may depend on different brain processes.","zh":"近期記憶可能依賴不同的大腦過程。"},{"en":"Recent memory is memory of things that happened not long ago.","zh":"recent memory 是對不久前發生事情的記憶。"},{"en":"Remembering where you put your keys this morning uses recent memory.","zh":"記得今早把鎖匙放在哪裏，就是使用近期記憶。"},{"en":"Recent memory can be fragile because it has not always become fully stable.","zh":"近期記憶可能脆弱，因為它不一定已完全穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts new memories with memories from the distant past.","zh":"這個短語把新記憶與久遠記憶作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"remote memory","meaning":"久遠記憶","examples":[{"en":"Remote memory refers to memories formed much earlier.","zh":"久遠記憶指很早以前形成的記憶。"},{"en":"Remote memory is memory of events or information from the distant past.","zh":"remote memory 是對遙遠過去事件或資訊的記憶。"},{"en":"An adult’s memory of a primary school teacher may be a remote memory.","zh":"成年人對小學老師的記憶可能是久遠記憶。"},{"en":"Remote memories may survive even when recent memories are damaged.","zh":"即使近期記憶受損，久遠記憶可能仍保留下來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes older memories stored over a long period.","zh":"這個短語描述長時間儲存的較舊記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"react to","meaning":"對……作出反應","examples":[{"en":"Humans must react to a rapidly changing environment.","zh":"人類必須對迅速變化的環境作出反應。"},{"en":"To react to something means to respond to it with action, thought or feeling.","zh":"react to 某事，指用行動、想法或感受回應它。"},{"en":"A driver must react to a child running across the road.","zh":"司機必須對孩子跑過馬路作出反應。"},{"en":"Fast reaction can prevent accidents and help people adapt to new conditions.","zh":"快速反應可以防止意外並幫助人適應新情況。"},{"en":"The phrase describes responding to a change or event.","zh":"這個短語描述對變化或事件作出回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"rapidly changing environment","meaning":"迅速變化的環境","examples":[{"en":"Rapid memory formation helps us adapt to a rapidly changing environment.","zh":"迅速形成記憶幫助我們適應迅速變化的環境。"},{"en":"A rapidly changing environment is a situation or place where conditions change quickly.","zh":"rapidly changing environment 是條件快速改變的情況或地方。"},{"en":"A busy road is a rapidly changing environment because cars, lights and pedestrians keep moving.","zh":"繁忙道路是迅速變化的環境，因為汽車、交通燈和行人不斷移動。"},{"en":"People need quick memory and attention to stay safe when surroundings change fast.","zh":"當周圍環境快速改變，人們需要快速記憶和注意力來保持安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an environment that demands quick adjustment.","zh":"這個短語描述要求快速調整的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"current building codes","meaning":"現行建築規例","examples":[{"en":"Current building codes require steps to be equal in height.","zh":"現行建築規例要求梯級高度相等。"},{"en":"Current building codes are the rules now used to control how buildings should be designed and built.","zh":"current building codes 是現時用來規管建築物如何設計和建造的規則。"},{"en":"A school staircase must follow current building codes so students can use it safely.","zh":"學校樓梯必須符合現行建築規例，讓學生安全使用。"},{"en":"Building codes reduce accidents by setting standards for height, strength and access.","zh":"建築規例透過設定高度、強度和通道標準來減少意外。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to present official construction rules.","zh":"這個短語指現行官方建築規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the heights of all steps","meaning":"所有梯級的高度","examples":[{"en":"Building codes regulate the heights of all steps in a staircase.","zh":"建築規例規管樓梯中所有梯級的高度。"},{"en":"The heights of all steps means how tall each stair is from one level to the next.","zh":"heights of all steps 指每級樓梯由一層到下一層的高度。"},{"en":"A builder must check the heights of all steps before opening a staircase to the public.","zh":"建築工人在向公眾開放樓梯前，必須檢查所有梯級的高度。"},{"en":"Unequal step heights can surprise walkers and cause falls.","zh":"梯級高度不一會令行人意外失足並跌倒。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on a safety detail in stair design.","zh":"這個短語重點在樓梯設計中的安全細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a staircase","meaning":"樓梯","examples":[{"en":"Uneven steps in a staircase can cause accidents.","zh":"樓梯中不平的梯級可以造成意外。"},{"en":"A staircase is a set of steps that allows people to move between different levels of a building.","zh":"staircase 是讓人們在建築物不同樓層之間移動的一組梯級。"},{"en":"Students use a staircase every day to go from one floor to another.","zh":"學生每天使用樓梯由一層到另一層。"},{"en":"If a staircase is poorly designed, people may trip, fall or avoid using it.","zh":"如果樓梯設計差劣，人們可能絆倒、跌倒或避免使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the whole structure made of steps.","zh":"這個短語指由梯級組成的整個結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take a couple of steps","meaning":"走幾級樓梯","examples":[{"en":"After we take a couple of steps, we remember their height.","zh":"我們走幾級樓梯後，便記住它們的高度。"},{"en":"To take a couple of steps means to walk two or a few steps forward or upward.","zh":"take a couple of steps 指向前或向上走兩三步。"},{"en":"A child may take a couple of steps onto a stage before realising it is higher than expected.","zh":"孩子可能走上舞台幾步後，才意識到它比預期高。"},{"en":"Just a few steps can give the body information about height, rhythm and balance.","zh":"只是幾步已可給身體關於高度、節奏和平衡的資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small amount of walking movement.","zh":"這個短語描述少量步行動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"implicitly remember","meaning":"不自覺地記住","examples":[{"en":"We implicitly remember the height of the first few steps.","zh":"我們不自覺地記住最初幾級樓梯的高度。"},{"en":"To implicitly remember something means to remember it without consciously thinking about it.","zh":"implicitly remember 某事，指不用有意識思考也記住它。"},{"en":"A student may implicitly remember the route to class without naming every corridor.","zh":"學生可能不自覺地記住去課室的路，而不用說出每條走廊名稱。"},{"en":"Implicit memory helps people act smoothly without stopping to calculate each movement.","zh":"內隱記憶幫助人順暢行動，不必停下來計算每個動作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes hidden, automatic remembering.","zh":"這個短語描述隱藏而自動的記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"implicit memory","meaning":"內隱記憶","examples":[{"en":"Implicit memory helps us move safely through familiar environments.","zh":"內隱記憶幫助我們在熟悉環境中安全移動。"},{"en":"Implicit memory is memory that affects behaviour without conscious awareness.","zh":"implicit memory 是在沒有有意識察覺下影響行為的記憶。"},{"en":"A cyclist uses implicit memory when balancing without thinking about every movement.","zh":"單車手不用思考每個動作也能平衡時，就是使用內隱記憶。"},{"en":"Because implicit memory works automatically, it supports everyday habits and routines.","zh":"因為內隱記憶自動運作，它支援日常習慣和例行動作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to memory shown through action rather than deliberate recall.","zh":"這個短語指透過行動而非刻意回想顯示出的記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"assume that","meaning":"假設","examples":[{"en":"We assume that the remaining steps will have the same height.","zh":"我們假設剩餘梯級有相同高度。"},{"en":"To assume that something is true means to believe it without checking fully.","zh":"assume that 某事為真，指在未完全查核下相信它。"},{"en":"A student may assume that tomorrow’s lesson is in the same classroom as usual.","zh":"學生可能假設明天課堂仍在平常同一間課室。"},{"en":"Assumptions save time, but wrong assumptions can lead to mistakes.","zh":"假設可以節省時間，但錯誤假設會導致錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes taking something as likely or true.","zh":"這個短語描述把某事視為可能或真實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be likely to trip and fall","meaning":"很可能絆倒","examples":[{"en":"People are likely to trip and fall if the steps are uneven.","zh":"如果梯級不平，人們很可能絆倒並跌下。"},{"en":"To be likely to trip and fall means to have a high chance of stumbling and falling down.","zh":"be likely to trip and fall 指很有可能失足並跌倒。"},{"en":"A child is likely to trip and fall if toys are left on the floor.","zh":"如果玩具留在地上，孩子很可能絆倒並跌下。"},{"en":"Uneven surfaces increase accident risk because the body expects a regular pattern.","zh":"不平表面增加意外風險，因為身體預期有規律模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a probable physical accident.","zh":"這個短語描述可能發生的身體意外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lack of","meaning":"缺乏……","examples":[{"en":"A lack of rapidly formed memory would make daily activities dangerous.","zh":"缺乏迅速形成的記憶會令日常活動變得危險。"},{"en":"A lack of something means not having enough of it.","zh":"lack of 某物，指沒有足夠的它。"},{"en":"A lack of sleep can make students tired and careless in class.","zh":"缺乏睡眠可以令學生在課堂上疲倦和粗心。"},{"en":"When an important ability is lacking, ordinary tasks can become difficult or risky.","zh":"當重要能力缺乏，普通任務可以變得困難或有風險。"},{"en":"The phrase points to absence or shortage as the cause of a problem.","zh":"這個短語指出缺失或不足是問題原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rapidly created memory","meaning":"迅速形成的記憶","examples":[{"en":"Rapidly created memory supports ordinary physical actions.","zh":"迅速形成的記憶支援普通身體動作。"},{"en":"Rapidly created memory is memory formed quickly after an experience or action.","zh":"rapidly created memory 是經歷或行動後快速形成的記憶。"},{"en":"After stepping onto a new staircase, rapidly created memory helps a person adjust to the height of each step.","zh":"踏上新樓梯後，迅速形成的記憶幫助人適應每級高度。"},{"en":"Without quick memory formation, people would need to relearn small details constantly.","zh":"沒有快速記憶形成，人們就要不斷重新學習小細節。"},{"en":"The phrase describes memory that appears quickly enough to guide immediate behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述快得足以引導即時行為的記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be of little value to","meaning":"對……沒有甚麼價值","examples":[{"en":"A delayed memory of the steps would be of little value to us.","zh":"延遲後才出現的樓梯記憶對我們沒有甚麼價值。"},{"en":"To be of little value to someone means to be not very useful or helpful to that person.","zh":"be of little value to 某人，指對該人不是很有用或幫助不大。"},{"en":"Exam advice given after the exam is over is of little value to students.","zh":"考試結束後才給出的考試建議，對學生沒有甚麼價值。"},{"en":"Information is useful only if it arrives when people can still act on it.","zh":"資訊只有在人們仍能按它行動時才有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that has limited practical benefit.","zh":"這個短語描述實際好處有限的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"only after a delay","meaning":"只在延遲後","examples":[{"en":"The information would be useless if we remembered it only after a delay.","zh":"如果我們只在延遲後才記得該資訊，它就會沒有用。"},{"en":"Only after a delay means not immediately, but after some time has passed.","zh":"only after a delay 指不是立即，而是在一段時間過去後。"},{"en":"If a fire alarm warning arrives only after a delay, people may already be in danger.","zh":"如果火警警告只在延遲後才到達，人們可能已經身處危險。"},{"en":"Delayed information can be less useful when quick action is needed.","zh":"當需要快速行動，延遲資訊可能較不有用。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that timing is too late for immediate use.","zh":"這個短語強調時間太晚，不能即時使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"become consolidated","meaning":"得到鞏固","examples":[{"en":"The memory becomes consolidated several hours after learning.","zh":"記憶在學習後數小時得到鞏固。"},{"en":"To become consolidated means to become stable, stronger and more permanent.","zh":"become consolidated 指變得穩定、更強和更持久。"},{"en":"A student’s understanding may become consolidated after she explains the topic to a classmate.","zh":"學生向同學解釋題目後，理解可能得到鞏固。"},{"en":"Once a memory is consolidated, it is less easily lost or disrupted.","zh":"一旦記憶得到鞏固，它就較不容易失去或受干擾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the process of becoming firmly stored.","zh":"這個短語描述變得牢固儲存的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"consolidate slowly over time","meaning":"隨時間逐漸鞏固","examples":[{"en":"Lasting memories appear to consolidate slowly over time.","zh":"長久記憶似乎會隨時間逐漸鞏固。"},{"en":"To consolidate slowly over time means to become stable gradually rather than immediately.","zh":"consolidate slowly over time 指逐漸變得穩定，而不是立即完成。"},{"en":"A student’s grammar knowledge may consolidate slowly over time through repeated use.","zh":"學生的文法知識可能透過反覆使用隨時間逐漸鞏固。"},{"en":"Slow consolidation explains why rest and later review can matter after learning.","zh":"緩慢鞏固解釋了為何學習後休息和後續複習可以重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual strengthening across hours, days or longer.","zh":"這個短語描述在數小時、數日或更長時間中逐漸強化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be supported primarily by","meaning":"主要得到……支持","examples":[{"en":"The hypothesis is supported primarily by clinical evidence.","zh":"該假說主要得到臨床證據支持。"},{"en":"To be supported primarily by something means to depend mainly on that type of evidence or support.","zh":"be supported primarily by 某物，指主要依靠該類證據或支持。"},{"en":"A school policy may be supported primarily by attendance records rather than student opinions.","zh":"學校政策可能主要得到出席記錄支持，而不是學生意見。"},{"en":"If a claim is supported mainly by one kind of evidence, researchers may seek other kinds to confirm it.","zh":"如果一項主張主要由一種證據支持，研究人員可能尋找其他種類來確認它。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main source of support.","zh":"這個短語指出主要支持來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"formation of long-term memory","meaning":"長期記憶的形成","examples":[{"en":"Brain disorders can affect the formation of long-term memory.","zh":"腦部疾病可以影響長期記憶的形成。"},{"en":"The formation of long-term memory means the process by which lasting memories are created.","zh":"formation of long-term memory 指長久記憶被建立的過程。"},{"en":"A student’s formation of long-term memory is helped when she reviews vocabulary over several days.","zh":"當學生在數天內複習詞彙，長期記憶的形成會得到幫助。"},{"en":"If this formation is interrupted, information may be learned briefly but not stored well.","zh":"如果這個形成過程被打斷，資訊可能短暫學會但未能妥善儲存。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how durable memory begins.","zh":"這個短語重點在持久記憶如何開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be influenced by","meaning":"受……影響","examples":[{"en":"Long-term memory is influenced by treatments that affect the brain.","zh":"長期記憶受影響大腦的處理方法影響。"},{"en":"To be influenced by something means to be changed or affected by it.","zh":"be influenced by 某事，指被它改變或影響。"},{"en":"A student’s mood may be influenced by sleep, food and pressure at home.","zh":"學生心情可能受睡眠、食物和家庭壓力影響。"},{"en":"When memory is influenced by a treatment, performance may improve or worsen.","zh":"當記憶受某處理影響，表現可能改善或惡化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an effect from one thing on another.","zh":"這個短語描述一件事對另一件事的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"affect brain functioning","meaning":"影響大腦功能","examples":[{"en":"Some treatments and disorders affect brain functioning.","zh":"有些處理和疾病會影響大腦功能。"},{"en":"To affect brain functioning means to change how the brain works.","zh":"affect brain functioning 指改變大腦運作方式。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can affect brain functioning by weakening attention and memory.","zh":"缺乏睡眠可以透過削弱注意力和記憶來影響大腦功能。"},{"en":"When brain functioning changes, behaviour, learning and emotion may also change.","zh":"當大腦功能改變，行為、學習和情緒也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an influence on the brain’s normal operation.","zh":"這個短語描述對大腦正常運作的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"indicate more directly that","meaning":"更直接顯示","examples":[{"en":"Other evidence indicates more directly that consolidation continues after learning.","zh":"其他證據更直接顯示鞏固在學習後繼續進行。"},{"en":"To indicate more directly that something is true means to show it with clearer or less indirect evidence.","zh":"indicate more directly that 某事為真，指以更清楚或較少間接的證據顯示它。"},{"en":"A student’s improved test score indicates more directly that extra practice helped.","zh":"學生成績改善更直接顯示額外練習有幫助。"},{"en":"Direct evidence is useful because it reduces the need for guessing.","zh":"直接證據有用，因為它減少猜測需要。"},{"en":"The phrase compares stronger evidence with less direct support.","zh":"這個短語把較強證據與較間接支持作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"after learning","meaning":"學習之後","examples":[{"en":"Memory-related changes continue for hours after learning.","zh":"與記憶相關的變化在學習之後持續數小時。"},{"en":"After learning means following the period when new information or a new skill has been acquired.","zh":"after learning 指在新資訊或新技能被學會的時段之後。"},{"en":"After learning new vocabulary, students may review examples to strengthen memory.","zh":"學生學習新詞彙之後，可能複習例句來強化記憶。"},{"en":"What happens after learning can affect how much is remembered later.","zh":"學習之後發生的事情可以影響之後記得多少。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the period after the initial learning event.","zh":"這個短語指出初始學習事件後的時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"human subjects trained in","meaning":"接受……訓練的人類實驗對象","examples":[{"en":"Karni and Sagi studied human subjects trained in a visual skill.","zh":"Karni 和 Sagi 研究接受視覺技能訓練的人類實驗對象。"},{"en":"Human subjects trained in something are people who have been taught or practised a particular task for a study.","zh":"human subjects trained in 某事，是為研究而被教導或練習特定任務的人。"},{"en":"Researchers may study human subjects trained in typing to measure learning speed.","zh":"研究人員可能研究接受打字訓練的人類實驗對象，以量度學習速度。"},{"en":"Training subjects in one skill helps researchers observe changes caused by that learning.","zh":"讓實驗對象接受一項技能訓練，有助研究人員觀察由該學習造成的變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes study participants who receive specific training.","zh":"這個短語描述接受特定訓練的研究參與者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"visual skill","meaning":"視覺技能","examples":[{"en":"The subjects were trained to perform a visual skill.","zh":"實驗對象接受訓練以執行一項視覺技能。"},{"en":"A visual skill is an ability that depends mainly on seeing and interpreting visual information.","zh":"visual skill 是主要依靠觀看和解讀視覺資訊的能力。"},{"en":"Reading small letters on an eye chart uses a visual skill.","zh":"閱讀視力表上的小字會使用視覺技能。"},{"en":"Visual skills can improve with practice because the brain learns what to notice.","zh":"視覺技能可以透過練習改善，因為大腦學會注意甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a skill based on sight.","zh":"這個短語指基於視覺的技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"performance did not improve until","meaning":"表現直至……才有改善","examples":[{"en":"The subjects’ performance did not improve until eight hours after training.","zh":"實驗對象的表現直至訓練後八小時才有改善。"},{"en":"Performance did not improve until a time means ability stayed the same before that point and improved only later.","zh":"performance did not improve until 某時間，指能力在該時間前保持不變，只在之後才改善。"},{"en":"A student’s pronunciation may not improve until she has practised the same sounds for several days.","zh":"學生的發音可能直至她練習同一批音幾天後才有改善。"},{"en":"Delayed improvement suggests that learning can continue after practice ends.","zh":"延遲改善顯示學習可以在練習結束後繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights that progress appeared only after a delay.","zh":"這個短語突出進步只在延遲後出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"after the training was completed","meaning":"訓練完成後","examples":[{"en":"Improvement appeared several hours after the training was completed.","zh":"改善在訓練完成後數小時出現。"},{"en":"After the training was completed means after the practice or learning session had ended.","zh":"after the training was completed 指練習或學習時段結束之後。"},{"en":"A trainee may feel improvement after the training was completed because the brain continues processing the skill.","zh":"受訓者可能在訓練完成後感到進步，因為大腦繼續處理該技能。"},{"en":"Results that appear later show that learning is not limited to the training period itself.","zh":"之後才出現的結果顯示學習不限於訓練時段本身。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the time after formal practice has finished.","zh":"這個短語標記正式練習結束後的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"even greater the following day","meaning":"翌日改善得更明顯","examples":[{"en":"The improvement was even greater the following day.","zh":"翌日改善得更明顯。"},{"en":"Even greater the following day means the improvement became stronger on the next day.","zh":"even greater the following day 指改善在第二天變得更強。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may be even greater the following day after she sleeps on a difficult lesson.","zh":"學生在困難課堂後睡一晚，翌日信心可能更大。"},{"en":"This kind of delayed gain suggests that the brain continues to process learning overnight.","zh":"這種延遲得益顯示大腦在夜間仍繼續處理學習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improvement that increases after time has passed.","zh":"這個短語描述在時間過去後增加的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"retain a skill","meaning":"保持一項技能","examples":[{"en":"The subjects retained the skill for several years.","zh":"實驗對象保持該技能數年。"},{"en":"To retain a skill means to keep the ability to do it after learning it.","zh":"retain a skill 指學會後仍保留做該事的能力。"},{"en":"A person may retain the skill of cycling even after not riding for years.","zh":"一個人即使多年沒有踏單車，仍可能保持踏單車的技能。"},{"en":"Skills are retained better when they are practised, meaningful or deeply learned.","zh":"當技能被練習、有意義或學得深入，就較容易保留。"},{"en":"The phrase describes keeping an ability over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間保留一項能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"for several years","meaning":"持續數年","examples":[{"en":"The visual skill was retained for several years.","zh":"該視覺技能被保留了數年。"},{"en":"For several years means during a period lasting more than two years.","zh":"for several years 指持續超過兩年的一段時間。"},{"en":"A student may remember a favourite teacher’s advice for several years.","zh":"學生可能記住喜愛老師的建議數年。"},{"en":"If a skill lasts for several years, it has entered a durable form of memory.","zh":"如果一項技能持續數年，它已進入持久記憶形式。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a long but not exact period of time.","zh":"這個短語給出長但不精確的時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"human brain imaging","meaning":"人腦成像","examples":[{"en":"Researchers use human brain imaging to study neural changes.","zh":"研究人員使用人腦成像來研究神經變化。"},{"en":"Human brain imaging is the use of technology to view or measure activity in the human brain.","zh":"human brain imaging 是使用科技查看或量度人腦活動。"},{"en":"Doctors may use brain imaging to check which areas are active during a memory task.","zh":"醫生可能使用腦成像檢查人在記憶任務中哪些區域活躍。"},{"en":"Imaging helps researchers see changes that cannot be observed from behaviour alone.","zh":"成像幫助研究人員看見單靠行為無法觀察到的變化。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to scientific methods for studying the living brain.","zh":"這個短語指研究活人大腦的科學方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"neural activity","meaning":"神經活動","examples":[{"en":"Learning produces changes in neural activity.","zh":"學習會產生神經活動的變化。"},{"en":"Neural activity is the electrical and chemical activity of nerve cells in the brain or nervous system.","zh":"neural activity 是大腦或神經系統中神經細胞的電和化學活動。"},{"en":"A brain scan may show neural activity increasing when a student solves a puzzle.","zh":"當學生解難題時，腦掃描可能顯示神經活動增加。"},{"en":"Changes in neural activity can reveal which brain areas are involved in learning.","zh":"神經活動變化可以揭示哪些大腦區域參與學習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the working activity of neurons.","zh":"這個短語描述神經元的運作活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be induced by learning","meaning":"由學習引起","examples":[{"en":"Changes in neural activity can be induced by learning.","zh":"神經活動變化可以由學習引起。"},{"en":"To be induced by learning means to be caused or brought about by the act of learning.","zh":"be induced by learning 指由學習行為造成或引發。"},{"en":"New study habits may be induced by learning that old habits are ineffective.","zh":"當學生知道舊習慣無效，新學習習慣可能由此引起。"},{"en":"If brain changes are induced by learning, practice has physically affected the system.","zh":"如果大腦變化由學習引起，練習就已對系統產生實際影響。"},{"en":"The phrase links learning with a resulting change.","zh":"這個短語把學習與產生的變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"continue to develop","meaning":"繼續發展","examples":[{"en":"The changes continue to develop for hours after training.","zh":"這些變化在訓練後數小時仍繼續發展。"},{"en":"To continue to develop means to keep growing, changing or becoming more complete.","zh":"continue to develop 指持續成長、變化或變得更完整。"},{"en":"A student’s essay plan may continue to develop after she discusses it with classmates.","zh":"學生與同學討論後，文章計劃可能繼續發展。"},{"en":"Development after training suggests the process does not stop when practice ends.","zh":"訓練後仍有發展，顯示過程不會在練習結束時停止。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ongoing change.","zh":"這個短語描述持續變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"innovative study","meaning":"創新研究","examples":[{"en":"Shadmehr and Holcomb conducted an innovative brain-imaging study.","zh":"Shadmehr 和 Holcomb 進行了一項創新人腦成像研究。"},{"en":"An innovative study uses new methods or ideas to investigate a question.","zh":"innovative study 是使用新方法或新想法研究問題的研究。"},{"en":"A teacher may design an innovative study using phone recordings to track speaking progress.","zh":"老師可能設計創新研究，使用手機錄音追蹤口語進步。"},{"en":"Innovative research can reveal patterns older methods could not show.","zh":"創新研究可以揭示舊方法無法顯示的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research that is original and methodologically fresh.","zh":"這個短語描述原創且方法新穎的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"functional imaging","meaning":"功能成像","examples":[{"en":"Functional imaging reveals which brain regions are active.","zh":"功能成像揭示哪些大腦區域處於活躍狀態。"},{"en":"Functional imaging is brain imaging that shows activity or function rather than only structure.","zh":"functional imaging 是顯示活動或功能，而不只是結構的腦成像。"},{"en":"Doctors may use functional imaging to see which brain areas respond during a movement task.","zh":"醫生可能使用功能成像查看人在動作任務中哪些腦區有反應。"},{"en":"This method helps researchers connect mental activity with specific brain regions.","zh":"這種方法幫助研究人員把心理活動與特定腦區連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to imaging that shows what the brain is doing.","zh":"這個短語指顯示大腦正在做甚麼的成像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"examine brain activity","meaning":"檢視大腦活動","examples":[{"en":"The researchers examined brain activity after motor training.","zh":"研究人員在動作訓練後檢視大腦活動。"},{"en":"To examine brain activity means to study how active different parts of the brain are.","zh":"examine brain activity 指研究大腦不同部分有多活躍。"},{"en":"A psychologist may examine brain activity while volunteers read emotional words.","zh":"心理學家可能在志願者閱讀情緒詞語時檢視大腦活動。"},{"en":"Examining activity helps show which systems are involved in a task.","zh":"檢視活動有助顯示哪些系統參與任務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful scientific observation of the working brain.","zh":"這個短語描述對運作中大腦的仔細科學觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"brain regions","meaning":"大腦區域","examples":[{"en":"Different brain regions became active at different times.","zh":"不同大腦區域在不同時間變得活躍。"},{"en":"Brain regions are specific areas of the brain that may have different functions.","zh":"brain regions 是大腦中特定區域，可能有不同功能。"},{"en":"Some brain regions help with movement, while others help with language or emotion.","zh":"有些大腦區域幫助動作，另一些幫助語言或情緒。"},{"en":"If different regions become active, researchers can infer that several systems are involved.","zh":"如果不同區域變得活躍，研究人員可推斷幾個系統都參與其中。"},{"en":"The phrase divides the brain into functional areas.","zh":"這個短語把大腦分成不同功能區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"shortly after","meaning":"在……後不久","examples":[{"en":"Brain activity was measured shortly after the subjects completed training.","zh":"大腦活動在實驗對象完成訓練後不久被量度。"},{"en":"Shortly after means a short time after something happens.","zh":"shortly after 指某事發生後很短時間。"},{"en":"A teacher may give feedback shortly after a presentation so students still remember their performance.","zh":"老師可能在匯報後不久給予回饋，讓學生仍記得自己的表現。"},{"en":"Measuring soon after an event helps capture early effects.","zh":"在事件後不久量度，有助捕捉早期影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes close timing after an action.","zh":"這個短語描述行動後接近的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"motor learning task","meaning":"動作學習任務","examples":[{"en":"The participants were trained in a motor learning task.","zh":"參與者接受一項動作學習任務的訓練。"},{"en":"A motor learning task is an activity that teaches the body to perform a movement more accurately.","zh":"motor learning task 是教身體更準確執行動作的活動。"},{"en":"Practising a new piano finger pattern is a motor learning task.","zh":"練習新的鋼琴指法是一項動作學習任務。"},{"en":"Repetition in such tasks helps the brain control movement more smoothly.","zh":"這類任務中的重複練習幫助大腦更順暢地控制動作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to learning a physical movement skill.","zh":"這個短語指學習身體動作技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"require arm and hand movements","meaning":"需要手臂及手部動作","examples":[{"en":"The task required arm and hand movements.","zh":"該任務需要手臂及手部動作。"},{"en":"To require arm and hand movements means to need actions made by the arms and hands.","zh":"require arm and hand movements 指需要由手臂和手做出的動作。"},{"en":"Typing, drawing and throwing a ball all require arm and hand movements.","zh":"打字、畫畫和投球都需要手臂及手部動作。"},{"en":"Tasks involving these movements can show how the brain learns motor control.","zh":"涉及這些動作的任務可以顯示大腦如何學習動作控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the physical actions needed for a task.","zh":"這個短語描述任務所需的身體動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"remain stable","meaning":"保持穩定","examples":[{"en":"The subjects’ performance remained stable for several hours.","zh":"實驗對象的表現在數小時內保持穩定。"},{"en":"To remain stable means to stay at the same level without major change.","zh":"remain stable 指保持在相同水平，沒有重大變化。"},{"en":"A student’s test scores may remain stable if her study routine does not change.","zh":"如果學生的學習習慣沒有改變，她的測驗成績可能保持穩定。"},{"en":"Stable performance helps researchers separate immediate improvement from later improvement.","zh":"穩定表現幫助研究人員分開即時改善與後來改善。"},{"en":"The phrase describes consistency over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間保持一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"after completion of","meaning":"在……完成後","examples":[{"en":"Brain activity was examined after completion of the training.","zh":"大腦活動在訓練完成後被檢視。"},{"en":"After completion of something means after it has been finished.","zh":"after completion of 某事，指在它完成之後。"},{"en":"After completion of a school project, students may reflect on what they learned.","zh":"在學校項目完成後，學生可能反思自己學到了甚麼。"},{"en":"Studying what happens after completion can reveal delayed effects.","zh":"研究完成後發生的事，可以揭示延遲影響。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the period following the end of an activity.","zh":"這個短語標記活動結束後的時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"predominantly active","meaning":"主要處於活躍狀態","examples":[{"en":"Different regions were predominantly active at different times.","zh":"不同區域在不同時間主要處於活躍狀態。"},{"en":"Predominantly active means mainly or most strongly active.","zh":"predominantly active 指主要或最強烈地活躍。"},{"en":"During reading, language-related brain areas may be predominantly active.","zh":"閱讀時，與語言相關的大腦區域可能主要處於活躍狀態。"},{"en":"If one area is predominantly active, it may be playing a major role at that moment.","zh":"如果某區域主要活躍，它當刻可能正在發揮主要作用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where most activity is concentrated.","zh":"這個短語描述活動主要集中在哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"over a period of several hours","meaning":"在數小時內","examples":[{"en":"The pattern changed over a period of several hours.","zh":"這個模式在數小時內改變。"},{"en":"Over a period of several hours means during a time span lasting a few hours.","zh":"over a period of several hours 指在持續幾小時的一段時間中。"},{"en":"A student’s headache may improve over a period of several hours after rest and water.","zh":"學生休息和喝水後，頭痛可能在數小時內改善。"},{"en":"Slow change over hours suggests a process rather than an instant reaction.","zh":"數小時內的緩慢變化顯示這是一個過程，而不是即時反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual development across a short but meaningful time.","zh":"這個短語描述在短但有意義時間中的逐漸發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"shift from…to…","meaning":"從……轉移至……","examples":[{"en":"Brain activity shifted from the prefrontal cortex to motor regions.","zh":"大腦活動從前額葉皮層轉移至運動區域。"},{"en":"To shift from A to B means to move or change from one place, state or focus to another.","zh":"shift from A to B 指由一個地方、狀態或焦點移到另一個。"},{"en":"A lesson may shift from teacher explanation to student practice.","zh":"一堂課可能從老師解釋轉移至學生練習。"},{"en":"A shift shows that the main role or attention has moved elsewhere.","zh":"轉移顯示主要角色或注意力已移到別處。"},{"en":"The phrase describes change in position, focus or responsibility.","zh":"這個短語描述位置、焦點或責任的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"prefrontal cortex","meaning":"前額葉皮層","examples":[{"en":"The prefrontal cortex was active shortly after training.","zh":"前額葉皮層在訓練後不久處於活躍狀態。"},{"en":"The prefrontal cortex is a front part of the brain involved in planning, decision-making and control.","zh":"prefrontal cortex 是大腦前方一個參與規劃、決策和控制的部分。"},{"en":"Students use functions linked to the prefrontal cortex when they plan an essay before writing.","zh":"學生寫作前規劃文章時，會使用與前額葉皮層相關的功能。"},{"en":"If this area is active early, it may be helping organise a newly learned task.","zh":"如果這個區域早期活躍，它可能正在幫助組織新學會的任務。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific brain region near the front of the head.","zh":"這個短語指出頭部前方附近的特定大腦區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be involved in controlling","meaning":"參與控制……","examples":[{"en":"The motor cortex is involved in controlling movement.","zh":"運動皮層參與控制動作。"},{"en":"To be involved in controlling something means to take part in managing or directing it.","zh":"be involved in controlling 某事，指參與管理或指揮它。"},{"en":"The school office is involved in controlling attendance records.","zh":"校務處參與控制出席紀錄。"},{"en":"If a brain area is involved in controlling movement, damage there may affect physical actions.","zh":"如果某大腦區域參與控制動作，該處受損可能影響身體行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes participation in regulation or management.","zh":"這個短語描述參與調節或管理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"motor cortex","meaning":"運動皮層","examples":[{"en":"Activity later increased in the motor cortex.","zh":"之後運動皮層中的活動增加。"},{"en":"The motor cortex is a brain region important for planning and controlling voluntary movement.","zh":"motor cortex 是對規劃和控制自主動作很重要的大腦區域。"},{"en":"When a student practises handwriting, the motor cortex helps control finger and hand movements.","zh":"當學生練習書寫時，運動皮層幫助控制手指和手部動作。"},{"en":"Increased activity there may show that a movement skill is being strengthened.","zh":"該處活動增加可能顯示動作技能正在被強化。"},{"en":"The phrase names a brain area linked to movement.","zh":"這個短語指出與動作相關的大腦區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cerebellar cortex","meaning":"小腦皮層","examples":[{"en":"The cerebellar cortex also helps control movements.","zh":"小腦皮層也幫助控制動作。"},{"en":"The cerebellar cortex is part of the cerebellum involved in coordinating movement and balance.","zh":"cerebellar cortex 是小腦的一部分，參與協調動作和平衡。"},{"en":"A dancer relies on brain systems including the cerebellar cortex to move smoothly.","zh":"舞者依靠包括小腦皮層在內的大腦系統來順暢移動。"},{"en":"If movement needs fine timing and coordination, this region may become important.","zh":"如果動作需要精細時間掌握和協調，這個區域可能變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase names a brain area linked to skilled physical control.","zh":"這個短語指出與熟練身體控制相關的大腦區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"motor skill","meaning":"動作技能","examples":[{"en":"The experiment examined consolidation of a motor skill.","zh":"該實驗檢視一項動作技能的鞏固。"},{"en":"A motor skill is an ability involving controlled body movement.","zh":"motor skill 是涉及受控制身體動作的能力。"},{"en":"Typing, cycling, drawing and playing piano are motor skills.","zh":"打字、踏單車、畫畫和彈鋼琴都是動作技能。"},{"en":"Motor skills improve when the brain and muscles learn to work together efficiently.","zh":"當大腦和肌肉學會高效配合，動作技能就會改善。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to learned physical ability.","zh":"這個短語指後天學會的身體能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"involve activation of","meaning":"涉及……的啟動","examples":[{"en":"Motor-memory consolidation appeared to involve activation of several systems.","zh":"動作記憶鞏固似乎涉及幾個系統的啟動。"},{"en":"To involve activation of something means to require certain systems or parts to become active.","zh":"involve activation of 某物，指需要某些系統或部分變得活躍。"},{"en":"Solving a maths problem may involve activation of attention, memory and reasoning systems.","zh":"解數學題可能涉及注意力、記憶和推理系統的啟動。"},{"en":"If several systems are activated, the task may depend on more than one brain process.","zh":"如果幾個系統被啟動，任務可能依賴多於一種大腦過程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the turning on or engagement of systems.","zh":"這個短語描述系統被打開或參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"neural systems","meaning":"神經系統","examples":[{"en":"Different neural systems contributed to memory consolidation.","zh":"不同神經系統對記憶鞏固作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Neural systems are networks of nerve cells that work together to perform a function.","zh":"neural systems 是共同工作以執行某功能的神經細胞網絡。"},{"en":"Reading aloud may involve neural systems for vision, speech and hearing.","zh":"朗讀可能涉及視覺、說話和聽覺神經系統。"},{"en":"When several neural systems work together, complex skills become possible.","zh":"當幾個神經系統共同工作，複雜技能就成為可能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised brain networks.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的大腦網絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"increase the stability of","meaning":"提高……的穩定性","examples":[{"en":"These systems increased the stability of the underlying brain processes.","zh":"這些系統提高了背後大腦過程的穩定性。"},{"en":"To increase the stability of something means to make it stronger, less fragile or less likely to change suddenly.","zh":"increase the stability of 某物，指令它更強、較不脆弱或較不容易突然改變。"},{"en":"Regular revision can increase the stability of a student’s vocabulary knowledge.","zh":"定期複習可以提高學生詞彙知識的穩定性。"},{"en":"More stability means a memory or skill is harder to disrupt.","zh":"穩定性越高，記憶或技能就越難被干擾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making something more reliable over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間令某物更可靠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"brain processes underlying the skill","meaning":"技能背後的大腦過程","examples":[{"en":"Consolidation stabilised the brain processes underlying the skill.","zh":"鞏固穩定了該技能背後的大腦過程。"},{"en":"Brain processes underlying the skill are the neural activities that support that ability.","zh":"brain processes underlying the skill 是支援該能力的神經活動。"},{"en":"When a pianist practises, brain processes underlying the skill of finger control become more stable.","zh":"當鋼琴手練習時，手指控制技能背後的大腦過程會變得更穩定。"},{"en":"If these processes strengthen, the skill can be performed more smoothly later.","zh":"如果這些過程強化，之後技能可以更順暢地執行。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the hidden brain work behind a learned ability.","zh":"這個短語指出已學能力背後隱藏的大腦工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"learning-induced changes","meaning":"學習引起的變化","examples":[{"en":"Learning-induced changes can continue for many days.","zh":"學習引起的變化可以持續多天。"},{"en":"Learning-induced changes are changes caused by learning.","zh":"learning-induced changes 是由學習造成的變化。"},{"en":"A student’s faster reading speed may be a learning-induced change after weeks of practice.","zh":"學生閱讀速度變快，可能是數星期練習後學習引起的變化。"},{"en":"Such changes show that learning can affect behaviour and the brain beyond the lesson itself.","zh":"這類變化顯示學習可以在課堂之外影響行為和大腦。"},{"en":"The phrase describes results produced by learning activity.","zh":"這個短語描述由學習活動產生的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"activity of neurons","meaning":"神經元活動","examples":[{"en":"The activity of neurons changed after training.","zh":"訓練後神經元活動發生變化。"},{"en":"The activity of neurons means how nerve cells send signals and respond.","zh":"activity of neurons 指神經細胞如何發送訊號和作出反應。"},{"en":"When a person learns a new sound, the activity of neurons in hearing areas may change.","zh":"當一個人學習新聲音時，聽覺區域的神經元活動可能改變。"},{"en":"Changes in neuron activity can show that the brain has adapted to experience.","zh":"神經元活動變化可以顯示大腦已適應經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the working behaviour of nerve cells.","zh":"這個短語描述神經細胞的運作行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cerebral cortex","meaning":"大腦皮層","examples":[{"en":"The cerebral cortex showed long-lasting changes after learning.","zh":"大腦皮層在學習後顯示出長久變化。"},{"en":"The cerebral cortex is the outer layer of the brain involved in many higher mental functions.","zh":"cerebral cortex 是大腦外層，參與許多高階心理功能。"},{"en":"Reading, planning and movement all involve parts of the cerebral cortex.","zh":"閱讀、規劃和動作都涉及大腦皮層的部分區域。"},{"en":"Changes in this area can reflect learning, memory and skill development.","zh":"這個區域的變化可以反映學習、記憶和技能發展。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major outer part of the brain.","zh":"這個短語指出大腦主要外層部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an extensive series of studies","meaning":"一系列廣泛研究","examples":[{"en":"Weinberger conducted an extensive series of studies using rats.","zh":"Weinberger 使用老鼠進行一系列廣泛研究。"},{"en":"An extensive series of studies is a large set of related research projects.","zh":"extensive series of studies 是一大組相關研究項目。"},{"en":"A university may run an extensive series of studies on how sleep affects exam performance.","zh":"大學可能進行一系列廣泛研究，探討睡眠如何影響考試表現。"},{"en":"Many related studies give stronger evidence than one small experiment alone.","zh":"許多相關研究比單一小實驗提供更強證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated, broad research on a topic.","zh":"這個短語描述對某題目的反覆而廣泛研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"electrodes implanted in","meaning":"電極被植入……","examples":[{"en":"The rats had electrodes implanted in their auditory cortex.","zh":"老鼠的聽覺皮層被植入電極。"},{"en":"Electrodes implanted in a body part are small devices placed inside to record or stimulate electrical activity.","zh":"electrodes implanted in 某身體部位，是放入內部以記錄或刺激電活動的小裝置。"},{"en":"In a medical test, electrodes may be placed on or inside the body to monitor signals.","zh":"在醫學檢查中，電極可能被放在身體表面或內部來監測訊號。"},{"en":"Implanted electrodes let researchers measure activity from a precise location.","zh":"植入電極讓研究人員從精確位置量度活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes devices inserted for scientific or medical measurement.","zh":"這個短語描述為科學或醫學量度而插入的裝置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"auditory cortex","meaning":"聽覺皮層","examples":[{"en":"The auditory cortex processes sounds.","zh":"聽覺皮層處理聲音。"},{"en":"The auditory cortex is the brain area involved in receiving and interpreting sound.","zh":"auditory cortex 是參與接收和解讀聲音的大腦區域。"},{"en":"When a student listens to a teacher’s explanation, the auditory cortex helps process speech sounds.","zh":"當學生聆聽老師解釋時，聽覺皮層幫助處理語音。"},{"en":"If this area changes after training, the brain may be learning to respond differently to sounds.","zh":"如果這個區域在訓練後改變，大腦可能正在學習對聲音作出不同反應。"},{"en":"The phrase names a brain region linked to hearing.","zh":"這個短語指出與聽覺相關的大腦區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a tone of specific frequency","meaning":"特定頻率的聲音","examples":[{"en":"The rats heard a tone of a specific frequency.","zh":"老鼠聽到特定頻率的聲音。"},{"en":"A tone of specific frequency is a sound at a particular pitch.","zh":"tone of specific frequency 是特定音高的聲音。"},{"en":"A hearing test may play a tone of a specific frequency to check what a patient can hear.","zh":"聽力測試可能播放特定頻率的聲音，以檢查病人能聽到甚麼。"},{"en":"Using one exact frequency helps researchers test whether the brain responds selectively.","zh":"使用一個精確頻率幫助研究人員測試大腦是否選擇性反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a controlled sound used in an experiment.","zh":"這個短語描述實驗中使用的受控聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be paired with","meaning":"與……配對","examples":[{"en":"The tone was paired with a mild footshock.","zh":"該聲音與輕微足部電擊配對。"},{"en":"To be paired with something means to be repeatedly presented or connected together with it.","zh":"be paired with 某事，指反覆與它一起呈現或連繫。"},{"en":"A new vocabulary word may be paired with a picture to help students remember it.","zh":"新詞彙可能與圖片配對，以幫助學生記住。"},{"en":"When two things are paired often, the brain may learn to associate them.","zh":"當兩件事經常配對，大腦可能學會把它們聯繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes linking two experiences in learning.","zh":"這個短語描述在學習中連結兩種經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"footshock","meaning":"足部電擊","examples":[{"en":"The rats learned to associate the tone with a footshock.","zh":"老鼠學會把該聲音與足部電擊聯繫起來。"},{"en":"A footshock is a mild electric shock delivered to an animal’s feet in an experiment.","zh":"footshock 是在實驗中施加於動物腳部的輕微電擊。"},{"en":"In animal research, a footshock may be used carefully to study fear learning.","zh":"在動物研究中，足部電擊可能被謹慎用來研究恐懼學習。"},{"en":"The unpleasant shock can make the animal remember the sound connected with it.","zh":"這種不愉快電擊可以令動物記住與它相連的聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific experimental stimulus.","zh":"這個短語指出一種特定實驗刺激。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"respond more to","meaning":"對……反應更強","examples":[{"en":"The neurons responded more to the trained tone.","zh":"神經元對受訓聲音反應更強。"},{"en":"To respond more to something means to react more strongly to it than before or than to other things.","zh":"respond more to 某事，指比以前或比對其他事物反應更強。"},{"en":"A student may respond more to visual examples than to long explanations.","zh":"學生可能對視覺例子比對長篇解釋反應更強。"},{"en":"Stronger response shows that the system has become more sensitive to that stimulus.","zh":"更強反應顯示系統對該刺激變得更敏感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes increased reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述反應增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"tones of other frequencies","meaning":"其他頻率的聲音","examples":[{"en":"The neurons responded less to tones of other frequencies.","zh":"神經元對其他頻率的聲音反應較弱。"},{"en":"Tones of other frequencies are sounds with different pitches from the trained sound.","zh":"tones of other frequencies 是與受訓聲音音高不同的聲音。"},{"en":"In a hearing test, tones of other frequencies help check whether a person hears high and low sounds differently.","zh":"在聽力測試中，其他頻率的聲音幫助檢查人是否以不同方式聽到高低音。"},{"en":"Comparing responses to different tones shows whether learning is specific.","zh":"比較對不同聲音的反應，可以顯示學習是否具體。"},{"en":"The phrase describes alternative sound pitches used for comparison.","zh":"這個短語描述用於比較的其他聲音音高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the selectivity of","meaning":"……的選擇性","examples":[{"en":"The selectivity of the neurons’ response increased after training.","zh":"訓練後，神經元反應的選擇性增加。"},{"en":"The selectivity of a response is how specifically it reacts to one stimulus rather than others.","zh":"selectivity of 反應，指它對一種刺激而非其他刺激作出特定反應的程度。"},{"en":"A student’s ear may develop selectivity when she can hear the difference between similar English sounds.","zh":"當學生能聽出相似英語音之間的差異，耳朵可能發展出選擇性。"},{"en":"Increased selectivity means the system is better at separating the target from distractions.","zh":"選擇性增加表示系統更能把目標與干擾分開。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how focused or specific a response becomes.","zh":"這個短語描述反應變得多集中或多具體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"response to a specific tone","meaning":"對特定聲音的反應","examples":[{"en":"The neurons strengthened their response to a specific tone.","zh":"神經元加強了對特定聲音的反應。"},{"en":"Response to a specific tone means reaction to one particular sound frequency.","zh":"response to a specific tone 指對某一特定聲音頻率的反應。"},{"en":"A singer may train her response to a specific tone so she can match pitch accurately.","zh":"歌手可能訓練自己對特定聲音的反應，以準確配合音高。"},{"en":"When the brain responds more strongly to one tone, it shows learning has become selective.","zh":"當大腦對一個聲音反應更強，顯示學習已變得有選擇性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes targeted reaction to a particular sound.","zh":"這個短語描述對特定聲音的定向反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"continue to increase","meaning":"持續增加","examples":[{"en":"The selectivity continued to increase for several days.","zh":"選擇性在數天內持續增加。"},{"en":"To continue to increase means to keep becoming greater over time.","zh":"continue to increase 指隨時間繼續變得更大。"},{"en":"A student’s reading speed may continue to increase after several weeks of daily practice.","zh":"學生每天練習數星期後，閱讀速度可能持續增加。"},{"en":"Continued increase suggests that improvement does not stop immediately after training.","zh":"持續增加顯示改善不會在訓練後立即停止。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ongoing growth.","zh":"這個短語描述持續增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"terminate the training","meaning":"結束訓練","examples":[{"en":"The neural changes continued after the researchers terminated the training.","zh":"研究人員結束訓練後，神經變化仍然繼續。"},{"en":"To terminate the training means to end the training session or programme.","zh":"terminate the training 指結束訓練時段或訓練計劃。"},{"en":"A coach may terminate the training early if the weather becomes dangerous.","zh":"如果天氣變得危險，教練可能提早結束訓練。"},{"en":"If changes continue after training is terminated, learning processes may still be active.","zh":"如果訓練結束後變化仍持續，學習過程可能仍然活躍。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formally stopping a period of practice.","zh":"這個短語描述正式停止一段練習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not intuitively obvious","meaning":"從直覺上並不明顯","examples":[{"en":"It is not intuitively obvious why lasting memory forms slowly.","zh":"為何長久記憶形成得慢，從直覺上並不明顯。"},{"en":"Not intuitively obvious means not easy to understand immediately by common sense.","zh":"not intuitively obvious 指不能立即用常識理解。"},{"en":"It is not intuitively obvious why sleeping after study can improve later performance.","zh":"為何溫習後睡覺能改善之後表現，從直覺上並不明顯。"},{"en":"Some scientific truths feel strange until experiments explain them.","zh":"有些科學真相在實驗解釋前會令人覺得奇怪。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an idea that needs evidence or explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述需要證據或解釋的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"one can wonder why","meaning":"人們可能會疑問為何……","examples":[{"en":"One can wonder why long-term memory is initially so fragile.","zh":"人們可能會疑問為何長期記憶最初如此脆弱。"},{"en":"One can wonder why means it is reasonable to ask why something is true.","zh":"one can wonder why 指人們合理地可以問為何某事為真。"},{"en":"One can wonder why students forget simple words after learning them once.","zh":"人們可能會疑問為何學生只學一次後就忘記簡單詞語。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a thoughtful question rather than a direct answer.","zh":"這個短語引出深思問題，而不是直接答案。"},{"en":"It is used when something seems surprising or puzzling.","zh":"它用於某事令人驚訝或困惑時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rely on","meaning":"依賴……","examples":[{"en":"We rely on long-term memory for many hours, days or even a lifetime.","zh":"我們依賴長期記憶數小時、數天，甚至一生。"},{"en":"To rely on something means to depend on it for help, success or normal functioning.","zh":"rely on 某物，指依靠它來獲得幫助、成功或正常運作。"},{"en":"Students rely on memory when they answer exam questions without notes.","zh":"學生不看筆記回答考試題時，依賴記憶。"},{"en":"If a system we rely on fails, daily tasks become harder.","zh":"如果我們依賴的系統失效，日常任務會變得更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dependence on something important.","zh":"這個短語描述對重要事物的依靠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be susceptible to disruption","meaning":"容易受到干擾","examples":[{"en":"Newly formed memories are susceptible to disruption.","zh":"新形成的記憶容易受到干擾。"},{"en":"To be susceptible to disruption means to be easily disturbed, damaged or interrupted.","zh":"be susceptible to disruption 指容易被打擾、損害或中斷。"},{"en":"A student’s concentration is susceptible to disruption when her phone keeps ringing.","zh":"當手機不停響，學生的專注力容易受到干擾。"},{"en":"Fragile memories can be lost if the brain is disturbed soon after learning.","zh":"如果學習後不久大腦受干擾，脆弱記憶可能會消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes vulnerability to interference.","zh":"這個短語描述容易受干擾的脆弱性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"shortly after it is initiated","meaning":"在開始形成後不久","examples":[{"en":"Memory remains vulnerable shortly after it is initiated.","zh":"記憶在開始形成後不久仍然脆弱。"},{"en":"Shortly after it is initiated means soon after the process has begun.","zh":"shortly after it is initiated 指該過程開始後很短時間。"},{"en":"A new habit is fragile shortly after it is initiated because it has not become routine.","zh":"新習慣在開始後不久很脆弱，因為它尚未成為例行習慣。"},{"en":"Early disturbance can matter more when a process has only just started.","zh":"當過程剛開始，早期干擾可能更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the vulnerable beginning stage.","zh":"這個短語指出脆弱的開始階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"brain system","meaning":"大腦系統","examples":[{"en":"A specialised brain system consolidates long-term memories.","zh":"一個專門大腦系統鞏固長期記憶。"},{"en":"A brain system is a set of brain areas or processes that work together for a function.","zh":"brain system 是共同為某功能運作的一組大腦區域或過程。"},{"en":"A brain system for language helps people understand words and produce sentences.","zh":"語言大腦系統幫助人理解詞語並產生句子。"},{"en":"When a system is specialised, it performs a particular job more effectively.","zh":"當系統專門化，它會更有效執行特定工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an organised set of brain functions.","zh":"這個短語描述一組有組織的大腦功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a late development in","meaning":"……中的較後期發展","examples":[{"en":"One suggestion was that consolidation was a late development in evolution.","zh":"有一個說法認為記憶鞏固是演化中的較後期發展。"},{"en":"A late development in something is a feature that appeared only in a later stage of its history.","zh":"late development in 某事，是只在其歷史較後階段才出現的特徵。"},{"en":"Written exams were a late development in education compared with oral teaching.","zh":"與口頭教學相比，筆試是教育中的較後期發展。"},{"en":"If something is a late development, it was not present in earlier forms.","zh":"如果某事是較後期發展，它在早期形式中並不存在。"},{"en":"The phrase describes when a feature appeared in a long process.","zh":"這個短語描述某特徵在長過程中何時出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"vertebrate evolution","meaning":"脊椎動物演化","examples":[{"en":"The proposed explanation concerned vertebrate evolution.","zh":"該建議解釋涉及脊椎動物演化。"},{"en":"Vertebrate evolution is the evolutionary history of animals with backbones.","zh":"vertebrate evolution 是有脊骨動物的演化歷史。"},{"en":"Fish, birds, reptiles and mammals are all part of vertebrate evolution.","zh":"魚類、鳥類、爬行類和哺乳類都是脊椎動物演化的一部分。"},{"en":"Studying vertebrate evolution helps scientists compare brain features across related animals.","zh":"研究脊椎動物演化幫助科學家比較相關動物的大腦特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to how backbone animals changed over time.","zh":"這個短語指有脊骨動物如何隨時間改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"mammalian brains","meaning":"哺乳類動物大腦","examples":[{"en":"Mammalian brains are large and highly complex.","zh":"哺乳類動物大腦龐大且高度複雜。"},{"en":"Mammalian brains are the brains of mammals, such as humans, dogs, rats and whales.","zh":"mammalian brains 是人類、狗、老鼠和鯨魚等哺乳類動物的大腦。"},{"en":"Scientists study mammalian brains to understand learning, emotion and movement.","zh":"科學家研究哺乳類動物大腦，以理解學習、情緒和動作。"},{"en":"Their complexity can make memory processes difficult but valuable to study.","zh":"其複雜性令記憶過程難以研究，但也很有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to brains belonging to mammals.","zh":"這個短語指屬於哺乳類動物的大腦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"enormously complex","meaning":"極其複雜","examples":[{"en":"The human brain is enormously complex.","zh":"人類大腦極其複雜。"},{"en":"Enormously complex means extremely complicated, with many parts interacting.","zh":"enormously complex 指極度複雜，有許多部分互相影響。"},{"en":"A city’s transport system can be enormously complex because trains, buses and roads affect one another.","zh":"城市交通系統可以極其複雜，因為火車、巴士和道路互相影響。"},{"en":"Complex systems are hard to understand because changing one part can affect many others.","zh":"複雜系統難以理解，因為改變一部分可以影響許多其他部分。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly emphasises great complexity.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調高度複雜性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"readily reject","meaning":"可以輕易否定","examples":[{"en":"The evidence allows researchers to readily reject these explanations.","zh":"證據讓研究人員可以輕易否定這些解釋。"},{"en":"To readily reject something means to dismiss it easily because the evidence against it is clear.","zh":"readily reject 某事，指因反對證據清楚而容易駁回它。"},{"en":"A teacher can readily reject an answer if it directly contradicts the passage.","zh":"如果答案直接與文章矛盾，老師可以輕易否定它。"},{"en":"Strong contrary evidence makes an explanation difficult to defend.","zh":"強烈相反證據令解釋難以辯護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rejecting an idea without much hesitation.","zh":"這個短語描述不太猶豫地拒絕一個想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"all species studied to date","meaning":"至今研究過的所有物種","examples":[{"en":"All species studied to date have short- and long-term memory.","zh":"至今研究過的所有物種都有短期和長期記憶。"},{"en":"All species studied to date means every species examined up to the present point in the research.","zh":"all species studied to date 指研究至目前為止檢視過的每個物種。"},{"en":"All classes surveyed to date have reported that students want clearer examples.","zh":"至今調查過的所有班級都報告學生想要更清楚例子。"},{"en":"The phrase is careful because future research may add new evidence.","zh":"這個短語很謹慎，因為未來研究可能加入新證據。"},{"en":"It describes the current scope of available studies.","zh":"它描述目前可用研究的範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be susceptible to","meaning":"容易受到……影響","examples":[{"en":"All the animals studied are susceptible to retrograde amnesia.","zh":"所有被研究的動物都容易受到逆行性失憶影響。"},{"en":"To be susceptible to something means to be easily affected by it.","zh":"be susceptible to 某事，指容易受它影響。"},{"en":"Young children may be susceptible to illness when many classmates are sick.","zh":"當許多同學生病，年幼孩子可能容易受到疾病影響。"},{"en":"If a memory system is susceptible to disruption, it can be damaged by certain events.","zh":"如果記憶系統容易受干擾，它可以被某些事件損害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes vulnerability.","zh":"這個短語描述脆弱性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"retrograde amnesia","meaning":"逆行性失憶","examples":[{"en":"Retrograde amnesia causes the loss of memories formed before an event.","zh":"逆行性失憶導致某事件前形成的記憶喪失。"},{"en":"Retrograde amnesia is a condition in which a person or animal loses memories from before an injury or treatment.","zh":"retrograde amnesia 是人或動物失去受傷或治療前記憶的狀況。"},{"en":"A patient with retrograde amnesia may forget what happened before a car accident.","zh":"患有逆行性失憶的病人可能忘記車禍前發生的事。"},{"en":"Studying this condition helps scientists understand how memories are stored and disrupted.","zh":"研究這種狀況幫助科學家理解記憶如何被儲存和干擾。"},{"en":"The phrase names a type of memory loss that looks backward in time.","zh":"這個短語指出一種向時間較早方向影響的記憶喪失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"molluscs","meaning":"軟體動物","examples":[{"en":"Molluscs also form long-term memories slowly.","zh":"軟體動物也會緩慢形成長期記憶。"},{"en":"Molluscs are soft-bodied animals such as snails, clams and octopuses.","zh":"molluscs 是蝸牛、蛤蜊和八爪魚等身體柔軟的動物。"},{"en":"Scientists may study molluscs because their nervous systems can be simpler to observe.","zh":"科學家可能研究軟體動物，因為其神經系統可較容易觀察。"},{"en":"Finding memory consolidation in molluscs suggests the process is evolutionarily old.","zh":"在軟體動物中發現記憶鞏固，顯示該過程在演化上很古老。"},{"en":"The word names a broad group of animals.","zh":"這個詞指出一大類動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"emerge early in evolution","meaning":"在演化早期出現","examples":[{"en":"Memory consolidation clearly emerged early in evolution.","zh":"記憶鞏固明顯在演化早期出現。"},{"en":"To emerge early in evolution means to appear in ancient stages of biological development.","zh":"emerge early in evolution 指在生物發展的古老階段出現。"},{"en":"Basic pain responses emerged early in evolution because they helped animals avoid danger.","zh":"基本痛覺反應在演化早期出現，因為它幫助動物避開危險。"},{"en":"If a feature appears in many distant species, it may have emerged early.","zh":"如果某特徵出現在許多相距甚遠的物種中，它可能很早出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an ancient biological origin.","zh":"這個短語描述古老的生物起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be conserved","meaning":"在演化中被保留下來","examples":[{"en":"The process was conserved across many animal species.","zh":"這個過程在許多動物物種中被保留下來。"},{"en":"To be conserved in evolution means to be preserved across species over a long time.","zh":"be conserved 在演化中指在漫長時間內於不同物種中被保存。"},{"en":"Some basic cell processes are conserved because they are useful for survival.","zh":"有些基本細胞過程因對生存有用而被保留下來。"},{"en":"If a feature is conserved, it likely serves an important function.","zh":"如果某特徵被保留下來，它很可能發揮重要功能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something kept through evolutionary history.","zh":"這個短語描述某事在演化歷史中被保留。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"compelling reason","meaning":"具說服力的理由","examples":[{"en":"There is no compelling reason to think the brain could not form memories quickly.","zh":"沒有具說服力的理由認為大腦不能快速形成記憶。"},{"en":"A compelling reason is a strong and convincing reason.","zh":"compelling reason 是強而有說服力的理由。"},{"en":"A school needs a compelling reason before cancelling an important exam.","zh":"學校在取消重要考試前需要具說服力的理由。"},{"en":"Without a compelling reason, an explanation may remain weak or speculative.","zh":"沒有具說服力的理由，解釋可能仍然薄弱或只是推測。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence or logic strong enough to persuade.","zh":"這個短語描述足以說服人的證據或邏輯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"biological system","meaning":"生物系統","examples":[{"en":"The brain is a highly complex biological system.","zh":"大腦是一個高度複雜的生物系統。"},{"en":"A biological system is a living system made of interacting parts.","zh":"biological system 是由互相作用部分組成的生命系統。"},{"en":"The human body’s immune system is a biological system that fights infection.","zh":"人體免疫系統是一個對抗感染的生物系統。"},{"en":"Biological systems are complex because chemicals, cells and organs influence one another.","zh":"生物系統複雜，因為化學物、細胞和器官互相影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised processes in living organisms.","zh":"這個短語指生物體內有組織的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the fact is that","meaning":"事實是","examples":[{"en":"The fact is that animal brains do not create lasting memories instantly.","zh":"事實是，動物大腦不會即時創造長久記憶。"},{"en":"The fact is that introduces a statement the writer presents as true or important.","zh":"the fact is that 引出作者視為真實或重要的陳述。"},{"en":"The fact is that students cannot improve writing without regular practice.","zh":"事實是，學生沒有定期練習就不能改善寫作。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to correct misunderstanding or emphasise reality.","zh":"這個短語用來糾正誤解或強調現實。"},{"en":"It signals that the speaker wants readers to focus on a key truth.","zh":"它標示說話者希望讀者集中於一個關鍵事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"serve an adaptive function","meaning":"發揮適應性功能","examples":[{"en":"Memory consolidation must serve an important adaptive function.","zh":"記憶鞏固必定發揮重要適應性功能。"},{"en":"To serve an adaptive function means to help an organism survive or adjust to its environment.","zh":"serve an adaptive function 指幫助生物生存或適應環境。"},{"en":"Fear of dangerous roads can serve an adaptive function by making children more careful.","zh":"對危險道路的恐懼可以透過令孩子更小心而發揮適應性功能。"},{"en":"If a process has been conserved in evolution, it may serve a useful survival purpose.","zh":"如果某過程在演化中被保留下來，它可能發揮有用的生存功能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a function that helps adaptation.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助適應的功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"considerable evidence","meaning":"相當多證據","examples":[{"en":"There is considerable evidence supporting an adaptive explanation.","zh":"有相當多證據支持適應性解釋。"},{"en":"Considerable evidence means a large and meaningful amount of evidence.","zh":"considerable evidence 指大量且有意義的證據。"},{"en":"There is considerable evidence that feedback improves student writing.","zh":"有相當多證據顯示回饋能改善學生寫作。"},{"en":"Considerable evidence makes an explanation more credible than a simple guess.","zh":"相當多證據令解釋比單純猜測更可信。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that support is not small or weak.","zh":"這個短語強調支持並不少或薄弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"slow consolidation","meaning":"緩慢的記憶鞏固","examples":[{"en":"Slow consolidation may allow later events to affect memory strength.","zh":"緩慢的記憶鞏固可能容許後來事件影響記憶強度。"},{"en":"Slow consolidation is gradual stabilisation of memory over time.","zh":"slow consolidation 是記憶隨時間逐漸穩定下來。"},{"en":"A student’s memory of a lesson may strengthen slowly after review and sleep.","zh":"學生對一堂課的記憶可能在複習和睡眠後慢慢強化。"},{"en":"Because consolidation is slow, events after learning can still change the final memory.","zh":"因為鞏固是緩慢的，學習後的事件仍可以改變最終記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase describes memory becoming stable through a delayed process.","zh":"這個短語描述記憶透過延遲過程變得穩定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be adaptive","meaning":"具有適應作用","examples":[{"en":"The slow process may be adaptive rather than inefficient.","zh":"這個緩慢過程可能具有適應作用，而不是低效率。"},{"en":"To be adaptive means to help an organism adjust, survive or function better in its environment.","zh":"be adaptive 指幫助生物適應、生存或在環境中更好運作。"},{"en":"Forgetting some unimportant details may be adaptive because it saves mental energy.","zh":"忘記某些不重要細節可能具有適應作用，因為它節省心理能量。"},{"en":"A feature can look inefficient at first but still be useful for survival.","zh":"一項特徵起初可能看似低效，但仍可能對生存有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes biological usefulness.","zh":"這個短語描述生物上的有用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"enable a process to","meaning":"使某個過程能夠……","examples":[{"en":"Slow consolidation enables later biological processes to influence memory.","zh":"緩慢鞏固使後來的生物過程能夠影響記憶。"},{"en":"To enable a process to do something means to make it possible for that process to act.","zh":"enable a process to do something 指使該過程有可能發揮作用。"},{"en":"Clear instructions enable a class project to run smoothly.","zh":"清楚指示使班級項目能夠順利進行。"},{"en":"If one process enables another, it creates the conditions needed for the second process.","zh":"如果一個過程使另一過程能夠發生，它就創造了第二個過程所需條件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making an action possible.","zh":"這個短語描述令某行動成為可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"neurobiological processes","meaning":"神經生物學過程","examples":[{"en":"Neurobiological processes after learning can alter memory strength.","zh":"學習後的神經生物學過程可以改變記憶強度。"},{"en":"Neurobiological processes are processes in the nervous system involving neurons, chemicals and brain activity.","zh":"neurobiological processes 是神經系統中涉及神經元、化學物和大腦活動的過程。"},{"en":"Sleep may support neurobiological processes that strengthen memory after study.","zh":"睡眠可能支援學習後強化記憶的神經生物學過程。"},{"en":"These processes matter because they connect behaviour with physical changes in the brain.","zh":"這些過程重要，因為它們把行為與大腦中的實際變化連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to biological activity within the nervous system.","zh":"這個短語指神經系統內的生物活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"occur shortly after learning","meaning":"在學習後不久發生","examples":[{"en":"Important biological processes occur shortly after learning.","zh":"重要生物過程在學習後不久發生。"},{"en":"To occur shortly after learning means to happen soon after new information or a skill is acquired.","zh":"occur shortly after learning 指在新資訊或技能被學會後很快發生。"},{"en":"A student may benefit from quiet rest because some memory processes occur shortly after learning.","zh":"學生可能從安靜休息中受益，因為某些記憶過程在學習後不久發生。"},{"en":"Events soon after study can matter because the brain is still processing the experience.","zh":"學習後不久發生的事件可能重要，因為大腦仍在處理該經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the early post-learning period.","zh":"這個短語標記早期學習後時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"influence the strength of memory","meaning":"影響記憶的強度","examples":[{"en":"Later experiences can influence the strength of memory.","zh":"後來經歷可以影響記憶的強度。"},{"en":"To influence the strength of memory means to make a memory stronger or weaker.","zh":"influence the strength of memory 指令記憶變強或變弱。"},{"en":"Reviewing a lesson after dinner can influence the strength of memory by reinforcing it.","zh":"晚飯後複習課堂可以透過強化它來影響記憶強度。"},{"en":"Stress, sleep and repetition can all change how strongly information is stored.","zh":"壓力、睡眠和重複都可以改變資訊儲存得有多牢固。"},{"en":"The phrase describes factors that affect how durable a memory becomes.","zh":"這個短語描述影響記憶變得多持久的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"memory for experiences","meaning":"對經歷的記憶","examples":[{"en":"The brain adjusts the strength of memory for experiences.","zh":"大腦調整對經歷的記憶強度。"},{"en":"Memory for experiences means memory of events that a person or animal has lived through.","zh":"memory for experiences 指對人或動物經歷過的事件的記憶。"},{"en":"A child’s memory for experiences may include the first day of school or a family trip.","zh":"孩子對經歷的記憶可能包括第一天上學或家庭旅行。"},{"en":"Emotional or repeated experiences often become stronger memories than ordinary moments.","zh":"情緒強烈或反覆出現的經歷，常比普通時刻成為更強記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on remembered life events, not isolated facts only.","zh":"這個短語重點在被記住的人生事件，而不只是孤立事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be enhanced","meaning":"得到增強","examples":[{"en":"Memory can be enhanced by treatment administered after learning.","zh":"記憶可以透過學習後施予的處理得到增強。"},{"en":"To be enhanced means to be improved or made stronger.","zh":"be enhanced 指被改善或變得更強。"},{"en":"A student’s understanding can be enhanced by clear examples and timely feedback.","zh":"學生理解可以透過清楚例子和及時回饋得到增強。"},{"en":"If memory is enhanced after learning, the brain stores the experience more strongly.","zh":"如果記憶在學習後得到增強，大腦會更牢固地儲存該經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improvement beyond the original level.","zh":"這個短語描述超越原本水平的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as well as impaired","meaning":"既可增強，也可受損","examples":[{"en":"Memory can be enhanced as well as impaired.","zh":"記憶既可增強，也可受損。"},{"en":"As well as impaired means not only made worse, but also possibly improved.","zh":"as well as impaired 指不只可能變差，也可能改善。"},{"en":"A student’s performance can be helped by good sleep as well as impaired by stress.","zh":"學生表現可以因睡眠良好而受幫助，也可以因壓力而受損。"},{"en":"This contrast shows that memory is not only vulnerable to harm; it can also be strengthened.","zh":"這個對比顯示記憶不只是容易受害，也可以被強化。"},{"en":"The phrase presents two opposite possible effects.","zh":"這個短語呈現兩種相反的可能效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"administer treatment shortly after","meaning":"在……後不久施予治療","examples":[{"en":"Researchers administered treatments shortly after training.","zh":"研究人員在訓練後不久施予處理。"},{"en":"To administer treatment shortly after something means to give the treatment soon after that event.","zh":"administer treatment shortly after 某事，指在該事件後很快給予治療。"},{"en":"A doctor may administer treatment shortly after an allergic reaction begins.","zh":"醫生可能在過敏反應開始後不久施予治療。"},{"en":"The timing matters because early treatment may affect the outcome more strongly.","zh":"時間很重要，因為早期治療可能更強烈影響結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving an intervention soon after a key event.","zh":"這個短語描述在關鍵事件後不久給予干預。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"provide intriguing support for","meaning":"為……提供耐人尋味的支持","examples":[{"en":"The findings provide intriguing support for the hypothesis.","zh":"這些發現為該假說提供耐人尋味的支持。"},{"en":"To provide intriguing support for something means to give interesting evidence that seems to support it.","zh":"provide intriguing support for 某事，指給出有趣而似乎支持它的證據。"},{"en":"A school survey may provide intriguing support for the idea that short breaks improve focus.","zh":"學校調查可能為短休息改善專注力這個想法提供耐人尋味的支持。"},{"en":"Intriguing support encourages further research because it is suggestive but may not be final proof.","zh":"耐人尋味的支持會鼓勵進一步研究，因為它有啟示性但未必是最終證明。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence that is interesting and supportive.","zh":"這個短語描述有趣且支持性的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Choose the correct letter for each multiple-choice question.","zh":"為每條多項選擇題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choose the correct letter means select the option letter that matches the right answer.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選出符合正確答案的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may choose the correct letter after comparing all options with the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能在把所有選項與文章比較後選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Choosing too quickly can lead to mistakes if two options look similar.","zh":"如果兩個選項看起來相似，太快選擇可能導致錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction for multiple-choice tasks.","zh":"這個短語是多項選擇題的常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"experiments described in","meaning":"文中描述的實驗","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to experiments described in the passage.","zh":"題目指文中描述的實驗。"},{"en":"Experiments described in a passage are the studies that the text explains or reports.","zh":"experiments described in 文章，是文本解釋或報告的研究。"},{"en":"Students should answer using experiments described in the article, not experiments they know from outside class.","zh":"學生應使用文章中描述的實驗作答，而不是使用課外知道的實驗。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds candidates to stay close to the source material.","zh":"這個短語提醒考生緊扣來源材料。"},{"en":"It is useful in exam questions that test specific passage details.","zh":"它適合用於測試特定文章細節的考題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"at different stages of","meaning":"在……的不同階段","examples":[{"en":"The goldfish were injected at different stages of the experiments.","zh":"金魚在實驗的不同階段被注射。"},{"en":"At different stages of something means at different points in a process.","zh":"at different stages of 某事，指在一個過程中的不同時間點。"},{"en":"A teacher may give feedback at different stages of essay writing: planning, drafting and editing.","zh":"老師可能在文章寫作的不同階段給回饋：規劃、起稿和修改。"},{"en":"Comparing stages helps people see when an action has the strongest effect.","zh":"比較不同階段幫助人看出某行動何時效果最強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes timing within a longer process.","zh":"這個短語描述較長過程中的時間安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"different types of task","meaning":"不同種類的任務","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to training animals to do different types of task.","zh":"該選項指訓練動物做不同種類的任務。"},{"en":"Different types of task are different kinds of activities or jobs someone is asked to perform.","zh":"different types of task 是某人被要求執行的不同種類活動或工作。"},{"en":"A language lesson may include different types of task, such as listening, speaking and sentence completion.","zh":"語文課可能包括不同種類的任務，例如聆聽、說話和句子填空。"},{"en":"Using different tasks helps test whether learning works in more than one situation.","zh":"使用不同任務幫助測試學習是否在多於一種情況中有效。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses variety in assigned activities.","zh":"這個短語強調指定活動的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"different types of treatment","meaning":"不同種類的治療","examples":[{"en":"Researchers sometimes use different types of treatment.","zh":"研究人員有時使用不同種類的處理。"},{"en":"Different types of treatment are different interventions, methods or medicines used to affect a condition.","zh":"different types of treatment 是用來影響某狀況的不同干預、方法或藥物。"},{"en":"A doctor may compare different types of treatment for headaches, such as rest, medicine and lifestyle changes.","zh":"醫生可能比較不同種類的頭痛治療，例如休息、藥物和生活習慣改變。"},{"en":"Comparing treatments helps reveal which one is effective or what process it affects.","zh":"比較治療幫助揭示哪一種有效或它影響甚麼過程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes variety in interventions.","zh":"這個短語描述干預方式的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"compare the performance of","meaning":"比較……的表現","examples":[{"en":"The researchers could compare the performance of different subjects.","zh":"研究人員可以比較不同實驗對象的表現。"},{"en":"To compare the performance of people or animals means to examine how well each one does a task.","zh":"compare the performance of 人或動物，指檢視每個做任務的表現如何。"},{"en":"A teacher may compare the performance of two classes after using different teaching methods.","zh":"老師可能在使用不同教學方法後比較兩班的表現。"},{"en":"Comparison helps show whether a treatment, method or condition makes a difference.","zh":"比較有助顯示處理、方法或條件是否帶來差異。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on judging results side by side.","zh":"這個短語重點在並排判斷結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"recent studies suggest that","meaning":"近期研究顯示","examples":[{"en":"Recent studies suggest that memory systems may operate independently.","zh":"近期研究顯示記憶系統可能獨立運作。"},{"en":"Recent studies suggest that means newer research points towards a possible conclusion.","zh":"recent studies suggest that 指較新的研究指向一個可能結論。"},{"en":"Recent studies suggest that sleep quality affects students’ attention in class.","zh":"近期研究顯示睡眠質素影響學生課堂注意力。"},{"en":"The phrase is cautious because studies may support an idea without proving it completely.","zh":"這個短語較謹慎，因為研究可能支持一個想法，但未完全證明。"},{"en":"It links modern research with a developing claim.","zh":"它把現代研究與發展中的主張連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"normally affect","meaning":"一般會影響","examples":[{"en":"Some treatments do not normally affect short-term memory.","zh":"有些處理一般不會影響短期記憶。"},{"en":"Normally affect means usually influence or change something.","zh":"normally affect 指通常影響或改變某事。"},{"en":"A small amount of background noise may not normally affect an experienced student’s reading.","zh":"少量背景噪音一般不會影響有經驗學生的閱讀。"},{"en":"If something does not normally affect a process, its impact is not expected in ordinary cases.","zh":"如果某事一般不會影響某過程，其影響在普通情況中並不預期會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the usual effect of something.","zh":"這個短語描述某事通常帶來的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"build upon","meaning":"以……為基礎逐步形成","examples":[{"en":"One theory proposed that long-term memory builds upon short-term memory.","zh":"有一個理論提出長期記憶以短期記憶為基礎逐步形成。"},{"en":"To build upon something means to use it as a foundation for further development.","zh":"build upon 某事，指以它作為基礎作進一步發展。"},{"en":"A student builds upon basic grammar when she learns complex sentence structures.","zh":"學生學習複雜句式時，是以基本文法為基礎逐步發展。"},{"en":"If one stage builds upon another, the later stage depends on the earlier one.","zh":"如果一個階段建基於另一階段，較後階段便依賴較早階段。"},{"en":"The phrase describes development based on a prior foundation.","zh":"這個短語描述建基於先前基礎的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be formed by separate processes","meaning":"由不同過程形成","examples":[{"en":"Short- and long-term memories may be formed by separate processes.","zh":"短期和長期記憶可能由不同過程形成。"},{"en":"To be formed by separate processes means to be created through different mechanisms rather than one shared pathway.","zh":"be formed by separate processes 指透過不同機制形成，而不是同一條共同路徑。"},{"en":"Speaking and writing skills may be formed by separate processes, even though both use language.","zh":"說話和寫作技能可能由不同過程形成，雖然兩者都使用語言。"},{"en":"If two abilities are formed separately, improving one may not automatically improve the other.","zh":"如果兩種能力分開形成，改善其中一種未必自動改善另一種。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses independent development.","zh":"這個短語強調獨立發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"affect both…and…","meaning":"同時影響……和……","examples":[{"en":"Some treatments may affect both short- and long-term memory.","zh":"有些處理可能同時影響短期和長期記憶。"},{"en":"Affect both A and B means influence two things, not just one.","zh":"affect both A and B 指影響兩件事，而不只是一件。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can affect both concentration and mood.","zh":"睡眠不足可以同時影響專注力和心情。"},{"en":"If one factor affects both systems, researchers must separate its effects carefully.","zh":"如果一個因素同時影響兩個系統，研究人員必須仔細分開其效果。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that two areas are influenced together.","zh":"這個短語強調兩個範疇一起受影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"what does the writer want to show?","meaning":"作者想說明甚麼？","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what the writer wants to show through an example.","zh":"題目問作者想透過例子說明甚麼。"},{"en":"What does the writer want to show asks about the purpose or message behind a detail.","zh":"what does the writer want to show 問的是細節背後的目的或訊息。"},{"en":"In a reading exam, students should ask what the writer wants to show when an example seems unusual.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，當例子看似不尋常，學生應問作者想說明甚麼。"},{"en":"Understanding purpose helps students choose answers based on meaning, not keywords alone.","zh":"理解目的幫助學生根據意思而不只關鍵詞選答案。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the writer’s intention.","zh":"這個短語重點在作者意圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"prompt memory formation","meaning":"迅速形成記憶","examples":[{"en":"Prompt memory formation supports everyday behaviour.","zh":"迅速形成記憶支援日常行為。"},{"en":"Prompt memory formation means memory forming quickly after an experience.","zh":"prompt memory formation 指經歷後快速形成記憶。"},{"en":"A student uses prompt memory formation when she remembers a new classroom after one visit.","zh":"學生去過一次新課室後就記得位置，就是使用迅速記憶形成。"},{"en":"Quick memory formation helps people adjust before mistakes or accidents happen.","zh":"快速記憶形成幫助人在錯誤或意外發生前作出調整。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fast creation of useful memory.","zh":"這個短語描述有用記憶的快速建立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"underlie the performance of","meaning":"是執行……的基礎","examples":[{"en":"Memory processes underlie the performance of everyday tasks.","zh":"記憶過程是執行日常任務的基礎。"},{"en":"To underlie the performance of something means to form the hidden basis that makes it possible.","zh":"underlie the performance of 某事，指形成使它成為可能的隱藏基礎。"},{"en":"Basic grammar knowledge underlies the performance of good writing.","zh":"基本文法知識是良好寫作表現的基礎。"},{"en":"If hidden processes are weak, visible performance may also suffer.","zh":"如果隱藏過程薄弱，可見表現也可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the deeper support behind an action.","zh":"這個短語指出行動背後的深層支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"everyday tasks","meaning":"日常任務","examples":[{"en":"Rapid memory is important for everyday tasks.","zh":"快速記憶對日常任務很重要。"},{"en":"Everyday tasks are ordinary activities people do in daily life.","zh":"everyday tasks 是人們日常生活中做的普通活動。"},{"en":"Brushing teeth, using stairs, shopping and taking a bus are everyday tasks.","zh":"刷牙、使用樓梯、購物和乘巴士都是日常任務。"},{"en":"Many everyday tasks depend on memory even when people do not notice it.","zh":"許多日常任務依賴記憶，即使人們沒有察覺。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to normal routine activities.","zh":"這個短語指普通例行活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be carried out unconsciously","meaning":"在無意識下進行","examples":[{"en":"Some routine tasks can be carried out unconsciously.","zh":"有些例行任務可以在無意識下進行。"},{"en":"To be carried out unconsciously means to be done without deliberate thought or awareness.","zh":"be carried out unconsciously 指不用刻意思考或察覺也能完成。"},{"en":"An experienced typist may press many keys correctly without consciously thinking about each letter.","zh":"有經驗的打字員可能不用有意識想每個字母，也能正確按下許多鍵。"},{"en":"Unconscious action is useful because it saves attention for harder tasks.","zh":"無意識行動有用，因為它為較困難任務節省注意力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes automatic behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述自動化行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"physical accidents","meaning":"身體意外","examples":[{"en":"Uneven steps can cause physical accidents.","zh":"不平的梯級可以造成身體意外。"},{"en":"Physical accidents are accidents that injure the body or involve bodily harm.","zh":"physical accidents 是造成身體受傷或涉及身體傷害的意外。"},{"en":"Slipping on a wet floor is a physical accident.","zh":"在濕地板滑倒就是身體意外。"},{"en":"Good design and warning signs can reduce physical accidents in public places.","zh":"良好設計和警告標誌可以減少公共地方的身體意外。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on accidents affecting the body rather than only feelings or plans.","zh":"這個短語重點在影響身體的意外，而不只是感受或計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"impair the function of","meaning":"損害……的功能","examples":[{"en":"Injury can impair the function of memory.","zh":"受傷可以損害記憶功能。"},{"en":"To impair the function of something means to damage or weaken how it works.","zh":"impair the function of 某物，指損害或削弱其運作方式。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can impair the function of attention during class.","zh":"缺乏睡眠可以損害課堂注意力功能。"},{"en":"When a function is impaired, performance becomes less reliable or less effective.","zh":"當功能受損，表現會變得較不可靠或較低效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weakening an ability or system.","zh":"這個短語描述削弱能力或系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complex information","meaning":"複雜資料","examples":[{"en":"Complex information may take longer to retain.","zh":"複雜資料可能需要更長時間保留。"},{"en":"Complex information is information with many parts, relationships or details.","zh":"complex information 是包含許多部分、關係或細節的資訊。"},{"en":"A timetable with many rooms, teachers and exceptions contains complex information.","zh":"包含許多課室、老師和例外情況的時間表含有複雜資料。"},{"en":"Complex information often needs organisation, examples and repeated review.","zh":"複雜資料通常需要組織、例子和反覆複習。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts detailed difficult information with simple facts.","zh":"這個短語把詳細困難資料與簡單事實作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be retained by memory","meaning":"被記憶保留","examples":[{"en":"Important information must be retained by memory.","zh":"重要資訊必須被記憶保留。"},{"en":"To be retained by memory means to be kept in the mind for later use.","zh":"be retained by memory 指被頭腦保存以供日後使用。"},{"en":"A student needs key formulas to be retained by memory before a maths exam.","zh":"數學考試前，學生需要關鍵公式被記憶保留。"},{"en":"Information is retained better when it is meaningful and practised often.","zh":"當資訊有意義並經常練習，它會被更好地保留。"},{"en":"The phrase describes successful storage in memory.","zh":"這個短語描述成功儲存在記憶中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"observations about","meaning":"關於……的觀察","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about Karni and Sagi’s observations about memory.","zh":"題目問 Karni 和 Sagi 關於記憶的觀察。"},{"en":"Observations about something are things noticed, recorded or concluded from watching carefully.","zh":"observations about 某事，是透過仔細觀察而注意、記錄或得出的事情。"},{"en":"A teacher’s observations about student behaviour can help improve classroom rules.","zh":"老師關於學生行為的觀察可以幫助改善課室規則。"},{"en":"Scientific observations become useful when they reveal a pattern or support a conclusion.","zh":"當科學觀察揭示模式或支持結論時，就變得有用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to carefully noticed information on a topic.","zh":"這個短語指關於某主題的仔細觀察資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"cast doubt on","meaning":"令人質疑……","examples":[{"en":"New evidence may cast doubt on an existing hypothesis.","zh":"新證據可能令人質疑現有假說。"},{"en":"To cast doubt on something means to make people question whether it is true.","zh":"cast doubt on 某事，指令人懷疑它是否真確。"},{"en":"A second witness may cast doubt on the first report of an accident.","zh":"第二名目擊者可能令人質疑第一份意外報告。"},{"en":"Evidence casts doubt when it does not fit the expected explanation.","zh":"當證據不符合預期解釋，它就會令人質疑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weakening confidence in a claim.","zh":"這個短語描述削弱對某主張的信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"existing hypotheses","meaning":"現有假說","examples":[{"en":"Researchers test existing hypotheses about memory.","zh":"研究人員測試關於記憶的現有假說。"},{"en":"Existing hypotheses are theories or explanations that already exist before new research is done.","zh":"existing hypotheses 是新研究進行前已存在的理論或解釋。"},{"en":"A science class may test existing hypotheses about which conditions help plants grow.","zh":"科學課可能測試關於哪些條件有助植物生長的現有假說。"},{"en":"Testing old ideas helps researchers confirm, reject or revise them.","zh":"測試舊想法幫助研究人員確認、否定或修正它們。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to current theories under examination.","zh":"這個短語指正在被檢驗的當前理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"relate only to","meaning":"只與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The experiment did not relate only to short-term memory.","zh":"該實驗並不只與短期記憶有關。"},{"en":"To relate only to something means to concern just that one thing and nothing else.","zh":"relate only to 某事，指只涉及那一件事而不涉及其他。"},{"en":"A school rule about phones may not relate only to lessons; it may also concern safety.","zh":"關於手機的校規未必只與課堂有關；它也可能涉及安全。"},{"en":"If a study does not relate only to one area, its findings may have wider meaning.","zh":"如果研究不只與一個範疇有關，其發現可能有更廣泛意義。"},{"en":"The phrase limits or denies the scope of connection.","zh":"這個短語限制或否定關聯範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be based on tasks involving","meaning":"基於涉及……的任務","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to studies based on tasks involving hearing.","zh":"該選項指基於涉及聽覺任務的研究。"},{"en":"To be based on tasks involving something means to use activities that require that ability or sense.","zh":"be based on tasks involving 某事，指使用需要該能力或感官的活動。"},{"en":"A spelling study may be based on tasks involving listening to words and writing them down.","zh":"串字研究可能基於涉及聆聽詞語並寫下來的任務。"},{"en":"The task type matters because it shapes what kind of learning is being tested.","zh":"任務類型重要，因為它塑造正在測試哪種學習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the foundation of a study’s method.","zh":"這個短語描述研究方法的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"confirm other findings","meaning":"證實其他研究結果","examples":[{"en":"The observations confirmed other experimental findings.","zh":"這些觀察證實了其他實驗結果。"},{"en":"To confirm other findings means to support or verify results from previous studies.","zh":"confirm other findings 指支持或驗證先前研究的結果。"},{"en":"A new class survey may confirm other findings that students learn better with examples.","zh":"新班級調查可能證實其他發現：學生透過例子學得更好。"},{"en":"Confirmation from different studies makes a conclusion stronger.","zh":"不同研究的確認令結論更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence agreeing with earlier results.","zh":"這個短語描述與早前結果一致的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"gradually move from…to…","meaning":"逐漸從……轉移到……","examples":[{"en":"Brain activity gradually moved from one area to other areas.","zh":"大腦活動逐漸從一個區域轉移到其他區域。"},{"en":"To gradually move from A to B means to shift slowly from one place, stage or focus to another.","zh":"gradually move from A to B 指慢慢由一個地方、階段或焦點轉移到另一個。"},{"en":"A lesson may gradually move from simple examples to harder exam questions.","zh":"一堂課可能逐漸從簡單例子轉移到較難考試題。"},{"en":"Gradual movement suggests a process of transition rather than sudden change.","zh":"逐漸轉移顯示這是一個過渡過程，而不是突然改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow change in focus or position.","zh":"這個短語描述焦點或位置的緩慢變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"continue to get better at","meaning":"在……方面持續進步","examples":[{"en":"Some subjects continue to get better at a task after training.","zh":"有些實驗對象在訓練後仍在某項任務上持續進步。"},{"en":"To continue to get better at something means to keep improving in that skill.","zh":"continue to get better at 某事，指在該技能上繼續改善。"},{"en":"A student may continue to get better at pronunciation after class if she keeps listening and practising.","zh":"如果學生持續聆聽和練習，課後可能在發音方面持續進步。"},{"en":"Improvement after practice suggests that learning continues beyond the lesson.","zh":"練習後仍有改善，顯示學習在課堂以外繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ongoing progress.","zh":"這個短語描述持續進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"treatment given to subjects","meaning":"向實驗對象施予的治療","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to treatment given to the subjects.","zh":"該選項指向實驗對象施予的處理。"},{"en":"Treatment given to subjects means an intervention applied to people or animals in a study.","zh":"treatment given to subjects 指在研究中施加於人或動物的干預。"},{"en":"In a memory experiment, treatment given to subjects may include a drug, sound or sleep condition.","zh":"在記憶實驗中，向實驗對象施予的處理可能包括藥物、聲音或睡眠條件。"},{"en":"Researchers compare results before and after treatment to see its effect.","zh":"研究人員比較處理前後結果，以觀察其效果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what participants receive during an experiment.","zh":"這個短語描述參與者在實驗中接受甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"agree with the views of","meaning":"與作者的觀點相符","examples":[{"en":"Decide whether each statement agrees with the views of the writer.","zh":"判斷每項陳述是否與作者的觀點相符。"},{"en":"To agree with the views of the writer means to match the writer’s opinion or interpretation.","zh":"agree with the views of the writer 指與作者的意見或詮釋相符。"},{"en":"A statement may agree with the writer’s views even if it uses different words from the passage.","zh":"即使使用與文章不同的詞語，陳述仍可能與作者觀點相符。"},{"en":"Students must identify attitude and meaning, not only repeated vocabulary.","zh":"學生必須辨認態度和意思，而不只是重複詞彙。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in YES/NO/NOT GIVEN reading questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 YES/NO/NOT GIVEN 閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與作者的觀點矛盾","examples":[{"en":"Write “NO” if the statement contradicts the writer’s views.","zh":"如果陳述與作者觀點矛盾，就寫 “NO”。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of the writer means to go against what the writer believes or argues.","zh":"contradict the views of the writer 指與作者相信或主張的內容相反。"},{"en":"If the writer says a method is useful, a statement saying it is useless contradicts the writer’s views.","zh":"如果作者說某方法有用，而陳述說它無用，就是與作者觀點矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should mark “NO” only when the opposite view is supported by the passage.","zh":"學生只有在文章支持相反觀點時才應標示 “NO”。"},{"en":"The phrase describes disagreement with the writer’s opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述與作者意見不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Choose “NOT GIVEN” if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"如果無法判斷作者怎樣想，就選 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資訊作出判斷。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions a researcher’s age, it is impossible to say how old they were.","zh":"如果文章從未提到研究人員年齡，就無法判斷他們當時幾歲。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge to fill gaps in the passage.","zh":"學生不應使用外部知識填補文章空白。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a situation where the text gives no clear answer.","zh":"這個短語描述文本沒有給出清楚答案的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be repeated over several days","meaning":"在數天內重複進行","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that the training was repeated over several days.","zh":"該選項暗示訓練在數天內重複進行。"},{"en":"To be repeated over several days means to happen again on more than one day.","zh":"be repeated over several days 指在多於一天中再次發生。"},{"en":"Vocabulary practice repeated over several days is usually easier to remember than one long session.","zh":"在數天內重複進行的詞彙練習，通常比一次長時間練習更容易記住。"},{"en":"Repetition across days can strengthen learning and reveal gradual improvement.","zh":"跨日重複可以強化學習並顯示逐漸改善。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated action across a multi-day period.","zh":"這個短語描述在多天期間反覆行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"associate a sound with","meaning":"將聲音與……聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"The rats learned to associate a sound with an unpleasant experience.","zh":"老鼠學會將聲音與不愉快經歷聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To associate a sound with something means to connect that sound in memory with an event, feeling or result.","zh":"associate a sound with 某事，指在記憶中把該聲音與事件、感受或結果連繫起來。"},{"en":"A student may associate a school bell with the end of a lesson.","zh":"學生可能把學校鐘聲與課堂結束聯繫起來。"},{"en":"When two experiences happen together repeatedly, the brain may link them.","zh":"當兩種經驗反覆一起出現，大腦可能把它們連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learned connection in memory.","zh":"這個短語描述記憶中後天建立的聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"specific experience","meaning":"特定經歷","examples":[{"en":"The rats associated the tone with a specific experience.","zh":"老鼠把該聲音與特定經歷聯繫起來。"},{"en":"A specific experience is one particular event or situation someone has gone through.","zh":"specific experience 是某人經歷過的一件特定事件或情況。"},{"en":"A child may remember a specific experience, such as getting lost in a shopping mall.","zh":"孩子可能記得一段特定經歷，例如在商場迷路。"},{"en":"Specific experiences can become strong memories if they are emotional or unusual.","zh":"如果特定經歷帶有情緒或不尋常，它可以成為強烈記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a particular lived event, not a general idea.","zh":"這個短語指特定親身事件，而不是一般想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"learned associations","meaning":"後天建立的聯繫","examples":[{"en":"The rats formed learned associations between sounds and events.","zh":"老鼠在聲音和事件之間形成後天建立的聯繫。"},{"en":"Learned associations are connections formed through experience or training.","zh":"learned associations 是透過經驗或訓練形成的聯繫。"},{"en":"A student may form learned associations between a red pen mark and a grammar mistake.","zh":"學生可能在紅筆標記和文法錯誤之間形成後天建立的聯繫。"},{"en":"Repeated pairing makes learned associations stronger.","zh":"反覆配對會令後天聯繫更強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes connections that are acquired rather than inborn.","zh":"這個短語描述後天習得而非天生的連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"increase with time","meaning":"隨時間增強","examples":[{"en":"The strength of the association appeared to increase with time.","zh":"該聯繫的強度似乎隨時間增強。"},{"en":"To increase with time means to become stronger, larger or clearer as time passes.","zh":"increase with time 指隨時間過去變得更強、更大或更清楚。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may increase with time if she practises speaking every week.","zh":"如果學生每星期練習說話，信心可能隨時間增強。"},{"en":"If a memory increases with time, later brain processes may be strengthening it.","zh":"如果記憶隨時間增強，後來的大腦過程可能正在強化它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growth across time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"evolutionary advantage","meaning":"演化優勢","examples":[{"en":"The slow formation of memory may provide an evolutionary advantage.","zh":"記憶的緩慢形成可能提供演化優勢。"},{"en":"An evolutionary advantage is a feature that helps a species survive or reproduce better over time.","zh":"evolutionary advantage 是幫助物種隨時間更好地生存或繁殖的特徵。"},{"en":"Good night vision may provide an evolutionary advantage to animals that hunt in darkness.","zh":"良好夜視能力可能為夜間捕獵的動物提供演化優勢。"},{"en":"If slow memory consolidation improves survival decisions, it may be preserved by evolution.","zh":"如果緩慢記憶鞏固改善生存決策，它可能被演化保留下來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a survival benefit shaped by evolution.","zh":"這個短語描述由演化塑造的生存好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"more stable than","meaning":"比……更穩定","examples":[{"en":"The option compares whether human memories are more stable than those of animals.","zh":"該選項比較人類記憶是否比動物記憶更穩定。"},{"en":"More stable than means less likely to change, disappear or be disrupted than something else.","zh":"more stable than 指比另一事物較不容易改變、消失或受干擾。"},{"en":"A printed timetable is usually more stable than a rumour about lesson changes.","zh":"印刷時間表通常比關於課堂改動的傳聞更穩定。"},{"en":"If one memory is more stable than another, it is harder to weaken or erase.","zh":"如果一段記憶比另一段更穩定，它就較難被削弱或抹走。"},{"en":"The phrase compares reliability or durability.","zh":"這個短語比較可靠性或持久性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Complete the summary using words from the list.","zh":"使用列表中的詞語完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill in missing words in a shortened version of the passage.","zh":"complete the summary 指在文章的簡短版本中填入缺失詞語。"},{"en":"Students complete the summary by matching meaning, grammar and word limits.","zh":"學生透過配對意思、文法和字數限制來完成摘要。"},{"en":"This task tests whether students understand the overall passage, not only single words.","zh":"這項任務測試學生是否理解整篇文章，而不只是單字。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"examine the way","meaning":"研究……的方式","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have examined the way lasting memories are formed.","zh":"研究人員研究長久記憶形成的方式。"},{"en":"To examine the way something happens means to study the process or method by which it happens.","zh":"examine the way 某事發生，指研究它發生的過程或方法。"},{"en":"A school may examine the way students revise before changing its study-skills programme.","zh":"學校在改變學習技巧課程前，可能研究學生溫習的方式。"},{"en":"Examining the way a process works helps people improve or explain it.","zh":"研究一個過程如何運作，幫助人改善或解釋它。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on studying how something happens.","zh":"這個短語重點在研究某事如何發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"laboratory experiments","meaning":"實驗室實驗","examples":[{"en":"Laboratory experiments allow researchers to control treatments and conditions.","zh":"實驗室實驗讓研究人員控制處理方法和條件。"},{"en":"Laboratory experiments are studies carried out in a controlled research setting.","zh":"laboratory experiments 是在受控研究環境中進行的研究。"},{"en":"Students may do simple laboratory experiments to test how light affects plant growth.","zh":"學生可能做簡單實驗室實驗，測試光線如何影響植物生長。"},{"en":"Controlled experiments help researchers separate cause and effect more clearly.","zh":"受控實驗幫助研究人員更清楚分開因果。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to planned scientific tests in a lab.","zh":"這個短語指在實驗室進行的有計劃科學測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"teach subjects to do something","meaning":"教實驗對象做某事","examples":[{"en":"Researchers teach subjects to do something new.","zh":"研究人員教實驗對象做新的事情。"},{"en":"To teach subjects to do something means to train study participants in a new task or skill.","zh":"teach subjects to do something 指訓練研究參與者完成新任務或技能。"},{"en":"A memory study may teach subjects to press a button when they see a particular shape.","zh":"記憶研究可能教實驗對象在看見特定形狀時按按鈕。"},{"en":"Teaching a new task gives researchers a clear starting point for measuring learning.","zh":"教新任務給研究人員一個清楚起點來量度學習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes training participants during an experiment.","zh":"這個短語描述在實驗中訓練參與者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"mild electric shocks","meaning":"輕微電擊","examples":[{"en":"Some laboratory studies use mild electric shocks.","zh":"有些實驗室研究使用輕微電擊。"},{"en":"Mild electric shocks are small electrical stimuli used in controlled experiments.","zh":"mild electric shocks 是受控實驗中使用的小型電刺激。"},{"en":"In animal learning research, mild electric shocks may be used to create an unpleasant association.","zh":"在動物學習研究中，輕微電擊可能被用來建立不愉快聯繫。"},{"en":"Because shocks can cause discomfort, researchers must use them carefully and ethically.","zh":"因為電擊可能造成不適，研究人員必須小心且合乎倫理地使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weak electrical stimulation, not severe injury.","zh":"這個短語描述弱電刺激，而不是嚴重傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"sophisticated equipment","meaning":"精密儀器","examples":[{"en":"Researchers use sophisticated equipment to observe brain activity.","zh":"研究人員使用精密儀器觀察大腦活動。"},{"en":"Sophisticated equipment is advanced, complex equipment designed for precise work.","zh":"sophisticated equipment 是為精確工作而設計的先進複雜設備。"},{"en":"A hospital may use sophisticated equipment to scan a patient’s brain.","zh":"醫院可能使用精密儀器掃描病人大腦。"},{"en":"Advanced equipment can reveal details that ordinary tools cannot detect.","zh":"先進設備可以揭示普通工具偵測不到的細節。"},{"en":"The phrase describes high-level scientific or technical tools.","zh":"這個短語描述高階科學或技術工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"monitor behaviour","meaning":"監察行為","examples":[{"en":"Some studies monitor behaviour after a learning experience.","zh":"有些研究在學習經歷後監察行為。"},{"en":"To monitor behaviour means to watch and record how someone or something acts over time.","zh":"monitor behaviour 指隨時間觀察並記錄某人或某物如何行動。"},{"en":"A teacher may monitor behaviour after changing classroom seating.","zh":"老師改變課室座位後，可能監察學生行為。"},{"en":"Monitoring helps show whether a treatment or learning experience has changed actions.","zh":"監察有助顯示處理或學習經歷是否改變行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes systematic observation of behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述對行為的有系統觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"learning experience","meaning":"學習經歷","examples":[{"en":"Behaviour may change after a learning experience.","zh":"行為可能在學習經歷後改變。"},{"en":"A learning experience is an event or activity through which someone gains knowledge or skill.","zh":"learning experience 是讓某人獲得知識或技能的事件或活動。"},{"en":"A difficult group project can be a learning experience if students understand teamwork better afterwards.","zh":"如果學生之後更理解團隊合作，困難小組項目可以是學習經歷。"},{"en":"Learning experiences can change behaviour because they create new memories and expectations.","zh":"學習經歷可以改變行為，因為它們創造新記憶和預期。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an experience that teaches something.","zh":"這個短語指能教會某事的經歷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"observe brain activity","meaning":"觀察大腦活動","examples":[{"en":"Brain-imaging equipment is used to observe brain activity.","zh":"腦成像設備被用來觀察大腦活動。"},{"en":"To observe brain activity means to watch or measure how the brain works during a task or after an event.","zh":"observe brain activity 指觀察或量度大腦在任務期間或事件後如何運作。"},{"en":"Researchers may observe brain activity while a person remembers a word list.","zh":"研究人員可能在一個人記憶詞表時觀察大腦活動。"},{"en":"Observing the brain helps connect behaviour with physical changes inside the head.","zh":"觀察大腦幫助把行為與頭腦內部的實際變化連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes scientific measurement of the working brain.","zh":"這個短語描述對運作中大腦的科學量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"results are generally consistent","meaning":"研究結果大致一致","examples":[{"en":"The results of different studies are generally consistent.","zh":"不同研究的結果大致一致。"},{"en":"Results are generally consistent means findings from different studies mostly agree with one another.","zh":"results are generally consistent 指不同研究的發現大多彼此一致。"},{"en":"If several classes improve after using examples, the results are generally consistent.","zh":"如果幾個班級使用例子後都有進步，結果就是大致一致。"},{"en":"Consistent results make a conclusion more trustworthy.","zh":"一致結果令結論更可信。"},{"en":"The phrase describes agreement across evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述證據之間的吻合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a lengthy biological process","meaning":"漫長的生物過程","examples":[{"en":"Lasting memory results from a lengthy biological process.","zh":"長久記憶來自漫長的生物過程。"},{"en":"A lengthy biological process is a long process inside living systems involving cells, chemicals or organs.","zh":"lengthy biological process 是生物系統內涉及細胞、化學物或器官的長時間過程。"},{"en":"Healing a broken bone is a lengthy biological process that takes weeks.","zh":"骨折癒合是需要數星期的漫長生物過程。"},{"en":"If memory depends on such a process, it may not become permanent immediately.","zh":"如果記憶依賴這樣的過程，它可能不會立即變成永久。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a slow natural process in the body or brain.","zh":"這個短語描述身體或大腦中的緩慢自然過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"share this trait with","meaning":"與……共有這種特徵","examples":[{"en":"Humans share this trait with many other species.","zh":"人類與許多其他物種共有這種特徵。"},{"en":"To share this trait with others means to have the same characteristic as them.","zh":"share this trait with 其他群體，指與它們擁有相同特徵。"},{"en":"Humans share the need for sleep with many animals.","zh":"人類與許多動物共有睡眠需要。"},{"en":"Shared traits suggest that different species may have common biological solutions.","zh":"共有特徵顯示不同物種可能有共同生物解決方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a characteristic found in more than one group.","zh":"這個短語描述出現在多於一個群體中的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"evolutionary history","meaning":"演化歷史","examples":[{"en":"Memory consolidation developed early in evolutionary history.","zh":"記憶鞏固在演化歷史中很早便發展出來。"},{"en":"Evolutionary history is the long record of how living things changed over time.","zh":"evolutionary history 是生物如何隨時間改變的漫長記錄。"},{"en":"Scientists study evolutionary history to understand why animals have certain behaviours.","zh":"科學家研究演化歷史，以理解動物為何有某些行為。"},{"en":"If a feature appears early in evolutionary history, it may be very ancient and important.","zh":"如果某特徵在演化歷史中早期出現，它可能非常古老且重要。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the timeline of biological change.","zh":"這個短語指生物變化的時間線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 115 - The creation of lasting memories.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 116":[{"front":"pottery production","meaning":"陶器生產","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.","zh":"文章探討古代 Akrotiri 的陶器生產。"},{"en":"Pottery production is the process of making clay objects such as jars, bowls, and containers.","zh":"pottery production 指製作陶罐、碗和容器等黏土物件的過程。"},{"en":"A village may develop pottery production if local clay is easy to find and people need storage vessels.","zh":"如果本地容易找到黏土，而人們需要貯存容器，村落可能發展陶器生產。"},{"en":"Pottery production can become more organised when many households or traders need similar containers.","zh":"當許多家庭或商人需要相似容器時，陶器生產可以變得更有組織。"},{"en":"This phrase refers not only to making pots, but also to the skills, tools, workers, and systems behind them.","zh":"這個短語不只指製作陶器，也包括背後的技術、工具、工人和制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ancient Akrotiri","meaning":"古代 Akrotiri","examples":[{"en":"Ancient Akrotiri had a highly developed pottery industry.","zh":"古代 Akrotiri 有高度發展的陶器產業。"},{"en":"Ancient Akrotiri refers to the early settlement of Akrotiri before modern times.","zh":"ancient Akrotiri 指現代以前的早期 Akrotiri 聚居地。"},{"en":"A history teacher may use ancient Akrotiri to show how coastal communities traded goods.","zh":"歷史老師可能用古代 Akrotiri 來展示沿海社群如何交易貨物。"},{"en":"Studying ancient Akrotiri helps researchers understand craft production in the Aegean world.","zh":"研究古代 Akrotiri 有助研究者理解愛琴海世界的工藝生產。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific ancient place, not ancient Greece in general.","zh":"這個短語指一個特定古代地方，而不是泛指古希臘。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"excavations at the site of","meaning":"在……遺址進行的發掘","examples":[{"en":"Excavations at the site of prehistoric Akrotiri have revealed important evidence.","zh":"在史前 Akrotiri 遺址進行的發掘揭示了重要證據。"},{"en":"Excavations at the site of a place are careful digs carried out where ancient remains are found.","zh":"excavations at the site of a place 指在發現古代遺物的地點進行的小心挖掘。"},{"en":"Excavations at the site of an old village may uncover tools, walls, and cooking pots.","zh":"在古村落遺址進行的發掘可能揭露工具、牆壁和煮食陶器。"},{"en":"Such excavations can reveal how people lived, worked, traded, and stored food.","zh":"這類發掘可以揭示人們如何生活、工作、交易和儲存食物。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when describing archaeological work at a specific location.","zh":"描述特定地點的考古工作時，這個短語很常見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"prehistoric Akrotiri","meaning":"史前 Akrotiri","examples":[{"en":"Prehistoric Akrotiri was located near the Aegean Sea.","zh":"史前 Akrotiri 位於愛琴海附近。"},{"en":"Prehistoric Akrotiri means Akrotiri before written historical records from the settlement are available.","zh":"prehistoric Akrotiri 指在該聚居地有文字歷史記錄以前的 Akrotiri。"},{"en":"A museum display may show prehistoric Akrotiri through pottery, wall paintings, and tools.","zh":"博物館展示可能透過陶器、壁畫和工具呈現史前 Akrotiri。"},{"en":"Because written records are limited, objects from prehistoric Akrotiri become especially important.","zh":"由於文字記錄有限，來自史前 Akrotiri 的物件變得特別重要。"},{"en":"This phrase places Akrotiri in an early period known mainly through archaeology.","zh":"這個短語把 Akrotiri 放在一個主要透過考古了解的早期時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on the coast of","meaning":"位於……海岸","examples":[{"en":"Akrotiri was situated on the coast of the Aegean Sea.","zh":"Akrotiri 位於愛琴海海岸。"},{"en":"On the coast of a place means beside the sea or along the edge of a body of water.","zh":"on the coast of a place 指在海邊或沿着水域邊緣。"},{"en":"A restaurant on the coast of an island may serve fresh seafood every day.","zh":"位於島嶼海岸的餐廳可能每天供應新鮮海鮮。"},{"en":"Coastal locations often support fishing, travel, and trade because boats can arrive easily.","zh":"沿海位置常支持捕魚、交通和貿易，因為船隻容易到達。"},{"en":"This phrase gives geographical position near water.","zh":"這個短語提供靠近水域的地理位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the Aegean Sea","meaning":"愛琴海","examples":[{"en":"Ancient trade routes crossed the Aegean Sea.","zh":"古代貿易路線橫越愛琴海。"},{"en":"The Aegean Sea is the sea between Greece and Turkey, with many islands and coastal settlements.","zh":"Aegean Sea 指位於希臘和土耳其之間、擁有許多島嶼和沿海聚居地的海域。"},{"en":"A geography lesson may use the Aegean Sea to explain why sea trade was important in the ancient world.","zh":"地理課可能用愛琴海解釋為何海上貿易在古代世界很重要。"},{"en":"Communities around the Aegean Sea could exchange pottery, food, metals, and ideas by ship.","zh":"愛琴海周邊社群可以透過船隻交換陶器、食物、金屬和思想。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific sea connected with ancient Mediterranean trade.","zh":"這個短語指與古代地中海貿易有關的一個特定海域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"reveal much about","meaning":"揭示許多關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"The excavations revealed much about pottery manufacture.","zh":"發掘揭示了許多關於陶器製造的資料。"},{"en":"To reveal much about something means to provide a lot of information about it.","zh":"reveal much about something 指提供很多關於某事的資訊。"},{"en":"A student’s notebook can reveal much about how carefully they revise.","zh":"學生的筆記可以揭示許多關於他們溫習是否仔細的資料。"},{"en":"Archaeological finds reveal much about the past when there are few written records.","zh":"當文字記錄很少，考古發現能揭示許多關於過去的資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence helps people understand a hidden topic.","zh":"當證據幫助人理解隱藏議題時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"technical aspects of","meaning":"……的技術層面","examples":[{"en":"The finds provide evidence about the technical aspects of pottery production.","zh":"這些發現提供了關於陶器生產技術層面的證據。"},{"en":"Technical aspects of something are the practical skills, methods, and tools involved in doing it.","zh":"technical aspects of something 指做某事所涉及的實際技能、方法和工具。"},{"en":"A cooking class may teach the technical aspects of baking, such as temperature and timing.","zh":"烹飪課可能教授烘焙的技術層面，例如溫度和時間。"},{"en":"Understanding technical aspects helps people see how a product was actually made.","zh":"理解技術層面幫助人看出產品實際如何製成。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on method and skill rather than social meaning alone.","zh":"這個短語集中於方法和技能，而不只是社會意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pottery manufacture","meaning":"陶器製造","examples":[{"en":"Pottery manufacture was one of Akrotiri’s basic industries.","zh":"陶器製造是 Akrotiri 的基礎產業之一。"},{"en":"Pottery manufacture means the making of clay vessels and objects, usually through shaping and firing.","zh":"pottery manufacture 指製作黏土器皿和物件，通常包括塑形和燒製。"},{"en":"A craft centre may demonstrate pottery manufacture by showing how clay becomes a bowl.","zh":"工藝中心可能透過展示黏土如何變成碗來示範陶器製造。"},{"en":"Pottery manufacture requires clay, water, shaping skills, drying time, and heat from a kiln.","zh":"陶器製造需要黏土、水、塑形技巧、乾燥時間和窯爐熱力。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than simply saying “making pots.”","zh":"這個短語比簡單說 “making pots” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"indisputably","meaning":"毫無疑問地","examples":[{"en":"Pottery was indisputably an important local industry.","zh":"陶器毫無疑問是重要的本地產業。"},{"en":"Indisputably means so clearly true that it is very difficult to argue against.","zh":"indisputably 指某事明顯真實，以致很難反駁。"},{"en":"If every student passes a course, the teacher has indisputably achieved strong results.","zh":"如果每名學生都通過課程，老師毫無疑問取得了強勁成果。"},{"en":"Large quantities of pottery make its importance difficult to deny.","zh":"大量陶器令其重要性難以否認。"},{"en":"This word strengthens a claim by showing that the evidence is very clear.","zh":"這個字透過顯示證據非常清楚來加強說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"basic industries","meaning":"基礎產業","examples":[{"en":"Pottery manufacture was one of the city’s basic industries.","zh":"陶器製造是該城市的基礎產業之一。"},{"en":"Basic industries are important economic activities that support daily life and trade.","zh":"basic industries 指支持日常生活和貿易的重要經濟活動。"},{"en":"In a farming town, food processing may be one of the basic industries.","zh":"在農業城鎮，食品加工可能是基礎產業之一。"},{"en":"A basic industry supplies goods or services that many people regularly need.","zh":"基礎產業提供許多人定期需要的商品或服務。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to core economic activities, not minor hobbies.","zh":"這個短語指核心經濟活動，而不是小興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"considerably less is known about","meaning":"人們對……所知少得多","examples":[{"en":"Considerably less is known about how pottery production was organised.","zh":"人們對陶器生產如何組織所知少得多。"},{"en":"Considerably less is known about something means people have much less information about it.","zh":"considerably less is known about something 指人們對某事掌握的資訊少得多。"},{"en":"A school may know much about exam scores, but considerably less is known about students’ sleep habits.","zh":"學校可能很了解考試分數，但對學生睡眠習慣所知少得多。"},{"en":"Less evidence makes researchers more cautious when drawing conclusions.","zh":"證據較少會令研究者在下結論時更謹慎。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a gap in knowledge.","zh":"這個短語突出知識上的缺口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"socio-economic context","meaning":"社會經濟背景","examples":[{"en":"The socio-economic context of pottery production remains uncertain.","zh":"陶器生產的社會經濟背景仍不確定。"},{"en":"Socio-economic context means the social and economic situation surrounding an activity.","zh":"socio-economic context 指圍繞某活動的社會和經濟情況。"},{"en":"To understand a student’s results, teachers may consider the socio-economic context of family income and study space.","zh":"為理解學生成績，老師可能考慮家庭收入和學習空間等社會經濟背景。"},{"en":"In pottery production, this context includes workers, trade, demand, and social organisation.","zh":"在陶器生產中，這個背景包括工人、貿易、需求和社會組織。"},{"en":"This phrase asks not just how something was made, but how it fitted into society.","zh":"這個短語不只問某物如何製造，也問它如何融入社會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the way production was organised","meaning":"生產的組織方式","examples":[{"en":"Researchers know little about the way production was organised.","zh":"研究者對生產的組織方式所知甚少。"},{"en":"The way production was organised means how workers, materials, tools, and tasks were arranged.","zh":"way production was organised 指工人、材料、工具和任務如何被安排。"},{"en":"In a bakery, the way production is organised decides who mixes dough, who bakes, and who sells bread.","zh":"在麵包店中，生產組織方式決定誰搓麵糰、誰烘焙、誰賣麵包。"},{"en":"Good organisation can allow many similar products to be made quickly and consistently.","zh":"良好組織可以讓大量相似產品快速而穩定地製成。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the system behind making things.","zh":"這個短語集中於製造事物背後的制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the bulk of","meaning":"大部分……","examples":[{"en":"The bulk of the pottery found at Akrotiri was locally made.","zh":"在 Akrotiri 發現的大部分陶器都是本地製造的。"},{"en":"The bulk of something means the largest part or majority of it.","zh":"the bulk of something 指某事物的最大部分或大多數。"},{"en":"The bulk of a student’s revision should focus on topics they do not yet understand.","zh":"學生溫習的大部分時間應集中於尚未理解的題目。"},{"en":"If the bulk of pottery is local, researchers can infer strong local production.","zh":"如果大部分陶器都是本地製造，研究者可推斷當地生產能力強。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to most of something, not necessarily all of it.","zh":"這個短語指大部分，而不一定是全部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"locally made","meaning":"本地製造的","examples":[{"en":"Most of the pottery was locally made rather than imported.","zh":"大部分陶器都是本地製造的，而不是進口的。"},{"en":"Locally made means produced in the same area where it was found or used.","zh":"locally made 指在發現或使用地區內製造。"},{"en":"A café may sell locally made cakes from a nearby bakery.","zh":"咖啡店可能售賣附近麵包店本地製造的蛋糕。"},{"en":"Locally made goods can show what materials and skills existed in a community.","zh":"本地製造的貨品可以顯示社區中有甚麼材料和技能。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts local production with goods brought from elsewhere.","zh":"這個短語把本地生產與外地運來的貨品作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"date from","meaning":"可追溯至","examples":[{"en":"The pottery dates from the late fifteenth century BC.","zh":"這些陶器可追溯至公元前15世紀後期。"},{"en":"To date from a period means to come from or belong to that time.","zh":"date from a period 指來自或屬於某時期。"},{"en":"An old school building may date from the 1930s.","zh":"一座舊校舍可能可追溯至1930年代。"},{"en":"Dating an object helps people place it in the right historical context.","zh":"確定物件年代幫助人把它放在正確歷史背景中。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when identifying the age or period of something.","zh":"指出某物年代或時期時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the late fifteenth century BC","meaning":"公元前15世紀後期","examples":[{"en":"Many pots date from the late fifteenth century BC.","zh":"許多陶罐可追溯至公元前15世紀後期。"},{"en":"The late fifteenth century BC means the later part of the 1400s before Christ.","zh":"late fifteenth century BC 指公元前1400年代的後期。"},{"en":"A museum label may place an object in the late fifteenth century BC to show its historical age.","zh":"博物館標籤可能把一件物件標示為公元前15世紀後期，以顯示其歷史年代。"},{"en":"Naming a specific period helps researchers compare objects from the same time.","zh":"指出特定時期有助研究者比較同一時期的物件。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate ancient date.","zh":"這個短語提供古代的大約日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fulfil a vast range of requirements","meaning":"滿足廣泛的需求","examples":[{"en":"The pottery fulfilled a vast range of the settlement’s requirements.","zh":"這些陶器滿足了該聚居地廣泛的需求。"},{"en":"To fulfil a vast range of requirements means to meet many different practical needs.","zh":"fulfil a vast range of requirements 指滿足許多不同的實際需要。"},{"en":"A school library fulfils a wide range of needs by offering books, computers, and quiet study space.","zh":"學校圖書館透過提供書本、電腦和安靜自修空間，滿足廣泛需求。"},{"en":"Different pottery shapes were needed because people stored, cooked, poured, and drank different things.","zh":"人們需要不同陶器形狀，因為他們要貯存、烹煮、傾倒和飲用不同東西。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one category of objects served many functions.","zh":"這個短語顯示同一類物件具有許多功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a vast range of","meaning":"廣泛多樣的……","examples":[{"en":"Akrotiri produced a vast range of pottery types.","zh":"Akrotiri 生產了廣泛多樣的陶器類型。"},{"en":"A vast range of something means a very large variety of it.","zh":"a vast range of something 指某物種類非常多。"},{"en":"A supermarket offers a vast range of food, from rice and fruit to frozen meals.","zh":"超級市場提供廣泛多樣的食物，從米和水果到冷凍餐都有。"},{"en":"A wide range often appears when people have many different needs.","zh":"當人們有許多不同需要時，廣泛種類常會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses both number and variety.","zh":"這個短語同時強調數量和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"settlement’s requirements","meaning":"聚居地的需求","examples":[{"en":"The pots met many of the settlement’s practical requirements.","zh":"這些陶罐滿足了該聚居地許多實際需求。"},{"en":"A settlement’s requirements are the needs of the people living in a community.","zh":"settlement’s requirements 指生活在某社群中的人的需要。"},{"en":"A new housing estate has requirements such as shops, schools, transport, and clinics.","zh":"新住宅區有商店、學校、交通和診所等需求。"},{"en":"In ancient settlements, requirements included storing food, carrying liquids, and preparing meals.","zh":"在古代聚居地，需求包括貯存食物、運送液體和準備膳食。"},{"en":"This phrase links objects to the daily needs of a community.","zh":"這個短語把物件與社群日常需要連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be distinguished","meaning":"可被區分","examples":[{"en":"More than fifty different types of pot can be distinguished.","zh":"超過五十種不同陶罐類型可被區分。"},{"en":"To be distinguished means to be recognised as different from others.","zh":"be distinguished 指能被辨認為與其他事物不同。"},{"en":"Different school uniforms can be distinguished by colour, badge, or design.","zh":"不同校服可以透過顏色、校章或設計被區分。"},{"en":"Pot types can be distinguished when their shapes, sizes, or uses are clearly different.","zh":"當陶器的形狀、大小或用途明顯不同，類型就可被區分。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on telling categories apart.","zh":"這個短語集中於分辨類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a wide variety of","meaning":"各式各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"The pottery includes a wide variety of functional types.","zh":"這批陶器包括各式各樣的功能類型。"},{"en":"A wide variety of something means many different kinds of it.","zh":"a wide variety of something 指許多不同種類的某物。"},{"en":"A good canteen offers a wide variety of food so students with different tastes can eat well.","zh":"好的飯堂提供各式各樣的食物，讓不同口味的學生都能吃得好。"},{"en":"Variety appears when one product category serves many tasks.","zh":"當一類產品服務許多任務，就會出現多樣性。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses diversity rather than a single repeated form.","zh":"這個短語強調多樣，而不是單一重複形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"functional types","meaning":"功能類型","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists identified many functional types of pottery.","zh":"考古學家辨認出許多陶器功能類型。"},{"en":"Functional types are categories based on what objects are used for.","zh":"functional types 指根據物件用途劃分的類別。"},{"en":"In a kitchen, cups, plates, pans, and storage boxes are different functional types.","zh":"在廚房中，杯、碟、鍋和平盒是不同功能類型。"},{"en":"Identifying functional types helps researchers connect shape with daily activity.","zh":"辨認功能類型有助研究者把形狀與日常活動連起來。"},{"en":"This phrase classifies objects by purpose, not decoration.","zh":"這個短語按用途分類物件，而不是按裝飾分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"storage jars","meaning":"貯存罐","examples":[{"en":"Large storage jars were used to hold commodities.","zh":"大型貯存罐用來盛載商品。"},{"en":"Storage jars are containers used to keep food, liquids, or other goods for later use.","zh":"storage jars 指用來保存食物、液體或其他貨物以供日後使用的容器。"},{"en":"A family may use storage jars for rice, beans, sugar, or tea leaves.","zh":"家庭可能使用貯存罐放米、豆、糖或茶葉。"},{"en":"In ancient trade, storage jars helped preserve goods before they were sold or transported.","zh":"在古代貿易中，貯存罐幫助貨物在出售或運輸前得以保存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes containers for keeping things, not for serving them immediately.","zh":"這個短語描述用來保存物品的容器，而不是立即上菜用的器皿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"smaller containers","meaning":"較小型容器","examples":[{"en":"Smaller containers were suitable for transport.","zh":"較小型容器適合運輸。"},{"en":"Smaller containers are vessels that are easier to carry because they hold less.","zh":"smaller containers 指容量較少、因而較容易搬運的器皿。"},{"en":"A student uses a smaller water bottle when a large one is too heavy.","zh":"當大水樽太重，學生會使用較小型水樽。"},{"en":"Smaller containers make transport easier because people can lift and move them more comfortably.","zh":"較小型容器令運輸更容易，因為人們能更舒適地提起和移動它們。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts portable vessels with large storage jars.","zh":"這個短語把可攜式容器與大型貯存罐作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pouring vessels","meaning":"傾倒液體用器皿","examples":[{"en":"Pouring vessels were designed for serving liquids.","zh":"傾倒液體用器皿是為盛奉液體而設計的。"},{"en":"Pouring vessels are containers shaped to pour liquids smoothly.","zh":"pouring vessels 指形狀適合順暢倒出液體的容器。"},{"en":"A teapot is a pouring vessel because its spout helps control the flow of tea.","zh":"茶壺是一種傾倒液體用器皿，因為壺嘴有助控制茶水流動。"},{"en":"Good pouring vessels reduce spilling and make serving easier.","zh":"好的傾倒器皿可以減少潑灑，令上菜或倒飲品更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes vessels whose shape supports the action of pouring.","zh":"這個短語描述形狀支援傾倒動作的器皿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cooking pots","meaning":"炊具；煮食陶鍋","examples":[{"en":"Cooking pots were produced for food preparation.","zh":"炊具是為準備食物而生產的。"},{"en":"Cooking pots are vessels used to cook food over heat.","zh":"cooking pots 指用來加熱烹煮食物的器皿。"},{"en":"A family may use a cooking pot to boil soup or stew vegetables.","zh":"家庭可能用煮食陶鍋煲湯或燉蔬菜。"},{"en":"Cooking pots need to withstand heat, so their material and shape matter.","zh":"炊具需要承受高溫，因此材料和形狀很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pottery used in preparing meals.","zh":"這個短語描述用於準備膳食的陶器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"drinking vessels","meaning":"飲用器皿","examples":[{"en":"Drinking vessels formed one category of pottery.","zh":"飲用器皿構成陶器的一個類別。"},{"en":"Drinking vessels are cups, bowls, or containers used for drinking liquids.","zh":"drinking vessels 指用來飲用液體的杯、碗或容器。"},{"en":"A child’s small cup is a drinking vessel designed for easy handling.","zh":"孩子的小杯是一種設計成容易拿取的飲用器皿。"},{"en":"Different drinking vessels may reflect different habits, drinks, or social customs.","zh":"不同飲用器皿可能反映不同習慣、飲品或社交習俗。"},{"en":"This phrase classifies pottery by its use in drinking.","zh":"這個短語按飲用用途分類陶器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"relate to specific activities","meaning":"與特定活動有關","examples":[{"en":"Different types of pots related to specific activities.","zh":"不同種類陶罐與特定活動有關。"},{"en":"To relate to specific activities means to be connected with particular tasks or uses.","zh":"relate to specific activities 指與特定任務或用途相連。"},{"en":"Sports shoes relate to running, while school shoes relate to daily uniform wear.","zh":"運動鞋與跑步有關，而校鞋與日常校服穿着有關。"},{"en":"Pottery shapes developed because cooking, storing, pouring, and drinking required different designs.","zh":"陶器形狀之所以發展，是因為烹煮、貯存、傾倒和飲用需要不同設計。"},{"en":"This phrase links object type with practical action.","zh":"這個短語把物件類型與實際行動連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"with those activities in mind","meaning":"考慮到那些活動的需要","examples":[{"en":"The vessels were made and distributed with particular activities in mind.","zh":"這些器皿在製作和分配時考慮到特定活動的需要。"},{"en":"With those activities in mind means considering those uses while making decisions.","zh":"with those activities in mind 指在作決定時考慮那些用途。"},{"en":"A teacher designs a worksheet with exam practice in mind.","zh":"老師設計工作紙時，會考慮到考試練習需要。"},{"en":"If a pot is made with transport in mind, it may be smaller and easier to carry.","zh":"如果陶罐製作時考慮到運輸需要，它可能較小且較易搬運。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that design choices were guided by intended use.","zh":"這個短語顯示設計選擇受預定用途引導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"given the large number of","meaning":"鑑於大量的……","examples":[{"en":"Given the large number of shapes, production was probably specialised.","zh":"鑑於大量形狀，生產很可能是專門化的。"},{"en":"Given the large number of something means considering that there are many of them.","zh":"given the large number of something 指考慮到某物數量很多。"},{"en":"Given the large number of students, the school arranged extra classrooms.","zh":"鑑於學生人數眾多，學校安排了額外課室。"},{"en":"A large number of shapes suggests that makers had different skills or production plans.","zh":"大量形狀暗示製作者可能具備不同技能或生產計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a reason for a conclusion.","zh":"這個短語引出得出結論的理由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"relatively high degree of","meaning":"相對較高程度的……","examples":[{"en":"The pottery shows a relatively high degree of standardisation.","zh":"這批陶器顯示相對較高程度的標準化。"},{"en":"A relatively high degree of something means a fairly strong level compared with what might be expected.","zh":"relatively high degree of something 指與預期相比程度相當高。"},{"en":"A class may show a relatively high degree of discipline if most students follow routines without reminders.","zh":"如果大多數學生無需提醒便遵守常規，班級可能顯示相對較高程度的紀律。"},{"en":"A high degree of standardisation suggests repeated control over shape and size.","zh":"高程度標準化暗示形狀和尺寸受到反覆控制。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a careful comparison without sounding absolute.","zh":"這個短語作出謹慎比較，而不是絕對說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"standardisation","meaning":"標準化","examples":[{"en":"The high level of standardisation suggests organised production.","zh":"高水平標準化暗示有組織的生產。"},{"en":"Standardisation means making things according to shared sizes, forms, rules, or measurements.","zh":"standardisation 指按共同尺寸、形式、規則或度量製造事物。"},{"en":"School uniforms show standardisation because many students wear the same design.","zh":"校服顯示標準化，因為許多學生穿着同一設計。"},{"en":"Standardisation makes trade easier because people know what quantity or quality to expect.","zh":"標準化令貿易更容易，因為人們知道可預期的數量或質素。"},{"en":"This word describes consistency across many items.","zh":"這個字描述多件物品之間的一致性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"it has generally been assumed that","meaning":"人們普遍認為","examples":[{"en":"It has generally been assumed that specialists produced the pottery.","zh":"人們普遍認為陶器由專家製作。"},{"en":"It has generally been assumed that means most people have accepted an idea without complete proof.","zh":"it has generally been assumed that 指大多數人在沒有完整證明下接受某想法。"},{"en":"It has generally been assumed that students learn better in quiet rooms, though some prefer background sound.","zh":"人們普遍認為學生在安靜房間學得更好，雖然有些人喜歡背景聲。"},{"en":"Assumptions can guide research, but they still need evidence.","zh":"假設可以引導研究，但仍需要證據。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a widely held but possibly uncertain belief.","zh":"這個短語引出廣泛持有但可能仍不確定的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"most, if not all, of","meaning":"大部分、甚至全部……","examples":[{"en":"Most, if not all, of the pottery may have been made by specialists.","zh":"大部分、甚至全部陶器可能由專家製作。"},{"en":"Most, if not all, of something means nearly all, and possibly every single one.","zh":"most, if not all, of something 指幾乎全部，甚至可能每一個都是。"},{"en":"Most, if not all, of the students understood the rule after the teacher gave examples.","zh":"老師給出例子後，大部分、甚至全部學生都理解了規則。"},{"en":"This phrase allows a strong claim while leaving a small space for exceptions.","zh":"這個短語容許作出強烈說法，同時為例外留下一點空間。"},{"en":"It is useful when evidence suggests almost complete coverage but not absolute certainty.","zh":"當證據暗示幾乎完全涵蓋但未能絕對確定時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"specialised craftsmen","meaning":"專門工匠","examples":[{"en":"Specialised craftsmen probably produced pottery on a large scale.","zh":"專門工匠可能以大規模方式生產陶器。"},{"en":"Specialised craftsmen are skilled workers who focus on a particular craft or product.","zh":"specialised craftsmen 指專注於某種工藝或產品的熟練工人。"},{"en":"A specialised carpenter may spend years making only fine furniture.","zh":"專門木匠可能多年來只製作精緻家具。"},{"en":"Specialisation can improve quality and speed because workers repeat and refine the same skill.","zh":"專門化可以提高質素和速度，因為工人反覆練習並完善同一技能。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to trained makers, not casual household producers.","zh":"這個短語指受訓製作者，而不是普通家庭製作者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"non-domestic context","meaning":"非家庭式環境","examples":[{"en":"The pottery was probably produced in a non-domestic context.","zh":"這些陶器很可能在非家庭式環境中生產。"},{"en":"A non-domestic context is a setting outside ordinary household activity.","zh":"non-domestic context 指普通家庭活動以外的場景。"},{"en":"A bakery is a non-domestic context for making bread because it produces for customers, not just family.","zh":"麵包店是製作麵包的非家庭式環境，因為它為顧客而不只是家人生產。"},{"en":"Large-scale production usually happens outside the home because it needs space, tools, and organisation.","zh":"大規模生產通常發生在家居以外，因為它需要空間、工具和組織。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts workshop production with household production.","zh":"這個短語把工場生產與家庭生產作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"potters’ workshops","meaning":"陶工工場","examples":[{"en":"The potters’ workshops have not yet been found.","zh":"陶工工場尚未被發現。"},{"en":"Potters’ workshops are places where potters shape, dry, and prepare clay vessels.","zh":"potters’ workshops 指陶工塑形、乾燥和準備陶器的地方。"},{"en":"A modern pottery workshop may contain clay, wheels, shelves, tools, and drying areas.","zh":"現代陶器工場可能有黏土、拉坯輪、架子、工具和乾燥區。"},{"en":"Finding workshops would help archaeologists understand how production was organised.","zh":"發現工場將有助考古學家理解生產如何組織。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to work spaces for making pottery.","zh":"這個短語指製作陶器的工作空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"kilns","meaning":"窯爐","examples":[{"en":"No pottery kilns have been discovered within the excavated area.","zh":"在已發掘範圍內尚未發現陶器窯爐。"},{"en":"Kilns are ovens or furnaces used to heat clay objects until they become hard pottery.","zh":"kilns 指用來加熱黏土物件，使其變成堅硬陶器的爐。"},{"en":"A pottery class may use a kiln to fire students’ clay cups.","zh":"陶藝班可能使用窯爐燒製學生的黏土杯。"},{"en":"Without kilns, shaped clay may remain fragile and unsuitable for long use.","zh":"沒有窯爐，成形黏土可能仍很脆弱，不適合長期使用。"},{"en":"This word names an important tool in pottery manufacture.","zh":"這個字指出陶器製造中的重要工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"within the excavated area","meaning":"在已發掘範圍內","examples":[{"en":"The workshops were not found within the excavated area.","zh":"工場沒有在已發掘範圍內被發現。"},{"en":"Within the excavated area means inside the part of the site that has already been dug and studied.","zh":"within the excavated area 指在已經被挖掘和研究的遺址部分之內。"},{"en":"If no kitchen is found within the excavated area of a house, it may be in an unexcavated part.","zh":"如果一座房屋已發掘範圍內沒有廚房，廚房可能在尚未發掘部分。"},{"en":"Absence within the excavated area does not prove absence from the whole site.","zh":"在已發掘範圍內沒有發現，並不證明整個遺址都沒有。"},{"en":"This phrase limits a claim to the area already investigated.","zh":"這個短語把說法限制於已調查地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ceramic workshops","meaning":"陶器工場","examples":[{"en":"The ceramic workshops may have stood outside the main settlement.","zh":"陶器工場可能位於主要聚居地外。"},{"en":"Ceramic workshops are workspaces where clay goods such as pottery are made.","zh":"ceramic workshops 指製作陶器等黏土製品的工作空間。"},{"en":"A modern ceramic workshop may produce cups, tiles, and decorative bowls.","zh":"現代陶器工場可能生產杯、瓷磚和裝飾碗。"},{"en":"Workshops may be placed away from homes because firing pottery produces heat, smoke, and smell.","zh":"工場可能設於住宅以外，因為燒製陶器會產生熱力、煙和氣味。"},{"en":"This phrase is broader than potters’ workshops because it can include different clay products.","zh":"這個短語比 potters’ workshops 更廣，因為可包括不同黏土產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be located on the periphery of","meaning":"位於……的邊緣","examples":[{"en":"The workshops may have been located on the periphery of the site.","zh":"工場可能位於該遺址的邊緣。"},{"en":"To be located on the periphery of a place means to be situated near its outer edge.","zh":"be located on the periphery of a place 指位於某地外圍或邊緣附近。"},{"en":"A car park may be located on the periphery of a school campus to reduce traffic near classrooms.","zh":"停車場可能位於校園邊緣，以減少課室附近交通。"},{"en":"Workshops may be placed on the edge when they need space or produce smoke and noise.","zh":"當工場需要空間或會產生煙和噪音，可能設於邊緣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes edge location rather than central position.","zh":"這個短語描述邊緣位置，而不是中央位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not yet been excavated","meaning":"尚未被發掘","examples":[{"en":"The outer area of the site has not yet been excavated.","zh":"該遺址外圍地區尚未被發掘。"},{"en":"Not yet been excavated means not dug or studied archaeologically so far.","zh":"not yet been excavated 指到目前為止尚未被考古挖掘或研究。"},{"en":"A buried garden behind an old house may not yet have been excavated by researchers.","zh":"舊屋後方被埋藏的花園可能尚未被研究者發掘。"},{"en":"If an area has not been excavated, important evidence may still be hidden there.","zh":"如果某地尚未發掘，重要證據可能仍藏在那裡。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that current knowledge may be incomplete.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們現有知識可能不完整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in any event","meaning":"無論如何","examples":[{"en":"In any event, the pottery appears to have been mass-produced.","zh":"無論如何，這些陶器似乎是大量生產的。"},{"en":"In any event means whatever the exact situation is, the following point still matters.","zh":"in any event 指無論確切情況如何，接下來的重點仍然成立。"},{"en":"The meeting may be online or in person; in any event, students must prepare their questions.","zh":"會議可能網上或面對面舉行；無論如何，學生都必須準備問題。"},{"en":"This phrase moves the argument forward despite uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語在有不確定之處時推進論點。"},{"en":"It is useful when one detail is unresolved but the main conclusion remains.","zh":"當某細節未解決但主要結論仍成立時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ubiquity of","meaning":"……的普遍存在","examples":[{"en":"The ubiquity of pottery suggests that it was produced on a large scale.","zh":"陶器的普遍存在暗示它是大規模生產的。"},{"en":"The ubiquity of something means its presence almost everywhere.","zh":"ubiquity of something 指某物幾乎到處存在。"},{"en":"The ubiquity of smartphones has changed how students communicate and study.","zh":"智能手機的普遍存在改變了學生溝通和學習的方式。"},{"en":"If pottery is found everywhere at a site, it suggests people used it constantly.","zh":"如果陶器在遺址各處都有發現，便暗示人們經常使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses how widespread something is.","zh":"這個短語強調某物分布非常廣泛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"consistent repetition of","meaning":"……的一再穩定重現","examples":[{"en":"The consistent repetition of the same types suggests industrial production.","zh":"相同類型的一再穩定重現暗示工業式生產。"},{"en":"Consistent repetition of something means the same form or pattern appears again and again.","zh":"consistent repetition of something 指同一形式或模式反覆出現。"},{"en":"The consistent repetition of a spelling mistake may show that a student has misunderstood a rule.","zh":"同一拼字錯誤一再穩定出現，可能顯示學生誤解了規則。"},{"en":"Repeated pottery forms suggest makers followed shared models or measurements.","zh":"陶器形式反覆出現暗示製作者遵循共同模型或度量。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights regularity rather than random similarity.","zh":"這個短語強調規律性，而不是隨機相似。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in different sizes","meaning":"以不同尺寸","examples":[{"en":"The same types of vessel were produced in different sizes.","zh":"相同類型的器皿以不同尺寸生產。"},{"en":"In different sizes means made larger or smaller while keeping the same general type.","zh":"in different sizes 指在保持同一基本類型下製成較大或較小版本。"},{"en":"A shop may sell the same water bottle in different sizes for children and adults.","zh":"商店可能以不同尺寸售賣同款水樽，供兒童和成人使用。"},{"en":"Producing vessels in different sizes helps meet different storage or transport needs.","zh":"以不同尺寸生產器皿有助滿足不同貯存或運輸需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes size variation within the same category.","zh":"這個短語描述同一類別內的尺寸變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"production on an industrial scale","meaning":"工業規模生產","examples":[{"en":"The evidence suggests production on an industrial scale.","zh":"證據暗示工業規模生產。"},{"en":"Production on an industrial scale means making goods in large quantities through organised systems.","zh":"production on an industrial scale 指透過有組織制度大量製造貨品。"},{"en":"A factory produces lunch boxes on an industrial scale when thousands are made every week.","zh":"工廠每星期製造數千個飯盒，就是以工業規模生產。"},{"en":"Industrial-scale production requires planning, repeated designs, labour, and steady demand.","zh":"工業規模生產需要規劃、重複設計、勞動力和穩定需求。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts mass production with small household craft.","zh":"這個短語把大量生產與小型家庭手工藝作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"respond to pressures beyond","meaning":"回應超出……範圍的壓力","examples":[{"en":"Akrotirian potters responded to pressures beyond their own households.","zh":"Akrotiri 的陶工回應了超出自己家庭範圍的壓力。"},{"en":"To respond to pressures beyond something means to react to demands from a wider outside system.","zh":"respond to pressures beyond something 指回應來自更廣泛外部系統的需求。"},{"en":"A small bakery may respond to pressures beyond local customers when supermarkets start ordering bread.","zh":"當超級市場開始訂購麵包，小麵包店可能回應超出本地顧客範圍的壓力。"},{"en":"External demand can push producers to make more goods and standardise their products.","zh":"外部需求可以推動生產者製造更多貨品並把產品標準化。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that production was influenced by forces outside the home.","zh":"這個短語顯示生產受到家庭以外力量影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"increasing complexity of","meaning":"……日益增加的複雜性","examples":[{"en":"Craft production reflected the increasing complexity of regional trade.","zh":"工藝生產反映區域貿易日益增加的複雜性。"},{"en":"The increasing complexity of something means it is becoming more detailed, organised, or difficult to manage.","zh":"increasing complexity of something 指某事變得更細緻、更有組織或更難管理。"},{"en":"A school timetable shows increasing complexity when more subjects, clubs, and room changes are added.","zh":"當更多科目、學會和課室調動加入，學校時間表就顯示日益增加的複雜性。"},{"en":"Trade becomes more complex when goods, routes, buyers, and measurements multiply.","zh":"當貨物、路線、買家和度量增加，貿易會變得更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a process becoming less simple over time.","zh":"這個短語描述某過程隨時間變得不再簡單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"regional distribution","meaning":"區域分銷","examples":[{"en":"Regional distribution systems created demand for standard vessels.","zh":"區域分銷系統創造了對標準器皿的需求。"},{"en":"Regional distribution is the movement of goods across an area or region.","zh":"regional distribution 指貨物在一個地區內的流動和分配。"},{"en":"A bakery with regional distribution sends bread to shops in several towns.","zh":"具有區域分銷的麵包店會把麵包送到幾個城鎮的商店。"},{"en":"Distribution systems need containers that can be counted, carried, and trusted by traders.","zh":"分銷系統需要商人能點算、搬運和信任的容器。"},{"en":"This phrase connects local production with wider movement of goods.","zh":"這個短語把本地生產與更廣泛的貨物流動連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"exchange systems","meaning":"交易系統","examples":[{"en":"Pottery production supported regional exchange systems.","zh":"陶器生產支援區域交易系統。"},{"en":"Exchange systems are organised ways in which people trade goods, services, or resources.","zh":"exchange systems 指人們交換貨物、服務或資源的有組織方式。"},{"en":"A school book exchange is a simple exchange system where students swap used books.","zh":"學校舊書交換是一個簡單交易系統，學生互換二手書。"},{"en":"Standard containers make exchange systems easier because quantities become clearer.","zh":"標準容器令交易系統更容易，因為數量變得更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trade networks rather than one isolated sale.","zh":"這個短語描述貿易網絡，而不是單一買賣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"full-time craftsmen","meaning":"全職工匠","examples":[{"en":"The potters may have worked as full-time craftsmen.","zh":"陶工可能以全職工匠身份工作。"},{"en":"Full-time craftsmen are skilled workers whose main job is their craft.","zh":"full-time craftsmen 指以某工藝作主要工作的熟練工人。"},{"en":"A full-time jeweller spends the working day designing, making, and repairing jewellery.","zh":"全職珠寶匠會在工作日設計、製作和修理珠寶。"},{"en":"Full-time craft work becomes possible when there is enough demand to support the worker.","zh":"當需求足以支持工人生活，全職工藝工作才變得可行。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts professional makers with people who make things only occasionally.","zh":"這個短語把專業製作者與偶爾製作物品的人作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"work permanently in","meaning":"長期從事……","examples":[{"en":"They may have worked permanently in pottery manufacture.","zh":"他們可能長期從事陶器製造。"},{"en":"To work permanently in a field means to do that work as a regular long-term occupation.","zh":"work permanently in a field 指把某工作作為長期固定職業。"},{"en":"A teacher works permanently in education if teaching is their main career.","zh":"如果教學是主要職業，老師就是長期從事教育工作。"},{"en":"Permanent work in pottery suggests steady demand and specialised skills.","zh":"長期從事陶器製造暗示穩定需求和專門技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing employment rather than occasional help.","zh":"這個短語描述持續職業，而不是偶爾幫忙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"high production-rate craft","meaning":"高產量工藝","examples":[{"en":"Pottery manufacture was a high production-rate craft.","zh":"陶器製造是一種高產量工藝。"},{"en":"A high production-rate craft is a craft that can produce many items in a short time.","zh":"high production-rate craft 指能在短時間內製造大量物件的工藝。"},{"en":"A workshop making hundreds of lunch boxes each week has a high production rate.","zh":"每週製作數百個飯盒的工場具有高產量。"},{"en":"High production rates are needed when many households or traders require the same goods.","zh":"當許多家庭或商人需要同類貨品，就需要高產量。"},{"en":"This phrase combines craft skill with large output.","zh":"這個短語把工藝技能與大量產出結合起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"support themselves entirely from","meaning":"完全依靠……維生","examples":[{"en":"The craftsmen may have supported themselves entirely from their work.","zh":"工匠可能完全依靠自己的工作維生。"},{"en":"To support themselves entirely from something means to earn enough from it to live on.","zh":"support themselves entirely from something 指靠某事賺取足夠收入生活。"},{"en":"A musician supports herself entirely from performances if she pays all bills with concert income.","zh":"如果音樂家用演出收入支付所有開支，她就是完全依靠表演維生。"},{"en":"Craftsmen can do this only when buyers regularly pay for their products.","zh":"只有買家定期購買產品，工匠才可以這樣維生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes full financial dependence on one activity.","zh":"這個短語描述在經濟上完全依賴某活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"proceeds of their craft","meaning":"工藝所得收入","examples":[{"en":"The potters lived on the proceeds of their craft.","zh":"陶工靠其工藝所得收入生活。"},{"en":"The proceeds of a craft are the money or goods earned from selling the products of that craft.","zh":"proceeds of a craft 指出售該工藝產品所得的金錢或貨物。"},{"en":"A baker may live on the proceeds of selling bread and cakes.","zh":"麵包師可能靠賣麵包和蛋糕所得收入生活。"},{"en":"If craft proceeds are steady, a worker can specialise instead of farming for food.","zh":"如果工藝收入穩定，工人可以專門從事工藝，而不必種田自給。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to income from skilled work.","zh":"這個短語指熟練工作帶來的收入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in view of the above","meaning":"鑑於上述情況","examples":[{"en":"In view of the above, pottery may have been mass-produced.","zh":"鑑於上述情況，陶器可能曾被大量生產。"},{"en":"In view of the above means considering the evidence or points already mentioned.","zh":"in view of the above 指考慮到前面已提及的證據或觀點。"},{"en":"In view of the above, a teacher may decide that students need another revision lesson.","zh":"鑑於上述情況，老師可能決定學生需要另一節溫習課。"},{"en":"This phrase links a conclusion to earlier evidence.","zh":"這個短語把結論與較早證據連起來。"},{"en":"It is formal and useful in academic writing.","zh":"它較正式，適合學術寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"speak in terms of","meaning":"從……角度來說","examples":[{"en":"Researchers can speak in terms of organised mass production.","zh":"研究者可以從有組織的大量生產角度來說。"},{"en":"To speak in terms of something means to describe or understand an issue using that idea.","zh":"speak in terms of something 指用某概念來描述或理解一個議題。"},{"en":"A teacher may speak in terms of effort rather than talent when discussing improvement.","zh":"老師討論進步時，可能從努力而非天分角度來說。"},{"en":"Using a particular term shapes how people understand evidence.","zh":"使用某個術語會塑造人們如何理解證據。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the framework used to discuss a topic.","zh":"這個短語引出討論某主題所用的框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"mass-produced pottery","meaning":"大量生產的陶器","examples":[{"en":"Akrotiri may have had mass-produced pottery by 1500 BC.","zh":"到公元前1500年，Akrotiri 可能已有大量生產的陶器。"},{"en":"Mass-produced pottery is pottery made in large quantities, often with repeated standard forms.","zh":"mass-produced pottery 指大量製造、通常具有重複標準形式的陶器。"},{"en":"A factory today may make mass-produced cups that look almost identical.","zh":"今日工廠可能製造看起來幾乎相同的大量生產杯子。"},{"en":"Mass production helps meet wide demand but may require organised labour and standard measurements.","zh":"大量生產有助滿足廣泛需求，但可能需要有組織勞動和標準度量。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts large-scale output with one-off handmade pieces.","zh":"這個短語把大規模產出與一次性手製作品作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"organised workshops","meaning":"有組織的工場","examples":[{"en":"The evidence suggests the existence of organised workshops.","zh":"證據暗示有組織的工場存在。"},{"en":"Organised workshops are workspaces where production is planned and divided among workers.","zh":"organised workshops 指生產經過規劃並在工人之間分工的工作空間。"},{"en":"A repair workshop is organised when each worker handles a clear task and tools are stored properly.","zh":"如果維修工場每名工人負責清楚任務，工具亦妥善存放，該工場就是有組織的。"},{"en":"Organisation helps workshops produce goods faster and with fewer mistakes.","zh":"組織良好有助工場更快生產貨物並減少錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a structured workplace rather than casual home production.","zh":"這個短語暗示結構化工作場所，而不是隨意家庭生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"remain an open question","meaning":"仍是未有定論的問題","examples":[{"en":"How pottery production was organised remains an open question.","zh":"陶器生產如何組織仍是未有定論的問題。"},{"en":"To remain an open question means to still be uncertain and not fully answered.","zh":"remain an open question 指某事仍不確定，尚未完全得到解答。"},{"en":"Why some students improve faster than others may remain an open question without more data.","zh":"如果沒有更多數據，為何有些學生進步較快仍可能是未有定論的問題。"},{"en":"Open questions invite further research because current evidence is incomplete.","zh":"未有定論的問題需要進一步研究，因為現有證據不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies something scholars still need to investigate.","zh":"這個短語指出學者仍需調查的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"documentary evidence","meaning":"文獻證據","examples":[{"en":"There is no real documentary evidence about the workshops.","zh":"關於這些工場並沒有真正的文獻證據。"},{"en":"Documentary evidence is information from written records, official documents, or inscriptions.","zh":"documentary evidence 指來自文字記錄、官方文件或銘文的資料。"},{"en":"A school receipt can be documentary evidence that a fee was paid.","zh":"學校收據可以作為已繳費的文獻證據。"},{"en":"Without documentary evidence, researchers must rely more heavily on physical objects.","zh":"沒有文獻證據時，研究者必須更依賴實體物件。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to written proof, not television documentaries.","zh":"這個短語指書面證明，而不是電視紀錄片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"entire knowledge","meaning":"全部知識","examples":[{"en":"Our entire knowledge comes from the ceramic material itself.","zh":"我們的全部知識來自陶器材料本身。"},{"en":"Entire knowledge means all the information people have about a topic.","zh":"entire knowledge 指人們對某主題擁有的全部資訊。"},{"en":"If a teacher loses the lesson record, her entire knowledge of attendance may come from students’ messages.","zh":"如果老師遺失課堂記錄，她對出席情況的全部了解可能來自學生訊息。"},{"en":"When knowledge comes from one source only, conclusions must be careful.","zh":"當知識只來自一種來源，結論必須謹慎。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that no other evidence is available.","zh":"這個短語強調沒有其他證據可用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ceramic material","meaning":"陶器材料","examples":[{"en":"Researchers must rely on the ceramic material itself.","zh":"研究者必須依靠陶器材料本身。"},{"en":"Ceramic material means the pottery pieces, clay objects, and related fired-clay evidence from a site.","zh":"ceramic material 指遺址中的陶器碎片、黏土物件和相關燒製黏土證據。"},{"en":"A museum curator may study ceramic material to understand ancient cooking and storage.","zh":"博物館策展人可能研究陶器材料，以理解古代烹飪和貯存。"},{"en":"Ceramic material survives well because fired clay can last for thousands of years.","zh":"陶器材料保存良好，因為燒製黏土可以留存數千年。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to physical pottery evidence.","zh":"這個短語指實體陶器證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tentative conclusions","meaning":"初步結論；暫定結論","examples":[{"en":"Only tentative conclusions can be drawn from the surviving pottery.","zh":"只能從保存下來的陶器得出初步結論。"},{"en":"Tentative conclusions are careful conclusions that may change when more evidence appears.","zh":"tentative conclusions 指可能在更多證據出現後改變的謹慎結論。"},{"en":"A doctor may give a tentative conclusion before all test results return.","zh":"醫生可能在所有測試結果回來前給出暫定結論。"},{"en":"Researchers use tentative conclusions when evidence is useful but incomplete.","zh":"當證據有用但不完整，研究者會使用初步結論。"},{"en":"This phrase shows caution rather than certainty.","zh":"這個短語顯示謹慎，而不是確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be drawn from","meaning":"從……得出","examples":[{"en":"Several conclusions can be drawn from the archaeological evidence.","zh":"可以從考古證據得出幾個結論。"},{"en":"To be drawn from evidence means to be reached or inferred based on that evidence.","zh":"be drawn from evidence 指根據證據得出或推斷出來。"},{"en":"A teacher may draw conclusions from students’ mistakes about which grammar point needs review.","zh":"老師可能從學生錯誤中得出哪個文法點需要重溫的結論。"},{"en":"Good conclusions depend on whether the evidence is strong enough.","zh":"好的結論取決於證據是否足夠有力。"},{"en":"This phrase connects evidence with interpretation.","zh":"這個短語把證據與詮釋連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"invention of units of quantity","meaning":"數量單位的發明","examples":[{"en":"The invention of units of quantity was important for trade.","zh":"數量單位的發明對貿易很重要。"},{"en":"The invention of units of quantity means creating standard ways to measure amounts.","zh":"invention of units of quantity 指創造量度數量的標準方法。"},{"en":"Shops need units of quantity such as litres, kilograms, and boxes to sell goods clearly.","zh":"商店需要公升、公斤和箱等數量單位，才能清楚售賣貨品。"},{"en":"Standard units make exchange fairer because buyers and sellers know how much is being traded.","zh":"標準單位令交易更公平，因為買賣雙方知道交易了多少。"},{"en":"This phrase connects measurement with organised commerce.","zh":"這個短語把度量與有組織商業連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"numerical system","meaning":"數字系統","examples":[{"en":"A numerical system was needed to count standard units.","zh":"需要數字系統來點算標準單位。"},{"en":"A numerical system is a way of using numbers to count, measure, and record amounts.","zh":"numerical system 指使用數字來點算、量度和記錄數量的方法。"},{"en":"Students use a numerical system every day when they count marks or calculate prices.","zh":"學生每天點算分數或計算價格時，都在使用數字系統。"},{"en":"Trade requires numbers because people must compare quantities and values.","zh":"貿易需要數字，因為人們必須比較數量和價值。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised counting, not random guessing.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的計算，而不是隨機猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"of capital importance","meaning":"極為重要","examples":[{"en":"Measurement was of capital importance to an exchange-based society.","zh":"度量對以交換為基礎的社會極為重要。"},{"en":"Of capital importance means extremely important or essential.","zh":"of capital importance 指極其重要或不可或缺。"},{"en":"Clear instructions are of capital importance during a fire drill.","zh":"在消防演習中，清楚指示極為重要。"},{"en":"If trade depends on measured quantities, measurement becomes central to fairness and trust.","zh":"如果貿易依賴已量度數量，度量就成為公平和信任的核心。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and stronger than simply saying “important.”","zh":"這個短語較正式，比單純說 “important” 更強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"exchange-geared society","meaning":"以交易為導向的社會","examples":[{"en":"Akrotiri was an exchange-geared society.","zh":"Akrotiri 是一個以交易為導向的社會。"},{"en":"An exchange-geared society is a society strongly organised around trade and exchange.","zh":"exchange-geared society 指高度圍繞貿易和交換組織起來的社會。"},{"en":"A market town can be exchange-geared if many people earn a living by buying, selling, and transporting goods.","zh":"如果許多人靠買賣和運輸貨物維生，市場城鎮可以是以交易為導向的社會。"},{"en":"Such a society needs reliable measures, containers, routes, and trust.","zh":"這類社會需要可靠的度量、容器、路線和信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an economy shaped by exchange rather than only self-sufficiency.","zh":"這個短語描述由交易而不只是自給自足塑造的經濟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in spite of","meaning":"儘管","examples":[{"en":"In spite of the absence of written records, measurement systems existed.","zh":"儘管缺乏文字記錄，度量制度仍然存在。"},{"en":"In spite of means despite or although something is true.","zh":"in spite of 指儘管或雖然某事屬實。"},{"en":"In spite of heavy rain, students still arrived for the exam on time.","zh":"儘管下大雨，學生仍準時到達考試。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast between an obstacle and what still happened.","zh":"這個短語引出障礙與仍然發生之事之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when evidence survives even though we expected difficulty.","zh":"當我們原本預期會有困難但證據仍存在時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"absence of written records","meaning":"缺乏文字記錄","examples":[{"en":"The absence of written records limits our knowledge.","zh":"缺乏文字記錄限制了我們的知識。"},{"en":"Absence of written records means there are no surviving documents or texts about the topic.","zh":"absence of written records 指沒有保存下來的文件或文字談及該主題。"},{"en":"If a school has no attendance records, teachers must rely on memory or messages.","zh":"如果學校沒有出席記錄，老師必須依靠記憶或訊息。"},{"en":"Without written records, archaeologists depend more on objects, buildings, and remains.","zh":"沒有文字記錄時，考古學家更依賴物件、建築和遺骸。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why historical certainty may be limited.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何歷史確定性可能有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"archaeological evidence","meaning":"考古證據","examples":[{"en":"Archaeological evidence reveals the use of measurements.","zh":"考古證據揭示了度量的使用。"},{"en":"Archaeological evidence is physical evidence from past human activity, such as tools, bones, buildings, or pottery.","zh":"archaeological evidence 指來自過去人類活動的實體證據，例如工具、骨頭、建築或陶器。"},{"en":"A broken jar can be archaeological evidence if it shows how ancient people stored food.","zh":"如果破陶罐顯示古人如何貯存食物，它可以成為考古證據。"},{"en":"Archaeological evidence matters when written records are missing or incomplete.","zh":"當文字記錄缺失或不完整，考古證據就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to material clues from the past.","zh":"這個短語指來自過去的物質線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"concepts of measurement","meaning":"度量概念","examples":[{"en":"The inhabitants had formulated concepts of measurement.","zh":"居民已建立度量概念。"},{"en":"Concepts of measurement are ideas about how to count, weigh, or measure things consistently.","zh":"concepts of measurement 指關於如何一致地點算、稱重或量度事物的想法。"},{"en":"Children learn concepts of measurement when they compare litres, centimetres, and kilograms.","zh":"兒童比較公升、厘米和公斤時，就是在學習度量概念。"},{"en":"Trade becomes easier when people share the same measurement concepts.","zh":"當人們共享相同度量概念，貿易會更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the thinking behind standard units.","zh":"這個短語描述標準單位背後的思維。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"both of weight and number","meaning":"重量和數量兩方面","examples":[{"en":"The measurements concerned both weight and number.","zh":"這些度量涉及重量和數量兩方面。"},{"en":"Both of weight and number means involving how heavy things are and how many units there are.","zh":"both of weight and number 指涉及物件有多重以及有多少單位。"},{"en":"A shopkeeper needs both weight and number when selling apples by kilogram and by piece.","zh":"店主按公斤和按個出售蘋果時，就需要重量和數量兩方面。"},{"en":"Trade can require different forms of measurement depending on the goods.","zh":"貿易可能因貨品不同而需要不同形式的度量。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that measurement was not limited to one method.","zh":"這個短語顯示度量不只限於一種方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be formulated","meaning":"被建立；被制定","examples":[{"en":"Concepts of measurement had already been formulated.","zh":"度量概念已經被建立。"},{"en":"To be formulated means to be created, developed, or clearly worked out.","zh":"be formulated 指被創造、發展或清楚構思出來。"},{"en":"A school rule must be formulated clearly before teachers can apply it fairly.","zh":"校規必須清楚制定，老師才能公平執行。"},{"en":"Ideas become useful when they are formulated into shared systems or rules.","zh":"當想法被制定成共享制度或規則，它們就變得有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the development of an idea into a clearer form.","zh":"這個短語描述想法發展成較清楚形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"standard measures","meaning":"標準度量單位","examples":[{"en":"Standard measures may have been in operation.","zh":"標準度量單位可能已經在使用。"},{"en":"Standard measures are agreed units used to measure quantity, weight, volume, or size.","zh":"standard measures 指用來量度數量、重量、容量或尺寸的共同認可單位。"},{"en":"Litres and kilograms are standard measures used in modern shops.","zh":"公升和公斤是現代商店使用的標準度量單位。"},{"en":"Standard measures reduce confusion because buyers and sellers use the same system.","zh":"標準度量單位減少混亂，因為買賣雙方使用同一制度。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to shared measurement units.","zh":"這個短語指共享的度量單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be in operation","meaning":"正在使用；已實施","examples":[{"en":"A system of standard weights may already have been in operation.","zh":"一套標準重量制度可能已經正在使用。"},{"en":"To be in operation means to be working, functioning, or being used.","zh":"be in operation 指正在運作、發揮功能或被使用。"},{"en":"A new bus route is in operation once passengers can use it every day.","zh":"新巴士路線一旦乘客每天可使用，就已投入運作。"},{"en":"A measurement system in operation affects how people trade and record goods.","zh":"正在使用的度量制度會影響人們如何交易和記錄貨物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a system that is active, not just planned.","zh":"這個短語描述活躍運作的制度，而不只是計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be evidenced by","meaning":"由……證明","examples":[{"en":"Standard measurements are evidenced by a series of lead weights.","zh":"標準度量由一系列鉛製砝碼證明。"},{"en":"To be evidenced by something means to be shown or supported by that evidence.","zh":"be evidenced by something 指由某證據顯示或支持。"},{"en":"A student’s effort is evidenced by careful notes, corrections, and regular homework.","zh":"學生的努力可以由仔細筆記、修改和定期功課證明。"},{"en":"Physical objects can evidence systems that were never written down.","zh":"實體物件可以證明從未被文字記錄下來的制度。"},{"en":"This phrase links a claim with the evidence supporting it.","zh":"這個短語把說法與支持它的證據連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"graduated series of","meaning":"按級別排列的一系列……","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists found a graduated series of lead weights.","zh":"考古學家發現一系列按級別排列的鉛製砝碼。"},{"en":"A graduated series of things is a set arranged in increasing or decreasing steps.","zh":"graduated series of things 指按遞增或遞減級別排列的一組事物。"},{"en":"Measuring cups often form a graduated series from small to large volumes.","zh":"量杯常由小到大構成按級別排列的一系列容量。"},{"en":"A graduated series of weights suggests a system for measuring different quantities.","zh":"按級別排列的一系列砝碼暗示一套量度不同數量的制度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordered levels, not random objects.","zh":"這個短語描述有次序的級別，而不是隨機物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lead weights","meaning":"鉛製砝碼","examples":[{"en":"Disc-shaped lead weights may represent standard units.","zh":"圓盤形鉛製砝碼可能代表標準單位。"},{"en":"Lead weights are heavy objects made of lead and used for weighing things.","zh":"lead weights 指用鉛製成、用來稱重的重物。"},{"en":"A market trader may use weights to measure goods on a balance scale.","zh":"市場商人可能用砝碼在天平上量度貨物。"},{"en":"Standard weights make trade more trustworthy because quantities can be checked.","zh":"標準砝碼令貿易更可信，因為數量可以被檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to physical measuring tools.","zh":"這個短語指實體量度工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"disc form","meaning":"圓盤形","examples":[{"en":"The lead weights were made in disc form.","zh":"這些鉛製砝碼製成圓盤形。"},{"en":"Disc form means shaped like a flat round circle.","zh":"disc form 指形狀像扁平圓形。"},{"en":"A coin is usually in disc form because it is flat and round.","zh":"硬幣通常是圓盤形，因為它扁而圓。"},{"en":"Disc-shaped objects are easy to stack, handle, and compare by size.","zh":"圓盤形物件容易堆疊、拿取和按大小比較。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shape.","zh":"這個短語描述形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"units of capacity","meaning":"容量單位","examples":[{"en":"The containers provide evidence of units of capacity.","zh":"這些容器提供容量單位的證據。"},{"en":"Units of capacity are standard amounts used to measure how much a container can hold.","zh":"units of capacity 指量度容器能盛載多少的標準單位。"},{"en":"Litres and millilitres are units of capacity used on drink bottles today.","zh":"公升和毫升是今日飲品樽上使用的容量單位。"},{"en":"Capacity units are important when liquids such as oil or wine are traded.","zh":"貿易葡萄酒或食油等液體時，容量單位很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase measures volume, not weight.","zh":"這個短語量度容積，而不是重量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Late Bronze Age","meaning":"青銅時代晚期","examples":[{"en":"The pottery dates from the Late Bronze Age.","zh":"這些陶器可追溯至青銅時代晚期。"},{"en":"The Late Bronze Age is a later part of the Bronze Age, when bronze tools and complex trade were important.","zh":"Late Bronze Age 指青銅時代較後期，當時青銅工具和複雜貿易很重要。"},{"en":"A museum timeline may place pottery, weapons, and buildings in the Late Bronze Age.","zh":"博物館時間線可能把陶器、武器和建築放在青銅時代晚期。"},{"en":"Naming this period helps archaeologists compare objects across regions.","zh":"為這個時期命名有助考古學家跨地區比較物件。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific ancient historical period.","zh":"這個短語指一個特定古代歷史時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"notation of units","meaning":"單位標記","examples":[{"en":"Researchers found the notation of units on containers.","zh":"研究者在容器上發現單位標記。"},{"en":"Notation of units means marks or signs showing measurement units.","zh":"notation of units 指顯示度量單位的標記或符號。"},{"en":"A measuring cup has notation of units such as 100 ml and 200 ml.","zh":"量杯上有 100 ml 和 200 ml 等單位標記。"},{"en":"Unit notation helps users know quantity without guessing.","zh":"單位標記幫助使用者知道數量，而不用猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to written or marked measurement information.","zh":"這個短語指書寫或標示出的度量資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"liquid measure","meaning":"液體度量單位","examples":[{"en":"The markings represented a liquid measure for wine.","zh":"這些標記代表葡萄酒的液體度量單位。"},{"en":"A liquid measure is a standard amount used to measure liquids.","zh":"liquid measure 指用來量度液體的標準數量。"},{"en":"A recipe uses liquid measures when it asks for 500 ml of water.","zh":"食譜要求 500 毫升水時，就是使用液體度量單位。"},{"en":"Liquid measures make trade easier because sellers can state how much wine or oil is being sold.","zh":"液體度量令貿易更容易，因為賣家可以說明出售多少葡萄酒或食油。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to measuring volume of liquids.","zh":"這個短語指液體容量量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"excavated containers","meaning":"出土容器","examples":[{"en":"Marks were found on excavated containers.","zh":"標記在出土容器上被發現。"},{"en":"Excavated containers are vessels that have been dug up from an archaeological site.","zh":"excavated containers 指從考古遺址挖掘出來的器皿。"},{"en":"A museum may display excavated containers after they are cleaned and recorded.","zh":"博物館可能在清潔和記錄後展示出土容器。"},{"en":"Marks on excavated containers can reveal how people measured, stored, or traded goods.","zh":"出土容器上的標記可以揭示人們如何量度、貯存或交易貨物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to containers recovered through excavation.","zh":"這個短語指透過發掘取得的容器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"it must be recognised that","meaning":"必須承認","examples":[{"en":"It must be recognised that function affects the design of pottery.","zh":"必須承認，器皿功能會影響陶器設計。"},{"en":"It must be recognised that means people should clearly accept an important fact.","zh":"it must be recognised that 指人們應清楚接受某個重要事實。"},{"en":"It must be recognised that students need rest as well as homework.","zh":"必須承認，學生需要休息，也需要功課。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to emphasise a point that should not be ignored.","zh":"作者使用這個短語來強調不應被忽視的重點。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an important acknowledgement.","zh":"這個短語引出重要承認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"play a very important role in","meaning":"在……方面擔當非常重要的角色","examples":[{"en":"The function of a vessel plays a very important role in its design.","zh":"器皿功能在其設計方面擔當非常重要的角色。"},{"en":"To play a very important role in something means to strongly influence it.","zh":"play a very important role in something 指強烈影響某事。"},{"en":"Sleep plays a very important role in memory and concentration.","zh":"睡眠在記憶和專注方面擔當非常重要的角色。"},{"en":"If a pot is meant for cooking, its function influences the clay, thickness, and shape.","zh":"如果陶罐是用來煮食，其功能會影響黏土、厚度和形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor is central to a result.","zh":"這個短語顯示某因素對結果非常核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"determine the characteristics of","meaning":"決定……的特徵","examples":[{"en":"Intended use helps determine the characteristics of a pot.","zh":"預定用途有助決定陶罐的特徵。"},{"en":"To determine the characteristics of something means to influence its main features.","zh":"determine the characteristics of something 指影響某物的主要特徵。"},{"en":"A schoolbag’s purpose determines its characteristics, such as size, pockets, and straps.","zh":"書包用途決定其大小、口袋和肩帶等特徵。"},{"en":"A pot’s use affects whether it needs to be strong, light, wide, or heat-resistant.","zh":"陶罐用途會影響它是否需要堅固、輕便、寬闊或耐熱。"},{"en":"This phrase connects function with design features.","zh":"這個短語把功能與設計特徵連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"intended function","meaning":"預定用途","examples":[{"en":"The intended function affects the vessel’s material and form.","zh":"預定用途影響器皿的材料和形式。"},{"en":"Intended function means the purpose something is designed to serve.","zh":"intended function 指某物被設計來服務的目的。"},{"en":"The intended function of a lunch box is to hold food safely until mealtime.","zh":"飯盒的預定用途是安全盛載食物直到用餐時間。"},{"en":"Designers choose materials and shapes according to intended function.","zh":"設計者會根據預定用途選擇材料和形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why an object has a particular design.","zh":"這個短語解釋物件為何有特定設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"choice of clay","meaning":"黏土的選擇","examples":[{"en":"The intended purpose influenced the choice of clay.","zh":"預定目的影響黏土的選擇。"},{"en":"Choice of clay means deciding which type of clay to use for making a vessel.","zh":"choice of clay 指決定用哪種類型的黏土製作器皿。"},{"en":"A potter may choose stronger clay for a cooking pot that must survive heat.","zh":"陶工可能為需要承受高溫的煮食陶鍋選擇較堅固黏土。"},{"en":"Different clays can affect colour, strength, weight, and firing result.","zh":"不同黏土可以影響顏色、強度、重量和燒製結果。"},{"en":"This phrase connects raw material selection with product function.","zh":"這個短語把原材料選擇與產品功能連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"production technique","meaning":"生產技術","examples":[{"en":"Different vessels required different production techniques.","zh":"不同器皿需要不同生產技術。"},{"en":"A production technique is a method used to make something.","zh":"production technique 指用來製造某物的方法。"},{"en":"A bakery uses different production techniques for bread, cakes, and biscuits.","zh":"麵包店製作麵包、蛋糕和餅乾時使用不同生產技術。"},{"en":"Technique matters because shape, strength, and speed depend on how an item is made.","zh":"技術很重要，因為形狀、強度和速度取決於物件如何製成。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the practical method of manufacture.","zh":"這個短語集中於製造的實際方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"large storage jars","meaning":"大型貯存陶罐","examples":[{"en":"Large storage jars were needed to store commodities.","zh":"貯存商品需要大型貯存陶罐。"},{"en":"Large storage jars are big containers used to keep goods such as grain, oil, or wine.","zh":"large storage jars 指用來保存穀物、食油或葡萄酒等貨物的大型容器。"},{"en":"A restaurant may use large storage containers for rice and flour.","zh":"餐廳可能使用大型貯存容器存放米和麵粉。"},{"en":"Large jars are useful when goods must be kept for a long time or in large amounts.","zh":"當貨物需要長期或大量保存，大型陶罐很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes big vessels for storage, not small portable containers.","zh":"這個短語描述大型貯存器皿，而不是小型可攜容器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pithoi","meaning":"大型貯存陶罐（pithoi）","examples":[{"en":"Pithoi were large jars used to store commodities.","zh":"pithoi 是用來貯存商品的大型陶罐。"},{"en":"Pithoi are very large ancient storage jars, often used for goods such as grain, oil, or wine.","zh":"pithoi 指非常大型的古代貯存陶罐，常用於穀物、食油或葡萄酒等貨品。"},{"en":"A museum may display pithoi to show how ancient communities stored large quantities of food.","zh":"博物館可能展示 pithoi，以說明古代社群如何貯存大量食物。"},{"en":"Their size suggests they were meant for storage rather than easy transport.","zh":"它們的尺寸暗示用途是貯存，而不是方便運輸。"},{"en":"This word names a specific type of large ancient jar.","zh":"這個字指出一種特定大型古代陶罐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"store commodities","meaning":"貯存商品","examples":[{"en":"Large jars were used to store commodities such as wine.","zh":"大型陶罐用來貯存葡萄酒等商品。"},{"en":"To store commodities means to keep goods safely until they are used, sold, or transported.","zh":"store commodities 指安全保存貨物，直到使用、出售或運送。"},{"en":"A shop may store commodities like rice, oil, and canned food in a back room.","zh":"商店可能在後房貯存米、食油和罐頭食品等商品。"},{"en":"Good storage prevents goods from spilling, spoiling, or being wasted.","zh":"良好貯存防止貨物洩漏、變壞或浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for practical storage of trade goods.","zh":"這個短語用於商品的實際貯存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be used for transport","meaning":"用於運輸","examples":[{"en":"Smaller containers would have been used for transport.","zh":"較小型容器應該用於運輸。"},{"en":"To be used for transport means to serve the purpose of carrying goods from one place to another.","zh":"be used for transport 指用來把貨物從一地運到另一地。"},{"en":"A backpack is used for transport when students carry books to school.","zh":"學生用背包把書帶到學校時，背包就是用於運輸。"},{"en":"Containers for transport must be strong enough to move and small enough to handle.","zh":"運輸用容器必須足夠堅固以移動，也要小到可以搬運。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on movement rather than storage in one place.","zh":"這個短語集中於移動，而不是固定貯存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"limit the size of","meaning":"限制……的大小","examples":[{"en":"The length of a man’s arm limited the size of a portable pot.","zh":"人的手臂長度限制了可攜陶罐的大小。"},{"en":"To limit the size of something means to set a maximum or restrict how large it can be.","zh":"limit the size of something 指設定最大值或限制某物可以有多大。"},{"en":"A small desk limits the size of the computer monitor a student can use.","zh":"小書桌限制學生可使用的電腦螢幕大小。"},{"en":"Human strength and reach can limit the size of objects meant to be carried.","zh":"人的力量和伸展距離會限制可搬運物件的大小。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a practical constraint with design.","zh":"這個短語把實際限制與設計連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"capacity of about twenty litres","meaning":"約二十公升的容量","examples":[{"en":"A smaller pot had a capacity of about twenty litres.","zh":"較小陶罐有約二十公升的容量。"},{"en":"Capacity of about twenty litres means the container could hold roughly twenty litres of liquid or material.","zh":"capacity of about twenty litres 指容器大約可盛載二十公升液體或物料。"},{"en":"A large water bottle for camping may have a capacity of several litres.","zh":"露營用大型水樽可能有數公升容量。"},{"en":"Capacity matters because traders need to know how much a container holds.","zh":"容量很重要，因為商人需要知道容器能盛載多少。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate volume.","zh":"這個短語給出近似容積。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"maximum someone can comfortably carry","meaning":"某人能舒適搬運的最大重量／容量","examples":[{"en":"Twenty litres was about the maximum a person could comfortably carry.","zh":"二十公升大約是一個人能舒適搬運的最大容量。"},{"en":"The maximum someone can comfortably carry is the largest amount a person can move without too much strain.","zh":"maximum someone can comfortably carry 指某人不會太吃力地搬運的最大分量。"},{"en":"A student’s schoolbag should not exceed the maximum they can comfortably carry.","zh":"學生書包不應超過他們能舒適搬運的最大重量。"},{"en":"If a container is too heavy, transport becomes slow, unsafe, and impractical.","zh":"如果容器太重，運輸會變慢、不安全且不實際。"},{"en":"This phrase links human physical ability with object size.","zh":"這個短語把人的身體能力與物件大小連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"various sizes of container","meaning":"不同尺寸的容器","examples":[{"en":"Various sizes of container represented standard quantities.","zh":"不同尺寸的容器代表標準數量。"},{"en":"Various sizes of container means different container sizes used for different amounts.","zh":"various sizes of container 指用於不同分量的不同容器尺寸。"},{"en":"Shops sell drinks in various sizes of bottle, such as small, medium, and large.","zh":"商店以小、中、大等不同尺寸的瓶子售賣飲品。"},{"en":"Different sizes help buyers choose the amount they need without measuring each time.","zh":"不同尺寸幫助買家選擇所需分量，而不用每次量度。"},{"en":"This phrase connects container size with quantity.","zh":"這個短語把容器尺寸與數量連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"represent standard quantities of","meaning":"代表……的標準數量","examples":[{"en":"The containers represented standard quantities of a commodity.","zh":"這些容器代表某種商品的標準數量。"},{"en":"To represent standard quantities of something means to stand for fixed amounts of that good.","zh":"represent standard quantities of something 指代表某種貨品的固定分量。"},{"en":"A one-litre milk carton represents a standard quantity of milk.","zh":"一公升牛奶盒代表牛奶的標準數量。"},{"en":"Standard quantities reduce confusion because each container signals a known amount.","zh":"標準數量減少混亂，因為每個容器都表示已知分量。"},{"en":"This phrase links physical containers with measured trade units.","zh":"這個短語把實體容器與量度交易單位連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fundamental element in","meaning":"……中的基本要素","examples":[{"en":"Standard quantities were a fundamental element in commercial exchange.","zh":"標準數量是商業交換中的基本要素。"},{"en":"A fundamental element in something is a basic and necessary part of it.","zh":"fundamental element in something 指某系統中基本而必要的部分。"},{"en":"Trust is a fundamental element in teamwork because members depend on one another.","zh":"信任是團隊合作中的基本要素，因為成員互相依賴。"},{"en":"Trade needs standard quantities because people must know what they are giving and receiving.","zh":"貿易需要標準數量，因為人們必須知道自己給出和收到甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies something essential to a system.","zh":"這個短語指出系統中不可或缺的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"function of exchange","meaning":"交易功能","examples":[{"en":"Standard containers supported the function of exchange.","zh":"標準容器支援交易功能。"},{"en":"The function of exchange means the role of enabling goods to be traded or swapped.","zh":"function of exchange 指促成貨物買賣或交換的作用。"},{"en":"Money supports the function of exchange because it lets people buy different goods easily.","zh":"金錢支援交易功能，因為它讓人容易購買不同貨品。"},{"en":"Containers with known capacity help exchange because traders can compare amounts.","zh":"容量已知的容器有助交易，因為商人能比較分量。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how something helps trade work.","zh":"這個短語集中於某物如何幫助貿易運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"handle a commodity","meaning":"處理某種商品","examples":[{"en":"Merchants handling a commodity needed to know its quantity.","zh":"處理某種商品的商人需要知道其數量。"},{"en":"To handle a commodity means to deal with, store, transport, or sell a trade good.","zh":"handle a commodity 指處理、貯存、運輸或出售一種貿易貨品。"},{"en":"A shop assistant handling rice must know the weight and price before selling it.","zh":"店員處理米時，出售前必須知道重量和價格。"},{"en":"People handling goods need clear measures to avoid mistakes and disputes.","zh":"處理貨物的人需要清楚度量，以避免錯誤和爭議。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical management of goods in trade.","zh":"這個短語描述貿易中對貨物的實際管理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"determine easily","meaning":"輕易確定","examples":[{"en":"Merchants could determine easily how much wine they carried.","zh":"商人可以輕易確定自己運載了多少葡萄酒。"},{"en":"To determine easily means to find out something without difficulty.","zh":"determine easily 指毫不困難地查明某事。"},{"en":"A student can determine easily how many pages remain if the chapter numbers are clear.","zh":"如果章節頁碼清楚，學生可以輕易確定還剩多少頁。"},{"en":"Standard containers help traders determine quantities quickly.","zh":"標準容器幫助商人快速確定數量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes simple and reliable calculation or judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單可靠的計算或判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"amount of wine","meaning":"葡萄酒的數量","examples":[{"en":"The number of containers revealed the amount of wine on board.","zh":"容器數量揭示船上葡萄酒的數量。"},{"en":"Amount of wine means the quantity of wine being stored, carried, or sold.","zh":"amount of wine 指正在貯存、運載或出售的葡萄酒分量。"},{"en":"A restaurant checks the amount of wine left before ordering new bottles.","zh":"餐廳在訂購新酒前會檢查剩餘葡萄酒數量。"},{"en":"If each container holds the same volume, counting containers shows the total amount.","zh":"如果每個容器盛載相同容量，點算容器就能顯示總量。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to quantity, not wine quality.","zh":"這個短語指數量，而不是葡萄酒品質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"transport in ships","meaning":"以船隻運輸","examples":[{"en":"Merchants transported wine in ships.","zh":"商人以船隻運輸葡萄酒。"},{"en":"To transport in ships means to move goods by boat across water.","zh":"transport in ships 指透過船隻在水上運送貨物。"},{"en":"Companies transport furniture in ships when goods must cross oceans.","zh":"當貨物需要橫越海洋，公司會以船隻運輸家具。"},{"en":"Sea transport allows large quantities to move farther than people could carry by hand.","zh":"海上運輸讓大量貨物能移動到比人手搬運更遠的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes water-based trade or movement.","zh":"這個短語描述水路貿易或運輸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"capacity of each container","meaning":"每個容器的容量","examples":[{"en":"The capacity of each container was known.","zh":"每個容器的容量都是已知的。"},{"en":"Capacity of each container means how much every vessel can hold.","zh":"capacity of each container 指每個器皿能盛載多少。"},{"en":"A delivery worker can count bottles quickly if the capacity of each container is printed on the label.","zh":"如果每個容器的容量印在標籤上，送貨員可以快速點算瓶數。"},{"en":"Knowing container capacity helps calculate total volume without opening every vessel.","zh":"知道容器容量有助計算總容量，而不用打開每個器皿。"},{"en":"This phrase connects container size with measurement.","zh":"這個短語把容器大小與度量連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"draw a parallel with","meaning":"與……作類比","examples":[{"en":"We can draw a parallel with the modern sale of oil in tins.","zh":"我們可以與現代以罐裝出售食油作類比。"},{"en":"To draw a parallel with something means to compare it with a similar situation.","zh":"draw a parallel with something 指把某事與相似情況比較。"},{"en":"A teacher may draw a parallel between ancient trade and modern supermarkets.","zh":"老師可能把古代貿易與現代超級市場作類比。"},{"en":"Parallels help students understand unfamiliar history through familiar examples.","zh":"類比幫助學生透過熟悉例子理解陌生歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a comparison that clarifies meaning.","zh":"這個短語引入有助澄清意思的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"current practice","meaning":"現行做法","examples":[{"en":"The writer compares ancient vessels with current practice in Greece.","zh":"作者把古代器皿與希臘現行做法作比較。"},{"en":"Current practice means the way something is commonly done now.","zh":"current practice 指現時常見的做法。"},{"en":"Current practice in many schools is to submit homework online.","zh":"許多學校的現行做法是網上交功課。"},{"en":"Comparing current practice with ancient practice can make old systems easier to understand.","zh":"把現行做法與古代做法比較，可以令舊制度更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to present-day habits or methods.","zh":"這個短語指今日的習慣或方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sell oil in tins","meaning":"以罐裝出售食油","examples":[{"en":"Oil is commonly sold in standard-sized tins.","zh":"食油通常以標準尺寸罐裝出售。"},{"en":"To sell oil in tins means to package and sell oil in metal containers of known size.","zh":"sell oil in tins 指把食油包裝在已知尺寸的金屬罐中出售。"},{"en":"A grocery store may sell olive oil in tins of one litre or five litres.","zh":"雜貨店可能以一公升或五公升罐裝出售橄欖油。"},{"en":"Standard tins help customers know how much oil they are buying.","zh":"標準罐幫助顧客知道自己買了多少食油。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how container size supports trade.","zh":"這個短語顯示容器尺寸如何支援貿易。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be indicative of","meaning":"顯示；反映……","examples":[{"en":"The shape of a vessel may be indicative of its contents.","zh":"器皿形狀可能顯示其內容物。"},{"en":"To be indicative of something means to suggest or show it.","zh":"be indicative of something 指暗示、顯示或反映某事。"},{"en":"A student’s tired face may be indicative of lack of sleep.","zh":"學生疲倦的臉色可能反映睡眠不足。"},{"en":"If a vessel shape is linked with one product, traders can recognise its contents quickly.","zh":"如果某器皿形狀與某產品相關，商人便能快速辨認其內容物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence that points to a likely meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述指向可能意思的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"commodity contained","meaning":"所盛載的商品","examples":[{"en":"The vessel’s decoration could indicate the commodity contained inside.","zh":"器皿裝飾可以顯示內裡所盛載的商品。"},{"en":"Commodity contained means the goods or product held inside a container.","zh":"commodity contained 指容器內盛載的貨物或產品。"},{"en":"A label on a bottle tells customers the commodity contained inside it.","zh":"瓶上的標籤告訴顧客其中所盛載的商品。"},{"en":"Decoration or shape may help identify contents when written labels are absent.","zh":"當沒有文字標籤，裝飾或形狀可能幫助辨認內容物。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what the container holds.","zh":"這個短語集中於容器盛載的是甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"individual transactions","meaning":"個別交易","examples":[{"en":"Individual transactions involved different quantities of goods.","zh":"個別交易涉及不同數量的貨物。"},{"en":"Individual transactions are separate acts of buying, selling, or exchanging goods.","zh":"individual transactions 指個別買入、出售或交換貨物的行為。"},{"en":"Each purchase at a market stall is an individual transaction.","zh":"在市場攤檔的每次購買都是一筆個別交易。"},{"en":"Different transactions may require different container sizes depending on the amount sold.","zh":"不同交易可能因出售分量不同而需要不同容器尺寸。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to separate deals rather than trade as a whole.","zh":"這個短語指一筆一筆交易，而不是整體貿易。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a given commodity","meaning":"某一指定商品","examples":[{"en":"Traders needed several vessel sizes for a given commodity.","zh":"商人需要幾種容器尺寸來盛載某一指定商品。"},{"en":"A given commodity means one particular good being discussed.","zh":"a given commodity 指正在討論的某一特定貨品。"},{"en":"For a given drink, a shop may offer small, medium, and large bottles.","zh":"對某一種飲品，商店可能提供小、中、大瓶裝。"},{"en":"Different container sizes allow the same commodity to be sold in different quantities.","zh":"不同容器尺寸讓同一商品能以不同數量出售。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows attention to one specific product.","zh":"這個短語把注意力收窄到一種特定產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a range of standardised types","meaning":"一系列標準化類型","examples":[{"en":"A range of standardised types was needed for trade.","zh":"貿易需要一系列標準化類型。"},{"en":"A range of standardised types means several fixed and recognised forms or sizes.","zh":"range of standardised types 指幾種固定並被認可的形式或尺寸。"},{"en":"A café may use a range of standardised cup sizes: small, regular, and large.","zh":"咖啡店可能使用一系列標準化杯尺寸：小杯、普通杯和大杯。"},{"en":"Standardised types help buyers and sellers avoid confusion about quantity.","zh":"標準化類型幫助買賣雙方避免對數量產生混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase combines variety with consistency.","zh":"這個短語結合多樣性和一致性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"meet traders’ requirements","meaning":"滿足商人的需求","examples":[{"en":"Different vessel sizes were produced to meet traders’ requirements.","zh":"不同器皿尺寸被生產出來，以滿足商人的需求。"},{"en":"To meet traders’ requirements means to satisfy what merchants need for buying, selling, or transport.","zh":"meet traders’ requirements 指滿足商人在買賣或運輸上的需要。"},{"en":"A delivery company meets traders’ requirements by offering boxes in different sizes.","zh":"物流公司透過提供不同尺寸盒子來滿足商人的需求。"},{"en":"If traders need clear quantities, producers may make standard containers.","zh":"如果商人需要清楚數量，生產者可能製作標準容器。"},{"en":"This phrase links production choices with commercial needs.","zh":"這個短語把生產選擇與商業需要連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reconstruct systems of capacity","meaning":"重建容量制度","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists try to reconstruct systems of capacity from pottery.","zh":"考古學家嘗試從陶器重建容量制度。"},{"en":"To reconstruct systems of capacity means to rebuild an understanding of old volume-measurement systems.","zh":"reconstruct systems of capacity 指重新建立對古代容量度量制度的理解。"},{"en":"A teacher may reconstruct a lost timetable by using students’ notes and room bookings.","zh":"老師可能利用學生筆記和課室預約重建遺失的時間表。"},{"en":"Pottery volumes help researchers infer how ancient people measured liquids or goods.","zh":"陶器容積幫助研究者推斷古人如何量度液體或貨物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rebuilding a system from surviving evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述從保存證據重建一套制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"measure the volume of","meaning":"量度……的容積","examples":[{"en":"Researchers measure the volume of excavated pottery.","zh":"研究者量度出土陶器的容積。"},{"en":"To measure the volume of something means to find out how much space it can hold.","zh":"measure the volume of something 指找出某物能盛載多少空間。"},{"en":"A student can measure the volume of a bottle by filling it with water.","zh":"學生可以把水注入瓶中來量度瓶子的容積。"},{"en":"Measuring volume helps identify whether containers were made for standard quantities.","zh":"量度容積有助識別容器是否按標準數量製作。"},{"en":"This phrase is about capacity, not weight or decoration.","zh":"這個短語關於容量，而不是重量或裝飾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"generous range of tolerances","meaning":"較寬鬆的誤差範圍","examples":[{"en":"A generous range of tolerances must be allowed.","zh":"必須容許較寬鬆的誤差範圍。"},{"en":"A generous range of tolerances means a fairly wide margin of acceptable error.","zh":"generous range of tolerances 指相當寬的可接受誤差範圍。"},{"en":"A handmade cake may be accepted with a generous range of tolerances because each one is slightly different.","zh":"手製蛋糕可能容許較寬鬆的誤差範圍，因為每個都略有不同。"},{"en":"Ancient pots could vary because potters lacked modern measuring tools.","zh":"古代陶罐可能有差異，因為陶工缺乏現代量度工具。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that exact equality should not always be expected.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們不應總是期待完全相等。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"specific sizes in mind","meaning":"心中有特定尺寸","examples":[{"en":"The potters probably had specific vessel sizes in mind.","zh":"陶工心中很可能有特定器皿尺寸。"},{"en":"To have specific sizes in mind means to plan for particular sizes before making something.","zh":"have specific sizes in mind 指製作前已計劃好特定尺寸。"},{"en":"A carpenter has specific shelf sizes in mind before cutting wood.","zh":"木匠在切木前心中已有特定層架尺寸。"},{"en":"Planned sizes help makers reproduce objects for repeated use or sale.","zh":"計劃好的尺寸幫助製作者重複製作用於使用或出售的物件。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests intention rather than accidental shape.","zh":"這個短語暗示有意圖，而不是偶然形成的形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reproduce them","meaning":"仿製；重現它們","examples":[{"en":"Potters tried to reproduce standard vessel sizes.","zh":"陶工嘗試重現標準器皿尺寸。"},{"en":"To reproduce them means to make the same forms or sizes again.","zh":"reproduce them 指再次製作相同形式或尺寸。"},{"en":"A teacher may reproduce a worksheet so every student has the same exercise.","zh":"老師可能複印工作紙，讓每名學生都有同一份練習。"},{"en":"Reproducing standard sizes helps create consistency across many products.","zh":"重現標準尺寸有助在大量產品之間建立一致性。"},{"en":"This phrase means copying or repeating an existing model.","zh":"這個短語指複製或重複現有模型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"specific type and amount of clay","meaning":"特定種類及分量的黏土","examples":[{"en":"They used a specific type and amount of clay for each pot.","zh":"他們為每個陶罐使用特定種類及分量的黏土。"},{"en":"A specific type and amount of clay means a particular clay kind and measured quantity.","zh":"specific type and amount of clay 指某一種黏土和已量度分量。"},{"en":"A baker uses a specific type and amount of flour to make bread consistently.","zh":"麵包師使用特定種類及分量的麵粉，以穩定製作麵包。"},{"en":"Using the same material and quantity helps makers control size and quality.","zh":"使用相同材料和分量有助製作者控制尺寸和質素。"},{"en":"This phrase connects raw material control with standard production.","zh":"這個短語把原材料控制與標準化生產連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"achieve the exact size required","meaning":"達到所需的準確尺寸","examples":[{"en":"It was difficult to achieve the exact size required every time.","zh":"每次都達到所需的準確尺寸是困難的。"},{"en":"To achieve the exact size required means to make something match the planned size perfectly.","zh":"achieve the exact size required 指使某物完全符合計劃尺寸。"},{"en":"A tailor may struggle to achieve the exact size required if the customer’s measurements change.","zh":"如果顧客身體尺寸改變，裁縫可能難以達到所需的準確尺寸。"},{"en":"Handmade production makes exact size difficult because small variations happen naturally.","zh":"手工生產令準確尺寸困難，因為細微差異會自然發生。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses precision in making an object.","zh":"這個短語強調製作物件時的精確性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"mechanical means of","meaning":"……的機械方法","examples":[{"en":"The potters had no mechanical means of controlling dimensions.","zh":"陶工沒有控制尺寸的機械方法。"},{"en":"Mechanical means of doing something are machine-based methods or tools used to do it.","zh":"mechanical means of doing something 指用機器或機械工具做某事的方法。"},{"en":"A factory has mechanical means of cutting paper evenly, unlike someone using scissors by hand.","zh":"工廠有機械方法把紙切齊，不像人手用剪刀剪。"},{"en":"Without mechanical means, workers depend more on skill and judgement.","zh":"沒有機械方法時，工人更依賴技術和判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts machine control with manual craft.","zh":"這個短語把機器控制與手工技藝作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"regulate symmetry","meaning":"調節對稱度","examples":[{"en":"Modern instruments can regulate symmetry more precisely.","zh":"現代工具可以更精確地調節對稱度。"},{"en":"To regulate symmetry means to control how evenly balanced the two sides or parts of something are.","zh":"regulate symmetry 指控制某物兩邊或各部分是否均衡。"},{"en":"A graphic design app can regulate symmetry when making a logo.","zh":"圖像設計應用程式製作標誌時可以調節對稱度。"},{"en":"Better tools reduce uneven shapes by helping makers check balance and proportion.","zh":"更好的工具透過幫助製作者檢查平衡和比例來減少不均形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on controlling evenness in form.","zh":"這個短語集中於控制形態上的均衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"wall thickness","meaning":"器壁厚度","examples":[{"en":"Variations in wall thickness affected the vessel’s capacity.","zh":"器壁厚度的差異影響器皿容量。"},{"en":"Wall thickness means how thick the sides of a container are.","zh":"wall thickness 指容器側壁有多厚。"},{"en":"A mug with thick walls may hold less coffee than a thinner mug of the same outer size.","zh":"外形相同但器壁較厚的杯，可能比薄壁杯盛載較少咖啡。"},{"en":"If a pot’s walls are thicker, its inside space becomes smaller.","zh":"如果陶罐器壁較厚，內部空間就會變小。"},{"en":"This phrase links container structure with capacity.","zh":"這個短語把容器結構與容量連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"more skilled than others","meaning":"比其他人更熟練","examples":[{"en":"Some potters would have been more skilled than others.","zh":"有些陶工應該比其他人更熟練。"},{"en":"More skilled than others means having better ability or technique than some other people.","zh":"more skilled than others 指比另一些人有更好的能力或技術。"},{"en":"In a class, some students are more skilled than others at drawing graphs neatly.","zh":"在班上，有些學生比其他人更擅長整齊地畫圖表。"},{"en":"Skill differences can produce differences in shape, size, and finish.","zh":"技術差異可以造成形狀、尺寸和表面處理上的差異。"},{"en":"This phrase compares levels of ability.","zh":"這個短語比較能力水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"variations in the repetition of","meaning":"重複製作……時出現的差異","examples":[{"en":"Variations occurred in the repetition of standard types.","zh":"重複製作標準類型時出現了差異。"},{"en":"Variations in the repetition of something are small differences that appear when the same thing is made again and again.","zh":"variations in the repetition of something 指反覆製作同一事物時出現的小差異。"},{"en":"Handmade cookies may show variations in the repetition of the same recipe.","zh":"手製曲奇即使用同一食譜，重複製作時也可能出現差異。"},{"en":"Repeated production can still produce differences if tools and hands are not perfectly precise.","zh":"如果工具和人手不完全精確，重複生產仍可能產生差異。"},{"en":"This phrase describes imperfect consistency.","zh":"這個短語描述不完美的一致性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unforeseen circumstances","meaning":"無法預見的情況","examples":[{"en":"Unforeseen circumstances could affect the finished vessel.","zh":"無法預見的情況可能影響成品器皿。"},{"en":"Unforeseen circumstances are unexpected situations that were not planned for.","zh":"unforeseen circumstances 指未能預先計劃到的意外情況。"},{"en":"A school trip may be delayed by unforeseen circumstances such as sudden heavy rain.","zh":"學校旅行可能因突如其來的大雨等無法預見情況而延誤。"},{"en":"In pottery, small accidents during shaping can change the final size or form.","zh":"在製陶過程中，塑形時的小意外可以改變最終尺寸或形態。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why plans do not always produce perfect results.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何計劃不一定產生完美結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"throwing process","meaning":"拉坯過程","examples":[{"en":"Problems could occur during the throwing process.","zh":"拉坯過程中可能出現問題。"},{"en":"The throwing process is the shaping of clay on a potter’s wheel.","zh":"throwing process 指在陶輪上塑造黏土的過程。"},{"en":"In a pottery class, students learn the throwing process by centring clay and forming a bowl.","zh":"在陶藝課中，學生透過把黏土置中並塑成碗來學習拉坯過程。"},{"en":"Mistakes during throwing can make a pot uneven, too thin, or too small.","zh":"拉坯時的錯誤可以令陶器不均、太薄或太小。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific pottery-making technique.","zh":"這個短語指一種特定製陶技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"For instance, a piece of grit could damage the rim.","zh":"例如，一粒沙石可能損壞罐口。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance 指例如。"},{"en":"Some students lose marks through small mistakes; for instance, they may forget capital letters.","zh":"有些學生因小錯誤失分；例如，他們可能忘記大寫字母。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to make a general point clearer with a specific example.","zh":"作者使用這個短語，以具體例子令一般觀點更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces evidence or illustration.","zh":"這個短語引出證據或例證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"destroy the entire pot","meaning":"毀掉整個陶罐","examples":[{"en":"The potter did not always need to destroy the entire pot.","zh":"陶工不一定需要毀掉整個陶罐。"},{"en":"To destroy the entire pot means to ruin or discard the whole vessel.","zh":"destroy the entire pot 指毀壞或丟棄整個器皿。"},{"en":"A chef may not need to throw away the entire dish if only one topping is burnt.","zh":"如果只有一種配料燒焦，廚師未必需要丟掉整道菜。"},{"en":"If only the rim is damaged, a potter may cut it off and make a smaller vessel.","zh":"如果只有罐口受損，陶工可能切掉它並製成較小器皿。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts total loss with partial repair.","zh":"這個短語把完全損失與局部修補作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rim","meaning":"罐口；器皿邊緣","examples":[{"en":"A defect in the rim could alter the final size of the pot.","zh":"罐口的缺陷可能改變陶罐的最終尺寸。"},{"en":"The rim is the edge around the opening of a cup, bowl, jar, or pot.","zh":"rim 指杯、碗、罐或陶器開口周圍的邊緣。"},{"en":"A chipped rim on a mug can make it uncomfortable to drink from.","zh":"杯口崩裂會令飲用時不舒服。"},{"en":"If a potter cuts off the rim, the vessel becomes shorter and may hold less.","zh":"如果陶工切掉罐口，器皿會變矮，容量也可能減少。"},{"en":"This word names the upper edge of a container.","zh":"這個字指出容器上方邊緣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"contain a piece of grit","meaning":"含有一粒沙石","examples":[{"en":"The clay in the rim might contain a piece of grit.","zh":"罐口的黏土可能含有一粒沙石。"},{"en":"To contain a piece of grit means to have a small hard grain of sand or stone inside.","zh":"contain a piece of grit 指內部有一粒細小堅硬沙粒或石粒。"},{"en":"A shoe may contain a piece of grit after someone walks on a sandy road.","zh":"人走過沙路後，鞋內可能含有一粒沙石。"},{"en":"Grit in clay can scratch, weaken, or damage a pot during shaping.","zh":"黏土中的沙石可能在塑形時刮花、削弱或損壞陶器。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small impurity inside a material.","zh":"這個短語描述材料中的小雜質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"cut off the rim","meaning":"切掉器皿邊緣","examples":[{"en":"The potter could produce a smaller vessel by cutting off the rim.","zh":"陶工可以透過切掉器皿邊緣製作較小器皿。"},{"en":"To cut off the rim means to remove the upper edge of a vessel.","zh":"cut off the rim 指移除器皿的上方邊緣。"},{"en":"A craft worker may cut off a damaged edge instead of discarding the whole object.","zh":"工匠可能切掉受損邊緣，而不是丟棄整個物件。"},{"en":"Cutting off the rim can save a pot but also reduce its height and capacity.","zh":"切掉罐口可以保留陶罐，但也會減少高度和容量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repair or adjustment during production.","zh":"這個短語描述生產過程中的修補或調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"noticeable external difference","meaning":"明顯的外觀差異","examples":[{"en":"There might be no noticeable external difference between two pots.","zh":"兩個陶罐之間可能沒有明顯的外觀差異。"},{"en":"Noticeable external difference means a visible difference on the outside.","zh":"noticeable external difference 指外部可見的差異。"},{"en":"Two phones may have no noticeable external difference but very different storage capacity.","zh":"兩部手機可能沒有明顯外觀差異，但儲存容量很不同。"},{"en":"Objects can look the same outside while differing in thickness or internal volume.","zh":"物件外面可以看似相同，但厚度或內部容量不同。"},{"en":"This phrase separates outer appearance from hidden features.","zh":"這個短語把外觀與隱藏特徵分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be meant to contain","meaning":"原本用來盛載……","examples":[{"en":"The pots were meant to contain the same quantity.","zh":"這些陶罐原本用來盛載相同數量。"},{"en":"To be meant to contain something means to be designed or intended to hold it.","zh":"be meant to contain something 指被設計或預定用來盛載某物。"},{"en":"A lunch box is meant to contain food, not heavy tools.","zh":"飯盒原本用來盛載食物，而不是沉重工具。"},{"en":"If two vessels are meant to contain the same quantity, their capacity should be similar.","zh":"如果兩個器皿原本用來盛載相同數量，它們容量應相近。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intended capacity or purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述預定容量或用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"differences in capacity","meaning":"容量差異","examples":[{"en":"Similar-looking vessels could have differences in capacity.","zh":"外觀相似的器皿可能有容量差異。"},{"en":"Differences in capacity are differences in how much containers can hold.","zh":"differences in capacity 指容器能盛載多少方面的差別。"},{"en":"Two cups may look similar but have differences in capacity if one has thicker walls.","zh":"兩隻杯可能外觀相似，但如果其中一隻器壁較厚，就會有容量差異。"},{"en":"Capacity differences matter in trade because quantity affects price.","zh":"容量差異在貿易中很重要，因為數量影響價格。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on internal volume, not appearance.","zh":"這個短語集中於內部容積，而不是外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"reach one or two litres","meaning":"達到一至兩公升","examples":[{"en":"The difference in capacity could reach one or two litres.","zh":"容量差異可能達到一至兩公升。"},{"en":"To reach one or two litres means to amount to as much as one or two litres.","zh":"reach one or two litres 指數量多至一至兩公升。"},{"en":"A measuring error in a large water tank could reach several litres.","zh":"大水箱中的量度誤差可能達到幾公升。"},{"en":"Even a small-looking difference can matter when many containers are traded.","zh":"當大量容器被交易，看似小的差異也可能重要。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the possible size of a difference.","zh":"這個短語給出差異可能有多大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"deviation from","meaning":"與……的偏差","examples":[{"en":"In one case, the deviation from the required size was substantial.","zh":"在一個個案中，與所需尺寸的偏差相當大。"},{"en":"Deviation from something means a difference from the expected or standard form.","zh":"deviation from something 指與預期或標準形式之間的差異。"},{"en":"A student’s answer may show deviation from the model structure if it misses the conclusion.","zh":"如果學生答案沒有結論，就可能顯示與標準結構有偏差。"},{"en":"Deviations can occur when production is handmade or conditions change suddenly.","zh":"當生產是手工或情況突然改變時，偏差可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement away from a standard.","zh":"這個短語描述偏離標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"as much as 10–20 per cent","meaning":"高達百分之十至二十","examples":[{"en":"The deviation appears to have been as much as 10–20 per cent.","zh":"這個偏差似乎高達百分之十至二十。"},{"en":"As much as 10–20 per cent means reaching a surprisingly large range of ten to twenty per cent.","zh":"as much as 10–20 per cent 指達到令人注意的百分之十至二十範圍。"},{"en":"A shop discount of as much as 20 per cent can make customers buy more.","zh":"高達百分之二十的商店折扣可以令顧客購買更多。"},{"en":"In container capacity, a 10–20 per cent difference can affect trade calculations.","zh":"在容器容量中，百分之十至二十差異可以影響貿易計算。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the amount is quite large.","zh":"這個短語強調數量相當大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"establishment of regular trade routes","meaning":"定期貿易路線的建立","examples":[{"en":"The establishment of regular trade routes increased the movement of goods.","zh":"定期貿易路線的建立增加了貨物流動。"},{"en":"Establishment of regular trade routes means creating fixed paths used repeatedly for trade.","zh":"establishment of regular trade routes 指建立反覆用於貿易的固定路線。"},{"en":"A delivery company improves service by establishing regular routes between towns.","zh":"物流公司透過在城鎮之間建立固定路線改善服務。"},{"en":"Regular routes make exchange easier because traders know where and when goods can move.","zh":"固定路線令交換更容易，因為商人知道貨物可在何時何地流動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the creation of dependable trade connections.","zh":"這個短語描述可靠貿易連繫的建立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"lead to increased movement of goods","meaning":"導致貨物流動增加","examples":[{"en":"Regular trade routes led to increased movement of goods.","zh":"定期貿易路線導致貨物流動增加。"},{"en":"To lead to increased movement of goods means to cause more products to be transported or exchanged.","zh":"lead to increased movement of goods 指導致更多產品被運輸或交換。"},{"en":"A new railway can lead to increased movement of goods between cities.","zh":"新鐵路可以導致城市之間貨物流動增加。"},{"en":"Better routes lower transport difficulty and encourage trade.","zh":"更好的路線降低運輸困難並鼓勵貿易。"},{"en":"This phrase connects transport systems with higher trade activity.","zh":"這個短語把運輸系統與更高貿易活動連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"consequently","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"Consequently, regular exchanges of goods became possible.","zh":"因此，貨物的定期交換變得可行。"},{"en":"Consequently means as a result.","zh":"consequently 指因此或作為結果。"},{"en":"The bus service improved; consequently, more students arrived on time.","zh":"巴士服務改善；因此，更多學生準時到達。"},{"en":"This word shows that one event happens because of an earlier point.","zh":"這個字顯示一件事因較早提及的情況而發生。"},{"en":"It is useful for explaining cause and effect in formal writing.","zh":"在正式寫作中解釋因果關係時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"regular exchange of","meaning":"……的定期交換","examples":[{"en":"Transport advances allowed the regular exchange of local goods.","zh":"運輸進步使本地貨物的定期交換成為可能。"},{"en":"Regular exchange of something means repeated and organised trading or sharing of it.","zh":"regular exchange of something 指反覆且有組織地交易或分享某物。"},{"en":"A school may organise regular exchange of library books between classes.","zh":"學校可能安排班級之間定期交換圖書館書籍。"},{"en":"Regular exchange becomes easier when people have stable routes and clear rules.","zh":"當人們有穩定路線和清楚規則，定期交換就更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated movement of goods or resources.","zh":"這個短語描述貨物或資源的反覆流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"local, luxury and surplus goods","meaning":"本地、奢侈及剩餘商品","examples":[{"en":"Traders exchanged local, luxury and surplus goods.","zh":"商人交換本地、奢侈及剩餘商品。"},{"en":"Local, luxury and surplus goods are everyday regional products, high-value items, and extra goods beyond immediate need.","zh":"local, luxury and surplus goods 指本地日用品、高價值物品，以及超出即時需要的多餘貨物。"},{"en":"A market may sell local vegetables, luxury jewellery, and surplus grain.","zh":"市場可能售賣本地蔬菜、奢侈珠寶和剩餘穀物。"},{"en":"Different types of goods create different needs for storage, transport, and measurement.","zh":"不同種類貨物對貯存、運輸和度量有不同需求。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the variety of goods involved in trade.","zh":"這個短語顯示貿易所涉及貨品的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"become feasible","meaning":"變得可行","examples":[{"en":"Long-distance trade became feasible because transport improved.","zh":"由於運輸改善，長途貿易變得可行。"},{"en":"To become feasible means to become possible and practical.","zh":"become feasible 指變得可能且實際可行。"},{"en":"Online lessons became feasible when students had stable internet access.","zh":"當學生有穩定網絡，網上課堂變得可行。"},{"en":"A plan becomes feasible when the necessary tools, time, money, or routes are available.","zh":"當所需工具、時間、金錢或路線具備，計劃就變得可行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something changing from difficult to workable.","zh":"這個短語描述某事從困難變成可操作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"as a result of","meaning":"由於……","examples":[{"en":"Trade increased as a result of advances in transport technology.","zh":"貿易由於運輸技術進步而增加。"},{"en":"As a result of means because of something.","zh":"as a result of 指由於某事。"},{"en":"A student may improve as a result of daily reading practice.","zh":"學生可能由於每日閱讀練習而進步。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links a cause with its effect.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接原因與結果。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining why a change happened.","zh":"解釋變化為何發生時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"advances in transport technology","meaning":"運輸技術的進步","examples":[{"en":"Advances in transport technology encouraged wider trade.","zh":"運輸技術的進步鼓勵了更廣泛貿易。"},{"en":"Advances in transport technology are improvements in the tools and methods used to move people or goods.","zh":"advances in transport technology 指運送人或貨物的工具和方法有所改善。"},{"en":"Faster trains are advances in transport technology because they reduce travel time.","zh":"更快的火車是運輸技術的進步，因為它們減少旅行時間。"},{"en":"Better transport allows goods to travel farther, faster, and more reliably.","zh":"更好的運輸讓貨物能更遠、更快、更可靠地移動。"},{"en":"This phrase connects movement with economic development.","zh":"這個短語把移動與經濟發展連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"increased demand for","meaning":"對……日益增加的需求","examples":[{"en":"There was increased demand for standardised exchanges.","zh":"對標準化交易的需求日益增加。"},{"en":"Increased demand for something means more people need or want it than before.","zh":"increased demand for something 指比以前更多人需要或想要某物。"},{"en":"Hot weather can create increased demand for bottled water.","zh":"炎熱天氣可以造成對樽裝水日益增加的需求。"},{"en":"Increased demand often pushes producers to make more goods or improve systems.","zh":"需求增加常推動生產者製造更多貨物或改善制度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rising need or market pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述上升的需要或市場壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"standardised exchanges","meaning":"標準化交易","examples":[{"en":"Standardised exchanges required containers of known capacity.","zh":"標準化交易需要容量已知的容器。"},{"en":"Standardised exchanges are trades carried out using shared measures, units, or agreed forms.","zh":"standardised exchanges 指使用共同度量、單位或認可形式進行的交易。"},{"en":"A shop uses standardised exchange when every bottle is labelled with the same volume and price system.","zh":"當商店每個瓶子都標示相同容量和價格制度，就是使用標準化交易。"},{"en":"Standardisation reduces arguments because both sides understand the quantity being traded.","zh":"標準化減少爭議，因為雙方都理解交易數量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exchange made clear and regular by standards.","zh":"這個短語描述透過標準變得清楚和規律的交換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"inextricably linked to","meaning":"與……密不可分","examples":[{"en":"Standard measurements were inextricably linked to commercial transactions.","zh":"標準度量與商業交易密不可分。"},{"en":"Inextricably linked to something means so closely connected that the two cannot easily be separated.","zh":"inextricably linked to something 指與某事緊密相連，難以分開。"},{"en":"In modern schools, online homework is inextricably linked to internet access.","zh":"在現代學校，網上功課與網絡使用密不可分。"},{"en":"Trade and measurement are closely connected because price depends on quantity.","zh":"貿易與度量密切相關，因為價格取決於數量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very strong relationship between two things.","zh":"這個短語描述兩件事之間非常強的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"commercial transactions","meaning":"商業交易","examples":[{"en":"Standardised containers made commercial transactions easier.","zh":"標準化容器令商業交易更容易。"},{"en":"Commercial transactions are business exchanges involving buying, selling, or trading goods or services.","zh":"commercial transactions 指涉及買入、出售或交換貨品和服務的商業活動。"},{"en":"Paying for lunch at a café is a simple commercial transaction.","zh":"在咖啡店付款買午餐是一項簡單商業交易。"},{"en":"Clear quantities and prices make transactions faster and fairer.","zh":"清楚數量和價格令交易更快、更公平。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to business dealings.","zh":"這個短語指商業往來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"main factors which led to","meaning":"導致……的主要因素","examples":[{"en":"Trade may have been one of the main factors which led to standardisation.","zh":"貿易可能是導致標準化的主要因素之一。"},{"en":"Main factors which led to something are the most important causes behind it.","zh":"main factors which led to something 指造成某事的最重要原因。"},{"en":"Practice and feedback are main factors which led to a student’s improvement.","zh":"練習和回饋是導致學生進步的主要因素。"},{"en":"Identifying main factors helps explain why a change happened.","zh":"找出主要因素有助解釋變化為何發生。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces major causes rather than minor details.","zh":"這個短語引出主要原因，而不是次要細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"standardisation of pottery production","meaning":"陶器生產的標準化","examples":[{"en":"Commerce may have encouraged the standardisation of pottery production.","zh":"商業可能鼓勵陶器生產的標準化。"},{"en":"Standardisation of pottery production means making pottery in more regular and repeated forms or sizes.","zh":"standardisation of pottery production 指以更規律和重複的形式或尺寸製作陶器。"},{"en":"A workshop standardises production when every bowl follows the same basic measurements.","zh":"當工場每個碗都遵循相同基本尺寸，就是把生產標準化。"},{"en":"Trade encourages standardisation because buyers need predictable quantities and forms.","zh":"貿易鼓勵標準化，因為買家需要可預測的數量和形式。"},{"en":"This phrase links pottery-making with organised economic demand.","zh":"這個短語把陶器製作與有組織的經濟需求連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"whole network of","meaning":"整個……網絡","examples":[{"en":"The whole network of production and exchange depended on the regional economy.","zh":"整個生產與交換網絡取決於區域經濟。"},{"en":"The whole network of something means the entire connected system of people, activities, and relationships.","zh":"whole network of something 指由人、活動和關係組成的整個相連制度。"},{"en":"A school lunch programme depends on a whole network of cooks, suppliers, drivers, and staff.","zh":"學校午餐計劃依靠由廚師、供應商、司機和職員組成的整個網絡。"},{"en":"If one part of a network fails, the whole system may slow down.","zh":"如果網絡其中一部分出問題，整個系統可能變慢。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that many connected parts are involved.","zh":"這個短語強調涉及許多相連部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"ceramic production and exchange","meaning":"陶器生產與交易","examples":[{"en":"Ceramic production and exchange were closely connected.","zh":"陶器生產與交易密切相連。"},{"en":"Ceramic production and exchange means making clay goods and trading or distributing them.","zh":"ceramic production and exchange 指製作黏土製品，並交易或分銷它們。"},{"en":"A craft fair connects ceramic production and exchange when potters sell bowls directly to buyers.","zh":"當陶工在工藝市集直接向買家售賣碗，陶器生產與交易便連在一起。"},{"en":"Production grows when exchange systems create steady demand.","zh":"當交易系統創造穩定需求，生產就會增長。"},{"en":"This phrase links making goods with moving them through trade.","zh":"這個短語把製造貨物與透過貿易流動連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"depend on","meaning":"取決於","examples":[{"en":"The production network depended on regional economic conditions.","zh":"生產網絡取決於區域經濟狀況。"},{"en":"To depend on something means to be affected or made possible by it.","zh":"depend on something 指受某事影響或由某事使之成為可能。"},{"en":"A student’s exam result may depend on sleep, practice, and understanding.","zh":"學生考試結果可能取決於睡眠、練習和理解。"},{"en":"Pottery production depends on demand, materials, workers, and trade routes.","zh":"陶器生產取決於需求、材料、工人和貿易路線。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one thing relies on another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一件事依賴另一件事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"regional economic conditions","meaning":"區域經濟狀況","examples":[{"en":"Pottery production reflected regional economic conditions.","zh":"陶器生產反映區域經濟狀況。"},{"en":"Regional economic conditions are the trade, demand, resources, and wealth patterns of an area.","zh":"regional economic conditions 指一個地區的貿易、需求、資源和財富模式。"},{"en":"A town’s job market reflects regional economic conditions such as tourism or factory work.","zh":"城鎮就業市場反映旅遊業或工廠工作等區域經濟狀況。"},{"en":"If regional trade grows, craft production may become more specialised.","zh":"如果區域貿易增長，工藝生產可能變得更專門化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the economic situation across a wider area.","zh":"這個短語描述較大地區的經濟情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reflect the socio-economic structure","meaning":"反映社會經濟結構","examples":[{"en":"The pottery industry reflected the socio-economic structure of Akrotiri.","zh":"陶器產業反映了 Akrotiri 的社會經濟結構。"},{"en":"To reflect the socio-economic structure means to show how society and the economy were organised.","zh":"reflect the socio-economic structure 指顯示社會和經濟如何組織。"},{"en":"A city’s housing pattern may reflect its socio-economic structure by showing rich and poor districts.","zh":"一座城市的住屋模式可能透過富裕和貧窮地區顯示其社會經濟結構。"},{"en":"Craft production can reveal whether workers were specialised, full-time, or connected to trade.","zh":"工藝生產可以揭示工人是否專門化、全職或與貿易相連。"},{"en":"This phrase links material evidence with social and economic organisation.","zh":"這個短語把物質證據與社會和經濟組織連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生為每條題目選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option marked by the right letter.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選出以正確字母標示的答案選項。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students must check whether the answer should be A, B, C, or D.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生必須檢查答案應是 A、B、C 還是 D。"},{"en":"Choosing the wrong letter loses marks even if the student understands the idea.","zh":"即使學生理解意思，選錯字母也會失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in multiple-choice instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於多項選擇題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"items of pottery","meaning":"陶器物品","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about items of pottery excavated at Akrotiri.","zh":"題目問關於在 Akrotiri 出土的陶器物品。"},{"en":"Items of pottery are individual clay objects such as jars, bowls, cups, or fragments.","zh":"items of pottery 指陶罐、碗、杯或碎片等個別黏土物件。"},{"en":"A museum may label each item of pottery with its date and use.","zh":"博物館可能為每件陶器物品標上年代和用途。"},{"en":"Studying many pottery items helps researchers identify patterns in production and trade.","zh":"研究大量陶器物品有助研究者辨認生產和貿易模式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to separate pottery objects.","zh":"這個短語指一件件陶器物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be excavated at","meaning":"在……被發掘出土","examples":[{"en":"Many pottery items were excavated at Akrotiri.","zh":"許多陶器物品在 Akrotiri 被發掘出土。"},{"en":"To be excavated at a place means to be dug up from that archaeological site.","zh":"be excavated at a place 指從某考古遺址被挖掘出來。"},{"en":"Ancient coins may be excavated at the site of an old market.","zh":"古錢幣可能在舊市場遺址被發掘出土。"},{"en":"Where an object is excavated helps researchers understand its original context.","zh":"物件在哪裡出土，有助研究者理解其原本背景。"},{"en":"This phrase links a find with the place where it was discovered.","zh":"這個短語把發現物與其出土地點連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"very little duplication","meaning":"幾乎沒有重複","examples":[{"en":"One option suggests that there was very little duplication among the pots.","zh":"一個選項暗示陶罐之間幾乎沒有重複。"},{"en":"Very little duplication means very few repeated examples or copies.","zh":"very little duplication 指重複例子或複製品很少。"},{"en":"A worksheet has very little duplication if every question tests a different skill.","zh":"如果工作紙每條題目都測試不同技能，就幾乎沒有重複。"},{"en":"Little duplication would suggest variety rather than standardised production.","zh":"幾乎沒有重複會暗示多樣性，而不是標準化生產。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lack of repeated forms.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏重複形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"meet a wide variety of needs","meaning":"滿足各式各樣的需要","examples":[{"en":"The pottery would have met a wide variety of needs.","zh":"這些陶器應能滿足各式各樣的需要。"},{"en":"To meet a wide variety of needs means to serve many different purposes.","zh":"meet a wide variety of needs 指服務許多不同目的。"},{"en":"A community centre meets a wide variety of needs by offering study rooms, sports classes, and elderly services.","zh":"社區中心透過提供自修室、運動班和長者服務，滿足各式各樣的需要。"},{"en":"Different pot types were needed because people cooked, stored, transported, and served goods.","zh":"人們需要不同陶器類型，因為他們要烹煮、貯存、運輸和盛奉貨物。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one set of objects supported many activities.","zh":"這個短語顯示一組物件支援許多活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be imported from","meaning":"從……進口","examples":[{"en":"Some pottery may have been imported from other places.","zh":"有些陶器可能從其他地方進口。"},{"en":"To be imported from somewhere means to be brought in from another place or country.","zh":"be imported from somewhere 指從另一地方或國家運入。"},{"en":"A shop may sell tea imported from Japan or India.","zh":"商店可能售賣從日本或印度進口的茶。"},{"en":"Imported goods can show trade links between regions.","zh":"進口貨品可以顯示地區之間的貿易聯繫。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts goods brought from outside with locally made goods.","zh":"這個短語把外地運入的貨品與本地製造貨品作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"intended purpose","meaning":"預定用途","examples":[{"en":"The intended purpose of many vessels can be inferred from their design.","zh":"許多器皿的預定用途可以從其設計推斷出來。"},{"en":"Intended purpose means the use something was designed for.","zh":"intended purpose 指某物被設計用來做的事。"},{"en":"The intended purpose of a school timetable is to organise lessons clearly.","zh":"學校時間表的預定用途是清楚組織課堂。"},{"en":"Shape, material, and size often reveal what an object was meant to do.","zh":"形狀、材料和尺寸常揭示物件原本用來做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase connects design with function.","zh":"這個短語把設計與功能連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"assumption that","meaning":"……的假設","examples":[{"en":"The question concerns the assumption that specialists produced the pottery.","zh":"題目涉及專家製作陶器這一假設。"},{"en":"An assumption that something is true is a belief accepted before full proof is available.","zh":"assumption that something is true 指在完整證據出現前被接受的信念。"},{"en":"A teacher may question the assumption that quiet students do not understand.","zh":"老師可能質疑安靜學生不明白這一假設。"},{"en":"Assumptions help people start thinking, but evidence must test them.","zh":"假設幫助人開始思考，但必須由證據檢驗。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a belief that may need support.","zh":"這個短語引出可能需要支持的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be partly based on","meaning":"部分以……為根據","examples":[{"en":"The conclusion is partly based on the wide range of vessel shapes.","zh":"這個結論部分以器皿形狀廣泛多樣為根據。"},{"en":"To be partly based on something means that one piece of evidence or reason supports it, but not the only one.","zh":"be partly based on something 指某證據或理由支持某事，但不是唯一根據。"},{"en":"A teacher’s grade may be partly based on homework and partly on tests.","zh":"老師給分可能部分以功課為根據，部分以測驗為根據。"},{"en":"Strong conclusions often come from several sources rather than one fact alone.","zh":"有力結論通常來自多個來源，而不是單一事實。"},{"en":"This phrase shows partial support.","zh":"這個短語顯示部分支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"discovery of kilns","meaning":"窯爐的發現","examples":[{"en":"The discovery of kilns would provide direct evidence of production.","zh":"窯爐的發現將提供生產的直接證據。"},{"en":"Discovery of kilns means finding the ovens used to fire pottery.","zh":"discovery of kilns 指發現用來燒製陶器的爐。"},{"en":"If archaeologists discover kilns near a village, they may conclude pottery was made there.","zh":"如果考古學家在村落附近發現窯爐，他們可能推斷陶器在那裡製造。"},{"en":"Kilns are direct evidence because they are part of the manufacturing process.","zh":"窯爐是直接證據，因為它們是製造過程的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to finding production equipment.","zh":"這個短語指發現生產設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"central location","meaning":"中央位置","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to the central location of workshops.","zh":"該選項提到工場的中央位置。"},{"en":"Central location means a position near the middle of an area or settlement.","zh":"central location 指位於某區域或聚居地接近中心的位置。"},{"en":"A school office usually has a central location so students and parents can find it easily.","zh":"學校辦公室通常位於中央位置，讓學生和家長容易找到。"},{"en":"A central workshop might suggest that production was visible and important to the settlement.","zh":"位於中央的工場可能暗示生產對聚居地可見且重要。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts middle position with edge or peripheral location.","zh":"這個短語把中心位置與邊緣或外圍位置作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"sophistication of decorative patterns","meaning":"裝飾圖案的精細程度","examples":[{"en":"Decorative patterns may show a high level of sophistication.","zh":"裝飾圖案可能顯示高度精細程度。"},{"en":"Sophistication of decorative patterns means the designs are detailed, skilful, and carefully planned.","zh":"sophistication of decorative patterns 指設計細緻、熟練且經仔細規劃。"},{"en":"A handmade bowl with complex repeated shapes shows sophistication in decoration.","zh":"有複雜重複形狀的手製碗顯示裝飾上的精細程度。"},{"en":"Sophisticated patterns may suggest skilled craftsmen or strong artistic traditions.","zh":"精細圖案可能暗示熟練工匠或強大的藝術傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on artistic complexity, not practical function alone.","zh":"這個短語集中於藝術複雜性，而不只是實際功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"wide range of shapes represented","meaning":"所呈現的廣泛形狀","examples":[{"en":"The pottery includes a wide range of shapes.","zh":"這批陶器包括廣泛多樣的形狀。"},{"en":"A wide range of shapes represented means many different forms are present in the evidence.","zh":"wide range of shapes represented 指證據中出現許多不同形式。"},{"en":"A kitchen shop may have a wide range of shapes represented in its cups, bowls, and pans.","zh":"廚具店的杯、碗和鍋可能呈現廣泛形狀。"},{"en":"Many shapes suggest that vessels served many different purposes.","zh":"多種形狀暗示器皿服務許多不同用途。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights variety in form.","zh":"這個短語突出形態上的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete each sentence","meaning":"完成每個句子","examples":[{"en":"Students complete each sentence with the correct ending.","zh":"學生用正確句末完成每個句子。"},{"en":"To complete each sentence means to add the missing part so the sentence becomes full and correct.","zh":"complete each sentence 指加入缺失部分，使句子完整且正確。"},{"en":"In a grammar exercise, students complete each sentence by choosing the right verb form.","zh":"在文法練習中，學生透過選擇正確動詞形式完成每個句子。"},{"en":"Completing sentences checks whether students understand grammar, meaning, and logic.","zh":"完成句子可檢查學生是否理解文法、意思和邏輯。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"correct ending","meaning":"正確句末","examples":[{"en":"Each sentence must be matched with the correct ending.","zh":"每個句子必須與正確句末配對。"},{"en":"A correct ending is the option that completes a sentence accurately in meaning and grammar.","zh":"correct ending 指在意思和文法上準確完成句子的選項。"},{"en":"A student should read the whole sentence before choosing the correct ending.","zh":"學生應先讀完整句，才選擇正確句末。"},{"en":"The wrong ending may sound possible but fail to match the passage.","zh":"錯誤句末可能聽起來可行，但不符合文章。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the right final part of a sentence.","zh":"這個短語指句子的正確最後部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"standard units of weight","meaning":"標準重量單位","examples":[{"en":"The metal discs may provide evidence of standard units of weight.","zh":"金屬圓盤可能提供標準重量單位的證據。"},{"en":"Standard units of weight are agreed measures used to weigh goods consistently.","zh":"standard units of weight 指用來一致稱量貨物的共同認可單位。"},{"en":"Kilograms and grams are standard units of weight in modern markets.","zh":"公斤和克是現代市場中的標準重量單位。"},{"en":"Standard weights make trade fairer because buyers can check how much they receive.","zh":"標準重量令貿易更公平，因為買家可以檢查自己收到多少。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to shared measures of heaviness.","zh":"這個短語指共同使用的重量度量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be in use","meaning":"正在使用","examples":[{"en":"Standard units of weight may have been in use.","zh":"標準重量單位可能正在使用。"},{"en":"To be in use means to be actively used by people.","zh":"be in use 指正被人實際使用。"},{"en":"The old school hall is still in use for exams and meetings.","zh":"舊學校禮堂仍正在用於考試和會議。"},{"en":"If a system is in use, it affects real daily activities, not only ideas.","zh":"如果一套制度正在使用，它會影響真實日常活動，而不只是想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something currently or historically being used.","zh":"這個短語描述某物現在或過去被使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"以……為根據","examples":[{"en":"The assumption could be based on archaeological finds.","zh":"這個假設可能以考古發現為根據。"},{"en":"To be based on something means to use it as the evidence, reason, or foundation.","zh":"be based on something 指把某事作為證據、理由或基礎。"},{"en":"A teacher’s advice may be based on years of classroom experience.","zh":"老師的建議可能以多年課堂經驗為根據。"},{"en":"Strong arguments are based on evidence rather than guesses.","zh":"有力論點以證據而不是猜測為根據。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a conclusion with its support.","zh":"這個短語把結論與支持它的根據連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"collection of metal discs","meaning":"一批金屬圓盤","examples":[{"en":"A collection of metal discs may have served as weights.","zh":"一批金屬圓盤可能曾用作砝碼。"},{"en":"A collection of metal discs is a group of flat round metal objects found together.","zh":"collection of metal discs 指一起發現的一組扁平圓形金屬物件。"},{"en":"A box of coins is a simple collection of metal discs in daily life.","zh":"一盒硬幣就是日常生活中的一批金屬圓盤。"},{"en":"If the discs form different standard sizes, they may have been used for weighing.","zh":"如果這些圓盤形成不同標準尺寸，它們可能曾用於稱重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a group of objects that may reveal a measurement system.","zh":"這個短語描述可能揭示度量制度的一組物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"units of volume","meaning":"標準容量單位","examples":[{"en":"Marks on vessels provide evidence of standard units of volume.","zh":"器皿上的標記提供標準容量單位的證據。"},{"en":"Units of volume are measures used to show how much space or liquid something contains.","zh":"units of volume 指用來顯示某物包含多少空間或液體的度量。"},{"en":"Litres and millilitres are units of volume used on drink bottles.","zh":"公升和毫升是飲品樽上使用的容量單位。"},{"en":"Volume units help traders calculate liquids without measuring each container separately.","zh":"容量單位幫助商人計算液體，而不用逐個容器量度。"},{"en":"This phrase is about capacity rather than weight.","zh":"這個短語關於容量，而不是重量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be provided by","meaning":"由……提供","examples":[{"en":"Evidence of liquid measurement is provided by marks on containers.","zh":"液體度量的證據由容器上的標記提供。"},{"en":"To be provided by something means to be given, supplied, or shown by it.","zh":"be provided by something 指由某物給出、提供或顯示。"},{"en":"Evidence of attendance may be provided by school entry records.","zh":"出席證據可能由學校入閘記錄提供。"},{"en":"Marks on objects can provide evidence when written documents are absent.","zh":"當文字文件缺乏時，物件上的標記可以提供證據。"},{"en":"This phrase links information with its source.","zh":"這個短語把資訊與其來源連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"marks found on","meaning":"在……上發現的標記","examples":[{"en":"Marks found on wine containers indicated units of capacity.","zh":"在葡萄酒容器上發現的標記顯示容量單位。"},{"en":"Marks found on something are signs, scratches, symbols, or labels discovered on its surface.","zh":"marks found on something 指在某物表面發現的符號、刮痕、標記或標籤。"},{"en":"Marks found on a student’s desk may show where a compass was used.","zh":"在學生書桌上發現的痕跡可能顯示曾使用圓規。"},{"en":"Marks can reveal ownership, quantity, use, or measurement.","zh":"標記可以揭示擁有權、數量、用途或度量。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on physical signs discovered on an object.","zh":"這個短語集中於物件上發現的實體痕跡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"sailing ships in use","meaning":"當時使用的帆船","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to the size and type of sailing ships in use.","zh":"該選項提到當時使用的帆船大小和類型。"},{"en":"Sailing ships in use are boats or ships powered by sails that were actually being used at the time.","zh":"sailing ships in use 指當時實際使用、由帆推動的船隻。"},{"en":"A harbour museum may show sailing ships in use during different historical periods.","zh":"港口博物館可能展示不同歷史時期使用的帆船。"},{"en":"The type of ships available can affect how much cargo traders can carry.","zh":"可用船隻類型會影響商人能運載多少貨物。"},{"en":"This phrase connects transport technology with historical trade.","zh":"這個短語把運輸技術與歷史貿易連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"physical characteristics","meaning":"身體特徵","examples":[{"en":"The size of portable containers was limited by human physical characteristics.","zh":"可攜容器的大小受人類身體特徵限制。"},{"en":"Physical characteristics are features of the body, such as height, strength, arm length, or weight.","zh":"physical characteristics 指身體特徵，例如身高、力量、手臂長度或重量。"},{"en":"A chair’s design should consider the physical characteristics of the people who use it.","zh":"椅子設計應考慮使用者的身體特徵。"},{"en":"If workers must carry containers by hand, body size and strength affect container design.","zh":"如果工人必須用手搬運容器，身體大小和力量會影響容器設計。"},{"en":"This phrase connects human bodies with practical limits.","zh":"這個短語把人體與實際限制連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"workmen","meaning":"工人","examples":[{"en":"The physical characteristics of workmen affected what they could carry.","zh":"工人的身體特徵影響他們能搬運甚麼。"},{"en":"Workmen are workers, especially people doing physical or manual jobs.","zh":"workmen 指工人，尤其是從事體力或手工工作的人。"},{"en":"Workmen on a building site may carry tools, bricks, or pipes.","zh":"建築地盤工人可能搬運工具、磚塊或管道。"},{"en":"What workers can carry affects how goods and containers are designed.","zh":"工人能搬運甚麼會影響貨物和容器如何設計。"},{"en":"This word refers to labourers or manual workers.","zh":"這個字指勞動者或體力工人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"intended capacity","meaning":"預定容量","examples":[{"en":"Researchers try to identify the intended capacity of ancient containers.","zh":"研究者嘗試辨認古代容器的預定容量。"},{"en":"Intended capacity means the amount a container was designed to hold.","zh":"intended capacity 指容器被設計來盛載的分量。"},{"en":"A water bottle’s intended capacity may be printed as 500 ml on its label.","zh":"水樽的預定容量可能在標籤上印為 500 毫升。"},{"en":"Identifying intended capacity helps researchers understand trade quantities.","zh":"辨認預定容量幫助研究者理解貿易數量。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on planned volume, not accidental volume.","zh":"這個短語集中於計劃容量，而不是偶然容量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be complicated by","meaning":"因……而變得複雜","examples":[{"en":"Capacity estimates are complicated by variations in pottery manufacture.","zh":"容量估算因陶器製造差異而變得複雜。"},{"en":"To be complicated by something means to become more difficult because of it.","zh":"be complicated by something 指因某事而變得更困難。"},{"en":"A school timetable is complicated by part-time teachers and room shortages.","zh":"學校時間表因兼職老師和課室不足而變得複雜。"},{"en":"Capacity estimates become harder when similar pots have different thicknesses and shapes.","zh":"當相似陶罐有不同厚度和形狀，容量估算會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a factor that makes judgement less simple.","zh":"這個短語引入令判斷不再簡單的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"exact shape and thickness","meaning":"準確形狀和厚度","examples":[{"en":"Similar containers varied in their exact shape and thickness.","zh":"相似容器在準確形狀和厚度上有所不同。"},{"en":"Exact shape and thickness mean the precise form of an object and how thick its walls are.","zh":"exact shape and thickness 指物件的精確形態及器壁有多厚。"},{"en":"Two bowls may look alike but differ in exact shape and thickness when measured carefully.","zh":"兩隻碗可能看似相同，但仔細量度時準確形狀和厚度不同。"},{"en":"Small differences in shape and thickness can change capacity.","zh":"形狀和厚度上的小差異可以改變容量。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on precise physical features.","zh":"這個短語集中於精確的實體特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"agree with the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether statements agree with the writer’s views.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與作者的觀點一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the views of someone means to match what that person thinks or argues.","zh":"agree with the views of someone 指與某人的想法或論點相符。"},{"en":"A reading answer agrees with the writer only if the passage clearly supports it.","zh":"只有文章清楚支持某答案時，它才與作者觀點一致。"},{"en":"Students should not use personal knowledge when judging the writer’s view.","zh":"學生判斷作者觀點時，不應使用個人知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in Yes, No, Not Given tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於 Yes, No, Not Given 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相反","examples":[{"en":"A “No” statement contradicts the views of the writer.","zh":"“No” 陳述與作者的觀點相反。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what that person believes or argues.","zh":"contradict the views of someone 指說出與某人信念或論點相反的意思。"},{"en":"If a passage says pottery was local, a statement saying it was all imported contradicts the writer.","zh":"如果文章說陶器是本地製造，而陳述說全部進口，就與作者觀點相反。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be clear from the text, not based on outside guessing.","zh":"矛盾必須從文本清楚看出，而不是基於外部猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a direct conflict with a stated view.","zh":"這個短語描述與已表明觀點直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Students choose “Not Given” when it is impossible to determine the writer’s view.","zh":"當無法判斷作者觀點時，學生選擇 “Not Given”。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資料作出判斷。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions the potter’s age, it is impossible to say how old he was.","zh":"如果文章從未提到陶工年齡，就無法判斷他幾歲。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when the text gives no evidence.","zh":"當文本沒有證據，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase explains uncertainty caused by missing information.","zh":"這個短語解釋因資料缺失造成的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"plans to excavate","meaning":"發掘……的計劃","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to plans to excavate new areas.","zh":"該陳述提到發掘新區域的計劃。"},{"en":"Plans to excavate are intentions or arrangements to dig and study archaeological areas.","zh":"plans to excavate 指挖掘和研究考古區域的意圖或安排。"},{"en":"A research team may make plans to excavate a newly discovered burial site.","zh":"研究團隊可能制定發掘新發現墓地的計劃。"},{"en":"Excavation plans depend on funding, permission, safety, and research priorities.","zh":"發掘計劃取決於資金、許可、安全和研究優先次序。"},{"en":"This phrase describes future archaeological work.","zh":"這個短語描述未來考古工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"in the near future","meaning":"在不久將來","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether further excavation will occur in the near future.","zh":"該選項問進一步發掘是否會在不久將來發生。"},{"en":"In the near future means soon, but not necessarily immediately.","zh":"in the near future 指很快，但不一定立即。"},{"en":"A school may open a new library in the near future after renovation is completed.","zh":"學校可能在翻新完成後於不久將來開放新圖書館。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a coming time that is relatively close.","zh":"這個短語指相對接近的未來時間。"},{"en":"It is less exact than giving a date.","zh":"它不如給出日期般精確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"evidence concerning","meaning":"關於……的證據","examples":[{"en":"The passage contains evidence concerning pottery production.","zh":"文章包含關於陶器生產的證據。"},{"en":"Evidence concerning something is information or proof about that topic.","zh":"evidence concerning something 指關於某主題的資訊或證明。"},{"en":"A teacher may collect evidence concerning why students missed a deadline.","zh":"老師可能收集關於學生為何錯過限期的證據。"},{"en":"Evidence concerning production can include tools, materials, finished products, and waste.","zh":"關於生產的證據可以包括工具、材料、成品和廢料。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what the evidence is about.","zh":"這個短語引出證據涉及甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"come from written records","meaning":"來自文字記錄","examples":[{"en":"Little evidence about pottery production comes from written records.","zh":"關於陶器生產的證據很少來自文字記錄。"},{"en":"To come from written records means to be based on documents, inscriptions, or texts.","zh":"come from written records 指基於文件、銘文或文本。"},{"en":"A family history may come from written records such as letters and certificates.","zh":"家族歷史可能來自書信和證書等文字記錄。"},{"en":"If evidence does not come from written records, researchers must use objects or physical remains.","zh":"如果證據不是來自文字記錄，研究者就必須使用物件或實體遺存。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies documents as the source of information.","zh":"這個短語指出文件是資訊來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"transporting liquids","meaning":"運送液體","examples":[{"en":"Some containers were designed for transporting liquids.","zh":"有些容器是為運送液體而設計的。"},{"en":"Transporting liquids means carrying fluids such as water, oil, or wine from one place to another.","zh":"transporting liquids 指把水、油或葡萄酒等液體從一地運到另一地。"},{"en":"A delivery worker transporting soup needs a sealed container to prevent spills.","zh":"送貨員運送湯時需要密封容器，以防潑灑。"},{"en":"Liquid transport requires vessels that are portable, strong, and not too heavy.","zh":"液體運輸需要容器可搬運、堅固且不太重。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on moving liquids safely.","zh":"這個短語集中於安全移動液體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"hold no more than","meaning":"容量不超過……","examples":[{"en":"A portable vessel could hold no more than about twenty litres.","zh":"可攜器皿容量不超過約二十公升。"},{"en":"To hold no more than a number means to have a maximum capacity of that amount.","zh":"hold no more than a number 指最大容量為該數量。"},{"en":"A classroom box may hold no more than thirty books before it becomes too heavy.","zh":"課室箱子最多可能只可裝三十本書，否則會太重。"},{"en":"Capacity limits matter when people must carry containers by hand.","zh":"當人們必須手提容器，容量限制很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an upper limit.","zh":"這個短語給出上限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"calculate how much","meaning":"計算有多少……","examples":[{"en":"Merchants could calculate how much wine their ships carried.","zh":"商人可以計算船隻運載了多少葡萄酒。"},{"en":"To calculate how much means to work out the quantity or amount.","zh":"calculate how much 指計算數量或分量。"},{"en":"A student can calculate how much money is needed for lunch by adding the prices.","zh":"學生可以把價格加起來，計算午餐需要多少錢。"},{"en":"Standard container sizes make calculation easier because each unit represents a known amount.","zh":"標準容器尺寸令計算更容易，因為每個單位代表已知分量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finding a total.","zh":"這個短語描述找出總數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"differ by up to","meaning":"差異高達……","examples":[{"en":"Containers intended for equal quantities could differ by up to twenty per cent.","zh":"原本用於相同數量的容器，差異可能高達百分之二十。"},{"en":"To differ by up to a number means to vary by as much as that amount.","zh":"differ by up to a number 指差異最高可達該數值。"},{"en":"Two online prices may differ by up to 20 per cent during a sale.","zh":"促銷期間，兩個網上價格可能差異高達百分之二十。"},{"en":"Large differences can affect fairness when goods are sold by container size.","zh":"當貨物按容器尺寸出售，重大差異會影響公平。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the maximum possible variation.","zh":"這個短語給出可能變化的最大幅度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"regular trading of goods","meaning":"定期商品貿易","examples":[{"en":"Regular trading of goods developed throughout the Aegean.","zh":"定期商品貿易在整個愛琴海地區發展。"},{"en":"Regular trading of goods means goods were exchanged repeatedly and predictably.","zh":"regular trading of goods 指貨物被反覆而可預測地交換。"},{"en":"A weekly farmers’ market creates regular trading of vegetables and fruit.","zh":"每週農墟創造蔬菜和水果的定期商品貿易。"},{"en":"Regular trade needs routes, trust, containers, and shared measures.","zh":"定期貿易需要路線、信任、容器和共同度量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated commerce rather than occasional exchange.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆商業活動，而不是偶爾交換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"general standardisation of quantities","meaning":"數量的普遍標準化","examples":[{"en":"Trade encouraged the general standardisation of quantities.","zh":"貿易鼓勵數量的普遍標準化。"},{"en":"General standardisation of quantities means making amounts more regular across many goods or transactions.","zh":"general standardisation of quantities 指在許多貨物或交易中令數量更規律。"},{"en":"Shops standardise quantities when drinks are sold in 250 ml, 500 ml, and one-litre bottles.","zh":"當飲品以 250 毫升、500 毫升和一公升瓶出售，商店就在標準化數量。"},{"en":"Standard quantities help buyers compare prices and sellers organise stock.","zh":"標準數量幫助買家比較價格，也幫助賣家管理庫存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wider agreement about how much is being traded.","zh":"這個短語描述對交易數量更廣泛的共識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"standardisation of container sizes","meaning":"容器尺寸標準化","examples":[{"en":"The writer discusses the standardisation of container sizes.","zh":"作者討論容器尺寸標準化。"},{"en":"Standardisation of container sizes means making containers in repeated, recognised sizes.","zh":"standardisation of container sizes 指按重複且被認可的尺寸製造容器。"},{"en":"Food shops standardise container sizes when they sell small, medium, and large boxes.","zh":"食品店售賣小、中、大盒時，就是把容器尺寸標準化。"},{"en":"Standard sizes make counting, pricing, and transport easier.","zh":"標準尺寸令點算、定價和運輸更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase connects design consistency with practical exchange.","zh":"這個短語把設計一致性與實際交換連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"look the same from the outside","meaning":"從外觀看起來相同","examples":[{"en":"Some containers looked the same from the outside.","zh":"有些容器從外觀看起來相同。"},{"en":"To look the same from the outside means to have a similar external appearance.","zh":"look the same from the outside 指外部外觀相似。"},{"en":"Two apartments may look the same from the outside but have different layouts inside.","zh":"兩個單位從外觀看起來可能相同，但內部布局不同。"},{"en":"External similarity can hide differences in capacity, thickness, or structure.","zh":"外觀相似可以隱藏容量、厚度或結構差異。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts appearance with hidden internal features.","zh":"這個短語把外觀與隱藏內部特徵作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"vary in capacity","meaning":"容量有所不同","examples":[{"en":"Containers with similar appearances could vary in capacity.","zh":"外觀相似的容器容量可能有所不同。"},{"en":"To vary in capacity means to differ in how much they can hold.","zh":"vary in capacity 指能盛載的分量不同。"},{"en":"Two school bottles may look alike but vary in capacity if one is taller inside.","zh":"兩個學校水樽可能外觀相似，但如果其中一個內部較高，容量就有所不同。"},{"en":"Capacity variation can make trade calculations less exact.","zh":"容量差異會令貿易計算較不準確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes differences in volume.","zh":"這個短語描述容積上的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"instruments used to control","meaning":"用來控制……的工具","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to instruments used to control container size.","zh":"該選項提到用來控制容器尺寸的工具。"},{"en":"Instruments used to control something are tools that help measure, regulate, or check it.","zh":"instruments used to control something 指幫助量度、調節或檢查某事的工具。"},{"en":"A ruler is an instrument used to control the length of a drawing.","zh":"間尺是用來控制圖畫長度的工具。"},{"en":"Without such instruments, handmade products may vary more in size.","zh":"沒有這類工具，手製產品在尺寸上可能有更多差異。"},{"en":"This phrase connects tools with precision.","zh":"這個短語把工具與精確度連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be unreliable","meaning":"不可靠","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that measuring instruments were unreliable.","zh":"該選項暗示量度工具不可靠。"},{"en":"To be unreliable means not to be consistently accurate or trustworthy.","zh":"be unreliable 指不穩定準確或不可信。"},{"en":"An unreliable bus may arrive early one day and late the next.","zh":"不可靠的巴士可能一天早到，翌日遲到。"},{"en":"If measuring tools are unreliable, products may not match the intended size.","zh":"如果量度工具不可靠，產品可能不符合預定尺寸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that cannot be depended on.","zh":"這個短語描述不能依賴的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"unsystematic use of","meaning":"缺乏系統地使用……","examples":[{"en":"The option blames the unsystematic use of different types of clay.","zh":"該選項把問題歸咎於缺乏系統地使用不同種類黏土。"},{"en":"Unsystematic use of something means using it without a clear method, plan, or pattern.","zh":"unsystematic use of something 指在沒有清楚方法、計劃或模式下使用某物。"},{"en":"A student’s unsystematic use of revision notes may lead to repeated mistakes.","zh":"學生缺乏系統地使用溫習筆記，可能導致重複錯誤。"},{"en":"Unsystematic use of materials can produce inconsistent results.","zh":"缺乏系統地使用材料可以產生不一致結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disorderly practice rather than planned variation.","zh":"這個短語描述混亂做法，而不是有計劃的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"result in size variations","meaning":"導致尺寸差異","examples":[{"en":"Differences in production could result in size variations.","zh":"生產差異可能導致尺寸差異。"},{"en":"To result in size variations means to cause differences in size.","zh":"result in size variations 指造成尺寸上的差別。"},{"en":"Using different baking tins can result in size variations among cakes.","zh":"使用不同蛋糕模具可以導致蛋糕尺寸差異。"},{"en":"In pottery, changes in clay amount, wall thickness, or trimming can change final size.","zh":"在陶器中，黏土分量、器壁厚度或修整方式變化都會改變最終尺寸。"},{"en":"This phrase links causes with differences in dimensions.","zh":"這個短語把原因與尺寸差異連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"discard containers","meaning":"丟棄容器","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that potters discarded non-standard containers.","zh":"該選項暗示陶工丟棄非標準容器。"},{"en":"To discard containers means to throw them away or stop using them.","zh":"discard containers 指把容器丟掉或停止使用。"},{"en":"A café may discard cracked cups because customers could cut their lips.","zh":"咖啡店可能丟棄裂開的杯，因為顧客可能割傷嘴唇。"},{"en":"Craftsmen may discard products only when defects make them unusable or unacceptable.","zh":"只有當缺陷令產品不能使用或不能接受，工匠才可能丟棄產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rejecting objects instead of keeping or repairing them.","zh":"這個短語描述拒收物件，而不是保留或修補。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"non-standard size","meaning":"非標準尺寸","examples":[{"en":"A vessel of a non-standard size might still have been used.","zh":"非標準尺寸的器皿可能仍曾被使用。"},{"en":"Non-standard size means a size that does not match the usual or agreed measurement.","zh":"non-standard size 指不符合一般或認可度量的尺寸。"},{"en":"A non-standard school notebook may not fit neatly into a normal folder.","zh":"非標準尺寸的學校筆記本可能不能整齊放入普通文件夾。"},{"en":"Non-standard objects can still be useful if their function is not badly affected.","zh":"如果功能沒有嚴重受影響，非標準物件仍可以有用。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts unusual size with standard size.","zh":"這個短語把不尋常尺寸與標準尺寸作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"main purpose of","meaning":"……的主要目的","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the main purpose of the passage.","zh":"題目問文章的主要目的。"},{"en":"The main purpose of something is its most important aim or function.","zh":"main purpose of something 指某事最重要的目標或功能。"},{"en":"The main purpose of a timetable is to show when and where activities happen.","zh":"時間表的主要目的是顯示活動在何時何地發生。"},{"en":"Finding the main purpose helps students avoid focusing only on small details.","zh":"找出主要目的幫助學生避免只集中於小細節。"},{"en":"This phrase asks what the whole text or activity is mainly trying to do.","zh":"這個短語詢問整篇文本或整項活動主要想做甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"evaluate the quality of","meaning":"評估……的質素","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not simply evaluate the quality of pottery containers.","zh":"文章並不只是評估陶器容器的質素。"},{"en":"To evaluate the quality of something means to judge how good, strong, useful, or well-made it is.","zh":"evaluate the quality of something 指判斷某物有多好、多堅固、多有用或製作多精良。"},{"en":"A teacher may evaluate the quality of an essay by checking ideas, organisation, and language.","zh":"老師可能透過檢查內容、組織和語言來評估作文質素。"},{"en":"Quality evaluation focuses on standard, not necessarily on social meaning or economic context.","zh":"質素評估集中於水平，而不一定是社會意義或經濟背景。"},{"en":"This phrase describes judging how good something is.","zh":"這個短語描述判斷某物有多好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"features of pottery production","meaning":"陶器生產的特點","examples":[{"en":"The passage links features of pottery production to regional developments.","zh":"文章把陶器生產的特點與區域發展連起來。"},{"en":"Features of pottery production are noticeable aspects of how pottery was made, such as standardisation or scale.","zh":"features of pottery production 指陶器製作方式中可注意到的方面，例如標準化或規模。"},{"en":"A report may discuss features of school teaching, such as class size and feedback style.","zh":"報告可能討論學校教學特點，例如班級大小和回饋方式。"},{"en":"Production features can reveal wider changes in trade and society.","zh":"生產特點可以揭示貿易和社會方面更廣泛的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase points to important characteristics of the production process.","zh":"這個短語指出生產過程的重要特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"reflect other developments","meaning":"反映其他發展","examples":[{"en":"Standardisation may reflect other developments in the region.","zh":"標準化可能反映該地區的其他發展。"},{"en":"To reflect other developments means to show or be connected with wider changes happening elsewhere.","zh":"reflect other developments 指顯示或連繫到其他地方正在發生的更廣泛變化。"},{"en":"More online homework may reflect other developments in school technology.","zh":"更多網上功課可能反映學校科技方面的其他發展。"},{"en":"Pottery standardisation may reflect changes in trade, measurement, and economic organisation.","zh":"陶器標準化可能反映貿易、度量和經濟組織上的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase links one visible change to broader background changes.","zh":"這個短語把一個可見變化與更廣泛背景變化連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"outline the development of","meaning":"概述……的發展","examples":[{"en":"One option suggests that the passage outlines the development of pottery-making skills.","zh":"一個選項暗示文章概述陶器製作技術的發展。"},{"en":"To outline the development of something means to give a general description of how it changed over time.","zh":"outline the development of something 指概括描述某事如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"A teacher may outline the development of a student’s writing from simple sentences to full essays.","zh":"老師可能概述學生寫作如何由簡單句發展到完整文章。"},{"en":"An outline gives the main stages without every small detail.","zh":"概述會給出主要階段，而不是每個小細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes summarising progress over time.","zh":"這個短語描述總結隨時間而來的進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"pottery-making skills","meaning":"陶器製作技術","examples":[{"en":"Pottery-making skills varied among individual craftsmen.","zh":"個別工匠之間的陶器製作技術有所不同。"},{"en":"Pottery-making skills are the abilities needed to shape, decorate, dry, and fire clay vessels.","zh":"pottery-making skills 指塑造、裝飾、乾燥和燒製黏土器皿所需的能力。"},{"en":"A beginner in a pottery class learns basic pottery-making skills by forming simple bowls.","zh":"陶藝班初學者透過製作簡單碗來學習基本陶器製作技術。"},{"en":"Better skills can produce thinner walls, smoother shapes, and more regular sizes.","zh":"更好技術可以製作出更薄器壁、更平滑形狀和更規律尺寸。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical craft ability.","zh":"這個短語指實際工藝能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"methods for storing and transporting","meaning":"貯存及運送……的方法","examples":[{"en":"Different vessels provided methods for storing and transporting goods.","zh":"不同器皿提供貯存及運送貨物的方法。"},{"en":"Methods for storing and transporting something are practical ways to keep it safe and move it.","zh":"methods for storing and transporting something 指安全保存和移動某物的實際方法。"},{"en":"Lunch boxes and insulated bags are methods for storing and transporting food.","zh":"飯盒和保溫袋是貯存及運送食物的方法。"},{"en":"Good methods prevent goods from spilling, breaking, spoiling, or being lost.","zh":"好方法可以防止貨物洩漏、破裂、變壞或遺失。"},{"en":"This phrase connects container design with practical movement and storage.","zh":"這個短語把容器設計與實際移動和貯存連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"household goods","meaning":"家居用品","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to household goods in prehistoric societies.","zh":"該選項提到史前社會中的家居用品。"},{"en":"Household goods are objects used in daily home life, such as bowls, tools, mats, or storage jars.","zh":"household goods 指日常家居生活使用的物件，例如碗、工具、蓆或貯存罐。"},{"en":"A family moving house packs household goods like plates, blankets, and cooking pots.","zh":"家庭搬屋時會打包碟、毛毯和煮食鍋等家居用品。"},{"en":"Household goods reveal ordinary routines because they are used for eating, cleaning, storing, and cooking.","zh":"家居用品揭示普通日常，因為它們用於進食、清潔、貯存和烹煮。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to everyday domestic objects.","zh":"這個短語指日常家庭物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"prehistoric societies","meaning":"史前社會","examples":[{"en":"Standard containers were important in many prehistoric societies.","zh":"標準容器在許多史前社會中很重要。"},{"en":"Prehistoric societies are human communities that existed before written historical records.","zh":"prehistoric societies 指文字歷史記錄出現以前的人類社群。"},{"en":"Archaeologists study prehistoric societies through tools, bones, pottery, and settlement remains.","zh":"考古學家透過工具、骨頭、陶器和聚居遺跡研究史前社會。"},{"en":"Because writing is absent or limited, physical evidence is especially important.","zh":"由於文字缺乏或有限，實體證據特別重要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to early human societies known mainly through archaeology.","zh":"這個短語指主要透過考古了解的早期人類社會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 116 - Pottery production in ancient Akrotiri.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 117":[{"front":"recover a damaged reputation","meaning":"挽回受損聲譽","examples":[{"en":"Climate scientists needed to recover a damaged reputation after the controversy.","zh":"氣候科學家在爭議後需要挽回受損聲譽。"},{"en":"To recover a damaged reputation means to win back trust after people have lost confidence in you.","zh":"recover a damaged reputation 指在人們失去信心後重新贏回信任。"},{"en":"A school may need to recover a damaged reputation after several complaints from parents.","zh":"學校在收到多宗家長投訴後，可能需要挽回受損聲譽。"},{"en":"Honest apologies, clear action and better communication can help an organisation recover a damaged reputation.","zh":"真誠道歉、清晰行動和更好溝通可以幫助機構挽回受損聲譽。"},{"en":"A damaged reputation is rarely recovered by silence alone.","zh":"受損聲譽很少能單靠沉默挽回。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"damaged reputation","meaning":"受損聲譽","examples":[{"en":"The scandal left climate science with a damaged reputation.","zh":"這宗醜聞令氣候科學留下受損聲譽。"},{"en":"A damaged reputation is the loss of public respect, trust or confidence.","zh":"damaged reputation 指公眾尊重、信任或信心受損。"},{"en":"A restaurant may have a damaged reputation after customers report poor hygiene.","zh":"餐廳在顧客舉報衛生差後，可能有受損聲譽。"},{"en":"A damaged reputation can lead to fewer customers, less support and more criticism.","zh":"受損聲譽可以導致顧客減少、支持下降和批評增加。"},{"en":"It takes time to repair a damaged reputation because trust is rebuilt slowly.","zh":"修補受損聲譽需要時間，因為信任要慢慢重建。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"it was revealed that","meaning":"據揭露","examples":[{"en":"In 2009, it was revealed that some published information had been inaccurate.","zh":"據揭露，在 2009 年，有些已發表資料並不準確。"},{"en":"It was revealed that means information became known to the public after being hidden or unknown.","zh":"it was revealed that 指原本隱藏或未知的資料被公眾知道。"},{"en":"It was revealed that the shop had charged customers the wrong price for months.","zh":"據揭露，該商店幾個月來向顧客收取錯誤價格。"},{"en":"When it is revealed that an organisation made mistakes, public trust may fall quickly.","zh":"當據揭露某機構犯錯，公眾信任可能迅速下降。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces surprising or damaging information.","zh":"這個短語常引入令人驚訝或造成傷害的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"information published by","meaning":"由……發表的資料","examples":[{"en":"Some information published by the Climatic Research Unit was inaccurate.","zh":"由氣候研究組發表的部分資料並不準確。"},{"en":"Information published by an organisation is material that the organisation has officially released.","zh":"information published by an organisation 指該機構正式發布的資料。"},{"en":"Information published by a school should be clear because parents rely on it.","zh":"由學校發表的資料應該清楚，因為家長會依賴它。"},{"en":"If information published by a company is wrong, customers may make bad decisions.","zh":"如果由公司發表的資料錯誤，顧客可能作出錯誤決定。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who released the information.","zh":"這個短語指出資料由誰發布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Climatic Research Unit","meaning":"氣候研究組","examples":[{"en":"The Climatic Research Unit became involved in a major controversy.","zh":"氣候研究組捲入一場重大爭議。"},{"en":"The Climatic Research Unit is a research body connected with climate data and climate science.","zh":"Climatic Research Unit 指與氣候數據和氣候科學有關的研究機構。"},{"en":"A student reading about climate science may see the Climatic Research Unit mentioned in discussions of climate records.","zh":"學生閱讀氣候科學時，可能在氣候記錄討論中看到氣候研究組。"},{"en":"When a research unit becomes controversial, people may question its methods and data.","zh":"當研究機構捲入爭議，人們可能質疑其方法和數據。"},{"en":"This name refers to a specific institution, not climate science as a whole.","zh":"這個名稱指特定機構，而不是整個氣候科學界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"concerning climate change","meaning":"關於氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"The information concerning climate change had been inaccurate.","zh":"關於氣候變化的資料並不準確。"},{"en":"Concerning climate change means about or related to climate change.","zh":"concerning climate change 指關於或涉及氣候變化。"},{"en":"A teacher may show students a chart concerning climate change and rising sea levels.","zh":"老師可能向學生展示關於氣候變化和海平面上升的圖表。"},{"en":"Inaccurate information concerning climate change can confuse the public and weaken trust.","zh":"關於氣候變化的不準確資料可以令公眾困惑並削弱信任。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in reports or articles.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於報告或文章。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be alleged that","meaning":"據稱","examples":[{"en":"It was alleged that some relevant statistics had been withheld.","zh":"據稱，一些相關統計數據被扣起而未有發表。"},{"en":"It is alleged that means someone claims something happened, but it may not yet be proven.","zh":"it is alleged that 指有人聲稱某事發生，但未必已被證明。"},{"en":"It was alleged that the company ignored safety warnings before the accident.","zh":"據稱，該公司在意外前忽視安全警告。"},{"en":"Allegations can damage trust even before an investigation reaches a conclusion.","zh":"即使調查尚未有結論，指控也可以損害信任。"},{"en":"This phrase should be used carefully because it reports a claim, not necessarily a fact.","zh":"這個短語應小心使用，因為它報道的是聲稱，而不一定是事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"relevant statistics","meaning":"相關統計數據","examples":[{"en":"Some of the relevant statistics had allegedly been withheld from publication.","zh":"據稱，部分相關統計數據被扣起而未有發表。"},{"en":"Relevant statistics are numbers or data that are directly connected to the issue being discussed.","zh":"relevant statistics 指與正在討論的議題直接相關的數字或數據。"},{"en":"In a school survey, attendance rates are relevant statistics when discussing student absence.","zh":"在學校調查中，討論學生缺席時，出席率就是相關統計數據。"},{"en":"Without relevant statistics, people may argue from emotion rather than evidence.","zh":"沒有相關統計數據，人們可能根據情緒而不是證據爭論。"},{"en":"This phrase means useful data, not random numbers.","zh":"這個短語指有用數據，而不是隨機數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be withheld from publication","meaning":"被扣起而未有發表","examples":[{"en":"Some statistics had been withheld from publication.","zh":"有些統計數據被扣起而未有發表。"},{"en":"To be withheld from publication means to be kept back and not released publicly.","zh":"be withheld from publication 指資料被保留，沒有公開發布。"},{"en":"A report may be withheld from publication until the school checks all personal information.","zh":"報告可能在學校檢查所有個人資料前被扣起而未有發表。"},{"en":"If important data are withheld from publication, people may suspect unfairness or secrecy.","zh":"如果重要數據被扣起而未有發表，人們可能懷疑不公平或隱瞞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information being deliberately kept from public release.","zh":"這個短語描述資料被刻意不公開發布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ensuing controversy","meaning":"隨之而來的爭議","examples":[{"en":"The ensuing controversy damaged the reputation of several organisations.","zh":"隨之而來的爭議損害了幾個機構的聲譽。"},{"en":"An ensuing controversy is an argument or public dispute that follows an event.","zh":"ensuing controversy 指某事件之後出現的爭論或公共爭議。"},{"en":"After the exam paper was leaked, the ensuing controversy forced the school to investigate.","zh":"試卷外洩後，隨之而來的爭議迫使學校調查。"},{"en":"An ensuing controversy can grow quickly if people feel facts are unclear.","zh":"如果人們覺得事實不清，隨之而來的爭議可以迅速擴大。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the dispute that comes after a problem is revealed.","zh":"這個短語著重問題被揭露後出現的爭議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"affect the reputation of","meaning":"影響……的聲譽","examples":[{"en":"The controversy affected the reputation of climate scientists in general.","zh":"這場爭議影響了整體氣候科學家的聲譽。"},{"en":"To affect the reputation of someone means to change how people view or trust them.","zh":"affect the reputation of someone 指改變人們如何看待或信任某人。"},{"en":"Poor customer service can affect the reputation of a shop.","zh":"差劣顧客服務可以影響商店的聲譽。"},{"en":"A public mistake can affect reputation even if the organisation later explains itself.","zh":"公開錯誤可以影響聲譽，即使機構之後作出解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe damage or improvement, depending on the context.","zh":"這個短語可描述損害或改善，視乎語境而定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not only…but also…","meaning":"不但……而且……","examples":[{"en":"The controversy affected not only the CRU but also the IPCC.","zh":"這場爭議不但影響 CRU，而且影響 IPCC。"},{"en":"Not only A but also B means both A and B are included.","zh":"not only A but also B 指 A 和 B 都包括在內。"},{"en":"The new library helps not only students but also teachers.","zh":"新圖書館不但幫助學生，而且幫助老師。"},{"en":"This structure adds a second point and makes the connection stronger.","zh":"這個結構加入第二個重點，使連繫更強。"},{"en":"It is useful when one effect spreads beyond the first obvious target.","zh":"當一種影響超出第一個明顯目標時，這個結構很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"institution","meaning":"機構","examples":[{"en":"The reputation of that institution was damaged by the controversy.","zh":"該機構的聲譽被爭議損害。"},{"en":"An institution is an established organisation, such as a university, hospital, court or research body.","zh":"institution 指已建立的組織，例如大學、醫院、法院或研究機構。"},{"en":"A local hospital is an institution that many families depend on.","zh":"本地醫院是許多家庭依賴的機構。"},{"en":"If an institution loses trust, people may question its decisions and services.","zh":"如果機構失去信任，人們可能質疑其決定和服務。"},{"en":"This word usually refers to an organisation with public importance or a formal role.","zh":"這個詞通常指具有公共重要性或正式角色的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change","meaning":"政府間氣候變化專門委員會","examples":[{"en":"The Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change was also affected by the controversy.","zh":"政府間氣候變化專門委員會也受到這場爭議影響。"},{"en":"The Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change is an international body that assesses climate science for governments.","zh":"Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change 指為各國政府評估氣候科學的國際機構。"},{"en":"Students may see the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change mentioned in reports about global warming.","zh":"學生可能在全球暖化報告中看到政府間氣候變化專門委員會被提及。"},{"en":"When a major climate body is criticised, public confidence in climate information may be affected.","zh":"當主要氣候機構受到批評，公眾對氣候資訊的信心可能受影響。"},{"en":"This name refers to a specific international institution.","zh":"這個名稱指一個特定國際機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be closely involved with","meaning":"與……密切相關","examples":[{"en":"The CRU is closely involved with the IPCC.","zh":"CRU 與 IPCC 密切相關。"},{"en":"To be closely involved with something means to have a strong working connection with it.","zh":"be closely involved with something 指與某事有密切工作關係。"},{"en":"A parent-teacher association may be closely involved with school events.","zh":"家教會可能與學校活動密切相關。"},{"en":"If one organisation is closely involved with another, problems in one may affect the other.","zh":"如果一個機構與另一個機構密切相關，其中一方的問題可能影響另一方。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a close relationship, not a distant connection.","zh":"這個短語顯示緊密關係，而不是疏遠連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in general","meaning":"整體而言","examples":[{"en":"The controversy affected climate scientists in general.","zh":"這場爭議影響了整體氣候科學家。"},{"en":"In general means as a whole or in most cases, rather than referring to one specific person.","zh":"in general 指整體而言或在大多數情況下，而不是指某一個人。"},{"en":"Students in general prefer clear examples to abstract explanations.","zh":"整體而言，學生較喜歡清楚例子，而不是抽象解釋。"},{"en":"A scandal involving a few people can affect how the public sees a profession in general.","zh":"涉及少數人的醜聞可以影響公眾如何看待整個專業。"},{"en":"This phrase moves from individual cases to the broader group.","zh":"這個短語把焦點由個別例子移到較大群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"claims of misconduct","meaning":"行為失當的指控","examples":[{"en":"The claims of misconduct were eventually proven to be largely untrue.","zh":"行為失當的指控最終大致被證明不真實。"},{"en":"Claims of misconduct are accusations that someone behaved wrongly or unprofessionally.","zh":"claims of misconduct 指指控某人行為錯誤或不專業。"},{"en":"A company may investigate claims of misconduct after staff complain about unfair treatment.","zh":"員工投訴受到不公平對待後，公司可能調查行為失當的指控。"},{"en":"Even unproven claims of misconduct can damage trust while people wait for evidence.","zh":"即使未經證實，行為失當的指控也可以在人們等待證據期間損害信任。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to accusations, not necessarily confirmed wrongdoing.","zh":"這個短語指指控，不一定是已確認的不當行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"incompetence","meaning":"無能；不稱職","examples":[{"en":"The scientists also faced claims of incompetence.","zh":"科學家也面對無能的指控。"},{"en":"Incompetence means not having the skill or ability needed to do a job properly.","zh":"incompetence 指沒有做好某工作所需的技能或能力。"},{"en":"A manager may be accused of incompetence if repeated mistakes damage the team.","zh":"如果經理反覆犯錯並損害團隊，可能被指不稱職。"},{"en":"Claims of incompetence can be serious because they question a person’s professional ability.","zh":"無能的指控很嚴重，因為它質疑一個人的專業能力。"},{"en":"This word is stronger than simply saying someone made one mistake.","zh":"這個詞比單純說某人犯了一次錯更強烈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"eventually proven to be","meaning":"最終被證明為","examples":[{"en":"The claims were eventually proven to be largely untrue.","zh":"這些指控最終被證明大致不真實。"},{"en":"Eventually proven to be means shown to be true or false after time, evidence or investigation.","zh":"eventually proven to be 指經過時間、證據或調查後被證明為真或假。"},{"en":"The missing homework was eventually proven to be submitted online before the deadline.","zh":"那份失蹤功課最終被證明已在截止日期前網上提交。"},{"en":"Investigation can eventually prove whether an accusation is fair or mistaken.","zh":"調查最終可以證明指控是合理還是錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that proof came later, not immediately.","zh":"這個短語顯示證明是後來才出現，而不是立即出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"largely untrue","meaning":"大致不真實","examples":[{"en":"The allegations were found to be largely untrue.","zh":"這些指控被發現大致不真實。"},{"en":"Largely untrue means mostly false, though there may be small parts connected to reality.","zh":"largely untrue 指大部分是假的，雖然可能有小部分與現實有關。"},{"en":"A rumour that a school would close was largely untrue if only one classroom was being repaired.","zh":"如果只是其中一間課室維修，學校將會關閉的謠言就是大致不真實。"},{"en":"Claims that are largely untrue can still spread quickly if people are angry or worried.","zh":"大致不真實的說法，如果人們憤怒或擔心，仍可以迅速傳開。"},{"en":"This phrase does not always mean every detail is false.","zh":"這個短語不一定表示每個細節都是假的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be confined to","meaning":"限於……","examples":[{"en":"Some problems may have been confined to a few individuals.","zh":"有些問題可能只限於少數個人。"},{"en":"To be confined to something means to be limited to that person, place, group or area.","zh":"be confined to something 指被限制於某個人、地方、群體或範圍。"},{"en":"The power cut was confined to one building, so the rest of the school continued lessons.","zh":"停電只限於一座建築物，所以學校其他地方繼續上課。"},{"en":"If a problem is confined to a few people, it should not automatically damage everyone’s reputation.","zh":"如果問題只限於少數人，就不應自動損害所有人的聲譽。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a clear limit or boundary.","zh":"這個短語顯示清楚限制或界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the damage was done","meaning":"傷害已經造成","examples":[{"en":"Even if the claims were untrue, the damage was done.","zh":"即使指控不真實，傷害已經造成。"},{"en":"The damage was done means harm had already happened and could not easily be undone.","zh":"the damage was done 指傷害已經發生，而且不容易逆轉。"},{"en":"After a false rumour spread through a school, the apology came late because the damage was done.","zh":"假謠言在學校傳開後，道歉來得太遲，因為傷害已經造成。"},{"en":"Once public trust falls, later explanations may not fully repair the harm.","zh":"一旦公眾信任下降，之後的解釋未必能完全修補傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that consequences can remain even after the facts are corrected.","zh":"這個短語強調即使事實被糾正，後果仍可能存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"perceived wrongdoings","meaning":"被認為的不當行為","examples":[{"en":"The perceived wrongdoings of a few people raised doubts about many scientists.","zh":"少數人被認為的不當行為引起了對許多科學家的疑慮。"},{"en":"Perceived wrongdoings are actions that people believe are wrong, even if they may not be fully proven.","zh":"perceived wrongdoings 指人們認為是錯誤的行為，即使未必完全證實。"},{"en":"A teacher’s perceived unfairness can upset students even before the school investigates.","zh":"老師被認為不公平，即使學校尚未調查，也可以令學生不滿。"},{"en":"Perceived wrongdoings can damage trust because public reaction depends partly on appearance.","zh":"被認為的不當行為可以損害信任，因為公眾反應部分取決於表面印象。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how behaviour is seen by others.","zh":"這個短語著重行為如何被他人看待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"raise doubts about","meaning":"引起對……的疑慮","examples":[{"en":"The scandal raised doubts about climate science as a whole.","zh":"這宗醜聞引起了對整個氣候科學的疑慮。"},{"en":"To raise doubts about something means to make people question whether it is true, honest or reliable.","zh":"raise doubts about something 指令人質疑某事是否真實、誠實或可靠。"},{"en":"Missing receipts may raise doubts about how a club spent its money.","zh":"收據缺失可能引起對學會如何花錢的疑慮。"},{"en":"Doubts can spread when evidence is unclear or communication is poor.","zh":"當證據不清或溝通差，疑慮可以擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning or strengthening of suspicion.","zh":"這個短語描述懷疑的開始或加深。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the response of","meaning":"……的回應","examples":[{"en":"The response of most climate scientists was to keep quiet.","zh":"大多數氣候科學家的回應是保持沉默。"},{"en":"The response of a person or group is what they do or say after something happens.","zh":"the response of a person or group 指某事發生後，他們做了甚麼或說了甚麼。"},{"en":"The response of the school to bullying complaints was to hold a meeting with parents.","zh":"學校對欺凌投訴的回應是與家長開會。"},{"en":"A weak response can make a problem look worse than it first appeared.","zh":"軟弱回應可以令問題看起來比一開始更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on reaction after an event.","zh":"這個短語著重事件後的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cross one’s fingers","meaning":"祈求好運","examples":[{"en":"Most climate scientists seemed to cross their fingers and hope for the best.","zh":"大多數氣候科學家似乎只是祈求好運並希望有好結果。"},{"en":"To cross one’s fingers means to hope that something will go well, often without doing much more.","zh":"cross one’s fingers 指希望事情順利，通常沒有做更多實際行動。"},{"en":"A student who did not revise may cross her fingers before the test begins.","zh":"沒有溫習的學生在測驗前可能祈求好運。"},{"en":"Crossing one’s fingers is not a real plan because it depends on luck.","zh":"祈求好運不是真正計劃，因為它依賴運氣。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests passive hope rather than active action.","zh":"這個短語常暗示被動希望，而不是主動行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hope for the best","meaning":"希望有好結果","examples":[{"en":"Their strategy was to keep a low profile and hope for the best.","zh":"他們的策略是保持低調並希望有好結果。"},{"en":"To hope for the best means to wish for a good outcome, especially when the situation is uncertain.","zh":"hope for the best 指希望有好結果，尤其是在情況不確定時。"},{"en":"A shop owner may hope for the best after reopening during bad weather.","zh":"店主在惡劣天氣中重新開店後，可能希望有好結果。"},{"en":"Hoping for the best may feel comforting, but it does not solve problems by itself.","zh":"希望有好結果可能令人安慰，但它本身不能解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears when people have limited control or avoid action.","zh":"這個短語常出現在人們控制有限或避免行動時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"keep a low profile","meaning":"保持低調","examples":[{"en":"Many climate scientists kept a low profile after the scandal.","zh":"許多氣候科學家在醜聞後保持低調。"},{"en":"To keep a low profile means to avoid public attention.","zh":"keep a low profile 指避免受到公眾注意。"},{"en":"A student who made a mistake in class may keep a low profile for the rest of the day.","zh":"在課堂上犯錯的學生可能當天餘下時間保持低調。"},{"en":"Keeping a low profile can reduce attention temporarily, but it may also look like avoidance.","zh":"保持低調可以暫時減少注意，但也可能看似逃避。"},{"en":"This phrase describes staying quiet and unnoticed.","zh":"這個短語描述保持安靜和不引人注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"no doubt","meaning":"毫無疑問","examples":[{"en":"Many no doubt hoped that independent inquiries would solve the problem.","zh":"毫無疑問，許多人希望獨立調查能解決問題。"},{"en":"No doubt means very probably or almost certainly.","zh":"no doubt 指很可能或幾乎肯定。"},{"en":"Parents no doubt want clear information when a school changes its exam policy.","zh":"當學校改變考試政策，家長毫無疑問會想要清楚資料。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the writer is confident about a likely feeling or situation.","zh":"這個短語顯示作者對可能的感受或情況有信心。"},{"en":"It does not always mean there is literal proof; it often signals strong assumption.","zh":"它不一定表示有字面上的證據；常表示強烈推測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"subsequent independent inquiries","meaning":"隨後的獨立調查","examples":[{"en":"Subsequent independent inquiries were expected to examine the IPCC and CRU.","zh":"隨後的獨立調查預期會審查 IPCC 和 CRU。"},{"en":"Subsequent independent inquiries are later investigations carried out by bodies not directly controlled by those being investigated.","zh":"subsequent independent inquiries 指之後由不受被調查者直接控制的機構進行的調查。"},{"en":"After complaints about exam marking, subsequent independent inquiries may review the results.","zh":"考試評分受到投訴後，隨後的獨立調查可能覆核結果。"},{"en":"Independent inquiries can help rebuild trust if people believe the investigation is fair.","zh":"如果人們相信調查公平，獨立調查可以幫助重建信任。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses both timing and independence.","zh":"這個短語同時強調時間和獨立性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"inquiry into","meaning":"對……的調查","examples":[{"en":"There were independent inquiries into the IPCC and CRU.","zh":"有獨立調查針對 IPCC 和 CRU。"},{"en":"An inquiry into something is an official investigation of that issue or organisation.","zh":"inquiry into something 指對該議題或機構進行的正式調查。"},{"en":"A school may hold an inquiry into missing exam papers.","zh":"學校可能對失蹤試卷進行調查。"},{"en":"An inquiry into a scandal can reveal mistakes, responsibility and possible reforms.","zh":"對醜聞的調查可以揭示錯誤、責任和可能改革。"},{"en":"This phrase describes focused investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述有焦點的調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"draw a line under","meaning":"使……告一段落","examples":[{"en":"Scientists hoped the inquiries would draw a line under their problems.","zh":"科學家希望調查能使他們的問題告一段落。"},{"en":"To draw a line under something means to end it and move on from it.","zh":"draw a line under something 指結束某事並繼續向前。"},{"en":"After a class argument, the teacher may ask everyone to apologise and draw a line under it.","zh":"班上爭執後，老師可能要求所有人道歉並使事件告一段落。"},{"en":"People can draw a line under a problem only when they feel it has been dealt with properly.","zh":"只有當人們覺得問題已妥善處理，才可以使問題告一段落。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests closure after a difficult period.","zh":"這個短語暗示困難時期後的結束。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be likely to help","meaning":"很可能有幫助","examples":[{"en":"The inquiries were likely to help the scientists.","zh":"這些調查很可能對科學家有幫助。"},{"en":"To be likely to help means to probably improve the situation.","zh":"be likely to help 指很可能改善情況。"},{"en":"Extra reading practice is likely to help students who struggle with vocabulary.","zh":"額外閱讀練習很可能幫助詞彙薄弱的學生。"},{"en":"A fair investigation is likely to help rebuild trust if people believe its results.","zh":"如果人們相信調查結果，公平調查很可能有助重建信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a probable benefit, not a guaranteed result.","zh":"這個短語描述可能的好處，而不是保證結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be unlikely to undo","meaning":"不大可能消除……","examples":[{"en":"The inquiries were unlikely to undo the harm caused by hostile reports.","zh":"這些調查不大可能消除帶敵意報道造成的傷害。"},{"en":"To be unlikely to undo something means probably not able to reverse or repair it.","zh":"be unlikely to undo something 指很可能無法逆轉或修補某事。"},{"en":"A late apology is unlikely to undo the hurt caused by a public insult.","zh":"遲來的道歉不大可能消除公開侮辱造成的傷害。"},{"en":"Some damage lasts because people remember the first negative story more than the later correction.","zh":"有些傷害會持續，因為人們更記得最初的負面故事，而不是後來的更正。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited ability to repair past harm.","zh":"這個短語描述修補過去傷害的能力有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"undo the harm","meaning":"消除傷害","examples":[{"en":"Independent reports could not easily undo the harm caused by months of criticism.","zh":"獨立報告不能輕易消除數月批評造成的傷害。"},{"en":"To undo the harm means to repair or reverse the damage already caused.","zh":"undo the harm 指修補或逆轉已造成的損害。"},{"en":"A school cannot easily undo the harm if a false rumour has spread among parents.","zh":"如果假謠言已在家長之間傳開，學校不能輕易消除傷害。"},{"en":"Harm is harder to undo when people have already changed their opinions.","zh":"當人們已經改變看法，傷害就更難消除。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on repairing consequences, not just explaining the mistake.","zh":"這個短語著重修補後果，而不只是解釋錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"harm caused by","meaning":"由……造成的傷害","examples":[{"en":"The harm caused by hostile news reports was serious.","zh":"由帶敵意新聞報道造成的傷害很嚴重。"},{"en":"Harm caused by something is damage that results from that action or event.","zh":"harm caused by something 指由某行動或事件造成的損害。"},{"en":"The harm caused by online rumours can affect a student’s confidence.","zh":"由網上謠言造成的傷害可以影響學生信心。"},{"en":"Identifying the harm caused by a mistake helps people decide how to repair it.","zh":"找出錯誤造成的傷害，有助人們決定如何修補。"},{"en":"This phrase connects damage with its source.","zh":"這個短語把傷害與其來源連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"hostile news reports","meaning":"帶敵意的新聞報道","examples":[{"en":"Hostile news reports damaged public confidence in climate science.","zh":"帶敵意的新聞報道損害了公眾對氣候科學的信心。"},{"en":"Hostile news reports are media stories that attack, criticise or present someone very negatively.","zh":"hostile news reports 指攻擊、批評或非常負面地呈現某人的媒體報道。"},{"en":"Hostile news reports about a school can make parents worry before hearing the full facts.","zh":"關於學校的帶敵意新聞報道，可以在完整事實公布前令家長擔心。"},{"en":"Repeated hostile reports can shape public opinion even if later corrections appear.","zh":"反覆的帶敵意報道可以塑造公眾意見，即使之後有更正。"},{"en":"This phrase describes news coverage with a strongly negative tone.","zh":"這個短語描述帶有強烈負面語氣的新聞報道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"attacks by critics","meaning":"批評者的攻擊","examples":[{"en":"The scientists faced months of attacks by critics.","zh":"科學家面對數月來批評者的攻擊。"},{"en":"Attacks by critics are strong public criticisms from people who oppose or question someone.","zh":"attacks by critics 指反對或質疑某人的人提出的強烈公開批評。"},{"en":"A new school policy may face attacks by critics if parents think it is unfair.","zh":"如果家長認為新校政不公平，它可能面對批評者的攻擊。"},{"en":"Repeated attacks by critics can pressure an organisation to explain itself clearly.","zh":"反覆的批評者攻擊可以迫使機構清楚解釋自己。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to verbal or written criticism, not necessarily physical attack.","zh":"這個短語指口頭或書面批評，不一定是身體攻擊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"should not be underestimated","meaning":"不應被低估","examples":[{"en":"The damage that has been done should not be underestimated.","zh":"已造成的傷害不應被低估。"},{"en":"Should not be underestimated means should not be treated as smaller or less serious than it really is.","zh":"should not be underestimated 指不應被視為比實際更小或不嚴重。"},{"en":"The stress caused by exams should not be underestimated by teachers or parents.","zh":"老師和家長不應低估考試造成的壓力。"},{"en":"Underestimating damage can lead to weak action and slower recovery.","zh":"低估傷害可以導致行動不足和恢復較慢。"},{"en":"This phrase warns readers to take something seriously.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者認真看待某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"public opinion","meaning":"公眾意見","examples":[{"en":"Public opinion moved against climate scientists after the scandal.","zh":"醜聞後，公眾意見轉向不利於氣候科學家。"},{"en":"Public opinion is what many ordinary people think about an issue, person or organisation.","zh":"public opinion 指許多普通人對某議題、人物或機構的看法。"},{"en":"Public opinion may change after a government announces a new transport policy.","zh":"政府公布新交通政策後，公眾意見可能改變。"},{"en":"If public opinion turns negative, leaders may feel pressure to respond.","zh":"如果公眾意見變得負面，領袖可能感到需要回應的壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to broad social attitudes, not one person’s view.","zh":"這個短語指廣泛社會態度，而不是一個人的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"move toward the view that","meaning":"逐漸傾向認為","examples":[{"en":"Public opinion moved toward the view that scientists might suppress ideas.","zh":"公眾意見逐漸傾向認為科學家可能壓制想法。"},{"en":"To move toward the view that means to gradually begin accepting or leaning toward a particular belief.","zh":"move toward the view that 指逐漸開始接受或傾向某種信念。"},{"en":"Parents may move toward the view that homework should be reduced after seeing children become exhausted.","zh":"家長看到孩子筋疲力盡後，可能逐漸傾向認為功課應該減少。"},{"en":"People often move toward a view when repeated stories or evidence point in the same direction.","zh":"當反覆故事或證據指向同一方向，人們常會逐漸傾向某看法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gradual shift in belief.","zh":"這個短語描述信念的逐步轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"suppress alternative hypotheses","meaning":"壓制另類假說","examples":[{"en":"Some people believed scientists tried to suppress alternative hypotheses.","zh":"有些人相信科學家試圖壓制另類假說。"},{"en":"To suppress alternative hypotheses means to stop different explanations from being discussed or considered.","zh":"suppress alternative hypotheses 指阻止不同解釋被討論或考慮。"},{"en":"A teacher should not suppress alternative hypotheses when students suggest different reasons for a historical event.","zh":"當學生提出歷史事件的不同原因，老師不應壓制另類假說。"},{"en":"Suppressing alternative ideas can make people suspect that the debate is unfair.","zh":"壓制另類想法可以令人懷疑討論不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase describes blocking competing explanations.","zh":"這個短語描述阻止競爭性解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"alternative hypotheses","meaning":"另類假說","examples":[{"en":"Scientists were accused of suppressing alternative hypotheses and ideas.","zh":"科學家被指壓制另類假說和想法。"},{"en":"Alternative hypotheses are different possible explanations for the same evidence or problem.","zh":"alternative hypotheses 指對同一證據或問題的不同可能解釋。"},{"en":"In science class, students may suggest alternative hypotheses for why a plant stopped growing.","zh":"在科學課中，學生可能提出植物停止生長的另類假說。"},{"en":"Testing alternative hypotheses helps people avoid jumping to one conclusion too quickly.","zh":"測試另類假說幫助人們避免太快跳到單一結論。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to competing explanations, not random opinions.","zh":"這個短語指競爭性解釋，而不是隨機意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"withhold data","meaning":"隱瞞數據","examples":[{"en":"Some members of the public believed scientists might withhold data.","zh":"有些公眾相信科學家可能隱瞞數據。"},{"en":"To withhold data means to keep information back instead of sharing it.","zh":"withhold data 指保留資料而不分享。"},{"en":"A company should not withhold safety data from customers.","zh":"公司不應向顧客隱瞞安全數據。"},{"en":"Withholding data can make people suspect that the full truth is being hidden.","zh":"隱瞞數據可以令人懷疑完整真相被隱藏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes not releasing information that others expect to see.","zh":"這個短語描述不公開他人期望看到的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"manipulate peer review","meaning":"操控同行評審","examples":[{"en":"Critics claimed that scientists might manipulate peer review.","zh":"批評者聲稱科學家可能操控同行評審。"},{"en":"To manipulate peer review means to unfairly influence the expert-checking process for research.","zh":"manipulate peer review 指不公平地影響研究的專家審查過程。"},{"en":"A researcher manipulates peer review if they try to block honest criticism from other experts.","zh":"如果研究人員試圖阻止其他專家的真誠批評，就是操控同行評審。"},{"en":"Manipulating peer review damages scientific trust because research depends on fair checking.","zh":"操控同行評審會損害科學信任，因為研究依賴公平審查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unfair control over an academic review process.","zh":"這個短語描述對學術評審過程的不公平控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"peer review","meaning":"同行評審","examples":[{"en":"Peer review is central to scientific credibility.","zh":"同行評審對科學公信力至關重要。"},{"en":"Peer review is the process in which experts check research before or after publication.","zh":"peer review 指專家在發表前或發表後審查研究的過程。"},{"en":"A journal may send a paper to several scientists for peer review.","zh":"期刊可能把論文交給幾位科學家進行同行評審。"},{"en":"Peer review helps catch mistakes and improve the quality of research.","zh":"同行評審幫助發現錯誤並提升研究質素。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to expert checking, not general public comments.","zh":"這個短語指專家審查，而不是一般公眾評論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"prevent dissent","meaning":"阻止異議","examples":[{"en":"Some people believed scientists tried to prevent dissent.","zh":"有些人相信科學家試圖阻止異議。"},{"en":"To prevent dissent means to stop disagreement or opposing views from being expressed.","zh":"prevent dissent 指阻止不同意見或反對觀點被表達。"},{"en":"A fair classroom should not prevent dissent when students respectfully challenge an idea.","zh":"公平課室不應在學生尊重地挑戰想法時阻止異議。"},{"en":"Preventing dissent can make people believe that only one opinion is allowed.","zh":"阻止異議可以令人相信只有一種意見被容許。"},{"en":"This phrase describes blocking disagreement.","zh":"這個短語描述阻止不同意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"conclude that","meaning":"總結認為","examples":[{"en":"Cicerone concluded that a few scientists could damage science as a whole.","zh":"Cicerone 總結認為，少數科學家可以損害整個科學界。"},{"en":"To conclude that means to reach an opinion after considering evidence or arguments.","zh":"conclude that 指在考慮證據或論點後得出看法。"},{"en":"After reading the survey results, a principal may conclude that students need more counselling support.","zh":"校長閱讀調查結果後，可能總結認為學生需要更多輔導支援。"},{"en":"People conclude something when the evidence points strongly in one direction.","zh":"當證據強烈指向某方向，人們就會得出結論。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a final judgement or interpretation.","zh":"這個短語引入最終判斷或詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"perceived misbehavior","meaning":"被認為的不當行為","examples":[{"en":"The perceived misbehavior of a few scientists can damage public trust.","zh":"少數科學家被認為的不當行為可以損害公眾信任。"},{"en":"Perceived misbehavior is behaviour that people believe is wrong, whether or not it has been fully proven.","zh":"perceived misbehavior 指人們認為錯誤的行為，不論是否已完全證實。"},{"en":"A worker’s perceived misbehavior can harm team trust even before a manager investigates.","zh":"員工被認為的不當行為，即使經理尚未調查，也可以損害團隊信任。"},{"en":"Public trust may fall because people react to what they think happened.","zh":"公眾信任可能下降，因為人們會對他們認為發生了的事作出反應。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on public perception of wrongdoing.","zh":"這個短語著重公眾對不當行為的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"diminish the credibility of","meaning":"削弱……的公信力","examples":[{"en":"The scandal could diminish the credibility of science as a whole.","zh":"這宗醜聞可能削弱整個科學界的公信力。"},{"en":"To diminish the credibility of something means to weaken people’s belief that it is reliable or trustworthy.","zh":"diminish the credibility of something 指削弱人們對某事可靠或可信的信念。"},{"en":"A false advertisement can diminish the credibility of a brand.","zh":"虛假廣告可以削弱品牌的公信力。"},{"en":"Credibility falls when people think facts are hidden, changed or poorly checked.","zh":"當人們認為事實被隱藏、改動或審查不足，公信力就會下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a loss of trustworthiness.","zh":"這個短語描述可信度下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"science as a whole","meaning":"整個科學界","examples":[{"en":"The controversy damaged trust in science as a whole.","zh":"這場爭議損害了對整個科學界的信任。"},{"en":"Science as a whole means the entire scientific community and method, not just one study or field.","zh":"science as a whole 指整個科學社群和科學方法，而不只是某項研究或領域。"},{"en":"One medical error should not make people reject science as a whole.","zh":"一次醫療錯誤不應令人否定整個科學界。"},{"en":"When trust in science as a whole falls, public health and education may suffer.","zh":"當對整個科學界的信任下降，公共健康和教育可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase broadens the focus beyond a single branch of science.","zh":"這個短語把焦點擴展到單一科學分支以外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"opinion poll","meaning":"民意調查","examples":[{"en":"An opinion poll found that trust in climate scientists had fallen.","zh":"一項民意調查發現，對氣候科學家的信任下降了。"},{"en":"An opinion poll is a survey that asks people what they think about an issue.","zh":"opinion poll 指詢問人們對某議題看法的調查。"},{"en":"A school may use an opinion poll to ask students whether they want longer library hours.","zh":"學校可能使用民意調查詢問學生是否想延長圖書館開放時間。"},{"en":"Opinion polls can show changes in public attitudes over time.","zh":"民意調查可以顯示公眾態度隨時間的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to measured public views, not private guesses.","zh":"這個短語指被量度的公眾看法，而不是私人猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at the beginning of","meaning":"在……開始時","examples":[{"en":"An opinion poll was taken at the beginning of 2010.","zh":"一項民意調查在 2010 年開始時進行。"},{"en":"At the beginning of means near the start of a period, event or process.","zh":"at the beginning of 指在某段時間、事件或過程的開始附近。"},{"en":"At the beginning of the school year, teachers explain class rules.","zh":"在學年開始時，老師會解釋班規。"},{"en":"Information collected at the beginning of a period can be compared with later results.","zh":"在某段時間開始時收集的資料，可以與之後結果比較。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a time point near the start.","zh":"這個短語給出接近開始的時間點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the proportion of people","meaning":"人口比例","examples":[{"en":"The proportion of people who trusted scientists had dropped.","zh":"信任科學家的人口比例下降了。"},{"en":"The proportion of people means the share or percentage of a group.","zh":"the proportion of people 指某群體中的比例或百分比。"},{"en":"The proportion of students who walk to school may rise after a new footbridge opens.","zh":"新行人天橋開通後，步行上學的學生比例可能上升。"},{"en":"Changes in proportion show whether a view is becoming more or less common.","zh":"比例變化顯示某看法是否變得更普遍或更少見。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing survey results.","zh":"這個短語適合討論調查結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"trust someone as a source of information","meaning":"信任某人作為資料來源","examples":[{"en":"Fewer people trusted scientists as a source of information about global warming.","zh":"較少人信任科學家作為全球暖化資料來源。"},{"en":"To trust someone as a source of information means to believe that the information they provide is reliable.","zh":"trust someone as a source of information 指相信某人提供的資料可靠。"},{"en":"Parents may trust a school nurse as a source of information about student health.","zh":"家長可能信任學校護士作為學生健康資料來源。"},{"en":"If people stop trusting a source, they may look for answers elsewhere.","zh":"如果人們不再信任某資料來源，可能會到其他地方尋找答案。"},{"en":"This phrase links trust with information reliability.","zh":"這個短語把信任與資訊可靠性連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"global warming","meaning":"全球暖化","examples":[{"en":"The poll concerned public trust in information about global warming.","zh":"這項調查關於公眾對全球暖化資訊的信任。"},{"en":"Global warming is the long-term rise in Earth’s average temperature.","zh":"global warming 指地球平均溫度長期上升。"},{"en":"Students may learn about global warming through lessons on heatwaves, sea levels and extreme weather.","zh":"學生可能透過熱浪、海平面和極端天氣課題學習全球暖化。"},{"en":"Confusing information about global warming can make public action harder.","zh":"關於全球暖化的混亂資訊可以令公眾行動更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a major part of climate change.","zh":"這個短語指氣候變化的一個重要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"drop from…to…","meaning":"從……下降至……","examples":[{"en":"Trust in scientists dropped from 83 percent to 74 percent.","zh":"對科學家的信任從 83% 下降至 74%。"},{"en":"Drop from A to B means decrease from the first number to the second number.","zh":"drop from A to B 指由第一個數字下降到第二個數字。"},{"en":"A student’s score dropped from 80 to 65 after missing several lessons.","zh":"學生缺席幾堂課後，分數從 80 分下降至 65 分。"},{"en":"A drop from one figure to another shows the size of the decline clearly.","zh":"從一個數字下降至另一個數字，可以清楚顯示跌幅。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for numbers, percentages and levels.","zh":"這個短語用於數字、百分比和水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"survey carried out by","meaning":"由……進行的調查","examples":[{"en":"Another survey carried out by the BBC found lower public belief in climate change.","zh":"另一項由 BBC 進行的調查發現，公眾對氣候變化的相信程度較低。"},{"en":"A survey carried out by an organisation is a survey conducted or organised by that body.","zh":"survey carried out by an organisation 指由該機構進行或組織的調查。"},{"en":"A survey carried out by a school may ask students about homework pressure.","zh":"由學校進行的調查可能詢問學生功課壓力。"},{"en":"Who carried out a survey matters because people judge the reliability of the source.","zh":"誰進行調查很重要，因為人們會判斷來源是否可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the organisation responsible for the survey.","zh":"這個短語指出負責調查的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be confirmed as","meaning":"被證實為","examples":[{"en":"Only 26 percent of British people believed climate change was confirmed as human-made.","zh":"只有 26% 英國人相信氣候變化被證實為人類造成。"},{"en":"To be confirmed as something means to be officially or strongly shown to be that thing.","zh":"be confirmed as something 指被正式或有力地顯示為某事。"},{"en":"A student’s absence may be confirmed as illness after a doctor’s note arrives.","zh":"醫生紙到達後，學生缺席可能被證實為因病。"},{"en":"Confirmation matters because people are more likely to accept a claim when evidence is strong.","zh":"證實很重要，因為當證據強，人們較可能接受說法。"},{"en":"This phrase indicates a claim has been supported or verified.","zh":"這個短語表示某說法已獲支持或核實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"largely human-made","meaning":"主要由人類造成的","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe climate change is largely human-made.","zh":"有些人相信氣候變化主要由人類造成。"},{"en":"Largely human-made means mainly caused by human actions.","zh":"largely human-made 指主要由人類行動造成。"},{"en":"A city’s air pollution may be largely human-made if it comes mostly from traffic and factories.","zh":"如果城市空氣污染主要來自交通和工廠，它可能主要由人類造成。"},{"en":"If a problem is largely human-made, human choices can also help reduce it.","zh":"如果問題主要由人類造成，人類選擇也可以幫助減少它。"},{"en":"This phrase means human activity is the main cause, not necessarily the only cause.","zh":"這個短語表示人類活動是主要原因，不一定是唯一原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"down from","meaning":"低於之前的……","examples":[{"en":"The figure was down from 41 percent in November 2009.","zh":"該數字低於 2009 年 11 月的 41%。"},{"en":"Down from means lower than a previous number or level.","zh":"down from 指低於之前的數字或水平。"},{"en":"Library visits were down from 500 a week to 350 after the timetable changed.","zh":"時間表改變後，圖書館每週到訪人次由 500 降至 350。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare a current figure with an earlier one.","zh":"這個短語幫助把現時數字與早前數字比較。"},{"en":"It is commonly used in reports about falling numbers.","zh":"它常用於關於數字下降的報告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"regain confidence and trust","meaning":"重拾信心和信任","examples":[{"en":"Regaining the confidence and trust of the public is never easy.","zh":"重拾公眾的信心和信任從來不容易。"},{"en":"To regain confidence and trust means to win back people’s belief after it has been lost.","zh":"regain confidence and trust 指在失去後重新贏回人們的信念。"},{"en":"A school may need to regain confidence and trust after mishandling student safety complaints.","zh":"學校在處理學生安全投訴不當後，可能需要重拾信心和信任。"},{"en":"Transparency and consistent action help people believe that change is real.","zh":"透明度和一致行動幫助人們相信改變是真實的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rebuilding belief, not simply asking people to forget.","zh":"這個短語描述重建信念，而不是單純要求人們忘記。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hunker down","meaning":"躲起來避風頭","examples":[{"en":"Hunkering down and hoping for the best made recovery almost impossible.","zh":"躲起來避風頭並希望有好結果，令恢復幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"To hunker down means to keep quiet, stay defensive and wait for trouble to pass.","zh":"hunker down 指保持沉默、採取防守姿態並等待麻煩過去。"},{"en":"A company may hunker down after bad news by refusing interviews and avoiding customers.","zh":"公司在負面新聞後可能拒絕訪問並迴避顧客，躲起來避風頭。"},{"en":"Hunkering down can make recovery harder because people may read silence as guilt.","zh":"躲起來避風頭可以令恢復更難，因為人們可能把沉默解讀為有罪。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests withdrawal rather than open communication.","zh":"這個短語暗示退縮，而不是公開溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"current strategy","meaning":"當前策略","examples":[{"en":"Climate science’s current strategy was unlikely to rebuild trust.","zh":"氣候科學的當前策略不大可能重建信任。"},{"en":"A current strategy is the plan or approach being used now.","zh":"current strategy 指現在正在使用的計劃或方法。"},{"en":"A student’s current strategy for revision may be to practise one past paper every weekend.","zh":"學生當前的溫習策略可能是每週末練習一份 past paper。"},{"en":"If a current strategy fails, people need to adjust their approach.","zh":"如果當前策略失敗，人們需要調整方法。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the method currently being followed.","zh":"這個短語指目前正在採用的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"make it almost impossible","meaning":"令……幾乎不可能","examples":[{"en":"The strategy made it almost impossible to regain public trust.","zh":"這個策略令重拾公眾信任幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"To make it almost impossible means to make something extremely difficult to achieve.","zh":"make it almost impossible 指令某事極難達成。"},{"en":"Missing many lessons can make it almost impossible to follow a fast-moving course.","zh":"缺席很多課可以令跟上快速課程幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"Poor communication can make it almost impossible to repair a reputation.","zh":"溝通差可以令修補聲譽幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that success is not fully impossible, but very unlikely.","zh":"這個短語顯示成功並非完全不可能，但非常不大可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"learn from","meaning":"向……學習","examples":[{"en":"Climate scientists should learn from organisations that faced similar crises.","zh":"氣候科學家應向面對類似危機的機構學習。"},{"en":"To learn from someone or something means to use their experience to improve your own actions.","zh":"learn from someone or something 指利用他們的經驗來改善自己的行動。"},{"en":"A new teacher can learn from experienced colleagues by watching how they manage a class.","zh":"新老師可以透過觀察有經驗同事如何管理課堂向他們學習。"},{"en":"Learning from past mistakes helps people avoid repeating them.","zh":"從過去錯誤中學習可以幫助人避免重複犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase turns another person’s success or failure into guidance.","zh":"這個短語把他人的成功或失敗轉化為指引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"successes and failures","meaning":"成功與失敗經驗","examples":[{"en":"They should learn from the successes and failures of other organisations.","zh":"他們應向其他機構的成功與失敗經驗學習。"},{"en":"Successes and failures are examples of what worked well and what went wrong.","zh":"successes and failures 指有效做法和出錯情況的例子。"},{"en":"A school club can learn from past successes and failures before organising another charity event.","zh":"學校學會在再次舉辦慈善活動前，可以從過去成功與失敗經驗中學習。"},{"en":"Studying both success and failure gives a fuller picture than studying only good results.","zh":"同時研究成功和失敗，比只研究好結果更全面。"},{"en":"This phrase means useful lessons can come from both positive and negative outcomes.","zh":"這個短語表示正面和負面結果都可以帶來有用教訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"deal with similar blows","meaning":"應對類似打擊","examples":[{"en":"Other organisations had dealt with similar blows to their public standing.","zh":"其他機構曾應對對其公眾形象造成的類似打擊。"},{"en":"To deal with similar blows means to handle similar serious damage or setbacks.","zh":"deal with similar blows 指處理類似的嚴重損害或挫折。"},{"en":"A company may deal with similar blows after a product recall hurts customer trust.","zh":"公司在產品回收損害顧客信任後，可能需要應對類似打擊。"},{"en":"Organisations that handle reputation damage well can offer useful lessons to others.","zh":"能妥善處理聲譽損害的機構，可以給其他人有用教訓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes coping with a comparable crisis.","zh":"這個短語描述應對可比較的危機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"public standing","meaning":"公眾形象；社會聲望","examples":[{"en":"The scandal damaged the public standing of climate science.","zh":"醜聞損害了氣候科學的公眾形象。"},{"en":"Public standing is the level of respect or status a person, profession or organisation has in society.","zh":"public standing 指某人、專業或機構在社會中的尊重程度或地位。"},{"en":"A charity’s public standing may rise after years of honest community work.","zh":"慈善機構多年誠實服務社區後，公眾形象可能提升。"},{"en":"Public standing can fall quickly if people believe an institution behaved dishonestly.","zh":"如果人們相信機構行為不誠實，公眾形象可以迅速下降。"},{"en":"This phrase is close to reputation, but it emphasises social status and respect.","zh":"這個短語接近 reputation，但更強調社會地位和尊重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"professional help","meaning":"專業協助","examples":[{"en":"Climate science needs professional help to rebuild its reputation.","zh":"氣候科學需要專業協助來重建聲譽。"},{"en":"Professional help is advice or support from people trained in a specialised area.","zh":"professional help 指來自受過專業訓練人士的建議或支援。"},{"en":"A family may seek professional help from a counsellor when conflict becomes serious.","zh":"當家庭衝突變得嚴重，家人可能向輔導員尋求專業協助。"},{"en":"Professional help can prevent people from handling complex problems blindly.","zh":"專業協助可以防止人盲目處理複雜問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests expertise is needed, not just goodwill.","zh":"這個短語暗示需要專門知識，而不只是善意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rebuild one’s reputation","meaning":"重建聲譽","examples":[{"en":"Climate scientists need to rebuild their reputation after the scandal.","zh":"氣候科學家需要在醜聞後重建聲譽。"},{"en":"To rebuild one’s reputation means to restore trust and respect after it has been damaged.","zh":"rebuild one’s reputation 指在聲譽受損後恢復信任和尊重。"},{"en":"A shop can rebuild its reputation by refunding customers and improving service.","zh":"商店可以透過退款和改善服務來重建聲譽。"},{"en":"Rebuilding reputation requires repeated good actions, not one quick statement.","zh":"重建聲譽需要反覆良好行動，而不是一句快速聲明。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-term repair of public trust.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾信任的長期修補。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"could do worse than","meaning":"不妨……；可以考慮……","examples":[{"en":"Climate science could do worse than follow Gaines-Ross’s advice.","zh":"氣候科學不妨跟從 Gaines-Ross 的建議。"},{"en":"Could do worse than means it would be a sensible or useful choice to do that thing.","zh":"could do worse than 指做某事會是合理或有用的選擇。"},{"en":"A nervous student could do worse than practise speaking with a supportive friend.","zh":"緊張的學生不妨與支持自己的朋友練習說話。"},{"en":"This phrase is understated: it often means the option is actually quite good.","zh":"這個短語語氣低調；它常表示該選項其實相當不錯。"},{"en":"It is a polite way to suggest a helpful course of action.","zh":"這是建議有用做法的禮貌方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"follow the advice given by","meaning":"跟從……給予的建議","examples":[{"en":"The scientists could follow the advice given by a reputation strategist.","zh":"科學家可以跟從聲譽策略師給予的建議。"},{"en":"To follow the advice given by someone means to act according to that person’s recommendations.","zh":"follow the advice given by someone 指按照某人的建議行事。"},{"en":"A patient should follow the advice given by a doctor about medicine and rest.","zh":"病人應跟從醫生給予的關於藥物和休息的建議。"},{"en":"Following expert advice can help people avoid repeating avoidable mistakes.","zh":"跟從專家建議可以幫助人避免重複可避免的錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses using guidance from a particular source.","zh":"這個短語強調採用來自特定來源的指引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reputation strategist","meaning":"聲譽策略師","examples":[{"en":"Leslie Gaines-Ross is described as a reputation strategist.","zh":"Leslie Gaines-Ross 被描述為聲譽策略師。"},{"en":"A reputation strategist is a specialist who advises people or organisations on how to protect or repair public trust.","zh":"reputation strategist 指就如何保護或修補公眾信任向個人或機構提供建議的專家。"},{"en":"A company may hire a reputation strategist after a public complaint becomes widely discussed online.","zh":"當公開投訴在網上廣泛討論，公司可能聘請聲譽策略師。"},{"en":"Reputation strategists help plan messages, actions and long-term trust-building.","zh":"聲譽策略師幫助規劃訊息、行動和長期信任建立。"},{"en":"This phrase names a professional role in reputation management.","zh":"這個短語命名聲譽管理中的專業角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"public relations company","meaning":"公關公司","examples":[{"en":"She works at the public relations company Weber Shandwick.","zh":"她在公關公司 Weber Shandwick 工作。"},{"en":"A public relations company helps clients communicate with the public, media and stakeholders.","zh":"public relations company 指幫助客戶與公眾、傳媒和持份者溝通的公司。"},{"en":"A school may ask a public relations company for help after a serious public misunderstanding.","zh":"學校在嚴重公眾誤解後，可能向公關公司求助。"},{"en":"Public relations companies can advise on statements, interviews and reputation repair.","zh":"公關公司可以就聲明、訪問和聲譽修補提供建議。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a professional communication business.","zh":"這個短語指專業溝通業務機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"safeguard and recover reputation","meaning":"保護和挽回聲譽","examples":[{"en":"Her book discusses how to safeguard and recover reputation.","zh":"她的書討論如何保護和挽回聲譽。"},{"en":"To safeguard and recover reputation means to protect trust before damage and restore it after damage.","zh":"safeguard and recover reputation 指在受損前保護信任，並在受損後恢復信任。"},{"en":"A business can safeguard and recover reputation by being honest with customers before and after problems.","zh":"企業可以透過在問題前後都對顧客誠實，來保護和挽回聲譽。"},{"en":"Safeguarding prevents harm, while recovery deals with harm that has already happened.","zh":"保護是預防傷害，而挽回是處理已經發生的傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both prevention and repair.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋預防和修補。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"基於……","examples":[{"en":"Gaines-Ross’s strategy is based on her analysis of crisis responses.","zh":"Gaines-Ross 的策略基於她對危機回應的分析。"},{"en":"To be based on something means to use it as the foundation or reason.","zh":"be based on something 指以某事作為基礎或理由。"},{"en":"A teacher’s lesson plan may be based on students’ common mistakes.","zh":"老師的教案可能基於學生常犯錯誤。"},{"en":"A strategy based on evidence is usually stronger than one based on guesswork.","zh":"基於證據的策略通常比基於猜測的策略更強。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the source or foundation of an idea.","zh":"這個短語解釋想法的來源或基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"analysis of","meaning":"對……的分析","examples":[{"en":"Her strategy is based on an analysis of how organisations respond to crises.","zh":"她的策略基於對機構如何應對危機的分析。"},{"en":"An analysis of something is a careful study of its parts, causes or effects.","zh":"analysis of something 指仔細研究某事的部分、原因或影響。"},{"en":"A school may conduct an analysis of exam results to find weak topics.","zh":"學校可能對考試成績進行分析，以找出薄弱課題。"},{"en":"Careful analysis helps people understand what went wrong and what should change.","zh":"仔細分析幫助人理解出了甚麼錯和應該改變甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to detailed examination, not a quick opinion.","zh":"這個短語指詳細檢視，而不是快速意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"respond to crises","meaning":"應對危機","examples":[{"en":"Different organisations respond to crises in different ways.","zh":"不同機構以不同方式應對危機。"},{"en":"To respond to crises means to act or communicate when serious problems arise.","zh":"respond to crises 指在嚴重問題出現時採取行動或溝通。"},{"en":"A hospital must respond to crises quickly when many patients arrive after an accident.","zh":"當意外後大量病人抵達，醫院必須快速應對危機。"},{"en":"A good crisis response can reduce harm and preserve trust.","zh":"良好危機回應可以減少傷害並保護信任。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on action during difficult and urgent situations.","zh":"這個短語著重在困難和緊急情況中的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"desktop-printer firm","meaning":"桌面打印機公司","examples":[{"en":"Xerox is mentioned as a desktop-printer firm.","zh":"Xerox 被提及為桌面打印機公司。"},{"en":"A desktop-printer firm is a company that makes or sells printers for offices and personal desks.","zh":"desktop-printer firm 指製造或銷售辦公室和個人桌面打印機的公司。"},{"en":"A small office may buy supplies from a desktop-printer firm to print invoices and letters.","zh":"小型辦公室可能向桌面打印機公司購買用品，以列印發票和信件。"},{"en":"If business falls, a desktop-printer firm may need to change products or strategy.","zh":"如果業務下跌，桌面打印機公司可能需要改變產品或策略。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the type of company being discussed.","zh":"這個短語指出正在討論的公司類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"business plummeted","meaning":"業務暴跌","examples":[{"en":"Xerox’s business plummeted during the 1990s.","zh":"Xerox 的業務在 1990 年代暴跌。"},{"en":"If business plummeted, sales, income or activity fell very sharply.","zh":"business plummeted 指銷售、收入或活動急劇下降。"},{"en":"A restaurant’s business may plummet after several bad food reviews.","zh":"餐廳在幾篇差劣食評後，業務可能暴跌。"},{"en":"When business plummets, companies may cut costs, change leaders or rebuild trust.","zh":"當業務暴跌，公司可能削減成本、改變領導層或重建信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sudden and serious decline.","zh":"這個短語描述突然且嚴重的下跌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"shuttle disaster","meaning":"航天飛機災難","examples":[{"en":"NASA faced a crisis after the Columbia shuttle disaster.","zh":"NASA 在 Columbia 航天飛機災難後面對危機。"},{"en":"A shuttle disaster is a serious accident involving a space shuttle.","zh":"shuttle disaster 指涉及航天飛機的嚴重事故。"},{"en":"A science class may discuss a shuttle disaster when learning how safety systems fail.","zh":"科學課學習安全系統如何失效時，可能討論航天飛機災難。"},{"en":"Such disasters can lead to investigations, mourning and major changes in procedure.","zh":"這類災難可以導致調查、哀悼和程序上的重大改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a major spaceflight tragedy.","zh":"這個短語指重大太空飛行悲劇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take the heat","meaning":"承受壓力；承擔責任","examples":[{"en":"The first step is to take the heat, leader first.","zh":"第一步是承受壓力，領袖先行。"},{"en":"To take the heat means to accept criticism, pressure or blame during a difficult situation.","zh":"take the heat 指在困難情況中接受批評、壓力或責備。"},{"en":"A principal may take the heat after a school event is poorly organised.","zh":"如果學校活動安排差，校長可能要承受壓力。"},{"en":"Leaders who take the heat show that they do not hide behind junior staff.","zh":"願意承受壓力的領袖顯示他們不躲在初級職員背後。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests accepting responsibility under public pressure.","zh":"這個短語暗示在公眾壓力下承擔責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"leader first","meaning":"領袖先行","examples":[{"en":"Gaines-Ross argues that leaders should take the heat first.","zh":"Gaines-Ross 認為領袖應先承受壓力。"},{"en":"Leader first means the person in charge should act before others and accept responsibility first.","zh":"leader first 指負責人應先行動並先承擔責任。"},{"en":"In a school crisis, “leader first” means the principal speaks before blaming teachers.","zh":"在學校危機中，「領袖先行」即校長先發言，而不是責怪老師。"},{"en":"When leaders act first, the public may believe the organisation is serious about change.","zh":"當領袖先行動，公眾可能相信機構認真改變。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights responsibility at the top.","zh":"這個短語突出最高層的責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in many cases","meaning":"在很多情況下","examples":[{"en":"In many cases, public acceptance of responsibility can help.","zh":"在很多情況下，公開承擔責任可以有幫助。"},{"en":"In many cases means often, though not always.","zh":"in many cases 指經常如此，但不是永遠如此。"},{"en":"In many cases, students learn vocabulary faster when examples come from daily life.","zh":"在很多情況下，當例子來自日常生活，學生學詞彙會更快。"},{"en":"This phrase allows a general rule without claiming it is true every time.","zh":"這個短語容許提出一般規律，而不聲稱每次都正確。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving advice that usually works but has exceptions.","zh":"當提供通常有效但有例外的建議時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"chief executives","meaning":"行政總裁","examples":[{"en":"Chief executives may need to accept responsibility for corporate failings.","zh":"行政總裁可能需要為企業失誤承擔責任。"},{"en":"Chief executives are the top leaders responsible for running companies or organisations.","zh":"chief executives 指負責營運公司或機構的最高領袖。"},{"en":"A chief executive may speak publicly when a company’s product has safety problems.","zh":"當公司產品有安全問題，行政總裁可能公開發言。"},{"en":"Because chief executives hold authority, people often expect them to accept responsibility.","zh":"因為行政總裁掌握權力，人們常期望他們承擔責任。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to senior leaders, not ordinary staff.","zh":"這個短語指高層領袖，而不是普通員工。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"publicly accept responsibility for","meaning":"公開為……承擔責任","examples":[{"en":"Leaders can help by publicly accepting responsibility for failings.","zh":"領袖可以透過公開為失誤承擔責任來提供幫助。"},{"en":"To publicly accept responsibility for something means to admit before others that you are accountable.","zh":"publicly accept responsibility for something 指在他人面前承認自己需要負責。"},{"en":"A head teacher may publicly accept responsibility for poor communication with parents.","zh":"校長可能公開為與家長溝通差承擔責任。"},{"en":"Public responsibility can calm anger because people see that leaders are not hiding.","zh":"公開承擔責任可以平息憤怒，因為人們看見領袖沒有躲避。"},{"en":"This phrase describes open accountability.","zh":"這個短語描述公開問責。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"corporate failings","meaning":"企業失誤","examples":[{"en":"Corporate failings can seriously damage a company’s reputation.","zh":"企業失誤可以嚴重損害公司的聲譽。"},{"en":"Corporate failings are mistakes or failures by a company in management, ethics, service or safety.","zh":"corporate failings 指公司在管理、道德、服務或安全方面的錯誤或失敗。"},{"en":"Ignoring customer complaints is a corporate failing if it becomes part of company culture.","zh":"如果忽視顧客投訴成為公司文化，就是企業失誤。"},{"en":"Corporate failings can lead to lost sales, legal trouble and public anger.","zh":"企業失誤可以導致銷售流失、法律麻煩和公眾憤怒。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organisational failure, not one small personal mistake.","zh":"這個短語指組織層面的失敗，而不是一個小個人錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"begin to reverse","meaning":"開始扭轉","examples":[{"en":"Accepting responsibility can begin to reverse reputational damage.","zh":"承擔責任可以開始扭轉聲譽損害。"},{"en":"To begin to reverse something means to start changing a bad situation back in a better direction.","zh":"begin to reverse something 指開始把壞情況轉回較好方向。"},{"en":"A student can begin to reverse poor grades by attending class regularly and asking for help.","zh":"學生可以透過定期上課和求助來開始扭轉差成績。"},{"en":"Reversal takes time because early action only starts the recovery process.","zh":"扭轉需要時間，因為早期行動只是開始恢復過程。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the first step toward improvement.","zh":"這個短語顯示改善的第一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"freefall of reputation","meaning":"聲譽急跌","examples":[{"en":"A leader may reverse the freefall of a company’s reputation.","zh":"領袖可能扭轉公司聲譽急跌。"},{"en":"A freefall of reputation is a rapid and serious collapse in public trust or respect.","zh":"freefall of reputation 指公眾信任或尊重迅速而嚴重崩跌。"},{"en":"A brand may suffer a freefall of reputation after customers discover unsafe products.","zh":"顧客發現產品不安全後，品牌可能經歷聲譽急跌。"},{"en":"Quick and honest action can slow a reputation freefall before more damage occurs.","zh":"快速而誠實的行動可以在更多傷害發生前減慢聲譽急跌。"},{"en":"This phrase uses the image of falling fast and uncontrollably.","zh":"這個短語使用快速且失控下墜的圖像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be held responsible for","meaning":"被認為要為……負責","examples":[{"en":"A leader may be held responsible for an organisation’s failure.","zh":"領袖可能被認為要為機構失敗負責。"},{"en":"To be held responsible for something means to be judged as accountable for it.","zh":"be held responsible for something 指被判定需要為某事負責。"},{"en":"A team captain may be held responsible for poor behaviour during a match.","zh":"隊長可能因比賽中的不良行為被認為要負責。"},{"en":"People often hold leaders responsible because leaders have power to set direction.","zh":"人們常把責任歸於領袖，因為領袖有權設定方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes responsibility assigned by others.","zh":"這個短語描述由他人賦予的責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at least partly responsible","meaning":"至少要負部分責任","examples":[{"en":"The leader was held at least partly responsible for the fall from grace.","zh":"該領袖被認為至少要為聲譽墮落負部分責任。"},{"en":"At least partly responsible means responsible for some part of the problem, even if not all of it.","zh":"at least partly responsible 指至少對問題的某部分負責，即使不是全部責任。"},{"en":"A student may be at least partly responsible for a group project’s failure if they missed every meeting.","zh":"如果學生每次小組會議都缺席，就可能至少要為項目失敗負部分責任。"},{"en":"Shared responsibility can still require a leader to explain their role.","zh":"共同責任仍可能要求領袖解釋自己的角色。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids saying one person caused everything.","zh":"這個短語避免說一個人造成全部問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fall from grace","meaning":"失寵；聲譽墮落","examples":[{"en":"A serious scandal can cause a dramatic fall from grace.","zh":"嚴重醜聞可以造成戲劇性的聲譽墮落。"},{"en":"A fall from grace is a sudden loss of respect, status or public approval.","zh":"fall from grace 指突然失去尊重、地位或公眾認可。"},{"en":"A famous athlete may suffer a fall from grace after cheating is revealed.","zh":"著名運動員被揭發作弊後，可能經歷聲譽墮落。"},{"en":"A fall from grace feels dramatic because the person or organisation was once admired.","zh":"聲譽墮落感覺戲劇性，因為該人或機構曾經受人敬重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reputation collapsing from a high position.","zh":"這個短語描述聲譽從高位崩落。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"convince critics that","meaning":"使批評者相信","examples":[{"en":"It is hard to convince critics that the same leader can create change.","zh":"要使批評者相信同一位領袖可以創造改變很困難。"},{"en":"To convince critics that something is true means to make sceptical people believe it.","zh":"convince critics that something is true 指使持懷疑態度的人相信某事。"},{"en":"A school must convince critics that a new safety policy will actually protect students.","zh":"學校必須使批評者相信新的安全政策真的會保護學生。"},{"en":"Critics are hard to convince when past behaviour has damaged trust.","zh":"當過去行為已損害信任，批評者很難被說服。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on persuading people who already doubt you.","zh":"這個短語著重說服已經懷疑你的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"new direction can be charted","meaning":"可以制定新方向","examples":[{"en":"Critics may doubt that a new direction can be charted.","zh":"批評者可能懷疑是否可以制定新方向。"},{"en":"If a new direction can be charted, a new plan or path can be clearly set.","zh":"if a new direction can be charted 指可以清楚設定新的計劃或路線。"},{"en":"A school can chart a new direction by changing its teaching methods and assessment style.","zh":"學校可以透過改變教學方法和評估方式來制定新方向。"},{"en":"A new direction needs clear leadership, not only words of regret.","zh":"新方向需要清晰領導，而不只是後悔的說話。"},{"en":"This phrase uses the image of mapping a new route.","zh":"這個短語使用繪製新路線的圖像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at the helm","meaning":"掌舵；掌權","examples":[{"en":"It is difficult to chart a new direction with the same person at the helm.","zh":"同一人掌舵時，要制定新方向很困難。"},{"en":"At the helm means in control or in charge of an organisation or situation.","zh":"at the helm 指掌控或負責某機構或情況。"},{"en":"A new principal at the helm can change how a school communicates with parents.","zh":"新校長掌舵可以改變學校與家長溝通的方式。"},{"en":"When the same person remains at the helm after failure, critics may doubt real change.","zh":"失敗後同一人仍然掌舵，批評者可能懷疑是否有真正改變。"},{"en":"This phrase comes from steering a ship and means leadership control.","zh":"這個短語來自駕駛船隻，意思是掌握領導控制權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the dilemma facing","meaning":"……所面對的困境","examples":[{"en":"This is the dilemma facing the heads of the IPCC and CRU.","zh":"這就是 IPCC 和 CRU 負責人所面對的困境。"},{"en":"The dilemma facing someone is the difficult choice or problem they must deal with.","zh":"the dilemma facing someone 指某人必須處理的艱難選擇或問題。"},{"en":"The dilemma facing many students is whether to work part-time or focus fully on study.","zh":"許多學生所面對的困境是兼職還是全心學習。"},{"en":"A dilemma is hard because each option has disadvantages.","zh":"困境之所以困難，是因為每個選項都有缺點。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the difficult situation a person or group faces.","zh":"這個短語引入某人或群體面對的困難情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"heads of","meaning":"……的負責人","examples":[{"en":"The heads of the IPCC and CRU faced public criticism.","zh":"IPCC 和 CRU 的負責人面對公眾批評。"},{"en":"The heads of organisations are their leaders or people in charge.","zh":"heads of organisations 指機構的領袖或負責人。"},{"en":"The heads of several schools may meet to discuss student safety.","zh":"幾間學校的負責人可能開會討論學生安全。"},{"en":"When problems occur, the heads of organisations are often expected to respond first.","zh":"問題發生時，機構負責人常被期望首先回應。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to senior leaders, not ordinary members.","zh":"這個短語指高層領袖，而不是普通成員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be blamed for","meaning":"因……而被責備","examples":[{"en":"Both leaders were blamed for their organisations’ problems.","zh":"兩位領袖都因其機構的問題而被責備。"},{"en":"To be blamed for something means to be accused of causing or failing to prevent it.","zh":"be blamed for something 指被指造成某事或未能阻止某事。"},{"en":"A coach may be blamed for a team’s poor preparation before a match.","zh":"球隊賽前準備不足時，教練可能被責備。"},{"en":"Leaders are often blamed when systems fail because they are expected to manage them.","zh":"系統失敗時，領袖常被責備，因為他們被期望管理系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes responsibility assigned through criticism.","zh":"這個短語描述透過批評賦予責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not least for","meaning":"尤其是因為","examples":[{"en":"They were criticised not least for the way they dealt with critics.","zh":"他們受到批評，尤其是因為他們應對批評者的方式。"},{"en":"Not least for means especially because of one important reason among others.","zh":"not least for 指在多個原因中，尤其因為某個重要原因。"},{"en":"The school trip was unpopular, not least for its high cost.","zh":"學校旅行不受歡迎，尤其是因為費用高。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a reason that is particularly important, though not the only one.","zh":"這個短語突出一個特別重要但不是唯一的原因。"},{"en":"It is useful when adding emphasis to one cause of criticism.","zh":"當強調某個被批評原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the way in which","meaning":"……的方式","examples":[{"en":"They were criticised for the way in which they dealt with critics.","zh":"他們因應對批評者的方式而受到批評。"},{"en":"The way in which something is done means the method or manner used to do it.","zh":"the way in which something is done 指做某事所用的方法或方式。"},{"en":"Parents may judge a school by the way in which it handles complaints.","zh":"家長可能根據學校處理投訴的方式來評價學校。"},{"en":"Sometimes people criticise not the decision itself, but the way in which it was explained.","zh":"有時人們批評的不是決定本身，而是解釋該決定的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on manner, process or method.","zh":"這個短語著重方式、過程或方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"deal with critics","meaning":"應對批評者","examples":[{"en":"The organisations were criticised for how they dealt with critics.","zh":"這些機構因其應對批評者的方式而受到批評。"},{"en":"To deal with critics means to respond to people who question or attack your actions.","zh":"deal with critics 指回應質疑或攻擊你行動的人。"},{"en":"A writer must learn to deal with critics after publishing a controversial article.","zh":"作家發表具爭議文章後，必須學會應對批評者。"},{"en":"Dealing with critics badly can make criticism grow stronger.","zh":"應對批評者不當可以令批評更強。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to handling opposition, not simply silencing it.","zh":"這個短語指處理反對聲音，而不是單純壓制它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be subjected to","meaning":"遭受；受到","examples":[{"en":"Both leaders were subjected to public calls for their removal.","zh":"兩位領袖都受到公眾要求撤換的壓力。"},{"en":"To be subjected to something means to experience something unpleasant or difficult.","zh":"be subjected to something 指經歷不愉快或困難的事情。"},{"en":"A student may be subjected to unfair comments online after a misunderstanding.","zh":"學生在誤會後可能遭受網上不公平評論。"},{"en":"Being subjected to public pressure can force leaders to respond quickly.","zh":"受到公眾壓力可以迫使領袖快速回應。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes being exposed to criticism, pressure or treatment.","zh":"這個短語常描述承受批評、壓力或對待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"public calls for","meaning":"公眾要求……","examples":[{"en":"There were public calls for the removal of both leaders.","zh":"當時有公眾要求撤換兩位領袖。"},{"en":"Public calls for something are open demands made by members of the public.","zh":"public calls for something 指公眾公開提出的要求。"},{"en":"After a serious accident, there may be public calls for better road safety.","zh":"嚴重意外後，可能有公眾要求改善道路安全。"},{"en":"Public calls can put pressure on leaders because many people are asking for action.","zh":"公眾要求可以向領袖施壓，因為許多人要求行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible public demand.","zh":"這個短語描述可見的公眾要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"removal","meaning":"免職；撤換","examples":[{"en":"Some critics called for the removal of the organisations’ heads.","zh":"有些批評者要求撤換這些機構的負責人。"},{"en":"Removal means taking someone out of a position or taking something away.","zh":"removal 指把某人從職位上移走，或把某物拿走。"},{"en":"Parents may call for the removal of a dangerous playground structure.","zh":"家長可能要求移除危險的遊樂場設施。"},{"en":"Removal of a leader may signal that an organisation wants a new start.","zh":"撤換領袖可能表示機構想重新開始。"},{"en":"This word can refer to dismissal, replacement or physical taking away.","zh":"這個詞可指免職、替換或實際移走。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"appear to believe","meaning":"似乎相信","examples":[{"en":"Both organisations appear to believe they can repair their reputations.","zh":"兩個機構似乎相信自己可以修補聲譽。"},{"en":"Appear to believe means seem to think something is true, based on their actions or words.","zh":"appear to believe 指根據行動或說話，看起來認為某事是真的。"},{"en":"The school appears to believe that shorter tests will reduce student stress.","zh":"學校似乎相信較短測驗會減少學生壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the writer is making a careful judgement, not claiming direct knowledge.","zh":"當作者作出謹慎判斷，而不是聲稱直接知道時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It suggests an interpretation from outside observation.","zh":"它暗示根據外部觀察作出的詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"repair reputations","meaning":"修補聲譽","examples":[{"en":"The organisations wanted to repair their reputations without changing leaders.","zh":"這些機構想在不更換領袖的情況下修補聲譽。"},{"en":"To repair reputations means to restore public trust after reputations have been damaged.","zh":"repair reputations 指在聲譽受損後恢復公眾信任。"},{"en":"A shop may repair its reputation by replacing faulty goods and apologising clearly.","zh":"商店可以透過更換有問題貨品和清楚道歉來修補聲譽。"},{"en":"Repairing reputations takes repeated honest action because trust does not return immediately.","zh":"修補聲譽需要反覆誠實行動，因為信任不會立即回來。"},{"en":"This phrase is similar to rebuilding reputation, but it can suggest fixing specific damage.","zh":"這個短語與重建聲譽相近，但可暗示修復特定損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"change of leadership","meaning":"領導層變動","examples":[{"en":"Some critics believed a change of leadership was necessary.","zh":"有些批評者相信領導層變動是必要的。"},{"en":"A change of leadership means replacing the people in charge.","zh":"change of leadership 指更換負責人。"},{"en":"A company may need a change of leadership after repeated failures in safety management.","zh":"公司在安全管理反覆失敗後，可能需要領導層變動。"},{"en":"Changing leadership can signal a new direction, but it does not solve every problem by itself.","zh":"更換領導層可以表示新方向，但本身不能解決所有問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on replacing leaders, not just changing policy.","zh":"這個短語著重更換領袖，而不只是改變政策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be outlined by","meaning":"由……概述","examples":[{"en":"The second step outlined by Gaines-Ross is to communicate tirelessly.","zh":"由 Gaines-Ross 概述的第二步是不懈地溝通。"},{"en":"To be outlined by someone means to be briefly explained or presented by that person.","zh":"be outlined by someone 指由某人簡要解釋或提出。"},{"en":"The homework rules outlined by the teacher helped students understand what to submit.","zh":"由老師概述的功課規則幫助學生明白要提交甚麼。"},{"en":"Outlining steps makes a complex plan easier to follow.","zh":"概述步驟令複雜計劃更容易跟從。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who presented the main points.","zh":"這個短語指出誰提出主要重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"communicate tirelessly","meaning":"不懈地溝通","examples":[{"en":"Organisations in crisis should communicate tirelessly.","zh":"處於危機中的機構應不懈地溝通。"},{"en":"To communicate tirelessly means to keep explaining, answering and updating without giving up.","zh":"communicate tirelessly 指不停解釋、回答和更新，而不放棄。"},{"en":"During a school closure, staff may communicate tirelessly with parents through messages and meetings.","zh":"學校停課期間，職員可能透過訊息和會議與家長不懈地溝通。"},{"en":"Tireless communication reduces rumours because people receive clearer information.","zh":"不懈溝通可以減少謠言，因為人們收到更清楚資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests repeated, patient and active communication.","zh":"這個短語暗示反覆、耐心和主動的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"avoid the media and the public","meaning":"迴避傳媒和公眾","examples":[{"en":"Many climate researchers avoided the media and the public.","zh":"許多氣候研究人員迴避傳媒和公眾。"},{"en":"To avoid the media and the public means to refuse interviews, public appearances or direct communication.","zh":"avoid the media and the public 指拒絕訪問、公眾露面或直接溝通。"},{"en":"A company under criticism may avoid the media and the public by sending only short written statements.","zh":"受批評的公司可能只發短書面聲明，迴避傳媒和公眾。"},{"en":"Avoiding public contact can make people suspect that questions are being dodged.","zh":"迴避公眾接觸可以令人懷疑問題被逃避。"},{"en":"This phrase describes withdrawal from public communication.","zh":"這個短語描述退出公共溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at least until","meaning":"至少直到……","examples":[{"en":"They avoided interviews at least until the enquiries were finished.","zh":"他們至少直到調查完成前都迴避訪問。"},{"en":"At least until means not before a certain time, and possibly longer.","zh":"at least until 指不早於某時間，並可能更久。"},{"en":"Students may not receive their results at least until the marking is complete.","zh":"學生可能至少直到評分完成前都不會收到成績。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a minimum waiting time.","zh":"這個短語設定最低等待時間。"},{"en":"It suggests the action may continue even after that point.","zh":"它暗示該行動可能在該時間點後仍繼續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"official enquiries","meaning":"官方調查","examples":[{"en":"The researchers waited for official enquiries to conclude their reports.","zh":"研究人員等待官方調查完成報告。"},{"en":"Official enquiries are formal investigations carried out by authorised bodies.","zh":"official enquiries 指由授權機構進行的正式調查。"},{"en":"After a building accident, official enquiries may examine safety records and witness statements.","zh":"建築事故後，官方調查可能審查安全紀錄和證人陳述。"},{"en":"Official enquiries can give authority to findings because they follow formal procedures.","zh":"官方調查因遵循正式程序，可以令結果更具權威。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal investigations, not casual questioning.","zh":"這個短語指正式調查，而不是隨便提問。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"conclude reports","meaning":"完成報告","examples":[{"en":"The official enquiries had not yet concluded their reports.","zh":"官方調查尚未完成報告。"},{"en":"To conclude reports means to finish them and reach final findings or statements.","zh":"conclude reports 指完成報告並得出最終結果或陳述。"},{"en":"A school committee may conclude its report after interviewing teachers, students and parents.","zh":"學校委員會訪問老師、學生和家長後，可能完成報告。"},{"en":"Reports cannot guide action properly until they are concluded and released.","zh":"報告在完成和發布前，不能有效指導行動。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on finishing an official written investigation.","zh":"這個短語著重完成正式書面調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reaction may be understandable","meaning":"這種反應可以理解","examples":[{"en":"This reaction may be understandable, but it has backfired.","zh":"這種反應可以理解，但它適得其反。"},{"en":"Reaction may be understandable means people can see why someone acted that way, even if it was not wise.","zh":"reaction may be understandable 指人們可以明白某人為何那樣做，即使做法未必明智。"},{"en":"A student’s nervous silence after being blamed may be understandable.","zh":"學生被責備後緊張地沉默，這種反應可以理解。"},{"en":"An understandable reaction can still create bad results if it is poorly judged.","zh":"可以理解的反應，如果判斷不佳，仍可能造成壞結果。"},{"en":"This phrase separates sympathy for the reaction from approval of it.","zh":"這個短語把對反應的理解與贊同分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"backfire","meaning":"適得其反","examples":[{"en":"Avoiding the media has backfired.","zh":"迴避傳媒已經適得其反。"},{"en":"To backfire means to produce the opposite result from the one intended.","zh":"backfire 指產生與原意相反的結果。"},{"en":"A student who lies to avoid punishment may find that the lie backfires.","zh":"學生為避免受罰而說謊，可能發現謊言適得其反。"},{"en":"A plan can backfire when people interpret it in a negative way.","zh":"當人們以負面方式解讀計劃，計劃就可能適得其反。"},{"en":"This word describes a strategy turning against the person who used it.","zh":"這個詞描述策略反過來傷害使用它的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"journalists following the story","meaning":"追蹤事件的記者","examples":[{"en":"Journalists following the story could not find spokespeople.","zh":"追蹤事件的記者找不到發言人。"},{"en":"Journalists following the story are reporters who are actively covering and investigating an issue.","zh":"journalists following the story 指正在積極報道和調查某議題的記者。"},{"en":"Journalists following a school scandal may contact parents, teachers and officials.","zh":"追蹤學校醜聞的記者可能聯絡家長、老師和官員。"},{"en":"If journalists cannot find clear voices, they may rely more on critics or rumours.","zh":"如果記者找不到清楚聲音，可能更依賴批評者或謠言。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reporters tracking an ongoing event.","zh":"這個短語描述追蹤持續事件的記者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be unable to find","meaning":"找不到","examples":[{"en":"Journalists were unable to find people willing to defend climate science.","zh":"記者找不到願意為氣候科學辯護的人。"},{"en":"To be unable to find someone or something means to fail to locate or identify it.","zh":"be unable to find someone or something 指未能找到或識別某人或某物。"},{"en":"A student may be unable to find a quiet place to study during lunchtime.","zh":"學生午飯時間可能找不到安靜地方溫習。"},{"en":"If reporters are unable to find official voices, public discussion may become one-sided.","zh":"如果記者找不到官方聲音，公眾討論可能變得片面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes failure to locate what is needed.","zh":"這個短語描述未能找到所需事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"spokespeople willing to","meaning":"願意……的發言人","examples":[{"en":"Journalists could not find spokespeople willing to defend climate science.","zh":"記者找不到願意為氣候科學辯護的發言人。"},{"en":"Spokespeople willing to do something are representatives prepared to speak publicly or explain a position.","zh":"spokespeople willing to do something 指準備公開發言或解釋立場的代表。"},{"en":"A hospital may need spokespeople willing to answer questions after a medical mistake.","zh":"醫院在醫療錯誤後，可能需要願意回答問題的發言人。"},{"en":"Without willing spokespeople, an organisation’s side may not be heard clearly.","zh":"沒有願意發言的發言人，機構一方可能無法被清楚聽見。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on representatives who are ready to speak.","zh":"這個短語著重準備發言的代表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"defend climate science","meaning":"為氣候科學辯護","examples":[{"en":"Few spokespeople were willing to defend climate science publicly.","zh":"很少發言人願意公開為氣候科學辯護。"},{"en":"To defend climate science means to explain and support its evidence, methods and credibility against criticism.","zh":"defend climate science 指面對批評時解釋並支持其證據、方法和可信度。"},{"en":"A science teacher may defend climate science by showing students how temperature records are checked.","zh":"科學老師可能透過展示溫度記錄如何被核查來為氣候科學辯護。"},{"en":"Public defence matters when critics are shaping the story.","zh":"當批評者正在塑造故事時，公開辯護很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase means answering criticism, not attacking people personally.","zh":"這個短語指回應批評，而不是人身攻擊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"no comment","meaning":"無可奉告","examples":[{"en":"In this case, no comment was not an effective response.","zh":"在這個情況下，無可奉告不是有效回應。"},{"en":"No comment is a phrase used when someone refuses to answer a question publicly.","zh":"no comment 是某人公開拒絕回答問題時使用的短語。"},{"en":"A politician may say “no comment” when reporters ask about an ongoing investigation.","zh":"當記者問及進行中的調查，政治人物可能說「無可奉告」。"},{"en":"Saying no comment can protect legal interests, but it may also look evasive.","zh":"說無可奉告可以保護法律利益，但也可能看似逃避。"},{"en":"This phrase often creates suspicion if people expect explanation.","zh":"如果人們期待解釋，這個短語常引起懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be interpreted as","meaning":"被解讀為","examples":[{"en":"No comment is commonly interpreted as an admission of guilt.","zh":"無可奉告通常被解讀為認罪。"},{"en":"To be interpreted as something means to be understood or read in that way by others.","zh":"be interpreted as something 指被他人理解或解讀為某意思。"},{"en":"A student’s silence may be interpreted as agreement, even if they are only shy.","zh":"學生的沉默可能被解讀為同意，即使他只是害羞。"},{"en":"Public actions can be interpreted differently from what the speaker intended.","zh":"公開行動可能被解讀成與說話者原意不同的意思。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how others understand a sign or response.","zh":"這個短語著重他人如何理解某信號或回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"admission of guilt","meaning":"認罪；承認有罪","examples":[{"en":"Silence was interpreted as an admission of collective guilt.","zh":"沉默被解讀為承認集體有罪。"},{"en":"An admission of guilt is a statement or sign that someone accepts they did something wrong.","zh":"admission of guilt 指某人承認自己做錯事的說法或跡象。"},{"en":"Returning stolen money can look like an admission of guilt if no explanation is given.","zh":"如果沒有解釋，歸還偷來的錢可能看似認罪。"},{"en":"People may see silence as guilt when they already distrust the speaker.","zh":"當人們已經不信任說話者，可能把沉默看作有罪。"},{"en":"This phrase is serious because it suggests responsibility for wrongdoing.","zh":"這個短語很嚴重，因為它暗示要為不當行為負責。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"silent, collective guilt","meaning":"沉默的集體罪責","examples":[{"en":"No comment was interpreted as silent, collective guilt.","zh":"無可奉告被解讀為沉默的集體罪責。"},{"en":"Silent, collective guilt means a group seems guilty because no one speaks to defend it.","zh":"silent, collective guilt 指因沒有人開口辯護，整個群體看似有罪。"},{"en":"If a whole class stays silent after cheating is discovered, teachers may suspect collective guilt.","zh":"如果作弊被發現後全班沉默，老師可能懷疑存在集體罪責。"},{"en":"Silence can wrongly make everyone appear responsible for the actions of a few.","zh":"沉默可以錯誤地令所有人看似要為少數人的行為負責。"},{"en":"This phrase links lack of response with group responsibility.","zh":"這個短語把缺乏回應與群體責任連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"remaining visible","meaning":"保持曝光","examples":[{"en":"Remaining visible is only a start for climate scientists.","zh":"對氣候科學家來說，保持曝光只是開始。"},{"en":"Remaining visible means continuing to appear publicly and communicate rather than disappearing from attention.","zh":"remaining visible 指繼續公開露面和溝通，而不是從公眾注意中消失。"},{"en":"A school principal remains visible during a crisis by meeting parents and answering questions.","zh":"學校危機期間，校長透過會見家長和回答問題保持曝光。"},{"en":"Visibility helps reduce rumours because people can see leaders responding.","zh":"曝光有助減少謠言，因為人們看見領袖正在回應。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses public presence, not hiding.","zh":"這個短語強調公開存在，而不是躲藏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"only a start","meaning":"只是開始","examples":[{"en":"Speaking to the public is only a start.","zh":"向公眾說話只是開始。"},{"en":"Only a start means just the first step, not a complete solution.","zh":"only a start 指只是第一步，不是完整解決方法。"},{"en":"Buying a grammar book is only a start; students still need practice and feedback.","zh":"購買文法書只是開始；學生仍需要練習和回饋。"},{"en":"A first apology may begin repair, but deeper change must follow.","zh":"第一次道歉可能開始修補，但之後必須有更深層改變。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that more work is needed.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者仍需要更多工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be careful what one says","meaning":"小心自己的說話","examples":[{"en":"Climate scientists need to be careful what they say.","zh":"氣候科學家需要小心自己的說話。"},{"en":"To be careful what one says means to choose words wisely because the situation is sensitive.","zh":"be careful what one says 指因情況敏感而謹慎選擇用語。"},{"en":"A teacher should be careful what she says when discussing a student’s private problem.","zh":"老師討論學生私人問題時，應小心自己的說話。"},{"en":"Careless words can create new misunderstandings during a crisis.","zh":"危機期間，粗心說話可以造成新誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that speech can have serious consequences.","zh":"這個短語提醒說話可能有嚴重後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"face doubts about","meaning":"面對對……的疑慮","examples":[{"en":"They face doubts about their results, conduct and honesty.","zh":"他們面對對其結果、行為和誠信的疑慮。"},{"en":"To face doubts about something means to experience public questioning or suspicion about it.","zh":"face doubts about something 指某事受到公眾質疑或懷疑。"},{"en":"A charity may face doubts about its spending after unclear financial reports.","zh":"慈善機構在財務報告不清後，可能面對對其開支的疑慮。"},{"en":"Doubts about honesty are serious because they affect trust more deeply than simple mistakes.","zh":"對誠信的疑慮很嚴重，因為它比簡單錯誤更深地影響信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being questioned by others.","zh":"這個短語描述受到他人質疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"published results","meaning":"已發表的研究結果","examples":[{"en":"The public questioned the scientists’ published results.","zh":"公眾質疑科學家已發表的研究結果。"},{"en":"Published results are findings that have been formally released in reports, papers or articles.","zh":"published results 指已在報告、論文或文章中正式發布的研究發現。"},{"en":"A university may publish results from a study on student sleep and exam performance.","zh":"大學可能發表關於學生睡眠和考試表現的研究結果。"},{"en":"If published results contain errors, the researchers may need to correct them publicly.","zh":"如果已發表的研究結果含有錯誤，研究人員可能需要公開更正。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to research findings that others can read.","zh":"這個短語指他人可以閱讀的研究發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"conduct and honesty","meaning":"行為和誠信","examples":[{"en":"The scandal raised doubts about scientists’ conduct and honesty.","zh":"醜聞引起對科學家行為和誠信的疑慮。"},{"en":"Conduct and honesty refer to how people behave and whether they tell the truth.","zh":"conduct and honesty 指人們如何行事，以及是否誠實。"},{"en":"A school leader’s conduct and honesty matter when handling parent complaints.","zh":"學校領袖處理家長投訴時，其行為和誠信很重要。"},{"en":"If conduct and honesty are questioned, technical explanations may not be enough to restore trust.","zh":"如果行為和誠信受到質疑，技術解釋可能不足以恢復信任。"},{"en":"This phrase joins behaviour with moral credibility.","zh":"這個短語把行為與道德可信度連在一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"it simply won’t work for","meaning":"對……來說根本行不通","examples":[{"en":"It simply won’t work for scientists to ignore questions about integrity.","zh":"對科學家來說，忽視關於誠信的問題根本行不通。"},{"en":"It simply won’t work for someone to do something means that approach will not succeed.","zh":"it simply won’t work for someone to do something 指某做法不會成功。"},{"en":"It simply won’t work for students to memorise essays without understanding the question.","zh":"對學生來說，只背文章而不理解題目根本行不通。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly rejects a strategy as ineffective.","zh":"這個短語強烈否定某策略，認為它無效。"},{"en":"It is useful when a plan is clearly unsuitable for the problem.","zh":"當計劃明顯不適合問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"appeal to","meaning":"訴諸；依靠","examples":[{"en":"Scientists continued to appeal to the weight of the evidence.","zh":"科學家繼續訴諸氣候變化證據的份量。"},{"en":"To appeal to something means to rely on it as support for an argument.","zh":"appeal to something 指依靠某事作為論點支持。"},{"en":"A student may appeal to exam data to show that extra practice improved results.","zh":"學生可能依靠考試數據來顯示額外練習改善了成績。"},{"en":"Appealing to evidence works best when people trust the evidence and the people presenting it.","zh":"訴諸證據最有效，是在人們信任證據和提出證據的人時。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using a source of authority or support.","zh":"這個短語描述使用權威或支持來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the weight of the evidence","meaning":"證據的份量","examples":[{"en":"Scientists appealed to the weight of the evidence on climate change.","zh":"科學家訴諸氣候變化方面證據的份量。"},{"en":"The weight of the evidence means the overall strength of many pieces of evidence taken together.","zh":"the weight of the evidence 指多項證據合起來的整體力量。"},{"en":"A teacher may look at homework, tests and classwork to judge the weight of the evidence about a student’s progress.","zh":"老師可能查看功課、測驗和課堂表現，以判斷關於學生進步的證據份量。"},{"en":"One weak detail may matter less if the weight of the evidence points clearly one way.","zh":"如果證據的整體份量清楚指向一方，一個薄弱細節可能較不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the total force of evidence, not one isolated fact.","zh":"這個短語著重證據的總體力量，而不是單一孤立事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"refuse to discuss","meaning":"拒絕討論","examples":[{"en":"Scientists could not rebuild trust while refusing to discuss integrity.","zh":"科學家在拒絕討論誠信時，無法重建信任。"},{"en":"To refuse to discuss something means to deliberately avoid talking about it.","zh":"refuse to discuss something 指刻意避免談論某事。"},{"en":"A company that refuses to discuss customer complaints may look irresponsible.","zh":"拒絕討論顧客投訴的公司可能看似不負責任。"},{"en":"Refusing discussion can make people believe there is something to hide.","zh":"拒絕討論可以令人相信有事情要隱瞞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active avoidance of a topic.","zh":"這個短語描述主動迴避某話題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"integrity of the profession","meaning":"專業操守","examples":[{"en":"The public questioned the integrity of the scientific profession.","zh":"公眾質疑科學專業的專業操守。"},{"en":"The integrity of the profession means the honesty, ethical standards and trustworthiness of a professional group.","zh":"integrity of the profession 指某專業群體的誠實、道德標準和可信度。"},{"en":"Cheating in exams can damage the integrity of the teaching profession if teachers are involved.","zh":"如果老師涉及考試作弊，就可能損害教育專業的專業操守。"},{"en":"If professional integrity is doubted, people may reject even accurate advice.","zh":"如果專業操守受到懷疑，人們甚至可能拒絕準確建議。"},{"en":"This phrase concerns moral trust in a whole profession.","zh":"這個短語關乎對整個專業的道德信任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be increased by","meaning":"因……而加劇","examples":[{"en":"The harm was increased by a perceived reluctance to admit mistakes.","zh":"傷害因被認為不願承認錯誤而加劇。"},{"en":"To be increased by something means to become greater because of that factor.","zh":"be increased by something 指因某因素而變得更大。"},{"en":"Student stress may be increased by unclear exam instructions.","zh":"學生壓力可能因考試指示不清而加劇。"},{"en":"Damage can be increased when people feel leaders are not being honest.","zh":"當人們覺得領袖不誠實，傷害可以加劇。"},{"en":"This phrase links a worsening result with its cause.","zh":"這個短語把惡化結果與原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"perceived reluctance to","meaning":"被認為不願意……","examples":[{"en":"The perceived reluctance to admit mistakes increased the damage.","zh":"被認為不願承認錯誤加劇了傷害。"},{"en":"Perceived reluctance to do something means people think someone is unwilling to do it.","zh":"perceived reluctance to do something 指人們認為某人不願做某事。"},{"en":"A manager’s perceived reluctance to apologise can make staff angrier.","zh":"經理被認為不願道歉，可以令員工更憤怒。"},{"en":"Even if the reluctance is only perceived, it can still affect trust.","zh":"即使不願意只是被認為存在，它仍可以影響信任。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how unwillingness appears to others.","zh":"這個短語著重不願意在他人眼中如何呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"admit the possibility of","meaning":"承認……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"Scientists needed to admit the possibility of mistakes.","zh":"科學家需要承認錯誤的可能性。"},{"en":"To admit the possibility of something means to accept that it may have happened or may be true.","zh":"admit the possibility of something 指接受某事可能已發生或可能是真實的。"},{"en":"A teacher should admit the possibility of marking errors when several students raise the same concern.","zh":"當幾名學生提出同一疑慮，老師應承認評分錯誤的可能性。"},{"en":"Admitting possibility does not always mean admitting guilt; it shows openness to checking.","zh":"承認可能性不一定等於認罪；它顯示願意核查。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing uncertainty honestly.","zh":"當誠實討論不確定性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"mistakes or wrongdoing","meaning":"錯誤或不當行為","examples":[{"en":"The public wanted scientists to discuss possible mistakes or wrongdoing.","zh":"公眾希望科學家討論可能的錯誤或不當行為。"},{"en":"Mistakes or wrongdoing means errors, poor judgement or unethical behaviour.","zh":"mistakes or wrongdoing 指錯誤、判斷失誤或不道德行為。"},{"en":"A school investigation may examine whether a problem came from mistakes or wrongdoing.","zh":"學校調查可能審視問題是來自錯誤還是不當行為。"},{"en":"Mistakes may require correction, while wrongdoing may require accountability.","zh":"錯誤可能需要更正，而不當行為可能需要問責。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both accidental errors and more serious misconduct.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋意外錯誤和更嚴重的行為失當。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be put forward by","meaning":"由……提出","examples":[{"en":"The third step put forward by Gaines-Ross concerns critics and competitors.","zh":"由 Gaines-Ross 提出的第三步涉及批評者和競爭者。"},{"en":"To be put forward by someone means to be proposed or suggested by that person.","zh":"be put forward by someone 指由某人提出或建議。"},{"en":"A new recycling plan was put forward by the student council.","zh":"一項新回收計劃由學生會提出。"},{"en":"Ideas put forward by experts may guide action during difficult situations.","zh":"由專家提出的想法可以在困難情況中指導行動。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who proposed the idea.","zh":"這個短語指出誰提出該想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"underestimate critics and competitors","meaning":"低估批評者和競爭者","examples":[{"en":"Organisations should not underestimate their critics and competitors.","zh":"機構不應低估其批評者和競爭者。"},{"en":"To underestimate critics and competitors means to think they are less skilful, serious or influential than they really are.","zh":"underestimate critics and competitors 指以為他們的技巧、嚴重性或影響力比實際低。"},{"en":"A small shop should not underestimate online competitors that offer fast delivery.","zh":"小店不應低估提供快速送貨的網上競爭者。"},{"en":"Underestimating critics can leave an organisation unprepared for strong public arguments.","zh":"低估批評者可以令機構對強烈公共論點準備不足。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against dismissing opponents too easily.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要太輕易看低對手。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"recognise the skill with which","meaning":"承認……的技巧","examples":[{"en":"Climate scientists should recognise the skill with which critics used the media.","zh":"氣候科學家應承認批評者使用媒體的技巧。"},{"en":"To recognise the skill with which someone does something means to acknowledge how effectively they do it.","zh":"recognise the skill with which someone does something 指承認某人做某事很有效率或很有技巧。"},{"en":"A teacher may recognise the skill with which a student explains a difficult idea.","zh":"老師可能承認學生解釋困難概念的技巧。"},{"en":"Recognising an opponent’s skill helps people respond more realistically.","zh":"承認對手的技巧有助人更現實地回應。"},{"en":"This phrase means admitting ability, even when you disagree with the person.","zh":"這個短語表示承認能力，即使你不同意那個人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"opponents of climate research","meaning":"氣候研究的反對者","examples":[{"en":"Opponents of climate research executed effective campaigns.","zh":"氣候研究的反對者執行了有效宣傳活動。"},{"en":"Opponents of climate research are people or groups who challenge, criticise or reject that research.","zh":"opponents of climate research 指挑戰、批評或拒絕該研究的人或群體。"},{"en":"Opponents of a school policy may write letters, attend meetings and speak to the media.","zh":"學校政策的反對者可能寫信、出席會議並向傳媒發言。"},{"en":"Opponents can shape public debate if they organise their message effectively.","zh":"如果反對者有效組織訊息，就可以塑造公共辯論。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies people on the opposing side of the issue.","zh":"這個短語指出議題中站在反對一方的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"execute campaigns","meaning":"執行宣傳活動","examples":[{"en":"Critics executed campaigns through Internet blogs and other media.","zh":"批評者透過網誌和其他媒體執行宣傳活動。"},{"en":"To execute campaigns means to carry out organised efforts to influence people.","zh":"execute campaigns 指實施有組織的行動以影響人們。"},{"en":"A charity may execute a campaign to encourage blood donation.","zh":"慈善機構可能執行宣傳活動，鼓勵捐血。"},{"en":"Well-executed campaigns can change public opinion by repeating clear messages.","zh":"執行良好的宣傳活動可以透過反覆清晰訊息改變公眾意見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes putting a planned campaign into action.","zh":"這個短語描述把計劃好的活動付諸行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Internet blogs","meaning":"網誌","examples":[{"en":"Critics used Internet blogs to spread their arguments.","zh":"批評者使用網誌傳播他們的論點。"},{"en":"Internet blogs are online pages where individuals or groups publish opinions, stories or analysis.","zh":"Internet blogs 指個人或群體發布意見、故事或分析的網上頁面。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to read Internet blogs carefully and check whether sources are reliable.","zh":"老師可能要求學生仔細閱讀網誌，並檢查來源是否可靠。"},{"en":"Internet blogs can spread ideas quickly because readers can share posts easily.","zh":"網誌可以快速傳播想法，因為讀者可以容易分享文章。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to online writing platforms, not printed newspapers.","zh":"這個短語指網上寫作平台，而不是印刷報紙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"other media","meaning":"其他媒體","examples":[{"en":"Opponents used Internet blogs and other media effectively.","zh":"反對者有效使用網誌和其他媒體。"},{"en":"Other media means additional communication channels, such as newspapers, television, radio or social platforms.","zh":"other media 指其他溝通渠道，例如報紙、電視、電台或社交平台。"},{"en":"A school may use newsletters, websites and other media to inform parents.","zh":"學校可能使用通訊、網站和其他媒體通知家長。"},{"en":"Using other media helps a message reach different audiences.","zh":"使用其他媒體幫助訊息接觸不同受眾。"},{"en":"This phrase broadens the communication methods beyond the first example mentioned.","zh":"這個短語把溝通方法擴展到首先提到的例子以外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"acknowledge the validity of","meaning":"承認……的合理性","examples":[{"en":"Scientists should acknowledge the validity of some criticisms.","zh":"科學家應承認部分批評的合理性。"},{"en":"To acknowledge the validity of something means to accept that it has some truth or reasonable basis.","zh":"acknowledge the validity of something 指承認某事有一定真實性或合理基礎。"},{"en":"A teacher may acknowledge the validity of students’ complaints about too many tests.","zh":"老師可能承認學生關於測驗太多的投訴有合理性。"},{"en":"Acknowledging valid criticism can make later disagreement more credible.","zh":"承認合理批評可以令之後的不同意見更可信。"},{"en":"This phrase means accepting a fair point, not surrendering completely.","zh":"這個短語表示接受合理之處，而不是完全讓步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"some of their criticisms","meaning":"他們部分批評","examples":[{"en":"Some of their criticisms were valid.","zh":"他們部分批評是合理的。"},{"en":"Some of their criticisms means not all, but a portion of the points they made.","zh":"some of their criticisms 指不是全部，而是他們提出的部分批評。"},{"en":"Parents may be wrong about one school policy but correct in some of their criticisms about communication.","zh":"家長對某校政可能錯，但他們對溝通的部分批評可能正確。"},{"en":"Recognising some criticisms as fair can reduce hostility in a debate.","zh":"承認部分批評公平，可以減少辯論中的敵意。"},{"en":"This phrase separates valid points from weaker or unfair ones.","zh":"這個短語把合理觀點與較弱或不公平觀點分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"For instance, climate scientists need better standards of transparency.","zh":"例如，氣候科學家需要更好的透明度標準。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance 指例如。"},{"en":"Some school rules protect safety; for instance, students must wear goggles in the laboratory.","zh":"有些學校規則保障安全；例如，學生在實驗室必須戴護目鏡。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a specific example to support a general point.","zh":"這個短語引入具體例子，以支持一般論點。"},{"en":"It helps readers move from an idea to a concrete case.","zh":"它幫助讀者由概念走向具體案例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"standards of transparency","meaning":"透明度標準","examples":[{"en":"Climate scientists need better standards of transparency.","zh":"氣候科學家需要更好的透明度標準。"},{"en":"Standards of transparency are rules or expectations about how openly information is shared.","zh":"standards of transparency 指關於資訊應多公開分享的規則或期望。"},{"en":"A school can improve standards of transparency by publishing clear fee lists and decision processes.","zh":"學校可以透過發布清晰收費表和決策流程來改善透明度標準。"},{"en":"Better transparency standards reduce suspicion because people can see how decisions are made.","zh":"更好的透明度標準可以減少懷疑，因為人們能看到決定如何作出。"},{"en":"This phrase connects openness with trust.","zh":"這個短語把公開性與信任連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"allow for scrutiny","meaning":"容許審查","examples":[{"en":"Better transparency would allow for scrutiny by peers and critics.","zh":"更好的透明度會容許同行和批評者審查。"},{"en":"To allow for scrutiny means to make it possible for others to examine something closely.","zh":"allow for scrutiny 指使他人能夠仔細檢查某事。"},{"en":"A charity can allow for scrutiny by publishing detailed accounts online.","zh":"慈善機構可以透過在網上發布詳細帳目來容許審查。"},{"en":"Scrutiny can expose errors, but it can also strengthen trust when work is sound.","zh":"審查可以揭露錯誤，但當工作可靠時，也可以加強信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making close checking possible.","zh":"這個短語描述使仔細檢查成為可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"peers","meaning":"同行","examples":[{"en":"Scientific work should be open to scrutiny by peers.","zh":"科學工作應開放給同行審查。"},{"en":"Peers are people at a similar professional level or with similar expertise.","zh":"peers 指處於相似專業水平或有相似專門知識的人。"},{"en":"A student may ask peers to read an essay before handing it in.","zh":"學生可能請同學在提交前閱讀文章。"},{"en":"Peer checking helps because people with similar knowledge can spot problems.","zh":"同行檢查有幫助，因為有相似知識的人可以發現問題。"},{"en":"This word often refers to professional equals, not superiors.","zh":"這個詞常指專業上的同等人士，而不是上司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"outside the world of research","meaning":"研究界以外","examples":[{"en":"Critics from outside the world of research also wanted scrutiny.","zh":"研究界以外的批評者也希望審查。"},{"en":"Outside the world of research means not belonging to the professional research community.","zh":"outside the world of research 指不屬於專業研究社群。"},{"en":"Parents outside the world of education may still ask fair questions about school policy.","zh":"教育界以外的家長仍可能對學校政策提出合理問題。"},{"en":"People outside a profession can notice communication problems that experts overlook.","zh":"專業以外的人可以注意到專家忽略的溝通問題。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts specialists with outsiders.","zh":"這個短語把專家與外界人士作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"engage with","meaning":"與……接觸；交流","examples":[{"en":"Climate scientists need to engage with their critics.","zh":"氣候科學家需要與批評者接觸。"},{"en":"To engage with someone means to communicate seriously with them instead of ignoring them.","zh":"engage with someone 指認真與某人溝通，而不是忽視他們。"},{"en":"A school should engage with parents who disagree with a new policy.","zh":"學校應與不同意新政策的家長交流。"},{"en":"Engaging with critics can clarify misunderstandings and reveal valid concerns.","zh":"與批評者交流可以澄清誤解並揭示合理憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active discussion, not automatic agreement.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動討論，而不是自動同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"concede to","meaning":"向……讓步","examples":[{"en":"Engaging with critics does not mean conceding to unfounded arguments.","zh":"與批評者交流並不代表向無根據的論點讓步。"},{"en":"To concede to something means to accept it or give way to it.","zh":"concede to something 指接受某事或向某事讓步。"},{"en":"A teacher may listen to complaints without conceding to unfair demands.","zh":"老師可以聆聽投訴，而不向不公平要求讓步。"},{"en":"It is possible to discuss criticism respectfully without accepting weak arguments.","zh":"人們可以尊重地討論批評，而不接受薄弱論點。"},{"en":"This phrase often means yielding in an argument or dispute.","zh":"這個短語常指在爭論或衝突中讓步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"unfounded arguments","meaning":"無根據的論點","examples":[{"en":"Scientists should not concede to unfounded arguments.","zh":"科學家不應向無根據的論點讓步。"},{"en":"Unfounded arguments are claims that lack evidence or reasonable support.","zh":"unfounded arguments 指缺乏證據或合理支持的說法。"},{"en":"A rumour that a teacher changed marks for friends would be unfounded if no evidence exists.","zh":"如果沒有證據，說老師為朋友改分數的謠言就是無根據論點。"},{"en":"Accepting unfounded arguments can make misinformation look credible.","zh":"接受無根據的論點可以令錯誤資訊看似可信。"},{"en":"This phrase describes claims that are not properly supported.","zh":"這個短語描述未獲適當支持的說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be based on prejudice rather than evidence","meaning":"基於偏見而非證據","examples":[{"en":"Some arguments are based on prejudice rather than evidence.","zh":"有些論點基於偏見而非證據。"},{"en":"To be based on prejudice rather than evidence means to depend on unfair beliefs instead of facts.","zh":"be based on prejudice rather than evidence 指依賴不公平信念，而不是事實。"},{"en":"A hiring decision based on prejudice rather than evidence is unfair to applicants.","zh":"基於偏見而非證據的招聘決定對申請者不公平。"},{"en":"Arguments based on prejudice can harm debate because they ignore real information.","zh":"基於偏見的論點會傷害討論，因為它們忽視真實資料。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly contrasts bias with facts.","zh":"這個短語清楚對比偏見與事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"there is an obligation to","meaning":"有責任去……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have an obligation to help the public understand climate change.","zh":"科學家有責任幫助公眾理解氣候變化。"},{"en":"There is an obligation to do something means there is a duty or responsibility to do it.","zh":"there is an obligation to do something 指有義務或責任去做某事。"},{"en":"Teachers have an obligation to keep students safe during school activities.","zh":"老師在學校活動期間有責任保障學生安全。"},{"en":"An obligation is stronger than a casual choice because others depend on it.","zh":"責任比隨意選擇更強，因為他人依賴它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moral, professional or legal responsibility.","zh":"這個短語描述道德、專業或法律責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"help the public understand","meaning":"幫助公眾理解","examples":[{"en":"Scientists should help the public understand the causes of climate change.","zh":"科學家應幫助公眾理解氣候變化的成因。"},{"en":"To help the public understand means to explain an issue clearly to ordinary people.","zh":"help the public understand 指向普通人清楚解釋某議題。"},{"en":"Doctors help the public understand vaccines by answering common questions in simple language.","zh":"醫生透過用簡單語言回答常見問題，幫助公眾理解疫苗。"},{"en":"Clear explanations reduce fear, confusion and misinformation.","zh":"清楚解釋可以減少恐懼、混亂和錯誤資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on public education.","zh":"這個短語著重公眾教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"causes of climate change","meaning":"氣候變化的成因","examples":[{"en":"The public needs to understand the causes of climate change.","zh":"公眾需要理解氣候變化的成因。"},{"en":"The causes of climate change are the factors that make Earth’s climate change over time.","zh":"causes of climate change 指令地球氣候隨時間改變的因素。"},{"en":"Students may study the causes of climate change through lessons on energy use, transport and industry.","zh":"學生可能透過能源使用、交通和工業課題學習氣候變化的成因。"},{"en":"Understanding causes helps people see which actions may reduce future harm.","zh":"理解成因幫助人們看見哪些行動可能減少未來傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase asks why climate change happens, not only what its effects are.","zh":"這個短語問的是氣候變化為何發生，而不只是其影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"options for avoiding","meaning":"避免……的選項","examples":[{"en":"The public should understand the options for avoiding serious consequences.","zh":"公眾應理解避免嚴重後果的選項。"},{"en":"Options for avoiding something are possible actions that can prevent or reduce it.","zh":"options for avoiding something 指可防止或減少某事的可能行動。"},{"en":"Students should know their options for avoiding exam stress, such as planning and regular breaks.","zh":"學生應知道避免考試壓力的選項，例如規劃和定時休息。"},{"en":"When people understand their options, they can choose practical ways to reduce risk.","zh":"當人們理解自己的選項，就能選擇實際方法降低風險。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on possible preventive actions.","zh":"這個短語著重可能的預防行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"dealing with the consequences","meaning":"處理後果","examples":[{"en":"Scientists should explain options for dealing with the consequences.","zh":"科學家應解釋處理後果的選項。"},{"en":"Dealing with the consequences means managing the results after a problem has happened.","zh":"dealing with the consequences 指在問題發生後處理其結果。"},{"en":"After a flood, a community must deal with the consequences by cleaning homes and supporting families.","zh":"水災後，社區必須透過清理家園和支援家庭來處理後果。"},{"en":"Prevention is ideal, but people also need plans for dealing with consequences.","zh":"預防最理想，但人們也需要處理後果的計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on response after harm or change occurs.","zh":"這個短語著重在傷害或變化發生後的回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"begin the process of","meaning":"開始……的過程","examples":[{"en":"Climate scientists need to begin the process of rebuilding trust.","zh":"氣候科學家需要開始重建信任的過程。"},{"en":"To begin the process of something means to take the first steps toward a longer goal.","zh":"begin the process of something 指朝較長遠目標採取第一步。"},{"en":"A student can begin the process of improving writing by correcting one paragraph each day.","zh":"學生可以透過每天修改一段文字，開始改善寫作的過程。"},{"en":"Starting the process matters because large problems are not solved at once.","zh":"開始過程很重要，因為大型問題不會一次解決。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the work will continue over time.","zh":"這個短語顯示工作會隨時間繼續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"rebuilding trust","meaning":"重建信任","examples":[{"en":"Rebuilding trust in climate science will take time.","zh":"重建對氣候科學的信任需要時間。"},{"en":"Rebuilding trust means restoring people’s belief that someone or something is reliable.","zh":"rebuilding trust 指恢復人們對某人或某事可靠性的信念。"},{"en":"A teacher can start rebuilding trust with students by keeping promises consistently.","zh":"老師可以透過持續遵守承諾，開始與學生重建信任。"},{"en":"Trust is rebuilt through repeated honest action, not one dramatic speech.","zh":"信任透過反覆誠實行動重建，而不是靠一次戲劇性演講。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a slow recovery of confidence.","zh":"這個短語描述信心的緩慢恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"trust in their profession","meaning":"對其專業的信任","examples":[{"en":"Climate scientists need to rebuild trust in their profession.","zh":"氣候科學家需要重建對其專業的信任。"},{"en":"Trust in their profession means confidence in the honesty and ability of that professional group.","zh":"trust in their profession 指對該專業群體的誠信和能力有信心。"},{"en":"Doctors protect trust in their profession by explaining risks honestly to patients.","zh":"醫生透過向病人誠實解釋風險來保護對其專業的信任。"},{"en":"When trust in a profession falls, people may ignore even good advice.","zh":"當對某專業的信任下降，人們可能連良好建議也忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on public confidence in a whole professional field.","zh":"這個短語著重公眾對整個專業領域的信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"just the start","meaning":"只是開始","examples":[{"en":"Following the three steps is just the start.","zh":"跟從這三個步驟只是開始。"},{"en":"Just the start means only the beginning of a longer process.","zh":"just the start 指只是較長過程的開端。"},{"en":"Finishing one practice essay is just the start of improving writing.","zh":"完成一篇練習作文只是改善寫作的開始。"},{"en":"When a problem is serious, the first steps must be followed by sustained effort.","zh":"當問題嚴重，第一步之後必須有持續努力。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds people not to stop too early.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要太早停止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"estimate that","meaning":"估計","examples":[{"en":"Gaines-Ross estimates that reputation recovery usually takes years.","zh":"Gaines-Ross 估計聲譽恢復通常需要多年。"},{"en":"To estimate that means to make a careful judgement based on available knowledge or data.","zh":"estimate that 指根據現有知識或數據作出謹慎判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher may estimate that a student needs three months to improve grammar accuracy.","zh":"老師可能估計學生需要三個月改善文法準確度。"},{"en":"Estimates help people plan when exact results cannot be known in advance.","zh":"當無法預先知道確切結果，估計有助人們規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an informed prediction, not a random guess.","zh":"這個短語引入有根據的預測，而不是隨意猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"typically takes","meaning":"通常需要","examples":[{"en":"It typically takes four years to restore a broken reputation.","zh":"恢復破損聲譽通常需要四年。"},{"en":"Typically takes means usually requires a certain amount of time.","zh":"typically takes 指通常需要某段時間。"},{"en":"It typically takes several weeks for beginners to feel comfortable speaking in English.","zh":"初學者通常需要幾星期才會對用英語說話感到自在。"},{"en":"Knowing how long something typically takes helps people set realistic expectations.","zh":"知道某事通常需要多久，有助人們設定現實期望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a normal or common time frame.","zh":"這個短語描述正常或常見時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"rescue and restore","meaning":"挽救並恢復","examples":[{"en":"A company may need years to rescue and restore its reputation.","zh":"公司可能需要多年來挽救並恢復其聲譽。"},{"en":"To rescue and restore something means to save it from serious damage and bring it back to a better state.","zh":"rescue and restore something 指把某物從嚴重損害中救回，並帶回較好狀態。"},{"en":"A school may rescue and restore trust after a crisis by listening and changing policy.","zh":"學校可能透過聆聽和改變政策，在危機後挽救並恢復信任。"},{"en":"Rescue comes first when damage is severe; restoration follows through long-term action.","zh":"當傷害嚴重，挽救先發生；恢復則靠長期行動。"},{"en":"This phrase combines urgent saving with gradual repair.","zh":"這個短語結合緊急拯救和逐步修補。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"broken reputation","meaning":"破損的聲譽","examples":[{"en":"A broken reputation cannot be repaired quickly.","zh":"破損的聲譽不能快速修復。"},{"en":"A broken reputation is public trust that has been badly damaged.","zh":"broken reputation 指公眾信任受到嚴重損害。"},{"en":"A sports club may have a broken reputation after repeated cheating scandals.","zh":"體育會在反覆作弊醜聞後，可能有破損的聲譽。"},{"en":"A broken reputation takes time to repair because people need evidence of change.","zh":"破損的聲譽需要時間修補，因為人們需要改變的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests deeper damage than a minor complaint.","zh":"這個短語暗示比輕微投訴更深的損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"win back public confidence","meaning":"贏回公眾信心","examples":[{"en":"Scientists need to win back public confidence.","zh":"科學家需要贏回公眾信心。"},{"en":"To win back public confidence means to regain people’s trust after losing it.","zh":"win back public confidence 指在失去後重新取得人們的信任。"},{"en":"A hospital may need to win back public confidence after a serious service failure.","zh":"醫院在嚴重服務失誤後，可能需要贏回公眾信心。"},{"en":"Public confidence returns when people see honesty, competence and visible improvement.","zh":"當人們看見誠實、能力和可見改善，公眾信心才會回來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes earning trust again, not demanding it.","zh":"這個短語描述重新贏得信任，而不是要求別人信任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a marathon, not a sprint","meaning":"是馬拉松，不是短跑","examples":[{"en":"Winning back public confidence is a marathon, not a sprint.","zh":"贏回公眾信心是馬拉松，不是短跑。"},{"en":"A marathon, not a sprint means a long process that requires patience, not a quick effort.","zh":"a marathon, not a sprint 指需要耐心的長期過程，而不是快速努力。"},{"en":"Learning academic writing is a marathon, not a sprint, because improvement comes from repeated practice.","zh":"學術寫作是馬拉松，不是短跑，因為進步來自反覆練習。"},{"en":"Reputation recovery takes time because trust must be proven again and again.","zh":"聲譽恢復需要時間，因為信任必須一次又一次被證明。"},{"en":"This phrase warns people not to expect instant results.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要期望即時結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"step up to the starting line","meaning":"走到起跑線","examples":[{"en":"You cannot win if you do not step up to the starting line.","zh":"如果你不走到起跑線，就不可能勝出。"},{"en":"To step up to the starting line means to begin the challenge instead of avoiding it.","zh":"step up to the starting line 指開始面對挑戰，而不是逃避。"},{"en":"A student cannot improve speaking if they never step up to the starting line and try answering aloud.","zh":"如果學生從不走到起跑線並嘗試開口回答，就不能改善口語。"},{"en":"Taking the first step matters because recovery cannot happen without action.","zh":"採取第一步很重要，因為沒有行動就不會恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a race image to mean beginning the effort.","zh":"這個短語用比賽圖像表示開始努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"agree with the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether statements agree with the views of the writer.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與作者的觀點一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the views of someone means to match that person’s opinion or position.","zh":"agree with the views of someone 指與某人的意見或立場相符。"},{"en":"In a reading test, an answer agrees with the writer’s views only if the writer clearly supports it.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，只有當作者清楚支持，答案才與作者觀點一致。"},{"en":"Students should not use their own opinions when judging whether a statement agrees with the writer.","zh":"判斷陳述是否與作者一致時，學生不應使用自己的意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in Yes, No and Not Given questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 Yes、No 和 Not Given 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A “No” answer contradicts the views of the writer.","zh":"“No” 答案與作者的觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what that person thinks.","zh":"contradict the views of someone 指說法與某人的想法相反。"},{"en":"If a writer supports school uniforms, a statement rejecting uniforms contradicts the writer’s views.","zh":"如果作者支持校服，拒絕校服的陳述就與作者觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students choose No when the statement clearly conflicts with the writer’s opinion.","zh":"當陳述清楚與作者意見衝突，學生選 No。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disagreement with a stated viewpoint.","zh":"這個短語描述與已表達觀點不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"The answer is not given if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"如果無法判斷作者想法，答案就是 Not Given。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to know the answer.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資料知道答案。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions the writer’s opinion on homework, it is impossible to say whether the writer supports it.","zh":"如果文章從未提及作者對功課的看法，就無法判斷作者是否支持功課。"},{"en":"Students should choose Not Given when the text does not provide enough evidence.","zh":"當文本沒有提供足夠證據時，學生應選 Not Given。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against guessing beyond the passage.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要超出文章猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be cleared of misconduct","meaning":"洗脫行為失當指控","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists were eventually cleared of misconduct.","zh":"有些科學家最終洗脫行為失當指控。"},{"en":"To be cleared of misconduct means to be officially found not guilty of wrongdoing.","zh":"be cleared of misconduct 指被正式判定沒有不當行為。"},{"en":"A teacher may be cleared of misconduct after an investigation finds the complaint was false.","zh":"如果調查發現投訴不實，老師可能洗脫行為失當指控。"},{"en":"Being cleared can help repair reputation, but suspicion may still remain for some people.","zh":"洗脫指控可以幫助修補聲譽，但部分人可能仍有懷疑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being freed from an accusation.","zh":"這個短語描述擺脫指控。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the public would be satisfied","meaning":"公眾會感到滿意","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether the public would be satisfied.","zh":"題目問公眾是否會感到滿意。"},{"en":"The public would be satisfied means ordinary people would accept the result or feel reassured.","zh":"the public would be satisfied 指普通人會接受結果或感到安心。"},{"en":"Parents would be satisfied if a school explained a safety problem clearly and fixed it quickly.","zh":"如果學校清楚解釋安全問題並迅速修正，家長會感到滿意。"},{"en":"Public satisfaction depends on whether people believe the response is honest and sufficient.","zh":"公眾是否滿意取決於人們是否相信回應誠實且足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes whether the public feels the issue has been properly handled.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾是否覺得議題已妥善處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in the aftermath of","meaning":"在……之後","examples":[{"en":"In the aftermath of the scandal, many scientists avoided attention.","zh":"在醜聞之後，許多科學家避免受到注意。"},{"en":"In the aftermath of something means in the period after a damaging or important event.","zh":"in the aftermath of something 指在有害或重要事件之後的一段時期。"},{"en":"In the aftermath of a typhoon, families may repair homes and schools may close temporarily.","zh":"颱風之後，家庭可能修理房屋，學校可能暫時停課。"},{"en":"The aftermath of a crisis is often when trust, safety and communication matter most.","zh":"危機之後常是信任、安全和溝通最重要的時候。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what happens after the main event.","zh":"這個短語著重主要事件之後發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"CRU scandal","meaning":"CRU 醜聞","examples":[{"en":"The CRU scandal damaged public trust in climate science.","zh":"CRU 醜聞損害了公眾對氣候科學的信任。"},{"en":"The CRU scandal refers to the controversy involving the Climatic Research Unit and climate data.","zh":"CRU scandal 指涉及氣候研究組和氣候數據的爭議。"},{"en":"A student reading about science communication may study the CRU scandal as a reputation crisis.","zh":"研究科學溝通的學生可能把 CRU 醜聞作為聲譽危機來學習。"},{"en":"Scandals can damage trust when people believe information has been hidden or mishandled.","zh":"當人們相信資訊被隱藏或處理不當，醜聞可以損害信任。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific controversy connected with climate science.","zh":"這個短語命名與氣候科學相關的特定爭議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"avoid attention","meaning":"避免受到注意","examples":[{"en":"Most scientists avoided attention after the scandal.","zh":"大多數科學家在醜聞後避免受到注意。"},{"en":"To avoid attention means to stay out of public view and not attract notice.","zh":"avoid attention 指避開公眾視線並不引人注意。"},{"en":"A student who feels embarrassed may avoid attention by sitting quietly at the back.","zh":"感到尷尬的學生可能安靜坐在後排以避免受到注意。"},{"en":"Avoiding attention can protect someone briefly, but it may look like hiding in a crisis.","zh":"避免受到注意可以短暫保護某人，但在危機中可能看似躲避。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deliberate low visibility.","zh":"這個短語描述刻意保持低曝光。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"defend someone against critics","meaning":"為某人抵禦批評者","examples":[{"en":"Journalists did not defend the CRU and IPCC against their critics.","zh":"記者沒有為 CRU 和 IPCC 抵禦批評者。"},{"en":"To defend someone against critics means to support or protect them when they are being attacked in public.","zh":"defend someone against critics 指在某人受到公開攻擊時支持或保護他們。"},{"en":"A principal may defend teachers against unfair critics after exam results are misunderstood.","zh":"考試結果被誤解後，校長可能為老師抵禦不公平批評者。"},{"en":"Defence against critics usually requires clear evidence and careful explanation.","zh":"抵禦批評者通常需要清楚證據和仔細解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public support during criticism.","zh":"這個短語描述在批評期間的公開支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"regard damage as extending beyond","meaning":"認為損害延伸至……之外","examples":[{"en":"Cicerone regarded the damage as extending beyond climate science.","zh":"Cicerone 認為損害延伸至氣候科學之外。"},{"en":"To regard damage as extending beyond something means to believe the harm reaches further than that area.","zh":"regard damage as extending beyond something 指認為傷害達到該範圍以外。"},{"en":"A principal may regard bullying as extending beyond one classroom if it affects the whole school culture.","zh":"如果欺凌影響整個學校文化，校長可能認為損害延伸至一間課室之外。"},{"en":"Damage can extend beyond the first target when it changes how people view a wider group.","zh":"當損害改變人們對更大群體的看法，就可以延伸至第一個目標之外。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harm spreading to a broader area.","zh":"這個短語描述傷害擴散至更廣範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the field of climate science","meaning":"氣候科學領域","examples":[{"en":"The scandal affected trust beyond the field of climate science.","zh":"這宗醜聞影響了氣候科學領域以外的信任。"},{"en":"The field of climate science is the area of study concerned with climate systems and climate change.","zh":"the field of climate science 指研究氣候系統和氣候變化的學術範疇。"},{"en":"A university course in the field of climate science may include weather patterns, oceans and carbon emissions.","zh":"氣候科學領域的大學課程可能包括天氣模式、海洋和碳排放。"},{"en":"When trust in one field falls, related fields may also be questioned.","zh":"當某一領域的信任下降，相關領域也可能受到質疑。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific academic and scientific area.","zh":"這個短語指特定學術和科學範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"confidence in climate science","meaning":"對氣候科學的信心","examples":[{"en":"Confidence in climate science fell after the controversy.","zh":"爭議後，對氣候科學的信心下降了。"},{"en":"Confidence in climate science means public trust in climate research, evidence and experts.","zh":"confidence in climate science 指公眾對氣候研究、證據和專家的信任。"},{"en":"Clear explanations from scientists can help improve confidence in climate science.","zh":"科學家的清楚解釋可以幫助提升對氣候科學的信心。"},{"en":"Confidence falls when people believe data or methods are not transparent.","zh":"當人們相信數據或方法不透明，信心就會下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trust in a scientific field.","zh":"這個短語描述對某科學領域的信任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"rise slightly","meaning":"輕微上升","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether confidence has risen slightly.","zh":"題目問信心是否輕微上升。"},{"en":"To rise slightly means to increase by a small amount.","zh":"rise slightly 指小幅增加。"},{"en":"Attendance at the library rose slightly after opening hours were extended.","zh":"圖書館延長開放時間後，到訪人數輕微上升。"},{"en":"A slight rise may show improvement, but not a dramatic change.","zh":"輕微上升可能顯示改善，但不是巨大變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for small upward changes in numbers or levels.","zh":"這個短語用於數字或水平的小幅上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"take professional advice on","meaning":"就……尋求專業意見","examples":[{"en":"Climate scientists should take professional advice on reputation recovery.","zh":"氣候科學家應就聲譽恢復尋求專業意見。"},{"en":"To take professional advice on something means to seek guidance from trained experts about that matter.","zh":"take professional advice on something 指就某事向受訓專家尋求指引。"},{"en":"A family may take professional advice on legal documents before buying a flat.","zh":"家庭買樓前可能就法律文件尋求專業意見。"},{"en":"Professional advice helps people avoid mistakes in areas they do not fully understand.","zh":"專業意見幫助人們避免在自己不完全理解的範疇犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests expert guidance is needed.","zh":"這個短語暗示需要專家指導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"regaining public confidence","meaning":"重拾公眾信心","examples":[{"en":"Professional advice may help scientists with regaining public confidence.","zh":"專業意見可能幫助科學家重拾公眾信心。"},{"en":"Regaining public confidence means winning back the trust of ordinary people.","zh":"regaining public confidence 指重新贏回普通人的信任。"},{"en":"A school can begin regaining public confidence by admitting problems and explaining changes clearly.","zh":"學校可以透過承認問題並清楚解釋改變，開始重拾公眾信心。"},{"en":"Public confidence returns slowly when people see repeated evidence of improvement.","zh":"當人們反覆看到改善證據，公眾信心會慢慢回來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rebuilding trust from the public.","zh":"這個短語描述重建來自公眾的信任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"考生應為每題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option that matches the passage or question.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇與文章或題目相符的答案選項。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may choose the correct letter from A, B, C or D.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能從 A、B、C 或 D 中選出正確字母。"},{"en":"Careless reading can lead students to choose the wrong letter even when they understand the topic.","zh":"粗心閱讀可以令學生即使理解主題，也選錯字母。"},{"en":"This phrase is a standard multiple-choice instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準多項選擇題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"in accordance with","meaning":"按照……","examples":[{"en":"The answer should be in accordance with Gaines-Ross’s views.","zh":"答案應按照 Gaines-Ross 的觀點。"},{"en":"In accordance with means following or matching a rule, view or instruction.","zh":"in accordance with 指依照或符合某規則、觀點或指示。"},{"en":"Students should answer in accordance with the passage, not their own opinion.","zh":"學生應按照文章作答，而不是按自己意見。"},{"en":"A company should act in accordance with safety regulations to avoid accidents.","zh":"公司應按照安全規定行事，以避免意外。"},{"en":"This phrase means consistent with or according to.","zh":"這個短語意思是符合或根據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"resign from one’s post","meaning":"辭去職位","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether the heads should have resigned from their posts.","zh":"題目問負責人是否本應辭去職位。"},{"en":"To resign from one’s post means to formally leave a job or position.","zh":"resign from one’s post 指正式離開某工作或職位。"},{"en":"A club chairman may resign from his post after failing to manage funds properly.","zh":"學會主席未能妥善管理資金後，可能辭去職位。"},{"en":"Resignation can signal responsibility, but it may also create leadership uncertainty.","zh":"辭職可以表示承擔責任，但也可能造成領導不確定性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to voluntarily stepping down from a role.","zh":"這個短語指自願卸下職務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"accept responsibility","meaning":"承擔責任","examples":[{"en":"Leaders may need to accept responsibility for organisational failings.","zh":"領袖可能需要為機構失誤承擔責任。"},{"en":"To accept responsibility means to admit that you are accountable for a problem or duty.","zh":"accept responsibility 指承認自己需要為問題或職責負責。"},{"en":"A student should accept responsibility after missing a group project deadline.","zh":"學生錯過小組項目期限後，應承擔責任。"},{"en":"Accepting responsibility can reduce anger because people see honesty.","zh":"承擔責任可以減少憤怒，因為人們看見誠實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ownership of mistakes or duties.","zh":"這個短語描述承認錯誤或職責屬於自己。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"continue in one’s post","meaning":"留任","examples":[{"en":"A leader may accept responsibility and continue in his or her post.","zh":"領袖可能承擔責任並留任。"},{"en":"To continue in one’s post means to remain in the same job or position.","zh":"continue in one’s post 指繼續留在同一工作或職位。"},{"en":"A principal may continue in her post after apologising and promising reforms.","zh":"校長道歉並承諾改革後，可能留任。"},{"en":"Staying in a post after failure can be controversial if people want new leadership.","zh":"失敗後留任可能具爭議，因為人們可能想要新領導。"},{"en":"This phrase describes remaining in office rather than resigning.","zh":"這個短語描述留在職位上，而不是辭職。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"shift attention onto","meaning":"將注意力轉移到……","examples":[{"en":"They should not shift attention onto more junior staff.","zh":"他們不應將注意力轉移到較初級職員身上。"},{"en":"To shift attention onto someone means to move public focus or blame toward that person.","zh":"shift attention onto someone 指把公眾焦點或責任轉向某人。"},{"en":"A manager should not shift attention onto interns when senior staff made the decision.","zh":"當決定由高級職員作出，經理不應把注意力轉移到實習生身上。"},{"en":"Shifting attention can look unfair if it protects those with more power.","zh":"如果轉移注意力是在保護較有權力的人，可能看似不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes redirecting blame.","zh":"這個短語常描述轉移責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"junior staff","meaning":"初級職員","examples":[{"en":"Junior staff should not be blamed for leadership failures.","zh":"初級職員不應為領導層失敗受責備。"},{"en":"Junior staff are employees with lower rank, less experience or less authority.","zh":"junior staff 指職級較低、經驗較少或權力較少的員工。"},{"en":"A junior staff member may handle paperwork but not make major company decisions.","zh":"初級職員可能處理文書工作，但不作重大公司決定。"},{"en":"Blaming junior staff for senior decisions can damage morale and seem unfair.","zh":"把高層決定歸咎於初級職員可以打擊士氣並顯得不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts lower-level workers with managers or leaders.","zh":"這個短語把低層員工與經理或領袖作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"ignore criticisms directed at","meaning":"無視針對……的批評","examples":[{"en":"Organisations should not ignore criticisms directed at them.","zh":"機構不應無視針對它們的批評。"},{"en":"To ignore criticisms directed at someone means to refuse to respond to complaints or attacks aimed at them.","zh":"ignore criticisms directed at someone 指拒絕回應針對某人的投訴或攻擊。"},{"en":"A school should not ignore criticisms directed at its homework policy if many parents complain.","zh":"如果許多家長投訴，學校不應無視針對其功課政策的批評。"},{"en":"Ignoring criticism can make people think leaders are arrogant or careless.","zh":"無視批評可以令人覺得領袖傲慢或粗心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes failing to engage with targeted criticism.","zh":"這個短語描述未能處理有目標的批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"make a mistake","meaning":"犯錯","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which mistake staff at the CRU and IPCC made.","zh":"題目問 CRU 和 IPCC 職員犯了哪個錯。"},{"en":"To make a mistake means to do something wrong or choose an incorrect action.","zh":"make a mistake 指做錯事或選擇錯誤行動。"},{"en":"A student may make a mistake by answering a True or False question from memory instead of the text.","zh":"學生如果憑記憶而不是按文本回答 True or False 題，就可能犯錯。"},{"en":"Mistakes can become serious if people hide them rather than correct them.","zh":"如果人們隱瞞錯誤而不是糾正，錯誤可以變得嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase is broad and can describe small errors or serious judgement problems.","zh":"這個短語很廣，可以描述小錯或嚴重判斷問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"publicly acknowledge failings","meaning":"公開承認失誤","examples":[{"en":"Organisations in crisis may need to publicly acknowledge failings.","zh":"處於危機中的機構可能需要公開承認失誤。"},{"en":"To publicly acknowledge failings means to openly admit mistakes or weaknesses.","zh":"publicly acknowledge failings 指公開承認錯誤或弱點。"},{"en":"A hospital may publicly acknowledge failings after a patient safety incident.","zh":"醫院在病人安全事件後可能公開承認失誤。"},{"en":"Public acknowledgement can begin to rebuild trust because it shows honesty.","zh":"公開承認可以開始重建信任，因為它顯示誠實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes open admission rather than private regret.","zh":"這個短語描述公開承認，而不是私下後悔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"avoid interviews with the press","meaning":"迴避傳媒訪問","examples":[{"en":"Some climate researchers avoided interviews with the press.","zh":"有些氣候研究人員迴避傳媒訪問。"},{"en":"To avoid interviews with the press means to refuse or stay away from media questioning.","zh":"avoid interviews with the press 指拒絕或避開媒體提問。"},{"en":"A company director may avoid interviews with the press during a product scandal.","zh":"公司董事可能在產品醜聞期間迴避傳媒訪問。"},{"en":"Avoiding interviews can reduce immediate pressure, but it may leave critics to control the story.","zh":"迴避訪問可以減少即時壓力，但可能讓批評者控制故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes avoiding direct media communication.","zh":"這個短語描述避免直接媒體溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"conflicting public statements","meaning":"互相矛盾的公開聲明","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether they made conflicting public statements.","zh":"題目問他們是否作出互相矛盾的公開聲明。"},{"en":"Conflicting public statements are public messages that disagree with each other.","zh":"conflicting public statements 指彼此不一致的公開訊息。"},{"en":"Parents may become confused if a school sends conflicting public statements about exam dates.","zh":"如果學校發出關於考試日期的互相矛盾公開聲明，家長可能感到混亂。"},{"en":"Conflicting statements damage trust because people cannot tell which message is reliable.","zh":"互相矛盾的聲明會損害信任，因為人們無法判斷哪個訊息可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inconsistency in official communication.","zh":"這個短語描述官方溝通中的不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"challenge the evidence of","meaning":"質疑……的證據","examples":[{"en":"Some people challenge the evidence of climate change.","zh":"有些人質疑氣候變化的證據。"},{"en":"To challenge the evidence of something means to question whether the evidence is strong, accurate or reliable.","zh":"challenge the evidence of something 指質疑證據是否有力、準確或可靠。"},{"en":"A lawyer may challenge the evidence of a witness if the story keeps changing.","zh":"如果證人故事不斷改變，律師可能質疑其證據。"},{"en":"Challenging evidence can be useful when done honestly, but harmful when based on prejudice.","zh":"誠實地質疑證據可以有用，但基於偏見就有害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes questioning the support behind a claim.","zh":"這個短語描述質疑某說法背後的支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"present one’s case poorly","meaning":"拙劣地陳述理據","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that critics presented their case poorly.","zh":"該選項暗示批評者拙劣地陳述理據。"},{"en":"To present one’s case poorly means to explain one’s argument in an unclear or ineffective way.","zh":"present one’s case poorly 指以不清楚或無效方式解釋自己的論點。"},{"en":"A student may present her case poorly if she gives opinions without examples.","zh":"如果學生只給意見而沒有例子，她可能拙劣地陳述理據。"},{"en":"Even a valid argument can fail if it is presented poorly.","zh":"即使論點有效，如果陳述得差，也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on communication quality, not necessarily truth.","zh":"這個短語著重溝通質素，而不一定是真偽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"miss opportunities for publicity","meaning":"錯失宣傳機會","examples":[{"en":"Critics did not necessarily miss opportunities for publicity.","zh":"批評者不一定錯失宣傳機會。"},{"en":"To miss opportunities for publicity means to fail to use chances to gain public attention.","zh":"miss opportunities for publicity 指未能利用獲得公眾注意的機會。"},{"en":"A charity may miss opportunities for publicity if it never shares successful community stories.","zh":"如果慈善機構從不分享成功社區故事，可能錯失宣傳機會。"},{"en":"Publicity opportunities matter because they help a message reach more people.","zh":"宣傳機會重要，因為它們幫助訊息接觸更多人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes failing to use moments when attention is available.","zh":"這個短語描述未能利用可獲注意的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"justified criticisms","meaning":"合理的批評","examples":[{"en":"Some critics made justified criticisms about transparency.","zh":"有些批評者就透明度提出合理的批評。"},{"en":"Justified criticisms are criticisms that are reasonable and supported by evidence.","zh":"justified criticisms 指有理據並獲證據支持的批評。"},{"en":"Students may make justified criticisms if a timetable is changed without warning.","zh":"如果時間表在沒有預告下改變，學生可能提出合理的批評。"},{"en":"Responding to justified criticisms can improve systems and rebuild trust.","zh":"回應合理批評可以改善系統並重建信任。"},{"en":"This phrase separates fair criticism from unfair attack.","zh":"這個短語把公平批評與不公平攻擊分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"dishonest in one’s statements","meaning":"在言論中不誠實","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that critics were dishonest in their statements.","zh":"該選項暗示批評者在言論中不誠實。"},{"en":"To be dishonest in one’s statements means to say things that are knowingly false or misleading.","zh":"be dishonest in one’s statements 指說出明知為假或誤導的話。"},{"en":"A student is dishonest in his statement if he says he submitted homework when he did not.","zh":"如果學生沒有交功課卻說自己已交，他就在言論中不誠實。"},{"en":"Dishonest statements damage trust because people feel deliberately misled.","zh":"不誠實言論會損害信任，因為人們覺得被刻意誤導。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lack of truthfulness in what someone says.","zh":"這個短語描述某人說話中缺乏真實性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"reference to","meaning":"提及……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what the reference to a marathon indicates.","zh":"題目問提及馬拉松表示甚麼。"},{"en":"A reference to something is a mention of it, often to explain or symbolise another idea.","zh":"reference to something 指提到某物，常用來解釋或象徵另一概念。"},{"en":"A speech may include a reference to a bridge to suggest connection between communities.","zh":"演講可能提及橋樑，以暗示社區之間的連繫。"},{"en":"References help writers explain abstract ideas through familiar images.","zh":"提及某物幫助作者透過熟悉圖像解釋抽象概念。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies something mentioned in the text.","zh":"這個短語指出文本中提到的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"indicate","meaning":"表示","examples":[{"en":"The marathon image indicates that rebuilding trust will take time.","zh":"馬拉松圖像表示重建信任需要時間。"},{"en":"To indicate means to show, suggest or point to something.","zh":"indicate 指顯示、暗示或指向某事。"},{"en":"Dark clouds may indicate that rain is coming.","zh":"烏雲可能表示快要下雨。"},{"en":"In reading, an image can indicate the writer’s deeper meaning.","zh":"在閱讀中，圖像可以表示作者的深層意思。"},{"en":"This verb is useful when explaining what evidence, signs or metaphors show.","zh":"這個動詞適合解釋證據、跡象或比喻顯示甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"rate at which","meaning":"……的速度","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to the rate at which the climate is changing.","zh":"該選項提到氣候變化的速度。"},{"en":"The rate at which something happens is the speed or pace of that process.","zh":"rate at which something happens 指某過程發生的速度或步伐。"},{"en":"Teachers may monitor the rate at which students improve their reading speed.","zh":"老師可能監察學生閱讀速度改善的速度。"},{"en":"A faster rate of change can make planning more urgent.","zh":"更快的變化速度可以令規劃更迫切。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how quickly something happens.","zh":"這個短語著重某事發生得多快。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"rival theories","meaning":"互相競爭的理論","examples":[{"en":"The option mentions competition between rival theories of climate change.","zh":"該選項提到氣候變化互相競爭的理論之間的競爭。"},{"en":"Rival theories are competing explanations for the same issue or evidence.","zh":"rival theories 指對同一議題或證據的競爭性解釋。"},{"en":"In history class, students may compare rival theories about why an empire collapsed.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生可能比較關於帝國為何崩潰的互相競爭理論。"},{"en":"Rival theories should be tested against evidence, not chosen by popularity alone.","zh":"互相競爭的理論應以證據測試，而不是只按受歡迎程度選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes competing explanations.","zh":"這個短語描述競爭性解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"ongoing need for","meaning":"對……的持續需要","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to the ongoing need for new climate data.","zh":"該選項提到對新氣候數據的持續需要。"},{"en":"An ongoing need for something is a continuing requirement for it.","zh":"ongoing need for something 指對某物持續存在的需求。"},{"en":"Schools have an ongoing need for clear communication with parents.","zh":"學校對與家長清楚溝通有持續需要。"},{"en":"An ongoing need exists when the problem does not disappear after one action.","zh":"當問題不會在一次行動後消失，就存在持續需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a need that continues over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間持續的需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"new climate data","meaning":"新氣候數據","examples":[{"en":"Scientists continue to collect new climate data.","zh":"科學家繼續收集新氣候數據。"},{"en":"New climate data are recent measurements or records about temperature, rainfall, oceans or the atmosphere.","zh":"new climate data 指關於溫度、降雨、海洋或大氣的最新量度或記錄。"},{"en":"A weather station may provide new climate data every month.","zh":"氣象站可能每月提供新氣候數據。"},{"en":"New data help scientists check whether earlier predictions remain accurate.","zh":"新數據幫助科學家檢查早前預測是否仍準確。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to fresh evidence about climate systems.","zh":"這個短語指關於氣候系統的新證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"the time it might take","meaning":"可能需要的時間","examples":[{"en":"The marathon image refers to the time it might take to win back confidence.","zh":"馬拉松圖像指贏回信心可能需要的時間。"},{"en":"The time it might take means the possible amount of time needed to finish something.","zh":"the time it might take 指完成某事可能需要的時間量。"},{"en":"A teacher may discuss the time it might take for a beginner to improve speaking fluency.","zh":"老師可能討論初學者改善口語流利度可能需要的時間。"},{"en":"Estimating time helps people prepare for a long effort instead of expecting quick results.","zh":"估計時間幫助人們準備長期努力，而不是期待快速結果。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on duration.","zh":"這個短語著重持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to complete the summary using the list of words.","zh":"考生需要使用詞語列表完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill in missing words so the shortened text makes sense.","zh":"complete the summary 指填入缺失字詞，使簡短文本意思完整。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole summary before choosing answers from the word list.","zh":"學生在從詞語列表選答案前，應閱讀整段摘要。"},{"en":"Grammar and meaning around each blank help identify the correct word.","zh":"每個空格周圍的文法和意思幫助找出正確字詞。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"list of words and phrases","meaning":"詞語及短語列表","examples":[{"en":"The summary should be completed using the list of words and phrases.","zh":"摘要應使用詞語及短語列表完成。"},{"en":"A list of words and phrases is a set of answer choices provided for a task.","zh":"list of words and phrases 指為題目提供的一組答案選項。"},{"en":"In an exam, students may choose from a list of words and phrases to fill blanks.","zh":"在考試中，學生可能從詞語及短語列表中選擇填空答案。"},{"en":"The list limits possible answers, so students should compare each option carefully.","zh":"該列表限制可能答案，所以學生應仔細比較每個選項。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the supplied answer bank.","zh":"這個短語指所提供的答案庫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"revelation","meaning":"揭露","examples":[{"en":"The revelation damaged the reputation of climate scientists.","zh":"這次揭露損害了氣候科學家的聲譽。"},{"en":"A revelation is new information that becomes known, often surprising or damaging.","zh":"revelation 指新被知道的資料，常令人驚訝或造成傷害。"},{"en":"The revelation that exam papers had been leaked shocked the school community.","zh":"試卷外洩的揭露震驚了學校社群。"},{"en":"A revelation can change public opinion quickly because it gives people new facts.","zh":"揭露可以迅速改變公眾意見，因為它給人新事實。"},{"en":"This word often refers to information that was previously hidden.","zh":"這個詞常指以前被隱藏的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"present inaccurate information","meaning":"提供不準確資料","examples":[{"en":"The CRU was accused of presenting inaccurate information.","zh":"CRU 被指提供不準確資料。"},{"en":"To present inaccurate information means to give or publish information that is wrong or misleading.","zh":"present inaccurate information 指提供或發布錯誤或誤導性資料。"},{"en":"A shop presents inaccurate information if its price label does not match the actual charge.","zh":"如果商店價錢牌與實際收費不符，就是提供不準確資料。"},{"en":"Inaccurate information can damage trust because people depend on facts to make decisions.","zh":"不準確資料可以損害信任，因為人們依賴事實作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes communicating information that is not correct.","zh":"這個短語描述傳達不正確資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"conceal statistics","meaning":"隱瞞統計數據","examples":[{"en":"The scientists were accused of concealing some statistics.","zh":"科學家被指隱瞞部分統計數據。"},{"en":"To conceal statistics means to hide numerical data from others.","zh":"conceal statistics 指向他人隱藏數字數據。"},{"en":"A school should not conceal statistics about bullying complaints from parents.","zh":"學校不應向家長隱瞞欺凌投訴的統計數據。"},{"en":"Concealing statistics can make people suspect that the full picture is being hidden.","zh":"隱瞞統計數據可以令人懷疑完整情況被隱藏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deliberately keeping numbers secret.","zh":"這個短語描述刻意保密數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"have a serious effect on","meaning":"對……有嚴重影響","examples":[{"en":"The scandal had a serious effect on their reputation.","zh":"這宗醜聞對他們的聲譽有嚴重影響。"},{"en":"To have a serious effect on something means to influence it strongly, often in a harmful way.","zh":"have a serious effect on something 指強烈影響某事，常帶有傷害性。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can have a serious effect on students’ memory and mood.","zh":"睡眠不足可以對學生記憶和情緒有嚴重影響。"},{"en":"Serious effects require serious responses because they do not disappear by themselves.","zh":"嚴重影響需要認真回應，因為它們不會自行消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong impact.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"in order to address","meaning":"為了處理……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists needed expert help in order to address the problem.","zh":"科學家需要專家協助，為了處理這個問題。"},{"en":"In order to address something means so as to deal with or solve it.","zh":"in order to address something 指為了處理或解決某事。"},{"en":"A school may hire counsellors in order to address rising student stress.","zh":"學校可能聘請輔導員，為了處理學生壓力上升。"},{"en":"Problems are addressed better when people understand their causes.","zh":"當人們理解原因，問題會被處理得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links an action with its purpose.","zh":"這個短語清楚把行動與目的連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"turn to experts in","meaning":"向……方面的專家求助","examples":[{"en":"Climate scientists should turn to experts in public relations.","zh":"氣候科學家應向公共關係方面的專家求助。"},{"en":"To turn to experts in a field means to seek help or advice from specialists in that area.","zh":"turn to experts in a field 指向某領域專家尋求幫助或建議。"},{"en":"A school may turn to experts in mental health when students show serious anxiety.","zh":"當學生出現嚴重焦慮，學校可能向精神健康方面的專家求助。"},{"en":"Turning to experts can save time because they understand common mistakes and solutions.","zh":"向專家求助可以節省時間，因為他們理解常見錯誤和解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes seeking specialist support.","zh":"這個短語描述尋求專門支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"public relations","meaning":"公共關係；公關","examples":[{"en":"Public relations experts can advise on reputation recovery.","zh":"公關專家可以就聲譽恢復提供建議。"},{"en":"Public relations is the work of managing communication between an organisation and the public.","zh":"public relations 指管理機構與公眾之間溝通的工作。"},{"en":"A hospital may use public relations to explain changes after a service problem.","zh":"醫院可能使用公關方法，解釋服務問題後的改變。"},{"en":"Good public relations can reduce misunderstanding by making messages clear and timely.","zh":"良好公共關係可以透過清晰和及時訊息減少誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to professional communication with the public.","zh":"這個短語指與公眾進行專業溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"publish guidelines","meaning":"發表指引","examples":[{"en":"Leslie Gaines-Ross has published guidelines on recovering reputation.","zh":"Leslie Gaines-Ross 發表了關於挽回聲譽的指引。"},{"en":"To publish guidelines means to release advice, rules or steps for others to follow.","zh":"publish guidelines 指發布供他人遵循的建議、規則或步驟。"},{"en":"A school may publish guidelines on how students should use AI tools responsibly.","zh":"學校可能發表關於學生如何負責任使用 AI 工具的指引。"},{"en":"Guidelines help people act consistently when they face similar problems.","zh":"指引幫助人們在面對類似問題時一致地行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making practical advice publicly available.","zh":"這個短語描述公開提供實用建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"crisis management","meaning":"危機管理","examples":[{"en":"Her advice is based on studies of crisis management.","zh":"她的建議基於危機管理研究。"},{"en":"Crisis management is the process of handling serious problems that threaten an organisation or community.","zh":"crisis management 指處理威脅機構或社區的嚴重問題的過程。"},{"en":"A school uses crisis management when it responds to a serious accident on campus.","zh":"學校回應校園嚴重意外時，就是在進行危機管理。"},{"en":"Good crisis management reduces harm, communicates clearly and plans recovery.","zh":"良好危機管理減少傷害、清楚溝通並規劃恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised action during and after a crisis.","zh":"這個短語指危機期間和之後的有組織行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"commercial organisations","meaning":"商業機構","examples":[{"en":"The book analyses crisis management in commercial organisations.","zh":"這本書分析商業機構中的危機管理。"},{"en":"Commercial organisations are businesses that operate to sell goods or services and earn money.","zh":"commercial organisations 指銷售商品或服務並賺取金錢的企業。"},{"en":"Shops, airlines and technology companies are commercial organisations.","zh":"商店、航空公司和科技公司都是商業機構。"},{"en":"Commercial organisations must protect reputation because customers can choose competitors.","zh":"商業機構必須保護聲譽，因為顧客可以選擇競爭者。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts businesses with charities or government bodies.","zh":"這個短語把企業與慈善或政府機構作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"public-sector organisations","meaning":"公營機構","examples":[{"en":"The book also considers public-sector organisations.","zh":"這本書也考慮公營機構。"},{"en":"Public-sector organisations are government-funded or government-run bodies that provide public services.","zh":"public-sector organisations 指由政府資助或運作、提供公共服務的機構。"},{"en":"Schools, hospitals and transport authorities can be public-sector organisations.","zh":"學校、醫院和交通部門可以是公營機構。"},{"en":"Public-sector organisations depend on public trust because they serve the community.","zh":"公營機構依賴公眾信任，因為它們服務社區。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts government-related bodies with private businesses.","zh":"這個短語把政府相關機構與私營企業作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"amongst other things","meaning":"其中包括","examples":[{"en":"Amongst other things, Gaines-Ross advises scientists to confront critics.","zh":"其中包括，Gaines-Ross 建議科學家面對批評者。"},{"en":"Amongst other things means as one example among several points or actions.","zh":"amongst other things 指作為多項重點或行動之一。"},{"en":"A good study plan should include, amongst other things, revision, rest and feedback.","zh":"良好學習計劃其中包括溫習、休息和回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the writer is mentioning only part of a larger list.","zh":"這個短語顯示作者只提到較大列表中的一部分。"},{"en":"It is useful when you do not need to list everything.","zh":"當你不需要列出所有內容時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"confront one’s critics","meaning":"面對批評者","examples":[{"en":"Climate scientists should confront their critics rather than avoid them.","zh":"氣候科學家應面對批評者，而不是迴避他們。"},{"en":"To confront one’s critics means to face criticism directly and respond to it.","zh":"confront one’s critics 指直接面對批評並回應它。"},{"en":"A school principal may confront critics by holding a public meeting and answering difficult questions.","zh":"校長可能透過舉行公開會議並回答困難問題來面對批評者。"},{"en":"Confronting critics can rebuild trust if the response is honest and respectful.","zh":"如果回應誠實且尊重，面對批評者可以重建信任。"},{"en":"This phrase means engaging with criticism, not attacking critics personally.","zh":"這個短語指處理批評，而不是人身攻擊批評者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 117 - Recovering a damaged reputation.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 118":[{"front":"video game research","meaning":"電子遊戲研究","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses video game research for preschool children.","zh":"文章討論針對學前兒童的電子遊戲研究。"},{"en":"Video game research is the study of how people use, understand, enjoy, or struggle with video games.","zh":"video game research 指研究人們如何使用、理解、享受電子遊戲，或在使用時遇到困難。"},{"en":"A teacher may read video game research to decide whether a learning game is suitable for young students.","zh":"老師可能閱讀電子遊戲研究，以判斷某個學習遊戲是否適合年幼學生。"},{"en":"Good video game research can help designers make games safer, clearer, and more useful.","zh":"良好的電子遊戲研究可以幫助設計者製作更安全、更清晰和更有用的遊戲。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to systematic study, not simply playing games for fun.","zh":"這個短語指有系統的研究，而不是單純為娛樂而打機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be first developed for","meaning":"最初為……而開發","examples":[{"en":"Video games were first developed for adults.","zh":"電子遊戲最初是為成年人而開發的。"},{"en":"To be first developed for someone means to be originally designed with that group in mind.","zh":"be first developed for someone 指最初以某群體為對象而設計。"},{"en":"Many office apps were first developed for workers before students started using them.","zh":"許多辦公應用程式最初為工作者開發，之後學生才開始使用。"},{"en":"If a product was first developed for adults, children may find it difficult to use.","zh":"如果產品最初為成年人而開發，兒童可能會覺得難以使用。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the original target user, not later users.","zh":"這個短語重點是原本目標用戶，而不是後來的使用者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"no longer exclusively reserved for","meaning":"不再只限於……","examples":[{"en":"Video games are no longer exclusively reserved for grown-ups.","zh":"電子遊戲不再只限於成年人。"},{"en":"No longer exclusively reserved for means something is not limited to one group anymore.","zh":"no longer exclusively reserved for 指某物不再只限於某一群體。"},{"en":"Online banking is no longer exclusively reserved for young people, as many older adults now use it.","zh":"網上銀行不再只限於年輕人，因為許多長者現在也使用它。"},{"en":"When a product spreads beyond its first audience, designers must consider new users’ needs.","zh":"當產品擴展至原本受眾以外，設計者必須考慮新用戶需要。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that access has become wider than before.","zh":"這個短語顯示使用範圍比以前更廣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"grown-ups","meaning":"成年人","examples":[{"en":"Video games are not only for the grown-ups in the home.","zh":"電子遊戲不只是家中成年人使用的東西。"},{"en":"Grown-ups are adults, especially when contrasted with children.","zh":"grown-ups 指成年人，尤其是與兒童作對比時使用。"},{"en":"A child may say that the television remote belongs to the grown-ups.","zh":"孩子可能會說電視遙控器是成年人用的。"},{"en":"When a product is used by both grown-ups and children, safety and simplicity become more important.","zh":"當產品同時由成年人和兒童使用，安全和簡單度就變得更重要。"},{"en":"The word is informal and often used from a child’s point of view.","zh":"這個詞較口語化，常從孩子角度使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as many as","meaning":"多達","examples":[{"en":"As many as 29 percent of preschool children had played console video games.","zh":"多達百分之二十九的學前兒童曾玩過家用遊戲機遊戲。"},{"en":"As many as is used to emphasise that a number is surprisingly large.","zh":"as many as 用來強調某個數字大得令人注意。"},{"en":"As many as thirty students joined the reading club after one teacher promoted it.","zh":"一位老師推廣後，多達三十名學生加入閱讀學會。"},{"en":"Using this phrase makes the figure sound noteworthy rather than ordinary.","zh":"使用這個短語會令數字聽起來值得注意，而不是普通資料。"},{"en":"It is often used before statistics to stress scale.","zh":"它常放在統計數字前，用來強調規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"preschool children","meaning":"學前兒童","examples":[{"en":"Preschool children are children between two and six years old.","zh":"學前兒童是二至六歲之間的兒童。"},{"en":"Preschool children are young children who have not yet started formal primary school.","zh":"preschool children 指尚未正式入讀小學的年幼兒童。"},{"en":"Preschool children may enjoy picture books because they can follow images before reading words.","zh":"學前兒童可能喜歡圖畫書，因為他們在讀字前已能跟隨圖像。"},{"en":"Because their skills are still developing, products for preschool children must be simple and safe.","zh":"由於他們的能力仍在發展，為學前兒童設計的產品必須簡單和安全。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an age group before primary school.","zh":"這個短語指小學前的年齡組別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"console video games","meaning":"家用遊戲機遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Many preschool children had played console video games.","zh":"許多學前兒童曾玩過家用遊戲機遊戲。"},{"en":"Console video games are games played on a home gaming machine connected to a television or screen.","zh":"console video games 指在連接電視或螢幕的家用遊戲機上玩的遊戲。"},{"en":"A family may play console video games together in the living room after dinner.","zh":"一家人可能晚飯後在客廳一起玩家用遊戲機遊戲。"},{"en":"Because console games are often designed for older users, young children may struggle with the controls.","zh":"因為家用遊戲機遊戲常為較年長用戶設計，年幼兒童可能難以操控。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts home gaming systems with mobile or hand-held games.","zh":"這個短語把家用遊戲系統與手機或手提式遊戲作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hand-held ones","meaning":"手提式遊戲機","examples":[{"en":"Some preschool children had played hand-held ones.","zh":"有些學前兒童曾玩過手提式遊戲機。"},{"en":"Hand-held ones means portable game devices that can be held in the hands.","zh":"hand-held ones 指可以拿在手上的便攜式遊戲裝置。"},{"en":"A child may play a hand-held game on the bus while waiting to arrive at school.","zh":"孩子可能在巴士上等待到校時玩手提式遊戲。"},{"en":"Hand-held devices are easier to carry, so younger children may use them more often.","zh":"手提式裝置較容易攜帶，所以年幼兒童可能更常使用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to hand-held video games or systems.","zh":"這個短語指回手提式電子遊戲或系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"given","meaning":"鑑於","examples":[{"en":"Given young children’s eagerness to learn, preschoolers may adopt video games.","zh":"鑑於年幼兒童對學習的熱切，學前兒童可能會開始使用電子遊戲。"},{"en":"Given means considering or taking something into account.","zh":"given 指考慮到或鑑於某事。"},{"en":"Given the heavy rain, the school decided to move sports day indoors.","zh":"鑑於大雨，學校決定把運動會移到室內。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a reason that helps explain the following conclusion.","zh":"這個短語引入一個有助解釋後續結論的原因。"},{"en":"It is useful when one fact makes another result more understandable.","zh":"當一個事實令另一個結果更易理解時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"insatiable eagerness to learn","meaning":"對學習無窮的渴望","examples":[{"en":"Young children have an insatiable eagerness to learn.","zh":"年幼兒童對學習有無窮的渴望。"},{"en":"Insatiable eagerness to learn means a very strong desire to keep learning more.","zh":"insatiable eagerness to learn 指非常強烈、想不斷學更多的欲望。"},{"en":"A child with an insatiable eagerness to learn may ask questions about every insect in the garden.","zh":"對學習有無窮渴望的孩子，可能會問花園裏每種昆蟲的問題。"},{"en":"This eagerness can make children explore new tools quickly, including games and screens.","zh":"這種渴望可以令兒童快速探索新工具，包括遊戲和屏幕。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests curiosity that is difficult to satisfy.","zh":"這個短語暗示一種難以滿足的好奇心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"coupled with","meaning":"加上；連同","examples":[{"en":"Children’s eagerness is coupled with the fact that they are surrounded by media.","zh":"兒童的熱切學習欲望，加上他們被媒體包圍這個事實。"},{"en":"Coupled with means together with another factor.","zh":"coupled with 指加上或連同另一個因素。"},{"en":"Long working hours, coupled with poor sleep, can make a student feel exhausted.","zh":"長時間工作加上睡眠不足，可以令學生感到疲憊。"},{"en":"When two factors are coupled, they may strengthen each other’s effect.","zh":"當兩個因素結合，它們可能互相加強影響。"},{"en":"The phrase links two reasons that work together.","zh":"這個短語把兩個共同起作用的原因連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be surrounded by","meaning":"被……包圍","examples":[{"en":"Young children are clearly surrounded by these media.","zh":"年幼兒童明顯被這些媒體包圍。"},{"en":"To be surrounded by something means to have it all around you or in your daily environment.","zh":"be surrounded by something 指某物在你周圍或存在於你的日常環境中。"},{"en":"A student may be surrounded by English signs, songs, and videos in a bilingual school.","zh":"學生在雙語學校可能被英文標誌、歌曲和影片包圍。"},{"en":"When children are surrounded by media, they are more likely to notice and try it.","zh":"當兒童被媒體包圍，他們更可能注意到並嘗試使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe physical surroundings or everyday exposure.","zh":"這個短語可以描述實體環境或日常接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"these media","meaning":"這些媒體","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers are increasingly surrounded by these media.","zh":"學前兒童越來越被這些媒體包圍。"},{"en":"These media refers to communication or entertainment forms already mentioned, such as television, games, or digital devices.","zh":"these media 指前文提到的溝通或娛樂形式，例如電視、遊戲或數碼裝置。"},{"en":"Parents may limit these media during homework time so children can concentrate.","zh":"家長可能在做功課時間限制這些媒體，讓孩子可以專心。"},{"en":"When children use many media often, they may develop strong habits around screens.","zh":"當兒童經常使用多種媒體，他們可能形成強烈屏幕習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase points back to the media being discussed.","zh":"這個短語指回正在討論的媒體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"predict that","meaning":"預測","examples":[{"en":"The researchers predict that preschoolers will adopt video games.","zh":"研究人員預測學前兒童將開始使用電子遊戲。"},{"en":"To predict that means to say what is likely to happen in the future.","zh":"predict that 指說出將來可能發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Teachers may predict that students will find a grammar test difficult if the topic is new.","zh":"如果文法課題是新的，老師可能預測學生會覺得測驗困難。"},{"en":"Predictions are stronger when they are based on evidence rather than guesses.","zh":"當預測建基於證據而不是猜測，它會更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a forecast or expected result.","zh":"這個短語引入預測或預期結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"increasingly begin to","meaning":"越來越開始","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers will increasingly begin to adopt video games.","zh":"學前兒童將越來越開始使用電子遊戲。"},{"en":"Increasingly begin to means start doing something more and more over time.","zh":"increasingly begin to 指隨時間越來越多地開始做某事。"},{"en":"Students may increasingly begin to use online dictionaries as homework becomes harder.","zh":"隨着功課變難，學生可能越來越開始使用網上字典。"},{"en":"When access grows, a behaviour can become more common gradually.","zh":"當接觸機會增加，某種行為可以逐漸變得更普遍。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises a rising trend at the start of a new habit.","zh":"這個短語強調新習慣開始時的上升趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"adopt video games","meaning":"開始使用電子遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers may adopt video games for personal enjoyment.","zh":"學前兒童可能為個人娛樂而開始使用電子遊戲。"},{"en":"To adopt video games means to start using video games as part of one’s activities.","zh":"adopt video games 指開始把電子遊戲納入自己的活動中。"},{"en":"A family may adopt educational games to help children practise spelling.","zh":"家庭可能開始使用教育遊戲，幫助孩子練習串字。"},{"en":"If children adopt games early, designers must think carefully about age-appropriate design.","zh":"如果兒童很早開始使用遊戲，設計者必須仔細考慮適齡設計。"},{"en":"The phrase means taking up use, not legally adopting anything.","zh":"這個短語指開始使用，不是法律上的領養。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"personal enjoyment","meaning":"個人娛樂","examples":[{"en":"Children may use video games for personal enjoyment.","zh":"兒童可能為個人娛樂而使用電子遊戲。"},{"en":"Personal enjoyment is pleasure or fun felt by the individual user.","zh":"personal enjoyment 指個人使用者感受到的樂趣或享受。"},{"en":"A student may read comics for personal enjoyment after finishing homework.","zh":"學生完成功課後可能為個人娛樂而閱讀漫畫。"},{"en":"If a game gives personal enjoyment, children may return to it again and again.","zh":"如果遊戲帶來個人樂趣，兒童可能一再回到該遊戲。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on private pleasure, not school achievement or parental goals.","zh":"這個短語重點是個人享受，而不是學業成就或家長目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the majority of","meaning":"大部分","examples":[{"en":"The majority of gaming equipment is designed for older users.","zh":"大部分遊戲設備是為較年長用戶設計的。"},{"en":"The majority of means most or more than half of a group.","zh":"the majority of 指大多數或超過一半。"},{"en":"The majority of students in the class preferred examples from daily life.","zh":"班中大部分學生較喜歡來自日常生活的例子。"},{"en":"If most equipment is designed for older users, younger users may face difficulties.","zh":"如果大部分設備是為較年長用戶設計，較年幼用戶可能面對困難。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the larger part of a group.","zh":"這個短語指出群體中較大部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"gaming equipment","meaning":"遊戲設備","examples":[{"en":"Most gaming equipment is designed for a much older target audience.","zh":"大多數遊戲設備是為年長得多的目標受眾設計的。"},{"en":"Gaming equipment is the hardware or devices used to play video games.","zh":"gaming equipment 指用來玩電子遊戲的硬件或裝置。"},{"en":"A console, controller, headset, or hand-held device can be gaming equipment.","zh":"家用遊戲機、控制器、耳機或手提式裝置都可以是遊戲設備。"},{"en":"If gaming equipment has small buttons, young children may find it hard to use.","zh":"如果遊戲設備有細小按鈕，年幼兒童可能覺得難以使用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the physical tools for gaming, not the game story itself.","zh":"這個短語指遊戲的實體工具，而不是遊戲故事本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be designed for","meaning":"為……而設計","examples":[{"en":"Gaming equipment is usually designed for older players.","zh":"遊戲設備通常為較年長玩家而設計。"},{"en":"To be designed for someone means to be made with that user’s needs in mind.","zh":"be designed for someone 指製作時考慮該使用者的需要。"},{"en":"School desks are designed for students, so their height should fit children’s bodies.","zh":"學校書桌為學生而設計，所以高度應配合兒童身體。"},{"en":"If a product is not designed for young children, it may be too complex or unsafe.","zh":"如果產品不是為年幼兒童而設計，它可能太複雜或不安全。"},{"en":"The phrase connects design choices with intended users.","zh":"這個短語把設計選擇與預定使用者連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"target audience","meaning":"目標受眾","examples":[{"en":"Most gaming equipment has a much older target audience.","zh":"大多數遊戲設備的目標受眾年齡大得多。"},{"en":"A target audience is the group of people a product, message, or service is meant for.","zh":"target audience 指某產品、訊息或服務所針對的人群。"},{"en":"A children’s storybook has a different target audience from a business report.","zh":"兒童故事書與商業報告有不同目標受眾。"},{"en":"Knowing the target audience helps designers choose language, images, and difficulty level.","zh":"了解目標受眾幫助設計者選擇語言、圖像和難度。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to intended users or viewers.","zh":"這個短語指預定使用者或觀眾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"enter the household","meaning":"進入家庭","examples":[{"en":"Once a game system enters the household, it may be used by children.","zh":"一旦遊戲系統進入家庭，它可能被兒童使用。"},{"en":"To enter the household means to become present or available in the home.","zh":"enter the household 指某物出現在家中或可在家中使用。"},{"en":"Once a tablet enters the household, younger siblings may begin using it too.","zh":"一旦平板電腦進入家庭，年幼兄弟姊妹也可能開始使用。"},{"en":"A device brought for adults can quickly become shared by the whole family.","zh":"為成年人帶回家的裝置可以很快變成全家共享。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a product becoming part of home life.","zh":"這個短語描述產品成為家庭生活一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be potentially available for","meaning":"可能可供……使用","examples":[{"en":"A game system is potentially available for all family members.","zh":"遊戲系統可能可供所有家庭成員使用。"},{"en":"To be potentially available for someone means that person could use it if conditions allow.","zh":"be potentially available for someone 指在條件容許下，某人可能可以使用它。"},{"en":"A shared laptop is potentially available for every child in the family.","zh":"共享手提電腦可能可供家庭中每個孩子使用。"},{"en":"If something is available to many users, designers cannot assume only one age group will use it.","zh":"如果某物可供許多用戶使用，設計者不能假設只有一個年齡組別會使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase means possible access, not guaranteed use.","zh":"這個短語指可能接觸，而不是保證使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"family members","meaning":"家庭成員","examples":[{"en":"Game systems may be available for all family members.","zh":"遊戲系統可能可供所有家庭成員使用。"},{"en":"Family members are the people who belong to the same family or household.","zh":"family members 指屬於同一家庭或住戶的人。"},{"en":"Parents, children, grandparents, and siblings are family members.","zh":"父母、子女、祖父母和兄弟姊妹都是家庭成員。"},{"en":"When one device is shared by family members, younger children may use it without it being designed for them.","zh":"當一部裝置由家庭成員共享，年幼兒童可能使用本來不是為他們設計的產品。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people in a family group.","zh":"這個短語指家庭群體中的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"portable systems","meaning":"便攜式系統","examples":[{"en":"Portable systems have successfully reached younger users.","zh":"便攜式系統成功接觸到較年幼用戶。"},{"en":"Portable systems are devices that are easy to carry and use in different places.","zh":"portable systems 指容易攜帶並可在不同地方使用的裝置。"},{"en":"A portable game system can be used in the car, at home, or while waiting at a clinic.","zh":"便攜式遊戲系統可以在車上、家中或診所等候時使用。"},{"en":"Because portable systems are small and accessible, children may use them more often.","zh":"因為便攜式系統細小且容易接觸，兒童可能更常使用它們。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights mobility and convenience.","zh":"這個短語突出流動性和方便性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"do a good job of","meaning":"在……方面做得好","examples":[{"en":"Portable systems have done a good job of reaching the younger market.","zh":"便攜式系統在接觸較年幼市場方面做得好。"},{"en":"To do a good job of doing something means to perform that task successfully.","zh":"do a good job of doing something 指成功地完成某項任務。"},{"en":"A teacher does a good job of explaining grammar when weak students can follow the lesson.","zh":"當較弱學生也能跟上課堂，老師就在解釋文法方面做得好。"},{"en":"When a product reaches its intended users well, the company may gain a stronger market.","zh":"當產品能很好地接觸預定使用者，公司可能得到更強市場。"},{"en":"The phrase gives positive judgement about performance.","zh":"這個短語對表現作出正面判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"penetrate the younger market","meaning":"打入年幼用戶市場","examples":[{"en":"Portable systems have penetrated the younger market.","zh":"便攜式系統已打入年幼用戶市場。"},{"en":"To penetrate the younger market means to successfully enter and attract younger consumers.","zh":"penetrate the younger market 指成功進入並吸引較年幼消費者。"},{"en":"A toy company may penetrate the younger market by making safer and simpler products.","zh":"玩具公司可能透過製作更安全和更簡單的產品打入年幼市場。"},{"en":"When a product reaches young users, companies may design more content for them.","zh":"當產品接觸到年幼用戶，公司可能為他們設計更多內容。"},{"en":"The phrase is a business expression about entering a market group.","zh":"這個短語是關於進入某市場群體的商業表達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"video game market","meaning":"電子遊戲市場","examples":[{"en":"Research in the video game market is usually done late in development.","zh":"電子遊戲市場中的研究通常在開發後期進行。"},{"en":"The video game market is the business area involving the creation, sale, and use of video games.","zh":"video game market 指涉及電子遊戲創作、銷售和使用的商業領域。"},{"en":"Companies study the video game market to learn what players are buying and enjoying.","zh":"公司研究電子遊戲市場，以了解玩家正在購買和享受甚麼。"},{"en":"Market research can affect pricing, advertising, and product design.","zh":"市場研究可以影響定價、廣告和產品設計。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the industry and consumers around video games.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞電子遊戲的行業和消費者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be typically done","meaning":"通常進行","examples":[{"en":"Research is typically done at two stages.","zh":"研究通常在兩個階段進行。"},{"en":"To be typically done means to be usually carried out in a certain way or time.","zh":"be typically done 指通常以某種方式或在某個時間進行。"},{"en":"In many schools, speaking practice is typically done in pairs or small groups.","zh":"在許多學校，口語練習通常以二人或小組形式進行。"},{"en":"Usual practice may not be best for every group, especially young children.","zh":"通常做法不一定最適合每個群體，尤其是年幼兒童。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what normally happens.","zh":"這個短語描述一般會發生的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"product cycle","meaning":"產品周期","examples":[{"en":"Research is often carried out near the end of the product cycle.","zh":"研究常在產品周期接近尾聲時進行。"},{"en":"A product cycle is the series of stages a product goes through from idea to design, testing, launch, and later updates.","zh":"product cycle 指產品由想法到設計、測試、推出和後續更新的一連串階段。"},{"en":"A phone’s product cycle may include planning, making prototypes, testing, advertising, and selling.","zh":"手機的產品周期可能包括規劃、製作原型、測試、宣傳和銷售。"},{"en":"If research happens too late in the cycle, designers may have little time to change the product.","zh":"如果研究在周期太晚才發生，設計者可能沒有太多時間修改產品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the life process of a product.","zh":"這個短語描述產品的生命過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in order to","meaning":"為了","examples":[{"en":"Research is done in order to get feedback from consumers.","zh":"研究是為了從消費者獲得意見而進行。"},{"en":"In order to means for the purpose of doing something.","zh":"in order to 指為了達到某目的。"},{"en":"Students practise past papers in order to understand the exam format.","zh":"學生練習歷屆試題是為了理解考試格式。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an action with its purpose.","zh":"這個短語把行動與目的連起來。"},{"en":"It is more formal than simply saying “to”.","zh":"它比單純說 “to” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get feedback from","meaning":"從……獲得意見","examples":[{"en":"Game companies get feedback from consumers before launch.","zh":"遊戲公司在推出前從消費者獲得意見。"},{"en":"To get feedback from someone means to receive their opinions, comments, or suggestions.","zh":"get feedback from someone 指收到某人的意見、評論或建議。"},{"en":"A teacher may get feedback from students after trying a new worksheet.","zh":"老師試用新工作紙後，可能從學生獲得意見。"},{"en":"Feedback helps designers see problems that they may not notice themselves.","zh":"回饋幫助設計者看見自己可能沒有注意到的問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning from users’ responses.","zh":"這個短語描述從使用者反應中學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"consumers","meaning":"消費者","examples":[{"en":"Research helps companies understand consumers.","zh":"研究幫助公司了解消費者。"},{"en":"Consumers are people who buy or use products and services.","zh":"consumers 指購買或使用產品和服務的人。"},{"en":"Parents are consumers when they buy learning apps for their children.","zh":"家長為孩子購買學習應用程式時就是消費者。"},{"en":"Understanding consumers helps companies design products people can actually use.","zh":"了解消費者幫助公司設計人們真正能使用的產品。"},{"en":"The word refers to buyers or users, not producers.","zh":"這個詞指買家或用戶，而不是生產者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"marketing strategy","meaning":"市場推廣策略","examples":[{"en":"Consumer feedback helps developers create a marketing strategy.","zh":"消費者回饋幫助開發者建立市場推廣策略。"},{"en":"A marketing strategy is a plan for promoting and selling a product to the right audience.","zh":"marketing strategy 指向合適受眾推廣和銷售產品的計劃。"},{"en":"A school may create a marketing strategy before advertising a new summer course.","zh":"學校宣傳新暑期課程前，可能制定市場推廣策略。"},{"en":"Good strategy depends on knowing who the audience is and what they care about.","zh":"好策略取決於了解受眾是誰以及他們關心甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to business planning for reaching customers.","zh":"這個短語指接觸顧客的商業規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be developed","meaning":"被制定","examples":[{"en":"A marketing strategy can be developed from consumer feedback.","zh":"市場推廣策略可以根據消費者回饋被制定出來。"},{"en":"To be developed means to be created, improved, or worked out over time.","zh":"be developed 指被創造、改善或逐步形成。"},{"en":"A new school rule may be developed after teachers discuss repeated problems.","zh":"老師討論反覆出現的問題後，新的校規可能被制定。"},{"en":"When ideas are developed carefully, they become more practical and complete.","zh":"當想法被仔細發展，它們會變得更實用和完整。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growth from an initial idea into a usable plan or product.","zh":"這個短語描述由初步想法成長為可用計劃或產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at the very end of","meaning":"在……的最後階段","examples":[{"en":"Some research is done at the very end of the product cycle.","zh":"有些研究在產品周期的最後階段進行。"},{"en":"At the very end of something means in the final stage or last part.","zh":"at the very end of something 指在某過程的最終階段或最後部分。"},{"en":"Students often check spelling at the very end of an essay-writing task.","zh":"學生常在作文任務最後階段檢查串字。"},{"en":"If testing happens at the very end, major changes may be harder to make.","zh":"如果測試在最後階段才發生，重大修改可能較難進行。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses lateness in a process.","zh":"這個短語強調過程中的後期時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fix bugs","meaning":"修復錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Developers test games to fix bugs.","zh":"開發者測試遊戲以修復錯誤。"},{"en":"To fix bugs means to find and correct errors in software or a game.","zh":"fix bugs 指找出並修正軟件或遊戲中的錯誤。"},{"en":"A school app may need programmers to fix bugs when students cannot log in.","zh":"當學生無法登入，學校應用程式可能需要程式員修復錯誤。"},{"en":"Bugs can make a game freeze, crash, or behave in unexpected ways.","zh":"錯誤可以令遊戲定格、當機或出現意外行為。"},{"en":"The phrase is about correcting technical mistakes, not insects.","zh":"這個短語關於修正技術錯誤，不是昆蟲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"deal with","meaning":"處理；應付","examples":[{"en":"Late-stage research may be appropriate for dealing with adult consumers.","zh":"後期研究可能適合用來處理成年消費者。"},{"en":"To deal with something means to handle, manage, or respond to it.","zh":"deal with something 指處理、管理或回應某事。"},{"en":"A teacher deals with late homework by setting a clear deadline and consequence.","zh":"老師透過設定清楚限期和後果來處理遲交功課。"},{"en":"Different problems require different ways of dealing with them.","zh":"不同問題需要不同處理方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical handling of a situation.","zh":"這個短語描述實際處理情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"adult consumers","meaning":"成年消費者","examples":[{"en":"Traditional market research often focuses on adult consumers.","zh":"傳統市場研究常集中於成年消費者。"},{"en":"Adult consumers are grown-up buyers or users of products and services.","zh":"adult consumers 指成年買家或產品服務使用者。"},{"en":"A supermarket survey may ask adult consumers which brands they buy most often.","zh":"超級市場調查可能詢問成年消費者最常購買哪些品牌。"},{"en":"Products for adult consumers can be more complex because adults usually read instructions better.","zh":"面向成年消費者的產品可以較複雜，因為成年人通常較能閱讀指示。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts adults with children or other special user groups.","zh":"這個短語把成年人與兒童或其他特殊用戶群作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"aid in","meaning":"有助於","examples":[{"en":"Late-stage research does not aid in designing better games.","zh":"後期研究無助於設計更好的遊戲。"},{"en":"To aid in something means to help or support that process.","zh":"aid in something 指幫助或支援某個過程。"},{"en":"Clear examples aid in students’ understanding of difficult grammar.","zh":"清晰例子有助於學生理解困難文法。"},{"en":"If research happens early, it can aid in design by showing what users need.","zh":"如果研究早期進行，它可以透過顯示用戶需要而有助於設計。"},{"en":"The phrase means help with, especially in a process or task.","zh":"這個短語意思是幫助某過程或任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"when it comes to","meaning":"當談到……時","examples":[{"en":"Special research is needed when it comes to designing games for preschoolers.","zh":"當談到為學前兒童設計遊戲時，需要特別研究。"},{"en":"When it comes to means when talking about or dealing with a particular topic.","zh":"when it comes to 指當談論或處理某個特定題目時。"},{"en":"When it comes to exams, many students know the content but struggle with time.","zh":"當談到考試時，許多學生懂內容，但時間管理有困難。"},{"en":"The phrase helps narrow a general discussion to one specific area.","zh":"這個短語幫助把一般討論收窄到特定範圍。"},{"en":"It is common in both speaking and writing.","zh":"它在口語和寫作中都很常見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"particular needs","meaning":"特定需要","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers and senior citizens may have particular needs.","zh":"學前兒童和長者可能有特定需要。"},{"en":"Particular needs are special requirements that a certain group has.","zh":"particular needs 指某群體具有的特殊要求。"},{"en":"A child with weak eyesight may have particular needs in the classroom.","zh":"視力較弱的孩子在課室中可能有特定需要。"},{"en":"If designers ignore particular needs, users may feel confused, unsafe, or excluded.","zh":"如果設計者忽視特定需要，使用者可能感到困惑、不安全或被排除。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that one design may not fit everyone.","zh":"這個短語強調一種設計不一定適合所有人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"senior citizens","meaning":"長者","examples":[{"en":"Senior citizens may need specifically designed games.","zh":"長者可能需要專門設計的遊戲。"},{"en":"Senior citizens are older adults, usually people at or beyond retirement age.","zh":"senior citizens 指年長成年人，通常是達到或超過退休年齡的人。"},{"en":"A community centre may offer computer classes for senior citizens.","zh":"社區中心可能為長者提供電腦課程。"},{"en":"Products for senior citizens may need larger text, clearer sound, and simpler steps.","zh":"為長者設計的產品可能需要較大文字、較清晰聲音和較簡單步驟。"},{"en":"The phrase is a polite term for older people.","zh":"這個短語是對年長人士的禮貌稱呼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"exploratory and formative research","meaning":"探索性和形成性研究","examples":[{"en":"Exploratory and formative research is needed to understand young users.","zh":"需要探索性和形成性研究來了解年幼用戶。"},{"en":"Exploratory and formative research is early research used to discover needs and shape a product before it is finished.","zh":"exploratory and formative research 指在產品完成前，用來發現需要並塑造產品的早期研究。"},{"en":"A school may use exploratory research before creating a new reading programme.","zh":"學校在創建新閱讀計劃前，可能使用探索性研究。"},{"en":"Early research can prevent designers from building a product that users cannot handle.","zh":"早期研究可以防止設計者製作出用戶無法使用的產品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research that guides development, not research done only after launch.","zh":"這個短語描述指導開發的研究，而不是只在推出後才做的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be undertaken","meaning":"被進行","examples":[{"en":"Formative research has to be undertaken before designing better games.","zh":"形成性研究必須在設計更好遊戲之前進行。"},{"en":"To be undertaken means to be carried out or done, usually as a planned task.","zh":"be undertaken 指被執行或進行，通常是有計劃的任務。"},{"en":"A safety check must be undertaken before students enter the laboratory.","zh":"學生進入實驗室前，必須進行安全檢查。"},{"en":"If research is undertaken early, designers can use the findings before final decisions are made.","zh":"如果研究早期進行，設計者可以在最終決定前使用研究結果。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and means “be done”.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是「被做」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"truly understand","meaning":"真正了解","examples":[{"en":"Designers need research to truly understand their audience.","zh":"設計者需要研究來真正了解他們的受眾。"},{"en":"To truly understand something means to know it deeply, not just guess from the outside.","zh":"truly understand something 指深入了解某事，而不只是從外面猜測。"},{"en":"A teacher truly understands a class after seeing how students learn, make mistakes, and ask questions.","zh":"老師看見學生如何學習、犯錯和提問後，才真正了解一班學生。"},{"en":"Without real user research, designers may misunderstand what children can actually do.","zh":"沒有真正用戶研究，設計者可能誤解兒童實際能做甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses deep and accurate understanding.","zh":"這個短語強調深入而準確的理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"abilities","meaning":"能力","examples":[{"en":"Researchers must understand preschoolers’ abilities.","zh":"研究人員必須了解學前兒童的能力。"},{"en":"Abilities are the skills or powers people have to do something.","zh":"abilities 指人們做某事所具備的技能或能力。"},{"en":"A teacher checks students’ reading abilities before choosing a book for the class.","zh":"老師在為全班選書前，會檢查學生的閱讀能力。"},{"en":"If a game demands abilities children do not yet have, they may feel frustrated.","zh":"如果遊戲要求兒童尚未具備的能力，他們可能感到挫敗。"},{"en":"The word refers to what users can actually do.","zh":"這個詞指使用者實際能做到甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"perspectives","meaning":"觀點；角度","examples":[{"en":"Designers need to understand users’ perspectives.","zh":"設計者需要了解使用者的觀點。"},{"en":"Perspectives are the ways people see, understand, or experience a situation.","zh":"perspectives 指人們看待、理解或經歷某情況的方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students for their perspectives before changing homework rules.","zh":"老師改變功課規則前，可能先詢問學生的觀點。"},{"en":"Understanding users’ perspectives helps designers avoid making confusing products.","zh":"了解使用者角度有助設計者避免製作令人困惑的產品。"},{"en":"The word focuses on viewpoint and experience.","zh":"這個詞重點是觀點和經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"production team","meaning":"製作團隊","examples":[{"en":"The preschool-game production team studied the Nintendo DS.","zh":"學前兒童遊戲製作團隊研究了 Nintendo DS。"},{"en":"A production team is the group of people who create and develop a product, film, game, or programme.","zh":"production team 指創作和開發產品、電影、遊戲或節目的一組人。"},{"en":"A school play production team may include actors, directors, sound helpers, and stage managers.","zh":"學校話劇製作團隊可能包括演員、導演、音響助手和舞台經理。"},{"en":"Different team members bring different skills, so the final product can be stronger.","zh":"不同團隊成員帶來不同技能，所以最終產品可以更好。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the people making the product together.","zh":"這個短語指共同製作產品的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have a hunch that","meaning":"有預感；直覺認為","examples":[{"en":"The production team had a hunch that the Nintendo DS was suitable for preschoolers.","zh":"製作團隊直覺認為 Nintendo DS 適合學前兒童。"},{"en":"To have a hunch that means to have a feeling or guess that something may be true.","zh":"have a hunch that 指有感覺或猜想某事可能是真的。"},{"en":"A teacher may have a hunch that a quiet student understands more than she says.","zh":"老師可能直覺認為一位安靜學生理解得比她說出來的更多。"},{"en":"A hunch can start research, but evidence is needed to confirm it.","zh":"直覺可以引發研究，但需要證據確認。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an instinctive belief, not a proven conclusion.","zh":"這個短語描述本能相信，而不是已證明結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"new features","meaning":"新功能","examples":[{"en":"The Nintendo DS had new features such as a microphone and portability.","zh":"Nintendo DS 有新功能，例如咪高峰和便攜性。"},{"en":"New features are new functions or design parts added to a product.","zh":"new features 指加入產品的新功能或設計部分。"},{"en":"A learning app may add new features such as voice recording and progress charts.","zh":"學習應用程式可能加入錄音和進度圖表等新功能。"},{"en":"New features can make a product easier, more enjoyable, or more suitable for different users.","zh":"新功能可以令產品更容易、更有趣或更適合不同用戶。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on added functions, not simply a new colour.","zh":"這個短語重點是新增功能，而不只是新顏色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"small size and portability","meaning":"體積小巧和便攜性","examples":[{"en":"The DS appealed to young users because of its small size and portability.","zh":"DS 因體積小巧和便攜性而吸引年幼用戶。"},{"en":"Small size and portability mean a device is compact and easy to carry.","zh":"small size and portability 指裝置小巧且容易攜帶。"},{"en":"A small portable speaker is useful because students can carry it between classrooms.","zh":"小型便攜式揚聲器很有用，因為學生可以在課室之間攜帶它。"},{"en":"If a device is small and portable, children can hold it more easily and use it in more places.","zh":"如果裝置小巧便攜，兒童可以更容易拿着它，並在更多地方使用。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights physical convenience.","zh":"這個短語突出實體便利性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"relatively low price point","meaning":"相對較低的價格定位","examples":[{"en":"The Nintendo DS had a relatively low price point.","zh":"Nintendo DS 有相對較低的價格定位。"},{"en":"A relatively low price point means the product is sold at a lower price compared with similar products.","zh":"relatively low price point 指產品相較同類產品以較低價格出售。"},{"en":"A school may choose tablets with a relatively low price point to stay within budget.","zh":"學校可能選擇價格定位相對較低的平板電腦，以符合預算。"},{"en":"Lower prices can make a product more accessible to families.","zh":"較低價格可以令產品更容易被家庭負擔。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to pricing position, not necessarily cheap quality.","zh":"這個短語指價格位置，不一定代表質素低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ripe gaming platform","meaning":"適合發展的遊戲平台","examples":[{"en":"The team thought the Nintendo DS was a ripe gaming platform for preschoolers.","zh":"團隊認為 Nintendo DS 是適合學前兒童發展的遊戲平台。"},{"en":"A ripe gaming platform is a game system that seems ready and suitable for new development.","zh":"ripe gaming platform 指看來已準備好且適合新開發的遊戲系統。"},{"en":"A popular school tablet may be a ripe platform for new learning apps.","zh":"受歡迎的學校平板電腦可能是新學習應用程式的適合發展平台。"},{"en":"When a platform has useful features and a reachable audience, developers may see an opportunity.","zh":"當平台有有用功能和可接觸受眾，開發者可能看見機會。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests the time and conditions are right.","zh":"這個短語暗示時間和條件都合適。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"games on the market","meaning":"市面上的遊戲","examples":[{"en":"There were a few games on the market for young children.","zh":"市面上有少數為年幼兒童而設的遊戲。"},{"en":"Games on the market are games already available for people to buy or use.","zh":"games on the market 指已可供人購買或使用的遊戲。"},{"en":"Parents often compare games on the market before choosing one for a child.","zh":"家長為孩子選遊戲前，常比較市面上的遊戲。"},{"en":"If few suitable games are on the market, a company may see space for a new product.","zh":"如果市面上合適遊戲很少，公司可能看見新產品空間。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to commercially available games.","zh":"這個短語指可在市場上取得的遊戲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at the time","meaning":"當時","examples":[{"en":"There were only a few suitable games on the market at the time.","zh":"當時市面上只有少數合適遊戲。"},{"en":"At the time means during the period being discussed.","zh":"at the time 指在所討論的那段時期。"},{"en":"At the time, the school had only one computer room for all students.","zh":"當時學校只有一間電腦室供所有學生使用。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds readers that the situation may have changed later.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者情況後來可能已經改變。"},{"en":"It is used to place information in a specific past period.","zh":"它用來把資訊放在特定過去時期中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"appeal to","meaning":"吸引","examples":[{"en":"Some characters appealed to the younger set.","zh":"一些角色吸引較年幼的一群。"},{"en":"To appeal to someone means to attract or interest that person.","zh":"appeal to someone 指吸引某人或令某人感興趣。"},{"en":"Bright pictures and simple stories often appeal to young children.","zh":"鮮明圖畫和簡單故事常吸引年幼兒童。"},{"en":"If a game appeals to children, they may want to play it again.","zh":"如果遊戲吸引兒童，他們可能想再玩。"},{"en":"The phrase describes attraction, not a legal appeal.","zh":"這個短語描述吸引力，不是法律上訴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the younger set","meaning":"較年幼的一群","examples":[{"en":"The characters in some games appealed to the younger set.","zh":"一些遊戲中的角色吸引較年幼的一群。"},{"en":"The younger set means younger people or children as a group.","zh":"the younger set 指較年幼的人或兒童群體。"},{"en":"A cartoon café may attract the younger set because of its colourful design.","zh":"卡通主題咖啡店可能因色彩鮮明設計而吸引較年幼的一群。"},{"en":"When a product appeals to the younger set, companies may simplify language and controls.","zh":"當產品吸引較年幼的一群，公司可能簡化語言和控制方式。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and refers to younger users or audiences.","zh":"這個短語較口語，指較年幼用戶或觀眾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"game producers","meaning":"遊戲製作人","examples":[{"en":"The game producers questioned whether the designs were suitable.","zh":"遊戲製作人質疑這些設計是否合適。"},{"en":"Game producers are people who manage or guide the creation of video games.","zh":"game producers 指管理或指導電子遊戲創作的人。"},{"en":"Game producers may decide the schedule, budget, target audience, and main features.","zh":"遊戲製作人可能決定時間表、預算、目標受眾和主要功能。"},{"en":"If producers notice a design problem early, the team can improve the game before release.","zh":"如果製作人早期注意到設計問題，團隊可以在推出前改善遊戲。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people responsible for producing games.","zh":"這個短語指負責製作遊戲的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"game mechanics","meaning":"遊戲機制","examples":[{"en":"The producers did not think the game mechanics were appropriate for preschoolers.","zh":"製作人認為遊戲機制不適合學前兒童。"},{"en":"Game mechanics are the rules, controls, actions, and systems that make a game work.","zh":"game mechanics 指令遊戲運作的規則、控制方式、行動和系統。"},{"en":"Jumping, collecting points, dragging objects, and pressing buttons are examples of game mechanics.","zh":"跳躍、收集分數、拖曽物件和按按鈕都是遊戲機制例子。"},{"en":"If game mechanics are too complex, young players may not understand what to do.","zh":"如果遊戲機制太複雜，年幼玩家可能不知道要做甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to how the game functions, not only its story or characters.","zh":"這個短語指遊戲如何運作，而不只是故事或角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"appropriate for","meaning":"適合……","examples":[{"en":"The game design was not appropriate for preschoolers.","zh":"這個遊戲設計不適合學前兒童。"},{"en":"Appropriate for means suitable for a particular person, age, purpose, or situation.","zh":"appropriate for 指適合某人、年齡、目的或情況。"},{"en":"A picture book with simple words is appropriate for beginner readers.","zh":"用字簡單的圖畫書適合初學閱讀者。"},{"en":"If content is not appropriate for children, it may confuse or upset them.","zh":"如果內容不適合兒童，它可能令他們困惑或不安。"},{"en":"The phrase judges suitability for a specific group.","zh":"這個短語判斷對特定群體的適合度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a bit of a mystery","meaning":"有點神秘；不太清楚","examples":[{"en":"What preschoolers could do with the system was a bit of a mystery.","zh":"學前兒童能用這個系統做到甚麼有點不太清楚。"},{"en":"A bit of a mystery means something is not fully known or understood.","zh":"a bit of a mystery 指某事尚未完全被知道或理解。"},{"en":"Why a student suddenly became quiet may be a bit of a mystery to the teacher.","zh":"學生為何突然變得安靜，對老師來說可能有點神秘。"},{"en":"When something is unclear, research can help turn guesses into evidence.","zh":"當事情不清楚，研究可以把猜測變成證據。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests uncertainty, but not complete ignorance.","zh":"這個短語暗示不確定，但不是完全不知道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"set about doing","meaning":"開始着手做……","examples":[{"en":"The team set about doing a study to answer the question.","zh":"團隊開始着手進行研究，以回答這個問題。"},{"en":"To set about doing something means to start doing it with purpose and effort.","zh":"set about doing something 指有目的、有努力地開始做某事。"},{"en":"After finding many spelling mistakes, the student set about correcting the essay carefully.","zh":"發現許多串字錯誤後，學生開始仔細修改作文。"},{"en":"People set about a task when they decide it needs serious action.","zh":"當人們認為任務需要認真行動，他們就會着手處理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes beginning work actively.","zh":"這個短語描述主動開始工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"answer the query","meaning":"回答疑問","examples":[{"en":"The study was designed to answer the query about preschool game play.","zh":"該研究旨在回答關於學前兒童遊戲玩法的疑問。"},{"en":"To answer the query means to respond to a question or uncertainty.","zh":"answer the query 指回應一個問題或不確定之處。"},{"en":"A school survey may answer the query of why students prefer online homework.","zh":"學校調查可能回答學生為何較喜歡網上功課這個疑問。"},{"en":"A clear answer helps people make decisions with less guessing.","zh":"清楚答案幫助人減少猜測並作決定。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and means to answer the question.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是回答問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be capable of","meaning":"有能力","examples":[{"en":"The researchers asked what preschoolers were capable of doing.","zh":"研究人員問學前兒童有能力做到甚麼。"},{"en":"To be capable of doing something means to have the ability to do it.","zh":"be capable of doing something 指有能力做某事。"},{"en":"A child may be capable of choosing a picture but not reading a written menu.","zh":"孩子可能有能力選擇圖畫，但未必能讀書面選單。"},{"en":"If a game asks children to do more than they are capable of, they may give up.","zh":"如果遊戲要求兒童做超出其能力的事，他們可能放棄。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on actual ability.","zh":"這個短語重點是實際能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the context of","meaning":"在……的背景下","examples":[{"en":"The team studied children’s abilities in the context of hand-held game play.","zh":"團隊在手提式遊戲玩法的背景下研究兒童能力。"},{"en":"In the context of means within a particular situation, setting, or topic.","zh":"in the context of 指在某特定情況、環境或題目之中。"},{"en":"A teacher may study vocabulary in the context of real reading passages.","zh":"老師可能在真實閱讀篇章的背景下研究詞彙。"},{"en":"Abilities can look different in different contexts, so the setting matters.","zh":"能力在不同背景下可能看起來不同，所以情境很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase tells readers the situation in which something is being examined.","zh":"這個短語告訴讀者某事是在甚麼情況中被檢視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hand-held game play","meaning":"手提式遊戲玩法","examples":[{"en":"The researchers examined preschoolers in the context of hand-held game play.","zh":"研究人員在手提式遊戲玩法的背景下檢視學前兒童。"},{"en":"Hand-held game play is playing games on a portable device held in the hands.","zh":"hand-held game play 指在手中拿着的便攜式裝置上玩遊戲。"},{"en":"A child using a small game device on a sofa is engaging in hand-held game play.","zh":"孩子坐在梳化上使用小型遊戲裝置，就是進行手提式遊戲玩法。"},{"en":"This type of play requires touch, hand control, and attention to a small screen.","zh":"這種玩法需要觸控、手部控制和注意小螢幕。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the playing situation and device type.","zh":"這個短語重點是遊玩情境和裝置類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"child development literature","meaning":"兒童發展文獻","examples":[{"en":"The team used child development literature to guide game design.","zh":"團隊使用兒童發展文獻來指導遊戲設計。"},{"en":"Child development literature is research writing about how children grow, learn, think, and move.","zh":"child development literature 指關於兒童如何成長、學習、思考和活動的研究文獻。"},{"en":"Teachers may read child development literature to understand why young children need play.","zh":"老師可能閱讀兒童發展文獻，以理解年幼兒童為何需要遊戲。"},{"en":"Using this literature helps designers match tasks to children’s developmental stage.","zh":"使用這類文獻幫助設計者把任務配合兒童發展階段。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to academic knowledge about children’s growth.","zh":"這個短語指關於兒童成長的學術知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"inform us","meaning":"為我們提供參考","examples":[{"en":"The literature could inform the team as they designed the game.","zh":"這些文獻可以在團隊設計遊戲時為他們提供參考。"},{"en":"To inform someone means to guide their thinking by giving useful knowledge.","zh":"inform someone 指透過提供有用知識來引導某人的思考。"},{"en":"Exam results can inform a teacher’s decision about what to teach next.","zh":"考試結果可以為老師決定下一步教甚麼提供參考。"},{"en":"Good information prevents people from designing only by guesswork.","zh":"良好資訊防止人只靠猜測來設計。"},{"en":"The phrase means to provide guidance, not just to announce news.","zh":"這個短語意思是提供指引，不只是宣布消息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"proceed with","meaning":"繼續進行","examples":[{"en":"The team proceeded with the creation of a new outlet.","zh":"團隊繼續進行新途徑的創造。"},{"en":"To proceed with something means to continue or move forward with a plan.","zh":"proceed with something 指繼續或推進某個計劃。"},{"en":"After the principal approved the budget, the teachers proceeded with the school fair.","zh":"校長批准預算後，老師們繼續進行學校嘉年華。"},{"en":"People proceed when they believe they have enough information or permission to act.","zh":"當人們認為已有足夠資訊或許可，他們就會繼續行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continuing with a planned action.","zh":"這個短語描述繼續推行計劃中的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the creation of","meaning":"……的創造","examples":[{"en":"Research informed the creation of a new outlet for preschoolers.","zh":"研究為學前兒童新途徑的創造提供參考。"},{"en":"The creation of something is the process of making or developing it.","zh":"creation of something 指製作或發展某事物的過程。"},{"en":"The creation of a school garden may involve students, teachers, and parents.","zh":"學校花園的創造可能涉及學生、老師和家長。"},{"en":"When research guides creation, the final product is more likely to meet real needs.","zh":"當研究指導創造，最終產品更可能滿足真實需要。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on making something new.","zh":"這個短語重點是製造新事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a new outlet for","meaning":"……的新途徑","examples":[{"en":"The Nintendo DS became a possible new outlet for this age group.","zh":"Nintendo DS 成為這個年齡組別可能的新途徑。"},{"en":"A new outlet for a group is a new way, channel, or platform for that group to do something.","zh":"new outlet for a group 指某群體做某事的新方式、渠道或平台。"},{"en":"A school podcast can become a new outlet for students to practise speaking.","zh":"學校播客可以成為學生練習口語的新途徑。"},{"en":"New outlets create opportunities, but they also require careful design.","zh":"新途徑創造機會，但也需要仔細設計。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a new path or medium for activity.","zh":"這個短語描述活動的新路徑或媒介。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"this age group","meaning":"這個年齡組別","examples":[{"en":"The team designed games for this age group.","zh":"團隊為這個年齡組別設計遊戲。"},{"en":"This age group means the group of people of the age being discussed.","zh":"this age group 指正在討論的年齡群體。"},{"en":"This age group may need larger pictures and shorter instructions than older students.","zh":"這個年齡組別可能比年長學生需要更大圖像和更短指示。"},{"en":"Designing for a specific age group helps avoid tasks that are too easy or too difficult.","zh":"為特定年齡組別設計，有助避免任務太易或太難。"},{"en":"The phrase points back to the age range already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指回前文提到的年齡範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"result from","meaning":"由……產生","examples":[{"en":"The games that resulted were released in other regions.","zh":"由此產生的遊戲在其他地區推出。"},{"en":"To result from something means to happen or be produced because of it.","zh":"result from something 指因某事而發生或被產生。"},{"en":"Better test scores may result from regular practice and clear feedback.","zh":"更好的考試分數可能由定期練習和清楚回饋產生。"},{"en":"If research guides design, more suitable products may result.","zh":"如果研究指導設計，可能產生更合適的產品。"},{"en":"The phrase links an outcome to its cause.","zh":"這個短語把結果與原因連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be released in","meaning":"在……推出","examples":[{"en":"The games were released in other regions.","zh":"這些遊戲在其他地區推出。"},{"en":"To be released in a place means to be made available there for people to buy or use.","zh":"be released in a place 指在某地正式供人購買或使用。"},{"en":"A film may be released in Hong Kong a month after it appears in Japan.","zh":"一部電影可能在日本上映一個月後才在香港推出。"},{"en":"Releasing a product in more regions can reach more users and markets.","zh":"在更多地區推出產品可以接觸更多用戶和市場。"},{"en":"The phrase describes official availability in a location.","zh":"這個短語描述某地的正式供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"other regions","meaning":"其他地區","examples":[{"en":"The games were also released in other regions.","zh":"這些遊戲也在其他地區推出。"},{"en":"Other regions are places or markets outside the first area being discussed.","zh":"other regions 指正在討論的第一個地區以外的地方或市場。"},{"en":"A textbook popular in Hong Kong may later be sold in other regions.","zh":"一本在香港受歡迎的教科書，之後可能在其他地區出售。"},{"en":"If a product works in other regions, its characters or design may have wider appeal.","zh":"如果產品在其他地區也成功，其角色或設計可能有更廣泛吸引力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to additional geographical areas.","zh":"這個短語指額外地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"due to","meaning":"由於","examples":[{"en":"The games reached other regions due to the characters’ international appeal.","zh":"這些遊戲由於角色的國際吸引力而到達其他地區。"},{"en":"Due to means because of.","zh":"due to 指因為或由於。"},{"en":"The picnic was cancelled due to heavy rain.","zh":"野餐由於大雨而取消。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the reason for an event or result.","zh":"這個短語引入事件或結果的原因。"},{"en":"It is often used in formal explanation.","zh":"它常用於正式解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"broad international reach","meaning":"廣泛的國際影響力","examples":[{"en":"The characters had broad international reach.","zh":"這些角色有廣泛的國際影響力。"},{"en":"Broad international reach means the ability to attract or be recognised by people in many countries.","zh":"broad international reach 指能吸引或被許多國家的人認識。"},{"en":"A cartoon with broad international reach may be watched by children on several continents.","zh":"有廣泛國際影響力的卡通可能被幾個大洲的兒童觀看。"},{"en":"International reach helps companies sell products beyond one local market.","zh":"國際影響力幫助公司把產品銷售到本地市場以外。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses wide cross-border appeal.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛跨國吸引力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in order to design","meaning":"為了設計","examples":[{"en":"Research was conducted in order to design the best possible DS product.","zh":"研究是為了設計盡可能最好的 DS 產品而進行。"},{"en":"In order to design means for the purpose of creating or planning a product carefully.","zh":"in order to design 指為了仔細創造或規劃某產品。"},{"en":"A teacher may interview students in order to design a better revision course.","zh":"老師可能訪問學生，為了設計更好的溫習課程。"},{"en":"Understanding users first can make the final design more useful.","zh":"先了解使用者可以令最終設計更有用。"},{"en":"The phrase connects research with the goal of design.","zh":"這個短語把研究與設計目標連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the best possible","meaning":"盡可能最好的","examples":[{"en":"The team wanted to design the best possible DS product.","zh":"團隊希望設計盡可能最好的 DS 產品。"},{"en":"The best possible means as good as it can reasonably be under the conditions.","zh":"best possible 指在現有條件下合理地做到最好。"},{"en":"A student may write the best possible essay by planning, drafting, and checking carefully.","zh":"學生可以透過構思、起稿和仔細檢查，寫出盡可能最好的作文。"},{"en":"To achieve the best possible result, people need clear goals and useful feedback.","zh":"要取得盡可能最好的結果，人們需要清楚目標和有用回饋。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses maximum quality within realistic limits.","zh":"這個短語強調在現實限制內達到最高質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"preschool audience","meaning":"學前兒童受眾","examples":[{"en":"The DS product was designed for a preschool audience.","zh":"這個 DS 產品是為學前兒童受眾而設計的。"},{"en":"A preschool audience is a group of very young children before primary school age.","zh":"preschool audience 指小學前的年幼兒童群體。"},{"en":"A puppet show for a preschool audience uses simple words and bright actions.","zh":"面向學前兒童受眾的木偶劇會使用簡單詞語和鮮明動作。"},{"en":"If the audience is preschool-aged, instructions must be short, spoken, and visual.","zh":"如果受眾是學前兒童，指示必須簡短、口頭和視覺化。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies young children as the intended users or viewers.","zh":"這個短語指出年幼兒童是預定使用者或觀眾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be fully committed to","meaning":"完全致力於","examples":[{"en":"The team was fully committed to a user-centred approach.","zh":"團隊完全致力於以用戶為中心的方法。"},{"en":"To be fully committed to something means to support it seriously and consistently.","zh":"be fully committed to something 指認真而持續地支持某事。"},{"en":"A school may be fully committed to helping weaker students, not only top students.","zh":"學校可能完全致力於幫助較弱學生，而不只是尖子。"},{"en":"Full commitment affects decisions, resources, and daily practice.","zh":"完全投入會影響決定、資源和日常做法。"},{"en":"The phrase shows strong dedication, not casual interest.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈投入，而不是隨便感興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the ideals of","meaning":"……的理念","examples":[{"en":"The team followed the ideals of a user-centred approach.","zh":"團隊遵循以用戶為中心方法的理念。"},{"en":"The ideals of something are its guiding principles or values.","zh":"ideals of something 指某事背後的指導原則或價值。"},{"en":"The ideals of good teaching include fairness, clarity, patience, and useful feedback.","zh":"良好教學的理念包括公平、清晰、耐性和有用回饋。"},{"en":"Ideals guide decisions when people face practical problems or trade-offs.","zh":"當人們面對實際問題或取捨時，理念會指導決定。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to values behind an approach.","zh":"這個短語指某方法背後的價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"user-centred approach","meaning":"以用戶為中心的方法","examples":[{"en":"The researchers used a user-centred approach to game design.","zh":"研究人員使用以用戶為中心的方法來設計遊戲。"},{"en":"A user-centred approach is a way of designing that begins with the needs, abilities, and experiences of users.","zh":"user-centred approach 指從使用者需要、能力和經驗出發的設計方法。"},{"en":"A school website designed with a user-centred approach would be easy for parents to find notices.","zh":"以用戶為中心設計的學校網站，應讓家長容易找到通告。"},{"en":"This approach can prevent designers from building something only adults understand.","zh":"這種方法可以防止設計者製作出只有成年人明白的東西。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses designing around real users.","zh":"這個短語強調圍繞真實使用者設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"assume that","meaning":"假設；認為","examples":[{"en":"A user-centred approach assumes that users should be considered.","zh":"以用戶為中心的方法認為使用者應被考慮。"},{"en":"To assume that means to take something as true or important when thinking or planning.","zh":"assume that 指在思考或規劃時把某事視為真實或重要。"},{"en":"A teacher should not assume that all students have quiet places to study at home.","zh":"老師不應假設所有學生家中都有安靜溫習地方。"},{"en":"Wrong assumptions can lead to poor design or unfair decisions.","zh":"錯誤假設可以導致差劣設計或不公平決定。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a belief behind an argument or plan.","zh":"這個短語引入論點或計劃背後的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be considered","meaning":"被考慮","examples":[{"en":"Users should be considered during the development process.","zh":"使用者應在開發過程中被考慮。"},{"en":"To be considered means to be thought about carefully when decisions are made.","zh":"be considered 指在作決定時被仔細想及。"},{"en":"Students’ travel time should be considered before a school changes its start time.","zh":"學校改變上課時間前，應考慮學生通勤時間。"},{"en":"If users are not considered, a product may fail even if the technology is strong.","zh":"如果使用者沒有被考慮，即使技術強，產品也可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase means being included in planning and judgement.","zh":"這個短語指被納入規劃和判斷之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ideally consulted","meaning":"理想情況下被諮詢","examples":[{"en":"Users should ideally be consulted during development.","zh":"使用者在開發期間理想情況下應被諮詢。"},{"en":"Ideally consulted means, in the best situation, users are asked for their opinions before decisions are final.","zh":"ideally consulted 指在最好情況下，使用者會在最終決定前被詢問意見。"},{"en":"Students should ideally be consulted before a school changes the lunch menu.","zh":"學校改變午餐餐單前，理想情況下應諮詢學生。"},{"en":"Consultation can reveal problems planners may not see from their own position.","zh":"諮詢可以揭示規劃者從自身位置看不到的問題。"},{"en":"The phrase shows what should happen in a good design process.","zh":"這個短語顯示良好設計過程中應發生甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"development process","meaning":"開發過程","examples":[{"en":"Children should be considered during the development process.","zh":"兒童應在開發過程中被考慮。"},{"en":"The development process is the series of steps used to create, test, and improve a product.","zh":"development process 指創造、測試和改善產品的一連串步驟。"},{"en":"A school app’s development process may include planning, testing with teachers, and revising.","zh":"學校應用程式的開發過程可能包括規劃、與老師測試和修改。"},{"en":"If users are included early in the process, the product can better match their needs.","zh":"如果使用者早期被納入過程，產品可以更符合他們需要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the path from idea to finished product.","zh":"這個短語描述由想法到完成產品的路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"after all","meaning":"畢竟","examples":[{"en":"After all, young children have specific physical and cognitive abilities.","zh":"畢竟，年幼兒童有特定身體和認知能力。"},{"en":"After all is used to remind readers of an important reason that supports the point.","zh":"after all 用來提醒讀者一個支持該觀點的重要原因。"},{"en":"We should give students breaks; after all, they cannot concentrate for hours without rest.","zh":"我們應給學生休息；畢竟，他們不能連續幾小時不休息地專心。"},{"en":"The phrase often explains why the previous claim is reasonable.","zh":"這個短語常解釋為何前一句說法合理。"},{"en":"It means “when you consider this important fact”.","zh":"它意思是「考慮到這個重要事實」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"interactive product","meaning":"互動產品","examples":[{"en":"A video game is an interactive product.","zh":"電子遊戲是一種互動產品。"},{"en":"An interactive product is something users actively control, respond to, or change while using it.","zh":"interactive product 指使用者在使用時會主動控制、回應或改變的產品。"},{"en":"A learning app is interactive if students tap, speak, choose answers, and receive feedback.","zh":"如果學生要點擊、說話、選答案並收到回饋，學習應用程式就是互動的。"},{"en":"Interactive products must match users’ abilities because users are not just watching passively.","zh":"互動產品必須配合使用者能力，因為使用者不是只被動觀看。"},{"en":"The phrase describes products that require user action.","zh":"這個短語描述需要使用者行動的產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"child market","meaning":"兒童市場","examples":[{"en":"Introducing products to the child market requires careful research.","zh":"把產品引入兒童市場需要仔細研究。"},{"en":"The child market is the group of children and families targeted by products for children.","zh":"child market 指兒童產品所針對的兒童和家庭群體。"},{"en":"Toy companies study the child market before designing new puzzles or games.","zh":"玩具公司在設計新拼圖或遊戲前會研究兒童市場。"},{"en":"Because children have limited skills and depend on parents, this market needs special care.","zh":"因為兒童能力有限且依賴家長，這個市場需要特別小心。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to children as product users or consumers.","zh":"這個短語指作為產品使用者或消費者的兒童。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"particularly","meaning":"尤其","examples":[{"en":"The issue is important, particularly for very young children.","zh":"這個問題很重要，尤其對非常年幼的兒童而言。"},{"en":"Particularly means especially or more than usual in a specific case.","zh":"particularly 指尤其，或在某特定情況下比平常更重要。"},{"en":"Clear instructions are important for all students, particularly for beginners.","zh":"清楚指示對所有學生都重要，尤其對初學者。"},{"en":"The word highlights the group or situation that needs extra attention.","zh":"這個詞突出需要額外關注的群體或情況。"},{"en":"It helps narrow a general point to a special case.","zh":"它幫助把一般重點收窄到特殊情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"young age group","meaning":"年幼年齡組別","examples":[{"en":"The researchers focused on a very young age group.","zh":"研究人員集中於一個非常年幼的年齡組別。"},{"en":"A young age group is a set of people who are close in age and still early in development.","zh":"young age group 指年齡相近且仍處於早期發展階段的一群人。"},{"en":"A kindergarten class is a young age group that needs short activities and simple language.","zh":"幼稚園班級是一個年幼年齡組別，需要短活動和簡單語言。"},{"en":"The younger the age group, the more important developmental limits become.","zh":"年齡組別越年幼，發展限制就越重要。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies children by age and stage.","zh":"這個短語按年齡和階段辨認兒童。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"it is crucial to","meaning":"……是至關重要的","examples":[{"en":"It is crucial to assess children’s physical and cognitive abilities.","zh":"評估兒童的身體和認知能力是至關重要的。"},{"en":"It is crucial to means it is extremely important to do something.","zh":"it is crucial to 指做某事極為重要。"},{"en":"It is crucial to check a child’s allergy record before serving school lunch.","zh":"在提供學校午餐前，檢查孩子的過敏紀錄是至關重要的。"},{"en":"If a crucial step is missed, the final decision may be unsafe or ineffective.","zh":"如果錯過關鍵步驟，最終決定可能不安全或無效。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that something is necessary, not optional.","zh":"這個短語強調某事是必要的，不是可有可無。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"assess the range of","meaning":"評估……的範圍","examples":[{"en":"Researchers must assess the range of children’s abilities.","zh":"研究人員必須評估兒童能力的範圍。"},{"en":"To assess the range of something means to evaluate how broad, varied, or limited it is.","zh":"assess the range of something 指評估某事有多廣、多樣或有限。"},{"en":"A teacher may assess the range of students’ writing skills before planning lessons.","zh":"老師在規劃課堂前，可能評估學生寫作能力的範圍。"},{"en":"Knowing the range prevents tasks from being too hard for some users and too easy for others.","zh":"了解範圍可以防止任務對部分使用者太難、對另一些太易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful evaluation of variation.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細評估差異範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"physical and cognitive abilities","meaning":"身體和認知能力","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers have developing physical and cognitive abilities.","zh":"學前兒童有正在發展中的身體和認知能力。"},{"en":"Physical and cognitive abilities are body skills and thinking skills.","zh":"physical and cognitive abilities 指身體技能和思考技能。"},{"en":"A child’s physical abilities include hand control, while cognitive abilities include memory and understanding.","zh":"兒童的身體能力包括手部控制，而認知能力包括記憶和理解。"},{"en":"If both types of ability are still developing, a game must use simple actions and ideas.","zh":"如果兩類能力仍在發展，遊戲就必須使用簡單動作和概念。"},{"en":"The phrase covers what children can do with their bodies and minds.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋兒童用身體和頭腦能做到甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be associated with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Abilities are associated with a child’s developmental stage.","zh":"能力與兒童的發展階段有關。"},{"en":"To be associated with something means to be connected with it.","zh":"be associated with something 指與某事有關聯。"},{"en":"Tiredness is often associated with poor sleep and heavy homework.","zh":"疲倦常與睡眠不足和功課繁重有關。"},{"en":"If abilities are linked to development, designers must consider age and maturity.","zh":"如果能力與發展有關，設計者必須考慮年齡和成熟程度。"},{"en":"The phrase shows connection, not always direct cause.","zh":"這個短語顯示關聯，不一定是直接原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"specific developmental stage","meaning":"特定發展階段","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers are at a specific developmental stage.","zh":"學前兒童處於一個特定發展階段。"},{"en":"A specific developmental stage is a particular point in a child’s physical, mental, and social growth.","zh":"specific developmental stage 指兒童身體、心理和社交成長中的某一特定階段。"},{"en":"A toddler and a six-year-old are at different developmental stages, so they need different tasks.","zh":"幼兒和六歲兒童處於不同發展階段，所以需要不同任務。"},{"en":"If a task does not match the stage, the child may be confused or frustrated.","zh":"如果任務不配合該階段，孩子可能困惑或挫敗。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to where a child is in the growth process.","zh":"這個短語指兒童在成長過程中的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"review some of","meaning":"回顧部分……","examples":[{"en":"Revelle and Medoff review some of the basic reasons for the problem.","zh":"Revelle 和 Medoff 回顧了造成該問題的部分基本原因。"},{"en":"To review some of something means to examine or discuss part of it again or in summary.","zh":"review some of something 指重新檢視或概括討論其中一部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may review some of the common mistakes before returning essays.","zh":"老師派回作文前，可能回顧部分常見錯誤。"},{"en":"Reviewing key reasons helps readers understand the problem step by step.","zh":"回顧關鍵原因幫助讀者逐步理解問題。"},{"en":"The phrase means looking at selected points, not every possible detail.","zh":"這個短語意思是檢視選定重點，而不是每個可能細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"basic reasons why","meaning":"……的基本原因","examples":[{"en":"The authors explain the basic reasons why games are difficult for preschoolers.","zh":"作者解釋遊戲對學前兒童困難的基本原因。"},{"en":"Basic reasons why means the main simple causes that explain a situation.","zh":"basic reasons why 指解釋某情況的主要簡單原因。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain the basic reasons why students lose marks in writing.","zh":"老師可能解釋學生作文失分的基本原因。"},{"en":"Understanding basic reasons helps people fix the root of a problem.","zh":"理解基本原因幫助人處理問題根源。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces clear causes, not complicated side details.","zh":"這個短語引入清楚原因，而不是複雜旁枝細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"home entertainment systems","meaning":"家庭娛樂系統","examples":[{"en":"Home entertainment systems can be difficult for preschoolers to use.","zh":"家庭娛樂系統對學前兒童來說可能難以使用。"},{"en":"Home entertainment systems are devices at home used for games, films, music, or television.","zh":"home entertainment systems 指家中用於遊戲、電影、音樂或電視的裝置。"},{"en":"A television, game console, speaker, and remote control can be part of a home entertainment system.","zh":"電視、遊戲機、揚聲器和遙控器都可以是家庭娛樂系統的一部分。"},{"en":"If a system has many menus and buttons, young children may need adult help.","zh":"如果系統有許多選單和按鈕，年幼兒童可能需要成人協助。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to entertainment technology used in the home.","zh":"這個短語指家中使用的娛樂科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"electronic gaming devices","meaning":"電子遊戲裝置","examples":[{"en":"Electronic gaming devices are often difficult for preschoolers to use.","zh":"電子遊戲裝置對學前兒童來說通常難以使用。"},{"en":"Electronic gaming devices are machines or handheld tools used to play digital games.","zh":"electronic gaming devices 指用來玩數碼遊戲的機器或手提工具。"},{"en":"A console controller, tablet, or hand-held game machine can be an electronic gaming device.","zh":"遊戲機控制器、平板電腦或手提式遊戲機都可以是電子遊戲裝置。"},{"en":"Devices with small buttons or complex menus can frustrate young users.","zh":"有細小按鈕或複雜選單的裝置可以令年幼用戶挫敗。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the hardware used for digital play.","zh":"這個短語重點是用於數碼遊戲的硬件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"difficult for someone to use","meaning":"對某人來說難以使用","examples":[{"en":"Many gaming devices are difficult for preschoolers to use.","zh":"許多遊戲裝置對學前兒童來說難以使用。"},{"en":"Difficult for someone to use means that person struggles to operate or understand it.","zh":"difficult for someone to use 指某人在操作或理解某物時有困難。"},{"en":"A website with tiny text is difficult for older users to use.","zh":"文字很小的網站對長者來說難以使用。"},{"en":"If a tool is difficult to use, people may avoid it or make repeated mistakes.","zh":"如果工具難以使用，人們可能會避開它或反覆犯錯。"},{"en":"The phrase connects difficulty with a specific user group.","zh":"這個短語把困難與特定使用者群體連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in addition to","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"In addition to developing motor skills, preschoolers face cognitive challenges.","zh":"除了動作技能仍在發展之外，學前兒童還面對認知挑戰。"},{"en":"In addition to means as well as or besides another thing.","zh":"in addition to 指除了某事之外，也包括另一事。"},{"en":"In addition to vocabulary, students need grammar and organisation for good writing.","zh":"除了詞彙之外，學生需要文法和組織能力才能寫好文章。"},{"en":"The phrase adds another important point to the discussion.","zh":"這個短語為討論加入另一個重要重點。"},{"en":"It shows that more than one factor matters.","zh":"它顯示重要因素不止一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"still developing motor skills","meaning":"仍在發展中的動作技能","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers have still developing motor skills.","zh":"學前兒童有仍在發展中的動作技能。"},{"en":"Still developing motor skills are movement abilities that are not yet fully mature.","zh":"still developing motor skills 指尚未完全成熟的動作能力。"},{"en":"A young child with still developing motor skills may find scissors difficult to control.","zh":"有仍在發展中動作技能的年幼孩子，可能覺得剪刀難以控制。"},{"en":"If motor skills are still developing, small buttons and precise movements can be hard.","zh":"如果動作技能仍在發展，細小按鈕和精確動作可能很困難。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why physical controls may be challenging for children.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何實體控制對兒童可能具挑戰性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"manipulate a controller","meaning":"操控控制器","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers may find it difficult to manipulate a controller.","zh":"學前兒童可能覺得難以操控控制器。"},{"en":"To manipulate a controller means to hold and operate it accurately with the hands.","zh":"manipulate a controller 指用手準確拿着和操作控制器。"},{"en":"A child may struggle to manipulate a controller if the buttons are too small.","zh":"如果按鈕太小，孩子可能難以操控控制器。"},{"en":"Poor control can make the character move incorrectly and frustrate the player.","zh":"控制不好會令角色錯誤移動，並令玩家挫敗。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on physical handling and control.","zh":"這個短語重點是身體操作和控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"small buttons","meaning":"細小按鈕","examples":[{"en":"Controllers with small buttons are difficult for young children.","zh":"有細小按鈕的控制器對年幼兒童來說很困難。"},{"en":"Small buttons are tiny controls that must be pressed with the fingers.","zh":"small buttons 指必須用手指按下的微小控制鍵。"},{"en":"A remote control with small buttons may be hard for a grandparent or child to use.","zh":"有細小按鈕的遙控器可能對祖父母或孩子來說難以使用。"},{"en":"Small buttons require fine finger control, so young children may press the wrong one.","zh":"細小按鈕需要精細手指控制，所以年幼兒童可能按錯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a physical design feature that affects usability.","zh":"這個短語描述影響易用性的實體設計特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"major stumbling blocks","meaning":"主要障礙","examples":[{"en":"Many of the major stumbling blocks are cognitive.","zh":"許多主要障礙屬於認知方面。"},{"en":"Major stumbling blocks are big obstacles that make progress difficult.","zh":"major stumbling blocks 指令進展困難的重大障礙。"},{"en":"For many students, fear of speaking is a major stumbling block in English learning.","zh":"對許多學生來說，害怕開口是學英文的主要障礙。"},{"en":"If a stumbling block is cognitive, clearer explanations and simpler choices may help.","zh":"如果障礙是認知方面，更清楚解釋和更簡單選擇可能有幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase means serious barriers, not small inconveniences.","zh":"這個短語指嚴重障礙，而不是小不便。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cognitive","meaning":"認知方面的","examples":[{"en":"Many problems with game use are cognitive.","zh":"許多遊戲使用問題是認知方面的。"},{"en":"Cognitive means related to thinking, understanding, memory, and learning.","zh":"cognitive 指與思考、理解、記憶和學習有關。"},{"en":"Reading a timetable is a cognitive task because the student must understand symbols and times.","zh":"閱讀時間表是一項認知任務，因為學生必須理解符號和時間。"},{"en":"Cognitive difficulty can occur even when a child can physically press the button.","zh":"即使孩子能實際按按鈕，也可能出現認知困難。"},{"en":"The word refers to mental processes, not body movement.","zh":"這個詞指心理過程，而不是身體動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"think symbolically","meaning":"以符號方式思考","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers are learning to think symbolically.","zh":"學前兒童正在學習以符號方式思考。"},{"en":"To think symbolically means to understand that one thing can represent another thing.","zh":"think symbolically 指理解一件事物可以代表另一件事物。"},{"en":"A child thinks symbolically when she uses a block as a pretend phone.","zh":"孩子把積木當作假電話使用時，就是以符號方式思考。"},{"en":"Symbolic thinking helps children understand pictures, icons, and game characters.","zh":"符號思考幫助兒童理解圖畫、圖示和遊戲角色。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an important stage in mental development.","zh":"這個短語描述心智發展中的重要階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stand for","meaning":"代表","examples":[{"en":"Pictures can stand for real-life objects.","zh":"圖畫可以代表現實生活中的物件。"},{"en":"To stand for something means to represent it.","zh":"stand for something 指代表某事物。"},{"en":"A red traffic light stands for “stop”.","zh":"紅色交通燈代表「停止」。"},{"en":"If children know what icons stand for, they can use a game without reading words.","zh":"如果兒童知道圖示代表甚麼，他們即使不讀文字也能使用遊戲。"},{"en":"The phrase links a symbol with its meaning.","zh":"這個短語把符號與其意思連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"real-life objects","meaning":"現實生活中的物件","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers can understand that pictures represent real-life objects.","zh":"學前兒童可以理解圖畫代表現實生活中的物件。"},{"en":"Real-life objects are actual things that exist in the everyday world.","zh":"real-life objects 指日常世界中實際存在的東西。"},{"en":"A picture of an apple can represent the real-life object a child eats at lunch.","zh":"蘋果圖片可以代表孩子午餐時吃的現實生活物件。"},{"en":"Understanding this link helps children connect screen images with the world they know.","zh":"理解這種聯繫幫助兒童把屏幕圖像與他們熟悉的世界連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts real objects with pictures, symbols, or game images.","zh":"這個短語把真實物件與圖片、符號或遊戲圖像作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the vast majority","meaning":"絕大多數","examples":[{"en":"The vast majority of preschoolers are still unable to read and write.","zh":"絕大多數學前兒童仍然不能讀寫。"},{"en":"The vast majority means almost all or a very large proportion of a group.","zh":"the vast majority 指幾乎全部或非常大比例的人。"},{"en":"The vast majority of students need examples before they can use a new phrase well.","zh":"絕大多數學生需要例句，才可以好好使用新短語。"},{"en":"If the vast majority cannot read, written instructions will fail for most users.","zh":"如果絕大多數人不能閱讀，書面指示對大多數用戶都會失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly emphasises that most people in the group share the same condition.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調群體中大多數人有相同情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be unable to","meaning":"不能夠","examples":[{"en":"Most preschoolers are unable to read and write.","zh":"大多數學前兒童不能夠讀寫。"},{"en":"To be unable to do something means not to have the ability to do it.","zh":"be unable to do something 指沒有能力做某事。"},{"en":"A child may be unable to tie shoelaces before learning the steps slowly.","zh":"孩子在慢慢學習步驟前，可能不能夠綁鞋帶。"},{"en":"If users are unable to read, a product must use pictures or sound instead.","zh":"如果使用者不能閱讀，產品就必須改用圖像或聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lack of ability, not unwillingness.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏能力，而不是不願意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"read and write","meaning":"讀寫","examples":[{"en":"Preschool children are largely unable to read and write.","zh":"學前兒童大多不能讀寫。"},{"en":"To read and write means to understand written words and produce written language.","zh":"read and write 指理解書面文字並寫出文字。"},{"en":"A five-year-old may recognise some letters but not yet read and write full sentences.","zh":"五歲孩子可能認得一些字母，但尚未能讀寫完整句子。"},{"en":"If children cannot read and write, text-based games become difficult.","zh":"如果兒童不能讀寫，以文字為主的遊戲會變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to basic literacy skills.","zh":"這個短語指基本讀寫能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"text-based menu selections","meaning":"文字式選單選項","examples":[{"en":"Text-based menu selections are not suitable for preschoolers.","zh":"文字式選單選項不適合學前兒童。"},{"en":"Text-based menu selections are choices shown mainly through written words rather than pictures or sound.","zh":"text-based menu selections 指主要透過文字而不是圖像或聲音顯示的選項。"},{"en":"A restaurant app with text-based menu selections may be hard for a young child to use.","zh":"有文字式選單選項的餐廳應用程式，對年幼孩子可能難以使用。"},{"en":"If users cannot read, text menus prevent them from choosing independently.","zh":"如果使用者不能閱讀，文字選單會阻止他們獨立選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase describes written options in a digital interface.","zh":"這個短語描述數碼介面中的書面選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not viable","meaning":"不可行","examples":[{"en":"Using text-based menu selections is not viable for preschoolers.","zh":"對學前兒童使用文字式選單選項是不可行的。"},{"en":"Not viable means not practical or not able to work successfully.","zh":"not viable 指不實際或不能成功運作。"},{"en":"A study plan with ten hours of homework every night is not viable for most students.","zh":"每晚十小時功課的學習計劃對大多數學生來說不可行。"},{"en":"If most preschoolers cannot read, a text-only design is not viable.","zh":"如果大多數學前兒童不能閱讀，純文字設計就不可行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that cannot realistically succeed.","zh":"這個短語描述現實上不能成功的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mapping","meaning":"操作對應","examples":[{"en":"Mapping is another obstacle for preschool users.","zh":"操作對應是學前兒童用戶的另一個障礙。"},{"en":"Mapping is the connection between a user’s action and what happens on the screen.","zh":"mapping 指使用者動作與屏幕上發生事情之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"Pressing a right arrow and seeing a character move right is a simple example of mapping.","zh":"按向右箭嘴後看見角色向右移動，是操作對應的簡單例子。"},{"en":"If mapping is unclear, children may not understand why the screen changes.","zh":"如果操作對應不清楚，兒童可能不明白屏幕為何改變。"},{"en":"The word describes action-screen correspondence in game control.","zh":"這個詞描述遊戲控制中的動作與屏幕對應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"yet another obstacle","meaning":"另一個障礙","examples":[{"en":"Mapping is yet another obstacle for preschoolers.","zh":"操作對應是學前兒童的另一個障礙。"},{"en":"Yet another obstacle means one more difficulty in addition to the others already mentioned.","zh":"yet another obstacle 指除已提到的困難外，又多一個困難。"},{"en":"For a tired student, a noisy classroom is yet another obstacle to concentration.","zh":"對疲倦學生來說，嘈雜課室是專心的另一個障礙。"},{"en":"When obstacles add up, users may stop trying.","zh":"當障礙累積，使用者可能停止嘗試。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises that the problem is part of a growing list.","zh":"這個短語強調問題屬於一連串障礙之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"direct link between","meaning":"……之間的直接聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Children may not understand the direct link between the controller and the screen.","zh":"兒童可能不理解控制器和屏幕之間的直接聯繫。"},{"en":"A direct link between two things is a clear connection where one thing affects the other.","zh":"direct link between two things 指一件事會影響另一件事的清楚連接。"},{"en":"A child learns the direct link between touching a light switch and turning on the light.","zh":"孩子會學會觸摸電燈開關和開燈之間的直接聯繫。"},{"en":"If children do not see the link, they may press buttons randomly.","zh":"如果兒童看不見這種聯繫，他們可能隨意按按鈕。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an obvious cause-and-effect connection.","zh":"這個短語描述明顯因果連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"appear before them on screen","meaning":"出現在他們面前的屏幕上","examples":[{"en":"Activities appear before the children on screen.","zh":"活動出現在兒童面前的屏幕上。"},{"en":"To appear before someone on screen means to be shown visually on a digital display in front of them.","zh":"appear before someone on screen 指在某人面前的數碼顯示器上以視覺方式出現。"},{"en":"A picture may appear before students on screen during an online lesson.","zh":"網上課堂中，圖片可能出現在學生面前的屏幕上。"},{"en":"If actions appear on screen but do not match children’s controls, confusion can occur.","zh":"如果屏幕上的動作與兒童控制不相符，就可能產生困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what users see on a screen.","zh":"這個短語描述使用者在屏幕上看見的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"this aspect is changing","meaning":"這方面正在改變","examples":[{"en":"This aspect of game design is changing.","zh":"遊戲設計的這方面正在改變。"},{"en":"This aspect is changing means this particular part is becoming different over time.","zh":"this aspect is changing 指某一特定部分正隨時間變得不同。"},{"en":"The way students submit homework is changing as more schools use online platforms.","zh":"隨着更多學校使用網上平台，學生交功課的方式正在改變。"},{"en":"Change often happens when new technology makes older methods less necessary.","zh":"當新科技令舊方法較不必要，改變常會發生。"},{"en":"The phrase points to one part of a topic that is developing.","zh":"這個短語指出某主題中正在發展的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"traditional mapping systems","meaning":"傳統操作對應系統","examples":[{"en":"Traditional mapping systems can be difficult for preschoolers.","zh":"傳統操作對應系統對學前兒童來說可能很困難。"},{"en":"Traditional mapping systems are older ways of connecting controller actions to on-screen actions.","zh":"traditional mapping systems 指較舊的控制器動作與屏幕動作連接方式。"},{"en":"A traditional controller may require children to press arrows and buttons at the same time.","zh":"傳統控制器可能要求兒童同時按方向鍵和按鈕。"},{"en":"If the system does not match real-life movement, children may find it hard to understand.","zh":"如果系統不配合現實生活動作，兒童可能覺得難以理解。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to older control-action designs.","zh":"這個短語指較舊的控制與動作設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"real-life movements","meaning":"現實生活中的動作","examples":[{"en":"Real-life movements do not always translate into game-based activity.","zh":"現實生活中的動作不一定會轉化為遊戲中的活動。"},{"en":"Real-life movements are physical actions people make in the everyday world.","zh":"real-life movements 指人們在日常世界中做出的身體動作。"},{"en":"A child waving a hand or touching a picture is making real-life movements.","zh":"孩子揮手或觸摸圖片，就是在做現實生活中的動作。"},{"en":"If a game uses natural movements, young children may understand it more easily.","zh":"如果遊戲使用自然動作，年幼兒童可能更容易理解。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts body actions with actions inside a game.","zh":"這個短語把身體動作與遊戲內動作作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"translate into","meaning":"轉化為","examples":[{"en":"Real-life movements may not translate into game-based activity.","zh":"現實生活中的動作可能不會轉化為遊戲中的活動。"},{"en":"To translate into something means to turn into or correspond to another form or result.","zh":"translate into something 指變成或對應到另一形式或結果。"},{"en":"A student’s hard work may translate into better exam performance.","zh":"學生的努力可能轉化為更好的考試表現。"},{"en":"If hand movements do not translate clearly into screen actions, users may feel confused.","zh":"如果手部動作不能清楚轉化為屏幕動作，使用者可能感到困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes conversion from one form to another.","zh":"這個短語描述由一種形式轉成另一種形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"game-based activity","meaning":"遊戲中的活動","examples":[{"en":"Traditional controls do not always match game-based activity.","zh":"傳統控制方式不一定配合遊戲中的活動。"},{"en":"Game-based activity is the action that happens inside a video game.","zh":"game-based activity 指電子遊戲內發生的行動。"},{"en":"Jumping over a river, choosing a picture, or feeding a virtual pet are game-based activities.","zh":"跳過河流、選擇圖片或餵養虛擬寵物都是遊戲中的活動。"},{"en":"If controls do not match the activity, players may not understand what to do.","zh":"如果控制方式不配合活動，玩家可能不知道要做甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to actions within the game world.","zh":"這個短語指遊戲世界中的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"over the course of","meaning":"在……過程中","examples":[{"en":"Over the course of the study, the team gained many insights.","zh":"在研究過程中，團隊獲得許多洞見。"},{"en":"Over the course of means during the whole period of an activity or process.","zh":"over the course of 指在某活動或過程的整段期間。"},{"en":"Over the course of a school year, students slowly build stronger writing habits.","zh":"在一個學年過程中，學生會慢慢建立更強寫作習慣。"},{"en":"Long observation can reveal patterns that a single day cannot show.","zh":"長期觀察可以揭示單日看不到的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses development across time.","zh":"這個短語強調隨時間發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"gain insights into","meaning":"深入了解……","examples":[{"en":"The study helped the team gain insights into preschoolers’ behaviour.","zh":"該研究幫助團隊深入了解學前兒童的行為。"},{"en":"To gain insights into something means to understand it more deeply and clearly.","zh":"gain insights into something 指更深入和清楚地理解某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may gain insights into students’ learning by reading their drafts.","zh":"老師可能透過閱讀學生草稿深入了解他們的學習情況。"},{"en":"Insight helps people design better solutions because they understand the real problem.","zh":"洞見幫助人設計更好解決方法，因為他們理解真正問題。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests deeper understanding, not just collecting facts.","zh":"這個短語暗示更深理解，而不只是收集事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"interact with","meaning":"與……互動","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers interact with various gaming platforms in different ways.","zh":"學前兒童以不同方式與各種遊戲平台互動。"},{"en":"To interact with something means to use, respond to, or communicate with it actively.","zh":"interact with something 指主動使用、回應或與某物溝通。"},{"en":"Students interact with a touchscreen by tapping, dragging, and choosing answers.","zh":"學生透過點擊、拖動和選答案與觸控屏互動。"},{"en":"If children interact with a device differently from adults, the design must reflect that.","zh":"如果兒童與裝置互動的方式不同於成人，設計必須反映這一點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active engagement, not passive watching.","zh":"這個短語描述主動參與，而不是被動觀看。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"various platforms","meaning":"各種平台","examples":[{"en":"The researchers studied how children used various platforms.","zh":"研究人員研究兒童如何使用各種平台。"},{"en":"Various platforms are different systems or devices on which games or services can run.","zh":"various platforms 指遊戲或服務可以運行的不同系統或裝置。"},{"en":"Students may use various platforms for learning, such as tablets, laptops, and phones.","zh":"學生可能使用各種學習平台，例如平板電腦、手提電腦和手機。"},{"en":"Different platforms can create different user experiences and difficulties.","zh":"不同平台可以產生不同用戶體驗和困難。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses more than one type of system.","zh":"這個短語強調多於一種系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"For instance, preschoolers need voice-over instructions.","zh":"例如，學前兒童需要語音指示。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance 指例如。"},{"en":"Some school rules protect safety; for instance, students must wear goggles in the laboratory.","zh":"一些校規保護安全；例如，學生在實驗室必須戴護目鏡。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a clear example that supports the previous point.","zh":"這個短語引入支持前一點的清楚例子。"},{"en":"It helps make an abstract idea easier to understand.","zh":"它幫助令抽象想法更容易理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"instructions","meaning":"指示","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers need clear instructions in games.","zh":"學前兒童在遊戲中需要清楚指示。"},{"en":"Instructions are directions that tell people what to do and how to do it.","zh":"instructions 指告訴人做甚麼和如何做的指引。"},{"en":"A worksheet should give simple instructions before asking students to answer questions.","zh":"工作紙在要求學生回答問題前，應提供簡單指示。"},{"en":"If instructions are unclear, users may make mistakes or stop trying.","zh":"如果指示不清楚，使用者可能犯錯或停止嘗試。"},{"en":"The word refers to guidance for action.","zh":"這個詞指行動指引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"voice-over","meaning":"旁白；語音講解","examples":[{"en":"All instructions for preschoolers need to be in voice-over.","zh":"所有給學前兒童的指示都需要以語音講解呈現。"},{"en":"Voice-over is spoken sound added to explain what users should do or what is happening.","zh":"voice-over 指加入的口頭聲音，用來解釋使用者應做甚麼或正在發生甚麼。"},{"en":"A children’s story app may use voice-over to read words aloud.","zh":"兒童故事應用程式可能使用旁白把文字讀出來。"},{"en":"Voice-over helps young users who cannot read written instructions.","zh":"語音講解幫助不能閱讀書面指示的年幼用戶。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to recorded spoken guidance.","zh":"這個短語指錄製的口頭指引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"visual representations","meaning":"視覺表示","examples":[{"en":"Instructions should include visual representations.","zh":"指示應包括視覺表示。"},{"en":"Visual representations are pictures, icons, diagrams, or images that show information visually.","zh":"visual representations 指用視覺方式呈現資訊的圖畫、圖示、圖表或影像。"},{"en":"A map is a visual representation of roads and places.","zh":"地圖是道路和地點的視覺表示。"},{"en":"Visuals help young children understand tasks without relying only on words.","zh":"視覺圖像幫助年幼兒童理解任務，而不只依賴文字。"},{"en":"The phrase describes information shown through images.","zh":"這個短語描述透過圖像呈現的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"negotiate with respect to","meaning":"就……協調處理","examples":[{"en":"Voice-over instructions are difficult to negotiate with respect to DS game design.","zh":"就 DS 遊戲設計而言，語音指示難以協調處理。"},{"en":"To negotiate with respect to something means to manage or balance a difficulty in relation to that issue.","zh":"negotiate with respect to something 指就某議題處理或平衡困難。"},{"en":"A school must negotiate space problems with respect to adding new after-school clubs.","zh":"學校在增加新課後學會時，必須就空間問題作協調處理。"},{"en":"Designers may need to balance what users need with what technology can support.","zh":"設計者可能需要平衡使用者需要和科技能支援的內容。"},{"en":"The phrase describes handling a practical difficulty in a specific area.","zh":"這個短語描述在特定範疇中處理實際困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"with respect to","meaning":"關於","examples":[{"en":"This has been difficult with respect to game design on the DS.","zh":"關於 DS 上的遊戲設計，這一直很困難。"},{"en":"With respect to means regarding or in relation to a particular subject.","zh":"with respect to 指關於或就某特定主題而言。"},{"en":"With respect to homework, students need clearer deadlines.","zh":"關於功課，學生需要更清楚的限期。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows the discussion to one specific area.","zh":"這個短語把討論收窄到一個特定範疇。"},{"en":"It is formal and often used in academic or business writing.","zh":"它較正式，常用於學術或商業寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"game cartridges","meaning":"遊戲卡帶","examples":[{"en":"DS game cartridges have limited memory capacity.","zh":"DS 遊戲卡帶有有限記憶容量。"},{"en":"Game cartridges are small physical storage cards or units that contain video game data.","zh":"game cartridges 指儲存電子遊戲數據的小型實體卡帶或裝置。"},{"en":"Older hand-held game systems used cartridges that players inserted into the device.","zh":"較舊手提遊戲系統使用玩家插入裝置的卡帶。"},{"en":"If a cartridge has limited space, designers must choose what data to include.","zh":"如果卡帶空間有限，設計者必須選擇包括哪些數據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a physical game storage format.","zh":"這個短語指一種實體遊戲儲存形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"limited memory capacity","meaning":"有限記憶容量","examples":[{"en":"Game cartridges have very limited memory capacity.","zh":"遊戲卡帶有非常有限的記憶容量。"},{"en":"Limited memory capacity means a device can store only a small amount of data.","zh":"limited memory capacity 指裝置只能儲存少量數據。"},{"en":"An old phone with limited memory capacity may not hold many photos or apps.","zh":"有有限記憶容量的舊手機可能不能儲存很多照片或應用程式。"},{"en":"If memory is limited, sound files and graphics must be used carefully.","zh":"如果記憶體有限，聲音檔案和圖像就必須小心使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes storage restrictions.","zh":"這個短語描述儲存限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in comparison to","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"DS cartridges have limited memory capacity in comparison to console games.","zh":"與家用遊戲機遊戲相比，DS 卡帶記憶容量有限。"},{"en":"In comparison to means when compared with something else.","zh":"in comparison to 指與另一事物比較時。"},{"en":"A bicycle is cheap to maintain in comparison to a car.","zh":"與汽車相比，單車保養費便宜。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show difference by placing two things side by side.","zh":"這個短語透過把兩件事並列來顯示差異。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining relative strengths or limits.","zh":"它適合用於解釋相對優勢或限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"console games","meaning":"家用遊戲機遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Console games usually have more memory capacity.","zh":"家用遊戲機遊戲通常有更多記憶容量。"},{"en":"Console games are video games played on home gaming systems connected to a screen.","zh":"console games 指在連接螢幕的家用遊戲系統上玩的電子遊戲。"},{"en":"Families may play console games together using controllers in the living room.","zh":"家人可能在客廳用控制器一起玩家用遊戲機遊戲。"},{"en":"Because console systems can have more storage, they may include more sound and graphics.","zh":"因為家用遊戲系統可以有更多儲存空間，它們可能包括更多聲音和圖像。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts home-console games with hand-held games.","zh":"這個短語把家用遊戲機遊戲與手提式遊戲作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"capture large amounts of","meaning":"儲存大量……","examples":[{"en":"The cartridges cannot capture large amounts of voice-over data.","zh":"這些卡帶不能儲存大量語音資料。"},{"en":"To capture large amounts of data means to store or hold a lot of information.","zh":"capture large amounts of data 指儲存或容納大量資訊。"},{"en":"A camera with a small memory card cannot capture large amounts of video.","zh":"記憶卡很小的相機不能儲存大量影片。"},{"en":"If storage cannot capture enough sound, designers must reduce or compress audio files.","zh":"如果儲存空間不能容納足夠聲音，設計者必須減少或壓縮音訊檔案。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on data storage capacity.","zh":"這個短語重點是數據儲存能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"voice-over data","meaning":"語音資料","examples":[{"en":"Voice-over data takes up memory.","zh":"語音資料會佔用記憶體。"},{"en":"Voice-over data is digital sound information used for spoken instructions or narration.","zh":"voice-over data 指用於口頭指示或旁白的數碼聲音資訊。"},{"en":"A story app stores voice-over data so children can hear the words read aloud.","zh":"故事應用程式儲存語音資料，讓兒童聽到文字被讀出。"},{"en":"Because audio files can be large, voice-over data may reduce space for graphics or levels.","zh":"因為音訊檔案可能很大，語音資料可能減少圖像或關卡的空間。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to stored spoken audio in a digital product.","zh":"這個短語指數碼產品中儲存的口頭音訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"via sound files","meaning":"透過聲音檔案","examples":[{"en":"Voice-over data is stored via sound files.","zh":"語音資料透過聲音檔案儲存。"},{"en":"Via sound files means through digital audio files that contain recorded sound.","zh":"via sound files 指透過包含錄音的數碼音訊檔案。"},{"en":"A teacher may send listening practice via sound files to students before class.","zh":"老師可能在上課前透過聲音檔案把聆聽練習發給學生。"},{"en":"Sound files take memory, so using many of them affects storage limits.","zh":"聲音檔案會佔用記憶體，所以使用很多聲音檔案會影響儲存限制。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the method used to store or deliver audio.","zh":"這個短語解釋儲存或傳送音訊的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"become limited","meaning":"變得有限","examples":[{"en":"The ability to include voice-over data becomes limited.","zh":"加入語音資料的能力變得有限。"},{"en":"To become limited means to become restricted or less possible.","zh":"become limited 指變得受限制或較不可能。"},{"en":"A student’s revision time becomes limited if she starts studying too late.","zh":"如果學生太遲開始溫習，她的溫習時間會變得有限。"},{"en":"When storage is small, the number of sounds and images designers can include becomes limited.","zh":"當儲存空間很小，設計者可加入的聲音和圖像數量就變得有限。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growing restriction.","zh":"這個短語描述限制增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take up minimal memory","meaning":"佔用極少記憶體","examples":[{"en":"Text instructions take up minimal memory.","zh":"文字指示佔用極少記憶體。"},{"en":"To take up minimal memory means to use very little digital storage space.","zh":"take up minimal memory 指使用非常少數碼儲存空間。"},{"en":"A simple text note takes up minimal memory compared with a video file.","zh":"與影片檔相比，簡單文字筆記佔用極少記憶體。"},{"en":"When memory is limited, designers may prefer formats that use less space.","zh":"當記憶體有限，設計者可能較喜歡佔用較少空間的格式。"},{"en":"The phrase explains a technological advantage of text.","zh":"這個短語解釋文字的技術優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be preferable from","meaning":"從……角度來看較可取","examples":[{"en":"Text instructions are preferable from a technological perspective.","zh":"從技術角度來看，文字指示較可取。"},{"en":"To be preferable from a perspective means to be better or more suitable when judged in that way.","zh":"be preferable from a perspective 指從某角度判斷時較好或較合適。"},{"en":"Online forms may be preferable from an administrative perspective because they are easier to sort.","zh":"從行政角度來看，網上表格可能較可取，因為較容易整理。"},{"en":"Something can be technologically preferable but still unsuitable for young users.","zh":"某事可以在技術上較可取，但仍不適合年幼用戶。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that “better” depends on the viewpoint.","zh":"這個短語顯示「較好」取決於觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"technological perspective","meaning":"技術角度","examples":[{"en":"Text instructions are easier from a technological perspective.","zh":"從技術角度來看，文字指示較容易處理。"},{"en":"A technological perspective is a way of judging something based on technical limits, tools, or systems.","zh":"technological perspective 指根據技術限制、工具或系統來判斷某事的角度。"},{"en":"From a technological perspective, email is cheaper than printing thousands of letters.","zh":"從技術角度來看，電郵比列印數千封信便宜。"},{"en":"A design may look good technically but fail if users cannot understand it.","zh":"設計在技術上可能很好，但如果使用者不能理解，仍會失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on technology, not teaching, emotion, or culture.","zh":"這個短語重點是科技，而不是教學、情感或文化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"figure out ways to","meaning":"想出方法去……","examples":[{"en":"Designers must figure out ways to maximise sound and graphics files.","zh":"設計者必須想出方法去盡量善用聲音和圖像檔案。"},{"en":"To figure out ways to do something means to think of practical methods for achieving it.","zh":"figure out ways to do something 指想出實際方法去達成某事。"},{"en":"Students must figure out ways to remember vocabulary without simply copying words.","zh":"學生必須想出方法記住詞彙，而不是只抄字。"},{"en":"When limits exist, people need creative methods to reach their goal.","zh":"當存在限制，人們需要創意方法達成目標。"},{"en":"The phrase describes problem-solving.","zh":"這個短語描述解決問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"maximise sound and graphics files","meaning":"盡量善用聲音和圖像檔案","examples":[{"en":"The team tried to maximise sound and graphics files.","zh":"團隊嘗試盡量善用聲音和圖像檔案。"},{"en":"To maximise sound and graphics files means to use audio and image files as effectively as possible within limits.","zh":"maximise sound and graphics files 指在限制內盡可能有效使用音訊和圖像檔案。"},{"en":"A designer may compress pictures to maximise graphics files in a small app.","zh":"設計者可能壓縮圖片，以在小型應用程式中盡量善用圖像檔案。"},{"en":"When memory is limited, maximising files means balancing quality and storage space.","zh":"當記憶體有限，善用檔案代表要平衡質素和儲存空間。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on getting the most value from media files.","zh":"這個短語重點是從媒體檔案中取得最大價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"while retaining","meaning":"同時保留","examples":[{"en":"Designers must maximise files while retaining clear cues.","zh":"設計者必須盡量善用檔案，同時保留清晰提示。"},{"en":"While retaining means while still keeping something important.","zh":"while retaining 指同時仍然保留重要事物。"},{"en":"A teacher can shorten a worksheet while retaining the most useful practice questions.","zh":"老師可以縮短工作紙，同時保留最有用的練習題。"},{"en":"Good design often reduces unnecessary parts while retaining what users need most.","zh":"良好設計常會減少不必要部分，同時保留使用者最需要的內容。"},{"en":"The phrase shows balance between change and preservation.","zh":"這個短語顯示改變與保留之間的平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"visual and verbal cues","meaning":"視覺和語言提示","examples":[{"en":"Young players need clear visual and verbal cues.","zh":"年幼玩家需要清楚的視覺和語言提示。"},{"en":"Visual and verbal cues are picture-based and spoken or word-based signals that guide users.","zh":"visual and verbal cues 指以圖像和語音或文字形式引導使用者的訊號。"},{"en":"A classroom sign and a teacher’s spoken reminder are visual and verbal cues.","zh":"課室標誌和老師的口頭提醒都是視覺和語言提示。"},{"en":"Clear cues help children know where to look, what to press, and what to do next.","zh":"清楚提示幫助兒童知道看哪裏、按甚麼和下一步做甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase combines what users see and what they hear or read.","zh":"這個短語結合使用者看見和聽見或讀到的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be critical for","meaning":"對……至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Clear cues are critical for the youngest players.","zh":"清楚提示對最年幼玩家至關重要。"},{"en":"To be critical for someone means to be extremely important for them.","zh":"be critical for someone 指對某人極為重要。"},{"en":"Clear feedback is critical for students who are learning to write essays.","zh":"清楚回饋對正在學寫作文的學生至關重要。"},{"en":"If something critical is missing, the user may fail even with effort.","zh":"如果缺少關鍵因素，使用者即使努力也可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that a factor is essential, not merely useful.","zh":"這個短語表示某因素不可或缺，而不只是有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"youngest players","meaning":"最年幼玩家","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers are the youngest players in the market.","zh":"學前兒童是市場中最年幼玩家。"},{"en":"Youngest players are the players at the lowest age range among users.","zh":"youngest players 指使用者中年齡最低的一群玩家。"},{"en":"The youngest players in a sports club may need smaller balls and shorter rules.","zh":"運動會中最年幼玩家可能需要較小球和較短規則。"},{"en":"Products for the youngest players must match their limited reading, movement, and attention skills.","zh":"為最年幼玩家設計的產品必須配合他們有限的閱讀、動作和專注能力。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the least mature user group.","zh":"這個短語指出最不成熟的使用者群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a constant give-and-take","meaning":"持續的取捨","examples":[{"en":"Balancing memory and clear instructions is a constant give-and-take.","zh":"平衡記憶體和清楚指示是一種持續的取捨。"},{"en":"A constant give-and-take is an ongoing process of balancing one advantage against another.","zh":"constant give-and-take 指不斷在一個好處和另一個好處之間取得平衡的過程。"},{"en":"A teacher faces a constant give-and-take between giving enough homework and protecting students’ rest.","zh":"老師在給足夠功課和保障學生休息之間面對持續取捨。"},{"en":"If designers add more sound, they may have less space for graphics.","zh":"如果設計者加入更多聲音，他們可能有較少空間放圖像。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated trade-offs.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆出現的取捨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"another of our findings","meaning":"另一項研究發現","examples":[{"en":"Another of the findings concerned how children used the stylus.","zh":"另一項研究發現與兒童如何使用觸控筆有關。"},{"en":"Another of our findings means one more result discovered in the study.","zh":"another of our findings 指研究中發現的另一個結果。"},{"en":"Another of our findings was that students remembered phrases better with daily-life examples.","zh":"另一項研究發現是，學生透過日常生活例子更能記住短語。"},{"en":"Presenting findings one by one helps readers follow the research results clearly.","zh":"逐一呈現研究發現有助讀者清楚跟隨結果。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an additional research result.","zh":"這個短語引入額外研究結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"indicate that","meaning":"顯示","examples":[{"en":"The findings indicated that preschoolers may use either a stylus or their fingers.","zh":"研究發現顯示，學前兒童可能使用觸控筆或手指。"},{"en":"To indicate that means to show or suggest that something is true.","zh":"indicate that 指顯示或暗示某事屬實。"},{"en":"Low quiz scores may indicate that students need more practice with the topic.","zh":"測驗低分可能顯示學生需要更多練習該課題。"},{"en":"Evidence can indicate a pattern without proving every detail completely.","zh":"證據可以顯示一種模式，而不一定完全證明每個細節。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces what evidence suggests.","zh":"這個短語引入證據所暗示的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"stylus","meaning":"觸控筆","examples":[{"en":"Some preschoolers use a stylus when playing DS games.","zh":"有些學前兒童玩 DS 遊戲時使用觸控筆。"},{"en":"A stylus is a small pen-like tool used to touch or write on a screen.","zh":"stylus 指用來觸碰或在螢幕上書寫的小型筆狀工具。"},{"en":"A student may use a stylus to draw diagrams on a tablet.","zh":"學生可能使用觸控筆在平板電腦上畫圖表。"},{"en":"A stylus can allow precise input, but very young children may find it hard to control.","zh":"觸控筆可以提供精確輸入，但非常年幼的兒童可能難以控制。"},{"en":"The word refers to a touch-screen tool, not an ordinary ink pen.","zh":"這個詞指觸控螢幕工具，而不是普通墨水筆。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"not very accurate with","meaning":"使用……時不太準確","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers are not very accurate with either a stylus or their fingers.","zh":"學前兒童使用觸控筆或手指時都不太準確。"},{"en":"Not very accurate with something means unable to use it with much precision.","zh":"not very accurate with something 指使用某物時不太精準。"},{"en":"A young child may not be very accurate with scissors when first learning to cut paper.","zh":"年幼孩子初學剪紙時，使用剪刀可能不太準確。"},{"en":"If children are not accurate with a tool, games should allow larger targets and forgiving controls.","zh":"如果兒童使用工具時不準確，遊戲應提供較大目標和較寬容控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limited precision in using something.","zh":"這個短語描述使用某物時精準度有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"interesting aspects of","meaning":"……的有趣方面","examples":[{"en":"One of the interesting aspects of the DS is its touch interface.","zh":"DS 的有趣方面之一是其觸控介面。"},{"en":"Interesting aspects of something are features or parts that are worth noticing or studying.","zh":"interesting aspects of something 指值得注意或研究的特徵或部分。"},{"en":"One interesting aspect of online lessons is how shy students may speak more in chat.","zh":"網上課堂的一個有趣方面是害羞學生可能在聊天區更願意發言。"},{"en":"Noticing interesting aspects can lead researchers to ask better questions.","zh":"注意到有趣方面可以引導研究人員提出更好問題。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a notable feature.","zh":"這個短語引入值得注意的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"interface","meaning":"介面","examples":[{"en":"The DS interface responds to stylus interactions.","zh":"DS 介面會回應觸控筆操作。"},{"en":"An interface is the part of a device or program that users interact with.","zh":"interface 指使用者與裝置或程式互動的部分。"},{"en":"A phone’s interface includes its icons, menus, buttons, and touch screen.","zh":"手機介面包括圖示、選單、按鈕和觸控螢幕。"},{"en":"If the interface is confusing, users may not know how to control the product.","zh":"如果介面令人困惑，使用者可能不知道如何控制產品。"},{"en":"The word refers to the connection point between user and system.","zh":"這個詞指使用者與系統之間的接觸點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be designed to respond to","meaning":"被設計成會回應……","examples":[{"en":"The interface is designed to respond to stylus interactions.","zh":"這個介面被設計成會回應觸控筆操作。"},{"en":"To be designed to respond to something means to be made so it reacts when that input happens.","zh":"be designed to respond to something 指被製造成在某種輸入發生時作出反應。"},{"en":"A classroom light may be designed to respond to movement and turn on automatically.","zh":"課室燈可能被設計成會回應動作並自動亮起。"},{"en":"If a screen responds to stylus input, players can control the game by touching it.","zh":"如果螢幕會回應觸控筆輸入，玩家就可以透過觸碰控制遊戲。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the intended reaction of a system.","zh":"這個短語解釋系統的預定反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"stylus interactions","meaning":"觸控筆操作","examples":[{"en":"The DS interface responds to stylus interactions.","zh":"DS 介面會回應觸控筆操作。"},{"en":"Stylus interactions are actions made by touching or moving a stylus on a screen.","zh":"stylus interactions 指用觸控筆在螢幕上觸碰或移動所做出的操作。"},{"en":"Drawing a line, tapping an icon, and dragging an object are stylus interactions.","zh":"畫線、點擊圖示和拖曽物件都是觸控筆操作。"},{"en":"These interactions can be precise, but young children may not control them well.","zh":"這些操作可以很精準，但年幼兒童可能控制不好。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ways of using a stylus with a touch screen.","zh":"這個短語描述用觸控筆與觸控螢幕互動的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"effectively be used with","meaning":"可有效地用……操作","examples":[{"en":"The interface can effectively be used with the tip of the finger.","zh":"這個介面可有效地用指尖操作。"},{"en":"To effectively be used with something means to work well when operated by that thing.","zh":"effectively be used with something 指用某物操作時能良好運作。"},{"en":"A tablet can effectively be used with a finger even without a keyboard.","zh":"即使沒有鍵盤，平板電腦也可有效地用手指操作。"},{"en":"If a child can use a finger instead of a tool, control may become easier.","zh":"如果孩子可以用手指而不是工具操作，控制可能變得更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical usability with a particular method.","zh":"這個短語描述用特定方法操作時的實際可用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the tip of the finger","meaning":"指尖","examples":[{"en":"Children can use the tip of the finger on the DS screen.","zh":"兒童可以在 DS 螢幕上使用指尖。"},{"en":"The tip of the finger is the end part of a finger used for touching or pressing.","zh":"tip of the finger 指用來觸碰或按壓的手指末端部分。"},{"en":"A child may use the tip of the finger to tap a picture on a tablet.","zh":"孩子可能用指尖點擊平板電腦上的圖片。"},{"en":"Finger-tip control can feel more natural than holding a separate tool.","zh":"指尖控制可能比拿着另一工具更自然。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the small end area of the finger.","zh":"這個短語指手指末端的小範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"particularly noteworthy","meaning":"特別值得注意","examples":[{"en":"This feature is particularly noteworthy in the context of preschoolers.","zh":"在學前兒童的情況下，這項功能特別值得注意。"},{"en":"Particularly noteworthy means especially worth noticing or paying attention to.","zh":"particularly noteworthy 指尤其值得留意或關注。"},{"en":"A student’s sudden improvement is particularly noteworthy if she had struggled for months.","zh":"如果學生已困難數月，她突然進步就特別值得注意。"},{"en":"A feature becomes noteworthy when it solves an important problem.","zh":"當一項功能解決重要問題，它就值得注意。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights something that deserves special attention.","zh":"這個短語突出值得特別關注的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in the context of preschoolers","meaning":"在學前兒童的情況下","examples":[{"en":"Finger input is important in the context of preschoolers.","zh":"在學前兒童的情況下，手指輸入很重要。"},{"en":"In the context of preschoolers means when considering the needs and abilities of preschool children.","zh":"in the context of preschoolers 指在考慮學前兒童的需要和能力時。"},{"en":"In the context of preschoolers, a picture may be clearer than a written word.","zh":"在學前兒童的情況下，圖片可能比文字更清楚。"},{"en":"The same design feature may matter more when the users are very young.","zh":"當使用者非常年幼，同一設計功能可能更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows the discussion to preschool children’s situation.","zh":"這個短語把討論收窄到學前兒童的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"have trouble with","meaning":"在……方面有困難","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers have trouble with fine motor skills.","zh":"學前兒童在精細動作技能方面有困難。"},{"en":"To have trouble with something means to find it difficult.","zh":"have trouble with something 指覺得某事困難。"},{"en":"A student may have trouble with spelling long words.","zh":"學生可能在串寫長字方面有困難。"},{"en":"If children have trouble with a skill, tasks requiring that skill should be simplified.","zh":"如果兒童在某技能上有困難，需要該技能的任務應被簡化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes difficulty, not unwillingness.","zh":"這個短語描述困難，而不是不願意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"fine motor skills","meaning":"精細動作技能","examples":[{"en":"Fine motor skills are still developing in preschool children.","zh":"學前兒童的精細動作技能仍在發展。"},{"en":"Fine motor skills are small, precise movements of the hands and fingers.","zh":"fine motor skills 指手和手指的小型精確動作。"},{"en":"Holding a pencil, buttoning a shirt, and cutting paper require fine motor skills.","zh":"握鉛筆、扣恤衫鈕和剪紙都需要精細動作技能。"},{"en":"If fine motor skills are weak, a child may struggle with small buttons or styluses.","zh":"如果精細動作技能較弱，孩子可能難以使用細小按鈕或觸控筆。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to detailed hand control.","zh":"這個短語指細緻手部控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"hand-eye coordination","meaning":"手眼協調","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers’ hand-eye coordination is still in development.","zh":"學前兒童的手眼協調仍在發展中。"},{"en":"Hand-eye coordination is the ability to use the hands accurately while watching with the eyes.","zh":"hand-eye coordination 指一邊用眼看、一邊準確使用雙手的能力。"},{"en":"Catching a ball and drawing inside a line both require hand-eye coordination.","zh":"接球和在線內畫圖都需要手眼協調。"},{"en":"Weak hand-eye coordination can make touch-screen games harder for young children.","zh":"手眼協調較弱可以令觸控遊戲對年幼兒童更難。"},{"en":"The phrase connects seeing with hand movement.","zh":"這個短語把視覺和手部動作連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"still in development","meaning":"仍在發展中","examples":[{"en":"Hand-eye coordination is still in development in preschool children.","zh":"學前兒童的手眼協調仍在發展中。"},{"en":"Still in development means not yet fully formed or mature.","zh":"still in development 指尚未完全形成或成熟。"},{"en":"A beginner’s essay structure is still in development if ideas are clear but organisation is weak.","zh":"如果初學者作文想法清楚但組織較弱，其作文結構仍在發展中。"},{"en":"If a skill is still developing, adults should expect mistakes and provide support.","zh":"如果技能仍在發展，成人應預期錯誤並提供支援。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an ongoing growth process.","zh":"這個短語描述持續成長過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"less exact with","meaning":"在……方面較不準確","examples":[{"en":"Young children are less exact with their stylus movements.","zh":"年幼兒童在觸控筆動作方面較不準確。"},{"en":"Less exact with something means less precise when using or controlling it.","zh":"less exact with something 指使用或控制某物時較不精準。"},{"en":"A beginner may be less exact with a paintbrush than an experienced artist.","zh":"初學者使用畫筆時可能比有經驗藝術家較不準確。"},{"en":"If movements are less exact, games need larger touch areas and forgiving controls.","zh":"如果動作較不準確，遊戲需要較大觸控範圍和寬容控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lower precision.","zh":"這個短語描述精確度較低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"stylus movements","meaning":"觸控筆動作","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers may be less exact with their stylus movements.","zh":"學前兒童的觸控筆動作可能較不準確。"},{"en":"Stylus movements are the motions made when using a stylus on a touch screen.","zh":"stylus movements 指在觸控螢幕上使用觸控筆時做出的動作。"},{"en":"Drawing a circle or dragging an icon involves stylus movements.","zh":"畫圓或拖曳圖示都涉及觸控筆動作。"},{"en":"Young children may make wider or shakier movements than older users.","zh":"年幼兒童的動作可能比年長用戶更大幅或更不穩。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how the stylus is physically moved.","zh":"這個短語重點是觸控筆如何被實際移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"mimic the stylus","meaning":"模仿觸控筆","examples":[{"en":"Children’s small fingers can mimic the stylus effectively.","zh":"兒童的小手指可以有效模仿觸控筆。"},{"en":"To mimic the stylus means to perform a similar function to a stylus on a touch screen.","zh":"mimic the stylus 指在觸控螢幕上執行類似觸控筆的功能。"},{"en":"A finger can mimic a mouse click when a student taps a tablet icon.","zh":"當學生點擊平板電腦圖示時，手指可以模仿滑鼠點擊。"},{"en":"If fingers can mimic the tool, children may not need to hold a separate stylus.","zh":"如果手指能模仿工具，兒童可能不需要握住另一支觸控筆。"},{"en":"The phrase means act like the stylus, not copy its shape perfectly.","zh":"這個短語指像觸控筆一樣發揮作用，而不是完美複製其形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"by using their fingers","meaning":"透過使用手指","examples":[{"en":"By using their fingers, children can often be more accurate.","zh":"透過使用手指，兒童往往可以更準確。"},{"en":"By using their fingers means through the method of touching with fingers instead of another tool.","zh":"by using their fingers 指透過用手指觸碰，而不是使用另一工具。"},{"en":"A child may choose pictures more easily by using her fingers on a tablet.","zh":"孩子可能透過在平板電腦上使用手指，更容易選擇圖片。"},{"en":"Fingers can feel more natural than a stylus for very young users.","zh":"對非常年幼用戶來說，手指可能比觸控筆更自然。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the method that improves control.","zh":"這個短語引入改善控制的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"game interactions","meaning":"遊戲互動","examples":[{"en":"Children can become more accurate in their game interactions.","zh":"兒童在遊戲互動中可以變得更準確。"},{"en":"Game interactions are the actions players use to control, respond to, or affect a game.","zh":"game interactions 指玩家用來控制、回應或影響遊戲的行動。"},{"en":"Tapping a picture, dragging a character, and choosing an answer are game interactions.","zh":"點擊圖片、拖動角色和選擇答案都是遊戲互動。"},{"en":"Clear interactions help children understand the link between their actions and screen results.","zh":"清楚互動幫助兒童理解自己動作與屏幕結果之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the player’s active contact with the game.","zh":"這個短語重點是玩家與遊戲的主動接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agree with the claims of","meaning":"與……的主張一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether the statements agree with the claims of the writer.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與作者的主張一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the claims of the writer means to match what the writer says or argues.","zh":"agree with the claims of the writer 指與作者所說或所主張的內容相符。"},{"en":"If an article says games need voice instructions, a statement saying this agrees with the writer.","zh":"如果文章說遊戲需要語音指示，陳述這一點就與作者一致。"},{"en":"Students must check the writer’s exact meaning, not their own opinion.","zh":"學生必須檢查作者的確切意思，而不是自己的意見。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in YES, NO, NOT GIVEN reading questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 YES、NO、NOT GIVEN 閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the views of the writer","meaning":"作者的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The task asks whether each statement agrees with the views of the writer.","zh":"任務要求判斷每項陳述是否與作者的觀點一致。"},{"en":"The views of the writer are the writer’s opinions, claims, or position in the passage.","zh":"views of the writer 指作者在文章中的意見、主張或立場。"},{"en":"A reader must separate the views of the writer from examples quoted from other people.","zh":"讀者必須把作者觀點與引用他人的例子分開。"},{"en":"Misreading the writer’s view can lead to wrong YES or NO answers.","zh":"誤讀作者觀點可能導致 YES 或 NO 答案錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what the author thinks or argues.","zh":"這個短語指作者所想或所論證的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the views of the writer.","zh":"陳述可能與作者的觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of the writer means to say the opposite of what the writer believes or argues.","zh":"contradict the views of the writer 指說出與作者相信或主張相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the writer supports voice instructions, a statement rejecting them may contradict the writer.","zh":"如果作者支持語音指示，拒絕語音指示的陳述可能與作者矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be based on clear evidence in the passage.","zh":"判斷矛盾必須基於文章中的清楚證據。"},{"en":"The phrase means direct conflict with the author’s position.","zh":"這個短語指與作者立場直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"If there is not enough information, it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"如果資料不足，就無法判斷作者怎樣想。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough evidence to decide.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠證據作決定。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions parents’ opinions, it is impossible to say whether parents support the game.","zh":"如果文章從未提及家長意見，就無法判斷家長是否支持該遊戲。"},{"en":"Students should choose NOT GIVEN when the text does not provide proof.","zh":"當文本沒有提供證據，學生應選 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"The phrase signals uncertainty caused by missing information.","zh":"這個短語表示因資料缺失而不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"video game use","meaning":"電子遊戲使用","examples":[{"en":"Video game use among preschool children is expected to increase.","zh":"學前兒童當中的電子遊戲使用預期會增加。"},{"en":"Video game use means the act or habit of playing or using video games.","zh":"video game use 指玩或使用電子遊戲的行為或習慣。"},{"en":"Parents may monitor video game use during school nights.","zh":"家長可能在上學日晚間監察電子遊戲使用。"},{"en":"If video game use increases among young children, designers and parents need clearer guidance.","zh":"如果年幼兒童的電子遊戲使用增加，設計者和家長需要更清楚指引。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to usage, not the games themselves.","zh":"這個短語指使用情況，而不是遊戲本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"amongst preschool children","meaning":"在學前兒童當中","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to video game use amongst preschool children.","zh":"該陳述提到學前兒童當中的電子遊戲使用。"},{"en":"Amongst preschool children means within the group of children before primary school age.","zh":"amongst preschool children 指在小學前兒童這個群體之中。"},{"en":"Sharing toys is an important social skill amongst preschool children.","zh":"分享玩具是學前兒童當中的重要社交技能。"},{"en":"Studying behaviour among this group helps adults design age-appropriate activities.","zh":"研究這個群體的行為幫助成人設計適齡活動。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the group being discussed.","zh":"這個短語指出正在討論的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be higher than","meaning":"高於……","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether video game use is higher in the US than elsewhere.","zh":"該選項詢問美國的電子遊戲使用是否高於其他地方。"},{"en":"To be higher than means to be greater in number, level, or amount than something else.","zh":"be higher than 指數字、水平或數量比另一事物更高。"},{"en":"Attendance may be higher than last year if more students join the course.","zh":"如果更多學生參加課程，出席率可能高於去年。"},{"en":"Comparison helps readers decide whether one figure exceeds another.","zh":"比較幫助讀者判斷一個數字是否超過另一個。"},{"en":"The phrase describes relative quantity or level.","zh":"這個短語描述相對數量或水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the proportion of","meaning":"……的比例","examples":[{"en":"The proportion of preschool children using video games is likely to rise.","zh":"使用電子遊戲的學前兒童比例可能上升。"},{"en":"The proportion of a group means the part or percentage of that group.","zh":"proportion of a group 指該群體中的部分或百分比。"},{"en":"The proportion of students who walk to school may increase if buses become expensive.","zh":"如果巴士變貴，步行上學的學生比例可能增加。"},{"en":"A rising proportion shows that a behaviour is becoming more common within the group.","zh":"比例上升顯示某行為在群體中變得更常見。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on share, not just total number.","zh":"這個短語重點是所佔比例，而不只是總數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be likely to rise","meaning":"可能上升","examples":[{"en":"The proportion of preschool children using video games is likely to rise.","zh":"使用電子遊戲的學前兒童比例可能上升。"},{"en":"To be likely to rise means to probably increase in the future.","zh":"be likely to rise 指未來很可能增加。"},{"en":"Bus fares are likely to rise if fuel prices continue increasing.","zh":"如果燃油價格繼續上升，巴士票價可能上升。"},{"en":"When access and interest grow, usage figures often rise too.","zh":"當接觸機會和興趣增加，使用數字通常也會上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a probable upward trend.","zh":"這個短語描述可能向上的趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"own gaming equipment","meaning":"擁有遊戲設備","examples":[{"en":"Many families own gaming equipment at home.","zh":"許多家庭在家中擁有遊戲設備。"},{"en":"To own gaming equipment means to have game devices in one’s possession.","zh":"own gaming equipment 指擁有遊戲裝置。"},{"en":"A family may own gaming equipment such as a console, controllers, and handheld devices.","zh":"家庭可能擁有遊戲機、控制器和手提裝置等遊戲設備。"},{"en":"If a family owns such equipment, young children may have easier access to games.","zh":"如果家庭擁有這類設備，年幼兒童可能更容易接觸遊戲。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to possession of gaming hardware.","zh":"這個短語指擁有遊戲硬件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"generally allow someone to","meaning":"一般容許某人……","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether parents generally allow children to use gaming equipment.","zh":"該陳述問家長是否一般容許兒童使用遊戲設備。"},{"en":"To generally allow someone to do something means to usually permit them to do it.","zh":"generally allow someone to do something 指通常允許某人做某事。"},{"en":"Some parents generally allow children to watch cartoons after homework is finished.","zh":"有些家長一般容許孩子完成功課後看卡通。"},{"en":"If parents allow access often, children’s usage may increase.","zh":"如果家長經常允許接觸，兒童使用量可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes usual permission, not a one-time exception.","zh":"這個短語描述通常許可，而不是一次例外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"type of research","meaning":"研究類型","examples":[{"en":"The type of research usually done may not improve game design.","zh":"通常進行的研究類型可能無法改善遊戲設計。"},{"en":"Type of research means a particular kind or method of study.","zh":"type of research 指某種特定研究種類或方法。"},{"en":"A school may choose a different type of research, such as interviews rather than surveys.","zh":"學校可能選擇不同研究類型，例如訪問而不是問卷。"},{"en":"If the research type is wrong, it may answer the wrong question.","zh":"如果研究類型錯誤，它可能回答錯問題。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the approach used to gather knowledge.","zh":"這個短語指出獲取知識的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be aimed at","meaning":"旨在","examples":[{"en":"Some research is aimed at developing a marketing strategy.","zh":"有些研究旨在制定市場推廣策略。"},{"en":"To be aimed at something means to have that purpose or target.","zh":"be aimed at something 指以某事為目的或目標。"},{"en":"A school workshop may be aimed at helping parents support reading at home.","zh":"學校工作坊可能旨在幫助家長在家支持閱讀。"},{"en":"If research is aimed at marketing, it may not improve the product design itself.","zh":"如果研究旨在市場推廣，它未必改善產品設計本身。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the goal of an action.","zh":"這個短語解釋行動目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"improve game design","meaning":"改善遊戲設計","examples":[{"en":"Formative research can help improve game design.","zh":"形成性研究可以幫助改善遊戲設計。"},{"en":"To improve game design means to make a game easier, clearer, safer, or more enjoyable to use.","zh":"improve game design 指令遊戲更容易、更清晰、更安全或更有趣。"},{"en":"Testing with children can improve game design by showing where they get confused.","zh":"與兒童測試可以透過顯示他們在哪裏困惑來改善遊戲設計。"},{"en":"Better design can reduce frustration and keep young users engaged.","zh":"更好設計可以減少挫敗感，並讓年幼用戶保持投入。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on improving how the game works for players.","zh":"這個短語重點是改善遊戲對玩家的運作方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"younger and older consumers","meaning":"較年幼和較年長的消費者","examples":[{"en":"Younger and older consumers may both require targeted research.","zh":"較年幼和較年長的消費者可能都需要有目標的研究。"},{"en":"Younger and older consumers are age groups at different ends of the user range.","zh":"younger and older consumers 指使用者年齡範圍中不同兩端的群體。"},{"en":"A bank app may need testing with younger and older consumers because they use technology differently.","zh":"銀行應用程式可能需要與較年幼和較年長消費者測試，因為他們使用科技的方式不同。"},{"en":"Different age groups can have different abilities, habits, and concerns.","zh":"不同年齡組別可能有不同能力、習慣和關注。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights age-based user differences.","zh":"這個短語突出基於年齡的用戶差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"require specifically targeted research","meaning":"需要有特定目標的研究","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers and senior citizens require specifically targeted research.","zh":"學前兒童和長者需要有特定目標的研究。"},{"en":"To require specifically targeted research means to need research designed for a particular group’s needs.","zh":"require specifically targeted research 指需要為某特定群體需要而設計的研究。"},{"en":"A hospital may require targeted research before designing signs for elderly patients.","zh":"醫院在為長者病人設計指示牌前，可能需要有針對性的研究。"},{"en":"Without targeted research, designers may use assumptions that do not fit real users.","zh":"沒有針對性研究，設計者可能使用不符合真實用戶的假設。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that general research is not enough.","zh":"這個短語強調一般研究不足夠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the summary using the list of words and phrases.","zh":"考生使用字詞和短語列表完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill missing words in a shortened version of the passage.","zh":"complete the summary 指填補文章簡短版本中的缺漏字詞。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole summary before choosing words from the list.","zh":"學生應先讀完整個摘要，再從列表中選字。"},{"en":"Summary completion tests meaning, grammar, and exact word choice.","zh":"摘要填空測試意思、文法和準確用字。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"list of words and phrases","meaning":"字詞和短語列表","examples":[{"en":"The task provides a list of words and phrases.","zh":"任務提供一個字詞和短語列表。"},{"en":"A list of words and phrases is a set of possible answer choices.","zh":"list of words and phrases 指一組可能答案選項。"},{"en":"In a vocabulary exercise, students may choose answers from a list of words and phrases.","zh":"在詞彙練習中，學生可能從字詞和短語列表中選答案。"},{"en":"A list limits the answer options and helps students focus on meaning and grammar.","zh":"列表限制答案選項，幫助學生集中於意思和文法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the given pool of possible answers.","zh":"這個短語指所提供的可能答案庫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"problems for preschool users","meaning":"學前兒童用戶面對的問題","examples":[{"en":"The summary describes problems for preschool users of video games.","zh":"摘要描述電子遊戲的學前兒童用戶面對的問題。"},{"en":"Problems for preschool users are difficulties young children face when using a product.","zh":"problems for preschool users 指年幼兒童使用產品時面對的困難。"},{"en":"A tablet app may create problems for preschool users if the icons are too small.","zh":"如果圖示太小，平板應用程式可能為學前兒童用戶造成問題。"},{"en":"Understanding these problems helps designers make age-appropriate games.","zh":"理解這些問題幫助設計者製作適齡遊戲。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on obstacles faced by young users.","zh":"這個短語重點是年幼用戶面對的障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"preschool users of video games","meaning":"電子遊戲的學前兒童用戶","examples":[{"en":"Preschool users of video games may struggle with controls and instructions.","zh":"電子遊戲的學前兒童用戶可能在控制和指示方面遇到困難。"},{"en":"Preschool users of video games are young children before primary school age who play or use video games.","zh":"preschool users of video games 指小學前玩或使用電子遊戲的年幼兒童。"},{"en":"Preschool users may need pictures, sounds, and large buttons instead of written menus.","zh":"學前兒童用戶可能需要圖像、聲音和大按鈕，而不是書面選單。"},{"en":"If designers understand preschool users, games can become more accessible.","zh":"如果設計者理解學前兒童用戶，遊戲可以變得更易使用。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies young children as game users.","zh":"這個短語指出年幼兒童作為遊戲使用者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"electronic games","meaning":"電子遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Preschool children find many electronic games difficult.","zh":"學前兒童覺得許多電子遊戲困難。"},{"en":"Electronic games are games played on digital devices such as consoles, tablets, or handheld systems.","zh":"electronic games 指在遊戲機、平板或手提系統等數碼裝置上玩的遊戲。"},{"en":"A child may play electronic games on a family tablet after school.","zh":"孩子可能放學後在家庭平板電腦上玩電子遊戲。"},{"en":"If electronic games rely on reading, preschoolers may not be able to play independently.","zh":"如果電子遊戲依賴閱讀，學前兒童可能無法獨立玩。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to digital games, not board games or outdoor games.","zh":"這個短語指數碼遊戲，而不是桌上遊戲或戶外遊戲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"sufficiently developed","meaning":"發展得足夠成熟","examples":[{"en":"Children’s motor and cognitive skills are not sufficiently developed.","zh":"兒童的動作和認知技能尚未發展得足夠成熟。"},{"en":"Sufficiently developed means grown or improved enough for a particular task.","zh":"sufficiently developed 指已成長或改善到足以應付某任務。"},{"en":"A student’s writing may not be sufficiently developed if the ideas have no examples.","zh":"如果作文想法沒有例子，學生寫作可能未發展得足夠成熟。"},{"en":"If children’s skills are not sufficiently developed, complex controls may be too difficult.","zh":"如果兒童技能未發展成熟，複雜控制可能太困難。"},{"en":"The phrase means developed enough, not fully perfect.","zh":"這個短語意思是發展到足夠程度，不是完全完美。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"types of control","meaning":"控制方式","examples":[{"en":"Certain types of control are difficult for young children to manipulate.","zh":"某些控制方式對年幼兒童來說難以操控。"},{"en":"Types of control are different ways users operate a device or game.","zh":"types of control 指使用者操作裝置或遊戲的不同方式。"},{"en":"Buttons, joysticks, touch screens, and voice commands are types of control.","zh":"按鈕、搖桿、觸控螢幕和語音指令都是控制方式。"},{"en":"Some controls require more hand skill or understanding than others.","zh":"有些控制方式比其他方式更需要手部技能或理解。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to control methods in a device or interface.","zh":"這個短語指裝置或介面中的控制方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be hard for someone to manipulate","meaning":"對某人來說難以操控","examples":[{"en":"Small buttons can be hard for preschool children to manipulate.","zh":"細小按鈕對學前兒童來說可能難以操控。"},{"en":"To be hard for someone to manipulate means to be difficult for that person to control accurately by hand.","zh":"be hard for someone to manipulate 指某人難以用手準確控制某物。"},{"en":"Tiny zips may be hard for young children to manipulate when dressing themselves.","zh":"年幼兒童自己穿衣時，細小拉鏈可能難以操控。"},{"en":"If controls are hard to manipulate, children may press the wrong button repeatedly.","zh":"如果控制器難以操控，兒童可能反覆按錯按鈕。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical control difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述身體操作上的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"more effective than","meaning":"比……更有效","examples":[{"en":"Fingers can sometimes be more effective than styluses.","zh":"手指有時比觸控筆更有效。"},{"en":"More effective than means working better than another option.","zh":"more effective than 指比另一選項運作得更好。"},{"en":"Short daily practice can be more effective than one long study session before the test.","zh":"每天短時間練習可能比考試前一次長時間溫習更有效。"},{"en":"If fingers are easier to control, they may produce more accurate game interactions than a stylus.","zh":"如果手指更容易控制，它們可能比觸控筆產生更準確的遊戲互動。"},{"en":"The phrase compares usefulness or success.","zh":"這個短語比較有用程度或成功程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"have the ability to","meaning":"有能力去……","examples":[{"en":"Preschool children have the ability to relate pictures to objects.","zh":"學前兒童有能力把圖畫與物件聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To have the ability to do something means to be able to do it.","zh":"have the ability to do something 指有能力做某事。"},{"en":"A young child may have the ability to match animal sounds with pictures.","zh":"年幼孩子可能有能力把動物聲音與圖片配對。"},{"en":"If children have this ability, games can use images instead of written words.","zh":"如果兒童有這種能力，遊戲就可以使用圖像而不是文字。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on what someone can do.","zh":"這個短語重點是某人能做到甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"relate pictures to","meaning":"把圖畫與……聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"Children can relate pictures to real-world objects.","zh":"兒童可以把圖畫與現實世界中的物件聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To relate pictures to something means to connect an image with what it represents.","zh":"relate pictures to something 指把圖像與它所代表的事物連起來。"},{"en":"A child may relate a picture of a banana to the fruit on the kitchen table.","zh":"孩子可能把香蕉圖片與廚房桌上的水果聯繫起來。"},{"en":"This skill helps children use picture icons in games and apps.","zh":"這項技能幫助兒童使用遊戲和應用程式中的圖片圖示。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a mental connection between image and object.","zh":"這個短語描述在圖像和物件之間建立心理連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"real-world objects","meaning":"現實世界中的物件","examples":[{"en":"Pictures can represent real-world objects.","zh":"圖畫可以代表現實世界中的物件。"},{"en":"Real-world objects are actual things people can see, touch, or use outside a screen.","zh":"real-world objects 指人們在屏幕以外可以看見、觸摸或使用的真實事物。"},{"en":"A drawing of a cup can represent the real-world object a child drinks from.","zh":"杯子的畫可以代表孩子用來喝水的現實物件。"},{"en":"Connecting images to real objects helps children understand icons and instructions.","zh":"把圖像與真實物件連起來，幫助兒童理解圖示和指示。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts actual objects with pictures or digital symbols.","zh":"這個短語把真實物件與圖畫或數碼符號作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"understand the connection between","meaning":"理解……之間的聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Children may not understand the connection between actions and screen movements.","zh":"兒童可能不理解動作和屏幕移動之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"To understand the connection between two things means to know how one relates to or affects the other.","zh":"understand the connection between two things 指知道一件事如何與另一件事相關或影響另一件事。"},{"en":"A child learns the connection between turning a tap and water coming out.","zh":"孩子學會扭開水龍頭與水流出之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"If children do not understand the connection, they may not know why the game responds.","zh":"如果兒童不理解這種聯繫，他們可能不知道遊戲為何有反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recognising a relationship or cause-and-effect link.","zh":"這個短語描述辨認關係或因果連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"movements on the screen","meaning":"屏幕上的動作","examples":[{"en":"Children may not connect their actions with movements on the screen.","zh":"兒童可能無法把自己的動作與屏幕上的動作連起來。"},{"en":"Movements on the screen are visible changes or actions shown in a digital display.","zh":"movements on the screen 指數碼顯示器上可見的變化或行動。"},{"en":"A character jumping or a picture sliding are movements on the screen.","zh":"角色跳躍或圖片滑動都是屏幕上的動作。"},{"en":"If screen movements do not clearly match the child’s action, the game becomes confusing.","zh":"如果屏幕動作不能清楚配合孩子的動作，遊戲就會變得令人困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what visibly moves in the game or interface.","zh":"這個短語指遊戲或介面中可見的移動內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"written menus","meaning":"書面選單","examples":[{"en":"Very few preschool children can understand written menus.","zh":"很少學前兒童能理解書面選單。"},{"en":"Written menus are lists of choices shown in words rather than pictures or speech.","zh":"written menus 指以文字而不是圖像或語音顯示的選項列表。"},{"en":"A restaurant app with written menus may be difficult for children who cannot read.","zh":"有書面選單的餐廳應用程式，對不能閱讀的孩子可能很困難。"},{"en":"If children cannot understand written menus, designers should use icons and voice instructions.","zh":"如果兒童不能理解書面選單，設計者應使用圖示和語音指示。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to text-based choice lists.","zh":"這個短語指以文字為基礎的選項列表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"考生為每條問題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option labelled with the right letter.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇標有正確字母的答案選項。"},{"en":"If option B matches the passage, students should write B clearly on the answer sheet.","zh":"如果選項 B 符合文章，學生應在答題紙上清楚寫 B。"},{"en":"Choosing the wrong letter loses the mark even if the student understands the idea.","zh":"即使學生理解意思，選錯字母也會失分。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard instruction in multiple-choice questions.","zh":"這個短語是選擇題中的標準指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"come to a conclusion","meaning":"得出結論","examples":[{"en":"The game producers came to a conclusion about the preschool market.","zh":"遊戲製作人對學前兒童市場得出結論。"},{"en":"To come to a conclusion means to decide something after considering evidence or reasons.","zh":"come to a conclusion 指在考慮證據或理由後作出判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher may come to a conclusion about a student’s needs after reading several assignments.","zh":"老師閱讀幾份作業後，可能對學生需要得出結論。"},{"en":"Good conclusions are stronger when they are based on research rather than guesses.","zh":"當結論建基於研究而不是猜測，它會更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reaching a judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述形成判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"games producers","meaning":"遊戲製作人","examples":[{"en":"Games producers at Nickelodeon studied preschool game design.","zh":"Nickelodeon 的遊戲製作人研究學前兒童遊戲設計。"},{"en":"Games producers are people who oversee or guide the creation of video games.","zh":"games producers 指監督或指導電子遊戲創作的人。"},{"en":"A games producer may coordinate artists, programmers, writers, and testers.","zh":"遊戲製作人可能協調美術人員、程式員、編劇和測試員。"},{"en":"Producers make decisions that affect schedule, design, and target audience.","zh":"製作人作出的決定會影響時間表、設計和目標受眾。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the people responsible for producing games.","zh":"這個短語指負責製作遊戲的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"unlikely to be sufficiently profitable","meaning":"不大可能有足夠利潤","examples":[{"en":"The option says the preschool market was unlikely to be sufficiently profitable.","zh":"該選項說學前兒童市場不大可能有足夠利潤。"},{"en":"Unlikely to be sufficiently profitable means probably not able to earn enough money to justify the cost.","zh":"unlikely to be sufficiently profitable 指很可能不能賺取足夠金錢來支持成本。"},{"en":"A tiny café in a hidden street may be unlikely to be sufficiently profitable if few people pass by.","zh":"如果很少人經過，隱蔽街道上的小咖啡店可能不大可能有足夠利潤。"},{"en":"If a market is not profitable enough, companies may avoid developing products for it.","zh":"如果市場利潤不足，公司可能避免為它開發產品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a doubtful business return.","zh":"這個短語描述商業回報可疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"hardware products","meaning":"硬件產品","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to hardware products for preschoolers.","zh":"該選項提到為學前兒童而設的硬件產品。"},{"en":"Hardware products are physical devices or machines, not the software inside them.","zh":"hardware products 指實體裝置或機器，而不是其中的軟件。"},{"en":"A game console, controller, or tablet is a hardware product.","zh":"遊戲機、控制器或平板電腦都是硬件產品。"},{"en":"If hardware is designed for children, size, weight, and buttons must be considered.","zh":"如果硬件為兒童設計，就必須考慮大小、重量和按鈕。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to physical technology products.","zh":"這個短語指實體科技產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be suitable for","meaning":"適合……","examples":[{"en":"The Nintendo DS was probably suitable for preschoolers.","zh":"Nintendo DS 可能適合學前兒童。"},{"en":"To be suitable for someone means to fit that person’s needs, age, or ability.","zh":"be suitable for someone 指符合某人的需要、年齡或能力。"},{"en":"A short picture book is suitable for children who cannot read long stories yet.","zh":"短篇圖畫書適合尚未能讀長故事的兒童。"},{"en":"If a device is small, portable, and touch-based, it may be suitable for young users.","zh":"如果裝置小巧、便攜並以觸控操作，它可能適合年幼用戶。"},{"en":"The phrase judges whether something matches a user or purpose.","zh":"這個短語判斷某物是否配合使用者或目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"rival companies","meaning":"競爭公司","examples":[{"en":"The producers looked at games made by rival companies.","zh":"製作人研究競爭公司製作的遊戲。"},{"en":"Rival companies are businesses that compete in the same market.","zh":"rival companies 指在同一市場競爭的企業。"},{"en":"Two tutoring centres in the same district may be rival companies.","zh":"同一區內兩間補習中心可能是競爭公司。"},{"en":"Studying rivals helps a company understand what already exists and what can be improved.","zh":"研究競爭對手幫助公司理解市面已有甚麼和可改善甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to business competitors.","zh":"這個短語指商業競爭者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"completely inappropriate for","meaning":"對……完全不合適","examples":[{"en":"Some games were not completely inappropriate for preschoolers.","zh":"有些遊戲並非對學前兒童完全不合適。"},{"en":"Completely inappropriate for means totally unsuitable for a person, group, or situation.","zh":"completely inappropriate for 指對某人、群體或情況完全不適合。"},{"en":"A horror film is completely inappropriate for a kindergarten class.","zh":"恐怖電影對幼稚園班級完全不合適。"},{"en":"If something is only partly unsuitable, designers may still learn from its useful features.","zh":"如果某物只是部分不合適，設計者仍可從其有用特徵中學習。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses strong unsuitability.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈不適合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"put ideas into practice","meaning":"將想法付諸實行","examples":[{"en":"The producers considered putting their ideas into practice.","zh":"製作人考慮將想法付諸實行。"},{"en":"To put ideas into practice means to turn plans or theories into real actions or products.","zh":"put ideas into practice 指把計劃或理論變成真實行動或產品。"},{"en":"A student puts revision advice into practice when she actually uses it before exams.","zh":"學生在考試前真正使用溫習建議，就是將想法付諸實行。"},{"en":"Ideas only become useful when people test them in real situations.","zh":"想法只有在真實情況中被測試，才會變得有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving from thinking to doing.","zh":"這個短語描述由思考走向行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"carry out a study","meaning":"進行研究","examples":[{"en":"Nickelodeon carried out a study on preschool game play.","zh":"Nickelodeon 對學前兒童遊戲玩法進行研究。"},{"en":"To carry out a study means to conduct research in an organised way.","zh":"carry out a study 指以有組織方式進行研究。"},{"en":"A school may carry out a study to find out why students skip breakfast.","zh":"學校可能進行研究，了解學生為何不吃早餐。"},{"en":"Carrying out a study gives decision-makers evidence instead of guesses.","zh":"進行研究可以給決策者證據，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase describes doing research.","zh":"這個短語描述做研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"以……為基礎","examples":[{"en":"The study was based on children living in the United States.","zh":"該研究以住在美國的兒童為基礎。"},{"en":"To be based on something means to use it as the foundation or source of information.","zh":"be based on something 指以某事作為基礎或資訊來源。"},{"en":"A school policy may be based on survey results from parents and teachers.","zh":"學校政策可能以家長和老師的調查結果為基礎。"},{"en":"If research is based on one country, its findings may not apply everywhere.","zh":"如果研究以一個國家為基礎，其發現未必適用於所有地方。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the foundation of a claim or study.","zh":"這個短語指出主張或研究的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"various parts of the world","meaning":"世界各地","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to children living in various parts of the world.","zh":"該選項提到住在世界各地的兒童。"},{"en":"Various parts of the world means many different regions or countries.","zh":"various parts of the world 指許多不同地區或國家。"},{"en":"Students may compare school lunches in various parts of the world.","zh":"學生可能比較世界各地的學校午餐。"},{"en":"Research from many regions can reveal whether a finding is local or general.","zh":"來自多個地區的研究可以揭示某發現是本地性還是普遍性。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses geographical variety.","zh":"這個短語強調地理多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"集中於","examples":[{"en":"The study did not focus only on game content.","zh":"該研究並非只集中於遊戲內容。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give most attention to it.","zh":"focus on something 指把大部分注意力放在某事上。"},{"en":"A student should focus on the question before writing an essay.","zh":"學生寫作文前應集中於題目。"},{"en":"If research focuses only on content, it may miss controls, instructions, and user ability.","zh":"如果研究只集中於內容，它可能忽略控制、指示和用戶能力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes directing attention.","zh":"這個短語描述集中注意力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"game content","meaning":"遊戲內容","examples":[{"en":"Game content must interest preschoolers.","zh":"遊戲內容必須引起學前兒童興趣。"},{"en":"Game content is what appears inside a game, such as characters, stories, images, tasks, and sounds.","zh":"game content 指遊戲內出現的角色、故事、圖像、任務和聲音等內容。"},{"en":"A game with animals, colours, and songs may have content that appeals to young children.","zh":"有動物、顏色和歌曲的遊戲，可能有吸引年幼兒童的內容。"},{"en":"Good content attracts players, but controls and instructions must also be suitable.","zh":"好內容會吸引玩家，但控制方式和指示也必須合適。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what the game contains, not the device itself.","zh":"這個短語指遊戲包含的東西，而不是裝置本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"interest preschoolers","meaning":"引起學前兒童興趣","examples":[{"en":"Some characters and content interest preschoolers.","zh":"一些角色和內容引起學前兒童興趣。"},{"en":"To interest preschoolers means to attract the attention and curiosity of young children before primary school.","zh":"interest preschoolers 指吸引小學前兒童的注意和好奇心。"},{"en":"Bright animals, simple songs, and familiar routines often interest preschoolers.","zh":"鮮明動物、簡單歌曲和熟悉日常情境常引起學前兒童興趣。"},{"en":"If content interests children, they are more likely to keep playing and learning.","zh":"如果內容吸引兒童，他們更可能繼續玩和學習。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on appeal to a young age group.","zh":"這個短語重點是對年幼年齡組別的吸引力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"investigate specific characteristics","meaning":"研究特定特徵","examples":[{"en":"The study investigated specific characteristics of the target market.","zh":"該研究調查目標市場的特定特徵。"},{"en":"To investigate specific characteristics means to study particular features in detail.","zh":"investigate specific characteristics 指詳細研究某些特定特徵。"},{"en":"A school may investigate specific characteristics of late students, such as travel time and sleep habits.","zh":"學校可能研究遲到學生的特定特徵，例如通勤時間和睡眠習慣。"},{"en":"Studying details helps people design better solutions for a particular group.","zh":"研究細節幫助人為特定群體設計更好解決方法。"},{"en":"The phrase means looking closely at selected features.","zh":"這個短語指仔細檢視選定特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"target market","meaning":"目標市場","examples":[{"en":"Preschoolers were the target market for the game.","zh":"學前兒童是該遊戲的目標市場。"},{"en":"A target market is the group of consumers a product is designed and sold for.","zh":"target market 指產品設計和銷售所針對的消費者群體。"},{"en":"A company selling baby food has parents of infants as its target market.","zh":"售賣嬰兒食品的公司，其目標市場是嬰兒父母。"},{"en":"Knowing the target market helps businesses choose design, price, and advertising.","zh":"了解目標市場幫助企業選擇設計、價格和廣告。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to intended buyers or users.","zh":"這個短語指預定買家或使用者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"lead to products","meaning":"促成產品","examples":[{"en":"The study led to products released in several regions.","zh":"該研究促成了在幾個地區推出的產品。"},{"en":"To lead to products means to result in actual products being created or launched.","zh":"lead to products 指導致實際產品被創造或推出。"},{"en":"A school survey may lead to new lunch products in the tuck shop.","zh":"學校調查可能促成小食部推出新午餐產品。"},{"en":"Research becomes practical when it leads to real things users can use.","zh":"當研究帶來使用者可真正使用的東西，它就變得實用。"},{"en":"The phrase connects study with product outcomes.","zh":"這個短語把研究與產品結果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"appeal mainly to","meaning":"主要吸引……","examples":[{"en":"The products did not appeal mainly to US consumers.","zh":"這些產品並非主要吸引美國消費者。"},{"en":"To appeal mainly to a group means to attract that group more than others.","zh":"appeal mainly to a group 指比起其他人更吸引某群體。"},{"en":"A cartoon with local jokes may appeal mainly to children from that city.","zh":"有本地笑話的卡通可能主要吸引該城市的兒童。"},{"en":"If a product appeals internationally, it is not limited to one country’s consumers.","zh":"如果產品有國際吸引力，它就不限於一個國家的消費者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the main audience attracted by something.","zh":"這個短語描述某物主要吸引的受眾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"highlight concerning","meaning":"強調關於……的問題","examples":[{"en":"The writers highlight a problem concerning game instructions.","zh":"作者強調一個關於遊戲指示的問題。"},{"en":"To highlight concerning something means to draw attention to an issue related to it.","zh":"highlight concerning something 指把注意力引到與某事相關的問題上。"},{"en":"A teacher may highlight a problem concerning students’ use of online sources.","zh":"老師可能強調關於學生使用網上資料來源的問題。"},{"en":"Highlighting a problem helps readers see why the issue matters.","zh":"強調問題幫助讀者看見該議題為何重要。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an important concern about a topic.","zh":"這個短語引入關於某主題的重要關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"games instructions","meaning":"遊戲指示","examples":[{"en":"Games instructions for young children should be clear and spoken.","zh":"給年幼兒童的遊戲指示應清楚並以語音呈現。"},{"en":"Games instructions are directions that tell players what to do in a game.","zh":"games instructions 指告訴玩家在遊戲中做甚麼的指引。"},{"en":"A game may give instructions such as “tap the red apple” or “drag the animal home”.","zh":"遊戲可能給出「點擊紅蘋果」或「把動物拖回家」等指示。"},{"en":"If instructions are unclear, children may not know how to continue.","zh":"如果指示不清楚，兒童可能不知道如何繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to guidance inside or before a game.","zh":"這個短語指遊戲內或遊戲前的指引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"young children","meaning":"年幼兒童","examples":[{"en":"Young children need instructions they can hear and see.","zh":"年幼兒童需要能聽見和看見的指示。"},{"en":"Young children are children in the early years of life, before they have mature reading and thinking skills.","zh":"young children 指人生早期的兒童，他們尚未有成熟閱讀和思考能力。"},{"en":"Young children often learn better through pictures, sounds, movement, and play.","zh":"年幼兒童通常透過圖像、聲音、動作和遊戲學得更好。"},{"en":"Because young children are still developing, adult products may not fit their needs.","zh":"因為年幼兒童仍在發展，成人產品可能不符合他們需要。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to children who need simple and supportive design.","zh":"這個短語指需要簡單和支援性設計的兒童。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"spoken instructions","meaning":"口頭指示","examples":[{"en":"Spoken instructions take up memory in DS games.","zh":"口頭指示在 DS 遊戲中會佔用記憶體。"},{"en":"Spoken instructions are directions given through speech or recorded voice.","zh":"spoken instructions 指透過說話或錄音給出的指示。"},{"en":"A children’s app may use spoken instructions to tell users what to tap next.","zh":"兒童應用程式可能使用口頭指示告訴使用者下一步點擊甚麼。"},{"en":"Spoken instructions help non-readers but require audio storage space.","zh":"口頭指示幫助不能閱讀的人，但需要音訊儲存空間。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts voice guidance with written instructions.","zh":"這個短語把語音指引與書面指示作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"take up a lot of","meaning":"佔用大量……","examples":[{"en":"Spoken instructions can take up a lot of available memory.","zh":"口頭指示可能佔用大量可用記憶體。"},{"en":"To take up a lot of something means to use a large amount of it.","zh":"take up a lot of something 指使用大量某資源。"},{"en":"Videos take up a lot of phone storage compared with text messages.","zh":"與文字訊息相比，影片會佔用大量手機儲存空間。"},{"en":"If one feature takes up too much memory, other useful features may have to be reduced.","zh":"如果一項功能佔用太多記憶體，其他有用功能可能要被減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes heavy use of space, time, or resources.","zh":"這個短語描述大量使用空間、時間或資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"available memory","meaning":"可用記憶體","examples":[{"en":"Sound files use a lot of the available memory.","zh":"聲音檔案使用大量可用記憶體。"},{"en":"Available memory is the storage space still free for data or files.","zh":"available memory 指仍可用於數據或檔案的儲存空間。"},{"en":"A phone with little available memory may not let students download a learning app.","zh":"可用記憶體很少的手機，可能不讓學生下載學習應用程式。"},{"en":"When available memory is small, designers must choose which files are most important.","zh":"當可用記憶體很小，設計者必須選擇哪些檔案最重要。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to usable remaining storage.","zh":"這個短語指仍可使用的儲存空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"written instructions","meaning":"書面指示","examples":[{"en":"Written instructions are not suitable for most preschoolers.","zh":"書面指示不適合大多數學前兒童。"},{"en":"Written instructions are directions shown in words instead of spoken or visual form.","zh":"written instructions 指以文字而不是語音或視覺形式呈現的指示。"},{"en":"A medicine bottle may have written instructions for adults to read before use.","zh":"藥瓶可能有給成人使用前閱讀的書面指示。"},{"en":"If users cannot read, written instructions will not guide them effectively.","zh":"如果使用者不能閱讀，書面指示就不能有效引導他們。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts text guidance with voice or picture guidance.","zh":"這個短語把文字指引與語音或圖像指引作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be expressed very simply","meaning":"以非常簡單的方式表達","examples":[{"en":"Instructions for young children should be expressed very simply.","zh":"給年幼兒童的指示應以非常簡單的方式表達。"},{"en":"To be expressed very simply means to be explained in easy words or clear forms.","zh":"be expressed very simply 指用容易詞語或清楚形式解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may express a grammar rule very simply before giving harder examples.","zh":"老師可能先以非常簡單的方式表達文法規則，再給較難例子。"},{"en":"Simple expression helps children understand quickly and avoid frustration.","zh":"簡單表達幫助兒童快速理解並避免挫敗。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on clear, easy communication.","zh":"這個短語重點是清楚易明的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"follow instructions consistently","meaning":"持續按照指示做","examples":[{"en":"Some children may not follow instructions consistently.","zh":"有些兒童可能不能持續按照指示做。"},{"en":"To follow instructions consistently means to do what the instructions say each time without frequent mistakes.","zh":"follow instructions consistently 指每次都按指示做，而不是經常犯錯。"},{"en":"A student who sometimes skips steps does not follow instructions consistently.","zh":"有時跳過步驟的學生，並沒有持續按照指示做。"},{"en":"If children do not follow instructions consistently, a game may need reminders and clearer cues.","zh":"如果兒童不能持續跟隨指示，遊戲可能需要提醒和更清楚提示。"},{"en":"The phrase describes steady and repeated obedience to directions.","zh":"這個短語描述穩定而反覆地遵從指引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"distract attention from","meaning":"令人分心而忽略……","examples":[{"en":"Video images may distract attention from instructions.","zh":"影片影像可能令人分心而忽略指示。"},{"en":"To distract attention from something means to pull focus away from it.","zh":"distract attention from something 指把注意力從某事拉走。"},{"en":"Loud music can distract attention from a teacher’s explanation.","zh":"大聲音樂可以令人分心而忽略老師講解。"},{"en":"If animations are too exciting, children may miss important instructions.","zh":"如果動畫太刺激，兒童可能錯過重要指示。"},{"en":"The phrase describes attention being drawn away from the main point.","zh":"這個短語描述注意力被從重點移走。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"best title for","meaning":"……的最佳標題","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for the best title for the passage.","zh":"題目要求選出文章的最佳標題。"},{"en":"The best title for a passage is the heading that most accurately captures its main idea.","zh":"best title for a passage 指最準確概括文章主旨的標題。"},{"en":"A story about saving a wetland should have a title that reflects conservation, not only one animal.","zh":"關於拯救濕地的故事應有反映保育的標題，而不只是某一種動物。"},{"en":"Choosing the best title requires understanding the whole passage, not just one sentence.","zh":"選最佳標題需要理解整篇文章，而不只是其中一句。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the most suitable overall heading.","zh":"這個短語指最合適的整體標題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"an overview of","meaning":"……的概覽","examples":[{"en":"An overview of video game software would introduce the whole market.","zh":"電子遊戲軟件概覽會介紹整個市場。"},{"en":"An overview of something is a general summary of its main parts.","zh":"overview of something 指對某事主要部分的一般總結。"},{"en":"A teacher may give an overview of the exam before explaining each question type.","zh":"老師可能先給考試概覽，再解釋每種題型。"},{"en":"An overview helps readers see the big picture before details.","zh":"概覽幫助讀者先看見大圖像，再看細節。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broad introduction, not a deep analysis of every point.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛介紹，而不是對每點深入分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"video games software","meaning":"電子遊戲軟件","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to video games software for preschoolers.","zh":"該選項提到為學前兒童而設的電子遊戲軟件。"},{"en":"Video games software is the digital program or content that runs a video game.","zh":"video games software 指運行電子遊戲的數碼程式或內容。"},{"en":"A console is hardware, while the game installed on it is software.","zh":"遊戲機是硬件，而安裝在其中的遊戲是軟件。"},{"en":"Software design affects instructions, graphics, sound, and game mechanics.","zh":"軟件設計會影響指示、圖像、聲音和遊戲機制。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the digital game program, not the physical device.","zh":"這個短語指數碼遊戲程式，而不是實體裝置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"preschool market","meaning":"學前兒童市場","examples":[{"en":"The preschool market requires carefully designed games.","zh":"學前兒童市場需要仔細設計的遊戲。"},{"en":"The preschool market is the group of young children and families who may buy or use products for preschoolers.","zh":"preschool market 指可能購買或使用學前兒童產品的年幼兒童和家庭群體。"},{"en":"Toy companies study the preschool market before making learning puzzles.","zh":"玩具公司製作學習拼圖前會研究學前兒童市場。"},{"en":"Because users are young, the preschool market requires safety, simplicity, and parental trust.","zh":"因為使用者年幼，學前兒童市場需要安全、簡單和家長信任。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a consumer group based on age.","zh":"這個短語指基於年齡的消費者群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"researching and designing","meaning":"研究和設計","examples":[{"en":"The passage is about researching and designing games for preschool children.","zh":"文章是關於為學前兒童研究和設計遊戲。"},{"en":"Researching and designing means studying users first and then creating a product based on that knowledge.","zh":"researching and designing 指先研究使用者，然後根據該知識創造產品。"},{"en":"A teacher may research students’ needs before designing a new writing course.","zh":"老師可能先研究學生需要，再設計新寫作課程。"},{"en":"Researching before designing helps avoid products that look good but fail in use.","zh":"設計前先研究，有助避免產品看似好但實際使用失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase combines investigation with creation.","zh":"這個短語結合調查和創造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"effects of video games on","meaning":"電子遊戲對……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The passage is not mainly about the effects of video games on behaviour.","zh":"文章主要不是關於電子遊戲對行為的影響。"},{"en":"Effects of video games on something are the ways games influence that thing.","zh":"effects of video games on something 指遊戲如何影響某事。"},{"en":"Researchers may study the effects of video games on children’s attention or sleep.","zh":"研究人員可能研究電子遊戲對兒童專注力或睡眠的影響。"},{"en":"Studying effects asks what games do to users, not how games should be designed.","zh":"研究影響是在問遊戲對使用者做了甚麼，而不是遊戲應如何設計。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on impact or influence.","zh":"這個短語重點是影響或作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"behaviour of young children","meaning":"年幼兒童的行為","examples":[{"en":"Some research studies the behaviour of young children.","zh":"一些研究探討年幼兒童的行為。"},{"en":"Behaviour of young children means how young children act, respond, play, speak, or interact.","zh":"behaviour of young children 指年幼兒童如何行動、回應、玩耍、說話或互動。"},{"en":"Teachers observe the behaviour of young children during group play to understand sharing skills.","zh":"老師在小組遊戲中觀察年幼兒童的行為，以理解分享技能。"},{"en":"Understanding behaviour helps adults design safer and more suitable activities.","zh":"理解行為幫助成人設計更安全和更合適的活動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what children do, not just what they think.","zh":"這個短語指兒童做甚麼，而不只是他們想甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"assess the impact of","meaning":"評估……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Researchers may assess the impact of video games on learning.","zh":"研究人員可能評估電子遊戲對學習的影響。"},{"en":"To assess the impact of something means to evaluate its effect or influence.","zh":"assess the impact of something 指評估某事的效果或影響。"},{"en":"A school may assess the impact of a new homework policy on students’ stress.","zh":"學校可能評估新功課政策對學生壓力的影響。"},{"en":"Impact assessment helps people decide whether a change is helpful or harmful.","zh":"影響評估幫助人判斷改變有益還是有害。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on judging consequences.","zh":"這個短語重點是判斷後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"educational achievement","meaning":"教育成就；學業成就","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not focus on educational achievement.","zh":"文章並不集中於教育成就。"},{"en":"Educational achievement is success in learning, often shown through skills, grades, or qualifications.","zh":"educational achievement 指學習上的成功，通常透過技能、成績或資格顯示。"},{"en":"A student’s educational achievement may improve when she receives regular feedback and enough sleep.","zh":"當學生收到定期回饋並有足夠睡眠，她的學業成就可能改善。"},{"en":"If a study focuses on design rather than achievement, it may not measure test scores.","zh":"如果研究集中於設計而不是成就，它可能不量度考試分數。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to learning success, not entertainment value.","zh":"這個短語指學習成功，而不是娛樂價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 118 - Video game research.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 119":[{"front":"learn lessons from the past","meaning":"從歷史中汲取教訓","examples":[{"en":"Modern societies may be able to learn lessons from the past.","zh":"現代社會或許能夠從歷史中汲取教訓。"},{"en":"To learn lessons from the past means to understand earlier mistakes or successes and use that knowledge today.","zh":"learn lessons from the past 指理解早期錯誤或成功，並把這些知識用於今天。"},{"en":"A school may learn lessons from a failed exam policy and give students more practice next year.","zh":"學校可能從失敗的考試政策中汲取教訓，下一年給學生更多練習。"},{"en":"If people ignore past disasters, they may repeat the same poor decisions.","zh":"如果人們忽視過去災難，就可能重複同樣糟糕的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when history can guide present choices.","zh":"當歷史可以指引當前選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"past societies","meaning":"過去的社會","examples":[{"en":"Many past societies collapsed or vanished.","zh":"許多過去的社會崩潰或消失。"},{"en":"Past societies are human communities or civilisations that existed in earlier periods of history.","zh":"past societies 指存在於早期歷史時期的人類社群或文明。"},{"en":"Students study past societies to understand how people farmed, traded, governed, and survived.","zh":"學生研究過去的社會，以了解人們如何耕作、貿易、管治和生存。"},{"en":"When past societies leave records or ruins, historians can reconstruct parts of their lives.","zh":"當過去的社會留下紀錄或遺址，歷史學家就能重建其部分生活。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing earlier civilisations with modern ones.","zh":"比較早期文明和現代社會時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"collapse or vanish","meaning":"崩潰或消失","examples":[{"en":"Many powerful societies eventually collapsed or vanished.","zh":"許多強大的社會最終崩潰或消失。"},{"en":"To collapse or vanish means to break down as a society or disappear from history as an organised community.","zh":"collapse or vanish 指一個社會瓦解，或作為有組織社群從歷史中消失。"},{"en":"A small business may collapse if it loses customers, but a civilisation collapses on a much larger scale.","zh":"小企業如果失去顧客可能倒閉，但文明崩潰的規模大得多。"},{"en":"War, famine, environmental damage, or weak leadership can make societies collapse or vanish.","zh":"戰爭、饑荒、環境破壞或領導不善都可以令社會崩潰或消失。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing complete historical decline.","zh":"描述全面歷史衰落時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"leave behind","meaning":"留下……","examples":[{"en":"Past societies left behind monumental ruins.","zh":"過去的社會留下宏偉遺址。"},{"en":"To leave behind something means to leave it after going away, dying, collapsing, or disappearing.","zh":"leave behind something 指離開、死亡、崩潰或消失後留下某物。"},{"en":"A graduating class may leave behind old photos and school traditions.","zh":"畢業班可能留下舊照片和學校傳統。"},{"en":"When a civilisation disappears, the objects it leaves behind become evidence for later researchers.","zh":"當文明消失，它留下的物件就成為後來研究人員的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something remains after people are gone.","zh":"當人在離去後仍有東西留下時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"monumental ruins","meaning":"宏偉遺址","examples":[{"en":"Many vanished civilisations left behind monumental ruins.","zh":"許多已消失的文明留下宏偉遺址。"},{"en":"Monumental ruins are large, impressive remains of old buildings or structures.","zh":"monumental ruins 指古老建築或結構留下的大型而令人印象深刻的遺跡。"},{"en":"Tourists may visit monumental ruins to see temples, walls, towers, or palaces from the past.","zh":"遊客可能參觀宏偉遺址，觀看過去的神廟、城牆、塔樓或宮殿。"},{"en":"Such ruins show that earlier societies had workers, resources, planning, and power.","zh":"這類遺址顯示早期社會曾擁有工人、資源、規劃和權力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing ancient sites that still look impressive today.","zh":"討論今天仍令人印象深刻的古代地點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a drastic decrease in","meaning":"……的大幅下降","examples":[{"en":"A collapse involves a drastic decrease in population or social complexity.","zh":"崩潰涉及人口或社會複雜程度的大幅下降。"},{"en":"A drastic decrease in something means a very large and serious fall in amount, number, or level.","zh":"drastic decrease in something 指數量、數字或水平非常大而嚴重地下降。"},{"en":"A restaurant may face a drastic decrease in customers after a serious food-safety scandal.","zh":"餐廳在嚴重食物安全醜聞後，可能面對顧客人數大幅下降。"},{"en":"A drastic decrease in population can weaken farming, defence, trade, and government.","zh":"人口大幅下降可以削弱農業、防衛、貿易和政府。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a sharp decline, not a small change.","zh":"描述急劇衰退而不是小變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"human population size","meaning":"人類人口規模","examples":[{"en":"The definition of collapse includes a decrease in human population size.","zh":"崩潰的定義包括人類人口規模下降。"},{"en":"Human population size means the number of people living in a society, region, or world.","zh":"human population size 指生活在某個社會、地區或世界中的人數。"},{"en":"A town’s human population size may grow when new jobs attract families.","zh":"當新工作吸引家庭到來，城鎮的人口規模可能增長。"},{"en":"If population size falls sharply, schools, markets, farms, and armies may all be affected.","zh":"如果人口規模急劇下降，學校、市場、農場和軍隊都可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing demographic change.","zh":"討論人口變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"political, economic and social complexity","meaning":"政治、經濟及社會複雜程度","examples":[{"en":"Some societies suffered a decline in political, economic and social complexity.","zh":"有些社會在政治、經濟及社會複雜程度上出現下降。"},{"en":"Political, economic and social complexity means how developed a society’s government, trade, work roles, institutions, and relationships are.","zh":"political, economic and social complexity 指一個社會的政府、貿易、工作角色、制度和關係有多發達。"},{"en":"A small village may have less complexity than a modern city with courts, banks, schools, and transport systems.","zh":"與擁有法院、銀行、學校和交通系統的現代城市相比，小村莊的複雜程度可能較低。"},{"en":"When complexity declines, governments may weaken, markets may shrink, and social organisation may break down.","zh":"當複雜程度下降，政府可能變弱，市場可能縮小，社會組織可能瓦解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing how advanced or organised a society is.","zh":"描述社會有多先進或有組織時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"over a considerable area","meaning":"在相當廣闊的地區","examples":[{"en":"The decline occurred over a considerable area.","zh":"衰退發生在相當廣闊的地區。"},{"en":"Over a considerable area means across a large or important stretch of land.","zh":"over a considerable area 指跨越大片或重要範圍的土地。"},{"en":"Flooding may damage homes over a considerable area after days of heavy rain.","zh":"連日大雨後，水災可能在相當廣闊的地區破壞房屋。"},{"en":"If decline spreads over a wide area, the problem is not just local or temporary.","zh":"如果衰退擴散到廣闊地區，問題就不只是本地或短暫的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing the geographical scale of a change.","zh":"顯示變化的地理規模時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for an extended time","meaning":"持續一段長時間","examples":[{"en":"A full collapse continues for an extended time.","zh":"全面崩潰會持續一段長時間。"},{"en":"For an extended time means for a long period, not just briefly.","zh":"for an extended time 指持續很久，而不是短暫地。"},{"en":"A student who is ill for an extended time may need extra help to catch up.","zh":"如果學生病了一段長時間，可能需要額外幫助追上進度。"},{"en":"A society can survive short crises, but long-lasting decline may become much more dangerous.","zh":"社會可以承受短期危機，但長期衰退可能變得危險得多。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when duration matters.","zh":"當持續時間重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"by those standards","meaning":"按照那些標準","examples":[{"en":"By those standards, several ancient societies experienced complete collapse.","zh":"按照那些標準，幾個古代社會經歷了完全崩潰。"},{"en":"By those standards means judged according to the rules, measures, or definitions just mentioned.","zh":"by those standards 指根據剛才提到的規則、量度或定義來判斷。"},{"en":"If passing requires 80 marks, then by those standards a score of 75 is not enough.","zh":"如果合格要求是80分，那麼按照那些標準，75分就不夠。"},{"en":"Standards change how we judge whether something counts as success, failure, or collapse.","zh":"標準會改變我們如何判斷某事是否算成功、失敗或崩潰。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when applying a definition to examples.","zh":"把定義應用到例子時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"victims of","meaning":"……的受害者","examples":[{"en":"Many ancient civilisations were victims of full-scale collapse.","zh":"許多古代文明是全面崩潰的受害者。"},{"en":"Victims of something are people, groups, or societies harmed by it.","zh":"victims of something 指受到某事傷害的人、群體或社會。"},{"en":"Families may become victims of flooding if their homes are built too close to a river.","zh":"如果房屋建得太近河流，家庭可能成為水災的受害者。"},{"en":"A civilisation can become a victim of collapse when several problems overwhelm its systems.","zh":"當多個問題壓垮社會系統，文明可能成為崩潰的受害者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing that something suffered serious harm.","zh":"顯示某事物受到嚴重傷害時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"full-fledged collapse","meaning":"全面崩潰","examples":[{"en":"The Maya cities experienced a full-fledged collapse rather than a minor decline.","zh":"瑪雅城市經歷的是全面崩潰，而不是輕微衰退。"},{"en":"A full-fledged collapse is a complete and serious breakdown, not a small or temporary weakening.","zh":"full-fledged collapse 指完整而嚴重的瓦解，而不是小幅或暫時變弱。"},{"en":"A company faces full-fledged collapse when it loses money, workers, customers, and leadership at the same time.","zh":"當公司同時失去金錢、員工、顧客和領導，它就面對全面崩潰。"},{"en":"Full collapse can involve population loss, abandoned buildings, broken trade, and weakened authority.","zh":"全面崩潰可能涉及人口流失、建築棄置、貿易斷裂和權威削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the decline is broad and severe.","zh":"當衰退廣泛而嚴重時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"The societies suffered complete collapse rather than a minor decline.","zh":"這些社會遭受的是完全崩潰，而不是輕微衰退。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of, and it clearly contrasts two possibilities.","zh":"rather than 指而不是，並清楚對比兩種可能性。"},{"en":"A student may need rest rather than more homework if tiredness is the real problem.","zh":"如果真正問題是疲倦，學生可能需要休息，而不是更多功課。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate the actual situation from a weaker or different alternative.","zh":"這個短語幫助把實際情況與較弱或不同的選項分開。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing that one explanation is more accurate than another.","zh":"顯示一個解釋比另一個更準確時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"minor decline","meaning":"輕微衰退","examples":[{"en":"The changes amounted to more than a minor decline.","zh":"這些變化不只是輕微衰退。"},{"en":"A minor decline is a small decrease or weakening that is not very serious.","zh":"minor decline 指小幅下降或變弱，並不非常嚴重。"},{"en":"A shop may face a minor decline in sales during rainy weather but recover the next week.","zh":"商店在雨天可能銷售輕微下降，但下星期恢復。"},{"en":"A minor decline becomes more worrying if it continues for years or spreads widely.","zh":"如果輕微衰退持續多年或廣泛擴散，就會變得更令人擔心。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting small decline with major collapse.","zh":"對比小幅衰退和重大崩潰時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"within the boundaries of","meaning":"在……的疆界內","examples":[{"en":"Cahokia was located within the boundaries of the modern US.","zh":"Cahokia 位於現代美國的疆界內。"},{"en":"Within the boundaries of means inside the official or recognised limits of a place.","zh":"within the boundaries of 指位於某地官方或公認界限之內。"},{"en":"A school park may be within the boundaries of the campus, even if it is beside a public road.","zh":"學校公園即使位於公共道路旁，也可能在校園疆界內。"},{"en":"Boundaries help readers understand which modern country or region an old site belongs to today.","zh":"疆界有助讀者理解古代遺址今天屬於哪個現代國家或地區。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when connecting historical places with modern maps.","zh":"把歷史地點與現代地圖連接時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hold a fascination for","meaning":"對……有吸引力","examples":[{"en":"Ancient ruins hold a fascination for people throughout the world.","zh":"古代遺址對世界各地的人都有吸引力。"},{"en":"To hold a fascination for someone means to strongly attract their interest and imagination.","zh":"hold a fascination for someone 指強烈吸引某人的興趣和想像。"},{"en":"Old castles hold a fascination for children who enjoy stories about kings and battles.","zh":"舊城堡對喜歡國王和戰爭故事的孩子有吸引力。"},{"en":"Mystery, beauty, and history can make a place fascinating long after its builders are gone.","zh":"神秘、美感和歷史可以令一個地方在建造者消失很久後仍令人着迷。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something continues to attract curiosity.","zh":"當某事物持續吸引好奇心時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"marvel at","meaning":"對……感到驚歎","examples":[{"en":"We often marvel at the size and beauty of monumental ruins.","zh":"我們常對宏偉遺址的規模和美感到驚歎。"},{"en":"To marvel at something means to feel great surprise, admiration, or wonder because of it.","zh":"marvel at something 指因某事而感到非常驚訝、欽佩或讚嘆。"},{"en":"Visitors may marvel at a huge bridge when they learn it was built without modern machines.","zh":"當遊客知道一座巨橋在沒有現代機器下建成，可能會感到驚歎。"},{"en":"People marvel at ruins because they show skill, labour, and ambition from long ago.","zh":"人們對遺址感到驚歎，因為它們展示久遠以前的技術、勞力和野心。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something impresses people deeply.","zh":"當某物深深令人印象深刻時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"learn of something through","meaning":"透過……認識某事物","examples":[{"en":"Many children first learn of ancient civilisations through pictures.","zh":"許多孩子最初透過圖片認識古代文明。"},{"en":"To learn of something through a source means to hear about or discover it by using that source.","zh":"learn of something through a source 指透過某來源聽說或發現某事。"},{"en":"Students may learn of climate change through documentaries before studying it in science class.","zh":"學生可能在科學課學習氣候變化前，先透過紀錄片認識它。"},{"en":"Pictures, stories, and films can introduce people to topics they have never seen directly.","zh":"圖片、故事和電影可以把人們從未親眼見過的主題介紹給他們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how someone first discovers information.","zh":"解釋某人如何首次獲得資訊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"plan a vacation to","meaning":"計劃旅行去……","examples":[{"en":"Many adults plan a vacation to visit famous ruins.","zh":"許多成年人計劃旅行去參觀著名遺址。"},{"en":"To plan a vacation to somewhere means to arrange a holiday trip to that place.","zh":"plan a vacation to somewhere 指安排假期前往某地方。"},{"en":"A family may plan a vacation to Kyoto after seeing photos of its temples.","zh":"一家人看見京都寺廟照片後，可能計劃旅行去京都。"},{"en":"Famous historical sites can attract travellers who want both leisure and learning.","zh":"著名歷史地點可以吸引想兼顧休閒和學習的旅客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing travel decisions.","zh":"討論旅遊決定時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in order to experience","meaning":"為了體驗……","examples":[{"en":"People travel in order to experience the ruins at first hand.","zh":"人們旅行是為了親身體驗那些遺址。"},{"en":"In order to experience something means for the purpose of seeing, feeling, or trying it personally.","zh":"in order to experience something 指為了親自看見、感受或嘗試某事。"},{"en":"Students may visit a court in order to experience how real legal cases are handled.","zh":"學生可能參觀法院，以體驗真實法律案件如何處理。"},{"en":"Direct experience can make history feel more vivid than reading about it only.","zh":"直接體驗可以令歷史比只閱讀文字更鮮活。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the purpose of an action.","zh":"解釋行動目的時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at first hand","meaning":"親身；第一手","examples":[{"en":"Many visitors want to experience ancient ruins at first hand.","zh":"許多遊客想親身體驗古代遺址。"},{"en":"At first hand means directly and personally, not through another person’s report.","zh":"at first hand 指直接而親身地，而不是透過他人報告。"},{"en":"A student may understand poverty better after volunteering at first hand in a community centre.","zh":"學生在社區中心親身做義工後，可能更理解貧窮。"},{"en":"First-hand experience can change how people feel about a topic.","zh":"第一手經驗可以改變人們對一個主題的感受。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when direct experience matters.","zh":"當直接經驗重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"feel drawn to","meaning":"被……吸引","examples":[{"en":"Visitors feel drawn to the beauty and mystery of ancient sites.","zh":"遊客被古代遺址的美和神秘感吸引。"},{"en":"To feel drawn to something means to feel attracted to it in a strong or natural way.","zh":"feel drawn to something 指強烈或自然地被某事吸引。"},{"en":"A student may feel drawn to history after hearing stories about old cities and lost kingdoms.","zh":"學生聽過古城和失落王國的故事後，可能被歷史吸引。"},{"en":"Beauty, mystery, and unanswered questions can make people want to know more.","zh":"美、神秘和未解問題可以令人想知道更多。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when attraction is emotional rather than purely practical.","zh":"當吸引力是情感性的，而不只是實用性的，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"spectacular and haunting beauty","meaning":"壯觀而令人難忘的美","examples":[{"en":"The ruins possess a spectacular and haunting beauty.","zh":"這些遺址具有壯觀而令人難忘的美。"},{"en":"Spectacular and haunting beauty means beauty that is impressive but also sad, mysterious, or unforgettable.","zh":"spectacular and haunting beauty 指令人印象深刻，但同時帶有哀傷、神秘或難忘感的美。"},{"en":"An abandoned theatre may have spectacular and haunting beauty when sunlight falls through broken windows.","zh":"當陽光穿過破窗照入廢棄劇院，它可能有壯觀而令人難忘的美。"},{"en":"Ruins can feel beautiful and unsettling because they show both achievement and loss.","zh":"遺址可以既美麗又令人不安，因為它們同時展示成就和失落。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing places that are visually powerful and emotionally memorable.","zh":"描述視覺上強烈且情感上難忘的地方時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pose a mystery","meaning":"帶來一個謎團","examples":[{"en":"The disappearance of the builders poses a mystery.","zh":"建造者的消失帶來一個謎團。"},{"en":"To pose a mystery means to create a question that is difficult to explain.","zh":"pose a mystery 指產生一個難以解釋的問題。"},{"en":"An empty classroom with all the lights on may pose a mystery to the teacher.","zh":"一間空課室所有燈都開着，可能令老師感到有謎團。"},{"en":"When great buildings remain but their society disappears, people naturally ask what happened.","zh":"當宏偉建築仍在，但其社會消失，人們自然會問發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something invites investigation.","zh":"當某事引發調查時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the scale of","meaning":"……的規模","examples":[{"en":"The scale of the ruins reveals the power of their builders.","zh":"遺址的規模顯示其建造者的力量。"},{"en":"The scale of something means its size, extent, or level of importance.","zh":"scale of something 指某事的大小、範圍或重要程度。"},{"en":"The scale of a school fair becomes clear when hundreds of students, parents, and teachers attend.","zh":"當數百名學生、家長和老師參加，學校嘉年華的規模就變得清楚。"},{"en":"Large-scale buildings suggest that a society had organisation, labour, and resources.","zh":"大規模建築暗示一個社會曾有組織、勞力和資源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when size shows significance.","zh":"當大小顯示重要性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"testify to","meaning":"證明；見證","examples":[{"en":"The ruins testify to the former wealth of the society.","zh":"這些遺址證明該社會昔日的財富。"},{"en":"To testify to something means to serve as evidence or proof of it.","zh":"testify to something 指作為某事的證據或證明。"},{"en":"A student’s neat notebook can testify to their careful study habits.","zh":"學生整齊的筆記可以證明其仔細的學習習慣。"},{"en":"Massive ruins testify to the skills and resources once available to their builders.","zh":"巨大遺址見證建造者曾擁有的技術和資源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when physical evidence proves something about the past.","zh":"當實體證據證明過去某事時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"former wealth and power","meaning":"昔日的財富和權力","examples":[{"en":"The structures testify to the builders’ former wealth and power.","zh":"這些建築見證建造者昔日的財富和權力。"},{"en":"Former wealth and power means the money, resources, influence, and authority a person or society once had.","zh":"former wealth and power 指一個人或社會曾經擁有的金錢、資源、影響力和權威。"},{"en":"An old mansion may reveal a family’s former wealth and power even after the family loses its fortune.","zh":"即使一個家族失去財富，舊大宅仍可能顯示其昔日財富和權力。"},{"en":"Large monuments require resources, so they can show how strong a society used to be.","zh":"大型紀念建築需要資源，因此可以顯示一個社會曾經多強大。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when past strength is visible in remaining objects.","zh":"當過去力量可從留下的物件中看見時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"abandon great structures","meaning":"棄置宏偉建築","examples":[{"en":"The builders eventually abandoned the great structures they had created.","zh":"建造者最終棄置了他們創造的宏偉建築。"},{"en":"To abandon great structures means to leave large important buildings unused or empty.","zh":"abandon great structures 指把大型重要建築空置或不再使用。"},{"en":"A company may abandon a large factory when production moves to another city.","zh":"當生產搬到另一個城市，公司可能棄置大型工廠。"},{"en":"If people abandon major buildings, it may show population loss, danger, or economic failure.","zh":"如果人們棄置主要建築，可能顯示人口流失、危險或經濟失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when impressive buildings are left behind.","zh":"當令人印象深刻的建築被留下不用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"with such effort","meaning":"費盡心力地","examples":[{"en":"They abandoned the structures they had created with such effort.","zh":"他們棄置了自己費盡心力創造的建築。"},{"en":"With such effort means with so much hard work, time, skill, or energy.","zh":"with such effort 指用大量辛勞、時間、技術或精力。"},{"en":"A student may feel sad if a project made with such effort is ignored by the class.","zh":"如果一份費盡心力完成的專題被全班忽視，學生可能感到難過。"},{"en":"When something made with great effort is abandoned, the loss feels more dramatic.","zh":"當費盡心力製造的東西被棄置，損失感會更強烈。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when emphasising how hard something was to create.","zh":"強調某物創造得多辛苦時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"once so mighty","meaning":"曾經如此強大","examples":[{"en":"A society that was once so mighty could still collapse.","zh":"一個曾經如此強大的社會仍可能崩潰。"},{"en":"Once so mighty means formerly very powerful, impressive, or influential.","zh":"once so mighty 指過去非常強大、令人印象深刻或有影響力。"},{"en":"A company once so mighty may decline if it ignores new technology and customer needs.","zh":"一間曾經如此強大的公司，如果忽視新科技和顧客需要，也可能衰落。"},{"en":"Past power does not guarantee future survival.","zh":"過去的力量不保證未來生存。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing contrast between former strength and later weakness.","zh":"顯示昔日強盛與後來衰弱之間的對比時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"end up collapsing","meaning":"最終崩潰","examples":[{"en":"Even a powerful society may end up collapsing.","zh":"即使強大的社會也可能最終崩潰。"},{"en":"To end up collapsing means finally collapse after a process or series of problems.","zh":"end up collapsing 指經歷一個過程或一連串問題後最終崩潰。"},{"en":"A badly managed club may end up collapsing if members stop joining and money runs out.","zh":"如果會員停止加入且資金用盡，管理不善的學會可能最終瓦解。"},{"en":"Small problems can accumulate until a system can no longer function.","zh":"小問題可以累積，直到系統無法再運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the final result is negative and gradual.","zh":"當最終結果是負面且逐漸形成時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it has long been suspected that","meaning":"長久以來一直有人懷疑","examples":[{"en":"It has long been suspected that ecological damage contributed to many collapses.","zh":"長久以來一直有人懷疑生態破壞促成許多崩潰。"},{"en":"It has long been suspected that means people have believed or guessed something for a long time, though proof may have come later.","zh":"it has long been suspected that 指人們長時間以來相信或猜測某事，但證據可能較後才出現。"},{"en":"It has long been suspected that poor sleep affects learning, and recent studies have added evidence.","zh":"長久以來一直有人懷疑睡眠不足影響學習，而近期研究增加了證據。"},{"en":"Long-held suspicions become stronger when new research confirms them.","zh":"當新研究確認，長期懷疑就會變得更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an old idea is later supported by evidence.","zh":"當舊想法後來獲證據支持時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mysterious abandonment","meaning":"神秘的棄置現象","examples":[{"en":"Environmental problems may explain some mysterious abandonments.","zh":"環境問題可能解釋一些神秘的棄置現象。"},{"en":"Mysterious abandonment means the unexplained leaving behind of a place, building, or settlement.","zh":"mysterious abandonment 指一個地方、建築或聚落被棄置，而原因未明。"},{"en":"An empty village with food jars and tools left inside houses may suggest mysterious abandonment.","zh":"如果一條空村的屋內仍留下食物罐和工具，可能暗示神秘棄置。"},{"en":"Environmental stress can force people to leave even places they once valued deeply.","zh":"環境壓力可以迫使人離開他們曾經非常重視的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when people left a site and the reason is unclear.","zh":"當人們離開一個地點而原因不清楚時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at least partly triggered by","meaning":"至少部分由……引發","examples":[{"en":"The collapse was at least partly triggered by ecological problems.","zh":"這場崩潰至少部分由生態問題引發。"},{"en":"At least partly triggered by means caused in some degree by a factor, even if other causes also existed.","zh":"at least partly triggered by 指某因素在某程度上造成某事，即使還有其他原因。"},{"en":"A student’s poor result may be at least partly triggered by illness during revision week.","zh":"學生成績欠佳可能至少部分由溫習週生病引發。"},{"en":"Complex events usually have several causes, so one factor may trigger only part of the outcome.","zh":"複雜事件通常有多個原因，所以一個因素可能只引發部分結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when avoiding a single-cause explanation.","zh":"避免單一原因解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ecological problems","meaning":"生態問題","examples":[{"en":"Ecological problems contributed to the decline of many societies.","zh":"生態問題促成許多社會的衰落。"},{"en":"Ecological problems are difficulties involving the natural environment, such as damaged forests, soil, water, or wildlife.","zh":"ecological problems 指涉及自然環境的困難，例如森林、土壤、水或野生生物受損。"},{"en":"A farming village may face ecological problems if its soil becomes too dry or salty.","zh":"如果土壤變得太乾或太鹹，農村可能面對生態問題。"},{"en":"When ecological problems reduce food and water, social and political problems may follow.","zh":"當生態問題減少食物和水，社會及政治問題可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when nature and human survival are connected.","zh":"當自然和人類生存相連時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"inadvertently destroy","meaning":"無意中破壞","examples":[{"en":"People may inadvertently destroy resources on which they depend.","zh":"人們可能無意中破壞自己賴以生存的資源。"},{"en":"To inadvertently destroy something means to damage or ruin it without intending to do so.","zh":"inadvertently destroy something 指在沒有意圖下損害或毀掉某物。"},{"en":"A family may inadvertently destroy a garden by using too much chemical cleaner nearby.","zh":"家庭可能因在附近使用太多化學清潔劑而無意中破壞花園。"},{"en":"Societies can harm forests, soil, or water while simply trying to feed and support themselves.","zh":"社會可能在只是想養活和支持自身時傷害森林、土壤或水源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when damage is accidental but still serious.","zh":"當破壞是意外但仍嚴重時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"environmental resources","meaning":"環境資源","examples":[{"en":"Societies depend heavily on environmental resources.","zh":"社會高度依賴環境資源。"},{"en":"Environmental resources are natural things people use, such as water, soil, forests, fish, minerals, and clean air.","zh":"environmental resources 指人們使用的自然事物，例如水、土壤、森林、魚類、礦物和清潔空氣。"},{"en":"A village near a river may depend on environmental resources for farming, drinking water, and transport.","zh":"河邊村莊可能依賴環境資源來耕作、取得飲用水和運輸。"},{"en":"If environmental resources are overused, communities may face food shortages or economic decline.","zh":"如果環境資源被過度使用，社區可能面對食物短缺或經濟衰退。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing nature as a basis for human life.","zh":"討論自然作為人類生活基礎時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"resources on which society depends","meaning":"社會賴以生存的資源","examples":[{"en":"People destroyed some of the resources on which their society depended.","zh":"人們破壞了一些社會賴以生存的資源。"},{"en":"Resources on which society depends are the natural or human-made supports that allow a society to survive.","zh":"resources on which society depends 指讓社會能夠生存的自然或人造支撐。"},{"en":"A fishing town depends on clean seas, boats, workers, and markets.","zh":"漁村依賴清潔海洋、船隻、工人和市場。"},{"en":"Destroying key resources can weaken food supply, jobs, health, and political stability.","zh":"破壞關鍵資源可以削弱食物供應、工作、健康和政治穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing that survival relies on certain foundations.","zh":"顯示生存依賴某些基礎時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"unintended ecological suicide","meaning":"非蓄意的生態自殺","examples":[{"en":"The author describes environmental self-destruction as unintended ecological suicide.","zh":"作者把環境上的自我破壞描述為非蓄意的生態自殺。"},{"en":"Unintended ecological suicide means a society accidentally destroys the environment it needs in order to survive.","zh":"unintended ecological suicide 指社會意外地破壞自己生存所需的環境。"},{"en":"A town that cuts all nearby forests may later suffer floods, heat, and soil loss without meaning to harm itself.","zh":"一個城鎮砍光附近森林後，可能無意中令自己遭受水災、高溫和土壤流失。"},{"en":"The damage is unintended because people may be trying to solve short-term problems.","zh":"這種破壞是非蓄意的，因為人們可能只是試圖解決短期問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when human actions slowly destroy their own natural support system.","zh":"當人類行動慢慢摧毀自身自然支撐系統時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ecocide","meaning":"生態毀滅","examples":[{"en":"Ecocide occurs when people destroy the environment that supports them.","zh":"當人們破壞支撐自己的環境時，就會發生生態毀滅。"},{"en":"Ecocide means severe destruction of an ecosystem, especially through human action.","zh":"ecocide 指嚴重破壞生態系統，尤其是由人類行動造成。"},{"en":"A region may face ecocide if forests are cleared, rivers are poisoned, and wildlife disappears.","zh":"如果森林被清除、河流被污染、野生生物消失，某地區可能面對生態毀滅。"},{"en":"Ecocide can harm food supplies, health, climate, and long-term survival.","zh":"生態毀滅可以傷害食物供應、健康、氣候和長期生存。"},{"en":"This word is useful when environmental damage is extreme and life-supporting systems are destroyed.","zh":"當環境破壞極端並摧毀生命支撐系統時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be confirmed by discoveries","meaning":"得到研究發現證實","examples":[{"en":"The theory has been confirmed by discoveries made in recent decades.","zh":"這個理論已得到近數十年研究發現證實。"},{"en":"Be confirmed by discoveries means be supported or proven more likely by new findings.","zh":"be confirmed by discoveries 指受到新發現支持，或被證明更可能正確。"},{"en":"A teacher’s guess about weak vocabulary may be confirmed by students’ reading test results.","zh":"老師對學生詞彙薄弱的猜測，可能由閱讀測驗結果證實。"},{"en":"When new evidence supports an old theory, researchers become more confident in it.","zh":"當新證據支持舊理論，研究人員會對它更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research findings strengthen an explanation.","zh":"當研究發現加強一個解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in recent decades","meaning":"在近數十年","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have made important discoveries in recent decades.","zh":"研究人員在近數十年取得重要發現。"},{"en":"In recent decades means during the last several ten-year periods.","zh":"in recent decades 指在最近幾個十年期間。"},{"en":"In recent decades, mobile phones have changed how families communicate.","zh":"在近數十年，手提電話改變了家庭溝通方式。"},{"en":"New tools and methods often lead to new discoveries over time.","zh":"新工具和方法常隨時間帶來新發現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing relatively recent historical change.","zh":"描述相對近期的歷史變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"archaeologists","meaning":"考古學家","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists have studied the remains of collapsed societies.","zh":"考古學家研究了崩潰社會的遺存。"},{"en":"Archaeologists are researchers who study past human life through objects, buildings, bones, tools, and ruins.","zh":"archaeologists 指透過物件、建築、骨骼、工具和遺址研究過去人類生活的研究人員。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may dig carefully at an old site to find pottery or walls.","zh":"考古學家可能在古老遺址仔細挖掘，以尋找陶器或牆壁。"},{"en":"Their work helps explain how people lived, traded, worshipped, and sometimes collapsed.","zh":"他們的工作幫助解釋人們如何生活、貿易、崇拜，以及有時如何崩潰。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing evidence from ancient human societies.","zh":"討論古代人類社會證據時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"climatologists","meaning":"氣候學家","examples":[{"en":"Climatologists examine how changes in climate affected past societies.","zh":"氣候學家研究氣候變化如何影響過去的社會。"},{"en":"Climatologists are scientists who study climate patterns and long-term changes in weather conditions.","zh":"climatologists 指研究氣候模式和長期天氣條件變化的科學家。"},{"en":"A climatologist may study tree rings or ice records to understand old droughts.","zh":"氣候學家可能研究樹輪或冰層紀錄，以了解古代乾旱。"},{"en":"Climate evidence can show whether drought, cooling, or rainfall change affected agriculture.","zh":"氣候證據可以顯示乾旱、降溫或降雨變化是否影響農業。"},{"en":"This word is useful when environmental history involves climate.","zh":"當環境歷史涉及氣候時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"paleontologists","meaning":"古生物學家","examples":[{"en":"Paleontologists contributed evidence about environmental change.","zh":"古生物學家提供了關於環境變化的證據。"},{"en":"Paleontologists are scientists who study ancient life through fossils and remains.","zh":"paleontologists 指透過化石和遺骸研究古代生命的科學家。"},{"en":"A paleontologist may study fossil shells to understand past sea conditions.","zh":"古生物學家可能研究貝殼化石，以了解過去海洋狀況。"},{"en":"Fossil evidence can show how environments changed before or during human settlement.","zh":"化石證據可以顯示環境在人類定居前或期間如何改變。"},{"en":"This word is useful when studying very old life and environments.","zh":"研究非常古老的生命和環境時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"palynologists","meaning":"孢粉學家","examples":[{"en":"Palynologists study pollen to understand past environments.","zh":"孢粉學家研究花粉，以了解過去環境。"},{"en":"Palynologists are scientists who analyse pollen grains preserved in soil, lakes, or sediments.","zh":"palynologists 指分析保存在土壤、湖泊或沉積物中的花粉粒的科學家。"},{"en":"A palynologist may identify ancient forest types by examining pollen under a microscope.","zh":"孢粉學家可能透過顯微鏡檢查花粉，以識別古代森林類型。"},{"en":"Pollen evidence can reveal whether land was forested, farmed, dry, or wet.","zh":"花粉證據可以揭示土地曾是森林、農田、乾地還是濕地。"},{"en":"This word is useful when tiny plant evidence helps reconstruct history.","zh":"當微小植物證據幫助重建歷史時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pollen scientists","meaning":"花粉科學家","examples":[{"en":"Palynologists are scientists who specialise in the study of pollen.","zh":"孢粉學家是專門研究花粉的科學家。"},{"en":"Pollen scientists study pollen to learn about plants, climate, farming, and environmental change.","zh":"pollen scientists 指研究花粉以了解植物、氣候、農業和環境變化的科學家。"},{"en":"A pollen scientist may examine lake mud to find traces of ancient crops.","zh":"花粉科學家可能檢查湖泥，以尋找古代作物痕跡。"},{"en":"Because pollen can survive for long periods, it provides clues about past landscapes.","zh":"因為花粉可以保存很久，它能提供關於過去景觀的線索。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining palynology in simpler words.","zh":"用較簡單文字解釋孢粉學時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"undermine themselves","meaning":"削弱自身","examples":[{"en":"Some societies undermined themselves by damaging their environments.","zh":"有些社會透過破壞環境而削弱自身。"},{"en":"To undermine themselves means to weaken their own position, strength, or survival chances.","zh":"undermine themselves 指削弱自己的地位、力量或生存機會。"},{"en":"A student undermines themselves if they stay up all night before an important exam.","zh":"學生在重要考試前通宵不睡，就是削弱自己。"},{"en":"A society can undermine itself when short-term gains destroy long-term resources.","zh":"當社會為短期利益破壞長期資源，它就可能削弱自身。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when people unintentionally weaken their own future.","zh":"當人們無意中削弱自己的未來時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"damage the environment","meaning":"破壞環境","examples":[{"en":"Past societies sometimes damaged the environment that supported them.","zh":"過去的社會有時破壞支撐自己的環境。"},{"en":"To damage the environment means to harm land, water, air, plants, animals, or ecosystems.","zh":"damage the environment 指傷害土地、水、空氣、植物、動物或生態系統。"},{"en":"A factory may damage the environment if it releases waste into a river.","zh":"如果工廠把廢物排入河流，就可能破壞環境。"},{"en":"Environmental damage can reduce food, water, health, and economic stability.","zh":"環境破壞可以減少食物、水、健康和經濟穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when human activity harms natural systems.","zh":"當人類活動傷害自然系統時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fall into eight categories","meaning":"分為八個類別","examples":[{"en":"The environmental processes fall into eight categories.","zh":"這些環境過程分為八個類別。"},{"en":"Fall into eight categories means can be divided into eight groups or types.","zh":"fall into eight categories 指可以分成八組或八種類型。"},{"en":"A teacher may say common grammar mistakes fall into five categories.","zh":"老師可能說常見文法錯誤分為五個類別。"},{"en":"Categories help people organise complex information into clearer parts.","zh":"類別幫助人們把複雜資料整理成更清楚的部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when classifying causes or problems.","zh":"分類原因或問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"relative importance","meaning":"相對重要性","examples":[{"en":"The relative importance of each factor differs between societies.","zh":"每個因素的相對重要性在不同社會之間有所不同。"},{"en":"Relative importance means how important something is compared with other factors.","zh":"relative importance 指某事與其他因素相比有多重要。"},{"en":"In exam preparation, the relative importance of grammar, vocabulary, and planning may vary by student.","zh":"在備考中，文法、詞彙和規劃的相對重要性可能因學生而異。"},{"en":"A cause may be important in one case but less important in another.","zh":"某原因在一個情況中可能重要，在另一個情況中則較不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing several contributing factors.","zh":"比較幾個促成因素時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"differ from case to case","meaning":"因情況而異","examples":[{"en":"The causes of collapse differ from case to case.","zh":"崩潰的原因因情況而異。"},{"en":"Differ from case to case means change depending on the particular situation.","zh":"differ from case to case 指會根據具體情況而改變。"},{"en":"The best way to learn English may differ from case to case because students have different weaknesses.","zh":"最佳英語學習方法可能因情況而異，因為學生有不同弱點。"},{"en":"When cases differ, one simple explanation cannot fit every example.","zh":"當個案不同，一個簡單解釋不能適用於所有例子。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when avoiding overgeneralisation.","zh":"避免過度概括時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"deforestation and habitat destruction","meaning":"砍伐森林及破壞棲息地","examples":[{"en":"Deforestation and habitat destruction weakened some societies.","zh":"砍伐森林及破壞棲息地削弱了一些社會。"},{"en":"Deforestation and habitat destruction mean cutting down forests and damaging the places where plants and animals live.","zh":"deforestation and habitat destruction 指砍掉森林並破壞動植物生活的地方。"},{"en":"A village may suffer if nearby forests are cleared and wildlife disappears.","zh":"如果附近森林被清除且野生生物消失，村莊可能受害。"},{"en":"Losing forests can reduce soil quality, water control, fuel, building materials, and food sources.","zh":"失去森林可以降低土壤質素、水源控制、燃料、建材和食物來源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing environmental causes of decline.","zh":"討論衰落的環境原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"soil problems","meaning":"土壤問題","examples":[{"en":"Poor farming practices may create serious soil problems.","zh":"不良耕作方式可能造成嚴重土壤問題。"},{"en":"Soil problems are difficulties with the land used for growing crops, such as erosion, salinity, or loss of nutrients.","zh":"soil problems 指用來種植作物的土地出現問題，例如侵蝕、鹽化或養分流失。"},{"en":"A farm may face soil problems if the same crop is planted every year without rest or fertiliser.","zh":"如果農場每年種植同一作物而不休耕或施肥，可能面對土壤問題。"},{"en":"When soil becomes weak, harvests fall and food shortages may follow.","zh":"當土壤變弱，收成會下降，食物短缺可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when farming and land quality are connected.","zh":"當農業和土地質素有關時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"water management problems","meaning":"水資源管理問題","examples":[{"en":"Water management problems can threaten agricultural societies.","zh":"水資源管理問題可以威脅農業社會。"},{"en":"Water management problems are difficulties in storing, controlling, sharing, or using water properly.","zh":"water management problems 指在儲存、控制、分配或適當使用水方面的困難。"},{"en":"A town may face water management problems if old pipes leak and reservoirs dry up.","zh":"如果舊水管漏水且水庫乾涸，城鎮可能面對水資源管理問題。"},{"en":"Poor water management can damage crops, spread disease, or create conflict between communities.","zh":"水資源管理不善可以破壞作物、傳播疾病，或造成社群衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when water supply affects survival.","zh":"當水供應影響生存時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"overhunting","meaning":"過度狩獵","examples":[{"en":"Overhunting can reduce important animal populations.","zh":"過度狩獵可以減少重要動物數量。"},{"en":"Overhunting means killing too many wild animals faster than they can reproduce.","zh":"overhunting 指捕殺太多野生動物，速度快於牠們繁殖恢復的速度。"},{"en":"A village may face food problems if hunters take too many deer from nearby forests.","zh":"如果獵人從附近森林捕獵太多鹿，村莊可能面對食物問題。"},{"en":"Overhunting can remove key species and damage the balance of an ecosystem.","zh":"過度狩獵可以移除關鍵物種並破壞生態系統平衡。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing human pressure on wildlife.","zh":"討論人類對野生生物的壓力時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"overfishing","meaning":"過度捕魚","examples":[{"en":"Overfishing can exhaust an important source of food.","zh":"過度捕魚可以耗盡重要食物來源。"},{"en":"Overfishing means catching too many fish so that fish populations cannot recover.","zh":"overfishing 指捕撈太多魚，令魚群無法恢復。"},{"en":"A coastal town may suffer if overfishing leaves fewer fish for local families and markets.","zh":"如果過度捕魚令本地家庭和市場可得魚類減少，海岸小鎮可能受害。"},{"en":"Overfishing can harm food supply, jobs, and marine ecosystems.","zh":"過度捕魚可以傷害食物供應、工作和海洋生態系統。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing unsustainable use of the sea.","zh":"討論不可持續地使用海洋時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"introduced species","meaning":"外來物種","examples":[{"en":"Introduced species may damage local ecosystems.","zh":"外來物種可能破壞本地生態系統。"},{"en":"Introduced species are plants or animals brought to a place where they did not originally live.","zh":"introduced species 指被帶到原本不生活於該地的植物或動物。"},{"en":"A pet released into the wild may become an introduced species if it survives and spreads.","zh":"被放生到野外的寵物如果存活並擴散，可能成為外來物種。"},{"en":"Introduced species can compete with native species, eat them, or bring new diseases.","zh":"外來物種可以與本土物種競爭、捕食牠們，或帶來新疾病。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing ecological disruption.","zh":"討論生態干擾時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"native species","meaning":"本土物種","examples":[{"en":"Introduced animals may threaten native species.","zh":"外來動物可能威脅本土物種。"},{"en":"Native species are plants or animals that naturally belong to a particular place.","zh":"native species 指自然屬於某一地方的植物或動物。"},{"en":"Native birds may decline if introduced cats hunt them.","zh":"如果外來貓捕食本土鳥類，本土鳥類數量可能下降。"},{"en":"Protecting native species helps preserve the original balance of an ecosystem.","zh":"保護本土物種有助保存生態系統原有平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing local wildlife with introduced organisms.","zh":"比較本地野生生物與外來生物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"human population growth","meaning":"人口增長","examples":[{"en":"Human population growth places greater pressure on resources.","zh":"人口增長對資源造成更大壓力。"},{"en":"Human population growth means an increase in the number of people living in a society or region.","zh":"human population growth 指居住在某社會或地區的人數增加。"},{"en":"A city may build more schools when human population growth brings more children.","zh":"當人口增長帶來更多兒童，城市可能興建更多學校。"},{"en":"More people usually need more food, water, housing, energy, and waste management.","zh":"更多人口通常需要更多食物、水、住屋、能源和廢物管理。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing pressure on resources.","zh":"討論資源壓力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"increased per-capita impact","meaning":"人均影響增加","examples":[{"en":"Increased per-capita impact can intensify environmental damage.","zh":"人均影響增加可以加劇環境破壞。"},{"en":"Increased per-capita impact means each person uses more resources or causes more environmental pressure than before.","zh":"increased per-capita impact 指每個人比以前使用更多資源或造成更大環境壓力。"},{"en":"A city’s per-person impact rises if everyone starts using more electricity and buying more goods.","zh":"如果每個人開始用更多電和購買更多商品，城市的人均影響就會上升。"},{"en":"Even without population growth, higher consumption per person can increase total damage.","zh":"即使人口沒有增長，每人消費增加也可以提高總破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when environmental pressure comes from individual consumption.","zh":"當環境壓力來自個人消費時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tend to follow","meaning":"往往遵循……","examples":[{"en":"Past collapses tended to follow somewhat similar courses.","zh":"過去的崩潰往往遵循略為相似的發展過程。"},{"en":"Tend to follow means usually move or develop in a certain pattern, though not always.","zh":"tend to follow 指通常以某種模式移動或發展，但不是永遠如此。"},{"en":"Students tend to follow a routine when they revise at the same time each day.","zh":"如果學生每天同一時間溫習，他們往往遵循一套規律。"},{"en":"If many collapses follow a similar pattern, historians can compare their stages.","zh":"如果許多崩潰遵循相似模式，歷史學家就能比較其階段。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a general tendency rather than a fixed rule.","zh":"描述一般傾向而非固定規則時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a similar course","meaning":"類似的發展過程","examples":[{"en":"Several civilisations followed a similar course of decline.","zh":"幾個文明遵循類似的衰退過程。"},{"en":"A similar course means a comparable path, process, or pattern of development.","zh":"similar course 指相近的路徑、過程或發展模式。"},{"en":"Two students may follow a similar course of improvement if both practise daily and get feedback.","zh":"如果兩名學生都每天練習並得到回饋，他們可能遵循類似的進步過程。"},{"en":"Similar courses allow researchers to look for shared causes.","zh":"類似的過程讓研究人員尋找共同原因。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing how different cases develop over time.","zh":"比較不同個案如何隨時間發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"variations on a theme","meaning":"同一主題的不同變奏","examples":[{"en":"The different collapses were variations on a theme.","zh":"不同崩潰是同一主題的不同變奏。"},{"en":"Variations on a theme are different versions of the same basic pattern or idea.","zh":"variations on a theme 指同一基本模式或想法的不同版本。"},{"en":"Several students may write different essays that are variations on the same theme of friendship.","zh":"幾名學生可能寫出不同文章，但都是友誼這一主題的不同變奏。"},{"en":"Collapses may differ in detail but still share repeated problems such as resource pressure.","zh":"崩潰在細節上可能不同，但仍共享資源壓力等反覆問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when cases are not identical but clearly related.","zh":"當個案不完全相同但明顯相關時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"find it tempting to","meaning":"很容易想要……","examples":[{"en":"Writers find it tempting to compare societies with individual people.","zh":"作家很容易想要把社會與個人作比較。"},{"en":"To find it tempting to do something means feel strongly attracted to doing it, even if it may not be wise.","zh":"find it tempting to do something 指強烈想做某事，即使未必明智。"},{"en":"A student may find it tempting to copy an answer when the homework is difficult.","zh":"當功課困難時，學生可能很容易想要抄答案。"},{"en":"Simple comparisons can be tempting because they make complex ideas easier to explain.","zh":"簡單比較很吸引，因為它令複雜想法較容易解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an idea is attractive but needs caution.","zh":"當一個想法很吸引但需要謹慎時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"draw analogies between","meaning":"把……作類比","examples":[{"en":"Writers often draw analogies between societies and human lives.","zh":"作家常把社會和人的一生作類比。"},{"en":"To draw analogies between two things means to compare them because they share some features.","zh":"draw analogies between two things 指因兩者有某些共同特徵而作比較。"},{"en":"A teacher may draw analogies between learning a language and training for a sport.","zh":"老師可能把學語言和體育訓練作類比。"},{"en":"Analogies can clarify ideas, but they can mislead if the two things differ too much.","zh":"類比可以澄清想法，但如果兩者差異太大，也可能誤導。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining through comparison.","zh":"透過比較作解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the course of human societies","meaning":"人類社會的發展歷程","examples":[{"en":"The course of human societies is sometimes compared with a human life.","zh":"人類社會的發展歷程有時被拿來與人的一生比較。"},{"en":"The course of human societies means the way societies develop, change, rise, and decline over time.","zh":"course of human societies 指社會如何隨時間發展、改變、興起和衰落。"},{"en":"A history course may examine the course of human societies from farming villages to modern cities.","zh":"歷史課可能檢視人類社會由農村到現代城市的發展歷程。"},{"en":"Studying this course helps people see patterns of growth, stress, reform, and collapse.","zh":"研究這個歷程幫助人們看見增長、壓力、改革和崩潰的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing long-term social development.","zh":"討論長期社會發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"individual human lives","meaning":"個人的一生","examples":[{"en":"A society’s development cannot always be compared with individual human lives.","zh":"一個社會的發展不總能與個人的一生相比。"},{"en":"Individual human lives are the life paths of single people, from birth through growth to death.","zh":"individual human lives 指單個人的人生歷程，由出生、成長到死亡。"},{"en":"A biography follows an individual human life, while history studies whole communities.","zh":"傳記追蹤個人的一生，而歷史研究整個社群。"},{"en":"Societies are more complex than individuals because many people and institutions interact.","zh":"社會比個人更複雜，因為許多人和制度互相作用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting personal life with social history.","zh":"對比個人生命和社會歷史時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"eventual death","meaning":"最終死亡","examples":[{"en":"The metaphor compares social collapse with eventual death.","zh":"這個比喻把社會崩潰與最終死亡相比。"},{"en":"Eventual death means death that finally happens after time has passed.","zh":"eventual death 指經過一段時間後最終發生的死亡。"},{"en":"A plant without water may not die immediately, but eventual death becomes likely.","zh":"缺水的植物未必立即死亡，但最終死亡會變得可能。"},{"en":"Comparing a society with a living person suggests that decline must end in death.","zh":"把社會與活人相比，暗示衰退必定以死亡告終。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a final outcome after a process.","zh":"描述一個過程後的最終結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prove erroneous","meaning":"證實是錯誤的","examples":[{"en":"The human-life metaphor proves erroneous for many societies.","zh":"對許多社會而言，人生比喻證實是錯誤的。"},{"en":"Prove erroneous means turn out to be wrong or inaccurate.","zh":"prove erroneous 指結果顯示是錯誤或不準確的。"},{"en":"A student’s first answer may prove erroneous after they check the passage more carefully.","zh":"學生更仔細查看文章後，最初答案可能證實是錯誤的。"},{"en":"A comparison can seem useful at first but prove erroneous when evidence is examined.","zh":"一個比較起初可能看似有用，但在檢查證據後證實錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an idea is later shown to be false.","zh":"當一個想法後來被證明錯誤時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"decline rapidly","meaning":"迅速衰落","examples":[{"en":"Some societies declined rapidly after reaching their peak.","zh":"有些社會在達到頂峰後迅速衰落。"},{"en":"To decline rapidly means to become weaker or worse very quickly.","zh":"decline rapidly 指非常快速地變弱或惡化。"},{"en":"A shop may decline rapidly if a new mall takes away most of its customers.","zh":"如果新商場搶走大部分顧客，小店可能迅速衰落。"},{"en":"Rapid decline can shock people because the earlier situation seemed strong.","zh":"迅速衰落可以令人震驚，因為早前情況看似強大。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when change is both negative and fast.","zh":"當變化既負面又快速時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reach peak numbers and power","meaning":"達到人口和權力頂峰","examples":[{"en":"Several societies collapsed after reaching peak numbers and power.","zh":"幾個社會在達到人口和權力頂峰後崩潰。"},{"en":"To reach peak numbers and power means to arrive at the highest level of population and influence.","zh":"reach peak numbers and power 指達到人口數量和影響力的最高水平。"},{"en":"A club may reach peak numbers when membership is at its highest and activities are most successful.","zh":"當會員人數最高且活動最成功時，學會可能達到人數頂峰。"},{"en":"A society can still be vulnerable even at its strongest point.","zh":"一個社會即使在最強盛時仍可能脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when collapse follows a period of maximum strength.","zh":"當崩潰發生在最強盛時期之後，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"come as a surprise and shock","meaning":"令人感到意外和震驚","examples":[{"en":"The rapid decline must have come as a surprise and shock to citizens.","zh":"這種迅速衰退必定令市民感到意外和震驚。"},{"en":"To come as a surprise and shock means to happen unexpectedly and cause strong emotional reaction.","zh":"come as a surprise and shock 指事情突然發生，並引起強烈情緒反應。"},{"en":"A sudden school closure may come as a surprise and shock to students and parents.","zh":"學校突然關閉可能令學生和家長感到意外和震驚。"},{"en":"When people believe their society is stable, collapse can feel impossible until it happens.","zh":"當人們相信自己的社會穩定，崩潰在發生前可能感覺不可能。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a negative event is unexpected.","zh":"當負面事件出乎意料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"follow a trajectory","meaning":"遵循某種發展軌跡","examples":[{"en":"Not every society followed the same trajectory.","zh":"並非每個社會都遵循相同的發展軌跡。"},{"en":"To follow a trajectory means to develop along a particular path or pattern over time.","zh":"follow a trajectory 指隨時間沿着某一路徑或模式發展。"},{"en":"Two students may follow different trajectories even if they start with the same English level.","zh":"即使兩名學生開始時英語水平相同，他們也可能遵循不同發展軌跡。"},{"en":"A society’s trajectory can change because of decisions, disasters, resources, and contact with others.","zh":"社會的發展軌跡可以因決策、災難、資源和與他人接觸而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing long-term development.","zh":"描述長期發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"unvaryingly to completion","meaning":"毫無例外地走到終點","examples":[{"en":"Societies did not follow this course unvaryingly to completion.","zh":"社會並沒有毫無例外地沿這條路走到終點。"},{"en":"Unvaryingly to completion means in exactly the same way until the full process is finished.","zh":"unvaryingly to completion 指完全以同一方式走完整個過程。"},{"en":"Students rarely follow a study plan unvaryingly to completion because illness or exams may interrupt it.","zh":"學生很少毫無變化地完成學習計劃，因為疾病或考試可能打斷它。"},{"en":"Historical processes often change direction before reaching the expected end.","zh":"歷史過程常在到達預期終點前改變方向。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when rejecting an overly fixed pattern.","zh":"拒絕過於固定的模式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"collapse to different degrees","meaning":"以不同程度崩潰","examples":[{"en":"Different societies collapsed to different degrees.","zh":"不同社會以不同程度崩潰。"},{"en":"To collapse to different degrees means to break down with different levels of severity.","zh":"collapse to different degrees 指以不同嚴重程度瓦解。"},{"en":"After a storm, some shops may suffer minor damage while others close completely.","zh":"暴風雨後，有些商店只受輕微損害，另一些則完全關閉。"},{"en":"Not all collapse is total; some societies lose cities but keep smaller communities alive.","zh":"並非所有崩潰都是全面的；有些社會失去城市但保留小社群。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing levels of decline.","zh":"比較衰退程度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in somewhat different ways","meaning":"以略有不同的方式","examples":[{"en":"Past societies declined in somewhat different ways.","zh":"過去的社會以略有不同的方式衰落。"},{"en":"In somewhat different ways means in ways that are partly different but still comparable.","zh":"in somewhat different ways 指方式有部分不同，但仍可比較。"},{"en":"Two students may improve in somewhat different ways: one through reading, another through speaking practice.","zh":"兩名學生可能以略有不同的方式進步：一人透過閱讀，另一人透過口語練習。"},{"en":"Similar causes can still produce different results depending on local conditions.","zh":"相似原因仍可因本地條件不同而產生不同結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing cases without pretending they are identical.","zh":"比較個案但不假裝它們完全相同時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not collapse at all","meaning":"完全沒有崩潰","examples":[{"en":"Many societies did not collapse at all.","zh":"許多社會完全沒有崩潰。"},{"en":"Not collapse at all means continue existing instead of breaking down.","zh":"not collapse at all 指繼續存在，而不是瓦解。"},{"en":"A school facing financial pressure may not collapse at all if the community helps it recover.","zh":"面對財政壓力的學校，如果社區幫助它復原，可能完全不會倒閉。"},{"en":"Some societies adapt, reform, or reduce pressure before problems become fatal.","zh":"有些社會會在問題變得致命前適應、改革或減少壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing that decline is not inevitable.","zh":"顯示衰落並非必然時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"overshadow all other threats","meaning":"令所有其他威脅顯得次要","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe environmental problems overshadow all other threats.","zh":"有些人相信環境問題令所有其他威脅顯得次要。"},{"en":"To overshadow all other threats means to seem more serious or important than every other danger.","zh":"overshadow all other threats 指看起來比所有其他危險更嚴重或更重要。"},{"en":"During an exam week, one urgent assignment may overshadow all other school concerns.","zh":"考試週期間，一份緊急功課可能令其他學校憂慮都顯得次要。"},{"en":"If climate risks feel overwhelming, people may treat them as more urgent than war, disease, or economic problems.","zh":"如果氣候風險感覺壓倒性，人們可能把它視為比戰爭、疾病或經濟問題更迫切。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one danger appears dominant.","zh":"當一個危險看似佔主導時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"global civilisation","meaning":"全球文明","examples":[{"en":"Environmental damage may threaten global civilisation.","zh":"環境破壞可能威脅全球文明。"},{"en":"Global civilisation means the modern worldwide network of societies, economies, technologies, and cultures.","zh":"global civilisation 指現代世界各社會、經濟、科技和文化互相連接的整體網絡。"},{"en":"Air travel, internet communication, trade, and medicine connect today’s global civilisation.","zh":"航空旅遊、網絡通訊、貿易和醫療連接今天的全球文明。"},{"en":"Because the world is connected, problems in one region can affect many others.","zh":"因為世界互相連接，一個地區的問題可以影響許多其他地區。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing humanity as one interconnected system.","zh":"把人類視為一個互相連接的系統來討論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"human-caused climate change","meaning":"人為氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"Human-caused climate change is a major modern environmental problem.","zh":"人為氣候變化是重大現代環境問題。"},{"en":"Human-caused climate change means long-term climate change driven mainly by human activities.","zh":"human-caused climate change 指主要由人類活動推動的長期氣候變化。"},{"en":"Burning coal, oil, and gas can contribute to human-caused climate change.","zh":"燃燒煤、石油和天然氣可以促成人為氣候變化。"},{"en":"Climate change can affect weather, farming, sea levels, health, and migration.","zh":"氣候變化可以影響天氣、農業、海平面、健康和遷徙。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when distinguishing human influence from natural climate variation.","zh":"區分人類影響和自然氣候變動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"buildup of toxic chemicals","meaning":"有毒化學物質的累積","examples":[{"en":"The buildup of toxic chemicals threatens the environment.","zh":"有毒化學物質的累積威脅環境。"},{"en":"Buildup of toxic chemicals means the gradual accumulation of harmful substances in air, water, soil, or living bodies.","zh":"buildup of toxic chemicals 指有害物質在空氣、水、土壤或生物體內逐漸累積。"},{"en":"A lake may suffer when toxic chemicals build up from factory waste and farm runoff.","zh":"如果工廠廢物和農田徑流令有毒化學物質累積，湖泊可能受害。"},{"en":"Chemical buildup can poison wildlife, contaminate food, and harm human health.","zh":"化學物質累積可以毒害野生生物、污染食物並傷害人類健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when pollution increases over time.","zh":"當污染隨時間增加時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"energy shortages","meaning":"能源短缺","examples":[{"en":"Energy shortages may create serious economic and social problems.","zh":"能源短缺可能造成嚴重經濟和社會問題。"},{"en":"Energy shortages happen when there is not enough fuel, electricity, or power to meet demand.","zh":"energy shortages 指燃料、電力或能源不足以滿足需求。"},{"en":"A city may face energy shortages during extreme heat if everyone uses air conditioning at once.","zh":"極端高溫期間，如果所有人同時使用冷氣，城市可能面對能源短缺。"},{"en":"Energy shortages can close factories, raise prices, and disrupt daily life.","zh":"能源短缺可以令工廠停工、價格上升並擾亂日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing resources needed for modern society.","zh":"討論現代社會所需資源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"full human utilisation of","meaning":"人類完全利用……","examples":[{"en":"The author discusses the full human utilisation of the Earth’s photosynthetic capacity.","zh":"作者討論人類完全利用地球光合作用能力。"},{"en":"Full human utilisation of something means humans use nearly all of that resource or capacity.","zh":"full human utilisation of something 指人類幾乎使用某項資源或能力的全部。"},{"en":"A school has full utilisation of its classrooms if every room is used all day.","zh":"如果學校每間課室整天都被使用，就是完全利用課室容量。"},{"en":"When humans use too much of a natural capacity, less remains for other species and ecosystems.","zh":"當人類使用過多自然能力，留給其他物種和生態系統的就更少。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing limits to resource use.","zh":"討論資源使用極限時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"photosynthetic capacity","meaning":"光合作用能力","examples":[{"en":"Human activity increasingly uses the Earth’s photosynthetic capacity.","zh":"人類活動越來越多地使用地球的光合作用能力。"},{"en":"Photosynthetic capacity means the ability of plants and other organisms to use sunlight to produce biological energy.","zh":"photosynthetic capacity 指植物和其他生物利用陽光製造生物能量的能力。"},{"en":"Forests, crops, and algae all contribute to the planet’s photosynthetic capacity.","zh":"森林、農作物和藻類都對地球光合作用能力有貢獻。"},{"en":"If humans claim too much plant production for food, fuel, or land use, ecosystems may be strained.","zh":"如果人類為食物、燃料或土地使用佔用太多植物生產力，生態系統可能承受壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing biological productivity.","zh":"討論生物生產力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the seriousness of","meaning":"……的嚴重程度","examples":[{"en":"The seriousness of current environmental problems is debated.","zh":"當前環境問題的嚴重程度受到爭論。"},{"en":"The seriousness of something means how severe, dangerous, or important it is.","zh":"seriousness of something 指某事有多嚴重、危險或重要。"},{"en":"A doctor must judge the seriousness of a patient’s symptoms before deciding treatment.","zh":"醫生必須判斷病人症狀的嚴重程度，然後決定治療。"},{"en":"People may disagree about seriousness when evidence is complex or future effects are uncertain.","zh":"當證據複雜或未來影響不確定，人們可能對嚴重程度意見不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evaluating risk.","zh":"評估風險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be vigorously debated","meaning":"被激烈爭論","examples":[{"en":"The risks posed by environmental problems are vigorously debated.","zh":"環境問題構成的風險被激烈爭論。"},{"en":"Be vigorously debated means be discussed with strong disagreement, energy, and argument.","zh":"be vigorously debated 指被有力、激烈且帶有強烈分歧地討論。"},{"en":"School phone bans are vigorously debated when parents, teachers, and students hold different views.","zh":"當家長、老師和學生有不同看法，校園手機禁令會被激烈爭論。"},{"en":"Debate becomes vigorous when the issue affects many people and evidence is contested.","zh":"當議題影響許多人且證據有爭議，辯論就會變得激烈。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when disagreement is active and serious.","zh":"當分歧活躍而嚴肅時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"greatly exaggerated","meaning":"被大幅誇大","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe environmental risks are greatly exaggerated.","zh":"有些人認為環境風險被大幅誇大。"},{"en":"Greatly exaggerated means described as much larger, worse, or more serious than it really is.","zh":"greatly exaggerated 指被描述得比實際大、差或嚴重得多。"},{"en":"A student may say a test was impossible, but that may be greatly exaggerated if most classmates passed.","zh":"學生可能說測驗不可能完成，但如果大多數同學合格，這說法可能被大幅誇大。"},{"en":"People who think risks are exaggerated may resist costly action.","zh":"認為風險被誇大的人，可能反對昂貴行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when questioning whether a claim is overstated.","zh":"質疑某說法是否過度誇張時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"conversely","meaning":"相反地","examples":[{"en":"Some consider the risks exaggerated; conversely, others think they are underestimated.","zh":"有些人認為風險被誇大；相反地，另一些人認為風險被低估。"},{"en":"Conversely means in the opposite way or from the opposite point of view.","zh":"conversely 指以相反方式或從相反觀點來看。"},{"en":"Some students prefer group study; conversely, others concentrate better alone.","zh":"有些學生喜歡小組溫習；相反地，另一些學生獨自學習時更專注。"},{"en":"This word helps present a contrasting opinion clearly.","zh":"這個詞幫助清楚呈現相反意見。"},{"en":"It is useful when two views point in opposite directions.","zh":"當兩種觀點方向相反時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be underestimated","meaning":"被低估","examples":[{"en":"The dangers of environmental damage may be underestimated.","zh":"環境破壞的危險可能被低估。"},{"en":"Be underestimated means be judged as less serious, strong, or important than it really is.","zh":"be underestimated 指被判斷得比實際較不嚴重、較不強或較不重要。"},{"en":"A quiet student’s ability may be underestimated if teachers only notice outspoken classmates.","zh":"如果老師只注意健談同學，安靜學生的能力可能被低估。"},{"en":"Underestimated risks can become dangerous because people prepare too little.","zh":"被低估的風險可能變危險，因為人們準備太少。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when hidden danger is not taken seriously enough.","zh":"當隱藏危險沒有被充分重視時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"solve our problems","meaning":"解決我們的問題","examples":[{"en":"Some people expect modern technology to solve our problems.","zh":"有些人期望現代科技能解決我們的問題。"},{"en":"To solve our problems means to find effective answers to difficulties we face.","zh":"solve our problems 指為我們面對的困難找到有效答案。"},{"en":"A school may use tutoring to solve students’ reading problems.","zh":"學校可能使用補習來解決學生閱讀問題。"},{"en":"Technology can solve some problems, but it may not fix poor decisions or unfair systems.","zh":"科技可以解決某些問題，但未必能修正糟糕決策或不公平制度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing practical answers to difficulties.","zh":"討論困難的實際答案時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"create new problems faster than","meaning":"製造新問題的速度比……更快","examples":[{"en":"Technology may create new problems faster than it solves old ones.","zh":"科技製造新問題的速度可能比解決舊問題更快。"},{"en":"Create new problems faster than means produce new difficulties at a higher speed than existing problems are fixed.","zh":"create new problems faster than 指產生新困難的速度比修正現有問題更高。"},{"en":"A school app may create new problems faster than it solves old ones if it confuses parents and teachers.","zh":"如果學校應用程式令家長和老師困惑，它製造新問題的速度可能比解決舊問題更快。"},{"en":"Solutions can backfire when people ignore side effects.","zh":"當人們忽視副作用，解決方案可能適得其反。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when progress has hidden costs.","zh":"當進步有隱藏成本時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"deplete a resource","meaning":"耗盡資源","examples":[{"en":"Human activity can deplete a natural resource.","zh":"人類活動可以耗盡自然資源。"},{"en":"To deplete a resource means to use it up until little remains.","zh":"deplete a resource 指把資源用到所剩無幾。"},{"en":"A village may deplete a forest if it cuts trees faster than new ones grow.","zh":"如果村莊砍樹速度快於新樹生長，就可能耗盡森林資源。"},{"en":"Depleted resources can cause shortages, higher prices, and conflict.","zh":"資源耗盡可以造成短缺、價格上升和衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing overuse.","zh":"討論過度使用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"count on being able to","meaning":"指望能夠……","examples":[{"en":"We cannot always count on being able to replace a depleted resource.","zh":"我們不能總是指望能夠取代已耗盡的資源。"},{"en":"Count on being able to means depend confidently on having the ability to do something.","zh":"count on being able to 指有信心地依賴自己能做某事。"},{"en":"A student should not count on being able to finish a project in one night if it needs research.","zh":"如果專題需要研究，學生不應指望能夠一晚完成。"},{"en":"If replacement is uncertain, using resources carelessly becomes risky.","zh":"如果替代方案不確定，隨意使用資源就會變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when warning against overconfidence.","zh":"警告不要過度自信時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"substitute a new resource","meaning":"以新資源取代","examples":[{"en":"Societies may try to substitute a new resource for one that has been depleted.","zh":"社會可能嘗試以新資源取代已耗盡的資源。"},{"en":"To substitute a new resource means to use a different resource in place of the old one.","zh":"substitute a new resource 指使用不同資源來代替舊資源。"},{"en":"A family may substitute solar power for expensive electricity from the grid.","zh":"家庭可能以太陽能取代昂貴的電網電力。"},{"en":"Substitution works only if the new resource is available, affordable, and suitable.","zh":"替代只有在新資源可取得、可負擔且合適時才有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing replacement.","zh":"討論替代時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"farmed fish","meaning":"養殖魚","examples":[{"en":"Farmed fish may be used as an alternative to wild ocean fish.","zh":"養殖魚可以作為野生海魚的替代品。"},{"en":"Farmed fish are fish raised in controlled ponds, tanks, or sea farms rather than caught in the wild.","zh":"farmed fish 指在受控制魚塘、水箱或海上養殖場飼養，而不是在野外捕捉的魚。"},{"en":"Supermarkets may sell farmed fish when wild fish supplies become limited.","zh":"當野生魚供應有限，超級市場可能售賣養殖魚。"},{"en":"Fish farming can reduce pressure on wild stocks, but it can also create pollution or disease risks.","zh":"養魚可以減少對野生魚群的壓力，但也可能帶來污染或疾病風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing food supply and resource substitution.","zh":"討論食物供應和資源替代時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the rate of population growth","meaning":"人口增長率","examples":[{"en":"The rate of human population growth has begun to decline.","zh":"人類人口增長率已開始下降。"},{"en":"The rate of population growth means how quickly the number of people is increasing.","zh":"rate of population growth 指人口數量增加得有多快。"},{"en":"A city’s population may still grow even if the rate of population growth slows down.","zh":"即使人口增長率放慢，城市人口仍可能繼續增加。"},{"en":"Slower growth can reduce future pressure on housing, food, schools, and healthcare.","zh":"較慢增長可以減少未來對住屋、食物、學校和醫療的壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing demographic trends.","zh":"討論人口趨勢時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be on course for","meaning":"正朝着……發展","examples":[{"en":"The world may be on course for its population to stabilise.","zh":"世界人口可能正朝着穩定下來的方向發展。"},{"en":"Be on course for something means be moving toward a likely future result.","zh":"be on course for something 指正朝着某個可能的未來結果前進。"},{"en":"A student who revises daily is on course for better exam performance.","zh":"每天溫習的學生正朝着更好考試表現發展。"},{"en":"Current trends can suggest where a situation is heading, though they do not guarantee the outcome.","zh":"當前趨勢可以暗示情況走向，但不保證結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when predicting a future direction.","zh":"預測未來方向時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"level off at","meaning":"在……水平趨於穩定","examples":[{"en":"The population may eventually level off at a manageable figure.","zh":"人口最終可能在一個可控制的數字水平趨於穩定。"},{"en":"To level off at a number means to stop rising or falling and become stable at that level.","zh":"level off at a number 指停止上升或下降，並在該水平穩定下來。"},{"en":"A student’s stress may level off after exams end and the timetable becomes calmer.","zh":"考試結束且時間表變得較平靜後，學生壓力可能趨於穩定。"},{"en":"When population levels off, pressure may become easier to plan for.","zh":"當人口趨於穩定，壓力可能較容易規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when growth slows and becomes stable.","zh":"當增長放慢並變穩定時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a manageable number","meaning":"可控制的數目","examples":[{"en":"Some people expect the population to stabilise at a manageable number.","zh":"有些人預期人口會穩定在一個可控制的數目。"},{"en":"A manageable number is a number that can be controlled, supported, or dealt with successfully.","zh":"manageable number 指可以被控制、支援或成功處理的數量。"},{"en":"A class of twenty students may be a manageable number for one teacher.","zh":"對一位老師來說，二十人的班級可能是可控制的數目。"},{"en":"If a population is manageable, food, housing, water, and services may be easier to provide.","zh":"如果人口數目可控制，食物、住屋、水和服務可能較容易提供。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing whether a level is practical.","zh":"討論某水平是否實際可行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"questions like these","meaning":"這類問題","examples":[{"en":"Questions like these reveal the complexity of environmental debate.","zh":"這類問題揭示環境爭論的複雜性。"},{"en":"Questions like these means this kind of question or similar questions.","zh":"questions like these 指這種類型或相似的問題。"},{"en":"Questions like these often arise when students compare safety, cost, and fairness in school rules.","zh":"當學生比較校規中的安全、成本和公平時，這類問題常會出現。"},{"en":"Difficult questions show that a topic may not have one simple answer.","zh":"困難問題顯示一個主題可能沒有單一簡單答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when referring back to several issues just mentioned.","zh":"回指剛提到的幾個議題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"illustrate why","meaning":"說明為何……","examples":[{"en":"These questions illustrate why past collapses remain relevant.","zh":"這些問題說明為何過去的崩潰仍然相關。"},{"en":"To illustrate why means to show or make clear the reason for something.","zh":"illustrate why 指顯示或清楚說明某事的原因。"},{"en":"A failed group project can illustrate why clear roles matter.","zh":"失敗的小組專題可以說明為何清晰角色很重要。"},{"en":"Examples help readers understand reasons more concretely than explanation alone.","zh":"例子比單靠解釋更具體地幫助讀者理解原因。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence explains importance.","zh":"當證據解釋重要性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take on more meaning than","meaning":"具有超越……的意義","examples":[{"en":"Past collapses have taken on more meaning than that of a romantic mystery.","zh":"過去的崩潰具有超越浪漫神秘感的意義。"},{"en":"To take on more meaning than something means to become more significant than that earlier or simpler idea.","zh":"take on more meaning than something 指變得比原先或較簡單的想法更有意義。"},{"en":"A family photo may take on more meaning than decoration after a grandparent dies.","zh":"祖父母去世後，家庭照片可能具有超越裝飾的意義。"},{"en":"Ancient ruins become more than beautiful objects when they offer warnings for today.","zh":"當古代遺址為今天提供警示，它們就不只是美麗物件。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something gains deeper importance.","zh":"當某事物獲得更深重要性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a romantic mystery","meaning":"浪漫而神秘的事物","examples":[{"en":"Ancient ruins represent more than a romantic mystery.","zh":"古代遺址代表的不只是浪漫而神秘的事物。"},{"en":"A romantic mystery is something attractive, emotional, and mysterious, but not necessarily practical.","zh":"romantic mystery 指吸引人、帶情感和神秘感，但未必實用的事物。"},{"en":"An old abandoned house may seem like a romantic mystery to children who imagine stories about it.","zh":"一間廢棄舊屋對想像故事的孩子來說，可能像浪漫而神秘的事物。"},{"en":"Ruins may feel mysterious and beautiful, but they can also teach practical lessons.","zh":"遺址可能感覺神秘而美麗，但也可以教人實際教訓。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when beauty and mystery are not the whole meaning.","zh":"當美感和神秘感不是全部意義時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"practical lessons","meaning":"實際教訓","examples":[{"en":"Past collapses may offer practical lessons for modern societies.","zh":"過去的崩潰可能為現代社會提供實際教訓。"},{"en":"Practical lessons are useful ideas that can guide real decisions and actions.","zh":"practical lessons 指能指導真實決策和行動的有用想法。"},{"en":"A failed school event may offer practical lessons about planning, timing, and communication.","zh":"失敗的學校活動可能提供關於規劃、時間和溝通的實際教訓。"},{"en":"Lessons are practical when they help people avoid mistakes or improve results.","zh":"當教訓能幫助人避免錯誤或改善結果，它就是實際的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when history has real-world value.","zh":"當歷史具有現實價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"learn from past collapses","meaning":"從過去的崩潰中學習","examples":[{"en":"Modern societies may learn from past collapses.","zh":"現代社會可能從過去的崩潰中學習。"},{"en":"To learn from past collapses means to study earlier societal failures and use the knowledge to avoid similar mistakes.","zh":"learn from past collapses 指研究早期社會失敗，並利用這些知識避免類似錯誤。"},{"en":"A city may learn from past flood disasters by improving drainage and warning systems.","zh":"城市可能從過去水災中學習，改善排水和警報系統。"},{"en":"Learning from collapse requires honest attention to causes, not just admiration for ruins.","zh":"從崩潰中學習需要誠實注意原因，而不只是欣賞遺址。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when past failures can guide present prevention.","zh":"當過去失敗能指導現在預防時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"differences between","meaning":"……之間的差異","examples":[{"en":"There are important differences between modern and past societies.","zh":"現代社會和過去社會之間有重要差異。"},{"en":"Differences between two things are the ways in which they are not the same.","zh":"differences between two things 指兩者不同之處。"},{"en":"Students may notice differences between online lessons and face-to-face lessons.","zh":"學生可能注意到網上課堂和面授課堂之間的差異。"},{"en":"Recognising differences prevents people from applying old lessons too directly.","zh":"承認差異可以防止人們過於直接地套用舊教訓。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparison requires caution.","zh":"當比較需要謹慎時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be so naive as to think","meaning":"天真得以為……","examples":[{"en":"We should not be so naive as to think that history provides simple answers.","zh":"我們不應天真得以為歷史會提供簡單答案。"},{"en":"Be so naive as to think means be too innocent or unrealistic in believing something.","zh":"be so naive as to think 指過於天真或不現實地相信某事。"},{"en":"We should not be so naive as to think one extra lesson will solve every learning problem.","zh":"我們不應天真得以為多上一堂課就能解決所有學習問題。"},{"en":"Complex problems rarely have simple answers, even when history offers useful warnings.","zh":"複雜問題很少有簡單答案，即使歷史提供有用警示。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when criticising an over-simple belief.","zh":"批評過度簡化的信念時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the study of the past","meaning":"對歷史的研究","examples":[{"en":"The study of the past can help us understand present risks.","zh":"對歷史的研究可以幫助我們理解當前風險。"},{"en":"The study of the past means examining history, evidence, events, and earlier societies.","zh":"study of the past 指檢視歷史、證據、事件和早期社會。"},{"en":"Students study the past through books, photographs, maps, ruins, and personal stories.","zh":"學生透過書籍、照片、地圖、遺址和個人故事研究過去。"},{"en":"Understanding the past can show how present problems developed over time.","zh":"理解過去可以顯示當前問題如何隨時間形成。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when history helps explain the present.","zh":"當歷史有助解釋現在時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"yield simple solutions","meaning":"產生簡單的解決方法","examples":[{"en":"The study of history will not yield simple solutions to modern problems.","zh":"歷史研究不會為現代問題產生簡單解決方法。"},{"en":"To yield simple solutions means to produce easy answers or fixes.","zh":"yield simple solutions 指產生容易的答案或修正方法。"},{"en":"A survey may not yield simple solutions if students are stressed for many different reasons.","zh":"如果學生因許多不同原因感到壓力，問卷未必能產生簡單解決方法。"},{"en":"Historical study can guide thinking, but modern problems may require new policies and careful adaptation.","zh":"歷史研究可以指導思考，但現代問題可能需要新政策和謹慎調整。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when results are helpful but not easy.","zh":"當結果有幫助但並不簡單時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"directly transferable to","meaning":"可直接套用於……","examples":[{"en":"Historical solutions are not always directly transferable to modern societies.","zh":"歷史解決方法不總是可直接套用於現代社會。"},{"en":"Directly transferable to means able to be moved or applied to another situation without major changes.","zh":"directly transferable to 指能不經重大改變地轉移或應用到另一情況。"},{"en":"A teaching method that works for adults may not be directly transferable to young children.","zh":"適用於成人的教學方法未必可直接套用於幼童。"},{"en":"Different conditions require adaptation before a lesson can be used safely.","zh":"不同條件需要調整，教訓才能安全使用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when warning that copying may not work.","zh":"警告不可盲目複製時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"differ from past societies","meaning":"與過去的社會不同","examples":[{"en":"Modern societies differ from past societies in several respects.","zh":"現代社會在幾方面與過去的社會不同。"},{"en":"Differ from past societies means be unlike earlier societies in important ways.","zh":"differ from past societies 指在重要方面不同於早期社會。"},{"en":"Modern schools differ from past schools because technology, exams, and student needs have changed.","zh":"現代學校與過去學校不同，因為科技、考試和學生需要已經改變。"},{"en":"Differences in population, medicine, trade, and technology change the risks societies face.","zh":"人口、醫療、貿易和科技差異會改變社會面對的風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing past and present.","zh":"比較過去和現在時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in some respects","meaning":"在某些方面","examples":[{"en":"In some respects, modern societies face lower risks.","zh":"在某些方面，現代社會面對較低風險。"},{"en":"In some respects means in some ways or from certain points of view.","zh":"in some respects 指在某些方面或從某些角度來看。"},{"en":"In some respects, online lessons are convenient, but they may reduce classroom interaction.","zh":"在某些方面，網上課堂很方便，但它們可能減少課堂互動。"},{"en":"This phrase allows a balanced argument because it avoids saying something is entirely good or bad.","zh":"這個短語讓論點更平衡，因為它避免說某事完全好或壞。"},{"en":"It is useful when only part of a comparison is true.","zh":"當比較只在部分情況成立時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"put someone at lower risk","meaning":"令某人面對較低風險","examples":[{"en":"Modern medicine may put us at lower risk than past societies.","zh":"現代醫學可能令我們面對比過去社會較低的風險。"},{"en":"Put someone at lower risk means make someone less likely to suffer harm or danger.","zh":"put someone at lower risk 指令某人較不可能遭受傷害或危險。"},{"en":"Seat belts put drivers at lower risk during car accidents.","zh":"安全帶令司機在車禍中面對較低風險。"},{"en":"Better healthcare can reduce deaths from diseases that once destroyed communities.","zh":"更好的醫療可以減少曾經摧毀社群的疾病死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something improves safety.","zh":"當某事提高安全性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"beneficial effects","meaning":"有利影響","examples":[{"en":"Powerful technology can have beneficial effects.","zh":"強大的科技可以有有利影響。"},{"en":"Beneficial effects are helpful or positive results.","zh":"beneficial effects 指有幫助或正面的結果。"},{"en":"Regular exercise has beneficial effects on sleep, mood, and heart health.","zh":"定期運動對睡眠、情緒和心臟健康有有利影響。"},{"en":"Technology can improve farming, communication, medicine, and disaster warning systems.","zh":"科技可以改善農業、溝通、醫療和災害警報系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing advantages.","zh":"討論優點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"greater knowledge of","meaning":"對……有更深入認識","examples":[{"en":"We have greater knowledge of past and distant societies.","zh":"我們對過去和遠方社會有更深入認識。"},{"en":"Greater knowledge of something means deeper or wider understanding of it than before.","zh":"greater knowledge of something 指比以前更深入或更廣泛地理解某事。"},{"en":"Students gain greater knowledge of grammar when they see many clear examples.","zh":"學生看到許多清楚例子時，會對文法有更深入認識。"},{"en":"More knowledge helps people compare cases and avoid simple assumptions.","zh":"更多知識幫助人們比較個案並避免簡單假設。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when learning or research improves understanding.","zh":"當學習或研究改善理解時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"put someone at greater risk","meaning":"令某人面對較高風險","examples":[{"en":"Some features of modern life put us at greater risk.","zh":"現代生活的某些特徵令我們面對較高風險。"},{"en":"Put someone at greater risk means make someone more likely to face harm, failure, or danger.","zh":"put someone at greater risk 指令某人更可能面對傷害、失敗或危險。"},{"en":"Driving while tired puts passengers at greater risk of accidents.","zh":"疲勞駕駛令乘客面對較高車禍風險。"},{"en":"Powerful technology can increase risk if its destructive effects are not controlled.","zh":"如果強大科技的破壞性影響未被控制，它可以增加風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a factor makes danger more likely.","zh":"當某因素令危險更可能發生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"potent technology","meaning":"強大而具影響力的技術","examples":[{"en":"Potent technology can cause enormous unintended damage.","zh":"強大而具影響力的技術可以造成巨大非蓄意破壞。"},{"en":"Potent technology is powerful technology that can produce strong effects.","zh":"potent technology 指能產生強大影響的科技。"},{"en":"Artificial intelligence is potent technology because it can change work, learning, and communication quickly.","zh":"人工智能是強大而具影響力的技術，因為它能迅速改變工作、學習和溝通。"},{"en":"Powerful tools can help society, but they can also magnify mistakes.","zh":"強大工具可以幫助社會，但也可以放大錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when technology is both useful and risky.","zh":"當科技既有用又有風險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"unintended destructive effects","meaning":"非蓄意的破壞性影響","examples":[{"en":"Modern technology may have unintended destructive effects.","zh":"現代科技可能有非蓄意的破壞性影響。"},{"en":"Unintended destructive effects are harmful results that people did not plan or expect.","zh":"unintended destructive effects 指人們沒有計劃或預期的有害結果。"},{"en":"A new road may have unintended destructive effects if it cuts through a quiet neighbourhood.","zh":"如果新道路穿過安靜社區，可能帶來非蓄意的破壞性影響。"},{"en":"Even helpful inventions can create damage when their wider consequences are ignored.","zh":"即使有用的發明，在其更廣泛後果被忽視時也可能造成損害。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when good intentions lead to harmful outcomes.","zh":"當好意導致有害結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"such that","meaning":"以致；因而","examples":[{"en":"Globalisation connects societies such that a local problem can spread worldwide.","zh":"全球化把社會連接起來，以致本地問題可以擴散到全世界。"},{"en":"Such that means in a way that produces a particular result.","zh":"such that 指以某種方式造成特定結果。"},{"en":"The timetable was arranged such that students had a short break after every long lesson.","zh":"時間表被安排成每節長課後學生都有短休息。"},{"en":"When systems are tightly connected, one failure can affect many other parts.","zh":"當系統緊密連接，一處失敗可以影響許多其他部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how one condition leads to a result.","zh":"解釋一種條件如何導致結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"affect all the rest","meaning":"影響其餘所有地區","examples":[{"en":"A problem in one part of the world may affect all the rest.","zh":"世界某一地區的問題可能影響其餘所有地區。"},{"en":"Affect all the rest means influence all other people, places, or parts in the system.","zh":"affect all the rest 指影響系統中所有其他人、地方或部分。"},{"en":"If one teacher changes the exam date, it may affect all the rest of the class schedule.","zh":"如果一位老師更改考試日期，可能影響整個課程表其餘部分。"},{"en":"In a connected world, local problems can spread through trade, travel, finance, or climate systems.","zh":"在互相連接的世界中，本地問題可以透過貿易、旅遊、金融或氣候系統擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one part of a system influences everything else.","zh":"當系統一部分影響其他所有部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"dependence on","meaning":"對……的依賴","examples":[{"en":"Millions of people have a strong dependence on modern medicine.","zh":"數以百萬計的人對現代醫學有強烈依賴。"},{"en":"Dependence on something means needing it in order to function, survive, or live normally.","zh":"dependence on something 指需要某物才能運作、生存或正常生活。"},{"en":"A student may develop dependence on a dictionary if they never try to guess meaning from context.","zh":"如果學生從不嘗試根據語境猜意思，可能對字典產生依賴。"},{"en":"Dependence can become risky if the system people rely on fails.","zh":"如果人們依賴的系統失效，依賴就可能變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when people need something strongly.","zh":"當人們強烈需要某物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"for our survival","meaning":"為了維持生存","examples":[{"en":"Many people depend on modern medicine for their survival.","zh":"許多人為了維持生存而依賴現代醫學。"},{"en":"For our survival means in order for us to stay alive.","zh":"for our survival 指為了讓我們活下去。"},{"en":"Clean water is necessary for our survival because the body cannot function without it.","zh":"清潔食水對我們生存是必要的，因為身體不能在沒有水下運作。"},{"en":"If a society depends on one system for survival, failure of that system can be dangerous.","zh":"如果社會為維持生存而依賴單一系統，該系統失效就可能很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is essential to life.","zh":"當某物對生命必不可少時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"much larger human population","meaning":"大得多的人口","examples":[{"en":"The modern world has a much larger human population.","zh":"現代世界擁有大得多的人口。"},{"en":"Much larger human population means far more people than in an earlier period or comparison group.","zh":"much larger human population 指人數遠多於較早時期或比較對象。"},{"en":"A city with a much larger population needs more schools, hospitals, transport, and housing.","zh":"人口大得多的城市需要更多學校、醫院、交通和住屋。"},{"en":"More people can increase resource pressure even when technology improves.","zh":"即使科技改善，更多人口仍可增加資源壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when population size changes risk and planning.","zh":"當人口規模改變風險和規劃時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"only if","meaning":"只有在……的情況下","examples":[{"en":"We can learn from the past only if we examine it carefully.","zh":"只有在仔細檢視歷史的情況下，我們才能從過去學習。"},{"en":"Only if means something will happen on the condition that another thing happens first.","zh":"only if 指只有在另一件事先發生的條件下，某事才會發生。"},{"en":"A student can improve only if they practise regularly and correct their mistakes.","zh":"學生只有在定期練習並改正錯誤的情況下才能進步。"},{"en":"Lessons from history are useful only when people study them honestly and carefully.","zh":"只有當人們誠實而仔細地研究歷史，歷史教訓才有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stating a necessary condition.","zh":"說明必要條件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"think carefully about","meaning":"仔細思考……","examples":[{"en":"We must think carefully about the lessons of history.","zh":"我們必須仔細思考歷史教訓。"},{"en":"To think carefully about something means to consider it slowly, seriously, and with attention to detail.","zh":"think carefully about something 指慢慢、認真並注意細節地考慮某事。"},{"en":"Students should think carefully about a question before choosing an answer.","zh":"學生選答案前應仔細思考問題。"},{"en":"Careful thinking helps people avoid simple conclusions and emotional reactions.","zh":"仔細思考幫助人們避免簡單結論和情緒反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a topic is complex or important.","zh":"當主題複雜或重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"describe the impact of","meaning":"描述……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The question asks the writer to describe the impact of monumental ruins.","zh":"題目要求作者描述宏偉遺址的影響。"},{"en":"To describe the impact of something means to explain the effect it has on people, places, or ideas.","zh":"describe the impact of something 指解釋某事對人、地方或想法造成的影響。"},{"en":"A student may describe the impact of social media on teenagers’ sleep and confidence.","zh":"學生可能描述社交媒體對青少年睡眠和信心的影響。"},{"en":"Describing impact requires more than naming the thing; it explains what changes because of it.","zh":"描述影響不只是命名事物；它要解釋因它而出現甚麼改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in essay and reading questions.","zh":"這個短語適用於文章和閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"emphasise","meaning":"強調","examples":[{"en":"The writer emphasises the emotional appeal of ancient ruins.","zh":"作者強調古代遺址的情感吸引力。"},{"en":"To emphasise something means to give it special importance or attention.","zh":"emphasise something 指特別重視或突出某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may emphasise planning before students start writing an essay.","zh":"老師可能在學生開始寫文章前強調規劃。"},{"en":"Emphasis guides readers toward what the writer thinks matters most.","zh":"強調會引導讀者注意作者認為最重要的地方。"},{"en":"This word is useful when identifying a writer’s focus.","zh":"辨認作者焦點時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"generate income from tourism","meaning":"從旅遊業帶來收入","examples":[{"en":"Historic sites can generate income from tourism.","zh":"歷史地點可以從旅遊業帶來收入。"},{"en":"To generate income from tourism means to earn money when visitors pay for travel, tickets, food, hotels, or services.","zh":"generate income from tourism 指透過遊客支付旅費、門票、食物、酒店或服務來賺錢。"},{"en":"A small town may generate income from tourism if people visit its old temples.","zh":"如果人們參觀小鎮的古寺，小鎮可能從旅遊業帶來收入。"},{"en":"Tourism income can support local jobs, but it may also create crowding or pressure on heritage sites.","zh":"旅遊收入可以支持本地工作，但也可能造成擁擠或對遺產地點造成壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the economic value of attractions.","zh":"討論景點的經濟價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"occupy an area of land","meaning":"佔用一片土地","examples":[{"en":"Monumental ruins may occupy a large area of land.","zh":"宏偉遺址可能佔用一大片土地。"},{"en":"To occupy an area of land means to cover, use, or take up that space.","zh":"occupy an area of land 指覆蓋、使用或佔據某片空間。"},{"en":"A school campus may occupy an area of land that includes classrooms, playgrounds, and gardens.","zh":"學校校園可能佔用一片包含課室、操場和花園的土地。"},{"en":"Large ruins require space, so they can affect modern planning and conservation.","zh":"大型遺址需要空間，因此可以影響現代規劃和保育。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the physical size of a site.","zh":"描述地點實際面積時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"archaeological value","meaning":"考古價值","examples":[{"en":"Ancient ruins may have considerable archaeological value.","zh":"古代遺址可能有相當大的考古價值。"},{"en":"Archaeological value means importance for understanding human history through physical evidence.","zh":"archaeological value 指透過實體證據理解人類歷史的重要性。"},{"en":"Broken pots in an old village may have archaeological value because they show how people cooked and traded.","zh":"舊村莊中的破陶器可能有考古價值，因為它們顯示人們如何煮食和貿易。"},{"en":"A site with archaeological value should be protected before construction damages it.","zh":"有考古價值的地點應在施工破壞前受到保護。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why old remains matter.","zh":"解釋古老遺存為何重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"romantic appeal","meaning":"浪漫吸引力","examples":[{"en":"The ruins have a strong romantic appeal for modern visitors.","zh":"這些遺址對現代遊客有強烈浪漫吸引力。"},{"en":"Romantic appeal means emotional attraction created by beauty, mystery, history, or imagination.","zh":"romantic appeal 指由美、神秘、歷史或想像創造的情感吸引。"},{"en":"An old railway station may have romantic appeal because people imagine past journeys there.","zh":"舊火車站可能有浪漫吸引力，因為人們想像過去旅程。"},{"en":"Romantic appeal can attract tourists even before they understand the historical details.","zh":"即使遊客尚未理解歷史細節，浪漫吸引力也可以吸引他們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a place feels beautiful and mysterious.","zh":"當地方感覺美麗而神秘時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"recent findings concerning","meaning":"有關……的近期研究發現","examples":[{"en":"Recent findings concerning vanished civilisations support the ecological theory.","zh":"有關已消失文明的近期研究發現支持生態理論。"},{"en":"Recent findings concerning something are new discoveries or evidence about that topic.","zh":"recent findings concerning something 指關於某主題的新發現或證據。"},{"en":"Recent findings concerning student sleep may change how schools design timetables.","zh":"有關學生睡眠的近期研究發現可能改變學校如何設計時間表。"},{"en":"New findings can strengthen, weaken, or revise older explanations.","zh":"新發現可以加強、削弱或修正舊解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research updates understanding.","zh":"當研究更新理解時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"vanished civilisations","meaning":"已消失的文明","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have studied many vanished civilisations.","zh":"研究人員研究了許多已消失的文明。"},{"en":"Vanished civilisations are societies that once existed but later disappeared or lost their organised form.","zh":"vanished civilisations 指曾經存在但後來消失或失去組織形式的社會。"},{"en":"Students may learn about vanished civilisations through ruins, artefacts, and old writings.","zh":"學生可能透過遺址、文物和古老文字了解已消失的文明。"},{"en":"Studying vanished civilisations helps people ask why complex societies fail.","zh":"研究已消失的文明幫助人們思考複雜社會為何失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing lost societies of the past.","zh":"討論過去失落社會時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"overturn long-held beliefs","meaning":"推翻長久以來的觀念","examples":[{"en":"New evidence can overturn long-held beliefs.","zh":"新證據可以推翻長久以來的觀念。"},{"en":"To overturn long-held beliefs means to show that ideas believed for a long time are wrong or incomplete.","zh":"overturn long-held beliefs 指顯示長時間被相信的想法錯誤或不完整。"},{"en":"A new medical study may overturn long-held beliefs about diet and heart health.","zh":"新醫學研究可能推翻長久以來關於飲食和心臟健康的觀念。"},{"en":"Strong evidence can change what experts and the public accept as true.","zh":"強而有力的證據可以改變專家和公眾接受為真的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when new findings challenge old assumptions.","zh":"當新發現挑戰舊假設時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cause controversy amongst","meaning":"在……之間引起爭議","examples":[{"en":"The findings did not necessarily cause controversy amongst scientists.","zh":"這些發現不一定在科學家之間引起爭議。"},{"en":"To cause controversy amongst a group means to create disagreement or debate within that group.","zh":"cause controversy amongst a group 指在某群體內造成分歧或辯論。"},{"en":"A new homework policy may cause controversy amongst parents if some think it is too demanding.","zh":"如果部分家長認為新功課政策要求太高，它可能在家長之間引起爭議。"},{"en":"Controversy appears when evidence or values are interpreted differently.","zh":"當證據或價值觀被不同解讀時，爭議就會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a claim leads to disagreement.","zh":"當某說法引發分歧時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a variety of disciplines","meaning":"多個不同學科","examples":[{"en":"The discoveries came from a variety of academic disciplines.","zh":"這些發現來自多個不同學科。"},{"en":"A variety of disciplines means several different fields of study or expertise.","zh":"variety of disciplines 指幾個不同研究領域或專業範疇。"},{"en":"A project about climate may use a variety of disciplines, including science, geography, economics, and politics.","zh":"關於氣候的專題可能使用多個不同學科，包括科學、地理、經濟和政治。"},{"en":"Complex problems often require evidence from more than one field.","zh":"複雜問題常需要來自多於一個領域的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when knowledge comes from several areas.","zh":"當知識來自幾個範疇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"identify one main cause","meaning":"找出一個主要成因","examples":[{"en":"The researchers did not identify one main cause of every collapse.","zh":"研究人員沒有找出每次崩潰的一個主要成因。"},{"en":"To identify one main cause means to find a single most important reason for something.","zh":"identify one main cause 指找出某事的單一最重要原因。"},{"en":"A teacher may not identify one main cause of weak writing because grammar, vocabulary, and planning all matter.","zh":"老師可能無法找出寫作薄弱的一個主要成因，因為文法、詞彙和規劃都重要。"},{"en":"When many factors interact, searching for one cause can oversimplify the problem.","zh":"當許多因素互動，尋找一個原因可能會過度簡化問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining complex causation.","zh":"解釋複雜因果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"environmental damage","meaning":"環境破壞","examples":[{"en":"Environmental damage contributed to the decline of some societies.","zh":"環境破壞促成一些社會的衰落。"},{"en":"Environmental damage means harm done to natural systems such as forests, soil, rivers, animals, or climate.","zh":"environmental damage 指對森林、土壤、河流、動物或氣候等自然系統造成的傷害。"},{"en":"A town may suffer environmental damage if factories pollute its river.","zh":"如果工廠污染河流，城鎮可能遭受環境破壞。"},{"en":"Damaged environments can reduce food, health, income, and long-term security.","zh":"受破壞環境可以減少食物、健康、收入和長期安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when nature is harmed by human activity or disaster.","zh":"當自然因人類活動或災難而受害時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the ways in which","meaning":"……的方式","examples":[{"en":"The question concerns the ways in which former societies collapsed.","zh":"題目涉及過去社會崩潰的方式。"},{"en":"The ways in which means the methods, patterns, or processes by which something happens.","zh":"ways in which 指某事發生的方法、模式或過程。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask about the ways in which students prepare for exams.","zh":"老師可能詢問學生備考的方式。"},{"en":"Looking at different ways helps avoid assuming that all cases are the same.","zh":"觀察不同方式有助避免假設所有個案都相同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when analysing processes.","zh":"分析過程時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"former societies","meaning":"過去的社會","examples":[{"en":"Former societies collapsed at different rates and to different degrees.","zh":"過去的社會以不同速度和不同程度崩潰。"},{"en":"Former societies are societies that existed in the past but no longer exist in the same form.","zh":"former societies 指過去存在但不再以同一形式存在的社會。"},{"en":"Students compare former societies with modern societies to understand change over time.","zh":"學生比較過去社會和現代社會，以理解隨時間發生的變化。"},{"en":"Studying former societies can reveal both human achievement and human vulnerability.","zh":"研究過去的社會可以揭示人類成就和人類脆弱性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing historical communities.","zh":"討論歷史社群時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the pace of decline","meaning":"衰退速度","examples":[{"en":"The pace of decline varied among past civilisations.","zh":"衰退速度在過去文明之間有所不同。"},{"en":"The pace of decline means how quickly weakening or collapse happens.","zh":"pace of decline 指衰弱或崩潰發生得有多快。"},{"en":"A shop’s pace of decline may be slow if customers leave gradually over several years.","zh":"如果顧客在幾年間逐漸離開，商店衰退速度可能很慢。"},{"en":"Fast decline can shock people, while slow decline may be easier to ignore.","zh":"快速衰退可以令人震驚，而慢速衰退可能較容易被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing the speed of worsening.","zh":"比較惡化速度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the likelihood of collapse","meaning":"崩潰的可能性","examples":[{"en":"The likelihood of collapse may not have been foreseeable.","zh":"崩潰的可能性未必曾經可預見。"},{"en":"The likelihood of collapse means the chance or probability that a breakdown will happen.","zh":"likelihood of collapse 指瓦解會發生的機會或可能性。"},{"en":"A business owner may judge the likelihood of collapse by looking at debt, sales, and customer numbers.","zh":"企業東主可能透過查看債務、銷售和顧客數量來判斷倒閉可能性。"},{"en":"If danger is not visible, people may fail to prepare for collapse.","zh":"如果危險不可見，人們可能未能為崩潰作準備。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing risk and prediction.","zh":"討論風險和預測時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be foreseeable","meaning":"可預見","examples":[{"en":"The rapid decline would not necessarily have been foreseeable.","zh":"這種迅速衰退未必是可預見的。"},{"en":"Be foreseeable means be possible to predict before it happens.","zh":"be foreseeable 指在事情發生前可以預測。"},{"en":"A traffic jam may be foreseeable if a major concert ends at the same time as rush hour.","zh":"如果大型演唱會結束時間與繁忙時間重疊，交通擠塞可能是可預見的。"},{"en":"Some disasters seem obvious only after they happen.","zh":"有些災難只有在發生後才顯得明顯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing whether people could have predicted a result.","zh":"討論人們是否能預測結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"deterioration","meaning":"惡化；衰退","examples":[{"en":"Deterioration did not invariably lead to total collapse.","zh":"惡化並不一定導致全面崩潰。"},{"en":"Deterioration means a process of becoming worse in quality, condition, or strength.","zh":"deterioration 指質素、狀況或力量逐漸變差的過程。"},{"en":"A building shows deterioration when paint falls off, pipes leak, and walls crack.","zh":"當油漆剝落、水管漏水、牆壁裂開，建築就顯示惡化。"},{"en":"Deterioration can be stopped if people repair the problem early enough.","zh":"如果人們及早修補問題，惡化可以被阻止。"},{"en":"This word is useful when describing worsening over time.","zh":"描述隨時間變差時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"invariably lead to","meaning":"一定導致","examples":[{"en":"Environmental deterioration did not invariably lead to total collapse.","zh":"環境惡化並不一定導致全面崩潰。"},{"en":"Invariably lead to means always result in something, without exception.","zh":"invariably lead to 指毫無例外地總是導致某結果。"},{"en":"Missing one lesson does not invariably lead to failure if the student catches up quickly.","zh":"如果學生很快補上，一次缺課不一定導致失敗。"},{"en":"The passage rejects the idea that environmental decline always has the same final result.","zh":"文章否定環境衰退總是帶來同一最終結果的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing whether a cause always produces an effect.","zh":"討論原因是否總會產生某結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"total collapse","meaning":"全面崩潰","examples":[{"en":"Some societies experienced decline without total collapse.","zh":"有些社會經歷衰退但沒有全面崩潰。"},{"en":"Total collapse means complete breakdown of a society, organisation, or system.","zh":"total collapse 指社會、組織或系統完全瓦解。"},{"en":"A club may lose members and activities without facing total collapse if leaders rebuild it.","zh":"如果領導者重建學會，學會可能流失會員和活動，但不會全面崩潰。"},{"en":"Total collapse is more severe than temporary difficulty or partial decline.","zh":"全面崩潰比暫時困難或部分衰退更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when distinguishing complete failure from weaker decline.","zh":"區分完全失敗和較弱衰退時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"influence the course of events","meaning":"影響事態發展","examples":[{"en":"Individuals may sometimes influence the course of events.","zh":"個人有時可能影響事態發展。"},{"en":"To influence the course of events means to affect how a situation develops over time.","zh":"influence the course of events 指影響某情況如何隨時間發展。"},{"en":"A principal’s decision can influence the course of events during a school crisis.","zh":"校長的決定可以影響學校危機中的事態發展。"},{"en":"One action can change later outcomes by shifting choices, timing, or public reaction.","zh":"一個行動可以透過改變選擇、時機或公眾反應來改變後來結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when people affect historical or social developments.","zh":"當人影響歷史或社會發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"agree with the views of","meaning":"與作者觀點一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether statements agree with the views of the writer.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與作者觀點一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the views of someone means match that person’s opinion or argument.","zh":"agree with the views of someone 指符合某人的意見或論點。"},{"en":"A statement agrees with the writer’s view only if the text clearly supports it.","zh":"只有文本清楚支持某陳述，它才與作者觀點一致。"},{"en":"Students should not use their own opinion when judging the writer’s view.","zh":"判斷作者觀點時，學生不應使用自己的意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in YES, NO, NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 YES, NO, NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與作者觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the views expressed in the passage.","zh":"一個陳述可能與文章中表達的觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to state the opposite of what that person believes or argues.","zh":"contradict the views of someone 指說出與某人信念或論點相反的內容。"},{"en":"If a writer says history gives useful warnings, a statement saying history is useless may contradict the view.","zh":"如果作者說歷史提供有用警示，而陳述說歷史毫無用處，就可能與觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must come from the passage, not from personal knowledge.","zh":"矛盾必須來自文章，而不是個人知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying NO answers.","zh":"辨認 NO 答案時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Write “NOT GIVEN” when it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"當無法判斷作者想法時，寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to give a definite answer.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資料給出確定答案。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions the writer’s opinion on tourism income, it is impossible to say what they think.","zh":"如果文章從未提到作者對旅遊收入的看法，就無法判斷他們怎樣想。"},{"en":"Students should choose NOT GIVEN when the passage is silent about a claim.","zh":"當文章沒有提及某說法時，學生應選 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence is missing.","zh":"當證據缺失時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be widely believed that","meaning":"人們普遍認為","examples":[{"en":"It is widely believed that environmental problems threaten modern society.","zh":"人們普遍認為環境問題威脅現代社會。"},{"en":"Be widely believed that means many people accept or think something is true.","zh":"be widely believed that 指許多人接受或認為某事是真。"},{"en":"It is widely believed that regular reading helps improve vocabulary.","zh":"人們普遍認為定期閱讀有助提升詞彙量。"},{"en":"A belief can be widespread even when experts still debate details.","zh":"即使專家仍在爭論細節，某信念也可以很普遍。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting a common view.","zh":"報告常見觀點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"represent the main danger","meaning":"構成主要危險","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe environmental problems represent the main danger facing the world.","zh":"有些人相信環境問題構成世界面對的主要危險。"},{"en":"To represent the main danger means to be seen as the most important threat.","zh":"represent the main danger 指被視為最重要的威脅。"},{"en":"For a small school, falling student numbers may represent the main danger to its future.","zh":"對小學校來說，學生人數下降可能構成其未來的主要危險。"},{"en":"If one risk is viewed as the main danger, it may receive most attention and resources.","zh":"如果一種風險被視為主要危險，它可能得到最多關注和資源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when ranking threats.","zh":"排列威脅的重要程度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be faced by","meaning":"被……面對","examples":[{"en":"Modern societies are faced by numerous environmental threats.","zh":"現代社會面對眾多環境威脅。"},{"en":"Be faced by means have to deal with or confront something difficult.","zh":"be faced by 指必須處理或面對困難事情。"},{"en":"Students are faced by heavy pressure when several exams happen in the same week.","zh":"當幾場考試在同一星期舉行，學生會面對沉重壓力。"},{"en":"When a society is faced by threats, it must decide which problems to address first.","zh":"當社會面對威脅，就必須決定先處理哪些問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing challenges.","zh":"描述挑戰時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"accumulation of poisonous substances","meaning":"有毒物質的累積","examples":[{"en":"The accumulation of poisonous substances is a modern environmental problem.","zh":"有毒物質的累積是一個現代環境問題。"},{"en":"Accumulation of poisonous substances means harmful materials slowly build up in the environment or body.","zh":"accumulation of poisonous substances 指有害物質在環境或身體中慢慢累積。"},{"en":"A river may suffer from accumulation of poisonous substances if factories discharge waste for years.","zh":"如果工廠多年排放廢物，河流可能受有毒物質累積影響。"},{"en":"Long-term accumulation can be dangerous because damage may appear only after many years.","zh":"長期累積可能很危險，因為損害可能多年後才出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when pollution grows gradually.","zh":"當污染逐漸增加時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"relatively modern problem","meaning":"相對現代的問題","examples":[{"en":"Toxic chemical buildup is a relatively modern problem.","zh":"有毒化學物質累積是一個相對現代的問題。"},{"en":"A relatively modern problem is a problem that appeared mainly in recent historical times.","zh":"relatively modern problem 指主要在較近期歷史時期出現的問題。"},{"en":"Cyberbullying is a relatively modern problem because it depends on digital communication.","zh":"網絡欺凌是相對現代的問題，因為它依賴數碼溝通。"},{"en":"New technologies and industries can create problems earlier societies did not face.","zh":"新科技和工業可以創造早期社會沒有面對的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing old and new risks.","zh":"比較舊風險和新風險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"general agreement","meaning":"普遍共識","examples":[{"en":"There is no general agreement about the seriousness of the risks.","zh":"對於風險的嚴重程度，並沒有普遍共識。"},{"en":"General agreement means broad shared acceptance among many people.","zh":"general agreement 指許多人之間廣泛共享的接受或認同。"},{"en":"There may be no general agreement among parents about the best amount of homework.","zh":"家長之間可能沒有關於最佳功課量的普遍共識。"},{"en":"Without agreement, policy debates can become slower and more heated.","zh":"沒有共識時，政策討論可能變得較慢和更激烈。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when views remain divided.","zh":"當觀點仍然分歧時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"threats posed by","meaning":"由……構成的威脅","examples":[{"en":"The threats posed by environmental problems are widely debated.","zh":"由環境問題構成的威脅受到廣泛爭論。"},{"en":"Threats posed by something are dangers created or presented by it.","zh":"threats posed by something 指由某事造成或帶來的危險。"},{"en":"The threats posed by heavy traffic include accidents, air pollution, and stress.","zh":"由嚴重交通構成的威脅包括意外、空氣污染和壓力。"},{"en":"Identifying threats helps people decide how urgently they must act.","zh":"識別威脅幫助人們決定行動有多迫切。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining what dangers come from a cause.","zh":"解釋危險來自甚麼原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"resemble present-day societies","meaning":"與現代社會相似","examples":[{"en":"Some past societies may have resembled present-day societies.","zh":"有些過去社會可能與現代社會相似。"},{"en":"To resemble present-day societies means to be similar to modern societies in some features.","zh":"resemble present-day societies 指在某些特徵上與現代社會相似。"},{"en":"An ancient trading city may resemble present-day cities if it had markets, migration, and long-distance exchange.","zh":"如果古代貿易城市有市場、移民和長途交流，它可能與現代城市相似。"},{"en":"Similarities can make history feel relevant, but differences still matter.","zh":"相似之處可以令歷史顯得相關，但差異仍然重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing past and present societies.","zh":"比較過去和現在社會時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"more closely than","meaning":"比……更相似","examples":[{"en":"Some ancient societies resembled modern ones more closely than others did.","zh":"有些古代社會比其他古代社會更接近現代社會。"},{"en":"More closely than means with a stronger or greater degree of similarity than another comparison.","zh":"more closely than 指相似程度比另一比較對象更高。"},{"en":"One student’s essay may resemble the model answer more closely than another student’s essay.","zh":"一名學生的文章可能比另一名學生的文章更接近範文。"},{"en":"Stronger resemblance can make comparison more useful, but it still requires caution.","zh":"相似度較高可以令比較更有用，但仍需要謹慎。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing degrees of similarity.","zh":"比較相似程度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"draw comparisons between","meaning":"把……作比較","examples":[{"en":"We should be careful when drawing comparisons between past and present.","zh":"當我們把過去和現在作比較時，應該小心。"},{"en":"To draw comparisons between two things means to examine their similarities and differences.","zh":"draw comparisons between two things 指檢視兩者的相似和差異。"},{"en":"A teacher may draw comparisons between two essays to show why one is clearer.","zh":"老師可能比較兩篇文章，以顯示為何其中一篇較清晰。"},{"en":"Comparisons help learning, but they can mislead if important differences are ignored.","zh":"比較有助學習，但如果忽視重要差異，就可能誤導。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing cases thoughtfully.","zh":"審慎比較個案時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete each sentence with","meaning":"用……完成每句","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete each sentence with the correct ending.","zh":"考生用正確句末完成每句。"},{"en":"Complete each sentence with something means finish the sentence by adding the required word, phrase, or ending.","zh":"complete each sentence with something 指透過加入指定詞語、短語或句末來完成句子。"},{"en":"Students may complete each sentence with a verb from the box.","zh":"學生可能用方框中的動詞完成每句。"},{"en":"The sentence must remain grammatical and match the meaning of the passage.","zh":"句子必須保持文法正確，並符合文章意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading and grammar instructions.","zh":"這個短語適用於閱讀和文法指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the correct ending","meaning":"正確句末","examples":[{"en":"Each sentence must be matched with the correct ending.","zh":"每句都必須與正確句末配對。"},{"en":"The correct ending is the sentence ending that fits both grammar and meaning.","zh":"correct ending 指同時符合文法和意思的句子結尾。"},{"en":"In a matching task, students choose the correct ending from several options.","zh":"在配對題中，學生從幾個選項中選擇正確句末。"},{"en":"A wrong ending may sound grammatical but fail to match the passage.","zh":"錯誤句末可能聽起來文法正確，但不符合文章。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in sentence-completion questions.","zh":"這個短語適用於句子完成題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"evidence of greatness","meaning":"偉大的證據","examples":[{"en":"Monumental ruins provide evidence of the greatness of former civilisations.","zh":"宏偉遺址提供過去文明偉大的證據。"},{"en":"Evidence of greatness means proof that something was impressive, powerful, skilful, or important.","zh":"evidence of greatness 指證明某事曾令人印象深刻、強大、有技術或重要的證據。"},{"en":"A school trophy room can provide evidence of greatness in sport and music.","zh":"學校獎盃室可以提供體育和音樂方面偉大的證據。"},{"en":"Large structures show greatness because they required planning, labour, wealth, and technical ability.","zh":"大型結構顯示偉大，因為它們需要規劃、勞力、財富和技術能力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when remains prove past achievement.","zh":"當遺存證明過去成就時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"former civilisations","meaning":"過去的文明","examples":[{"en":"Physical structures remain from many former civilisations.","zh":"許多過去文明留下實體建築。"},{"en":"Former civilisations are complex societies that existed in the past.","zh":"former civilisations 指存在於過去的複雜社會。"},{"en":"Museums display objects from former civilisations to show how people once lived.","zh":"博物館展示來自過去文明的物件，以顯示人們曾如何生活。"},{"en":"The remains of former civilisations can teach us about wealth, religion, trade, and collapse.","zh":"過去文明的遺存可以教我們了解財富、宗教、貿易和崩潰。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing ancient or vanished societies.","zh":"討論古代或已消失社會時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"provide grounds for","meaning":"為……提供理據","examples":[{"en":"Modern technology may provide grounds for an optimistic outlook.","zh":"現代科技可能為樂觀展望提供理據。"},{"en":"To provide grounds for something means to give reasons or evidence that support it.","zh":"provide grounds for something 指提供支持某事的理由或證據。"},{"en":"Better exam results may provide grounds for confidence in a new teaching method.","zh":"更好的考試成績可能為相信新教學方法提供理據。"},{"en":"A claim is stronger when there are clear grounds for believing it.","zh":"當有清楚理據支持，相信某說法就更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why a view may be reasonable.","zh":"解釋某觀點為何可能合理時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"an optimistic outlook","meaning":"樂觀展望","examples":[{"en":"Some people have an optimistic outlook because of modern technology.","zh":"有些人因現代科技而抱有樂觀展望。"},{"en":"An optimistic outlook is a hopeful view of the future.","zh":"optimistic outlook 指對未來抱有希望的看法。"},{"en":"A student may have an optimistic outlook after improving steadily for several months.","zh":"學生持續幾個月穩定進步後，可能抱有樂觀展望。"},{"en":"Optimism can encourage action, but it may be risky if it ignores real problems.","zh":"樂觀可以鼓勵行動，但如果忽視真實問題，就可能有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing positive expectations.","zh":"討論正面期望時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"exist in the form of","meaning":"以……形式存在","examples":[{"en":"Evidence of former power exists in the form of physical structures.","zh":"昔日權力的證據以實體建築形式存在。"},{"en":"Exist in the form of means appear or remain as a particular type of thing.","zh":"exist in the form of 指以某一特定類型的事物出現或保留下來。"},{"en":"A student’s progress may exist in the form of better essays, clearer notes, and higher confidence.","zh":"學生的進步可能以更好的文章、更清晰筆記和更高信心的形式存在。"},{"en":"Past wealth can survive as buildings even after the society itself disappears.","zh":"即使社會本身消失，昔日財富仍可以建築形式保存。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence appears in a specific form.","zh":"當證據以特定形式出現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"physical structures","meaning":"實體建築","examples":[{"en":"Monumental ruins are physical structures left by earlier societies.","zh":"宏偉遺址是早期社會留下的實體建築。"},{"en":"Physical structures are solid built objects such as walls, buildings, roads, bridges, or temples.","zh":"physical structures 指牆、建築、道路、橋樑或神廟等堅固建造物。"},{"en":"A city’s physical structures include schools, hospitals, roads, and apartment blocks.","zh":"城市的實體建築包括學校、醫院、道路和住宅大廈。"},{"en":"Structures can survive longer than people, so they become evidence for historians.","zh":"建築可以比人存留更久，因此成為歷史學家的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing material remains.","zh":"討論物質遺存時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"not necessarily valid","meaning":"不一定成立","examples":[{"en":"The comparison between a society and a human life is not necessarily valid.","zh":"社會與人的一生之間的比較不一定成立。"},{"en":"Not necessarily valid means not always correct, fair, or logically acceptable.","zh":"not necessarily valid 指不總是正確、公平或合乎邏輯。"},{"en":"Comparing two students only by exam marks is not necessarily valid if one faced serious illness.","zh":"如果其中一名學生曾患重病，只按考試分數比較兩名學生不一定成立。"},{"en":"A comparison may sound attractive but fail when important differences are considered.","zh":"一個比較可能聽起來吸引，但在考慮重要差異後未必成立。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when questioning an argument.","zh":"質疑論點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"potentially both positive and negative","meaning":"可能同時有正面及負面作用","examples":[{"en":"The power of modern technology is potentially both positive and negative.","zh":"現代科技的力量可能同時有正面及負面作用。"},{"en":"Potentially both positive and negative means something may bring benefits and harm depending on how it is used.","zh":"potentially both positive and negative 指某事可能帶來好處和傷害，視乎如何使用。"},{"en":"Social media is potentially both positive and negative because it can connect people but also spread misinformation.","zh":"社交媒體可能同時有正面及負面作用，因為它可以連接人，也可以傳播錯誤資訊。"},{"en":"Powerful tools require careful management because their effects are not one-sided.","zh":"強大工具需要謹慎管理，因為其影響不是單方面的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving a balanced evaluation.","zh":"作平衡評價時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"provide direct solutions","meaning":"提供直接解決方法","examples":[{"en":"Historical study will not provide direct solutions to every present problem.","zh":"歷史研究不會為每個當前問題提供直接解決方法。"},{"en":"To provide direct solutions means to give immediate, ready-made answers to a problem.","zh":"provide direct solutions 指為問題提供即時、現成的答案。"},{"en":"A parenting book may not provide direct solutions to every child’s behaviour issue.","zh":"育兒書未必能為每個兒童行為問題提供直接解決方法。"},{"en":"Complex problems usually require adaptation, judgement, and local knowledge.","zh":"複雜問題通常需要調整、判斷和本地知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when warning that guidance is not the same as a complete answer.","zh":"警告指引不等於完整答案時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"present problems","meaning":"當前問題","examples":[{"en":"Lessons from history cannot automatically solve present problems.","zh":"歷史教訓不能自動解決當前問題。"},{"en":"Present problems are difficulties that exist now, in the current time.","zh":"present problems 指目前存在的困難。"},{"en":"A school’s present problems may include stress, late homework, and poor attendance.","zh":"學校的當前問題可能包括壓力、遲交功課和出席率低。"},{"en":"Present problems may have roots in the past, but they still need current action.","zh":"當前問題可能有歷史根源，但仍需要現時行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when distinguishing today’s challenges from historical ones.","zh":"區分今天的挑戰和歷史問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a consideration of","meaning":"對……的考慮；分析","examples":[{"en":"A consideration of historical events may offer useful lessons.","zh":"對歷史事件的分析可能提供有用教訓。"},{"en":"A consideration of something means careful thought, examination, or analysis of it.","zh":"consideration of something 指仔細思考、檢視或分析某事。"},{"en":"A consideration of students’ sleep habits may help a school design a better timetable.","zh":"對學生睡眠習慣的考慮可能幫助學校設計更好的時間表。"},{"en":"Careful consideration can reveal causes and consequences that are not obvious at first.","zh":"仔細分析可以揭示起初不明顯的原因和後果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in formal academic writing.","zh":"這個短語適用於正式學術寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"historical events and trends","meaning":"歷史事件和趨勢","examples":[{"en":"We should carefully examine historical events and trends.","zh":"我們應該仔細檢視歷史事件和趨勢。"},{"en":"Historical events and trends are important past happenings and longer patterns of change.","zh":"historical events and trends 指重要的過去事件和較長期的變化模式。"},{"en":"A history lesson may study both one revolution and wider trends in population or trade.","zh":"歷史課可能同時研究一次革命和人口或貿易方面的更廣泛趨勢。"},{"en":"Events show what happened at certain moments, while trends show how conditions changed over time.","zh":"事件顯示某些時刻發生了甚麼，而趨勢顯示條件如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when history includes both specific incidents and broad patterns.","zh":"當歷史包含具體事件和廣泛模式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the main argument of","meaning":"……的主要論點","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for the main argument of the passage.","zh":"題目要求找出文章的主要論點。"},{"en":"The main argument of a text is its central claim or message.","zh":"main argument of a text 指文本的核心主張或訊息。"},{"en":"A student should identify the main argument of an essay before analysing examples.","zh":"學生分析例子前，應先找出文章主要論點。"},{"en":"Understanding the main argument prevents readers from focusing only on minor details.","zh":"理解主要論點可以防止讀者只聚焦細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading comprehension and essay analysis.","zh":"這個短語適用於閱讀理解和文章分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"differences as well as similarities","meaning":"差異以及相似之處","examples":[{"en":"There are differences as well as similarities between past and present societies.","zh":"過去和現在社會之間既有差異，也有相似之處。"},{"en":"Differences as well as similarities means both what is unlike and what is alike must be considered.","zh":"differences as well as similarities 指不同之處和相似之處都必須考慮。"},{"en":"When comparing two schools, students should note differences as well as similarities in rules and teaching style.","zh":"比較兩所學校時，學生應注意規則和教學風格上的差異以及相似之處。"},{"en":"A balanced comparison avoids pretending that two cases are either totally identical or totally unrelated.","zh":"平衡比較避免假裝兩個個案完全相同或完全無關。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when making careful comparisons.","zh":"作謹慎比較時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"preserve the physical remains of","meaning":"保存……的實體遺跡","examples":[{"en":"Governments may work to preserve the physical remains of earlier civilisations.","zh":"政府可能努力保存早期文明的實體遺跡。"},{"en":"To preserve the physical remains of something means to protect its surviving material objects, buildings, or sites.","zh":"preserve the physical remains of something 指保護其仍然存在的物件、建築或地點。"},{"en":"A museum may preserve the physical remains of an old village by protecting tools, walls, and pottery.","zh":"博物館可能透過保護工具、牆壁和陶器，保存舊村落的實體遺跡。"},{"en":"Preservation prevents weather, construction, and tourism from destroying evidence.","zh":"保存工作防止天氣、施工和旅遊破壞證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing heritage protection.","zh":"討論文化遺產保護時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"historical accounts","meaning":"歷史記載","examples":[{"en":"Historical accounts may provide evidence about vanished societies.","zh":"歷史記載可能提供關於已消失社會的證據。"},{"en":"Historical accounts are written or spoken records describing past events, people, or places.","zh":"historical accounts 指描述過去事件、人物或地方的書面或口述紀錄。"},{"en":"A diary from a traveller can be a historical account of daily life in an old city.","zh":"旅客日記可以是關於舊城市日常生活的歷史記載。"},{"en":"Accounts can help historians, but they may contain bias or missing information.","zh":"記載可以幫助歷史學家，但也可能包含偏見或缺失資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing written evidence from the past.","zh":"討論來自過去的文字證據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be dependent on each other","meaning":"互相依賴","examples":[{"en":"Modern societies are increasingly dependent on each other.","zh":"現代社會越來越互相依賴。"},{"en":"Be dependent on each other means rely on one another for goods, services, information, resources, or support.","zh":"dependent on each other 指彼此依靠貨物、服務、資訊、資源或支援。"},{"en":"Two classmates may be dependent on each other in a group project if each controls part of the work.","zh":"如果兩名同學各自負責小組專題的一部分，他們可能互相依賴。"},{"en":"Interdependence can make cooperation easier but also spreads problems faster.","zh":"相互依賴可以令合作更容易，但也會令問題傳播更快。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when systems are connected.","zh":"當系統互相連接時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"continuing survival","meaning":"持續生存","examples":[{"en":"Environmental resources are essential to a society’s continuing survival.","zh":"環境資源對一個社會的持續生存至關重要。"},{"en":"Continuing survival means ongoing existence over time, not just short-term success.","zh":"continuing survival 指隨時間繼續存在，而不只是短期成功。"},{"en":"A small school’s continuing survival may depend on enough students, teachers, and funding.","zh":"小型學校的持續生存可能取決於足夠學生、老師和資金。"},{"en":"If essential resources disappear, survival becomes harder year after year.","zh":"如果必要資源消失，生存會一年比一年困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing long-term existence and stability.","zh":"討論長期存在和穩定時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 119 - Learning lessons from the past.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 121":[{"front":"The Future of Fish","meaning":"魚類的未來","examples":[{"en":"The future of fish depends on how effectively humanity protects marine ecosystems.","zh":"魚類的未來取決於人類保護海洋生態系統的成效。"},{"en":"The future of fish means what will happen to fish populations, fisheries, and marine life in the years ahead.","zh":"「The Future of Fish」意思是未來魚類種群、漁業和海洋生命將會如何。"},{"en":"A student may discuss the future of fish when writing about food security and ocean protection.","zh":"學生寫食物安全和海洋保護時，可能討論魚類的未來。"},{"en":"If people continue overfishing, the future of fish may become uncertain and dangerous.","zh":"如果人們繼續過度捕魚，魚類的未來可能變得不確定而危險。"},{"en":"The phrase links fish survival with human choices today.","zh":"這個短語把魚類存續與今日人類選擇連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the face of the ocean","meaning":"海洋的面貌","examples":[{"en":"The face of the ocean has changed completely because of intensive fishing.","zh":"由於密集捕魚，海洋的面貌已徹底改變。"},{"en":"The face of the ocean means the overall condition, appearance, and character of marine ecosystems.","zh":"「the face of the ocean」指海洋生態系統的整體狀況、面貌和特徵。"},{"en":"Pollution, warming, and overfishing can all change the face of the ocean.","zh":"污染、暖化和過度捕魚都可以改變海洋的面貌。"},{"en":"If large fish disappear and food webs shift, the ocean no longer looks or functions as it once did.","zh":"如果大型魚類消失，食物網轉變，海洋就不再像以前一樣運作或呈現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad visible and ecological change.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛而可見的生態變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"change completely","meaning":"徹底改變","examples":[{"en":"Commercial fishing has changed marine ecosystems completely.","zh":"商業捕魚已徹底改變海洋生態系統。"},{"en":"To change completely means to become very different from the original state.","zh":"「change completely」意思是變得與原本狀態非常不同。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood can change completely when old shops are replaced by large shopping centres.","zh":"當舊商店被大型商場取代，社區可以徹底改變。"},{"en":"If fishing removes key species, the whole ecosystem may change completely.","zh":"如果捕魚移除關鍵物種，整個生態系統可能徹底改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep change, not a small adjustment.","zh":"這個短語描述深層改變，而不是小調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"commercial fishers","meaning":"商業漁民","examples":[{"en":"Commercial fishers have used nets and hooks for more than a thousand years.","zh":"商業漁民使用漁網和魚鈎已有一千多年。"},{"en":"Commercial fishers are people who catch fish to sell, not simply for personal food.","zh":"「commercial fishers」是捕魚出售的人，而不只是為自己食用而捕魚。"},{"en":"A coastal town may depend on commercial fishers for jobs and fresh seafood.","zh":"沿海城鎮可能依靠商業漁民提供工作和新鮮海鮮。"},{"en":"If commercial fishers catch too much, fish stocks may decline over time.","zh":"如果商業漁民捕撈過量，魚類資源量可能隨時間下降。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to fishing as a business activity.","zh":"這個短語指作為商業活動的捕魚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cast their nets and hooks","meaning":"撒網和下鈎","examples":[{"en":"Early commercial fishers cast their nets and hooks into the sea.","zh":"早期商業漁民把漁網和魚鈎撒入海中。"},{"en":"To cast nets and hooks means to throw or place fishing equipment into water to catch fish.","zh":"「cast nets and hooks」意思是把捕魚工具拋入或放入水中捕魚。"},{"en":"Fishermen may cast their nets before sunrise when fish are closer to the shore.","zh":"漁民可能在日出前撒網，因為魚較接近岸邊。"},{"en":"If more people cast nets in the same area, fish may have less chance to reproduce.","zh":"如果更多人在同一地區撒網，魚類繁殖機會可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the physical act of fishing.","zh":"這個短語描述捕魚的實際動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"over a thousand years ago","meaning":"一千多年前","examples":[{"en":"Commercial fishing began over a thousand years ago.","zh":"商業捕魚在一千多年前已經開始。"},{"en":"Over a thousand years ago means more than one thousand years before the present time.","zh":"「over a thousand years ago」意思是距今超過一千年前。"},{"en":"Some temples were built over a thousand years ago and still attract visitors today.","zh":"有些寺廟在一千多年前建成，今天仍吸引遊客。"},{"en":"If a practice began over a thousand years ago, it has a very long history.","zh":"如果一種做法始於一千多年前，它就有非常悠久歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises great historical depth.","zh":"這個短語強調深遠的歷史時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fisheries intensified","meaning":"捕魚活動加劇","examples":[{"en":"Fisheries intensified gradually over the centuries.","zh":"幾個世紀以來，捕魚活動逐漸加劇。"},{"en":"Fisheries intensified means fishing activity became stronger, larger, or more frequent.","zh":"「fisheries intensified」意思是捕魚活動變得更強、更大規模或更頻繁。"},{"en":"Traffic intensified after a new shopping centre opened near the school.","zh":"新商場在學校附近開幕後，交通加劇了。"},{"en":"If fisheries intensify without control, fish populations may fall faster than they can recover.","zh":"如果捕魚活動在沒有管制下加劇，魚類種群可能下降得比恢復更快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes increasing pressure from fishing.","zh":"這個短語描述捕魚壓力增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"over the centuries","meaning":"幾個世紀以來","examples":[{"en":"Fishing pressure increased steadily over the centuries.","zh":"幾個世紀以來，捕魚壓力穩步增加。"},{"en":"Over the centuries means during many hundreds of years.","zh":"「over the centuries」意思是在許多百年間。"},{"en":"Over the centuries, languages change as people invent new words and borrow from others.","zh":"幾個世紀以來，語言會因人們創造新詞和借用外來詞而改變。"},{"en":"If human activity builds up over centuries, its environmental effects can become enormous.","zh":"如果人類活動累積數百年，其環境影響可以變得巨大。"},{"en":"The phrase shows change across a very long period.","zh":"這個短語顯示跨越很長時間的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"it was still felt that","meaning":"當時人們仍然認為","examples":[{"en":"It was still felt that the resources of the sea were practically unlimited.","zh":"當時人們仍然認為海洋資源幾乎無限。"},{"en":"It was still felt that means people still believed or assumed something at that time.","zh":"「it was still felt that」意思是當時人們仍然相信或假定某事。"},{"en":"It was still felt that online lessons were temporary before they became common.","zh":"在網課變得普遍之前，當時人們仍然認為網課只是暫時安排。"},{"en":"If people believed the sea was unlimited, they saw little need for strict controls.","zh":"如果人們相信海洋無限，他們就覺得幾乎沒有需要嚴格管制。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a belief that may later prove wrong.","zh":"這個短語引出一個後來可能被證明錯誤的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"justifiably","meaning":"有充分理由地","examples":[{"en":"People once believed, justifiably at the time, that many fish stocks were beyond reach.","zh":"人們曾經有充分理由地相信，當時許多魚類資源超出捕撈範圍。"},{"en":"Justifiably means with a good reason or in a way that can be defended.","zh":"「justifiably」意思是有好理由，或可以被合理辯護地。"},{"en":"Parents may be justifiably worried if a child walks home alone late at night.","zh":"如果孩子深夜獨自回家，父母可能有充分理由地擔心。"},{"en":"If old fishing boats could not reach deep waters, people were justifiably confident that many fish were safe.","zh":"如果舊式漁船不能到達深水區，人們有充分理由相信許多魚是安全的。"},{"en":"The word shows that a belief or action had reasonable support at the time.","zh":"這個詞顯示某信念或行動在當時有合理支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"plentiful resources","meaning":"豐富資源","examples":[{"en":"The sea was once believed to contain plentiful resources.","zh":"人們曾相信海洋含有豐富資源。"},{"en":"Plentiful resources are supplies that exist in large amounts.","zh":"「plentiful resources」是大量存在的供應或資源。"},{"en":"A school with plentiful resources may have enough books, computers, teachers, and space.","zh":"資源豐富的學校可能有足夠書本、電腦、老師和空間。"},{"en":"If people believe resources are plentiful, they may use them less carefully.","zh":"如果人們相信資源豐富，他們可能較不小心使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes abundance, but abundance may not last forever.","zh":"這個短語描述富足，但富足未必永遠持續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for the most part","meaning":"大致上；在大多數情況下","examples":[{"en":"Fish stocks were, for the most part, beyond the reach of traditional fishing.","zh":"魚類資源在大多數情況下超出傳統捕魚所能到達的範圍。"},{"en":"For the most part means mainly or in most cases.","zh":"「for the most part」意思是主要地或在大多數情況下。"},{"en":"The class was, for the most part, ready for the exam, although a few students needed help.","zh":"全班大致上已準備好考試，雖然少數學生仍需要幫助。"},{"en":"If fish were mostly beyond reach, fishing pressure was once naturally limited.","zh":"如果魚類大多超出捕撈範圍，捕魚壓力曾自然受到限制。"},{"en":"The phrase allows a general statement while leaving room for exceptions.","zh":"這個短語容許作出概括說法，同時保留例外空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"beyond the reach of","meaning":"超出……所能到達的範圍","examples":[{"en":"Many marine resources were once beyond the reach of fishing fleets.","zh":"許多海洋資源曾經超出漁船隊所能到達的範圍。"},{"en":"Beyond the reach of something means too far away or too difficult for it to access.","zh":"「beyond the reach of」某物，意思是太遠或太難以被它接觸到。"},{"en":"Some mountain villages were once beyond the reach of reliable internet service.","zh":"有些山村曾經超出可靠互聯網服務所能到達的範圍。"},{"en":"If deep-sea fish are beyond the reach of small boats, they remain protected by distance.","zh":"如果深海魚類超出小船可到達範圍，它們就因距離而受到保護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limits of access or ability.","zh":"這個短語描述接觸或能力上的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"little need to","meaning":"幾乎沒有需要……","examples":[{"en":"There appeared to be little need to restrict fishing.","zh":"當時看來幾乎沒有需要限制捕魚。"},{"en":"Little need to do something means there seems to be almost no reason to do it.","zh":"「little need to」做某事，意思是似乎幾乎沒有理由做它。"},{"en":"If students already understand a topic, there may be little need to repeat the whole lesson.","zh":"如果學生已理解某題目，可能幾乎沒有需要重複整堂課。"},{"en":"If fish seemed unlimited, governments saw little need to control catches.","zh":"如果魚類看似無限，政府就覺得幾乎沒有需要管制捕獲量。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that an action appears unnecessary.","zh":"這個短語顯示某行動看似不必要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"restrict fishing","meaning":"限制捕魚","examples":[{"en":"Governments were slow to restrict fishing in the open ocean.","zh":"政府遲遲未在公海限制捕魚。"},{"en":"To restrict fishing means to limit where, when, how much, or how people can catch fish.","zh":"「restrict fishing」意思是限制人們在哪裡、何時、捕多少或如何捕魚。"},{"en":"A coastal park may restrict fishing during breeding season.","zh":"沿海公園可能在繁殖季節限制捕魚。"},{"en":"If fishing is not restricted, too many fish may be removed before they reproduce.","zh":"如果捕魚不受限制，太多魚可能在繁殖前被捕走。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rules that reduce fishing pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述減少捕魚壓力的規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"create protected areas","meaning":"設立保護區","examples":[{"en":"Protected areas can reduce pressure on marine wildlife.","zh":"保護區可以減少海洋野生生物所受壓力。"},{"en":"To create protected areas means to set aside places where nature receives legal or practical protection.","zh":"「create protected areas」意思是劃出受法律或實際保護的自然地區。"},{"en":"A city may create protected areas in wetlands so birds can breed safely.","zh":"城市可能在濕地設立保護區，讓雀鳥安全繁殖。"},{"en":"If protected areas are well managed, wildlife can recover from human pressure.","zh":"如果保護區管理良好，野生生物可以從人類壓力中恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase describes establishing safe zones for nature.","zh":"這個短語描述為自然建立安全區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"herald an escalation in","meaning":"預示……急劇增加","examples":[{"en":"The twentieth century heralded an escalation in fishing intensity.","zh":"二十世紀預示捕魚強度急劇增加。"},{"en":"To herald an escalation in something means to mark the beginning of a sharp increase in it.","zh":"「herald an escalation in」某事，意思是標誌着它急劇增加的開始。"},{"en":"The arrival of smartphones heralded an escalation in daily screen use.","zh":"智能手機出現預示日常屏幕使用急劇增加。"},{"en":"If new engines and sonar appeared, they could mark a major increase in fishing power.","zh":"如果新引擎和聲納出現，它們可能標誌捕魚能力大幅增加。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the start of a significant rise.","zh":"這個短語引出顯著上升的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fishing intensity","meaning":"捕魚強度","examples":[{"en":"Modern technology has greatly increased fishing intensity.","zh":"現代科技大幅提高了捕魚強度。"},{"en":"Fishing intensity means the level of fishing pressure, including how often, how widely, and how efficiently fish are caught.","zh":"「fishing intensity」意思是捕魚壓力水平，包括捕魚頻率、範圍和效率。"},{"en":"Fishing intensity rises when more boats work longer hours with better equipment.","zh":"當更多漁船用更好設備工作更長時間，捕魚強度就會上升。"},{"en":"If fishing intensity becomes too high, fish populations may not recover between seasons.","zh":"如果捕魚強度太高，魚類種群可能無法在季節之間恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase measures how strong the pressure from fishing is.","zh":"這個短語量度捕魚壓力有多強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"unprecedented in the history of","meaning":"在……歷史上前所未有","examples":[{"en":"The current level of exploitation is unprecedented in the history of the oceans.","zh":"目前的開發利用水平在海洋歷史上前所未有。"},{"en":"Unprecedented in the history of something means never seen before in its whole recorded past.","zh":"「unprecedented in the history of」某事，意思是在其整個記錄過去中從未見過。"},{"en":"The school’s exam results were unprecedented in its history because every student passed.","zh":"學校考試成績在其歷史上前所未有，因為每位學生都及格。"},{"en":"If ocean exploitation is unprecedented, old assumptions about endless fish are no longer safe.","zh":"如果海洋開發利用前所未有，關於魚類無盡的舊假設就不再安全。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises that the situation is historically new and extreme.","zh":"這個短語強調情況在歷史上既新且極端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"modern fishing technologies","meaning":"現代捕魚技術","examples":[{"en":"Modern fishing technologies allow fleets to locate fish more efficiently.","zh":"現代捕魚技術讓船隊更有效地定位魚類。"},{"en":"Modern fishing technologies are advanced tools, machines, and systems used to find and catch fish.","zh":"「modern fishing technologies」是用來尋找和捕捉魚類的先進工具、機器和系統。"},{"en":"GPS, sonar, stronger nets, and large freezer ships are examples of modern fishing technologies.","zh":"GPS、聲納、更強漁網和大型冷凍船都是現代捕魚技術的例子。"},{"en":"If technology makes fish easier to find, natural hiding places become less effective.","zh":"如果科技令魚更容易被找到，天然躲藏地點就變得較不有效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the equipment that increases fishing power.","zh":"這個短語描述增加捕魚能力的設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"leave fish no place to hide","meaning":"令魚類無處躲藏","examples":[{"en":"Advanced equipment leaves fish no place to hide.","zh":"先進設備令魚類無處躲藏。"},{"en":"To leave fish no place to hide means to make it almost impossible for fish to escape being found or caught.","zh":"「leave fish no place to hide」意思是令魚幾乎不可能逃過被發現或捕捉。"},{"en":"A classroom camera in every corner would leave students no place to hide from supervision.","zh":"如果課室每個角落都有攝影機，學生就無處避開監察。"},{"en":"If fishing technology can search deep and distant waters, fewer fish refuges remain.","zh":"如果捕魚科技能搜尋深水和遠海，剩下的魚類庇護地就更少。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses the loss of safety or refuge.","zh":"這個短語表達安全地點或庇護地的喪失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"refuges from fishing","meaning":"免受捕魚影響的庇護地","examples":[{"en":"Marine reserves provide refuges from fishing.","zh":"海洋保護區提供免受捕魚影響的庇護地。"},{"en":"Refuges from fishing are places where fish are protected from being caught.","zh":"「refuges from fishing」是魚類受到保護、不被捕撈的地方。"},{"en":"A quiet library corner can be a refuge from noise for students who need to focus.","zh":"安靜圖書館角落可以成為需要專注的學生逃離噪音的庇護地。"},{"en":"If fish have refuges from fishing, they can grow, breed, and help rebuild populations.","zh":"如果魚類有免受捕魚影響的庇護地，它們可以成長、繁殖並幫助重建種群。"},{"en":"The phrase describes safe spaces away from fishing pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述遠離捕魚壓力的安全空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"deliberately create","meaning":"刻意設立","examples":[{"en":"Today, most effective marine refuges are ones that humans deliberately create.","zh":"今天，大多數有效海洋庇護地都是人類刻意設立的。"},{"en":"To deliberately create something means to make it intentionally, not by accident.","zh":"「deliberately create」某物，意思是有意地製造或建立，而不是偶然形成。"},{"en":"A teacher may deliberately create mixed groups so stronger students can support weaker ones.","zh":"老師可能刻意設立混合小組，讓較強學生支援較弱學生。"},{"en":"If natural refuges disappear, people may need to create protected zones on purpose.","zh":"如果天然庇護地消失，人們可能需要有目的地建立保護區。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses conscious planning and intention.","zh":"這個短語強調有意識的規劃和意圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"trail far behind","meaning":"遠遠落後於……","examples":[{"en":"Marine protection trails far behind protection on land.","zh":"海洋保護遠遠落後於陸地保護。"},{"en":"To trail far behind means to make much less progress than another person, group, or area.","zh":"「trail far behind」意思是進展遠遠少於另一人、群體或範疇。"},{"en":"A student may trail far behind classmates if they miss several months of school.","zh":"如果學生缺課數月，可能遠遠落後於同學。"},{"en":"If ocean protection trails behind land protection, marine species remain more exposed to harm.","zh":"如果海洋保護落後於陸地保護，海洋物種仍更容易受害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large gap in progress.","zh":"這個短語描述進展上的巨大差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in terms of","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"The sea trails behind the land in terms of environmental protection.","zh":"就環境保護而言，海洋落後於陸地。"},{"en":"In terms of something means when considering that particular aspect.","zh":"「in terms of」某事，意思是從該方面考慮。"},{"en":"In terms of price, the smaller phone is the better choice.","zh":"就價格而言，較小的電話是較好選擇。"},{"en":"If we compare land and sea in terms of protection, the ocean is much less protected.","zh":"如果我們就保護程度比較陸地和海洋，海洋受到的保護少很多。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows the comparison to one area.","zh":"這個短語把比較收窄至某一方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the area and quality of protection","meaning":"保護範圍和質素","examples":[{"en":"Both the area and quality of marine protection remain inadequate.","zh":"海洋保護的範圍和質素仍然不足。"},{"en":"The area and quality of protection means how much space is protected and how strong that protection is.","zh":"「the area and quality of protection」意思是受保護空間有多大，以及保護有多強。"},{"en":"A park may have a large protected area but poor protection if illegal hunting continues.","zh":"如果非法狩獵持續，公園可能有很大保護範圍，但保護質素差。"},{"en":"If a marine reserve is small or weakly enforced, its protection may not be enough.","zh":"如果海洋保護區細小或執法薄弱，其保護可能不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds us that size and strictness both matter.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們面積和嚴格程度同樣重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fishing and commerce","meaning":"捕魚與商業活動","examples":[{"en":"Fishing and commerce have expanded across the world’s oceans.","zh":"捕魚與商業活動已擴展到世界各大洋。"},{"en":"Fishing and commerce means fishing activity and business or trade connected with the sea.","zh":"「fishing and commerce」意思是捕魚活動以及與海洋有關的商業或貿易。"},{"en":"Ports grow when fishing and commerce bring jobs, ships, and markets to a town.","zh":"當捕魚與商業活動為城鎮帶來工作、船隻和市場，港口就會發展。"},{"en":"If fishing and commerce expand without limits, marine ecosystems may suffer.","zh":"如果捕魚與商業活動無限制擴張，海洋生態系統可能受害。"},{"en":"The phrase links ocean use with economic activity.","zh":"這個短語把海洋使用與經濟活動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hold onto the notion that","meaning":"堅持……的觀念","examples":[{"en":"People have held onto the notion that the sea should remain freely accessible.","zh":"人們一直堅持海洋應維持自由進出的觀念。"},{"en":"To hold onto the notion that means to continue believing an idea, even when it is questioned.","zh":"「hold onto the notion that」意思是即使受到質疑，仍繼續相信某個想法。"},{"en":"Some parents hold onto the notion that children learn best only through strict discipline.","zh":"有些父母堅持孩子只靠嚴格紀律學得最好的觀念。"},{"en":"If people keep believing the ocean is free for all, they may resist conservation rules.","zh":"如果人們一直相信海洋人人可自由使用，可能抗拒保育規則。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a belief that persists strongly.","zh":"這個短語暗示某信念強烈地持續存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"view something as","meaning":"將……視為","examples":[{"en":"Many people still view the ocean as an unlimited public resource.","zh":"許多人仍將海洋視為無限的公共資源。"},{"en":"To view something as something means to see, understand, or treat it in that way.","zh":"「view something as」某物，意思是以那種方式看待、理解或對待它。"},{"en":"Some students view mistakes as chances to learn rather than signs of failure.","zh":"有些學生將錯誤視為學習機會，而不是失敗標誌。"},{"en":"If people view the sea as unlimited, they may not feel responsible for protecting it.","zh":"如果人們將海洋視為無限，他們可能不覺得自己有責任保護它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a way of thinking about something.","zh":"這個短語描述看待某事的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be free to come and go","meaning":"可自由進出","examples":[{"en":"People and nations expect to be free to come and go at will.","zh":"人們和國家期望可以任意自由進出。"},{"en":"To be free to come and go means to have the right or ability to enter and leave without restriction.","zh":"「be free to come and go」意思是有權或有能力在不受限制下進入和離開。"},{"en":"Visitors are free to come and go during museum opening hours.","zh":"參觀者在博物館開放時間內可自由進出。"},{"en":"If fishing fleets can come and go freely, controlling catches becomes harder.","zh":"如果漁船隊可以自由進出，控制捕獲量就更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unrestricted movement.","zh":"這個短語描述不受限制的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at will","meaning":"隨意地；任意地","examples":[{"en":"Fishing fleets have traditionally travelled across the seas at will.","zh":"漁船隊傳統上可在海上任意航行。"},{"en":"At will means whenever and however someone wants, without needing permission.","zh":"「at will」意思是隨時、以自己想要的方式，不需要許可。"},{"en":"In a flexible library, students may choose books at will from open shelves.","zh":"在彈性圖書館中，學生可以從開放書架上任意選書。"},{"en":"If boats fish at will, rules may be too weak to protect marine life.","zh":"如果船隻任意捕魚，規則可能太弱，無法保護海洋生命。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests freedom without strict control.","zh":"這個短語暗示沒有嚴格管制的自由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be free for us to exploit","meaning":"可供我們自由開發利用","examples":[{"en":"The ocean has often been treated as a resource that is free for us to exploit.","zh":"海洋常被當作可供我們自由開發利用的資源。"},{"en":"To be free for us to exploit means to be seen as available for human use without cost or limit.","zh":"「be free for us to exploit」意思是被視為可供人類無成本或無限制使用。"},{"en":"A forest should not be treated as free for anyone to exploit simply because no fence surrounds it.","zh":"森林不應只因沒有圍欄，就被視為任何人都可自由開發利用。"},{"en":"If people exploit a shared resource freely, they may damage it for everyone.","zh":"如果人們自由開發共享資源，可能令所有人都受損。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises careless use of nature.","zh":"這個短語批評對自然的粗心使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be reluctant to","meaning":"不願意；不情願","examples":[{"en":"Many governments have been reluctant to protect large areas of ocean.","zh":"許多政府一直不願意保護大片海洋。"},{"en":"To be reluctant to do something means to be unwilling or hesitant to do it.","zh":"「be reluctant to」做某事，意思是不願意或猶豫去做。"},{"en":"A student may be reluctant to ask questions because they fear sounding foolish.","zh":"學生可能因害怕顯得愚蠢而不願意發問。"},{"en":"If governments are reluctant to restrict fishing, conservation may be delayed.","zh":"如果政府不願限制捕魚，保育可能被延誤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes hesitation or unwillingness.","zh":"這個短語描述猶豫或不情願。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"protected areas have proliferated","meaning":"保護區大量增加","examples":[{"en":"Protected areas on land have proliferated as populations have grown.","zh":"隨着人口增長，陸地保護區已大量增加。"},{"en":"If protected areas have proliferated, their number has increased quickly or widely.","zh":"如果「protected areas have proliferated」，意思是保護區數量快速或廣泛增加。"},{"en":"Coffee shops have proliferated near the station because many commuters pass through.","zh":"車站附近咖啡店大量增加，因為很多通勤者經過。"},{"en":"If land reserves increase while marine reserves remain few, ocean protection falls behind.","zh":"如果陸地保護區增加而海洋保護區仍很少，海洋保護就落後。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rapid growth in number.","zh":"這個短語描述數量快速增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"human populations","meaning":"人口","examples":[{"en":"Growing human populations place additional pressure on natural resources.","zh":"不斷增長的人口對自然資源造成額外壓力。"},{"en":"Human populations are groups or numbers of people living in particular places or across the world.","zh":"「human populations」是生活在特定地方或全球的人群或人數。"},{"en":"Human populations in cities need housing, transport, food, and clean water.","zh":"城市人口需要住屋、交通、食物和潔淨食水。"},{"en":"If human populations grow, demand for fish and other resources may also increase.","zh":"如果人口增長，對魚類和其他資源的需求也可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes people collectively as a population.","zh":"這個短語把人作為整體人口來描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Compared with the ocean, a much larger proportion of land is protected.","zh":"與海洋相比，受保護的陸地比例大得多。"},{"en":"Compared with means when one thing is examined in relation to another.","zh":"「compared with」意思是把一件事與另一件事放在一起考察。"},{"en":"Compared with buses, trains may be faster during rush hour.","zh":"與巴士相比，火車在繁忙時間可能較快。"},{"en":"If land is more protected than sea, conservation policy is uneven.","zh":"如果陸地比海洋受到更多保護，保育政策就不平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a direct comparison.","zh":"這個短語引出直接比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"make greater headway","meaning":"取得較大進展","examples":[{"en":"Humanity has made greater headway in protecting wildlife on land.","zh":"人類在保護陸地野生生物方面取得較大進展。"},{"en":"To make greater headway means to make more progress than before or than another area.","zh":"「make greater headway」意思是比以前或比另一範疇取得更多進展。"},{"en":"A student makes greater headway in writing when feedback is specific and regular.","zh":"當回饋具體而定期，學生在寫作上會取得較大進展。"},{"en":"If land conservation has made progress but ocean conservation has not, priorities may need to change.","zh":"如果陸地保育有進展而海洋保育沒有，優先事項可能需要改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes meaningful progress.","zh":"這個短語描述有意義的進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in our struggle to","meaning":"在我們努力……的過程中","examples":[{"en":"Protected areas help in our struggle to conserve biodiversity.","zh":"保護區在我們努力保育生物多樣性的過程中有幫助。"},{"en":"In our struggle to do something means in our difficult effort to achieve it.","zh":"「in our struggle to」做某事，意思是在我們艱難努力達成它的過程中。"},{"en":"Libraries help in our struggle to improve literacy among children.","zh":"圖書館在我們努力提升兒童讀寫能力的過程中有幫助。"},{"en":"If conserving biodiversity is difficult, protected areas become important tools.","zh":"如果保育生物多樣性很困難，保護區就成為重要工具。"},{"en":"The phrase makes the effort sound serious and ongoing.","zh":"這個短語令努力顯得嚴肅且持續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"maintain the richness and variety of","meaning":"維持……的豐富性和多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Conservation aims to maintain the richness and variety of wildlife.","zh":"保育旨在維持野生生物的豐富性和多樣性。"},{"en":"To maintain the richness and variety of something means to keep its many forms, types, and qualities alive.","zh":"「maintain the richness and variety of」某物，意思是保持其多種形式、類型和特質存在。"},{"en":"Schools can maintain the richness and variety of local culture by teaching dialects, songs, and festivals.","zh":"學校可以透過教授方言、歌曲和節日來維持本地文化的豐富性和多樣性。"},{"en":"If too many species disappear, ecosystems lose richness and become less stable.","zh":"如果太多物種消失，生態系統會失去豐富性並變得較不穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes protecting diversity and abundance.","zh":"這個短語描述保護多樣性和豐富性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"wildlife and landscape","meaning":"野生生物和自然景觀","examples":[{"en":"Protected areas conserve both wildlife and landscape.","zh":"保護區同時保育野生生物和自然景觀。"},{"en":"Wildlife and landscape means animals, plants, and the natural scenery or landforms around them.","zh":"「wildlife and landscape」意思是動植物，以及它們周圍的自然景色或地貌。"},{"en":"A national park protects wildlife and landscape by limiting construction and hunting.","zh":"國家公園透過限制建築和狩獵來保護野生生物和自然景觀。"},{"en":"If the landscape is damaged, wildlife may lose shelter, food, and breeding places.","zh":"如果自然景觀受損，野生生物可能失去棲息地、食物和繁殖地。"},{"en":"The phrase links living species with their physical environment.","zh":"這個短語把生物物種與其物理環境連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be contained in","meaning":"被納入……之中","examples":[{"en":"A significant proportion of the world’s land is contained in protected areas.","zh":"世界陸地中相當大比例被納入保護區之中。"},{"en":"To be contained in something means to be included within it.","zh":"「be contained in」某物，意思是被包括在其中。"},{"en":"The answer to the question is contained in the second paragraph of the passage.","zh":"該問題的答案被包含在文章第二段中。"},{"en":"If land is contained in a protected area, certain activities may be limited there.","zh":"如果土地被納入保護區，某些活動可能在那裡受到限制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being inside a larger category or space.","zh":"這個短語描述處於較大類別或空間之內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the corresponding figure","meaning":"相應數字","examples":[{"en":"The corresponding figure for protected ocean is much lower.","zh":"受保護海洋的相應數字低得多。"},{"en":"The corresponding figure means the matching number used for comparison in another category.","zh":"「the corresponding figure」意思是在另一類別中用作比較的相應數字。"},{"en":"If 80% of boys passed the test, the corresponding figure for girls was 85%.","zh":"如果80%男生通過測驗，女生的相應數字是85%。"},{"en":"If the land figure is high but the ocean figure is low, the gap becomes clear.","zh":"如果陸地數字高而海洋數字低，差距就變得清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when comparing statistics.","zh":"這個短語適合用於比較數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"three-fifths of one percent","meaning":"百分之零點六","examples":[{"en":"Only three-fifths of one percent of the sea was fully protected.","zh":"只有百分之零點六的海洋受到全面保護。"},{"en":"Three-fifths of one percent means 0.6 percent.","zh":"「three-fifths of one percent」意思是百分之零點六。"},{"en":"If only three-fifths of one percent of a budget is spent on repairs, maintenance may be inadequate.","zh":"如果維修只佔預算百分之零點六，保養可能不足。"},{"en":"If such a tiny share of the sea is fully protected, most marine life remains exposed.","zh":"如果只有這麼小比例的海洋受到全面保護，大部分海洋生命仍暴露於風險中。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses a very small proportion.","zh":"這個短語表達非常小的比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"worse still","meaning":"更糟的是","examples":[{"en":"Worse still, many marine protected areas continue to permit fishing.","zh":"更糟的是，許多海洋保護區仍容許捕魚。"},{"en":"Worse still means even worse than what has just been mentioned.","zh":"「worse still」意思是比剛提到的情況更糟。"},{"en":"The bus was late; worse still, it was too full to board.","zh":"巴士遲到；更糟的是，它太滿而不能上車。"},{"en":"If protected areas are already few and many still allow fishing, the problem becomes more serious.","zh":"如果保護區已經很少，而很多仍容許捕魚，問題就變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an additional negative point.","zh":"這個短語引出額外負面點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"marine protected areas","meaning":"海洋保護區","examples":[{"en":"Marine protected areas vary greatly in the level of protection they provide.","zh":"海洋保護區提供的保護程度差異很大。"},{"en":"Marine protected areas are parts of the sea managed to protect marine life, habitats, or ecosystems.","zh":"「marine protected areas」是為保護海洋生命、棲息地或生態系統而管理的海域。"},{"en":"A marine protected area may ban fishing, restrict tourism, or protect coral reefs.","zh":"海洋保護區可能禁止捕魚、限制旅遊或保護珊瑚礁。"},{"en":"If rules are weak, a marine protected area may protect little in practice.","zh":"如果規則薄弱，海洋保護區在實際上可能保護很少。"},{"en":"The phrase names ocean zones created for conservation.","zh":"這個短語指出為保育而設的海洋區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"allow fishing to continue","meaning":"容許捕魚繼續","examples":[{"en":"Many supposedly protected areas allow fishing to continue.","zh":"許多所謂保護區仍容許捕魚繼續。"},{"en":"To allow fishing to continue means to permit people to keep catching fish in an area.","zh":"「allow fishing to continue」意思是准許人們在某區繼續捕魚。"},{"en":"A lake park may allow fishing to continue only on weekends and only with permits.","zh":"湖泊公園可能只在週末並只持許可證時容許捕魚繼續。"},{"en":"If fishing continues inside a reserve, fish populations may not recover fully.","zh":"如果保護區內捕魚繼續，魚類種群可能無法完全恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase describes permission for ongoing fishing activity.","zh":"這個短語描述對持續捕魚活動的許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be off-limits to","meaning":"禁止……進入或使用","examples":[{"en":"Some marine areas are completely off-limits to fishing.","zh":"有些海域完全禁止捕魚。"},{"en":"To be off-limits to someone or something means to be forbidden or not allowed.","zh":"「be off-limits to」某人或某事，意思是被禁止或不容許。"},{"en":"The science lab is off-limits to students unless a teacher is present.","zh":"除非老師在場，科學實驗室禁止學生進入。"},{"en":"If an area is off-limits to fishing, fish can breed without direct capture pressure.","zh":"如果某區禁止捕魚，魚類可以在沒有直接捕撈壓力下繁殖。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strict prohibition.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴格禁止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"all exploitation","meaning":"一切開發利用","examples":[{"en":"Only a tiny fraction of the oceans is protected from all exploitation.","zh":"只有極小部分海洋受到保護，免受一切開發利用。"},{"en":"All exploitation means every form of using or extracting resources from an area.","zh":"「all exploitation」意思是對某區進行的所有資源使用或開採形式。"},{"en":"A forest protected from all exploitation would not allow logging, mining, or hunting.","zh":"免受一切開發利用的森林不會容許伐木、採礦或狩獵。"},{"en":"If a marine area is protected from all exploitation, fishing and resource extraction are stopped.","zh":"如果海域免受一切開發利用，捕魚和資源開採都會停止。"},{"en":"The phrase describes complete protection from human use.","zh":"這個短語描述免受人類使用的全面保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"something like","meaning":"大約；差不多","examples":[{"en":"Fully protected areas cover something like one five-thousandth of the oceans.","zh":"全面保護區覆蓋大約五千分之一的海洋。"},{"en":"Something like means approximately or roughly.","zh":"「something like」意思是大約或差不多。"},{"en":"The walk to school takes something like twenty minutes.","zh":"步行上學大約需要二十分鐘。"},{"en":"If a protected area covers something like a tiny fraction, the exact number is less important than its smallness.","zh":"如果保護區覆蓋差不多只是極小比例，精確數字不如其細小程度重要。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate figure.","zh":"這個短語提供近似數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the total area of","meaning":"……的總面積","examples":[{"en":"Strict reserves cover only a tiny share of the total area of the world’s seas.","zh":"嚴格保護區只覆蓋世界海洋總面積的極小部分。"},{"en":"The total area of something means the full amount of space it covers.","zh":"「the total area of」某物，意思是它覆蓋的完整空間量。"},{"en":"The total area of a classroom includes the space under desks and around the door.","zh":"課室總面積包括桌下和門口周圍的空間。"},{"en":"If a reserve protects only a tiny share of the total sea area, most ocean space remains unprotected.","zh":"如果保護區只保護海洋總面積中的極小部分，大多數海洋空間仍未受保護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes complete spatial extent.","zh":"這個短語描述完整空間範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"belatedly come to realise","meaning":"遲來地開始明白","examples":[{"en":"Governments are belatedly coming to realise the value of natural refuges.","zh":"政府正遲來地開始明白天然庇護地的價值。"},{"en":"To belatedly come to realise something means to understand it late, after a delay.","zh":"「belatedly come to realise」某事，意思是延遲後才明白它。"},{"en":"A student may belatedly realise that daily revision was needed only after failing a test.","zh":"學生可能在考試失敗後，才遲來地明白需要每日溫習。"},{"en":"If governments recognise marine refuges too late, some ecosystems may already be damaged.","zh":"如果政府太遲認識海洋庇護地，有些生態系統可能已受損。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests delayed understanding.","zh":"這個短語暗示理解來得太遲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"natural refuges","meaning":"天然庇護地","examples":[{"en":"Natural refuges once protected fish from intensive fishing.","zh":"天然庇護地曾保護魚類免受密集捕魚影響。"},{"en":"Natural refuges are places in nature where animals are naturally safer from danger or human activity.","zh":"「natural refuges」是自然界中動物自然較安全、較少受危險或人類活動影響的地方。"},{"en":"A rocky cliff can be a natural refuge for birds that need safe nesting places.","zh":"岩石懸崖可以成為需要安全築巢地點的雀鳥的天然庇護地。"},{"en":"If deep waters once protected fish, technology can remove that natural refuge.","zh":"如果深水曾保護魚類，科技可以消除那種天然庇護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes protection created by geography or nature, not by law.","zh":"這個短語描述由地理或自然形成，而非法律設立的保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"play a critical role in","meaning":"在……中發揮關鍵作用","examples":[{"en":"Natural refuges play a critical role in sustaining fish populations.","zh":"天然庇護地在維持魚類種群方面發揮關鍵作用。"},{"en":"To play a critical role in something means to be extremely important to it.","zh":"「play a critical role in」某事，意思是對它極其重要。"},{"en":"Parents play a critical role in helping young children build reading habits.","zh":"父母在幫助幼兒建立閱讀習慣方面發揮關鍵作用。"},{"en":"If refuges protect breeding fish, they become essential for future fish stocks.","zh":"如果庇護地保護繁殖中的魚，它們就對未來魚類資源至關重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a key function in success or survival.","zh":"這個短語描述成功或生存中的關鍵功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sustain fisheries","meaning":"維持漁業","examples":[{"en":"Healthy ecosystems help sustain fisheries over the long term.","zh":"健康生態系統有助長期維持漁業。"},{"en":"To sustain fisheries means to keep fish populations and fishing livelihoods continuing without collapse.","zh":"「sustain fisheries」意思是保持魚類種群和捕魚生計持續，而不崩潰。"},{"en":"A village can sustain fisheries by limiting catches during breeding seasons.","zh":"村莊可以透過在繁殖季節限制捕撈來維持漁業。"},{"en":"If young fish survive and reproduce, fisheries can continue feeding people.","zh":"如果幼魚存活並繁殖，漁業就能繼續為人們提供食物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes maintaining fishing resources for the future.","zh":"這個短語描述為未來維持捕魚資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"healthy and diverse marine ecosystems","meaning":"健康而多樣化的海洋生態系統","examples":[{"en":"Marine reserves support healthy and diverse marine ecosystems.","zh":"海洋保護區支持健康而多樣化的海洋生態系統。"},{"en":"Healthy and diverse marine ecosystems are ocean environments with many species and functioning natural processes.","zh":"「healthy and diverse marine ecosystems」是有許多物種和正常自然過程的海洋環境。"},{"en":"A coral reef with fish, turtles, seaweed, and clean water is a healthy and diverse marine ecosystem.","zh":"有魚、海龜、海藻和潔淨水的珊瑚礁，是健康而多樣化的海洋生態系統。"},{"en":"If ecosystems are healthy and diverse, they can better resist shocks and support fisheries.","zh":"如果生態系統健康而多樣化，它們較能抵抗衝擊並支持漁業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong ocean systems with rich life.","zh":"這個短語描述生命豐富而強健的海洋系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"rebuild fisheries","meaning":"恢復漁業資源","examples":[{"en":"Marine reserves can help rebuild fisheries but cannot do so alone.","zh":"海洋保護區可以幫助恢復漁業資源，但不能單獨做到。"},{"en":"To rebuild fisheries means to restore fish populations and fishing productivity after decline.","zh":"「rebuild fisheries」意思是在衰退後恢復魚類種群和漁業生產力。"},{"en":"A coastal community may rebuild fisheries by protecting breeding areas and reducing catches.","zh":"沿海社區可以透過保護繁殖區和減少捕獲量來恢復漁業資源。"},{"en":"If reserves allow fish to grow and reproduce, nearby fishing grounds may recover.","zh":"如果保護區讓魚成長和繁殖，附近漁場可能恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repairing damaged fishing resources.","zh":"這個短語描述修復受損捕魚資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"on their own","meaning":"單靠本身","examples":[{"en":"Marine reserves cannot solve every fisheries problem on their own.","zh":"海洋保護區單靠本身不能解決所有漁業問題。"},{"en":"On their own means alone, without help from other measures or people.","zh":"「on their own」意思是單獨地，沒有其他措施或人幫助。"},{"en":"A student cannot improve writing on their own if they never receive feedback.","zh":"如果學生從不接受回饋，單靠自己可能難以改善寫作。"},{"en":"If reserves are not combined with catch limits, overfishing may continue outside them.","zh":"如果保護區沒有與捕獲限制結合，過度捕魚可能在區外繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that one solution alone is not enough.","zh":"這個短語強調單一解決方法不足夠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"management measures","meaning":"管理措施","examples":[{"en":"Additional management measures are required to control fishing pressure.","zh":"需要額外管理措施來控制捕魚壓力。"},{"en":"Management measures are rules, actions, or systems used to control and organise an activity.","zh":"「management measures」是用來控制和組織活動的規則、行動或系統。"},{"en":"A school may use management measures such as sign-up lists to prevent overcrowding in clubs.","zh":"學校可能使用報名表等管理措施，防止學會過度擁擠。"},{"en":"If fishing pressure is high, measures such as catch limits and protected zones may be needed.","zh":"如果捕魚壓力高，可能需要捕獲限制和保護區等措施。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical tools for control.","zh":"這個短語描述用於管控的實際工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"constitute","meaning":"構成","examples":[{"en":"Fully protected areas constitute an essential part of fisheries reform.","zh":"全面保護區構成漁業改革的重要部分。"},{"en":"To constitute something means to form or make up that thing.","zh":"「constitute」意思是形成或組成某事物。"},{"en":"Clear rules and fair marking constitute an important part of a good exam system.","zh":"清楚規則和公平評分構成良好考試制度的重要部分。"},{"en":"If reserves constitute part of reform, they are not optional decoration but a real component.","zh":"如果保護區構成改革的一部分，它們就不是可有可無的裝飾，而是真正組成部分。"},{"en":"The word describes what forms a larger whole.","zh":"這個詞描述甚麼組成較大的整體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a package of reform","meaning":"一套改革措施","examples":[{"en":"Marine reserves form part of a broader package of reform.","zh":"海洋保護區構成更廣泛一套改革措施的一部分。"},{"en":"A package of reform is a group of changes designed to fix a system.","zh":"「a package of reform」是一組旨在修正某系統的改變。"},{"en":"A school may introduce a package of reform including smaller classes, better training, and new textbooks.","zh":"學校可能推出一套改革措施，包括縮小班級、改善培訓和新課本。"},{"en":"If fisheries need many changes, reserves should work with other rules and policies.","zh":"如果漁業需要許多改變，保護區應與其他規則和政策配合。"},{"en":"The phrase describes several reforms used together.","zh":"這個短語描述多項改革一起使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fisheries management","meaning":"漁業管理","examples":[{"en":"Effective fisheries management must combine protection and regulation.","zh":"有效漁業管理必須結合保護和規管。"},{"en":"Fisheries management is the planning and control of fishing so fish populations and livelihoods can continue.","zh":"「fisheries management」是對捕魚作出規劃和控制，使魚類種群和生計能持續。"},{"en":"Fisheries management may include catch limits, seasons, licences, and marine reserves.","zh":"漁業管理可能包括捕獲限制、季節、牌照和海洋保護區。"},{"en":"If fisheries management fails, fish stocks may collapse and fishing communities may suffer.","zh":"如果漁業管理失敗，魚類資源可能崩潰，漁業社區可能受苦。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised control of fishing activity.","zh":"這個短語描述對捕魚活動的有組織控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"underpin and enhance","meaning":"支持並加強","examples":[{"en":"Marine reserves underpin and enhance other conservation efforts.","zh":"海洋保護區支持並加強其他保育工作。"},{"en":"To underpin and enhance something means to support it at a basic level and make it stronger.","zh":"「underpin and enhance」某事，意思是在基礎層面支持它並令它更強。"},{"en":"Good grammar underpins and enhances clear writing.","zh":"良好文法支持並加強清晰寫作。"},{"en":"If reserves support catch limits and habitat protection, the whole conservation system becomes stronger.","zh":"如果保護區支持捕獲限制和棲息地保護，整個保育系統會變得更強。"},{"en":"The phrase combines foundation and improvement.","zh":"這個短語結合基礎支撐和改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"other efforts","meaning":"其他工作；其他努力","examples":[{"en":"Strict reserves can strengthen other efforts to restore fish stocks.","zh":"嚴格保護區可以加強恢復魚類資源量的其他工作。"},{"en":"Other efforts are additional actions taken alongside the main measure.","zh":"「other efforts」是與主要措施並行的額外行動。"},{"en":"A student’s tutoring works better when other efforts, such as reading and revision, continue at home.","zh":"如果學生在家繼續閱讀和溫習等其他努力，補習效果會更好。"},{"en":"If marine reserves support other efforts, conservation becomes more complete.","zh":"如果海洋保護區支持其他工作，保育就更完整。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to extra supporting actions.","zh":"這個短語指額外支援行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"limits to protection","meaning":"保護措施的局限","examples":[{"en":"There are limits to what environmental protection can achieve.","zh":"環境保護能達成的事情有其局限。"},{"en":"Limits to protection are the points beyond which protection cannot fully solve a problem.","zh":"「limits to protection」是保護無法完全解決問題的界限。"},{"en":"A helmet reduces injury risk, but there are limits to protection if a crash is severe.","zh":"頭盔降低受傷風險，但如果撞擊嚴重，保護仍有局限。"},{"en":"If a species has disappeared globally, ordinary protection can no longer save it.","zh":"如果某物種已全球消失，普通保護就再也不能拯救它。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds us that prevention must happen before damage becomes irreversible.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，預防必須在損害不可逆前發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bring back","meaning":"令……重現；挽回","examples":[{"en":"Conservation cannot bring back a species that has disappeared globally.","zh":"保育不能令一個已全球消失的物種重現。"},{"en":"To bring back something means to restore it or make it return.","zh":"「bring back」某物，意思是恢復它或令它回來。"},{"en":"A school may bring back a reading club if enough students show interest.","zh":"如果有足夠學生表示興趣，學校可能恢復閱讀學會。"},{"en":"If a species is globally extinct, humans cannot simply bring it back through protection.","zh":"如果物種已全球絕種，人類不能單靠保護令它重現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes restoring something lost.","zh":"這個短語描述恢復失去的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"die out","meaning":"絕種","examples":[{"en":"A species dies out when its last surviving population disappears.","zh":"當某物種最後僅存的種群消失時，該物種便絕種。"},{"en":"To die out means to disappear completely because no living members remain.","zh":"「die out」意思是因沒有存活成員而完全消失。"},{"en":"A local tradition may die out if young people never learn or practise it.","zh":"如果年輕人從不學習或實踐，本地傳統可能消失。"},{"en":"If a fish species dies out, it can no longer reproduce or return naturally.","zh":"如果魚類物種絕種，它就再不能繁殖或自然回來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extinction or disappearance over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間滅絕或消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"resurrect extinct species","meaning":"令已絕種物種復活","examples":[{"en":"Science cannot currently resurrect globally extinct species.","zh":"科學目前不能令全球已絕種物種復活。"},{"en":"To resurrect extinct species means to bring species that have disappeared completely back to life.","zh":"「resurrect extinct species」意思是令已完全消失的物種重新活過來。"},{"en":"Films may imagine scientists resurrecting dinosaurs, but real conservation is much harder.","zh":"電影可能想像科學家令恐龍復活，但真實保育困難得多。"},{"en":"If a species is already gone everywhere, protecting habitat alone cannot restore it.","zh":"如果物種已在各地消失，單靠保護棲息地不能恢復它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a dramatic return from extinction.","zh":"這個短語描述從絕種中戲劇性回歸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"globally extinct species","meaning":"全球已絕種物種","examples":[{"en":"Globally extinct species cannot be restored through ordinary conservation.","zh":"全球已絕種物種不能透過普通保育恢復。"},{"en":"Globally extinct species are species with no living individuals anywhere in the world.","zh":"「globally extinct species」是世界任何地方都沒有存活個體的物種。"},{"en":"The dodo is a well-known example of a globally extinct species.","zh":"渡渡鳥是著名的全球已絕種物種例子。"},{"en":"If a species is globally extinct, no remaining population exists to rebuild it naturally.","zh":"如果物種全球已絕種，就沒有僅餘種群可自然重建它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes total extinction across the planet.","zh":"這個短語描述遍及全球的完全絕種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"locally extinct animals","meaning":"在本地已絕種的動物","examples":[{"en":"Locally extinct animals may sometimes be reintroduced from elsewhere.","zh":"在本地已絕種的動物有時可以從其他地方重新引入。"},{"en":"Locally extinct animals are animals that have disappeared from one area but still survive somewhere else.","zh":"「locally extinct animals」是在某地已消失，但仍在其他地方存活的動物。"},{"en":"A bird may be locally extinct in one city but common in another country.","zh":"一種鳥可能在某城市本地絕種，但在另一國家仍很常見。"},{"en":"If animals still exist elsewhere, conservationists may bring them back to a suitable habitat.","zh":"如果動物仍在其他地方存在，保育人士可能把它們帶回合適棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes regional disappearance, not global extinction.","zh":"這個短語描述地區性消失，而不是全球絕種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"require reintroductions","meaning":"需要重新引入","examples":[{"en":"Restoring a lost population may require reintroductions from another region.","zh":"恢復失去的種群可能需要從另一地區重新引入。"},{"en":"To require reintroductions means to need animals or plants to be brought back from elsewhere.","zh":"「require reintroductions」意思是需要從其他地方把動物或植物帶回來。"},{"en":"A forest may require reintroduction of native birds if local populations have vanished.","zh":"如果本地種群消失，森林可能需要重新引入本土雀鳥。"},{"en":"If natural return is unlikely, conservationists may move individuals into the area deliberately.","zh":"如果自然回歸不大可能，保育人士可能刻意把個體遷入該區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active restoration by bringing species back.","zh":"這個短語描述透過帶回物種進行主動恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"natural dispersal","meaning":"自然擴散","examples":[{"en":"Natural dispersal may allow animals to recolonise suitable habitats.","zh":"自然擴散可能讓動物重新定居於合適棲息地。"},{"en":"Natural dispersal is the process by which animals, plants, or seeds spread to new areas by themselves.","zh":"「natural dispersal」是動物、植物或種子自行擴展到新地區的過程。"},{"en":"Birds may reach a new island through natural dispersal after a storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，鳥類可能透過自然擴散到達新島嶼。"},{"en":"If remaining populations are close enough, natural dispersal may restore an empty habitat.","zh":"如果僅餘種群距離足夠近，自然擴散可能恢復空置棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement without human reintroduction.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有人工重新引入的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"remaining populations","meaning":"僅餘的種群","examples":[{"en":"Small remaining populations may be unable to restore former habitats naturally.","zh":"細小僅餘種群可能無法自然恢復過往棲息地。"},{"en":"Remaining populations are the groups of a species that still survive after decline or disappearance elsewhere.","zh":"「remaining populations」是某物種在其他地方衰退或消失後仍存活的群體。"},{"en":"A few remaining populations of a rare frog may survive in protected wetlands.","zh":"稀有青蛙的幾個僅餘種群可能在受保護濕地中存活。"},{"en":"If remaining populations are too small or far away, natural recovery becomes difficult.","zh":"如果僅餘種群太小或太遠，自然恢復就變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to survivors left after loss.","zh":"這個短語指損失後留下的倖存群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be insufficient","meaning":"不足夠","examples":[{"en":"Natural dispersal may be insufficient to restore a locally extinct species.","zh":"自然擴散可能不足以恢復本地已絕種物種。"},{"en":"To be insufficient means to be not enough for the purpose.","zh":"「be insufficient」意思是不足以達成目的。"},{"en":"One hour of sleep is insufficient for most students before an exam.","zh":"對大多數學生而言，考試前睡一小時是不足夠的。"},{"en":"If too few animals remain nearby, natural dispersal may not rebuild the population.","zh":"如果附近僅餘動物太少，自然擴散可能無法重建種群。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a lack of enough quantity or strength.","zh":"這個短語描述數量或力量不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in cases such as","meaning":"在……這類個案中","examples":[{"en":"In cases such as northern cod, fishing has transformed the ecosystem.","zh":"在北方鱈魚這類個案中，捕魚已改變生態系統。"},{"en":"In cases such as means in examples like the one mentioned.","zh":"「in cases such as」意思是在像所提及例子這類情況中。"},{"en":"In cases such as exam anxiety, sleep and preparation both matter.","zh":"在考試焦慮這類個案中，睡眠和準備都重要。"},{"en":"If one case shows deep ecosystem change, it can warn us about similar situations elsewhere.","zh":"如果一個個案顯示深層生態改變，它可以警告其他地方的相似情況。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a specific example of a wider problem.","zh":"這個短語引出更廣泛問題中的具體例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"northern cod","meaning":"北方鱈魚","examples":[{"en":"Northern cod populations in Canada collapsed after severe overfishing.","zh":"加拿大北方鱈魚種群在嚴重過度捕魚後崩潰。"},{"en":"Northern cod are cod fish populations found in colder northern Atlantic waters, especially near Canada.","zh":"「northern cod」是生活於較寒冷北大西洋海域，尤其加拿大附近的鱈魚種群。"},{"en":"A lesson on fisheries may use northern cod as an example of overfishing and collapse.","zh":"漁業課可能用北方鱈魚作為過度捕魚和崩潰的例子。"},{"en":"If northern cod decline sharply, fishing communities that depend on them suffer too.","zh":"如果北方鱈魚急劇減少，依賴它們的漁業社區也會受苦。"},{"en":"The phrase names a fish stock strongly associated with fisheries collapse.","zh":"這個短語指出與漁業崩潰密切相關的魚類資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"shift ecosystems into different states","meaning":"使生態系統轉變成不同狀態","examples":[{"en":"Intensive fishing can shift ecosystems into different states.","zh":"密集捕魚可以使生態系統轉變成不同狀態。"},{"en":"To shift ecosystems into different states means to change them into new forms with different species and processes.","zh":"「shift ecosystems into different states」意思是把生態系統改變成有不同物種和過程的新形態。"},{"en":"Too much pollution can shift a clear pond into a green, algae-filled state.","zh":"過多污染可以使清澈池塘轉變成充滿綠藻的狀態。"},{"en":"If predators are removed, the whole food web may reorganise around other species.","zh":"如果捕食者被移除，整個食物網可能圍繞其他物種重新組織。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep ecological transformation.","zh":"這個短語描述深層生態轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"different mixes of species","meaning":"不同的物種組合","examples":[{"en":"Altered ecosystems may support different mixes of species.","zh":"已改變的生態系統可能支持不同的物種組合。"},{"en":"Different mixes of species means different combinations of plants, animals, or organisms living together.","zh":"「different mixes of species」意思是不同動植物或生物共同生活的組合。"},{"en":"A city park and a mountain forest contain different mixes of species.","zh":"城市公園和山林有不同的物種組合。"},{"en":"If large fish disappear, smaller or less desirable species may become more common.","zh":"如果大型魚類消失，較小或較不理想的物種可能變得更常見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changes in which species dominate an ecosystem.","zh":"這個短語描述哪些物種主導生態系統的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prevail","meaning":"佔優勢；盛行","examples":[{"en":"After ecological change, less desirable species may prevail.","zh":"生態改變後，較不理想的物種可能佔優勢。"},{"en":"To prevail means to become dominant, common, or successful in a situation.","zh":"「prevail」意思是在某情況中變得主導、常見或成功。"},{"en":"In a noisy classroom, confusion may prevail if the teacher gives unclear instructions.","zh":"在嘈吵課室中，如果老師指示不清，混亂可能盛行。"},{"en":"If major fish are removed, species with fewer predators may prevail.","zh":"如果主要魚類被移除，天敵較少的物種可能佔優勢。"},{"en":"The word describes one thing becoming stronger than others.","zh":"這個詞描述某事物變得比其他事物更強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"less desirable","meaning":"較不理想的","examples":[{"en":"The species that replace major fish stocks may be less desirable commercially.","zh":"取代主要魚類資源的物種在商業上可能較不理想。"},{"en":"Less desirable means less wanted, useful, valuable, or attractive.","zh":"「less desirable」意思是較不被想要、較不有用、較不有價值或較不吸引。"},{"en":"A flat far from transport may be less desirable than one near a station.","zh":"遠離交通的單位可能比近車站的單位較不理想。"},{"en":"If valuable fish are replaced by less desirable species, fisheries may earn less money.","zh":"如果有價值魚類被較不理想物種取代，漁業收入可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase shows lower value or preference.","zh":"這個短語顯示較低價值或偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"prime fishing targets","meaning":"主要捕撈目標","examples":[{"en":"Many prime fishing targets have declined sharply.","zh":"許多主要捕撈目標已急劇下降。"},{"en":"Prime fishing targets are the species fishers most want to catch because they are valuable or popular.","zh":"「prime fishing targets」是漁民最想捕捉的物種，因為它們有價值或受歡迎。"},{"en":"Tuna and cod can be prime fishing targets in some markets.","zh":"在某些市場中，吞拿魚和鱈魚可以是主要捕撈目標。"},{"en":"If prime targets decline, fleets may turn to smaller or less valuable species.","zh":"如果主要目標減少，船隊可能轉向較小或較低價值物種。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the main species sought by fishers.","zh":"這個短語指漁民主要尋找的物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be much reduced in numbers","meaning":"數量大幅減少","examples":[{"en":"Some commercially important species are much reduced in numbers.","zh":"有些商業上重要的物種數量大幅減少。"},{"en":"To be much reduced in numbers means to have far fewer individuals than before.","zh":"「be much reduced in numbers」意思是個體數量比以前少很多。"},{"en":"A school club may be much reduced in numbers after many senior students graduate.","zh":"許多高年級學生畢業後，學會人數可能大幅減少。"},{"en":"If fish numbers are greatly reduced, breeding and recovery become harder.","zh":"如果魚類數量大幅減少，繁殖和恢復就變得更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a serious population decline.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重種群下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be difficult to reverse","meaning":"難以逆轉","examples":[{"en":"Changes to marine food webs may be difficult to reverse.","zh":"海洋食物網的變化可能難以逆轉。"},{"en":"To be difficult to reverse means to be hard to undo or return to the original condition.","zh":"「be difficult to reverse」意思是難以取消、修復或回到原本狀態。"},{"en":"Bad study habits can be difficult to reverse if they last for years.","zh":"如果壞學習習慣持續多年，可能難以逆轉。"},{"en":"If an ecosystem shifts to a new state, simply stopping fishing may not restore it quickly.","zh":"如果生態系統轉入新狀態，單純停止捕魚未必能快速恢復它。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that damage may not be easily undone.","zh":"這個短語警告損害未必容易修復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a complete moratorium on","meaning":"對……的全面暫停","examples":[{"en":"Even a complete moratorium on fishing may not restore an altered ecosystem.","zh":"即使全面暫停捕魚，也未必能恢復已改變的生態系統。"},{"en":"A complete moratorium on something is a full temporary ban or suspension of that activity.","zh":"「a complete moratorium on」某事，是對該活動的全面臨時禁止或暫停。"},{"en":"A school may place a complete moratorium on outdoor sports during dangerous weather.","zh":"在危險天氣期間，學校可能全面暫停戶外運動。"},{"en":"If fishing damage has changed the ecosystem deeply, a ban alone may not be enough.","zh":"如果捕魚傷害已深深改變生態系統，單靠禁令可能不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a total pause in an activity.","zh":"這個短語描述對某活動的全面停止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the Mediterranean sailed by Ulysses","meaning":"Ulysses 航行過的地中海","examples":[{"en":"The ancient Mediterranean associated with Ulysses supported abundant marine life.","zh":"與 Ulysses 有關的古代地中海孕育大量海洋生命。"},{"en":"The Mediterranean sailed by Ulysses refers to the ancient sea world imagined in Greek legend.","zh":"「the Mediterranean sailed by Ulysses」指希臘傳說中想像的古代地中海世界。"},{"en":"A literature teacher may mention Ulysses when discussing ancient journeys across the Mediterranean.","zh":"文學老師討論古代地中海航行時，可能提到 Ulysses。"},{"en":"If the ancient Mediterranean held more wildlife, modern decline becomes clearer by comparison.","zh":"如果古代地中海有更多野生生物，現代衰退透過比較就更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase uses a legendary reference to describe an older, richer sea.","zh":"這個短語用傳說典故描述較古老、較豐富的海洋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"legendary king","meaning":"傳說中的國王","examples":[{"en":"Ulysses was a legendary king of ancient Greece.","zh":"Ulysses 是古希臘傳說中的國王。"},{"en":"A legendary king is a ruler known mainly through old stories, myths, or heroic tales.","zh":"「legendary king」是主要透過古老故事、神話或英雄傳說而聞名的統治者。"},{"en":"King Arthur is often described as a legendary king in British stories.","zh":"亞瑟王常被描述為英國故事中傳說中的國王。"},{"en":"If a writer mentions a legendary king, the reference may create a sense of ancient history.","zh":"如果作者提到傳說中的國王，該典故可能營造古代歷史感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a ruler from legend rather than ordinary record.","zh":"這個短語描述來自傳說而非普通記錄的統治者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"support abundant wildlife","meaning":"孕育大量野生生物","examples":[{"en":"The ancient Mediterranean supported abundant marine wildlife.","zh":"古代地中海孕育大量海洋野生生物。"},{"en":"To support abundant wildlife means to provide enough food, shelter, and habitat for many wild species.","zh":"「support abundant wildlife」意思是提供足夠食物、庇護和棲息地，讓許多野生物種生存。"},{"en":"A healthy wetland can support abundant wildlife, including birds, fish, and insects.","zh":"健康濕地可以孕育大量野生生物，包括雀鳥、魚和昆蟲。"},{"en":"If a sea supports abundant wildlife, its ecosystem is likely rich and productive.","zh":"如果海洋孕育大量野生生物，其生態系統很可能豐富且高產。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an environment that can sustain many living creatures.","zh":"這個短語描述能支持許多生命的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"monk seals","meaning":"僧海豹","examples":[{"en":"Monk seals once lived in large numbers in the Mediterranean.","zh":"僧海豹曾大量生活在地中海。"},{"en":"Monk seals are marine mammals that live along some coasts and islands.","zh":"「monk seals」是生活於某些海岸和島嶼附近的海洋哺乳動物。"},{"en":"A wildlife documentary may show monk seals resting on quiet beaches.","zh":"野生動物紀錄片可能展示僧海豹在安靜海灘上休息。"},{"en":"If monk seals lose habitat or are hunted, their numbers can fall sharply.","zh":"如果僧海豹失去棲息地或被獵捕，數量可能急劇下降。"},{"en":"The phrase names a seal species used as an example of marine decline.","zh":"這個短語指出一種用作海洋衰退例子的海豹物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"loggerhead turtles","meaning":"赤蠵龜","examples":[{"en":"Loggerhead turtles have been harmed by hunting and fishing.","zh":"赤蠵龜已受到獵捕和捕魚傷害。"},{"en":"Loggerhead turtles are large sea turtles with powerful jaws and broad heads.","zh":"「loggerhead turtles」是有強壯顎部和寬頭的大型海龜。"},{"en":"A beach conservation group may protect loggerhead turtle nests from disturbance.","zh":"海灘保育組織可能保護赤蠵龜巢穴免受干擾。"},{"en":"If turtles are caught accidentally in fishing gear, their populations may decline.","zh":"如果海龜意外被漁具捕獲，其種群可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase names a sea turtle affected by human activity.","zh":"這個短語指出一種受人類活動影響的海龜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"porpoises","meaning":"鼠海豚","examples":[{"en":"Porpoises were once more abundant in the Mediterranean.","zh":"鼠海豚曾在地中海更為豐富。"},{"en":"Porpoises are small marine mammals related to dolphins.","zh":"「porpoises」是與海豚有親緣關係的小型海洋哺乳動物。"},{"en":"Tourists may spot porpoises near a coast if the water is clean and quiet.","zh":"如果海水清潔安靜，遊客可能在海岸附近看見鼠海豚。"},{"en":"If fishing nets trap porpoises, their populations can shrink.","zh":"如果漁網困住鼠海豚，其種群可能縮小。"},{"en":"The phrase names a sea mammal often affected by marine change.","zh":"這個短語指出一種常受海洋變化影響的海洋哺乳動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"disappearance through hunting","meaning":"因獵捕而消失","examples":[{"en":"The disappearance of several species was partly caused by hunting.","zh":"幾個物種的消失部分是由獵捕造成的。"},{"en":"Disappearance through hunting means species vanish from an area because people kill or capture too many of them.","zh":"「disappearance through hunting」意思是因人們殺死或捕捉過多，物種從某地消失。"},{"en":"A bird species may disappear through hunting if no rules protect it during breeding season.","zh":"如果沒有規則在繁殖季節保護雀鳥，某鳥類可能因獵捕而消失。"},{"en":"If hunting removes animals faster than they reproduce, local extinction can follow.","zh":"如果獵捕移除動物的速度快於其繁殖，本地絕種可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"The phrase links human hunting with species loss.","zh":"這個短語把人類獵捕與物種喪失連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"overfishing","meaning":"過度捕魚","examples":[{"en":"Overfishing can remove major species from marine ecosystems.","zh":"過度捕魚可以把主要物種從海洋生態系統中移除。"},{"en":"Overfishing means catching fish faster than populations can replace themselves.","zh":"「overfishing」意思是捕魚速度快於種群自我補充的速度。"},{"en":"A lake may suffer overfishing if everyone catches young fish before they breed.","zh":"如果人人在幼魚繁殖前捕走牠們，湖泊可能遭受過度捕魚。"},{"en":"If overfishing continues, catches may fall and food webs may change.","zh":"如果過度捕魚持續，捕獲量可能下降，食物網可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fishing beyond sustainable limits.","zh":"這個短語描述超出可持續限度的捕魚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"restructure food webs","meaning":"重組食物網","examples":[{"en":"The loss of predators can totally restructure food webs.","zh":"捕食者的喪失可以完全重組食物網。"},{"en":"To restructure food webs means to change the relationships between predators, prey, and other species.","zh":"「restructure food webs」意思是改變捕食者、獵物和其他物種之間的關係。"},{"en":"Removing cats from an area may restructure a local food web by changing bird and mouse numbers.","zh":"從某地移除貓可能透過改變鳥和老鼠數量來重組本地食物網。"},{"en":"If top predators disappear, smaller species may increase and alter the whole system.","zh":"如果頂級捕食者消失，較小物種可能增加並改變整個系統。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep change in feeding relationships.","zh":"這個短語描述進食關係中的深層改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"food webs","meaning":"食物網","examples":[{"en":"Marine food webs connect predators, prey and their shared environment.","zh":"海洋食物網連接捕食者、獵物和它們共同的環境。"},{"en":"Food webs are networks showing how living things eat and depend on one another.","zh":"「food webs」是顯示生物如何進食和互相依賴的網絡。"},{"en":"In a pond food web, insects may be eaten by fish, and fish may be eaten by birds.","zh":"在池塘食物網中，昆蟲可能被魚吃，而魚可能被鳥吃。"},{"en":"If one species disappears, many parts of the food web may be affected.","zh":"如果一個物種消失，食物網的許多部分可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ecological feeding connections.","zh":"這個短語描述生態中的進食連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be harder to achieve than","meaning":"比……更難達成","examples":[{"en":"Ecological recovery is often harder to achieve than destruction.","zh":"生態恢復通常比破壞更難達成。"},{"en":"To be harder to achieve than something means to require more effort, time, or difficulty than it.","zh":"「be harder to achieve than」某事，意思是比它需要更多努力、時間或困難。"},{"en":"Building trust is harder to achieve than losing it after one dishonest action.","zh":"建立信任比一次不誠實行為後失去信任更難達成。"},{"en":"If ecosystems are easy to damage but hard to restore, early protection is essential.","zh":"如果生態系統容易破壞卻難以恢復，早期保護就非常重要。"},{"en":"The phrase compares difficulty between two outcomes.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個結果的困難程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the sooner…, the more certain…","meaning":"越早……，就越有把握……","examples":[{"en":"The sooner we protect marine life, the more certain our success will be.","zh":"我們越早保護海洋生命，成功就越有把握。"},{"en":"The sooner…, the more certain… means earlier action increases the chance of success.","zh":"「the sooner…, the more certain…」意思是行動越早，成功機會越大。"},{"en":"The sooner students start revising, the more certain their improvement will be.","zh":"學生越早開始溫習，進步就越有把握。"},{"en":"If protection begins before collapse, recovery becomes more likely.","zh":"如果保護在崩潰前開始，恢復就更可能。"},{"en":"The structure links early action with stronger confidence in the result.","zh":"這個結構把早期行動與對結果更大信心連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"act to protect","meaning":"採取行動保護","examples":[{"en":"Governments must act to protect vulnerable marine life.","zh":"政府必須採取行動保護脆弱海洋生命。"},{"en":"To act to protect something means to take real steps to keep it safe.","zh":"「act to protect」某物，意思是採取實際步驟保持其安全。"},{"en":"A school must act to protect students if bullying is reported.","zh":"如果有欺凌報告，學校必須採取行動保護學生。"},{"en":"If governments delay action, vulnerable species may decline further.","zh":"如果政府延遲行動，脆弱物種可能進一步下降。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses action rather than discussion only.","zh":"這個短語強調行動，而不只是討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"an admission of failure","meaning":"承認失敗","examples":[{"en":"Some managers regard marine reserves as an admission of failure.","zh":"有些管理人員把海洋保護區視為承認失敗。"},{"en":"An admission of failure is an act or statement showing that a previous approach has not worked.","zh":"「an admission of failure」是顯示先前方法沒有奏效的行動或說法。"},{"en":"Asking for help is not always an admission of failure; it can be a sensible step.","zh":"尋求幫助不一定是承認失敗；它可以是明智一步。"},{"en":"If managers see reserves as admitting defeat, they may resist using them early.","zh":"如果管理者把保護區視為承認失敗，他們可能抗拒早期使用它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes acknowledging that something has gone wrong.","zh":"這個短語描述承認某事出了問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"according to their logic","meaning":"按照他們的邏輯","examples":[{"en":"According to their logic, reserves would be unnecessary under perfect management.","zh":"按照他們的邏輯，在完美管理下保護區就不必要。"},{"en":"According to their logic means based on the reasoning or thinking they use.","zh":"「according to their logic」意思是根據他們使用的推理或想法。"},{"en":"According to their logic, homework is unnecessary if students already understand the lesson.","zh":"按照他們的邏輯，如果學生已明白課堂，功課就不必要。"},{"en":"If the logic is flawed, the conclusion may also be wrong.","zh":"如果邏輯有缺陷，結論也可能錯。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces someone else’s line of reasoning.","zh":"這個短語引出別人的推理方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"manage the uses we make of the sea","meaning":"管理我們利用海洋的方式","examples":[{"en":"Authorities must manage the uses we make of the sea responsibly.","zh":"當局必須負責任地管理我們利用海洋的方式。"},{"en":"To manage the uses we make of the sea means to control fishing, transport, tourism, mining, and other ocean activities.","zh":"「manage the uses we make of the sea」意思是管控捕魚、運輸、旅遊、採礦和其他海洋活動。"},{"en":"A coastal city manages sea use by separating swimming areas from boat routes.","zh":"沿海城市透過把游泳區與船隻航線分開來管理海洋使用。"},{"en":"If sea use is not managed, different industries may damage habitats and each other.","zh":"如果海洋使用不受管理，不同行業可能損害棲息地並互相影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes responsible control of human ocean activities.","zh":"這個短語描述對人類海洋活動的負責任管控。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fisheries managers","meaning":"漁業管理人員","examples":[{"en":"Fisheries managers use scientific models to recommend catch limits.","zh":"漁業管理人員使用科學模型建議捕獲限制。"},{"en":"Fisheries managers are officials or experts responsible for controlling fishing activity and protecting fish stocks.","zh":"「fisheries managers」是負責控制捕魚活動和保護魚類資源的官員或專家。"},{"en":"Fisheries managers may meet fishers, scientists, and politicians before setting rules.","zh":"漁業管理人員在制定規則前，可能與漁民、科學家和政治人物會面。"},{"en":"If managers ignore scientific warnings, fish stocks may decline further.","zh":"如果管理人員忽視科學警告，魚類資源可能進一步下降。"},{"en":"The phrase names people responsible for fisheries policy and control.","zh":"這個短語指出負責漁業政策和管控的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be wedded to the idea that","meaning":"執着於……的想法","examples":[{"en":"Some managers remain wedded to the idea that their models will eventually succeed.","zh":"有些管理人員仍執着於他們的模型最終會成功的想法。"},{"en":"To be wedded to the idea that means to be strongly attached to a belief and unwilling to let it go.","zh":"「be wedded to the idea that」意思是強烈依附某信念，且不願放手。"},{"en":"A teacher may be wedded to the idea that strict memorisation is the only way to learn.","zh":"老師可能執着於嚴格背誦是唯一學習方式的想法。"},{"en":"If managers cling to old models, they may reject better conservation tools.","zh":"如果管理人員執着於舊模型，可能拒絕更好的保育工具。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests stubborn commitment to an idea.","zh":"這個短語暗示對想法的固執投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"one day their models will work","meaning":"有一天他們的模型會奏效","examples":[{"en":"Some experts still believe that one day their models will work perfectly.","zh":"有些專家仍相信有一天他們的模型會完美奏效。"},{"en":"One day their models will work means they expect their prediction systems to succeed in the future.","zh":"「one day their models will work」意思是他們預期自己的預測系統將來會成功。"},{"en":"A student may believe that one day their study plan will work, even if it has failed before.","zh":"學生可能相信有一天自己的學習計劃會奏效，即使它以前失敗過。"},{"en":"If managers keep waiting for models to improve, urgent protection may be delayed.","zh":"如果管理者一直等待模型改善，迫切保護可能被延誤。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses hope in future success despite present failure.","zh":"這個短語表達對未來成功的希望，即使目前失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"listen to their advice","meaning":"聽取他們的意見","examples":[{"en":"Scientific management fails when politicians refuse to listen to expert advice.","zh":"當政治人物拒絕聽取專家意見，科學管理就會失敗。"},{"en":"To listen to their advice means to take someone’s suggestions seriously and act on them.","zh":"「listen to their advice」意思是認真看待某人的建議並採取行動。"},{"en":"Students improve faster when they listen to their teacher’s advice after marking.","zh":"學生在批改後聽取老師意見，會進步得更快。"},{"en":"If politicians ignore scientists, management rules may become weaker than evidence requires.","zh":"如果政治人物忽視科學家，管理規則可能比證據要求的更弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes accepting guidance from others.","zh":"這個短語描述接受他人指導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"give the approach time","meaning":"給予這種方法時間","examples":[{"en":"Supporters argue that society should give the approach more time.","zh":"支持者認為社會應給予這種方法更多時間。"},{"en":"To give an approach time means to allow a method longer to show whether it works.","zh":"「give an approach time」意思是讓一種方法有更長時間顯示是否有效。"},{"en":"A teacher may give a new reading method time before judging its success.","zh":"老師可能在判斷新閱讀方法是否成功前，給予它時間。"},{"en":"If an approach has already failed for decades, giving it more time may be risky.","zh":"如果一種方法已失敗數十年，再給它時間可能有風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes patience with a method.","zh":"這個短語描述對方法保持耐性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"success will be theirs","meaning":"他們終會成功","examples":[{"en":"Some managers continue to believe that success will eventually be theirs.","zh":"有些管理人員繼續相信他們終會成功。"},{"en":"Success will be theirs means they believe they will finally succeed.","zh":"「success will be theirs」意思是他們相信自己最終會成功。"},{"en":"A team may believe success will be theirs if they keep training and improving.","zh":"如果球隊持續訓練和改進，可能相信自己終會成功。"},{"en":"If confidence becomes blind, people may ignore evidence that their method is failing.","zh":"如果信心變得盲目，人們可能忽視方法正在失敗的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses expectation of future victory.","zh":"這個短語表達對未來勝利的預期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"How much time have we got?","meaning":"我們還有多少時間？","examples":[{"en":"The question “How much time have we got?” stresses the urgency of action.","zh":"「我們還有多少時間？」這個問題強調行動的迫切性。"},{"en":"How much time have we got? asks how long remains before it is too late.","zh":"「How much time have we got?」是在問距離太遲之前還剩多少時間。"},{"en":"A doctor may ask how much time a patient has if treatment must begin urgently.","zh":"如果治療必須緊急開始，醫生可能問病人還有多少時間。"},{"en":"If fish stocks are collapsing, waiting for perfect management may waste precious time.","zh":"如果魚類資源正在崩潰，等待完美管理可能浪費寶貴時間。"},{"en":"The question creates pressure to act quickly.","zh":"這個問題製造快速行動的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be tried and refined","meaning":"經過試行和改良","examples":[{"en":"The management approach has been tried and refined for decades.","zh":"這種管理方法已經過數十年試行和改良。"},{"en":"To be tried and refined means to be tested and improved over time.","zh":"「be tried and refined」意思是經過測試並隨時間改善。"},{"en":"A teaching method may be tried and refined after several school terms.","zh":"一種教學方法可能經過幾個學期試行和改良。"},{"en":"If a policy has been tried and refined but still fails, a new approach may be needed.","zh":"如果政策經過試行和改良仍然失敗，可能需要新方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated testing and adjustment.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆測試和調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"for the last 50 years","meaning":"過去五十年來","examples":[{"en":"Conventional fisheries management has been used for the last 50 years.","zh":"傳統漁業管理在過去五十年來一直被使用。"},{"en":"For the last 50 years means during the most recent fifty-year period.","zh":"「for the last 50 years」意思是在最近五十年間。"},{"en":"The family business has served the neighbourhood for the last 50 years.","zh":"這間家族企業在過去五十年來服務該社區。"},{"en":"If a policy has worked poorly for fifty years, patience alone may not solve the problem.","zh":"如果政策五十年來表現欠佳，單靠耐性可能不能解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a long recent time frame.","zh":"這個短語提供很長的近期時間範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"few successes","meaning":"成功例子寥寥可數","examples":[{"en":"The policy has produced few lasting successes.","zh":"該政策產生的持久成功例子寥寥可數。"},{"en":"Few successes means only a small number of successful results.","zh":"「few successes」意思是成功結果數量很少。"},{"en":"A study plan with few successes may need to be changed before the final exam.","zh":"如果學習計劃成功例子寥寥可數，期末考前可能需要改變。"},{"en":"If fisheries management has few successes, fish stocks may still be in trouble.","zh":"如果漁業管理成功例子很少，魚類資源可能仍有問題。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests disappointing results.","zh":"這個短語暗示令人失望的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"feather someone’s cap","meaning":"為某人增光；成為某人的功績","examples":[{"en":"There have been few achievements with which to feather the managers’ caps.","zh":"可為管理人員增光的成就寥寥可數。"},{"en":"To feather someone’s cap means to give them an achievement they can be proud of.","zh":"「feather someone’s cap」意思是給某人一項值得自豪的成就。"},{"en":"Winning a scholarship can feather a student’s cap when applying to university.","zh":"獲得獎學金可以在申請大學時為學生增光。"},{"en":"If a policy has few successes, managers have little to boast about.","zh":"如果政策成功例子很少，管理人員就幾乎沒有可誇耀之處。"},{"en":"The phrase is idiomatic and means to add to someone’s reputation.","zh":"這個短語是習語，意思是增加某人的聲譽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a growing litany of failure","meaning":"越來越多失敗事例","examples":[{"en":"The history of conventional management contains a growing litany of failure.","zh":"傳統管理的歷史包含越來越多失敗事例。"},{"en":"A growing litany of failure is a long and increasing list of things that have gone wrong.","zh":"「a growing litany of failure」是一長串且不斷增加的失敗事情。"},{"en":"A company with repeated delays, complaints, and losses may face a growing litany of failure.","zh":"如果公司反覆延誤、投訴和虧損，可能面對越來越多失敗事例。"},{"en":"If failures keep accumulating, confidence in the old system decreases.","zh":"如果失敗不斷累積，人們對舊系統的信心會下降。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly criticises repeated unsuccessful results.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評重複不成功的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Common Fisheries Policy","meaning":"共同漁業政策","examples":[{"en":"The Common Fisheries Policy regulates fisheries within the European Union.","zh":"共同漁業政策規管歐盟內的漁業。"},{"en":"The Common Fisheries Policy is a European Union policy for managing fishing and aquaculture.","zh":"「Common Fisheries Policy」是歐盟用來管理捕魚和水產養殖的政策。"},{"en":"A geography class may study the Common Fisheries Policy when discussing European fishing rules.","zh":"地理課討論歐洲捕魚規則時，可能研究共同漁業政策。"},{"en":"If the policy sets weak limits, fish stocks may still decline despite regulation.","zh":"如果該政策設定薄弱限制，即使有規管，魚類資源仍可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific fisheries-management policy.","zh":"這個短語指出一項特定漁業管理政策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"an instrument for","meaning":"用於……的手段","examples":[{"en":"The policy is an instrument for the management of fisheries and aquaculture.","zh":"該政策是用於管理漁業和水產養殖的手段。"},{"en":"An instrument for something is a tool or method used to achieve it.","zh":"「an instrument for」某事，是用來達成它的工具或方法。"},{"en":"Exams can be an instrument for measuring what students have learned.","zh":"考試可以是用於量度學生所學內容的手段。"},{"en":"If a policy is an instrument for management, its design affects whether management succeeds.","zh":"如果政策是管理手段，其設計會影響管理是否成功。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a means used for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述用於某目的的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"aquaculture","meaning":"水產養殖","examples":[{"en":"Aquaculture involves farming fish and other aquatic organisms.","zh":"水產養殖涉及養殖魚類和其他水生生物。"},{"en":"Aquaculture is the farming of fish, shellfish, seaweed, or other water-based organisms.","zh":"「aquaculture」是養殖魚、貝類、海藻或其他水生生物。"},{"en":"A fish farm that raises salmon in cages is an example of aquaculture.","zh":"在魚籠中養殖三文魚的魚場就是水產養殖例子。"},{"en":"If wild fish stocks decline, aquaculture may provide more seafood but must be managed carefully.","zh":"如果野生魚類資源下降，水產養殖可能提供更多海鮮，但必須小心管理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes farming in water rather than catching from the wild.","zh":"這個短語描述在水中養殖，而不是從野外捕捉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"exemplify the worst pitfalls","meaning":"體現最嚴重的弊端","examples":[{"en":"The policy exemplifies some of the worst pitfalls of fisheries management.","zh":"該政策體現漁業管理中一些最嚴重的弊端。"},{"en":"To exemplify the worst pitfalls means to clearly show the most serious mistakes or dangers.","zh":"「exemplify the worst pitfalls」意思是清楚展示最嚴重錯誤或危險。"},{"en":"A rushed group project can exemplify the pitfalls of poor planning.","zh":"倉促完成的小組專題可以體現規劃不善的弊端。"},{"en":"If a policy shows flawed models and weak political decisions, it reveals what management must avoid.","zh":"如果政策顯示有缺陷模型和薄弱政治決定，它就揭示管理必須避免的事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serving as a clear negative example.","zh":"這個短語描述成為清楚的負面例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"flawed models","meaning":"有缺陷的模型","examples":[{"en":"Flawed models can produce unreliable estimates of sustainable catches.","zh":"有缺陷的模型可能產生不可靠的可持續捕獲量估算。"},{"en":"Flawed models are prediction systems or explanations with serious weaknesses or errors.","zh":"「flawed models」是有嚴重弱點或錯誤的預測系統或解釋。"},{"en":"A weather forecast based on flawed models may give the wrong warning.","zh":"基於有缺陷模型的天氣預報可能發出錯誤警告。"},{"en":"If fisheries models are flawed, catch limits may be too high.","zh":"如果漁業模型有缺陷，捕獲限制可能太高。"},{"en":"The phrase describes tools that look scientific but may mislead.","zh":"這個短語描述看似科學但可能誤導的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"flawed advice","meaning":"有缺陷的意見","examples":[{"en":"Flawed scientific models may lead to flawed advice.","zh":"有缺陷的科學模型可能導致有缺陷的意見。"},{"en":"Flawed advice is guidance that is wrong, weak, or based on poor information.","zh":"「flawed advice」是錯誤、薄弱或基於劣質資料的指導。"},{"en":"A student who follows flawed advice about revision may waste time on the wrong topics.","zh":"如果學生聽從有缺陷的溫習建議，可能把時間浪費在錯誤題目上。"},{"en":"If advice is based on inaccurate fish estimates, policy decisions may become dangerous.","zh":"如果意見建基於不準確魚類估算，政策決定可能變得危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unreliable guidance.","zh":"這個短語描述不可靠的指導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"watered-down recommendations","meaning":"被削弱的建議","examples":[{"en":"Government officials sometimes issue watered-down recommendations.","zh":"政府官員有時發出被削弱的建議。"},{"en":"Watered-down recommendations are advice or rules made weaker than the original version.","zh":"「watered-down recommendations」是比原本版本更弱的建議或規則。"},{"en":"A teacher’s strict phone ban may become a watered-down recommendation if students are only asked to use phones less.","zh":"如果老師原本嚴格禁用電話，後來只要求學生少用電話，這可能變成被削弱的建議。"},{"en":"If scientific advice is watered down, political convenience may weaken conservation.","zh":"如果科學建議被削弱，政治方便可能削弱保育。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recommendations that have lost force.","zh":"這個短語描述失去力度的建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"government bureaucrats","meaning":"政府官僚","examples":[{"en":"Government bureaucrats may modify scientific recommendations before implementation.","zh":"政府官僚可能在實施前修改科學建議。"},{"en":"Government bureaucrats are officials who work in government departments and manage rules, paperwork, and procedures.","zh":"「government bureaucrats」是在政府部門工作、管理規則、文件和程序的官員。"},{"en":"Government bureaucrats may review applications before funding is approved.","zh":"政府官僚可能在資助批准前審查申請。"},{"en":"If bureaucrats weaken scientific advice, final policy may not match the evidence.","zh":"如果官僚削弱科學建議，最終政策可能不符合證據。"},{"en":"The phrase often refers to administrative officials rather than elected politicians.","zh":"這個短語通常指行政官員，而不是民選政治人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"disregard advice","meaning":"漠視意見","examples":[{"en":"Politicians may disregard advice that requires unpopular restrictions.","zh":"政治人物可能漠視需要不受歡迎限制的意見。"},{"en":"To disregard advice means to ignore it or choose not to follow it.","zh":"「disregard advice」意思是忽視建議或選擇不跟從。"},{"en":"A patient may get worse if they disregard a doctor’s advice about medicine.","zh":"如果病人漠視醫生關於藥物的建議，病情可能惡化。"},{"en":"If politicians disregard scientific warnings, environmental damage may continue.","zh":"如果政治人物漠視科學警告，環境傷害可能持續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ignoring guidance deliberately or carelessly.","zh":"這個短語描述有意或粗心地忽略指導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"go wrong","meaning":"出問題；失敗","examples":[{"en":"Fisheries policy can go wrong when evidence is ignored.","zh":"當證據被忽視，漁業政策可能出問題。"},{"en":"To go wrong means to fail, develop problems, or produce a bad result.","zh":"「go wrong」意思是失敗、出現問題或產生壞結果。"},{"en":"A group project can go wrong if no one knows their responsibilities.","zh":"如果沒有人知道自己的責任，小組專題可能出問題。"},{"en":"If policy ignores science and politics weakens rules, management may fail.","zh":"如果政策忽視科學，而政治削弱規則，管理可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a situation becoming unsuccessful.","zh":"這個短語描述情況變得不成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"inevitably","meaning":"無可避免地","examples":[{"en":"A badly designed policy will inevitably produce poor results.","zh":"設計差劣的政策無可避免地會產生差劣結果。"},{"en":"Inevitably means in a way that is almost certain to happen and difficult to avoid.","zh":"「inevitably」意思是某事幾乎肯定會發生，且難以避免。"},{"en":"If students never practise speaking, they will inevitably feel nervous in an oral exam.","zh":"如果學生從不練習說話，他們在口試中無可避免地會緊張。"},{"en":"If catch limits are too high, fish stocks will almost certainly decline.","zh":"如果捕獲限制太高，魚類資源幾乎肯定會下降。"},{"en":"The word signals an unavoidable or highly predictable result.","zh":"這個詞表示無法避免或高度可預測的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"send boats to other countries","meaning":"派遣漁船到其他國家","examples":[{"en":"Europe sent fishing boats to other countries when local stocks declined.","zh":"當本地魚類資源下降，歐洲派遣漁船到其他國家。"},{"en":"To send boats to other countries means to move fishing vessels into foreign waters to catch fish.","zh":"「send boats to other countries」意思是把漁船派往外國水域捕魚。"},{"en":"A company may send trucks to other cities when local demand is too low.","zh":"當本地需求太低，公司可能派貨車到其他城市。"},{"en":"If local fish stocks decline, fleets may search elsewhere instead of reducing pressure.","zh":"如果本地魚類資源下降，船隊可能尋找其他地方，而不是減少壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shifting fishing effort to foreign waters.","zh":"這個短語描述把捕魚努力轉移到外國水域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in order to obtain","meaning":"為了取得……","examples":[{"en":"Foreign waters were exploited in order to obtain additional fish.","zh":"外國水域被開發利用，是為了取得額外魚類。"},{"en":"In order to obtain something means for the purpose of getting it.","zh":"「in order to obtain」某物，意思是為了得到它。"},{"en":"Students may join a workshop in order to obtain extra writing practice.","zh":"學生可能參加工作坊，為了取得額外寫作練習。"},{"en":"If fleets enter foreign waters to obtain fish, pressure spreads beyond local seas.","zh":"如果船隊進入外國水域為了取得魚類，壓力就會擴散到本地海域以外。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly states purpose.","zh":"這個短語清楚說明目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"for far less than they were worth","meaning":"遠低於其實際價值","examples":[{"en":"Fish were obtained for far less than their true economic value.","zh":"魚類以遠低於其實際經濟價值的價格取得。"},{"en":"For far less than they were worth means at a price much lower than the real value.","zh":"「for far less than they were worth」意思是以遠低於真正價值的價格取得。"},{"en":"A family heirloom should not be sold for far less than it is worth.","zh":"家傳物品不應以遠低於其價值的價格出售。"},{"en":"If rich countries buy fish cheaply from poor waters, local communities may lose fair value.","zh":"如果富裕國家從貧困水域廉價購買魚類，本地社區可能失去公平價值。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests unfair or undervalued exchange.","zh":"這個短語暗示不公平或被低估的交換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"squander the wealth of oceans","meaning":"揮霍海洋資源","examples":[{"en":"Humanity is squandering the wealth of the oceans through overexploitation.","zh":"人類正透過過度開發揮霍海洋資源。"},{"en":"To squander the wealth of oceans means to waste valuable marine resources carelessly.","zh":"「squander the wealth of oceans」意思是粗心浪費寶貴海洋資源。"},{"en":"A student squanders time when they scroll online instead of preparing for an exam.","zh":"學生如果滑手機而不準備考試，就是浪費時間。"},{"en":"If people overfish, pollute, and destroy habitats, ocean wealth is used up foolishly.","zh":"如果人們過度捕魚、污染並破壞棲息地，海洋財富就被愚蠢耗盡。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly criticises wasteful treatment of the sea.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評對海洋的浪費使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"break out of","meaning":"擺脫……","examples":[{"en":"Governments must break out of the current cycle of failure.","zh":"政府必須擺脫目前的失敗循環。"},{"en":"To break out of something means to escape from a repeated pattern or limiting situation.","zh":"「break out of」某事，意思是逃離重複模式或限制性情況。"},{"en":"A student can break out of bad study habits by setting small daily goals.","zh":"學生可以透過設定每日小目標擺脫壞學習習慣。"},{"en":"If governments change old policies, they may escape repeated fisheries failure.","zh":"如果政府改變舊政策，可能逃離反覆漁業失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes escaping a trap or cycle.","zh":"這個短語描述逃出陷阱或循環。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cycle of failure","meaning":"失敗循環","examples":[{"en":"Weak regulation has created a damaging cycle of failure.","zh":"薄弱規管造成了有害的失敗循環。"},{"en":"A cycle of failure is a repeated pattern in which problems keep causing more problems.","zh":"「cycle of failure」是一種問題不斷造成更多問題的重複模式。"},{"en":"A student may fall into a cycle of failure if fear leads to avoidance and avoidance leads to worse results.","zh":"如果恐懼導致逃避，而逃避又導致更差結果，學生可能陷入失敗循環。"},{"en":"If poor management causes stock decline and decline causes desperate fishing, failure repeats.","zh":"如果管理不善造成資源下降，而下降又造成絕望捕魚，失敗就會重複。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a harmful repeating loop.","zh":"這個短語描述有害的重複循環。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a key source of protein","meaning":"主要蛋白質來源","examples":[{"en":"Fish are a key source of protein for millions of people.","zh":"魚類是數百萬人的主要蛋白質來源。"},{"en":"A key source of protein is an important food supply that provides protein for the body.","zh":"「a key source of protein」是為身體提供蛋白質的重要食物來源。"},{"en":"Eggs, beans, and fish can all be key sources of protein in different diets.","zh":"雞蛋、豆類和魚在不同飲食中都可以是主要蛋白質來源。"},{"en":"If fish supplies decline, many communities may lose an important part of their diet.","zh":"如果魚類供應下降，許多社區可能失去飲食中的重要部分。"},{"en":"The phrase links fish with nutrition and food security.","zh":"這個短語把魚類與營養和食物安全連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"much more besides","meaning":"除此之外還有更多","examples":[{"en":"The oceans provide food and much more besides.","zh":"海洋提供食物，除此之外還有更多。"},{"en":"Much more besides means many additional things beyond what has already been mentioned.","zh":"「much more besides」意思是除了已提及的事物之外，還有許多額外東西。"},{"en":"A good library offers books and much more besides, such as study space and community events.","zh":"好圖書館提供書本，除此之外還有更多，例如自修空間和社區活動。"},{"en":"If oceans provide climate regulation and nutrient cycling, they matter beyond seafood.","zh":"如果海洋提供氣候調節和養分循環，它們的重要性就超越海鮮。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests extra value beyond the obvious.","zh":"這個短語暗示除明顯價值外還有額外價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"disrupt natural ecosystem processes","meaning":"擾亂自然生態系統過程","examples":[{"en":"Overfishing can disrupt natural ecosystem processes.","zh":"過度捕魚可以擾亂自然生態系統過程。"},{"en":"To disrupt natural ecosystem processes means to disturb the normal ways an ecosystem functions.","zh":"「disrupt natural ecosystem processes」意思是干擾生態系統正常運作的方式。"},{"en":"Building on wetlands can disrupt natural water flow and bird breeding.","zh":"在濕地上建築可以擾亂自然水流和雀鳥繁殖。"},{"en":"If major fish are removed, feeding relationships and nutrient cycles may be disturbed.","zh":"如果主要魚類被移除，進食關係和養分循環可能受干擾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes damage to how nature normally works.","zh":"這個短語描述對自然正常運作方式的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"water purification","meaning":"水質淨化","examples":[{"en":"Marine ecosystems contribute to natural water purification.","zh":"海洋生態系統有助自然水質淨化。"},{"en":"Water purification is the process of removing dirt, pollutants, or harmful substances from water.","zh":"「water purification」是從水中去除污垢、污染物或有害物質的過程。"},{"en":"Wetlands support water purification by trapping sediments and breaking down waste.","zh":"濕地透過困住沉積物和分解廢物來支持水質淨化。"},{"en":"If ecosystems are damaged, natural water cleaning may become weaker.","zh":"如果生態系統受損，自然水質淨化可能變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making water cleaner.","zh":"這個短語描述令水更潔淨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"nutrient cycling","meaning":"養分循環","examples":[{"en":"Healthy ecosystems support nutrient cycling.","zh":"健康生態系統支持養分循環。"},{"en":"Nutrient cycling is the movement and reuse of nutrients through living things, soil, water, and the environment.","zh":"「nutrient cycling」是養分在生物、土壤、水和環境中流動和再利用的過程。"},{"en":"Fallen leaves support nutrient cycling when they decay and feed the soil.","zh":"落葉腐爛並滋養泥土時，支持養分循環。"},{"en":"If marine food webs are damaged, nutrient cycling may become less balanced.","zh":"如果海洋食物網受損，養分循環可能變得較不平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes nature’s recycling of nutrients.","zh":"這個短語描述大自然對養分的循環再用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"carbon storage","meaning":"碳儲存","examples":[{"en":"Oceans play a major role in carbon storage.","zh":"海洋在碳儲存中發揮重要作用。"},{"en":"Carbon storage is the holding of carbon in oceans, forests, soils, or other natural systems.","zh":"「carbon storage」是把碳保存在海洋、森林、土壤或其他自然系統中。"},{"en":"Trees support carbon storage by taking carbon dioxide from the air.","zh":"樹木透過從空氣吸收二氧化碳來支持碳儲存。"},{"en":"If ocean ecosystems are damaged, their ability to store carbon may be weakened.","zh":"如果海洋生態系統受損，其儲存碳的能力可能被削弱。"},{"en":"The phrase connects ecosystems with climate regulation.","zh":"這個短語把生態系統與氣候調節連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have ramifications for","meaning":"對……產生深遠影響","examples":[{"en":"Damage to marine ecosystems could have ramifications for human life.","zh":"海洋生態系統受損可能對人類生活產生深遠影響。"},{"en":"To have ramifications for something means to have serious consequences or wider effects on it.","zh":"「have ramifications for」某事，意思是對它有嚴重後果或更廣泛影響。"},{"en":"A sudden school closure can have ramifications for parents’ work schedules.","zh":"學校突然停課可能對家長工作安排產生深遠影響。"},{"en":"If ocean systems fail, food supply, climate, and livelihoods may all be affected.","zh":"如果海洋系統失效，食物供應、氣候和生計都可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes far-reaching results.","zh":"這個短語描述深遠結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"human life itself","meaning":"人類生命本身","examples":[{"en":"The destruction of ecosystem processes may threaten human life itself.","zh":"生態系統過程被破壞可能威脅人類生命本身。"},{"en":"Human life itself means the basic survival and well-being of people as a whole.","zh":"「human life itself」意思是人類整體的基本生存和福祉。"},{"en":"Clean water is important not just for comfort but for human life itself.","zh":"潔淨食水不只是為了舒適，而是關乎人類生命本身。"},{"en":"If food systems and climate systems are damaged, human survival may be affected.","zh":"如果食物系統和氣候系統受損，人類生存可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises the most fundamental human stakes.","zh":"這個短語強調最根本的人類利害關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"go a long way to","meaning":"對……大有幫助","examples":[{"en":"Better management can go a long way to avoiding ecological disaster.","zh":"更好的管理可以對避免生態災難大有幫助。"},{"en":"To go a long way to doing something means to help greatly in achieving it.","zh":"「go a long way to」做某事，意思是大大幫助達成它。"},{"en":"Clear feedback can go a long way to improving a student’s writing.","zh":"清楚回饋可以對改善學生寫作大有幫助。"},{"en":"If marine reserves and catch limits are used well, they can greatly reduce risk.","zh":"如果海洋保護區和捕獲限制使用得當，它們可以大幅降低風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a major contribution, not solving everything alone.","zh":"這個短語描述作出重大貢獻，而不是單獨解決所有問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"avoid a catastrophic mistake","meaning":"避免災難性的錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Humanity can still avoid a catastrophic mistake through effective action.","zh":"人類仍可透過有效行動避免災難性的錯誤。"},{"en":"To avoid a catastrophic mistake means to prevent a disastrous error before it happens.","zh":"「avoid a catastrophic mistake」意思是在災難性錯誤發生前防止它。"},{"en":"A company can avoid a catastrophic mistake by testing a product before selling it widely.","zh":"公司可以透過在大規模銷售前測試產品來避免災難性錯誤。"},{"en":"If ocean collapse can still be prevented, urgent management is necessary.","zh":"如果海洋崩潰仍可避免，迫切管理就是必要的。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that wrong choices could have severe consequences.","zh":"這個短語警告錯誤選擇可能有嚴重後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"common-sense management","meaning":"合乎常理的管理","examples":[{"en":"The oceans need simple, common-sense management.","zh":"海洋需要簡單、合乎常理的管理。"},{"en":"Common-sense management is practical control based on obvious, reasonable judgement.","zh":"「common-sense management」是基於明顯、合理判斷的實際管理。"},{"en":"A classroom needs common-sense management, such as clear rules and enough time for questions.","zh":"課室需要合乎常理的管理，例如清楚規則和足夠提問時間。"},{"en":"If fish are declining, common sense says catches should be reduced and refuges created.","zh":"如果魚類正在下降，常理會說應減少捕獲量並設立庇護地。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests practical solutions rather than complicated excuses.","zh":"這個短語暗示實際解決方法，而不是複雜藉口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lie at the heart of","meaning":"是……的核心","examples":[{"en":"Marine reserves lie at the heart of fisheries reform.","zh":"海洋保護區是漁業改革的核心。"},{"en":"To lie at the heart of something means to be central or most important to it.","zh":"「lie at the heart of」某事，意思是成為它的中心或最重要部分。"},{"en":"Trust lies at the heart of a strong friendship.","zh":"信任是牢固友誼的核心。"},{"en":"If reserves are central to reform, they should guide other management decisions.","zh":"如果保護區是改革核心，它們應指導其他管理決定。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the core of an issue or system.","zh":"這個短語指出議題或系統的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be sufficient","meaning":"足夠","examples":[{"en":"Marine reserves alone will not be sufficient to restore the oceans.","zh":"單靠海洋保護區不足以恢復海洋。"},{"en":"To be sufficient means to be enough for a purpose.","zh":"「be sufficient」意思是足以達成某目的。"},{"en":"One example may not be sufficient to prove a difficult argument.","zh":"一個例子可能不足以證明困難論點。"},{"en":"If reserves are not combined with wider rules, they may not restore marine ecosystems fully.","zh":"如果保護區不與更廣泛規則結合，它們可能不足以完全恢復海洋生態系統。"},{"en":"The phrase describes whether something is enough.","zh":"這個短語描述某物是否足夠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"here and there","meaning":"零星地；到處一點","examples":[{"en":"A few small reserves established here and there will not be enough.","zh":"零星設立幾個小保護區是不足夠的。"},{"en":"Here and there means in scattered places, without a strong overall plan.","zh":"「here and there」意思是在零散地方，沒有強而整體的計劃。"},{"en":"A student who revises here and there may not build a complete understanding.","zh":"學生如果只是零星溫習，可能無法建立完整理解。"},{"en":"If reserves are only scattered in a few places, they may not protect whole ecosystems.","zh":"如果保護區只零散分佈於少數地方，可能無法保護整個生態系統。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests something is too limited or irregular.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事太有限或不規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"shore up","meaning":"支撐；勉強維持","examples":[{"en":"Small reserves should not merely shore up a failing management system.","zh":"小型保護區不應只是支撐一個失敗的管理系統。"},{"en":"To shore up something means to support or strengthen something weak or unstable.","zh":"「shore up」某物，意思是支持或加強薄弱或不穩定的東西。"},{"en":"A company may shore up its finances by cutting waste and finding new customers.","zh":"公司可能透過削減浪費和尋找新客戶來支撐財務。"},{"en":"If reserves only support a failing system, the deeper problems remain unsolved.","zh":"如果保護區只是支撐失敗系統，更深層問題仍未解決。"},{"en":"The phrase describes holding up something that may collapse.","zh":"這個短語描述支撐可能倒塌的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the crumbling edifice of","meaning":"……搖搖欲墜的體系","examples":[{"en":"Reserves cannot simply support the crumbling edifice of failed policy.","zh":"保護區不能只是支撐失敗政策搖搖欲墜的體系。"},{"en":"The crumbling edifice of something means a large system that is weakening, failing, or falling apart.","zh":"「the crumbling edifice of」某事，意思是一個正在變弱、失敗或崩塌的大系統。"},{"en":"Extra tutoring cannot fix the crumbling edifice of a school system that ignores basic literacy.","zh":"額外補習不能修復忽視基本讀寫能力的學校制度這個搖搖欲墜的體系。"},{"en":"If old fisheries policy is already failing, small reserves should not just prop it up.","zh":"如果舊漁業政策已經失敗，小型保護區不應只是支撐它。"},{"en":"The phrase uses a building image to describe a failing system.","zh":"這個短語用建築意象描述失敗系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rational fisheries management","meaning":"理性漁業管理","examples":[{"en":"Earlier scientists envisioned a system of rational fisheries management.","zh":"早期科學家構想了一套理性漁業管理制度。"},{"en":"Rational fisheries management means managing fishing through reason, evidence, and long-term planning.","zh":"「rational fisheries management」意思是透過理性、證據和長遠規劃管理捕魚。"},{"en":"Rational school management uses data, teacher feedback, and student needs before changing rules.","zh":"理性學校管理會在改變規則前使用數據、教師回饋和學生需要。"},{"en":"If fisheries management is rational, catch limits should match what fish populations can sustain.","zh":"如果漁業管理是理性的，捕獲限制應符合魚類種群可承受的水平。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sensible, evidence-based control of fishing.","zh":"這個短語描述明智、基於證據的捕魚管控。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be envisioned by","meaning":"由……構想","examples":[{"en":"The management system was envisioned by scientists in the mid-twentieth century.","zh":"這套管理制度由二十世紀中期的科學家構想。"},{"en":"To be envisioned by someone means to be imagined or planned by that person.","zh":"「be envisioned by」某人，意思是由該人想像或規劃。"},{"en":"The new community centre was envisioned by residents who wanted a shared space.","zh":"新社區中心由想要共享空間的居民構想。"},{"en":"If scientists envisioned rational management, they imagined a system guided by evidence.","zh":"如果科學家構想理性管理，他們想像的是由證據引導的制度。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who first imagined or designed an idea.","zh":"這個短語指出誰最先想像或設計某想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be placed centre stage","meaning":"被置於核心位置","examples":[{"en":"Marine reserves must be placed centre stage in ocean policy.","zh":"海洋保護區必須在海洋政策中被置於核心位置。"},{"en":"To be placed centre stage means to be given the most important and visible position.","zh":"「be placed centre stage」意思是被放在最重要、最受注意的位置。"},{"en":"Student well-being should be placed centre stage in school reform.","zh":"學校改革應把學生福祉置於核心位置。"},{"en":"If marine reserves are placed centre stage, other policies will be built around them.","zh":"如果海洋保護區被置於核心位置，其他政策就會圍繞它們建立。"},{"en":"The phrase means something should become a main priority.","zh":"這個短語意思是某事應成為主要優先事項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a fundamental underpinning","meaning":"根本支柱","examples":[{"en":"Strict protection should be a fundamental underpinning of marine management.","zh":"嚴格保護應是海洋管理的根本支柱。"},{"en":"A fundamental underpinning is a basic support or foundation that other things depend on.","zh":"「a fundamental underpinning」是其他事物依靠的基本支撐或基礎。"},{"en":"Trust is a fundamental underpinning of good teamwork.","zh":"信任是良好團隊合作的根本支柱。"},{"en":"If strict protection underpins marine management, every policy begins from conservation.","zh":"如果嚴格保護支撐海洋管理，每項政策都從保育出發。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a core foundation.","zh":"這個短語描述核心基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"everything we do in the oceans","meaning":"我們在海洋中所做的一切","examples":[{"en":"Conservation should underpin everything we do in the oceans.","zh":"保育應支撐我們在海洋中所做的一切。"},{"en":"Everything we do in the oceans means all human activities at sea, including fishing, transport, tourism, and extraction.","zh":"「everything we do in the oceans」意思是所有海上人類活動，包括捕魚、運輸、旅遊和開採。"},{"en":"Safety rules should guide everything we do in a science laboratory.","zh":"安全規則應指導我們在科學實驗室中所做的一切。"},{"en":"If conservation guides all ocean activity, development must respect ecological limits.","zh":"如果保育指導所有海洋活動，發展就必須尊重生態限制。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises total coverage of human actions.","zh":"這個短語強調涵蓋所有人類行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a first resort","meaning":"首要措施","examples":[{"en":"Marine reserves should be a first resort in fisheries management.","zh":"海洋保護區應是漁業管理的首要措施。"},{"en":"A first resort is the first measure people use when dealing with a problem.","zh":"「a first resort」是人們處理問題時首先使用的措施。"},{"en":"For mild stress, rest and honest planning may be a first resort before medication is considered.","zh":"對輕微壓力而言，休息和誠實規劃可能是在考慮藥物前的首要措施。"},{"en":"If reserves are used early, ecosystems may be protected before collapse occurs.","zh":"如果保護區早期使用，生態系統可能在崩潰前受到保護。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts early action with last-minute action.","zh":"這個短語把早期行動與最後一刻行動作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a final resort","meaning":"最後手段","examples":[{"en":"Protection should not be treated as a final resort.","zh":"保護不應被視為最後手段。"},{"en":"A final resort is the last measure used only after other options have failed.","zh":"「a final resort」是在其他選項失敗後才使用的最後措施。"},{"en":"Surgery may be a final resort when medicine and therapy cannot solve the problem.","zh":"當藥物和治療不能解決問題時，手術可能是最後手段。"},{"en":"If marine protection is delayed until all else fails, recovery may become much harder.","zh":"如果海洋保護延遲到其他方法都失敗才使用，恢復可能變得更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a last option, not an early priority.","zh":"這個短語描述最後選項，而不是早期優先事項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"when all else fails","meaning":"當其他一切方法都失敗時","examples":[{"en":"Reserves should not be introduced only when all else fails.","zh":"保護區不應只在其他一切方法都失敗時才引入。"},{"en":"When all else fails means after every other method has failed.","zh":"「when all else fails」意思是在其他所有方法都失敗之後。"},{"en":"A student should not ask for help only when all else fails; early help is better.","zh":"學生不應只在其他方法都失敗時才求助；早些求助更好。"},{"en":"If conservation begins only after total failure, species may already be lost.","zh":"如果保育只在完全失敗後才開始，物種可能已經消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a last-minute response.","zh":"這個短語描述最後一刻的回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"agree with the views of","meaning":"符合作者觀點","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the views of the writer.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否符合作者觀點。"},{"en":"To agree with the views of someone means to match that person’s opinions or arguments.","zh":"「agree with the views of」某人，意思是符合該人的意見或論點。"},{"en":"In a reading exam, students must decide whether a statement agrees with the writer’s view, not their own opinion.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生必須判斷陳述是否符合作者觀點，而不是自己的意見。"},{"en":"If the writer supports marine reserves, a statement opposing them may not agree with the writer.","zh":"如果作者支持海洋保護區，反對保護區的陳述可能不符合作者觀點。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in YES/NO/NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於 YES/NO/NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與作者觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the views expressed in the passage.","zh":"陳述可能與文章表達的觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what that person believes or argues.","zh":"「contradict the views of」某人，意思是說出與該人信念或論點相反的內容。"},{"en":"If a teacher says revision is essential, claiming revision is useless contradicts the teacher’s view.","zh":"如果老師說溫習必不可少，聲稱溫習無用就與老師觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"If the writer says urgent action is needed, saying there is no problem contradicts the passage.","zh":"如果作者說需要迫切行動，說沒有問題就與文章相矛盾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct disagreement with an opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述與意見直接相反。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"It is impossible to say when the passage gives no clear information.","zh":"當文章沒有提供清楚資料時，便無法判斷。"},{"en":"To be impossible to say means there is not enough evidence to decide.","zh":"「be impossible to say」意思是證據不足，不能決定。"},{"en":"If a timetable is not published, it is impossible to say when the exam will start.","zh":"如果時間表未公布，就無法判斷考試何時開始。"},{"en":"If the passage does not mention a point, students should not guess the answer.","zh":"如果文章沒有提及某點，學生不應猜答案。"},{"en":"The phrase signals uncertainty caused by missing information.","zh":"這個短語表示因資料缺失而不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"catch fish for commercial use","meaning":"捕魚作商業用途","examples":[{"en":"People have caught fish for commercial use for more than a thousand years.","zh":"人們捕魚作商業用途已有一千多年。"},{"en":"To catch fish for commercial use means to catch fish in order to sell them or use them in business.","zh":"「catch fish for commercial use」意思是為出售或商業使用而捕魚。"},{"en":"A fishing company catches fish for commercial use and sends them to markets and restaurants.","zh":"漁業公司捕魚作商業用途，並把魚送到市場和餐廳。"},{"en":"If fish are caught for profit, pressure on wild populations may increase.","zh":"如果捕魚是為盈利，野生種群壓力可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase separates business fishing from personal fishing.","zh":"這個短語把商業捕魚與個人捕魚分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"open access to the oceans","meaning":"可自由使用海洋","examples":[{"en":"Open access to the oceans allows fleets to fish with few restrictions.","zh":"可自由使用海洋讓船隊在少數限制下捕魚。"},{"en":"Open access to the oceans means people or nations can use ocean areas with little control.","zh":"「open access to the oceans」意思是人們或國家可在很少管制下使用海洋區域。"},{"en":"Open access to a school computer room may sound convenient but can cause crowding without rules.","zh":"學校電腦室自由使用聽起來方便，但沒有規則可能造成擁擠。"},{"en":"If ocean access is too open, shared resources may be overused.","zh":"如果海洋使用太開放，共享資源可能被過度使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes freedom of use that may need regulation.","zh":"這個短語描述可能需要規管的使用自由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be regarded as desirable","meaning":"被視為理想","examples":[{"en":"Some people still regard unrestricted access to the sea as desirable.","zh":"有些人仍把不受限制使用海洋視為理想。"},{"en":"To be regarded as desirable means to be seen as good, attractive, or worth wanting.","zh":"「be regarded as desirable」意思是被視為好、吸引或值得想要。"},{"en":"Flexible working hours are often regarded as desirable by employees.","zh":"彈性工作時間常被員工視為理想。"},{"en":"If free access is seen as desirable, people may resist limits even when resources decline.","zh":"如果自由使用被視為理想，即使資源下降，人們也可能抗拒限制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a positive judgment or preference.","zh":"這個短語描述正面判斷或偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be completely banned","meaning":"被全面禁止","examples":[{"en":"Fishing is not completely banned in every marine protected area.","zh":"並非每個海洋保護區都全面禁止捕魚。"},{"en":"To be completely banned means to be fully forbidden with no permission given.","zh":"「be completely banned」意思是被完全禁止，沒有任何許可。"},{"en":"Smoking is completely banned inside many hospitals.","zh":"許多醫院內全面禁止吸煙。"},{"en":"If fishing is not completely banned, protection levels may vary greatly.","zh":"如果捕魚沒有被全面禁止，保護程度可能差異很大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes total prohibition.","zh":"這個短語描述完全禁止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the majority of protected areas","meaning":"大多數保護區","examples":[{"en":"The level of restriction varies across the majority of protected areas.","zh":"大多數保護區的限制程度各有不同。"},{"en":"The majority of protected areas means most of the places that have protected status.","zh":"「the majority of protected areas」意思是大部分具有保護地位的地方。"},{"en":"The majority of school libraries now provide both printed books and digital resources.","zh":"大多數學校圖書館現在同時提供印刷書和數碼資源。"},{"en":"If most protected areas still allow some fishing, legal protection may not mean full protection.","zh":"如果大多數保護區仍容許某些捕魚，法律保護未必代表全面保護。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to more than half or most of a group.","zh":"這個短語指一組中的超過一半或大部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"reduce the amount of fish consumed","meaning":"減少食魚量","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to reducing the amount of fish people consume.","zh":"該選項指減少人們食魚量。"},{"en":"To reduce the amount of fish consumed means to lower how much fish people eat.","zh":"「reduce the amount of fish consumed」意思是降低人們吃魚的數量。"},{"en":"A family may reduce the amount of fish consumed by choosing beans or eggs on some days.","zh":"家庭可能透過某些日子選擇豆類或雞蛋來減少食魚量。"},{"en":"If demand for fish falls, fishing pressure may also decrease.","zh":"如果魚類需求下降，捕魚壓力也可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lowering consumption, not directly protecting habitats.","zh":"這個短語描述減少消費，而不是直接保護棲息地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"reintroduction of certain mammals","meaning":"重新引入某些哺乳動物","examples":[{"en":"The reintroduction of certain mammals may require careful planning.","zh":"重新引入某些哺乳動物可能需要仔細規劃。"},{"en":"Reintroduction of certain mammals means bringing particular mammal species back to an area where they disappeared.","zh":"「reintroduction of certain mammals」意思是把某些哺乳動物帶回牠們曾消失的地區。"},{"en":"Conservationists may plan the reintroduction of beavers to restore wetland habitats.","zh":"保育人士可能計劃重新引入海狸，以恢復濕地棲息地。"},{"en":"If mammals are reintroduced without enough food or space, the project may fail.","zh":"如果重新引入哺乳動物時沒有足夠食物或空間，項目可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deliberate species restoration.","zh":"這個短語描述刻意的物種恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a straightforward task","meaning":"簡單直接的工作","examples":[{"en":"Restoring a damaged ecosystem is rarely a straightforward task.","zh":"恢復受損生態系統很少是簡單直接的工作。"},{"en":"A straightforward task is a simple job with clear steps and few complications.","zh":"「a straightforward task」是步驟清楚、複雜因素很少的簡單工作。"},{"en":"Washing a cup is a straightforward task, but repairing a broken phone is not.","zh":"洗杯是簡單直接的工作，但修理壞手機不是。"},{"en":"If many species and food webs have changed, restoration becomes complicated.","zh":"如果許多物種和食物網已改變，恢復就變得複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used to say something is not simple.","zh":"這個短語常用來說某事並不簡單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"what the writer means by","meaning":"作者所指的是","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what the writer means by an urgent rhetorical question.","zh":"題目問作者透過迫切的修辭問題所指的是甚麼。"},{"en":"What the writer means by something asks for the intended meaning behind a phrase or sentence.","zh":"「what the writer means by」某事，是問某短語或句子背後的意圖意思。"},{"en":"In reading lessons, students often explain what the writer means by a metaphor.","zh":"在閱讀課中，學生常解釋作者透過隱喻所指的是甚麼。"},{"en":"If a phrase is indirect, students must infer the writer’s meaning from context.","zh":"如果短語是間接的，學生必須從語境推斷作者意思。"},{"en":"The phrase points to interpretation, not just word translation.","zh":"這個短語指向詮釋，而不只是字面翻譯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be based on uncertain estimates","meaning":"以不確定估算為基礎","examples":[{"en":"Some fisheries policies may be based on uncertain estimates.","zh":"有些漁業政策可能以不確定估算為基礎。"},{"en":"To be based on uncertain estimates means to depend on calculations that may be inaccurate or incomplete.","zh":"「be based on uncertain estimates」意思是依賴可能不準確或不完整的計算。"},{"en":"A school budget based on uncertain estimates may run out of money before term ends.","zh":"以不確定估算為基礎的學校預算，可能在學期結束前用完。"},{"en":"If fish numbers are estimated poorly, catch limits may be unsafe.","zh":"如果魚類數量估算不佳，捕獲限制可能不安全。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that weak data can weaken decisions.","zh":"這個短語警告薄弱數據會削弱決策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"accurate predictions","meaning":"準確預測","examples":[{"en":"Accurate predictions can help governments establish sustainable catch limits.","zh":"準確預測可以幫助政府制定可持續捕獲限制。"},{"en":"Accurate predictions are forecasts that correctly estimate what is likely to happen.","zh":"「accurate predictions」是正確估計可能發生事情的預測。"},{"en":"Accurate weather predictions help schools decide whether to cancel outdoor activities.","zh":"準確天氣預測幫助學校決定是否取消戶外活動。"},{"en":"If fish population predictions are accurate, managers can set safer catch levels.","zh":"如果魚類種群預測準確，管理者可以設定更安全的捕獲水平。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reliable forecasts.","zh":"這個短語描述可靠預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"plan properly","meaning":"作出妥善規劃","examples":[{"en":"Governments need reliable information to plan properly.","zh":"政府需要可靠資料來作出妥善規劃。"},{"en":"To plan properly means to prepare in a sensible, careful, and effective way.","zh":"「plan properly」意思是以明智、仔細和有效的方式準備。"},{"en":"Students plan properly when they divide revision into small tasks before the exam.","zh":"學生在考試前把溫習分成小任務，就是作出妥善規劃。"},{"en":"If governments lack reliable data, their fishing rules may be too weak or too late.","zh":"如果政府缺乏可靠數據，其捕魚規則可能太弱或太遲。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful preparation based on good information.","zh":"這個短語描述基於良好資料的仔細準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"provide clearer information","meaning":"提供更清晰資料","examples":[{"en":"Fisheries managers should provide clearer information to policymakers.","zh":"漁業管理人員應向政策制定者提供更清晰資料。"},{"en":"To provide clearer information means to give facts or explanations that are easier to understand and use.","zh":"「provide clearer information」意思是提供更容易理解和使用的事實或解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher can provide clearer information by giving examples instead of vague instructions.","zh":"老師可以透過給例子而不是模糊指示來提供更清晰資料。"},{"en":"If policymakers receive clear data, they can make better decisions.","zh":"如果政策制定者收到清楚數據，他們可以作出更好決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improving communication of evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述改善證據傳達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"fish stocks","meaning":"魚類資源量","examples":[{"en":"Urgent action is needed to protect declining fish stocks.","zh":"需要緊急行動保護正在下降的魚類資源量。"},{"en":"Fish stocks are populations of fish available in a particular area or fishery.","zh":"「fish stocks」是某地區或漁業中可捕或存在的魚類種群。"},{"en":"A fishing report may estimate fish stocks before setting catch limits.","zh":"漁業報告可能在設定捕獲限制前估算魚類資源量。"},{"en":"If fish stocks fall too low, both ecosystems and fishing jobs may suffer.","zh":"如果魚類資源量降得太低，生態系統和捕魚工作都可能受苦。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to fish populations as a managed resource.","zh":"這個短語把魚類種群視為可管理資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be urgently needed","meaning":"迫切需要","examples":[{"en":"Stronger protection is urgently needed to prevent further decline.","zh":"迫切需要更強保護以防止進一步下降。"},{"en":"To be urgently needed means to be required very quickly because the situation is serious.","zh":"「be urgently needed」意思是因情況嚴重而非常快速地需要。"},{"en":"Extra doctors are urgently needed when a hospital is overwhelmed.","zh":"當醫院不勝負荷時，迫切需要額外醫生。"},{"en":"If fish stocks are collapsing, delayed action may come too late.","zh":"如果魚類資源正在崩潰，延遲行動可能太遲。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses immediate necessity.","zh":"這個短語強調即時必要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the writer’s comment on","meaning":"作者對……的評論","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for the writer’s comment on the Common Fisheries Policy.","zh":"題目要求指出作者對共同漁業政策的評論。"},{"en":"The writer’s comment on something is the opinion or judgment the writer gives about it.","zh":"「the writer’s comment on」某事，是作者對它給出的意見或判斷。"},{"en":"In a reading exam, students must identify the writer’s comment on a policy from the wording used.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生必須從用字判斷作者對某政策的評論。"},{"en":"If the writer uses negative phrases, the comment is probably critical.","zh":"如果作者使用負面短語，評論很可能是批評性的。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for interpretation of the writer’s attitude.","zh":"這個短語要求理解作者態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"advocate measures","meaning":"提倡措施","examples":[{"en":"A policy may advocate measures to reduce overfishing.","zh":"一項政策可能提倡減少過度捕魚的措施。"},{"en":"To advocate measures means to publicly support actions or policies.","zh":"「advocate measures」意思是公開支持行動或政策。"},{"en":"Doctors may advocate measures such as vaccination and handwashing during flu season.","zh":"醫生在流感季節可能提倡疫苗接種和洗手等措施。"},{"en":"If scientists advocate stronger fishing limits, politicians must decide whether to follow them.","zh":"如果科學家提倡更嚴捕魚限制，政治人物必須決定是否跟從。"},{"en":"The phrase describes supporting practical actions.","zh":"這個短語描述支持實際行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be hastily implemented","meaning":"被倉促推行","examples":[{"en":"Conservation measures may fail if they are hastily implemented.","zh":"如果保育措施被倉促推行，可能會失敗。"},{"en":"To be hastily implemented means to be put into action too quickly and without enough planning.","zh":"「be hastily implemented」意思是太快且沒有足夠規劃地付諸實行。"},{"en":"A school rule may fail if it is hastily implemented before teachers understand it.","zh":"如果學校規則在老師理解前被倉促推行，可能會失敗。"},{"en":"If conservation is rushed without local support, people may resist it.","zh":"如果保育在沒有本地支持下匆忙進行，人們可能抗拒它。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against careless speed in action.","zh":"這個短語警告行動不可粗心求快。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"exaggerate recommendations","meaning":"誇大建議","examples":[{"en":"Officials may exaggerate or weaken scientific recommendations.","zh":"官員可能誇大或削弱科學建議。"},{"en":"To exaggerate recommendations means to present advice as stronger or more extreme than it really is.","zh":"「exaggerate recommendations」意思是把建議說得比實際更強或更極端。"},{"en":"A student may exaggerate a teacher’s recommendation by claiming everyone must study six hours a day.","zh":"學生可能誇大老師建議，聲稱人人必須每天溫習六小時。"},{"en":"If advice is exaggerated, people may lose trust or react against it.","zh":"如果建議被誇大，人們可能失去信任或反感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes distorting guidance by overstating it.","zh":"這個短語描述透過誇張來扭曲指導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"policymakers","meaning":"政策制定者","examples":[{"en":"Policymakers must balance scientific evidence and political pressures.","zh":"政策制定者必須平衡科學證據和政治壓力。"},{"en":"Policymakers are people who create or decide official rules, laws, or government plans.","zh":"「policymakers」是制定或決定官方規則、法律或政府計劃的人。"},{"en":"Education policymakers decide school funding, curriculum, and exam rules.","zh":"教育政策制定者決定學校資金、課程和考試規則。"},{"en":"If policymakers ignore science, environmental policy may become ineffective.","zh":"如果政策制定者忽視科學，環境政策可能變得無效。"},{"en":"The phrase names people with decision-making power over policy.","zh":"這個短語指出對政策有決策權的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"acquire a good reputation","meaning":"建立良好聲譽","examples":[{"en":"Successful policymakers may acquire a good reputation.","zh":"成功的政策制定者可能建立良好聲譽。"},{"en":"To acquire a good reputation means to gradually become known and respected for good work.","zh":"「acquire a good reputation」意思是逐漸因良好工作而被認識和尊重。"},{"en":"A teacher can acquire a good reputation by being fair, patient, and well prepared.","zh":"老師可以透過公平、有耐性和準備充足來建立良好聲譽。"},{"en":"If policymakers protect fish stocks successfully, people may trust them more.","zh":"如果政策制定者成功保護魚類資源，人們可能更信任他們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes earning public respect over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間贏得公眾尊重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"conclusion concerning","meaning":"關於……的結論","examples":[{"en":"The writer reaches a clear conclusion concerning marine decline.","zh":"作者得出關於海洋衰退的清楚結論。"},{"en":"A conclusion concerning something is a final judgment or idea about that topic.","zh":"「conclusion concerning」某事，是關於該題目的最終判斷或想法。"},{"en":"A science report may end with a conclusion concerning the effect of light on plant growth.","zh":"科學報告可能以關於光線對植物生長影響的結論作結。"},{"en":"If evidence shows repeated failure, the conclusion may call for urgent reform.","zh":"如果證據顯示反覆失敗，結論可能要求迫切改革。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the writer’s final position on an issue.","zh":"這個短語引出作者對議題的最終立場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"decline of marine resources","meaning":"海洋資源衰退","examples":[{"en":"The decline of marine resources threatens food security and ecosystems.","zh":"海洋資源衰退威脅食物安全和生態系統。"},{"en":"Decline of marine resources means a reduction in fish, habitats, biodiversity, or other useful ocean systems.","zh":"「decline of marine resources」意思是魚類、棲息地、生物多樣性或其他有用海洋系統減少。"},{"en":"A coastal village may feel the decline of marine resources when catches become smaller each year.","zh":"當捕獲量逐年減少，沿海村莊可能感受到海洋資源衰退。"},{"en":"If marine resources decline, food supplies and jobs can both be affected.","zh":"如果海洋資源衰退，食物供應和工作都可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weakening ocean wealth and life.","zh":"這個短語描述海洋財富和生命力變弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"worst outcomes","meaning":"最壞後果","examples":[{"en":"Effective management may help avoid the worst outcomes.","zh":"有效管理可能幫助避免最壞後果。"},{"en":"Worst outcomes are the most serious or damaging possible results.","zh":"「worst outcomes」是最嚴重或最具破壞性的可能結果。"},{"en":"Wearing a seat belt can help avoid the worst outcomes in a car accident.","zh":"繫安全帶可以幫助避免車禍中的最壞後果。"},{"en":"If ocean policy improves now, total ecosystem collapse may be avoided.","zh":"如果海洋政策現在改善，全面生態崩潰可能可以避免。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the most harmful consequences.","zh":"這個短語描述最有害後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"need to be prioritised","meaning":"需要獲優先處理","examples":[{"en":"The most effective conservation measures need to be prioritised.","zh":"最有效的保育措施需要獲優先處理。"},{"en":"To need to be prioritised means to need to be treated as more important than other actions.","zh":"「need to be prioritised」意思是需要被視為比其他行動更重要。"},{"en":"Before exams, weak topics need to be prioritised in revision.","zh":"考試前，薄弱題目需要在溫習中獲優先處理。"},{"en":"If time is limited, the strongest protective measures should come first.","zh":"如果時間有限，最有力的保護措施應先進行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deciding what deserves attention first.","zh":"這個短語描述決定甚麼應先受到關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"measures already taken","meaning":"已採取的措施","examples":[{"en":"Measures already taken have not been sufficient to reverse the decline.","zh":"已採取的措施不足以逆轉衰退。"},{"en":"Measures already taken are actions that have already been introduced or carried out.","zh":"「measures already taken」是已經引入或執行的行動。"},{"en":"If measures already taken by a school do not stop bullying, stronger action is needed.","zh":"如果學校已採取的措施未能阻止欺凌，就需要更強行動。"},{"en":"If past ocean policies have failed, new protection may be necessary.","zh":"如果過去海洋政策失敗，可能需要新的保護。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to actions completed before the present moment.","zh":"這個短語指目前之前已完成的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"avoid a crisis","meaning":"避免危機","examples":[{"en":"Strong protection may still help avoid a marine crisis.","zh":"強力保護仍可能幫助避免海洋危機。"},{"en":"To avoid a crisis means to prevent a serious emergency or breakdown from happening.","zh":"「avoid a crisis」意思是防止嚴重緊急情況或崩潰發生。"},{"en":"A family can avoid a financial crisis by saving money and reducing unnecessary spending.","zh":"家庭可以透過儲錢和減少不必要開支來避免財政危機。"},{"en":"If fish stocks are protected early, food shortages and ecological collapse may be avoided.","zh":"如果魚類資源及早受到保護，食物短缺和生態崩潰可能可以避免。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preventing a dangerous situation.","zh":"這個短語描述防止危險情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no likely solution","meaning":"沒有可行的解決方法","examples":[{"en":"The writer does not suggest that there is no likely solution.","zh":"作者並沒有暗示沒有可行的解決方法。"},{"en":"No likely solution means no realistic or probable way to solve a problem.","zh":"「no likely solution」意思是沒有現實或可能的解決方法。"},{"en":"A maths problem may seem to have no likely solution until the teacher explains the method.","zh":"數學題在老師解釋方法前，可能看似沒有可行解法。"},{"en":"If the writer offers marine reserves and better management, the situation is serious but not hopeless.","zh":"如果作者提出海洋保護區和更好管理，情況嚴重但並非絕望。"},{"en":"The phrase describes absence of a practical answer.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏實際答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the most effective measures","meaning":"最有效的措施","examples":[{"en":"Scientists continue to debate the most effective measures for protecting fish.","zh":"科學家繼續討論保護魚類最有效的措施。"},{"en":"The most effective measures are the actions that are most likely to produce the best results.","zh":"「the most effective measures」是最有可能產生最佳結果的行動。"},{"en":"For improving English, the most effective measures may include reading, feedback, and regular writing.","zh":"對改善英文而言，最有效的措施可能包括閱讀、回饋和定期寫作。"},{"en":"If resources are limited, governments should choose measures that protect the most marine life.","zh":"如果資源有限，政府應選擇能保護最多海洋生命的措施。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the strongest practical actions.","zh":"這個短語指出最有力的實際行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using items from the list.","zh":"學生使用列表中的項目完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill in missing parts of a shortened version of the passage.","zh":"「complete the summary」意思是填補篇章簡短版本中的缺失部分。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete the summary by matching meaning and grammar.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過配合意思和文法來完成摘要。"},{"en":"If one item does not fit the sentence, the summary becomes inaccurate.","zh":"如果一個項目不符合句子，摘要就變得不準確。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction in reading exams.","zh":"這個短語是閱讀考試中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the world’s supply of fish","meaning":"全球魚類供應","examples":[{"en":"The world’s supply of fish once appeared sufficient for human needs.","zh":"全球魚類供應曾看似足以滿足人類需要。"},{"en":"The world’s supply of fish means the total amount of fish available globally for ecosystems and people.","zh":"「the world’s supply of fish」意思是全球可供生態系統和人類使用的魚類總量。"},{"en":"Markets depend on the world’s supply of fish for seafood, jobs, and trade.","zh":"市場依靠全球魚類供應提供海鮮、工作和貿易。"},{"en":"If global fish supply declines, food security may suffer in many countries.","zh":"如果全球魚類供應下降，許多國家的食物安全可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fish as a worldwide resource.","zh":"這個短語把魚類描述為全球資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be sufficient for","meaning":"足以應付……","examples":[{"en":"Fish stocks were once believed to be sufficient for the world’s needs.","zh":"人們曾相信魚類資源足以應付世界需要。"},{"en":"To be sufficient for something means to be enough for that purpose or demand.","zh":"「be sufficient for」某事，意思是足夠達到該目的或需求。"},{"en":"One classroom may not be sufficient for a school with too many students.","zh":"對學生太多的學校而言，一間課室可能不足以應付需要。"},{"en":"If fish stocks are no longer sufficient, people must reduce pressure or find alternatives.","zh":"如果魚類資源不再足夠，人們必須減少壓力或尋找替代。"},{"en":"The phrase judges whether supply meets need.","zh":"這個短語判斷供應是否滿足需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"introduce controls","meaning":"引入管制措施","examples":[{"en":"Governments initially saw no need to introduce controls on fishing.","zh":"政府起初認為沒有需要引入捕魚管制措施。"},{"en":"To introduce controls means to create rules or limits to manage an activity.","zh":"「introduce controls」意思是制定規則或限制來管理活動。"},{"en":"A school may introduce controls on phone use during lessons.","zh":"學校可能引入課堂使用電話的管制措施。"},{"en":"If fishing becomes too intense, governments may need to introduce catch limits and closed areas.","zh":"如果捕魚變得太密集，政府可能需要引入捕獲限制和禁捕區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes starting regulation.","zh":"這個短語描述開始規管。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be inaccessible","meaning":"無法到達","examples":[{"en":"Large areas of the oceans were once inaccessible to fishing vessels.","zh":"大片海洋曾經是漁船無法到達的。"},{"en":"To be inaccessible means to be impossible or very difficult to reach or use.","zh":"「be inaccessible」意思是無法或非常難以到達或使用。"},{"en":"A village may be inaccessible after heavy rain destroys the road.","zh":"大雨毀壞道路後，村莊可能無法到達。"},{"en":"If deep waters are inaccessible, fish there are naturally protected from boats.","zh":"如果深水區無法到達，那裡的魚就自然免受漁船捕撈。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lack of access.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏可達性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"fishing techniques","meaning":"捕魚技術","examples":[{"en":"Improved fishing techniques allowed fleets to reach previously protected stocks.","zh":"改良捕魚技術讓船隊到達以前受保護的魚類資源。"},{"en":"Fishing techniques are the methods and tools used to catch fish.","zh":"「fishing techniques」是用來捕魚的方法和工具。"},{"en":"Netting, longlining, and using sonar are different fishing techniques.","zh":"撒網、延繩釣和使用聲納都是不同捕魚技術。"},{"en":"If techniques become more powerful, fish that were once safe may become catchable.","zh":"如果技術變得更強，以前安全的魚可能變得可捕。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how fishing is carried out.","zh":"這個短語描述捕魚如何進行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"regulate fish catches","meaning":"規管捕魚量","examples":[{"en":"Policies were introduced to regulate fish catches.","zh":"政策被引入以規管捕魚量。"},{"en":"To regulate fish catches means to control how many fish can be caught and under what conditions.","zh":"「regulate fish catches」意思是控制可捕魚數量以及捕魚條件。"},{"en":"A lake authority may regulate fish catches by setting a daily limit for each fisher.","zh":"湖泊管理機構可能透過為每名釣魚者設定每日限額來規管捕魚量。"},{"en":"If catches are regulated well, fish populations have more chance to recover.","zh":"如果捕獲量規管得好，魚類種群有更多機會恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase describes controlling fishing output.","zh":"這個短語描述控制捕魚產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"by comparison with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"By comparison with the land, very little of the sea is fully protected.","zh":"與陸地相比，完全受保護的海洋非常少。"},{"en":"By comparison with means when compared to another thing.","zh":"「by comparison with」意思是與另一事物比較時。"},{"en":"By comparison with city rents, village rents may seem affordable.","zh":"與城市租金相比，鄉村租金可能顯得可負擔。"},{"en":"If the sea is less protected by comparison with land, conservation efforts are uneven.","zh":"如果海洋與陸地相比保護較少，保育努力就不平均。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a comparative judgment.","zh":"這個短語引出比較判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"legal protection","meaning":"法律保障","examples":[{"en":"The oceans currently receive relatively little legal protection.","zh":"海洋目前得到的法律保障相對較少。"},{"en":"Legal protection is protection provided by laws, rules, or official regulations.","zh":"「legal protection」是由法律、規則或官方規例提供的保護。"},{"en":"Historic buildings may receive legal protection so owners cannot destroy them freely.","zh":"歷史建築可能獲法律保障，使業主不能任意拆毀。"},{"en":"If marine areas lack legal protection, fishing and exploitation may continue unchecked.","zh":"如果海域缺乏法律保障，捕魚和開發可能不受控制地持續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes protection backed by law.","zh":"這個短語描述有法律支持的保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"have doubts about","meaning":"對……抱有疑問","examples":[{"en":"Some officials continue to have doubts about marine reserves.","zh":"有些官員仍對海洋保護區抱有疑問。"},{"en":"To have doubts about something means to feel uncertain or unconvinced about it.","zh":"「have doubts about」某事，意思是對它感到不確定或未被說服。"},{"en":"A parent may have doubts about a new school policy if details are unclear.","zh":"如果新校政細節不清，家長可能對它抱有疑問。"},{"en":"If officials doubt marine reserves, they may delay creating them.","zh":"如果官員懷疑海洋保護區，他們可能延遲設立。"},{"en":"The phrase describes uncertainty or hesitation.","zh":"這個短語描述不確定或猶豫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the concept of","meaning":"……的概念","examples":[{"en":"The concept of marine reserves remains controversial among some managers.","zh":"海洋保護區的概念在某些管理人員之中仍具爭議。"},{"en":"The concept of something means the general idea behind it.","zh":"「the concept of」某事，意思是其背後的一般想法。"},{"en":"The concept of homework is simple, but students disagree about how much is fair.","zh":"功課的概念很簡單，但學生對多少才公平有分歧。"},{"en":"If people reject the concept of reserves, they may resist even small protected areas.","zh":"如果人們拒絕保護區概念，他們可能連小型保護區也抗拒。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an idea rather than one specific example.","zh":"這個短語指一種想法，而不是某一具體例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be at the heart of","meaning":"位於……的核心","examples":[{"en":"Marine reserves should be at the heart of ocean conservation.","zh":"海洋保護區應位於海洋保育的核心。"},{"en":"To be at the heart of something means to be central or most important to it.","zh":"「be at the heart of」某事，意思是成為它的中心或最重要部分。"},{"en":"Clear communication is at the heart of good customer service.","zh":"清晰溝通是良好客戶服務的核心。"},{"en":"If reserves are at the heart of conservation, other rules should support them.","zh":"如果保護區是保育核心，其他規則應支持它們。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main centre of a plan or issue.","zh":"這個短語指出計劃或議題的主要中心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"consequences of further failure","meaning":"進一步失敗的後果","examples":[{"en":"The consequences of further failure could be extremely serious.","zh":"進一步失敗的後果可能極其嚴重。"},{"en":"Consequences of further failure are the harmful results that may happen if failure continues.","zh":"「consequences of further failure」是如果失敗持續可能發生的有害結果。"},{"en":"If a student keeps ignoring weak grammar, the consequences of further failure may include lower exam confidence.","zh":"如果學生繼續忽視薄弱文法，進一步失敗的後果可能包括考試信心下降。"},{"en":"If fisheries management fails again, fish stocks and human food supplies may be at risk.","zh":"如果漁業管理再次失敗，魚類資源和人類食物供應可能面臨風險。"},{"en":"The phrase warns about what happens if problems are not solved.","zh":"這個短語警告問題未解決時會發生甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"continuing existence","meaning":"持續生存","examples":[{"en":"Damage to ocean ecosystems may ultimately affect humanity’s continuing existence.","zh":"海洋生態系統受損最終可能影響人類持續生存。"},{"en":"Continuing existence means ongoing survival into the future.","zh":"「continuing existence」意思是持續到未來的生存。"},{"en":"Clean water is necessary for a village’s continuing existence.","zh":"潔淨食水對村莊的持續生存是必要的。"},{"en":"If ecosystems that support food and climate are destroyed, human survival may be threatened.","zh":"如果支持食物和氣候的生態系統被破壞，人類生存可能受威脅。"},{"en":"The phrase describes remaining alive or present over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間繼續存活或存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 121 - The Future of fish.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 122":[{"front":"pronunciation and physiognomy","meaning":"發音與相貌","examples":[{"en":"The passage explores the possible relationship between pronunciation and physiognomy.","zh":"文章探討發音與相貌之間可能存在的關係。"},{"en":"Pronunciation and physiognomy refer to how people speak and how their facial features appear.","zh":"發音與相貌指人們如何說話，以及其面部特徵如何呈現。"},{"en":"A language teacher may notice both pronunciation and physiognomy when students practise difficult mouth movements.","zh":"當學生練習困難口腔動作時，語言老師可能同時注意到發音與相貌。"},{"en":"If certain sounds use the jaw or lips repeatedly, some people wonder whether speech habits may affect facial appearance.","zh":"如果某些聲音反覆使用下顎或嘴唇，有些人會思考說話習慣是否影響面部外貌。"},{"en":"The phrase connects speech sounds with visible facial form, but it does not prove a simple cause.","zh":"這個短語把語音與可見面貌連繫起來，但並不證明簡單因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"imagine the scene","meaning":"想像一下這個情景","examples":[{"en":"Imagine the scene: you are sitting on the tube when a stranger gets on.","zh":"想像一下這個情景：你坐在地鐵上，這時一名陌生人上車。"},{"en":"Imagine the scene means picture the situation clearly in your mind before the explanation begins.","zh":"“Imagine the scene” 指在解釋開始前，先在腦海中清楚想像該情況。"},{"en":"A teacher may say “imagine the scene” before asking students to think about a crowded bus.","zh":"老師可能先說「想像一下這個情景」，再要求學生思考一架擁擠巴士。"},{"en":"If readers imagine the scene, they can understand the example more personally.","zh":"如果讀者想像該場景，就能更個人化地理解例子。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used to introduce a vivid situation.","zh":"這個短語常用來引入一個生動情境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sit on the tube","meaning":"坐地鐵","examples":[{"en":"You are sitting on the tube when someone gets on.","zh":"你正坐在地鐵上，這時有人上車。"},{"en":"To sit on the tube means to sit inside the London Underground while travelling.","zh":"“Sit on the tube” 指乘搭倫敦地鐵時坐在車廂內。"},{"en":"A commuter may sit on the tube every morning on the way to work.","zh":"通勤者可能每天早上坐地鐵上班。"},{"en":"If someone sits on the tube, they may notice other passengers’ clothes, accents or behaviour.","zh":"如果某人坐地鐵，他可能注意到其他乘客的衣着、口音或行為。"},{"en":"The phrase is British English and refers to travelling by underground train.","zh":"這個短語屬英式英語，指乘搭地下鐵路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"instinctively believe","meaning":"本能地相信","examples":[{"en":"You instinctively believe that the stranger is American.","zh":"你本能地相信那名陌生人是美國人。"},{"en":"To instinctively believe something means to feel it is true immediately, before careful reasoning.","zh":"本能地相信某事，指在仔細推理前立即覺得它是真的。"},{"en":"A teacher may instinctively believe a student is nervous after seeing their shaking hands.","zh":"老師看見學生雙手顫抖後，可能本能地相信他很緊張。"},{"en":"If you instinctively believe something, your judgement may come from small clues you barely notice.","zh":"如果你本能地相信某事，你的判斷可能來自自己幾乎沒有注意到的小線索。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a quick feeling of certainty rather than a proven conclusion.","zh":"這個短語描述快速的確信感，而不是已證明的結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get on","meaning":"上車","examples":[{"en":"Someone whom you believe to be American gets on the train.","zh":"你認為是美國人的某人上了火車。"},{"en":"To get on a train, bus or plane means to enter it in order to travel.","zh":"“Get on” 火車、巴士或飛機，指進入其中以乘搭。"},{"en":"Students get on the school bus outside the gate every morning.","zh":"學生每天早上在校門外上校巴。"},{"en":"If many passengers get on at the same stop, the carriage becomes crowded quickly.","zh":"如果許多乘客在同一站上車，車廂很快會變得擁擠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes boarding a vehicle.","zh":"這個短語描述登上交通工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確定；確認","examples":[{"en":"To make sure, you ask the stranger what time it is.","zh":"為了確認，你問那名陌生人現在幾點。"},{"en":"To make sure means to check something so that you know it is correct.","zh":"“Make sure” 指檢查某事，以知道它是正確的。"},{"en":"A student may read the question twice to make sure they understand it.","zh":"學生可能把題目讀兩次，以確定自己理解。"},{"en":"If you are unsure about a person’s accent, asking a simple question may help confirm it.","zh":"如果你不肯定某人的口音，問一條簡單問題可能有助確認。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when someone wants confirmation before deciding.","zh":"這個短語用於某人在作決定前想得到確認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ask someone the time","meaning":"問某人時間","examples":[{"en":"You ask the stranger the time to hear their accent.","zh":"你問那名陌生人時間，以聽到他的口音。"},{"en":"To ask someone the time means to ask what time it is.","zh":"問某人時間，指問現在幾點。"},{"en":"A traveller may ask someone the time if their phone battery has died.","zh":"如果手機沒電，旅客可能問別人時間。"},{"en":"If you ask someone the time, their short answer may reveal their accent.","zh":"如果你問某人時間，他的簡短回答可能透露其口音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a simple everyday question.","zh":"這個短語描述一條簡單日常問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"how did you know?","meaning":"你是怎樣知道的？","examples":[{"en":"You were right about the person’s nationality, but how did you know?","zh":"你猜對了那個人的國籍，但你是怎樣知道的？"},{"en":"How did you know? asks what clues or reasoning helped someone reach the correct answer.","zh":"“How did you know?” 是問甚麼線索或推理幫助某人得出正確答案。"},{"en":"A student may ask “How did you know?” when a friend guesses the answer before seeing the solution.","zh":"當朋友在看答案前猜中，學生可能問：「你是怎樣知道的？」"},{"en":"If someone identifies an accent correctly, this question asks what evidence guided them.","zh":"如果某人正確辨認出口音，這個問題就是問甚麼證據引導了他。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses curiosity about the source of someone’s knowledge.","zh":"這個短語表達對某人知識來源的好奇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"look American","meaning":"看起來像美國人","examples":[{"en":"People sometimes claim that someone “looks American”.","zh":"人們有時聲稱某人「看起來像美國人」。"},{"en":"To look American means to appear, from someone’s point of view, to have features or style associated with Americans.","zh":"看起來像美國人，指從某人的角度看，似乎有與美國人相關的特徵或風格。"},{"en":"A tourist may be said to look American because of clothing, gestures, confidence or facial expression.","zh":"遊客可能因衣着、手勢、自信或面部表情而被說成看起來像美國人。"},{"en":"If Americans do not belong to one single race, the phrase cannot simply refer to ethnicity.","zh":"如果美國人不屬於單一種族，這個短語就不能單純指族裔。"},{"en":"The phrase describes perception and stereotype, not a scientific category.","zh":"這個短語描述觀感和刻板印象，而不是科學分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"take into consideration","meaning":"將……考慮在內","examples":[{"en":"We take dress, mannerisms, and physical appearance into consideration.","zh":"我們將衣着、舉止和外貌考慮在內。"},{"en":"To take something into consideration means to include it when making a judgement or decision.","zh":"將某事考慮在內，指在作判斷或決定時包括它。"},{"en":"A teacher takes effort, improvement and accuracy into consideration when marking speaking practice.","zh":"老師評改口語練習時，會將努力、進步和準確度考慮在內。"},{"en":"If people judge nationality, they may consider clothing, behaviour and facial features together.","zh":"如果人們判斷國籍，可能會把衣着、行為和面部特徵一起考慮。"},{"en":"The phrase means not to ignore a relevant factor.","zh":"這個短語指不要忽略相關因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mannerisms","meaning":"習慣性動作；舉止","examples":[{"en":"A person’s mannerisms may influence how others perceive them.","zh":"一個人的習慣性動作可能影響他人如何看待他。"},{"en":"Mannerisms are small repeated habits in movement, speech or expression.","zh":"習慣性動作是動作、說話或表情中的小型重複習慣。"},{"en":"A student’s mannerisms may include tapping a pen, smiling often or avoiding eye contact.","zh":"學生的習慣性動作可能包括敲筆、經常微笑或避免眼神接觸。"},{"en":"If someone has confident mannerisms, others may assume they are calm or experienced.","zh":"如果某人有自信的舉止，別人可能以為他冷靜或有經驗。"},{"en":"The word refers to habitual behaviour, not deep personality itself.","zh":"這個詞指習慣性行為，而不是深層性格本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"physical appearance","meaning":"外貌","examples":[{"en":"Dress and physical appearance can affect our first impressions.","zh":"衣着和外貌可以影響我們的第一印象。"},{"en":"Physical appearance means how a person looks, including face, body, hair, clothing and posture.","zh":"外貌指一個人的樣子，包括面容、身形、頭髮、衣着和姿勢。"},{"en":"In a job interview, neat physical appearance may help create a professional first impression.","zh":"在求職面試中，整潔外貌可能有助建立專業第一印象。"},{"en":"If people rely too much on physical appearance, they may make unfair assumptions.","zh":"如果人們過分依賴外貌，可能作出不公平假設。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to visible features rather than character or ability.","zh":"這個短語指可見特徵，而不是性格或能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"constitute one single race","meaning":"構成單一種族","examples":[{"en":"Americans do not constitute one single race.","zh":"美國人並不構成單一種族。"},{"en":"To constitute one single race means to form one unified racial group.","zh":"構成單一種族，指形成一個統一的種族群體。"},{"en":"A country with immigrants from many backgrounds does not constitute one single ethnic group.","zh":"一個有許多不同背景移民的國家，並不構成單一族群。"},{"en":"If a population is racially diverse, appearance cannot be explained by race alone.","zh":"如果人口在種族上多元，外貌就不能單靠種族解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase challenges oversimplified racial assumptions.","zh":"這個短語挑戰過分簡化的種族假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what exactly is meant by","meaning":"……究竟是甚麼意思","examples":[{"en":"What exactly is meant by saying that someone looks American?","zh":"說某人看起來像美國人，究竟是甚麼意思？"},{"en":"What exactly is meant by asks for the precise meaning of a phrase or claim.","zh":"“What exactly is meant by” 是要求說明某短語或主張的精確意思。"},{"en":"A student may ask what exactly is meant by “good communication skills” in a job ad.","zh":"學生可能問招聘廣告中的「良好溝通能力」究竟是甚麼意思。"},{"en":"If a phrase sounds vague, this question forces the speaker to explain it clearly.","zh":"如果短語聽起來含糊，這個問題會迫使說話者清楚解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful for challenging unclear or stereotyped language.","zh":"這個短語有助挑戰不清楚或刻板的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"salient feature","meaning":"顯著特徵","examples":[{"en":"One salient feature is a pronounced widening around the jaw.","zh":"一個顯著特徵是在下顎周圍明顯擴闊。"},{"en":"A salient feature is a very noticeable or important characteristic.","zh":"顯著特徵是非常明顯或重要的特點。"},{"en":"A salient feature of a good classroom is that students feel safe to ask questions.","zh":"好課室的一個顯著特徵，是學生感到安全，可以發問。"},{"en":"If a facial feature is salient, people notice it quickly when forming an impression.","zh":"如果面部特徵很顯著，人們形成印象時會很快注意到它。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a feature that stands out.","zh":"這個短語指出突出的特點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pronounced widening","meaning":"明顯擴闊","examples":[{"en":"Some observers have noticed a pronounced widening around the jaw.","zh":"一些觀察者注意到下顎周圍明顯擴闊。"},{"en":"Pronounced widening means a clearly visible increase in width.","zh":"明顯擴闊指寬度清楚可見地增加。"},{"en":"A road may show pronounced widening near a busy junction to allow more cars to pass.","zh":"道路在繁忙路口附近可能明顯擴闊，以讓更多車輛通過。"},{"en":"If the jaw shows pronounced widening, it appears broader than before or than expected.","zh":"如果下顎明顯擴闊，它就比以前或預期看起來更寬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a noticeable change in shape.","zh":"這個短語描述形狀上可注意到的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"around the jaw","meaning":"在下顎周圍","examples":[{"en":"The physical difference is most visible around the jaw.","zh":"這種身體差異在下顎周圍最明顯。"},{"en":"Around the jaw means in the area near the lower part of the face where the jawbone is.","zh":"在下顎周圍，指臉部下方接近下顎骨的區域。"},{"en":"A dentist may notice swelling around the jaw after a tooth infection.","zh":"牙齒感染後，牙醫可能注意到下顎周圍腫脹。"},{"en":"If muscles around the jaw are used often, the lower face may feel tense.","zh":"如果下顎周圍肌肉經常使用，下半張臉可能感到繃緊。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the location of a facial feature.","zh":"這個短語給出面部特徵的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"well-documented phenomenon","meaning":"有充分記錄的現象","examples":[{"en":"The widening of the jaw is described as a well-documented phenomenon.","zh":"下顎擴闊被描述為有充分記錄的現象。"},{"en":"A well-documented phenomenon is something recorded or observed many times with supporting evidence.","zh":"有充分記錄的現象，是被多次記錄或觀察並有支持證據的事情。"},{"en":"The effect of poor sleep on memory is a well-documented phenomenon in education and health research.","zh":"睡眠不足影響記憶，是教育和健康研究中有充分記錄的現象。"},{"en":"If many observers have recorded the same pattern, it becomes harder to dismiss casually.","zh":"如果許多觀察者記錄了同一模式，就較難隨便否定。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that a claim has some recorded basis.","zh":"這個短語暗示某主張有一定記錄基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"once remarked that","meaning":"曾經評論說","examples":[{"en":"Arthur Koestler once remarked that his friends’ appearances had changed.","zh":"Arthur Koestler 曾經評論說他的朋友外貌已經改變。"},{"en":"Once remarked that means said or commented at one time in the past.","zh":"“Once remarked that” 指在過去某一時候說過或評論過。"},{"en":"A teacher once remarked that quiet students often notice the most details.","zh":"一位老師曾經評論說，安靜學生往往注意到最多細節。"},{"en":"If a writer once remarked on a pattern, later researchers may revisit the idea.","zh":"如果作家曾經評論某個模式，後來研究者可能重新審視該想法。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a past observation or comment.","zh":"這個短語引出過去的觀察或評論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"thirty years after","meaning":"三十年後","examples":[{"en":"He met his friends thirty years after they had emigrated.","zh":"他在朋友移居三十年後與他們見面。"},{"en":"Thirty years after means three decades later than a particular event.","zh":"三十年後，指在某事件之後三個十年。"},{"en":"A student may visit their old school thirty years after graduation.","zh":"學生可能在畢業三十年後回訪舊校。"},{"en":"If someone sees friends thirty years after migration, long-term changes may be easier to notice.","zh":"如果某人在朋友移民三十年後再見他們，長期變化可能更容易注意到。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a long time gap after an event.","zh":"這個短語給出事件後的長時間間隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"emigrate to","meaning":"移居到","examples":[{"en":"Several of Koestler’s friends had emigrated to the United States.","zh":"Koestler 的幾位朋友已移居到美國。"},{"en":"To emigrate to a country means to leave one’s own country and move there to live.","zh":"移居到某國，指離開自己的國家並搬到該國生活。"},{"en":"A family may emigrate to Canada for work, education or safety.","zh":"一個家庭可能因工作、教育或安全而移居到加拿大。"},{"en":"If people emigrate to a new country, their speech, habits and appearance may change over time.","zh":"如果人們移居到新國家，他們的說話、習慣和外貌可能隨時間改變。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on moving abroad to settle.","zh":"這個短語強調搬到海外定居。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"acquire an American physiognomy","meaning":"形成美國人的相貌特徵","examples":[{"en":"His friends appeared to have acquired an American physiognomy.","zh":"他的朋友看來已形成美國人的相貌特徵。"},{"en":"To acquire an American physiognomy means gradually to develop facial features or expressions associated with Americans.","zh":"形成美國人的相貌特徵，指逐漸發展出與美國人相關的面部特徵或表情。"},{"en":"An immigrant may acquire local speech habits after living in a new country for decades.","zh":"移民在新國家生活數十年後，可能形成當地說話習慣。"},{"en":"If pronunciation affects facial muscles, long-term use of American English might change the face slightly.","zh":"如果發音影響面部肌肉，長期使用美式英語可能稍微改變面容。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a possible acquired appearance, not a change of ancestry.","zh":"這個短語描述可能後天形成的外貌，而不是血統改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"broadened jaw","meaning":"較寬的下顎","examples":[{"en":"The so-called American physiognomy included a broadened jaw.","zh":"所謂美國人的相貌特徵包括較寬的下顎。"},{"en":"A broadened jaw is a jaw that appears wider than before or wider than average.","zh":"較寬的下顎，是看起來比以前或平均水平更寬的下顎。"},{"en":"A dentist may notice a broadened jaw shape when comparing old and recent facial photos.","zh":"牙醫比較舊近面部照片時，可能注意到較寬的下顎形狀。"},{"en":"If jaw muscles are used strongly over years, some people speculate the jaw may appear broader.","zh":"如果下顎肌肉多年來被強烈使用，有些人推測下顎可能顯得更寬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a visible feature of the lower face.","zh":"這個短語描述下半張臉的可見特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be prevalent in","meaning":"在……中很普遍","examples":[{"en":"A broadened jaw is also prevalent in the indigenous population.","zh":"較寬下顎在本地原有居民中也很普遍。"},{"en":"To be prevalent in a group means to be common or widespread among that group.","zh":"在某群體中很普遍，指在該群體中常見或廣泛存在。"},{"en":"Smartphone use is prevalent in many schools, even when phones are not allowed in class.","zh":"智能手機使用在許多學校很普遍，即使課堂不准使用手機。"},{"en":"If a feature is prevalent in a population, many people in that group show it.","zh":"如果某特徵在人口中很普遍，該群體中許多人都有它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how common something is within a group.","zh":"這個短語描述某事在群體內有多常見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"indigenous population","meaning":"本地原有居民","examples":[{"en":"The feature is common among the indigenous population.","zh":"這個特徵在本地原有居民中很常見。"},{"en":"The indigenous population is the original native people of a region.","zh":"本地原有居民是某地區最初的原住民。"},{"en":"A country’s indigenous population may have languages and traditions that existed before later settlers arrived.","zh":"一個國家的本地原有居民可能擁有早於後來移民到達前已存在的語言和傳統。"},{"en":"If a feature is common among indigenous people, it may be linked to ancestry, environment or long-term lifestyle.","zh":"如果某特徵在原住民中常見，它可能與血統、環境或長期生活方式有關。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to native communities, not recent immigrants.","zh":"這個短語指原住社群，而不是近期移民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"anthropologist friend","meaning":"人類學家朋友","examples":[{"en":"An anthropologist friend offered an explanation for the change.","zh":"一位人類學家朋友為這種改變提出解釋。"},{"en":"An anthropologist friend is a friend who studies human societies, cultures and physical variation.","zh":"人類學家朋友，是研究人類社會、文化和身體差異的朋友。"},{"en":"An anthropologist friend may explain why people in different communities eat, speak or dress differently.","zh":"人類學家朋友可能解釋為何不同社群的人吃、說話或穿着不同。"},{"en":"If a writer consults an anthropologist, the explanation may involve culture, biology or social behaviour.","zh":"如果作者請教人類學家，解釋可能涉及文化、生物或社會行為。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a friend with specialist knowledge about humans.","zh":"這個短語指出一位擁有人類研究專門知識的朋友。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"attribute something to","meaning":"將……歸因於","examples":[{"en":"The anthropologist attributed the change to increased use of the jaw muscles.","zh":"人類學家將這種改變歸因於下顎肌肉使用增加。"},{"en":"To attribute something to a cause means to say that the cause explains it.","zh":"將某事歸因於某原因，指說該原因解釋了它。"},{"en":"A doctor may attribute tiredness to lack of sleep after checking other symptoms.","zh":"醫生檢查其他症狀後，可能將疲倦歸因於睡眠不足。"},{"en":"If facial change is attributed to pronunciation, speech habits are being treated as a possible cause.","zh":"如果面部改變被歸因於發音，說話習慣就是被視為可能原因。"},{"en":"The phrase links an effect with an explanation.","zh":"這個短語把結果與解釋連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"increased use of","meaning":"更頻繁使用……","examples":[{"en":"The theory focuses on the increased use of the jaw musculature.","zh":"這個理論集中於更頻繁使用下顎肌肉組織。"},{"en":"Increased use of something means using it more often or more strongly than before.","zh":"更頻繁使用某物，指比以前更常或更強烈地使用它。"},{"en":"Increased use of laptops in class can change how students take notes.","zh":"課堂中更頻繁使用手提電腦，可以改變學生做筆記的方式。"},{"en":"If a sound requires more jaw movement, increased use of jaw muscles may occur over time.","zh":"如果某個音需要更多下顎動作，下顎肌肉使用可能隨時間增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a rise in frequency or intensity of use.","zh":"這個短語描述使用頻率或強度上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"jaw musculature","meaning":"下顎肌肉組織","examples":[{"en":"American pronunciation may involve greater use of the jaw musculature.","zh":"美式發音可能涉及更多使用下顎肌肉組織。"},{"en":"Jaw musculature means the muscles around the jaw that help move the mouth.","zh":"下顎肌肉組織指下顎周圍幫助口部移動的肌肉。"},{"en":"A speech therapist may study jaw musculature when helping a patient speak more clearly.","zh":"言語治療師幫助病人說話更清楚時，可能研究下顎肌肉組織。"},{"en":"If jaw musculature is used repeatedly, the lower face may feel tired after practice.","zh":"如果下顎肌肉組織被反覆使用，練習後下半張臉可能感到疲累。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the muscle system of the jaw.","zh":"這個短語指下顎的肌肉系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"American enunciation","meaning":"美式咬字方式","examples":[{"en":"The anthropologist linked the change to American enunciation.","zh":"人類學家把這種改變與美式咬字方式連繫起來。"},{"en":"American enunciation means the way sounds are clearly pronounced in American English.","zh":"美式咬字方式指美式英語中清楚發出聲音的方式。"},{"en":"An actor may practise American enunciation to make a role sound convincing.","zh":"演員可能練習美式咬字方式，使角色聽起來可信。"},{"en":"If American enunciation uses the jaw differently, it may create different mouth movements.","zh":"如果美式咬字方式以不同方式使用下顎，就可能產生不同口部動作。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on clear speech style, not just vocabulary.","zh":"這個短語強調清晰說話方式，而不只是詞彙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"change of countenance","meaning":"面容的變化","examples":[{"en":"The change of countenance in immigrants had been observed earlier.","zh":"移民面容的變化早前已被觀察到。"},{"en":"A change of countenance is a change in someone’s face, expression or general facial appearance.","zh":"面容的變化，是某人的面部、表情或整體面貌發生改變。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice a change of countenance when a confident student suddenly becomes worried.","zh":"當自信學生突然變得擔心，老師可能注意到其面容變化。"},{"en":"If immigrants show a change of countenance over many years, researchers may ask what caused it.","zh":"如果移民多年後出現面容變化，研究者可能追問原因。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and refers to visible facial change.","zh":"這個短語較正式，指可見的面部改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be observed by","meaning":"被……觀察到","examples":[{"en":"The phenomenon had already been observed by a historian.","zh":"這個現象已被一位歷史學家觀察到。"},{"en":"To be observed by someone means to be noticed, recorded or studied by that person.","zh":"被某人觀察到，指被該人注意、記錄或研究。"},{"en":"A change in student behaviour may be observed by teachers before parents notice it.","zh":"學生行為變化可能在家長注意前，已被老師觀察到。"},{"en":"If a pattern is observed by different researchers, it may deserve closer study.","zh":"如果某模式被不同研究者觀察到，它可能值得更仔細研究。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who noticed or recorded something.","zh":"這個短語指出誰注意或記錄某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"paraphrase someone","meaning":"改述某人的話","examples":[{"en":"To paraphrase Emerson, certain groups develop a distinguishing appearance.","zh":"改述 Emerson 的話，某些群體會形成獨特外貌。"},{"en":"To paraphrase someone means to restate their idea in different words.","zh":"改述某人的話，指用不同字眼重新表達其想法。"},{"en":"A student may paraphrase a writer’s argument to show understanding without copying.","zh":"學生可能改述作者論點，以顯示理解而不抄襲。"},{"en":"If you paraphrase an author, the meaning should stay faithful even when the wording changes.","zh":"如果你改述作者，措辭即使改變，意思也應保持忠實。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an idea borrowed and reworded from another person.","zh":"這個短語引出借用並重新措辭的他人想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"national, social and religious groups","meaning":"國家、社會及宗教群體","examples":[{"en":"Different national, social and religious groups may develop recognisable looks.","zh":"不同國家、社會及宗教群體可能形成可辨認的外貌。"},{"en":"National, social and religious groups are communities defined by country, social role or faith.","zh":"國家、社會及宗教群體，是由國家、社會角色或信仰界定的社群。"},{"en":"School uniforms, work habits or religious practices may shape how different groups appear.","zh":"校服、工作習慣或宗教實踐可能塑造不同群體的外觀。"},{"en":"If a group shares a way of life for many years, members may develop similar expressions or mannerisms.","zh":"如果某群體多年共享一種生活方式，成員可能形成相似表情或舉止。"},{"en":"The phrase groups people by identity, lifestyle and belief.","zh":"這個短語按身份、生活方式和信念把人分組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"aging actors","meaning":"年長演員","examples":[{"en":"Aging actors are given as one example of a distinctive social group.","zh":"年長演員被列為一個具獨特性的社會群體例子。"},{"en":"Aging actors are performers who have grown older after years in theatre, film or television.","zh":"年長演員是經多年劇場、電影或電視表演後變老的表演者。"},{"en":"Aging actors may carry habits of facial expression developed through years of performance.","zh":"年長演員可能帶有多年表演形成的面部表情習慣。"},{"en":"If actors spend decades using expressive faces on stage, their appearance may become distinctive.","zh":"如果演員數十年在舞台上使用豐富表情，其外貌可能變得獨特。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to older performers as a group shaped by their profession.","zh":"這個短語指由職業塑造的一群較年長表演者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"long-term convicts","meaning":"長期囚犯","examples":[{"en":"Long-term convicts may develop recognisable expressions or mannerisms.","zh":"長期囚犯可能形成可辨認的表情或舉止。"},{"en":"Long-term convicts are prisoners who have spent many years in prison.","zh":"長期囚犯是在監獄中度過多年的人。"},{"en":"A long-term convict may develop guarded expressions because prison life requires caution.","zh":"長期囚犯可能形成戒備表情，因為監獄生活需要謹慎。"},{"en":"If someone lives under strict control for years, their posture and face may change.","zh":"如果某人多年生活在嚴格控制下，其姿勢和面容可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase connects long imprisonment with possible visible habits.","zh":"這個短語把長期監禁與可能可見的習慣連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"celibate priests","meaning":"獨身神職人員","examples":[{"en":"Celibate priests are another example mentioned in the passage.","zh":"獨身神職人員是文章提到的另一個例子。"},{"en":"Celibate priests are priests who do not marry or have sexual relationships for religious reasons.","zh":"獨身神職人員，是因宗教理由而不結婚或不發生性關係的神職人員。"},{"en":"A celibate priest may live a disciplined life shaped by church rules and daily rituals.","zh":"獨身神職人員可能過着受教會規則和日常儀式塑造的自律生活。"},{"en":"If a group shares strict habits for many years, outsiders may think they have a recognisable look.","zh":"如果某群體多年共享嚴格習慣，外人可能認為他們有可辨認外貌。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to religious figures defined partly by a vow of celibacy.","zh":"這個短語指部分由獨身誓願界定的宗教人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"to give just a few examples","meaning":"只舉幾個例子","examples":[{"en":"Aging actors and convicts are mentioned, to give just a few examples.","zh":"年長演員和囚犯被提及，只舉幾個例子。"},{"en":"To give just a few examples means the speaker is listing only some possible examples, not all of them.","zh":"“To give just a few examples” 指說話者只列出一些可能例子，而不是全部。"},{"en":"School stress can come from exams, homework and family expectations, to give just a few examples.","zh":"學校壓力可以來自考試、功課和家庭期望，只舉幾個例子。"},{"en":"If a writer uses this phrase, the list is meant to illustrate a wider pattern.","zh":"如果作者使用這個短語，列表是用來說明更大模式。"},{"en":"The phrase prevents readers from thinking the list is complete.","zh":"這個短語避免讀者以為列表完整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"develop a distinguishing look","meaning":"形成獨特外貌","examples":[{"en":"Certain social groups may develop a distinguishing look.","zh":"某些社會群體可能形成獨特外貌。"},{"en":"To develop a distinguishing look means gradually to acquire an appearance that makes a group recognisable.","zh":"形成獨特外貌，指逐漸形成一種令群體可被辨認的外觀。"},{"en":"A sports team may develop a distinguishing look through uniforms, posture and training habits.","zh":"運動隊可能透過制服、姿勢和訓練習慣形成獨特外貌。"},{"en":"If people share work, stress and habits for years, their expressions may become similar.","zh":"如果人們多年共享工作、壓力和習慣，其表情可能變得相似。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an appearance that marks a group apart.","zh":"這個短語描述令群體與別不同的外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not easily defined","meaning":"不容易界定","examples":[{"en":"The appearance is not easily defined but can still be recognised.","zh":"這種外貌不容易界定，但仍可以被辨認。"},{"en":"Not easily defined means difficult to explain clearly in exact words.","zh":"不容易界定指難以用準確文字清楚解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher’s warm classroom style may be not easily defined, but students can feel it.","zh":"老師溫暖的課堂風格可能不容易界定，但學生感受得到。"},{"en":"If a group’s look is subtle, people may recognise it without knowing how to describe it.","zh":"如果群體外貌很微妙，人們可能認得出卻不知道如何描述。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something recognisable but hard to define precisely.","zh":"這個短語描述可辨認但難以精確界定的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"readily recognised","meaning":"很容易辨認","examples":[{"en":"A group’s characteristic appearance may be readily recognised.","zh":"一個群體的特徵外貌可能很容易辨認。"},{"en":"Readily recognised means easily and quickly identified.","zh":"很容易辨認，指容易且快速地識別出來。"},{"en":"A school uniform is readily recognised by people living near the school.","zh":"住在學校附近的人很容易辨認該校校服。"},{"en":"If a facial expression is readily recognised, observers do not need long explanation.","zh":"如果面部表情很容易辨認，觀察者不需要長篇解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something easy to notice and identify.","zh":"這個短語描述容易注意和識別的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"way of life","meaning":"生活方式","examples":[{"en":"A person’s way of life may affect their physical appearance.","zh":"一個人的生活方式可能影響其外貌。"},{"en":"A way of life is the usual pattern of daily habits, work, beliefs and behaviour.","zh":"生活方式是日常習慣、工作、信念和行為的通常模式。"},{"en":"A farmer’s way of life may involve early mornings, outdoor work and physical labour.","zh":"農夫的生活方式可能包括清晨起床、戶外工作和體力勞動。"},{"en":"If a way of life changes after migration, speech and body habits may also change.","zh":"如果移民後生活方式改變，說話和身體習慣也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how people live, not just where they live.","zh":"這個短語描述人們如何生活，而不只是他們住在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"affect facial expression","meaning":"影響面部表情","examples":[{"en":"Lifestyle can affect facial expression and physical features.","zh":"生活方式可以影響面部表情和身體特徵。"},{"en":"To affect facial expression means to influence how the face usually looks or moves.","zh":"影響面部表情，指影響面部通常如何呈現或移動。"},{"en":"A person who works in customer service may develop a habit of smiling often.","zh":"從事客戶服務的人可能形成經常微笑的習慣。"},{"en":"If someone spends years under stress, their facial expression may appear tense.","zh":"如果某人多年處於壓力下，其面部表情可能顯得繃緊。"},{"en":"The phrase connects daily experience with visible expression.","zh":"這個短語把日常經驗與可見表情連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"physical features","meaning":"身體特徵；外貌特徵","examples":[{"en":"Physical features may be influenced by both lifestyle and heredity.","zh":"身體特徵可能同時受生活方式和遺傳影響。"},{"en":"Physical features are visible parts of a person’s body or face, such as height, jaw shape or cheekbones.","zh":"身體特徵是一個人身體或面部可見部分，例如身高、下顎形狀或顴骨。"},{"en":"Doctors may look at physical features when checking a child’s growth.","zh":"醫生檢查孩子成長時，可能觀察身體特徵。"},{"en":"If physical features are partly shaped by habits, appearance is not only genetic.","zh":"如果身體特徵部分由習慣塑造，外貌就不只是基因造成。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to visible bodily characteristics.","zh":"這個短語指可見的身體特質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"give the mistaken impression that","meaning":"令人誤以為","examples":[{"en":"These features may give the mistaken impression that they are hereditary.","zh":"這些特徵可能令人誤以為它們是遺傳的。"},{"en":"To give the mistaken impression that something is true means to make people wrongly believe it.","zh":"令人誤以為某事為真，指使人錯誤相信它。"},{"en":"A quiet student may give the mistaken impression that they are not interested.","zh":"安靜學生可能令人誤以為他沒有興趣。"},{"en":"If lifestyle shapes appearance, people may wrongly think the feature comes only from genes.","zh":"如果生活方式塑造外貌，人們可能錯誤以為特徵只來自基因。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that first impressions can be misleading.","zh":"這個短語提醒第一印象可能具誤導性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hereditary origin","meaning":"遺傳來源","examples":[{"en":"Some traits may appear to have a hereditary origin.","zh":"一些特徵可能看似有遺傳來源。"},{"en":"A hereditary origin means something comes from genes passed from parents to children.","zh":"遺傳來源指某事來自父母傳給子女的基因。"},{"en":"Eye colour usually has a hereditary origin because children inherit genes from their parents.","zh":"眼睛顏色通常有遺傳來源，因為孩子從父母繼承基因。"},{"en":"If a feature is actually shaped by lifestyle, calling it hereditary may be mistaken.","zh":"如果某特徵實際由生活方式塑造，把它稱為遺傳可能錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase explains a biological source across generations.","zh":"這個短語解釋跨代生物來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"racial origin","meaning":"種族根源","examples":[{"en":"Observers may wrongly assume that certain facial traits have a racial origin.","zh":"觀察者可能錯誤假設某些面部特徵有種族根源。"},{"en":"Racial origin means a source related to a person’s race or ancestry.","zh":"種族根源指與某人的種族或血統相關的來源。"},{"en":"People should be cautious before claiming that a behaviour has a racial origin.","zh":"人們在聲稱某行為有種族根源前應謹慎。"},{"en":"If facial habits come from lifestyle or pronunciation, race may not be the real explanation.","zh":"如果面部習慣來自生活方式或發音，種族未必是真正解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase is sensitive and should be used carefully.","zh":"這個短語較敏感，應小心使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"contribute to","meaning":"導致；促成","examples":[{"en":"Many environmental and hereditary factors contribute to appearance.","zh":"許多環境和遺傳因素促成外貌。"},{"en":"To contribute to something means to help cause it or add to it.","zh":"“Contribute to” 某事指幫助造成它或增加它。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can contribute to poor concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致課堂專注力差。"},{"en":"If both genes and lifestyle contribute to appearance, no single factor explains everything.","zh":"如果基因和生活方式都影響外貌，就沒有單一因素能解釋一切。"},{"en":"The phrase shows partial cause, not always the only cause.","zh":"這個短語顯示部分原因，而不一定是唯一原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as well as heredity","meaning":"以及遺傳因素","examples":[{"en":"Lifestyle contributes to appearance, as well as heredity.","zh":"生活方式和遺傳因素一樣，都會影響外貌。"},{"en":"As well as heredity means in addition to inherited genetic factors.","zh":"“As well as heredity” 指除了遺傳基因因素之外。"},{"en":"A child’s learning depends on teaching and practice, as well as natural ability.","zh":"孩子的學習取決於教學和練習，以及天生能力。"},{"en":"If lifestyle matters as well as heredity, appearance may change through lived experience.","zh":"如果生活方式和遺傳都重要，外貌可能透過生活經驗而改變。"},{"en":"The phrase adds another factor to genetics.","zh":"這個短語在基因之外加入另一因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"appearance being affected by","meaning":"外貌受到……影響","examples":[{"en":"The question of appearance being affected by pronunciation deserves study.","zh":"外貌受到發音影響這個問題值得研究。"},{"en":"Appearance being affected by something means someone’s visible look is influenced by that factor.","zh":"外貌受到某事影響，指某人的可見樣貌受該因素影響。"},{"en":"Skin appearance being affected by sunlight is easy to understand after years outdoors.","zh":"長年在戶外後，皮膚外貌受陽光影響很容易理解。"},{"en":"If pronunciation affects appearance, repeated speech movements may slowly shape facial muscles.","zh":"如果發音影響外貌，重複說話動作可能慢慢塑造面部肌肉。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a possible influence on how people look.","zh":"這個短語描述某因素對外貌的可能影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in the case of","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"The theory is particularly interesting in the case of immigrants.","zh":"這個理論就移民而言尤其有趣。"},{"en":"In the case of means when discussing or considering a particular person, group or situation.","zh":"“In the case of” 指在討論或考慮某特定人、群體或情況時。"},{"en":"In the case of young children, teachers often use pictures before abstract explanations.","zh":"就年幼兒童而言，老師常先使用圖片，再作抽象解釋。"},{"en":"If immigrants change language after moving, their case may reveal long-term speech effects.","zh":"如果移民搬遷後改變語言，他們的個案可能揭示長期語音影響。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows a general idea to one example.","zh":"這個短語把一般想法收窄至一個例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"English-speaking countries","meaning":"英語國家","examples":[{"en":"The immigrants included people from other English-speaking countries.","zh":"這些移民包括來自其他英語國家的人。"},{"en":"English-speaking countries are countries where English is widely used as a main or official language.","zh":"英語國家是英語被廣泛作為主要或官方語言使用的國家。"},{"en":"Canada, Australia and New Zealand are often described as English-speaking countries.","zh":"加拿大、澳洲和新西蘭常被描述為英語國家。"},{"en":"If immigrants already speak English, differences in accent rather than language may become important.","zh":"如果移民本來已說英語，重要的可能是口音差異而不是語言差異。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies countries by common language use.","zh":"這個短語以共同語言使用來識別國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"over the course of many years","meaning":"經過多年","examples":[{"en":"Pronunciation patterns may affect the face over the course of many years.","zh":"發音模式可能經過多年影響面部。"},{"en":"Over the course of many years means gradually during a long period of time.","zh":"經過多年，指在漫長時間中逐漸發生。"},{"en":"A student’s handwriting may improve over the course of many years of practice.","zh":"學生的字體可能經過多年練習而改善。"},{"en":"If speech movements are repeated daily for decades, small physical effects may accumulate.","zh":"如果說話動作數十年每天重複，小型身體效果可能累積。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses slow long-term change.","zh":"這個短語強調緩慢的長期變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be of great interest","meaning":"很值得關注","examples":[{"en":"The possible link between pronunciation and appearance is of great interest.","zh":"發音與外貌之間的可能關係很值得關注。"},{"en":"To be of great interest means to be very interesting or important to study.","zh":"很值得關注，指非常有趣或很重要，值得研究。"},{"en":"The way children learn accents is of great interest to language teachers.","zh":"孩子如何學習口音，對語言老師很值得關注。"},{"en":"If a theory could help speech therapy, it is of great interest to researchers.","zh":"如果理論可以幫助言語治療，它就很值得研究者關注。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that a topic deserves attention.","zh":"這個短語表示某題目值得注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"call for further study","meaning":"需要進一步研究","examples":[{"en":"The theory calls for further study into voice production.","zh":"這個理論需要對語音產生作進一步研究。"},{"en":"To call for further study means to need more research before a conclusion can be trusted.","zh":"需要進一步研究，指在結論可信前仍需要更多研究。"},{"en":"A new teaching method may call for further study before schools adopt it widely.","zh":"新教學方法在學校廣泛採用前，可能需要進一步研究。"},{"en":"If evidence is interesting but not complete, researchers should investigate more carefully.","zh":"如果證據有趣但不完整，研究者應更仔細調查。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a question is not yet settled.","zh":"這個短語顯示問題尚未定論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"science of voice production","meaning":"語音產生的科學","examples":[{"en":"The science of voice production may explain how accents affect facial muscles.","zh":"語音產生的科學可能解釋口音如何影響面部肌肉。"},{"en":"The science of voice production studies how the lungs, vocal cords, tongue, lips and mouth create speech sounds.","zh":"語音產生的科學研究肺、聲帶、舌頭、嘴唇和口腔如何創造語音。"},{"en":"Speech therapists use the science of voice production when helping patients speak clearly.","zh":"言語治療師幫助病人清楚說話時，會使用語音產生的科學。"},{"en":"If researchers understand voice production, they can study which muscles different accents use.","zh":"如果研究者理解語音產生，就能研究不同口音使用哪些肌肉。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the physical study of how speech is made.","zh":"這個短語指對說話如何形成的身體研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"benefit those working in","meaning":"令從事……的人受益","examples":[{"en":"Further research could benefit those working in speech-related fields.","zh":"進一步研究可以令從事語言相關範疇的人受益。"},{"en":"To benefit those working in a field means to help people employed or active in that area.","zh":"令從事某領域的人受益，指幫助在該範疇工作或活動的人。"},{"en":"Better classroom research can benefit those working in education.","zh":"更好的課堂研究可以令從事教育的人受益。"},{"en":"If pronunciation research improves training methods, teachers and therapists may gain useful tools.","zh":"如果發音研究改善訓練方法，老師和治療師可能得到有用工具。"},{"en":"The phrase shows who may gain from new knowledge.","zh":"這個短語顯示誰可能從新知識中得益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"speech therapy","meaning":"言語治療","examples":[{"en":"Research into pronunciation may benefit the field of speech therapy.","zh":"對發音的研究可能有利於言語治療領域。"},{"en":"Speech therapy helps people improve communication, pronunciation, voice or swallowing difficulties.","zh":"言語治療幫助人改善溝通、發音、聲線或吞嚥困難。"},{"en":"A child with unclear speech may attend speech therapy every week.","zh":"說話不清楚的孩子可能每週接受言語治療。"},{"en":"If therapists understand mouth muscles better, they can design more useful exercises.","zh":"如果治療師更了解口部肌肉，就能設計更有用練習。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to professional treatment for speech and communication problems.","zh":"這個短語指針對語言和溝通問題的專業治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"elocution","meaning":"演說及發音訓練","examples":[{"en":"Knowledge of voice production is useful in elocution training.","zh":"語音產生知識對演說及發音訓練有用。"},{"en":"Elocution is training in clear, correct or effective speech.","zh":"演說及發音訓練是清晰、正確或有效說話的訓練。"},{"en":"An actor may take elocution lessons to speak clearly on stage.","zh":"演員可能上演說及發音課，以便在舞台上清楚說話。"},{"en":"If someone practises elocution, they may work on rhythm, sound, mouth shape and projection.","zh":"如果某人練習演說發音，可能會訓練節奏、聲音、口形和投射。"},{"en":"The word refers to formal speech training.","zh":"這個詞指正式說話訓練。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pronunciation of foreign languages","meaning":"外語發音","examples":[{"en":"The research may help people teaching the pronunciation of foreign languages.","zh":"這項研究可能幫助教授外語發音的人。"},{"en":"Pronunciation of foreign languages means how learners produce the sounds of languages that are not their first language.","zh":"外語發音指學習者如何發出非母語語言的聲音。"},{"en":"A Japanese learner of English may practise the pronunciation of foreign languages by listening and repeating.","zh":"日本英語學習者可能透過聆聽和重複來練習外語發音。"},{"en":"If teachers know which mouth muscles are needed, they can explain difficult sounds more clearly.","zh":"如果老師知道需要哪些口部肌肉，就能更清楚解釋困難聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on speaking sounds, not grammar or vocabulary.","zh":"這個短語強調說話聲音，而不是文法或詞彙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"physiological point of view","meaning":"從生理角度","examples":[{"en":"The theory may help language students from a physiological point of view.","zh":"從生理角度來看，這個理論可能幫助語言學生。"},{"en":"A physiological point of view looks at the body and how its parts work.","zh":"生理角度是觀察身體及其各部分如何運作。"},{"en":"From a physiological point of view, pronunciation involves muscles, breathing and mouth position.","zh":"從生理角度來看，發音涉及肌肉、呼吸和口腔位置。"},{"en":"If students understand the body movements behind sounds, they may practise more effectively.","zh":"如果學生理解聲音背後的身體動作，就可能更有效練習。"},{"en":"The phrase means examining something through physical function.","zh":"這個短語指透過身體功能檢視某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"psychological factors","meaning":"心理因素","examples":[{"en":"Psychological factors may prevent adult learners from improving their pronunciation.","zh":"心理因素可能阻止成年學習者改善發音。"},{"en":"Psychological factors are mental or emotional influences, such as fear, confidence or motivation.","zh":"心理因素是思想或情緒上的影響，例如恐懼、信心或動機。"},{"en":"A shy student may speak quietly because psychological factors affect their confidence.","zh":"害羞學生可能因心理因素影響信心而說話很小聲。"},{"en":"If learners fear sounding foolish, they may avoid practising unfamiliar sounds.","zh":"如果學習者害怕聽起來愚蠢，可能避免練習陌生聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what happens in the mind, not the mouth alone.","zh":"這個短語指腦海中發生的事情，而不只是口部問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"socio-linguistic factors","meaning":"社會語言學因素","examples":[{"en":"Socio-linguistic factors can also affect the way adults learn accents.","zh":"社會語言學因素也可以影響成年人學習口音的方式。"},{"en":"Socio-linguistic factors are social influences on language, such as identity, class, community and attitudes.","zh":"社會語言學因素是對語言造成影響的社會因素，例如身份、階級、社群和態度。"},{"en":"A student may avoid a new accent because they do not want to sound unlike their friends.","zh":"學生可能避免使用新口音，因為不想聽起來不像朋友。"},{"en":"If pronunciation is tied to identity, social pressure can affect how people speak.","zh":"如果發音與身份相連，社會壓力就能影響人們如何說話。"},{"en":"The phrase connects language learning with society.","zh":"這個短語把語言學習與社會連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"inhibit someone from doing something","meaning":"阻礙某人做某事","examples":[{"en":"Several factors inhibit adult learners from acquiring good pronunciation.","zh":"多種因素阻礙成年學習者掌握良好發音。"},{"en":"To inhibit someone from doing something means to prevent or discourage them from doing it.","zh":"阻礙某人做某事，指阻止或打擊某人做該事。"},{"en":"Fear of mistakes can inhibit students from speaking English in class.","zh":"害怕犯錯可以阻礙學生在課堂上說英語。"},{"en":"If adults feel embarrassed, that feeling may stop them from practising new sounds freely.","zh":"如果成年人感到尷尬，這種感覺可能阻止他們自由練習新聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a barrier that holds someone back.","zh":"這個短語描述阻止某人前進的障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"adult learners","meaning":"成年學習者","examples":[{"en":"Adult learners often find it difficult to acquire a new pronunciation.","zh":"成年學習者常覺得掌握新發音很困難。"},{"en":"Adult learners are people who study a subject or skill after childhood.","zh":"成年學習者是在童年後學習某科目或技能的人。"},{"en":"Adult learners may study English after work because they need it for travel or promotion.","zh":"成年學習者可能下班後學英文，因為旅行或升職需要。"},{"en":"If adult learners already have fixed speech habits, new sounds may feel unnatural at first.","zh":"如果成年學習者已有固定說話習慣，新聲音起初可能感覺不自然。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to grown-up students.","zh":"這個短語指成人學生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"acquire good pronunciation","meaning":"掌握良好發音","examples":[{"en":"Many adult learners struggle to acquire good pronunciation.","zh":"許多成年學習者難以掌握良好發音。"},{"en":"To acquire good pronunciation means to gradually learn to produce sounds clearly and accurately.","zh":"掌握良好發音，指逐漸學會清楚而準確地發出聲音。"},{"en":"A student can acquire good pronunciation by listening carefully, repeating often and receiving feedback.","zh":"學生可以透過仔細聆聽、經常重複和接受回饋來掌握良好發音。"},{"en":"If learners practise the wrong mouth position, improvement may be slow.","zh":"如果學習者練習錯誤口腔位置，進步可能緩慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a gradual learning process, not instant success.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步學習過程，而不是即時成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"constitute a different issue","meaning":"構成另一個問題","examples":[{"en":"Psychological barriers constitute a different issue from facial physiology.","zh":"心理障礙構成與面部生理不同的另一個問題。"},{"en":"To constitute a different issue means to be a separate problem or topic.","zh":"構成另一個問題，指成為一個獨立的問題或題目。"},{"en":"A student’s grammar mistakes constitute a different issue from their lack of confidence.","zh":"學生的文法錯誤與缺乏信心構成不同問題。"},{"en":"If one issue is mental and another is physical, they should not be confused.","zh":"如果一個問題屬心理，另一個屬身體，就不應混淆。"},{"en":"The phrase separates one question from another.","zh":"這個短語把一個問題與另一個分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"no less important","meaning":"同樣重要","examples":[{"en":"These psychological factors are different but no less important.","zh":"這些心理因素不同，但同樣重要。"},{"en":"No less important means equally important, even if the issue is different.","zh":"同樣重要指即使問題不同，也一樣重要。"},{"en":"Pronunciation is important, but confidence is no less important in speaking tests.","zh":"發音很重要，但在口語考試中信心同樣重要。"},{"en":"If psychological barriers stop practice, they matter as much as physical technique.","zh":"如果心理障礙阻止練習，它們就和身體技巧一樣重要。"},{"en":"The phrase prevents readers from treating a different issue as a minor one.","zh":"這個短語避免讀者把不同問題視為次要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"require separate investigation","meaning":"需要另行研究","examples":[{"en":"The psychological barriers require separate investigation.","zh":"這些心理障礙需要另行研究。"},{"en":"To require separate investigation means to need to be studied on its own, apart from other issues.","zh":"需要另行研究，指需要獨立研究，而不是與其他問題混在一起。"},{"en":"A school’s falling results and students’ anxiety may require separate investigations.","zh":"學校成績下降和學生焦慮可能需要分開調查。"},{"en":"If two causes are different, studying them separately can produce clearer answers.","zh":"如果兩個原因不同，分開研究可以得出更清楚答案。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that one topic should not be mixed carelessly with another.","zh":"這個短語暗示不應草率把一個題目與另一個混合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"various forms of English","meaning":"各種英語變體","examples":[{"en":"The various forms of English place the voice differently in the mouth.","zh":"各種英語變體把聲音放在口腔不同位置。"},{"en":"Various forms of English are different accents or varieties of English used in different regions or communities.","zh":"各種英語變體，是不同地區或社群使用的不同英語口音或變體。"},{"en":"British, American, Australian and Singaporean English are various forms of English.","zh":"英式、美式、澳式和新加坡英語都是各種英語變體。"},{"en":"If forms of English use different mouth positions, learners may need different pronunciation habits.","zh":"如果英語變體使用不同口腔位置，學習者可能需要不同發音習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to English variety, not different languages entirely.","zh":"這個短語指英語內部差異，而不是完全不同語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"around the world today","meaning":"在現今世界各地","examples":[{"en":"Different forms of English are spoken around the world today.","zh":"在現今世界各地，人們使用不同形式的英語。"},{"en":"Around the world today means in many countries and regions in the present time.","zh":"在現今世界各地，指在目前許多國家和地區。"},{"en":"Students around the world today use online videos to learn languages.","zh":"在現今世界各地，學生使用網上影片學習語言。"},{"en":"If English is used around the world today, it naturally develops many local accents.","zh":"如果英語在現今世界各地使用，它自然會發展出許多本地口音。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a present-day global setting.","zh":"這個短語給出當代全球背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"place the voice","meaning":"將聲音置於某個位置","examples":[{"en":"Different accents appear to place the voice in different parts of the mouth.","zh":"不同口音似乎把聲音置於口腔不同部位。"},{"en":"To place the voice means to produce sound from a particular position or feeling in the mouth, throat or face.","zh":"將聲音置於某個位置，指從口腔、喉嚨或面部的特定位置或感覺發聲。"},{"en":"A singing teacher may ask students to place the voice forward to make the sound clearer.","zh":"歌唱老師可能要求學生把聲音放前，使聲音更清楚。"},{"en":"If an accent places the voice near the nose or jaw, it may change how the face moves.","zh":"如果口音把聲音放在鼻腔或下顎附近，就可能改變面部如何移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the physical focus of sound production.","zh":"這個短語描述發聲的身體焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"different parts of the mouth","meaning":"口腔的不同部位","examples":[{"en":"Accents use different parts of the mouth to produce sounds.","zh":"口音使用口腔的不同部位來發出聲音。"},{"en":"Different parts of the mouth include the lips, tongue, teeth, jaw, palate and throat area.","zh":"口腔的不同部位包括嘴唇、舌頭、牙齒、下顎、上顎和喉部區域。"},{"en":"A language learner may use a mirror to see which parts of the mouth move for a new sound.","zh":"語言學習者可能用鏡子觀察新音需要口腔哪些部位移動。"},{"en":"If a sound needs the tongue and teeth together, mouth position becomes important.","zh":"如果某個音需要舌頭和牙齒一起使用，口腔位置就很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase explains where pronunciation is physically made.","zh":"這個短語解釋發音在身體上由哪裡產生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"speech organs","meaning":"發音器官","examples":[{"en":"We use our speech organs in particular ways when speaking.","zh":"我們說話時以特定方式使用發音器官。"},{"en":"Speech organs are body parts used for producing speech, such as the tongue, lips, teeth, vocal cords and lungs.","zh":"發音器官是用來產生語音的身體部位，例如舌頭、嘴唇、牙齒、聲帶和肺。"},{"en":"A speech therapist may train a patient to use speech organs more accurately.","zh":"言語治療師可能訓練病人更準確使用發音器官。"},{"en":"If speech organs move differently in another language, pronunciation can feel difficult at first.","zh":"如果另一語言中的發音器官移動方式不同，發音起初可能感覺困難。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the physical tools of speaking.","zh":"這個短語指說話的身體工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in certain ways","meaning":"以某些方式","examples":[{"en":"Each accent uses the speech organs in certain ways.","zh":"每種口音以某些方式使用發音器官。"},{"en":"In certain ways means in particular or specific ways.","zh":"以某些方式，指以特定方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain that good essays organise ideas in certain ways.","zh":"老師可能解釋好文章以某些方式組織想法。"},{"en":"If an accent uses the tongue and jaw in certain ways, learners must practise those patterns.","zh":"如果口音以某些方式使用舌頭和下顎，學習者就必須練習那些模式。"},{"en":"The phrase points to specific methods or patterns, not random behaviour.","zh":"這個短語指特定方法或模式，而不是隨機行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"produce specific sounds","meaning":"發出特定聲音","examples":[{"en":"The mouth muscles work together to produce specific sounds.","zh":"口腔肌肉一起運作，以發出特定聲音。"},{"en":"To produce specific sounds means to create particular speech sounds accurately.","zh":"發出特定聲音，指準確產生特定語音。"},{"en":"Students may practise tongue position to produce specific sounds like “th” or “r”.","zh":"學生可能練習舌頭位置，以發出 “th” 或 “r” 等特定聲音。"},{"en":"If the mouth is in the wrong position, the desired sound may not come out clearly.","zh":"如果口腔位置錯誤，所需聲音可能不能清楚發出。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on making exact sounds, not just speaking generally.","zh":"這個短語強調製造精確聲音，而不是泛泛說話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"practise to learn","meaning":"需要練習才能學會","examples":[{"en":"The relevant muscles have to practise to learn new phonemes.","zh":"相關肌肉需要練習才能學會新音位。"},{"en":"To practise to learn something means to repeat an action until skill develops.","zh":"需要練習才能學會某事，指反覆做某動作直到技能形成。"},{"en":"A student practises to learn handwriting by writing letters again and again.","zh":"學生透過反覆書寫字母練習，才能學會書寫。"},{"en":"If mouth muscles are not trained, unfamiliar sounds may remain difficult.","zh":"如果口腔肌肉沒有被訓練，陌生聲音可能仍然困難。"},{"en":"The phrase connects repetition with improvement.","zh":"這個短語把重複與進步連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"new phonemes","meaning":"新音位","examples":[{"en":"Learning an accent requires the speaker to produce new phonemes.","zh":"學習口音需要說話者發出新音位。"},{"en":"New phonemes are unfamiliar speech sounds that help distinguish words in a language or accent.","zh":"新音位是陌生語音單位，能幫助區分語言或口音中的詞語。"},{"en":"English learners may find new phonemes difficult if those sounds do not exist in their first language.","zh":"如果英語學習者的母語沒有某些聲音，他們可能覺得新音位困難。"},{"en":"If a learner cannot hear a new phoneme clearly, producing it accurately becomes harder.","zh":"如果學習者不能清楚聽出新音位，就更難準確發出它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to new sound units, not new vocabulary.","zh":"這個短語指新的聲音單位，而不是新詞彙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"look in the mirror","meaning":"照鏡子","examples":[{"en":"Learners can look in the mirror while practising an accent.","zh":"學習者可以在練習口音時照鏡子。"},{"en":"To look in the mirror means to watch one’s own face or body in a mirror.","zh":"照鏡子指在鏡中觀看自己的臉或身體。"},{"en":"A student may look in the mirror to check whether their mouth shape matches the teacher’s example.","zh":"學生可能照鏡子檢查自己的口形是否符合老師示範。"},{"en":"If learners see their jaw and lips move, they can adjust pronunciation more consciously.","zh":"如果學習者看到下顎和嘴唇移動，就能更有意識地調整發音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a simple self-checking method.","zh":"這個短語描述一種簡單自我檢查方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"while repeating","meaning":"在重複……時","examples":[{"en":"Non-Americans can observe their jaws while repeating a sentence.","zh":"非美國人在重複一句話時，可以觀察自己的下顎。"},{"en":"While repeating means during the action of saying the same words again.","zh":"在重複時，指在再次說出相同詞語的動作期間。"},{"en":"A child may notice their mistakes while repeating a poem after the teacher.","zh":"孩子跟老師重複詩句時，可能注意到自己的錯誤。"},{"en":"If learners watch their mouth while repeating a sound, they may see which muscles move.","zh":"如果學習者在重複聲音時觀察口部，可能看見哪些肌肉移動。"},{"en":"The phrase shows two actions happening at the same time.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個動作同時發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"with full use of","meaning":"充分運用","examples":[{"en":"The sentence should be spoken with full use of the American /r/ sound.","zh":"這句話應充分運用美式 /r/ 音來說。"},{"en":"With full use of something means using it completely or strongly, not lightly or partially.","zh":"充分運用某物，指完整或強烈使用它，而不是輕微或部分使用。"},{"en":"A singer performs better with full use of breath support.","zh":"歌手充分運用呼吸支撐時，表演會更好。"},{"en":"If learners use the American /r/ fully, their tongue and jaw movements may become more noticeable.","zh":"如果學習者充分使用美式 /r/，其舌頭和下顎動作可能更明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses complete use of a feature or technique.","zh":"這個短語強調完整使用某特徵或技巧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"retroflex /r/ phoneme","meaning":"捲舌 /r/ 音位","examples":[{"en":"The retroflex /r/ phoneme is a noticeable feature of American English.","zh":"捲舌 /r/ 音位是美式英語一個明顯特徵。"},{"en":"The retroflex /r/ phoneme is an /r/ sound made with the tongue curled or pulled back.","zh":"捲舌 /r/ 音位是舌頭捲起或向後收所發出的 /r/ 音。"},{"en":"English learners may practise the retroflex /r/ by watching the tongue position carefully.","zh":"英語學習者可能透過仔細觀察舌位來練習捲舌 /r/。"},{"en":"If the tongue is not placed correctly, the American /r/ may sound weak or unclear.","zh":"如果舌頭位置不正確，美式 /r/ 可能聽起來微弱或不清晰。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific sound feature in pronunciation.","zh":"這個短語指出發音中的特定聲音特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"note what happens to","meaning":"留意……發生甚麼變化","examples":[{"en":"Learners should note what happens to their jawbones.","zh":"學習者應留意自己的下顎骨發生甚麼變化。"},{"en":"To note what happens to something means to observe and remember the change carefully.","zh":"留意某物發生甚麼變化，指仔細觀察並記住變化。"},{"en":"A science student may note what happens to water when it is heated.","zh":"科學學生可能留意水加熱後發生甚麼變化。"},{"en":"If learners note jaw movement during pronunciation, they can understand the physical effort involved.","zh":"如果學習者留意發音時的下顎動作，就能理解當中的身體用力。"},{"en":"The phrase encourages careful observation.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵仔細觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"after several repetitions","meaning":"重複數次後","examples":[{"en":"The jaw may move noticeably after several repetitions.","zh":"重複數次後，下顎可能明顯移動。"},{"en":"After several repetitions means after saying or doing the same thing a few times.","zh":"重複數次後，指說或做同一件事幾次之後。"},{"en":"A student may remember a new word better after several repetitions.","zh":"學生重複數次後，可能更好記住新詞。"},{"en":"If a sound is repeated several times, the learner may notice which muscles become tired.","zh":"如果某聲音被重複數次，學習者可能注意到哪些肌肉變累。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a short period of repeated practice.","zh":"這個短語給出一段短時間的重複練習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"imagine the effect of","meaning":"想像……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Imagine the effect of these movements after twenty years.","zh":"想像這些動作二十年後的影響。"},{"en":"To imagine the effect of something means to think about what result it might produce.","zh":"想像某事的影響，指思考它可能產生甚麼結果。"},{"en":"Imagine the effect of poor posture after ten years of sitting badly at a desk.","zh":"想像長期坐姿不良十年後的影響。"},{"en":"If small movements are repeated for decades, their possible effect becomes worth considering.","zh":"如果小動作被重複數十年，其可能影響就值得考慮。"},{"en":"The phrase asks readers to think about long-term consequences.","zh":"這個短語要求讀者思考長期後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"jaw muscles","meaning":"下顎肌肉","examples":[{"en":"Repeated pronunciation patterns may affect the jaw muscles.","zh":"重複的發音模式可能影響下顎肌肉。"},{"en":"Jaw muscles are the muscles that move the lower jaw when speaking, chewing or opening the mouth.","zh":"下顎肌肉是說話、咀嚼或張口時移動下顎的肌肉。"},{"en":"A dentist may ask whether a patient’s jaw muscles feel tight after grinding their teeth.","zh":"牙醫可能問病人磨牙後下顎肌肉是否繃緊。"},{"en":"If pronunciation repeatedly uses these muscles, they may become more active or tense.","zh":"如果發音反覆使用這些肌肉，它們可能變得更活躍或繃緊。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the muscles involved in lower-face movement.","zh":"這個短語指涉及下半臉動作的肌肉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"one of the most noticeable features","meaning":"最明顯特徵之一","examples":[{"en":"The American /r/ is one of the most noticeable features of US English.","zh":"美式 /r/ 是美式英語最明顯特徵之一。"},{"en":"One of the most noticeable features means one of the easiest characteristics to observe or hear.","zh":"最明顯特徵之一，指最容易觀察或聽到的特點之一。"},{"en":"A school’s bright red uniform may be one of its most noticeable features.","zh":"學校鮮紅色校服可能是其最明顯特徵之一。"},{"en":"If a sound stands out strongly, people may copy it first when mimicking an accent.","zh":"如果某聲音非常突出，人們模仿口音時可能最先模仿它。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a feature that attracts attention quickly.","zh":"這個短語指出很快吸引注意的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"US English","meaning":"美式英語","examples":[{"en":"The retroflex /r/ is strongly associated with US English.","zh":"捲舌 /r/ 與美式英語密切相關。"},{"en":"US English is the form of English commonly used in the United States.","zh":"美式英語是在美國常用的英語形式。"},{"en":"A learner may study US English if they plan to work with American clients.","zh":"如果學習者計劃與美國客戶工作，可能學習美式英語。"},{"en":"If a speaker uses strong /r/ sounds, listeners may associate the accent with US English.","zh":"如果說話者使用強烈 /r/ 音，聽者可能把該口音與美式英語連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to American English as a language variety.","zh":"這個短語指美國英語這一語言變體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"exaggerate when mimicking","meaning":"模仿時誇大","examples":[{"en":"Non-Americans often exaggerate the /r/ sound when mimicking the accent.","zh":"非美國人在模仿該口音時常誇大 /r/ 音。"},{"en":"To exaggerate when mimicking means to copy something in an overdone or too obvious way.","zh":"模仿時誇大，指以過度或太明顯的方式模仿某事。"},{"en":"A student may exaggerate a teacher’s slow speech when joking with friends.","zh":"學生與朋友開玩笑時，可能誇大老師慢慢說話的方式。"},{"en":"If people imitate an accent too strongly, the result may sound comic or inaccurate.","zh":"如果人們過度模仿口音，結果可能聽起來滑稽或不準確。"},{"en":"The phrase describes over-emphasised imitation.","zh":"這個短語描述過分強調的模仿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"mimic an accent","meaning":"模仿口音","examples":[{"en":"People often exaggerate distinctive sounds when they mimic an accent.","zh":"人們模仿口音時，常誇大獨特聲音。"},{"en":"To mimic an accent means to copy the way people from a region or group speak.","zh":"模仿口音指模仿某地區或群體的人說話方式。"},{"en":"An actor may mimic an accent after listening carefully to native speakers.","zh":"演員可能仔細聽母語者說話後模仿口音。"},{"en":"If someone mimics an accent carelessly, it may become a stereotype rather than accurate speech.","zh":"如果某人草率模仿口音，它可能變成刻板印象，而不是準確說話。"},{"en":"The phrase describes imitation of pronunciation and rhythm.","zh":"這個短語描述對發音和節奏的模仿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"likewise","meaning":"同樣地","examples":[{"en":"Likewise, standard British pronunciation is often exaggerated for comic effect.","zh":"同樣地，標準英式發音常被誇大以製造喜劇效果。"},{"en":"Likewise means in the same way or similarly.","zh":"“Likewise” 指以相同方式或類似地。"},{"en":"A teacher may praise one student’s clear examples; likewise, another student’s structure may deserve praise.","zh":"老師可能稱讚一名學生例子清楚；同樣地，另一名學生的結構也值得讚賞。"},{"en":"If American /r/ is exaggerated, British RP can also be exaggerated in parody.","zh":"如果美式 /r/ 被誇大，英式 RP 也可以在模仿中被誇大。"},{"en":"The word introduces a similar point.","zh":"這個詞引出相似觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"standard British RP","meaning":"標準英式公認發音","examples":[{"en":"Standard British RP is often parodied by speakers.","zh":"標準英式公認發音常被說話者滑稽模仿。"},{"en":"Standard British RP refers to Received Pronunciation, a traditionally prestigious British accent.","zh":"標準英式 RP 指 Received Pronunciation，是傳統上具聲望的英國口音。"},{"en":"Actors may learn standard British RP when playing upper-class characters.","zh":"演員飾演上流社會角色時，可能學習標準英式 RP。"},{"en":"If RP is associated with social status, people may mock it as sounding superior.","zh":"如果 RP 與社會地位相關，人們可能嘲笑它聽起來有優越感。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific British accent, not all British English.","zh":"這個短語指出一種特定英國口音，而不是所有英式英語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be parodied","meaning":"被滑稽模仿","examples":[{"en":"Standard British RP is often parodied and mocked.","zh":"標準英式 RP 常被滑稽模仿和嘲弄。"},{"en":"To be parodied means to be imitated in an exaggerated way for humour or criticism.","zh":"被滑稽模仿，指被以誇張方式模仿，用於幽默或批評。"},{"en":"A famous politician’s speaking style may be parodied on a comedy show.","zh":"著名政治人物的說話風格可能在喜劇節目中被滑稽模仿。"},{"en":"If an accent is parodied, its most noticeable sounds may be exaggerated.","zh":"如果口音被滑稽模仿，其最明顯聲音可能被誇大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes humorous or critical imitation.","zh":"這個短語描述幽默或批判性的模仿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"whine of superiority","meaning":"帶優越感的尖聲語調","examples":[{"en":"Critics sometimes mock what they hear as a whine of superiority.","zh":"批評者有時嘲笑他們聽成帶優越感的尖聲語調。"},{"en":"A whine of superiority is a complaining or nasal tone that seems to express arrogance.","zh":"帶優越感的尖聲語調，是聽起來像抱怨或帶鼻音，並似乎表達傲慢的聲音。"},{"en":"A speaker may sound like they have a whine of superiority if they talk down to others.","zh":"如果說話者用高高在上的方式說話，可能聽起來像有優越感的尖聲語調。"},{"en":"If an accent is associated with class privilege, listeners may unfairly hear it as superior.","zh":"如果某口音與階級特權相關，聽者可能不公平地把它聽成優越。"},{"en":"The phrase is critical and describes how a voice is perceived.","zh":"這個短語帶批評意味，描述聲音如何被感知。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be mocked to the point of","meaning":"被嘲弄到……的地步","examples":[{"en":"The accent is mocked to the point of changing the speaker’s facial expression.","zh":"這種口音被嘲弄到改變說話者面部表情的地步。"},{"en":"To be mocked to the point of something means to be imitated or ridiculed so much that a particular result happens.","zh":"被嘲弄到某地步，指被模仿或取笑得太多，以致產生某種結果。"},{"en":"A cartoon villain’s laugh may be mocked to the point of becoming a school joke.","zh":"卡通反派的笑聲可能被嘲弄到成為學校笑話的地步。"},{"en":"If an accent is mocked with exaggerated face movements, voice and appearance become connected.","zh":"如果口音被配合誇張面部動作來嘲弄，聲音和外貌就被連接起來。"},{"en":"The phrase shows an extreme level of mockery.","zh":"這個短語顯示極端程度的嘲弄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"turn one’s nose up","meaning":"仰起鼻子；擺出高傲姿態","examples":[{"en":"A person parodying RP may turn their nose up dramatically.","zh":"模仿 RP 的人可能戲劇化地仰起鼻子。"},{"en":"To turn one’s nose up means to raise the nose in a way that suggests arrogance or disdain.","zh":"仰起鼻子，指把鼻子抬高，姿態暗示傲慢或輕蔑。"},{"en":"A child may turn their nose up at vegetables if they think the food is boring.","zh":"如果孩子覺得蔬菜沉悶，可能對蔬菜嗤之以鼻。"},{"en":"If someone turns their nose up while imitating an accent, the gesture suggests social superiority.","zh":"如果某人模仿口音時仰起鼻子，這個動作暗示社會優越感。"},{"en":"The phrase can be physical, but it often means rejecting something proudly.","zh":"這個短語可以是身體動作，但常指高傲地拒絕某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as much as possible","meaning":"盡可能地","examples":[{"en":"The speaker may turn the end of their nose up as much as possible.","zh":"說話者可能盡可能地把鼻尖向上翹。"},{"en":"As much as possible means to the greatest degree that can reasonably be done.","zh":"盡可能地，指在合理可行範圍內達到最大程度。"},{"en":"A student should practise speaking as much as possible before an oral exam.","zh":"學生應在口試前盡可能多練習說話。"},{"en":"If a parody exaggerates facial movement as much as possible, it becomes comic.","zh":"如果滑稽模仿盡可能誇大面部動作，它就會變得搞笑。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses maximum effort or extent.","zh":"這個短語強調最大努力或程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not only…, but also…","meaning":"不但……，而且……","examples":[{"en":"The facial movement not only enhances the performance but also raises a question.","zh":"這個面部動作不但加強表演效果，而且提出一個問題。"},{"en":"Not only A, but also B means both A and B are true, with B often adding emphasis.","zh":"“Not only A, but also B” 指 A 和 B 都成立，而 B 常帶有強調作用。"},{"en":"Reading aloud not only improves pronunciation but also builds confidence.","zh":"朗讀不但改善發音，而且建立信心。"},{"en":"If a gesture improves the parody and suggests a deeper issue, it has two effects.","zh":"如果一個動作改善模仿效果並暗示更深問題，它就有兩個作用。"},{"en":"The structure is used to add a second important point.","zh":"這個結構用來加入第二個重要觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"enhance the performance","meaning":"加強表演效果","examples":[{"en":"Exaggerated facial movements can enhance the performance.","zh":"誇張面部動作可以加強表演效果。"},{"en":"To enhance the performance means to make the acting, speech or presentation stronger and more effective.","zh":"加強表演效果，指令演出、演說或展示更有力、更有效。"},{"en":"A student can enhance a speech performance by using clear gestures and eye contact.","zh":"學生可以透過清楚手勢和眼神接觸來加強演講表現。"},{"en":"If facial movement makes an accent parody funnier, it enhances the performance.","zh":"如果面部動作令口音模仿更有趣，它就加強表演效果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improving how something is delivered.","zh":"這個短語描述改善某事的呈現方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"beg the question of whether","meaning":"引起……是否成立的問題","examples":[{"en":"The parody begs the question of whether appearance influenced the expression.","zh":"這種滑稽模仿引起外貌是否影響該表達方式的問題。"},{"en":"To beg the question of whether means to raise or make people ask a particular question.","zh":"“Beg the question of whether” 指引起或令人提出某個問題。"},{"en":"A sudden rise in exam failure begs the question of whether teaching methods have changed.","zh":"考試不合格率突然上升，引起教學方法是否改變的問題。"},{"en":"If a facial movement appears in accent parody, it raises the question of whether speech and appearance are linked.","zh":"如果面部動作出現在口音模仿中，就引起語音與外貌是否相關的問題。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a question naturally caused by evidence or observation.","zh":"這個短語引出由證據或觀察自然產生的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the origin of the expression","meaning":"該用語的起源","examples":[{"en":"The writer wonders about the origin of the expression “stuck up”.","zh":"作者思考 “stuck up” 這個用語的起源。"},{"en":"The origin of the expression means where a phrase first came from or how it began.","zh":"該用語的起源，指某短語最初來自哪裡或如何開始。"},{"en":"Students may ask about the origin of an idiom when its meaning seems strange.","zh":"當成語意思看似奇怪時，學生可能詢問其起源。"},{"en":"If a gesture resembles an idiom, people may wonder whether one influenced the other.","zh":"如果一個動作類似某個成語，人們可能想知道兩者是否互相影響。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the historical beginning of a saying.","zh":"這個短語強調說法的歷史開端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stuck up","meaning":"自命不凡的；高傲的","examples":[{"en":"The expression “stuck up” describes someone who appears arrogant.","zh":"“Stuck up” 這個表達形容看起來傲慢的人。"},{"en":"Stuck up means believing or acting as if one is better than other people.","zh":"自命不凡或高傲，指相信或表現得像自己比其他人優越。"},{"en":"A student may seem stuck up if they refuse to work with classmates they think are weaker.","zh":"如果學生拒絕與他認為較弱的同學合作，可能顯得自命不凡。"},{"en":"If someone speaks down to others, people may judge them as stuck up.","zh":"如果某人居高臨下地說話，人們可能判斷他高傲。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and critical.","zh":"這個短語較口語，並帶批評意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"point to","meaning":"指向","examples":[{"en":"A friend pointed to a fellow passenger on a Birmingham bus.","zh":"一位朋友指向伯明翰巴士上的一名同車乘客。"},{"en":"To point to someone or something means to direct attention toward them, often with a finger or gesture.","zh":"指向某人或某物，指通常用手指或動作把注意力引向他們。"},{"en":"A teacher may point to a word on the board while explaining pronunciation.","zh":"老師解釋發音時，可能指向黑板上的一個詞。"},{"en":"If someone points to a passenger, they are drawing another person’s attention to that passenger.","zh":"如果某人指向一名乘客，他就是把另一人的注意力引到該乘客身上。"},{"en":"The phrase can mean physically indicating something or using it as evidence.","zh":"這個短語可以指身體上指出某物，也可以指把某物用作證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fellow passenger","meaning":"同車乘客","examples":[{"en":"The friend commented on the accent of a fellow passenger.","zh":"這位朋友評論一名同車乘客的口音。"},{"en":"A fellow passenger is another person travelling in the same vehicle.","zh":"同車乘客是乘坐同一交通工具的另一個人。"},{"en":"On a long train journey, a fellow passenger may start a conversation about the weather.","zh":"在長途火車旅程中，同車乘客可能開始談論天氣。"},{"en":"If a fellow passenger speaks loudly, others may notice their accent.","zh":"如果同車乘客大聲說話，其他人可能注意到他的口音。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to someone sharing the same trip or vehicle.","zh":"這個短語指共享同一旅程或交通工具的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Brummie accent","meaning":"伯明翰口音","examples":[{"en":"A Brummie accent is associated with Birmingham.","zh":"伯明翰口音與伯明翰有關。"},{"en":"A Brummie accent is the regional accent of Birmingham in England.","zh":"伯明翰口音是英格蘭伯明翰地區的地方口音。"},{"en":"An actor playing a character from Birmingham may learn a Brummie accent.","zh":"飾演來自伯明翰角色的演員可能學習伯明翰口音。"},{"en":"If listeners recognise certain vowels or tones, they may identify the speaker as Brummie.","zh":"如果聽者認出某些元音或語調，可能把說話者識別為伯明翰人。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific local English accent.","zh":"這個短語指出一種特定本地英語口音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be written all over someone’s face","meaning":"清楚顯現在某人臉上","examples":[{"en":"The friend claimed that the man’s accent was written all over his face.","zh":"這位朋友聲稱那名男子的口音清楚寫在他臉上。"},{"en":"If something is written all over someone’s face, it is very obvious from their expression or appearance.","zh":"如果某事清楚顯現在某人臉上，就是從其表情或外貌非常明顯。"},{"en":"A student’s disappointment may be written all over their face after a difficult exam.","zh":"困難考試後，學生的失望可能清楚顯現在臉上。"},{"en":"If an accent seems visible in someone’s face, the speaker believes appearance reveals speech background.","zh":"如果口音似乎在某人臉上可見，說話者就是相信外貌透露語音背景。"},{"en":"The phrase means a feeling or clue is clearly shown, not literally written.","zh":"這個短語指感受或線索清楚呈現，而不是字面寫上去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"normally make","meaning":"通常會作出","examples":[{"en":"The friend would not normally make careless generalisations.","zh":"這位朋友通常不會作出草率概括。"},{"en":"Normally make means usually say, do or produce something in ordinary circumstances.","zh":"“Normally make” 指在普通情況下通常說、做或產生某事。"},{"en":"A careful teacher does not normally make unfair comments about students.","zh":"謹慎老師通常不會對學生作出不公平評論。"},{"en":"If someone does not normally make generalisations, their unusual comment may seem worth examining.","zh":"如果某人通常不作概括，他不尋常的評論可能值得檢視。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to usual behaviour.","zh":"這個短語指通常行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"crass generalisations","meaning":"粗疏武斷的概括","examples":[{"en":"The speaker was not normally known for making crass generalisations.","zh":"說話者通常並不以作出粗疏武斷概括聞名。"},{"en":"Crass generalisations are crude, careless and oversimplified statements about a group.","zh":"粗疏武斷的概括，是對某群體作出粗糙、草率和過分簡化的說法。"},{"en":"Saying all teenagers are lazy is a crass generalisation.","zh":"說所有青少年都懶惰，就是粗疏武斷的概括。"},{"en":"If people make crass generalisations from one accent or face, their judgement may be unfair.","zh":"如果人們從一種口音或一張臉作出粗疏概括，其判斷可能不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly criticises careless stereotyping.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評草率刻板化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"establish whether","meaning":"確定是否","examples":[{"en":"The writer wants to establish whether accent causes certain facial features.","zh":"作者想確定口音是否造成某些面部特徵。"},{"en":"To establish whether something is true means to find out or prove it through evidence.","zh":"確定某事是否為真，指透過證據查明或證明它。"},{"en":"A doctor may run tests to establish whether a patient has an infection.","zh":"醫生可能進行測試，以確定病人是否感染。"},{"en":"If researchers want to know whether accent affects appearance, they need data rather than guesses.","zh":"如果研究者想知道口音是否影響外貌，就需要數據而不是猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase describes confirming a possibility.","zh":"這個短語描述確認某種可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"thin lips","meaning":"薄嘴唇","examples":[{"en":"Thin lips are mentioned as a possible feature linked to Midlands English.","zh":"薄嘴唇被提及為可能與英格蘭中部英語相關的特徵。"},{"en":"Thin lips are lips that appear narrow or not very full.","zh":"薄嘴唇是看起來較窄或不豐滿的嘴唇。"},{"en":"A portrait artist may notice thin lips when drawing a person’s face.","zh":"肖像畫家畫人臉時，可能注意到薄嘴唇。"},{"en":"If a speech habit keeps the lips tight, some people may wonder whether it affects lip appearance.","zh":"如果說話習慣令嘴唇保持緊繃，有些人可能思考它是否影響嘴唇外觀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a visible facial feature.","zh":"這個短語描述可見面部特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tense, prominent chin","meaning":"繃緊而突出的下巴","examples":[{"en":"A tense, prominent chin may be associated with the local accent.","zh":"繃緊而突出的下巴可能與本地口音有關。"},{"en":"A tense, prominent chin is a tight-looking chin that sticks out noticeably.","zh":"繃緊而突出的下巴，是看起來很緊並明顯向外突出的下巴。"},{"en":"A photographer may notice a tense, prominent chin when a person is concentrating hard.","zh":"當某人高度集中時，攝影師可能注意到繃緊而突出的下巴。"},{"en":"If an accent requires tight jaw movement, the chin may appear more tense during speech.","zh":"如果某口音需要緊繃下顎動作，說話時下巴可能顯得更緊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both muscle tension and facial shape.","zh":"這個短語同時描述肌肉張力和面部形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be a result of","meaning":"是……的結果","examples":[{"en":"The facial features may be a result of the way Midlands English is spoken.","zh":"這些面部特徵可能是英格蘭中部英語說話方式的結果。"},{"en":"To be a result of something means to happen because of it.","zh":"是某事的結果，指因它而發生。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be a result of sleeping only four hours.","zh":"學生疲倦可能是只睡四小時的結果。"},{"en":"If facial shape is a result of pronunciation, speech habits are treated as the cause.","zh":"如果面部形狀是發音的結果，說話習慣就被視為原因。"},{"en":"The phrase explains an effect by pointing to its cause.","zh":"這個短語透過指出原因來解釋結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be the cause of","meaning":"是……的原因","examples":[{"en":"The facial shape might be the cause of the pronunciation rather than its result.","zh":"面部形狀可能是該發音的原因，而不是其結果。"},{"en":"To be the cause of something means to be the reason it happens.","zh":"是某事的原因，指是它發生的理由。"},{"en":"Poor lighting may be the cause of students’ headaches in a classroom.","zh":"課室燈光不足可能是學生頭痛的原因。"},{"en":"If facial shape causes pronunciation, the body influences speech rather than speech influencing the body.","zh":"如果面部形狀造成發音，就是身體影響語音，而不是語音影響身體。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of an effect.","zh":"這個短語指出結果的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a mixture of both","meaning":"兩者兼有","examples":[{"en":"The relationship may be a mixture of both cause and effect.","zh":"這種關係可能是原因和結果兩者兼有。"},{"en":"A mixture of both means two factors are both involved, not just one.","zh":"兩者兼有，指兩個因素都涉及其中，而不只是其中一個。"},{"en":"A student’s weak speaking may be a mixture of both poor practice and low confidence.","zh":"學生口語弱可能是練習不足和信心低兩者兼有。"},{"en":"If pronunciation affects appearance and appearance affects pronunciation, the relationship is circular.","zh":"如果發音影響外貌，而外貌也影響發音，這種關係就是循環的。"},{"en":"The phrase avoids choosing only one explanation.","zh":"這個短語避免只選一種解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"similarly","meaning":"同樣地","examples":[{"en":"Similarly, questions can be asked about the Liverpool accent.","zh":"同樣地，也可以對利物浦口音提出問題。"},{"en":"Similarly means in a similar way or for a similar reason.","zh":"“Similarly” 指以相似方式或基於相似原因。"},{"en":"Teachers worry about homework pressure; similarly, parents worry about children’s sleep.","zh":"老師擔心功課壓力；同樣地，家長擔心孩子睡眠。"},{"en":"If one accent may relate to appearance, another accent can be examined in the same way.","zh":"如果一種口音可能與外貌相關，另一種口音也可以用同樣方式研究。"},{"en":"The word introduces a comparable point.","zh":"這個詞引出可比較的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in the case of Liverpool","meaning":"就利物浦而言","examples":[{"en":"In the case of Liverpool, the writer discusses the Scouse accent.","zh":"就利物浦而言，作者討論利物浦口音。"},{"en":"In the case of Liverpool means when considering Liverpool as the example.","zh":"就利物浦而言，指以利物浦作為例子來考慮。"},{"en":"In the case of Hong Kong, language use is shaped by Cantonese, English and Putonghua.","zh":"就香港而言，語言使用受廣東話、英語和普通話塑造。"},{"en":"If a writer shifts from Birmingham to Liverpool, the new city becomes the next case study.","zh":"如果作者從伯明翰轉到利物浦，新城市就成為下一個個案。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows a general discussion to one place.","zh":"這個短語把一般討論收窄至一個地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"distinctive Scouse accent","meaning":"獨特的利物浦口音","examples":[{"en":"The distinctive Scouse accent may be linked to local facial features.","zh":"獨特的利物浦口音可能與本地面部特徵有關。"},{"en":"The distinctive Scouse accent is the recognisable accent associated with Liverpool.","zh":"獨特的利物浦口音，是與利物浦相關、可辨認的口音。"},{"en":"An actor may need voice coaching to produce a distinctive Scouse accent convincingly.","zh":"演員可能需要聲線訓練，才能可信地發出獨特利物浦口音。"},{"en":"If an accent is distinctive, listeners can often identify it after only a few words.","zh":"如果口音獨特，聽者通常只聽幾個詞就能識別。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a clearly recognisable Liverpool way of speaking.","zh":"這個短語指清楚可辨認的利物浦說話方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the reason for","meaning":"……的原因","examples":[{"en":"The accent may be the reason for certain facial characteristics.","zh":"口音可能是某些面部特徵的原因。"},{"en":"The reason for something is the cause or explanation behind it.","zh":"某事的原因，是其背後的成因或解釋。"},{"en":"The reason for a student’s silence may be shyness, not lack of knowledge.","zh":"學生沉默的原因可能是害羞，而不是缺乏知識。"},{"en":"If accent is the reason for facial features, repeated pronunciation is being treated as the cause.","zh":"如果口音是面部特徵的原因，重複發音就被視為成因。"},{"en":"The phrase asks why something happens or exists.","zh":"這個短語詢問某事為何發生或存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the result of","meaning":"……的結果","examples":[{"en":"The accent may instead be the result of those facial characteristics.","zh":"口音反而可能是那些面部特徵的結果。"},{"en":"The result of something is what happens because of it.","zh":"某事的結果，是因它而發生的事情。"},{"en":"A high test score may be the result of steady practice over several months.","zh":"高分可能是數月穩定練習的結果。"},{"en":"If accent is the result of facial shape, body structure may influence pronunciation.","zh":"如果口音是面部形狀的結果，身體結構可能影響發音。"},{"en":"The phrase points to an effect produced by a cause.","zh":"這個短語指出由原因產生的效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"frequency of high cheekbones","meaning":"高顴骨常見的情況","examples":[{"en":"The writer notes the frequency of high cheekbones in Liverpool.","zh":"作者注意到利物浦高顴骨常見的情況。"},{"en":"Frequency of high cheekbones means how often high cheekbones appear in a group or place.","zh":"高顴骨常見的情況，指高顴骨在某群體或地方出現得有多頻繁。"},{"en":"A researcher may study the frequency of a health condition in different neighbourhoods.","zh":"研究者可能研究某健康狀況在不同社區中的常見程度。"},{"en":"If high cheekbones are common in a local population, people may wonder about ancestry or environment.","zh":"如果高顴骨在本地人口中常見，人們可能思考血統或環境因素。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how common a visible feature is.","zh":"這個短語描述某可見特徵有多常見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"local population","meaning":"本地人口","examples":[{"en":"High cheekbones may be relatively common in the local population.","zh":"高顴骨在本地人口中可能相對常見。"},{"en":"The local population is the group of people who live in a particular area.","zh":"本地人口是住在某特定地區的一群人。"},{"en":"A hospital plans services by studying the needs of the local population.","zh":"醫院透過研究本地人口需要來規劃服務。"},{"en":"If a feature appears often in the local population, it may become associated with that place.","zh":"如果某特徵常在本地人口中出現，它可能與該地方產生關聯。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people living in a specific community or region.","zh":"這個短語指居住在特定社區或地區的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"learn another accent","meaning":"學習另一種口音","examples":[{"en":"Actors often have to learn another accent for a performance.","zh":"演員常需要為表演學習另一種口音。"},{"en":"To learn another accent means to practise speaking in a different regional or social pronunciation style.","zh":"學習另一種口音，指練習用不同地區或社會發音風格說話。"},{"en":"A drama student may learn another accent to play a character from another city.","zh":"戲劇學生可能學習另一種口音，以飾演來自另一城市的角色。"},{"en":"If an actor cannot master the accent, the role may sound unconvincing.","zh":"如果演員無法掌握口音，角色可能聽起來不可信。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deliberate accent training.","zh":"這個短語描述有意識的口音訓練。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as in the theatre","meaning":"例如在劇院表演中","examples":[{"en":"People may learn accents professionally, as in the theatre.","zh":"人們可能專業地學習口音，例如在劇院表演中。"},{"en":"As in the theatre means as happens in theatre or stage performance.","zh":"“As in the theatre” 指如劇場或舞台表演中發生的那樣。"},{"en":"Voice projection matters in public speaking, as in the theatre.","zh":"聲音投射在公開演說中很重要，如劇院表演中一樣。"},{"en":"If actors learn accents for stage roles, pronunciation becomes part of professional performance.","zh":"如果演員為舞台角色學習口音，發音就成為專業表演的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives theatre as an example of the point.","zh":"這個短語把劇場作為例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"voice coaches","meaning":"聲線教練；發音教練","examples":[{"en":"Voice coaches help actors acquire particular accents.","zh":"聲線教練幫助演員掌握特定口音。"},{"en":"Voice coaches are specialists who train people to use their voice, pronunciation and accent effectively.","zh":"聲線教練是訓練人有效使用聲音、發音和口音的專家。"},{"en":"A public speaker may work with a voice coach to sound clearer and more confident.","zh":"公開演說者可能與聲線教練合作，使自己聽起來更清楚和自信。"},{"en":"If an actor needs a regional accent, a voice coach may teach mouth position and rhythm.","zh":"如果演員需要地區口音，發音教練可能教授口形和節奏。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to professional trainers of speech and voice.","zh":"這個短語指語音和聲線的專業訓練者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"resort to images","meaning":"借助意象","examples":[{"en":"Voice coaches often resort to images when explaining an accent.","zh":"發音教練解釋口音時，常借助意象。"},{"en":"To resort to images means to use mental pictures when ordinary explanation is not enough.","zh":"借助意象，指在普通解釋不足時使用心像。"},{"en":"A teacher may resort to images by telling students to imagine their voice as a bouncing ball.","zh":"老師可能借助意象，叫學生想像自己的聲音像彈跳球。"},{"en":"If a sound is hard to explain technically, an image can make the mouth movement easier to feel.","zh":"如果聲音難以用技術方式解釋，意象可以令人更容易感受口部動作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using imaginative aids to solve a teaching problem.","zh":"這個短語描述使用想像輔助來解決教學問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"help someone acquire","meaning":"幫助某人掌握","examples":[{"en":"Mental images can help students acquire a distinctive sound.","zh":"心像可以幫助學生掌握獨特聲音。"},{"en":"To help someone acquire something means to assist them in gradually gaining a skill, habit or ability.","zh":"幫助某人掌握某事，指協助他逐漸獲得技能、習慣或能力。"},{"en":"Regular reading can help students acquire natural sentence patterns.","zh":"定期閱讀可以幫助學生掌握自然句式。"},{"en":"If images make pronunciation easier to feel, they can help learners acquire an accent.","zh":"如果意象令人更容易感受發音，它就可以幫助學習者掌握口音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes support in a learning process.","zh":"這個短語描述學習過程中的支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"distinctive sound","meaning":"獨特聲音","examples":[{"en":"Every regional accent has its own distinctive sound.","zh":"每種地區口音都有自己的獨特聲音。"},{"en":"A distinctive sound is a sound that is easy to recognise because it is different from others.","zh":"獨特聲音是因與其他聲音不同而容易辨認的聲音。"},{"en":"A school bell has a distinctive sound that students recognise immediately.","zh":"學校鐘聲有獨特聲音，學生一聽就認得。"},{"en":"If an accent has a distinctive sound, listeners may identify the speaker’s region quickly.","zh":"如果口音有獨特聲音，聽者可能很快識別說話者地區。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a recognisable auditory feature.","zh":"這個短語指出可辨認的聽覺特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"target pronunciation","meaning":"目標發音","examples":[{"en":"The coach helps the learner produce the target pronunciation.","zh":"教練幫助學習者發出目標發音。"},{"en":"Target pronunciation is the specific pronunciation that a learner is trying to achieve.","zh":"目標發音是學習者試圖達到的特定發音。"},{"en":"In an English lesson, the target pronunciation may be the difference between “ship” and “sheep”.","zh":"在英語課中，目標發音可能是 “ship” 和 “sheep” 的分別。"},{"en":"If learners know the target pronunciation clearly, they can compare their own speech with it.","zh":"如果學習者清楚知道目標發音，就能把自己的說話與它比較。"},{"en":"The phrase names the sound goal of pronunciation practice.","zh":"這個短語指出發音練習的聲音目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"mental aid","meaning":"心像輔助方法","examples":[{"en":"A mental aid can make an unfamiliar accent easier to produce.","zh":"心像輔助方法可以令陌生口音更容易發出。"},{"en":"A mental aid is an idea, image or memory that helps someone perform a task.","zh":"心像輔助方法是一種幫助某人完成任務的想法、圖像或記憶。"},{"en":"A student may use a mental aid, such as imagining a picture, to remember vocabulary.","zh":"學生可能使用心像輔助方法，例如想像圖片，來記住詞彙。"},{"en":"If an accent is difficult, a mental image can guide the mouth toward the right sound.","zh":"如果口音困難，心像可以引導口部走向正確聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a thinking tool that supports learning.","zh":"這個短語描述支援學習的思考工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be employed","meaning":"被採用","examples":[{"en":"A particular mental image is employed when teaching Scouse.","zh":"教授利物浦口音時，會採用某個特定心像。"},{"en":"To be employed means to be used for a particular purpose.","zh":"被採用，指為某特定目的而被使用。"},{"en":"A simple diagram may be employed to explain how blood moves through the heart.","zh":"簡單圖表可能被採用來解釋血液如何流經心臟。"},{"en":"If a teaching image is employed well, students may understand a difficult sound faster.","zh":"如果教學意象被妥善採用，學生可能更快理解困難聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase means used, not necessarily hired for a job.","zh":"這個短語指被使用，不一定指受僱工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"push one’s cheekbones up","meaning":"將顴骨向上提","examples":[{"en":"Learners are told to push their cheekbones up in a smile.","zh":"學習者被告知要微笑，將顴骨向上提。"},{"en":"To push one’s cheekbones up means to raise the cheeks as if smiling strongly.","zh":"將顴骨向上提，指像強烈微笑一樣抬高臉頰。"},{"en":"A drama teacher may ask students to push their cheekbones up to create a bright expression.","zh":"戲劇老師可能要求學生將顴骨向上提，以創造明亮表情。"},{"en":"If learners raise their cheekbones, the shape of the mouth and sound may change.","zh":"如果學習者抬起顴骨，口形和聲音可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a facial movement used for accent practice.","zh":"這個短語描述用於口音練習的面部動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as high as they will go","meaning":"提到最高位置","examples":[{"en":"The cheekbones should be raised as high as they will go.","zh":"顴骨應被提到最高位置。"},{"en":"As high as they will go means to the highest position possible.","zh":"提到最高位置，指達到可能的最高位置。"},{"en":"A child may stretch their arms as high as they will go to reach a shelf.","zh":"孩子可能把手臂伸到最高位置，以拿到架上的東西。"},{"en":"If cheekbones are raised fully, the mouth may form the target accent more easily.","zh":"如果顴骨完全抬高，口部可能更容易形成目標口音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reaching the maximum physical limit.","zh":"這個短語描述達到最大身體極限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"slack mouth","meaning":"鬆弛的口腔","examples":[{"en":"The learner imagines having a very slack mouth.","zh":"學習者想像自己有非常鬆弛的口腔。"},{"en":"A slack mouth is a loose, relaxed mouth with little tension.","zh":"鬆弛的口腔，是缺少張力、放鬆的口部。"},{"en":"Someone who is very tired may speak with a slack mouth and unclear sounds.","zh":"很疲倦的人可能用鬆弛的口部說話，聲音不清楚。"},{"en":"If learners relax the mouth too much, the accent may sound softer or less precise.","zh":"如果學習者過度放鬆口部，口音可能聽起來較柔和或不夠精確。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a loose mouth position.","zh":"這個短語描述鬆散的口部位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a mouth full of cotton wool","meaning":"滿口棉花","examples":[{"en":"The learner imagines having a mouth full of cotton wool.","zh":"學習者想像自己滿口棉花。"},{"en":"A mouth full of cotton wool is a mental image of speaking as if soft material fills the mouth.","zh":"滿口棉花是一種心像，指說話時彷彿柔軟材料塞滿口腔。"},{"en":"A voice coach may use this image to make students loosen and thicken certain sounds.","zh":"發音教練可能使用這個意象，令學生放鬆並加厚某些聲音。"},{"en":"If someone imagines cotton wool in the mouth, their speech may become less sharp.","zh":"如果某人想像口中有棉花，說話可能變得沒那麼尖銳。"},{"en":"The phrase is not literal; it is a pronunciation teaching image.","zh":"這個短語不是字面意思，而是一個發音教學意象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"spring off","meaning":"從……彈出","examples":[{"en":"The Scouse sound seems to spring off the sides of the face.","zh":"利物浦口音聲音似乎從臉部兩側彈出。"},{"en":"To spring off something means to bounce or seem to come energetically from that surface or area.","zh":"從某物彈出，指從該表面或位置彈開，或似乎有力量地發出。"},{"en":"A ball may spring off a wall if it hits the surface hard.","zh":"如果球用力撞牆，它可能從牆上彈出。"},{"en":"If a sound seems to spring off the face, the speaker feels it moving outward with energy.","zh":"如果聲音似乎從面部彈出，說話者會感到它有力量地向外移動。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a vivid image of sound direction.","zh":"這個短語營造聲音方向的生動畫面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"outwards and upwards","meaning":"向外及向上","examples":[{"en":"The sound appears to move outwards and upwards.","zh":"聲音似乎向外及向上移動。"},{"en":"Outwards and upwards means away from the centre and toward a higher position.","zh":"向外及向上，指離開中心並朝較高位置移動。"},{"en":"A dancer may move their arms outwards and upwards to create a larger shape.","zh":"舞者可能把手臂向外及向上移動，以創造更大形態。"},{"en":"If a voice coach says the sound moves outwards and upwards, learners imagine direction in the face.","zh":"如果聲線教練說聲音向外及向上移動，學習者就會想像面部中的方向。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a physical direction for movement or sound.","zh":"這個短語給出動作或聲音的身體方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tighten the sides of the jaw","meaning":"收緊下顎兩側","examples":[{"en":"For a Belfast accent, learners tighten the sides of the jaw.","zh":"對於貝爾法斯特口音，學習者要收緊下顎兩側。"},{"en":"To tighten the sides of the jaw means to make the jaw muscles on both sides tense.","zh":"收緊下顎兩側，指令下顎兩邊肌肉變得繃緊。"},{"en":"A person may tighten the sides of the jaw when trying not to speak angrily.","zh":"一個人試圖不要生氣說話時，可能收緊下顎兩側。"},{"en":"If learners tighten the jaw, the mouth opening and sound quality may change.","zh":"如果學習者收緊下顎，嘴巴開合和聲音質素可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a physical technique for pronunciation.","zh":"這個短語描述發音中的身體技巧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"maximum tension","meaning":"最大繃緊程度","examples":[{"en":"The jaw is held at maximum tension.","zh":"下顎保持在最大繃緊程度。"},{"en":"Maximum tension means the greatest possible tightness in the muscles.","zh":"最大繃緊程度指肌肉可能達到的最高緊張狀態。"},{"en":"A violin string under maximum tension may snap if tightened further.","zh":"小提琴弦在最大張力下，如果再收緊可能斷裂。"},{"en":"If jaw muscles are held at maximum tension, speech may sound tight and controlled.","zh":"如果下顎肌肉保持最大繃緊程度，說話可能聽起來緊而受控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the strongest level of physical tightness.","zh":"這個短語描述最強的身體繃緊程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"open the lips as little as possible","meaning":"盡量少張開嘴唇","examples":[{"en":"The learner speaks while opening the lips as little as possible.","zh":"學習者說話時盡量少張開嘴唇。"},{"en":"To open the lips as little as possible means to speak with a very small mouth opening.","zh":"盡量少張開嘴唇，指用非常小的嘴巴開口說話。"},{"en":"A person whispering in a library may open the lips as little as possible.","zh":"在圖書館小聲說話的人，可能盡量少張開嘴唇。"},{"en":"If learners keep the lips almost closed, the sound may become tighter or more compressed.","zh":"如果學習者幾乎閉着嘴唇，聲音可能變得更緊或更壓縮。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a specific mouth-position instruction.","zh":"這個短語給出特定口形指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"give rise to","meaning":"產生；引起","examples":[{"en":"This pronunciation pattern gives rise to the “Ulster jaw”.","zh":"這種發音模式產生「阿爾斯特下顎」現象。"},{"en":"To give rise to something means to cause it to happen or develop.","zh":"產生或引起某事，指造成它發生或發展。"},{"en":"Poor classroom ventilation can give rise to headaches and tiredness.","zh":"課室通風差可以引起頭痛和疲倦。"},{"en":"If repeated jaw tension changes appearance, pronunciation may give rise to a visible facial effect.","zh":"如果反覆下顎緊繃改變外貌，發音可能產生可見面部效果。"},{"en":"The phrase links a cause with a later result.","zh":"這個短語把原因與後來結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"well-known phenomenon","meaning":"廣為人知的現象","examples":[{"en":"The “Ulster jaw” is described as a well-known phenomenon.","zh":"「阿爾斯特下顎」被描述為廣為人知的現象。"},{"en":"A well-known phenomenon is something many people have heard of or recognised.","zh":"廣為人知的現象，是許多人聽過或認得的事情。"},{"en":"Exam stress is a well-known phenomenon among senior students.","zh":"考試壓力是高中學生中廣為人知的現象。"},{"en":"If a facial effect is well known locally, people may mention it even without scientific proof.","zh":"如果某面部效果在本地廣為人知，人們即使沒有科學證明也可能提到它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something familiar or widely recognised.","zh":"這個短語描述熟悉或廣泛被認識的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Ulster jaw","meaning":"「阿爾斯特下顎」現象","examples":[{"en":"The term “Ulster jaw” refers to a facial effect linked to a Belfast accent.","zh":"「阿爾斯特下顎」這個詞指與貝爾法斯特口音相關的面部效果。"},{"en":"Ulster jaw is a name for a jaw appearance supposedly associated with speech habits in Ulster or Belfast.","zh":"「阿爾斯特下顎」是據稱與阿爾斯特或貝爾法斯特說話習慣相關的下顎外觀名稱。"},{"en":"A voice coach may mention Ulster jaw when teaching learners how to hold the jaw tightly.","zh":"發音教練教授學習者如何緊繃下顎時，可能提到「阿爾斯特下顎」。"},{"en":"If an accent encourages jaw tension, people may connect the sound with a facial look.","zh":"如果口音鼓勵下顎繃緊，人們可能把聲音與面部外觀連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase names a claimed accent-related facial feature.","zh":"這個短語指出一種據稱與口音相關的面部特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"involve imagining","meaning":"涉及想像","examples":[{"en":"Learning an Australian accent involves imagining a difficult environment.","zh":"學習澳洲口音涉及想像一個艱難環境。"},{"en":"To involve imagining something means to require someone to create a mental picture of it.","zh":"涉及想像某事，指需要某人在腦海中創造它的畫面。"},{"en":"Drama training may involve imagining a cold room so actors change their body language.","zh":"戲劇訓練可能涉及想像寒冷房間，令演員改變身體語言。"},{"en":"If learners imagine heat and bright sunlight, their facial expression may help produce the accent.","zh":"如果學習者想像酷熱和刺眼陽光，其面部表情可能有助發出該口音。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that mental images can support physical performance.","zh":"這個短語顯示心像可以支援身體表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the ordeals of","meaning":"……所經歷的苦難","examples":[{"en":"Learners imagine the ordeals of the first Western settlers.","zh":"學習者想像第一批西方移民所經歷的苦難。"},{"en":"The ordeals of a group are the severe difficulties and suffering they experienced.","zh":"某群體所經歷的苦難，是他們遭遇的嚴重困難和痛苦。"},{"en":"A history lesson may discuss the ordeals of refugees crossing dangerous seas.","zh":"歷史課可能討論難民橫渡危險海域所經歷的苦難。"},{"en":"If learners imagine harsh conditions, they may adopt the facial tension linked to that environment.","zh":"如果學習者想像惡劣環境，可能採用與該環境相關的面部繃緊。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to difficult experiences, not ordinary inconvenience.","zh":"這個短語指艱難經歷，而不是普通不便。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"first Westerners","meaning":"第一批西方人","examples":[{"en":"The first Westerners were transported to the other side of the world.","zh":"第一批西方人被運送到世界的另一端。"},{"en":"The first Westerners means the earliest people from Western countries to arrive in a particular place.","zh":"第一批西方人，指最早到達某地的西方國家人士。"},{"en":"The first Westerners in a remote region may have faced unfamiliar climate, food and geography.","zh":"到達偏遠地區的第一批西方人，可能面對陌生氣候、食物和地理環境。"},{"en":"If settlers came from Europe to Australia, the environment could feel strange and harsh.","zh":"如果殖民者從歐洲來到澳洲，環境可能感覺陌生而嚴酷。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies an early group by origin and arrival.","zh":"這個短語按來源和到達時間識別早期群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be transported to","meaning":"被運送到","examples":[{"en":"Many early settlers were transported to Australia.","zh":"許多早期移民被運送到澳洲。"},{"en":"To be transported to a place means to be taken or sent there, often over a long distance.","zh":"被運送到某地，指被帶到或送到那裡，通常跨越長距離。"},{"en":"Injured patients may be transported to hospital by ambulance.","zh":"受傷病人可能由救護車運送到醫院。"},{"en":"If people were transported across the world, the journey itself could be difficult and frightening.","zh":"如果人們被運送到世界另一端，旅程本身可能困難又可怕。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on being moved from one place to another.","zh":"這個短語強調由一地移到另一地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the other side of the world","meaning":"世界的另一端","examples":[{"en":"Australia was on the other side of the world from Europe.","zh":"澳洲位於歐洲世界的另一端。"},{"en":"The other side of the world means a place extremely far away.","zh":"世界的另一端指極其遙遠的地方。"},{"en":"A student studying abroad in Canada may feel they are on the other side of the world from home.","zh":"在加拿大留學的學生可能覺得自己離家到了世界另一端。"},{"en":"If settlers travel to the other side of the world, climate and culture may feel unfamiliar.","zh":"如果殖民者前往世界另一端，氣候和文化可能感覺陌生。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses great distance.","zh":"這個短語強調極大距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be exposed to","meaning":"暴露於","examples":[{"en":"The settlers were exposed to intense sunlight and heat.","zh":"這些移民暴露於強烈陽光和酷熱之中。"},{"en":"To be exposed to something means to experience it directly, often without protection.","zh":"暴露於某事，指直接經歷它，通常沒有保護。"},{"en":"Construction workers may be exposed to loud noise if they do not wear ear protection.","zh":"如果建築工人不戴耳罩，可能暴露於巨大噪音中。"},{"en":"If people are exposed to strong sun every day, they may narrow their eyes often.","zh":"如果人們每天暴露於強烈陽光下，可能常瞇起眼睛。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct contact with a condition or influence.","zh":"這個短語描述直接接觸某條件或影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"merciless glare","meaning":"刺眼而猛烈的陽光","examples":[{"en":"The merciless glare of the sun made people narrow their eyes.","zh":"刺眼而猛烈的陽光令人瞇起眼睛。"},{"en":"Merciless glare means extremely bright light that feels harsh and gives no relief.","zh":"刺眼而猛烈的陽光，指極度明亮、嚴酷且毫不舒緩的光線。"},{"en":"Drivers may struggle under the merciless glare of afternoon sunlight on a highway.","zh":"司機在高速公路下午刺眼陽光下可能很吃力。"},{"en":"If glare is intense, people instinctively squint to protect their eyes.","zh":"如果眩光強烈，人們會本能地瞇眼保護眼睛。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a strong image of harsh brightness.","zh":"這個短語營造嚴酷亮光的強烈畫面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unremitting heat","meaning":"持續不斷的酷熱","examples":[{"en":"The settlers endured the unremitting heat of the southern sun.","zh":"這些移民忍受南方烈日持續不斷的酷熱。"},{"en":"Unremitting heat is heat that continues without stopping or easing.","zh":"持續不斷的酷熱，是不停止或不減弱的高溫。"},{"en":"Workers on an outdoor site may feel exhausted after hours of unremitting heat.","zh":"戶外工地工人在數小時持續酷熱後可能筋疲力竭。"},{"en":"If heat is unremitting, people may tense their faces and narrow their eyes for protection.","zh":"如果酷熱持續不斷，人們可能繃緊面部並瞇眼保護自己。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continuous harsh heat.","zh":"這個短語描述持續而嚴酷的熱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"southern sun","meaning":"南方烈日","examples":[{"en":"The southern sun exposed settlers to intense heat and glare.","zh":"南方烈日令移民暴露於強烈高溫和刺眼陽光下。"},{"en":"Southern sun refers to the strong sunlight in a southern or hot region.","zh":"南方烈日指位於南方或炎熱地區的強烈陽光。"},{"en":"Travellers unused to the southern sun may need hats, sunglasses and water.","zh":"不習慣南方烈日的旅客可能需要帽、太陽眼鏡和水。"},{"en":"If people live under strong sun, facial habits like squinting may develop.","zh":"如果人們在強烈陽光下生活，瞇眼等面部習慣可能形成。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a sense of hot climate and bright light.","zh":"這個短語帶出炎熱氣候和強光感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"instinctively screw up one’s eyes","meaning":"本能地瞇起眼睛","examples":[{"en":"People instinctively screw up their eyes in harsh sunlight.","zh":"人們在強烈陽光下會本能地瞇起眼睛。"},{"en":"To instinctively screw up one’s eyes means to narrow the eyes automatically to protect them.","zh":"本能地瞇起眼睛，指自動收窄眼睛以保護它們。"},{"en":"A child may screw up their eyes when stepping from a dark cinema into bright daylight.","zh":"孩子從黑暗戲院走到明亮日光下時，可能瞇起眼睛。"},{"en":"If sunlight is painfully bright, people do not think first; their eyes narrow by reflex.","zh":"如果陽光刺眼得令人疼痛，人們不會先思考；眼睛會反射地收窄。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an automatic protective facial movement.","zh":"這個短語描述自動保護性的面部動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"grimace for protection","meaning":"為了保護自己而皺面","examples":[{"en":"People may grimace for protection against the heat and glare.","zh":"人們可能為了抵禦酷熱和眩光而皺面保護自己。"},{"en":"To grimace for protection means to twist the face in discomfort to shield oneself from something unpleasant.","zh":"為了保護自己而皺面，指因不適而扭曲面部，以保護自己免受不愉快事物影響。"},{"en":"A cyclist may grimace for protection when dust blows into their face.","zh":"當灰塵吹到臉上，騎單車的人可能為保護自己而皺面。"},{"en":"If people repeatedly grimace in harsh weather, the expression may become habitual.","zh":"如果人們在惡劣天氣中反覆皺面，表情可能變成習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase connects facial tension with self-protection.","zh":"這個短語把面部繃緊與自我保護連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"contribute to an Australian look","meaning":"促成澳洲人的外貌特徵","examples":[{"en":"The climate may have contributed to a recognisable Australian look.","zh":"氣候可能促成可辨認的澳洲人外貌特徵。"},{"en":"To contribute to an Australian look means to help create facial features or expressions associated with Australians.","zh":"促成澳洲人的外貌特徵，指幫助創造與澳洲人相關的面部特徵或表情。"},{"en":"Strong sunlight may contribute to a local look if people often squint outdoors.","zh":"如果人們常在戶外瞇眼，強烈陽光可能促成本地外貌特徵。"},{"en":"If climate shapes facial habits over many years, it can affect how a population is perceived.","zh":"如果氣候多年塑造面部習慣，它可以影響人們如何看待某人口。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests one possible influence on national appearance.","zh":"這個短語暗示國民外貌的一種可能影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"vice versa","meaning":"反之亦然","examples":[{"en":"Pronunciation may affect appearance, or vice versa.","zh":"發音可能影響外貌，反之亦然。"},{"en":"Vice versa means the opposite direction may also be true.","zh":"“Vice versa” 指相反方向也可能成立。"},{"en":"Stress can affect sleep, and vice versa, because poor sleep can increase stress.","zh":"壓力可以影響睡眠，反之亦然，因為睡眠差也會增加壓力。"},{"en":"If pronunciation shapes the face, it is also possible that face shape influences pronunciation.","zh":"如果發音塑造面部，也可能是面部形狀影響發音。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when two things may affect each other both ways.","zh":"這個短語用於兩件事可能互相雙向影響時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"chicken-and-egg conundrum","meaning":"雞先還是蛋先的難題","examples":[{"en":"The relationship between accent and appearance is a chicken-and-egg conundrum.","zh":"口音與外貌之間的關係是雞先還是蛋先的難題。"},{"en":"A chicken-and-egg conundrum is a problem where it is hard to know which of two things came first.","zh":"雞先還是蛋先的難題，是難以知道兩件事中哪一件先出現的問題。"},{"en":"In education, confidence and success can be a chicken-and-egg problem because each can create the other.","zh":"在教育中，信心和成功可以是雞先還是蛋先的問題，因為兩者可互相造成。"},{"en":"If accent may cause facial features and facial features may cause accent, the direction is unclear.","zh":"如果口音可能造成面部特徵，而面部特徵也可能造成口音，方向就不清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes circular cause and effect.","zh":"這個短語描述循環因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ultimately irrelevant","meaning":"最終並不重要","examples":[{"en":"The precise direction of cause and effect may be ultimately irrelevant.","zh":"因果的精確方向最終可能並不重要。"},{"en":"Ultimately irrelevant means not important in the final analysis.","zh":"最終並不重要，指在最後分析中不重要。"},{"en":"If a student improves, whether confidence came before practice may be ultimately irrelevant.","zh":"如果學生進步了，信心是否先於練習可能最終並不重要。"},{"en":"If both accent and appearance influence each other, choosing one first cause may not matter much.","zh":"如果口音和外貌互相影響，選出單一先因可能不太重要。"},{"en":"The phrase dismisses a detail as not central to the main point.","zh":"這個短語把某細節視為不是核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"other factors affect","meaning":"其他因素影響","examples":[{"en":"Other factors also affect the way people look and sound.","zh":"其他因素也影響人們的外貌和聲音。"},{"en":"Other factors affect something means additional causes also influence it.","zh":"其他因素影響某事，指額外原因也對它有作用。"},{"en":"A student’s performance is affected by study habits, sleep and family support.","zh":"學生表現受學習習慣、睡眠和家庭支持影響。"},{"en":"If climate, heredity and lifestyle all matter, pronunciation is not the only possible cause.","zh":"如果氣候、遺傳和生活方式都重要，發音就不是唯一可能原因。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds readers that explanations are often multi-causal.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者，解釋通常有多重原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be inaccurate to suggest that","meaning":"認為……並不準確","examples":[{"en":"It would be inaccurate to suggest that all speakers share one appearance.","zh":"認為所有說話者都有同一外貌並不準確。"},{"en":"To be inaccurate to suggest that means it would be wrong or misleading to claim that.","zh":"認為某事並不準確，指作出該主張會錯誤或具誤導性。"},{"en":"It is inaccurate to suggest that all quiet students lack confidence.","zh":"認為所有安靜學生都缺乏信心並不準確。"},{"en":"If many exceptions exist, a simple statement about all speakers cannot be true.","zh":"如果有許多例外，關於所有說話者的簡單說法就不可能是真的。"},{"en":"The phrase corrects an overgeneralisation.","zh":"這個短語糾正過度概括。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"one form of a language","meaning":"一種語言形式","examples":[{"en":"People who speak one form of a language do not all look alike.","zh":"說一種語言形式的人並不全都長得一樣。"},{"en":"One form of a language is one variety, dialect or accent within a larger language.","zh":"一種語言形式，是較大語言中的一個變體、方言或口音。"},{"en":"Australian English is one form of English, but Australians do not all have the same face.","zh":"澳洲英語是英語的一種形式，但澳洲人並不都有同一張臉。"},{"en":"If a language form includes many speakers, their appearance will still vary widely.","zh":"如果一種語言形式包含許多說話者，他們的外貌仍會差異很大。"},{"en":"The phrase helps distinguish language variety from physical uniformity.","zh":"這個短語幫助區分語言變體與身體一致性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"dialect","meaning":"方言","examples":[{"en":"A dialect does not give every speaker exactly the same appearance.","zh":"方言不會令每名說話者都有完全相同的外貌。"},{"en":"A dialect is a form of a language used by a particular region or social group.","zh":"方言是特定地區或社會群體使用的一種語言形式。"},{"en":"Cantonese is often described as a Chinese variety with its own sounds, words and expressions.","zh":"廣東話常被描述為有自己聲音、詞語和表達方式的中文變體。"},{"en":"If people share a dialect, they may share speech habits but not identical faces.","zh":"如果人們共享方言，他們可能共享說話習慣，但不會有相同面孔。"},{"en":"The word refers to language variation within a wider language system.","zh":"這個詞指較大語言系統內的語言差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"set physiognomy","meaning":"固定相貌","examples":[{"en":"Speakers of an accent do not necessarily have a set physiognomy.","zh":"說某口音的人不一定有固定相貌。"},{"en":"A set physiognomy means one fixed facial appearance shared by all members of a group.","zh":"固定相貌指某群體所有成員共享的一種固定面部外觀。"},{"en":"It would be wrong to say that all singers have a set physiognomy simply because they use their mouths often.","zh":"只因歌手常使用口部，就說所有歌手都有固定相貌，是錯誤的。"},{"en":"If people vary in genetics, age and lifestyle, one accent cannot produce one exact face.","zh":"如果人們在基因、年齡和生活方式上不同，一種口音不能產生一張完全相同的臉。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against oversimplifying appearance.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要過分簡化外貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"pronunciation patterns","meaning":"發音模式","examples":[{"en":"Long-term pronunciation patterns may influence facial muscles.","zh":"長期發音模式可能影響面部肌肉。"},{"en":"Pronunciation patterns are repeated ways of producing sounds in speech.","zh":"發音模式是說話中反覆出現的發聲方式。"},{"en":"A learner’s pronunciation patterns may show the influence of their first language.","zh":"學習者的發音模式可能顯示其母語影響。"},{"en":"If a pattern uses the same muscles repeatedly, it may become a habit over time.","zh":"如果某模式反覆使用同一肌肉，久而久之可能變成習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to regular sound habits rather than one isolated word.","zh":"這個短語指規律的聲音習慣，而不是單一孤立詞語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a large enough number","meaning":"數量足夠多的人","examples":[{"en":"A large enough number of people appear to show similar features.","zh":"數量足夠多的人似乎顯示相似特徵。"},{"en":"A large enough number means enough cases to make a pattern worth noticing.","zh":"數量足夠多，指個案足以令某模式值得注意。"},{"en":"If a large enough number of students misunderstand the same question, the teacher may need to explain it again.","zh":"如果足夠多學生誤解同一題目，老師可能需要重新解釋。"},{"en":"If many speakers show similar features, researchers may decide the pattern deserves investigation.","zh":"如果許多說話者顯示相似特徵，研究者可能認為該模式值得研究。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests sufficient quantity for attention, not absolute proof.","zh":"這個短語暗示數量足以引起注意，但不是絕對證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be worth investigating","meaning":"值得研究","examples":[{"en":"The apparent pattern is worth investigating scientifically.","zh":"這個表面模式值得以科學方式研究。"},{"en":"To be worth investigating means to deserve careful study because it may reveal something useful.","zh":"值得研究，指因可能揭示有用東西而值得仔細探討。"},{"en":"If many students make the same grammar mistake, the cause is worth investigating.","zh":"如果許多學生犯同一文法錯誤，原因就值得研究。"},{"en":"If accent and appearance seem connected, researchers should test the idea systematically.","zh":"如果口音與外貌似乎相關，研究者應有系統地測試這個想法。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests curiosity supported by possible importance.","zh":"這個短語暗示由可能重要性支持的好奇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"establish something as a factor","meaning":"確立……為其中一個因素","examples":[{"en":"The writer wants to establish pronunciation as a factor in physiognomy.","zh":"作者想確立發音為相貌的一個因素。"},{"en":"To establish something as a factor means to show that it is one influence among others.","zh":"確立某事為一個因素，指顯示它是眾多影響之一。"},{"en":"Researchers may establish sleep as a factor in exam performance.","zh":"研究者可能確立睡眠是考試表現的一個因素。"},{"en":"If pronunciation is established as a factor, it would not mean it is the only cause of appearance.","zh":"如果發音被確立為一個因素，並不代表它是外貌唯一原因。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies one contributing influence in a complex issue.","zh":"這個短語指出複雜問題中的一項促成影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"determine physiognomy","meaning":"決定相貌","examples":[{"en":"Pronunciation may be one of the factors that determine physiognomy.","zh":"發音可能是決定相貌的因素之一。"},{"en":"To determine physiognomy means to influence or shape a person’s facial appearance.","zh":"決定相貌，指影響或塑造一個人的面部外觀。"},{"en":"Genetics, age and lifestyle can help determine physiognomy over time.","zh":"基因、年齡和生活方式可以隨時間幫助決定相貌。"},{"en":"If speech habits affect muscles, they may partly determine facial form.","zh":"如果說話習慣影響肌肉，它們可能部分決定面部形態。"},{"en":"The phrase discusses causes of facial appearance.","zh":"這個短語討論面部外貌的成因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"gain a deeper insight into","meaning":"更深入了解","examples":[{"en":"The research could help us gain a deeper insight into speech.","zh":"這項研究可以幫助我們更深入了解語音。"},{"en":"To gain a deeper insight into something means to understand it more clearly and profoundly.","zh":"更深入了解某事，指更清楚、更深刻地理解它。"},{"en":"Interviewing patients can help medical students gain a deeper insight into illness.","zh":"訪問病人可以幫助醫科學生更深入了解疾病。"},{"en":"If researchers study mouth movement and accent, they may understand speech beyond sound alone.","zh":"如果研究者研究口部動作和口音，就可能理解語音不只是聲音本身。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving from surface knowledge to deeper understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述由表面知識走向更深理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"origins and nature","meaning":"起源和本質","examples":[{"en":"Scientists want to understand the origins and nature of speech sounds.","zh":"科學家想了解語音的起源和本質。"},{"en":"Origins and nature mean where something comes from and what it is fundamentally like.","zh":"起源和本質指某事來自哪裡，以及其根本性質是甚麼。"},{"en":"A history lesson may explore the origins and nature of democracy.","zh":"歷史課可能探討民主的起源和本質。"},{"en":"If researchers study both origin and nature, they ask how something began and how it works.","zh":"如果研究者研究起源和本質，他們就是問某事如何開始及如何運作。"},{"en":"The phrase combines beginning and basic character.","zh":"這個短語結合開端和基本特性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"sounds of speech","meaning":"語音","examples":[{"en":"The study could explain the physical nature of the sounds of speech.","zh":"這項研究可以解釋語音的身體本質。"},{"en":"Sounds of speech are the sounds people make when speaking a language.","zh":"語音是人們說一種語言時發出的聲音。"},{"en":"English sounds of speech include vowels, consonants and connected speech features.","zh":"英語語音包括元音、輔音和連讀特徵。"},{"en":"If students hear and feel speech sounds clearly, they can improve pronunciation more effectively.","zh":"如果學生清楚聽到並感受到語音，就能更有效改善發音。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to spoken sound units, not written letters.","zh":"這個短語指口語聲音單位，而不是書寫字母。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"one’s own group","meaning":"自己所屬的群體","examples":[{"en":"The writer wonders what characteristic look their own group may have.","zh":"作者思考自己所屬群體可能有甚麼特徵外貌。"},{"en":"One’s own group means the community, nationality, class or speech group that a person belongs to.","zh":"自己所屬的群體，指某人所屬的社區、國籍、階級或語音群體。"},{"en":"A student may notice habits in their own group only after meeting people from other schools.","zh":"學生可能在認識其他學校的人後，才注意到自己群體中的習慣。"},{"en":"If people study other groups, they may begin to question what marks their own group as distinctive.","zh":"如果人們研究其他群體，可能開始追問自己群體有何獨特標記。"},{"en":"The phrase turns observation back onto the observer’s community.","zh":"這個短語把觀察轉回觀察者自己的社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"look at the following people","meaning":"查看以下人物","examples":[{"en":"Candidates look at the following people and match them with statements.","zh":"考生查看以下人物，並把他們與陳述配對。"},{"en":"Look at the following people means read the list of names provided in the question.","zh":"查看以下人物，指閱讀題目提供的姓名列表。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should look at the following people before scanning for their ideas.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先查看以下人物，再掃讀他們的想法。"},{"en":"If a name appears in the passage, students should note what that person said or believed.","zh":"如果某姓名出現在文章中，學生應記下該人說過或相信甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase is an exam instruction for matching tasks.","zh":"這個短語是配對題中的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"list of statements","meaning":"陳述列表","examples":[{"en":"The task provides a list of statements about the writers and researchers.","zh":"題目提供關於作者和研究者的陳述列表。"},{"en":"A list of statements is a set of sentences or claims that students must match or judge.","zh":"陳述列表是一組學生必須配對或判斷的句子或主張。"},{"en":"In reading practice, a list of statements may include ideas from different paragraphs.","zh":"在閱讀練習中，陳述列表可能包括來自不同段落的想法。"},{"en":"If students read the list first, they know what information to search for.","zh":"如果學生先閱讀列表，就知道要搜尋甚麼資料。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the answer options or claims in a task.","zh":"這個短語指題目中的答案選項或主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"match each person with","meaning":"將每個人物與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match each person with the correct statement.","zh":"學生將每個人物與正確陳述配對。"},{"en":"To match each person with something means to connect every name to the right idea, action or description.","zh":"將每個人物與某事配對，指把每個姓名連接到正確想法、行動或描述。"},{"en":"Students may match each scientist with the discovery mentioned in the passage.","zh":"學生可能把每位科學家與文章中提到的發現配對。"},{"en":"If two people have similar views, students must read carefully before matching.","zh":"如果兩個人看法相似，學生配對前必須仔細閱讀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common reading-test task.","zh":"這個短語描述常見閱讀測驗題型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"use their jaws more to enunciate","meaning":"更頻繁運用下顎咬字","examples":[{"en":"One theory states that Americans use their jaws more to enunciate.","zh":"一種理論認為美國人更頻繁運用下顎咬字。"},{"en":"To use their jaws more to enunciate means to rely more strongly on jaw movement when pronouncing words clearly.","zh":"更頻繁運用下顎咬字，指清楚發音時更強烈依賴下顎動作。"},{"en":"A speech coach may ask learners to use their jaws more when a sound is too weak.","zh":"當某聲音太弱，發音教練可能要求學習者更多使用下顎。"},{"en":"If a group uses the jaw more in daily speech, jaw muscles may become more active.","zh":"如果一個群體在日常說話中更多使用下顎，下顎肌肉可能變得更活躍。"},{"en":"The phrase links clear pronunciation with physical mouth movement.","zh":"這個短語把清晰發音與口部身體動作連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"physiognomical features","meaning":"相貌特徵","examples":[{"en":"Immigrants may acquire physiognomical features common in the local population.","zh":"移民可能形成本地人口中常見的相貌特徵。"},{"en":"Physiognomical features are visible facial features or characteristics of appearance.","zh":"相貌特徵是可見的面部特徵或外貌特點。"},{"en":"Cheekbones, jaw shape and habitual expressions can be described as physiognomical features.","zh":"顴骨、下顎形狀和習慣性表情都可被描述為相貌特徵。"},{"en":"If immigrants acquire local speech habits, some people wonder whether facial features may also change.","zh":"如果移民形成本地說話習慣，有些人會思考面部特徵是否也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and relates to face and appearance.","zh":"這個短語較正式，與面部和外貌相關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"common among","meaning":"在……中常見","examples":[{"en":"The broadened jaw is common among parts of the indigenous population.","zh":"較寬闊的下顎在部分本地原有居民中常見。"},{"en":"Common among a group means often found in that group.","zh":"在某群體中常見，指經常在該群體中出現。"},{"en":"Wearing uniforms is common among students in many Hong Kong schools.","zh":"穿校服在許多香港學校的學生中很常見。"},{"en":"If a feature is common among local people, outsiders may associate it with that region.","zh":"如果某特徵在本地人中常見，外人可能把它與該地區聯繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes frequency within a group.","zh":"這個短語描述某事在群體中的出現頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be hereditary","meaning":"是遺傳的","examples":[{"en":"Some people mistakenly believe that facial features are entirely hereditary.","zh":"有些人錯誤地相信面部特徵完全是遺傳的。"},{"en":"To be hereditary means to be passed from parents to children through genes.","zh":"是遺傳的，指透過基因由父母傳給子女。"},{"en":"Eye colour can be hereditary, but habits and environment also affect appearance.","zh":"眼睛顏色可以是遺傳的，但習慣和環境也影響外貌。"},{"en":"If a feature is not hereditary, it may come from lifestyle, climate or repeated movement.","zh":"如果某特徵不是遺傳的，它可能來自生活方式、氣候或反覆動作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes genetic inheritance.","zh":"這個短語描述基因遺傳。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"lifestyle affects physiognomy","meaning":"生活方式影響相貌","examples":[{"en":"Emerson’s idea suggests that lifestyle affects physiognomy.","zh":"Emerson 的想法暗示生活方式影響相貌。"},{"en":"Lifestyle affects physiognomy means daily habits and social roles may influence facial appearance.","zh":"生活方式影響相貌，指日常習慣和社會角色可能影響面部外貌。"},{"en":"Outdoor workers may develop different facial lines from office workers because of sun and weather.","zh":"因陽光和天氣影響，戶外工人可能形成不同於辦公室員工的面部線條。"},{"en":"If work, stress and speech habits shape the face, appearance is partly learned through life.","zh":"如果工作、壓力和說話習慣塑造面部，外貌就部分由生活經歷形成。"},{"en":"The phrase argues that how people live can affect how they look.","zh":"這個短語主張人們如何生活會影響其外貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"broadened jaws","meaning":"較寬闊的下顎","examples":[{"en":"Americans are described as having relatively broadened jaws.","zh":"美國人被描述為有相對較寬闊的下顎。"},{"en":"Broadened jaws are jaws that appear wider or more developed than before or than average.","zh":"較寬闊的下顎，是比以前或平均水平看起來更寬或更發達的下顎。"},{"en":"A researcher may compare photographs to see whether broadened jaws become more common after migration.","zh":"研究者可能比較照片，看移民後較寬闊下顎是否變得更常見。"},{"en":"If jaw use increases over time, some theories suggest the lower face may broaden.","zh":"如果下顎使用隨時間增加，一些理論認為下半臉可能變寬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a physical facial characteristic.","zh":"這個短語描述身體面部特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"since they moved to","meaning":"自他們搬到……以來","examples":[{"en":"Koestler noticed that his friends had changed since they moved to America.","zh":"Koestler 注意到他的朋友自搬到美國以來已經改變。"},{"en":"Since they moved to a place means from the time they began living there until now or another later time.","zh":"自他們搬到某地以來，指從他們開始住在那裡直到現在或另一較後時間。"},{"en":"Since they moved to the city, the children have become more used to public transport.","zh":"自孩子搬到城市以來，他們更習慣公共交通。"},{"en":"If people change after moving, the new environment may have influenced them.","zh":"如果人們搬遷後改變，新環境可能影響了他們。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a period beginning with relocation.","zh":"這個短語標示由搬遷開始的一段時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be unremarkable","meaning":"並不顯著","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that the change of countenance was unremarkable.","zh":"該選項暗示面容變化並不顯著。"},{"en":"To be unremarkable means to be ordinary and not especially noticeable.","zh":"並不顯著，指普通且不特別引人注意。"},{"en":"A student’s pronunciation change may be unremarkable if listeners barely notice it.","zh":"如果聽者幾乎注意不到，學生的發音改變可能並不顯著。"},{"en":"If a facial change is obvious to old friends, it is not unremarkable.","zh":"如果面部變化對舊朋友來說很明顯，它就不是不顯著。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something not worth special attention.","zh":"這個短語描述不值得特別注意的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reflect the claims of","meaning":"反映……的主張","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether statements reflect the claims of the writer.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否反映作者的主張。"},{"en":"To reflect the claims of someone means to match or represent what that person argues.","zh":"反映某人的主張，指符合或代表該人的論點。"},{"en":"A summary should reflect the claims of an article without adding personal opinions.","zh":"摘要應反映文章主張，而不加入個人意見。"},{"en":"If a statement changes the writer’s meaning, it does not reflect the claim accurately.","zh":"如果陳述改變作者意思，就不能準確反映主張。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful in reading questions about views and arguments.","zh":"這個短語常用於關於觀點和論點的閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"considerable sums of money","meaning":"大筆金錢","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether further research would cost considerable sums of money.","zh":"該陳述問進一步研究是否會花費大筆金錢。"},{"en":"Considerable sums of money means large amounts of money.","zh":"大筆金錢指大量金錢。"},{"en":"Building a new hospital requires considerable sums of money for land, equipment and staff.","zh":"興建新醫院需要大筆金錢購買土地、設備和聘請員工。"},{"en":"If research needs special laboratories and many participants, the cost may be high.","zh":"如果研究需要特殊實驗室和大量參與者，成本可能很高。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses financial scale.","zh":"這個短語強調財務規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"make it difficult for","meaning":"令……變得困難","examples":[{"en":"Psychological factors make it difficult for adults to learn pronunciation.","zh":"心理因素令成年人學習發音變得困難。"},{"en":"To make it difficult for someone to do something means to create obstacles that prevent success.","zh":"令某人做某事變得困難，指製造阻礙，使成功較難。"},{"en":"Noise in a classroom can make it difficult for students to concentrate.","zh":"課室噪音可以令學生專心變得困難。"},{"en":"If adults fear embarrassment, that fear can make pronunciation practice harder.","zh":"如果成年人害怕尷尬，這種恐懼會令發音練習更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how a condition creates difficulty.","zh":"這個短語解釋某條件如何造成困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"not as important as","meaning":"不及……重要","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not describe socio-linguistic factors as less important than physiology.","zh":"文章並沒有把社會語言學因素描述為不及生理因素重要。"},{"en":"Not as important as means having less importance than another factor.","zh":"不及某事重要，指重要性低於另一因素。"},{"en":"A student’s neat handwriting is not as important as clear ideas in an essay.","zh":"在作文中，整潔字體不及清晰想法重要。"},{"en":"If psychological and social factors are no less important, they should not be treated as minor.","zh":"如果心理和社會因素同樣重要，就不應把它們視為次要。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a comparison of importance.","zh":"這個短語建立重要性的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"make fun of","meaning":"取笑","examples":[{"en":"People often make fun of standard British RP.","zh":"人們常取笑標準英式 RP。"},{"en":"To make fun of something means to laugh at it or mock it.","zh":"取笑某事，指嘲笑或戲弄它。"},{"en":"Students should not make fun of a classmate’s accent or pronunciation mistakes.","zh":"學生不應取笑同學的口音或發音錯誤。"},{"en":"If people make fun of an accent, speakers may feel embarrassed or judged.","zh":"如果人們取笑一種口音，說話者可能感到尷尬或被評判。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ridicule, often in an unkind way.","zh":"這個短語描述嘲弄，常帶不友善意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"incomprehensibility","meaning":"難以理解的程度","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to the possible incomprehensibility of Midlands English.","zh":"該陳述提到英格蘭中部英語可能難以理解的程度。"},{"en":"Incomprehensibility means the quality of being very difficult or impossible to understand.","zh":"難以理解的程度，指非常難或無法理解的性質。"},{"en":"A lecture’s incomprehensibility may come from too much jargon and no examples.","zh":"講座難以理解，可能來自太多術語且沒有例子。"},{"en":"If an accent is unfamiliar, listeners may wrongly judge it as incomprehensible.","zh":"如果口音陌生，聽者可能錯誤判斷它難以理解。"},{"en":"The word describes difficulty in understanding speech or information.","zh":"這個詞描述理解說話或資料的困難程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete each statement with","meaning":"用……完成每句陳述","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete each statement with the best ending.","zh":"考生用最合適的句尾完成每句陳述。"},{"en":"To complete each statement with something means to finish each sentence using the correct option.","zh":"用某物完成每句陳述，指使用正確選項完成每個句子。"},{"en":"In a grammar exercise, students complete each statement with the correct verb form.","zh":"在文法練習中，學生用正確動詞形式完成每句陳述。"},{"en":"If the ending changes the meaning, students must choose the one that matches the passage.","zh":"如果句尾改變意思，學生必須選擇與文章相符的一項。"},{"en":"The phrase is a reading-test instruction for sentence completion.","zh":"這個短語是句子完成閱讀題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the best ending","meaning":"最合適的句尾","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the best ending from the box.","zh":"學生從方框中選擇最合適的句尾。"},{"en":"The best ending is the option that most accurately completes the sentence according to the text.","zh":"最合適的句尾，是根據文本最準確完成句子的選項。"},{"en":"A student should read the whole sentence before choosing the best ending.","zh":"學生選擇最合適句尾前，應先閱讀整句。"},{"en":"If two endings sound possible, the passage evidence should decide the better one.","zh":"如果兩個句尾聽起來都可能，文章證據應決定較好的一個。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the most suitable final part of a sentence.","zh":"這個短語指句子最適合的結尾部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be achieved by using","meaning":"可透過使用……達到","examples":[{"en":"A target accent can sometimes be achieved by using a mental aid.","zh":"目標口音有時可透過使用心像輔助方法達到。"},{"en":"To be achieved by using something means to be successfully reached through that method or tool.","zh":"可透過使用某物達到，指透過該方法或工具成功實現。"},{"en":"Better pronunciation can be achieved by using recordings and repeated practice.","zh":"更好發音可以透過使用錄音和反覆練習達到。"},{"en":"If a mental image guides the mouth correctly, the target sound may be reached more easily.","zh":"如果心像正確引導口部，目標聲音可能更容易達到。"},{"en":"The phrase links a result with the method used to reach it.","zh":"這個短語把結果與達成它的方法連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"use images to assist","meaning":"運用意象協助","examples":[{"en":"Voice coaches use images to assist students with pronunciation.","zh":"聲線教練運用意象協助學生發音。"},{"en":"To use images to assist means to use mental pictures to help someone understand or perform a task.","zh":"運用意象協助，指使用心像幫助某人理解或完成任務。"},{"en":"A teacher may use images to assist students in remembering the difference between similar words.","zh":"老師可能運用意象協助學生記住相似詞的分別。"},{"en":"If learners cannot understand a technical instruction, an image may make the sound easier to produce.","zh":"如果學習者不能理解技術指示，意象可能令聲音更容易發出。"},{"en":"The phrase describes imaginative support for learning.","zh":"這個短語描述對學習的想像性支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"desired pronunciation","meaning":"所需的發音","examples":[{"en":"Mental images may help students produce the desired pronunciation.","zh":"心像可能幫助學生發出所需的發音。"},{"en":"Desired pronunciation is the pronunciation that a learner wants or needs to produce.","zh":"所需的發音，是學習者想要或需要發出的發音。"},{"en":"A student may repeat a recording many times to reach the desired pronunciation.","zh":"學生可能多次重複錄音，以達到所需發音。"},{"en":"If the mouth position is wrong, the desired pronunciation may not appear even after effort.","zh":"如果口腔位置錯誤，即使努力也未必能發出所需發音。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the pronunciation goal.","zh":"這個短語指出發音目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"help learners achieve","meaning":"幫助學習者掌握","examples":[{"en":"Physical and mental techniques can help learners achieve the target pronunciation.","zh":"身體和心理技巧可以幫助學習者掌握目標發音。"},{"en":"To help learners achieve something means to support students until they reach a learning goal.","zh":"幫助學習者掌握某事，指支援學生直到他們達到學習目標。"},{"en":"Clear examples help learners achieve better grammar because they show how rules work.","zh":"清楚例子幫助學習者掌握更好文法，因為它們展示規則如何運作。"},{"en":"If a technique helps learners control their mouth, pronunciation may improve.","zh":"如果技巧幫助學習者控制口部，發音可能改善。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on support that leads to success.","zh":"這個短語強調帶來成功的支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"affect appearance","meaning":"影響外貌","examples":[{"en":"Long-term pronunciation habits may affect appearance.","zh":"長期發音習慣可能影響外貌。"},{"en":"To affect appearance means to influence how someone or something looks.","zh":"影響外貌，指影響某人或某物看起來的樣子。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can affect appearance by making a person look tired.","zh":"睡眠不足可以令人看起來疲倦，從而影響外貌。"},{"en":"If mouth movements are repeated for many years, they may possibly affect facial expression.","zh":"如果口部動作多年反覆出現，它們可能影響面部表情。"},{"en":"The phrase describes influence on visible form.","zh":"這個短語描述對可見形態的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"make someone smile","meaning":"令某人微笑","examples":[{"en":"The mental image used for Scouse makes the learner smile.","zh":"用於利物浦口音的心像令學習者微笑。"},{"en":"To make someone smile means to cause them to form a smile or feel pleased.","zh":"令某人微笑，指使某人露出笑容或感到高興。"},{"en":"A funny classroom example can make students smile and remember the lesson.","zh":"有趣的課堂例子可以令學生微笑並記住課堂。"},{"en":"If a pronunciation image makes learners smile, it changes cheek position and mouth shape.","zh":"如果發音意象令學習者微笑，它會改變臉頰位置和口形。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe either an emotional reaction or a physical facial movement.","zh":"這個短語可以描述情緒反應，也可以描述身體面部動作"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 122 - Pronunciation and physiognomy.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 123":[{"front":"fuelling the future","meaning":"為未來提供燃料","examples":[{"en":"Governments are exploring alternative fuels as a way of fuelling the future.","zh":"政府正在探索替代燃料，作為為未來提供燃料的方法。"},{"en":"Fuelling the future means providing the energy needed for transport, industry, and daily life in the years ahead.","zh":"fuelling the future 指為未來的交通、工業和日常生活提供所需能源。"},{"en":"A city may invest in electric buses and solar power as part of fuelling the future.","zh":"城市可能投資電動巴士和太陽能，作為為未來提供燃料的一部分。"},{"en":"If oil becomes expensive or polluting, countries must find cleaner ways to fuel future growth.","zh":"如果石油變得昂貴或造成污染，各國必須尋找更潔淨方式為未來增長提供能源。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing long-term energy choices.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論長遠能源選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"motor vehicles","meaning":"機動車輛","examples":[{"en":"The world’s motor vehicles produce enormous quantities of carbon dioxide.","zh":"全球機動車輛產生大量二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Motor vehicles are vehicles powered by engines, such as cars, buses, trucks, and motorcycles.","zh":"motor vehicles 是由引擎驅動的車輛，例如汽車、巴士、貨車和電單車。"},{"en":"A busy road full of motor vehicles can create noise, fumes, and traffic jams.","zh":"充滿機動車輛的繁忙道路可以造成噪音、廢氣和交通擠塞。"},{"en":"If the number of motor vehicles rises, fuel use and air pollution may also rise.","zh":"如果機動車輛數量上升，燃料使用和空氣污染也可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to engine-powered road transport.","zh":"這個片語指以引擎推動的道路交通工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"emit carbon dioxide","meaning":"排放二氧化碳","examples":[{"en":"Motor vehicles emit millions of tonnes of carbon dioxide each year.","zh":"機動車輛每年排放數百萬噸二氧化碳。"},{"en":"To emit carbon dioxide means to release CO2 into the air.","zh":"emit carbon dioxide 指把二氧化碳釋放到空氣中。"},{"en":"A factory may emit carbon dioxide when it burns coal for energy.","zh":"工廠燃燒煤炭供能時可能排放二氧化碳。"},{"en":"If vehicles emit less carbon dioxide, their impact on climate may be reduced.","zh":"如果車輛排放較少二氧化碳，其對氣候的影響可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common form of greenhouse gas release.","zh":"這個片語描述一種常見的溫室氣體釋放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"well over","meaning":"遠超過","examples":[{"en":"Vehicles emit well over 900 million metric tonnes of carbon dioxide annually.","zh":"車輛每年排放遠超過九億公噸二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Well over means much more than a stated number or amount.","zh":"well over 指遠多於某個數字或數量。"},{"en":"The school raised well over ten thousand dollars for charity.","zh":"學校為慈善籌得遠超過一萬元。"},{"en":"If emissions are well over the safe level, stronger action may be needed.","zh":"如果排放遠超過安全水平，可能需要更強行動。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the amount is clearly above the number given.","zh":"這個片語強調數量明顯高於所給數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"metric tonnes","meaning":"公噸","examples":[{"en":"Carbon emissions are often measured in metric tonnes.","zh":"碳排放常以公噸量度。"},{"en":"Metric tonnes are units of mass, with one metric tonne equal to 1,000 kilograms.","zh":"metric tonnes 是重量單位，一公噸等於一千公斤。"},{"en":"A large truck may carry several metric tonnes of goods.","zh":"大型貨車可能運載數公噸貨物。"},{"en":"If emissions are measured in metric tonnes, countries can compare pollution levels more clearly.","zh":"如果排放以公噸量度，各國就能更清楚比較污染水平。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reports about weight, trade, and emissions.","zh":"這個片語常見於關於重量、貿易和排放的報告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"traffic-related air pollution","meaning":"與交通有關的空氣污染","examples":[{"en":"Traffic-related air pollution causes serious public-health problems.","zh":"與交通有關的空氣污染造成嚴重公共健康問題。"},{"en":"Traffic-related air pollution is dirty air caused by vehicles, especially exhaust fumes.","zh":"traffic-related air pollution 是由車輛造成的污濁空氣，尤其是廢氣。"},{"en":"Children living near busy roads may breathe more traffic-related air pollution.","zh":"住在繁忙道路附近的兒童可能吸入更多與交通有關的空氣污染。"},{"en":"If traffic pollution increases, hospitals may see more patients with breathing problems.","zh":"如果交通污染增加，醫院可能見到更多有呼吸問題的病人。"},{"en":"This phrase connects road transport with air-quality damage.","zh":"這個片語把道路交通與空氣質素破壞連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"account for deaths","meaning":"導致死亡；佔死亡個案","examples":[{"en":"Traffic-related air pollution is estimated to account for many deaths each year.","zh":"據估計，與交通有關的空氣污染每年導致許多死亡個案。"},{"en":"To account for deaths means to be responsible for causing a number of deaths.","zh":"account for deaths 指要為一定數量的死亡負責。"},{"en":"Smoking can account for many preventable deaths in a population.","zh":"吸煙可以導致人口中許多可預防死亡個案。"},{"en":"If pollution accounts for deaths, reducing it becomes a public-health priority.","zh":"如果污染導致死亡，減少污染就成為公共健康優先事項。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when identifying the cause behind death statistics.","zh":"這個片語用於指出死亡統計背後的成因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be associated with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Air pollution is associated with several serious illnesses.","zh":"空氣污染與幾種嚴重疾病有關。"},{"en":"To be associated with something means to be connected with it, even if the exact cause may need more study.","zh":"be associated with something 指與某事有關，即使確切因果可能仍需更多研究。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep is often associated with poor concentration.","zh":"睡眠不足常與專注力差有關。"},{"en":"If a disease is associated with pollution, doctors and governments may investigate the link.","zh":"如果某疾病與污染有關，醫生和政府可能調查這種關聯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a connection between two things.","zh":"這個片語描述兩件事之間的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"certain forms of leukaemia","meaning":"某些類型的白血病","examples":[{"en":"Traffic pollution has been associated with certain forms of leukaemia.","zh":"交通污染被認為與某些類型的白血病有關。"},{"en":"Certain forms of leukaemia means particular types of blood cancer.","zh":"certain forms of leukaemia 指某些特定類型的血癌。"},{"en":"Doctors classify illnesses into forms so treatment can be chosen more accurately.","zh":"醫生把疾病分成不同類型，以便更準確選擇治療。"},{"en":"If a pollutant is linked to certain forms of leukaemia, public-health experts will study exposure levels.","zh":"如果某污染物與某些類型的白血病有關，公共健康專家會研究暴露水平。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to specific kinds of a serious disease.","zh":"這個片語指嚴重疾病中的特定類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"inflammatory lung diseases","meaning":"炎症性肺病","examples":[{"en":"Air pollution can contribute to inflammatory lung diseases.","zh":"空氣污染可以促成炎症性肺病。"},{"en":"Inflammatory lung diseases are lung conditions involving swelling, irritation, or inflammation in the airways.","zh":"inflammatory lung diseases 是涉及氣道腫脹、刺激或發炎的肺部疾病。"},{"en":"A person with inflammatory lung disease may cough, wheeze, or find breathing difficult.","zh":"有炎症性肺病的人可能咳嗽、喘鳴或呼吸困難。"},{"en":"If polluted air irritates the lungs, inflammation can worsen over time.","zh":"如果受污染空氣刺激肺部，炎症可能隨時間惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes diseases that damage breathing through inflammation.","zh":"這個片語描述透過發炎損害呼吸的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cardiovascular disease","meaning":"心血管疾病","examples":[{"en":"Long-term exposure to pollution may increase the risk of cardiovascular disease.","zh":"長期接觸污染可能增加心血管疾病風險。"},{"en":"Cardiovascular disease refers to diseases of the heart and blood vessels.","zh":"cardiovascular disease 指心臟和血管的疾病。"},{"en":"High blood pressure and heart attacks are connected with cardiovascular health.","zh":"高血壓和心臟病發與心血管健康有關。"},{"en":"If pollution affects the heart and circulation, it may increase long-term health risks.","zh":"如果污染影響心臟和血液循環，它可能增加長期健康風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in medical and public-health writing.","zh":"這個片語常見於醫學和公共健康寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"low-birth-weight babies","meaning":"出生體重偏低的嬰兒","examples":[{"en":"Air pollution has been linked to low-birth-weight babies.","zh":"空氣污染被指與出生體重偏低的嬰兒有關。"},{"en":"Low-birth-weight babies are newborns who weigh less than expected at birth.","zh":"low-birth-weight babies 是出生時體重低於預期的新生兒。"},{"en":"Doctors may monitor low-birth-weight babies more closely after delivery.","zh":"醫生可能在分娩後更密切監察出生體重偏低的嬰兒。"},{"en":"If pregnant women breathe heavy pollution, some research suggests babies may be affected before birth.","zh":"如果孕婦吸入嚴重污染，一些研究指出嬰兒可能在出生前受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a newborn health concern.","zh":"這個片語描述一種新生兒健康問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"male infertility","meaning":"男性不育","examples":[{"en":"Some research has associated air pollution with male infertility.","zh":"一些研究把空氣污染與男性不育聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Male infertility means difficulty for a man to father a child because of reproductive problems.","zh":"male infertility 指男性因生殖問題而難以成為孩子父親。"},{"en":"A doctor may investigate male infertility through medical history and laboratory tests.","zh":"醫生可能透過病歷和實驗室測試調查男性不育。"},{"en":"If pollution affects reproductive health, it may create long-term family and social concerns.","zh":"如果污染影響生殖健康，可能造成長期家庭和社會憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a health problem related to male reproduction.","zh":"這個片語指與男性生殖相關的健康問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"it stands to reason that","meaning":"按道理說；理所當然","examples":[{"en":"It stands to reason that governments should tackle serious air pollution.","zh":"按道理說，政府應處理嚴重空氣污染。"},{"en":"It stands to reason that means it seems logical or obvious that something should be true.","zh":"it stands to reason that 指某事看來合乎邏輯或理所當然。"},{"en":"It stands to reason that students who practise daily usually improve faster.","zh":"按道理說，每天練習的學生通常進步較快。"},{"en":"If a problem causes illness and death, it is logical for governments to address it.","zh":"如果問題造成疾病和死亡，政府處理它是合乎邏輯的。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a conclusion that feels reasonable.","zh":"這個片語引入看來合理的結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tackle air pollution","meaning":"處理空氣污染問題","examples":[{"en":"Governments need effective policies to tackle air pollution.","zh":"政府需要有效政策來處理空氣污染問題。"},{"en":"To tackle air pollution means to deal with it actively and try to reduce it.","zh":"tackle air pollution 指積極處理並嘗試減少空氣污染。"},{"en":"A city can tackle air pollution by improving public transport and limiting dirty vehicles.","zh":"城市可以透過改善公共交通和限制高污染車輛來處理空氣污染。"},{"en":"If pollution is not tackled, health costs and environmental damage may rise.","zh":"如果污染沒有被處理，醫療成本和環境破壞可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct action against polluted air.","zh":"這個片語描述針對污濁空氣的直接行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be high on a government’s list of priorities","meaning":"在政府的優先事項中佔重要位置","examples":[{"en":"Reducing traffic pollution should be high on every government’s list of priorities.","zh":"減少交通污染應在每個政府的優先事項中佔重要位置。"},{"en":"To be high on a government’s list of priorities means to be one of the most important issues for officials to handle.","zh":"be high on a government’s list of priorities 指成為官員最需要處理的重要議題之一。"},{"en":"During a disease outbreak, hospital safety should be high on the government’s list of priorities.","zh":"疫情爆發期間，醫院安全應在政府優先事項中佔重要位置。"},{"en":"If a problem affects millions of people, it should receive urgent policy attention.","zh":"如果問題影響數百萬人，它應得到緊急政策關注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that deserves strong official focus.","zh":"這個片語描述某事值得政府高度重視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in an attempt to","meaning":"為了嘗試……","examples":[{"en":"Governments are developing cleaner fuels in an attempt to reduce emissions.","zh":"政府正在開發更潔淨燃料，為了嘗試減少排放。"},{"en":"In an attempt to means in order to try to do something.","zh":"in an attempt to 指為了嘗試做某事。"},{"en":"A student may rewrite an essay in an attempt to improve the structure.","zh":"學生可能重寫文章，為了嘗試改善結構。"},{"en":"If a policy is introduced in an attempt to solve a problem, its success still needs to be tested.","zh":"如果政策為了解決問題而推出，其成功仍需要測試。"},{"en":"This phrase shows purpose, but not guaranteed success.","zh":"這個片語表示目的，但不保證成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"address a problem","meaning":"處理問題","examples":[{"en":"Many countries are introducing new policies to address the pollution problem.","zh":"許多國家正在推出新政策來處理污染問題。"},{"en":"To address a problem means to deal with it seriously and try to solve it.","zh":"address a problem 指認真處理並嘗試解決問題。"},{"en":"A school may address bullying by creating clear reporting procedures.","zh":"學校可能透過建立清晰舉報程序來處理欺凌問題。"},{"en":"If a problem is ignored, it may become harder and more expensive to fix later.","zh":"如果問題被忽視，日後可能更難和更昂貴去修正。"},{"en":"This phrase describes purposeful action toward a difficulty.","zh":"這個片語描述有目的地處理困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"implement alternative fuel sources","meaning":"推行替代燃料來源","examples":[{"en":"Governments are looking for ways to implement alternative fuel sources.","zh":"政府正在尋找方法推行替代燃料來源。"},{"en":"To implement alternative fuel sources means to put new non-traditional fuels into practical use.","zh":"implement alternative fuel sources 指把新的非傳統燃料投入實際使用。"},{"en":"A bus company may implement alternative fuel sources by buying electric or ethanol-compatible buses.","zh":"巴士公司可能透過購買電動或適合乙醇燃料的巴士來推行替代燃料來源。"},{"en":"If alternative fuels are implemented poorly, drivers may face high costs or limited refuelling options.","zh":"如果替代燃料推行不善，司機可能面對高成本或有限加油選項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes turning a fuel idea into a real system.","zh":"這個片語描述把燃料想法變成實際系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the most widely accepted way","meaning":"最廣為接受的方法","examples":[{"en":"The most widely accepted way is to replace crude oil with renewable fuel.","zh":"最廣為接受的方法是以可再生燃料取代原油。"},{"en":"The most widely accepted way means the method most people or experts agree is suitable.","zh":"most widely accepted way 指最多人或專家同意適合的方法。"},{"en":"Regular practice is the most widely accepted way to improve speaking confidence.","zh":"定期練習是改善口語信心最廣為接受的方法。"},{"en":"If one solution is widely accepted, governments may choose it before trying riskier ideas.","zh":"如果某解決方案廣為接受，政府可能先選它，而不是嘗試風險較高的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the approach with broad support.","zh":"這個片語突出得到廣泛支持的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"replace something with","meaning":"以……取代……","examples":[{"en":"Some governments want to replace crude oil with cleaner alternatives.","zh":"一些政府希望以較潔淨替代品取代原油。"},{"en":"To replace something with another thing means to remove the old one and use the new one instead.","zh":"replace something with another thing 指移除舊事物並改用新事物。"},{"en":"A school may replace paper notices with online messages.","zh":"學校可能以網上訊息取代紙本通告。"},{"en":"If petrol is replaced with cleaner fuel, vehicle emissions may fall.","zh":"如果汽油被較潔淨燃料取代，車輛排放可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly shows substitution.","zh":"這個片語清楚表示替換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"crude oil","meaning":"原油","examples":[{"en":"Most conventional vehicle fuels are produced from crude oil.","zh":"大多數傳統車用燃料由原油製成。"},{"en":"Crude oil is natural oil taken from underground before it is refined into fuels and chemicals.","zh":"crude oil 是從地下開採、未經精煉成燃料和化學品的天然石油。"},{"en":"Petrol, diesel, and many plastics are made from crude oil.","zh":"汽油、柴油和許多塑膠都由原油製成。"},{"en":"If crude oil prices rise, transport and production costs may increase.","zh":"如果原油價格上升，交通和生產成本可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an important fossil-fuel raw material.","zh":"這個片語指重要的化石燃料原材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"vehicles run on","meaning":"車輛以……作燃料","examples":[{"en":"Most vehicles currently run on petrol or diesel.","zh":"大多數車輛目前以汽油或柴油作燃料。"},{"en":"Vehicles run on a fuel means they use that fuel to operate.","zh":"vehicles run on a fuel 指車輛使用某種燃料運作。"},{"en":"Some buses run on electricity instead of diesel.","zh":"一些巴士以電力而非柴油行駛。"},{"en":"If vehicles run on cleaner fuels, cities may have better air quality.","zh":"如果車輛以較潔淨燃料行駛，城市空氣質素可能更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what powers a vehicle.","zh":"這個片語描述車輛由甚麼提供動力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"renewable alternatives","meaning":"可再生替代品","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol is often presented as a renewable alternative to petrol.","zh":"乙醇常被呈現為汽油的可再生替代品。"},{"en":"Renewable alternatives are replacement options made from sources that can be naturally replenished.","zh":"renewable alternatives 是由可自然補充的來源製成的替代選項。"},{"en":"Solar power is a renewable alternative to electricity generated from coal.","zh":"太陽能是由煤炭發電的可再生替代品。"},{"en":"If a fuel comes from crops that can be grown again, it may be described as renewable.","zh":"如果燃料來自可以再次種植的作物，它可被描述為可再生。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts replaceable energy sources with fossil fuels.","zh":"這個片語把可補充能源與化石燃料作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"environmentally friendly","meaning":"環保的","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol is promoted as a more environmentally friendly fuel.","zh":"乙醇被宣傳為較環保的燃料。"},{"en":"Environmentally friendly means causing less harm to nature, air, water, or climate.","zh":"environmentally friendly 指對自然、空氣、水或氣候造成較少傷害。"},{"en":"A reusable bottle is more environmentally friendly than a single-use plastic bottle.","zh":"可重用水樽比一次性塑膠樽更環保。"},{"en":"If a product is truly environmentally friendly, its production and use should both cause less damage.","zh":"如果產品真正環保，其生產和使用都應造成較少破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something designed to reduce environmental harm.","zh":"這個片語描述旨在減少環境傷害的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a serious contender","meaning":"有力競爭者；可認真考慮的方案","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol is a serious contender in the search for cleaner transport fuels.","zh":"在尋找更潔淨運輸燃料的過程中，乙醇是一個有力競爭者。"},{"en":"A serious contender is an option that has a real chance of being chosen or succeeding.","zh":"serious contender 是有真正機會被選中或成功的選項。"},{"en":"A small café can become a serious contender if its food and service are excellent.","zh":"如果食物和服務出色，小咖啡店可以成為有力競爭者。"},{"en":"If a fuel is cheaper, cleaner, and practical, it may become a serious contender.","zh":"如果燃料更便宜、更潔淨且實用，它可能成為可認真考慮的方案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something worth considering seriously.","zh":"這個片語描述值得認真考慮的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"put forward as","meaning":"被提出作為……","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol has been put forward as a solution to vehicle pollution.","zh":"乙醇被提出作為車輛污染的解決方案。"},{"en":"To be put forward as something means to be proposed or suggested as that thing.","zh":"be put forward as something 指被建議或提出為某事物。"},{"en":"Online lessons were put forward as a way to help students during school closures.","zh":"網上課堂被提出作為停課期間幫助學生的方法。"},{"en":"If an idea is put forward, people still need to test whether it works.","zh":"如果想法被提出，人們仍需要測試它是否有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a proposal being presented.","zh":"這個片語描述建議被呈現出來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a solution to","meaning":"……的解決方案","examples":[{"en":"Alternative fuel may provide a solution to the pollution problem.","zh":"替代燃料可能為污染問題提供解決方案。"},{"en":"A solution to a problem is a way to reduce or fix it.","zh":"solution to a problem 是減少或解決問題的方法。"},{"en":"More buses may be a solution to traffic congestion near schools.","zh":"增加巴士可能是學校附近交通擠塞的解決方案。"},{"en":"If a solution is too expensive, it may be difficult to use widely.","zh":"如果解決方案太昂貴，就可能難以廣泛使用。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a method with the problem it aims to solve.","zh":"這個片語把方法與它旨在解決的問題連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a type of alcohol","meaning":"一種酒精","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol is a type of alcohol produced from plant material.","zh":"乙醇是一種由植物原料製成的酒精。"},{"en":"A type of alcohol means one chemical form within the alcohol family.","zh":"a type of alcohol 指酒精類化學物中的一種形式。"},{"en":"The alcohol in hand sanitiser and the alcohol in drinks are used for very different purposes.","zh":"消毒搓手液中的酒精和飲品中的酒精用途非常不同。"},{"en":"If ethanol is used as fuel, it is treated as an energy source rather than a drink.","zh":"如果乙醇用作燃料，它會被視為能源來源，而不是飲品。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a simple scientific classification.","zh":"這個片語給出簡單科學分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ferment plant material","meaning":"發酵植物原料","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers ferment plant material to produce ethanol.","zh":"製造商發酵植物原料來生產乙醇。"},{"en":"To ferment plant material means to use microorganisms to break down plant sugars and produce alcohol.","zh":"ferment plant material 指利用微生物分解植物糖分並產生酒精。"},{"en":"People ferment grapes to make wine and ferment grains to make beer.","zh":"人們發酵葡萄來製酒，發酵穀物來製啤酒。"},{"en":"If crops contain sugar or starch, they can often be fermented into ethanol.","zh":"如果作物含有糖或澱粉，通常可以發酵成乙醇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the biological process behind ethanol production.","zh":"這個片語描述乙醇生產背後的生物過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"organic matter","meaning":"有機物質","examples":[{"en":"Water is mixed with organic matter from plants.","zh":"水會與來自植物的有機物質混合。"},{"en":"Organic matter is material that comes from living or once-living things, such as plants or animals.","zh":"organic matter 是來自活生物或曾經活着的生物的物質，例如植物或動物。"},{"en":"Fallen leaves become organic matter that enriches garden soil.","zh":"落葉會變成有機物質，令花園土壤更肥沃。"},{"en":"If organic matter breaks down, it can release nutrients or produce gases.","zh":"如果有機物質分解，它可以釋放養分或產生氣體。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to natural biological material.","zh":"這個片語指天然生物物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"corn, sorghum, sugar cane and wood","meaning":"玉米、高粱、甘蔗和木材","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol can be produced from corn, sorghum, sugar cane and wood.","zh":"乙醇可以由玉米、高粱、甘蔗和木材製成。"},{"en":"Corn, sorghum, sugar cane and wood are plant materials that can provide sugars or fibres for ethanol production.","zh":"corn, sorghum, sugar cane and wood 是可以為乙醇生產提供糖分或纖維的植物原料。"},{"en":"Farmers may grow corn and sugar cane for both food and fuel markets.","zh":"農民可能種植玉米和甘蔗，以供食品和燃料市場使用。"},{"en":"If many crops are used for fuel, food prices and land use may be affected.","zh":"如果許多作物被用作燃料，食品價格和土地使用可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase lists common raw materials for making ethanol.","zh":"這個片語列出製造乙醇的常見原材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be mixed together","meaning":"混合在一起","examples":[{"en":"Water and plant material are mixed together before fermentation.","zh":"水和植物原料在發酵前會混合在一起。"},{"en":"To be mixed together means to be combined into one mixture.","zh":"be mixed together 指被結合成一種混合物。"},{"en":"Flour, eggs, and milk are mixed together before making pancakes.","zh":"製作班戟前，麵粉、雞蛋和牛奶會混合在一起。"},{"en":"If ingredients are not mixed together evenly, the final product may be poor.","zh":"如果材料沒有均勻混合在一起，最終產品可能質素差。"},{"en":"This phrase describes combining separate materials.","zh":"這個片語描述把分開的材料結合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"after fermentation","meaning":"發酵後","examples":[{"en":"Three separate layers remain after fermentation.","zh":"發酵後會留下三個分開的層。"},{"en":"After fermentation means after microorganisms have changed sugars into alcohol or other products.","zh":"after fermentation 指微生物把糖分轉化為酒精或其他產品之後。"},{"en":"After fermentation, grape juice becomes wine.","zh":"發酵後，葡萄汁會變成葡萄酒。"},{"en":"If fermentation is complete, the liquid may contain alcohol and leftover solids.","zh":"如果發酵完成，液體可能含有酒精和剩餘固體。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the stage following a chemical or biological process.","zh":"這個片語標示化學或生物過程之後的階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"small particles of grain","meaning":"細小穀物顆粒","examples":[{"en":"The first layer contains water, alcohol and small particles of grain.","zh":"第一層含有水、酒精和細小穀物顆粒。"},{"en":"Small particles of grain are tiny pieces of cereal crops left in a mixture.","zh":"small particles of grain 是混合物中留下的細小穀類碎片。"},{"en":"After blending oats with water, small particles of grain may remain in the drink.","zh":"把燕麥和水攪拌後，飲品中可能留下細小穀物顆粒。"},{"en":"If particles are not removed, the liquid may become thick or cloudy.","zh":"如果顆粒沒有被移除，液體可能變得濃稠或混濁。"},{"en":"This phrase describes tiny solid pieces from grain.","zh":"這個片語描述來自穀物的細小固體碎片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take on a syrup-like consistency","meaning":"呈糖漿狀","examples":[{"en":"The first layer takes on a syrup-like consistency.","zh":"第一層呈糖漿狀。"},{"en":"To take on a syrup-like consistency means to become thick, sticky, and liquid like syrup.","zh":"take on a syrup-like consistency 指變得像糖漿一樣濃稠、黏滑且流動。"},{"en":"If fruit juice is boiled with sugar, it may take on a syrup-like consistency.","zh":"如果果汁與糖一起煮，它可能呈糖漿狀。"},{"en":"A thick mixture can be harder to pour or separate from other layers.","zh":"濃稠混合物可能較難倒出或與其他層分離。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change in texture.","zh":"這個片語描述質感變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the remaining grain","meaning":"剩餘穀物","examples":[{"en":"The second layer consists mainly of the remaining grain.","zh":"第二層主要由剩餘穀物組成。"},{"en":"The remaining grain means the grain left after part of it has been processed or removed.","zh":"remaining grain 指一部分經處理或移除後留下的穀物。"},{"en":"After making oat milk, the remaining grain can sometimes be used in baking.","zh":"製作燕麥奶後，剩餘穀物有時可用於烘焙。"},{"en":"If remaining grain still contains nutrients, it may become animal feed.","zh":"如果剩餘穀物仍含有營養，它可能成為動物飼料。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to leftover grain material.","zh":"這個片語指剩下的穀物材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"dry matter","meaning":"乾物質","examples":[{"en":"The remaining grain contains about 17% dry matter.","zh":"剩餘穀物含有約17%乾物質。"},{"en":"Dry matter is the solid material left after water is removed.","zh":"dry matter 是移除水分後留下的固體物質。"},{"en":"Farmers measure dry matter in animal feed to know how much real food it contains.","zh":"農民量度動物飼料中的乾物質，以知道它含有多少實際食物。"},{"en":"If a crop has high dry matter, it may provide more usable material after drying.","zh":"如果作物乾物質高，乾燥後可能提供更多可用材料。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when comparing solid content with water content.","zh":"這個片語用於比較固體含量和水分含量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the actual ethanol","meaning":"真正的乙醇","examples":[{"en":"The third layer contains the actual ethanol.","zh":"第三層含有真正的乙醇。"},{"en":"The actual ethanol means the real alcohol product being produced, not the waste or leftover material.","zh":"actual ethanol 指正在生產的真正酒精產品，而不是廢料或剩餘物。"},{"en":"In a factory process, the useful product must be separated from other layers.","zh":"在工廠流程中，有用產品必須與其他層分開。"},{"en":"If the ethanol layer is collected carefully, it can be refined and sold as fuel.","zh":"如果乙醇層被仔細收集，它可以被精煉並作燃料出售。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the main desired product.","zh":"這個片語指出主要目標產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"colourless, volatile and flammable","meaning":"無色、易揮發且易燃的","examples":[{"en":"Pure ethanol is a colourless, volatile and flammable liquid.","zh":"純乙醇是一種無色、易揮發且易燃的液體。"},{"en":"Colourless, volatile and flammable means it has no colour, evaporates easily, and can catch fire.","zh":"colourless, volatile and flammable 指沒有顏色、容易蒸發並可以着火。"},{"en":"Laboratory alcohol must be handled carefully because it is volatile and flammable.","zh":"實驗室酒精必須小心處理，因為它易揮發且易燃。"},{"en":"If a liquid is flammable, it should be kept away from flames and heat.","zh":"如果液體易燃，就應遠離火焰和高溫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes important chemical properties.","zh":"這個片語描述重要化學特性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be sold commercially","meaning":"作商業出售","examples":[{"en":"Only the ethanol layer is sold commercially.","zh":"只有乙醇層會作商業出售。"},{"en":"To be sold commercially means to be sold as a product in the market.","zh":"be sold commercially 指作為產品在市場出售。"},{"en":"A home recipe becomes sold commercially when a company packages and sells it in shops.","zh":"當公司把家庭食譜包裝並在商店出售，它就變成作商業出售。"},{"en":"If a material has no market value, it may not be sold commercially.","zh":"如果材料沒有市場價值，它可能不會作商業出售。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sale for business purposes.","zh":"這個片語描述以商業用途出售。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"account for one-third of","meaning":"佔……的三分之一","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol accounts for exactly one-third of the dry matter used in production.","zh":"乙醇正好佔生產中所用乾物質的三分之一。"},{"en":"To account for one-third of something means to make up one out of three equal parts of it.","zh":"account for one-third of something 指構成某物三等份中的一份。"},{"en":"Transport may account for one-third of a family’s monthly spending.","zh":"交通可能佔家庭每月開支的三分之一。"},{"en":"If one ingredient accounts for a large share, changes in its price can affect the whole product.","zh":"如果某材料佔很大比例，其價格變化可以影響整個產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes proportion or share.","zh":"這個片語描述比例或份額。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fuel for transportation","meaning":"運輸燃料","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol can be used as a fuel for transportation.","zh":"乙醇可以用作運輸燃料。"},{"en":"Fuel for transportation is energy used to move vehicles such as cars, buses, trucks, or planes.","zh":"fuel for transportation 是用來推動汽車、巴士、貨車或飛機等車輛的能源。"},{"en":"Petrol, diesel, electricity, and ethanol can all serve as fuels for transport.","zh":"汽油、柴油、電力和乙醇都可以作為運輸燃料。"},{"en":"If cleaner fuels are used for transportation, traffic pollution may fall.","zh":"如果運輸使用較潔淨燃料，交通污染可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase connects energy sources with moving people and goods.","zh":"這個片語把能源來源與運送人和貨物連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a blend of","meaning":"……的混合物","examples":[{"en":"E10 is a blend of ethanol and unleaded petrol.","zh":"E10 是乙醇和無鉛汽油的混合物。"},{"en":"A blend of two things is a mixture that combines them together.","zh":"blend of two things 是把兩種東西結合起來的混合物。"},{"en":"A smoothie may be a blend of fruit, milk, and yoghurt.","zh":"沙冰可以是水果、牛奶和乳酪的混合物。"},{"en":"If a fuel is a blend, its performance depends on the proportion of each ingredient.","zh":"如果燃料是混合物，其表現取決於每種成分的比例。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mixed product.","zh":"這個片語描述混合產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"10% ethanol with 90% unleaded fuel","meaning":"一成乙醇與九成無鉛燃料的混合物","examples":[{"en":"E10 contains 10% ethanol mixed with 90% unleaded fuel.","zh":"E10 含有一成乙醇與九成無鉛燃料的混合物。"},{"en":"10% ethanol with 90% unleaded fuel means one part ethanol and nine parts unleaded petrol in every ten parts of fuel.","zh":"10% ethanol with 90% unleaded fuel 指每十份燃料中有一份乙醇和九份無鉛汽油。"},{"en":"A driver using E10 is mostly using petrol, with a small ethanol component.","zh":"使用 E10 的司機主要仍是在用汽油，只是含有少量乙醇成分。"},{"en":"If the ethanol percentage rises, the fuel may affect engines differently.","zh":"如果乙醇比例上升，燃料可能對引擎有不同影響。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the exact mixture in E10 fuel.","zh":"這個片語解釋 E10 燃料的確切混合比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"unleaded fuel","meaning":"無鉛燃料","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol is commonly blended with unleaded fuel.","zh":"乙醇常與無鉛燃料混合。"},{"en":"Unleaded fuel is petrol that does not contain lead additives.","zh":"unleaded fuel 是不含鉛添加劑的汽油。"},{"en":"Most modern cars use unleaded fuel rather than older leaded petrol.","zh":"大多數現代汽車使用無鉛燃料，而不是舊式含鉛汽油。"},{"en":"If ethanol is mixed with unleaded fuel, the result is an ethanol blend such as E10.","zh":"如果乙醇與無鉛燃料混合，結果就是 E10 等乙醇混合燃料。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a standard type of petrol.","zh":"這個片語指一種標準汽油。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a component of","meaning":"……的組成部分","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol can be used as a component of reformulated gasoline.","zh":"乙醇可以用作重新配方汽油的組成部分。"},{"en":"A component of something is one part or ingredient of a larger whole.","zh":"component of something 是較大整體中的一部分或成分。"},{"en":"Grammar is one component of strong writing, but ideas and organisation matter too.","zh":"文法是優秀寫作的一個組成部分，但觀點和組織也重要。"},{"en":"If ethanol is a fuel component, it changes the fuel’s properties and emissions.","zh":"如果乙醇是燃料組成部分，它會改變燃料特性和排放。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one part within a mixture or system.","zh":"這個片語描述混合物或系統中的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"reformulated gasoline","meaning":"重新配方汽油","examples":[{"en":"Reformulated gasoline is designed to produce fewer harmful emissions.","zh":"重新配方汽油旨在產生較少有害排放。"},{"en":"Reformulated gasoline is petrol whose composition has been changed to burn more cleanly.","zh":"reformulated gasoline 是成分經改變、燃燒較潔淨的汽油。"},{"en":"A city with severe smog may encourage drivers to use reformulated gasoline.","zh":"嚴重霧霾城市可能鼓勵司機使用重新配方汽油。"},{"en":"If fuel is reformulated, it may reduce some pollutants from vehicle exhaust.","zh":"如果燃料重新配方，它可能減少車輛廢氣中的某些污染物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to modified petrol made for cleaner performance.","zh":"這個片語指為更潔淨表現而改良的汽油。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a primary fuel","meaning":"主要燃料","examples":[{"en":"E-85 uses ethanol as its primary fuel.","zh":"E-85 使用乙醇作為主要燃料。"},{"en":"A primary fuel is the main fuel used to power a vehicle or machine.","zh":"primary fuel 是用來推動車輛或機器的主要燃料。"},{"en":"Diesel is the primary fuel for many long-distance trucks.","zh":"柴油是許多長途貨車的主要燃料。"},{"en":"If ethanol is the primary fuel, the engine must be designed or adjusted to use it.","zh":"如果乙醇是主要燃料，引擎必須被設計或調校成可使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main energy source.","zh":"這個片語指出主要能源來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be blended with","meaning":"與……混合","examples":[{"en":"In E-85, ethanol is blended with a smaller amount of unleaded fuel.","zh":"在 E-85 中，乙醇與較少量無鉛燃料混合。"},{"en":"To be blended with something means to be mixed together with it.","zh":"be blended with something 指與某物混合在一起。"},{"en":"Fruit juice can be blended with yoghurt to make a smoothie.","zh":"果汁可以與乳酪混合製作沙冰。"},{"en":"If ethanol is blended with petrol, the fuel’s cost, energy content, and emissions may change.","zh":"如果乙醇與汽油混合，燃料成本、能量含量和排放可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes combining substances into one mixture.","zh":"這個片語描述把物質結合成一種混合物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lamp fuel","meaning":"燈用燃料","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol was first used as lamp fuel in the United States.","zh":"乙醇在美國最初被用作燈用燃料。"},{"en":"Lamp fuel is fuel burned to produce light in lamps.","zh":"lamp fuel 是在燈中燃燒以產生光的燃料。"},{"en":"Before electric lights, many homes used lamp fuel at night.","zh":"在電燈出現前，許多家庭晚上使用燈用燃料。"},{"en":"If a liquid burns cleanly, it may be useful as lamp fuel.","zh":"如果液體燃燒潔淨，它可能適合作燈用燃料。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to fuel used for lighting rather than transport.","zh":"這個片語指用於照明而非交通的燃料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"later on","meaning":"後來","examples":[{"en":"Later on, ethanol was introduced as a vehicle fuel.","zh":"後來，乙醇被引入作車用燃料。"},{"en":"Later on means at a later time after something else has happened.","zh":"later on 指在某事發生之後的較後時間。"},{"en":"A student may learn basic grammar first and study essay style later on.","zh":"學生可能先學基本文法，後來再學文章風格。"},{"en":"If a material is first used for one purpose, it may later be adapted for another.","zh":"如果材料最初用於一種用途，後來可能被改作另一用途。"},{"en":"This phrase shows time sequence.","zh":"這個片語顯示時間先後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"due to skyrocketing oil prices","meaning":"由於油價飆升","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol became more attractive due to skyrocketing oil prices.","zh":"由於油價飆升，乙醇變得更具吸引力。"},{"en":"Due to skyrocketing oil prices means because oil prices were rising extremely fast.","zh":"due to skyrocketing oil prices 指因為油價極快速上升。"},{"en":"Families may use public transport more due to skyrocketing petrol prices.","zh":"由於汽油價格飆升，家庭可能更多使用公共交通。"},{"en":"If oil prices rise sharply, alternative fuels may become more competitive.","zh":"如果油價急升，替代燃料可能變得更有競爭力。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how sudden cost increases create pressure for change.","zh":"這個片語解釋成本突然上升如何造成改變壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fuel extender","meaning":"延長燃料供應的添加物","examples":[{"en":"E10 was produced as a fuel extender during the oil crisis.","zh":"石油危機期間，E10 被製成延長燃料供應的添加物。"},{"en":"A fuel extender is something added to fuel so the main fuel supply lasts longer.","zh":"fuel extender 是加入燃料中，讓主要燃料供應維持更久的物質。"},{"en":"A bakery may mix cheaper grains into flour as an extender when wheat is expensive.","zh":"當小麥昂貴時，麵包店可能把較便宜穀物混入麵粉作延伸材料。"},{"en":"If petrol is scarce, adding ethanol can stretch the available petrol supply.","zh":"如果汽油短缺，加入乙醇可以延長可用汽油供應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an additive used to make fuel go further.","zh":"這個片語描述用來令燃料更耐用的添加物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ethanol-blended fuels","meaning":"乙醇混合燃料","examples":[{"en":"Brazil has used ethanol-blended fuels for many years.","zh":"巴西多年來一直使用乙醇混合燃料。"},{"en":"Ethanol-blended fuels are fuels made by mixing ethanol with petrol or another conventional fuel.","zh":"ethanol-blended fuels 是把乙醇與汽油或另一種傳統燃料混合而成的燃料。"},{"en":"A driver may use ethanol-blended fuel if their car is designed for it.","zh":"如果汽車設計上適合，司機可以使用乙醇混合燃料。"},{"en":"If ethanol-blended fuels are widely available, consumers may depend less on pure petrol.","zh":"如果乙醇混合燃料廣泛供應，消費者可能較少依賴純汽油。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fuel mixtures containing ethanol.","zh":"這個片語描述含乙醇的燃料混合物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"prompt a government mandate","meaning":"促使政府頒布命令","examples":[{"en":"High oil prices prompted a government mandate in Brazil.","zh":"高油價促使巴西政府頒布命令。"},{"en":"To prompt a government mandate means to cause the government to issue an official requirement.","zh":"prompt a government mandate 指促使政府發布官方強制要求。"},{"en":"A serious safety problem may prompt a government mandate for seat belts on buses.","zh":"嚴重安全問題可能促使政府頒布巴士安全帶命令。"},{"en":"If market pressure becomes strong, governments may create compulsory rules.","zh":"如果市場壓力變得強烈，政府可能制定強制規則。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a problem with an official order.","zh":"這個片語把問題與官方命令連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"government mandate","meaning":"政府法令；強制規定","examples":[{"en":"A government mandate required the production of ethanol-powered vehicles.","zh":"一項政府法令要求生產乙醇動力車輛。"},{"en":"A government mandate is an official order or requirement made by the government.","zh":"government mandate 是政府作出的官方命令或要求。"},{"en":"A government mandate may require schools to report serious accidents.","zh":"政府法令可能要求學校報告嚴重意外。"},{"en":"If a mandate is introduced, companies may have to change what they produce.","zh":"如果強制規定推出，公司可能必須改變生產內容。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a compulsory government rule.","zh":"這個片語描述政府強制規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be fuelled by","meaning":"以……作燃料","examples":[{"en":"Some Brazilian vehicles can be fuelled by pure ethanol.","zh":"一些巴西車輛可以以純乙醇作燃料。"},{"en":"To be fuelled by something means to use it as the energy source for operation.","zh":"be fuelled by something 指使用某物作為運作能源。"},{"en":"A bus can be fuelled by diesel, electricity, or hydrogen.","zh":"巴士可以以柴油、電力或氫氣作燃料。"},{"en":"If a vehicle is fuelled by ethanol, petrol use may be reduced.","zh":"如果車輛以乙醇作燃料，汽油使用可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what powers a machine or vehicle.","zh":"這個片語描述機器或車輛由甚麼提供動力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pure ethanol","meaning":"純乙醇","examples":[{"en":"Brazil introduced vehicles capable of running on pure ethanol.","zh":"巴西引入能以純乙醇行駛的車輛。"},{"en":"Pure ethanol means ethanol that is not mixed with petrol or other fuels.","zh":"pure ethanol 指沒有與汽油或其他燃料混合的乙醇。"},{"en":"A laboratory may use pure ethanol for cleaning or experiments, but it must be handled carefully.","zh":"實驗室可能使用純乙醇清潔或做實驗，但必須小心處理。"},{"en":"If a vehicle uses pure ethanol, its engine must be compatible with that fuel.","zh":"如果車輛使用純乙醇，其引擎必須與該燃料相容。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ethanol without major fuel blending.","zh":"這個片語描述沒有大量混合其他燃料的乙醇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ethanol-powered vehicles","meaning":"乙醇動力車輛","examples":[{"en":"Millions of ethanol-powered vehicles are used in Brazil.","zh":"巴西使用數以百萬計乙醇動力車輛。"},{"en":"Ethanol-powered vehicles are vehicles designed to run partly or entirely on ethanol fuel.","zh":"ethanol-powered vehicles 是設計成部分或完全使用乙醇燃料行駛的車輛。"},{"en":"A government fleet may buy ethanol-powered vehicles to reduce petrol use.","zh":"政府車隊可能購買乙醇動力車輛以減少汽油使用。"},{"en":"If ethanol-powered vehicles become common, fuel stations must supply suitable fuel.","zh":"如果乙醇動力車輛變得普遍，加油站必須供應合適燃料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes vehicles using ethanol as an energy source.","zh":"這個片語描述使用乙醇作能源的車輛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"passenger-carrying vehicles","meaning":"載客車輛","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol-powered cars account for a large share of passenger-carrying vehicles.","zh":"乙醇動力汽車佔載客車輛很大比例。"},{"en":"Passenger-carrying vehicles are vehicles used to transport people rather than goods.","zh":"passenger-carrying vehicles 是用來運載乘客而不是貨物的車輛。"},{"en":"Buses, taxis, minibuses, and private cars can be passenger-carrying vehicles.","zh":"巴士、的士、小巴和私家車都可以是載客車輛。"},{"en":"If many passenger vehicles use cleaner fuel, urban air pollution may fall.","zh":"如果許多載客車輛使用較潔淨燃料，城市空氣污染可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase distinguishes people transport from freight transport.","zh":"這個片語把載人交通與貨運交通區分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"consume annually","meaning":"每年消耗","examples":[{"en":"Brazilian vehicles consume billions of gallons of ethanol annually.","zh":"巴西車輛每年消耗數十億加侖乙醇。"},{"en":"To consume annually means to use a certain amount each year.","zh":"consume annually 指每年使用某個數量。"},{"en":"A school may consume thousands of sheets of paper annually.","zh":"學校每年可能消耗數千張紙。"},{"en":"If vehicles consume more ethanol annually, demand for ethanol production rises.","zh":"如果車輛每年消耗更多乙醇，對乙醇生產的需求會上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes yearly use.","zh":"這個片語描述年度使用量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the largest ethanol fuel market","meaning":"最大的乙醇燃料市場","examples":[{"en":"Brazil has one of the largest transportation ethanol fuel markets in the world.","zh":"巴西擁有世界上最大的運輸乙醇燃料市場之一。"},{"en":"The largest ethanol fuel market means a place where ethanol fuel is bought and used on a very large scale.","zh":"largest ethanol fuel market 指大量購買和使用乙醇燃料的地方。"},{"en":"A country with many ethanol cars and fuel stations may have a large ethanol market.","zh":"擁有許多乙醇車和加油站的國家可能有大型乙醇市場。"},{"en":"If a market is large, producers have more incentive to invest in supply.","zh":"如果市場很大，生產商會有更多誘因投資供應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the size of ethanol use and sales.","zh":"這個片語描述乙醇使用和銷售的規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be made from a variety of","meaning":"由多種……製成","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol is made from a variety of plant substances.","zh":"乙醇由多種植物原料製成。"},{"en":"To be made from a variety of things means to be produced using many different materials.","zh":"be made from a variety of things 指使用許多不同材料製造。"},{"en":"A smoothie can be made from a variety of fruits.","zh":"沙冰可以由多種水果製成。"},{"en":"If ethanol can be made from many crops, producers have more flexibility.","zh":"如果乙醇可以由許多作物製成，生產商會有更大彈性。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights multiple possible raw materials.","zh":"這個片語突出多種可能原材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"plant substances","meaning":"植物原料","examples":[{"en":"Many different plant substances can be fermented into ethanol.","zh":"許多不同植物原料可以發酵成乙醇。"},{"en":"Plant substances are materials that come from plants, such as grains, stalks, leaves, or wood.","zh":"plant substances 是來自植物的材料，例如穀物、莖、葉或木材。"},{"en":"Farmers may sell plant substances for food, animal feed, or fuel production.","zh":"農民可能出售植物原料，用作食物、動物飼料或燃料生產。"},{"en":"If plant substances contain sugar or starch, they may be useful for fermentation.","zh":"如果植物原料含有糖或澱粉，就可能適合發酵。"},{"en":"This phrase refers broadly to plant-based raw materials.","zh":"這個片語泛指以植物為基礎的原材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"increase the monetary value of","meaning":"提高……的金錢價值","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol production can increase the monetary value of feed grains.","zh":"乙醇生產可以提高飼料穀物的金錢價值。"},{"en":"To increase the monetary value of something means to make it worth more money.","zh":"increase the monetary value of something 指令某物更值錢。"},{"en":"Good packaging can increase the monetary value of handmade products.","zh":"良好包裝可以提高手工產品的金錢價值。"},{"en":"If crops can be sold for fuel as well as food, their market value may rise.","zh":"如果作物除了作食物外也可作燃料出售，其市場價值可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes raising financial worth.","zh":"這個片語描述提升金錢價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"feed grains","meaning":"飼料穀物","examples":[{"en":"Corn and other feed grains can be used to make ethanol.","zh":"玉米和其他飼料穀物可用來製造乙醇。"},{"en":"Feed grains are grains grown mainly to feed animals, such as corn or sorghum.","zh":"feed grains 是主要用作動物飼料的穀物，例如玉米或高粱。"},{"en":"Farmers may sell feed grains to livestock farms.","zh":"農民可能把飼料穀物賣給畜牧場。"},{"en":"If feed grains are also used for fuel, their price may change.","zh":"如果飼料穀物也用作燃料，其價格可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to grain crops used in animal feed and sometimes fuel production.","zh":"這個片語指用於動物飼料、有時也用於燃料生產的穀物作物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be grown by farmers","meaning":"由農民種植","examples":[{"en":"The crops used for ethanol are grown by farmers.","zh":"用於乙醇的作物由農民種植。"},{"en":"To be grown by farmers means to be planted, cared for, and harvested by people working in agriculture.","zh":"be grown by farmers 指由從事農業的人種植、照料和收割。"},{"en":"Vegetables sold in markets are grown by farmers before reaching consumers.","zh":"市場出售的蔬菜在到達消費者前由農民種植。"},{"en":"If ethanol demand rises, farmers may grow more suitable crops.","zh":"如果乙醇需求上升，農民可能種植更多合適作物。"},{"en":"This phrase connects raw materials with agricultural production.","zh":"這個片語把原材料與農業生產連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ethanol-consuming nation","meaning":"乙醇消耗國","examples":[{"en":"The United States is a major ethanol-consuming nation.","zh":"美國是一個主要乙醇消耗國。"},{"en":"An ethanol-consuming nation is a country that uses large amounts of ethanol fuel.","zh":"ethanol-consuming nation 是大量使用乙醇燃料的國家。"},{"en":"A country with many ethanol fuel stations may become an ethanol-consuming nation.","zh":"擁有許多乙醇加油站的國家可能成為乙醇消耗國。"},{"en":"If a nation consumes more ethanol, it needs stable production or imports.","zh":"如果國家消耗更多乙醇，就需要穩定生產或進口。"},{"en":"This phrase describes national fuel use.","zh":"這個片語描述國家層面的燃料使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"add to the farm economy","meaning":"為農業經濟帶來收益","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol production adds billions of dollars to the farm economy.","zh":"乙醇生產為農業經濟帶來數十億美元收益。"},{"en":"To add to the farm economy means to bring extra income or business to agriculture.","zh":"add to the farm economy 指為農業帶來額外收入或商業活動。"},{"en":"A farmers’ market can add to the farm economy by helping growers sell directly to customers.","zh":"農墟可以幫助種植者直接向顧客銷售，從而為農業經濟帶來收益。"},{"en":"If crops are used for fuel, farmers may gain a new source of income.","zh":"如果作物用於燃料，農民可能獲得新收入來源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes economic benefit for agricultural communities.","zh":"這個片語描述對農業社群的經濟好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a bushel of corn","meaning":"一蒲式耳玉米","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol production can increase the value of a bushel of corn.","zh":"乙醇生產可以提高一蒲式耳玉米的價值。"},{"en":"A bushel of corn is a traditional unit used to measure an amount of corn.","zh":"bushel of corn 是用來量度玉米數量的傳統單位。"},{"en":"Farmers may sell corn by the bushel in agricultural markets.","zh":"農民可能在農產品市場按蒲式耳出售玉米。"},{"en":"If demand for ethanol rises, the price of a bushel of corn may increase.","zh":"如果乙醇需求上升，一蒲式耳玉米的價格可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a measured quantity of corn in farming trade.","zh":"這個片語指農業貿易中一個量度玉米的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"deputy chief","meaning":"副主管","examples":[{"en":"Brian Keating was a deputy chief at CSIRO.","zh":"Brian Keating 是 CSIRO 的副主管。"},{"en":"A deputy chief is a senior person who supports or acts below the chief leader.","zh":"deputy chief 是支援或位於最高主管之下的高級人員。"},{"en":"A deputy chief in a school may help the principal manage daily operations.","zh":"學校副主管可能幫助校長管理日常運作。"},{"en":"If the chief is absent, the deputy chief may make important decisions.","zh":"如果主管缺席，副主管可能作出重要決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a high-ranking assistant leader.","zh":"這個片語描述高級副手領導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ethanol blend","meaning":"乙醇混合燃料","examples":[{"en":"An ethanol blend contains ethanol mixed with conventional fuel.","zh":"乙醇混合燃料含有與傳統燃料混合的乙醇。"},{"en":"An ethanol blend is fuel made by combining ethanol with petrol or another fuel.","zh":"ethanol blend 是把乙醇與汽油或另一種燃料結合而成的燃料。"},{"en":"Drivers may choose an ethanol blend if their vehicle can safely use it.","zh":"如果車輛能安全使用，司機可能選擇乙醇混合燃料。"},{"en":"If the ethanol percentage is high, some older engines may not be suitable.","zh":"如果乙醇比例高，一些較舊引擎可能不適合。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fuel that contains ethanol as one ingredient.","zh":"這個片語描述含有乙醇作其中一種成分的燃料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reduce greenhouse gas emissions","meaning":"減少溫室氣體排放","examples":[{"en":"An E10 blend may reduce greenhouse gas emissions.","zh":"E10 混合燃料可能減少溫室氣體排放。"},{"en":"To reduce greenhouse gas emissions means to lower the amount of heat-trapping gases released into the air.","zh":"reduce greenhouse gas emissions 指降低釋放到空氣中的困熱氣體數量。"},{"en":"A factory can reduce greenhouse gas emissions by using renewable electricity.","zh":"工廠可以透過使用可再生電力減少溫室氣體排放。"},{"en":"If vehicles release fewer greenhouse gases, their climate impact may decrease.","zh":"如果車輛釋放較少溫室氣體，其氣候影響可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one goal of cleaner fuel policy.","zh":"這個片語描述潔淨燃料政策的一個目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"over the full lifecycle of","meaning":"在……的整個生命週期內","examples":[{"en":"The environmental impact must be measured over the full lifecycle of ethanol.","zh":"環境影響必須在乙醇的整個生命週期內量度。"},{"en":"Over the full lifecycle of something means from production to use and final disposal or outcome.","zh":"over the full lifecycle of something 指從生產到使用，再到最終處理或結果的所有階段。"},{"en":"A reusable bag should be judged over its full lifecycle, not just by its first use.","zh":"可重用袋應按其整個生命週期判斷，而不只是第一次使用。"},{"en":"If a fuel is clean when burned but dirty to produce, its full lifecycle benefit may be smaller.","zh":"如果燃料燃燒時潔淨但生產時污染，其整個生命週期好處可能較小。"},{"en":"This phrase asks people to examine every stage.","zh":"這個片語要求人們檢視每個階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ethanol production and consumption","meaning":"乙醇的生產與使用","examples":[{"en":"Researchers examine both ethanol production and consumption.","zh":"研究人員同時檢視乙醇的生產與使用。"},{"en":"Ethanol production and consumption means the making of ethanol and its use as fuel or another product.","zh":"ethanol production and consumption 指乙醇的製造，以及它作為燃料或其他產品的使用。"},{"en":"A country must consider both ethanol production and consumption when planning fuel policy.","zh":"國家規劃燃料政策時，必須同時考慮乙醇的生產與使用。"},{"en":"If production is polluting but consumption is cleaner, the total benefit may be mixed.","zh":"如果生產污染但使用較潔淨，整體好處可能好壞參半。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both supply and use.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋供應和使用兩方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the precise benefits","meaning":"實際好處","examples":[{"en":"The precise benefits of ethanol depend on how it is produced.","zh":"乙醇的實際好處取決於它如何生產。"},{"en":"The precise benefits are the exact advantages after all details are considered.","zh":"precise benefits 是考慮所有細節後的確切優點。"},{"en":"The precise benefits of online learning depend on teaching quality and student discipline.","zh":"網上學習的實際好處取決於教學質素和學生自律。"},{"en":"If production methods vary, the benefits of a fuel may vary as well.","zh":"如果生產方法不同，燃料好處也可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that benefits must be measured carefully.","zh":"這個片語強調好處必須仔細量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"depend on specific factors","meaning":"取決於特定因素","examples":[{"en":"The environmental benefits depend on specific factors in the production cycle.","zh":"環境好處取決於生產週期中的特定因素。"},{"en":"To depend on specific factors means to be decided by particular details or conditions.","zh":"depend on specific factors 指由特定細節或條件決定。"},{"en":"A student’s progress may depend on specific factors such as sleep, practice, and feedback.","zh":"學生進步可能取決於睡眠、練習和回饋等特定因素。"},{"en":"If factories use coal, ethanol’s environmental benefit may be reduced.","zh":"如果工廠使用煤炭，乙醇的環境好處可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that the answer is not simple or automatic.","zh":"這個片語提醒答案並不簡單或自動成立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"production cycle","meaning":"生產週期","examples":[{"en":"The energy source is an important part of the production cycle.","zh":"能源來源是生產週期中的重要部分。"},{"en":"A production cycle is the full set of stages involved in making a product.","zh":"production cycle 是製造產品所涉及的整套階段。"},{"en":"A bakery’s production cycle includes mixing, baking, cooling, and packaging.","zh":"麵包店的生產週期包括混合、烘焙、冷卻和包裝。"},{"en":"If one stage of the production cycle uses dirty energy, the final product may be less green.","zh":"如果生產週期某一階段使用高污染能源，最終產品可能不那麼環保。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process from raw material to finished product.","zh":"這個片語描述從原材料到成品的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an important component of","meaning":"……的重要部分","examples":[{"en":"The energy source is an important component of ethanol production.","zh":"能源來源是乙醇生產的重要部分。"},{"en":"An important component of something is a key part that affects how the whole thing works.","zh":"important component of something 是影響整體如何運作的關鍵部分。"},{"en":"Feedback is an important component of language learning.","zh":"回饋是語言學習的重要部分。"},{"en":"If a key component is weak, the final result may be poor.","zh":"如果關鍵部分薄弱，最終結果可能不理想。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a part that strongly matters.","zh":"這個片語指出非常重要的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"energy source","meaning":"能源來源","examples":[{"en":"The environmental impact depends partly on the factory’s energy source.","zh":"環境影響部分取決於工廠的能源來源。"},{"en":"An energy source is something used to provide power, such as coal, oil, wind, solar energy, or electricity.","zh":"energy source 是用來提供動力的東西，例如煤、石油、風能、太陽能或電力。"},{"en":"A school may choose solar panels as a cleaner energy source.","zh":"學校可能選擇太陽能板作為較潔淨能源來源。"},{"en":"If a factory’s energy source is coal, production may create more emissions.","zh":"如果工廠能源來源是煤炭，生產可能產生更多排放。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where power comes from.","zh":"這個片語指出能源從何而來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be powered by coal or oil","meaning":"以煤或石油供能","examples":[{"en":"Some ethanol factories are powered by coal or oil.","zh":"一些乙醇工廠以煤或石油供能。"},{"en":"To be powered by coal or oil means to use these fossil fuels to run machines or produce energy.","zh":"be powered by coal or oil 指使用這些化石燃料運作機器或產生能源。"},{"en":"An old power station may be powered by coal rather than renewable energy.","zh":"舊發電站可能以煤供能，而不是可再生能源。"},{"en":"If a clean fuel is made in a coal-powered factory, its environmental benefit may be reduced.","zh":"如果潔淨燃料在燃煤工廠製造，其環境好處可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that production can still rely on fossil fuels.","zh":"這個片語顯示生產仍可能依賴化石燃料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"associated greenhouse gas emissions","meaning":"相關的溫室氣體排放","examples":[{"en":"Fossil-fuel use creates associated greenhouse gas emissions.","zh":"化石燃料使用會產生相關的溫室氣體排放。"},{"en":"Associated greenhouse gas emissions are heat-trapping gases released as a result of a related activity.","zh":"associated greenhouse gas emissions 是某相關活動造成的困熱氣體釋放。"},{"en":"A delivery service may have associated emissions from vans and packaging production.","zh":"送貨服務可能有來自貨車和包裝生產的相關排放。"},{"en":"If a factory uses oil, the associated emissions must be counted in environmental analysis.","zh":"如果工廠使用石油，相關排放必須計入環境分析。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emissions linked to a process.","zh":"這個片語描述與某過程相連的排放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"create new market opportunities","meaning":"創造新的市場機會","examples":[{"en":"Environmental laws created new market opportunities for cleaner fuels.","zh":"環境法律為更潔淨燃料創造新的市場機會。"},{"en":"To create new market opportunities means to open chances for businesses to sell new products or services.","zh":"create new market opportunities 指為企業銷售新產品或服務打開機會。"},{"en":"A new school lunch policy can create market opportunities for healthy food suppliers.","zh":"新學校午餐政策可以為健康食品供應商創造市場機會。"},{"en":"If governments support cleaner fuels, companies may invest in producing them.","zh":"如果政府支持更潔淨燃料，公司可能投資生產它們。"},{"en":"This phrase links policy or change with new business possibilities.","zh":"這個片語把政策或變化與新商業可能性連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cleaner, more efficient fuels","meaning":"更潔淨、更具效率的燃料","examples":[{"en":"Governments are encouraging the use of cleaner, more efficient fuels.","zh":"政府正在鼓勵使用更潔淨、更具效率的燃料。"},{"en":"Cleaner, more efficient fuels produce less pollution and use energy more effectively.","zh":"cleaner, more efficient fuels 產生較少污染，並更有效使用能源。"},{"en":"A bus company may switch to cleaner, more efficient fuels to reduce smoke and fuel costs.","zh":"巴士公司可能轉用更潔淨、更具效率的燃料，以減少煙霧和燃料成本。"},{"en":"If fuels become cleaner and more efficient, cities may benefit from better air quality.","zh":"如果燃料變得更潔淨和更有效率，城市可能受惠於更好空氣質素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fuels that aim to reduce waste and pollution.","zh":"這個片語描述旨在減少浪費和污染的燃料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"state governments","meaning":"州政府","examples":[{"en":"Several state governments have purchased ethanol-compatible vehicles.","zh":"幾個州政府已購買可使用乙醇的車輛。"},{"en":"State governments are regional governments within a country, especially in federal systems.","zh":"state governments 是一個國家內的地區政府，尤其在聯邦制度中。"},{"en":"A state government may manage roads, schools, hospitals, or local transport policy.","zh":"州政府可能管理道路、學校、醫院或本地交通政策。"},{"en":"If state governments buy cleaner vehicles, they can create demand for alternative fuels.","zh":"如果州政府購買較潔淨車輛，就可以為替代燃料創造需求。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to government below the national level.","zh":"這個片語指國家層級以下的政府。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fleet vehicles","meaning":"車隊車輛","examples":[{"en":"Some governments purchase fleet vehicles capable of using E-85.","zh":"一些政府購買能使用 E-85 的車隊車輛。"},{"en":"Fleet vehicles are vehicles owned and used by an organisation, company, or government.","zh":"fleet vehicles 是由組織、公司或政府擁有和使用的車輛。"},{"en":"A delivery company’s vans are fleet vehicles.","zh":"速遞公司的貨車就是車隊車輛。"},{"en":"If a government fleet changes fuel, it can affect fuel demand quickly.","zh":"如果政府車隊改變燃料，它可以快速影響燃料需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes vehicles managed as a group.","zh":"這個片語描述作為一組管理的車輛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be capable of running on","meaning":"能以……行駛","examples":[{"en":"The vehicles are capable of running on E-85 fuel.","zh":"這些車輛能以 E-85 燃料行駛。"},{"en":"To be capable of running on a fuel means to be able to operate using that fuel.","zh":"be capable of running on a fuel 指能使用某種燃料運作。"},{"en":"Some buses are capable of running on electricity for short routes.","zh":"一些巴士能以電力行駛短途路線。"},{"en":"If a car is not capable of running on high-ethanol fuel, the engine may be damaged.","zh":"如果汽車不能使用高乙醇燃料，引擎可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fuel compatibility.","zh":"這個片語描述燃料相容性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"documented drawbacks","meaning":"有記錄的缺點","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have documented several drawbacks of ethanol.","zh":"研究人員記錄了乙醇的幾項缺點。"},{"en":"Documented drawbacks are disadvantages that have been recorded or supported by evidence.","zh":"documented drawbacks 是已被記錄或有證據支持的缺點。"},{"en":"A school may list documented drawbacks before choosing a new software system.","zh":"學校在選擇新軟件系統前，可能列出有記錄的缺點。"},{"en":"If drawbacks are documented, decision-makers cannot ignore them easily.","zh":"如果缺點有記錄，決策者就不能輕易忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence-backed disadvantages.","zh":"這個片語描述有證據支持的缺點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the economics of production","meaning":"生產的經濟效益","examples":[{"en":"The economics of ethanol production are improving with technology.","zh":"隨着科技進步，乙醇生產的經濟效益正在改善。"},{"en":"The economics of production means the costs, profits, efficiency, and financial practicality of making something.","zh":"economics of production 指製造某物的成本、利潤、效率和財務可行性。"},{"en":"A bakery studies the economics of production before deciding whether to make cakes in-house.","zh":"麵包店在決定是否自行製作蛋糕前，會研究生產的經濟效益。"},{"en":"If production becomes cheaper, a product may become more competitive.","zh":"如果生產變得更便宜，產品可能更具競爭力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the financial side of manufacturing.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於製造的財務層面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as technology improves","meaning":"隨着科技進步","examples":[{"en":"Production costs may fall as technology improves.","zh":"隨着科技進步，生產成本可能下降。"},{"en":"As technology improves means while tools, machines, or methods become better.","zh":"as technology improves 指當工具、機器或方法變得更好時。"},{"en":"As technology improves, online lessons can become more interactive.","zh":"隨着科技進步，網上課堂可以變得更互動。"},{"en":"If machines become more efficient, factories may need less energy per product.","zh":"如果機器變得更有效率，工廠每件產品可能需要較少能源。"},{"en":"This phrase links progress in technology with later benefits.","zh":"這個片語把科技進步與後來好處連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"absorb water","meaning":"吸收水分","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol can absorb water from its surroundings.","zh":"乙醇可以從周圍環境吸收水分。"},{"en":"To absorb water means to take in water from the air or nearby materials.","zh":"absorb water 指從空氣或附近材料吸入水分。"},{"en":"A sponge absorbs water quickly when placed in a sink.","zh":"海綿放在洗手盆中會快速吸收水分。"},{"en":"If fuel absorbs water, it may damage parts of an engine or fuel system.","zh":"如果燃料吸收水分，它可能損害引擎或燃料系統部件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking water into a material or liquid.","zh":"這個片語描述材料或液體吸入水分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cause oxidation, rust and corrosion","meaning":"導致氧化、生銹和腐蝕","examples":[{"en":"Absorbed water can cause oxidation, rust and corrosion.","zh":"被吸收的水分可以導致氧化、生銹和腐蝕。"},{"en":"To cause oxidation, rust and corrosion means to trigger chemical damage to metals or materials.","zh":"cause oxidation, rust and corrosion 指引發金屬或材料的化學損害。"},{"en":"Leaving a bicycle in the rain can cause rust and corrosion over time.","zh":"把單車留在雨中，久而久之可以導致生銹和腐蝕。"},{"en":"If water enters a fuel system, metal parts may gradually weaken.","zh":"如果水進入燃料系統，金屬部件可能逐漸變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes material damage caused by chemical reaction and moisture.","zh":"這個片語描述由化學反應和濕氣造成的材料損壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"possible damage to vehicles","meaning":"對車輛的潛在損害","examples":[{"en":"Higher ethanol blends may cause possible damage to vehicles.","zh":"較高乙醇比例的混合燃料可能對車輛造成潛在損害。"},{"en":"Possible damage to vehicles means harm that may occur to engines, fuel systems, or other parts of vehicles.","zh":"possible damage to vehicles 指可能對引擎、燃料系統或其他車輛部件造成傷害。"},{"en":"Using the wrong fuel can cause possible damage to a car’s engine.","zh":"使用錯誤燃料可能對汽車引擎造成潛在損害。"},{"en":"If drivers ignore fuel guidance, repair costs may rise.","zh":"如果司機忽視燃料指引，維修成本可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase warns about a risk rather than a certain result.","zh":"這個片語警告風險，而不是確定結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"blends above 10%","meaning":"乙醇比例高於一成的混合燃料","examples":[{"en":"Some manufacturers have raised concerns about ethanol blends above 10%.","zh":"一些製造商對乙醇比例高於一成的混合燃料表示憂慮。"},{"en":"Blends above 10% are fuel mixtures containing more than ten percent ethanol.","zh":"blends above 10% 是含有超過百分之十乙醇的燃料混合物。"},{"en":"A car manual may warn drivers not to use ethanol blends above 10%.","zh":"汽車手冊可能警告司機不要使用乙醇比例高於一成的混合燃料。"},{"en":"If the ethanol level is too high for an engine, parts may wear out faster.","zh":"如果乙醇水平對引擎而言太高，部件可能更快磨損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fuel mixtures exceeding a common ethanol limit.","zh":"這個片語描述超過常見乙醇限制的燃料混合物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"attract considerable negative publicity","meaning":"引起大量負面報道","examples":[{"en":"Claims of vehicle damage have attracted considerable negative publicity.","zh":"車輛損壞的說法引起大量負面報道。"},{"en":"To attract considerable negative publicity means to receive a lot of unfavourable media attention.","zh":"attract considerable negative publicity 指受到大量不利傳媒關注。"},{"en":"A restaurant may attract negative publicity if customers report food poisoning.","zh":"如果顧客報稱食物中毒，餐廳可能引起負面報道。"},{"en":"If a fuel is linked to engine damage, public confidence may fall.","zh":"如果燃料與引擎損壞有關，公眾信心可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious public criticism or bad press.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重公眾批評或負面新聞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Compared with diesel, ethanol has a lower energy content.","zh":"與柴油相比，乙醇的能量含量較低。"},{"en":"Compared with means when one thing is considered beside another.","zh":"compared with 指把一件事與另一件事並列考慮。"},{"en":"Compared with walking, cycling is usually faster for short city journeys.","zh":"與步行相比，踩單車通常對城市短途旅程較快。"},{"en":"If one fuel has lower energy content than another, a vehicle may need more of it.","zh":"如果一種燃料能量含量低於另一種，車輛可能需要更多燃料。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a comparison.","zh":"這個片語引入比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the standard fuel","meaning":"標準燃料","examples":[{"en":"Diesel is the standard fuel in much of the heavy transport industry.","zh":"柴油是大部分重型運輸業的標準燃料。"},{"en":"The standard fuel is the fuel normally used in a particular industry or situation.","zh":"standard fuel 是某行業或情況中通常使用的燃料。"},{"en":"Petrol is the standard fuel for many private cars in some countries.","zh":"在一些國家，汽油是許多私家車的標準燃料。"},{"en":"If an alternative fuel wants to compete, it must perform well against the standard fuel.","zh":"如果替代燃料想競爭，就必須與標準燃料相比有良好表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the usual or accepted fuel choice.","zh":"這個片語描述通常或被接受的燃料選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"heavy transport industry","meaning":"重型運輸業","examples":[{"en":"Diesel is commonly used in the heavy transport industry.","zh":"柴油常用於重型運輸業。"},{"en":"The heavy transport industry includes trucks, freight vehicles, and other large vehicles that move goods.","zh":"heavy transport industry 包括貨車、貨運車輛和其他運送貨物的大型車輛。"},{"en":"Long-distance lorries are a major part of the heavy transport industry.","zh":"長途貨車是重型運輸業的重要部分。"},{"en":"If fuel prices rise, heavy transport companies may face higher operating costs.","zh":"如果燃料價格上升，重型運輸公司可能面對較高營運成本。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to businesses moving heavy goods by road or similar vehicles.","zh":"這個片語指透過道路或類似車輛運送重貨的行業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lower energy content","meaning":"較低能量含量","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol has a lower energy content than diesel.","zh":"乙醇的能量含量低於柴油。"},{"en":"Lower energy content means less usable energy in each litre or unit of fuel.","zh":"lower energy content 指每公升或每單位燃料含有較少可用能量。"},{"en":"A snack with lower energy content gives the body fewer calories.","zh":"能量含量較低的小食給身體較少卡路里。"},{"en":"If a fuel has lower energy content, a vehicle may need more fuel to travel the same distance.","zh":"如果燃料能量含量較低，車輛可能需要更多燃料才能行駛相同距離。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why range and tank size may be affected.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何續航距離和油缸大小可能受影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"require larger fuel tanks","meaning":"需要較大的油缸","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol-powered trucks require larger fuel tanks.","zh":"乙醇動力貨車需要較大的油缸。"},{"en":"To require larger fuel tanks means to need bigger tanks to carry enough fuel.","zh":"require larger fuel tanks 指需要更大的油缸來裝載足夠燃料。"},{"en":"A delivery van with poor fuel efficiency may require a larger tank for long routes.","zh":"燃油效率差的送貨車可能需要較大油缸行駛長路線。"},{"en":"If fuel contains less energy per litre, vehicles may need to carry more of it.","zh":"如果每公升燃料含有較少能量，車輛可能需要攜帶更多燃料。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a practical design consequence.","zh":"這個片語顯示實際設計後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"achieve the same range","meaning":"達到相同續航距離","examples":[{"en":"A larger tank is needed to achieve the same range as a diesel vehicle.","zh":"需要較大油缸才能達到與柴油車相同的續航距離。"},{"en":"To achieve the same range means to travel the same distance before refuelling.","zh":"achieve the same range 指在補充燃料前行駛相同距離。"},{"en":"An electric car needs a strong battery to achieve the same range as a petrol car.","zh":"電動車需要強大電池才能達到與汽油車相同的續航距離。"},{"en":"If fuel has lower energy content, a vehicle may need more fuel to go as far.","zh":"如果燃料能量含量較低，車輛可能需要更多燃料才能行駛同樣遠。"},{"en":"This phrase compares travel distance between vehicles.","zh":"這個片語比較車輛之間的行駛距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"diesel-powered vehicle","meaning":"柴油車輛","examples":[{"en":"A diesel-powered vehicle can travel farther on a smaller amount of fuel.","zh":"柴油車輛可以用較少燃料行駛更遠。"},{"en":"A diesel-powered vehicle is a vehicle that runs on diesel fuel.","zh":"diesel-powered vehicle 是以柴油作燃料行駛的車輛。"},{"en":"Many buses and trucks are diesel-powered vehicles because diesel is efficient for heavy loads.","zh":"許多巴士和貨車都是柴油車輛，因為柴油對重載較有效率。"},{"en":"If diesel prices rise, operating diesel-powered vehicles becomes more expensive.","zh":"如果柴油價格上升，營運柴油車輛會變得更昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes vehicles powered by diesel engines.","zh":"這個片語描述由柴油引擎驅動的車輛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a government review into","meaning":"政府對……進行的檢討","examples":[{"en":"Australia conducted a government review into the effects of ethanol blends.","zh":"澳洲政府對乙醇混合燃料的影響進行檢討。"},{"en":"A government review into something is an official investigation or assessment by the government.","zh":"government review into something 是政府進行的官方調查或評估。"},{"en":"A government review into school safety may examine accidents, rules, and staff training.","zh":"政府對學校安全進行檢討時，可能檢視意外、規則和員工培訓。"},{"en":"If a new fuel may damage vehicles, a review can collect evidence before policy changes.","zh":"如果新燃料可能損壞車輛，檢討可以在政策改變前收集證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal government examination.","zh":"這個片語描述正式政府審視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the impacts of","meaning":"……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The review examined the impacts of a 20% ethanol blend on vehicles.","zh":"該檢討研究20%乙醇混合燃料對車輛的影響。"},{"en":"The impacts of something are the effects or consequences it has.","zh":"impacts of something 是某事帶來的效果或後果。"},{"en":"A school may study the impacts of later start times on student sleep.","zh":"學校可能研究較遲上課時間對學生睡眠的影響。"},{"en":"If a fuel affects engines, costs, and emissions, its impacts must be assessed widely.","zh":"如果燃料影響引擎、成本和排放，其影響必須廣泛評估。"},{"en":"This phrase asks what results something produces.","zh":"這個片語詢問某事產生甚麼結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"insufficient or conflicting","meaning":"不足或互相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"The available information was considered insufficient or conflicting.","zh":"可用資料被認為不足或互相矛盾。"},{"en":"Insufficient or conflicting means not enough, or saying different things that do not agree.","zh":"insufficient or conflicting 指資料不夠，或不同資料說法不一致。"},{"en":"A teacher cannot judge a complaint fairly if the evidence is insufficient or conflicting.","zh":"如果證據不足或互相矛盾，老師不能公平判斷投訴。"},{"en":"If data is weak or contradictory, decision-makers may delay action.","zh":"如果數據薄弱或矛盾，決策者可能延遲行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence that is not reliable enough for a firm conclusion.","zh":"這個片語描述不足以得出堅定結論的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"identify a number of problems","meaning":"發現多項問題","examples":[{"en":"The review identified a number of possible technical problems.","zh":"該檢討發現多項可能的技術問題。"},{"en":"To identify a number of problems means to find and name several issues.","zh":"identify a number of problems 指找出並指出幾個問題。"},{"en":"A school audit may identify a number of problems with fire exits and classroom wiring.","zh":"學校審核可能發現消防出口和課室電線有多項問題。"},{"en":"If problems are identified early, they can be fixed before wider damage occurs.","zh":"如果問題及早被發現，就能在更大損害發生前修正。"},{"en":"This phrase describes discovering multiple difficulties.","zh":"這個片語描述發現多個困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"perishing and swelling","meaning":"老化及膨脹","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol may cause the perishing and swelling of some materials.","zh":"乙醇可能導致某些材料老化及膨脹。"},{"en":"Perishing and swelling means materials may break down, weaken, expand, or change shape.","zh":"perishing and swelling 指材料可能分解、變弱、膨脹或變形。"},{"en":"Old rubber bands may perish and crack after years in a drawer.","zh":"舊橡筋放在抽屜多年後可能老化裂開。"},{"en":"If fuel makes rubber swell, seals and tubes may stop fitting properly.","zh":"如果燃料令橡膠膨脹，密封圈和管道可能不再合適。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical damage to materials.","zh":"這個片語描述材料的物理損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"elastomeric materials","meaning":"彈性體物料","examples":[{"en":"Some elastomeric materials may be damaged by high ethanol concentrations.","zh":"一些彈性體物料可能被高濃度乙醇損壞。"},{"en":"Elastomeric materials are rubber-like materials that can stretch and return to shape.","zh":"elastomeric materials 是像橡膠一樣能拉伸並回復形狀的材料。"},{"en":"Seals, hoses, and gaskets in vehicles may contain elastomeric materials.","zh":"車輛中的密封圈、喉管和墊片可能含有彈性體物料。"},{"en":"If these materials swell or crack, fuel systems may leak.","zh":"如果這些材料膨脹或裂開，燃料系統可能洩漏。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to flexible technical materials.","zh":"這個片語指具彈性的技術材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"plastic materials","meaning":"塑膠物料","examples":[{"en":"Plastic materials in fuel systems may swell or deteriorate.","zh":"燃料系統中的塑膠物料可能膨脹或變差。"},{"en":"Plastic materials are man-made materials that can be shaped into parts, containers, or surfaces.","zh":"plastic materials 是可被塑造成零件、容器或表面的人工材料。"},{"en":"Cars, phones, and lunch boxes often contain plastic materials.","zh":"汽車、手機和飯盒常含有塑膠物料。"},{"en":"If a chemical reacts badly with plastic, the plastic may weaken or change shape.","zh":"如果化學物與塑膠反應不良，塑膠可能變弱或變形。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to synthetic materials used in many products.","zh":"這個片語指用於許多產品的合成材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fuel systems","meaning":"燃料系統","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol blends may affect materials used in fuel systems.","zh":"乙醇混合燃料可能影響燃料系統中使用的材料。"},{"en":"Fuel systems are the parts of a vehicle that store, carry, and deliver fuel to the engine.","zh":"fuel systems 是車輛中儲存、輸送並把燃料送到引擎的部件。"},{"en":"A mechanic checks the fuel system if a car smells strongly of petrol.","zh":"如果汽車有強烈汽油味，技工會檢查燃料系統。"},{"en":"If fuel damages hoses or seals, the fuel system may leak or fail.","zh":"如果燃料損壞喉管或密封圈，燃料系統可能洩漏或故障。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the vehicle system that handles fuel.","zh":"這個片語描述處理燃料的車輛系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"industry stakeholders","meaning":"業界持份者","examples":[{"en":"Industry stakeholders have raised concerns about vehicle warranties.","zh":"業界持份者對車輛保養提出憂慮。"},{"en":"Industry stakeholders are people or organisations affected by decisions in an industry.","zh":"industry stakeholders 是受某行業決策影響的人或組織。"},{"en":"In education, stakeholders may include teachers, students, parents, and school managers.","zh":"在教育中，持份者可能包括老師、學生、家長和學校管理層。"},{"en":"If stakeholders raise concerns, policymakers may need to consult them before acting.","zh":"如果持份者提出憂慮，政策制定者可能需要在行動前諮詢他們。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to parties with an interest in an issue.","zh":"這個片語指對某議題有利益關係的各方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"motor vehicle industry","meaning":"汽車業","examples":[{"en":"The motor vehicle industry has questioned the use of high ethanol blends.","zh":"汽車業質疑高乙醇混合燃料的使用。"},{"en":"The motor vehicle industry includes companies that design, make, sell, repair, or service vehicles.","zh":"motor vehicle industry 包括設計、製造、銷售、維修或服務車輛的公司。"},{"en":"Car manufacturers, parts suppliers, and repair garages are part of the motor vehicle industry.","zh":"汽車製造商、零件供應商和修車房都是汽車業的一部分。"},{"en":"If a new fuel may damage cars, the industry may oppose its widespread use.","zh":"如果新燃料可能損壞汽車，業界可能反對其廣泛使用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the business sector connected with vehicles.","zh":"這個片語指與車輛相關的商業界別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"vehicle warranties","meaning":"車輛保養","examples":[{"en":"Vehicle warranties may be affected by fuel containing too much ethanol.","zh":"含太多乙醇的燃料可能影響車輛保養。"},{"en":"Vehicle warranties are promises by manufacturers to repair certain problems within a set period.","zh":"vehicle warranties 是製造商承諾在特定期間內維修某些問題。"},{"en":"A new car’s warranty may cover engine problems for several years.","zh":"新車保養可能在數年內涵蓋引擎問題。"},{"en":"If drivers use unsuitable fuel, the warranty may no longer apply.","zh":"如果司機使用不合適燃料，保養可能不再適用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to official repair protection for vehicles.","zh":"這個片語指車輛的官方維修保障。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pump-dispensing equipment","meaning":"油泵分配設備","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol may also affect pump-dispensing equipment.","zh":"乙醇也可能影響油泵分配設備。"},{"en":"Pump-dispensing equipment is machinery at fuel stations that pumps fuel into vehicles.","zh":"pump-dispensing equipment 是加油站把燃料泵入車輛的機械設備。"},{"en":"A petrol station must maintain pump-dispensing equipment to avoid leaks and inaccurate measurement.","zh":"加油站必須保養油泵分配設備，以避免洩漏和量度不準。"},{"en":"If ethanol damages hoses or seals in pumps, stations may need expensive repairs.","zh":"如果乙醇損壞油泵中的喉管或密封圈，油站可能需要昂貴維修。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fuel-station equipment used for delivery of fuel.","zh":"這個片語描述用於輸送燃料的加油站設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be at risk","meaning":"面臨風險","examples":[{"en":"Some warranties could be at risk if high-ethanol fuel is used.","zh":"如果使用高乙醇燃料，一些保養可能面臨風險。"},{"en":"To be at risk means to be in danger of being harmed, lost, or affected.","zh":"be at risk 指處於可能受害、失去或受影響的危險中。"},{"en":"A student’s place in a course may be at risk if they miss too many lessons.","zh":"如果學生缺課太多，其課程名額可能面臨風險。"},{"en":"If a driver uses the wrong fuel, their engine and warranty may both be at risk.","zh":"如果司機使用錯誤燃料，引擎和保養都可能面臨風險。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that something valuable may be threatened.","zh":"這個片語警告有價值的東西可能受威脅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"principal economist","meaning":"首席經濟學家","examples":[{"en":"Andrew Dickson was a principal economist with an Australian government bureau.","zh":"Andrew Dickson 是澳洲一個政府部門的首席經濟學家。"},{"en":"A principal economist is a senior economist who analyses financial and economic issues.","zh":"principal economist 是分析財政和經濟議題的高級經濟學家。"},{"en":"A principal economist may advise a government on fuel prices or farming policy.","zh":"首席經濟學家可能就燃料價格或農業政策向政府提供建議。"},{"en":"If an economist studies a policy, they may examine costs, incentives, and market effects.","zh":"如果經濟學家研究政策，他們可能檢視成本、誘因和市場影響。"},{"en":"This phrase names a high-level economic expert.","zh":"這個片語指高級經濟專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"point out that","meaning":"指出","examples":[{"en":"Dickson points out that ethanol demand does not directly determine sugar prices.","zh":"Dickson 指出乙醇需求並不直接決定糖價。"},{"en":"To point out that means to mention or explain an important fact.","zh":"point out that 指提及或解釋一個重要事實。"},{"en":"A teacher may point out that a good essay needs clear examples, not only big words.","zh":"老師可能指出好文章需要清楚例子，而不只是艱深詞語。"},{"en":"If someone points out a weakness, the argument may need to be revised.","zh":"如果有人指出弱點，論點可能需要修正。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a fact someone wants others to notice.","zh":"這個片語引入某人希望他人注意的事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sugar-cane growers","meaning":"甘蔗種植者","examples":[{"en":"Sugar-cane growers may not automatically benefit from ethanol production.","zh":"甘蔗種植者未必會自動從乙醇生產中受益。"},{"en":"Sugar-cane growers are farmers who grow sugar cane.","zh":"sugar-cane growers 是種植甘蔗的農民。"},{"en":"Sugar-cane growers sell their crop to sugar mills or ethanol producers.","zh":"甘蔗種植者把作物賣給糖廠或乙醇生產商。"},{"en":"If cane prices are controlled by the global market, local ethanol demand may not raise farmers’ income.","zh":"如果甘蔗價格受全球市場控制，本地乙醇需求未必提高農民收入。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to farmers in the sugar-cane industry.","zh":"這個片語指甘蔗產業中的農民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"domestic consumption","meaning":"本地消耗量","examples":[{"en":"Domestic consumption of ethanol does not directly determine cane prices.","zh":"乙醇本地消耗量並不直接決定甘蔗價格。"},{"en":"Domestic consumption means use within a country’s own market.","zh":"domestic consumption 指在一個國家本地市場內的使用量。"},{"en":"Domestic consumption of rice may rise if more families eat at home.","zh":"如果更多家庭在家吃飯，米的本地消耗量可能上升。"},{"en":"If domestic consumption is small compared with world trade, it may not control prices.","zh":"如果本地消耗量與全球貿易相比很小，它可能無法控制價格。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts local use with global demand.","zh":"這個片語把本地使用與全球需求作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"domestic demand","meaning":"本地需求","examples":[{"en":"Domestic demand for ethanol may not increase farmers’ income.","zh":"乙醇本地需求未必會增加農民收入。"},{"en":"Domestic demand means demand from buyers within the same country.","zh":"domestic demand 指來自同一國家內買家的需求。"},{"en":"Domestic demand for school uniforms rises before the new academic year.","zh":"新學年前，校服本地需求上升。"},{"en":"If domestic demand is not strong enough, producers may still depend on export markets.","zh":"如果本地需求不夠強，生產商可能仍依賴出口市場。"},{"en":"This phrase describes local market demand.","zh":"這個片語描述本地市場需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be entirely determined by","meaning":"完全由……決定","examples":[{"en":"The price of sugar cane is largely determined by the global market.","zh":"甘蔗價格很大程度上由全球市場決定。"},{"en":"To be entirely determined by something means to be completely decided by that factor.","zh":"be entirely determined by something 指完全由某因素決定。"},{"en":"A student’s final grade should not be entirely determined by one test.","zh":"學生最終成績不應完全由一次測驗決定。"},{"en":"If prices are determined by global trade, local policy may have limited effect.","zh":"如果價格由全球貿易決定，本地政策可能作用有限。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong control by one factor.","zh":"這個片語顯示某因素具有強控制力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the world sugar market","meaning":"全球食糖市場","examples":[{"en":"Farmers’ income is influenced by the world sugar market.","zh":"農民收入受全球食糖市場影響。"},{"en":"The world sugar market is the global system of buying and selling sugar.","zh":"world sugar market 是全球買賣食糖的市場系統。"},{"en":"If world sugar prices fall, sugar-cane growers may earn less.","zh":"如果全球糖價下跌，甘蔗種植者可能收入減少。"},{"en":"A local farmer may be affected by prices set far beyond their own country.","zh":"本地農民可能受遠在自己國家之外制定的價格影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the international market for sugar.","zh":"這個片語描述國際食糖市場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"world trade in molasses","meaning":"全球糖蜜貿易","examples":[{"en":"Molasses prices are affected by world trade in molasses.","zh":"糖蜜價格受全球糖蜜貿易影響。"},{"en":"World trade in molasses means the international buying and selling of molasses.","zh":"world trade in molasses 指糖蜜的國際買賣。"},{"en":"A change in global shipping costs can affect world trade in farm products.","zh":"全球航運成本變化可以影響農產品的世界貿易。"},{"en":"If molasses is traded globally, local prices may follow international demand.","zh":"如果糖蜜在全球交易，本地價格可能跟隨國際需求。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a product’s price with global trade.","zh":"這個片語把產品價格與全球貿易連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"molasses","meaning":"糖蜜","examples":[{"en":"Molasses is a by-product that can be used in ethanol production.","zh":"糖蜜是一種可用於乙醇生產的副產品。"},{"en":"Molasses is a thick dark syrup left after sugar is made from sugar cane or sugar beet.","zh":"molasses 是從甘蔗或甜菜製糖後留下的深色濃糖漿。"},{"en":"Some bakers use molasses to give bread or biscuits a strong sweet flavour.","zh":"一些麵包師使用糖蜜為麵包或餅乾帶來濃烈甜味。"},{"en":"If molasses can be turned into ethanol, waste from sugar production may gain value.","zh":"如果糖蜜可以轉化為乙醇，製糖廢料可能增加價值。"},{"en":"This word refers to a sugary by-product of the sugar industry.","zh":"這個詞指製糖業的含糖副產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"benefit from the existence of","meaning":"從……的存在中得益","examples":[{"en":"The sugar industry may benefit from the existence of an ethanol industry only indirectly.","zh":"糖業可能只是間接地從乙醇產業的存在中得益。"},{"en":"To benefit from the existence of something means to gain advantages because that thing exists.","zh":"benefit from the existence of something 指因某事物存在而獲得好處。"},{"en":"A small café may benefit from the existence of a nearby school because students buy snacks.","zh":"小咖啡店可能因附近學校的存在而受益，因為學生會買小食。"},{"en":"If ethanol factories exist, related industries may gain new buyers or business links.","zh":"如果乙醇工廠存在，相關行業可能獲得新買家或商業連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes indirect advantage from another system or industry.","zh":"這個片語描述從另一系統或產業獲得的間接好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"invest in the industry","meaning":"投資於該行業","examples":[{"en":"Sugar producers may need to invest in the ethanol industry themselves.","zh":"食糖生產商可能需要親自投資於乙醇行業。"},{"en":"To invest in the industry means to put money, resources, or effort into that business sector.","zh":"invest in the industry 指把金錢、資源或努力投入某個商業界別。"},{"en":"A company may invest in the technology industry by funding a start-up.","zh":"公司可能透過資助初創企業投資於科技行業。"},{"en":"If farmers invest in ethanol plants, they may share in the profits.","zh":"如果農民投資乙醇廠，他們可能分享利潤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes financial participation in a sector.","zh":"這個片語描述在某個界別中的財務參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"what incentive do they have to","meaning":"他們有甚麼誘因去……","examples":[{"en":"If prices do not rise, what incentive do farmers have to produce more?","zh":"如果價格不上升，農民有甚麼誘因去生產更多？"},{"en":"What incentive do they have to asks what reason or reward would make people take action.","zh":"what incentive do they have to 問有甚麼理由或回報會令某人採取行動。"},{"en":"If overtime is unpaid, what incentive do workers have to stay late?","zh":"如果加班沒有薪酬，工人有甚麼誘因留下來工作至很晚？"},{"en":"If farmers earn no extra income, they may not choose to grow more fuel crops.","zh":"如果農民沒有額外收入，他們未必選擇種植更多燃料作物。"},{"en":"This phrase questions the motivation behind an action.","zh":"這個片語質疑行動背後的動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"production costs","meaning":"生產成本","examples":[{"en":"High production costs create difficulties for the ethanol industry.","zh":"高生產成本為乙醇產業帶來困難。"},{"en":"Production costs are the expenses involved in making a product.","zh":"production costs 是製造產品所涉及的開支。"},{"en":"A bakery’s production costs include flour, electricity, rent, and workers’ wages.","zh":"麵包店的生產成本包括麵粉、電力、租金和員工薪金。"},{"en":"If production costs are too high, a product may need government support or higher prices.","zh":"如果生產成本太高，產品可能需要政府支持或更高售價。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the money needed to produce something.","zh":"這個片語描述生產某物所需金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"represent a challenge","meaning":"構成挑戰","examples":[{"en":"The cost of ethanol production represents a major challenge.","zh":"乙醇生產成本構成重大挑戰。"},{"en":"To represent a challenge means to create a difficulty that must be dealt with.","zh":"represent a challenge 指造成必須處理的困難。"},{"en":"Teaching a large mixed-ability class can represent a challenge for new teachers.","zh":"教授一個程度混雜的大班，對新老師而言可能構成挑戰。"},{"en":"If costs are high, companies may struggle to sell a product at a competitive price.","zh":"如果成本高，公司可能難以用具競爭力價格銷售產品。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies something as a serious difficulty.","zh":"這個片語把某事指出為嚴重困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"per litre","meaning":"每公升","examples":[{"en":"Fuel prices are commonly compared on a per-litre basis.","zh":"燃料價格通常以每公升為基礎比較。"},{"en":"Per litre means for each litre of liquid.","zh":"per litre 指每一公升液體。"},{"en":"A drink may cost ten dollars per litre if sold in a large bottle.","zh":"如果飲品以大瓶出售，價格可能是每公升十元。"},{"en":"Comparing fuel per litre helps drivers understand running costs.","zh":"按每公升比較燃料，有助司機了解行車成本。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when measuring or pricing liquids.","zh":"這個片語用於量度或定價液體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"compared with unleaded petrol","meaning":"與無鉛汽油相比","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol costs considerably more than unleaded petrol in Australia.","zh":"在澳洲，乙醇成本比無鉛汽油高得多。"},{"en":"Compared with unleaded petrol means when ethanol is measured against standard petrol without lead.","zh":"compared with unleaded petrol 指把乙醇與不含鉛的標準汽油作比較。"},{"en":"Compared with unleaded petrol, electricity may be cheaper for some short car journeys.","zh":"與無鉛汽油相比，電力對某些短途車程可能更便宜。"},{"en":"If ethanol costs more than petrol, drivers may avoid it without subsidies.","zh":"如果乙醇比汽油昂貴，沒有補貼時司機可能避免使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase sets up a fuel-price comparison.","zh":"這個片語建立燃料價格比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"government assistance","meaning":"政府援助","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol producers often require government assistance.","zh":"乙醇生產商常需要政府援助。"},{"en":"Government assistance is support from the government, such as money, tax relief, or special rules.","zh":"government assistance 是政府提供的支持，例如金錢、稅務減免或特殊規則。"},{"en":"Small businesses may need government assistance after a major flood.","zh":"大水災後，小企業可能需要政府援助。"},{"en":"If a fuel is too expensive to compete, subsidies may help producers survive.","zh":"如果燃料太昂貴而無法競爭，補貼可能幫助生產商生存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official support for people or industries.","zh":"這個片語描述對個人或行業的官方支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cost more than diesel","meaning":"成本高於柴油","examples":[{"en":"Even with assistance, ethanol may cost more than diesel.","zh":"即使有援助，乙醇成本也可能高於柴油。"},{"en":"To cost more than diesel means to be more expensive than diesel fuel.","zh":"cost more than diesel 指比柴油燃料更昂貴。"},{"en":"If a train ticket costs more than driving, some passengers may choose the car.","zh":"如果火車票比駕車更貴，一些乘客可能選擇汽車。"},{"en":"If ethanol costs more than diesel, transport companies may resist switching fuels.","zh":"如果乙醇成本高於柴油，運輸公司可能抗拒轉換燃料。"},{"en":"This phrase compares fuel prices directly.","zh":"這個片語直接比較燃料價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"consequently","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol is expensive; consequently, producers need government support.","zh":"乙醇昂貴；因此，生產商需要政府支持。"},{"en":"Consequently means as a result.","zh":"consequently 指因此或作為結果。"},{"en":"The bus broke down; consequently, many students arrived late.","zh":"巴士壞了；因此，許多學生遲到。"},{"en":"If a product costs too much to make, it may need subsidies to survive.","zh":"如果產品製造成本太高，它可能需要補貼才能生存。"},{"en":"This word links a cause with a result.","zh":"這個詞把原因與結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be competitive","meaning":"具競爭力","examples":[{"en":"Government assistance may be needed for ethanol to be competitive.","zh":"乙醇可能需要政府援助才能具競爭力。"},{"en":"To be competitive means to be able to compete successfully in price, quality, or performance.","zh":"be competitive 指能在價格、質素或表現上成功競爭。"},{"en":"A small shop can be competitive if it offers better service than large chains.","zh":"如果小店提供比大型連鎖店更好的服務，它可以具競爭力。"},{"en":"If ethanol is too expensive, it may not be competitive with petrol or diesel.","zh":"如果乙醇太昂貴，就可能無法與汽油或柴油競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes whether something can succeed against alternatives.","zh":"這個片語描述某物能否勝過替代選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"large-scale production","meaning":"大規模生產","examples":[{"en":"Large-scale production requires substantial investment.","zh":"大規模生產需要大量投資。"},{"en":"Large-scale production means making something in very large quantities.","zh":"large-scale production 指大量製造某物。"},{"en":"A factory may need new machines before large-scale production can begin.","zh":"工廠在開始大規模生產前可能需要新機器。"},{"en":"If production becomes large-scale, costs per unit may fall over time.","zh":"如果生產變成大規模，每單位成本可能隨時間下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes industrial production at high volume.","zh":"這個片語描述高產量的工業生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"commercially viable","meaning":"具商業可行性","examples":[{"en":"Without assistance, ethanol production may not be commercially viable.","zh":"沒有援助，乙醇生產可能不具商業可行性。"},{"en":"Commercially viable means able to succeed financially as a business.","zh":"commercially viable 指能在商業上取得財務成功。"},{"en":"A product may be popular but not commercially viable if it costs too much to make.","zh":"如果產品製造成本太高，即使受歡迎，也可能不具商業可行性。"},{"en":"If ethanol cannot be sold at a profit, producers may stop making it.","zh":"如果乙醇不能以盈利方式出售，生產商可能停止製造。"},{"en":"This phrase describes whether an idea can work in the market.","zh":"這個片語描述想法能否在市場中運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"regardless of whether","meaning":"不論是否……","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol production may expand regardless of whether sugar growers benefit directly.","zh":"不論甘蔗種植者是否直接受益，乙醇生產都可能擴大。"},{"en":"Regardless of whether means no matter whether something is true or not.","zh":"regardless of whether 指不管某事是否屬實。"},{"en":"Students must submit homework regardless of whether they find the topic easy.","zh":"不論學生是否覺得題目容易，都必須交功課。"},{"en":"If policy continues regardless of farmers’ direct benefit, some groups may feel ignored.","zh":"如果政策不論農民是否直接受益都繼續，一些群體可能感到被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one outcome may happen in either case.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩種情況下某結果都可能發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"mandated ethanol mix","meaning":"強制規定的乙醇混合比例","examples":[{"en":"The government considered a mandated 10% ethanol mix.","zh":"政府考慮強制規定一成乙醇混合比例。"},{"en":"A mandated ethanol mix is a fuel blend with an ethanol percentage required by law or official rule.","zh":"mandated ethanol mix 是由法律或官方規則要求的乙醇燃料混合比例。"},{"en":"A country may require petrol stations to sell a mandated ethanol mix.","zh":"國家可能要求加油站銷售強制規定的乙醇混合燃料。"},{"en":"If a mix is mandated, drivers and suppliers may have less choice.","zh":"如果混合比例被強制規定，司機和供應商可能較少選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a compulsory fuel-blending rule.","zh":"這個片語描述強制燃料混合規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"expansion of production","meaning":"擴大生產","examples":[{"en":"The expansion of ethanol production could help farming regions.","zh":"擴大乙醇生產可能幫助農業地區。"},{"en":"Expansion of production means an increase in how much is made.","zh":"expansion of production 指製造數量增加。"},{"en":"A bakery may need more ovens for the expansion of production.","zh":"麵包店可能因擴大生產而需要更多焗爐。"},{"en":"If ethanol production expands, more crops, factories, and workers may be needed.","zh":"如果乙醇生產擴大，可能需要更多作物、工廠和工人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth in manufacturing output.","zh":"這個片語描述製造產出增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lead to increased economic activity","meaning":"帶來更多經濟活動","examples":[{"en":"New ethanol plants could lead to increased economic activity.","zh":"新乙醇廠可能帶來更多經濟活動。"},{"en":"To lead to increased economic activity means to create more business, jobs, spending, or production.","zh":"lead to increased economic activity 指創造更多商業、工作、消費或生產。"},{"en":"A new railway station can lead to increased economic activity near local shops.","zh":"新鐵路站可以為附近本地商店帶來更多經濟活動。"},{"en":"If factories open in farming areas, workers may earn wages and spend money locally.","zh":"如果工廠在農業地區開設，工人可能賺取工資並在本地消費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes economic growth caused by a new development.","zh":"這個片語描述由新發展造成的經濟增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"farming areas","meaning":"農業地區","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol plants may create new employment in farming areas.","zh":"乙醇廠可能在農業地區創造新就業。"},{"en":"Farming areas are places where agriculture is a major land use and economic activity.","zh":"farming areas 是以農業作為主要土地用途和經濟活動的地方。"},{"en":"Villages surrounded by crops and livestock farms are farming areas.","zh":"被農作物和畜牧場包圍的村莊就是農業地區。"},{"en":"If new industries open in farming areas, rural workers may have more job choices.","zh":"如果新產業在農業地區開設，鄉郊工人可能有更多工作選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to agricultural regions.","zh":"這個片語指農業區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"it is inevitable that","meaning":"無可避免的是","examples":[{"en":"It is inevitable that industrial expansion will affect existing businesses.","zh":"無可避免的是，工業擴張會影響現有企業。"},{"en":"It is inevitable that means something is certain or almost certain to happen.","zh":"it is inevitable that 指某事必然或幾乎必然會發生。"},{"en":"It is inevitable that students feel nervous before an important exam.","zh":"無可避免的是，學生在重要考試前會緊張。"},{"en":"If one industry expands quickly, it is almost certain to affect workers and competitors.","zh":"如果一個產業快速擴張，幾乎必然會影響工人和競爭者。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an unavoidable result.","zh":"這個片語引入不可避免的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"at the expense of","meaning":"以犧牲……為代價","examples":[{"en":"Some expansion may occur at the expense of existing industries.","zh":"一些擴張可能以犧牲現有產業為代價。"},{"en":"At the expense of something means causing harm, loss, or sacrifice to it.","zh":"at the expense of something 指對某事造成傷害、損失或犧牲。"},{"en":"A student should not improve grades at the expense of sleep and health.","zh":"學生不應以犧牲睡眠和健康為代價提高成績。"},{"en":"If new factories grow by taking workers from old industries, existing businesses may suffer.","zh":"如果新工廠透過從舊產業吸走工人而成長，現有企業可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one gain may create another loss.","zh":"這個片語顯示一方得益可能造成另一方損失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"existing industry","meaning":"現有產業","examples":[{"en":"New ethanol facilities may compete with existing industry.","zh":"新乙醇設施可能與現有產業競爭。"},{"en":"Existing industry means businesses or sectors already operating in an area.","zh":"existing industry 指一個地區中已經運作的企業或界別。"},{"en":"A new shopping mall may affect existing industry in a town centre.","zh":"新商場可能影響市中心現有產業。"},{"en":"If a new sector attracts workers and investment, older industries may face pressure.","zh":"如果新界別吸引工人和投資，舊產業可能面對壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to industries that are already established.","zh":"這個片語指已建立的產業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"become more popular","meaning":"變得更普及","examples":[{"en":"More production plants will be built if ethanol becomes more popular.","zh":"如果乙醇變得更普及，將會建造更多生產廠房。"},{"en":"To become more popular means to be liked, used, or accepted by more people.","zh":"become more popular 指被更多人喜歡、使用或接受。"},{"en":"A school club may become more popular after students see a successful performance.","zh":"學生看到成功表演後，學校社團可能變得更受歡迎。"},{"en":"If ethanol becomes popular, companies may invest in more factories and fuel stations.","zh":"如果乙醇變得普及，公司可能投資更多工廠和加油站。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rising public or market acceptance.","zh":"這個片語描述公眾或市場接受度上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"production plants","meaning":"生產廠房","examples":[{"en":"New production plants would create employment opportunities.","zh":"新生產廠房會創造就業機會。"},{"en":"Production plants are factories where products are made on a large scale.","zh":"production plants 是大規模製造產品的工廠。"},{"en":"A car company may build production plants near ports to reduce transport costs.","zh":"汽車公司可能在港口附近建造生產廠房，以減少運輸成本。"},{"en":"If production plants open in rural areas, they can create jobs and demand for local services.","zh":"如果生產廠房在鄉郊地區開設，可以創造工作和本地服務需求。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to manufacturing facilities.","zh":"這個片語指製造設施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a need for workers","meaning":"對工人的需求","examples":[{"en":"New ethanol plants would create a need for workers.","zh":"新乙醇廠會創造對工人的需求。"},{"en":"A need for workers means a demand for people to do jobs.","zh":"need for workers 指對人手工作的需求。"},{"en":"A new hospital creates a need for nurses, cleaners, doctors, and clerks.","zh":"新醫院會創造對護士、清潔工、醫生和文員的需求。"},{"en":"If factories expand, the need for workers may raise local employment.","zh":"如果工廠擴張，對工人的需求可能提高本地就業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes labour demand.","zh":"這個片語描述勞動力需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"project that","meaning":"預計；推算","examples":[{"en":"The coalition projects that the industry will create thousands of jobs.","zh":"該聯盟預計該行業將創造數千個職位。"},{"en":"To project that means to estimate or predict something based on available information.","zh":"project that 指根據現有資料估計或預測某事。"},{"en":"A school may project that enrolment will rise next year.","zh":"學校可能預計明年收生人數會上升。"},{"en":"If a group projects job growth, others may ask what data supports the estimate.","zh":"如果一個團體推算就業增長，其他人可能問有甚麼數據支持該估算。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a forecast or calculation.","zh":"這個片語引入預測或計算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"employment will be boosted","meaning":"就業機會將會增加","examples":[{"en":"The expansion of ethanol production could mean that employment will be boosted.","zh":"擴大乙醇生產可能意味着就業機會將會增加。"},{"en":"Employment will be boosted means more jobs will be created or job opportunities will improve.","zh":"employment will be boosted 指會創造更多工作或改善就業機會。"},{"en":"A new airport may mean employment will be boosted in hotels, transport, and retail.","zh":"新機場可能意味着酒店、交通和零售業的就業機會將會增加。"},{"en":"If production grows, companies may hire more workers.","zh":"如果生產增長，公司可能聘請更多工人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increase in jobs.","zh":"這個片語描述職位增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the balance of trade","meaning":"貿易差額","examples":[{"en":"Domestic fuel production may improve the balance of trade.","zh":"本地燃料生產可能改善貿易差額。"},{"en":"The balance of trade is the difference between a country’s exports and imports.","zh":"balance of trade 是一個國家出口與進口之間的差額。"},{"en":"If a country imports less fuel and exports more goods, its balance of trade may improve.","zh":"如果國家進口較少燃料並出口更多貨物，其貿易差額可能改善。"},{"en":"Producing fuel locally can reduce money spent on imported oil.","zh":"本地生產燃料可以減少花在進口石油上的金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in economic discussions about international trade.","zh":"這個片語用於關於國際貿易的經濟討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be improved by","meaning":"改善了……","examples":[{"en":"The balance of trade could be improved by billions of dollars.","zh":"貿易差額可能改善數十億美元。"},{"en":"To be improved by an amount means to become better by that amount.","zh":"be improved by an amount 指按某數量變得更好。"},{"en":"A school’s exam results may be improved by better teaching and more practice.","zh":"學校考試成績可能因更好教學和更多練習而改善。"},{"en":"If fuel imports fall, the country’s trade position may improve financially.","zh":"如果燃料進口下降，國家的貿易狀況可能在財政上改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes measurable improvement.","zh":"這個片語描述可量度的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"look promising","meaning":"看來前景理想","examples":[{"en":"The future of ethanol looks promising despite its disadvantages.","zh":"儘管有缺點，乙醇的未來看來前景理想。"},{"en":"To look promising means to seem likely to succeed or produce good results.","zh":"look promising 指看來有可能成功或產生好結果。"},{"en":"A student’s first draft looks promising if the ideas are clear and well organised.","zh":"如果學生初稿觀點清楚且組織良好，就看來前景不錯。"},{"en":"If early results are positive, a new technology may attract more investment.","zh":"如果早期結果正面，新科技可能吸引更多投資。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses cautious optimism.","zh":"這個片語表達謹慎樂觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"for better or worse","meaning":"無論結果是好是壞","examples":[{"en":"For better or worse, ethanol is likely to remain an important fuel option.","zh":"無論結果是好是壞，乙醇都可能仍是一個重要燃料選項。"},{"en":"For better or worse means whether the result is good or bad.","zh":"for better or worse 指無論結果是好還是壞。"},{"en":"For better or worse, smartphones have changed how students communicate.","zh":"無論好壞，智能手機已改變學生溝通方式。"},{"en":"If a technology becomes common, society must deal with both its benefits and problems.","zh":"如果科技變得普遍，社會必須處理其好處和問題。"},{"en":"This phrase accepts that something will happen with mixed consequences.","zh":"這個片語承認某事會發生並帶來好壞參半的後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"tomorrow’s fuel","meaning":"未來燃料","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol may become one of tomorrow’s major fuels.","zh":"乙醇可能成為未來主要燃料之一。"},{"en":"Tomorrow’s fuel means a fuel that may be important in the future.","zh":"tomorrow’s fuel 指未來可能重要的燃料。"},{"en":"Hydrogen is sometimes discussed as one of tomorrow’s fuels for transport.","zh":"氫氣有時被討論為運輸的未來燃料之一。"},{"en":"If a fuel is cleaner and affordable, it may become widely used later.","zh":"如果燃料更潔淨且可負擔，它日後可能被廣泛使用。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when imagining future energy sources.","zh":"這個片語用於想像未來能源來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"agree with the claims of","meaning":"與作者的說法一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether each statement agrees with the claims of the writer.","zh":"考生判斷每項陳述是否與作者的說法一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the claims of the writer means to match what the writer says or argues.","zh":"agree with the claims of the writer 指符合作者所說或所主張的內容。"},{"en":"In a reading test, a statement may agree with the writer even if it uses different words.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，陳述即使用不同字眼，也可能與作者一致。"},{"en":"If a statement adds an idea the writer never mentions, it may not agree with the claims.","zh":"如果陳述加入作者從未提及的想法，它可能不符合作者說法。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in YES, NO, NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於 YES、NO、NOT GIVEN 題型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與作者的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A negative response means the statement contradicts the writer’s views.","zh":"否定答案表示該陳述與作者的觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what that person believes or states.","zh":"contradict the views of someone 指說出與某人相信或陳述相反的內容。"},{"en":"If an author supports cleaner fuels, saying he rejects all alternatives may contradict his view.","zh":"如果作者支持更潔淨燃料，說他拒絕所有替代方案可能與其觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"When a statement directly conflicts with the passage, students should not mark it as true.","zh":"當陳述與篇章直接衝突，學生不應把它標為正確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disagreement with a stated viewpoint.","zh":"這個片語描述與已表明觀點不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"“Not Given” means that it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"“Not Given” 表示無法判斷作者怎樣想。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資料作出判斷。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions price, it is impossible to say whether the fuel is cheap.","zh":"如果篇章從未提及價格，就無法判斷燃料是否便宜。"},{"en":"When evidence is missing, students should avoid guessing from common knowledge.","zh":"當證據缺失，學生應避免用常識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why an answer may be NOT GIVEN.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何答案可能是 NOT GIVEN。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"come into use","meaning":"開始被使用","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol came into wider use during periods of high oil prices.","zh":"乙醇在高油價時期開始被更廣泛使用。"},{"en":"To come into use means to start being used by people or organisations.","zh":"come into use 指開始被人或組織使用。"},{"en":"Online payment came into use in many small shops after customers began asking for it.","zh":"當顧客開始要求後，網上支付在許多小店開始被使用。"},{"en":"If oil becomes expensive, alternative fuels may come into use more quickly.","zh":"如果石油變得昂貴，替代燃料可能更快開始被使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of practical adoption.","zh":"這個片語描述實際採用的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"use more ethanol for transportation","meaning":"使用更多乙醇作運輸燃料","examples":[{"en":"Some countries use more ethanol for transportation than others.","zh":"一些國家比其他國家使用更多乙醇作運輸燃料。"},{"en":"To use more ethanol for transportation means to rely on ethanol more heavily as vehicle fuel.","zh":"use more ethanol for transportation 指更大程度依賴乙醇作車輛燃料。"},{"en":"A country with many ethanol-compatible cars will use more ethanol for transport.","zh":"擁有許多乙醇相容汽車的國家會使用更多乙醇作運輸燃料。"},{"en":"If fuel stations sell ethanol widely, drivers can use it more easily.","zh":"如果加油站廣泛銷售乙醇，司機就更容易使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase compares national or regional fuel habits.","zh":"這個片語比較國家或地區的燃料使用習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"selected food crops","meaning":"指定糧食作物","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol production can increase the value of selected food crops.","zh":"乙醇生產可以提高指定糧食作物的價值。"},{"en":"Selected food crops are particular crops chosen for a specific purpose, such as fuel production.","zh":"selected food crops 是為特定目的選出的某些作物，例如燃料生產。"},{"en":"Corn and sugar cane may be selected food crops for ethanol.","zh":"玉米和甘蔗可能是用於乙醇的指定糧食作物。"},{"en":"If selected food crops become useful for fuel, farmers may plant more of them.","zh":"如果指定糧食作物可用於燃料，農民可能種植更多。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to specific crops, not all foods.","zh":"這個片語指特定作物，而不是所有食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"benefit from production","meaning":"從生產中得益","examples":[{"en":"Not every agricultural industry will necessarily benefit from ethanol production.","zh":"並非每個農業行業都必然從乙醇生產中得益。"},{"en":"To benefit from production means to gain money, jobs, or other advantages because something is being made.","zh":"benefit from production 指因某物被製造而獲得金錢、工作或其他好處。"},{"en":"Local workers may benefit from production if a new factory hires them.","zh":"如果新工廠聘請本地工人，本地工人可能從生產中得益。"},{"en":"If farmers do not own factories or receive higher crop prices, they may not benefit directly.","zh":"如果農民沒有擁有工廠或獲得更高作物價格，他們未必直接受益。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gaining advantage from manufacturing activity.","zh":"這個片語描述從製造活動中獲得好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"primary ethanol fuel","meaning":"以乙醇為主的燃料","examples":[{"en":"E-85 uses ethanol as its primary fuel.","zh":"E-85 使用乙醇作為主要燃料。"},{"en":"Primary ethanol fuel means a fuel in which ethanol is the main energy source.","zh":"primary ethanol fuel 指以乙醇作為主要能源來源的燃料。"},{"en":"A car designed for primary ethanol fuel needs a compatible engine and fuel system.","zh":"為以乙醇為主的燃料而設計的汽車，需要相容引擎和燃料系統。"},{"en":"If ethanol is the main fuel, drivers need stations that supply enough ethanol blend.","zh":"如果乙醇是主要燃料，司機需要有足夠乙醇混合燃料供應的加油站。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fuel where ethanol is not just a small additive.","zh":"這個片語描述乙醇不只是少量添加物的燃料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be extensively tested","meaning":"經過廣泛測試","examples":[{"en":"New fuel blends should be extensively tested before widespread use.","zh":"新燃料混合物在廣泛使用前應經過廣泛測試。"},{"en":"To be extensively tested means to be examined carefully in many conditions.","zh":"be extensively tested 指在多種條件下被仔細檢查。"},{"en":"New medicine must be extensively tested before doctors prescribe it widely.","zh":"新藥在醫生廣泛處方前必須經過廣泛測試。"},{"en":"If a fuel is tested in different engines and climates, hidden problems may be found earlier.","zh":"如果燃料在不同引擎和氣候中測試，隱藏問題可能更早被發現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes thorough safety and performance checking.","zh":"這個片語描述徹底安全和性能檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a list of descriptions","meaning":"一系列描述","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match a list of descriptions with different fuel types.","zh":"考生把一系列描述與不同燃料種類配對。"},{"en":"A list of descriptions is a set of statements explaining features, uses, or qualities.","zh":"list of descriptions 是一組解釋特徵、用途或質素的陳述。"},{"en":"A reading exercise may give a list of descriptions and ask students to match them with paragraphs.","zh":"閱讀練習可能提供一系列描述，要求學生與段落配對。"},{"en":"If descriptions are similar, students must read carefully for exact meaning.","zh":"如果描述相似，學生必須仔細閱讀確切意思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a group of clues in a matching task.","zh":"這個片語描述配對題中的一組線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"match each description to","meaning":"把每項描述配對至……","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match each description to the appropriate type of fuel.","zh":"考生把每項描述配對至適當燃料種類。"},{"en":"To match each description to something means to connect every statement with the correct category or answer.","zh":"match each description to something 指把每項陳述連接到正確類別或答案。"},{"en":"Students may match each description to the correct character in a story.","zh":"學生可能把每項描述配對至故事中的正確人物。"},{"en":"If one description mentions diesel, it should not be matched to petrol carelessly.","zh":"如果某描述提到柴油，就不應草率配對至汽油。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in classification tasks.","zh":"這個片語是分類題中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"fuel type","meaning":"燃料種類","examples":[{"en":"The exercise compares four different fuel types.","zh":"練習比較四種不同燃料種類。"},{"en":"A fuel type is a category of fuel, such as petrol, diesel, ethanol, or electricity.","zh":"fuel type 是燃料類別，例如汽油、柴油、乙醇或電力。"},{"en":"Drivers must choose the correct fuel type for their vehicle.","zh":"司機必須為車輛選擇正確燃料種類。"},{"en":"If the wrong fuel type is used, the engine may be damaged.","zh":"如果使用錯誤燃料種類，引擎可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to categories of energy used to power vehicles or machines.","zh":"這個片語指為車輛或機器供能的能源類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"use a letter more than once","meaning":"多次使用同一字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates may use the same letter more than once.","zh":"考生可以多次使用同一字母。"},{"en":"To use a letter more than once means the same answer option can be repeated.","zh":"use a letter more than once 指同一答案選項可以重複使用。"},{"en":"In a matching task, answer B may be used for two different descriptions.","zh":"在配對題中，答案 B 可能用於兩項不同描述。"},{"en":"If students assume each letter can be used only once, they may make avoidable mistakes.","zh":"如果學生假設每個字母只能用一次，可能犯可避免錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase explains an exam rule about repeated answers.","zh":"這個片語解釋關於重複答案的考試規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"regular gasoline","meaning":"普通汽油","examples":[{"en":"Regular gasoline is a conventional vehicle fuel.","zh":"普通汽油是一種傳統車用燃料。"},{"en":"Regular gasoline is ordinary petrol commonly used in many cars.","zh":"regular gasoline 是許多汽車常用的普通汽油。"},{"en":"A driver may choose regular gasoline if the car does not require a special fuel.","zh":"如果汽車不需要特殊燃料，司機可能選擇普通汽油。"},{"en":"If regular gasoline is cheaper than alternatives, many drivers may keep using it.","zh":"如果普通汽油比替代品便宜，許多司機可能繼續使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to standard petrol used in everyday vehicles.","zh":"這個片語指日常車輛使用的標準汽油。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"unleaded gasoline","meaning":"無鉛汽油","examples":[{"en":"Unleaded gasoline is blended with ethanol in E10 and E-85.","zh":"在 E10 和 E-85 中，無鉛汽油與乙醇混合。"},{"en":"Unleaded gasoline is petrol without lead additives.","zh":"unleaded gasoline 是不含鉛添加劑的汽油。"},{"en":"Most modern petrol cars are designed to use unleaded gasoline.","zh":"大多數現代汽油車都設計成使用無鉛汽油。"},{"en":"If unleaded gasoline is mixed with ethanol, the final blend may produce different emissions.","zh":"如果無鉛汽油與乙醇混合，最終混合燃料可能產生不同排放。"},{"en":"This phrase names a common modern vehicle fuel.","zh":"這個片語指出一種常見現代車用燃料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"diesel","meaning":"柴油","examples":[{"en":"Diesel is widely used in heavy transport.","zh":"柴油廣泛用於重型運輸。"},{"en":"Diesel is a fuel commonly used in trucks, buses, ships, and some cars.","zh":"diesel 是常用於貨車、巴士、船隻和一些汽車的燃料。"},{"en":"A delivery company may choose diesel vehicles for long-distance routes.","zh":"速遞公司可能為長途路線選擇柴油車輛。"},{"en":"If diesel prices rise, transport costs can increase across the economy.","zh":"如果柴油價格上升，整個經濟的運輸成本可能增加。"},{"en":"This word refers to a powerful fuel often used for heavy vehicles.","zh":"這個詞指常用於重型車輛的強力燃料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"cost about half the price of","meaning":"價格約為……的一半","examples":[{"en":"Unleaded petrol may cost about half the price of ethanol.","zh":"無鉛汽油價格可能約為乙醇的一半。"},{"en":"To cost about half the price of something means to be roughly 50 percent as expensive as it.","zh":"cost about half the price of something 指價格大約是某物的百分之五十。"},{"en":"A second-hand textbook may cost about half the price of a new one.","zh":"二手教科書價格可能約為新書的一半。"},{"en":"If one fuel costs only half as much, consumers may prefer it unless the alternative has clear benefits.","zh":"如果一種燃料成本只有一半，除非替代品有明顯好處，消費者可能偏好較便宜者。"},{"en":"This phrase compares prices in a simple way.","zh":"這個片語以簡單方式比較價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"react poorly with","meaning":"與……產生不良反應","examples":[{"en":"Some materials react poorly with high concentrations of ethanol.","zh":"一些材料與高濃度乙醇產生不良反應。"},{"en":"To react poorly with something means to be damaged or affected badly when in contact with it.","zh":"react poorly with something 指接觸某物時受到損害或有不良影響。"},{"en":"Some skin reacts poorly with strong soap and becomes dry or red.","zh":"有些皮膚與強力肥皂產生不良反應，變得乾燥或發紅。"},{"en":"If vehicle materials react poorly with ethanol, fuel systems may deteriorate.","zh":"如果車輛材料與乙醇產生不良反應，燃料系統可能劣化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unsuitable chemical or physical interaction.","zh":"這個片語描述不合適的化學或物理相互作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be fitted with","meaning":"裝設有……","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol trucks may be fitted with larger fuel tanks.","zh":"乙醇貨車可能裝設有較大的油缸。"},{"en":"To be fitted with something means to have that part installed or attached.","zh":"be fitted with something 指安裝或附有某部件。"},{"en":"A classroom may be fitted with new speakers and a projector.","zh":"課室可能裝設有新揚聲器和投影機。"},{"en":"If trucks need more fuel storage, they may be fitted with larger tanks.","zh":"如果貨車需要更多燃料儲存空間，它們可能裝設較大油缸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes equipment being added to something.","zh":"這個片語描述某物被加裝設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"larger fuel tanks","meaning":"較大的油缸","examples":[{"en":"Lower energy content means that trucks need larger fuel tanks.","zh":"較低能量含量意味着貨車需要較大的油缸。"},{"en":"Larger fuel tanks are bigger containers for storing fuel in vehicles.","zh":"larger fuel tanks 是車輛中用來儲存燃料的較大容器。"},{"en":"Long-distance buses may need larger fuel tanks if refuelling points are far apart.","zh":"如果加油點相距很遠，長途巴士可能需要較大的油缸。"},{"en":"If a fuel provides less energy per litre, carrying more fuel can help maintain range.","zh":"如果每公升燃料提供較少能量，攜帶更多燃料可以幫助維持續航。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a design response to fuel needs.","zh":"這個片語指對燃料需求的設計回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"trucking industry","meaning":"貨運業","examples":[{"en":"Diesel is commonly used in the trucking industry.","zh":"柴油常用於貨運業。"},{"en":"The trucking industry is the business of transporting goods by trucks.","zh":"trucking industry 是透過貨車運送貨物的行業。"},{"en":"Supermarkets depend on the trucking industry to deliver food to stores.","zh":"超級市場依靠貨運業把食物送到店舖。"},{"en":"If fuel costs rise, the trucking industry may raise delivery charges.","zh":"如果燃料成本上升，貨運業可能提高送貨費。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to road freight transport businesses.","zh":"這個片語指道路貨物運輸行業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"classify statements according to","meaning":"按照……把陳述分類","examples":[{"en":"Candidates classify the statements according to the country they apply to.","zh":"考生按照陳述適用的國家把它們分類。"},{"en":"To classify statements according to something means to sort them into groups based on that feature.","zh":"classify statements according to something 指根據某特徵把陳述分組。"},{"en":"Students may classify examples according to whether they describe cause, effect, or contrast.","zh":"學生可能按照例子描述原因、結果或對比來分類。"},{"en":"If a statement applies to both countries, it should not be forced into only one group.","zh":"如果陳述適用於兩個國家，就不應強行只歸入一組。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organising information by category.","zh":"這個片語描述按類別組織資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"apply to","meaning":"適用於……","examples":[{"en":"Each statement may apply to one country, both countries or neither country.","zh":"每項陳述可能適用於一個國家、兩個國家或兩者皆不適用。"},{"en":"To apply to something means to be relevant or true for it.","zh":"apply to something 指對某事相關或屬實。"},{"en":"A school rule may apply to all students, not only senior forms.","zh":"學校規則可能適用於所有學生，而不只是高中。"},{"en":"If a description applies to both cases, students must mark both rather than choose randomly.","zh":"如果描述適用於兩種情況，學生必須標示兩者，而不是隨便選。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relevance or suitability.","zh":"這個片語描述相關性或適用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the appropriate letters","meaning":"適當的字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the appropriate letters in the answer boxes.","zh":"考生在答案框中寫上適當的字母。"},{"en":"The appropriate letters are the correct letter choices for the answers.","zh":"appropriate letters 是答案的正確字母選項。"},{"en":"If a statement applies to both countries, students must write the letters showing both.","zh":"如果陳述適用於兩個國家，學生必須寫上表示兩者的字母。"},{"en":"Using the wrong letter can lose marks even when the idea is understood.","zh":"即使理解意思，使用錯誤字母也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds students to follow the answer-code system.","zh":"這個片語提醒學生遵守答案代碼系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"make ethanol from sugar cane","meaning":"以甘蔗製造乙醇","examples":[{"en":"Some countries make ethanol from sugar cane.","zh":"一些國家以甘蔗製造乙醇。"},{"en":"To make ethanol from sugar cane means to use sugar cane as the raw material for ethanol production.","zh":"make ethanol from sugar cane 指使用甘蔗作為乙醇生產的原材料。"},{"en":"A factory may crush sugar cane and ferment its sugars to produce ethanol.","zh":"工廠可能壓榨甘蔗並發酵其中糖分來製造乙醇。"},{"en":"If a country grows a lot of sugar cane, it may have a natural supply for ethanol fuel.","zh":"如果國家種植大量甘蔗，它可能有天然乙醇燃料供應來源。"},{"en":"This phrase links ethanol production with a specific crop.","zh":"這個片語把乙醇生產與特定作物連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"receive government assistance","meaning":"獲得政府援助","examples":[{"en":"Ethanol producers may receive government assistance.","zh":"乙醇生產商可能獲得政府援助。"},{"en":"To receive government assistance means to get support from the government, such as subsidies or tax benefits.","zh":"receive government assistance 指獲得政府支持，例如補貼或稅務優惠。"},{"en":"Farmers may receive government assistance after drought destroys their crops.","zh":"乾旱摧毀作物後，農民可能獲得政府援助。"},{"en":"If ethanol is too costly to produce, assistance can help companies stay competitive.","zh":"如果乙醇生產成本太高，援助可以幫助公司保持競爭力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes getting official support.","zh":"這個片語描述獲得官方支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"prove that production is costly","meaning":"證明生產成本高昂","examples":[{"en":"Studies may prove that ethanol production is costly.","zh":"研究可能證明乙醇生產成本高昂。"},{"en":"To prove that production is costly means to show with evidence that making something requires a lot of money.","zh":"prove that production is costly 指用證據顯示製造某物需要大量金錢。"},{"en":"A school budget review may prove that running a swimming pool is costly.","zh":"學校預算檢討可能證明營運游泳池成本高昂。"},{"en":"If production is proven costly, governments may consider subsidies or cheaper technology.","zh":"如果生產被證明成本高昂，政府可能考慮補貼或較便宜科技。"},{"en":"This phrase connects evidence with high manufacturing expense.","zh":"這個片語把證據與高製造成本連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"ethanol-friendly vehicles","meaning":"適合使用乙醇燃料的車輛","examples":[{"en":"Some governments have purchased ethanol-friendly vehicles for official fleets.","zh":"一些政府為官方車隊購買適合使用乙醇燃料的車輛。"},{"en":"Ethanol-friendly vehicles are vehicles designed or approved to use ethanol-blended fuels safely.","zh":"ethanol-friendly vehicles 是設計或獲准安全使用乙醇混合燃料的車輛。"},{"en":"A driver should check the manual before assuming a car is ethanol-friendly.","zh":"司機不應假設汽車適合乙醇燃料，而應先查看手冊。"},{"en":"If governments buy ethanol-friendly vehicles, they can support demand for ethanol fuel.","zh":"如果政府購買適合使用乙醇燃料的車輛，就能支持乙醇燃料需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes vehicles compatible with ethanol fuels.","zh":"這個片語描述與乙醇燃料相容的車輛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 123 - FUELING THE FUTURE.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 124":[{"front":"forces of gravitation","meaning":"萬有引力","examples":[{"en":"Without forces of gravitation, planets could not remain in orbit.","zh":"沒有萬有引力，行星就不能維持在軌道上。"},{"en":"Forces of gravitation are the attractive forces between objects that have mass.","zh":"forces of gravitation 指有質量物體之間的吸引力。"},{"en":"The forces of gravitation keep the Moon close to Earth instead of letting it fly away.","zh":"萬有引力使月球靠近地球，而不是飛離。"},{"en":"If these forces disappeared, planets, moons, and satellites would no longer follow stable paths.","zh":"如果這些力消失，行星、月球和衛星就不再沿穩定路徑運行。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to gravity acting between bodies in space.","zh":"這個片語指太空中物體之間的重力作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be unable to","meaning":"無法……","examples":[{"en":"Without gravitation, Earth would be unable to stay in its orbit.","zh":"沒有萬有引力，地球就無法維持在其軌道上。"},{"en":"Be unable to means not have the ability or possibility to do something.","zh":"be unable to 指沒有能力或可能性做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be unable to finish homework if the instructions are unclear.","zh":"如果指示不清楚，學生可能無法完成功課。"},{"en":"If a machine loses power, it may be unable to operate safely.","zh":"如果機器失去電力，它可能無法安全運作。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something cannot happen because a necessary condition is missing.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事因缺少必要條件而不能發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"stay in orbit","meaning":"維持在軌道上","examples":[{"en":"Gravity allows planets to stay in orbit around the Sun.","zh":"重力使行星能夠圍繞太陽維持在軌道上。"},{"en":"Stay in orbit means continue moving around another object in a stable path.","zh":"stay in orbit 指繼續沿穩定路徑圍繞另一物體運行。"},{"en":"A satellite must stay in orbit to keep sending weather data back to Earth.","zh":"衛星必須維持在軌道上，才能持續把天氣數據傳回地球。"},{"en":"If a spacecraft slows down too much, it may fail to stay in orbit and fall back.","zh":"如果太空船減速太多，就可能無法維持在軌道上並墜回。"},{"en":"The phrase describes controlled movement around a larger body.","zh":"這個片語描述圍繞較大天體的受控運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"orbit the Earth","meaning":"環繞地球運行","examples":[{"en":"The Moon is able to orbit the Earth because of gravity.","zh":"月球因重力而能夠環繞地球運行。"},{"en":"Orbit the Earth means move around Earth in a curved path.","zh":"orbit the Earth 指沿彎曲路徑圍繞地球移動。"},{"en":"Communication satellites orbit the Earth so phones and televisions can receive signals.","zh":"通訊衛星環繞地球運行，讓電話和電視能接收訊號。"},{"en":"If an object moves too slowly, it cannot orbit the Earth successfully.","zh":"如果物體移動得太慢，就不能成功環繞地球運行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes circular or elliptical movement around our planet.","zh":"這個片語描述圍繞我們星球的圓形或橢圓形運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tidal waves","meaning":"潮汐","examples":[{"en":"The gravitational pull of the Moon contributes to tidal waves.","zh":"月球的引力有助形成潮汐。"},{"en":"Tidal waves are large movements of seawater linked to tides and gravitational effects.","zh":"tidal waves 指與潮汐和引力作用有關的大規模海水運動。"},{"en":"People living near the coast pay attention to tides because sea levels can rise and fall each day.","zh":"住在海岸附近的人會留意潮汐，因為海平面每天會升降。"},{"en":"If the Moon pulls on Earth’s oceans, the water level changes and tides are produced.","zh":"如果月球拉動地球海洋，水位就會改變並產生潮汐。"},{"en":"The phrase is connected with the movement of ocean water.","zh":"這個片語與海水運動有關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"convection of hot air or water","meaning":"熱空氣或熱水的對流","examples":[{"en":"Gravity makes the convection of hot air or water possible.","zh":"重力使熱空氣或熱水的對流成為可能。"},{"en":"Convection of hot air or water is the movement caused when warmer, lighter material rises and cooler material sinks.","zh":"convection of hot air or water 指較暖、較輕物質上升，而較冷物質下沉所造成的流動。"},{"en":"Hot air rises above a heater, while cooler air moves in to replace it.","zh":"暖氣機上方的熱空氣會上升，而較冷空氣會移入取代它。"},{"en":"If gravity did not pull cooler, denser material downward, convection would not work in the same way.","zh":"如果重力沒有把較冷、較密的物質向下拉，對流就不會以同樣方式運作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes heat transfer through moving air or liquid.","zh":"這個片語描述透過空氣或液體流動進行的熱傳遞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"gravitational phenomenon","meaning":"引力現象","examples":[{"en":"Gravitation is a phenomenon that causes matter to attract other matter.","zh":"萬有引力是一種使物質吸引其他物質的現象。"},{"en":"A gravitational phenomenon is an event or effect caused by gravity or attraction between masses.","zh":"gravitational phenomenon 指由重力或質量之間的吸引造成的事件或效果。"},{"en":"The tides are a familiar gravitational phenomenon because the Moon pulls on Earth’s oceans.","zh":"潮汐是熟悉的引力現象，因為月球拉動地球海洋。"},{"en":"If objects with mass attract one another, the result can be described as gravitational.","zh":"如果有質量的物體互相吸引，其結果可以被描述為引力作用。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when explaining effects produced by gravity.","zh":"這個片語用於解釋由重力產生的效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"allow objects to attract","meaning":"使物體能夠吸引……","examples":[{"en":"Gravitation allows objects to attract other matter.","zh":"萬有引力使物體能夠吸引其他物質。"},{"en":"Allow objects to attract means make it possible for things with mass to pull other things towards them.","zh":"allow objects to attract 指使有質量的物體能把其他物體拉向自己。"},{"en":"Earth’s gravity allows objects to attract towards its surface.","zh":"地球重力使物體能被吸引到其表面。"},{"en":"If an object has more mass, its ability to attract other matter is usually stronger.","zh":"如果物體質量較大，它吸引其他物質的能力通常較強。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what gravitation enables objects to do.","zh":"這個片語解釋萬有引力使物體能做甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"attract other matter","meaning":"吸引其他物質","examples":[{"en":"Objects with mass can attract other matter through gravitation.","zh":"有質量的物體可以透過萬有引力吸引其他物質。"},{"en":"Attract other matter means pull other physical material towards oneself.","zh":"attract other matter 指把其他實體物質拉向自己。"},{"en":"A magnet attracts metal, but gravity allows masses to attract other matter.","zh":"磁石吸引金屬，而重力使有質量物體吸引其他物質。"},{"en":"If a planet has enough mass, it can attract gas, dust, and moons.","zh":"如果行星有足夠質量，它可以吸引氣體、塵埃和衛星。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the pulling effect of an object.","zh":"這個片語描述物體的拉動效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"theory of relativity","meaning":"相對論","examples":[{"en":"The theory of relativity helps explain the physics of gravity.","zh":"相對論有助解釋重力的物理學。"},{"en":"The theory of relativity is Einstein’s theory explaining space, time, motion, and gravity in a new way.","zh":"theory of relativity 指愛因斯坦以新方式解釋空間、時間、運動和重力的理論。"},{"en":"Students may first hear about the theory of relativity when learning why time and space are not fixed.","zh":"學生學習時間和空間並非固定時，可能首次聽到相對論。"},{"en":"If gravity is linked to curved space-time, relativity gives a deeper explanation than simple pulling.","zh":"如果重力與彎曲時空有關，相對論就比簡單拉力提供更深解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a major modern scientific theory.","zh":"這個片語指一項重要現代科學理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Newton’s law of universal gravitation","meaning":"牛頓萬有引力定律","examples":[{"en":"Newton’s law of universal gravitation explains the attraction between masses.","zh":"牛頓萬有引力定律解釋質量之間的吸引。"},{"en":"Newton’s law of universal gravitation says that every mass attracts every other mass.","zh":"Newton’s law of universal gravitation 指每個有質量物體都會吸引其他有質量物體的定律。"},{"en":"A physics class may use this law to calculate the force between Earth and the Moon.","zh":"物理課可能使用這條定律計算地球與月球之間的力。"},{"en":"If two objects have greater mass or are closer together, their gravitational attraction becomes stronger.","zh":"如果兩個物體質量更大或距離更近，它們之間的引力會更強。"},{"en":"The phrase names Newton’s classic explanation of gravity.","zh":"這個片語指出牛頓對重力的經典解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"attempts to explain","meaning":"解釋……的嘗試","examples":[{"en":"Attempts to explain gravity date back to ancient times.","zh":"解釋重力的嘗試可追溯至古代。"},{"en":"Attempts to explain are efforts to understand or describe why something happens.","zh":"attempts to explain 指努力理解或描述某事為何發生。"},{"en":"Teachers make attempts to explain grammar by using simple examples and clear rules.","zh":"老師會透過簡單例子和清楚規則嘗試解釋文法。"},{"en":"If people do not understand a natural event, they create theories to explain it.","zh":"如果人們不理解自然事件，就會建立理論來解釋它。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the process of trying to understand.","zh":"這個片語強調嘗試理解的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"date back to","meaning":"追溯至……","examples":[{"en":"The earliest theories of gravity date back to ancient times.","zh":"最早的重力理論可追溯至古代。"},{"en":"Date back to means have existed since a particular time in the past.","zh":"date back to 指自過去某個時期以來已經存在。"},{"en":"Some local festivals date back to farming traditions hundreds of years ago.","zh":"有些本地節日可追溯至數百年前的農業傳統。"},{"en":"If an idea dates back to ancient times, people have discussed it for a very long period.","zh":"如果一個想法追溯至古代，人們已討論它很長時間。"},{"en":"The phrase connects something today with its historical origin.","zh":"這個片語把今天的事物與其歷史起源連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ancient times","meaning":"古代","examples":[{"en":"People have attempted to explain gravity since ancient times.","zh":"人們自古代以來已嘗試解釋重力。"},{"en":"Ancient times refers to a very early period in human history.","zh":"ancient times 指人類歷史中非常早期的時期。"},{"en":"Ancient times include the eras of early Greek, Egyptian, Chinese, and Roman civilisations.","zh":"古代包括早期希臘、埃及、中國和羅馬文明時期。"},{"en":"If an idea began in ancient times, modern science may have developed from very old questions.","zh":"如果一個想法始於古代，現代科學可能由非常古老的問題發展而來。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a broad historical period, not an exact date.","zh":"這個片語給出廣闊歷史時期，而不是精確日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Greek philosopher","meaning":"希臘哲學家","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle was an influential Greek philosopher.","zh":"亞里士多德是一位具影響力的希臘哲學家。"},{"en":"A Greek philosopher was a thinker from ancient Greece who studied questions about nature, knowledge, and life.","zh":"Greek philosopher 指來自古希臘、研究自然、知識和人生問題的思想家。"},{"en":"Students often learn about Greek philosophers when studying the origins of Western science.","zh":"學生研究西方科學起源時，常會學到希臘哲學家。"},{"en":"If a philosopher’s ideas shaped later beliefs, those ideas may remain influential for centuries.","zh":"如果哲學家的思想塑造後來信念，那些思想可能影響幾百年。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a thinker from ancient Greek intellectual tradition.","zh":"這個片語描述古希臘知識傳統中的思想家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"develop the hypothesis that","meaning":"提出……的假說","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle developed the hypothesis that objects were drawn to their correct positions.","zh":"亞里士多德提出物體會被吸引到其正確位置的假說。"},{"en":"Develop the hypothesis that means form a possible explanation for something.","zh":"develop the hypothesis that 指形成對某事的可能解釋。"},{"en":"A doctor may develop the hypothesis that poor sleep is causing a patient’s headaches.","zh":"醫生可能提出睡眠不足導致病人頭痛的假說。"},{"en":"If evidence supports a hypothesis, researchers may test it more seriously.","zh":"如果證據支持某假說，研究人員可能更認真測試它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes building a tentative explanation.","zh":"這個片語描述建立暫時性解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be drawn into","meaning":"被吸引至……","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle believed that objects were drawn into their correct positions.","zh":"亞里士多德相信物體會被吸引至其正確位置。"},{"en":"Be drawn into means be pulled or attracted towards a place or situation.","zh":"be drawn into 指被拉向或吸引到某地方或情況中。"},{"en":"A child may be drawn into a story when the characters feel real.","zh":"當角色感覺真實，孩子可能被故事吸引。"},{"en":"If an object is drawn toward Earth, gravity is pulling it downward.","zh":"如果物體被吸向地球，重力正在把它向下拉。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe physical attraction or involvement in a situation.","zh":"這個片語既可描述物理吸引，也可描述捲入某情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"correct position","meaning":"正確位置","examples":[{"en":"Ancient thinkers believed that every object had a correct position.","zh":"古代思想家相信每個物體都有正確位置。"},{"en":"A correct position is the place where something is thought to belong or function properly.","zh":"correct position 指某物被認為應該屬於或正常運作的位置。"},{"en":"In a classroom, desks must be in the correct position so students can see the board.","zh":"在課室中，書桌必須放在正確位置，學生才能看見黑板。"},{"en":"If a machine part is not in the correct position, the machine may stop working.","zh":"如果機器零件不在正確位置，機器可能停止運作。"},{"en":"The phrase means the proper place for something.","zh":"這個片語指某物的合適位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"crystalline spheres","meaning":"水晶天球","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle believed that crystalline spheres guided objects into position.","zh":"亞里士多德相信水晶天球引導物體到其位置。"},{"en":"Crystalline spheres were imaginary transparent spheres once thought to carry heavenly bodies.","zh":"crystalline spheres 指古人想像中承載天體的透明球體。"},{"en":"Ancient astronomy sometimes imagined planets attached to perfect invisible spheres.","zh":"古代天文學有時想像行星附着在完美的隱形球體上。"},{"en":"If people lacked modern telescopes and physics, crystalline spheres offered an early explanation of the sky.","zh":"如果人們沒有現代望遠鏡和物理學，水晶天球就提供了早期天空解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase belongs to an old model of the universe.","zh":"這個片語屬於舊宇宙模型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"physical mass","meaning":"實體質量","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle believed that a physical mass would fall towards the Earth.","zh":"亞里士多德相信實體質量會向地球墜落。"},{"en":"Physical mass means a material object with measurable matter.","zh":"physical mass 指具有可量度物質的實體物件。"},{"en":"A stone, a book, and a person all have physical mass.","zh":"石頭、書本和人都有實體質量。"},{"en":"If something has physical mass, gravity can act on it.","zh":"如果某物有實體質量，重力就能作用於它。"},{"en":"The phrase separates real material objects from abstract ideas.","zh":"這個片語把真實物質物體與抽象概念分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fall towards the Earth","meaning":"向地球墜落","examples":[{"en":"A physical mass falls towards the Earth because of gravity.","zh":"實體質量因重力而向地球墜落。"},{"en":"Fall towards the Earth means move downward in the direction of Earth’s surface.","zh":"fall towards the Earth 指向地球表面方向向下移動。"},{"en":"A dropped pencil will fall towards the Earth rather than float in the air.","zh":"掉下的鉛筆會向地球墜落，而不是漂浮在空中。"},{"en":"If gravity pulls an object downward, it accelerates towards the ground.","zh":"如果重力把物體向下拉，它就會向地面加速。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the everyday effect of Earth’s gravity.","zh":"這個片語描述地球重力的日常效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in direct proportion to","meaning":"與……成正比","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle believed that falling speed was in direct proportion to weight.","zh":"亞里士多德相信下墜速度與重量成正比。"},{"en":"In direct proportion to means one thing increases or decreases at the same rate as another.","zh":"in direct proportion to 指一件事隨另一件事以相同比例增加或減少。"},{"en":"In some jobs, pay is in direct proportion to the number of hours worked.","zh":"在某些工作中，薪金與工作時數成正比。"},{"en":"If cost is in direct proportion to weight, a heavier parcel costs more to send.","zh":"如果費用與重量成正比，較重包裹寄送費用就較高。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a clear mathematical relationship.","zh":"這個片語描述清楚的數學關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the late 16th century","meaning":"在十六世紀末","examples":[{"en":"Galileo developed new ideas about gravity in the late 16th century.","zh":"伽利略在十六世紀末發展出關於重力的新想法。"},{"en":"In the late 16th century means during the later years of the 1500s.","zh":"in the late 16th century 指在1500年代後期。"},{"en":"A history lesson may discuss scientific change in the late 16th century and early 17th century.","zh":"歷史課可能討論十六世紀末和十七世紀初的科學變化。"},{"en":"If an idea appeared in the late 16th century, it came before much of modern physics.","zh":"如果一個想法出現在十六世紀末，它就早於許多現代物理學。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate historical period.","zh":"這個片語給出大約歷史時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"deduce that","meaning":"推斷","examples":[{"en":"Galileo deduced that gravity propels all objects at the same rate.","zh":"伽利略推斷重力以相同速度推動所有物體。"},{"en":"Deduce that means reach a conclusion by reasoning from evidence.","zh":"deduce that 指根據證據和推理得出結論。"},{"en":"A teacher may deduce that students are confused if many make the same mistake.","zh":"如果許多學生犯同一錯誤，老師可能推斷他們感到困惑。"},{"en":"If observations do not match an old belief, scientists may deduce a new explanation.","zh":"如果觀察與舊信念不吻合，科學家可能推斷出新解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful reasoning, not random guessing.","zh":"這個片語描述仔細推理，而不是隨意猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"propel objects to the ground","meaning":"推動物體落向地面","examples":[{"en":"Gravitation propels objects towards the ground.","zh":"萬有引力推動物體落向地面。"},{"en":"Propel objects to the ground means push or pull objects downward until they reach the ground.","zh":"propel objects to the ground 指推動或拉動物體向下，直到到達地面。"},{"en":"Gravity propels a dropped ball to the ground after it leaves a child’s hand.","zh":"球離開孩子手後，重力推動它落向地面。"},{"en":"If nothing supports an object, gravity causes it to move downward.","zh":"如果沒有東西支撐物體，重力會使它向下移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the downward motion caused by gravity.","zh":"這個片語描述由重力造成的向下運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at the same rate","meaning":"以相同速度","examples":[{"en":"Galileo argued that objects fall at the same rate without air resistance.","zh":"伽利略主張在沒有空氣阻力下，物體會以相同速度下墜。"},{"en":"At the same rate means at equal speed or with the same level of change.","zh":"at the same rate 指以相同速度或相同變化程度。"},{"en":"Two runners moving at the same rate stay side by side.","zh":"兩名跑手以相同速度前進時，會並排而行。"},{"en":"If there is no air resistance, objects of different weights can accelerate equally.","zh":"如果沒有空氣阻力，不同重量物體可以同樣加速。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when comparing speed or change.","zh":"這個片語用於比較速度或變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"air resistance","meaning":"空氣阻力","examples":[{"en":"Air resistance can affect how quickly an object appears to fall.","zh":"空氣阻力可以影響物體看起來下墜得多快。"},{"en":"Air resistance is the force of air pushing against a moving object.","zh":"air resistance 指空氣對移動物體產生的阻力。"},{"en":"A feather falls slowly because air resistance affects it more than a stone.","zh":"羽毛下墜得慢，因為空氣阻力對它的影響比石頭更大。"},{"en":"If an object has a large surface area, air resistance can slow it down.","zh":"如果物體表面面積很大，空氣阻力可以令它減速。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why some falling objects seem slower than others.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何有些下墜物體看起來較慢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"result in","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"Air resistance can result in heavier objects appearing to fall faster.","zh":"空氣阻力可以導致較重物體看起來下墜得較快。"},{"en":"Result in means cause something to happen.","zh":"result in 指造成某事發生。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can result in weak concentration during lessons.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致上課時專注力差。"},{"en":"If air resistance slows light objects more, heavier objects may appear to reach the ground first.","zh":"如果空氣阻力使較輕物體減速更多，較重物體可能看起來先到達地面。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a cause with an outcome.","zh":"這個片語把原因與結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"appear to fall more quickly","meaning":"看起來下墜得較快","examples":[{"en":"Heavier objects may appear to fall more quickly because of air resistance.","zh":"較重物體可能因空氣阻力而看起來下墜得較快。"},{"en":"Appear to fall more quickly means seem to move downward faster, even if the deeper cause is different.","zh":"appear to fall more quickly 指看似向下移動得更快，即使深層原因不同。"},{"en":"A flat sheet of paper appears to fall more slowly than a crumpled one because air pushes against it.","zh":"平鋪紙張因受空氣阻擋，看起來比揉成團的紙下墜得慢。"},{"en":"If air resistance affects objects differently, what we see may not reveal the full rule.","zh":"如果空氣阻力對物體影響不同，我們看到的未必顯示完整規律。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses visible appearance, not necessarily true acceleration.","zh":"這個片語強調可見表象，而不一定是真正加速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"contradict earlier beliefs","meaning":"與早期觀念相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"Galileo’s theories contradicted earlier beliefs about falling objects.","zh":"伽利略的理論與早期關於下墜物體的觀念相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradict earlier beliefs means go against ideas that people previously accepted.","zh":"contradict earlier beliefs 指與人們先前接受的想法相反。"},{"en":"New medical research may contradict earlier beliefs about what causes a disease.","zh":"新醫學研究可能與早期關於疾病成因的觀念相矛盾。"},{"en":"If experiments show a different result, old beliefs must be questioned.","zh":"如果實驗顯示不同結果，舊觀念就必須被質疑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes conflict between new evidence and old ideas.","zh":"這個片語描述新證據與舊想法之間的衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"belief systems","meaning":"信念體系","examples":[{"en":"Galileo challenged belief systems established by Aristotle.","zh":"伽利略挑戰了亞里士多德建立的信念體系。"},{"en":"Belief systems are organised sets of ideas that shape how people understand the world.","zh":"belief systems 指一套有組織、影響人們如何理解世界的想法。"},{"en":"A school’s belief system about learning affects how teachers treat mistakes.","zh":"學校對學習的信念體系會影響老師如何看待錯誤。"},{"en":"If a belief system becomes too rigid, new evidence may be ignored.","zh":"如果信念體系太僵化，新證據可能被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to connected ideas, not one isolated opinion.","zh":"這個片語指互相關連的想法，而不是單一意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"established by","meaning":"由……建立","examples":[{"en":"Earlier theories had been established by Aristotle and other thinkers.","zh":"早期理論由亞里士多德和其他思想家建立。"},{"en":"Established by means created, developed, or made accepted by someone.","zh":"established by 指由某人創立、發展或使其被接受。"},{"en":"A school rule may be established by the principal and teachers.","zh":"學校規則可能由校長和老師建立。"},{"en":"If an idea is established by respected thinkers, people may accept it for a long time.","zh":"如果一個想法由受尊敬的思想家建立，人們可能長期接受它。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who created or gave authority to something.","zh":"這個片語指出誰創造或賦予某事權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pave the way for","meaning":"為……鋪路","examples":[{"en":"Galileo’s work paved the way for modern theories of gravity.","zh":"伽利略的研究為現代重力理論鋪路。"},{"en":"Pave the way for means make later progress or development possible.","zh":"pave the way for 指使後來的進步或發展成為可能。"},{"en":"Learning basic grammar can pave the way for stronger writing.","zh":"學好基本文法可以為更強寫作能力鋪路。"},{"en":"If one discovery changes how people think, it can prepare the ground for later theories.","zh":"如果一項發現改變人們思考方式，就能為後來理論奠定基礎。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an important earlier step.","zh":"這個片語描述重要的早期步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"formulation of modern theories","meaning":"現代理論的建立","examples":[{"en":"Galileo’s research contributed to the formulation of modern theories.","zh":"伽利略的研究促成了現代理論的建立。"},{"en":"Formulation of modern theories means the development and shaping of new scientific explanations.","zh":"formulation of modern theories 指新科學解釋的發展和形成。"},{"en":"Careful classroom observations can contribute to the formulation of better teaching methods.","zh":"仔細課堂觀察可以促成更好教學方法的建立。"},{"en":"If experiments provide clear results, they help scientists build stronger theories.","zh":"如果實驗提供清楚結果，就能幫助科學家建立更有力理論。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on creating organised explanations.","zh":"這個片語集中於創造有組織的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be used interchangeably","meaning":"可互換使用","examples":[{"en":"The terms gravity and gravitation are often used interchangeably.","zh":"gravity 和 gravitation 這兩個詞常可互換使用。"},{"en":"Be used interchangeably means two words are used as if they have the same meaning.","zh":"be used interchangeably 指兩個詞被當作意思相同般使用。"},{"en":"In casual speech, people may use “film” and “movie” interchangeably.","zh":"在日常說話中，人們可能把 “film” 和 “movie” 互換使用。"},{"en":"If two terms are used interchangeably, students may not notice a technical difference between them.","zh":"如果兩個術語可互換使用，學生可能不會注意到它們之間的技術差異。"},{"en":"The phrase describes word usage, not physical exchange.","zh":"這個片語描述詞語用法，而不是實物交換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in everyday speech","meaning":"在日常用語中","examples":[{"en":"The two terms are commonly treated as identical in everyday speech.","zh":"這兩個詞在日常用語中通常被視為相同。"},{"en":"In everyday speech means in ordinary conversation, not in formal or technical writing.","zh":"in everyday speech 指在普通對話中，而不是正式或技術寫作中。"},{"en":"In everyday speech, people often say “weight” when they may technically mean “mass”.","zh":"在日常用語中，人們常說 “weight”，即使技術上可能指 “mass”。"},{"en":"If a word is used loosely in daily conversation, science may still define it more precisely.","zh":"如果一個詞在日常對話中被寬鬆使用，科學仍可能更精確地界定它。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts casual language with specialist language.","zh":"這個片語把日常語言與專門語言作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have distinct meanings","meaning":"有不同的意思","examples":[{"en":"Gravity and gravitation have distinct meanings in scientific usage.","zh":"gravity 和 gravitation 在科學用語中有不同的意思。"},{"en":"Have distinct meanings means have clearly different meanings.","zh":"have distinct meanings 指有清楚不同的意思。"},{"en":"“Borrow” and “lend” have distinct meanings, although learners often confuse them.","zh":"“borrow” 和 “lend” 有不同意思，雖然學習者常混淆。"},{"en":"If two scientific terms have distinct meanings, using them carelessly can cause misunderstanding.","zh":"如果兩個科學術語有不同意思，粗心使用可能造成誤解。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses clear difference.","zh":"這個片語強調清楚差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in scientific usage","meaning":"在科學用語中","examples":[{"en":"The terms have more precise meanings in scientific usage.","zh":"這些詞在科學用語中有更精確的意思。"},{"en":"In scientific usage means in the way words are used by scientists or in scientific writing.","zh":"in scientific usage 指科學家或科學寫作中使用詞語的方式。"},{"en":"In scientific usage, “theory” does not simply mean a casual guess.","zh":"在科學用語中，“theory” 不只是隨便猜測。"},{"en":"If a word has a special scientific meaning, students should not rely only on daily usage.","zh":"如果一個詞有特殊科學意思，學生不應只依賴日常用法。"},{"en":"The phrase points to technical language.","zh":"這個片語指向技術性語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"relate to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Gravitation relates to the influence exerted by objects on other matter.","zh":"萬有引力與物體對其他物質施加的影響有關。"},{"en":"Relate to means be connected with or concern something.","zh":"relate to 指與某事有連繫或涉及某事。"},{"en":"A school policy may relate to attendance, homework, or student safety.","zh":"學校政策可能與出席、功課或學生安全有關。"},{"en":"If a term relates to attraction between masses, it belongs to the study of gravity.","zh":"如果一個術語與質量之間的吸引有關，它就屬於重力研究。"},{"en":"The phrase shows connection or relevance.","zh":"這個片語顯示連繫或相關性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"influence exerted by","meaning":"由……施加的影響","examples":[{"en":"Gravitation describes the influence exerted by objects with mass.","zh":"萬有引力描述由有質量物體施加的影響。"},{"en":"Influence exerted by means the effect or force produced by someone or something.","zh":"influence exerted by 指由某人或某物產生的影響或力量。"},{"en":"The influence exerted by a good teacher can change how students see learning.","zh":"好老師施加的影響可以改變學生對學習的看法。"},{"en":"If a massive planet affects nearby objects, that is an influence exerted through gravity.","zh":"如果巨大行星影響附近物體，那就是透過重力施加的影響。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the source of an effect.","zh":"這個片語突出效果的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"whereas","meaning":"然而；而","examples":[{"en":"Gravitation describes attraction, whereas gravity refers to the force involved.","zh":"gravitation 描述吸引作用，而 gravity 指所涉及的力。"},{"en":"Whereas means while, and it is used to contrast two facts or ideas.","zh":"whereas 指然而或而，用來對比兩個事實或想法。"},{"en":"Some students learn better by reading, whereas others need spoken explanation.","zh":"有些學生透過閱讀學得較好，而另一些則需要口頭解釋。"},{"en":"If one term describes a relationship whereas another describes a force, the distinction matters.","zh":"如果一個術語描述關係，而另一個描述力，區別就很重要。"},{"en":"The word helps compare two different points clearly.","zh":"這個詞幫助清楚比較兩個不同點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"refer specifically to","meaning":"特別指……","examples":[{"en":"Gravity refers specifically to the force possessed by an object.","zh":"gravity 特別指物體所具有的力。"},{"en":"Refer specifically to means point to one exact thing rather than a general idea.","zh":"refer specifically to 指指向某個確切事物，而不是籠統概念。"},{"en":"In a school notice, “Form Six students” refers specifically to the final-year students.","zh":"在學校通告中，“Form Six students” 特別指最後一年級學生。"},{"en":"If a term refers specifically to force, it should not be used for every related concept.","zh":"如果術語特別指力，就不應用於每個相關概念。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows the meaning.","zh":"這個片語收窄意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"force possessed by","meaning":"……所具有的力","examples":[{"en":"Gravity is the force possessed by an object with mass.","zh":"重力是有質量物體所具有的力。"},{"en":"Force possessed by means the force that something has because of its nature or properties.","zh":"force possessed by 指某物因其性質或特徵而具有的力。"},{"en":"A strong magnet has a force possessed by its magnetic material.","zh":"強磁石具有由其磁性材料產生的力。"},{"en":"If an object has more mass, the gravitational force it possesses is usually greater.","zh":"如果物體質量較大，它所具有的重力通常較大。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what owns or carries the force.","zh":"這個片語指出誰擁有或帶有該力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"facilitate gravitation","meaning":"促成引力作用","examples":[{"en":"The force of gravity facilitates gravitational attraction.","zh":"重力促成引力吸引作用。"},{"en":"Facilitate gravitation means help make gravitational attraction happen or operate.","zh":"facilitate gravitation 指幫助引力吸引發生或運作。"},{"en":"Clear instructions facilitate learning because students know what to do.","zh":"清楚指示促進學習，因為學生知道要做甚麼。"},{"en":"If gravity provides the pulling force, it facilitates the attraction between masses.","zh":"如果重力提供拉力，它就促成質量之間的吸引。"},{"en":"The phrase means make a process easier or possible.","zh":"這個片語指令某過程更容易或成為可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"scientific theories hold that","meaning":"一些科學理論認為","examples":[{"en":"Certain scientific theories hold that gravitation has several causes.","zh":"一些科學理論認為萬有引力有幾個成因。"},{"en":"Scientific theories hold that means scientific explanations claim or maintain that something is true.","zh":"scientific theories hold that 指科學解釋主張或認為某事為真。"},{"en":"Some learning theories hold that students remember better when they use information actively.","zh":"有些學習理論認為，學生主動使用資訊時記得更好。"},{"en":"If a theory holds that several factors are involved, it rejects a single simple cause.","zh":"如果理論認為涉及幾個因素，它就否定單一簡單成因。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces what a theory says.","zh":"這個片語引出理論的說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be initiated by","meaning":"由……引發","examples":[{"en":"Gravitation may be initiated by a combination of factors.","zh":"萬有引力可能由多項因素結合引發。"},{"en":"Be initiated by means be started or caused by something.","zh":"be initiated by 指由某事開始或造成。"},{"en":"A school project may be initiated by students who notice a community problem.","zh":"學校項目可能由注意到社區問題的學生發起。"},{"en":"If a process is initiated by several factors, no single factor fully explains it.","zh":"如果過程由幾個因素引發，單一因素就不能完全解釋它。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on what starts a process.","zh":"這個片語集中於甚麼開始某過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a combination of factors","meaning":"多項因素的結合","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists believe that gravity involves a combination of factors.","zh":"有些科學家相信重力涉及多項因素的結合。"},{"en":"A combination of factors means several causes or influences working together.","zh":"a combination of factors 指幾個原因或影響共同作用。"},{"en":"Poor sleep, stress, and weak revision can be a combination of factors behind low marks.","zh":"睡眠不足、壓力和溫習薄弱可以是低分背後的多項因素結合。"},{"en":"If several factors act together, the result may be difficult to explain simply.","zh":"如果幾個因素共同作用，結果可能難以簡單解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when one cause is not enough.","zh":"這個片語適用於單一原因不足夠的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not simply … alone","meaning":"並非單單由……","examples":[{"en":"Gravitation may not result simply from the existence of gravity alone.","zh":"萬有引力可能並非單單由重力存在本身造成。"},{"en":"Not simply A alone means not only because of A; other factors may also matter.","zh":"not simply A alone 指不只是因為 A，其他因素也可能重要。"},{"en":"A student’s success is not simply talent alone; practice and feedback matter too.","zh":"學生成功並非單單靠天份；練習和回饋也重要。"},{"en":"If a problem has several causes, blaming one factor alone gives an incomplete explanation.","zh":"如果問題有幾個原因，單靠指責一個因素就是不完整解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against oversimplification.","zh":"這個片語提醒不要過分簡化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"doubts have been raised","meaning":"有人提出質疑","examples":[{"en":"Doubts have been raised regarding some theories of gravity.","zh":"有人對某些重力理論提出質疑。"},{"en":"Doubts have been raised means people have begun to question whether something is true or reliable.","zh":"doubts have been raised 指人們開始質疑某事是否真實或可靠。"},{"en":"Doubts may be raised about a school policy if it creates unfair results.","zh":"如果學校政策造成不公平結果，就可能有人提出質疑。"},{"en":"If evidence is weak, researchers may raise doubts about the explanation.","zh":"如果證據薄弱，研究人員可能對該解釋提出質疑。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces scepticism.","zh":"這個片語引出懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"regarding","meaning":"關於","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have raised doubts regarding certain explanations.","zh":"科學家已關於某些解釋提出質疑。"},{"en":"Regarding means about or concerning something.","zh":"regarding 指關於或涉及某事。"},{"en":"Parents may ask questions regarding school safety after a traffic accident nearby.","zh":"附近發生交通意外後，家長可能提出關於學校安全的問題。"},{"en":"If researchers disagree regarding an explanation, more evidence is needed.","zh":"如果研究人員關於某解釋意見不一，就需要更多證據。"},{"en":"The word introduces the topic being discussed.","zh":"這個詞引出正在討論的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"directly proportional to","meaning":"與……成正比","examples":[{"en":"Gravity is directly proportional to mass.","zh":"重力與質量成正比。"},{"en":"Directly proportional to means one quantity increases when another increases in a fixed relationship.","zh":"directly proportional to 指一個量隨另一個量以固定關係增加。"},{"en":"In some delivery services, the fee is directly proportional to parcel weight.","zh":"在某些送貨服務中，費用與包裹重量成正比。"},{"en":"If mass increases, gravitational force generally increases too.","zh":"如果質量增加，引力通常也會增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a mathematical relationship between two quantities.","zh":"這個片語描述兩個量之間的數學關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"possess less gravity","meaning":"具有較弱的重力","examples":[{"en":"A smaller object normally possesses less gravity.","zh":"較小的物體通常具有較弱的重力。"},{"en":"Possess less gravity means have a weaker gravitational pull.","zh":"possess less gravity 指具有較弱的引力。"},{"en":"The Moon possesses less gravity than Earth, so astronauts can jump higher there.","zh":"月球重力比地球弱，所以太空人在那裡可以跳得更高。"},{"en":"If an object has less mass, it usually has less gravity.","zh":"如果物體質量較小，它通常具有較弱重力。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the strength of gravity between objects.","zh":"這個片語比較不同物體之間的重力強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"to illustrate","meaning":"舉例說明","examples":[{"en":"To illustrate, the Moon has much less gravity than the Earth.","zh":"舉例說明，月球的重力比地球小得多。"},{"en":"To illustrate means to give an example that makes an idea clearer.","zh":"to illustrate 指給出例子，使想法更清楚。"},{"en":"To illustrate, a teacher may show two sentences to explain a grammar rule.","zh":"舉例說明，老師可能展示兩句句子來解釋文法規則。"},{"en":"If a concept is abstract, a concrete example can help students understand it.","zh":"如果概念抽象，具體例子可以幫助學生理解。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an example.","zh":"這個片語引出例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a quarter of the Earth’s size","meaning":"地球大小的四分之一","examples":[{"en":"The Moon is approximately a quarter of the Earth’s size.","zh":"月球約為地球大小的四分之一。"},{"en":"A quarter of the Earth’s size means about one fourth as large as Earth.","zh":"a quarter of the Earth’s size 指約為地球大小的四分之一。"},{"en":"A cake cut into four equal pieces has each piece as a quarter of the whole cake.","zh":"蛋糕被切成四等份時，每一份都是整個蛋糕的四分之一。"},{"en":"If the Moon is much smaller than Earth, its gravity is also much weaker.","zh":"如果月球比地球小得多，其重力也弱得多。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a size comparison using one fourth.","zh":"這個片語用四分之一作大小比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"one-sixth of its gravity","meaning":"其重力的六分之一","examples":[{"en":"The Moon possesses about one-sixth of the Earth’s gravity.","zh":"月球具有約地球重力的六分之一。"},{"en":"One-sixth of its gravity means only one part out of six compared with another body’s gravity.","zh":"one-sixth of its gravity 指與另一個天體重力相比只有六分之一。"},{"en":"If a child’s bag weighs six kilograms on Earth, it would feel much lighter under one-sixth gravity.","zh":"如果孩子的書包在地球重六公斤，在六分之一重力下會感覺輕得多。"},{"en":"Lower gravity allows astronauts to jump higher and move differently.","zh":"較低重力使太空人能跳得更高並以不同方式移動。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a fractional comparison of gravitational strength.","zh":"這個片語用分數比較重力強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be spread out proportionally","meaning":"按比例均勻分佈","examples":[{"en":"The Earth’s mass is not spread out proportionally.","zh":"地球的質量並非按比例均勻分佈。"},{"en":"Be spread out proportionally means be distributed evenly according to size or shape.","zh":"be spread out proportionally 指按照大小或形狀均衡分佈。"},{"en":"If students are spread out proportionally in classrooms, each room has a fair number of students.","zh":"如果學生按比例分佈在課室中，每個課室就有公平人數。"},{"en":"If Earth’s mass is unevenly distributed, gravity can vary from place to place.","zh":"如果地球質量分佈不均，重力就可能因地而異。"},{"en":"The phrase describes balanced or proportional distribution.","zh":"這個片語描述均衡或按比例的分佈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"flatter at the poles","meaning":"兩極較扁平","examples":[{"en":"The Earth is flatter at the poles than at the equator.","zh":"地球在兩極比赤道較扁平。"},{"en":"Flatter at the poles means less rounded at the northern and southern ends of Earth.","zh":"flatter at the poles 指地球南北兩端較不圓。"},{"en":"A ball pressed gently at the top and bottom becomes flatter at those points.","zh":"球體在上下兩端被輕壓時，那些位置會變得較扁平。"},{"en":"Earth’s rotation helps make the planet slightly flattened at the poles.","zh":"地球自轉有助令地球在兩極略為扁平。"},{"en":"The phrase describes Earth’s shape, not the weather at the poles.","zh":"這個片語描述地球形狀，而不是兩極天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the equator","meaning":"赤道","examples":[{"en":"The Earth is wider at the equator than at the poles.","zh":"地球在赤道比兩極更寬。"},{"en":"The equator is the imaginary line around the middle of Earth, halfway between the North and South Poles.","zh":"the equator 指環繞地球中部、位於南北極正中間的想像線。"},{"en":"Countries near the equator often have warm climates throughout the year.","zh":"赤道附近國家通常全年氣候溫暖。"},{"en":"Because Earth bulges slightly at the equator, gravity can differ from polar regions.","zh":"由於地球在赤道略為隆起，重力可以與極地不同。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a central geographical line.","zh":"這個片語指一條中央地理線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as a result of its rotation","meaning":"由於其自轉","examples":[{"en":"The Earth is flatter at the poles as a result of its rotation.","zh":"地球由於其自轉而在兩極較扁平。"},{"en":"As a result of its rotation means because it spins around its axis.","zh":"as a result of its rotation 指因為它圍繞自身軸線旋轉。"},{"en":"A washing machine pushes clothes outward as a result of its rotation.","zh":"洗衣機由於其旋轉而把衣物向外推。"},{"en":"Because Earth rotates, its shape and gravity are not perfectly even everywhere.","zh":"由於地球自轉，其形狀和重力並非處處完全一致。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an effect with spinning motion.","zh":"這個片語把效果與旋轉運動連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"gravitational pull","meaning":"引力","examples":[{"en":"Gravitational pull varies in different parts of the world.","zh":"引力在世界不同地方有所不同。"},{"en":"Gravitational pull is the force by which one body attracts another.","zh":"gravitational pull 指一個物體吸引另一物體的力。"},{"en":"Earth’s gravitational pull keeps people, buildings, and oceans on the planet.","zh":"地球引力使人、建築物和海洋留在地球上。"},{"en":"If an area has slightly less mass beneath it, its gravitational pull may be weaker.","zh":"如果某地地下質量略少，其引力可能較弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the strength of gravity as a pulling force.","zh":"這個片語把重力描述為拉力強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"different locations throughout the world","meaning":"世界各地不同位置","examples":[{"en":"Gravity varies at different locations throughout the world.","zh":"重力在世界各地不同位置有所不同。"},{"en":"Different locations throughout the world means many different places across Earth.","zh":"different locations throughout the world 指地球上許多不同地方。"},{"en":"Weather, food prices, and transport systems vary at different locations throughout the world.","zh":"天氣、食物價格和交通系統在世界各地不同位置有所不同。"},{"en":"If gravity changes from place to place, scientists must measure it globally.","zh":"如果重力因地而異，科學家就必須在全球測量它。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses worldwide variation.","zh":"這個片語強調全球差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"worldwide gravity fields","meaning":"全球重力場","examples":[{"en":"Researchers studied worldwide gravity fields in the 1960s.","zh":"研究人員在二十世紀六十年代研究全球重力場。"},{"en":"Worldwide gravity fields are patterns of gravitational strength across the whole Earth.","zh":"worldwide gravity fields 指整個地球上的重力強度模式。"},{"en":"Scientists use maps of gravity fields to study hidden structures beneath Earth’s surface.","zh":"科學家使用重力場地圖研究地球表面下的隱藏結構。"},{"en":"If gravity fields differ from place to place, they can reveal unusual underground features.","zh":"如果重力場因地而異，就能揭示異常地下特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase describes global patterns of gravity.","zh":"這個片語描述全球重力模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"it was discovered that","meaning":"人們發現","examples":[{"en":"It was discovered that Hudson Bay had unusually low gravity.","zh":"人們發現哈德遜灣的重力異常偏低。"},{"en":"It was discovered that means researchers found out something after investigation.","zh":"it was discovered that 指研究或調查後發現某事。"},{"en":"It was discovered that the leak came from an old pipe under the kitchen.","zh":"人們發現漏水來自廚房下方的舊水管。"},{"en":"If scientists discover an unusual pattern, they then look for possible causes.","zh":"如果科學家發現異常模式，就會尋找可能原因。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a finding.","zh":"這個片語引出發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"inexplicably","meaning":"難以解釋地","examples":[{"en":"Inexplicably, the region appeared to have lower gravity than expected.","zh":"難以解釋地，該地區似乎比預期有更低重力。"},{"en":"Inexplicably means in a way that is difficult to explain or understand.","zh":"inexplicably 指以難以解釋或理解的方式。"},{"en":"The computer inexplicably shut down even though the battery was full.","zh":"電腦電池明明充足，卻難以解釋地關機。"},{"en":"If data behave inexplicably, researchers must look for hidden causes.","zh":"如果數據表現難以解釋，研究人員必須尋找隱藏原因。"},{"en":"The word signals surprise and lack of an obvious explanation.","zh":"這個詞表示驚訝和缺乏明顯解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"areas around and including","meaning":"……周圍及包括……的地區","examples":[{"en":"Areas around and including Hudson Bay showed unusual gravity levels.","zh":"哈德遜灣周圍及包括哈德遜灣的地區顯示異常重力水平。"},{"en":"Areas around and including means the named place and nearby surrounding places.","zh":"areas around and including 指所指地方以及附近周邊地方。"},{"en":"Areas around and including the school may be closed during the roadworks.","zh":"學校周圍及包括學校的地區可能在道路工程期間封閉。"},{"en":"If an anomaly covers a central place and nearby areas, it is larger than a single point.","zh":"如果異常覆蓋一個中心地點和附近區域，它就不只是一個點。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a broad but centred location.","zh":"這個片語給出以某地為中心的較廣位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Hudson Bay","meaning":"哈德遜灣","examples":[{"en":"The Hudson Bay region has lower gravity than many other areas.","zh":"哈德遜灣地區的重力比許多其他地區低。"},{"en":"Hudson Bay is a large body of water in northeastern Canada.","zh":"Hudson Bay 指加拿大東北部的一大片水域。"},{"en":"A geography map shows Hudson Bay as a huge bay connected to the Arctic region.","zh":"地理地圖顯示哈德遜灣是一個與北極地區相連的大海灣。"},{"en":"If a whole region around Hudson Bay has unusual gravity, scientists must study its geology and ice-age history.","zh":"如果哈德遜灣周邊整個地區有異常重力，科學家就必須研究其地質和冰河時代歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase names the location of the gravity anomaly.","zh":"這個片語指出重力異常的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"significantly lower levels of","meaning":"顯著較低水平的……","examples":[{"en":"The region possesses significantly lower levels of gravity.","zh":"該地區具有顯著較低水平的重力。"},{"en":"Significantly lower levels of means much less of something in a meaningful way.","zh":"significantly lower levels of 指某物在有意義的程度上少得多。"},{"en":"A school may have significantly lower levels of noise after installing soundproof windows.","zh":"學校安裝隔音窗後，噪音水平可能顯著較低。"},{"en":"If gravity is significantly lower, normal explanations may not be enough.","zh":"如果重力顯著較低，一般解釋可能不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a noticeable and important decrease.","zh":"這個片語強調明顯而重要的下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"other parts of the globe","meaning":"全球其他地區","examples":[{"en":"Hudson Bay has lower gravity than many other parts of the globe.","zh":"哈德遜灣的重力比全球其他許多地區低。"},{"en":"Other parts of the globe means other regions of the world.","zh":"other parts of the globe 指世界其他區域。"},{"en":"Students can compare weather in Hong Kong with other parts of the globe.","zh":"學生可以把香港天氣與全球其他地區比較。"},{"en":"If one region differs from other parts of the globe, it may have special local conditions.","zh":"如果某地區與全球其他地區不同，它可能有特殊本地條件。"},{"en":"The phrase broadens comparison to the whole world.","zh":"這個片語把比較擴展到全世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reasons for this dissimilarity","meaning":"出現這種差異的原因","examples":[{"en":"Scientists investigated the reasons for this dissimilarity.","zh":"科學家調查出現這種差異的原因。"},{"en":"Reasons for this dissimilarity are the causes of the difference between one thing and another.","zh":"reasons for this dissimilarity 指一件事與另一件事不同的原因。"},{"en":"A teacher may study the reasons for dissimilarity in class results between two groups.","zh":"老師可能研究兩組學生班級成績差異的原因。"},{"en":"If one place has lower gravity than others, researchers must explain why it is different.","zh":"如果一個地方的重力比其他地方低，研究人員必須解釋它為何不同。"},{"en":"The phrase asks why two things are not alike.","zh":"這個片語詢問兩件事為何不相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"extensively investigated","meaning":"被廣泛深入研究","examples":[{"en":"The gravity anomaly has been extensively investigated.","zh":"這個重力異常已被廣泛深入研究。"},{"en":"Extensively investigated means studied carefully and in great detail.","zh":"extensively investigated 指被仔細而詳細地研究。"},{"en":"A serious accident should be extensively investigated before new safety rules are made.","zh":"嚴重意外應在制定新安全規則前被廣泛深入調查。"},{"en":"If a mystery is extensively investigated, researchers collect data from many sources.","zh":"如果一個謎團被廣泛深入研究，研究人員會從許多來源收集數據。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses deep and thorough study.","zh":"這個片語強調深入而徹底的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"result in two explanations","meaning":"得出兩種解釋","examples":[{"en":"The investigations resulted in two possible explanations.","zh":"這些調查得出兩種可能解釋。"},{"en":"Result in two explanations means lead researchers to propose two possible causes.","zh":"result in two explanations 指使研究人員提出兩個可能原因。"},{"en":"A school survey may result in two explanations for lateness: traffic and unclear timetables.","zh":"學校調查可能得出兩種遲到解釋：交通和時間表不清。"},{"en":"If evidence supports more than one cause, scientists may keep both explanations open.","zh":"如果證據支持多於一個原因，科學家可能保留兩種解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research producing possible answers.","zh":"這個片語描述研究產生可能答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"original theory","meaning":"最初的理論","examples":[{"en":"The original theory linked the anomaly to activity in the mantle.","zh":"最初的理論把該異常與地幔活動連繫起來。"},{"en":"The original theory is the first explanation proposed for a problem or observation.","zh":"original theory 指對某問題或觀察最早提出的解釋。"},{"en":"The original theory about a broken machine may be wrong once technicians inspect it.","zh":"關於機器故障的最初理論，在技術員檢查後可能是錯的。"},{"en":"If later evidence appears, an original theory may be revised or combined with another theory.","zh":"如果後來出現證據，最初理論可能被修訂或與另一理論結合。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the earliest explanation.","zh":"這個片語指最早的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"attribute something to","meaning":"將……歸因於……","examples":[{"en":"The original theory attributed the anomaly to activity below the surface.","zh":"最初的理論將該異常歸因於地表下的活動。"},{"en":"Attribute something to means say that something is caused by a particular factor.","zh":"attribute something to 指說某事由某特定因素造成。"},{"en":"A doctor may attribute tiredness to lack of sleep and poor diet.","zh":"醫生可能將疲倦歸因於睡眠不足和飲食不良。"},{"en":"If scientists attribute an anomaly to mantle activity, they think that activity caused it.","zh":"如果科學家將異常歸因於地幔活動，他們認為該活動造成了異常。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an effect with a proposed cause.","zh":"這個片語把結果與提出的原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"gravity anomaly","meaning":"重力異常","examples":[{"en":"Scientists proposed two explanations for the gravity anomaly.","zh":"科學家為這個重力異常提出兩種解釋。"},{"en":"A gravity anomaly is an unusual difference in gravitational strength in a particular area.","zh":"gravity anomaly 指某一地區重力強度出現不尋常差異。"},{"en":"A map may show a gravity anomaly where underground rock is unusually dense or light.","zh":"地圖可能在地下岩石異常密集或輕的地方顯示重力異常。"},{"en":"If gravity is lower than expected, scientists search for hidden geological or historical causes.","zh":"如果重力低於預期，科學家會尋找隱藏的地質或歷史原因。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gravity that does not match the normal pattern.","zh":"這個片語描述不符合正常模式的重力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"below the Earth’s surface","meaning":"地球表面之下","examples":[{"en":"The relevant activity occurs deep below the Earth’s surface.","zh":"相關活動發生在地球表面深處之下。"},{"en":"Below the Earth’s surface means under the ground or under the outer layer of Earth.","zh":"below the Earth’s surface 指在地面或地球外層之下。"},{"en":"Underground water moves below the Earth’s surface through cracks and rock layers.","zh":"地下水透過裂縫和岩層在地球表面之下移動。"},{"en":"If processes occur deep below the surface, they may be invisible but still affect the land above.","zh":"如果過程發生在地表深處，可能看不見，但仍會影響上方土地。"},{"en":"The phrase points to hidden underground activity.","zh":"這個片語指隱藏的地下活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"layer known as the mantle","meaning":"被稱為地幔的地層","examples":[{"en":"The activity occurs within the layer known as the mantle.","zh":"該活動發生在被稱為地幔的地層內。"},{"en":"The layer known as the mantle is the thick part of Earth between the crust and the core.","zh":"layer known as the mantle 指地殼與地核之間厚厚的地球內部部分。"},{"en":"Geography students learn that the mantle lies below the crust.","zh":"地理學生學到地幔位於地殼之下。"},{"en":"If mantle material moves, it can affect plates and surface features.","zh":"如果地幔物質移動，就能影響板塊和地表特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a major layer inside Earth.","zh":"這個片語指出地球內部一個主要層次。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"mantle","meaning":"地幔","examples":[{"en":"The mantle lies beneath the Earth’s crust.","zh":"地幔位於地殼之下。"},{"en":"The mantle is the hot, thick layer of Earth between the crust and the core.","zh":"mantle 指位於地殼與地核之間的高溫厚層。"},{"en":"Students often draw Earth as layers: crust, mantle, outer core, and inner core.","zh":"學生常把地球畫成幾層：地殼、地幔、外核和內核。"},{"en":"If the mantle moves slowly, it can help drive plate movement.","zh":"如果地幔緩慢移動，就能推動板塊運動。"},{"en":"The word names a major internal layer of Earth.","zh":"這個詞指出地球內部一個主要層次。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"consist of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"The mantle consists of extremely hot rock.","zh":"地幔由極熱岩石組成。"},{"en":"Consist of means be made up of particular parts or materials.","zh":"consist of 指由特定部分或材料構成。"},{"en":"A simple lunch may consist of rice, vegetables, and fish.","zh":"一份簡單午餐可能由米飯、蔬菜和魚組成。"},{"en":"If a layer consists of hot rock, heat and movement inside it can affect Earth’s surface.","zh":"如果某層由熱岩石組成，其內部熱力和運動能影響地表。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what something contains.","zh":"這個片語解釋某物包含甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"molten rock","meaning":"熔岩","examples":[{"en":"The mantle contains hot molten rock.","zh":"地幔含有高溫熔岩。"},{"en":"Molten rock is rock that has become liquid or partly liquid because of heat.","zh":"molten rock 指因高熱而變成液體或部分液體的岩石。"},{"en":"Lava from a volcano is molten rock that has reached the surface.","zh":"火山熔岩是到達地表的熔融岩石。"},{"en":"If molten rock moves underground, it can transfer heat and affect tectonic plates.","zh":"如果熔岩在地下移動，就能傳遞熱力並影響板塊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rock changed by extreme heat.","zh":"這個片語描述被極高熱力改變的岩石。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"known as magma","meaning":"被稱為岩漿","examples":[{"en":"Hot molten rock beneath the surface is known as magma.","zh":"地表下的高溫熔融岩石被稱為岩漿。"},{"en":"Known as magma means called magma in scientific language.","zh":"known as magma 指在科學語言中被稱為 magma。"},{"en":"When molten rock stays underground, it is known as magma, but when it reaches the surface, it is called lava.","zh":"當熔融岩石留在地下時，它被稱為岩漿；到達地表後則稱為熔岩。"},{"en":"If students learn the name magma, they can distinguish underground molten rock from lava.","zh":"如果學生學會 magma 這個名稱，就能區分地下熔融岩石與地表熔岩。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the correct technical name.","zh":"這個片語引出正確技術名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"flow beneath","meaning":"在……下方流動","examples":[{"en":"Magma flows beneath the Earth’s surface.","zh":"岩漿在地球表面下方流動。"},{"en":"Flow beneath means move underneath something.","zh":"flow beneath 指在某物下方移動。"},{"en":"Water can flow beneath a road through underground pipes.","zh":"水可以透過地下管道在道路下方流動。"},{"en":"If magma flows beneath a region, it may change underground mass and pressure.","zh":"如果岩漿在某地區下方流動，可能改變地下質量和壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes hidden movement below a surface.","zh":"這個片語描述表面下的隱藏流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"convection currents","meaning":"對流","examples":[{"en":"The movement of magma creates convection currents.","zh":"岩漿的移動產生對流。"},{"en":"Convection currents are circular movements caused by warmer material rising and cooler material sinking.","zh":"convection currents 指較暖物質上升、較冷物質下沉所造成的循環流動。"},{"en":"Hot soup in a pot can form convection currents as heat rises from the bottom.","zh":"鍋中的熱湯會因底部熱力上升而形成對流。"},{"en":"If convection currents move inside Earth, they can help shift plates over time.","zh":"如果對流在地球內部移動，就能隨時間幫助板塊移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes heat-driven circulation.","zh":"這個片語描述由熱力推動的循環。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"result in the lowering of","meaning":"導致……下降","examples":[{"en":"Convection currents can result in the lowering of continental plates.","zh":"對流可以導致大陸板塊下降。"},{"en":"Result in the lowering of means cause something to move downward or become lower.","zh":"result in the lowering of 指造成某物向下移動或變低。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can result in the lowering of a hillside path if soil is washed away.","zh":"暴雨沖走泥土後，可能導致山路下陷。"},{"en":"If plates are pulled downward, the land above may have slightly less mass beneath it.","zh":"如果板塊被向下拉，上方土地下方的質量可能略少。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a cause with downward movement.","zh":"這個片語把原因與向下移動連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"continental plates","meaning":"大陸板塊","examples":[{"en":"Continental plates make up much of the Earth’s surface.","zh":"大陸板塊組成地球表面的大部分。"},{"en":"Continental plates are huge pieces of Earth’s outer layer that carry continents or parts of continents.","zh":"continental plates 指承載大陸或部分大陸的巨大地球外層板塊。"},{"en":"Geography students study continental plates when learning about earthquakes and volcanoes.","zh":"地理學生學習地震和火山時會研究大陸板塊。"},{"en":"If plates move, mountains, earthquakes, and ocean basins can form.","zh":"如果板塊移動，山脈、地震和海盆可能形成。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to large moving sections of Earth’s crust and upper mantle.","zh":"這個片語指地殼和上地幔中大型移動部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make up","meaning":"組成","examples":[{"en":"Continental plates make up the Earth’s outer surface.","zh":"大陸板塊組成地球外層表面。"},{"en":"Make up means form or compose something.","zh":"make up 指形成或組成某物。"},{"en":"Students from different classes make up the school choir.","zh":"來自不同班級的學生組成學校合唱團。"},{"en":"If small parts make up a larger structure, removing one part can affect the whole.","zh":"如果小部分組成更大結構，移除其中一部分可以影響整體。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what something is composed of.","zh":"這個片語解釋某物由甚麼構成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"when this occurs","meaning":"當此情況發生時","examples":[{"en":"When this occurs, the mass and gravity of the area are reduced.","zh":"當此情況發生時，該地區的質量和重力會減少。"},{"en":"When this occurs means when the event just described happens.","zh":"when this occurs 指當剛才描述的事件發生時。"},{"en":"A student may forget a deadline; when this occurs, the teacher should remind them calmly.","zh":"學生可能忘記截止日期；當此情況發生時，老師應冷靜提醒他們。"},{"en":"If plates lower and mass is reduced, gravity in the area may also become weaker.","zh":"如果板塊下降而質量減少，該地區重力也可能變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase links a described event with its result.","zh":"這個片語把已描述事件與其結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be reduced","meaning":"被減少","examples":[{"en":"The mass in the affected area may be reduced.","zh":"受影響地區的質量可能被減少。"},{"en":"Be reduced means become smaller, lower, or less.","zh":"be reduced 指變得較小、較低或較少。"},{"en":"Electricity bills can be reduced if families use energy-saving appliances.","zh":"如果家庭使用節能電器，電費可以被減少。"},{"en":"If underground mass is reduced, gravity may also be reduced.","zh":"如果地下質量減少，重力也可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a decrease.","zh":"這個片語描述下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"research findings indicated that","meaning":"研究結果顯示","examples":[{"en":"Research findings indicated that mantle activity had occurred in Hudson Bay.","zh":"研究結果顯示哈德遜灣曾發生地幔活動。"},{"en":"Research findings indicated that means the results of a study showed or suggested something.","zh":"research findings indicated that 指研究結果顯示或暗示某事。"},{"en":"Survey findings may indicate that students need more quiet study areas.","zh":"調查結果可能顯示學生需要更多安靜自修區。"},{"en":"If findings indicate past mantle activity, scientists can use them to support a theory.","zh":"如果研究結果顯示過去有地幔活動，科學家可用它支持理論。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence-based information.","zh":"這個片語引出以證據為基礎的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"such activity","meaning":"這類活動","examples":[{"en":"Scientists found evidence that such activity had affected the region.","zh":"科學家找到證據顯示這類活動影響了該地區。"},{"en":"Such activity means the type of activity just mentioned.","zh":"such activity 指剛才提到的那類活動。"},{"en":"If a teacher mentions bullying, such activity should be reported immediately.","zh":"如果老師提到欺凌，這類活動應立即報告。"},{"en":"If mantle movement occurred, such activity could change mass below the surface.","zh":"如果地幔運動發生，這類活動可能改變地表下的質量。"},{"en":"The phrase avoids repeating a longer description.","zh":"這個片語避免重複較長描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"more recently","meaning":"較近期","examples":[{"en":"More recently, scientists proposed a second explanation.","zh":"較近期，科學家提出第二種解釋。"},{"en":"More recently means in a later period closer to the present.","zh":"more recently 指在較接近現在的較後時期。"},{"en":"More recently, many schools have started using online homework platforms.","zh":"較近期，許多學校開始使用網上功課平台。"},{"en":"If a newer explanation appears, it may revise or add to older theories.","zh":"如果較新的解釋出現，它可能修訂或補充舊理論。"},{"en":"The phrase signals a shift from older ideas to newer ones.","zh":"這個片語標示從舊想法轉向新想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"second conjecture","meaning":"第二個推測","examples":[{"en":"A second conjecture linked the anomaly to the Ice Age.","zh":"第二個推測把該異常與冰河時期連繫起來。"},{"en":"A second conjecture is another possible explanation or educated guess.","zh":"second conjecture 指另一個可能解釋或有根據的猜測。"},{"en":"If a phone stops working, one conjecture may be battery failure and a second conjecture may be water damage.","zh":"如果電話停止運作，一個推測可能是電池故障，第二個推測可能是入水損壞。"},{"en":"If evidence supports a second conjecture, scientists may consider more than one cause.","zh":"如果證據支持第二個推測，科學家可能考慮多於一個原因。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an additional proposed explanation.","zh":"這個片語引出額外提出的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"suggest that","meaning":"顯示；提出","examples":[{"en":"The newer theory suggests that the Ice Age affected gravity levels.","zh":"較新的理論提出冰河時期影響了重力水平。"},{"en":"Suggest that means show, imply, or make something seem likely.","zh":"suggest that 指顯示、暗示或令某事看似可能。"},{"en":"Dark clouds suggest that rain may come soon.","zh":"烏雲顯示可能很快下雨。"},{"en":"If satellite data match the ice sheet’s former shape, they may suggest a connection.","zh":"如果衛星數據與冰原昔日形狀吻合，可能顯示兩者有關。"},{"en":"The phrase is cautious and does not always mean complete proof.","zh":"這個片語較謹慎，不一定表示完全證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"The lower gravity may, in fact, result partly from ancient ice.","zh":"較低重力事實上可能部分來自古代冰層。"},{"en":"In fact introduces information that is true or stronger than what was just suggested.","zh":"in fact 引出真實或比剛才所說更強的資訊。"},{"en":"The shop looks small; in fact, it has three floors inside.","zh":"這間店看起來很小；事實上，它內部有三層。"},{"en":"If new evidence changes the explanation, “in fact” can correct an earlier assumption.","zh":"如果新證據改變解釋，in fact 可以修正早前假設。"},{"en":"The phrase often adds emphasis or clarification.","zh":"這個片語常加入強調或澄清。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be a result of","meaning":"是……的結果","examples":[{"en":"The unusual gravity is partly a result of Ice Age conditions.","zh":"異常重力部分是冰河時期環境的結果。"},{"en":"Be a result of means be caused by something.","zh":"be a result of 指由某事造成。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may be a result of regular practice and kind feedback.","zh":"學生的信心可能是定期練習和友善回饋的結果。"},{"en":"If land was pressed down by ice, lower gravity may partly result from that pressure.","zh":"如果土地曾被冰層壓下，較低重力可能部分來自該壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an outcome with its cause.","zh":"這個片語把結果與原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"occurrences during the Ice Age","meaning":"冰河時期發生的事情","examples":[{"en":"The second theory focuses on occurrences during the Ice Age.","zh":"第二個理論聚焦於冰河時期發生的事情。"},{"en":"Occurrences during the Ice Age are events or processes that happened in that cold period.","zh":"occurrences during the Ice Age 指在該寒冷時期發生的事件或過程。"},{"en":"A history lesson may focus on occurrences during a war, such as migration and food shortages.","zh":"歷史課可能聚焦戰爭期間發生的事情，例如遷徙和食物短缺。"},{"en":"If huge ice sheets formed during the Ice Age, they could leave long-term effects after melting.","zh":"如果巨大冰原在冰河時期形成，融化後仍可能留下長遠影響。"},{"en":"The phrase points to events within a specific period.","zh":"這個片語指特定時期內的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Laurentide Ice Sheet","meaning":"勞倫泰德冰原","examples":[{"en":"The Laurentide Ice Sheet once covered most of Canada.","zh":"勞倫泰德冰原曾覆蓋加拿大大部分地區。"},{"en":"The Laurentide Ice Sheet was a massive ice sheet that covered large parts of North America during the Ice Age.","zh":"Laurentide Ice Sheet 指冰河時期覆蓋北美洲大片地區的巨大冰原。"},{"en":"Geography students may study the Laurentide Ice Sheet when learning about glaciation in Canada.","zh":"地理學生學習加拿大冰川作用時，可能研究勞倫泰德冰原。"},{"en":"If an ice sheet is several kilometres thick, its weight can press down the land below.","zh":"如果冰原厚達數公里，其重量可以壓下下方土地。"},{"en":"The phrase names the ancient ice sheet linked to Hudson Bay.","zh":"這個片語指出與哈德遜灣有關的古代冰原。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cover most of","meaning":"覆蓋……大部分地區","examples":[{"en":"The Laurentide Ice Sheet covered most of Canada.","zh":"勞倫泰德冰原覆蓋加拿大大部分地區。"},{"en":"Cover most of means extend over the largest part of an area.","zh":"cover most of 指延伸覆蓋某地區的大部分。"},{"en":"Heavy snow may cover most of a playground after a winter storm.","zh":"冬季風暴後，大雪可能覆蓋操場大部分地方。"},{"en":"If ice covers most of a country, its weight can reshape the land below.","zh":"如果冰覆蓋一個國家大部分地區，其重量可以重塑下方土地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes wide physical coverage.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛的實體覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"northern tip","meaning":"北端","examples":[{"en":"The ice sheet also covered the northern tip of the USA.","zh":"冰原也覆蓋美國北端。"},{"en":"Northern tip means the farthest northern end of an area.","zh":"northern tip 指一個地區最北的末端。"},{"en":"A map may show a lighthouse at the northern tip of an island.","zh":"地圖可能顯示島嶼北端有一座燈塔。"},{"en":"If ice reached the northern tip of a country, the glacier extended beyond its main region.","zh":"如果冰到達一個國家的北端，冰川就延伸超出其主要區域。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the topmost part on a map.","zh":"這個片語指出地圖上最上方的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"until it melted","meaning":"直至它融化","examples":[{"en":"The ice sheet covered the region until it melted about 10,000 years ago.","zh":"冰原覆蓋該地區，直至它約一萬年前融化。"},{"en":"Until it melted means up to the time when the ice turned into water and disappeared.","zh":"until it melted 指直到冰變成水並消失的時候。"},{"en":"Snow stayed on the school field until it melted in the afternoon sun.","zh":"雪留在學校操場上，直至它在午後陽光下融化。"},{"en":"If ice remained until a certain time, its pressure affected the land until then.","zh":"如果冰一直留到某時，其壓力就影響土地直到那時。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the endpoint of ice coverage.","zh":"這個片語標示冰覆蓋的終點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be thought to have been","meaning":"被認為曾經是……","examples":[{"en":"The ice sheet is thought to have been more than three kilometres thick.","zh":"這片冰原被認為曾厚達三公里以上。"},{"en":"Be thought to have been means experts believe something was true in the past.","zh":"be thought to have been 指專家相信某事在過去曾經如此。"},{"en":"An old building is thought to have been a market before it became a museum.","zh":"一座舊建築被認為曾經是市場，後來才成為博物館。"},{"en":"If no one directly observed an ancient ice sheet, scientists estimate its thickness from evidence.","zh":"如果沒有人直接觀察古代冰原，科學家會根據證據估算其厚度。"},{"en":"The phrase reports a reasoned belief about the past.","zh":"這個片語報告對過去的有根據看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sheer weight","meaning":"巨大的重量","examples":[{"en":"The sheer weight of the ice depressed the Earth’s surface.","zh":"冰層巨大的重量令地球表面下陷。"},{"en":"Sheer weight means the enormous heaviness of something by itself.","zh":"sheer weight 指某物本身極大的重量。"},{"en":"The sheer weight of too many books can damage a weak shelf.","zh":"太多書的巨大重量可以壓壞脆弱書架。"},{"en":"If ice is kilometres thick, its sheer weight can push the ground downward.","zh":"如果冰層厚達數公里，其巨大重量可以把地面向下壓。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises weight as the main force.","zh":"這個片語強調重量本身是主要力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ice layer","meaning":"冰層","examples":[{"en":"The enormous ice layer pressed down on the land.","zh":"巨大的冰層壓在土地上。"},{"en":"An ice layer is a sheet or thickness of ice covering a surface.","zh":"ice layer 指覆蓋表面的一片或一層冰。"},{"en":"A thin ice layer may form on a road during a freezing night.","zh":"在寒冷夜晚，道路上可能形成薄冰層。"},{"en":"If an ice layer is extremely thick, it can reshape the ground below it.","zh":"如果冰層極厚，它可以重塑下方地面。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a covering of ice.","zh":"這個片語描述冰的覆蓋層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"depress the Earth’s surface","meaning":"令地球表面下陷","examples":[{"en":"The weight of the ice depressed the Earth’s surface beneath it.","zh":"冰的重量令其下方地球表面下陷。"},{"en":"Depress the Earth’s surface means push the ground downward.","zh":"depress the Earth’s surface 指把地面向下壓。"},{"en":"A heavy table can depress a soft carpet and leave marks.","zh":"沉重桌子可以壓低柔軟地毯並留下痕跡。"},{"en":"If an ice sheet pushes the land down, the surface may remain lower after the ice melts.","zh":"如果冰原把土地向下壓，冰融化後地表可能仍較低。"},{"en":"The phrase describes downward deformation of land.","zh":"這個片語描述土地向下變形。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"once the ice melted","meaning":"冰層融化後","examples":[{"en":"Once the ice melted, a deep indentation remained.","zh":"冰層融化後，留下了一個深凹痕。"},{"en":"Once the ice melted means after the ice disappeared by turning into water.","zh":"once the ice melted 指冰變成水並消失之後。"},{"en":"Once the rain stopped, students went back to the playground.","zh":"雨停後，學生回到操場。"},{"en":"If the land was pressed down for thousands of years, it might not recover immediately once the ice melted.","zh":"如果土地被壓下數千年，冰層融化後未必立即恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces what happened after melting.","zh":"這個片語引出融化後發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"deep indentation","meaning":"深凹痕","examples":[{"en":"A deep indentation remained after the ice disappeared.","zh":"冰層消失後留下了一個深凹痕。"},{"en":"A deep indentation is a hollow or depression pressed into a surface.","zh":"deep indentation 指壓入表面形成的凹陷或低窪。"},{"en":"A heavy chair can leave a deep indentation in soft ground.","zh":"沉重椅子可以在軟地上留下深凹痕。"},{"en":"If an ice sheet leaves an indentation, the land may take thousands of years to rebound.","zh":"如果冰原留下凹痕，土地可能需要數千年才回彈。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a sunken mark or hollow.","zh":"這個片語描述下陷痕跡或凹位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"remain","meaning":"留下；持續存在","examples":[{"en":"The depression remained long after the ice had melted.","zh":"冰融化很久之後，凹陷仍然存在。"},{"en":"Remain means continue to exist or stay in the same condition.","zh":"remain 指繼續存在或保持同一狀態。"},{"en":"A stain may remain on a shirt even after washing.","zh":"污漬可能在清洗後仍留在恤衫上。"},{"en":"If land remains depressed after ice melts, recovery is not immediate.","zh":"如果冰融化後土地仍然下陷，恢復就不是即時的。"},{"en":"The word stresses continuation over time.","zh":"這個詞強調隨時間持續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"become thinner","meaning":"變得較薄","examples":[{"en":"The area around Hudson Bay became thinner under the ice’s weight.","zh":"哈德遜灣周圍地區在冰的重量下變得較薄。"},{"en":"Become thinner means lose thickness or have less material than before.","zh":"become thinner 指失去厚度或比以前有較少材料。"},{"en":"A notebook becomes thinner as pages are torn out.","zh":"筆記簿被撕走頁面後會變得較薄。"},{"en":"If land material is pushed away, the crust in that area can become thinner.","zh":"如果土地物質被推走，該區地殼可以變得較薄。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a reduction in thickness.","zh":"這個片語描述厚度減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be pushed towards","meaning":"被推向……","examples":[{"en":"Material was pushed towards the edges of the ice sheet.","zh":"物質被推向冰原邊緣。"},{"en":"Be pushed towards means be forced in the direction of something.","zh":"be pushed towards 指被迫朝某方向移動。"},{"en":"During a crowded assembly, students may be pushed towards the doors.","zh":"在擁擠集會中，學生可能被推向門口。"},{"en":"If heavy ice presses down, underground material may move outward to the edges.","zh":"如果厚冰向下施壓，地下物質可能向外移到邊緣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement caused by pressure.","zh":"這個片語描述由壓力造成的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"edges of the ice sheet","meaning":"冰原邊緣","examples":[{"en":"Material accumulated near the edges of the ice sheet.","zh":"物質在冰原邊緣附近積聚。"},{"en":"Edges of the ice sheet are the outer boundaries of a large mass of ice.","zh":"edges of the ice sheet 指大片冰層的外圍邊界。"},{"en":"Meltwater often flows near the edges of a glacier or ice sheet.","zh":"融水常在冰川或冰原邊緣附近流動。"},{"en":"If material is pushed from the centre, it may build up around the edges.","zh":"如果物質從中心被推開，就可能在邊緣周圍積聚。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the outer parts of the ice cover.","zh":"這個片語指出冰覆蓋的外圍部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"extensive investigation","meaning":"廣泛深入的調查","examples":[{"en":"Extensive investigation has been carried out into the gravity anomaly.","zh":"對該重力異常已進行廣泛深入的調查。"},{"en":"Extensive investigation means a large, detailed study of a question or problem.","zh":"extensive investigation 指對某問題進行大型而詳細的研究。"},{"en":"A serious school accident requires extensive investigation before blame is assigned.","zh":"嚴重校園意外在歸咎前需要廣泛深入調查。"},{"en":"If a scientific mystery lasts for decades, extensive investigation may involve many tools and teams.","zh":"如果科學謎團持續數十年，廣泛調查可能涉及許多工具和團隊。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses breadth and depth of study.","zh":"這個片語強調研究的廣度和深度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be carried out","meaning":"被進行","examples":[{"en":"Research was carried out using satellite data.","zh":"研究使用衛星數據進行。"},{"en":"Be carried out means be done or conducted.","zh":"be carried out 指被執行或進行。"},{"en":"A fire drill is carried out so students know how to leave safely.","zh":"學校進行火警演習，讓學生知道如何安全離開。"},{"en":"If research is carried out carefully, its findings are more reliable.","zh":"如果研究被仔細進行，其結果就更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an action being performed.","zh":"這個片語描述行動被執行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Harvard-Smithsonian Center for Astrophysics","meaning":"哈佛—史密松天體物理中心","examples":[{"en":"The Harvard-Smithsonian Center for Astrophysics analysed the satellite data.","zh":"哈佛—史密松天體物理中心分析了衛星數據。"},{"en":"The Harvard-Smithsonian Center for Astrophysics is a research centre that studies space and astrophysical phenomena.","zh":"Harvard-Smithsonian Center for Astrophysics 指研究太空和天體物理現象的研究中心。"},{"en":"A major research centre may analyse satellite data that individual schools cannot process.","zh":"大型研究中心可能分析普通學校無法處理的衛星數據。"},{"en":"If specialists analyse gravity data, they can create more accurate maps of Earth’s gravity field.","zh":"如果專家分析重力數據，就能製作更準確的地球重力場地圖。"},{"en":"The phrase names the institution involved in the research.","zh":"這個片語指出參與研究的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"data collected by satellites","meaning":"衛星收集的數據","examples":[{"en":"The researchers used data collected by satellites.","zh":"研究人員使用衛星收集的數據。"},{"en":"Data collected by satellites are measurements gathered by machines orbiting above Earth.","zh":"data collected by satellites 指由在地球上空運行的機器收集的測量資料。"},{"en":"Weather forecasts often use data collected by satellites to track storms.","zh":"天氣預報常使用衛星收集的數據追蹤風暴。"},{"en":"If satellites measure tiny changes in distance and gravity, scientists can study large regions from space.","zh":"如果衛星測量距離和重力的微小變化，科學家就能從太空研究大片地區。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to information gathered remotely from orbit.","zh":"這個片語指從軌道遠距收集的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Gravity Recovery and Climate Experiment","meaning":"重力恢復與氣候實驗","examples":[{"en":"The Gravity Recovery and Climate Experiment measured changes in gravity.","zh":"重力恢復與氣候實驗測量了重力變化。"},{"en":"The Gravity Recovery and Climate Experiment was a satellite mission designed to measure Earth’s gravity field.","zh":"Gravity Recovery and Climate Experiment 指一項設計用來測量地球重力場的衛星任務。"},{"en":"Students may see the short name GRACE when reading about satellite studies of gravity.","zh":"學生閱讀關於重力的衛星研究時，可能看見 GRACE 這個縮寫。"},{"en":"If a mission measures tiny gravity changes, it can reveal hidden mass differences on Earth.","zh":"如果任務測量微小重力變化，就能揭示地球上的隱藏質量差異。"},{"en":"The phrase names the research mission used in the passage.","zh":"這個片語指出文章中使用的研究任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be placed apart","meaning":"相隔……放置","examples":[{"en":"The two satellites were placed 220 kilometres apart.","zh":"兩顆衛星相隔220公里放置。"},{"en":"Be placed apart means be positioned with a certain distance between them.","zh":"be placed apart 指以某一距離分開放置。"},{"en":"Exam desks are placed apart so students cannot easily copy answers.","zh":"考試桌相隔放置，使學生不易抄答案。"},{"en":"If two satellites are placed apart, changes in their distance can reveal gravity differences.","zh":"如果兩顆衛星相隔放置，其距離變化可以揭示重力差異。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deliberate spacing.","zh":"這個片語描述刻意保持距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"orbit above Earth","meaning":"在地球上空運行","examples":[{"en":"The satellites orbit about 500 kilometres above Earth.","zh":"衛星在地球上空約500公里運行。"},{"en":"Orbit above Earth means circle the planet at a height above its surface.","zh":"orbit above Earth 指在地球表面上方某高度圍繞地球運行。"},{"en":"Weather satellites orbit above Earth to observe clouds and storms.","zh":"天氣衛星在地球上空運行，以觀察雲和風暴。"},{"en":"If satellites orbit at the right height, they can collect data over large areas.","zh":"如果衛星在合適高度運行，就能收集大片地區的數據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement around Earth from space.","zh":"這個片語描述從太空圍繞地球運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"extremely sensitive to","meaning":"對……極為敏感","examples":[{"en":"The satellites are extremely sensitive to minor gravity differences.","zh":"這些衛星對微小重力差異極為敏感。"},{"en":"Extremely sensitive to means able to detect or react to very small changes.","zh":"extremely sensitive to 指能偵測或回應非常小的變化。"},{"en":"Some smoke alarms are extremely sensitive to tiny amounts of smoke.","zh":"有些煙霧警報器對極少量煙霧極為敏感。"},{"en":"If an instrument is extremely sensitive, it can measure differences humans cannot feel.","zh":"如果儀器極為敏感，就能測量人類感覺不到的差異。"},{"en":"The phrase describes high precision in detection or response.","zh":"這個片語描述偵測或反應上的高精確度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"minor differences in","meaning":"……方面的微小差異","examples":[{"en":"The equipment can detect minor differences in gravitational pull.","zh":"設備可以偵測引力方面的微小差異。"},{"en":"Minor differences in something are small variations that may still matter.","zh":"minor differences in something 指某方面的小變化，即使細小仍可能重要。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice minor differences in pronunciation between two students.","zh":"老師可能注意到兩名學生發音上的微小差異。"},{"en":"If instruments detect minor differences in gravity, they can reveal hidden mass changes.","zh":"如果儀器偵測到重力微小差異，就能揭示隱藏質量變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes small but measurable differences.","zh":"這個片語描述細小但可測量的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"areas they pass over","meaning":"它們飛越的地區","examples":[{"en":"The satellites measure the gravity of areas they pass over.","zh":"衛星測量它們飛越地區的重力。"},{"en":"Areas they pass over are the places directly below the satellites as they move.","zh":"areas they pass over 指衛星移動時正下方的地方。"},{"en":"A drone can photograph areas it passes over during a survey.","zh":"無人機在調查期間可以拍攝它飛越的地區。"},{"en":"If satellites repeatedly pass over the same region, they can compare measurements over time.","zh":"如果衛星反覆飛越同一地區，就能比較不同時間的測量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes places underneath a moving object.","zh":"這個片語描述移動物體下方的地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"enter an area with lower gravity","meaning":"進入重力較低的地區","examples":[{"en":"The first satellite moves when it enters an area with lower gravity.","zh":"第一顆衛星進入重力較低的地區時會移動。"},{"en":"Enter an area with lower gravity means move into a region where gravitational pull is weaker.","zh":"enter an area with lower gravity 指移入引力較弱的地區。"},{"en":"A car may slow down when it enters an area with heavy traffic.","zh":"汽車進入交通繁忙地區時可能減速。"},{"en":"If a satellite enters lower gravity, its motion changes slightly.","zh":"如果衛星進入較低重力區，其運動會略為改變。"},{"en":"The phrase connects movement into a place with a change in force.","zh":"這個片語把進入某地與力的變化連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"move slightly away from","meaning":"稍微遠離……","examples":[{"en":"The satellite moves slightly away from the Earth.","zh":"衛星稍微遠離地球。"},{"en":"Move slightly away from means shift a small distance farther from something.","zh":"move slightly away from 指與某物拉開一小段距離。"},{"en":"A student may move slightly away from a noisy window to hear the teacher better.","zh":"學生可能稍微遠離嘈吵窗戶，以便更清楚聽老師說話。"},{"en":"If gravity is weaker below a satellite, its position may change by a tiny amount.","zh":"如果衛星下方重力較弱，其位置可能改變極微小幅度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small movement away.","zh":"這個片語描述輕微遠離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"farther from","meaning":"距離……更遠","examples":[{"en":"The first satellite moves farther from the satellite behind it.","zh":"第一顆衛星距離後方衛星更遠。"},{"en":"Farther from means at a greater distance from something.","zh":"farther from 指與某物之間有更大距離。"},{"en":"A seat farther from the stage may be cheaper but harder for seeing details.","zh":"距離舞台較遠的座位可能較便宜，但較難看清細節。"},{"en":"If one satellite speeds or shifts slightly, the distance between the two changes.","zh":"如果一顆衛星加速或略為移動，兩者距離就會改變。"},{"en":"The phrase compares physical distance.","zh":"這個片語比較實際距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"following satellite","meaning":"後方的衛星","examples":[{"en":"The following satellite detects the first satellite’s movement.","zh":"後方的衛星偵測第一顆衛星的移動。"},{"en":"The following satellite is the satellite travelling behind another one.","zh":"following satellite 指在另一顆衛星後方運行的衛星。"},{"en":"In a race, the following runner watches the leader’s pace carefully.","zh":"在比賽中，後方跑手會仔細觀察領先者速度。"},{"en":"If the leading satellite changes position, the following satellite can measure the change in distance.","zh":"如果前方衛星位置改變，後方衛星可以測量距離變化。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the object behind the first one.","zh":"這個片語指出位於第一個物體後方的物體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"allow scientists to","meaning":"使科學家能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The movements allow scientists to map gravitational fields.","zh":"這些移動使科學家能夠繪製重力場地圖。"},{"en":"Allow scientists to means make it possible for scientists to do something.","zh":"allow scientists to 指使科學家能夠做某事。"},{"en":"Clear microscope images allow scientists to see cell structures.","zh":"清晰顯微鏡影像使科學家能夠看見細胞結構。"},{"en":"If satellite movements are measured precisely, they allow scientists to detect gravity changes.","zh":"如果衛星移動被精確測量，就能使科學家偵測重力變化。"},{"en":"The phrase shows what evidence makes possible.","zh":"這個片語顯示證據使甚麼成為可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"create maps of","meaning":"繪製……的地圖","examples":[{"en":"Scientists use satellite movements to create maps of gravity fields.","zh":"科學家使用衛星移動來繪製重力場地圖。"},{"en":"Create maps of means make visual representations of where something is located or how it varies.","zh":"create maps of 指製作顯示某物位置或變化的視覺圖。"},{"en":"Students may create maps of traffic noise around their school.","zh":"學生可能繪製學校周圍交通噪音地圖。"},{"en":"If scientists create maps of gravity, they can compare regions more easily.","zh":"如果科學家繪製重力地圖，就能更容易比較地區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes turning data into a map.","zh":"這個片語描述把數據變成地圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"GRACE findings","meaning":"GRACE 實驗結果","examples":[{"en":"The GRACE findings provided evidence about the Hudson Bay anomaly.","zh":"GRACE 實驗結果提供了關於哈德遜灣異常的證據。"},{"en":"GRACE findings are the results produced by the Gravity Recovery and Climate Experiment mission.","zh":"GRACE findings 指重力恢復與氣候實驗任務產生的結果。"},{"en":"Scientific findings from satellites can reveal things that cannot be seen from the ground.","zh":"來自衛星的科學發現可以揭示地面看不見的東西。"},{"en":"If GRACE findings match the former ice sheet, they support the ice-age explanation.","zh":"如果 GRACE 結果與昔日冰原吻合，就支持冰河時期解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to research results from the GRACE mission.","zh":"這個片語指 GRACE 任務的研究結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"estimate the appearance of","meaning":"推算……的面貌","examples":[{"en":"The data allowed scientists to estimate the appearance of ancient Hudson Bay.","zh":"數據使科學家能推算古代哈德遜灣的面貌。"},{"en":"Estimate the appearance of means make a reasoned guess about what something looked like.","zh":"estimate the appearance of 指根據理由推測某物看起來如何。"},{"en":"Archaeologists estimate the appearance of ancient houses from foundations and tools.","zh":"考古學家根據地基和工具推算古代房屋的面貌。"},{"en":"If scientists know where thick ice once lay, they can reconstruct the shape of the old land surface.","zh":"如果科學家知道厚冰曾位於哪裡，就能重建舊地表形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using evidence to imagine past form.","zh":"這個片語描述用證據想像過去形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"prior to","meaning":"在……之前","examples":[{"en":"The scientists reconstructed Hudson Bay prior to the great thaw.","zh":"科學家重建了大規模融冰期之前的哈德遜灣。"},{"en":"Prior to means before a particular time or event.","zh":"prior to 指在某特定時間或事件之前。"},{"en":"Students should read the instructions prior to starting the exam.","zh":"學生應在開始考試之前閱讀指示。"},{"en":"If land looked different prior to melting, scientists must reconstruct its earlier shape.","zh":"如果土地在融冰前外觀不同，科學家就必須重建其早期形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to say before.","zh":"這個片語是 before 的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"great thaw","meaning":"大規模融冰期","examples":[{"en":"The great thaw caused the Laurentide Ice Sheet to melt.","zh":"大規模融冰期使勞倫泰德冰原融化。"},{"en":"The great thaw was a major warming and melting period after the Ice Age.","zh":"great thaw 指冰河時期後一次重大的變暖和融冰時期。"},{"en":"A small thaw happens when snow melts after a cold night; a great thaw happens on a much larger scale.","zh":"寒冷夜晚後雪融化是小規模融冰；大規模融冰則發生在更大尺度。"},{"en":"If a huge ice sheet melts, the land below begins to recover slowly.","zh":"如果巨大冰原融化，下方土地會開始慢慢恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase describes large-scale melting after a cold period.","zh":"這個片語描述寒冷時期後的大規模融化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"possess the lowest gravity","meaning":"具有最低重力","examples":[{"en":"Some parts of Hudson Bay possess the lowest gravity in the region.","zh":"哈德遜灣部分地區具有該區最低重力。"},{"en":"Possess the lowest gravity means have the weakest gravitational pull compared with nearby areas.","zh":"possess the lowest gravity 指與附近地區相比具有最弱引力。"},{"en":"The lowest point in a park may collect water after heavy rain.","zh":"公園最低處可能在大雨後積水。"},{"en":"If one part has the lowest gravity, scientists ask what makes that location different.","zh":"如果某部分具有最低重力，科學家會問該地點有何不同。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the area with the weakest measured gravity.","zh":"這個片語指出測得重力最弱的地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"correlate with","meaning":"與……互相關聯","examples":[{"en":"The lowest-gravity areas correlate with the thickest ancient ice.","zh":"最低重力地區與最厚的古代冰層互相關聯。"},{"en":"Correlate with means show a connection or pattern with something else.","zh":"correlate with 指與另一事物顯示連繫或模式。"},{"en":"More study time may correlate with better test scores, although it is not the only factor.","zh":"更多學習時間可能與較好測驗成績相關，雖然不是唯一因素。"},{"en":"If low gravity areas match old ice thickness, the two may be related.","zh":"如果低重力地區與昔日冰層厚度吻合，兩者可能有關。"},{"en":"The phrase shows relationship, not automatic proof of cause.","zh":"這個片語顯示關係，不自動證明因果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"thickest layers of ice","meaning":"最厚的冰層","examples":[{"en":"The lowest gravity occurs where the thickest layers of ice once existed.","zh":"最低重力出現在曾經存在最厚冰層的地方。"},{"en":"Thickest layers of ice are the parts of an ice sheet with the greatest depth.","zh":"thickest layers of ice 指冰原中深度最大的部分。"},{"en":"The thickest layer of snow on a roof may press down hardest on the structure.","zh":"屋頂上最厚的雪層可能對結構施加最大壓力。"},{"en":"If the thickest ice pressed the land most strongly, that area may still show lower gravity.","zh":"如果最厚冰層對土地壓力最大，該地區可能仍顯示較低重力。"},{"en":"The phrase compares ice thickness across a region.","zh":"這個片語比較一個地區內的冰層厚度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"both theories","meaning":"兩個理論","examples":[{"en":"Researchers now believe that both theories are accurate.","zh":"研究人員現在相信兩個理論都是準確的。"},{"en":"Both theories means the two explanations being discussed.","zh":"both theories 指正在討論的兩個解釋。"},{"en":"If two students explain a problem differently, both theories may be partly correct.","zh":"如果兩名學生以不同方式解釋問題，兩個理論可能都有部分正確。"},{"en":"If mantle activity and ice pressure both affected gravity, one explanation does not cancel the other.","zh":"如果地幔活動和冰層壓力都影響重力，一個解釋不會取消另一個。"},{"en":"The phrase keeps two explanations together.","zh":"這個片語把兩個解釋一起保留。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"regarding","meaning":"關於","examples":[{"en":"Both theories regarding reduced gravity are now considered valid.","zh":"關於較低重力水平的兩個理論現在都被視為有效。"},{"en":"Regarding means about or concerning a particular subject.","zh":"regarding 指關於或涉及某一特定主題。"},{"en":"The school sent parents a notice regarding exam arrangements.","zh":"學校向家長發出關於考試安排的通告。"},{"en":"If two theories regarding the same anomaly are valid, they may explain different parts of it.","zh":"如果關於同一異常的兩個理論都有效，它們可能解釋不同部分。"},{"en":"The word introduces the topic under discussion.","zh":"這個詞引出正在討論的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"reduced gravity levels","meaning":"較低的重力水平","examples":[{"en":"The Hudson Bay region has reduced gravity levels.","zh":"哈德遜灣地區有較低的重力水平。"},{"en":"Reduced gravity levels are lower-than-normal measurements of gravitational pull.","zh":"reduced gravity levels 指低於正常的引力測量值。"},{"en":"Astronauts experience reduced gravity levels in space compared with Earth.","zh":"太空人在太空經歷比地球較低的重力水平。"},{"en":"If a region has reduced gravity levels, scientists look for missing mass or past pressure.","zh":"如果某地區有較低重力水平，科學家會尋找質量缺失或過去壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gravity that is weaker than expected.","zh":"這個片語描述比預期弱的重力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be accurate","meaning":"是準確的","examples":[{"en":"Scientists believe that both explanations are accurate.","zh":"科學家相信兩個解釋都是準確的。"},{"en":"Be accurate means be correct or close to the truth.","zh":"be accurate 指正確或接近事實。"},{"en":"A weather forecast is accurate if the predicted rain actually arrives.","zh":"如果預測的雨真的出現，天氣預報就是準確的。"},{"en":"If measurements are accurate, scientists can trust them when building an explanation.","zh":"如果測量是準確的，科學家在建立解釋時就能信任它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes correctness.","zh":"這個片語描述正確性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"area’s characteristics","meaning":"該地區的特徵","examples":[{"en":"The area’s characteristics result from both ancient ice and magma activity.","zh":"該地區的特徵同時來自古代冰層和岩漿活動。"},{"en":"Area’s characteristics are the special features or qualities of a place.","zh":"area’s characteristics 指某地的特殊特徵或性質。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood’s characteristics may include narrow streets, old shops, and quiet parks.","zh":"社區的特徵可能包括狹窄街道、舊商店和安靜公園。"},{"en":"If a region has unusual gravity, its characteristics may come from several hidden causes.","zh":"如果某地區有異常重力，其特徵可能來自幾個隱藏原因。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what makes a place distinctive.","zh":"這個片語指令某地與眾不同的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a result of both … and …","meaning":"同時由……和……造成","examples":[{"en":"The anomaly is a result of both mantle activity and the ice sheet.","zh":"這個異常同時由地幔活動和冰原造成。"},{"en":"A result of both A and B means caused by two factors together.","zh":"a result of both A and B 指由兩個因素共同造成。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be a result of both hard work and helpful feedback.","zh":"學生進步可能同時由努力和有用回饋造成。"},{"en":"If two processes shaped one anomaly, scientists should not choose only one explanation.","zh":"如果兩個過程塑造同一異常，科學家就不應只選一個解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase shows shared causation.","zh":"這個片語顯示共同成因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"magma activity","meaning":"岩漿活動","examples":[{"en":"Magma activity contributed greatly to the gravity reduction.","zh":"岩漿活動大大促成重力減少。"},{"en":"Magma activity is the movement or behaviour of molten rock beneath Earth’s surface.","zh":"magma activity 指地球表面下熔融岩石的移動或活動。"},{"en":"Volcanic regions often show signs of magma activity below the ground.","zh":"火山地區常顯示地下岩漿活動的跡象。"},{"en":"If magma activity changes underground mass, it can affect gravity measurements.","zh":"如果岩漿活動改變地下質量，就能影響重力測量。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to deep geological movement.","zh":"這個片語指深層地質運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"impact of the ice sheet","meaning":"冰原的影響","examples":[{"en":"The impact of the ice sheet also reduced the region’s gravity.","zh":"冰原的影響也降低了該地區的重力。"},{"en":"Impact of the ice sheet means the effect caused by the ice sheet’s weight and presence.","zh":"impact of the ice sheet 指冰原重量和存在所造成的影響。"},{"en":"The impact of heavy snow on a roof may include cracks or bending.","zh":"厚雪對屋頂的影響可能包括裂縫或彎曲。"},{"en":"If an ice sheet pressed land downward, its impact may remain long after melting.","zh":"如果冰原把土地壓下，它的影響可能在融化很久後仍存在。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the consequences of ancient ice cover.","zh":"這個片語描述古代冰覆蓋的後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"it has been estimated that","meaning":"據估計","examples":[{"en":"It has been estimated that magma explains most of the reduction.","zh":"據估計，岩漿解釋了大部分重力減少。"},{"en":"It has been estimated that means experts have calculated or judged something approximately.","zh":"it has been estimated that 指專家約略計算或判斷某事。"},{"en":"It has been estimated that the repair will cost more than expected.","zh":"據估計，維修費用會比預期高。"},{"en":"If exact measurement is difficult, scientists may use models to estimate a result.","zh":"如果精確測量困難，科學家可能使用模型估算結果。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an approximate expert calculation.","zh":"這個片語引出專家的大約計算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the former","meaning":"前者","examples":[{"en":"The former explanation refers to magma activity.","zh":"前者解釋指岩漿活動。"},{"en":"The former means the first of two things just mentioned.","zh":"the former 指剛提到的兩者中的第一個。"},{"en":"If we compare buses and taxis, the former are usually cheaper.","zh":"如果比較巴士和的士，前者通常較便宜。"},{"en":"When two theories are listed, “the former” helps avoid repeating the first theory’s name.","zh":"當列出兩個理論時，the former 有助避免重複第一個理論的名稱。"},{"en":"The phrase must refer back clearly to two earlier items.","zh":"這個片語必須清楚回指前面兩項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"account for","meaning":"佔；解釋……的成因","examples":[{"en":"Magma activity may account for most of the gravity reduction.","zh":"岩漿活動可能解釋大部分重力減少。"},{"en":"Account for means explain the reason for something or make up a share of it.","zh":"account for 指解釋某事原因，或佔其中一部分。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep may account for a student’s poor concentration.","zh":"睡眠不足可能解釋學生專注力差。"},{"en":"If magma activity accounts for most of the anomaly, it is the larger cause.","zh":"如果岩漿活動解釋大部分異常，它就是較大的成因。"},{"en":"The phrase can mean explain or represent a proportion.","zh":"這個片語可指解釋或佔比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"gravity reduction","meaning":"重力減少","examples":[{"en":"Two processes contributed to the gravity reduction.","zh":"兩個過程促成重力減少。"},{"en":"Gravity reduction means a decrease in gravitational strength.","zh":"gravity reduction 指重力強度下降。"},{"en":"Astronauts experience gravity reduction when they move far from Earth’s surface.","zh":"太空人遠離地球表面時會經歷重力減少。"},{"en":"If mass beneath a region is lower, gravity reduction may be measured there.","zh":"如果某地區下方質量較低，就可能測到重力減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gravity becoming weaker.","zh":"這個片語描述重力變弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"pressure resulting from","meaning":"由……產生的壓力","examples":[{"en":"Pressure resulting from the ice sheet caused part of the anomaly.","zh":"由冰原產生的壓力造成部分異常。"},{"en":"Pressure resulting from means force or stress caused by something.","zh":"pressure resulting from 指由某事造成的力量或壓力。"},{"en":"Back pain may result from pressure caused by carrying a heavy bag badly.","zh":"背痛可能來自不當背重書包所造成的壓力。"},{"en":"If a massive ice sheet presses on land, the resulting pressure can deform the surface.","zh":"如果巨大冰原壓在土地上，由此產生的壓力可以使地表變形。"},{"en":"The phrase links pressure with its source.","zh":"這個片語把壓力與其來源連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the latter","meaning":"後者","examples":[{"en":"The latter explanation concerns the Laurentide Ice Sheet.","zh":"後者解釋涉及勞倫泰德冰原。"},{"en":"The latter means the second of two things just mentioned.","zh":"the latter 指剛提到的兩者中的第二個。"},{"en":"If we compare studying alone and studying with feedback, the latter often helps students improve faster.","zh":"如果比較獨自溫習和帶回饋溫習，後者常幫助學生更快進步。"},{"en":"When two causes are listed, “the latter” refers to the second cause.","zh":"當列出兩個原因時，the latter 指第二個原因。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful only when two items have clearly been introduced.","zh":"這個片語只在已清楚介紹兩項時有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"effects of","meaning":"……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The effects of the ancient ice sheet are reversible.","zh":"古代冰原的影響是可逆的。"},{"en":"Effects of something are the results or changes caused by it.","zh":"effects of something 指由某事造成的結果或變化。"},{"en":"The effects of poor sleep include tiredness, weak memory, and irritability.","zh":"睡眠不足的影響包括疲倦、記憶力弱和易怒。"},{"en":"If the effects of ice pressure remain, scientists can still measure them long after melting.","zh":"如果冰壓影響仍存在，科學家在融化很久後仍可測量它們。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on consequences.","zh":"這個片語集中於後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be reversible","meaning":"是可逆的","examples":[{"en":"The depression of the land is gradually reversible.","zh":"土地下陷是逐漸可逆的。"},{"en":"Be reversible means be able to change back to an earlier condition.","zh":"be reversible 指能回復到早前狀態。"},{"en":"Some lifestyle-related health problems may be reversible if habits improve early.","zh":"如果及早改善習慣，有些與生活方式有關的健康問題可能是可逆的。"},{"en":"If land rises after ice melts, the depression is partly reversible.","zh":"如果冰融化後土地上升，下陷就部分可逆。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change that can be undone.","zh":"這個片語描述可以被恢復的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"capability to rebound","meaning":"回彈能力","examples":[{"en":"The Earth’s layers have the capability to rebound.","zh":"地球各層具有回彈能力。"},{"en":"Capability to rebound means the ability to rise back or recover after being pressed down.","zh":"capability to rebound 指受壓後重新升起或恢復的能力。"},{"en":"A sponge has the capability to rebound after being squeezed.","zh":"海綿被擠壓後具有回彈能力。"},{"en":"If land has rebound capability, it can slowly rise after the weight above it is removed.","zh":"如果土地有回彈能力，上方重量移除後就能慢慢上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recovery after pressure.","zh":"這個片語描述受壓後的恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in response to","meaning":"回應……；因應……","examples":[{"en":"The land rebounds in response to the removal of weight.","zh":"土地因應重量移除而回彈。"},{"en":"In response to means as a reaction to something that has happened.","zh":"in response to 指作為對已發生事情的反應。"},{"en":"A school may add more buses in response to parents’ complaints about transport.","zh":"學校可能因應家長對交通的投訴而增加校巴。"},{"en":"If ice weight is removed, the land reacts by slowly rising.","zh":"如果冰的重量被移除，土地會透過慢慢上升作出反應。"},{"en":"The phrase links an action with the reaction it causes.","zh":"這個片語把行動與其造成的反應連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"removal of the weight","meaning":"重量的移除","examples":[{"en":"The removal of the ice’s weight allows the land to rise.","zh":"冰層重量的移除使土地得以上升。"},{"en":"Removal of the weight means taking away the heavy pressure from something.","zh":"removal of the weight 指把沉重壓力從某物上移走。"},{"en":"A shelf may bend less after the removal of heavy books.","zh":"移走沉重書本後，書架可能彎曲得較少。"},{"en":"If the weight of ice disappears, the land below can begin to recover.","zh":"如果冰的重量消失，下方土地就能開始恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pressure being taken away.","zh":"這個片語描述壓力被拿走。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"restrict","meaning":"限制","examples":[{"en":"The ice once restricted the Earth’s surface from rising.","zh":"冰層曾限制地球表面上升。"},{"en":"Restrict means limit or prevent movement, freedom, or action.","zh":"restrict 指限制或阻止移動、自由或行動。"},{"en":"A school may restrict phone use during lessons so students can focus.","zh":"學校可能限制上課時使用手機，使學生能專心。"},{"en":"If heavy ice restricts land movement, the surface cannot rebound until the weight is removed.","zh":"如果厚冰限制土地移動，地表要到重量移除後才能回彈。"},{"en":"The word describes a limiting force or rule.","zh":"這個詞描述限制性的力量或規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"return to the original position","meaning":"回復原來位置","examples":[{"en":"The land is slowly returning to its original position.","zh":"土地正慢慢回復原來位置。"},{"en":"Return to the original position means move back to where something was before.","zh":"return to the original position 指移回某物以前所在的位置。"},{"en":"After using a chair, students should return it to its original position under the desk.","zh":"學生使用椅子後，應把它放回書桌下的原來位置。"},{"en":"If land was pressed down by ice, it may slowly rise back after the ice melts.","zh":"如果土地曾被冰壓下，冰融化後它可能慢慢升回去。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recovery of position.","zh":"這個片語描述位置恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"extremely slow process","meaning":"極其緩慢的過程","examples":[{"en":"The recovery of the land is an extremely slow process.","zh":"土地恢復是一個極其緩慢的過程。"},{"en":"An extremely slow process is a change that happens very gradually over a long time.","zh":"extremely slow process 指在很長時間內非常逐漸發生的變化。"},{"en":"Learning a difficult language can be an extremely slow process without regular practice.","zh":"如果沒有定期練習，學習困難語言可以是一個極其緩慢的過程。"},{"en":"If land rises only a little each year, full recovery may take thousands of years.","zh":"如果土地每年只上升少許，完全恢復可能需要數千年。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that change is not quick.","zh":"這個片語提醒變化並不快速。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"take a further 5,000 years","meaning":"還需要五千年","examples":[{"en":"The region may take a further 5,000 years to recover fully.","zh":"該地區可能還需要五千年才能完全恢復。"},{"en":"Take a further 5,000 years means need another five thousand years from now or from the stated time.","zh":"take a further 5,000 years 指從現在或所述時間起還需要五千年。"},{"en":"A project may take a further two weeks if workers find hidden damage.","zh":"如果工人發現隱藏損壞，項目可能還需要兩星期。"},{"en":"If land recovery is extremely slow, thousands more years may be needed.","zh":"如果土地恢復極其緩慢，就可能還需要數千年。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an additional time required for completion.","zh":"這個片語給出完成所需的額外時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"recover the altitude","meaning":"恢復原有海拔高度","examples":[{"en":"The land will eventually recover the altitude it once possessed.","zh":"土地最終會恢復它曾擁有的海拔高度。"},{"en":"Recover the altitude means regain the height above sea level that existed before.","zh":"recover the altitude 指重新取得以前的海拔高度。"},{"en":"A balloon may recover altitude after losing height if more hot air is added.","zh":"如果加入更多熱空氣，氣球在下降後可能恢復高度。"},{"en":"If land rebounds after ice melts, it slowly regains its former height.","zh":"如果冰融化後土地回彈，它會慢慢恢復以前高度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes returning to a previous elevation.","zh":"這個片語描述回到以前的海拔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"prior to the ice sheet","meaning":"在冰原形成之前","examples":[{"en":"The region was higher prior to the Laurentide Ice Sheet.","zh":"該地區在勞倫泰德冰原形成之前較高。"},{"en":"Prior to the ice sheet means before the ice sheet formed or covered the area.","zh":"prior to the ice sheet 指在冰原形成或覆蓋該地區之前。"},{"en":"Prior to the renovation, the classroom had old desks and poor lighting.","zh":"翻新前，課室有舊書桌和差劣照明。"},{"en":"If land was higher before the ice sheet, later ice pressure must have pushed it down.","zh":"如果土地在冰原形成前較高，後來冰壓必定把它壓低。"},{"en":"The phrase compares conditions before ice coverage.","zh":"這個片語比較冰覆蓋前的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"rebound activity","meaning":"地殼回彈活動","examples":[{"en":"Scientists can measure rebound activity around Hudson Bay.","zh":"科學家可以測量哈德遜灣周圍的地殼回彈活動。"},{"en":"Rebound activity is the gradual rising of land after heavy ice has melted.","zh":"rebound activity 指厚冰融化後土地逐漸上升。"},{"en":"A sponge’s rebound after being pressed is a simple everyday comparison.","zh":"海綿被壓後回彈，是一個簡單日常比較。"},{"en":"If rebound activity continues, sea levels relative to the land may appear to fall.","zh":"如果回彈活動持續，相對於土地的海平面可能看似下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the land’s slow recovery movement.","zh":"這個片語描述土地緩慢恢復運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be measurable through","meaning":"可透過……測量","examples":[{"en":"The rebound is measurable through observations of sea level.","zh":"回彈可透過海平面觀察測量。"},{"en":"Be measurable through means able to be detected or calculated by using a particular method.","zh":"be measurable through 指能透過某特定方法偵測或計算。"},{"en":"Student progress is measurable through regular quizzes and writing tasks.","zh":"學生進步可透過定期小測和寫作任務測量。"},{"en":"If land rises, sea-level observations can help measure that change.","zh":"如果土地上升，海平面觀察可以幫助測量該變化。"},{"en":"The phrase connects measurement with method.","zh":"這個片語把測量與方法連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"observation of sea levels","meaning":"海平面觀察","examples":[{"en":"Observation of sea levels provides evidence of land rebound.","zh":"海平面觀察提供土地回彈的證據。"},{"en":"Observation of sea levels means careful monitoring of how high the sea is over time.","zh":"observation of sea levels 指仔細監測海水高度如何隨時間變化。"},{"en":"Coastal cities use observation of sea levels to prepare for flooding risks.","zh":"沿海城市使用海平面觀察來準備洪水風險。"},{"en":"If land rises while the ocean stays similar, local sea level may seem to fall.","zh":"如果土地上升而海洋大致不變，本地海平面可能看似下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes collecting evidence from sea-height changes.","zh":"這個片語描述從海水高度變化收集證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"unlike the rest of the world","meaning":"與世界其他地區不同","examples":[{"en":"Unlike the rest of the world, sea levels are falling in this region.","zh":"與世界其他地區不同，該地區的海平面正在下降。"},{"en":"Unlike the rest of the world means different from what is happening in most other places.","zh":"unlike the rest of the world 指與大多數其他地方正在發生的情況不同。"},{"en":"Unlike the rest of the class, one student finished the task early.","zh":"與班上其他同學不同，一名學生很早完成任務。"},{"en":"If sea levels fall locally while rising globally, local land movement may be the cause.","zh":"如果本地海平面下降，而全球海平面上升，原因可能是本地土地運動。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights an exception to a general pattern.","zh":"這個片語突出一般模式中的例外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"as a result of melting icecaps","meaning":"由冰帽融化造成","examples":[{"en":"Sea levels usually rise as a result of melting icecaps.","zh":"海平面通常由冰帽融化造成而上升。"},{"en":"As a result of melting icecaps means because large areas of polar ice are melting.","zh":"as a result of melting icecaps 指因大片極地冰層正在融化。"},{"en":"Coastal flooding may increase as a result of higher sea levels.","zh":"海平面上升可能導致沿海洪水增加。"},{"en":"If icecaps melt, water enters the oceans and can raise global sea levels.","zh":"如果冰帽融化，水進入海洋並可提高全球海平面。"},{"en":"The phrase links melting ice with sea-level rise.","zh":"這個片語把冰融化與海平面上升連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"recover its previous form","meaning":"恢復原來形態","examples":[{"en":"The land is slowly recovering its previous form.","zh":"土地正慢慢恢復原來形態。"},{"en":"Recover its previous form means return gradually to the shape or condition it had before.","zh":"recover its previous form 指逐漸回到以前的形狀或狀態。"},{"en":"A squeezed cushion can recover its previous form after the pressure is removed.","zh":"被擠壓的咕(cid:0)在壓力移除後可以恢復原來形態。"},{"en":"If ice pressure disappears, the land may slowly regain its earlier shape.","zh":"如果冰壓消失，土地可能慢慢恢復早前形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual restoration.","zh":"這個片語描述逐漸復原。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"research conducted into","meaning":"對……進行的研究","examples":[{"en":"Research conducted into the ice sheet has global importance.","zh":"對冰原進行的研究具有全球重要性。"},{"en":"Research conducted into something means a study carried out about that subject.","zh":"research conducted into something 指對某主題進行的研究。"},{"en":"Research conducted into student stress can help schools change homework policies.","zh":"對學生壓力進行的研究可以幫助學校改變功課政策。"},{"en":"If research into an ice sheet explains land change, it may also help climate science.","zh":"如果對冰原的研究解釋土地變化，也可能幫助氣候科學。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the topic being studied.","zh":"這個片語指出被研究的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"have significant implications","meaning":"有重大影響；有重要啟示","examples":[{"en":"The research has significant implications for understanding climate change.","zh":"這項研究對理解氣候變化有重要啟示。"},{"en":"Have significant implications means have important effects, meanings, or lessons for something else.","zh":"have significant implications 指對其他事情有重要影響、意義或啟示。"},{"en":"Exam results can have significant implications for university choices.","zh":"考試成績可以對大學選擇有重大影響。"},{"en":"If ice-age changes still affect Earth today, the findings matter for future climate predictions.","zh":"如果冰河時期變化至今仍影響地球，這些發現對未來氣候預測就很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase points to wider importance beyond the immediate topic.","zh":"這個片語指出超越眼前主題的更廣泛重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"on a global scale","meaning":"在全球層面","examples":[{"en":"The findings are important on a global scale.","zh":"這些發現在全球層面都很重要。"},{"en":"On a global scale means across the whole world or in relation to worldwide systems.","zh":"on a global scale 指在全世界範圍內，或與全球系統有關。"},{"en":"Plastic pollution is a problem on a global scale because oceans connect countries.","zh":"塑膠污染是在全球層面的問題，因為海洋連接各國。"},{"en":"If a local study helps explain worldwide climate change, its value becomes global.","zh":"如果本地研究有助解釋全球氣候變化，其價值就變成全球性的。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses worldwide importance.","zh":"這個片語強調全球重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"increased knowledge of","meaning":"對……有更深入的認識","examples":[{"en":"Increased knowledge of Hudson Bay can improve predictions elsewhere.","zh":"對哈德遜灣有更深入的認識，可以改善其他地方的預測。"},{"en":"Increased knowledge of means a deeper or larger understanding of something.","zh":"increased knowledge of 指對某事有更深或更多理解。"},{"en":"Increased knowledge of nutrition can help families choose healthier meals.","zh":"對營養有更深入認識，可以幫助家庭選擇更健康膳食。"},{"en":"If scientists understand one region better, they may apply lessons carefully to other regions.","zh":"如果科學家更了解一個地區，就可能謹慎地把經驗應用到其他地區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improved understanding.","zh":"這個片語描述理解增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"change over time","meaning":"隨時間改變","examples":[{"en":"The research shows how the region has changed over time.","zh":"研究顯示該地區如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"Change over time means become different gradually or across a period.","zh":"change over time 指在一段時間內逐漸變得不同。"},{"en":"A student’s writing can change over time with practice and feedback.","zh":"學生的寫作可以透過練習和回饋隨時間改變。"},{"en":"If land rises slowly for thousands of years, its shape changes over time.","zh":"如果土地在數千年間慢慢上升，其形狀就會隨時間改變。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on development across time.","zh":"這個片語集中於跨時間的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"long-term implications","meaning":"長遠影響","examples":[{"en":"The Ice Age had long-term implications for the Earth’s surface.","zh":"冰河時期對地球表面有長遠影響。"},{"en":"Long-term implications are effects or meanings that continue far into the future.","zh":"long-term implications 指持續到很久以後的影響或意義。"},{"en":"Poor study habits can have long-term implications for confidence and exam results.","zh":"不良學習習慣可以對信心和考試成績有長遠影響。"},{"en":"If ancient ice still affects land today, its implications are clearly long-term.","zh":"如果古代冰層至今仍影響土地，其影響顯然是長遠的。"},{"en":"The phrase points to consequences that last.","zh":"這個片語指出持久後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"pave the way to","meaning":"為……鋪路","examples":[{"en":"The findings pave the way to a better understanding of future changes.","zh":"這些發現為更深入理解未來變化鋪路。"},{"en":"Pave the way to means make progress towards something possible.","zh":"pave the way to 指使朝某事邁進成為可能。"},{"en":"Learning basic vocabulary can pave the way to more confident speaking.","zh":"學習基本詞彙可以為更有信心的口語鋪路。"},{"en":"If one study explains past change, it may help scientists understand future change.","zh":"如果一項研究解釋過去變化，就可能幫助科學家理解未來變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preparing for a later achievement.","zh":"這個片語描述為後來成就作準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a better understanding of","meaning":"對……有更深入的理解","examples":[{"en":"The research provides a better understanding of long-term change.","zh":"這項研究提供了對長期變化更深入的理解。"},{"en":"A better understanding of something means clearer and deeper knowledge of it.","zh":"a better understanding of something 指對某事有更清楚、更深入的認識。"},{"en":"Examples give students a better understanding of difficult vocabulary.","zh":"例子讓學生對困難詞彙有更深入理解。"},{"en":"If scientists understand past land movement better, they can interpret present changes more carefully.","zh":"如果科學家更了解過去土地運動，就能更謹慎解讀現在變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improved comprehension.","zh":"這個片語描述理解改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"current changes elsewhere","meaning":"其他地方目前的變化","examples":[{"en":"The findings may help scientists understand current changes elsewhere.","zh":"這些發現可能幫助科學家理解其他地方目前的變化。"},{"en":"Current changes elsewhere are changes happening now in other places.","zh":"current changes elsewhere 指正在其他地方發生的變化。"},{"en":"A study of one school may help explain current changes elsewhere if other schools face similar problems.","zh":"如果其他學校面對相似問題，一所學校的研究可能有助解釋其他地方目前的變化。"},{"en":"If one region’s long-term recovery is understood, scientists may compare it with present climate effects in other regions.","zh":"如果理解某地區的長期恢復，科學家可把它與其他地區目前氣候影響比較。"},{"en":"The phrase connects one study with changes beyond its location.","zh":"這個片語把一項研究與其所在地以外的變化連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"manifest themselves","meaning":"顯現出來","examples":[{"en":"Environmental changes may manifest themselves gradually over time.","zh":"環境變化可能隨時間逐漸顯現出來。"},{"en":"Manifest themselves means become visible, noticeable, or clear.","zh":"manifest themselves 指變得可見、可察覺或清楚。"},{"en":"Stress may manifest itself as headaches, poor sleep, or irritability.","zh":"壓力可能以頭痛、睡眠差或易怒形式顯現出來。"},{"en":"If climate effects manifest themselves slowly, people may not notice them immediately.","zh":"如果氣候影響慢慢顯現，人們可能不會立即注意到。"},{"en":"The phrase describes hidden changes becoming observable.","zh":"這個片語描述隱藏變化變得可觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"over the long term","meaning":"從長遠來看","examples":[{"en":"The effects of climate change may become clearer over the long term.","zh":"氣候變化的影響從長遠來看可能變得更清楚。"},{"en":"Over the long term means across a long period of time.","zh":"over the long term 指在很長一段時間內。"},{"en":"Regular reading improves vocabulary over the long term.","zh":"定期閱讀從長遠來看會改善詞彙量。"},{"en":"If land rebounds slowly, its full effect can only be seen over the long term.","zh":"如果土地慢慢回彈，其完整影響只能從長遠來看才看見。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts lasting development with immediate results.","zh":"這個片語把持久發展與即時結果作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct heading for each paragraph.","zh":"學生為每段選出正確標題。"},{"en":"Choose the correct heading means select the title that best matches a paragraph’s main idea.","zh":"choose the correct heading 指選出最符合段落主旨的標題。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should read the whole paragraph before choosing the heading.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先讀完整段才選標題。"},{"en":"If a heading only matches one detail, it may not be the correct heading.","zh":"如果標題只符合一個細節，就未必是正確標題。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見閱讀考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The list of headings contains more choices than needed.","zh":"標題列表包含比需要更多的選項。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a group of possible paragraph titles.","zh":"list of headings 指一組可能的段落標題。"},{"en":"Students should cross out headings already used if each one can be used only once.","zh":"如果每個標題只能用一次，學生應劃走已用標題。"},{"en":"If the list has extra headings, students must avoid attractive but incorrect options.","zh":"如果列表有多餘標題，學生必須避開吸引但錯誤的選項。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the answer choices in a matching task.","zh":"這個片語指配對題中的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"write the correct number","meaning":"寫上正確編號","examples":[{"en":"Students write the correct number in each answer box.","zh":"學生在每個答案框中寫上正確編號。"},{"en":"Write the correct number means put the number of the chosen answer in the required space.","zh":"write the correct number 指把所選答案的編號填在指定位置。"},{"en":"In matching questions, students may write a Roman numeral instead of a word.","zh":"在配對題中，學生可能要寫羅馬數字而不是字詞。"},{"en":"If the number is copied wrongly, the answer may be marked incorrect even if the idea is right.","zh":"如果編號抄錯，即使想法正確，答案也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an exam-answer instruction.","zh":"這個片語給出考試作答指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"historic theories","meaning":"歷史上的理論","examples":[{"en":"The first paragraph describes historic theories of gravity.","zh":"第一段描述歷史上的重力理論。"},{"en":"Historic theories are old explanations developed in earlier periods of history.","zh":"historic theories 指在較早歷史時期發展出的舊解釋。"},{"en":"Science classes often compare historic theories with modern scientific models.","zh":"科學課常比較歷史上的理論與現代科學模型。"},{"en":"If historic theories are later disproved, they can still show how human understanding developed.","zh":"即使歷史理論後來被推翻，它們仍能顯示人類理解如何發展。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to theories from the past.","zh":"這個片語指過去的理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"scientific definition","meaning":"科學定義","examples":[{"en":"The passage provides a scientific definition of gravitation.","zh":"文章提供了萬有引力的科學定義。"},{"en":"A scientific definition is a precise explanation used in science.","zh":"scientific definition 指科學中使用的精確解釋。"},{"en":"A scientific definition of “mass” is more exact than everyday ideas about heaviness.","zh":"“mass” 的科學定義比日常對重量的想法更精確。"},{"en":"If a word has a scientific definition, students should use it carefully in exams.","zh":"如果一個詞有科學定義，學生在考試中應謹慎使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes technical meaning.","zh":"這個片語描述技術性意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"contemporary views","meaning":"當代觀點","examples":[{"en":"The paragraph also discusses contemporary views of gravity.","zh":"該段也討論重力的當代觀點。"},{"en":"Contemporary views are modern or current opinions and explanations.","zh":"contemporary views 指現代或目前的意見和解釋。"},{"en":"Contemporary views on education often stress creativity as well as exam results.","zh":"當代教育觀點常強調創意以及考試成績。"},{"en":"If contemporary views differ from ancient theories, knowledge has changed over time.","zh":"如果當代觀點與古代理論不同，知識就已隨時間改變。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts present thinking with older thinking.","zh":"這個片語把當前思想與較舊思想作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"general rule of gravity","meaning":"重力的一般規律","examples":[{"en":"Gravity is generally proportional to mass.","zh":"重力通常與質量成正比。"},{"en":"The general rule of gravity is the broad principle that greater mass usually means stronger gravity.","zh":"general rule of gravity 指質量越大，重力通常越強的廣泛原則。"},{"en":"A physics teacher may teach the general rule before showing exceptions and complications.","zh":"物理老師可能先教一般規律，再展示例外和複雜情況。"},{"en":"If one place breaks the general rule, scientists look for unusual local causes.","zh":"如果某地方違反一般規律，科學家會尋找異常本地原因。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the normal pattern, not every special case.","zh":"這個片語指正常模式，而不是每個特殊情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"an exception","meaning":"例外情況","examples":[{"en":"The Hudson Bay region appears to be an exception to the general rule.","zh":"哈德遜灣地區似乎是一般規律的例外情況。"},{"en":"An exception is a case that does not follow the normal rule or pattern.","zh":"an exception 指不遵循正常規則或模式的情況。"},{"en":"Most students arrived on time; one late student was the exception.","zh":"大部分學生準時到達；一名遲到學生就是例外。"},{"en":"If Hudson Bay has lower gravity than expected, it needs a special explanation.","zh":"如果哈德遜灣重力低於預期，就需要特殊解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase marks something unusual.","zh":"這個片語標示不尋常情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"initial explanation","meaning":"最初的解釋","examples":[{"en":"Mantle activity provided the initial explanation for the anomaly.","zh":"地幔活動為該異常提供了最初的解釋。"},{"en":"An initial explanation is the first reason offered to explain something.","zh":"initial explanation 指用來解釋某事的第一個原因。"},{"en":"A doctor’s initial explanation for a cough may change after test results arrive.","zh":"醫生對咳嗽的最初解釋可能在檢查結果出來後改變。"},{"en":"If later evidence appears, the initial explanation may be refined.","zh":"如果後來出現證據，最初解釋可能被修正。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the earliest proposed answer.","zh":"這個片語指最早提出的答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"alternative viewpoint","meaning":"另一種觀點","examples":[{"en":"The Ice Age theory offered an alternative viewpoint.","zh":"冰河時期理論提供了另一種觀點。"},{"en":"An alternative viewpoint is a different way of understanding the same issue.","zh":"alternative viewpoint 指理解同一問題的不同方式。"},{"en":"In class discussion, an alternative viewpoint can help students see a problem from another angle.","zh":"在課堂討論中，另一種觀點可以幫助學生從另一角度看問題。"},{"en":"If one theory focuses on magma, an alternative viewpoint may focus on ancient ice.","zh":"如果一個理論聚焦岩漿，另一種觀點可能聚焦古代冰層。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces another perspective.","zh":"這個片語引出另一個角度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"substantiate a hypothesis","meaning":"證實假說","examples":[{"en":"The satellite data helped substantiate the Ice Age hypothesis.","zh":"衛星數據幫助證實冰河時期假說。"},{"en":"Substantiate a hypothesis means support a possible explanation with evidence.","zh":"substantiate a hypothesis 指用證據支持一個可能解釋。"},{"en":"A student can substantiate an argument by giving examples from the passage.","zh":"學生可以透過引用文章例子來證實論點。"},{"en":"If satellite data match the predicted pattern, they strengthen the hypothesis.","zh":"如果衛星數據與預測模式吻合，就會加強該假說。"},{"en":"The phrase means provide evidence, not merely repeat a claim.","zh":"這個片語指提供證據，而不只是重複主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"consolidate theories","meaning":"整合多個理論","examples":[{"en":"Later researchers consolidated the two theories into one explanation.","zh":"後來研究人員把兩個理論整合成一個解釋。"},{"en":"Consolidate theories means combine separate theories into a stronger or more complete explanation.","zh":"consolidate theories 指把分開的理論結合成更有力或更完整的解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may consolidate students’ ideas into one clear class summary.","zh":"老師可能把學生的想法整合成一份清晰課堂總結。"},{"en":"If two explanations each account for part of the evidence, they can be combined.","zh":"如果兩個解釋各自說明部分證據，它們就可以被結合。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bringing ideas together.","zh":"這個片語描述把想法合併。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"return to previous form","meaning":"回復原來形態","examples":[{"en":"The land is slowly returning to its previous form.","zh":"土地正慢慢回復原來形態。"},{"en":"Return to previous form means gradually go back to an earlier shape or condition.","zh":"return to previous form 指逐漸回到較早的形狀或狀態。"},{"en":"A bent plastic ruler may return to its previous form after pressure is released.","zh":"彎曲膠尺在壓力釋放後可能回復原來形態。"},{"en":"If Earth’s surface rebounds, the land slowly recovers its earlier shape.","zh":"如果地球表面回彈，土地就慢慢恢復早前形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes restoration after change.","zh":"這個片語描述改變後復原。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"relevance to our future","meaning":"與我們未來的關聯","examples":[{"en":"The findings have relevance to our future understanding of climate change.","zh":"這些發現與我們未來理解氣候變化有關。"},{"en":"Relevance to our future means importance for what people will need to know or do later.","zh":"relevance to our future 指對人們將來需要知道或做的事有重要性。"},{"en":"Digital skills have relevance to students’ future work and communication.","zh":"數碼技能與學生未來工作和溝通有關。"},{"en":"If past climate effects lasted thousands of years, they matter for future planning.","zh":"如果過去氣候影響持續數千年，它們就對未來規劃有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase connects present knowledge with future needs.","zh":"這個片語把現在知識與未來需要連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與文章資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷每句陳述是否與文章一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the information means match what the text says.","zh":"agree with the information 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"In a True/False question, an answer is true if it agrees with the information in the passage.","zh":"在 True/False 題中，如果答案與文章資料一致，就是 True。"},{"en":"If a statement changes an important detail, it no longer agrees with the text.","zh":"如果陳述改變重要細節，就不再與文章一致。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in reading comprehension instructions.","zh":"這個片語常見於閱讀理解指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文章資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information given.","zh":"False 陳述與所給資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradict the information means say the opposite of what the text states.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章內容相反的意思。"},{"en":"If a passage says the Moon has less gravity, a statement saying it has more gravity contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說月球重力較低，而陳述說月球重力較高，就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should look for direct conflict before choosing False.","zh":"學生選 False 前應尋找直接衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a clear mismatch with the text.","zh":"這個片語描述與文章清楚不吻合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有關於此事的資料","examples":[{"en":"Not Given means that the passage provides no information on the point.","zh":"Not Given 指文章沒有關於該點的資料。"},{"en":"No information on this means the text does not tell us whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有告訴我們該陳述是真還是假。"},{"en":"If a passage discusses gravity but not the cost of satellites, there is no information on that cost.","zh":"如果文章討論重力但沒有討論衛星成本，文章就沒有關於該成本的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when the passage gives no information.","zh":"當文章沒有資料時，學生不應使用外部知識作答。"},{"en":"The phrase explains when to choose Not Given.","zh":"這個片語解釋何時選 Not Given。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"differentiation between","meaning":"……之間的區別","examples":[{"en":"The question concerns the differentiation between gravity and gravitation.","zh":"題目關於 gravity 和 gravitation 之間的區別。"},{"en":"Differentiation between means the distinction or difference between two things.","zh":"differentiation between 指兩件事之間的區分或差異。"},{"en":"Teachers explain the differentiation between “borrow” and “lend” because students often confuse them.","zh":"老師解釋 borrow 和 lend 之間的區別，因為學生常混淆。"},{"en":"If two terms seem similar, careful differentiation prevents mistakes.","zh":"如果兩個術語看似相似，仔細區分可避免錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on separating meanings.","zh":"這個片語集中於分辨意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"generally only made by","meaning":"通常只由……作出","examples":[{"en":"The distinction may be generally only made by scientific specialists.","zh":"這種區別通常只由科學專家作出。"},{"en":"Generally only made by means usually recognised or used only by a particular group.","zh":"generally only made by 指通常只由某特定群體認出或使用。"},{"en":"Some grammar distinctions are generally only made by teachers and language editors.","zh":"有些文法區別通常只由老師和語言編輯作出。"},{"en":"If ordinary speakers do not make a distinction, it may still matter in technical writing.","zh":"如果普通說話者不作區分，它在技術寫作中仍可能重要。"},{"en":"The phrase shows limited or specialist usage.","zh":"這個片語顯示有限或專門用法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"academics in the field","meaning":"該領域的學者","examples":[{"en":"Academics in the field use the terms more precisely.","zh":"該領域的學者更精確地使用這些術語。"},{"en":"Academics in the field are scholars or researchers who specialise in that subject.","zh":"academics in the field 指專門研究該主題的學者或研究人員。"},{"en":"Academics in the field of medicine may use terms differently from ordinary patients.","zh":"醫學領域的學者可能使用與普通病人不同的術語。"},{"en":"If specialists use language precisely, students should follow that usage in exams.","zh":"如果專家精確使用語言，學生在考試中應跟隨該用法。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies expert users of a subject’s terminology.","zh":"這個片語指出某學科術語的專家使用者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"around the equator","meaning":"赤道附近","examples":[{"en":"Gravity varies between areas around the equator and the poles.","zh":"重力在赤道附近和兩極地區之間有所不同。"},{"en":"Around the equator means near the imaginary line around the middle of Earth.","zh":"around the equator 指靠近環繞地球中部的想像線。"},{"en":"Countries around the equator often have warm weather throughout the year.","zh":"赤道附近國家通常全年天氣溫暖。"},{"en":"Because Earth bulges around the equator, gravity there can differ slightly from gravity at the poles.","zh":"由於地球在赤道附近隆起，那裡重力可能與兩極略有不同。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a location near Earth’s middle.","zh":"這個片語給出接近地球中部的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"significantly higher than","meaning":"顯著高於……","examples":[{"en":"The statement compares whether gravity is significantly higher in one region.","zh":"該陳述比較某地區重力是否顯著高於另一地區。"},{"en":"Significantly higher than means much greater than something else in an important way.","zh":"significantly higher than 指在重要程度上比另一事物高很多。"},{"en":"Rent may be significantly higher in the city centre than in outer districts.","zh":"市中心租金可能顯著高於外圍地區。"},{"en":"If one region’s gravity is significantly higher, scientists look for more mass or different shape.","zh":"如果某地區重力顯著較高，科學家會尋找更多質量或不同形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an important upward comparison.","zh":"這個片語描述重要的向上比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be attributed to","meaning":"被歸因於……","examples":[{"en":"The gravity anomaly was initially attributed to mantle activity.","zh":"重力異常最初被歸因於地幔活動。"},{"en":"Be attributed to means be explained as the result of a particular cause.","zh":"be attributed to 指被解釋為由某特定原因造成。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be attributed to regular practice.","zh":"學生進步可能被歸因於定期練習。"},{"en":"If an anomaly is attributed to mantle movement, scientists think that movement caused it.","zh":"如果異常被歸因於地幔運動，科學家認為該運動造成了它。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an effect with a proposed explanation.","zh":"這個片語把結果與提出的解釋連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"location between","meaning":"位於……之間的位置","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to Hudson Bay’s location between the poles and equator.","zh":"該陳述提到哈德遜灣位於兩極與赤道之間的位置。"},{"en":"Location between means the position of something in relation to two other places or points.","zh":"location between 指某物相對於另外兩個地方或點的位置。"},{"en":"A school’s location between two railway stations may make it easy to reach.","zh":"學校位於兩個鐵路站之間的位置，可能使它容易到達。"},{"en":"If a region lies between the equator and poles, latitude may affect its gravity slightly.","zh":"如果某地區位於赤道和兩極之間，緯度可能略微影響其重力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes relative position.","zh":"這個片語描述相對位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"molten rock activity","meaning":"熔岩活動","examples":[{"en":"Molten rock activity beneath the surface affects continental plates.","zh":"地表下的熔岩活動影響大陸板塊。"},{"en":"Molten rock activity is the movement or flow of hot liquid rock underground.","zh":"molten rock activity 指地下高溫液態岩石的移動或流動。"},{"en":"Volcano monitoring often looks for signs of molten rock activity below the surface.","zh":"火山監測常尋找地表下熔岩活動的跡象。"},{"en":"If molten rock moves, it can create pressure and help shift plates.","zh":"如果熔岩移動，就能產生壓力並幫助板塊移動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to underground geological activity.","zh":"這個片語指地下地質活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"have less of an impact on","meaning":"對……影響較小","examples":[{"en":"The statement compares which process had less of an impact on gravity.","zh":"該陳述比較哪個過程對重力影響較小。"},{"en":"Have less of an impact on means affect something less strongly than another factor does.","zh":"have less of an impact on 指比另一因素對某事影響較弱。"},{"en":"A short delay may have less of an impact on students than a cancelled lesson.","zh":"短暫延誤對學生的影響可能比取消課堂小。"},{"en":"If ice pressure accounts for less gravity reduction than magma activity, it has less of an impact.","zh":"如果冰壓解釋的重力減少少於岩漿活動，它的影響就較小。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the strength of effects.","zh":"這個片語比較影響強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"main focus","meaning":"主要焦點","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Canada was the project’s main focus.","zh":"該陳述問加拿大是否是項目的主要焦點。"},{"en":"Main focus means the central subject or most important area of attention.","zh":"main focus 指中心主題或最重要的注意範圍。"},{"en":"A lesson’s main focus may be speaking practice rather than grammar drills.","zh":"一堂課的主要焦點可能是口語練習，而不是文法操練。"},{"en":"If a project’s main focus is gravity, Canada may be one example rather than the whole purpose.","zh":"如果項目主要焦點是重力，加拿大可能只是例子，而不是整個目的。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what receives the most attention.","zh":"這個片語指出最受關注的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"once thought to be covered by","meaning":"曾被認為由……覆蓋","examples":[{"en":"The area was once thought to be covered by a thick ice sheet.","zh":"該地區曾被認為由厚冰原覆蓋。"},{"en":"Once thought to be covered by means people previously believed something was covered by something else.","zh":"once thought to be covered by 指人們以前相信某物曾被另一物覆蓋。"},{"en":"A ruined wall was once thought to be covered by forest until archaeologists cleared the site.","zh":"一堵廢墟牆曾被認為由森林覆蓋，直到考古學家清理現場。"},{"en":"If evidence changes, earlier beliefs about what covered a region may be corrected.","zh":"如果證據改變，關於某地曾被甚麼覆蓋的早期看法可能被修正。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a former belief.","zh":"這個片語描述過去的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"complete the sentences below","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the sentences with words from the box.","zh":"學生使用方格內的詞語完成以下句子。"},{"en":"Complete the sentences below means fill in the missing words in the sentences that follow.","zh":"complete the sentences below 指填入後面句子中的缺失字詞。"},{"en":"In grammar practice, students complete sentences by choosing the correct verb form.","zh":"在文法練習中，學生透過選擇正確動詞形式完成句子。"},{"en":"If the word must come from a box, students should not invent their own answer.","zh":"如果字詞必須來自方格，學生不應自己創造答案。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"words from the box","meaning":"方格內的詞語","examples":[{"en":"The answers must be selected from the words in the box.","zh":"答案必須從方格內的詞語中選出。"},{"en":"Words from the box are the answer choices provided in a word bank.","zh":"words from the box 指詞庫中提供的答案選項。"},{"en":"Students should check spelling carefully when copying words from the box.","zh":"學生抄寫方格內的詞語時應仔細檢查拼寫。"},{"en":"If a word is not in the box, it may not be accepted even if the meaning is close.","zh":"如果某詞不在方格內，即使意思相近，也可能不被接受。"},{"en":"The phrase tells students where answers must come from.","zh":"這個片語告訴學生答案必須來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"impact on objects falling","meaning":"對下墜物體的影響","examples":[{"en":"Air resistance has an impact on objects falling to the ground.","zh":"空氣阻力對落向地面的物體有影響。"},{"en":"Impact on objects falling means an effect on how things move downward.","zh":"impact on objects falling 指對物體向下移動方式的影響。"},{"en":"A parachute has a strong impact on a person falling because it slows the descent.","zh":"降落傘對下墜的人有強烈影響，因為它減慢下降。"},{"en":"If air resistance affects a feather more than a stone, the two objects fall differently.","zh":"如果空氣阻力對羽毛影響比石頭更大，兩件物體下墜方式就不同。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a force with falling motion.","zh":"這個片語把力量與下墜運動連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"not considered by","meaning":"未被……考慮","examples":[{"en":"Air resistance was not considered by Aristotle.","zh":"空氣阻力未被亞里士多德考慮。"},{"en":"Not considered by means not included in someone’s thinking or explanation.","zh":"not considered by 指沒有被某人納入思考或解釋之中。"},{"en":"Student travel time may not be considered by a school when setting early activities.","zh":"學校安排早上活動時，學生交通時間可能未被考慮。"},{"en":"If a factor is not considered, an explanation may be incomplete.","zh":"如果某因素未被考慮，解釋可能不完整。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies something left out.","zh":"這個片語指出被遺漏的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"investigations of gravity fields","meaning":"對重力場的調查","examples":[{"en":"Investigations of gravity fields revealed the Hudson Bay anomaly.","zh":"對重力場的調查揭示了哈德遜灣異常。"},{"en":"Investigations of gravity fields are studies of how gravity varies across places.","zh":"investigations of gravity fields 指研究重力如何因地而異。"},{"en":"Scientists may use satellites in investigations of gravity fields over oceans and continents.","zh":"科學家可能使用衛星調查海洋和大陸上的重力場。"},{"en":"If gravity-field investigations show unexpected values, they can reveal hidden features.","zh":"如果重力場調查顯示意外數值，就能揭示隱藏特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to research into gravity patterns.","zh":"這個片語指對重力模式的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"lead to the discovery of","meaning":"導致發現……","examples":[{"en":"Satellite research led to the discovery of unusual gravity levels.","zh":"衛星研究導致發現異常重力水平。"},{"en":"Lead to the discovery of means cause people to find something previously unknown.","zh":"lead to the discovery of 指使人們發現以前未知的事物。"},{"en":"A student survey may lead to the discovery of hidden bullying problems.","zh":"學生調查可能導致發現隱藏欺凌問題。"},{"en":"If new tools measure more accurately, they may reveal patterns people missed before.","zh":"如果新工具測量更準確，就可能揭示人們以前錯過的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase connects investigation with a new finding.","zh":"這個片語把調查與新發現連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"unusual gravity levels","meaning":"異常重力水平","examples":[{"en":"Scientists discovered unusual gravity levels around Hudson Bay.","zh":"科學家在哈德遜灣周圍發現異常重力水平。"},{"en":"Unusual gravity levels are gravity measurements that differ from what is normally expected.","zh":"unusual gravity levels 指與正常預期不同的重力測量值。"},{"en":"A thermometer showing an unusual temperature level would make a doctor check again.","zh":"如果溫度計顯示異常體溫，醫生會再次檢查。"},{"en":"If gravity levels are unusual, scientists look for geological or historical causes.","zh":"如果重力水平異常，科學家會尋找地質或歷史原因。"},{"en":"The phrase describes abnormal measurements of gravity.","zh":"這個片語描述不正常的重力測量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be observed to sink","meaning":"被觀察到下沉","examples":[{"en":"The Earth’s surface has been observed to sink under great weight.","zh":"地球表面被觀察到在巨大重量下下沉。"},{"en":"Be observed to sink means be seen or measured moving downward.","zh":"be observed to sink 指被看見或測量到向下移動。"},{"en":"A sofa may be observed to sink into a soft carpet over time.","zh":"沙發可能被觀察到隨時間陷入柔軟地毯。"},{"en":"If land sinks under ice weight, the surface may remain lower for thousands of years.","zh":"如果土地在冰重下下沉，地表可能在數千年間仍然較低。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a measured downward movement.","zh":"這個片語描述被測得的向下移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"as a direct result of","meaning":"作為……的直接結果","examples":[{"en":"The surface sank as a direct result of pressure from the ice.","zh":"地表下沉是冰層壓力的直接結果。"},{"en":"As a direct result of means clearly caused by something, without many steps in between.","zh":"as a direct result of 指清楚由某事造成，中間沒有很多間接步驟。"},{"en":"The classroom became quieter as a direct result of closing the windows.","zh":"關窗後課室變安靜，是關窗的直接結果。"},{"en":"If heavy ice presses on land, sinking can be a direct result of that pressure.","zh":"如果厚冰壓在土地上，下沉可以是該壓力的直接結果。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a clear cause-and-effect relationship.","zh":"這個片語強調清楚的因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"largest part of","meaning":"……最大的部分","examples":[{"en":"The largest part of the ice sheet covered much of Canada.","zh":"冰原最大的部分覆蓋加拿大大部分地區。"},{"en":"Largest part of means the biggest section or portion of something.","zh":"largest part of 指某事物中最大的部分或份額。"},{"en":"The largest part of a school budget may be spent on teachers’ salaries.","zh":"學校預算最大的部分可能用於教師薪金。"},{"en":"If the largest part of an ice sheet covers one country, that country experiences the strongest pressure.","zh":"如果冰原最大的部分覆蓋某國，該國就承受最強壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the biggest share.","zh":"這個片語指出最大份額。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be several kilometres thick","meaning":"厚達數公里","examples":[{"en":"The ancient ice sheet was several kilometres thick.","zh":"古代冰原厚達數公里。"},{"en":"Be several kilometres thick means have a depth or thickness of several kilometres.","zh":"be several kilometres thick 指深度或厚度達數公里。"},{"en":"A cake cannot be several kilometres thick, but an ice sheet can be that enormous.","zh":"蛋糕不可能厚達數公里，但冰原可以巨大到這種程度。"},{"en":"If ice is several kilometres thick, its weight can press the land far downward.","zh":"如果冰厚達數公里，其重量可以把土地大幅向下壓。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses extreme thickness.","zh":"這個片語強調極大厚度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 124 - GRAVITY.pdf","sourcePage":22}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 125":[{"front":"memory decoding","meaning":"記憶解碼","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines how memory decoding techniques allow people to remember extraordinary amounts of information.","zh":"文章探討記憶解碼技巧如何令人記住大量非凡資訊。"},{"en":"Memory decoding means turning hard-to-remember information into easier mental patterns, images, or routes.","zh":"記憶解碼指把難記的資料轉化成較容易記住的心理模式、影像或路線。"},{"en":"A student may use memory decoding by turning a history date into a funny picture.","zh":"學生可能透過把歷史日期變成有趣圖像來使用記憶解碼。"},{"en":"If information is decoded into vivid images, it becomes easier to store and recall later.","zh":"如果資料被解碼成鮮明影像，它之後就更容易儲存和回想。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a method of making memory more manageable, not simply trying harder.","zh":"這個片語描述令記憶更易處理的方法，而不是單純更努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an austere building","meaning":"一座簡樸莊嚴的建築物","examples":[{"en":"The Examinations School is an austere building with large Gothic windows.","zh":"考試學校是一座有大型哥德式窗戶的簡樸莊嚴建築物。"},{"en":"An austere building is plain, serious, and formal rather than colourful or comfortable-looking.","zh":"Austere building 指樸素、嚴肅和正式，而不是色彩繽紛或看起來舒適的建築物。"},{"en":"A courthouse may be an austere building because its stone walls and high ceilings feel strict and official.","zh":"法院可能是一座簡樸莊嚴的建築物，因為石牆和高天花令人感到嚴肅正式。"},{"en":"If a building looks austere, visitors may feel quiet and respectful inside it.","zh":"如果建築物看起來簡樸莊嚴，訪客在內可能會安靜而尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a severe and dignified appearance.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴肅而莊重的外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"oak-paneled rooms","meaning":"橡木牆板房間","examples":[{"en":"The building contains several oak-paneled rooms.","zh":"這座建築物內有幾間橡木牆板房間。"},{"en":"Oak-paneled rooms are rooms whose walls are covered with wooden panels made from oak.","zh":"Oak-paneled rooms 是牆壁鋪有橡木木板的房間。"},{"en":"An old university may use oak-paneled rooms for formal meetings and ceremonies.","zh":"古老大學可能使用橡木牆板房間舉行正式會議和典禮。"},{"en":"If a room has oak panels, it may feel traditional, serious, and expensive.","zh":"如果房間有橡木牆板，它可能令人感到傳統、嚴肅和昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a visual image of old-fashioned wooden interiors.","zh":"這個片語呈現舊式木製室內空間的視覺畫面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Gothic windows","meaning":"哥德式窗戶","examples":[{"en":"Large Gothic windows contribute to the building’s historic appearance.","zh":"大型哥德式窗戶有助形成建築物的歷史外觀。"},{"en":"Gothic windows are tall, pointed, decorative windows often found in old churches or historic buildings.","zh":"Gothic windows 是高身、尖拱、具裝飾性的窗戶，常見於古老教堂或歷史建築。"},{"en":"A school chapel may have Gothic windows that make the room feel solemn and ancient.","zh":"學校小教堂可能有哥德式窗戶，令房間感覺莊嚴古老。"},{"en":"If a building has Gothic windows, people may connect it with medieval architecture.","zh":"如果建築物有哥德式窗戶，人們可能把它與中世紀建築聯繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a historical architectural feature.","zh":"這個片語描述一種歷史建築特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"looming portraits","meaning":"高懸而令人敬畏的肖像","examples":[{"en":"Looming portraits of eminent figures hang throughout the building.","zh":"顯赫人物高懸而令人敬畏的肖像掛滿整座建築物。"},{"en":"Looming portraits are large pictures of people that seem to hang over viewers in an imposing way.","zh":"Looming portraits 是大型人物肖像，看起來以有壓迫感的方式懸在觀看者上方。"},{"en":"A headmaster’s large portrait in a school hall may feel like a looming portrait to nervous students.","zh":"校長大型肖像掛在學校禮堂中，對緊張學生來說可能像高懸而令人敬畏的肖像。"},{"en":"If portraits loom over a room, they can make the place feel formal or intimidating.","zh":"如果肖像在房間中高高懸掛，它們可以令地方感覺正式或令人畏懼。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests portraits that feel powerful, old, and slightly overwhelming.","zh":"這個片語暗示肖像有權威感、古老感和些微壓迫感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"eminent dukes and earls","meaning":"顯赫的公爵和伯爵","examples":[{"en":"The walls display portraits of eminent dukes and earls.","zh":"牆上展示顯赫的公爵和伯爵的肖像。"},{"en":"Eminent dukes and earls are high-ranking nobles who are well known or respected.","zh":"Eminent dukes and earls 是著名或受尊重的高級貴族。"},{"en":"A history museum may display paintings of eminent dukes and earls who once owned local land.","zh":"歷史博物館可能展示曾擁有本地土地的顯赫公爵和伯爵畫像。"},{"en":"If a building is filled with such portraits, it may seem connected to privilege and tradition.","zh":"如果建築物滿是這類肖像，它可能顯得與特權和傳統有關。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to important aristocratic figures.","zh":"這個片語指重要的貴族人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"generations of students","meaning":"一代又一代的學生","examples":[{"en":"Generations of Oxford students have taken their final examinations there.","zh":"一代又一代的牛津學生在那裡參加期末考試。"},{"en":"Generations of students means many groups of students over many years.","zh":"Generations of students 指多年來許多批學生。"},{"en":"Generations of students have used the same library tables to revise before exams.","zh":"一代又一代的學生使用同一批圖書館桌子在考試前溫習。"},{"en":"If generations of students pass through one building, the place gains history and emotional meaning.","zh":"如果一代又一代學生經過同一座建築物，該地方就會累積歷史和情感意義。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long continuity across time.","zh":"這個片語強調跨越時間的長久延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"test their memory","meaning":"測試記憶力","examples":[{"en":"Students have traditionally tested their memory in final examinations.","zh":"學生傳統上在期末考試中測試記憶力。"},{"en":"To test their memory means to check how much information they can remember and use.","zh":"To test their memory 指檢查他們能記住並使用多少資料。"},{"en":"A teacher may test students’ memory by asking them to recall key vocabulary without looking at notes.","zh":"老師可能要求學生不看筆記回想重要詞彙，以測試他們的記憶力。"},{"en":"If students only test their memory, they may know facts but not fully understand them.","zh":"如果學生只測試記憶力，他們可能知道事實，但未必完全理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes checking recall ability.","zh":"這個片語描述檢查回想能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"final exams","meaning":"期末考試","examples":[{"en":"Oxford students have taken their final exams in the historic building.","zh":"牛津學生曾在這座歷史建築中參加期末考試。"},{"en":"Final exams are major tests taken at the end of a course, term, or degree.","zh":"Final exams 是課程、學期或學位結束時進行的重要考試。"},{"en":"Students often revise for final exams by reviewing notes, past papers, and teacher feedback.","zh":"學生通常透過重溫筆記、歷屆試題和老師回饋來準備期末考試。"},{"en":"If final exams count heavily, students may feel pressure for several weeks before them.","zh":"如果期末考試佔分很重，學生可能在考前幾星期感到壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to end-stage examinations, not small class quizzes.","zh":"這個片語指最後階段的大型考試，而不是小測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"contestants gathered at","meaning":"參賽者聚集於……","examples":[{"en":"Thirty-four contestants gathered at the World Memory Championships.","zh":"三十四名參賽者聚集於世界記憶錦標賽。"},{"en":"Contestants gathered at a place means competitors came together there for an event.","zh":"Contestants gathered at a place 指參賽者為一項活動來到某處集合。"},{"en":"Students gathered at the school hall before the debate competition began.","zh":"辯論比賽開始前，學生聚集於學校禮堂。"},{"en":"If contestants gather at a championship, they are usually prepared to compete under rules.","zh":"如果參賽者聚集於錦標賽，他們通常已準備好按規則比賽。"},{"en":"This phrase describes competitors assembling for a contest.","zh":"這個片語描述參賽者為比賽集合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the World Memory Championships","meaning":"世界記憶錦標賽","examples":[{"en":"The World Memory Championships tests feats of exceptional memory.","zh":"世界記憶錦標賽測試非凡記憶壯舉。"},{"en":"The World Memory Championships is an international competition where people compete in memory tasks.","zh":"World Memory Championships 是一項國際比賽，人們在記憶任務中競爭。"},{"en":"A contestant in the World Memory Championships may memorise cards, numbers, names, or poems.","zh":"世界記憶錦標賽的參賽者可能記住啤牌、數字、姓名或詩。"},{"en":"If someone wins such a competition, they have shown highly trained recall skills.","zh":"如果有人贏得這類比賽，他展示了高度訓練的回想技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific memory competition.","zh":"這個片語命名一項特定記憶比賽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be examined in a different manner","meaning":"以不同方式接受考驗","examples":[{"en":"The contestants were examined in an entirely different manner from university students.","zh":"參賽者以與大學生完全不同的方式接受考驗。"},{"en":"To be examined in a different manner means to be tested in a different way or format.","zh":"To be examined in a different manner 指以不同方式或形式接受測試。"},{"en":"Speaking students are examined in a different manner from writing students because they must answer aloud.","zh":"口語學生與寫作學生接受考核方式不同，因為他們必須口頭回答。"},{"en":"If the examination method changes, students may need different preparation strategies.","zh":"如果考核方式改變，學生可能需要不同準備策略。"},{"en":"This phrase compares forms of assessment.","zh":"這個片語比較不同評估形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"timed trials","meaning":"計時測試","examples":[{"en":"The contestants completed a series of timed trials.","zh":"參賽者完成一系列計時測試。"},{"en":"Timed trials are tests where people must complete a task within a set time.","zh":"Timed trials 是人們必須在指定時間內完成任務的測試。"},{"en":"A teacher may use timed trials to help students practise quick reading before an exam.","zh":"老師可能使用計時測試，幫助學生在考試前練習快速閱讀。"},{"en":"If a task is timed, speed becomes part of the challenge.","zh":"如果任務是計時的，速度就成為挑戰的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes performance measured against the clock.","zh":"這個片語描述以時間作標準量度表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be challenged to","meaning":"被要求挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Contestants were challenged to memorise poems, numbers and names.","zh":"參賽者被要求挑戰記住詩、數字和姓名。"},{"en":"To be challenged to do something means to be given a difficult task to complete.","zh":"To be challenged to do something 指被要求完成一項困難任務。"},{"en":"Students may be challenged to write an essay in thirty minutes.","zh":"學生可能被要求挑戰在三十分鐘內寫一篇文章。"},{"en":"If people are challenged to do something hard, they must use skill, focus, and effort.","zh":"如果人們被要求挑戰困難任務，他們必須使用技巧、專注力和努力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the task is demanding.","zh":"這個片語顯示任務具挑戰性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"recite a poem","meaning":"背誦一首詩","examples":[{"en":"The contestants had to look at and then recite a two-page poem.","zh":"參賽者必須先看一首兩頁長的詩，然後背誦它。"},{"en":"To recite a poem means to say a poem aloud from memory.","zh":"To recite a poem 指憑記憶大聲說出一首詩。"},{"en":"A student may recite a poem at a school assembly after practising every line.","zh":"學生練習每一行後，可能在學校早會上背誦一首詩。"},{"en":"If a poem is long, reciting it accurately requires both memory and rhythm.","zh":"如果詩很長，準確背誦需要記憶力和節奏感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes spoken performance from memory.","zh":"這個片語描述憑記憶進行的口頭表演。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rows of 40-digit numbers","meaning":"一排排四十位數字","examples":[{"en":"One test required contestants to memorise rows of 40-digit numbers.","zh":"其中一項測試要求參賽者記住一排排四十位數字。"},{"en":"Rows of 40-digit numbers are lines containing long sequences of forty numerals.","zh":"Rows of 40-digit numbers 是包含四十個數字長串的一行行數字。"},{"en":"A password sheet filled with rows of long numbers would be very hard to remember without a system.","zh":"一張填滿長數字串的密碼紙，如果沒有系統會很難記住。"},{"en":"If numbers are arranged in rows, competitors must remember both digits and order.","zh":"如果數字排列成一行行，參賽者必須記住數字和次序。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a demanding numerical memory task.","zh":"這個片語描述要求很高的數字記憶任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"recall the names of","meaning":"憶起……的姓名","examples":[{"en":"Contestants had to recall the names of 110 people.","zh":"參賽者必須憶起一百一十人的姓名。"},{"en":"To recall the names of people means to remember and say or write their names correctly.","zh":"To recall the names of people 指正確記起並說出或寫出他們的姓名。"},{"en":"A new teacher may try to recall the names of all students after the first week.","zh":"新老師可能在第一週後嘗試記起所有學生的姓名。"},{"en":"If you connect a face with a story, it may be easier to recall the person’s name.","zh":"如果你把面孔與故事連接起來，可能更容易記起那人的名字。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on retrieving names from memory.","zh":"這個片語著重從記憶中提取姓名。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"after looking at","meaning":"看過……之後","examples":[{"en":"They recalled the names after looking at photographs of the people.","zh":"他們看過那些人的照片後憶起姓名。"},{"en":"After looking at something means following the act of seeing or examining it.","zh":"After looking at something 指在看見或檢視某物之後。"},{"en":"After looking at the timetable, a student realised the test was on Friday.","zh":"學生看過時間表後，發現測驗在星期五。"},{"en":"If contestants see photos briefly, they must form fast mental links before recalling names.","zh":"如果參賽者短暫看過照片，他們必須在回想姓名前快速建立心理連結。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an earlier visual step with a later action.","zh":"這個片語把較早的視覺步驟與之後的行動連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"perform feats of","meaning":"完成……的非凡壯舉","examples":[{"en":"The mental athletes performed feats of extraordinary retention.","zh":"腦力運動員完成非凡記憶保持能力的壯舉。"},{"en":"To perform feats of something means to do impressive acts that show a special ability.","zh":"To perform feats of something 指完成展示特殊能力的精彩行動。"},{"en":"A gymnast performs feats of balance when she holds difficult positions without falling.","zh":"體操運動員保持困難姿勢而不跌倒時，就是完成平衡能力的壯舉。"},{"en":"If someone performs feats of memory, observers may wonder whether special training is involved.","zh":"如果有人完成記憶壯舉，旁觀者可能想知道是否涉及特殊訓練。"},{"en":"This phrase describes impressive achievement, not ordinary performance.","zh":"這個片語描述令人印象深刻的成就，而不是普通表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"extraordinary retention","meaning":"非凡的記憶保持能力","examples":[{"en":"The competition tests the contestants’ extraordinary retention of information.","zh":"比賽測試參賽者對資料的非凡記憶保持能力。"},{"en":"Extraordinary retention is the unusual ability to keep large amounts of information in memory.","zh":"Extraordinary retention 是把大量資訊保留在記憶中的不尋常能力。"},{"en":"A student with extraordinary retention may remember a whole speech after reading it only a few times.","zh":"有非凡記憶保持能力的學生，可能只讀幾次就記住整篇演講。"},{"en":"If retention is extraordinary, information remains available even after pressure or delay.","zh":"如果記憶保持能力非凡，即使有壓力或延遲，資訊仍能被提取。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unusually strong memory storage.","zh":"這個片語描述異常強大的記憶儲存能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"last for hours","meaning":"持續數小時","examples":[{"en":"Some memory tests lasted for several hours.","zh":"一些記憶測試持續數小時。"},{"en":"To last for hours means to continue for a long period of time.","zh":"To last for hours 指持續一段很長時間。"},{"en":"A school concert may last for hours if every class performs.","zh":"如果每班都表演，學校音樂會可能持續數小時。"},{"en":"If a test lasts for hours, participants need stamina as well as skill.","zh":"如果測試持續數小時，參加者除了技巧外也需要耐力。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long duration.","zh":"這個片語強調時間長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the years since","meaning":"自……以來的年間","examples":[{"en":"Several records have been broken in the years since the competition was founded.","zh":"自比賽創立以來的年間，幾項紀錄已被打破。"},{"en":"In the years since means during the period after a particular event.","zh":"In the years since 指在某事件之後的年月中。"},{"en":"In the years since a new principal arrived, the school library has become busier.","zh":"自新校長到任以來的年間，學校圖書館變得更繁忙。"},{"en":"If records improve in the years since an event began, training methods may have advanced.","zh":"如果紀錄在活動開始後多年不斷提升，訓練方法可能已進步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes change over the years after a starting point.","zh":"這個片語描述某起點之後多年中的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be founded","meaning":"創立","examples":[{"en":"The World Memory Championships was founded more than a decade ago.","zh":"世界記憶錦標賽在十多年前創立。"},{"en":"To be founded means to be officially started or established.","zh":"To be founded 指被正式開始或成立。"},{"en":"A student charity club may be founded by a group of classmates who want to help elderly people.","zh":"學生慈善會可能由一群想幫助長者的同學創立。"},{"en":"If an organisation is founded well, it can continue after its first members leave.","zh":"如果組織創立得好，它可以在首批成員離開後繼續存在。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of an institution, group, or event.","zh":"這個片語描述機構、團體或活動的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"memorise the order of","meaning":"記住……的次序","examples":[{"en":"Competitors try to memorise the order of an entire deck of cards.","zh":"參賽者嘗試記住整副啤牌的次序。"},{"en":"To memorise the order of things means to remember their exact sequence.","zh":"To memorise the order of things 指記住事物的準確排列次序。"},{"en":"A student may memorise the order of steps in a science experiment before entering the lab.","zh":"學生進入實驗室前，可能記住科學實驗步驟的次序。"},{"en":"If the order is wrong, the recalled information may become useless even if the items are correct.","zh":"如果次序錯誤，即使項目本身正確，回想出的資料也可能無用。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on sequence, not just individual items.","zh":"這個片語著重順序，而不只是個別項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a shuffled deck of cards","meaning":"一副經洗牌的啤牌","examples":[{"en":"The contestants memorise a shuffled deck of playing cards.","zh":"參賽者記住一副經洗牌的啤牌。"},{"en":"A shuffled deck of cards is a pack of cards arranged in random order.","zh":"Shuffled deck of cards 是一副以隨機次序排列的啤牌。"},{"en":"Friends may use a shuffled deck of cards before starting a fair game.","zh":"朋友開始公平遊戲前，可能使用一副經洗牌的啤牌。"},{"en":"If the deck is shuffled, competitors cannot rely on a familiar pattern.","zh":"如果牌被洗過，參賽者就不能依賴熟悉模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a randomly mixed pack of playing cards.","zh":"這個片語描述一副被隨機混合的啤牌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in less than 30 seconds","meaning":"在少於三十秒內","examples":[{"en":"No competitor had completed the task in less than 30 seconds.","zh":"沒有參賽者曾在少於三十秒內完成該任務。"},{"en":"In less than 30 seconds means before thirty seconds have passed.","zh":"In less than 30 seconds 指在三十秒過去之前。"},{"en":"A student may answer a simple grammar question in less than 30 seconds if the rule is familiar.","zh":"如果文法規則很熟悉，學生可能在少於三十秒內回答簡單文法題。"},{"en":"If a task is finished in less than 30 seconds, speed is extremely important.","zh":"如果任務在少於三十秒內完成，速度就極其重要。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a very short time limit.","zh":"這個片語強調非常短的時間限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a nice round number","meaning":"一個整數目標","examples":[{"en":"Thirty seconds became a nice round number for memory competitors to target.","zh":"三十秒成為記憶參賽者想達到的一個整數目標。"},{"en":"A nice round number is a simple, memorable number, often ending in zero.","zh":"Nice round number 是簡單、容易記住的數字，通常以零結尾。"},{"en":"A teacher may set a nice round number, such as 100 words, for a short writing task.","zh":"老師可能為短寫作任務設定一個整數目標，例如一百字。"},{"en":"If a goal is a round number, people may remember it more easily and aim for it.","zh":"如果目標是整數，人們可能更容易記住並以它為目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clean and convenient numerical target.","zh":"這個片語描述乾淨方便的數字目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the four-minute mile of","meaning":"……中極具象徵性的突破目標","examples":[{"en":"The 30-second deck became the four-minute mile of competitive memory.","zh":"三十秒記住一副牌成為競技記憶中極具象徵性的突破目標。"},{"en":"The four-minute mile of something is a famous symbolic barrier that many people try to break.","zh":"The four-minute mile of something 指某領域中著名而具象徵性的難破障礙。"},{"en":"A school may treat a perfect exam score as the four-minute mile of its debating programme.","zh":"學校可能把考試滿分視為其辯論計劃中極具象徵性的突破目標。"},{"en":"If a target seems almost impossible, breaking it can inspire everyone in the field.","zh":"如果目標看似幾乎不可能，突破它可以激勵整個領域的人。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a difficult milestone with a legendary sporting achievement.","zh":"這個片語把困難里程碑比作傳奇體育成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"competitive memory","meaning":"競技記憶","examples":[{"en":"The tournament attracts leading competitors in competitive memory.","zh":"該錦標賽吸引競技記憶中的頂尖參賽者。"},{"en":"Competitive memory is the sport-like activity of competing to memorise and recall information quickly and accurately.","zh":"Competitive memory 是像運動一樣比賽快速而準確記住及回想資料的活動。"},{"en":"A student interested in competitive memory may practise cards, numbers, names, and poems.","zh":"對競技記憶有興趣的學生可能練習啤牌、數字、姓名和詩。"},{"en":"If memory becomes competitive, training methods and records become important.","zh":"如果記憶變成競技，訓練方法和紀錄就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase treats memory as a contest rather than only a school skill.","zh":"這個片語把記憶視為比賽，而不只是學校技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a benchmark","meaning":"基準；指標","examples":[{"en":"The 30-second record is an important benchmark for mental athletes.","zh":"三十秒紀錄是腦力運動員的重要基準。"},{"en":"A benchmark is a standard used to measure progress or compare performance.","zh":"Benchmark 是用來量度進步或比較表現的標準。"},{"en":"A school may use past exam results as a benchmark for this year’s improvement.","zh":"學校可能使用過往考試成績作為今年進步的基準。"},{"en":"If students reach a benchmark, teachers can set a higher target next time.","zh":"如果學生達到基準，老師下次可以設定更高目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reference point for judging achievement.","zh":"這個片語描述評估成就的參照點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mental athletes","meaning":"記憶競技選手；腦力運動員","examples":[{"en":"Some memory competitors describe themselves as mental athletes.","zh":"一些記憶比賽參賽者把自己稱為腦力運動員。"},{"en":"Mental athletes are people who train their minds for competitions involving memory, calculation, or other cognitive skills.","zh":"Mental athletes 是為記憶、計算或其他認知技能比賽訓練大腦的人。"},{"en":"A mental athlete may practise every day just as a runner trains for a race.","zh":"腦力運動員可能每天練習，就像跑手為比賽訓練。"},{"en":"If mental athletes train systematically, they can improve speed, accuracy, and endurance.","zh":"如果腦力運動員有系統地訓練，他們可以提升速度、準確度和耐力。"},{"en":"This phrase compares brain training with physical sport.","zh":"這個片語把大腦訓練比作體育運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"close in on","meaning":"逐漸接近","examples":[{"en":"The world’s best competitors are closing in on the 30-second record.","zh":"世界最佳參賽者正逐漸接近三十秒紀錄。"},{"en":"To close in on a target means to get nearer to reaching it.","zh":"To close in on a target 指逐漸接近達成某目標。"},{"en":"A student who keeps improving essay marks may be closing in on a top grade.","zh":"作文分數不斷進步的學生，可能正逐漸接近最高等級。"},{"en":"If competitors close in on a record, the old limit may soon be broken.","zh":"如果參賽者逐漸接近紀錄，舊限制可能很快被打破。"},{"en":"This phrase describes steady progress toward a goal.","zh":"這個片語描述朝目標穩步進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"claim to have","meaning":"聲稱擁有","examples":[{"en":"Most contestants claim to have only average memories.","zh":"大多數參賽者聲稱自己只擁有普通記憶力。"},{"en":"To claim to have something means to say that you possess it, whether others believe it or not.","zh":"To claim to have something 指說自己擁有某物，不論他人是否相信。"},{"en":"A student may claim to have finished homework, but the teacher may ask to see it.","zh":"學生可能聲稱已完成功課，但老師可能要求查看。"},{"en":"If champions claim to have average memories, researchers may test whether training explains their success.","zh":"如果冠軍聲稱自己記憶力普通，研究人員可能測試訓練是否解釋其成功。"},{"en":"This phrase reports what people say about themselves.","zh":"這個片語報告人們對自己的說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"average memories","meaning":"普通的記憶力","examples":[{"en":"Many successful contestants say that they have average memories.","zh":"許多成功參賽者說自己擁有普通的記憶力。"},{"en":"Average memories are normal memory abilities, not unusually weak or unusually strong.","zh":"Average memories 是正常記憶能力，既不特別弱，也不特別強。"},{"en":"A student with an average memory may remember vocabulary better after review and examples.","zh":"記憶力普通的學生，在複習和例句幫助下可能更好地記住詞彙。"},{"en":"If people with average memories use good techniques, they may still perform very well.","zh":"如果記憶力普通的人使用好技巧，他們仍可能表現非常好。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts ordinary memory with natural genius.","zh":"這個片語把普通記憶與天生天才作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"scientific testing","meaning":"科學測試","examples":[{"en":"Scientific testing confirms that the competitors do not have naturally exceptional memories.","zh":"科學測試證實參賽者並非天生擁有非凡記憶力。"},{"en":"Scientific testing means using controlled methods and evidence to check whether something is true.","zh":"Scientific testing 指使用受控方法和證據檢查某事是否真實。"},{"en":"Doctors use scientific testing to find whether a medicine is safe and effective.","zh":"醫生使用科學測試判斷藥物是否安全有效。"},{"en":"If testing contradicts popular belief, people may need to rethink their assumptions.","zh":"如果測試結果與普遍信念相反，人們可能需要重新思考假設。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence-based investigation.","zh":"這個片語描述以證據為基礎的調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not just being modest","meaning":"並非只是謙虛","examples":[{"en":"The tests confirm that the contestants are not just being modest.","zh":"測試證實參賽者並非只是謙虛。"},{"en":"Not just being modest means they are not merely downplaying their ability out of politeness.","zh":"Not just being modest 指他們不只是出於禮貌而低估自己的能力。"},{"en":"If a top student says the exam was hard, she may not just be being modest if many classmates agree.","zh":"如果尖子說考試很難，而許多同學也同意，她可能並非只是謙虛。"},{"en":"When evidence supports a humble claim, the claim may be accurate rather than polite.","zh":"當證據支持謙遜說法時，該說法可能是準確，而不只是客氣。"},{"en":"This phrase separates real fact from social humility.","zh":"這個片語區分真實事實與社交謙遜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be based on tricks","meaning":"建基於技巧","examples":[{"en":"The contestants’ feats are based on special memory tricks.","zh":"參賽者的壯舉建基於特殊記憶技巧。"},{"en":"To be based on tricks means to depend on clever techniques rather than natural talent alone.","zh":"To be based on tricks 指依靠巧妙方法，而不只是天賦。"},{"en":"A student’s fast mental maths may be based on tricks for splitting numbers.","zh":"學生快速心算可能建基於拆分數字的技巧。"},{"en":"If success is based on tricks, ordinary learners can improve by learning the same methods.","zh":"如果成功建基於技巧，普通學習者就可以透過學習相同方法進步。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests practical techniques behind impressive results.","zh":"這個片語暗示令人印象深刻結果背後有實用技巧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"capitalise on","meaning":"充分利用","examples":[{"en":"Memory techniques capitalise on the way the brain encodes information.","zh":"記憶技巧充分利用大腦編碼資料的方式。"},{"en":"To capitalise on something means to use an advantage fully and effectively.","zh":"To capitalise on something 指充分而有效地利用某個優勢。"},{"en":"A student may capitalise on a quiet morning by doing the hardest revision first.","zh":"學生可能充分利用安靜的早上，先做最困難的溫習。"},{"en":"If a method capitalises on the brain’s strengths, learning becomes easier.","zh":"如果方法充分利用大腦強項，學習就會變得更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making good use of an existing advantage.","zh":"這個片語描述好好利用既有優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"encode information","meaning":"編碼資料","examples":[{"en":"The human brain encodes visual and spatial information effectively.","zh":"人類大腦能有效編碼視覺和空間資料。"},{"en":"To encode information means to turn information into a form the brain or a system can store.","zh":"To encode information 指把資料轉化成大腦或系統可以儲存的形式。"},{"en":"A student may encode a spelling rule by linking it with a rhyme.","zh":"學生可能透過把拼字規則連接到押韻句來編碼資料。"},{"en":"If information is encoded clearly, it is easier to retrieve later.","zh":"如果資料被清楚編碼，之後就更容易提取。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first stage of storing information.","zh":"這個片語描述儲存資料的第一階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"anyone can learn them","meaning":"任何人都能學會","examples":[{"en":"The researchers believe that anyone can learn these memory techniques.","zh":"研究人員相信任何人都能學會這些記憶技巧。"},{"en":"Anyone can learn them means the skills are teachable and not limited to special people.","zh":"Anyone can learn them 指這些技能可以被教授，並非只限特殊人物。"},{"en":"Anyone can learn basic essay structure if the teacher explains it step by step.","zh":"如果老師一步一步解釋，任何人都能學會基本作文結構。"},{"en":"If a technique is learnable, practice matters more than natural talent.","zh":"如果技巧可以學會，練習就比天賦更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages ordinary learners by stressing accessibility.","zh":"這個片語透過強調可接觸性來鼓勵普通學習者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"authors of the monograph","meaning":"專題著作的作者","examples":[{"en":"Elizabeth Valentine and John Wilding are authors of the monograph Superior Memory.","zh":"Elizabeth Valentine 和 John Wilding 是《Superior Memory》這本專題著作的作者。"},{"en":"Authors of the monograph are the people who wrote a detailed academic work on one subject.","zh":"Authors of the monograph 是撰寫一部關於單一主題的詳細學術作品的人。"},{"en":"Students may cite the authors of a monograph when writing a research essay.","zh":"學生寫研究文章時，可能引用專題著作的作者。"},{"en":"If authors specialise in one topic, their work may give detailed evidence and analysis.","zh":"如果作者專門研究某一題目，他們的作品可能提供詳細證據和分析。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the writers of a focused scholarly book.","zh":"這個片語指出一部聚焦學術著作的作者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a monograph","meaning":"專題學術著作","examples":[{"en":"Superior Memory is a monograph about exceptional memory ability.","zh":"《Superior Memory》是一部關於非凡記憶能力的專題學術著作。"},{"en":"A monograph is a detailed academic book or study about one specific subject.","zh":"Monograph 是關於某一特定主題的詳細學術書籍或研究。"},{"en":"A university library may keep a monograph on the history of one small village.","zh":"大學圖書館可能收藏一部關於某小村歷史的專題學術著作。"},{"en":"If a topic needs deep research, a monograph can explain it more fully than a short article.","zh":"如果題目需要深入研究，專題學術著作可以比短文章更完整地解釋它。"},{"en":"This word describes a focused scholarly work.","zh":"這個詞描述聚焦的學術作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"team up with","meaning":"與……合作","examples":[{"en":"The psychologists teamed up with a neuroscientist to study memory competitors.","zh":"心理學家與一名神經科學家合作研究記憶參賽者。"},{"en":"To team up with someone means to work together with them on a shared task.","zh":"To team up with someone 指與某人合作完成共同任務。"},{"en":"A student may team up with a classmate to prepare a science presentation.","zh":"學生可能與同學合作準備科學匯報。"},{"en":"If experts from different fields team up, they can study a problem from more than one angle.","zh":"如果不同領域專家合作，他們可以從多於一個角度研究問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cooperation.","zh":"這個片語描述合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a neuroscientist","meaning":"神經科學家","examples":[{"en":"Eleanor Maguire is a neuroscientist at University College London.","zh":"Eleanor Maguire 是倫敦大學學院的神經科學家。"},{"en":"A neuroscientist is a scientist who studies the brain and nervous system.","zh":"Neuroscientist 是研究大腦和神經系統的科學家。"},{"en":"A neuroscientist may examine how sleep, memory, or emotion affects learning.","zh":"神經科學家可能研究睡眠、記憶或情緒如何影響學習。"},{"en":"If a neuroscientist studies memory champions, brain scans may reveal how they use their minds.","zh":"如果神經科學家研究記憶冠軍，腦掃描可能揭示他們如何使用大腦。"},{"en":"This word describes a researcher of the brain.","zh":"這個詞描述研究大腦的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"finish near the top of","meaning":"取得接近最高名次","examples":[{"en":"Karsten had finished near the top of the World Memory Championships.","zh":"Karsten 在世界記憶錦標賽中取得接近最高名次。"},{"en":"To finish near the top of a competition means to achieve one of the highest positions.","zh":"To finish near the top of a competition 指取得最高位置之一。"},{"en":"A student who finishes near the top of the class has performed better than most classmates.","zh":"在班中取得接近最高名次的學生，表現比大多數同學好。"},{"en":"If someone finishes near the top repeatedly, their skill is probably strong and consistent.","zh":"如果某人反覆取得接近最高名次，他的能力很可能強而穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a high ranking without necessarily winning first place.","zh":"這個片語描述高排名，但不一定是第一名。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be different in some way","meaning":"在某方面有所不同","examples":[{"en":"The researchers wondered whether the contestants’ brains were different in some way.","zh":"研究人員想知道參賽者的大腦是否在某方面有所不同。"},{"en":"To be different in some way means to have a difference, even if the exact difference is unclear.","zh":"To be different in some way 指存在某種差異，即使確切差異尚不清楚。"},{"en":"A teacher may wonder whether successful readers study differently in some way.","zh":"老師可能想知道成功讀者是否在某方面以不同方式學習。"},{"en":"If two groups perform differently, researchers may check whether their habits or brains differ.","zh":"如果兩組人表現不同，研究人員可能檢查他們的習慣或大腦是否不同。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses an open question about possible difference.","zh":"這個片語表達對可能差異的開放問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a group of control subjects","meaning":"一組對照研究對象","examples":[{"en":"The competitors were compared with a group of control subjects.","zh":"參賽者與一組對照研究對象作比較。"},{"en":"A group of control subjects is a comparison group used in research to judge whether the tested group is different.","zh":"Group of control subjects 是研究中的比較組，用來判斷受測組是否不同。"},{"en":"In a study of a new teaching method, one class may be the control group using normal lessons.","zh":"在研究新教學方法時，一班使用正常課堂的學生可能是對照組。"},{"en":"If researchers compare champions with control subjects, they can see what is special about champions.","zh":"如果研究人員把冠軍與對照對象比較，他們可以看出冠軍有甚麼特別。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the comparison group in an experiment.","zh":"這個片語描述實驗中的比較組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an MRI machine","meaning":"磁力共振掃描儀","examples":[{"en":"The researchers put the participants into an MRI machine.","zh":"研究人員把參加者放進磁力共振掃描儀。"},{"en":"An MRI machine is a medical scanner that creates detailed images of the inside of the body or brain.","zh":"MRI machine 是一種醫療掃描儀，可以產生身體或大腦內部的詳細影像。"},{"en":"A doctor may use an MRI machine to check a patient’s injured knee or brain.","zh":"醫生可能使用磁力共振掃描儀檢查病人的膝傷或大腦。"},{"en":"If participants are scanned in an MRI machine, researchers can observe which brain areas become active.","zh":"如果參加者在磁力共振掃描儀中接受掃描，研究人員可以觀察哪些腦區變得活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to advanced scanning equipment.","zh":"這個片語指先進掃描設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"perform memory tests","meaning":"進行記憶測試","examples":[{"en":"The participants performed several memory tests inside the scanner.","zh":"參加者在掃描儀內進行幾項記憶測試。"},{"en":"To perform memory tests means to complete tasks designed to measure recall or recognition.","zh":"To perform memory tests 指完成用來量度回想或識別能力的任務。"},{"en":"Students may perform memory tests by recalling vocabulary after a short delay.","zh":"學生可能透過短暫延遲後回想詞彙來進行記憶測試。"},{"en":"If people perform memory tests under scanning, researchers can link behaviour with brain activity.","zh":"如果人們在掃描下進行記憶測試，研究人員可以把行為與大腦活動連接。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doing tasks that measure memory.","zh":"這個片語描述做量度記憶的任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"while their brains were being scanned","meaning":"在大腦接受掃描期間","examples":[{"en":"The subjects completed the tasks while their brains were being scanned.","zh":"研究對象在大腦接受掃描期間完成任務。"},{"en":"While their brains were being scanned means during the time when machines were recording brain activity.","zh":"While their brains were being scanned 指機器正在記錄大腦活動的期間。"},{"en":"A volunteer may answer questions while their brain is being scanned in a research study.","zh":"志願者可能在研究中一邊回答問題，一邊接受大腦掃描。"},{"en":"If tasks are done during scanning, scientists can see which brain areas are used.","zh":"如果任務在掃描期間完成，科學家可以看見哪些腦區被使用。"},{"en":"This phrase connects behaviour with simultaneous brain measurement.","zh":"這個片語把行為與同步大腦量度連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"when it came to","meaning":"說到……；在……方面","examples":[{"en":"When it came to memorising numbers, the competitors performed extremely well.","zh":"說到記住數字，參賽者表現極佳。"},{"en":"When it came to something means regarding that particular task, subject, or situation.","zh":"When it came to something 指關於某個特定任務、主題或情況。"},{"en":"When it came to grammar, the student was confident, but speaking still made him nervous.","zh":"說到文法，該學生很有信心，但口語仍令他緊張。"},{"en":"If someone performs well when it comes to one task, it does not mean they are equally good at everything.","zh":"如果某人在某一任務方面表現好，不代表他在所有事情上同樣出色。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows the discussion to one area.","zh":"這個片語把討論範圍收窄到一個方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sequences of three-digit numbers","meaning":"一連串三位數字","examples":[{"en":"The competitors memorised sequences of three-digit numbers.","zh":"參賽者記住一連串三位數字。"},{"en":"Sequences of three-digit numbers are ordered groups of numbers, each made of three digits.","zh":"Sequences of three-digit numbers 是有次序的數字組，每個數字由三位組成。"},{"en":"A security exercise may ask workers to remember sequences of three-digit codes.","zh":"保安練習可能要求員工記住一連串三位密碼。"},{"en":"If the sequence is long, remembering the order becomes harder than remembering each number alone.","zh":"如果數列很長，記住次序會比單獨記住每個數字更難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordered numerical information.","zh":"這個片語描述有次序的數字資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as expected","meaning":"正如預期","examples":[{"en":"As expected, the memory contestants performed better on familiar tasks.","zh":"正如預期，記憶參賽者在熟悉任務中表現較好。"},{"en":"As expected means the result was what people thought would probably happen.","zh":"As expected 指結果正是人們認為很可能會發生的。"},{"en":"As expected, students who revised earlier felt calmer before the test.","zh":"正如預期，較早溫習的學生在測驗前感覺較平靜。"},{"en":"If a result happens as expected, it confirms earlier predictions.","zh":"如果結果正如預期，它確認了早前預測。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an unsurprising outcome.","zh":"這個片語引出不令人意外的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"an immense difference","meaning":"巨大差異","examples":[{"en":"There was an immense difference between the two groups in the number test.","zh":"兩組人在數字測試中有巨大差異。"},{"en":"An immense difference is a very large and noticeable difference.","zh":"Immense difference 是非常大而明顯的差別。"},{"en":"There may be an immense difference between studying for ten minutes and studying every day for a month.","zh":"溫習十分鐘和每天溫習一個月之間可能有巨大差異。"},{"en":"If practice creates an immense difference, training is likely to be important.","zh":"如果練習造成巨大差異，訓練很可能十分重要。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the gap is huge.","zh":"這個片語強調差距很大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be shown photographs of","meaning":"獲展示……的照片","examples":[{"en":"The participants were shown photographs of magnified snowflakes.","zh":"參加者獲展示放大雪花的照片。"},{"en":"To be shown photographs of something means to be given pictures to look at.","zh":"To be shown photographs of something 指獲提供圖片觀看。"},{"en":"Students may be shown photographs of historical buildings before a field trip.","zh":"學生在實地考察前，可能獲展示歷史建築的照片。"},{"en":"If people are shown unfamiliar images, they cannot rely on previous knowledge.","zh":"如果人們獲展示不熟悉的影像，他們不能依賴先前知識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visual presentation step in a task.","zh":"這個片語描述任務中的視覺展示步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"magnified snowflakes","meaning":"放大的雪花","examples":[{"en":"The researchers used images of magnified snowflakes in an unfamiliar memory task.","zh":"研究人員在一項不熟悉的記憶任務中使用放大雪花影像。"},{"en":"Magnified snowflakes are snowflakes shown larger than normal so their details can be seen.","zh":"Magnified snowflakes 是被放大顯示、讓細節可見的雪花。"},{"en":"A science teacher may show magnified snowflakes to explain natural patterns and symmetry.","zh":"科學老師可能展示放大的雪花，以解釋自然圖案和對稱。"},{"en":"If snowflakes are magnified, tiny differences become easier to observe.","zh":"如果雪花被放大，微小差異就更容易觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase describes enlarged images of small ice crystals.","zh":"這個片語描述小冰晶的放大影像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have never tried to memorise before","meaning":"以前從未嘗試記住","examples":[{"en":"The competitors were tested on images they had never tried to memorise before.","zh":"參賽者接受他們以前從未嘗試記住的影像測試。"},{"en":"To have never tried to memorise something before means to have no previous practice with that material.","zh":"To have never tried to memorise something before 指以前沒有練習記住該材料。"},{"en":"A student may struggle with a poem they have never tried to memorise before.","zh":"學生面對以前從未嘗試記住的詩，可能會吃力。"},{"en":"If people face material they have never practised, their usual advantage may disappear.","zh":"如果人們面對從未練習過的材料，他們平時的優勢可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights unfamiliarity and lack of training.","zh":"這個片語強調不熟悉和缺乏訓練。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"do no better than","meaning":"表現並不比……好","examples":[{"en":"The champions did no better than the control subjects on the unfamiliar task.","zh":"冠軍在不熟悉任務中的表現並不比對照研究對象好。"},{"en":"To do no better than another group means to perform at the same level, not higher.","zh":"To do no better than another group 指表現處於相同水平，而不是更高。"},{"en":"A student who guesses may do no better than classmates who did not study.","zh":"靠猜的學生表現可能並不比沒有溫習的同學好。"},{"en":"If experts do no better on unfamiliar tasks, their skill may be specialised.","zh":"如果專家在不熟悉任務中表現並不更好，他們的技能可能是專門化的。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the absence of an advantage.","zh":"這個片語顯示沒有優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the control group","meaning":"對照組","examples":[{"en":"The memory champions performed similarly to the control group in one test.","zh":"記憶冠軍在其中一項測試中表現與對照組相似。"},{"en":"The control group is the comparison group in an experiment that does not receive the special treatment or have the special skill being studied.","zh":"Control group 是實驗中的比較組，沒有接受特殊處理或沒有被研究的特殊技能。"},{"en":"In a teaching study, the control group may learn through normal lessons while another group uses a new method.","zh":"在教學研究中，對照組可能使用正常課堂學習，而另一組使用新方法。"},{"en":"If the test group performs better than the control group, the difference may reveal an effect.","zh":"如果測試組表現比對照組好，差異可能揭示某種效果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the baseline group for comparison.","zh":"這個片語描述用作比較基準的組別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"analyse brain scans","meaning":"分析腦部掃描影像","examples":[{"en":"The researchers analysed the participants’ brain scans.","zh":"研究人員分析參加者的腦部掃描影像。"},{"en":"To analyse brain scans means to study brain images carefully to find patterns or differences.","zh":"To analyse brain scans 指仔細研究大腦影像，以尋找模式或差異。"},{"en":"Doctors may analyse brain scans to locate an injury after an accident.","zh":"意外後，醫生可能分析腦部掃描影像以找出受傷位置。"},{"en":"If scans show different activity, researchers may connect it with different thinking strategies.","zh":"如果掃描顯示不同活動，研究人員可能把它與不同思考策略連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful examination of brain images.","zh":"這個片語描述對大腦影像的仔細檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"memory champions","meaning":"記憶比賽冠軍","examples":[{"en":"The memory champions used particular brain regions during the tests.","zh":"記憶比賽冠軍在測試期間使用特定大腦區域。"},{"en":"Memory champions are people who win or perform at the highest level in memory competitions.","zh":"Memory champions 是在記憶比賽中勝出或表現達最高水平的人。"},{"en":"A memory champion may train daily with cards, numbers, and imagined routes.","zh":"記憶比賽冠軍可能每天用啤牌、數字和想像路線訓練。"},{"en":"If memory champions use special techniques, their success may be learned rather than purely natural.","zh":"如果記憶冠軍使用特殊技巧，他們的成功可能是學回來的，而不純粹是天生。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to top performers in memory contests.","zh":"這個片語指記憶競賽中的頂尖表現者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"activate brain regions","meaning":"啟動大腦區域","examples":[{"en":"The competitors activated brain regions associated with visual memory.","zh":"參賽者啟動了與視覺記憶有關的大腦區域。"},{"en":"To activate brain regions means to make particular areas of the brain become active during a task.","zh":"To activate brain regions 指在任務期間使特定大腦區域變得活躍。"},{"en":"Listening to music may activate brain regions linked with rhythm and emotion.","zh":"聆聽音樂可能啟動與節奏和情緒有關的大腦區域。"},{"en":"If a task activates visual areas, the person may be using images to think.","zh":"如果任務啟動視覺區域，當事人可能正在用圖像思考。"},{"en":"This phrase connects mental activity with specific parts of the brain.","zh":"這個片語把心理活動與特定大腦部分連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be different from those","meaning":"與那些……不同","examples":[{"en":"The regions they activated were different from those used by the control subjects.","zh":"他們啟動的區域與對照研究對象使用的那些區域不同。"},{"en":"To be different from those means to not be the same as the ones already mentioned.","zh":"To be different from those 指與前面提到的那些事物不相同。"},{"en":"The mistakes made by advanced students may be different from those made by beginners.","zh":"高階學生犯的錯誤可能與初學者犯的那些錯誤不同。"},{"en":"If one group uses different brain areas from another, they may be using different strategies.","zh":"如果一組人使用與另一組不同的大腦區域，他們可能正在使用不同策略。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one set with another set.","zh":"這個片語比較一組事物與另一組事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the right posterior hippocampus","meaning":"右後海馬體","examples":[{"en":"The right posterior hippocampus was active during the competitors’ memory tasks.","zh":"右後海馬體在參賽者的記憶任務期間活躍。"},{"en":"The right posterior hippocampus is a back part of the hippocampus on the right side of the brain, linked with memory and spatial processing.","zh":"Right posterior hippocampus 是大腦右側海馬體後部，與記憶和空間處理有關。"},{"en":"A neuroscientist may study the right posterior hippocampus when researching navigation or memory routes.","zh":"神經科學家研究導航或記憶路線時，可能研究右後海馬體。"},{"en":"If this area becomes active, the person may be using spatial memory to organise information.","zh":"如果這個區域變得活躍，當事人可能正在使用空間記憶組織資料。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific brain region.","zh":"這個片語命名特定大腦區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be known to be involved in","meaning":"已知與……有關","examples":[{"en":"These brain regions are known to be involved in spatial navigation.","zh":"這些大腦區域已知與空間導航有關。"},{"en":"To be known to be involved in something means research has shown that something plays a part in it.","zh":"To be known to be involved in something 指研究已顯示某事物在其中發揮作用。"},{"en":"Sleep is known to be involved in memory because tired students often recall less.","zh":"睡眠已知與記憶有關，因為疲倦學生通常記得較少。"},{"en":"If a brain area is known to be involved in navigation, its activity during memory tasks may be meaningful.","zh":"如果某腦區已知與導航有關，它在記憶任務中活躍可能有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase presents an established connection.","zh":"這個片語呈現已確立的關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"visual memory","meaning":"視覺記憶","examples":[{"en":"The memory contestants relied heavily on visual memory.","zh":"記憶參賽者非常依賴視覺記憶。"},{"en":"Visual memory is the ability to remember images, shapes, colours, places, or scenes.","zh":"Visual memory 是記住影像、形狀、顏色、地方或場景的能力。"},{"en":"A student uses visual memory when remembering where a word appeared on a page.","zh":"學生記得某字在頁面上哪個位置時，就是使用視覺記憶。"},{"en":"If information is turned into pictures, visual memory can help store it more strongly.","zh":"如果資料被轉化成圖像，視覺記憶可以幫助更牢固地儲存它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes memory based on seeing or imagining.","zh":"這個片語描述基於看見或想像的記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"spatial navigation","meaning":"空間導航能力","examples":[{"en":"Spatial navigation helps competitors organise remembered images.","zh":"空間導航能力幫助參賽者組織已記住的影像。"},{"en":"Spatial navigation is the ability to understand where things are and move through places mentally or physically.","zh":"Spatial navigation 是理解物件位置並在心理上或實際上穿越空間的能力。"},{"en":"A child uses spatial navigation when finding the way from the classroom to the playground.","zh":"孩子從課室找到前往操場的路時，就是使用空間導航能力。"},{"en":"If a memory technique uses imagined routes, spatial navigation helps organise the information.","zh":"如果記憶技巧使用想像路線，空間導航能力就幫助組織資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes knowing locations and routes.","zh":"這個片語描述知道位置和路線的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"it might seem odd that","meaning":"……看來可能很奇怪","examples":[{"en":"It might seem odd that people use spatial navigation to remember numbers.","zh":"人們用空間導航來記住數字，看來可能很奇怪。"},{"en":"It might seem odd that means something may look strange or surprising at first.","zh":"It might seem odd that 指某事起初可能看起來奇怪或令人驚訝。"},{"en":"It might seem odd that drawing pictures can help with vocabulary, but images can make words easier to remember.","zh":"畫圖能幫助詞彙學習看來可能很奇怪，但影像可以令詞語更易記住。"},{"en":"If an idea seems odd at first, explanation may show why it works.","zh":"如果想法起初看來奇怪，解釋可能顯示它為何有效。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces something unexpected.","zh":"這個片語引出出乎意料的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"visual imagery","meaning":"視覺意象","examples":[{"en":"Memory competitors transform numbers and cards into visual imagery.","zh":"記憶參賽者把數字和啤牌轉化成視覺意象。"},{"en":"Visual imagery means mental pictures created in the mind.","zh":"Visual imagery 指在腦中創造的心理圖像。"},{"en":"A student may use visual imagery by imagining a giant apple to remember the word “fruit”.","zh":"學生可能想像一個巨大蘋果，以使用視覺意象記住 “fruit” 一詞。"},{"en":"If an image is funny or unusual, visual imagery may make the memory stronger.","zh":"如果影像有趣或奇特，視覺意象可能令記憶更牢固。"},{"en":"This phrase describes thinking in pictures.","zh":"這個片語描述以圖像思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"make sense","meaning":"合乎道理","examples":[{"en":"The unusual brain activity makes sense when the techniques are explained.","zh":"當技巧被解釋後，這種不尋常的大腦活動便合乎道理。"},{"en":"To make sense means to become understandable, logical, or reasonable.","zh":"To make sense 指變得可理解、合邏輯或合理。"},{"en":"A grammar rule may make sense after the teacher shows three clear examples.","zh":"老師展示三個清楚例子後，文法規則可能變得合乎道理。"},{"en":"If a strange result makes sense after explanation, the explanation has connected the missing pieces.","zh":"如果奇怪結果在解釋後合乎道理，該解釋就把缺失部分連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes understanding something that first seemed confusing.","zh":"這個片語描述理解起初令人困惑的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reveal a technique","meaning":"揭示一種技巧","examples":[{"en":"The competitors’ methods become understandable when their techniques are revealed.","zh":"當參賽者的技巧被揭示後，他們的方法就變得可理解。"},{"en":"To reveal a technique means to show or explain a method that was previously hidden.","zh":"To reveal a technique 指展示或解釋之前隱藏的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may reveal a technique for finding answers quickly in a reading passage.","zh":"老師可能揭示一種在閱讀文章中快速找答案的技巧。"},{"en":"If a technique is revealed, a difficult performance may seem less mysterious.","zh":"如果技巧被揭示，困難表現可能顯得不那麼神秘。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a method known.","zh":"這個片語描述令方法被人知道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cognitive-science graduate student","meaning":"認知科學研究生","examples":[{"en":"Cooke was a cognitive-science graduate student.","zh":"Cooke 是一名認知科學研究生。"},{"en":"A cognitive-science graduate student is a postgraduate student studying how the mind thinks, learns, remembers, and understands.","zh":"Cognitive-science graduate student 是研究心智如何思考、學習、記憶和理解的研究生。"},{"en":"A cognitive-science graduate student may research attention, language, memory, or decision-making.","zh":"認知科學研究生可能研究注意力、語言、記憶或決策。"},{"en":"If such a student studies memory, they may combine psychology, neuroscience, and computer science.","zh":"如果這類學生研究記憶，他們可能結合心理學、神經科學和電腦科學。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an advanced student in the science of the mind.","zh":"這個片語描述研究心智科學的高階學生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a shoulder-length mop of curly hair","meaning":"一頭及肩濃密曲髮","examples":[{"en":"Cooke had a shoulder-length mop of curly hair.","zh":"Cooke 有一頭及肩濃密曲髮。"},{"en":"A shoulder-length mop of curly hair means thick, messy curly hair reaching the shoulders.","zh":"Shoulder-length mop of curly hair 指到肩膀長度、濃密而略亂的曲髮。"},{"en":"A musician with a shoulder-length mop of curly hair may be easy to recognise on stage.","zh":"舞台上有一頭及肩濃密曲髮的音樂人可能很容易被認出。"},{"en":"If a description includes hair like this, it helps readers picture the person clearly.","zh":"如果描述包括這種頭髮，它能幫助讀者清楚想像人物。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a vivid physical description.","zh":"這個片語提供鮮明的外貌描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a grand master of","meaning":"……的大師","examples":[{"en":"Cooke is described as a grand master of brain storage.","zh":"Cooke 被形容為大腦資料儲存的大師。"},{"en":"A grand master of something is someone with extremely high skill in that area.","zh":"Grand master of something 是在某範疇有極高技能的人。"},{"en":"A chess player may be called a grand master after reaching an elite level.","zh":"棋手達到精英水平後，可能被稱為大師。"},{"en":"If someone is a grand master of a skill, beginners may study their methods carefully.","zh":"如果某人是某技能的大師，初學者可能仔細研究其方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes expert-level ability.","zh":"這個片語描述專家級能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"brain storage","meaning":"大腦資料儲存","examples":[{"en":"Cooke has developed highly effective brain-storage techniques.","zh":"Cooke 發展出非常有效的大腦資料儲存技巧。"},{"en":"Brain storage means the way the mind stores information for later recall.","zh":"Brain storage 指心智儲存資料以便日後回想的方式。"},{"en":"A student improves brain storage when they connect new vocabulary with pictures and examples.","zh":"學生把新詞彙與圖像和例句連接時，就是改善大腦資料儲存。"},{"en":"If information enters brain storage clearly, it is less likely to disappear before the test.","zh":"如果資料清楚進入大腦儲存，它在測驗前較不容易消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental storage, not a computer hard drive.","zh":"這個片語描述心理儲存，而不是電腦硬碟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in less than an hour","meaning":"在少於一小時內","examples":[{"en":"He can memorise ten decks of cards in less than an hour.","zh":"他可以在少於一小時內記住十副啤牌。"},{"en":"In less than an hour means before sixty minutes have passed.","zh":"In less than an hour 指在六十分鐘過去之前。"},{"en":"A focused student may finish a short revision worksheet in less than an hour.","zh":"專注的學生可能在少於一小時內完成一份短溫習工作紙。"},{"en":"If someone completes a hard task in less than an hour, both speed and skill are impressive.","zh":"如果有人在少於一小時內完成困難任務，速度和技巧都令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a short time for a demanding task.","zh":"這個片語強調用很短時間完成高要求任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"close in on the record","meaning":"逐漸接近紀錄","examples":[{"en":"Cooke is closing in on the 30-second record.","zh":"Cooke 正逐漸接近三十秒紀錄。"},{"en":"To close in on the record means to get closer to matching or breaking the best known result.","zh":"To close in on the record 指越來越接近追平或打破最佳已知成績。"},{"en":"A runner may close in on the school record after months of training.","zh":"跑手經過數月訓練後，可能逐漸接近校內紀錄。"},{"en":"If someone keeps improving, the record may soon be within reach.","zh":"如果某人不斷進步，紀錄可能很快變得觸手可及。"},{"en":"This phrase describes approaching a performance milestone.","zh":"這個片語描述接近表現里程碑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pull out a deck of cards","meaning":"拿出一副啤牌","examples":[{"en":"Cooke pulled out a deck of cards to demonstrate his technique.","zh":"Cooke 拿出一副啤牌來示範他的技巧。"},{"en":"To pull out a deck of cards means to take a pack of cards from a pocket, bag, or table to use it.","zh":"To pull out a deck of cards 指從口袋、袋或桌上取出一副啤牌來使用。"},{"en":"A magician may pull out a deck of cards before performing a trick.","zh":"魔術師可能在表演戲法前拿出一副啤牌。"},{"en":"If someone pulls out cards during an explanation, they are likely preparing a demonstration.","zh":"如果某人在解釋期間拿出啤牌，他很可能正準備示範。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking out a pack of playing cards.","zh":"這個片語描述取出一副啤牌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"shuffle the cards","meaning":"洗牌","examples":[{"en":"Cooke shuffled the cards before memorising them.","zh":"Cooke 在記住啤牌前先洗牌。"},{"en":"To shuffle the cards means to mix the cards into a random order.","zh":"To shuffle the cards 指把啤牌混合成隨機次序。"},{"en":"Before a card game, players shuffle the cards so no one knows the sequence.","zh":"啤牌遊戲開始前，玩家會洗牌，讓沒有人知道牌序。"},{"en":"If the cards are shuffled well, memorising their order becomes more difficult.","zh":"如果牌洗得充分，記住其次序就更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mixing a deck before use.","zh":"這個片語描述使用前混合整副牌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hold up","meaning":"舉起；展示","examples":[{"en":"He held up three cards for the demonstration.","zh":"他舉起三張牌作示範。"},{"en":"To hold up something means to raise it so other people can see it.","zh":"To hold up something 指把某物舉起，讓其他人看見。"},{"en":"A teacher may hold up a flashcard so the whole class can read the word.","zh":"老師可能舉起字卡，讓全班看見該詞。"},{"en":"If someone holds up an object while explaining, it becomes easier for listeners to follow.","zh":"如果某人一邊解釋一邊展示物件，聽者就更容易跟上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes showing something physically.","zh":"這個片語描述實際展示某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the seven of spades","meaning":"黑桃七","examples":[{"en":"The first card he held up was the seven of spades.","zh":"他舉起的第一張牌是黑桃七。"},{"en":"The seven of spades is the playing card showing the number seven in the spades suit.","zh":"Seven of spades 是黑桃花色中顯示數字七的啤牌。"},{"en":"A memory competitor may link the seven of spades with a person or image.","zh":"記憶參賽者可能把黑桃七與某個人物或影像聯繫起來。"},{"en":"If each card has a fixed meaning, the seven of spades can quickly trigger a mental picture.","zh":"如果每張牌都有固定意思，黑桃七可以快速觸發心理圖像。"},{"en":"This phrase names one specific playing card.","zh":"這個片語命名一張特定啤牌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the queen of clubs","meaning":"梅花女王","examples":[{"en":"The queen of clubs represented a particular action in Cooke’s system.","zh":"梅花女王在 Cooke 的系統中代表一個特定動作。"},{"en":"The queen of clubs is the playing card showing a queen in the clubs suit.","zh":"Queen of clubs 是梅花花色中顯示女王的啤牌。"},{"en":"In a memory system, the queen of clubs may stand for a person, action, or object.","zh":"在記憶系統中，梅花女王可能代表人物、動作或物件。"},{"en":"If the card has a fixed association, seeing it can help the competitor build a scene.","zh":"如果該牌有固定聯想，看見它可以幫助參賽者建立場景。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific playing card.","zh":"這個片語命名一張特定啤牌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the ten of spades","meaning":"黑桃十","examples":[{"en":"The ten of spades formed the third part of an imagined scene.","zh":"黑桃十構成想像場景中的第三部分。"},{"en":"The ten of spades is the playing card showing the number ten in the spades suit.","zh":"Ten of spades 是黑桃花色中顯示數字十的啤牌。"},{"en":"A competitor may use the ten of spades as an object in a memory image.","zh":"參賽者可能把黑桃十用作記憶影像中的物件。"},{"en":"If the ten of spades always represents the same thing, recall becomes faster.","zh":"如果黑桃十永遠代表同一事物，回想就會更快。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies one exact card in a deck.","zh":"這個片語指出牌組中的一張確切啤牌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"whack someone with","meaning":"用……猛打某人","examples":[{"en":"Cooke imagined Destiny’s Child whacking Franz Schubert with handbags.","zh":"Cooke 想像 Destiny’s Child 用手袋猛打 Franz Schubert。"},{"en":"To whack someone with something means to hit them hard using that object.","zh":"To whack someone with something 指用某物用力打某人。"},{"en":"In a cartoon, a character may whack a thief with an umbrella.","zh":"在卡通中，角色可能用雨傘猛打小偷。"},{"en":"If a mental image is silly or violent in an exaggerated way, it may be easier to remember.","zh":"如果心理影像以誇張方式顯得荒謬或暴力，它可能更容易被記住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a forceful hitting action.","zh":"這個片語描述用力擊打的動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the king of hearts","meaning":"紅心王","examples":[{"en":"The next group began with the king of hearts.","zh":"下一組以紅心王開始。"},{"en":"The king of hearts is the playing card showing a king in the hearts suit.","zh":"King of hearts 是紅心花色中顯示國王的啤牌。"},{"en":"A card player may remember the king of hearts because it looks bright and familiar.","zh":"啤牌玩家可能因紅心王看起來鮮明又熟悉而記住它。"},{"en":"If the first card represents a person, the king of hearts may begin a new imagined scene.","zh":"如果第一張牌代表人物，紅心王可能開始一個新的想像場景。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific card.","zh":"這個片語命名一張特定啤牌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the king of spades","meaning":"黑桃王","examples":[{"en":"The king of spades was the second card in the next group.","zh":"黑桃王是下一組中的第二張牌。"},{"en":"The king of spades is the playing card showing a king in the spades suit.","zh":"King of spades 是黑桃花色中顯示國王的啤牌。"},{"en":"In a memory system, the king of spades may represent an action or object.","zh":"在記憶系統中，黑桃王可能代表一個動作或物件。"},{"en":"If a player confuses the king of spades with the king of hearts, the recalled order may be wrong.","zh":"如果玩家把黑桃王與紅心王混淆，回想出的次序可能錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies one exact playing card.","zh":"這個片語指出一張確切啤牌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the jack of clubs","meaning":"梅花積","examples":[{"en":"The third card in the group was the jack of clubs.","zh":"該組中的第三張牌是梅花積。"},{"en":"The jack of clubs is the playing card showing a jack in the clubs suit.","zh":"Jack of clubs 是梅花花色中顯示積的啤牌。"},{"en":"A competitor may attach the jack of clubs to a fixed object in their memory system.","zh":"參賽者可能把梅花積連接到記憶系統中的固定物件。"},{"en":"If every card has a clear role, even the jack of clubs can be recalled quickly.","zh":"如果每張牌都有清晰角色，即使梅花積也能被快速回想。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific card in a standard deck.","zh":"這個片語命名標準牌組中的一張特定啤牌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"associate A with B","meaning":"把A與B聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"Cooke associates each card with a person, action and object.","zh":"Cooke 把每張牌與一個人物、動作和物件聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To associate A with B means to connect one thing with another in the mind.","zh":"To associate A with B 指在腦中把一件事與另一件事連接。"},{"en":"A student may associate the word “hospital” with doctors, nurses, and medicine.","zh":"學生可能把 “hospital” 一詞與醫生、護士和藥物聯繫起來。"},{"en":"If a card is associated with a vivid image, it becomes easier to remember.","zh":"如果一張牌與鮮明影像聯繫起來，它就更容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes forming a mental link.","zh":"這個片語描述建立心理連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"each card in the deck","meaning":"牌組中的每一張牌","examples":[{"en":"He has created fixed associations for each card in the deck.","zh":"他為牌組中的每一張牌建立固定聯想。"},{"en":"Each card in the deck means every individual card in a pack of playing cards.","zh":"Each card in the deck 指一副啤牌中的每一張個別牌。"},{"en":"A magician may know the position of each card in the deck after arranging it secretly.","zh":"魔術師暗中排列啤牌後，可能知道牌組中每一張牌的位置。"},{"en":"If each card has a fixed meaning, a full deck can be turned into a sequence of images.","zh":"如果每張牌都有固定意思，整副牌就可以轉化成一連串影像。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that no card is left out.","zh":"這個片語強調沒有任何牌被遺漏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in this case","meaning":"在這個情況下","examples":[{"en":"In this case, the seven of spades represents several people.","zh":"在這個情況下，黑桃七代表幾個人。"},{"en":"In this case means in this particular example or situation.","zh":"In this case 指在這個特定例子或情況中。"},{"en":"In this case, the student should choose “Not Given” because the passage gives no evidence.","zh":"在這個情況下，學生應選 “Not Given”，因為文章沒有提供證據。"},{"en":"If a phrase has several meanings, the context tells us which meaning fits in this case.","zh":"如果片語有幾個意思，語境會告訴我們在這個情況下哪個意思合適。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows the explanation to one specific situation.","zh":"這個片語把解釋收窄到一個特定情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a singing group","meaning":"歌唱組合","examples":[{"en":"The card is associated with the singing group Destiny’s Child.","zh":"這張牌與歌唱組合 Destiny’s Child 聯繫起來。"},{"en":"A singing group is a group of people who perform songs together.","zh":"Singing group 是一群一起表演歌曲的人。"},{"en":"Students may form a singing group for the school talent show.","zh":"學生可能為學校才藝表演組成歌唱組合。"},{"en":"If a singing group is famous, its image may be easy to remember.","zh":"如果歌唱組合很有名，其形象可能容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes performers who sing as a group.","zh":"這個片語描述以組合形式唱歌的表演者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"survive a storm","meaning":"在暴風雨中生還","examples":[{"en":"One of Cooke’s memorised actions is surviving a storm.","zh":"Cooke 記住的其中一個動作是在暴風雨中生還。"},{"en":"To survive a storm means to remain alive or safe through dangerous weather.","zh":"To survive a storm 指在危險天氣中仍然活着或安全。"},{"en":"A family may survive a storm by staying indoors and keeping emergency supplies ready.","zh":"家庭可能透過留在室內並準備緊急物資，在暴風雨中生還。"},{"en":"If a boat survives a storm, it has endured strong wind and rough water.","zh":"如果船在暴風雨中生還，它經受了強風和惡劣海況。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe physical survival or getting through a difficult situation.","zh":"這個片語可以描述實際生存，也可以描述捱過困難情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a dinghy","meaning":"小艇","examples":[{"en":"The object connected with the card is a dinghy.","zh":"與這張牌連接的物件是一艘小艇。"},{"en":"A dinghy is a small boat, often used for short trips or emergencies.","zh":"Dinghy 是小船，通常用於短途航行或緊急情況。"},{"en":"A sailing club may use a dinghy to teach beginners basic boat control.","zh":"帆船會可能使用小艇教初學者基本控船。"},{"en":"If a large boat sinks, a dinghy may help people reach safety.","zh":"如果大船下沉，小艇可能幫助人到達安全地方。"},{"en":"This word describes a small, simple boat.","zh":"這個詞描述小型而簡單的船。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"thwack with a handbag","meaning":"用手袋猛打","examples":[{"en":"Cooke associates one card with the action of thwacking someone with a handbag.","zh":"Cooke 把其中一張牌與用手袋猛打某人的動作聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To thwack with a handbag means to hit someone sharply with a handbag.","zh":"To thwack with a handbag 指用手袋猛力打某人。"},{"en":"In a comedy scene, an angry grandmother may thwack a thief with a handbag.","zh":"在喜劇場景中，憤怒的祖母可能用手袋猛打小偷。"},{"en":"If an action is exaggerated and funny, it may form a memorable mental image.","zh":"如果動作誇張又有趣，它可能形成令人難忘的心理影像。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a striking action that is vivid and slightly comic.","zh":"這個片語描述鮮明且帶點喜劇感的擊打動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"designer clothes","meaning":"名牌服裝","examples":[{"en":"He imagines wardrobes filled with designer clothes.","zh":"他想像衣櫃裏裝滿名牌服裝。"},{"en":"Designer clothes are expensive or fashionable clothes made by well-known designers or brands.","zh":"Designer clothes 是由著名設計師或品牌製作的昂貴或時尚衣服。"},{"en":"A shop selling designer clothes may display bags, dresses, and suits behind glass.","zh":"售賣名牌服裝的商店可能把手袋、裙和西裝放在玻璃後展示。"},{"en":"If a memory image includes designer clothes, the luxury detail may make it more vivid.","zh":"如果記憶影像包括名牌服裝，奢華細節可能令它更鮮明。"},{"en":"This phrase describes branded, stylish, and usually costly clothing.","zh":"這個片語描述有品牌、時尚且通常昂貴的衣服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"commit something to memory","meaning":"把……牢記","examples":[{"en":"Cooke commits an entire deck of cards to memory.","zh":"Cooke 把整副啤牌牢記。"},{"en":"To commit something to memory means to learn it carefully so you can recall it later without looking.","zh":"To commit something to memory 指仔細學習某事，以便之後不看也能回想。"},{"en":"A student may commit a speech to memory before speaking on stage.","zh":"學生可能在上台演講前把演講稿牢記。"},{"en":"If you repeat and organise information, you can commit it to memory more securely.","zh":"如果你重複並組織資料，就可以更穩固地把它牢記。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deliberate memorisation.","zh":"這個片語描述有意識的記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"three cards at a time","meaning":"每次三張牌","examples":[{"en":"He memorises the deck three cards at a time.","zh":"他每次三張牌地記住整副牌。"},{"en":"Three cards at a time means handling or learning cards in groups of three.","zh":"Three cards at a time 指以三張為一組處理或學習啤牌。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to learn vocabulary three words at a time to avoid overload.","zh":"老師可能要求學生每次學三個詞，以避免負荷過重。"},{"en":"If information is grouped, it may become easier to manage.","zh":"如果資料被分組，它可能變得更容易處理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes breaking a large task into small fixed groups.","zh":"這個片語描述把大型任務拆成固定小組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a three-card group","meaning":"三張牌的一組","examples":[{"en":"Each three-card group becomes a single imagined scene.","zh":"每組三張牌變成一個單一想像場景。"},{"en":"A three-card group is a set of three cards treated as one unit.","zh":"Three-card group 是被視為一個單位的三張牌。"},{"en":"A memory competitor may turn a three-card group into one person-action-object image.","zh":"記憶參賽者可能把三張牌的一組轉化成一個人物、動作、物件影像。"},{"en":"If three cards become one scene, the number of things to remember is reduced.","zh":"如果三張牌變成一個場景，需要記住的項目數量就減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small unit used for organising memory.","zh":"這個片語描述用來組織記憶的小單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"form a single image","meaning":"形成一幅單一影像","examples":[{"en":"Every group of cards forms a single image in his mind.","zh":"每組啤牌在他腦中形成一幅單一影像。"},{"en":"To form a single image means to combine several details into one mental picture.","zh":"To form a single image 指把幾個細節結合成一幅心理圖像。"},{"en":"A student may form a single image of a burning candle to remember heat, light, and wax together.","zh":"學生可能形成一幅燃燒蠟燭的單一影像，以同時記住熱、光和蠟。"},{"en":"If details become one image, memory may become faster and more compact.","zh":"如果細節變成一幅影像，記憶可能變得更快和更精簡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes combining information visually.","zh":"這個片語描述以視覺方式結合資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a person doing something to an object","meaning":"一個人對某件物件做某事","examples":[{"en":"The image contains a person doing something to an object.","zh":"該影像包含一個人對某件物件做某事。"},{"en":"A person doing something to an object is a simple scene with a character, an action, and a thing affected by the action.","zh":"A person doing something to an object 是有角色、動作和受動作影響的物件的簡單場景。"},{"en":"A student may imagine a teacher throwing a book into a river to remember three words.","zh":"學生可能想像老師把書丟進河裏，以記住三個詞。"},{"en":"If a scene has a person, action, and object, it is often easier to remember than isolated details.","zh":"如果場景有人物、動作和物件，它通常比孤立細節更容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the structure of a vivid memory image.","zh":"這個片語描述鮮明記憶影像的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the first card in the triplet","meaning":"三張一組中的第一張牌","examples":[{"en":"The first card in the triplet represents a person.","zh":"三張一組中的第一張牌代表人物。"},{"en":"The first card in the triplet means the first card in a group of three cards.","zh":"First card in the triplet 指一組三張牌中的第一張牌。"},{"en":"In a classroom game, the first card in a triplet may tell students who the character is.","zh":"在課堂遊戲中，三張一組中的第一張牌可能告訴學生角色是誰。"},{"en":"If the first card gives the person, the next cards can add action and object.","zh":"如果第一張牌提供人物，接下來的牌就可以加入動作和物件。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the first part of a three-card memory unit.","zh":"這個片語指出三張牌記憶單位中的第一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"become the person","meaning":"代表人物","examples":[{"en":"The first card becomes the person in the imagined scene.","zh":"第一張牌代表想像場景中的人物。"},{"en":"To become the person means to represent the character in a mental image.","zh":"To become the person 指代表心理影像中的角色。"},{"en":"In a memory game, the word “doctor” may become the person in a hospital scene.","zh":"在記憶遊戲中，“doctor” 一詞可能代表醫院場景中的人物。"},{"en":"If one item becomes a person, the memory image can feel more alive and memorable.","zh":"如果某項資料代表人物，記憶影像可以變得更生動和易記。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how information is converted into a character.","zh":"這個片語解釋資料如何被轉化成角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"become the verb","meaning":"代表動作","examples":[{"en":"The second card becomes the verb or action.","zh":"第二張牌代表動詞或動作。"},{"en":"To become the verb means to represent what the person is doing in the imagined scene.","zh":"To become the verb 指代表想像場景中人物正在做甚麼。"},{"en":"In a memory picture, “jump” may become the verb linking a boy and a chair.","zh":"在記憶圖像中，“jump” 可能代表連接男孩和椅子的動作。"},{"en":"If one card gives the action, the scene becomes easier to replay later.","zh":"如果一張牌提供動作，場景之後就更容易重播。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how information is turned into movement or action.","zh":"這個片語解釋資料如何被轉化成動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"become the object","meaning":"代表物件","examples":[{"en":"The third card becomes the object in the scene.","zh":"第三張牌代表場景中的物件。"},{"en":"To become the object means to represent the thing that receives or completes the action.","zh":"To become the object 指代表承受或完成動作的事物。"},{"en":"In a memory image, a pencil may become the object that a teacher is throwing.","zh":"在記憶影像中，鉛筆可能代表老師正在丟出的物件。"},{"en":"If the third item becomes an object, the scene has a clear ending point.","zh":"如果第三項資料代表物件，場景就有清楚終點。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the object part of a person-action-object memory system.","zh":"這個片語解釋人物—動作—物件記憶系統中的物件部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"place images along a route","meaning":"沿着路線放置影像","examples":[{"en":"Cooke places the imagined images along a familiar route.","zh":"Cooke 沿着一條熟悉路線放置想像影像。"},{"en":"To place images along a route means to mentally put pictures at different points on a path.","zh":"To place images along a route 指在腦中把圖像放在路徑上的不同位置。"},{"en":"A student may place vocabulary images along the route from home to school.","zh":"學生可能把詞彙影像沿着從家到學校的路線放置。"},{"en":"If each image has a location, recalling the route can bring back the information in order.","zh":"如果每個影像都有位置，回想路線就能按次序帶回資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using space to organise memory.","zh":"這個片語描述使用空間來組織記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a specific familiar route","meaning":"一條特定而熟悉的路線","examples":[{"en":"He uses a specific familiar route to organise the images.","zh":"他使用一條特定而熟悉的路線來組織影像。"},{"en":"A specific familiar route is a particular path the person knows well.","zh":"Specific familiar route 是某人很熟悉的一條特定路徑。"},{"en":"A student may use the route from the front door to the classroom as a familiar route for revision points.","zh":"學生可能使用從家門到課室的路線，作為溫習重點的熟悉路線。"},{"en":"If the route is familiar, the learner does not waste effort remembering the path itself.","zh":"如果路線熟悉，學習者就不用花力氣記住路徑本身。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a known route used as a memory structure.","zh":"這個片語描述用作記憶結構的已知路線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"an imaginary route","meaning":"想像中的路線","examples":[{"en":"Cooke uses an imaginary route during competitions.","zh":"Cooke 在比賽中使用想像中的路線。"},{"en":"An imaginary route is a path created in the mind rather than walked physically.","zh":"Imaginary route 是在腦中創造，而不是實際行走的路線。"},{"en":"A student may imagine walking through a dream school to remember five essay points.","zh":"學生可能想像走過一間夢中學校，以記住五個作文重點。"},{"en":"If the route exists only in the mind, it can still organise information clearly.","zh":"即使路線只存在於腦中，它仍可以清楚組織資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mental path used for memory.","zh":"這個片語描述用於記憶的心理路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"design something to be","meaning":"把……設計成","examples":[{"en":"He designed the route to be as smooth as possible.","zh":"他把路線設計成盡可能順暢。"},{"en":"To design something to be a certain way means to plan it so it has that quality.","zh":"To design something to be a certain way 指規劃某物，使它具備某種特質。"},{"en":"A teacher may design a worksheet to be simple, clear, and easy to check.","zh":"老師可能把工作紙設計成簡單、清晰和容易檢查。"},{"en":"If a route is designed to be smooth, recalling it may require less effort.","zh":"如果路線被設計成順暢，回想它可能需要較少力氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planning something with a desired feature.","zh":"這個片語描述以理想特徵規劃某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as smooth and downhill as possible","meaning":"盡可能順暢及向下延伸","examples":[{"en":"The imaginary route is designed to be as smooth and downhill as possible.","zh":"想像中的路線被設計成盡可能順暢及向下延伸。"},{"en":"As smooth and downhill as possible means made easy to follow, with little mental resistance.","zh":"As smooth and downhill as possible 指被設計得容易跟隨，心理阻力很少。"},{"en":"A teacher may arrange a lesson to be as smooth as possible by moving from easy examples to harder ones.","zh":"老師可能由簡單例子推進到較難例子，把課堂安排得盡可能順暢。"},{"en":"If a route feels smooth and downhill, the mind can move through it quickly during recall.","zh":"如果路線感覺順暢且向下延伸，大腦在回想時可以快速穿過它。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests ease, flow, and low effort.","zh":"這個片語暗示容易、流暢和低費力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"when it comes time to recall","meaning":"到需要回想時","examples":[{"en":"When it comes time to recall the cards, Cooke mentally follows the route.","zh":"到需要回想啤牌時，Cooke 會在腦中跟隨路線。"},{"en":"When it comes time to recall means when the moment arrives to remember and produce the information.","zh":"When it comes time to recall 指到了需要記起並說出或寫出資料的時刻。"},{"en":"When it comes time to recall vocabulary in a test, examples can help students remember meanings.","zh":"到測驗中需要回想詞彙時，例句可以幫助學生記起意思。"},{"en":"If information was stored in order, recalling it later becomes less chaotic.","zh":"如果資料已按次序儲存，之後回想就不那麼混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the retrieval stage of memory.","zh":"這個片語指出記憶的提取階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"take a mental walk","meaning":"在腦海中沿路走一遍","examples":[{"en":"Cooke takes a mental walk along his imaginary route.","zh":"Cooke 在腦海中沿着他的想像路線走一遍。"},{"en":"To take a mental walk means to imagine moving through a place in your mind.","zh":"To take a mental walk 指在腦中想像穿過某個地方。"},{"en":"A student may take a mental walk through her bedroom to remember items on a shopping list.","zh":"學生可能在腦海中走過自己的睡房，以記住購物清單上的物品。"},{"en":"If each memory is placed along the route, the mental walk helps bring them back in order.","zh":"如果每段記憶都放在路線上，這趟心理步行就能幫助按次序帶回它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using imagined movement to recall information.","zh":"這個片語描述使用想像中的移動來回想資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"translate images into cards","meaning":"把影像轉換回啤牌","examples":[{"en":"He translates the remembered images back into playing cards.","zh":"他把記住的影像轉換回啤牌。"},{"en":"To translate images into cards means to change mental pictures back into the card values they represent.","zh":"To translate images into cards 指把心理圖像轉回它們所代表的啤牌牌值。"},{"en":"A student may translate a drawing back into vocabulary words during revision.","zh":"學生可能在溫習時把圖畫轉換回詞彙。"},{"en":"If the image-card links are clear, the competitor can recover the original order quickly.","zh":"如果影像與啤牌的連結清楚，參賽者可以快速恢復原來次序。"},{"en":"This phrase describes converting memory images back into information.","zh":"這個片語描述把記憶影像轉回資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"show activation in","meaning":"顯示……出現活動","examples":[{"en":"The MRI scans showed activation in regions linked to spatial memory.","zh":"磁力共振掃描顯示與空間記憶有關的區域出現活動。"},{"en":"To show activation in a brain area means to show that the area became active during a task.","zh":"To show activation in a brain area 指顯示該腦區在任務期間變得活躍。"},{"en":"A scan may show activation in language areas when a person reads aloud.","zh":"當一個人大聲閱讀時，掃描可能顯示語言區域出現活動。"},{"en":"If activation appears in spatial regions, the task may involve mental routes or locations.","zh":"如果空間區域出現活動，該任務可能涉及心理路線或位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence of brain activity.","zh":"這個片語描述大腦活動的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"brain areas associated with","meaning":"與……有關的大腦區域","examples":[{"en":"The contestants used brain areas associated with visual imagery.","zh":"參賽者使用與視覺意象有關的大腦區域。"},{"en":"Brain areas associated with something are regions linked by research to that mental function.","zh":"Brain areas associated with something 是研究上與某心理功能有關的區域。"},{"en":"Brain areas associated with hearing become active when people listen to speech.","zh":"人們聆聽說話時，與聽覺有關的大腦區域會變得活躍。"},{"en":"If memory champions use areas associated with imagery, they may be remembering through pictures.","zh":"如果記憶冠軍使用與意象有關的區域，他們可能透過圖像記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a researched connection between brain regions and functions.","zh":"這個片語描述腦區與功能之間的研究關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the more…the more…","meaning":"越……就越……","examples":[{"en":"The more resonant the images are, the more difficult they are to forget.","zh":"影像越能引起強烈聯想，就越難忘記。"},{"en":"The more…the more… shows that one thing increases as another thing increases.","zh":"The more…the more… 顯示一件事增加時，另一件事也增加。"},{"en":"The more often students review vocabulary, the more confidently they can use it.","zh":"學生越經常複習詞彙，就越能有信心地使用它。"},{"en":"If images become stranger and more emotional, they may become harder to forget.","zh":"如果影像變得越奇怪和越有情緒，它們可能越難忘記。"},{"en":"This structure shows a direct relationship between two changes.","zh":"這個結構顯示兩種變化之間的直接關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"resonant images","meaning":"能引起強烈聯想的影像","examples":[{"en":"Emotionally resonant images are easier to remember.","zh":"情感上能引起強烈聯想的影像較容易記住。"},{"en":"Resonant images are mental pictures that feel strong, meaningful, emotional, or memorable.","zh":"Resonant images 是感覺強烈、有意義、有情緒或令人難忘的心理圖像。"},{"en":"A student may remember a word better if it is linked to a resonant image from family life.","zh":"如果詞語與家庭生活中能引起強烈聯想的影像連接，學生可能更易記住它。"},{"en":"If an image connects with emotion, it stays in memory more firmly.","zh":"如果影像與情緒連接，它會更牢固地留在記憶中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes images that echo strongly in the mind.","zh":"這個片語描述在腦中強烈迴響的影像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be difficult to forget","meaning":"難以忘記","examples":[{"en":"Unusual and vivid images are difficult to forget.","zh":"不尋常而鮮明的影像難以忘記。"},{"en":"To be difficult to forget means to stay strongly in memory.","zh":"To be difficult to forget 指強烈留在記憶中。"},{"en":"A teacher’s funny example may be difficult to forget because it makes the class laugh.","zh":"老師有趣的例子可能因令全班大笑而難以忘記。"},{"en":"If information is emotional, strange, or personal, it often becomes harder to forget.","zh":"如果資料帶有情緒、奇特或個人性質，它通常更難忘記。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong memorability.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈的可記憶性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"meaningful information","meaning":"有意義的資料","examples":[{"en":"Even meaningful information can be difficult to remember in large quantities.","zh":"即使是有意義的資料，數量很大時也可能難以記住。"},{"en":"Meaningful information is information that has clear sense, value, or connection to what we know.","zh":"Meaningful information 是有清楚意思、價值或與我們所知有連結的資料。"},{"en":"A student may find a story easier to remember than a random list because it contains meaningful information.","zh":"學生可能覺得故事比隨機清單更容易記住，因為故事包含有意義的資料。"},{"en":"If meaningful information is too large in amount, it still needs organisation.","zh":"如果有意義的資料數量太大，它仍需要組織。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts useful content with meaningless data.","zh":"這個片語把有用內容與無意義資料作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"when there is a lot of it","meaning":"當數量很多時","examples":[{"en":"Information becomes harder to remember when there is a lot of it.","zh":"當資料數量很多時，它會變得更難記住。"},{"en":"When there is a lot of it means when the amount is large.","zh":"When there is a lot of it 指數量很大時。"},{"en":"Vocabulary feels harder to revise when there is a lot of it on one page.","zh":"當一頁上詞彙數量很多時，溫習會感覺更困難。"},{"en":"If there is too much information, students may need grouping, summaries, or diagrams.","zh":"如果資料太多，學生可能需要分組、摘要或圖表。"},{"en":"This phrase explains that quantity can create difficulty.","zh":"這個片語解釋數量可以造成困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"competitive memorisers","meaning":"競技記憶選手","examples":[{"en":"Competitive memorisers use spatial routes to organise information.","zh":"競技記憶選手使用空間路線來組織資料。"},{"en":"Competitive memorisers are people who train to memorise information quickly in contests.","zh":"Competitive memorisers 是訓練自己在比賽中快速記住資料的人。"},{"en":"A competitive memoriser may practise daily with random numbers and cards.","zh":"競技記憶選手可能每天用隨機數字和啤牌練習。"},{"en":"If competitive memorisers use routes, they can recall information in a planned order.","zh":"如果競技記憶選手使用路線，他們可以按計劃次序回想資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trained memory competitors.","zh":"這個片語描述受過訓練的記憶參賽者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be known as","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"The technique is known as the loci method.","zh":"這種技巧被稱為地點記憶法。"},{"en":"To be known as something means to have that name or be called by that term.","zh":"To be known as something 指有某名稱或被稱作某術語。"},{"en":"A school writing structure may be known as PEEL among students.","zh":"某種學校寫作結構可能在學生中被稱為 PEEL。"},{"en":"If a method is widely known as a certain name, people can discuss it more easily.","zh":"如果方法普遍被稱為某名稱，人們就能更容易討論它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the common name of something.","zh":"這個片語引出某事物的常用名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the loci method","meaning":"地點記憶法；位置記憶法","examples":[{"en":"The loci method connects information with imagined locations.","zh":"地點記憶法把資料與想像位置連接起來。"},{"en":"The loci method is a memory technique that places information in familiar mental locations.","zh":"Loci method 是一種把資料放在熟悉心理位置中的記憶技巧。"},{"en":"A student may use the loci method by placing essay points around their bedroom in imagination.","zh":"學生可能使用地點記憶法，在想像中把作文重點放在睡房各處。"},{"en":"If each point has a location, walking through the mental space helps recall the points in order.","zh":"如果每個重點都有位置，在心理空間中走一遍就能幫助按次序回想重點。"},{"en":"This phrase names a spatial memory technique.","zh":"這個片語命名一種空間記憶技巧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reportedly originate in","meaning":"據報起源於","examples":[{"en":"The loci method reportedly originated in ancient Greece.","zh":"據報地點記憶法起源於古希臘。"},{"en":"To reportedly originate in a place means people say or evidence suggests it began there.","zh":"To reportedly originate in a place 指人們說或證據顯示某事源自該地。"},{"en":"A local festival reportedly originated in a farming village centuries ago.","zh":"據報某本地節日起源於數百年前的一條農村。"},{"en":"If a method reportedly began in ancient times, its exact origin may not be fully certain.","zh":"如果方法據報始於古代，其確切起源可能未完全確定。"},{"en":"This phrase presents a claimed or reported origin.","zh":"這個片語呈現被報道或聲稱的起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the Greek poet","meaning":"希臘詩人","examples":[{"en":"The technique is associated with the Greek poet Simonides of Ceos.","zh":"這種技巧與希臘詩人 Simonides of Ceos 有關。"},{"en":"The Greek poet means a poet from ancient Greece.","zh":"Greek poet 指來自古希臘的詩人。"},{"en":"A literature class may study a Greek poet to understand early European storytelling.","zh":"文學課可能研究希臘詩人，以理解早期歐洲敘事。"},{"en":"If a memory method is linked to a Greek poet, it suggests the technique has ancient cultural roots.","zh":"如果記憶方法與希臘詩人有關，它暗示該技巧有古代文化根源。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a poet by nationality and historical culture.","zh":"這個片語以國族和歷史文化識別詩人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the sole survivor of","meaning":"……的唯一生還者","examples":[{"en":"Simonides was the sole survivor of a roof collapse.","zh":"Simonides 是屋頂倒塌事故的唯一生還者。"},{"en":"The sole survivor of an accident is the only person who remains alive after it.","zh":"Sole survivor of an accident 是事故後唯一仍然生還的人。"},{"en":"A news report may describe one passenger as the sole survivor of a crash.","zh":"新聞報道可能把一名乘客描述為墜機事故的唯一生還者。"},{"en":"If someone is the sole survivor, their memory may become important evidence.","zh":"如果某人是唯一生還者，他的記憶可能成為重要證據。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that everyone else involved died or was lost.","zh":"這個片語強調其他涉事者都死亡或失去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a roof collapse","meaning":"屋頂倒塌","examples":[{"en":"A roof collapse killed the other guests at the banquet.","zh":"屋頂倒塌令宴會中的其他賓客喪生。"},{"en":"A roof collapse happens when the top structure of a building falls down.","zh":"Roof collapse 指建築物頂部結構倒下。"},{"en":"An old market may suffer a roof collapse after heavy rain weakens the structure.","zh":"舊市場可能在大雨削弱結構後發生屋頂倒塌。"},{"en":"If a roof collapses, people inside may be injured, trapped, or killed.","zh":"如果屋頂倒塌，裏面的人可能受傷、被困或死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious building failure.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重建築結構事故。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a royal banquet","meaning":"王室宴會","examples":[{"en":"The accident occurred during a royal banquet.","zh":"事故發生在一場王室宴會期間。"},{"en":"A royal banquet is a formal meal held for or by a king, queen, or royal family.","zh":"Royal banquet 是為國王、女王或王室舉行，或由他們主持的正式宴會。"},{"en":"A palace may hold a royal banquet for visiting leaders.","zh":"宮殿可能為到訪領袖舉行王室宴會。"},{"en":"If an accident occurs during a royal banquet, many important guests may be affected.","zh":"如果事故發生在王室宴會期間，許多重要賓客可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a grand official meal connected with royalty.","zh":"這個片語描述與王室有關的盛大正式餐宴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be mangled beyond recognition","meaning":"損毀至無法辨認","examples":[{"en":"The victims’ bodies were mangled beyond recognition.","zh":"受害者遺體損毀至無法辨認。"},{"en":"To be mangled beyond recognition means to be so badly damaged that people cannot identify the original form.","zh":"To be mangled beyond recognition 指損毀嚴重到人們無法辨認原本形狀。"},{"en":"A bicycle hit by a truck may be mangled beyond recognition.","zh":"被貨車撞到的單車可能損毀至無法辨認。"},{"en":"If bodies are beyond recognition, investigators may need other evidence to identify them.","zh":"如果遺體無法辨認，調查人員可能需要其他證據識別身份。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extreme physical damage.","zh":"這個片語描述極端身體損毀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reconstruct the guest list","meaning":"重組賓客名單","examples":[{"en":"Simonides reconstructed the guest list from his memory of the seating arrangement.","zh":"Simonides 根據自己對座位安排的記憶重組賓客名單。"},{"en":"To reconstruct the guest list means to rebuild the list of guests from memory or evidence.","zh":"To reconstruct the guest list 指從記憶或證據重新建立賓客名單。"},{"en":"After losing the attendance sheet, a teacher may reconstruct the guest list from photos and messages.","zh":"老師遺失出席名單後，可能從照片和訊息重組賓客名單。"},{"en":"If the seating plan is remembered clearly, missing names can be recovered.","zh":"如果座位圖被清楚記住，遺失的姓名可以被找回。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rebuilding information that has been lost.","zh":"這個片語描述重建已遺失的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"close his eyes","meaning":"閉上眼睛","examples":[{"en":"He reconstructed the scene by closing his eyes.","zh":"他透過閉上眼睛重組場景。"},{"en":"To close his eyes means to shut his eyes, often to concentrate, rest, or imagine.","zh":"To close his eyes 指把眼睛合上，通常為了集中、休息或想像。"},{"en":"A student may close her eyes to picture a map before answering a geography question.","zh":"學生回答地理題前，可能閉上眼睛想像地圖。"},{"en":"If someone closes their eyes, distractions may reduce and mental images may become clearer.","zh":"如果某人閉上眼睛，干擾可能減少，心理影像可能更清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase can show concentration or visualisation.","zh":"這個片語可以表示集中或視覺化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"recall each individual","meaning":"記起每一個人","examples":[{"en":"Simonides recalled each individual seated around the table.","zh":"Simonides 記起圍坐在餐桌旁的每一個人。"},{"en":"To recall each individual means to remember every separate person.","zh":"To recall each individual 指記住每一個獨立的人。"},{"en":"A teacher may recall each individual in a small class after learning their names carefully.","zh":"老師仔細學習學生名字後，可能記起小班中的每一個人。"},{"en":"If people are placed in clear positions, recalling each individual becomes easier.","zh":"如果人們被放在清楚位置中，記起每一個人會更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses remembering people one by one.","zh":"這個片語強調逐一記住每個人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"around the dinner table","meaning":"圍坐在餐桌旁","examples":[{"en":"He remembered where each guest had been sitting around the dinner table.","zh":"他記得每位賓客當時圍坐在餐桌旁的位置。"},{"en":"Around the dinner table means seated or gathered near the table used for a meal.","zh":"Around the dinner table 指坐在或聚集於用餐桌旁。"},{"en":"A family may discuss school, work, and weekend plans around the dinner table.","zh":"家庭可能圍坐在餐桌旁討論學校、工作和週末計劃。"},{"en":"If people sit in fixed places around a table, their positions can help memory.","zh":"如果人們圍坐在餐桌旁固定位置，他們的位置可以幫助記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a familiar social setting for a meal.","zh":"這個片語描述熟悉的用餐社交場景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"exceptionally good at","meaning":"非常擅長","examples":[{"en":"Human brains are exceptionally good at remembering spatial information.","zh":"人類大腦非常擅長記住空間資料。"},{"en":"To be exceptionally good at something means to be unusually skilled at it.","zh":"To be exceptionally good at something 指在某事上有不尋常的高超能力。"},{"en":"Some students are exceptionally good at noticing small pronunciation differences.","zh":"有些學生非常擅長注意微小發音差異。"},{"en":"If the brain is exceptionally good at locations, memory techniques can use places as hooks.","zh":"如果大腦非常擅長位置，記憶技巧就可以用地方作掛鉤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ability far above ordinary level.","zh":"這個片語描述遠高於普通水平的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"spatial information","meaning":"空間資料","examples":[{"en":"The loci method takes advantage of our ability to remember spatial information.","zh":"地點記憶法利用我們記住空間資料的能力。"},{"en":"Spatial information is information about places, positions, directions, and distances.","zh":"Spatial information 是關於地方、位置、方向和距離的資料。"},{"en":"A student uses spatial information when remembering where the library is in a school building.","zh":"學生記住圖書館在校舍哪裡時，就是使用空間資料。"},{"en":"If information is linked to locations, spatial memory can help recall it.","zh":"如果資料與位置連接，空間記憶可以幫助回想它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes knowledge about where things are.","zh":"這個片語描述關於事物位置的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"evolutionary psychologists","meaning":"進化心理學家","examples":[{"en":"Evolutionary psychologists have proposed an explanation for this ability.","zh":"進化心理學家為這種能力提出了解釋。"},{"en":"Evolutionary psychologists study how human thoughts and behaviours may have developed to solve survival problems.","zh":"Evolutionary psychologists 研究人類思想和行為如何可能發展出來以解決生存問題。"},{"en":"Evolutionary psychologists may ask why people remember danger or food locations so well.","zh":"進化心理學家可能問為何人們如此擅長記住危險或食物位置。"},{"en":"If a mental ability helped ancestors survive, it may remain strong today.","zh":"如果某心理能力幫助祖先生存，它今天可能仍然強大。"},{"en":"This phrase names psychologists who explain behaviour through evolution.","zh":"這個片語命名透過進化解釋行為的心理學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"offer an explanation","meaning":"提出解釋","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have offered an evolutionary explanation for spatial memory.","zh":"研究人員為空間記憶提出了進化解釋。"},{"en":"To offer an explanation means to suggest a reason why something happens.","zh":"To offer an explanation 指提出某事發生的原因。"},{"en":"A teacher may offer an explanation for why students confuse two similar words.","zh":"老師可能解釋為何學生混淆兩個相似詞語。"},{"en":"If an explanation fits the evidence, people may accept it as useful.","zh":"如果解釋符合證據，人們可能接受它是有用的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes proposing a possible reason.","zh":"這個片語描述提出可能原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"presumably","meaning":"據推測；大概","examples":[{"en":"Presumably, spatial memory helped our ancestors survive.","zh":"據推測，空間記憶幫助我們的祖先生存。"},{"en":"Presumably means something is likely or reasonable to believe, although not completely proven.","zh":"Presumably 指某事很可能或合理相信如此，但未完全證實。"},{"en":"Presumably, the student was late because the bus broke down, but the teacher still needs confirmation.","zh":"該學生遲到大概是因為巴士壞了，但老師仍需要確認。"},{"en":"If a claim begins with presumably, it is presented as a cautious inference.","zh":"如果主張以 presumably 開始，它就是一個謹慎推論。"},{"en":"This word signals a reasonable guess.","zh":"這個詞表示合理猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"our ancestors","meaning":"我們的祖先","examples":[{"en":"Our ancestors needed to remember the locations of food and shelter.","zh":"我們的祖先需要記住食物和庇護所的位置。"},{"en":"Our ancestors are the people from earlier generations from whom we are descended.","zh":"Our ancestors 是較早世代、我們從其後代而來的人。"},{"en":"Our ancestors lived without maps, phones, or supermarkets.","zh":"我們的祖先生活中沒有地圖、電話或超級市場。"},{"en":"If our ancestors remembered safe paths and food sources, they had a better chance of survival.","zh":"如果我們的祖先記住安全路線和食物來源，他們生存機會更高。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people in the human past.","zh":"這個片語指人類過去的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"recall where","meaning":"記起……的位置","examples":[{"en":"Our ancestors needed to recall where they had found food.","zh":"我們的祖先需要記起他們在哪裡找到食物。"},{"en":"To recall where something is means to remember its location.","zh":"To recall where something is 指記住某物的位置。"},{"en":"A student may recall where a library book was placed after seeing the shelf in their mind.","zh":"學生可能在腦中看見書架後，記起圖書館書本的位置。"},{"en":"If people can recall where resources are, they can return to them later.","zh":"如果人們能記起資源的位置，他們之後可以回到那裡。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on remembering place.","zh":"這個片語著重記住地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"find their last meal","meaning":"找到上一頓食物","examples":[{"en":"They needed to remember where they had found their last meal.","zh":"他們需要記得自己在哪裡找到上一頓食物。"},{"en":"To find their last meal means to locate the place where food was last obtained.","zh":"To find their last meal 指找到上次取得食物的地方。"},{"en":"A hiker may remember where she found berries so she can return if she needs food.","zh":"行山者可能記得在哪裡找到莓果，以便需要食物時回去。"},{"en":"If early humans remembered food locations, they could survive better during shortages.","zh":"如果早期人類記住食物位置，他們在短缺期間可以更好地生存。"},{"en":"This phrase connects memory with finding food.","zh":"這個片語把記憶與尋找食物連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the way back to","meaning":"返回……的路","examples":[{"en":"Spatial memory helped people find the way back to their shelter.","zh":"空間記憶幫助人們找到返回庇護所的路。"},{"en":"The way back to a place is the route returning to it.","zh":"The way back to a place 是回到該地的路線。"},{"en":"A child may learn the way back to the classroom after visiting the library.","zh":"孩子參觀圖書館後，可能學會返回課室的路。"},{"en":"If people cannot find the way back, they may become lost or unsafe.","zh":"如果人們找不到返回的路，他們可能迷路或不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a return route.","zh":"這個片語描述返回路線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"become popular across","meaning":"在……各地流行起來","examples":[{"en":"The loci method became popular across ancient Greece.","zh":"地點記憶法在古希臘各地流行起來。"},{"en":"To become popular across a place means to be widely used or liked in many parts of that area.","zh":"To become popular across a place 指在該地許多地方被廣泛使用或喜愛。"},{"en":"A study app may become popular across schools if students find it helpful.","zh":"如果學生覺得學習應用程式有幫助，它可能在各校流行起來。"},{"en":"If a method works well, it can spread from one community to many others.","zh":"如果方法有效，它可以從一個社群傳到許多其他社群。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wide popularity over an area.","zh":"這個片語描述在某地區廣泛流行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"memorise speeches and texts","meaning":"記住演說和文章","examples":[{"en":"People used the method to memorise speeches and texts.","zh":"人們使用這種方法記住演說和文章。"},{"en":"To memorise speeches and texts means to learn spoken or written passages by heart.","zh":"To memorise speeches and texts 指把口頭或書面段落背熟。"},{"en":"A student actor may memorise speeches and texts before a school play.","zh":"學生演員可能在學校戲劇前記住演說和文章。"},{"en":"If printed materials are rare, memorising long texts becomes more important.","zh":"如果印刷材料稀少，記住長篇文本就變得更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deliberate learning of language passages.","zh":"這個片語描述有意識地學會語言段落。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a number of treatises","meaning":"多篇專門論述","examples":[{"en":"A number of treatises on memory were published in Rome.","zh":"羅馬出版了多篇關於記憶的專門論述。"},{"en":"A number of treatises means several formal written works about a subject.","zh":"A number of treatises 指幾篇關於某主題的正式書面著作。"},{"en":"A university course may use a number of treatises on law, medicine, or philosophy.","zh":"大學課程可能使用多篇關於法律、醫學或哲學的專門論述。"},{"en":"If many treatises are written on a topic, the topic was probably considered important.","zh":"如果許多專門論述都寫某題目，該題目很可能被視為重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes several serious academic writings.","zh":"這個片語描述幾篇嚴肅學術作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the art of memory","meaning":"記憶術","examples":[{"en":"Ancient scholars wrote treatises on the art of memory.","zh":"古代學者撰寫關於記憶術的專門論述。"},{"en":"The art of memory means a set of techniques for remembering information effectively.","zh":"Art of memory 指一套有效記住資料的技巧。"},{"en":"A speaker may study the art of memory to deliver a long speech without notes.","zh":"演講者可能學習記憶術，以不用筆記發表長篇演說。"},{"en":"If people practise memory as an art, they treat it as a skill that can be trained.","zh":"如果人們把記憶當成一門技藝練習，他們就把它視為可訓練的技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes memory as a learned technique, not only natural ability.","zh":"這個片語描述記憶是學回來的技巧，而不只是天生能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"printed books","meaning":"印刷書籍","examples":[{"en":"The art of memory was especially important before printed books became common.","zh":"在印刷書籍普及前，記憶術尤其重要。"},{"en":"Printed books are books produced in many copies by printing rather than by hand copying.","zh":"Printed books 是透過印刷而非手抄大量製作的書籍。"},{"en":"Before printed books were cheap, students often depended more on listening and memorising.","zh":"在印刷書籍便宜之前，學生通常更依賴聆聽和記憶。"},{"en":"If books are rare, memory becomes a more important way to preserve knowledge.","zh":"如果書籍稀少，記憶就成為保存知識更重要的方法。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to mass-produced written texts.","zh":"這個片語指大量製作的書面文本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a staple of","meaning":"……的基本部分","examples":[{"en":"Memory training was considered a staple of classical education.","zh":"記憶訓練被視為古典教育的基本部分。"},{"en":"A staple of something is a basic and important part of it.","zh":"Staple of something 是某事物中基本而重要的一部分。"},{"en":"Reading aloud is a staple of many language classes.","zh":"大聲朗讀是許多語言課的基本部分。"},{"en":"If a skill is a staple of education, most students are expected to learn it.","zh":"如果某技能是教育的基本部分，大多數學生都被期望學會它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something central and regularly included.","zh":"這個片語描述核心且經常包含的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"classical education","meaning":"古典教育","examples":[{"en":"The art of memory was an important part of classical education.","zh":"記憶術是古典教育的重要部分。"},{"en":"Classical education is traditional education based on subjects such as grammar, logic, rhetoric, literature, and ancient learning.","zh":"Classical education 是以文法、邏輯、修辭、文學和古代學問等科目為基礎的傳統教育。"},{"en":"A school with classical education may ask students to study Latin, debate, and memorise speeches.","zh":"採用古典教育的學校可能要求學生學拉丁文、辯論和背誦演說。"},{"en":"If memory was central in classical education, students were trained to speak and think without constant written aids.","zh":"如果記憶在古典教育中是核心，學生就被訓練在不經常依賴文字輔助下說話和思考。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an old scholarly model of education.","zh":"這個片語描述古老的學術教育模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"on a par with","meaning":"與……同等重要","examples":[{"en":"Memory training was considered on a par with grammar and rhetoric.","zh":"記憶訓練被視為與文法和修辭同等重要。"},{"en":"To be on a par with something means to be equal in level, value, or importance.","zh":"To be on a par with something 指在水平、價值或重要性上相等。"},{"en":"A school may treat speaking skills as on a par with writing skills.","zh":"學校可能把口語能力視為與寫作能力同等重要。"},{"en":"If memory was on a par with grammar, it was not seen as a minor skill.","zh":"如果記憶與文法同等重要，它就不被視為次要技能。"},{"en":"This phrase shows equality of importance.","zh":"這個片語顯示重要性相等。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"grammar, logic and rhetoric","meaning":"文法、邏輯與修辭","examples":[{"en":"Classical education included grammar, logic and rhetoric.","zh":"古典教育包括文法、邏輯與修辭。"},{"en":"Grammar, logic and rhetoric are traditional subjects involving correct language, reasoning, and persuasive speech.","zh":"Grammar, logic and rhetoric 是涉及準確語言、推理和有說服力演說的傳統科目。"},{"en":"Students study grammar to write accurately, logic to reason clearly, and rhetoric to speak persuasively.","zh":"學生學文法以準確寫作，學邏輯以清晰推理，學修辭以有說服力地表達。"},{"en":"If education includes these three areas, it trains both language and thinking.","zh":"如果教育包括這三個範疇，它就同時訓練語言和思考。"},{"en":"This phrase names core subjects in classical learning.","zh":"這個片語命名古典學習中的核心科目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the most famous of","meaning":"……之中最著名的","examples":[{"en":"Shereshevski was the most famous of the naturally gifted memorisers.","zh":"Shereshevski 是天生記憶力超凡的人之中最著名的一位。"},{"en":"The most famous of a group means the best known person or thing among them.","zh":"The most famous of a group 指該群體中最為人熟知的人或事物。"},{"en":"Shakespeare is often the most famous of English playwrights studied in school.","zh":"Shakespeare 常是學校中所學英國劇作家之中最著名的一位。"},{"en":"If someone becomes the most famous example, later discussions often return to their case.","zh":"如果某人成為最著名例子，之後討論常會回到他的個案。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the best-known member of a category.","zh":"這個片語指出某類別中最知名的成員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"natural memorisers","meaning":"天生記憶力超凡的人","examples":[{"en":"Some people were regarded as natural memorisers.","zh":"有些人被視為天生記憶力超凡的人。"},{"en":"Natural memorisers are people thought to have unusually strong memory without special training.","zh":"Natural memorisers 是被認為沒有特殊訓練也有異常強大記憶力的人。"},{"en":"A child who remembers every bus route after one trip may be seen as a natural memoriser.","zh":"一次車程後就記住每條巴士路線的孩子，可能被視為天生記憶力超凡的人。"},{"en":"If someone is a natural memoriser, people may assume their ability was born rather than learned.","zh":"如果某人是天生記憶者，人們可能假設他的能力是天生而不是學來的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes apparently innate memory talent.","zh":"這個片語描述看似天生的記憶天賦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"recall long lists of","meaning":"憶起長串……","examples":[{"en":"Shereshevski could recall long lists of numbers.","zh":"Shereshevski 能憶起長串數字。"},{"en":"To recall long lists of something means to remember many items in order or detail.","zh":"To recall long lists of something 指按次序或細節記起許多項目。"},{"en":"A waiter may recall long lists of orders during a busy lunch hour.","zh":"侍應在繁忙午餐時段可能憶起長串點餐。"},{"en":"If a list is long, grouping items can make recall easier.","zh":"如果清單很長，把項目分組可以令回想更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes remembering many items, not just one fact.","zh":"這個片語描述記住許多項目，而不只是單一事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"decades earlier","meaning":"數十年前","examples":[{"en":"He recalled information that he had memorised decades earlier.","zh":"他憶起自己數十年前記住的資料。"},{"en":"Decades earlier means many tens of years before the present or the time being discussed.","zh":"Decades earlier 指在現在或所討論時間之前許多個十年。"},{"en":"A grandfather may remember a school song he learned decades earlier.","zh":"祖父可能記得自己數十年前學過的校歌。"},{"en":"If someone recalls information from decades earlier, their long-term memory is unusually strong.","zh":"如果某人能憶起數十年前的資料，他的長期記憶異常強大。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a very long time gap.","zh":"這個片語強調很長時間差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"strings of nonsense syllables","meaning":"一連串無意義音節","examples":[{"en":"He could memorise strings of nonsense syllables.","zh":"他能記住一連串無意義音節。"},{"en":"Strings of nonsense syllables are sequences of meaningless sound units.","zh":"Strings of nonsense syllables 是一串沒有意思的聲音單位。"},{"en":"A memory test may use strings of nonsense syllables so students cannot rely on meaning.","zh":"記憶測試可能使用一連串無意義音節，令學生不能依賴意思。"},{"en":"If material has no meaning, people must use sound, rhythm, or memory techniques to remember it.","zh":"如果材料沒有意思，人們必須使用聲音、節奏或記憶技巧來記住它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaningless verbal sequences.","zh":"這個片語描述無意義的語音序列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"just about anything else","meaning":"幾乎任何其他事物","examples":[{"en":"He could remember just about anything else he was asked to learn.","zh":"他幾乎能記住任何被要求學習的其他事物。"},{"en":"Just about anything else means almost every other thing.","zh":"Just about anything else 指幾乎每一樣其他東西。"},{"en":"A strong student may help with grammar, vocabulary, pronunciation, and just about anything else in English.","zh":"能力強的學生可能幫助英文文法、詞彙、發音和幾乎任何其他方面。"},{"en":"If someone can remember just about anything, their ability seems extremely broad.","zh":"如果某人幾乎能記住任何事物，他的能力就顯得極其廣泛。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises near-complete range.","zh":"這個片語強調接近完整的範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the capacity of his memory","meaning":"他的記憶容量","examples":[{"en":"The capacity of his memory appeared to have no clear limit.","zh":"他的記憶容量似乎沒有清楚界限。"},{"en":"The capacity of his memory means how much information his memory could hold.","zh":"Capacity of his memory 指他的記憶能容納多少資訊。"},{"en":"A student may test the capacity of memory by seeing how many vocabulary words can be recalled after a week.","zh":"學生可能透過檢查一星期後能回想多少詞彙來測試記憶容量。"},{"en":"If memory capacity seems huge, people may wonder whether special brain features or techniques are involved.","zh":"如果記憶容量看似巨大，人們可能想知道是否涉及特殊大腦特徵或技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the amount a person can remember.","zh":"這個片語描述一個人能記住多少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"have no distinct limits","meaning":"沒有明確界限","examples":[{"en":"His memory seemed to have no distinct limits.","zh":"他的記憶似乎沒有明確界限。"},{"en":"To have no distinct limits means to show no clear boundary or maximum.","zh":"To have no distinct limits 指沒有顯示清楚邊界或最大限度。"},{"en":"A child’s curiosity may seem to have no distinct limits when they ask questions all day.","zh":"孩子整天問問題時，好奇心可能看似沒有明確界限。"},{"en":"If an ability has no clear limit, researchers may study it carefully.","zh":"如果一種能力沒有清楚限制，研究人員可能仔細研究它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that appears almost unlimited.","zh":"這個片語描述看似幾乎無限的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"synesthesia","meaning":"聯覺","examples":[{"en":"Shereshevski also experienced synesthesia.","zh":"Shereshevski 也有聯覺。"},{"en":"Synesthesia is a condition in which one sense or idea automatically triggers another sense or experience.","zh":"Synesthesia 是一種一種感官或概念自動觸發另一種感官或經驗的狀況。"},{"en":"A person with synesthesia may see colours when hearing music.","zh":"有聯覺的人聽音樂時可能看見顏色。"},{"en":"If numbers create colours in the mind, they may become easier to remember.","zh":"如果數字在腦中產生顏色，它們可能變得更容易記住。"},{"en":"This word describes unusual linking between senses.","zh":"這個詞描述感官之間不尋常的連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a rare condition","meaning":"一種罕見狀況","examples":[{"en":"Synesthesia is a rare neurological condition.","zh":"聯覺是一種罕見神經狀況。"},{"en":"A rare condition is an unusual medical or mental state found in relatively few people.","zh":"Rare condition 是相對少數人擁有的不尋常醫學或心理狀態。"},{"en":"A doctor may refer a patient to a specialist if they show signs of a rare condition.","zh":"如果病人顯示罕見狀況的跡象，醫生可能轉介他到專科。"},{"en":"If a condition is rare, researchers may need many years to collect enough cases.","zh":"如果狀況罕見，研究人員可能需要多年收集足夠個案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something uncommon in health or biology.","zh":"這個片語描述健康或生物學上不常見的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the senses become intertwined","meaning":"不同感官互相交織","examples":[{"en":"In synesthesia, different senses become intertwined.","zh":"在聯覺中，不同感官互相交織。"},{"en":"When senses become intertwined, one sense becomes linked with another in experience.","zh":"When senses become intertwined 指一種感官在經驗中與另一種感官連接起來。"},{"en":"A person may hear a word and immediately experience a colour if their senses are intertwined.","zh":"如果感官互相交織，一個人聽到某詞時可能立即感到一種顏色。"},{"en":"If senses are linked, memory may gain extra cues from colour, sound, or taste.","zh":"如果感官被連接，記憶可能從顏色、聲音或味道獲得額外線索。"},{"en":"This phrase describes senses mixing or connecting.","zh":"這個片語描述感官混合或連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be associated with a colour","meaning":"與某種顏色聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"For some people with synesthesia, every number is associated with a colour.","zh":"對一些有聯覺的人來說，每個數字都與某種顏色聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To be associated with a colour means to be mentally linked to a particular colour.","zh":"To be associated with a colour 指在心理上與某種特定顏色連接。"},{"en":"A child may associate Monday with blue because the school timetable uses blue for that day.","zh":"孩子可能把星期一與藍色聯繫起來，因為學校時間表用藍色代表那一天。"},{"en":"If numbers are linked with colours, remembering a number sequence may feel like remembering a colour pattern.","zh":"如果數字與顏色連接，記住數列可能感覺像記住顏色圖案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mental colour connection.","zh":"這個片語描述心理上的顏色連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be associated with a taste","meaning":"與某種味道聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"A word may be associated with a particular taste.","zh":"一個詞可能與某種特定味道聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To be associated with a taste means to be mentally linked to a flavour or mouth sensation.","zh":"To be associated with a taste 指在心理上與某種味道或口腔感覺連接。"},{"en":"A person may associate the word “lemon” with a sharp sour taste.","zh":"一個人可能把 “lemon” 一詞與強烈酸味聯繫起來。"},{"en":"If a word triggers a taste, the extra sensation may make it more memorable.","zh":"如果詞語觸發味道，額外感覺可能令它更容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a connection between language and taste.","zh":"這個片語描述語言與味覺之間的連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"synesthetic reactions","meaning":"聯覺反應","examples":[{"en":"Synesthetic reactions can strengthen a person’s memory.","zh":"聯覺反應可以加強一個人的記憶。"},{"en":"Synesthetic reactions are automatic sensory responses triggered by words, numbers, sounds, or other stimuli.","zh":"Synesthetic reactions 是由詞語、數字、聲音或其他刺激自動觸發的感官反應。"},{"en":"A sound that automatically creates a colour in someone’s mind is a synesthetic reaction.","zh":"聲音自動在某人腦中產生顏色，就是聯覺反應。"},{"en":"If a word produces extra sensory responses, the memory has more cues attached to it.","zh":"如果詞語產生額外感官反應，記憶就附有更多線索。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sensory cross-links that may support memory.","zh":"這個片語描述可能支持記憶的感官交叉連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"evoke a response","meaning":"引起反應","examples":[{"en":"A sound or word may evoke a response in several brain regions.","zh":"聲音或詞語可能在幾個大腦區域引起反應。"},{"en":"To evoke a response means to cause a reaction, feeling, memory, or brain activity.","zh":"To evoke a response 指造成反應、感受、記憶或大腦活動。"},{"en":"A familiar smell may evoke a response by reminding someone of home.","zh":"熟悉氣味可能透過令人想起家而引起反應。"},{"en":"If one word evokes several responses, it may become easier to remember.","zh":"如果一個詞引起幾種反應，它可能更容易被記住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes triggering a reaction.","zh":"這個片語描述觸發反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in more areas of the brain","meaning":"在更多大腦區域","examples":[{"en":"Synesthetic experiences produce responses in more areas of the brain.","zh":"聯覺經驗會在更多大腦區域產生反應。"},{"en":"In more areas of the brain means across a larger number of brain regions.","zh":"In more areas of the brain 指橫跨更多腦區。"},{"en":"Reading aloud may involve more areas of the brain than silent reading because it uses speech and hearing.","zh":"大聲閱讀可能比默讀涉及更多大腦區域，因為它使用說話和聽覺。"},{"en":"If more brain areas respond, a memory may have more connections.","zh":"如果更多腦區作出反應，記憶可能有更多連結。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broader brain involvement.","zh":"這個片語描述更廣泛的大腦參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"make memory easier","meaning":"令記憶變得更容易","examples":[{"en":"Additional sensory associations can make memory easier.","zh":"額外感官聯想可以令記憶變得更容易。"},{"en":"To make memory easier means to help people store or recall information with less effort.","zh":"To make memory easier 指幫助人用較少力氣儲存或回想資料。"},{"en":"Colour-coding notes can make memory easier for visual learners.","zh":"用顏色標示筆記可以令視覺型學習者記憶更容易。"},{"en":"If information has several cues, students may find it easier to remember later.","zh":"如果資料有幾個線索，學生之後可能更容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing the difficulty of remembering.","zh":"這個片語描述降低記憶難度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"acquire someone’s skills","meaning":"掌握某人的技能","examples":[{"en":"Ericsson believes that anyone can acquire Shereshevski’s skills.","zh":"Ericsson 相信任何人都能掌握 Shereshevski 的技能。"},{"en":"To acquire someone’s skills means to learn and develop abilities similar to theirs.","zh":"To acquire someone’s skills 指學習並發展與某人相似的能力。"},{"en":"A student can acquire a good speaker’s skills by practising structure, tone, and examples.","zh":"學生可以透過練習結構、語氣和例子，掌握優秀演講者的技能。"},{"en":"If skills can be acquired, training matters more than admiration from a distance.","zh":"如果技能可以被掌握，訓練就比遠距離羨慕更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning abilities over time.","zh":"這個片語描述隨時間學會能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"cite an experiment","meaning":"引述一項實驗","examples":[{"en":"Ericsson cites an experiment involving an undergraduate student.","zh":"Ericsson 引述一項涉及本科生的實驗。"},{"en":"To cite an experiment means to mention it as evidence for an argument.","zh":"To cite an experiment 指提及某實驗作為論點證據。"},{"en":"A teacher may cite an experiment to show that sleep improves learning.","zh":"老師可能引述一項實驗，顯示睡眠改善學習。"},{"en":"If an expert cites research, the claim becomes more evidence-based.","zh":"如果專家引用研究，主張就更有證據基礎。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using a study to support a point.","zh":"這個片語描述使用研究支持觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a standard test of memory","meaning":"標準記憶測試","examples":[{"en":"The digit-span task is a standard test of memory.","zh":"數字記憶廣度任務是一項標準記憶測試。"},{"en":"A standard test of memory is a commonly used task for measuring memory ability.","zh":"Standard test of memory 是常用來量度記憶能力的任務。"},{"en":"A psychologist may use a standard memory test to compare a patient with people of the same age.","zh":"心理學家可能使用標準記憶測試，把病人與同齡人士比較。"},{"en":"If a test is standard, results can be compared across studies.","zh":"如果測試是標準化的，結果就可以在不同研究之間比較。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a recognised way to assess memory.","zh":"這個片語描述公認的記憶評估方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"digit span","meaning":"數字記憶廣度","examples":[{"en":"A digit span measures how many numbers a person can hold in mind.","zh":"數字記憶廣度量度一個人能在腦中記住多少數字。"},{"en":"Digit span is the number of digits someone can remember in the correct order for a short time.","zh":"Digit span 是某人在短時間內能按正確次序記住的數字數量。"},{"en":"A student with a longer digit span may repeat a phone number more accurately.","zh":"數字記憶廣度較長的學生，可能更準確重複電話號碼。"},{"en":"If digit span improves, the person can hold more numerical information at once.","zh":"如果數字記憶廣度提升，該人就能一次容納更多數字資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes short-term memory for numbers.","zh":"這個片語描述對數字的短期記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"for one hour a day","meaning":"每日一小時","examples":[{"en":"The student practised the test for one hour a day.","zh":"該學生每日一小時練習該測試。"},{"en":"For one hour a day means during a daily period of sixty minutes.","zh":"For one hour a day 指每天一段六十分鐘時間。"},{"en":"A student may read English for one hour a day before a public exam.","zh":"學生可能在公開試前每日一小時閱讀英文。"},{"en":"If practice happens for one hour a day, progress can build steadily over weeks.","zh":"如果練習每日一小時進行，進步可以在幾星期內穩步累積。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a regular daily practice period.","zh":"這個片語描述固定的每日練習時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"two or three days a week","meaning":"每星期兩至三日","examples":[{"en":"He completed the training two or three days a week.","zh":"他每星期兩至三日完成訓練。"},{"en":"Two or three days a week means on some days each week, but not every day.","zh":"Two or three days a week 指每星期其中幾天，但不是每天。"},{"en":"A student may attend tutorial lessons two or three days a week during exam season.","zh":"學生可能在考試季每星期兩至三日上補習課。"},{"en":"If practice happens several times a week, improvement can continue without daily training.","zh":"如果每星期練習幾次，即使不是每日訓練，進步仍可持續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a moderate weekly frequency.","zh":"這個片語描述中等程度的每週頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"hold digits in his head","meaning":"在腦中記住數字","examples":[{"en":"At first, he could hold only about seven digits in his head.","zh":"起初，他一次只能在腦中記住約七個數字。"},{"en":"To hold digits in his head means to keep numbers in short-term memory without writing them down.","zh":"To hold digits in his head 指不用寫下來，把數字保存在短期記憶中。"},{"en":"A cashier may hold a few digits in her head while entering a price code.","zh":"收銀員輸入價格編碼時，可能在腦中記住幾個數字。"},{"en":"If too many digits must be held at once, mistakes become more likely.","zh":"如果一次要記住太多數字，錯誤就更可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mentally keeping numbers for a short time.","zh":"這個片語描述短時間在腦中保留數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"at any given time","meaning":"在任何特定時刻","examples":[{"en":"Most people can remember about seven digits at any given time.","zh":"大多數人在任何特定時刻能記住約七個數字。"},{"en":"At any given time means at one particular moment.","zh":"At any given time 指在某一個特定時刻。"},{"en":"A teacher can usually answer only one student’s question at any given time.","zh":"老師通常在任何特定時刻只能回答一名學生的問題。"},{"en":"If memory capacity is limited at any given time, grouping information becomes useful.","zh":"如果記憶容量在任何特定時刻有限，把資料分組就變得有用。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what is possible at a single moment.","zh":"這個片語著重單一時刻能做到甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the length of a phone number","meaning":"電話號碼的長度","examples":[{"en":"Seven digits was conveniently the length of a phone number.","zh":"七個數字剛好是電話號碼的長度。"},{"en":"The length of a phone number means how many digits a telephone number contains.","zh":"Length of a phone number 指電話號碼包含多少個數字。"},{"en":"A child may remember the length of a phone number by counting each digit aloud.","zh":"孩子可能透過大聲數每個數字來記住電話號碼的長度。"},{"en":"If a number is the same length as a phone number, it may feel familiar and manageable.","zh":"如果一個數字串與電話號碼長度相同，它可能感覺熟悉而易處理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the number of digits in a telephone number.","zh":"這個片語描述電話號碼中的數字數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"over two years","meaning":"在兩年期間","examples":[{"en":"The participant completed hundreds of hours of testing over two years.","zh":"參加者在兩年期間完成數百小時測試。"},{"en":"Over two years means during a period lasting two years.","zh":"Over two years 指在長達兩年的期間內。"},{"en":"A student may improve pronunciation over two years of regular speaking practice.","zh":"學生可能透過兩年定期口語練習改善發音。"},{"en":"If training continues over two years, small gains can become major improvement.","zh":"如果訓練持續兩年，小進步可以變成重大改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes progress across a long period.","zh":"這個片語描述長時間內的進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete 250 hours of testing","meaning":"完成二百五十小時測試","examples":[{"en":"The student completed 250 hours of memory testing.","zh":"該學生完成了二百五十小時記憶測試。"},{"en":"To complete 250 hours of testing means to spend a total of 250 hours doing test sessions.","zh":"To complete 250 hours of testing 指總共花二百五十小時進行測試時段。"},{"en":"A language learner may complete many hours of listening practice before noticing real improvement.","zh":"語言學習者可能完成許多小時聆聽練習後，才注意到真正進步。"},{"en":"If someone completes hundreds of hours of testing, the result reflects serious training.","zh":"如果某人完成數百小時測試，結果反映認真訓練。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large amount of measured practice.","zh":"這個片語描述大量可量度的練習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"stretch something from…to…","meaning":"把……由……提升至……","examples":[{"en":"He stretched his digit span from seven to more than eighty.","zh":"他把數字記憶廣度由七個提升至超過八十個。"},{"en":"To stretch something from one level to another means to extend or increase it greatly.","zh":"To stretch something from one level to another 指大幅延伸或增加某事物。"},{"en":"A student may stretch her reading time from ten minutes to one hour a day.","zh":"學生可能把每日閱讀時間由十分鐘提升至一小時。"},{"en":"If training stretches an ability from low to high, practice has created major change.","zh":"如果訓練把能力由低提升至高，練習就造成重大改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes expansion from a starting point to a higher point.","zh":"這個片語描述從起點擴展到更高點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"more than eighty digits","meaning":"超過八十個數字","examples":[{"en":"After extensive practice, he could remember more than eighty digits.","zh":"經過大量練習後，他能記住超過八十個數字。"},{"en":"More than eighty digits means a sequence containing over eighty numerical characters.","zh":"More than eighty digits 指包含八十多個數字字符的序列。"},{"en":"Remembering more than eighty digits would be difficult without grouping or memory techniques.","zh":"如果沒有分組或記憶技巧，記住超過八十個數字會很困難。"},{"en":"If a person can recall more than eighty digits, their trained memory span is far beyond normal.","zh":"如果一個人能回想超過八十個數字，他受訓後的記憶廣度遠超正常水平。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very large number of digits to remember.","zh":"這個片語描述需要記住的非常大量數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"lead someone to believe that","meaning":"令某人相信","examples":[{"en":"The study led Ericsson to believe that superior memory can be trained.","zh":"這項研究令 Ericsson 相信優越記憶可以訓練出來。"},{"en":"To lead someone to believe that something is true means to make them reach that belief because of evidence or experience.","zh":"To lead someone to believe that something is true 指因證據或經驗而令某人形成該信念。"},{"en":"Repeated improvement may lead a teacher to believe that a new method is working.","zh":"反覆進步可能令老師相信新方法有效。"},{"en":"If an experiment changes a researcher’s view, the evidence has influenced their belief.","zh":"如果實驗改變研究人員的看法，證據就影響了他的信念。"},{"en":"This phrase connects evidence with a conclusion.","zh":"這個片語把證據與結論連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"innately superior memory","meaning":"天生優越的記憶力","examples":[{"en":"Ericsson questions whether innately superior memory exists.","zh":"Ericsson 質疑天生優越的記憶力是否存在。"},{"en":"Innately superior memory is memory that is naturally excellent from birth rather than developed through training.","zh":"Innately superior memory 是從出生起自然優秀，而不是透過訓練發展出來的記憶力。"},{"en":"A child may appear to have innately superior memory if they remember long stories without practice.","zh":"如果孩子不用練習也能記住長故事，他可能看似有天生優越的記憶力。"},{"en":"If exceptional memory is trained, the idea of innate superiority becomes less convincing.","zh":"如果非凡記憶是訓練出來的，天生優越這個想法就較不具說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts natural talent with learned skill.","zh":"這個片語把天賦與學來技能作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"not exist at all","meaning":"根本不存在","examples":[{"en":"He believes that innately superior memory may not exist at all.","zh":"他相信天生優越的記憶力可能根本不存在。"},{"en":"To not exist at all means to be completely absent or unreal.","zh":"To not exist at all 指完全不存在或並不真實。"},{"en":"A rumoured school rule may not exist at all if no teacher has ever announced it.","zh":"如果沒有老師曾宣布，傳聞中的校規可能根本不存在。"},{"en":"If natural memory genius does not exist at all, training becomes the main explanation.","zh":"如果天生記憶天才根本不存在，訓練就成為主要解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly denies the presence of something.","zh":"這個片語強烈否定某事物的存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"review original case studies","meaning":"審視原始個案研究","examples":[{"en":"Ericsson reviewed original case studies of exceptional memorisers.","zh":"Ericsson 審視記憶力超凡者的原始個案研究。"},{"en":"To review original case studies means to examine earlier detailed reports about real individuals or cases.","zh":"To review original case studies 指檢視早期關於真實個人或個案的詳細報告。"},{"en":"A medical student may review original case studies to understand a rare illness.","zh":"醫科學生可能審視原始個案研究，以理解罕見疾病。"},{"en":"If old cases are reviewed carefully, new explanations may appear.","zh":"如果舊個案被仔細重新審視，新的解釋可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes re-examining detailed evidence from previous research.","zh":"這個片語描述重新檢查早前研究中的詳細證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"exceptional memorisers","meaning":"記憶力超凡的人","examples":[{"en":"Exceptional memorisers often rely on learned techniques.","zh":"記憶力超凡的人通常依靠學回來的技巧。"},{"en":"Exceptional memorisers are people who can remember unusually large amounts of information.","zh":"Exceptional memorisers 是能記住異常大量資料的人。"},{"en":"An exceptional memoriser may recall a long poem after only a short study period.","zh":"記憶力超凡的人可能在短時間學習後回想整首長詩。"},{"en":"If exceptional memorisers use techniques, their ability may be teachable.","zh":"如果記憶力超凡的人使用技巧，他們的能力可能可以被教授。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people with unusually strong memory performance.","zh":"這個片語描述記憶表現異常強的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"without realising it","meaning":"在沒有察覺的情況下","examples":[{"en":"Some people use memory techniques without realising it.","zh":"有些人在沒有察覺的情況下使用記憶技巧。"},{"en":"Without realising it means without being aware that one is doing something.","zh":"Without realising it 指沒有意識到自己正在做某事。"},{"en":"A student may organise notes by colour without realising it is helping memory.","zh":"學生可能用顏色整理筆記，卻沒有察覺這正在幫助記憶。"},{"en":"If people use a strategy unconsciously, they may not be able to explain why it works.","zh":"如果人們無意識地使用策略，他們可能無法解釋它為何有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an action done without conscious awareness.","zh":"這個片語描述在沒有自覺下完成的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"lots of practice","meaning":"大量練習","examples":[{"en":"Exceptional performance generally requires lots of practice.","zh":"非凡表現通常需要大量練習。"},{"en":"Lots of practice means a large amount of repeated training.","zh":"Lots of practice 指大量重複訓練。"},{"en":"A student needs lots of practice to speak English smoothly under pressure.","zh":"學生需要大量練習，才能在壓力下流暢說英文。"},{"en":"If practice is repeated often, skills become faster and more automatic.","zh":"如果練習經常重複，技能就會變得更快和更自動。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses effort and repetition.","zh":"這個片語強調努力和重複。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a single type of material","meaning":"單一類型的材料","examples":[{"en":"An exceptional memory may apply to only a single type of material.","zh":"非凡記憶可能只適用於單一類型的材料。"},{"en":"A single type of material means one specific kind of information, such as numbers, faces, or poems.","zh":"Single type of material 指一種特定資料，例如數字、面孔或詩。"},{"en":"A student may be excellent at remembering song lyrics but not dates or formulas.","zh":"學生可能很擅長記歌詞，但不擅長記日期或公式。"},{"en":"If a memory skill works only for one material type, it may depend on specialised practice.","zh":"如果記憶技能只適用於一種材料，它可能依賴專門練習。"},{"en":"This phrase limits ability to one category.","zh":"這個片語把能力限制於一個類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"memory tasks","meaning":"記憶任務","examples":[{"en":"Most people spend very little time practising unusual memory tasks.","zh":"大多數人很少花時間練習不尋常的記憶任務。"},{"en":"Memory tasks are activities designed to test or train remembering.","zh":"Memory tasks 是用來測試或訓練記憶的活動。"},{"en":"Matching names to faces is a common memory task in school ice-breaking games.","zh":"在學校破冰遊戲中，把姓名與面孔配對是常見記憶任務。"},{"en":"If memory tasks are practised repeatedly, performance can improve even without natural talent.","zh":"如果記憶任務被反覆練習，即使沒有天賦，表現也可以改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exercises involving recall or recognition.","zh":"這個片語描述涉及回想或識別的練習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be exceptional at","meaning":"在……方面表現非凡","examples":[{"en":"Many people could become exceptional at a task through practice.","zh":"許多人可以透過練習在某項任務方面表現非凡。"},{"en":"To be exceptional at something means to be unusually good at it.","zh":"To be exceptional at something 指在某事上異常出色。"},{"en":"A student may become exceptional at dictation after months of careful listening practice.","zh":"學生經過數月仔細聆聽練習後，可能在默書方面表現非凡。"},{"en":"If someone practises one task deeply, they may become excellent in that narrow area.","zh":"如果某人深入練習一項任務，他可能在該狹窄範疇變得優秀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes outstanding skill in a specific task.","zh":"這個片語描述特定任務中的傑出技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"across a number of tasks","meaning":"在多項任務中","examples":[{"en":"It is rare for one person to be exceptional across a number of tasks.","zh":"一個人在多項任務中都表現非凡是罕見的。"},{"en":"Across a number of tasks means in several different activities or test types.","zh":"Across a number of tasks 指在幾種不同活動或測試類型中。"},{"en":"A student may be strong across a number of tasks, including speaking, writing, and reading.","zh":"學生可能在多項任務中都表現強，包括口語、寫作和閱讀。"},{"en":"If someone performs well across many tasks, their ability is broad rather than specialised.","zh":"如果某人在許多任務中都表現好，他的能力就是廣泛而非專門化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes performance over multiple areas.","zh":"這個片語描述跨越多個範疇的表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"compelling evidence","meaning":"有說服力的證據","examples":[{"en":"Ericsson sees no compelling evidence for naturally universal memory talent.","zh":"Ericsson 看不到支持天生全面記憶天賦的有說服力證據。"},{"en":"Compelling evidence is strong evidence that makes an argument hard to reject.","zh":"Compelling evidence 是強而有力、令人難以否定某論點的證據。"},{"en":"Clear test results from many students can be compelling evidence that a teaching method works.","zh":"來自許多學生的清楚測驗結果，可以成為某教學方法有效的有說服力證據。"},{"en":"If evidence is not compelling, researchers should avoid making strong claims.","zh":"如果證據不夠有說服力，研究人員應避免作出強烈主張。"},{"en":"This phrase describes proof that is persuasive and powerful.","zh":"這個片語描述具說服力而強大的證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"which paragraph contains","meaning":"哪一段包含","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which paragraph contains each piece of information.","zh":"學生識別哪一段包含每項資料。"},{"en":"Which paragraph contains means which section of the passage includes the required detail.","zh":"Which paragraph contains 指文章哪一部分包括所需細節。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may find which paragraph contains a scientific experiment.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能找出哪一段包含科學實驗。"},{"en":"If two paragraphs discuss memory, students should choose the one with the exact information.","zh":"如果兩段都討論記憶，學生應選擇含有準確資料的一段。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in paragraph-matching questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於段落配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the following information","meaning":"以下資料","examples":[{"en":"The questions ask students to locate the following information.","zh":"題目要求學生找出以下資料。"},{"en":"The following information means the details listed after the instruction.","zh":"The following information 指指示後列出的細節。"},{"en":"Students should read the following information before scanning the passage.","zh":"學生應在掃讀文章前先閱讀以下資料。"},{"en":"If the wording is paraphrased, students must match the meaning instead of only the exact words.","zh":"如果措辭被改寫，學生必須配對意思，而不只是找完全相同字眼。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the items students need to find.","zh":"這個片語引出學生需要尋找的項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"exceptional memory skills","meaning":"非凡記憶技巧","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains the development of exceptional memory skills.","zh":"文章解釋非凡記憶技巧的發展。"},{"en":"Exceptional memory skills are unusually strong abilities to store and recall information.","zh":"Exceptional memory skills 是儲存和回想資料的異常強大能力。"},{"en":"A student with exceptional memory skills may remember long vocabulary lists accurately.","zh":"有非凡記憶技巧的學生可能準確記住長詞彙表。"},{"en":"If such skills are trained, more learners can improve through method and practice.","zh":"如果這些技巧可以被訓練，更多學習者就能透過方法和練習進步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very high-level memory ability.","zh":"這個片語描述高水平記憶能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be significant in academic settings","meaning":"在學術環境中具有重要性","examples":[{"en":"Memory techniques were once significant in academic settings.","zh":"記憶技巧曾經在學術環境中具有重要性。"},{"en":"To be significant in academic settings means to be important in schools, universities, or scholarly learning.","zh":"To be significant in academic settings 指在學校、大學或學術學習中重要。"},{"en":"Essay structure is significant in academic settings because it helps readers follow arguments.","zh":"文章結構在學術環境中具有重要性，因為它幫助讀者跟隨論點。"},{"en":"If books are rare, memory becomes more significant in education.","zh":"如果書本稀少，記憶在教育中就變得更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes importance within formal learning environments.","zh":"這個片語描述在正式學習環境中的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"mention of a competition","meaning":"提及一項比賽","examples":[{"en":"One paragraph contains mention of a long-running memory competition.","zh":"其中一段提及一項舉辦多年的記憶比賽。"},{"en":"Mention of a competition means a short reference to a contest or event.","zh":"Mention of a competition 指簡短提到一場比賽或活動。"},{"en":"A reading passage may include mention of a science fair without describing every project.","zh":"閱讀文章可能提及科學展，但不描述每個項目。"},{"en":"If a question asks for mention of something, students only need to locate where it appears.","zh":"如果題目要求找出提及某事的位置，學生只需要定位它出現的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reference, not a full explanation.","zh":"這個片語描述提及，而不是完整解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"held over many years","meaning":"舉辦多年","examples":[{"en":"The World Memory Championships has been held over many years.","zh":"世界記憶錦標賽已舉辦多年。"},{"en":"Held over many years means organised repeatedly across a long period.","zh":"Held over many years 指在長時間中反覆舉辦。"},{"en":"A school music festival may be held over many years and become a tradition.","zh":"學校音樂節可能舉辦多年，並成為傳統。"},{"en":"If an event continues for many years, it may gain records, famous competitors, and history.","zh":"如果活動持續多年，它可能累積紀錄、著名參賽者和歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-term continuation of an event.","zh":"這個片語描述活動的長期延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a demonstration of","meaning":"對……的示範","examples":[{"en":"The passage includes a demonstration of an unusual memory technique.","zh":"文章包括對一種不尋常記憶技巧的示範。"},{"en":"A demonstration of something is a clear showing of how it works.","zh":"Demonstration of something 是清楚展示某事如何運作。"},{"en":"A teacher may give a demonstration of how to organise notes before asking students to try.","zh":"老師可能先示範如何整理筆記，再要求學生嘗試。"},{"en":"If a method is demonstrated, learners can see the steps rather than only hear theory.","zh":"如果方法被示範，學習者可以看見步驟，而不只是聽理論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical showing.","zh":"這個片語描述實際展示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"perform an unusual recall task","meaning":"完成不尋常的回想任務","examples":[{"en":"Cooke performs an unusual recall task involving playing cards.","zh":"Cooke 完成一項涉及啤牌的不尋常回想任務。"},{"en":"To perform an unusual recall task means to complete a memory challenge that is not part of everyday life.","zh":"To perform an unusual recall task 指完成一項不屬於日常生活的記憶挑戰。"},{"en":"A student may perform an unusual recall task by remembering fifty random colours in order.","zh":"學生可能透過按次序記住五十種隨機顏色，完成不尋常的回想任務。"},{"en":"If a task is unusual, ordinary memory habits may not be enough.","zh":"如果任務不尋常，普通記憶習慣可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a special challenge in remembering information.","zh":"這個片語描述記住資料方面的特殊挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a belief that","meaning":"一種認為……的看法","examples":[{"en":"One researcher expresses a belief that memory can be improved through practice.","zh":"一名研究人員表達一種認為記憶可以透過練習改善的看法。"},{"en":"A belief that something is true is an opinion or view held by someone.","zh":"Belief that something is true 是某人持有的意見或觀點。"},{"en":"A teacher may have a belief that weak writers can improve with clear feedback.","zh":"老師可能有一種看法，認為寫作弱的學生可以透過清晰回饋進步。"},{"en":"If evidence supports a belief, it becomes more persuasive.","zh":"如果證據支持某看法，它就變得更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what someone thinks is true.","zh":"這個片語引出某人認為真實的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be gained through practice","meaning":"可透過練習獲得","examples":[{"en":"Extraordinary memory skills may be gained through enough practice.","zh":"非凡記憶技巧可能可透過足夠練習獲得。"},{"en":"To be gained through practice means to be developed by repeated training rather than received naturally.","zh":"To be gained through practice 指透過反覆訓練發展出來，而不是天生得到。"},{"en":"Confidence in speaking can be gained through practice with real questions.","zh":"口語信心可以透過練習真實問題獲得。"},{"en":"If a skill is gained through practice, beginners should focus on method and repetition.","zh":"如果技能可透過練習獲得，初學者應專注方法和重複。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ability built over time.","zh":"這個片語描述能力隨時間建立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"a rare ability","meaning":"罕見能力","examples":[{"en":"Synesthesia is a rare ability that may support exceptional memory.","zh":"聯覺是一種可能支持非凡記憶的罕見能力。"},{"en":"A rare ability is an uncommon skill or mental feature found in few people.","zh":"Rare ability 是少數人擁有的不常見技能或心理特徵。"},{"en":"Perfect pitch is a rare ability that helps some musicians identify notes instantly.","zh":"絕對音感是一種罕見能力，幫助一些音樂人即時辨認音符。"},{"en":"If a rare ability adds extra memory cues, it may help performance.","zh":"如果罕見能力加入額外記憶線索，它可能幫助表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unusual capacity.","zh":"這個片語描述不尋常能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"aid exceptional memory","meaning":"幫助形成非凡記憶力","examples":[{"en":"Additional sensory associations may aid exceptional memory.","zh":"額外感官聯想可能幫助形成非凡記憶力。"},{"en":"To aid exceptional memory means to help unusually strong remembering happen.","zh":"To aid exceptional memory 指幫助異常強大的記憶發生。"},{"en":"Colour, sound, and rhythm can aid memory when students learn vocabulary.","zh":"學生學詞彙時，顏色、聲音和節奏可以幫助記憶。"},{"en":"If extra senses are involved, the brain may have more routes to recall information.","zh":"如果涉及額外感官，大腦可能有更多路徑回想資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes helping high-level memory performance.","zh":"這個片語描述幫助高水平記憶表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"complete the following summary","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the following summary using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the following summary means to fill in missing words in the summary that comes next.","zh":"To complete the following summary 指填補接下來摘要中的缺失字詞。"},{"en":"In a reading exam, students should read the following summary before searching for answers.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生應先閱讀以下摘要，再尋找答案。"},{"en":"If the summary paraphrases the passage, meaning matters more than identical wording.","zh":"如果摘要改寫文章，意思比完全相同字眼更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction for gap-filling questions.","zh":"這個片語是填空題常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"investigate and explain","meaning":"研究並解釋","examples":[{"en":"Researchers investigated and explained the use of visual imagery.","zh":"研究人員研究並解釋視覺意象的運用。"},{"en":"To investigate and explain something means to study it carefully and then make it understandable.","zh":"To investigate and explain something 指仔細研究某事，然後令它變得可理解。"},{"en":"A teacher may investigate and explain why students keep misusing a tense.","zh":"老師可能研究並解釋為何學生不斷誤用某時態。"},{"en":"If researchers investigate a technique, they can explain how and why it works.","zh":"如果研究人員研究一種技巧，他們就可以解釋它如何及為何有效。"},{"en":"This phrase combines research with clear explanation.","zh":"這個片語結合研究和清晰解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the use of visual imagery","meaning":"視覺意象的運用","examples":[{"en":"The experiment examined the use of visual imagery in memorising numbers.","zh":"該實驗檢視在記住數字時視覺意象的運用。"},{"en":"The use of visual imagery means using mental pictures to help understand or remember something.","zh":"Use of visual imagery 指使用心理圖像來幫助理解或記住某事。"},{"en":"A student may use visual imagery by imagining a tiny king to remember the word “monarch”.","zh":"學生可能想像一個細小國王，以運用視覺意象記住 “monarch” 一詞。"},{"en":"If abstract numbers become pictures, they may be easier to recall.","zh":"如果抽象數字變成圖像，它們可能更容易回想。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a memory strategy based on images.","zh":"這個片語描述以影像為基礎的記憶策略。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"remember numbers","meaning":"記住數字","examples":[{"en":"Competitive memorisers use spatial techniques to remember numbers.","zh":"競技記憶選手使用空間技巧來記住數字。"},{"en":"To remember numbers means to keep numerical information in memory and recall it correctly.","zh":"To remember numbers 指把數字資料保存在記憶中並正確回想。"},{"en":"A student may remember numbers better by grouping a long code into smaller chunks.","zh":"學生可能透過把長密碼分成較小組來更好地記住數字。"},{"en":"If numbers have no meaning, linking them to images can make them easier to remember.","zh":"如果數字沒有意思，把它們與影像連接可以令它們更容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recalling numerical information.","zh":"這個片語描述回想數字資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"speak a string of odd words","meaning":"說出一連串奇怪詞語","examples":[{"en":"Cooke spoke a string of odd words while demonstrating his technique.","zh":"Cooke 在示範技巧時說出一連串奇怪詞語。"},{"en":"To speak a string of odd words means to say a sequence of strange or unexpected words.","zh":"To speak a string of odd words 指說出一連串奇怪或出乎意料的詞語。"},{"en":"A student may speak a string of odd words when using a silly rhyme to remember a list.","zh":"學生使用荒謬押韻句記住清單時，可能說出一連串奇怪詞語。"},{"en":"If odd words are linked to images, they may help recall hidden information.","zh":"如果奇怪詞語與影像連接，它們可能幫助回想隱藏資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes saying unusual words in sequence.","zh":"這個片語描述按次序說出不尋常詞語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"hold up a card","meaning":"舉起一張牌","examples":[{"en":"He spoke the words when he held up the seven of spades.","zh":"他舉起黑桃七時說出那些詞語。"},{"en":"To hold up a card means to raise a card so others can see it.","zh":"To hold up a card 指把一張牌舉起，讓其他人看見。"},{"en":"A teacher may hold up a card with a vocabulary word for the class to read.","zh":"老師可能舉起一張有詞彙的卡，讓全班閱讀。"},{"en":"If someone holds up a card during a demonstration, the card becomes part of the explanation.","zh":"如果某人在示範時舉起一張牌，該牌就成為解釋的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes showing a card visibly.","zh":"這個片語描述可見地展示一張牌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"encode something as","meaning":"把……編碼成","examples":[{"en":"Cooke encodes each card as part of an imagined scene.","zh":"Cooke 把每張牌編碼成想像場景的一部分。"},{"en":"To encode something as something else means to turn it into a different form for storage or understanding.","zh":"To encode something as something else 指把某事轉化成另一種形式，以便儲存或理解。"},{"en":"A student may encode a formula as a short song to remember it.","zh":"學生可能把公式編碼成一首短歌來記住它。"},{"en":"If cards are encoded as images, they can be stored through visual memory.","zh":"如果啤牌被編碼成影像，它們就可以透過視覺記憶儲存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing information into a memorable form.","zh":"這個片語描述把資料轉化成易記形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"in groups of","meaning":"以……為一組","examples":[{"en":"He memorises playing cards in groups of three.","zh":"他以三張為一組記住啤牌。"},{"en":"In groups of a number means arranged or handled in sets of that size.","zh":"In groups of a number 指按該數量排列或處理成一組。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to practise vocabulary in groups of five.","zh":"老師可能要求學生以五個為一組練習詞彙。"},{"en":"If information is learned in groups, it may feel less overwhelming.","zh":"如果資料以小組方式學習，它可能感覺不那麼令人負擔過重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dividing items into fixed sets.","zh":"這個片語描述把項目分成固定組別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"when it is time to recall","meaning":"到需要回想時","examples":[{"en":"When it is time to recall the cards, he mentally follows his route.","zh":"到需要回想啤牌時，他會在腦中跟隨自己的路線。"},{"en":"When it is time to recall means when the person needs to bring stored information back to mind.","zh":"When it is time to recall 指當某人需要把已儲存資料帶回腦中時。"},{"en":"When it is time to recall examples in an exam, students benefit from clear organisation.","zh":"到考試中需要回想例子時，學生會受惠於清晰組織。"},{"en":"If information was stored along a route, recall can follow the same route.","zh":"如果資料沿着路線儲存，回想就可以跟隨同一路線。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the moment of memory retrieval.","zh":"這個片語標示記憶提取的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"translate imagined scenes into","meaning":"把想像場景轉換成……","examples":[{"en":"Cooke translates imagined scenes into playing cards.","zh":"Cooke 把想像場景轉換成啤牌。"},{"en":"To translate imagined scenes into something means to convert mental pictures back into the information they represent.","zh":"To translate imagined scenes into something 指把心理圖像轉回它們代表的資料。"},{"en":"A student may translate imagined scenes into essay points during a test.","zh":"學生可能在測驗中把想像場景轉換成作文重點。"},{"en":"If the imagined scenes are clear, the original information can be recovered accurately.","zh":"如果想像場景清楚，原本資料就能準確恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes decoding mental images back into data.","zh":"這個片語描述把心理影像解碼回資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be traced to","meaning":"可追溯至","examples":[{"en":"The superior-memory technique can be traced to ancient Greece.","zh":"這種優越記憶技巧可追溯至古希臘。"},{"en":"To be traced to a place or time means to have an origin that can be followed back there.","zh":"To be traced to a place or time 指其起源可以追查回某地或某時期。"},{"en":"A family recipe may be traced to a village where grandparents once lived.","zh":"家庭食譜可能可追溯至祖父母曾居住的村莊。"},{"en":"If a method can be traced to ancient Greece, it has a very long history.","zh":"如果一種方法可追溯至古希臘，它就有非常悠久歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finding the historical source of something.","zh":"這個片語描述尋找某事物的歷史來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"become a major subject","meaning":"成為主要科目","examples":[{"en":"The art of memory became a major subject in classical education.","zh":"記憶術成為古典教育中的主要科目。"},{"en":"To become a major subject means to become an important area of study.","zh":"To become a major subject 指成為重要學習範疇。"},{"en":"Computer literacy has become a major subject in many modern schools.","zh":"電腦素養已成為許多現代學校的主要科目。"},{"en":"If a skill becomes a major subject, schools devote time and teachers to it.","zh":"如果某技能成為主要科目，學校就會投入時間和教師。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a topic gaining educational importance.","zh":"這個片語描述某題目獲得教育重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"choose two correct letters","meaning":"選出兩個正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose two correct letters from the answer options.","zh":"學生從答案選項中選出兩個正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose two correct letters means to select two answer choices that are right.","zh":"To choose two correct letters 指選擇兩個正確答案選項。"},{"en":"In a multiple-answer question, students may need to choose two correct letters instead of one.","zh":"在多選題中，學生可能需要選出兩個正確字母，而不是一個。"},{"en":"If only one answer is chosen when two are required, the response may be incomplete.","zh":"如果題目要求兩個答案但只選一個，回答可能不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"according to the passage","meaning":"根據文章","examples":[{"en":"Students select the activities included according to the passage.","zh":"學生根據文章選出包括在內的活動。"},{"en":"According to the passage means based only on what the text says.","zh":"According to the passage 指只根據文本所說內容。"},{"en":"According to the passage, students should not use outside knowledge to answer the question.","zh":"根據文章，學生不應使用外部知識作答。"},{"en":"If an option sounds true but is not stated in the passage, it may still be wrong.","zh":"如果選項聽起來正確但文章沒有說，它仍可能是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds learners to rely on the text.","zh":"這個片語提醒學習者依據文本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be included in","meaning":"包括在……之內","examples":[{"en":"Several memory tasks were included in the championships.","zh":"幾項記憶任務包括在錦標賽之內。"},{"en":"To be included in something means to be part of it.","zh":"To be included in something 指成為某事物的一部分。"},{"en":"Speaking practice may be included in an English course if oral skills are important.","zh":"如果口語能力重要，英語課程可能包括口語練習。"},{"en":"If a task is included in a competition, contestants must prepare for it.","zh":"如果一項任務包括在比賽之內，參賽者必須準備它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being one element within a larger whole.","zh":"這個片語描述作為較大整體中的一個元素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"a long sequence of digits","meaning":"一長串數字","examples":[{"en":"Contestants memorised a long sequence of digits.","zh":"參賽者記住一長串數字。"},{"en":"A long sequence of digits is a lengthy ordered series of numbers.","zh":"Long sequence of digits 是一串很長且有次序的數字。"},{"en":"A bank code or serial number may contain a long sequence of digits that is hard to remember.","zh":"銀行編碼或序列號可能包含一長串難記的數字。"},{"en":"If digits must be recalled in order, one wrong digit can spoil the whole answer.","zh":"如果數字必須按次序回想，一個數字錯誤就可能破壞整個答案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a long ordered number string.","zh":"這個片語描述很長的有序數字串。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"recall people’s faces","meaning":"記起人們的面孔","examples":[{"en":"One option refers to recalling people’s faces.","zh":"其中一個選項提到記起人們的面孔。"},{"en":"To recall people’s faces means to remember what people look like after seeing them.","zh":"To recall people’s faces 指看過別人後記得他們的樣貌。"},{"en":"A new teacher may recall students’ faces before remembering all their names.","zh":"新老師可能先記起學生面孔，再記住所有姓名。"},{"en":"If faces are distinctive, they are usually easier to recall.","zh":"如果面孔有特色，通常更容易記起。"},{"en":"This phrase describes remembering visual features of people.","zh":"這個片語描述記住人的視覺特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"recite a long poem","meaning":"背誦一首長詩","examples":[{"en":"Contestants were required to recite a long poem.","zh":"參賽者被要求背誦一首長詩。"},{"en":"To recite a long poem means to say a lengthy poem aloud from memory.","zh":"To recite a long poem 指憑記憶大聲說出一首篇幅長的詩。"},{"en":"A student may recite a long poem during a speech festival after weeks of practice.","zh":"學生可能經過數星期練習後，在朗誦節背誦一首長詩。"},{"en":"If the poem is long, the speaker must remember both words and rhythm.","zh":"如果詩很長，朗誦者必須記住文字和節奏。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a demanding memorised oral performance.","zh":"這個片語描述要求很高的背誦口頭表演。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"match names with photographs","meaning":"把姓名與照片配對","examples":[{"en":"Contestants matched people’s names with their photographs.","zh":"參賽者把人們的姓名與照片配對。"},{"en":"To match names with photographs means to connect each person’s name to the correct picture.","zh":"To match names with photographs 指把每個人的姓名連接到正確照片。"},{"en":"A new class teacher may match names with photographs to learn students faster.","zh":"新班主任可能把姓名與照片配對，以更快認識學生。"},{"en":"If the name-photo link is weak, people may remember the face but forget the name.","zh":"如果姓名和照片的連結薄弱，人們可能記得面孔但忘記名字。"},{"en":"This phrase describes connecting verbal and visual information.","zh":"這個片語描述把文字和視覺資料連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"facial features","meaning":"面部特徵","examples":[{"en":"Photographs showed the individuals’ facial features.","zh":"照片顯示個別人士的面部特徵。"},{"en":"Facial features are parts of a person’s face, such as eyes, nose, mouth, and shape.","zh":"Facial features 是人的面部部分，例如眼睛、鼻、口和面形。"},{"en":"A police artist may ask a witness to describe facial features carefully.","zh":"警方畫像師可能要求目擊者仔細描述面部特徵。"},{"en":"If facial features are distinctive, a person may be easier to recognise.","zh":"如果面部特徵鮮明，一個人可能更容易被認出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible details of the face.","zh":"這個片語描述面孔上的可見細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"conduct an MRI experiment","meaning":"進行磁力共振實驗","examples":[{"en":"The psychologists conducted an MRI experiment with memory competitors.","zh":"心理學家與記憶參賽者進行磁力共振實驗。"},{"en":"To conduct an MRI experiment means to carry out a study using MRI brain scanning.","zh":"To conduct an MRI experiment 指使用磁力共振腦掃描進行研究。"},{"en":"Researchers may conduct an MRI experiment to see which brain areas respond to music.","zh":"研究人員可能進行磁力共振實驗，看看哪些腦區對音樂有反應。"},{"en":"If an MRI experiment is well designed, it can connect brain activity with behaviour.","zh":"如果磁力共振實驗設計良好，它可以把大腦活動與行為連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes running a brain-scanning research study.","zh":"這個片語描述進行腦掃描研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"differ from those of","meaning":"與……的有所不同","examples":[{"en":"The researchers investigated whether the champions’ brains differed from those of ordinary people.","zh":"研究人員調查冠軍的大腦是否與普通人的大腦有所不同。"},{"en":"To differ from those of another group means to be unlike the ones belonging to that group.","zh":"To differ from those of another group 指與屬於另一群體的那些事物不同。"},{"en":"The study habits of top students may differ from those of students who revise only at the last minute.","zh":"尖子學生的學習習慣可能與只在最後一刻溫習的學生有所不同。"},{"en":"If champions’ brains differ from ordinary people’s brains, researchers may look for structural or activity differences.","zh":"如果冠軍的大腦與普通人的大腦有所不同，研究人員可能尋找結構或活動差異。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one group’s features with another group’s features.","zh":"這個片語比較一群人的特徵與另一群人的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"ordinary people","meaning":"普通人","examples":[{"en":"The memory champions were compared with ordinary control subjects.","zh":"記憶冠軍與普通對照研究對象作比較。"},{"en":"Ordinary people are people without special status, training, or exceptional ability in the context being discussed.","zh":"Ordinary people 是在所討論語境中沒有特殊身份、訓練或非凡能力的人。"},{"en":"Ordinary people can often improve memory by using simple organisation and repetition.","zh":"普通人通常可以透過簡單組織和重複來改善記憶。"},{"en":"If champions outperform ordinary people only on trained tasks, practice may explain the difference.","zh":"如果冠軍只在受訓任務中勝過普通人，練習可能解釋差異。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts typical people with specialists or experts.","zh":"這個片語把一般人與專家或專門人士作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"differences in brain scans","meaning":"腦部掃描差異","examples":[{"en":"The experiment revealed differences in the participants’ brain scans.","zh":"實驗揭示參加者腦部掃描影像中的差異。"},{"en":"Differences in brain scans are visible or measured variations in brain images or activity patterns.","zh":"Differences in brain scans 是腦部影像或活動模式中可見或可量度的變化。"},{"en":"Doctors may look for differences in brain scans before and after treatment.","zh":"醫生可能比較治療前後的腦部掃描差異。"},{"en":"If scans differ between groups, researchers may ask what strategy or condition caused the difference.","zh":"如果不同組別的掃描有所不同，研究人員可能問是哪種策略或狀況造成差異。"},{"en":"This phrase describes measurable brain-image differences.","zh":"這個片語描述可量度的腦部影像差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"appear when","meaning":"在……時出現","examples":[{"en":"Different patterns appeared when contestants completed certain memory tasks.","zh":"當參賽者完成某些記憶任務時，不同模式出現。"},{"en":"Appear when means become visible or noticeable at the time something happens.","zh":"Appear when 指在某事發生時變得可見或可察覺。"},{"en":"Careless mistakes often appear when students rush through the final questions.","zh":"當學生匆忙完成最後幾題時，粗心錯誤常常出現。"},{"en":"If brain patterns appear during a task, the task may be linked to those brain activities.","zh":"如果大腦模式在任務期間出現，該任務可能與那些大腦活動有關。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a result with the time or condition that produces it.","zh":"這個片語把結果與產生它的時間或條件連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"perform much worse","meaning":"表現差得多","examples":[{"en":"The champions did not perform much worse on the unfamiliar visual task.","zh":"冠軍在不熟悉的視覺任務中並沒有表現差得多。"},{"en":"To perform much worse means to do far less well than another group or than before.","zh":"To perform much worse 指比另一組或比以前表現差很多。"},{"en":"A student may perform much worse in a listening test if the audio is unclear.","zh":"如果音訊不清楚，學生在聆聽測驗中可能表現差得多。"},{"en":"If champions do not perform worse, the unfamiliar task may not disadvantage them strongly.","zh":"如果冠軍沒有表現較差，不熟悉任務可能沒有大幅削弱他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large drop in performance.","zh":"這個片語描述表現大幅下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"activate more brain regions","meaning":"啟動更多大腦區域","examples":[{"en":"One option suggests that the champions activated more brain regions.","zh":"其中一個選項指出冠軍啟動更多大腦區域。"},{"en":"To activate more brain regions means to use a larger number of brain areas during a task.","zh":"To activate more brain regions 指在任務期間使用更多腦區。"},{"en":"Speaking a foreign language may activate more brain regions than simply reading silently.","zh":"說外語可能比單純默讀啟動更多大腦區域。"},{"en":"If more regions are activated, the task may involve several kinds of processing.","zh":"如果更多區域被啟動，該任務可能涉及幾種處理方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wider brain activity.","zh":"這個片語描述更廣泛的大腦活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"be involved in visual and spatial memory","meaning":"與視覺及空間記憶有關","examples":[{"en":"Some brain regions are involved in visual and spatial memory.","zh":"一些大腦區域與視覺及空間記憶有關。"},{"en":"To be involved in visual and spatial memory means to play a role in remembering images, places, and routes.","zh":"To be involved in visual and spatial memory 指在記住影像、地方和路線方面發揮作用。"},{"en":"A student uses visual and spatial memory when remembering a diagram and where each label appears.","zh":"學生記住圖表以及每個標籤的位置時，就是使用視覺及空間記憶。"},{"en":"If these brain regions are active, the person may be using pictures and locations to remember.","zh":"如果這些腦區活躍，當事人可能正在用圖像和位置來記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes brain participation in image-based and place-based memory.","zh":"這個片語描述大腦參與以影像和地方為基礎的記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 125 - Memory Decoding.pdf","sourcePage":24}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 126":[{"front":"Is Graffiti Art or Crime?","meaning":"塗鴉是藝術還是罪行？","examples":[{"en":"The passage considers whether graffiti should be regarded as art or crime.","zh":"文章思考塗鴉應被視為藝術還是罪行。"},{"en":"“Is graffiti art or crime?” asks whether graffiti should be valued as creative expression or punished as illegal damage.","zh":"“Is graffiti art or crime?” 問的是塗鴉應被珍視為創意表達，還是被懲罰為非法破壞。"},{"en":"A city may face this question when a beautiful mural appears on a wall without permission.","zh":"當一幅美麗壁畫未經許可出現在牆上，城市可能面對這個問題。"},{"en":"If the owner did not agree to it, even attractive graffiti can create legal and repair problems.","zh":"如果物主沒有同意，即使吸引的塗鴉也可以造成法律和維修問題。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a debate because graffiti can be visually impressive but still unauthorised.","zh":"這個短語引出爭議，因為塗鴉可以在視覺上令人欣賞，但仍可能未經授權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"derive from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"The term “graffiti” derives from the Italian word “graffito”.","zh":"“graffiti” 這個詞源自意大利語 “graffito”。"},{"en":"To derive from something means to come from it as an origin or source.","zh":"derive from 某物，指以它為起源或來源。"},{"en":"Many English words derive from Latin, French or Greek.","zh":"許多英文詞源自拉丁語、法語或希臘語。"},{"en":"Knowing where a word derives from can help students remember its meaning.","zh":"知道一個詞源自哪裏，可以幫助學生記住其意思。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used to explain the history or origin of a word, idea or practice.","zh":"這個短語常用來解釋詞語、想法或做法的歷史或來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"can be defined as","meaning":"可界定為……","examples":[{"en":"Graffiti can be defined as unauthorised marking or writing on a surface.","zh":"塗鴉可界定為在表面上未經授權作出的標記或文字。"},{"en":"Can be defined as means can be explained or described as a particular thing.","zh":"can be defined as 指可被解釋或描述為某種事物。"},{"en":"A “deadline” can be defined as the final time by which work must be finished.","zh":"“deadline” 可界定為工作必須完成的最後時間。"},{"en":"Clear definitions help students avoid confusing similar words.","zh":"清楚定義幫助學生避免混淆相似詞語。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when giving a formal meaning before discussing examples.","zh":"這個短語適合在討論例子前給出正式意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"uninvited marking or writing","meaning":"未經許可的標記或文字","examples":[{"en":"Graffiti consists of uninvited marking or writing on property.","zh":"塗鴉包括在財物上未經許可的標記或文字。"},{"en":"Uninvited marking or writing means words or marks put on something without the owner’s permission.","zh":"uninvited marking or writing 指未經物主同意而加上的文字或標記。"},{"en":"A student who writes on a classroom desk creates uninvited marking or writing.","zh":"學生在課室桌面寫字，就是造成未經許可的標記或文字。"},{"en":"Such writing can upset owners because they must spend time or money removing it.","zh":"這類文字會令物主不滿，因為他們要花時間或金錢清除。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the problem is not only the mark, but the lack of permission.","zh":"這個短語強調問題不只是標記本身，而是沒有許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be applied to","meaning":"被施加於……","examples":[{"en":"Graffiti may be scratched into or applied to many kinds of surface.","zh":"塗鴉可以被刻入或施加於許多種類的表面。"},{"en":"To be applied to a surface means to be put, spread or placed on it.","zh":"be applied to 某表面，指被放上、塗上或施加在該表面。"},{"en":"Paint can be applied to a wall with a brush or spray.","zh":"油漆可以用掃或噴霧施加於牆上。"},{"en":"If the wrong chemical is applied to old stone, it may damage the surface.","zh":"如果錯誤化學品被施加於舊石材上，可能會損害表面。"},{"en":"The phrase describes putting a material, mark or treatment onto something.","zh":"這個短語描述把物料、標記或處理方式加到某物上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"built structures","meaning":"建築構築物","examples":[{"en":"Graffiti is frequently found on built structures.","zh":"塗鴉經常出現在建築構築物上。"},{"en":"Built structures are human-made things such as buildings, bridges, walls and tunnels.","zh":"built structures 是人造的東西，例如建築物、橋樑、牆壁和隧道。"},{"en":"A railway station, a school wall and a public footbridge are built structures.","zh":"火車站、學校牆壁和公共行人天橋都是建築構築物。"},{"en":"Graffiti on built structures may make an area look neglected.","zh":"建築構築物上的塗鴉可能令地區看起來被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts human-made surfaces with natural features like rocks or cliffs.","zh":"這個短語把人造表面與岩石或峭壁等自然地貌作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"natural features","meaning":"自然地貌","examples":[{"en":"Graffiti may also be applied to natural features such as rocks.","zh":"塗鴉也可能被施加於岩石等自然地貌。"},{"en":"Natural features are parts of the environment not made by people, such as rocks, trees, cliffs and caves.","zh":"natural features 是非人造的環境部分，例如岩石、樹木、峭壁和洞穴。"},{"en":"A visitor who scratches words onto a rock damages a natural feature.","zh":"訪客把文字刻在石上，就是損害自然地貌。"},{"en":"Marking natural features can harm scenery and may be difficult to repair.","zh":"在自然地貌上作標記可以破壞景觀，而且可能難以修復。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to nature-based surfaces rather than buildings.","zh":"這個短語指自然表面，而不是建築物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"not a new phenomenon","meaning":"並非新現象","examples":[{"en":"Graffiti is not a new phenomenon.","zh":"塗鴉並非新現象。"},{"en":"Not a new phenomenon means something has existed for a long time, not only recently.","zh":"not a new phenomenon 指某事已存在很久，並不是近年才有。"},{"en":"Complaints about noisy neighbours are not a new phenomenon in crowded cities.","zh":"在擠迫城市中，投訴鄰居嘈吵並非新現象。"},{"en":"If something is not new, history may help us understand why it continues.","zh":"如果某事並不新，歷史可能幫助我們理解它為何持續。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to correct the idea that a problem or practice is purely modern.","zh":"這個短語用來糾正某問題或做法純粹現代才有的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ancient structures","meaning":"古代建築","examples":[{"en":"Examples of graffiti can be found on ancient structures.","zh":"在古代建築上可以找到塗鴉例子。"},{"en":"Ancient structures are very old buildings, walls or monuments from earlier civilisations.","zh":"ancient structures 是來自早期文明的非常古老建築、牆壁或紀念物。"},{"en":"Tourists may visit ancient structures such as temples, city walls or tombs.","zh":"遊客可能參觀寺廟、城牆或陵墓等古代建築。"},{"en":"Damage to ancient structures is serious because they cannot easily be replaced.","zh":"對古代建築造成損害很嚴重，因為它們不容易被取代。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to historical physical remains built long ago.","zh":"這個短語指很久以前建造的歷史實體遺存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"predate the Greeks and Romans","meaning":"早於古希臘及古羅馬時期","examples":[{"en":"Some examples of graffiti predate the Greeks and Romans.","zh":"有些塗鴉例子早於古希臘及古羅馬時期。"},{"en":"To predate the Greeks and Romans means to exist before ancient Greek and Roman civilisation.","zh":"predate the Greeks and Romans 指在古希臘和古羅馬文明之前已存在。"},{"en":"Some tools and cave paintings predate written history.","zh":"有些工具和洞穴畫早於有文字記載的歷史。"},{"en":"If an object predates a famous period, it may be older than many people expect.","zh":"如果某物早於著名時期，它可能比許多人預期更古老。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to show that something is extremely old.","zh":"這個短語用來顯示某物極其古老。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in such circumstances","meaning":"在這種情況下","examples":[{"en":"In such circumstances, graffiti can have considerable historical value.","zh":"在這種情況下，塗鴉可以有相當大的歷史價值。"},{"en":"In such circumstances means in that particular situation or under those conditions.","zh":"in such circumstances 指在該特定情況或條件下。"},{"en":"If a student is sick on exam day, in such circumstances the school may arrange another assessment.","zh":"如果學生考試當日生病，在這種情況下學校可能安排另一次評估。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show that a judgement depends on context.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示判斷取決於語境。"},{"en":"It is useful when the same thing may be viewed differently in different situations.","zh":"當同一件事在不同情況下可有不同看法時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"acquire significance","meaning":"具有……意義；價值","examples":[{"en":"Ancient graffiti has acquired historical and archaeological significance.","zh":"古代塗鴉已具有歷史及考古價值。"},{"en":"To acquire significance means to gain importance or value over time or in a particular context.","zh":"acquire significance 指隨時間或在特定語境中獲得重要性或價值。"},{"en":"An old family letter may acquire significance when historians study life in that period.","zh":"當歷史學家研究某時期生活時，一封舊家書可能具有意義。"},{"en":"Objects may become important because they reveal details that official records ignore.","zh":"物件可能因揭示官方記錄忽略的細節而變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something becoming meaningful or valuable.","zh":"這個短語描述某事變得有意義或有價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"historical and archaeological significance","meaning":"歷史及考古價值","examples":[{"en":"Ancient graffiti may have invaluable historical and archaeological significance.","zh":"古代塗鴉可能有無價的歷史及考古價值。"},{"en":"Historical and archaeological significance means value for understanding the past and material remains of earlier societies.","zh":"historical and archaeological significance 指對理解過去和早期社會實物遺存有價值。"},{"en":"A broken pot may have historical and archaeological significance if it shows how people cooked.","zh":"如果破陶器顯示人們如何煮食，它可能有歷史及考古價值。"},{"en":"Such significance can help museums, researchers and communities understand earlier lives.","zh":"這種價值可以幫助博物館、研究人員和社區理解早期生活。"},{"en":"The phrase describes value for both history and archaeology.","zh":"這個短語描述對歷史和考古學均有價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"provide a social history of","meaning":"提供……的社會史資料","examples":[{"en":"Graffiti can provide a social history of life during an earlier period.","zh":"塗鴉可以提供較早時期生活的社會史資料。"},{"en":"To provide a social history of something means to show how ordinary people lived, thought or behaved in the past.","zh":"provide a social history of 某事，指顯示過去普通人如何生活、思考或行動。"},{"en":"Old shop signs can provide a social history of what people bought and sold.","zh":"舊商店招牌可以提供人們買賣甚麼的社會史資料。"},{"en":"Informal records may reveal voices that official documents leave out.","zh":"非正式記錄可能揭示官方文件遺漏的聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence about everyday society, not only kings or wars.","zh":"這個短語描述關於日常社會的證據，而不只是君王或戰爭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"become pervasive","meaning":"變得非常普遍","examples":[{"en":"Modern graffiti has become pervasive in many urban areas.","zh":"現代塗鴉在許多城市地區已變得非常普遍。"},{"en":"To become pervasive means to spread widely and appear in many places.","zh":"become pervasive 指廣泛擴散並出現在許多地方。"},{"en":"Smartphone use has become pervasive in schools, transport and family life.","zh":"智能手機使用在學校、交通和家庭生活中已變得非常普遍。"},{"en":"When something becomes pervasive, people may begin to see it as normal even if it causes problems.","zh":"當某事變得非常普遍，人們即使它造成問題，也可能開始視之為正常。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses widespread presence.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as a result of","meaning":"由於……","examples":[{"en":"Graffiti has spread partly as a result of cheap marking materials.","zh":"塗鴉擴散的部分原因是由於廉價標記材料。"},{"en":"As a result of means because of something.","zh":"as a result of 指由於某事。"},{"en":"A shop may close early as a result of staff illness.","zh":"商店可能由於員工生病而提早關門。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause to a later effect.","zh":"這個短語把原因與之後的結果連起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining why a situation has changed.","zh":"它適合用於解釋情況為何改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the availability of","meaning":"……的普及；容易取得","examples":[{"en":"The problem has increased because of the availability of cheap paints and pens.","zh":"由於廉價油漆和筆容易取得，問題有所增加。"},{"en":"The availability of something means how easy it is to get or use it.","zh":"availability of 某物，指它有多容易取得或使用。"},{"en":"The availability of online lessons helps students who live far from tutorial centres.","zh":"網上課程的普及幫助住得離補習中心很遠的學生。"},{"en":"When tools become cheap and easy to obtain, more people can use them.","zh":"當工具變得便宜且容易取得，更多人就能使用它們。"},{"en":"The phrase often explains why a practice becomes more common.","zh":"這個短語常用來解釋某做法為何變得更常見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"means of mark-making","meaning":"製作標記的方法","examples":[{"en":"Spray paint provides a cheap and quick means of mark-making.","zh":"噴漆提供一種廉價而快速的製作標記方法。"},{"en":"A means of mark-making is a method or tool used to leave marks on a surface.","zh":"means of mark-making 是用來在表面留下標記的方法或工具。"},{"en":"Chalk is a simple means of mark-making on a blackboard or pavement.","zh":"粉筆是在黑板或行人路上製作標記的簡單方法。"},{"en":"Easy mark-making tools can make graffiti quicker to create and harder to prevent.","zh":"容易使用的標記工具可以令塗鴉更快出現，也更難預防。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the method used to create visible marks.","zh":"這個短語指製作可見標記所用的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be considered a priority","meaning":"被視為優先事項","examples":[{"en":"Rapid graffiti removal is usually considered a priority.","zh":"快速清除塗鴉通常被視為優先事項。"},{"en":"To be considered a priority means to be regarded as something that should be dealt with first.","zh":"be considered a priority 指被認為應先處理。"},{"en":"In a hospital, serious injuries are considered a priority over minor cuts.","zh":"在醫院，嚴重傷勢會比小割傷被視為優先事項。"},{"en":"If graffiti is left for too long, more graffiti may appear, so quick removal becomes important.","zh":"如果塗鴉被放置太久，更多塗鴉可能出現，因此快速清除變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one task is treated as more urgent than others.","zh":"這個短語顯示某任務被視為比其他事情更迫切。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"remove something as quickly as possible","meaning":"盡快清除……","examples":[{"en":"Building owners are advised to remove graffiti as quickly as possible.","zh":"建築物業主被建議盡快清除塗鴉。"},{"en":"To remove something as quickly as possible means to take it away with the least delay.","zh":"remove something as quickly as possible 指以最少延誤把某物清除。"},{"en":"A parent should remove broken glass as quickly as possible to keep children safe.","zh":"家長應盡快清除碎玻璃，以保障兒童安全。"},{"en":"Quick removal can stop a small problem from becoming larger.","zh":"快速清除可以防止小問題變得更大。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses urgency in getting rid of something unwanted.","zh":"這個短語強調緊急移除不想要的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"prevent copycat graffiti","meaning":"防止仿效式塗鴉","examples":[{"en":"Rapid removal may prevent copycat graffiti.","zh":"快速清除可能防止仿效式塗鴉。"},{"en":"To prevent copycat graffiti means to stop others from copying the graffiti and making more of it.","zh":"prevent copycat graffiti 指阻止其他人模仿該塗鴉並製造更多塗鴉。"},{"en":"If one wall is covered quickly, students may be less likely to copy the idea on another wall.","zh":"如果一面牆很快被遮蓋，學生可能較不會在另一面牆模仿這個做法。"},{"en":"Visible graffiti can encourage imitation because it shows a place is not being protected.","zh":"可見塗鴉可以鼓勵模仿，因為它顯示某地方沒有被保護。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on stopping repeated behaviour caused by imitation.","zh":"這個短語重點在阻止由模仿引起的重複行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"once a clean surface is defaced","meaning":"一旦乾淨表面被污損","examples":[{"en":"Further graffiti may appear once a clean surface is defaced.","zh":"一旦乾淨表面被污損，更多塗鴉可能出現。"},{"en":"Once a clean surface is defaced means after a previously clean surface has been spoiled by marks.","zh":"once a clean surface is defaced 指原本乾淨的表面被標記破壞之後。"},{"en":"Once a clean classroom desk is defaced, other students may start writing on it too.","zh":"一旦乾淨課桌被污損，其他學生也可能開始在上面寫字。"},{"en":"A first mark can signal that people are allowed to damage the surface.","zh":"第一個標記可能發出訊號，令人覺得可以破壞該表面。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how one act of damage can invite more damage.","zh":"這個短語描述一次破壞如何引來更多破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"racist or otherwise offensive","meaning":"帶種族歧視或其他冒犯性","examples":[{"en":"Some graffiti may be racist or otherwise offensive.","zh":"有些塗鴉可能帶種族歧視或其他冒犯性。"},{"en":"Racist or otherwise offensive means insulting people because of race or in another hurtful way.","zh":"racist or otherwise offensive 指因種族或以其他傷害方式侮辱別人。"},{"en":"A message on a wall that attacks a group of people is racist or otherwise offensive.","zh":"牆上攻擊某群體的訊息就是帶種族歧視或其他冒犯性。"},{"en":"Offensive graffiti can make residents feel unsafe or unwelcome.","zh":"冒犯性塗鴉可以令居民感到不安全或不受歡迎。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both racist abuse and other insulting content.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋種族辱罵和其他侮辱性內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have a policy of","meaning":"訂有……政策","examples":[{"en":"Many councils have a policy of rapidly removing offensive graffiti.","zh":"許多地方議會訂有快速清除冒犯性塗鴉的政策。"},{"en":"To have a policy of doing something means to follow an official rule or regular approach.","zh":"have a policy of doing something 指遵循官方規則或固定處理方法。"},{"en":"A school may have a policy of contacting parents after repeated lateness.","zh":"學校可能訂有政策，在學生多次遲到後聯絡家長。"},{"en":"Policies make action faster because staff know what to do.","zh":"政策令行動更快，因為職員知道應做甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an organised rule, not a one-time decision.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的規則，而不是一次性決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"within an hour or two","meaning":"在一兩小時內","examples":[{"en":"Some offensive graffiti is removed within an hour or two.","zh":"有些冒犯性塗鴉會在一兩小時內被清除。"},{"en":"Within an hour or two means before one or two hours have passed.","zh":"within an hour or two 指在一至兩小時過去之前。"},{"en":"A school may repair a broken classroom lock within an hour or two if safety is at risk.","zh":"如果安全受威脅，學校可能在一兩小時內修好壞掉的課室門鎖。"},{"en":"Fast action can show the public that a problem is being taken seriously.","zh":"快速行動可以向公眾顯示問題受到認真處理。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a short time limit.","zh":"這個短語給出短時間限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be reported","meaning":"被舉報","examples":[{"en":"The council acts quickly after offensive graffiti is reported.","zh":"冒犯性塗鴉被舉報後，地方議會會迅速行動。"},{"en":"To be reported means to be officially told to a person or organisation responsible for dealing with it.","zh":"be reported 指被正式告知負責處理的人或機構。"},{"en":"A broken lift should be reported to building management.","zh":"壞掉的升降機應向大廈管理處舉報。"},{"en":"Problems cannot be dealt with quickly if no one reports them.","zh":"如果沒有人舉報，問題就不能迅速處理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formally bringing a problem to attention.","zh":"這個短語描述正式把問題提出來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"dry out over time","meaning":"隨時間乾固","examples":[{"en":"Paints, glues and inks dry out over time.","zh":"油漆、膠水和墨水會隨時間乾固。"},{"en":"To dry out over time means to gradually lose moisture and become dry.","zh":"dry out over time 指逐漸失去水分並變乾。"},{"en":"A marker pen may dry out over time if the cap is left open.","zh":"如果筆蓋沒有蓋好，箱頭筆可能會隨時間乾掉。"},{"en":"When paint dries out, it may stick more firmly to the surface.","zh":"當油漆乾固，它可能更牢固地黏在表面上。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a gradual drying process.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸乾燥的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"increasingly difficult to remove","meaning":"愈來愈難清除","examples":[{"en":"Dried paint becomes increasingly difficult to remove.","zh":"乾固油漆會變得愈來愈難清除。"},{"en":"Increasingly difficult to remove means harder and harder to take away as time passes or conditions change.","zh":"increasingly difficult to remove 指隨時間或情況改變而愈來愈難拿走或清理。"},{"en":"Old stains on a school uniform become increasingly difficult to remove if they are not washed quickly.","zh":"如果不快點清洗，校服上的舊污漬會愈來愈難清除。"},{"en":"Delay can make cleaning more expensive and less successful.","zh":"延誤可以令清潔更昂貴且較不成功。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that removal becomes harder over time.","zh":"這個短語強調清除會隨時間變得更困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be best dealt with","meaning":"最好加以處理","examples":[{"en":"Fresh graffiti is best dealt with as soon as possible.","zh":"新鮮塗鴉最好盡快加以處理。"},{"en":"To be best dealt with means to be handled most effectively in a particular way.","zh":"be best dealt with 指以某特定方式處理最有效。"},{"en":"A small leak is best dealt with before it damages the whole ceiling.","zh":"小漏水最好在損害整個天花板前加以處理。"},{"en":"Early action often prevents a simple problem from becoming serious.","zh":"早期行動常防止簡單問題變嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase recommends the most suitable way to handle something.","zh":"這個短語建議處理某事的最合適方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"more serious forms of vandalism","meaning":"更嚴重的蓄意破壞行為","examples":[{"en":"Graffiti can lead to more serious forms of vandalism.","zh":"塗鴉可以導致更嚴重的蓄意破壞行為。"},{"en":"More serious forms of vandalism are worse acts of deliberate damage to property.","zh":"more serious forms of vandalism 是更惡劣、有意破壞財物的行為。"},{"en":"Breaking windows, damaging seats and cutting wires are more serious forms of vandalism.","zh":"打破窗戶、破壞座椅和剪斷電線都是更嚴重的蓄意破壞行為。"},{"en":"If small acts are ignored, offenders may feel encouraged to do greater damage.","zh":"如果小破壞被忽視，犯事者可能覺得可進一步造成更大破壞。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stronger or more harmful property damage.","zh":"這個短語描述更強或更有害的財物破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"deterioration of an area","meaning":"地區環境惡化","examples":[{"en":"Persistent vandalism can contribute to the deterioration of an area.","zh":"持續蓄意破壞可以促成地區環境惡化。"},{"en":"Deterioration of an area means a place becoming worse in condition, appearance or safety.","zh":"deterioration of an area 指一個地方在狀況、外觀或安全方面變差。"},{"en":"A shopping street may suffer deterioration if lights are broken and rubbish is not collected.","zh":"如果街燈壞掉而垃圾沒人收集，購物街可能出現環境惡化。"},{"en":"When an area deteriorates, residents may feel less proud and visitors may stay away.","zh":"當地區惡化，居民可能較少自豪感，訪客也可能卻步。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual decline in a place.","zh":"這個短語描述地方逐漸衰退。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"contribute to social decline","meaning":"導致社會衰退","examples":[{"en":"Graffiti and vandalism may contribute to social decline.","zh":"塗鴉和蓄意破壞可能導致社會衰退。"},{"en":"To contribute to social decline means to help make a community weaker, less safe or less orderly.","zh":"contribute to social decline 指促使社區變得較弱、較不安全或較缺乏秩序。"},{"en":"Poor lighting, litter and repeated vandalism can contribute to social decline in a neighbourhood.","zh":"差劣照明、垃圾和反覆破壞可以導致社區社會衰退。"},{"en":"When public spaces look neglected, people may trust the area less.","zh":"當公共空間看起來被忽視，人們可能較不信任該地區。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one problem can be part of a wider community decline.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個問題可以是更廣泛社區衰退的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be regarded as an eyesore","meaning":"被視為礙眼之物","examples":[{"en":"Modern graffiti is often regarded as an eyesore.","zh":"現代塗鴉常被視為礙眼之物。"},{"en":"To be regarded as an eyesore means to be seen as something ugly or unpleasant to look at.","zh":"be regarded as an eyesore 指被看作醜陋或看起來令人不快的東西。"},{"en":"A pile of rubbish outside a school gate may be regarded as an eyesore.","zh":"學校門外一堆垃圾可能被視為礙眼之物。"},{"en":"Eyesores can make residents feel embarrassed about their neighbourhood.","zh":"礙眼之物可以令居民對自己的社區感到尷尬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes negative visual judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述負面的視覺判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a proposal to remove","meaning":"清除……的建議","examples":[{"en":"A proposal to remove graffiti from a historic building requires careful thought.","zh":"清除歷史建築上塗鴉的建議需要仔細思考。"},{"en":"A proposal to remove something is a suggested plan for taking it away.","zh":"proposal to remove 某物，是把它移除的建議計劃。"},{"en":"A school may discuss a proposal to remove old lockers from a corridor.","zh":"學校可能討論清除走廊舊儲物櫃的建議。"},{"en":"Removal proposals need care when the object or surface might be damaged.","zh":"當物件或表面可能受損，清除建議需要謹慎。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a suggested action, not an action already taken.","zh":"這個短語指建議中的行動，而不是已經採取的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sensitive historic surfaces","meaning":"容易受損的歷史建築表面","examples":[{"en":"Aggressive cleaning can damage sensitive historic surfaces.","zh":"強力清潔可以損害容易受損的歷史建築表面。"},{"en":"Sensitive historic surfaces are old surfaces that can easily be harmed because of their age, material or historical value.","zh":"sensitive historic surfaces 是因年代、物料或歷史價值而容易受傷害的舊表面。"},{"en":"An ancient stone wall may have a sensitive historic surface that cannot handle strong chemicals.","zh":"古石牆可能有容易受損的歷史表面，不能承受強化學品。"},{"en":"If such surfaces are cleaned carelessly, original material may be lost forever.","zh":"如果這類表面被粗心清潔，原有物料可能永久失去。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses fragility and heritage value.","zh":"這個短語強調脆弱性和文化遺產價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be carefully considered","meaning":"應仔細考慮","examples":[{"en":"Any cleaning proposal should be carefully considered.","zh":"任何清潔建議都應仔細考慮。"},{"en":"To be carefully considered means to be thought about seriously before a decision is made.","zh":"be carefully considered 指在作決定前被認真思考。"},{"en":"A school trip to a difficult mountain should be carefully considered for safety reasons.","zh":"基於安全原因，前往困難山區的學校旅行應仔細考慮。"},{"en":"Careful consideration reduces the chance of expensive or dangerous mistakes.","zh":"仔細考慮可減少昂貴或危險錯誤的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the need for thoughtful decision-making.","zh":"這個短語強調需要深思熟慮地決策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be designed for","meaning":"為……而設計","examples":[{"en":"Some cleaning techniques are designed for stronger modern surfaces.","zh":"有些清潔技術是為較堅固的現代表面而設計。"},{"en":"To be designed for something means to be made or planned for that specific purpose or situation.","zh":"be designed for 某事，指為特定目的或情況而製造或規劃。"},{"en":"A child’s chair is designed for a smaller body, not for an adult.","zh":"兒童椅是為較小身體而設計，不是給成年人使用。"},{"en":"If a tool is used on the wrong surface, it may cause damage.","zh":"如果工具用在錯誤表面上，可能會造成損害。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the intended use of a method, product or object.","zh":"這個短語解釋方法、產品或物件的預定用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"robust or utilitarian surfaces","meaning":"堅固或純功能性表面","examples":[{"en":"Abrasive methods may be suitable only for robust or utilitarian surfaces.","zh":"磨蝕方法可能只適合堅固或純功能性表面。"},{"en":"Robust or utilitarian surfaces are strong or purely practical surfaces that can tolerate rough treatment better.","zh":"robust or utilitarian surfaces 是較堅固或純實用、較能承受粗暴處理的表面。"},{"en":"A concrete service wall is more robust and utilitarian than a painted historic doorway.","zh":"混凝土服務牆比上漆歷史門口更堅固和功能性。"},{"en":"Rough cleaning methods may be acceptable on strong surfaces but dangerous on delicate ones.","zh":"粗糙清潔方法在堅固表面上可能可接受，但在脆弱表面上很危險。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts practical durability with fragile appearance or heritage value.","zh":"這個短語對比實用耐用性與脆弱外觀或文化遺產價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"result in considerable damage","meaning":"造成嚴重損害","examples":[{"en":"The wrong cleaning method may result in considerable damage.","zh":"錯誤清潔方法可能造成嚴重損害。"},{"en":"To result in considerable damage means to cause serious harm or loss.","zh":"result in considerable damage 指造成嚴重傷害或損失。"},{"en":"Using bleach on the wrong fabric may result in considerable damage to school uniforms.","zh":"在錯誤布料上使用漂白水，可能對校服造成嚴重損害。"},{"en":"A poor decision can make a small problem much more expensive to fix.","zh":"差劣決定可以令小問題變得更昂貴才可修復。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that an action may have harmful consequences.","zh":"這個短語提醒某行動可能有有害後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the event of","meaning":"如果發生……","examples":[{"en":"In the event of a graffiti incident, the building owner should record the damage.","zh":"如果發生塗鴉事件，建築物業主應記錄損害。"},{"en":"In the event of means if something happens.","zh":"in the event of 指如果某事發生。"},{"en":"In the event of a fire alarm, students should leave the classroom calmly.","zh":"如果發生火警鐘響，學生應冷靜離開課室。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in rules, plans and safety instructions.","zh":"這個短語常用於規則、計劃和安全指示。"},{"en":"It prepares people for what to do if a particular situation occurs.","zh":"它讓人準備在特定情況發生時應做甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be aware of the approach to take","meaning":"清楚知道應採取的方法","examples":[{"en":"Owners should be aware of the approach to take when graffiti appears.","zh":"業主應清楚知道塗鴉出現時應採取的方法。"},{"en":"To be aware of the approach to take means to know the correct method or next steps.","zh":"be aware of the approach to take 指知道正確方法或下一步。"},{"en":"Teachers should be aware of the approach to take when a student reports bullying.","zh":"當學生舉報欺凌，老師應清楚知道應採取的方法。"},{"en":"Knowing the right approach prevents panic and reduces mistakes.","zh":"知道正確方法可以防止恐慌並減少錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses practical knowledge before action is needed.","zh":"這個短語強調在需要行動前具備實用知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"deal with the problem","meaning":"處理問題","examples":[{"en":"Specialist advice may be needed to deal with the problem safely.","zh":"可能需要專家建議來安全地處理問題。"},{"en":"To deal with the problem means to handle, manage or solve it.","zh":"deal with the problem 指處理、管理或解決問題。"},{"en":"A school may call a counsellor to deal with the problem of repeated bullying.","zh":"學校可能請輔導員處理反覆欺凌的問題。"},{"en":"If a problem is handled badly, it may become worse or create new problems.","zh":"如果問題處理不當，它可能惡化或產生新問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes taking practical action in response to difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述因應困難採取實際行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the police should be informed","meaning":"應通知警方","examples":[{"en":"The police should be informed when related attacks may have occurred.","zh":"當可能發生相關破壞事件時，應通知警方。"},{"en":"The police should be informed means the police should be told about the incident officially.","zh":"the police should be informed 指應正式告知警方該事件。"},{"en":"If a shop is broken into, the police should be informed immediately.","zh":"如果商店被爆竊，應立即通知警方。"},{"en":"Informing the police helps create a record and may connect several incidents.","zh":"通知警方有助建立記錄，並可能連繫幾宗事件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reporting a matter to law enforcement.","zh":"這個短語描述向執法部門舉報事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"related attacks occurring locally","meaning":"當區發生的相關破壞事件","examples":[{"en":"The graffiti may be connected to related attacks occurring locally.","zh":"該塗鴉可能與當區發生的相關破壞事件有關。"},{"en":"Related attacks occurring locally are similar acts of damage happening in the same area.","zh":"related attacks occurring locally 是在同一地區發生的相似破壞行為。"},{"en":"Several broken bus shelters in one district may suggest related attacks occurring locally.","zh":"同一區內幾個巴士亭被破壞，可能顯示當區發生相關破壞事件。"},{"en":"Seeing a local pattern helps police understand whether incidents are linked.","zh":"看出本地模式有助警方理解事件是否相連。"},{"en":"The phrase describes nearby connected offences or damage.","zh":"這個短語描述附近相關罪行或破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"incident pattern","meaning":"事件模式","examples":[{"en":"An incident pattern may help the police connect several attacks.","zh":"事件模式可能幫助警方把幾宗破壞事件連繫起來。"},{"en":"An incident pattern is a repeated way in which similar events happen.","zh":"incident pattern 是相似事件反覆發生的方式。"},{"en":"If bicycle thefts happen near the station every Friday, that is an incident pattern.","zh":"如果單車盜竊每逢星期五都在車站附近發生，那就是事件模式。"},{"en":"Patterns help investigators predict where or when another offence may occur.","zh":"模式幫助調查人員預測另一宗罪行可能在何處或何時發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated features across different incidents.","zh":"這個短語描述不同事件之間反覆出現的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"identify possible culprits","meaning":"找出可能肇事者","examples":[{"en":"Repeated styles may help the police identify possible culprits.","zh":"重複風格可能幫助警方找出可能肇事者。"},{"en":"To identify possible culprits means to work out who may be responsible for an offence or problem.","zh":"identify possible culprits 指判斷誰可能對罪行或問題負責。"},{"en":"Camera footage may help a school identify possible culprits after lockers are damaged.","zh":"儲物櫃被破壞後，閉路電視片段可能幫助學校找出可能肇事者。"},{"en":"Repeated signs, habits or patterns can point investigators towards likely offenders.","zh":"重複標誌、習慣或模式可以把調查人員引向可能犯事者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes finding suspects, not necessarily proving guilt.","zh":"這個短語描述找出嫌疑人，而不一定證明有罪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stylised signatures or nicknames","meaning":"風格化簽名或綽號","examples":[{"en":"Graffiti writers often use stylised signatures or nicknames.","zh":"塗鴉者常使用風格化簽名或綽號。"},{"en":"Stylised signatures or nicknames are specially designed names or marks used to identify a person.","zh":"stylised signatures or nicknames 是用來辨認某人的特別設計名稱或標記。"},{"en":"A student may use a stylised nickname in artwork, but not on someone else’s wall.","zh":"學生可能在藝術作品中使用風格化綽號，但不應寫在別人的牆上。"},{"en":"Repeated signatures can help people recognise the same writer’s work.","zh":"重複出現的簽名可以幫助人認出同一作者的作品。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to distinctive personal marks.","zh":"這個短語指獨特個人標記。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be known as tags","meaning":"被稱為「簽名式塗鴉」","examples":[{"en":"These distinctive signatures are known as tags.","zh":"這些獨特簽名被稱為「簽名式塗鴉」。"},{"en":"To be known as tags means to be called tags by people who discuss graffiti.","zh":"be known as tags 指在討論塗鴉的人口中被稱為 tags。"},{"en":"A short nickname painted repeatedly on walls may be known as a tag.","zh":"反覆畫在牆上的短綽號可能被稱為 tag。"},{"en":"Tags can help identify a graffiti writer, but they can also damage public or private property.","zh":"簽名式塗鴉可以幫助辨認塗鴉者，但也會損害公共或私人財物。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the special name for a type of graffiti signature.","zh":"這個短語解釋一種塗鴉簽名的專門名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be familiar to","meaning":"為……所熟悉","examples":[{"en":"A particular tag may already be familiar to the local police.","zh":"某個特定簽名式塗鴉可能已為當地警方所熟悉。"},{"en":"To be familiar to someone means to be recognised or known by that person.","zh":"be familiar to 某人，指被該人認出或知道。"},{"en":"A student’s handwriting may be familiar to a teacher after many assignments.","zh":"老師批改多份功課後，可能熟悉某學生的筆跡。"},{"en":"Familiar signs help people identify patterns more quickly.","zh":"熟悉的標誌幫助人更快識別模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recognition through previous experience.","zh":"這個短語描述透過過往經驗而辨認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"record graffiti incidents","meaning":"記錄塗鴉事件","examples":[{"en":"Photographs should be taken to record graffiti incidents.","zh":"應拍照以記錄塗鴉事件。"},{"en":"To record graffiti incidents means to keep evidence and details of when and where graffiti happened.","zh":"record graffiti incidents 指保存塗鴉何時何地發生的證據和細節。"},{"en":"A building manager may photograph graffiti before cleaning it off.","zh":"大廈經理可能在清除塗鴉前先拍照。"},{"en":"Records help with police reports, insurance claims and future prevention.","zh":"記錄有助警方報告、保險索償和未來預防。"},{"en":"The phrase describes documenting the incident before it disappears.","zh":"這個短語描述在事件消失前加以記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"assist the police in bringing a prosecution","meaning":"協助警方提出檢控","examples":[{"en":"Clear photographs may assist the police in bringing a prosecution.","zh":"清晰照片可能協助警方提出檢控。"},{"en":"To assist the police in bringing a prosecution means to help them collect evidence for legal action.","zh":"assist the police in bringing a prosecution 指幫助警方收集法律行動所需證據。"},{"en":"A shop’s security video may assist the police in bringing a prosecution after theft.","zh":"商店保安錄像可能在盜竊後協助警方提出檢控。"},{"en":"Strong evidence makes it easier to show what happened and who was involved.","zh":"有力證據令警方更容易顯示發生了甚麼和誰涉及其中。"},{"en":"The phrase connects evidence with taking a case to court.","zh":"這個短語把證據與把案件帶上法庭連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be required for insurance claims","meaning":"保險索償所需","examples":[{"en":"Photographic evidence may be required for insurance claims.","zh":"照片證據可能是保險索償所需。"},{"en":"To be required for insurance claims means to be needed before an insurer will consider paying compensation.","zh":"be required for insurance claims 指保險公司考慮賠償前所需要的東西。"},{"en":"A homeowner may need photos of flood damage for an insurance claim.","zh":"屋主可能需要水浸損害照片作保險索償。"},{"en":"Without evidence, an insurance company may refuse or delay payment.","zh":"沒有證據，保險公司可能拒絕或延遲賠償。"},{"en":"The phrase describes documents or proof needed for claiming insurance money.","zh":"這個短語描述索取保險賠償所需文件或證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cleaning operatives","meaning":"清潔技術人員","examples":[{"en":"The photographs can also help cleaning operatives prepare for the job.","zh":"照片也可以幫助清潔技術人員準備工作。"},{"en":"Cleaning operatives are trained workers who carry out cleaning tasks.","zh":"cleaning operatives 是受訓並執行清潔任務的工人。"},{"en":"A hospital uses cleaning operatives to disinfect rooms safely.","zh":"醫院會使用清潔技術人員安全地為房間消毒。"},{"en":"If operatives know the surface and stain type in advance, they can bring the right equipment.","zh":"如果技術人員預先知道表面和污漬種類，就能帶備正確設備。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people who do practical cleaning work.","zh":"這個短語指進行實際清潔工作的人員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"before arriving on site","meaning":"到達現場前","examples":[{"en":"Operatives can examine the damage before arriving on site.","zh":"技術人員可以在到達現場前檢視損害。"},{"en":"Before arriving on site means before reaching the place where the work will happen.","zh":"before arriving on site 指到達實際工作地點之前。"},{"en":"A repair worker may check photos of a broken window before arriving on site.","zh":"維修工人可能在到達現場前查看破窗照片。"},{"en":"Preparing before arrival saves time and reduces wrong equipment choices.","zh":"到達前準備可以節省時間並減少帶錯設備的情況。"},{"en":"The phrase describes planning before going to the actual location.","zh":"這個短語描述前往實際地點前的規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a variety of removal methods","meaning":"多種清除方法","examples":[{"en":"A variety of removal methods are available.","zh":"有多種清除方法可用。"},{"en":"A variety of removal methods means several different ways to take something away.","zh":"a variety of removal methods 指幾種不同的移除方法。"},{"en":"A cleaner may use a variety of removal methods for stains, such as water, detergent or brushing.","zh":"清潔工可能用多種方法清除污漬，例如清水、清潔劑或刷洗。"},{"en":"Different methods are needed because surfaces and materials react differently.","zh":"需要不同方法，因為表面和材料反應不同。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that there is more than one possible approach.","zh":"這個短語強調不止一種可行方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"divide broadly into","meaning":"大致分為……","examples":[{"en":"Graffiti-removal methods divide broadly into two categories.","zh":"塗鴉清除方法大致分為兩類。"},{"en":"To divide broadly into categories means to separate something into general groups.","zh":"divide broadly into 類別，指把某事大致分成幾組。"},{"en":"School activities may divide broadly into academic, sports and arts programmes.","zh":"學校活動可大致分為學術、體育和藝術項目。"},{"en":"Broad categories help people understand a complicated topic before studying details.","zh":"大類別幫助人在研究細節前先理解複雜題目。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a simple first-level classification.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單的第一層分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"chemical and mechanical systems","meaning":"化學及機械清除系統","examples":[{"en":"The main approaches are chemical and mechanical systems.","zh":"主要方法是化學及機械清除系統。"},{"en":"Chemical and mechanical systems are methods using chemicals or physical force to remove material.","zh":"chemical and mechanical systems 是使用化學品或物理力量移除物料的方法。"},{"en":"Cleaning paint with a solvent is chemical, while scraping it off is mechanical.","zh":"用溶劑清除油漆屬化學方法，而刮走油漆屬機械方法。"},{"en":"Both systems can work, but both may also damage a surface if used badly.","zh":"兩種系統都可能有效，但如果使用不當也可能損害表面。"},{"en":"The phrase names two broad types of cleaning approach.","zh":"這個短語指出兩大類清潔方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"chemical preparations","meaning":"化學製劑","examples":[{"en":"Chemical preparations dissolve paint, glue or ink.","zh":"化學製劑可溶解油漆、膠水或墨水。"},{"en":"Chemical preparations are specially made chemical products used for a particular task.","zh":"chemical preparations 是為特定任務而製成的化學產品。"},{"en":"A cleaner may use a chemical preparation to remove old glue from a window.","zh":"清潔工可能使用化學製劑去除窗上的舊膠水。"},{"en":"Strong preparations can work quickly but may require protective equipment.","zh":"強效製劑可以快速見效，但可能需要防護裝備。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to prepared chemical products, not ordinary water alone.","zh":"這個短語指配製好的化學產品，而不只是普通清水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be based on dissolving","meaning":"以溶解……為原理","examples":[{"en":"Chemical treatments are based on dissolving the graffiti material.","zh":"化學處理以溶解塗鴉物料為原理。"},{"en":"To be based on dissolving something means the method works by breaking it down into liquid or removable form.","zh":"be based on dissolving 某物，指方法透過把它分解成液態或可移除形式來運作。"},{"en":"Nail polish remover is based on dissolving polish so it can be wiped away.","zh":"洗甲水以溶解指甲油為原理，使其可被擦走。"},{"en":"If the solvent cannot dissolve the material, the treatment may fail.","zh":"如果溶劑不能溶解該物料，處理可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the working principle of a chemical method.","zh":"這個短語解釋化學方法的運作原理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"solvents can range from…to…","meaning":"溶劑由……至……不等","examples":[{"en":"Solvents can range from water to powerful chemical mixtures.","zh":"溶劑由清水至強力混合化學劑不等。"},{"en":"Solvents can range from A to B means solvents may vary from a mild type to a much stronger type.","zh":"solvents can range from A to B 指溶劑可以由溫和種類到強效種類不等。"},{"en":"Cleaning products can range from simple soap to strong disinfectants.","zh":"清潔產品可以由普通肥皂至強力消毒劑不等。"},{"en":"A wide range means users must choose carefully according to the surface and risk.","zh":"範圍很廣代表使用者必須按表面和風險小心選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase shows variation between two extremes.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個極端之間的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"potentially hazardous chemical cocktails","meaning":"可能有危險的混合化學劑","examples":[{"en":"Some treatments contain potentially hazardous chemical cocktails.","zh":"有些處理方法含有可能有危險的混合化學劑。"},{"en":"Potentially hazardous chemical cocktails are mixtures of chemicals that may be dangerous.","zh":"potentially hazardous chemical cocktails 是可能有危險的化學混合物。"},{"en":"A strong cleaning mixture may irritate skin, eyes or breathing if used without protection.","zh":"如果沒有防護使用，強力清潔混合劑可能刺激皮膚、眼睛或呼吸。"},{"en":"Mixing chemicals carelessly can create risks for workers and passers-by.","zh":"粗心混合化學品可以為工人和路人帶來風險。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that a chemical mixture may harm people or surfaces.","zh":"這個短語提醒某種化學混合物可能傷害人或表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"wire-brushing","meaning":"鋼絲刷清理","examples":[{"en":"Wire-brushing is a mechanical method of graffiti removal.","zh":"鋼絲刷清理是一種機械式塗鴉清除方法。"},{"en":"Wire-brushing means cleaning or scraping a surface with a brush made of metal wires.","zh":"wire-brushing 指用金屬絲製成的刷子清潔或刮擦表面。"},{"en":"A worker may use wire-brushing to remove rust from a metal gate.","zh":"工人可能用鋼絲刷清理金屬閘上的鐵鏽。"},{"en":"Because it is rough, wire-brushing can damage soft stone, paint or historic surfaces.","zh":"因為它較粗糙，鋼絲刷清理可以損害軟石、油漆或歷史表面。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a physical scraping method.","zh":"這個短語描述物理刮擦方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"grit-blasting","meaning":"噴砂清理","examples":[{"en":"Grit-blasting removes markings by firing abrasive particles at the surface.","zh":"噴砂清理透過向表面噴射磨蝕性粒子來清除標記。"},{"en":"Grit-blasting is a cleaning method that shoots small rough particles onto a surface.","zh":"grit-blasting 是把細小粗糙粒子射向表面的清潔方法。"},{"en":"A company may use grit-blasting to clean a strong metal structure.","zh":"公司可能使用噴砂清理堅固金屬結構。"},{"en":"The force can remove paint, but it may also wear away the original surface.","zh":"這種力量可以清除油漆，但也可能磨走原有表面。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a powerful mechanical cleaning method.","zh":"這個短語描述強力機械清潔方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"abrade or chip away","meaning":"磨蝕或鑿除","examples":[{"en":"Mechanical systems abrade or chip away the graffiti material.","zh":"機械系統會磨蝕或鑿除塗鴉物料。"},{"en":"To abrade or chip away means to wear down or remove small pieces by rubbing, scraping or impact.","zh":"abrade or chip away 指透過摩擦、刮擦或撞擊磨掉或移除小碎片。"},{"en":"Repeated rubbing can abrade the surface of a wooden desk.","zh":"反覆摩擦可以磨蝕木桌表面。"},{"en":"If cleaning chips away original stone, the damage may be permanent.","zh":"如果清潔鑿走原有石材，損害可能是永久的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical removal by force.","zh":"這個短語描述以物理力量移除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take care to comply with","meaning":"注意遵守……","examples":[{"en":"Cleaning companies must take care to comply with safety rules.","zh":"清潔公司必須注意遵守安全規則。"},{"en":"To take care to comply with something means to be careful to follow rules or requirements.","zh":"take care to comply with 某事，指小心遵從規則或要求。"},{"en":"A restaurant must take care to comply with food hygiene regulations.","zh":"餐廳必須注意遵守食物衛生規例。"},{"en":"Failing to comply can lead to accidents, fines or legal trouble.","zh":"未能遵守可能導致意外、罰款或法律問題。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses careful obedience to rules.","zh":"這個短語強調小心服從規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"health and safety legislation","meaning":"健康及安全法例","examples":[{"en":"Operatives must comply with health and safety legislation.","zh":"技術人員必須遵守健康及安全法例。"},{"en":"Health and safety legislation means laws that protect people from injury or illness at work or in public settings.","zh":"health and safety legislation 指保護人在工作或公共場所免受傷害或疾病的法律。"},{"en":"A construction company must follow health and safety legislation when workers use ladders.","zh":"建築公司在工人使用梯子時，必須遵守健康及安全法例。"},{"en":"These laws reduce accidents by requiring training, equipment and safe procedures.","zh":"這些法律透過要求培訓、設備和安全程序來減少意外。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to legal rules about protection and workplace safety.","zh":"這個短語指關於保護和工作安全的法律規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"with regard to","meaning":"關於……","examples":[{"en":"Special precautions are necessary with regard to public safety.","zh":"關於公眾安全，特別預防措施是必要的。"},{"en":"With regard to means concerning or about a particular subject.","zh":"with regard to 指關於某個特定主題。"},{"en":"With regard to exam preparation, students should practise timing as well as content.","zh":"關於備考，學生應練習時間控制，也要練習內容。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses attention on one specific area of concern.","zh":"這個短語把注意力集中在一個特定關注範疇。"},{"en":"It is a formal way to introduce the topic being discussed.","zh":"它是引入討論主題的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"protection of passers-by","meaning":"對路人的保護","examples":[{"en":"The work must include adequate protection of passers-by.","zh":"這項工作必須包括對路人的充分保護。"},{"en":"Protection of passers-by means measures that keep people walking nearby safe.","zh":"protection of passers-by 指確保附近行人安全的措施。"},{"en":"Workers may put up barriers to protect passers-by from falling tools.","zh":"工人可能設置圍欄，以保護路人免受墜落工具傷害。"},{"en":"If passers-by are not protected, cleaning chemicals or debris may injure them.","zh":"如果路人沒有受到保護，清潔化學品或碎屑可能傷害他們。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on public safety around work areas.","zh":"這個短語重點在工作範圍附近的公眾安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"carry out the cleaning","meaning":"進行清潔工作","examples":[{"en":"Only properly trained people should carry out the cleaning.","zh":"只有受過適當訓練的人才應進行清潔工作。"},{"en":"To carry out the cleaning means to perform the cleaning work.","zh":"carry out the cleaning 指執行清潔工作。"},{"en":"A school may hire trained staff to carry out the cleaning after a chemical spill.","zh":"化學品濺漏後，學校可能聘請受訓職員進行清潔工作。"},{"en":"If untrained people do the work, they may damage the surface or hurt themselves.","zh":"如果未受訓的人做這項工作，可能損害表面或傷害自己。"},{"en":"The phrase describes doing the practical cleaning task.","zh":"這個短語描述執行實際清潔任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"follow product guidelines","meaning":"遵從產品指引","examples":[{"en":"Operatives should follow product guidelines carefully.","zh":"技術人員應仔細遵從產品指引。"},{"en":"To follow product guidelines means to use a product according to the maker’s instructions.","zh":"follow product guidelines 指按照製造商指示使用產品。"},{"en":"A cleaner should follow product guidelines when mixing or applying disinfectant.","zh":"清潔工混合或施用消毒劑時，應遵從產品指引。"},{"en":"Ignoring guidelines can make a product ineffective or dangerous.","zh":"忽視指引可能令產品無效或危險。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses correct and safe use of a product.","zh":"這個短語強調正確且安全地使用產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in terms of","meaning":"就……而言；在……方面","examples":[{"en":"The manufacturer provides instructions in terms of application and removal.","zh":"製造商就施用及清除方面提供指示。"},{"en":"In terms of means in relation to a particular aspect or area.","zh":"in terms of 指就某個特定方面或範疇而言。"},{"en":"In terms of grammar, the essay is strong, but its examples need more detail.","zh":"就文法而言，文章很強，但例子需要更多細節。"},{"en":"This phrase helps narrow a discussion to one part of a bigger topic.","zh":"這個短語幫助把討論收窄到大題目中的一部分。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing or explaining specific aspects.","zh":"它適合用於比較或解釋特定方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"application and removal","meaning":"施用及清除","examples":[{"en":"Product guidelines should explain both application and removal.","zh":"產品指引應同時解釋施用及清除。"},{"en":"Application and removal mean how to put a product on and how to take it off.","zh":"application and removal 指如何塗上或使用產品，以及如何把它清除。"},{"en":"Hair dye instructions usually explain application and removal clearly.","zh":"染髮劑指示通常清楚解釋施用及清除。"},{"en":"If people know only how to apply a product but not remove it, damage may result.","zh":"如果人們只知道如何施用產品而不知道如何清除，可能導致損害。"},{"en":"The phrase covers the full use cycle of a product or treatment.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋產品或處理方法的完整使用周期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"appropriate protective equipment","meaning":"適當防護裝備","examples":[{"en":"Operatives must wear appropriate protective equipment.","zh":"技術人員必須佩戴適當防護裝備。"},{"en":"Appropriate protective equipment is safety gear suitable for the risks of the job.","zh":"appropriate protective equipment 是適合該工作風險的安全裝備。"},{"en":"A lab student may need gloves and goggles as appropriate protective equipment.","zh":"實驗室學生可能需要手套和護目鏡作為適當防護裝備。"},{"en":"Without proper protection, chemicals, dust or sharp tools may harm workers.","zh":"沒有適當保護，化學品、灰塵或鋒利工具可能傷害工人。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to safety items chosen for a specific task.","zh":"這個短語指為特定任務選擇的安全用品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"measures must be taken to ensure","meaning":"必須採取措施確保……","examples":[{"en":"Measures must be taken to ensure that the public is protected.","zh":"必須採取措施確保公眾受到保護。"},{"en":"Measures must be taken to ensure something means actions are necessary to make that result happen.","zh":"measures must be taken to ensure 某事，指必須採取行動來令該結果發生。"},{"en":"Measures must be taken to ensure students can leave the school safely during heavy rain.","zh":"暴雨期間，必須採取措施確保學生能安全離開學校。"},{"en":"Without clear measures, good intentions may not lead to real protection.","zh":"沒有清楚措施，良好意願未必帶來真正保護。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when practical steps are required.","zh":"這個短語用於需要實際步驟時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"run-off, aerial mists, drips and splashes","meaning":"流出液、空氣噴霧、滴漏及濺液","examples":[{"en":"Run-off, aerial mists, drips and splashes must be carefully controlled.","zh":"流出液、空氣噴霧、滴漏及濺液都必須小心控制。"},{"en":"Run-off, aerial mists, drips and splashes are ways liquid chemicals can spread beyond the work area.","zh":"run-off, aerial mists, drips and splashes 是液體化學品擴散到工作範圍外的不同方式。"},{"en":"During cleaning, run-off may flow onto the pavement while splashes may reach nearby people.","zh":"清潔期間，流出液可能流到行人路上，而濺液可能濺到附近的人。"},{"en":"If these liquids are not controlled, they can harm passers-by or nearby materials.","zh":"如果這些液體不受控制，它們可以傷害路人或附近物料。"},{"en":"The phrase lists different forms of chemical spread.","zh":"這個短語列出化學品擴散的不同形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"threaten unprotected members of the public","meaning":"危害未受保護的公眾","examples":[{"en":"Hazardous chemicals must not threaten unprotected members of the public.","zh":"危險化學品不得危害未受保護的公眾。"},{"en":"To threaten unprotected members of the public means to put nearby people at risk when they have no safety gear.","zh":"threaten unprotected members of the public 指在附近人士沒有安全裝備時令他們承受風險。"},{"en":"Strong cleaning spray near a busy pavement may threaten unprotected members of the public.","zh":"在繁忙行人路附近使用強力清潔噴霧，可能危害未受保護的公眾。"},{"en":"Public safety measures prevent people from being exposed to chemicals by accident.","zh":"公眾安全措施防止人們意外接觸化學品。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on risks to ordinary passers-by.","zh":"這個短語重點在普通路人的風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"examine a graffiti incident","meaning":"檢視塗鴉事件","examples":[{"en":"A specialist should examine a graffiti incident before choosing a treatment.","zh":"專家應在選擇處理方法前檢視塗鴉事件。"},{"en":"To examine a graffiti incident means to inspect the graffiti, surface and damage carefully.","zh":"examine a graffiti incident 指仔細檢查塗鴉、表面和損害。"},{"en":"A building manager may ask an expert to examine a graffiti incident on old stonework.","zh":"大廈經理可能請專家檢視舊石工上的塗鴉事件。"},{"en":"Examination helps choose a method that removes the mark without harming the surface.","zh":"檢視有助選擇能清除標記而不傷害表面的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful inspection before action.","zh":"這個短語描述行動前的仔細檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"assess the ability of the substrate","meaning":"評估基底材料的承受能力","examples":[{"en":"The cleaner must assess the ability of the substrate to resist damage.","zh":"清潔人員必須評估基底材料抵抗損害的能力。"},{"en":"To assess the ability of the substrate means to judge whether the underlying surface can withstand treatment.","zh":"assess the ability of the substrate 指判斷底層表面是否能承受處理。"},{"en":"Before cleaning tiles, a worker should assess whether the substrate beneath them is weak.","zh":"清潔瓷磚前，工人應評估其下方基底是否脆弱。"},{"en":"If the substrate is fragile, strong treatment may cause deeper damage.","zh":"如果基底脆弱，強力處理可能造成更深層損害。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on checking the strength of the surface material.","zh":"這個短語重點在檢查表面物料的強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"withstand the prescribed treatment","meaning":"承受指定處理方法","examples":[{"en":"The historic surface may not withstand the prescribed treatment.","zh":"歷史表面可能無法承受指定處理方法。"},{"en":"To withstand the prescribed treatment means to survive the recommended treatment without damage.","zh":"withstand the prescribed treatment 指在不受損的情況下承受建議處理方法。"},{"en":"Old paper may not withstand the prescribed cleaning method if it involves moisture.","zh":"如果指定清潔方法涉及水分，舊紙張可能無法承受。"},{"en":"A treatment that is safe for modern concrete may harm older materials.","zh":"對現代混凝土安全的處理方法，可能會傷害較舊物料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes whether a surface can tolerate a chosen method.","zh":"這個短語描述表面是否能承受所選方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"if there is any doubt regarding","meaning":"如對……有任何疑問","examples":[{"en":"If there is any doubt regarding the surface, a test should be conducted.","zh":"如對表面有任何疑問，應進行測試。"},{"en":"If there is any doubt regarding something means if people are uncertain about it.","zh":"if there is any doubt regarding 某事，指如果人們對它不確定。"},{"en":"If there is any doubt regarding a student’s allergy, the school should check with parents first.","zh":"如對學生的過敏情況有任何疑問，學校應先向家長查核。"},{"en":"Doubt is a reason to test carefully rather than act immediately.","zh":"有疑問就是應仔細測試，而不是立即行動的理由。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a cautious condition.","zh":"這個短語引出謹慎條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"small trial areas","meaning":"小範圍試驗區","examples":[{"en":"The cleaning method should first be tested on small trial areas.","zh":"清潔方法應先在小範圍試驗區測試。"},{"en":"Small trial areas are limited patches used to test a method before treating the whole surface.","zh":"small trial areas 是在處理整個表面前用來測試方法的有限小區域。"},{"en":"A painter may test a colour on a small trial area before painting the entire room.","zh":"油漆工可能先在小範圍試驗區測試顏色，再粉刷整個房間。"},{"en":"Trial areas reveal possible problems before they spread across a larger surface.","zh":"試驗區能在問題擴散到更大表面前揭示可能問題。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to testing on a small sample area.","zh":"這個短語指在小樣本區域上測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"assess the impact of","meaning":"評估……的影響","examples":[{"en":"A trial helps assess the impact of the proposed treatment.","zh":"試驗有助評估建議處理方法的影響。"},{"en":"To assess the impact of something means to judge what effect it has.","zh":"assess the impact of 某事，指判斷它有甚麼效果。"},{"en":"A school may assess the impact of a new homework policy by checking stress and grades.","zh":"學校可能透過檢查壓力和成績，評估新功課政策的影響。"},{"en":"Understanding impact helps people decide whether to continue, change or stop an action.","zh":"理解影響幫助人決定繼續、改變還是停止行動。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on evaluating results or effects.","zh":"這個短語重點在評估結果或效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"more extensive treatment","meaning":"更大範圍的處理","examples":[{"en":"Testing should take place before more extensive treatment begins.","zh":"在開始更大範圍的處理前，應先進行測試。"},{"en":"More extensive treatment means treatment over a larger area or with greater depth.","zh":"more extensive treatment 指在更大範圍或更深入程度上進行處理。"},{"en":"A doctor may try a small test first before recommending more extensive treatment.","zh":"醫生可能先進行小測試，再建議更大範圍的治療。"},{"en":"Testing first reduces the risk of spreading damage widely.","zh":"先測試可減少大範圍擴散損害的風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a bigger or fuller stage of treatment.","zh":"這個短語描述更大或更完整的處理階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"preventive strategies","meaning":"預防策略","examples":[{"en":"Several preventive strategies can reduce recurring graffiti.","zh":"幾種預防策略可以減少反覆出現的塗鴉。"},{"en":"Preventive strategies are planned methods used to stop a problem before it happens again.","zh":"preventive strategies 是用來阻止問題再次發生的計劃方法。"},{"en":"A school may use preventive strategies such as better lighting and staff patrols to reduce vandalism.","zh":"學校可能使用改善照明和職員巡邏等預防策略來減少破壞。"},{"en":"Prevention is often cheaper than repairing repeated damage.","zh":"預防通常比反覆修復損害更便宜。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on stopping future problems rather than only fixing past damage.","zh":"這個短語重點在阻止未來問題，而不只是修復過去損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be adopted to combat","meaning":"被採用來應對……","examples":[{"en":"Different measures can be adopted to combat repeated attacks.","zh":"不同措施可以被採用來應對反覆破壞。"},{"en":"To be adopted to combat something means to be chosen and used to fight or reduce it.","zh":"be adopted to combat 某事，指被選擇並用來對抗或減少它。"},{"en":"A school may adopt new entry rules to combat theft from lockers.","zh":"學校可能採用新的出入規則來應對儲物櫃盜竊。"},{"en":"Measures are adopted when ordinary responses are not enough.","zh":"當普通回應不足，措施就會被採用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes choosing practical action against a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇實際行動來對付問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a recurring problem","meaning":"反覆出現的問題","examples":[{"en":"Graffiti may become a recurring problem at an unprotected site.","zh":"在沒有保護的地點，塗鴉可能成為反覆出現的問題。"},{"en":"A recurring problem is a problem that happens again and again.","zh":"recurring problem 是一次又一次發生的問題。"},{"en":"If the same classroom light breaks every month, it is a recurring problem.","zh":"如果同一間課室的燈每月都壞，那就是反覆出現的問題。"},{"en":"Recurring problems need prevention, not only repeated repair.","zh":"反覆出現的問題需要預防，而不只是反覆維修。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses repetition over time.","zh":"這個短語強調隨時間重複發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at a given site","meaning":"在指定地點","examples":[{"en":"The best solution depends on conditions at a given site.","zh":"最佳解決方案取決於指定地點的情況。"},{"en":"At a given site means at a particular place being considered.","zh":"at a given site 指在正在考慮的特定地點。"},{"en":"At a given school, the best security plan depends on entrances, lighting and student movement.","zh":"在指定學校，最佳保安計劃取決於入口、照明和學生流動。"},{"en":"Different sites have different risks, so one solution may not fit all places.","zh":"不同地點有不同風險，所以一個方案未必適合所有地方。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the specific location under discussion.","zh":"這個短語重點在討論中的特定位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"no two sites are the same","meaning":"每個地點的情況都不同","examples":[{"en":"No two sites are the same, so each requires a separate assessment.","zh":"每個地點的情況都不同，所以每個都需要分開評估。"},{"en":"No two sites are the same means every location has its own conditions and risks.","zh":"no two sites are the same 指每個地點都有自己的條件和風險。"},{"en":"No two schools are the same, so a discipline policy may need local adjustment.","zh":"每間學校情況都不同，所以紀律政策可能需要本地調整。"},{"en":"Treating all places identically can lead to unsuitable decisions.","zh":"以完全相同方式處理所有地方，可能導致不合適決定。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the need for individual judgement.","zh":"這個短語強調需要個別判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"no one set of protection measures","meaning":"沒有一套統一的保護措施","examples":[{"en":"No one set of protection measures will work everywhere.","zh":"沒有一套統一的保護措施能在所有地方有效。"},{"en":"No one set of protection measures means there is no single package of safeguards suitable for all places.","zh":"no one set of protection measures 指沒有一套單一防護方案適合所有地方。"},{"en":"A security plan for a shopping mall may not work for a small village library.","zh":"適用於商場的保安計劃，未必適用於小村圖書館。"},{"en":"Protection must match the site, the risk and the people using the space.","zh":"保護措施必須配合地點、風險和使用空間的人。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against using one standard solution for every situation.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要把同一標準方案套用到所有情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be suitable for all situations","meaning":"適用於所有情況","examples":[{"en":"A single preventive method will not be suitable for all situations.","zh":"單一預防方法不會適用於所有情況。"},{"en":"To be suitable for all situations means to work well in every possible context.","zh":"be suitable for all situations 指在所有可能語境中都有效。"},{"en":"One teaching method is rarely suitable for all situations because students learn differently.","zh":"一種教學方法很少適用於所有情況，因為學生學習方式不同。"},{"en":"A method that works on concrete may not work on old brick or wood.","zh":"適用於混凝土的方法，未必適用於舊磚或木材。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used to show the limits of a general solution.","zh":"這個短語常用來顯示通用方案的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be looked at individually","meaning":"須個別評估","examples":[{"en":"Each vulnerable location must be looked at individually.","zh":"每個容易受破壞的位置都須個別評估。"},{"en":"To be looked at individually means to be examined separately rather than as part of a general group.","zh":"be looked at individually 指被分開檢視，而不是只作為一般群組的一部分。"},{"en":"A teacher should look at each student’s writing problem individually.","zh":"老師應個別評估每位學生的寫作問題。"},{"en":"Separate assessment helps people choose a response that fits the real need.","zh":"分開評估幫助人選擇符合真正需要的回應。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses case-by-case judgement.","zh":"這個短語強調逐個個案判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"surveillance systems","meaning":"監察系統","examples":[{"en":"Surveillance systems can discourage graffiti and other offences.","zh":"監察系統可以阻止塗鴉和其他罪行。"},{"en":"Surveillance systems are cameras or monitoring methods used to watch an area.","zh":"surveillance systems 是用來監察某區域的攝影機或監控方法。"},{"en":"A school may install surveillance systems near entrances to prevent theft.","zh":"學校可能在入口附近安裝監察系統以防盜竊。"},{"en":"When people know they are being watched, they may be less likely to break rules.","zh":"當人們知道自己被監察，可能較不會違規。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to organised monitoring for security.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的保安監控。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"closed-circuit television","meaning":"閉路電視","examples":[{"en":"Closed-circuit television is widely used to monitor public areas.","zh":"閉路電視被廣泛用於監察公共區域。"},{"en":"Closed-circuit television is a camera system that records or shows images for security purposes.","zh":"closed-circuit television 是為保安目的記錄或顯示影像的攝影機系統。"},{"en":"A shopping centre may use closed-circuit television to watch entrances and corridors.","zh":"商場可能使用閉路電視監察入口和走廊。"},{"en":"CCTV footage can help identify what happened during an incident.","zh":"閉路電視片段可以幫助辨認事件中發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the security camera system commonly called CCTV.","zh":"這個短語指通常稱為 CCTV 的保安攝影系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"prominently placed cameras","meaning":"設於顯眼位置的攝影機","examples":[{"en":"Prominently placed cameras can discourage anti-social behaviour.","zh":"設於顯眼位置的攝影機可以阻止反社會行為。"},{"en":"Prominently placed cameras are cameras installed where people can easily see them.","zh":"prominently placed cameras 是安裝在人們容易看見位置的攝影機。"},{"en":"A school may put visible cameras near bicycle racks to prevent theft.","zh":"學校可能在單車架附近設置顯眼攝影機以防盜竊。"},{"en":"Visible cameras can deter offenders because they fear being recorded.","zh":"可見攝影機可以阻嚇犯事者，因為他們害怕被錄下。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the cameras are noticeable, not hidden.","zh":"這個短語強調攝影機是明顯可見，而不是隱藏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be shown to reduce","meaning":"已證實可減少……","examples":[{"en":"Visible cameras have been shown to reduce vandalism.","zh":"顯眼攝影機已證實可減少蓄意破壞。"},{"en":"To be shown to reduce something means evidence has demonstrated that it makes the problem smaller.","zh":"be shown to reduce 某事，指證據已顯示它能令問題減少。"},{"en":"Regular handwashing has been shown to reduce the spread of some illnesses.","zh":"定期洗手已證實可減少某些疾病傳播。"},{"en":"Evidence matters because a method may sound useful but not actually work.","zh":"證據重要，因為一種方法聽起來有用，但未必真的有效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a result supported by evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述有證據支持的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"anti-social behaviour","meaning":"反社會行為","examples":[{"en":"Graffiti is sometimes treated as a form of anti-social behaviour.","zh":"塗鴉有時被視為一種反社會行為。"},{"en":"Anti-social behaviour is behaviour that harms, annoys or intimidates other people in a community.","zh":"anti-social behaviour 是傷害、滋擾或恐嚇社區中其他人的行為。"},{"en":"Loud shouting at night, vandalism and harassment can be anti-social behaviour.","zh":"夜間大聲叫喊、蓄意破壞和騷擾都可以是反社會行為。"},{"en":"Such behaviour can make residents feel unsafe or uncomfortable.","zh":"這類行為可以令居民感到不安全或不舒服。"},{"en":"The phrase describes actions that damage public order and community life.","zh":"這個短語描述破壞公共秩序和社區生活的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"security patrols","meaning":"保安巡邏","examples":[{"en":"Security patrols can protect sites that are repeatedly attacked.","zh":"保安巡邏可以保護反覆被破壞的地點。"},{"en":"Security patrols are regular checks made by guards or security staff.","zh":"security patrols 是由保安或保安職員定期進行的檢查。"},{"en":"A school may arrange security patrols around the playground after repeated vandalism.","zh":"學校可能在反覆破壞後安排操場周邊保安巡邏。"},{"en":"Patrols make it harder for offenders to act without being seen.","zh":"巡邏令犯事者較難在不被看見的情況下行動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to active movement and checking for protection.","zh":"這個短語指為保護而進行的主動走動和檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"act as a deterrent","meaning":"發揮阻嚇作用","examples":[{"en":"The presence of guards may act as a deterrent.","zh":"保安在場可能發揮阻嚇作用。"},{"en":"To act as a deterrent means to discourage people from doing something wrong.","zh":"act as a deterrent 指阻止人做錯事。"},{"en":"A visible teacher near the school gate may act as a deterrent to fighting.","zh":"校門附近一位明顯可見的老師可能對打架發揮阻嚇作用。"},{"en":"Deterrents work by increasing the chance of being noticed or punished.","zh":"阻嚇因素透過增加被發現或受罰機會而起作用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that prevents behaviour by creating fear of consequences.","zh":"這個短語描述透過令人害怕後果來防止行為的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"prevent recurring attacks","meaning":"防止再次破壞","examples":[{"en":"Regular patrols may help prevent recurring attacks.","zh":"定期巡邏可能有助防止再次破壞。"},{"en":"To prevent recurring attacks means to stop repeated acts of damage or offence from happening again.","zh":"prevent recurring attacks 指阻止重複的破壞或罪行再次發生。"},{"en":"Extra staff near lockers may prevent recurring attacks on students’ belongings.","zh":"在儲物櫃附近增加職員，可能防止學生財物再次被破壞。"},{"en":"Prevention works best when it targets the reason attacks keep happening.","zh":"當預防措施針對破壞反覆發生的原因，效果最好。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on stopping repeated incidents, not just one event.","zh":"這個短語重點在阻止重複事件，而不只是一次事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the cost may be too high","meaning":"成本可能過高","examples":[{"en":"The cost of permanent security may be too high for many sites.","zh":"對許多地點來說，永久保安的成本可能過高。"},{"en":"The cost may be too high means the price may be more than people can afford or justify.","zh":"the cost may be too high 指價格可能超出人們能負擔或合理支持的水平。"},{"en":"A small school may want a new sports hall, but the cost may be too high.","zh":"小學校可能想要新體育館，但成本可能過高。"},{"en":"When costs are too high, organisations may need cheaper alternatives.","zh":"當成本過高，機構可能需要較便宜替代方案。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why a useful idea may not be practical.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何有用想法未必實際可行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"physical barriers","meaning":"實體屏障","examples":[{"en":"Physical barriers include walls, railings, doors and gates.","zh":"實體屏障包括牆、欄杆、門和閘。"},{"en":"Physical barriers are solid objects that block or limit access to a place.","zh":"physical barriers 是阻擋或限制進入某地方的實體物件。"},{"en":"A school may use physical barriers to stop cars entering a pedestrian area.","zh":"學校可能使用實體屏障阻止汽車進入行人區。"},{"en":"Barriers can protect property, but they may also affect appearance and movement.","zh":"屏障可以保護財物，但也可能影響外觀和流動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to material obstacles, not rules alone.","zh":"這個短語指實物障礙，而不只是規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"discourage unauthorised access","meaning":"阻止未經許可進入","examples":[{"en":"Railings may discourage unauthorised access to the property.","zh":"欄杆可能阻止未經許可進入該物業。"},{"en":"To discourage unauthorised access means to make it less likely that people enter without permission.","zh":"discourage unauthorised access 指令人較不可能在沒有許可下進入。"},{"en":"A locked gate can discourage unauthorised access to a school playground at night.","zh":"上鎖閘門可以阻止夜間未經許可進入學校操場。"},{"en":"If access is easy, damage or theft becomes more likely.","zh":"如果容易進入，破壞或盜竊就更可能發生。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on preventing entry by people who are not allowed in.","zh":"這個短語重點在防止沒有准許的人進入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a vulnerable site","meaning":"容易受破壞的地點","examples":[{"en":"A gate may help protect a vulnerable site.","zh":"閘門可能有助保護容易受破壞的地點。"},{"en":"A vulnerable site is a place that is easy to damage, attack or enter without permission.","zh":"vulnerable site 是容易被破壞、攻擊或未經許可進入的地方。"},{"en":"An empty building beside a dark alley may be a vulnerable site.","zh":"黑暗小巷旁的空置建築可能是容易受破壞的地點。"},{"en":"Vulnerable sites need extra protection because offenders may target them repeatedly.","zh":"容易受破壞的地點需要額外保護，因為犯事者可能反覆針對它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a location at risk.","zh":"這個短語描述有風險的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"consideration has to be given to","meaning":"必須考慮……","examples":[{"en":"Consideration has to be given to the appearance of the historic structure.","zh":"必須考慮歷史建築的外觀。"},{"en":"Consideration has to be given to something means people must think carefully about it before acting.","zh":"consideration has to be given to 某事，指人們行動前必須仔細思考它。"},{"en":"Consideration has to be given to student safety before organising an overnight trip.","zh":"組織過夜旅行前必須考慮學生安全。"},{"en":"Ignoring an important factor may lead to a decision that solves one problem but creates another.","zh":"忽視重要因素可能令決定解決一個問題，卻造成另一問題。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that something must not be overlooked.","zh":"這個短語強調某事不能被忽略。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the impact on the structure","meaning":"對建築物的影響","examples":[{"en":"Owners should assess the impact of barriers on the structure.","zh":"業主應評估屏障對建築物的影響。"},{"en":"The impact on the structure means the effect that an action has on a building or object.","zh":"impact on the structure 指某行動對建築物或物件造成的影響。"},{"en":"Installing heavy signs may have an impact on the structure of an old wall.","zh":"安裝沉重招牌可能對舊牆結構有影響。"},{"en":"If the impact is harmful, the protection measure may not be acceptable.","zh":"如果影響有害，保護措施可能不可接受。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how a structure may be changed or damaged.","zh":"這個短語重點在結構可能如何被改變或損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in the worst cases","meaning":"在最壞情況下","examples":[{"en":"In the worst cases, the preventive measures damage the surroundings.","zh":"在最壞情況下，預防措施會損害周圍環境。"},{"en":"In the worst cases means in the most serious or harmful situations.","zh":"in the worst cases 指在最嚴重或最有害的情況中。"},{"en":"In the worst cases, untreated stress can lead to serious health problems.","zh":"在最壞情況下，未處理的壓力可以導致嚴重健康問題。"},{"en":"This phrase warns readers about the strongest possible negative result.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者最嚴重的可能負面結果。"},{"en":"It is used when discussing risk or danger.","zh":"它用於討論風險或危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as damaging as","meaning":"與……同樣具破壞性","examples":[{"en":"Poorly designed barriers may be as damaging as the graffiti itself.","zh":"設計差劣的屏障可能與塗鴉本身同樣具破壞性。"},{"en":"As damaging as means causing the same level of harm as something else.","zh":"as damaging as 指造成與另一事物同等程度的傷害。"},{"en":"A rushed repair may be as damaging as the original leak if it breaks the pipe further.","zh":"如果匆忙維修令水管破得更嚴重，它可能與原本漏水同樣具破壞性。"},{"en":"A solution can be harmful if it creates a problem equal to the one it tries to fix.","zh":"如果解決方案造成與原問題相等的問題，它也可能有害。"},{"en":"The phrase compares two sources of damage.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個損害來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"provide a new surface for","meaning":"為……提供新表面","examples":[{"en":"A solid wall may simply provide a new surface for graffiti.","zh":"實心牆可能只是為塗鴉提供新表面。"},{"en":"To provide a new surface for something means to create another place where it can appear.","zh":"provide a new surface for 某事，指創造另一個可讓它出現的地方。"},{"en":"A blank noticeboard may provide a new surface for students to post messages.","zh":"空白告示板可能為學生張貼訊息提供新表面。"},{"en":"If a barrier creates a fresh blank wall, it may attract the same problem it was meant to stop.","zh":"如果屏障創造出新的空白牆面，它可能吸引本來想阻止的同一問題。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how a solution can unintentionally create an opportunity.","zh":"這個短語顯示解決方案如何無意中創造機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"problems associated with","meaning":"與……相關的問題","examples":[{"en":"Repeated cleaning is one of the main problems associated with graffiti removal.","zh":"反覆清潔是與塗鴉清除相關的主要問題之一。"},{"en":"Problems associated with something are difficulties connected to it.","zh":"problems associated with 某事，是與它相連的困難。"},{"en":"One problem associated with online learning is that some students lack quiet space at home.","zh":"與網上學習相關的一個問題是有些學生家中缺乏安靜空間。"},{"en":"Identifying related problems helps people design better solutions.","zh":"找出相關問題幫助人設計更好解決方案。"},{"en":"The phrase describes issues linked to a topic.","zh":"這個短語描述與某主題相連的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"repeatedly attacked surfaces","meaning":"反覆被塗鴉的表面","examples":[{"en":"Repeatedly attacked surfaces may suffer permanent damage.","zh":"反覆被塗鴉的表面可能遭受永久損害。"},{"en":"Repeatedly attacked surfaces are surfaces that are damaged or marked again and again.","zh":"repeatedly attacked surfaces 是一次又一次被損壞或標記的表面。"},{"en":"A school wall that is painted on every weekend is a repeatedly attacked surface.","zh":"每個週末都被塗畫的學校牆壁，就是反覆被塗鴉的表面。"},{"en":"Repeated attacks make each later cleaning more risky.","zh":"反覆破壞令每次之後的清潔更有風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes surfaces exposed to repeated harm.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆受到傷害的表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"under these circumstances","meaning":"在這些情況下","examples":[{"en":"Under these circumstances, even gentle cleaning can be harmful.","zh":"在這些情況下，即使溫和清潔也可能有害。"},{"en":"Under these circumstances means in this particular situation.","zh":"under these circumstances 指在這個特定情況中。"},{"en":"If a student is ill and exhausted, under these circumstances extra homework may be unfair.","zh":"如果學生生病又疲累，在這些情況下額外功課可能不公平。"},{"en":"Context can change whether an action is sensible or harmful.","zh":"語境可以改變某行動是合理還是有害。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a judgement based on specific conditions.","zh":"這個短語引出基於特定條件的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"repeated removal","meaning":"反覆清除","examples":[{"en":"Repeated removal gradually wears away the original surface.","zh":"反覆清除會逐漸磨走原有表面。"},{"en":"Repeated removal means taking something away again and again over time.","zh":"repeated removal 指隨時間一次又一次地移除某物。"},{"en":"Repeated removal of stickers from a laptop may damage the paint.","zh":"反覆清除手提電腦上的貼紙，可能損害油漆。"},{"en":"Even careful removal can cause wear if it happens too often.","zh":"即使小心清除，如果次數太多也會造成磨損。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses damage caused by frequency.","zh":"這個短語強調由頻率造成的損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"even the most gentle methods","meaning":"即使最溫和的方法","examples":[{"en":"Even the most gentle methods can cause cumulative damage.","zh":"即使最溫和的方法也可能造成累積損害。"},{"en":"Even the most gentle methods means even the softest or least aggressive approaches.","zh":"even the most gentle methods 指即使是最柔和或最不強烈的方法。"},{"en":"Even the most gentle soap can irritate very sensitive skin if used too often.","zh":"如果使用太頻繁，即使最溫和的肥皂也可能刺激非常敏感的皮膚。"},{"en":"A method may be safe once but harmful after repeated use.","zh":"一種方法使用一次可能安全，但反覆使用後可能有害。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights that low risk does not mean no risk.","zh":"這個短語突出低風險不等於零風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ultimately cause damage to","meaning":"最終對……造成損害","examples":[{"en":"Frequent cleaning will ultimately cause damage to the surface material.","zh":"頻繁清潔最終會對表面物料造成損害。"},{"en":"To ultimately cause damage to something means to harm it in the end after a process continues.","zh":"ultimately cause damage to 某物，指一個過程持續後最終傷害它。"},{"en":"Poor posture may ultimately cause damage to a student’s back.","zh":"差劣姿勢最終可能對學生背部造成損害。"},{"en":"Some harm appears only after repeated pressure or long delay.","zh":"有些傷害只有在反覆壓力或長時間延誤後才出現。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the final harmful result.","zh":"這個短語重點在最後的有害結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"surface material","meaning":"表面物料","examples":[{"en":"Abrasive cleaning may remove part of the surface material.","zh":"磨蝕性清潔可能移除部分表面物料。"},{"en":"Surface material is the outer layer or substance that a surface is made of.","zh":"surface material 是表面所由構成的外層或物質。"},{"en":"A wooden table, stone wall and painted door all have different surface materials.","zh":"木桌、石牆和油漆門都有不同表面物料。"},{"en":"Cleaning must match the surface material, or damage may occur.","zh":"清潔方法必須配合表面物料，否則可能造成損害。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the material at the outside of an object.","zh":"這個短語指物件外層的物料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not a viable proposition","meaning":"並非可行方案","examples":[{"en":"Permanent security may not be a viable proposition at every location.","zh":"永久保安在每個地點未必都是可行方案。"},{"en":"Not a viable proposition means not a practical or realistic option.","zh":"not a viable proposition 指並非實際或現實可行的選項。"},{"en":"Hiring a private tutor every day may not be a viable proposition for many families.","zh":"對許多家庭來說，每天聘請私人補習老師未必是可行方案。"},{"en":"A plan can be useful in theory but impossible because of cost, time or staffing.","zh":"一個計劃理論上可以有用，但可能因成本、時間或人手而不可能。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why an idea may not work in real life.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何一個想法在現實中未必行得通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"anti-graffiti coatings","meaning":"防塗鴉塗層","examples":[{"en":"Anti-graffiti coatings can protect vulnerable surfaces.","zh":"防塗鴉塗層可以保護容易受破壞的表面。"},{"en":"Anti-graffiti coatings are protective layers applied to surfaces to make graffiti easier to remove.","zh":"anti-graffiti coatings 是施加於表面的保護層，使塗鴉較容易清除。"},{"en":"A city may put anti-graffiti coatings on walls near train stations.","zh":"城市可能在火車站附近牆壁上塗上防塗鴉塗層。"},{"en":"These coatings can reduce damage because cleaning may require less force.","zh":"這些塗層可以減少損害，因為清潔可能需要較少力度。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to protective surface treatments against graffiti.","zh":"這個短語指防止塗鴉的保護性表面處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be applied by brush or spray","meaning":"以掃塗或噴塗方式施用","examples":[{"en":"The protective coating may be applied by brush or spray.","zh":"保護塗層可以掃塗或噴塗方式施用。"},{"en":"To be applied by brush or spray means to be put onto a surface using a brush or spraying device.","zh":"be applied by brush or spray 指用掃或噴霧裝置把它施加到表面。"},{"en":"Paint can be applied by brush or spray depending on the size of the wall.","zh":"油漆可根據牆面大小以掃塗或噴塗方式施用。"},{"en":"The application method affects speed, thickness and how even the coating looks.","zh":"施用方法會影響速度、厚度和塗層是否均勻。"},{"en":"The phrase describes two practical ways to put a coating on a surface.","zh":"這個短語描述把塗層加到表面的兩種實際方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"leave a thin veneer","meaning":"留下一層薄薄的保護膜","examples":[{"en":"The coating leaves a thin veneer over the original surface.","zh":"該塗層在原有表面上留下一層薄薄的保護膜。"},{"en":"To leave a thin veneer means to create a very thin covering layer on top.","zh":"leave a thin veneer 指在上方形成非常薄的覆蓋層。"},{"en":"A protective phone film leaves a thin layer over the screen.","zh":"手機保護貼會在螢幕上留下一層薄膜。"},{"en":"A thin layer can protect the surface while keeping its appearance mostly visible.","zh":"薄層可以保護表面，同時大致保留其外觀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a light covering, not a thick replacement.","zh":"這個短語描述輕薄覆蓋，而不是厚厚替換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"serve to isolate…from…","meaning":"用以把……與……隔開","examples":[{"en":"The coating serves to isolate the graffiti from the historic surface.","zh":"該塗層用以把塗鴉與歷史表面隔開。"},{"en":"To serve to isolate A from B means to act as a barrier separating A from B.","zh":"serve to isolate A from B 指作為屏障把 A 與 B 分開。"},{"en":"A phone case serves to isolate the phone body from scratches and dirt.","zh":"手機殼用以把手機機身與刮痕和污垢隔開。"},{"en":"If graffiti sits on a coating rather than the original stone, removal is safer.","zh":"如果塗鴉停留在塗層上，而不是原有石材上，清除會較安全。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how a protective layer prevents direct contact.","zh":"這個短語解釋保護層如何防止直接接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be treated in this way","meaning":"以這種方式處理","examples":[{"en":"Graffiti is easier to remove from a surface treated in this way.","zh":"塗鴉較容易從以這種方式處理的表面清除。"},{"en":"To be treated in this way means to receive the particular treatment just described.","zh":"be treated in this way 指接受剛描述的特定處理方法。"},{"en":"A wooden table treated in this way may resist water stains better.","zh":"以這種方式處理的木桌可能更能抵抗水漬。"},{"en":"Once a surface has been protected, later cleaning may be quicker and gentler.","zh":"表面一旦受到保護，之後清潔可能更快且更溫和。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to a specific method already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指回已提及的特定方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"low-pressure water","meaning":"低壓水","examples":[{"en":"The coating usually allows cleaning with low-pressure water.","zh":"該塗層通常容許用低壓水清潔。"},{"en":"Low-pressure water is water used with gentle force rather than a powerful jet.","zh":"low-pressure water 是以溫和力度而非強力水柱使用的水。"},{"en":"A worker may use low-pressure water to rinse a delicate painted surface.","zh":"工人可能用低壓水沖洗脆弱上漆表面。"},{"en":"Lower pressure reduces the chance of wearing away fragile material.","zh":"較低壓力減少磨走脆弱物料的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a gentler washing method.","zh":"這個短語描述較溫和的沖洗方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reduce the possibility of damage","meaning":"減低損害的可能性","examples":[{"en":"Gentle washing can reduce the possibility of damage.","zh":"溫和清洗可以減低損害的可能性。"},{"en":"To reduce the possibility of damage means to lower the chance that harm will occur.","zh":"reduce the possibility of damage 指降低傷害發生的機會。"},{"en":"Wearing a phone case can reduce the possibility of damage if the phone falls.","zh":"手機套可以在手機跌落時減低損害的可能性。"},{"en":"Careful methods do not remove all risk, but they make harm less likely.","zh":"小心方法不能消除所有風險，但會令傷害較不可能發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lowering risk rather than guaranteeing safety.","zh":"這個短語描述降低風險，而不是保證安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"depending on","meaning":"視乎……","examples":[{"en":"The coating may need to be renewed depending on the barrier selected.","zh":"塗層可能需要更新，視乎所選屏障而定。"},{"en":"Depending on means according to or controlled by a particular factor.","zh":"depending on 指根據某特定因素或受其影響。"},{"en":"Students may bring an umbrella depending on the weather forecast.","zh":"學生可能視乎天氣預報而帶雨傘。"},{"en":"Different conditions lead to different decisions.","zh":"不同條件會導致不同決定。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the result is not fixed but changes with circumstances.","zh":"這個短語顯示結果不是固定，而是隨情況改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the type of barrier selected","meaning":"所選屏障的類型","examples":[{"en":"Maintenance requirements depend on the type of barrier selected.","zh":"保養要求取決於所選屏障的類型。"},{"en":"The type of barrier selected means the particular protective barrier that has been chosen.","zh":"type of barrier selected 指已被選擇的特定保護屏障。"},{"en":"A school’s cleaning plan may depend on the type of floor material selected.","zh":"學校清潔計劃可能取決於所選地板物料類型。"},{"en":"Different barrier types may need different repair, renewal or cleaning schedules.","zh":"不同屏障類型可能需要不同維修、更新或清潔時間表。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how the chosen option affects later work.","zh":"這個短語重點在所選選項如何影響之後工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reapply the coating","meaning":"重新塗上塗層","examples":[{"en":"Workers may need to reapply the coating after cleaning.","zh":"工人可能需要在清潔後重新塗上塗層。"},{"en":"To reapply the coating means to put the protective layer on again.","zh":"reapply the coating 指再次加上保護層。"},{"en":"A student may reapply sunscreen after swimming because the first layer has washed off.","zh":"學生游泳後可能需要重新塗上防曬霜，因為第一層已被洗走。"},{"en":"Some coatings stop working after removal or cleaning, so renewal is needed.","zh":"有些塗層在清除或清潔後不再有效，所以需要更新。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeating the application of a protective layer.","zh":"這個短語描述重複施加保護層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"after each removal exercise","meaning":"每次清除作業後","examples":[{"en":"Some coatings must be renewed after each removal exercise.","zh":"有些塗層必須在每次清除作業後更新。"},{"en":"After each removal exercise means after every separate act of cleaning or taking graffiti away.","zh":"after each removal exercise 指每一次分開的清潔或清除塗鴉行動之後。"},{"en":"A school may check equipment after each fire drill to make sure nothing is missing.","zh":"學校可能在每次火警演習後檢查設備，確保沒有遺漏。"},{"en":"Repeating a check after every operation helps maintain protection.","zh":"每次操作後重複檢查有助維持保護。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what must happen after each individual cleaning event.","zh":"這個短語指每次單獨清潔事件後必須發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"which paragraph contains","meaning":"哪一段包含……","examples":[{"en":"Students must identify which paragraph contains each piece of information.","zh":"學生必須辨認哪一段包含每項資料。"},{"en":"Which paragraph contains means which paragraph includes or mentions the information.","zh":"which paragraph contains 指哪一段包括或提及該資料。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may need to find which paragraph contains a definition or example.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能需要找出哪一段包含定義或例子。"},{"en":"This question type tests scanning and understanding of paragraph content.","zh":"這種題型測試掃讀和理解段落內容的能力。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in paragraph-matching tasks.","zh":"這個短語用於段落配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"chemical cleaning","meaning":"化學清潔","examples":[{"en":"Chemical cleaning can damage a surface if the solvent is too strong.","zh":"如果溶劑太強，化學清潔可以損害表面。"},{"en":"Chemical cleaning means cleaning by using chemical substances to dissolve or loosen dirt, paint or stains.","zh":"chemical cleaning 指使用化學物質溶解或鬆開污垢、油漆或污漬的清潔方式。"},{"en":"A cleaner may use chemical cleaning to remove grease from a kitchen wall.","zh":"清潔工可能使用化學清潔去除廚房牆上的油脂。"},{"en":"Strong chemicals can work quickly, but they may harm delicate materials.","zh":"強力化學品可以快速有效，但可能傷害脆弱物料。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to cleaning through chemical action rather than physical scraping.","zh":"這個短語指透過化學作用清潔，而不是物理刮擦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the benefit of a precautionary measure","meaning":"預防措施的好處","examples":[{"en":"A trial patch demonstrates the benefit of a precautionary measure.","zh":"試驗區顯示預防措施的好處。"},{"en":"The benefit of a precautionary measure is the useful protection gained by acting carefully before risk occurs.","zh":"benefit of a precautionary measure 是風險發生前小心行動所帶來的保護作用。"},{"en":"Testing a new cleaner on a hidden corner shows the benefit of a precautionary measure.","zh":"在隱蔽角落測試新清潔劑，能顯示預防措施的好處。"},{"en":"Precautions can prevent expensive mistakes before they spread widely.","zh":"預防措施可以在錯誤大範圍擴散前防止昂貴失誤。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the value of careful prevention.","zh":"這個短語重點在小心預防的價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"gentle removal","meaning":"溫和清除","examples":[{"en":"A protective coating allows gentler removal of graffiti.","zh":"保護塗層容許較溫和清除塗鴉。"},{"en":"Gentle removal means taking something away with less force and lower risk of damage.","zh":"gentle removal 指以較少力度和較低損害風險移除某物。"},{"en":"A teacher may remove tape gently from a student’s poster so the paper does not tear.","zh":"老師可能溫和地從學生海報上撕下膠紙，以免紙張撕裂。"},{"en":"Gentle removal is important when the surface underneath is delicate.","zh":"當底下表面脆弱，溫和清除很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful cleaning rather than harsh scraping.","zh":"這個短語描述小心清潔，而不是強力刮擦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"damaging cumulative impact","meaning":"逐漸累積的破壞性影響","examples":[{"en":"Repeated cleaning can have a damaging cumulative impact on a surface.","zh":"反覆清潔可以對表面造成逐漸累積的破壞性影響。"},{"en":"A damaging cumulative impact is harm that builds up gradually after repeated actions.","zh":"damaging cumulative impact 是反覆行動後逐漸累積的傷害。"},{"en":"Rubbing a phone screen too hard every day may have a damaging cumulative impact.","zh":"每天太用力擦手機螢幕，可能造成逐漸累積的破壞性影響。"},{"en":"Small amounts of damage may seem harmless at first but become serious over time.","zh":"少量損害起初可能看似無害，但隨時間會變嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses harm caused by accumulation.","zh":"這個短語強調由累積造成的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"involve the police","meaning":"讓警方介入","examples":[{"en":"Building owners are advised to involve the police after an attack.","zh":"建築物業主被建議在受到破壞後讓警方介入。"},{"en":"To involve the police means to report the matter to them and let them take part.","zh":"involve the police 指向警方舉報並讓他們參與處理。"},{"en":"A shop owner may involve the police after repeated thefts.","zh":"商店老闆可能在多次盜竊後讓警方介入。"},{"en":"Police involvement can help identify patterns, collect evidence and discourage further offences.","zh":"警方介入可以幫助辨認模式、收集證據和阻止進一步罪行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bringing law enforcement into a situation.","zh":"這個短語描述把執法部門帶入某情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the reasons for removing graffiti promptly","meaning":"盡快清除塗鴉的原因","examples":[{"en":"The passage gives several reasons for removing graffiti promptly.","zh":"文章給出幾個盡快清除塗鴉的原因。"},{"en":"The reasons for removing graffiti promptly are the explanations for why it should be cleaned quickly.","zh":"reasons for removing graffiti promptly 是解釋為何應快速清理塗鴉的原因。"},{"en":"A council may remove graffiti promptly to prevent imitation and reduce public offence.","zh":"地方議會可能盡快清除塗鴉，以防止模仿並減少公眾冒犯感。"},{"en":"Quick removal also helps because paint becomes harder to clean when it dries.","zh":"快速清除也有幫助，因為油漆乾後會更難清潔。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on why speed matters in graffiti removal.","zh":"這個短語重點在為何速度對清除塗鴉重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"concerning the removal of","meaning":"關於清除……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which statements are true concerning the removal of graffiti.","zh":"題目問哪些陳述關於清除塗鴉是正確的。"},{"en":"Concerning the removal of something means about the process of taking it away.","zh":"concerning the removal of 某物，指關於移除它的過程。"},{"en":"A notice concerning the removal of old lockers should explain the date and reason.","zh":"關於清除舊儲物櫃的通知應解釋日期和原因。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows attention to one topic within a larger passage.","zh":"這個短語把注意力收窄到較長文章中的一個主題。"},{"en":"It is a formal way to say “about removing.”","zh":"它是 “about removing” 的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be safer than","meaning":"比……更安全","examples":[{"en":"Water is not always safer than every chemical treatment.","zh":"清水不一定比每種化學處理都更安全。"},{"en":"To be safer than something means to involve less risk or danger than it.","zh":"be safer than 某物，指比它涉及較少風險或危險。"},{"en":"Walking on a lit main road may be safer than taking a dark shortcut at night.","zh":"夜晚走有燈的主路，可能比走黑暗捷徑更安全。"},{"en":"Safety depends on context, so the safer option is not always obvious.","zh":"安全取決於語境，所以更安全的選項不一定明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase compares levels of risk.","zh":"這個短語比較風險程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a small test patch","meaning":"小面積測試區","examples":[{"en":"A small test patch should be tried before full cleaning begins.","zh":"在全面清潔開始前，應先試用小面積測試區。"},{"en":"A small test patch is a limited area used to test a treatment before applying it widely.","zh":"small test patch 是在大範圍施用前用來測試處理方法的小區域。"},{"en":"A painter may use a small test patch to check whether a colour suits the wall.","zh":"油漆工可能使用小面積測試區，查看顏色是否適合牆面。"},{"en":"Testing a patch first can reveal damage before the whole surface is affected.","zh":"先測試小區域可以在整個表面受影響前揭示損害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a cautious trial area.","zh":"這個短語描述謹慎的試驗區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"large-scale removal","meaning":"大規模清除","examples":[{"en":"Testing is advisable before large-scale removal.","zh":"在大規模清除前，進行測試是明智的。"},{"en":"Large-scale removal means removing something over a wide area or in a major operation.","zh":"large-scale removal 指在大範圍或大型行動中移除某物。"},{"en":"A city may plan large-scale removal of posters from public walls after an election.","zh":"選舉後，城市可能計劃大規模清除公共牆上的海報。"},{"en":"Large-scale work carries higher risk because mistakes affect more surfaces.","zh":"大規模工作風險較高，因為錯誤會影響更多表面。"},{"en":"The phrase describes removal that is broad, extensive or major.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛、大範圍或大型清除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the most expensive removal method","meaning":"最昂貴的清除方法","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not identify the most expensive removal method.","zh":"文章沒有指出最昂貴的清除方法。"},{"en":"The most expensive removal method is the method that costs more than all the others.","zh":"most expensive removal method 是比所有其他方法成本更高的清除方法。"},{"en":"A school may reject the most expensive cleaning method if a cheaper one works safely.","zh":"如果較便宜方法能安全有效，學校可能拒絕最昂貴的清潔方法。"},{"en":"Knowing cost matters because budgets limit what organisations can do.","zh":"知道成本很重要，因為預算限制機構能做甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase compares methods by price.","zh":"這個短語按價格比較方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"risks with both methods","meaning":"兩種方法均有風險","examples":[{"en":"There are risks with both chemical and mechanical methods.","zh":"化學及機械兩種方法均有風險。"},{"en":"Risks with both methods means each of the two approaches can cause problems or harm.","zh":"risks with both methods 指兩種方法各自都可能造成問題或傷害。"},{"en":"Both driving and cycling have risks if road users ignore safety rules.","zh":"如果道路使用者忽視安全規則，駕駛和踏單車兩者均有風險。"},{"en":"Comparing risks helps people choose the least harmful option.","zh":"比較風險幫助人選擇傷害最少的選項。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that neither method is automatically safe.","zh":"這個短語提醒人兩種方法都不自動安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be more suitable than","meaning":"比……更適合","examples":[{"en":"Mechanical cleaning is not automatically more suitable than chemical treatment.","zh":"機械清潔不會自動比化學處理更適合。"},{"en":"To be more suitable than something means to fit the situation better than it.","zh":"be more suitable than 某物，指比它更符合情況。"},{"en":"Online lessons may be more suitable than face-to-face lessons for a sick student at home.","zh":"對在家生病的學生來說，網上課可能比面授課更適合。"},{"en":"Suitability depends on the goal, the people involved and the risks.","zh":"適合程度取決於目標、涉及的人和風險。"},{"en":"The phrase compares how appropriate two options are.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個選項的合適程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"preventive measures against graffiti","meaning":"防止塗鴉的措施","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes several preventive measures against graffiti.","zh":"文章描述幾項防止塗鴉的措施。"},{"en":"Preventive measures against graffiti are actions taken to stop graffiti from happening or returning.","zh":"preventive measures against graffiti 是為阻止塗鴉發生或重現而採取的行動。"},{"en":"Better lighting, cameras and protective coatings can be preventive measures against graffiti.","zh":"改善照明、攝影機和保護塗層都可以是防止塗鴉的措施。"},{"en":"Prevention reduces the need for repeated cleaning and repair.","zh":"預防減少反覆清潔和維修的需要。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on stopping graffiti before it appears.","zh":"這個短語重點在塗鴉出現前阻止它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"anti-graffiti campaigns","meaning":"反塗鴉運動","examples":[{"en":"Community groups sometimes organise anti-graffiti campaigns.","zh":"社區團體有時組織反塗鴉運動。"},{"en":"Anti-graffiti campaigns are organised efforts to reduce graffiti through education, cleaning or enforcement.","zh":"anti-graffiti campaigns 是透過教育、清潔或執法減少塗鴉的有組織努力。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood may run an anti-graffiti campaign by painting murals with permission.","zh":"社區可能透過在獲許可下繪畫壁畫來推行反塗鴉運動。"},{"en":"Campaigns can change behaviour by involving schools, residents and local businesses.","zh":"運動可以透過讓學校、居民和本地企業參與來改變行為。"},{"en":"The phrase describes public action against graffiti.","zh":"這個短語描述反對塗鴉的公共行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"increase police patrols","meaning":"增加警方巡邏","examples":[{"en":"Some communities propose increasing police patrols.","zh":"有些社區建議增加警方巡邏。"},{"en":"To increase police patrols means to have police check an area more often.","zh":"increase police patrols 指讓警方更頻繁檢查某區域。"},{"en":"A district may increase police patrols after several bicycle thefts.","zh":"一區在幾宗單車盜竊後可能增加警方巡邏。"},{"en":"More patrols can deter crime, but they require time, staff and money.","zh":"更多巡邏可以阻嚇罪案，但需要時間、人手和金錢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stronger police presence in an area.","zh":"這個短語描述加強某區域的警力存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"water-repellent materials","meaning":"防水物料","examples":[{"en":"Water-repellent materials can protect some exterior surfaces.","zh":"防水物料可以保護某些外部表面。"},{"en":"Water-repellent materials are materials that resist water and stop it from soaking in easily.","zh":"water-repellent materials 是能抗水並阻止水容易滲入的材料。"},{"en":"A raincoat is made from water-repellent material to keep the wearer dry.","zh":"雨衣由防水物料製成，以保持穿着者乾爽。"},{"en":"On buildings, such materials can reduce water damage and make some stains easier to clean.","zh":"在建築物上，這類物料可以減少水損，並令某些污漬較易清除。"},{"en":"The phrase describes materials designed to resist water.","zh":"這個短語描述為抗水而設計的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"visible security cameras","meaning":"顯眼的保安攝影機","examples":[{"en":"Visible security cameras can discourage anti-social behaviour.","zh":"顯眼的保安攝影機可以阻止反社會行為。"},{"en":"Visible security cameras are cameras placed where people can clearly see them.","zh":"visible security cameras 是放在人們清楚看得見位置的攝影機。"},{"en":"A shop may put visible security cameras near the entrance to reduce theft.","zh":"商店可能在入口附近放置顯眼的保安攝影機以減少盜竊。"},{"en":"When offenders see cameras, they may fear being identified.","zh":"當犯事者看見攝影機，他們可能害怕被辨認。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the camera’s visibility is part of its deterrent effect.","zh":"這個短語強調攝影機的可見性是其阻嚇效果的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"apply a chemical coating","meaning":"塗上化學保護層","examples":[{"en":"A protective chemical coating can be applied to a vulnerable surface.","zh":"可以在容易受破壞的表面塗上化學保護層。"},{"en":"To apply a chemical coating means to put a protective chemical layer onto a surface.","zh":"apply a chemical coating 指在表面加上一層保護性化學層。"},{"en":"A worker may apply a chemical coating to a wall before graffiti becomes a problem.","zh":"工人可能在塗鴉成為問題前，先在牆上塗上化學保護層。"},{"en":"The coating can make later cleaning easier and less damaging.","zh":"該塗層可以令之後清潔更容易且較少損害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adding a protective chemical layer.","zh":"這個短語描述加入保護性化學層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the entire surface","meaning":"整個表面","examples":[{"en":"The treatment may need to cover the entire surface.","zh":"處理方法可能需要覆蓋整個表面。"},{"en":"The entire surface means the whole outside area, not just one small part.","zh":"entire surface 指整個外部範圍，而不只是一小部分。"},{"en":"A painter must cover the entire surface of a wall if the colour is to look even.","zh":"如果要顏色看起來均勻，油漆工必須覆蓋整面牆的表面。"},{"en":"If only part is treated, untreated areas may still be vulnerable.","zh":"如果只處理一部分，未處理位置仍可能容易受損。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses complete coverage.","zh":"這個短語強調完整覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的詞語完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill in missing words in a shortened version of the text.","zh":"complete the summary 指在文本的簡短版本中填上缺失詞語。"},{"en":"In a reading exam, students complete a summary by finding exact words from the passage.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生透過從文章找出原詞來完成摘要。"},{"en":"They must understand the main idea and also check grammar around each blank.","zh":"他們必須理解主旨，也要檢查每個空格前後的文法。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction in reading-completion tasks.","zh":"這個短語是閱讀填空題的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不超過兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer must contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案必須不超過兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means one or two words only, not three or more.","zh":"no more than two words 指只可一個或兩個英文詞，不可三個或以上。"},{"en":"If the answer is “protective coating,” it fits because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “protective coating”，它符合要求，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing too many words can make an otherwise correct answer wrong.","zh":"寫太多詞可以令本來正確的答案變錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語在考試指示中給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"record the social history of","meaning":"記錄……的社會史","examples":[{"en":"Ancient graffiti can record the social history of an earlier period.","zh":"古代塗鴉可以記錄較早時期的社會史。"},{"en":"To record the social history of something means to preserve evidence of ordinary people’s daily life and behaviour.","zh":"record the social history of 某事，指保存普通人日常生活和行為的證據。"},{"en":"Old market posters can record the social history of food prices and shopping habits.","zh":"舊市場海報可以記錄食物價格和購物習慣的社會史。"},{"en":"Such records help historians understand people who may not appear in official documents.","zh":"這類記錄幫助歷史學家了解未必出現在官方文件中的人。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on everyday life in the past.","zh":"這個短語重點在過去的日常生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"recognise graffiti by its signature","meaning":"從簽名辨認塗鴉","examples":[{"en":"The police may recognise graffiti by its distinctive signature.","zh":"警方可能從獨特簽名辨認塗鴉。"},{"en":"To recognise graffiti by its signature means to identify it from the special tag or style used.","zh":"recognise graffiti by its signature 指透過所用的特別簽名式塗鴉或風格辨認它。"},{"en":"A teacher may recognise a student’s drawing by its repeated cartoon face.","zh":"老師可能透過反覆出現的卡通臉辨認某學生的畫。"},{"en":"Repeated signatures help link separate pieces of graffiti to the same writer.","zh":"重複簽名有助把分開的塗鴉與同一作者連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes identifying something through a unique mark.","zh":"這個短語描述透過獨特標記辨認某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"comply with relevant rules","meaning":"遵守相關規則","examples":[{"en":"Cleaning operatives must comply with relevant rules.","zh":"清潔技術人員必須遵守相關規則。"},{"en":"To comply with relevant rules means to follow the rules that apply to the situation.","zh":"comply with relevant rules 指遵從適用於該情況的規則。"},{"en":"A laboratory student must comply with relevant rules before using chemicals.","zh":"實驗室學生使用化學品前，必須遵守相關規則。"},{"en":"Following rules protects workers, the public and the surface being treated.","zh":"遵守規則能保護工人、公眾和正在處理的表面。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses legal or procedural obedience.","zh":"這個短語強調法律或程序上的服從。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"suitable protective equipment","meaning":"合適的防護裝備","examples":[{"en":"Operatives must wear suitable protective equipment.","zh":"技術人員必須穿戴合適的防護裝備。"},{"en":"Suitable protective equipment is safety gear appropriate for the danger involved.","zh":"suitable protective equipment 是適合相關危險的安全裝備。"},{"en":"A cyclist needs suitable protective equipment such as a helmet and lights.","zh":"單車手需要頭盔和車燈等合適防護裝備。"},{"en":"The wrong equipment may give a false sense of safety.","zh":"錯誤裝備可能給人錯誤安全感。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to protection that matches the real risk.","zh":"這個短語指配合真實風險的保護用品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a coated surface","meaning":"有保護塗層的表面","examples":[{"en":"Graffiti is easier to remove from a coated surface.","zh":"塗鴉較容易從有保護塗層的表面清除。"},{"en":"A coated surface is a surface covered with a protective layer.","zh":"coated surface 是覆蓋了保護層的表面。"},{"en":"A coated table may resist stains better than untreated wood.","zh":"有保護塗層的桌子可能比未處理木材更能抵抗污漬。"},{"en":"The coating separates dirt or paint from the original material underneath.","zh":"塗層把污垢或油漆與下面原有物料隔開。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a protected surface, not a bare one.","zh":"這個短語描述受保護的表面，而不是裸露表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"remove something more conveniently","meaning":"更方便地清除……","examples":[{"en":"A protective layer allows graffiti to be removed more conveniently.","zh":"保護層讓塗鴉能更方便地被清除。"},{"en":"To remove something more conveniently means to take it away more easily, quickly or with less difficulty.","zh":"remove something more conveniently 指更容易、更快速或較少困難地移除某物。"},{"en":"A removable phone case lets users clean dust more conveniently.","zh":"可拆式手機殼讓使用者更方便地清除灰塵。"},{"en":"If graffiti does not stick directly to the surface, workers can remove it with less effort.","zh":"如果塗鴉沒有直接黏在表面上，工人就能較省力地清除它。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on making removal simpler and more practical.","zh":"這個短語重點在令清除更簡單和更實際。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 126 - Is Graffiti Art or Crime.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 127":[{"front":"the Mpemba Effect","meaning":"姆潘巴效應","examples":[{"en":"The Mpemba Effect describes situations in which warmer water freezes faster than colder water.","zh":"姆潘巴效應描述較暖的水比較冷的水更快結冰的情況。"},{"en":"The Mpemba Effect is a surprising phenomenon in which hot or warm water may become ice sooner than cooler water.","zh":"姆潘巴效應是一種令人驚訝的現象，其中熱水或暖水可能比冷水更早變成冰。"},{"en":"If two bowls of water are put in a freezer, the warmer bowl may sometimes freeze first because of the Mpemba Effect.","zh":"如果兩碗水被放進冰格，較暖的那碗有時可能因姆潘巴效應而先結冰。"},{"en":"The Mpemba Effect can happen only under certain conditions, so it does not mean hot water always freezes faster.","zh":"姆潘巴效應只會在某些條件下出現，因此並不表示熱水總是更快結冰。"},{"en":"This effect is counter-intuitive because most people expect colder water to freeze first.","zh":"這個效應違反直覺，因為大多數人預期較冷的水會先結冰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"famous philosopher","meaning":"著名哲學家","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle was a famous philosopher who wrote about the phenomenon.","zh":"亞里士多德是一位著名哲學家，曾寫及這個現象。"},{"en":"A famous philosopher is a well-known thinker who studies big questions about life, knowledge, nature, or reality.","zh":"著名哲學家是研究人生、知識、自然或現實等重大問題的知名思想家。"},{"en":"A student may learn about famous philosophers such as Aristotle or Plato in a history lesson.","zh":"學生可能在歷史課中學到亞里士多德或柏拉圖等著名哲學家。"},{"en":"Famous philosophers can influence later science because their observations and questions encourage further investigation.","zh":"著名哲學家可以影響後來的科學，因為他們的觀察和問題會鼓勵進一步研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone known for deep thinking, not simply someone who is famous.","zh":"這個短語描述以深刻思考聞名的人，而不只是有名的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"strange phenomenon","meaning":"奇怪現象","examples":[{"en":"Aristotle described a strange phenomenon involving the cooling of water.","zh":"亞里士多德描述了一個涉及水冷卻的奇怪現象。"},{"en":"A strange phenomenon is an event or pattern that seems unusual and difficult to explain.","zh":"奇怪現象是看起來不尋常且難以解釋的事件或模式。"},{"en":"Warm water freezing faster than cold water is a strange phenomenon because it goes against common sense.","zh":"暖水比冷水更快結冰是一種奇怪現象，因為它違反常識。"},{"en":"Strange phenomena often lead scientists to design experiments and test possible explanations.","zh":"奇怪現象常會促使科學家設計實驗並測試可能解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when something happens in a way people do not expect.","zh":"當某事以人們意想不到的方式發生時，就可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"observe a phenomenon","meaning":"觀察到某種現象","examples":[{"en":"Several philosophers observed the same phenomenon over the centuries.","zh":"幾位哲學家在數個世紀中觀察到相同現象。"},{"en":"To observe a phenomenon means to notice and record something that happens in the real world.","zh":"觀察到某種現象，是指注意並記錄現實世界中發生的事情。"},{"en":"A student may observe a phenomenon when salt makes ice melt faster on a cold day.","zh":"學生可能在寒冷日子看見鹽令冰更快融化時，觀察到某種現象。"},{"en":"Repeatedly observing a phenomenon can help people decide whether it is real or just a mistake.","zh":"反覆觀察某種現象，可以幫助人們判斷它是真實存在還是只是錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in science because observation is often the first step before explanation.","zh":"這個短語常見於科學，因為觀察通常是解釋之前的第一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cool water quickly","meaning":"迅速冷卻水","examples":[{"en":"Some people heated water before trying to cool it quickly.","zh":"有些人在嘗試迅速冷卻水之前先把水加熱。"},{"en":"To cool water quickly means to make the temperature of water fall rapidly.","zh":"迅速冷卻水，是指令水的溫度快速下降。"},{"en":"You can cool water quickly by putting it in a fridge or adding ice cubes.","zh":"你可以把水放進雪櫃或加入冰塊，從而迅速冷卻水。"},{"en":"Water may cool more quickly when there is a large temperature difference between the water and the surrounding air.","zh":"當水和周圍空氣之間有很大溫差時，水可能冷卻得更快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of reducing water temperature, not necessarily freezing it completely.","zh":"這個短語描述降低水溫的過程，而不一定是完全結冰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"begin by doing something","meaning":"先做某事","examples":[{"en":"They began by putting the water in the sun.","zh":"他們先把水放在陽光下。"},{"en":"To begin by doing something means to start a process with that first action.","zh":"先做某事，是指以該第一個行動開始一個過程。"},{"en":"A science teacher may begin by asking students to record the starting temperature.","zh":"科學老師可能先要求學生記錄起始溫度。"},{"en":"Beginning with careful measurement helps make an experiment fairer and easier to compare.","zh":"先進行仔細測量，有助令實驗更公平，也更容易比較。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining steps in a method or procedure.","zh":"這個短語適合用來解釋方法或程序中的步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"over the ages","meaning":"歷代以來","examples":[{"en":"Other philosophers over the ages recorded similar observations.","zh":"歷代以來，其他哲學家也記錄了類似觀察。"},{"en":"Over the ages means across a very long period of history.","zh":"歷代以來，是指橫跨很長一段歷史時期。"},{"en":"Over the ages, people have noticed many natural events that they could not immediately explain.","zh":"歷代以來，人們注意到許多一時無法解釋的自然事件。"},{"en":"When the same idea appears over the ages, it suggests that many people have found it worth recording.","zh":"當同一想法歷代以來反覆出現，這暗示很多人都認為它值得記錄。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a sense of long historical continuity.","zh":"這個短語帶出長久歷史延續感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"note the same result","meaning":"記錄到相同結果","examples":[{"en":"Several thinkers noted the same result but could not explain it.","zh":"幾位思想家記錄到相同結果，但無法解釋。"},{"en":"To note the same result means to record or recognise the same outcome.","zh":"記錄到相同結果，是指記下或察覺同一個結果。"},{"en":"In a school experiment, two groups may note the same result even if they use different bowls.","zh":"在學校實驗中，兩組學生即使用不同的碗，也可能記錄到相同結果。"},{"en":"When many observers note the same result, the finding becomes harder to dismiss.","zh":"當許多觀察者記錄到相同結果，該發現就較難被否定。"},{"en":"This phrase connects repeated observation with possible evidence.","zh":"這個短語把反覆觀察與可能證據連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be unable to explain","meaning":"無法解釋","examples":[{"en":"Early philosophers were unable to explain the surprising effect.","zh":"早期哲學家無法解釋這個令人驚訝的效應。"},{"en":"To be unable to explain something means not to know why it happens.","zh":"無法解釋某事，是指不知道它為何發生。"},{"en":"A student may be unable to explain why one plant grows faster than another without checking light and water.","zh":"如果沒有檢查光線和水分，學生可能無法解釋為何一株植物比另一株長得快。"},{"en":"Being unable to explain a result often leads researchers to test more variables.","zh":"無法解釋某個結果，往往會令研究人員測試更多變數。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a limit in understanding, not necessarily a mistake.","zh":"這個短語顯示理解上的限制，而不一定是錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"young Tanzanian student","meaning":"年輕的坦桑尼亞學生","examples":[{"en":"Erasto Mpemba was a young Tanzanian student.","zh":"Erasto Mpemba 是一名年輕的坦桑尼亞學生。"},{"en":"A young Tanzanian student is a student from Tanzania who is still young.","zh":"年輕的坦桑尼亞學生，是指來自坦桑尼亞、年紀尚輕的學生。"},{"en":"A young Tanzanian student may notice something important in a classroom experiment.","zh":"一名年輕的坦桑尼亞學生也可能在課堂實驗中注意到重要現象。"},{"en":"Mpemba’s example shows that scientific questions can come from students, not only professors.","zh":"Mpemba 的例子顯示，科學問題可以來自學生，而不只是教授。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies Mpemba’s age, nationality, and role.","zh":"這個短語指出 Mpemba 的年齡、國籍和身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"notice that","meaning":"注意到","examples":[{"en":"Mpemba noticed that his warm ice-cream mixture froze unusually quickly.","zh":"Mpemba 注意到他的暖雪糕混合物異常快速地冷凍。"},{"en":"To notice that something happens means to become aware of it.","zh":"注意到某事，是指意識到它發生。"},{"en":"A child may notice that wet clothes dry faster in the sun than indoors.","zh":"小朋友可能注意到濕衣服在陽光下比在室內更快乾。"},{"en":"Careful noticing can lead to useful questions because it turns small details into evidence.","zh":"仔細注意可以帶來有用問題，因為它把小細節變成證據。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces something observed by a person.","zh":"這個短語引入某人觀察到的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"freeze faster","meaning":"冷凍得更快","examples":[{"en":"The warm mixture appeared to freeze faster than the cooler mixture.","zh":"較暖的混合物看似比較冷的混合物冷凍得更快。"},{"en":"To freeze faster means to become solid ice in less time.","zh":"冷凍得更快，是指用較少時間變成固體冰。"},{"en":"In a freezer, a thin layer of water may freeze faster than a deep cup of water.","zh":"在冰格中，一層薄水可能比一杯深水冷凍得更快。"},{"en":"Water may freeze faster if it loses heat quickly through its surface and container.","zh":"如果水透過表面和容器迅速失去熱量，它可能冷凍得更快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes freezing speed, not simply how cold the water feels.","zh":"這個短語描述結冰速度，而不只是水感覺有多冷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ice-cream mixture","meaning":"雪糕混合物","examples":[{"en":"Mpemba placed the warm ice-cream mixture directly in the freezer.","zh":"Mpemba 把暖的雪糕混合物直接放進冰格。"},{"en":"An ice-cream mixture is the liquid or semi-liquid mixture used before it becomes ice cream.","zh":"雪糕混合物是變成雪糕之前的液體或半液體混合物。"},{"en":"At home, an ice-cream mixture may contain milk, sugar, cream, and flavouring.","zh":"在家中，雪糕混合物可能含有牛奶、糖、忌廉和調味料。"},{"en":"If the ice-cream mixture is still warm, it may affect the freezer and the freezing process.","zh":"如果雪糕混合物仍然溫暖，它可能影響冰格和冷凍過程。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the material being frozen, not the finished ice cream.","zh":"這個短語指被冷凍的材料，而不是已完成的雪糕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be placed in the freezer","meaning":"被放進冰格","examples":[{"en":"The mixture was placed in the freezer while it was still warm.","zh":"混合物仍然溫暖時被放進冰格。"},{"en":"To be placed in the freezer means to be put inside the part of a fridge that freezes food or liquid.","zh":"被放進冰格，是指被放入雪櫃中能冷凍食物或液體的部分。"},{"en":"Ice trays are placed in the freezer so that liquid water can become ice cubes.","zh":"冰格被用來放冰格盤，讓液態水變成冰塊。"},{"en":"If two samples are placed in the freezer at different times, the comparison may be unfair.","zh":"如果兩個樣本在不同時間被放進冰格，比較可能不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the action of putting something into a cold freezing space.","zh":"這個短語描述把某物放入寒冷冷凍空間的動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at room temperature","meaning":"在室溫下","examples":[{"en":"The cooler mixture was already at room temperature.","zh":"較冷的混合物已在室溫下。"},{"en":"At room temperature means at the normal temperature of the surrounding room, without heating or cooling.","zh":"在室溫下，是指處於周圍房間的正常溫度，沒有加熱或冷卻。"},{"en":"A cup of tea left on a table for an hour may cool to room temperature.","zh":"一杯茶放在桌上一小時後，可能冷卻至室溫。"},{"en":"Starting at room temperature gives a sample less heat to lose than a hot sample.","zh":"從室溫開始的樣本，需要散失的熱量比熱樣本少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a moderate temperature, not a fixed exact number in every room.","zh":"這個短語描述中等溫度，而不是每個房間都固定的精確數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"persist in questioning","meaning":"堅持追問","examples":[{"en":"Mpemba persisted in questioning why the result occurred.","zh":"Mpemba 堅持追問為何會出現這個結果。"},{"en":"To persist in questioning means to continue asking about something even when others ignore or reject the question.","zh":"堅持追問，是指即使別人忽視或否定問題，仍繼續發問。"},{"en":"A student may persist in questioning a maths answer if the method does not make sense.","zh":"如果計算方法不合理，學生可能會堅持追問一道數學答案。"},{"en":"Persistence can turn a small classroom puzzle into a serious investigation.","zh":"堅持可以把一個小小課堂謎團變成認真調查。"},{"en":"This phrase shows curiosity, confidence, and refusal to give up.","zh":"這個短語顯示好奇心、信心和不放棄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"eventually","meaning":"最終","examples":[{"en":"Eventually, a physicist began to investigate the observation seriously.","zh":"最終，一位物理學家開始認真調查這項觀察。"},{"en":"Eventually means after some time or after several earlier events.","zh":"最終，是指經過一段時間或幾件較早事件之後。"},{"en":"A student may ask the same question many times, and eventually a teacher may test it with the class.","zh":"學生可能多次問同一問題，最終老師會和全班一起測試它。"},{"en":"This word shows that the result did not happen immediately.","zh":"這個詞顯示結果並非立即發生。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing a process that develops slowly.","zh":"它適合描述慢慢發展的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"serious investigation into","meaning":"對……進行認真調查","examples":[{"en":"Denis Osborne began a serious investigation into the phenomenon.","zh":"Denis Osborne 開始對這個現象進行認真調查。"},{"en":"A serious investigation into something is a careful and systematic attempt to understand it.","zh":"對某事進行認真調查，是指仔細而有系統地嘗試理解它。"},{"en":"A doctor may begin a serious investigation into repeated stomach pain if simple explanations do not work.","zh":"如果簡單解釋不成立，醫生可能會對反覆胃痛進行認真調查。"},{"en":"Serious investigation can reveal which possible causes are important and which are not.","zh":"認真調查可以揭示哪些可能原因重要、哪些不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal study, not casual guessing.","zh":"這個短語描述正式研究，而不是隨意猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be known as","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"The phenomenon is now known as the Mpemba Effect.","zh":"這個現象現在被稱為姆潘巴效應。"},{"en":"To be known as something means to be called by that name.","zh":"被稱為某物，是指以該名稱命名或稱呼。"},{"en":"The building is known as the old town hall because it once housed the local government.","zh":"這座建築被稱為舊市政廳，因為它曾是地方政府所在地。"},{"en":"A scientific phenomenon may become known as the name of the person who made it famous.","zh":"一個科學現象可能以令它成名的人命名。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the name or label used for something.","zh":"這個短語引入某事物所使用的名稱或標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"co-author a paper","meaning":"合著一篇論文","examples":[{"en":"Mpemba and Osborne co-authored a scientific paper.","zh":"Mpemba 和 Osborne 合著一篇科學論文。"},{"en":"To co-author a paper means to write an academic article together with another person.","zh":"合著一篇論文，是指與另一人共同撰寫學術文章。"},{"en":"A student and a professor may co-author a paper after completing a successful experiment.","zh":"學生和教授完成成功實驗後，可能合著一篇論文。"},{"en":"Co-authoring a paper shows that both people contributed to the research.","zh":"合著論文顯示雙方都對研究有貢獻。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in academic contexts when more than one person writes the same study.","zh":"這個短語用於多於一人共同撰寫同一項研究的學術語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"scientific descriptions of","meaning":"對……的科學描述","examples":[{"en":"Their paper provided scientific descriptions of several possible factors.","zh":"他們的論文提供了對幾個可能因素的科學描述。"},{"en":"Scientific descriptions of something explain it using evidence, measurement, and scientific ideas.","zh":"對某事的科學描述，是使用證據、測量和科學概念來解釋它。"},{"en":"A textbook may give scientific descriptions of evaporation, condensation, and freezing.","zh":"教科書可能對蒸發、凝結和結冰作出科學描述。"},{"en":"Scientific descriptions help people understand why an effect may happen, not just that it happens.","zh":"科學描述幫助人們理解某效應為何可能發生，而不只是知道它發生。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to evidence-based explanation.","zh":"這個短語指基於證據的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"factors at work","meaning":"起作用的因素","examples":[{"en":"Many different factors may be at work when water freezes.","zh":"水結冰時可能有許多不同因素起作用。"},{"en":"Factors at work are causes or influences that are operating in a situation.","zh":"起作用的因素，是在某情況中正在發揮影響的原因或力量。"},{"en":"If a student performs poorly, stress, sleep, and preparation may all be factors at work.","zh":"如果學生表現差，壓力、睡眠和準備都可能是起作用的因素。"},{"en":"In freezing water, several factors at work can make the result different from what people expect.","zh":"在水結冰時，幾個起作用的因素可以令結果不同於人們預期。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a situation has more than one possible cause.","zh":"當某情況有多於一個可能原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"initially hypothesised","meaning":"最初被假設","examples":[{"en":"It was initially hypothesised that the warm bowl melted the ice beneath it.","zh":"最初有人假設暖碗融化了下面的冰。"},{"en":"Initially hypothesised means first suggested as a possible explanation before further testing.","zh":"最初被假設，是指在進一步測試前，最早被提出作為可能解釋。"},{"en":"Doctors initially hypothesised that the illness was caused by food, but later tests showed it was a virus.","zh":"醫生最初假設病因是食物，但後來測試顯示是病毒。"},{"en":"An idea that is initially hypothesised may later be supported, rejected, or changed.","zh":"最初被假設的想法，後來可能被支持、否定或修改。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an early scientific guess.","zh":"這個短語描述早期科學推測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"melt itself a place","meaning":"融出一個位置","examples":[{"en":"The warm container appeared to melt itself a place in the ice.","zh":"暖容器看似在冰中為自己融出一個位置。"},{"en":"To melt itself a place means to melt nearby ice and create a small hollow where something can sit.","zh":"融出一個位置，是指融化附近的冰，形成一個可放置的小凹位。"},{"en":"A hot cup placed on snow may melt itself a place and sink slightly.","zh":"熱杯放在雪上，可能會融出一個位置並稍微下陷。"},{"en":"This could increase contact between the container and the cold surface.","zh":"這可能增加容器與冷表面的接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a vivid picture of heat changing the ice underneath.","zh":"這個短語生動描繪熱量改變下方冰面的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"freezer shelf","meaning":"冰格層架","examples":[{"en":"The bowl rested directly on the freezer shelf.","zh":"碗直接放在冰格層架上。"},{"en":"A freezer shelf is the rack or surface inside a freezer where food or containers are placed.","zh":"冰格層架是冰格內放置食物或容器的架子或表面。"},{"en":"Ice trays usually sit on a freezer shelf until the water turns into ice.","zh":"冰格盤通常放在冰格層架上，直到水變成冰。"},{"en":"The material and temperature of the freezer shelf may affect how quickly heat leaves a container.","zh":"冰格層架的材料和溫度可能影響熱量離開容器的速度。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the physical surface inside the freezer.","zh":"這個短語指冰格內的實體放置表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"embed its base in","meaning":"把底部嵌入……","examples":[{"en":"The warm bowl embedded its base in a small hollow of ice.","zh":"暖碗把底部嵌入一個小冰凹中。"},{"en":"To embed its base in something means to have its bottom part fitted or pressed into that material.","zh":"把底部嵌入某物，是指底部貼合或壓入該材料之中。"},{"en":"A heavy chair leg may embed its base in soft soil after rain.","zh":"大雨後，沉重椅腳可能把底部嵌入鬆軟泥土中。"},{"en":"If a warm bowl embeds its base in ice, it may seem to touch the cold surface more closely.","zh":"如果暖碗把底部嵌入冰中，它可能看似更緊密接觸冷表面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how the bottom of an object sits inside another material.","zh":"這個短語描述物件底部如何坐落於另一種材料中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a nest of ice","meaning":"冰窩","examples":[{"en":"The bowl appeared to sit in a nest of ice.","zh":"碗看似坐在一個冰窩中。"},{"en":"A nest of ice is a small hollow or surrounding shape of ice around an object.","zh":"冰窩是圍繞物件的小凹位或冰形成的包圍形狀。"},{"en":"A bottle left in melting ice may settle into a nest of ice.","zh":"放在融冰中的瓶子可能會陷入一個冰窩。"},{"en":"A nest of ice might seem to cool the container more effectively by increasing contact.","zh":"冰窩可能看似透過增加接觸而更有效冷卻容器。"},{"en":"This phrase is descriptive and visual, not a technical term.","zh":"這個短語具描寫和視覺效果，不是技術術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"accelerate freezing","meaning":"加速結冰","examples":[{"en":"Researchers wondered whether the ice nest could accelerate freezing.","zh":"研究人員想知道冰窩是否能加速結冰。"},{"en":"To accelerate freezing means to make the freezing process happen faster.","zh":"加速結冰，是指令結冰過程更快發生。"},{"en":"A thin metal tray may accelerate freezing because it helps remove heat quickly.","zh":"薄金屬盤可能加速結冰，因為它幫助快速移走熱量。"},{"en":"If a factor accelerates freezing, the water reaches a solid state sooner.","zh":"如果某因素加速結冰，水會更早達到固體狀態。"},{"en":"This phrase describes anything that speeds up the formation of ice.","zh":"這個短語描述任何加快冰形成的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"test a hypothesis","meaning":"檢驗假設","examples":[{"en":"The researchers tested the hypothesis by changing the surface beneath the bowls.","zh":"研究人員透過改變碗下方的表面來檢驗假設。"},{"en":"To test a hypothesis means to perform an experiment to see whether a possible explanation is supported.","zh":"檢驗假設，是指進行實驗以查看某個可能解釋是否得到支持。"},{"en":"A student can test a hypothesis about plant growth by giving one plant more sunlight than another.","zh":"學生可以透過讓一株植物比另一株得到更多陽光，來檢驗植物生長的假設。"},{"en":"Testing a hypothesis helps show whether an idea is likely to be true or false.","zh":"檢驗假設有助顯示某想法可能是真還是假。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to the scientific method.","zh":"這個短語是科學方法的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"compare the result","meaning":"比較結果","examples":[{"en":"They compared the result under two different conditions.","zh":"他們比較兩種不同條件下的結果。"},{"en":"To compare the result means to look at two or more outcomes side by side.","zh":"比較結果，是指把兩個或多個結果並列檢視。"},{"en":"A class may compare the result of freezing water in a metal cup and a plastic cup.","zh":"一班學生可能比較用金屬杯和膠杯冷凍水的結果。"},{"en":"Comparing results helps identify which condition makes a difference.","zh":"比較結果有助識別哪個條件造成差異。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a basic step in fair experiments.","zh":"這個短語描述公平實驗中的基本步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"dry wire shelf","meaning":"乾燥的金屬網架","examples":[{"en":"One warm bowl was placed on a dry wire shelf.","zh":"一個暖碗被放在乾燥的金屬網架上。"},{"en":"A dry wire shelf is a metal rack without water or ice on it.","zh":"乾燥的金屬網架是沒有水或冰的金屬架。"},{"en":"In a kitchen, cakes may cool on a dry wire shelf after baking.","zh":"在廚房中，蛋糕焗好後可能放在乾燥的金屬網架上冷卻。"},{"en":"Using a dry wire shelf helped researchers test whether ice under the bowl mattered.","zh":"使用乾燥金屬網架有助研究人員測試碗底下的冰是否重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific surface used in the experiment.","zh":"這個短語描述實驗中使用的特定表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"demonstrate that","meaning":"證明","examples":[{"en":"The comparison demonstrated that the ice nest had little effect.","zh":"比較證明冰窩幾乎沒有影響。"},{"en":"To demonstrate that means to show something clearly through evidence or example.","zh":"證明某事，是指透過證據或例子清楚顯示某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may demonstrate that warm air rises by using smoke in a glass tube.","zh":"老師可能用玻璃管中的煙來證明暖空氣會上升。"},{"en":"When an experiment demonstrates that a factor has little effect, that explanation becomes weaker.","zh":"當實驗證明某因素影響很小，該解釋就變得較弱。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a conclusion supported by evidence.","zh":"這個短語引入有證據支持的結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have little effect","meaning":"幾乎沒有影響","examples":[{"en":"The surface beneath the bowl had little effect on the result.","zh":"碗下方的表面對結果幾乎沒有影響。"},{"en":"To have little effect means to make only a small difference.","zh":"幾乎沒有影響，是指只造成很小差異。"},{"en":"Changing the colour of a cup may have little effect on how quickly water freezes.","zh":"改變杯子的顏色可能對水結冰速度幾乎沒有影響。"},{"en":"If a factor has little effect, it is unlikely to be the main cause.","zh":"如果某因素幾乎沒有影響，它不太可能是主要原因。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weak influence.","zh":"這個短語描述微弱影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a second suggestion","meaning":"第二種說法","examples":[{"en":"A second suggestion concerned evaporation from the water surface.","zh":"第二種說法與水面蒸發有關。"},{"en":"A second suggestion is another possible explanation after the first one.","zh":"第二種說法是在第一個解釋之後的另一個可能解釋。"},{"en":"After blaming the freezer shelf, a second suggestion may focus on the amount of water lost.","zh":"在歸因於冰格層架之後，第二種說法可能聚焦水量流失。"},{"en":"Considering a second suggestion helps researchers avoid depending on only one explanation.","zh":"考慮第二種說法有助研究人員避免只依賴一個解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when presenting several hypotheses in order.","zh":"這個短語適合按次序呈現多個假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"evaporate at the surface","meaning":"在表面蒸發","examples":[{"en":"Warm water evaporates more rapidly at the surface.","zh":"暖水在表面蒸發得更快。"},{"en":"To evaporate at the surface means to change from liquid into vapour at the top layer of the water.","zh":"在表面蒸發，是指在水的最上層由液體變成水蒸氣。"},{"en":"Soup left uncovered may evaporate at the surface while it is hot.","zh":"熱湯如果不加蓋，可能會在表面蒸發。"},{"en":"When water evaporates at the surface, the amount of liquid left to freeze becomes smaller.","zh":"當水在表面蒸發，剩下需要結冰的液體量會變少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical change at the boundary between water and air.","zh":"這個短語描述水和空氣交界處的物理變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reduce the volume","meaning":"減少體積","examples":[{"en":"Evaporation reduces the volume of water that needs to freeze.","zh":"蒸發減少需要結冰的水的體積。"},{"en":"To reduce the volume means to make the amount or size smaller.","zh":"減少體積，是指令數量或大小變小。"},{"en":"Boiling soup for too long can reduce the volume of liquid in the pot.","zh":"湯煮太久會減少鍋中液體的體積。"},{"en":"If evaporation reduces the volume of water, there is less liquid left to turn into ice.","zh":"如果蒸發減少水的體積，剩下要變成冰的液體就較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decrease in quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述數量下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"need to be frozen","meaning":"需要被冷凍","examples":[{"en":"A smaller quantity of water needs to be frozen.","zh":"較少量的水需要被冷凍。"},{"en":"Need to be frozen means must become solid ice.","zh":"需要被冷凍，是指必須變成固體冰。"},{"en":"If a cup contains less water, less liquid needs to be frozen before the whole sample becomes solid.","zh":"如果杯中水較少，在整個樣本變成固體前，需要被冷凍的液體也較少。"},{"en":"A smaller amount may freeze sooner because there is less material to cool.","zh":"較少的量可能較早結冰，因為需要冷卻的物質較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the remaining task in the freezing process.","zh":"這個短語描述結冰過程中剩下的任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be shown to be insignificant","meaning":"被證明並不重要","examples":[{"en":"The effect of evaporation was shown to be insignificant.","zh":"蒸發的影響被證明並不重要。"},{"en":"To be shown to be insignificant means evidence showed that something was not important.","zh":"被證明並不重要，是指證據顯示某事不是重要因素。"},{"en":"In an experiment, a small difference in cup colour may be shown to be insignificant.","zh":"在實驗中，杯子顏色的小差異可能被證明並不重要。"},{"en":"If evaporation is insignificant, it cannot fully explain why warmer water freezes first.","zh":"如果蒸發並不重要，它就不能完全解釋為何較暖的水先結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when testing weakens a proposed explanation.","zh":"這個短語用於測試削弱某個可能解釋時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"thermometers placed in","meaning":"放在……中的溫度計","examples":[{"en":"Thermometers placed in the bowls recorded the changing temperatures.","zh":"放在碗中的溫度計記錄變化中的溫度。"},{"en":"Thermometers placed in something are temperature-measuring tools put inside it.","zh":"放在某物中的溫度計，是置於其中的測溫工具。"},{"en":"A nurse may use a thermometer placed under the tongue to check body temperature.","zh":"護士可能使用放在舌下的溫度計來量度體溫。"},{"en":"Thermometers placed in water help researchers see exactly when the temperature changes.","zh":"放在水中的溫度計幫助研究人員準確看見溫度何時改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where the measuring equipment is located.","zh":"這個短語描述測量設備的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"drop to freezing temperature","meaning":"降至冰點","examples":[{"en":"The cooler water dropped to freezing temperature first.","zh":"較冷的水先降至冰點。"},{"en":"To drop to freezing temperature means to cool down to the point where freezing can begin.","zh":"降至冰點，是指冷卻到可以開始結冰的溫度。"},{"en":"Water in a shallow tray may drop to freezing temperature faster than water in a deep cup.","zh":"淺盤中的水可能比深杯中的水更快降至冰點。"},{"en":"Reaching freezing temperature is not always the same as becoming completely solid.","zh":"達到冰點不一定等於完全變成固體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fall in temperature to the freezing point.","zh":"這個短語描述溫度下降到冰點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"well before","meaning":"遠早於","examples":[{"en":"The cooler bowl reached zero degrees well before the warmer one.","zh":"較冷的碗遠早於較暖的碗達到零度。"},{"en":"Well before means much earlier than another event.","zh":"遠早於，是指比另一事件早得多。"},{"en":"A student may arrive well before class starts if they want to prepare quietly.","zh":"如果學生想安靜準備，可能會遠早於上課時間到達。"},{"en":"If one sample reaches zero well before another, there is a clear time gap between them.","zh":"如果一個樣本遠早於另一個達到零度，兩者之間就有明顯時間差距。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than simply saying before.","zh":"這個短語比簡單說 before 更強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the latter","meaning":"後者","examples":[{"en":"The latter bowl nevertheless froze solid first.","zh":"然而，後者的碗先完全結冰。"},{"en":"The latter means the second of two things just mentioned.","zh":"後者，是指剛剛提到的兩者中的第二個。"},{"en":"If a teacher mentions a red cup and a blue cup, the latter means the blue cup.","zh":"如果老師提到紅杯和藍杯，後者就是藍杯。"},{"en":"This word helps writers avoid repeating the same noun.","zh":"這個詞幫助作者避免重複同一名詞。"},{"en":"To understand the latter, readers must look back at the order of the two things.","zh":"要理解後者，讀者必須回看兩件事的先後次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"freeze solid","meaning":"完全結冰","examples":[{"en":"The warmer water sometimes froze solid before the cooler water.","zh":"較暖的水有時比比較冷的水先完全結冰。"},{"en":"To freeze solid means to become completely frozen, not just cold or icy at the surface.","zh":"完全結冰，是指完全變成冰，而不只是變冷或表面結冰。"},{"en":"A bottle of water may look icy outside but not freeze solid at the centre.","zh":"一瓶水外面可能看似有冰，但中心仍未完全結冰。"},{"en":"If a sample freezes solid first, the whole body of water has turned into ice sooner.","zh":"如果某樣本先完全結冰，整個水體就更早變成冰。"},{"en":"This phrase is important because different researchers may define freezing differently.","zh":"這個短語很重要，因為不同研究人員可能用不同方式界定結冰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"experiments at different temperatures","meaning":"在不同溫度下進行的實驗","examples":[{"en":"Experiments at different temperatures produced unexpected results.","zh":"在不同溫度下進行的實驗產生了意想不到的結果。"},{"en":"Experiments at different temperatures test samples that begin at different levels of heat or cold.","zh":"在不同溫度下進行的實驗，是測試起始冷熱程度不同的樣本。"},{"en":"A class may compare water starting at 5 degrees, 20 degrees, and 35 degrees.","zh":"一班學生可能比較由 5 度、20 度和 35 度開始的水。"},{"en":"Testing different temperatures can show whether an effect happens only within a certain range.","zh":"測試不同溫度可以顯示某效應是否只在特定範圍內出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes experiments with varied starting conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述起始條件不同的實驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"conventional freezer","meaning":"一般冰格","examples":[{"en":"The experiments were carried out in a conventional freezer.","zh":"這些實驗在一般冰格中進行。"},{"en":"A conventional freezer is an ordinary freezer, like one found in a home or basic laboratory.","zh":"一般冰格是普通冷凍設備，例如家中或基本實驗室中的冰格。"},{"en":"A family may use a conventional freezer to make ice cubes or store frozen food.","zh":"家庭可能使用一般冰格製作冰塊或儲存冷凍食物。"},{"en":"A conventional freezer may introduce extra variables, such as thermostat response and uneven cooling.","zh":"一般冰格可能引入額外變數，例如恆溫器反應和不均勻冷卻。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts ordinary equipment with specialised scientific equipment.","zh":"這個短語把普通設備與專門科學設備作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"on further examination","meaning":"經進一步研究","examples":[{"en":"On further examination, an explanation began to emerge.","zh":"經進一步研究，一個解釋開始浮現。"},{"en":"On further examination means after looking more carefully at the evidence or results.","zh":"經進一步研究，是指更仔細檢視證據或結果之後。"},{"en":"On further examination, a doctor may realise that a cough is caused by allergies, not a cold.","zh":"經進一步檢查，醫生可能發現咳嗽是由敏感而非感冒引起。"},{"en":"Further examination can reveal details missed in the first observation.","zh":"進一步研究可以揭示初次觀察中遺漏的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a deeper analysis after an initial finding.","zh":"這個短語引入初步發現之後的深入分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"explanation for a paradox","meaning":"對悖論的解釋","examples":[{"en":"Researchers searched for an explanation for this paradox.","zh":"研究人員尋找對這個悖論的解釋。"},{"en":"An explanation for a paradox is a reason that makes a seemingly contradictory result understandable.","zh":"對悖論的解釋，是令看似矛盾的結果變得可理解的原因。"},{"en":"If a poor student suddenly gets the highest mark, teachers may look for an explanation for the paradox.","zh":"如果一名成績差的學生突然取得最高分，老師可能會尋找對這個悖論的解釋。"},{"en":"A good explanation for a paradox shows why the result is less impossible than it first seems.","zh":"好的悖論解釋會顯示為何結果不像起初看來那麼不可能。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a puzzling result with logical reasoning.","zh":"這個短語把令人困惑的結果與邏輯推理連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"begin to emerge","meaning":"開始浮現","examples":[{"en":"A possible explanation gradually began to emerge.","zh":"一個可能解釋逐漸開始浮現。"},{"en":"To begin to emerge means to start becoming clear or visible.","zh":"開始浮現，是指開始變得清楚或可見。"},{"en":"After several interviews, the real reason for the problem began to emerge.","zh":"經過幾次訪問後，問題的真正原因開始浮現。"},{"en":"In research, an explanation may begin to emerge only after many small clues are compared.","zh":"在研究中，解釋可能要到許多小線索被比較後才開始浮現。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests gradual discovery.","zh":"這個短語暗示逐步發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"heat loss","meaning":"熱量流失","examples":[{"en":"The explanation focused on heat loss from the water.","zh":"這個解釋聚焦水的熱量流失。"},{"en":"Heat loss is the process by which heat leaves an object or substance.","zh":"熱量流失是熱離開物件或物質的過程。"},{"en":"A cup of hot tea cools because of heat loss to the surrounding air.","zh":"一杯熱茶會冷卻，是因為熱量流失到周圍空氣中。"},{"en":"Faster heat loss can make water cool and freeze more quickly.","zh":"更快的熱量流失可以令水更快冷卻和結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to understanding why temperature changes.","zh":"這個短語是理解溫度變化的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"occur at the points where","meaning":"發生在……的位置","examples":[{"en":"Heat loss occurs at the points where the water touches colder air.","zh":"熱量流失發生在水接觸較冷空氣的位置。"},{"en":"Occur at the points where means happen in the exact places where a condition is present.","zh":"發生在某些位置，是指在某條件存在的具體地方發生。"},{"en":"Rust may occur at the points where metal stays wet for a long time.","zh":"鐵鏽可能發生在金屬長時間保持潮濕的位置。"},{"en":"In freezing water, heat loss occurs where the water meets colder surroundings.","zh":"在水結冰時，熱量流失發生在水接觸較冷環境的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain the location of a process.","zh":"這個短語有助解釋過程發生的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be in touch with","meaning":"與……接觸","examples":[{"en":"The sides and surface of the water are in touch with the cold air.","zh":"水的側面和表面與冷空氣接觸。"},{"en":"To be in touch with something means to be physically connected to or in contact with it.","zh":"與某物接觸，是指與它有實體連接或碰觸。"},{"en":"Food spoils faster if it is in touch with warm air for too long.","zh":"食物如果與暖空氣接觸太久，會更快變壞。"},{"en":"When water is in touch with cold air, heat can leave the water more easily.","zh":"當水與冷空氣接觸，熱量可以更容易離開水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes contact between two things.","zh":"這個短語描述兩者之間的接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"colder atmosphere","meaning":"較冷的環境","examples":[{"en":"The water loses heat to the colder atmosphere of the freezer.","zh":"水把熱量流失到冰格較冷的環境中。"},{"en":"A colder atmosphere is the surrounding air or environment with a lower temperature.","zh":"較冷的環境，是溫度較低的周圍空氣或環境。"},{"en":"A warm lunchbox cools down when it is placed in the colder atmosphere of a fridge.","zh":"暖飯盒放進雪櫃較冷的環境後會冷卻。"},{"en":"The greater the difference between warm water and the colder atmosphere, the faster heat may escape.","zh":"暖水和較冷環境之間的差異越大，熱量可能散失得越快。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the cold environment around the object.","zh":"這個短語指物件周圍的寒冷環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"namely","meaning":"即是；也就是","examples":[{"en":"Heat escapes at several points, namely the sides and the surface.","zh":"熱量從幾個位置散失，即是側面和表面。"},{"en":"Namely means that is to say, and it introduces specific examples or details.","zh":"即是或也就是，是用來引出具體例子或細節。"},{"en":"The project needs three things, namely time, money, and trained workers.","zh":"這個項目需要三樣東西，即是時間、金錢和受訓工人。"},{"en":"This word makes a sentence more precise by naming exactly what is meant.","zh":"這個詞透過明確指出所指內容，令句子更精確。"},{"en":"It is useful when moving from a general idea to clear examples.","zh":"它適合用於由概括想法轉向清楚例子時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lose heat faster","meaning":"更快失去熱量","examples":[{"en":"A warm surface will lose heat faster than a cold surface.","zh":"暖表面會比冷表面更快失去熱量。"},{"en":"To lose heat faster means to transfer heat away more quickly.","zh":"更快失去熱量，是指更迅速把熱量轉移出去。"},{"en":"Hot soup loses heat faster when it is poured into a wide bowl.","zh":"熱湯倒進寬碗後會更快失去熱量。"},{"en":"A larger temperature difference can cause an object to lose heat faster.","zh":"較大的溫差可以令物件更快失去熱量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how quickly heat leaves something.","zh":"這個短語描述熱量離開某物的速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"contrast between temperatures","meaning":"溫度之間的差異","examples":[{"en":"The contrast between temperatures increases the rate of heat loss.","zh":"溫度之間的差異會增加熱量流失速度。"},{"en":"Contrast between temperatures means the difference between two levels of heat or cold.","zh":"溫度之間的差異，是兩個冷熱水平之間的差別。"},{"en":"There is a strong contrast between hot tea and winter air.","zh":"熱茶和冬天空氣之間有強烈溫度差異。"},{"en":"A greater contrast between temperatures can make heat leave more quickly.","zh":"較大的溫度差異可以令熱量更快離開。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why temperature difference matters.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何溫差重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"heat to be lost","meaning":"需要散失的熱量","examples":[{"en":"The warmer bowl also contains more heat to be lost.","zh":"較暖的碗也含有更多需要散失的熱量。"},{"en":"Heat to be lost is the heat that must leave something before it becomes colder or freezes.","zh":"需要散失的熱量，是某物變冷或結冰前必須離開的熱量。"},{"en":"A hot bowl of soup has more heat to be lost than a bowl at room temperature.","zh":"一碗熱湯比一碗室溫湯有更多需要散失的熱量。"},{"en":"More heat to be lost usually means more cooling is needed.","zh":"需要散失的熱量越多，通常需要更多冷卻。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why warmer water should normally take longer to freeze.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何較暖的水通常應該需要更久才結冰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be kept at a higher temperature","meaning":"維持在較高溫度","examples":[{"en":"The surface may be kept at a higher temperature by circulating water.","zh":"水面可能因水流循環而維持在較高溫度。"},{"en":"To be kept at a higher temperature means to remain warmer than another part or surrounding area.","zh":"維持在較高溫度，是指保持比另一部分或周圍地區更暖。"},{"en":"A room may be kept at a higher temperature if the heater stays on.","zh":"如果暖爐一直開着，房間可能維持在較高溫度。"},{"en":"Circulating warm water can keep the surface warmer and maintain faster heat loss.","zh":"循環中的暖水可以令表面保持較暖，並維持較快熱量流失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a temperature is maintained.","zh":"這個短語描述溫度如何被保持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rate of heat loss","meaning":"熱量流失速度","examples":[{"en":"A warmer surface maintains a higher rate of heat loss.","zh":"較暖表面維持較高熱量流失速度。"},{"en":"Rate of heat loss means how quickly heat leaves a substance or object.","zh":"熱量流失速度，是熱離開某物質或物件的快慢。"},{"en":"A metal spoon in hot soup may have a high rate of heat loss because metal conducts heat well.","zh":"熱湯中的金屬匙可能有較高熱量流失速度，因為金屬導熱良好。"},{"en":"A higher rate of heat loss can help water cool faster.","zh":"較高熱量流失速度可以幫助水更快冷卻。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the speed of thermal transfer.","zh":"這個短語指熱轉移速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as long as","meaning":"只要","examples":[{"en":"As long as the water remains liquid, circulation can continue.","zh":"只要水仍維持液態，循環便可繼續。"},{"en":"As long as means provided that a condition is true.","zh":"只要，是指在某條件成立的情況下。"},{"en":"As long as the classroom is quiet, students can focus on reading.","zh":"只要課室安靜，學生就可以專心閱讀。"},{"en":"In water, circulation can continue as long as there is liquid water and a temperature difference.","zh":"在水中，只要仍有液態水和溫差，循環就可以繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a condition that allows something to happen.","zh":"這個短語引入讓某事發生的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"remain liquid","meaning":"維持液態","examples":[{"en":"The water continues circulating while it remains liquid.","zh":"水在維持液態時會繼續循環。"},{"en":"To remain liquid means to stay in liquid form instead of becoming solid.","zh":"維持液態，是指保持液體狀態，而不是變成固體。"},{"en":"Honey may remain liquid in a warm kitchen but become thicker in a cold room.","zh":"蜜糖在溫暖廚房中可能維持液態，但在冷房中會變得較稠。"},{"en":"Water can circulate only while it remains liquid, because solid ice cannot flow in the same way.","zh":"水只有在維持液態時才能循環，因為固體冰不能以同樣方式流動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical state of a substance.","zh":"這個短語描述物質的物理狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cooling portion","meaning":"正在冷卻的部分","examples":[{"en":"The cooling portion at the surface sinks towards the bottom.","zh":"表面正在冷卻的部分向底部下沉。"},{"en":"A cooling portion is the part of a liquid that is losing heat and becoming colder.","zh":"正在冷卻的部分，是液體中正在失去熱量並變冷的部分。"},{"en":"In a cup of hot water, the cooling portion near the surface may begin to move downward.","zh":"在一杯熱水中，靠近表面正在冷卻的部分可能開始向下移動。"},{"en":"When a cooling portion sinks, warmer water can rise and replace it.","zh":"當正在冷卻的部分下沉，較暖的水可以上升並取代它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one part of the liquid during the cooling process.","zh":"這個短語描述冷卻過程中的其中一部分液體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sink to the bottom","meaning":"沉到底部","examples":[{"en":"Cooler water sinks to the bottom of the bowl.","zh":"較冷的水沉到碗底部。"},{"en":"To sink to the bottom means to move downward until reaching the lowest part.","zh":"沉到底部，是指向下移動直到最低部分。"},{"en":"A stone sinks to the bottom of a pond because it is denser than water.","zh":"石頭會沉到池塘底部，因為它比水密度高。"},{"en":"Cooler water may sink to the bottom because it becomes denser than warmer water.","zh":"較冷的水可能沉到底部，因為它變得比暖水密度更高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes downward movement inside a liquid or container.","zh":"這個短語描述液體或容器內的向下移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rise to take its place","meaning":"上升並取代其位置","examples":[{"en":"Warmer water rises to take the cooler water’s place.","zh":"較暖的水上升並取代較冷水的位置。"},{"en":"To rise to take its place means to move upward and replace what has moved away.","zh":"上升並取代其位置，是指向上移動並替代已離開的部分。"},{"en":"In a busy shop, another worker may step forward to take a colleague’s place at the counter.","zh":"在繁忙商店中，另一名員工可能上前取代同事在櫃檯的位置。"},{"en":"When cooler water sinks, warmer water rises to take its place and keeps circulation going.","zh":"當較冷水下沉，較暖水會上升並取代其位置，使循環繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase explains replacement within a moving system.","zh":"這個短語解釋移動系統中的替代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"early freezing","meaning":"早期結冰","examples":[{"en":"Early freezing may occur along the sides of the container.","zh":"早期結冰可能發生在容器側面。"},{"en":"Early freezing means ice begins to form before the whole body of water is frozen.","zh":"早期結冰，是指整體水體完全結冰前，冰已開始形成。"},{"en":"In an ice tray, early freezing may appear first at the edges.","zh":"在冰格盤中，早期結冰可能最先出現在邊緣。"},{"en":"Early freezing along the sides can change how the remaining liquid moves.","zh":"側面的早期結冰會改變剩餘液體如何移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first stage of ice formation.","zh":"這個短語描述冰形成的第一階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sides and base","meaning":"側面和底部","examples":[{"en":"Ice may first form along the sides and base of the bowl.","zh":"冰可能最先沿着碗的側面和底部形成。"},{"en":"The sides and base are the walls and bottom of a container.","zh":"側面和底部是容器的壁和底。"},{"en":"When washing a lunchbox, you should clean the sides and base because food may stick there.","zh":"清洗飯盒時，你應清潔側面和底部，因為食物可能黏在那裡。"},{"en":"In freezing, the sides and base can remove heat from water because they touch the cold environment.","zh":"在結冰過程中，側面和底部因接觸冷環境而可以從水中移走熱量。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main contact areas of a container.","zh":"這個短語指出容器的主要接觸區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"amplify the effect","meaning":"加強該效應","examples":[{"en":"Freezing around the container may amplify the cooling effect.","zh":"容器周圍結冰可能加強冷卻效應。"},{"en":"To amplify the effect means to make the effect stronger.","zh":"加強該效應，是指令該效應變得更強。"},{"en":"A microphone can amplify a teacher’s voice so that the whole hall can hear it.","zh":"麥克風可以放大老師的聲音，讓整個禮堂都聽見。"},{"en":"If ice forms around a container, it may amplify cooling by changing heat transfer.","zh":"如果冰在容器周圍形成，它可能透過改變熱傳遞來加強冷卻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strengthening an existing effect.","zh":"這個短語描述強化已有的效應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"more uniformly cold","meaning":"整體溫度較平均地低","examples":[{"en":"The cooler bowl becomes more uniformly cold.","zh":"較冷的碗整體溫度變得較平均地低。"},{"en":"More uniformly cold means cold more evenly throughout the whole body of water.","zh":"整體溫度較平均地低，是指整個水體更均勻地寒冷。"},{"en":"A drink becomes more uniformly cold after it is stirred with ice.","zh":"飲品用冰攪拌後，整體溫度會變得較平均地低。"},{"en":"If water is more uniformly cold, there may be less internal movement caused by temperature differences.","zh":"如果水整體溫度較平均地低，由溫差造成的內部流動可能較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an even temperature distribution.","zh":"這個短語描述均勻的溫度分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"temperature difference","meaning":"溫差","examples":[{"en":"A smaller temperature difference produces weaker circulation.","zh":"較小溫差會產生較弱循環。"},{"en":"Temperature difference means the gap between two temperatures.","zh":"溫差是兩個溫度之間的差距。"},{"en":"There is a big temperature difference between hot coffee and ice cream.","zh":"熱咖啡和雪糕之間有很大溫差。"},{"en":"A large temperature difference can make heat move faster from a warm object to a cold environment.","zh":"大溫差可以令熱量更快由暖物件移向冷環境。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when explaining cooling and heat loss.","zh":"這個短語在解釋冷卻和熱量流失時很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"water flow","meaning":"水流","examples":[{"en":"The water flow inside a uniformly cold bowl will be minimal.","zh":"整體均冷的碗內部水流會非常少。"},{"en":"Water flow means the movement of water inside a container or system.","zh":"水流是水在容器或系統內的移動。"},{"en":"In a sink, strong water flow can help wash away soap and dirt.","zh":"在洗手盆中，強水流可以幫助沖走肥皂和污垢。"},{"en":"In a bowl of cooling water, weaker water flow may slow the movement of heat from the centre.","zh":"在一碗正在冷卻的水中，較弱水流可能減慢中心熱量的移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how water moves.","zh":"這個短語描述水如何移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be minimal","meaning":"減至最低；非常少","examples":[{"en":"Circulation becomes minimal when temperature differences are small.","zh":"當溫差很小，循環會變得非常少。"},{"en":"To be minimal means to be extremely small or very limited.","zh":"非常少或減至最低，是指極小或非常有限。"},{"en":"If only two students are absent, the effect on the class may be minimal.","zh":"如果只有兩名學生缺席，對全班的影響可能非常少。"},{"en":"When circulation is minimal, the water inside the container barely moves.","zh":"當循環非常少，容器內的水幾乎不移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very low level of something.","zh":"這個短語描述某事處於很低水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"inhibiting factor","meaning":"抑制因素","examples":[{"en":"Surface ice is another inhibiting factor.","zh":"表面冰是另一個抑制因素。"},{"en":"An inhibiting factor is something that slows down or prevents a process.","zh":"抑制因素是減慢或阻止某過程的東西。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can be an inhibiting factor when students try to concentrate.","zh":"睡眠不足可以是學生嘗試集中精神時的抑制因素。"},{"en":"Surface ice may inhibit freezing by blocking circulation and heat loss from the water below.","zh":"表面冰可能透過阻礙循環和下方水的熱量流失而抑制結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a factor that limits progress.","zh":"這個短語描述限制進展的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"form quite quickly","meaning":"很快形成","examples":[{"en":"Ice can form quite quickly on the surface of cooler water.","zh":"冰可以在較冷水的表面很快形成。"},{"en":"To form quite quickly means to appear or develop in a short time.","zh":"很快形成，是指在短時間內出現或發展。"},{"en":"A thin skin can form quite quickly on hot milk if it is left uncovered.","zh":"熱牛奶如果不加蓋，表面可能很快形成薄膜。"},{"en":"If surface ice forms quite quickly, it may block movement in the water below.","zh":"如果表面冰很快形成，它可能阻礙下方水的移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rapid formation.","zh":"這個短語描述快速形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"act as insulation","meaning":"發揮隔熱作用","examples":[{"en":"The layer of ice acts as insulation.","zh":"這層冰發揮隔熱作用。"},{"en":"To act as insulation means to reduce heat transfer between two areas.","zh":"發揮隔熱作用，是指減少兩個區域之間的熱傳遞。"},{"en":"A thick jacket acts as insulation by keeping body heat inside.","zh":"厚外套透過把身體熱量留在裡面而發揮隔熱作用。"},{"en":"Surface ice can act as insulation between liquid water and cold freezer air.","zh":"表面冰可以在液態水和冰格冷空氣之間發揮隔熱作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a barrier that slows heat movement.","zh":"這個短語描述減慢熱量移動的屏障。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"virtually stop","meaning":"幾乎完全停止","examples":[{"en":"The surface ice can virtually stop internal circulation.","zh":"表面冰可以幾乎完全停止內部循環。"},{"en":"Virtually stop means almost completely stop.","zh":"幾乎完全停止，是指差不多完全停止。"},{"en":"A road accident can virtually stop traffic during rush hour.","zh":"交通意外可以在繁忙時間幾乎完全停止車流。"},{"en":"If surface ice virtually stops circulation, warmer water below cannot easily reach the surface.","zh":"如果表面冰幾乎完全停止循環，下方較暖的水就不容易到達表面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a process being nearly halted.","zh":"這個短語描述某過程接近停頓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"helpful effects of","meaning":"……的有利作用","examples":[{"en":"The ice blocks the helpful effects of water circulation.","zh":"冰阻擋水循環的有利作用。"},{"en":"Helpful effects of something are useful results produced by it.","zh":"某事的有利作用，是它產生的有用結果。"},{"en":"The helpful effects of exercise include better sleep and stronger muscles.","zh":"運動的有利作用包括更好睡眠和更強肌肉。"},{"en":"Water circulation has helpful effects because it carries heat from inside the water to the surface.","zh":"水循環有有利作用，因為它把水內部的熱量帶到表面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the positive role something can play.","zh":"這個短語描述某事可以發揮的正面作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"circulate inside","meaning":"在內部循環","examples":[{"en":"Liquid water circulates inside the bowl.","zh":"液態水在碗內部循環。"},{"en":"To circulate inside means to move around within a container or space.","zh":"在內部循環，是指在容器或空間內移動。"},{"en":"Air can circulate inside a classroom if the windows and fans are open.","zh":"如果窗戶和風扇打開，空氣可以在課室內部循環。"},{"en":"When liquid water circulates inside a bowl, heat can be carried from one part to another.","zh":"當液態水在碗內部循環，熱量可以由一部分帶到另一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement within a closed or partly closed space.","zh":"這個短語描述在封閉或半封閉空間內的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ultimately","meaning":"最終","examples":[{"en":"Ultimately, the warmer bowl may freeze completely first.","zh":"最終，較暖的碗可能先完全結冰。"},{"en":"Ultimately means in the end, after all stages have happened.","zh":"最終，是指在所有階段發生之後的最後。"},{"en":"A student may struggle at first but ultimately pass the exam after months of practice.","zh":"學生起初可能很吃力，但經過數月練習後最終通過考試。"},{"en":"In an experiment, early temperature changes may be different from the ultimate result.","zh":"在實驗中，早期溫度變化可能不同於最終結果。"},{"en":"This word introduces the final outcome.","zh":"這個詞引入最後結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rate of cooling","meaning":"冷卻速度","examples":[{"en":"The rate of cooling at the centre may become extremely slow.","zh":"中心部分的冷卻速度可能變得極慢。"},{"en":"Rate of cooling means how quickly temperature falls.","zh":"冷卻速度，是溫度下降的快慢。"},{"en":"A large pot of soup has a slower rate of cooling than a small bowl of soup.","zh":"一大鍋湯的冷卻速度比一小碗湯慢。"},{"en":"If the rate of cooling at the centre is slow, the whole sample may take longer to freeze solid.","zh":"如果中心部分冷卻速度慢，整個樣本可能需要更長時間才完全結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cooling speed.","zh":"這個短語描述冷卻快慢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"core of the water","meaning":"水體中心部分","examples":[{"en":"The core of the cooler body of water loses heat slowly.","zh":"較冷水體的中心部分緩慢失去熱量。"},{"en":"The core of the water is the central part of the water, away from the surface and edges.","zh":"水體中心部分，是遠離表面和邊緣的中間部分。"},{"en":"In a thick bowl of soup, the core may stay hot even when the surface is cooler.","zh":"在一碗厚湯中，即使表面較冷，中心部分仍可能保持熱。"},{"en":"If surface ice blocks heat loss, the core of the water may remain liquid for longer.","zh":"如果表面冰阻礙熱量流失，水體中心部分可能更長時間保持液態。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the middle part of the water mass.","zh":"這個短語聚焦水體的中間部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fully frozen","meaning":"完全結冰","examples":[{"en":"The initially warmer water may become fully frozen first.","zh":"起初較暖的水可能先完全結冰。"},{"en":"Fully frozen means completely changed into ice.","zh":"完全結冰，是指完全變成冰。"},{"en":"A drink is not fully frozen if the centre is still liquid.","zh":"如果飲品中心仍是液態，它就不是完全結冰。"},{"en":"Whether water is fully frozen depends on the whole sample, not just the surface.","zh":"水是否完全結冰取決於整個樣本，而不只是表面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the final solid state.","zh":"這個短語描述最終固體狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"limitations to","meaning":"……的限制","examples":[{"en":"There are important limitations to this comparison.","zh":"這個比較有重要限制。"},{"en":"Limitations to something are conditions that restrict how far it can be applied or trusted.","zh":"某事的限制，是限制它可應用或可信範圍的條件。"},{"en":"A survey of ten students has limitations because it may not represent the whole school.","zh":"只調查十名學生的問卷有限制，因為它未必代表整間學校。"},{"en":"Limitations to an experiment help explain why results may not appear in every situation.","zh":"實驗限制有助解釋為何結果不會在每種情況下都出現。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces caution and prevents overgeneralisation.","zh":"這個短語引入謹慎態度並避免過度概括。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"extreme temperature difference","meaning":"極大的溫差","examples":[{"en":"The effect may not occur with an extreme temperature difference.","zh":"在極大的溫差下，該效應可能不會出現。"},{"en":"An extreme temperature difference is a very large gap between two temperatures.","zh":"極大的溫差，是兩個溫度之間非常大的差距。"},{"en":"There is an extreme temperature difference between boiling water and ice water.","zh":"沸水和冰水之間有極大的溫差。"},{"en":"If the starting temperatures are too far apart, the Mpemba Effect may not appear.","zh":"如果起始溫度相差太遠，姆潘巴效應可能不會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a condition that can change the result of an experiment.","zh":"這個短語描述可以改變實驗結果的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"counter-intuitive result","meaning":"違反直覺的結果","examples":[{"en":"The Mpemba Effect is a counter-intuitive result.","zh":"姆潘巴效應是一個違反直覺的結果。"},{"en":"A counter-intuitive result is an outcome that goes against what people normally expect.","zh":"違反直覺的結果，是與人們通常預期相反的結果。"},{"en":"It is counter-intuitive when a shorter route takes longer because of heavy traffic.","zh":"如果較短路線因塞車而需時更久，這就是違反直覺的結果。"},{"en":"Counter-intuitive results often make people question their assumptions.","zh":"違反直覺的結果常令人質疑自己的假設。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when reality seems to oppose common sense.","zh":"當現實看似與常識相反時，就可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hold true","meaning":"適用；成立","examples":[{"en":"The result appears to hold true within a limited temperature range.","zh":"這個結果似乎只在有限溫度範圍內成立。"},{"en":"To hold true means to remain valid or correct under certain conditions.","zh":"成立，是指在某些條件下保持有效或正確。"},{"en":"A grammar rule may hold true in most sentences but not in every exception.","zh":"一條文法規則可能在大多數句子中成立，但不適用於每個例外。"},{"en":"The Mpemba Effect may hold true only when the starting temperatures fall within a certain range.","zh":"姆潘巴效應可能只在起始溫度落入某個範圍時成立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited validity.","zh":"這個短語描述有限有效性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"within a range of","meaning":"在……範圍內","examples":[{"en":"The effect was observed within a range of five to thirty-five degrees.","zh":"該效應在五至三十五度範圍內被觀察到。"},{"en":"Within a range of means between specified lower and upper limits.","zh":"在某範圍內，是指位於指定的下限和上限之間。"},{"en":"The teacher may accept essays within a range of 300 to 350 words.","zh":"老師可能接受 300 至 350 字範圍內的文章。"},{"en":"A result observed within a range may not apply outside that range.","zh":"在某範圍內觀察到的結果，未必適用於該範圍之外。"},{"en":"This phrase gives boundaries for a measurement or condition.","zh":"這個短語為測量或條件給出邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"indicated previously","meaning":"先前指出的","examples":[{"en":"The relevant temperature range was indicated previously.","zh":"相關溫度範圍是先前指出的。"},{"en":"Indicated previously means mentioned or shown earlier.","zh":"先前指出的，是指較早提及或顯示的。"},{"en":"If a worksheet indicated previously that answers must use two words, students should follow that rule later.","zh":"如果工作紙先前指出答案必須用兩個詞，學生之後就應遵守該規則。"},{"en":"This phrase points readers back to information already given.","zh":"這個短語把讀者帶回已給出的資訊。"},{"en":"It helps connect later statements with earlier details.","zh":"它有助把後文陳述與前文細節連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"validity of research findings","meaning":"研究結果的有效性","examples":[{"en":"Reviewers have questioned the validity of the research findings.","zh":"評論者質疑研究結果的有效性。"},{"en":"Validity of research findings means whether the results are reliable, fair, and properly supported by evidence.","zh":"研究結果的有效性，是指結果是否可靠、公平，並有證據充分支持。"},{"en":"If an experiment has too few samples, people may question the validity of its findings.","zh":"如果實驗樣本太少，人們可能質疑其研究結果的有效性。"},{"en":"Weak definitions and uncontrolled variables can reduce the validity of research findings.","zh":"定義薄弱和變數不受控制，會降低研究結果的有效性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to how trustworthy research results are.","zh":"這個短語指研究結果有多可信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be questioned by","meaning":"受到……質疑","examples":[{"en":"The original conclusions have been questioned by several reviewers.","zh":"原本結論受到幾位評論者質疑。"},{"en":"To be questioned by someone means to be challenged, doubted, or criticised by them.","zh":"受到某人質疑，是指被他們挑戰、懷疑或批評。"},{"en":"A school rule may be questioned by parents if it seems unfair.","zh":"如果校規看似不公平，可能受到家長質疑。"},{"en":"Scientific conclusions are often questioned by other researchers before they are accepted.","zh":"科學結論在被接受前，常受到其他研究人員質疑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes critical examination.","zh":"這個短語描述批判性審視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a number of reviewers","meaning":"多名評論者","examples":[{"en":"A number of reviewers criticised the experimental design.","zh":"多名評論者批評該實驗設計。"},{"en":"A number of reviewers means several people who examined and commented on the work.","zh":"多名評論者，是指幾位檢視並評論該作品的人。"},{"en":"A number of reviewers may read an academic paper before it is published.","zh":"一篇學術論文出版前，可能由多名評論者閱讀。"},{"en":"If several reviewers raise the same concern, the weakness may be serious.","zh":"如果幾位評論者提出同一擔憂，該弱點可能很嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces multiple critics or evaluators.","zh":"這個短語引入多位批評者或評估者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"point out that","meaning":"指出","examples":[{"en":"Critics point out that the initial question was not clearly defined.","zh":"批評者指出，最初問題沒有被清楚界定。"},{"en":"To point out that means to draw attention to a fact, problem, or detail.","zh":"指出某事，是指引人注意某個事實、問題或細節。"},{"en":"A teacher may point out that a student has answered the wrong question.","zh":"老師可能指出學生答錯了問題。"},{"en":"Reviewers point out weaknesses so that research can become clearer and stronger.","zh":"評論者指出弱點，是為了令研究更清楚和更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces criticism or clarification.","zh":"這個短語常引入批評或澄清。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"initial experimental question","meaning":"最初的實驗問題","examples":[{"en":"The initial experimental question lacked a precise definition.","zh":"最初的實驗問題缺乏精確定義。"},{"en":"The initial experimental question is the first research question that guides an experiment.","zh":"最初的實驗問題，是指引實驗的第一個研究問題。"},{"en":"In a class experiment, the initial experimental question might be whether salt water freezes more slowly than pure water.","zh":"在課堂實驗中，最初的實驗問題可能是鹽水是否比純水結冰更慢。"},{"en":"If the initial experimental question is unclear, the results may be difficult to interpret.","zh":"如果最初的實驗問題不清楚，結果可能難以解讀。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the starting question of an experiment.","zh":"這個短語指實驗的起始問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be clearly defined","meaning":"被清楚界定","examples":[{"en":"The meaning of freezing needed to be clearly defined.","zh":"結冰的意思需要被清楚界定。"},{"en":"To be clearly defined means to be explained exactly and without confusion.","zh":"被清楚界定，是指被準確且不令人混淆地解釋。"},{"en":"In a school project, success should be clearly defined before students begin.","zh":"在學校項目中，成功應在學生開始前被清楚界定。"},{"en":"If freezing is not clearly defined, one researcher may mean reaching zero while another means becoming fully solid.","zh":"如果結冰沒有被清楚界定，一名研究人員可能指達到零度，另一名則指完全變成固體。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the need for precise meaning.","zh":"這個短語強調精確意思的需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"decide on exactly what","meaning":"準確決定甚麼才算……","examples":[{"en":"The researchers needed to decide on exactly what counted as freezing.","zh":"研究人員需要準確決定甚麼才算結冰。"},{"en":"To decide on exactly what something means is to choose a clear and precise standard.","zh":"準確決定某事是甚麼意思，是指選定清楚而精確的標準。"},{"en":"A teacher must decide exactly what counts as late homework.","zh":"老師必須準確決定甚麼才算遲交功課。"},{"en":"In the Mpemba Effect, researchers must decide exactly what counts as freezing before measuring time.","zh":"在姆潘巴效應中，研究人員必須在量度時間前準確決定甚麼才算結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes setting a clear definition.","zh":"這個短語描述設定清晰定義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"constitute freezing","meaning":"構成結冰；算是結冰","examples":[{"en":"Different researchers may define what constitutes freezing differently.","zh":"不同研究人員可能用不同方式界定甚麼算是結冰。"},{"en":"To constitute freezing means to count as freezing according to a chosen definition.","zh":"構成結冰，是指按照某個選定定義算作結冰。"},{"en":"Some researchers may say reaching zero degrees constitutes freezing, while others may require solid ice.","zh":"有些研究人員可能認為達到零度就算結冰，而另一些則要求變成固體冰。"},{"en":"Different definitions of what constitutes freezing can lead to different results.","zh":"對甚麼構成結冰有不同定義，可能導致不同結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and useful when precision matters.","zh":"這個短語正式，適合用於需要精確的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"depend on","meaning":"取決於","examples":[{"en":"The rate at which water freezes depends on many variables.","zh":"水結冰的速度取決於許多變數。"},{"en":"To depend on something means to be affected or determined by it.","zh":"取決於某事，是指受它影響或由它決定。"},{"en":"A student’s exam result may depend on sleep, revision, and question difficulty.","zh":"學生的考試成績可能取決於睡眠、溫習和題目難度。"},{"en":"Freezing time depends on container size, water purity, starting temperature, and freezer conditions.","zh":"結冰時間取決於容器大小、水的純度、起始溫度和冰格條件。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one result is controlled by other factors.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個結果由其他因素控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a large number of variables","meaning":"大量變數","examples":[{"en":"The freezing process is affected by a large number of variables.","zh":"結冰過程受大量變數影響。"},{"en":"A large number of variables means many different factors can change the result.","zh":"大量變數，是指許多不同因素可以改變結果。"},{"en":"In cooking rice, water amount, heat level, and cooking time are variables.","zh":"煮飯時，水量、火力和烹煮時間都是變數。"},{"en":"A large number of variables makes an experiment difficult to control and repeat.","zh":"大量變數會令實驗難以控制和重複。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the situation is complex.","zh":"這個短語強調情況複雜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"container size","meaning":"容器大小","examples":[{"en":"Container size can influence whether the effect is observed.","zh":"容器大小可以影響該效應是否被觀察到。"},{"en":"Container size means how large or small the bowl, cup, or vessel is.","zh":"容器大小，是指碗、杯或器皿有多大或多小。"},{"en":"A shallow dish and a deep mug have different container sizes.","zh":"淺碟和深杯有不同的容器大小。"},{"en":"Container size matters because it affects surface area, water circulation, and heat loss.","zh":"容器大小很重要，因為它影響表面面積、水循環和熱量流失。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an important experimental variable.","zh":"這個短語指重要實驗變數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be large enough to","meaning":"足夠大以便……","examples":[{"en":"The container must be large enough to allow water to circulate freely.","zh":"容器必須足夠大，以便水可以自由循環。"},{"en":"To be large enough to do something means to have sufficient size for that purpose.","zh":"足夠大以便做某事，是指大小足以達成該目的。"},{"en":"A classroom must be large enough to hold all the students safely.","zh":"課室必須足夠大，以便安全容納所有學生。"},{"en":"A container must be large enough to let warmer and cooler water move inside it.","zh":"容器必須足夠大，以便較暖和較冷的水能在內部移動。"},{"en":"This phrase connects size with function.","zh":"這個短語把大小與功能連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"free circulation of water","meaning":"水的自由循環","examples":[{"en":"The effect requires free circulation of water inside the container.","zh":"該效應需要容器內水的自由循環。"},{"en":"Free circulation of water means water can move around without being blocked.","zh":"水的自由循環，是指水可以不受阻礙地流動。"},{"en":"In a fish tank, free circulation of water helps spread oxygen evenly.","zh":"在魚缸中，水的自由循環有助氧氣均勻分布。"},{"en":"Free circulation of water allows warm water to rise and cooler water to sink.","zh":"水的自由循環讓暖水上升、冷水下沉。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unrestricted water movement.","zh":"這個短語描述不受限制的水流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take place","meaning":"發生；進行","examples":[{"en":"Water circulation must be able to take place.","zh":"水循環必須能夠發生。"},{"en":"To take place means to happen or occur.","zh":"發生或進行，是指某事出現或展開。"},{"en":"The school concert will take place in the hall on Friday.","zh":"學校音樂會將於星期五在禮堂舉行。"},{"en":"If water circulation cannot take place, heat may not move efficiently through the bowl.","zh":"如果水循環不能發生，熱量可能無法有效地在碗中移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when describing events or processes.","zh":"這個短語常用於描述事件或過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"yet small enough for","meaning":"同時又要足夠小以便……","examples":[{"en":"The bowl must also be small enough for its sides to extract heat effectively.","zh":"碗同時又要足夠小，以便側面有效抽走熱量。"},{"en":"Yet small enough for means but also sufficiently small to allow another condition to work.","zh":"同時又要足夠小以便，是指但也要小到能讓另一條件發揮作用。"},{"en":"A school bag should be large enough for books, yet small enough for a child to carry comfortably.","zh":"書包應足夠大以放書，同時又要足夠小，讓孩子舒服地背起。"},{"en":"In this experiment, the container must balance two needs: circulation and effective heat extraction.","zh":"在這個實驗中，容器必須平衡兩種需要：循環和有效抽走熱量。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two opposite-looking requirements must both be met.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個看似相反的要求都必須滿足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"freezing areas","meaning":"結冰區域","examples":[{"en":"The freezing areas include the sides and base of the container.","zh":"結冰區域包括容器側面和底部。"},{"en":"Freezing areas are the parts where ice begins to form or where cooling is strongest.","zh":"結冰區域是冰開始形成或冷卻最強的位置。"},{"en":"In an ice tray, the corners may become freezing areas first.","zh":"在冰格盤中，角位可能最先成為結冰區域。"},{"en":"Freezing areas matter because they can remove heat from nearby liquid.","zh":"結冰區域很重要，因為它們可以從附近液體移走熱量。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the active places where freezing starts or develops.","zh":"這個短語指出結冰開始或發展的活躍位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be effective at","meaning":"在……方面有效","examples":[{"en":"The container walls must be effective at extracting heat.","zh":"容器壁必須在抽走熱量方面有效。"},{"en":"To be effective at something means to do it successfully or well.","zh":"在某方面有效，是指能成功或良好地做到該事。"},{"en":"A good umbrella is effective at keeping rain off your clothes.","zh":"好雨傘在防止衣服被雨淋濕方面有效。"},{"en":"A metal container may be effective at extracting heat because metal transfers heat quickly.","zh":"金屬容器可能在抽走熱量方面有效，因為金屬傳熱快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical performance.","zh":"這個短語描述實際表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"extract heat","meaning":"抽走熱量","examples":[{"en":"The sides and base help extract heat from the water.","zh":"側面和底部有助從水中抽走熱量。"},{"en":"To extract heat means to remove heat from something.","zh":"抽走熱量，是指從某物移除熱。"},{"en":"A fridge extracts heat from food to keep it cold.","zh":"雪櫃會從食物中抽走熱量，使食物保持寒冷。"},{"en":"If the container can extract heat quickly, the water may cool faster.","zh":"如果容器能快速抽走熱量，水可能冷卻得更快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the removal of thermal energy.","zh":"這個短語描述移除熱能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be affected by","meaning":"受到……影響","examples":[{"en":"The effect may be affected by water purity.","zh":"該效應可能受到水的純度影響。"},{"en":"To be affected by something means to be influenced or changed by it.","zh":"受到某事影響，是指被它影響或改變。"},{"en":"A student’s concentration may be affected by noise in the classroom.","zh":"學生的專注力可能受到課室噪音影響。"},{"en":"The freezing result may be affected by impurities, container size, and freezer behaviour.","zh":"結冰結果可能受到雜質、容器大小和冰格運作影響。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor can change another thing.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個因素可以改變另一件事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"water purity","meaning":"水的純度","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have investigated the role of water purity.","zh":"研究人員調查過水的純度所起的作用。"},{"en":"Water purity means how free water is from impurities, minerals, gases, or tiny particles.","zh":"水的純度，是指水有多不含雜質、礦物質、氣體或微小粒子。"},{"en":"Distilled water has higher water purity than ordinary tap water.","zh":"蒸餾水比普通自來水有更高水的純度。"},{"en":"Water purity may affect freezing because dissolved substances can change the freezing point.","zh":"水的純度可能影響結冰，因為溶解物質可以改變冰點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the chemical cleanliness of water.","zh":"這個短語描述水在化學上的潔淨程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"dissolved gas","meaning":"溶解氣體","examples":[{"en":"Dissolved gas may influence how water freezes.","zh":"溶解氣體可能影響水如何結冰。"},{"en":"Dissolved gas is gas that is mixed into a liquid.","zh":"溶解氣體是混入液體中的氣體。"},{"en":"Fizzy drinks contain dissolved gas, which forms bubbles when released.","zh":"有汽飲品含有溶解氣體，釋放時會形成氣泡。"},{"en":"Dissolved gas in water may affect bubbles, freezing behaviour, or heat transfer.","zh":"水中的溶解氣體可能影響氣泡、結冰行為或熱傳遞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gas present inside a liquid rather than above it.","zh":"這個短語描述存在於液體內，而不是液體上方的氣體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"distilled water","meaning":"蒸餾水","examples":[{"en":"Distilled water contains very few impurities.","zh":"蒸餾水含有極少雜質。"},{"en":"Distilled water is water purified by evaporation and condensation.","zh":"蒸餾水是透過蒸發和凝結淨化的水。"},{"en":"Science laboratories often use distilled water because it has fewer dissolved substances.","zh":"科學實驗室常使用蒸餾水，因為它含有較少溶解物質。"},{"en":"Using distilled water can help researchers test whether impurities affect freezing.","zh":"使用蒸餾水可以幫助研究人員測試雜質是否影響結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to highly purified water.","zh":"這個短語指高度淨化的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be totally free of","meaning":"完全不含……","examples":[{"en":"Distilled water is totally free of many common particles.","zh":"蒸餾水完全不含許多常見微粒。"},{"en":"To be totally free of something means to contain none of it.","zh":"完全不含某物，是指其中沒有該物。"},{"en":"A clean classroom floor should be totally free of broken glass before students return.","zh":"在學生回來前，乾淨的課室地板應完全不含碎玻璃。"},{"en":"If water is totally free of certain particles, researchers can compare it with ordinary water.","zh":"如果水完全不含某些微粒，研究人員就可以把它與普通水比較。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete absence.","zh":"這個短語描述完全沒有。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"particles common in","meaning":"在……中常見的微粒","examples":[{"en":"Normal drinking water contains particles common in natural water sources.","zh":"一般食水含有天然水源中常見的微粒。"},{"en":"Particles common in a place are tiny substances often found there.","zh":"在某處常見的微粒，是該處經常出現的細小物質。"},{"en":"Dust and pollen are particles common in outdoor air.","zh":"灰塵和花粉是戶外空氣中常見的微粒。"},{"en":"Particles common in natural water may affect how ice crystals form.","zh":"天然水中常見的微粒可能影響冰晶如何形成。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies typical small substances found in a particular source.","zh":"這個短語指出某來源中典型的細小物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"normal drinking water","meaning":"一般食水","examples":[{"en":"Normal drinking water contains dissolved substances and particles.","zh":"一般食水含有溶解物質和微粒。"},{"en":"Normal drinking water is ordinary water that is safe for people to drink.","zh":"一般食水是可供人安全飲用的普通水。"},{"en":"Tap water in a home is usually normal drinking water, not distilled water.","zh":"家中的自來水通常是一般食水，而不是蒸餾水。"},{"en":"Normal drinking water may freeze differently from distilled water because it contains minerals and particles.","zh":"一般食水可能因含有礦物質和微粒而與蒸餾水結冰方式不同。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts everyday water with laboratory-purified water.","zh":"這個短語把日常用水與實驗室淨化水作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"mineral water","meaning":"礦泉水","examples":[{"en":"Mineral water contains substances that distilled water lacks.","zh":"礦泉水含有蒸餾水沒有的物質。"},{"en":"Mineral water is water that contains naturally occurring minerals.","zh":"礦泉水是含有天然礦物質的水。"},{"en":"People may buy mineral water because they prefer its taste to ordinary tap water.","zh":"人們可能購買礦泉水，因為他們較喜歡它的味道。"},{"en":"Minerals in water can slightly change its freezing or boiling behaviour.","zh":"水中的礦物質可以輕微改變其結冰或沸騰行為。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to water with dissolved minerals.","zh":"這個短語指含有溶解礦物質的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be suspended in water","meaning":"懸浮在水中","examples":[{"en":"Tiny particles may be suspended in water.","zh":"微小粒子可能懸浮在水中。"},{"en":"To be suspended in water means to float or remain spread through the water instead of settling immediately.","zh":"懸浮在水中，是指漂浮或分散在水中，而不是立即沉底。"},{"en":"Muddy water contains soil particles suspended in water.","zh":"泥水含有懸浮在水中的泥土微粒。"},{"en":"Particles suspended in water may give ice crystals places to begin forming.","zh":"懸浮在水中的微粒可能為冰晶提供開始形成的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes small materials held inside liquid.","zh":"這個短語描述停留在液體內的小材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have a small effect on","meaning":"對……有輕微影響","examples":[{"en":"Suspended particles may have a small effect on cooling speed.","zh":"懸浮微粒可能對冷卻速度有輕微影響。"},{"en":"To have a small effect on something means to influence it slightly.","zh":"對某事有輕微影響，是指稍微影響它。"},{"en":"Sitting near a window may have a small effect on how cold a student feels.","zh":"坐近窗邊可能對學生感覺有多冷有輕微影響。"},{"en":"Even a small effect can matter if an experiment is very sensitive.","zh":"如果實驗非常敏感，即使輕微影響也可能重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited influence, not a major cause.","zh":"這個短語描述有限影響，而不是主要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"speed of cooling","meaning":"冷卻速度","examples":[{"en":"Impurities can influence the speed of cooling.","zh":"雜質可以影響冷卻速度。"},{"en":"Speed of cooling means how quickly something loses heat and becomes colder.","zh":"冷卻速度，是某物失去熱量並變冷的快慢。"},{"en":"A small cup of tea has a faster speed of cooling than a full teapot.","zh":"一小杯茶的冷卻速度比一整壺茶快。"},{"en":"The speed of cooling can affect when water reaches freezing temperature.","zh":"冷卻速度會影響水何時達到冰點。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to temperature change over time.","zh":"這個短語指隨時間發生的溫度變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ice molecules","meaning":"冰分子","examples":[{"en":"Ice molecules tend to exclude some dissolved particles.","zh":"冰分子往往會排斥某些溶解微粒。"},{"en":"Ice molecules are water molecules arranged in the solid structure of ice.","zh":"冰分子是排列成冰的固體結構的水分子。"},{"en":"In science class, students learn that ice molecules are arranged differently from liquid water molecules.","zh":"在科學課中，學生會學到冰分子的排列不同於液態水分子。"},{"en":"When ice molecules form a crystal, some impurities may be pushed out into the remaining water.","zh":"當冰分子形成晶體，某些雜質可能被推到剩餘水中。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the microscopic structure of frozen water.","zh":"這個短語指冷凍水的微觀結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tend to expel","meaning":"往往會排出","examples":[{"en":"Forming ice tends to expel impurities into the remaining liquid.","zh":"形成中的冰往往會把雜質排入剩餘液體。"},{"en":"To tend to expel something means to usually push it out or force it away.","zh":"往往會排出某物，是指通常把它推出或迫走。"},{"en":"A school may expel a student only after very serious rule-breaking.","zh":"學校只有在學生嚴重違規後，才可能開除學生。"},{"en":"In freezing water, forming ice tends to expel impurities because the ice structure does not easily include them.","zh":"在結冰水中，形成中的冰往往會排出雜質，因為冰結構不容易包含它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated tendency to push something out.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆出現的排出傾向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"surrounding water","meaning":"周圍的水","examples":[{"en":"The particles are forced into the surrounding water.","zh":"微粒被迫進入周圍的水中。"},{"en":"Surrounding water is the liquid water around a forming ice crystal or object.","zh":"周圍的水，是形成中的冰晶或物件附近的液態水。"},{"en":"A fish releases waste into the surrounding water in a tank.","zh":"魚在魚缸中把廢物排入周圍的水。"},{"en":"When impurities are pushed out of ice, they become concentrated in the surrounding water.","zh":"當雜質被冰推出，它們會在周圍的水中變得濃縮。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the nearby liquid environment.","zh":"這個短語指出附近的液體環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"become more concentrated","meaning":"變得更濃縮","examples":[{"en":"The remaining particles become more concentrated.","zh":"剩餘微粒變得更濃縮。"},{"en":"To become more concentrated means to have more substance within the same or a smaller amount of liquid.","zh":"變得更濃縮，是指在相同或較少液體中含有更多物質。"},{"en":"Soup becomes more concentrated when water boils away.","zh":"當水煮走後，湯會變得更濃縮。"},{"en":"As ice forms, impurities left in the liquid may become more concentrated.","zh":"當冰形成，留在液體中的雜質可能變得更濃縮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increase in strength or density of a substance.","zh":"這個短語描述物質強度或密度增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"just as","meaning":"正如","examples":[{"en":"Just as salt alters boiling point, impurities can alter freezing point.","zh":"正如鹽會改變沸點，雜質也可以改變冰點。"},{"en":"Just as introduces a comparison between two similar ideas.","zh":"正如，用來引入兩個相似想法之間的比較。"},{"en":"Just as exercise strengthens the body, practice strengthens writing skills.","zh":"正如運動強化身體，練習也會強化寫作能力。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain a new idea through a familiar one.","zh":"這個短語透過熟悉事物解釋新想法。"},{"en":"It is often used for analogy.","zh":"它常用於類比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"salt dissolved in water","meaning":"溶於水中的鹽","examples":[{"en":"Salt dissolved in water changes its freezing temperature.","zh":"溶於水中的鹽會改變水的結冰溫度。"},{"en":"Salt dissolved in water is salt that has mixed into water so that it is no longer visible as separate grains.","zh":"溶於水中的鹽，是已混入水中、不再以獨立鹽粒出現的鹽。"},{"en":"When you stir salt into soup, the salt becomes dissolved in water.","zh":"當你把鹽攪入湯中，鹽便溶於水中。"},{"en":"Salt dissolved in water can lower the temperature at which the water freezes.","zh":"溶於水中的鹽可以降低水結冰時的溫度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a solution made from salt and water.","zh":"這個短語描述由鹽和水形成的溶液。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"raise the boiling point","meaning":"提高沸點","examples":[{"en":"Dissolved salt can raise the boiling point of water.","zh":"溶解鹽可以提高水的沸點。"},{"en":"To raise the boiling point means to increase the temperature at which a liquid boils.","zh":"提高沸點，是指增加液體沸騰時的溫度。"},{"en":"Adding salt can raise the boiling point of water slightly.","zh":"加鹽可以稍微提高水的沸點。"},{"en":"This example shows that dissolved substances can change the physical behaviour of water.","zh":"這個例子顯示溶解物質可以改變水的物理行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an upward change in a temperature threshold.","zh":"這個短語描述溫度臨界點上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lower the temperature at which","meaning":"降低……發生時的溫度","examples":[{"en":"Salt lowers the temperature at which water freezes.","zh":"鹽會降低水結冰時的溫度。"},{"en":"To lower the temperature at which something happens means to make it happen only at a colder temperature.","zh":"降低某事發生時的溫度，是指令它只在更低溫度下才發生。"},{"en":"Salt on icy roads lowers the temperature at which ice remains frozen, helping it melt.","zh":"撒在結冰道路上的鹽會降低冰保持結冰狀態的溫度，幫助冰融化。"},{"en":"If impurities lower the temperature at which water freezes, extra cooling may be needed.","zh":"如果雜質降低水結冰時的溫度，就可能需要額外冷卻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a downward change in a temperature threshold.","zh":"這個短語描述溫度臨界點下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"final portion","meaning":"最後一部分","examples":[{"en":"The final portion of ordinary water may require additional cooling.","zh":"一般水的最後一部分可能需要額外冷卻。"},{"en":"Final portion means the last remaining part of something.","zh":"最後一部分，是某物剩下的最後部分。"},{"en":"The final portion of a meal may be saved for later if someone is full.","zh":"如果有人吃飽，一餐的最後一部分可能會留待之後吃。"},{"en":"In freezing water, the final portion may contain concentrated impurities and freeze later.","zh":"在水結冰時，最後一部分可能含有濃縮雜質，因此較遲結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the last part left in a process.","zh":"這個短語指過程中剩下的最後部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"extra cooling","meaning":"額外冷卻","examples":[{"en":"The remaining liquid may need extra cooling before freezing.","zh":"剩餘液體在結冰前可能需要額外冷卻。"},{"en":"Extra cooling means additional lowering of temperature beyond what was first expected.","zh":"額外冷卻，是指比最初預期更多地降低溫度。"},{"en":"A drink may need extra cooling if the fridge is not cold enough.","zh":"如果雪櫃不夠冷，飲品可能需要額外冷卻。"},{"en":"Impure water may need extra cooling because its freezing point is lower than pure water’s.","zh":"含雜質的水可能需要額外冷卻，因為它的冰點比純水低。"},{"en":"This phrase describes additional cooling needed to reach a result.","zh":"這個短語描述為達到某結果而需要的額外冷卻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"below zero","meaning":"低於零度","examples":[{"en":"Some water may remain liquid below zero degrees.","zh":"有些水可能在低於零度時仍保持液態。"},{"en":"Below zero means lower than zero degrees Celsius.","zh":"低於零度，是指低於攝氏零度。"},{"en":"On a winter morning, the temperature may fall below zero and make roads icy.","zh":"在冬天早上，氣溫可能降至低於零度，令道路結冰。"},{"en":"Water can sometimes remain liquid below zero if it is supercooled.","zh":"如果水處於過冷狀態，它有時可以在低於零度時仍維持液態。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a temperature lower than the normal freezing point of pure water.","zh":"這個短語描述低於純水正常冰點的溫度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"distort the effect","meaning":"扭曲該效應","examples":[{"en":"Experimental timing can distort the observed effect.","zh":"實驗時間安排可能扭曲觀察到的效應。"},{"en":"To distort the effect means to change or misrepresent what the result appears to show.","zh":"扭曲該效應，是指改變或錯誤呈現結果看似顯示的內容。"},{"en":"A badly worded survey question can distort the results of a school survey.","zh":"措辭差的問卷題目可以扭曲學校問卷結果。"},{"en":"If one bowl is placed in the freezer earlier than another, timing may distort the effect.","zh":"如果一個碗比另一個更早放進冰格，時間安排可能扭曲該效應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes interference with accurate observation.","zh":"這個短語描述對準確觀察的干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be placed simultaneously","meaning":"被同時放置","examples":[{"en":"The bowls should be placed simultaneously in the freezer.","zh":"這些碗應被同時放進冰格。"},{"en":"To be placed simultaneously means to be put somewhere at the same time.","zh":"被同時放置，是指在同一時間被放到某處。"},{"en":"In a fair race, all runners should start simultaneously.","zh":"在公平比賽中，所有跑手應同時起步。"},{"en":"If bowls are placed simultaneously, timing is less likely to affect the comparison.","zh":"如果碗被同時放置，時間安排較不可能影響比較。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled timing in an experiment.","zh":"這個短語描述實驗中的受控時間安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in the same freezer","meaning":"在同一個冰格內","examples":[{"en":"Both samples must be tested in the same freezer.","zh":"兩個樣本必須在同一個冰格內測試。"},{"en":"In the same freezer means under the same freezing environment and machine conditions.","zh":"在同一個冰格內，是指處於相同冷凍環境和機器條件下。"},{"en":"Two lunchboxes in the same freezer experience more similar cooling conditions than lunchboxes in different freezers.","zh":"放在同一個冰格內的兩個飯盒，比放在不同冰格內的飯盒有更相似的冷卻條件。"},{"en":"Testing samples in the same freezer reduces differences caused by equipment.","zh":"在同一個冰格內測試樣本，可以減少由設備造成的差異。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses experimental consistency.","zh":"這個短語強調實驗一致性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"freezer thermostat","meaning":"冰格恆溫器","examples":[{"en":"The freezer thermostat responds to changes in internal temperature.","zh":"冰格恆溫器會對內部溫度變化作出反應。"},{"en":"A freezer thermostat is a device that senses and controls the temperature inside a freezer.","zh":"冰格恆溫器是感應並控制冰格內部溫度的裝置。"},{"en":"A home air conditioner also has a thermostat that switches cooling on or off.","zh":"家用冷氣也有恆溫器，用來開啟或關閉冷卻。"},{"en":"If a hot bowl raises the freezer temperature, the thermostat may activate stronger cooling.","zh":"如果熱碗提高冰格溫度，恆溫器可能啟動更強冷卻。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the freezer’s temperature-control system.","zh":"這個短語指冰格的溫度控制系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"register the presence of","meaning":"偵測到……的存在","examples":[{"en":"The thermostat is more likely to register the presence of a hotter bowl.","zh":"恆溫器較可能偵測到較熱的碗存在。"},{"en":"To register the presence of something means to detect that it is there.","zh":"偵測到某物的存在，是指感應到它在那裡。"},{"en":"A motion sensor may register the presence of a person in a hallway.","zh":"動作感應器可能偵測到走廊中有人存在。"},{"en":"If the freezer registers the presence of a hot bowl, it may switch on extra cooling.","zh":"如果冰格偵測到熱碗的存在，它可能啟動額外冷卻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes detection by a device or system.","zh":"這個短語描述裝置或系統的偵測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"internal temperature","meaning":"內部溫度","examples":[{"en":"A hot container can raise the freezer’s internal temperature.","zh":"熱容器可以提高冰格內部溫度。"},{"en":"Internal temperature is the temperature inside a space, object, or system.","zh":"內部溫度是某空間、物件或系統內部的溫度。"},{"en":"A doctor may check a patient’s internal temperature to see whether they have a fever.","zh":"醫生可能檢查病人的內部溫度，以判斷是否發燒。"},{"en":"A freezer’s internal temperature may rise briefly when hot food is placed inside.","zh":"當熱食物被放進去，冰格內部溫度可能短暫上升。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to temperature within something, not outside it.","zh":"這個短語指某物內部，而不是外部的溫度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"cause a boost of","meaning":"令……增強","examples":[{"en":"The temperature change may cause a boost of freezing power.","zh":"溫度變化可能令冷凍能力增強。"},{"en":"To cause a boost of something means to produce a temporary increase in it.","zh":"令某事增強，是指造成某事短暫增加。"},{"en":"Extra advertising may cause a boost of sales during a holiday.","zh":"額外廣告可能在假期期間令銷售增強。"},{"en":"A hot bowl may cause a boost of cooling because the freezer motor turns on.","zh":"熱碗可能因令冰格馬達啟動而造成冷卻能力增強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increase triggered by a particular cause.","zh":"這個短語描述由特定原因觸發的增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"freezing power","meaning":"冷凍能力","examples":[{"en":"The freezer may temporarily produce greater freezing power.","zh":"冰格可能暫時產生更大的冷凍能力。"},{"en":"Freezing power is the freezer’s ability to remove heat and make things freeze.","zh":"冷凍能力是冰格移除熱量並令物件結冰的能力。"},{"en":"A commercial freezer has more freezing power than a small home freezer.","zh":"商用冰格比小型家用冰格有更強冷凍能力。"},{"en":"Greater freezing power can change how quickly a sample cools and freezes.","zh":"更大冷凍能力可以改變樣本冷卻和結冰的速度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the strength of a freezer’s cooling ability.","zh":"這個短語描述冰格冷卻能力的強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"motor is activated","meaning":"馬達被啟動","examples":[{"en":"The cooling motor is activated when the thermostat detects extra heat.","zh":"當恆溫器偵測到額外熱量，冷卻馬達會被啟動。"},{"en":"Motor is activated means the motor starts working.","zh":"馬達被啟動，是指馬達開始運作。"},{"en":"In an automatic door, the motor is activated when the sensor detects movement.","zh":"在自動門中，感應器偵測到移動時，馬達會被啟動。"},{"en":"When the freezer motor is activated, the freezer may cool more strongly for a short time.","zh":"當冰格馬達被啟動，冰格可能短時間內更強力冷卻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mechanical response.","zh":"這個短語描述機械反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"not fully understood","meaning":"尚未完全理解","examples":[{"en":"The Mpemba Effect is still not fully understood.","zh":"姆潘巴效應仍尚未完全理解。"},{"en":"Not fully understood means experts do not yet have a complete explanation.","zh":"尚未完全理解，是指專家仍未有完整解釋。"},{"en":"A medicine may work well but still not be fully understood by researchers.","zh":"一種藥物可能有效，但研究人員仍尚未完全理解其作用。"},{"en":"The Mpemba Effect is not fully understood because many variables may be involved.","zh":"姆潘巴效應尚未完全理解，因為可能涉及許多變數。"},{"en":"This phrase signals remaining uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語表示仍有不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"continue to delve into","meaning":"繼續深入研究","examples":[{"en":"Researchers continue to delve into the physics behind the effect.","zh":"研究人員繼續深入研究該效應背後的物理。"},{"en":"To continue to delve into something means to keep studying it deeply and carefully.","zh":"繼續深入研究某事，是指持續深入而仔細地研究它。"},{"en":"Teachers may continue to delve into why students struggle with grammar.","zh":"老師可能繼續深入研究學生為何在文法上有困難。"},{"en":"Scientists continue to delve into the Mpemba Effect because no single explanation has fully settled the debate.","zh":"科學家繼續深入研究姆潘巴效應，因為尚未有單一解釋完全平息爭論。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than simply saying keep studying.","zh":"這個短語比 simply keep studying 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"underlying physics","meaning":"背後的物理原理","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are still investigating the underlying physics.","zh":"科學家仍在研究背後的物理原理。"},{"en":"Underlying physics means the basic physical principles behind a phenomenon.","zh":"背後的物理原理，是某現象背後的基本物理法則。"},{"en":"The underlying physics of a fridge involves heat transfer and pressure changes.","zh":"雪櫃背後的物理原理涉及熱傳遞和壓力變化。"},{"en":"Understanding the underlying physics can explain why the Mpemba Effect appears only in some situations.","zh":"理解背後的物理原理可以解釋為何姆潘巴效應只在某些情況中出現。"},{"en":"This phrase points to deeper mechanisms, not surface observation.","zh":"這個短語指更深層機制，而不是表面觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"reach consensus","meaning":"達成共識","examples":[{"en":"Physicists have not yet reached consensus.","zh":"物理學家尚未達成共識。"},{"en":"To reach consensus means to arrive at general agreement.","zh":"達成共識，是指取得普遍同意。"},{"en":"A class may reach consensus after discussing which charity to support.","zh":"一班學生討論支持哪個慈善機構後，可能達成共識。"},{"en":"If scientists have not reached consensus, different explanations are still being debated.","zh":"如果科學家尚未達成共識，就表示不同解釋仍在被討論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shared agreement among a group.","zh":"這個短語描述群體之間的共同同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"supercooling","meaning":"過冷現象","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers believe that supercooling is involved.","zh":"有些研究人員認為過冷現象涉及其中。"},{"en":"Supercooling occurs when a liquid remains liquid below its normal freezing point.","zh":"過冷現象是液體在低於正常冰點時仍維持液態。"},{"en":"A bottle of very pure water may supercool and then suddenly freeze when shaken.","zh":"一瓶非常純的水可能出現過冷，然後在被搖動時突然結冰。"},{"en":"Supercooling may explain why some colder water does not freeze immediately at zero degrees.","zh":"過冷現象可能解釋為何有些較冷的水在零度時沒有立即結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a liquid staying unfrozen even below its freezing point.","zh":"這個短語指液體即使低於冰點仍未結冰的狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be involved","meaning":"涉及其中","examples":[{"en":"Several physical processes may be involved.","zh":"幾個物理過程可能涉及其中。"},{"en":"To be involved means to be part of a situation, event, or process.","zh":"涉及其中，是指成為某情況、事件或過程的一部分。"},{"en":"Several teachers may be involved in organising a school trip.","zh":"幾位老師可能涉及組織一次學校旅行。"},{"en":"In the Mpemba Effect, evaporation, circulation, supercooling, and container size may all be involved.","zh":"在姆潘巴效應中，蒸發、循環、過冷和容器大小都可能涉及其中。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something plays a role in a larger process.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事在較大過程中發揮角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"molecular bonds","meaning":"分子鍵","examples":[{"en":"Molecular bonds in water may affect freezing behaviour.","zh":"水中的分子鍵可能影響結冰行為。"},{"en":"Molecular bonds are forces or connections that hold atoms or molecules together.","zh":"分子鍵是把原子或分子連接在一起的力量或連結。"},{"en":"In chemistry class, students learn that molecular bonds affect a substance’s properties.","zh":"在化學課中，學生會學到分子鍵影響物質性質。"},{"en":"Changes in molecular bonds may influence how water cools, freezes, or releases heat.","zh":"分子鍵的變化可能影響水如何冷卻、結冰或釋放熱量。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to structure at a microscopic level.","zh":"這個短語指微觀層面的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"affect the rate of","meaning":"影響……的速度","examples":[{"en":"The structure of water may affect the rate of cooling.","zh":"水的結構可能影響冷卻速度。"},{"en":"To affect the rate of something means to change how fast it happens.","zh":"影響某事的速度，是指改變它發生的快慢。"},{"en":"Heavy traffic can affect the rate of buses arriving at school.","zh":"交通擠塞可以影響巴士到校的速度。"},{"en":"Container material can affect the rate of heat loss from water.","zh":"容器材料可以影響水的熱量流失速度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes influence on speed.","zh":"這個短語描述對速度的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"competition to explain","meaning":"解釋……的比賽","examples":[{"en":"A competition was held to explain the phenomenon.","zh":"曾舉辦一場解釋該現象的比賽。"},{"en":"A competition to explain something invites people to propose the best explanation for it.","zh":"解釋某事的比賽，是邀請人們提出最佳解釋的比賽。"},{"en":"A school may hold a competition to explain why plants grow differently in different classrooms.","zh":"學校可能舉辦一場比賽，解釋為何植物在不同課室中生長不同。"},{"en":"Such a competition can attract many ideas and public interest.","zh":"這類比賽可以吸引許多想法和公眾興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a contest focused on giving an explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述以提出解釋為重點的競賽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be run by","meaning":"由……舉辦","examples":[{"en":"The competition was run by the Royal Society of Chemistry.","zh":"該比賽由皇家化學學會舉辦。"},{"en":"To be run by an organisation means to be organised or managed by it.","zh":"由某組織舉辦，是指由它組織或管理。"},{"en":"A school fair may be run by teachers, parents, and student volunteers.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能由老師、家長和學生義工舉辦。"},{"en":"When a competition is run by a scientific society, it may attract serious explanations.","zh":"當比賽由科學學會舉辦，它可能吸引認真的解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who is responsible for an event or programme.","zh":"這個短語指出誰負責某活動或計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"attract more than","meaning":"吸引超過……","examples":[{"en":"The competition attracted more than twenty-two thousand entries.","zh":"該比賽吸引超過二萬二千份參賽作品。"},{"en":"To attract more than a number means to receive or draw in a number greater than that amount.","zh":"吸引超過某數量，是指收到或吸引多於該數量。"},{"en":"A popular school concert may attract more than five hundred parents.","zh":"受歡迎的學校音樂會可能吸引超過五百名家長。"},{"en":"If a competition attracts more than twenty-two thousand entries, it clearly interests many people.","zh":"如果比賽吸引超過二萬二千份作品，這清楚顯示它令許多人感興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows large scale or popularity.","zh":"這個短語顯示大規模或受歡迎程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"winning entry","meaning":"得獎作品","examples":[{"en":"The winning entry highlighted the possible role of supercooling.","zh":"得獎作品強調過冷現象可能扮演的角色。"},{"en":"A winning entry is the answer, essay, or submission judged best in a competition.","zh":"得獎作品是在比賽中被評為最佳的答案、文章或提交作品。"},{"en":"The winning entry in a school science contest may explain a difficult idea clearly.","zh":"學校科學比賽的得獎作品可能清楚解釋一個困難概念。"},{"en":"A winning entry may be persuasive, but it does not always settle a scientific debate forever.","zh":"得獎作品可能具說服力，但不一定永遠解決科學爭論。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the selected best submission.","zh":"這個短語指被選出的最佳提交作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"important factor","meaning":"重要因素","examples":[{"en":"Supercooling was suggested as an important factor.","zh":"過冷現象被提出為一個重要因素。"},{"en":"An important factor is a cause or influence that matters significantly.","zh":"重要因素是具有顯著影響的原因或因素。"},{"en":"Sleep is an important factor in a student’s ability to concentrate.","zh":"睡眠是學生集中精神能力的重要因素。"},{"en":"Supercooling may be an important factor, but it may not be the only explanation.","zh":"過冷現象可能是重要因素，但未必是唯一解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights something that plays a major role.","zh":"這個短語突出發揮主要作用的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"underlying explanation","meaning":"背後的解釋","examples":[{"en":"The underlying explanation remains the subject of debate.","zh":"背後的解釋仍是爭論主題。"},{"en":"An underlying explanation is the deeper reason behind a phenomenon or problem.","zh":"背後的解釋是某現象或問題較深層的原因。"},{"en":"If a student is always late, the underlying explanation may be poor sleep or a long commute.","zh":"如果學生總是遲到，背後的解釋可能是睡眠差或通勤時間長。"},{"en":"The underlying explanation of the Mpemba Effect is debated because several processes may be involved.","zh":"姆潘巴效應背後的解釋仍有爭議，因為可能涉及幾個過程。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the deeper cause, not just the visible result.","zh":"這個短語指更深層原因，而不只是可見結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"continue to fascinate","meaning":"繼續令人着迷","examples":[{"en":"The phenomenon continues to fascinate scientists and the public.","zh":"這個現象繼續令科學家和公眾着迷。"},{"en":"To continue to fascinate means to keep attracting strong interest and curiosity.","zh":"繼續令人着迷，是指持續吸引強烈興趣和好奇心。"},{"en":"Space travel continues to fascinate children because it feels mysterious and exciting.","zh":"太空旅行繼續令孩子着迷，因為它感覺神秘又刺激。"},{"en":"The Mpemba Effect continues to fascinate people because it seems to contradict common sense.","zh":"姆潘巴效應繼續令人着迷，因為它似乎違反常識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lasting curiosity.","zh":"這個短語描述持久好奇心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"write the correct letter","meaning":"填寫正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students write the correct letter in each answer box.","zh":"學生在每個答案格填寫正確字母。"},{"en":"To write the correct letter means to choose the option letter that matches the answer.","zh":"填寫正確字母，是指選擇與答案相符的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice question, students may write A, B, C, or D.","zh":"在多項選擇題中，學生可能填寫 A、B、C 或 D。"},{"en":"Writing the wrong letter can lose marks even if the student understands the passage.","zh":"即使學生理解篇章，填錯字母也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is an exam instruction about answer format.","zh":"這個短語是關於答案格式的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"raise the temperature of","meaning":"提高……的溫度","examples":[{"en":"The summary refers to raising the temperature of cold water.","zh":"摘要提到提高冷水的溫度。"},{"en":"To raise the temperature of something means to make it warmer.","zh":"提高某物的溫度，是指令它變暖。"},{"en":"Turning on a heater can raise the temperature of a classroom.","zh":"開暖爐可以提高課室的溫度。"},{"en":"Raising the temperature of water gives it more heat to lose before freezing.","zh":"提高水的溫度會令它在結冰前有更多熱量需要流失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes warming something.","zh":"這個短語描述令某物變暖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"result in more rapid cooling","meaning":"導致更快速冷卻","examples":[{"en":"Heating the water may result in more rapid cooling.","zh":"加熱水可能導致更快速冷卻。"},{"en":"To result in more rapid cooling means to cause temperature to fall faster.","zh":"導致更快速冷卻，是指造成溫度更快下降。"},{"en":"Spreading hot food thinly on a plate may result in more rapid cooling.","zh":"把熱食物薄薄鋪在碟上，可能導致更快速冷卻。"},{"en":"A larger temperature difference may result in more rapid cooling at the surface.","zh":"較大溫差可能導致表面更快速冷卻。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with faster loss of heat.","zh":"這個短語把原因與更快熱量流失連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"create its own icy hollow","meaning":"形成自己的冰凹位","examples":[{"en":"The early theory suggested that a warm container created its own icy hollow.","zh":"早期理論認為暖容器形成自己的冰凹位。"},{"en":"To create its own icy hollow means to melt a small space in ice and sit inside it.","zh":"形成自己的冰凹位，是指在冰中融出一個小空間並坐在其中。"},{"en":"A warm bowl placed on ice may create its own icy hollow beneath the base.","zh":"暖碗放在冰上，可能在底部下方形成自己的冰凹位。"},{"en":"This hollow was thought to improve contact with ice and possibly speed freezing.","zh":"人們曾認為這個凹位改善與冰的接觸，並可能加速結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an early proposed explanation, not the final answer.","zh":"這個短語描述早期提出的解釋，而不是最終答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"rest on","meaning":"放置在……上","examples":[{"en":"The containers were compared while resting on different surfaces.","zh":"這些容器在放置於不同表面上時被比較。"},{"en":"To rest on a surface means to be placed or supported on it.","zh":"放置在某表面上，是指被放在其上或由其支撐。"},{"en":"A laptop should rest on a flat table so that it does not fall.","zh":"手提電腦應放置在平坦桌面上，以免跌落。"},{"en":"In the experiment, bowls resting on different surfaces helped test whether the surface mattered.","zh":"在實驗中，放置在不同表面上的碗有助測試表面是否重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical position of an object.","zh":"這個短語描述物件的實體位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"indicate that","meaning":"顯示","examples":[{"en":"The comparisons indicated that the original theory was inaccurate.","zh":"比較結果顯示原本理論並不準確。"},{"en":"To indicate that means to show or suggest that something is true.","zh":"顯示某事，是指表明或暗示某事為真。"},{"en":"Dark clouds may indicate that rain is coming.","zh":"烏雲可能顯示快要下雨。"},{"en":"If experiment results indicate that a theory is inaccurate, researchers need another explanation.","zh":"如果實驗結果顯示某理論不準確，研究人員就需要另一個解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase presents evidence or signs that point to a conclusion.","zh":"這個短語呈現指向結論的證據或跡象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"prove not to be","meaning":"證明並非","examples":[{"en":"Evaporation proved not to be a significant factor.","zh":"蒸發證明並非重要因素。"},{"en":"To prove not to be something means evidence showed that it was not that thing.","zh":"證明並非某事，是指證據顯示它不是該事。"},{"en":"The missing homework proved not to be lost; it was in the student’s bag.","zh":"失蹤的功課證明並非遺失；它在學生書包裡。"},{"en":"If evaporation proved not to be significant, scientists had to look for other causes.","zh":"如果蒸發證明並非重要因素，科學家就要尋找其他原因。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when evidence rejects an earlier possibility.","zh":"這個短語用於證據否定早前可能性時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"significant factor","meaning":"重要因素","examples":[{"en":"The researchers examined whether evaporation was a significant factor.","zh":"研究人員檢視蒸發是否是重要因素。"},{"en":"A significant factor is an important influence on the result.","zh":"重要因素是對結果有重要影響的因素。"},{"en":"Family support can be a significant factor in a student’s confidence.","zh":"家庭支持可以是學生自信心的重要因素。"},{"en":"A factor may exist but still not be significant enough to explain the whole result.","zh":"一個因素可以存在，但仍未必重要到足以解釋整個結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that matters in a situation.","zh":"這個短語描述在某情況中有重要性的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"temperature measurements","meaning":"溫度測量結果","examples":[{"en":"Temperature measurements showed which sample reached zero first.","zh":"溫度測量結果顯示哪個樣本先達到零度。"},{"en":"Temperature measurements are recorded readings of how hot or cold something is.","zh":"溫度測量結果是記錄某物冷熱程度的讀數。"},{"en":"A nurse takes temperature measurements to check whether a patient has a fever.","zh":"護士會量度體溫，以檢查病人是否發燒。"},{"en":"Temperature measurements help researchers compare samples accurately.","zh":"溫度測量結果幫助研究人員準確比較樣本。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to numerical data about temperature.","zh":"這個短語指關於溫度的數字資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"take longer to solidify","meaning":"需要更長時間凝固","examples":[{"en":"The cooler sample sometimes took longer to solidify.","zh":"較冷樣本有時需要更長時間凝固。"},{"en":"To take longer to solidify means to need more time to become solid.","zh":"需要更長時間凝固，是指需要更多時間變成固體。"},{"en":"Jelly in a large bowl may take longer to solidify than jelly in small cups.","zh":"大碗啫喱可能比小杯啫喱需要更長時間凝固。"},{"en":"A sample may reach freezing temperature but still take longer to solidify completely.","zh":"樣本可能達到冰點，但仍需要更長時間才完全凝固。"},{"en":"This phrase describes delayed change from liquid to solid.","zh":"這個短語描述由液體變成固體的延遲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"provided there is","meaning":"只要存在……","examples":[{"en":"Provided there is a temperature difference, circulation can continue.","zh":"只要存在溫差，循環便可繼續。"},{"en":"Provided there is means if there is or as long as there is.","zh":"只要存在，是指如果有或只要有。"},{"en":"Students can work outside provided there is no heavy rain.","zh":"只要沒有大雨，學生就可以在戶外工作。"},{"en":"Water can keep circulating provided there is enough temperature difference inside the bowl.","zh":"只要碗內存在足夠溫差，水就可以繼續循環。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a condition that must be met.","zh":"這個短語引入必須滿足的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"continue to circulate","meaning":"繼續循環","examples":[{"en":"Water will continue to circulate while temperature differences remain.","zh":"只要溫差仍存在，水便會繼續循環。"},{"en":"To continue to circulate means to keep moving around within a system.","zh":"繼續循環，是指在系統內持續移動。"},{"en":"Air will continue to circulate in a room if the fan stays on.","zh":"如果風扇一直開着，空氣會在房間內繼續循環。"},{"en":"Water continues to circulate when cooler water sinks and warmer water rises.","zh":"當較冷的水下沉而較暖的水上升時，水會繼續循環。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing internal movement.","zh":"這個短語描述持續的內部移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"less water circulation","meaning":"較少水流循環","examples":[{"en":"Cooler water may have less water circulation.","zh":"較冷的水可能有較少水流循環。"},{"en":"Less water circulation means weaker or reduced movement of water inside a container.","zh":"較少水流循環，是指容器內水的移動較弱或較少。"},{"en":"A blocked pipe may cause less water circulation in a fish tank.","zh":"堵塞的水管可能導致魚缸中的水流循環較少。"},{"en":"If cooler water has less circulation, heat from the centre may move outward more slowly.","zh":"如果較冷的水循環較少，中心熱量可能較慢向外移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reduced internal flow.","zh":"這個短語描述內部流動減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"slower rate of freezing","meaning":"較慢的結冰速度","examples":[{"en":"Reduced circulation may produce a slower rate of freezing.","zh":"循環減少可能產生較慢的結冰速度。"},{"en":"A slower rate of freezing means ice forms more slowly.","zh":"較慢的結冰速度，是指冰形成得更慢。"},{"en":"A large bottle of juice may have a slower rate of freezing than a thin ice tray.","zh":"一大瓶果汁的結冰速度可能比薄冰格盤慢。"},{"en":"If water circulation is blocked, the centre may freeze at a slower rate.","zh":"如果水循環被阻礙，中心部分可能以較慢速度結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decrease in freezing speed.","zh":"這個短語描述結冰速度下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"further slow the process","meaning":"進一步減慢過程","examples":[{"en":"Surface ice may further slow the process of freezing.","zh":"表面冰可能進一步減慢結冰過程。"},{"en":"To further slow the process means to make an already slow process even slower.","zh":"進一步減慢過程，是指令已經較慢的過程變得更慢。"},{"en":"Heavy traffic can further slow the process of getting to school.","zh":"嚴重塞車可以進一步減慢上學過程。"},{"en":"Surface ice can further slow freezing by acting as insulation.","zh":"表面冰可以透過發揮隔熱作用進一步減慢結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an additional delaying effect.","zh":"這個短語描述額外延遲效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與文章資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否與篇章一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information means to match what the text says.","zh":"與文章資料一致，是指符合文本所說內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says evaporation was insignificant, a statement saying the same thing agrees with the information.","zh":"如果篇章說蒸發並不重要，而某陳述說相同內容，它就與文章資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when deciding whether a statement agrees with the information.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與文章資料一致時，不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN reading questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文章資料相反","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與篇章資料相反。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"與資料相反，是指說出與篇章內容相反的東西。"},{"en":"If the passage says the effect is not fully understood, a statement saying it is completely explained contradicts the information.","zh":"如果篇章說該效應尚未完全理解，而陳述說它已被完全解釋，就是與文章資料相反。"},{"en":"A contradiction must be based on clear conflict with the text.","zh":"矛盾必須基於與文本的清楚衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase usually points to a FALSE answer in reading tests.","zh":"這個短語在閱讀測驗中通常指向 FALSE 答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students select “NOT GIVEN” when there is no information on the point.","zh":"當文中沒有相關資料時，學生選擇 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not give enough evidence to decide.","zh":"文中沒有相關資料，是指篇章沒有提供足夠證據作判斷。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions who paid for an experiment, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果篇章從未提及誰支付實驗費用，文中就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when there is no information on this in the text.","zh":"當文本沒有相關資料時，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase corresponds to NOT GIVEN.","zh":"這個短語對應 NOT GIVEN。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"cannot be seen when","meaning":"在……情況下無法觀察到","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether the effect cannot be seen under certain conditions.","zh":"該陳述問該效應是否在某些情況下無法觀察到。"},{"en":"Cannot be seen when means cannot be observed if a particular condition exists.","zh":"在某情況下無法觀察到，是指如果某條件存在，就看不到它。"},{"en":"Stars cannot be seen when the sky is covered by thick clouds.","zh":"當天空被厚雲覆蓋，星星就無法被看見。"},{"en":"The Mpemba Effect may not be seen when the temperature difference is too extreme.","zh":"當溫差太極端，姆潘巴效應可能無法被觀察到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a condition that prevents observation.","zh":"這個短語描述阻止觀察的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"extreme temperature difference","meaning":"極端溫差","examples":[{"en":"An extreme temperature difference may prevent the effect from appearing.","zh":"極端溫差可能阻止該效應出現。"},{"en":"An extreme temperature difference is a very large gap between two temperatures.","zh":"極端溫差，是兩個溫度之間非常大的差距。"},{"en":"There is an extreme temperature difference between boiling soup and frozen ice cream.","zh":"沸騰的湯和冷凍雪糕之間有極端溫差。"},{"en":"If the temperature difference is extreme, the usual Mpemba comparison may not work.","zh":"如果溫差極端，通常的姆潘巴效應比較可能不成立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a condition that can limit the effect.","zh":"這個短語描述可以限制該效應的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be widely accepted","meaning":"被廣泛接受","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether the original results are still widely accepted.","zh":"該陳述問原本結果是否仍被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"To be widely accepted means to be generally believed or approved by many people.","zh":"被廣泛接受，是指被許多人普遍相信或認同。"},{"en":"A school policy is widely accepted if most teachers, parents, and students agree with it.","zh":"如果大多數老師、家長和學生都同意某校規，它就是被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"Scientific results are widely accepted only when enough reliable evidence supports them.","zh":"科學結果只有在有足夠可靠證據支持時，才會被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad agreement.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"alter the effect","meaning":"改變該效應","examples":[{"en":"The size of the container may alter the effect.","zh":"容器大小可能改變該效應。"},{"en":"To alter the effect means to change how the effect appears or behaves.","zh":"改變該效應，是指改變該效應如何出現或表現。"},{"en":"Using a different study method may alter the effect of revision on exam results.","zh":"使用不同溫習方法可能改變溫習對考試成績的效果。"},{"en":"In freezing experiments, container size may alter the effect by changing circulation and heat loss.","zh":"在結冰實驗中，容器大小可能透過改變循環和熱量流失而改變該效應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a condition changing the result.","zh":"這個短語描述某條件改變結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"experiment on","meaning":"對……進行實驗","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether the researchers experimented on different types of water.","zh":"該陳述問研究人員是否對不同種類的水進行實驗。"},{"en":"To experiment on something means to test it scientifically.","zh":"對某物進行實驗，是指科學地測試它。"},{"en":"A class may experiment on different soils to see which one helps plants grow best.","zh":"一班學生可能對不同泥土進行實驗，以看看哪種最有利植物生長。"},{"en":"Researchers may experiment on pure and impure water to compare freezing behaviour.","zh":"研究人員可能對純水和含雜質的水進行實驗，以比較結冰行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the object being tested.","zh":"這個短語描述被測試的對象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"pure and impure water","meaning":"純水和含雜質的水","examples":[{"en":"Later studies considered both pure and impure water.","zh":"後來研究考慮了純水和含雜質的水。"},{"en":"Pure water has very few impurities, while impure water contains particles, minerals, or dissolved substances.","zh":"純水含有很少雜質，而含雜質的水含有微粒、礦物質或溶解物質。"},{"en":"Distilled water is closer to pure water than tap water.","zh":"蒸餾水比自來水更接近純水。"},{"en":"Comparing pure and impure water helps researchers test whether impurities affect freezing.","zh":"比較純水和含雜質的水，有助研究人員測試雜質是否影響結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts two types of water samples.","zh":"這個短語對比兩種水樣本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"one variable","meaning":"其中一個變數","examples":[{"en":"The timing of the containers is one experimental variable.","zh":"容器放入時間是其中一個實驗變數。"},{"en":"One variable is one factor that can change in an experiment.","zh":"其中一個變數，是實驗中可以改變的一個因素。"},{"en":"In a cooking test, oven temperature is one variable.","zh":"在烹飪測試中，焗爐溫度是其中一個變數。"},{"en":"If one variable is not controlled, it may affect the result.","zh":"如果其中一個變數沒有被控制，它可能影響結果。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies one influence among many possible influences.","zh":"這個短語指出眾多可能影響中的一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"timing of containers","meaning":"放入容器的時間","examples":[{"en":"The timing of containers entering the freezer may affect the result.","zh":"放入容器的時間可能影響結果。"},{"en":"Timing of containers means when each container is placed into the freezer.","zh":"放入容器的時間，是指每個容器何時被放進冰格。"},{"en":"In a race, the timing of each runner’s start must be fair.","zh":"在比賽中，每位跑手起步的時間安排必須公平。"},{"en":"If one container enters the freezer earlier, the timing may distort the experiment.","zh":"如果一個容器較早放進冰格，時間安排可能扭曲實驗。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to when the containers are introduced into the freezing environment.","zh":"這個短語指容器何時被放入冷凍環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"account for","meaning":"解釋；說明……的成因","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether supercooling fully accounts for the effect.","zh":"該陳述問過冷現象是否完全解釋該效應。"},{"en":"To account for something means to explain its cause or reason.","zh":"解釋某事，是指說明其成因或理由。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep may account for why a student cannot concentrate in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可能解釋學生為何在課堂上不能集中精神。"},{"en":"Supercooling may account for part of the Mpemba Effect, but it may not explain everything.","zh":"過冷現象可能解釋姆潘巴效應的一部分，但未必能解釋全部。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing causes.","zh":"這個短語用於討論原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be best summed up as","meaning":"最能概括為","examples":[{"en":"The effect is best summed up as a surprising observation about freezing water.","zh":"該效應最能概括為一項關於水結冰的驚人觀察。"},{"en":"To be best summed up as something means to be most accurately described in a short way.","zh":"最能概括為某事，是指用最準確簡短的方式描述它。"},{"en":"The story is best summed up as a lesson about asking good questions.","zh":"這個故事最能概括為一個關於提出好問題的教訓。"},{"en":"A title question often asks which option best sums up the main idea.","zh":"標題題常問哪個選項最能概括主旨。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the clearest overall summary.","zh":"這個短語聚焦最清楚的整體摘要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"observation that","meaning":"……這一觀察結果","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines the observation that warmer water may freeze faster.","zh":"篇章探討較暖的水可能更快結冰這一觀察結果。"},{"en":"Observation that introduces something noticed, recorded, or studied.","zh":"……這一觀察結果，用來引入被注意、記錄或研究的事情。"},{"en":"The observation that students learn better after sleep has influenced school discussions.","zh":"學生睡眠後學習得更好這一觀察結果，影響了學校討論。"},{"en":"An observation can become important even before people fully explain it.","zh":"觀察結果即使尚未被完全解釋，也可以變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the key noticed fact.","zh":"這個短語引入關鍵觀察事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"different sources of heat","meaning":"不同熱源","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to different sources of heat.","zh":"該選項提到不同熱源。"},{"en":"Different sources of heat are different things or processes that provide thermal energy.","zh":"不同熱源，是提供熱能的不同物件或過程。"},{"en":"Sunlight, a stove, and a heater are different sources of heat.","zh":"陽光、爐火和暖爐都是不同熱源。"},{"en":"Different sources of heat may warm water in different ways, but the passage focuses mainly on temperature and freezing.","zh":"不同熱源可能以不同方式加熱水，但篇章主要聚焦溫度和結冰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where heat comes from.","zh":"這個短語描述熱量來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"cool at different rates","meaning":"以不同速度冷卻","examples":[{"en":"Water may cool at different rates under different conditions.","zh":"水在不同條件下可能以不同速度冷卻。"},{"en":"To cool at different rates means to lose heat at different speeds.","zh":"以不同速度冷卻，是指以不同快慢失去熱量。"},{"en":"Soup in a wide bowl and soup in a deep pot cool at different rates.","zh":"寬碗中的湯和深鍋中的湯會以不同速度冷卻。"},{"en":"Water can cool at different rates because of container size, air temperature, and circulation.","zh":"水可能因容器大小、空氣溫度和循環而以不同速度冷卻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes variation in cooling speed.","zh":"這個短語描述冷卻速度差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"freeze at a lower temperature","meaning":"在較低溫度下結冰","examples":[{"en":"Salt water freezes at a lower temperature than pure water.","zh":"鹽水比純水在較低溫度下結冰。"},{"en":"To freeze at a lower temperature means to become solid only when it is colder than the usual freezing point.","zh":"在較低溫度下結冰，是指要比通常冰點更冷才變成固體。"},{"en":"Sea water freezes at a lower temperature because it contains salt.","zh":"海水因含有鹽而在較低溫度下結冰。"},{"en":"If water freezes at a lower temperature, it may need extra cooling before becoming solid.","zh":"如果水在較低溫度下結冰，它可能需要額外冷卻才變成固體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lowered freezing point.","zh":"這個短語描述冰點降低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"warmer water can freeze faster","meaning":"較暖的水可以比較冷的水更快結冰","examples":[{"en":"The Mpemba Effect suggests that warmer water can freeze faster than colder water.","zh":"姆潘巴效應指出，較暖的水可以比較冷的水更快結冰。"},{"en":"Warmer water can freeze faster means hotter water may sometimes become ice sooner than cooler water.","zh":"較暖的水可以更快結冰，是指較熱的水有時可能比比較冷的水更早變成冰。"},{"en":"In a carefully controlled experiment, warmer water can freeze faster under certain starting conditions.","zh":"在仔細控制的實驗中，較暖的水可以在某些起始條件下更快結冰。"},{"en":"This does not always happen because freezing depends on many variables.","zh":"這並不總是發生，因為結冰取決於許多變數。"},{"en":"This phrase summarises the central puzzle of the passage.","zh":"這個短語概括篇章的核心謎團。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 127 - THE MPEMBA EFFECT.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 128":[{"front":"human remains","meaning":"人類遺骸","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes the discovery of human remains in the Green Sahara.","zh":"文章描述在綠色撒哈拉發現人類遺骸。"},{"en":"Human remains are the bones, bodies, or body parts of people who died long ago.","zh":"human remains 指很久以前去世的人留下的骨頭、身體或身體部分。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may study human remains to learn about diet, disease, and burial customs.","zh":"考古學家可能研究人類遺骸，以了解飲食、疾病和埋葬習俗。"},{"en":"Human remains must be handled carefully because they are scientific evidence and also once belonged to real people.","zh":"人類遺骸必須小心處理，因為它們既是科學證據，也曾屬於真實的人。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in archaeology, crime investigation, and history when referring to dead bodies or bones.","zh":"這個短語用於考古、刑事調查和歷史研究，指死者身體或骨骼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the Green Sahara","meaning":"綠色撒哈拉","examples":[{"en":"The Green Sahara was once wetter and more habitable than it is today.","zh":"綠色撒哈拉曾經比今日更濕潤，也更適合居住。"},{"en":"The Green Sahara refers to a past period when parts of the Sahara had lakes, plants, and enough water for people and animals.","zh":"Green Sahara 指撒哈拉部分地區曾有湖泊、植物和足夠水源供人與動物生活的時期。"},{"en":"A geography lesson may use the Green Sahara to show that deserts can change over time.","zh":"地理課可能用綠色撒哈拉來展示沙漠可以隨時間改變。"},{"en":"Wetter climate allowed people to fish, hunt, and live in areas that are now dry desert.","zh":"較濕潤的氣候讓人能在今日乾旱沙漠地區捕魚、狩獵和生活。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the ancient Sahara with the harsh desert we know today.","zh":"這個短語把古代撒哈拉與我們今日認識的嚴酷沙漠作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a small team of paleontologists","meaning":"一小隊古生物學家","examples":[{"en":"A small team of paleontologists was led by Paul Sereno.","zh":"一小隊古生物學家由 Paul Sereno 帶領。"},{"en":"A small team of paleontologists is a small group of scientists who study ancient life through fossils.","zh":"small team of paleontologists 指一小群透過化石研究古代生命的科學家。"},{"en":"A museum may send a small team of paleontologists to search for dinosaur bones in a remote area.","zh":"博物館可能派一小隊古生物學家到偏遠地區尋找恐龍骨頭。"},{"en":"Small teams can work carefully, but they may face limits in equipment, time, and manpower.","zh":"小隊可以仔細工作，但可能在設備、時間和人手上有限制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a research group studying fossils, not modern animals.","zh":"這個短語描述研究化石的研究隊伍，而不是研究現代動物的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"led by","meaning":"由……帶領","examples":[{"en":"The expedition was led by Paul Sereno of the University of Chicago.","zh":"這次考察由芝加哥大學的 Paul Sereno 帶領。"},{"en":"Led by someone means guided, organised, or directed by that person.","zh":"led by someone 指由某人引導、組織或指揮。"},{"en":"A school trip led by an experienced teacher is usually safer and better organised.","zh":"由有經驗老師帶領的學校旅行通常更安全、更有組織。"},{"en":"Strong leadership can help a team make decisions quickly in difficult conditions.","zh":"有力領導可以幫助團隊在困難情況下快速作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the person in charge of a group or activity.","zh":"這個短語指出負責某團隊或活動的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"clamber out of","meaning":"艱難地爬出……","examples":[{"en":"The paleontologists clambered out of three battered Land Rovers.","zh":"古生物學家艱難地從三輛破舊 Land Rover 越野車爬出來。"},{"en":"To clamber out of something means to climb out awkwardly or with effort.","zh":"clamber out of something 指笨拙或費力地爬出某物。"},{"en":"After a long bus ride, students may clamber out of the vehicle with heavy bags.","zh":"長途巴士旅程後，學生可能背着沉重書包艱難爬出車外。"},{"en":"People clamber out when the space is cramped, the ground is rough, or they are tired.","zh":"當空間狹窄、地面崎嶇或人很疲倦時，就可能會艱難爬出。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests movement that is difficult, not smooth or graceful.","zh":"這個短語暗示動作困難，而不是流暢或優雅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"battered Land Rovers","meaning":"破舊的 Land Rover 越野車","examples":[{"en":"The team travelled through the desert in battered Land Rovers.","zh":"團隊乘坐破舊的 Land Rover 越野車穿越沙漠。"},{"en":"Battered Land Rovers are old, damaged, or heavily used off-road vehicles.","zh":"battered Land Rovers 指老舊、受損或被長期使用的越野車。"},{"en":"A rescue team may use battered vehicles because they can still handle rough roads.","zh":"救援隊可能使用破舊車輛，因為它們仍能應付崎嶇道路。"},{"en":"Desert travel can leave vehicles scratched, dusty, and mechanically worn.","zh":"沙漠行車可以令車輛刮花、滿是塵土並出現機械磨損。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests tough but worn-out vehicles used in difficult terrain.","zh":"這個短語暗示在艱難地形中使用的堅固但殘舊車輛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fill one’s water bottles","meaning":"裝滿水樽","examples":[{"en":"The researchers filled their water bottles before walking across the desert.","zh":"研究者在步行穿越沙漠前裝滿水樽。"},{"en":"To fill one’s water bottles means to put drinking water into bottles before a journey or activity.","zh":"fill one’s water bottles 指在旅程或活動前把飲用水裝進水樽。"},{"en":"Hikers should fill their water bottles before starting a long trail.","zh":"行山者在開始長路線前應裝滿水樽。"},{"en":"Filling bottles is important because dehydration can become dangerous quickly in hot places.","zh":"裝滿水樽很重要，因為在炎熱地方脫水可以很快變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical preparation for travel, sport, or outdoor work.","zh":"這個短語描述為旅行、運動或戶外工作作實際準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"scatter on foot across","meaning":"徒步分散走過……","examples":[{"en":"The team scattered on foot across the sands of the Tenere desert.","zh":"團隊徒步分散走過泰內雷沙漠的沙地。"},{"en":"To scatter on foot across an area means to spread out and walk in different directions over it.","zh":"scatter on foot across an area 指人們分散開來，向不同方向步行穿過某地。"},{"en":"Students may scatter on foot across a sports field to collect rubbish after an event.","zh":"活動後，學生可能徒步分散到運動場各處拾垃圾。"},{"en":"A team scatters when covering a large area is more useful than staying together.","zh":"當覆蓋大範圍比聚在一起更有用，團隊就會分散行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people walking separately across open ground.","zh":"這個短語描述人們分開步行穿過開闊地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"toffee-coloured sands","meaning":"太妃糖色的沙地","examples":[{"en":"The team crossed the toffee-coloured sands of the Tenere desert.","zh":"團隊穿過泰內雷沙漠太妃糖色的沙地。"},{"en":"Toffee-coloured sands are sands with a warm brown colour like toffee candy.","zh":"toffee-coloured sands 指像太妃糖一樣呈暖啡色的沙地。"},{"en":"A photographer may describe a beach at sunset as having toffee-coloured sands.","zh":"攝影師可能把日落時的沙灘描述為太妃糖色沙地。"},{"en":"Colour descriptions help readers picture a landscape more clearly.","zh":"顏色描寫幫助讀者更清楚想像景觀。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a visual image of the desert rather than scientific information.","zh":"這個短語提供沙漠的視覺畫面，而不是科學資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the Tenere desert","meaning":"泰內雷沙漠","examples":[{"en":"The Tenere desert lies in northern Niger.","zh":"泰內雷沙漠位於尼日爾北部。"},{"en":"The Tenere desert is a very dry and remote desert region within the Sahara.","zh":"Tenere desert 指撒哈拉中一個非常乾旱而偏遠的沙漠地區。"},{"en":"A geography teacher may use the Tenere desert as an example of an extremely harsh landscape.","zh":"地理老師可能用泰內雷沙漠作為極端嚴酷地貌的例子。"},{"en":"Its heat, wind, and isolation make travel and research difficult.","zh":"其高溫、強風和孤立環境令旅行和研究變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific desert area, not the whole Sahara.","zh":"這個短語指特定沙漠地區，而不是整個撒哈拉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"northern Niger","meaning":"尼日爾北部","examples":[{"en":"The Tenere desert is located in northern Niger.","zh":"泰內雷沙漠位於尼日爾北部。"},{"en":"Northern Niger means the northern part of the West African country of Niger.","zh":"northern Niger 指西非國家尼日爾的北部。"},{"en":"A map can help students locate northern Niger near the Sahara.","zh":"地圖可以幫助學生找出靠近撒哈拉的尼日爾北部。"},{"en":"Knowing the location helps explain why the area is dry, remote, and difficult to cross.","zh":"知道位置有助解釋為何該區乾旱、偏遠且難以穿越。"},{"en":"This phrase gives geographical position.","zh":"這個短語提供地理位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the southern flank of","meaning":"……的南側","examples":[{"en":"The Tenere lies on the southern flank of the Sahara.","zh":"泰內雷位於撒哈拉的南側。"},{"en":"The southern flank of a place means its southern side or edge.","zh":"southern flank of a place 指某地的南面或南側邊緣。"},{"en":"A village on the southern flank of a mountain may receive more sunlight than the northern side.","zh":"位於山脈南側的村莊可能比北側得到更多陽光。"},{"en":"Saying “flank” makes the place sound like part of a larger geographical body.","zh":"使用 flank 令該地聽起來像較大地理體的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position along the side of a large area or landform.","zh":"這個短語描述位於大型地區或地貌側面的方位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rank among","meaning":"位列……之中","examples":[{"en":"The Tenere ranks among the most desolate landscapes on Earth.","zh":"泰內雷位列地球上最荒涼的地貌之一。"},{"en":"To rank among something means to be included in a particular group because it has that quality strongly.","zh":"rank among something 指因強烈具有某特質而被列入某群體。"},{"en":"A school may rank among the best in the city if its students perform very well.","zh":"如果學生表現非常好，一間學校可能位列全城最佳學校之中。"},{"en":"Places rank among extremes when they clearly show unusual heat, cold, danger, or beauty.","zh":"當地方清楚展現異常高溫、寒冷、危險或美麗，就可能位列極端類別之中。"},{"en":"This phrase places something within a notable category.","zh":"這個短語把某物放入一個值得注意的類別中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the most desolate landscapes","meaning":"最荒涼的地貌","examples":[{"en":"The Tenere is one of the most desolate landscapes on Earth.","zh":"泰內雷是地球上最荒涼的地貌之一。"},{"en":"The most desolate landscapes are extremely empty, harsh, and lonely places.","zh":"most desolate landscapes 指極度空曠、嚴酷和孤寂的地方。"},{"en":"A rocky desert with no trees, houses, or water may feel like a desolate landscape.","zh":"沒有樹木、房屋或水源的岩石沙漠，可能感覺像荒涼地貌。"},{"en":"Desolate landscapes are difficult to live in because food, shelter, and water are scarce.","zh":"荒涼地貌難以居住，因為食物、庇護和水源都稀少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place that feels bare and unforgiving.","zh":"這個短語描述一個裸露而不留情的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on Earth","meaning":"在地球上","examples":[{"en":"The desert is among the harshest landscapes on Earth.","zh":"這片沙漠是地球上最嚴酷的地貌之一。"},{"en":"On Earth means in the world or on this planet.","zh":"on Earth 指在世界上或在這個星球上。"},{"en":"Some of the coldest places on Earth are found near the poles.","zh":"地球上一些最寒冷的地方位於兩極附近。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to compare something with all other places in the world.","zh":"作者使用這個短語，把某物與世界上所有其他地方比較。"},{"en":"It can make a description sound broad and dramatic.","zh":"它可以令描述聽起來更廣闊、更具戲劇性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the Tuareg","meaning":"圖阿雷格人","examples":[{"en":"The Tuareg are turbaned nomads who have long lived in the region.","zh":"圖阿雷格人是長期生活在該地區、戴頭巾的遊牧民族。"},{"en":"The Tuareg are a people traditionally associated with desert life in parts of the Sahara.","zh":"Tuareg 指傳統上與撒哈拉部分地區沙漠生活有關的一個民族。"},{"en":"A history lesson may mention the Tuareg when discussing trade routes across North Africa.","zh":"歷史課討論北非貿易路線時，可能提到圖阿雷格人。"},{"en":"Their knowledge of desert travel can make them valuable guides in harsh regions.","zh":"他們對沙漠旅行的知識可以令他們成為嚴酷地區中的重要嚮導。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a cultural group, not simply any desert traveller.","zh":"這個短語指一個文化群體，而不只是任何沙漠旅人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"turbaned nomads","meaning":"戴頭巾的遊牧民族","examples":[{"en":"The Tuareg are described as turbaned nomads.","zh":"圖阿雷格人被描述為戴頭巾的遊牧民族。"},{"en":"Turbaned nomads are people who wear turbans and traditionally move from place to place.","zh":"turbaned nomads 指戴頭巾並傳統上逐地遷移的人。"},{"en":"Nomads may move with animals or trade goods when water and pasture change.","zh":"當水源和牧草變化時，遊牧民族可能帶着動物或貨物遷移。"},{"en":"Turbans can protect people from sun, wind, and sand in desert regions.","zh":"在沙漠地區，頭巾可以保護人免受陽光、風和沙影響。"},{"en":"This phrase combines clothing and lifestyle.","zh":"這個短語結合衣着和生活方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"for centuries","meaning":"數百年來","examples":[{"en":"The Tuareg have ruled this barren realm for centuries.","zh":"圖阿雷格人數百年來統治這片貧瘠之地。"},{"en":"For centuries means for hundreds of years.","zh":"for centuries 指長達數百年。"},{"en":"A temple may have stood in the same village for centuries.","zh":"一座寺廟可能數百年來一直矗立在同一條村。"},{"en":"When a tradition lasts for centuries, it becomes deeply connected to local identity.","zh":"當一項傳統延續數百年，它就會與本地身份深深相連。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a very long period of time.","zh":"這個短語顯示非常長的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"barren realm","meaning":"貧瘠之地","examples":[{"en":"The Tuareg once ruled this barren realm.","zh":"圖阿雷格人曾統治這片貧瘠之地。"},{"en":"A barren realm is a large area that is empty, dry, and difficult for life.","zh":"barren realm 指一大片空曠、乾燥且不利生命的地方。"},{"en":"A rocky island with almost no plants may look like a barren realm.","zh":"幾乎沒有植物的岩石島可能看起來像貧瘠之地。"},{"en":"Barren places are hard to farm because there is little water or fertile soil.","zh":"貧瘠地方難以耕種，因為水和肥沃泥土很少。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds literary and describes a harsh land.","zh":"這個短語帶文學感，用來描述嚴酷土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"refer to something as","meaning":"將某物稱為……","examples":[{"en":"The Tuareg refer to the Tenere as a desert within a desert.","zh":"圖阿雷格人將泰內雷稱為沙漠中的沙漠。"},{"en":"To refer to something as a name means to call or describe it by that name.","zh":"refer to something as a name 指以某名稱稱呼或描述某物。"},{"en":"Students may refer to a difficult exam as a nightmare.","zh":"學生可能將困難考試稱為噩夢。"},{"en":"The name people use often shows how they understand or feel about a place.","zh":"人們使用的名稱常顯示他們如何理解或感受一個地方。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a label or description used by others.","zh":"這個短語引出他人使用的標籤或描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a desert within a desert","meaning":"沙漠中的沙漠","examples":[{"en":"The Tenere is sometimes called a desert within a desert.","zh":"泰內雷有時被稱為沙漠中的沙漠。"},{"en":"A desert within a desert means an especially dry and empty part inside a larger desert.","zh":"desert within a desert 指位於更大沙漠之中，尤其乾旱空曠的一部分。"},{"en":"A quiet room in a noisy school may feel like a calm place within a busy place.","zh":"在嘈吵學校中的安靜房間，可能像繁忙地方中的平靜空間。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the Tenere is extreme even by Sahara standards.","zh":"這個短語強調即使以撒哈拉標準看，泰內雷也非常極端。"},{"en":"It suggests deep isolation inside an already harsh environment.","zh":"它暗示在本已嚴酷環境中的深層孤立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"California-size","meaning":"加州大小的","examples":[{"en":"The Tenere is a California-size ocean of sand and rock.","zh":"泰內雷是一片加州大小的沙石之海。"},{"en":"California-size means roughly as large as the US state of California.","zh":"California-size 指大約如美國加州一樣大。"},{"en":"A country-sized forest would be easier to imagine if described as California-size.","zh":"如果把一片國家大小的森林描述為加州大小，讀者會較容易想像。"},{"en":"Comparing an area to a familiar place helps readers understand scale.","zh":"把面積與熟悉地方比較，有助讀者理解規模。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to make a large size feel more concrete.","zh":"這個短語用來令龐大面積更具體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ocean of sand and rock","meaning":"沙石之海","examples":[{"en":"The Tenere is described as an ocean of sand and rock.","zh":"泰內雷被描述為沙石之海。"},{"en":"An ocean of sand and rock is a huge continuous area covered by sand and stones.","zh":"ocean of sand and rock 指一大片連綿不斷、覆蓋着沙和石的地區。"},{"en":"From a hilltop, a desert may look like an ocean of sand with no clear end.","zh":"從山頂望去，沙漠可能像沒有盡頭的沙海。"},{"en":"This image helps readers feel the scale and emptiness of the landscape.","zh":"這個意象幫助讀者感受景觀的規模和空曠。"},{"en":"It is a metaphor, not a real ocean with water.","zh":"這是比喻，不是真正有水的海洋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"massive dune","meaning":"巨型沙丘","examples":[{"en":"A single massive dune might stretch a hundred miles.","zh":"單一巨型沙丘可能延伸一百英里。"},{"en":"A massive dune is an extremely large hill or ridge of sand.","zh":"massive dune 指極大的沙丘或沙脊。"},{"en":"Children may see small dunes at a beach, but desert dunes can be far larger.","zh":"孩子可能在沙灘看到小沙丘，但沙漠沙丘可以大得多。"},{"en":"Wind builds dunes by moving and piling up sand over time.","zh":"風透過長時間移動和堆積沙粒形成沙丘。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a huge sand formation.","zh":"這個短語描述巨大的沙質地貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stretch a hundred miles","meaning":"延伸一百英里","examples":[{"en":"A massive dune in the Tenere might stretch a hundred miles.","zh":"泰內雷的一座巨型沙丘可能延伸一百英里。"},{"en":"To stretch a hundred miles means to extend across a distance of about one hundred miles.","zh":"stretch a hundred miles 指橫跨約一百英里的距離。"},{"en":"A traffic jam after a storm would be shocking if it stretched for several miles.","zh":"暴風雨後，如果交通擠塞延伸數英里，會令人震驚。"},{"en":"Long distances make travel, rescue, and research more difficult.","zh":"距離長會令旅行、救援和研究更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses physical length.","zh":"這個短語強調實際長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the combination of","meaning":"……的結合","examples":[{"en":"The combination of heat and wind makes the desert extremely dangerous.","zh":"高溫和強風的結合令沙漠極度危險。"},{"en":"The combination of two things means the effect created when they happen together.","zh":"combination of two things 指兩件事同時出現時產生的效果。"},{"en":"The combination of tiredness and hunger can make a child lose patience quickly.","zh":"疲倦和飢餓的結合可以令孩子很快失去耐性。"},{"en":"Two problems together can be worse than either one alone.","zh":"兩個問題加在一起可能比任何一個單獨出現更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why several factors produce one result.","zh":"解釋多個因素如何產生一個結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"120-degree heat","meaning":"120華氏度高溫","examples":[{"en":"The region can experience 120-degree heat.","zh":"該地區可能經歷120華氏度高溫。"},{"en":"120-degree heat means extremely hot weather around 120 degrees Fahrenheit.","zh":"120-degree heat 指約華氏120度的極端高溫。"},{"en":"In such heat, outdoor workers need water, shade, and frequent breaks.","zh":"在這種高溫下，戶外工人需要水、遮蔭和頻繁休息。"},{"en":"Extreme heat can cause dehydration and heat illness very quickly.","zh":"極端高溫可以很快造成脫水和中暑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dangerous temperature, not just warm weather.","zh":"這個短語描述危險溫度，而不只是天氣暖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"inexorable winds","meaning":"無法阻擋的強風","examples":[{"en":"Inexorable winds can dry out a human body quickly.","zh":"無法阻擋的強風可以快速令人體變乾。"},{"en":"Inexorable winds are strong winds that seem impossible to stop or escape.","zh":"inexorable winds 指似乎無法停止或逃避的強風。"},{"en":"Campers may struggle to set up tents when inexorable winds keep blowing across a campsite.","zh":"當強風不斷吹過營地，露營者可能難以搭帳篷。"},{"en":"Such winds can increase dehydration because they remove moisture from skin and clothing.","zh":"這類風會帶走皮膚和衣物中的水分，增加脫水風險。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests relentless natural force.","zh":"這個短語暗示無情的自然力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"wick the water from","meaning":"抽乾……的水分","examples":[{"en":"The heat and winds can wick the water from a human body.","zh":"高溫和強風可以抽乾人體的水分。"},{"en":"To wick the water from something means to draw moisture out of it.","zh":"wick the water from something 指把水分從某物中吸走或抽走。"},{"en":"A dry towel can wick water from wet hair after swimming.","zh":"游泳後，乾毛巾可以吸走濕髮中的水分。"},{"en":"In a desert, hot wind can remove sweat so quickly that the body loses water dangerously fast.","zh":"在沙漠中，熱風可以很快帶走汗水，使身體危險地快速失水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moisture being pulled away.","zh":"這個短語描述水分被抽離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in less than a day","meaning":"不足一天內","examples":[{"en":"The desert can dehydrate a person in less than a day.","zh":"這片沙漠可以在不足一天內令人脫水。"},{"en":"In less than a day means in under twenty-four hours.","zh":"in less than a day 指少於二十四小時內。"},{"en":"A phone battery may die in less than a day if many apps run at the same time.","zh":"如果許多應用程式同時運行，手機電池可能不足一天就耗盡。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that something happens quickly.","zh":"這個短語強調某事發生得很快。"},{"en":"In dangerous environments, a short period can be enough to create serious harm.","zh":"在危險環境中，短時間已足以造成嚴重傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"harsh conditions","meaning":"惡劣環境","examples":[{"en":"Harsh conditions have kept the region largely unexplored.","zh":"惡劣環境使該地區大部分仍未被探索。"},{"en":"Harsh conditions are difficult, dangerous, or uncomfortable circumstances.","zh":"harsh conditions 指困難、危險或令人不適的情況。"},{"en":"Workers face harsh conditions when they work outside in extreme heat without shade.","zh":"工人在極端高溫、沒有遮蔭的戶外工作時，會面對惡劣環境。"},{"en":"Harsh conditions can slow research because people and equipment may not survive easily.","zh":"惡劣環境可以拖慢研究，因為人和設備都不容易承受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an environment that is hard to live or work in.","zh":"這個短語描述難以生活或工作的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"intermittent conflict","meaning":"間歇性衝突","examples":[{"en":"Intermittent conflict made research in the region difficult.","zh":"間歇性衝突令該地區的研究變得困難。"},{"en":"Intermittent conflict means fighting or unrest that happens from time to time, not continuously.","zh":"intermittent conflict 指不時發生而非持續不斷的戰鬥或動亂。"},{"en":"A school project may be delayed by intermittent conflict between group members.","zh":"小組成員之間間歇性衝突可能拖延學校專題。"},{"en":"Even occasional conflict can make travel unsafe and planning uncertain.","zh":"即使只是偶爾衝突，也可以令旅行不安全、計劃不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated but irregular trouble.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆但不規律的麻煩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"keep the region largely unexplored","meaning":"使該地區大部分仍未被探索","examples":[{"en":"The harsh conditions kept the region largely unexplored.","zh":"惡劣環境使該地區大部分仍未被探索。"},{"en":"To keep a region largely unexplored means to make it remain mostly unstudied or unvisited.","zh":"keep a region largely unexplored 指令某地大部分仍未被研究或到訪。"},{"en":"Dangerous roads can keep a mountain village largely unexplored by tourists.","zh":"危險道路可以使一條山村大部分仍未被遊客探索。"},{"en":"If a place is hard to reach, fewer scientists can collect evidence there.","zh":"如果一個地方難以到達，較少科學家能在那裡收集證據。"},{"en":"This phrase links difficulty with lack of exploration.","zh":"這個短語把困難與缺乏探索連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"accompany the team","meaning":"隨隊同行","examples":[{"en":"Mike Hettwer was a photographer accompanying the team.","zh":"Mike Hettwer 是一名隨隊同行的攝影師。"},{"en":"To accompany the team means to go with the team during a trip or activity.","zh":"accompany the team 指在旅程或活動中與團隊同行。"},{"en":"A nurse may accompany a school team on a hiking trip for safety.","zh":"護士可能在學校隊伍行山時隨隊同行，以保障安全。"},{"en":"Someone accompanying a team may not be the leader but still plays an important role.","zh":"隨隊同行的人未必是領隊，但仍可能扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes travelling or working alongside a group.","zh":"這個短語描述與團隊一起旅行或工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"head off by oneself","meaning":"獨自出發","examples":[{"en":"Hettwer headed off by himself toward a trio of small dunes.","zh":"Hettwer 獨自出發，走向三個小沙丘。"},{"en":"To head off by oneself means to leave alone and go in a particular direction.","zh":"head off by oneself 指獨自離開並朝某方向前進。"},{"en":"A student may head off by herself to the library after lunch.","zh":"學生可能午飯後獨自前往圖書館。"},{"en":"Going alone can lead to discovery, but it can also be risky in unfamiliar places.","zh":"獨自行動可能帶來發現，但在陌生地方也可能有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes independent movement away from a group.","zh":"這個短語描述離開團隊後的獨自行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a trio of","meaning":"三個一組的……","examples":[{"en":"He walked toward a trio of small dunes.","zh":"他走向三個一組的小沙丘。"},{"en":"A trio of something means a group of three.","zh":"a trio of something 指三個組成的一組。"},{"en":"A trio of students may work together on a science project.","zh":"三名學生可能組成一組做科學專題。"},{"en":"The word trio is often used when the three things are seen as a small set.","zh":"trio 常用於把三件事物視為一小組時。"},{"en":"This phrase is a more polished way to say “three.”","zh":"這個短語是 “three” 的較文雅說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"small dunes","meaning":"小沙丘","examples":[{"en":"Hettwer walked towards several small dunes.","zh":"Hettwer 走向幾個小沙丘。"},{"en":"Small dunes are low hills or mounds of sand made by wind.","zh":"small dunes 指由風形成的低矮沙丘或沙堆。"},{"en":"Children may climb small dunes at a beach during a family trip.","zh":"孩子可能在家庭旅行中爬上海灘小沙丘。"},{"en":"Even small dunes can hide objects or bones until someone walks over them.","zh":"即使是小沙丘，也可能藏住物件或骨頭，直到有人走過才發現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes modest sand formations.","zh":"這個短語描述規模不大的沙地形。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"crest the first slope","meaning":"登上第一個斜坡頂","examples":[{"en":"He crested the first slope and saw bones.","zh":"他登上第一個斜坡頂，然後看見骨頭。"},{"en":"To crest a slope means to reach the top of a hill or rise.","zh":"crest a slope 指到達山坡或斜坡的頂端。"},{"en":"A runner may crest the final slope and suddenly see the finish line.","zh":"跑手可能登上最後斜坡頂後，突然看見終點線。"},{"en":"Reaching the top changes what a person can see on the other side.","zh":"到達頂部會改變一個人能看見的另一邊景象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arriving at the highest point of an incline.","zh":"這個短語描述到達斜坡最高點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"stare in amazement","meaning":"驚訝地凝視","examples":[{"en":"Hettwer stared in amazement at the bones.","zh":"Hettwer 驚訝地凝視着那些骨頭。"},{"en":"To stare in amazement means to look fixedly because something is surprising or hard to believe.","zh":"stare in amazement 指因某事令人驚訝或難以置信而定定地看。"},{"en":"A child may stare in amazement when a magician makes a coin disappear.","zh":"當魔術師令硬幣消失時，孩子可能驚訝地凝視。"},{"en":"People stare when their surprise is so strong that they pause before reacting.","zh":"當驚訝太強烈，人們會先停住凝視，然後才反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shocked or fascinated look.","zh":"這個短語描述震驚或着迷的凝望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"spill over with","meaning":"滿是……","examples":[{"en":"The dunes were spilling over with bones.","zh":"沙丘滿是骨頭。"},{"en":"To spill over with something means to be full of it, almost as if it is overflowing.","zh":"spill over with something 指充滿某物，幾乎像要溢出來。"},{"en":"A classroom may spill over with books after a donation drive.","zh":"捐書活動後，課室可能滿是書本。"},{"en":"This phrase creates the image of more objects than the space can comfortably hold.","zh":"這個短語製造出物件多得空間幾乎容納不下的畫面。"},{"en":"It is used to describe abundance in a vivid way.","zh":"它用生動方式描述大量存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take a few shots","meaning":"拍幾張照片","examples":[{"en":"He took a few shots with his digital camera.","zh":"他用數碼相機拍了幾張照片。"},{"en":"To take a few shots means to take several photographs.","zh":"take a few shots 指拍幾張照片。"},{"en":"A tourist may take a few shots of a street market before leaving.","zh":"遊客離開前可能拍幾張街市照片。"},{"en":"Taking photos helps record evidence before objects are moved or disturbed.","zh":"拍照有助在物件被移動或干擾前記錄證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and often used for photography.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常用於攝影。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"digital camera","meaning":"數碼相機","examples":[{"en":"Hettwer photographed the bones with his digital camera.","zh":"Hettwer 用數碼相機拍下那些骨頭。"},{"en":"A digital camera is a camera that stores photographs electronically rather than on film.","zh":"digital camera 指以電子方式而不是菲林儲存照片的相機。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a digital camera to record a class project display.","zh":"老師可能用數碼相機記錄班級專題展示。"},{"en":"Digital photos can be checked, copied, and shared quickly.","zh":"數碼照片可以快速查看、複製和分享。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to camera technology, not the act of photography itself.","zh":"這個短語指相機技術，而不是攝影動作本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hurry back to","meaning":"匆忙返回……","examples":[{"en":"He hurried back to the Land Rovers.","zh":"他匆忙返回 Land Rover 越野車。"},{"en":"To hurry back to a place means to return there quickly.","zh":"hurry back to a place 指快速返回某地。"},{"en":"A student may hurry back to class after realising the bell has rung.","zh":"學生聽到鐘聲響起後，可能匆忙返回課室。"},{"en":"People hurry back when they have urgent news or need help.","zh":"當人有緊急消息或需要幫助時，就會匆忙返回。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests quick return, often because something important has happened.","zh":"這個短語暗示快速返回，通常因為發生了重要事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"when the team had regrouped","meaning":"當隊伍重新集合時","examples":[{"en":"Hettwer reported the discovery when the team had regrouped.","zh":"當隊伍重新集合時，Hettwer 報告了這個發現。"},{"en":"When the team had regrouped means after the team came back together again.","zh":"when the team had regrouped 指團隊再次聚集起來之後。"},{"en":"After searching different parts of a park, students shared findings when the group had regrouped.","zh":"學生搜尋公園不同地方後，重新集合時分享發現。"},{"en":"Regrouping allows scattered members to exchange information and plan the next step.","zh":"重新集合讓分散的成員交換資訊並計劃下一步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a moment after separate work has ended.","zh":"這個短語描述分開工作結束後的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not dinosaurs but human","meaning":"不是恐龍而是人類","examples":[{"en":"The bones were not dinosaurs but human.","zh":"那些骨頭不是恐龍，而是人類。"},{"en":"Not A but B means the correct answer is B, not A.","zh":"not A but B 指正確答案是 B，而不是 A。"},{"en":"The problem was not laziness but lack of clear instructions.","zh":"問題不是懶惰，而是缺乏清楚指示。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects an assumption by replacing it with a more accurate explanation.","zh":"這個短語透過更準確解釋取代原本假設。"},{"en":"It is useful when the real identity of something is surprising.","zh":"當某物的真正身份令人驚訝時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"contact someone","meaning":"聯絡某人","examples":[{"en":"Sereno contacted Elena Garcea in the spring of 2005.","zh":"Sereno 在2005年春天聯絡 Elena Garcea。"},{"en":"To contact someone means to communicate with that person by phone, email, message, or another method.","zh":"contact someone 指透過電話、電郵、訊息或其他方式與某人溝通。"},{"en":"A parent may contact a teacher if a child keeps losing homework.","zh":"如果孩子經常遺失功課，家長可能聯絡老師。"},{"en":"People contact experts when they need advice, confirmation, or cooperation.","zh":"當人們需要建議、確認或合作時，會聯絡專家。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching out to another person.","zh":"這個短語描述主動找另一個人聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"archaeologist","meaning":"考古學家","examples":[{"en":"Elena Garcea is an archaeologist at the University of Cassino.","zh":"Elena Garcea 是卡西諾大學的考古學家。"},{"en":"An archaeologist is a person who studies past human life through objects, buildings, bones, and sites.","zh":"archaeologist 指透過物件、建築、骨骼和遺址研究過去人類生活的人。"},{"en":"An archaeologist may examine pottery to learn how ancient people cooked and stored food.","zh":"考古學家可能檢查陶器，以了解古人如何烹煮和儲存食物。"},{"en":"Archaeologists protect evidence by digging carefully and recording where things are found.","zh":"考古學家透過仔細發掘並記錄物件出土地點來保護證據。"},{"en":"This word refers to someone who studies human history, not dinosaur fossils mainly.","zh":"這個字主要指研究人類歷史的人，而不是主要研究恐龍化石的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"invite someone to accompany","meaning":"邀請某人陪同","examples":[{"en":"Sereno invited Garcea to accompany him on a return to the site.","zh":"Sereno 邀請 Garcea 陪同他返回該遺址。"},{"en":"To invite someone to accompany you means to ask that person to go with you.","zh":"invite someone to accompany you 指邀請某人與你同行。"},{"en":"A teacher may invite a nurse to accompany students on a hiking trip.","zh":"老師可能邀請護士陪同學生行山。"},{"en":"People invite experts to accompany them when special knowledge is needed.","zh":"當需要專門知識，人們會邀請專家同行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes asking someone to join a journey or activity.","zh":"這個短語描述邀請某人加入旅程或活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"return to the site","meaning":"返回該遺址","examples":[{"en":"Garcea agreed to return to the site with Sereno.","zh":"Garcea 同意與 Sereno 返回該遺址。"},{"en":"To return to the site means to go back to the exact place being studied or investigated.","zh":"return to the site 指回到正在研究或調查的確切地方。"},{"en":"Police may return to the site of an accident to collect more evidence.","zh":"警方可能返回意外現場收集更多證據。"},{"en":"Researchers return to a site when the first visit raises new questions.","zh":"當第一次考察提出新問題，研究者會返回遺址。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in archaeology, science, and investigation.","zh":"這個短語常見於考古、科學和調查語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"spend three decades doing","meaning":"花三十年做……","examples":[{"en":"Garcea had spent three decades working digs in North Africa.","zh":"Garcea 花了三十年在北非參與考古發掘。"},{"en":"To spend three decades doing something means to spend about thirty years doing it.","zh":"spend three decades doing something 指花約三十年做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may spend three decades helping students learn to write clearly.","zh":"老師可能花三十年幫助學生學會清楚寫作。"},{"en":"Long experience can make a person better at judging unusual claims.","zh":"長時間經驗可以令一個人更善於判斷不尋常說法。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses deep experience over a very long period.","zh":"這個短語強調非常長時間累積的深厚經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"working digs","meaning":"參與考古發掘","examples":[{"en":"She had spent decades working digs along the Nile.","zh":"她花了數十年在尼羅河沿岸參與考古發掘。"},{"en":"Working digs means taking part in archaeological excavations.","zh":"working digs 指參與考古發掘工作。"},{"en":"Students on a summer archaeology programme may work digs under expert supervision.","zh":"參加暑期考古課程的學生可能在專家監督下參與發掘。"},{"en":"Dig work involves careful digging, recording, cleaning, and protecting finds.","zh":"發掘工作包括仔細挖掘、記錄、清潔和保護出土物。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and refers to practical field excavation.","zh":"這個短語較口語，指實際野外發掘。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"along the Nile","meaning":"沿着尼羅河","examples":[{"en":"Garcea had worked digs along the Nile in Sudan.","zh":"Garcea 曾在蘇丹沿着尼羅河參與考古發掘。"},{"en":"Along the Nile means beside or following the course of the Nile River.","zh":"along the Nile 指在尼羅河旁或沿着其河道。"},{"en":"Ancient towns often developed along rivers because water supported farming and travel.","zh":"古代城鎮常沿河發展，因為水源支持農業和交通。"},{"en":"Archaeological sites along the Nile can reveal how people lived near water in dry regions.","zh":"尼羅河沿岸的考古遺址可以揭示人們如何在乾旱地區靠近水源生活。"},{"en":"This phrase gives location by reference to the river.","zh":"這個短語透過河流指出位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the Libyan Desert","meaning":"利比亞沙漠","examples":[{"en":"She had also worked in the mountains of the Libyan Desert.","zh":"她也曾在利比亞沙漠的山區工作。"},{"en":"The Libyan Desert is a dry desert region in North Africa.","zh":"Libyan Desert 指北非的一個乾旱沙漠地區。"},{"en":"A geography lesson may compare the Libyan Desert with other parts of the Sahara.","zh":"地理課可能把利比亞沙漠與撒哈拉其他部分作比較。"},{"en":"Desert mountains can preserve rock art, tools, and traces of ancient people.","zh":"沙漠山區可以保存岩畫、工具和古人痕跡。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific desert region.","zh":"這個短語指特定沙漠地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be well acquainted with","meaning":"對……非常熟悉","examples":[{"en":"Garcea was well acquainted with the ancient peoples of the Sahara.","zh":"Garcea 對撒哈拉古代民族非常熟悉。"},{"en":"To be well acquainted with something means to know it well through study or experience.","zh":"be well acquainted with something 指透過研究或經驗對某事非常了解。"},{"en":"A teacher is well acquainted with common grammar mistakes after marking many essays.","zh":"老師批改很多作文後，會非常熟悉常見文法錯誤。"},{"en":"Strong familiarity helps experts judge whether a discovery is unusual or believable.","zh":"深厚熟悉度幫助專家判斷一項發現是否不尋常或可信。"},{"en":"This phrase means more than simply having heard of something.","zh":"這個短語不只是曾經聽過某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ancient peoples","meaning":"古代民族","examples":[{"en":"She knew a great deal about the ancient peoples of the Sahara.","zh":"她非常了解撒哈拉的古代民族。"},{"en":"Ancient peoples are groups of humans who lived long ago.","zh":"ancient peoples 指很久以前生活的人類群體。"},{"en":"Museums use tools and pottery to teach visitors about ancient peoples.","zh":"博物館使用工具和陶器向訪客介紹古代民族。"},{"en":"Studying ancient peoples helps us understand how humans adapted to climate and landscape.","zh":"研究古代民族有助我們理解人類如何適應氣候和地貌。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to past human communities, not modern ethnic groups only.","zh":"這個短語指過去的人類社群，而不只是現代族群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have never heard of","meaning":"從未聽過……","examples":[{"en":"Garcea had never heard of Paul Sereno before.","zh":"Garcea 之前從未聽過 Paul Sereno。"},{"en":"To have never heard of someone means to know nothing about that person’s name or reputation.","zh":"have never heard of someone 指對某人的名字或聲譽完全不知道。"},{"en":"A student may have never heard of a writer before reading their story in class.","zh":"學生在課堂讀某作家的故事前，可能從未聽過該作家。"},{"en":"Not knowing someone can make their surprising claim harder to judge at first.","zh":"不認識某人會令其驚人說法一開始較難判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete unfamiliarity with a person or thing.","zh":"這個短語描述對某人或某事完全陌生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"claim to have found","meaning":"聲稱已發現……","examples":[{"en":"Sereno claimed to have found many skeletons in one place.","zh":"Sereno 聲稱在同一地方發現許多骸骨。"},{"en":"To claim to have found something means to say that one has discovered it.","zh":"claim to have found something 指聲稱自己已發現某物。"},{"en":"A student may claim to have found the answer, but the teacher may ask for proof.","zh":"學生可能聲稱已找到答案，但老師可能要求證據。"},{"en":"Claims need evidence when they sound surprising or unlikely.","zh":"當說法令人驚訝或不太可能時，就需要證據。"},{"en":"This phrase reports what someone says, without automatically proving it true.","zh":"這個短語報告某人說法，但不自動證明它是真的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"skeletons","meaning":"骨骼；骸骨","examples":[{"en":"The site contained many human skeletons.","zh":"該遺址包含許多人類骸骨。"},{"en":"Skeletons are the bone frameworks of bodies.","zh":"skeletons 指身體的骨架。"},{"en":"A biology classroom may have a model skeleton to teach students about bones.","zh":"生物課室可能有骨骼模型，讓學生學習骨頭。"},{"en":"Archaeological skeletons can reveal age, health, injuries, and sometimes lifestyle.","zh":"考古骸骨可以揭示年齡、健康、傷痕，有時也揭示生活方式。"},{"en":"This word can refer to human or animal bones that remain after soft tissues decay.","zh":"這個字可指人類或動物軟組織腐爛後留下的骨頭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in one place","meaning":"在同一地方","examples":[{"en":"His claim to have found many skeletons in one place seemed unusual.","zh":"他聲稱在同一地方發現許多骸骨，聽起來很不尋常。"},{"en":"In one place means in the same location, not spread across many locations.","zh":"in one place 指在同一位置，而不是分散在多個地方。"},{"en":"A teacher may collect all worksheets in one place so students can find them easily.","zh":"老師可能把所有工作紙放在同一地方，讓學生容易找到。"},{"en":"Finding many objects in one place can suggest a special site, such as a cemetery.","zh":"在同一地方發現許多物件，可能暗示那是特殊遺址，例如墓地。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses concentration in a single location.","zh":"這個短語強調集中於單一位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"seem far-fetched","meaning":"聽起來牽強","examples":[{"en":"The claim seemed far-fetched to some archaeologists.","zh":"這個說法對一些考古學家來說聽起來牽強。"},{"en":"To seem far-fetched means to sound unlikely, exaggerated, or hard to believe.","zh":"seem far-fetched 指聽起來不太可能、誇張或難以相信。"},{"en":"A student’s excuse may seem far-fetched if every bus and train supposedly failed on the same morning.","zh":"如果學生聲稱同一早上所有巴士和火車都故障，這個藉口可能聽起來牽強。"},{"en":"Far-fetched claims usually need strong evidence before people accept them.","zh":"牽強說法通常需要強證據，人們才會接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doubt about whether something is believable.","zh":"這個短語描述對某事是否可信的懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"given that","meaning":"鑑於","examples":[{"en":"The claim seemed unlikely, given that no similar cemetery had been found.","zh":"鑑於沒有發現類似墓地，這個說法似乎不太可能。"},{"en":"Given that means considering the fact that.","zh":"given that 指考慮到某個事實。"},{"en":"Given that the exam is tomorrow, students should not start a new topic tonight.","zh":"鑑於明天就是考試，學生今晚不應開始新題目。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a reason that affects judgement.","zh":"這個短語引出影響判斷的理由。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining why something seems likely or unlikely.","zh":"解釋某事為何似乎可能或不可能時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Neolithic cemetery","meaning":"新石器時代墓地","examples":[{"en":"No other Neolithic cemetery contained more than a dozen or so skeletons.","zh":"沒有其他新石器時代墓地包含超過大約十多具骸骨。"},{"en":"A Neolithic cemetery is a burial place from the New Stone Age.","zh":"Neolithic cemetery 指新石器時代的埋葬地。"},{"en":"Archaeologists study a Neolithic cemetery to learn how early farming or village communities buried their dead.","zh":"考古學家研究新石器時代墓地，以了解早期農耕或村落社群如何埋葬死者。"},{"en":"Grave goods, body positions, and bones can reveal beliefs and daily life.","zh":"隨葬品、身體姿勢和骨骼可以揭示信仰和日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an ancient burial site, not a modern graveyard.","zh":"這個短語指古代墓葬遺址，而不是現代墳場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a dozen or so","meaning":"大約十多個","examples":[{"en":"No comparable cemetery contained more than a dozen or so skeletons.","zh":"沒有可比較的墓地包含超過大約十多具骸骨。"},{"en":"A dozen or so means about twelve, perhaps a little more or less.","zh":"a dozen or so 指大約十二個，可能多一點或少一點。"},{"en":"A teacher may bring a dozen or so extra worksheets in case students lose theirs.","zh":"老師可能帶大約十多份額外工作紙，以防學生遺失。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate number, not an exact count.","zh":"這個短語提供近似數字，而不是準確數目。"},{"en":"It is useful when the precise number is not important.","zh":"當精確數目不重要時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be skeptical","meaning":"持懷疑態度","examples":[{"en":"Some archaeologists would later be skeptical of Sereno’s claim.","zh":"一些考古學家後來會對 Sereno 的說法持懷疑態度。"},{"en":"To be skeptical means to doubt something and want stronger evidence before accepting it.","zh":"be skeptical 指懷疑某事，並希望有更強證據才接受。"},{"en":"A teacher may be skeptical if a student says the dog ate every page of homework.","zh":"如果學生說狗吃掉了每一頁功課，老師可能持懷疑態度。"},{"en":"Skepticism can protect researchers from accepting exciting claims too quickly.","zh":"懷疑精神可以防止研究者太快接受令人興奮的說法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful doubt, not automatic rejection.","zh":"這個短語描述謹慎懷疑，而不是自動否定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"snipe that","meaning":"尖刻地批評說","examples":[{"en":"One critic sniped that Sereno was only a moonlighting paleontologist.","zh":"一位批評者尖刻地批評說 Sereno 只是兼職考古的古生物學家。"},{"en":"To snipe that means to make a sharp, critical, and often slightly unfair comment.","zh":"snipe that 指作出尖銳、批判性，而且常有點不公平的評論。"},{"en":"A classmate may snipe that a group leader only wants credit, not teamwork.","zh":"同學可能尖刻地說組長只想要功勞，而不是團隊合作。"},{"en":"Sniping can damage discussion because it attacks the person more than the evidence.","zh":"尖刻批評會損害討論，因為它攻擊人多於攻擊證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a cutting remark.","zh":"這個短語描述刻薄的評論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"moonlighting paleontologist","meaning":"兼職考古的古生物學家","examples":[{"en":"One archaeologist dismissed Sereno as a moonlighting paleontologist.","zh":"一位考古學家把 Sereno 貶稱為兼職考古的古生物學家。"},{"en":"A moonlighting paleontologist is a paleontologist doing work in another field as a side activity.","zh":"moonlighting paleontologist 指在另一領域兼做工作的古生物學家。"},{"en":"A full-time accountant who teaches music at night could be called a moonlighting music teacher.","zh":"全職會計晚上教音樂，可以被稱為兼職音樂老師。"},{"en":"Calling someone moonlighting can suggest they are not a true specialist in the second field.","zh":"稱某人 moonlighting 可以暗示他在第二領域不是真正專家。"},{"en":"This phrase was used critically to question Sereno’s authority in archaeology.","zh":"這個短語在文中帶批評意味，用來質疑 Sereno 在考古學上的權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"too intrigued to","meaning":"太感興趣而不能……","examples":[{"en":"Garcea was too intrigued to dismiss Sereno’s claim.","zh":"Garcea 太感興趣，不能就這樣否定 Sereno 的說法。"},{"en":"Too intrigued to do something means so interested that one cannot simply ignore it.","zh":"too intrigued to do something 指太感興趣，以致不能簡單忽略某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may be too intrigued by a student’s unusual answer to mark it wrong immediately.","zh":"老師可能對學生不尋常答案太感興趣，而不會立即判錯。"},{"en":"Curiosity can make people investigate a claim even when it seems unlikely.","zh":"好奇心可以令人調查一個看似不太可能的說法。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that interest prevents rejection.","zh":"這個短語顯示興趣阻止人拒絕某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"dismiss someone as","meaning":"將某人視為……而不理會","examples":[{"en":"Garcea did not dismiss Sereno as an interloper.","zh":"Garcea 沒有將 Sereno 視為外來插手者而不理會。"},{"en":"To dismiss someone as something means to reject that person by labelling them negatively.","zh":"dismiss someone as something 指用負面標籤否定某人。"},{"en":"A teacher should not dismiss a quiet student as lazy without understanding the reason.","zh":"老師不應未了解原因就把安靜學生視為懶惰而不理會。"},{"en":"Dismissing people too quickly can make us miss useful ideas.","zh":"太快否定別人可能令我們錯過有用想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rejection based on a judgement about identity or status.","zh":"這個短語描述基於身份或地位判斷而拒絕某人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"interloper","meaning":"外來插手者","examples":[{"en":"Some experts may have seen Sereno as an interloper in archaeology.","zh":"有些專家可能把 Sereno 視為考古學中的外來插手者。"},{"en":"An interloper is someone who enters a field, place, or situation where others feel they do not belong.","zh":"interloper 指進入某領域、地方或情況，而他人覺得其不屬於那裡的人。"},{"en":"A new manager may be treated as an interloper if staff think she does not understand their work.","zh":"如果員工認為新經理不了解他們的工作，她可能被視為外來插手者。"},{"en":"Experts may resent interlopers when they feel their professional territory is being invaded.","zh":"當專家覺得自己的專業領域被侵犯時，可能反感外來插手者。"},{"en":"This word usually carries a negative tone.","zh":"這個字通常帶負面語氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"agree to join","meaning":"同意加入","examples":[{"en":"Garcea agreed to join Sereno’s expedition.","zh":"Garcea 同意加入 Sereno 的考察隊。"},{"en":"To agree to join something means to say yes to taking part in it.","zh":"agree to join something 指答應參與某事。"},{"en":"A student may agree to join a debate team after a teacher encourages her.","zh":"老師鼓勵後，學生可能同意加入辯論隊。"},{"en":"People agree to join when they see value, interest, or responsibility in the activity.","zh":"當人們看見活動有價值、有趣或有責任感，就會同意加入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accepting an invitation to participate.","zh":"這個短語描述接受邀請參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fishing-based culture","meaning":"以捕魚為主的文化","examples":[{"en":"The Kiffian were a fishing-based culture.","zh":"基菲安人是一種以捕魚為主的文化。"},{"en":"A fishing-based culture is a society whose food, tools, and daily life depend heavily on fishing.","zh":"fishing-based culture 指食物、工具和日常生活都高度依賴捕魚的社會。"},{"en":"A lakeside village may become fishing-based if most families catch, dry, and trade fish.","zh":"如果大多數家庭捕魚、曬魚和賣魚，湖邊村落可能成為以捕魚為主的文化。"},{"en":"Water, boats, hooks, and fish bones can all show that fishing shaped a community.","zh":"水源、船、魚鈎和魚骨都可以顯示捕魚塑造了一個社群。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a way of life centred on fish and water.","zh":"這個短語描述以魚和水為中心的生活方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the earliest wet period","meaning":"最早的濕潤時期","examples":[{"en":"The Kiffian lived during the earliest wet period.","zh":"基菲安人生活在最早的濕潤時期。"},{"en":"The earliest wet period means the first known time when the region became wetter.","zh":"earliest wet period 指該地區最早已知變得較濕潤的時期。"},{"en":"A geography chart may show an early wet period before the land dried again.","zh":"地理圖表可能顯示土地再次乾旱前的早期濕潤時期。"},{"en":"Wet periods allow lakes, plants, animals, and human communities to expand.","zh":"濕潤時期讓湖泊、植物、動物和人類社群擴展。"},{"en":"This phrase places a people or event within a climate phase.","zh":"這個短語把民族或事件放入氣候階段中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"between…and…years ago","meaning":"在……至……年前之間","examples":[{"en":"The Kiffian lived between 8,000 and 10,000 years ago.","zh":"基菲安人生活在八千至一萬年前之間。"},{"en":"Between X and Y years ago means during a time range before the present.","zh":"between X and Y years ago 指距今某兩個時間點之間的時段。"},{"en":"A museum label may say a tool was made between 2,000 and 3,000 years ago.","zh":"博物館標籤可能寫着一件工具製於二千至三千年前之間。"},{"en":"Time ranges are used when exact dates are uncertain.","zh":"當確切日期不確定時，會使用時間範圍。"},{"en":"This phrase helps place ancient evidence on a timeline.","zh":"這個短語幫助把古代證據放到時間線上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sherd","meaning":"陶片","examples":[{"en":"Garcea held a Kiffian sherd next to a Tenerian one.","zh":"Garcea 把一塊基菲安陶片放在一塊特內里安陶片旁邊。"},{"en":"A sherd is a broken piece of pottery found by archaeologists.","zh":"sherd 指考古學家發現的破碎陶器片。"},{"en":"A small pottery sherd can show the colour, decoration, or material used by ancient people.","zh":"一小塊陶片可以顯示古人使用的顏色、裝飾或材料。"},{"en":"Sherds matter because even broken pieces can reveal trade, cooking, and daily life.","zh":"陶片重要，因為即使是破碎片段，也能揭示貿易、烹飪和日常生活。"},{"en":"This word is common in archaeology and is more specific than “piece.”","zh":"這個字常見於考古學，比 “piece” 更具體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"next to","meaning":"在……旁邊","examples":[{"en":"She held a Kiffian sherd next to a Tenerian sherd.","zh":"她把一塊基菲安陶片放在一塊特內里安陶片旁邊。"},{"en":"Next to means beside or very close to something.","zh":"next to 指在某物旁邊或非常接近某物。"},{"en":"A student may sit next to a friend during lunch.","zh":"學生午飯時可能坐在朋友旁邊。"},{"en":"Putting two objects next to each other makes comparison easier.","zh":"把兩件物件放在旁邊，可以令比較更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical position.","zh":"這個短語描述實際位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"more than a thousand years apart","meaning":"相隔一千多年","examples":[{"en":"The two groups lived more than a thousand years apart.","zh":"這兩個群體相隔一千多年。"},{"en":"More than a thousand years apart means separated by over one thousand years in time.","zh":"more than a thousand years apart 指在時間上相隔超過一千年。"},{"en":"Two buildings may look similar but have been built more than a hundred years apart.","zh":"兩座建築可能看起來相似，但建成時間相隔一百多年。"},{"en":"Large time gaps can explain why cultures, tools, and lifestyles differ.","zh":"長時間差距可以解釋文化、工具和生活方式為何不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distance in time, not physical distance.","zh":"這個短語描述時間距離，而不是實際距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"over the next three weeks","meaning":"在接下來三星期","examples":[{"en":"Over the next three weeks, the team made a detailed map of the site.","zh":"在接下來三星期，團隊製作了該遺址的詳細地圖。"},{"en":"Over the next three weeks means during the following three-week period.","zh":"over the next three weeks 指在接下來三星期的期間。"},{"en":"Over the next three weeks, students may prepare presentations and practise speaking.","zh":"在接下來三星期，學生可能準備簡報並練習演說。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that work happened gradually across a set period.","zh":"這個短語顯示工作是在一段固定時間內逐步發生。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing a planned sequence of activity.","zh":"描述有計劃的一系列活動時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"excavators","meaning":"發掘人員","examples":[{"en":"Five American excavators joined the expedition.","zh":"五名美國發掘人員加入考察隊。"},{"en":"Excavators are people who dig carefully at archaeological sites to uncover evidence.","zh":"excavators 指在考古遺址小心挖掘以揭露證據的人。"},{"en":"Excavators may use small tools and brushes rather than large machines near fragile bones.","zh":"發掘人員在脆弱骨骼附近可能使用小工具和刷子，而不是大型機器。"},{"en":"Careful excavators prevent important objects from being damaged or moved without record.","zh":"細心的發掘人員可以防止重要物件受損或在沒有記錄下被移動。"},{"en":"In archaeology, this word usually refers to dig workers, not construction machines.","zh":"在考古中，這個字通常指發掘工人，而不是建築機械。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Tuareg guides","meaning":"圖阿雷格嚮導","examples":[{"en":"Tuareg guides helped the researchers work in the desert.","zh":"圖阿雷格嚮導幫助研究者在沙漠中工作。"},{"en":"Tuareg guides are local guides from the Tuareg people who know desert routes and conditions.","zh":"Tuareg guides 指來自圖阿雷格人、熟悉沙漠路線和環境的本地嚮導。"},{"en":"Travellers may rely on Tuareg guides to find safe paths and water sources.","zh":"旅人可能依靠圖阿雷格嚮導尋找安全路徑和水源。"},{"en":"Local guides can reduce danger because they understand weather, terrain, and risks.","zh":"本地嚮導能減少危險，因為他們了解天氣、地形和風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people who guide others through a difficult region.","zh":"這個短語描述引導他人穿越困難地區的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"soldiers from Niger’s army","meaning":"尼日爾軍隊士兵","examples":[{"en":"Soldiers from Niger’s army were sent to protect the camp.","zh":"尼日爾軍隊士兵被派去保護營地。"},{"en":"Soldiers from Niger’s army are military personnel belonging to Niger’s national army.","zh":"soldiers from Niger’s army 指屬於尼日爾國家軍隊的軍事人員。"},{"en":"Soldiers may protect researchers when fieldwork takes place in an unsafe region.","zh":"當野外工作在不安全地區進行，士兵可能保護研究者。"},{"en":"Military protection can be needed when bandits or conflict threaten a camp.","zh":"當土匪或衝突威脅營地，可能需要軍事保護。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who provided security.","zh":"這個短語指出誰提供保安。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be sent to protect","meaning":"被派去保護","examples":[{"en":"Soldiers were sent to protect the camp from bandits.","zh":"士兵被派去保護營地免受土匪侵害。"},{"en":"To be sent to protect a place means to be ordered to go there to keep it safe.","zh":"be sent to protect a place 指被命令前往某地以保障其安全。"},{"en":"Extra staff may be sent to protect students during a crowded school event.","zh":"在擁擠的學校活動中，額外職員可能被派去保護學生。"},{"en":"Protection is needed when there is a real risk of danger or attack.","zh":"當有真正危險或攻擊風險時，就需要保護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sending people for security.","zh":"這個短語描述派人提供安全保障。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"protect the camp from","meaning":"保護營地免受……侵害","examples":[{"en":"The soldiers protected the camp from bandits.","zh":"士兵保護營地免受土匪侵害。"},{"en":"To protect the camp from something means to keep the camp safe from that danger.","zh":"protect the camp from something 指保護營地不受某種危險影響。"},{"en":"Teachers protect students from heat by arranging shade and water during outdoor sports.","zh":"老師在戶外運動時安排遮蔭和水，保護學生免受高溫傷害。"},{"en":"Protection works by reducing the chance of harm before it happens.","zh":"保護的作用是在傷害發生前減少其可能性。"},{"en":"This phrase links a place with the threat it faces.","zh":"這個短語把一個地方與它面對的威脅連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bandits","meaning":"土匪；強盜","examples":[{"en":"The camp needed protection from bandits.","zh":"營地需要保護，以防土匪侵害。"},{"en":"Bandits are robbers or armed criminals, often in remote areas.","zh":"bandits 指強盜或持械罪犯，常出現在偏遠地區。"},{"en":"Travellers may avoid a road if bandits have attacked vehicles there before.","zh":"如果土匪曾在某道路襲擊車輛，旅人可能避開那條路。"},{"en":"The risk of bandits can make scientific fieldwork more dangerous.","zh":"土匪風險可以令科學野外工作更危險。"},{"en":"This word refers to criminal attackers, not ordinary poor people.","zh":"這個字指犯罪襲擊者，而不是普通貧困人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make a detailed map of","meaning":"製作……的詳細地圖","examples":[{"en":"The researchers made a detailed map of the site.","zh":"研究者製作了該遺址的詳細地圖。"},{"en":"To make a detailed map of a place means to record its layout carefully and accurately.","zh":"make a detailed map of a place 指仔細而準確地記錄某地布局。"},{"en":"Students may make a detailed map of a school garden before redesigning it.","zh":"學生在重新設計學校花園前，可能先製作詳細地圖。"},{"en":"In archaeology, maps help show where bones, tools, and burials were found.","zh":"在考古學中，地圖幫助顯示骨骼、工具和墓葬的發現位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful visual recording of a place.","zh":"這個短語描述對某地作仔細視覺記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dub something","meaning":"將某物命名為……","examples":[{"en":"The team dubbed the site Gobero.","zh":"團隊將該遺址命名為 Gobero。"},{"en":"To dub something a name means to give it that name.","zh":"dub something a name 指給某物取某個名稱。"},{"en":"Students may dub a quiet corner of the library “the study cave.”","zh":"學生可能把圖書館安靜角落命名為「自修洞穴」。"},{"en":"Naming a place makes it easier for people to refer to and study it.","zh":"為地方命名使人們更容易提及和研究它。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when a new or informal name is created.","zh":"當創造新名稱或非正式名稱時，常使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"after the Tuareg name","meaning":"按照圖阿雷格語名稱","examples":[{"en":"They dubbed the site Gobero after the Tuareg name for the area.","zh":"他們按照該地區的圖阿雷格語名稱，把遺址命名為 Gobero。"},{"en":"After the Tuareg name means using the Tuareg name as the basis for naming it.","zh":"after the Tuareg name 指以圖阿雷格語名稱作為命名基礎。"},{"en":"A school garden may be named after an old village name to honour local history.","zh":"學校花園可能按舊村名命名，以尊重本地歷史。"},{"en":"Naming a site after a local name can respect the people connected to the land.","zh":"按本地名稱命名遺址可以尊重與土地有關的人。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the source of a name.","zh":"這個短語解釋名稱的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"exhume burials","meaning":"發掘墓葬","examples":[{"en":"The team exhumed eight burials at Gobero.","zh":"團隊在 Gobero 發掘了八個墓葬。"},{"en":"To exhume burials means to dig up buried bodies or graves for study.","zh":"exhume burials 指為研究而挖出埋葬的屍體或墳墓。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may exhume burials carefully to study ancient health and customs.","zh":"考古學家可能小心發掘墓葬，以研究古代健康和習俗。"},{"en":"Exhuming burials requires respect because the remains belonged to real people.","zh":"發掘墓葬需要尊重，因為遺骸曾屬於真實的人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a formal and careful archaeological act.","zh":"這個短語描述正式而小心的考古行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"collect scores of artifacts","meaning":"收集大量文物","examples":[{"en":"The researchers collected scores of artifacts from both cultures.","zh":"研究者從兩種文化中收集了大量文物。"},{"en":"To collect scores of artifacts means to gather many human-made objects from a site.","zh":"collect scores of artifacts 指從遺址收集許多人造物件。"},{"en":"A museum team may collect scores of artifacts after a careful excavation.","zh":"博物館團隊可能在仔細發掘後收集大量文物。"},{"en":"Many artifacts help researchers compare tools, habits, and cultural differences.","zh":"大量文物幫助研究者比較工具、習慣和文化差異。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that a large number of objects were found.","zh":"這個短語強調發現了很多物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"artifacts","meaning":"文物","examples":[{"en":"The team collected artifacts from the Kiffian and Tenerian cultures.","zh":"團隊收集了基菲安和特內里安文化的文物。"},{"en":"Artifacts are objects made or used by humans, especially in the past.","zh":"artifacts 指由人製造或使用的物件，尤其是過去的物件。"},{"en":"Pottery, tools, beads, and weapons can all be artifacts.","zh":"陶器、工具、珠飾和武器都可以是文物。"},{"en":"Artifacts help archaeologists understand how people worked, ate, traded, and lived.","zh":"文物幫助考古學家理解人們如何工作、飲食、交易和生活。"},{"en":"This word refers to human-made evidence, not natural rocks.","zh":"這個字指人造證據，而不是天然岩石。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"both cultures","meaning":"兩種文化","examples":[{"en":"The site contained artifacts from both cultures.","zh":"該遺址包含來自兩種文化的文物。"},{"en":"Both cultures means the two cultural groups being discussed.","zh":"both cultures 指正在討論的兩個文化群體。"},{"en":"A museum display may compare pottery from both cultures side by side.","zh":"博物館展示可能把兩種文化的陶器並排比較。"},{"en":"Evidence from both cultures helps researchers see similarities and differences.","zh":"來自兩種文化的證據幫助研究者看見相似與差異。"},{"en":"This phrase includes two groups together, not just one.","zh":"這個短語同時包括兩個群體，而不只是其中一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dry lake bed","meaning":"乾涸湖床","examples":[{"en":"The team found tools in a dry lake bed near the dunes.","zh":"團隊在沙丘附近的乾涸湖床中發現工具。"},{"en":"A dry lake bed is the flat area left behind after a lake loses its water.","zh":"dry lake bed 指湖水消失後留下的平坦地面。"},{"en":"Children may see cracked mud in a dry pond bed after a long summer.","zh":"漫長夏天後，孩子可能在乾涸池塘底看到裂開泥土。"},{"en":"Dry lake beds can preserve shells, tools, bones, and signs of past water.","zh":"乾涸湖床可以保存貝殼、工具、骨頭和過去有水的跡象。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the area once had water but is now dry.","zh":"這個短語顯示該地曾有水，但現在乾了。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"adjacent to","meaning":"鄰近……","examples":[{"en":"The dry lake bed was adjacent to the dunes.","zh":"乾涸湖床鄰近沙丘。"},{"en":"Adjacent to means next to or very close to something.","zh":"adjacent to 指在某物旁邊或非常接近某物。"},{"en":"A playground adjacent to a school is easy for students to reach.","zh":"鄰近學校的遊樂場方便學生到達。"},{"en":"Location matters because nearby features may be connected historically or practically.","zh":"位置很重要，因為鄰近特徵可能在歷史或實際上有關。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than “beside.”","zh":"這個短語比 “beside” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fishhooks and harpoons","meaning":"魚鈎和魚叉","examples":[{"en":"The team found fishhooks and harpoons carved from animal bone.","zh":"團隊發現由動物骨頭雕成的魚鈎和魚叉。"},{"en":"Fishhooks and harpoons are tools used to catch fish or large water animals.","zh":"fishhooks and harpoons 指用來捕魚或大型水生動物的工具。"},{"en":"A fishing museum may display old fishhooks and harpoons beside modern nets.","zh":"漁業博物館可能把古代魚鈎和魚叉與現代漁網一起展示。"},{"en":"These tools suggest that people depended on water and aquatic food.","zh":"這些工具暗示人們依賴水源和水產食物。"},{"en":"This phrase points to fishing or hunting in lakes and rivers.","zh":"這個短語指向湖泊和河流中的捕魚或狩獵活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"carved from animal bone","meaning":"由動物骨頭雕成","examples":[{"en":"The harpoons were carved from animal bone.","zh":"魚叉由動物骨頭雕成。"},{"en":"Carved from animal bone means shaped by cutting or scraping bone into a tool or object.","zh":"carved from animal bone 指透過切割或刮削骨頭，把它塑造成工具或物件。"},{"en":"Ancient people may carve needles, hooks, or ornaments from animal bone.","zh":"古人可能由動物骨頭雕成針、魚鈎或飾物。"},{"en":"Bone was useful because it was hard, workable, and available after hunting or fishing.","zh":"骨頭有用，因為它堅硬、可加工，而且在狩獵或捕魚後可取得。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the material and method used to make an object.","zh":"這個短語描述物件使用的材料和製作方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"apparently","meaning":"顯然","examples":[{"en":"Apparently, the Kiffian fishermen caught more than small fish.","zh":"顯然，基菲安漁民捕到的不只是小魚。"},{"en":"Apparently means it seems true based on the evidence available.","zh":"apparently 指根據現有證據看來似乎是真的。"},{"en":"Apparently, the meeting was cancelled because no one arrived on time.","zh":"顯然，會議取消是因為沒有人準時到達。"},{"en":"This word lets a writer make a careful conclusion without claiming complete certainty.","zh":"這個字讓作者作出謹慎結論，而不聲稱完全確定。"},{"en":"It is useful when evidence strongly suggests something.","zh":"當證據強烈暗示某事時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"go after small fry","meaning":"追捕小魚；只針對小目標","examples":[{"en":"The Kiffian fishermen were not just going after small fry.","zh":"基菲安漁民並不只是追捕小魚。"},{"en":"To go after small fry means to target small fish or, more generally, small and easy targets.","zh":"go after small fry 指追捕小魚，或更廣義地指只針對小而容易的目標。"},{"en":"A company chasing only small clients may be going after small fry rather than major contracts.","zh":"只追逐小客戶而不爭取大合約的公司，可能只是在追逐小目標。"},{"en":"In the passage, larger animal remains show the fishermen pursued bigger catches too.","zh":"在文章中，較大型動物遺骸顯示漁民也追捕更大的獵物。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal about fish or figurative about unimportant targets.","zh":"這個短語可以字面指魚，也可以比喻指不重要的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"scattered near","meaning":"散落在……附近","examples":[{"en":"Animal remains were scattered near the dunes.","zh":"動物遺骸散落在沙丘附近。"},{"en":"Scattered near a place means spread loosely around that area.","zh":"scattered near a place 指鬆散分布在某地周圍。"},{"en":"After lunch, wrappers may be scattered near a school bench if students do not clean up.","zh":"午飯後，如果學生不清理，包裝紙可能散落在學校長椅附近。"},{"en":"Scattered objects can show where people worked, ate, or lived.","zh":"散落物件可以顯示人們在哪裡工作、進食或生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distribution around a location.","zh":"這個短語描述物件在某位置周圍的分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"remains of","meaning":"……的遺骸","examples":[{"en":"The team found the remains of Nile perch near the dunes.","zh":"團隊在沙丘附近發現尼羅河鱸魚的遺骸。"},{"en":"Remains of something are the parts left after the original thing has died, broken, or decayed.","zh":"remains of something 指某物死亡、破碎或腐爛後留下的部分。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may find the remains of meals in ancient fireplaces.","zh":"考古學家可能在古代火塘中發現餐食遺留物。"},{"en":"Remains can provide evidence even when the whole object or animal is gone.","zh":"即使完整物件或動物已不存在，遺骸仍能提供證據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to what is left behind.","zh":"這個短語指留下來的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Nile perch","meaning":"尼羅河鱸魚","examples":[{"en":"The remains of Nile perch were found near the dunes.","zh":"尼羅河鱸魚的遺骸在沙丘附近被發現。"},{"en":"Nile perch is a large freshwater fish associated with African waters.","zh":"Nile perch 指一種與非洲水域有關的大型淡水魚。"},{"en":"Finding Nile perch bones in a desert suggests that water once existed nearby.","zh":"在沙漠中發現尼羅河鱸魚骨，暗示附近曾經有水。"},{"en":"Large fish remains can show that ancient people had access to rich aquatic resources.","zh":"大型魚類遺骸可以顯示古人曾接觸豐富水產資源。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific kind of fish.","zh":"這個短語指一種特定魚類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a beast of a fish","meaning":"巨型魚","examples":[{"en":"The Nile perch is described as a beast of a fish.","zh":"尼羅河鱸魚被描述為巨型魚。"},{"en":"A beast of a fish means an unusually large or powerful fish.","zh":"beast of a fish 指異常巨大或強壯的魚。"},{"en":"A fisherman might call a huge tuna a beast of a fish after struggling to pull it in.","zh":"漁民艱難拉上一條巨型吞拿魚後，可能稱它為巨型魚。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the animal sound impressive and difficult to catch.","zh":"這個短語令動物聽起來令人印象深刻且難以捕捉。"},{"en":"It is informal and vivid, not a technical scientific label.","zh":"它是生動口語說法，不是技術性科學名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"weigh nearly","meaning":"重近……","examples":[{"en":"A Nile perch can weigh nearly 300 pounds.","zh":"尼羅河鱸魚可重近三百磅。"},{"en":"To weigh nearly a number means to have a weight close to that number.","zh":"weigh nearly a number 指重量接近某個數字。"},{"en":"A heavy suitcase may weigh nearly 30 kilograms after a long trip.","zh":"長途旅行後，沉重行李箱可能重近三十公斤。"},{"en":"Using “nearly” shows the amount is close but not exactly equal.","zh":"使用 nearly 顯示數量接近但並非完全相等。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate weight.","zh":"這個短語給出近似重量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"以及","examples":[{"en":"The team found Nile perch, as well as crocodile and hippo bones.","zh":"團隊發現尼羅河鱸魚，以及鱷魚和河馬骨頭。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to.","zh":"as well as 指以及、除了……之外還有。"},{"en":"A student may study vocabulary as well as grammar before an English exam.","zh":"學生在英文考試前可能溫習詞彙以及文法。"},{"en":"This phrase adds extra information without starting a new sentence.","zh":"這個短語加入額外資訊，而不用開始新句。"},{"en":"It is useful when listing more than one item.","zh":"列出多於一項事物時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"crocodile and hippo bones","meaning":"鱷魚和河馬骨頭","examples":[{"en":"Crocodile and hippo bones were found near the dunes.","zh":"鱷魚和河馬骨頭在沙丘附近被發現。"},{"en":"Crocodile and hippo bones are remains of large animals that need water-rich environments.","zh":"crocodile and hippo bones 指需要水源豐富環境的大型動物遺骸。"},{"en":"Finding such bones in a desert can suggest that lakes or wetlands once existed there.","zh":"在沙漠中發現這類骨頭，可以暗示當地曾有湖泊或濕地。"},{"en":"Animal bones help scientists reconstruct past landscapes and climates.","zh":"動物骨頭幫助科學家重建過去景觀和氣候。"},{"en":"This phrase points to evidence of a wetter ancient environment.","zh":"這個短語指向古代較濕潤環境的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fly home with","meaning":"帶着……乘飛機回家","examples":[{"en":"Sereno flew home with the most important skeletons and artifacts.","zh":"Sereno 帶着最重要的骸骨和文物乘飛機回家。"},{"en":"To fly home with something means to take it back by plane.","zh":"fly home with something 指乘飛機把某物帶回去。"},{"en":"A researcher may fly home with soil samples after fieldwork abroad.","zh":"研究者可能在海外野外工作後帶着泥土樣本乘飛機回家。"},{"en":"Important finds are transported carefully so they can be studied in a laboratory.","zh":"重要發現會被小心運送，以便在實驗室研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bringing objects back during air travel.","zh":"這個短語描述乘飛機時把物件帶回。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"immediately begin planning","meaning":"立即開始計劃","examples":[{"en":"Sereno immediately began planning for the next field season.","zh":"Sereno 立即開始計劃下一個野外考察季。"},{"en":"To immediately begin planning means to start organising the next steps without delay.","zh":"immediately begin planning 指毫不拖延地開始組織下一步。"},{"en":"After a successful school fair, teachers may immediately begin planning next year’s event.","zh":"成功舉辦學校嘉年華後，老師可能立即開始計劃翌年活動。"},{"en":"Quick planning helps a team use fresh information while it is still clear.","zh":"快速計劃有助團隊在資訊仍清晰時加以運用。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests urgency and momentum.","zh":"這個短語暗示迫切感和推進力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"field season","meaning":"野外考察季","examples":[{"en":"The next field season would involve further excavation.","zh":"下一個野外考察季將涉及進一步發掘。"},{"en":"A field season is a period when researchers work outside at a site rather than in a classroom or lab.","zh":"field season 指研究者在野外遺址而不是課室或實驗室工作的時期。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may plan a field season during cooler months to avoid extreme heat.","zh":"考古學家可能把野外考察季安排在較涼月份，以避開極端高溫。"},{"en":"Field seasons are important because remote sites cannot be studied all year easily.","zh":"野外考察季很重要，因為偏遠遺址不容易全年研究。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to scheduled outdoor research time.","zh":"這個短語指預先安排的戶外研究時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in the meantime","meaning":"與此同時","examples":[{"en":"In the meantime, Sereno sent teeth to a laboratory for dating.","zh":"與此同時，Sereno 把牙齒送往實驗室作定年。"},{"en":"In the meantime means during the time between two events or while waiting for something else.","zh":"in the meantime 指在兩件事之間的時間，或等待另一事時。"},{"en":"The school hall is being repaired; in the meantime, assemblies will be held outside.","zh":"學校禮堂正在維修；與此同時，早會將在戶外舉行。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what happens while another plan is not yet ready.","zh":"這個短語顯示在另一計劃尚未準備好時發生甚麼。"},{"en":"It helps connect parallel actions in time.","zh":"它幫助連接同時期進行的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"remove one tooth from","meaning":"從……取下一隻牙齒","examples":[{"en":"He carefully removed one tooth from each of four skulls.","zh":"他小心地從四個頭骨各取下一隻牙齒。"},{"en":"To remove one tooth from something means to take a single tooth out of it.","zh":"remove one tooth from something 指從某物中取出一隻牙齒。"},{"en":"A dentist may remove one tooth from a patient if it is badly damaged.","zh":"如果牙齒嚴重受損，牙醫可能從病人口中拔掉一隻牙。"},{"en":"In archaeology, teeth can be removed for testing because they may preserve chemical or DNA evidence.","zh":"在考古學中，牙齒可被取出測試，因為它們可能保存化學或 DNA 證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking out a specific small part.","zh":"這個短語描述取出一個特定小部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"skulls","meaning":"頭骨","examples":[{"en":"Sereno removed teeth from four skulls for testing.","zh":"Sereno 從四個頭骨取下牙齒作測試。"},{"en":"Skulls are the bones of the head that protect the brain and form the face.","zh":"skulls 指保護大腦並形成面部的頭部骨骼。"},{"en":"A biology model of a skull can help students learn where teeth and eye sockets are located.","zh":"頭骨生物模型可以幫助學生學習牙齒和眼窩位置。"},{"en":"Archaeological skulls can provide evidence about age, health, ancestry, and injury.","zh":"考古頭骨可以提供關於年齡、健康、祖源和受傷的證據。"},{"en":"This word refers specifically to head bones.","zh":"這個字特指頭部骨骼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"send something to a lab","meaning":"將某物送往實驗室","examples":[{"en":"He sent the teeth to a lab for radiocarbon dating.","zh":"他將牙齒送往實驗室作放射性碳定年。"},{"en":"To send something to a lab means to deliver it to a laboratory for scientific testing.","zh":"send something to a lab 指把某物送到實驗室作科學測試。"},{"en":"A doctor may send a blood sample to a lab to check for infection.","zh":"醫生可能把血液樣本送往實驗室，以檢查感染。"},{"en":"Lab testing can reveal information that cannot be seen by eye.","zh":"實驗室測試可以揭示肉眼看不到的資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving a sample from fieldwork to scientific analysis.","zh":"這個短語描述把樣本從野外工作轉入科學分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"radiocarbon dating","meaning":"放射性碳定年法","examples":[{"en":"Radiocarbon dating helped determine the age of the burials.","zh":"放射性碳定年法幫助確定墓葬年代。"},{"en":"Radiocarbon dating is a scientific method used to estimate the age of once-living material.","zh":"radiocarbon dating 是用來估計曾經有生命材料年代的科學方法。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may use radiocarbon dating on bone, charcoal, or wood.","zh":"考古學家可能對骨頭、木炭或木材使用放射性碳定年法。"},{"en":"This method helps place ancient remains on a timeline.","zh":"這種方法幫助把古代遺骸放到時間線上。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a dating technique, not ordinary calendar dating.","zh":"這個短語指一種定年技術，而不是普通日曆日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"peg the age of","meaning":"確定……的年代為","examples":[{"en":"The results pegged the age of the burials at roughly 9,000 years old.","zh":"結果將這些墓葬的年代確定為大約九千年前。"},{"en":"To peg the age of something at a number means to estimate or fix its age at that number.","zh":"peg the age of something at a number 指估計或確定某物年代為某數字。"},{"en":"A museum expert may peg the age of a vase at about 500 years.","zh":"博物館專家可能把一個花瓶年代確定為約五百年。"},{"en":"Test results can make an age estimate more precise and believable.","zh":"測試結果可以令年代估計更精確、更可信。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when evidence gives a fairly firm estimate.","zh":"當證據給出相當穩固估計時，常使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tightly bundled burials","meaning":"緊緊捆成一團的墓葬","examples":[{"en":"The tightly bundled burials were about 9,000 years old.","zh":"這些緊緊捆成一團的墓葬約有九千年歷史。"},{"en":"Tightly bundled burials are graves where bodies were placed in a compact, closely folded or wrapped position.","zh":"tightly bundled burials 指屍體以緊密、折起或包裹姿勢放置的墓葬。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may notice tightly bundled burials when bones are crowded close together.","zh":"當骨骼非常緊密地聚在一起，考古學家可能注意到這是緊緊捆成一團的墓葬。"},{"en":"Burial position can reveal ritual practice or practical treatment of the dead.","zh":"埋葬姿勢可以揭示儀式做法或對死者的實際處理方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how the bodies were arranged.","zh":"這個短語描述屍體如何被安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"roughly","meaning":"大約","examples":[{"en":"The burials were roughly 9,000 years old.","zh":"這些墓葬大約有九千年歷史。"},{"en":"Roughly means approximately or about.","zh":"roughly 指大約或約莫。"},{"en":"A teacher may say a presentation should last roughly five minutes.","zh":"老師可能說簡報應大約五分鐘。"},{"en":"This word is used when an exact number is not necessary or not known.","zh":"當不需要或不知道精確數字時，可以使用這個字。"},{"en":"It makes a number sound like an estimate.","zh":"它令數字聽起來像估計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the heart of","meaning":"……的核心時期","examples":[{"en":"The burials dated to the heart of the Kiffian era.","zh":"這些墓葬年代屬於基菲安時代的核心時期。"},{"en":"The heart of a period means its central or main part.","zh":"heart of a period 指某時期的中心或主要部分。"},{"en":"The heart of the school year may be the months when major lessons and tests happen.","zh":"學年的核心時期可能是主要課堂和測驗發生的月份。"},{"en":"Evidence from the heart of a period can show what life was like at its most typical stage.","zh":"來自一個時期核心階段的證據，可以顯示生活最典型時的樣子。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean a physical heart; it means the core time.","zh":"這個短語不是指實體心臟，而是指核心時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Kiffian era","meaning":"基菲安時代","examples":[{"en":"The older burials belonged to the Kiffian era.","zh":"較古老的墓葬屬於基菲安時代。"},{"en":"The Kiffian era refers to the period associated with the Kiffian people or culture.","zh":"Kiffian era 指與基菲安人或基菲安文化相關的時期。"},{"en":"A museum timeline may separate the Kiffian era from the later Tenerian period.","zh":"博物館時間線可能把基菲安時代與較後的特內里安時期分開。"},{"en":"Naming eras helps researchers organise evidence by time and culture.","zh":"為時代命名有助研究者按時間和文化組織證據。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies an archaeological period.","zh":"這個短語指出一個考古時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sleeping skeletons","meaning":"睡姿骸骨","examples":[{"en":"The smaller sleeping skeletons belonged to the Tenerian period.","zh":"較小的睡姿骸骨屬於特內里安時期。"},{"en":"Sleeping skeletons are skeletons arranged in positions that look as if the people were sleeping.","zh":"sleeping skeletons 指姿勢看起來像死者正在睡覺的骸骨。"},{"en":"A burial with knees bent and arms close to the body may look like a sleeping skeleton.","zh":"膝蓋彎曲、手臂靠近身體的墓葬可能看似睡姿骸骨。"},{"en":"Such positions can reflect burial customs rather than the person’s position at death.","zh":"這類姿勢可以反映埋葬習俗，而不是死者死亡時的姿勢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the visual impression of the burial.","zh":"這個短語描述墓葬帶來的視覺印象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"turn out to be","meaning":"結果是","examples":[{"en":"The smaller skeletons turned out to be about 6,000 years old.","zh":"較小的骸骨結果是約六千年歷史。"},{"en":"To turn out to be means to be discovered later as a certain thing or result.","zh":"turn out to be 指後來被發現是某種情況或結果。"},{"en":"A lost notebook may turn out to be in a student’s locker after all.","zh":"遺失的筆記本最後可能結果是在學生儲物櫃中。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when later evidence reveals the true situation.","zh":"當後來證據揭示真實情況時，可以使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It often introduces a result that was not known at first.","zh":"它常引出一開始並不知道的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"well within","meaning":"明顯屬於……之內","examples":[{"en":"The smaller skeletons were well within the Tenerian period.","zh":"較小骸骨明顯屬於特內里安時期之內。"},{"en":"Well within means clearly inside a particular range or period.","zh":"well within 指清楚處於某範圍或時期之內。"},{"en":"A student who finishes an exam in forty minutes is well within a one-hour time limit.","zh":"學生四十分鐘完成一小時考試，就是明顯在時限之內。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is not near the edge of a range.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事不是接近範圍邊緣。"},{"en":"It gives confidence that the classification is secure.","zh":"它讓分類顯得更穩妥。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Tenerian period","meaning":"特內里安時期","examples":[{"en":"The younger skeletons belonged to the Tenerian period.","zh":"較年輕的骸骨屬於特內里安時期。"},{"en":"The Tenerian period refers to a later archaeological period associated with the Tenerian people or culture.","zh":"Tenerian period 指與特內里安人或文化相關的較後考古時期。"},{"en":"Researchers compare the Tenerian period with the earlier Kiffian era to study change over time.","zh":"研究者把特內里安時期與較早基菲安時代比較，以研究隨時間出現的變化。"},{"en":"A period name helps separate different lifestyles, tools, and burial practices.","zh":"時期名稱有助區分不同生活方式、工具和埋葬習俗。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific later phase at the site.","zh":"這個短語指出該遺址的一個特定後期階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"know who was who","meaning":"分辨誰是誰","examples":[{"en":"The scientists finally knew who was who.","zh":"科學家終於能分辨誰是誰。"},{"en":"To know who was who means to identify which people or remains belonged to which group.","zh":"know who was who 指辨認哪些人或遺骸屬於哪個群體。"},{"en":"A teacher sorting old class photos may finally know who was who after reading name labels.","zh":"老師整理舊班相時，讀到名牌後可能終於分辨誰是誰。"},{"en":"Correct identification helps researchers compare groups accurately.","zh":"正確識別有助研究者準確比較不同群體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes solving confusion about identity.","zh":"這個短語描述解決身份上的混亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"return to","meaning":"返回……","examples":[{"en":"The researchers returned to Gobero in the fall of 2006.","zh":"研究者於2006年秋天返回 Gobero。"},{"en":"To return to a place means to go back there after leaving it.","zh":"return to a place 指離開後再回到某地。"},{"en":"Students may return to school after a holiday.","zh":"學生假期後會返回學校。"},{"en":"Researchers return to sites when they need more evidence or further excavation.","zh":"當研究者需要更多證據或進一步發掘時，就會返回遺址。"},{"en":"This phrase describes going back to a previous location.","zh":"這個短語描述回到之前去過的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be accompanied by","meaning":"由……陪同","examples":[{"en":"They were accompanied by a larger dig crew.","zh":"他們由一支較大的發掘隊伍陪同。"},{"en":"To be accompanied by someone means to be joined or supported by that person or group.","zh":"be accompanied by someone 指有某人或某群體同行或支援。"},{"en":"A child may be accompanied by a parent on the first day of school.","zh":"孩子第一天上學可能由父母陪同。"},{"en":"Extra people can make difficult work safer and faster.","zh":"額外人手可以令困難工作更安全、更快速。"},{"en":"This phrase describes having others go with you.","zh":"這個短語描述有人同行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"larger dig crew","meaning":"較大的發掘隊伍","examples":[{"en":"A larger dig crew joined the second expedition.","zh":"較大的發掘隊伍加入第二次考察。"},{"en":"A larger dig crew is a bigger group of people working on an archaeological excavation.","zh":"larger dig crew 指參與考古發掘的更大團隊。"},{"en":"A larger crew may be needed when a site contains many burials.","zh":"當遺址包含許多墓葬時，可能需要較大的發掘隊伍。"},{"en":"More workers allow careful digging, recording, and protection to happen at the same time.","zh":"更多人手讓仔細挖掘、記錄和保護可以同時進行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increased manpower for excavation.","zh":"這個短語描述發掘工作中增加的人手。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"additional scientists","meaning":"額外的科學家","examples":[{"en":"Six additional scientists accompanied the team.","zh":"六名額外的科學家陪同團隊。"},{"en":"Additional scientists are extra researchers who join a project beyond the original group.","zh":"additional scientists 指在原有團隊以外加入項目的額外研究者。"},{"en":"A school science fair may invite additional judges if many students enter.","zh":"如果很多學生參加，學校科學展可能邀請額外評判。"},{"en":"Extra experts can bring new skills, such as dating, bone analysis, or DNA work.","zh":"額外專家可以帶來新技能，例如定年、骨骼分析或 DNA 工作。"},{"en":"This phrase means scientists added to the team.","zh":"這個短語指加入團隊的科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"hope to excavate","meaning":"希望發掘","examples":[{"en":"Garcea hoped to excavate about 80 burials.","zh":"Garcea 希望發掘約八十個墓葬。"},{"en":"To hope to excavate something means to want and plan to dig it up carefully for study.","zh":"hope to excavate something 指希望並計劃小心挖出某物作研究。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may hope to excavate a building before a road project destroys it.","zh":"考古學家可能希望在道路工程破壞一座建築前發掘它。"},{"en":"Excavation goals depend on time, safety, funding, and site conditions.","zh":"發掘目標取決於時間、安全、資金和遺址情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an intended digging plan.","zh":"這個短語描述預定的挖掘計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"begin digging","meaning":"開始挖掘","examples":[{"en":"The team began digging at the site.","zh":"團隊開始在遺址挖掘。"},{"en":"To begin digging means to start removing soil, sand, or sediment to uncover something.","zh":"begin digging 指開始移除泥土、沙或沉積物，以揭露某物。"},{"en":"Gardeners begin digging before planting new flowers.","zh":"園丁在種新花前會開始挖掘。"},{"en":"Archaeologists dig slowly because one careless movement can damage evidence.","zh":"考古學家會慢慢挖，因為一次粗心動作就可能破壞證據。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the start of excavation work.","zh":"這個短語標示發掘工作的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"emerge from the dunes","meaning":"從沙丘中顯露出來","examples":[{"en":"The skeletons began to emerge from the dunes.","zh":"骸骨開始從沙丘中顯露出來。"},{"en":"To emerge from the dunes means to become visible as sand is removed or blown away.","zh":"emerge from the dunes 指沙被移除或吹走後，某物變得可見。"},{"en":"After strong wind, buried rocks may emerge from dunes near a beach.","zh":"強風吹過後，埋着的石頭可能從沙灘沙丘中顯露出來。"},{"en":"Objects emerge when covering material is removed by nature or excavation.","zh":"當覆蓋物被自然力量或發掘移除，物件就會顯露。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something hidden becoming visible.","zh":"這個短語描述隱藏物變得可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"present a fresh riddle","meaning":"帶來新的謎團","examples":[{"en":"Each skeleton presented a fresh riddle.","zh":"每具骸骨都帶來新的謎團。"},{"en":"To present a fresh riddle means to create a new question or mystery that needs explanation.","zh":"present a fresh riddle 指產生一個需要解釋的新問題或新謎團。"},{"en":"A student’s unusual exam answer may present a fresh riddle for the teacher.","zh":"學生不尋常的考試答案可能為老師帶來新謎團。"},{"en":"New evidence can solve one problem while creating another.","zh":"新證據可以解決一個問題，同時產生另一個問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a new puzzle caused by a discovery.","zh":"這個短語描述由發現造成的新謎題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"especially those of","meaning":"尤其是……的那些","examples":[{"en":"The Tenerian skeletons presented especially difficult riddles.","zh":"特內里安骸骨帶來尤其困難的謎團。"},{"en":"Especially those of means particularly the ones belonging to a certain group.","zh":"especially those of 指尤其是屬於某群體的那些。"},{"en":"Many homework mistakes were confusing, especially those of students who usually wrote clearly.","zh":"許多功課錯誤令人困惑，尤其是平時寫得很清楚的學生那些錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows attention to the most notable examples in a larger set.","zh":"這個短語把注意力收窄到較大集合中最值得注意的例子。"},{"en":"It helps show which group deserves special focus.","zh":"它幫助顯示哪個群體值得特別關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be buried with","meaning":"與……一起下葬","examples":[{"en":"A male skeleton had been buried with a finger in his mouth.","zh":"一具男性骸骨下葬時手指放在口中。"},{"en":"To be buried with something means to be placed in a grave together with that object or body position.","zh":"be buried with something 指與某物或某身體姿勢一起被放入墓中。"},{"en":"Ancient people may be buried with beads, tools, or food offerings.","zh":"古人可能與珠飾、工具或食物供品一起下葬。"},{"en":"What a person is buried with can reveal beliefs, status, or burial customs.","zh":"一個人與甚麼一起下葬，可以揭示信仰、地位或埋葬習俗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes items or features included in a burial.","zh":"這個短語描述墓葬中包含的物品或特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"bioarchaeologist","meaning":"生物考古學家","examples":[{"en":"Chris Stojanowski is a bioarchaeologist at Arizona State University.","zh":"Chris Stojanowski 是亞利桑那州立大學的生物考古學家。"},{"en":"A bioarchaeologist studies human remains from archaeological sites to understand past lives.","zh":"bioarchaeologist 指研究考古遺址中人類遺骸，以理解過去生活的人。"},{"en":"A bioarchaeologist may examine bones to learn about diet, disease, work, and injury.","zh":"生物考古學家可能檢查骨骼，以了解飲食、疾病、工作和受傷情況。"},{"en":"This field connects biology with archaeology.","zh":"這個領域把生物學與考古學連結起來。"},{"en":"This word refers to a specialist who studies ancient human bodies.","zh":"這個字指研究古代人體的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"piece together clues","meaning":"拼湊線索","examples":[{"en":"Stojanowski began to piece together clues from the bones.","zh":"Stojanowski 開始從骨骼中拼湊線索。"},{"en":"To piece together clues means to combine small pieces of evidence to understand what happened.","zh":"piece together clues 指把小證據組合起來，以理解發生了甚麼事。"},{"en":"A teacher may piece together clues from attendance, homework, and mood to see why a student is struggling.","zh":"老師可能從出席、功課和情緒中拼湊線索，了解學生為何遇到困難。"},{"en":"Separate clues become more useful when they are connected carefully.","zh":"分散線索被仔細連接後會更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes solving a puzzle step by step.","zh":"這個短語描述一步一步解開謎題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"judging by","meaning":"根據……判斷","examples":[{"en":"Judging by the bones, the Kiffian seemed peaceful and hardworking.","zh":"根據骨骼判斷，基菲安人似乎和平而勤勞。"},{"en":"Judging by something means forming an opinion based on that evidence.","zh":"judging by something 指根據某證據形成看法。"},{"en":"Judging by the empty plates, the students enjoyed the lunch.","zh":"根據空盤子判斷，學生很享受午餐。"},{"en":"This phrase lets the speaker show what evidence supports their conclusion.","zh":"這個短語讓說話者顯示甚麼證據支持其結論。"},{"en":"It is useful when making a careful inference.","zh":"作出謹慎推論時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"peaceful, hardworking people","meaning":"和平、勤勞的人","examples":[{"en":"The Kiffian appeared to be peaceful, hardworking people.","zh":"基菲安人看來是和平、勤勞的人。"},{"en":"Peaceful, hardworking people are people who seem non-violent and used to effortful daily work.","zh":"peaceful, hardworking people 指看似不暴力，而且習慣費力日常工作的人。"},{"en":"A farming family may appear hardworking if their tools and bones show years of physical labour.","zh":"如果工具和骨骼顯示多年體力勞動，農民家庭可能看來很勤勞。"},{"en":"Lack of battle injuries can suggest peaceful life, while strong bones can suggest hard work.","zh":"缺少戰鬥傷痕可以暗示和平生活，而強壯骨骼可以暗示辛勤工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both social behaviour and lifestyle.","zh":"這個短語同時描述社會行為和生活方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lack of","meaning":"缺乏……","examples":[{"en":"The lack of injuries suggested that the Kiffian were not often fighting.","zh":"缺乏傷痕顯示基菲安人不常打鬥。"},{"en":"Lack of something means not having enough of it or not having it at all.","zh":"lack of something 指沒有足夠某物，或完全沒有某物。"},{"en":"A lack of sleep can make students tired and careless.","zh":"缺乏睡眠可以令學生疲倦和粗心。"},{"en":"In archaeology, lack of injuries may suggest that violent conflict was uncommon.","zh":"在考古學中，缺乏傷痕可能暗示暴力衝突不常見。"},{"en":"This phrase points to absence as meaningful evidence.","zh":"這個短語指出「缺席」本身也可成為有意義證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"head and forearm injuries","meaning":"頭部和前臂傷痕","examples":[{"en":"The skeletons showed few head and forearm injuries.","zh":"這些骸骨顯示很少頭部和前臂傷痕。"},{"en":"Head and forearm injuries are wounds or damage to the skull and lower arm bones.","zh":"head and forearm injuries 指頭骨和前臂骨上的傷口或損傷。"},{"en":"Defensive injuries may appear on forearms when people protect themselves in fights.","zh":"當人在打鬥中保護自己，防衛性傷痕可能出現在前臂。"},{"en":"Few such injuries can suggest that violent fighting was not common.","zh":"這類傷痕很少，可以暗示暴力打鬥不常見。"},{"en":"This phrase names body areas that can reveal conflict or accidents.","zh":"這個短語指出能揭示衝突或意外的身體部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"suggest that","meaning":"顯示","examples":[{"en":"The lack of injuries suggests that they were not doing much fighting.","zh":"缺乏傷痕顯示他們不常打鬥。"},{"en":"To suggest that means to indicate or imply that something is likely.","zh":"suggest that 指顯示或暗示某事很可能是真的。"},{"en":"A quiet classroom may suggest that students are concentrating.","zh":"安靜課室可能顯示學生正在集中精神。"},{"en":"Evidence can suggest a conclusion even if it does not prove it completely.","zh":"證據可以暗示一個結論，即使未完全證明。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an inference from evidence.","zh":"這個短語引出由證據得出的推論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"do much fighting","meaning":"經常打鬥","examples":[{"en":"The Kiffian did not seem to do much fighting.","zh":"基菲安人似乎不常打鬥。"},{"en":"To do much fighting means to fight often or take part in many violent conflicts.","zh":"do much fighting 指經常打鬥或參與很多暴力衝突。"},{"en":"If two classmates rarely argue or hit each other, they do not do much fighting.","zh":"如果兩名同學很少爭吵或打架，他們就不常打鬥。"},{"en":"Few injury marks can support the idea that fighting was uncommon.","zh":"少量傷痕可以支持打鬥不常見的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frequent physical conflict.","zh":"這個短語描述頻繁的身體衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"point to","meaning":"指向","examples":[{"en":"Stojanowski pointed to a ridge running along a femur.","zh":"Stojanowski 指向沿着股骨延伸的一條隆起。"},{"en":"To point to something means to direct attention toward it, often with a finger or explanation.","zh":"point to something 指把注意力引向某物，常用手指或解釋指出。"},{"en":"A teacher may point to a sentence on the board to explain a grammar mistake.","zh":"老師可能指向黑板上一句句子來解釋文法錯誤。"},{"en":"Pointing to evidence helps listeners see exactly what supports the argument.","zh":"指向證據幫助聽者清楚看見甚麼支持論點。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean physically indicate or logically suggest.","zh":"這個短語可以指實際指示，也可以指邏輯上暗示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"long, narrow ridge","meaning":"又長又窄的隆起","examples":[{"en":"A long, narrow ridge ran along the femur.","zh":"一條又長又窄的隆起沿着股骨延伸。"},{"en":"A long, narrow ridge is a raised line that is thin and extends over a distance.","zh":"long, narrow ridge 指一條細長並延伸一段距離的凸起線。"},{"en":"A long, narrow ridge on a desk may be felt by running a finger across the wood.","zh":"手指滑過木桌時，可能感覺到桌上一條又長又窄的隆起。"},{"en":"On bone, such ridges can show where strong muscles were attached.","zh":"在骨頭上，這類隆起可以顯示強壯肌肉曾附着的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shape and texture.","zh":"這個短語描述形狀和質感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"run along","meaning":"沿着……延伸","examples":[{"en":"The ridge ran along the femur.","zh":"這條隆起沿着股骨延伸。"},{"en":"To run along something means to extend beside or across its length.","zh":"run along something 指沿着某物的長度旁邊或表面延伸。"},{"en":"A path may run along a river for several kilometres.","zh":"一條小路可能沿着河流延伸數公里。"},{"en":"Lines or ridges that run along a surface can show structure or direction.","zh":"沿表面延伸的線或隆起可以顯示結構或方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how something is positioned lengthwise.","zh":"這個短語描述某物如何沿長度排列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"femur","meaning":"股骨","examples":[{"en":"The femur showed evidence of strong leg muscles.","zh":"股骨顯示強壯腿部肌肉的證據。"},{"en":"The femur is the thigh bone, the long bone between the hip and the knee.","zh":"femur 指大腿骨，即髖部和膝部之間的長骨。"},{"en":"A biology teacher may use a skeleton model to show students the femur.","zh":"生物老師可能用骨骼模型向學生展示股骨。"},{"en":"Because the femur supports walking and running, it can reveal physical activity.","zh":"由於股骨支撐走路和跑步，它可以揭示身體活動情況。"},{"en":"This word names a specific bone in the leg.","zh":"這個字指出腿部一塊特定骨頭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"muscle attachment","meaning":"肌肉附着點","examples":[{"en":"The ridge was the muscle attachment.","zh":"這條隆起是肌肉附着點。"},{"en":"A muscle attachment is the place where muscle connects to bone.","zh":"muscle attachment 指肌肉連接到骨頭的位置。"},{"en":"Doctors and scientists can examine muscle attachments to understand how strongly a body was used.","zh":"醫生和科學家可以檢查肌肉附着點，以了解身體被使用的強度。"},{"en":"Larger attachment areas may suggest repeated or powerful movement.","zh":"較大的附着區域可能暗示反覆或強力動作。"},{"en":"This phrase links bone shape with muscle activity.","zh":"這個短語把骨骼形態與肌肉活動連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"this individual","meaning":"這個個體","examples":[{"en":"This individual had huge leg muscles.","zh":"這個個體有巨大的腿部肌肉。"},{"en":"This individual means this particular person being discussed.","zh":"this individual 指正在討論的這個特定人。"},{"en":"In a medical report, this individual may refer to one patient among many.","zh":"在醫療報告中，this individual 可指眾多病人中的一名。"},{"en":"Researchers use this phrase when focusing on one person’s evidence rather than the whole group.","zh":"研究者集中於一個人的證據而不是整個群體時會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It is more formal than saying “this person.”","zh":"它比 “this person” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"huge leg muscles","meaning":"巨大的腿部肌肉","examples":[{"en":"The Kiffian skeleton showed huge leg muscles.","zh":"基菲安骸骨顯示巨大的腿部肌肉。"},{"en":"Huge leg muscles means very large and strong muscles in the legs.","zh":"huge leg muscles 指腿部非常大而強壯的肌肉。"},{"en":"A cyclist may develop huge leg muscles after years of training.","zh":"單車手多年訓練後可能發展出巨大的腿部肌肉。"},{"en":"In ancient bones, strong muscle marks can suggest a physically demanding lifestyle.","zh":"在古代骨骼中，強壯肌肉痕跡可以暗示體力要求高的生活方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strength and repeated use of the legs.","zh":"這個短語描述腿部力量和反覆使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"eat a lot of protein","meaning":"攝取大量蛋白質","examples":[{"en":"The bones suggested that the person ate a lot of protein.","zh":"骨骼顯示該人攝取大量蛋白質。"},{"en":"To eat a lot of protein means to consume plenty of foods such as fish, meat, eggs, or beans.","zh":"eat a lot of protein 指攝取大量魚、肉、蛋或豆類等食物。"},{"en":"Athletes may eat a lot of protein to support muscle repair.","zh":"運動員可能攝取大量蛋白質，以支持肌肉修復。"},{"en":"Diet can leave chemical clues in bones and teeth.","zh":"飲食可以在骨骼和牙齒中留下化學線索。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a diet rich in body-building nutrients.","zh":"這個短語描述富含建構身體營養素的飲食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"strenuous lifestyle","meaning":"艱苦而費力的生活方式","examples":[{"en":"The individual had a strenuous lifestyle.","zh":"這個個體過着艱苦而費力的生活方式。"},{"en":"A strenuous lifestyle involves hard physical work and repeated effort.","zh":"strenuous lifestyle 指涉及繁重體力工作和反覆努力的生活方式。"},{"en":"Farmers who carry heavy tools and work long hours may have a strenuous lifestyle.","zh":"長時間工作並搬運沉重工具的農民，可能有艱苦費力的生活方式。"},{"en":"Such a lifestyle can strengthen muscles and leave marks on bones.","zh":"這種生活方式可以強化肌肉，並在骨骼上留下痕跡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes daily life that is physically demanding.","zh":"這個短語描述日常生活在體力上要求很高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be consistent with","meaning":"與……一致","examples":[{"en":"The evidence was consistent with a fishing way of life.","zh":"這些證據與捕魚生活方式一致。"},{"en":"To be consistent with something means to fit it or support it without contradiction.","zh":"be consistent with something 指與某事相符或支持它而不矛盾。"},{"en":"A student’s neat notes are consistent with the teacher’s view that she studies carefully.","zh":"學生整齊的筆記與老師認為她認真學習的看法一致。"},{"en":"Evidence becomes stronger when several clues are consistent with the same explanation.","zh":"當多個線索與同一解釋一致，證據就變得更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when evidence matches an idea.","zh":"當證據與某想法相符時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"fishing way of life","meaning":"捕魚生活方式","examples":[{"en":"The bones were consistent with a fishing way of life.","zh":"骨骼與捕魚生活方式一致。"},{"en":"A fishing way of life is daily life centred on catching, preparing, and depending on fish.","zh":"fishing way of life 指以捕魚、處理魚和依賴魚為中心的日常生活。"},{"en":"A lakeside family that fishes every day and sells dried fish has a fishing way of life.","zh":"每天捕魚並出售魚乾的湖邊家庭，就有捕魚生活方式。"},{"en":"Such a lifestyle can shape tools, diet, muscles, and settlement location.","zh":"這種生活方式可以塑造工具、飲食、肌肉和聚居地點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes more than a hobby; it describes survival and routine.","zh":"這個短語不只是指興趣，而是指生存和常規。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"for contrast","meaning":"作為對比","examples":[{"en":"For contrast, Stojanowski showed the femur of a Tenerian male.","zh":"作為對比，Stojanowski 展示了一名特內里安男性的股骨。"},{"en":"For contrast means to show a difference by placing one example beside another.","zh":"for contrast 指透過把一個例子放在另一個例子旁來顯示差異。"},{"en":"A teacher may show a weak paragraph and, for contrast, a strong one.","zh":"老師可能展示一段弱文章，然後作為對比展示一段強文章。"},{"en":"Contrast helps people notice features that would be less clear alone.","zh":"對比幫助人注意到單獨看時較不清楚的特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a comparison.","zh":"這個短語引出比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"Tenerian male","meaning":"特內里安男性","examples":[{"en":"The femur of a Tenerian male showed a different lifestyle.","zh":"一名特內里安男性的股骨顯示不同生活方式。"},{"en":"A Tenerian male is a male individual belonging to the Tenerian people or period.","zh":"Tenerian male 指屬於特內里安人或特內里安時期的男性個體。"},{"en":"Researchers may compare a Tenerian male with a Kiffian male to study cultural change.","zh":"研究者可能把特內里安男性與基菲安男性比較，以研究文化變化。"},{"en":"Differences in bones can suggest differences in work, diet, or activity.","zh":"骨骼差異可以暗示工作、飲食或活動上的差異。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both sex and archaeological group.","zh":"這個短語同時指出性別和考古群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"barely perceptible","meaning":"幾乎看不見","examples":[{"en":"The ridge on the Tenerian femur was barely perceptible.","zh":"特內里安股骨上的隆起幾乎看不見。"},{"en":"Barely perceptible means almost impossible to see, hear, or notice.","zh":"barely perceptible 指幾乎無法看見、聽見或注意到。"},{"en":"A tiny crack in a phone screen may be barely perceptible until light hits it.","zh":"手機螢幕上的細小裂痕可能在光線照到前幾乎看不見。"},{"en":"If a bone ridge is barely perceptible, the muscle attachment was probably weaker.","zh":"如果骨頭隆起幾乎看不見，肌肉附着點很可能較弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something very faint.","zh":"這個短語描述非常微弱的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"much less strenuous lifestyle","meaning":"較不費力的生活方式","examples":[{"en":"The Tenerian male had a much less strenuous lifestyle.","zh":"這名特內里安男性過着較不費力的生活方式。"},{"en":"A much less strenuous lifestyle involves far less heavy physical effort.","zh":"much less strenuous lifestyle 指包含少得多繁重體力勞動的生活方式。"},{"en":"An office worker usually has a less strenuous lifestyle than a construction worker.","zh":"辦公室職員通常比建築工人有較不費力的生活方式。"},{"en":"Less physical strain may leave weaker muscle marks on bones.","zh":"較少體力負荷可能在骨骼上留下較弱肌肉痕跡。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two levels of daily physical effort.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種日常體力消耗水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"expect of","meaning":"可預期於……","examples":[{"en":"A less strenuous lifestyle is what one might expect of a herder.","zh":"較不費力的生活方式是人們可預期於牧民的情況。"},{"en":"To expect something of someone means to think that quality or behaviour is likely for that person.","zh":"expect something of someone 指認為某種特質或行為可能出現在某人身上。"},{"en":"A teacher might expect neat notes of a very organised student.","zh":"老師可能預期一名非常有條理的學生會有整齊筆記。"},{"en":"Expectations come from what we know about someone’s role or lifestyle.","zh":"預期來自我們對某人角色或生活方式的了解。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a prediction with a person or group.","zh":"這個短語把預測與某人或群體連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"herder","meaning":"牧民","examples":[{"en":"A herder usually has a less strenuous lifestyle than a fishing-based group.","zh":"牧民通常比以捕魚為主的群體有較不費力的生活方式。"},{"en":"A herder is a person who looks after animals such as cattle, goats, or sheep.","zh":"herder 指照顧牛、山羊或綿羊等動物的人。"},{"en":"A herder may move animals to fresh grass and water during the year.","zh":"牧民可能在一年中把動物帶到新的草地和水源。"},{"en":"Herding still involves work, but it may use different muscles from fishing or hunting.","zh":"放牧仍然涉及工作，但使用的肌肉可能不同於捕魚或狩獵。"},{"en":"This word describes a livestock-based occupation.","zh":"這個字描述以牲畜為基礎的職業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"assessment","meaning":"評估","examples":[{"en":"Stojanowski’s assessment fits the prevailing view among scholars.","zh":"Stojanowski 的評估符合學者之間的主流看法。"},{"en":"An assessment is a careful judgement based on evidence.","zh":"assessment 指基於證據的仔細判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher’s assessment of a student’s writing may include grammar, structure, and ideas.","zh":"老師對學生寫作的評估可能包括文法、結構和內容。"},{"en":"Good assessment depends on clear criteria and reliable evidence.","zh":"良好評估取決於清楚準則和可靠證據。"},{"en":"This word means evaluation, not just a quick opinion.","zh":"這個字指評價，而不只是快速意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"fit the prevailing view","meaning":"符合主流看法","examples":[{"en":"The assessment fits the prevailing view among scholars.","zh":"這項評估符合學者之間的主流看法。"},{"en":"To fit the prevailing view means to agree with the opinion most commonly accepted.","zh":"fit the prevailing view 指與最普遍被接受的意見一致。"},{"en":"A new exam result may fit the prevailing view that regular practice improves writing.","zh":"新考試結果可能符合定期練習改善寫作的主流看法。"},{"en":"When evidence fits the prevailing view, it supports what many experts already think.","zh":"當證據符合主流看法，它就支持許多專家已有的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase links new evidence with a dominant opinion.","zh":"這個短語把新證據與主導意見連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"prevailing view","meaning":"主流看法","examples":[{"en":"The prevailing view is that drier conditions favoured herding.","zh":"主流看法是較乾燥的環境有利於放牧。"},{"en":"The prevailing view is the opinion most widely accepted at a particular time.","zh":"prevailing view 指某一時期最廣泛被接受的意見。"},{"en":"The prevailing view in a school may be that phones distract students during lessons.","zh":"學校中的主流看法可能是手機會令學生上課分心。"},{"en":"Prevailing views can change when new evidence appears.","zh":"當新證據出現，主流看法可以改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the dominant opinion, not necessarily the final truth.","zh":"這個短語描述主導意見，不一定是最終真相。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"among scholars","meaning":"在學者之間","examples":[{"en":"The idea was widely accepted among scholars.","zh":"這個想法在學者之間被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"Among scholars means within the community of academic experts.","zh":"among scholars 指在學術專家群體之中。"},{"en":"A theory may be popular among scholars but unfamiliar to the general public.","zh":"一個理論可能在學者之間流行，但一般公眾不熟悉。"},{"en":"Academic agreement matters because scholars compare evidence carefully.","zh":"學術共識重要，因為學者會仔細比較證據。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the expert group holding an opinion.","zh":"這個短語指出持有某意見的專家群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"drier conditions","meaning":"較乾燥的環境","examples":[{"en":"Drier conditions favoured herding over hunting.","zh":"較乾燥的環境較有利於放牧而非狩獵。"},{"en":"Drier conditions are environmental conditions with less rainfall or water.","zh":"drier conditions 指降雨或水源較少的環境條件。"},{"en":"Farmers may plant different crops when drier conditions reduce soil moisture.","zh":"當較乾燥環境減少土壤水分，農民可能種植不同作物。"},{"en":"In dry areas, herding may be easier than farming or fishing because animals can move to water.","zh":"在乾旱地區，放牧可能比耕種或捕魚更容易，因為動物可以移動到水源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes climate or environmental change toward dryness.","zh":"這個短語描述氣候或環境變得較乾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"favour something over something","meaning":"較有利於……而非……","examples":[{"en":"Drier conditions favoured herding over hunting.","zh":"較乾燥的環境較有利於放牧而非狩獵。"},{"en":"To favour A over B means to make A more suitable or more likely than B.","zh":"favour A over B 指令 A 比 B 更合適或更可能出現。"},{"en":"A quiet library favours individual study over noisy group discussion.","zh":"安靜圖書館較有利於個人學習，而非嘈吵小組討論。"},{"en":"Environmental change can favour one lifestyle while making another harder.","zh":"環境變化可以有利於一種生活方式，同時令另一種更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly compares two options.","zh":"這個短語清楚比較兩個選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"herding over hunting","meaning":"放牧而非狩獵","examples":[{"en":"Scholars believe that drier conditions favoured herding over hunting.","zh":"學者相信較乾燥的環境有利於放牧而非狩獵。"},{"en":"Herding over hunting means keeping animals became more suitable than catching wild animals.","zh":"herding over hunting 指飼養動物變得比捕獵野生動物更合適。"},{"en":"A family may choose home cooking over takeaway if food prices rise.","zh":"如果食物價格上升，家庭可能選擇在家煮飯而非叫外賣。"},{"en":"Choosing one way over another usually reflects changing needs or conditions.","zh":"選擇一種方式而非另一種通常反映需要或條件改變。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts two ways of getting food.","zh":"這個短語對比兩種取得食物的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"point out","meaning":"指出","examples":[{"en":"Sereno pointed out that few herd animals were found at the site.","zh":"Sereno 指出該遺址發現的畜群動物很少。"},{"en":"To point out something means to mention it because it is important or easily missed.","zh":"point out something 指因某事重要或容易被忽略而提及它。"},{"en":"A teacher may point out that a student answered the wrong question.","zh":"老師可能指出學生答錯了題目。"},{"en":"Pointing out a detail can challenge an explanation or add balance.","zh":"指出一個細節可以挑戰某解釋或增加平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes drawing attention to a fact.","zh":"這個短語描述把注意力引向某個事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"turn up at the site","meaning":"在遺址出現；被發現","examples":[{"en":"Hundreds of animal bones turned up at the site.","zh":"數百塊動物骨頭在該遺址被發現。"},{"en":"To turn up at the site means to be found or discovered there.","zh":"turn up at the site 指在遺址中出現或被發現。"},{"en":"More old coins may turn up at a construction site after workers dig deeper.","zh":"工人挖得更深後，建築地盤可能發現更多舊硬幣。"},{"en":"Discoveries often turn up gradually as excavation continues.","zh":"隨着發掘繼續，發現通常會逐步出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and describes evidence appearing.","zh":"這個短語較口語，描述證據出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"belong to","meaning":"屬於……","examples":[{"en":"None of the bones belonged to goats or sheep.","zh":"沒有任何骨頭屬於山羊或綿羊。"},{"en":"To belong to a species or group means to be part of that species or group.","zh":"belong to a species or group 指屬於某物種或群體。"},{"en":"A lost schoolbag may belong to a student in the next classroom.","zh":"遺失書包可能屬於隔壁課室的學生。"},{"en":"Identifying what bones belong to helps researchers reconstruct ancient animals and diets.","zh":"識別骨頭屬於甚麼，有助研究者重建古代動物和飲食。"},{"en":"This phrase links an object or remains with its owner or category.","zh":"這個短語把物件或遺骸與其主人或類別連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"goats or sheep","meaning":"山羊或綿羊","examples":[{"en":"No bones from goats or sheep were found at the site.","zh":"該遺址沒有發現山羊或綿羊的骨頭。"},{"en":"Goats or sheep are common herd animals kept for meat, milk, wool, or trade.","zh":"goats or sheep 指常見畜群動物，可供肉、奶、羊毛或交易。"},{"en":"A herding community may move goats or sheep between grazing areas.","zh":"放牧社群可能把山羊或綿羊在不同牧地之間遷移。"},{"en":"If no goat or sheep bones are found, evidence for herding may be less direct.","zh":"如果沒有發現山羊或綿羊骨頭，放牧證據可能較不直接。"},{"en":"This phrase names typical animals linked with pastoral life.","zh":"這個短語指出與牧民生活相關的典型動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"cow species","meaning":"牛類物種","examples":[{"en":"Only three bones came from a cow species.","zh":"只有三塊骨頭來自牛類物種。"},{"en":"A cow species is a type of cattle or cattle-like animal.","zh":"cow species 指牛或類牛動物的一種類型。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may identify a cow species from the size and shape of bones.","zh":"考古學家可能從骨頭大小和形狀辨認牛類物種。"},{"en":"Cattle bones can suggest herding, but a few bones alone may not prove a fully pastoral culture.","zh":"牛骨可以暗示放牧，但少量骨頭本身未必證明完全牧民文化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an animal category related to cows.","zh":"這個短語描述與牛有關的動物類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"not unusual for","meaning":"對……來說並不罕見","examples":[{"en":"It is not unusual for herders to avoid slaughtering cattle.","zh":"牧民避免宰殺牛隻並不罕見。"},{"en":"Not unusual for someone means fairly normal or expected for that group.","zh":"not unusual for someone 指對某群體來說相當正常或可預期。"},{"en":"It is not unusual for students to feel nervous before their first speaking exam.","zh":"學生第一次口試前感到緊張並不罕見。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain why something that looks surprising may actually be normal.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋為何看似驚訝的事其實可能正常。"},{"en":"It reduces the force of an objection.","zh":"它削弱反對意見的力度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"herding culture","meaning":"放牧文化","examples":[{"en":"A herding culture may not slaughter cattle in a cemetery.","zh":"放牧文化可能不會在墓地宰殺牛隻。"},{"en":"A herding culture is a society whose life depends heavily on keeping animals.","zh":"herding culture 指生活高度依賴飼養動物的社會。"},{"en":"A herding culture may move with cattle, goats, or sheep to find water and grass.","zh":"放牧文化可能帶着牛、山羊或綿羊遷移尋找水和草。"},{"en":"Animals can be wealth, food, and social value in such cultures.","zh":"在這類文化中，動物可以是財富、食物和社會價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a way of life built around livestock.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞牲畜建立的生活方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"slaughter cattle","meaning":"宰殺牛隻","examples":[{"en":"Some pastoralists are reluctant to slaughter cattle.","zh":"有些牧民不願宰殺牛隻。"},{"en":"To slaughter cattle means to kill cows or cattle for meat or ritual use.","zh":"slaughter cattle 指為肉食或儀式用途殺死牛隻。"},{"en":"A farmer may slaughter cattle only for special occasions if animals are valuable.","zh":"如果動物很有價值，農民可能只在特殊場合宰殺牛隻。"},{"en":"If cattle represent wealth, people may avoid killing them often.","zh":"如果牛代表財富，人們可能避免經常殺牛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the killing of livestock, not ordinary animal care.","zh":"這個短語描述殺死牲畜，而不是普通照顧動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"particularly in","meaning":"尤其在……","examples":[{"en":"It is unusual to slaughter cattle, particularly in a cemetery.","zh":"宰殺牛隻是不尋常的，尤其在墓地。"},{"en":"Particularly in means especially in a certain place or situation.","zh":"particularly in 指尤其在某地方或情況下。"},{"en":"Loud noise is disturbing, particularly in a library.","zh":"噪音令人困擾，尤其在圖書館。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the situation where something is most important or surprising.","zh":"這個短語突出某事最重要或最令人意外的情況。"},{"en":"It narrows a general statement to a specific context.","zh":"它把一般說法收窄到特定語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"cemetery","meaning":"墓地","examples":[{"en":"The site included a Neolithic cemetery.","zh":"該遺址包括一個新石器時代墓地。"},{"en":"A cemetery is a place where dead people are buried.","zh":"cemetery 指埋葬死者的地方。"},{"en":"A village cemetery may contain graves from many generations.","zh":"村莊墓地可能包含許多世代的墳墓。"},{"en":"Archaeological cemeteries can reveal burial customs, family groups, and beliefs about death.","zh":"考古墓地可以揭示埋葬習俗、家庭群體和死亡信仰。"},{"en":"This word refers to a burial place.","zh":"這個字指埋葬場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"noting that","meaning":"並指出","examples":[{"en":"Garcea responded, noting that modern pastoralists also avoid butchering animals.","zh":"Garcea 回應，並指出現代牧民也避免屠宰動物。"},{"en":"Noting that means adding or pointing out a fact while speaking or writing.","zh":"noting that 指在說話或寫作時補充或指出某個事實。"},{"en":"A teacher may praise a student, noting that the essay has improved in structure.","zh":"老師可能讚賞學生，並指出文章結構已有改善。"},{"en":"This phrase adds supporting information to a response.","zh":"這個短語為回應加入支持資訊。"},{"en":"It is common in formal explanation and reporting.","zh":"它常見於正式解釋和報告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"modern pastoralists","meaning":"現代牧民","examples":[{"en":"Modern pastoralists may be reluctant to butcher animals from their herd.","zh":"現代牧民可能不願屠宰自己畜群中的動物。"},{"en":"Modern pastoralists are people today who live by raising and moving livestock.","zh":"modern pastoralists 指今日靠飼養和遷移牲畜生活的人。"},{"en":"Some modern pastoralists move cattle seasonally to find water and grass.","zh":"有些現代牧民會季節性遷移牛隻，以尋找水和草。"},{"en":"Their habits can help researchers understand ancient herding societies.","zh":"他們的習慣可以幫助研究者理解古代放牧社會。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to present-day livestock-keeping communities.","zh":"這個短語指現今以牲畜為生的社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be loath to","meaning":"不願意……","examples":[{"en":"Pastoralists are often loath to butcher animals in their herd.","zh":"牧民通常不願意屠宰自己畜群中的動物。"},{"en":"To be loath to do something means to be unwilling or reluctant to do it.","zh":"be loath to do something 指不願意或勉強去做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be loath to delete an essay after spending hours writing it.","zh":"學生花了數小時寫作文後，可能不願刪除它。"},{"en":"People are loath to lose something when it has practical or emotional value.","zh":"當某物有實際或情感價值，人們會不願失去它。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses strong reluctance.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈不情願。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"butcher an animal","meaning":"屠宰動物","examples":[{"en":"Some pastoralists are loath to butcher even one animal.","zh":"有些牧民甚至不願屠宰一隻動物。"},{"en":"To butcher an animal means to kill and cut it up for meat.","zh":"butcher an animal 指殺死並分割動物作肉食。"},{"en":"A family may butcher an animal only during an important festival.","zh":"家庭可能只在重要節日時屠宰動物。"},{"en":"If animals represent wealth, butchering them reduces the herd.","zh":"如果動物代表財富，屠宰牠們會減少畜群。"},{"en":"This phrase describes killing and preparing livestock for food.","zh":"這個短語描述殺死並處理牲畜作食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in their herd","meaning":"在他們的畜群中","examples":[{"en":"Pastoralists may avoid killing animals in their herd.","zh":"牧民可能避免殺死他們畜群中的動物。"},{"en":"In their herd means among the animals they own or look after.","zh":"in their herd 指在他們擁有或照顧的動物群中。"},{"en":"A farmer may know each cow in his herd by its markings.","zh":"農民可能根據斑紋認得畜群中的每頭牛。"},{"en":"Animals in a herd can represent food, income, transport, or social status.","zh":"畜群中的動物可以代表食物、收入、運輸或社會地位。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies animals belonging to a livestock group.","zh":"這個短語指出屬於某個牲畜群的動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reasoned","meaning":"推論","examples":[{"en":"Sereno reasoned that the Tenerian may have been a transitional group.","zh":"Sereno 推論特內里安人可能是一個過渡群體。"},{"en":"To reason means to reach a conclusion by thinking through evidence logically.","zh":"reason 指透過邏輯思考證據而得出結論。"},{"en":"A teacher may reason that a student is tired if homework quality drops after late activities.","zh":"如果學生晚間活動後功課質素下降，老師可能推論他很疲倦。"},{"en":"Reasoning connects clues instead of guessing randomly.","zh":"推論會連接線索，而不是隨機猜測。"},{"en":"This word describes logical thinking toward a conclusion.","zh":"這個字描述朝向結論的邏輯思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"transitional group","meaning":"過渡群體","examples":[{"en":"The Tenerian at Gobero may have been a transitional group.","zh":"Gobero 的特內里安人可能是一個過渡群體。"},{"en":"A transitional group is a group moving between one way of life and another.","zh":"transitional group 指正從一種生活方式轉向另一種生活方式的群體。"},{"en":"A family moving from village farming to city jobs may be in a transitional stage.","zh":"從鄉村農耕轉向城市工作的家庭，可能處於過渡階段。"},{"en":"Transitional groups often show mixed evidence from old and new practices.","zh":"過渡群體常同時顯示舊做法和新做法的混合證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes change that is not yet complete.","zh":"這個短語描述尚未完成的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"fully adopt herding","meaning":"完全採用放牧生活","examples":[{"en":"The Tenerian may not have fully adopted herding.","zh":"特內里安人可能尚未完全採用放牧生活。"},{"en":"To fully adopt herding means to completely take up animal-raising as a main way of life.","zh":"fully adopt herding 指完全把飼養動物作為主要生活方式。"},{"en":"A community may adopt online learning partly, but not fully, if some lessons remain face-to-face.","zh":"如果部分課堂仍面授，社群可能只是部分採用網上學習，而非完全採用。"},{"en":"Partial adoption can leave mixed evidence in tools, bones, and diet.","zh":"部分採用可以在工具、骨骼和飲食中留下混合證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete acceptance of a new lifestyle.","zh":"這個短語描述完全接受一種新生活方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"rely heavily on","meaning":"嚴重依賴","examples":[{"en":"They may have still relied heavily on hunting and fishing.","zh":"他們可能仍然嚴重依賴狩獵和捕魚。"},{"en":"To rely heavily on something means to depend on it very much.","zh":"rely heavily on something 指非常依賴某事。"},{"en":"A student who relies heavily on translation apps may struggle without a phone.","zh":"嚴重依賴翻譯應用程式的學生，沒有手機時可能很吃力。"},{"en":"Heavy reliance shows that something is central to survival or success.","zh":"高度依賴顯示某事對生存或成功非常核心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong dependence.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"hunting and fishing","meaning":"狩獵和捕魚","examples":[{"en":"The Tenerian may have relied on hunting and fishing as well as herding.","zh":"特內里安人可能依賴狩獵和捕魚，也依賴放牧。"},{"en":"Hunting and fishing are ways of obtaining food by catching wild animals and fish.","zh":"hunting and fishing 指透過捕捉野生動物和魚來取得食物的方式。"},{"en":"A lakeside community may combine hunting and fishing with gathering plants.","zh":"湖邊社群可能把狩獵和捕魚與採集植物結合。"},{"en":"These activities depend on local animals, water, tools, and seasonal conditions.","zh":"這些活動依賴本地動物、水源、工具和季節條件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes food-gathering activities before or alongside farming and herding.","zh":"這個短語描述農耕和放牧之前或同時存在的取食活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"continue to analyse","meaning":"繼續分析","examples":[{"en":"Stojanowski continues to analyse the Gobero bones.","zh":"Stojanowski 繼續分析 Gobero 的骨骼。"},{"en":"To continue to analyse something means to keep studying it carefully.","zh":"continue to analyse something 指持續仔細研究某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may continue to analyse exam mistakes after noticing a pattern.","zh":"老師注意到模式後，可能繼續分析考試錯誤。"},{"en":"Ongoing analysis can reveal details missed in the first study.","zh":"持續分析可以揭示第一次研究中錯過的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research that is still in progress.","zh":"這個短語描述仍在進行中的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"clues to","meaning":"關於……的線索","examples":[{"en":"The bones may provide clues to health and diet.","zh":"骨骼可能提供關於健康和飲食的線索。"},{"en":"Clues to something are pieces of evidence that help explain it.","zh":"clues to something 指有助解釋某事的證據。"},{"en":"A student’s tired eyes and unfinished homework may be clues to stress.","zh":"學生疲倦的眼神和未完成功課，可能是關於壓力的線索。"},{"en":"In archaeology, bones can give clues to what people ate and how they lived.","zh":"在考古學中，骨骼可以提供人們吃甚麼和如何生活的線索。"},{"en":"This phrase links evidence with the question it helps answer.","zh":"這個短語把證據與它幫助回答的問題連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"health and diet","meaning":"健康和飲食","examples":[{"en":"The bones contain clues to the Green Saharans’ health and diet.","zh":"骨骼包含關於綠色撒哈拉人健康和飲食的線索。"},{"en":"Health and diet mean people’s physical condition and the food they ate.","zh":"health and diet 指人們的身體狀況和所吃食物。"},{"en":"Doctors ask about health and diet because food affects energy, growth, and illness.","zh":"醫生詢問健康和飲食，因為食物影響能量、成長和疾病。"},{"en":"Ancient bones and teeth can preserve evidence of disease, injury, and nutrition.","zh":"古代骨骼和牙齒可以保存疾病、受傷和營養證據。"},{"en":"This phrase connects body condition with eating habits.","zh":"這個短語把身體狀況與飲食習慣連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"derive DNA from","meaning":"從……提取 DNA","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are trying to derive DNA from the teeth.","zh":"科學家正嘗試從牙齒提取 DNA。"},{"en":"To derive DNA from something means to extract genetic material from it.","zh":"derive DNA from something 指從某物提取遺傳物質。"},{"en":"A lab may derive DNA from hair or saliva in a medical test.","zh":"實驗室可能在醫學測試中從頭髮或唾液提取 DNA。"},{"en":"Teeth can sometimes preserve DNA better than other body parts.","zh":"牙齒有時比其他身體部分更能保存 DNA。"},{"en":"This phrase describes obtaining genetic evidence from a sample.","zh":"這個短語描述從樣本取得基因證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"reveal the genetic origins of","meaning":"揭示……的基因起源","examples":[{"en":"DNA could reveal the genetic origins of the Kiffian and Tenerian.","zh":"DNA 可以揭示基菲安人和特內里安人的基因起源。"},{"en":"To reveal the genetic origins of a group means to show where their ancestry may come from.","zh":"reveal the genetic origins of a group 指顯示該群體祖源可能來自哪裡。"},{"en":"DNA tests can sometimes reveal the genetic origins of a family line.","zh":"DNA 測試有時可以揭示一個家族線的基因起源。"},{"en":"Genetic evidence can connect ancient people with regions or populations.","zh":"基因證據可以把古人與地區或人口連起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using DNA to understand ancestry.","zh":"這個短語描述使用 DNA 理解祖源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"genetic origins","meaning":"基因起源","examples":[{"en":"Scientists hope to learn the genetic origins of the two groups.","zh":"科學家希望了解這兩個群體的基因起源。"},{"en":"Genetic origins are the ancestral roots shown through DNA.","zh":"genetic origins 指透過 DNA 顯示的祖源。"},{"en":"A person may study genetic origins to understand family history more deeply.","zh":"一個人可能研究基因起源，以更深入理解家族歷史。"},{"en":"Genetic origins can show connections that are not visible from tools or bones alone.","zh":"基因起源可以顯示單靠工具或骨骼看不到的關聯。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to ancestry at the DNA level.","zh":"這個短語指 DNA 層面的祖源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"possibly link someone to","meaning":"可能將某人與……聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"DNA could possibly link them to descendants living today.","zh":"DNA 可能將他們與現今仍在世的後裔聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To possibly link someone to another group means to suggest a potential connection, but not yet prove it fully.","zh":"possibly link someone to another group 指暗示可能有關聯，但尚未完全證明。"},{"en":"A family record may possibly link a student to relatives overseas.","zh":"家族記錄可能把學生與海外親戚聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Researchers use cautious language when evidence may show a connection but is not final.","zh":"當證據可能顯示關聯但尚未定論，研究者會使用謹慎語言。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible relationship based on evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述基於證據的可能關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"descendants living today","meaning":"現今仍在世的後裔","examples":[{"en":"The researchers hope to link the ancient people to descendants living today.","zh":"研究者希望將古人與現今仍在世的後裔聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Descendants living today are modern people who may come from the same ancestral line.","zh":"descendants living today 指可能來自同一祖先線的現代人。"},{"en":"A family tree can connect great-grandparents with descendants living today.","zh":"家譜可以把曾祖父母與現今仍在世的後裔連起來。"},{"en":"Linking ancient remains to modern descendants can help trace population history.","zh":"把古代遺骸與現代後裔連繫起來，可以幫助追溯人口歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to present-day people connected to earlier generations.","zh":"這個短語指與早期世代有關的當代人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"estimate that","meaning":"估計","examples":[{"en":"Sereno and Garcea estimate that many burials remain.","zh":"Sereno 和 Garcea 估計仍有許多墓葬。"},{"en":"To estimate that means to make a careful guess based on available evidence.","zh":"estimate that 指根據現有證據作出仔細估算。"},{"en":"A teacher may estimate that half the class needs more practice after checking homework.","zh":"老師檢查功課後，可能估計半班需要更多練習。"},{"en":"Estimates are useful when exact counting is not yet possible.","zh":"當尚未能精確計算時，估計很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a reasoned approximation.","zh":"這個短語引出有根據的近似判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"remain to be excavated","meaning":"仍有待發掘","examples":[{"en":"About a hundred burials remain to be excavated.","zh":"約一百個墓葬仍有待發掘。"},{"en":"To remain to be excavated means still need to be dug up and studied.","zh":"remain to be excavated 指仍需要被挖出並研究。"},{"en":"Several rooms in an old building may remain to be inspected after the first visit.","zh":"初次到訪後，舊建築中幾個房間可能仍有待檢查。"},{"en":"Work remains when a site contains more evidence than the team has already uncovered.","zh":"當遺址含有比團隊已揭露更多的證據時，工作就仍未完成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unfinished excavation.","zh":"這個短語描述尚未完成的發掘。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"harsh Tenere winds","meaning":"泰內雷的強烈風沙","examples":[{"en":"Harsh Tenere winds continue to erode the dunes.","zh":"泰內雷的強烈風沙繼續侵蝕沙丘。"},{"en":"Harsh Tenere winds are strong, dry desert winds in the Tenere region.","zh":"harsh Tenere winds 指泰內雷地區強烈而乾燥的沙漠風。"},{"en":"Strong winds can make desert fieldwork difficult by blowing sand into eyes and equipment.","zh":"強風會把沙吹入眼睛和設備，使沙漠野外工作困難。"},{"en":"Over time, harsh winds can uncover bones but also destroy them.","zh":"長時間下，強風可以揭露骨骼，但也可以摧毀它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a local natural force that threatens the site.","zh":"這個短語描述威脅遺址的本地自然力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"erode the dunes","meaning":"侵蝕沙丘","examples":[{"en":"The winds continue to erode the dunes.","zh":"風繼續侵蝕沙丘。"},{"en":"To erode the dunes means to wear away sand hills gradually by wind or water.","zh":"erode the dunes 指風或水逐漸磨蝕沙丘。"},{"en":"Waves can erode sand dunes along a beach after a storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，海浪可以侵蝕沙灘上的沙丘。"},{"en":"Erosion can reveal buried objects but also damage them if exposure continues.","zh":"侵蝕可以揭露被埋物件，但若繼續暴露，也可以損害它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual destruction of sand formations.","zh":"這個短語描述沙地形的逐步破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"time is running out","meaning":"時間所剩無幾","examples":[{"en":"Time is running out for the Gobero site.","zh":"Gobero 遺址時間所剩無幾。"},{"en":"Time is running out means there is little time left before action becomes impossible or too late.","zh":"time is running out 指在行動變得不可能或太遲之前，剩下時間很少。"},{"en":"Time is running out for students who have not started revising before an exam.","zh":"考試前仍未開始溫習的學生時間所剩無幾。"},{"en":"When a site is being destroyed by nature, researchers must work quickly.","zh":"當遺址正被自然力量破壞，研究者必須快速工作。"},{"en":"This phrase creates urgency.","zh":"這個短語營造迫切感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"archaeological site","meaning":"考古遺址","examples":[{"en":"Every archaeological site has a life cycle.","zh":"每個考古遺址都有生命周期。"},{"en":"An archaeological site is a place where evidence of past human activity is preserved.","zh":"archaeological site 指保存過去人類活動證據的地方。"},{"en":"Old villages, burial grounds, caves, and temples can all be archaeological sites.","zh":"古村落、墓地、洞穴和寺廟都可以是考古遺址。"},{"en":"Sites must be protected because digging, weather, and development can destroy evidence.","zh":"遺址必須受保護，因為挖掘、天氣和發展可以摧毀證據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a place studied by archaeologists.","zh":"這個短語指考古學家研究的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"life cycle","meaning":"生命周期","examples":[{"en":"Garcea says every archaeological site has a life cycle.","zh":"Garcea 說每個考古遺址都有生命周期。"},{"en":"A life cycle is the series of stages something goes through from beginning to end.","zh":"life cycle 指某物從開始到結束所經歷的一系列階段。"},{"en":"A school club has a life cycle when it is founded, grows, declines, and ends.","zh":"學會成立、成長、衰落和結束，就是一個生命周期。"},{"en":"Archaeological sites also change as people use them, abandon them, and nature damages them.","zh":"考古遺址也會隨着人們使用、棄用和自然破壞而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stages of existence.","zh":"這個短語描述存在的不同階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"disuse","meaning":"棄用；不再使用","examples":[{"en":"After people stop using a place, a period of disuse begins.","zh":"當人們停止使用一個地方後，棄用時期便開始。"},{"en":"Disuse means a state in which something is no longer used.","zh":"disuse 指某物不再被使用的狀態。"},{"en":"A playground may fall into disuse if children move to a new neighbourhood.","zh":"如果孩子搬到新社區，遊樂場可能被棄用。"},{"en":"During disuse, buildings, tools, or sites may decay because no one maintains them.","zh":"在棄用期間，建築、工具或遺址可能因無人維護而腐爛。"},{"en":"This word describes abandonment or lack of use.","zh":"這個字描述被放棄或不再使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"nature takes over","meaning":"大自然接管","examples":[{"en":"After disuse, nature takes over.","zh":"棄用之後，大自然接管。"},{"en":"Nature takes over means plants, weather, animals, and natural processes begin to control a place again.","zh":"nature takes over 指植物、天氣、動物和自然過程開始重新控制某地。"},{"en":"If an old playground is abandoned, weeds may grow and nature takes over.","zh":"如果舊遊樂場被棄用，雜草可能生長，大自然接管。"},{"en":"Natural processes can hide, damage, or destroy human-made structures.","zh":"自然過程可以隱藏、損壞或摧毀人造結構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes land returning to natural forces after human use stops.","zh":"這個短語描述人類停止使用後，土地回到自然力量之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"at the end of its life","meaning":"走到生命盡頭","examples":[{"en":"Gobero is at the end of its life.","zh":"Gobero 已走到生命盡頭。"},{"en":"At the end of its life means reaching the final stage before disappearing or becoming unusable.","zh":"at the end of its life 指到達消失或不能再使用前的最後階段。"},{"en":"An old school computer may be at the end of its life when it can no longer run basic programmes.","zh":"當舊學校電腦不能再運行基本程式，它可能已走到生命盡頭。"},{"en":"A site reaches this stage when erosion or damage threatens to erase it.","zh":"當侵蝕或破壞威脅抹去遺址，該遺址就到達這個階段。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a final and fragile stage.","zh":"這個短語描述最後而脆弱的階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether the statements agree with the information given.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與所給資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should choose TRUE only when the statement is supported by the text.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，只有陳述得到文本支持時，學生才應選 TRUE。"},{"en":"Personal knowledge does not matter if the passage gives different information.","zh":"如果文章提供不同資料，個人知識並不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in True, False, Not Given questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 True, False, Not Given 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章內容相反的意思。"},{"en":"If a passage says the team arrived in 2006, a statement saying 2005 contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說團隊於2006年抵達，而陳述說2005年，就與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be clear in the text, not guessed from outside knowledge.","zh":"矛盾必須在文本中清楚可見，而不是從外部知識猜出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a direct conflict with given facts.","zh":"這個短語描述與所給事實直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"The answer is not given if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果沒有這方面的資料，答案就是 not given。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not say anything about that point.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有提到該點。"},{"en":"If a passage names a researcher but not her age, there is no information on her age.","zh":"如果文章說出研究者名字但沒有說年齡，就沒有她年齡方面的資料。"},{"en":"Students should choose NOT GIVEN when evidence is missing.","zh":"當缺乏證據時，學生應選 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"This phrase warns students not to guess beyond the text.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生不要超出文本猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"accidentally found","meaning":"意外發現","examples":[{"en":"Hettwer accidentally found human remains in the desert.","zh":"Hettwer 在沙漠中意外發現人類遺骸。"},{"en":"Accidentally found means discovered by chance, not through a planned search.","zh":"accidentally found 指偶然發現，而不是透過計劃好的搜尋發現。"},{"en":"A student may accidentally find an old photo inside a library book.","zh":"學生可能在圖書館書中意外發現一張舊照片。"},{"en":"Accidental discoveries can still become important if people recognise their value.","zh":"意外發現如果被人看出價值，仍可以變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a chance discovery.","zh":"這個短語描述偶然發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"cooperate on archaeological projects","meaning":"合作進行考古項目","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Sereno and Garcea had cooperated on archaeological projects before.","zh":"題目問 Sereno 和 Garcea 以前是否曾合作進行考古項目。"},{"en":"To cooperate on archaeological projects means to work together on studies of ancient human sites or objects.","zh":"cooperate on archaeological projects 指共同研究古代人類遺址或物件。"},{"en":"Two universities may cooperate on archaeological projects by sharing experts and equipment.","zh":"兩間大學可能透過分享專家和設備合作進行考古項目。"},{"en":"Cooperation helps when a project needs different skills, such as excavation and bone analysis.","zh":"當項目需要不同技能，例如發掘和骨骼分析時，合作很有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes professional teamwork in archaeology.","zh":"這個短語描述考古學中的專業團隊合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"rock engravings","meaning":"岩石刻畫","examples":[{"en":"The question mentions rock engravings found in the Green Sahara.","zh":"題目提到在綠色撒哈拉發現的岩石刻畫。"},{"en":"Rock engravings are images or marks carved into stone surfaces.","zh":"rock engravings 指刻在石面上的圖像或痕跡。"},{"en":"Ancient people may make rock engravings of animals, people, or hunting scenes.","zh":"古人可能製作動物、人物或狩獵場面的岩石刻畫。"},{"en":"Engravings can preserve cultural memory even when buildings and tools disappear.","zh":"即使建築和工具消失，刻畫仍可保存文化記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to carved images, not paintings made with colour.","zh":"這個短語指雕刻圖像，而不是用顏料畫出的圖畫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be similar to","meaning":"與……相似","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether the engravings are similar to those found elsewhere.","zh":"題目問這些刻畫是否與其他地方發現的刻畫相似。"},{"en":"To be similar to something means to share features with it.","zh":"be similar to something 指與某物有共同特徵。"},{"en":"Two students’ essays may be similar to each other if they use the same examples and structure.","zh":"如果兩名學生的作文使用相同例子和結構，它們可能彼此相似。"},{"en":"Similarity can suggest connection, influence, or common conditions.","zh":"相似性可以暗示關聯、影響或共同條件。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for comparison.","zh":"這個短語用於比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"provide answers to","meaning":"回答……","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to provide answers to the questions below.","zh":"考生需要回答以下問題。"},{"en":"To provide answers to questions means to give the required responses.","zh":"provide answers to questions 指給出所需答案。"},{"en":"Students should provide answers to all parts of a worksheet before checking the key.","zh":"學生應先回答工作紙所有部分，再核對答案。"},{"en":"Clear answers help examiners see whether the student understood the text.","zh":"清楚答案幫助考官看出學生是否理解文本。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in test instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"no more than three words and/or a number","meaning":"不多於三個字及／或一個數字","examples":[{"en":"The answer should contain no more than three words and/or a number.","zh":"答案應包含不多於三個字及／或一個數字。"},{"en":"No more than three words and/or a number means the answer must be short and may include a number.","zh":"no more than three words and/or a number 指答案必須簡短，並可包括一個數字。"},{"en":"“three weeks” follows the rule, but “during the next three weeks” may be too long.","zh":"“three weeks” 符合規則，但 “during the next three weeks” 可能太長。"},{"en":"Word limits matter because extra words can make an answer wrong.","zh":"字數限制很重要，因為多寫字可能令答案錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict exam-answer limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格的考試答案限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"from the passage","meaning":"從文章中","examples":[{"en":"The answers must be taken from the passage.","zh":"答案必須從文章中取得。"},{"en":"From the passage means using words or information found in the reading text.","zh":"from the passage 指使用閱讀文本中的字詞或資料。"},{"en":"In IELTS reading, students should answer from the passage, not from memory.","zh":"在 IELTS 閱讀中，學生應從文章作答，而不是靠記憶。"},{"en":"This rule prevents students from adding outside knowledge.","zh":"這條規則防止學生加入外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds candidates to stay close to the text.","zh":"這個短語提醒考生緊扣文本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"initial weeks before excavation","meaning":"發掘前最初幾星期","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what was produced during the initial weeks before excavation.","zh":"題目問發掘前最初幾星期製作了甚麼。"},{"en":"Initial weeks before excavation means the first few weeks before digging began.","zh":"initial weeks before excavation 指正式挖掘開始前的最初幾星期。"},{"en":"Before a school renovation starts, the initial weeks may be used for planning and mapping.","zh":"學校翻新開始前，最初幾星期可能用於規劃和繪圖。"},{"en":"Early preparation helps teams avoid damaging evidence when excavation begins.","zh":"早期準備幫助團隊在發掘開始時避免破壞證據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the preparation stage before actual digging.","zh":"這個短語指實際挖掘前的準備階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"send something to the laboratory","meaning":"將某物送往實驗室","examples":[{"en":"Sereno sent teeth to the laboratory for dating.","zh":"Sereno 將牙齒送往實驗室作定年。"},{"en":"To send something to the laboratory means to deliver a sample for scientific testing.","zh":"send something to the laboratory 指把樣本送去作科學測試。"},{"en":"A doctor may send a throat sample to the laboratory to identify an infection.","zh":"醫生可能把喉嚨樣本送往實驗室，以識別感染。"},{"en":"Laboratory testing can provide information that field observation cannot.","zh":"實驗室測試可以提供野外觀察無法提供的資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving evidence to a place where it can be analysed.","zh":"這個短語描述把證據送到可分析的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"tightly bundled burials","meaning":"緊緊捆成一團的墓葬","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the age of the larger, tightly bundled burials.","zh":"題目問較大、緊緊捆成一團的墓葬的年代。"},{"en":"Tightly bundled burials are graves where bodies were placed in a compact folded or wrapped position.","zh":"tightly bundled burials 指屍體以緊密折起或包裹姿勢放置的墓葬。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may describe a burial as tightly bundled when the bones are close together.","zh":"當骨骼緊靠在一起，考古學家可能把墓葬描述為緊緊捆成一團。"},{"en":"Such body position can help distinguish one burial style from another.","zh":"這種身體姿勢可以幫助區分一種埋葬風格與另一種。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how the dead were arranged in the grave.","zh":"這個短語描述死者在墓中的安排方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"examine to determine","meaning":"檢驗以確定……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists examined teeth to determine genetic origins.","zh":"科學家檢驗牙齒以確定基因起源。"},{"en":"To examine something to determine something means to study it carefully in order to find out an answer.","zh":"examine something to determine something 指仔細研究某物，以找出答案。"},{"en":"A doctor may examine blood to determine whether a patient has an infection.","zh":"醫生可能檢驗血液，以確定病人是否感染。"},{"en":"Careful examination turns physical samples into useful information.","zh":"仔細檢驗可以把實體樣本轉化為有用資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes investigation with a clear purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述有明確目的的調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"complete the following summary","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to complete the following summary using words from the passage.","zh":"考生需要使用文章中的字詞完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the following summary means to fill blanks in a shortened version of the text.","zh":"complete the following summary 指填補文本簡短版本中的空格。"},{"en":"Students complete a summary by choosing words that fit both grammar and meaning.","zh":"學生透過選擇符合文法和意思的字詞來完成摘要。"},{"en":"This task checks whether readers understand the main information accurately.","zh":"這項任務檢查讀者是否準確理解主要資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading-exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"using no more than two words","meaning":"使用不多於兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should answer using no more than two words from the passage.","zh":"考生應使用文章中不多於兩個字作答。"},{"en":"Using no more than two words means the answer must contain one or two words only.","zh":"using no more than two words 指答案只能包含一個或兩個字。"},{"en":"If the answer is “human remains,” it fits the rule; adding extra words may make it wrong.","zh":"如果答案是 “human remains”，就符合規則；加入額外字詞可能令答案錯。"},{"en":"Word limits force students to choose the exact words needed.","zh":"字數限制迫使學生選擇所需的準確字詞。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict instruction about answer length.","zh":"這個短語給出關於答案長度的嚴格指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"judging from the bones","meaning":"根據骨骼判斷","examples":[{"en":"Judging from the bones, the Kiffian appeared to be peaceful people.","zh":"根據骨骼判斷，基菲安人看來是和平的人。"},{"en":"Judging from the bones means forming a conclusion based on evidence found in the skeletons.","zh":"judging from the bones 指根據骸骨中的證據得出結論。"},{"en":"Judging from a student’s handwriting and corrections, a teacher may see that the work was rushed.","zh":"根據學生筆跡和修改痕跡，老師可能看出功課做得很匆忙。"},{"en":"Bones can reveal injury, diet, muscle use, and sometimes lifestyle.","zh":"骨骼可以揭示受傷、飲食、肌肉使用，有時也揭示生活方式。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an inference from physical evidence.","zh":"這個短語引出從實體證據得出的推論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"appear to be","meaning":"看來是","examples":[{"en":"The Kiffian appeared to be peaceful and hardworking.","zh":"基菲安人看來是和平而勤勞的。"},{"en":"To appear to be means to seem to be, based on available evidence.","zh":"appear to be 指根據現有證據看起來是。"},{"en":"A student may appear to be confident, but still feel nervous inside.","zh":"學生可能看來很有信心，但內心仍緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase allows a careful judgement without claiming absolute certainty.","zh":"這個短語容許作出謹慎判斷，而不聲稱絕對確定。"},{"en":"It is useful when evidence suggests something but does not prove everything.","zh":"當證據暗示某事但未證明一切時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"no injuries were found","meaning":"沒有發現傷痕","examples":[{"en":"The summary mentions that no injuries were found on certain bones.","zh":"摘要提到某些骨頭上沒有發現傷痕。"},{"en":"No injuries were found means researchers did not see damage or wounds in the examined bones.","zh":"no injuries were found 指研究者在檢查的骨頭中沒有看到損傷或傷口。"},{"en":"If no injuries are found after a playground fall, the child may only need rest.","zh":"如果孩子在遊樂場跌倒後沒有發現傷痕，可能只需要休息。"},{"en":"In archaeology, absence of injury can suggest limited violence or accidents.","zh":"在考古學中，缺少傷痕可以暗示暴力或意外較少。"},{"en":"This phrase reports a negative finding from examination.","zh":"這個短語報告檢查中的陰性發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"heads or forearms","meaning":"頭部或前臂","examples":[{"en":"The summary refers to injuries on heads or forearms.","zh":"摘要提到頭部或前臂上的傷痕。"},{"en":"Heads or forearms means the skull area or the lower part of the arms.","zh":"heads or forearms 指頭骨區域或手臂下半部分。"},{"en":"In a fight, people may receive injuries on heads or forearms while attacking or defending themselves.","zh":"打鬥中，人們可能在攻擊或自衛時頭部或前臂受傷。"},{"en":"These body areas are useful because they can show signs of violence.","zh":"這些身體部位有用，因為它們可以顯示暴力跡象。"},{"en":"This phrase names specific parts of the body.","zh":"這個短語指出特定身體部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"diet contained plenty of","meaning":"飲食含有大量……","examples":[{"en":"Their diet contained plenty of protein.","zh":"他們的飲食含有大量蛋白質。"},{"en":"If a diet contained plenty of something, that food or nutrient was present in large amounts.","zh":"diet contained plenty of something 指某種食物或營養在飲食中大量存在。"},{"en":"A child’s diet may contain plenty of fruit if the family eats apples and bananas daily.","zh":"如果家庭每天吃蘋果和香蕉，孩子的飲食可能含有大量水果。"},{"en":"Protein-rich diets can support muscle growth and repair.","zh":"富含蛋白質的飲食可以支持肌肉生長和修復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what a person regularly ate.","zh":"這個短語描述一個人經常吃甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"by contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"By contrast, the Tenerian seemed to have a less strenuous lifestyle.","zh":"相比之下，特內里安人似乎有較不費力的生活方式。"},{"en":"By contrast means compared with what was just mentioned, the next point is different.","zh":"by contrast 指與剛才提到的相比，下一點不同。"},{"en":"Some students like group work; by contrast, others prefer quiet individual study.","zh":"有些學生喜歡小組工作；相比之下，另一些學生偏好安靜個人學習。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers see a clear difference between two groups or ideas.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者看見兩個群體或想法之間的清楚差異。"},{"en":"It is useful in comparison writing.","zh":"它適合用於比較寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"prefer something to something","meaning":"較喜歡……而非……","examples":[{"en":"Stojanowski believed the Tenerian preferred herding to hunting.","zh":"Stojanowski 認為特內里安人較喜歡放牧而非狩獵。"},{"en":"To prefer A to B means to like or choose A more than B.","zh":"prefer A to B 指比起 B 更喜歡或選擇 A。"},{"en":"A student may prefer reading to watching videos when revising vocabulary.","zh":"學生溫習詞彙時可能較喜歡閱讀而非看影片。"},{"en":"Preference can reflect habit, need, environment, or personal choice.","zh":"偏好可以反映習慣、需要、環境或個人選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly compares two options.","zh":"這個短語清楚比較兩個選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"only a few bones from","meaning":"只有少量來自……的骨頭","examples":[{"en":"Only a few bones from herd animals were found.","zh":"只有少量來自畜群動物的骨頭被發現。"},{"en":"Only a few bones from something means just a small number of bones belonging to that group were discovered.","zh":"only a few bones from something 指只發現屬於該群體的少量骨頭。"},{"en":"If only a few books from a class set are missing, most students returned theirs.","zh":"如果一套班書只有少量遺失，代表大多數學生都交還了。"},{"en":"Small quantities can make researchers cautious about drawing strong conclusions.","zh":"數量少會令研究者對作出強結論更謹慎。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses limited evidence.","zh":"這個短語強調證據有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"lead someone to suggest","meaning":"令某人提出","examples":[{"en":"The limited evidence led Sereno to suggest another possibility.","zh":"有限證據令 Sereno 提出另一種可能性。"},{"en":"To lead someone to suggest something means to cause that person to propose an idea.","zh":"lead someone to suggest something 指令某人提出某個想法。"},{"en":"Repeated absences may lead a teacher to suggest that a student needs support.","zh":"反覆缺席可能令老師提出學生需要支援。"},{"en":"Evidence can lead researchers to suggest a new explanation when the old one seems incomplete.","zh":"當舊解釋似乎不完整，證據可以令研究者提出新解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase connects evidence with a proposed conclusion.","zh":"這個短語把證據與提出的結論連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"at the time","meaning":"當時","examples":[{"en":"The Tenerian may have been a transitional group at the time.","zh":"特內里安人當時可能是一個過渡群體。"},{"en":"At the time means during that particular period in the past.","zh":"at the time 指在過去那個特定時期。"},{"en":"A student may not have understood the rule at the time, but later realised its purpose.","zh":"學生當時可能不明白規則，但後來理解其目的。"},{"en":"This phrase places a statement in a specific historical or personal moment.","zh":"這個短語把某說法放在特定歷史或個人時刻中。"},{"en":"It helps avoid confusing past conditions with present ones.","zh":"它有助避免把過去情況與現在情況混淆。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 128 - Human remain in Green Sahara.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 129":[{"front":"the bite that heals","meaning":"具有療效的咬傷","examples":[{"en":"The passage explores the idea of the bite that heals.","zh":"文章探討具有療效的咬傷這個概念。"},{"en":"The bite that heals refers to the surprising idea that venom from a bite or sting may lead to medical treatment.","zh":"the bite that heals 指一個令人驚訝的想法：來自咬傷或螫傷的毒液可能帶來醫療用途。"},{"en":"A science teacher may use the bite that heals to show students that dangerous substances can sometimes inspire medicines.","zh":"科學老師可能用具有療效的咬傷來向學生展示，危險物質有時可以啟發藥物研發。"},{"en":"This idea is surprising because venom can harm the body, yet some venom compounds may help researchers treat disease.","zh":"這個概念令人驚訝，因為毒液可以傷害身體，但某些毒液化合物可能幫助研究人員治療疾病。"},{"en":"The phrase should not mean people should seek bites; it means scientists can study venom safely for medicine.","zh":"這個短語不是指人們應主動尋求被咬，而是指科學家可以安全研究毒液作醫學用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"unlock the medical potential of","meaning":"發掘……的醫學潛力","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are unlocking the medical potential of venom.","zh":"科學家正在發掘毒液的醫學潛力。"},{"en":"To unlock the medical potential of something means to discover how it can be used to treat illness or improve health.","zh":"unlock the medical potential of something 指發現某物如何可用於治療疾病或改善健康。"},{"en":"Researchers may unlock the medical potential of sea plants by testing whether their chemicals fight infection.","zh":"研究人員可能透過測試海洋植物的化學物質是否能對抗感染，來發掘其醫學潛力。"},{"en":"Careful study can unlock medical potential because useful effects may be hidden inside dangerous substances.","zh":"仔細研究可以發掘醫學潛力，因為有用效果可能隱藏在危險物質之中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes scientific discovery, not casual use at home.","zh":"這個短語描述科學發現，而不是在家中隨便使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"medical potential","meaning":"醫學潛力","examples":[{"en":"Venom may have significant medical potential.","zh":"毒液可能具有重要醫學潛力。"},{"en":"Medical potential is the possibility that something may become useful in medicine.","zh":"medical potential 指某物有可能在醫學上變得有用。"},{"en":"A plant extract has medical potential if early tests show that it may reduce pain or infection.","zh":"如果早期測試顯示某種植物萃取物可能減輕疼痛或感染，它就有醫學潛力。"},{"en":"Medical potential must be tested carefully before a substance can become a safe treatment.","zh":"醫學潛力必須經過仔細測試，某物質才可以成為安全治療。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests promise, not proof that something is already a medicine.","zh":"這個短語表示有前景，而不是證明某物已經是藥物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"venom","meaning":"毒液","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are studying venom for possible medical uses.","zh":"科學家正在研究毒液可能的醫學用途。"},{"en":"Venom is a toxic substance injected by animals such as snakes, spiders, scorpions, or jellyfish.","zh":"venom 指蛇、蜘蛛、蠍子或水母等動物注入體內的有毒物質。"},{"en":"A doctor treating a snakebite needs to know what kind of venom entered the patient’s body.","zh":"醫生治療蛇咬時，需要知道哪種毒液進入了病人體內。"},{"en":"Venom can harm nerves, blood, muscles, or tissues, so bites and stings need serious attention.","zh":"毒液可以傷害神經、血液、肌肉或組織，因此咬傷和螫傷需要認真處理。"},{"en":"Although venom is dangerous, its molecules can teach scientists how the body works.","zh":"雖然毒液危險，但其分子可以教科學家了解身體如何運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"go for a swim","meaning":"去游水","examples":[{"en":"Michael decided to go for a swim during his vacation.","zh":"Michael 在度假期間決定去游水。"},{"en":"To go for a swim means to enter water and swim for exercise, relaxation, or enjoyment.","zh":"go for a swim 指下水游泳作運動、放鬆或娛樂。"},{"en":"After a hot school sports day, some students may go for a swim at the public pool.","zh":"炎熱的學校運動日後，有些學生可能到公眾泳池去游水。"},{"en":"People often go for a swim to cool down, but they should check that the water is safe first.","zh":"人們常去游水降溫，但應先確認水域安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a casual swimming activity, not a professional race.","zh":"這個短語描述輕鬆的游泳活動，而不是專業比賽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on vacation with","meaning":"與……一起度假","examples":[{"en":"Michael was on vacation with his family in Mexico.","zh":"Michael 與家人在墨西哥一起度假。"},{"en":"To be on vacation with someone means to travel or rest away from normal work or school together.","zh":"be on vacation with someone 指與某人一起離開日常工作或學校去旅行或休息。"},{"en":"A child may be on vacation with her grandparents during the summer holiday.","zh":"孩子可能在暑假與祖父母一起度假。"},{"en":"Being on vacation with family can create happy memories, but unexpected accidents can still happen.","zh":"與家人一起度假可以創造美好回憶，但意外仍可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase tells us who accompanies someone during a holiday.","zh":"這個短語告訴我們某人度假時與誰同行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hotter than blazes","meaning":"熱得要命","examples":[{"en":"It was hotter than blazes in Guerrero, Mexico.","zh":"墨西哥 Guerrero 熱得要命。"},{"en":"Hotter than blazes means extremely hot.","zh":"hotter than blazes 指極度炎熱。"},{"en":"A classroom without fans can feel hotter than blazes on a summer afternoon.","zh":"夏日下午沒有風扇的課室可以熱得要命。"},{"en":"When it is hotter than blazes, people may look for shade, cold drinks, or a swimming pool.","zh":"當天氣熱得要命，人們可能尋找陰涼處、凍飲或泳池。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and stronger than simply saying “very hot”.","zh":"這個短語較口語，比單純說 “very hot” 更強烈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"swimming trunks","meaning":"男裝泳褲","examples":[{"en":"Michael grabbed his swimming trunks from a chair.","zh":"Michael 從椅子上拿起男裝泳褲。"},{"en":"Swimming trunks are shorts worn by men or boys for swimming.","zh":"swimming trunks 指男性或男孩游泳時穿的短泳褲。"},{"en":"A student may pack swimming trunks for a school swimming lesson.","zh":"學生可能為學校游泳課帶備男裝泳褲。"},{"en":"If swimming trunks are left outside, insects or small animals may hide inside them.","zh":"如果男裝泳褲放在戶外，昆蟲或小動物可能躲在裡面。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to swimwear, not ordinary shorts for daily clothing.","zh":"這個短語指泳裝，而不是日常穿着的普通短褲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"slide something on","meaning":"穿上……","examples":[{"en":"He slid his swimming trunks on and jumped into the pool.","zh":"他穿上男裝泳褲，然後跳進泳池。"},{"en":"To slide something on means to put clothing on quickly and smoothly.","zh":"slide something on 指快速而順手地穿上衣物。"},{"en":"A child may slide on a jacket before running to catch the school bus.","zh":"孩子可能在趕校巴前快速穿上外套。"},{"en":"People slide clothes on quickly when they are in a hurry, so they may not check them carefully.","zh":"人們匆忙時會快速穿上衣物，因此未必仔細檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for clothes that can be pulled on easily.","zh":"這個短語常用於容易拉上身的衣物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"instead of","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Instead of cool relief, Michael felt a burning pain.","zh":"Michael 感到的不是涼快舒緩，而是灼痛。"},{"en":"Instead of means in place of something expected or chosen.","zh":"instead of 指取代某個預期或選擇的事物。"},{"en":"Instead of taking the bus, a student may walk home to save money.","zh":"學生可能步行回家，而不是乘巴士，以節省金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase shows contrast between what was expected and what actually happened.","zh":"這個短語顯示預期情況與實際發生之事的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when one result replaces another.","zh":"當一個結果取代另一個結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cool relief","meaning":"涼快舒緩的感覺","examples":[{"en":"Michael expected cool relief when he jumped into the pool.","zh":"Michael 跳進泳池時期待涼快舒緩的感覺。"},{"en":"Cool relief is the pleasant feeling of becoming cooler and more comfortable after heat or discomfort.","zh":"cool relief 指在炎熱或不適後變得較涼和較舒服的愉快感覺。"},{"en":"After walking home in the sun, a cold drink can bring cool relief.","zh":"在烈日下走路回家後，一杯凍飲可以帶來涼快舒緩的感覺。"},{"en":"People seek cool relief when heat makes them tired, sweaty, or uncomfortable.","zh":"當炎熱令人疲倦、流汗或不舒服，人們會尋求涼快舒緩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical comfort that comes from cooling down.","zh":"這個短語描述由降溫帶來的身體舒適感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"burning pain","meaning":"灼痛","examples":[{"en":"A burning pain ripped through the back of his thigh.","zh":"一陣灼痛猛烈襲向他的大腿後側。"},{"en":"Burning pain is pain that feels hot, sharp, or like the skin is being burned.","zh":"burning pain 指感覺像發熱、刺痛或皮膚被燒的疼痛。"},{"en":"A person may feel burning pain after touching a hot pan or being stung by an insect.","zh":"人碰到熱鍋或被昆蟲螫傷後，可能感到灼痛。"},{"en":"Burning pain can make someone panic because it feels intense and sudden.","zh":"灼痛可以令人驚慌，因為它強烈又突然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the quality of the pain, not the actual cause.","zh":"這個短語描述疼痛的感覺，而不一定描述真正原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rip through","meaning":"猛烈穿過；劇痛襲來","examples":[{"en":"A burning pain ripped through the back of his thigh.","zh":"一陣灼痛猛烈襲向他的大腿後側。"},{"en":"To rip through something means to move through it violently, suddenly, or intensely.","zh":"rip through something 指猛烈、突然或強烈地穿過某物。"},{"en":"A loud scream ripped through the classroom when the fire alarm went off.","zh":"火警鐘響起時，一聲尖叫劃破課室。"},{"en":"When pain rips through the body, it feels sudden and difficult to ignore.","zh":"當疼痛猛烈襲過身體，它會感覺突然且難以忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the movement or feeling sound forceful and dramatic.","zh":"這個短語令動作或感覺聽起來強烈而戲劇化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the back of his thigh","meaning":"大腿後側","examples":[{"en":"The sting caused pain in the back of his thigh.","zh":"螫傷令他的大腿後側疼痛。"},{"en":"The back of his thigh is the rear part of the upper leg between the hip and the knee.","zh":"the back of his thigh 指臀部與膝蓋之間的大腿後方部分。"},{"en":"A runner may stretch the back of his thigh before training to avoid injury.","zh":"跑手訓練前可能伸展大腿後側以避免受傷。"},{"en":"Pain in the back of the thigh can make walking, sitting, or climbing stairs difficult.","zh":"大腿後側疼痛可以令走路、坐下或上樓梯變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the exact body area affected.","zh":"這個短語指出受影響的確切身體部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tear off","meaning":"急忙脫下","examples":[{"en":"Michael tore off his swimming trunks after feeling the pain.","zh":"Michael 感到疼痛後急忙脫下男裝泳褲。"},{"en":"To tear off clothing means to remove it very quickly, often because of fear, pain, or urgency.","zh":"tear off clothing 指非常快速地脫下衣物，常因恐懼、疼痛或急迫。"},{"en":"A child may tear off a sweater if a bee gets trapped inside it.","zh":"如果蜜蜂困在毛衣裡，孩子可能急忙脫下毛衣。"},{"en":"People tear off clothing when they think something dangerous is touching their skin.","zh":"當人們以為有危險東西接觸皮膚，就會急忙脫下衣物。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests sudden, panicked removal.","zh":"這個短語暗示突然、驚慌地脫下。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"leap from","meaning":"從……跳出","examples":[{"en":"He leaped naked from the pool.","zh":"他赤身露體地從泳池跳出來。"},{"en":"To leap from somewhere means to jump quickly out of or away from that place.","zh":"leap from somewhere 指快速從某地方跳出或跳離。"},{"en":"A student may leap from a chair if they see a cockroach nearby.","zh":"如果學生看見附近有曱甴，可能從椅子上跳起來。"},{"en":"People often leap from danger before they stop to think clearly.","zh":"人們常在清楚思考前先從危險中跳開。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a sudden and energetic jump.","zh":"這個短語暗示突然且有力的跳躍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"his leg on fire","meaning":"他的腿像火燒般痛","examples":[{"en":"Michael felt as if his leg was on fire.","zh":"Michael 感到他的腿像火燒般痛。"},{"en":"If someone feels their leg is on fire, the pain feels extremely hot and intense.","zh":"如果某人覺得腿像火燒般痛，表示疼痛極熱、極強烈。"},{"en":"After a bad insect sting, a child may say their arm feels on fire.","zh":"嚴重昆蟲螫傷後，孩子可能說手臂像火燒般痛。"},{"en":"This expression is used when pain burns so strongly that it feels unbearable.","zh":"當疼痛灼熱得令人難以忍受時，會使用這個說法。"},{"en":"It is a metaphor for burning pain, not a literal fire.","zh":"這是形容灼痛的比喻，不是真的着火。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tread water","meaning":"踩水；在水中保持浮起","examples":[{"en":"A small yellow creature was treading water behind him.","zh":"一隻細小黃色生物在他身後踩水。"},{"en":"To tread water means to stay floating upright in water by moving the arms and legs.","zh":"tread water 指透過移動手腳，在水中直立保持浮起。"},{"en":"A swimming coach teaches beginners to tread water so they can stay safe in deep water.","zh":"游泳教練教初學者踩水，使他們在深水中保持安全。"},{"en":"If someone can tread water, they can keep their head above water while waiting for help.","zh":"如果某人能踩水，就能在等待救援時保持頭部在水面上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes staying afloat rather than swimming forward.","zh":"這個短語描述保持浮起，而不是向前游。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"scoop something into","meaning":"把某物舀進……","examples":[{"en":"He scooped the creature into a container.","zh":"他把那隻生物舀進一個容器。"},{"en":"To scoop something into a container means to lift or gather it and put it inside.","zh":"scoop something into a container 指把某物舀起或收集起來，放入容器中。"},{"en":"A child may scoop sand into a bucket at the beach.","zh":"孩子可能在沙灘把沙舀進水桶。"},{"en":"Scooping a small animal into a container can help people identify it safely without touching it.","zh":"把小動物舀進容器，可以幫助人安全辨認牠而不直接觸摸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a careful lifting-and-placing action.","zh":"這個短語描述小心舀起並放入的動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"caretaker of the house","meaning":"房子的看管人","examples":[{"en":"The caretaker of the house rushed Michael to the local Red Cross facility.","zh":"房子的看管人急忙把 Michael 送到當地紅十字會設施。"},{"en":"The caretaker of the house is the person responsible for looking after the property.","zh":"caretaker of the house 指負責照看該物業的人。"},{"en":"A caretaker of a holiday house may check rooms, repair small problems, and help guests.","zh":"度假屋看管人可能檢查房間、修理小問題並幫助住客。"},{"en":"If an emergency happens, a caretaker may know the nearest clinic or hospital.","zh":"如果發生緊急情況，看管人可能知道最近的診所或醫院。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the person managing or watching over a house.","zh":"這個短語指管理或看守房子的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rush someone to","meaning":"急忙送某人到……","examples":[{"en":"The caretaker rushed Michael to the local Red Cross facility.","zh":"看管人急忙把 Michael 送到當地紅十字會設施。"},{"en":"To rush someone to a place means to take them there quickly because the situation is urgent.","zh":"rush someone to a place 指因情況緊急而快速把某人送到某地。"},{"en":"A parent may rush a child to hospital after a serious allergic reaction.","zh":"孩子出現嚴重過敏反應後，家長可能急忙把孩子送院。"},{"en":"People rush someone to medical care when waiting could make the condition worse.","zh":"當等待可能令病情惡化，人們會急忙把某人送去接受醫療。"},{"en":"This phrase shows speed, urgency, and concern.","zh":"這個短語顯示速度、緊急和關心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"local Red Cross facility","meaning":"當地紅十字會設施","examples":[{"en":"Doctors at the local Red Cross facility identified the scorpion.","zh":"當地紅十字會設施的醫生辨認出那隻蠍子。"},{"en":"A local Red Cross facility is a nearby medical or emergency-help centre connected with the Red Cross.","zh":"local Red Cross facility 指附近與紅十字會相關的醫療或緊急援助中心。"},{"en":"Travellers may visit a local Red Cross facility if they need urgent help in an unfamiliar town.","zh":"旅客在陌生城鎮需要緊急幫助時，可能前往當地紅十字會設施。"},{"en":"Such facilities can provide first aid, emergency support, or referral to further care.","zh":"這類設施可以提供急救、緊急支援或轉介進一步護理。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a nearby aid centre, not a large private hospital necessarily.","zh":"這個短語指附近援助中心，不一定是大型私家醫院。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"identify his attacker","meaning":"辨認出襲擊他的生物","examples":[{"en":"Doctors immediately identified his attacker as a bark scorpion.","zh":"醫生立即辨認出襲擊他的生物是一隻樹皮蠍。"},{"en":"To identify his attacker means to find out what creature or person caused the injury.","zh":"identify his attacker 指查明是哪種生物或人物造成傷害。"},{"en":"After a dog bite, doctors may identify the attacker to decide whether rabies treatment is needed.","zh":"狗咬後，醫生可能辨認襲擊者，以決定是否需要狂犬病治療。"},{"en":"Identifying the attacker helps medical staff choose the right treatment.","zh":"辨認出襲擊來源幫助醫護人員選擇正確治療。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when knowing the source of harm matters.","zh":"當知道傷害來源很重要時，就會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"bark scorpion","meaning":"樹皮蠍","examples":[{"en":"A bark scorpion had stung Michael.","zh":"一隻樹皮蠍螫傷了 Michael。"},{"en":"A bark scorpion is a type of scorpion known for a painful and potentially dangerous sting.","zh":"bark scorpion 指一種以疼痛且可能危險的螫傷聞名的蠍子。"},{"en":"Travellers in desert regions should shake out shoes and clothes in case a bark scorpion is hiding inside.","zh":"到沙漠地區旅行的人應抖一抖鞋和衣服，以防樹皮蠍躲在裡面。"},{"en":"A bark scorpion sting can require medical care because venom affects nerves and causes severe pain.","zh":"樹皮蠍螫傷可能需要醫療護理，因為毒液影響神經並造成劇痛。"},{"en":"This phrase names the specific creature responsible for the sting.","zh":"這個短語命名造成螫傷的特定生物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"venomous species","meaning":"有毒物種","examples":[{"en":"The bark scorpion is one of the most venomous species in North America.","zh":"樹皮蠍是北美最有毒的物種之一。"},{"en":"A venomous species is an animal species that can inject venom through a bite, sting, or specialised body part.","zh":"venomous species 指能透過咬、螫或特化身體部位注入毒液的動物物種。"},{"en":"Some snakes, spiders, scorpions, and jellyfish are venomous species.","zh":"有些蛇、蜘蛛、蠍子和水母都是有毒物種。"},{"en":"Venomous species can be dangerous because their toxins may affect blood, nerves, or muscles.","zh":"有毒物種可能危險，因為其毒素可能影響血液、神經或肌肉。"},{"en":"This phrase should not be confused with poisonous species, which harm when touched or eaten.","zh":"這個短語不應與 poisonous species 混淆，後者指被觸摸或吞食時造成傷害的物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fierce pain","meaning":"劇痛","examples":[{"en":"The fierce pain from a scorpion sting can be followed by electric shocks.","zh":"蠍子螫傷造成的劇痛之後可能出現電擊般感覺。"},{"en":"Fierce pain is very strong, sharp, and difficult to bear.","zh":"fierce pain 指非常強烈、尖銳且難以忍受的疼痛。"},{"en":"A broken bone may cause fierce pain when the injured person tries to move.","zh":"骨折者嘗試移動時可能感到劇痛。"},{"en":"Fierce pain can make someone seek help immediately because it feels alarming.","zh":"劇痛會令人立即尋求幫助，因為感覺令人警覺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intense pain, not mild discomfort.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈疼痛，而不是輕微不適。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"scorpion sting","meaning":"蠍子螫傷","examples":[{"en":"A scorpion sting can cause fierce pain.","zh":"蠍子螫傷可以造成劇痛。"},{"en":"A scorpion sting is an injury caused when a scorpion injects venom with its stinger.","zh":"scorpion sting 指蠍子用螫針注入毒液所造成的傷害。"},{"en":"A camper may suffer a scorpion sting if they put a hand near rocks without looking.","zh":"露營者若未看清就把手伸近石頭，可能遭受蠍子螫傷。"},{"en":"A scorpion sting can cause pain, swelling, numbness, or more serious symptoms.","zh":"蠍子螫傷可以造成疼痛、腫脹、麻木或更嚴重症狀。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the injury, not the animal itself.","zh":"這個短語指傷害，而不是蠍子本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be followed by","meaning":"隨後出現……","examples":[{"en":"The fierce pain is typically followed by electric shocks.","zh":"劇痛通常隨後出現電擊般感覺。"},{"en":"To be followed by something means that another event or feeling comes after it.","zh":"be followed by something 指另一事件或感覺在其後出現。"},{"en":"A loud thunderclap may be followed by heavy rain.","zh":"一聲巨雷之後可能隨後出現大雨。"},{"en":"Doctors ask what symptoms are followed by others to understand how a condition develops.","zh":"醫生會問哪些症狀之後出現其他症狀，以了解病情如何發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sequence: first one thing happens, then another.","zh":"這個短語描述先後次序：先發生一件事，然後另一件事發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what feels like","meaning":"感覺像……的東西","examples":[{"en":"Victims may feel what feels like electric shocks.","zh":"受害者可能感到像電擊一樣的感覺。"},{"en":"What feels like means the sensation is similar to something, even if it is not exactly that thing.","zh":"what feels like 指感覺類似某事，即使不完全就是那事。"},{"en":"A person with a trapped nerve may feel what feels like pins in the arm.","zh":"神經受壓的人可能感到手臂像被針刺一樣。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe sensations that are hard to explain directly.","zh":"這個短語幫助描述難以直接解釋的感覺。"},{"en":"It compares the feeling with something familiar.","zh":"它把感覺與熟悉事物作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"electric shocks","meaning":"電擊","examples":[{"en":"The sting can cause sensations like electric shocks.","zh":"螫傷可以造成像電擊一樣的感覺。"},{"en":"Electric shocks are sudden painful feelings like electricity passing through the body.","zh":"electric shocks 指像電流穿過身體般突然且疼痛的感覺。"},{"en":"Someone may feel electric shocks in the hand after touching a faulty plug.","zh":"某人碰到故障插頭後，可能感到手部電擊。"},{"en":"When venom affects nerves, victims may describe the pain as electric shocks.","zh":"當毒液影響神經，受害者可能把疼痛形容為電擊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sharp nerve-like pain, not always real electricity.","zh":"這個短語描述尖銳的神經痛，不一定是真正電流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rack the body","meaning":"使全身劇痛；折磨身體","examples":[{"en":"Electric shocks seemed to rack Michael’s body.","zh":"電擊般感覺似乎折磨 Michael 的全身。"},{"en":"To rack the body means to cause severe pain or distress throughout the body.","zh":"rack the body 指令全身承受嚴重疼痛或痛苦。"},{"en":"A high fever can rack the body with chills and aching muscles.","zh":"高燒可以以寒顫和肌肉痠痛折磨全身。"},{"en":"When pain racks the body, the person may be unable to rest or move normally.","zh":"當疼痛折磨身體，患者可能無法休息或正常移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intense suffering affecting the whole body.","zh":"這個短語描述影響全身的強烈痛苦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"occasionally victims die","meaning":"偶爾會有受害者死亡","examples":[{"en":"Occasionally victims die after being stung by this scorpion.","zh":"被這種蠍子螫傷後，偶爾會有受害者死亡。"},{"en":"Occasionally victims die means death happens sometimes, though not in most cases.","zh":"occasionally victims die 指死亡有時會發生，雖然不是大多數情況。"},{"en":"Occasionally patients die from severe allergic reactions if treatment is delayed.","zh":"如果治療延誤，偶爾會有病人因嚴重過敏反應死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a risk is rare but serious.","zh":"這個短語提醒風險罕見但嚴重。"},{"en":"It reminds readers that even uncommon outcomes should be taken seriously.","zh":"它提醒讀者，即使不常見的後果也應認真看待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"luckily for","meaning":"對……來說幸運的是","examples":[{"en":"Luckily for Michael, antivenom was readily available.","zh":"對 Michael 來說幸運的是，抗毒血清很容易取得。"},{"en":"Luckily for someone means that something fortunate happened for that person.","zh":"luckily for someone 指對某人而言有幸運的事情發生。"},{"en":"Luckily for the student, the lost wallet was found before the bus arrived.","zh":"對學生來說幸運的是，丟失的錢包在巴士到達前被找回。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a positive turn in a dangerous or difficult situation.","zh":"這個短語引入危險或困難情況中的正面轉折。"},{"en":"It often shows that the outcome could have been worse.","zh":"它常顯示結果本來可能更糟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ask someone not to","meaning":"要求某人不要……","examples":[{"en":"Michael asked the writer not to give his full name.","zh":"Michael 要求作者不要透露他的全名。"},{"en":"To ask someone not to do something means to request that they avoid a particular action.","zh":"ask someone not to do something 指要求某人避免某個行動。"},{"en":"A student may ask a teacher not to share private family problems with the class.","zh":"學生可能要求老師不要在班上分享私人家庭問題。"},{"en":"People ask others not to reveal information when privacy matters.","zh":"當私隱重要時，人們會要求別人不要透露資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a polite or direct request to prevent an action.","zh":"這個短語描述禮貌或直接地要求阻止某行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"full name","meaning":"全名","examples":[{"en":"Michael asked the writer not to give his full name.","zh":"Michael 要求作者不要透露他的全名。"},{"en":"A full name is a person’s complete name, usually including first name and surname.","zh":"full name 指一個人的完整姓名，通常包括名字和姓氏。"},{"en":"A school form may ask for a student’s full name to avoid confusion.","zh":"學校表格可能要求學生填寫全名，以避免混淆。"},{"en":"People may avoid giving their full name when a story involves private medical information.","zh":"當故事涉及私人醫療資料，人們可能避免提供全名。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to complete identification, not just a nickname.","zh":"這個短語指完整身份識別，而不只是暱稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"common in the area","meaning":"在該區常見","examples":[{"en":"The bark scorpion is common in the area.","zh":"樹皮蠍在該區常見。"},{"en":"Common in the area means often found in that place.","zh":"common in the area 指經常在該地方找到。"},{"en":"Mosquitoes are common in the area near the wet market after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，街市附近一帶蚊子常見。"},{"en":"If a dangerous animal is common in the area, local clinics may prepare suitable treatment.","zh":"如果危險動物在該區常見，當地診所可能準備合適治療。"},{"en":"This phrase describes local frequency or presence.","zh":"這個短語描述本地出現頻率或存在情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"antivenom","meaning":"抗毒血清","examples":[{"en":"Antivenom was readily available in the area.","zh":"該區很容易取得抗毒血清。"},{"en":"Antivenom is a medical treatment that helps neutralise venom after a bite or sting.","zh":"antivenom 指在咬傷或螫傷後幫助中和毒液的醫療治療。"},{"en":"A hospital in a snakebite-prone region may keep antivenom in emergency storage.","zh":"蛇咬高發地區的醫院可能在緊急儲備中保存抗毒血清。"},{"en":"Antivenom can reduce danger when it is given quickly and correctly by medical staff.","zh":"當醫護人員快速而正確地使用抗毒血清，它可以降低危險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a medical product, not a home remedy.","zh":"這個短語指醫療產品，而不是家居偏方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"readily available","meaning":"隨時可取得；容易獲得","examples":[{"en":"The antivenom was readily available.","zh":"抗毒血清很容易取得。"},{"en":"Readily available means easy to obtain or access when needed.","zh":"readily available 指需要時容易取得或使用。"},{"en":"Clean drinking water should be readily available in schools during hot weather.","zh":"炎熱天氣時，學校應隨時可取得清潔飲用水。"},{"en":"When emergency medicine is readily available, patients can be treated faster.","zh":"當急救藥物容易取得，病人可以更快接受治療。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that can be obtained without long delay.","zh":"這個短語描述不需長時間等待即可取得的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have an injection","meaning":"接受注射","examples":[{"en":"Michael had an injection and was released a few hours later.","zh":"Michael 接受注射，數小時後獲准離開。"},{"en":"To have an injection means to receive medicine through a needle.","zh":"have an injection 指透過針筒接受藥物。"},{"en":"A child may have an injection at a clinic before travelling abroad.","zh":"孩子出國旅行前可能在診所接受注射。"},{"en":"Injections can deliver medicine quickly when tablets would be too slow or unsuitable.","zh":"當藥片太慢或不合適，注射可以快速輸送藥物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving medical treatment by needle.","zh":"這個短語描述透過針筒接受醫療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be released","meaning":"獲准離開","examples":[{"en":"Michael was released a few hours later.","zh":"Michael 數小時後獲准離開。"},{"en":"To be released from a medical facility means to be allowed to leave after treatment or observation.","zh":"be released from a medical facility 指在治療或觀察後獲准離開醫療設施。"},{"en":"A patient may be released from hospital when the doctor believes they are stable.","zh":"當醫生認為病人情況穩定，病人可能獲准離開醫院。"},{"en":"Being released does not always mean full recovery; it may mean the immediate danger has passed.","zh":"獲准離開不一定代表完全康復；可能只是即時危險已過。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official permission to leave.","zh":"這個短語描述正式獲准離開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a few hours later","meaning":"數小時後","examples":[{"en":"He was released a few hours later.","zh":"他數小時後獲准離開。"},{"en":"A few hours later means after a short period of several hours.","zh":"a few hours later 指幾個小時之後的一段短時間後。"},{"en":"A student visited the clinic in the morning and returned to class a few hours later.","zh":"學生早上去診所，數小時後回到課室。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the next event happened on the same day, not much later.","zh":"這個短語顯示下一件事在同一天發生，沒有隔很久。"},{"en":"It is useful for telling a simple sequence of events.","zh":"它適合用來敘述簡單事件次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the pain was gone","meaning":"疼痛消失了","examples":[{"en":"In about 30 hours, the pain was gone.","zh":"大約 30 小時後，疼痛消失了。"},{"en":"The pain was gone means the person no longer felt pain.","zh":"the pain was gone 指某人不再感到疼痛。"},{"en":"After resting for two days, the student’s headache was gone.","zh":"休息兩天後，學生的頭痛消失了。"},{"en":"When pain is gone, a person may move, sleep, and work more normally.","zh":"當疼痛消失，人可以較正常地活動、睡眠和工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relief after discomfort has ended.","zh":"這個短語描述不適結束後的舒緩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"could not have been predicted","meaning":"本來無法預測","examples":[{"en":"What happened next could not have been predicted.","zh":"接下來發生的事本來無法預測。"},{"en":"Could not have been predicted means no one could reasonably have known it would happen beforehand.","zh":"could not have been predicted 指沒有人能合理地事先知道它會發生。"},{"en":"The sudden success of a small school project could not have been predicted at the start.","zh":"一個小型學校項目的突然成功，在開始時本來無法預測。"},{"en":"Unexpected results can surprise people because they do not follow the normal pattern.","zh":"意外結果令人驚訝，因為它們不依循正常模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something truly unforeseen.","zh":"這個短語描述真正無法預見的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"endure a condition called","meaning":"忍受一種名為……的病","examples":[{"en":"Michael had endured a condition called ankylosing spondylitis.","zh":"Michael 一直忍受一種名為強直性脊椎炎的病。"},{"en":"To endure a condition called something means to live with and suffer from a named illness or disorder.","zh":"endure a condition called something 指長期承受並患有某種有名稱的疾病或病症。"},{"en":"A patient may endure a condition called asthma for many years.","zh":"病人可能多年忍受一種名為哮喘的病。"},{"en":"Long-term conditions can affect work, sleep, movement, and mood.","zh":"長期病症可以影響工作、睡眠、活動和心情。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests ongoing difficulty, not a short mild illness.","zh":"這個短語暗示持續困難，而不是短暫輕微疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ankylosing spondylitis","meaning":"強直性脊椎炎","examples":[{"en":"Michael suffered from ankylosing spondylitis for eight years.","zh":"Michael 患強直性脊椎炎八年。"},{"en":"Ankylosing spondylitis is a long-term inflammatory disease that mainly affects the spine and joints.","zh":"ankylosing spondylitis 指主要影響脊椎和關節的長期炎症性疾病。"},{"en":"A patient with ankylosing spondylitis may feel back pain and stiffness in the morning.","zh":"強直性脊椎炎患者早上可能感到背痛和僵硬。"},{"en":"Severe ankylosing spondylitis can make movement difficult and reduce quality of life.","zh":"嚴重強直性脊椎炎可以令活動困難並降低生活質素。"},{"en":"This term names a specific medical condition, not general back pain.","zh":"這個詞命名一種特定醫療狀況，而不是一般背痛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"chronic autoimmune disease","meaning":"慢性自身免疫病","examples":[{"en":"Ankylosing spondylitis is a chronic autoimmune disease.","zh":"強直性脊椎炎是一種慢性自身免疫病。"},{"en":"A chronic autoimmune disease is a long-term illness in which the immune system wrongly attacks the body.","zh":"chronic autoimmune disease 指免疫系統錯誤攻擊身體的長期疾病。"},{"en":"A person with a chronic autoimmune disease may need regular check-ups and long-term medicine.","zh":"慢性自身免疫病患者可能需要定期覆診和長期服藥。"},{"en":"Such diseases can flare up because the body’s own defence system becomes overactive.","zh":"這類疾病可能突然惡化，因為身體自身防禦系統變得過度活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase combines long duration with immune-system malfunction.","zh":"這個短語結合長期持續與免疫系統失調兩個意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the skeleton","meaning":"骨骼系統","examples":[{"en":"The disease affects the skeleton.","zh":"這種疾病影響骨骼系統。"},{"en":"The skeleton is the framework of bones that supports the body.","zh":"skeleton 指支撐身體的骨頭框架。"},{"en":"A science class may study the skeleton to understand how bones protect organs.","zh":"科學課可能研究骨骼系統，以理解骨頭如何保護器官。"},{"en":"If a disease affects the skeleton, movement and posture may become painful or limited.","zh":"如果疾病影響骨骼系統，活動和姿勢可能變得疼痛或受限制。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the body’s bone structure.","zh":"這個短語指身體的骨骼結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"spinal arthritis","meaning":"脊椎關節炎","examples":[{"en":"The condition is a sort of spinal arthritis.","zh":"這種病是一種脊椎關節炎。"},{"en":"Spinal arthritis is inflammation or disease affecting the joints of the spine.","zh":"spinal arthritis 指影響脊椎關節的炎症或疾病。"},{"en":"A person with spinal arthritis may find it painful to bend, twist, or sit for long periods.","zh":"脊椎關節炎患者可能覺得彎腰、轉身或久坐都疼痛。"},{"en":"Inflammation in the spine can cause stiffness and long-term discomfort.","zh":"脊椎炎症可以造成僵硬和長期不適。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arthritis located in the back or spine.","zh":"這個短語描述位於背部或脊椎的關節炎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"trigger a disease","meaning":"引發疾病","examples":[{"en":"No one knows what triggers ankylosing spondylitis.","zh":"沒有人知道甚麼會引發強直性脊椎炎。"},{"en":"To trigger a disease means to start it or cause it to become active.","zh":"trigger a disease 指開始某種疾病或令其變得活躍。"},{"en":"Certain foods may trigger a skin condition in some people.","zh":"某些食物可能在某些人身上引發皮膚病。"},{"en":"Finding what triggers a disease can help doctors prevent flare-ups or reduce risk.","zh":"找出引發疾病的因素可以幫助醫生預防惡化或降低風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the cause that sets a medical problem in motion.","zh":"這個短語描述使醫療問題開始運作的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in the worst cases","meaning":"在最嚴重的情況下","examples":[{"en":"In the worst cases, the spine may fuse.","zh":"在最嚴重的情況下，脊椎可能融合。"},{"en":"In the worst cases means when the situation is most severe.","zh":"in the worst cases 指情況最嚴重時。"},{"en":"In the worst cases, a flu infection may require hospital care.","zh":"在最嚴重的情況下，流感感染可能需要住院護理。"},{"en":"This phrase warns readers about the most serious possible outcome.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者最嚴重的可能結果。"},{"en":"It does not mean the worst outcome happens to everyone.","zh":"它不表示最壞結果會發生在每個人身上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the spine may fuse","meaning":"脊椎可能融合","examples":[{"en":"In severe cases, the spine may fuse.","zh":"在嚴重情況下，脊椎可能融合。"},{"en":"The spine may fuse means the bones of the spine may join together and lose flexibility.","zh":"the spine may fuse 指脊椎骨可能連接在一起並失去彈性。"},{"en":"A doctor may use scans to check whether parts of a patient’s spine have begun to fuse.","zh":"醫生可能使用掃描檢查病人脊椎部分是否開始融合。"},{"en":"If the spine fuses, bending and turning can become very difficult.","zh":"如果脊椎融合，彎腰和轉身可能變得非常困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious structural change in the backbone.","zh":"這個短語描述脊骨的嚴重結構變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"leave the patient","meaning":"令病人……","examples":[{"en":"The disease may leave the patient forever stooped.","zh":"這種疾病可能令病人永遠彎腰駝背。"},{"en":"To leave the patient in a condition means to cause them to remain in that state.","zh":"leave the patient in a condition 指使病人長期處於某種狀態。"},{"en":"A serious accident may leave the patient unable to walk without support.","zh":"嚴重意外可能令病人無法在沒有支撐下行走。"},{"en":"Long-term illness can leave patients tired, anxious, or physically limited.","zh":"長期疾病可以令病人疲倦、焦慮或身體受限。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the lasting result of an illness or injury.","zh":"這個短語描述疾病或傷害的持久後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"forever stooped","meaning":"永遠彎腰駝背","examples":[{"en":"The disease can leave a patient forever stooped.","zh":"這種疾病可以令病人永遠彎腰駝背。"},{"en":"Forever stooped means permanently bent forward in posture.","zh":"forever stooped 指姿勢永久向前彎曲。"},{"en":"An elderly person with severe back disease may become stooped and unable to stand straight.","zh":"患嚴重背部疾病的長者可能變得駝背，無法站直。"},{"en":"Being forever stooped can affect walking, breathing, confidence, and daily comfort.","zh":"永遠彎腰駝背可以影響走路、呼吸、自信和日常舒適度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lasting physical posture, not a temporary bend.","zh":"這個短語描述持久身體姿勢，而不是暫時彎腰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in anguish","meaning":"處於痛苦之中","examples":[{"en":"Some patients are left stooped and in anguish.","zh":"有些病人變得駝背並處於痛苦之中。"},{"en":"In anguish means in extreme physical or emotional suffering.","zh":"in anguish 指處於極度身體或情緒痛苦之中。"},{"en":"A parent may be in anguish while waiting for news about an injured child.","zh":"家長等待受傷孩子消息時，可能處於痛苦之中。"},{"en":"Severe chronic pain can leave people in anguish for long periods.","zh":"嚴重慢性疼痛可以令人成長時間處於痛苦之中。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than simply saying “upset” or “uncomfortable”.","zh":"這個短語比單純說「不開心」或「不舒服」更強烈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"flare-ups","meaning":"病情突然惡化","examples":[{"en":"Michael could barely walk during bad flare-ups.","zh":"Michael 在嚴重病情突然惡化時幾乎不能走路。"},{"en":"Flare-ups are sudden periods when an illness or symptom becomes worse.","zh":"flare-ups 指疾病或症狀突然變差的一段時期。"},{"en":"A person with eczema may have flare-ups when the weather is dry.","zh":"濕疹患者在天氣乾燥時可能出現病情突然惡化。"},{"en":"Flare-ups can interrupt work, school, sleep, and daily routines.","zh":"病情突然惡化可以打斷工作、學校、睡眠和日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for long-term conditions that worsen from time to time.","zh":"這個短語常用於會不時惡化的長期病症。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"during bad flare-ups","meaning":"在病情嚴重發作時","examples":[{"en":"During bad flare-ups, Michael could not even walk.","zh":"在病情嚴重發作時，Michael 甚至不能走路。"},{"en":"During bad flare-ups means while symptoms are becoming especially severe.","zh":"during bad flare-ups 指症狀變得特別嚴重的期間。"},{"en":"During bad asthma flare-ups, a child may need to use an inhaler more often.","zh":"在哮喘嚴重發作時，孩子可能需要更頻繁使用吸入器。"},{"en":"People may need rest, medicine, or medical advice during bad flare-ups.","zh":"人們在病情嚴重發作時可能需要休息、藥物或醫療建議。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the most difficult periods of a long-term condition.","zh":"這個短語指出長期病症中最困難的時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"days after","meaning":"在……數天後","examples":[{"en":"Days after the scorpion sting, Michael’s pain went away.","zh":"在蠍子螫傷數天後，Michael 的疼痛消失了。"},{"en":"Days after means several days following an event.","zh":"days after 指某事件之後數天。"},{"en":"Days after a school interview, the student received an offer.","zh":"學校面試數天後，學生收到取錄通知。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show the time gap between one event and another.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示一件事與另一件事之間的時間差。"},{"en":"It suggests the change did not happen immediately but soon afterwards.","zh":"它暗示變化不是立即發生，而是不久後發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"go away","meaning":"消失；減退","examples":[{"en":"The pain went away after the scorpion sting.","zh":"疼痛在蠍子螫傷後消失了。"},{"en":"To go away means to disappear, stop, or become much less noticeable.","zh":"go away 指消失、停止或變得不再明顯。"},{"en":"A headache may go away after sleep and enough water.","zh":"頭痛可能在睡眠和補充足夠水分後減退。"},{"en":"When a symptom goes away, people often feel relief and return to normal activities.","zh":"當症狀消失，人們常感到舒緩並回到正常活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is simple and common for pain, problems, or feelings disappearing.","zh":"這個短語簡單常見，可用於疼痛、問題或感覺消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"remain essentially pain-free","meaning":"基本上沒有痛楚","examples":[{"en":"Two years later, Michael remains essentially pain-free.","zh":"兩年後，Michael 仍基本上沒有痛楚。"},{"en":"To remain essentially pain-free means to continue living with little or no pain.","zh":"remain essentially pain-free 指持續生活在幾乎沒有或完全沒有疼痛的狀態。"},{"en":"After successful treatment, a patient may remain essentially pain-free for months.","zh":"成功治療後，病人可能數月基本上沒有痛楚。"},{"en":"Being pain-free can greatly improve sleep, movement, work, and mood.","zh":"沒有痛楚可以大大改善睡眠、活動、工作和心情。"},{"en":"“Essentially” allows for small discomfort while showing that major pain is gone.","zh":"“Essentially” 容許有少量不適，但顯示主要疼痛已消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be off medication","meaning":"已停用藥物","examples":[{"en":"Michael is now off most of his medications.","zh":"Michael 現在已停用大部分藥物。"},{"en":"To be off medication means to no longer take a medicine that one used to take.","zh":"be off medication 指不再服用以前服用的藥物。"},{"en":"A patient may be off medication only after a doctor says it is safe.","zh":"病人只有在醫生說安全後，才可能停用藥物。"},{"en":"Stopping medication without medical advice can be dangerous.","zh":"未經醫療建議自行停藥可能很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change in treatment, not necessarily a complete cure.","zh":"這個短語描述治療上的改變，不一定代表完全康復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be cautious about","meaning":"對……保持謹慎","examples":[{"en":"Michael is cautious about overstating the role of venom.","zh":"Michael 對誇大毒液作用保持謹慎。"},{"en":"To be cautious about something means to be careful and avoid making strong claims too quickly.","zh":"be cautious about something 指小心並避免太快作出強烈說法。"},{"en":"A teacher may be cautious about blaming one student before hearing all sides.","zh":"老師在聽完各方說法前，可能對責怪某個學生保持謹慎。"},{"en":"Caution matters when evidence is limited or the result may have several causes.","zh":"當證據有限或結果可能有多種原因時，謹慎很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows careful judgement rather than blind confidence.","zh":"這個短語顯示審慎判斷，而不是盲目信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"overstate the role of","meaning":"誇大……的作用","examples":[{"en":"Michael does not want to overstate the role of the scorpion’s venom.","zh":"Michael 不想誇大蠍子毒液的作用。"},{"en":"To overstate the role of something means to make its importance sound greater than it really is.","zh":"overstate the role of something 指把某事的重要性說得比實際更大。"},{"en":"A student should not overstate the role of luck in exam success when hard work also mattered.","zh":"當努力也很重要時，學生不應誇大運氣在考試成功中的作用。"},{"en":"Overstating one cause can hide other possible explanations.","zh":"誇大一個原因可能掩蓋其他可能解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against exaggerating importance.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要誇大重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"remission","meaning":"病情緩解","examples":[{"en":"The scorpion sting may have played a role in Michael’s remission.","zh":"蠍子螫傷可能在 Michael 的病情緩解中發揮了作用。"},{"en":"Remission is a period when symptoms of a disease become weaker or disappear.","zh":"remission 指疾病症狀減弱或消失的一段時期。"},{"en":"A cancer patient may be in remission after treatment reduces signs of the disease.","zh":"癌症病人在治療減少疾病跡象後，可能進入病情緩解期。"},{"en":"Remission can bring relief, but doctors may still monitor the patient carefully.","zh":"病情緩解可以帶來舒緩，但醫生仍可能仔細監察病人。"},{"en":"This word does not always mean the disease is permanently cured.","zh":"這個詞不一定表示疾病已永久治癒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"come back","meaning":"復發；回來","examples":[{"en":"Michael said he would accept another sting if his pain came back.","zh":"Michael 說如果疼痛復發，他會接受再被螫一次。"},{"en":"To come back means to return after being absent or gone.","zh":"come back 指在消失或離開後再次回來。"},{"en":"A headache may come back if a student sleeps too little again.","zh":"如果學生再次睡眠不足，頭痛可能復發。"},{"en":"When symptoms come back, people may need medical advice or further treatment.","zh":"當症狀復發，人們可能需要醫療建議或進一步治療。"},{"en":"This phrase is common for returning pain, illness, feelings, or problems.","zh":"這個短語常用於疼痛、疾病、感覺或問題再次出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the stuff that drips from","meaning":"從……滴出的東西","examples":[{"en":"Venom is the stuff that drips from fangs and stingers.","zh":"毒液是從毒牙和螫針滴出的東西。"},{"en":"The stuff that drips from something means the liquid substance that falls in small drops from it.","zh":"the stuff that drips from something 指從某物以小滴落下的液體物質。"},{"en":"Honey is the sticky stuff that drips from a spoon when it is lifted from a jar.","zh":"蜂蜜是匙羹從罐中拿起時滴下的黏稠東西。"},{"en":"In this passage, the phrase makes venom sound physical and vivid.","zh":"在這篇文章中，這個短語令毒液聽起來具體而生動。"},{"en":"It is informal, so it explains the idea in a direct, everyday way.","zh":"它較口語，因此以直接日常方式解釋概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fangs and stingers","meaning":"毒牙和螫針","examples":[{"en":"Venom drips from the fangs and stingers of certain creatures.","zh":"毒液從某些生物的毒牙和螫針滴出。"},{"en":"Fangs and stingers are specialised body parts used by some animals to bite or sting.","zh":"fangs and stingers 指某些動物用來咬或螫的特化身體部位。"},{"en":"A snake uses fangs, while a bee uses a stinger.","zh":"蛇使用毒牙，而蜜蜂使用螫針。"},{"en":"These body parts can deliver venom into another animal’s body.","zh":"這些身體部位可以把毒液送入另一動物體內。"},{"en":"This phrase names the tools that venomous animals use to inject venom.","zh":"這個短語命名有毒動物用來注入毒液的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"creatures lurking","meaning":"潛伏的生物","examples":[{"en":"Venom comes from creatures lurking on trails or hiding in cellars.","zh":"毒液來自潛伏在小徑上或躲在地窖裡的生物。"},{"en":"Creatures lurking are animals staying hidden or waiting quietly, often in a way that feels threatening.","zh":"creatures lurking 指隱藏或靜靜等待的動物，常帶有威脅感。"},{"en":"A spider may be lurking behind boxes in a storeroom.","zh":"蜘蛛可能潛伏在儲物室箱子後面。"},{"en":"Lurking creatures can surprise people because they are not easily seen.","zh":"潛伏的生物不容易看見，因此可以令人受驚。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a sense of hidden danger.","zh":"這個短語營造隱藏危險的感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hiking trail","meaning":"遠足徑","examples":[{"en":"Some venomous creatures lurk on hiking trails.","zh":"有些有毒生物潛伏在遠足徑上。"},{"en":"A hiking trail is a path used for walking through hills, forests, or natural areas.","zh":"hiking trail 指用於穿過山丘、森林或自然地區的步行路徑。"},{"en":"Families may follow a hiking trail on a weekend to enjoy fresh air and scenery.","zh":"家庭週末可能沿遠足徑行走，以享受新鮮空氣和風景。"},{"en":"On hiking trails, people should watch where they step because animals may hide under rocks or leaves.","zh":"在遠足徑上，人們應留意腳下，因為動物可能躲在石頭或葉子下。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an outdoor walking route, not an ordinary city pavement.","zh":"這個短語指戶外步行路線，而不是普通城市行人路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hiding in the cellar","meaning":"躲在地窖裏","examples":[{"en":"Venomous creatures may be hiding in the cellar.","zh":"有毒生物可能躲在地窖裏。"},{"en":"Hiding in the cellar means staying out of sight in a storage area beneath or below a house.","zh":"hiding in the cellar 指躲在房屋下方或地下的儲物空間中，不被看見。"},{"en":"A family may find insects hiding in the cellar among old boxes.","zh":"家庭可能在地窖舊箱子之間發現昆蟲躲藏。"},{"en":"Dark, quiet places can attract small animals because they offer shelter.","zh":"黑暗安靜的地方可以吸引小動物，因為提供藏身處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a hidden location where people may not expect danger.","zh":"這個短語描述人們可能沒想到有危險的隱蔽位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"under the woodpile","meaning":"在柴堆下面","examples":[{"en":"Some creatures hide under the woodpile.","zh":"有些生物躲在柴堆下面。"},{"en":"Under the woodpile means beneath a stack of wood kept for fuel or storage.","zh":"under the woodpile 指在作燃料或儲存用的一堆木材下方。"},{"en":"A gardener should wear gloves before moving logs from under the woodpile.","zh":"園丁從柴堆下面搬木頭前應戴手套。"},{"en":"Woodpiles can shelter insects, spiders, or small animals because they are dark and undisturbed.","zh":"柴堆陰暗且少被打擾，可以讓昆蟲、蜘蛛或小動物藏身。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common hiding place outdoors.","zh":"這個短語描述戶外常見的藏身處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"nature’s most efficient killer","meaning":"大自然最有效率的殺手","examples":[{"en":"Venom is nature’s most efficient killer.","zh":"毒液是大自然最有效率的殺手。"},{"en":"Nature’s most efficient killer means something in nature that can kill quickly and effectively.","zh":"nature’s most efficient killer 指自然界中能快速而有效殺死獵物的東西。"},{"en":"A documentary may describe a predator’s bite as nature’s most efficient weapon.","zh":"紀錄片可能把捕食者的咬擊描述為大自然最有效率的武器。"},{"en":"Venom is efficient because a small amount can stop nerves, blood, or muscles.","zh":"毒液有效率，因為少量即可阻止神經、血液或肌肉正常運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is dramatic and emphasises venom’s power.","zh":"這個短語具戲劇性，強調毒液的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"exquisitely honed","meaning":"被精密地磨練","examples":[{"en":"Venom is exquisitely honed to stop a body in its tracks.","zh":"毒液被精密地磨練，以令身體即時停下來。"},{"en":"Exquisitely honed means finely shaped, improved, or perfected for a specific purpose.","zh":"exquisitely honed 指為特定目的被精細塑造、改善或完善。"},{"en":"A surgeon’s hand skills are exquisitely honed after years of careful practice.","zh":"外科醫生的手部技巧經多年細心練習後被精密磨練。"},{"en":"Evolution can hone venom over time until it attacks very specific body systems.","zh":"演化可以隨時間磨練毒液，直到它能攻擊非常特定的身體系統。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests precision, not rough power alone.","zh":"這個短語暗示精準，而不只是粗暴力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stop a body in its tracks","meaning":"令身體即時停下來","examples":[{"en":"Venom can stop a body in its tracks.","zh":"毒液可以令身體即時停下來。"},{"en":"To stop a body in its tracks means to halt movement or function suddenly.","zh":"stop a body in its tracks 指突然停止身體活動或功能。"},{"en":"A sudden sharp pain can stop a runner in his tracks during a race.","zh":"比賽中突如其來的劇痛可以令跑手即時停下來。"},{"en":"Venom may stop a body by paralysing muscles or disrupting the heart.","zh":"毒液可能透過麻痺肌肉或干擾心臟來令身體停下。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an immediate and powerful interruption.","zh":"這個短語暗示即時而強大的中斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"complex soup","meaning":"複雜的混合物","examples":[{"en":"Venom is a complex soup of toxic proteins and peptides.","zh":"毒液是由有毒蛋白質和肽組成的複雜混合物。"},{"en":"A complex soup means a mixture containing many different substances working together.","zh":"complex soup 指含有許多不同物質並共同作用的混合物。"},{"en":"Blood is a complex soup of cells, proteins, nutrients, and chemical signals.","zh":"血液是由細胞、蛋白質、養分和化學訊號組成的複雜混合物。"},{"en":"Venom is hard to study because its “soup” contains many molecules with different effects.","zh":"毒液難以研究，因為這種「混合物」含有許多作用不同的分子。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and vivid, not a literal bowl of soup.","zh":"這個短語較口語且生動，不是真的一碗湯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"toxic proteins and peptides","meaning":"有毒蛋白質和肽","examples":[{"en":"Venom contains toxic proteins and peptides.","zh":"毒液含有有毒蛋白質和肽。"},{"en":"Toxic proteins and peptides are harmful biological molecules that can affect cells, nerves, blood, or tissues.","zh":"toxic proteins and peptides 指能影響細胞、神經、血液或組織的有害生物分子。"},{"en":"A laboratory may study toxic proteins and peptides to learn how they bind to human cells.","zh":"實驗室可能研究有毒蛋白質和肽，以了解它們如何與人體細胞結合。"},{"en":"These molecules can be dangerous, but they may also reveal useful medical targets.","zh":"這些分子可以很危險，但也可能揭示有用醫學目標。"},{"en":"This phrase names important active substances inside venom.","zh":"這個短語命名毒液中的重要活性物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"amino acids","meaning":"氨基酸","examples":[{"en":"Peptides are short strings of amino acids.","zh":"肽是由氨基酸組成的短鏈。"},{"en":"Amino acids are small molecules that link together to form proteins and peptides.","zh":"amino acids 指連接在一起形成蛋白質和肽的小分子。"},{"en":"A biology student learns that food proteins are broken down into amino acids during digestion.","zh":"生物學生會學到食物蛋白質在消化時被分解成氨基酸。"},{"en":"Different sequences of amino acids can create molecules with very different effects.","zh":"不同氨基酸序列可以形成作用非常不同的分子。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the basic building blocks of proteins.","zh":"這個短語指蛋白質的基本組成單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"targets and effects","meaning":"目標和作用","examples":[{"en":"The molecules in venom may have different targets and effects.","zh":"毒液中的分子可能有不同目標和作用。"},{"en":"Targets and effects are the body parts or molecules a substance acts on and the results it produces.","zh":"targets and effects 指某物質作用於的身體部位或分子，以及它造成的結果。"},{"en":"A medicine’s target may be a pain signal, and its effect may be reduced pain.","zh":"藥物的目標可能是疼痛訊號，而其作用可能是減輕疼痛。"},{"en":"Venom is complex because different toxins may have different targets and effects at the same time.","zh":"毒液很複雜，因為不同毒素可能同時有不同目標和作用。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain how one mixture can produce many symptoms.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋一種混合物如何產生多種症狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"work synergistically","meaning":"產生協同作用","examples":[{"en":"Venom molecules work synergistically for a powerful effect.","zh":"毒液分子產生協同作用，帶來強大效果。"},{"en":"To work synergistically means to work together so the combined effect is stronger than separate effects.","zh":"work synergistically 指共同作用，使整體效果比分開作用更強。"},{"en":"In a classroom, clear notes and practice questions work synergistically to improve learning.","zh":"在課室中，清楚筆記和練習題可以產生協同作用，改善學習。"},{"en":"Venom toxins may work synergistically when one toxin weakens the body and another finishes the attack.","zh":"當一種毒素削弱身體，另一種毒素完成攻擊，毒液毒素可能產生協同作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes teamwork between parts inside a system.","zh":"這個短語描述系統內各部分之間的合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the mightiest punch","meaning":"最強大的打擊","examples":[{"en":"The molecules work together for the mightiest punch.","zh":"這些分子共同作用，形成最強大的打擊。"},{"en":"The mightiest punch means the strongest possible impact or effect.","zh":"the mightiest punch 指最強烈的影響或效果。"},{"en":"A charity campaign may combine real stories and clear statistics for the mightiest punch.","zh":"慈善宣傳可能結合真實故事和清楚統計，以產生最強大的打擊。"},{"en":"Venom delivers the mightiest punch when several toxins attack different body systems together.","zh":"當多種毒素共同攻擊不同身體系統，毒液就能造成最強打擊。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and vivid, showing maximum force.","zh":"這個短語較口語且生動，顯示最大力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"go for the nervous system","meaning":"攻擊神經系統","examples":[{"en":"Some venom molecules go for the nervous system.","zh":"有些毒液分子攻擊神經系統。"},{"en":"To go for the nervous system means to attack or affect the body’s nerves and signalling system.","zh":"go for the nervous system 指攻擊或影響身體的神經和訊號系統。"},{"en":"A doctor may suspect nerve involvement if a patient feels numbness, tingling, or electric pain.","zh":"如果病人感到麻木、刺痛或電擊般疼痛，醫生可能懷疑神經受影響。"},{"en":"Venom that goes for the nervous system can cause paralysis, pain, or loss of muscle control.","zh":"攻擊神經系統的毒液可以造成癱瘓、疼痛或肌肉控制喪失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the target of the toxin.","zh":"這個短語描述毒素的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"paralyse by blocking","meaning":"透過阻截……使癱瘓","examples":[{"en":"Some toxins paralyse victims by blocking messages between nerves and muscles.","zh":"有些毒素透過阻截神經和肌肉之間的訊息，使受害者癱瘓。"},{"en":"To paralyse by blocking something means to stop movement by preventing signals from passing.","zh":"paralyse by blocking something 指透過阻止訊號通過而停止活動。"},{"en":"A machine may stop working if a broken wire blocks messages between its controls and motor.","zh":"如果斷線阻截控制器和馬達之間的訊息，機器可能停止運作。"},{"en":"When nerve signals are blocked, muscles may no longer receive instructions to move.","zh":"當神經訊號被阻截，肌肉可能不再收到移動指令。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the mechanism behind paralysis.","zh":"這個短語解釋癱瘓背後的機制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"block messages between","meaning":"阻截……之間的訊息","examples":[{"en":"Some toxins block messages between nerves and muscles.","zh":"有些毒素阻截神經和肌肉之間的訊息。"},{"en":"To block messages between two parts means to stop communication from passing from one to the other.","zh":"block messages between two parts 指阻止訊息從一方傳到另一方。"},{"en":"A faulty Internet connection can block messages between a teacher and students in an online lesson.","zh":"故障網絡連接可以阻截網課中老師與學生之間的訊息。"},{"en":"If messages between nerves and muscles are blocked, the body cannot move normally.","zh":"如果神經和肌肉之間的訊息被阻截，身體就不能正常移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes interrupted communication.","zh":"這個短語描述溝通被中斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"nerves and muscles","meaning":"神經和肌肉","examples":[{"en":"Venom can block signals between nerves and muscles.","zh":"毒液可以阻截神經和肌肉之間的訊號。"},{"en":"Nerves and muscles work together so the body can sense, move, and respond.","zh":"nerves and muscles 共同運作，使身體能感知、移動和反應。"},{"en":"When you pick up a pencil, nerves send signals and muscles carry out the movement.","zh":"當你拿起鉛筆，神經發送訊號，肌肉執行動作。"},{"en":"If communication between nerves and muscles fails, movement may weaken or stop.","zh":"如果神經和肌肉之間的溝通失效，動作可能變弱或停止。"},{"en":"This phrase names two body systems that must cooperate for movement.","zh":"這個短語命名兩個必須合作以產生活動的身體系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"eat away at","meaning":"侵蝕","examples":[{"en":"Some toxins eat away at molecules.","zh":"有些毒素會侵蝕分子。"},{"en":"To eat away at something means to gradually destroy, damage, or break it down.","zh":"eat away at something 指逐漸破壞、損害或分解某物。"},{"en":"Acid can eat away at metal if it is left on the surface too long.","zh":"如果酸液在金屬表面停留太久，可能侵蝕金屬。"},{"en":"Toxins that eat away at body molecules can cause cells and tissues to fail.","zh":"侵蝕身體分子的毒素可以令細胞和組織失效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow or progressive damage.","zh":"這個短語描述緩慢或逐步的損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cells and tissues collapse","meaning":"細胞和組織崩潰","examples":[{"en":"Cells and tissues collapse when certain molecules are destroyed.","zh":"當某些分子被破壞，細胞和組織就會崩潰。"},{"en":"Cells and tissues collapse means the body’s small living units and structures stop functioning properly.","zh":"cells and tissues collapse 指身體的小型生命單位和結構停止正常運作。"},{"en":"A doctor worries when infected tissue begins to break down and lose structure.","zh":"當受感染組織開始分解並失去結構，醫生會感到擔心。"},{"en":"If toxins destroy key molecules, cells and tissues may collapse because their support systems fail.","zh":"如果毒素破壞關鍵分子，細胞和組織可能因支撐系統失效而崩潰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious biological breakdown.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重生物崩解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"clot blood","meaning":"使血液凝結","examples":[{"en":"Venom can kill by clotting blood.","zh":"毒液可以透過使血液凝結而殺死受害者。"},{"en":"To clot blood means to make blood thicken and form clumps.","zh":"clot blood 指令血液變稠並形成血塊。"},{"en":"Blood normally clots to stop bleeding after a small cut.","zh":"血液通常在小傷口後凝結，以停止出血。"},{"en":"If blood clots in the wrong place, it can block circulation and become dangerous.","zh":"如果血液在錯誤位置凝結，可能阻塞循環並變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes blood changing from liquid flow into thicker material.","zh":"這個短語描述血液從流動液體變成較稠物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stop the heart","meaning":"使心臟停頓","examples":[{"en":"Some venom can stop the heart.","zh":"有些毒液可以使心臟停頓。"},{"en":"To stop the heart means to cause the heart to stop beating.","zh":"stop the heart 指令心臟停止跳動。"},{"en":"Severe electric shock can stop the heart if emergency help is not given quickly.","zh":"如果沒有快速急救，嚴重電擊可以使心臟停頓。"},{"en":"If the heart stops, oxygen cannot be pumped around the body.","zh":"如果心臟停頓，氧氣就不能被泵送到全身。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a life-threatening medical emergency.","zh":"這個短語描述危及生命的醫療緊急情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"prevent clotting","meaning":"阻止凝血","examples":[{"en":"Some venom kills by preventing clotting.","zh":"有些毒液透過阻止凝血而致命。"},{"en":"To prevent clotting means to stop blood from forming clots.","zh":"prevent clotting 指阻止血液形成血塊。"},{"en":"Certain medicines prevent clotting to reduce the risk of dangerous blood clots.","zh":"某些藥物阻止凝血，以降低危險血栓風險。"},{"en":"If clotting is prevented after injury, bleeding may continue and become dangerous.","zh":"如果受傷後凝血被阻止，出血可能持續並變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes blocking the body’s normal blood-sealing process.","zh":"這個短語描述阻止身體正常封住血液流失的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"trigger a killer bleed","meaning":"引發致命出血","examples":[{"en":"Venom can trigger a killer bleed.","zh":"毒液可以引發致命出血。"},{"en":"To trigger a killer bleed means to cause severe bleeding that may be fatal.","zh":"trigger a killer bleed 指造成可能致命的嚴重出血。"},{"en":"A doctor treats uncontrolled bleeding as an emergency because blood loss can kill quickly.","zh":"醫生把失控出血視為緊急情況，因為失血可以迅速致命。"},{"en":"Venom may trigger a killer bleed by stopping blood from clotting properly.","zh":"毒液可能透過阻止血液正常凝結來引發致命出血。"},{"en":"This phrase is dramatic and refers to life-threatening bleeding.","zh":"這個短語具戲劇性，指危及生命的出血。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"multifaceted and multitasking","meaning":"多面向且具多重功能","examples":[{"en":"All venom is multifaceted and multitasking.","zh":"所有毒液都是多面向且具多重功能的。"},{"en":"Multifaceted and multitasking means having many sides and doing several jobs at once.","zh":"multifaceted and multitasking 指有多個層面並同時執行多項功能。"},{"en":"A good school app can be multifaceted and multitasking if it handles homework, messages, and attendance.","zh":"如果一個好學校應用程式能處理功課、訊息和出席紀錄，它就是多面向且具多重功能。"},{"en":"Venom is powerful because its different molecules can attack several body systems at once.","zh":"毒液強大，因為其中不同分子可以同時攻擊幾個身體系統。"},{"en":"This phrase shows complexity and multiple functions.","zh":"這個短語顯示複雜性和多重功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the difference between…and…","meaning":"……和……之間的分別","examples":[{"en":"The difference between venom and poison is how they enter the body.","zh":"毒液和毒物之間的分別在於它們如何進入身體。"},{"en":"The difference between A and B means the point that makes A not the same as B.","zh":"the difference between A and B 指令 A 和 B 不同的重點。"},{"en":"The difference between studying and memorising is that studying includes understanding, not just repetition.","zh":"學習和死記之間的分別是學習包括理解，而不只是重複。"},{"en":"Clear differences help students avoid confusing similar words.","zh":"清楚分別幫助學生避免混淆相似字詞。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a comparison that separates two ideas.","zh":"這個短語引入分開兩個概念的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be injected into","meaning":"被注入……","examples":[{"en":"Venom is injected into victims through specialised body parts.","zh":"毒液透過特化身體部位被注入受害者體內。"},{"en":"To be injected into something means to be pushed into it through a needle, fang, or similar tool.","zh":"be injected into something 指透過針、毒牙或類似工具被推入某物內。"},{"en":"A vaccine is injected into the arm by a trained nurse.","zh":"疫苗由受訓護士注入手臂。"},{"en":"Venom becomes dangerous because it is injected directly into the body.","zh":"毒液危險，是因為它被直接注入身體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes entry by force through a sharp or specialised part.","zh":"這個短語描述透過尖銳或特化部位強行進入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"by way of","meaning":"經由；透過","examples":[{"en":"Venom enters victims by way of specialised body parts.","zh":"毒液經由特化身體部位進入受害者體內。"},{"en":"By way of means through or by means of a particular route or method.","zh":"by way of 指經由某路線或透過某方法。"},{"en":"A student may submit homework by way of an online platform.","zh":"學生可能透過網上平台提交功課。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the route or channel through which something happens.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事發生的路徑或渠道。"},{"en":"It is more formal than simply saying “through”.","zh":"它比單純說 “through” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"specialised body parts","meaning":"特化身體部位","examples":[{"en":"Venom is delivered through specialised body parts.","zh":"毒液透過特化身體部位送入。"},{"en":"Specialised body parts are body structures adapted for a particular job.","zh":"specialised body parts 指適應特定工作的身體結構。"},{"en":"A bird’s beak is a specialised body part that helps it eat certain foods.","zh":"鳥喙是幫助鳥類吃特定食物的特化身體部位。"},{"en":"In venomous animals, specialised body parts such as fangs or stingers deliver venom efficiently.","zh":"在有毒動物中，毒牙或螫針等特化身體部位能有效輸送毒液。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how animal bodies are adapted for specific functions.","zh":"這個短語解釋動物身體如何適應特定功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"poison is ingested","meaning":"毒物是經吞食進入體內的","examples":[{"en":"Poison is ingested rather than injected.","zh":"毒物是經吞食而不是注射進入體內的。"},{"en":"Poison is ingested means poison enters the body by being eaten, drunk, or swallowed.","zh":"poison is ingested 指毒物透過吃下、喝下或吞下進入身體。"},{"en":"A child may ingest poison if they drink cleaning liquid by mistake.","zh":"如果孩子誤飲清潔劑，就可能吞入毒物。"},{"en":"Poison differs from venom because it usually harms through swallowing or contact, not injection.","zh":"毒物與毒液不同，因為毒物通常透過吞食或接觸造成傷害，而不是注入。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the route by which poison enters the body.","zh":"這個短語解釋毒物進入身體的途徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"dozens, even hundreds, of","meaning":"數十種，甚至數百種","examples":[{"en":"Dozens, even hundreds, of toxins can be delivered in one bite.","zh":"一次咬擊可以送入數十種，甚至數百種毒素。"},{"en":"Dozens, even hundreds, of something means a very large number, ranging from many tens to possibly hundreds.","zh":"dozens, even hundreds, of something 指非常大的數量，由很多個十到可能數百。"},{"en":"A busy school office may receive dozens, even hundreds, of forms before a deadline.","zh":"繁忙學校辦公室在截止日期前可能收到數十份，甚至數百份表格。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the number is much larger than expected.","zh":"這個短語強調數量比預期大得多。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing scale or complexity.","zh":"它適合用來顯示規模或複雜性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be delivered in","meaning":"在……中被送入","examples":[{"en":"Many toxins can be delivered in a single bite.","zh":"許多毒素可以在一次咬擊中被送入。"},{"en":"To be delivered in something means to be sent, introduced, or carried through that event or method.","zh":"be delivered in something 指透過某事件或方法被送出、引入或帶入。"},{"en":"A vaccine can be delivered in one injection at a clinic.","zh":"疫苗可以在診所一次注射中被送入體內。"},{"en":"Venom toxins are delivered in a bite when fangs push them into the victim.","zh":"當毒牙把毒液推入受害者體內，毒液毒素就在咬擊中被送入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the method or moment of delivery.","zh":"這個短語描述輸送的方法或時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a single bite","meaning":"一次咬擊","examples":[{"en":"One bite can deliver many toxins.","zh":"一次咬擊可以送入許多毒素。"},{"en":"A single bite means one act of biting.","zh":"a single bite 指一次咬的動作。"},{"en":"A dog can break the skin with a single bite if it bites hard enough.","zh":"如果狗咬得夠用力，一次咬擊就可以咬破皮膚。"},{"en":"In venomous animals, a single bite may introduce several harmful chemicals at once.","zh":"在有毒動物中，一次咬擊可能同時引入幾種有害化學物質。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that even one bite can be serious.","zh":"這個短語強調即使一次咬擊也可能嚴重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"redundant jobs","meaning":"重複功能","examples":[{"en":"Some toxins have redundant jobs, while others have unique ones.","zh":"有些毒素具有重複功能，而另一些則有獨特功能。"},{"en":"Redundant jobs are repeated or overlapping functions that more than one part can perform.","zh":"redundant jobs 指多於一個部分可以執行的重複或重疊功能。"},{"en":"In a school office, two staff members may have redundant jobs if both record the same attendance data.","zh":"在學校辦公室，如果兩名職員都記錄同一出席資料，他們的工作可能有重複功能。"},{"en":"Redundancy can provide backup because one part can still work if another fails.","zh":"重複可以提供後備，因為一部分失效時另一部分仍可運作。"},{"en":"This phrase means repeated function, not necessarily useless work.","zh":"這個短語指功能重複，不一定是無用工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"unique ones","meaning":"獨特的功能","examples":[{"en":"Some toxins have unique roles in venom.","zh":"有些毒素在毒液中有獨特功能。"},{"en":"Unique ones are special functions or items that are different from all the others.","zh":"unique ones 指與其他所有都不同的特殊功能或項目。"},{"en":"In a group project, one student may have a unique role if only she can edit the video.","zh":"在小組項目中，如果只有一名學生能剪片，她就可能有獨特角色。"},{"en":"Unique functions matter because they do something no other part can do.","zh":"獨特功能很重要，因為它們做其他部分不能做的事。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts special roles with repeated or shared roles.","zh":"這個短語把特殊角色與重複或共享角色作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"evolutionary arms race","meaning":"演化軍備競賽","examples":[{"en":"Predators and prey are involved in an evolutionary arms race.","zh":"捕食者和獵物參與演化軍備競賽。"},{"en":"An evolutionary arms race is a long process in which two species keep adapting against each other.","zh":"evolutionary arms race 指兩個物種長期不斷互相適應和對抗的過程。"},{"en":"If insects evolve resistance to pesticides, farmers may develop stronger controls in an arms race.","zh":"如果昆蟲演化出對農藥的抗性，農民可能發展更強控制方法，形成軍備競賽。"},{"en":"Predators improve weapons while prey improve defences, so both sides keep changing.","zh":"捕食者改良武器，獵物改良防禦，因此雙方不斷改變。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why biological tools such as venom can become highly specialised.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何毒液等生物工具可以變得高度專門化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"predator and prey","meaning":"捕食者和獵物","examples":[{"en":"Venom evolves in the arms race between predator and prey.","zh":"毒液在捕食者和獵物之間的軍備競賽中演化。"},{"en":"Predator and prey are animals where one hunts and the other is hunted.","zh":"predator and prey 指一方捕獵，另一方被捕獵的動物。"},{"en":"A cat and a mouse can be an example of predator and prey.","zh":"貓和老鼠可以是捕食者和獵物的例子。"},{"en":"Predators may develop better attack methods while prey develop better escape methods.","zh":"捕食者可能發展更好攻擊方法，而獵物發展更好逃脫方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a basic relationship in nature.","zh":"這個短語描述自然界中的基本關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"weapons and defences","meaning":"武器和防禦","examples":[{"en":"Weapons and defences are constantly tweaked in evolution.","zh":"武器和防禦在演化中不斷被微調。"},{"en":"Weapons and defences are attack tools and protection methods used by living things.","zh":"weapons and defences 指生物使用的攻擊工具和保護方法。"},{"en":"A bee’s sting is a weapon, while a turtle’s shell is a defence.","zh":"蜜蜂螫針是武器，而烏龜殼是防禦。"},{"en":"Evolution changes weapons and defences because survival depends on catching food or avoiding danger.","zh":"演化會改變武器和防禦，因為生存取決於捕食或避開危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both sides of biological competition.","zh":"這個短語描述生物競爭的兩方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be constantly tweaked","meaning":"不斷被微調","examples":[{"en":"Venom is constantly tweaked by evolution.","zh":"毒液被演化不斷微調。"},{"en":"To be constantly tweaked means to be repeatedly adjusted in small ways.","zh":"be constantly tweaked 指反覆被小幅調整。"},{"en":"A teacher’s lesson plan may be constantly tweaked after seeing what students understand.","zh":"老師看到學生理解情況後，課堂計劃可能不斷被微調。"},{"en":"Small repeated changes can gradually produce a much better system.","zh":"細小而反覆的改變可以逐漸產生更好的系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing fine adjustment, not one big redesign.","zh":"這個短語描述持續精細調整，而不是一次大型重設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"drastically potent concoctions","meaning":"極其強效的混合毒液","examples":[{"en":"Evolution can produce drastically potent concoctions.","zh":"演化可以產生極其強效的混合毒液。"},{"en":"Drastically potent concoctions are extremely powerful mixtures of substances.","zh":"drastically potent concoctions 指由物質組成、力量極強的混合物。"},{"en":"A dangerous cleaning mixture can become a potent concoction if people combine chemicals wrongly.","zh":"如果人們錯誤混合化學品，危險清潔劑混合物可能變成強效混合物。"},{"en":"Venom can be drastically potent because different toxins intensify each other’s effects.","zh":"毒液可以極其強效，因為不同毒素會加強彼此作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mixture with unusually strong power.","zh":"這個短語描述具有異常強大力量的混合物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"administer poison to","meaning":"向……施毒","examples":[{"en":"Imagine administering poison to an adversary.","zh":"想像向對手施毒。"},{"en":"To administer poison to someone means to give or apply poison to that person.","zh":"administer poison to someone 指向某人給予或施加毒物。"},{"en":"In crime fiction, a villain may administer poison to a victim through a drink.","zh":"在犯罪小說中，反派可能透過飲品向受害者施毒。"},{"en":"Administering poison is dangerous and illegal when done to harm someone.","zh":"為傷害某人而施毒是危險且違法的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the act of delivering poison.","zh":"這個短語描述投放毒物的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"adversary","meaning":"對手；敵人","examples":[{"en":"An adversary is an opponent or enemy.","zh":"adversary 指對手或敵人。"},{"en":"An adversary is someone who fights, competes against, or strongly opposes another person.","zh":"adversary 指與另一人作戰、競爭或強烈反對的人。"},{"en":"In a debate, the opposing speaker is an adversary, not necessarily a personal enemy.","zh":"在辯論中，對方講者是對手，但不一定是私人敵人。"},{"en":"Having an adversary can force people to prepare better and defend their ideas clearly.","zh":"有對手可以迫使人準備得更好並清楚捍衛想法。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than “opponent”.","zh":"這個詞比 “opponent” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"jab someone with","meaning":"用……刺某人","examples":[{"en":"The image compares venom to jabbing someone with a knife.","zh":"這個畫面把毒液比作拿刀刺某人。"},{"en":"To jab someone with something means to poke or stab them quickly with a sharp object.","zh":"jab someone with something 指用尖銳物快速戳或刺某人。"},{"en":"A nurse may jab a patient with a needle quickly but carefully during an injection.","zh":"護士注射時可能快速但小心地用針刺病人。"},{"en":"A jab can hurt because force is concentrated in a small point.","zh":"刺一下會痛，因為力量集中在一個小點上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a quick sharp action.","zh":"這個短語描述快速尖銳的動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"finish someone off","meaning":"終結某人；給予致命一擊","examples":[{"en":"The example imagines finishing an adversary off with a final attack.","zh":"這個例子想像以最後一擊終結對手。"},{"en":"To finish someone off means to defeat, kill, or completely overcome them.","zh":"finish someone off 指擊敗、殺死或完全壓倒某人。"},{"en":"In a video game, a player may finish an enemy off with one final move.","zh":"在電子遊戲中，玩家可能用最後一招終結敵人。"},{"en":"This phrase is forceful and can sound violent, so it should be used carefully.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈且可能帶暴力意味，因此應小心使用。"},{"en":"It describes the final action that ends someone’s resistance.","zh":"它描述結束某人抵抗的最後行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at work","meaning":"正在發揮作用","examples":[{"en":"That is venom at work.","zh":"那就是毒液正在發揮作用。"},{"en":"At work means actively operating and producing an effect.","zh":"at work 指正在運作並產生效果。"},{"en":"When students become calmer after clear instructions, good classroom management is at work.","zh":"當學生在清楚指示後變得較冷靜，就是良好課室管理正在發揮作用。"},{"en":"Venom at work means its chemicals are acting inside the body.","zh":"venom at work 指其化學物質正在身體內起作用。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the process causing the visible result.","zh":"這個短語指出造成可見結果的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ironically","meaning":"諷刺的是","examples":[{"en":"Ironically, the same properties make venom useful for medicine.","zh":"諷刺的是，正是同樣特性令毒液對醫學有用。"},{"en":"Ironically means in a surprising way that is opposite to what one might expect.","zh":"ironically 指以令人意外、與預期相反的方式。"},{"en":"Ironically, a student who feared public speaking later became a drama teacher.","zh":"諷刺的是，一名害怕公開演說的學生後來成為戲劇老師。"},{"en":"This word is used when reality turns against the obvious expectation.","zh":"當現實與表面預期相反時，會使用這個詞。"},{"en":"Here, it is ironic because a deadly substance may also help save lives.","zh":"在這裡，諷刺之處在於致命物質也可能幫助拯救生命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"properties that make","meaning":"令……的特性","examples":[{"en":"The properties that make venom deadly also make it valuable.","zh":"令毒液致命的特性也令它有價值。"},{"en":"Properties that make something do something are its qualities or features that cause that result.","zh":"properties that make something do something 指某物造成某結果的品質或特徵。"},{"en":"The properties that make glass clear also make it useful for windows.","zh":"令玻璃透明的特性也令它適合用作窗戶。"},{"en":"A substance’s properties can create both danger and usefulness depending on context.","zh":"某物質的特性可以因語境不同而產生危險和用途。"},{"en":"This phrase links a feature with the effect it produces.","zh":"這個短語把特徵與它產生的效果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"valuable for medicine","meaning":"對醫學有價值","examples":[{"en":"Venom can be valuable for medicine.","zh":"毒液可以對醫學有價值。"},{"en":"Valuable for medicine means useful for developing treatments, understanding disease, or improving health.","zh":"valuable for medicine 指對研發治療、理解疾病或改善健康有用。"},{"en":"A rare plant may be valuable for medicine if it contains a compound that lowers fever.","zh":"如果稀有植物含有能退燒的化合物，它可能對醫學有價值。"},{"en":"Venom is valuable for medicine because its toxins can target body systems very precisely.","zh":"毒液對醫學有價值，因為其毒素可以非常精準地針對身體系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes scientific usefulness, not ordinary safety.","zh":"這個短語描述科學用途，而不是日常安全性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"target the same molecules","meaning":"針對相同分子","examples":[{"en":"Many venom toxins target the same molecules that medicine needs to control.","zh":"許多毒液毒素針對醫學需要控制的相同分子。"},{"en":"To target the same molecules means to act on the same tiny structures inside the body.","zh":"target the same molecules 指作用於身體內相同的微小結構。"},{"en":"Two different medicines may target the same molecules involved in blood pressure.","zh":"兩種不同藥物可能針對與血壓有關的相同分子。"},{"en":"If venom and medicine target similar molecules, venom can help scientists design better drugs.","zh":"如果毒液和藥物針對類似分子，毒液可以幫助科學家設計更好藥物。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why dangerous toxins can be useful for research.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何危險毒素能對研究有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"treat diseases","meaning":"治療疾病","examples":[{"en":"Some toxins may help scientists treat diseases.","zh":"有些毒素可能幫助科學家治療疾病。"},{"en":"To treat diseases means to use medical methods to reduce, control, or cure illnesses.","zh":"treat diseases 指使用醫療方法減輕、控制或治癒疾病。"},{"en":"Doctors treat diseases with medicine, surgery, lifestyle advice, or therapy.","zh":"醫生透過藥物、手術、生活方式建議或治療來治療疾病。"},{"en":"New treatments are valuable when existing methods do not work well enough.","zh":"當現有方法效果不足，新治療就有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to medical care aimed at improving illness.","zh":"這個短語指旨在改善疾病的醫療護理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"work fast","meaning":"作用迅速","examples":[{"en":"Venom works fast and is highly specific.","zh":"毒液作用迅速，而且高度針對性。"},{"en":"To work fast means to produce an effect quickly.","zh":"work fast 指快速產生效果。"},{"en":"A painkiller that works fast may reduce a headache within minutes.","zh":"作用迅速的止痛藥可能在幾分鐘內減輕頭痛。"},{"en":"Venom must work fast because predators need prey to stop moving quickly.","zh":"毒液必須作用迅速，因為捕食者需要獵物快速停止移動。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on speed of action.","zh":"這個短語著重作用速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"highly specific","meaning":"高度針對性","examples":[{"en":"Venom is highly specific in its effects.","zh":"毒液的作用高度針對性。"},{"en":"Highly specific means acting on a precise target rather than affecting everything generally.","zh":"highly specific 指作用於精確目標，而不是廣泛影響所有東西。"},{"en":"A highly specific medicine may affect one type of receptor without disturbing many others.","zh":"高度針對性的藥物可能影響一種受體，而不干擾許多其他受體。"},{"en":"Specificity matters because it can reduce unwanted side effects.","zh":"針對性很重要，因為它可以減少不想要的副作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes precision and selectivity.","zh":"這個短語描述精準和選擇性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"active components","meaning":"活性成分","examples":[{"en":"The active components of venom include peptides and proteins.","zh":"毒液的活性成分包括肽和蛋白質。"},{"en":"Active components are the parts of a substance that produce biological or chemical effects.","zh":"active components 指某物質中產生生物或化學作用的部分。"},{"en":"The active component in a headache tablet is the chemical that reduces pain.","zh":"頭痛藥中的活性成分是減輕疼痛的化學物質。"},{"en":"Identifying active components helps scientists separate useful effects from harmful ones.","zh":"識別活性成分幫助科學家把有用效果與有害效果分開。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the working parts of a mixture.","zh":"這個短語指混合物中真正起作用的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"toxins and enzymes","meaning":"毒素和酶","examples":[{"en":"The active components work as toxins and enzymes.","zh":"這些活性成分以毒素和酶的形式發揮作用。"},{"en":"Toxins and enzymes are biological molecules that can harm cells or speed up chemical reactions.","zh":"toxins and enzymes 指可以傷害細胞或加快化學反應的生物分子。"},{"en":"In digestion, enzymes help break food down into smaller substances.","zh":"在消化中，酶幫助把食物分解成較小物質。"},{"en":"In venom, toxins and enzymes can damage tissue, affect nerves, or change blood behaviour.","zh":"在毒液中，毒素和酶可以損害組織、影響神經或改變血液行為。"},{"en":"This phrase names two types of active biological substances.","zh":"這個短語命名兩類活性生物物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"particular molecules","meaning":"特定分子","examples":[{"en":"Venom toxins target particular molecules.","zh":"毒液毒素針對特定分子。"},{"en":"Particular molecules are specific tiny chemical structures in the body.","zh":"particular molecules 指身體內特定的微小化學結構。"},{"en":"A medicine may be designed to attach to particular molecules on cancer cells.","zh":"藥物可能被設計成附着在癌細胞上的特定分子。"},{"en":"Targeting particular molecules can make a treatment more precise.","zh":"針對特定分子可以令治療更精準。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the action is selective, not random.","zh":"這個短語顯示作用是有選擇性的，而不是隨機的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fit into","meaning":"契合；嵌入","examples":[{"en":"The molecules fit into targets like keys into locks.","zh":"這些分子像鑰匙插入鎖一樣契合目標。"},{"en":"To fit into something means to match its shape or space closely enough to enter or attach.","zh":"fit into something 指形狀或空間配合得足以進入或附着。"},{"en":"A phone charger plug must fit into the correct socket before it can work.","zh":"手機充電器插頭必須插入正確插座才能運作。"},{"en":"Molecules that fit into biological targets can start, stop, or change body processes.","zh":"能嵌入生物目標的分子可以啟動、停止或改變身體過程。"},{"en":"This phrase explains physical or molecular matching.","zh":"這個短語解釋實體或分子層面的配合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"like keys into locks","meaning":"像鑰匙插入鎖一樣","examples":[{"en":"Venom molecules fit into targets like keys into locks.","zh":"毒液分子像鑰匙插入鎖一樣嵌入目標。"},{"en":"Like keys into locks means with a precise shape match between two parts.","zh":"like keys into locks 指兩個部分在形狀上精確配合。"},{"en":"A password works like a key into a lock when it opens only the correct account.","zh":"當密碼只能打開正確帳戶，它就像鑰匙插入鎖一樣發揮作用。"},{"en":"This comparison helps explain why some molecules affect only certain targets.","zh":"這個比較幫助解釋為何某些分子只影響特定目標。"},{"en":"It shows precision, not rough contact.","zh":"它顯示精準，而不是粗略接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"molecular locks","meaning":"分子鎖","examples":[{"en":"Medicines work by fitting into molecular locks.","zh":"藥物透過嵌入分子鎖來發揮作用。"},{"en":"Molecular locks are specific biological targets that molecules can attach to, like keys fitting into locks.","zh":"molecular locks 指分子可以附着的特定生物目標，就像鑰匙配合鎖一樣。"},{"en":"A drug may open or block a molecular lock on a cell surface.","zh":"藥物可能打開或阻塞細胞表面的分子鎖。"},{"en":"Understanding molecular locks helps scientists design drugs with fewer side effects.","zh":"理解分子鎖幫助科學家設計副作用較少的藥物。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a simple image to explain precise molecular targeting.","zh":"這個短語用簡單圖像解釋精準分子靶向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"thwart ill effects","meaning":"阻止不良影響","examples":[{"en":"Medicines control molecular locks to thwart ill effects.","zh":"藥物控制分子鎖，以阻止不良影響。"},{"en":"To thwart ill effects means to prevent or reduce harmful results.","zh":"thwart ill effects 指防止或減少有害結果。"},{"en":"Sunscreen can thwart ill effects of strong sunlight by protecting the skin.","zh":"防曬用品可以透過保護皮膚來阻止強烈陽光的不良影響。"},{"en":"A medicine may thwart ill effects by blocking a harmful chemical signal.","zh":"藥物可能透過阻塞有害化學訊號來阻止不良影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stopping damage before it becomes worse.","zh":"這個短語描述在損害惡化前阻止它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a challenge to find","meaning":"尋找……是一項挑戰","examples":[{"en":"It is a challenge to find a toxin that hits only one target.","zh":"尋找只擊中一個目標的毒素是一項挑戰。"},{"en":"A challenge to find something means it is difficult to discover or identify it.","zh":"a challenge to find something 指發現或識別某物很困難。"},{"en":"It is a challenge to find quiet study space in a crowded school library.","zh":"在擠迫的學校圖書館尋找安靜自修空間是一項挑戰。"},{"en":"Finding a specific toxin is hard because venom contains many similar molecules.","zh":"尋找特定毒素很難，因為毒液含有許多相似分子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficulty in searching.","zh":"這個短語描述搜尋上的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"hit only a certain target","meaning":"只擊中某個特定目標","examples":[{"en":"Researchers need toxins that hit only a certain target.","zh":"研究人員需要只擊中某個特定目標的毒素。"},{"en":"To hit only a certain target means to affect one specific thing and avoid others.","zh":"hit only a certain target 指只影響某一特定事物並避開其他事物。"},{"en":"A good grammar exercise should hit only a certain target, such as articles, before moving to harder skills.","zh":"好的文法練習在進入更難技巧前，應只擊中某個特定目標，例如冠詞。"},{"en":"In medicine, hitting only one target can reduce unwanted side effects.","zh":"在醫學中，只擊中一個目標可以減少不想要的副作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes precision and selectivity.","zh":"這個短語描述精準和選擇性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"top medicines for","meaning":"治療……的重要藥物","examples":[{"en":"Top medicines for heart disease and diabetes have been derived from venom.","zh":"治療心臟病和糖尿病的重要藥物有些源自毒液。"},{"en":"Top medicines for a disease are important or widely used treatments for that condition.","zh":"top medicines for a disease 指治療某疾病的重要或廣泛使用藥物。"},{"en":"Doctors choose top medicines for high blood pressure based on evidence, safety, and patient needs.","zh":"醫生根據證據、安全性和病人需要，選擇治療高血壓的重要藥物。"},{"en":"A medicine becomes important when it works reliably for many patients.","zh":"當藥物對許多病人可靠有效，它就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies leading treatments in a medical area.","zh":"這個短語指出某醫學範疇中的主要治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be derived from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"Some medicines are derived from venom.","zh":"有些藥物源自毒液。"},{"en":"To be derived from something means to come from it or be developed from it.","zh":"be derived from something 指來自某物或由某物發展而來。"},{"en":"Some modern drugs are derived from chemicals first found in plants.","zh":"有些現代藥物源自最初在植物中發現的化學物質。"},{"en":"A medicine derived from venom may be changed and tested before it becomes safe for patients.","zh":"源自毒液的藥物可能經過改造和測試，才變得對病人安全。"},{"en":"This phrase explains origin or source.","zh":"這個短語解釋來源或起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"heart disease and diabetes","meaning":"心臟病和糖尿病","examples":[{"en":"Venom-derived drugs can treat heart disease and diabetes.","zh":"源自毒液的藥物可以治療心臟病和糖尿病。"},{"en":"Heart disease and diabetes are common serious illnesses affecting the heart, blood vessels, or blood sugar control.","zh":"heart disease and diabetes 指影響心臟、血管或血糖控制的常見嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"A clinic may monitor patients with heart disease and diabetes regularly.","zh":"診所可能定期監察患有心臟病和糖尿病的病人。"},{"en":"Better medicines for heart disease and diabetes can prevent complications and save lives.","zh":"更好的心臟病和糖尿病藥物可以預防併發症並拯救生命。"},{"en":"This phrase names two major long-term health problems.","zh":"這個短語命名兩種主要長期健康問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"autoimmune diseases","meaning":"自身免疫病","examples":[{"en":"New treatments for autoimmune diseases may become available.","zh":"治療自身免疫病的新方法可能會出現。"},{"en":"Autoimmune diseases are illnesses in which the immune system attacks the body’s own tissues.","zh":"autoimmune diseases 指免疫系統攻擊身體自身組織的疾病。"},{"en":"A patient with an autoimmune disease may experience tiredness, pain, swelling, or flare-ups.","zh":"自身免疫病患者可能經歷疲倦、疼痛、腫脹或病情發作。"},{"en":"New treatments matter because autoimmune diseases can be long-term and hard to control.","zh":"新治療很重要，因為自身免疫病可以長期且難以控制。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a group of immune-system disorders.","zh":"這個短語指一類免疫系統疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"within a decade","meaning":"在十年內","examples":[{"en":"New treatments could be available within a decade.","zh":"新治療可能在十年內可用。"},{"en":"Within a decade means within ten years.","zh":"within a decade 指在十年之內。"},{"en":"A school may hope to rebuild its old library within a decade.","zh":"學校可能希望在十年內重建舊圖書館。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a long but limited future time frame.","zh":"這個短語給出較長但有限的未來時間框架。"},{"en":"It suggests something is not immediate but may happen within a realistic period.","zh":"它暗示某事不是立即發生，但可能在現實時期內出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"novel drugs","meaning":"新型藥物","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are not talking about just a few novel drugs.","zh":"研究人員談論的不只是幾種新型藥物。"},{"en":"Novel drugs are new medicines that work in new ways or treat conditions differently.","zh":"novel drugs 指以新方式發揮作用或以不同方法治療病症的新藥。"},{"en":"A hospital may join a clinical trial for a novel drug when existing treatment is not enough.","zh":"當現有治療不足，醫院可能參與新型藥物的臨床試驗。"},{"en":"Novel drugs can create hope, but they must be tested carefully for safety and effectiveness.","zh":"新型藥物可以帶來希望，但必須仔細測試其安全性和有效性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to new medical treatments, not simply newly packaged old medicine.","zh":"這個短語指新的醫療治療，而不只是重新包裝的舊藥。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"entire classes of drugs","meaning":"整類藥物","examples":[{"en":"Venom may lead to entire classes of drugs.","zh":"毒液可能帶來整類藥物。"},{"en":"Entire classes of drugs are whole groups of medicines that share a similar mechanism or purpose.","zh":"entire classes of drugs 指具有相似機制或用途的整組藥物。"},{"en":"Antibiotics are an entire class of drugs used to treat bacterial infections.","zh":"抗生素是用來治療細菌感染的整類藥物。"},{"en":"Discovering one useful toxin can sometimes inspire many related medicines.","zh":"發現一種有用毒素有時可以啟發許多相關藥物。"},{"en":"This phrase means much more than one or two individual drugs.","zh":"這個短語表示遠多於一兩種個別藥物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"toxinologist","meaning":"毒素學家","examples":[{"en":"Zoltan Takacs is a toxinologist and herpetologist.","zh":"Zoltan Takacs 是毒素學家和爬蟲及兩棲動物學家。"},{"en":"A toxinologist is a scientist who studies toxins, especially how they affect living organisms.","zh":"toxinologist 指研究毒素，尤其是其如何影響生物的科學家。"},{"en":"A toxinologist may study snake venom to understand how it changes blood clotting.","zh":"毒素學家可能研究蛇毒，以了解它如何改變血液凝結。"},{"en":"Toxinologists help medicine by identifying dangerous and useful effects of toxins.","zh":"毒素學家透過識別毒素的危險和有用效果來幫助醫學。"},{"en":"This word names a specialist in the science of toxins.","zh":"這個詞命名研究毒素科學的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"herpetologist","meaning":"爬蟲及兩棲動物學家","examples":[{"en":"A herpetologist studies reptiles and amphibians.","zh":"爬蟲及兩棲動物學家研究爬蟲類和兩棲動物。"},{"en":"A herpetologist is a scientist who studies animals such as snakes, lizards, frogs, and salamanders.","zh":"herpetologist 指研究蛇、蜥蜴、青蛙和蠑螈等動物的科學家。"},{"en":"A museum may invite a herpetologist to explain how snakes use venom.","zh":"博物館可能邀請爬蟲及兩棲動物學家解釋蛇如何使用毒液。"},{"en":"Herpetologists help protect species by studying their habitats, behaviour, and threats.","zh":"爬蟲及兩棲動物學家透過研究棲息地、行為和威脅來幫助保護物種。"},{"en":"This word names a specialist in reptiles and amphibians.","zh":"這個詞命名爬蟲類和兩棲動物方面的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"so far","meaning":"到目前為止","examples":[{"en":"So far, fewer than a thousand toxins have been studied for medicinal value.","zh":"到目前為止，少於一千種毒素被研究其藥用價值。"},{"en":"So far means up to the present point in time.","zh":"so far 指到目前這個時間點為止。"},{"en":"So far, the class has learned ten new grammar patterns this term.","zh":"到目前為止，這班今個學期已學了十個新文法句式。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that more may happen later.","zh":"這個短語暗示之後可能還會有更多進展。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing progress that is not yet complete.","zh":"當描述尚未完成的進度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"fewer than","meaning":"少於","examples":[{"en":"Fewer than a thousand toxins have been scrutinised for medicinal value.","zh":"少於一千種毒素被仔細研究其藥用價值。"},{"en":"Fewer than means a smaller number than the number mentioned.","zh":"fewer than 指數量少於所提及的數字。"},{"en":"Fewer than ten students arrived before eight o’clock.","zh":"少於十名學生在八點前到達。"},{"en":"This phrase is used with countable things, such as people, books, or toxins.","zh":"這個短語用於可數事物，例如人、書或毒素。"},{"en":"It shows that the actual number is below a stated limit.","zh":"它顯示實際數量低於某個限度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be scrutinised for","meaning":"因……而被仔細研究","examples":[{"en":"Venom toxins are scrutinised for medicinal value.","zh":"毒液毒素因藥用價值而被仔細研究。"},{"en":"To be scrutinised for something means to be examined very carefully to find that quality or use.","zh":"be scrutinised for something 指為找出某種特質或用途而被非常仔細地檢查。"},{"en":"A school’s safety plan may be scrutinised for weaknesses before a trip.","zh":"學校旅行前，安全計劃可能因弱點而被仔細審視。"},{"en":"Scientists scrutinise toxins for medical value because small details can matter greatly.","zh":"科學家仔細研究毒素的醫學價值，因為細微差異可以非常重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful, detailed examination.","zh":"這個短語描述細緻而仔細的檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"medicinal value","meaning":"藥用價值","examples":[{"en":"Many toxins may have medicinal value.","zh":"許多毒素可能有藥用價值。"},{"en":"Medicinal value is usefulness for treating disease, reducing symptoms, or improving health.","zh":"medicinal value 指對治療疾病、減輕症狀或改善健康有用。"},{"en":"A herb has medicinal value only if careful testing shows that it helps safely.","zh":"草藥只有在仔細測試顯示安全有效時，才有藥用價值。"},{"en":"Medicinal value must be separated from danger through research and testing.","zh":"藥用價值必須透過研究和測試與危險分開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes possible medical usefulness.","zh":"這個短語描述可能的醫學用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a dozen or so","meaning":"大約十多種","examples":[{"en":"A dozen or so major drugs have made it to market.","zh":"大約十多種重要藥物已成功推出市場。"},{"en":"A dozen or so means about twelve, not an exact number.","zh":"a dozen or so 指大約十二個，不是精確數字。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students a dozen or so practice questions before a test.","zh":"老師可能在測驗前給學生大約十多條練習題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the number is approximate but close to twelve.","zh":"當數字是約數但接近十二時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It suggests a small but noticeable group.","zh":"它暗示一個小但值得注意的群組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"major drugs","meaning":"重要藥物","examples":[{"en":"A dozen or so major drugs have come from venom research.","zh":"大約十多種重要藥物來自毒液研究。"},{"en":"Major drugs are important medicines that are widely used or medically significant.","zh":"major drugs 指廣泛使用或在醫學上重要的藥物。"},{"en":"A major drug for high blood pressure can help many patients avoid complications.","zh":"治療高血壓的重要藥物可以幫助許多病人避免併發症。"},{"en":"Drugs become major when doctors rely on them and evidence supports their use.","zh":"當醫生依賴某些藥物且證據支持其使用，它們就成為重要藥物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to important medicines, not minor experimental compounds.","zh":"這個短語指重要藥物，而不是次要實驗化合物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make it to market","meaning":"成功推出市場","examples":[{"en":"Only a small number of venom-based drugs have made it to market.","zh":"只有少數毒液基礎藥物成功推出市場。"},{"en":"To make it to market means to pass development and approval so a product can be sold.","zh":"make it to market 指通過開發和批准，使產品可以出售。"},{"en":"Many student business ideas never make it to market because they are too expensive to produce.","zh":"許多學生商業想法因生產成本太高而無法成功推出市場。"},{"en":"A drug must pass strict testing before it can make it to market.","zh":"藥物必須通過嚴格測試，才可以成功推出市場。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching real public availability.","zh":"這個短語描述真正達到公眾可獲得的階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"upwards of","meaning":"多達；超過","examples":[{"en":"There could be upwards of 20 million venom toxins.","zh":"毒液毒素可能多達二千萬種。"},{"en":"Upwards of means more than or at least a very large number.","zh":"upwards of 指超過或至少達到一個很大的數字。"},{"en":"A popular school event may attract upwards of 500 visitors.","zh":"受歡迎的學校活動可能吸引多達 500 名訪客。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the number may be surprisingly high.","zh":"這個短語強調數字可能高得令人驚訝。"},{"en":"It is often used before large estimates.","zh":"它常用於大型估算前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"waiting to be screened","meaning":"等待被篩選","examples":[{"en":"Millions of venom toxins may be waiting to be screened.","zh":"數以百萬計的毒液毒素可能仍等待被篩選。"},{"en":"Waiting to be screened means not yet tested or examined for a particular purpose.","zh":"waiting to be screened 指尚未為特定目的接受測試或檢查。"},{"en":"Job applications may be waiting to be screened before interviews are arranged.","zh":"求職申請可能等待被篩選，之後才安排面試。"},{"en":"Toxins waiting to be screened may contain useful compounds that scientists have not yet found.","zh":"等待被篩選的毒素可能含有科學家尚未發現的有用化合物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a backlog of items still needing examination.","zh":"這個短語描述仍需檢查的大量項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"open up whole new avenues of","meaning":"開拓……的全新途徑","examples":[{"en":"Venom has opened up whole new avenues of pharmacology.","zh":"毒液開拓了藥理學的全新途徑。"},{"en":"To open up whole new avenues of something means to create completely new directions for study, work, or development.","zh":"open up whole new avenues of something 指為研究、工作或發展創造全新方向。"},{"en":"Online learning opened up whole new avenues of education for students in remote areas.","zh":"網上學習為偏遠地區學生開拓了教育的全新途徑。"},{"en":"New discoveries open up new avenues when they allow researchers to ask questions that were impossible before.","zh":"當新發現讓研究人員提出以前不可能提出的問題，就開拓了新途徑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes major expansion of possibilities.","zh":"這個短語描述可能性的重大擴展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"pharmacology","meaning":"藥理學","examples":[{"en":"Venom research has influenced pharmacology.","zh":"毒液研究影響了藥理學。"},{"en":"Pharmacology is the scientific study of drugs and how they affect the body.","zh":"pharmacology 指研究藥物及其如何影響身體的科學。"},{"en":"A pharmacology student learns why one medicine lowers blood pressure and another reduces pain.","zh":"藥理學學生學習為何一種藥物降低血壓，而另一種減輕疼痛。"},{"en":"Pharmacology helps doctors use medicines safely and helps scientists design new ones.","zh":"藥理學幫助醫生安全用藥，也幫助科學家設計新藥。"},{"en":"This word refers to the science behind medicines.","zh":"這個詞指藥物背後的科學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"venom and poison sources","meaning":"毒液和毒物來源","examples":[{"en":"Toxins from venom and poison sources are useful for research.","zh":"來自毒液和毒物來源的毒素對研究有用。"},{"en":"Venom and poison sources are animals, plants, or substances that produce toxic chemicals.","zh":"venom and poison sources 指產生有毒化學物質的動物、植物或物質。"},{"en":"A laboratory may study venom and poison sources such as snakes, puffer fish, and poisonous plants.","zh":"實驗室可能研究蛇、河豚和有毒植物等毒液和毒物來源。"},{"en":"These sources help researchers understand how toxins affect cells and organs.","zh":"這些來源幫助研究人員理解毒素如何影響細胞和器官。"},{"en":"This phrase groups together different origins of toxins.","zh":"這個短語把毒素的不同來源歸在一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"give us a clearer picture of","meaning":"讓我們更清楚了解……","examples":[{"en":"Toxins give us a clearer picture of cellular functions.","zh":"毒素讓我們更清楚了解細胞功能。"},{"en":"To give us a clearer picture of something means to help us understand it better.","zh":"give us a clearer picture of something 指幫助我們更好理解某事。"},{"en":"A school survey can give teachers a clearer picture of why students are stressed.","zh":"學校調查可以讓老師更清楚了解學生為何有壓力。"},{"en":"Clearer understanding helps people make better decisions and ask better questions.","zh":"更清楚理解幫助人們作更好決定並提出更好問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improved knowledge or insight.","zh":"這個短語描述知識或洞察的提升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"crucial cellular functions","meaning":"重要細胞功能","examples":[{"en":"Proteins control many crucial cellular functions.","zh":"蛋白質控制許多重要細胞功能。"},{"en":"Crucial cellular functions are essential activities that cells need in order to live and work.","zh":"crucial cellular functions 指細胞生存和運作所需的必要活動。"},{"en":"Cells need crucial cellular functions such as energy production, communication, and repair.","zh":"細胞需要能量生產、溝通和修復等重要細胞功能。"},{"en":"If a toxin disrupts crucial cellular functions, tissues may become damaged.","zh":"如果毒素干擾重要細胞功能，組織可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to basic life processes inside cells.","zh":"這個短語指細胞內的基本生命過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"deadly poison","meaning":"致命毒素","examples":[{"en":"Tetrodotoxin is a deadly poison from puffer fish.","zh":"河豚毒素是來自河豚的致命毒素。"},{"en":"A deadly poison is a toxic substance that can kill if it enters the body in enough quantity.","zh":"deadly poison 指若足量進入身體即可致命的有毒物質。"},{"en":"A bottle of cleaning chemical can be a deadly poison if a child drinks it.","zh":"如果孩子飲下清潔化學品，一瓶清潔劑可以成為致命毒物。"},{"en":"Deadly poisons must be handled with strict care because even small amounts may be dangerous.","zh":"致命毒素必須嚴格小心處理，因為即使少量也可能危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extreme toxicity.","zh":"這個短語描述極高毒性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"tetrodotoxin","meaning":"河豚毒素","examples":[{"en":"Tetrodotoxin has helped scientists study nerve cells.","zh":"河豚毒素幫助科學家研究神經細胞。"},{"en":"Tetrodotoxin is a powerful toxin found in puffer fish and some other animals.","zh":"tetrodotoxin 指存在於河豚和一些其他動物中的強力毒素。"},{"en":"A biology class may learn about tetrodotoxin when studying how nerve signals move.","zh":"生物課研究神經訊號如何移動時，可能會學到河豚毒素。"},{"en":"Tetrodotoxin is dangerous because it can block nerve signals, but that same action makes it useful for research.","zh":"河豚毒素危險，因為它可以阻截神經訊號，但同一作用也令它對研究有用。"},{"en":"This word names a specific toxin, not a general category of poison.","zh":"這個詞命名一種特定毒素，而不是泛指毒物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"puffer fish","meaning":"河豚","examples":[{"en":"Puffer fish produce tetrodotoxin.","zh":"河豚會產生河豚毒素。"},{"en":"Puffer fish are fish known for inflating their bodies and containing dangerous toxin in some tissues.","zh":"puffer fish 指以身體膨脹和某些組織含危險毒素而聞名的魚。"},{"en":"A student may see puffer fish in an aquarium and notice their rounded shape.","zh":"學生可能在水族館看見河豚，並注意到牠們圓圓的形狀。"},{"en":"Because some puffer fish contain deadly toxin, preparing them as food can be dangerous without expert training.","zh":"因為有些河豚含致命毒素，沒有專家訓練而把牠們作食物處理可能很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase names the animal associated with tetrodotoxin.","zh":"這個短語命名與河豚毒素相關的動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"Studies of tetrodotoxin, for instance, have revealed details about nerve cells.","zh":"例如，河豚毒素研究揭示了神經細胞的細節。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance 指例如。"},{"en":"Some school rules protect safety; for instance, students must wear goggles in the laboratory.","zh":"有些學校規則保護安全；例如，學生在實驗室必須戴護目鏡。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a specific example to support a general point.","zh":"這個短語引入具體例子，以支持一般論點。"},{"en":"It helps readers move from an idea to a concrete case.","zh":"它幫助讀者由概念走向具體案例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reveal intricate details about","meaning":"揭示關於……的複雜細節","examples":[{"en":"Tetrodotoxin studies reveal intricate details about nerve communication.","zh":"河豚毒素研究揭示神經溝通的複雜細節。"},{"en":"To reveal intricate details about something means to show complex and precise information about it.","zh":"reveal intricate details about something 指展示有關某事的複雜而精確資料。"},{"en":"A medical scan can reveal intricate details about a patient’s heart structure.","zh":"醫學掃描可以揭示病人心臟結構的複雜細節。"},{"en":"Detailed research reveals hidden mechanisms that ordinary observation cannot show.","zh":"詳細研究揭示普通觀察看不到的隱藏機制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep, careful discovery.","zh":"這個短語描述深入而仔細的發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"nerve cells communicate","meaning":"神經細胞互相傳遞訊息","examples":[{"en":"Scientists study how nerve cells communicate.","zh":"科學家研究神經細胞如何互相傳遞訊息。"},{"en":"Nerve cells communicate by sending electrical and chemical signals to one another.","zh":"nerve cells communicate 指神經細胞透過電和化學訊號互相傳遞訊息。"},{"en":"A biology teacher may compare nerve cells communicating to students passing messages in a classroom.","zh":"生物老師可能把神經細胞溝通比作學生在課室傳遞訊息。"},{"en":"If nerve cells cannot communicate properly, movement, feeling, or thought may be affected.","zh":"如果神經細胞不能正常溝通，活動、感覺或思考可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how the nervous system sends information.","zh":"這個短語描述神經系統如何傳送資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be motivated to","meaning":"有動力去……","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are motivated to look for new compounds.","zh":"研究人員有動力去尋找新化合物。"},{"en":"To be motivated to do something means to have a strong reason or desire to do it.","zh":"be motivated to do something 指有強烈理由或願望去做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be motivated to revise after seeing clear improvement in practice tests.","zh":"學生看到練習測驗中有明顯進步後，可能有動力去溫習。"},{"en":"Motivation helps people continue difficult work even when results are slow.","zh":"動力幫助人即使結果緩慢，也繼續困難工作。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what drives someone to act.","zh":"這個短語解釋推動某人行動的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"new compounds","meaning":"新化合物","examples":[{"en":"Scientists look for new compounds that may reduce suffering.","zh":"科學家尋找可能減輕痛苦的新化合物。"},{"en":"New compounds are newly discovered or newly designed chemical substances.","zh":"new compounds 指新發現或新設計的化學物質。"},{"en":"A laboratory may test new compounds to see whether they can fight bacteria.","zh":"實驗室可能測試新化合物，看看它們能否對抗細菌。"},{"en":"New compounds can become medicines only after careful safety and effectiveness testing.","zh":"新化合物只有在仔細安全和有效性測試後，才可以成為藥物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to chemical candidates, not finished drugs necessarily.","zh":"這個短語指化學候選物，不一定是完成的藥物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lessen human suffering","meaning":"減輕人類痛苦","examples":[{"en":"Researchers hope to find compounds that lessen human suffering.","zh":"研究人員希望找到能減輕人類痛苦的化合物。"},{"en":"To lessen human suffering means to reduce pain, illness, fear, or hardship experienced by people.","zh":"lessen human suffering 指減少人們經歷的疼痛、疾病、恐懼或艱難。"},{"en":"A new pain treatment can lessen human suffering if it helps patients sleep and move again.","zh":"如果新止痛治療幫助病人重新睡覺和活動，就能減輕人類痛苦。"},{"en":"Medical research matters because it can turn scientific discovery into relief for real people.","zh":"醫學研究重要，因為它可以把科學發現轉化為真實人的舒緩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a humane goal behind science and medicine.","zh":"這個短語描述科學和醫學背後的人道目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"while doing that","meaning":"在做那件事的同時","examples":[{"en":"While doing that, researchers may uncover unexpected findings.","zh":"在做那件事的同時，研究人員可能發現意想不到的結果。"},{"en":"While doing that means during the process of doing the action just mentioned.","zh":"while doing that 指在進行剛提到的行動期間。"},{"en":"A student may organise old notes and, while doing that, find a useful exam tip.","zh":"學生整理舊筆記時，可能在做那件事的同時找到有用考試提示。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one discovery happens during another activity.","zh":"這個短語顯示一項發現發生於另一活動期間。"},{"en":"It connects the main task with a side result.","zh":"它把主要任務與附帶結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"uncover things","meaning":"發現事情","examples":[{"en":"Researchers may uncover things they do not expect.","zh":"研究人員可能發現他們沒有預期的事情。"},{"en":"To uncover things means to discover facts, details, or evidence that were hidden or unknown.","zh":"uncover things 指發現原本隱藏或未知的事實、細節或證據。"},{"en":"A school survey may uncover problems that students were afraid to mention openly.","zh":"學校調查可能發現學生害怕公開提及的問題。"},{"en":"Research can uncover things unexpectedly because careful observation reveals patterns.","zh":"研究可以意外發現事情，因為仔細觀察會揭示模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes discovery, often of something hidden.","zh":"這個短語描述發現，常指發現隱藏事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"driven in part by","meaning":"部分由……推動","examples":[{"en":"Yanagihara was driven in part by revenge for a jellyfish sting.","zh":"Yanagihara 的研究部分由對水母螫傷的報復心理推動。"},{"en":"Driven in part by something means partly motivated or caused by it.","zh":"driven in part by something 指部分受到某事推動或造成。"},{"en":"A student’s decision to study medicine may be driven in part by a family illness.","zh":"學生選擇讀醫可能部分由家庭疾病經歷推動。"},{"en":"People often have more than one reason for choosing a difficult path.","zh":"人們選擇困難道路時，常有多於一個原因。"},{"en":"This phrase shows one influence among several.","zh":"這個短語顯示多個影響因素中的其中一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"out of revenge for","meaning":"出於對……的報復心理","examples":[{"en":"She began the work partly out of revenge for a box jellyfish sting.","zh":"她開始這項工作部分出於對箱形水母螫傷的報復心理。"},{"en":"Out of revenge for something means because someone wants to respond to harm or hurt they experienced.","zh":"out of revenge for something 指因想回應自己曾經受到的傷害而行動。"},{"en":"A child may refuse to share toys out of revenge for being ignored earlier.","zh":"孩子可能因早前被忽視而出於報復心理拒絕分享玩具。"},{"en":"Revenge can motivate action, but it may also make judgement emotional.","zh":"報復心理可以推動行動，但也可能令判斷變得情緒化。"},{"en":"This phrase explains an action driven by a desire to get back at something or someone.","zh":"這個短語解釋由想報復某事或某人而驅動的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"box jellyfish sting","meaning":"箱形水母螫傷","examples":[{"en":"A box jellyfish sting motivated Yanagihara’s research.","zh":"箱形水母螫傷推動了 Yanagihara 的研究。"},{"en":"A box jellyfish sting is an injury caused by contact with the tentacles of a box jellyfish.","zh":"box jellyfish sting 指接觸箱形水母觸手所造成的傷害。"},{"en":"A swimmer may suffer a box jellyfish sting in tropical waters if warning signs are ignored.","zh":"如果忽視警告標誌，泳客可能在熱帶水域遭受箱形水母螫傷。"},{"en":"Box jellyfish stings can be extremely painful and may require urgent medical care.","zh":"箱形水母螫傷可以極度疼痛，並可能需要緊急醫療護理。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific and potentially dangerous marine injury.","zh":"這個短語命名一種特定且可能危險的海洋傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"endure a sting","meaning":"忍受螫傷","examples":[{"en":"Yanagihara endured a box jellyfish sting 15 years ago.","zh":"Yanagihara 在十五年前忍受了一次箱形水母螫傷。"},{"en":"To endure a sting means to suffer through the pain and effects of being stung.","zh":"endure a sting 指承受被螫後的疼痛和影響。"},{"en":"A child may endure a bee sting during a picnic and need first aid.","zh":"孩子在野餐期間可能忍受蜜蜂螫傷並需要急救。"},{"en":"Stings can be frightening because pain may appear suddenly and spread quickly.","zh":"螫傷可以令人害怕，因為疼痛可能突然出現並迅速擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests experiencing and surviving an unpleasant injury.","zh":"這個短語暗示經歷並撐過不愉快傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"potential wound-healing agent","meaning":"潛在傷口癒合劑","examples":[{"en":"She discovered a potential wound-healing agent.","zh":"她發現了一種潛在傷口癒合劑。"},{"en":"A potential wound-healing agent is a substance that may help damaged tissue repair itself.","zh":"potential wound-healing agent 指可能幫助受損組織自行修復的物質。"},{"en":"A laboratory may test a new gel as a potential wound-healing agent for burns.","zh":"實驗室可能測試一種新凝膠，作為治療燒傷的潛在傷口癒合劑。"},{"en":"Such an agent must be tested carefully before doctors use it on patients.","zh":"這類物質在醫生用於病人前必須仔細測試。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests possible medical use, not confirmed treatment.","zh":"這個短語表示可能的醫學用途，而不是已確定治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"wound-healing","meaning":"促進傷口癒合的","examples":[{"en":"The discovery may have wound-healing properties.","zh":"這項發現可能具有促進傷口癒合的特性。"},{"en":"Wound-healing means helping injured skin or tissue repair and close.","zh":"wound-healing 指幫助受傷皮膚或組織修復和閉合。"},{"en":"A cream with wound-healing effects may help a small cut close faster.","zh":"具有傷口癒合作用的藥膏可能幫助小傷口更快閉合。"},{"en":"Good wound-healing reduces infection risk and helps the body recover.","zh":"良好傷口癒合可以降低感染風險並幫助身體恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the repair of physical injury.","zh":"這個短語描述身體損傷的修復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"within the tubules","meaning":"在小管內","examples":[{"en":"The potential agent was found within the tubules that contain jellyfish venom.","zh":"這種潛在物質在含有水母毒液的小管內被發現。"},{"en":"Within the tubules means inside small tube-like structures.","zh":"within the tubules 指在細小管狀結構內。"},{"en":"A biology diagram may show fluid moving within the tubules of a plant or animal organ.","zh":"生物圖可能顯示液體在植物或動物器官的小管內流動。"},{"en":"Finding a compound within tubules helps scientists locate exactly where it is stored.","zh":"在小管內找到化合物，幫助科學家精確定位其儲存位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position inside tiny tubes.","zh":"這個短語描述位於微小管道內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"jellyfish venom","meaning":"水母毒液","examples":[{"en":"The tubules contain jellyfish venom.","zh":"這些小管含有水母毒液。"},{"en":"Jellyfish venom is the toxic substance delivered by jellyfish stinging cells or tentacles.","zh":"jellyfish venom 指由水母刺細胞或觸手送入的有毒物質。"},{"en":"A swimmer may feel burning pain if jellyfish venom enters the skin.","zh":"如果水母毒液進入皮膚，泳客可能感到灼痛。"},{"en":"Jellyfish venom can be dangerous because it may affect skin, nerves, or the heart.","zh":"水母毒液可能危險，因為它可能影響皮膚、神經或心臟。"},{"en":"This phrase names the venom produced by jellyfish.","zh":"這個短語命名水母產生的毒液。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"have nothing to do with","meaning":"與……無關","examples":[{"en":"The agent had nothing to do with the venom itself.","zh":"這種物質與毒液本身無關。"},{"en":"To have nothing to do with something means to be unrelated to it.","zh":"have nothing to do with something 指與某事無關。"},{"en":"A student’s headache may have nothing to do with homework if it was caused by lack of sleep.","zh":"如果學生頭痛是由睡眠不足造成，就可能與功課無關。"},{"en":"This phrase separates one possible cause from the real situation.","zh":"這個短語把一個可能原因與真實情況分開。"},{"en":"It is useful when correcting a wrong connection.","zh":"當糾正錯誤連繫時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"get intimate with","meaning":"深入接觸……","examples":[{"en":"By getting intimate with a noxious animal, she learned unexpected things.","zh":"透過深入接觸有害動物，她學到意想不到的事情。"},{"en":"To get intimate with something means to study it very closely and in great detail.","zh":"get intimate with something 指非常仔細而深入地研究某物。"},{"en":"A mechanic gets intimate with an engine by taking it apart and learning every part.","zh":"機械師拆開引擎並學習每個部分，就是深入了解引擎。"},{"en":"Close study can reveal details that casual observation misses.","zh":"深入研究可以揭示普通觀察錯過的細節。"},{"en":"In this context, the phrase means deep scientific familiarity, not romance.","zh":"在這個語境中，這個短語指深入科學熟悉，而不是浪漫關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"noxious animal","meaning":"有害動物","examples":[{"en":"A jellyfish can be a noxious animal.","zh":"水母可以是有害動物。"},{"en":"A noxious animal is an animal that can harm, poison, sting, or irritate humans or other animals.","zh":"noxious animal 指能傷害、下毒、螫傷或刺激人類或其他動物的動物。"},{"en":"A scorpion is a noxious animal because its sting can cause pain and illness.","zh":"蠍子是有害動物，因為其螫傷可以造成疼痛和疾病。"},{"en":"Noxious animals require caution because contact with them may cause injury.","zh":"有害動物需要小心，因為接觸牠們可能造成傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harmful animals, not simply ugly or unpopular ones.","zh":"這個短語描述有害動物，而不只是難看或不受歡迎的動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"beyond my expectations","meaning":"遠超我的預期","examples":[{"en":"Yanagihara said she had been informed way beyond her expectations.","zh":"Yanagihara 說她得到的啟發遠超她的預期。"},{"en":"Beyond my expectations means more than I expected or better than I imagined.","zh":"beyond my expectations 指比我預期更多或比我想像更好。"},{"en":"A student may say the teacher’s feedback helped beyond his expectations.","zh":"學生可能說老師的回饋幫助遠超他的預期。"},{"en":"Results beyond expectations can encourage people to continue difficult work.","zh":"超出預期的結果可以鼓勵人繼續困難工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an outcome that exceeds the original hope or prediction.","zh":"這個短語描述超越原本希望或預測的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"evolve to produce","meaning":"演化出產生……的能力","examples":[{"en":"More than 100,000 animals have evolved to produce venom.","zh":"超過十萬種動物演化出產生毒液的能力。"},{"en":"To evolve to produce something means to develop that ability gradually over many generations.","zh":"evolve to produce something 指經過許多世代逐漸發展出產生某物的能力。"},{"en":"Some plants evolved to produce bitter chemicals that stop animals from eating them.","zh":"有些植物演化出產生苦味化學物質的能力，以阻止動物吃掉它們。"},{"en":"Evolution creates useful traits when they help living things survive or reproduce.","zh":"當某些特徵幫助生物生存或繁殖，演化就會創造這些有用特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes biological development over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間發生的生物發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"glands to house it","meaning":"用來儲存它的腺體","examples":[{"en":"Venomous animals have glands to house venom.","zh":"有毒動物有腺體用來儲存毒液。"},{"en":"Glands to house it are body structures that store the venom inside the animal.","zh":"glands to house it 指在動物體內儲存毒液的身體結構。"},{"en":"A biology teacher may compare venom glands to small storage rooms in the body.","zh":"生物老師可能把毒液腺體比作身體中的小儲物室。"},{"en":"Without glands to house venom, an animal could not keep the venom ready for use.","zh":"如果沒有儲存毒液的腺體，動物就不能讓毒液隨時可用。"},{"en":"This phrase explains where venom is stored.","zh":"這個短語解釋毒液儲存在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"apparatuses to expel it","meaning":"用來排出它的器官","examples":[{"en":"Venomous animals have apparatuses to expel venom.","zh":"有毒動物有器官用來排出毒液。"},{"en":"Apparatuses to expel it are body structures used to push venom out.","zh":"apparatuses to expel it 指用來把毒液推出體外的身體結構。"},{"en":"A snake’s fangs and a scorpion’s stinger are apparatuses that expel venom.","zh":"蛇的毒牙和蠍子的螫針都是排出毒液的器官。"},{"en":"Storage alone is not enough; venomous animals need a way to deliver venom.","zh":"單靠儲存並不足夠；有毒動物需要輸送毒液的方法。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the delivery equipment of venomous animals.","zh":"這個短語解釋有毒動物的毒液輸送設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"cone snails","meaning":"芋螺","examples":[{"en":"Cone snails are among the animals that produce venom.","zh":"芋螺是會產生毒液的動物之一。"},{"en":"Cone snails are marine snails that use venom to capture prey.","zh":"cone snails 指用毒液捕捉獵物的海洋蝸牛。"},{"en":"A visitor at an aquarium may learn that some cone snails can be dangerous despite their beautiful shells.","zh":"水族館訪客可能學到，有些芋螺雖然外殼漂亮，但可以很危險。"},{"en":"Cone snail venom is useful for research because it contains many precise toxins.","zh":"芋螺毒液對研究有用，因為它含有許多精準毒素。"},{"en":"This phrase names a group of venomous sea snails.","zh":"這個短語命名一類有毒海螺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"duck-billed platypus","meaning":"鴨嘴獸","examples":[{"en":"The male duck-billed platypus is a venomous mammal.","zh":"雄性鴨嘴獸是有毒哺乳動物。"},{"en":"A duck-billed platypus is an unusual mammal with a bill, webbed feet, and egg-laying reproduction.","zh":"duck-billed platypus 指有鴨嘴、蹼足並以產卵繁殖的奇特哺乳動物。"},{"en":"A child may be surprised to learn that the duck-billed platypus is a mammal that lays eggs.","zh":"孩子可能驚訝地得知鴨嘴獸是會產卵的哺乳動物。"},{"en":"Male platypuses can use venom during competition with other males.","zh":"雄性鴨嘴獸可以在與其他雄性競爭時使用毒液。"},{"en":"This phrase names a distinctive Australian animal.","zh":"這個短語命名一種獨特的澳洲動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"ankle spurs","meaning":"踝刺","examples":[{"en":"The male platypus carries venom inside ankle spurs.","zh":"雄性鴨嘴獸在踝刺內攜帶毒液。"},{"en":"Ankle spurs are sharp structures near the ankle that some animals use for defence or attack.","zh":"ankle spurs 指靠近腳踝、某些動物用於防禦或攻擊的尖銳結構。"},{"en":"A museum display may show the ankle spurs of a male platypus beside its skeleton.","zh":"博物館展覽可能在雄性鴨嘴獸骨架旁展示其踝刺。"},{"en":"In male platypuses, ankle spurs can deliver venom during fights.","zh":"在雄性鴨嘴獸身上，踝刺可以在打鬥中輸送毒液。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the body part that stores or delivers venom.","zh":"這個短語指出儲存或輸送毒液的身體部位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"venomous mammals","meaning":"有毒哺乳動物","examples":[{"en":"The platypus is one of the few venomous mammals.","zh":"鴨嘴獸是少數有毒哺乳動物之一。"},{"en":"Venomous mammals are mammals that can produce and deliver venom.","zh":"venomous mammals 指能產生並輸送毒液的哺乳動物。"},{"en":"Most mammals are not venomous, so the platypus is unusual.","zh":"大多數哺乳動物沒有毒，因此鴨嘴獸很特別。"},{"en":"Studying venomous mammals helps scientists understand how venom evolved in different animal groups.","zh":"研究有毒哺乳動物幫助科學家理解毒液如何在不同動物類群中演化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rare type of mammal.","zh":"這個短語描述罕見類型的哺乳動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"emerge independently","meaning":"獨立出現","examples":[{"en":"Venom emerged independently in different animal groups.","zh":"毒液在不同動物類群中獨立出現。"},{"en":"To emerge independently means to develop separately in different places or groups.","zh":"emerge independently 指在不同地方或群體中分別發展出來。"},{"en":"Similar school rules may emerge independently in different schools facing the same safety problem.","zh":"面對同一安全問題的不同學校，可能獨立出現類似校規。"},{"en":"Venom emerged independently because different animals faced similar needs for hunting or defence.","zh":"毒液獨立出現，是因為不同動物面對相似的捕食或防禦需要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows separate origins, not one shared source.","zh":"這個短語顯示分開起源，而不是共同來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"again and again","meaning":"一次又一次","examples":[{"en":"Venom emerged again and again in evolution.","zh":"毒液在演化中一次又一次出現。"},{"en":"Again and again means repeatedly, many times.","zh":"again and again 指反覆、多次。"},{"en":"A student may make the same spelling mistake again and again before finally remembering it.","zh":"學生可能一次又一次犯同一拼字錯誤，最後才記住。"},{"en":"When a useful solution appears again and again, it suggests strong pressure or need.","zh":"當有用解決方案一次又一次出現，表示存在強大壓力或需要。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses repetition over time.","zh":"這個短語強調隨時間重複發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"animal groups","meaning":"動物類群","examples":[{"en":"Venom evolved in different animal groups.","zh":"毒液在不同動物類群中演化。"},{"en":"Animal groups are categories of animals that share certain features or ancestry.","zh":"animal groups 指共享某些特徵或祖先的動物分類。"},{"en":"Birds, reptiles, mammals, insects, and fish are broad animal groups.","zh":"鳥類、爬蟲類、哺乳類、昆蟲和魚類都是廣義動物類群。"},{"en":"Studying different animal groups helps scientists see whether traits evolved once or many times.","zh":"研究不同動物類群幫助科學家了解某特徵是演化一次還是多次。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to biological categories, not random collections of animals.","zh":"這個短語指生物分類，而不是隨機動物集合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"composition of the venom","meaning":"毒液成分","examples":[{"en":"The composition of the venom varies among snakes.","zh":"蛇之間的毒液成分有所不同。"},{"en":"The composition of the venom means what substances the venom contains and in what mixture.","zh":"composition of the venom 指毒液含有甚麼物質，以及它們如何混合。"},{"en":"A scientist may compare the composition of venom from young and adult snakes.","zh":"科學家可能比較幼蛇和成年蛇的毒液成分。"},{"en":"Different compositions can produce different symptoms and require different treatments.","zh":"不同成分可以產生不同症狀，並需要不同治療。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what venom is made of.","zh":"這個短語描述毒液由甚麼構成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a single snake species","meaning":"單一蛇種","examples":[{"en":"The venom of a single snake species can vary by location.","zh":"單一蛇種的毒液可以因地點而異。"},{"en":"A single snake species means one specific kind of snake.","zh":"a single snake species 指一種特定蛇類。"},{"en":"Researchers may study a single snake species across several regions to compare its venom.","zh":"研究人員可能研究分布於幾個地區的單一蛇種，以比較其毒液。"},{"en":"Even one species can vary because diet, habitat, and age may differ.","zh":"即使同一物種也可能不同，因為飲食、棲息地和年齡可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows the discussion to one type of snake.","zh":"這個短語把討論收窄到一種蛇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"vary from place to place","meaning":"因地區而異","examples":[{"en":"Snake venom can vary from place to place.","zh":"蛇毒可以因地區而異。"},{"en":"To vary from place to place means to be different in different locations.","zh":"vary from place to place 指在不同地點有所不同。"},{"en":"School lunch prices may vary from place to place depending on rent and food costs.","zh":"學校午餐價格可能因租金和食物成本而因地區而異。"},{"en":"Venom may vary by location because snakes eat different prey in different environments.","zh":"毒液可能因地點而不同，因為蛇在不同環境吃不同獵物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes geographical difference.","zh":"這個短語描述地理差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"between adults and their young","meaning":"成年個體與幼體之間","examples":[{"en":"Venom can differ between adults and their young.","zh":"毒液在成年個體與幼體之間可以不同。"},{"en":"Between adults and their young means comparing mature animals with their offspring.","zh":"between adults and their young 指比較成熟動物與其幼體。"},{"en":"A zoo keeper may notice differences in diet between adults and their young.","zh":"動物園管理員可能注意到成年個體與幼體之間的飲食差異。"},{"en":"Venom can differ by age because young animals and adults may hunt different prey.","zh":"毒液可以因年齡而不同，因為幼體和成年個體可能捕食不同獵物。"},{"en":"This phrase compares life stages within the same animal group.","zh":"這個短語比較同一動物類群內的生命階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"change with its diet","meaning":"隨其飲食而改變","examples":[{"en":"An individual snake’s venom may change with its diet.","zh":"單一蛇的毒液可能隨其飲食而改變。"},{"en":"To change with its diet means to become different when the animal eats different foods.","zh":"change with its diet 指當動物吃不同食物時變得不同。"},{"en":"A pet’s weight and energy may change with its diet if the owner changes its food.","zh":"如果主人更換寵物食物，寵物的體重和精力可能隨其飲食而改變。"},{"en":"A snake’s venom may change because different prey create different evolutionary pressures.","zh":"蛇毒可能改變，因為不同獵物創造不同演化壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase connects food intake with biological change.","zh":"這個短語把食物攝取與生物變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"fine-tune compounds","meaning":"微調化合物","examples":[{"en":"Evolution has been fine-tuning these compounds for millions of years.","zh":"演化數百萬年來一直微調這些化合物。"},{"en":"To fine-tune compounds means to adjust chemical substances in small precise ways.","zh":"fine-tune compounds 指以細小而精準的方式調整化學物質。"},{"en":"A chef fine-tunes a sauce by adding a little salt, sugar, or lemon juice.","zh":"廚師透過加入少量鹽、糖或檸檬汁來微調醬汁。"},{"en":"Evolution fine-tunes venom compounds when small changes improve survival.","zh":"當細小改變改善生存，演化就會微調毒液化合物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual precise adjustment.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步而精準的調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"molecular architecture","meaning":"分子結構","examples":[{"en":"Venom’s molecular architecture has existed for a very long time.","zh":"毒液的分子結構已存在很長時間。"},{"en":"Molecular architecture is the structure and arrangement of molecules.","zh":"molecular architecture 指分子的結構和排列。"},{"en":"A biology model can show the molecular architecture of DNA as a twisted ladder.","zh":"生物模型可以把 DNA 的分子結構展示成扭曲梯子。"},{"en":"Molecular architecture matters because shape affects how molecules fit into targets.","zh":"分子結構很重要，因為形狀影響分子如何嵌入目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes structure at the molecular level.","zh":"這個短語描述分子層面的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be in place","meaning":"已經存在","examples":[{"en":"The molecular architecture of venom has been in place much longer.","zh":"毒液的分子結構早已存在更長時間。"},{"en":"To be in place means to already exist or be established.","zh":"be in place 指已經存在或已經建立。"},{"en":"A school can start online lessons quickly if the technology is already in place.","zh":"如果科技已經到位，學校可以快速開始網課。"},{"en":"When a system is in place, new uses can build on it more easily.","zh":"當系統已經存在，新用途就能更容易在其上建立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something ready or established before a later development.","zh":"這個短語描述某物在後來發展前已準備好或已建立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"repurpose key molecules","meaning":"重新利用關鍵分子","examples":[{"en":"Nature repurposes key molecules from around the body.","zh":"大自然重新利用身體各處的關鍵分子。"},{"en":"To repurpose key molecules means to use important molecules for a new function.","zh":"repurpose key molecules 指把重要分子用於新的功能。"},{"en":"A school may repurpose old tablets as e-book readers instead of throwing them away.","zh":"學校可能把舊平板重新用作電子書閱讀器，而不是丟棄。"},{"en":"Nature can repurpose molecules when an existing structure becomes useful for defence or predation.","zh":"當現有結構對防禦或捕食變得有用，大自然可以重新利用分子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving something an additional or new role.","zh":"這個短語描述給予某物額外或新的角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"digestive tract","meaning":"消化道","examples":[{"en":"Nature may borrow molecules from the digestive tract.","zh":"大自然可能從消化道借用分子。"},{"en":"The digestive tract is the system of organs that breaks down food and absorbs nutrients.","zh":"digestive tract 指分解食物並吸收養分的器官系統。"},{"en":"A health teacher may explain how food travels through the digestive tract after eating.","zh":"健康老師可能解釋食物進食後如何通過消化道。"},{"en":"Molecules from the digestive tract may be useful elsewhere because they already break down substances.","zh":"來自消化道的分子可能在其他地方有用，因為它們本已能分解物質。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the body system involved in digestion.","zh":"這個短語指參與消化的身體系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"serve animals for","meaning":"為動物在……方面服務","examples":[{"en":"Repurposed molecules serve animals for predation or protection.","zh":"被重新利用的分子為動物在捕食或保護方面服務。"},{"en":"To serve animals for a purpose means to help animals achieve that purpose.","zh":"serve animals for a purpose 指幫助動物達成某目的。"},{"en":"Sharp claws serve cats for climbing, hunting, and defence.","zh":"尖爪為貓在攀爬、捕獵和防禦方面服務。"},{"en":"Molecules can serve animals for survival when they help capture prey or avoid attack.","zh":"當分子幫助捕捉獵物或避免攻擊，它們就為動物生存服務。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the function of a biological feature.","zh":"這個短語解釋生物特徵的功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"predation or protection","meaning":"捕食或保護","examples":[{"en":"Venom can serve animals for predation or protection.","zh":"毒液可以為動物在捕食或保護方面服務。"},{"en":"Predation or protection means hunting other animals for food or defending oneself from danger.","zh":"predation or protection 指捕獵其他動物作食物，或保護自己免受危險。"},{"en":"A spider uses venom for predation when it traps and bites an insect.","zh":"蜘蛛困住並咬昆蟲時，就是用毒液作捕食。"},{"en":"A bee uses venom for protection when it stings an animal that threatens the hive.","zh":"蜜蜂螫威脅蜂巢的動物時，就是用毒液作保護。"},{"en":"This phrase names two common survival functions of venom.","zh":"這個短語命名毒液兩種常見生存功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"it makes sense for","meaning":"……是合理的","examples":[{"en":"It makes sense for nature to reuse existing molecular scaffolds.","zh":"大自然重用現有分子骨架是合理的。"},{"en":"It makes sense for someone or something to do something means it is logical or reasonable.","zh":"it makes sense for someone or something to do something 指某人或某物做某事合乎邏輯或合理。"},{"en":"It makes sense for students to review mistakes before doing new exercises.","zh":"學生在做新練習前檢討錯誤是合理的。"},{"en":"Reusing what already works can save time and energy.","zh":"重用已經有效的東西可以節省時間和能源。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why an action is sensible.","zh":"這個短語解釋某行動為何合理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"molecular scaffolds","meaning":"分子骨架","examples":[{"en":"Nature reuses molecular scaffolds that are already in place.","zh":"大自然重用已經存在的分子骨架。"},{"en":"Molecular scaffolds are basic molecular structures that can be modified for different functions.","zh":"molecular scaffolds 指可被改造成不同功能的基本分子結構。"},{"en":"A drug designer may use a molecular scaffold as the starting shape for a new medicine.","zh":"藥物設計師可能使用分子骨架作為新藥的起始形狀。"},{"en":"Reusing scaffolds is efficient because the basic structure already works in the body.","zh":"重用骨架很有效率，因為基本結構已能在身體中運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reusable molecular frameworks.","zh":"這個短語描述可重用的分子框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a template from","meaning":"來自……的模板","examples":[{"en":"Nature can take a template from the brain to make a toxin.","zh":"大自然可以從腦部取一個模板來製造毒素。"},{"en":"A template from somewhere is a model or pattern taken from that source.","zh":"template from somewhere 指從某來源取得的模型或模式。"},{"en":"A student may take a template from a teacher’s essay plan before writing their own essay.","zh":"學生寫自己的文章前，可能從老師的文章計劃取一個模板。"},{"en":"Templates help because they provide a structure that can be adapted.","zh":"模板有幫助，因為它提供可被改造的結構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using an existing pattern as a starting point.","zh":"這個短語描述使用現有模式作起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"wreck the nervous system","meaning":"破壞神經系統","examples":[{"en":"A toxin may be designed to wreck the nervous system.","zh":"毒素可能被設計來破壞神經系統。"},{"en":"To wreck the nervous system means to seriously damage the body’s nerve communication and control.","zh":"wreck the nervous system 指嚴重損害身體的神經溝通和控制。"},{"en":"A severe injury can wreck the nervous system if it damages the spinal cord.","zh":"如果嚴重受傷損害脊髓，就可能破壞神經系統。"},{"en":"Venom that wrecks the nervous system can cause paralysis, pain, or loss of control.","zh":"破壞神經系統的毒液可以造成癱瘓、疼痛或控制喪失。"},{"en":"This phrase is strong and informal, showing serious destruction.","zh":"這個短語強烈而口語化，顯示嚴重破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"tiny changes","meaning":"微小改變","examples":[{"en":"Nature can make tiny changes to turn a molecule into a toxin.","zh":"大自然可以作出微小改變，把分子變成毒素。"},{"en":"Tiny changes are very small adjustments.","zh":"tiny changes 指非常細小的調整。"},{"en":"A teacher may make tiny changes to a worksheet so weaker students can understand it better.","zh":"老師可能對工作紙作出微小改變，使較弱學生更容易理解。"},{"en":"Tiny changes in a molecule can create large differences in how it affects the body.","zh":"分子的微小改變可以對其如何影響身體造成巨大差異。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that small adjustments can have big results.","zh":"這個短語顯示小調整可以帶來大結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"there you have it","meaning":"就這樣","examples":[{"en":"Make some tiny changes, and there you have it: a toxin.","zh":"作出一些微小改變，就這樣：一種毒素誕生了。"},{"en":"There you have it means that the result or explanation is now clear or complete.","zh":"there you have it 指結果或解釋現在已清楚或完整。"},{"en":"Add a title, examples, and a conclusion, and there you have it: a simple essay plan.","zh":"加上題目、例子和結論，就這樣：一個簡單文章計劃完成了。"},{"en":"This phrase is used after showing how something is made or explained.","zh":"這個短語用於展示某物如何製成或某事如何解釋之後。"},{"en":"It often gives a neat, conversational ending to an explanation.","zh":"它常為解釋帶來簡潔、口語化的結尾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"nonlethal defence","meaning":"非致命防禦","examples":[{"en":"Bees use venom as a nonlethal defence.","zh":"蜜蜂把毒液用作非致命防禦。"},{"en":"A nonlethal defence is a protective method that stops or warns an attacker without usually killing it.","zh":"nonlethal defence 指通常不殺死攻擊者，但能阻止或警告它的保護方法。"},{"en":"A school security alarm is a nonlethal defence because it scares intruders and alerts staff.","zh":"學校保安警鐘是非致命防禦，因為它嚇阻闖入者並提醒職員。"},{"en":"Bees can use stings to protect the hive even when the goal is not to kill the threat.","zh":"蜜蜂可以用螫針保護蜂巢，即使目的不是殺死威脅。"},{"en":"This phrase describes defence that is protective rather than necessarily deadly.","zh":"這個短語描述保護性而不一定致命的防禦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"rival males","meaning":"競爭雄性","examples":[{"en":"The male platypus uses venom to dominate rival males.","zh":"雄性鴨嘴獸使用毒液壓制競爭雄性。"},{"en":"Rival males are males competing with one another for mates, territory, or status.","zh":"rival males 指為交配、領地或地位互相競爭的雄性。"},{"en":"In some animal species, rival males fight during mating season.","zh":"在某些動物物種中，競爭雄性會在交配季節打鬥。"},{"en":"Competition between rival males can lead to displays, threats, or physical conflict.","zh":"競爭雄性之間的競爭可以導致展示、威嚇或身體衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes male-to-male competition in animals.","zh":"這個短語描述動物中雄性之間的競爭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"show someone who’s boss","meaning":"向某人顯示誰是老大","examples":[{"en":"The male platypus uses venom to show rival males who’s boss.","zh":"雄性鴨嘴獸使用毒液向競爭雄性顯示誰是老大。"},{"en":"To show someone who’s boss means to prove dominance or authority over them.","zh":"show someone who’s boss 指向某人證明自己的支配地位或權威。"},{"en":"A strict manager may try to show new workers who’s boss by controlling every decision.","zh":"嚴厲經理可能透過控制每個決定，向新員工顯示誰是老大。"},{"en":"In animals, showing who’s boss can reduce conflict by establishing rank.","zh":"在動物中，顯示誰是老大可以透過建立等級來減少衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often sounds forceful.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常聽起來有強硬意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"mating season","meaning":"交配季節","examples":[{"en":"The male platypus uses venom during mating season.","zh":"雄性鴨嘴獸在交配季節使用毒液。"},{"en":"Mating season is the time of year when animals seek partners and reproduce.","zh":"mating season 指動物尋找伴侶並繁殖的一年中特定時期。"},{"en":"During mating season, birds may sing more loudly to attract mates.","zh":"在交配季節，鳥類可能更大聲鳴叫以吸引伴侶。"},{"en":"Competition and display often increase during mating season.","zh":"競爭和展示常在交配季節增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a seasonal period linked to reproduction.","zh":"這個短語描述與繁殖有關的季節性時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"immobilise","meaning":"使……無法動彈","examples":[{"en":"Venom is often used to immobilise an animal’s next meal.","zh":"毒液常用來使動物的下一餐無法動彈。"},{"en":"To immobilise something means to stop it from moving.","zh":"immobilise 指使某物不能移動。"},{"en":"A cast can immobilise a broken arm so the bone can heal.","zh":"石膏可以固定骨折手臂，使骨頭癒合。"},{"en":"Predators immobilise prey so it cannot escape or fight back.","zh":"捕食者使獵物無法動彈，令牠不能逃走或反抗。"},{"en":"This verb describes making movement impossible or very difficult.","zh":"這個動詞描述令活動變得不可能或非常困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"accidental victims","meaning":"意外受害者","examples":[{"en":"Humans are often accidental victims of venomous animals.","zh":"人類常是有毒動物的意外受害者。"},{"en":"Accidental victims are people harmed unintentionally, not because they were the intended target.","zh":"accidental victims 指非預定目標、意外受到傷害的人。"},{"en":"A swimmer may become an accidental victim of a jellyfish while entering the sea.","zh":"泳客入海時可能成為水母的意外受害者。"},{"en":"Many bites happen when humans disturb animals by mistake.","zh":"許多咬傷在人類誤打擾動物時發生。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that harm can happen without deliberate attack.","zh":"這個短語顯示傷害可能不是蓄意攻擊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the World Health Organization estimates that","meaning":"世界衞生組織估計","examples":[{"en":"The World Health Organization estimates that millions of bites occur each year.","zh":"世界衞生組織估計每年發生數以百萬計咬傷。"},{"en":"The World Health Organization estimates that means this international health body gives an informed calculation or judgement.","zh":"the World Health Organization estimates that 指這個國際衞生組織給出有根據的計算或判斷。"},{"en":"The World Health Organization may estimate that a disease affects more people than official reports show.","zh":"世界衞生組織可能估計某疾病影響的人數比官方報告更多。"},{"en":"Such estimates are useful when exact counts are difficult to collect.","zh":"當精確數字難以收集，這類估計很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an authority-based estimate.","zh":"這個短語引入來自權威機構的估算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"some five million bites","meaning":"約五百萬宗咬傷","examples":[{"en":"Some five million bites occur every year.","zh":"每年約有五百萬宗咬傷。"},{"en":"Some five million bites means about five million bite cases.","zh":"some five million bites 指大約五百萬宗咬傷個案。"},{"en":"A report may say some five thousand visitors attended a festival, meaning roughly that number.","zh":"報告可能說約五千名訪客參加節日，意思是大約那個數字。"},{"en":"Using “some” before a number shows approximation rather than exact counting.","zh":"在數字前使用 “some” 顯示是約數而不是精確點算。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a large estimated number.","zh":"這個短語給出大型估算數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"actual number","meaning":"實際數字","examples":[{"en":"The actual number is presumed to be much higher.","zh":"實際數字被推定為高得多。"},{"en":"The actual number is the real total, not just the reported or estimated figure.","zh":"actual number 指真實總數，而不只是報告或估算數字。"},{"en":"The actual number of absent students may be higher if some parents have not called the school.","zh":"如果有些家長沒有致電學校，缺席學生的實際數字可能更高。"},{"en":"Official records can miss cases, so the actual number may be uncertain.","zh":"官方紀錄可能漏掉個案，因此實際數字可能不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts reality with recorded data.","zh":"這個短語把現實與記錄數據作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be presumed to be","meaning":"被推定為","examples":[{"en":"The actual number is presumed to be much higher.","zh":"實際數字被推定為高得多。"},{"en":"To be presumed to be something means to be believed likely, though not fully proven.","zh":"be presumed to be something 指被認為很可能是某情況，但未完全證實。"},{"en":"A missing library book is presumed to be lost until a student returns it.","zh":"失蹤的圖書在學生歸還前被推定為遺失。"},{"en":"Presumptions are made when evidence points one way but certainty is unavailable.","zh":"當證據指向某方向但沒有確定性，人們會作出推定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reasonable assumption.","zh":"這個短語描述合理假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"rural areas","meaning":"鄉郊地區","examples":[{"en":"Most bites occur in rural areas of developing countries.","zh":"大多數咬傷發生在發展中國家的鄉郊地區。"},{"en":"Rural areas are countryside regions with villages, farms, and lower population density.","zh":"rural areas 指有村莊、農田且人口密度較低的鄉村地區。"},{"en":"A rural area may have fewer clinics than a large city.","zh":"鄉郊地區可能比大城市有較少診所。"},{"en":"Venomous bites can be more dangerous in rural areas if treatment is far away.","zh":"如果治療地點很遠，有毒咬傷在鄉郊地區可能更危險。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts countryside places with urban areas.","zh":"這個短語把鄉村地方與城市地區作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"developing countries","meaning":"發展中國家","examples":[{"en":"Many venomous bites occur in developing countries.","zh":"許多有毒咬傷發生在發展中國家。"},{"en":"Developing countries are countries with lower average incomes and less developed infrastructure than wealthier nations.","zh":"developing countries 指平均收入較低、基礎設施比富裕國家較少發達的國家。"},{"en":"A developing country may have rural clinics with limited medicine and transport.","zh":"發展中國家的鄉郊診所可能藥物和交通有限。"},{"en":"Health problems can be harder to treat when hospitals, roads, and records are limited.","zh":"當醫院、道路和紀錄有限，健康問題可能更難治療。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad economic and infrastructure conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛的經濟和基礎設施情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"get treatment","meaning":"接受治療","examples":[{"en":"Victims may not be able to get treatment.","zh":"受害者可能無法接受治療。"},{"en":"To get treatment means to receive medical help for an illness or injury.","zh":"get treatment 指因疾病或受傷而接受醫療幫助。"},{"en":"A student with a broken wrist needs to get treatment at a clinic or hospital.","zh":"手腕骨折的學生需要在診所或醫院接受治療。"},{"en":"If bite victims cannot get treatment quickly, symptoms may become more serious.","zh":"如果咬傷受害者不能快速接受治療，症狀可能變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes access to medical care.","zh":"這個短語描述獲得醫療護理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"traditional therapies","meaning":"傳統療法","examples":[{"en":"Some victims choose traditional therapies instead of formal treatment.","zh":"有些受害者選擇傳統療法，而不是正式治療。"},{"en":"Traditional therapies are treatments based on local customs, inherited knowledge, or non-modern medical practice.","zh":"traditional therapies 指基於本地習俗、傳承知識或非現代醫學做法的治療。"},{"en":"A family may use traditional therapies for mild stomach discomfort before visiting a doctor.","zh":"家庭可能在看醫生前，用傳統療法處理輕微胃部不適。"},{"en":"Traditional therapies may offer comfort, but serious bites still require proper medical care.","zh":"傳統療法可能帶來安慰，但嚴重咬傷仍需要正規醫療護理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes culturally rooted treatment methods.","zh":"這個短語描述植根於文化的治療方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"not counted","meaning":"沒有被計算在內","examples":[{"en":"Victims who use traditional therapies may not be counted.","zh":"使用傳統療法的受害者可能沒有被計算在內。"},{"en":"Not counted means not included in official numbers or records.","zh":"not counted 指沒有被納入官方數字或紀錄。"},{"en":"Students who forget to sign the attendance sheet may not be counted as present.","zh":"忘記在出席表簽名的學生可能沒有被計算為出席。"},{"en":"If cases are not counted, the official total may be lower than the real number.","zh":"如果個案沒有被計算在內，官方總數可能低於真實數字。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how records can underestimate a problem.","zh":"這個短語解釋紀錄如何低估問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所提供資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether statements agree with the information given.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與所提供資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the passage says venom is injected, a statement saying the same thing agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說毒液是被注入，而陳述說同一件事，就是與資料一致。"},{"en":"Candidates should choose TRUE only when the text clearly supports the statement.","zh":"只有當文本清楚支持陳述時，考生才應選 TRUE。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE, FALSE and NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE、FALSE 和 NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the information in the passage.","zh":"陳述可能與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說法與文章內容相反。"},{"en":"If the passage says poison is ingested but the statement says poison is injected, it contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說毒物是吞食進入體內，但陳述說毒物是注入的，就是與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Candidates choose FALSE when the text clearly disagrees with the statement.","zh":"當文本清楚與陳述不一致時，考生選 FALSE。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct conflict with the source text.","zh":"這個短語描述與來源文本直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果沒有這方面的資料，考生寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有說明該陳述是真還是假。"},{"en":"If the passage never mentions the victim’s age, there is no information on that point.","zh":"如果文章從未提及受害者年齡，就沒有這方面的資料。"},{"en":"Candidates should not guess from outside knowledge when the text is silent.","zh":"當文本沒有提及時，考生不應根據外部知識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase explains when NOT GIVEN is the correct choice.","zh":"這個短語解釋何時 NOT GIVEN 是正確選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"electric-shock-like pain","meaning":"像電擊一樣的疼痛","examples":[{"en":"Michael experienced electric-shock-like pain after the sting.","zh":"Michael 在被螫後經歷像電擊一樣的疼痛。"},{"en":"Electric-shock-like pain is pain that feels like sudden electrical jolts through the body.","zh":"electric-shock-like pain 指感覺像突然電流衝過身體的疼痛。"},{"en":"A patient with nerve irritation may describe electric-shock-like pain in the arm.","zh":"神經受刺激的病人可能形容手臂有像電擊一樣的疼痛。"},{"en":"This kind of pain often suggests that nerves are involved.","zh":"這種疼痛常暗示神經受到影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the feeling of the pain, not necessarily real electricity.","zh":"這個短語描述疼痛感覺，而不一定是真正電流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"nearly lose one’s life","meaning":"幾乎喪命","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Michael nearly lost his life.","zh":"該陳述問 Michael 是否幾乎喪命。"},{"en":"To nearly lose one’s life means to almost die.","zh":"nearly lose one’s life 指差點死亡。"},{"en":"A swimmer may nearly lose his life if he is caught in a strong current.","zh":"如果泳客被強流捲住，可能幾乎喪命。"},{"en":"People who nearly lose their lives often need emergency help and later recovery time.","zh":"幾乎喪命的人通常需要緊急救援和之後的恢復時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very close escape from death.","zh":"這個短語描述非常接近死亡的逃生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"suffer from","meaning":"患有","examples":[{"en":"Michael suffered from ankylosing spondylitis for eight years.","zh":"Michael 患有強直性脊椎炎八年。"},{"en":"To suffer from an illness means to have it and experience its unpleasant effects.","zh":"suffer from an illness 指患有某疾病並經歷其不良影響。"},{"en":"A student who suffers from asthma may need an inhaler during exercise.","zh":"患有哮喘的學生在運動期間可能需要吸入器。"},{"en":"Long-term suffering can affect daily routines, sleep, and emotional health.","zh":"長期患病可以影響日常生活、睡眠和情緒健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for diseases, pain, or ongoing problems.","zh":"這個短語用於疾病、疼痛或持續問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"be caused by an accident","meaning":"由意外造成","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Michael’s disease was caused by an accident.","zh":"該陳述問 Michael 的疾病是否由意外造成。"},{"en":"To be caused by an accident means to happen as a result of an unexpected harmful event.","zh":"be caused by an accident 指因意外有害事件而發生。"},{"en":"A broken wrist may be caused by an accident during a basketball game.","zh":"手腕骨折可能由籃球比賽中的意外造成。"},{"en":"Not every medical condition is caused by an accident; some develop gradually or genetically.","zh":"並非每種病都由意外造成；有些逐漸發展或與基因有關。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies an accidental event as the cause.","zh":"這個短語指出意外事件是原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"be grateful for","meaning":"對……心存感激","examples":[{"en":"Michael may be grateful for the scorpion sting because his pain disappeared.","zh":"Michael 可能對蠍子螫傷心存感激，因為他的疼痛消失了。"},{"en":"To be grateful for something means to feel thankful because it helped or benefited you.","zh":"be grateful for something 指因某事幫助或有益而感到感謝。"},{"en":"A student may be grateful for honest feedback that helps improve an essay.","zh":"學生可能對幫助改善文章的真誠回饋心存感激。"},{"en":"People can be grateful for difficult experiences if those experiences lead to unexpected good results.","zh":"如果困難經歷帶來意外好結果，人們也可能對它心存感激。"},{"en":"This phrase describes thankfulness, often after help or relief.","zh":"這個短語描述感謝，常出現在得到幫助或舒緩之後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"recover from","meaning":"從……康復","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses whether Michael recovered from his condition.","zh":"文章討論 Michael 是否從他的病情中康復。"},{"en":"To recover from something means to get better after illness, injury, or difficulty.","zh":"recover from something 指在疾病、受傷或困難後好轉。"},{"en":"A worker may need several weeks to recover from a broken leg.","zh":"工人腿骨折後可能需要幾星期康復。"},{"en":"Recovery can be partial or complete, depending on the condition.","zh":"康復可以是部分或完全，視乎病情而定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improvement after a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述問題後的改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"perform just one function","meaning":"只執行一項功能","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether any venom performs just one function.","zh":"題目問是否有任何毒液只執行一項功能。"},{"en":"To perform just one function means to do only one job.","zh":"perform just one function 指只做一項工作。"},{"en":"A simple calculator may perform just one function if it only adds numbers.","zh":"如果簡單計算機只會加數，它可能只執行一項功能。"},{"en":"Venom usually does not perform just one function because it contains many active molecules.","zh":"毒液通常不只執行一項功能，因為它含有許多活性分子。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts single-purpose action with multiple functions.","zh":"這個短語把單一用途與多重功能作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"no difference between","meaning":"……之間沒有分別","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether there is no difference between venom and poison.","zh":"該陳述問毒液和毒物之間是否沒有分別。"},{"en":"No difference between two things means they are exactly the same in the relevant way.","zh":"no difference between two things 指兩者在相關方面完全相同。"},{"en":"There is no difference between two identical answer sheets if every word and mark matches.","zh":"如果兩份答案紙每個字和每個標記都一樣，它們之間就沒有分別。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students must check whether the passage actually says two things are the same.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生必須檢查文章是否真的說兩件事相同。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to deny or question distinction.","zh":"這個短語用來否定或質疑差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"be used as medicine","meaning":"被用作藥物","examples":[{"en":"Venom can be used as medicine to save lives.","zh":"毒液可以被用作藥物來拯救生命。"},{"en":"To be used as medicine means to be developed or applied as a treatment for illness.","zh":"be used as medicine 指被發展或應用為疾病治療。"},{"en":"A plant chemical may be used as medicine after doctors prove it is safe and effective.","zh":"植物化學物質在醫生證明安全有效後，可能被用作藥物。"},{"en":"Dangerous substances can sometimes be used as medicine only after careful purification and testing.","zh":"危險物質有時只有經仔細純化和測試後，才可以被用作藥物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled medical use, not casual self-treatment.","zh":"這個短語描述受控制的醫療用途，而不是隨便自行治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"save lives","meaning":"拯救生命","examples":[{"en":"Venom-derived medicines may save lives.","zh":"源自毒液的藥物可能拯救生命。"},{"en":"To save lives means to prevent people from dying.","zh":"save lives 指防止人死亡。"},{"en":"Seat belts save lives by reducing injuries during car crashes.","zh":"安全帶透過減少車禍受傷來拯救生命。"},{"en":"A medicine can save lives if it treats a dangerous disease effectively.","zh":"如果藥物能有效治療危險疾病，就可以拯救生命。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preventing death through action, treatment, or protection.","zh":"這個短語描述透過行動、治療或保護防止死亡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"available on the market","meaning":"已在市場上推出","examples":[{"en":"Some venom-derived drugs are already available on the market.","zh":"有些源自毒液的藥物已在市場上推出。"},{"en":"Available on the market means that a product can be legally bought or obtained by customers or patients.","zh":"available on the market 指產品可由顧客或病人合法購買或取得。"},{"en":"A new phone becomes available on the market when shops begin selling it.","zh":"當商店開始銷售新手機，它就已在市場上推出。"},{"en":"A drug available on the market has usually passed approval rules.","zh":"已在市場上推出的藥物通常已通過審批規則。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public availability after development.","zh":"這個短語描述開發後的公眾可獲得性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"be checked for medical use","meaning":"被檢查是否具醫療用途","examples":[{"en":"Many venom toxins have not yet been checked for medical use.","zh":"許多毒液毒素尚未被檢查是否具醫療用途。"},{"en":"To be checked for medical use means to be tested to see whether something can help treat disease safely.","zh":"be checked for medical use 指接受測試，以了解某物是否能安全幫助治病。"},{"en":"A new plant extract must be checked for medical use before it is given to patients.","zh":"新植物萃取物在給病人前，必須被檢查是否具醫療用途。"},{"en":"Without checking, scientists cannot know whether a toxin is useful, harmful, or both.","zh":"沒有檢查，科學家無法知道毒素是有用、有害，還是兩者皆有。"},{"en":"This phrase describes early scientific and medical evaluation.","zh":"這個短語描述早期科學和醫學評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"the majority of mammals","meaning":"大多數哺乳動物","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether the majority of mammals carry venom.","zh":"該陳述問大多數哺乳動物是否帶有毒液。"},{"en":"The majority of mammals means more than half of all mammal species.","zh":"the majority of mammals 指所有哺乳動物物種中超過一半。"},{"en":"The majority of students in a class means most students, not just a few.","zh":"一班中的大多數學生指大部分學生，而不是少數。"},{"en":"If only a few mammals are venomous, then the majority of mammals are not.","zh":"如果只有少數哺乳動物有毒，那麼大多數哺乳動物就沒有毒。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to discuss proportions.","zh":"這個短語用於討論比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"complete the sentences below","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the sentences below with words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成以下句子。"},{"en":"To complete the sentences below means to fill in missing words in the sentences that follow.","zh":"complete the sentences below 指填寫下方句子中的缺失字詞。"},{"en":"In a reading test, candidates should check grammar before filling each blank.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，考生填每個空格前應檢查文法。"},{"en":"The words must usually fit both the meaning and the word limit.","zh":"答案通常必須同時符合意思和字數限制。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should use no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案應使用不多於兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must contain one or two words only.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案只能包含一個或兩個詞。"},{"en":"If the limit is no more than two words, “active components” is acceptable.","zh":"如果限制是不多於兩個詞，“active components” 是可以的。"},{"en":"Writing three words can lose marks even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫三個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict answer-length rule.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格答案長度規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"be compared to","meaning":"被比作","examples":[{"en":"The way venom works is compared to the way medicines work.","zh":"毒液的作用方式被比作藥物的作用方式。"},{"en":"To be compared to something means to be described as similar to it in some way.","zh":"be compared to something 指被描述為在某方面與某物相似。"},{"en":"A teacher may compare the brain to a computer to explain memory and processing.","zh":"老師可能把大腦比作電腦，以解釋記憶和處理。"},{"en":"Comparisons help students understand difficult ideas through familiar images.","zh":"比較幫助學生透過熟悉圖像理解困難概念。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces similarity, not complete equality.","zh":"這個短語引入相似性，而不是完全相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"venom source","meaning":"毒液來源","examples":[{"en":"A venom source such as puffer fish can help scientists study nerve cells.","zh":"河豚等毒液來源可以幫助科學家研究神經細胞。"},{"en":"A venom source is an animal or organism from which venom or toxin can be obtained for study.","zh":"venom source 指可供研究取得毒液或毒素的動物或生物。"},{"en":"A laboratory may use a snake as a venom source for testing blood-clotting effects.","zh":"實驗室可能使用蛇作為毒液來源，以測試血液凝結作用。"},{"en":"Different venom sources give scientists different molecules to investigate.","zh":"不同毒液來源給科學家不同分子去研究。"},{"en":"This phrase names the origin of venom used in research.","zh":"這個短語命名研究所用毒液的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"complex details","meaning":"複雜細節","examples":[{"en":"Tetrodotoxin has revealed complex details about nerve communication.","zh":"河豚毒素揭示了神經溝通的複雜細節。"},{"en":"Complex details are small, difficult, and interconnected pieces of information.","zh":"complex details 指細小、困難且互相關連的資訊。"},{"en":"A doctor’s report may contain complex details about how a patient’s organs are working.","zh":"醫生報告可能包含有關病人器官如何運作的複雜細節。"},{"en":"Complex details help experts understand a system more deeply.","zh":"複雜細節幫助專家更深入理解系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information that is precise and not simple.","zh":"這個短語描述精確而不簡單的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"tens of thousands of animals","meaning":"數以萬計的動物","examples":[{"en":"Tens of thousands of animals have developed venom systems.","zh":"數以萬計的動物已發展出毒液系統。"},{"en":"Tens of thousands of animals means a very large number of animals, at least many tens of thousands.","zh":"tens of thousands of animals 指非常大量的動物，至少有很多個一萬。"},{"en":"Tens of thousands of birds may migrate through a wetland each year.","zh":"每年可能有數以萬計的鳥類遷徙經過濕地。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the number is far beyond a few examples.","zh":"這個短語強調數量遠超少數例子。"},{"en":"It is used when exact counting is difficult but the scale is clearly large.","zh":"當精確點算困難但規模明顯很大時，會使用它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"be responsible for","meaning":"負責","examples":[{"en":"Glands and apparatuses are responsible for storing and releasing venom.","zh":"腺體和器官負責儲存和釋放毒液。"},{"en":"To be responsible for something means to have the job or role of causing or managing it.","zh":"be responsible for something 指有造成、管理或執行某事的工作或角色。"},{"en":"In a school, the office is responsible for keeping student records.","zh":"在學校中，辦公室負責保存學生紀錄。"},{"en":"Body parts responsible for venom storage and release make venom delivery possible.","zh":"負責儲存和釋放毒液的身體部位使毒液輸送成為可能。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the part or person that performs a function.","zh":"這個短語指出執行功能的部分或人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"store and release venom","meaning":"儲存和釋放毒液","examples":[{"en":"Special body parts store and release venom.","zh":"特殊身體部位儲存和釋放毒液。"},{"en":"To store and release venom means to keep venom inside the body and push it out when needed.","zh":"store and release venom 指把毒液保存在身體內，並在需要時推出。"},{"en":"A snake’s venom glands store venom, and its fangs help release it during a bite.","zh":"蛇的毒腺儲存毒液，毒牙在咬擊時幫助釋放毒液。"},{"en":"Storing venom keeps it ready, while releasing it delivers the effect.","zh":"儲存毒液令它隨時可用，而釋放毒液則輸送其效果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the two-step system of venom use.","zh":"這個短語描述毒液使用的兩步系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"snake’s venom","meaning":"蛇的毒液","examples":[{"en":"A snake’s venom may change with its diet.","zh":"蛇的毒液可能隨其飲食而改變。"},{"en":"A snake’s venom is the toxic mixture produced by a snake and delivered through its fangs.","zh":"snake’s venom 指蛇產生並透過毒牙輸送的有毒混合物。"},{"en":"A researcher may compare a snake’s venom before and after a change in prey.","zh":"研究人員可能比較蛇在獵物改變前後的毒液。"},{"en":"A snake’s venom can vary because different prey may require different toxins.","zh":"蛇的毒液可以有所不同，因為不同獵物可能需要不同毒素。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the venom of one snake or snake species.","zh":"這個短語指某條蛇或某蛇種的毒液。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"warn rival males of","meaning":"警告競爭雄性關於……","examples":[{"en":"Some animals use venom to warn rival males of their dominance.","zh":"有些動物使用毒液來警告競爭雄性關於自己的支配地位。"},{"en":"To warn rival males of something means to signal that competing males should recognise it.","zh":"warn rival males of something 指發出訊號，令競爭雄性知道某事。"},{"en":"A male bird may use loud calls to warn rival males of its territory.","zh":"雄鳥可能用響亮叫聲警告競爭雄性關於自己的領地。"},{"en":"Warning rivals can prevent repeated fights by showing strength early.","zh":"警告對手可以透過早早展示力量來避免反覆打鬥。"},{"en":"This phrase describes communication during competition.","zh":"這個短語描述競爭期間的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"dominance","meaning":"支配地位；優勢","examples":[{"en":"Some animals use venom to show dominance during mating season.","zh":"有些動物在交配季節使用毒液來顯示支配地位。"},{"en":"Dominance is the position of having power, control, or higher rank over others.","zh":"dominance 指對其他個體擁有權力、控制或較高地位。"},{"en":"In a group of animals, one male may show dominance by winning fights or displays.","zh":"在一群動物中，某隻雄性可能透過打鬥或展示勝出來顯示支配地位。"},{"en":"Dominance can affect access to mates, territory, food, or social rank.","zh":"支配地位可以影響取得伴侶、領地、食物或社會等級。"},{"en":"This word describes control or superiority within a group.","zh":"這個詞描述群體中的控制或優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 129 - The Bite That Heals.pdf","sourcePage":25}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 130":[{"front":"detection of a meteorite lake","meaning":"隕石湖的探測","examples":[{"en":"The project contributed to the detection and investigation of a meteorite lake.","zh":"這個項目促成了隕石湖的探測和研究。"},{"en":"Detection of a meteorite lake means finding evidence that a lake was formed by a meteorite impact.","zh":"detection of a meteorite lake 指找出證據，顯示一個湖由隕石撞擊形成。"},{"en":"Scientists may use maps, rock samples, and sound waves for the detection of a meteorite lake.","zh":"科學家可能使用地圖、岩石樣本和聲波來進行隕石湖的探測。"},{"en":"Once detection is confirmed, researchers can study the crater, sediments, and impact history.","zh":"一旦探測得到確認，研究人員可以研究隕石坑、沉積物和撞擊歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on discovering and identifying the lake’s origin, not simply seeing water.","zh":"這個短語重點是發現並辨認湖的起源，而不只是看見水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as the sun rose over","meaning":"當太陽從……升起時","examples":[{"en":"As the sun rose over Lake Bosumtwi, the research team prepared for work.","zh":"當太陽從 Bosumtwi 湖升起時，研究團隊準備開始工作。"},{"en":"As the sun rose over a place means when morning sunlight began to appear above it.","zh":"as the sun rose over a place 指早晨陽光開始在某地上方出現時。"},{"en":"As the sun rose over the school playground, students gathered for sports day.","zh":"當太陽從學校操場升起時，學生集合準備運動會。"},{"en":"This phrase often sets the time and scene before an action begins.","zh":"這個短語常用來設定時間和場景，然後才描述行動。"},{"en":"It creates a clear morning image and tells readers when something happened.","zh":"它創造清楚的早晨畫面，並告訴讀者事情何時發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"picturesque","meaning":"風景如畫的","examples":[{"en":"Lake Bosumtwi is surrounded by picturesque scenery.","zh":"Bosumtwi 湖被風景如畫的景色包圍。"},{"en":"Picturesque means attractive in a way that looks suitable for a painting or photograph.","zh":"picturesque 指漂亮得像適合入畫或拍照。"},{"en":"A small village with old houses and green hills can look picturesque.","zh":"有舊房子和綠色山丘的小村莊可以看起來風景如畫。"},{"en":"Picturesque places often attract tourists because people enjoy taking photos there.","zh":"風景如畫的地方常吸引遊客，因為人們喜歡在那裏拍照。"},{"en":"The word describes visual beauty, not necessarily convenience or comfort.","zh":"這個詞描述視覺上的美，不一定指方便或舒適。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a team of researchers","meaning":"一隊研究人員","examples":[{"en":"A team of researchers spent several weeks studying the lake.","zh":"一隊研究人員花了數星期研究該湖。"},{"en":"A team of researchers is a group of scientists working together on a study.","zh":"a team of researchers 指一組共同進行研究的科學家。"},{"en":"A team of researchers may visit a hospital to study how patients recover after surgery.","zh":"一隊研究人員可能到醫院研究病人手術後如何康復。"},{"en":"Working as a team allows researchers to share skills, equipment, and observations.","zh":"以團隊方式工作讓研究人員分享技能、設備和觀察。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises organised scientific cooperation, not one person working alone.","zh":"這個短語強調有組織的科學合作，而不是一個人獨自工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"prepare for another day of","meaning":"準備展開另一天的……","examples":[{"en":"The scientists prepared for another day of collecting data.","zh":"科學家準備展開另一天的數據收集。"},{"en":"To prepare for another day of something means to get ready to continue the same work the next day.","zh":"prepare for another day of something 指準備好在下一天繼續同一工作。"},{"en":"Teachers prepared for another day of marking exam papers after school.","zh":"老師放學後準備展開另一天的試卷批改。"},{"en":"Preparation helps people work smoothly because tools, plans, and roles are ready.","zh":"準備工作令工具、計劃和角色都就緒，使人工作更順利。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests repeated effort over several days.","zh":"這個短語暗示連續多天的努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"state-of-the-art equipment","meaning":"最先進的設備","examples":[{"en":"The researchers used state-of-the-art equipment to examine the lake.","zh":"研究人員使用最先進的設備檢查該湖。"},{"en":"State-of-the-art equipment is the most advanced and modern equipment available.","zh":"state-of-the-art equipment 指現時可用的最先進和最新式設備。"},{"en":"A hospital may use state-of-the-art equipment to scan patients more accurately.","zh":"醫院可能使用最先進的設備，更準確地掃描病人。"},{"en":"Advanced equipment can produce clearer data and reduce uncertainty.","zh":"先進設備可以產生更清晰數據並減少不確定性。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights high technology, not ordinary tools.","zh":"這個短語突出高科技，而不是普通工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"map the lake bottom","meaning":"繪製湖底地圖","examples":[{"en":"The equipment helped the scientists map the lake bottom.","zh":"這些設備幫助科學家繪製湖底地圖。"},{"en":"To map the lake bottom means to create a detailed picture or plan of the shape beneath the water.","zh":"map the lake bottom 指建立水下地形的詳細圖像或平面圖。"},{"en":"Engineers may map a harbour bottom before building a new pier.","zh":"工程師興建新碼頭前，可能會繪製港口底部地圖。"},{"en":"Mapping the bottom helps researchers locate deep areas, slopes, and hidden features.","zh":"繪製底部地圖幫助研究人員找出深水區、斜坡和隱藏特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase means measuring and recording underwater landforms, not drawing a simple surface map.","zh":"這個短語指量度和記錄水下地貌，而不是畫簡單水面地圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be nestled in the heart of","meaning":"坐落於……的中心","examples":[{"en":"Lake Bosumtwi is nestled in the heart of Ghana.","zh":"Bosumtwi 湖坐落於加納的中心。"},{"en":"To be nestled in the heart of a place means to be located comfortably or closely within its central area.","zh":"be nestled in the heart of a place 指舒適地或緊密地位於某地的中心區域。"},{"en":"A small café may be nestled in the heart of an old neighbourhood.","zh":"一間小咖啡店可能坐落於舊社區的中心。"},{"en":"Places described this way often feel protected, quiet, or surrounded by scenery.","zh":"以這種方式描述的地方常令人感覺受保護、安靜或被景色包圍。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a warm image of location, not just a map position.","zh":"這個短語給出溫暖的位置意象，而不只是地圖位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an untapped reservoir of information","meaning":"尚未開發的龐大資料庫","examples":[{"en":"The lake holds an untapped reservoir of scientific information.","zh":"該湖蘊藏尚未開發的龐大科學資料庫。"},{"en":"An untapped reservoir of information is a large source of knowledge that has not yet been fully used.","zh":"an untapped reservoir of information 指尚未被充分使用的大量知識來源。"},{"en":"Old school records can be an untapped reservoir of information about students’ learning needs.","zh":"舊學校紀錄可以是關於學生學習需要的尚未開發資料庫。"},{"en":"When researchers study such a source, they may discover evidence no one has used before.","zh":"當研究人員研究這類來源，他們可能發現以前沒有人使用過的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase compares hidden knowledge to stored water waiting to be used.","zh":"這個短語把隱藏知識比作等待使用的儲水庫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"help someone predict","meaning":"幫助某人預測","examples":[{"en":"The evidence may help scientists predict future climate changes.","zh":"這些證據可能幫助科學家預測未來氣候變化。"},{"en":"To help someone predict something means to give information that makes future events easier to estimate.","zh":"help someone predict something 指提供資訊，使人更容易估計未來事件。"},{"en":"Weather records help farmers predict when crops may need more water.","zh":"天氣紀錄幫助農夫預測作物何時可能需要更多水。"},{"en":"Better evidence improves predictions because people can compare past patterns with present trends.","zh":"更好的證據會改善預測，因為人們可以比較過去模式和現時趨勢。"},{"en":"The phrase connects information with forecasting.","zh":"這個短語把資訊與預測連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"future climate changes","meaning":"未來氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"The lake may contain evidence of future climate changes.","zh":"該湖可能包含未來氣候變化的證據。"},{"en":"Future climate changes are changes in temperature, rainfall, storms, or weather patterns that may happen later.","zh":"future climate changes 指日後可能發生的氣溫、降雨、風暴或天氣模式變化。"},{"en":"City planners study future climate changes before designing drainage systems.","zh":"城市規劃者在設計排水系統前會研究未來氣候變化。"},{"en":"If rainfall becomes less predictable, farming and water supply may be affected.","zh":"如果降雨變得較難預測，農業和供水可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to possible later changes in the climate system.","zh":"這個短語指氣候系統中可能出現的日後變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"look at evidence from the past","meaning":"研究過去的證據","examples":[{"en":"Scientists can make predictions by looking at evidence from the past.","zh":"科學家可以透過研究過去的證據作出預測。"},{"en":"To look at evidence from the past means to study old records, samples, or traces to understand earlier conditions.","zh":"look at evidence from the past 指研究舊紀錄、樣本或痕跡，以了解早前情況。"},{"en":"Doctors may look at evidence from the past by checking a patient’s medical history.","zh":"醫生可能透過查看病人病歷來研究過去的證據。"},{"en":"Past evidence can reveal patterns that help explain what may happen next.","zh":"過去證據可以揭示模式，幫助解釋接下來可能發生甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses learning from history, not guessing without proof.","zh":"這個短語強調從歷史學習，而不是無證據猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"improve someone’s understanding of","meaning":"加深某人對……的了解","examples":[{"en":"The data will improve scientists’ understanding of meteorite impacts.","zh":"這些數據將加深科學家對隕石撞擊的了解。"},{"en":"To improve someone’s understanding of something means to make them know it more clearly or deeply.","zh":"improve someone’s understanding of something 指令某人更清楚或更深入了解某事。"},{"en":"Feedback can improve a student’s understanding of why her essay lost marks.","zh":"回饋可以加深學生對作文為何失分的了解。"},{"en":"Better understanding often leads to better questions, methods, and decisions.","zh":"更好的理解通常帶來更好的問題、方法和決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gaining clearer knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述獲得更清晰知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"occur in a region","meaning":"在某地區發生","examples":[{"en":"The researchers studied changes that occur in a meteorite-struck region.","zh":"研究人員研究在受隕石撞擊地區發生的變化。"},{"en":"To occur in a region means to happen within a particular area.","zh":"occur in a region 指在某一特定地區內發生。"},{"en":"Flooding may occur in a low-lying region after heavy rain.","zh":"暴雨後，水浸可能在低窪地區發生。"},{"en":"Studying where changes occur helps people understand local causes and effects.","zh":"研究變化在哪裏發生，有助人理解本地原因和影響。"},{"en":"The phrase links an event or process to a specific place.","zh":"這個短語把事件或過程與具體地方連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be struck by","meaning":"被……撞擊","examples":[{"en":"The region was struck by a massive meteorite.","zh":"該地區被巨型隕石撞擊。"},{"en":"To be struck by something means to be hit strongly by it.","zh":"be struck by something 指被某物強力擊中。"},{"en":"A coastal town may be struck by a powerful storm during typhoon season.","zh":"沿海城鎮可能在颱風季被強烈風暴襲擊。"},{"en":"A strong impact can change the shape, safety, or history of a place.","zh":"強烈撞擊可以改變一個地方的形狀、安全或歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase often describes sudden force or impact.","zh":"這個短語常描述突然的力量或撞擊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"massive meteorite","meaning":"巨型隕石","examples":[{"en":"A massive meteorite created the lake’s crater.","zh":"一顆巨型隕石形成了該湖的隕石坑。"},{"en":"A massive meteorite is a very large rock from space that reaches Earth.","zh":"massive meteorite 指到達地球的非常大型太空岩石。"},{"en":"A science museum may show a small meteorite beside a model of a massive meteorite impact.","zh":"科學博物館可能把小隕石放在巨型隕石撞擊模型旁展示。"},{"en":"When a massive meteorite hits the ground, it can form a crater.","zh":"當巨型隕石撞擊地面，它可以形成隕石坑。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the size and destructive power of the space rock.","zh":"這個短語強調太空岩石的大小和破壞力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be led by","meaning":"由……領導","examples":[{"en":"The research project was led by Professor Christopher Scholz.","zh":"這個研究項目由 Christopher Scholz 教授領導。"},{"en":"To be led by someone means that person directed or managed the work.","zh":"be led by someone 指某人指導或管理該工作。"},{"en":"A school trip may be led by a teacher who checks safety and timing.","zh":"學校旅行可能由一位老師領導，負責檢查安全和時間安排。"},{"en":"Strong leadership helps a project stay organised and solve problems quickly.","zh":"有力領導幫助項目保持有組織，並快速解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the person in charge.","zh":"這個短語指出負責人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"earth sciences professor","meaning":"地球科學教授","examples":[{"en":"Christopher Scholz is an earth sciences professor.","zh":"Christopher Scholz 是地球科學教授。"},{"en":"An earth sciences professor is a university teacher and researcher who studies Earth’s rocks, water, climate, or physical systems.","zh":"earth sciences professor 指研究地球岩石、水、氣候或物理系統的大學教師和研究人員。"},{"en":"An earth sciences professor may teach students how earthquakes and volcanoes form.","zh":"地球科學教授可能教學生地震和火山如何形成。"},{"en":"Such experts help explain natural processes that shape the planet.","zh":"這類專家幫助解釋塑造地球的自然過程。"},{"en":"The phrase names an academic specialist in Earth-related science.","zh":"這個短語命名地球相關科學的學術專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be funded by","meaning":"由……資助","examples":[{"en":"The project was funded by the National Science Foundation.","zh":"該項目由國家科學基金會資助。"},{"en":"To be funded by an organisation means that organisation paid for or supported the work financially.","zh":"be funded by an organisation 指該機構為工作付款或提供財政支援。"},{"en":"A school reading programme may be funded by a local charity.","zh":"學校閱讀計劃可能由本地慈善機構資助。"},{"en":"Funding allows researchers to buy equipment, travel, and hire staff.","zh":"資助讓研究人員購買設備、出行和聘請人員。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of financial support.","zh":"這個短語指出財政支援來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"large-scale effort","meaning":"大規模工作；大型研究","examples":[{"en":"This was the first large-scale effort to study the lake.","zh":"這是首次研究該湖的大規模工作。"},{"en":"A large-scale effort is a big organised project involving many people, resources, or time.","zh":"large-scale effort 指涉及許多人、資源或時間的大型有組織項目。"},{"en":"A city may launch a large-scale effort to clean beaches after severe pollution.","zh":"嚴重污染後，城市可能展開大規模清潔海灘工作。"},{"en":"Large projects can collect more complete information than small informal attempts.","zh":"大型項目比小型非正式嘗試能收集更完整資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses size, planning, and seriousness.","zh":"這個短語強調規模、計劃和認真程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"form when","meaning":"在……時形成","examples":[{"en":"The lake formed when a giant meteor crashed into the Earth.","zh":"該湖在一顆巨大流星撞向地球時形成。"},{"en":"Form when means come into existence at the time a particular event happens.","zh":"form when 指在某特定事件發生時出現或形成。"},{"en":"A puddle forms when rainwater collects in a hole in the road.","zh":"當雨水聚集在路面坑洞中，水氹就會形成。"},{"en":"Knowing when something forms helps explain its cause.","zh":"知道某物何時形成，有助解釋其原因。"},{"en":"The phrase connects the creation of something with a triggering event.","zh":"這個短語把某物的形成與觸發事件連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"crash into","meaning":"撞向……","examples":[{"en":"A giant meteor crashed into the Earth’s surface.","zh":"一顆巨大流星撞向地球表面。"},{"en":"To crash into something means to hit it suddenly and violently.","zh":"crash into something 指突然猛烈撞上某物。"},{"en":"A cyclist may crash into a fence if the brakes fail.","zh":"如果煞車失靈，單車手可能撞向圍欄。"},{"en":"A violent crash can damage the object hit and change its shape.","zh":"猛烈撞擊可以破壞被撞物並改變其形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong accidental or forceful impact.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈意外或有力撞擊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the Earth’s surface","meaning":"地球表面","examples":[{"en":"The meteor created a crater in the Earth’s surface.","zh":"隕石在地球表面形成了一個隕石坑。"},{"en":"The Earth’s surface is the outer layer of the planet, including land and ocean floors.","zh":"the Earth’s surface 指地球最外層，包括陸地和海底。"},{"en":"Mountains, deserts, forests, and lakes all appear on the Earth’s surface.","zh":"山脈、沙漠、森林和湖泊都出現在地球表面。"},{"en":"Impacts, erosion, and plate movement can change the surface over time.","zh":"撞擊、侵蝕和板塊移動可以隨時間改變地表。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the planet’s outside layer, not its deep interior.","zh":"這個短語指地球外部層面，而不是深層內部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the resulting crater","meaning":"由此形成的隕石坑","examples":[{"en":"The resulting crater later filled with water.","zh":"由此形成的隕石坑後來注滿了水。"},{"en":"The resulting crater is the hole or depression created as a result of an impact or explosion.","zh":"resulting crater 指因撞擊或爆炸而形成的坑洞或凹陷。"},{"en":"After a small explosion at a construction site, the resulting crater had to be filled safely.","zh":"建築地盤小型爆破後，由此形成的坑洞必須安全填平。"},{"en":"If a crater fills with water, it may eventually become a lake.","zh":"如果隕石坑注滿水，它最終可能變成湖。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the landform caused by an earlier event.","zh":"這個短語指出由早前事件造成的地貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"well-preserved","meaning":"保存完好的","examples":[{"en":"Lake Bosumtwi occupies a well-preserved crater.","zh":"Bosumtwi 湖位於一個保存完好的隕石坑內。"},{"en":"Well-preserved means kept in good condition, with important features still visible.","zh":"well-preserved 指保持良好狀態，重要特徵仍清晰可見。"},{"en":"A well-preserved old building can show how people lived a century ago.","zh":"保存完好的舊建築可以顯示一百年前人們如何生活。"},{"en":"Good preservation helps researchers study original shapes, materials, and history.","zh":"良好保存幫助研究人員研究原本形狀、材料和歷史。"},{"en":"The word describes condition, not beauty alone.","zh":"這個詞描述狀態，而不只是美觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"geologically young","meaning":"從地質角度而言年輕的","examples":[{"en":"The crater is considered geologically young.","zh":"這個隕石坑被視為從地質角度而言年輕。"},{"en":"Geologically young means young when measured by Earth’s very long geological timescale.","zh":"geologically young 指按地球極漫長的地質時間尺度衡量時仍算年輕。"},{"en":"A volcanic island may be geologically young even if it is thousands of years old.","zh":"火山島即使有數千年歷史，從地質角度而言仍可能年輕。"},{"en":"Young landforms may be better preserved because erosion has had less time to damage them.","zh":"年輕地貌可能保存較好，因為侵蝕沒有太長時間破壞它。"},{"en":"The phrase compares age using geological time, not human age.","zh":"這個短語用地質時間比較年齡，而不是人類年齡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"collaborate on a project with","meaning":"與……合作進行項目","examples":[{"en":"Scholz collaborated on the project with researchers from several universities.","zh":"Scholz 與幾所大學的研究人員合作進行該項目。"},{"en":"To collaborate on a project with someone means to work together with them on the same task.","zh":"collaborate on a project with someone 指與某人共同處理同一任務。"},{"en":"Two schools may collaborate on a project with local museums to teach history.","zh":"兩所學校可能與本地博物館合作進行歷史教學項目。"},{"en":"Collaboration allows people to combine knowledge, equipment, and different viewpoints.","zh":"合作讓人結合知識、設備和不同觀點。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses joint work rather than separate efforts.","zh":"這個短語強調共同工作，而不是各自努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"provide information about","meaning":"提供有關……的資料","examples":[{"en":"The collected data should provide information about meteorite impacts.","zh":"收集到的數據應能提供有關隕石撞擊的資料。"},{"en":"To provide information about something means to give facts or details that help people understand it.","zh":"provide information about something 指提供有助理解某事的事實或細節。"},{"en":"A school survey can provide information about students’ sleep habits.","zh":"學校調查可以提供有關學生睡眠習慣的資料。"},{"en":"Good information helps people make better explanations and decisions.","zh":"良好資訊幫助人作出更好解釋和決定。"},{"en":"The phrase links evidence with understanding.","zh":"這個短語把證據與理解連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"an impact hits","meaning":"撞擊發生於……","examples":[{"en":"The research examines what happens when an impact hits hard rock.","zh":"該研究檢視撞擊發生於堅硬岩石時會出現甚麼。"},{"en":"When an impact hits, a strong collision strikes a surface or material.","zh":"when an impact hits 指強烈碰撞擊中表面或材料。"},{"en":"Engineers study what happens when an impact hits a car door during a crash test.","zh":"工程師會研究碰撞測試中撞擊發生於車門時會怎樣。"},{"en":"The force of impact can break, bend, heat, or reshape materials.","zh":"撞擊力量可以打碎、彎曲、加熱或重塑材料。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the moment of collision and its effects.","zh":"這個短語重點是碰撞一刻及其影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pre-Cambrian rocks","meaning":"前寒武紀岩石","examples":[{"en":"The meteor struck pre-Cambrian rocks beneath the region.","zh":"隕石撞擊了該地區下方的前寒武紀岩石。"},{"en":"Pre-Cambrian rocks are extremely old rocks formed before the Cambrian period.","zh":"pre-Cambrian rocks 指形成於寒武紀之前的極古老岩石。"},{"en":"A geology class may examine pre-Cambrian rocks to learn about Earth’s early history.","zh":"地質課可能研究前寒武紀岩石，以了解地球早期歷史。"},{"en":"Very old rocks can preserve clues about ancient environments and impacts.","zh":"非常古老的岩石可以保存古代環境和撞擊的線索。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rocks from a very early geological age.","zh":"這個短語描述來自非常早期地質年代的岩石。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"crystalline rocks","meaning":"結晶岩","examples":[{"en":"The crater formed in hard crystalline rocks.","zh":"這個隕石坑形成於堅硬結晶岩中。"},{"en":"Crystalline rocks are rocks made of interlocking mineral crystals.","zh":"crystalline rocks 指由互相嵌合的礦物晶體組成的岩石。"},{"en":"Granite is a common crystalline rock used in buildings and monuments.","zh":"花崗岩是一種常見結晶岩，常用於建築和紀念碑。"},{"en":"Hard crystalline rocks may react differently to impact than soft sediments.","zh":"堅硬結晶岩面對撞擊時，反應可能不同於柔軟沉積物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the structure and hardness of certain rocks.","zh":"這個短語描述某些岩石的結構和硬度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a billion years old","meaning":"有十億年歷史","examples":[{"en":"Some of the rocks are approximately a billion years old.","zh":"其中一些岩石大約有十億年歷史。"},{"en":"A billion years old means having existed for about one thousand million years.","zh":"a billion years old 指已存在大約十億年。"},{"en":"A museum may display a rock that is a billion years old to show Earth’s deep history.","zh":"博物館可能展示一塊有十億年歷史的岩石，以顯示地球深遠歷史。"},{"en":"Very old rocks help scientists study events far beyond human history.","zh":"非常古老的岩石幫助科學家研究遠超人類歷史的事件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes geological age on an enormous timescale.","zh":"這個短語描述極大時間尺度上的地質年齡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"equally important","meaning":"同樣重要的是","examples":[{"en":"Equally important is the fact that the lake has no natural outlet.","zh":"同樣重要的是，該湖沒有天然出水口這個事實。"},{"en":"Equally important means just as important as the point already mentioned.","zh":"equally important 指與剛提到的重點同樣重要。"},{"en":"Good exam content matters; equally important is clear handwriting on the answer sheet.","zh":"良好考試內容很重要；同樣重要的是答題紙上的字跡清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that another factor deserves the same attention.","zh":"這個短語表示另一因素值得同樣關注。"},{"en":"It helps writers add a second key point without making it seem minor.","zh":"它幫助作者加入第二個關鍵點，而不令其顯得次要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the fact that","meaning":"……這個事實","examples":[{"en":"The scientists considered the fact that the lake has no natural outlet.","zh":"科學家考慮到該湖沒有天然出水口這個事實。"},{"en":"The fact that introduces a piece of information treated as real or important.","zh":"the fact that 用來引入被視為真實或重要的一項資料。"},{"en":"The fact that a student misses breakfast may help explain poor concentration.","zh":"學生不吃早餐這個事實，可能有助解釋專注力差。"},{"en":"Important facts can change how people interpret a situation.","zh":"重要事實可以改變人們如何理解某情況。"},{"en":"The phrase presents evidence that supports later reasoning.","zh":"這個短語呈現支持後續推理的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in diameter","meaning":"直徑為……","examples":[{"en":"The lake is about eight kilometres in diameter.","zh":"該湖直徑約八公里。"},{"en":"In diameter means measured straight across the widest part of a circle or round object.","zh":"in diameter 指從圓形或近圓形物體最寬處橫跨量度。"},{"en":"A round table may be one metre in diameter.","zh":"一張圓桌直徑可能為一米。"},{"en":"Diameter helps people understand the size of circular lakes, wheels, or plates.","zh":"直徑幫助人理解圓形湖泊、車輪或碟子的大小。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a width measurement across the centre.","zh":"這個短語提供穿過中心的寬度量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"natural outlet","meaning":"天然出水口","examples":[{"en":"Lake Bosumtwi has no natural outlet.","zh":"Bosumtwi 湖沒有天然出水口。"},{"en":"A natural outlet is a river or channel through which water can leave a lake naturally.","zh":"natural outlet 指水可以自然離開湖泊的河流或水道。"},{"en":"A pond without a natural outlet may lose water mainly through evaporation.","zh":"沒有天然出水口的池塘可能主要透過蒸發流失水分。"},{"en":"If a lake has no outlet, minerals and sediments may remain trapped inside it.","zh":"如果湖泊沒有出水口，礦物和沉積物可能留在湖內。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a natural exit for water, not a man-made drain.","zh":"這個短語指水的自然出口，而不是人造排水渠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the rim of the crater","meaning":"隕石坑邊緣","examples":[{"en":"The rim of the crater rises high above the lake.","zh":"隕石坑邊緣高高升起在湖面上方。"},{"en":"The rim of the crater is the raised edge around an impact hole or volcanic crater.","zh":"rim of the crater 指撞擊坑或火山口周圍升高的邊緣。"},{"en":"Hikers may stand on the rim of a crater to look down into it.","zh":"遠足者可能站在火山口邊緣向下望。"},{"en":"A high rim can trap water and help form a lake inside the crater.","zh":"高邊緣可以困住水，幫助在坑內形成湖泊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the outer edge of a crater.","zh":"這個短語描述隕石坑的外緣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rise above","meaning":"高出……","examples":[{"en":"The crater rim rises about 250 metres above the water’s surface.","zh":"隕石坑邊緣高出水面約250米。"},{"en":"To rise above something means to extend higher than it.","zh":"rise above something 指延伸至比某物更高的位置。"},{"en":"A tall tower may rise above nearby houses and be visible from far away.","zh":"高塔可能高出附近房屋，從遠處也能看見。"},{"en":"When land rises above water, it can form a clear boundary around a lake.","zh":"當陸地高出水面，它可以在湖周圍形成清楚界線。"},{"en":"The phrase describes height in relation to another level.","zh":"這個短語描述相對於另一水平的高度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the water’s surface","meaning":"水面","examples":[{"en":"The crater rim is clearly visible above the water’s surface.","zh":"隕石坑邊緣在水面上方清晰可見。"},{"en":"The water’s surface is the top layer of a body of water that people can see.","zh":"water’s surface 指人們看得見的水體最上層。"},{"en":"Leaves may float on the water’s surface after a storm.","zh":"風暴後，樹葉可能漂浮在水面上。"},{"en":"Objects above the surface can be seen, while objects below may need special equipment.","zh":"水面以上的物件可以被看見，而水面以下的物件可能需要特殊設備。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the visible upper level of water.","zh":"這個短語指水的可見上層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"flow into","meaning":"流入……","examples":[{"en":"Several streams flow into the lake.","zh":"幾條溪流流入該湖。"},{"en":"To flow into a place means for water or liquid to move towards and enter it.","zh":"flow into a place 指水或液體向某處移動並進入其中。"},{"en":"Rainwater may flow into street drains during a storm.","zh":"暴風雨時，雨水可能流入街道排水渠。"},{"en":"Streams flowing into a lake bring water, sediment, and sometimes pollution.","zh":"流入湖泊的溪流會帶來水、沉積物，有時也帶來污染。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement into a body or space.","zh":"這個短語描述進入某水體或空間的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"leave by evaporation","meaning":"透過蒸發流失","examples":[{"en":"Some lake water leaves by evaporation.","zh":"部分湖水透過蒸發流失。"},{"en":"To leave by evaporation means water disappears into the air as vapour.","zh":"leave by evaporation 指水變成水蒸氣進入空氣而消失。"},{"en":"Water in a shallow bowl may leave by evaporation on a hot day.","zh":"炎熱日子裏，淺碗中的水可能透過蒸發流失。"},{"en":"If a lake has no outlet, evaporation can be one of the main ways water is lost.","zh":"如果湖泊沒有出水口，蒸發可以是主要失水方式之一。"},{"en":"The phrase describes water loss through heat and air, not drainage.","zh":"這個短語描述透過熱力和空氣失水，而不是排水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"seep through","meaning":"滲過……","examples":[{"en":"Water can seep through the lake sediments.","zh":"水可以滲過湖底沉積物。"},{"en":"To seep through something means to pass slowly through small spaces in it.","zh":"seep through something 指慢慢穿過其中的小空隙。"},{"en":"Rainwater may seep through a cracked roof and stain the ceiling.","zh":"雨水可能滲過有裂縫的屋頂並弄污天花板。"},{"en":"Slow seepage can move water without creating a visible stream.","zh":"緩慢滲透可以移動水分，而不形成可見水流。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual movement through tiny gaps.","zh":"這個短語描述透過微小縫隙的逐步移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lake sediments","meaning":"湖底沉積物","examples":[{"en":"The lake sediments contain a record of past climatic conditions.","zh":"湖底沉積物包含過去氣候狀況的記錄。"},{"en":"Lake sediments are layers of mud, sand, minerals, and organic material that settle at the bottom of a lake.","zh":"lake sediments 指沉積在湖底的泥、沙、礦物和有機物層。"},{"en":"Scientists may collect lake sediments to study old pollution or rainfall patterns.","zh":"科學家可能收集湖底沉積物，以研究舊污染或降雨模式。"},{"en":"As sediments build up over time, they can preserve a history of environmental change.","zh":"隨着沉積物隨時間累積，它們可以保存環境變化歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to material on or below the lake bottom.","zh":"這個短語指湖底表面或以下的物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"act as a tropical rain gauge","meaning":"發揮熱帶雨量計的作用","examples":[{"en":"The lake has acted as a tropical rain gauge for a million years.","zh":"該湖在一百萬年間發揮熱帶雨量計的作用。"},{"en":"To act as a tropical rain gauge means to record rainfall changes in a tropical region over time.","zh":"act as a tropical rain gauge 指記錄熱帶地區隨時間出現的降雨變化。"},{"en":"A school garden pond can act as a simple rain gauge if students measure water level changes.","zh":"如果學生量度水位變化，學校花園池塘可以像簡單雨量計一樣發揮作用。"},{"en":"When rainfall increases or decreases, lake levels and sediments may change accordingly.","zh":"當降雨增加或減少，湖水水位和沉積物可能相應改變。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the lake to a measuring tool for rain.","zh":"這個短語把湖泊比作量度降雨的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fill and dry","meaning":"水位上升和乾涸","examples":[{"en":"The lake fills and dries in response to rainfall changes.","zh":"該湖會因應降雨變化而水位上升和乾涸。"},{"en":"To fill and dry means to become fuller with water and then lose water during drier periods.","zh":"fill and dry 指在有水時變得更滿，然後在較乾時期失水。"},{"en":"A playground puddle may fill and dry repeatedly during a rainy week.","zh":"雨季一星期內，操場水氹可能反覆注滿又乾掉。"},{"en":"Changes between wet and dry conditions can leave marks in sediments.","zh":"濕和乾之間的變化可以在沉積物中留下痕跡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated water-level change.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆的水位變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"changes in precipitation","meaning":"降水量變化","examples":[{"en":"The sediment records changes in precipitation.","zh":"沉積物記錄降水量變化。"},{"en":"Changes in precipitation are increases or decreases in rain, snow, or other forms of water falling from the sky.","zh":"changes in precipitation 指雨、雪或其他從天空落下的水分增加或減少。"},{"en":"Farmers watch changes in precipitation because crops need enough water.","zh":"農夫留意降水量變化，因為作物需要足夠水分。"},{"en":"If precipitation drops for many years, lakes may shrink and soils may dry.","zh":"如果降水多年下降，湖泊可能縮小，土壤可能變乾。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on changes in rainfall or similar water input.","zh":"這個短語重點是降雨或類似水分輸入的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"tropical climate","meaning":"熱帶氣候","examples":[{"en":"The lake provides evidence about changes in the tropical climate.","zh":"該湖提供有關熱帶氣候變化的證據。"},{"en":"Tropical climate is the climate of warm regions near the equator, often with wet and dry seasons.","zh":"tropical climate 指赤道附近溫暖地區的氣候，通常有雨季和旱季。"},{"en":"A tropical climate may bring heavy rain, high humidity, and warm temperatures.","zh":"熱帶氣候可能帶來大雨、高濕度和溫暖氣溫。"},{"en":"Changes in tropical climate can affect forests, farming, and water supply.","zh":"熱帶氣候變化可以影響森林、農業和供水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes climate in tropical regions, not simply hot weather.","zh":"這個短語描述熱帶地區氣候，而不只是炎熱天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a record of","meaning":"……的記錄","examples":[{"en":"The sediment contains a record of climatic change.","zh":"沉積物包含氣候變化的記錄。"},{"en":"A record of something is evidence or information that preserves what happened before.","zh":"a record of something 指保存過去發生事情的證據或資訊。"},{"en":"A student’s report cards contain a record of academic progress.","zh":"學生成績表包含學業進步的記錄。"},{"en":"Records help people compare the past with the present.","zh":"記錄幫助人把過去與現在比較。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stored evidence, not only written documents.","zh":"這個短語描述被保存的證據，不只是書面文件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be hidden in","meaning":"隱藏在……之中","examples":[{"en":"The record of climate change is hidden in the sediment.","zh":"氣候變化記錄隱藏在沉積物之中。"},{"en":"To be hidden in something means to be present there but not immediately visible.","zh":"be hidden in something 指存在於某物之中，但不是立即可見。"},{"en":"A useful clue may be hidden in a student’s repeated grammar mistake.","zh":"有用線索可能隱藏在學生反覆出現的文法錯誤之中。"},{"en":"Hidden evidence often requires special tools or careful analysis to find.","zh":"隱藏證據通常需要特殊工具或仔細分析才能找出。"},{"en":"The phrase describes information that exists but must be uncovered.","zh":"這個短語描述存在但需要被揭示的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"below the lake bottom","meaning":"在湖底以下","examples":[{"en":"Important evidence lies below the lake bottom.","zh":"重要證據位於湖底以下。"},{"en":"Below the lake bottom means under the surface layer at the bottom of a lake.","zh":"below the lake bottom 指在湖底表層之下。"},{"en":"Engineers may study soil below the harbour bottom before building a bridge.","zh":"工程師建橋前可能研究港底以下的土壤。"},{"en":"Material below the bottom can preserve older layers that surface inspection cannot show.","zh":"底部以下的物質可以保存表面檢查看不到的較舊層次。"},{"en":"The phrase points to hidden underground or underwater layers.","zh":"這個短語指出隱藏的地下或水下層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"one of the best sites for","meaning":"研究……的最佳地點之一","examples":[{"en":"The lake is one of the best sites for studying tropical climate change.","zh":"該湖是研究熱帶氣候變化的最佳地點之一。"},{"en":"One of the best sites for something means one of the most useful or suitable places for that activity.","zh":"one of the best sites for something 指進行某活動最有用或最合適的地點之一。"},{"en":"A quiet library may be one of the best sites for exam revision.","zh":"安靜圖書館可能是考試溫習的最佳地點之一。"},{"en":"A good study site gives researchers clear evidence and practical access.","zh":"好的研究地點能提供清楚證據和實際進入條件。"},{"en":"The phrase praises a place’s value for a particular purpose.","zh":"這個短語讚揚某地方對特定目的的價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the study of","meaning":"對……的研究","examples":[{"en":"The site is valuable for the study of ancient climates.","zh":"該地點對古代氣候研究很有價值。"},{"en":"The study of something means careful learning, research, or investigation about it.","zh":"the study of something 指對某事的仔細學習、研究或調查。"},{"en":"The study of local history can help students understand their community.","zh":"對本地歷史的研究可以幫助學生理解自己的社區。"},{"en":"Careful study produces knowledge that casual observation may miss.","zh":"仔細研究能產生隨意觀察可能看漏的知識。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and often used in academic contexts.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於學術語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the heat engine for","meaning":"……的熱力引擎","examples":[{"en":"The tropics are sometimes described as the heat engine for the Earth’s climate.","zh":"熱帶地區有時被形容為地球氣候的熱力引擎。"},{"en":"The heat engine for something is the main source of heat energy that drives a larger system.","zh":"heat engine for something 指推動較大系統的主要熱能來源。"},{"en":"A busy kitchen can feel like the heat engine for a restaurant because it drives all meal service.","zh":"繁忙廚房可像餐廳的熱力引擎，因為它推動所有膳食服務。"},{"en":"Tropical heat affects winds, rainfall, and global climate patterns.","zh":"熱帶熱量影響風、降雨和全球氣候模式。"},{"en":"The phrase is a metaphor for the source that powers a system.","zh":"這個短語是比喻，指為系統提供動力的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"global climate","meaning":"全球氣候","examples":[{"en":"Tropical regions play a major role in the global climate.","zh":"熱帶地區在全球氣候中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"Global climate means the overall climate system of the whole Earth.","zh":"global climate 指整個地球的整體氣候系統。"},{"en":"Scientists study global climate by comparing oceans, forests, ice, and atmosphere.","zh":"科學家透過比較海洋、森林、冰層和大氣來研究全球氣候。"},{"en":"Changes in one region can affect global climate through winds and ocean currents.","zh":"一個地區的變化可以透過風和洋流影響全球氣候。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to worldwide climate patterns, not one city’s weather.","zh":"這個短語指全球氣候模式，而不是某城市天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"records of climate change","meaning":"氣候變化記錄","examples":[{"en":"Scientists need records of climate change from different regions.","zh":"科學家需要來自不同地區的氣候變化記錄。"},{"en":"Records of climate change are evidence showing how climate has changed over time.","zh":"records of climate change 指顯示氣候如何隨時間改變的證據。"},{"en":"Tree rings can provide records of climate change by showing good and bad growth years.","zh":"樹木年輪可以透過顯示好壞生長年份，提供氣候變化記錄。"},{"en":"Many records from different places help scientists see global patterns more clearly.","zh":"來自不同地方的許多記錄幫助科學家更清楚看見全球模式。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to preserved evidence of past climate shifts.","zh":"這個短語指保存下來的過去氣候變化證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sites around the world","meaning":"世界各地的地點","examples":[{"en":"Climate records are collected from sites around the world.","zh":"氣候記錄從世界各地的地點收集得來。"},{"en":"Sites around the world are locations in many different countries or regions.","zh":"sites around the world 指位於許多不同國家或地區的位置。"},{"en":"A charity may collect survey answers from sites around the world to compare living conditions.","zh":"慈善機構可能從世界各地的地點收集調查答案，以比較生活條件。"},{"en":"Global evidence becomes stronger when it comes from many separate places.","zh":"當全球證據來自許多不同地方，它會變得更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses broad geographical coverage.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛地理涵蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"explore the lake’s subsurface","meaning":"探索湖底以下的地層","examples":[{"en":"The researchers used sound energy to explore the lake’s subsurface.","zh":"研究人員使用聲能探索湖底以下的地層。"},{"en":"To explore the lake’s subsurface means to investigate the layers below the lake bottom.","zh":"explore the lake’s subsurface 指調查湖底下方的層次。"},{"en":"Engineers may explore the subsurface below a building site before construction begins.","zh":"工程師可能在施工前探索建築地盤地下地層。"},{"en":"Subsurface exploration can reveal hidden layers, cracks, and buried structures.","zh":"地下探索可以揭示隱藏層次、裂縫和埋藏結構。"},{"en":"The phrase describes studying what lies below the visible bottom.","zh":"這個短語描述研究可見湖底以下的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"working deck area","meaning":"可供工作的甲板空間","examples":[{"en":"The boat needed a large working deck area for the equipment.","zh":"這艘船需要大型可供工作的甲板空間放置設備。"},{"en":"A working deck area is open space on a boat where people can place and operate equipment.","zh":"working deck area 指船上可供人放置和操作設備的開放空間。"},{"en":"A fishing boat needs enough deck area for nets, boxes, and workers.","zh":"漁船需要足夠甲板空間放魚網、箱子和工人。"},{"en":"Without enough deck space, equipment may be unsafe or difficult to use.","zh":"沒有足夠甲板空間，設備可能不安全或難以使用。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on practical workspace on a vessel.","zh":"這個短語重點是船上的實用工作空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"carry eight tons of","meaning":"運載八噸……","examples":[{"en":"The boat was designed to carry eight tons of scientific equipment.","zh":"這艘船被設計來運載八噸科學設備。"},{"en":"To carry eight tons of something means to transport a load weighing eight tons.","zh":"carry eight tons of something 指運送重達八噸的貨物。"},{"en":"A delivery truck may be built to carry several tons of building materials.","zh":"送貨貨車可能被設計來運載數噸建築材料。"},{"en":"If a boat carries heavy equipment, it must be strong and stable enough.","zh":"如果船隻運載重型設備，它必須足夠堅固和穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes transport capacity and weight.","zh":"這個短語描述運輸能力和重量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"scientific equipment","meaning":"科學設備","examples":[{"en":"The research vessel carried several tons of scientific equipment.","zh":"研究船運載了數噸科學設備。"},{"en":"Scientific equipment is tools and machines used to collect, measure, or analyse research data.","zh":"scientific equipment 指用來收集、量度或分析研究數據的工具和機器。"},{"en":"A school laboratory uses scientific equipment such as microscopes and measuring cylinders.","zh":"學校實驗室使用顯微鏡和量筒等科學設備。"},{"en":"Good equipment helps researchers collect accurate and reliable results.","zh":"良好設備幫助研究人員收集準確可靠的結果。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to tools for investigation, not ordinary office supplies.","zh":"這個短語指調查用工具，而不是普通辦公用品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be dubbed","meaning":"被命名為；被稱為","examples":[{"en":"The research boat was dubbed R/V Kilindi.","zh":"這艘研究船被命名為 R/V Kilindi。"},{"en":"To be dubbed something means to be given a name or nickname.","zh":"be dubbed something 指被賦予名稱或暱稱。"},{"en":"Students dubbed their study corner “the grammar station” because they practised there every day.","zh":"學生把學習角稱為「文法站」，因為他們每天在那裏練習。"},{"en":"A memorable name can make a project or object easier to identify.","zh":"好記的名稱可以令項目或物件更容易辨認。"},{"en":"The phrase often means “be called” in an informal or descriptive way.","zh":"這個短語常以較非正式或描述性的方式表示「被稱為」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be constructed in modules","meaning":"以組件形式建造","examples":[{"en":"The boat was constructed in modules so that it could be transported.","zh":"這艘船以組件形式建造，以便運輸。"},{"en":"To be constructed in modules means to be built in separate parts that can be joined later.","zh":"be constructed in modules 指以分開部件建造，之後可以組合起來。"},{"en":"Some classrooms are constructed in modules and moved to schools by truck.","zh":"一些課室以組件形式建造，然後由貨車運到學校。"},{"en":"Modular construction makes transport and assembly easier.","zh":"組件式建造令運輸和組裝更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes building something in detachable sections.","zh":"這個短語描述以可拆分部分建造某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be dismantled","meaning":"被拆卸","examples":[{"en":"The boat was dismantled before being shipped to Ghana.","zh":"這艘船在運往加納前被拆卸。"},{"en":"To be dismantled means to be taken apart into separate pieces.","zh":"be dismantled 指被拆開成獨立部件。"},{"en":"Workers dismantled the stage after the school concert ended.","zh":"學校音樂會結束後，工人拆卸舞台。"},{"en":"Dismantling a large object can make it easier to move or store.","zh":"拆卸大型物件可以令它更容易搬運或儲存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes taking something apart, not destroying it permanently.","zh":"這個短語描述拆開某物，而不是永久破壞它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be packed inside","meaning":"被裝入……內","examples":[{"en":"The boat’s modules were packed inside a shipping container.","zh":"船的組件被裝入貨運貨櫃內。"},{"en":"To be packed inside something means to be placed and stored within it for transport or protection.","zh":"be packed inside something 指被放入並存放在某物內，以便運輸或保護。"},{"en":"School computers may be packed inside boxes before moving to a new campus.","zh":"學校電腦搬到新校舍前，可能被裝入箱內。"},{"en":"Careful packing prevents damage during transport.","zh":"仔細包裝可以防止運輸期間損壞。"},{"en":"The phrase describes putting items into a container.","zh":"這個短語描述把物件放入容器中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"shipping container","meaning":"貨運貨櫃","examples":[{"en":"The dismantled boat was transported in a shipping container.","zh":"拆卸後的船被放在貨運貨櫃中運輸。"},{"en":"A shipping container is a large metal box used for transporting goods by ship, train, or truck.","zh":"shipping container 指用於船、火車或貨車運送貨物的大型金屬箱。"},{"en":"Shops often receive imported goods packed inside shipping containers.","zh":"商店常收到裝在貨運貨櫃內的進口貨物。"},{"en":"Containers protect goods and make long-distance transport more organised.","zh":"貨櫃保護貨物，並令長距離運輸更有組織。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a standard transport box, not ordinary packaging.","zh":"這個短語指標準運輸箱，而不是普通包裝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be reassembled","meaning":"被重新組裝","examples":[{"en":"The research vessel was reassembled in Ghana.","zh":"研究船在加納被重新組裝。"},{"en":"To be reassembled means to be put back together after being taken apart.","zh":"be reassembled 指拆開後被重新組合起來。"},{"en":"A desk may be reassembled after being moved to a new classroom.","zh":"書桌搬到新課室後可能被重新組裝。"},{"en":"Reassembly requires matching the parts correctly so the object works again.","zh":"重新組裝需要正確配對部件，使物件再次運作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rebuilding from separated components.","zh":"這個短語描述由分開組件重新建成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"over a ten-day period","meaning":"在十天期間","examples":[{"en":"The boat was reassembled over a ten-day period.","zh":"這艘船在十天期間被重新組裝。"},{"en":"Over a ten-day period means during a span of ten days.","zh":"over a ten-day period 指在一段十天的時間內。"},{"en":"Students revised the whole grammar booklet over a ten-day period before the exam.","zh":"學生在考試前十天期間複習整本文法小冊子。"},{"en":"Spreading work over several days can make a large task manageable.","zh":"把工作分散在幾天內可以令大型任務較易處理。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the duration of an activity.","zh":"這個短語給出活動持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rural village","meaning":"鄉郊村落","examples":[{"en":"The vessel was rebuilt in the rural village of Abono.","zh":"這艘船在 Abono 鄉郊村落被重建。"},{"en":"A rural village is a small settlement in the countryside, away from large cities.","zh":"rural village 指遠離大城市、位於鄉郊的小聚落。"},{"en":"A rural village may have farms, small roads, and close community ties.","zh":"鄉郊村落可能有農田、小路和緊密社區關係。"},{"en":"Working in a rural village can require extra planning because services may be limited.","zh":"在鄉郊村落工作可能需要額外規劃，因為服務可能有限。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both size and countryside location.","zh":"這個短語同時描述規模和鄉郊位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"spend the next two weeks doing","meaning":"用接下來兩星期做……","examples":[{"en":"The team spent the next two weeks testing the equipment.","zh":"團隊用接下來兩星期測試設備。"},{"en":"To spend the next two weeks doing something means to use the following fourteen days for that activity.","zh":"spend the next two weeks doing something 指把隨後十四天用於某活動。"},{"en":"A student may spend the next two weeks preparing for a speaking exam.","zh":"學生可能用接下來兩星期準備口語考試。"},{"en":"Setting aside two weeks gives people enough time to check problems carefully.","zh":"預留兩星期讓人有足夠時間仔細檢查問題。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a planned period of focused work.","zh":"這個短語突出一段有計劃的專注工作時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"test the boat and equipment","meaning":"測試船隻及設備","examples":[{"en":"The researchers tested the boat and equipment before beginning their work.","zh":"研究人員開始工作前測試船隻及設備。"},{"en":"To test the boat and equipment means to check that the vessel and tools work safely and correctly.","zh":"test the boat and equipment 指檢查船隻和工具能否安全正確運作。"},{"en":"A teacher tests the projector and microphone before a school assembly.","zh":"老師在學校集會前測試投影機和咪高峰。"},{"en":"Testing prevents delays because problems can be fixed before real work starts.","zh":"測試能防止延誤，因為問題可在正式工作開始前修好。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preparation through checking function and safety.","zh":"這個短語描述透過檢查功能和安全作準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"return to the United States","meaning":"返回美國","examples":[{"en":"The team returned to the United States for the holidays.","zh":"團隊返回美國度假。"},{"en":"To return to the United States means to go back to the US after being somewhere else.","zh":"return to the United States 指在身處其他地方後回到美國。"},{"en":"An exchange student may return to the United States after a semester abroad.","zh":"交換生在海外讀完一個學期後可能返回美國。"},{"en":"Returning home can allow people to rest, report progress, or prepare for the next stage.","zh":"回家可以讓人休息、匯報進度或準備下一階段。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement back to the US.","zh":"這個短語描述回到美國的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in mid-January","meaning":"在一月中旬","examples":[{"en":"Five members of the team returned to Ghana in mid-January.","zh":"團隊五名成員在一月中旬返回加納。"},{"en":"In mid-January means around the middle of January.","zh":"in mid-January 指大約在一月中間。"},{"en":"A school may hold mock exams in mid-January after the winter break.","zh":"學校可能在寒假後的一月中旬舉行模擬考試。"},{"en":"Giving this time phrase helps readers place events in the year.","zh":"提供這個時間短語幫助讀者把事件放在一年之中。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate date, not one exact day.","zh":"這個短語給出大約日期，而不是確切某一天。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"graduate student","meaning":"研究院學生","examples":[{"en":"Keely Brooks was an earth sciences graduate student.","zh":"Keely Brooks 是地球科學研究院學生。"},{"en":"A graduate student is a university student studying for a master’s or doctoral degree.","zh":"graduate student 指正在修讀碩士或博士學位的大學學生。"},{"en":"A graduate student may help a professor collect data and write research papers.","zh":"研究院學生可能協助教授收集數據和撰寫研究論文。"},{"en":"Graduate study often involves more independent research than undergraduate study.","zh":"研究院學習通常比本科學習涉及更多獨立研究。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a student at an advanced university level.","zh":"這個短語指出高等大學階段的學生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"research analyst","meaning":"研究分析員","examples":[{"en":"Peter Cattaneo worked as a research analyst.","zh":"Peter Cattaneo 擔任研究分析員。"},{"en":"A research analyst is a person who collects, organises, and interprets data for a study or organisation.","zh":"research analyst 指為研究或機構收集、整理和詮釋數據的人。"},{"en":"A company may hire a research analyst to study customer feedback.","zh":"公司可能聘請研究分析員研究顧客回饋。"},{"en":"Good analysis turns raw data into useful conclusions.","zh":"良好分析把原始數據變成有用結論。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to someone who works with information and evidence.","zh":"這個短語指處理資訊和證據的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"postdoctoral scholar","meaning":"博士後研究員","examples":[{"en":"Kiram Lezzar was a postdoctoral scholar.","zh":"Kiram Lezzar 是博士後研究員。"},{"en":"A postdoctoral scholar is a researcher who has completed a Ph.D. and continues advanced research.","zh":"postdoctoral scholar 指已完成博士學位並繼續進行高階研究的人。"},{"en":"A postdoctoral scholar may work in a university laboratory before becoming a professor.","zh":"博士後研究員可能在成為教授前於大學實驗室工作。"},{"en":"Postdoctoral work helps researchers build expertise and publish more studies.","zh":"博士後工作幫助研究人員建立專業能力並發表更多研究。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies an early-career researcher after doctoral training.","zh":"這個短語指出博士訓練後的早期職業研究人員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"geophysical field engineer","meaning":"地球物理實地工程師","examples":[{"en":"James McGill worked as a geophysical field engineer.","zh":"James McGill 擔任地球物理實地工程師。"},{"en":"A geophysical field engineer is an engineer who uses instruments outdoors to measure Earth’s physical features.","zh":"geophysical field engineer 指在戶外使用儀器量度地球物理特徵的工程師。"},{"en":"A geophysical field engineer may test soil and rock conditions before tunnel construction.","zh":"地球物理實地工程師可能在隧道施工前測試土壤和岩石狀況。"},{"en":"Field engineers help collect reliable data outside the laboratory.","zh":"實地工程師幫助在實驗室以外收集可靠數據。"},{"en":"The phrase combines Earth science, engineering, and practical fieldwork.","zh":"這個短語結合地球科學、工程和實地工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Ph.D. student","meaning":"博士研究生","examples":[{"en":"Nick Peters was a Ph.D. student in geophysics.","zh":"Nick Peters 是地球物理學博士研究生。"},{"en":"A Ph.D. student is a doctoral student doing advanced research in a specialised field.","zh":"Ph.D. student 指在專門領域進行高階研究的博士學生。"},{"en":"A Ph.D. student may spend years writing a thesis on one research question.","zh":"博士研究生可能花多年時間撰寫關於一個研究問題的論文。"},{"en":"Doctoral research trains students to produce original knowledge.","zh":"博士研究訓練學生產生原創知識。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to someone studying for a doctorate.","zh":"這個短語指正在修讀博士學位的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"collect data about","meaning":"收集有關……的數據","examples":[{"en":"The researchers began collecting data about the lake’s subsurface.","zh":"研究人員開始收集有關湖底以下地層的數據。"},{"en":"To collect data about something means to gather measurements, observations, or information about it.","zh":"collect data about something 指收集關於某事的量度、觀察或資訊。"},{"en":"A teacher may collect data about attendance to understand why students miss lessons.","zh":"老師可能收集有關出席率的數據，以了解學生為何缺課。"},{"en":"Data collection helps people move from guesses to evidence-based conclusions.","zh":"數據收集幫助人由猜測走向基於證據的結論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gathering information for analysis.","zh":"這個短語描述收集資訊以供分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"seismic reflection profiling","meaning":"地震反射剖面技術","examples":[{"en":"The team used a technique called seismic reflection profiling.","zh":"團隊使用一種稱為地震反射剖面技術的方法。"},{"en":"Seismic reflection profiling is a method that uses reflected sound waves to study layers below the ground or lake bottom.","zh":"seismic reflection profiling 指利用反射聲波研究地下或湖底以下層次的方法。"},{"en":"Engineers may use seismic reflection profiling before building tunnels or offshore platforms.","zh":"工程師在建隧道或離岸平台前，可能使用地震反射剖面技術。"},{"en":"Reflected waves can reveal hidden structures without digging directly into them.","zh":"反射波可以揭示隱藏結構，而不需直接挖掘。"},{"en":"The phrase names a geophysical imaging technique.","zh":"這個短語命名一種地球物理成像技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in this process","meaning":"在這個過程中","examples":[{"en":"In this process, sound waves are sent beneath the lake bottom.","zh":"在這個過程中，聲波被送到湖底以下。"},{"en":"In this process means during the method or series of steps just described.","zh":"in this process 指在剛描述的方法或一連串步驟中。"},{"en":"In this process, students first plan, then draft, then revise their essays.","zh":"在這個過程中，學生先構思，然後起草，再修改作文。"},{"en":"The phrase helps guide readers through a sequence of actions.","zh":"這個短語幫助引導讀者理解一連串行動。"},{"en":"It refers back to the procedure being explained.","zh":"它指回正在解釋的程序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"high-pressure air gun","meaning":"高壓氣槍","examples":[{"en":"A high-pressure air gun created small explosions in the water.","zh":"高壓氣槍在水中產生小型爆破。"},{"en":"A high-pressure air gun is a device that releases compressed air with great force.","zh":"high-pressure air gun 指以強大力量釋放壓縮空氣的裝置。"},{"en":"Engineers may use a high-pressure tool to clean blocked pipes.","zh":"工程師可能使用高壓工具清理堵塞喉管。"},{"en":"Strong air pressure can create sound energy for underwater research.","zh":"強大氣壓可以產生用於水下研究的聲能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a technical device powered by compressed air.","zh":"這個短語描述由壓縮空氣驅動的技術裝置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be used to create","meaning":"被用作產生……","examples":[{"en":"The air gun was used to create pneumatic explosions.","zh":"氣槍被用作產生氣壓爆破。"},{"en":"To be used to create something means to serve as the tool or method for producing it.","zh":"be used to create something 指作為產生某物的工具或方法。"},{"en":"A projector is used to create a large image on a classroom wall.","zh":"投影機被用作在課室牆上產生大型影像。"},{"en":"The tool chosen affects the quality, safety, and usefulness of the result.","zh":"所選工具會影響結果的質素、安全和用途。"},{"en":"The phrase explains purpose and function.","zh":"這個短語解釋目的和功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pneumatic explosions","meaning":"氣壓爆破","examples":[{"en":"Small pneumatic explosions generated sound energy.","zh":"小型氣壓爆破產生聲能。"},{"en":"Pneumatic explosions are bursts produced by compressed air rather than chemical explosives.","zh":"pneumatic explosions 指由壓縮空氣而不是化學炸藥產生的爆發。"},{"en":"A workshop may use pneumatic tools that are powered by air pressure.","zh":"工場可能使用由氣壓驅動的氣動工具。"},{"en":"In lake research, controlled pneumatic explosions can send sound waves downward.","zh":"在湖泊研究中，受控氣壓爆破可以把聲波向下傳送。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to air-pressure bursts, not large destructive bombs.","zh":"這個短語指氣壓爆發，而不是大型破壞性炸彈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sound energy","meaning":"聲能","examples":[{"en":"The explosions produced sound energy beneath the boat.","zh":"爆破在船下方產生聲能。"},{"en":"Sound energy is energy carried by vibrations travelling through air, water, or solid material.","zh":"sound energy 指由震動透過空氣、水或固體材料傳遞的能量。"},{"en":"A speaker uses sound energy to send music through a classroom.","zh":"揚聲器使用聲能把音樂傳遍課室。"},{"en":"Sound energy can bounce off hidden layers and return as useful signals.","zh":"聲能可以從隱藏層反彈並作為有用訊號返回。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to energy from sound vibrations.","zh":"這個短語指來自聲音震動的能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"penetrate into","meaning":"穿透進入……","examples":[{"en":"The sound energy penetrated deep into the lake’s subsurface.","zh":"聲能深深穿透進入湖底以下地層。"},{"en":"To penetrate into something means to enter deeply into it.","zh":"penetrate into something 指深入進入某物之中。"},{"en":"Rainwater may penetrate into dry soil after a long storm.","zh":"長時間暴雨後，雨水可能穿透進入乾燥泥土。"},{"en":"When sound penetrates into layers, it can reveal what lies below.","zh":"當聲音穿透進入層次，它可以揭示下方有甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep entry, not surface contact only.","zh":"這個短語描述深入進入，而不只是表面接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bounce back to the surface","meaning":"反彈回水面","examples":[{"en":"The sound waves bounced back to the surface of the water.","zh":"聲波反彈回水面。"},{"en":"To bounce back to the surface means to return upward after hitting something below.","zh":"bounce back to the surface 指撞到下方某物後向上返回表面。"},{"en":"A ball dropped into a pool may bounce back to the surface if it floats.","zh":"如果球能浮起，掉進泳池後可能反彈回水面。"},{"en":"Returning waves can be recorded and used to understand what they struck.","zh":"返回的波可以被記錄，並用來了解它們撞到甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes upward return after reflection.","zh":"這個短語描述反射後向上返回。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reflected sound energy","meaning":"反射聲能","examples":[{"en":"The researchers recorded the reflected sound energy.","zh":"研究人員記錄反射聲能。"},{"en":"Reflected sound energy is sound energy that has bounced back after hitting a surface or layer.","zh":"reflected sound energy 指撞到表面或層次後反彈回來的聲能。"},{"en":"Echoes in a hall are reflected sound energy returning from walls.","zh":"大廳中的回聲是從牆壁返回的反射聲能。"},{"en":"Scientists analyse reflected energy to identify hidden shapes or materials.","zh":"科學家分析反射能量，以識別隱藏形狀或材料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sound after it returns from something it struck.","zh":"這個短語描述聲音撞到某物後返回的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be detected by","meaning":"被……探測到","examples":[{"en":"The returning sound energy was detected by underwater microphones.","zh":"返回的聲能被水底咪高峰探測到。"},{"en":"To be detected by something means to be noticed or measured by an instrument or person.","zh":"be detected by something 指被儀器或人注意到或量度到。"},{"en":"A fever can be detected by a thermometer.","zh":"發燒可以被溫度計探測到。"},{"en":"Detection tools help people find signals that human senses cannot easily notice.","zh":"探測工具幫助人找出人類感官不易注意到的訊號。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the method or instrument that finds something.","zh":"這個短語指出找出某物的方法或儀器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"underwater microphones","meaning":"水底咪高峰","examples":[{"en":"Underwater microphones detected the returning sound waves.","zh":"水底咪高峰探測到返回的聲波。"},{"en":"Underwater microphones are devices that listen to or record sounds beneath the water.","zh":"underwater microphones 指聆聽或記錄水下聲音的裝置。"},{"en":"Marine biologists use underwater microphones to record whale calls.","zh":"海洋生物學家使用水底咪高峰記錄鯨魚叫聲。"},{"en":"These devices allow researchers to study sounds that cannot be heard clearly from the surface.","zh":"這些裝置讓研究人員研究從水面上聽不清楚的聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to sound-recording tools used in water.","zh":"這個短語指在水中使用的錄音工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hydrophones","meaning":"水聽器","examples":[{"en":"The underwater microphones used in the project are called hydrophones.","zh":"該項目使用的水底咪高峰稱為水聽器。"},{"en":"Hydrophones are special microphones designed to detect sound underwater.","zh":"hydrophones 指專門設計來探測水下聲音的咪高峰。"},{"en":"Scientists may place hydrophones in the sea to monitor ships or marine animals.","zh":"科學家可能把水聽器放在海中監測船隻或海洋動物。"},{"en":"Hydrophones turn underwater vibrations into signals researchers can record.","zh":"水聽器把水下震動轉換成研究人員可以記錄的訊號。"},{"en":"The word names a technical tool for listening below water.","zh":"這個詞命名用於水下聆聽的技術工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be embedded in","meaning":"嵌入……之中","examples":[{"en":"The hydrophones were embedded in a long cable.","zh":"水聽器嵌入一條長纜線之中。"},{"en":"To be embedded in something means to be fixed firmly inside it.","zh":"be embedded in something 指被牢固地固定在某物內。"},{"en":"Small lights may be embedded in a classroom display board.","zh":"小燈可能嵌入課室展示板之中。"},{"en":"Embedded devices stay in place and can work as part of a larger system.","zh":"嵌入式裝置會保持位置，並作為較大系統的一部分運作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being placed securely within another object.","zh":"這個短語描述被安全放置於另一物件之內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a 50-metre-long cable","meaning":"五十米長的纜線","examples":[{"en":"The microphones were attached to a 50-metre-long cable.","zh":"這些咪高峰連接到一條五十米長的纜線。"},{"en":"A 50-metre-long cable is a cable measuring fifty metres from end to end.","zh":"50-metre-long cable 指由一端到另一端長五十米的纜線。"},{"en":"A school stage may use a long cable to connect microphones to speakers.","zh":"學校舞台可能使用長纜線把咪高峰連接到揚聲器。"},{"en":"A longer cable allows equipment to be spread out or pulled behind a vehicle or boat.","zh":"較長纜線讓設備可以分散放置或拖在車船後方。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the cable’s length and purpose.","zh":"這個短語提供纜線長度和用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be towed behind","meaning":"被拖在……後方","examples":[{"en":"The cable was towed behind the research boat.","zh":"纜線被拖在研究船後方。"},{"en":"To be towed behind something means to be pulled along after it.","zh":"be towed behind something 指在某物後面被拉動。"},{"en":"A broken car may be towed behind a tow truck.","zh":"故障汽車可能被拖在拖車後方。"},{"en":"Towing equipment behind a boat lets it collect data while the boat moves.","zh":"把設備拖在船後方，可以讓它在船移動時收集數據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being pulled from the rear.","zh":"這個短語描述從後方被拖行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cross the lake","meaning":"橫越湖面","examples":[{"en":"The boat crossed the lake repeatedly while gathering data.","zh":"這艘船在收集數據時反覆橫越湖面。"},{"en":"To cross the lake means to travel from one side or part of the lake to another.","zh":"cross the lake 指由湖的一邊或一處移動到另一邊或另一處。"},{"en":"A small ferry may cross the lake every morning to take students to school.","zh":"小渡輪可能每天早上橫越湖面接送學生上學。"},{"en":"Repeated crossings allow researchers to collect data from many positions.","zh":"反覆橫越讓研究人員能從許多位置收集數據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement across the water surface.","zh":"這個短語描述在水面上橫向移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a carefully designed grid pattern","meaning":"經精心設計的網格路線","examples":[{"en":"The boat followed a carefully designed grid pattern.","zh":"這艘船沿着經精心設計的網格路線行駛。"},{"en":"A carefully designed grid pattern is a planned route made of crossing lines, like squares on a map.","zh":"carefully designed grid pattern 指由交叉線組成、像地圖方格一樣的計劃路線。"},{"en":"Students may search a classroom in a grid pattern to find a lost earring.","zh":"學生可能以網格方式搜尋課室，尋找遺失耳環。"},{"en":"A grid helps researchers cover an area systematically and avoid missing sections.","zh":"網格幫助研究人員有系統地覆蓋區域，避免漏掉部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised movement, not random travel.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織移動，而不是隨機行駛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on-board computers","meaning":"船上電腦","examples":[{"en":"On-board computers recorded the signals from the hydrophones.","zh":"船上電腦記錄來自水聽器的訊號。"},{"en":"On-board computers are computers carried on a vehicle, boat, or aircraft and used during operation.","zh":"on-board computers 指安裝或攜帶於車輛、船隻或飛機上並在操作期間使用的電腦。"},{"en":"A bus may use on-board computers to track location and passenger numbers.","zh":"巴士可能使用車上電腦追蹤位置和乘客數量。"},{"en":"Computers on board can record data immediately while the equipment is working.","zh":"船上或車上電腦可以在設備運作時立即記錄數據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to computers installed or carried on the vehicle.","zh":"這個短語指安裝或攜帶在交通工具上的電腦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"record the signals","meaning":"記錄訊號","examples":[{"en":"The computers recorded the returning sound signals.","zh":"電腦記錄返回的聲音訊號。"},{"en":"To record the signals means to capture and store measurable messages from instruments.","zh":"record the signals 指捕捉並儲存來自儀器的可量度訊息。"},{"en":"A heart monitor records signals from a patient’s heartbeat.","zh":"心臟監測器會記錄病人心跳訊號。"},{"en":"Recorded signals can later be checked, compared, and analysed.","zh":"被記錄的訊號之後可以被檢查、比較和分析。"},{"en":"The phrase describes saving data for later study.","zh":"這個短語描述保存數據以供後續研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the resulting data","meaning":"由此獲得的數據","examples":[{"en":"The resulting data were later analysed by the researchers.","zh":"由此獲得的數據後來由研究人員分析。"},{"en":"The resulting data are the information produced from a process, test, or measurement.","zh":"resulting data 指由某個過程、測試或量度產生的資訊。"},{"en":"After a class survey, the resulting data showed how many students preferred online homework.","zh":"班級調查後，由此獲得的數據顯示有多少學生較喜歡網上功課。"},{"en":"Data produced by an experiment must be organised before conclusions can be drawn.","zh":"實驗產生的數據必須先整理，然後才能得出結論。"},{"en":"The phrase points to information created by earlier work.","zh":"這個短語指出由早前工作產生的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be processed and analysed","meaning":"被處理和分析","examples":[{"en":"The data were processed and analysed in the laboratory.","zh":"這些數據在實驗室內被處理和分析。"},{"en":"To be processed and analysed means to be organised, cleaned, examined, and interpreted.","zh":"be processed and analysed 指被整理、清理、檢視和詮釋。"},{"en":"Exam results are processed and analysed before teachers decide what to reteach.","zh":"考試成績在老師決定重教甚麼前會被處理和分析。"},{"en":"Processing turns raw information into a form that can reveal patterns.","zh":"處理會把原始資訊變成能揭示模式的形式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the work done after data collection.","zh":"這個短語描述數據收集後進行的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the laboratory","meaning":"在實驗室內","examples":[{"en":"The research team analysed the data in the laboratory.","zh":"研究團隊在實驗室內分析數據。"},{"en":"In the laboratory means inside a controlled place where scientific tests or analysis are done.","zh":"in the laboratory 指在進行科學測試或分析的受控地方內。"},{"en":"Students may test water samples in the laboratory during a science lesson.","zh":"學生可能在科學課於實驗室內測試水樣本。"},{"en":"Laboratory analysis can be more precise than field observation alone.","zh":"實驗室分析可以比單靠野外觀察更精確。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the scientific workplace used for testing.","zh":"這個短語指出用於測試的科學工作場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"give someone a good idea of","meaning":"令某人充分了解……","examples":[{"en":"The results will give scientists a good idea of the basin’s shape.","zh":"結果將令科學家充分了解盆地的形狀。"},{"en":"To give someone a good idea of something means to help them understand it fairly clearly.","zh":"give someone a good idea of something 指幫助某人相當清楚地理解某事。"},{"en":"A practice test gives students a good idea of how hard the real exam will be.","zh":"模擬測驗令學生充分了解正式考試會有多難。"},{"en":"Clear results help people picture something they cannot directly see.","zh":"清楚結果幫助人想像不能直接看見的事物。"},{"en":"The phrase means provide a useful understanding, not complete certainty.","zh":"這個短語指提供有用理解，而不是完全確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the shape of the basin","meaning":"盆地的形狀","examples":[{"en":"The signals revealed the shape of the lake basin.","zh":"訊號揭示了湖盆的形狀。"},{"en":"The shape of the basin is the form and outline of the hollow area holding the lake.","zh":"shape of the basin 指盛載湖水的低陷區域的形態和輪廓。"},{"en":"Engineers study the shape of a harbour basin before planning boat routes.","zh":"工程師規劃船隻路線前會研究港盆形狀。"},{"en":"Basin shape affects water depth, sediment movement, and where samples should be taken.","zh":"盆地形狀會影響水深、沉積物移動和採樣位置。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the physical form of a low area.","zh":"這個短語指低地區域的實體形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"layers of sediment","meaning":"沉積層","examples":[{"en":"The lake contains many layers of sediment.","zh":"該湖包含許多沉積層。"},{"en":"Layers of sediment are separate levels of mud, sand, minerals, or organic material built up over time.","zh":"layers of sediment 指隨時間累積的泥、沙、礦物或有機物的不同層次。"},{"en":"A gardener may see layers of soil when digging a deep hole.","zh":"園丁挖深洞時，可能看見不同土壤層。"},{"en":"Each layer can preserve evidence from a different period.","zh":"每一層都可以保存不同時期的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stacked natural material.","zh":"這個短語描述一層層堆疊的自然物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sediment accumulation","meaning":"沉積物累積","examples":[{"en":"The researchers identified changes in sediment accumulation.","zh":"研究人員識別出沉積物累積的變化。"},{"en":"Sediment accumulation is the gradual build-up of mud, sand, minerals, or organic matter.","zh":"sediment accumulation 指泥、沙、礦物或有機物逐漸堆積。"},{"en":"A drain can be blocked by sediment accumulation after heavy rain washes soil into it.","zh":"大雨把泥土沖進排水渠後，沉積物累積可能令它堵塞。"},{"en":"Changes in accumulation can show changes in water flow, rainfall, or erosion.","zh":"累積變化可以顯示水流、降雨或侵蝕變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes material slowly collecting over time.","zh":"這個短語描述物質隨時間慢慢聚集。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"major changes in","meaning":"……的重大變化","examples":[{"en":"The data revealed major changes in sediment accumulation.","zh":"數據揭示沉積物累積的重大變化。"},{"en":"Major changes in something are large or important differences over time.","zh":"major changes in something 指某事隨時間出現的大幅或重要差異。"},{"en":"A school may see major changes in attendance after bus routes are improved.","zh":"巴士路線改善後，學校可能看見出席率的重大變化。"},{"en":"Major changes often require explanation because they affect the overall pattern.","zh":"重大變化通常需要解釋，因為它們影響整體模式。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the difference is significant, not minor.","zh":"這個短語表示差異重要，而不是輕微。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"develop a three-dimensional perspective of","meaning":"建立……的立體視圖","examples":[{"en":"The scientists developed a three-dimensional perspective of the lake’s subsurface.","zh":"科學家建立了湖底以下地層的立體視圖。"},{"en":"To develop a three-dimensional perspective of something means to build a view showing depth, width, and height.","zh":"develop a three-dimensional perspective of something 指建立顯示深度、寬度和高度的視圖。"},{"en":"Architects use computer models to develop a three-dimensional perspective of a new school building.","zh":"建築師使用電腦模型建立新校舍的立體視圖。"},{"en":"A 3D view helps people understand shapes that flat diagrams may hide.","zh":"立體視圖幫助人理解平面圖可能隱藏的形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating a fuller spatial understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述建立更完整的空間理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"three-dimensional perspective","meaning":"三維視角；立體視圖","examples":[{"en":"The research produced a three-dimensional perspective of the basin.","zh":"這項研究產生了盆地的三維視角。"},{"en":"A three-dimensional perspective is a view that shows an object’s depth as well as its length and width.","zh":"three-dimensional perspective 指顯示物件深度以及長度和寬度的視圖。"},{"en":"A 3D classroom model gives students a three-dimensional perspective of a volcano.","zh":"立體火山模型給學生一個三維視角來理解火山。"},{"en":"Seeing depth helps people understand how parts connect in space.","zh":"看見深度幫助人理解各部分在空間中如何連接。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts with a flat two-dimensional picture.","zh":"這個短語與平面的二維圖像形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be laid down","meaning":"被沉積下來","examples":[{"en":"Layers of sediment were laid down over thousands of years.","zh":"沉積層在數千年間被沉積下來。"},{"en":"To be laid down means to be deposited or placed gradually in layers.","zh":"be laid down 指逐漸以層狀沉積或放置下來。"},{"en":"Dust may be laid down on a shelf if no one cleans it for months.","zh":"如果幾個月沒有人清潔，灰塵可能在架上沉積下來。"},{"en":"Sediment laid down over time can preserve a sequence of past conditions.","zh":"隨時間沉積下來的沉積物可以保存過去狀況的次序。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual deposition, not someone placing it by hand.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步沉積，而不是有人親手放下。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"spend four weeks doing","meaning":"花四星期做……","examples":[{"en":"Team members spent four weeks collecting data in Ghana.","zh":"團隊成員花四星期在加納收集數據。"},{"en":"To spend four weeks doing something means to use a period of four weeks for that activity.","zh":"spend four weeks doing something 指用四星期時間進行某活動。"},{"en":"Students may spend four weeks preparing for a public speaking contest.","zh":"學生可能花四星期準備公開演講比賽。"},{"en":"A fixed research period helps teams plan equipment, staff, and daily work.","zh":"固定研究時間幫助團隊規劃設備、人手和每日工作。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the time devoted to a task.","zh":"這個短語突出用於任務的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"seven days a week","meaning":"每星期七天","examples":[{"en":"The researchers worked seven days a week.","zh":"研究人員每星期七天工作。"},{"en":"Seven days a week means every day, from Monday to Sunday.","zh":"seven days a week 指每天，從星期一到星期日。"},{"en":"A convenience store may open seven days a week to serve nearby residents.","zh":"便利店可能每星期七天營業，服務附近居民。"},{"en":"Working every day can increase progress but may also create tiredness.","zh":"每天工作可以加快進度，但也可能造成疲倦。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that there were no rest days.","zh":"這個短語強調沒有休息日。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"just after sunrise","meaning":"日出後不久","examples":[{"en":"The team usually arrived at the lake just after sunrise.","zh":"團隊通常在日出後不久到達湖邊。"},{"en":"Just after sunrise means shortly after the sun has come up in the morning.","zh":"just after sunrise 指早上太陽升起後不久。"},{"en":"Farmers often start work just after sunrise to avoid the midday heat.","zh":"農夫常在日出後不久開始工作，以避開中午炎熱。"},{"en":"Arriving early can give researchers more daylight for fieldwork.","zh":"早到可以給研究人員更多日光進行野外工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a time very early in the day.","zh":"這個短語描述一天中非常早的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"go as planned","meaning":"按計劃進行","examples":[{"en":"On a good day, everything went as planned.","zh":"在順利的日子，一切按計劃進行。"},{"en":"To go as planned means to happen in the way people expected or arranged.","zh":"go as planned 指事情按人們預期或安排的方式發生。"},{"en":"A school trip goes as planned when the bus arrives on time and the weather stays fine.","zh":"當巴士準時到達且天氣良好，學校旅行就按計劃進行。"},{"en":"When work goes as planned, fewer delays and corrections are needed.","zh":"當工作按計劃進行，需要的延誤和修正較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes successful execution of a plan.","zh":"這個短語描述計劃成功執行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be back at the dock","meaning":"返回碼頭","examples":[{"en":"The team could be back at the dock by early afternoon.","zh":"團隊可以在下午較早時間前返回碼頭。"},{"en":"To be back at the dock means to have returned to the place where the boat is tied or loaded.","zh":"be back at the dock 指已回到船隻停泊或裝卸的地方。"},{"en":"Fishermen hope to be back at the dock before the weather changes.","zh":"漁民希望在天氣轉壞前返回碼頭。"},{"en":"Returning to the dock allows people to unload equipment and check results safely.","zh":"返回碼頭讓人安全卸下設備和檢查結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes returning to the boat’s base point.","zh":"這個短語描述回到船的基地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"by early afternoon","meaning":"在下午較早時間之前","examples":[{"en":"The researchers often finished their work by early afternoon.","zh":"研究人員常在下午較早時間之前完成工作。"},{"en":"By early afternoon means no later than the first part of the afternoon.","zh":"by early afternoon 指不遲於下午初段。"},{"en":"Students should submit the project by early afternoon if teachers need time to check it.","zh":"如果老師需要時間檢查，學生應在下午較早時間之前提交項目。"},{"en":"Finishing early can leave time for repairs, rest, or planning the next day.","zh":"早完成可以留下時間維修、休息或規劃翌日工作。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a deadline or completion time.","zh":"這個短語給出限期或完成時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"relatively minor adjustments","meaning":"相對輕微的調整","examples":[{"en":"The equipment required only a few relatively minor adjustments.","zh":"設備只需要少量相對輕微的調整。"},{"en":"Relatively minor adjustments are small changes compared with larger possible problems.","zh":"relatively minor adjustments 指相對於較大問題而言的小改動。"},{"en":"A teacher may make relatively minor adjustments to a worksheet after spotting two unclear questions.","zh":"老師發現兩條題目不清楚後，可能對工作紙作相對輕微的調整。"},{"en":"Small adjustments can improve performance without changing the whole system.","zh":"小調整可以改善表現，而不用改變整個系統。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests the problem was limited and manageable.","zh":"這個短語暗示問題有限且可處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"work well","meaning":"運作良好","examples":[{"en":"The boat and scientific equipment worked well.","zh":"船隻和科學設備運作良好。"},{"en":"To work well means to operate effectively and produce the expected results.","zh":"work well 指有效運作並產生預期結果。"},{"en":"A classroom microphone works well if everyone can hear the teacher clearly.","zh":"如果所有人都能清楚聽到老師說話，課室咪高峰就運作良好。"},{"en":"Equipment that works well saves time and reduces stress.","zh":"運作良好的設備可以節省時間並減少壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes good function, not hard work by a person.","zh":"這個短語描述功能良好，而不是人努力工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"problems that arose","meaning":"出現的問題","examples":[{"en":"Most of the problems that arose were not scientific.","zh":"大多數出現的問題並非科學方面。"},{"en":"Problems that arose are difficulties that appeared during a process.","zh":"problems that arose 指在過程中出現的困難。"},{"en":"The problems that arose during the school trip included rain and a late bus.","zh":"學校旅行期間出現的問題包括下雨和巴士遲到。"},{"en":"When problems arise, teams must decide whether they are serious or manageable.","zh":"當問題出現，團隊必須判斷它們是否嚴重或可處理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes issues that emerge after work has begun.","zh":"這個短語描述工作開始後出現的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"primarily non-scientific","meaning":"主要並非科學方面的","examples":[{"en":"The difficulties were primarily non-scientific.","zh":"困難主要並非科學方面的。"},{"en":"Primarily non-scientific means mainly not related to scientific theory, data, or method.","zh":"primarily non-scientific 指主要與科學理論、數據或方法無關。"},{"en":"A school project may face primarily non-scientific problems, such as room booking or transport.","zh":"學校項目可能面對主要並非科學方面的問題，例如預訂房間或交通。"},{"en":"Non-scientific difficulties can still delay research if they affect access or equipment.","zh":"非科學困難若影響進入地點或設備，仍可延誤研究。"},{"en":"The phrase separates practical or social problems from scientific ones.","zh":"這個短語把實際或社會問題與科學問題分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"tree stumps","meaning":"樹樁","examples":[{"en":"The boat had to avoid tree stumps in the lake.","zh":"這艘船必須避開湖中的樹樁。"},{"en":"Tree stumps are the remaining lower parts of trees after the trunks have been cut or broken.","zh":"tree stumps 指樹幹被砍斷或折斷後留下的下部。"},{"en":"A hiker may trip over tree stumps hidden under leaves.","zh":"遠足者可能被藏在落葉下的樹樁絆倒。"},{"en":"In water, tree stumps can damage boats or equipment if they are not avoided.","zh":"在水中，若不避開樹樁，它們可以損壞船隻或設備。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to leftover tree bases, not whole trees.","zh":"這個短語指剩下的樹基部，而不是整棵樹。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fishing nets","meaning":"魚網","examples":[{"en":"Fishing nets created obstacles for the research boat.","zh":"魚網為研究船造成障礙。"},{"en":"Fishing nets are nets used to catch fish in lakes, rivers, or seas.","zh":"fishing nets 指用於在湖、河或海中捕魚的網。"},{"en":"Fishermen may leave fishing nets in the water overnight.","zh":"漁民可能把魚網留在水中過夜。"},{"en":"Nets can catch equipment, block movement, or create safety risks for boats.","zh":"魚網可以纏住設備、阻礙移動或為船隻造成安全風險。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to tools for fishing that can also become obstacles.","zh":"這個短語指捕魚工具，也可能成為障礙物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cultural barriers","meaning":"文化障礙","examples":[{"en":"The researchers occasionally faced cultural barriers.","zh":"研究人員偶爾面對文化障礙。"},{"en":"Cultural barriers are difficulties caused by differences in beliefs, customs, language, or social expectations.","zh":"cultural barriers 指由信念、習俗、語言或社會期望差異造成的困難。"},{"en":"A teacher may face cultural barriers when explaining school rules to families from different backgrounds.","zh":"老師向不同背景家庭解釋校規時，可能面對文化障礙。"},{"en":"Cultural barriers can create misunderstanding unless people communicate patiently.","zh":"文化障礙若沒有耐心溝通，可能造成誤會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes social and cultural obstacles, not physical walls.","zh":"這個短語描述社會和文化障礙，而不是實體牆壁。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"occasional misunderstandings","meaning":"偶爾出現的誤會","examples":[{"en":"Occasional misunderstandings occurred between the team and local people.","zh":"團隊與本地人之間偶爾出現誤會。"},{"en":"Occasional misunderstandings are small or infrequent situations where people do not understand each other correctly.","zh":"occasional misunderstandings 指人們彼此理解不正確的小型或不頻繁情況。"},{"en":"Occasional misunderstandings may happen when classmates work quickly on a group project.","zh":"同學在小組項目中太急着做事時，可能偶爾出現誤會。"},{"en":"Clear explanation can prevent small misunderstandings from becoming serious conflict.","zh":"清楚解釋可以防止小誤會變成嚴重衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests problems happened sometimes, not constantly.","zh":"這個短語暗示問題有時發生，而不是不斷發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"local villagers","meaning":"本地村民","examples":[{"en":"The researchers explained the project to local villagers.","zh":"研究人員向本地村民解釋該項目。"},{"en":"Local villagers are people who live in the village or nearby rural community.","zh":"local villagers 指住在該村或附近鄉郊社區的人。"},{"en":"Local villagers may know paths, weather patterns, and traditions better than visitors.","zh":"本地村民可能比外來者更熟悉小路、天氣模式和傳統。"},{"en":"Working respectfully with villagers can make field research smoother.","zh":"尊重地與村民合作可以令野外研究更順利。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to residents of the local village area.","zh":"這個短語指本地村落地區的居民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"natural freshwater lake","meaning":"天然淡水湖","examples":[{"en":"Lake Bosumtwi is Ghana’s largest natural freshwater lake.","zh":"Bosumtwi 湖是加納最大的天然淡水湖。"},{"en":"A natural freshwater lake is a lake formed by nature and filled with non-salty water.","zh":"natural freshwater lake 指由自然形成並含非鹹水的湖泊。"},{"en":"A natural freshwater lake may provide drinking water, fish, and recreation for nearby communities.","zh":"天然淡水湖可以為附近社區提供飲用水、魚類和休閒活動。"},{"en":"Freshwater lakes are important because many people and animals depend on them.","zh":"淡水湖很重要，因為許多人和動物依賴它們。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts natural lakes with artificial reservoirs and saltwater bodies.","zh":"這個短語把天然湖與人工水庫和鹹水水體作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be sacred to","meaning":"對……來說是神聖的","examples":[{"en":"Lake Bosumtwi is sacred to the Ashanti people.","zh":"Bosumtwi 湖對阿散蒂族人來說是神聖的。"},{"en":"To be sacred to a group means to be deeply respected for religious or spiritual reasons.","zh":"be sacred to a group 指因宗教或精神原因而被某群體深深尊重。"},{"en":"A temple may be sacred to a community because ancestors worshipped there for generations.","zh":"寺廟可能因祖先世代在那裏祭祀，而對社區來說是神聖的。"},{"en":"Sacred places often have special rules about behaviour and access.","zh":"神聖地方常有關於行為和進入的特別規則。"},{"en":"The phrase describes spiritual importance, not simply popularity.","zh":"這個短語描述精神重要性，而不只是受歡迎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the Ashanti people","meaning":"阿散蒂族人","examples":[{"en":"The Ashanti people attach spiritual importance to the lake.","zh":"阿散蒂族人賦予該湖精神重要性。"},{"en":"The Ashanti people are an ethnic group in Ghana with their own history, culture, and traditions.","zh":"Ashanti people 指加納一個有自身歷史、文化和傳統的族群。"},{"en":"Researchers working near Ashanti communities should respect local customs and beliefs.","zh":"在阿散蒂社區附近工作的研究人員應尊重本地習俗和信仰。"},{"en":"Understanding local people’s beliefs helps outsiders avoid offence and build trust.","zh":"理解本地人的信仰幫助外來者避免冒犯並建立信任。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific cultural group.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定文化群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"bid farewell to","meaning":"向……道別","examples":[{"en":"The Ashanti believe that their souls come to the lake to bid farewell to their god.","zh":"阿散蒂族人相信他們的靈魂會來到湖邊向神道別。"},{"en":"To bid farewell to someone means to say goodbye to them, often formally or emotionally.","zh":"bid farewell to someone 指向某人道別，通常較正式或帶情感。"},{"en":"Students may bid farewell to a favourite teacher at a graduation ceremony.","zh":"學生可能在畢業典禮向喜愛的老師道別。"},{"en":"Farewell rituals help people mark endings and show respect.","zh":"道別儀式幫助人標記結束並表示尊重。"},{"en":"The phrase is more formal or poetic than simply “say goodbye”.","zh":"這個短語比 simply “say goodbye” 更正式或詩意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the primary source of","meaning":"……的主要來源","examples":[{"en":"The lake is the primary source of fish for nearby villages.","zh":"該湖是附近村落魚類的主要來源。"},{"en":"The primary source of something is the main place or thing it comes from.","zh":"primary source of something 指某物最主要來自的地方或事物。"},{"en":"Textbooks may be the primary source of information for students before an exam.","zh":"考試前，教科書可能是學生資訊的主要來源。"},{"en":"If a community depends on one primary source, damage to it can create serious problems.","zh":"如果社區依賴單一主要來源，它受損時可能造成嚴重問題。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the most important supply or origin.","zh":"這個短語指出最重要的供應或來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"surrounding villages","meaning":"周邊村落","examples":[{"en":"Twenty-six surrounding villages depend on the lake for fish.","zh":"二十六個周邊村落依靠該湖獲取魚類。"},{"en":"Surrounding villages are villages located around or near a central place.","zh":"surrounding villages 指位於某中心地點周圍或附近的村落。"},{"en":"A hospital may serve many surrounding villages that do not have their own clinics.","zh":"一間醫院可能服務許多沒有自己診所的周邊村落。"},{"en":"When a lake supports surrounding villages, changes to the lake affect many families.","zh":"當湖泊支持周邊村落，湖泊變化會影響許多家庭。"},{"en":"The phrase describes nearby communities around a place.","zh":"這個短語描述某地周圍的附近社區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"conventional canoes and boats","meaning":"傳統獨木舟及船隻","examples":[{"en":"Conventional canoes and boats are forbidden on the lake.","zh":"傳統獨木舟及船隻在該湖上被禁止。"},{"en":"Conventional canoes and boats are ordinary traditional or standard watercraft used for travelling on water.","zh":"conventional canoes and boats 指用於水上出行的普通傳統或標準船隻。"},{"en":"In some protected wetlands, conventional boats may be banned to protect wildlife.","zh":"在一些受保護濕地，普通船隻可能被禁止以保護野生動物。"},{"en":"If normal boats are forbidden, local people must use another approved method of travel.","zh":"如果正常船隻被禁止，本地人必須使用另一種獲准出行方式。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts ordinary boats with special or traditional alternatives.","zh":"這個短語把普通船隻與特殊或傳統替代方式作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be forbidden","meaning":"被禁止","examples":[{"en":"Ordinary boats are forbidden on the sacred lake.","zh":"普通船隻在這個神聖湖泊上被禁止。"},{"en":"To be forbidden means to be officially or strongly not allowed.","zh":"be forbidden 指被正式或強烈不允許。"},{"en":"Mobile phones may be forbidden during an exam.","zh":"考試期間手提電話可能被禁止。"},{"en":"If something is forbidden, breaking the rule may lead to punishment or offence.","zh":"如果某事被禁止，違反規則可能帶來懲罰或冒犯他人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes prohibition, not simple dislike.","zh":"這個短語描述禁止，而不是單純不喜歡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"float on traditional planks","meaning":"乘着傳統木板漂浮","examples":[{"en":"Fishermen float on traditional planks instead of using boats.","zh":"漁民乘着傳統木板漂浮，而不是使用船隻。"},{"en":"To float on traditional planks means to move on water while standing or sitting on long pieces of wood.","zh":"float on traditional planks 指站或坐在長木板上在水面移動。"},{"en":"Children may float on wooden boards in shallow water during a village game.","zh":"孩子可能在村落遊戲中乘着木板在淺水漂浮。"},{"en":"If boats are not allowed, planks can offer a culturally accepted way to fish.","zh":"如果船隻不被允許，木板可以提供文化上被接受的捕魚方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a local water-travel method.","zh":"這個短語描述本地水上移動方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"propel something with","meaning":"用……推動某物","examples":[{"en":"The fishermen propel the planks with small paddles.","zh":"漁民用小槳推動木板。"},{"en":"To propel something with a tool means to push it forward using that tool.","zh":"propel something with a tool 指使用某工具把物件向前推動。"},{"en":"A kayaker propels the kayak with a double-ended paddle.","zh":"獨木舟手用雙頭槳推動獨木舟。"},{"en":"Without something to propel the plank, it would drift with wind or water.","zh":"如果沒有東西推動木板，它就會隨風或水漂流。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the force used to move an object.","zh":"這個短語描述用來移動物件的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"small paddles","meaning":"小槳","examples":[{"en":"Local fishermen use small paddles to move across the lake.","zh":"本地漁民使用小槳橫越湖面。"},{"en":"Small paddles are short hand-held tools used to push water and move a boat or plank.","zh":"small paddles 指用手拿着、用來推水並移動船或木板的短工具。"},{"en":"A child may use small paddles to move a toy boat in a pond.","zh":"孩子可能用小槳在池塘推動玩具船。"},{"en":"Paddles work by pushing water backward so the person or object moves forward.","zh":"槳透過把水向後推，使人或物件向前移動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to simple manual tools for moving on water.","zh":"這個短語指用於水上移動的簡單手動工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Ghanaian counterparts","meaning":"加納的合作伙伴","examples":[{"en":"Scholz worked closely with his Ghanaian counterparts.","zh":"Scholz 與他的加納合作伙伴緊密合作。"},{"en":"Ghanaian counterparts are people in Ghana who have similar roles to the foreign team members.","zh":"Ghanaian counterparts 指在加納擔任與外國團隊成員相似角色的人。"},{"en":"A visiting teacher may work with local counterparts to understand a school system.","zh":"到訪老師可能與本地合作伙伴合作，以理解學校制度。"},{"en":"Local counterparts help outsiders follow rules, communicate, and respect culture.","zh":"本地合作伙伴幫助外來者遵守規則、溝通並尊重文化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes partners with matching professional roles.","zh":"這個短語描述具有相應專業角色的伙伴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"secure special permission","meaning":"取得特別許可","examples":[{"en":"The team had to secure special permission before using the boat.","zh":"團隊使用船隻前必須取得特別許可。"},{"en":"To secure special permission means to successfully obtain approval for something not normally allowed.","zh":"secure special permission 指成功取得對通常不被允許事情的批准。"},{"en":"A student may need to secure special permission to enter the laboratory after school.","zh":"學生放學後進入實驗室可能需要取得特別許可。"},{"en":"Permission protects rules, safety, and local concerns.","zh":"許可可以保護規則、安全和本地關注。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses official approval before action.","zh":"這個短語強調行動前的正式批准。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tribal chiefs","meaning":"部族酋長","examples":[{"en":"Tribal chiefs gave permission for the research vessel to enter the lake.","zh":"部族酋長准許研究船進入湖中。"},{"en":"Tribal chiefs are traditional leaders of a tribe or local community.","zh":"tribal chiefs 指部族或本地社區的傳統領袖。"},{"en":"Visitors may meet tribal chiefs before beginning work in a rural area.","zh":"外來者在鄉郊地區開始工作前，可能會會見部族酋長。"},{"en":"Chiefs can protect local customs by deciding what outsiders may do.","zh":"酋長可以透過決定外來者可做甚麼來保護本地習俗。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to traditional authority, not modern company managers.","zh":"這個短語指傳統權威，而不是現代公司經理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"put a boat on the lake","meaning":"讓船隻駛進湖中","examples":[{"en":"The researchers needed permission to put R/V Kilindi on the lake.","zh":"研究人員需要許可，才能讓 R/V Kilindi 駛進湖中。"},{"en":"To put a boat on the lake means to launch or place a boat onto the water for use.","zh":"put a boat on the lake 指把船放到湖面上使用或讓船下水。"},{"en":"A family may ask permission before putting a boat on a private lake.","zh":"家庭可能在私人湖泊放船前先請求許可。"},{"en":"When a lake is sacred or protected, putting a boat on it may require approval.","zh":"當湖泊神聖或受保護，讓船進入其中可能需要批准。"},{"en":"The phrase describes placing a boat into the water, not storing it nearby.","zh":"這個短語描述把船放入水中，而不是存放在附近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"begin gathering data","meaning":"開始收集數據","examples":[{"en":"The researchers began gathering data after receiving permission.","zh":"研究人員獲得許可後開始收集數據。"},{"en":"To begin gathering data means to start collecting information or measurements for research.","zh":"begin gathering data 指開始為研究收集資訊或量度結果。"},{"en":"Students began gathering data for a survey after the teacher approved their questions.","zh":"老師批准問題後，學生開始為調查收集數據。"},{"en":"Data gathering can start only when tools, access, and permission are ready.","zh":"只有當工具、進入權和許可都準備好，數據收集才可以開始。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the start of evidence collection.","zh":"這個短語標示證據收集的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rumours flew around","meaning":"謠言四起","examples":[{"en":"Rumours flew around the lake when the project began.","zh":"項目開始時，湖邊謠言四起。"},{"en":"Rumours flew around means many unofficial stories spread quickly among people.","zh":"rumours flew around 指許多非正式說法在人群中迅速傳開。"},{"en":"Rumours flew around the school when students heard a new principal was coming.","zh":"當學生聽說新校長快來時，學校裏謠言四起。"},{"en":"Rumours spread faster when people do not have clear information.","zh":"當人們沒有清楚資訊，謠言會傳得更快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rapid informal talk, not literal flying.","zh":"這個短語描述快速流傳的非正式談論，而不是字面飛行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as to why","meaning":"關於為何……","examples":[{"en":"Local people speculated as to why the researchers were there.","zh":"本地人猜測研究人員為何在那裏。"},{"en":"As to why means about the reason why something happened or was true.","zh":"as to why 指關於某事為何發生或為何屬實的原因。"},{"en":"Parents may ask as to why a school trip was cancelled so suddenly.","zh":"家長可能詢問學校旅行為何如此突然取消。"},{"en":"People speculate about reasons when they lack clear explanations.","zh":"當人們缺乏清楚解釋，他們就會猜測原因。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and introduces a question about cause.","zh":"這個短語較正式，用來引入關於原因的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"dredge the lake for gold","meaning":"疏浚湖底尋找黃金","examples":[{"en":"Some villagers thought the researchers were dredging the lake for gold.","zh":"一些村民以為研究人員正在疏浚湖底尋找黃金。"},{"en":"To dredge the lake for gold means to dig or suck up material from the lake bottom to search for gold.","zh":"dredge the lake for gold 指挖掘或抽取湖底物質以尋找黃金。"},{"en":"Workers may dredge a river to remove mud and make boats pass more easily.","zh":"工人可能疏浚河流，清除淤泥並讓船更易通過。"},{"en":"Dredging can disturb sediments, water quality, and local fishing.","zh":"疏浚可以擾亂沉積物、水質和本地捕魚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a heavy physical search under water, not ordinary scientific measurement.","zh":"這個短語描述水下重型搜尋，而不是普通科學量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"drain the lake","meaning":"抽乾湖水","examples":[{"en":"Others believed the team intended to drain the lake.","zh":"另一些人相信團隊打算抽乾湖水。"},{"en":"To drain the lake means to remove the water from it.","zh":"drain the lake 指把湖中的水移走。"},{"en":"Workers may drain a swimming pool before repairing cracked tiles.","zh":"工人修補破裂瓷磚前，可能先抽乾泳池水。"},{"en":"Draining a lake would damage fish, plants, and communities that depend on it.","zh":"抽乾湖水會破壞依賴它的魚類、植物和社區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes emptying water from a lake or similar body.","zh":"這個短語描述把湖泊或類似水體中的水排空。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"once someone understood","meaning":"當某人明白之後","examples":[{"en":"Once local people understood the project, they became helpful.","zh":"當本地人明白該項目之後，他們變得樂意幫忙。"},{"en":"Once someone understood means after that person clearly understood the situation.","zh":"once someone understood 指某人清楚理解情況之後。"},{"en":"Once students understood the marking criteria, their essays became more focused.","zh":"當學生明白評分準則後，他們的作文變得更集中。"},{"en":"Understanding often reduces fear, rumours, and resistance.","zh":"理解通常能減少恐懼、謠言和抗拒。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the point when confusion changes into cooperation or action.","zh":"這個短語標示困惑轉變為合作或行動的一刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be very helpful","meaning":"非常樂意幫忙","examples":[{"en":"The local villagers were very helpful after the project was explained.","zh":"項目被解釋後，本地村民非常樂意幫忙。"},{"en":"To be very helpful means to give useful support, information, or assistance.","zh":"be very helpful 指提供有用支援、資訊或協助。"},{"en":"A librarian can be very helpful when students cannot find suitable sources.","zh":"當學生找不到合適資料來源，圖書館員可以非常樂意幫忙。"},{"en":"Helpful local people can make fieldwork safer and easier.","zh":"樂意幫忙的本地人可以令野外工作更安全和容易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active support, not merely being friendly.","zh":"這個短語描述積極支援，而不只是友善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料一致","examples":[{"en":"A true statement agrees with the information given in the passage.","zh":"正確陳述與文章所給資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the text says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文本所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the passage says the lake has no outlet, a statement saying this is true agrees with the text.","zh":"如果文章說該湖沒有出水口，陳述這一點為真就與文本一致。"},{"en":"Students should check the exact meaning before choosing TRUE.","zh":"學生選 TRUE 前應檢查確切意思。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in reading tasks to test textual accuracy.","zh":"這個短語用於閱讀題，以測試文本準確度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文本所說相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says the boat was reassembled in Ghana, saying it was built in Canada contradicts it.","zh":"如果文章說船在加納重新組裝，說它在加拿大建造就是相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be based on clear evidence from the passage.","zh":"判斷矛盾必須基於文章中的清楚證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct conflict with given information.","zh":"這個短語描述與所給資料直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"Write “NOT GIVEN” when there is no information on the statement.","zh":"當文章沒有該陳述方面的資料時，寫 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not tell us enough to decide.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文章沒有告訴我們足夠資料去判斷。"},{"en":"If a text describes a lake’s size but not its fish prices, there is no information on fish prices.","zh":"如果文本描述湖的大小但沒有提及魚價，就沒有魚價方面的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge to answer a NOT GIVEN question.","zh":"學生不應用外部知識回答 NOT GIVEN 題目。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the answer cannot be proved from the passage.","zh":"這個短語表示答案不能從文章中證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"by investigating the lake","meaning":"透過研究該湖","examples":[{"en":"Scientists may learn about future climate change by investigating the lake.","zh":"科學家可能透過研究該湖了解未來氣候變化。"},{"en":"By investigating the lake means through careful scientific study of the lake.","zh":"by investigating the lake 指透過對該湖進行仔細科學研究。"},{"en":"Students can learn about water quality by investigating a pond near school.","zh":"學生可以透過研究學校附近池塘了解水質。"},{"en":"Investigation can reveal evidence that simple observation would miss.","zh":"研究可以揭示簡單觀察會看漏的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the method used to gain knowledge.","zh":"這個短語顯示獲取知識的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be able to predict","meaning":"能夠預測","examples":[{"en":"The researchers may be able to predict future climatic patterns.","zh":"研究人員可能能夠預測未來氣候模式。"},{"en":"To be able to predict something means to have enough information to estimate what may happen.","zh":"be able to predict something 指有足夠資訊估計可能發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Teachers may be able to predict exam difficulties after studying students’ mock results.","zh":"老師研究學生模擬考結果後，可能能夠預測考試困難。"},{"en":"More accurate records make prediction more reliable.","zh":"更準確紀錄令預測更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the ability to forecast, not guaranteed certainty.","zh":"這個短語描述預測能力，而不是保證確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"result from a meteorite impact","meaning":"由隕石撞擊形成","examples":[{"en":"The crater resulted from a meteorite impact.","zh":"這個隕石坑由隕石撞擊形成。"},{"en":"To result from a meteorite impact means to be caused by a meteorite hitting the Earth.","zh":"result from a meteorite impact 指由隕石撞擊地球造成。"},{"en":"A dent in a car may result from a falling branch striking the roof.","zh":"汽車凹痕可能由樹枝掉下撞擊車頂造成。"},{"en":"If a crater results from impact, its rocks may show signs of shock and heat.","zh":"如果坑洞由撞擊形成，其岩石可能顯示受震和受熱跡象。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the cause of a landform.","zh":"這個短語解釋地貌的成因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the largest and best-preserved","meaning":"最大且保存得最好的","examples":[{"en":"The question compares the crater with the largest and best-preserved craters.","zh":"題目把該隕石坑與最大且保存得最好的隕石坑比較。"},{"en":"The largest and best-preserved means the biggest and kept in the best condition.","zh":"largest and best-preserved 指最大並且保存狀態最佳。"},{"en":"A museum may display the largest and best-preserved fossil in its collection.","zh":"博物館可能展示其收藏中最大且保存得最好的化石。"},{"en":"Large, well-preserved examples are valuable because they show many details clearly.","zh":"大型且保存良好的例子很有價值，因為它們清楚顯示許多細節。"},{"en":"The phrase combines size and condition.","zh":"這個短語結合大小和保存狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"leave only by","meaning":"只透過……流失","examples":[{"en":"The lake water leaves only by evaporation or seepage.","zh":"湖水只透過蒸發或滲漏流失。"},{"en":"To leave only by certain ways means there are no other exits or methods for leaving.","zh":"leave only by certain ways 指沒有其他出口或離開方法。"},{"en":"In a closed bottle, water can leave only by being poured out or evaporating slowly.","zh":"在密封瓶中，水只可以透過倒出或慢慢蒸發而離開。"},{"en":"If lake water leaves only by slow processes, materials may stay trapped longer.","zh":"如果湖水只透過緩慢過程流失，物質可能被困更久。"},{"en":"The phrase limits the possible ways something can exit.","zh":"這個短語限制某物可以離開的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"historical climate changes","meaning":"歷史氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"Sediment can preserve evidence of historical climate changes.","zh":"沉積物可以保存歷史氣候變化的證據。"},{"en":"Historical climate changes are climate changes that happened in the past.","zh":"historical climate changes 指過去曾發生的氣候變化。"},{"en":"Ice cores can show historical climate changes through trapped air and dust.","zh":"冰芯可以透過困住的空氣和塵埃顯示歷史氣候變化。"},{"en":"Past climate changes help scientists understand present and future risks.","zh":"過去氣候變化幫助科學家理解現在和未來風險。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to earlier climate shifts, not current daily weather.","zh":"這個短語指較早的氣候轉變，而不是現時每日天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be detected by","meaning":"可透過……探測","examples":[{"en":"Past climatic changes can be detected by analysing sediment.","zh":"過去氣候變化可透過分析沉積物探測到。"},{"en":"To be detected by a method means to be found or identified through that method.","zh":"be detected by a method 指透過某方法被發現或辨認。"},{"en":"A hidden leak can be detected by checking a water meter.","zh":"隱藏漏水可透過檢查水錶探測到。"},{"en":"Careful analysis can reveal signs that are not visible at first.","zh":"仔細分析可以揭示起初不可見的跡象。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies how evidence is found.","zh":"這個短語指出證據如何被找出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"analysis of the sediment","meaning":"對沉積物的分析","examples":[{"en":"Analysis of the sediment can reveal past rainfall patterns.","zh":"對沉積物的分析可以揭示過去降雨模式。"},{"en":"Analysis of the sediment means careful scientific examination of material from the lake bottom.","zh":"analysis of the sediment 指對湖底物質進行仔細科學檢查。"},{"en":"A laboratory analysis of soil can show whether a garden lacks nutrients.","zh":"實驗室對泥土的分析可以顯示花園是否缺乏養分。"},{"en":"Sediment analysis can uncover changes in water, climate, or erosion.","zh":"沉積物分析可以揭示水、氣候或侵蝕變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes studying sediment to extract information.","zh":"這個短語描述研究沉積物以取得資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the greatest obstacle faced by","meaning":"研究人員面對的最大障礙","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the greatest obstacle faced by the researchers.","zh":"題目問研究人員面對的最大障礙。"},{"en":"The greatest obstacle faced by someone is the biggest difficulty they had to deal with.","zh":"greatest obstacle faced by someone 指某人必須處理的最大困難。"},{"en":"The greatest obstacle faced by many students is not vocabulary but lack of practice time.","zh":"許多學生面對的最大障礙不是詞彙，而是缺乏練習時間。"},{"en":"Identifying the greatest obstacle helps people focus on the most urgent problem.","zh":"找出最大障礙幫助人集中處理最迫切問題。"},{"en":"The phrase compares difficulties and points to the most serious one.","zh":"這個短語比較困難並指出最嚴重的一項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"local opposition","meaning":"本地反對","examples":[{"en":"The team did not face serious local opposition after explaining the project.","zh":"團隊解釋項目後，沒有面對嚴重本地反對。"},{"en":"Local opposition is resistance or disagreement from people living in the area.","zh":"local opposition 指住在該地區的人反對或抗拒。"},{"en":"A new road may face local opposition if residents fear noise and pollution.","zh":"如果居民擔心噪音和污染，新道路可能面對本地反對。"},{"en":"Clear explanation can reduce opposition by answering people’s concerns.","zh":"清楚解釋可以透過回應人們關注來減少反對。"},{"en":"The phrase describes community resistance, not technical difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述社區阻力，而不是技術困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"indigenous beliefs","meaning":"原住民信仰","examples":[{"en":"The lake is protected by the indigenous beliefs of the Ashanti people.","zh":"該湖受到阿散蒂族人原住民信仰保護。"},{"en":"Indigenous beliefs are traditional beliefs held by the original or long-established people of a place.","zh":"indigenous beliefs 指某地原住或長期居住群體所持有的傳統信念。"},{"en":"Indigenous beliefs may guide how a community treats forests, rivers, or sacred sites.","zh":"原住民信仰可能指引社區如何對待森林、河流或神聖地點。"},{"en":"Respecting these beliefs helps outsiders work without damaging trust.","zh":"尊重這些信仰幫助外來者工作時不破壞信任。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to local traditional belief systems.","zh":"這個短語指本地傳統信仰系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete the flow chart","meaning":"完成流程圖","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the flow chart with words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成流程圖。"},{"en":"To complete the flow chart means to fill missing steps or labels in a process diagram.","zh":"complete the flow chart 指填補流程圖中缺少的步驟或標籤。"},{"en":"Students may complete a flow chart showing how rainwater becomes drinking water.","zh":"學生可能完成一個顯示雨水如何變成飲用水的流程圖。"},{"en":"Flow charts test whether readers understand order and cause in a process.","zh":"流程圖測試讀者是否理解過程中的次序和因果。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the steps used to","meaning":"用作……的步驟","examples":[{"en":"The flow chart shows the steps used to collect scientific data.","zh":"流程圖顯示用作收集科學數據的步驟。"},{"en":"The steps used to do something are the actions taken in order to complete it.","zh":"steps used to do something 指為完成某事而按次序採取的行動。"},{"en":"A recipe shows the steps used to bake a cake.","zh":"食譜顯示用作焗蛋糕的步驟。"},{"en":"Clear steps help people repeat a method correctly.","zh":"清楚步驟幫助人正確重複方法。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on procedure and sequence.","zh":"這個短語重點是程序和次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"collect data from","meaning":"從……收集數據","examples":[{"en":"The researchers used sound waves to collect data from the lake.","zh":"研究人員使用聲波從該湖收集數據。"},{"en":"To collect data from a place means to gather information or measurements there.","zh":"collect data from a place 指在某地收集資訊或量度結果。"},{"en":"Students may collect data from a local park by counting birds each morning.","zh":"學生可能每天早上數鳥，從本地公園收集數據。"},{"en":"Data collected from a site can reveal patterns specific to that place.","zh":"從某地收集的數據可以揭示該地特有模式。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of the information.","zh":"這個短語指出資訊來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete the following summary","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the following summary using words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the following summary means to fill blanks in the short text below the instruction.","zh":"complete the following summary 指填補指示下方短文中的空格。"},{"en":"Students should check grammar and word limits when completing a summary.","zh":"學生完成摘要時應檢查文法和字數限制。"},{"en":"This task tests whether readers understand the main ideas and exact wording.","zh":"這項任務測試讀者是否理解主要意思和準確用字。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個詞","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than three words.","zh":"每個答案應包含不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must use one, two, or three words only.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案只能使用一個、兩個或三個詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “shipping container”, it fits because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “shipping container”，它符合要求，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing four words may lose marks even when the meaning is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫四個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit for exam answers.","zh":"這個短語為考試答案給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"before crossing the lake","meaning":"在橫越湖面之前","examples":[{"en":"The boat was fully tested before crossing the lake.","zh":"這艘船在橫越湖面之前已經完全測試。"},{"en":"Before crossing the lake means before travelling across the lake by boat.","zh":"before crossing the lake 指在乘船橫越湖面之前。"},{"en":"A ferry should be checked before crossing a wide lake with passengers.","zh":"渡輪載客橫越寬闊湖面之前應先檢查。"},{"en":"Testing first reduces the chance of equipment failure during the crossing.","zh":"先測試可以減少橫越期間設備故障的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a safety step before movement over water.","zh":"這個短語設定水上移動前的安全步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be stored in","meaning":"被存放在……","examples":[{"en":"The dismantled boat was stored in a shipping container.","zh":"拆卸後的船被存放在貨運貨櫃中。"},{"en":"To be stored in something means to be kept inside it until needed.","zh":"be stored in something 指被保存在某物內，直到需要使用。"},{"en":"School sports equipment may be stored in a locked cupboard.","zh":"學校運動器材可能被存放在上鎖櫃中。"},{"en":"Proper storage protects items from damage, loss, or weather.","zh":"妥善存放可以保護物件免受損壞、遺失或天氣影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where something is kept.","zh":"這個短語描述某物被保存在哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"separate equipment","meaning":"獨立設備","examples":[{"en":"Separate equipment collected the returning sound waves.","zh":"獨立設備收集返回的聲波。"},{"en":"Separate equipment means different tools or devices used apart from the main system.","zh":"separate equipment 指與主要系統分開使用的不同工具或裝置。"},{"en":"A teacher may use separate equipment for sound recording during a school play.","zh":"老師可能在學校話劇中使用獨立設備錄音。"},{"en":"Using separate tools can make each part of a process more accurate.","zh":"使用獨立工具可以令過程中每一部分更準確。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the task was done by another device.","zh":"這個短語強調該任務由另一裝置完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"returning waves","meaning":"返回的波浪；反射波","examples":[{"en":"Hydrophones detected the returning waves beneath the boat.","zh":"水聽器探測到船下方返回的波浪。"},{"en":"Returning waves are waves that come back after hitting a surface or layer.","zh":"returning waves 指撞到表面或層次後返回的波。"},{"en":"An echo is made by returning sound waves from a wall.","zh":"回聲由從牆壁返回的聲波形成。"},{"en":"By studying returning waves, scientists can infer what lies below.","zh":"透過研究返回的波，科學家可以推斷下方有甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes waves after reflection.","zh":"這個短語描述反射後的波。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"avoid physical barriers","meaning":"避開實體障礙物","examples":[{"en":"The boat had to avoid physical barriers on the lake.","zh":"這艘船必須避開湖上的實體障礙物。"},{"en":"To avoid physical barriers means to move around solid obstacles that could block or damage movement.","zh":"avoid physical barriers 指繞過可能阻礙或損壞移動的實體障礙物。"},{"en":"A wheelchair user may need to avoid physical barriers such as steps and narrow doors.","zh":"輪椅使用者可能需要避開樓梯和狹窄門口等實體障礙物。"},{"en":"Avoiding obstacles prevents accidents, delays, and equipment damage.","zh":"避開障礙物可以防止意外、延誤和設備損壞。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on real objects that get in the way.","zh":"這個短語重點是真正擋路的物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"float on the lake’s surface","meaning":"漂浮在湖面上","examples":[{"en":"Fishing nets and other objects could float on the lake’s surface.","zh":"魚網和其他物件可能漂浮在湖面上。"},{"en":"To float on the lake’s surface means to rest or move on top of the water without sinking.","zh":"float on the lake’s surface 指停留或移動於湖水表面而不下沉。"},{"en":"Leaves often float on a pond’s surface after windy weather.","zh":"大風後，樹葉常漂浮在池塘水面上。"},{"en":"Floating objects can create hazards for boats and scientific equipment.","zh":"漂浮物可以為船隻和科學設備造成危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something staying on the top layer of lake water.","zh":"這個短語描述某物停留在湖水最上層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 130 - Detection of a meteorite Lake.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 131":[{"front":"Bondi Beach","meaning":"邦迪海灘","examples":[{"en":"Bondi Beach is one of Australia’s most famous coastal destinations.","zh":"邦迪海灘是澳洲最著名的海岸目的地之一。"},{"en":"Bondi Beach is a well-known beach area in Sydney, famous for swimming, surfing, tourism, and seaside culture.","zh":"Bondi Beach 指悉尼一個著名海灘地區，以游泳、衝浪、旅遊和海濱文化聞名。"},{"en":"A visitor to Sydney may spend an afternoon at Bondi Beach to walk, swim, or eat near the sea.","zh":"到悉尼的遊客可能花一個下午到邦迪海灘散步、游泳或在海邊用餐。"},{"en":"Because Bondi Beach is so famous, it attracts both local residents and overseas tourists.","zh":"因為邦迪海灘非常著名，它吸引本地居民和海外遊客。"},{"en":"This name is useful when discussing Australian tourism, beach culture, or Sydney landmarks.","zh":"討論澳洲旅遊、海灘文化或悉尼地標時，這個名稱很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Australia’s most famous beach","meaning":"澳洲最著名的海灘","examples":[{"en":"Bondi Beach is widely described as Australia’s most famous beach.","zh":"邦迪海灘被廣泛描述為澳洲最著名的海灘。"},{"en":"Australia’s most famous beach means the beach most strongly recognised by people in Australia and overseas.","zh":"Australia’s most famous beach 指在澳洲和海外最廣為人知的海灘。"},{"en":"A travel guide may introduce Bondi as Australia’s most famous beach before naming smaller beaches nearby.","zh":"旅遊指南可能先介紹邦迪為澳洲最著名的海灘，再介紹附近較小的海灘。"},{"en":"Being called the most famous beach can increase tourism, business, and media attention.","zh":"被稱為最著名的海灘，可以增加旅遊、商業和媒體關注。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a place with national and international recognition.","zh":"描述具有全國和國際知名度的地方時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be located in","meaning":"位於……","examples":[{"en":"Bondi Beach is located in the suburb of Bondi.","zh":"邦迪海灘位於 Bondi 這個市郊。"},{"en":"Be located in means be situated or found in a particular place.","zh":"be located in 指位於或坐落於某個特定地方。"},{"en":"A school may be located in a quiet residential district near a park.","zh":"一所學校可能位於公園附近一個安靜住宅區。"},{"en":"Saying where something is located helps readers understand its geography and access.","zh":"說明某物位於哪裏，有助讀者理解其地理位置和交通可達性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving the position of a place.","zh":"說明地方位置時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the suburb of","meaning":"……的市郊","examples":[{"en":"The beach lies in the suburb of Bondi near central Sydney.","zh":"這個海灘位於悉尼市中心附近的 Bondi 市郊。"},{"en":"The suburb of something means a residential district or local area outside or near a city centre.","zh":"suburb of something 指城市中心外圍或附近的住宅區或本地區域。"},{"en":"A family may live in the suburb of Sha Tin but travel to the city centre for work.","zh":"一個家庭可能住在沙田市郊，但到市中心上班。"},{"en":"Suburbs often grow when people want homes near, but not inside, busy urban centres.","zh":"當人們想住近城市但不在繁忙市中心內，市郊常會發展起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing local districts around a city.","zh":"描述城市周邊本地區域時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Local Government Area","meaning":"地方政府區","examples":[{"en":"Bondi is situated within the Local Government Area of Waverley.","zh":"Bondi 位於 Waverley 地方政府區內。"},{"en":"A Local Government Area is an administrative district managed by a local council or authority.","zh":"Local Government Area 指由地方議會或地方當局管理的行政區。"},{"en":"A local government area may handle rubbish collection, parks, roads, and community services.","zh":"地方政府區可能負責垃圾收集、公園、道路和社區服務。"},{"en":"Knowing the local government area helps residents understand which council provides services.","zh":"知道地方政府區有助居民了解哪個議會提供服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing civic administration and local planning.","zh":"討論城市行政和地方規劃時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"seven kilometres from","meaning":"距離……七公里","examples":[{"en":"The beach is approximately seven kilometres from central Sydney.","zh":"這個海灘距離悉尼市中心約七公里。"},{"en":"Seven kilometres from something means located at a distance of about seven kilometres away.","zh":"seven kilometres from something 指位於距離某地約七公里的位置。"},{"en":"A student who lives seven kilometres from school may take a bus instead of walking.","zh":"住在距離學校七公里的學生可能乘巴士，而不是步行。"},{"en":"A short distance from the city centre can make a beach easy for visitors to reach.","zh":"距離市中心不遠，可以令海灘較容易讓遊客到達。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving approximate distance.","zh":"提供大約距離時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the centre of Sydney","meaning":"悉尼市中心","examples":[{"en":"Bondi Beach is easily accessible from the centre of Sydney.","zh":"從悉尼市中心可以容易到達邦迪海灘。"},{"en":"The centre of Sydney means the main central area of the city where business, transport, and attractions are concentrated.","zh":"centre of Sydney 指悉尼主要中心區，商業、交通和景點集中於此。"},{"en":"Tourists often stay near the centre of Sydney because it is convenient for transport.","zh":"遊客常住在悉尼市中心附近，因為交通方便。"},{"en":"If a beach is close to the city centre, more people can visit it after work or school.","zh":"如果海灘靠近市中心，更多人可以在下班或放學後到訪。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing distance from a major urban core.","zh":"描述與主要城市核心的距離時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Aboriginal word","meaning":"澳洲原住民詞語","examples":[{"en":"“Bondi” is believed to come from an Aboriginal word.","zh":"“Bondi” 被認為來自一個澳洲原住民詞語。"},{"en":"An Aboriginal word is a word from the languages of Australia’s Indigenous peoples.","zh":"Aboriginal word 指來自澳洲原住民族語言的詞語。"},{"en":"Many Australian place names come from Aboriginal words that describe land, water, animals, or local features.","zh":"許多澳洲地名來自描述土地、水、動物或本地特徵的原住民詞語。"},{"en":"Keeping Aboriginal words in place names can preserve traces of older cultural history.","zh":"在地名中保留原住民詞語，可以保存較古老文化歷史的痕跡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing Australian language and heritage.","zh":"討論澳洲語言和文化遺產時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mean water breaking over rocks","meaning":"意指海水拍打岩石","examples":[{"en":"The name may mean water breaking over rocks.","zh":"這個名稱可能意指海水拍打岩石。"},{"en":"Mean water breaking over rocks means refer to waves crashing or breaking against rocks.","zh":"mean water breaking over rocks 指指向海浪衝擊或拍打岩石的情景。"},{"en":"A coastal place name may describe the sound or movement of waves against the shore.","zh":"海岸地名可能描述海浪拍岸的聲音或動作。"},{"en":"If a name comes from a natural feature, it helps people remember the landscape.","zh":"如果名稱來自自然特徵，它有助人們記住當地景觀。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the possible meaning of a place name.","zh":"解釋地名可能含義時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the sound of breaking waves","meaning":"海浪拍岸的聲音","examples":[{"en":"The word may refer to the sound of breaking waves.","zh":"這個詞可能指海浪拍岸的聲音。"},{"en":"The sound of breaking waves is the noise made when waves crash onto rocks, sand, or the shore.","zh":"sound of breaking waves 指海浪衝向岩石、沙灘或岸邊時發出的聲音。"},{"en":"A person staying near the coast may fall asleep to the sound of breaking waves.","zh":"住在海邊的人可能伴着海浪拍岸的聲音入睡。"},{"en":"A word based on wave sounds connects language with the physical environment.","zh":"以浪聲為基礎的詞語，把語言和自然環境連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing coastal atmosphere.","zh":"描述海岸氣氛時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"record that","meaning":"記載；記錄","examples":[{"en":"The Australian Museum records that the name may have another meaning.","zh":"澳洲博物館記載，這個名稱可能有另一個意思。"},{"en":"Record that means officially state, note, or preserve information in writing.","zh":"record that 指正式陳述、記下或以文字保存資料。"},{"en":"A school report may record that a student has improved in reading.","zh":"學校報告可能記錄某學生在閱讀方面有進步。"},{"en":"When an institution records information, later readers can check and compare it.","zh":"當機構記錄資料，後來的讀者就可以查閱和比較。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when referring to documented information.","zh":"引用有文獻記錄的資料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a flight of nullas","meaning":"投擲多支木棒","examples":[{"en":"One interpretation links the name to a flight of nullas.","zh":"其中一種解釋把這個名稱與投擲多支木棒連繫起來。"},{"en":"A flight of nullas refers to several nulla-nullas, or wooden clubs, being thrown through the air.","zh":"flight of nullas 指幾支 nulla-nulla 木棒被投擲到空中的情景。"},{"en":"A museum guide may explain that an old place name describes a traditional event or object.","zh":"博物館導賞員可能解釋舊地名描述一個傳統事件或物件。"},{"en":"If a place name refers to thrown wooden clubs, it preserves a memory of local Indigenous culture.","zh":"如果地名指向投擲木棒，它就保存了本地原住民文化記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing historical interpretations of Aboriginal names.","zh":"討論原住民名稱的歷史解讀時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"take place","meaning":"發生","examples":[{"en":"The museum records that such an event took place in the area.","zh":"博物館記載，這類事件曾在該區發生。"},{"en":"Take place means happen or occur.","zh":"take place 指發生或進行。"},{"en":"A school concert may take place in the hall on Friday evening.","zh":"學校音樂會可能在星期五晚上於禮堂舉行。"},{"en":"Knowing where an event took place helps connect the story to a real location.","zh":"知道事件在哪裏發生，有助把故事連接到真實地點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing when or where something happened.","zh":"描述某事何時或在哪裏發生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Aboriginal rock carvings","meaning":"澳洲原住民岩刻","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal rock carvings can still be found near Bondi Beach.","zh":"邦迪海灘附近仍可找到澳洲原住民岩刻。"},{"en":"Aboriginal rock carvings are images or marks cut into rock by Australia’s Indigenous peoples.","zh":"Aboriginal rock carvings 指由澳洲原住民族人在岩石上刻出的圖像或痕跡。"},{"en":"Visitors may see Aboriginal rock carvings during a guided coastal walk.","zh":"遊客可能在有導賞的海岸步道中看見澳洲原住民岩刻。"},{"en":"Such carvings help preserve cultural memory and show long human connection to the land.","zh":"這些岩刻有助保存文化記憶，並顯示人類與土地的長久連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing Indigenous heritage sites.","zh":"討論原住民文化遺產地點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the northern end of","meaning":"……的北端","examples":[{"en":"Some carvings are located at the northern end of the beach.","zh":"有些岩刻位於海灘的北端。"},{"en":"The northern end of something is the part nearest the north side.","zh":"northern end of something 指某地最接近北面的一端。"},{"en":"A café at the northern end of a park may be quieter than the main entrance.","zh":"公園北端的咖啡店可能比正門附近較安靜。"},{"en":"Giving the exact end of a place helps visitors find a site more easily.","zh":"說明某地的具體一端，有助遊客更容易找到景點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing location within a larger area.","zh":"描述較大區域內的位置時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"coastal walk","meaning":"海岸步道","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can see cultural sites along the coastal walk.","zh":"遊客可以沿海岸步道看到文化遺址。"},{"en":"A coastal walk is a walking route that follows the coastline.","zh":"coastal walk 指沿着海岸線而行的步行路線。"},{"en":"Families may take a coastal walk to enjoy sea views without swimming.","zh":"家庭可能沿海岸步道散步，在不游泳的情況下欣賞海景。"},{"en":"Coastal walks can connect beaches, cliffs, parks, and cultural landmarks.","zh":"海岸步道可以連接海灘、懸崖、公園和文化地標。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing seaside recreation and tourism.","zh":"討論海濱康樂和旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"indigenous people","meaning":"原住民","examples":[{"en":"The indigenous people of the area lived there before European settlement.","zh":"該區原住民在歐洲人殖民定居前已在當地生活。"},{"en":"Indigenous people are the original peoples of a place, with long-standing cultural ties to the land.","zh":"indigenous people 指某地的原本民族，與土地有長久文化連繫。"},{"en":"Schools may teach students about indigenous people through language, history, art, and land stories.","zh":"學校可能透過語言、歷史、藝術和土地故事教學生認識原住民。"},{"en":"Recognising indigenous people helps correct the idea that history began only with colonisation.","zh":"承認原住民有助糾正歷史只由殖民開始的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing original communities and cultural heritage.","zh":"討論原初社群和文化遺產時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at the time of","meaning":"在……的時期","examples":[{"en":"The Eora lived in the region at the time of European settlement.","zh":"在歐洲人殖民定居的時期，Eora 人居住在該地區。"},{"en":"At the time of means during the period when something happened.","zh":"at the time of 指在某事發生的時期。"},{"en":"At the time of the school’s opening, the area had very few public facilities.","zh":"在學校開辦的時期，該區公共設施很少。"},{"en":"This phrase helps place people or events in a specific historical moment.","zh":"這個短語幫助把人物或事件放在特定歷史時刻中。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining what was happening during a major event.","zh":"解釋重大事件期間發生甚麼時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"European settlement","meaning":"歐洲人殖民定居","examples":[{"en":"European settlement significantly changed the Sydney region.","zh":"歐洲人殖民定居大大改變了悉尼地區。"},{"en":"European settlement means the arrival and establishment of European colonists in a place.","zh":"European settlement 指歐洲殖民者到達並在某地建立定居點。"},{"en":"European settlement often changed land use, local populations, languages, and power structures.","zh":"歐洲人殖民定居常改變土地使用、本地人口、語言和權力結構。"},{"en":"In Australia, European settlement deeply affected Indigenous communities and their lands.","zh":"在澳洲，歐洲人殖民定居深深影響原住民社群和土地。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing colonisation and historical change.","zh":"討論殖民和歷史變遷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"generally be referred to as","meaning":"一般被稱為","examples":[{"en":"The indigenous population has generally been referred to as the Eora.","zh":"該原住民人口一般被稱為 Eora。"},{"en":"Generally be referred to as means usually be called by a certain name.","zh":"generally be referred to as 指通常被稱作某個名稱。"},{"en":"A teacher may generally be referred to as “Miss Chan” by students.","zh":"學生一般可能稱呼老師為「陳老師」。"},{"en":"A name commonly used in records may not always capture every local group accurately.","zh":"紀錄中常用的名稱未必總能準確涵蓋每個本地群體。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining a commonly used label.","zh":"解釋常用標籤時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the Sydney people","meaning":"悉尼地區的原住民","examples":[{"en":"The Eora were sometimes described as the Sydney people.","zh":"Eora 有時被描述為悉尼地區的原住民。"},{"en":"The Sydney people means the Indigenous people associated with the Sydney region.","zh":"Sydney people 指與悉尼地區相關的原住民。"},{"en":"A historian may use the term “Sydney people” to help readers connect a group with a place.","zh":"歷史學家可能使用 “Sydney people” 一詞，幫助讀者把某群體與地方連接起來。"},{"en":"Place-based names can make history easier to understand, but they may simplify complex identities.","zh":"以地方為基礎的名稱可以令歷史較容易理解，但也可能簡化複雜身份。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining regional identity.","zh":"解釋地區身份時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a sub-group of","meaning":"……的一個分支群體","examples":[{"en":"One theory describes the Eora as a sub-group of the Darug language group.","zh":"一個理論把 Eora 描述為 Darug 語言群體的一個分支群體。"},{"en":"A sub-group of something is a smaller group within a larger group.","zh":"sub-group of something 指較大群體中的一個較小群體。"},{"en":"In a school club, beginners may form a sub-group of the whole debating team.","zh":"在學校學會中，初學者可能構成整個辯論隊的一個分支小組。"},{"en":"Calling a community a sub-group suggests it belongs to a wider cultural or language system.","zh":"把一個社群稱為分支群體，暗示它屬於更大的文化或語言系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing classification within a larger category.","zh":"描述較大類別中的分類時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"language group","meaning":"語言群體","examples":[{"en":"The Darug were an important language group in the region.","zh":"Darug 是該地區一個重要語言群體。"},{"en":"A language group is a community or set of people connected by a shared language or related languages.","zh":"language group 指由共同語言或相關語言連接起來的社群或人群。"},{"en":"A language group may include several local communities that speak similar varieties.","zh":"一個語言群體可能包括幾個說相似語言變體的本地社群。"},{"en":"Language groups help historians understand cultural connections across different places.","zh":"語言群體幫助歷史學家理解不同地方之間的文化連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing Indigenous history and linguistic identity.","zh":"討論原住民歷史和語言身份時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"occupy the Cumberland Plain","meaning":"居住於坎伯蘭平原","examples":[{"en":"The Darug language group occupied the Cumberland Plain.","zh":"Darug 語言群體居住於坎伯蘭平原。"},{"en":"To occupy the Cumberland Plain means to live in, use, and be connected with that region.","zh":"occupy the Cumberland Plain 指在坎伯蘭平原生活、使用該地並與之有連繫。"},{"en":"A farming community may occupy a valley for generations if the land supports crops and animals.","zh":"如果土地適合種植和養殖，農業社群可能世代居住於山谷。"},{"en":"Occupying a place over time creates cultural knowledge of water, plants, tracks, and seasons.","zh":"長時間居住在一個地方，會形成關於水源、植物、路徑和季節的文化知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing historical land connection.","zh":"描述歷史土地連繫時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"west to the Blue Mountains","meaning":"向西延伸至藍山","examples":[{"en":"Their territory extended west to the Blue Mountains.","zh":"他們的領土向西延伸至藍山。"},{"en":"West to the Blue Mountains means reaching in a westward direction as far as the Blue Mountains.","zh":"west to the Blue Mountains 指向西方延伸，直到藍山為止。"},{"en":"A bus route may run west to a country town from the city centre.","zh":"一條巴士路線可能由市中心向西延伸至鄉鎮。"},{"en":"Describing the direction and endpoint helps readers imagine the size of a territory.","zh":"描述方向和終點有助讀者想像領土大小。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining geographical range.","zh":"解釋地理範圍時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"another theory suggests that","meaning":"另一個理論認為","examples":[{"en":"Another theory suggests that the Eora formed a distinct language group.","zh":"另一個理論認為 Eora 形成一個獨立語言群體。"},{"en":"Another theory suggests that means a different explanation proposes a different idea.","zh":"another theory suggests that 指另一種解釋提出不同想法。"},{"en":"One theory says poor sleep affects marks; another theory suggests that stress is the main cause.","zh":"一個理論說睡眠不足影響分數；另一個理論認為壓力才是主因。"},{"en":"Presenting another theory shows that scholars may not fully agree.","zh":"呈現另一個理論顯示學者未必完全一致。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing competing interpretations.","zh":"討論互相競爭的詮釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a distinct language group","meaning":"獨立的語言群體","examples":[{"en":"The Eora may have been a distinct language group of their own.","zh":"Eora 可能本身是一個獨立的語言群體。"},{"en":"A distinct language group is a separate group with its own language identity.","zh":"distinct language group 指具有自身語言身份的獨立群體。"},{"en":"A mountain community may form a distinct language group if its speech differs clearly from nearby areas.","zh":"如果山區社群的說話方式與附近地區明顯不同，它可能形成獨立語言群體。"},{"en":"Being distinct suggests the group should not simply be treated as part of another group.","zh":"distinct 暗示該群體不應簡單被視為另一群體的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing separate cultural or linguistic identity.","zh":"討論獨立文化或語言身份時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"of their own","meaning":"他們本身獨有的","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers believe the Eora had a language group of their own.","zh":"有些研究人員相信 Eora 有他們本身獨有的語言群體。"},{"en":"Of their own means belonging specifically to them, not borrowed from or shared entirely with others.","zh":"of their own 指特別屬於他們，而不是借來或完全與別人共享。"},{"en":"Children may want a study space of their own when they grow older.","zh":"孩子長大後可能想有自己獨有的學習空間。"},{"en":"Having something of their own can show independence and separate identity.","zh":"擁有本身獨有的東西可以顯示獨立和獨特身份。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when emphasising ownership or distinctiveness.","zh":"強調擁有或獨特性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"no clear evidence for","meaning":"沒有關於……的明確證據","examples":[{"en":"There is no clear evidence for the exact name of the local band.","zh":"沒有關於本地部族群體確切名稱的明確證據。"},{"en":"No clear evidence for something means there is not enough reliable proof to support it.","zh":"no clear evidence for something 指沒有足夠可靠證據支持某事。"},{"en":"There may be no clear evidence for a rumour about a school rule if no official notice exists.","zh":"如果沒有正式通告，可能就沒有關於某校規傳聞的明確證據。"},{"en":"Without clear evidence, historians should be cautious about making firm claims.","zh":"沒有清楚證據時，歷史學家應謹慎作出肯定說法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when information is uncertain.","zh":"當資料不確定時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"particular bands","meaning":"特定部族群體","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are uncertain about the particular bands that lived in Waverley.","zh":"研究人員不確定哪些特定部族群體曾居住在 Waverley。"},{"en":"Particular bands means specific small local groups within a wider Indigenous population.","zh":"particular bands 指較大原住民人口中的特定小型本地群體。"},{"en":"A historian may know the wider nation but not the particular bands that used one valley.","zh":"歷史學家可能知道較大的民族，但不知道使用某山谷的特定部族群體。"},{"en":"Identifying particular bands is difficult when early records are incomplete or written by outsiders.","zh":"當早期紀錄不完整或由外來者書寫，識別特定部族群體會很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing local Indigenous groups.","zh":"討論本地原住民群體時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"roam an area","meaning":"在某地區遊走生活","examples":[{"en":"Indigenous groups once roamed what is now the Waverley area.","zh":"原住民群體曾在現今 Waverley 地區遊走生活。"},{"en":"To roam an area means to move around and live or travel through that area rather than stay in one fixed place.","zh":"roam an area 指在某地區移動、生活或穿行，而不是固定留在一處。"},{"en":"Children may roam a neighbourhood park during a weekend treasure hunt.","zh":"孩子可能在週末尋寶活動中在社區公園四處走動。"},{"en":"Groups may roam an area to find food, water, shelter, or seasonal resources.","zh":"群體可能在某地區遊走，以尋找食物、水、庇護或季節性資源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing movement across land.","zh":"描述在土地上移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what is now","meaning":"現今的……","examples":[{"en":"They lived in what is now the modern Waverley area.","zh":"他們曾生活在現今的 Waverley 地區。"},{"en":"What is now means the place as it is known or named today.","zh":"what is now 指某地現今被認識或命名的形式。"},{"en":"A village once stood in what is now a busy shopping district.","zh":"一條村莊曾位於現今繁忙購物區的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an older historical place with its modern name or form.","zh":"這個短語把較古老的歷史地點與現代名稱或形態連接起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing past and present geography.","zh":"比較過去和現在的地理時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a number of place names","meaning":"多個地方名稱","examples":[{"en":"A number of local place names come from Aboriginal languages.","zh":"多個本地地方名稱來自澳洲原住民語言。"},{"en":"A number of place names means several names of locations.","zh":"a number of place names 指幾個地點名稱。"},{"en":"A number of place names in a city may come from rivers, hills, old villages, or local families.","zh":"城市中多個地方名稱可能來自河流、山丘、舊村落或本地家族。"},{"en":"Place names can preserve history even after communities and landscapes change.","zh":"即使社群和景觀改變，地名仍可以保存歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing names on maps and their origins.","zh":"討論地圖上的名稱及其起源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be based on words derived from","meaning":"以源自……的詞語為基礎","examples":[{"en":"Several names are based on words derived from Aboriginal languages.","zh":"幾個名稱以源自澳洲原住民語言的詞語為基礎。"},{"en":"Be based on words derived from something means be formed from words that originally came from that source.","zh":"be based on words derived from something 指由原本來自某來源的詞語構成。"},{"en":"Many English scientific terms are based on words derived from Latin or Greek.","zh":"許多英文科學術語以源自拉丁語或希臘語的詞語為基礎。"},{"en":"Names based on older languages can carry cultural memory into the present.","zh":"以較古老語言為基礎的名稱，可以把文化記憶帶到現在。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining word origins.","zh":"解釋詞源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Aboriginal languages","meaning":"澳洲原住民語言","examples":[{"en":"Many Australian place names preserve words from Aboriginal languages.","zh":"許多澳洲地名保存了來自澳洲原住民語言的詞語。"},{"en":"Aboriginal languages are the languages of Australia’s Indigenous peoples.","zh":"Aboriginal languages 指澳洲原住民族群的語言。"},{"en":"A school may teach local Aboriginal languages to help students understand the history of the land.","zh":"學校可能教授本地原住民語言，以幫助學生理解土地歷史。"},{"en":"When place names come from Aboriginal languages, they remind people of older cultural presence.","zh":"當地名來自原住民語言，它們提醒人們較古老文化的存在。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing language, heritage, and identity in Australia.","zh":"討論澳洲語言、文化遺產和身份時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the Sydney region","meaning":"悉尼地區","examples":[{"en":"Bondi is one of several Aboriginal place names in the Sydney region.","zh":"Bondi 是悉尼地區幾個原住民地名之一。"},{"en":"The Sydney region means the wider area around the city of Sydney.","zh":"Sydney region 指悉尼市及其周邊較廣泛區域。"},{"en":"Tourists may explore beaches, suburbs, parks, and historic sites across the Sydney region.","zh":"遊客可能在悉尼地區探索海灘、市郊、公園和歷史景點。"},{"en":"A regional view helps readers see Bondi as part of a wider cultural and geographical landscape.","zh":"以地區角度看，有助讀者把邦迪視為更廣泛文化和地理景觀的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing places beyond the city centre.","zh":"討論市中心以外地方時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"from the mid-1800s","meaning":"從十九世紀中葉起","examples":[{"en":"From the mid-1800s, Bondi became popular for family outings.","zh":"從十九世紀中葉起，邦迪成為家庭郊遊的熱門地點。"},{"en":"From the mid-1800s means starting around the middle of the nineteenth century.","zh":"from the mid-1800s 指從十九世紀中期左右開始。"},{"en":"From the mid-1800s, some cities began expanding rapidly because of industry and railways.","zh":"從十九世紀中葉起，一些城市因工業和鐵路而迅速擴張。"},{"en":"Giving this time period helps readers understand when Bondi’s public popularity began.","zh":"提供這個時期有助讀者理解邦迪何時開始受公眾歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing historical change from a particular period.","zh":"描述從某一時期開始的歷史變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a favourite location for","meaning":"……的熱門地點","examples":[{"en":"Bondi Beach became a favourite location for outings and picnics.","zh":"邦迪海灘成為郊遊和野餐的熱門地點。"},{"en":"A favourite location for something is a place people especially like using for that activity.","zh":"favourite location for something 指人們特別喜歡用來進行某活動的地方。"},{"en":"A quiet library corner may become a favourite location for students to revise.","zh":"圖書館安靜角落可能成為學生溫習的熱門地點。"},{"en":"A pleasant location becomes popular when it is easy to reach and offers enjoyable surroundings.","zh":"當一個地方容易到達並提供愉快環境，它就會變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing why people repeatedly choose a place.","zh":"描述人們為何反覆選擇某地時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"family outings","meaning":"家庭郊遊","examples":[{"en":"Families travelled to Bondi for outings by the sea.","zh":"家庭前往邦迪，在海邊郊遊。"},{"en":"Family outings are short trips taken by family members for enjoyment or relaxation.","zh":"family outings 指家庭成員一起進行的短途休閒或放鬆活動。"},{"en":"A family outing may involve visiting a park, beach, museum, or restaurant together.","zh":"家庭郊遊可能包括一起去公園、海灘、博物館或餐廳。"},{"en":"Family outings help people spend time together away from daily routines.","zh":"家庭郊遊幫助人們離開日常規律，一起共度時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing leisure and family life.","zh":"討論休閒和家庭生活時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"go back to","meaning":"追溯至……","examples":[{"en":"The beginnings of the suburb go back to the early nineteenth century.","zh":"這個市郊的起源可追溯至十九世紀初。"},{"en":"Go back to means date from or have origins in an earlier time.","zh":"go back to 指追溯到或起源於較早時期。"},{"en":"A school tradition may go back to the first year the school opened.","zh":"學校傳統可能追溯至學校開辦的第一年。"},{"en":"When something goes back many years, it has a long history behind its present form.","zh":"當某事可追溯多年，它的現代形式背後就有悠久歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when tracing origins.","zh":"追溯起源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"early road builder","meaning":"早期道路建造者","examples":[{"en":"William Roberts was an early road builder in the area.","zh":"William Roberts 是該區一位早期道路建造者。"},{"en":"An early road builder is someone involved in constructing roads during the early development of a place.","zh":"early road builder 指在某地早期發展階段參與修建道路的人。"},{"en":"An early road builder may help connect farms, villages, beaches, and markets.","zh":"早期道路建造者可能幫助連接農場、村莊、海灘和市場。"},{"en":"Roads can shape settlement because they make travel and trade easier.","zh":"道路可以塑造定居發展，因為它們令出行和貿易更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing early infrastructure development.","zh":"討論早期基建發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"receive a grant of land","meaning":"獲批一幅土地","examples":[{"en":"William Roberts received a grant of 81 hectares of land.","zh":"William Roberts 獲批一幅81公頃土地。"},{"en":"To receive a grant of land means to be officially given land by an authority.","zh":"receive a grant of land 指由當局正式授予土地。"},{"en":"A settler might receive a grant of land from a colonial government to encourage farming.","zh":"殖民政府可能向定居者批出土地，以鼓勵農業發展。"},{"en":"Land grants can change who controls and uses a place.","zh":"土地批給可以改變誰控制和使用某地。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing colonial settlement and property history.","zh":"討論殖民定居和土地歷史時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"hectares","meaning":"公頃","examples":[{"en":"The original land grant covered 81 hectares.","zh":"原本的土地批給面積為81公頃。"},{"en":"Hectares are units used to measure land area; one hectare is 10,000 square metres.","zh":"hectares 是量度土地面積的單位；一公頃等於10,000平方米。"},{"en":"A large park may cover several hectares of land.","zh":"大型公園可能佔地數公頃。"},{"en":"Using hectares helps readers understand the size of farms, estates, and reserves.","zh":"使用公頃有助讀者理解農場、莊園和保護區的大小。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing land, planning, and property.","zh":"討論土地、規劃和物業時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"business and residential area","meaning":"商業及住宅區","examples":[{"en":"The former grant now includes much of Bondi’s business and residential area.","zh":"以前批出的土地現在包括邦迪大部分商業及住宅區。"},{"en":"A business and residential area contains both commercial activity and homes.","zh":"business and residential area 指同時包含商業活動和住宅的地區。"},{"en":"A street with shops on the ground floor and flats above is part of a business and residential area.","zh":"地舖是商店、樓上是住宅單位的街道，就是商業及住宅區的一部分。"},{"en":"Mixed areas develop when people need places to live, work, shop, and eat nearby.","zh":"當人們需要在附近居住、工作、購物和用餐，混合用途地區就會發展起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing urban land use.","zh":"描述城市土地用途時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"purchase 200 acres","meaning":"購買二百英畝土地","examples":[{"en":"Two men purchased 200 acres of the Bondi area in 1851.","zh":"兩名男子於1851年購買邦迪地區二百英畝土地。"},{"en":"To purchase 200 acres means to buy a large piece of land measuring 200 acres.","zh":"purchase 200 acres 指購買面積為二百英畝的大幅土地。"},{"en":"A farming company may purchase 200 acres to grow crops or raise animals.","zh":"農業公司可能購買二百英畝土地來種植作物或飼養動物。"},{"en":"Buying a large coastal area can affect future public access and development.","zh":"購買大片海岸土地可以影響未來公眾使用權和發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing land ownership.","zh":"討論土地擁有權時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"embrace almost the whole frontage","meaning":"涵蓋幾乎整段臨海地帶","examples":[{"en":"The estate embraced almost the whole frontage of Bondi Beach.","zh":"該莊園涵蓋邦迪海灘幾乎整段臨海地帶。"},{"en":"To embrace almost the whole frontage means to include nearly the entire front-facing coastal edge.","zh":"embrace almost the whole frontage 指包含幾乎整個面向海岸的前方地帶。"},{"en":"A hotel site may embrace almost the whole frontage of a small bay if it stretches across the beachside road.","zh":"如果酒店地皮橫跨整條海邊道路，它可能涵蓋小海灣幾乎整段臨海地帶。"},{"en":"Controlling most of the frontage can give owners strong influence over access and development.","zh":"控制大部分臨海地帶，可以令擁有人對通道和發展有很大影響力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing property that covers a large visible edge of land.","zh":"描述覆蓋大片可見土地邊緣的物業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"beach frontage","meaning":"海灘臨海地帶","examples":[{"en":"The property included a large section of beach frontage.","zh":"該物業包括一大片海灘臨海地帶。"},{"en":"Beach frontage is land that directly faces or borders a beach.","zh":"beach frontage 指直接面向或接壤海灘的土地。"},{"en":"Hotels with beach frontage can charge more because guests can see the sea easily.","zh":"擁有海灘臨海地帶的酒店可以收取較高價格，因為住客容易看到海。"},{"en":"Beach frontage is valuable because it offers access, views, and commercial opportunity.","zh":"海灘臨海地帶有價值，因為它提供通道、景觀和商業機會。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing coastal property.","zh":"討論海岸物業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be named","meaning":"被命名為","examples":[{"en":"The property was named the Bondi Estate.","zh":"該物業被命名為 Bondi Estate。"},{"en":"Be named means be given a particular name.","zh":"be named 指被給予某個名稱。"},{"en":"A new park may be named after a local community leader.","zh":"新公園可能以本地社區領袖命名。"},{"en":"Naming a property can give it identity and make it easier to discuss in records.","zh":"為物業命名可以給它身份，並令它在紀錄中較容易被討論。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how places receive names.","zh":"解釋地方如何得到名稱時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"purchase someone’s share","meaning":"購買某人的土地份額","examples":[{"en":"O’Brien later purchased Hall’s share of the land.","zh":"O’Brien 後來購買了 Hall 的土地份額。"},{"en":"To purchase someone’s share means to buy that person’s part of a jointly owned property or business.","zh":"purchase someone’s share 指買入某人在共同擁有物業或業務中的部分。"},{"en":"One partner may purchase another partner’s share of a café before running it alone.","zh":"一名合夥人可能購買另一名合夥人的咖啡店份額，然後獨自經營。"},{"en":"Buying another person’s share can give one owner more control over the whole property.","zh":"買入另一人的份額可以令一名擁有人對整個物業有更大控制權。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing ownership and partnership.","zh":"討論擁有權和合夥關係時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"rename the land","meaning":"將土地重新命名","examples":[{"en":"O’Brien renamed the land the O’Brien Estate.","zh":"O’Brien 將土地重新命名為 O’Brien Estate。"},{"en":"To rename the land means to give the land a new name.","zh":"rename the land 指給土地一個新名稱。"},{"en":"A town may rename a street to honour a historical figure.","zh":"城鎮可能重新命名街道，以紀念歷史人物。"},{"en":"Renaming land can signal a change in ownership, identity, or purpose.","zh":"重新命名土地可以表示擁有權、身份或用途的改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing changes in place names.","zh":"討論地名變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make land available to the public","meaning":"開放土地給公眾使用","examples":[{"en":"O’Brien made the beach and surrounding land available to the public.","zh":"O’Brien 開放海灘及周邊土地給公眾使用。"},{"en":"To make land available to the public means to allow ordinary people to enter or use the land.","zh":"make land available to the public 指容許普通人進入或使用該土地。"},{"en":"A council may make land available to the public by opening it as a park.","zh":"議會可能把土地開放為公園，讓公眾使用。"},{"en":"Public access can turn private land into a shared leisure space.","zh":"公眾使用權可以把私人土地變成共享休閒空間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing access rights and public recreation.","zh":"討論使用權和公共康樂時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"picnic ground","meaning":"野餐地點","examples":[{"en":"The beach became a popular picnic ground.","zh":"這個海灘成為受歡迎的野餐地點。"},{"en":"A picnic ground is a place where people gather to eat outdoors and relax.","zh":"picnic ground 指人們聚集戶外用餐和放鬆的地方。"},{"en":"A park with grass, shade, and tables can become a favourite picnic ground for families.","zh":"有草地、樹蔭和桌子的公園可以成為家庭喜愛的野餐地點。"},{"en":"A pleasant picnic ground attracts visitors because people can spend several hours there cheaply.","zh":"宜人的野餐地點吸引遊客，因為人們可以低成本地在那裏待上幾小時。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing outdoor leisure places.","zh":"描述戶外休閒場所時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"amusement resort","meaning":"娛樂度假地","examples":[{"en":"The estate was developed as an amusement resort.","zh":"該莊園被發展成娛樂度假地。"},{"en":"An amusement resort is a leisure place with entertainment, attractions, and holiday activities.","zh":"amusement resort 指有娛樂、景點和度假活動的休閒地方。"},{"en":"A seaside amusement resort may offer rides, food stalls, games, and beach access.","zh":"海濱娛樂度假地可能提供機動遊戲、小食攤、遊戲和海灘通道。"},{"en":"Turning land into an amusement resort can bring visitors and business to the area.","zh":"把土地變成娛樂度假地可以為該區帶來遊客和商業活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing tourism development.","zh":"討論旅遊發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"become increasingly popular","meaning":"變得越來越受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Bondi Beach became increasingly popular with the public.","zh":"邦迪海灘變得越來越受公眾歡迎。"},{"en":"Become increasingly popular means become more and more liked or visited over time.","zh":"become increasingly popular 指隨時間變得越來越受喜愛或越多人到訪。"},{"en":"A café may become increasingly popular after students recommend it online.","zh":"咖啡店在學生於網上推薦後，可能變得越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"As more visitors come, businesses, transport, and facilities often grow around the place.","zh":"隨着更多遊客到來，商業、交通和設施通常會在周邊增長。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing rising public interest.","zh":"描述公眾興趣上升時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"threaten to stop public access","meaning":"威脅停止公眾使用權","examples":[{"en":"O’Brien threatened to stop public access to the beach.","zh":"O’Brien 威脅停止公眾使用海灘的權利。"},{"en":"To threaten to stop public access means to warn that ordinary people may no longer be allowed to enter or use a place.","zh":"threaten to stop public access 指警告普通人可能不再被允許進入或使用某地。"},{"en":"A private owner may threaten to stop public access to a path if visitors leave rubbish.","zh":"如果遊客留下垃圾，私人業主可能威脅停止公眾使用小徑。"},{"en":"Threats to access can lead councils or residents to demand legal protection.","zh":"對使用權的威脅可以令議會或居民要求法律保護。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing conflict over public space.","zh":"討論公共空間爭議時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"public beach access","meaning":"公眾使用海灘的權利","examples":[{"en":"The council wanted to preserve public beach access.","zh":"議會希望保留公眾使用海灘的權利。"},{"en":"Public beach access means the right or ability of ordinary people to reach and use a beach.","zh":"public beach access 指普通人到達和使用海灘的權利或能力。"},{"en":"A town may build a walkway to improve public beach access for families and older people.","zh":"城鎮可能修建步道，改善家庭和長者使用海灘的便利。"},{"en":"If public beach access is restricted, only private owners or paying guests may enjoy the shore.","zh":"如果公眾使用海灘權利受限制，可能只有私人業主或付費住客能享受海岸。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing beaches as shared public spaces.","zh":"討論海灘作為共享公共空間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Municipal Council","meaning":"市議會","examples":[{"en":"The Municipal Council believed that official action was necessary.","zh":"市議會認為官方行動是必要的。"},{"en":"A Municipal Council is a local government body responsible for services and decisions in a town or district.","zh":"Municipal Council 指負責城鎮或地區服務和決策的地方政府機構。"},{"en":"A municipal council may manage roads, public parks, rubbish collection, and local planning.","zh":"市議會可能管理道路、公園、垃圾收集和地方規劃。"},{"en":"Councils often act when public access, safety, or local services are at risk.","zh":"當公眾使用權、安全或本地服務受威脅，議會常會採取行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing local government.","zh":"討論地方政府時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"government intervention","meaning":"政府介入","examples":[{"en":"The council called for government intervention to protect public access.","zh":"議會呼籲政府介入，以保護公眾使用權。"},{"en":"Government intervention means official action by the government to deal with a problem.","zh":"government intervention 指政府為處理問題而採取的官方行動。"},{"en":"Government intervention may be needed if private companies block access to a public road.","zh":"如果私人公司阻塞公共道路，可能需要政府介入。"},{"en":"Intervention can protect rights, regulate development, or solve conflicts that individuals cannot handle alone.","zh":"介入可以保護權利、規管發展，或解決個人無法獨自處理的衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing public policy and official action.","zh":"討論公共政策和官方行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make the beach a public reserve","meaning":"將海灘列為公共保留地","examples":[{"en":"The authorities wanted to make the beach a public reserve.","zh":"當局希望將海灘列為公共保留地。"},{"en":"To make the beach a public reserve means to legally protect it as land for public use.","zh":"make the beach a public reserve 指依法保護海灘，使其成為公眾可使用的土地。"},{"en":"A council may make a riverside area a public reserve so everyone can walk there.","zh":"議會可能把河邊地區列為公共保留地，讓每個人都可在那裏散步。"},{"en":"Public reserve status can prevent private owners from closing important shared spaces.","zh":"公共保留地身份可以防止私人業主關閉重要共享空間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing legal protection of public land.","zh":"討論公共土地法律保護時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"become associated with","meaning":"與……聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"Bondi Beach became associated with health, leisure and democracy.","zh":"邦迪海灘變得與健康、休閒和民主聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Become associated with means become connected in people’s minds with a particular idea or value.","zh":"become associated with 指在人們心中與某個想法或價值連接起來。"},{"en":"A school may become associated with music if its choir wins many prizes.","zh":"如果學校合唱團贏得許多獎項，該校可能變得與音樂聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Places gain symbolic meaning when people repeatedly use them in the same way.","zh":"當人們反覆以同一方式使用地方，地方就會獲得象徵意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing reputation or cultural meaning.","zh":"描述聲譽或文化意義時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"health, leisure and democracy","meaning":"健康、休閒和民主","examples":[{"en":"The beach came to represent health, leisure and democracy.","zh":"這個海灘開始代表健康、休閒和民主。"},{"en":"Health, leisure and democracy refer to ideas of well-being, free time, and equal public enjoyment.","zh":"health, leisure and democracy 指身心健康、自由休閒時間和平等公共享用的理念。"},{"en":"A public park can symbolise health, leisure and democracy when rich and poor families all use it.","zh":"當富裕和貧窮家庭都使用公共公園，它就可以象徵健康、休閒和民主。"},{"en":"A shared beach may represent democracy because it is not only for wealthy people.","zh":"共享海灘可以代表民主，因為它不只屬於富人。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a public place carries social values.","zh":"當公共地方承載社會價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a playground everyone could enjoy","meaning":"人人都可享用的遊樂地","examples":[{"en":"Bondi was seen as a playground everyone could enjoy equally.","zh":"邦迪被視為人人都可平等享用的遊樂地。"},{"en":"A playground everyone could enjoy means a public leisure place open to people from different backgrounds.","zh":"playground everyone could enjoy 指向不同背景人士開放的公共休閒場所。"},{"en":"A clean public swimming pool can become a playground everyone could enjoy in summer.","zh":"乾淨的公共泳池可以在夏天成為人人都可享用的遊樂地。"},{"en":"Equal access makes a place feel democratic and shared.","zh":"平等使用權令地方感覺民主和共享。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing public recreation without social exclusion.","zh":"描述沒有社會排斥的公共康樂時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"working-class suburb","meaning":"工人階級市郊","examples":[{"en":"Bondi was a working-class suburb for much of the twentieth century.","zh":"邦迪在二十世紀大部分時間是一個工人階級市郊。"},{"en":"A working-class suburb is a residential area where many residents are manual, service, or lower-income workers.","zh":"working-class suburb 指許多居民從事體力、服務或較低收入工作的住宅區。"},{"en":"A working-class suburb may have modest homes, local shops, and strong community ties.","zh":"工人階級市郊可能有樸素住宅、本地商店和強烈社區連繫。"},{"en":"As property prices rise, a working-class suburb may gradually become wealthier and less affordable.","zh":"隨着樓價上升，工人階級市郊可能逐漸變得富裕但較難負擔。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing class and urban history.","zh":"討論階級和城市歷史時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"throughout most of","meaning":"在……的大部分時期","examples":[{"en":"Bondi retained its working-class character throughout most of the century.","zh":"邦迪在該世紀大部分時期保留其工人階級特色。"},{"en":"Throughout most of something means during the greater part of a period.","zh":"throughout most of something 指在某段時間的大部分期間。"},{"en":"A shop may remain family-run throughout most of its history.","zh":"一間商店可能在其大部分歷史中保持家族經營。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a condition lasted for a long time, though not necessarily the whole period.","zh":"這個短語顯示某狀況持續很長時間，但不一定是整段時期。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing historical continuity.","zh":"描述歷史延續性時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"migrants from New Zealand","meaning":"來自新西蘭的移民","examples":[{"en":"Migrants from New Zealand formed a large part of the local population.","zh":"來自新西蘭的移民構成本地人口的一大部分。"},{"en":"Migrants from New Zealand are people who moved from New Zealand to live in another place.","zh":"migrants from New Zealand 指從新西蘭搬到另一地方生活的人。"},{"en":"A city may have many migrants from New Zealand because of work, study, or family links.","zh":"因工作、學習或家庭連繫，一個城市可能有許多來自新西蘭的移民。"},{"en":"Migration can change the language, food, sports culture, and community networks of an area.","zh":"移民可以改變一個地區的語言、食物、體育文化和社區網絡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing population change.","zh":"討論人口變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"comprise the majority of","meaning":"佔……的大多數","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand migrants comprised the majority of the local population.","zh":"新西蘭移民佔本地人口的大多數。"},{"en":"Comprise the majority of means make up more than half of a group.","zh":"comprise the majority of 指構成某群體超過一半。"},{"en":"Students may comprise the majority of customers in a café near a university.","zh":"在大學附近的咖啡店，學生可能佔顧客的大多數。"},{"en":"If one group comprises the majority, it can strongly shape local culture and services.","zh":"如果某一群體佔大多數，它可以強烈塑造本地文化和服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing population composition.","zh":"討論人口構成時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"local population","meaning":"本地人口","examples":[{"en":"The composition of Bondi’s local population changed over time.","zh":"邦迪本地人口的構成隨時間改變。"},{"en":"Local population means the people who live in a particular area.","zh":"local population 指居住在某一特定地區的人。"},{"en":"A new railway station can change the local population by attracting more residents.","zh":"新火車站可以透過吸引更多居民而改變本地人口。"},{"en":"When the local population changes, schools, shops, housing, and community life may change too.","zh":"當本地人口改變，學校、商店、住屋和社區生活也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing people living in a place.","zh":"討論居住在某地的人時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tramway","meaning":"電車路線","examples":[{"en":"The first tramway reached Bondi Beach in 1884.","zh":"第一條電車路線於1884年到達邦迪海灘。"},{"en":"A tramway is a track system used by trams for public transport.","zh":"tramway 指電車用作公共交通的軌道系統。"},{"en":"A tramway through a city can connect homes, shops, beaches, and workplaces.","zh":"穿過城市的電車路線可以連接住宅、商店、海灘和工作地點。"},{"en":"When a tramway reaches a beach, more people can visit without needing private transport.","zh":"當電車路線到達海灘，更多人無需私人交通工具也能到訪。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing older urban transport.","zh":"討論舊式城市交通時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"form of public transport","meaning":"公共交通工具","examples":[{"en":"The tram became Bondi’s first form of public transport.","zh":"電車成為邦迪第一種公共交通工具。"},{"en":"A form of public transport is a transport method available for shared public use.","zh":"form of public transport 指可供公眾共同使用的交通方式。"},{"en":"Buses, trains, ferries, and trams are forms of public transport.","zh":"巴士、火車、渡輪和電車都是公共交通工具。"},{"en":"Public transport can make recreation spaces more equal because more people can reach them.","zh":"公共交通可以令康樂空間更平等，因為更多人能到達。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing transport options.","zh":"比較交通選項時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, the beach became accessible to more people.","zh":"因此，更多人能夠到達這個海灘。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what happened before, this consequence followed.","zh":"as a result 指因為之前發生的事情，所以出現這個結果。"},{"en":"The school added more buses; as a result, fewer students arrived late.","zh":"學校增加巴士；因此，較少學生遲到。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links a cause with an effect.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接原因和結果。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining consequences.","zh":"解釋後果時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"end a situation in which","meaning":"結束……的情況","examples":[{"en":"The tram ended a situation in which only wealthy people could visit easily.","zh":"電車結束了只有富裕人士能輕易到訪的情況。"},{"en":"End a situation in which means stop a condition where something was happening.","zh":"end a situation in which 指停止某種一直存在的狀況。"},{"en":"Online booking ended a situation in which patients had to queue for hours at the clinic.","zh":"網上預約結束了病人必須在診所排隊數小時的情況。"},{"en":"Better transport can end unfair access by letting more social groups reach a place.","zh":"更好的交通可以讓更多社會群體到達某地，從而結束不公平使用情況。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing how a change removes an old problem.","zh":"描述某改變如何移除舊問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"draw local visitors","meaning":"吸引本地遊客","examples":[{"en":"By the 1930s, Bondi was drawing many local visitors.","zh":"到1930年代，邦迪吸引了許多本地遊客。"},{"en":"To draw local visitors means to attract people who live nearby or in the same region.","zh":"draw local visitors 指吸引住在附近或同一地區的人到訪。"},{"en":"A weekend market can draw local visitors if it sells fresh food and crafts.","zh":"如果週末市集售賣新鮮食物和手工藝品，就能吸引本地遊客。"},{"en":"Local visitors help keep a place active even outside peak tourist seasons.","zh":"本地遊客有助地方即使在旅遊淡季仍保持活力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how attractions bring people in.","zh":"討論景點如何吸引人時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"people from elsewhere","meaning":"來自其他地方的人","examples":[{"en":"The beach also attracted people from elsewhere in Australia.","zh":"這個海灘也吸引來自澳洲其他地方的人。"},{"en":"People from elsewhere means people from other places, not from the immediate local area.","zh":"people from elsewhere 指來自其他地方、不是本地附近的人。"},{"en":"A famous hospital may attract patients from elsewhere in the country.","zh":"著名醫院可能吸引國內其他地方的病人。"},{"en":"When people from elsewhere visit, a local place can gain a wider reputation.","zh":"當來自其他地方的人到訪，本地地方可以獲得更廣泛聲譽。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing visitors from outside the area.","zh":"描述外地遊客時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"overseas visitors","meaning":"海外遊客","examples":[{"en":"Bondi eventually became popular with overseas visitors.","zh":"邦迪最終受到海外遊客歡迎。"},{"en":"Overseas visitors are people who travel from other countries.","zh":"overseas visitors 指從其他國家來的遊客。"},{"en":"Hotels near famous beaches often depend on overseas visitors during holiday seasons.","zh":"著名海灘附近的酒店在假期旺季常依賴海外遊客。"},{"en":"Overseas visitors can bring income but also increase pressure on transport and housing.","zh":"海外遊客可以帶來收入，但也會增加交通和住屋壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing international tourism.","zh":"討論國際旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"advertising at the time","meaning":"當時的廣告","examples":[{"en":"Advertising at the time promoted Bondi as a major attraction.","zh":"當時的廣告把邦迪宣傳為主要景點。"},{"en":"Advertising at the time means promotional material used during that historical period.","zh":"advertising at the time 指在該歷史時期使用的宣傳材料。"},{"en":"Advertising at the time may show what people valued, such as health, leisure, or modernity.","zh":"當時的廣告可能顯示人們重視甚麼，例如健康、休閒或現代感。"},{"en":"Old advertisements can shape a place’s image and attract new visitors.","zh":"舊廣告可以塑造地方形象並吸引新遊客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing historical marketing.","zh":"討論歷史行銷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"refer to something as","meaning":"將……稱為","examples":[{"en":"Advertisements referred to Bondi as the Playground of the Pacific.","zh":"廣告將邦迪稱為「太平洋遊樂場」。"},{"en":"To refer to something as a name means to call or describe it using that name.","zh":"refer to something as a name 指用某個名稱稱呼或描述某事物。"},{"en":"A school may refer to its library as the heart of the campus.","zh":"學校可能將圖書館稱為校園的心臟。"},{"en":"The name chosen can shape how people imagine the place.","zh":"被選用的名稱可以塑造人們如何想像該地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining labels, titles, or descriptions.","zh":"解釋標籤、稱號或描述時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Playground of the Pacific","meaning":"太平洋遊樂場","examples":[{"en":"Bondi was promoted as the Playground of the Pacific.","zh":"邦迪被宣傳為太平洋遊樂場。"},{"en":"Playground of the Pacific presents Bondi as a fun leisure destination in the Pacific region.","zh":"Playground of the Pacific 把邦迪呈現為太平洋地區一個有趣的休閒目的地。"},{"en":"A tourist slogan can make a beach sound lively, healthy, and exciting.","zh":"旅遊口號可以令海灘聽起來充滿活力、健康和刺激。"},{"en":"Calling Bondi a playground encouraged people to see it as a place for relaxation and pleasure.","zh":"把邦迪稱為遊樂場，鼓勵人們把它視為放鬆和享樂之地。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing tourism branding.","zh":"討論旅遊品牌塑造時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prefer doing A rather than B","meaning":"寧願做 A 而不是 B","examples":[{"en":"Many people preferred relaxing by the sea rather than living in unhealthy cities.","zh":"許多人寧願在海邊放鬆，而不是住在不利健康的城市。"},{"en":"Prefer doing A rather than B means like or choose one action more than another.","zh":"prefer doing A rather than B 指較喜歡或選擇做 A，而不是做 B。"},{"en":"Some students prefer revising with examples rather than memorising long rules.","zh":"有些學生寧願用例子溫習，而不是背誦長規則。"},{"en":"The contrast shows that people saw the seaside as healthier than crowded urban life.","zh":"這個對比顯示人們把海邊視為比擁擠城市生活更健康。"},{"en":"This structure is useful when showing a clear preference between two choices.","zh":"在兩個選擇之間顯示明確偏好時，這個結構很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"relax by the seaside","meaning":"在海邊休息","examples":[{"en":"City residents increasingly wanted to relax by the seaside.","zh":"城市居民越來越想在海邊休息。"},{"en":"To relax by the seaside means to rest near the sea, often by walking, swimming, or sitting on the beach.","zh":"relax by the seaside 指在海邊休息，通常包括散步、游泳或坐在沙灘上。"},{"en":"A family may relax by the seaside after a busy week of work and school.","zh":"一個家庭可能在忙碌的一週工作和上學後，到海邊休息。"},{"en":"Sea air, open space, and waves can make seaside relaxation feel healthier than city life.","zh":"海風、開闊空間和海浪可以令海邊休息感覺比城市生活更健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing leisure and coastal tourism.","zh":"討論休閒和海岸旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"unhealthy cities","meaning":"不利健康的城市","examples":[{"en":"Industrial cities were sometimes viewed as unhealthy places to live.","zh":"工業城市有時被視為不利健康的居住地方。"},{"en":"Unhealthy cities are urban areas associated with pollution, crowding, poor housing, or limited fresh air.","zh":"unhealthy cities 指與污染、擁擠、惡劣住屋或新鮮空氣不足有關的城市地區。"},{"en":"A city with heavy traffic and little green space may feel unhealthy to residents.","zh":"交通繁忙且綠化空間少的城市，可能令居民覺得不利健康。"},{"en":"If people see cities as unhealthy, they may seek parks, beaches, and cleaner air.","zh":"如果人們視城市為不健康，就可能尋找公園、海灘和更清新空氣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing urban living conditions.","zh":"討論城市居住條件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"increasing popularity of","meaning":"……越來越普及","examples":[{"en":"The increasing popularity of sea bathing raised safety concerns.","zh":"海中暢泳越來越普及，引起安全方面的關注。"},{"en":"Increasing popularity of something means more and more people are becoming interested in or using it.","zh":"increasing popularity of something 指越來越多人對某事感興趣或使用它。"},{"en":"The increasing popularity of cycling may lead a city to build more bike lanes.","zh":"踩單車越來越普及，可能令城市興建更多單車徑。"},{"en":"When an activity becomes popular, authorities may need new rules, facilities, or safety measures.","zh":"當一項活動變得受歡迎，當局可能需要新規則、設施或安全措施。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when growing public interest creates consequences.","zh":"當公眾興趣增長並帶來後果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sea bathing","meaning":"海中暢泳","examples":[{"en":"Sea bathing became increasingly popular in the late nineteenth century.","zh":"海中暢泳在十九世紀末變得越來越普及。"},{"en":"Sea bathing means swimming or bathing in the sea for health, leisure, or enjoyment.","zh":"sea bathing 指為健康、休閒或享受而在海中游泳或浸浴。"},{"en":"Families may go sea bathing on a hot summer day.","zh":"家庭可能在炎熱夏日去海中暢泳。"},{"en":"As sea bathing becomes popular, lifesaving services become more important.","zh":"隨着海中暢泳普及，救生服務變得更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing old and modern beach culture.","zh":"討論舊式和現代海灘文化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"raise concerns about","meaning":"引起對……的關注","examples":[{"en":"The popularity of swimming raised concerns about public safety.","zh":"游泳的普及引起對公眾安全的關注。"},{"en":"To raise concerns about something means to make people worried or aware of a possible problem.","zh":"raise concerns about something 指令人擔心或意識到可能存在的問題。"},{"en":"A rise in school bullying may raise concerns about student mental health.","zh":"校園欺凌增加可能引起對學生心理健康的關注。"},{"en":"More swimmers can increase the risk of accidents, so safety concerns become stronger.","zh":"游泳人士增加可能提高意外風險，因此安全關注會變強。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when growth creates possible risks.","zh":"當增長帶來可能風險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"public safety","meaning":"公眾安全","examples":[{"en":"Lifesaving organisations were formed to improve public safety.","zh":"救生組織成立，以改善公眾安全。"},{"en":"Public safety means the protection of ordinary people from danger in shared spaces.","zh":"public safety 指在共享空間中保護普通人免受危險。"},{"en":"Street lighting, lifeguards, traffic rules, and fire exits all support public safety.","zh":"街燈、救生員、交通規則和走火通道都支持公眾安全。"},{"en":"When more people use a beach, public safety becomes harder and more important to manage.","zh":"當更多人使用海灘，公眾安全就更難管理，也更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing community protection.","zh":"討論社區保護時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"prevent someone from drowning","meaning":"防止某人溺水","examples":[{"en":"Lifesavers were trained to prevent swimmers from drowning.","zh":"救生員接受訓練，以防止泳客溺水。"},{"en":"To prevent someone from drowning means to stop a person from dying or being harmed in water.","zh":"prevent someone from drowning 指阻止某人在水中死亡或受傷。"},{"en":"Swimming lessons can help prevent children from drowning in pools or at beaches.","zh":"游泳課可以幫助防止兒童在泳池或海灘溺水。"},{"en":"Lifeguards watch swimmers closely so they can act before danger becomes fatal.","zh":"救生員密切觀察泳客，以便在危險致命前行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing water safety.","zh":"討論水上安全時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in response","meaning":"作為回應","examples":[{"en":"In response, a formal surf lifesaving club was established.","zh":"作為回應，一個正式海灘救生會成立了。"},{"en":"In response means as a reaction to a problem, event, or need.","zh":"in response 指作為對某問題、事件或需要的反應。"},{"en":"In response to traffic accidents, a school may add a crossing guard.","zh":"作為對交通意外的回應，學校可能增設過路護導員。"},{"en":"When safety concerns grow, communities often create organisations to deal with them.","zh":"當安全憂慮增加，社區常會建立組織來處理它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one action follows from a previous problem.","zh":"當一個行動源自先前問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"formally documented","meaning":"有正式文獻記錄的","examples":[{"en":"The club is described as the world’s first formally documented surf lifesaving club.","zh":"該會被描述為世界上第一個有正式文獻記錄的海灘救生會。"},{"en":"Formally documented means officially recorded in written or reliable records.","zh":"formally documented 指在正式文字或可靠紀錄中被官方記載。"},{"en":"A school policy is formally documented when it appears in an official handbook.","zh":"當學校政策出現在正式手冊中，它就是有正式文獻記錄的。"},{"en":"Formal documentation matters because it helps prove when an organisation began.","zh":"正式紀錄很重要，因為它有助證明組織何時開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing verified historical records.","zh":"討論經驗證的歷史紀錄時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"surf lifesaving club","meaning":"海灘救生會","examples":[{"en":"Bondi’s surf lifesaving club was formed in 1907.","zh":"邦迪的海灘救生會於1907年成立。"},{"en":"A surf lifesaving club is an organisation that trains people to rescue swimmers and improve beach safety.","zh":"surf lifesaving club 指訓練人員拯救泳客並改善海灘安全的組織。"},{"en":"A surf lifesaving club may run patrols, first-aid training, and rescue drills.","zh":"海灘救生會可能進行巡邏、急救訓練和救援演習。"},{"en":"Such clubs become important when many people swim in dangerous surf conditions.","zh":"當許多人在危險浪況中游泳，這類組織就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing beach safety organisations.","zh":"討論海灘安全組織時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be formed","meaning":"成立","examples":[{"en":"The Bondi Surf Bathers’ Life Saving Club was formed in 1907.","zh":"Bondi Surf Bathers’ Life Saving Club 於1907年成立。"},{"en":"Be formed means be created, established, or officially started.","zh":"be formed 指被創立、建立或正式開始。"},{"en":"A student committee may be formed to organise the graduation dinner.","zh":"學生委員會可能成立，以籌辦畢業晚宴。"},{"en":"Organisations are often formed when people need to solve a shared problem.","zh":"當人們需要解決共同問題，組織常會成立。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the beginning of a group.","zh":"描述團體的開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be powerfully reinforced by","meaning":"因……而大大加強","examples":[{"en":"The image of the lifesaver was powerfully reinforced by Black Sunday.","zh":"救生員的形象因黑色星期日而大大加強。"},{"en":"Be powerfully reinforced by means be strongly strengthened or confirmed by an event or example.","zh":"be powerfully reinforced by 指因某事件或例子而被強烈加強或確認。"},{"en":"A school’s reputation for kindness may be powerfully reinforced by how it supports students after a tragedy.","zh":"學校在悲劇後如何支援學生，可能大大加強其關愛聲譽。"},{"en":"Dramatic rescue events can strengthen public respect for lifesavers.","zh":"戲劇性的救援事件可以加強公眾對救生員的尊敬。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an event makes an image or belief much stronger.","zh":"當事件令形象或信念變得更強時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dramatic events","meaning":"戲劇性的事件","examples":[{"en":"Dramatic events in 1938 demonstrated the importance of lifesavers.","zh":"1938年的戲劇性事件展示了救生員的重要性。"},{"en":"Dramatic events are sudden, serious, exciting, or emotionally powerful happenings.","zh":"dramatic events 指突然、嚴重、刺激或情感衝擊很強的事件。"},{"en":"A fire drill becomes more memorable if a dramatic event shows why safety rules matter.","zh":"如果一件戲劇性事件顯示安全規則為何重要，消防演習就會更令人記得。"},{"en":"Dramatic events can change public opinion because people remember them vividly.","zh":"戲劇性事件可以改變公眾意見，因為人們會鮮明記住它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing events with strong impact.","zh":"描述有強烈影響的事件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Black Sunday","meaning":"黑色星期日","examples":[{"en":"Black Sunday became a defining event in Bondi’s history.","zh":"黑色星期日成為邦迪歷史中的標誌性事件。"},{"en":"Black Sunday refers to a serious 1938 incident at Bondi when huge waves swept many people into the sea.","zh":"Black Sunday 指1938年邦迪的一次嚴重事件，當時巨浪把許多人捲入海中。"},{"en":"A community may remember a disaster by giving it a name that marks its seriousness.","zh":"社區可能透過給災難命名來標記其嚴重性。"},{"en":"The event strengthened the cultural importance of surf lifesavers in Australia.","zh":"這件事件加強了海灘救生員在澳洲文化中的重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing Bondi’s rescue history.","zh":"討論邦迪救援歷史時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be about to start","meaning":"正準備開始","examples":[{"en":"A group of lifesavers was about to start a surf race.","zh":"一群救生員正準備開始一場衝浪比賽。"},{"en":"Be about to start means be ready to begin very soon.","zh":"be about to start 指即將開始、很快會開始。"},{"en":"A teacher is about to start the lesson when students open their books and stop talking.","zh":"當學生打開課本並停止聊天時，老師正準備開始上課。"},{"en":"This phrase creates tension because something unexpected may happen just before the planned action.","zh":"這個短語營造緊張感，因為計劃行動前可能突然發生意外。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing the moment immediately before an event begins.","zh":"描述事件開始前一刻時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"freak waves","meaning":"反常巨浪","examples":[{"en":"Three freak waves suddenly struck the crowded beach.","zh":"三個反常巨浪突然衝擊擠滿人的海灘。"},{"en":"Freak waves are unusually large or unexpected waves that can be dangerous.","zh":"freak waves 指異常巨大或意料之外、可能危險的海浪。"},{"en":"Lifeguards may close a beach if freak waves appear during bad weather.","zh":"如果惡劣天氣中出現反常巨浪，救生員可能關閉海灘。"},{"en":"Freak waves can sweep swimmers away before they have time to react.","zh":"反常巨浪可以在人們來不及反應前把泳客捲走。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing rare and dangerous sea conditions.","zh":"描述罕見而危險的海況時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hit the beach","meaning":"衝擊海灘","examples":[{"en":"The freak waves hit the beach without warning.","zh":"反常巨浪毫無預警地衝擊海灘。"},{"en":"Hit the beach means strike or reach the beach with force.","zh":"hit the beach 指以力量撞向或到達海灘。"},{"en":"Strong winds can make waves hit the beach harder than usual.","zh":"強風可以令海浪比平時更猛烈地衝擊海灘。"},{"en":"When waves hit the beach suddenly, people near the water may be knocked down or swept away.","zh":"當海浪突然衝擊海灘，靠近海邊的人可能被撞倒或捲走。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing forceful wave impact.","zh":"描述海浪強力衝擊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sweep people out to sea","meaning":"把人捲出外海","examples":[{"en":"The waves swept hundreds of people out to sea.","zh":"海浪把數百人捲出外海。"},{"en":"To sweep people out to sea means to carry people away from the shore into deeper water.","zh":"sweep people out to sea 指把人從岸邊帶離，捲到較深海水中。"},{"en":"A strong current can sweep swimmers out to sea even if they are close to the beach.","zh":"強水流可以把泳客捲出外海，即使他們原本靠近海灘。"},{"en":"When people are swept out to sea, lifesavers must act quickly to prevent drowning.","zh":"當人被捲出外海，救生員必須迅速行動以防溺水。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing beach danger and rescue.","zh":"討論海灘危險和救援時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rescue 300 people","meaning":"救出三百人","examples":[{"en":"Lifesavers rescued approximately 300 people.","zh":"救生員救出大約三百人。"},{"en":"To rescue 300 people means to save around 300 people from danger.","zh":"rescue 300 people 指從危險中拯救約三百人。"},{"en":"Emergency workers may rescue many people after flooding traps families in their homes.","zh":"水災把家庭困在家中後，救援人員可能救出許多人。"},{"en":"A large rescue shows both the danger of the event and the skill of the rescuers.","zh":"大型救援同時顯示事件的危險和救援者的能力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the scale of a lifesaving action.","zh":"描述救生活動規模時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"mass rescue","meaning":"大規模救援","examples":[{"en":"The event became the largest mass rescue in surf-bathing history.","zh":"這次事件成為海中暢泳歷史上最大規模救援。"},{"en":"A mass rescue is a rescue operation involving many people at the same time.","zh":"mass rescue 指同時涉及許多人的救援行動。"},{"en":"A ferry accident may require a mass rescue if many passengers fall into the water.","zh":"如果渡輪意外令許多乘客落水，可能需要大規模救援。"},{"en":"Mass rescues need teamwork, training, equipment, and fast decisions.","zh":"大規模救援需要團隊合作、訓練、設備和快速決策。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing large emergency operations.","zh":"討論大型緊急行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the history of","meaning":"在……歷史上","examples":[{"en":"It was the largest rescue in the history of surf bathing.","zh":"這是海中暢泳歷史上最大規模的救援。"},{"en":"In the history of something means within the full recorded past of that activity, place, or field.","zh":"in the history of something 指在某活動、地方或領域的完整歷史紀錄中。"},{"en":"A school may celebrate the highest exam result in the history of the campus.","zh":"學校可能慶祝校史上最高的考試成績。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an event is exceptional when compared with everything before it.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事件與之前所有事件相比非常突出。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing records and major milestones.","zh":"描述紀錄和重大里程碑時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"confirm the place of","meaning":"確立……的地位","examples":[{"en":"The rescue confirmed the place of lifesavers in Australian culture.","zh":"這次救援確立了救生員在澳洲文化中的地位。"},{"en":"To confirm the place of someone means to strengthen or prove their importance in a culture, system, or memory.","zh":"confirm the place of someone 指加強或證明某人在文化、系統或記憶中的重要性。"},{"en":"A brave teacher’s actions may confirm the place of educators as community protectors.","zh":"勇敢老師的行動可能確立教育工作者作為社區守護者的地位。"},{"en":"After a major rescue, lifesavers may become symbols of courage and service.","zh":"重大救援後，救生員可能成為勇氣和服務的象徵。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an event secures someone’s cultural role.","zh":"當事件確立某人的文化角色時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"national imagination","meaning":"國民集體想像","examples":[{"en":"The lifesaver became an important figure in the national imagination.","zh":"救生員成為國民集體想像中的重要人物。"},{"en":"National imagination means the shared images, stories, and symbols through which a nation sees itself.","zh":"national imagination 指一個國家用來看待自身的共同圖像、故事和象徵。"},{"en":"A firefighter may become part of the national imagination after being linked with bravery and service.","zh":"消防員如果與勇氣和服務連繫起來，可能成為國民集體想像的一部分。"},{"en":"When a figure enters the national imagination, people see them as representing wider values.","zh":"當某人物進入國民集體想像，人們會把他視為代表更廣泛價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing culture, identity, and symbolism.","zh":"討論文化、身份和象徵時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"endpoint of","meaning":"……的終點","examples":[{"en":"Bondi Beach is the endpoint of the annual City to Surf Fun Run.","zh":"邦迪海灘是一年一度 City to Surf Fun Run 的終點。"},{"en":"The endpoint of something is the place where a route, race, or process finishes.","zh":"endpoint of something 指路線、比賽或過程結束的地方。"},{"en":"A school gate may be the endpoint of a charity walk.","zh":"學校大門可能是慈善步行的終點。"},{"en":"Choosing a famous endpoint can make an event feel more exciting and memorable.","zh":"選擇著名終點可以令活動更刺激和令人記得。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing races, journeys, or routes.","zh":"描述比賽、旅程或路線時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be held each year","meaning":"每年舉行","examples":[{"en":"The City to Surf Fun Run is held each year in August.","zh":"City to Surf Fun Run 每年八月舉行。"},{"en":"Be held each year means be organised annually.","zh":"be held each year 指每年被舉辦一次。"},{"en":"A school sports day is held each year so students can compete and celebrate together.","zh":"學校運動會每年舉行，讓學生一起比賽和慶祝。"},{"en":"Annual events build tradition because people expect them to return at the same time.","zh":"年度活動會建立傳統，因為人們期待它在同一時間再次出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing recurring events.","zh":"描述定期重複活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"surf carnivals","meaning":"海灘嘉年華","examples":[{"en":"Australian surf carnivals strengthened Bondi’s cultural image.","zh":"澳洲海灘嘉年華加強了邦迪的文化形象。"},{"en":"Surf carnivals are beach events involving surf sports, lifesaving competitions, displays, and public celebration.","zh":"surf carnivals 指涉及海浪運動、救生比賽、表演和公眾慶祝的海灘活動。"},{"en":"Families may attend surf carnivals to watch races and enjoy seaside entertainment.","zh":"家庭可能參加海灘嘉年華，觀看比賽並享受海邊娛樂。"},{"en":"Such events can make a beach feel like a national playground and sporting centre.","zh":"這類活動可以令海灘感覺像國家遊樂場和體育中心。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing beach culture and public events.","zh":"討論海灘文化和公共活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"instil an image","meaning":"深植某種形象","examples":[{"en":"Surf carnivals further instilled the image of Bondi as a national playground.","zh":"海灘嘉年華進一步深植邦迪作為國家遊樂場的形象。"},{"en":"To instil an image means to gradually plant or strengthen a particular picture in people’s minds.","zh":"instil an image 指逐漸在人們心中植入或強化某種圖像。"},{"en":"School posters can instil an image of reading as fun and social.","zh":"學校海報可以深植閱讀有趣且具社交性的形象。"},{"en":"Repeated events and advertisements can shape how the public imagines a place.","zh":"反覆出現的活動和廣告可以塑造公眾如何想像某地。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing reputation and cultural branding.","zh":"討論聲譽和文化品牌塑造時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Royal Surf Carnival","meaning":"皇家海灘嘉年華","examples":[{"en":"A Royal Surf Carnival was held during Queen Elizabeth II’s visit.","zh":"在英女王伊利沙伯二世訪問期間，舉行了一場皇家海灘嘉年華。"},{"en":"A Royal Surf Carnival is a surf carnival connected with a royal visit or royal occasion.","zh":"Royal Surf Carnival 指與皇室訪問或皇室場合有關的海灘嘉年華。"},{"en":"A city may organise a special public event when an important visitor arrives.","zh":"當重要訪客到訪，城市可能舉辦特別公共活動。"},{"en":"Linking a beach event with royalty can increase public attention and historical importance.","zh":"把海灘活動與皇室連結起來，可以增加公眾關注和歷史重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing ceremonial beach events.","zh":"討論儀式性海灘活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"during her first visit","meaning":"在她首次訪問期間","examples":[{"en":"The carnival took place during the Queen’s first visit to Australia.","zh":"嘉年華在女王首次訪問澳洲期間舉行。"},{"en":"During her first visit means while she was visiting a place for the first time.","zh":"during her first visit 指在她第一次到訪某地期間。"},{"en":"A mayor may open a new library during her first visit to a district.","zh":"市長可能在她首次訪問某區期間開幕一座新圖書館。"},{"en":"Events held during a first visit often receive extra attention because the occasion feels historic.","zh":"在首次訪問期間舉行的活動常獲得額外關注，因為場合感覺具歷史意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when placing an event within someone’s visit.","zh":"把事件放在某人訪問期間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a member of the British Royal Family","meaning":"英國皇室成員","examples":[{"en":"Many members of the British Royal Family have visited Australia.","zh":"許多英國皇室成員曾訪問澳洲。"},{"en":"A member of the British Royal Family is a person who belongs to Britain’s royal household.","zh":"member of the British Royal Family 指屬於英國皇室家族的人。"},{"en":"A city may prepare special security when a member of the British Royal Family visits.","zh":"當英國皇室成員到訪，城市可能準備特別保安。"},{"en":"Royal visits can attract crowds, media attention, and ceremonial events.","zh":"皇室訪問可以吸引群眾、媒體關注和儀式活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing royal visits and public ceremonies.","zh":"討論皇室訪問和公共儀式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in addition to","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"In addition to sporting events, Bondi hosts weekly markets.","zh":"除了體育活動之外，邦迪還舉辦每週市集。"},{"en":"In addition to means besides or as well as something already mentioned.","zh":"in addition to 指除了已提到的某事之外。"},{"en":"In addition to homework, students should read English for pleasure.","zh":"除了功課之外，學生也應為興趣閱讀英文。"},{"en":"This phrase helps add extra information without replacing the first point.","zh":"這個短語幫助加入額外資料，而不是取代第一點。"},{"en":"It is useful when listing more than one feature or activity.","zh":"列出多於一項特徵或活動時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Bondi Beach Markets","meaning":"邦迪海灘市集","examples":[{"en":"The Bondi Beach Markets are open every Sunday.","zh":"邦迪海灘市集每逢星期日開放。"},{"en":"Bondi Beach Markets are regular markets near Bondi Beach where people can shop, browse, and socialise.","zh":"Bondi Beach Markets 指邦迪海灘附近定期舉行、讓人購物、閒逛和社交的市集。"},{"en":"Visitors may go to Bondi Beach Markets to buy clothes, crafts, food, or gifts.","zh":"遊客可能到邦迪海灘市集購買衣服、手工藝品、食物或禮物。"},{"en":"Weekly markets can add local character to a tourist area.","zh":"每週市集可以為旅遊區增添本地特色。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing community events and beach tourism.","zh":"討論社區活動和海灘旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"wealthy visitors","meaning":"富裕遊客","examples":[{"en":"Many wealthy visitors spend Christmas Day at the beach.","zh":"許多富裕遊客在海灘度過聖誕節。"},{"en":"Wealthy visitors are tourists or guests who have a lot of money to spend.","zh":"wealthy visitors 指有很多錢可消費的遊客或訪客。"},{"en":"A luxury hotel may design expensive packages for wealthy visitors.","zh":"豪華酒店可能為富裕遊客設計昂貴套票。"},{"en":"When wealthy visitors arrive, property prices and local businesses may change.","zh":"當富裕遊客到來，樓價和本地商業可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing tourism, class, and spending power.","zh":"討論旅遊、階級和消費能力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a shortage of housing","meaning":"房屋短缺","examples":[{"en":"A shortage of housing developed as more people moved towards the seaside.","zh":"隨着更多人搬向海邊，房屋短缺出現了。"},{"en":"A shortage of housing happens when there are not enough homes for the number of people who want to live somewhere.","zh":"shortage of housing 指某地可供居住的房屋不足以滿足想住在那裏的人數。"},{"en":"A university town may face a shortage of housing when many new students arrive.","zh":"當大量新學生到來，大學城可能面對房屋短缺。"},{"en":"Housing shortages can raise rent, crowd homes, and push poorer residents away.","zh":"房屋短缺可以推高租金、令住所擠迫，並迫使較貧窮居民離開。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing urban growth and accommodation problems.","zh":"討論城市增長和住宿問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"large numbers of people","meaning":"大量人口","examples":[{"en":"Large numbers of people crowded into coastal areas.","zh":"大量人口湧入海岸地區。"},{"en":"Large numbers of people means many people, often enough to create pressure or visible change.","zh":"large numbers of people 指許多人，通常多到造成壓力或明顯變化。"},{"en":"Large numbers of people may use public transport after a concert ends.","zh":"演唱會結束後，大量人口可能使用公共交通。"},{"en":"When many people move to one area, demand for housing, shops, and services rises.","zh":"當許多人搬到同一地區，對住屋、商店和服務的需求會上升。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing population pressure.","zh":"描述人口壓力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"crowd to the seaside","meaning":"湧往海邊","examples":[{"en":"People crowded to the seaside in search of a healthier lifestyle.","zh":"人們為尋求較健康的生活方式而湧往海邊。"},{"en":"To crowd to the seaside means many people move or travel toward the coast at the same time.","zh":"crowd to the seaside 指許多人同時移居或前往海岸地區。"},{"en":"Families may crowd to the seaside during a heatwave to escape the city.","zh":"熱浪期間，家庭可能湧往海邊逃離城市。"},{"en":"When people crowd to one area, transport, housing, and public space can become strained.","zh":"當人們湧向一個地區，交通、住屋和公共空間可能承受壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing mass movement toward coastal places.","zh":"描述大量人群前往海岸地方時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"seaside town","meaning":"海濱小鎮","examples":[{"en":"Manly is another well-known seaside town near Sydney.","zh":"Manly 是悉尼附近另一個知名海濱小鎮。"},{"en":"A seaside town is a town located beside the sea, often with beaches, tourism, and leisure activities.","zh":"seaside town 指位於海邊的城鎮，通常有海灘、旅遊和休閒活動。"},{"en":"A seaside town may have hotels, seafood restaurants, souvenir shops, and walking paths.","zh":"海濱小鎮可能有酒店、海鮮餐廳、紀念品店和步行徑。"},{"en":"Seaside towns often grow when people want holidays, fresh air, and sea views.","zh":"當人們想度假、呼吸新鮮空氣和看海景，海濱小鎮常會發展起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing coastal settlements.","zh":"描述海岸聚居地時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"address a problem","meaning":"處理問題","examples":[{"en":"Manly took steps to address the shortage of accommodation.","zh":"Manly 採取措施處理住宿短缺問題。"},{"en":"To address a problem means to deal with it directly and try to solve it.","zh":"address a problem 指直接處理問題並試圖解決它。"},{"en":"A school may address a bullying problem by improving supervision and counselling.","zh":"學校可能透過加強監管和輔導來處理欺凌問題。"},{"en":"Ignoring a problem usually allows it to grow worse.","zh":"忽視問題通常會讓它惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing practical action.","zh":"討論實際行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"preferred destination","meaning":"首選目的地","examples":[{"en":"Bondi remained the preferred destination for many visitors.","zh":"邦迪仍然是許多遊客的首選目的地。"},{"en":"A preferred destination is the place people choose over other possible places.","zh":"preferred destination 指人們在其他可能地方之中選擇的地方。"},{"en":"A quiet library may be the preferred destination for students who need to study before exams.","zh":"對考試前需要溫習的學生來說，安靜圖書館可能是首選目的地。"},{"en":"A destination remains preferred when people see it as more attractive, convenient, or meaningful.","zh":"當人們認為某目的地更吸引、方便或有意義，它就會維持首選地位。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing choices in travel or leisure.","zh":"比較旅遊或休閒選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Many visitors chose Bondi rather than Manly.","zh":"許多遊客選擇邦迪，而不是 Manly。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of or in preference to another option.","zh":"rather than 指而不是，或比另一選項更偏好。"},{"en":"A student may choose the bus rather than the train if the bus stops closer to home.","zh":"如果巴士站離家較近，學生可能選擇巴士而不是火車。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a contrast between two choices clear.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示兩個選擇之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining preference or replacement.","zh":"解釋偏好或取代時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"commercial area","meaning":"商業區","examples":[{"en":"Bondi has a busy commercial area along Campbell Parade.","zh":"邦迪在 Campbell Parade 沿線有一個繁忙商業區。"},{"en":"A commercial area is a district with shops, restaurants, offices, and other businesses.","zh":"commercial area 指有商店、餐廳、辦公室和其他商業活動的地區。"},{"en":"A commercial area near a station may be crowded during lunch time.","zh":"車站附近的商業區可能在午飯時間很擁擠。"},{"en":"Tourism can make a beachside commercial area busier and more expensive.","zh":"旅遊業可以令海邊商業區更繁忙和更昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing business activity in a place.","zh":"描述某地商業活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"adjacent side streets","meaning":"相鄰橫街","examples":[{"en":"Cafes and restaurants also occupy adjacent side streets.","zh":"咖啡店和餐廳也佔據相鄰橫街。"},{"en":"Adjacent side streets are smaller streets next to or near a main road.","zh":"adjacent side streets 指位於主要道路旁邊或附近的小街。"},{"en":"A popular bakery may be hidden in one of the adjacent side streets behind a shopping centre.","zh":"一間受歡迎麵包店可能藏在購物中心後面其中一條相鄰橫街。"},{"en":"Businesses spread into side streets when the main street becomes crowded or expensive.","zh":"當主街變得擁擠或昂貴，商業會擴展到橫街。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a local street layout.","zh":"描述本地街道佈局時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"feature popular cafes","meaning":"設有受歡迎的咖啡店","examples":[{"en":"The commercial district features many popular cafes and restaurants.","zh":"這個商業區設有許多受歡迎的咖啡店和餐廳。"},{"en":"To feature popular cafes means to include well-liked places where people can drink, eat, and socialise.","zh":"feature popular cafes 指包含人們喜歡用來飲食和社交的咖啡店。"},{"en":"A university neighbourhood may feature popular cafes where students study after class.","zh":"大學社區可能設有受歡迎的咖啡店，讓學生課後溫習。"},{"en":"Popular cafes can make an area feel lively and attract visitors who are not only going to the beach.","zh":"受歡迎的咖啡店可以令地區更有活力，並吸引不只是去海灘的人。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing local attractions and business life.","zh":"描述本地景點和商業生活時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"views of the beach","meaning":"海灘景觀","examples":[{"en":"Many hotels and restaurants offer views of the beach.","zh":"許多酒店和餐廳提供海灘景觀。"},{"en":"Views of the beach are sights or visual outlooks looking toward the sand, sea, and coastline.","zh":"views of the beach 指望向沙灘、海洋和海岸線的景觀。"},{"en":"A restaurant with views of the beach may charge more for window seats.","zh":"有海灘景觀的餐廳可能對窗邊座位收取更高價格。"},{"en":"Sea views increase demand because people enjoy eating, staying, or relaxing near beautiful scenery.","zh":"海景會增加需求，因為人們喜歡在美麗景色旁用餐、住宿或放鬆。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing tourism and property value.","zh":"討論旅遊和物業價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"contemporary beach","meaning":"現代化海灘","examples":[{"en":"Modern businesses overlook the contemporary beach.","zh":"現代商業場所俯瞰這片現代化海灘。"},{"en":"A contemporary beach is a modern beach environment shaped by current tourism, business, design, and leisure culture.","zh":"contemporary beach 指由當代旅遊、商業、設計和休閒文化塑造的現代海灘環境。"},{"en":"A contemporary beach may include cafés, hotels, markets, fitness activities, and public events.","zh":"現代化海灘可能包括咖啡店、酒店、市集、健身活動和公共活動。"},{"en":"Modern development can make a beach more convenient but may also change its older character.","zh":"現代發展可以令海灘更方便，但也可能改變其舊有特色。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting present-day beach culture with the past.","zh":"對比現今海灘文化與過去時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be depicted as","meaning":"被描繪為","examples":[{"en":"Bondi is sometimes depicted as wholly modern and European.","zh":"邦迪有時被描繪為完全現代化和歐洲化。"},{"en":"Be depicted as means be shown or described in a particular way.","zh":"be depicted as 指以某種方式被呈現或描述。"},{"en":"A city may be depicted as crowded in one film but peaceful in another.","zh":"一座城市在一部電影中可能被描繪為擁擠，在另一部中則被描繪為平靜。"},{"en":"How a place is depicted can affect what visitors expect before arriving.","zh":"一個地方如何被描繪，可以影響遊客到達前的期望。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing representation in writing, media, or advertising.","zh":"討論寫作、媒體或廣告中的呈現方式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"wholly modern and European","meaning":"完全現代化和歐洲化","examples":[{"en":"The area is often presented as wholly modern and European in character.","zh":"該區常被呈現為完全現代化和歐洲化。"},{"en":"Wholly modern and European means completely shaped by modern design and European-style culture or architecture.","zh":"wholly modern and European 指完全由現代設計和歐洲式文化或建築特色塑造。"},{"en":"A shopping district may look wholly modern and European if it has glass cafés, stylish apartments, and imported design styles.","zh":"如果購物區有玻璃咖啡店、時尚住宅和外來設計風格，它可能看似完全現代化和歐洲化。"},{"en":"Such a description can overlook older Indigenous history and local cultural layers.","zh":"這種描述可能忽略較古老的原住民歷史和本地文化層次。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how a place’s image may be simplified.","zh":"討論地方形象如何被簡化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in the last decade","meaning":"在過去十年間","examples":[{"en":"Property development increased sharply in the last decade.","zh":"在過去十年間，物業發展大幅增加。"},{"en":"In the last decade means during the most recent ten-year period being discussed.","zh":"in the last decade 指在所討論的最近十年期間。"},{"en":"In the last decade, many neighbourhoods have changed because of new transport links.","zh":"在過去十年間，許多社區因新交通連接而改變。"},{"en":"A sharp change within ten years can make older residents feel the area has transformed quickly.","zh":"十年內的急劇變化可以令舊居民覺得地區轉變很快。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing recent trends.","zh":"描述近期趨勢時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"unique position","meaning":"獨特位置","examples":[{"en":"Bondi’s unique coastal position has increased demand for property.","zh":"邦迪獨特的海岸位置增加了物業需求。"},{"en":"A unique position is a special location or situation that gives a place advantages not easily found elsewhere.","zh":"unique position 指一個特別位置或情況，令某地擁有其他地方不易找到的優勢。"},{"en":"A shop near both a school and a train station has a unique position for attracting customers.","zh":"同時靠近學校和火車站的商店，有吸引顧客的獨特位置。"},{"en":"When a place has a unique position, demand may rise because people cannot easily find an alternative.","zh":"當地方有獨特位置，需求可能上升，因為人們難以找到替代選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why a location is valuable.","zh":"解釋地點為何有價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"see a dramatic rise in","meaning":"見證……大幅增加","examples":[{"en":"The area has seen a dramatic rise in stylish houses and apartments.","zh":"該區見證時尚房屋和住宅單位大幅增加。"},{"en":"See a dramatic rise in something means experience a large and noticeable increase.","zh":"see a dramatic rise in something 指經歷巨大而明顯的增加。"},{"en":"A school may see a dramatic rise in applications after its exam results improve.","zh":"學校考試成績改善後，可能見證申請人數大幅增加。"},{"en":"A dramatic rise in housing development can change the look and affordability of a neighbourhood.","zh":"房屋發展大幅增加可以改變社區外觀和負擔能力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing strong growth.","zh":"描述強勁增長時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"stylish houses and apartments","meaning":"時尚的房屋和住宅單位","examples":[{"en":"Stylish houses and apartments have been built near the beach.","zh":"海灘附近興建了時尚的房屋和住宅單位。"},{"en":"Stylish houses and apartments are attractive, fashionable homes designed to look modern or elegant.","zh":"stylish houses and apartments 指外觀吸引、時尚、設計現代或優雅的住宅。"},{"en":"A developer may build stylish apartments with sea views, balconies, and open kitchens.","zh":"發展商可能建造有海景、露台和開放式廚房的時尚住宅單位。"},{"en":"Stylish housing can attract wealthy buyers and raise property prices.","zh":"時尚住宅可以吸引富裕買家並推高樓價。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing modern residential development.","zh":"討論現代住宅發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take advantage of","meaning":"充分利用","examples":[{"en":"Developers built coastal properties to take advantage of the views.","zh":"發展商興建海岸物業，以充分利用景觀。"},{"en":"To take advantage of something means to use a good opportunity or useful feature for benefit.","zh":"take advantage of something 指利用好機會或有用特徵來取得好處。"},{"en":"A student may take advantage of a quiet morning to finish difficult homework.","zh":"學生可能充分利用安靜早上完成困難功課。"},{"en":"Developers take advantage of sea views because buyers are willing to pay more for them.","zh":"發展商充分利用海景，因為買家願意為海景付更多錢。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone uses favourable conditions.","zh":"當某人利用有利條件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the scent of the sea","meaning":"海洋氣息","examples":[{"en":"Residents can enjoy the views and scent of the sea.","zh":"居民可以享受景觀和海洋氣息。"},{"en":"The scent of the sea is the smell of salt water, sea air, and the coastline.","zh":"scent of the sea 指鹹水、海風和海岸線的氣味。"},{"en":"People may enjoy the scent of the sea while walking along a beach at sunrise.","zh":"人們可能在日出時沿海灘散步，享受海洋氣息。"},{"en":"Pleasant sea air can make coastal living feel relaxing and healthy.","zh":"宜人的海風可以令海岸生活感覺放鬆和健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the sensory appeal of seaside life.","zh":"描述海濱生活的感官吸引力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"valley running down to the beach","meaning":"向海灘伸延的山谷","examples":[{"en":"The valley running down to the beach offers a distinctive view.","zh":"向海灘伸延的山谷提供獨特景觀。"},{"en":"A valley running down to the beach is a low stretch of land sloping toward the shore.","zh":"valley running down to the beach 指一段向海岸傾斜的低地或山谷。"},{"en":"A road through a valley running down to the beach may give drivers a sudden view of the sea.","zh":"穿過向海灘伸延山谷的道路，可能讓司機突然看見大海。"},{"en":"Landform shapes how people see and experience a coastal place.","zh":"地形會塑造人們如何觀看和體驗海岸地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing coastal geography.","zh":"描述海岸地理時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be famous the world over","meaning":"聞名全球","examples":[{"en":"The Bondi landscape is famous the world over.","zh":"邦迪景觀聞名全球。"},{"en":"Be famous the world over means be known in many countries around the world.","zh":"be famous the world over 指在世界許多國家都為人所知。"},{"en":"A singer may become famous the world over after one song spreads online.","zh":"歌手可能因一首歌在網上傳播而聞名全球。"},{"en":"International fame brings visitors, media attention, and commercial value.","zh":"國際知名度會帶來遊客、媒體關注和商業價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing global recognition.","zh":"描述全球知名度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"distinctive red-tiled roofs","meaning":"獨特的紅瓦屋頂","examples":[{"en":"The area is known for its distinctive red-tiled roofs.","zh":"該區以獨特的紅瓦屋頂聞名。"},{"en":"Distinctive red-tiled roofs are easily recognised roofs covered with red tiles.","zh":"distinctive red-tiled roofs 指容易被辨認、覆蓋紅色瓦片的屋頂。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood with distinctive roofs can be identified quickly in photographs.","zh":"有獨特屋頂的社區可以在照片中很快被認出。"},{"en":"Architectural details such as roof colour help create a place’s visual identity.","zh":"屋頂顏色等建築細節有助創造地方的視覺身份。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing local architecture.","zh":"描述本地建築時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be deeply influenced by","meaning":"深受……影響","examples":[{"en":"Bondi’s architecture is deeply influenced by British coastal towns.","zh":"邦迪的建築深受英國海濱城鎮影響。"},{"en":"Be deeply influenced by means be strongly shaped by something.","zh":"be deeply influenced by 指受到某事強烈塑造。"},{"en":"A student’s writing may be deeply influenced by books they read as a child.","zh":"學生的寫作可能深受童年閱讀的書影響。"},{"en":"Strong influence can appear in design, language, habits, or values.","zh":"強烈影響可以出現在設計、語言、習慣或價值觀中。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining where a style comes from.","zh":"解釋風格來源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"British coastal towns","meaning":"英國海濱城鎮","examples":[{"en":"The red-roofed buildings resemble those in British coastal towns.","zh":"這些紅屋頂建築像英國海濱城鎮中的建築。"},{"en":"British coastal towns are seaside towns in Britain, often associated with beaches, promenades, hotels, and holiday culture.","zh":"British coastal towns 指英國的海濱城鎮，常與海灘、海濱大道、酒店和度假文化有關。"},{"en":"A British coastal town may have old guesthouses, fish-and-chip shops, and sea views.","zh":"英國海濱城鎮可能有舊旅館、炸魚薯條店和海景。"},{"en":"If Bondi buildings resemble British coastal towns, colonial architectural influence may be visible.","zh":"如果邦迪建築像英國海濱城鎮，就可能看見殖民建築影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing seaside architecture.","zh":"比較海濱建築時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"host a competition","meaning":"主辦比賽","examples":[{"en":"Bondi Beach hosted an Olympic beach volleyball competition.","zh":"邦迪海灘主辦了一項奧運沙灘排球比賽。"},{"en":"To host a competition means to provide the place and organisation for a contest to take place.","zh":"host a competition 指提供場地和組織安排，讓比賽舉行。"},{"en":"A school may host a debate competition for students from several districts.","zh":"學校可能主辦來自幾個地區學生的辯論比賽。"},{"en":"Hosting a competition can bring visitors, media coverage, and temporary facilities.","zh":"主辦比賽可以帶來遊客、媒體報道和臨時設施。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing events held at a venue.","zh":"討論在某場地舉行的活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"beach volleyball competition","meaning":"沙灘排球比賽","examples":[{"en":"The beach volleyball competition took place during the 2000 Olympics.","zh":"沙灘排球比賽在2000年奧運期間舉行。"},{"en":"A beach volleyball competition is a sporting event in which teams play volleyball on sand.","zh":"beach volleyball competition 指隊伍在沙地上進行排球比賽的體育活動。"},{"en":"A beach volleyball competition needs sand courts, nets, referees, players, and spectators.","zh":"沙灘排球比賽需要沙地球場、球網、裁判、球員和觀眾。"},{"en":"Holding the sport on a famous beach can make the event more visually memorable.","zh":"在著名海灘舉行該運動，可以令活動在視覺上更令人記得。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing seaside sporting events.","zh":"討論海濱體育活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"temporary stadium","meaning":"臨時運動場","examples":[{"en":"A temporary stadium was constructed on the beach.","zh":"一座臨時運動場在海灘上建成。"},{"en":"A temporary stadium is a sports venue built for short-term use and removed after the event.","zh":"temporary stadium 指為短期使用而建，活動後會拆除的體育場地。"},{"en":"A city may build a temporary stadium for a festival, concert, or international match.","zh":"城市可能為節日、演唱會或國際賽事建造臨時運動場。"},{"en":"Temporary stadiums can solve event needs but may disturb public space during construction.","zh":"臨時運動場可以滿足活動需要，但施工期間可能干擾公共空間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing short-term event infrastructure.","zh":"討論短期活動基建時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ten-thousand-seat stadium","meaning":"可容納一萬人的運動場","examples":[{"en":"The event required a temporary ten-thousand-seat stadium.","zh":"這項活動需要一座臨時可容納一萬人的運動場。"},{"en":"A ten-thousand-seat stadium is a venue with space for 10,000 spectators.","zh":"ten-thousand-seat stadium 指有一萬個觀眾座位的場地。"},{"en":"A concert organiser may need a ten-thousand-seat stadium if demand for tickets is high.","zh":"如果門票需求很高，演唱會主辦方可能需要可容納一萬人的場地。"},{"en":"Large seating capacity can bring crowds but also requires transport, safety, and crowd-control planning.","zh":"大座位容量可以帶來人潮，但也需要交通、安全和人流控制規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the scale of a sports venue.","zh":"描述體育場地規模時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"warm-up courts","meaning":"熱身場地","examples":[{"en":"Two warm-up courts were created for the tournament.","zh":"該賽事設置了兩個熱身場地。"},{"en":"Warm-up courts are practice courts where athletes prepare before competition.","zh":"warm-up courts 指運動員比賽前準備和練習的球場。"},{"en":"Players may use warm-up courts to stretch, practise serves, and adjust to the sand.","zh":"球員可能使用熱身場地伸展、練習發球並適應沙地。"},{"en":"Warm-up areas help athletes perform safely and confidently in the main event.","zh":"熱身區幫助運動員在正式比賽中更安全和有信心地表現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing sports facilities.","zh":"討論體育設施時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"training courts","meaning":"訓練場地","examples":[{"en":"Three training courts were also set up.","zh":"另外還設置了三個訓練場地。"},{"en":"Training courts are courts used for athletes to practise and prepare for competition.","zh":"training courts 指運動員練習和準備比賽的球場。"},{"en":"A tennis tournament may provide training courts so players can practise between matches.","zh":"網球賽事可能提供訓練場地，讓球員在賽事之間練習。"},{"en":"Training courts reduce pressure on the main competition court.","zh":"訓練場地可以減輕正式比賽場地的壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing sports preparation facilities.","zh":"描述體育準備設施時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be set up to host","meaning":"為舉辦……而設立","examples":[{"en":"Several temporary facilities were set up to host the tournament.","zh":"多項臨時設施為舉辦該錦標賽而設立。"},{"en":"Be set up to host something means be arranged or built so an event can take place.","zh":"be set up to host something 指被安排或建造，以便某活動能舉行。"},{"en":"A school hall may be set up to host an exam by adding desks, signs, and clocks.","zh":"學校禮堂可能透過加設桌子、指示牌和時鐘，為舉辦考試而設置。"},{"en":"Temporary facilities are often set up when a place normally serves a different purpose.","zh":"當一個地方平時用途不同，臨時設施常會被設置起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing event preparation.","zh":"討論活動準備時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stand for just six weeks","meaning":"只存在六星期","examples":[{"en":"The temporary stadium stood for just six weeks.","zh":"這座臨時運動場只存在六星期。"},{"en":"Stand for just six weeks means remain built or in place for only six weeks.","zh":"stand for just six weeks 指只維持建成或設置狀態六星期。"},{"en":"A festival stage may stand for just one weekend before being removed.","zh":"節日舞台可能只存在一個週末，之後就被拆除。"},{"en":"Short-term structures can still create disruption while they exist.","zh":"短期結構即使存在時間短，仍可能造成干擾。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing temporary construction.","zh":"描述臨時建設時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"campaigners","meaning":"社會運動人士","examples":[{"en":"Campaigners opposed the planned development.","zh":"社會運動人士反對計劃中的發展項目。"},{"en":"Campaigners are people who actively work to support or oppose a public issue.","zh":"campaigners 指積極支持或反對公共議題的人。"},{"en":"Campaigners may collect signatures, speak to the media, and attend public meetings.","zh":"社會運動人士可能收集簽名、向媒體發言並參加公眾會議。"},{"en":"Campaigners often act when they believe a place, right, or community is at risk.","zh":"當他們相信某地方、權利或社區受威脅時，社會運動人士常會行動。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing social movements and public protest.","zh":"討論社會運動和公眾抗議時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"oppose the consequences of","meaning":"反對……所帶來的後果","examples":[{"en":"Campaigners opposed the social and environmental consequences of the stadium.","zh":"社會運動人士反對該運動場所帶來的社會及環境後果。"},{"en":"To oppose the consequences of something means to object to the results or damage it may cause.","zh":"oppose the consequences of something 指反對某事可能造成的結果或傷害。"},{"en":"Residents may oppose the consequences of a new highway if it brings noise and pollution.","zh":"如果新公路帶來噪音和污染，居民可能反對它所帶來的後果。"},{"en":"People may not oppose an event itself, but they may oppose the harm caused by its construction.","zh":"人們未必反對活動本身，但可能反對其建設造成的傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when protest focuses on effects rather than the idea alone.","zh":"當抗議聚焦於影響而不只是理念本身時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"social and environmental consequences","meaning":"社會及環境後果","examples":[{"en":"The development had potential social and environmental consequences.","zh":"該發展項目有潛在社會及環境後果。"},{"en":"Social and environmental consequences are effects on people, communities, land, water, wildlife, or public space.","zh":"social and environmental consequences 指對人、社區、土地、水、野生生物或公共空間造成的影響。"},{"en":"A new airport may have social and environmental consequences such as noise, relocation, and habitat loss.","zh":"新機場可能有噪音、搬遷和棲息地流失等社會及環境後果。"},{"en":"Considering these consequences helps planners avoid harming residents or nature.","zh":"考慮這些後果有助規劃者避免傷害居民或自然環境。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the wider impact of development.","zh":"討論發展的更廣泛影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"divide the beach in two","meaning":"將海灘一分為二","examples":[{"en":"The stadium would have divided the beach in two.","zh":"該運動場會將海灘一分為二。"},{"en":"To divide the beach in two means to split the beach into two separate parts.","zh":"divide the beach in two 指把海灘分成兩個分隔部分。"},{"en":"A temporary fence can divide a playground in two and stop children from using the whole space.","zh":"臨時圍欄可以把遊樂場一分為二，阻止孩子使用整個空間。"},{"en":"Dividing a beach can reduce public movement and change how people enjoy the area.","zh":"把海灘分開可以減少公眾流動，並改變人們享用該區的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when construction cuts through shared space.","zh":"當建設切開共享空間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"seriously restrict public access","meaning":"嚴重限制公眾使用權","examples":[{"en":"The development would seriously restrict public access to the beach.","zh":"該發展項目會嚴重限制公眾使用海灘的權利。"},{"en":"Seriously restrict public access means greatly limit ordinary people’s ability to enter or use a place.","zh":"seriously restrict public access 指大大限制普通人進入或使用某地的能力。"},{"en":"A locked gate can seriously restrict public access to a riverside path.","zh":"上鎖閘門可以嚴重限制公眾使用河邊小徑。"},{"en":"When access is restricted, a place may feel less democratic and less shared.","zh":"當使用權受限制，地方可能感覺較不民主、較不共享。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing threats to public space.","zh":"討論公共空間受到威脅時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"outdoor recreation","meaning":"戶外康樂活動","examples":[{"en":"Swimming and walking are popular forms of outdoor recreation.","zh":"游泳和散步是受歡迎的戶外康樂活動。"},{"en":"Outdoor recreation means leisure activities done outside, especially in natural or open spaces.","zh":"outdoor recreation 指在戶外，尤其在自然或開放空間中進行的休閒活動。"},{"en":"Hiking, cycling, swimming, and picnicking are forms of outdoor recreation.","zh":"行山、踩單車、游泳和野餐都是戶外康樂活動。"},{"en":"Outdoor recreation supports health because people move, relax, and spend time in fresh air.","zh":"戶外康樂活動有助健康，因為人們活動身體、放鬆並呼吸新鮮空氣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing public parks, beaches, and healthy lifestyles.","zh":"討論公園、海灘和健康生活方式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"protest for their right to","meaning":"為爭取……權利而抗議","examples":[{"en":"Residents protested for their right to an unspoilt seaside.","zh":"居民為爭取擁有未受破壞海濱的權利而抗議。"},{"en":"To protest for their right to something means to publicly demand protection of something they believe they should have.","zh":"protest for their right to something 指公開要求保護他們認為應該擁有的東西。"},{"en":"Residents may protest for their right to clean air if a factory pollutes the area.","zh":"如果工廠污染該區，居民可能為爭取清潔空氣的權利而抗議。"},{"en":"Protests often happen when people feel official decisions threaten shared rights.","zh":"當人們覺得官方決定威脅共享權利，抗議常會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when public action is linked to rights.","zh":"當公共行動與權利有關時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unspoilt seaside","meaning":"未受破壞的海濱","examples":[{"en":"Campaigners wanted to preserve an unspoilt seaside.","zh":"社會運動人士希望保護未受破壞的海濱。"},{"en":"An unspoilt seaside is a coastal area that remains natural, clean, open, and not damaged by excessive development.","zh":"unspoilt seaside 指仍然自然、乾淨、開放且未被過度發展破壞的海岸地區。"},{"en":"A small beach without large buildings or pollution may feel like an unspoilt seaside.","zh":"沒有大型建築或污染的小海灘可能感覺像未受破壞的海濱。"},{"en":"Once heavy construction begins, an unspoilt seaside can lose its quiet and natural character.","zh":"一旦大型施工開始，未受破壞的海濱可能失去安靜和自然特色。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing conservation of coastal places.","zh":"討論海岸地方保育時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"argue for","meaning":"主張；爭取","examples":[{"en":"Residents argued for a healthy life and an accessible beach.","zh":"居民主張健康生活和可使用的海灘。"},{"en":"To argue for something means to give reasons in support of it.","zh":"argue for something 指提出理由支持某事。"},{"en":"A student may argue for shorter school days by explaining stress and sleep needs.","zh":"學生可能透過解釋壓力和睡眠需要，主張縮短上課日。"},{"en":"People argue for public access when they believe a place should remain open to everyone.","zh":"當人們相信某地方應向所有人開放，他們就會爭取公共使用權。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when presenting a position in a debate.","zh":"在辯論中表達立場時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be prepared to risk","meaning":"願意冒……的風險","examples":[{"en":"Critics claimed that organisers were prepared to risk lives and the environment.","zh":"批評者聲稱主辦方願意冒人命和環境受損的風險。"},{"en":"Be prepared to risk something means be willing to endanger it for another goal.","zh":"be prepared to risk something 指願意為另一目標而使某事物陷入危險。"},{"en":"A company should not be prepared to risk worker safety just to finish a project faster.","zh":"公司不應只為更快完成項目而願意冒工人安全的風險。"},{"en":"If organisers risk public safety or nature, people may see the event as irresponsible.","zh":"如果主辦方冒公眾安全或自然環境的風險，人們可能視活動為不負責任。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when criticising dangerous priorities.","zh":"批評危險優先次序時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"for the sake of","meaning":"為了……","examples":[{"en":"Campaigners opposed risking the beach for the sake of a short tournament.","zh":"社會運動人士反對為了一場短期錦標賽而冒海灘受損的風險。"},{"en":"For the sake of means for the purpose or benefit of something.","zh":"for the sake of 指為了某目的或利益。"},{"en":"Parents may move closer to school for the sake of their children’s education.","zh":"父母可能為了子女教育而搬近學校。"},{"en":"The phrase can show that one value is being sacrificed for another.","zh":"這個短語可以顯示一種價值正被犧牲以換取另一種價值。"},{"en":"It is useful when questioning whether a goal is worth the cost.","zh":"質疑某目標是否值得付出代價時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"construction lawyer","meaning":"建築法律師","examples":[{"en":"Stephen Uniacke was a construction lawyer involved in the campaign.","zh":"Stephen Uniacke 是一名參與該運動的建築法律師。"},{"en":"A construction lawyer is a legal professional who deals with building projects, contracts, planning, and disputes.","zh":"construction lawyer 指處理建築項目、合約、規劃和爭議的法律專業人士。"},{"en":"A construction lawyer may advise residents if a development affects public access.","zh":"如果發展項目影響公眾使用權，建築法律師可能向居民提供意見。"},{"en":"Legal knowledge can help campaigners challenge unsafe or unfair construction plans.","zh":"法律知識可以幫助社會運動人士挑戰不安全或不公平的建設計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing law and building development.","zh":"討論法律和建築發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be involved in","meaning":"參與……","examples":[{"en":"Several local professionals were involved in the campaign.","zh":"幾名本地專業人士參與了該運動。"},{"en":"Be involved in means take part in or have a role in an activity.","zh":"be involved in 指參加某活動或在其中扮演角色。"},{"en":"A parent may be involved in a school fundraising event by helping at a stall.","zh":"家長可能透過協助攤位參與學校籌款活動。"},{"en":"When more people are involved in a campaign, it can gain skills, contacts, and credibility.","zh":"當更多人參與運動，它可以獲得技能、人脈和可信度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing participation.","zh":"描述參與時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"environmental concerns","meaning":"環境方面的憂慮","examples":[{"en":"The stadium proposal raised several environmental concerns.","zh":"運動場提案引起幾項環境方面的憂慮。"},{"en":"Environmental concerns are worries about possible harm to land, water, air, wildlife, or natural systems.","zh":"environmental concerns 指對土地、水、空氣、野生生物或自然系統可能受害的擔憂。"},{"en":"A new road through a forest may raise environmental concerns about habitat loss.","zh":"穿過森林的新道路可能引起關於棲息地流失的環境憂慮。"},{"en":"Environmental concerns can lead to protests, studies, and changes in construction plans.","zh":"環境憂慮可以引發抗議、研究和施工計劃修改。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing development and nature.","zh":"討論發展和自然環境時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"include the possibility that","meaning":"包括……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"The concerns included the possibility that disturbed soil might become acidic.","zh":"這些憂慮包括受擾動土壤可能變酸的可能性。"},{"en":"Include the possibility that means contain a concern or chance that something may happen.","zh":"include the possibility that 指包含某事可能發生的憂慮或機會。"},{"en":"A medical test may include the possibility that symptoms are caused by stress.","zh":"醫學檢查可能包括症狀由壓力引起的可能性。"},{"en":"Considering possible risks helps planners act before damage occurs.","zh":"考慮可能風險有助規劃者在損害發生前行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when listing uncertain but important risks.","zh":"列出不確定但重要的風險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"dredge up","meaning":"挖起；掘出","examples":[{"en":"Construction work could dredge up soil from below the sand.","zh":"施工工程可能從沙層下面挖起土壤。"},{"en":"To dredge up means to dig or bring material up from below a surface, often from water, sand, or earth.","zh":"dredge up 指從表面下挖出或帶出物質，常見於水、沙或泥土中。"},{"en":"Workers may dredge up mud from a harbour to make it deep enough for boats.","zh":"工人可能從港口挖起淤泥，使其深度足夠船隻通行。"},{"en":"Bringing buried material to the surface can create environmental problems if it reacts with air or water.","zh":"把埋藏物質帶到地面，如果它與空氣或水反應，就可能造成環境問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing excavation and hidden material.","zh":"討論挖掘和隱藏物質時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"from below the sand","meaning":"從沙層下面","examples":[{"en":"Potentially harmful soil might be brought up from below the sand.","zh":"可能有害的土壤可能從沙層下面被帶出。"},{"en":"From below the sand means from underneath the sandy surface.","zh":"from below the sand 指從沙表面以下的位置。"},{"en":"Children digging at the beach may find shells from below the sand.","zh":"孩子在海灘挖沙時，可能從沙層下面找到貝殼。"},{"en":"Material buried under sand can behave differently when exposed to air.","zh":"埋在沙下的物質接觸空氣後，可能有不同反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing hidden layers beneath a beach surface.","zh":"描述海灘表面下的隱藏層時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"acidify","meaning":"變酸；酸化","examples":[{"en":"Some buried soil may acidify when exposed to air.","zh":"有些埋藏土壤接觸空氣時可能變酸。"},{"en":"To acidify means to become more acidic or to make something more acidic.","zh":"acidify 指變得更酸，或令某物變得更酸。"},{"en":"Water in a pond may acidify if pollutants change its chemical balance.","zh":"如果污染物改變池塘的化學平衡，池水可能酸化。"},{"en":"Acidic soil can harm plants, water quality, and local ecosystems.","zh":"酸性土壤可以傷害植物、水質和本地生態系統。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing environmental chemistry.","zh":"討論環境化學時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be brought to the surface","meaning":"被帶到地面","examples":[{"en":"Soil may react differently when it is brought to the surface.","zh":"土壤被帶到地面時，反應可能不同。"},{"en":"Be brought to the surface means be moved from underground or underwater to the top layer where it is exposed.","zh":"be brought to the surface 指從地下或水下移到暴露的表層。"},{"en":"Construction can bring old pipes to the surface during road repairs.","zh":"道路維修期間，施工可能把舊水管帶到地面。"},{"en":"Once buried soil is exposed, sunlight, air, and water can change its chemical behaviour.","zh":"一旦埋藏土壤暴露，陽光、空氣和水可以改變其化學行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing excavation and environmental risk.","zh":"討論挖掘和環境風險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"符合文中資料","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether statements agree with the information given in the passage.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否符合文章中提供的資料。"},{"en":"Agree with the information given means match what the passage clearly says or supports.","zh":"agree with the information given 指符合文章清楚說明或支持的內容。"},{"en":"If the text says the club was formed in 1907, the same statement agrees with the information given.","zh":"如果文本說該會於1907年成立，相同陳述就符合文中資料。"},{"en":"Students should check the passage carefully rather than rely on memory or outside knowledge.","zh":"學生應仔細查看文章，而不是依賴記憶或外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN reading questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN 閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文中資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the information in the passage.","zh":"一個陳述可能與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage states.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章所述相反的意思。"},{"en":"If the passage says Bondi is near Sydney, a statement saying it is near Perth contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說邦迪近悉尼，而陳述說它近珀斯，就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be based on the text, not on what a student thinks is likely.","zh":"矛盾必須基於文本，而不是學生覺得可能的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying FALSE answers.","zh":"辨認 FALSE 答案時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"The correct response is used when there is no information on this.","zh":"當文中沒有相關資料時，使用正確回應。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not provide enough evidence to say true or false.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有提供足夠證據判斷真假。"},{"en":"If a text describes a beach but never mentions ticket prices, there is no information on ticket cost.","zh":"如果文本描述海灘但從未提到票價，就沒有關於票價的相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should choose NOT GIVEN when the passage is silent about the point.","zh":"當文章沒有提及某點，學生應選 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading-comprehension questions.","zh":"這個短語適用於閱讀理解題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be first named by","meaning":"最初由……命名","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Bondi Beach was first named by British settlers.","zh":"題目問邦迪海灘是否最初由英國殖民者命名。"},{"en":"Be first named by means receive its earliest known name from a particular person or group.","zh":"be first named by 指由某人或某群體給予最早已知名稱。"},{"en":"A street may be first named by a town council before residents begin using the name daily.","zh":"街道可能先由市議會命名，然後居民才日常使用該名稱。"},{"en":"Asking who first named a place can reveal questions about power, language, and history.","zh":"詢問某地最初由誰命名，可以揭示權力、語言和歷史問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the origin of place names.","zh":"討論地名起源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"British settlers","meaning":"英國殖民者","examples":[{"en":"British settlers arrived in the Sydney region during European colonisation.","zh":"英國殖民者在歐洲殖民期間到達悉尼地區。"},{"en":"British settlers were people from Britain who moved to live permanently in another land, often during colonial expansion.","zh":"British settlers 指從英國遷往另一土地永久居住的人，常見於殖民擴張期間。"},{"en":"British settlers often brought their own laws, farming methods, architecture, and place names.","zh":"英國殖民者常帶來自己的法律、農業方法、建築和地名。"},{"en":"Settlement by outsiders can deeply affect Indigenous communities already living there.","zh":"外來者定居可以深深影響原本居住在當地的原住民社群。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing colonial history.","zh":"討論殖民歷史時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"differ from","meaning":"與……不同","examples":[{"en":"Aboriginal culture differs from European culture in many respects.","zh":"澳洲原住民文化在許多方面與歐洲文化不同。"},{"en":"Differ from means be unlike or not the same as something else.","zh":"differ from 指與某物不相同或有所不同。"},{"en":"School life in a small village may differ from school life in a large city.","zh":"小村莊的學校生活可能與大城市的學校生活不同。"},{"en":"Differences may appear in language, customs, beliefs, food, family patterns, and land use.","zh":"差異可能出現在語言、習俗、信念、食物、家庭模式和土地使用中。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing two cultures or systems.","zh":"比較兩種文化或制度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"Aboriginal culture","meaning":"澳洲原住民文化","examples":[{"en":"The passage includes references to Aboriginal language and cultural sites.","zh":"文章包含對澳洲原住民語言和文化遺址的提及。"},{"en":"Aboriginal culture includes the languages, stories, beliefs, art, land knowledge, and practices of Australia’s Indigenous peoples.","zh":"Aboriginal culture 包括澳洲原住民族群的語言、故事、信念、藝術、土地知識和習俗。"},{"en":"Aboriginal culture can be seen in rock carvings, place names, oral history, and ceremonies.","zh":"澳洲原住民文化可以在岩刻、地名、口述歷史和儀式中看見。"},{"en":"Protecting cultural sites helps preserve Aboriginal culture for future generations.","zh":"保護文化遺址有助為後代保存澳洲原住民文化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing Australian heritage and identity.","zh":"討論澳洲文化遺產和身份時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contemporary hotels","meaning":"現代化酒店","examples":[{"en":"Bondi’s commercial district contains contemporary hotels and restaurants.","zh":"邦迪商業區有現代化酒店和餐廳。"},{"en":"Contemporary hotels are modern hotels designed for present-day travellers and current tastes.","zh":"contemporary hotels 指為當代旅客和現今品味而設計的現代酒店。"},{"en":"Contemporary hotels may include simple design, online booking, cafés, gyms, and sea-view rooms.","zh":"現代化酒店可能包括簡約設計、網上預訂、咖啡店、健身室和海景房。"},{"en":"New hotels can make a beach area more convenient but also more commercialised.","zh":"新酒店可以令海灘區更方便，但也更商業化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing modern tourism facilities.","zh":"描述現代旅遊設施時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"seaside architecture","meaning":"海濱建築","examples":[{"en":"Bondi’s seaside architecture reflects several overseas influences.","zh":"邦迪的海濱建築反映幾種海外影響。"},{"en":"Seaside architecture means the buildings and design styles found in coastal towns or beach areas.","zh":"seaside architecture 指海岸城鎮或海灘地區中的建築和設計風格。"},{"en":"Seaside architecture may include balconies, red roofs, hotels, cafés, and buildings facing the sea.","zh":"海濱建築可能包括露台、紅屋頂、酒店、咖啡店和面向大海的建築物。"},{"en":"Architecture near the sea often responds to views, wind, tourism, and leisure culture.","zh":"海邊建築常回應景觀、風、旅遊和休閒文化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing coastal design.","zh":"討論海岸設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reflect British influence","meaning":"反映英國影響","examples":[{"en":"The characteristic roofs reflect British influence.","zh":"具特色的屋頂反映英國影響。"},{"en":"To reflect British influence means to show signs of British style, history, culture, or design.","zh":"reflect British influence 指顯示英國風格、歷史、文化或設計的痕跡。"},{"en":"A school uniform may reflect British influence if it follows an old colonial style.","zh":"如果校服沿用舊殖民風格，它可能反映英國影響。"},{"en":"Architecture can reveal influence through roof shapes, materials, street layouts, or building names.","zh":"建築可以透過屋頂形狀、材料、街道佈局或建築名稱顯示影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing colonial or cultural influence.","zh":"討論殖民或文化影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"characteristic red colour","meaning":"具特色的紅色","examples":[{"en":"The buildings are recognised by their characteristic red colour.","zh":"這些建築因其具特色的紅色而被認出。"},{"en":"A characteristic red colour is a distinctive shade of red that helps identify something.","zh":"characteristic red colour 指幫助辨認某物的獨特紅色色調。"},{"en":"A school building with characteristic red walls may be easy for visitors to find.","zh":"有具特色紅牆的學校建築，可能很容易讓訪客找到。"},{"en":"Colour can become part of a place’s identity when it appears repeatedly in local buildings.","zh":"當顏色反覆出現在本地建築中，它可以成為地方身份的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing visual features.","zh":"描述視覺特徵時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"live near the seashore","meaning":"居住在海岸附近","examples":[{"en":"Many people choose to live near the seashore.","zh":"許多人選擇居住在海岸附近。"},{"en":"To live near the seashore means to have a home close to the sea or coast.","zh":"live near the seashore 指住在靠近大海或海岸的地方。"},{"en":"A retired couple may live near the seashore because they enjoy walking by the water.","zh":"退休夫婦可能因喜歡在水邊散步而住在海岸附近。"},{"en":"Living near the seashore can offer views and fresh air, but property may be expensive.","zh":"居住在海岸附近可以提供景觀和新鮮空氣，但物業可能昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing coastal lifestyle.","zh":"討論海岸生活方式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be beneficial for health","meaning":"對健康有益","examples":[{"en":"Access to fresh air and recreation may be beneficial for health.","zh":"接觸新鮮空氣和康樂活動可能對健康有益。"},{"en":"Be beneficial for health means help improve or protect physical or mental well-being.","zh":"be beneficial for health 指有助改善或保護身體或心理健康。"},{"en":"Regular walking can be beneficial for health because it strengthens the heart and reduces stress.","zh":"定期步行對健康有益，因為它強化心臟並減少壓力。"},{"en":"Beaches may support health by encouraging exercise, relaxation, and time outdoors.","zh":"海灘可以透過鼓勵運動、放鬆和戶外活動來支持健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing positive effects on well-being.","zh":"討論對身心健康的正面影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"provide answers using","meaning":"使用……作答","examples":[{"en":"Students provide answers using words taken directly from the passage.","zh":"學生使用直接取自文章的詞語作答。"},{"en":"Provide answers using something means write answers with the required source, form, or wording.","zh":"provide answers using something 指使用指定來源、形式或字眼寫答案。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may provide answers using no more than two words from the text.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能需要使用文本中不多於兩個詞作答。"},{"en":"Following the instruction matters because correct ideas can still lose marks if the form is wrong.","zh":"遵守指示很重要，因為即使意思正確，形式錯誤仍可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining exam requirements.","zh":"解釋考試要求時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than two words and/or a number","meaning":"不多於兩個詞及／或一個數字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer must contain no more than two words and/or a number.","zh":"每個答案必須包含不多於兩個詞及／或一個數字。"},{"en":"No more than two words and/or a number means the answer may include one or two words, a number, or both.","zh":"no more than two words and/or a number 指答案可以包含一個或兩個詞、一個數字，或兩者兼有。"},{"en":"An answer like “1884” follows the rule because it is a number only.","zh":"像 “1884” 這樣的答案符合規則，因為它只有一個數字。"},{"en":"Writing extra words can break the instruction even if the information is correct.","zh":"即使資料正確，寫多餘字詞也可能違反指示。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in IELTS-style completion questions.","zh":"這個短語在 IELTS 類填空題中很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"at the end of the nineteenth century","meaning":"在十九世紀末","examples":[{"en":"Public transport reached Bondi at the end of the nineteenth century.","zh":"公共交通在十九世紀末到達邦迪。"},{"en":"At the end of the nineteenth century means around the late 1800s.","zh":"at the end of the nineteenth century 指約在1800年代後期。"},{"en":"At the end of the nineteenth century, many cities expanded their rail and tram systems.","zh":"在十九世紀末，許多城市擴展鐵路和電車系統。"},{"en":"This time phrase helps place transport development in historical context.","zh":"這個時間短語有助把交通發展放入歷史背景中。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing events near the close of a century.","zh":"描述接近某世紀結尾的事件時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reach Bondi","meaning":"到達邦迪","examples":[{"en":"Improved transport allowed more people to reach Bondi.","zh":"改善了的交通讓更多人能到達邦迪。"},{"en":"To reach Bondi means to arrive at Bondi or gain physical access to it.","zh":"reach Bondi 指到達邦迪或能實際前往該地。"},{"en":"A new bus route can help students reach a school that was previously difficult to access.","zh":"新巴士路線可以幫助學生到達以前難以前往的學校。"},{"en":"Better transport changes who can visit a place, not just how quickly they travel.","zh":"更好的交通改變的不只是出行速度，也改變誰能到訪某地。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing accessibility.","zh":"討論可達性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"British royalty","meaning":"英國皇室","examples":[{"en":"British royalty has made numerous visits to Australia.","zh":"英國皇室曾多次訪問澳洲。"},{"en":"British royalty means members of Britain’s royal family.","zh":"British royalty 指英國皇室成員。"},{"en":"A visit by British royalty may involve ceremonies, security planning, and public gatherings.","zh":"英國皇室到訪可能涉及儀式、保安安排和公眾聚會。"},{"en":"Royal visits can strengthen symbolic links between countries or historical institutions.","zh":"皇室訪問可以加強國家或歷史制度之間的象徵連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing monarchy and public events.","zh":"討論君主制度和公共活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"Olympic event","meaning":"奧運項目","examples":[{"en":"Bondi hosted an Olympic event during the Sydney Games.","zh":"邦迪在悉尼奧運會期間主辦了一項奧運項目。"},{"en":"An Olympic event is a competition that forms part of the Olympic Games.","zh":"Olympic event 指奧林匹克運動會中的一項比賽。"},{"en":"A city hosting an Olympic event must prepare venues, transport, security, and media facilities.","zh":"主辦奧運項目的城市必須準備場地、交通、保安和媒體設施。"},{"en":"Olympic events can bring global attention to local places.","zh":"奧運項目可以為本地地方帶來全球關注。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing international sport.","zh":"討論國際體育時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"Sydney Olympic Games","meaning":"悉尼奧運會","examples":[{"en":"The 2000 Sydney Olympic Games included events at Bondi Beach.","zh":"2000年悉尼奧運會包括在邦迪海灘舉行的項目。"},{"en":"The Sydney Olympic Games refers to the Olympic Games hosted by Sydney in 2000.","zh":"Sydney Olympic Games 指悉尼於2000年主辦的奧林匹克運動會。"},{"en":"A host city often uses famous local landmarks during the Olympic Games.","zh":"主辦城市常在奧運會期間使用著名本地地標。"},{"en":"Hosting Olympic events can leave memories, publicity, and sometimes debate over public space.","zh":"主辦奧運項目可以留下記憶、宣傳，有時也留下公共空間爭議。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing Australia’s Olympic history.","zh":"討論澳洲奧運歷史時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be damaged by development","meaning":"因發展工程而受破壞","examples":[{"en":"The beach environment could have been damaged by the development.","zh":"海灘環境本可能因發展工程而受破壞。"},{"en":"Be damaged by development means be harmed by building work, construction, or urban expansion.","zh":"be damaged by development 指因建築工程、施工或城市擴張而受害。"},{"en":"A wetland may be damaged by development if roads cut through animal habitats.","zh":"如果道路切穿動物棲息地，濕地可能因發展工程而受破壞。"},{"en":"Development can bring facilities but also disturb soil, restrict access, or harm ecosystems.","zh":"發展可以帶來設施，但也可能擾動土壤、限制使用權或傷害生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing environmental risk.","zh":"討論環境風險時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的詞語完成摘要。"},{"en":"Complete the summary means fill in missing words in a short version of the text.","zh":"complete the summary 指填寫文本簡短版本中的缺漏詞語。"},{"en":"Students should complete the summary by finding the matching information in the passage.","zh":"學生應透過在文章中找出對應資料來完成摘要。"},{"en":"Summary completion tests understanding, grammar, and accurate word choice.","zh":"摘要填空測試理解、文法和準確選詞。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"hold major sporting events","meaning":"舉辦大型體育活動","examples":[{"en":"Bondi Beach holds major sporting events throughout the year.","zh":"邦迪海灘全年舉辦大型體育活動。"},{"en":"To hold major sporting events means to organise or host important sports competitions or activities.","zh":"hold major sporting events 指組織或主辦重要體育比賽或活動。"},{"en":"A stadium may hold major sporting events such as finals, tournaments, and international matches.","zh":"運動場可能舉辦決賽、錦標賽和國際賽事等大型體育活動。"},{"en":"Major events can attract crowds, sponsors, media, and pressure on local services.","zh":"大型活動可以吸引人潮、贊助商、媒體，也會對本地服務造成壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing sport and tourism.","zh":"討論體育和旅遊時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"attract many visitors","meaning":"吸引大量遊客","examples":[{"en":"The beach attracts many local and overseas visitors.","zh":"這個海灘吸引大量本地和海外遊客。"},{"en":"To attract many visitors means to draw large numbers of people to a place.","zh":"attract many visitors 指吸引大量人到某地。"},{"en":"A museum may attract many visitors if it opens a popular exhibition.","zh":"如果博物館開設受歡迎展覽，可能吸引大量遊客。"},{"en":"Many visitors can support local businesses but also create crowding and waste.","zh":"大量遊客可以支持本地商業，但也會造成擁擠和垃圾。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing tourism and popularity.","zh":"討論旅遊和受歡迎程度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"spend holidays there","meaning":"在當地度假","examples":[{"en":"Many visitors choose to spend holidays there.","zh":"許多遊客選擇在當地度假。"},{"en":"To spend holidays there means to use vacation time in that place.","zh":"spend holidays there 指在該地方度過假期。"},{"en":"Families may spend holidays at the seaside because children can swim and play outdoors.","zh":"家庭可能在海邊度假，因為孩子可以游泳和戶外玩耍。"},{"en":"When many tourists spend holidays in one area, accommodation demand rises sharply.","zh":"當許多遊客在同一地區度假，住宿需求會急劇上升。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing travel habits.","zh":"討論旅遊習慣時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"local accommodation","meaning":"本地住宿","examples":[{"en":"Local accommodation may not meet the demand during busy periods.","zh":"旺季期間，本地住宿可能無法滿足需求。"},{"en":"Local accommodation means hotels, guesthouses, apartments, or rooms available in the area.","zh":"local accommodation 指該區可供住宿的酒店、賓館、公寓或房間。"},{"en":"A small town may lack local accommodation when a festival attracts thousands of visitors.","zh":"當節日吸引數千遊客，小鎮可能缺乏本地住宿。"},{"en":"If accommodation is limited, visitors may stay in nearby towns or pay higher prices.","zh":"如果住宿有限，遊客可能住在附近城鎮或支付更高價格。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing tourism capacity.","zh":"討論旅遊接待能力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"meet growing demand","meaning":"滿足日益增加的需求","examples":[{"en":"Developers have struggled to meet growing demand for accommodation.","zh":"發展商一直難以滿足日益增加的住宿需求。"},{"en":"To meet growing demand means to provide enough supply for an increasing need.","zh":"meet growing demand 指提供足夠供應以應付不斷增加的需要。"},{"en":"A school may hire more teachers to meet growing demand for English classes.","zh":"學校可能聘請更多老師，以滿足日益增加的英語課程需求。"},{"en":"If demand grows faster than supply, prices rise and shortages appear.","zh":"如果需求增長快於供應，價格會上升並出現短缺。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing housing, services, and business planning.","zh":"討論住屋、服務和商業規劃時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"provide a solution","meaning":"提供解決方法","examples":[{"en":"A nearby town attempted to provide a solution to the housing shortage.","zh":"附近一個城鎮嘗試為房屋短缺提供解決方法。"},{"en":"To provide a solution means to offer a way to solve or reduce a problem.","zh":"provide a solution 指提供解決或減輕問題的方法。"},{"en":"Extra buses can provide a solution when many students cannot reach school on time.","zh":"當許多學生不能準時到校，增加巴士可以提供解決方法。"},{"en":"A solution works best when it addresses the real cause of the problem.","zh":"解決方法在處理問題真正原因時最有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing problem-solving.","zh":"討論解難時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"nevertheless","meaning":"儘管如此","examples":[{"en":"Nevertheless, Bondi remains more popular than nearby alternatives.","zh":"儘管如此，邦迪仍然比附近其他選擇更受歡迎。"},{"en":"Nevertheless means despite what has just been said.","zh":"nevertheless 指儘管剛才所說的情況如此。"},{"en":"The restaurant is expensive; nevertheless, many people still book tables there.","zh":"這間餐廳很昂貴；儘管如此，仍有許多人訂位。"},{"en":"This word introduces a contrast between expectation and reality.","zh":"這個詞引出預期與現實之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when something remains true despite an opposing point.","zh":"當某事在相反因素存在下仍然成立時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"prefer something as a destination","meaning":"首選……作為目的地","examples":[{"en":"Many tourists prefer Bondi as their destination.","zh":"許多遊客首選邦迪作為目的地。"},{"en":"To prefer something as a destination means to choose that place over other possible places to visit.","zh":"prefer something as a destination 指在其他可到訪地方之中選擇某地。"},{"en":"Families may prefer a beach as a destination because it offers both relaxation and activities.","zh":"家庭可能首選海灘作為目的地，因為它同時提供放鬆和活動。"},{"en":"A preferred destination usually feels more attractive, famous, convenient, or meaningful.","zh":"首選目的地通常感覺更吸引、著名、方便或有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing tourist choice.","zh":"討論遊客選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"seaside buildings","meaning":"海濱建築物","examples":[{"en":"Bondi’s seaside buildings are a distinctive part of the landscape.","zh":"邦迪的海濱建築物是景觀中具特色的一部分。"},{"en":"Seaside buildings are buildings located near the sea or along the coast.","zh":"seaside buildings 指位於海邊或沿海岸線的建築物。"},{"en":"Seaside buildings may include hotels, restaurants, apartments, changing rooms, and cafés.","zh":"海濱建築物可能包括酒店、餐廳、住宅單位、更衣室和咖啡店。"},{"en":"Buildings near the sea often affect how people see and experience the beach.","zh":"海邊建築常影響人們如何觀看和體驗海灘。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing coastal architecture.","zh":"討論海岸建築時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"pleasant scent","meaning":"宜人的氣息","examples":[{"en":"Residents value the pleasant scent of the sea.","zh":"居民重視海洋宜人的氣息。"},{"en":"A pleasant scent is a smell that people find enjoyable or refreshing.","zh":"pleasant scent 指令人覺得愉快或清新的氣味。"},{"en":"A bakery has a pleasant scent when fresh bread is coming out of the oven.","zh":"當新鮮麵包出爐，麵包店會有宜人的氣息。"},{"en":"The pleasant scent of sea air can make coastal living feel relaxing and attractive.","zh":"海風宜人的氣息可以令海岸生活感覺放鬆和吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing smell in a positive way.","zh":"以正面方式描述氣味時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 131 - Bondi Beach.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 132":[{"front":"handle the sun","meaning":"應對陽光","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains how people can handle the sun safely.","zh":"文章解釋人們如何安全地應對陽光。"},{"en":"To handle the sun means to deal with sunlight in a sensible way so that people gain benefits but avoid harm.","zh":"「handle the sun」意思是以明智方式處理日曬，讓人得到好處但避免傷害。"},{"en":"Beach visitors handle the sun better when they wear hats, use sunscreen, and rest in the shade.","zh":"到海灘的人戴帽、使用防曬產品並在陰影下休息時，就能更好地應對陽光。"},{"en":"If people do not handle the sun carefully, they may suffer sunburn, eye damage, or heat illness.","zh":"如果人們不小心應對陽光，可能會曬傷、眼睛受損或患上熱病。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on managing sun exposure, not avoiding the sun completely.","zh":"這個短語集中於管理日曬，而不是完全避開陽光。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the medical world","meaning":"醫學界","examples":[{"en":"The medical world remains divided over some effects of sunlight.","zh":"醫學界對陽光某些影響仍有分歧。"},{"en":"The medical world means doctors, researchers, hospitals, and other people or institutions involved in medicine.","zh":"「the medical world」指醫生、研究人員、醫院，以及其他參與醫學的人或機構。"},{"en":"The medical world often studies whether new treatments are safe before recommending them.","zh":"醫學界通常會研究新療法是否安全，然後才推薦使用。"},{"en":"If the medical world is divided, patients may hear different advice from different experts.","zh":"如果醫學界有分歧，病人可能從不同專家聽到不同建議。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the professional field of medicine as a whole.","zh":"這個短語指整個醫學專業領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"appear to be divided on","meaning":"對……似乎意見分歧","examples":[{"en":"The medical world appears to be divided on the effects of the sun.","zh":"醫學界對陽光的影響似乎意見分歧。"},{"en":"To appear to be divided on something means to seem to have different opinions about it.","zh":"「appear to be divided on」某事，意思是對它似乎有不同意見。"},{"en":"Teachers appear to be divided on whether homework should be given every day.","zh":"老師對是否應每天派功課似乎意見分歧。"},{"en":"If experts are divided on an issue, the evidence may still be incomplete or difficult to interpret.","zh":"如果專家對某議題有分歧，證據可能仍不完整或難以解讀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes disagreement, but with a careful tone.","zh":"這個短語描述分歧，但語氣較謹慎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the effects of the sun on","meaning":"陽光對……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Doctors continue to study the effects of the sun on the human body.","zh":"醫生繼續研究陽光對人體的影響。"},{"en":"The effects of the sun on something are the ways sunlight changes or influences it.","zh":"「the effects of the sun on」某物，是陽光改變或影響它的方式。"},{"en":"Scientists study the effects of the sun on plants by measuring growth and leaf colour.","zh":"科學家透過量度生長和葉色，研究陽光對植物的影響。"},{"en":"If sunlight affects skin, eyes, and vitamin D production, doctors need to balance benefits and risks.","zh":"如果陽光影響皮膚、眼睛和維他命 D 生成，醫生就需要平衡好處和風險。"},{"en":"The phrase connects sunlight with its results on a target.","zh":"這個短語把陽光與其對某對象造成的結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the human body","meaning":"人體","examples":[{"en":"Sunlight can have both beneficial and harmful effects on the human body.","zh":"陽光對人體可以有有益和有害的影響。"},{"en":"The human body means the complete physical structure of a person, including organs, skin, bones, and blood.","zh":"「the human body」指人的完整身體結構，包括器官、皮膚、骨骼和血液。"},{"en":"Exercise affects the human body by strengthening muscles and improving circulation.","zh":"運動透過強化肌肉和改善循環影響人體。"},{"en":"If sunlight reaches the skin, the human body may produce vitamin D but may also suffer damage from overexposure.","zh":"如果陽光照到皮膚，人體可能產生維他命 D，但過度曝曬也可能造成傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people physically, not their thoughts or emotions alone.","zh":"這個短語指人的身體，而不只是思想或情緒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"no known relationship between","meaning":"……之間沒有已知關係","examples":[{"en":"Some doctors say there is no known relationship between a suntan and health.","zh":"有些醫生說曬黑膚色與健康之間沒有已知關係。"},{"en":"No known relationship between two things means there is no proven connection between them.","zh":"「no known relationship between」兩件事，意思是兩者之間沒有已被證實的關聯。"},{"en":"There may be no known relationship between a student’s handwriting style and intelligence.","zh":"學生的字體風格與智力之間可能沒有已知關係。"},{"en":"If no relationship has been shown, people should be careful about making strong claims.","zh":"如果尚未證明有關係，人們就應小心作出強烈主張。"},{"en":"The phrase does not mean a link is impossible; it means no link has been clearly established.","zh":"這個短語不是說關聯不可能存在，而是說尚未清楚建立關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a tan and health","meaning":"曬黑膚色與健康","examples":[{"en":"The relationship between a tan and health remains uncertain.","zh":"曬黑膚色與健康之間的關係仍不確定。"},{"en":"A tan and health refers to the possible connection between darker skin from sunlight and a person’s physical well-being.","zh":"「a tan and health」指由陽光造成的較深膚色與身體健康之間可能存在的關係。"},{"en":"Some people think a tan looks healthy, but appearance alone does not prove good health.","zh":"有些人認為曬黑膚色看起來健康，但外表本身不能證明健康良好。"},{"en":"If a tan is caused by too much sun, it may signal skin stress rather than health.","zh":"如果曬黑是由過度日曬造成，它可能顯示皮膚受壓，而不是健康。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts outward colour with actual physical condition.","zh":"這個短語把外在膚色與實際身體狀況作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sun-tanned skin","meaning":"曬黑了的皮膚","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers have considered whether sun-tanned skin absorbs ultraviolet rays.","zh":"有些研究人員曾考慮曬黑了的皮膚是否會吸收紫外線。"},{"en":"Sun-tanned skin is skin that has become darker after exposure to sunlight.","zh":"「sun-tanned skin」是接觸陽光後變深色的皮膚。"},{"en":"A person may have sun-tanned skin after spending several days outdoors without enough shade.","zh":"一個人在戶外待數天且沒有足夠遮蔭後，可能會有曬黑了的皮膚。"},{"en":"If skin becomes tanned, it has reacted to sunlight by producing more pigment.","zh":"如果皮膚被曬黑，它就是透過產生更多色素來對陽光作出反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a visible skin change caused by the sun.","zh":"這個短語描述由陽光造成的可見皮膚變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"absorb ultraviolet rays","meaning":"吸收紫外線","examples":[{"en":"Sun-tanned skin may absorb ultraviolet rays differently.","zh":"曬黑了的皮膚可能以不同方式吸收紫外線。"},{"en":"To absorb ultraviolet rays means to take in UV radiation instead of reflecting or blocking it completely.","zh":"「absorb ultraviolet rays」意思是吸收紫外線輻射，而不是完全反射或阻隔它。"},{"en":"Good sunglasses absorb ultraviolet rays to protect the eyes.","zh":"好太陽眼鏡會吸收紫外線，以保護眼睛。"},{"en":"If skin absorbs too many ultraviolet rays, cells may be damaged.","zh":"如果皮膚吸收過多紫外線，細胞可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how a material or body part takes in harmful light energy.","zh":"這個短語描述材料或身體部位如何吸收有害光能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"convert something into","meaning":"將……轉化為……","examples":[{"en":"One theory suggests that the skin converts ultraviolet rays into helpful energy.","zh":"一個理論認為皮膚會將紫外線轉化為有益能量。"},{"en":"To convert something into something else means to change it from one form into another.","zh":"「convert something into」另一物，意思是把某物由一種形式變成另一種形式。"},{"en":"Solar panels convert sunlight into electricity.","zh":"太陽能板將陽光轉化為電力。"},{"en":"If the body converts sunlight into vitamin-related benefits, moderate exposure may be useful.","zh":"如果身體把陽光轉化為與維他命相關的好處，適量曝曬可能有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes transformation from one state or form to another.","zh":"這個短語描述由一種狀態或形式變成另一種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"helpful energy","meaning":"有益能量","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers have speculated about sunlight being converted into helpful energy.","zh":"有些研究人員推測陽光會被轉化為有益能量。"},{"en":"Helpful energy means energy that supports the body or makes a useful process possible.","zh":"「helpful energy」是支持身體或令有用過程成為可能的能量。"},{"en":"Food provides helpful energy that allows students to think, walk, and study.","zh":"食物提供有益能量，讓學生思考、步行和學習。"},{"en":"If sunlight helps the body produce vitamin D, it can be seen as supporting a useful process.","zh":"如果陽光幫助身體產生維他命 D，它就可以被視為支持有用過程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes energy that benefits rather than harms.","zh":"這個短語描述帶來好處而非傷害的能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"remain a topic of research","meaning":"仍是研究課題","examples":[{"en":"Several effects of sunlight remain a topic of research.","zh":"陽光的幾種影響仍是研究課題。"},{"en":"To remain a topic of research means to continue being studied because the answer is not fully settled.","zh":"「remain a topic of research」意思是因答案尚未完全確定而繼續被研究。"},{"en":"The long-term effects of heavy screen use remain a topic of research.","zh":"長時間使用電子屏幕的長期影響仍是研究課題。"},{"en":"If scientists still lack complete evidence, a question remains open for further study.","zh":"如果科學家仍缺乏完整證據，問題就仍然有待進一步研究。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an issue that researchers are still investigating.","zh":"這個短語描述研究人員仍在調查的議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"agree on","meaning":"對……有共識","examples":[{"en":"Doctors generally agree on the importance of vitamin D.","zh":"醫生普遍對維他命 D 的重要性有共識。"},{"en":"To agree on something means to share the same opinion or decision about it.","zh":"「agree on」某事，意思是對它有相同意見或決定。"},{"en":"Students in a group project must agree on who will present each section.","zh":"小組專題中的學生必須就誰負責匯報每一部分達成共識。"},{"en":"If doctors agree on a point, advice to patients becomes clearer.","zh":"如果醫生對某點有共識，給病人的建議就更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shared agreement about a topic or plan.","zh":"這個短語描述對題目或計劃有共同看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"one of the benefits of","meaning":"……的其中一項好處","examples":[{"en":"Vitamin D production is one of the benefits of sunlight.","zh":"產生維他命 D 是陽光的其中一項好處。"},{"en":"One of the benefits of something means one advantage among several possible advantages.","zh":"「one of the benefits of」某事，意思是幾個可能好處中的其中一個。"},{"en":"One of the benefits of walking to school is getting light exercise every day.","zh":"步行上學的其中一項好處是每天得到輕量運動。"},{"en":"If sunlight has benefits, people still need to balance them against the risks of overexposure.","zh":"如果陽光有好處，人們仍需要把它們與過度曝曬的風險平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces one positive effect without saying it is the only one.","zh":"這個短語引出一項正面影響，而不是說它是唯一好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"vitamin D","meaning":"維他命 D","examples":[{"en":"The human body can acquire vitamin D through direct sunlight.","zh":"人體可以透過直接陽光獲得維他命 D。"},{"en":"Vitamin D is a nutrient that helps the body use calcium and maintain healthy bones.","zh":"維他命 D 是幫助身體使用鈣質並維持骨骼健康的營養素。"},{"en":"Doctors may check vitamin D levels when a patient feels tired or has bone problems.","zh":"當病人感到疲倦或有骨骼問題時，醫生可能檢查維他命 D 水平。"},{"en":"If people get too little sunlight or dietary vitamin D, their bones may become weaker.","zh":"如果人們得到太少陽光或飲食中的維他命 D，骨骼可能變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase names a vitamin linked with sunlight and health.","zh":"這個短語指出一種與陽光和健康有關的維他命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"it is well known that","meaning":"眾所周知","examples":[{"en":"It is well known that direct sunlight helps the body produce vitamin D.","zh":"眾所周知，直接陽光幫助身體產生維他命 D。"},{"en":"It is well known that means many people accept or understand this as true.","zh":"「it is well known that」意思是許多人接受或理解某事為真。"},{"en":"It is well known that regular sleep helps students concentrate better.","zh":"眾所周知，定時睡眠幫助學生更好地集中。"},{"en":"If a fact is well known, writers may use the phrase to introduce common knowledge.","zh":"如果一項事實廣為人知，作者可能用這個短語引入常識。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the information is widely recognised.","zh":"這個短語表示資料被廣泛認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be acquired from","meaning":"從……獲得","examples":[{"en":"Vitamin D can be acquired from the direct rays of the sun.","zh":"維他命 D 可以從太陽直射光線獲得。"},{"en":"To be acquired from something means to be obtained or gained from that source.","zh":"「be acquired from」某物，意思是從該來源得到或獲得。"},{"en":"Language skills can be acquired from reading, listening, and daily conversation.","zh":"語言技能可以從閱讀、聆聽和日常對話中獲得。"},{"en":"If vitamin D can be acquired from sunlight, moderate outdoor time may be useful.","zh":"如果維他命 D 可以從陽光獲得，適量戶外時間可能有用。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source from which something is gained.","zh":"這個短語指出某物獲得的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"direct rays of the sun","meaning":"太陽直射光線","examples":[{"en":"The direct rays of the sun help the skin produce vitamin D.","zh":"太陽直射光線幫助皮膚產生維他命 D。"},{"en":"Direct rays of the sun are sunlight that reaches the skin or surface without being blocked by shade or clouds.","zh":"「direct rays of the sun」是沒有被陰影或雲層阻擋而到達皮膚或表面的陽光。"},{"en":"A person standing under a tree receives less direct sunlight than someone standing in an open field.","zh":"站在樹下的人比站在空地上的人接收到較少直接陽光。"},{"en":"If skin receives direct rays for a short time, vitamin D production may begin.","zh":"如果皮膚短時間接收太陽直射光線，維他命 D 生成可能開始。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unblocked sunlight.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有被阻隔的陽光。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an entirely separate process","meaning":"完全不同的過程","examples":[{"en":"Vitamin D production is an entirely separate process from tanning.","zh":"維他命 D 的產生與曬黑皮膚是完全不同的過程。"},{"en":"An entirely separate process means a completely different action or biological mechanism.","zh":"「an entirely separate process」意思是完全不同的行動或生物機制。"},{"en":"Learning pronunciation is an entirely separate process from memorising spelling.","zh":"學習發音與記憶串字是完全不同的過程。"},{"en":"If two processes are separate, one should not be confused with the other.","zh":"如果兩個過程是分開的，就不應把其中一個與另一個混淆。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses complete difference between two processes.","zh":"這個短語強調兩個過程完全不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sun tanning","meaning":"曬黑皮膚","examples":[{"en":"Vitamin D production should not be confused with sun tanning.","zh":"維他命 D 的產生不應與曬黑皮膚混淆。"},{"en":"Sun tanning is the process of the skin becoming darker after exposure to sunlight.","zh":"「sun tanning」是皮膚接觸陽光後變深色的過程。"},{"en":"Some people go to the beach mainly for sun tanning, but too much exposure can harm the skin.","zh":"有些人去海灘主要為了曬黑皮膚，但過度曝曬會傷害皮膚。"},{"en":"If tanning becomes an obsession, people may ignore warnings about skin damage.","zh":"如果曬黑變成迷戀，人們可能忽視皮膚受損警告。"},{"en":"The phrase describes darkening of skin caused by the sun.","zh":"這個短語描述由陽光造成的皮膚變深。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"penetrate the skin","meaning":"穿透皮膚","examples":[{"en":"Ultraviolet rays penetrate only a tiny distance into the skin.","zh":"紫外線只穿透皮膚極淺的距離。"},{"en":"To penetrate the skin means to pass into or through the outer surface of the skin.","zh":"「penetrate the skin」意思是進入或穿過皮膚外層表面。"},{"en":"A medical cream may penetrate the skin to reach the area it is meant to treat.","zh":"醫療藥膏可能穿透皮膚，到達需要治療的區域。"},{"en":"If ultraviolet rays penetrate the skin, they can affect substances and cells near the surface.","zh":"如果紫外線穿透皮膚，它們可以影響表面附近的物質和細胞。"},{"en":"The phrase describes entering the skin, not merely touching it.","zh":"這個短語描述進入皮膚，而不只是接觸皮膚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"only a tiny amount","meaning":"只有極少量","examples":[{"en":"The rays penetrate only a tiny amount into human skin.","zh":"這些光線只穿透人體皮膚極少量。"},{"en":"Only a tiny amount means a very small quantity or distance.","zh":"「only a tiny amount」意思是非常少的數量或距離。"},{"en":"A tiny amount of chilli can change the taste of soup.","zh":"只有極少量辣椒也可以改變湯的味道。"},{"en":"If light penetrates only a tiny amount, its effect may be limited to the skin’s surface layers.","zh":"如果光線只穿透極少量，其影響可能限於皮膚表層。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the amount is very small.","zh":"這個短語強調數量非常小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in the process","meaning":"在過程中","examples":[{"en":"In the process, the rays affect a substance in the skin.","zh":"在過程中，這些光線影響皮膚中的一種物質。"},{"en":"In the process means while that action or change is happening.","zh":"「in the process」意思是在該行動或變化發生期間。"},{"en":"A student may organise old notes and, in the process, discover missing homework.","zh":"學生整理舊筆記時，可能在過程中發現遺漏的功課。"},{"en":"If sunlight penetrates the skin, it may trigger chemical changes in the process.","zh":"如果陽光穿透皮膚，它可能在過程中觸發化學變化。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an additional result with an ongoing action.","zh":"這個短語把額外結果與正在進行的行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"irradiate an element","meaning":"照射某種成分","examples":[{"en":"The ultraviolet rays irradiate an element called ergosterol.","zh":"紫外線照射一種名為麥角固醇的成分。"},{"en":"To irradiate an element means to expose a substance to radiation or strong rays.","zh":"「irradiate an element」意思是使某物質暴露於輻射或強光線下。"},{"en":"In a laboratory, scientists may irradiate a sample to see how light changes it.","zh":"在實驗室中，科學家可能照射樣本，以觀察光如何改變它。"},{"en":"If ultraviolet rays irradiate a skin substance, a chemical change may take place.","zh":"如果紫外線照射皮膚中的物質，化學變化可能發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes exposure to radiation for an effect.","zh":"這個短語描述為產生效果而暴露於輻射。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"an element in the skin","meaning":"皮膚中的一種成分","examples":[{"en":"Ergosterol is an element found in the skin.","zh":"麥角固醇是在皮膚中找到的一種成分。"},{"en":"An element in the skin means a substance or component present in the skin.","zh":"「an element in the skin」意思是存在於皮膚中的物質或組成部分。"},{"en":"Oil is an element in the skin’s natural protective surface.","zh":"油脂是皮膚天然保護表面中的一種成分。"},{"en":"If an element in the skin reacts to sunlight, the body may produce useful substances.","zh":"如果皮膚中的某種成分對陽光作出反應，身體可能產生有用物質。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one part of the skin’s chemical make-up.","zh":"這個短語描述皮膚化學組成中的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ergosterol","meaning":"麥角固醇","examples":[{"en":"Ergosterol stores reserves of vitamin D received from sunlight.","zh":"麥角固醇儲存從陽光獲得的維他命 D 存量。"},{"en":"Ergosterol is a substance mentioned in the passage as being involved in vitamin D-related processes in the skin.","zh":"「ergosterol」是文章提到的一種物質，參與皮膚中與維他命 D 相關的過程。"},{"en":"A biology teacher may introduce ergosterol when explaining how sunlight affects skin chemistry.","zh":"生物老師解釋陽光如何影響皮膚化學時，可能介紹麥角固醇。"},{"en":"If ultraviolet rays act on ergosterol, the body may gain vitamin-related benefits.","zh":"如果紫外線作用於麥角固醇，身體可能得到與維他命相關的好處。"},{"en":"The word names a specific skin-related substance in the passage.","zh":"這個詞指出文章中的一種特定皮膚相關物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"store up reserves of","meaning":"儲存……的存量","examples":[{"en":"Ergosterol stores up reserves of vitamin D.","zh":"麥角固醇儲存維他命 D 的存量。"},{"en":"To store up reserves of something means to keep extra amounts for later use.","zh":"「store up reserves of」某物，意思是保存額外數量以供日後使用。"},{"en":"Families may store up reserves of food before a typhoon.","zh":"家庭可能在颱風前儲存食物存量。"},{"en":"If the body stores reserves of a nutrient, it can use them when intake is lower.","zh":"如果身體儲存某營養素的存量，攝取較少時仍可使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes saving something for future need.","zh":"這個短語描述為未來需要而保存某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"healthy and beneficial","meaning":"健康而有益的","examples":[{"en":"Moderate sunlight can be healthy and beneficial for human skin.","zh":"適量陽光對人體皮膚可以是健康而有益的。"},{"en":"Healthy and beneficial means good for health and helpful in producing a positive effect.","zh":"「healthy and beneficial」意思是對健康有好處，並能產生正面效果。"},{"en":"Regular walking is healthy and beneficial for people who sit for long hours.","zh":"定期步行對長時間坐着的人健康而有益。"},{"en":"If sunlight is moderate, it may help the body without causing serious damage.","zh":"如果陽光適量，它可能幫助身體而不造成嚴重傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that supports well-being.","zh":"這個短語描述支持健康的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"develop an obsession with","meaning":"對……產生迷戀","examples":[{"en":"People throughout the Western world have developed an obsession with suntanning.","zh":"西方世界各地的人對曬黑產生了迷戀。"},{"en":"To develop an obsession with something means to become excessively interested in it.","zh":"「develop an obsession with」某事，意思是對它產生過度興趣。"},{"en":"Some students develop an obsession with exam scores and forget to rest.","zh":"有些學生對考試分數產生迷戀，並忘記休息。"},{"en":"If people become obsessed with tanning, they may ignore the risks of skin damage.","zh":"如果人們迷戀曬黑，他們可能忽視皮膚受損風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes interest becoming too strong or unhealthy.","zh":"這個短語描述興趣變得太強或不健康。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Western world","meaning":"西方世界","examples":[{"en":"Suntanning has become highly popular throughout the Western world.","zh":"曬黑在整個西方世界變得非常流行。"},{"en":"The Western world usually refers to Europe, North America, and societies culturally linked to them.","zh":"「the Western world」通常指歐洲、北美，以及與它們文化上有關的社會。"},{"en":"Many fashion trends spread quickly through the Western world before reaching other regions.","zh":"許多時尚潮流先在西方世界迅速傳播，然後到達其他地區。"},{"en":"If a habit becomes popular across the Western world, media and culture may reinforce it.","zh":"如果一種習慣在西方世界流行，媒體和文化可能加強它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broad cultural region, not one single country.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛文化區域，而不是單一國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a suntan","meaning":"曬黑的膚色","examples":[{"en":"A suntan is often associated with an active outdoor lifestyle.","zh":"曬黑的膚色常與活躍的戶外生活方式有關。"},{"en":"A suntan is a darker skin colour caused by exposure to sunlight.","zh":"「a suntan」是由接觸陽光造成的較深膚色。"},{"en":"Someone who works on a farm may develop a suntan after long days outdoors.","zh":"在農場工作的人長時間戶外工作後，可能形成曬黑膚色。"},{"en":"If a suntan comes from too much sun, it may also involve skin damage.","zh":"如果曬黑膚色來自過多陽光，它也可能涉及皮膚受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes appearance, not necessarily health.","zh":"這個短語描述外觀，而不一定代表健康。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"become the trademark of","meaning":"成為……的標誌","examples":[{"en":"A suntan has become the trademark of a healthy, active person.","zh":"曬黑膚色已成為健康活躍人士的標誌。"},{"en":"To become the trademark of something means to become a clear sign or symbol associated with it.","zh":"「become the trademark of」某事，意思是成為與它有關的清楚標誌或象徵。"},{"en":"A warm smile may become the trademark of a popular teacher.","zh":"溫暖笑容可能成為受歡迎老師的標誌。"},{"en":"If society links tanned skin with outdoor activity, a suntan may become a symbol of health.","zh":"如果社會把曬黑膚色與戶外活動連繫起來，它可能成為健康的象徵。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something becoming a recognisable sign.","zh":"這個短語描述某物成為可辨認標誌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"healthy, active, outdoor person","meaning":"健康、活躍而喜愛戶外活動的人","examples":[{"en":"A suntan is often linked with a healthy, active, outdoor person.","zh":"曬黑膚色常與健康、活躍而喜愛戶外活動的人有關。"},{"en":"A healthy, active, outdoor person is someone who seems fit, energetic, and often spends time outside.","zh":"「healthy, active, outdoor person」是看似健康、有活力並常在戶外活動的人。"},{"en":"A coach who hikes, swims, and cycles may be seen as a healthy, active, outdoor person.","zh":"經常遠足、游泳和踩單車的教練可能被視為健康、活躍而喜愛戶外活動的人。"},{"en":"If tanned skin is associated with such a lifestyle, people may mistake appearance for health.","zh":"如果曬黑膚色與這種生活方式有關，人們可能把外表誤認為健康。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a social image of energy and outdoor living.","zh":"這個短語描述精力和戶外生活的社會形象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reddish hue","meaning":"淡紅色調","examples":[{"en":"A basic reddish hue can be seen beneath the skin.","zh":"皮膚下面可以看到基本的淡紅色調。"},{"en":"A reddish hue is a slight red colour or tone.","zh":"「reddish hue」是輕微的紅色或紅色色調。"},{"en":"A person’s cheeks may have a reddish hue after exercise.","zh":"一個人運動後，臉頰可能有淡紅色調。"},{"en":"If blood flow increases near the skin, a reddish hue may become more visible.","zh":"如果皮膚附近血流增加，淡紅色調可能更明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes colour, not a strong red paint-like appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述顏色，而不是像紅漆一樣強烈的紅色外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"beneath the surface of","meaning":"在……表面之下","examples":[{"en":"The reddish colour lies just beneath the surface of the skin.","zh":"紅色色彩就在皮膚表面之下。"},{"en":"Beneath the surface of something means just under its outer layer.","zh":"「beneath the surface of」某物，意思是在其外層下面。"},{"en":"Tiny roots may grow beneath the surface of the soil.","zh":"細小根部可能在泥土表面之下生長。"},{"en":"If colour lies beneath the skin surface, it may come from blood vessels below.","zh":"如果顏色位於皮膚表面之下，它可能來自下面的血管。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something located under the visible outside layer.","zh":"這個短語描述位於可見外層之下的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"outward reflection of","meaning":"……的外在反映","examples":[{"en":"The colour is the outward reflection of blood flowing through tiny vessels.","zh":"這種顏色是血液流經微小血管的外在反映。"},{"en":"An outward reflection of something is a visible sign of an internal condition or process.","zh":"「outward reflection of」某事，是內部狀態或過程的可見跡象。"},{"en":"A tired face can be an outward reflection of poor sleep.","zh":"疲倦的臉色可以是睡眠不足的外在反映。"},{"en":"If blood moves near the skin surface, skin colour may reflect that internal flow.","zh":"如果血液在皮膚表面附近流動，膚色可能反映這種內部血流。"},{"en":"The phrase connects what we see outside with what happens inside.","zh":"這個短語把外在所見與內部發生的事連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"red corpuscles","meaning":"紅血球","examples":[{"en":"Millions of red corpuscles flow through the body’s blood vessels.","zh":"數以百萬計紅血球流經身體血管。"},{"en":"Red corpuscles are red blood cells that carry oxygen through the body.","zh":"「red corpuscles」是把氧氣帶到全身的紅血球。"},{"en":"Doctors may check red corpuscles when testing whether a patient is anaemic.","zh":"醫生檢查病人是否貧血時，可能檢查紅血球。"},{"en":"If red blood cells carry less oxygen, a person may feel weak or tired.","zh":"如果紅血球攜帶較少氧氣，人可能感到虛弱或疲倦。"},{"en":"The phrase is an older or more formal way to refer to red blood cells.","zh":"這個短語是指紅血球的較舊或較正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tiny blood vessels","meaning":"微小血管","examples":[{"en":"Red corpuscles flow through tiny blood vessels beneath the skin.","zh":"紅血球流經皮膚下的微小血管。"},{"en":"Tiny blood vessels are very small tubes that carry blood through the body.","zh":"「tiny blood vessels」是把血液帶到全身的非常細小管道。"},{"en":"A small cut may bleed because tiny blood vessels near the skin have broken.","zh":"小傷口可能流血，因為皮膚附近的微小血管破裂。"},{"en":"If tiny blood vessels widen, the skin may look redder.","zh":"如果微小血管擴張，皮膚可能看起來更紅。"},{"en":"The phrase describes small parts of the circulation system.","zh":"這個短語描述循環系統中的細小部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be most noticeable in","meaning":"在……中最明顯","examples":[{"en":"The natural reddish colour is most noticeable in a baby’s skin.","zh":"天然淡紅色在嬰兒皮膚中最明顯。"},{"en":"To be most noticeable in something means to be easiest to see or recognise there.","zh":"「be most noticeable in」某物，意思是在那裡最容易看見或辨認。"},{"en":"A spelling mistake is most noticeable in a short sentence because there are fewer words.","zh":"串字錯誤在短句中最明顯，因為字數較少。"},{"en":"If baby skin is thin and pale, changes in colour may show more clearly.","zh":"如果嬰兒皮膚較薄且較白，顏色變化可能更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase points to where a feature is especially easy to observe.","zh":"這個短語指出某特徵在哪裡尤其容易觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"change in a moment","meaning":"瞬間改變","examples":[{"en":"A baby’s skin colour can change in a moment.","zh":"嬰兒的膚色可以瞬間改變。"},{"en":"To change in a moment means to change very quickly.","zh":"「change in a moment」意思是非常快速地改變。"},{"en":"The weather can change in a moment during a summer storm.","zh":"夏天暴風雨期間，天氣可以瞬間改變。"},{"en":"If a baby becomes hot or angry, skin colour may change almost immediately.","zh":"如果嬰兒變熱或生氣，膚色可能幾乎立即改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a sudden or very rapid change.","zh":"這個短語描述突然或非常快速的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"porcelain white","meaning":"瓷白色","examples":[{"en":"A baby’s skin may appear porcelain white when calm.","zh":"嬰兒平靜時，皮膚可能呈瓷白色。"},{"en":"Porcelain white means very pale, smooth, and white, like fine china.","zh":"「porcelain white」意思是像精美瓷器一樣非常蒼白、光滑而白。"},{"en":"A person’s face may turn porcelain white after hearing shocking news.","zh":"一個人聽到震驚消息後，臉色可能變成瓷白色。"},{"en":"If blood flow near the skin decreases, the skin may look unusually pale.","zh":"如果皮膚附近血流減少，皮膚可能看起來異常蒼白。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a delicate, very pale colour.","zh":"這個短語描述細緻而非常淡白的顏色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a switch in temperature","meaning":"溫度的突然轉變","examples":[{"en":"A switch in temperature can alter a baby’s skin colour.","zh":"溫度的突然轉變可以改變嬰兒膚色。"},{"en":"A switch in temperature means a sudden change from warm to cold or cold to warm.","zh":"「a switch in temperature」意思是由暖變冷或由冷變暖的突然轉變。"},{"en":"Moving from an air-conditioned room into hot sun creates a switch in temperature.","zh":"從冷氣房走到烈日下會造成溫度的突然轉變。"},{"en":"If temperature changes suddenly, the body may react through sweating, shivering, or skin colour change.","zh":"如果溫度突然轉變，身體可能透過流汗、發抖或膚色改變來反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a quick change in heat conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述熱度條件的快速改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"turn crimson","meaning":"變成深紅色","examples":[{"en":"A baby’s skin can turn crimson with anger or heat.","zh":"嬰兒皮膚可能因憤怒或炎熱而變成深紅色。"},{"en":"To turn crimson means to become deep red in colour.","zh":"「turn crimson」意思是顏色變成深紅。"},{"en":"A runner’s face may turn crimson after a hard race.","zh":"跑手在艱辛比賽後，臉可能變成深紅色。"},{"en":"If blood flow increases strongly near the skin, the skin may become deep red.","zh":"如果皮膚附近血流強烈增加，皮膚可能變成深紅色。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong red colour change.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈紅色變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Caucasians","meaning":"白種人","examples":[{"en":"In Caucasians, the natural colouring may be hidden by pigment.","zh":"在白種人身上，天然膚色可能被色素遮蓋。"},{"en":"Caucasians is an older term often used to refer to people with European ancestry or lighter skin.","zh":"「Caucasians」是較舊用語，常指有歐洲血統或較淺膚色的人。"},{"en":"Medical writing may use the term Caucasians when comparing skin reactions across groups.","zh":"醫學寫作比較不同群體的皮膚反應時，可能使用 Caucasians 這個詞。"},{"en":"If skin colour differs between groups, sunlight effects may appear differently.","zh":"如果群體之間膚色不同，陽光影響可能呈現得不同。"},{"en":"The term is context-specific and can sound dated in modern everyday use.","zh":"這個詞有語境限制，在現代日常用語中可能顯得過時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be somewhat hidden by","meaning":"某程度上被……遮蓋","examples":[{"en":"The natural skin colour is somewhat hidden by acquired pigment.","zh":"天然膚色某程度上被後天色素遮蓋。"},{"en":"To be somewhat hidden by something means to be partly covered or made less visible by it.","zh":"「be somewhat hidden by」某物，意思是部分被它遮住或變得較不明顯。"},{"en":"A road sign may be somewhat hidden by tree branches.","zh":"路牌可能某程度上被樹枝遮蓋。"},{"en":"If pigment covers the natural redness of skin, the original colour becomes harder to see.","zh":"如果色素遮蓋皮膚的天然紅色，原本顏色就較難看見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes partial concealment, not total disappearance.","zh":"這個短語描述部分遮掩，而不是完全消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an acquired layer of","meaning":"後天形成的一層……","examples":[{"en":"Sun exposure creates an acquired layer of pigment.","zh":"日曬會形成後天形成的一層色素。"},{"en":"An acquired layer of something is a layer that develops later because of experience or exposure, not one present from birth.","zh":"「an acquired layer of」某物，是因經歷或接觸而後來形成，而不是天生存在的一層。"},{"en":"A table may develop an acquired layer of dust after being unused for weeks.","zh":"桌子數星期不用後，可能形成後天積聚的一層灰塵。"},{"en":"If skin is repeatedly exposed to sun, an acquired layer of pigment may form.","zh":"如果皮膚反覆接觸陽光，可能形成後天的一層色素。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something gained over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間獲得的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sun-made pigment","meaning":"日曬形成的色素","examples":[{"en":"Sun-made pigment changes the visible tone of the skin.","zh":"日曬形成的色素改變皮膚可見色調。"},{"en":"Sun-made pigment is pigment produced in the skin as a response to sunlight.","zh":"「sun-made pigment」是皮膚因應陽光而產生的色素。"},{"en":"People who work outdoors may develop more sun-made pigment than those who stay indoors.","zh":"在戶外工作的人可能比留在室內的人形成更多日曬色素。"},{"en":"If more pigment forms, the skin may appear darker or more tanned.","zh":"如果形成更多色素，皮膚可能看起來較深色或較曬黑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes colour produced by sun exposure.","zh":"這個短語描述由日曬產生的顏色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"vary in tone","meaning":"色調各有不同","examples":[{"en":"The pigment varies in tone from person to person.","zh":"色素色調因人而異。"},{"en":"To vary in tone means to differ in shade, colour, or quality.","zh":"「vary in tone」意思是在深淺、顏色或質感上有所不同。"},{"en":"Students’ voices vary in tone when they are excited, nervous, or tired.","zh":"學生興奮、緊張或疲倦時，聲音語調各有不同。"},{"en":"If pigment varies in tone, different people’s suntans will not look the same.","zh":"如果色素色調各有不同，不同人的曬黑膚色就不會一樣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes differences in colour or sound quality.","zh":"這個短語描述顏色或聲音質感上的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據；視乎","examples":[{"en":"Skin tone varies according to a person’s complexion and occupation.","zh":"膚色視乎一個人的膚色和職業而有所不同。"},{"en":"According to means depending on or based on a particular factor or source.","zh":"「according to」意思是視乎某因素或根據某來源。"},{"en":"Homework may vary according to the difficulty of the topic.","zh":"功課量可能根據題目難度而不同。"},{"en":"If skin exposure differs by occupation, suntan patterns may also differ.","zh":"如果不同職業的日曬程度不同，曬黑模式也可能不同。"},{"en":"The phrase links a result to the factor that affects it.","zh":"這個短語把結果與影響它的因素連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"complexion","meaning":"膚色；面色","examples":[{"en":"A person’s complexion affects how their suntan appears.","zh":"一個人的膚色影響其曬黑效果。"},{"en":"Complexion means the natural colour, texture, and appearance of a person’s facial skin.","zh":"「complexion」意思是一個人面部皮膚的天然顏色、質感和外觀。"},{"en":"A person’s complexion may look brighter after enough sleep and water.","zh":"一個人有足夠睡眠和飲水後，面色可能看起來更好。"},{"en":"If someone has a fair complexion, sunburn may occur more easily.","zh":"如果某人膚色較淺，可能更容易曬傷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the visible condition and colour of the skin.","zh":"這個短語描述皮膚可見狀態和顏色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"locale plays a big part in","meaning":"地點對……有重大影響","examples":[{"en":"Locale plays a big part in the effectiveness of a suntan.","zh":"地點對曬黑效果有重大影響。"},{"en":"If locale plays a big part in something, the place or environment strongly affects the result.","zh":"如果「locale plays a big part in」某事，意思是地點或環境強烈影響結果。"},{"en":"Locale plays a big part in house prices because transport, schools, and shops matter.","zh":"地點對樓價有重大影響，因為交通、學校和商店都重要。"},{"en":"If sunlight is stronger or cleaner in one place, tanning results may differ there.","zh":"如果某地陽光較強或較純淨，曬黑效果可能不同。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the importance of location.","zh":"這個短語強調位置的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"effectiveness of a suntan","meaning":"曬黑效果","examples":[{"en":"The effectiveness of a suntan depends partly on location.","zh":"曬黑效果部分取決於地點。"},{"en":"Effectiveness of a suntan means how strongly or successfully the skin darkens in the sun.","zh":"「effectiveness of a suntan」意思是皮膚在陽光下變深色的強度或成功程度。"},{"en":"A person may notice different suntan effects at the beach compared with the city.","zh":"一個人可能注意到在海灘與在城市的曬黑效果不同。"},{"en":"If pollution blocks sunlight, the suntan may be less noticeable.","zh":"如果污染阻隔陽光，曬黑效果可能較不明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how well tanning takes place.","zh":"這個短語描述曬黑發生得有多好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mountaintops and beaches","meaning":"山頂和海灘","examples":[{"en":"Mountaintops and beaches receive relatively pure sunlight.","zh":"山頂和海灘接收相對純淨的陽光。"},{"en":"Mountaintops and beaches are high mountain areas and coastal sandy areas exposed to open sunlight.","zh":"「mountaintops and beaches」是高山地區和沿海沙灘地區，通常暴露於開闊陽光下。"},{"en":"People often visit mountaintops and beaches for fresh air, views, and outdoor exercise.","zh":"人們常到山頂和海灘享受新鮮空氣、景色和戶外運動。"},{"en":"If these places have clearer air, sunlight may reach people with less filtering by pollution.","zh":"如果這些地方空氣較清澈，陽光可能較少被污染過濾而到達人們身上。"},{"en":"The phrase names locations often associated with strong natural sunlight.","zh":"這個短語指出常與強烈自然陽光有關的地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"nonpareil sun spas","meaning":"無可比擬的日光浴勝地","examples":[{"en":"Mountaintops and beaches are described as nonpareil sun spas.","zh":"山頂和海灘被形容為無可比擬的日光浴勝地。"},{"en":"Nonpareil sun spas means places for sun exposure that are unmatched or unusually excellent.","zh":"「nonpareil sun spas」意思是無可匹敵或特別出色的日曬場所。"},{"en":"A clean seaside resort may be advertised as a nonpareil place for rest and sunshine.","zh":"乾淨海濱度假村可能被宣傳為休息和享受陽光的無可比擬之地。"},{"en":"If a place has pure air and strong sunlight, writers may praise it as an ideal sun location.","zh":"如果某地有純淨空氣和強烈陽光，作者可能稱讚它是理想日光地點。"},{"en":"The phrase is literary and means an incomparable place for sun treatment or sunbathing.","zh":"這個短語較文雅，意思是無可比擬的日光治療或日光浴場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"receive purer sunlight","meaning":"接收較純淨的陽光","examples":[{"en":"Beaches and mountaintops receive purer sunlight than urban areas.","zh":"海灘和山頂比市區接收較純淨的陽光。"},{"en":"To receive purer sunlight means to get sunlight that is less blocked or polluted by dust, smoke, or smog.","zh":"「receive purer sunlight」意思是接收到較少被塵埃、煙霧或煙霞阻隔或污染的陽光。"},{"en":"A rural park may receive purer sunlight than a busy road surrounded by traffic fumes.","zh":"鄉郊公園可能比被交通廢氣包圍的繁忙道路接收較純淨的陽光。"},{"en":"If air is cleaner, sunlight may reach the skin with fewer pollutants in the way.","zh":"如果空氣較清潔，陽光到達皮膚時路上可能有較少污染物。"},{"en":"The phrase compares sunlight quality across locations.","zh":"這個短語比較不同地點的陽光質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the rest of the land","meaning":"其他陸地地區","examples":[{"en":"These locations receive purer sunlight than the rest of the land.","zh":"這些地點比其他陸地地區接收較純淨的陽光。"},{"en":"The rest of the land means all other land areas apart from the places already mentioned.","zh":"「the rest of the land」意思是除了已提及地方以外的所有其他陸地地區。"},{"en":"A mountain village may be cooler than the rest of the land during summer.","zh":"山村在夏天可能比其他陸地地區更涼快。"},{"en":"If beaches and mountaintops differ from other areas, their sunlight may have special qualities.","zh":"如果海灘和山頂與其他地區不同，其陽光可能有特殊質素。"},{"en":"The phrase separates specific places from all remaining areas.","zh":"這個短語把特定地方與其餘所有地區分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"urban areas","meaning":"市區","examples":[{"en":"Urban areas often contain smoke, dust, and smog.","zh":"市區通常含有煙、塵和煙霞。"},{"en":"Urban areas are towns and cities with many buildings, roads, people, and businesses.","zh":"「urban areas」是有許多建築物、道路、人口和商業活動的城鎮和城市。"},{"en":"Traffic noise and air pollution are common problems in urban areas.","zh":"交通噪音和空氣污染是市區常見問題。"},{"en":"If urban areas have heavy pollution, sunlight may be filtered before reaching people.","zh":"如果市區污染嚴重，陽光到達人們身上前可能被過濾。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts city environments with rural or natural areas.","zh":"這個短語把城市環境與鄉郊或自然地區作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"smoke and smog","meaning":"煙霧和煙霞","examples":[{"en":"Smoke and smog reduce the beneficial effects of sunlight.","zh":"煙霧和煙霞會減少陽光的有益效果。"},{"en":"Smoke and smog are dirty air conditions caused by burning, traffic, industry, or pollution.","zh":"「smoke and smog」是由燃燒、交通、工業或污染造成的污濁空氣狀況。"},{"en":"On days with heavy smoke and smog, people may avoid outdoor exercise.","zh":"在煙霧和煙霞嚴重的日子，人們可能避免戶外運動。"},{"en":"If smoke and smog filter sunlight, the body may receive less of its healthy effects.","zh":"如果煙霧和煙霞過濾陽光，身體可能較少得到其健康效果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes polluted air that affects visibility and health.","zh":"這個短語描述影響能見度和健康的污染空氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"act as a filter","meaning":"起過濾作用","examples":[{"en":"Urban pollution acts as a filter for sunlight.","zh":"城市污染對陽光起過濾作用。"},{"en":"To act as a filter means to block, reduce, or screen out part of something.","zh":"「act as a filter」意思是阻擋、減少或篩走某物的一部分。"},{"en":"Curtains act as a filter by reducing strong afternoon sunlight in a room.","zh":"窗簾透過減少房間內強烈午後陽光而起過濾作用。"},{"en":"If pollution filters sunlight, less direct light may reach the skin.","zh":"如果污染過濾陽光，較少直接光線可能到達皮膚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something functioning like a screen or barrier.","zh":"這個短語描述某物像屏障或過濾層一樣運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"remove the healthy properties of","meaning":"消除……的有益特性","examples":[{"en":"Pollution may remove some of the healthy properties of sunlight.","zh":"污染可能消除陽光的一些有益特性。"},{"en":"To remove the healthy properties of something means to take away the parts that make it beneficial.","zh":"「remove the healthy properties of」某物，意思是拿走令它有益的部分。"},{"en":"Overcooking vegetables may remove some of their healthy properties.","zh":"過度烹煮蔬菜可能消除它們的一些有益特性。"},{"en":"If smog blocks useful sunlight, people may receive fewer health benefits from being outdoors.","zh":"如果煙霞阻擋有用陽光，人們在戶外可能得到較少健康好處。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reducing or losing beneficial qualities.","zh":"這個短語描述有益特質減少或失去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the seashore","meaning":"海濱","examples":[{"en":"The seashore may be one of the best places for fresh air and sunlight.","zh":"海濱可能是享受新鮮空氣和陽光的最佳地方之一。"},{"en":"The seashore is the land along the edge of the sea.","zh":"「the seashore」是海邊沿岸的陸地。"},{"en":"Families often walk along the seashore to enjoy wind, waves, and open space.","zh":"家庭常沿海濱散步，享受海風、海浪和開闊空間。"},{"en":"If coastal air is cleaner, the seashore may feel healthier than crowded city streets.","zh":"如果沿海空氣較清潔，海濱可能比擠迫市區街道感覺更健康。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the area where land meets the sea.","zh":"這個短語描述陸地與海洋交接的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be estimated to have","meaning":"據估計含有","examples":[{"en":"Seashore air is estimated to have slightly more oxygen.","zh":"據估計，海濱空氣含有略多氧氣。"},{"en":"To be estimated to have something means people calculate or judge that it probably contains it.","zh":"「be estimated to have」某物，意思是人們計算或判斷它很可能含有該物。"},{"en":"A school hall may be estimated to have space for 300 students.","zh":"據估計，學校禮堂可容納300名學生。"},{"en":"If coastal air is estimated to contain more oxygen, writers may use this to explain its health appeal.","zh":"如果據估計沿海空氣含有較多氧氣，作者可能用這點解釋其健康吸引力。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate judgment, not an exact certainty.","zh":"這個短語提供近似判斷，而不是絕對確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a fifth of a per cent","meaning":"百分之零點二","examples":[{"en":"Coastal air may contain a fifth of a per cent more oxygen.","zh":"沿海空氣可能含有多百分之零點二的氧氣。"},{"en":"A fifth of a per cent means 0.2 percent.","zh":"「a fifth of a per cent」意思是百分之零點二。"},{"en":"A price increase of a fifth of a per cent is very small compared with a 10 percent increase.","zh":"百分之零點二的加價相比百分之十的加價非常小。"},{"en":"If oxygen is only slightly higher, the difference may still be described precisely.","zh":"如果氧氣只略高，差異仍可被精確描述。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses a very small percentage.","zh":"這個短語表達非常小的百分比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"inland air","meaning":"內陸空氣","examples":[{"en":"Seashore air may be cleaner than inland air.","zh":"海濱空氣可能比內陸空氣更清潔。"},{"en":"Inland air is air found away from the coast, farther inside the land.","zh":"「inland air」是遠離海岸、較深入陸地地區的空氣。"},{"en":"Inland air in a busy city may contain more dust and traffic pollution than coastal air.","zh":"繁忙城市的內陸空氣可能比沿海空氣含有更多塵埃和交通污染。"},{"en":"If inland air contains more allergens, some people may feel better near the sea.","zh":"如果內陸空氣含有更多致敏原，有些人在海邊可能感覺較好。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts air away from the sea with air at the coast.","zh":"這個短語把遠離海洋的空氣與沿海空氣作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be free of","meaning":"不含；沒有","examples":[{"en":"Coastal air is relatively free of city dust and allergens.","zh":"沿海空氣相對不含城市塵埃和致敏原。"},{"en":"To be free of something means to have none or very little of it.","zh":"「be free of」某物，意思是沒有或幾乎沒有該物。"},{"en":"A good study room should be free of loud noise and distractions.","zh":"好的自修室應沒有巨大噪音和令人分心的事物。"},{"en":"If air is free of dust and pollen, people with allergies may breathe more comfortably.","zh":"如果空氣沒有塵埃和花粉，過敏人士可能呼吸得較舒服。"},{"en":"The phrase describes absence or near absence of something unwanted.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有或幾乎沒有不想要的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pollen and allergens","meaning":"花粉和致敏原","examples":[{"en":"Coastal air may contain less pollen and fewer allergens.","zh":"沿海空氣可能含有較少花粉和較少致敏原。"},{"en":"Pollen and allergens are particles that can trigger allergic reactions, such as sneezing or itchy eyes.","zh":"「pollen and allergens」是可以引發過敏反應的微粒，例如打噴嚏或眼癢。"},{"en":"Some people avoid parks during spring because pollen and allergens make their nose run.","zh":"有些人春天避免到公園，因為花粉和致敏原令他們流鼻水。"},{"en":"If the air has fewer allergens, sensitive people may feel healthier outdoors.","zh":"如果空氣含有較少致敏原，敏感人士在戶外可能感覺較健康。"},{"en":"The phrase describes substances that can cause allergies.","zh":"這個短語描述會引起過敏的物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"nature’s greatest health giver","meaning":"大自然最重要的健康來源","examples":[{"en":"The sun has long been called nature’s greatest health giver.","zh":"太陽長久以來被稱為大自然最重要的健康來源。"},{"en":"Nature’s greatest health giver means a natural source believed to provide major health benefits.","zh":"「nature’s greatest health giver」意思是被認為提供重大健康益處的自然來源。"},{"en":"Fresh air is sometimes described as a natural health giver because it helps people feel refreshed.","zh":"新鮮空氣有時被形容為自然健康來源，因為它令人感到精神恢復。"},{"en":"If sunlight helps mood, skin, and vitamin D production, people may praise it in this way.","zh":"如果陽光幫助心情、皮膚和維他命 D 生成，人們可能這樣讚美它。"},{"en":"The phrase is positive and somewhat poetic, not a strict scientific label.","zh":"這個短語是正面且略帶詩意的說法，不是嚴格科學標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"play a chief role in","meaning":"在……中擔當主要角色","examples":[{"en":"Sunlight has played a chief role in some health treatments.","zh":"陽光在某些健康治療中擔當主要角色。"},{"en":"To play a chief role in something means to be one of the most important parts of it.","zh":"「play a chief role in」某事，意思是在其中成為最重要部分之一。"},{"en":"Good communication plays a chief role in successful teamwork.","zh":"良好溝通在成功團隊合作中擔當主要角色。"},{"en":"If sunlight is central to a treatment, doctors may control exposure carefully.","zh":"如果陽光是治療的核心，醫生可能會小心控制曝曬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes major importance in a process or situation.","zh":"這個短語描述在過程或情況中的重大重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"health resorts","meaning":"療養勝地","examples":[{"en":"Sun treatment has long been used at health resorts.","zh":"日光治療長久以來在療養勝地使用。"},{"en":"Health resorts are places people visit to rest, recover, or receive health-related treatments.","zh":"「health resorts」是人們到訪以休息、復原或接受健康相關治療的地方。"},{"en":"A mountain health resort may offer fresh air, exercise, and medical supervision.","zh":"山區療養勝地可能提供新鮮空氣、運動和醫療監督。"},{"en":"If a resort uses sunlight as treatment, location and climate become important.","zh":"如果療養地使用陽光作治療，地點和氣候就變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes places connected with rest and health improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述與休息和改善健康有關的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the father of heliotherapy","meaning":"日光療法之父","examples":[{"en":"August Rollier is described as the Swiss father of heliotherapy.","zh":"August Rollier 被形容為瑞士日光療法之父。"},{"en":"The father of heliotherapy means a person regarded as a major early leader or founder of sunlight treatment.","zh":"「the father of heliotherapy」意思是被視為日光治療早期重要領袖或創立者的人。"},{"en":"A scientist may be called the father of a field if he helped establish its methods.","zh":"如果科學家幫助建立某領域的方法，他可能被稱為該領域之父。"},{"en":"If Rollier opened a specialist sun-treatment centre, later writers may give him this title.","zh":"如果 Rollier 開設專門日光治療中心，後來作者可能給他這個稱號。"},{"en":"The phrase is an honorary title, not a literal family relationship.","zh":"這個短語是榮譽稱號，不是字面上的父子關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"heliotherapy","meaning":"日光療法","examples":[{"en":"Heliotherapy uses sunlight as part of medical treatment.","zh":"日光療法使用陽光作為醫療治療的一部分。"},{"en":"Heliotherapy is a form of treatment that uses controlled exposure to sunlight.","zh":"「heliotherapy」是一種使用受控制日曬的治療方式。"},{"en":"A doctor practising heliotherapy would need to consider skin condition, timing, and sun strength.","zh":"實行日光療法的醫生需要考慮皮膚狀況、時間和陽光強度。"},{"en":"If sunlight is used too long, heliotherapy may become harmful rather than helpful.","zh":"如果陽光使用太久，日光療法可能變得有害而不是有益。"},{"en":"The phrase names a medical approach based on sunlight.","zh":"這個短語指出一種以陽光為基礎的醫療方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"high-Alps sanatorium","meaning":"阿爾卑斯山高地療養院","examples":[{"en":"Rollier opened a high-Alps sanatorium in 1903.","zh":"Rollier 於1903年開設了一所阿爾卑斯山高地療養院。"},{"en":"A high-Alps sanatorium is a medical rest centre located high in the Alps.","zh":"「high-Alps sanatorium」是位於阿爾卑斯山高處的醫療療養中心。"},{"en":"Patients might visit a mountain sanatorium for fresh air, sunlight, and supervised recovery.","zh":"病人可能到山區療養院享受新鮮空氣、陽光和受監督復原。"},{"en":"If a sanatorium is high in the mountains, it may receive cleaner air and stronger sunlight.","zh":"如果療養院位於高山，它可能接收更清潔空氣和更強陽光。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specialised health facility in a high mountain region.","zh":"這個短語指出高山地區的專門健康設施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the sun cure","meaning":"日光療法","examples":[{"en":"The sun cure has been used to treat several skin conditions.","zh":"日光療法曾用於治療幾種皮膚狀況。"},{"en":"The sun cure is a treatment approach that uses sunlight to improve certain health problems.","zh":"「the sun cure」是一種利用陽光改善某些健康問題的治療方法。"},{"en":"In older medical practice, patients might be sent outdoors for a controlled sun cure.","zh":"在較舊醫療做法中，病人可能被安排到戶外接受受控制的日光療法。"},{"en":"If sunlight helps a skin condition, the treatment must still avoid burning the skin.","zh":"如果陽光幫助皮膚病，治療仍必須避免曬傷皮膚。"},{"en":"The phrase is another way to describe heliotherapy or sunlight treatment.","zh":"這個短語是日光療法或陽光治療的另一種說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a major factor in","meaning":"……中的重要因素","examples":[{"en":"Sunlight may be a major factor in the treatment of some diseases.","zh":"陽光可能是某些疾病治療中的重要因素。"},{"en":"A major factor in something is an important cause, influence, or part of the result.","zh":"「a major factor in」某事，是結果中的重要原因、影響或部分。"},{"en":"Regular practice is a major factor in language improvement.","zh":"定期練習是語言進步中的重要因素。"},{"en":"If sunlight is a major factor in treatment, doctors must control dose and timing carefully.","zh":"如果陽光是治療中的重要因素，醫生必須小心控制劑量和時間。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies something highly influential.","zh":"這個短語指出具有高度影響力的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"treatment of skin diseases","meaning":"皮膚病治療","examples":[{"en":"Sunlight has been used in the treatment of several skin diseases.","zh":"陽光曾用於幾種皮膚病治療。"},{"en":"Treatment of skin diseases means medical care used to improve illnesses that affect the skin.","zh":"「treatment of skin diseases」意思是用來改善影響皮膚疾病的醫療護理。"},{"en":"Creams, light therapy, and medicine may be used in the treatment of skin diseases.","zh":"藥膏、光療和藥物可能用於皮膚病治療。"},{"en":"If a skin disease improves with controlled sunlight, doctors may include it in treatment.","zh":"如果皮膚病在受控制陽光下改善，醫生可能把它納入治療。"},{"en":"The phrase describes medical management of skin conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述對皮膚狀況的醫療處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"range from…to…","meaning":"範圍由……至……","examples":[{"en":"The conditions range from acne and eczema to ulcers and wounds.","zh":"這些病況範圍由暗瘡和濕疹至潰瘍和傷口。"},{"en":"To range from A to B means to include many types between two examples or limits.","zh":"「range from A to B」意思是包括兩個例子或界限之間的許多種類。"},{"en":"School activities range from sports and music to debate and volunteer work.","zh":"學校活動範圍由運動和音樂至辯論和義工服務。"},{"en":"If symptoms range from mild to serious, treatment must depend on the patient’s condition.","zh":"如果症狀由輕微至嚴重不等，治療就必須視乎病人狀況。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a broad variety.","zh":"這個短語顯示廣泛多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"acne and eczema","meaning":"暗瘡和濕疹","examples":[{"en":"Acne and eczema are among the skin conditions mentioned.","zh":"暗瘡和濕疹是文中提到的皮膚病之一。"},{"en":"Acne and eczema are common skin problems involving spots, inflammation, itching, or irritation.","zh":"「acne and eczema」是常見皮膚問題，涉及粉刺、發炎、痕癢或刺激。"},{"en":"A teenager may see a doctor if acne and eczema affect confidence or sleep.","zh":"如果暗瘡和濕疹影響信心或睡眠，青少年可能看醫生。"},{"en":"If skin conditions are irritated by heat or sunlight, treatment must be adjusted carefully.","zh":"如果皮膚病被熱力或陽光刺激，治療必須小心調整。"},{"en":"The phrase names two familiar skin conditions.","zh":"這個短語指出兩種熟悉的皮膚狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ulcers and wounds","meaning":"潰瘍和傷口","examples":[{"en":"Sun treatment has also been used for ulcers and wounds.","zh":"日光治療也曾用於潰瘍和傷口。"},{"en":"Ulcers and wounds are damaged areas of skin or tissue that may need healing.","zh":"「ulcers and wounds」是皮膚或組織受損、可能需要癒合的地方。"},{"en":"A nurse cleans wounds carefully to prevent infection.","zh":"護士會仔細清潔傷口以防感染。"},{"en":"If ulcers do not heal properly, patients may need medical treatment and close monitoring.","zh":"如果潰瘍不能正常癒合，病人可能需要醫療治療和密切監察。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to visible injuries or sores on the body.","zh":"這個短語指身體上可見的損傷或瘡口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be helpful to persons suffering from","meaning":"對患有……的人有幫助","examples":[{"en":"Sun treatment may be helpful to persons suffering from general weakness.","zh":"日光治療可能對患有全身衰弱的人有幫助。"},{"en":"To be helpful to persons suffering from something means to benefit people who have that problem.","zh":"「be helpful to persons suffering from」某病，意思是對有該問題的人有益。"},{"en":"Gentle exercise may be helpful to persons suffering from stress or poor sleep.","zh":"輕量運動可能對患有壓力或睡眠欠佳的人有幫助。"},{"en":"If a treatment improves energy or mood, it may help people with general weakness.","zh":"如果治療改善精力或心情，它可能幫助全身衰弱的人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes who may benefit from a treatment or support.","zh":"這個短語描述哪些人可能從治療或支援中受益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"general debility","meaning":"全身衰弱","examples":[{"en":"Some specialists recommend sunlight for people suffering from general debility.","zh":"有些專家建議患有全身衰弱的人接觸陽光。"},{"en":"General debility means overall physical weakness or lack of strength.","zh":"「general debility」意思是整體身體虛弱或缺乏力量。"},{"en":"After a long illness, a patient may suffer general debility and need rest and nutrition.","zh":"長期患病後，病人可能出現全身衰弱並需要休息和營養。"},{"en":"If sunlight improves appetite or energy, it may be recommended for general weakness.","zh":"如果陽光改善食慾或精力，它可能被建議用於一般虛弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad weakness, not one specific disease.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛虛弱，而不是某一特定疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"repeated colds","meaning":"反覆感冒","examples":[{"en":"Sun treatment has been suggested for people with repeated colds.","zh":"日光治療曾被建議用於反覆感冒的人。"},{"en":"Repeated colds are colds that happen again and again over time.","zh":"「repeated colds」是隨時間一次又一次出現的感冒。"},{"en":"A child with repeated colds may miss many school days during winter.","zh":"反覆感冒的孩子可能在冬天缺課很多天。"},{"en":"If someone catches colds often, doctors may look at sleep, nutrition, and immune health.","zh":"如果某人經常感冒，醫生可能會查看睡眠、營養和免疫健康。"},{"en":"The phrase describes frequent episodes of the common cold.","zh":"這個短語描述普通感冒頻繁發作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"respiratory diseases","meaning":"呼吸系統疾病","examples":[{"en":"Some respiratory diseases may improve with appropriate sun treatment.","zh":"某些呼吸系統疾病可能因適當日光治療而改善。"},{"en":"Respiratory diseases are illnesses that affect breathing organs such as the lungs, throat, or airways.","zh":"「respiratory diseases」是影響肺、喉嚨或氣道等呼吸器官的疾病。"},{"en":"Asthma and bronchitis are examples of respiratory diseases.","zh":"哮喘和支氣管炎是呼吸系統疾病的例子。"},{"en":"If breathing is affected, patients may need clean air, medicine, and careful treatment.","zh":"如果呼吸受影響，病人可能需要潔淨空氣、藥物和小心治療。"},{"en":"The phrase describes diseases connected with breathing.","zh":"這個短語描述與呼吸有關的疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"and the like","meaning":"以及類似疾病","examples":[{"en":"The treatment has been suggested for influenza, colds, and the like.","zh":"這種治療曾被建議用於流感、感冒以及類似疾病。"},{"en":"And the like means and similar things.","zh":"「and the like」意思是以及類似事物。"},{"en":"Students should bring pens, notebooks, calculators, and the like to class.","zh":"學生應帶筆、筆記簿、計算機以及類似用品上課。"},{"en":"If a treatment is said to help colds and the like, it may be linked with similar minor illnesses.","zh":"如果一種治療被說能幫助感冒及類似疾病，它可能與相似輕微疾病有關。"},{"en":"The phrase avoids listing every example.","zh":"這個短語避免列出每一個例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"after a long winter","meaning":"經過漫長冬季後","examples":[{"en":"The return of sunlight after a long winter can stimulate the body.","zh":"經過漫長冬季後陽光回歸，可以刺激身體。"},{"en":"After a long winter means following many cold, dark months with little warmth or sunlight.","zh":"「after a long winter」意思是在經歷許多寒冷、陰暗、少溫暖或少陽光的月份之後。"},{"en":"After a long winter, many people enjoy walking outside again.","zh":"經過漫長冬季後，許多人喜歡再次到戶外散步。"},{"en":"If people have lacked sunlight for months, returning sunlight may feel especially energising.","zh":"如果人們數月缺乏陽光，重新接觸陽光可能特別令人有精神。"},{"en":"The phrase gives seasonal context for a change in health or mood.","zh":"這個短語為健康或心情變化提供季節背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"return to the sun","meaning":"重新接觸陽光","examples":[{"en":"The return to the sun may provide a general stimulus to the body.","zh":"重新接觸陽光可能為身體提供一般刺激。"},{"en":"Return to the sun means going back to sunlight after a period with little exposure.","zh":"「return to the sun」意思是在一段少接觸陽光後重新接觸陽光。"},{"en":"Office workers may feel refreshed by a return to the sun during a lunch break.","zh":"辦公室員工午飯時間重新接觸陽光，可能感到精神恢復。"},{"en":"If people have stayed indoors for weeks, sunlight may feel more powerful when they go outside again.","zh":"如果人們數星期待在室內，再次外出時陽光可能感覺更有力量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes renewed exposure to sunlight.","zh":"這個短語描述重新曝露於陽光下。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a general stimulus to","meaning":"對……的一般刺激","examples":[{"en":"Sunlight can act as a general stimulus to the body.","zh":"陽光可以對身體起一般刺激作用。"},{"en":"A general stimulus to something is something that broadly activates or energises it.","zh":"「a general stimulus to」某物，是廣泛激活或使其更有活力的東西。"},{"en":"Morning exercise can be a general stimulus to the mind before school.","zh":"早晨運動可以在上學前對心智起一般刺激作用。"},{"en":"If sunlight stimulates the body, people may feel more awake or lively.","zh":"如果陽光刺激身體，人們可能感到更清醒或更有活力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broad activating effect.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛的激活效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"more potent if","meaning":"如果……，作用會更強","examples":[{"en":"The effect may be more potent if sunlight has been lacking.","zh":"如果一直缺乏陽光，效果可能會更強。"},{"en":"More potent if means stronger when a certain condition is true.","zh":"「more potent if」意思是在某條件成立時作用更強。"},{"en":"Coffee may feel more potent if a person has not slept enough.","zh":"如果一個人睡眠不足，咖啡可能感覺作用更強。"},{"en":"If the body has lacked sunlight, the return of sunlight may produce a stronger response.","zh":"如果身體一直缺乏陽光，陽光回歸可能產生更強反應。"},{"en":"The phrase connects increased strength with a condition.","zh":"這個短語把強度增加與條件連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be applied after","meaning":"在……之後使用","examples":[{"en":"Sunlight may be more effective when applied after a period without it.","zh":"陽光在一段缺乏陽光之後使用時，可能更有效。"},{"en":"To be applied after something means to be used following a particular period or event.","zh":"「be applied after」某事，意思是在某時期或事件之後被使用。"},{"en":"A moisturiser is often applied after washing the face.","zh":"潤膚霜通常在洗臉後使用。"},{"en":"If sunlight is used after a dark winter, its effect may feel stronger.","zh":"如果陽光在黑暗冬季後被使用，其效果可能感覺更強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes timing: one action comes after another.","zh":"這個短語描述時間安排：一個行動在另一個之後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a period when it has been lacking","meaning":"一段缺乏陽光的時期","examples":[{"en":"The effect is stronger after a period when sunlight has been lacking.","zh":"在一段缺乏陽光的時期後，效果會更強。"},{"en":"A period when something has been lacking is a time during which there has not been enough of it.","zh":"「a period when it has been lacking」是某物不足的一段時間。"},{"en":"After a period when sleep has been lacking, a full night’s rest may feel especially restorative.","zh":"在一段缺乏睡眠的時期後，一整晚休息可能感覺特別恢復精神。"},{"en":"If sunlight has been absent for weeks, the body may respond strongly when it returns.","zh":"如果陽光缺席數星期，當它回來時身體可能反應強烈。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a time of shortage or absence.","zh":"這個短語描述短缺或缺乏的一段時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"gradually lose its effect","meaning":"逐漸失去作用","examples":[{"en":"Sunlight gradually loses its beneficial effect if exposure continues too long.","zh":"如果曝曬持續太久，陽光會逐漸失去其有益作用。"},{"en":"To gradually lose its effect means to become less useful or powerful over time.","zh":"「gradually lose its effect」意思是隨時間變得較不有用或較不有力。"},{"en":"A painkiller may gradually lose its effect if it is taken too often without medical advice.","zh":"如果止痛藥在沒有醫療建議下太常服用，可能逐漸失去作用。"},{"en":"If sun exposure continues too long, benefit may decrease and harm may increase.","zh":"如果日曬持續太久，好處可能減少而傷害可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a slow reduction in usefulness.","zh":"這個短語描述有用性慢慢下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"over-prolonged exposure","meaning":"過度延長的曝曬","examples":[{"en":"Over-prolonged exposure may reduce the benefits of sunlight.","zh":"過度延長的曝曬可能減少陽光的好處。"},{"en":"Over-prolonged exposure means being exposed to something for too long.","zh":"「over-prolonged exposure」意思是接觸某物的時間太長。"},{"en":"Over-prolonged exposure to loud music can damage hearing.","zh":"過度長時間接觸大聲音樂可能損害聽力。"},{"en":"If a person stays in strong sunlight for too long, the body may suffer instead of benefit.","zh":"如果一個人在強烈陽光下待太久，身體可能受害而不是受益。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against excessive duration.","zh":"這個短語警告時間過長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"even when not excessive","meaning":"即使並不過量","examples":[{"en":"Exposure may become less helpful even when it is not excessive.","zh":"曝曬即使並不過量，也可能變得較少幫助。"},{"en":"Even when not excessive means although it has not reached an obviously too-much level.","zh":"「even when not excessive」意思是雖然尚未達到明顯過多的程度。"},{"en":"Screen time may tire the eyes even when it is not excessive.","zh":"使用屏幕即使並不過量，也可能令眼睛疲累。"},{"en":"If the benefit fades before exposure becomes extreme, timing still matters.","zh":"如果好處在曝曬變得極端之前已減弱，時間安排仍然重要。"},{"en":"The phrase adds a careful qualification to a warning.","zh":"這個短語為警告加入謹慎限定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"over many years of study","meaning":"經過多年研究","examples":[{"en":"Dermatologists reached their conclusions over many years of study.","zh":"皮膚科醫生經過多年研究得出結論。"},{"en":"Over many years of study means after a long period of research and observation.","zh":"「over many years of study」意思是在長時間研究和觀察後。"},{"en":"Teachers improve their understanding of students over many years of classroom experience.","zh":"老師經過多年課堂經驗，會更了解學生。"},{"en":"If doctors study a problem for many years, their conclusions may become more reliable.","zh":"如果醫生多年研究一個問題，其結論可能更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses long-term evidence gathering.","zh":"這個短語強調長期收集證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dermatologists","meaning":"皮膚科醫生","examples":[{"en":"Dermatologists have studied the harmful effects of prolonged sunlight.","zh":"皮膚科醫生研究了長時間陽光照射的有害影響。"},{"en":"Dermatologists are doctors who specialise in skin, hair, and nail conditions.","zh":"「dermatologists」是專門處理皮膚、頭髮和指甲狀況的醫生。"},{"en":"A person with severe acne or unusual moles may visit a dermatologist.","zh":"有嚴重暗瘡或異常痣的人可能去看皮膚科醫生。"},{"en":"If dermatologists warn about sunlight, their advice is based on skin-health expertise.","zh":"如果皮膚科醫生警告陽光問題，其建議是基於皮膚健康專業知識。"},{"en":"The word names medical specialists in skin health.","zh":"這個詞指出皮膚健康方面的醫學專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"excessive exposure to sunlight","meaning":"過度曝曬於陽光","examples":[{"en":"Excessive exposure to sunlight can cause permanent skin damage.","zh":"過度曝曬於陽光可以造成永久性皮膚損傷。"},{"en":"Excessive exposure to sunlight means spending too much time in the sun, especially without protection.","zh":"「excessive exposure to sunlight」意思是在陽光下停留太久，尤其沒有保護。"},{"en":"A worker may suffer excessive exposure to sunlight if they work outdoors all day without a hat.","zh":"如果工人整天在戶外工作又不戴帽，可能過度曝曬於陽光。"},{"en":"If exposure is excessive, the skin may burn, age faster, or develop disease risks.","zh":"如果曝曬過量，皮膚可能曬傷、加速老化或增加患病風險。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against too much sun.","zh":"這個短語警告不要接觸太多陽光。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be responsible for","meaning":"導致；是……的成因","examples":[{"en":"Long-term sun exposure is responsible for many cases of skin cancer.","zh":"長期日曬導致許多皮膚癌個案。"},{"en":"To be responsible for something means to cause it or be the reason for it.","zh":"「be responsible for」某事，意思是造成它或成為它的原因。"},{"en":"Poor sleep may be responsible for a student’s weak concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可能是學生上課專注力弱的成因。"},{"en":"If sunlight causes many skin cancer cases, prevention becomes important.","zh":"如果陽光造成許多皮膚癌個案，預防就變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a cause.","zh":"這個短語指出原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a large proportion of","meaning":"很大比例的……","examples":[{"en":"Sun exposure is responsible for a large proportion of skin cancer cases.","zh":"日曬是很大比例皮膚癌個案的成因。"},{"en":"A large proportion of something means a big part or percentage of the total.","zh":"「a large proportion of」某物，意思是整體中的一大部分或百分比。"},{"en":"A large proportion of students may use public transport to get to school.","zh":"很大比例的學生可能使用公共交通上學。"},{"en":"If a large proportion of illness is linked to one cause, reducing that cause can have a major effect.","zh":"如果很大比例的疾病與一個原因有關，減少該原因可以有重大效果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a significant share of a whole.","zh":"這個短語描述整體中的重要份額。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"skin cancer","meaning":"皮膚癌","examples":[{"en":"Excessive sunlight can increase the risk of skin cancer.","zh":"過量陽光可以增加皮膚癌風險。"},{"en":"Skin cancer is cancer that develops in skin cells, often linked to sun damage.","zh":"「skin cancer」是在皮膚細胞中發展的癌症，常與陽光傷害有關。"},{"en":"Doctors may check unusual moles because they can sometimes be signs of skin cancer.","zh":"醫生可能檢查異常痣，因為它們有時可能是皮膚癌跡象。"},{"en":"If people protect their skin from excessive sun, they may reduce long-term risk.","zh":"如果人們保護皮膚免受過度日曬，就可能減低長期風險。"},{"en":"The phrase names a serious disease affecting the skin.","zh":"這個短語指出影響皮膚的嚴重疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"year-round outdoor workers","meaning":"全年在戶外工作的人","examples":[{"en":"Year-round outdoor workers face particularly high sun exposure.","zh":"全年在戶外工作的人面對特別高的日曬量。"},{"en":"Year-round outdoor workers are people who work outside throughout the whole year.","zh":"「year-round outdoor workers」是全年都在戶外工作的人。"},{"en":"Farmers, lifeguards, builders, and delivery workers may be year-round outdoor workers.","zh":"農民、救生員、建築工人和送貨員可能是全年在戶外工作的人。"},{"en":"If people work outdoors all year, their skin receives much more sunlight over time.","zh":"如果人們全年在戶外工作，皮膚隨時間接收的陽光會多很多。"},{"en":"The phrase describes workers with constant outdoor exposure.","zh":"這個短語描述持續戶外曝曬的工人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"face the greatest risk of","meaning":"面對……的最大風險","examples":[{"en":"Outdoor workers face the greatest risk of permanent skin damage.","zh":"戶外工作者面對永久性皮膚損傷的最大風險。"},{"en":"To face the greatest risk of something means to be most likely to experience that harm or problem.","zh":"「face the greatest risk of」某事，意思是最有可能經歷該傷害或問題。"},{"en":"Pedestrians face the greatest risk of injury when roads have no crossings.","zh":"當道路沒有過路處，行人面對受傷的最大風險。"},{"en":"If workers spend all day in the sun, their long-term skin risk becomes especially high.","zh":"如果工人整天在陽光下，其長期皮膚風險會特別高。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the group most exposed to danger.","zh":"這個短語指出最暴露於危險的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"permanent skin damage","meaning":"永久性皮膚損傷","examples":[{"en":"Years of sunlight can cause permanent skin damage.","zh":"多年陽光照射可以造成永久性皮膚損傷。"},{"en":"Permanent skin damage is lasting harm to the skin that does not fully disappear.","zh":"「permanent skin damage」是不能完全消失的長期皮膚傷害。"},{"en":"Repeated sunburn may lead to permanent skin damage over time.","zh":"反覆曬傷可能隨時間導致永久性皮膚損傷。"},{"en":"If skin damage is permanent, prevention is better than trying to repair it later.","zh":"如果皮膚損傷是永久性的，預防比日後修復更好。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long-lasting injury to the skin.","zh":"這個短語描述皮膚的長期傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"heavily exposed","meaning":"大量暴露於陽光下的","examples":[{"en":"The hands and face are often the most heavily exposed parts of the body.","zh":"雙手和臉通常是身體最常大量暴露於陽光下的部位。"},{"en":"Heavily exposed means receiving a lot of contact with something, especially a harmful condition.","zh":"「heavily exposed」意思是大量接觸某物，尤其是有害環境。"},{"en":"A cyclist’s arms may be heavily exposed to sunlight during a long ride.","zh":"長途踩單車時，騎手的手臂可能大量暴露於陽光下。"},{"en":"If the face and hands are rarely covered, they receive more sun over many years.","zh":"如果臉和手很少被遮蓋，多年來就會接收更多陽光。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong or frequent exposure.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈或頻繁曝露。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"first line of defence","meaning":"第一道防線","examples":[{"en":"The skin’s natural oils form the first line of defence against sunlight.","zh":"皮膚的天然油脂形成對抗陽光的第一道防線。"},{"en":"The first line of defence is the first protection against harm or danger.","zh":"「first line of defence」是面對傷害或危險時的第一層保護。"},{"en":"Washing hands is the first line of defence against many infections.","zh":"洗手是防止許多感染的第一道防線。"},{"en":"If the first protective layer is removed, the body becomes more vulnerable.","zh":"如果第一層保護被移除，身體會變得更脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the earliest or most immediate protection.","zh":"這個短語描述最早或最即時的保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"natural fatty matter","meaning":"天然脂質","examples":[{"en":"The skin produces natural fatty matter that helps protect it.","zh":"皮膚產生有助保護自身的天然脂質。"},{"en":"Natural fatty matter is oily material naturally produced by the skin.","zh":"「natural fatty matter」是皮膚自然產生的油性物質。"},{"en":"Some people have more natural fatty matter on the face, so their skin looks oily.","zh":"有些人面上有較多天然脂質，所以皮膚看起來油。"},{"en":"If natural oils are washed away too often, the skin may become dry or irritated.","zh":"如果天然油脂太常被洗走，皮膚可能變乾或受刺激。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the skin’s own protective oily substance.","zh":"這個短語描述皮膚自身的保護性油脂物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"combine to form","meaning":"結合形成","examples":[{"en":"Natural oils and sweat combine to form a protective shield.","zh":"天然油脂和汗水結合形成保護屏障。"},{"en":"To combine to form something means two or more things join together and create it.","zh":"「combine to form」某物，意思是兩個或更多東西結合並創造它。"},{"en":"Flour and water combine to form dough.","zh":"麵粉和水結合形成麵糰。"},{"en":"If oils and sweat combine on the skin, they can create a surface layer.","zh":"如果油脂和汗水在皮膚上結合，它們可以形成表層。"},{"en":"The phrase describes separate elements joining to create a result.","zh":"這個短語描述分開元素結合並創造結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"oily acid surface shield","meaning":"油性酸性表面保護層","examples":[{"en":"The skin has an oily acid surface shield against ultraviolet rays.","zh":"皮膚有一層抵抗紫外線的油性酸性表面保護層。"},{"en":"An oily acid surface shield is a thin protective layer on the skin made from natural oils, sweat, and acids.","zh":"「oily acid surface shield」是由天然油脂、汗水和酸性物質形成的皮膚薄保護層。"},{"en":"Gentle cleansing can help preserve the skin’s natural surface shield.","zh":"溫和清潔有助保存皮膚天然表面保護層。"},{"en":"If this shield is washed away, the skin may be less protected from sunlight.","zh":"如果這層保護被洗走，皮膚對陽光的保護可能較弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a natural protective coating on the skin.","zh":"這個短語描述皮膚上的天然保護膜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"protect against ultraviolet rays","meaning":"防止紫外線傷害","examples":[{"en":"The natural surface shield helps protect against ultraviolet rays.","zh":"天然表面保護層有助防止紫外線傷害。"},{"en":"To protect against ultraviolet rays means to reduce harm from UV radiation.","zh":"「protect against ultraviolet rays」意思是減少紫外線輻射造成的傷害。"},{"en":"Sunscreen and sunglasses help protect against ultraviolet rays.","zh":"防曬產品和太陽眼鏡有助防止紫外線傷害。"},{"en":"If people do not protect against UV rays, skin and eyes may be damaged.","zh":"如果人們不防護紫外線，皮膚和眼睛可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes defence against harmful sunlight.","zh":"這個短語描述抵禦有害陽光。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"saltwater washes away","meaning":"鹽水沖走……","examples":[{"en":"Saltwater washes away the skin’s natural oily coat.","zh":"鹽水會沖走皮膚的天然油脂保護層。"},{"en":"If saltwater washes away something, seawater removes it from the surface.","zh":"如果「saltwater washes away」某物，意思是海水把它從表面移除。"},{"en":"Sea swimming may wash away sunscreen, so people need to apply it again.","zh":"海泳可能沖走防曬產品，所以人們需要再次塗抹。"},{"en":"If the oily coat is washed away, the skin may lose part of its natural protection.","zh":"如果油脂保護層被沖走，皮膚可能失去部分天然保護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes removal by seawater.","zh":"這個短語描述被海水移除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"natural oily coat","meaning":"天然油脂保護層","examples":[{"en":"The skin’s natural oily coat provides some sun protection.","zh":"皮膚的天然油脂保護層提供一定防曬保護。"},{"en":"A natural oily coat is the thin layer of oil naturally present on the skin.","zh":"「natural oily coat」是皮膚上自然存在的薄油脂層。"},{"en":"Harsh soap may remove the skin’s natural oily coat and make it dry.","zh":"強力肥皂可能移除皮膚天然油脂保護層，使皮膚變乾。"},{"en":"If this coat remains, it can help keep the skin moist and partly protected.","zh":"如果這層保護仍在，它可以幫助皮膚保持濕潤並提供部分保護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the skin’s own oil layer.","zh":"這個短語描述皮膚自身的油脂層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"overwork the sweat glands","meaning":"令汗腺過度運作","examples":[{"en":"Intense heat can overwork the sweat glands.","zh":"強烈高溫會令汗腺過度運作。"},{"en":"To overwork the sweat glands means to make them work too hard for too long.","zh":"「overwork the sweat glands」意思是令汗腺長時間過度工作。"},{"en":"A runner in hot weather may overwork the sweat glands if they do not rest or drink water.","zh":"跑手在炎熱天氣下如果不休息或不飲水，可能令汗腺過度運作。"},{"en":"If sweat glands are overworked, sweat may no longer protect the body effectively.","zh":"如果汗腺過度運作，汗水可能不再有效保護身體。"},{"en":"The phrase describes excessive strain on the body’s cooling system.","zh":"這個短語描述身體降溫系統承受過度壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sweat glands","meaning":"汗腺","examples":[{"en":"The hot sun causes the sweat glands to work harder.","zh":"炎熱陽光令汗腺更努力運作。"},{"en":"Sweat glands are small organs in the skin that produce sweat.","zh":"「sweat glands」是皮膚中產生汗水的小器官。"},{"en":"Sweat glands help cool the body when people exercise or feel hot.","zh":"人們運動或感到熱時，汗腺幫助身體降溫。"},{"en":"If sweat glands cannot keep up with heat, the body may overheat.","zh":"如果汗腺不能跟上熱力，身體可能過熱。"},{"en":"The phrase names the skin structures involved in sweating.","zh":"這個短語指出與出汗有關的皮膚結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"excess sweat","meaning":"過量汗水","examples":[{"en":"Excess sweat may become ineffective as a protective mechanism.","zh":"過量汗水作為保護機制可能變得無效。"},{"en":"Excess sweat means more sweat than is useful or manageable.","zh":"「excess sweat」意思是超過有用或可處理程度的汗水。"},{"en":"During a hot commute, excess sweat can make a person uncomfortable and dehydrated.","zh":"在炎熱通勤途中，過量汗水會令人不適並脫水。"},{"en":"If sweat becomes excessive, the body may lose too much water and salt.","zh":"如果汗水過量，身體可能流失太多水分和鹽分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes too much sweating.","zh":"這個短語描述出汗太多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"dry wind","meaning":"乾燥的風","examples":[{"en":"Dry wind can contribute to dehydration of the skin.","zh":"乾燥的風會促成皮膚脫水。"},{"en":"Dry wind is wind with little moisture in the air.","zh":"「dry wind」是空氣中水分很少的風。"},{"en":"A dry wind on a winter day can make lips crack quickly.","zh":"冬天的乾燥風可以很快令嘴唇乾裂。"},{"en":"If dry wind removes moisture from the skin, the skin may feel tight and rough.","zh":"如果乾燥的風帶走皮膚水分，皮膚可能感到繃緊和粗糙。"},{"en":"The phrase describes air movement that can dry surfaces.","zh":"這個短語描述會令表面變乾的空氣流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"dehydrate the skin","meaning":"令皮膚脫水","examples":[{"en":"Hot sun and dry wind can dehydrate the skin.","zh":"炎熱陽光和乾燥的風會令皮膚脫水。"},{"en":"To dehydrate the skin means to remove moisture from it and make it dry.","zh":"「dehydrate the skin」意思是帶走皮膚水分並令它變乾。"},{"en":"Strong air-conditioning can dehydrate the skin during a long office day.","zh":"長時間在辦公室中，強冷氣可以令皮膚脫水。"},{"en":"If skin becomes dehydrated, it may feel tight, itchy, or flaky.","zh":"如果皮膚脫水，它可能感到繃緊、痕癢或脫皮。"},{"en":"The phrase describes loss of moisture from the skin.","zh":"這個短語描述皮膚失去水分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"show greater wisdom in","meaning":"在……方面表現得更明智","examples":[{"en":"Women have traditionally shown greater wisdom in caring for their skin.","zh":"女性傳統上在護理皮膚方面表現得更明智。"},{"en":"To show greater wisdom in something means to act more sensibly or carefully in that area.","zh":"「show greater wisdom in」某事，意思是在該方面行事更明智或更謹慎。"},{"en":"Experienced hikers show greater wisdom in preparing water, maps, and first-aid supplies.","zh":"經驗豐富的遠足者在準備水、地圖和急救用品方面表現得更明智。"},{"en":"If people protect their skin early, they may avoid problems later.","zh":"如果人們早早保護皮膚，之後可能避免問題。"},{"en":"The phrase praises careful judgment and practical sense.","zh":"這個短語讚賞謹慎判斷和實用智慧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"care of the skin","meaning":"皮膚護理","examples":[{"en":"Women have historically paid close attention to the care of their skin.","zh":"女性歷史上一直密切注意皮膚護理。"},{"en":"Care of the skin means actions taken to protect, clean, moisturise, and maintain healthy skin.","zh":"「care of the skin」意思是保護、清潔、保濕並維持皮膚健康的行動。"},{"en":"Daily skin care may include washing, moisturising, and using sunscreen.","zh":"日常皮膚護理可能包括清潔、保濕和使用防曬產品。"},{"en":"If people neglect skin care, dryness, irritation, or sun damage may become worse.","zh":"如果人們忽視皮膚護理，乾燥、刺激或陽光傷害可能變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase describes looking after skin health.","zh":"這個短語描述照顧皮膚健康。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ancient Egypt","meaning":"古埃及","examples":[{"en":"Women in ancient Egypt used animal fat on their faces.","zh":"古埃及女性在臉上使用動物脂肪。"},{"en":"Ancient Egypt refers to the civilisation that existed along the Nile thousands of years ago.","zh":"「ancient Egypt」指數千年前存在於尼羅河沿岸的文明。"},{"en":"Students learn about ancient Egypt through pyramids, mummies, temples, and writing.","zh":"學生透過金字塔、木乃伊、神廟和文字學習古埃及。"},{"en":"If people in ancient Egypt used skin treatments, skin care has a very long history.","zh":"如果古埃及人已使用皮膚護理，皮膚護理就有非常悠久歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase names a historical civilisation.","zh":"這個短語指出一個歷史文明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"apply something to the face","meaning":"將……塗在臉上","examples":[{"en":"Ancient Egyptian women applied animal fat to their faces.","zh":"古埃及女性將動物脂肪塗在臉上。"},{"en":"To apply something to the face means to put a substance on the skin of the face.","zh":"「apply something to the face」意思是把某物質塗在面部皮膚上。"},{"en":"People apply moisturiser to the face after washing it.","zh":"人們洗臉後會將潤膚霜塗在臉上。"},{"en":"If a cream is applied regularly, it may protect or soften the skin.","zh":"如果乳霜定期塗抹，它可能保護或柔軟皮膚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes putting a product directly on facial skin.","zh":"這個短語描述把產品直接塗在面部皮膚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"so-called sacred cats","meaning":"所謂的神聖貓隻","examples":[{"en":"The passage refers to the so-called sacred temple cats of Egypt.","zh":"文章提到埃及所謂的神廟神聖貓隻。"},{"en":"So-called sacred cats means cats described or believed by people to be sacred, though the writer may sound slightly cautious.","zh":"「so-called sacred cats」意思是被人描述或相信為神聖的貓，但作者語氣可能略帶保留。"},{"en":"A guidebook may mention so-called sacred animals worshipped in an ancient culture.","zh":"旅遊指南可能提到古代文化中所謂被崇拜的神聖動物。"},{"en":"If writers use “so-called”, they may be reporting a label without fully accepting it.","zh":"如果作者使用 “so-called”，他們可能是在報告某稱呼，而不完全接受它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cats given a religious or special status.","zh":"這個短語描述被賦予宗教或特殊地位的貓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be tireless in doing something","meaning":"不懈地做某事","examples":[{"en":"Women have been tireless in protecting their skin from the sun.","zh":"女性一直不懈地保護皮膚免受陽光傷害。"},{"en":"To be tireless in doing something means to keep doing it with great energy and persistence.","zh":"「be tireless in doing something」意思是以巨大精力和毅力持續做某事。"},{"en":"A parent may be tireless in helping a child prepare for an important exam.","zh":"父母可能不懈地幫助孩子準備重要考試。"},{"en":"If people are tireless in protecting their skin, they may develop strong long-term habits.","zh":"如果人們不懈地保護皮膚，他們可能建立強大的長期習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase praises continuous effort.","zh":"這個短語讚賞持續努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"wage a battle against","meaning":"與……抗爭","examples":[{"en":"People continue to wage a battle against sun damage.","zh":"人們繼續與陽光傷害抗爭。"},{"en":"To wage a battle against something means to struggle actively against a problem.","zh":"「wage a battle against」某事，意思是積極與某問題抗爭。"},{"en":"Schools wage a battle against bullying by teaching respect and responding quickly to complaints.","zh":"學校透過教導尊重並迅速處理投訴，與欺凌抗爭。"},{"en":"If sun damage is persistent, people must protect themselves again and again.","zh":"如果陽光傷害持續存在，人們必須反覆保護自己。"},{"en":"The phrase makes prevention sound like a long, active fight.","zh":"這個短語把預防形容成長期主動戰鬥。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"damage to the skin","meaning":"對皮膚的傷害","examples":[{"en":"Sunscreen helps reduce damage to the skin from sunlight.","zh":"防曬產品有助減少陽光對皮膚的傷害。"},{"en":"Damage to the skin means harm such as burning, dryness, irritation, ageing, or disease risk.","zh":"「damage to the skin」意思是曬傷、乾燥、刺激、老化或疾病風險等傷害。"},{"en":"Harsh chemicals can cause damage to the skin if gloves are not worn.","zh":"如果不戴手套，強烈化學品可能造成對皮膚的傷害。"},{"en":"If sunlight damages the skin repeatedly, the effects may become long-lasting.","zh":"如果陽光反覆傷害皮膚，影響可能變得長久。"},{"en":"The phrase describes harm affecting the skin.","zh":"這個短語描述影響皮膚的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"both sexes","meaning":"男女兩性","examples":[{"en":"Both sexes now spend substantial amounts on sunscreen.","zh":"男女兩性現在都在防曬產品上花大量金錢。"},{"en":"Both sexes means both men and women.","zh":"「both sexes」意思是男性和女性兩者。"},{"en":"Both sexes can benefit from regular exercise and healthy eating.","zh":"男女兩性都可以從定期運動和健康飲食中受益。"},{"en":"If both sexes use sunscreen, sun protection is no longer seen as only a women’s concern.","zh":"如果男女兩性都使用防曬產品，防曬就不再被視為只是女性關注。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to males and females together.","zh":"這個短語指男性和女性一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"contribute annually to","meaning":"每年為……帶來收入","examples":[{"en":"Consumers contribute annually to the global sunscreen industry.","zh":"消費者每年為全球防曬產品行業帶來收入。"},{"en":"To contribute annually to something means to add money, support, or activity to it every year.","zh":"「contribute annually to」某事，意思是每年為它增加金錢、支持或活動。"},{"en":"Families contribute annually to school fundraising by buying charity tickets.","zh":"家庭每年透過購買慈善券為學校籌款作出貢獻。"},{"en":"If millions of people buy sunscreen each year, they support a large industry.","zh":"如果數百萬人每年購買防曬產品，他們就支持一個大型產業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes yearly contribution or spending.","zh":"這個短語描述每年的貢獻或消費。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"multi-million-dollar business","meaning":"數以百萬計美元的生意","examples":[{"en":"Sunscreen has become a multi-million-dollar global business.","zh":"防曬產品已成為全球數以百萬計美元的生意。"},{"en":"A multi-million-dollar business is an industry or company worth many millions of dollars.","zh":"「multi-million-dollar business」是價值數以百萬美元計的行業或公司。"},{"en":"Online tutoring can become a multi-million-dollar business if many students pay for lessons.","zh":"如果許多學生付費上課，網上補習可以成為數以百萬計美元的生意。"},{"en":"If people spend heavily on sun protection, sunscreen becomes a major commercial market.","zh":"如果人們在防曬上花費巨大，防曬產品就成為重要商業市場。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a very large and profitable business.","zh":"這個短語描述非常大型且有利可圖的生意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sunscreen","meaning":"防曬產品","examples":[{"en":"Sunscreen helps protect the skin from harmful rays.","zh":"防曬產品有助保護皮膚免受有害光線傷害。"},{"en":"Sunscreen is a lotion, cream, spray, or product applied to the skin to reduce sun damage.","zh":"「sunscreen」是塗在皮膚上以減少陽光傷害的乳液、面霜、噴霧或產品。"},{"en":"Parents often put sunscreen on children before they swim outdoors.","zh":"父母常在孩子戶外游泳前為他們塗防曬產品。"},{"en":"If sunscreen is not reapplied after sweating or swimming, protection may weaken.","zh":"如果出汗或游泳後沒有再次塗防曬產品，保護可能變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase names a common product for sun protection.","zh":"這個短語指出常見防曬用品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tend to suffer from","meaning":"容易受到……傷害","examples":[{"en":"The eyes and hair also tend to suffer from sun exposure.","zh":"眼睛和頭髮也容易受到日曬傷害。"},{"en":"To tend to suffer from something means to often be harmed or affected by it.","zh":"「tend to suffer from」某事，意思是常常受其傷害或影響。"},{"en":"Students tend to suffer from tiredness when they sleep too late before school.","zh":"學生上學前太晚睡，容易受到疲倦影響。"},{"en":"If eyes and hair are exposed for long periods, they may gradually become damaged.","zh":"如果眼睛和頭髮長時間暴露，它們可能逐漸受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common tendency toward harm.","zh":"這個短語描述容易受到傷害的傾向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"exposure to the sun","meaning":"接觸陽光；曝曬","examples":[{"en":"Prolonged exposure to the sun can damage the eyes and hair.","zh":"長時間曝曬會損害眼睛和頭髮。"},{"en":"Exposure to the sun means being in sunlight, especially for a period of time.","zh":"「exposure to the sun」意思是接觸陽光，尤其是一段時間。"},{"en":"Gardeners have regular exposure to the sun when they work outdoors for hours.","zh":"園丁在戶外工作數小時時，會經常接觸陽光。"},{"en":"If exposure is too long, sunlight can harm body parts that are not protected.","zh":"如果曝曬太久，陽光會傷害沒有受保護的身體部位。"},{"en":"The phrase describes contact with sunlight.","zh":"這個短語描述與陽光接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"optometrists","meaning":"視光師","examples":[{"en":"Optometrists conducted studies on sunlight and vision.","zh":"視光師進行了關於陽光和視力的研究。"},{"en":"Optometrists are eye-care professionals who test vision and prescribe glasses or contact lenses.","zh":"「optometrists」是測試視力並配眼鏡或隱形眼鏡的眼科護理專業人士。"},{"en":"A student who cannot read the board clearly may visit an optometrist.","zh":"看不清黑板的學生可能去看視光師。"},{"en":"If optometrists study sunlight, they may focus on how bright light affects the eyes.","zh":"如果視光師研究陽光，他們可能集中於強光如何影響眼睛。"},{"en":"The word names professionals concerned with eyesight.","zh":"這個詞指出關注視力的專業人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"undertake studies","meaning":"進行研究","examples":[{"en":"Optometrists undertook studies to examine the effects of bright sunlight.","zh":"視光師進行研究，以考察強烈陽光的影響。"},{"en":"To undertake studies means to carry out research or investigations.","zh":"「undertake studies」意思是進行研究或調查。"},{"en":"A university may undertake studies on how sleep affects exam performance.","zh":"大學可能進行關於睡眠如何影響考試表現的研究。"},{"en":"If researchers undertake careful studies, they can support advice with evidence.","zh":"如果研究人員進行仔細研究，就可以用證據支持建議。"},{"en":"The phrase describes starting and conducting research.","zh":"這個短語描述開始並進行研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"examine the influence of","meaning":"研究……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The researchers examined the influence of sunlight on the eyes.","zh":"研究人員研究陽光對眼睛的影響。"},{"en":"To examine the influence of something means to study how it affects another thing.","zh":"「examine the influence of」某事，意思是研究它如何影響另一事物。"},{"en":"Teachers may examine the influence of class size on student participation.","zh":"老師可能研究班級人數對學生參與度的影響。"},{"en":"If sunlight affects vision, researchers need to measure the change carefully.","zh":"如果陽光影響視力，研究人員需要仔細量度變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes studying cause and effect.","zh":"這個短語描述研究因果影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Atlantic City lifeguards","meaning":"大西洋城救生員","examples":[{"en":"Atlantic City lifeguards participated in research on eyesight.","zh":"大西洋城救生員參與了關於視力的研究。"},{"en":"Atlantic City lifeguards are beach safety workers from Atlantic City who watch swimmers and rescue people in danger.","zh":"「Atlantic City lifeguards」是來自大西洋城、負責看守泳客並拯救遇險人士的海灘安全工作者。"},{"en":"Lifeguards spend many hours in bright sunlight while watching the sea.","zh":"救生員在看守海面時，會長時間處於強烈陽光下。"},{"en":"If lifeguards work without eye protection, their vision may be affected over time.","zh":"如果救生員工作時沒有眼睛保護，視力可能隨時間受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase names the group studied in the eyesight research.","zh":"這個短語指出視力研究中被研究的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"even a few hours","meaning":"即使只是數小時","examples":[{"en":"Even a few hours in bright sunlight can affect vision.","zh":"即使只是數小時處於強烈陽光下，也會影響視力。"},{"en":"Even a few hours means a surprisingly short period of time can still matter.","zh":"「even a few hours」意思是令人意外地短的時間仍然重要。"},{"en":"Even a few hours without water can make a hiker feel weak in hot weather.","zh":"在炎熱天氣中，即使只是數小時沒有飲水，也會令遠足者感到虛弱。"},{"en":"If eye damage can begin within hours, sunglasses become important during outdoor work.","zh":"如果眼睛傷害可在數小時內開始，戶外工作時太陽眼鏡就很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the effect can happen quickly.","zh":"這個短語強調效果可以很快發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"without sunglasses","meaning":"沒有戴太陽眼鏡","examples":[{"en":"Bright sunlight can damage the eyes when people are without sunglasses.","zh":"當人們沒有戴太陽眼鏡時，強烈陽光會損害眼睛。"},{"en":"Without sunglasses means not wearing protective dark glasses in bright light.","zh":"「without sunglasses」意思是在強光下沒有戴保護性的深色眼鏡。"},{"en":"A driver may find it hard to see clearly without sunglasses on a sunny road.","zh":"司機在陽光猛烈的道路上沒有戴太陽眼鏡，可能難以看清楚。"},{"en":"If people spend hours in bright sun without sunglasses, their eyes may become strained or damaged.","zh":"如果人們在強光下數小時沒有戴太陽眼鏡，眼睛可能疲勞或受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lack of eye protection from sunlight.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏陽光眼部保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cause a significant loss of vision","meaning":"導致視力明顯下降","examples":[{"en":"Strong sunlight can cause a significant loss of vision.","zh":"強烈陽光會導致視力明顯下降。"},{"en":"To cause a significant loss of vision means to produce a clear and important decrease in eyesight.","zh":"「cause a significant loss of vision」意思是造成清楚而重要的視力減退。"},{"en":"An eye injury can cause a significant loss of vision if it is not treated quickly.","zh":"如果眼傷沒有迅速治療，可能導致視力明顯下降。"},{"en":"If sunlight reduces vision noticeably, workers may not realise the damage at first.","zh":"如果陽光明顯削弱視力，工人起初可能未察覺傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious weakening of eyesight.","zh":"這個短語描述視力嚴重減弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"take several weeks to recover from","meaning":"需要數星期才能復原","examples":[{"en":"Sun-related vision loss may take several weeks to recover from.","zh":"與陽光有關的視力下降可能需要數星期才能復原。"},{"en":"To take several weeks to recover from something means to need a few weeks before returning to normal.","zh":"「take several weeks to recover from」某事，意思是需要幾星期才回復正常。"},{"en":"A sprained ankle may take several weeks to recover from if it is serious.","zh":"如果扭傷腳踝嚴重，可能需要數星期才能復原。"},{"en":"If eye damage takes weeks to heal, prevention is much better than waiting for recovery.","zh":"如果眼睛傷害需要數星期才能癒合，預防比等待復原好得多。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a slow recovery period.","zh":"這個短語描述緩慢復原期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"so gradual was the change that","meaning":"變化緩慢得令……","examples":[{"en":"So gradual was the change that the lifeguards did not notice it.","zh":"變化緩慢得令救生員沒有察覺。"},{"en":"So gradual was the change that means the change happened so slowly that a result followed.","zh":"「so gradual was the change that」意思是變化發生得如此緩慢，以致產生某結果。"},{"en":"So gradual was the improvement that the student did not realise how much better her writing had become.","zh":"進步緩慢得令學生沒有意識到自己的寫作改善了多少。"},{"en":"If damage develops slowly, people may fail to notice it until testing reveals it.","zh":"如果傷害慢慢發展，人們可能直到測試揭示才察覺。"},{"en":"The phrase uses inversion to emphasise how slow the change was.","zh":"這個短語使用倒裝，強調變化有多緩慢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be unaware that","meaning":"沒有察覺","examples":[{"en":"The lifeguards were unaware that their sight had been affected.","zh":"救生員沒有察覺自己的視力已受到影響。"},{"en":"To be unaware that something has happened means not to know it has happened.","zh":"「be unaware that」某事已發生，意思是不知道它已發生。"},{"en":"A student may be unaware that a deadline has changed if they miss the announcement.","zh":"如果學生錯過公告，可能沒有察覺截止日期已改變。"},{"en":"If damage happens gradually, people may be unaware until symptoms become obvious.","zh":"如果傷害逐漸發生，人們可能直到症狀明顯才察覺。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lack of knowledge or notice.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏知識或注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sight had been affected","meaning":"視力已受到影響","examples":[{"en":"Their sight had been affected without their realising it.","zh":"他們在沒有意識到的情況下，視力已受到影響。"},{"en":"If sight has been affected, a person’s ability to see has changed or worsened.","zh":"如果「sight has been affected」，意思是人的視覺能力已改變或變差。"},{"en":"After staring at a screen for hours, a student may feel that their sight has been affected temporarily.","zh":"學生盯着屏幕數小時後，可能覺得視力暫時受到影響。"},{"en":"If bright light affects sight slowly, people may not connect the problem with sunlight.","zh":"如果強光慢慢影響視力，人們可能不會把問題與陽光連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change in vision.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"introduce something as","meaning":"將……引入作為……","examples":[{"en":"Sunglasses were introduced as a standard part of the uniform.","zh":"太陽眼鏡被引入作為制服的標準部分。"},{"en":"To introduce something as something means to bring it in for a particular role or purpose.","zh":"「introduce something as」某物，意思是為特定角色或目的引入它。"},{"en":"A school may introduce tablets as part of classroom learning.","zh":"學校可能將平板電腦引入作為課堂學習的一部分。"},{"en":"If sunglasses are introduced as uniform, wearing them becomes normal rather than optional.","zh":"如果太陽眼鏡被引入作為制服，佩戴它就變成正常而不是可選。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adding something in a new official role.","zh":"這個短語描述把某物加入新的正式角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"standard part of","meaning":"……的標準部分","examples":[{"en":"Sunglasses became a standard part of the lifeguard uniform.","zh":"太陽眼鏡成為救生員制服的標準部分。"},{"en":"A standard part of something is a normal, expected, or required component.","zh":"「standard part of」某物，是正常、預期或要求的組成部分。"},{"en":"A school badge is a standard part of many school uniforms.","zh":"校章是許多校服的標準部分。"},{"en":"If sunglasses become standard equipment, workers are more likely to protect their eyes.","zh":"如果太陽眼鏡成為標準裝備，工人更可能保護眼睛。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that is officially or routinely included.","zh":"這個短語描述正式或慣常包含的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lifeguard uniform","meaning":"救生員制服","examples":[{"en":"Sunglasses were added to the lifeguard uniform.","zh":"太陽眼鏡被加入救生員制服中。"},{"en":"A lifeguard uniform is the clothing worn by lifeguards so they can be recognised and work safely.","zh":"「lifeguard uniform」是救生員穿着，使人能認出他們並安全工作的服裝。"},{"en":"A lifeguard uniform may include bright colours, a whistle, a hat, and protective glasses.","zh":"救生員制服可能包括鮮色衣物、哨子、帽子和保護眼鏡。"},{"en":"If sunglasses are part of the uniform, eye protection becomes part of the job.","zh":"如果太陽眼鏡是制服的一部分，保護眼睛就成為工作的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase names the official clothing for lifeguards.","zh":"這個短語指出救生員的正式服裝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be dark enough to","meaning":"深色得足以……","examples":[{"en":"The sunglasses were dark enough to absorb most harmful rays.","zh":"太陽眼鏡深色得足以吸收大部分有害光線。"},{"en":"To be dark enough to do something means to have enough darkness or shade for that purpose.","zh":"「be dark enough to」做某事，意思是顏色或遮光程度足以達到該目的。"},{"en":"Curtains may be dark enough to help a baby sleep during the day.","zh":"窗簾可能深色得足以幫助嬰兒在白天睡覺。"},{"en":"If sunglasses are dark enough, they can reduce the amount of harmful light reaching the eyes.","zh":"如果太陽眼鏡足夠深色，它可以減少到達眼睛的有害光線。"},{"en":"The phrase connects degree of darkness with function.","zh":"這個短語把深色程度與功能連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"absorb harmful rays","meaning":"吸收有害光線","examples":[{"en":"Good sunglasses absorb harmful infrared and ultraviolet rays.","zh":"好太陽眼鏡會吸收有害紅外線和紫外線。"},{"en":"To absorb harmful rays means to take in damaging light energy before it reaches the eyes or skin.","zh":"「absorb harmful rays」意思是在有害光能到達眼睛或皮膚前把它吸收。"},{"en":"A window coating can absorb harmful rays to protect furniture from fading.","zh":"窗戶塗層可以吸收有害光線，以保護家具免褪色。"},{"en":"If sunglasses absorb harmful rays, the eyes receive less damaging radiation.","zh":"如果太陽眼鏡吸收有害光線，眼睛接收的有害輻射就較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes protection by taking in harmful light.","zh":"這個短語描述透過吸收有害光線提供保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"infrared rays","meaning":"紅外線","examples":[{"en":"Sunglasses can reduce exposure to harmful infrared rays.","zh":"太陽眼鏡可以減少接觸有害紅外線。"},{"en":"Infrared rays are invisible light rays often felt as heat.","zh":"「infrared rays」是看不見的光線，常被感覺為熱力。"},{"en":"A remote control uses infrared signals to communicate with a television.","zh":"遙控器使用紅外線訊號與電視溝通。"},{"en":"If infrared rays are intense, they may contribute to heat-related discomfort or eye strain.","zh":"如果紅外線很強，它們可能促成熱相關不適或眼睛疲勞。"},{"en":"The phrase names a type of light energy beyond visible red light.","zh":"這個短語指出一種超出可見紅光的光能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"ultraviolet rays","meaning":"紫外線","examples":[{"en":"Ultraviolet rays can damage both the skin and the eyes.","zh":"紫外線可以傷害皮膚和眼睛。"},{"en":"Ultraviolet rays are invisible rays from the sun that can affect skin cells and eye tissues.","zh":"「ultraviolet rays」是來自太陽、看不見並會影響皮膚細胞和眼組織的光線。"},{"en":"Sunscreen is used because ultraviolet rays can cause sunburn.","zh":"人們使用防曬產品，因為紫外線可以造成曬傷。"},{"en":"If UV exposure is repeated over years, the risk of long-term damage may increase.","zh":"如果多年反覆接觸紫外線，長期傷害風險可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase names a harmful form of sunlight that needs protection.","zh":"這個短語指出一種需要防護的有害陽光。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have a lesser impact on","meaning":"對……影響較小","examples":[{"en":"The sun has a lesser impact on the hair than on the skin.","zh":"太陽對頭髮的影響比對皮膚較小。"},{"en":"To have a lesser impact on something means to affect it less strongly.","zh":"「have a lesser impact on」某物，意思是對它的影響較弱。"},{"en":"A short power cut has a lesser impact on a home than on a hospital.","zh":"短暫停電對家庭的影響比對醫院較小。"},{"en":"If sunlight affects hair less than skin, skin protection may be more urgent but hair still needs care.","zh":"如果陽光對頭髮影響比皮膚小，皮膚保護可能更迫切，但頭髮仍需護理。"},{"en":"The phrase compares different levels of effect.","zh":"這個短語比較不同程度的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"prolonged exposure","meaning":"長時間曝曬","examples":[{"en":"Prolonged exposure leaves the hair brittle and dry.","zh":"長時間曝曬會令頭髮變得脆弱而乾旱。"},{"en":"Prolonged exposure means being in contact with something for a long time.","zh":"「prolonged exposure」意思是長時間接觸某物。"},{"en":"Prolonged exposure to loud noise can harm hearing.","zh":"長時間接觸巨大噪音可以損害聽力。"},{"en":"If hair is exposed to sun for many hours, it may lose moisture and strength.","zh":"如果頭髮曝曬多小時，它可能失去水分和強度。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that duration matters.","zh":"這個短語提醒時間長短很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"brittle and dry","meaning":"脆弱而乾旱的","examples":[{"en":"Sun-damaged hair can become brittle and dry.","zh":"受陽光傷害的頭髮可能變得脆弱而乾旱。"},{"en":"Brittle and dry means easily broken and lacking moisture.","zh":"「brittle and dry」意思是容易斷裂並缺乏水分。"},{"en":"Hair may become brittle and dry after too much bleaching or heat styling.","zh":"頭髮在過度漂染或熱力造型後，可能變得脆弱而乾旱。"},{"en":"If sunlight removes moisture from hair, it may snap more easily.","zh":"如果陽光帶走頭髮水分，頭髮可能更容易折斷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weak, rough, unhealthy hair texture.","zh":"這個短語描述脆弱、粗糙、不健康的頭髮質感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"haircare professionals","meaning":"護髮專業人士","examples":[{"en":"Haircare professionals recommend treatments containing lanolin.","zh":"護髮專業人士建議使用含羊毛脂的護理產品。"},{"en":"Haircare professionals are people trained to care for, cut, treat, or style hair.","zh":"「haircare professionals」是受訓護理、修剪、治療或造型頭髮的人。"},{"en":"A haircare professional may suggest conditioner for hair damaged by sun or dye.","zh":"護髮專業人士可能為受陽光或染髮傷害的頭髮建議護髮素。"},{"en":"If hair becomes dry, professionals may recommend products that restore moisture.","zh":"如果頭髮變乾，專業人士可能建議恢復水分的產品。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to trained specialists in hair care.","zh":"這個短語指護髮方面的受訓專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"nutritional cream treatment","meaning":"滋養護髮霜療程","examples":[{"en":"A nutritional cream treatment may restore damaged hair.","zh":"滋養護髮霜療程可能修復受損頭髮。"},{"en":"A nutritional cream treatment is a rich hair or skin treatment that provides moisture and conditioning ingredients.","zh":"「nutritional cream treatment」是提供水分和護理成分的濃厚頭髮或皮膚護理。"},{"en":"A person with dry hair may use a nutritional cream treatment after swimming in the sea.","zh":"頭髮乾燥的人在海泳後可能使用滋養護髮霜療程。"},{"en":"If hair lacks moisture, a cream treatment can make it softer and easier to manage.","zh":"如果頭髮缺乏水分，護髮霜療程可以令它更柔順、更易打理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a nourishing care product.","zh":"這個短語描述滋養護理產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a substance containing lanolin","meaning":"含羊毛脂的物質","examples":[{"en":"Professionals recommend a treatment containing lanolin.","zh":"專業人士建議使用含羊毛脂的護理產品。"},{"en":"A substance containing lanolin is a product that includes lanolin, a waxy oil from sheep’s wool.","zh":"「a substance containing lanolin」是含有羊毛脂的產品；羊毛脂是來自羊毛的蠟狀油脂。"},{"en":"A hand cream containing lanolin may help soften rough skin.","zh":"含羊毛脂的護手霜可能幫助柔軟粗糙皮膚。"},{"en":"If a conditioner contains lanolin, it may help coat dry hair and reduce roughness.","zh":"如果護髮素含羊毛脂，它可能幫助包覆乾旱頭髮並減少粗糙。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a product ingredient.","zh":"這個短語描述產品成分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lanolin","meaning":"羊毛脂","examples":[{"en":"Lanolin is commonly used in treatments for dry hair.","zh":"羊毛脂常用於乾旱頭髮護理產品中。"},{"en":"Lanolin is a waxy substance from sheep’s wool, often used to moisturise skin or hair.","zh":"「lanolin」是來自羊毛的蠟狀物質，常用於滋潤皮膚或頭髮。"},{"en":"Some lip balms contain lanolin to help protect dry lips.","zh":"有些潤唇膏含有羊毛脂，以幫助保護乾裂嘴唇。"},{"en":"If hair is brittle, lanolin-based products may help restore softness.","zh":"如果頭髮脆弱，羊毛脂產品可能幫助恢復柔順。"},{"en":"The word names a moisturising ingredient used in care products.","zh":"這個詞指出護理產品中的滋潤成分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"restore natural softness","meaning":"恢復天然柔順","examples":[{"en":"A conditioning treatment can restore the hair’s natural softness.","zh":"護理療程可以恢復頭髮的天然柔順。"},{"en":"To restore natural softness means to bring back the smooth, gentle texture something had before.","zh":"「restore natural softness」意思是帶回某物原本順滑、柔和的質感。"},{"en":"Conditioner can restore natural softness after shampoo leaves hair dry.","zh":"洗髮水令頭髮乾燥後，護髮素可以恢復天然柔順。"},{"en":"If sun exposure makes hair rough, treatment may help it feel soft again.","zh":"如果日曬令頭髮粗糙，護理可能幫助它重新變得柔軟。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recovering a pleasant original texture.","zh":"這個短語描述恢復原本令人舒服的質感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"come in the form of","meaning":"以……的形式出現","examples":[{"en":"These treatments often come in the form of leave-in conditioners.","zh":"這些護理產品常以免沖洗護髮素的形式出現。"},{"en":"To come in the form of something means to appear or be sold as that type of product.","zh":"「come in the form of」某物，意思是以該類產品形式出現或出售。"},{"en":"Extra homework may come in the form of online quizzes rather than paper worksheets.","zh":"額外功課可能以網上小測而非紙本工作紙的形式出現。"},{"en":"If hair treatment comes as a leave-in conditioner, users do not need to rinse it out.","zh":"如果護髮產品以免沖洗護髮素形式出現，使用者就不需要沖洗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the form or type in which something appears.","zh":"這個短語描述某物出現的形式或種類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"leave-in conditioner","meaning":"免沖洗護髮素","examples":[{"en":"A leave-in conditioner remains on the hair after application.","zh":"免沖洗護髮素在使用後留在頭髮上。"},{"en":"A leave-in conditioner is a hair product applied after washing and left on without rinsing.","zh":"「leave-in conditioner」是洗髮後塗上並不用沖走的護髮產品。"},{"en":"People with dry hair may use leave-in conditioner before going outdoors.","zh":"頭髮乾燥的人可能在外出前使用免沖洗護髮素。"},{"en":"If conditioner stays on the hair, it can continue protecting or softening it.","zh":"如果護髮素留在頭髮上，它可以繼續保護或柔順頭髮。"},{"en":"The phrase names a haircare product that is not washed out immediately.","zh":"這個短語指出不會立即沖走的護髮產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be applied frequently","meaning":"應經常使用","examples":[{"en":"Conditioning treatments should be applied frequently.","zh":"護髮療程應經常使用。"},{"en":"To be applied frequently means to be put on often or at regular intervals.","zh":"「be applied frequently」意思是經常或定期塗上。"},{"en":"Hand cream should be applied frequently if the skin is dry from washing.","zh":"如果手因洗手而乾燥，護手霜應經常使用。"},{"en":"If sun exposure continues, protective products may need to be used repeatedly.","zh":"如果日曬持續，保護產品可能需要反覆使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated application.","zh":"這個短語描述重複塗抹。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"just as you would","meaning":"就像你會……一樣","examples":[{"en":"The treatment should be applied just as you would apply sunscreen.","zh":"這種護理產品應像你塗防曬產品一樣使用。"},{"en":"Just as you would means in the same way that you normally would do something else.","zh":"「just as you would」意思是以你平時做另一件事的相同方式。"},{"en":"Check your essay just as you would check an important email before sending it.","zh":"檢查作文時，就像你寄出重要電郵前會檢查一樣。"},{"en":"If a hair product protects against sun damage, it should be used with the same care as sunscreen.","zh":"如果護髮產品能防止陽光傷害，就應像防曬產品一樣小心使用。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a comparison with a familiar action.","zh":"這個短語與熟悉動作作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"dual effect","meaning":"雙重作用","examples":[{"en":"Wearing a hat has a dual effect.","zh":"戴帽有雙重作用。"},{"en":"A dual effect means two effects happening from one action or item.","zh":"「dual effect」意思是一個行動或物件產生兩種效果。"},{"en":"Walking to school has a dual effect: it saves transport money and gives exercise.","zh":"步行上學有雙重作用：節省交通費並提供運動。"},{"en":"If a hat protects hair and prevents sunstroke, it helps in two ways.","zh":"如果帽子保護頭髮並預防中暑，它就有兩方面幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase describes two benefits or results at the same time.","zh":"這個短語描述同時出現兩種好處或結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"protect the hair","meaning":"保護頭髮","examples":[{"en":"A hat protects the hair from prolonged sun exposure.","zh":"帽子保護頭髮免受長時間日曬。"},{"en":"To protect the hair means to prevent damage to it from sun, heat, chemicals, or dryness.","zh":"「protect the hair」意思是防止頭髮受到陽光、熱力、化學品或乾燥傷害。"},{"en":"Swimmers may wear caps to protect the hair from pool chemicals.","zh":"游泳者可能戴泳帽，以保護頭髮免受泳池化學品傷害。"},{"en":"If hair is protected from strong sunlight, it is less likely to become brittle and dry.","zh":"如果頭髮受到保護而免受強烈陽光，它較不容易變得脆弱乾旱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes actions that keep hair healthy.","zh":"這個短語描述保持頭髮健康的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"help to prevent","meaning":"幫助預防","examples":[{"en":"A hat can also help to prevent sunstroke.","zh":"帽子也可以幫助預防中暑。"},{"en":"To help to prevent something means to reduce the chance that it will happen.","zh":"「help to prevent」某事，意思是減少它發生的機會。"},{"en":"Washing hands can help to prevent the spread of germs in school.","zh":"洗手可以幫助預防細菌在學校傳播。"},{"en":"If a hat keeps the head cooler, it may reduce the risk of heat illness.","zh":"如果帽子令頭部較涼，它可能降低熱病風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lowering risk, not guaranteeing complete protection.","zh":"這個短語描述降低風險，而不是保證完全保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"outdoor affliction","meaning":"戶外疾病","examples":[{"en":"Sunstroke is one of the most dangerous outdoor afflictions.","zh":"中暑是最危險的戶外疾病之一。"},{"en":"An outdoor affliction is a health problem people may suffer while spending time outside.","zh":"「outdoor affliction」是人們在戶外活動時可能遭受的健康問題。"},{"en":"Heat exhaustion, insect bites, and sunburn are common outdoor afflictions.","zh":"熱衰竭、昆蟲叮咬和曬傷是常見戶外疾病或問題。"},{"en":"If people ignore heat and sunlight, outdoor activities can become dangerous.","zh":"如果人們忽視高溫和陽光，戶外活動可以變得危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an illness or problem linked with outdoor conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述與戶外環境有關的疾病或問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"sunstroke","meaning":"中暑","examples":[{"en":"Wearing a hat can reduce the risk of sunstroke.","zh":"戴帽可以減低中暑風險。"},{"en":"Sunstroke is a serious heat-related condition caused by too much heat and sun exposure.","zh":"「sunstroke」是由過多熱力和日曬造成的嚴重熱相關狀況。"},{"en":"A hiker without water or shade may suffer sunstroke on a hot afternoon.","zh":"在炎熱下午，沒有水或遮蔭的遠足者可能中暑。"},{"en":"If body temperature rises too high, sunstroke can become a medical emergency.","zh":"如果體溫升得太高，中暑可以變成醫療急症。"},{"en":"The phrase names a dangerous illness linked with heat and sun.","zh":"這個短語指出與高溫和陽光有關的危險疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"look at the following people","meaning":"查看以下人物","examples":[{"en":"Candidates look at the following people and match them with statements.","zh":"考生查看以下人物，並把他們與陳述配對。"},{"en":"Look at the following people means read the list of named people in the question.","zh":"「look at the following people」意思是閱讀題目中列出的人名。"},{"en":"In a matching task, students look at the following people before choosing the correct letters.","zh":"在配對題中，學生先查看以下人物，再選擇正確字母。"},{"en":"If candidates ignore the list, they may match statements to the wrong person.","zh":"如果考生忽略列表，可能把陳述配對到錯誤人物。"},{"en":"The phrase is an exam instruction directing attention to names.","zh":"這個短語是考試指示，要求注意人名。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"list of statements","meaning":"陳述列表","examples":[{"en":"The task provides a list of statements about medical specialists.","zh":"該題提供關於醫學專家的陳述列表。"},{"en":"A list of statements is a group of sentences or claims that students must check or match.","zh":"「list of statements」是一組學生必須核對或配對的句子或主張。"},{"en":"A reading test may give a list of statements and ask which paragraph supports each one.","zh":"閱讀測驗可能給出陳述列表，並要求指出哪段支持每項陳述。"},{"en":"If statements are similar, students must read carefully to avoid confusing them.","zh":"如果陳述相似，學生必須仔細閱讀，以避免混淆。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a set of exam claims.","zh":"這個短語描述一組考試陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"match each person with","meaning":"將每個人物與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match each person with the correct statement.","zh":"學生將每個人物與正確陳述配對。"},{"en":"To match each person with something means to connect every named person to the correct answer.","zh":"「match each person with」某物，意思是把每位具名人物連接到正確答案。"},{"en":"In a history quiz, students may match each inventor with their invention.","zh":"在歷史小測中，學生可能將每位發明家與其發明配對。"},{"en":"If students confuse two people’s views, the matching answer will be wrong.","zh":"如果學生混淆兩個人的觀點，配對答案就會錯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common reading-test task.","zh":"這個短語描述常見閱讀測驗任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"scientifically provable","meaning":"可由科學證明的","examples":[{"en":"Some benefits of sunlight may not yet be scientifically provable.","zh":"陽光某些好處可能尚未可由科學證明。"},{"en":"Scientifically provable means able to be shown as true through scientific evidence and testing.","zh":"「scientifically provable」意思是能透過科學證據和測試證明為真。"},{"en":"A health claim is stronger if it is scientifically provable through careful studies.","zh":"如果健康主張能透過仔細研究由科學證明，它就更有力。"},{"en":"If an effect is not scientifically provable, people should treat it cautiously.","zh":"如果某效果尚不可由科學證明，人們應謹慎看待。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence-based certainty.","zh":"這個短語描述基於證據的確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"claim to have discovered","meaning":"聲稱已發現","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to someone claiming to have discovered a vitamin.","zh":"該選項指某人聲稱已發現一種維他命。"},{"en":"To claim to have discovered something means to say that one has found it, whether or not others agree.","zh":"「claim to have discovered」某物，意思是聲稱自己已找到它，不論別人是否同意。"},{"en":"A student may claim to have discovered a shortcut, but the teacher may need to check it.","zh":"學生可能聲稱已發現捷徑，但老師可能需要檢查。"},{"en":"If someone claims a discovery, evidence is needed before others accept it.","zh":"如果有人聲稱有發現，就需要證據才能讓別人接受。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a discovery claim.","zh":"這個短語描述作出發現主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be released in the skin","meaning":"在皮膚內釋放","examples":[{"en":"Vitamin D is produced through processes occurring in the skin.","zh":"維他命 D 是透過皮膚內發生的過程產生的。"},{"en":"To be released in the skin means to be produced or made available within skin tissue.","zh":"「be released in the skin」意思是在皮膚組織內產生或變得可用。"},{"en":"Some medicines are released in the skin through special patches.","zh":"有些藥物透過特殊貼片在皮膚內釋放。"},{"en":"If a substance is released in the skin after sunlight exposure, it may affect the body locally or more widely.","zh":"如果某物在接觸陽光後於皮膚內釋放，它可能局部或更廣泛地影響身體。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something becoming available inside the skin.","zh":"這個短語描述某物在皮膚內變得可用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"an excellent healer","meaning":"很好的治療者","examples":[{"en":"Some specialists describe the sun as an excellent healer.","zh":"有些專家把太陽形容為很好的治療者。"},{"en":"An excellent healer is something or someone believed to help recovery very effectively.","zh":"「an excellent healer」是被認為能非常有效幫助復原的人或事物。"},{"en":"Rest can be an excellent healer after a period of stress and overwork.","zh":"經過壓力和過勞後，休息可以是很好的治療者。"},{"en":"If sunlight improves certain conditions, people may describe it as healing.","zh":"如果陽光改善某些狀況，人們可能把它形容為有治療作用。"},{"en":"The phrase praises strong healing power, sometimes in a broad or poetic way.","zh":"這個短語讚賞強大的治療力量，有時帶有較廣泛或詩意的說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"invent the first sunscreen","meaning":"發明首種防曬產品","examples":[{"en":"One option refers to the invention of the first sunscreen.","zh":"其中一個選項提到發明首種防曬產品。"},{"en":"To invent the first sunscreen means to create the earliest product designed to protect skin from the sun.","zh":"「invent the first sunscreen」意思是創造最早用來保護皮膚免受陽光傷害的產品。"},{"en":"A chemistry student might research who invented the first sunscreen and how it worked.","zh":"化學學生可能研究誰發明首種防曬產品以及它如何運作。"},{"en":"If the first sunscreen was created, later products could improve its protection and comfort.","zh":"如果首種防曬產品被創造出來，後來產品就能改善其保護力和舒適度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an early invention in sun protection.","zh":"這個短語描述防曬保護中的早期發明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"assist with common illnesses","meaning":"幫助治療常見疾病","examples":[{"en":"Sun treatment may assist with common illnesses such as colds.","zh":"日光治療可能幫助治療感冒等常見疾病。"},{"en":"To assist with common illnesses means to help improve ordinary health problems.","zh":"「assist with common illnesses」意思是幫助改善普通健康問題。"},{"en":"Warm drinks may assist with common illnesses by easing a sore throat.","zh":"暖飲可能透過舒緩喉嚨痛，幫助治療常見疾病。"},{"en":"If sunlight improves general strength, it may indirectly help people recover from minor illness.","zh":"如果陽光改善整體體力，它可能間接幫助人從輕微疾病中復原。"},{"en":"The phrase describes support rather than a guaranteed cure.","zh":"這個短語描述支援，而不是保證治癒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"initially be of benefit","meaning":"起初對身體有益","examples":[{"en":"Sunlight may initially be of benefit to the body.","zh":"陽光起初可能對身體有益。"},{"en":"To initially be of benefit means to be helpful at first.","zh":"「initially be of benefit」意思是一開始有幫助。"},{"en":"A short rest may initially be of benefit to a tired student before studying again.","zh":"對疲倦學生而言，短暫休息在再次學習前可能起初有益。"},{"en":"If exposure continues too long, an early benefit may fade or turn into harm.","zh":"如果曝曬持續太久，早期好處可能消退或變成傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the benefit may be temporary or limited.","zh":"這個短語強調好處可能是暫時或有限的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be unsure about","meaning":"對……沒有把握","examples":[{"en":"Doctors remain unsure about some claimed benefits of the sun.","zh":"醫生對陽光某些聲稱的好處仍沒有把握。"},{"en":"To be unsure about something means not to feel certain about it.","zh":"「be unsure about」某事，意思是對它不確定。"},{"en":"A student may be unsure about an answer if the passage gives only indirect evidence.","zh":"如果篇章只提供間接證據，學生可能對答案沒有把握。"},{"en":"If doctors are unsure, more research may be needed before giving firm advice.","zh":"如果醫生沒有把握，可能需要更多研究才可給出確定建議。"},{"en":"The phrase describes uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語描述不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"specialised hospital","meaning":"專門醫院","examples":[{"en":"August Rollier opened an early specialised hospital for sun treatment.","zh":"August Rollier 開設了一所早期日光治療專門醫院。"},{"en":"A specialised hospital is a hospital focused on a particular disease, treatment, or type of patient.","zh":"「specialised hospital」是專注於特定疾病、治療或病人類型的醫院。"},{"en":"A children’s hospital is a specialised hospital for young patients.","zh":"兒童醫院是為年輕病人服務的專門醫院。"},{"en":"If a hospital focuses on sun treatment, staff can develop specific experience in that method.","zh":"如果醫院專注於日光治療，員工可以在該方法上發展特定經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a medical centre with a special focus.","zh":"這個短語描述有特殊焦點的醫療中心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the information given.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否與所給資料相符。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"「agree with the information given」意思是符合篇章所說。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should look for exact support before choosing TRUE.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生選 TRUE 前應尋找準確支持。"},{"en":"If a statement changes an important detail, it may not agree with the information.","zh":"如果陳述改變重要細節，它可能不與資料相符。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds candidates to use the passage as evidence.","zh":"這個短語提醒考生以篇章為證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"「contradict the information」意思是說出與文本相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says sunlight can be harmful, saying it is always safe contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說陽光可能有害，說它永遠安全就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"When a statement contradicts the passage, the correct response is usually FALSE or NO.","zh":"當陳述與篇章矛盾，正確回應通常是 FALSE 或 NO。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct disagreement with the source.","zh":"這個短語描述與來源直接相反。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students select “NOT GIVEN” when there is no information on this.","zh":"當沒有相關資料時，學生選擇 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not provide evidence about the point.","zh":"「there is no information on this」意思是篇章沒有提供關於該點的證據。"},{"en":"If a text never states someone’s age, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文本從未說明某人的年齡，就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"If evidence is missing, students should not use outside knowledge to decide.","zh":"如果缺乏證據，學生不應用外部知識來判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when the passage neither confirms nor denies a statement.","zh":"這個短語用於篇章既不確認也不否定某陳述的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"when it comes to","meaning":"當談到……時","examples":[{"en":"Doctors do not all agree when it comes to the health effects of sunlight.","zh":"當談到陽光的健康影響時，醫生並非全都有共識。"},{"en":"When it comes to something means when discussing or considering that subject.","zh":"「when it comes to」某事，意思是當討論或考慮該主題時。"},{"en":"When it comes to exams, planning is as important as hard work.","zh":"當談到考試時，規劃與努力同樣重要。"},{"en":"If experts disagree when it comes to sunlight, advice may depend on the specific effect being discussed.","zh":"如果專家在談到陽光時有分歧，建議可能取決於正在討論的具體影響。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the topic under consideration.","zh":"這個短語引入正在考慮的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"health benefits of the sun","meaning":"陽光的健康益處","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes both potential health benefits and risks of sunlight.","zh":"文章描述陽光潛在的健康益處和風險。"},{"en":"Health benefits of the sun are positive effects sunlight may have on the body.","zh":"「health benefits of the sun」是陽光可能對身體產生的正面影響。"},{"en":"One health benefit of the sun is helping the body produce vitamin D.","zh":"陽光的一項健康益處是幫助身體產生維他命 D。"},{"en":"If people focus only on benefits, they may ignore the danger of too much exposure.","zh":"如果人們只集中於好處，可能忽視過度曝曬的危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes possible advantages of sunlight for health.","zh":"這個短語描述陽光對健康可能有的優點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"far less pollution","meaning":"少得多的污染","examples":[{"en":"Coastal air may contain far less pollution than urban air.","zh":"沿海空氣可能比城市空氣含有少得多的污染。"},{"en":"Far less pollution means a much smaller amount of harmful or dirty substances in the air, water, or environment.","zh":"「far less pollution」意思是空氣、水或環境中的有害或污濁物質少很多。"},{"en":"A park far from traffic may have far less pollution than a roadside bus stop.","zh":"遠離交通的公園可能比路邊巴士站有少得多的污染。"},{"en":"If air contains far less pollution, people may breathe more comfortably outdoors.","zh":"如果空氣含有少得多污染，人們在戶外可能呼吸得更舒服。"},{"en":"The phrase makes a strong comparison about cleanliness.","zh":"這個短語對清潔程度作強烈比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"for protection from","meaning":"用來防止……","examples":[{"en":"People have used oils and creams for protection from the sun.","zh":"人們曾使用油和乳霜來防止陽光傷害。"},{"en":"For protection from something means used to defend against harm from it.","zh":"「for protection from」某物，意思是用來防禦它造成的傷害。"},{"en":"Cyclists wear helmets for protection from head injuries.","zh":"單車手戴頭盔是為防止頭部受傷。"},{"en":"If creams protect people from sunlight, they may reduce burning and dryness.","zh":"如果乳霜保護人們免受陽光傷害，它們可能減少曬傷和乾燥。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the protective purpose of an item or action.","zh":"這個短語解釋物件或行動的保護目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"extended exposure","meaning":"長時間曝曬","examples":[{"en":"Extended exposure of the eyes to bright sunlight can affect vision.","zh":"眼睛長時間曝曬於強烈陽光下會影響視力。"},{"en":"Extended exposure means exposure that lasts for a long time.","zh":"「extended exposure」意思是持續很長時間的接觸或曝露。"},{"en":"Extended exposure to cold weather can make fingers numb.","zh":"長時間暴露於寒冷天氣會令手指麻木。"},{"en":"If eyes are exposed to bright light for hours, vision may become temporarily weaker.","zh":"如果眼睛數小時暴露於強光下，視力可能暫時變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase warns about long contact with a condition.","zh":"這個短語警告長時間接觸某種環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"lead to blindness","meaning":"導致失明","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether sun exposure can lead to blindness.","zh":"該陳述問日曬是否會導致失明。"},{"en":"To lead to blindness means to cause a person to lose the ability to see.","zh":"「lead to blindness」意思是導致一個人失去視力。"},{"en":"Some untreated eye diseases can lead to blindness over time.","zh":"有些未治療眼疾可能隨時間導致失明。"},{"en":"If bright sunlight damages the eyes severely, doctors worry about long-term vision loss.","zh":"如果強烈陽光嚴重損害眼睛，醫生會擔心長期視力喪失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a very serious result affecting sight.","zh":"這個短語描述影響視力的非常嚴重結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"heal itself","meaning":"自行復原","examples":[{"en":"The eye may recover gradually from some sunlight-related damage.","zh":"眼睛可能從某些陽光相關傷害中逐漸自行復原。"},{"en":"To heal itself means to repair naturally without major outside treatment.","zh":"「heal itself」意思是自然修復，而不需要重大外部治療。"},{"en":"A small scratch may heal itself if it is kept clean.","zh":"小擦傷如果保持清潔，可能自行復原。"},{"en":"If eye damage is mild, vision may improve slowly over several weeks.","zh":"如果眼部傷害輕微，視力可能在數星期內慢慢改善。"},{"en":"The phrase describes natural recovery by the body.","zh":"這個短語描述身體自然復原。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the summary using words from the box.","zh":"考生使用方框中的詞語完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill in missing words so the short version of the passage makes sense.","zh":"「complete the summary」意思是填入缺失詞語，使篇章簡短版本意思通順。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete a summary by choosing words that fit both grammar and meaning.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過選擇符合文法和意思的詞語完成摘要。"},{"en":"If one word does not fit the context, the whole summary sentence may become wrong.","zh":"如果一個詞不符合語境，整句摘要可能變錯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common reading-comprehension task.","zh":"這個短語描述常見閱讀理解任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"excessive exposure","meaning":"過度曝曬","examples":[{"en":"Excessive exposure to the sun can contribute to skin cancer.","zh":"過度曝曬於陽光可以促成皮膚癌。"},{"en":"Excessive exposure means too much contact with something, especially something harmful.","zh":"「excessive exposure」意思是過多接觸某物，尤其是有害事物。"},{"en":"Excessive exposure to loud noise can damage hearing.","zh":"過度接觸巨大噪音可以損害聽力。"},{"en":"If sun exposure is excessive, the risk of long-term skin damage increases.","zh":"如果日曬過度，長期皮膚損傷風險會增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes harmful overexposure.","zh":"這個短語描述有害的過度暴露。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"as far as…is concerned","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"As far as sun damage is concerned, the face and hands are highly exposed.","zh":"就陽光傷害而言，臉和手高度暴露。"},{"en":"As far as something is concerned means when considering that particular topic.","zh":"「as far as…is concerned」意思是就某特定題目而言。"},{"en":"As far as grammar is concerned, articles and verb forms need careful checking.","zh":"就文法而言，冠詞和動詞形式需要仔細檢查。"},{"en":"If the topic is sun damage, uncovered body parts matter most.","zh":"如果題目是陽光傷害，沒有遮蓋的身體部位最重要。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows attention to one issue.","zh":"這個短語把注意力收窄到一個議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"primarily affected","meaning":"主要受到影響","examples":[{"en":"The face and hands are primarily affected by long-term sunlight.","zh":"臉和手主要受到長期陽光影響。"},{"en":"Primarily affected means affected first, most directly, or most strongly.","zh":"「primarily affected」意思是首先、最直接或最強烈受到影響。"},{"en":"During a flood, low-lying homes are primarily affected.","zh":"在水災中，低窪住戶主要受到影響。"},{"en":"If face and hands receive the most sun, they may show damage earlier than covered areas.","zh":"如果臉和手接收最多陽光，它們可能比被遮蓋部位更早顯示傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main part or group affected.","zh":"這個短語指出主要受影響的部分或群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a blend of","meaning":"……的混合物","examples":[{"en":"The skin is protected by a blend of natural oils and acids.","zh":"皮膚由天然油脂和酸性物質的混合物保護。"},{"en":"A blend of things is a mixture of different elements.","zh":"「a blend of」幾種東西，是不同元素的混合物。"},{"en":"A smoothie may contain a blend of fruit, yoghurt, and ice.","zh":"奶昔可能含有水果、乳酪和冰的混合物。"},{"en":"If oils and acids mix on the skin, they can form a protective surface.","zh":"如果油脂和酸性物質在皮膚上混合，它們可以形成保護表面。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a combined mixture.","zh":"這個短語描述結合而成的混合物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"natural oils and acids","meaning":"天然油脂和酸性物質","examples":[{"en":"Natural oils and acids help form the skin’s protective surface.","zh":"天然油脂和酸性物質有助形成皮膚的保護表面。"},{"en":"Natural oils and acids are substances produced by the skin that help protect and maintain it.","zh":"「natural oils and acids」是皮膚產生、用來幫助保護和維持皮膚的物質。"},{"en":"Gentle soap is less likely to remove natural oils and acids from the skin.","zh":"溫和肥皂較不容易洗走皮膚上的天然油脂和酸性物質。"},{"en":"If these substances are stripped away, the skin may become dry or more vulnerable.","zh":"如果這些物質被剝走，皮膚可能變乾或更脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes part of the skin’s natural defence.","zh":"這個短語描述皮膚天然防線的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"for some time","meaning":"一段時間以來","examples":[{"en":"For some time, women have generally taken greater care of their skin.","zh":"一段時間以來，女性一般較重視皮膚護理。"},{"en":"For some time means for a period that is not short, though the exact length is not stated.","zh":"「for some time」意思是持續了一段不短的時間，但沒有說明確切長度。"},{"en":"The lift has been out of order for some time, so residents use the stairs.","zh":"升降機壞了一段時間，所以居民使用樓梯。"},{"en":"If a habit has existed for some time, it may be part of culture or routine.","zh":"如果習慣存在了一段時間，它可能已成為文化或日常的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate period of duration.","zh":"這個短語提供大約持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be effective in caring for","meaning":"善於護理……","examples":[{"en":"Women have traditionally been more effective in caring for their skin.","zh":"女性傳統上更善於護理自己的皮膚。"},{"en":"To be effective in caring for something means to look after it successfully.","zh":"「be effective in caring for」某物，意思是成功地照顧它。"},{"en":"A nurse is effective in caring for patients when she notices problems early.","zh":"護士能及早注意問題時，就是善於照顧病人。"},{"en":"If people use sunscreen and moisturiser regularly, they may be more effective in caring for their skin.","zh":"如果人們定期使用防曬產品和潤膚霜，他們可能更善於護理皮膚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes successful care or protection.","zh":"這個短語描述成功的照顧或保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"go undetected","meaning":"未被察覺","examples":[{"en":"Gradual damage to the eyes may go undetected.","zh":"眼睛的逐漸損傷可能未被察覺。"},{"en":"To go undetected means not to be noticed or discovered.","zh":"「go undetected」意思是沒有被注意或發現。"},{"en":"A small leak may go undetected until the wall becomes damp.","zh":"小漏水可能直到牆身變濕才被察覺。"},{"en":"If eye damage happens slowly, people may not realise their vision has changed.","zh":"如果眼睛傷害慢慢發生，人們可能沒有意識到視力已改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a hidden problem that is not noticed.","zh":"這個短語描述未被注意的隱藏問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"happen quite slowly","meaning":"相當緩慢地發生","examples":[{"en":"Sun-related changes to vision may happen quite slowly.","zh":"與陽光有關的視力變化可能相當緩慢地發生。"},{"en":"To happen quite slowly means to take place gradually rather than suddenly.","zh":"「happen quite slowly」意思是逐漸發生，而不是突然發生。"},{"en":"A student’s writing improvement may happen quite slowly over several months.","zh":"學生的寫作進步可能在幾個月內相當緩慢地發生。"},{"en":"If a change is slow, people may not notice it until they compare old and new results.","zh":"如果變化很慢，人們可能直到比較新舊結果才察覺。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual development.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"Hair, on the other hand, becomes brittle after prolonged exposure.","zh":"另一方面，頭髮長時間曝曬後會變得脆弱。"},{"en":"On the other hand introduces a contrast or another side of the discussion.","zh":"「on the other hand」引出對比或討論的另一面。"},{"en":"Sunlight helps vitamin D production; on the other hand, too much sunlight can damage skin.","zh":"陽光幫助維他命 D 生成；另一方面，太多陽光會傷害皮膚。"},{"en":"If one body part is affected differently from another, this phrase helps show the contrast.","zh":"如果一個身體部位與另一部位受影響不同，這個短語有助顯示對比。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful for comparing two ideas.","zh":"這個短語適合用來比較兩個想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"lanolin-based conditioner","meaning":"以羊毛脂為主要成分的護髮素","examples":[{"en":"A lanolin-based conditioner can help restore dry hair.","zh":"以羊毛脂為主要成分的護髮素可以幫助修復乾旱頭髮。"},{"en":"A lanolin-based conditioner is a hair product whose main moisturising ingredient is lanolin.","zh":"「lanolin-based conditioner」是主要滋潤成分為羊毛脂的護髮產品。"},{"en":"Someone with dry hair after swimming may use a lanolin-based conditioner.","zh":"游泳後頭髮乾旱的人可能使用以羊毛脂為主要成分的護髮素。"},{"en":"If hair loses softness after sun exposure, lanolin may help coat and soften it.","zh":"如果頭髮在日曬後失去柔順，羊毛脂可能幫助包覆並柔軟頭髮。"},{"en":"The phrase names a conditioner made mainly with lanolin.","zh":"這個短語指出主要由羊毛脂製成的護髮素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"overcome the problem","meaning":"解決問題","examples":[{"en":"A suitable conditioner may help overcome the problem of dry hair.","zh":"合適的護髮素可能幫助解決乾旱頭髮的問題。"},{"en":"To overcome the problem means to solve or reduce the difficulty successfully.","zh":"「overcome the problem」意思是成功解決或減少困難。"},{"en":"A student may overcome the problem of weak vocabulary by reading daily.","zh":"學生可能透過每天閱讀來解決詞彙薄弱問題。"},{"en":"If hair is dry because of sunlight, conditioner can reduce roughness and improve texture.","zh":"如果頭髮因陽光而乾燥，護髮素可以減少粗糙並改善質感。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dealing successfully with a difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述成功處理困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the best solution for","meaning":"解決……的最佳方法","examples":[{"en":"A simple hat may be the best solution for protecting the hair.","zh":"一頂簡單帽子可能是保護頭髮的最佳方法。"},{"en":"The best solution for something is the most suitable way to deal with that problem or need.","zh":"「the best solution for」某事，是最適合處理該問題或需要的方法。"},{"en":"For a noisy classroom, the best solution may be clearer rules and better seating.","zh":"對嘈吵課室而言，最佳方法可能是更清楚規則和更好座位安排。"},{"en":"If a hat protects both hair and health, it may be better than using hair products alone.","zh":"如果帽子同時保護頭髮和健康，它可能比單靠護髮產品更好。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the most effective answer to a problem.","zh":"這個短語指出解決問題的最有效答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 132 - How to handle the Sun.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 133":[{"front":"carbon capture and storage","meaning":"碳捕集與封存","examples":[{"en":"Carbon capture and storage may help reduce emissions from coal-fired power plants.","zh":"碳捕集與封存可能有助減少燃煤發電廠的排放。"},{"en":"Carbon capture and storage is a process that captures carbon dioxide and stores it underground instead of releasing it into the air.","zh":"碳捕集與封存是一個捕集二氧化碳並把它儲存在地下、而不是釋放到空氣中的過程。"},{"en":"A power company may use carbon capture and storage if it wants to keep using coal while reducing pollution.","zh":"如果電力公司想繼續使用煤炭同時減少污染，可能會使用碳捕集與封存。"},{"en":"If carbon dioxide is captured and buried safely, less of it enters the atmosphere.","zh":"如果二氧化碳被捕集並安全埋藏，進入大氣的二氧化碳就會較少。"},{"en":"The phrase is often shortened to CCS and is discussed as a climate-change technology.","zh":"這個短語常縮寫為 CCS，並被討論為一種氣候變化科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"high coal dependence","meaning":"高度依賴煤炭","examples":[{"en":"Many industrialised countries still have a high dependence on coal.","zh":"許多工業化國家仍高度依賴煤炭。"},{"en":"High coal dependence means a country or system relies heavily on coal for energy, industry or electricity.","zh":"高度依賴煤炭指一個國家或系統在能源、工業或電力方面非常依靠煤。"},{"en":"A city with many coal-fired power stations has high coal dependence.","zh":"一個有許多燃煤發電站的城市，就是高度依賴煤炭。"},{"en":"High coal dependence can make emissions hard to reduce because many homes and factories need coal-based power.","zh":"高度依賴煤炭會令減排困難，因為許多家庭和工廠需要燃煤電力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes energy reliance, not simply ownership of coal mines.","zh":"這個短語描述能源依賴，而不只是擁有煤礦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"renewable energy","meaning":"可再生能源","examples":[{"en":"Renewable energy is widely discussed as an alternative to fossil fuels.","zh":"可再生能源被廣泛討論為化石燃料的替代方案。"},{"en":"Renewable energy comes from sources that can naturally replenish, such as sunlight, wind and water.","zh":"可再生能源來自能自然補充的來源，例如陽光、風和水。"},{"en":"A school may install solar panels to use renewable energy for part of its electricity.","zh":"學校可能安裝太陽能板，用可再生能源供應部分電力。"},{"en":"If renewable energy becomes cheaper, countries can reduce their reliance on coal and oil.","zh":"如果可再生能源變得更便宜，國家就能減少對煤和石油的依賴。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts clean, replaceable energy sources with fuels that run out and pollute.","zh":"這個短語把清潔、可補充的能源與會耗盡和污染的燃料作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"play the greatest role in","meaning":"在……中發揮最大作用","examples":[{"en":"Coal still plays the greatest role in electricity generation worldwide.","zh":"煤炭在全球發電中仍發揮最大作用。"},{"en":"To play the greatest role in something means to be the most important factor or contributor.","zh":"在某事中發揮最大作用，指成為最重要因素或最大貢獻者。"},{"en":"In a classroom discussion, clear examples may play the greatest role in helping students understand.","zh":"在課堂討論中，清楚例子可能在幫助學生理解方面發揮最大作用。"},{"en":"If coal produces the largest share of electricity, it plays the greatest role in that energy system.","zh":"如果煤炭產生最大比例的電力，它就在該能源系統中發揮最大作用。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when comparing several influences and identifying the biggest one.","zh":"這個短語用於比較幾種影響並指出最大的一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the generation of electricity","meaning":"發電","examples":[{"en":"Coal remains important in the generation of electricity.","zh":"煤炭在發電中仍然重要。"},{"en":"The generation of electricity means the process of producing electrical power.","zh":"發電指產生電力的過程。"},{"en":"A wind farm contributes to the generation of electricity by turning wind into power.","zh":"風力發電場透過把風轉化為電力來參與發電。"},{"en":"If electricity generation relies on coal, carbon emissions may remain high.","zh":"如果發電依賴煤炭，碳排放可能仍然偏高。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on producing electricity, not using it at home.","zh":"這個短語強調生產電力，而不是在家中使用電力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"recent figures from","meaning":"來自……的最新數字","examples":[{"en":"Recent figures from the International Energy Agency show continued reliance on coal.","zh":"來自國際能源署的最新數字顯示各國仍依賴煤炭。"},{"en":"Recent figures from a source are the latest numbers or statistics provided by that source.","zh":"來自某來源的最新數字，是該來源提供的最新數據或統計。"},{"en":"Recent figures from a school survey may show that students are sleeping less than before.","zh":"來自學校調查的最新數字可能顯示學生睡眠比以前少。"},{"en":"If recent figures show rising electricity demand, governments may need new energy plans.","zh":"如果最新數字顯示電力需求上升，政府可能需要新的能源計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence based on updated data.","zh":"這個短語引出以最新數據為基礎的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rely on something for","meaning":"依賴……提供","examples":[{"en":"Some countries rely on coal for most of their electricity.","zh":"一些國家依賴煤炭提供大部分電力。"},{"en":"To rely on something for a need means to depend on it to provide that need.","zh":"依賴某物提供某需要，指靠它滿足該需要。"},{"en":"Many students rely on public transport for getting to school.","zh":"許多學生依賴公共交通上學。"},{"en":"If a town relies on one factory for jobs, closing that factory can damage the whole community.","zh":"如果城鎮依賴一間工廠提供職位，工廠關閉會損害整個社區。"},{"en":"The phrase shows dependence on a source for a specific purpose.","zh":"這個短語顯示為特定目的而依靠某來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be less reliant on","meaning":"較少依賴……","examples":[{"en":"Germany is less reliant on coal than China or Australia.","zh":"德國比中國或澳洲較少依賴煤炭。"},{"en":"To be less reliant on something means to depend on it to a smaller degree.","zh":"較少依賴某物，指對它的依靠程度較低。"},{"en":"A student becomes less reliant on a dictionary when their vocabulary improves.","zh":"當詞彙量改善，學生就會較少依賴字典。"},{"en":"If a country builds more wind and solar power, it may become less reliant on coal.","zh":"如果國家建設更多風能和太陽能，它可能較少依賴煤炭。"},{"en":"The phrase compares different levels of dependence.","zh":"這個短語比較不同程度的依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the global average","meaning":"全球平均水平","examples":[{"en":"Germany’s level of coal dependence is close to the global average.","zh":"德國對煤炭的依賴程度接近全球平均水平。"},{"en":"The global average is the average figure calculated across the whole world.","zh":"全球平均水平是按全世界計算出的平均數字。"},{"en":"A country’s internet speed may be above or below the global average.","zh":"一個國家的網速可能高於或低於全球平均水平。"},{"en":"If a country is close to the global average, it is not unusually high or unusually low compared with others.","zh":"如果一個國家接近全球平均水平，與其他國家相比就不是特別高或特別低。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a worldwide point of comparison.","zh":"這個短語提供全球範圍的比較點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"furthermore","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"Furthermore, many countries possess large coal deposits.","zh":"此外，許多國家擁有大型煤礦藏。"},{"en":"Furthermore means in addition to what has already been said.","zh":"“Furthermore” 指除了已說的內容之外。"},{"en":"The library is quiet; furthermore, it has free Wi-Fi and long opening hours.","zh":"圖書館很安靜；此外，它有免費 Wi-Fi 和長開放時間。"},{"en":"If a writer says “furthermore,” they are adding another reason or piece of evidence.","zh":"如果作者說 “furthermore”，就是在加入另一個理由或證據。"},{"en":"The word helps build an argument by adding a supporting point.","zh":"這個詞透過加入支持點來建立論證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"easily accessible deposits","meaning":"容易開採的礦藏","examples":[{"en":"Many countries have large, easily accessible deposits of coal.","zh":"許多國家有大型、容易開採的煤礦藏。"},{"en":"Easily accessible deposits are mineral or fuel reserves that can be reached and extracted without extreme difficulty.","zh":"容易開採的礦藏，是能在沒有極大困難下到達並開採的礦物或燃料儲量。"},{"en":"A quarry near a road has more easily accessible stone than one deep in a remote mountain.","zh":"靠近道路的採石場，比深山偏遠地區的石材更容易開採。"},{"en":"If coal deposits are easy to access, mining them may be cheaper and more attractive.","zh":"如果煤礦藏容易開採，開採成本可能較低，也更具吸引力。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why a resource may continue to be used.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何某資源可能繼續被使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"coal deposits","meaning":"煤礦藏","examples":[{"en":"Coal deposits remain economically important in many countries.","zh":"煤礦藏在許多國家仍具有經濟重要性。"},{"en":"Coal deposits are natural underground reserves of coal.","zh":"煤礦藏是天然存在於地下的煤炭儲量。"},{"en":"A mining town may grow around nearby coal deposits.","zh":"採礦城鎮可能圍繞附近煤礦藏發展起來。"},{"en":"If a country has large coal deposits, it may be tempted to keep using coal for energy.","zh":"如果一個國家有大型煤礦藏，它可能傾向繼續使用煤炭作能源。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to coal still lying in the ground, not coal already burnt.","zh":"這個短語指仍埋在地下的煤，而不是已燃燒的煤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"highly skilled workers","meaning":"高技能工人","examples":[{"en":"The industry employs many highly skilled miners, chemists and engineers.","zh":"該行業僱用許多高技能礦工、化學家和工程師。"},{"en":"Highly skilled workers are workers with advanced training, knowledge or technical ability.","zh":"高技能工人是擁有進階培訓、知識或技術能力的工人。"},{"en":"Hospitals need highly skilled workers such as surgeons, nurses and laboratory specialists.","zh":"醫院需要外科醫生、護士和實驗室專家等高技能工人。"},{"en":"If an industry depends on highly skilled workers, sudden closure can waste years of training.","zh":"如果一個行業依賴高技能工人，突然關閉可能浪費多年培訓。"},{"en":"The phrase describes labour that is specialised, not simple or untrained.","zh":"這個短語描述專門勞動，而不是簡單或未受訓工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"steel production","meaning":"鋼鐵生產","examples":[{"en":"Much of the world’s steel production requires coal.","zh":"世界大部分鋼鐵生產需要煤炭。"},{"en":"Steel production is the process of making steel for buildings, vehicles, tools and machines.","zh":"鋼鐵生產是製造供建築、車輛、工具和機器使用的鋼材的過程。"},{"en":"A construction company depends on steel production because bridges and skyscrapers need strong metal.","zh":"建築公司依賴鋼鐵生產，因為橋樑和摩天大廈需要堅固金屬。"},{"en":"If steel production uses coal, reducing coal use becomes harder for heavy industry.","zh":"如果鋼鐵生產使用煤炭，重工業減少用煤就更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to industrial manufacturing of steel, not small-scale metal repair.","zh":"這個短語指工業化製造鋼材，而不是小規模金屬維修。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"coal derivatives","meaning":"煤炭衍生物","examples":[{"en":"Some plastics and synthetic fibres are coal derivatives.","zh":"一些塑膠和合成纖維是煤炭衍生物。"},{"en":"Coal derivatives are materials or chemicals made from coal or produced through coal-related processes.","zh":"煤炭衍生物是由煤製成，或透過煤相關過程產生的材料或化學物。"},{"en":"A factory may use coal derivatives to make certain dyes, fibres or chemical products.","zh":"工廠可能使用煤炭衍生物來製造某些染料、纖維或化學產品。"},{"en":"If many products are coal derivatives, coal affects more than electricity generation.","zh":"如果許多產品是煤炭衍生物，煤炭影響的就不只是發電。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that coal can be a raw material, not only a fuel.","zh":"這個短語顯示煤可以是原材料，而不只是燃料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"coal-fired power plants","meaning":"燃煤發電廠","examples":[{"en":"Coal-fired power plants continue to meet enormous energy demands.","zh":"燃煤發電廠繼續滿足龐大能源需求。"},{"en":"Coal-fired power plants are power stations that burn coal to produce electricity.","zh":"燃煤發電廠是燃燒煤炭來發電的電站。"},{"en":"A city may receive electricity from a coal-fired power plant outside the urban area.","zh":"城市可能從市區外的燃煤發電廠取得電力。"},{"en":"If coal-fired power plants run day and night, they can emit large amounts of carbon dioxide.","zh":"如果燃煤發電廠日夜運作，它們可以排放大量二氧化碳。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a major source of electricity and pollution.","zh":"這個短語描述電力和污染的重要來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"feed a voracious appetite for","meaning":"滿足對……的龐大需求","examples":[{"en":"Power plants feed society’s voracious appetite for energy.","zh":"發電廠滿足社會對能源的龐大需求。"},{"en":"To feed a voracious appetite for something means to satisfy an extremely large and continuing demand for it.","zh":"滿足對某事的龐大需求，指滿足對它極大而持續的需求。"},{"en":"Streaming platforms feed people’s voracious appetite for entertainment by releasing new shows constantly.","zh":"串流平台透過不斷推出新節目，滿足人們對娛樂的龐大需求。"},{"en":"If society keeps demanding more electricity, power plants must produce more energy.","zh":"如果社會持續要求更多電力，發電廠就必須生產更多能源。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a demand that is huge, hungry and difficult to satisfy.","zh":"這個短語暗示需求巨大、飢餓且難以滿足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"produce something in staggering amounts","meaning":"產生數量驚人的……","examples":[{"en":"Coal-fired plants produce carbon dioxide in staggering amounts.","zh":"燃煤發電廠產生數量驚人的二氧化碳。"},{"en":"To produce something in staggering amounts means to create an extremely large and surprising quantity of it.","zh":"產生數量驚人的某物，指製造出極大量且令人吃驚的東西。"},{"en":"A busy takeaway shop may produce plastic waste in staggering amounts every weekend.","zh":"繁忙外賣店每個週末可能產生數量驚人的塑膠廢物。"},{"en":"If a power plant burns coal continuously, its emissions can become enormous.","zh":"如果發電廠持續燃煤，其排放量可以變得非常巨大。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the amount is shockingly high.","zh":"這個短語強調數量高得令人震驚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"staggering amounts","meaning":"驚人的數量","examples":[{"en":"Coal plants release staggering amounts of carbon dioxide.","zh":"燃煤電廠釋放驚人數量的二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Staggering amounts are extremely large amounts that surprise or shock people.","zh":"驚人的數量是極大量，令人驚訝或震驚。"},{"en":"A school can waste staggering amounts of paper if every notice is printed for every student.","zh":"如果每張通告都為每名學生列印，學校可能浪費驚人數量的紙張。"},{"en":"If emissions reach staggering amounts, ordinary small reductions may not be enough.","zh":"如果排放達到驚人數量，普通的小幅減少可能不足夠。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when the size of something feels almost unbelievable.","zh":"這個短語用於描述大得幾乎難以置信的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"urban residents","meaning":"城市居民","examples":[{"en":"Urban residents may complain about rising electricity bills.","zh":"城市居民可能抱怨電費上升。"},{"en":"Urban residents are people who live in cities or towns rather than rural areas.","zh":"城市居民是住在城市或城鎮，而不是鄉郊地區的人。"},{"en":"Urban residents often depend on public transport, apartment electricity and city services.","zh":"城市居民常依賴公共交通、公寓電力和城市服務。"},{"en":"If power prices rise, urban residents may feel the cost quickly in monthly bills.","zh":"如果電價上升，城市居民可能很快在每月帳單中感受到成本。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to city dwellers as a group.","zh":"這個短語把城市居住者作為一個群體來指稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"grumble about","meaning":"抱怨……","examples":[{"en":"Consumers often grumble about high monthly electricity bills.","zh":"消費者常抱怨每月電費高昂。"},{"en":"To grumble about something means to complain quietly or repeatedly about it.","zh":"“Grumble about” 某事指小聲或反覆抱怨它。"},{"en":"Students may grumble about homework when they feel tired after school.","zh":"學生放學後疲倦時，可能抱怨功課。"},{"en":"If electricity bills rise every month, families may grumble even if they still pay them.","zh":"如果電費每月上升，家庭即使仍然付款，也可能抱怨。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests everyday dissatisfaction rather than formal protest.","zh":"這個短語暗示日常不滿，而不是正式抗議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"monthly electricity bill","meaning":"每月電費","examples":[{"en":"The average monthly electricity bill can be a significant household expense.","zh":"平均每月電費可以是一項重要家庭開支。"},{"en":"A monthly electricity bill is the amount a household or business pays for electricity each month.","zh":"每月電費是家庭或企業每月為用電支付的金額。"},{"en":"A family may reduce its monthly electricity bill by turning off air-conditioning when no one is home.","zh":"家庭可以在無人在家時關掉冷氣，以減少每月電費。"},{"en":"If power prices rise, the monthly electricity bill becomes harder for low-income families to manage.","zh":"如果電價上升，低收入家庭會更難應付每月電費。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to regular payment for electricity use.","zh":"這個短語指為用電定期支付的費用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be charged for","meaning":"被收取……的費用","examples":[{"en":"Consumers are not directly charged for the carbon dioxide emitted by power plants.","zh":"消費者並沒有因發電廠排放的二氧化碳而被直接收費。"},{"en":"To be charged for something means to be required to pay money for it.","zh":"被收取某物的費用，指被要求為它付款。"},{"en":"A customer may be charged for extra luggage at the airport.","zh":"顧客在機場可能因額外行李而被收費。"},{"en":"If people are not charged for pollution, the environmental cost may be hidden.","zh":"如果人們沒有因污染被收費，環境成本可能被隱藏。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a cost with the person who pays it.","zh":"這個短語把成本與付款者連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"metric tons of CO₂","meaning":"公噸二氧化碳","examples":[{"en":"A large power plant may emit millions of metric tons of CO₂.","zh":"大型發電廠可能排放數百萬公噸二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Metric tons of CO₂ are measured amounts of carbon dioxide, with one metric ton equal to 1,000 kilograms.","zh":"公噸二氧化碳是量度二氧化碳的單位，一公噸等於一千公斤。"},{"en":"A climate report may compare how many metric tons of CO₂ different factories emit each year.","zh":"氣候報告可能比較不同工廠每年排放多少公噸二氧化碳。"},{"en":"If emissions are measured in millions of metric tons, the scale is very large.","zh":"如果排放以數百萬公噸計算，規模就非常大。"},{"en":"The phrase is used for quantifying carbon dioxide pollution.","zh":"這個短語用於量化二氧化碳污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be emitted by","meaning":"由……排放","examples":[{"en":"Large quantities of carbon dioxide are emitted by coal-fired plants.","zh":"大量二氧化碳由燃煤電廠排放。"},{"en":"To be emitted by something means to be released or sent out from that source.","zh":"由某物排放，指從該來源釋放或散發出來。"},{"en":"Smoke may be emitted by an old bus when its engine is poorly maintained.","zh":"如果引擎保養不佳，舊巴士可能排放煙霧。"},{"en":"If carbon dioxide is emitted by power plants, it enters the atmosphere and contributes to warming.","zh":"如果二氧化碳由發電廠排放，它就進入大氣並加劇暖化。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of a release.","zh":"這個短語指出釋放物的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"account for","meaning":"佔……","examples":[{"en":"Coal accounts for a large share of global carbon emissions.","zh":"煤炭佔全球碳排放很大比例。"},{"en":"To account for a share means to form or make up that portion of the total.","zh":"“Account for” 某比例指構成總量中的該部分。"},{"en":"Rent may account for half of a student’s monthly expenses.","zh":"租金可能佔學生每月開支的一半。"},{"en":"If coal accounts for a large part of emissions, cutting coal use can have a major effect.","zh":"如果煤炭佔排放很大部分，減少用煤就可以有重大影響。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to describe proportion or contribution.","zh":"這個短語用於描述比例或貢獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"global CO₂ emissions","meaning":"全球二氧化碳排放","examples":[{"en":"Coal is responsible for a substantial proportion of global CO₂ emissions.","zh":"煤炭負責全球二氧化碳排放中相當大的比例。"},{"en":"Global CO₂ emissions are the total carbon dioxide emissions released around the world.","zh":"全球二氧化碳排放是全世界釋放出的二氧化碳總量。"},{"en":"Scientists study global CO₂ emissions to understand how human activity affects climate.","zh":"科學家研究全球二氧化碳排放，以理解人類活動如何影響氣候。"},{"en":"If global CO₂ emissions continue rising, climate risks may become more severe.","zh":"如果全球二氧化碳排放持續上升，氣候風險可能變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to worldwide carbon dioxide pollution.","zh":"這個短語指全球範圍的二氧化碳污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fossil fuels","meaning":"化石燃料","examples":[{"en":"Coal, oil and natural gas are fossil fuels.","zh":"煤、石油和天然氣都是化石燃料。"},{"en":"Fossil fuels are fuels formed from ancient living matter over millions of years.","zh":"化石燃料是由遠古生物物質經數百萬年形成的燃料。"},{"en":"Cars, ships and power plants often use fossil fuels for energy.","zh":"汽車、船隻和發電廠常使用化石燃料作能源。"},{"en":"Burning fossil fuels releases carbon dioxide and other pollutants.","zh":"燃燒化石燃料會釋放二氧化碳和其他污染物。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to non-renewable energy sources such as coal, oil and gas.","zh":"這個短語指煤、石油和天然氣等不可再生能源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"skies fill with smog","meaning":"天空充滿煙霧","examples":[{"en":"In heavily polluted cities, the skies may fill with smog.","zh":"在嚴重污染的城市，天空可能充滿煙霧。"},{"en":"When skies fill with smog, polluted air makes the sky look grey, dirty or unclear.","zh":"當天空充滿煙霧，受污染空氣會令天空看起來灰暗、骯髒或不清晰。"},{"en":"During a pollution episode, urban residents may see the skies fill with smog by afternoon.","zh":"在污染事件中，城市居民下午可能看見天空充滿煙霧。"},{"en":"If skies fill with smog, people with breathing problems may need to stay indoors.","zh":"如果天空充滿煙霧，有呼吸問題的人可能需要留在室內。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visible air pollution.","zh":"這個短語描述可見的空氣污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"temperatures soar","meaning":"氣溫急升","examples":[{"en":"Global temperatures continue to soar as emissions rise.","zh":"隨着排放上升，全球氣溫繼續急升。"},{"en":"When temperatures soar, they rise quickly or to a very high level.","zh":"氣溫急升指氣溫快速上升或升至很高水平。"},{"en":"In summer, classroom temperatures may soar if the air-conditioning breaks down.","zh":"夏天如果冷氣壞掉，課室氣溫可能急升。"},{"en":"If greenhouse gases increase, average temperatures can rise over time.","zh":"如果溫室氣體增加，平均氣溫會隨時間上升。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a sharp and worrying increase in heat.","zh":"這個短語暗示熱度急劇而令人擔心地增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"crave clean air","meaning":"渴望清潔空氣","examples":[{"en":"People increasingly crave clean air and affordable energy.","zh":"人們越來越渴望清潔空氣和可負擔能源。"},{"en":"To crave clean air means to strongly want air that is safe and free from pollution.","zh":"渴望清潔空氣指強烈希望有安全、沒有污染的空氣。"},{"en":"Residents near a busy road may crave clean air after years of breathing exhaust fumes.","zh":"住在繁忙道路附近的居民多年吸入廢氣後，可能渴望清潔空氣。"},{"en":"If smog becomes common, public demand for clean air will grow.","zh":"如果煙霧變得常見，公眾對清潔空氣的需求會增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong human need, not just a mild preference.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈人類需要，而不只是輕微偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cheap power","meaning":"廉價電力","examples":[{"en":"Governments face pressure to provide both clean air and cheap power.","zh":"政府面對壓力，要同時提供清潔空氣和廉價電力。"},{"en":"Cheap power means electricity that people and businesses can afford.","zh":"廉價電力指市民和企業負擔得起的電力。"},{"en":"A factory may move away if cheap power is no longer available.","zh":"如果不再有廉價電力，工廠可能遷走。"},{"en":"If energy becomes expensive, families may struggle to pay monthly bills.","zh":"如果能源變昂貴，家庭可能難以支付每月帳單。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to affordable electricity, often in tension with environmental goals.","zh":"這個短語指可負擔電力，常與環境目標存在張力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change","meaning":"政府間氣候變化專門委員會","examples":[{"en":"The Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change advises governments on climate risks.","zh":"政府間氣候變化專門委員會就氣候風險向政府提供意見。"},{"en":"The Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change is an international scientific body that assesses climate-change evidence.","zh":"政府間氣候變化專門委員會是一個評估氣候變化證據的國際科學機構。"},{"en":"Students may read IPCC summaries to understand why scientists worry about global warming.","zh":"學生可能閱讀 IPCC 摘要，以理解科學家為何擔心全球暖化。"},{"en":"If governments need climate guidance, they may use IPCC reports to shape policy.","zh":"如果政府需要氣候指引，可能使用 IPCC 報告制定政策。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major international climate-science organisation.","zh":"這個短語指一個重要的國際氣候科學組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"advise the United Nations","meaning":"向聯合國提供意見","examples":[{"en":"The panel advises the United Nations on climate change.","zh":"該專門委員會就氣候變化向聯合國提供意見。"},{"en":"To advise the United Nations means to give expert guidance to the UN.","zh":"向聯合國提供意見指向聯合國給予專業指引。"},{"en":"Scientists may advise the United Nations on health risks, food security or climate action.","zh":"科學家可能就健康風險、糧食安全或氣候行動向聯合國提供意見。"},{"en":"If an expert group advises the UN, its findings can influence international policy.","zh":"如果專家組向聯合國提供意見，其研究結果可以影響國際政策。"},{"en":"The phrase describes providing specialist recommendations to a global organisation.","zh":"這個短語描述向全球組織提供專門建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a rise of just","meaning":"僅僅上升……","examples":[{"en":"A rise of just two degrees could cause serious harm.","zh":"僅僅上升兩度就可能造成嚴重損害。"},{"en":"A rise of just a certain amount means even that small increase may be important.","zh":"僅僅上升某數量，指即使這小幅增加也可能重要。"},{"en":"A rise of just five dollars in daily lunch costs can affect a student’s weekly budget.","zh":"每日午餐費僅僅上升五元，就可能影響學生每週預算。"},{"en":"If global temperature rises by only two degrees, the effects may still be severe.","zh":"如果全球氣溫只上升兩度，影響仍可能很嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that a seemingly small increase can matter greatly.","zh":"這個短語強調看似小的增加也可以非常重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mark the threshold of","meaning":"標誌着……的臨界點","examples":[{"en":"A two-degree increase may mark the threshold of serious environmental harm.","zh":"兩度升幅可能標誌着嚴重環境損害的臨界點。"},{"en":"To mark the threshold of something means to indicate the point at which it begins or becomes dangerous.","zh":"標誌着某事的臨界點，指指出某事開始或變得危險的界線。"},{"en":"A fever may mark the threshold of illness when body temperature rises above normal.","zh":"當體溫高於正常水平，發燒可能標誌着疾病的臨界點。"},{"en":"If warming passes a certain threshold, environmental damage may become much harder to control.","zh":"如果暖化越過某一臨界點，環境破壞可能更難控制。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a critical boundary.","zh":"這個短語指出關鍵界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"serious harm","meaning":"嚴重損害","examples":[{"en":"Further warming could cause serious harm to natural and human systems.","zh":"進一步暖化可能對自然和人類系統造成嚴重損害。"},{"en":"Serious harm means major damage that is difficult to ignore or repair.","zh":"嚴重損害指難以忽視或修復的重大傷害。"},{"en":"A chemical spill can cause serious harm to a river and the families who depend on it.","zh":"化學品洩漏可以對河流和依賴它的家庭造成嚴重損害。"},{"en":"If climate change causes crop failure and floods, the harm affects both nature and people.","zh":"如果氣候變化造成農作物歉收和洪水，損害就同時影響自然和人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes damage that is important and severe.","zh":"這個短語描述重要且嚴重的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"carbon emissions","meaning":"碳排放","examples":[{"en":"Carbon emissions must be reduced substantially.","zh":"碳排放必須大幅減少。"},{"en":"Carbon emissions are carbon-containing gases, especially carbon dioxide, released into the atmosphere.","zh":"碳排放是釋放到大氣中的含碳氣體，尤其是二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Driving less and using public transport can reduce personal carbon emissions.","zh":"少開車並使用公共交通可以減少個人碳排放。"},{"en":"If carbon emissions stay high, global warming becomes harder to limit.","zh":"如果碳排放維持高水平，限制全球暖化會更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase is central in discussions of climate change and energy use.","zh":"這個短語是氣候變化和能源使用討論中的核心概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be reduced by","meaning":"減少……","examples":[{"en":"Global emissions may need to be reduced by 80%.","zh":"全球排放可能需要減少80%。"},{"en":"To be reduced by a number means to decrease by that amount or percentage.","zh":"“Be reduced by” 某數字指按該數量或百分比下降。"},{"en":"A shop’s electricity bill may be reduced by 20% after it installs LED lights.","zh":"商店安裝 LED 燈後，電費可能減少20%。"},{"en":"If emissions are reduced by a large percentage, industries must change how they produce energy.","zh":"如果排放減少很大百分比，工業就必須改變生產能源的方式。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the size of a decrease.","zh":"這個短語給出下降幅度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"over the next 30 years","meaning":"在未來三十年內","examples":[{"en":"Major emissions reductions are required over the next 30 years.","zh":"在未來三十年內需要大幅減排。"},{"en":"Over the next 30 years means during the coming three decades.","zh":"在未來三十年內，指接下來三個十年期間。"},{"en":"A city may plan new railways over the next 30 years to reduce traffic.","zh":"城市可能在未來三十年內規劃新鐵路，以減少交通。"},{"en":"If changes are required over the next 30 years, governments must start planning early.","zh":"如果未來三十年內需要改變，政府就必須及早規劃。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a long future time frame.","zh":"這個短語給出長期未來時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"demand for energy","meaning":"能源需求","examples":[{"en":"Demand for energy is expected to continue rising.","zh":"能源需求預計會繼續上升。"},{"en":"Demand for energy means how much electricity, fuel or power people and businesses need.","zh":"能源需求指人們和企業需要多少電力、燃料或動力。"},{"en":"Demand for energy rises when more homes use air-conditioning in summer.","zh":"夏天更多家庭使用冷氣時，能源需求會上升。"},{"en":"If demand grows while emissions must fall, governments face a difficult energy problem.","zh":"如果需求增加而排放必須下降，政府就面對困難能源問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes society’s need for power.","zh":"這個短語描述社會對能源的需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be expected to rise","meaning":"預計會上升","examples":[{"en":"Global energy demand is expected to rise sharply.","zh":"全球能源需求預計會急劇上升。"},{"en":"To be expected to rise means people predict that something will increase.","zh":"預計會上升，指人們預測某事會增加。"},{"en":"Rent is expected to rise if many new workers move into the same district.","zh":"如果許多新工人搬到同一區，租金預計會上升。"},{"en":"If energy demand is expected to rise, planners must prepare enough supply.","zh":"如果能源需求預計會上升，規劃者就必須準備足夠供應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a predicted increase.","zh":"這個短語描述預測中的增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a proposed means of","meaning":"所提出的……方法","examples":[{"en":"CCS is a proposed means of reducing industrial emissions.","zh":"CCS 是所提出的減少工業排放方法。"},{"en":"A proposed means of doing something is a suggested method for achieving it.","zh":"所提出的做某事方法，是為達成該事而建議的方法。"},{"en":"Online appointments are a proposed means of reducing queues at clinics.","zh":"網上預約是所提出的減少診所排隊方法。"},{"en":"If a method is only proposed, it may still need testing, funding or public approval.","zh":"如果方法只是被提出，它可能仍需要測試、資金或公眾批准。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a suggested solution, not necessarily a proven one.","zh":"這個短語引出建議方案，不一定是已證實方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"achieve emissions reductions","meaning":"實現減排","examples":[{"en":"Governments are considering several ways to achieve emissions reductions.","zh":"政府正在考慮幾種方法來實現減排。"},{"en":"To achieve emissions reductions means to successfully lower the amount of pollution released.","zh":"實現減排指成功降低釋放出的污染量。"},{"en":"A school may achieve emissions reductions by using less electricity and reducing food waste.","zh":"學校可以透過少用電和減少廚餘來實現減排。"},{"en":"If a country changes transport, energy and industry, emissions may fall.","zh":"如果國家改變交通、能源和工業，排放可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on successfully reaching lower pollution levels.","zh":"這個短語強調成功達到較低污染水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"adopt carbon capture and storage","meaning":"採用碳捕集與封存","examples":[{"en":"Some countries may adopt carbon capture and storage at power plants.","zh":"一些國家可能在發電廠採用碳捕集與封存。"},{"en":"To adopt carbon capture and storage means to begin using CCS as part of an energy or climate policy.","zh":"採用碳捕集與封存，指開始把 CCS 作為能源或氣候政策的一部分使用。"},{"en":"A power company may adopt CCS when regulations require lower emissions.","zh":"當規例要求降低排放，電力公司可能採用 CCS。"},{"en":"If governments adopt CCS widely, power plants will need new equipment and storage sites.","zh":"如果政府廣泛採用 CCS，發電廠就需要新設備和儲存地點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes choosing and implementing this technology.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇並實施這項技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"underground carbon storage","meaning":"地下碳封存","examples":[{"en":"Underground carbon storage involves placing carbon dioxide below the surface.","zh":"地下碳封存涉及把二氧化碳放在地表以下。"},{"en":"Underground carbon storage is the practice of storing captured carbon dioxide deep underground.","zh":"地下碳封存是把捕集到的二氧化碳儲存在地底深處的做法。"},{"en":"Engineers may choose underground carbon storage in old oil fields or deep rock formations.","zh":"工程師可能在舊油田或深層岩層中選擇地下碳封存。"},{"en":"If underground storage leaks, captured carbon dioxide could return to the atmosphere.","zh":"如果地下封存洩漏，被捕集的二氧化碳可能回到大氣。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on where captured carbon is kept.","zh":"這個短語強調捕集到的碳被存放在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"CO₂ storage","meaning":"二氧化碳封存","examples":[{"en":"CO₂ storage is already practised in parts of the oil and gas industry.","zh":"二氧化碳封存已在部分石油及天然氣行業中實行。"},{"en":"CO₂ storage means keeping carbon dioxide in a place where it will not easily enter the atmosphere.","zh":"二氧化碳封存指把二氧化碳保存在不容易進入大氣的地方。"},{"en":"A company may use CO₂ storage after separating carbon dioxide from natural gas.","zh":"公司可能在從天然氣中分離二氧化碳後使用二氧化碳封存。"},{"en":"If storage is secure, emissions can be reduced without releasing the gas into the air.","zh":"如果封存安全，就能在不把氣體釋放到空氣中的情況下減排。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to storing carbon dioxide, usually underground.","zh":"這個短語指儲存二氧化碳，通常是在地下。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"carbon sequestration","meaning":"碳封存","examples":[{"en":"Carbon sequestration keeps captured carbon dioxide underground.","zh":"碳封存把捕集到的二氧化碳留在地下。"},{"en":"Carbon sequestration is the long-term storage of carbon dioxide so it does not enter the atmosphere.","zh":"碳封存是長期儲存二氧化碳，使其不進入大氣。"},{"en":"Forests can be a natural form of carbon sequestration because trees store carbon as they grow.","zh":"森林可以是天然碳封存形式，因為樹木生長時儲存碳。"},{"en":"If geological sequestration works safely, power plants may emit less CO₂ into the air.","zh":"如果地質封存能安全運作，發電廠排入空氣的二氧化碳可能較少。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used in climate and energy discussions.","zh":"這個短語常用於氣候和能源討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be practised by","meaning":"由……採用","examples":[{"en":"Carbon sequestration is practised by the oil and gas industry.","zh":"碳封存由石油及天然氣行業採用。"},{"en":"To be practised by a group means to be used or carried out by that group.","zh":"由某群體採用，指被該群體使用或實行。"},{"en":"Recycling is practised by many schools when students separate paper, plastic and metal.","zh":"許多學校在學生分類紙張、塑膠和金屬時採用回收做法。"},{"en":"If a method is practised by an industry, it has moved beyond pure theory in that context.","zh":"如果某方法由某行業採用，它在該語境中就已超越純理論。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who uses a practice.","zh":"這個短語指出誰使用某做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pump something into","meaning":"把某物泵入……","examples":[{"en":"Companies pump carbon dioxide into oil fields.","zh":"公司把二氧化碳泵入油田。"},{"en":"To pump something into a place means to force liquid or gas into it using a pump.","zh":"把某物泵入某處，指使用泵把液體或氣體強行送入該處。"},{"en":"Firefighters may pump water into a burning building to control the flames.","zh":"消防員可能把水泵入燃燒中的建築，以控制火焰。"},{"en":"If CO₂ is pumped into an oil field, it can help push oil out more easily.","zh":"如果二氧化碳被泵入油田，它可以幫助更容易把石油推出來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mechanical movement of a substance into a location.","zh":"這個短語描述以機械方式把物質送入某地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"oil fields","meaning":"油田","examples":[{"en":"Carbon dioxide can be injected into oil fields to improve extraction.","zh":"二氧化碳可以注入油田，以改善開採。"},{"en":"Oil fields are underground areas where oil is found and extracted.","zh":"油田是地下有石油並被開採的區域。"},{"en":"A country with large oil fields may depend heavily on petroleum exports.","zh":"擁有大型油田的國家可能高度依賴石油出口。"},{"en":"If CO₂ is injected into oil fields, companies may recover more oil from the ground.","zh":"如果二氧化碳被注入油田，公司可能從地下回收更多石油。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to places where oil is produced, not petrol stations.","zh":"這個短語指生產石油的地方，而不是加油站。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"maintain pressure","meaning":"維持壓力","examples":[{"en":"Injected carbon dioxide helps maintain pressure in an oil field.","zh":"注入的二氧化碳有助維持油田內的壓力。"},{"en":"To maintain pressure means to keep pressure at a level needed for a process to work.","zh":"維持壓力指把壓力保持在某過程運作所需水平。"},{"en":"A bicycle tyre must maintain pressure so the bike can move smoothly.","zh":"單車胎必須維持壓力，單車才能順暢行駛。"},{"en":"If pressure falls inside an oil field, extracting oil may become harder.","zh":"如果油田內壓力下降，開採石油可能變得更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes keeping force or pressure steady.","zh":"這個短語描述保持力量或壓力穩定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ease extraction","meaning":"使開採更容易","examples":[{"en":"The gas is used to ease the extraction of oil.","zh":"這種氣體用來使石油開採更容易。"},{"en":"To ease extraction means to make it easier to remove a resource from the ground or another source.","zh":"使開採更容易，指令從地下或其他來源取出資源變得較容易。"},{"en":"Warm water can ease the extraction of tea flavour from leaves.","zh":"熱水可以使茶味從茶葉中釋出得更容易。"},{"en":"If CO₂ helps oil flow, it eases extraction and can increase production.","zh":"如果二氧化碳幫助石油流動，它就使開採更容易，並可增加產量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reducing difficulty in taking something out.","zh":"這個短語描述降低取出某物的難度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"displace three barrels of oil","meaning":"置換約三桶石油","examples":[{"en":"One metric ton of carbon dioxide can displace about three barrels of oil.","zh":"一公噸二氧化碳可以置換約三桶石油。"},{"en":"To displace three barrels of oil means to push or replace that amount of oil so it can be extracted.","zh":"置換約三桶石油，指推動或取代該數量的石油，使其可以被開採。"},{"en":"In a simple experiment, water added to a container can displace air inside it.","zh":"在簡單實驗中，向容器加水可以置換其中空氣。"},{"en":"If CO₂ displaces oil underground, more oil may move toward the well.","zh":"如果二氧化碳在地下置換石油，更多石油可能流向油井。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a physical pushing or replacement effect.","zh":"這個短語描述物理上的推動或替換效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be separated from","meaning":"從……分離出來","examples":[{"en":"Carbon dioxide can be separated from natural gas.","zh":"二氧化碳可以從天然氣中分離出來。"},{"en":"To be separated from something means to be removed from a mixture or group.","zh":"從某物分離出來，指從混合物或群體中被移除。"},{"en":"Cream can be separated from milk during food processing.","zh":"食品加工中，忌廉可以從牛奶中分離出來。"},{"en":"If CO₂ is separated from natural gas, the remaining gas can be cleaner for use.","zh":"如果二氧化碳從天然氣中分離出來，剩餘氣體可更清潔地使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes removing one part from another.","zh":"這個短語描述把一部分從另一物中移除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"natural gas","meaning":"天然氣","examples":[{"en":"Natural gas can contain carbon dioxide that must be removed.","zh":"天然氣可以含有必須移除的二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Natural gas is a fossil fuel found underground and used for heating, cooking and electricity.","zh":"天然氣是在地下發現、用於供暖、煮食和發電的化石燃料。"},{"en":"Many homes use natural gas for hot water or kitchen stoves.","zh":"許多家庭使用天然氣供熱水或廚房爐具。"},{"en":"If natural gas contains impurities, companies may process it before selling it.","zh":"如果天然氣含有雜質，公司可能在出售前處理它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a fuel, not air in nature generally.","zh":"這個短語指一種燃料，而不是泛指自然界的空氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"exhausted coal fields","meaning":"枯竭煤田","examples":[{"en":"Carbon dioxide may be pumped into exhausted coal fields.","zh":"二氧化碳可能被泵入枯竭煤田。"},{"en":"Exhausted coal fields are coal-mining areas where most useful coal has already been removed.","zh":"枯竭煤田是大部分可用煤炭已被移除的採煤區。"},{"en":"An old mining town may sit beside exhausted coal fields that no longer produce much coal.","zh":"舊礦業城鎮可能位於已不再大量產煤的枯竭煤田旁。"},{"en":"If coal fields are exhausted, they may be considered for underground storage instead of mining.","zh":"如果煤田枯竭，它們可能被考慮用作地下儲存，而不是採礦。"},{"en":"The phrase describes former coal sites with little remaining extractable coal.","zh":"這個短語描述剩餘可開採煤很少的舊煤炭場地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"deep seams","meaning":"地底深層礦層","examples":[{"en":"Captured gas may be stored in deep underground seams.","zh":"捕集到的氣體可能儲存在地底深層礦層中。"},{"en":"Deep seams are layers of rock, coal or other material located far below the surface.","zh":"地底深層礦層是位於地表以下很深處的岩石、煤或其他物質層。"},{"en":"Miners may need special equipment to reach deep seams safely.","zh":"礦工可能需要特殊設備才能安全到達深層礦層。"},{"en":"If CO₂ is stored in deep seams, the aim is to keep it far from the atmosphere.","zh":"如果二氧化碳儲存在深層礦層中，目的就是使其遠離大氣。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a geological storage location.","zh":"這個短語給出地質儲存位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"remain underground","meaning":"留在地底","examples":[{"en":"Sequestered carbon dioxide is intended to remain underground permanently.","zh":"被封存的二氧化碳旨在永久留在地底。"},{"en":"To remain underground means to stay below the earth’s surface.","zh":"留在地底指停留在地球表面以下。"},{"en":"Water pipes may remain underground so streets stay clear and safe.","zh":"水管可能留在地底，使街道保持清晰和安全。"},{"en":"If stored CO₂ remains underground, it cannot contribute directly to atmospheric warming.","zh":"如果儲存的二氧化碳留在地底，它就不能直接造成大氣暖化。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses continued storage below the surface.","zh":"這個短語強調持續在地表以下儲存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be channelled into","meaning":"被輸送到……","examples":[{"en":"The captured gas can be channelled into underground reservoirs.","zh":"捕集到的氣體可以被輸送到地下儲層。"},{"en":"To be channelled into something means to be directed or guided into a particular place or system.","zh":"被輸送到某處，指被引導或導向特定地方或系統。"},{"en":"Rainwater can be channelled into storage tanks during heavy storms.","zh":"暴雨期間，雨水可以被輸送到儲水箱。"},{"en":"If CO₂ is channelled into reservoirs, pipelines or wells guide it to storage sites.","zh":"如果二氧化碳被輸送到儲層，管道或井會把它引向儲存地點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes controlled movement toward a destination.","zh":"這個短語描述朝目的地受控移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"disused sandstone reservoirs","meaning":"廢棄砂岩儲層","examples":[{"en":"Some proposals involve storing carbon dioxide in disused sandstone reservoirs.","zh":"一些建議涉及把二氧化碳儲存在廢棄砂岩儲層中。"},{"en":"Disused sandstone reservoirs are old rock storage spaces in sandstone that are no longer being used for their original purpose.","zh":"廢棄砂岩儲層是砂岩中不再用於原本用途的舊岩石儲存空間。"},{"en":"Engineers may study disused reservoirs to see whether they can safely hold gas.","zh":"工程師可能研究廢棄儲層，看它們能否安全容納氣體。"},{"en":"If a reservoir is no longer used, it may be considered for carbon storage.","zh":"如果儲層不再使用，它可能被考慮用於碳封存。"},{"en":"The phrase names one possible underground storage site.","zh":"這個短語指出一種可能的地下儲存地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the sale of oil and natural gas","meaning":"石油及天然氣銷售","examples":[{"en":"The sale of oil and natural gas helps cover storage costs.","zh":"石油及天然氣銷售有助支付儲存成本。"},{"en":"The sale of oil and natural gas means earning money by selling these fuels.","zh":"石油及天然氣銷售指透過出售這些燃料賺取收入。"},{"en":"A country may use the sale of natural gas to fund public services.","zh":"一個國家可能使用天然氣銷售收入資助公共服務。"},{"en":"If oil sales generate profit, companies may find it easier to pay for carbon storage.","zh":"如果石油銷售產生利潤，公司可能較容易支付碳封存成本。"},{"en":"The phrase connects fuel revenue with project costs.","zh":"這個短語把燃料收入與項目成本連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be profitable","meaning":"有利可圖","examples":[{"en":"Oil and gas extraction can be highly profitable.","zh":"石油和天然氣開採可以非常有利可圖。"},{"en":"To be profitable means to make more money than it costs.","zh":"有利可圖指賺到的錢多於成本。"},{"en":"A small café is profitable if its income is higher than rent, wages and food costs.","zh":"如果小咖啡店收入高於租金、工資和食材成本，它就是有利可圖。"},{"en":"If an energy project is profitable, companies may accept extra costs more easily.","zh":"如果能源項目有利可圖，公司可能更容易接受額外成本。"},{"en":"The phrase describes financial success.","zh":"這個短語描述財務上的成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sequestration cost","meaning":"碳封存成本","examples":[{"en":"The sequestration cost can be absorbed by profitable energy companies.","zh":"碳封存成本可以由有利可圖的能源公司承擔。"},{"en":"Sequestration cost is the money required to capture, move and store carbon dioxide safely.","zh":"碳封存成本是安全捕集、運輸和儲存二氧化碳所需的金錢。"},{"en":"A power company must calculate sequestration cost before deciding whether CCS is affordable.","zh":"電力公司決定 CCS 是否負擔得起前，必須計算碳封存成本。"},{"en":"If sequestration costs are high, electricity prices may rise.","zh":"如果碳封存成本高昂，電價可能上升。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the financial burden of carbon storage.","zh":"這個短語指碳儲存的財務負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be easily borne","meaning":"容易承擔","examples":[{"en":"The cost is more easily borne when the extracted oil can be sold.","zh":"當開採出的石油可以出售，成本就較容易承擔。"},{"en":"To be easily borne means to be paid, carried or tolerated without too much difficulty.","zh":"容易承擔指支付、承受或忍受某負擔時不太困難。"},{"en":"A school trip fee is more easily borne if families can pay in small instalments.","zh":"如果家庭可以分期付款，學校旅行費就較容易承擔。"},{"en":"If companies earn money from oil sales, they can bear storage costs more easily.","zh":"如果公司從石油銷售賺錢，就能較容易承擔儲存成本。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a burden that becomes manageable.","zh":"這個短語描述變得可處理的負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"injection of CO₂","meaning":"注入二氧化碳","examples":[{"en":"The injection of CO₂ into deep geological formations has been proposed.","zh":"有人提出把二氧化碳注入深層地質構造。"},{"en":"Injection of CO₂ means forcing carbon dioxide into a place, usually underground, through wells or pipes.","zh":"注入二氧化碳指透過井或管道把二氧化碳強行送入某處，通常是地下。"},{"en":"Doctors use injections to put medicine into the body; engineers use wells to inject gases underground.","zh":"醫生用注射把藥物送入身體；工程師用井把氣體注入地下。"},{"en":"If CO₂ is injected into suitable rock, it may remain trapped below the surface.","zh":"如果二氧化碳被注入合適岩石中，它可能被困在地表以下。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the method of putting carbon dioxide into storage.","zh":"這個短語描述把二氧化碳送入儲存地點的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"saline aquifers","meaning":"鹽水含水層","examples":[{"en":"Saline aquifers are underground rock formations containing salty water.","zh":"鹽水含水層是含有鹹水的地下岩層。"},{"en":"Saline aquifers are water-bearing underground layers where the water is too salty for normal use.","zh":"鹽水含水層是含水的地下層，其中水分太鹹，不適合一般使用。"},{"en":"Engineers may study saline aquifers as possible places for CO₂ storage.","zh":"工程師可能研究鹽水含水層作為可能的二氧化碳儲存地點。"},{"en":"If a saline aquifer is deep and sealed, it may trap injected carbon dioxide.","zh":"如果鹽水含水層夠深且被封閉，就可能困住注入的二氧化碳。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a specific geological formation, not a surface lake.","zh":"這個短語指特定地質構造，而不是地表湖泊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"beneath the seabed","meaning":"在海床以下","examples":[{"en":"Some aquifers lie about 1,000 metres beneath the seabed.","zh":"一些含水層位於海床以下約1,000米。"},{"en":"Beneath the seabed means under the floor of the sea.","zh":"在海床以下，指在海底地面之下。"},{"en":"Oil and gas wells may reach rock layers beneath the seabed.","zh":"石油和天然氣井可能到達海床以下的岩層。"},{"en":"If storage sites are beneath the seabed, engineers must consider pressure, leakage and drilling risks.","zh":"如果儲存地點位於海床以下，工程師必須考慮壓力、洩漏和鑽探風險。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an underwater geological location.","zh":"這個短語給出水下地質位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prevent its release into","meaning":"防止其釋放到……","examples":[{"en":"Underground storage is intended to prevent CO₂ from being released into the atmosphere.","zh":"地下儲存旨在防止二氧化碳釋放到大氣中。"},{"en":"To prevent its release into a place means to stop it from escaping or entering that place.","zh":"防止其釋放到某處，指阻止它逃出或進入該地方。"},{"en":"A sealed container can prevent a chemical’s release into the classroom air.","zh":"密封容器可以防止化學物釋放到課室空氣中。"},{"en":"If CO₂ is stored securely, its release into the atmosphere can be avoided.","zh":"如果二氧化碳被安全儲存，就能避免其釋放到大氣。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on stopping escape into an unwanted environment.","zh":"這個短語強調阻止物質逃入不希望出現的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the atmosphere","meaning":"大氣","examples":[{"en":"Carbon dioxide must be kept out of the atmosphere to limit warming.","zh":"二氧化碳必須被阻止進入大氣，以限制暖化。"},{"en":"The atmosphere is the layer of gases surrounding the Earth.","zh":"大氣是包圍地球的一層氣體。"},{"en":"Weather happens in the atmosphere, where clouds, wind and rain form.","zh":"天氣發生在大氣中，雲、風和雨都在其中形成。"},{"en":"If greenhouse gases build up in the atmosphere, they trap more heat.","zh":"如果溫室氣體在大氣中累積，它們會困住更多熱量。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the air system around the planet.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞地球的空氣系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"carbon capture","meaning":"碳捕集","examples":[{"en":"Carbon capture involves separating carbon dioxide from industrial emissions.","zh":"碳捕集涉及把二氧化碳從工業排放中分離出來。"},{"en":"Carbon capture is the process of collecting carbon dioxide before it enters the atmosphere.","zh":"碳捕集是在二氧化碳進入大氣前收集它的過程。"},{"en":"A factory may use carbon capture equipment on its chimney to reduce emissions.","zh":"工廠可能在煙囪上使用碳捕集設備來減少排放。"},{"en":"If carbon is captured but not stored safely, the climate benefit may be lost.","zh":"如果碳被捕集但沒有安全儲存，氣候效益可能會消失。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the first part of CCS: catching the carbon dioxide.","zh":"這個短語指 CCS 的第一部分：捕捉二氧化碳。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be accomplished","meaning":"已成功做到","examples":[{"en":"Underground storage has already been accomplished in some industries.","zh":"地下儲存在一些行業中已成功做到。"},{"en":"To be accomplished means to be successfully done or achieved.","zh":"已成功做到指已成功完成或達成。"},{"en":"A school project is accomplished when the research, model and presentation are all finished.","zh":"當研究、模型和匯報都完成，學校項目就已成功做到。"},{"en":"If storage has been accomplished before, supporters can argue that the method is possible.","zh":"如果儲存過去已成功做到，支持者就能主張方法可行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes successful completion.","zh":"這個短語描述成功完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"remain largely hypothetical","meaning":"大致仍停留在理論階段","examples":[{"en":"Capturing carbon from power plants remains largely hypothetical.","zh":"從發電廠捕集碳大致仍停留在理論階段。"},{"en":"To remain largely hypothetical means to still exist mostly as an idea rather than as proven practice.","zh":"大致仍停留在理論階段，指主要仍是想法，而不是已證實的實踐。"},{"en":"A school plan for a rooftop farm remains hypothetical until money and permission are secured.","zh":"在取得資金和批准前，學校天台農場計劃仍停留在理論階段。"},{"en":"If a technology has not been tested widely, its success is still uncertain.","zh":"如果技術尚未被廣泛測試，其成功仍不確定。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that something has not yet been fully demonstrated.","zh":"這個短語提醒某事尚未被充分證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"throughout Western Europe and North America","meaning":"遍及西歐及北美洲","examples":[{"en":"Several CCS plants are planned throughout Western Europe and North America.","zh":"多個 CCS 設施計劃遍及西歐及北美洲。"},{"en":"Throughout Western Europe and North America means across many places in those two regions.","zh":"遍及西歐及北美洲，指跨越這兩個地區中的許多地方。"},{"en":"A new teaching method may spread throughout schools in Western Europe and North America.","zh":"一種新教學方法可能在西歐及北美洲的學校中傳播。"},{"en":"If projects are planned throughout a region, interest is not limited to one country.","zh":"如果項目遍及某地區而規劃，興趣就不局限於一國。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a broad geographical range.","zh":"這個短語給出廣闊地理範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be on the drawing board","meaning":"仍在規劃階段","examples":[{"en":"Many proposed CCS projects are still on the drawing board.","zh":"許多擬議 CCS 項目仍在規劃階段。"},{"en":"To be on the drawing board means to still be in the planning or design stage.","zh":"仍在規劃階段，指仍處於計劃或設計階段。"},{"en":"A new school library may be on the drawing board before builders are hired.","zh":"新學校圖書館在聘請建築工人前可能仍在規劃階段。"},{"en":"If a project is still on the drawing board, it has not yet been built or tested in real life.","zh":"如果項目仍在規劃階段，它就尚未建成或在現實中測試。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a plan exists but is not yet reality.","zh":"這個短語顯示計劃存在，但尚未成為現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"three main forms of","meaning":"三種主要形式","examples":[{"en":"There are three main forms of carbon capture.","zh":"碳捕集有三種主要形式。"},{"en":"Three main forms of something are the three most important types or versions of it.","zh":"三種主要形式指某事物最重要的三種類型或版本。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain three main forms of writing: narrative, argumentative and descriptive.","zh":"老師可能解釋三種主要寫作形式：敘事、議論和描寫。"},{"en":"If a technology has several forms, comparing them helps people understand costs and benefits.","zh":"如果一種技術有幾種形式，比較它們有助人理解成本和好處。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a classification.","zh":"這個短語引出分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pre-combustion capture","meaning":"燃燒前碳捕集","examples":[{"en":"Pre-combustion capture removes carbon before the fuel is fully burnt.","zh":"燃燒前碳捕集在燃料完全燃燒前移除碳。"},{"en":"Pre-combustion capture is a method of capturing carbon before the main burning process produces electricity.","zh":"燃燒前碳捕集是在主要燃燒過程發電前捕集碳的方法。"},{"en":"In a factory system, engineers may remove unwanted gases before fuel reaches the final burner.","zh":"在工廠系統中，工程師可能在燃料到達最終燃燒器前移除不需要的氣體。"},{"en":"If carbon is removed earlier, later emissions may be lower.","zh":"如果碳較早被移除，之後排放可能較低。"},{"en":"The phrase means “capture before combustion,” not after smoke leaves the chimney.","zh":"這個短語意思是「燃燒前捕集」，不是煙離開煙囪後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"post-combustion capture","meaning":"燃燒後碳捕集","examples":[{"en":"Post-combustion capture separates carbon dioxide after combustion.","zh":"燃燒後碳捕集在燃燒後分離二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Post-combustion capture is a method that removes CO₂ from exhaust gases after fuel has been burnt.","zh":"燃燒後碳捕集是在燃料燃燒後，從廢氣中移除二氧化碳的方法。"},{"en":"An older power plant may add post-combustion equipment to clean gases leaving the boiler.","zh":"舊發電廠可能加裝燃燒後設備，以清潔離開鍋爐的氣體。"},{"en":"If the system is added after burning, existing plants may be adapted more easily.","zh":"如果系統是在燃燒後加入，現有發電廠可能較容易改裝。"},{"en":"The phrase means “capture after combustion.”","zh":"這個短語意思是「燃燒後捕集」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"oxy-firing","meaning":"富氧燃燒","examples":[{"en":"Oxy-firing burns coal in pure oxygen.","zh":"富氧燃燒在純氧中燃燒煤。"},{"en":"Oxy-firing is a combustion method that uses oxygen instead of ordinary air to burn fuel.","zh":"富氧燃燒是一種使用氧氣而不是普通空氣燃燒燃料的燃燒方法。"},{"en":"A special industrial furnace may use oxy-firing to control the gases produced during burning.","zh":"特殊工業爐可能使用富氧燃燒，以控制燃燒時產生的氣體。"},{"en":"If coal is burnt in pure oxygen, the resulting gas mixture can make CO₂ easier to capture.","zh":"如果煤在純氧中燃燒，所得氣體混合物可以令二氧化碳更容易捕集。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a specialised burning process.","zh":"這個短語指一種專門燃燒過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Congressional Budget Office","meaning":"美國國會預算辦公室","examples":[{"en":"The Congressional Budget Office assessed several carbon-capture methods.","zh":"美國國會預算辦公室評估了幾種碳捕集方法。"},{"en":"The Congressional Budget Office is a US government agency that analyses costs and economic effects for Congress.","zh":"美國國會預算辦公室是為美國國會分析成本和經濟影響的政府機構。"},{"en":"Lawmakers may use Congressional Budget Office reports before voting on expensive energy programmes.","zh":"立法者可能在表決昂貴能源計劃前使用國會預算辦公室報告。"},{"en":"If the office assesses a technology, its cost estimates can influence policy debate.","zh":"如果該辦公室評估某技術，其成本估算可影響政策辯論。"},{"en":"The phrase names an official US budget-analysis body.","zh":"這個短語指美國官方預算分析機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be viewed most favourably","meaning":"最受看好","examples":[{"en":"Post-combustion capture was viewed most favourably for existing plants.","zh":"對現有發電廠而言，燃燒後碳捕集最受看好。"},{"en":"To be viewed most favourably means to be considered the best or most attractive option.","zh":"最受看好指被認為是最佳或最有吸引力的選項。"},{"en":"Among several school trips, the museum visit may be viewed most favourably because it is cheap and educational.","zh":"在幾個學校旅行方案中，博物館參觀可能因便宜又有教育性而最受看好。"},{"en":"If a method can be used at existing plants, policymakers may prefer it.","zh":"如果一種方法可用於現有發電廠，政策制定者可能較喜歡它。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses positive evaluation compared with alternatives.","zh":"這個短語表達與其他選項比較下的正面評價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"existing power plants","meaning":"現有發電廠","examples":[{"en":"Existing power plants may be adapted to use post-combustion capture.","zh":"現有發電廠可能被改裝以使用燃燒後碳捕集。"},{"en":"Existing power plants are power stations that have already been built and are operating or available.","zh":"現有發電廠是已經建成並正在運作或可用的發電站。"},{"en":"A government may upgrade existing power plants instead of building new ones.","zh":"政府可能升級現有發電廠，而不是興建新發電廠。"},{"en":"If existing plants can be adapted, the transition may be faster than starting from zero.","zh":"如果現有發電廠可以改裝，轉型可能比從零開始更快。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts current infrastructure with entirely new construction.","zh":"這個短語把當前基建與全新建設作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be retrofitted with","meaning":"加裝……設備","examples":[{"en":"Older power plants can be retrofitted with carbon-capture equipment.","zh":"舊發電廠可以加裝碳捕集設備。"},{"en":"To be retrofitted with something means to have new equipment added to an older system.","zh":"加裝某設備，指把新設備加入舊系統。"},{"en":"An old school building may be retrofitted with lifts for wheelchair access.","zh":"舊校舍可能加裝升降機，以方便輪椅使用者進出。"},{"en":"If a plant is retrofitted with capture equipment, it can reduce emissions without being completely rebuilt.","zh":"如果發電廠加裝捕集設備，就能減排而不必完全重建。"},{"en":"The phrase describes upgrading old infrastructure.","zh":"這個短語描述升級舊基建。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"whereas","meaning":"然而；而","examples":[{"en":"Existing plants can be retrofitted, whereas other systems require new construction.","zh":"現有發電廠可以改裝，而其他系統需要新建。"},{"en":"Whereas is used to contrast two facts or situations.","zh":"“Whereas” 用來對比兩個事實或情況。"},{"en":"Some students learn best by listening, whereas others need diagrams and practice.","zh":"有些學生最能透過聆聽學習，而另一些需要圖表和練習。"},{"en":"If one technology can use old plants whereas another needs new ones, their costs may differ greatly.","zh":"如果一種技術可使用舊發電廠，而另一種需要新建，成本可能差別很大。"},{"en":"The word introduces a clear contrast.","zh":"這個詞引出清楚對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the construction of entirely new plants","meaning":"興建全新發電廠","examples":[{"en":"Some forms of CCS require the construction of entirely new plants.","zh":"某些 CCS 形式需要興建全新發電廠。"},{"en":"The construction of entirely new plants means building completely new power stations or industrial facilities.","zh":"興建全新發電廠指建造完全新的發電站或工業設施。"},{"en":"A city may avoid constructing an entirely new hospital if an old one can be upgraded.","zh":"如果舊醫院可以升級，城市可能避免興建全新醫院。"},{"en":"If CCS needs new plants, the cost and planning time increase sharply.","zh":"如果 CCS 需要新發電廠，成本和規劃時間會大幅增加。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts new building with modifying existing sites.","zh":"這個短語把新建與改裝現有場地作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"remove more CO₂","meaning":"移除更多二氧化碳","examples":[{"en":"Pre-combustion and oxy-firing can remove more CO₂.","zh":"燃燒前捕集和富氧燃燒可以移除更多二氧化碳。"},{"en":"To remove more CO₂ means to capture or eliminate a larger amount of carbon dioxide.","zh":"移除更多二氧化碳指捕集或消除較大量二氧化碳。"},{"en":"A better filter can remove more dust from classroom air.","zh":"更好的過濾器可以從課室空氣中移除更多塵埃。"},{"en":"If a system removes more CO₂, it may produce cleaner electricity but cost more.","zh":"如果系統移除更多二氧化碳，它可能產生較清潔電力，但成本更高。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the effectiveness of different technologies.","zh":"這個短語比較不同技術的效能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"generate more electricity","meaning":"產生更多電力","examples":[{"en":"Some newer systems can also generate more electricity.","zh":"一些較新的系統也可以產生更多電力。"},{"en":"To generate more electricity means to produce a larger amount of electrical power.","zh":"產生更多電力指生產較大量電能。"},{"en":"A school’s solar panels generate more electricity on sunny days than on rainy days.","zh":"學校太陽能板在晴天比雨天產生更多電力。"},{"en":"If a power plant generates more electricity from the same fuel, efficiency improves.","zh":"如果發電廠用同樣燃料產生更多電力，效率就提高。"},{"en":"The phrase describes increased power production.","zh":"這個短語描述電力生產增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be separated from gas","meaning":"從氣體中分離","examples":[{"en":"In post-combustion capture, CO₂ is separated from exhaust gas.","zh":"在燃燒後捕集中，二氧化碳從廢氣中分離。"},{"en":"To be separated from gas means to be removed from a mixture of gases.","zh":"從氣體中分離，指從氣體混合物中移除。"},{"en":"A kitchen extractor separates grease and smoke from air before releasing it outside.","zh":"廚房抽氣設備在把空氣排出室外前，會從空氣中分離油脂和煙。"},{"en":"If CO₂ is separated from exhaust gas, it can then be compressed and stored.","zh":"如果二氧化碳從廢氣中分離出來，之後就能被壓縮和儲存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a filtering or chemical separation process.","zh":"這個短語描述過濾或化學分離過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"after coal is burnt","meaning":"煤燃燒後","examples":[{"en":"Post-combustion capture occurs after coal is burnt.","zh":"燃燒後碳捕集發生在煤燃燒後。"},{"en":"After coal is burnt means after coal has been used as fuel and turned into heat, ash and gases.","zh":"煤燃燒後，指煤作為燃料使用並變成熱、灰和氣體之後。"},{"en":"After wood is burnt, smoke and ash remain.","zh":"木材燃燒後，會留下煙和灰。"},{"en":"If capture happens after coal is burnt, the system treats exhaust gases rather than the original coal.","zh":"如果捕集在煤燃燒後發生，系統處理的是廢氣，而不是原本的煤。"},{"en":"The phrase fixes the timing of the capture process.","zh":"這個短語確定捕集過程的時間點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"before electricity is generated","meaning":"在發電之前","examples":[{"en":"The carbon dioxide is removed before the final generation of electricity.","zh":"二氧化碳在最終發電之前被移除。"},{"en":"Before electricity is generated means before electrical power is actually produced.","zh":"在發電之前，指在電力真正產生之前。"},{"en":"In some systems, fuel is cleaned before electricity is generated to reduce pollution later.","zh":"在一些系統中，燃料會在發電之前被清潔，以減少之後污染。"},{"en":"If CO₂ is removed earlier, the final emissions can be lower.","zh":"如果二氧化碳較早被移除，最終排放可以較低。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a step that happens before power production is complete.","zh":"這個短語描述電力生產完成前發生的步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be combusted in pure oxygen","meaning":"在純氧中燃燒","examples":[{"en":"In oxy-firing, coal is combusted in pure oxygen.","zh":"在富氧燃燒中，煤在純氧中燃燒。"},{"en":"To be combusted in pure oxygen means to be burnt using oxygen rather than normal air.","zh":"在純氧中燃燒，指使用氧氣而不是普通空氣燃燒。"},{"en":"A laboratory flame may burn differently when fuel is combusted in pure oxygen.","zh":"當燃料在純氧中燃燒，實驗室火焰可能有不同表現。"},{"en":"If coal burns in pure oxygen, the resulting gases may be easier to process for CO₂ capture.","zh":"如果煤在純氧中燃燒，所得氣體可能較容易處理以捕集二氧化碳。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a specialised controlled-burning method.","zh":"這個短語描述一種專門的受控燃燒方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Integrated Gasification Combined Cycle system","meaning":"整體煤氣化聯合循環系統","examples":[{"en":"An Integrated Gasification Combined Cycle system produces electricity from synthetic gas.","zh":"整體煤氣化聯合循環系統從合成氣中發電。"},{"en":"An Integrated Gasification Combined Cycle system is a power system that turns coal into gas and uses that gas to generate electricity efficiently.","zh":"整體煤氣化聯合循環系統是一種把煤轉化為氣體，並利用該氣體有效發電的電力系統。"},{"en":"Engineers may choose an IGCC system when they want cleaner coal-based power.","zh":"當工程師想要較清潔的煤基電力時，可能選擇 IGCC 系統。"},{"en":"Because it uses both gas and steam turbines, the system can recover more energy from fuel.","zh":"因為它同時使用燃氣和蒸汽渦輪機，系統可以從燃料中回收更多能源。"},{"en":"The phrase is often shortened to IGCC.","zh":"這個短語常縮寫為 IGCC。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"burn together","meaning":"一起燃燒；一起處理","examples":[{"en":"Oxygen, coal and water are processed together to produce synthetic gas.","zh":"氧氣、煤和水一起處理以產生合成氣。"},{"en":"To burn together means to be used or reacted in the same energy process at the same time.","zh":"一起燃燒指在同一能源過程中同時被使用或反應。"},{"en":"In a campfire, dry wood and paper may burn together quickly.","zh":"在營火中，乾木和紙可能很快一起燃燒。"},{"en":"If materials are processed together in a power system, their reaction can create a useful fuel gas.","zh":"如果材料在發電系統中一起處理，其反應可以產生有用燃氣。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a combined process rather than separate steps.","zh":"這個短語強調組合過程，而不是分開步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"synthetic gas","meaning":"合成氣","examples":[{"en":"The process produces a synthetic gas known as syngas.","zh":"這個過程產生一種稱為 syngas 的合成氣。"},{"en":"Synthetic gas is a manufactured fuel gas produced from materials such as coal, water and oxygen.","zh":"合成氣是由煤、水和氧氣等材料製造出來的燃料氣體。"},{"en":"A power plant may burn synthetic gas to drive turbines.","zh":"發電廠可能燃燒合成氣來推動渦輪機。"},{"en":"If coal is converted into synthetic gas, carbon may be easier to remove before electricity is produced.","zh":"如果煤被轉化為合成氣，在發電前可能較容易移除碳。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to gas made industrially, not naturally occurring gas.","zh":"這個短語指工業製造的氣體，而不是天然存在的氣體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"syngas","meaning":"合成氣","examples":[{"en":"Syngas consists mainly of hydrogen.","zh":"合成氣主要由氫氣組成。"},{"en":"Syngas is a shortened name for synthetic gas, a fuel gas made through industrial processing.","zh":"Syngas 是 synthetic gas 的縮寫，指透過工業加工製成的燃料氣體。"},{"en":"Engineers may use syngas to power turbines in an advanced coal plant.","zh":"工程師可能在先進燃煤發電廠中使用合成氣推動渦輪機。"},{"en":"If syngas is mostly hydrogen, it can burn differently from ordinary coal.","zh":"如果合成氣主要是氫氣，它的燃燒方式可以不同於普通煤。"},{"en":"The word refers to a man-made gas used in energy systems.","zh":"這個詞指能源系統中使用的人造氣體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"mainly hydrogen","meaning":"主要是氫氣","examples":[{"en":"The synthetic gas is mainly hydrogen.","zh":"這種合成氣主要是氫氣。"},{"en":"Mainly hydrogen means hydrogen forms the largest or most important part of the gas.","zh":"主要是氫氣，指氫氣構成該氣體最大或最重要的部分。"},{"en":"A balloon gas mixture may be mainly helium if helium is the dominant gas inside it.","zh":"如果氦氣是氣球內主要氣體，氣球氣體混合物就主要是氦氣。"},{"en":"If a fuel gas is mainly hydrogen, its emissions profile may differ from coal’s.","zh":"如果燃料氣主要是氫氣，其排放特徵可能不同於煤。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main component of a mixture.","zh":"這個短語指出混合物的主要成分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"drive two sets of turbines","meaning":"推動兩組渦輪機","examples":[{"en":"The syngas drives two sets of turbines.","zh":"合成氣推動兩組渦輪機。"},{"en":"To drive two sets of turbines means to power two groups of rotating machines that generate electricity.","zh":"推動兩組渦輪機，指為兩組旋轉發電機械提供動力。"},{"en":"In a power station, moving steam can drive turbines and produce electricity.","zh":"在發電站中，流動蒸汽可以推動渦輪機並產生電力。"},{"en":"If one fuel stream drives two turbine systems, the plant may use energy more efficiently.","zh":"如果一股燃料流推動兩套渦輪系統，電廠可能更有效使用能源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how fuel energy is converted into mechanical power.","zh":"這個短語描述燃料能量如何轉化為機械動力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"gas-driven turbines","meaning":"燃氣渦輪機","examples":[{"en":"Syngas first powers gas-driven turbines.","zh":"合成氣首先推動燃氣渦輪機。"},{"en":"Gas-driven turbines are turbines powered by hot gas rather than steam or water.","zh":"燃氣渦輪機是由熱氣體而不是蒸汽或水推動的渦輪機。"},{"en":"A power plant may use gas-driven turbines when burning natural gas or syngas.","zh":"發電廠燃燒天然氣或合成氣時，可能使用燃氣渦輪機。"},{"en":"If gas expands through a turbine, it spins blades that help generate electricity.","zh":"如果氣體通過渦輪機膨脹，就會轉動葉片並幫助發電。"},{"en":"The phrase names one stage of a gas-based power system.","zh":"這個短語指出燃氣發電系統的一個階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"steam-driven turbines","meaning":"蒸汽渦輪機","examples":[{"en":"The process also powers steam-driven turbines.","zh":"這個過程也推動蒸汽渦輪機。"},{"en":"Steam-driven turbines are turbines turned by high-pressure steam.","zh":"蒸汽渦輪機是由高壓蒸汽轉動的渦輪機。"},{"en":"Many traditional power plants use steam-driven turbines after heating water in boilers.","zh":"許多傳統發電廠在鍋爐加熱水後使用蒸汽渦輪機。"},{"en":"If waste heat produces steam, the plant can generate extra electricity from the same fuel.","zh":"如果廢熱產生蒸汽，電廠就能用同一燃料產生額外電力。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies turbines powered by steam energy.","zh":"這個短語指出由蒸汽能量推動的渦輪機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be powered by steam","meaning":"由蒸汽推動","examples":[{"en":"The second set of turbines is powered by steam.","zh":"第二組渦輪機由蒸汽推動。"},{"en":"To be powered by steam means to receive energy from hot pressurised water vapour.","zh":"由蒸汽推動，指從高溫高壓水蒸氣取得能量。"},{"en":"Old locomotives were powered by steam produced in a boiler.","zh":"舊式火車頭由鍋爐產生的蒸汽推動。"},{"en":"If a turbine is powered by steam, heat energy is turned into motion and then electricity.","zh":"如果渦輪機由蒸汽推動，熱能就轉化為運動，再轉化為電力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the energy source of a machine.","zh":"這個短語描述機器的能源來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as the syngas cools","meaning":"當合成氣冷卻時","examples":[{"en":"Steam is produced as the syngas cools through water.","zh":"當合成氣經水冷卻時，蒸汽便產生。"},{"en":"As the syngas cools means while the hot synthetic gas loses heat.","zh":"當合成氣冷卻時，指熱合成氣正在失去熱量時。"},{"en":"Steam may form as hot metal cools near water in an industrial workshop.","zh":"在工業車間中，熱金屬靠近水冷卻時可能形成蒸汽。"},{"en":"If hot syngas is cooled through water, its heat can be used to produce steam.","zh":"如果熱合成氣經水冷卻，其熱量可以用來產生蒸汽。"},{"en":"The phrase explains timing and cause in the cooling process.","zh":"這個短語解釋冷卻過程中的時間和原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"emissions from the process","meaning":"該過程產生的排放","examples":[{"en":"Emissions from the IGCC process contain much less carbon dioxide.","zh":"IGCC 過程產生的排放含有少得多的二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Emissions from the process are gases or pollutants released as a result of that process.","zh":"該過程產生的排放，是由該過程釋放出的氣體或污染物。"},{"en":"Emissions from cooking can include smoke, steam and smells in a busy kitchen.","zh":"繁忙廚房中，烹調過程產生的排放可以包括煙、蒸汽和氣味。"},{"en":"If emissions from a power process contain less CO₂, the system may be cleaner.","zh":"如果發電過程產生的排放含較少二氧化碳，系統可能較清潔。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies pollution produced by a specific method.","zh":"這個短語指出由特定方法產生的污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"contain around ten percent of","meaning":"含有約……的一成","examples":[{"en":"The emissions contain around ten percent of the CO₂ produced by ordinary coal burning.","zh":"這些排放含有普通燃煤所產生二氧化碳約一成。"},{"en":"To contain around ten percent of something means to include about one tenth of that amount.","zh":"含有約某物的一成，指包含該數量的大約十分之一。"},{"en":"A fruit drink may contain around ten percent of real juice and the rest may be water and sugar.","zh":"水果飲品可能含有約一成真果汁，其餘可能是水和糖。"},{"en":"If emissions contain only ten percent as much CO₂, they are much lower than the comparison case.","zh":"如果排放只含有約一成二氧化碳，就比比較情況低得多。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate proportion.","zh":"這個短語給出約略比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the pros and cons of","meaning":"……的利弊","examples":[{"en":"Governments must consider the pros and cons of CCS.","zh":"政府必須考慮 CCS 的利弊。"},{"en":"The pros and cons of something are its advantages and disadvantages.","zh":"某事的利弊，是它的優點和缺點。"},{"en":"A family may discuss the pros and cons of moving closer to school.","zh":"家庭可能討論搬近學校的利弊。"},{"en":"If a technology reduces emissions but costs too much, both sides must be weighed.","zh":"如果一項技術能減排但成本太高，兩方面都必須權衡。"},{"en":"The phrase is used for balanced evaluation.","zh":"這個短語用於平衡評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be keen to scale up","meaning":"積極擴大……規模","examples":[{"en":"Several countries are keen to scale up carbon-capture projects.","zh":"幾個國家積極擴大碳捕集項目的規模。"},{"en":"To be keen to scale up something means to be eager to expand it to a larger size.","zh":"積極擴大某事規模，指熱切希望把它擴展到更大規模。"},{"en":"A school may be keen to scale up a successful reading programme to all classes.","zh":"學校可能積極把成功的閱讀計劃擴大至所有班級。"},{"en":"If a pilot project works well, governments may want to use it more widely.","zh":"如果試驗項目運作良好，政府可能想更廣泛使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase combines enthusiasm with expansion.","zh":"這個短語結合熱切態度和擴展行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"scale up CCS","meaning":"擴大碳捕集與封存規模","examples":[{"en":"Supporters want to scale up CCS rapidly.","zh":"支持者希望迅速擴大碳捕集與封存規模。"},{"en":"To scale up CCS means to expand carbon capture and storage from small projects to much larger use.","zh":"擴大 CCS 規模，指把碳捕集與封存由小型項目擴展至更大規模使用。"},{"en":"A company may scale up a recycling scheme after a small trial succeeds.","zh":"小型試驗成功後，公司可能擴大回收計劃規模。"},{"en":"If CCS is scaled up too quickly, costs, safety and storage capacity may become serious issues.","zh":"如果 CCS 擴展太快，成本、安全和儲存容量可能成為嚴重問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving from limited use to wider deployment.","zh":"這個短語描述由有限使用轉向更廣泛部署。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reduce carbon emissions quickly","meaning":"迅速減少碳排放","examples":[{"en":"CCS may reduce carbon emissions quickly.","zh":"CCS 可能迅速減少碳排放。"},{"en":"To reduce carbon emissions quickly means to lower CO₂ pollution within a short time.","zh":"迅速減少碳排放，指在短時間內降低二氧化碳污染。"},{"en":"A city can reduce emissions quickly by replacing old buses with electric buses.","zh":"城市可以透過以電動巴士取代舊巴士，迅速減少排放。"},{"en":"If rapid cuts are needed, technologies that work with existing power plants may seem attractive.","zh":"如果需要快速削減排放，能配合現有發電廠的技術可能顯得吸引。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses speed as well as environmental effect.","zh":"這個短語同時強調速度和環境效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"powerful lobby groups","meaning":"強大的游說團體","examples":[{"en":"Powerful lobby groups support large-scale carbon projects.","zh":"強大的游說團體支持大型碳項目。"},{"en":"Powerful lobby groups are organised groups that try to influence government decisions and have strong resources or connections.","zh":"強大的游說團體是試圖影響政府決定、並擁有強大資源或人脈的組織。"},{"en":"A transport lobby group may pressure officials to build more roads.","zh":"交通游說團體可能向官員施壓，要求興建更多道路。"},{"en":"If powerful lobby groups support CCS, politicians may pay more attention to it.","zh":"如果強大游說團體支持 CCS，政治人物可能更重視它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes political influence outside direct government.","zh":"這個短語描述政府外部的政治影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"professionals in mining and engineering","meaning":"採礦及工程專業人士","examples":[{"en":"Many professionals in mining and engineering support CCS.","zh":"許多採礦及工程專業人士支持 CCS。"},{"en":"Professionals in mining and engineering are trained workers and experts in extracting resources and designing technical systems.","zh":"採礦及工程專業人士是受過訓練、從事資源開採和技術系統設計的工人與專家。"},{"en":"A mining engineer may understand underground rock conditions better than the general public.","zh":"採礦工程師可能比一般公眾更了解地下岩石條件。"},{"en":"If these professionals support CCS, they may see technical or employment benefits.","zh":"如果這些專業人士支持 CCS，他們可能看見技術或就業好處。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to specialised workers in heavy industry and technical fields.","zh":"這個短語指重工業和技術領域中的專門工作者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"foundries and refineries","meaning":"鑄造廠及煉製廠","examples":[{"en":"Foundries and refineries may benefit from carbon-capture technology.","zh":"鑄造廠及煉製廠可能從碳捕集技術中受益。"},{"en":"Foundries and refineries are industrial sites that cast metal and process raw materials such as oil.","zh":"鑄造廠及煉製廠是鑄造金屬和加工石油等原材料的工業場所。"},{"en":"A refinery turns crude oil into fuels, while a foundry produces metal parts.","zh":"煉製廠把原油變成燃料，而鑄造廠生產金屬部件。"},{"en":"If these sites emit large amounts of carbon, carbon capture may help them meet cleaner rules.","zh":"如果這些場所排放大量碳，碳捕集可能幫助它們符合較清潔規則。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to heavy industrial facilities.","zh":"這個短語指重工業設施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"emit carbon","meaning":"排放碳","examples":[{"en":"Steel plants and refineries emit large amounts of carbon.","zh":"鋼鐵廠和煉製廠排放大量碳。"},{"en":"To emit carbon means to release carbon-containing gases, especially carbon dioxide, into the air.","zh":"排放碳指把含碳氣體，尤其是二氧化碳，釋放到空氣中。"},{"en":"Cars emit carbon when they burn petrol.","zh":"汽車燃燒汽油時會排放碳。"},{"en":"If factories emit carbon continuously, they contribute to climate change.","zh":"如果工廠持續排放碳，它們就會加劇氣候變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pollution released by human activity.","zh":"這個短語描述人類活動釋放的污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"may also benefit","meaning":"亦可能受益","examples":[{"en":"Heavy industries may also benefit from CCS investment.","zh":"重工業亦可能從 CCS 投資中受益。"},{"en":"May also benefit means might receive an advantage in addition to other groups or sectors.","zh":"亦可能受益，指除了其他群體或行業外，也可能得到好處。"},{"en":"If a school improves its library, parents may also benefit because children read more at home.","zh":"如果學校改善圖書館，家長亦可能受益，因為孩子在家閱讀更多。"},{"en":"If CCS funding creates new technology, related industries may gain contracts and jobs.","zh":"如果 CCS 資助創造新技術，相關行業可能獲得合約和職位。"},{"en":"The phrase adds another possible winner or advantage.","zh":"這個短語加入另一個可能得益者或好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"consume their products","meaning":"消耗其產品","examples":[{"en":"Power-plant equipment consumes products supplied by the oil and gas industry.","zh":"發電廠設備消耗石油和天然氣行業供應的產品。"},{"en":"To consume their products means to use goods or materials that those companies produce.","zh":"消耗其產品指使用那些公司生產的貨品或材料。"},{"en":"A restaurant consumes farmers’ products when it buys vegetables and meat for meals.","zh":"餐廳購買蔬菜和肉類做餐點時，就是消耗農民的產品。"},{"en":"If CCS equipment uses products from energy companies, those companies may profit from the technology.","zh":"如果 CCS 設備使用能源公司的產品，那些公司可能從技術中獲利。"},{"en":"The phrase links one industry’s demand with another industry’s supply.","zh":"這個短語把一個行業的需求與另一行業的供應連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"clean energy acts","meaning":"清潔能源法例","examples":[{"en":"Recent clean energy acts encourage lower-emission power generation.","zh":"近期清潔能源法例鼓勵較低排放的發電。"},{"en":"Clean energy acts are laws designed to promote cleaner energy and reduce pollution.","zh":"清潔能源法例是旨在推動較清潔能源並減少污染的法律。"},{"en":"A clean energy act may require electricity companies to use more wind or solar power.","zh":"清潔能源法例可能要求電力公司使用更多風能或太陽能。"},{"en":"If such laws reward low-emission systems, companies may invest in cleaner technology.","zh":"如果這些法律獎勵低排放系統，公司可能投資較清潔技術。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to energy legislation, not individual habits.","zh":"這個短語指能源法律，而不是個人習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mandate that","meaning":"規定……","examples":[{"en":"Some laws mandate that part of the electricity supply come from cleaner sources.","zh":"一些法律規定部分電力供應必須來自較清潔來源。"},{"en":"To mandate that something happen means to require it by law or official rule.","zh":"規定某事發生，指透過法律或官方規則要求它。"},{"en":"A school may mandate that students wear safety goggles in chemistry labs.","zh":"學校可能規定學生在化學實驗室佩戴護目鏡。"},{"en":"If a law mandates cleaner electricity, power companies must follow it.","zh":"如果法律規定使用較清潔電力，電力公司就必須遵守。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a compulsory requirement.","zh":"這個短語描述強制性要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a percentage of electricity","meaning":"一定比例的電力","examples":[{"en":"A percentage of electricity must be generated by cleaner systems.","zh":"一定比例的電力必須由較清潔系統產生。"},{"en":"A percentage of electricity means a certain share of the total electricity supply.","zh":"一定比例的電力指總電力供應中的某個份額。"},{"en":"A city may require 30% of electricity to come from renewable sources.","zh":"城市可能要求30%電力來自可再生來源。"},{"en":"If a fixed percentage must be clean, companies need to adjust their energy mix.","zh":"如果固定比例必須清潔，公司就需要調整能源組合。"},{"en":"The phrase describes part of the total power supply.","zh":"這個短語描述總電力供應的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be generated by renewables","meaning":"由可再生能源產生","examples":[{"en":"Some legislation requires electricity to be generated by renewables.","zh":"一些法例要求電力由可再生能源產生。"},{"en":"To be generated by renewables means to be produced from renewable energy sources such as wind, solar or water.","zh":"由可再生能源產生，指由風能、太陽能或水力等可再生能源來源生產。"},{"en":"A school’s lights may be generated by renewables if solar panels supply enough power.","zh":"如果太陽能板供應足夠電力，學校燈光可能由可再生能源產生。"},{"en":"If electricity is generated by renewables, emissions can be much lower than with coal.","zh":"如果電力由可再生能源產生，排放可以比用煤低得多。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the clean energy source of electricity.","zh":"這個短語指出電力的清潔能源來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"energy-efficient systems","meaning":"節能系統","examples":[{"en":"CCS is sometimes classified as a more energy-efficient system.","zh":"CCS 有時被歸類為較節能系統。"},{"en":"Energy-efficient systems use less energy to achieve the same or better result.","zh":"節能系統使用較少能源來達到相同或更好效果。"},{"en":"LED lights are energy-efficient systems because they need less electricity than old bulbs.","zh":"LED 燈是節能系統，因為它們比舊燈泡需要較少電力。"},{"en":"If a power system is more efficient, it may produce more electricity from the same fuel.","zh":"如果發電系統效率較高，它可能用同樣燃料產生更多電力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes technology that reduces wasted energy.","zh":"這個短語描述減少能源浪費的技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as with","meaning":"與……一樣","examples":[{"en":"As with desalination, large infrastructure projects often attract powerful supporters.","zh":"與海水化淡一樣，大型基建項目常吸引有權勢支持者。"},{"en":"As with something means in the same way as that other example.","zh":"“As with” 某事指與另一例子以相同方式。"},{"en":"As with exam preparation, learning a language requires steady practice.","zh":"與考試準備一樣，學習語言需要穩定練習。"},{"en":"If two technologies both need big companies and government support, they can be compared this way.","zh":"如果兩種技術都需要大公司和政府支持，就可以用這種方式比較。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a parallel example.","zh":"這個短語引出平行例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"desalination","meaning":"海水化淡","examples":[{"en":"Desalination turns seawater into usable fresh water.","zh":"海水化淡把海水轉化為可用淡水。"},{"en":"Desalination is the process of removing salt from seawater or salty water.","zh":"海水化淡是從海水或鹹水中去除鹽分的過程。"},{"en":"A dry coastal city may use desalination when rivers and reservoirs cannot provide enough water.","zh":"乾旱沿海城市在河流和水庫供水不足時，可能使用海水化淡。"},{"en":"If desalination plants are large and expensive, they may require strong government and industry support.","zh":"如果海水化淡廠大型而昂貴，它們可能需要強大政府和業界支持。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to making salty water suitable for use.","zh":"這個短語指把鹹水變成適合使用的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"wield influence","meaning":"發揮影響力","examples":[{"en":"Powerful industrial groups can wield considerable political influence.","zh":"強大的工業團體可以發揮相當大的政治影響力。"},{"en":"To wield influence means to use power or connections to affect decisions.","zh":"發揮影響力指使用權力或人脈來影響決定。"},{"en":"Parent groups may wield influence when many families demand safer school crossings.","zh":"當許多家庭要求更安全的學校過路處時，家長團體可能發揮影響力。"},{"en":"If an industry funds campaigns or lobbies officials, it may shape policy.","zh":"如果行業資助活動或游說官員，就可能塑造政策。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active use of influence.","zh":"這個短語描述主動使用影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"engage in large projects","meaning":"參與大型項目","examples":[{"en":"Governments may prefer to engage in large projects with a few major companies.","zh":"政府可能較喜歡與少數大型公司參與大型項目。"},{"en":"To engage in large projects means to become involved in major planned works or programmes.","zh":"參與大型項目指投入重大規劃工程或計劃。"},{"en":"A city may engage in a large transport project to build a new railway line.","zh":"城市可能參與大型交通項目，興建新鐵路線。"},{"en":"If governments work with a few large firms, coordination may be easier but public choice may narrow.","zh":"如果政府與少數大公司合作，協調可能較容易，但公眾選擇可能變窄。"},{"en":"The phrase describes participation in big organised undertakings.","zh":"這個短語描述參與大型有組織工程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a few major players","meaning":"少數主要參與者","examples":[{"en":"Large energy projects often involve only a few major players.","zh":"大型能源項目通常只涉及少數主要參與者。"},{"en":"A few major players are a small number of powerful companies or organisations in a field.","zh":"少數主要參與者是某領域中少數有權勢的公司或組織。"},{"en":"In the supermarket industry, a few major players may control most large stores.","zh":"在超市行業中，少數主要參與者可能控制大部分大型店舖。"},{"en":"If only a few major players are involved, smaller companies may have little influence.","zh":"如果只有少數主要參與者涉及其中，較小公司可能幾乎沒有影響力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes concentrated power in a market or project.","zh":"這個短語描述市場或項目中的權力集中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"change household behaviour","meaning":"改變家庭行為","examples":[{"en":"It may be harder to change household behaviour than to fund a single large project.","zh":"改變家庭行為可能比資助單一大型項目更困難。"},{"en":"To change household behaviour means to alter how families use energy, water, food or other resources at home.","zh":"改變家庭行為指改變家庭在家中使用能源、水、食物或其他資源的方式。"},{"en":"A government may try to change household behaviour by encouraging shorter showers and lower air-conditioning use.","zh":"政府可能透過鼓勵縮短淋浴時間和減少冷氣使用來改變家庭行為。"},{"en":"If many families change small daily habits, national energy demand can fall.","zh":"如果許多家庭改變小小日常習慣，國家能源需求可以下降。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on ordinary people’s routines, not industrial machines.","zh":"這個短語強調普通人的日常規律，而不是工業機器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on a scattered household scale","meaning":"在分散的家庭層面","examples":[{"en":"Energy conservation measures may need to operate on a scattered household scale.","zh":"節能措施可能需要在分散的家庭層面運作。"},{"en":"On a scattered household scale means across many separate homes rather than in one central place.","zh":"在分散的家庭層面，指跨越許多獨立家庭，而不是在一個中心地點。"},{"en":"Recycling works on a scattered household scale when every family separates waste at home.","zh":"當每個家庭在家分類垃圾，回收就是在分散家庭層面運作。"},{"en":"If action depends on thousands of homes, organisation and behaviour change become difficult.","zh":"如果行動依賴數以千計家庭，組織和行為改變就變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts many small domestic actions with one large project.","zh":"這個短語把許多小型家庭行動與一個大型項目作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"replace coal with","meaning":"以……取代煤炭","examples":[{"en":"Some environmentalists want to replace coal with solar power.","zh":"一些環保人士希望以太陽能取代煤炭。"},{"en":"To replace coal with something means to stop using coal and use another energy source instead.","zh":"以某物取代煤炭，指停止使用煤炭並改用另一種能源。"},{"en":"A school can replace paper notices with digital messages to reduce waste.","zh":"學校可以用電子訊息取代紙本通告，以減少浪費。"},{"en":"If coal is replaced with solar power, emissions from electricity generation may fall.","zh":"如果以太陽能取代煤炭，發電排放可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly shows substitution.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示替代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"zero-emission photovoltaic cells","meaning":"零排放光伏電池","examples":[{"en":"Zero-emission photovoltaic cells convert sunlight into electricity.","zh":"零排放光伏電池把陽光轉化為電力。"},{"en":"Zero-emission photovoltaic cells are solar cells that generate electricity without direct carbon emissions during operation.","zh":"零排放光伏電池是在運作期間不直接產生碳排放的太陽能電池。"},{"en":"A rooftop solar panel contains photovoltaic cells that turn sunlight into usable power.","zh":"天台太陽能板含有把陽光轉化為可用電力的光伏電池。"},{"en":"If these cells replace coal power, electricity can be generated with far less air pollution.","zh":"如果這些電池取代燃煤電力，就能以遠少得多的空氣污染發電。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to solar electricity technology.","zh":"這個短語指太陽能發電技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"produce solar energy","meaning":"生產太陽能","examples":[{"en":"Photovoltaic cells are used to produce solar energy.","zh":"光伏電池用來生產太陽能。"},{"en":"To produce solar energy means to generate usable power from sunlight.","zh":"生產太陽能指從陽光中產生可用能源。"},{"en":"A home can produce solar energy if panels are installed on its roof.","zh":"如果房屋屋頂安裝太陽能板，就可以生產太陽能。"},{"en":"If sunlight is strong and panels are efficient, solar output increases.","zh":"如果陽光強而太陽能板效率高，太陽能輸出就會增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes turning sunlight into electricity or heat.","zh":"這個短語描述把陽光轉化為電力或熱能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"require covering an area","meaning":"需要覆蓋一片地區","examples":[{"en":"Large solar projects may require covering an enormous area of land.","zh":"大型太陽能項目可能需要覆蓋一片巨大土地。"},{"en":"To require covering an area means to need a certain amount of land or surface to be occupied.","zh":"需要覆蓋一片地區，指需要佔用一定土地或表面範圍。"},{"en":"A school fair may require covering the playground with tents and stalls.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能需要用帳篷和攤位覆蓋操場。"},{"en":"If solar panels need a huge area, land use becomes an important concern.","zh":"如果太陽能板需要巨大面積，土地使用就成為重要關注。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the space requirement of a project.","zh":"這個短語描述項目的空間需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"roughly twice the size of","meaning":"約為……的兩倍","examples":[{"en":"The required area would be roughly twice the size of Lebanon.","zh":"所需面積約為黎巴嫩的兩倍。"},{"en":"Roughly twice the size of something means about two times as large as it.","zh":"約為某物的兩倍，指大約是它的兩倍大。"},{"en":"A new shopping centre might be roughly twice the size of the old one.","zh":"新購物中心可能約為舊商場的兩倍。"},{"en":"If a solar farm needs land twice the size of a country, the scale is enormous.","zh":"如果太陽能場需要一個國家兩倍大的土地，規模就非常巨大。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate size comparison.","zh":"這個短語給出約略大小比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reservations about","meaning":"對……的保留","examples":[{"en":"There are many reservations about the cost and safety of CCS.","zh":"人們對 CCS 的成本和安全有許多保留。"},{"en":"Reservations about something are doubts or concerns that prevent full support.","zh":"對某事的保留，是阻止完全支持它的疑慮或關注。"},{"en":"Parents may have reservations about a school trip if the travel plan is unclear.","zh":"如果旅行計劃不清楚，家長可能對學校旅行有保留。"},{"en":"If people have reservations about CCS, they may support cleaner energy but question this method.","zh":"如果人們對 CCS 有保留，他們可能支持較清潔能源，但質疑這種方法。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses cautious doubt, not complete rejection.","zh":"這個短語表達謹慎懷疑，而不是完全拒絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"principally","meaning":"主要地","examples":[{"en":"Principally, critics object to the enormous cost of CCS.","zh":"批評者主要反對 CCS 的巨大成本。"},{"en":"Principally means mainly or above all.","zh":"“Principally” 指主要地或最重要地。"},{"en":"Students may choose a library principally because it is quiet.","zh":"學生可能主要因圖書館安靜而選擇它。"},{"en":"If critics object principally to cost, money is their main concern.","zh":"如果批評者主要反對成本，金錢就是他們的主要關注。"},{"en":"The word introduces the most important reason.","zh":"這個詞引出最重要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"enormously expensive","meaning":"極其昂貴","examples":[{"en":"Carbon capture is enormously expensive.","zh":"碳捕集極其昂貴。"},{"en":"Enormously expensive means costing a very large amount of money.","zh":"極其昂貴指成本非常高。"},{"en":"Building a new airport is enormously expensive because it needs land, roads, terminals and safety systems.","zh":"興建新機場極其昂貴，因為它需要土地、道路、客運大樓和安全系統。"},{"en":"If a technology is enormously expensive, governments may need subsidies before companies use it.","zh":"如果技術極其昂貴，政府可能需要補貼，公司才會使用。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses very high cost.","zh":"這個短語強調非常高的成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"conservative estimates","meaning":"保守估計","examples":[{"en":"Even conservative estimates suggest that CCS electricity would be very costly.","zh":"即使保守估計也顯示 CCS 電力會非常昂貴。"},{"en":"Conservative estimates are cautious calculations that avoid exaggerating the size of a number.","zh":"保守估計是避免誇大數字大小的謹慎計算。"},{"en":"A teacher may give a conservative estimate of homework time so students do not panic.","zh":"老師可能對功課時間作保守估計，讓學生不會恐慌。"},{"en":"If even cautious estimates are high, the real cost may be a serious problem.","zh":"如果連謹慎估計也很高，真實成本可能是嚴重問題。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that the figure is not an extreme exaggeration.","zh":"這個短語暗示該數字不是極端誇大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"put the price at","meaning":"估計價格為……","examples":[{"en":"Some estimates put the price at more than five times the current level.","zh":"一些估計把價格定為現水平的五倍以上。"},{"en":"To put the price at a figure means to estimate or state that the price is that amount.","zh":"估計價格為某數字，指估算或說明價格是該金額。"},{"en":"A contractor may put the price of repairs at $20,000 after checking the damage.","zh":"承辦商檢查損壞後，可能估計維修價格為二萬元。"},{"en":"If estimates put CCS power far above current prices, consumers may resist it.","zh":"如果估計顯示 CCS 電力遠高於現價，消費者可能抗拒。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a cost estimate.","zh":"這個短語引出成本估算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"current retail price","meaning":"現時零售價格","examples":[{"en":"CCS electricity could cost several times the current retail price.","zh":"CCS 電力成本可能是現時零售價格的數倍。"},{"en":"Current retail price is the price ordinary consumers pay now when buying a product or service.","zh":"現時零售價格是普通消費者目前購買產品或服務時支付的價格。"},{"en":"A shop may compare a sale price with the current retail price to show the discount.","zh":"商店可能把減價後價格與現時零售價格比較，以顯示折扣。"},{"en":"If future electricity costs several times the current retail price, households may struggle.","zh":"如果未來電力成本是現時零售價格的數倍，家庭可能難以負擔。"},{"en":"The phrase gives today’s consumer price as a comparison point.","zh":"這個短語以今日消費者價格作比較點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bear a price hike","meaning":"承受加價","examples":[{"en":"Consumers may be unwilling to bear a substantial price hike.","zh":"消費者可能不願承受大幅加價。"},{"en":"To bear a price hike means to accept or pay a higher price.","zh":"承受加價指接受或支付較高價格。"},{"en":"Families may struggle to bear a rent hike if salaries stay the same.","zh":"如果薪金不變，家庭可能難以承受租金加價。"},{"en":"If electricity prices rise sharply, public anger may increase.","zh":"如果電價急升，公眾憤怒可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes carrying the burden of higher costs.","zh":"這個短語描述承擔較高成本的負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"massive state subsidies","meaning":"巨額政府補貼","examples":[{"en":"Massive state subsidies might be necessary to make CCS affordable.","zh":"可能需要巨額政府補貼，才能令 CCS 負擔得起。"},{"en":"Massive state subsidies are very large amounts of government financial support.","zh":"巨額政府補貼是非常大量的政府財政支援。"},{"en":"A government may provide massive subsidies to keep public transport fares low.","zh":"政府可能提供巨額補貼，以維持公共交通票價低廉。"},{"en":"If CCS is too costly for the market, public money may be needed to support it.","zh":"如果 CCS 對市場而言太昂貴，可能需要公共資金支持。"},{"en":"The phrase describes heavy government funding.","zh":"這個短語描述大量政府資助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be necessary for something to work","meaning":"是……得以運作所必需的","examples":[{"en":"Public subsidies may be necessary for CCS to work commercially.","zh":"公共補貼可能是 CCS 在商業上得以運作所必需的。"},{"en":"To be necessary for something to work means to be required for it to function successfully.","zh":"是某事得以運作所必需的，指它是某事成功運作所需要的條件。"},{"en":"Clear instructions are necessary for group work to work well.","zh":"清楚指示是小組工作順利運作所必需的。"},{"en":"If CCS cannot compete on price, subsidies may be necessary for it to survive in the market.","zh":"如果 CCS 在價格上無法競爭，補貼可能是它在市場中生存所必需的。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a condition for success.","zh":"這個短語指出成功所需條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"capital outlay","meaning":"資本支出","examples":[{"en":"The capital outlay for carbon-capture equipment is extremely high.","zh":"碳捕集設備的資本支出極高。"},{"en":"Capital outlay is the large upfront spending needed to buy, build or install major assets.","zh":"資本支出是購買、建造或安裝重大資產所需的大筆前期開支。"},{"en":"A restaurant’s capital outlay may include kitchen equipment, furniture and renovation.","zh":"餐廳的資本支出可能包括廚房設備、家具和裝修。"},{"en":"If capital outlay is high, companies may hesitate before investing.","zh":"如果資本支出高，公司投資前可能猶豫。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to initial investment costs, not daily operating expenses.","zh":"這個短語指初始投資成本，而不是日常營運開支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"purchase equipment","meaning":"購買設備","examples":[{"en":"Power companies must purchase expensive capture equipment.","zh":"電力公司必須購買昂貴捕集設備。"},{"en":"To purchase equipment means to buy tools, machines or devices needed for work.","zh":"購買設備指購買工作所需的工具、機器或裝置。"},{"en":"A school may purchase equipment such as projectors, tablets and laboratory tools.","zh":"學校可能購買投影機、平板電腦和實驗室工具等設備。"},{"en":"If equipment is expensive, small companies may need loans or subsidies.","zh":"如果設備昂貴，小公司可能需要貸款或補貼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes buying physical tools for a project or operation.","zh":"這個短語描述為項目或營運購買實體工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"retrofit existing power plants","meaning":"改裝現有發電廠","examples":[{"en":"Companies may retrofit existing power plants rather than build new ones.","zh":"公司可能改裝現有發電廠，而不是興建新發電廠。"},{"en":"To retrofit existing power plants means to add new technology to power stations already built.","zh":"改裝現有發電廠指把新技術加入已建成的發電站。"},{"en":"A city may retrofit old buildings with better insulation instead of replacing them.","zh":"城市可能為舊建築加裝更好隔熱設備，而不是替換它們。"},{"en":"If plants are retrofitted, construction may be cheaper than building entirely new facilities.","zh":"如果發電廠被改裝，建設成本可能低於建造全新設施。"},{"en":"The phrase describes upgrading current power infrastructure.","zh":"這個短語描述升級現有電力基建。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be high enough","meaning":"已經相當高","examples":[{"en":"The cost of retrofitting is already high enough to discourage investment.","zh":"改裝成本已經相當高，足以阻礙投資。"},{"en":"To be high enough means to reach a level that produces a particular result.","zh":"已經相當高，指達到會產生某結果的水平。"},{"en":"If bus fares are high enough, some students may start walking to school.","zh":"如果巴士車費高到一定程度，一些學生可能開始步行上學。"},{"en":"If retrofitting costs are high enough to discourage investors, the project may not begin.","zh":"如果改裝成本高到令投資者卻步，項目可能不會開始。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a level with its consequence.","zh":"這個短語把某水平與其後果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"one-third more coal","meaning":"多三分之一煤炭","examples":[{"en":"Capturing carbon may require one-third more coal to be burnt.","zh":"捕集碳可能需要燃燒多三分之一煤炭。"},{"en":"One-third more coal means an additional amount equal to about 33% of the original coal used.","zh":"多三分之一煤炭，指額外增加相當於原本用煤量約33%的煤。"},{"en":"If a bakery needs one-third more flour, it must buy much more than usual.","zh":"如果麵包店需要多三分之一麵粉，就必須比平常購買多得多。"},{"en":"If CCS requires more coal, part of its environmental benefit may be reduced by extra fuel use.","zh":"如果 CCS 需要更多煤，其部分環境效益可能被額外燃料使用削弱。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a proportional increase.","zh":"這個短語給出按比例增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"at least 75% more expensive","meaning":"至少貴七成半","examples":[{"en":"Building a new CCS plant may be at least 75% more expensive than retrofitting.","zh":"興建新的 CCS 發電廠可能比改裝至少貴七成半。"},{"en":"At least 75% more expensive means the cost is no less than 75% higher.","zh":"至少貴七成半，指成本不低於高出75%。"},{"en":"A new laptop may be at least 75% more expensive than repairing the old one.","zh":"新手提電腦可能比維修舊電腦至少貴七成半。"},{"en":"If new plants cost that much more, companies may prefer retrofitting.","zh":"如果新發電廠貴這麼多，公司可能較喜歡改裝。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a minimum level of extra cost.","zh":"這個短語設定額外成本的最低水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"untried technology","meaning":"未經驗證的技術","examples":[{"en":"Some carbon-capture technology remains untried.","zh":"一些碳捕集技術仍屬未經驗證的技術。"},{"en":"Untried technology is technology that has not yet been tested properly in real conditions.","zh":"未經驗證的技術，是尚未在真實條件下充分測試的技術。"},{"en":"A school may hesitate to buy untried teaching software before seeing evidence that it works.","zh":"學校在看見有效證據前，可能猶豫是否購買未經驗證的教學軟件。"},{"en":"If technology is untried, costs, safety and reliability are uncertain.","zh":"如果技術未經驗證，成本、安全和可靠性都不確定。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that a method may still be risky or experimental.","zh":"這個短語提醒某方法可能仍有風險或屬實驗性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"on an industrial scale","meaning":"在工業規模上","examples":[{"en":"Some syngas turbines have not yet been used on an industrial scale.","zh":"一些合成氣渦輪機尚未在工業規模上使用。"},{"en":"On an industrial scale means at a large size suitable for factories, power plants or mass production.","zh":"在工業規模上，指以適合工廠、發電廠或大規模生產的大小運作。"},{"en":"A recipe may work at home but fail on an industrial scale in a food factory.","zh":"食譜在家中可能可行，但在食品工廠的工業規模上可能失敗。"},{"en":"If a technology has not worked at industrial scale, it may still face practical problems.","zh":"如果技術尚未在工業規模上運作，它可能仍面對實際問題。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts laboratory trials with large real-world use.","zh":"這個短語把實驗室試驗與大型現實使用作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"after capture","meaning":"捕集後","examples":[{"en":"After capture, carbon dioxide must be compressed for transport.","zh":"捕集後，二氧化碳必須被壓縮以便運輸。"},{"en":"After capture means after the carbon dioxide has been separated and collected.","zh":"捕集後，指二氧化碳已被分離並收集之後。"},{"en":"After catching rainwater, a household may store it in a tank for later use.","zh":"家庭收集雨水後，可能把它儲存在水箱中供日後使用。"},{"en":"If CO₂ has been captured, the next step is usually compression, transport or storage.","zh":"如果二氧化碳已被捕集，下一步通常是壓縮、運輸或儲存。"},{"en":"The phrase marks what happens after the collection stage.","zh":"這個短語標示收集階段之後發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be compressed into","meaning":"被壓縮成……","examples":[{"en":"Carbon dioxide must be compressed into a dense liquid-like state.","zh":"二氧化碳必須被壓縮成濃密、類似液體的狀態。"},{"en":"To be compressed into something means to be squeezed under pressure until it changes form or density.","zh":"被壓縮成某物，指在壓力下被擠壓至形態或密度改變。"},{"en":"Clothes can be compressed into a small travel bag by using a vacuum bag.","zh":"衣物可以用真空袋壓縮成小旅行袋大小。"},{"en":"If CO₂ is compressed, it becomes easier to transport through pipelines.","zh":"如果二氧化碳被壓縮，就更容易透過管道運輸。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pressure changing the physical state or volume of something.","zh":"這個短語描述壓力改變某物的物理狀態或體積。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"supercritical liquid","meaning":"超臨界流體","examples":[{"en":"Captured CO₂ is compressed into a supercritical liquid for transport.","zh":"捕集到的二氧化碳被壓縮成超臨界流體以便運輸。"},{"en":"A supercritical liquid is a dense state where a substance behaves partly like a gas and partly like a liquid under high pressure.","zh":"超臨界流體是在高壓下物質部分像氣體、部分像液體的高密度狀態。"},{"en":"Engineers may use supercritical CO₂ because it can be moved more efficiently than ordinary gas.","zh":"工程師可能使用超臨界二氧化碳，因為它比普通氣體更容易有效運輸。"},{"en":"If CO₂ is compressed into this state, storage and transport become technically possible but costly.","zh":"如果二氧化碳被壓縮成這種狀態，儲存和運輸在技術上變得可行但昂貴。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a special high-pressure physical state.","zh":"這個短語指特殊的高壓物理狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"transport and storage","meaning":"運輸與儲存","examples":[{"en":"Compressing carbon dioxide for transport and storage is costly.","zh":"為運輸與儲存而壓縮二氧化碳成本高昂。"},{"en":"Transport and storage mean moving a substance to another place and keeping it there safely.","zh":"運輸與儲存指把某物移到另一地方並安全保存。"},{"en":"Food delivery requires transport and storage so meals arrive fresh and safe.","zh":"食物配送需要運輸與儲存，讓餐點新鮮安全送達。"},{"en":"If captured CO₂ must travel long distances, transport and storage costs increase.","zh":"如果捕集到的二氧化碳必須長距離運送，運輸與儲存成本會增加。"},{"en":"The phrase covers what happens after carbon dioxide is captured.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋二氧化碳被捕集後發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"predict that","meaning":"預測","examples":[{"en":"Researchers predict that CCS would produce vast volumes of compressed CO₂.","zh":"研究人員預測 CCS 會產生大量壓縮二氧化碳。"},{"en":"To predict that something will happen means to say it is likely to happen in the future.","zh":"預測某事會發生，指說它未來很可能發生。"},{"en":"Weather forecasters may predict that heavy rain will arrive tomorrow.","zh":"天氣預報員可能預測明天會有大雨。"},{"en":"If researchers predict huge waste volumes, policymakers must consider storage capacity early.","zh":"如果研究人員預測會有巨大廢料量，政策制定者就必須及早考慮儲存容量。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an evidence-based expectation.","zh":"這個短語引出基於證據的預期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be adopted modestly","meaning":"只作有限度採用","examples":[{"en":"Even if CCS were adopted modestly, enormous volumes of waste would be produced.","zh":"即使 CCS 只作有限度採用，也會產生巨大廢料量。"},{"en":"To be adopted modestly means to be used only to a limited or moderate extent.","zh":"只作有限度採用，指只以有限或中等程度使用。"},{"en":"A school may adopt tablets modestly by using them in only two subjects at first.","zh":"學校可能先只在兩科使用平板電腦，有限度採用它們。"},{"en":"If CCS creates huge waste even with limited use, full adoption would raise larger concerns.","zh":"如果 CCS 在有限使用下已產生巨大廢料，全面採用會引發更大關注。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses small-scale or cautious implementation.","zh":"這個短語強調小規模或謹慎實施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"barrels per day","meaning":"每日桶數","examples":[{"en":"The study expressed the volume in barrels per day.","zh":"該研究以每日桶數表示體積。"},{"en":"Barrels per day is a measurement of how many barrels of liquid or compressed substance are produced or moved each day.","zh":"每日桶數是量度每天生產或移動多少桶液體或壓縮物質的單位。"},{"en":"Oil production is often reported in barrels per day.","zh":"石油產量常以每日桶數報告。"},{"en":"If CO₂ waste is measured in barrels per day, readers can compare it with oil production.","zh":"如果二氧化碳廢料以每日桶數量度，讀者就能把它與石油產量比較。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a daily flow rate.","zh":"這個短語給出每日流量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"it is worth noting that","meaning":"值得注意的是","examples":[{"en":"It is worth noting that the predicted waste volume exceeds current oil production.","zh":"值得注意的是，預測廢料量超過現時石油產量。"},{"en":"It is worth noting that means the following point is important and should not be ignored.","zh":"“It is worth noting that” 指接下來的一點很重要，不應被忽視。"},{"en":"It is worth noting that a cheap product may cost more later if it breaks quickly.","zh":"值得注意的是，如果廉價產品很快損壞，之後可能花費更多。"},{"en":"If a detail changes how serious a problem seems, the writer may highlight it this way.","zh":"如果某細節改變問題看起來有多嚴重，作者可能用這方式突出它。"},{"en":"The phrase draws attention to an important observation.","zh":"這個短語把注意力引向重要觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"current oil production","meaning":"現時石油產量","examples":[{"en":"Current oil production is far below the projected volume of captured CO₂.","zh":"現時石油產量遠低於預測的捕集二氧化碳體積。"},{"en":"Current oil production means the amount of oil being produced at the present time.","zh":"現時石油產量指目前正在生產的石油數量。"},{"en":"Economists may compare current oil production with last year’s output to track market changes.","zh":"經濟學家可能比較現時石油產量與去年的產出，以追蹤市場變化。"},{"en":"If CO₂ waste exceeds current oil production, the storage challenge is enormous.","zh":"如果二氧化碳廢料超過現時石油產量，儲存挑戰就非常巨大。"},{"en":"The phrase gives today’s oil output as a comparison point.","zh":"這個短語以今日石油產出作比較點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"eleven times more waste","meaning":"多十一倍廢料","examples":[{"en":"CCS could produce eleven times more waste than the oil being extracted.","zh":"CCS 可能產生比所開採石油多十一倍的廢料。"},{"en":"Eleven times more waste means the waste amount would be eleven times as large as another amount.","zh":"多十一倍廢料，指廢料量是另一數量的十一倍。"},{"en":"A school event would be worrying if it produced eleven times more rubbish than usual.","zh":"如果學校活動產生比平常多十一倍垃圾，就令人擔心。"},{"en":"If CCS creates waste far beyond oil output, storage infrastructure must be extremely large.","zh":"如果 CCS 產生遠超石油產量的廢料，儲存基建就必須極大。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a very large comparison.","zh":"這個短語強調非常大的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"waste for burial","meaning":"供地下掩埋的廢料","examples":[{"en":"The process would create vast quantities of waste for underground burial.","zh":"這個過程會創造大量供地下掩埋的廢料。"},{"en":"Waste for burial is unwanted material that must be placed underground for disposal or storage.","zh":"供地下掩埋的廢料，是必須放入地下處置或儲存的不需要物質。"},{"en":"A landfill receives household waste for burial when recycling is not possible.","zh":"當無法回收時，堆填區接收供掩埋的家庭廢物。"},{"en":"If CCS creates waste for burial, safe underground space becomes essential.","zh":"如果 CCS 創造供掩埋的廢料，安全地下空間就變得必要。"},{"en":"The phrase presents captured CO₂ as a disposal problem.","zh":"這個短語把捕集到的二氧化碳呈現為處置問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"simultaneously be extracted","meaning":"同時被開採","examples":[{"en":"Oil would simultaneously be extracted while CO₂ was stored.","zh":"石油會在二氧化碳被儲存的同時被開採。"},{"en":"To simultaneously be extracted means to be removed at the same time another process is happening.","zh":"同時被開採，指在另一過程發生的同時被移除或取出。"},{"en":"In a factory, heat may be recovered while steam is simultaneously extracted for another use.","zh":"在工廠中，熱量可能被回收，同時蒸汽被抽取作其他用途。"},{"en":"If oil is extracted while CO₂ is stored, the project may reduce emissions but still support fossil-fuel production.","zh":"如果石油在二氧化碳儲存時被開採，項目可能減排但仍支持化石燃料生產。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights two processes happening together.","zh":"這個短語突出兩個過程同時發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be used successfully","meaning":"已獲成功使用","examples":[{"en":"Carbon sequestration has already been used successfully in some locations.","zh":"碳封存已在一些地點成功使用。"},{"en":"To be used successfully means to be applied and to work as intended.","zh":"已獲成功使用，指被應用並按預期運作。"},{"en":"A new reading programme is used successfully if students read more and understand better.","zh":"如果新閱讀計劃令學生閱讀更多並理解更好，它就是成功使用。"},{"en":"If sequestration has worked in some places, supporters can point to real examples.","zh":"如果封存在某些地方有效，支持者就能指出真實例子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes proven use in at least some cases.","zh":"這個短語描述至少在某些情況下已證實可用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a limited number of","meaning":"數量有限的……","examples":[{"en":"Only a limited number of geological sites have ideal storage conditions.","zh":"只有數量有限的地質地點具備理想儲存條件。"},{"en":"A limited number of something means not many of them are available.","zh":"數量有限的某物，指可用數量不多。"},{"en":"A school trip may have a limited number of seats on the bus.","zh":"學校旅行巴士座位可能數量有限。"},{"en":"If only a limited number of sites are suitable, CCS cannot be used everywhere easily.","zh":"如果只有有限地點合適，CCS 就不能輕易在各處使用。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses scarcity.","zh":"這個短語強調稀缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"optimal conditions","meaning":"最理想條件","examples":[{"en":"Safe sequestration requires optimal geological conditions.","zh":"安全封存需要最理想的地質條件。"},{"en":"Optimal conditions are the best possible conditions for something to work well.","zh":"最理想條件是某事順利運作的最佳可能條件。"},{"en":"Plants grow best under optimal conditions of light, water and soil.","zh":"植物在光照、水分和土壤最理想條件下生長最好。"},{"en":"If underground rock is unstable, conditions may not be optimal for CO₂ storage.","zh":"如果地下岩石不穩定，條件可能不適合二氧化碳儲存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ideal requirements, not merely acceptable ones.","zh":"這個短語描述理想要求，而不只是可接受要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"brittle rock","meaning":"易碎岩石","examples":[{"en":"Brittle rock may crack during an earthquake.","zh":"易碎岩石可能在地震期間裂開。"},{"en":"Brittle rock is rock that breaks or cracks easily under pressure.","zh":"易碎岩石是在壓力下容易破裂或開裂的岩石。"},{"en":"A builder may avoid brittle stone when constructing a wall that must last for years.","zh":"建築工人建造需要耐用多年的牆時，可能避免使用易碎石材。"},{"en":"If CO₂ is stored in brittle rock, cracks could allow gas to escape.","zh":"如果二氧化碳儲存在易碎岩石中，裂縫可能讓氣體逃出。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a geological weakness.","zh":"這個短語描述地質弱點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"release stored CO₂","meaning":"釋放已封存的二氧化碳","examples":[{"en":"Earthquakes could release stored CO₂ from brittle formations.","zh":"地震可能從易碎地層中釋放已封存的二氧化碳。"},{"en":"To release stored CO₂ means to let carbon dioxide that was kept underground escape.","zh":"釋放已封存的二氧化碳，指讓原本保存在地下的二氧化碳逃出。"},{"en":"A cracked container can release stored gas into a room.","zh":"破裂容器可以把儲存氣體釋放到房間中。"},{"en":"If stored CO₂ is released, the purpose of sequestration is partly defeated.","zh":"如果已封存二氧化碳被釋放，碳封存目的就部分失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a leakage risk.","zh":"這個短語描述洩漏風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"proposals are just proposals","meaning":"建議仍只是構想","examples":[{"en":"Plans to use saline aquifers are still only proposals.","zh":"使用鹽水含水層的計劃仍只是構想。"},{"en":"Proposals are just proposals means ideas have been suggested but not yet proven or carried out.","zh":"建議仍只是構想，意思是想法已被提出，但尚未被證實或實行。"},{"en":"A plan for a new school garden is just a proposal until land, money and approval are secured.","zh":"新學校花園計劃在取得土地、資金和批准前仍只是構想。"},{"en":"If CCS plans remain proposals, real-world risks and costs may still be unknown.","zh":"如果 CCS 計劃仍只是構想，現實風險和成本可能仍未知。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against treating plans as achievements.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要把計劃當成成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"never be attempted","meaning":"從未被嘗試","examples":[{"en":"Large-scale sequestration has never been attempted in saline aquifers.","zh":"大規模封存從未在鹽水含水層中被嘗試。"},{"en":"To never be attempted means no one has tried to do it before.","zh":"從未被嘗試指以前沒有人試過做。"},{"en":"A school may avoid a new exam system if it has never been attempted there.","zh":"如果某新考試制度從未在學校嘗試過，學校可能避免使用它。"},{"en":"If a method has never been attempted at scale, its success is uncertain.","zh":"如果一種方法從未在大規模下嘗試，其成功仍不確定。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses lack of real experience.","zh":"這個短語強調缺乏真實經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"most problematic of all","meaning":"最成問題的是","examples":[{"en":"Most problematic of all, CCS reduces emissions without eliminating them.","zh":"最成問題的是，CCS 減少排放但沒有消除排放。"},{"en":"Most problematic of all means the biggest or most serious problem is the one being introduced.","zh":"最成問題的是，指接下來介紹的是最大或最嚴重的問題。"},{"en":"A phone may be expensive and fragile; most problematic of all, its battery may fail quickly.","zh":"手機可能昂貴又易碎；最成問題的是，其電池可能很快失效。"},{"en":"If CCS cuts but does not end emissions, critics may see it as incomplete.","zh":"如果 CCS 減少但不終止排放，批評者可能視它為不完整。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the strongest objection.","zh":"這個短語突出最強反對理由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"end carbon emissions","meaning":"終止碳排放","examples":[{"en":"CCS does not completely end carbon emissions.","zh":"CCS 並沒有完全終止碳排放。"},{"en":"To end carbon emissions means to stop releasing carbon dioxide and similar greenhouse gases.","zh":"終止碳排放指停止釋放二氧化碳和類似溫室氣體。"},{"en":"A city cannot end transport emissions if many buses still burn diesel.","zh":"如果許多巴士仍燃燒柴油，城市就不能終止交通排放。"},{"en":"If a technology only captures part of the CO₂, emissions continue at a lower level.","zh":"如果技術只捕集部分二氧化碳，排放仍以較低水平繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes complete elimination, not partial reduction.","zh":"這個短語描述完全消除，而不是部分減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"render something a medium-term solution","meaning":"令某事物成為中期方案","examples":[{"en":"Its limitations render CCS a medium-term solution.","zh":"其限制令 CCS 成為中期方案。"},{"en":"To render something a medium-term solution means to make it suitable only for an intermediate period, not as a final answer.","zh":"令某事物成為中期方案，指使它只適合中間階段，而不是最終答案。"},{"en":"Renting a classroom may render temporary teaching possible, but it is not a permanent campus plan.","zh":"租用課室可以令臨時教學可行，但不是永久校園計劃。"},{"en":"If CCS cannot eliminate emissions, it may buy time while cleaner energy develops.","zh":"如果 CCS 不能消除排放，它可能在較清潔能源發展期間爭取時間。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why a solution is useful but limited.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何方案有用但有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reasonably priced alternatives","meaning":"價格合理的替代方案","examples":[{"en":"There are several reasonably priced alternatives to CCS.","zh":"CCS 有幾個價格合理的替代方案。"},{"en":"Reasonably priced alternatives are other options that cost a fair or affordable amount.","zh":"價格合理的替代方案，是成本公平或可負擔的其他選項。"},{"en":"A family may choose a reasonably priced alternative to an expensive overseas holiday.","zh":"家庭可能選擇昂貴海外旅行的價格合理替代方案。"},{"en":"If cleaner technologies are cheaper than CCS, governments may prefer them.","zh":"如果較清潔技術比 CCS 便宜，政府可能較喜歡它們。"},{"en":"The phrase compares cost and choice.","zh":"這個短語比較成本和選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"conventional pulverised-coal power plants","meaning":"傳統煤粉發電廠","examples":[{"en":"Conventional pulverised-coal power plants are being redesigned.","zh":"傳統煤粉發電廠正在重新設計。"},{"en":"Conventional pulverised-coal power plants are traditional plants that burn finely crushed coal to generate electricity.","zh":"傳統煤粉發電廠是燃燒磨得很細的煤粉來發電的傳統發電廠。"},{"en":"An old coal plant may use pulverised coal because fine particles burn more easily.","zh":"舊燃煤電廠可能使用煤粉，因為細小顆粒較容易燃燒。"},{"en":"If these plants are redesigned, they may produce more electricity with less coal.","zh":"如果這些發電廠重新設計，它們可能用較少煤產生更多電力。"},{"en":"The phrase names a common older coal-power technology.","zh":"這個短語指出一種常見較舊的燃煤發電技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"undergo redesign","meaning":"正在重新設計","examples":[{"en":"Some conventional power plants are undergoing redesign.","zh":"一些傳統發電廠正在重新設計。"},{"en":"To undergo redesign means to be changed or improved in design.","zh":"正在重新設計，指設計正在被改變或改善。"},{"en":"A school website may undergo redesign so parents can find notices more easily.","zh":"學校網站可能正在重新設計，讓家長更容易找到通告。"},{"en":"If a power plant undergoes redesign, engineers may improve efficiency or reduce emissions.","zh":"如果發電廠重新設計，工程師可能提高效率或減少排放。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a process of planned design change.","zh":"這個短語描述有計劃的設計改變過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"produce more electricity from less coal","meaning":"以較少煤炭生產更多電力","examples":[{"en":"New designs aim to produce more electricity from less coal.","zh":"新設計旨在以較少煤炭生產更多電力。"},{"en":"To produce more electricity from less coal means to increase efficiency by getting more power from a smaller fuel amount.","zh":"以較少煤炭生產更多電力，指從較少燃料中取得更多電力，從而提高效率。"},{"en":"A better stove can cook the same meal using less gas.","zh":"更好的爐具可以用較少煤氣煮同一餐。"},{"en":"If a plant produces more power from less coal, costs and emissions may both fall.","zh":"如果發電廠用較少煤產生更多電力，成本和排放都可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improved fuel efficiency.","zh":"這個短語描述燃料效率提升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be phased out","meaning":"被逐步淘汰","examples":[{"en":"Coal will eventually have to be phased out.","zh":"煤炭最終必須被逐步淘汰。"},{"en":"To be phased out means to be gradually reduced and finally stopped.","zh":"被逐步淘汰指逐漸減少並最終停止使用。"},{"en":"A school may phase out paper notices by slowly replacing them with digital messages.","zh":"學校可能透過慢慢以電子訊息取代紙本通告，逐步淘汰紙本通告。"},{"en":"If coal is phased out, workers and communities may need time to adjust.","zh":"如果煤炭被逐步淘汰，工人和社區可能需要時間適應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual removal, not sudden disappearance.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸移除，而不是突然消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"ultimately","meaning":"最終","examples":[{"en":"Ultimately, heavily polluting fuels will need to be replaced.","zh":"最終，嚴重污染的燃料將需要被取代。"},{"en":"Ultimately means in the end or after everything is considered.","zh":"“Ultimately” 指到最後或考慮一切之後。"},{"en":"A student may try many study methods, but ultimately they need regular practice.","zh":"學生可能嘗試許多學習方法，但最終仍需要定期練習。"},{"en":"If a fuel causes serious pollution, society may eventually need to stop relying on it.","zh":"如果燃料造成嚴重污染，社會最終可能需要停止依賴它。"},{"en":"The word introduces the final conclusion.","zh":"這個詞引出最終結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"cost-effective","meaning":"具成本效益","examples":[{"en":"Redesigned power plants could be more cost-effective.","zh":"重新設計的發電廠可能更具成本效益。"},{"en":"Cost-effective means giving good results for the money spent.","zh":"具成本效益指花費的金錢能帶來良好效果。"},{"en":"Buying durable school chairs may be cost-effective because they last for many years.","zh":"購買耐用學校椅子可能具成本效益，因為它們可使用多年。"},{"en":"If a power plant produces more electricity with less fuel, it may be more cost-effective.","zh":"如果發電廠用較少燃料產生更多電力，它可能更具成本效益。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on value, not simply low price.","zh":"這個短語強調價值，而不只是低價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"hybrid plants","meaning":"混合式發電廠","examples":[{"en":"Hybrid plants can use both natural gas and coal.","zh":"混合式發電廠可以同時使用天然氣和煤炭。"},{"en":"Hybrid plants are power plants that combine two fuels, technologies or energy systems.","zh":"混合式發電廠是結合兩種燃料、技術或能源系統的發電廠。"},{"en":"A hybrid car uses both an engine and an electric motor; a hybrid plant similarly combines systems.","zh":"混合動力汽車同時使用引擎和電動馬達；混合式發電廠也同樣結合系統。"},{"en":"If a plant can use gas and coal, it may switch fuels depending on cost or emissions rules.","zh":"如果發電廠可使用天然氣和煤，就可能根據成本或排放規則轉換燃料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a mixed energy system.","zh":"這個短語描述混合能源系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"natural gas on its own","meaning":"單獨使用天然氣","examples":[{"en":"Natural gas could also be used on its own.","zh":"天然氣也可以單獨使用。"},{"en":"Natural gas on its own means natural gas used by itself, without being mixed with coal or another fuel.","zh":"單獨使用天然氣，指只使用天然氣，而不與煤或另一種燃料混合。"},{"en":"A family may use gas on its own for cooking instead of combining it with electricity.","zh":"家庭可能單獨使用煤氣煮食，而不是與電力結合。"},{"en":"If natural gas is used alone, emissions may be lower than coal but not zero.","zh":"如果天然氣單獨使用，排放可能低於煤炭，但不是零。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights separate use rather than combined use.","zh":"這個短語強調分開使用，而不是混合使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"gain credibility","meaning":"日益獲得認可","examples":[{"en":"Solar power is rapidly gaining credibility.","zh":"太陽能正迅速日益獲得認可。"},{"en":"To gain credibility means to become more trusted, accepted or taken seriously.","zh":"日益獲得認可指變得更受信任、接受或重視。"},{"en":"A new teacher gains credibility when students see that lessons are useful and fair.","zh":"當學生看見課堂有用又公平，新老師就會獲得認可。"},{"en":"If solar power becomes cheaper and reliable, people take it more seriously as an energy source.","zh":"如果太陽能變得更便宜且可靠，人們就更認真看待它作為能源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growing trust.","zh":"這個短語描述信任增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"an agreed measure of cost","meaning":"一套公認的成本衡量方法","examples":[{"en":"Energy comparisons require an agreed measure of cost.","zh":"能源比較需要一套公認的成本衡量方法。"},{"en":"An agreed measure of cost is a shared standard used to compare how expensive different options are.","zh":"一套公認的成本衡量方法，是用來比較不同選項有多昂貴的共同標準。"},{"en":"A school may use cost per student as an agreed measure when comparing trips.","zh":"學校比較旅行時，可能使用每名學生成本作為公認衡量方法。"},{"en":"Without a common measure, comparing solar, gas and coal costs can be confusing.","zh":"沒有共同衡量方法，比較太陽能、天然氣和煤炭成本會令人混亂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a standard comparison tool.","zh":"這個短語描述標準化比較工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"electricity generation","meaning":"發電","examples":[{"en":"The cost of electricity generation varies by technology.","zh":"發電成本因技術而異。"},{"en":"Electricity generation is the production of electrical power from sources such as coal, gas, wind or sunlight.","zh":"發電是從煤、天然氣、風或陽光等來源產生電力。"},{"en":"A hydroelectric dam uses moving water for electricity generation.","zh":"水力發電壩利用流動水來發電。"},{"en":"If generation costs fall, electricity may become cheaper for consumers.","zh":"如果發電成本下降，消費者的電力可能變得更便宜。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to producing power before it reaches homes or businesses.","zh":"這個短語指電力到達家庭或企業前的生產過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"levelized cost of energy","meaning":"平準化能源成本","examples":[{"en":"The levelized cost of energy compares electricity costs over a plant’s lifetime.","zh":"平準化能源成本比較一座發電廠整個使用期內的電力成本。"},{"en":"The levelized cost of energy is a standard way to calculate the average cost of electricity from a power plant over its full life.","zh":"平準化能源成本是一種標準方法，用來計算發電廠整個壽命中的平均發電成本。"},{"en":"Energy planners use LCOE to compare solar farms, gas plants and coal plants fairly.","zh":"能源規劃者使用 LCOE 公平比較太陽能場、天然氣電廠和燃煤電廠。"},{"en":"If one technology has lower LCOE, it may be cheaper over the long term.","zh":"如果一種技術 LCOE 較低，它長遠可能較便宜。"},{"en":"The phrase is often shortened to LCOE.","zh":"這個短語常縮寫為 LCOE。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"average cost of producing electricity","meaning":"平均發電成本","examples":[{"en":"LCOE is the average cost of producing electricity over a power plant’s lifetime.","zh":"LCOE 是一座發電廠整個使用期內的平均發電成本。"},{"en":"Average cost of producing electricity means the typical cost per unit of power after all major costs are spread over time.","zh":"平均發電成本指把所有主要成本分攤到一段時間後，每單位電力的典型成本。"},{"en":"A family may calculate the average cost of meals by dividing grocery spending by the number of meals cooked.","zh":"家庭可能把買菜開支除以所煮餐數，計算每餐平均成本。"},{"en":"If construction costs are high, the average electricity cost may rise even if fuel is cheap.","zh":"如果建造成本高，即使燃料便宜，平均發電成本也可能上升。"},{"en":"The phrase helps compare different power technologies fairly.","zh":"這個短語幫助公平比較不同發電技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"over the lifetime of","meaning":"在……的整個使用期內","examples":[{"en":"The calculation covers costs over the lifetime of the power plant.","zh":"該計算涵蓋發電廠整個使用期內的成本。"},{"en":"Over the lifetime of something means during the whole period that it exists or operates.","zh":"在某物整個使用期內，指在它存在或運作的整段時間中。"},{"en":"A durable backpack may be cheaper over its lifetime than a low-quality one replaced every year.","zh":"耐用背包在整個使用期內，可能比每年更換的低質背包更便宜。"},{"en":"If a power plant lasts 30 years, costs must be judged across all those years.","zh":"如果發電廠可使用三十年，成本就必須跨越所有年份評估。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a long-term view of cost or performance.","zh":"這個短語給出成本或表現的長期視角。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"include construction, financing and operation","meaning":"包括建造、融資及營運","examples":[{"en":"LCOE calculations include construction, financing and operation.","zh":"LCOE 計算包括建造、融資及營運。"},{"en":"To include construction, financing and operation means to count building costs, borrowing costs and running costs together.","zh":"包括建造、融資及營運，指把建造成本、借貸成本和運作成本一起計算。"},{"en":"A school building budget should include construction, financing and operation, not just the price of bricks.","zh":"學校建築預算應包括建造、融資及營運，而不只是磚頭價格。"},{"en":"If all these costs are included, energy prices are compared more fairly.","zh":"如果所有這些成本都計算在內，能源價格比較就更公平。"},{"en":"The phrase lists the major cost categories in a project.","zh":"這個短語列出項目的主要成本類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"pollution is not counted","meaning":"污染成本不計算在內","examples":[{"en":"Pollution costs are not counted in the usual LCOE calculation.","zh":"污染成本不計算在通常的 LCOE 計算中。"},{"en":"If pollution is not counted, the environmental damage is left out of the cost calculation.","zh":"如果污染成本不計算在內，環境損害就被排除在成本計算之外。"},{"en":"A cheap product may seem cheaper if waste disposal is not counted.","zh":"如果廢物處理不計算在內，廉價產品可能看起來更便宜。"},{"en":"If coal power’s pollution is not counted, its true social cost may be underestimated.","zh":"如果燃煤電力污染成本不計算在內，其真實社會成本可能被低估。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that a price may exclude important hidden costs.","zh":"這個短語提醒某價格可能排除了重要隱藏成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"per kilowatt-hour","meaning":"每千瓦小時","examples":[{"en":"Electricity costs are often expressed per kilowatt-hour.","zh":"電力成本常以每千瓦小時表示。"},{"en":"Per kilowatt-hour means for each unit of electricity equal to one kilowatt used for one hour.","zh":"每千瓦小時指每一個電力單位，即一千瓦使用一小時。"},{"en":"A household electricity bill shows how many kilowatt-hours were used in a month.","zh":"家庭電費單顯示一個月使用了多少千瓦小時。"},{"en":"If power costs ten cents per kilowatt-hour, using more electricity directly increases the bill.","zh":"如果電力成本是每千瓦小時十仙，用電越多，帳單就直接增加。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard unit for comparing electricity prices.","zh":"這個短語是比較電價的標準單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"conventional natural-gas power plant","meaning":"傳統天然氣發電廠","examples":[{"en":"A conventional natural-gas power plant can produce relatively cheap electricity.","zh":"傳統天然氣發電廠可以生產相對廉價的電力。"},{"en":"A conventional natural-gas power plant is a standard power station that burns natural gas to generate electricity.","zh":"傳統天然氣發電廠是燃燒天然氣發電的標準發電站。"},{"en":"A city may use natural-gas plants when it needs flexible electricity supply.","zh":"城市需要彈性電力供應時，可能使用天然氣發電廠。"},{"en":"If natural gas prices are low, these plants may produce cheaper electricity than some alternatives.","zh":"如果天然氣價格低，這些發電廠可能比某些替代方案生產更便宜電力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to ordinary gas-based power generation without special capture systems.","zh":"這個短語指不設特殊捕集系統的普通天然氣發電。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"without CCS","meaning":"不設碳捕集與封存","examples":[{"en":"Natural-gas generation is cheaper when it operates without CCS.","zh":"天然氣發電在不設 CCS 時較便宜。"},{"en":"Without CCS means not using carbon capture and storage technology.","zh":"不設 CCS 指不使用碳捕集與封存技術。"},{"en":"A power plant without CCS may be cheaper to run but may emit more CO₂.","zh":"不設 CCS 的發電廠運作成本可能較低，但可能排放更多二氧化碳。"},{"en":"If carbon capture equipment is removed from the cost, electricity becomes less expensive.","zh":"如果成本中移除碳捕集設備，電力就變得較便宜。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts ordinary operation with operation using carbon capture.","zh":"這個短語把普通運作與使用碳捕集的運作作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the cheapest way to","meaning":"最便宜的……方法","examples":[{"en":"Natural gas may be the cheapest way to produce relatively clean energy.","zh":"天然氣可能是生產相對清潔能源最便宜的方法。"},{"en":"The cheapest way to do something is the method that costs the least.","zh":"做某事最便宜的方法，是成本最低的方法。"},{"en":"Taking the bus may be the cheapest way to get to school if taxis are expensive.","zh":"如果的士昂貴，乘巴士可能是上學最便宜的方法。"},{"en":"If natural gas is cheaper than CCS coal power, policymakers may choose it as a transition fuel.","zh":"如果天然氣比 CCS 燃煤電力便宜，政策制定者可能選它作為過渡燃料。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the lowest-cost option.","zh":"這個短語指出最低成本選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"solar-power costs","meaning":"太陽能成本","examples":[{"en":"Solar-power costs have fallen rapidly.","zh":"太陽能成本已迅速下降。"},{"en":"Solar-power costs are the costs of producing electricity from sunlight.","zh":"太陽能成本是從陽光生產電力的成本。"},{"en":"A school may consider solar panels if solar-power costs fall enough.","zh":"如果太陽能成本下降足夠多，學校可能考慮安裝太陽能板。"},{"en":"If solar power becomes cheaper, it can compete more strongly with coal and gas.","zh":"如果太陽能變得更便宜，它就能更有力地與煤和天然氣競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the price of solar electricity technology.","zh":"這個短語指太陽能發電技術的價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"fall rapidly","meaning":"迅速下降","examples":[{"en":"The price of solar electricity continues to fall rapidly.","zh":"太陽能電力價格繼續迅速下降。"},{"en":"To fall rapidly means to decrease quickly.","zh":"迅速下降指快速減少。"},{"en":"The price of old phone models may fall rapidly after a new model is released.","zh":"新型號手機推出後，舊型號手機價格可能迅速下降。"},{"en":"If solar costs fall rapidly, more households and businesses may adopt solar power.","zh":"如果太陽能成本迅速下降，更多家庭和企業可能採用太陽能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a fast downward trend.","zh":"這個短語描述快速向下趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"purchase agreement","meaning":"購電協議","examples":[{"en":"The electricity was supplied under a long-term purchase agreement.","zh":"該電力根據長期購電協議供應。"},{"en":"A purchase agreement is a contract in which one party agrees to buy something under set terms.","zh":"購買協議是一份合約，其中一方同意按既定條款購買某物。"},{"en":"A school may sign a purchase agreement with a food supplier for daily lunches.","zh":"學校可能與食物供應商簽訂購買協議，供應每日午餐。"},{"en":"If a solar plant has a long-term agreement, it can plan income more securely.","zh":"如果太陽能發電廠有長期協議，就能更穩定地規劃收入。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a formal buying contract.","zh":"這個短語指正式購買合約。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"large solar plant","meaning":"大型太陽能發電廠","examples":[{"en":"A large solar plant can supply electricity at a competitive price.","zh":"大型太陽能發電廠可以以具競爭力的價格供應電力。"},{"en":"A large solar plant is a big facility with many solar panels generating electricity.","zh":"大型太陽能發電廠是有許多太陽能板發電的大型設施。"},{"en":"A desert region may build a large solar plant because it receives strong sunlight.","zh":"沙漠地區可能建造大型太陽能發電廠，因為它接收強烈陽光。"},{"en":"If a solar plant is large enough, it can provide power to thousands of homes.","zh":"如果太陽能發電廠足夠大，就能為數千個家庭供電。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to utility-scale solar electricity production.","zh":"這個短語指公用事業規模的太陽能發電。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"review environmental projects","meaning":"評估環境項目","examples":[{"en":"Greentech Media reviews environmental and energy projects.","zh":"Greentech Media 評估環境和能源項目。"},{"en":"To review environmental projects means to examine and assess projects related to the environment or clean energy.","zh":"評估環境項目指檢視和評價與環境或清潔能源相關的項目。"},{"en":"A newspaper may review environmental projects to see whether they really reduce pollution.","zh":"報章可能評估環境項目，看它們是否真的減少污染。"},{"en":"If a project is reviewed by experts, its cost and performance can be compared more clearly.","zh":"如果項目由專家評估，其成本和表現就能更清楚比較。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evaluation, not simply description.","zh":"這個短語描述評價，而不只是描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"generate power for","meaning":"以……成本發電","examples":[{"en":"The solar project generates power for less than ten cents per kilowatt-hour.","zh":"該太陽能項目以每千瓦小時少於十仙的成本發電。"},{"en":"To generate power for a price means to produce electricity at that cost.","zh":"以某價格發電，指以該成本生產電力。"},{"en":"A wind farm may generate power for a lower price after construction costs fall.","zh":"建造成本下降後，風力發電場可能以較低價格發電。"},{"en":"If solar power is generated cheaply, it becomes more competitive with fossil fuels.","zh":"如果太陽能能廉價發電，它就更能與化石燃料競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase links electricity production with cost.","zh":"這個短語把電力生產與成本連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"while so much coal exists","meaning":"在仍有大量煤炭的情況下","examples":[{"en":"While so much coal remains available, an immediate transition may be difficult.","zh":"在仍有大量煤炭可用的情況下，立即轉型可能困難。"},{"en":"While so much coal exists means as long as large coal supplies are still present and usable.","zh":"在仍有大量煤炭的情況下，指只要大量煤炭供應仍存在並可使用。"},{"en":"While so much cheap plastic exists, shops may find it hard to move fully to reusable packaging.","zh":"在仍有大量廉價塑膠的情況下，商店可能難以完全轉向可重用包裝。"},{"en":"If coal is abundant and accessible, countries may resist switching quickly to cleaner energy.","zh":"如果煤炭充足且容易取得，國家可能抗拒迅速轉向較清潔能源。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a practical obstacle caused by resource availability.","zh":"這個短語引出由資源可得性造成的實際障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"decommission power plants","meaning":"使發電廠退役","examples":[{"en":"It may be unrealistic to decommission all coal-fired power plants immediately.","zh":"立即使所有燃煤發電廠退役可能不現實。"},{"en":"To decommission power plants means to formally shut them down and take them out of service.","zh":"使發電廠退役指正式關閉並停止使用它們。"},{"en":"A city may decommission an old bus depot when a new transport centre opens.","zh":"新交通中心開幕後，城市可能使舊巴士車廠退役。"},{"en":"If coal plants are decommissioned too quickly, electricity supply and jobs may be disrupted.","zh":"如果燃煤電廠太快退役，電力供應和職位可能受干擾。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to planned retirement of energy infrastructure.","zh":"這個短語指有計劃地淘汰能源基建。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be realistic","meaning":"實際可行","examples":[{"en":"Closing every coal plant in the near future may not be realistic.","zh":"在不久將來關閉每一座燃煤電廠可能並不實際可行。"},{"en":"To be realistic means to be practical and possible in real life.","zh":"實際可行指在現實生活中 practical 且可能做到。"},{"en":"Studying ten hours every night is not realistic for most students.","zh":"對大多數學生來說，每晚溫習十小時並不實際。"},{"en":"If energy demand is high, closing all coal plants immediately may be impossible.","zh":"如果能源需求高，立即關閉所有燃煤電廠可能不可能。"},{"en":"The phrase judges whether an idea can actually be done.","zh":"這個短語判斷想法是否真的能做到。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"whatever happens","meaning":"無論如何","examples":[{"en":"Whatever happens, societies will continue to demand affordable energy.","zh":"無論如何，社會都會繼續要求可負擔能源。"},{"en":"Whatever happens means no matter what situation develops.","zh":"“Whatever happens” 指無論情況如何發展。"},{"en":"Whatever happens in the exam, students should read the questions carefully.","zh":"無論考試發生甚麼，學生都應仔細閱讀題目。"},{"en":"Even if energy policy changes, people will still need power for homes, hospitals and transport.","zh":"即使能源政策改變，人們仍需要電力供家庭、醫院和交通使用。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a fact that remains true under different conditions.","zh":"這個短語引出在不同條件下仍然成立的事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the conundrum of","meaning":"……這個難題","examples":[{"en":"The conundrum of cheap power and clean air remains unresolved.","zh":"廉價電力與清潔空氣這個難題仍未解決。"},{"en":"The conundrum of something is a difficult problem or puzzle with no easy answer.","zh":"某事這個難題，是沒有簡單答案的困難問題或謎題。"},{"en":"The conundrum of homework is how to give useful practice without exhausting students.","zh":"功課這個難題，是如何提供有用練習而不令學生疲憊。"},{"en":"If society wants both low prices and low emissions, energy policy becomes complicated.","zh":"如果社會既想要低價格又想要低排放，能源政策就變得複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a difficult dilemma.","zh":"這個短語描述困難兩難局面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"remain unsolved","meaning":"仍未解決","examples":[{"en":"The conflict between low prices and low emissions may remain unsolved.","zh":"低價格與低排放之間的衝突可能仍未解決。"},{"en":"To remain unsolved means to continue without a clear solution.","zh":"仍未解決指繼續沒有清楚解決方法。"},{"en":"A classroom seating problem may remain unsolved if students keep arguing about where to sit.","zh":"如果學生持續爭論坐位安排，課室座位問題可能仍未解決。"},{"en":"If no technology can provide clean and cheap power at once, the energy problem remains unsolved.","zh":"如果沒有技術能同時提供清潔又廉價電力，能源問題就仍未解決。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an issue that is still unresolved.","zh":"這個短語描述尚未處理好的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for each multiple-choice question.","zh":"考生為每道選擇題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option marked by the right letter.","zh":"選出正確字母指選擇由正確字母標示的答案選項。"},{"en":"Students should read all options before choosing the correct letter.","zh":"學生應閱讀所有選項後才選出正確字母。"},{"en":"If two choices look similar, evidence from the passage should decide the answer.","zh":"如果兩個選項看似相似，文章證據應決定答案。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard instruction in reading tests.","zh":"這個短語是閱讀測驗中的標準指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"global average for","meaning":"……的全球平均水平","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for the global average for electricity generated from coal.","zh":"題目問燃煤發電所佔的全球平均水平。"},{"en":"The global average for something is the worldwide average figure for that item.","zh":"某事的全球平均水平，是該項目在全世界的平均數字。"},{"en":"A report may give the global average for daily screen time among teenagers.","zh":"報告可能提供青少年每日螢幕時間的全球平均水平。"},{"en":"If a country is above the global average for coal electricity, it relies on coal more than most places.","zh":"如果一個國家燃煤電力高於全球平均水平，它比大多數地方更依賴煤。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for a worldwide comparison figure.","zh":"這個短語要求找出全球比較數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"electricity generated from coal","meaning":"燃煤產生的電力","examples":[{"en":"Many countries still rely heavily on electricity generated from coal.","zh":"許多國家仍高度依賴燃煤產生的電力。"},{"en":"Electricity generated from coal is electrical power produced by burning coal.","zh":"燃煤產生的電力，是透過燃燒煤炭生產的電能。"},{"en":"A household may not realise that its lights are powered by electricity generated from coal.","zh":"家庭可能不知道自己的燈光是由燃煤產生的電力供應。"},{"en":"If electricity comes from coal, its carbon emissions are usually high.","zh":"如果電力來自煤，其碳排放通常很高。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the fuel source behind electricity.","zh":"這個短語指出電力背後的燃料來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"average American household","meaning":"一般美國家庭","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to what an average American household pays each month.","zh":"題目指一般美國家庭每月支付甚麼。"},{"en":"An average American household means a typical family or home in the United States.","zh":"一般美國家庭指美國典型家庭或住戶。"},{"en":"An average American household may use electricity for heating, cooling, cooking and appliances.","zh":"一般美國家庭可能用電供暖、製冷、煮食和使用電器。"},{"en":"If average bills rise, many ordinary families may feel financial pressure.","zh":"如果平均帳單上升，許多普通家庭可能感到財政壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a representative household, not every individual family.","zh":"這個短語指具代表性的家庭，而不是每個個別家庭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"pay each month for","meaning":"每月為……付款","examples":[{"en":"Consumers pay each month for electricity but not directly for carbon emissions.","zh":"消費者每月為電力付款，但不會直接為碳排放付款。"},{"en":"To pay each month for something means to make regular monthly payments for it.","zh":"每月為某事付款，指為它作出定期每月付款。"},{"en":"Many families pay each month for rent, phone service and electricity.","zh":"許多家庭每月為租金、電話服務和電力付款。"},{"en":"If people pay for electricity but not pollution, environmental costs remain hidden.","zh":"如果人們為電力付款但不為污染付款，環境成本就仍被隱藏。"},{"en":"The phrase describes monthly financial responsibility.","zh":"這個短語描述每月財務責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be produced by","meaning":"由……產生","examples":[{"en":"Carbon dioxide is produced by a local power plant.","zh":"二氧化碳由本地發電廠產生。"},{"en":"To be produced by something means to be made, created or generated by that source.","zh":"由某物產生，指由該來源製造、創造或生成。"},{"en":"The school newsletter is produced by a group of student editors.","zh":"學校通訊由一群學生編輯製作。"},{"en":"If CO₂ is produced by a power plant, that plant is part of the emissions problem.","zh":"如果二氧化碳由發電廠產生，該發電廠就是排放問題的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who or what creates something.","zh":"這個短語指出誰或甚麼創造某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"local power plant","meaning":"本地發電廠","examples":[{"en":"A local power plant may emit millions of tonnes of carbon dioxide.","zh":"本地發電廠可能排放數百萬噸二氧化碳。"},{"en":"A local power plant is a nearby facility that generates electricity for an area.","zh":"本地發電廠是為某地區發電的附近設施。"},{"en":"Residents may live near a local power plant without seeing the emissions it produces.","zh":"居民可能住在本地發電廠附近，卻看不到它產生的排放。"},{"en":"If the local plant burns coal, the community may depend on electricity that creates pollution.","zh":"如果本地電廠燃燒煤炭，社區可能依賴會造成污染的電力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a power station serving or located near a community.","zh":"這個短語指服務或位於某社區附近的發電站。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"label the diagrams","meaning":"標示圖表","examples":[{"en":"Candidates label the diagrams using terms from the list.","zh":"考生使用列表中的詞語標示圖表。"},{"en":"To label the diagrams means to put the correct words or letters on parts of the pictures.","zh":"標示圖表指把正確詞語或字母放在圖片的各部分上。"},{"en":"In biology class, students label diagrams of the heart and lungs.","zh":"在生物課中，學生標示心臟和肺部圖。"},{"en":"If a diagram has arrows and boxes, labels help identify each part or process.","zh":"如果圖表有箭嘴和方框，標籤有助識別各部分或過程。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction for visual information.","zh":"這個短語是視覺資料題中的常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"carbon-dioxide sequestration","meaning":"二氧化碳封存","examples":[{"en":"The diagram illustrates several methods of carbon-dioxide sequestration.","zh":"該圖表說明幾種二氧化碳封存方法。"},{"en":"Carbon-dioxide sequestration is the storage of CO₂ so it does not enter the atmosphere.","zh":"二氧化碳封存是儲存二氧化碳，使其不進入大氣。"},{"en":"A diagram of sequestration may show CO₂ being sent into oil fields or deep aquifers.","zh":"二氧化碳封存圖可能顯示二氧化碳被送入油田或深層含水層。"},{"en":"If sequestration works, carbon dioxide is kept away from the air for a long time.","zh":"如果封存有效，二氧化碳會長期遠離空氣。"},{"en":"The phrase is another way to describe CO₂ storage.","zh":"這個短語是描述二氧化碳儲存的另一種說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"correct letter","meaning":"正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Each diagram label must be matched with the correct letter.","zh":"每個圖表標籤必須與正確字母配對。"},{"en":"The correct letter is the answer choice that matches the information accurately.","zh":"正確字母是準確配合資料的答案選項。"},{"en":"In a matching question, students may choose the correct letter after locating the evidence in the passage.","zh":"在配對題中，學生可能在文章中找到證據後選擇正確字母。"},{"en":"If the wrong letter is written, the answer may be marked incorrect even if the idea is close.","zh":"如果寫錯字母，即使意思接近，答案也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the exact option required in an exam.","zh":"這個短語指考試中要求的準確選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"saline aquifer","meaning":"鹽水含水層","examples":[{"en":"A saline aquifer may be used for underground carbon storage.","zh":"鹽水含水層可能用於地下碳儲存。"},{"en":"A saline aquifer is an underground layer of rock that contains salty water.","zh":"鹽水含水層是含有鹹水的地下岩層。"},{"en":"Engineers may test a saline aquifer to see whether it can safely hold injected CO₂.","zh":"工程師可能測試鹽水含水層，看它能否安全容納注入的二氧化碳。"},{"en":"If the aquifer is deep and sealed, it may prevent carbon dioxide from escaping.","zh":"如果含水層夠深且密封，它可能防止二氧化碳逃出。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to one possible geological storage site.","zh":"這個短語指一種可能的地質儲存地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"syngas-driven turbines","meaning":"合成氣驅動渦輪機","examples":[{"en":"Syngas-driven turbines form the first stage of an IGCC system.","zh":"合成氣驅動渦輪機構成 IGCC 系統的第一階段。"},{"en":"Syngas-driven turbines are turbines powered by synthetic gas.","zh":"合成氣驅動渦輪機是由合成氣推動的渦輪機。"},{"en":"A power plant may use syngas-driven turbines before using waste heat to create steam.","zh":"發電廠可能先使用合成氣驅動渦輪機，再利用廢熱產生蒸汽。"},{"en":"If syngas drives turbines efficiently, the plant can produce electricity from gasified coal.","zh":"如果合成氣有效推動渦輪機，電廠就能從氣化煤中發電。"},{"en":"The phrase names a turbine stage in advanced coal power generation.","zh":"這個短語指出先進燃煤發電中的一個渦輪階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"complete the table below","meaning":"完成下表","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the table with information from the passage.","zh":"考生用文章資料完成下表。"},{"en":"Complete the table below means fill in missing information in the table printed under the question.","zh":"完成下表指填寫題目下方表格中的缺漏資料。"},{"en":"Students should check column headings before completing a table.","zh":"學生完成表格前應先查看欄目標題。"},{"en":"If the answer must come from the passage, copying the exact word may be necessary.","zh":"如果答案必須來自文章，可能需要抄寫準確詞語。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction in reading tests.","zh":"這個短語是閱讀測驗中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"no more than three words and/or a number","meaning":"不多於三個字及／或一個數字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer must contain no more than three words and/or a number.","zh":"每個答案必須包含不多於三個字及／或一個數字。"},{"en":"No more than three words and/or a number means the answer may include up to three words, plus a number if needed.","zh":"不多於三個字及／或一個數字，指答案最多可包含三個詞，如有需要可加一個數字。"},{"en":"“three barrels” fits because it contains a number and one word.","zh":"“three barrels” 符合要求，因為它包含一個數字和一個詞。"},{"en":"If students write too many words, the answer may be marked wrong.","zh":"如果學生寫太多詞，答案可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict answer-length rule.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格答案長度規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"advantages of CCS","meaning":"碳捕集與封存的優點","examples":[{"en":"The table compares the advantages of CCS with its disadvantages.","zh":"該表比較碳捕集與封存的優點和缺點。"},{"en":"Advantages of CCS are the possible benefits of using carbon capture and storage.","zh":"碳捕集與封存的優點，是使用 CCS 的可能好處。"},{"en":"One advantage of CCS is that it may reduce emissions from existing coal plants.","zh":"CCS 的一個優點是它可能減少現有燃煤電廠的排放。"},{"en":"If CCS protects some industrial jobs while cutting carbon, supporters may see it as useful.","zh":"如果 CCS 在減碳同時保護部分工業職位，支持者可能認為它有用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the positive side of this technology.","zh":"這個短語指這項技術的正面部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"disadvantages of CCS","meaning":"碳捕集與封存的缺點","examples":[{"en":"High cost is one of the major disadvantages of CCS.","zh":"高成本是碳捕集與封存的主要缺點之一。"},{"en":"Disadvantages of CCS are the problems, risks or costs connected with using carbon capture and storage.","zh":"碳捕集與封存的缺點，是與使用 CCS 相關的問題、風險或成本。"},{"en":"A disadvantage of CCS is that captured CO₂ must be transported and stored safely.","zh":"CCS 的一個缺點是捕集到的二氧化碳必須被安全運輸和儲存。"},{"en":"If the disadvantages are too serious, governments may choose other clean-energy options.","zh":"如果缺點太嚴重，政府可能選擇其他清潔能源選項。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the negative side of this technology.","zh":"這個短語指這項技術的負面部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the oil and gas sector","meaning":"石油及天然氣行業","examples":[{"en":"Sequestration is already used in the oil and gas sector.","zh":"封存已在石油及天然氣行業中使用。"},{"en":"The oil and gas sector is the part of the economy that extracts, processes and sells oil and natural gas.","zh":"石油及天然氣行業是經濟中開採、加工和銷售石油及天然氣的部分。"},{"en":"Workers in the oil and gas sector may include drillers, engineers, chemists and pipeline operators.","zh":"石油及天然氣行業的工人可能包括鑽探工人、工程師、化學家和管道操作員。"},{"en":"If CCS technology benefits this sector, industry support may increase.","zh":"如果 CCS 技術有利於該行業，業界支持可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to one branch of the energy industry.","zh":"這個短語指能源行業的一個分支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"cut emissions in a short time","meaning":"在短時間內減排","examples":[{"en":"Supporters argue that CCS could cut emissions in a short time.","zh":"支持者認為 CCS 可以在短時間內減排。"},{"en":"To cut emissions in a short time means to reduce pollution quickly.","zh":"在短時間內減排指迅速減少污染。"},{"en":"A city can cut emissions in a short time by replacing diesel buses with electric buses.","zh":"城市可以透過以電動巴士取代柴油巴士，在短時間內減排。"},{"en":"If climate targets are urgent, quick reductions become politically attractive.","zh":"如果氣候目標迫切，快速減排就變得具政治吸引力。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses speed in reducing pollution.","zh":"這個短語強調減少污染的速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"support CCS","meaning":"支持碳捕集與封存","examples":[{"en":"Powerful groups in labour, industry and government support CCS.","zh":"勞工、工業和政府中的強大團體支持碳捕集與封存。"},{"en":"To support CCS means to approve of or promote carbon capture and storage.","zh":"支持 CCS 指認可或推動碳捕集與封存。"},{"en":"A trade union may support CCS if it believes the technology protects industrial jobs.","zh":"如果工會相信這項技術能保護工業職位，可能支持 CCS。"},{"en":"If government and industry both support CCS, funding may become easier to obtain.","zh":"如果政府和業界都支持 CCS，資金可能更容易取得。"},{"en":"The phrase describes backing for a particular climate technology.","zh":"這個短語描述對某項氣候技術的支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"take up vast amounts of space","meaning":"佔用大量空間","examples":[{"en":"Some renewable-energy alternatives take up vast amounts of space.","zh":"一些可再生能源替代方案佔用大量空間。"},{"en":"To take up vast amounts of space means to occupy a very large area.","zh":"佔用大量空間指佔據非常大面積。"},{"en":"A festival can take up vast amounts of space if stalls, stages and crowds fill an entire park.","zh":"如果攤位、舞台和人群填滿整個公園，節日活動可以佔用大量空間。"},{"en":"If solar farms require huge land areas, space becomes a serious planning issue.","zh":"如果太陽能場需要巨大土地面積，空間就成為嚴重規劃問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large land-use requirement.","zh":"這個短語描述大型土地使用需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"converting existing plants","meaning":"改裝現有發電廠","examples":[{"en":"Converting existing plants to CCS is extremely expensive.","zh":"把現有發電廠改裝為 CCS 極其昂貴。"},{"en":"Converting existing plants means changing current power stations so they can use a new system or technology.","zh":"改裝現有發電廠，指改變目前發電站，使其能使用新系統或技術。"},{"en":"A school may convert an existing classroom into a computer room.","zh":"學校可能把現有課室改裝成電腦室。"},{"en":"If power plants are converted to CCS, they need new equipment, pipes and storage links.","zh":"如果發電廠改裝為 CCS，就需要新設備、管道和儲存連接。"},{"en":"The phrase describes modifying what already exists.","zh":"這個短語描述修改已有事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"liquefy and transport CO₂","meaning":"液化及運輸二氧化碳","examples":[{"en":"It is costly to liquefy and transport captured CO₂.","zh":"液化及運輸捕集到的二氧化碳成本高昂。"},{"en":"To liquefy and transport CO₂ means to compress carbon dioxide into a liquid-like state and move it elsewhere.","zh":"液化及運輸二氧化碳，指把二氧化碳壓縮成類似液體狀態並運到其他地方。"},{"en":"Factories liquefy and transport some gases so they can be stored in tanks.","zh":"工廠會液化及運輸某些氣體，以便把它們儲存在罐中。"},{"en":"If CO₂ must be liquefied and moved long distances, the whole CCS system becomes more expensive.","zh":"如果二氧化碳必須液化並長距離運輸，整個 CCS 系統會更昂貴。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a technical step after capture.","zh":"這個短語描述捕集後的一個技術步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the scale of sequestration","meaning":"碳封存的規模","examples":[{"en":"The scale of sequestration would be enormous.","zh":"碳封存的規模會非常巨大。"},{"en":"The scale of sequestration means the size or amount of carbon storage required.","zh":"碳封存的規模，指所需碳儲存的大小或數量。"},{"en":"The scale of recycling in a large city is far greater than in a small school.","zh":"大城市的回收規模遠大於小學校。"},{"en":"If billions of tonnes of CO₂ must be stored, the scale becomes a major challenge.","zh":"如果必須儲存數十億噸二氧化碳，規模就成為重大挑戰。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how large the storage operation must be.","zh":"這個短語強調儲存行動必須有多大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"require vast storage capacity","meaning":"需要龐大儲存容量","examples":[{"en":"Large-scale CCS would require vast underground storage capacity.","zh":"大規模 CCS 需要龐大地下儲存容量。"},{"en":"To require vast storage capacity means to need an extremely large amount of space for storage.","zh":"需要龐大儲存容量，指需要極大量儲存空間。"},{"en":"A city library requires storage capacity for books, archives and digital records.","zh":"城市圖書館需要儲存容量放置書籍、檔案和電子紀錄。"},{"en":"If CCS captures huge amounts of CO₂, underground space must be large and secure.","zh":"如果 CCS 捕集大量二氧化碳，地下空間必須巨大且安全。"},{"en":"The phrase links project size with storage needs.","zh":"這個短語把項目規模與儲存需要連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"untested technology","meaning":"未經測試的技術","examples":[{"en":"Some CCS technology remains untested.","zh":"一些 CCS 技術仍未經測試。"},{"en":"Untested technology is technology that has not yet been tried enough to prove it works safely and reliably.","zh":"未經測試的技術，是尚未經足夠試驗來證明其安全可靠的技術。"},{"en":"A hospital will not use untested equipment on patients without careful trials.","zh":"醫院不會在沒有仔細試驗下把未經測試的設備用於病人。"},{"en":"If a power system is untested, investors and the public may worry about failure.","zh":"如果發電系統未經測試，投資者和公眾可能擔心失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights uncertainty and risk.","zh":"這個短語突出不確定性和風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"earthquake-prone regions","meaning":"地震多發地區","examples":[{"en":"Storing carbon underground may be risky in earthquake-prone regions.","zh":"在地震多發地區，把碳儲存在地下可能有風險。"},{"en":"Earthquake-prone regions are areas where earthquakes happen relatively often.","zh":"地震多發地區是地震相對經常發生的地區。"},{"en":"Buildings in earthquake-prone regions need stronger designs and emergency plans.","zh":"地震多發地區的建築需要更堅固設計和緊急計劃。"},{"en":"If stored CO₂ lies under unstable ground, earthquakes could damage storage formations.","zh":"如果封存二氧化碳位於不穩定地下，地震可能破壞儲存地層。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies places with higher seismic risk.","zh":"這個短語指出地震風險較高的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"fear leaks","meaning":"擔心洩漏","examples":[{"en":"Geologists fear leaks from unstable underground formations.","zh":"地質學家擔心不穩定地下地層發生洩漏。"},{"en":"To fear leaks means to worry that stored gas or liquid may escape.","zh":"擔心洩漏指憂慮儲存的氣體或液體可能逃出。"},{"en":"A homeowner may fear leaks if water stains appear on the ceiling.","zh":"如果天花板出現水漬，業主可能擔心漏水。"},{"en":"If geologists fear CO₂ leaks, they may oppose storage in weak rock formations.","zh":"如果地質學家擔心二氧化碳洩漏，他們可能反對在脆弱岩層中儲存。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses concern about unwanted escape.","zh":"這個短語表達對不希望出現的逃逸的關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"natural gas and solar PV","meaning":"天然氣與太陽能光伏","examples":[{"en":"Natural gas and solar PV may produce cheaper electricity than CCS.","zh":"天然氣與太陽能光伏可能比 CCS 生產更便宜的電力。"},{"en":"Natural gas and solar PV are two energy options: one burns gas, and the other uses photovoltaic cells to convert sunlight into electricity.","zh":"天然氣與太陽能光伏是兩種能源選項：一種燃燒氣體，另一種用光伏電池把陽光轉成電力。"},{"en":"A government may compare natural gas and solar PV when planning future power supply.","zh":"政府規劃未來電力供應時，可能比較天然氣與太陽能光伏。"},{"en":"If both options cost less than CCS, they may become more attractive alternatives.","zh":"如果兩者成本都低於 CCS，它們可能成為更吸引的替代方案。"},{"en":"The phrase names two competing power-generation choices.","zh":"這個短語指出兩種互相競爭的發電選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"LCOE estimates","meaning":"平準化能源成本估算","examples":[{"en":"LCOE estimates allow different energy systems to be compared.","zh":"平準化能源成本估算讓不同能源系統可以被比較。"},{"en":"LCOE estimates are calculations of average electricity cost over a power plant’s lifetime.","zh":"平準化能源成本估算是計算發電廠整個使用期內平均電力成本的方法。"},{"en":"Energy planners use LCOE estimates to compare solar, gas, coal and CCS projects.","zh":"能源規劃者使用 LCOE 估算比較太陽能、天然氣、煤和 CCS 項目。"},{"en":"If LCOE estimates exclude pollution costs, they may understate the true cost of fossil fuels.","zh":"如果 LCOE 估算排除污染成本，它們可能低估化石燃料的真實成本。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to cost comparisons based on levelized energy cost.","zh":"這個短語指基於平準化能源成本的成本比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 133 - Carbon Capture and Storage.pdf","sourcePage":21}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 134":[{"front":"global warming","meaning":"全球暖化","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses conflicting views about the causes of global warming.","zh":"文章討論關於全球暖化成因的不同觀點。"},{"en":"Global warming means the long-term rise in the Earth’s average temperature.","zh":"global warming 指地球平均氣溫長期上升。"},{"en":"Students often learn about global warming when studying extreme weather and rising sea levels.","zh":"學生在學習極端天氣和海平面上升時，常會學到全球暖化。"},{"en":"If greenhouse gases increase in the atmosphere, global warming may become more serious.","zh":"如果大氣中的溫室氣體增加，全球暖化可能變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing climate change on a worldwide scale.","zh":"這個片語用於討論全球尺度的氣候變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"day after day","meaning":"日復一日","examples":[{"en":"Day after day, the public hears warnings about global warming.","zh":"日復一日，公眾聽到關於全球暖化的警告。"},{"en":"Day after day means repeatedly every day over a period of time.","zh":"day after day 指在一段時間內每天反覆發生。"},{"en":"Day after day, commuters wait for the same delayed bus.","zh":"日復一日，通勤者等待同一班延誤的巴士。"},{"en":"If people hear the same warning day after day, they may become worried or tired of it.","zh":"如果人們日復一日聽到同一警告，他們可能變得憂慮或厭倦。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses repetition over many days.","zh":"這個片語強調多天重複發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"anthropogenic development","meaning":"人為發展活動","examples":[{"en":"Some experts argue that anthropogenic development is warming the planet.","zh":"一些專家認為人為發展活動正在令地球變暖。"},{"en":"Anthropogenic development means human-made growth or activity, such as industry, transport, and urban expansion.","zh":"anthropogenic development 指由人類造成的發展或活動，例如工業、交通和城市擴張。"},{"en":"Building roads, factories, and power stations are examples of anthropogenic development.","zh":"建造道路、工廠和發電站都是人為發展活動的例子。"},{"en":"If anthropogenic development releases large amounts of carbon dioxide, it can affect the climate.","zh":"如果人為發展活動釋放大量二氧化碳，它可能影響氣候。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and means development caused by human beings.","zh":"這個片語較正式，意思是由人類造成的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cause global warming","meaning":"導致全球暖化","examples":[{"en":"Human activity may be causing global warming.","zh":"人類活動可能正在導致全球暖化。"},{"en":"To cause global warming means to make the Earth’s average temperature rise over time.","zh":"cause global warming 指令地球平均氣溫隨時間上升。"},{"en":"Burning coal and oil can cause global warming by releasing greenhouse gases.","zh":"燃燒煤和石油可以透過釋放溫室氣體導致全球暖化。"},{"en":"If more cars use petrol every day, their emissions may add to warming.","zh":"如果每天有更多汽車使用汽油，其排放可能加劇暖化。"},{"en":"This phrase links an action or factor with climate change.","zh":"這個片語把某行動或因素與氣候變化連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"increasingly vocal minority","meaning":"越來越敢於發聲的少數派","examples":[{"en":"An increasingly vocal minority questions the accepted explanation.","zh":"越來越敢於發聲的少數派質疑被接受的解釋。"},{"en":"An increasingly vocal minority is a small group of people who are speaking out more strongly over time.","zh":"increasingly vocal minority 指一小群人隨時間更強烈地公開表達意見。"},{"en":"In a school, an increasingly vocal minority of parents may oppose a new uniform rule.","zh":"在學校中，越來越敢於發聲的少數家長可能反對新校服規則。"},{"en":"If a minority becomes more vocal, public debate can become louder even if most people disagree.","zh":"如果少數派變得更敢於發聲，即使大多數人不同意，公共爭論也可能變得更激烈。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small but noticeable group expressing strong views.","zh":"這個片語描述一個細小但明顯、強烈表達意見的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ask ourselves","meaning":"問問自己","examples":[{"en":"We should ask ourselves whether every media claim is supported by evidence.","zh":"我們應問問自己，每個傳媒說法是否都有證據支持。"},{"en":"To ask ourselves something means to think carefully and honestly about a question.","zh":"ask ourselves something 指認真而誠實地思考某個問題。"},{"en":"Before buying an expensive course, students should ask themselves whether they really need it.","zh":"學生在購買昂貴課程前，應問問自己是否真的需要它。"},{"en":"If people ask themselves difficult questions, they may avoid accepting weak arguments too quickly.","zh":"如果人們問自己困難問題，就可能避免太快接受薄弱論點。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages reflection and self-questioning.","zh":"這個片語鼓勵反思和自我提問。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"how much of this","meaning":"這當中有多少","examples":[{"en":"We need to consider how much of this is based on reliable evidence.","zh":"我們需要考慮這當中有多少是建基於可靠證據。"},{"en":"How much of this asks what proportion of something is true, useful, or supported.","zh":"how much of this 問某事有多少比例是真實、有用或有支持的。"},{"en":"After hearing a rumour, a teacher may ask how much of this is fact and how much is exaggeration.","zh":"聽到謠言後，老師可能問這當中有多少是事實，有多少是誇張。"},{"en":"If only a small part is evidence-based, people should be cautious.","zh":"如果只有很小部分以證據為基礎，人們就應謹慎。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate reliable information from noise.","zh":"這個片語幫助把可靠資訊與雜音分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"media hype","meaning":"傳媒炒作","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe that reports of global warming involve media hype.","zh":"有些人認為全球暖化報道涉及傳媒炒作。"},{"en":"Media hype means exaggerated attention or excitement created by newspapers, television, or online platforms.","zh":"media hype 指報章、電視或網上平台製造的誇張關注或興奮情緒。"},{"en":"A new phone may receive media hype before anyone has tested it properly.","zh":"一部新手機可能在任何人正式測試前已受到傳媒炒作。"},{"en":"If media hype grows, people may become excited or frightened before checking evidence.","zh":"如果傳媒炒作增加，人們可能在查核證據前已變得興奮或害怕。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that publicity may be stronger than the facts justify.","zh":"這個片語暗示宣傳程度可能超出事實所支持的程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be based on real evidence","meaning":"以真實證據為基礎","examples":[{"en":"Scientific claims should be based on real evidence.","zh":"科學主張應以真實證據為基礎。"},{"en":"To be based on real evidence means to rely on facts, data, or observations rather than guesses.","zh":"be based on real evidence 指依靠事實、數據或觀察，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"A doctor’s diagnosis should be based on real evidence from tests and symptoms.","zh":"醫生的診斷應以測試和症狀中的真實證據為基礎。"},{"en":"If a claim is not based on evidence, it may sound convincing but still be wrong.","zh":"如果主張不是以證據為基礎，它可能聽起來有說服力但仍然錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the need for factual support.","zh":"這個片語強調需要事實支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as is so often the case","meaning":"正如經常出現的情況","examples":[{"en":"As is so often the case, different experts give different answers.","zh":"正如經常出現的情況，不同專家給出不同答案。"},{"en":"As is so often the case means as happens frequently in similar situations.","zh":"as is so often the case 指如同類似情況中經常發生的一樣。"},{"en":"As is so often the case, students learn faster when examples are clear.","zh":"正如經常出現的情況，例子清楚時學生學得更快。"},{"en":"When evidence is complex, experts often disagree about its meaning.","zh":"當證據複雜時，專家常對其意思意見不一。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces something familiar or commonly seen.","zh":"這個片語引入熟悉或常見的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"depend on","meaning":"取決於……","examples":[{"en":"The conclusion may depend on which statistics are examined.","zh":"結論可能取決於檢視哪些統計數據。"},{"en":"To depend on something means to be affected or decided by it.","zh":"depend on something 指受某事影響或由某事決定。"},{"en":"A student’s study plan may depend on the exam date and available time.","zh":"學生的溫習計劃可能取決於考試日期和可用時間。"},{"en":"If the answer depends on the data chosen, people may reach different conclusions.","zh":"如果答案取決於所選數據，人們可能得出不同結論。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one thing changes according to another.","zh":"這個片語顯示一件事會按另一件事而改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"which expert you listen to","meaning":"你聽取哪位專家的意見","examples":[{"en":"Your opinion may depend on which expert you listen to.","zh":"你的看法可能取決於你聽取哪位專家的意見。"},{"en":"Which expert you listen to means whose professional view you choose to trust.","zh":"which expert you listen to 指你選擇相信哪位專業人士的看法。"},{"en":"Patients may feel confused if different doctors give different advice.","zh":"如果不同醫生給出不同建議，病人可能感到困惑。"},{"en":"If experts disagree, choosing one source over another can shape your conclusion.","zh":"如果專家意見不一，選擇一個來源而非另一個會塑造你的結論。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds learners that expert opinion is not always uniform.","zh":"這個片語提醒學習者，專家意見並不總是一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"which statistics you study","meaning":"你研究哪些統計數據","examples":[{"en":"The answer can depend on which statistics you study.","zh":"答案可能取決於你研究哪些統計數據。"},{"en":"Which statistics you study means which sets of numerical data you choose to examine.","zh":"which statistics you study 指你選擇檢視哪些數字數據。"},{"en":"A school may look better or worse depending on which exam statistics are studied.","zh":"一所學校看起來較好或較差，可能取決於研究哪些考試統計數據。"},{"en":"If one person studies long-term data and another studies one year, their views may differ.","zh":"如果一人研究長期數據，另一人只研究一年，他們看法可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that data selection can affect conclusions.","zh":"這個片語顯示數據選擇可以影響結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a mass of evidence","meaning":"大量證據","examples":[{"en":"There is a mass of evidence indicating that the world is warming.","zh":"有大量證據顯示全球正在變暖。"},{"en":"A mass of evidence means a large amount of proof, data, or support.","zh":"a mass of evidence 指大量證明、數據或支持材料。"},{"en":"Police may need a mass of evidence before charging someone with a serious crime.","zh":"警方在控告某人嚴重罪行前，可能需要大量證據。"},{"en":"If many studies point in the same direction, a mass of evidence becomes hard to ignore.","zh":"如果許多研究都指向同一方向，大量證據就難以忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the quantity of supporting material.","zh":"這個片語強調支持材料的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"evidence to indicate that","meaning":"顯示……的證據","examples":[{"en":"There is evidence to indicate that global temperatures have risen.","zh":"有證據顯示全球氣溫已經上升。"},{"en":"Evidence to indicate that means information showing that something is probably true.","zh":"evidence to indicate that 指顯示某事很可能是真實的資料。"},{"en":"There is evidence to indicate that regular reading improves vocabulary.","zh":"有證據顯示定期閱讀能改善詞彙量。"},{"en":"If several measurements show the same trend, they indicate a real change.","zh":"如果幾項量度顯示同一趨勢，它們就顯示真正變化。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces support for a claim.","zh":"這個片語引入支持某主張的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the world is getting warmer","meaning":"全球正在變暖","examples":[{"en":"Many measurements suggest that the world is getting warmer.","zh":"許多量度顯示全球正在變暖。"},{"en":"The world is getting warmer means the Earth’s average temperature is rising over time.","zh":"the world is getting warmer 指地球平均氣溫隨時間上升。"},{"en":"People may notice warmer winters, hotter summers, and earlier springs.","zh":"人們可能注意到冬天較暖、夏天較熱、春天較早來臨。"},{"en":"If the world gets warmer, ice may melt and weather patterns may shift.","zh":"如果全球變暖，冰可能融化，天氣模式可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broad climate trend.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛的氣候趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"leading weather forecaster","meaning":"領先的天氣預測機構","examples":[{"en":"A leading weather forecaster reported an increase in air temperatures.","zh":"一個領先的天氣預測機構報告氣溫上升。"},{"en":"A leading weather forecaster is an important organisation or expert that predicts and studies weather.","zh":"leading weather forecaster 是預測和研究天氣的重要機構或專家。"},{"en":"A leading weather forecaster may warn the public before a dangerous storm arrives.","zh":"領先的天氣預測機構可能在危險風暴到來前警告公眾。"},{"en":"If a respected forecaster reports a trend, people may take the data more seriously.","zh":"如果受尊敬的預報機構報告某趨勢，人們可能更認真看待數據。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a highly recognised weather authority.","zh":"這個片語指出具高度認受性的天氣權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"air temperatures","meaning":"氣溫","examples":[{"en":"Global air temperatures have increased since the early twentieth century.","zh":"自二十世紀初以來，全球氣溫已經上升。"},{"en":"Air temperatures are measurements of how hot or cold the air is.","zh":"air temperatures 是空氣有多熱或多冷的量度。"},{"en":"Weather apps show daily air temperatures so people know what to wear.","zh":"天氣應用程式顯示每日氣溫，讓人知道穿甚麼。"},{"en":"If air temperatures rise for many years, scientists may study long-term climate change.","zh":"如果氣溫多年上升，科學家可能研究長期氣候變化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to temperature measured in the atmosphere near the surface.","zh":"這個片語指接近地表大氣中的溫度量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"show an increase of","meaning":"顯示增加了……","examples":[{"en":"The records show an increase of nearly half a degree Celsius.","zh":"記錄顯示增加了接近攝氏半度。"},{"en":"To show an increase of an amount means to provide data showing that something has risen by that amount.","zh":"show an increase of an amount 指提供數據顯示某物上升了某數量。"},{"en":"The school report may show an increase of ten students in the reading club.","zh":"學校報告可能顯示閱讀學會增加了十名學生。"},{"en":"If records show an increase, researchers can compare it with earlier levels.","zh":"如果記錄顯示增加，研究人員可以把它與早期水平比較。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a measured rise.","zh":"這個片語描述可量度的上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"just under","meaning":"略低於；不足","examples":[{"en":"The measured rise was just under half a degree Celsius.","zh":"量得的升幅略低於攝氏半度。"},{"en":"Just under means slightly less than a stated amount.","zh":"just under 指比某個數量稍微少一點。"},{"en":"The train journey takes just under one hour.","zh":"火車旅程需時略低於一小時。"},{"en":"If a number is just under a limit, it is close to the limit but does not reach it.","zh":"如果數字略低於限制，它接近限制但未達到。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a near but slightly lower amount.","zh":"這個片語表示接近但稍低的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"half a degree Celsius","meaning":"攝氏半度","examples":[{"en":"The recorded increase was close to half a degree Celsius.","zh":"記錄到的升幅接近攝氏半度。"},{"en":"Half a degree Celsius means 0.5°C, a small temperature unit that may still matter in climate science.","zh":"half a degree Celsius 指0.5°C，是一個小溫度單位，但在氣候科學中仍可能重要。"},{"en":"A fever thermometer may show a change of half a degree Celsius between morning and evening.","zh":"體溫計可能顯示早晚之間有攝氏半度變化。"},{"en":"In climate discussions, even half a degree can affect ice, storms, and heatwaves.","zh":"在氣候討論中，即使攝氏半度也可能影響冰、風暴和熱浪。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a specific temperature amount.","zh":"這個片語給出特定溫度數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"since the beginning of","meaning":"自……開始以來","examples":[{"en":"Temperatures have risen since the beginning of the twentieth century.","zh":"自二十世紀開始以來，氣溫已經上升。"},{"en":"Since the beginning of a period means from the start of that period until now or another later time.","zh":"since the beginning of a period 指由某段時期開始直至現在或之後某時間。"},{"en":"The school has used tablets since the beginning of this academic year.","zh":"自本學年開始以來，學校一直使用平板電腦。"},{"en":"If a trend continues since the beginning of a century, it covers many decades.","zh":"如果一個趨勢自某世紀開始以來持續，它就涵蓋許多十年。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a starting point in time.","zh":"這個片語標示時間起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"may not sound like","meaning":"聽起來可能不像……","examples":[{"en":"A small temperature rise may not sound like a serious problem.","zh":"小小氣溫上升聽起來可能不像嚴重問題。"},{"en":"May not sound like means may not seem to be something when first heard.","zh":"may not sound like 指初聽時可能不似某事。"},{"en":"Ten minutes of daily practice may not sound like much, but it can improve pronunciation.","zh":"每天十分鐘練習聽起來可能不多，但可以改善發音。"},{"en":"If a change sounds small, people may underestimate its long-term effect.","zh":"如果變化聽起來很小，人們可能低估其長遠影響。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast between first impression and real importance.","zh":"這個片語引入第一印象與真正重要性的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"worth losing sleep over","meaning":"值得令人憂心忡忡","examples":[{"en":"Half a degree may not seem worth losing sleep over.","zh":"攝氏半度可能看似不值得令人憂心忡忡。"},{"en":"Worth losing sleep over means serious enough to worry about deeply.","zh":"worth losing sleep over 指嚴重到值得深深擔心。"},{"en":"A spelling mistake in a casual message is not worth losing sleep over.","zh":"隨意訊息中的一個串字錯誤不值得令人憂心忡忡。"},{"en":"If a small risk can create huge future damage, it may be worth worrying about.","zh":"如果小風險可以造成巨大未來損害，它可能值得擔心。"},{"en":"This phrase usually appears in discussions about whether something deserves concern.","zh":"這個片語通常出現在討論某事是否值得憂慮時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"international press","meaning":"國際傳媒","examples":[{"en":"The international press frequently reports on climate change.","zh":"國際傳媒經常報道氣候變化。"},{"en":"The international press means newspapers, broadcasters, and news websites from many countries.","zh":"international press 指來自多個國家的報章、廣播機構和新聞網站。"},{"en":"The international press may cover major elections, wars, disasters, and scientific discoveries.","zh":"國際傳媒可能報道重大選舉、戰爭、災難和科學發現。"},{"en":"If the international press repeats a story often, people around the world notice it.","zh":"如果國際傳媒經常重複某故事，世界各地的人都會注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to global news media.","zh":"這個片語指全球新聞媒體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"would have us believe that","meaning":"試圖令我們相信","examples":[{"en":"The press would have us believe that the consequences will be devastating.","zh":"傳媒試圖令我們相信後果將會是災難性的。"},{"en":"Would have us believe that means tries to make us believe something, often with a hint of doubt.","zh":"would have us believe that 指試圖令我們相信某事，通常帶有一點懷疑意味。"},{"en":"Advertisements would have us believe that one drink can change our whole life.","zh":"廣告試圖令我們相信一杯飲品可以改變整個人生。"},{"en":"If someone would have us believe a dramatic claim, we should ask for evidence.","zh":"如果有人試圖令我們相信誇張主張，我們應要求證據。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests scepticism toward a message.","zh":"這個片語常暗示對訊息抱有懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"consequences could be devastating","meaning":"後果可能是災難性的","examples":[{"en":"Some reports warn that the consequences could be devastating.","zh":"一些報道警告後果可能是災難性的。"},{"en":"Consequences could be devastating means the results may cause very serious damage.","zh":"consequences could be devastating 指結果可能造成極嚴重破壞。"},{"en":"If a hospital loses electricity during surgery, the consequences could be devastating.","zh":"如果醫院在手術期間停電，後果可能是災難性的。"},{"en":"If climate change increases floods and droughts, communities may suffer greatly.","zh":"如果氣候變化增加洪水和乾旱，社群可能深受其害。"},{"en":"This phrase warns about possible severe outcomes.","zh":"這個片語警告可能出現嚴重後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be of the opinion that","meaning":"認為","examples":[{"en":"Other experts are of the opinion that the change is natural.","zh":"其他專家認為這種變化是自然的。"},{"en":"To be of the opinion that means to believe or think something.","zh":"be of the opinion that 指相信或認為某事。"},{"en":"Some teachers are of the opinion that students learn better through discussion.","zh":"一些老師認為學生透過討論學得更好。"},{"en":"If experts are of different opinions, readers should examine the evidence behind each view.","zh":"如果專家有不同意見，讀者應檢視每種觀點背後的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal way to express someone’s view.","zh":"這個片語是表達某人看法的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"natural upward and downward swing","meaning":"自然的上下波動","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists see the warming as part of a natural upward and downward swing.","zh":"一些科學家把暖化視為自然上下波動的一部分。"},{"en":"A natural upward and downward swing is a rise and fall that happens as part of nature’s normal pattern.","zh":"natural upward and downward swing 是自然正常模式中出現的上升和下降。"},{"en":"Shop sales may have upward and downward swings during holidays and quiet seasons.","zh":"店舖銷售在假期和淡季可能有上下波動。"},{"en":"If temperature changes are part of a natural swing, they may not be caused mainly by humans.","zh":"如果氣溫變化屬於自然波動，它們可能不是主要由人類造成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated natural movement up and down.","zh":"這個片語描述反覆的自然升降變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"part of the cycle","meaning":"循環的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Temperature changes have always been part of the global weather cycle.","zh":"氣溫變化一直是全球天氣循環的一部分。"},{"en":"Part of the cycle means one stage or element in a repeated pattern.","zh":"part of the cycle 指重複模式中的一個階段或元素。"},{"en":"Feeling tired after exams can be part of the cycle of hard work and recovery.","zh":"考試後感到疲倦可以是努力和恢復循環的一部分。"},{"en":"If a change is part of a cycle, it may return or reverse later.","zh":"如果變化是循環的一部分，它日後可能再次出現或逆轉。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests repeated natural or social patterns.","zh":"這個片語暗示重複的自然或社會模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"global weather","meaning":"全球天氣","examples":[{"en":"Natural cycles influence global weather.","zh":"自然循環影響全球天氣。"},{"en":"Global weather means weather patterns considered across the whole world.","zh":"global weather 指從全世界角度考慮的天氣模式。"},{"en":"Scientists study global weather by comparing storms, rainfall, heat, and winds in many regions.","zh":"科學家透過比較許多地區的風暴、降雨、熱力和風來研究全球天氣。"},{"en":"If ocean temperatures change, global weather patterns may also change.","zh":"如果海洋溫度改變，全球天氣模式也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to weather on a worldwide scale.","zh":"這個片語指全球尺度的天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"an analysis of","meaning":"對……的分析","examples":[{"en":"An analysis of meteorologists’ views produced surprising results.","zh":"對氣象學家觀點的分析產生了令人意外的結果。"},{"en":"An analysis of something is a careful study of its parts, patterns, or meaning.","zh":"analysis of something 是仔細研究某事的部分、模式或意義。"},{"en":"A teacher may do an analysis of students’ essays to find common grammar mistakes.","zh":"老師可能分析學生作文，以找出常見文法錯誤。"},{"en":"If an analysis is detailed, it can reveal patterns people missed before.","zh":"如果分析詳細，它可以揭示人們之前忽略的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces careful examination.","zh":"這個片語引入仔細檢視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"views of major meteorologists","meaning":"主要氣象學家的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The survey examined the views of major meteorologists in the United States.","zh":"該調查檢視美國主要氣象學家的觀點。"},{"en":"Views of major meteorologists means the opinions held by important weather experts.","zh":"views of major meteorologists 指重要天氣專家的意見。"},{"en":"A newspaper may report the views of major doctors during a health crisis.","zh":"在健康危機期間，報章可能報道主要醫生的觀點。"},{"en":"If major meteorologists disagree, the public may find the issue confusing.","zh":"如果主要氣象學家意見不一，公眾可能覺得問題令人困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to expert opinions from leading specialists.","zh":"這個片語指主要專家的專業意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"less than 20 per cent of","meaning":"少於百分之二十的……","examples":[{"en":"Less than 20 per cent of the meteorologists blamed humans.","zh":"少於百分之二十的氣象學家把責任歸咎於人類。"},{"en":"Less than 20 per cent of a group means fewer than one in five people or items.","zh":"less than 20 per cent of a group 指一個群體中少於五分之一的人或事物。"},{"en":"Less than 20 per cent of students chose the hardest question in the test.","zh":"少於百分之二十的學生選擇測驗中最難的題目。"},{"en":"If less than 20 per cent support an idea, it is a minority view.","zh":"如果少於百分之二十支持某想法，它就是少數觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a small proportion.","zh":"這個片語表示較小比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"change in temperature","meaning":"氣溫變化","examples":[{"en":"The researchers considered the change in temperature over a century.","zh":"研究人員考慮一個世紀以來的氣溫變化。"},{"en":"A change in temperature is a rise or fall in how hot or cold something is.","zh":"change in temperature 指某物冷熱程度的上升或下降。"},{"en":"A sudden change in temperature can make people feel unwell or uncomfortable.","zh":"氣溫突然變化可以令人感到不適或不舒服。"},{"en":"If temperature changes over many years, scientists may study climate patterns.","zh":"如果氣溫多年變化，科學家可能研究氣候模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes measurable warming or cooling.","zh":"這個片語描述可量度的變暖或變冷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"over the last hundred years","meaning":"在過去一百年間","examples":[{"en":"Global temperatures have changed over the last hundred years.","zh":"全球氣溫在過去一百年間發生變化。"},{"en":"Over the last hundred years means during the past century.","zh":"over the last hundred years 指在過去一個世紀期間。"},{"en":"The city has changed greatly over the last hundred years.","zh":"這座城市在過去一百年間變化很大。"},{"en":"If a trend lasts for a hundred years, it is not just a short-term event.","zh":"如果一個趨勢持續一百年，它就不只是短期事件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a long historical period.","zh":"這個片語描述一段很長的歷史時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be our own fault","meaning":"是我們自己的責任","examples":[{"en":"Only a minority believed that the warming was our own fault.","zh":"只有少數人相信暖化是我們自己的責任。"},{"en":"If something is our own fault, we are responsible for causing it.","zh":"be our own fault 指我們要為造成某事負責。"},{"en":"If a student forgets to submit homework, the missing mark may be their own fault.","zh":"如果學生忘記交功課，失分可能是他自己的責任。"},{"en":"If human activity causes climate change, people may need to accept responsibility.","zh":"如果人類活動造成氣候變化，人們可能需要承擔責任。"},{"en":"This phrase places blame on ourselves.","zh":"這個片語把責任歸於我們自己。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"attribute something to","meaning":"將……歸因於……","examples":[{"en":"Most meteorologists attributed the change to natural cycles.","zh":"大多數氣象學家將這種變化歸因於自然循環。"},{"en":"To attribute something to a cause means to say that the cause is responsible for it.","zh":"attribute something to a cause 指說某原因要為某事負責。"},{"en":"A teacher may attribute a student’s improvement to regular practice.","zh":"老師可能把學生的進步歸因於定期練習。"},{"en":"If scientists attribute warming to natural cycles, they see nature as the main explanation.","zh":"如果科學家把暖化歸因於自然循環，他們就把自然視為主要解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when explaining causes.","zh":"這個片語用於解釋成因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"natural cyclical changes","meaning":"自然的周期性變化","examples":[{"en":"Some experts attribute global warming to natural cyclical changes.","zh":"一些專家將全球暖化歸因於自然的周期性變化。"},{"en":"Natural cyclical changes are repeated changes in nature that happen over time.","zh":"natural cyclical changes 是自然界隨時間反覆出現的變化。"},{"en":"Seasons are natural cyclical changes that affect temperature and rainfall.","zh":"季節是影響氣溫和降雨的自然周期性變化。"},{"en":"If climate shifts follow natural cycles, the cause may not be purely human activity.","zh":"如果氣候轉變跟隨自然循環，成因可能不純粹是人類活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeating natural patterns.","zh":"這個片語描述重複出現的自然模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"there is no denying that","meaning":"無可否認","examples":[{"en":"There is no denying that scientists still have much to learn about weather.","zh":"無可否認，科學家對天氣仍有很多需要學習。"},{"en":"There is no denying that means it is impossible or unreasonable to reject a fact.","zh":"there is no denying that 指不可能或不合理地否認某事實。"},{"en":"There is no denying that sleep affects students’ concentration.","zh":"無可否認，睡眠會影響學生專注力。"},{"en":"If evidence is clear, people may admit a point even if they disagree about other details.","zh":"如果證據清楚，人們即使在其他細節上不同意，也可能承認某點。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a fact that is hard to dispute.","zh":"這個片語引入難以爭議的事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at a very early stage","meaning":"處於非常初期的階段","examples":[{"en":"We are still at a very early stage in understanding the climate system.","zh":"我們在了解氣候系統方面仍處於非常初期的階段。"},{"en":"At a very early stage means near the beginning of a process or area of knowledge.","zh":"at a very early stage 指接近某過程或知識領域的開始。"},{"en":"A new business may be at a very early stage before it has customers.","zh":"新企業在有顧客前可能處於非常初期的階段。"},{"en":"If research is still early, predictions may be uncertain.","zh":"如果研究仍在初期，預測可能不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that development or understanding is not yet mature.","zh":"這個片語顯示發展或理解尚未成熟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"understanding weather","meaning":"了解天氣","examples":[{"en":"Scientists remain at an early stage in understanding weather.","zh":"科學家在了解天氣方面仍處於初期階段。"},{"en":"Understanding weather means knowing how temperature, wind, clouds, rain, and pressure interact.","zh":"understanding weather 指知道氣溫、風、雲、雨和氣壓如何互相作用。"},{"en":"Children begin understanding weather by observing clouds and checking forecasts.","zh":"孩子透過觀察雲和查看天氣預報，開始了解天氣。"},{"en":"If scientists understand weather better, forecasts may become more accurate.","zh":"如果科學家更了解天氣，預報可能更準確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes knowledge of short-term atmospheric conditions.","zh":"這個片語描述對短期大氣狀況的認識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"effects of variables","meaning":"不同變數的影響","examples":[{"en":"The effects of many climatic variables are not fully understood.","zh":"許多氣候變數的影響尚未被充分理解。"},{"en":"Effects of variables are the ways different changing factors influence a result.","zh":"effects of variables 指不同變動因素影響結果的方式。"},{"en":"In an exam, sleep, practice, and stress are variables that affect performance.","zh":"在考試中，睡眠、練習和壓力都是影響表現的變數。"},{"en":"If scientists do not know each variable’s effect, predictions become harder.","zh":"如果科學家不知道每個變數的影響，預測會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when many factors interact.","zh":"這個片語適合用於許多因素互相作用的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"variables such as","meaning":"例如……等變數","examples":[{"en":"Weather depends on variables such as rainfall and cloud formation.","zh":"天氣取決於降雨和雲層形成等變數。"},{"en":"Variables such as introduces examples of factors that can change a result.","zh":"variables such as 用來引入可改變結果的因素例子。"},{"en":"Exam performance depends on variables such as preparation, sleep, and question difficulty.","zh":"考試表現取決於準備、睡眠和題目難度等變數。"},{"en":"If many variables are involved, simple explanations may be misleading.","zh":"如果涉及許多變數，簡單解釋可能有誤導性。"},{"en":"This phrase gives examples of changing factors.","zh":"這個片語給出變動因素的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cloud formation","meaning":"雲層形成","examples":[{"en":"Cloud formation has a complex effect on the climate.","zh":"雲層形成對氣候有複雜影響。"},{"en":"Cloud formation is the process by which water vapour becomes clouds in the atmosphere.","zh":"cloud formation 是水蒸氣在大氣中變成雲的過程。"},{"en":"Children can see cloud formation when warm moist air rises and cools.","zh":"當溫暖濕潤空氣上升並冷卻，孩子可以看到雲層形成。"},{"en":"If cloud formation changes, sunlight, rainfall, and temperature may also change.","zh":"如果雲層形成改變，陽光、降雨和氣溫也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how clouds develop.","zh":"這個片語描述雲如何形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"seas and oceans","meaning":"海洋","examples":[{"en":"The seas and oceans play an important role in global weather.","zh":"海洋在全球天氣中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"Seas and oceans are large bodies of salt water that cover most of the Earth.","zh":"seas and oceans 是覆蓋地球大部分面積的大型鹹水水體。"},{"en":"Fishing communities depend on seas and oceans for food and income.","zh":"漁業社群依靠海洋獲得食物和收入。"},{"en":"If oceans store heat, they can influence storms and rainfall patterns.","zh":"如果海洋儲存熱量，它們可以影響風暴和降雨模式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the world’s major saltwater systems.","zh":"這個片語指世界主要鹹水系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"methane and ozone","meaning":"甲烷和臭氧","examples":[{"en":"Methane and ozone are gases that can affect the atmosphere.","zh":"甲烷和臭氧是可以影響大氣層的氣體。"},{"en":"Methane and ozone are atmospheric gases that can influence climate and air quality.","zh":"methane and ozone 是可以影響氣候和空氣質素的大氣氣體。"},{"en":"Methane can come from farming and waste, while ozone can affect breathing near the ground.","zh":"甲烷可以來自農業和廢物，而近地面臭氧可以影響呼吸。"},{"en":"If these gases increase, they may change how heat and sunlight behave in the atmosphere.","zh":"如果這些氣體增加，它們可能改變熱量和陽光在大氣中的作用。"},{"en":"This phrase names two important gases in climate discussion.","zh":"這個片語指出氣候討論中的兩種重要氣體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"solar energy","meaning":"太陽能量","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are still studying the climatic effects of solar energy.","zh":"科學家仍在研究太陽能量的氣候影響。"},{"en":"Solar energy is energy that comes from the sun.","zh":"solar energy 是來自太陽的能量。"},{"en":"Solar panels use solar energy to produce electricity for homes and schools.","zh":"太陽能板使用太陽能量為家庭和學校發電。"},{"en":"If the amount of solar energy reaching Earth changes, climate may also be affected.","zh":"如果到達地球的太陽能量改變，氣候也可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to both sunlight’s natural energy and its practical use.","zh":"這個片語可指陽光的自然能量，也可指其實際用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not fully understood","meaning":"尚未被充分理解","examples":[{"en":"Many factors affecting the climate are not fully understood.","zh":"許多影響氣候的因素尚未被充分理解。"},{"en":"Not fully understood means not completely known or explained yet.","zh":"not fully understood 指尚未被完全知道或解釋。"},{"en":"A student’s anxiety may be not fully understood until teachers speak with the family.","zh":"學生的焦慮可能要到老師與家庭交談後才被充分理解。"},{"en":"If a system is not fully understood, predictions about it may be uncertain.","zh":"如果一個系統尚未被充分理解，關於它的預測可能不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that knowledge is incomplete.","zh":"這個片語顯示知識並不完整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make predictions","meaning":"作出預測","examples":[{"en":"Researchers use climate data to make predictions about future temperatures.","zh":"研究人員使用氣候數據作出關於未來氣溫的預測。"},{"en":"To make predictions means to say what is likely to happen in the future.","zh":"make predictions 指說出未來可能會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Teachers may make predictions about exam performance by looking at past practice papers.","zh":"老師可能透過查看過往練習卷，對考試表現作出預測。"},{"en":"If data is weak, predictions may be less reliable.","zh":"如果數據薄弱，預測可能較不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes forecasting future events.","zh":"這個片語描述預測未來事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cannot always be relied on","meaning":"並非總是可靠","examples":[{"en":"Predictions based on uncertain variables cannot always be relied on.","zh":"基於不確定變數的預測並非總是可靠。"},{"en":"Cannot always be relied on means cannot be trusted in every situation.","zh":"cannot always be relied on 指不能在每種情況下都被信任。"},{"en":"A bus timetable cannot always be relied on during bad weather.","zh":"惡劣天氣期間，巴士時間表並非總是可靠。"},{"en":"If a prediction uses incomplete data, people should treat it cautiously.","zh":"如果預測使用不完整數據，人們應謹慎看待。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that something may sometimes fail.","zh":"這個片語警告某事有時可能失效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"predict that","meaning":"預測","examples":[{"en":"Dr Hansen predicted that global temperatures would increase.","zh":"Hansen 博士預測全球氣溫會上升。"},{"en":"To predict that something will happen means to say it is likely to happen in the future.","zh":"predict that something will happen 指說某事將來很可能發生。"},{"en":"A teacher may predict that students will improve if they practise daily.","zh":"老師可能預測學生若每天練習就會進步。"},{"en":"If a scientist predicts warming, others may test the prediction against later data.","zh":"如果科學家預測暖化，其他人可能用後來數據測試該預測。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a forecast.","zh":"這個片語引入預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"raise global temperatures","meaning":"令全球氣溫上升","examples":[{"en":"Global warming was expected to raise global temperatures.","zh":"全球暖化被預期會令全球氣溫上升。"},{"en":"To raise global temperatures means to make average temperatures around the world higher.","zh":"raise global temperatures 指令世界各地平均氣溫變高。"},{"en":"Burning more fuel can raise air pollution and may raise global temperatures over time.","zh":"燃燒更多燃料可以增加空氣污染，並可能隨時間令全球氣溫上升。"},{"en":"If global temperatures rise, ice, rainfall, and farming conditions may change.","zh":"如果全球氣溫上升，冰、降雨和農業條件可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes worldwide warming as an effect.","zh":"這個片語把全球變暖描述為一種影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"disastrous consequences for","meaning":"對……造成災難性後果","examples":[{"en":"Hansen warned of disastrous consequences for humankind.","zh":"Hansen 警告這會對人類造成災難性後果。"},{"en":"Disastrous consequences for someone are extremely harmful results affecting them.","zh":"disastrous consequences for someone 指對某人造成極嚴重有害結果。"},{"en":"A serious mistake in hospital hygiene can have disastrous consequences for patients.","zh":"醫院衛生上的嚴重錯誤可以對病人造成災難性後果。"},{"en":"If climate change causes famine and floods, the consequences for people may be severe.","zh":"如果氣候變化造成饑荒和洪水，對人們的後果可能十分嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a group may suffer badly.","zh":"這個片語警告某群體可能嚴重受害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"humankind","meaning":"人類","examples":[{"en":"Climate change may have serious consequences for humankind.","zh":"氣候變化可能對人類造成嚴重後果。"},{"en":"Humankind means all human beings as one group.","zh":"humankind 指所有人類作為一個整體。"},{"en":"Medical discoveries can benefit humankind by reducing disease and suffering.","zh":"醫學發現可以透過減少疾病和痛苦造福人類。"},{"en":"If a problem affects humankind, it crosses national borders.","zh":"如果問題影響人類，它就跨越國界。"},{"en":"This word is formal and refers to humanity as a whole.","zh":"這個詞較正式，指整體人類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cause-and-effect relationship","meaning":"因果關係","examples":[{"en":"Hansen proposed a strong cause-and-effect relationship between human activity and climate.","zh":"Hansen 提出人類活動與氣候之間有強烈因果關係。"},{"en":"A cause-and-effect relationship means one thing directly influences or produces another.","zh":"cause-and-effect relationship 指一件事直接影響或造成另一件事。"},{"en":"Teachers show cause and effect when explaining how lack of sleep affects concentration.","zh":"老師解釋睡眠不足如何影響專注力時，就是展示因果關係。"},{"en":"If emissions cause warming, reducing emissions should help reduce the problem.","zh":"如果排放導致暖化，減少排放應有助減輕問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a link between a cause and its result.","zh":"這個片語描述原因與結果之間的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"current climate","meaning":"當前氣候","examples":[{"en":"Scientists examine the relationship between human activity and the current climate.","zh":"科學家檢視人類活動與當前氣候之間的關係。"},{"en":"Current climate means the climate conditions that exist now.","zh":"current climate 指現在存在的氣候條件。"},{"en":"Farmers study the current climate before choosing crops for the season.","zh":"農民在選擇當季作物前會研究當前氣候。"},{"en":"If the current climate is changing, old farming or building plans may no longer fit.","zh":"如果當前氣候正在改變，舊有農業或建築計劃可能不再適合。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to present-day climate conditions.","zh":"這個片語指現今氣候狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"human alteration of the atmosphere","meaning":"人類對大氣層的改變","examples":[{"en":"Industrial activity contributes to human alteration of the atmosphere.","zh":"工業活動促成人類對大氣層的改變。"},{"en":"Human alteration of the atmosphere means changes people make to the air around Earth.","zh":"human alteration of the atmosphere 指人類對地球周圍空氣造成的改變。"},{"en":"Factories and vehicles can alter the atmosphere by adding gases and particles.","zh":"工廠和車輛可以透過加入氣體和微粒改變大氣層。"},{"en":"If humans change the atmosphere, weather and climate may also change.","zh":"如果人類改變大氣層，天氣和氣候也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes human-caused atmospheric change.","zh":"這個片語描述由人類造成的大氣變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"go on record as stating that","meaning":"公開表明","examples":[{"en":"Hansen later went on record as stating that climate prediction was extremely difficult.","zh":"Hansen 後來公開表明氣候預測極為困難。"},{"en":"To go on record as stating that means to publicly and officially say something.","zh":"go on record as stating that 指公開而正式地說出某事。"},{"en":"A headteacher may go on record as stating that student safety is the school’s priority.","zh":"校長可能公開表明學生安全是學校優先事項。"},{"en":"If a scientist goes on record, their statement can be quoted and checked later.","zh":"如果科學家公開表明立場，其說法日後可以被引用和查核。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a public statement.","zh":"這個片語描述作出公開聲明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"artificial climate models","meaning":"人工氣候模型","examples":[{"en":"Scientists use artificial climate models to estimate future changes.","zh":"科學家使用人工氣候模型估算未來變化。"},{"en":"Artificial climate models are computer-based systems used to simulate climate behaviour.","zh":"artificial climate models 是用來模擬氣候行為的電腦系統。"},{"en":"Weather offices use models to estimate where storms may move.","zh":"氣象部門使用模型估算風暴可能移向何處。"},{"en":"If a model misses important variables, its predictions may be wrong.","zh":"如果模型遺漏重要變數，其預測可能錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to human-made tools for studying climate.","zh":"這個片語指研究氣候的人造工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"all but impossible","meaning":"幾乎不可能","examples":[{"en":"Accurate long-term climate prediction may be all but impossible.","zh":"準確的長期氣候預測可能幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"All but impossible means almost impossible.","zh":"all but impossible 指幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"Finding a lost ring on a crowded beach may be all but impossible.","zh":"在擁擠海灘找回遺失戒指可能幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"If a system is extremely complex, predicting it perfectly can be almost impossible.","zh":"如果系統極度複雜，完美預測它可能幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses very great difficulty.","zh":"這個片語強調極大困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rather than getting hotter","meaning":"並非變得更熱，而是……","examples":[{"en":"Hansen later suggested that the planet might be getting greener rather than merely hotter.","zh":"Hansen 後來提出，地球可能並非只是變得更熱，而是變得更綠。"},{"en":"Rather than getting hotter contrasts warming with another possible change, such as increased plant growth.","zh":"rather than getting hotter 把變暖與另一種可能變化作對比，例如植物增長。"},{"en":"A city may become more crowded rather than richer if new housing is not planned well.","zh":"如果新住房規劃不好，城市可能不是變得更富裕，而是變得更擁擠。"},{"en":"If one result happens instead of the expected one, writers use rather than to show contrast.","zh":"如果一個結果發生而不是預期結果，作者會用 rather than 表示對比。"},{"en":"This phrase separates one interpretation from another.","zh":"這個片語把一種詮釋與另一種分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get greener","meaning":"變得更綠","examples":[{"en":"Higher carbon dioxide levels may cause some regions to get greener.","zh":"較高二氧化碳水平可能令某些地區變得更綠。"},{"en":"To get greener means to have more plants, leaves, or vegetation.","zh":"get greener 指有更多植物、葉子或植被。"},{"en":"A school garden may get greener after students plant trees and water them regularly.","zh":"學生種樹並定期澆水後，學校花園可能變得更綠。"},{"en":"If warmer conditions allow plants to grow in cold areas, those areas may become greener.","zh":"如果較暖條件讓植物在寒冷地區生長，那些地區可能變得更綠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increase in vegetation.","zh":"這個片語描述植被增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as a result of","meaning":"由於；作為……的結果","examples":[{"en":"Vegetation may increase as a result of higher carbon dioxide levels.","zh":"由於二氧化碳水平較高，植被可能增加。"},{"en":"As a result of means because of something.","zh":"as a result of 指因為某事。"},{"en":"A student may improve as a result of regular feedback and practice.","zh":"學生可能由於定期回饋和練習而進步。"},{"en":"If carbon dioxide helps some plants grow, vegetation may increase in certain areas.","zh":"如果二氧化碳有助某些植物生長，某些地區的植被可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with an effect.","zh":"這個片語把原因與結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"increased carbon dioxide","meaning":"增加的二氧化碳","examples":[{"en":"Increased carbon dioxide may encourage plant growth in some areas.","zh":"增加的二氧化碳可能促進某些地區的植物生長。"},{"en":"Increased carbon dioxide means a higher amount of CO2 in the air.","zh":"increased carbon dioxide 指空氣中的二氧化碳含量更高。"},{"en":"A greenhouse may use extra carbon dioxide to help some plants grow faster.","zh":"溫室可能使用額外二氧化碳幫助某些植物更快生長。"},{"en":"If carbon dioxide increases in the atmosphere, it may also trap more heat.","zh":"如果大氣中的二氧化碳增加，它也可能困住更多熱量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rise in an important atmospheric gas.","zh":"這個片語描述一種重要大氣氣體上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"with the prospect of","meaning":"有可能出現……","examples":[{"en":"There is the prospect of more vegetation in previously frozen areas.","zh":"以前冰封的地區有可能出現更多植被。"},{"en":"With the prospect of something means with the possibility that it may happen in the future.","zh":"with the prospect of something 指某事將來有可能發生。"},{"en":"Students may study harder with the prospect of entering their preferred university.","zh":"學生可能因有機會入讀心儀大學而更努力讀書。"},{"en":"If frozen land becomes warmer, there may be the prospect of new plant growth.","zh":"如果冰封土地變暖，就可能出現新的植物生長。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a possible future development.","zh":"這個片語引入可能的未來發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"frozen wastelands","meaning":"冰封荒地","examples":[{"en":"Some frozen wastelands may support more vegetation in future.","zh":"一些冰封荒地日後可能支持更多植被。"},{"en":"Frozen wastelands are very cold, mostly empty areas where little grows.","zh":"frozen wastelands 是極寒、幾乎空曠、少有植物生長的地區。"},{"en":"A frozen wasteland may have ice, snow, rocks, and very few plants.","zh":"冰封荒地可能有冰、雪、岩石和極少植物。"},{"en":"If temperatures rise, some frozen wastelands may become suitable for mosses or shrubs.","zh":"如果氣溫上升，一些冰封荒地可能變得適合苔蘚或灌木生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harsh cold land with little life.","zh":"這個片語描述生命稀少的嚴寒土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"evidence to suggest that","meaning":"有證據顯示","examples":[{"en":"There is some evidence to suggest that earlier estimates were too high.","zh":"有一些證據顯示早期估算過高。"},{"en":"Evidence to suggest that means information that points toward a possible conclusion.","zh":"evidence to suggest that 指指向某個可能結論的資料。"},{"en":"There is evidence to suggest that students learn better with shorter, regular practice.","zh":"有證據顯示學生透過較短而定期的練習學得更好。"},{"en":"If evidence suggests a problem is smaller than expected, estimates may be revised.","zh":"如果證據顯示問題比預期小，估算可能被修正。"},{"en":"This phrase is cautious because it does not claim final proof.","zh":"這個片語較謹慎，因為它沒有聲稱最終證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"computer-based weather models","meaning":"電腦氣象模型","examples":[{"en":"Computer-based weather models have become increasingly sophisticated.","zh":"電腦氣象模型已變得越來越精密。"},{"en":"Computer-based weather models are computer systems that use data to simulate weather or climate.","zh":"computer-based weather models 是使用數據模擬天氣或氣候的電腦系統。"},{"en":"Weather forecasters use computer-based models to predict storms and rainfall.","zh":"天氣預報員使用電腦模型預測風暴和降雨。"},{"en":"If computers become faster, models can include more variables.","zh":"如果電腦速度變快，模型就能包括更多變數。"},{"en":"This phrase describes digital tools for weather prediction.","zh":"這個片語描述用於天氣預測的數碼工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"become more sophisticated","meaning":"變得更精密","examples":[{"en":"Climate models have become more sophisticated over time.","zh":"氣候模型隨時間變得更精密。"},{"en":"To become more sophisticated means to become more advanced, detailed, or capable.","zh":"become more sophisticated 指變得更先進、更詳細或更有能力。"},{"en":"Language-learning apps have become more sophisticated by adding speech recognition.","zh":"語言學習應用程式加入語音識別後變得更精密。"},{"en":"If models become more sophisticated, they may make better predictions.","zh":"如果模型變得更精密，它們可能作出更好預測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improvement in complexity and ability.","zh":"這個片語描述複雜度和能力上的提升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"predicted rises in temperature","meaning":"預測中的氣溫升幅","examples":[{"en":"The predicted rises in temperature have been reduced.","zh":"預測中的氣溫升幅已被調低。"},{"en":"Predicted rises in temperature are expected increases in how warm the air or climate will become.","zh":"predicted rises in temperature 是對空氣或氣候會變得多暖的預期升幅。"},{"en":"A weather report may show predicted rises in temperature during a heatwave.","zh":"天氣報告可能顯示熱浪期間預測中的氣溫升幅。"},{"en":"If models change, predicted rises may be raised or lowered.","zh":"如果模型改變，預測升幅可能被調高或調低。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to forecasted warming.","zh":"這個片語指預測中的變暖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be cut back","meaning":"被削減；被調低","examples":[{"en":"More advanced models have caused some temperature estimates to be cut back.","zh":"更先進的模型令一些氣溫估算被調低。"},{"en":"To be cut back means to be reduced.","zh":"be cut back 指被減少。"},{"en":"A school trip may be cut back if the budget is smaller than expected.","zh":"如果預算比預期少，學校旅行可能被削減。"},{"en":"If new evidence suggests a lower number, an earlier estimate may be cut back.","zh":"如果新證據顯示數字較低，早期估算可能被調低。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing a plan, amount, or estimate.","zh":"這個片語描述削減計劃、數量或估算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in addition","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"In addition, much of the recorded warming occurred relatively early.","zh":"此外，記錄到的暖化大部分相對較早發生。"},{"en":"In addition means also or furthermore.","zh":"in addition 指此外或另外。"},{"en":"The course teaches grammar; in addition, it gives students speaking practice.","zh":"這個課程教授文法；此外，它給學生口語練習。"},{"en":"Writers use in addition to add another point to an argument.","zh":"作者使用 in addition 為論點加入另一點。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect related ideas.","zh":"這個片語幫助連接相關想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"much-reported rise","meaning":"被廣泛報道的升幅","examples":[{"en":"A close analysis was made of the much-reported rise in global temperature.","zh":"人們對全球氣溫被廣泛報道的升幅作出了仔細分析。"},{"en":"A much-reported rise is an increase that has been discussed widely in the media.","zh":"much-reported rise 是被傳媒廣泛討論的上升。"},{"en":"A much-reported rise in rent may worry young families.","zh":"被廣泛報道的租金升幅可能令年輕家庭擔心。"},{"en":"If a rise is much reported, people may know about it before understanding its details.","zh":"如果升幅被廣泛報道，人們可能在理解細節前已知道它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increase that receives a lot of public attention.","zh":"這個片語描述受到大量公眾關注的增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"over the last century","meaning":"在過去一個世紀","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have examined temperature changes over the last century.","zh":"科學家檢視了過去一個世紀的氣溫變化。"},{"en":"Over the last century means during the past one hundred years.","zh":"over the last century 指在過去一百年期間。"},{"en":"Housing prices have changed greatly over the last century.","zh":"房價在過去一個世紀變化很大。"},{"en":"If a pattern appears over a century, it may reveal long-term change.","zh":"如果模式在一個世紀中出現，它可能揭示長期變化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a hundred-year period up to the present or a given point.","zh":"這個片語指直到現在或某時間點前的一百年。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"close analysis","meaning":"仔細分析","examples":[{"en":"A close analysis reveals when most of the warming occurred.","zh":"仔細分析揭示大部分暖化何時發生。"},{"en":"Close analysis means careful and detailed examination.","zh":"close analysis 指仔細而詳細的檢視。"},{"en":"A close analysis of a student’s essay can reveal repeated grammar problems.","zh":"對學生作文作仔細分析，可以揭示反覆出現的文法問題。"},{"en":"If data is analysed closely, hidden patterns may appear.","zh":"如果數據被仔細分析，隱藏模式可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful study rather than quick judgement.","zh":"這個片語描述仔細研究，而不是快速判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reveal that","meaning":"顯示","examples":[{"en":"The analysis reveals that much of the increase occurred before 1950.","zh":"分析顯示大部分升幅在1950年前發生。"},{"en":"To reveal that means to show or make known something previously unclear.","zh":"reveal that 指顯示或揭示先前不清楚的事情。"},{"en":"A survey may reveal that many students feel nervous before speaking tests.","zh":"調查可能顯示許多學生在口試前感到緊張。"},{"en":"If analysis reveals a hidden pattern, the original explanation may need to change.","zh":"如果分析揭示隱藏模式，原本解釋可能需要改變。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a finding.","zh":"這個片語引入研究發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the lion’s share of","meaning":"最大部分；絕大部分","examples":[{"en":"The lion’s share of the recorded rise occurred relatively early.","zh":"記錄升幅的最大部分相對較早發生。"},{"en":"The lion’s share of something means the largest part of it.","zh":"lion’s share of something 指某事物中最大的一部分。"},{"en":"One project may take the lion’s share of a school’s budget.","zh":"一個項目可能佔去學校預算的最大部分。"},{"en":"If one period contains the lion’s share of the increase, that period deserves close attention.","zh":"如果某時期包含升幅的最大部分，該時期就值得仔細注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the biggest portion.","zh":"這個片語描述最大份額。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"almost three quarters","meaning":"接近四分之三","examples":[{"en":"Almost three quarters of the increase occurred before the later industrial period.","zh":"接近四分之三的升幅發生在較後期工業時代之前。"},{"en":"Almost three quarters means nearly 75 percent.","zh":"almost three quarters 指接近百分之七十五。"},{"en":"Almost three quarters of the class chose the same essay question.","zh":"接近四分之三的班級選擇了同一道作文題。"},{"en":"If almost three quarters of a change happened early, later causes may explain less of it.","zh":"如果接近四分之三的變化早期已發生，後來原因可能只能解釋較少部分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a large proportion close to three-fourths.","zh":"這個片語表示接近四分之三的大比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in total","meaning":"總計","examples":[{"en":"The earlier rise represented almost three quarters in total.","zh":"較早期升幅總計接近四分之三。"},{"en":"In total means when all parts are added together.","zh":"in total 指把所有部分加起來。"},{"en":"The class raised 2,000 dollars in total for charity.","zh":"全班為慈善總共籌得二千元。"},{"en":"If several small increases are added in total, the final change may be large.","zh":"如果幾個小增幅總計起來，最終變化可能很大。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the complete combined amount.","zh":"這個片語給出完整合計數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"occur before","meaning":"在……之前發生","examples":[{"en":"Much of the temperature increase occurred before modern industrial expansion.","zh":"大部分氣溫升幅發生在現代工業擴張之前。"},{"en":"To occur before something means to happen earlier than it.","zh":"occur before something 指比某事更早發生。"},{"en":"Some exam stress occurs before students even receive the timetable.","zh":"有些考試壓力甚至在學生收到時間表之前已發生。"},{"en":"If a change occurs before a proposed cause, that cause may not fully explain it.","zh":"如果變化發生在某個被提出的原因之前，該原因可能不能完全解釋它。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare timing.","zh":"這個片語幫助比較時間先後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"industrial processes","meaning":"工業生產過程","examples":[{"en":"Industrial processes release gases into the atmosphere.","zh":"工業生產過程把氣體釋放到大氣中。"},{"en":"Industrial processes are activities used in factories and production, such as burning fuel or making materials.","zh":"industrial processes 是工廠和生產中使用的活動，例如燃燒燃料或製造材料。"},{"en":"Making steel, cement, and chemicals involves industrial processes.","zh":"製造鋼鐵、水泥和化學品涉及工業生產過程。"},{"en":"If industrial processes produce emissions, they can affect air quality and climate.","zh":"如果工業生產過程產生排放，它們可以影響空氣質素和氣候。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to methods used in large-scale production.","zh":"這個片語指大規模生產中使用的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"accompanying emissions","meaning":"隨之產生的排放","examples":[{"en":"Industrial development produces accompanying greenhouse gas emissions.","zh":"工業發展產生隨之而來的溫室氣體排放。"},{"en":"Accompanying emissions are emissions that happen together with an activity or process.","zh":"accompanying emissions 是與某活動或過程同時出現的排放。"},{"en":"More flights can bring economic benefits and accompanying emissions.","zh":"更多航班可以帶來經濟好處和隨之產生的排放。"},{"en":"If production increases, accompanying emissions may increase as well.","zh":"如果生產增加，隨之產生的排放也可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pollution that comes along with development or activity.","zh":"這個片語描述伴隨發展或活動而來的污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"greenhouse gas emissions","meaning":"溫室氣體排放","examples":[{"en":"Transport and industry produce greenhouse gas emissions.","zh":"交通和工業產生溫室氣體排放。"},{"en":"Greenhouse gas emissions are gases released into the air that trap heat, such as carbon dioxide and methane.","zh":"greenhouse gas emissions 是釋放到空氣中並困住熱量的氣體，例如二氧化碳和甲烷。"},{"en":"Driving petrol cars every day creates greenhouse gas emissions.","zh":"每天駕駛汽油車會產生溫室氣體排放。"},{"en":"If emissions rise, more heat may be trapped in the atmosphere.","zh":"如果排放上升，大氣中可能困住更多熱量。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to climate-change discussions.","zh":"這個片語是氣候變化討論的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the second half of","meaning":"……的後半段","examples":[{"en":"Industrial emissions grew rapidly in the second half of the twentieth century.","zh":"工業排放在二十世紀後半段快速增加。"},{"en":"The second half of a period means the later 50 percent of it.","zh":"second half of a period 指某段時期較後的百分之五十。"},{"en":"A film may become more exciting in the second half of the story.","zh":"電影可能在故事後半段變得更刺激。"},{"en":"If most emissions grew in the second half of the century, timing becomes important in the debate.","zh":"如果大部分排放在該世紀後半段增加，時間先後在爭論中就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase divides a period into earlier and later parts.","zh":"這個片語把一段時期分成前後兩部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pay attention to","meaning":"留意；重視","examples":[{"en":"The writer asks whether we should pay attention to dramatic media stories.","zh":"作者問我們是否應重視誇張的傳媒故事。"},{"en":"To pay attention to something means to notice it and think about it carefully.","zh":"pay attention to something 指留意某事並仔細思考。"},{"en":"Students should pay attention to word limits in reading questions.","zh":"學生應留意閱讀題目的字數限制。"},{"en":"If people pay attention only to headlines, they may miss the evidence behind them.","zh":"如果人們只注意標題，可能錯過背後證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful notice or focus.","zh":"這個片語描述仔細注意或專注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"scream out at us","meaning":"強烈吸引我們注意","examples":[{"en":"Alarmist headlines seem to scream out at us from the media.","zh":"危言聳聽的標題似乎從傳媒中強烈吸引我們注意。"},{"en":"To scream out at us means to demand our attention in a loud, dramatic, or forceful way.","zh":"scream out at us 指以大聲、誇張或強烈方式要求我們注意。"},{"en":"Bright sale signs scream out at shoppers as they walk past the store.","zh":"鮮艷減價標誌在顧客經過店舖時強烈吸引他們注意。"},{"en":"If headlines scream out at people, they may react emotionally before reading carefully.","zh":"如果標題強烈吸引人們注意，他們可能在仔細閱讀前已情緒化反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attention-grabbing messages.","zh":"這個片語描述吸引注意的訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"billboards","meaning":"廣告牌","examples":[{"en":"Billboards often carry dramatic environmental messages.","zh":"廣告牌常刊載誇張的環境訊息。"},{"en":"Billboards are large outdoor signs used for advertising or public messages.","zh":"billboards 是用於廣告或公共訊息的大型戶外標誌。"},{"en":"A bus stop may have a billboard promoting a new film.","zh":"巴士站可能有宣傳新電影的廣告牌。"},{"en":"If a billboard uses shocking images, people may notice the message quickly.","zh":"如果廣告牌使用震撼圖片，人們可能很快注意到訊息。"},{"en":"This word refers to large signs seen in public spaces.","zh":"這個詞指公共空間中的大型標誌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"television news headlines","meaning":"電視新聞標題","examples":[{"en":"Television news headlines frequently warn about climate change.","zh":"電視新聞標題經常警告氣候變化。"},{"en":"Television news headlines are the short main titles of news stories shown on TV.","zh":"television news headlines 是電視上新聞故事的簡短主要標題。"},{"en":"News headlines may tell viewers about storms, elections, accidents, or health warnings.","zh":"新聞標題可能告訴觀眾關於風暴、選舉、意外或健康警告的消息。"},{"en":"If headlines are dramatic, viewers may feel urgency before hearing full details.","zh":"如果標題誇張，觀眾在聽到完整細節前可能已感到急迫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes short news titles on television.","zh":"這個片語描述電視上的簡短新聞標題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"claim that","meaning":"聲稱","examples":[{"en":"Some headlines claim that human beings are destroying the environment.","zh":"一些標題聲稱人類正在破壞環境。"},{"en":"To claim that means to state something as true, sometimes without proving it fully.","zh":"claim that 指把某事說成真實，有時未完全證明。"},{"en":"A company may claim that its product works faster than all others.","zh":"公司可能聲稱其產品比所有其他產品更快見效。"},{"en":"If someone claims something serious, readers should ask what evidence supports it.","zh":"如果有人聲稱嚴重事情，讀者應問有甚麼證據支持。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a statement or assertion.","zh":"這個片語引入陳述或主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"inexhaustible dependence on","meaning":"對……無止境的依賴","examples":[{"en":"Modern society appears to have an inexhaustible dependence on oil.","zh":"現代社會似乎對石油有無止境的依賴。"},{"en":"Inexhaustible dependence on something means a seemingly endless reliance on it.","zh":"inexhaustible dependence on something 指看似沒有盡頭地依賴某物。"},{"en":"Some students seem to have an inexhaustible dependence on their phones for entertainment.","zh":"有些學生似乎對手機娛樂有無止境的依賴。"},{"en":"If society depends endlessly on oil, reducing emissions becomes harder.","zh":"如果社會無止境地依賴石油，減少排放會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises a reliance that seems difficult to stop.","zh":"這個片語批評一種似乎難以停止的依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"oil-based machinery","meaning":"以石油為能源的機械","examples":[{"en":"Much modern machinery depends on oil-based technology.","zh":"許多現代機械依賴以石油為能源的技術。"},{"en":"Oil-based machinery is equipment powered by oil, petrol, diesel, or products made from oil.","zh":"oil-based machinery 是由石油、汽油、柴油或石油產品驅動的設備。"},{"en":"Many trucks, ships, and factory machines are oil-based machinery.","zh":"許多貨車、船隻和工廠機器都是以石油為能源的機械。"},{"en":"If oil-based machinery is used heavily, fuel consumption and emissions rise.","zh":"如果大量使用以石油為能源的機械，燃料消耗和排放會上升。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to machines that rely on fossil fuels.","zh":"這個片語指依賴化石燃料的機器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ever more sophisticated","meaning":"越來越先進的","examples":[{"en":"Transport systems are becoming ever more sophisticated.","zh":"交通系統正變得越來越先進。"},{"en":"Ever more sophisticated means increasingly advanced and complex.","zh":"ever more sophisticated 指越來越先進和複雜。"},{"en":"Mobile phones have become ever more sophisticated, with better cameras and faster processors.","zh":"手機變得越來越先進，配備更好相機和更快處理器。"},{"en":"If transport becomes more sophisticated, it may also require more energy and infrastructure.","zh":"如果交通變得更先進，它也可能需要更多能源和基建。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continual advancement.","zh":"這個片語描述持續進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"forms of transport","meaning":"交通工具形式","examples":[{"en":"Modern forms of transport consume large quantities of fuel.","zh":"現代交通工具形式消耗大量燃料。"},{"en":"Forms of transport are different ways of moving people or goods from one place to another.","zh":"forms of transport 是把人或貨物從一地移到另一地的不同方法。"},{"en":"Buses, trains, bicycles, cars, and planes are forms of transport.","zh":"巴士、火車、單車、汽車和飛機都是交通工具形式。"},{"en":"If people choose cleaner forms of transport, pollution may fall.","zh":"如果人們選擇較清潔的交通方式，污染可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to transport methods.","zh":"這個片語指交通方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"nightmare level of","meaning":"令人恐懼的……水平","examples":[{"en":"Some reports describe a nightmare level of greenhouse gas emissions.","zh":"一些報道描述令人恐懼的溫室氣體排放水平。"},{"en":"A nightmare level of something means an extremely worrying or frightening amount of it.","zh":"nightmare level of something 指某事物的數量極令人憂慮或恐懼。"},{"en":"A hospital may face a nightmare level of patients during a severe outbreak.","zh":"在嚴重疫情期間，醫院可能面對令人恐懼的病人數量。"},{"en":"If emissions reach a nightmare level, governments may feel pressure to act quickly.","zh":"如果排放達到令人恐懼的水平，政府可能感到有壓力要迅速行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an alarming extreme.","zh":"這個片語描述令人警覺的極端狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"poison the environment","meaning":"污染；毒害環境","examples":[{"en":"Critics argue that industrial activity is poisoning the environment.","zh":"批評者認為工業活動正在污染環境。"},{"en":"To poison the environment means to damage air, water, soil, or wildlife with harmful substances.","zh":"poison the environment 指用有害物質破壞空氣、水、土壤或野生動物。"},{"en":"Dumping chemicals into a river can poison the environment for years.","zh":"把化學品倒入河流可以毒害環境多年。"},{"en":"If factories release toxic waste, nearby communities may suffer health problems.","zh":"如果工廠釋放有毒廢物，附近社群可能出現健康問題。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly describes environmental harm.","zh":"這個片語強烈描述環境傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rip open the ozone layer","meaning":"嚴重破壞臭氧層","examples":[{"en":"Dramatic reports claim that pollution is ripping open the ozone layer.","zh":"誇張報道聲稱污染正在嚴重破壞臭氧層。"},{"en":"To rip open the ozone layer means to damage it severely, especially by creating or enlarging holes in it.","zh":"rip open the ozone layer 指嚴重破壞臭氧層，特別是造成或擴大臭氧洞。"},{"en":"A headline may use this phrase to make environmental damage sound urgent and violent.","zh":"標題可能使用這個片語，令環境破壞聽起來緊急而猛烈。"},{"en":"If the ozone layer is damaged, more harmful radiation can reach Earth.","zh":"如果臭氧層受損，更多有害輻射可以到達地球。"},{"en":"This phrase is dramatic and often used in alarmist descriptions.","zh":"這個片語較誇張，常用於危言聳聽的描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ozone layer","meaning":"臭氧層","examples":[{"en":"The ozone layer protects the Earth from harmful radiation.","zh":"臭氧層保護地球免受有害輻射。"},{"en":"The ozone layer is a layer of gas high in the atmosphere that absorbs much of the sun’s ultraviolet radiation.","zh":"ozone layer 是大氣高層的一層氣體，可吸收大量太陽紫外線輻射。"},{"en":"Scientists monitor the ozone layer to see whether it is recovering.","zh":"科學家監測臭氧層，以了解它是否正在恢復。"},{"en":"If the ozone layer becomes thinner, people may face greater risk from ultraviolet light.","zh":"如果臭氧層變薄，人們可能面對更高紫外線風險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an important protective part of the atmosphere.","zh":"這個片語指大氣中重要的保護層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"doubters point to","meaning":"懷疑者指出","examples":[{"en":"Doubters point to evidence that they believe supports their position.","zh":"懷疑者指出他們認為支持其立場的證據。"},{"en":"Doubters point to something means sceptical people mention it as support for their argument.","zh":"doubters point to something 指懷疑的人提到某事作為其論點支持。"},{"en":"Doubters of a new school policy may point to past failures.","zh":"懷疑新校政的人可能指出過往失敗。"},{"en":"If doubters point to conflicting evidence, the debate becomes harder to settle.","zh":"如果懷疑者指出互相矛盾的證據，爭論會更難解決。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how sceptics defend their view.","zh":"這個片語描述懷疑者如何捍衛其觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"scientific evidence","meaning":"科學證據","examples":[{"en":"Both sides of the debate claim to have scientific evidence.","zh":"爭論雙方都聲稱擁有科學證據。"},{"en":"Scientific evidence is information gathered through observation, measurement, experiment, or careful research.","zh":"scientific evidence 是透過觀察、量度、實驗或仔細研究收集的資料。"},{"en":"Doctors use scientific evidence before recommending a new medicine.","zh":"醫生在建議新藥前會使用科學證據。"},{"en":"If both sides claim evidence, readers must examine how strong and relevant it is.","zh":"如果雙方都聲稱有證據，讀者必須檢視其強度和相關性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to evidence produced by scientific methods.","zh":"這個片語指由科學方法產生的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"of all the greenhouse gases","meaning":"在所有溫室氣體中","examples":[{"en":"The claim concerns the sources of all the greenhouse gases.","zh":"這項說法涉及所有溫室氣體的來源。"},{"en":"Of all the greenhouse gases means among the full group of gases that trap heat.","zh":"of all the greenhouse gases 指在所有困住熱量的氣體之中。"},{"en":"Of all the subjects, English may require the most daily practice for some students.","zh":"在所有科目中，英文對一些學生而言可能最需要每日練習。"},{"en":"If we compare all greenhouse gases, we must include both natural and human sources.","zh":"如果我們比較所有溫室氣體，就必須包括自然和人為來源。"},{"en":"This phrase sets up comparison within a whole category.","zh":"這個片語在整個類別內建立比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"man-made sources","meaning":"人為來源","examples":[{"en":"Some greenhouse gases come from man-made sources.","zh":"一些溫室氣體來自人為來源。"},{"en":"Man-made sources are causes created by human activity rather than nature.","zh":"man-made sources 是由人類活動而非自然造成的來源。"},{"en":"Traffic, factories, and power stations are man-made sources of air pollution.","zh":"交通、工廠和發電站是空氣污染的人為來源。"},{"en":"If emissions come from man-made sources, human choices can reduce them.","zh":"如果排放來自人為來源，人類選擇就可以減少它們。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts human causes with natural causes.","zh":"這個片語把人為原因與自然原因作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"natural emissions","meaning":"自然排放","examples":[{"en":"Many greenhouse gases also result from natural emissions.","zh":"許多溫室氣體也來自自然排放。"},{"en":"Natural emissions are gases or substances released by natural processes.","zh":"natural emissions 是由自然過程釋放的氣體或物質。"},{"en":"Volcanoes, wetlands, and forests can produce natural emissions.","zh":"火山、濕地和森林都可以產生自然排放。"},{"en":"If natural emissions are large, scientists must separate them from human-made emissions.","zh":"如果自然排放很大，科學家必須把它們與人為排放分開。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to pollution or gases released by nature.","zh":"這個片語指由自然釋放的污染物或氣體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"who to believe","meaning":"應該相信誰","examples":[{"en":"The conflicting evidence makes it difficult to know who to believe.","zh":"互相矛盾的證據令人難以知道應該相信誰。"},{"en":"Who to believe means which person or source should be trusted.","zh":"who to believe 指應該信任哪個人或來源。"},{"en":"If two doctors give different advice, a patient may not know who to believe.","zh":"如果兩位醫生給出不同建議，病人可能不知道應該相信誰。"},{"en":"When claims conflict, people should compare evidence rather than follow the loudest voice.","zh":"當主張互相衝突，人們應比較證據，而不是跟隨最大聲的人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uncertainty about trust.","zh":"這個片語描述信任上的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"environmentalist","meaning":"環保人士","examples":[{"en":"An environmentalist may encourage people to change their habits.","zh":"環保人士可能鼓勵人們改變習慣。"},{"en":"An environmentalist is a person who works to protect the natural environment.","zh":"environmentalist 是致力保護自然環境的人。"},{"en":"An environmentalist may campaign against plastic waste in the community.","zh":"環保人士可能在社區發起反塑膠廢物運動。"},{"en":"If environmentalists raise awareness, people may reduce waste or save energy.","zh":"如果環保人士提高意識，人們可能減少廢物或節省能源。"},{"en":"This word refers to someone concerned with environmental protection.","zh":"這個詞指關注環境保護的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"exhort someone to","meaning":"敦促某人……","examples":[{"en":"Environmentalists exhort the public to reduce unnecessary consumption.","zh":"環保人士敦促公眾減少不必要消費。"},{"en":"To exhort someone to do something means to strongly urge or encourage them to do it.","zh":"exhort someone to do something 指強烈敦促或鼓勵某人做某事。"},{"en":"A coach may exhort players to keep trying after a difficult first half.","zh":"教練可能在困難的上半場後敦促球員繼續努力。"},{"en":"If campaigners exhort people to act, they use strong language to push for change.","zh":"如果倡議者敦促人們行動，他們會使用強烈語言推動改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than simply “advise”.","zh":"這個片語比 simply “advise” 更強烈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"leave the car at home","meaning":"不駕車外出","examples":[{"en":"People are encouraged to leave the car at home and use public transport.","zh":"人們被鼓勵不駕車外出，改用公共交通。"},{"en":"To leave the car at home means not to drive and to use another way to travel.","zh":"leave the car at home 指不開車，使用另一種交通方式。"},{"en":"A student may leave the car at home and walk to school on a sunny day.","zh":"天氣晴朗時，學生可能不坐車而步行上學。"},{"en":"If more people leave cars at home, traffic and emissions may decrease.","zh":"如果更多人不駕車外出，交通擠塞和排放可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing not to drive.","zh":"這個片語描述選擇不開車。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reusable products","meaning":"可重複使用的產品","examples":[{"en":"Reusable products can reduce the amount of waste produced.","zh":"可重複使用的產品可以減少產生的廢物量。"},{"en":"Reusable products are items that can be used many times instead of being thrown away after one use.","zh":"reusable products 是可以多次使用，而不是用一次便丟棄的物品。"},{"en":"Water bottles, cloth bags, and food containers are reusable products.","zh":"水樽、布袋和食物盒都是可重複使用的產品。"},{"en":"If people use reusable products, fewer disposable items end up in landfills.","zh":"如果人們使用可重複使用的產品，較少一次性物品會進入堆填區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes products designed for repeated use.","zh":"這個片語描述設計作重複使用的產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"packaged in recycled paper","meaning":"以再造紙包裝","examples":[{"en":"Consumers may choose products packaged in recycled paper.","zh":"消費者可能選擇以再造紙包裝的產品。"},{"en":"Packaged in recycled paper means wrapped or contained in paper made from reused materials.","zh":"packaged in recycled paper 指用由再用材料製成的紙包裹或盛載。"},{"en":"A bakery may sell bread packaged in recycled paper bags.","zh":"麵包店可能出售以再造紙袋包裝的麵包。"},{"en":"If more products use recycled packaging, demand for new paper may fall.","zh":"如果更多產品使用再造包裝，對新紙張的需求可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an environmentally friendlier packaging choice.","zh":"這個片語描述較環保的包裝選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"recycled paper","meaning":"再造紙","examples":[{"en":"Using recycled paper can reduce demand for new materials.","zh":"使用再造紙可以減少對新材料的需求。"},{"en":"Recycled paper is paper made from used paper or recovered fibres.","zh":"recycled paper 是由舊紙或回收纖維製成的紙。"},{"en":"Schools may print notices on recycled paper to reduce waste.","zh":"學校可能用再造紙印通告，以減少廢物。"},{"en":"If recycled paper replaces new paper, fewer trees may need to be cut down.","zh":"如果再造紙取代新紙，可能需要砍伐較少樹木。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to paper made by reusing materials.","zh":"這個片語指透過重用材料製成的紙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"plant trees in the back yard","meaning":"在後院種樹","examples":[{"en":"Some environmentalists encourage people to plant trees in the back yard.","zh":"一些環保人士鼓勵人們在後院種樹。"},{"en":"To plant trees in the back yard means to grow trees in the garden or open space behind a home.","zh":"plant trees in the back yard 指在家後方花園或空地種植樹木。"},{"en":"A family may plant trees in the back yard to create shade in summer.","zh":"家庭可能在後院種樹，以在夏天製造陰影。"},{"en":"If more people plant trees, neighbourhoods may become cooler and greener.","zh":"如果更多人種樹，社區可能變得更涼爽和更綠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small personal action for the environment.","zh":"這個片語描述一項個人層面的環保小行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sceptics","meaning":"懷疑論者","examples":[{"en":"Climate sceptics question whether humans are the principal cause of warming.","zh":"氣候懷疑論者質疑人類是否是暖化的主要原因。"},{"en":"Sceptics are people who doubt or question a claim.","zh":"sceptics 是懷疑或質疑某主張的人。"},{"en":"Sceptics may ask for more evidence before accepting a new medicine or policy.","zh":"懷疑論者在接受新藥或政策前可能要求更多證據。"},{"en":"If sceptics raise fair questions, they can help improve the quality of debate.","zh":"如果懷疑論者提出合理問題，他們可以幫助提高辯論質素。"},{"en":"This word describes people who are not easily convinced.","zh":"這個詞描述不容易被說服的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"big businesses","meaning":"大型企業","examples":[{"en":"Many big businesses have a financial interest in the climate debate.","zh":"許多大型企業在氣候爭論中有經濟利益。"},{"en":"Big businesses are large companies with significant money, influence, and operations.","zh":"big businesses 是擁有大量資金、影響力和業務的大公司。"},{"en":"Big businesses may include oil companies, airlines, banks, and supermarket chains.","zh":"大型企業可能包括石油公司、航空公司、銀行和超級市場連鎖店。"},{"en":"If big businesses are affected by climate rules, they may try to influence policy.","zh":"如果大型企業受氣候規則影響，它們可能試圖影響政策。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to large powerful companies.","zh":"這個片語指大型且有權力的公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have the most to lose","meaning":"蒙受最大損失","examples":[{"en":"Some industries have the most to lose from stricter environmental rules.","zh":"一些行業會因更嚴格環境規則而蒙受最大損失。"},{"en":"To have the most to lose means to face the greatest possible loss or damage.","zh":"have the most to lose 指面對最大可能損失或損害。"},{"en":"A shop near a school has the most to lose if students stop coming during lunch.","zh":"如果學生午飯時間不再光顧，學校附近的小店可能蒙受最大損失。"},{"en":"If new laws reduce oil use, oil companies may lose more than other businesses.","zh":"如果新法律減少石油使用，石油公司可能比其他企業損失更多。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the group most at risk.","zh":"這個片語指出最有風險的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make a mountain out of a molehill","meaning":"小題大做","examples":[{"en":"Sceptics argue that society is making a mountain out of a molehill.","zh":"懷疑論者認為社會正在小題大做。"},{"en":"To make a mountain out of a molehill means to treat a small problem as if it were a huge one.","zh":"make a mountain out of a molehill 指把小問題當成大問題處理。"},{"en":"A student makes a mountain out of a molehill if they panic over one small spelling mistake.","zh":"如果學生因一個小串字錯誤而恐慌，就是小題大做。"},{"en":"If people exaggerate a minor issue, they may waste time and energy.","zh":"如果人們誇大輕微問題，可能浪費時間和精力。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises overreaction.","zh":"這個片語批評過度反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the jury is still out","meaning":"尚未有定論","examples":[{"en":"The jury is still out on the precise causes of recent climate change.","zh":"近期氣候變化的確切成因尚未有定論。"},{"en":"The jury is still out means no final decision or agreement has been reached.","zh":"the jury is still out 指尚未作出最終決定或達成共識。"},{"en":"The jury is still out on whether the new homework policy will improve results.","zh":"新功課政策是否會改善成績仍未有定論。"},{"en":"If evidence remains mixed, people may say the jury is still out.","zh":"如果證據仍然混雜，人們可能說尚未有定論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unresolved debate.","zh":"這個片語描述未解決的爭議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as far as I am concerned","meaning":"就我而言","examples":[{"en":"As far as I am concerned, the evidence remains inconclusive.","zh":"就我而言，證據仍未有定論。"},{"en":"As far as I am concerned means in my opinion or from my point of view.","zh":"as far as I am concerned 指在我看來或從我的角度而言。"},{"en":"As far as I am concerned, students learn best when they practise with feedback.","zh":"就我而言，學生在有回饋的練習中學得最好。"},{"en":"If a writer uses this phrase, they are clearly presenting a personal view.","zh":"如果作者使用這個片語，他是在清楚呈現個人看法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an opinion rather than a proven fact.","zh":"這個片語引入意見，而不是已證實事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生為每題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the letter option that matches the answer.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇與答案相符的字母選項。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may choose A, B, C, or D.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能選擇 A、B、C 或 D。"},{"en":"If students understand the meaning but write the wrong letter, they may lose marks.","zh":"如果學生理解意思但寫錯字母，可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"write the correct letter","meaning":"寫上正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students write the correct letter in the answer boxes.","zh":"學生在答案框中寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"To write the correct letter means to put the chosen answer letter in the required space.","zh":"write the correct letter 指把所選答案字母寫在指定位置。"},{"en":"If the answer is option C, students should write C, not the whole sentence.","zh":"如果答案是選項 C，學生應寫 C，而不是整句。"},{"en":"Following the answer format helps avoid losing marks unnecessarily.","zh":"遵守答案格式有助避免不必要失分。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds candidates how to record their answer.","zh":"這個片語提醒考生如何記錄答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"causes of global warming","meaning":"全球暖化的成因","examples":[{"en":"The questions examine different views about the causes of global warming.","zh":"這些問題檢視關於全球暖化成因的不同觀點。"},{"en":"Causes of global warming are factors that may make the Earth’s average temperature rise.","zh":"causes of global warming 是可能令地球平均氣溫上升的因素。"},{"en":"Burning fossil fuels is often discussed as one possible cause of global warming.","zh":"燃燒化石燃料常被討論為全球暖化的一個可能成因。"},{"en":"If people disagree about the causes, they may also disagree about the solutions.","zh":"如果人們對成因意見不一，他們也可能對解決方案意見不一。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on why warming happens.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於暖化為何發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"does not say what he believes","meaning":"沒有說明他的看法","examples":[{"en":"The writer does not clearly say what he believes about the cause.","zh":"作者沒有清楚說明他對成因的看法。"},{"en":"Does not say what he believes means the writer does not clearly reveal his personal opinion.","zh":"does not say what he believes 指作者沒有清楚透露其個人意見。"},{"en":"In an essay, a writer may discuss both sides but not say what he believes.","zh":"在文章中，作者可能討論雙方，但沒有說明他的看法。"},{"en":"If the writer’s view is not stated, readers should not invent it.","zh":"如果作者觀點沒有說出，讀者不應自行編造。"},{"en":"This phrase describes missing or unclear personal opinion.","zh":"這個片語描述個人意見缺失或不清楚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as to the cause of","meaning":"至於……的成因","examples":[{"en":"As to the cause of global warming, experts remain divided.","zh":"至於全球暖化的成因，專家仍意見分歧。"},{"en":"As to the cause of something means regarding or concerning why it happened.","zh":"as to the cause of something 指關於某事為何發生。"},{"en":"As to the cause of the accident, the police are still investigating.","zh":"至於意外的成因，警方仍在調查。"},{"en":"If people disagree as to the cause, solving the problem becomes harder.","zh":"如果人們對成因意見不一，解決問題會更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a topic about reasons.","zh":"這個片語引入關於原因的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"depend on whom you consult","meaning":"取決於你諮詢誰","examples":[{"en":"The answer may depend on whom you consult.","zh":"答案可能取決於你諮詢誰。"},{"en":"To depend on whom you consult means the answer may change according to which person you ask.","zh":"depend on whom you consult 指答案可能按你詢問哪個人而改變。"},{"en":"A patient may hear different treatment advice depending on which doctor they consult.","zh":"病人可能因諮詢不同醫生而聽到不同治療建議。"},{"en":"If experts hold different views, consulting different people can lead to different conclusions.","zh":"如果專家持不同觀點，諮詢不同人可能導致不同結論。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the source of advice matters.","zh":"這個片語強調意見來源很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"consult experts","meaning":"諮詢專家","examples":[{"en":"People often consult experts before reaching a conclusion.","zh":"人們在得出結論前常諮詢專家。"},{"en":"To consult experts means to ask knowledgeable specialists for advice or information.","zh":"consult experts 指向有知識的專家尋求建議或資訊。"},{"en":"A school may consult experts before changing its mental health policy.","zh":"學校在改變精神健康政策前可能諮詢專家。"},{"en":"If a topic is technical, consulting experts can prevent simple mistakes.","zh":"如果主題具技術性，諮詢專家可以避免簡單錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes seeking professional guidance.","zh":"這個片語描述尋求專業指導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be of the opinion that","meaning":"認為","examples":[{"en":"Most of the surveyed meteorologists were of the opinion that the change was natural.","zh":"大多數受訪氣象學家認為這種變化是自然的。"},{"en":"To be of the opinion that means to believe or think something.","zh":"be of the opinion that 指相信或認為某事。"},{"en":"Many parents are of the opinion that children need enough sleep before exams.","zh":"許多家長認為孩子考試前需要足夠睡眠。"},{"en":"If a majority is of one opinion, that view may carry weight in a debate.","zh":"如果大多數人持某意見，該觀點在爭論中可能有分量。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal way to report belief.","zh":"這個片語是報告信念的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be the result of","meaning":"是……的結果","examples":[{"en":"Some experts believe that warming is the result of natural cycles.","zh":"一些專家相信暖化是自然循環的結果。"},{"en":"To be the result of something means to be caused by it.","zh":"be the result of something 指由某事造成。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be the result of steady practice.","zh":"學生進步可能是穩定練習的結果。"},{"en":"If warming is the result of natural cycles, human responsibility may be seen differently.","zh":"如果暖化是自然循環的結果，人類責任可能被不同看待。"},{"en":"This phrase links an outcome to its cause.","zh":"這個片語把結果與原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"natural cyclical changes","meaning":"自然周期性變化","examples":[{"en":"Natural cyclical changes can cause temperatures to rise and fall.","zh":"自然周期性變化可以令氣溫上升和下降。"},{"en":"Natural cyclical changes are repeated changes that occur in nature over time.","zh":"natural cyclical changes 是自然界隨時間反覆發生的變化。"},{"en":"Ocean currents and seasons can be examples of natural cycles affecting weather.","zh":"洋流和季節可以是影響天氣的自然循環例子。"},{"en":"If a temperature rise follows a natural cycle, it may later slow or reverse.","zh":"如果氣溫上升跟隨自然循環，它日後可能放慢或逆轉。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recurring natural patterns.","zh":"這個片語描述反覆出現的自然模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"understanding of the weather","meaning":"對天氣的了解","examples":[{"en":"Our understanding of the weather is still limited.","zh":"我們對天氣的了解仍然有限。"},{"en":"Understanding of the weather means knowledge of how weather works and changes.","zh":"understanding of the weather 指對天氣如何運作和變化的認識。"},{"en":"Better understanding of the weather helps farmers decide when to plant crops.","zh":"更好了解天氣有助農民決定何時種植作物。"},{"en":"If our understanding is limited, forecasts may sometimes be wrong.","zh":"如果我們的理解有限，預報有時可能錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to knowledge about atmospheric conditions.","zh":"這個片語指對大氣狀況的認識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lead to reliable predictions","meaning":"得出可靠預測","examples":[{"en":"Better scientific knowledge may lead to reliable predictions.","zh":"更好的科學知識可能得出可靠預測。"},{"en":"To lead to reliable predictions means to make future forecasts more trustworthy.","zh":"lead to reliable predictions 指令未來預測更可信。"},{"en":"More exam practice data may lead to reliable predictions about student performance.","zh":"更多考試練習數據可能得出關於學生表現的可靠預測。"},{"en":"If scientists understand more variables, their weather predictions may improve.","zh":"如果科學家理解更多變數，他們的天氣預測可能改善。"},{"en":"This phrase connects better knowledge with better forecasting.","zh":"這個片語把更好知識與更好預測連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not very developed yet","meaning":"尚未充分發展","examples":[{"en":"Our understanding of complex climate systems is not very developed yet.","zh":"我們對複雜氣候系統的理解尚未充分發展。"},{"en":"Not very developed yet means still basic, incomplete, or immature.","zh":"not very developed yet 指仍然基礎、不完整或未成熟。"},{"en":"A child’s handwriting may be not very developed yet in the first year of school.","zh":"孩子入學第一年，字跡可能尚未充分發展。"},{"en":"If a field of research is not developed yet, conclusions may change later.","zh":"如果某研究領域尚未充分發展，結論日後可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something still at an early stage.","zh":"這個片語描述某事仍處於早期階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reflect someone’s current view","meaning":"反映某人目前的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which statement reflects Hansen’s current view.","zh":"題目問哪項陳述反映 Hansen 目前的觀點。"},{"en":"To reflect someone’s current view means to show what that person believes now.","zh":"reflect someone’s current view 指顯示某人現在相信甚麼。"},{"en":"A recent interview may reflect a politician’s current view better than an old speech.","zh":"最近訪問可能比舊演講更能反映政治人物目前的觀點。"},{"en":"If a person changes their opinion, old statements may not reflect their current view.","zh":"如果一個人改變意見，舊說法可能不能反映他目前觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on present opinion.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於當前意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"nearly impossible to predict","meaning":"幾乎不可能預測","examples":[{"en":"It may be nearly impossible to predict long-term climatic change accurately.","zh":"準確預測長期氣候變化可能幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"Nearly impossible to predict means extremely difficult to forecast correctly.","zh":"nearly impossible to predict 指極難正確預測。"},{"en":"It is nearly impossible to predict exactly what a baby will become as an adult.","zh":"要準確預測嬰兒長大後會成為怎樣的人，幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"If too many variables interact, accurate prediction becomes very difficult.","zh":"如果太多變數互相作用，準確預測會變得非常困難。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the limits of forecasting.","zh":"這個片語強調預測的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"significant link between","meaning":"……之間的重大關聯","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers propose a significant link between emissions and climate change.","zh":"一些研究人員提出排放與氣候變化之間有重大關聯。"},{"en":"A significant link between two things is an important connection between them.","zh":"significant link between two things 指兩者之間重要的連繫。"},{"en":"Researchers may find a significant link between sleep and exam performance.","zh":"研究人員可能發現睡眠與考試表現之間有重大關聯。"},{"en":"If emissions and warming are strongly linked, reducing emissions becomes important.","zh":"如果排放與暖化有強烈關聯，減少排放就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a meaningful relationship.","zh":"這個片語描述有意義的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"agree with the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the writer’s views.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否與作者觀點一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the views of someone means to match that person’s opinions.","zh":"agree with the views of someone 指符合某人的意見。"},{"en":"In a reading test, a statement may agree with the writer’s views even if it uses different words.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，陳述即使用不同字眼，也可能與作者觀點一致。"},{"en":"If the writer is doubtful, a statement showing certainty may not agree with his view.","zh":"如果作者抱懷疑態度，表示肯定的陳述可能不符合其觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in YES, NO, NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於 YES、NO、NOT GIVEN 題型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A “NO” answer means that the statement contradicts the writer’s views.","zh":"“NO” 答案表示該陳述與作者觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what that person believes.","zh":"contradict the views of someone 指說出與某人信念相反的內容。"},{"en":"If a writer supports public transport, a statement praising only private cars may contradict his views.","zh":"如果作者支持公共交通，只稱讚私家車的陳述可能與其觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"When a statement directly conflicts with the writer’s opinion, the answer is usually NO.","zh":"當陳述與作者意見直接衝突，答案通常是 NO。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disagreement with someone’s stated position.","zh":"這個片語描述與某人明確立場不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"“NOT GIVEN” means it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"“NOT GIVEN” 表示無法判斷作者怎樣想。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資料作出判斷。"},{"en":"If an article never mentions cost, it is impossible to say whether the plan is cheap.","zh":"如果文章從未提及成本，就無法判斷計劃是否便宜。"},{"en":"When evidence is missing, students should not guess from outside knowledge.","zh":"當證據缺失，學生不應使用外部知識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a situation where no safe conclusion can be made.","zh":"這個片語描述不能安全得出結論的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"at the same time that","meaning":"與……同時","examples":[{"en":"Weather models improved at the same time that computing power increased.","zh":"天氣模型改善，與電腦運算能力提升同時發生。"},{"en":"At the same time that means while another event or change was happening.","zh":"at the same time that 指當另一事件或變化發生時。"},{"en":"Students became more confident at the same time that they practised speaking weekly.","zh":"學生變得更有信心，與他們每週練習口語同時發生。"},{"en":"If two changes happen together, one may help explain the other.","zh":"如果兩種變化同時發生，其中一種可能幫助解釋另一種。"},{"en":"This phrase links two simultaneous developments.","zh":"這個片語連接兩個同時出現的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"weather forecasters","meaning":"天氣預報員","examples":[{"en":"Weather forecasters use computer models to predict future conditions.","zh":"天氣預報員使用電腦模型預測未來情況。"},{"en":"Weather forecasters are people or organisations that predict weather.","zh":"weather forecasters 是預測天氣的人或機構。"},{"en":"Weather forecasters warn the public about typhoons, heavy rain, and heatwaves.","zh":"天氣預報員警告公眾颱風、大雨和熱浪。"},{"en":"If forecasters have better data, their warnings may become more accurate.","zh":"如果預報員有更好數據，他們的警告可能更準確。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to professionals who make weather predictions.","zh":"這個片語指作出天氣預測的專業人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"become more expert","meaning":"變得更專業","examples":[{"en":"Greater experience may help weather forecasters become more expert.","zh":"更多經驗可能幫助天氣預報員變得更專業。"},{"en":"To become more expert means to become more skilled and knowledgeable.","zh":"become more expert 指變得更熟練和更有知識。"},{"en":"A teacher becomes more expert after years of marking essays and helping students.","zh":"老師在多年批改文章和幫助學生後會變得更專業。"},{"en":"If forecasters gain experience and better tools, their judgement may improve.","zh":"如果預報員累積經驗和更好工具，其判斷可能改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth in professional ability.","zh":"這個片語描述專業能力提升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"most of the increase","meaning":"大部分升幅","examples":[{"en":"The statement concerns when most of the temperature increase occurred.","zh":"該陳述關乎大部分氣溫升幅何時發生。"},{"en":"Most of the increase means the largest part of the rise.","zh":"most of the increase 指升幅中的最大部分。"},{"en":"Most of the increase in school applications happened after the open day.","zh":"學校申請數大部分升幅發生在開放日後。"},{"en":"If most of the increase happened early, later factors may not explain the whole trend.","zh":"如果大部分升幅早期已發生，後來因素可能不能解釋整個趨勢。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where the main rise occurred.","zh":"這個片語指出主要升幅在哪裡發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"blame ourselves for","meaning":"因……責怪自己","examples":[{"en":"Some media reports encourage us to blame ourselves for global warming.","zh":"一些傳媒報道鼓勵我們因全球暖化責怪自己。"},{"en":"To blame ourselves for something means to believe we are responsible for causing it.","zh":"blame ourselves for something 指相信我們要為造成某事負責。"},{"en":"A student may blame themselves for a poor mark if they did not revise.","zh":"如果學生沒有溫習，他可能因低分而責怪自己。"},{"en":"If people blame themselves, they may feel guilt and pressure to change behaviour.","zh":"如果人們責怪自己，他們可能感到內疚並有壓力改變行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes placing responsibility on oneself.","zh":"這個片語描述把責任放在自己身上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"encourage the public to","meaning":"鼓勵公眾去……","examples":[{"en":"Environmental campaigns encourage the public to change its behaviour.","zh":"環保宣傳活動鼓勵公眾改變行為。"},{"en":"To encourage the public to do something means to persuade ordinary people to take action.","zh":"encourage the public to do something 指說服普通市民採取行動。"},{"en":"Health campaigns encourage the public to wash hands and exercise regularly.","zh":"健康宣傳鼓勵公眾洗手和定期運動。"},{"en":"If the public changes behaviour, small actions may add up across society.","zh":"如果公眾改變行為，小行動可以在整個社會累積起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public persuasion.","zh":"這個片語描述對公眾的說服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"environmentally friendly vehicles","meaning":"環保車輛","examples":[{"en":"Electric cars are often promoted as environmentally friendly vehicles.","zh":"電動車常被宣傳為環保車輛。"},{"en":"Environmentally friendly vehicles are vehicles designed to reduce harm to the environment.","zh":"environmentally friendly vehicles 是設計上減少環境傷害的車輛。"},{"en":"Buses, bicycles, and electric cars may be seen as more environmentally friendly than petrol cars.","zh":"巴士、單車和電動車可能被視為比汽油車更環保。"},{"en":"If vehicles use less fuel, they may produce fewer emissions.","zh":"如果車輛使用較少燃料，它們可能產生較少排放。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transport options that are meant to be greener.","zh":"這個片語描述旨在更環保的交通選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"combat global warming","meaning":"應對全球暖化","examples":[{"en":"Reducing fossil-fuel use may help combat global warming.","zh":"減少使用化石燃料可能有助應對全球暖化。"},{"en":"To combat global warming means to fight against or reduce the problem of rising global temperatures.","zh":"combat global warming 指對抗或減少全球氣溫上升的問題。"},{"en":"A city can combat global warming by improving public transport and planting trees.","zh":"城市可以透過改善公共交通和種樹來應對全球暖化。"},{"en":"If emissions fall, efforts to combat warming may become more effective.","zh":"如果排放下降，應對暖化的努力可能更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active efforts to reduce climate change.","zh":"這個片語描述減少氣候變化的積極努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be effective at persuading","meaning":"善於說服……","examples":[{"en":"Some campaigners are highly effective at persuading people to act.","zh":"一些倡議者非常善於說服人們行動。"},{"en":"To be effective at persuading means to be good at convincing people to change their views or behaviour.","zh":"be effective at persuading 指擅長令人改變看法或行為。"},{"en":"A teacher is effective at persuading students when examples make the reason clear.","zh":"當例子令原因清楚，老師就善於說服學生。"},{"en":"If campaigners use personal stories, they may persuade the public more easily.","zh":"如果倡議者使用個人故事，他們可能更容易說服公眾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong persuasive ability.","zh":"這個片語描述強大的說服能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be kind to the environment","meaning":"愛護環境","examples":[{"en":"People are encouraged to be kind to the environment.","zh":"人們被鼓勵愛護環境。"},{"en":"To be kind to the environment means to act in ways that reduce harm to nature.","zh":"be kind to the environment 指以減少對自然傷害的方式行動。"},{"en":"Using less plastic and saving electricity are ways to be kind to the environment.","zh":"少用塑膠和節省電力都是愛護環境的方法。"},{"en":"If many people make small greener choices, overall damage may decrease.","zh":"如果許多人作出較環保的小選擇，整體破壞可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase gives environmental responsibility a simple moral tone.","zh":"這個片語用簡單道德語氣表達環境責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be on the side of","meaning":"支持……的一方","examples":[{"en":"Many large companies are on the side of the climate sceptics.","zh":"許多大型公司支持氣候懷疑論者的一方。"},{"en":"To be on the side of someone means to support their position in a disagreement.","zh":"be on the side of someone 指在分歧中支持某人的立場。"},{"en":"In a school debate, students may be on the side of stricter homework rules.","zh":"在學校辯論中，學生可能支持更嚴格功課規則的一方。"},{"en":"If a company has money to lose, it may support the side that resists regulation.","zh":"如果公司有金錢損失風險，它可能支持反對規管的一方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking or supporting one side in a dispute.","zh":"這個片語描述在爭議中站在或支持某一方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as regards","meaning":"關於；至於","examples":[{"en":"Opinion remains divided as regards the cause of global warming.","zh":"關於全球暖化的成因，意見仍然分歧。"},{"en":"As regards means concerning or about a particular subject.","zh":"as regards 指關於或至於某個特定主題。"},{"en":"As regards homework, students prefer shorter tasks with clearer instructions.","zh":"關於功課，學生較喜歡較短而指示清晰的任務。"},{"en":"If experts disagree as regards the cause, readers should compare their evidence.","zh":"如果專家關於成因意見不一，讀者應比較其證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal way to introduce a topic.","zh":"這個片語是引入主題的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"complete the sentences below","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the sentences using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用篇章中的字詞完成以下句子。"},{"en":"To complete the sentences below means to fill the blanks in the following sentences.","zh":"complete the sentences below 指填寫以下句子中的空格。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students must copy the exact words if the instruction requires it.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，如果指示要求，學生必須抄寫原文字詞。"},{"en":"If the completed sentence is ungrammatical, the answer may be wrong.","zh":"如果完成後的句子不合文法，答案可能錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than three words.","zh":"每個答案應不多於三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means one, two, or three words only.","zh":"no more than three words 指只能用一個、兩個或三個英文詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “recycled paper”, students should not add extra words.","zh":"如果答案是 “recycled paper”，學生不應加上額外字詞。"},{"en":"Writing four words may lose marks even if the meaning is close.","zh":"即使意思接近，寫四個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個片語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"blank space","meaning":"空格","examples":[{"en":"Each blank space must be completed with wording from the passage.","zh":"每個空格都必須用篇章中的字詞完成。"},{"en":"A blank space is an empty part of a sentence where an answer must be written.","zh":"blank space 是句子中需要填寫答案的空白部分。"},{"en":"In a grammar exercise, students fill each blank space with the correct verb form.","zh":"在文法練習中，學生在每個空格填入正確動詞形式。"},{"en":"If the blank space comes after “an”, the answer may need to begin with a vowel sound.","zh":"如果空格位於 “an” 之後，答案可能需要以元音開頭。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the empty answer position in a task.","zh":"這個片語指題目中的空白答案位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"As well as planting trees, people can reduce unnecessary car use.","zh":"除了種樹之外，人們還可以減少不必要的汽車使用。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to.","zh":"as well as 指除了某事之外。"},{"en":"As well as studying grammar, students should read good examples.","zh":"除了學習文法之外，學生也應閱讀好例子。"},{"en":"If people use public transport as well as recycling, their environmental impact may fall further.","zh":"如果人們除了回收之外還使用公共交通，他們的環境影響可能進一步下降。"},{"en":"This phrase adds one action or item to another.","zh":"這個片語把一個行動或項目加入另一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"choose products","meaning":"選擇產品","examples":[{"en":"Environmentally conscious consumers choose products carefully.","zh":"有環保意識的消費者會仔細選擇產品。"},{"en":"To choose products means to select items to buy or use.","zh":"choose products 指選擇要購買或使用的物品。"},{"en":"Shoppers may choose products with less packaging to reduce waste.","zh":"購物者可能選擇包裝較少的產品，以減少廢物。"},{"en":"If consumers choose greener products, companies may change what they sell.","zh":"如果消費者選擇較環保產品，公司可能改變銷售內容。"},{"en":"This phrase describes consumer decision-making.","zh":"這個片語描述消費者決策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be wrapped in","meaning":"以……包裝","examples":[{"en":"Some products are wrapped in recycled paper.","zh":"一些產品以再造紙包裝。"},{"en":"To be wrapped in something means to be covered or packaged with that material.","zh":"be wrapped in something 指用某材料包裹或包裝。"},{"en":"A gift may be wrapped in colourful paper before a birthday party.","zh":"禮物可能在生日會前以彩色紙包裝。"},{"en":"If products are wrapped in plastic, they may create more waste than paper packaging.","zh":"如果產品以塑膠包裝，它們可能比紙包裝製造更多廢物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes packaging material.","zh":"這個片語描述包裝材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be used more than once","meaning":"可以多次使用","examples":[{"en":"Reusable products can be used more than once.","zh":"可重複使用的產品可以多次使用。"},{"en":"To be used more than once means to be used repeatedly instead of thrown away after one use.","zh":"be used more than once 指可以重複使用，而不是用一次便丟棄。"},{"en":"A metal lunch box can be used more than once, unlike a disposable plastic box.","zh":"金屬飯盒可以多次使用，不像一次性塑膠盒。"},{"en":"If items are used many times, less rubbish is produced.","zh":"如果物品被多次使用，產生的垃圾會較少。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the basic idea of reuse.","zh":"這個片語解釋重用的基本概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make too much fuss about","meaning":"對……過分大驚小怪","examples":[{"en":"Some sceptics believe that people make too much fuss about global warming.","zh":"一些懷疑論者認為人們對全球暖化過分大驚小怪。"},{"en":"To make too much fuss about something means to worry, complain, or react more than necessary.","zh":"make too much fuss about something 指對某事過度擔心、抱怨或反應。"},{"en":"A student may make too much fuss about one small mistake in a long essay.","zh":"學生可能對長文中的一個小錯誤過分大驚小怪。"},{"en":"If a problem is genuinely serious, calling concern “too much fuss” may be unfair.","zh":"如果問題真的嚴重，把關注說成小題大做可能不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises exaggerated concern or reaction.","zh":"這個片語批評誇張的關注或反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"financial interests","meaning":"經濟利益","examples":[{"en":"Large businesses may have financial interests in the climate debate.","zh":"大型企業可能在氣候爭論中有經濟利益。"},{"en":"Financial interests are money-related benefits, risks, or reasons that may influence someone’s position.","zh":"financial interests 是可能影響某人立場的金錢相關好處、風險或原因。"},{"en":"A company has financial interests when a new law could affect its profits.","zh":"當新法律可能影響公司利潤時，該公司就有經濟利益。"},{"en":"If people have financial interests in a debate, their opinions may not be neutral.","zh":"如果人們在爭論中有經濟利益，他們的意見可能並不中立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes economic motives behind a view.","zh":"這個片語描述觀點背後的經濟動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"have much to lose","meaning":"可能蒙受重大損失","examples":[{"en":"Industries affected by environmental restrictions may have much to lose.","zh":"受環境限制影響的行業可能蒙受重大損失。"},{"en":"To have much to lose means to face serious possible loss if something happens.","zh":"have much to lose 指如果某事發生，可能面對嚴重損失。"},{"en":"A restaurant has much to lose if customers stop trusting its food safety.","zh":"如果顧客不再信任食物安全，餐廳可能蒙受重大損失。"},{"en":"If strict climate rules reduce profits, some companies may oppose them strongly.","zh":"如果嚴格氣候規則減少利潤，一些公司可能強烈反對。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a person or group may resist change.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何某人或群體可能抗拒改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 134 - Global Warming.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 135":[{"front":"extinct","meaning":"已滅絕的","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines why the giant deer became extinct.","zh":"文章探討巨鹿為何滅絕。"},{"en":"Extinct means a species no longer exists anywhere in the world.","zh":"extinct 指一個物種在世界任何地方都不再存在。"},{"en":"Dinosaurs are extinct, so no living dinosaur can be seen in a zoo.","zh":"恐龍已經滅絕，所以動物園中看不到活恐龍。"},{"en":"A species may become extinct when hunting, climate change, or habitat loss destroys its population.","zh":"當狩獵、氣候變化或棲息地喪失摧毀一個種群時，物種可能滅絕。"},{"en":"Extinct is stronger than rare: rare animals still exist, but extinct animals do not.","zh":"extinct 比 rare 更強烈：稀有動物仍然存在，但已滅絕動物則不存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"giant deer","meaning":"巨鹿","examples":[{"en":"The giant deer survived longer than scientists previously believed.","zh":"巨鹿生存的時間比科學家先前相信的更長。"},{"en":"The giant deer was a very large prehistoric deer known for its enormous antlers.","zh":"giant deer 指一種非常大型的史前鹿，以巨大鹿角聞名。"},{"en":"A museum may display giant deer skeletons to show how large some ancient animals were.","zh":"博物館可能展示巨鹿骨骼，以顯示某些古代動物有多巨大。"},{"en":"If new dating evidence is found, scientists may change their view of when the giant deer died out.","zh":"如果發現新的定年證據，科學家可能改變對巨鹿何時滅絕的看法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a particular extinct deer, not just any unusually large deer.","zh":"這個片語指一種特定已滅絕鹿類，而不只是任何特別大的鹿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"saber-toothed cats","meaning":"劍齒貓","examples":[{"en":"Saber-toothed cats were among the large mammals that disappeared after the ice age.","zh":"劍齒貓是冰河時期後消失的大型哺乳動物之一。"},{"en":"Saber-toothed cats were extinct predators with very long, curved canine teeth.","zh":"saber-toothed cats 指具有很長、彎曲犬齒的已滅絕捕食動物。"},{"en":"Children often recognise saber-toothed cats from museum models and prehistoric-animal books.","zh":"孩子常從博物館模型和史前動物書中認出劍齒貓。"},{"en":"If their prey disappeared, saber-toothed cats would have struggled to find enough food.","zh":"如果牠們的獵物消失，劍齒貓就會難以找到足夠食物。"},{"en":"The phrase names a group of prehistoric hunters, not ordinary modern cats.","zh":"這個片語指一類史前獵食者，而不是普通現代貓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mastodons","meaning":"乳齒象","examples":[{"en":"Mastodons became extinct near the end of the last ice age.","zh":"乳齒象在上一個冰河時期接近結束時滅絕。"},{"en":"Mastodons were large elephant-like mammals that lived in prehistoric times.","zh":"mastodons 指生活在史前時期、像大象的大型哺乳動物。"},{"en":"A science teacher may compare mastodons with mammoths to explain extinct megafauna.","zh":"科學老師可能把乳齒象與猛獁象比較，以解釋已滅絕巨型動物。"},{"en":"If forests and wetlands changed, mastodons may have lost important food sources.","zh":"如果森林和濕地改變，乳齒象可能失去重要食物來源。"},{"en":"The word refers to an extinct animal group related to, but different from, modern elephants.","zh":"這個詞指與現代大象有關但不同的已滅絕動物群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"giant sloths","meaning":"巨型地懶","examples":[{"en":"Giant sloths once lived alongside many other large mammals.","zh":"巨型地懶曾與許多其他大型哺乳動物共同生活。"},{"en":"Giant sloths were huge prehistoric relatives of modern sloths.","zh":"giant sloths 指現代樹懶的巨大史前親屬。"},{"en":"Unlike small tree sloths today, some giant sloths were large enough to stand as tall as a person.","zh":"與今天小型樹棲樹懶不同，有些巨型地懶大得站起來可與人一樣高。"},{"en":"If climate and vegetation changed, giant sloths may have found less suitable food.","zh":"如果氣候和植被改變，巨型地懶可能找到較少合適食物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extinct ground-dwelling animals, not the small sloths living in trees today.","zh":"這個片語描述已滅絕的地棲動物，而不是今天生活在樹上的小樹懶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"woolly rhinos","meaning":"披毛犀","examples":[{"en":"Woolly rhinos were adapted to cold glacial conditions.","zh":"披毛犀適應了寒冷冰川環境。"},{"en":"Woolly rhinos were extinct rhinoceroses covered with thick hair for cold climates.","zh":"woolly rhinos 指覆蓋厚毛、適應寒冷氣候的已滅絕犀牛。"},{"en":"A museum model of a woolly rhino may show a heavy body, a horn, and a shaggy coat.","zh":"披毛犀的博物館模型可能展示厚重身體、角和長毛外層。"},{"en":"If the climate became warmer, woolly rhinos may have lost the cold open habitats they needed.","zh":"如果氣候變暖，披毛犀可能失去牠們所需的寒冷開闊棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an ice-age animal, not a modern rhinoceros with ordinary skin.","zh":"這個片語指冰河時期動物，而不是普通皮膚的現代犀牛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"large, shaggy mammals","meaning":"大型長毛哺乳動物","examples":[{"en":"Many large, shaggy mammals disappeared during the same broad period.","zh":"許多大型長毛哺乳動物在同一大致時期消失。"},{"en":"Large, shaggy mammals are big animals with long, rough hair covering their bodies.","zh":"large, shaggy mammals 指身體覆蓋長而粗毛的大型動物。"},{"en":"A woolly mammoth is a familiar example of a large, shaggy mammal from the ice age.","zh":"披毛猛獁象是冰河時期大型長毛哺乳動物的常見例子。"},{"en":"Thick hair helped these animals survive cold conditions, but it did not protect them from every environmental change.","zh":"厚毛幫助這些動物在寒冷環境生存，但不能保護牠們免受所有環境變化影響。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a visual description of cold-adapted prehistoric animals.","zh":"這個片語對適應寒冷的史前動物作出視覺描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be widely thought to","meaning":"普遍被認為……","examples":[{"en":"These mammals are widely thought to have died out after the ice age.","zh":"這些哺乳動物普遍被認為在冰河時期後滅絕。"},{"en":"Be widely thought to means many people or experts generally believe something is true.","zh":"be widely thought to 指許多人或專家普遍相信某事是真的。"},{"en":"Exercise is widely thought to improve mood as well as physical health.","zh":"運動普遍被認為能改善心情以及身體健康。"},{"en":"If an idea is widely thought to be true, new evidence is needed to challenge it.","zh":"如果一個想法普遍被認為是真的，就需要新證據來挑戰它。"},{"en":"The phrase reports common belief, not necessarily final proof.","zh":"這個片語報告普遍看法，不一定是最終證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"die out","meaning":"滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Many large mammals died out thousands of years ago.","zh":"許多大型哺乳動物在數千年前滅絕。"},{"en":"Die out means disappear completely because all members of a group or species have died.","zh":"die out 指因一個群體或物種所有成員死亡而完全消失。"},{"en":"A local custom may die out if young people stop practising it.","zh":"如果年輕人停止實踐，本地習俗可能消失。"},{"en":"If animals cannot find food or reproduce successfully, their population may die out.","zh":"如果動物無法找到食物或成功繁殖，其種群可能滅絕。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe both biological extinction and the disappearance of traditions.","zh":"這個片語既可描述生物滅絕，也可描述傳統消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"around the end of","meaning":"大約在……結束時","examples":[{"en":"Many species disappeared around the end of the last ice age.","zh":"許多物種大約在上一個冰河時期結束時消失。"},{"en":"Around the end of means approximately at the time when something was finishing.","zh":"around the end of 指大約在某事即將結束或結束時。"},{"en":"Many shops close around the end of the school day because students are going home.","zh":"許多小店大約在放學時關門，因為學生正在回家。"},{"en":"If several species vanished around the same time, scientists may look for a shared cause.","zh":"如果幾個物種大約在同一時間消失，科學家可能尋找共同原因。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate time, not an exact date.","zh":"這個片語給出大約時間，而不是精確日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the last ice age","meaning":"上一個冰河時期","examples":[{"en":"The last ice age ended more than ten thousand years ago.","zh":"上一個冰河時期在一萬多年前結束。"},{"en":"The last ice age was the most recent long cold period when large ice sheets covered much of the Earth.","zh":"the last ice age 指最近一次漫長寒冷時期，當時大片冰蓋覆蓋地球許多地方。"},{"en":"Students may learn about the last ice age when studying mammoths and early humans.","zh":"學生研究猛獁象和早期人類時，可能會學習上一個冰河時期。"},{"en":"When the last ice age ended, climate, vegetation, and animal habitats changed greatly.","zh":"當上一個冰河時期結束，氣候、植被和動物棲息地都大幅改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a major climatic period in prehistory.","zh":"這個片語指史前一個重要氣候時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"also be known as","meaning":"亦稱為……","examples":[{"en":"The Irish elk is also known as the giant deer.","zh":"愛爾蘭巨鹿亦稱為巨鹿。"},{"en":"Also be known as means have another name.","zh":"also be known as 指有另一個名稱。"},{"en":"Hong Kong International Airport is also known as Chek Lap Kok Airport.","zh":"香港國際機場亦稱為赤鱲角機場。"},{"en":"If an animal has several names, scientific articles may mention both to avoid confusion.","zh":"如果動物有幾個名稱，科學文章可能同時提及，以避免混淆。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an alternative name.","zh":"這個片語引出另一個名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the Irish elk","meaning":"愛爾蘭巨鹿","examples":[{"en":"The Irish elk was a huge deer with exceptionally large antlers.","zh":"愛爾蘭巨鹿是一種有異常巨大鹿角的大型鹿。"},{"en":"The Irish elk was an extinct deer species, not a true elk in the modern sense.","zh":"the Irish elk 指一種已滅絕鹿類，並不是現代意義上的真正麋鹿。"},{"en":"A museum label may call the animal the Irish elk because many remains were found in Ireland.","zh":"博物館標籤可能稱這種動物為愛爾蘭巨鹿，因為許多遺骸在愛爾蘭被發現。"},{"en":"If students hear “elk”, they should still remember that this animal is often called the giant deer.","zh":"如果學生聽到 elk，仍應記得這種動物常被稱為巨鹿。"},{"en":"The phrase names a famous extinct animal with huge antlers.","zh":"這個片語指出一種以巨大鹿角聞名的已滅絕動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Megaloceros giganteus","meaning":"巨角鹿的學名","examples":[{"en":"Megaloceros giganteus is the scientific name of the giant deer.","zh":"Megaloceros giganteus 是巨鹿的學名。"},{"en":"Megaloceros giganteus is the formal Latin name used by scientists for the giant deer.","zh":"Megaloceros giganteus 是科學家用於巨鹿的正式拉丁名稱。"},{"en":"A biology textbook may use Megaloceros giganteus so readers know exactly which species is meant.","zh":"生物課本可能使用 Megaloceros giganteus，讓讀者確切知道所指物種。"},{"en":"Scientific names help avoid confusion when common names differ between languages.","zh":"當通俗名稱因語言而不同時，學名有助避免混淆。"},{"en":"The phrase is a species name, so it is more precise than “giant deer”.","zh":"這個片語是物種名稱，所以比「巨鹿」更精確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"analysis of ancient bones and teeth","meaning":"對古代骨骼和牙齒的分析","examples":[{"en":"Analysis of ancient bones and teeth revealed when the animal disappeared.","zh":"對古代骨骼和牙齒的分析揭示了該動物何時消失。"},{"en":"Analysis of ancient bones and teeth means careful scientific study of old skeletal material.","zh":"analysis of ancient bones and teeth 指對古老骨骼材料進行仔細科學研究。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may analyse ancient teeth to learn what people or animals ate.","zh":"考古學家可能分析古代牙齒，以了解人或動物吃過甚麼。"},{"en":"If bones and teeth can be dated, researchers can estimate when a species last lived.","zh":"如果骨骼和牙齒能被定年，研究人員就能估計某物種最後生活的時間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical evidence used to reconstruct the past.","zh":"這個片語描述用來重建過去的實物證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"scientists based in","meaning":"駐於……的科學家","examples":[{"en":"The research was conducted by scientists based in Britain and Russia.","zh":"這項研究由駐於英國和俄羅斯的科學家進行。"},{"en":"Scientists based in a place are researchers who work mainly from that country, city, or institution.","zh":"scientists based in a place 指主要在某國家、城市或機構工作的研究人員。"},{"en":"Scientists based in Hong Kong may collaborate with laboratories overseas.","zh":"駐於香港的科學家可能與海外實驗室合作。"},{"en":"If researchers are based in different countries, a project can combine different expertise and collections.","zh":"如果研究人員駐於不同國家，項目就能結合不同專業和收藏。"},{"en":"The phrase tells us where the researchers work, not necessarily where they were born.","zh":"這個片語告訴我們研究人員在哪裡工作，不一定指他們在哪裡出生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"huge herbivore","meaning":"巨型草食動物","examples":[{"en":"The huge herbivore survived until approximately 5,000 BC.","zh":"這種巨型草食動物生存至約公元前5000年。"},{"en":"A huge herbivore is a very large animal that eats plants.","zh":"huge herbivore 指非常大型、以植物為食的動物。"},{"en":"An elephant is a modern example of a huge herbivore.","zh":"大象是現代巨型草食動物的例子。"},{"en":"If a huge herbivore loses access to suitable plants, its survival becomes difficult.","zh":"如果巨型草食動物失去合適植物來源，其生存就變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both size and diet.","zh":"這個片語同時描述體型和飲食。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"survive until","meaning":"生存至……","examples":[{"en":"The giant deer survived until much later than expected.","zh":"巨鹿生存至比預期晚得多的時期。"},{"en":"Survive until means continue living up to a particular time.","zh":"survive until 指繼續生存到某一特定時間。"},{"en":"A small shop may survive until the end of the year if rent is reduced.","zh":"如果租金降低，小店可能生存至年底。"},{"en":"If a species survived until 5,000 BC, it lasted longer than scientists once thought.","zh":"如果某物種生存至公元前5000年，它就比科學家曾經認為的持續更久。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the endpoint of survival.","zh":"這個片語集中於生存的終點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"more than three millennia later","meaning":"遲了三千多年","examples":[{"en":"The animal survived more than three millennia later than previously believed.","zh":"這種動物比先前相信的時間遲了三千多年才滅絕。"},{"en":"More than three millennia later means over three thousand years later.","zh":"more than three millennia later 指遲了超過三千年。"},{"en":"An ancient building may have been used more than three millennia after it was first built.","zh":"古建築可能在最初建成後三千多年仍被使用。"},{"en":"If extinction happened more than three millennia later than expected, the old timeline needs revision.","zh":"如果滅絕時間比預期遲了三千多年，舊時間線就需要修訂。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a very large difference in time.","zh":"這個片語強調非常大的時間差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"previously believed","meaning":"先前所相信的","examples":[{"en":"The extinction occurred later than previously believed.","zh":"滅絕發生的時間比先前所相信的更晚。"},{"en":"Previously believed means thought to be true before new evidence appeared.","zh":"previously believed 指在新證據出現前被認為是真的。"},{"en":"A student may score better than previously believed possible after changing study methods.","zh":"學生改變學習方法後，成績可能比先前所相信的可能性更好。"},{"en":"If new evidence challenges what was previously believed, researchers must update their conclusions.","zh":"如果新證據挑戰先前所相信的內容，研究人員就必須更新結論。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts old belief with newer understanding.","zh":"這個片語把舊信念與新理解作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"research team","meaning":"研究團隊","examples":[{"en":"The research team investigated the final period of the deer’s existence.","zh":"研究團隊調查了這種鹿存在的最後時期。"},{"en":"A research team is a group of people working together to study a question.","zh":"research team 指共同研究某問題的一群人。"},{"en":"A school research team may survey students to understand why homework is stressful.","zh":"學校研究團隊可能調查學生，以了解功課為何造成壓力。"},{"en":"If a research team includes different specialists, it can examine evidence from several angles.","zh":"如果研究團隊包括不同專家，就能從幾個角度檢視證據。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights organised group investigation.","zh":"這個片語突出有組織的團隊調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"suggest that","meaning":"顯示；表明","examples":[{"en":"The findings suggest that climate change was not the only cause.","zh":"研究結果顯示氣候變化不是唯一成因。"},{"en":"Suggest that means indicate or make something seem likely without proving it completely.","zh":"suggest that 指指出或令某事看起來可能，但未必完全證明。"},{"en":"Dark clouds suggest that it may rain soon.","zh":"烏雲顯示很快可能下雨。"},{"en":"If several clues point in the same direction, they may suggest a reasonable explanation.","zh":"如果幾個線索指向同一方向，它們可能表明一個合理解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase is cautious and often used in research writing.","zh":"這個片語較謹慎，常用於研究寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"additional factors besides","meaning":"除……外的其他因素","examples":[{"en":"Additional factors besides climate change may have contributed to the extinction.","zh":"除氣候變化外，其他因素也可能促成滅絕。"},{"en":"Additional factors besides something are other causes apart from the main one mentioned.","zh":"additional factors besides something 指除了已提到的主要原因之外的其他成因。"},{"en":"Besides revision time, sleep and exam technique may also affect results.","zh":"除溫習時間外，睡眠和考試技巧也可能影響成績。"},{"en":"If extinction cannot be explained by climate alone, researchers must consider additional factors.","zh":"如果滅絕不能單靠氣候解釋，研究人員就必須考慮其他因素。"},{"en":"The phrase widens the explanation beyond one cause.","zh":"這個片語把解釋擴闊至不只一個原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hasten extinction","meaning":"加速滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Human activity may have hastened the giant deer’s extinction.","zh":"人類活動可能加速了巨鹿滅絕。"},{"en":"Hasten extinction means make a species disappear sooner or more quickly.","zh":"hasten extinction 指令某物種更早或更快消失。"},{"en":"Pollution can hasten the extinction of fish if it destroys breeding areas.","zh":"如果污染破壞繁殖地，就可能加速魚類滅絕。"},{"en":"If climate change weakens a species and hunting adds pressure, extinction may happen faster.","zh":"如果氣候變化削弱某物種，而狩獵又增加壓力，滅絕可能更快發生。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on speeding up a decline.","zh":"這個片語集中於加快衰退。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"eventual extinction","meaning":"最終滅絕","examples":[{"en":"The researchers examined the causes of the animal’s eventual extinction.","zh":"研究人員檢視了該動物最終滅絕的原因。"},{"en":"Eventual extinction means the final disappearance of a species after a process of decline.","zh":"eventual extinction 指物種經過衰退過程後最終消失。"},{"en":"A language may face eventual extinction if no children learn to speak it.","zh":"如果沒有孩子學會說某語言，該語言可能面臨最終消失。"},{"en":"If a population keeps falling and cannot recover, eventual extinction becomes possible.","zh":"如果種群不斷下降且無法恢復，最終滅絕就變得可能。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the final outcome, not just temporary danger.","zh":"這個片語指最後結果，而不只是暫時危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"habitat destruction","meaning":"棲息地破壞","examples":[{"en":"Habitat destruction by humans may have contributed to the decline.","zh":"人類造成的棲息地破壞可能促成了衰退。"},{"en":"Habitat destruction means damage to the places where animals or plants live.","zh":"habitat destruction 指動植物生活地方受到破壞。"},{"en":"Building roads through a forest can cause habitat destruction for birds and mammals.","zh":"在森林中修建道路可能對鳥類和哺乳動物造成棲息地破壞。"},{"en":"If habitat is destroyed, animals may lose food, shelter, and breeding sites.","zh":"如果棲息地被破壞，動物可能失去食物、庇護和繁殖地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one of the major causes of species decline.","zh":"這個片語描述物種衰退的主要原因之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"so-called because","meaning":"之所以這樣稱呼，是因為……","examples":[{"en":"The animal was so-called because many remains were found in Ireland.","zh":"這種動物之所以這樣稱呼，是因為許多遺骸在愛爾蘭被發現。"},{"en":"So-called because explains the reason for a name or label.","zh":"so-called because 用來解釋某名稱或標籤的原因。"},{"en":"The dish is so-called because it was first sold near a temple.","zh":"這道菜之所以這樣稱呼，是因為它最初在寺廟附近出售。"},{"en":"If a species is named after the place where fossils were found, the name may not show its full range.","zh":"如果物種因化石發現地而命名，名稱未必顯示其完整分布範圍。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why something received a particular name.","zh":"這個片語解釋某事物為何得到特定名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"well-preserved remains","meaning":"保存良好的遺骸","examples":[{"en":"Well-preserved remains have been found beneath Irish peat bogs.","zh":"保存良好的遺骸在愛爾蘭泥炭沼澤下被發現。"},{"en":"Well-preserved remains are old bones or body parts kept in good condition over time.","zh":"well-preserved remains 指長時間後仍保持良好狀態的古老骨骼或身體部分。"},{"en":"A dry cave may contain well-preserved remains of ancient animals.","zh":"乾燥洞穴可能保存有古代動物的良好遺骸。"},{"en":"If remains are well preserved, scientists can obtain more reliable information from them.","zh":"如果遺骸保存良好，科學家就能從中取得更可靠資料。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that ancient evidence has not been badly damaged.","zh":"這個片語強調古代證據沒有嚴重受損。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lake sediments","meaning":"湖泊沉積物","examples":[{"en":"The bones were often found in lake sediments.","zh":"骨骼常在湖泊沉積物中被發現。"},{"en":"Lake sediments are layers of mud, sand, and organic material deposited at the bottom of lakes.","zh":"lake sediments 指沉積在湖底的泥、沙和有機物層。"},{"en":"Scientists may study lake sediments to learn about past climate and vegetation.","zh":"科學家可能研究湖泊沉積物，以了解過去氣候和植被。"},{"en":"If bones are buried in sediments, they may be protected from weather and scavengers.","zh":"如果骨骼被埋在沉積物中，可能免受天氣和食腐動物破壞。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to material that settles in lakes over time.","zh":"這個片語指隨時間沉降在湖泊中的物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"peat bogs","meaning":"泥炭沼澤","examples":[{"en":"Many giant-deer remains were discovered under peat bogs in Ireland.","zh":"許多巨鹿遺骸在愛爾蘭泥炭沼澤下被發現。"},{"en":"Peat bogs are wetland areas where dead plant material builds up slowly and forms peat.","zh":"peat bogs 指枯死植物物質慢慢積累並形成泥炭的濕地。"},{"en":"Peat bogs can preserve old objects because the wet, low-oxygen conditions slow decay.","zh":"泥炭沼澤能保存舊物件，因為潮濕低氧環境會減慢腐爛。"},{"en":"If bones sink into peat, they may remain protected for thousands of years.","zh":"如果骨骼沉入泥炭，就可能被保護數千年。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a special wetland environment.","zh":"這個片語描述一種特殊濕地環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"first appear","meaning":"最早出現","examples":[{"en":"The Irish elk first appeared about 400,000 years ago.","zh":"愛爾蘭巨鹿約在四十萬年前最早出現。"},{"en":"First appear means be recorded or come into existence for the first time.","zh":"first appear 指首次被記錄或首次出現。"},{"en":"A new word may first appear in student writing before it becomes common in speech.","zh":"新詞可能先在學生寫作中出現，然後才在口語中變得常見。"},{"en":"If fossils first appear in older rocks, the species existed earlier than previously known.","zh":"如果化石最早出現在較古老岩層中，該物種就比先前所知更早存在。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the beginning of something’s known history.","zh":"這個片語標示某事已知歷史的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"through a combination of","meaning":"結合……的方法","examples":[{"en":"The team reached its conclusion through a combination of two research methods.","zh":"團隊透過結合兩種研究方法得出結論。"},{"en":"Through a combination of means by using two or more things together.","zh":"through a combination of 指透過同時使用兩種或更多事物。"},{"en":"A student may improve through a combination of daily reading, feedback, and revision.","zh":"學生可能透過結合每日閱讀、回饋和修改而進步。"},{"en":"If one method gives dates and another gives locations, combining them can produce a clearer picture.","zh":"如果一種方法提供日期，而另一種方法提供地點，把它們結合起來可以形成更清晰圖像。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that several methods work together.","zh":"這個片語顯示幾種方法一起發揮作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"radiocarbon dating","meaning":"放射性碳定年法","examples":[{"en":"Radiocarbon dating helped determine the age of the skeletal remains.","zh":"放射性碳定年法幫助判定骨骼遺骸的年代。"},{"en":"Radiocarbon dating is a scientific method used to estimate the age of once-living material.","zh":"radiocarbon dating 指用來估計曾經有生命材料年代的科學方法。"},{"en":"Archaeologists use radiocarbon dating to date wood, bone, cloth, or charcoal.","zh":"考古學家使用放射性碳定年法為木材、骨骼、布料或木炭定年。"},{"en":"If a bone contains enough carbon, radiocarbon dating can help place it on a timeline.","zh":"如果骨骼含有足夠碳，放射性碳定年法可以幫助把它放入時間線。"},{"en":"The phrase names an important dating technique for ancient remains.","zh":"這個片語指出古代遺骸的重要定年技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"skeletal remains","meaning":"骨骼遺骸","examples":[{"en":"The researchers used skeletal remains to trace the animal’s history.","zh":"研究人員使用骨骼遺骸追溯該動物的歷史。"},{"en":"Skeletal remains are bones left after a human or animal has died.","zh":"skeletal remains 指人或動物死亡後留下的骨骼。"},{"en":"Police or archaeologists may examine skeletal remains to learn age, diet, or injuries.","zh":"警方或考古學家可能檢查骨骼遺骸，以了解年齡、飲食或受傷情況。"},{"en":"If skeletal remains are dated and mapped, they can show where and when a species lived.","zh":"如果骨骼遺骸被定年並繪製分布，就能顯示某物種曾在何時何地生活。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to bone evidence.","zh":"這個片語指骨骼證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mapping of locations","meaning":"地點分布測繪","examples":[{"en":"Mapping of locations showed where the species had lived.","zh":"地點分布測繪顯示該物種曾經生活在哪裡。"},{"en":"Mapping of locations means recording places on a map to reveal distribution or pattern.","zh":"mapping of locations 指把地點記錄在地圖上，以顯示分布或模式。"},{"en":"A school may use mapping of student homes to plan safer bus routes.","zh":"學校可能使用學生住處地點分布測繪來規劃更安全校巴路線。"},{"en":"If fossil locations are mapped, scientists can see how a species’ range changed.","zh":"如果化石地點被繪製出來，科學家就能看見物種分布範圍如何改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes turning place data into a visual pattern.","zh":"這個片語描述把地點數據變成視覺模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be unearthed","meaning":"被發掘出來","examples":[{"en":"The remains were unearthed across several parts of Europe.","zh":"這些遺骸在歐洲幾個地區被發掘出來。"},{"en":"Be unearthed means be dug up from the ground or discovered after being hidden.","zh":"be unearthed 指從地下挖出，或在被隱藏後被發現。"},{"en":"Workers may unearth old coins while repairing a road.","zh":"工人修路時可能發掘出舊硬幣。"},{"en":"If fossils are unearthed in many places, they can reveal a species’ former range.","zh":"如果化石在許多地方被發掘出來，就能揭示物種過去的分布範圍。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used for archaeological or fossil discoveries.","zh":"這個片語常用於考古或化石發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be widespread across","meaning":"廣泛分布於……","examples":[{"en":"The Irish elk was once widespread across Europe.","zh":"愛爾蘭巨鹿曾廣泛分布於歐洲。"},{"en":"Be widespread across means be found over a large area.","zh":"be widespread across 指在大範圍地區被發現。"},{"en":"Smartphone use is now widespread across many age groups.","zh":"智能手機使用現在廣泛分布於許多年齡層。"},{"en":"If an animal was widespread across a continent, it once had a large range.","zh":"如果動物曾廣泛分布於一個大陸，它曾有很大的分布範圍。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad distribution.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the last big freeze","meaning":"最後一次大冰凍期","examples":[{"en":"The species occupied a large range before the last big freeze.","zh":"該物種在最後一次大冰凍期前佔據很大範圍。"},{"en":"The last big freeze refers to the final major cold phase of the ice-age period being discussed.","zh":"the last big freeze 指所討論冰河時期中的最後主要寒冷階段。"},{"en":"A science lesson may use “big freeze” to help students imagine a severe cold period.","zh":"科學課可能使用 big freeze 來幫助學生想像嚴重寒冷時期。"},{"en":"If animals lived before the last big freeze, later cooling may have changed their habitat.","zh":"如果動物在最後一次大冰凍期前生活，後來的寒冷可能改變其棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a less technical way to refer to a major cold episode.","zh":"這個片語以較不技術性的方式指一次重大寒冷事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the deer’s range","meaning":"鹿的分布範圍","examples":[{"en":"The deer’s range later became much smaller.","zh":"這種鹿的分布範圍後來變得小得多。"},{"en":"The deer’s range means the area where the deer lived or could be found.","zh":"the deer’s range 指這種鹿生活或可被找到的地區。"},{"en":"A bird’s range may expand if the climate becomes warmer.","zh":"如果氣候變暖，鳥類的分布範圍可能擴大。"},{"en":"If a species’ range shrinks, it has fewer places to find food and reproduce.","zh":"如果物種分布範圍縮小，它尋找食物和繁殖的地方就減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes geographical distribution.","zh":"這個片語描述地理分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"contract to","meaning":"縮小至……","examples":[{"en":"The animal’s range contracted to the Ural Mountains.","zh":"該動物的分布範圍縮小至烏拉爾山脈。"},{"en":"Contract to means shrink until only a smaller area remains.","zh":"contract to 指縮小到只剩較小範圍。"},{"en":"A company may contract to one office after closing several branches.","zh":"公司關閉幾間分行後，可能縮小至一個辦公室。"},{"en":"If a species’ range contracts to one region, it becomes more vulnerable to local change.","zh":"如果物種分布縮小至一個地區，就更容易受本地變化影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reduction in size or extent.","zh":"這個片語描述大小或範圍減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the Ural Mountains","meaning":"烏拉爾山脈","examples":[{"en":"The giant deer survived near the Ural Mountains.","zh":"巨鹿在烏拉爾山脈附近生存。"},{"en":"The Ural Mountains are a mountain range traditionally marking part of the boundary between Europe and Asia.","zh":"the Ural Mountains 指傳統上標示歐洲與亞洲部分邊界的山脈。"},{"en":"A geography teacher may use the Ural Mountains to explain where Europe and Asia meet.","zh":"地理老師可能用烏拉爾山脈解釋歐洲和亞洲在哪裡相接。"},{"en":"If an animal’s final population lived near the Urals, that region becomes important evidence.","zh":"如果某動物最後種群生活在烏拉爾附近，該地區就成為重要證據。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major Eurasian mountain range.","zh":"這個片語指出歐亞大陸的一條主要山脈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"modern-day Russia","meaning":"現今的俄羅斯","examples":[{"en":"The final population lived in an area of modern-day Russia.","zh":"最後的種群生活在現今俄羅斯的一個地區。"},{"en":"Modern-day Russia means the area belonging to Russia today, even if it had a different name in the past.","zh":"modern-day Russia 指今天屬於俄羅斯的地區，即使過去有不同名稱。"},{"en":"Ancient settlements in modern-day Turkey may have belonged to very different kingdoms long ago.","zh":"現今土耳其境內的古代聚落，久遠以前可能屬於非常不同的王國。"},{"en":"If researchers use modern-day country names, readers can locate old events on a current map.","zh":"如果研究人員使用現今國名，讀者就能在現代地圖上定位舊事件。"},{"en":"The phrase connects ancient geography with present political borders.","zh":"這個片語把古代地理與現代政治邊界連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"separate Europe from Asia","meaning":"將歐洲與亞洲分隔","examples":[{"en":"The Ural Mountains separate Europe from Asia.","zh":"烏拉爾山脈將歐洲與亞洲分隔。"},{"en":"Separate Europe from Asia means form a boundary or dividing line between the two regions.","zh":"separate Europe from Asia 指形成兩個地區之間的邊界或分界線。"},{"en":"A river can separate one district from another in a city.","zh":"河流可以把城市中一個區與另一個區分隔。"},{"en":"If mountains separate two regions, they can affect climate, travel, and animal movement.","zh":"如果山脈分隔兩個地區，它們可能影響氣候、交通和動物移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes geographical division.","zh":"這個片語描述地理分隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make its last stand","meaning":"在最後據點作最後生存","examples":[{"en":"The giant deer made its last stand in western Siberia.","zh":"巨鹿在西西伯利亞作最後生存。"},{"en":"Make its last stand means survive for the final time in one remaining place before disappearing.","zh":"make its last stand 指在消失前於最後一個剩餘地點作最後生存。"},{"en":"A small shop may make its last stand in an old market before closing for good.","zh":"小店可能在永久關閉前，在舊街市作最後支撐。"},{"en":"If a species has only one final stronghold, that area becomes its last stand.","zh":"如果某物種只剩一個最後據點，該地區就成為其最後生存地。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds dramatic and suggests final resistance before defeat.","zh":"這個片語帶戲劇性，暗示失敗前的最後抵抗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"western Siberia","meaning":"西西伯利亞","examples":[{"en":"The species’ final known population lived in western Siberia.","zh":"該物種最後已知種群生活在西西伯利亞。"},{"en":"Western Siberia is the western part of Siberia, a vast region in Russia.","zh":"western Siberia 指俄羅斯廣闊西伯利亞地區的西部。"},{"en":"A climate map may show western Siberia as a region with cold winters and wide plains.","zh":"氣候地圖可能顯示西西伯利亞是冬季寒冷、平原廣闊的地區。"},{"en":"If fossils are found in western Siberia, they can reveal what animals survived there late in prehistory.","zh":"如果化石在西西伯利亞被發現，就能揭示史前晚期哪些動物在那裡生存。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the location of the final known population.","zh":"這個片語給出最後已知種群的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ice sheets recede","meaning":"冰蓋消退","examples":[{"en":"The giant deer survived for thousands of years after the ice sheets receded.","zh":"巨鹿在冰蓋消退後仍生存了數千年。"},{"en":"Ice sheets recede means large areas of ice shrink back or melt away from land.","zh":"ice sheets recede 指大片冰層從土地上縮退或融化消失。"},{"en":"Glaciers recede when warmer temperatures cause more melting than snowfall.","zh":"當較高溫度造成融雪多於降雪時，冰川會消退。"},{"en":"If ice sheets recede, plants, animals, and people may move into newly exposed land.","zh":"如果冰蓋消退，植物、動物和人類可能進入新露出的土地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes retreating ice after a cold period.","zh":"這個片語描述寒冷時期後冰層退縮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"study’s co-author","meaning":"研究的共同作者","examples":[{"en":"Adrian Lister was the study’s co-author.","zh":"Adrian Lister 是該研究的共同作者。"},{"en":"A study’s co-author is one of the researchers who helped write or produce the study.","zh":"study’s co-author 指協助撰寫或完成該研究的研究人員之一。"},{"en":"A student project may have a co-author if two classmates write the report together.","zh":"如果兩位同學一起寫報告，學生項目可以有共同作者。"},{"en":"If a co-author is quoted, the statement comes from someone directly involved in the research.","zh":"如果共同作者被引用，該說法來自直接參與研究的人。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies shared responsibility for a study.","zh":"這個片語指出研究的共同責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"professor of palaeobiology","meaning":"古生物學教授","examples":[{"en":"Adrian Lister is a professor of palaeobiology.","zh":"Adrian Lister 是古生物學教授。"},{"en":"A professor of palaeobiology studies ancient life using fossils, bones, and evolutionary evidence.","zh":"professor of palaeobiology 指使用化石、骨骼和演化證據研究古代生命的教授。"},{"en":"A palaeobiology professor may teach students how extinct animals lived and died out.","zh":"古生物學教授可能教學生已滅絕動物如何生活和滅絕。"},{"en":"If a palaeobiologist studies deer fossils, they can connect anatomy with past environments.","zh":"如果古生物學家研究鹿化石，就能把解剖結構與過去環境連接起來。"},{"en":"The phrase names an academic expert in ancient life.","zh":"這個片語指出研究古代生命的學術專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"eastern foothills","meaning":"東部山麓","examples":[{"en":"The eastern foothills of the Urals became densely forested.","zh":"烏拉爾山脈東部山麓變成茂密森林。"},{"en":"Eastern foothills are lower slopes on the eastern side of a mountain range.","zh":"eastern foothills 指山脈東側較低的山坡地帶。"},{"en":"Villages may be built in foothills because the land is gentler than high mountains.","zh":"村莊可能建在山麓，因為土地比高山較平緩。"},{"en":"If foothills become forested, grazing animals may be pushed into more open land.","zh":"如果山麓變成森林，吃草動物可能被迫遷往較開闊土地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a specific landscape position.","zh":"這個片語描述特定地形位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"become densely forested","meaning":"變成茂密森林","examples":[{"en":"The foothills became densely forested as the climate changed.","zh":"隨着氣候改變，山麓變成茂密森林。"},{"en":"Become densely forested means become covered with thick, closely growing trees.","zh":"become densely forested 指被密集生長的樹木覆蓋。"},{"en":"An abandoned hillside may become densely forested after many years without farming.","zh":"被棄置的山坡在多年沒有耕作後，可能變成茂密森林。"},{"en":"If open land becomes densely forested, animals that prefer grassland may lose habitat.","zh":"如果開闊土地變成茂密森林，偏好草地的動物可能失去棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a major change in vegetation.","zh":"這個片語描述植被上的重大改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"push animals onto the plain","meaning":"迫使動物遷到平原","examples":[{"en":"The expanding forests may have pushed the deer onto the plain.","zh":"擴展中的森林可能迫使巨鹿遷到平原。"},{"en":"Push animals onto the plain means force animals to move from one habitat into open flat land.","zh":"push animals onto the plain 指迫使動物從某棲息地移到開闊平坦土地。"},{"en":"Building work near a park may push birds into quieter areas nearby.","zh":"公園附近的建築工程可能迫使鳥類遷到附近較安靜地區。"},{"en":"If forests expand into former grazing land, large herbivores may have to move to plains.","zh":"如果森林擴展到原本的放牧地，大型草食動物可能必須遷到平原。"},{"en":"The phrase describes habitat change forcing movement.","zh":"這個片語描述棲息地變化迫使動物移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pollen analysis","meaning":"花粉分析","examples":[{"en":"Pollen analysis revealed changes in the region’s vegetation.","zh":"花粉分析揭示了該地區植被的變化。"},{"en":"Pollen analysis is the study of ancient pollen grains to understand past plants and climates.","zh":"pollen analysis 指研究古代花粉粒，以了解過去植物和氣候。"},{"en":"Scientists can use pollen analysis from lake mud to learn what trees once grew nearby.","zh":"科學家可以使用湖泥中的花粉分析，了解附近曾生長甚麼樹。"},{"en":"If pollen types change over time, vegetation in the area probably changed too.","zh":"如果花粉種類隨時間改變，該地區植被很可能也改變。"},{"en":"The phrase names a method for reconstructing past environments.","zh":"這個片語指出重建過去環境的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"indicate that","meaning":"顯示","examples":[{"en":"Pollen evidence indicates that the region became extremely dry.","zh":"花粉證據顯示該地區變得極度乾燥。"},{"en":"Indicate that means show or suggest something clearly through evidence.","zh":"indicate that 指透過證據清楚顯示或暗示某事。"},{"en":"A red warning light indicates that a machine may have a problem.","zh":"紅色警示燈顯示機器可能有問題。"},{"en":"If pollen from dry-land plants increases, it may indicate that the climate became drier.","zh":"如果來自乾旱土地植物的花粉增加，可能顯示氣候變得更乾。"},{"en":"The phrase connects evidence with a conclusion.","zh":"這個片語把證據與結論連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in response to","meaning":"因應；由於……","examples":[{"en":"The environment became drier in response to further climatic change.","zh":"環境因應進一步氣候變化而變得更乾。"},{"en":"In response to means as a reaction to something that has happened.","zh":"in response to 指作為對已發生事情的反應。"},{"en":"A school may change its timetable in response to parents’ complaints.","zh":"學校可能因應家長投訴而改變時間表。"},{"en":"If temperature and rainfall patterns change, plants may shift in response.","zh":"如果氣溫和降雨模式改變，植物可能因應而轉移。"},{"en":"The phrase links an effect to the change that triggered it.","zh":"這個片語把效果與觸發它的變化連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"further climatic change","meaning":"進一步的氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"Further climatic change transformed the available vegetation.","zh":"進一步的氣候變化改變了可用植被。"},{"en":"Further climatic change means additional change in climate after earlier changes have already occurred.","zh":"further climatic change 指在早前氣候改變後又出現的額外氣候變化。"},{"en":"Further climatic change may make summers hotter and winters less predictable.","zh":"進一步的氣候變化可能令夏天更熱、冬天更難預測。"},{"en":"If a region becomes drier after previous warming, plants and animals face new stress.","zh":"如果地區在先前變暖後又變得更乾，植物和動物就面對新壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that climate did not change just once.","zh":"這個片語顯示氣候不是只改變一次。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lead to the loss of","meaning":"導致……流失","examples":[{"en":"The dry conditions led to the loss of important food plants.","zh":"乾燥環境導致重要食用植物流失。"},{"en":"Lead to the loss of means cause something valuable or necessary to disappear.","zh":"lead to the loss of 指導致有價值或必要的東西消失。"},{"en":"Poor storage can lead to the loss of important school records.","zh":"儲存不當可以導致重要學校記錄遺失。"},{"en":"If drought kills plants, animals depending on those plants may struggle to survive.","zh":"如果乾旱殺死植物，依賴那些植物的動物可能難以生存。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a cause with disappearance or damage.","zh":"這個片語把原因與消失或損害連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"important food plants","meaning":"重要食用植物","examples":[{"en":"The deer depended on important food plants for minerals.","zh":"這種鹿依賴重要食用植物取得礦物質。"},{"en":"Important food plants are plant species that provide essential nutrition for animals or people.","zh":"important food plants 指為動物或人類提供必要營養的植物物種。"},{"en":"Rice and vegetables are important food plants for many human communities.","zh":"米和蔬菜是許多人類社群的重要食用植物。"},{"en":"If important food plants disappear, herbivores may lose both calories and minerals.","zh":"如果重要食用植物消失，草食動物可能同時失去熱量和礦物質。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses food value, not just plant presence.","zh":"這個片語強調食物價值，而不只是植物存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in combination with","meaning":"與……結合","examples":[{"en":"Environmental change, in combination with human pressure, may have caused extinction.","zh":"環境變化與人類壓力結合，可能造成滅絕。"},{"en":"In combination with means together with another factor.","zh":"in combination with 指與另一因素一起。"},{"en":"Good teaching, in combination with regular practice, can improve exam performance.","zh":"良好教學與定期練習結合，可以改善考試表現。"},{"en":"If two pressures happen together, their effect may be stronger than either one alone.","zh":"如果兩種壓力同時發生，其效果可能比任何一方單獨更強。"},{"en":"The phrase shows combined causation.","zh":"這個片語顯示綜合成因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"human pressures","meaning":"人類造成的壓力","examples":[{"en":"Human pressures may have made survival more difficult.","zh":"人類造成的壓力可能令生存更困難。"},{"en":"Human pressures are stresses caused by people, such as hunting, farming, building, or habitat destruction.","zh":"human pressures 指由人類造成的壓力，例如狩獵、耕作、建設或棲息地破壞。"},{"en":"A wetland may face human pressures from pollution and nearby development.","zh":"濕地可能面對污染和附近發展帶來的人類壓力。"},{"en":"If animals already face climate stress, human pressures can make decline faster.","zh":"如果動物已面對氣候壓力，人類造成的壓力可能令衰退更快。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to human-caused difficulties for nature.","zh":"這個片語指人類為大自然造成的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"snuff something out","meaning":"使……徹底滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Climate change and human activity may finally have snuffed the species out.","zh":"氣候變化和人類活動最終可能使該物種徹底滅絕。"},{"en":"Snuff something out means end something completely and suddenly, like putting out a flame.","zh":"snuff something out 指像熄滅火焰一樣完全而突然地終結某事。"},{"en":"A strict rule can snuff out students’ curiosity if every question is punished.","zh":"如果每個問題都受到懲罰，嚴格規則可能扼殺學生的好奇心。"},{"en":"If a small population faces one final severe pressure, that pressure can snuff it out.","zh":"如果小種群面對最後一次嚴重壓力，該壓力可能把它徹底消滅。"},{"en":"The phrase is vivid and often suggests complete destruction.","zh":"這個片語很生動，常暗示完全破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be put forward as","meaning":"被提出作為……","examples":[{"en":"Hunting has often been put forward as a cause of extinction.","zh":"狩獵常被提出作為滅絕的原因。"},{"en":"Be put forward as means be suggested or proposed as an explanation or solution.","zh":"be put forward as 指被建議或提出作為解釋或解決方法。"},{"en":"Longer school hours may be put forward as a way to improve results, but evidence is still needed.","zh":"延長上課時間可能被提出作為改善成績的方法，但仍需要證據。"},{"en":"If a theory is put forward, other researchers can test whether it fits the facts.","zh":"如果理論被提出，其他研究人員可以測試它是否符合事實。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a proposed idea, not necessarily a proven one.","zh":"這個片語引出被提出的想法，不一定已被證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"contributory cause","meaning":"促成因素","examples":[{"en":"Human hunting may have been a contributory cause of the decline.","zh":"人類狩獵可能是衰退的促成因素。"},{"en":"A contributory cause is one factor that helps produce a result, but is not necessarily the only cause.","zh":"contributory cause 指有助產生某結果的一個因素，但不一定是唯一原因。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can be a contributory cause of poor exam performance.","zh":"睡眠不足可以是考試表現差的促成因素。"},{"en":"If climate change weakened the deer and hunting added pressure, hunting was contributory.","zh":"如果氣候變化削弱鹿群，而狩獵增加壓力，狩獵就是促成因素。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when several causes work together.","zh":"這個片語適合用於幾個原因共同作用的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Pleistocene megafauna","meaning":"更新世巨型動物群","examples":[{"en":"Many species of Pleistocene megafauna disappeared after the ice age.","zh":"許多更新世巨型動物群物種在冰河時期後消失。"},{"en":"Pleistocene megafauna means the very large animals that lived during the Pleistocene epoch.","zh":"Pleistocene megafauna 指生活在更新世時期的非常大型動物。"},{"en":"Mammoths, giant deer, and giant ground sloths are examples of Pleistocene megafauna.","zh":"猛獁象、巨鹿和巨型地懶都是更新世巨型動物群的例子。"},{"en":"If climate changed rapidly, many large animals with specialised habitats became vulnerable.","zh":"如果氣候快速改變，許多有專門棲息地的大型動物就變得脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to prehistoric large-animal communities.","zh":"這個片語指史前大型動物群落。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hint at","meaning":"暗示","examples":[{"en":"The new extinction date hints at another human-made problem.","zh":"新的滅絕日期暗示另一個人為問題。"},{"en":"Hint at means suggest something indirectly without saying it fully.","zh":"hint at 指間接暗示某事，而沒有完整說明。"},{"en":"A teacher’s smile may hint at good news before the results are announced.","zh":"老師的微笑可能在公布成績前暗示好消息。"},{"en":"If evidence hints at human impact, researchers need more data before making a firm claim.","zh":"如果證據暗示人類影響，研究人員在作出肯定主張前需要更多數據。"},{"en":"The phrase is weaker than prove.","zh":"這個片語比 prove 弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"human-made problem","meaning":"人為問題","examples":[{"en":"Habitat destruction was an additional human-made problem.","zh":"棲息地破壞是另一個人為問題。"},{"en":"A human-made problem is a difficulty caused by human actions rather than nature alone.","zh":"human-made problem 指由人類行動而非單靠自然造成的困難。"},{"en":"Traffic congestion is a human-made problem when poor planning puts too many cars on narrow roads.","zh":"如果規劃不善令太多車輛擠在狹窄道路上，交通擠塞就是人為問題。"},{"en":"If farming destroys habitat, the resulting animal decline is partly human-made.","zh":"如果農業破壞棲息地，隨之而來的動物衰退就部分是人為的。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies people as a cause of the problem.","zh":"這個片語指出人類是問題的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the first Neolithic people","meaning":"最早的新石器時代人類","examples":[{"en":"The first Neolithic people settled in the region about 7,000 years ago.","zh":"最早的新石器時代人類約在七千年前定居該地區。"},{"en":"The first Neolithic people were early farming communities from the New Stone Age.","zh":"the first Neolithic people 指新石器時代早期農業社群。"},{"en":"History students may learn that Neolithic people grew crops, kept animals, and made polished stone tools.","zh":"歷史學生可能學到新石器時代人類種植作物、飼養動物並製作磨製石器。"},{"en":"If farming people settled in a region, they often cleared land for fields and animals.","zh":"如果農業人群在某地定居，他們常為田地和牲畜清理土地。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to early agricultural humans, not hunter-gatherers only.","zh":"這個片語指早期農業人類，而不只是狩獵採集者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"settle in the region","meaning":"在該區定居","examples":[{"en":"Farming communities began to settle in the region.","zh":"農業社群開始在該區定居。"},{"en":"Settle in the region means move into an area and begin living there permanently or for a long time.","zh":"settle in the region 指遷入某地區並開始永久或長期生活。"},{"en":"A family may settle in a new district after finding work and school places nearby.","zh":"家庭在附近找到工作和學位後，可能在新區定居。"},{"en":"If farmers settle in a region, they may change the land by clearing forests and planting crops.","zh":"如果農民在某地區定居，可能透過清除森林和種植作物改變土地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long-term human occupation.","zh":"這個片語描述人類長期佔居。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"clear the land","meaning":"開墾土地；清除植被","examples":[{"en":"The early farmers would have cleared the land.","zh":"早期農民可能已開墾土地。"},{"en":"Clear the land means remove trees, bushes, or rocks so the area can be used.","zh":"clear the land 指移除樹木、灌木或石頭，以便使用該地區。"},{"en":"Builders may clear the land before constructing a new school.","zh":"建築商在興建新學校前可能清理土地。"},{"en":"If farmers clear land for crops, wild animals may lose shelter and food sources.","zh":"如果農民為作物清除土地，野生動物可能失去庇護和食物來源。"},{"en":"The phrase often describes the first step before farming or building.","zh":"這個片語常描述耕作或建築前的第一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the presence of humans","meaning":"人類的出現","examples":[{"en":"The presence of humans may explain the animal’s final disappearance.","zh":"人類的出現可能解釋了該動物最後消失。"},{"en":"The presence of humans means humans were living in, entering, or using a particular area.","zh":"the presence of humans 指人類正在某地生活、進入或使用該地。"},{"en":"The presence of humans can change animal behaviour near hiking trails.","zh":"人類的出現可以改變遠足徑附近的動物行為。"},{"en":"If humans arrive with tools, fire, and farming, they may place new pressure on wildlife.","zh":"如果人類帶着工具、火和農業到達，就可能對野生動物造成新壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on human occupation or activity in a place.","zh":"這個片語集中於某地的人類佔居或活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be unable to tough out","meaning":"無法捱過……","examples":[{"en":"The deer may have been unable to tough out the latest environmental changes.","zh":"這種鹿可能無法捱過最近的環境變化。"},{"en":"Be unable to tough out means not be able to endure a difficult situation until it passes.","zh":"be unable to tough out 指無法忍受困難情況直到它過去。"},{"en":"A small business may be unable to tough out a long period of high rent and low sales.","zh":"小企業可能無法捱過長期高租金和低銷售額。"},{"en":"If a species has survived earlier changes but faces several new pressures at once, it may finally fail.","zh":"如果物種曾捱過早期變化，但同時面對幾種新壓力，最終可能撐不下去。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and stresses endurance under hardship.","zh":"這個片語較口語，強調在困難中忍耐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"climatic fluctuations","meaning":"氣候波動","examples":[{"en":"The species had survived many climatic fluctuations in the past.","zh":"該物種過去曾捱過許多氣候波動。"},{"en":"Climatic fluctuations are changes or ups and downs in climate over time.","zh":"climatic fluctuations 指氣候隨時間出現的變化或起伏。"},{"en":"Farmers may struggle with climatic fluctuations when rainfall becomes unpredictable.","zh":"當降雨變得難以預測，農民可能因氣候波動而困難。"},{"en":"If animals survive repeated climatic fluctuations, they are usually adaptable.","zh":"如果動物能捱過反覆氣候波動，通常具有適應力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes climate variation rather than one single change.","zh":"這個片語描述氣候變化起伏，而不是單一次變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cast doubt on","meaning":"質疑……","examples":[{"en":"Lister cast doubt on the theory concerning the animal’s antlers.","zh":"Lister 質疑了關於該動物鹿角的理論。"},{"en":"Cast doubt on means make people question whether something is true.","zh":"cast doubt on 指令人質疑某事是否真實。"},{"en":"Missing receipts may cast doubt on a company’s financial report.","zh":"缺少收據可能令人質疑公司的財務報告。"},{"en":"If new evidence does not fit a theory, it can cast doubt on that explanation.","zh":"如果新證據不符合某理論，就可能質疑該解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase weakens confidence in a claim.","zh":"這個片語削弱人們對某主張的信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"possible explanation for","meaning":"……的可能解釋","examples":[{"en":"The antlers have been suggested as a possible explanation for the deer’s demise.","zh":"鹿角被提出作為這種鹿滅亡的可能解釋。"},{"en":"A possible explanation for something is a reason that may account for it but is not certain.","zh":"possible explanation for something 指可能解釋某事的原因，但尚未確定。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep is a possible explanation for a student’s poor concentration.","zh":"睡眠不足是學生專注力差的可能解釋。"},{"en":"If several possible explanations exist, researchers compare them with the evidence.","zh":"如果存在幾個可能解釋，研究人員會把它們與證據比較。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests caution because the answer is not fully confirmed.","zh":"這個片語暗示謹慎，因為答案尚未完全確認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the deer’s demise","meaning":"鹿的滅亡","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have proposed several explanations for the deer’s demise.","zh":"科學家提出了幾種解釋鹿的滅亡。"},{"en":"The deer’s demise means the decline and final extinction of the deer.","zh":"the deer’s demise 指這種鹿的衰退和最終滅絕。"},{"en":"A company’s demise may begin with falling sales and end with closure.","zh":"公司的衰亡可能由銷售下降開始，最後以結業告終。"},{"en":"If food plants disappeared and humans added pressure, both could contribute to the deer’s demise.","zh":"如果食用植物消失，而人類又增加壓力，兩者都可能促成鹿的滅亡。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds more formal than “death” and refers to an overall ending.","zh":"這個片語比 death 更正式，指整體終結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"huge antlers","meaning":"巨大鹿角","examples":[{"en":"The male giant deer developed exceptionally huge antlers.","zh":"雄性巨鹿長出異常巨大的鹿角。"},{"en":"Huge antlers are very large branching horns grown by male deer.","zh":"huge antlers 指雄鹿長出的非常大型分枝角。"},{"en":"A museum skeleton with huge antlers can immediately show why the giant deer is famous.","zh":"擁有巨大鹿角的博物館骨架可以立即顯示巨鹿為何著名。"},{"en":"If antlers are extremely large, they require energy and minerals to grow.","zh":"如果鹿角極大，其生長就需要能量和礦物質。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a striking physical feature of the animal.","zh":"這個片語指該動物醒目的身體特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"exaggerated feature","meaning":"異常誇大的特徵","examples":[{"en":"The oversized antlers were an exaggerated physical feature.","zh":"過大的鹿角是一種異常誇大的身體特徵。"},{"en":"An exaggerated feature is a body part or characteristic that is unusually large, strong, or noticeable.","zh":"exaggerated feature 指異常巨大、強烈或醒目的身體部分或特徵。"},{"en":"A cartoon may give a character exaggerated eyes to show surprise.","zh":"卡通可能給角色誇張的大眼睛來表現驚訝。"},{"en":"If a feature becomes too large, it may attract mates but also create practical problems.","zh":"如果特徵變得太大，可能吸引配偶，但也造成實際問題。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a trait pushed beyond ordinary size or form.","zh":"這個片語暗示某特徵超出普通大小或形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the result of","meaning":"……的結果","examples":[{"en":"The antlers may have been the result of female mate choice.","zh":"鹿角可能是雌鹿擇偶選擇的結果。"},{"en":"The result of means caused by or produced by something.","zh":"the result of 指由某事造成或產生。"},{"en":"A high score may be the result of careful revision and enough sleep.","zh":"高分可能是仔細溫習和充足睡眠的結果。"},{"en":"If females preferred larger antlers, males with large antlers had more offspring.","zh":"如果雌鹿偏好較大鹿角，擁有大鹿角的雄鹿就有更多後代。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an effect with its cause.","zh":"這個片語把結果與原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"females preferring stags","meaning":"雌鹿偏好雄鹿","examples":[{"en":"The feature may have developed because of females preferring stags with larger antlers.","zh":"這個特徵可能因雌鹿偏好鹿角較大的雄鹿而發展。"},{"en":"Females preferring stags means female deer choosing male deer with particular qualities.","zh":"females preferring stags 指雌鹿選擇具有某些特質的雄鹿。"},{"en":"In some animals, females prefer males with brighter colours or stronger calls.","zh":"在一些動物中，雌性偏好顏色更鮮艷或叫聲更強的雄性。"},{"en":"If females choose males with larger antlers, that trait can become more common over generations.","zh":"如果雌鹿選擇鹿角較大的雄鹿，這種特徵可能在幾代之間變得更常見。"},{"en":"The phrase explains sexual selection through female choice.","zh":"這個片語透過雌性選擇解釋性選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"advertise a male’s fitness","meaning":"展示雄性的強健程度","examples":[{"en":"Large antlers may have advertised a male’s fitness.","zh":"大鹿角可能展示雄性的強健程度。"},{"en":"Advertise a male’s fitness means show that a male is strong, healthy, or suitable as a mate.","zh":"advertise a male’s fitness 指顯示雄性強壯、健康或適合作配偶。"},{"en":"A bird’s bright feathers may advertise its fitness to potential mates.","zh":"鳥類鮮艷羽毛可能向潛在配偶展示其強健程度。"},{"en":"If a male can grow huge antlers, females may interpret this as a sign of good condition.","zh":"如果雄性能長出巨大鹿角，雌性可能把這解讀為狀態良好的標誌。"},{"en":"The phrase uses “advertise” metaphorically to mean display.","zh":"這個片語把 advertise 作比喻使用，意思是展示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"contribute to the downfall of","meaning":"導致……衰亡","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists believe the antlers contributed to the animal’s downfall.","zh":"有些科學家相信鹿角導致了該動物的衰亡。"},{"en":"Contribute to the downfall of means help cause the failure, collapse, or extinction of someone or something.","zh":"contribute to the downfall of 指有助造成某人或某物失敗、崩潰或滅絕。"},{"en":"Poor leadership can contribute to the downfall of a business.","zh":"糟糕領導可以導致企業衰亡。"},{"en":"If a useful feature becomes too costly, it may contribute to a species’ decline.","zh":"如果一個有用特徵變得代價太高，它可能導致物種衰退。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests one factor among several causes of failure.","zh":"這個片語暗示失敗的多個原因之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"serious inconvenience","meaning":"嚴重妨礙","examples":[{"en":"The huge antlers could have been a serious inconvenience in dense forests.","zh":"巨大鹿角在茂密森林中可能是嚴重妨礙。"},{"en":"A serious inconvenience is a major practical difficulty that makes movement or action harder.","zh":"serious inconvenience 指令移動或行動變得更困難的重大實際困難。"},{"en":"A broken lift is a serious inconvenience for elderly residents in a tall building.","zh":"電梯壞了對高樓長者居民是嚴重不便。"},{"en":"If huge antlers catch on branches, moving through forest becomes difficult.","zh":"如果巨大鹿角勾住樹枝，在森林中移動就變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something troublesome, not necessarily deadly by itself.","zh":"這個片語描述麻煩之處，本身不一定致命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dense forests","meaning":"茂密森林","examples":[{"en":"The forests became denser after the last ice age.","zh":"上一個冰河時期後，森林變得更茂密。"},{"en":"Dense forests are forests with many trees growing closely together.","zh":"dense forests 指許多樹木緊密生長的森林。"},{"en":"Walkers may find dense forests difficult to cross because there is little open space.","zh":"行山者可能覺得茂密森林難以穿越，因為開闊空間很少。"},{"en":"If grassland turns into dense forest, open-country animals may lose suitable habitat.","zh":"如果草地變成茂密森林，開闊地帶動物可能失去合適棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes thick woodland with limited gaps.","zh":"這個片語描述縫隙有限的濃密林地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"spread northward","meaning":"向北擴展","examples":[{"en":"Dense forests spread northward as the climate warmed.","zh":"隨着氣候變暖，茂密森林向北擴展。"},{"en":"Spread northward means expand or move toward the north.","zh":"spread northward 指向北方擴張或移動。"},{"en":"A plant disease may spread northward if warmer weather allows it to survive.","zh":"如果較暖天氣讓植物病害得以生存，它可能向北擴展。"},{"en":"If forests spread northward, animals in northern open habitats may face new competition.","zh":"如果森林向北擴展，北方開闊棲息地的動物可能面對新競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase describes directional movement or expansion.","zh":"這個片語描述有方向的移動或擴張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a hard argument to make","meaning":"難以成立的論點","examples":[{"en":"Lister considered the antler theory a hard argument to make.","zh":"Lister 認為鹿角理論是難以成立的論點。"},{"en":"A hard argument to make is a claim that is difficult to support with evidence or logic.","zh":"a hard argument to make 指難以用證據或邏輯支持的主張。"},{"en":"It is a hard argument to make that homework helps if students are too tired to learn from it.","zh":"如果學生累得無法從功課中學習，說功課有幫助就是難以成立的論點。"},{"en":"If evidence from earlier forests contradicts the antler theory, the theory becomes difficult to defend.","zh":"如果來自早期森林的證據與鹿角理論矛盾，該理論就難以辯護。"},{"en":"The phrase signals scepticism about an explanation.","zh":"這個片語表示對某解釋的懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"survive perfectly well through","meaning":"安然捱過……","examples":[{"en":"The deer had previously survived perfectly well through forested periods.","zh":"這種鹿先前曾安然捱過森林茂盛時期。"},{"en":"Survive perfectly well through means live successfully during a difficult period without major failure.","zh":"survive perfectly well through 指在困難時期中成功生存，沒有重大失敗。"},{"en":"A student may survive perfectly well through a busy term if they plan their time carefully.","zh":"如果學生仔細規劃時間，可能安然捱過繁忙學期。"},{"en":"If the deer survived earlier forested periods, forests alone may not explain its extinction.","zh":"如果巨鹿曾捱過早期森林期，單靠森林未必能解釋其滅絕。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises successful endurance.","zh":"這個片語強調成功忍耐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"wooded interglacials","meaning":"林木茂盛的間冰期","examples":[{"en":"The giant deer survived earlier wooded interglacials.","zh":"巨鹿曾捱過較早的林木茂盛間冰期。"},{"en":"Wooded interglacials are warmer periods between glacial periods when forests expanded.","zh":"wooded interglacials 指冰期之間較溫暖、森林擴張的時期。"},{"en":"A climate textbook may compare icy glacial periods with wooded interglacials.","zh":"氣候課本可能比較寒冷冰期與林木茂盛的間冰期。"},{"en":"If deer survived wooded interglacials before, they could cope with some forest expansion.","zh":"如果巨鹿以前曾在林木茂盛間冰期生存，就能應付某些森林擴張。"},{"en":"The phrase combines climate history with vegetation change.","zh":"這個片語結合氣候歷史與植被變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"high-quality forage","meaning":"高質素覓食植物","examples":[{"en":"The deer required sufficient high-quality forage.","zh":"這種鹿需要足夠高質素覓食植物。"},{"en":"High-quality forage is nutritious plant food eaten by grazing or browsing animals.","zh":"high-quality forage 指放牧或食葉動物食用的有營養植物食物。"},{"en":"Farmers provide high-quality forage so cattle can grow and produce milk.","zh":"農民提供高質素飼草，讓牛隻成長並產奶。"},{"en":"If high-quality forage disappears, large herbivores may become weak or reproduce less.","zh":"如果高質素覓食植物消失，大型草食動物可能變弱或繁殖減少。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on plant food that is nutritionally valuable.","zh":"這個片語集中於具營養價值的植物食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"calcium and phosphate compounds","meaning":"鈣及磷酸鹽化合物","examples":[{"en":"Calcium and phosphate compounds were needed to form the antlers.","zh":"鈣及磷酸鹽化合物是形成鹿角所必需的。"},{"en":"Calcium and phosphate compounds are mineral substances important for bones, teeth, and antlers.","zh":"calcium and phosphate compounds 指對骨骼、牙齒和鹿角重要的礦物質。"},{"en":"Milk and some vegetables provide minerals that help maintain human bones.","zh":"牛奶和一些蔬菜提供幫助維持人體骨骼的礦物質。"},{"en":"If a male deer cannot obtain enough minerals, growing large antlers becomes difficult.","zh":"如果雄鹿無法獲得足夠礦物質，長出大鹿角就會變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase names key mineral building materials.","zh":"這個片語指出關鍵礦物建材。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be required to form","meaning":"是形成……所必需的","examples":[{"en":"Large quantities of minerals were required to form the antlers.","zh":"大量礦物質是形成鹿角所必需的。"},{"en":"Be required to form means be necessary for creating or building something.","zh":"be required to form 指某物是創造或建構另一事物所必需的。"},{"en":"Protein and practice are required to build strong muscles.","zh":"蛋白質和練習是形成強壯肌肉所必需的。"},{"en":"If minerals are required to form antlers, food quality directly affects antler growth.","zh":"如果礦物質是形成鹿角所必需的，食物質素就直接影響鹿角生長。"},{"en":"The phrase shows what is necessary for formation.","zh":"這個片語顯示形成某物需要甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"massive structures","meaning":"巨大結構","examples":[{"en":"The antlers were massive structures requiring many nutrients.","zh":"鹿角是需要許多養分的巨大結構。"},{"en":"Massive structures are very large and heavy physical forms.","zh":"massive structures 指非常大型而沉重的實體形態。"},{"en":"A bridge is a massive structure that needs strong materials and careful design.","zh":"橋樑是需要堅固材料和仔細設計的巨大結構。"},{"en":"If an animal grows massive structures, its body must supply enough energy and minerals.","zh":"如果動物長出巨大結構，其身體必須供應足夠能量和礦物質。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses size and material demand.","zh":"這個片語強調大小和材料需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"meet this requirement","meaning":"滿足這項需求","examples":[{"en":"The males drew minerals from their bones to meet this requirement.","zh":"雄鹿從骨骼中提取礦物質，以滿足這項需求。"},{"en":"Meet this requirement means satisfy or provide what is needed.","zh":"meet this requirement 指滿足或提供所需要的東西。"},{"en":"A student may need two science subjects to meet a university entrance requirement.","zh":"學生可能需要兩科科學科目來滿足大學入學要求。"},{"en":"If food does not supply enough minerals, deer may use minerals stored in their bones.","zh":"如果食物不能供應足夠礦物質，鹿可能使用儲存在骨骼中的礦物質。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on fulfilling a need or condition.","zh":"這個片語集中於滿足需要或條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"draw minerals from","meaning":"從……提取礦物質","examples":[{"en":"The deer could draw minerals from their own bones.","zh":"鹿可以從自己的骨骼中提取礦物質。"},{"en":"Draw minerals from means take minerals out of a source and use them elsewhere.","zh":"draw minerals from 指從某來源取出礦物質並用於其他地方。"},{"en":"Plants draw minerals from soil through their roots.","zh":"植物透過根部從泥土中提取礦物質。"},{"en":"If deer draw minerals from bones, their bones may temporarily become weaker.","zh":"如果鹿從骨骼中提取礦物質，其骨骼可能暫時變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes taking nutrients from a stored source.","zh":"這個片語描述從儲存來源提取養分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"replenish minerals from","meaning":"從……補充礦物質","examples":[{"en":"The males replenished minerals from food plants.","zh":"雄鹿從食用植物中補充礦物質。"},{"en":"Replenish minerals from means replace used-up minerals by obtaining them from a source.","zh":"replenish minerals from 指從某來源取得礦物質，以補回已用掉的部分。"},{"en":"Athletes replenish water and salts from drinks after heavy exercise.","zh":"運動員在劇烈運動後從飲品中補充水分和鹽分。"},{"en":"If deer lose bone minerals while growing antlers, they need mineral-rich food to replace them.","zh":"如果鹿在長鹿角時流失骨骼礦物質，就需要富含礦物的食物補回。"},{"en":"The phrase describes restoring a supply.","zh":"這個片語描述恢復供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reclaim nutrients from","meaning":"從……重新吸收養分","examples":[{"en":"Some deer reclaim nutrients from antlers that have been shed.","zh":"有些鹿會從脫落的鹿角中重新吸收養分。"},{"en":"Reclaim nutrients from means recover useful nutrients from something that has been lost or discarded.","zh":"reclaim nutrients from 指從已失去或被丟棄的東西中回收有用養分。"},{"en":"A garden can reclaim nutrients from food scraps by turning them into compost.","zh":"花園可以透過把廚餘變成堆肥，從中重新獲得養分。"},{"en":"If deer eat shed antlers, they can reuse minerals rather than finding all minerals from plants.","zh":"如果鹿吃脫落鹿角，就能重用礦物質，而不必全靠植物取得。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recovering value from leftover material.","zh":"這個片語描述從剩餘材料中回收價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"discarded antlers","meaning":"脫落的鹿角","examples":[{"en":"Deer may obtain minerals from discarded antlers.","zh":"鹿可能從脫落的鹿角中取得礦物質。"},{"en":"Discarded antlers are antlers that have been shed or left behind.","zh":"discarded antlers 指已脫落或被留下的鹿角。"},{"en":"Hikers may find discarded antlers on the forest floor during the shedding season.","zh":"行山者可能在鹿角脫落季節於森林地面發現脫落鹿角。"},{"en":"If animals chew discarded antlers, they can recover calcium and other minerals.","zh":"如果動物咀嚼脫落鹿角，就能回收鈣和其他礦物質。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to antlers no longer attached to the animal.","zh":"這個片語指不再連在動物身上的鹿角。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"extant deer","meaning":"現存鹿類","examples":[{"en":"This behaviour has also been observed in extant deer.","zh":"這種行為也在現存鹿類中被觀察到。"},{"en":"Extant deer are deer species that still exist today.","zh":"extant deer 指今天仍然存在的鹿類物種。"},{"en":"Modern red deer are extant deer, while the giant deer is extinct.","zh":"現代赤鹿是現存鹿類，而巨鹿已滅絕。"},{"en":"If a behaviour appears in extant deer, it may help scientists interpret extinct relatives.","zh":"如果某行為出現在現存鹿類中，就可能幫助科學家解釋已滅絕親屬。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts living species with extinct ones.","zh":"這個片語把仍活着的物種與已滅絕物種作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"antler growth phase","meaning":"鹿角生長期","examples":[{"en":"The males lost bone minerals during the antler growth phase.","zh":"雄鹿在鹿角生長期流失骨骼礦物質。"},{"en":"The antler growth phase is the period when male deer are growing their antlers.","zh":"antler growth phase 指雄鹿長出鹿角的時期。"},{"en":"During a growth phase, the body needs extra nutrients to build new tissue.","zh":"在生長期，身體需要額外養分來建立新組織。"},{"en":"If antlers grow quickly, the deer may need large amounts of minerals in a short time.","zh":"如果鹿角快速生長，鹿可能在短時間內需要大量礦物質。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a specific biological stage.","zh":"這個片語指特定生物階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"suffer from a condition similar to","meaning":"出現類似……的狀況","examples":[{"en":"The giant deer suffered from a condition similar to osteoporosis.","zh":"巨鹿出現類似骨質疏鬆症的狀況。"},{"en":"Suffer from a condition similar to means experience a health problem that resembles another known condition.","zh":"suffer from a condition similar to 指經歷一種與另一已知疾病相似的健康問題。"},{"en":"A person with severe tiredness may suffer from symptoms similar to flu, even without infection.","zh":"嚴重疲倦的人可能出現類似流感的症狀，即使沒有感染。"},{"en":"If deer lose bone minerals, their bones may temporarily resemble bones affected by osteoporosis.","zh":"如果鹿流失骨骼礦物質，其骨骼可能暫時類似受骨質疏鬆影響的骨骼。"},{"en":"The phrase compares one medical condition with another.","zh":"這個片語比較一種醫學狀況與另一種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"osteoporosis","meaning":"骨質疏鬆症","examples":[{"en":"The temporary mineral loss resembled osteoporosis.","zh":"暫時性礦物質流失類似骨質疏鬆症。"},{"en":"Osteoporosis is a condition in which bones become weak because they lose density.","zh":"osteoporosis 指骨骼因密度下降而變弱的狀況。"},{"en":"Older adults may be checked for osteoporosis if they break bones easily.","zh":"如果長者容易骨折，可能會接受骨質疏鬆症檢查。"},{"en":"If bones lose minerals, they can become more fragile and easier to damage.","zh":"如果骨骼流失礦物質，就可能變得更脆弱、更容易受損。"},{"en":"The word refers to bone weakness, not muscle pain.","zh":"這個詞指骨骼變弱，而不是肌肉疼痛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the last glacial period","meaning":"上一個冰期","examples":[{"en":"The environment changed at the end of the last glacial period.","zh":"環境在上一個冰期結束時發生變化。"},{"en":"The last glacial period was the most recent long period when ice sheets expanded widely.","zh":"the last glacial period 指最近一次冰蓋廣泛擴展的漫長時期。"},{"en":"A climate chart may show colder temperatures during the last glacial period.","zh":"氣候圖可能顯示上一個冰期期間氣溫較低。"},{"en":"When a glacial period ends, plants and animals often face major habitat changes.","zh":"當冰期結束，植物和動物常面對重大棲息地變化。"},{"en":"The phrase is a technical way to refer to the last ice-age cold period.","zh":"這個片語是指上一個冰河寒冷時期的技術說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"vegetation in the animal’s habitat","meaning":"動物棲息地的植被","examples":[{"en":"The vegetation in the animal’s habitat changed as the climate warmed.","zh":"隨着氣候變暖，動物棲息地的植被發生變化。"},{"en":"Vegetation in the animal’s habitat means the plants growing in the place where the animal lives.","zh":"vegetation in the animal’s habitat 指生長在動物生活地點的植物。"},{"en":"If grassland vegetation changes to forest vegetation, grazing animals may struggle.","zh":"如果草地植被變成森林植被，吃草動物可能困難。"},{"en":"When habitat plants change, food supply and shelter also change.","zh":"當棲息地植物改變，食物供應和庇護也會改變。"},{"en":"The phrase connects plant life with the animal’s living environment.","zh":"這個片語把植物生命與動物生活環境連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sufficient amounts of","meaning":"足夠分量的……","examples":[{"en":"The new plants may not have provided sufficient amounts of minerals.","zh":"新植物可能沒有提供足夠分量的礦物質。"},{"en":"Sufficient amounts of means enough of something for a particular need.","zh":"sufficient amounts of 指足以滿足某特定需要的數量。"},{"en":"Students need sufficient amounts of sleep before an exam.","zh":"學生考試前需要足夠分量的睡眠。"},{"en":"If food does not provide sufficient minerals, animals may become weaker.","zh":"如果食物不能提供足夠礦物質，動物可能變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on having enough, not merely having some.","zh":"這個片語集中於足夠，而不只是有一些。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"required minerals","meaning":"所需礦物質","examples":[{"en":"The deer needed required minerals to produce its antlers.","zh":"這種鹿需要所需礦物質來長出鹿角。"},{"en":"Required minerals are mineral nutrients that are necessary for a biological process.","zh":"required minerals 指某生物過程所必需的礦物營養。"},{"en":"Humans need required minerals such as calcium and iron for healthy bodies.","zh":"人類需要鈣和鐵等所需礦物質來維持健康身體。"},{"en":"If required minerals are missing from food, growth or repair may be affected.","zh":"如果食物缺少所需礦物質，生長或修復可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses necessity for a specific function.","zh":"這個片語強調某特定功能的必要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"western part of its range","meaning":"其分布範圍的西部","examples":[{"en":"Food shortages may have been especially serious in the western part of its range.","zh":"食物短缺在其分布範圍的西部可能尤其嚴重。"},{"en":"Western part of its range means the western area where the species lived.","zh":"western part of its range 指該物種生活範圍中的西部地區。"},{"en":"A bird may be common in the eastern part of its range but rare in the western part.","zh":"鳥類可能在分布範圍東部常見，但在西部罕見。"},{"en":"If conditions worsen in one part of a species’ range, local populations may disappear first.","zh":"如果物種分布範圍某部分環境惡化，本地種群可能先消失。"},{"en":"The phrase divides a species’ distribution by direction.","zh":"這個片語按方向劃分物種分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"extinction of megafauna","meaning":"巨型動物群滅絕","examples":[{"en":"The extinction of megafauna was nearly complete by the end of the ice age.","zh":"到冰河時期結束時，巨型動物群滅絕幾乎完成。"},{"en":"Extinction of megafauna means the disappearance of very large animal species.","zh":"extinction of megafauna 指非常大型動物物種的消失。"},{"en":"The loss of mammoths and giant sloths is part of the extinction of megafauna.","zh":"猛獁象和巨型地懶的消失是巨型動物群滅絕的一部分。"},{"en":"If many large animals vanish in a short period, ecosystems can change dramatically.","zh":"如果許多大型動物在短時間內消失，生態系統可能大幅改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a broad prehistoric extinction pattern.","zh":"這個片語指廣泛的史前滅絕模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be almost completed","meaning":"幾乎完成","examples":[{"en":"The global extinction was almost completed by the end of the last ice age.","zh":"全球滅絕到上一個冰河時期結束時幾乎完成。"},{"en":"Be almost completed means be nearly finished, with only a small part remaining.","zh":"be almost completed 指幾乎結束，只剩少量部分。"},{"en":"A school renovation is almost completed when only painting and cleaning remain.","zh":"當學校翻新只剩油漆和清潔時，工程就幾乎完成。"},{"en":"If extinction was almost completed by a certain time, most affected species had already disappeared.","zh":"如果滅絕在某時已幾乎完成，大多數受影響物種已經消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a process close to its end.","zh":"這個片語描述接近終點的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"come into existence","meaning":"出現；開始存在","examples":[{"en":"Megafauna may have come into existence in response to cold conditions.","zh":"巨型動物群可能為適應寒冷環境而出現。"},{"en":"Come into existence means begin to exist.","zh":"come into existence 指開始存在。"},{"en":"A new school club may come into existence when students share a strong interest.","zh":"當學生有共同強烈興趣時，新學會可能出現。"},{"en":"If large animals evolved because of cold conditions, climate helped bring them into existence.","zh":"如果大型動物因寒冷環境而演化，氣候就幫助牠們開始存在。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the beginning of something.","zh":"這個片語標示某事物的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in response to glacial conditions","meaning":"為適應冰川環境","examples":[{"en":"Large mammals evolved in response to glacial conditions.","zh":"大型哺乳動物為適應冰川環境而演化。"},{"en":"In response to glacial conditions means as an adaptation or reaction to cold ice-age environments.","zh":"in response to glacial conditions 指作為對寒冷冰河時期環境的適應或反應。"},{"en":"Animals may grow thicker fur in response to colder winters.","zh":"動物可能因應較冷冬天而長出更厚毛髮。"},{"en":"If the environment becomes icy and open, species with cold-adapted bodies may survive better.","zh":"如果環境變得冰冷而開闊，具寒冷適應身體的物種可能更能生存。"},{"en":"The phrase links evolution with climate pressure.","zh":"這個片語把演化與氣候壓力連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the onset of warmer climates","meaning":"較溫暖氣候的開始","examples":[{"en":"Many cold-adapted species disappeared with the onset of warmer climates.","zh":"許多適應寒冷的物種隨着較溫暖氣候的開始而消失。"},{"en":"The onset of warmer climates means the beginning of a period of warmer weather patterns.","zh":"the onset of warmer climates 指較暖天氣模式時期的開始。"},{"en":"The onset of summer heat may change what clothes students wear to school.","zh":"夏季炎熱開始時，學生穿上學的衣服可能改變。"},{"en":"If warmer climates begin, species adapted to cold may lose suitable habitat.","zh":"如果較溫暖氣候開始，適應寒冷的物種可能失去合適棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the start of a climatic change.","zh":"這個片語標示氣候變化的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"tropical and subtropical areas","meaning":"熱帶及亞熱帶地區","examples":[{"en":"Tropical and subtropical areas experienced less severe climatic change.","zh":"熱帶及亞熱帶地區經歷較不嚴重的氣候變化。"},{"en":"Tropical and subtropical areas are warm regions near or relatively near the equator.","zh":"tropical and subtropical areas 指位於赤道附近或相對接近赤道的溫暖地區。"},{"en":"Hong Kong has a subtropical climate, while rainforests near the equator are tropical.","zh":"香港屬亞熱帶氣候，而赤道附近雨林屬熱帶。"},{"en":"If climate change was less severe there, animal communities may have survived better.","zh":"如果那裡氣候變化較不嚴重，動物群可能更能存活。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to warm climate regions.","zh":"這個片語指溫暖氣候地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"less radical climatic change","meaning":"較溫和的氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"Some regions experienced less radical climatic change.","zh":"有些地區經歷較溫和的氣候變化。"},{"en":"Less radical climatic change means climate changed less dramatically or less severely.","zh":"less radical climatic change 指氣候變化較不劇烈或較不嚴重。"},{"en":"A city may face less radical weather change if temperatures rise only slightly.","zh":"如果氣溫只是輕微上升，城市可能面對較溫和的天氣變化。"},{"en":"If climate change is less radical, plants and animals may have more time to adapt.","zh":"如果氣候變化較溫和，植物和動物可能有更多時間適應。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the severity of climate change.","zh":"這個片語比較氣候變化的嚴重程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the transformation of","meaning":"……的轉變","examples":[{"en":"The transformation of North Africa produced the world’s largest desert.","zh":"北非的轉變產生了世界最大的沙漠。"},{"en":"The transformation of something means a major change in its form, condition, or character.","zh":"the transformation of something 指某物在形態、狀況或特徵上的重大改變。"},{"en":"The transformation of an old factory into flats can change a whole neighbourhood.","zh":"舊工廠改造成住宅，可以改變整個社區。"},{"en":"If a wet region becomes desert, the transformation affects plants, animals, and people.","zh":"如果潮濕地區變成沙漠，這種轉變會影響植物、動物和人類。"},{"en":"The phrase describes large-scale change.","zh":"這個片語描述大規模改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a vast area of","meaning":"一大片……","examples":[{"en":"A vast area of North Africa became desert.","zh":"北非一大片地區變成沙漠。"},{"en":"A vast area of means a very large amount of land or space.","zh":"a vast area of 指非常大面積的土地或空間。"},{"en":"A vast area of farmland may be damaged by a flood.","zh":"一大片農地可能被洪水破壞。"},{"en":"If a vast area becomes dry, many habitats can disappear at once.","zh":"如果一大片地區變乾，許多棲息地可以同時消失。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses huge size.","zh":"這個片語強調面積巨大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"escape major faunal extinction","meaning":"逃過大規模動物群滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Africa escaped major faunal extinction.","zh":"非洲逃過大規模動物群滅絕。"},{"en":"Escape major faunal extinction means avoid a large-scale loss of animal species.","zh":"escape major faunal extinction 指避免大量動物物種消失。"},{"en":"A forest may escape serious damage if a fire stops before reaching it.","zh":"如果火災在到達森林前停止，森林可能逃過嚴重破壞。"},{"en":"If climate change was milder, an animal community may have avoided mass extinction.","zh":"如果氣候變化較溫和，動物群落可能避免大規模滅絕。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a region did not suffer the worst outcome.","zh":"這個片語顯示某地區沒有遭受最壞結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"human exodus from Africa","meaning":"人類離開非洲的大遷徙","examples":[{"en":"The human exodus from Africa coincided with environmental change.","zh":"人類離開非洲的大遷徙與環境變化同時發生。"},{"en":"Human exodus from Africa means the large movement of early humans out of Africa.","zh":"human exodus from Africa 指早期人類大規模離開非洲。"},{"en":"History lessons may discuss human migration from Africa when explaining how people spread around the world.","zh":"歷史課解釋人類如何遍布世界時，可能討論人類離開非洲的遷徙。"},{"en":"If migration happened during environmental change, the two events may have influenced each other.","zh":"如果遷徙發生於環境變化期間，兩件事可能互相影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a major prehistoric movement of people.","zh":"這個片語指史前一次重大人類移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"entrance into the Americas","meaning":"人類進入美洲","examples":[{"en":"Human entrance into the Americas was accompanied by climate change.","zh":"人類進入美洲伴隨着氣候變化。"},{"en":"Entrance into the Americas means humans arriving in North and South America for the first time.","zh":"entrance into the Americas 指人類首次抵達北美洲和南美洲。"},{"en":"Archaeologists study tools and bones to understand early human entrance into new regions.","zh":"考古學家研究工具和骨骼，以了解早期人類進入新地區。"},{"en":"If people entered the Americas during environmental change, animal populations faced several pressures.","zh":"如果人類在環境變化期間進入美洲，動物種群就面對幾種壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes arrival into a major geographical region.","zh":"這個片語描述進入一個主要地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be accompanied by","meaning":"伴隨着……","examples":[{"en":"Human migration was accompanied by major climatic change.","zh":"人類遷徙伴隨着重大氣候變化。"},{"en":"Be accompanied by means happen together with something else.","zh":"be accompanied by 指與另一事物同時發生或同行。"},{"en":"A school trip may be accompanied by a teacher and several parent volunteers.","zh":"學校旅行可能由一位老師和幾位家長義工陪同。"},{"en":"If human arrival was accompanied by climate change, it is hard to blame only one factor.","zh":"如果人類到達伴隨氣候變化，就很難只歸咎於單一因素。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that two things occurred together.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩件事同時發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"change from…to…","meaning":"從……轉變成……","examples":[{"en":"Australia’s climate changed from cold and dry to warm and dry.","zh":"澳洲氣候從寒冷乾燥轉變成溫暖乾燥。"},{"en":"Change from A to B means move or develop from one state into another.","zh":"change from A to B 指從一種狀態移向或發展成另一種狀態。"},{"en":"A student may change from nervous to confident after enough speaking practice.","zh":"學生在足夠口語練習後，可能從緊張轉變成自信。"},{"en":"If climate changes from cold to warm, species adapted to cold may struggle.","zh":"如果氣候從寒冷轉變成溫暖，適應寒冷的物種可能困難。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly shows before-and-after contrast.","zh":"這個片語清楚顯示前後對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"surface water became scarce","meaning":"地表水變得稀少","examples":[{"en":"Surface water became scarce as Australia grew warmer.","zh":"隨着澳洲變暖，地表水變得稀少。"},{"en":"Surface water became scarce means water in rivers, lakes, and ponds became difficult to find.","zh":"surface water became scarce 指河流、湖泊和池塘中的水變得難以找到。"},{"en":"During a drought, surface water may become scarce and farmers may depend on wells.","zh":"乾旱期間，地表水可能變得稀少，農民可能依賴水井。"},{"en":"If surface water is scarce, animals must move, adapt, or die.","zh":"如果地表水稀少，動物就必須遷移、適應或死亡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a serious shortage of accessible water.","zh":"這個片語描述可接觸水源嚴重短缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"inland lakes","meaning":"內陸湖泊","examples":[{"en":"Most inland lakes became completely or seasonally dry.","zh":"大多數內陸湖泊變得完全或季節性乾涸。"},{"en":"Inland lakes are lakes located away from the sea or coast.","zh":"inland lakes 指位於遠離海洋或海岸地區的湖泊。"},{"en":"A map may show inland lakes in the centre of a continent.","zh":"地圖可能顯示大陸中心的內陸湖泊。"},{"en":"If inland lakes dry out, animals depending on freshwater may lose habitat.","zh":"如果內陸湖泊乾涸，依賴淡水的動物可能失去棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lakes inside land areas.","zh":"這個片語描述陸地內部的湖泊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in the warmer seasons","meaning":"在較炎熱季節","examples":[{"en":"Many lakes dried out in the warmer seasons.","zh":"許多湖泊在較炎熱季節乾涸。"},{"en":"In the warmer seasons means during the hotter parts of the year.","zh":"in the warmer seasons 指在一年中較熱的時期。"},{"en":"In the warmer seasons, families may use fans and drink more water.","zh":"在較炎熱季節，家庭可能使用風扇並喝更多水。"},{"en":"If lakes dry in warm seasons, animals may face seasonal water shortages.","zh":"如果湖泊在暖季乾涸，動物可能面對季節性缺水。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an event with hotter times of year.","zh":"這個片語把事件與一年中較熱時期連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"predominantly browsing animals","meaning":"主要以樹葉為食的動物","examples":[{"en":"Predominantly browsing animals depended heavily on leafy vegetation.","zh":"主要以樹葉為食的動物高度依賴葉狀植被。"},{"en":"Predominantly browsing animals are animals that mainly feed on leaves, shoots, and shrubs.","zh":"predominantly browsing animals 指主要吃樹葉、嫩枝和灌木的動物。"},{"en":"Deer are often browsing animals when they eat leaves from bushes and young trees.","zh":"鹿吃灌木和幼樹葉子時，通常是食葉型動物。"},{"en":"If leafy vegetation disappears, browsing animals may lose their main food supply.","zh":"如果葉狀植被消失，食葉動物可能失去主要食物供應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes animals by their feeding style.","zh":"這個片語按覓食方式描述動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lose their habitat","meaning":"失去棲息地","examples":[{"en":"Many large animals lost their habitat as the environment dried.","zh":"隨着環境變乾，許多大型動物失去棲息地。"},{"en":"Lose their habitat means lose the natural place where they live, feed, and reproduce.","zh":"lose their habitat 指失去牠們生活、覓食和繁殖的自然地方。"},{"en":"Birds may lose their habitat when old trees are cut down for construction.","zh":"當老樹因建設被砍伐，鳥類可能失去棲息地。"},{"en":"If animals lose habitat, their population may fall even without direct hunting.","zh":"如果動物失去棲息地，即使沒有直接狩獵，種群也可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes loss of living space.","zh":"這個片語描述生活空間的失去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"retreat to a narrow band","meaning":"退守至狹窄地帶","examples":[{"en":"The surviving animals retreated to a narrow band in eastern Australia.","zh":"倖存動物退守至澳洲東部的一條狹窄地帶。"},{"en":"Retreat to a narrow band means move back into a small strip of remaining suitable habitat.","zh":"retreat to a narrow band 指退到仍然合適的細長棲息地。"},{"en":"During a flood, people may retreat to a narrow band of higher ground.","zh":"洪水期間，人們可能退守至一條較高地勢的狹窄地帶。"},{"en":"If only one strip still has water and vegetation, animals may concentrate there.","zh":"如果只有一條地帶仍有水和植被，動物可能集中在那裡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes survival in a reduced remaining area.","zh":"這個片語描述在縮小的剩餘區域中生存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"permanent water supplies","meaning":"永久水源","examples":[{"en":"Eastern Australia still had permanent water supplies.","zh":"澳洲東部仍有永久水源。"},{"en":"Permanent water supplies are sources of water that remain available all year.","zh":"permanent water supplies 指全年仍可使用的水源。"},{"en":"A village with permanent water supplies can farm more reliably during dry seasons.","zh":"擁有永久水源的村莊在旱季可以更可靠地耕作。"},{"en":"If animals have permanent water, they can survive when seasonal ponds dry out.","zh":"如果動物有永久水源，當季節性池塘乾涸時仍能生存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stable access to water.","zh":"這個片語描述穩定取得水的機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"better vegetation","meaning":"較茂盛的植被","examples":[{"en":"The remaining habitat provided better vegetation.","zh":"剩餘棲息地提供較茂盛的植被。"},{"en":"Better vegetation means more suitable, richer, or healthier plant cover.","zh":"better vegetation 指更合適、更豐富或更健康的植物覆蓋。"},{"en":"A park with better vegetation may provide more shade, insects, and bird habitat.","zh":"擁有較好植被的公園可能提供更多樹蔭、昆蟲和鳥類棲息地。"},{"en":"If animals find better vegetation, they may have more food and shelter.","zh":"如果動物找到較好植被，就可能有更多食物和庇護。"},{"en":"The phrase compares plant quality between places.","zh":"這個片語比較不同地方的植物質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"co-exist with humans","meaning":"與人類共存","examples":[{"en":"Australian megafauna may have co-existed with humans for thousands of years.","zh":"澳洲巨型動物群可能與人類共存了數千年。"},{"en":"Co-exist with humans means live in the same region at the same time as people.","zh":"co-exist with humans 指與人類在同一地區同時生活。"},{"en":"Urban birds co-exist with humans by nesting on buildings and eating food scraps.","zh":"城市鳥類透過在建築物築巢和吃食物殘渣與人類共存。"},{"en":"If animals co-exist with humans for a long time, human arrival alone may not explain their extinction.","zh":"如果動物與人類共存很長時間，單靠人類到達未必能解釋其滅絕。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shared presence, not necessarily peaceful interaction.","zh":"這個片語描述共同存在，不一定是和平互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Aboriginal hunting","meaning":"澳洲原住民狩獵","examples":[{"en":"Modern kangaroos survived thousands of years of Aboriginal hunting.","zh":"現代袋鼠捱過了數千年的澳洲原住民狩獵。"},{"en":"Aboriginal hunting refers to hunting by Indigenous Australian peoples.","zh":"Aboriginal hunting 指澳洲原住民族的狩獵活動。"},{"en":"History lessons may discuss Aboriginal hunting practices when studying traditional land use.","zh":"歷史課研究傳統土地使用時，可能討論澳洲原住民狩獵做法。"},{"en":"If kangaroos survived long-term Aboriginal hunting, hunting alone may not explain later declines.","zh":"如果袋鼠長期捱過澳洲原住民狩獵，單靠狩獵未必能解釋後來衰退。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a specific cultural and historical hunting context.","zh":"這個片語指出特定文化和歷史狩獵背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"an onslaught of","meaning":"大規模而猛烈的……","examples":[{"en":"Kangaroos also survived an onslaught of commercial hunting.","zh":"袋鼠也捱過了大規模而猛烈的商業狩獵。"},{"en":"An onslaught of something is a large, forceful, and often damaging amount of it.","zh":"an onslaught of something 指大量、猛烈且常具破壞性的某事。"},{"en":"A small business may face an onslaught of complaints after a delivery failure.","zh":"送貨失誤後，小企業可能面對大量猛烈投訴。"},{"en":"If animals survive an onslaught of hunting, their population must be relatively resilient.","zh":"如果動物能捱過大規模狩獵，其種群必定相對有韌性。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests intense pressure or attack.","zh":"這個片語暗示強烈壓力或攻擊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"commercial shooters","meaning":"商業獵人","examples":[{"en":"Commercial shooters killed large numbers of kangaroos.","zh":"商業獵人殺死了大量袋鼠。"},{"en":"Commercial shooters are people who hunt animals for money or business purposes.","zh":"commercial shooters 指為金錢或商業目的狩獵動物的人。"},{"en":"Commercial shooters may sell meat, skins, or other animal products.","zh":"商業獵人可能出售肉、皮或其他動物產品。"},{"en":"If commercial shooters target a species heavily, its population can fall quickly.","zh":"如果商業獵人大量針對某物種，其種群可能迅速下降。"},{"en":"The phrase distinguishes profit-based hunting from subsistence hunting.","zh":"這個片語把盈利狩獵與維生狩獵區分開來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a group of scientists led by","meaning":"由……領導的一組科學家","examples":[{"en":"A group of scientists led by A. J. Stuart examined extinction patterns.","zh":"由 A. J. Stuart 領導的一組科學家研究滅絕模式。"},{"en":"A group of scientists led by someone means a research team directed or headed by that person.","zh":"a group of scientists led by someone 指由某人指導或帶領的研究團隊。"},{"en":"A group of students led by their teacher may conduct a survey in the community.","zh":"由老師帶領的一組學生可能在社區進行調查。"},{"en":"If a named scientist leads a team, that person is usually responsible for guiding the study.","zh":"如果一位具名科學家領導團隊，該人通常負責指導研究。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies leadership within a research group.","zh":"這個片語指出研究團隊中的領導角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"聚焦於……","examples":[{"en":"The scientists focused on northern Eurasia.","zh":"科學家聚焦於歐亞大陸北部。"},{"en":"Focus on means give special attention to one subject, place, or problem.","zh":"focus on 指特別注意某一主題、地點或問題。"},{"en":"A student may focus on grammar before an English exam if that is the weakest area.","zh":"如果文法是最弱範疇，學生考英文前可能聚焦於文法。"},{"en":"If researchers focus on one region, they can study its evidence in more detail.","zh":"如果研究人員聚焦於一個地區，就能更仔細研究其證據。"},{"en":"The phrase shows concentration rather than general coverage.","zh":"這個片語顯示集中，而不是全面覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"northern Eurasia","meaning":"歐亞大陸北部","examples":[{"en":"The study examined Europe and Siberia in northern Eurasia.","zh":"該研究檢視歐亞大陸北部的歐洲和西伯利亞。"},{"en":"Northern Eurasia means the northern part of the large landmass containing Europe and Asia.","zh":"northern Eurasia 指包含歐洲和亞洲的大陸北部。"},{"en":"A climate map of northern Eurasia may show cold winters and wide open landscapes.","zh":"歐亞大陸北部的氣候圖可能顯示寒冷冬天和廣闊開闊景觀。"},{"en":"If extinction patterns differed there, they can be compared with North America or Africa.","zh":"如果那裡的滅絕模式不同，就可以與北美洲或非洲比較。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a broad geographical research area.","zh":"這個片語給出廣闊地理研究區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the best data show that","meaning":"最可靠的數據顯示","examples":[{"en":"The best data show that several species vanished during the Late Pleistocene.","zh":"最可靠的數據顯示，幾個物種在更新世晚期消失。"},{"en":"The best data show that means the strongest available evidence indicates something.","zh":"the best data show that 指目前最有力的證據顯示某事。"},{"en":"The best data show that students sleep better when homework deadlines are clear.","zh":"最可靠的數據顯示，當功課截止日期清晰時，學生睡得較好。"},{"en":"If the best data point to a pattern, researchers treat that pattern seriously.","zh":"如果最佳數據指向某模式，研究人員就會認真看待該模式。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses evidence-based conclusion.","zh":"這個片語強調以證據為本的結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the Late Pleistocene","meaning":"更新世晚期","examples":[{"en":"Many large animals became extinct during the Late Pleistocene.","zh":"許多大型動物在更新世晚期滅絕。"},{"en":"The Late Pleistocene was the later part of the Pleistocene epoch, close to the end of the last ice age.","zh":"the Late Pleistocene 指更新世較後期，接近上一個冰河時期結束。"},{"en":"Archaeology students may study the Late Pleistocene to understand early humans and extinct megafauna.","zh":"考古學生可能研究更新世晚期，以了解早期人類和已滅絕巨型動物群。"},{"en":"If extinction happened in the Late Pleistocene, it occurred in a period of major environmental change.","zh":"如果滅絕發生在更新世晚期，它就發生於重大環境變化時期。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific prehistoric time period.","zh":"這個片語指出特定史前時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"cold-adapted animals","meaning":"適應寒冷環境的動物","examples":[{"en":"Some cold-adapted animals survived until the final cold stage.","zh":"有些適應寒冷環境的動物生存至最後寒冷階段。"},{"en":"Cold-adapted animals are animals with bodies or behaviours suited to cold environments.","zh":"cold-adapted animals 指身體或行為適合寒冷環境的動物。"},{"en":"Polar bears are cold-adapted animals with thick fur and fat for insulation.","zh":"北極熊是適應寒冷環境的動物，具有厚毛和脂肪保溫。"},{"en":"If climates warm, cold-adapted animals may lose the habitats where they perform best.","zh":"如果氣候變暖，適應寒冷的動物可能失去最適合牠們的棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes species specialised for cold conditions.","zh":"這個片語描述專門適應寒冷條件的物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the final part of","meaning":"……的最後階段","examples":[{"en":"Several species survived into the final part of the cold stage.","zh":"幾個物種生存至寒冷階段的最後階段。"},{"en":"The final part of something means its last section or period.","zh":"the final part of something 指某事的最後部分或時期。"},{"en":"Students often feel tired during the final part of an exam.","zh":"學生在考試最後階段常感到疲倦。"},{"en":"If a species survives into the final part of a climate stage, it lasts almost until that stage ends.","zh":"如果物種生存至某氣候階段的最後部分，它就幾乎持續到該階段結束。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the last phase of a period.","zh":"這個片語集中於某時期的最後階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"two distinct phases","meaning":"兩個明顯不同的階段","examples":[{"en":"The evidence indicates two distinct phases of extinction.","zh":"證據顯示有兩個明顯不同的滅絕階段。"},{"en":"Two distinct phases are two clearly separate stages.","zh":"two distinct phases 指兩個清楚分開的階段。"},{"en":"A school project may have two distinct phases: research first, then presentation.","zh":"學校項目可能有兩個明顯不同的階段：先研究，後匯報。"},{"en":"If extinctions happened in two phases, they did not all occur at the same moment.","zh":"如果滅絕分兩個階段發生，就不是所有物種同時消失。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses separation and sequence.","zh":"這個片語強調分離和次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"coincide with","meaning":"與……同時發生","examples":[{"en":"Neither extinction phase clearly coincided with a change in human populations.","zh":"兩個滅絕階段都沒有明確與人類人口變化同時發生。"},{"en":"Coincide with means happen at the same time as something else.","zh":"coincide with 指與另一件事在同一時間發生。"},{"en":"A school fair may coincide with heavy rain, reducing visitor numbers.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能與大雨同時發生，令訪客人數減少。"},{"en":"If extinction coincides with human arrival, researchers may consider a possible link.","zh":"如果滅絕與人類到達同時發生，研究人員可能考慮兩者是否有關。"},{"en":"The phrase shows timing, not automatic causation.","zh":"這個片語顯示時間重疊，不自動代表因果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"replacement of Neanderthals","meaning":"尼安德特人被取代","examples":[{"en":"The extinctions did not coincide with the replacement of Neanderthals.","zh":"這些滅絕並沒有與尼安德特人被取代同時發生。"},{"en":"Replacement of Neanderthals means Neanderthal populations disappearing or being replaced by modern humans.","zh":"replacement of Neanderthals 指尼安德特人群消失或被現代人類取代。"},{"en":"History students may study the replacement of older tools by newer technologies.","zh":"歷史學生可能研究舊工具被新技術取代。"},{"en":"If extinction did not match the timing of Neanderthal replacement, that event may not explain it directly.","zh":"如果滅絕時間與尼安德特人被取代不吻合，該事件可能不能直接解釋滅絕。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a major prehistoric human population change.","zh":"這個片語描述史前一次重大人類種群變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"modern humans","meaning":"現代人類","examples":[{"en":"Modern humans were not the sole cause of the extinctions.","zh":"現代人類不是這些滅絕的唯一成因。"},{"en":"Modern humans are Homo sapiens, the human species living today.","zh":"modern humans 指 Homo sapiens，即今天仍存在的人類物種。"},{"en":"Archaeologists study modern humans by examining tools, bones, art, and settlements.","zh":"考古學家透過工具、骨骼、藝術和聚落研究現代人類。"},{"en":"If modern humans arrived before extinction but species survived for long periods, the cause may be complex.","zh":"如果現代人類在滅絕前已到達，但物種仍生存很久，原因可能很複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase distinguishes our species from earlier human relatives.","zh":"這個片語把我們的物種與更早的人類親屬區分開來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a simple correspondence between","meaning":"……之間的簡單對應關係","examples":[{"en":"There was no simple correspondence between extinction and human arrival.","zh":"滅絕與人類到達之間沒有簡單對應關係。"},{"en":"A simple correspondence between two things means a clear one-to-one match between them.","zh":"a simple correspondence between two things 指兩件事之間清楚的一對一配對。"},{"en":"There is no simple correspondence between study time and grades if sleep and exam technique also matter.","zh":"如果睡眠和考試技巧也重要，學習時間與成績之間就沒有簡單對應關係。"},{"en":"If extinctions do not occur exactly when humans arrive, the relationship is not simple.","zh":"如果滅絕沒有正好在人類到達時發生，兩者關係就不簡單。"},{"en":"The phrase rejects an overly neat connection.","zh":"這個片語否定過於整齊的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"human arrival","meaning":"人類到達","examples":[{"en":"The timing of human arrival influenced extinction patterns.","zh":"人類到達的時間影響了滅絕模式。"},{"en":"Human arrival means people entering a region where they had not lived before.","zh":"human arrival 指人類進入以前未曾居住的地區。"},{"en":"The arrival of people on an island can change animal behaviour and habitat use.","zh":"人類到達島嶼可以改變動物行為和棲息地使用。"},{"en":"If human arrival occurs during environmental stress, animal populations may face extra pressure.","zh":"如果人類到達發生在環境壓力期間，動物種群可能面對額外壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to when humans first reach a place.","zh":"這個片語指人類首次到達某地的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"climate change alone","meaning":"單靠氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"Climate change alone could not explain every extinction.","zh":"單靠氣候變化無法解釋每一次滅絕。"},{"en":"Climate change alone means climate change by itself, without other causes.","zh":"climate change alone 指只有氣候變化本身，不包括其他原因。"},{"en":"Poor marks may not be caused by study time alone; stress and sleep may also matter.","zh":"成績差未必單靠學習時間解釋；壓力和睡眠也可能重要。"},{"en":"If some extinctions do not match climate shifts, other pressures must be considered.","zh":"如果某些滅絕與氣候轉變不吻合，就必須考慮其他壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase separates one cause from a wider set of causes.","zh":"這個片語把單一原因與更廣泛原因區分開來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"evidence points to","meaning":"證據顯示","examples":[{"en":"The evidence points to a combined environmental and human effect.","zh":"證據顯示這是環境與人類共同造成的影響。"},{"en":"Evidence points to means the available facts suggest a particular explanation.","zh":"evidence points to 指現有事實指向某一特定解釋。"},{"en":"Wet streets and dark clouds point to recent rain.","zh":"濕街道和烏雲顯示剛下過雨。"},{"en":"If several kinds of evidence point to the same cause, the explanation becomes stronger.","zh":"如果幾種證據都指向同一原因，該解釋就變得更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase shows where the facts seem to lead.","zh":"這個片語顯示事實似乎導向哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a combined effect","meaning":"綜合影響","examples":[{"en":"The extinctions were probably caused by a combined effect.","zh":"這些滅絕很可能由綜合影響造成。"},{"en":"A combined effect is the result produced by two or more factors acting together.","zh":"a combined effect 指兩個或更多因素共同作用產生的結果。"},{"en":"Poor sleep and heavy homework can have a combined effect on student stress.","zh":"睡眠不足和功課沉重可以對學生壓力產生綜合影響。"},{"en":"If climate change and hunting act together, extinction risk can rise sharply.","zh":"如果氣候變化和狩獵共同作用，滅絕風險可以急升。"},{"en":"The phrase means the cause is shared, not single.","zh":"這個片語指原因是共同的，而非單一的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a fundamental change in climate","meaning":"根本性的氣候轉變","examples":[{"en":"A fundamental change in climate reorganised the vegetation.","zh":"根本性的氣候轉變重新改變了植被分布。"},{"en":"A fundamental change in climate is a deep and important shift in temperature, rainfall, or seasonal patterns.","zh":"a fundamental change in climate 指氣溫、降雨或季節模式上的深層而重要轉變。"},{"en":"A fundamental change in school policy can affect every class, not just one subject.","zh":"學校政策的根本改變可以影響每一班，而不只是一科。"},{"en":"If climate changes fundamentally, whole plant communities may be replaced.","zh":"如果氣候發生根本轉變，整個植物群落可能被取代。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a major underlying change.","zh":"這個片語強調重大根本變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"reorganise the vegetation","meaning":"重新改變植被分布","examples":[{"en":"Climate change reorganised the vegetation across the region.","zh":"氣候變化重新改變了整個地區的植被分布。"},{"en":"Reorganise the vegetation means change the pattern, location, or mixture of plant life.","zh":"reorganise the vegetation 指改變植物生命的模式、位置或組合。"},{"en":"A new park design can reorganise the vegetation by moving trees, grass, and flower beds.","zh":"新公園設計可以透過移動樹木、草地和花圃來重新安排植被。"},{"en":"If rainfall changes, forests may replace grasslands or dry plants may replace wetland plants.","zh":"如果降雨改變，森林可能取代草地，或乾旱植物可能取代濕地植物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large shift in plant distribution.","zh":"這個片語描述植物分布的大變動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"advanced Palaeolithic humans","meaning":"進步的舊石器時代人類","examples":[{"en":"Advanced Palaeolithic humans increased pressure on large animals.","zh":"進步的舊石器時代人類增加了大型動物的壓力。"},{"en":"Advanced Palaeolithic humans were later Stone Age people with more developed tools and hunting methods.","zh":"advanced Palaeolithic humans 指具有較發達工具和狩獵方法的較晚期石器時代人類。"},{"en":"History students may study Palaeolithic humans through cave art, stone tools, and hunting sites.","zh":"歷史學生可能透過洞穴藝術、石器和狩獵遺址研究舊石器時代人類。"},{"en":"If humans had better tools, they could hunt large animals more effectively.","zh":"如果人類有更好的工具，就能更有效狩獵大型動物。"},{"en":"The phrase links human technological development with prehistoric hunting pressure.","zh":"這個片語把人類技術發展與史前狩獵壓力連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a wave of extinction","meaning":"一波滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Environmental change and hunting caused a wave of extinction.","zh":"環境變化和狩獵造成一波滅絕。"},{"en":"A wave of extinction means many species disappearing during the same broad period.","zh":"a wave of extinction 指許多物種在同一大致時期消失。"},{"en":"A wave of shop closures may happen when rent rises and customers move online.","zh":"當租金上升而顧客轉到網上購物，可能出現一波店舖倒閉。"},{"en":"If several pressures hit ecosystems together, many species may decline in a wave.","zh":"如果幾種壓力同時打擊生態系統，許多物種可能一波接一波衰退。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a series of losses spreading through a group.","zh":"這個片語暗示一系列損失在群體中擴散。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"reveal a profound contrast","meaning":"顯示強烈對比","examples":[{"en":"The data reveal a profound contrast between two regions.","zh":"數據顯示兩個地區之間的強烈對比。"},{"en":"Reveal a profound contrast means show a deep and important difference.","zh":"reveal a profound contrast 指顯示深刻而重要的差異。"},{"en":"Exam results may reveal a profound contrast between students with regular feedback and those without it.","zh":"考試結果可能顯示有定期回饋和沒有回饋的學生之間有強烈對比。"},{"en":"If one region lost species suddenly and another lost them slowly, the contrast is important.","zh":"如果一個地區物種突然消失，而另一地區慢慢消失，這種對比就很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a difference that matters for explanation.","zh":"這個片語突出對解釋有意義的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"moderate and staggered","meaning":"程度較輕而且分階段發生","examples":[{"en":"Extinctions in northern Eurasia were moderate and staggered.","zh":"歐亞大陸北部的滅絕程度較輕，而且分階段發生。"},{"en":"Moderate and staggered means not extremely severe and happening in separate stages over time.","zh":"moderate and staggered 指不極端嚴重，並在不同階段隨時間發生。"},{"en":"A school may introduce moderate and staggered changes rather than changing every rule at once.","zh":"學校可能引入程度較溫和而分階段的改變，而不是一次過改所有規則。"},{"en":"If extinctions are staggered, species disappear at different times, not all together.","zh":"如果滅絕是分階段的，物種會在不同時間消失，而不是全部同時消失。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts with severe and sudden change.","zh":"這個片語與 severe and sudden 形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"severe and sudden","meaning":"嚴重而突然","examples":[{"en":"Extinctions in North America were severe and sudden.","zh":"北美洲的滅絕嚴重而突然。"},{"en":"Severe and sudden means very serious and happening quickly.","zh":"severe and sudden 指非常嚴重並且快速發生。"},{"en":"A severe and sudden storm can close roads within minutes.","zh":"嚴重而突然的暴風雨可以在數分鐘內封閉道路。"},{"en":"If extinction is severe and sudden, many species disappear in a short time.","zh":"如果滅絕嚴重而突然，許多物種會在短時間內消失。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both intensity and speed.","zh":"這個片語同時強調強度和速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"relate to differences in","meaning":"與……的差異有關","examples":[{"en":"These patterns relate to differences in the timing of human arrival.","zh":"這些模式與人類到達時間的差異有關。"},{"en":"Relate to differences in means be connected with the ways two things are not the same.","zh":"relate to differences in 指與兩件事不同之處有關。"},{"en":"Differences in exam results may relate to differences in sleep, practice, and feedback.","zh":"考試成績差異可能與睡眠、練習和回饋的差異有關。"},{"en":"If humans arrived earlier in one region than another, extinction patterns may differ too.","zh":"如果人類在一個地區比另一地區更早到達，滅絕模式也可能不同。"},{"en":"The phrase links a pattern to a comparison.","zh":"這個片語把模式與比較連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"timing of human arrival","meaning":"人類到達的時間","examples":[{"en":"The timing of human arrival varied between regions.","zh":"人類到達的時間因地區而異。"},{"en":"Timing of human arrival means when humans first reached a particular place.","zh":"timing of human arrival 指人類首次到達某地的時間。"},{"en":"The timing of a teacher’s feedback can affect whether students can improve before the exam.","zh":"老師回饋的時間會影響學生是否能在考試前進步。"},{"en":"If humans arrived during climate stress, animals may have faced several pressures at once.","zh":"如果人類在氣候壓力期間到達，動物可能同時面對幾種壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on when, not simply whether, humans arrived.","zh":"這個片語集中於何時到達，而不只是是否到達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"human predation","meaning":"人類獵殺","examples":[{"en":"Human predation contributed to the disappearance of large animals.","zh":"人類獵殺促成了大型動物的消失。"},{"en":"Human predation means humans hunting and killing animals as prey.","zh":"human predation 指人類狩獵並殺死動物作為獵物。"},{"en":"Overfishing is a form of human predation on fish populations.","zh":"過度捕魚是人類對魚類種群獵殺的一種形式。"},{"en":"If human predation increases while habitats shrink, animal populations may decline quickly.","zh":"如果人類獵殺增加，而棲息地同時縮小，動物種群可能快速下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes humans acting as predators.","zh":"這個片語描述人類作為捕食者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"only during periods of","meaning":"只在……時期","examples":[{"en":"Predation caused widespread extinction only during periods of environmental change.","zh":"捕食只在環境變化時期造成廣泛滅絕。"},{"en":"Only during periods of means only in particular times when something is happening.","zh":"only during periods of 指只在某事發生的特定時期。"},{"en":"Some shops become crowded only during periods of holiday sales.","zh":"有些商店只在假日減價時期變得擁擠。"},{"en":"If hunting is deadly only during environmental stress, the combination matters more than hunting alone.","zh":"如果狩獵只在環境壓力期間致命，組合因素就比單靠狩獵更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase limits when something is true.","zh":"這個片語限制某事成立的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"fundamental environmental change","meaning":"根本性的環境轉變","examples":[{"en":"Extinctions accelerated during periods of fundamental environmental change.","zh":"在根本性的環境轉變時期，滅絕加速。"},{"en":"Fundamental environmental change means deep changes in climate, vegetation, water, or habitat structure.","zh":"fundamental environmental change 指氣候、植被、水源或棲息地結構上的深層變化。"},{"en":"A city faces fundamental environmental change if coastlines flood and heatwaves become common.","zh":"如果海岸線被淹、水熱浪變得常見，城市就面對根本性環境轉變。"},{"en":"If environments change fundamentally, species may not adapt quickly enough.","zh":"如果環境發生根本變化，物種可能無法夠快適應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes major changes in the conditions of life.","zh":"這個片語描述生命條件中的重大變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"complete the following summary","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the following summary using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"Complete the following summary means fill in the missing information in the short text below.","zh":"complete the following summary 指填寫下面短文中缺失的資料。"},{"en":"In reading exams, students complete a summary by matching passage words with grammar and meaning.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生透過把文章字詞與文法和意思配合來完成摘要。"},{"en":"If the summary says “no more than three words”, answers that are too long lose marks.","zh":"如果摘要題說「不超過三個字」，答案太長會失分。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction in reading tests.","zh":"這個片語是閱讀測驗中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不超過三個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than three words.","zh":"每個答案應不超過三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must be three words or fewer.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案必須是三個詞或更少。"},{"en":"If the answer is “important food plants”, it follows a three-word limit.","zh":"如果答案是 “important food plants”，它符合三詞限制。"},{"en":"If students write four words when only three are allowed, the answer may be marked wrong.","zh":"如果只允許三個詞而學生寫四個詞，答案可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個片語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"remains were first found","meaning":"遺骸最早被發現","examples":[{"en":"The question asks when the animal’s remains were first found.","zh":"題目問該動物的遺骸最早何時被發現。"},{"en":"Remains were first found means the bones or body parts were discovered for the first time.","zh":"remains were first found 指骨骼或身體部分首次被發現。"},{"en":"A museum note may state when dinosaur remains were first found in a region.","zh":"博物館說明可能指出恐龍遺骸在某地區最早何時被發現。"},{"en":"If remains were first found long ago, early interpretations may later be corrected by new science.","zh":"如果遺骸很久以前最早被發現，早期解釋可能後來被新科學修正。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the first discovery of physical evidence.","zh":"這個片語集中於實物證據的首次發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"approximately","meaning":"大約","examples":[{"en":"The species first appeared approximately 400,000 years ago.","zh":"該物種大約在四十萬年前首次出現。"},{"en":"Approximately means about, not exactly.","zh":"approximately 指大約，而不是完全精確。"},{"en":"The bus journey takes approximately thirty minutes if traffic is light.","zh":"如果交通順暢，巴士車程大約三十分鐘。"},{"en":"If scientists say approximately, they allow for some uncertainty in the estimate.","zh":"如果科學家說 approximately，就是容許估算中有一定不確定性。"},{"en":"The word is useful when exact numbers are not known.","zh":"這個詞適合用於不知道精確數字時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be driven onto the plains","meaning":"被迫遷到平原","examples":[{"en":"The changing forests may have driven the animals onto the plains.","zh":"變化中的森林可能把動物迫遷到平原。"},{"en":"Be driven onto the plains means be forced to move onto open flat land.","zh":"be driven onto the plains 指被迫移到開闊平坦土地。"},{"en":"Flooding may drive families onto higher ground for safety.","zh":"洪水可能迫使家庭遷到高地以保安全。"},{"en":"If forests expand into former open areas, grazing animals may be driven onto remaining plains.","zh":"如果森林擴展到原本開闊地，吃草動物可能被迫遷到剩餘平原。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement caused by pressure, not free choice.","zh":"這個片語描述由壓力造成的移動，而不是自由選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"an important factor in","meaning":"……的重要因素","examples":[{"en":"Hunting was considered an important factor in the extinction.","zh":"狩獵被視為滅絕的重要因素。"},{"en":"An important factor in something is a major cause or influence affecting it.","zh":"an important factor in something 指影響某事的主要原因或力量。"},{"en":"Sleep is an important factor in memory and concentration.","zh":"睡眠是記憶和專注力的重要因素。"},{"en":"If hunting reduces an already weak population, it can become an important factor in extinction.","zh":"如果狩獵令已經脆弱的種群減少，它可以成為滅絕的重要因素。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies one significant part of an explanation.","zh":"這個片語指出解釋中的一個重要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"begin hunting","meaning":"開始狩獵","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to when humans began hunting the animals.","zh":"題目指人類何時開始狩獵這些動物。"},{"en":"Begin hunting means start killing animals for food, materials, or other purposes.","zh":"begin hunting 指開始為食物、材料或其他目的殺死動物。"},{"en":"A community may begin hunting a species when it becomes a common food source.","zh":"當某物種成為常見食物來源時，社區可能開始狩獵它。"},{"en":"If humans begin hunting large animals during environmental stress, the added pressure may be serious.","zh":"如果人類在環境壓力期間開始狩獵大型動物，額外壓力可能很嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the start of hunting activity.","zh":"這個片語標示狩獵活動的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a variety of climatic fluctuations","meaning":"多種氣候波動","examples":[{"en":"The species had survived a variety of climatic fluctuations.","zh":"該物種曾捱過多種氣候波動。"},{"en":"A variety of climatic fluctuations means several different changes in climate over time.","zh":"a variety of climatic fluctuations 指隨時間出現的幾種不同氣候變化。"},{"en":"Farmers may face a variety of weather changes, including drought, storms, and warmer winters.","zh":"農民可能面對多種天氣變化，包括乾旱、風暴和較暖冬天。"},{"en":"If a species survives many climate ups and downs, one final extinction event needs careful explanation.","zh":"如果某物種曾捱過許多氣候起伏，最後一次滅絕事件就需要仔細解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses multiple forms of climate variation.","zh":"這個片語強調多種形式的氣候變動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be controversial because","meaning":"因……而具爭議","examples":[{"en":"The antler theory is controversial because the deer survived earlier forests.","zh":"鹿角理論因為巨鹿曾在早期森林中生存而具爭議。"},{"en":"Be controversial because means cause disagreement for a particular reason.","zh":"be controversial because 指因某特定原因而引起分歧。"},{"en":"A school rule may be controversial because students think it is unfair.","zh":"學校規則可能因學生認為不公平而具爭議。"},{"en":"If evidence weakens a theory, the theory becomes controversial rather than accepted.","zh":"如果證據削弱某理論，該理論就變得具爭議，而不是被接受。"},{"en":"The phrase links disagreement with its reason.","zh":"這個片語把分歧與其原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"by the end of","meaning":"到……結束時","examples":[{"en":"Many large mammals had disappeared by the end of the last ice age.","zh":"到上一個冰河時期結束時，許多大型哺乳動物已經消失。"},{"en":"By the end of means before or at the final point of a period.","zh":"by the end of 指在某時期的最後時點前或當時。"},{"en":"Students should submit the report by the end of Friday.","zh":"學生應在星期五結束前提交報告。"},{"en":"If many species had vanished by the end of an era, extinction was mostly complete by then.","zh":"如果許多物種到某時代結束時已消失，滅絕在那時已大致完成。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a deadline or final time point.","zh":"這個片語給出截止或最後時間點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"provide answers to","meaning":"回答……","examples":[{"en":"Students provide answers to the questions using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞回答問題。"},{"en":"Provide answers to means give responses to questions or problems.","zh":"provide answers to 指對問題或難題給出回應。"},{"en":"A doctor may provide answers to a patient’s questions after the test results arrive.","zh":"檢查結果出來後，醫生可能回答病人的問題。"},{"en":"If students use passage words, their answers are more likely to match the exam requirement.","zh":"如果學生使用文章字詞，答案就更可能符合考試要求。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on supplying information requested.","zh":"這個片語集中於提供所要求的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a physical characteristic","meaning":"身體特徵","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which physical characteristic may have contributed to extinction.","zh":"題目問哪項身體特徵可能促成滅絕。"},{"en":"A physical characteristic is a body feature that can be seen or measured.","zh":"physical characteristic 指可被看見或量度的身體特徵。"},{"en":"Height, hair colour, wing length, and antler size are physical characteristics.","zh":"身高、髮色、翅膀長度和鹿角大小都是身體特徵。"},{"en":"If a physical characteristic becomes too costly to maintain, it may reduce survival.","zh":"如果某身體特徵維持成本太高，可能降低生存機會。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the body, not behaviour or climate.","zh":"這個片語指身體，而不是行為或氣候。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contribute to extinction","meaning":"導致滅絕","examples":[{"en":"A physical disadvantage may contribute to extinction.","zh":"身體上的不利條件可能導致滅絕。"},{"en":"Contribute to extinction means help cause a species to disappear completely.","zh":"contribute to extinction 指有助造成物種完全消失。"},{"en":"Habitat loss can contribute to extinction when animals cannot find safe breeding places.","zh":"當動物找不到安全繁殖地時，棲息地喪失可以導致滅絕。"},{"en":"If food shortage, disease, and hunting all occur together, each may contribute to extinction.","zh":"如果食物短缺、疾病和狩獵同時發生，每一項都可能促成滅絕。"},{"en":"The phrase does not always mean the only cause.","zh":"這個片語不一定指唯一原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"nutrients needed to maintain","meaning":"維持……所需的養分","examples":[{"en":"The antlers required nutrients needed to maintain their growth.","zh":"鹿角需要維持其生長所需的養分。"},{"en":"Nutrients needed to maintain something are food substances required to keep it growing or functioning.","zh":"nutrients needed to maintain something 指保持某物生長或運作所需的食物物質。"},{"en":"Children need nutrients to maintain healthy bones, muscles, and concentration.","zh":"孩子需要養分來維持健康骨骼、肌肉和專注力。"},{"en":"If animals cannot obtain these nutrients, large body structures may become harder to support.","zh":"如果動物無法獲得這些養分，大型身體結構可能更難支持。"},{"en":"The phrase connects nutrition with continued growth or function.","zh":"這個片語把營養與持續生長或功能連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"evidence from which region","meaning":"來自哪個地區的證據","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which region provided the relevant evidence.","zh":"題目問相關證據來自哪個地區。"},{"en":"Evidence from which region means the geographical area where the supporting data came from.","zh":"evidence from which region 指支持數據來自哪個地理區域。"},{"en":"A geography exam may ask evidence from which region supports a climate pattern.","zh":"地理考試可能問來自哪個地區的證據支持某氣候模式。"},{"en":"If evidence comes from northern Eurasia, it should not automatically be applied to every continent.","zh":"如果證據來自歐亞大陸北部，就不應自動套用到每個大陸。"},{"en":"The phrase asks students to connect evidence with location.","zh":"這個片語要求學生把證據與地點連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"megafaunal extinction","meaning":"巨型動物群滅絕","examples":[{"en":"The study examined whether human arrival contributed to megafaunal extinction.","zh":"該研究檢視人類到達是否促成巨型動物群滅絕。"},{"en":"Megafaunal extinction means the disappearance of very large animal species.","zh":"megafaunal extinction 指非常大型動物物種的消失。"},{"en":"Mammoth disappearance is one example of megafaunal extinction.","zh":"猛獁象消失是巨型動物群滅絕的一個例子。"},{"en":"If human arrival and climate change happened together, both may have contributed to megafaunal extinction.","zh":"如果人類到達和氣候變化同時發生，兩者都可能促成巨型動物群滅絕。"},{"en":"The phrase is a formal way to describe the loss of giant animals.","zh":"這個片語是描述巨型動物消失的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the region where","meaning":"……發生的地區","examples":[{"en":"Students identify the region where each condition applied.","zh":"學生識別每項情況發生的地區。"},{"en":"The region where means the area in which something happened or was true.","zh":"the region where 指某事發生或某情況成立的區域。"},{"en":"A weather report may identify the region where heavy rain is expected.","zh":"天氣報告可能指出預計有大雨的地區。"},{"en":"If an exam asks for the region where evidence was found, students must locate the correct place in the passage.","zh":"如果考試問證據來自哪個地區，學生必須在文章中定位正確地方。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a condition with a location.","zh":"這個片語把情況與位置連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"have little impact on","meaning":"對……影響不大","examples":[{"en":"Humans may have had little impact on extinction in some regions.","zh":"人類在某些地區可能對滅絕影響不大。"},{"en":"Have little impact on means affect something only slightly or not very much.","zh":"have little impact on 指只輕微影響某事，或影響不大。"},{"en":"A short power cut may have little impact on a school if backup lights work well.","zh":"如果後備燈運作良好，短暫停電可能對學校影響不大。"},{"en":"If animals had already adapted to humans, human presence may not greatly change their survival.","zh":"如果動物已適應人類，人類存在可能不大改變其生存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a weak effect.","zh":"這個片語描述較弱影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"climate change was mild","meaning":"氣候變化較溫和","examples":[{"en":"The fauna survived where climate change was mild.","zh":"在氣候變化較溫和的地方，動物群存活下來。"},{"en":"Climate change was mild means climate shifted only slightly or not severely.","zh":"climate change was mild 指氣候只有輕微或不嚴重的轉變。"},{"en":"If winter becomes only a little warmer, the climate change may be mild for some plants.","zh":"如果冬天只稍為變暖，對某些植物而言氣候變化可能較溫和。"},{"en":"Where climate change is mild, animals may have enough time and habitat to adapt.","zh":"在氣候變化較溫和的地方，動物可能有足夠時間和棲息地適應。"},{"en":"The phrase compares gentle change with drastic change.","zh":"這個片語把溫和變化與劇烈變化作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"fauna survived","meaning":"動物群存活下來","examples":[{"en":"The fauna survived major environmental transitions in some regions.","zh":"在某些地區，動物群在重大環境轉變中存活下來。"},{"en":"Fauna survived means the animal life in an area continued to exist.","zh":"fauna survived 指某地區的動物生命繼續存在。"},{"en":"After a storm, the local fauna may survive if shelters and food sources remain.","zh":"風暴後，如果庇護和食物來源仍在，本地動物群可能存活。"},{"en":"If fauna survived in tropical regions, their habitats may have changed less severely.","zh":"如果動物群在熱帶地區存活，其棲息地可能變化較不嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to animal communities, not plants.","zh":"這個片語指動物群落，而不是植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"both…and…contributed to","meaning":"……和……均導致……","examples":[{"en":"Both human activity and climate change contributed to extinction.","zh":"人類活動和氣候變化均導致滅絕。"},{"en":"Both A and B contributed to means two factors each helped cause the result.","zh":"both A and B contributed to 指兩個因素都幫助造成某結果。"},{"en":"Both lack of sleep and poor revision contributed to the student’s low mark.","zh":"睡眠不足和溫習不善均導致學生低分。"},{"en":"If climate reduced food and humans increased hunting, both factors mattered.","zh":"如果氣候減少食物，而人類增加狩獵，兩個因素都重要。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly shows shared responsibility.","zh":"這個片語清楚顯示共同責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"according to the findings","meaning":"根據研究結果","examples":[{"en":"Students identify the statement that is true according to the findings.","zh":"學生識別根據研究結果屬實的陳述。"},{"en":"According to the findings means based on what the research results show.","zh":"according to the findings 指根據研究結果所顯示的內容。"},{"en":"According to the findings of a school survey, students want more quiet study space.","zh":"根據學校調查結果，學生想要更多安靜自修空間。"},{"en":"If a statement goes beyond the findings, it should not be treated as proven by the study.","zh":"如果陳述超出研究結果，就不應被視為由該研究證明。"},{"en":"The phrase ties an answer to research evidence.","zh":"這個片語把答案與研究證據連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"The option contrasts Neanderthals rather than modern humans.","zh":"該選項對比的是尼安德特人，而不是現代人類。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of, and it creates a clear contrast.","zh":"rather than 指而不是，並建立清楚對比。"},{"en":"A student should correct the cause of a mistake rather than only memorising the right answer.","zh":"學生應改正錯誤原因，而不是只背正確答案。"},{"en":"If the issue is climate stress rather than human arrival alone, the explanation becomes more complex.","zh":"如果問題是氣候壓力，而不是單靠人類到達，解釋就變得更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase helps separate one idea from another.","zh":"這個片語幫助把一個想法與另一個想法分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be solely responsible for","meaning":"是……的唯一成因","examples":[{"en":"Climatic change was not solely responsible for the extinction.","zh":"氣候變化不是該次滅絕的唯一成因。"},{"en":"Be solely responsible for means be the only cause of something.","zh":"be solely responsible for 指是某事的唯一原因。"},{"en":"A teacher is not solely responsible for a student’s progress; practice at home also matters.","zh":"老師不是學生進步的唯一成因；在家練習也重要。"},{"en":"If several pressures caused extinction, no single factor was solely responsible.","zh":"如果幾種壓力造成滅絕，就沒有單一因素是唯一成因。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses exclusive responsibility.","zh":"這個片語強調獨占責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"moderate and staggered extinction","meaning":"程度較輕而分階段發生的滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Northern Eurasia experienced moderate and staggered extinction.","zh":"歐亞大陸北部經歷了程度較輕而分階段發生的滅絕。"},{"en":"Moderate and staggered extinction means species disappeared gradually and in stages, with less sudden severity.","zh":"moderate and staggered extinction 指物種逐漸並分階段消失，嚴重程度較不突然。"},{"en":"A town may face moderate and staggered shop closures if different businesses close over several years.","zh":"如果不同商店在幾年間陸續結業，小鎮可能面對程度較輕而分階段的店舖倒閉。"},{"en":"If extinction is staggered, causes may have acted at different times rather than all at once.","zh":"如果滅絕是分階段的，原因可能在不同時間作用，而不是一次過發生。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts with sudden mass extinction.","zh":"這個片語與突然大規模滅絕形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"mainly the result of","meaning":"主要是……的結果","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether extinction was mainly the result of climatic change.","zh":"題目問滅絕是否主要是氣候變化的結果。"},{"en":"Mainly the result of means mostly caused by one particular factor.","zh":"mainly the result of 指主要由某一特定因素造成。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be mainly the result of regular feedback and practice.","zh":"學生進步可能主要是定期回饋和練習的結果。"},{"en":"If extinction was mainly caused by climate, human activity would be a smaller factor.","zh":"如果滅絕主要由氣候造成，人類活動就會是較小因素。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the largest cause, not necessarily the only cause.","zh":"這個片語指出最大原因，但不一定是唯一原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 135 - Extinct - the Giant Deer.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 136":[{"front":"the Nagymaros Dam","meaning":"Nagymaros 水壩","examples":[{"en":"The Nagymaros Dam became the focus of a major environmental campaign.","zh":"Nagymaros 水壩成為一場大型環保運動的焦點。"},{"en":"The Nagymaros Dam was a proposed dam project that raised serious environmental and political concerns.","zh":"Nagymaros 水壩是一項曾引起嚴重環境和政治關注的水壩工程。"},{"en":"Students may study the Nagymaros Dam as an example of how one local project can become a national issue.","zh":"學生可能研究 Nagymaros 水壩，作為一項本地工程如何變成全國議題的例子。"},{"en":"If a dam threatens rivers, wetlands, and communities, it may attract public opposition.","zh":"如果水壩威脅河流、濕地和社區，它可能引起公眾反對。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific dam, not dams in general.","zh":"這個片語指一座特定水壩，而不是泛指所有水壩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Hungarian Academy of Sciences","meaning":"匈牙利科學院","examples":[{"en":"Janos Vargha was a biologist from the Hungarian Academy of Sciences.","zh":"Janos Vargha 是來自匈牙利科學院的生物學家。"},{"en":"The Hungarian Academy of Sciences is a major research institution in Hungary.","zh":"匈牙利科學院是匈牙利一所主要研究機構。"},{"en":"A scientist from the Hungarian Academy of Sciences may study biology, history, physics, or social issues.","zh":"來自匈牙利科學院的科學家可能研究生物、歷史、物理或社會議題。"},{"en":"If a researcher works at a respected academy, their warnings may carry more authority.","zh":"如果研究人員在受尊重的科學院工作，他們的警告可能更有權威。"},{"en":"This phrase names an institution, not a school classroom.","zh":"這個片語命名一所機構，而不是學校課室。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"begin a new career as","meaning":"開展……的新事業","examples":[{"en":"Vargha began a new career as a writer.","zh":"Vargha 開展了作家的新事業。"},{"en":"To begin a new career as something means to start working in a different professional role.","zh":"To begin a new career as something 指開始從事不同的專業角色。"},{"en":"A teacher may begin a new career as a counsellor after receiving extra training.","zh":"老師接受額外培訓後，可能開展輔導員的新事業。"},{"en":"If someone changes career, they may need new skills, contacts, and confidence.","zh":"如果某人轉換事業，他可能需要新技能、人脈和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major work change, not a short hobby.","zh":"這個片語描述重大的工作轉變，而不是短期興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"monthly nature magazine","meaning":"每月出版的自然雜誌","examples":[{"en":"He worked for a small monthly nature magazine called Buvar.","zh":"他為一本名為 Buvar 的小型每月出版自然雜誌工作。"},{"en":"A monthly nature magazine is a magazine about wildlife, landscapes, and environmental issues published once a month.","zh":"Monthly nature magazine 是每月出版一次、關於野生生物、景觀和環境議題的雜誌。"},{"en":"A student may read a monthly nature magazine to learn about birds, rivers, and forests.","zh":"學生可能閱讀每月出版的自然雜誌，以認識鳥類、河流和森林。"},{"en":"If a magazine appears monthly, editors have time to prepare longer articles and photographs.","zh":"如果雜誌每月出版，編輯有時間準備較長文章和照片。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both the topic and the publication schedule.","zh":"這個片語同時描述主題和出版頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the story behind","meaning":"……背後的故事","examples":[{"en":"The story behind the fall of the Berlin Wall had already begun.","zh":"柏林圍牆倒塌背後的故事其實早已開始。"},{"en":"The story behind something is the hidden background or earlier events that explain it.","zh":"The story behind something 指解釋某事的隱藏背景或較早事件。"},{"en":"A student may ask about the story behind a school rule to understand why it was created.","zh":"學生可能詢問校規背後的故事，以理解它為何被制定。"},{"en":"If people know only the final event, they may miss the causes that came before it.","zh":"如果人們只知道最後事件，就可能錯過之前的原因。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain what led to a major outcome.","zh":"這個片語幫助解釋重大結果如何形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the fall of the Berlin Wall","meaning":"柏林圍牆倒塌","examples":[{"en":"The fall of the Berlin Wall transformed European politics.","zh":"柏林圍牆倒塌改變了歐洲政治。"},{"en":"The fall of the Berlin Wall refers to the collapse of a major Cold War symbol dividing East and West Berlin.","zh":"The fall of the Berlin Wall 指分隔東西柏林的冷戰重要象徵倒塌。"},{"en":"In history lessons, students often study the fall of the Berlin Wall as a sign of political change.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生常把柏林圍牆倒塌視為政治變化的象徵來研究。"},{"en":"If a wall dividing people falls, it can become a symbol of freedom and reunification.","zh":"如果分隔人民的牆倒下，它可以成為自由和重新統一的象徵。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific historical event, not any ordinary wall falling down.","zh":"這個片語指特定歷史事件，而不是任何普通牆壁倒下。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"begin to unfold","meaning":"開始展開；逐漸顯現","examples":[{"en":"The political story had started to unfold several years earlier.","zh":"這個政治故事早在幾年前已開始展開。"},{"en":"To begin to unfold means to start becoming clear or visible over time.","zh":"To begin to unfold 指隨時間開始變得清楚或可見。"},{"en":"A school conflict may begin to unfold when students first complain about unfair rules.","zh":"當學生首次投訴規則不公平時，學校衝突可能開始展開。"},{"en":"If a problem unfolds slowly, people may not understand its full importance at first.","zh":"如果問題慢慢展開，人們起初可能不明白其全部重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a story or situation gradually developing.","zh":"這個片語描述故事或情況逐步發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"during his early research","meaning":"在他早期研究期間","examples":[{"en":"During his early research, Vargha visited the River Danube.","zh":"在他早期研究期間，Vargha 到訪了多瑙河。"},{"en":"During his early research means while he was doing the first stage of his study.","zh":"During his early research 指在他進行研究初期階段時。"},{"en":"During her early research, a student may visit libraries, interview people, and collect notes.","zh":"在她早期研究期間，學生可能到圖書館、訪問人士並收集筆記。"},{"en":"If early research reveals a serious problem, the direction of a project may change.","zh":"如果早期研究揭示嚴重問題，項目方向可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the beginning phase of an investigation.","zh":"這個片語指調查的開始階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"beauty spot","meaning":"風景名勝","examples":[{"en":"The Danube Bend was a well-known beauty spot.","zh":"多瑙河灣是一個著名風景名勝。"},{"en":"A beauty spot is a place famous for attractive natural scenery.","zh":"Beauty spot 是以迷人自然景色聞名的地方。"},{"en":"A lake surrounded by mountains may become a beauty spot for weekend visitors.","zh":"被群山環繞的湖泊可能成為週末遊客到訪的風景名勝。"},{"en":"If a beauty spot is damaged by construction, tourism and local pride may suffer.","zh":"如果風景名勝被工程破壞，旅遊業和本地自豪感可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a scenic place, not a mark on the skin in this context.","zh":"在此語境中，這個片語指風景優美的地方，而不是皮膚上的美人痣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the River Danube","meaning":"多瑙河","examples":[{"en":"The River Danube flows through several European countries.","zh":"多瑙河流經幾個歐洲國家。"},{"en":"The River Danube is one of Europe’s major rivers and has long been important for transport and settlement.","zh":"River Danube 是歐洲主要河流之一，長久以來對交通和聚居十分重要。"},{"en":"A geography class may trace the River Danube on a map to see how it connects countries.","zh":"地理課可能在地圖上追蹤多瑙河，看看它如何連接不同國家。"},{"en":"If a river crosses borders, development on it can affect more than one nation.","zh":"如果一條河流跨越國界，其開發可能影響多於一個國家。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific European river.","zh":"這個片語命名一條特定歐洲河流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"outside Budapest","meaning":"布達佩斯市外","examples":[{"en":"The Danube Bend is situated outside Budapest.","zh":"多瑙河灣位於布達佩斯市外。"},{"en":"Outside Budapest means not inside Hungary’s capital city, but near or beyond it.","zh":"Outside Budapest 指不在匈牙利首都布達佩斯之內，而是在附近或外圍。"},{"en":"A family may live outside Budapest and travel into the city for work.","zh":"一個家庭可能住在布達佩斯市外，並到市內工作。"},{"en":"If a tourist area lies outside a capital, it may still depend on visitors from the city.","zh":"如果旅遊區位於首都之外，它仍可能依賴來自城市的遊客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location in relation to Budapest.","zh":"這個片語以布達佩斯為參照描述位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be known as","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"The tree-lined area was known as the Danube Bend.","zh":"這片兩旁種滿樹木的地區被稱為多瑙河灣。"},{"en":"To be known as something means to have that name or reputation.","zh":"To be known as something 指擁有某個名稱或名聲。"},{"en":"A teacher may be known as a patient listener because students often ask for help.","zh":"老師可能因學生常向他求助而被稱為有耐性的聆聽者。"},{"en":"If a place is known as a beauty spot, more tourists may visit it.","zh":"如果某地被稱為風景名勝，更多遊客可能到訪。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what people call something.","zh":"這個片語指出人們如何稱呼某事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the Danube Bend","meaning":"多瑙河灣","examples":[{"en":"The Danube Bend was popular with Hungarian tourists.","zh":"多瑙河灣深受匈牙利遊客歡迎。"},{"en":"The Danube Bend is a scenic curve in the River Danube near Budapest.","zh":"The Danube Bend 是布達佩斯附近多瑙河上一段風景優美的河灣。"},{"en":"Families may visit the Danube Bend for fresh air, river views, and weekend walks.","zh":"家庭可能到多瑙河灣呼吸新鮮空氣、欣賞河景和週末散步。"},{"en":"If a dam floods the Danube Bend, a familiar landscape may disappear.","zh":"如果水壩淹沒多瑙河灣，熟悉的景觀可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase names a particular place along the Danube.","zh":"這個片語命名多瑙河沿岸一個特定地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"interview local officials about","meaning":"就……訪問地方官員","examples":[{"en":"Vargha interviewed local officials about development plans.","zh":"Vargha 就發展計劃訪問地方官員。"},{"en":"To interview local officials about something means to ask government or community representatives questions about it.","zh":"To interview local officials about something 指就某事向政府或社區代表提問。"},{"en":"A journalist may interview local officials about a new bus route.","zh":"記者可能就新巴士路線訪問地方官員。"},{"en":"If officials reveal hidden plans during an interview, the reporter may investigate further.","zh":"如果官員在訪問中透露隱藏計劃，記者可能進一步調查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gathering information directly from authorities.","zh":"這個片語描述直接向當局收集資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"plans to build","meaning":"興建……的計劃","examples":[{"en":"The officials discussed plans to build a small park.","zh":"官員討論興建一個小公園的計劃。"},{"en":"Plans to build something are proposals or intentions to construct it.","zh":"Plans to build something 是建造某物的建議或意圖。"},{"en":"A school may announce plans to build a new library beside the playground.","zh":"學校可能公布在操場旁興建新圖書館的計劃。"},{"en":"If plans to build a project are approved, workers may soon begin construction.","zh":"如果興建項目的計劃獲批准，工人可能很快開始施工。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to intended construction, not a completed building.","zh":"這個片語指計劃中的建造，而不是已完成的建築。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"site of an ancient capital","meaning":"古都遺址","examples":[{"en":"The park was planned for the site of an ancient Hungarian capital.","zh":"該公園計劃建於匈牙利古都遺址。"},{"en":"The site of an ancient capital is the place where an old capital city once stood.","zh":"Site of an ancient capital 是昔日古代首都所在的地方。"},{"en":"A museum may be built near the site of an ancient capital to explain its history.","zh":"博物館可能建於古都遺址附近，以解釋其歷史。"},{"en":"If a historic site is developed carelessly, important remains may be damaged.","zh":"如果歷史遺址被粗心開發，重要遺跡可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a present location with its historical importance.","zh":"這個片語把現時地點與其歷史重要性連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"mention in passing","meaning":"順帶一提","examples":[{"en":"One official mentioned the dam in passing.","zh":"一名官員順帶提到水壩。"},{"en":"To mention something in passing means to refer to it briefly without making it the main topic.","zh":"To mention something in passing 指簡短提及某事，而不把它作為主要話題。"},{"en":"A teacher may mention a test in passing while discussing next week’s schedule.","zh":"老師討論下星期時間表時，可能順帶提到測驗。"},{"en":"If someone mentions a serious plan only in passing, listeners may not notice its importance at first.","zh":"如果某人只順帶提到嚴重計劃，聽者起初可能沒有注意其重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a quick, almost casual reference.","zh":"這個片語描述快速、近乎隨意的提及。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tree-lined curve","meaning":"兩旁種滿樹木的河灣","examples":[{"en":"The dam would affect a tree-lined curve in the river.","zh":"水壩會影響河中一段兩旁種滿樹木的河灣。"},{"en":"A tree-lined curve is a bend in a road or river with trees growing along both sides.","zh":"Tree-lined curve 是道路或河流的彎位，兩旁長有樹木。"},{"en":"A village path may follow a tree-lined curve beside a stream.","zh":"村路可能沿着溪旁一段兩旁種滿樹木的彎位延伸。"},{"en":"If a tree-lined curve is flooded, both scenery and animal habitats may be lost.","zh":"如果兩旁種滿樹木的河灣被淹沒，景色和動物棲息地都可能失去。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear visual image of a natural place.","zh":"這個片語為自然地方提供清晰視覺意象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"popular tourist spot","meaning":"受歡迎的旅遊景點","examples":[{"en":"The Danube Bend was a popular tourist spot for Hungarians.","zh":"多瑙河灣是匈牙利人喜愛的旅遊景點。"},{"en":"A popular tourist spot is a place many visitors like to visit.","zh":"Popular tourist spot 是許多遊客喜歡到訪的地方。"},{"en":"A seaside town may become a popular tourist spot during school holidays.","zh":"海邊小鎮在學校假期期間可能成為受歡迎的旅遊景點。"},{"en":"If a tourist spot is damaged, local shops and guides may lose income.","zh":"如果旅遊景點受損，本地商店和導遊可能失去收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place attractive to visitors.","zh":"這個片語描述對遊客有吸引力的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be submerged by","meaning":"被……淹沒","examples":[{"en":"The tourist area was to be submerged by a giant dam.","zh":"該旅遊區將被巨型水壩淹沒。"},{"en":"To be submerged by water means to be covered or flooded completely.","zh":"To be submerged by water 指被水完全覆蓋或淹沒。"},{"en":"A road may be submerged by rainwater after a severe storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，道路可能被雨水淹沒。"},{"en":"If a valley is submerged by a reservoir, farms and homes may disappear under water.","zh":"如果山谷被水庫淹沒，農田和住宅可能消失在水下。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being covered by water, often permanently.","zh":"這個片語描述被水覆蓋，很多時是永久性的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"giant hydroelectric dam","meaning":"巨型水力發電水壩","examples":[{"en":"A giant hydroelectric dam was being planned for the area.","zh":"該地區正計劃興建一座巨型水力發電水壩。"},{"en":"A giant hydroelectric dam is a very large dam that uses river water to generate electricity.","zh":"Giant hydroelectric dam 是利用河水發電的非常大型水壩。"},{"en":"Engineers may build a hydroelectric dam where a river has enough flow and height difference.","zh":"工程師可能在河流水量和高低差足夠的地方興建水力發電水壩。"},{"en":"If a giant dam is built, it may produce power but also flood land and change ecosystems.","zh":"如果巨型水壩建成，它可能發電，但也可能淹沒土地並改變生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase combines size, water control, and electricity production.","zh":"這個片語結合了規模、水流控制和發電。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be planned in secret","meaning":"被秘密策劃","examples":[{"en":"The hydroelectric project was being planned in secret.","zh":"這項水力發電工程正被秘密策劃。"},{"en":"To be planned in secret means to be prepared without public knowledge or open discussion.","zh":"To be planned in secret 指在公眾不知情或沒有公開討論下被準備。"},{"en":"A company may plan a major closure in secret before telling workers.","zh":"公司可能在告知員工前，秘密策劃重大關閉安排。"},{"en":"If a public project is planned in secret, citizens may feel deceived when they discover it.","zh":"如果公共工程被秘密策劃，市民發現時可能感到被欺騙。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests hidden decision-making.","zh":"這個片語暗示隱蔽決策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"much-feared state agency","meaning":"令人畏懼的國家機構","examples":[{"en":"The project was controlled by a much-feared state agency.","zh":"該項目由一個令人畏懼的國家機構控制。"},{"en":"A much-feared state agency is a government body that people are afraid to challenge.","zh":"Much-feared state agency 是人們害怕挑戰的政府部門。"},{"en":"In an authoritarian system, citizens may avoid criticising a much-feared agency.","zh":"在威權制度中，市民可能避免批評令人畏懼的機構。"},{"en":"If an agency is feared, people may stay silent even when they disagree.","zh":"如果機構令人害怕，人們即使不同意也可能保持沉默。"},{"en":"This phrase shows both official power and public fear.","zh":"這個片語同時顯示官方權力和公眾恐懼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be known simply as","meaning":"簡稱為","examples":[{"en":"The agency was known simply as Water Management.","zh":"該機構簡稱為水利管理局。"},{"en":"To be known simply as something means to be commonly called by a short or plain name.","zh":"To be known simply as something 指通常以簡短或普通名稱被稱呼。"},{"en":"A long school committee may be known simply as the student council.","zh":"一個名稱很長的學校委員會可能簡稱為學生會。"},{"en":"If an organisation has a simple public name, people may use it more easily than its formal title.","zh":"如果組織有簡單公開名稱，人們可能比正式名稱更容易使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a shorter common name.","zh":"這個片語引出較短的常用名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Water Management","meaning":"水利管理局","examples":[{"en":"Water Management was the state agency responsible for the project.","zh":"水利管理局是負責該項目的國家機構。"},{"en":"Water Management was the agency connected with controlling rivers, dams, and water resources.","zh":"Water Management 是與控制河流、水壩和水資源有關的機構。"},{"en":"A water-management office may decide how reservoirs, drainage, and flood defences are run.","zh":"水利管理辦公室可能決定水庫、排水和防洪設施如何運作。"},{"en":"If such an agency controls a dam project, it may focus on engineering more than local concerns.","zh":"如果這類機構控制水壩項目，它可能比本地關注更重視工程。"},{"en":"This phrase names the authority behind the water project.","zh":"這個片語命名水利項目背後的當局。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"investigate and learn that","meaning":"調查後得知","examples":[{"en":"Vargha investigated and learned that the project posed serious risks.","zh":"Vargha 調查後得知該項目帶來嚴重風險。"},{"en":"To investigate and learn that something is true means to examine a matter and discover a fact.","zh":"To investigate and learn that something is true 指檢查某事並發現一項事實。"},{"en":"A journalist may investigate and learn that a school building has safety problems.","zh":"記者可能調查後得知學校建築有安全問題。"},{"en":"If someone investigates carefully, hidden risks may become clear.","zh":"如果某人仔細調查，隱藏風險可能變得清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase links research with discovery.","zh":"這個片語把研究與發現連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cause pollution","meaning":"造成污染","examples":[{"en":"The dam could cause pollution in the river.","zh":"該水壩可能在河中造成污染。"},{"en":"To cause pollution means to make air, water, or land dirty or harmful.","zh":"To cause pollution 指令空氣、水或土地變髒或有害。"},{"en":"A factory can cause pollution if it releases dirty water into a stream.","zh":"如果工廠把污水排入溪流，就可能造成污染。"},{"en":"If pollution enters a river, fish, plants, and drinking water may be affected.","zh":"如果污染進入河流，魚類、植物和食水可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on creating environmental harm.","zh":"這個片語著重造成環境傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"destroy underground water reserves","meaning":"破壞地下水儲備","examples":[{"en":"The project could destroy underground water reserves.","zh":"該項目可能破壞地下水儲備。"},{"en":"To destroy underground water reserves means to damage hidden supplies of water beneath the ground.","zh":"To destroy underground water reserves 指損害地下隱藏的水資源。"},{"en":"Careless drilling may destroy underground water reserves used by nearby farms.","zh":"粗心鑽探可能破壞附近農場使用的地下水儲備。"},{"en":"If underground water is polluted or drained, communities may lose a vital water source.","zh":"如果地下水被污染或抽乾，社區可能失去重要水源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious harm to water stored below the surface.","zh":"這個片語描述對地底儲水的嚴重傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"underground water reserves","meaning":"地下水儲備","examples":[{"en":"The dam threatened important underground water reserves.","zh":"該水壩威脅重要地下水儲備。"},{"en":"Underground water reserves are supplies of water stored naturally beneath the ground.","zh":"Underground water reserves 是自然儲存在地下的水源。"},{"en":"Villages may depend on underground water reserves when rivers dry up in summer.","zh":"當夏天河流乾涸，村莊可能依賴地下水儲備。"},{"en":"If these reserves are damaged, clean water may become harder to find.","zh":"如果這些儲備受損，清潔食水可能更難找到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hidden freshwater resources.","zh":"這個片語描述隱藏的淡水資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"dry out wetlands","meaning":"令濕地乾涸","examples":[{"en":"The development could dry out nearby wetlands.","zh":"該發展可能令附近濕地乾涸。"},{"en":"To dry out wetlands means to remove or reduce the water that keeps wetland areas alive.","zh":"To dry out wetlands 指移走或減少維持濕地生存的水。"},{"en":"A road project may dry out wetlands if it blocks the natural flow of water.","zh":"如果道路工程阻擋自然水流，它可能令濕地乾涸。"},{"en":"If wetlands dry out, birds, fish, and plants may lose their habitat.","zh":"如果濕地乾涸，鳥類、魚類和植物可能失去棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damage caused by taking water away from wet areas.","zh":"這個片語描述因水被帶走而造成的濕地破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"wetlands","meaning":"濕地","examples":[{"en":"The river supported valuable wetlands.","zh":"該河流支撐着寶貴濕地。"},{"en":"Wetlands are areas of land covered or soaked with water, such as marshes and swamps.","zh":"Wetlands 是被水覆蓋或浸濕的土地，例如沼澤和濕原。"},{"en":"Wetlands can filter water, store floodwater, and provide homes for birds and fish.","zh":"濕地可以過濾水、儲存洪水，並為鳥類和魚類提供棲息地。"},{"en":"If wetlands are drained, floods may become worse and wildlife may decline.","zh":"如果濕地被排乾，洪水可能變得更嚴重，野生生物可能減少。"},{"en":"This word refers to watery natural habitats.","zh":"這個詞指多水的自然棲息地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"wreck the ecosystem","meaning":"嚴重破壞生態系統","examples":[{"en":"Vargha believed that the dam would wreck the river’s ecosystem.","zh":"Vargha 相信水壩會嚴重破壞河流生態系統。"},{"en":"To wreck the ecosystem means to badly damage the plants, animals, water, and natural relationships in an area.","zh":"To wreck the ecosystem 指嚴重損害某地的植物、動物、水和自然關係。"},{"en":"Dumping chemicals into a lake can wreck the ecosystem by killing fish and insects.","zh":"把化學品倒入湖泊可能殺死魚和昆蟲，從而嚴重破壞生態系統。"},{"en":"If an ecosystem is wrecked, recovery may take many years.","zh":"如果生態系統被嚴重破壞，復原可能需要多年。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severe environmental destruction.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重環境破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"unique ecosystem","meaning":"獨特的生態系統","examples":[{"en":"The Danube contained a unique ecosystem.","zh":"多瑙河包含一個獨特的生態系統。"},{"en":"A unique ecosystem is a natural system with special plants, animals, and conditions found in few other places.","zh":"Unique ecosystem 是有特殊植物、動物和條件，且很少在其他地方找到的自然系統。"},{"en":"A coral reef can be a unique ecosystem because many species depend on it.","zh":"珊瑚礁可以是獨特的生態系統，因為許多物種依賴它。"},{"en":"If a unique ecosystem is destroyed, rare species and local knowledge may disappear.","zh":"如果獨特的生態系統被摧毀，稀有物種和本地知識可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the natural environment is special and hard to replace.","zh":"這個片語強調自然環境特別且難以取代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"central Europe’s longest river","meaning":"中歐最長的河流","examples":[{"en":"The Danube is central Europe’s longest river.","zh":"多瑙河是中歐最長的河流。"},{"en":"Central Europe’s longest river means the river that stretches farther than any other in that region.","zh":"Central Europe’s longest river 指在該地區延伸距離最長的河流。"},{"en":"Geography students may compare central Europe’s longest river with smaller local rivers.","zh":"地理學生可能把中歐最長的河流與較小的本地河流比較。"},{"en":"If a major river is changed, many towns and ecosystems along it may be affected.","zh":"如果一條主要河流被改變，沿岸許多城鎮和生態系統可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the Danube’s regional importance.","zh":"這個片語突顯多瑙河的地區重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"nobody objected","meaning":"沒有人反對","examples":[{"en":"At first, nobody objected publicly to the project.","zh":"起初，沒有人公開反對該項目。"},{"en":"Nobody objected means no one openly said they disagreed or opposed it.","zh":"Nobody objected 指沒有人公開表示不同意或反對。"},{"en":"In a meeting, nobody objected when the teacher changed the homework deadline.","zh":"在會議上，老師改變功課截止日期時沒有人反對。"},{"en":"If nobody objects, officials may assume the plan has public support.","zh":"如果沒有人反對，官員可能以為計劃得到公眾支持。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest silence, agreement, or fear of speaking out.","zh":"這個片語可以暗示沉默、同意或害怕發聲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"write an article","meaning":"撰寫文章","examples":[{"en":"Vargha wrote an article about the environmental risks.","zh":"Vargha 撰寫了一篇關於環境風險的文章。"},{"en":"To write an article means to prepare a written piece for a magazine, newspaper, website, or report.","zh":"To write an article 指為雜誌、報章、網站或報告準備一篇文字作品。"},{"en":"A student may write an article about plastic waste for the school newsletter.","zh":"學生可能為學校通訊撰寫一篇關於塑膠廢物的文章。"},{"en":"If an article explains a hidden problem clearly, it can inform and persuade readers.","zh":"如果文章清楚解釋隱藏問題，它可以告知並說服讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes producing a public written text.","zh":"這個片語描述製作公開文字內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"editorial board","meaning":"編輯委員會","examples":[{"en":"A director from Water Management sat on the magazine’s editorial board.","zh":"一名水利管理局主管是該雜誌編輯委員會成員。"},{"en":"An editorial board is a group of people who guide what a publication prints or supports.","zh":"Editorial board 是指導出版物刊登或支持甚麼內容的一組人。"},{"en":"A school magazine’s editorial board may choose articles, check facts, and decide headlines.","zh":"學校雜誌的編輯委員會可能選文章、核查事實並決定標題。"},{"en":"If a powerful official sits on an editorial board, sensitive articles may face pressure.","zh":"如果有權勢官員在編輯委員會中，敏感文章可能面對壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people who influence publication decisions.","zh":"這個片語指影響出版決定的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at the last minute","meaning":"在最後一刻","examples":[{"en":"The director stopped the article at the last minute.","zh":"該主管在最後一刻阻止文章刊登。"},{"en":"At the last minute means just before something is about to happen.","zh":"At the last minute 指就在某事即將發生之前。"},{"en":"A student may change an essay title at the last minute before submitting it.","zh":"學生可能在提交作文前最後一刻改題目。"},{"en":"If a decision is made at the last minute, people have little time to respond.","zh":"如果決定在最後一刻作出，人們幾乎沒有時間回應。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that something happens very late.","zh":"這個片語強調某事發生得很晚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"go to the printers","meaning":"前往印刷廠","examples":[{"en":"The official went to the printers to prevent publication.","zh":"該官員前往印刷廠阻止出版。"},{"en":"To go to the printers means to visit the place where a magazine or newspaper is physically printed.","zh":"To go to the printers 指到雜誌或報紙實際印刷的地方。"},{"en":"An editor may go to the printers to check the final version of a magazine.","zh":"編輯可能前往印刷廠檢查雜誌最終版本。"},{"en":"If someone goes to the printers to stop an article, censorship has reached the production stage.","zh":"如果有人前往印刷廠阻止文章，審查已到達製作階段。"},{"en":"This phrase describes action at the point of printing.","zh":"這個片語描述在印刷關口採取行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"stop the presses","meaning":"叫停印刷","examples":[{"en":"The official stopped the presses before the article appeared.","zh":"該官員在文章出現前叫停印刷。"},{"en":"To stop the presses means to halt printing, often because something must be changed or blocked.","zh":"To stop the presses 指停止印刷，通常因為內容必須更改或被阻止。"},{"en":"A newspaper may stop the presses if a major breaking story arrives.","zh":"如果重大突發新聞出現，報社可能叫停印刷。"},{"en":"If officials stop the presses, an article may disappear before readers see it.","zh":"如果官員叫停印刷，文章可能在讀者看到之前消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an urgent interruption of publication.","zh":"這個片語描述出版過程被緊急中斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"never be published","meaning":"從未獲刊登","examples":[{"en":"Vargha’s article was never published.","zh":"Vargha 的文章從未獲刊登。"},{"en":"To never be published means to never appear in print or online for readers to see.","zh":"To never be published 指從未以印刷或網上形式出現供讀者閱讀。"},{"en":"A school report may never be published if the data are incomplete.","zh":"如果數據不完整，學校報告可能從未獲刊登。"},{"en":"If an article is never published because of censorship, the public may lose important information.","zh":"如果文章因審查而從未獲刊登，公眾可能失去重要資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes writing that is blocked or left unseen.","zh":"這個片語描述被阻止或未被看見的文字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"frustrated and angry","meaning":"感到沮喪和憤怒","examples":[{"en":"Vargha felt frustrated and angry about the censorship.","zh":"Vargha 對審查制度感到沮喪和憤怒。"},{"en":"Frustrated and angry means upset because something unfair or difficult blocks what you want to do.","zh":"Frustrated and angry 指因不公平或困難阻礙自己想做的事而感到不快。"},{"en":"A student may feel frustrated and angry if their hard work is ignored.","zh":"如果努力被忽視，學生可能感到沮喪和憤怒。"},{"en":"If people feel silenced, frustration can turn into public protest.","zh":"如果人們感到被噤聲，沮喪可能變成公開抗議。"},{"en":"This phrase combines disappointment with strong irritation.","zh":"這個片語結合失望和強烈不滿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ultimately interested in","meaning":"最終對……產生興趣","examples":[{"en":"He was ultimately interested in why officials had banned the article.","zh":"他最終對官員為何禁止刊登文章產生興趣。"},{"en":"To be ultimately interested in something means to be most concerned with it after thinking more deeply.","zh":"To be ultimately interested in something 指經過深入思考後最關心某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may be ultimately interested in why students keep making the same mistake.","zh":"老師可能最終對學生為何不斷犯同一錯誤產生興趣。"},{"en":"If someone asks deeper questions, they may move from anger to investigation.","zh":"如果某人提出更深層問題，他可能由憤怒轉向調查。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the main concern behind a reaction.","zh":"這個片語指出反應背後的主要關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"care enough to","meaning":"十分在意，以致……","examples":[{"en":"The authorities cared enough to ban his article.","zh":"當局十分在意，以致禁止刊登他的文章。"},{"en":"To care enough to do something means to feel strongly enough about it to take action.","zh":"To care enough to do something 指對某事在意到足以採取行動。"},{"en":"A parent may care enough to speak to the school when a child is bullied.","zh":"當孩子被欺凌，家長可能十分在意，以致向學校反映。"},{"en":"If officials care enough to censor an article, they may fear its effect.","zh":"如果官員在意到審查一篇文章，他們可能害怕其影響。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that concern leads to action.","zh":"這個片語顯示關注導致行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ban an article","meaning":"禁止刊登文章","examples":[{"en":"The state agency banned the article before publication.","zh":"該國家機構在出版前禁止刊登文章。"},{"en":"To ban an article means to officially stop it from being published or read.","zh":"To ban an article 指正式阻止文章出版或被閱讀。"},{"en":"A school may ban an article from a newsletter if it reveals private information unfairly.","zh":"如果文章不公平地透露私人資料，學校可能禁止在通訊中刊登該文章。"},{"en":"If an article is banned for political reasons, readers may suspect censorship.","zh":"如果文章因政治原因被禁止刊登，讀者可能懷疑有審查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official prevention of publication.","zh":"這個片語描述官方阻止出版。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"part of a joint project","meaning":"聯合項目的一部分","examples":[{"en":"The dam was part of a joint project with Czechoslovakia.","zh":"該水壩是與捷克斯洛伐克合作的聯合項目一部分。"},{"en":"Part of a joint project means one element in a project shared by two or more groups or countries.","zh":"Part of a joint project 指由兩個或多個群體或國家共同進行的項目中的一部分。"},{"en":"A school garden may be part of a joint project between teachers, parents, and local volunteers.","zh":"學校花園可能是老師、家長和本地義工聯合項目的一部分。"},{"en":"If a project is joint, decisions may depend on several partners.","zh":"如果項目是聯合進行，決定可能取決於幾個合作方。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses cooperation and shared responsibility.","zh":"這個片語強調合作和共同責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"neighbouring Czechoslovakia","meaning":"鄰國捷克斯洛伐克","examples":[{"en":"Hungary was working with neighbouring Czechoslovakia.","zh":"匈牙利正與鄰國捷克斯洛伐克合作。"},{"en":"Neighbouring Czechoslovakia means the nearby country of Czechoslovakia, which bordered Hungary at the time.","zh":"Neighbouring Czechoslovakia 指當時與匈牙利接壤的鄰近國家捷克斯洛伐克。"},{"en":"A country may cooperate with a neighbouring country on transport, rivers, or trade.","zh":"一個國家可能與鄰國在交通、河流或貿易上合作。"},{"en":"If neighbouring countries share a river, one project can affect both sides of the border.","zh":"如果鄰國共享一條河流，一項工程可以影響邊界兩邊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes geographical closeness between countries.","zh":"這個片語描述國家之間的地理接近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"produce hydroelectricity","meaning":"生產水力電力","examples":[{"en":"The dams were intended to produce hydroelectricity.","zh":"這些水壩旨在生產水力電力。"},{"en":"To produce hydroelectricity means to generate electricity using the movement of water.","zh":"To produce hydroelectricity 指利用水流運動發電。"},{"en":"A mountain river may produce hydroelectricity if water can flow through turbines.","zh":"如果水能流過渦輪機，山區河流可能生產水力電力。"},{"en":"If a dam produces electricity, it may reduce fuel use but also alter the river.","zh":"如果水壩發電，它可能減少燃料使用，但也會改變河流。"},{"en":"This phrase describes power generation from water.","zh":"這個片語描述以水發電。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"irrigate farms","meaning":"灌溉農田","examples":[{"en":"The project was designed to irrigate farms.","zh":"該項目旨在灌溉農田。"},{"en":"To irrigate farms means to supply farmland with water for crops.","zh":"To irrigate farms 指向農田供水以種植農作物。"},{"en":"Farmers may irrigate farms during dry months when rain is not enough.","zh":"當乾旱月份雨水不足時，農民可能灌溉農田。"},{"en":"If irrigation works well, crop yields may increase.","zh":"如果灌溉成效良好，農作物產量可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bringing water to agricultural land.","zh":"這個片語描述把水帶到農業土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"enhance navigation","meaning":"改善航運","examples":[{"en":"The authorities claimed that the project would enhance navigation.","zh":"當局聲稱該項目會改善航運。"},{"en":"To enhance navigation means to improve the movement of boats or ships along a waterway.","zh":"To enhance navigation 指改善船隻沿水道航行的情況。"},{"en":"Deepening a harbour can enhance navigation for larger ships.","zh":"加深港口可以改善大型船隻航運。"},{"en":"If navigation improves, transport by river may become faster and safer.","zh":"如果航運改善，河道運輸可能變得更快和更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making travel on water easier.","zh":"這個片語描述令水上交通更容易。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"re-engineer the river","meaning":"改造河道","examples":[{"en":"The two countries planned to re-engineer the Danube.","zh":"兩國計劃改造多瑙河道。"},{"en":"To re-engineer a river means to redesign or physically alter its flow, banks, or channel.","zh":"To re-engineer a river 指重新設計或實體改變河流的流向、河岸或河道。"},{"en":"Engineers may re-engineer a river to reduce flooding near a town.","zh":"工程師可能改造河道，以減少城鎮附近水浸。"},{"en":"If a river is re-engineered, natural habitats and local communities may be changed.","zh":"如果河道被改造，自然棲息地和本地社區可能被改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes major human alteration of a river system.","zh":"這個片語描述人類對河流系統的重大改造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"form the border between","meaning":"構成……之間的邊界","examples":[{"en":"The river formed the border between the two countries.","zh":"該河流構成兩國之間的邊界。"},{"en":"To form the border between places means to act as the dividing line separating them.","zh":"To form the border between places 指作為分隔地方的界線。"},{"en":"A mountain range may form the border between two regions.","zh":"山脈可能構成兩個地區之間的邊界。"},{"en":"If a river forms a border, both countries may claim an interest in how it is used.","zh":"如果河流構成邊界，兩國都可能對其使用方式有利益。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a natural feature marking a boundary.","zh":"這個片語描述自然地貌標示邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"work together","meaning":"合作","examples":[{"en":"Russian officials were also working together with the project organisers.","zh":"俄羅斯官員也與項目組織者合作。"},{"en":"To work together means to cooperate on a shared task or goal.","zh":"To work together 指為共同任務或目標合作。"},{"en":"Students work together when they divide research, share notes, and prepare one presentation.","zh":"學生分工研究、分享筆記並準備同一份匯報時，就是合作。"},{"en":"If groups work together well, large projects may become easier to complete.","zh":"如果不同群體合作良好，大型項目可能更容易完成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cooperation, not simply being in the same place.","zh":"這個片語描述合作，而不只是身處同一地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take ships from A to B","meaning":"把船隻由A駛往B","examples":[{"en":"The Russians wanted to take large ships from the Black Sea to Austria.","zh":"俄羅斯人想把大型船隻由黑海駛往奧地利。"},{"en":"To take ships from A to B means to move vessels along a route from one place to another.","zh":"To take ships from A to B 指沿路線把船隻從一地移到另一地。"},{"en":"A canal can take ships from an inland city to the sea.","zh":"運河可以把船隻由內陸城市駛往大海。"},{"en":"If a route allows bigger ships to pass, trade may increase along the river.","zh":"如果路線容許更大型船隻通過，河流沿線貿易可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transport by water between two points.","zh":"這個片語描述兩點之間的水上運輸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the Black Sea","meaning":"黑海","examples":[{"en":"Large ships were expected to travel from the Black Sea.","zh":"大型船隻預計會從黑海出發。"},{"en":"The Black Sea is a large inland sea connected to eastern Europe and western Asia.","zh":"The Black Sea 是連接東歐和西亞的大型內海。"},{"en":"A geography lesson may show how the Black Sea links trade routes and river systems.","zh":"地理課可能展示黑海如何連接貿易路線和河流系統。"},{"en":"If ships travel from the Black Sea into rivers, inland transport networks may expand.","zh":"如果船隻從黑海駛入河流，內陸運輸網絡可能擴展。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific body of water.","zh":"這個片語命名一個特定水域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"right up to","meaning":"一直去到","examples":[{"en":"The ships would travel right up to the Austrian border.","zh":"這些船會一直去到奧地利邊界。"},{"en":"Right up to means all the way to a particular point or limit.","zh":"Right up to 指一直到達某個特定點或界限。"},{"en":"A bus may take students right up to the school gate.","zh":"巴士可能把學生一直送到校門口。"},{"en":"If ships can travel right up to a border, goods can move closer to inland markets.","zh":"如果船隻可以一直駛到邊界，貨物就能更接近內陸市場。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses reaching the full distance.","zh":"這個片語強調走完整段距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"border with Austria","meaning":"與奧地利接壤的邊界","examples":[{"en":"The planned route extended to the border with Austria.","zh":"計劃路線延伸至與奧地利接壤的邊界。"},{"en":"The border with Austria is the boundary where another country meets Austria.","zh":"Border with Austria 是另一國與奧地利相接的邊界。"},{"en":"A road near the border with Austria may carry travellers and goods between countries.","zh":"奧地利邊界附近的道路可能承載跨國旅客和貨物。"},{"en":"If a transport route reaches a national border, customs and international rules may matter.","zh":"如果運輸路線到達國界，海關和國際規則可能變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a boundary connected with Austria.","zh":"這個片語指出與奧地利有關的邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be under intense investigation","meaning":"受到嚴密調查","examples":[{"en":"Vargha was soon under intense investigation by the authorities.","zh":"Vargha 很快受到當局嚴密調查。"},{"en":"To be under intense investigation means to be closely examined, watched, or questioned.","zh":"To be under intense investigation 指被仔細審查、監視或盤問。"},{"en":"A company may be under intense investigation after customers report unsafe products.","zh":"顧客舉報產品不安全後，公司可能受到嚴密調查。"},{"en":"If activists are investigated intensely, it may discourage others from joining them.","zh":"如果活動人士受到嚴密調查，其他人可能不敢加入。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests heavy official scrutiny.","zh":"這個片語暗示強烈官方審查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get past the censors","meaning":"通過審查人員的把關","examples":[{"en":"Some of his articles managed to get past the censors.","zh":"他的一些文章成功通過審查人員的把關。"},{"en":"To get past the censors means to pass official checking and be published despite restrictions.","zh":"To get past the censors 指在限制下通過官方檢查並得以出版。"},{"en":"A writer may use indirect language to get past the censors in a strict political system.","zh":"在嚴格政治制度中，作家可能使用間接語言來通過審查人員把關。"},{"en":"If an article gets past the censors, readers may finally see information the state dislikes.","zh":"如果文章通過審查，讀者終於可能看到國家不喜歡的資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes avoiding or surviving censorship.","zh":"這個片語描述避開或通過審查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"censors","meaning":"審查人員","examples":[{"en":"State censors controlled what could be published.","zh":"國家審查人員控制可以出版的內容。"},{"en":"Censors are officials or authorities who examine material and block what they disapprove of.","zh":"Censors 是檢查材料並阻止他們不批准內容的官員或當局。"},{"en":"In some countries, censors may remove political criticism from newspapers.","zh":"在一些國家，審查人員可能從報紙刪除政治批評。"},{"en":"If censors control the media, public debate becomes limited.","zh":"如果審查人員控制傳媒，公共辯論就會受限制。"},{"en":"This word describes people who restrict information.","zh":"這個詞描述限制資訊的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"gather supporters","meaning":"爭取支持者","examples":[{"en":"Vargha gathered supporters over the following years.","zh":"Vargha 在隨後數年爭取支持者。"},{"en":"To gather supporters means to persuade or attract people who agree with a cause.","zh":"To gather supporters 指說服或吸引同意某理念的人。"},{"en":"A student may gather supporters for a recycling campaign by explaining its benefits.","zh":"學生可能透過解釋好處，為回收運動爭取支持者。"},{"en":"If more supporters join, a small complaint can become a movement.","zh":"如果更多支持者加入，小投訴可以變成運動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes building public backing.","zh":"這個片語描述建立公眾支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"over the following years","meaning":"在隨後數年","examples":[{"en":"The anti-dam movement grew over the following years.","zh":"反水壩運動在隨後數年壯大。"},{"en":"Over the following years means during the years after a particular event.","zh":"Over the following years 指在某事件之後的幾年期間。"},{"en":"A new school policy may improve slowly over the following years.","zh":"新校政策可能在隨後數年慢慢改善。"},{"en":"If an idea spreads over the following years, it can become normal in the community.","zh":"如果一個想法在隨後數年傳播，它可以在社區中變得正常。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual change after a starting point.","zh":"這個片語描述起點之後的逐步變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"one of only a few people","meaning":"僅有的少數人之一","examples":[{"en":"Vargha was one of only a few people who initially opposed the dam.","zh":"Vargha 是最初反對水壩的僅有少數人之一。"},{"en":"One of only a few people means one member of a very small group.","zh":"One of only a few people 指非常小群體中的其中一員。"},{"en":"A student may be one of only a few people willing to ask a difficult question.","zh":"學生可能是僅有少數願意提出困難問題的人之一。"},{"en":"If only a few people object at first, they may face pressure or isolation.","zh":"如果起初只有少數人反對，他們可能面對壓力或孤立。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses how rare someone’s action or opinion is.","zh":"這個片語強調某人的行動或意見十分罕見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hardly surprised","meaning":"一點也不感到意外","examples":[{"en":"He was hardly surprised when officials refused to debate.","zh":"當官員拒絕辯論時，他一點也不感到意外。"},{"en":"Hardly surprised means not surprised at all, because the result was expected.","zh":"Hardly surprised 指一點也不驚訝，因為結果早已預料到。"},{"en":"A teacher was hardly surprised when an unprepared student failed the quiz.","zh":"沒有準備的學生小測不合格，老師一點也不感到意外。"},{"en":"If officials often avoid criticism, campaigners may be hardly surprised when they refuse debate.","zh":"如果官員常避開批評，當他們拒絕辯論時，運動人士可能一點也不意外。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something disappointing was predictable.","zh":"這個片語顯示令人失望的事情本來可預料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"refuse to debate","meaning":"拒絕辯論","examples":[{"en":"Water Management refused to debate the project in public.","zh":"水利管理局拒絕公開辯論該項目。"},{"en":"To refuse to debate means to reject discussion or argument about an issue.","zh":"To refuse to debate 指拒絕就某議題進行討論或爭辯。"},{"en":"A school leader may refuse to debate a rule if the decision has already been made.","zh":"如果決定已經作出，學校領導可能拒絕辯論一條規則。"},{"en":"If authorities refuse debate, opponents may feel ignored and become more determined.","zh":"如果當局拒絕辯論，反對者可能感到被忽視並變得更堅定。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests avoiding open discussion.","zh":"這個片語暗示避開公開討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in public","meaning":"公開地","examples":[{"en":"The authorities would not discuss the dam in public.","zh":"當局不願公開討論水壩。"},{"en":"In public means openly, where ordinary people can hear, see, or take part.","zh":"In public 指公開地，讓普通人能聽到、看到或參與。"},{"en":"A principal may answer parents’ questions in public at a school meeting.","zh":"校長可能在學校會議上公開回答家長問題。"},{"en":"If decisions are not discussed in public, people may suspect secrecy.","zh":"如果決定沒有公開討論，人們可能懷疑有秘密安排。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts open discussion with private or hidden action.","zh":"這個片語把公開討論與私人或隱蔽行動作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"bureaucrats","meaning":"官僚","examples":[{"en":"The bureaucrats withdrew from the public meeting.","zh":"官僚退出了公開會議。"},{"en":"Bureaucrats are officials who work in government departments or large administrative systems.","zh":"Bureaucrats 是在政府部門或大型行政系統中工作的官員。"},{"en":"Citizens may need to speak with bureaucrats when applying for permits or benefits.","zh":"市民申請許可或福利時，可能需要與官僚打交道。"},{"en":"If bureaucrats avoid public questions, trust in the system may decline.","zh":"如果官僚避開公眾問題，人們對制度的信任可能下降。"},{"en":"This word often suggests officials focused on rules and procedure.","zh":"這個詞常暗示重視規則和程序的官員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pull out of","meaning":"退出","examples":[{"en":"The officials pulled out of the public meeting at the last minute.","zh":"官員在最後一刻退出公開會議。"},{"en":"To pull out of an event means to withdraw and decide not to take part.","zh":"To pull out of an event 指退出並決定不參加。"},{"en":"A speaker may pull out of a school talk because of illness.","zh":"講者可能因病退出學校講座。"},{"en":"If officials pull out of a meeting, the public may feel they are avoiding questions.","zh":"如果官員退出會議，公眾可能覺得他們在逃避問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes backing away from a planned commitment.","zh":"這個片語描述放棄原本承諾參與的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"public meeting","meaning":"公開會議","examples":[{"en":"A public meeting had been arranged to discuss the dam.","zh":"一場公開會議已安排來討論水壩。"},{"en":"A public meeting is a meeting open to ordinary citizens, often about a community issue.","zh":"Public meeting 是向普通市民開放、通常關於社區議題的會議。"},{"en":"Residents may attend a public meeting about traffic, housing, or school plans.","zh":"居民可能參加關於交通、住屋或學校計劃的公開會議。"},{"en":"If a public meeting is cancelled, people may lose a chance to ask questions.","zh":"如果公開會議取消，人們可能失去提問機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes open civic discussion.","zh":"這個片語描述公開的公民討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take the next step","meaning":"採取下一步行動","examples":[{"en":"Vargha knew that he had to take the next step.","zh":"Vargha 知道他必須採取下一步行動。"},{"en":"To take the next step means to move from one stage of action to a more serious or advanced one.","zh":"To take the next step 指從一個行動階段推進到更認真或更進一步的階段。"},{"en":"After collecting complaints, students may take the next step and ask for a meeting with teachers.","zh":"收集投訴後，學生可能採取下一步行動，要求與老師會面。"},{"en":"If writing articles is not enough, campaigners may organise a group.","zh":"如果撰寫文章不足夠，運動人士可能成立組織。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving forward in a plan.","zh":"這個片語描述計劃向前推進。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"it wasn’t enough to","meaning":"單是……並不足夠","examples":[{"en":"The campaigners decided that it wasn’t enough to talk and write.","zh":"運動人士認為單是談論和寫作並不足夠。"},{"en":"It wasn’t enough to do something means that action alone could not solve the problem.","zh":"It wasn’t enough to do something 指單靠某行動不能解決問題。"},{"en":"It wasn’t enough to complain about dirty classrooms; students also had to organise cleaning duties.","zh":"單是投訴課室骯髒並不足夠；學生還要組織清潔工作。"},{"en":"If words bring no change, people may decide stronger action is needed.","zh":"如果言語不能帶來改變，人們可能認為需要更強行動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a previous effort was insufficient.","zh":"這個片語顯示之前的努力不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"set up an organisation","meaning":"成立組織","examples":[{"en":"They set up an organisation called the Danube Circle.","zh":"他們成立了一個名為多瑙河圈的組織。"},{"en":"To set up an organisation means to create a group with a shared purpose.","zh":"To set up an organisation 指創立一個有共同目的的團體。"},{"en":"Students may set up an organisation to promote mental health at school.","zh":"學生可能成立組織，在學校推廣精神健康。"},{"en":"If people work through an organisation, they can coordinate meetings, petitions, and publicity.","zh":"如果人們透過組織工作，就能協調會議、請願和宣傳。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formally starting a group.","zh":"這個片語描述正式創立團體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the Danube Circle","meaning":"多瑙河圈","examples":[{"en":"The Danube Circle campaigned against the construction of the dam.","zh":"多瑙河圈反對水壩興建。"},{"en":"The Danube Circle was an environmental campaign group opposing the Danube dam project.","zh":"Danube Circle 是反對多瑙河水壩項目的環保運動組織。"},{"en":"A history class may study the Danube Circle as an example of civic resistance.","zh":"歷史課可能研究多瑙河圈，作為公民反抗的例子。"},{"en":"If a group challenges both pollution and censorship, it can become politically important.","zh":"如果一個團體同時挑戰污染和審查，它可以變得具有政治重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific activist organisation.","zh":"這個片語命名一個特定行動組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"disagree with censorship","meaning":"反對審查制度","examples":[{"en":"The organisation announced that it disagreed with censorship.","zh":"該組織宣布反對審查制度。"},{"en":"To disagree with censorship means to oppose the control or banning of information.","zh":"To disagree with censorship 指反對控制或禁止資訊。"},{"en":"A student newspaper may disagree with censorship if articles are blocked unfairly.","zh":"如果文章被不公平阻止刊登，學生報可能反對審查制度。"},{"en":"If people oppose censorship, they may demand open debate and free publication.","zh":"如果人們反對審查，他們可能要求公開辯論和自由出版。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rejection of information control.","zh":"這個片語描述拒絕資訊控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"act as if","meaning":"表現得彷彿","examples":[{"en":"The campaigners acted as if they were living in a democracy.","zh":"運動人士表現得彷彿他們生活在民主制度中。"},{"en":"To act as if something is true means to behave according to that idea, even if reality is different.","zh":"To act as if something is true 指按某想法行事，即使現實不同。"},{"en":"A nervous student may act as if they are confident until they feel calmer.","zh":"緊張的學生可能表現得彷彿自己很有信心，直到心情較平靜。"},{"en":"If citizens act as if they have rights, they may challenge limits placed on them.","zh":"如果市民表現得彷彿自己有權利，他們可能挑戰施加在身上的限制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes behaviour based on an assumed situation.","zh":"這個片語描述基於假定情況的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"live in a democracy","meaning":"生活在民主制度中","examples":[{"en":"They wanted to behave like citizens living in a democracy.","zh":"他們想像生活在民主制度中的市民一樣行事。"},{"en":"To live in a democracy means to live in a political system where citizens have rights and can take part in public decisions.","zh":"To live in a democracy 指生活在市民有權利並能參與公共決策的政治制度中。"},{"en":"People living in a democracy may expect open debate and fair elections.","zh":"生活在民主制度中的人可能期望公開辯論和公平選舉。"},{"en":"If citizens cannot speak freely, they may feel that democracy exists only in name.","zh":"如果市民不能自由發聲，他們可能覺得民主只是名義上存在。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a society with public participation and political rights.","zh":"這個片語描述有公共參與和政治權利的社會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"illegal organisation","meaning":"非法組織","examples":[{"en":"The Danube Circle was considered an illegal organisation.","zh":"多瑙河圈被視為非法組織。"},{"en":"An illegal organisation is a group that the authorities say is not allowed by law.","zh":"Illegal organisation 是當局指稱不被法律容許的團體。"},{"en":"In a strict regime, even a peaceful club may be labelled an illegal organisation.","zh":"在嚴格政權中，即使和平社團也可能被標籤為非法組織。"},{"en":"If a group is illegal, members may face arrest, dismissal, or surveillance.","zh":"如果團體是非法的，成員可能面臨拘捕、解僱或監視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes legal status imposed by the state.","zh":"這個片語描述由國家施加的法律地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"secret publications","meaning":"地下刊物","examples":[{"en":"The group produced secret publications opposing the dam.","zh":"該組織製作反對水壩的地下刊物。"},{"en":"Secret publications are written materials printed or shared without official approval or public visibility.","zh":"Secret publications 是未經官方批准或不公開地印刷和分享的文字材料。"},{"en":"Students in a repressive school story might pass secret publications under classroom desks.","zh":"在壓抑校園故事中，學生可能在課桌下傳遞地下刊物。"},{"en":"If normal newspapers are censored, activists may turn to secret publications.","zh":"如果正常報紙受審查，活動人士可能轉向地下刊物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hidden printed or copied materials.","zh":"這個片語描述隱蔽印刷或複製材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"samizdat leaflets","meaning":"地下出版傳單","examples":[{"en":"The Danube Circle distributed samizdat leaflets.","zh":"多瑙河圈派發地下出版傳單。"},{"en":"Samizdat leaflets are unofficial underground pamphlets copied and shared to avoid censorship.","zh":"Samizdat leaflets 是為避開審查而複製和分享的非官方地下小冊子。"},{"en":"Activists may use samizdat leaflets when newspapers refuse to print their views.","zh":"當報紙拒絕刊登觀點時，活動人士可能使用地下出版傳單。"},{"en":"If leaflets spread secretly, ideas can reach people despite state control.","zh":"如果傳單秘密傳播，思想仍可以在國家控制下到達人們手中。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to underground political or social writing.","zh":"這個片語指地下政治或社會文字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"extraordinary act of defiance","meaning":"非同尋常的反抗行動","examples":[{"en":"The petition was an extraordinary act of defiance.","zh":"這份請願書是一項非同尋常的反抗行動。"},{"en":"An extraordinary act of defiance is a very bold action that openly challenges authority.","zh":"Extraordinary act of defiance 是公開挑戰權威的非常大膽行動。"},{"en":"In a strict school, students signing a public complaint may be an act of defiance.","zh":"在嚴格學校中，學生簽署公開投訴可能是一種反抗行動。"},{"en":"If people risk punishment to speak out, their action shows unusual courage.","zh":"如果人們冒着受罰風險發聲，他們的行動顯示非凡勇氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes brave resistance, not ordinary disagreement.","zh":"這個片語描述勇敢反抗，而不是普通不同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"gather signatures for","meaning":"為……收集簽名","examples":[{"en":"The group gathered 10,000 signatures for a petition.","zh":"該組織為一份請願書收集了一萬個簽名。"},{"en":"To gather signatures for something means to collect people’s names to show support.","zh":"To gather signatures for something 指收集人們姓名以顯示支持。"},{"en":"Students may gather signatures for a request to keep the library open longer.","zh":"學生可能為要求圖書館延長開放時間收集簽名。"},{"en":"If many people sign, officials can see that support is not just individual.","zh":"如果許多人簽名，官員就能看見支持並非只有個別人士。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collecting public backing in written form.","zh":"這個片語描述以書面形式收集公眾支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"petition objecting to","meaning":"反對……的請願書","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of people signed a petition objecting to the dam.","zh":"數千人簽署了一份反對水壩的請願書。"},{"en":"A petition objecting to something is a written request signed by people who oppose it.","zh":"Petition objecting to something 是由反對某事的人簽署的書面請求。"},{"en":"Residents may sign a petition objecting to a noisy road project near their homes.","zh":"居民可能簽署反對住宅附近嘈雜道路工程的請願書。"},{"en":"If a petition attracts many names, authorities may face pressure to respond.","zh":"如果請願書吸引許多簽名，當局可能面對回應壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised written opposition.","zh":"這個片語描述有組織的書面反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make links with","meaning":"與……建立聯繫","examples":[{"en":"The group made links with environmentalists in the West.","zh":"該組織與西方環保人士建立聯繫。"},{"en":"To make links with people means to build connections or relationships with them.","zh":"To make links with people 指與他們建立連繫或關係。"},{"en":"A school club may make links with a local charity to organise volunteer work.","zh":"學校社團可能與本地慈善機構建立聯繫，以組織義工工作。"},{"en":"If campaigners make international links, their issue may receive more attention.","zh":"如果運動人士建立國際聯繫，他們的議題可能獲得更多關注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes building useful connections.","zh":"這個片語描述建立有用連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"environmentalists in the West","meaning":"西方環保人士","examples":[{"en":"Western environmentalists supported the Hungarian campaigners.","zh":"西方環保人士支持匈牙利運動人士。"},{"en":"Environmentalists in the West are people in Western countries who work to protect nature and the environment.","zh":"Environmentalists in the West 是西方國家中致力保護自然和環境的人。"},{"en":"Environmentalists in the West may support campaigns about rivers, forests, climate, or wildlife.","zh":"西方環保人士可能支持關於河流、森林、氣候或野生生物的運動。"},{"en":"If Western groups publicise a local issue, international pressure may increase.","zh":"如果西方團體宣傳本地議題，國際壓力可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies foreign supporters of an environmental cause.","zh":"這個片語指出環保理念的外國支持者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"press conference","meaning":"記者會","examples":[{"en":"Foreign environmentalists were invited to Budapest for a press conference.","zh":"外國環保人士被邀請到布達佩斯出席記者會。"},{"en":"A press conference is a meeting where people speak to journalists and answer questions.","zh":"Press conference 是人們向記者發言並回答問題的會議。"},{"en":"A hospital may hold a press conference to explain a public health emergency.","zh":"醫院可能舉行記者會，解釋公共衞生緊急情況。"},{"en":"If activists hold a press conference, their message may reach newspapers and television.","zh":"如果活動人士舉行記者會，他們的訊息可能到達報紙和電視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a public media event.","zh":"這個片語描述公開傳媒活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"enforce a news blackout","meaning":"實施新聞封鎖","examples":[{"en":"The Hungarian government enforced a news blackout on the dam.","zh":"匈牙利政府對水壩實施新聞封鎖。"},{"en":"To enforce a news blackout means to stop media from reporting information about an issue.","zh":"To enforce a news blackout 指阻止傳媒報道某議題的資訊。"},{"en":"A government may enforce a news blackout during a crisis to control public reaction.","zh":"政府可能在危機期間實施新聞封鎖，以控制公眾反應。"},{"en":"If news is blocked, rumours may spread because people lack reliable information.","zh":"如果新聞被封鎖，謠言可能傳播，因為人們缺乏可靠資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong control over reporting.","zh":"這個片語描述對報道的強力控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"news blackout","meaning":"新聞封鎖","examples":[{"en":"The news blackout prevented local reporting about the project.","zh":"新聞封鎖阻止本地報道該項目。"},{"en":"A news blackout is a ban or restriction on reporting information to the public.","zh":"News blackout 是禁止或限制向公眾報道資訊。"},{"en":"During a news blackout, citizens may not know what officials are planning.","zh":"在新聞封鎖期間，市民可能不知道官員正在計劃甚麼。"},{"en":"If a news blackout covers an environmental issue, public debate becomes difficult.","zh":"如果新聞封鎖覆蓋環境議題，公共辯論會變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the absence of news caused by control, not by lack of interest.","zh":"這個片語描述因控制而沒有新聞，而不是因缺乏興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"begin to appear in","meaning":"開始出現在……","examples":[{"en":"Articles about the Danube Circle began to appear in Western media.","zh":"關於多瑙河圈的文章開始出現在西方傳媒。"},{"en":"To begin to appear in a place means to start being seen or published there.","zh":"To begin to appear in a place 指開始在某處被看見或刊登。"},{"en":"A student’s artwork may begin to appear in school displays after winning a prize.","zh":"學生作品得獎後，可能開始出現在學校展示板上。"},{"en":"If a story appears in foreign media, it may become harder for local authorities to hide it.","zh":"如果故事出現在外國傳媒，本地當局可能更難隱藏它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first signs of public visibility.","zh":"這個片語描述公眾可見性的初步出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Western media","meaning":"西方傳媒","examples":[{"en":"The campaign received coverage in the Western media.","zh":"該運動獲得西方傳媒報道。"},{"en":"Western media refers to newspapers, magazines, radio, and television in Western countries.","zh":"Western media 指西方國家的報紙、雜誌、電台和電視。"},{"en":"A local protest may reach Western media if it connects with wider human-rights concerns.","zh":"如果本地抗議與更廣泛人權關注有關，它可能進入西方傳媒。"},{"en":"If Western media report an issue, international audiences may become aware of it.","zh":"如果西方傳媒報道某議題，國際觀眾可能開始知道它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes foreign news outlets from the West.","zh":"這個片語描述來自西方的外國新聞媒體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"public spokesman","meaning":"公開發言人","examples":[{"en":"Vargha became a public spokesman for the Danube Circle.","zh":"Vargha 成為多瑙河圈的公開發言人。"},{"en":"A public spokesman is a person who speaks openly on behalf of a group.","zh":"Public spokesman 是代表某團體公開發言的人。"},{"en":"A school club may choose a public spokesman to explain its campaign to teachers.","zh":"學校社團可能選出公開發言人，向老師解釋其運動。"},{"en":"If a group has a clear spokesman, its message may become easier to understand.","zh":"如果團體有清晰發言人，其訊息可能更容易被理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone who represents a cause in public.","zh":"這個片語描述在公開場合代表某理念的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"win an award","meaning":"獲得獎項","examples":[{"en":"The Circle and Vargha won an international award.","zh":"多瑙河圈和 Vargha 獲得一項國際獎項。"},{"en":"To win an award means to receive a prize or honour for achievement.","zh":"To win an award 指因成就而獲得獎項或榮譽。"},{"en":"A student may win an award for a science project that solves a community problem.","zh":"學生可能因解決社區問題的科學項目而獲獎。"},{"en":"If activists win an award, their cause may gain public respect.","zh":"如果活動人士獲得獎項，他們的理念可能獲得公眾尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal recognition of effort or success.","zh":"這個片語描述對努力或成功的正式認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Right Livelihood Award","meaning":"正確生活方式獎","examples":[{"en":"The campaigners received the Right Livelihood Award in 1985.","zh":"運動人士在1985年獲得正確生活方式獎。"},{"en":"The Right Livelihood Award is an international prize recognising practical work for social and environmental good.","zh":"Right Livelihood Award 是表揚社會和環境公益實踐工作的國際獎項。"},{"en":"A teacher may mention the Right Livelihood Award when discussing activists who challenge injustice.","zh":"老師討論挑戰不公義的活動人士時，可能提到正確生活方式獎。"},{"en":"If a small campaign wins such an award, its international profile may rise.","zh":"如果小型運動獲得這類獎項，它的國際知名度可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific global award.","zh":"這個片語命名一個特定全球獎項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"alternative Nobel Prize","meaning":"另類諾貝爾獎","examples":[{"en":"The Right Livelihood Award is known as the alternative Nobel Prize.","zh":"正確生活方式獎被稱為另類諾貝爾獎。"},{"en":"The alternative Nobel Prize is an informal name for an award seen as similar in prestige but focused on different kinds of work.","zh":"Alternative Nobel Prize 是某獎項的非正式名稱，表示它聲望相近但重點不同。"},{"en":"Journalists may call an award an alternative Nobel Prize to show that it is highly respected.","zh":"記者可能稱某獎項為另類諾貝爾獎，以顯示它備受尊重。"},{"en":"If an award has this nickname, winners may gain international attention.","zh":"如果獎項有這個稱號，得獎者可能獲得國際關注。"},{"en":"This phrase compares an award with the Nobel Prize without saying it is the same award.","zh":"這個片語把某獎項與諾貝爾獎比較，但不是說它就是同一個獎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be told not to","meaning":"被告知不要……","examples":[{"en":"Officials told Vargha not to accept the prize.","zh":"官員告訴 Vargha 不要接受獎項。"},{"en":"To be told not to do something means to be ordered or advised against doing it.","zh":"To be told not to do something 指被命令或勸告不要做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be told not to use a phone during an exam.","zh":"學生可能被告知不要在考試期間使用手機。"},{"en":"If someone is told not to accept an award, the authorities may want to control their public image.","zh":"如果某人被告知不要接受獎項，當局可能想控制其公眾形象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a direct instruction to avoid an action.","zh":"這個片語描述避免某行動的直接指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ignore the authorities","meaning":"無視當局","examples":[{"en":"Vargha ignored the authorities and accepted the award.","zh":"Vargha 無視當局並接受了獎項。"},{"en":"To ignore the authorities means to refuse to follow what officials say or demand.","zh":"To ignore the authorities 指拒絕遵從官員所說或要求。"},{"en":"A shop may ignore the authorities if it keeps opening after being ordered to close.","zh":"如果商店在被勒令關門後仍繼續營業，就是無視當局。"},{"en":"If activists ignore official warnings, they may face punishment but gain moral support.","zh":"如果活動人士無視官方警告，他們可能受罰，但也可能得到道義支持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes open refusal to obey authority.","zh":"這個片語描述公開拒絕服從權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"join a protest","meaning":"參加示威","examples":[{"en":"Austrian environmentalists joined a protest in Budapest.","zh":"奧地利環保人士參加了布達佩斯的一場示威。"},{"en":"To join a protest means to take part in a public action showing disagreement.","zh":"To join a protest 指參與表達不同意的公開行動。"},{"en":"Residents may join a protest if a park is going to be replaced by a car park.","zh":"如果公園將被停車場取代，居民可能參加示威。"},{"en":"If many people join a protest, authorities may feel stronger public pressure.","zh":"如果許多人參加示威，當局可能感受到更強公眾壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes participating in collective opposition.","zh":"這個片語描述參與集體反對行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be met with","meaning":"遭到……對付","examples":[{"en":"The protesters were met with tear gas and batons.","zh":"示威者遭到催淚氣體和警棍對付。"},{"en":"To be met with something means to receive a particular response when you act or arrive.","zh":"To be met with something 指在行動或到達時受到某種反應。"},{"en":"A student’s suggestion may be met with silence if classmates are unsure.","zh":"如果同學不確定，學生的建議可能遭到沉默回應。"},{"en":"If peaceful protesters are met with force, public anger may increase.","zh":"如果和平示威者遭到武力對付，公眾憤怒可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the reaction someone receives.","zh":"這個片語描述某人收到的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tear gas and batons","meaning":"催淚氣體和警棍","examples":[{"en":"The police used tear gas and batons against protesters.","zh":"警方對示威者使用催淚氣體和警棍。"},{"en":"Tear gas and batons are tools used by police to disperse or control crowds.","zh":"Tear gas and batons 是警方用來驅散或控制人群的工具。"},{"en":"News reports may mention tear gas and batons when a demonstration turns violent.","zh":"當示威變得暴力，新聞報道可能提到催淚氣體和警棍。"},{"en":"If police use such force, injuries and public criticism may follow.","zh":"如果警方使用這種武力，之後可能有傷者和公眾批評。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a harsh physical response to protest.","zh":"這個片語表示對示威的嚴厲身體回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the Politburo","meaning":"政治局","examples":[{"en":"The Politburo removed Vargha from his editorial position.","zh":"政治局解除了 Vargha 的編輯職務。"},{"en":"The Politburo was a powerful decision-making body in a Communist political system.","zh":"Politburo 是共產政治制度中有權力的決策機構。"},{"en":"In a one-party state, the Politburo may influence jobs, policies, and public organisations.","zh":"在一黨制國家中，政治局可能影響職位、政策和公共組織。"},{"en":"If the Politburo punishes a critic, political pressure becomes very clear.","zh":"如果政治局懲罰批評者，政治壓力就變得非常明顯。"},{"en":"This phrase names a high-level political authority.","zh":"這個片語命名高層政治權力機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"remove someone from a job","meaning":"解除某人的職務","examples":[{"en":"The Politburo removed Vargha from his new job.","zh":"政治局解除了 Vargha 的新職務。"},{"en":"To remove someone from a job means to take away their position or dismiss them from it.","zh":"To remove someone from a job 指奪去某人的職位或把他解僱。"},{"en":"A manager may remove an employee from a safety role after repeated mistakes.","zh":"員工多次犯錯後，經理可能解除他在安全崗位的職務。"},{"en":"If someone is removed for political reasons, the dismissal may be seen as punishment.","zh":"如果某人因政治原因被解除職務，該解僱可能被視為懲罰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes losing a position because others decide it.","zh":"這個片語描述因他人決定而失去職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"editor of","meaning":"……的編輯","examples":[{"en":"Vargha had become editor of the Hungarian version of Scientific American.","zh":"Vargha 曾成為《科學美國人》匈牙利版本的編輯。"},{"en":"The editor of a publication is the person responsible for choosing, preparing, and checking its content.","zh":"Editor of a publication 是負責選擇、準備和檢查其內容的人。"},{"en":"A school may appoint a student as editor of the annual magazine.","zh":"學校可能任命一名學生為年度雜誌的編輯。"},{"en":"If an editor supports controversial articles, they may face pressure from powerful people.","zh":"如果編輯支持具爭議文章，他可能面對有權勢人士的壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies someone’s publishing role.","zh":"這個片語指出某人的出版職責。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Hungarian version of","meaning":"……的匈牙利版本","examples":[{"en":"He edited the Hungarian version of Scientific American.","zh":"他編輯《科學美國人》的匈牙利版本。"},{"en":"The Hungarian version of something is the edition translated or adapted for Hungarian readers.","zh":"The Hungarian version of something 是為匈牙利讀者翻譯或改編的版本。"},{"en":"A textbook may have a local version with examples familiar to students.","zh":"教科書可能有本地版本，加入學生熟悉的例子。"},{"en":"If a magazine has a Hungarian version, readers can access global ideas in their own language.","zh":"如果雜誌有匈牙利版本，讀者就能用自己的語言接觸全球思想。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a language or regional edition.","zh":"這個片語描述語言或地區版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"become a focus for","meaning":"成為……的焦點","examples":[{"en":"The dam became a focus for opposition to the regime.","zh":"水壩成為反對該政權的焦點。"},{"en":"To become a focus for something means to become the main point around which attention or action gathers.","zh":"To become a focus for something 指成為注意力或行動聚集的主要點。"},{"en":"A closed playground may become a focus for community anger.","zh":"一個被關閉的遊樂場可能成為社區憤怒的焦點。"},{"en":"If many complaints gather around one project, that project can symbolise wider problems.","zh":"如果許多投訴集中在同一項目上，該項目可以象徵更廣泛問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how one issue attracts broader attention.","zh":"這個片語顯示單一議題如何吸引更廣泛關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"opposition to","meaning":"對……的反對","examples":[{"en":"The project attracted growing opposition to the government.","zh":"該項目引起對政府日益增加的反對。"},{"en":"Opposition to something means disagreement with it and resistance against it.","zh":"Opposition to something 指不同意某事並抵抗它。"},{"en":"Parents may express opposition to a school fee increase.","zh":"家長可能表達對學費上升的反對。"},{"en":"If opposition grows, leaders may need to explain, change, or cancel a plan.","zh":"如果反對增加，領導者可能需要解釋、修改或取消計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active disagreement.","zh":"這個片語描述積極不同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hated regime","meaning":"受人憎恨的政權","examples":[{"en":"The dam became associated with the hated Communist regime.","zh":"該水壩與受人憎恨的共產政權聯繫起來。"},{"en":"A hated regime is a government widely disliked or resented by the people.","zh":"Hated regime 是被人民廣泛厭惡或怨恨的政府。"},{"en":"People may fear a hated regime but still privately criticise it.","zh":"人們可能害怕受人憎恨的政權，但仍私下批評它。"},{"en":"If a project represents a hated regime, opposition to the project may become political.","zh":"如果某項目代表受人憎恨的政權，對項目的反對可能變成政治反對。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep public hostility toward a ruling system.","zh":"這個片語描述公眾對統治制度的深層敵意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hold back the waters","meaning":"阻擋河水","examples":[{"en":"The Communist authorities tried to hold back the waters of the Danube.","zh":"共產當局試圖阻擋多瑙河河水。"},{"en":"To hold back the waters means to stop or control the movement of water.","zh":"To hold back the waters 指阻止或控制水的流動。"},{"en":"A seawall can hold back the waters during a storm surge.","zh":"海堤可以在風暴潮期間阻擋海水。"},{"en":"If a dam holds back river water, it creates a reservoir and changes the natural flow.","zh":"如果水壩阻擋河水，它會形成水庫並改變自然水流。"},{"en":"This phrase can also suggest trying to resist a powerful force.","zh":"這個片語也可以暗示試圖抵抗強大力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"resist the will of the people","meaning":"抗拒民意","examples":[{"en":"The regime attempted to resist the will of the people.","zh":"該政權試圖抗拒民意。"},{"en":"To resist the will of the people means to oppose what most citizens want.","zh":"To resist the will of the people 指反對大多數市民想要的事情。"},{"en":"A council may resist the will of the people if it ignores a large public petition.","zh":"如果議會無視大型公眾請願，它可能是在抗拒民意。"},{"en":"If leaders resist public opinion for too long, anger may grow.","zh":"如果領導者長期抗拒民意，憤怒可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes political refusal to follow popular demand.","zh":"這個片語描述政治上拒絕順應公眾要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"oppose the state directly","meaning":"直接反對國家政權","examples":[{"en":"Opposing the state directly remained extremely difficult.","zh":"直接反對國家政權仍然極其困難。"},{"en":"To oppose the state directly means to challenge the government openly and politically.","zh":"To oppose the state directly 指公開並政治性地挑戰政府。"},{"en":"In an authoritarian country, citizens may avoid opposing the state directly because of punishment.","zh":"在威權國家，市民可能因害怕受罰而避免直接反對國家政權。"},{"en":"If direct opposition is dangerous, people may protest through environmental or social issues instead.","zh":"如果直接反對很危險，人們可能改用環境或社會議題抗議。"},{"en":"This phrase describes open resistance to government power.","zh":"這個片語描述對政府權力的公開反抗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"less of a hazard","meaning":"危險性較低","examples":[{"en":"Objecting to the dam was less of a hazard than direct political opposition.","zh":"反對水壩比直接政治反對危險性較低。"},{"en":"Less of a hazard means less dangerous or risky than another action.","zh":"Less of a hazard 指比另一行動較不危險或風險較低。"},{"en":"Asking a teacher for help is less of a hazard than pretending to understand before an exam.","zh":"向老師求助比考試前假裝明白危險性較低。"},{"en":"If environmental protest is safer than political protest, people may use it as an indirect channel.","zh":"如果環保抗議比政治抗議安全，人們可能把它用作間接渠道。"},{"en":"This phrase compares levels of risk.","zh":"這個片語比較風險程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"resistance to the state","meaning":"對國家政權的反抗","examples":[{"en":"Opposition to the dam was still considered resistance to the state.","zh":"反對水壩仍被視為對國家政權的反抗。"},{"en":"Resistance to the state means action against government authority or control.","zh":"Resistance to the state 指反對政府權威或控制的行動。"},{"en":"Refusing an unfair official order can be seen as resistance to the state.","zh":"拒絕不公平官方命令可以被視為對國家政權的反抗。"},{"en":"If a government treats criticism as resistance, ordinary protest becomes risky.","zh":"如果政府把批評視為反抗，普通抗議就變得有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes opposition that challenges state power.","zh":"這個片語描述挑戰國家權力的反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"under increasing pressure from","meaning":"面對來自……日益增加的壓力","examples":[{"en":"The government came under increasing pressure from the anti-dam movement.","zh":"政府面對來自反水壩運動日益增加的壓力。"},{"en":"To come under increasing pressure from someone means to face growing demands or criticism from them.","zh":"To come under increasing pressure from someone 指面對來自他們越來越大的要求或批評。"},{"en":"A school may come under increasing pressure from parents to improve lunch quality.","zh":"學校可能面對來自家長日益增加的壓力，要求改善午餐質素。"},{"en":"If pressure grows, leaders may be forced to change their position.","zh":"如果壓力增加，領導者可能被迫改變立場。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pressure that becomes stronger over time.","zh":"這個片語描述隨時間變強的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"anti-dam movement","meaning":"反水壩運動","examples":[{"en":"The anti-dam movement attracted growing public support.","zh":"反水壩運動吸引越來越多公眾支持。"},{"en":"An anti-dam movement is an organised campaign against the building of a dam.","zh":"Anti-dam movement 是反對興建水壩的有組織運動。"},{"en":"Villagers may form an anti-dam movement if their homes will be flooded.","zh":"如果村民住宅將被淹沒，他們可能組成反水壩運動。"},{"en":"If the movement explains environmental risks clearly, more people may join it.","zh":"如果該運動清楚解釋環境風險，更多人可能加入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collective opposition to a dam project.","zh":"這個片語描述對水壩項目的集體反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be divided","meaning":"出現分歧","examples":[{"en":"The Hungarian Communist Party was divided over the dam.","zh":"匈牙利共產黨在水壩問題上出現分歧。"},{"en":"To be divided over something means to have strong disagreement within a group about it.","zh":"To be divided over something 指一個群體內部對某事有強烈不同意見。"},{"en":"A class may be divided over whether phones should be allowed during lunch.","zh":"班上可能就午膳時是否容許手機而出現分歧。"},{"en":"If a ruling party is divided, it may struggle to make a clear decision.","zh":"如果執政黨出現分歧，它可能難以作出清晰決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes internal disagreement.","zh":"這個片語描述內部分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reformists","meaning":"改革派","examples":[{"en":"Reformists within the party began to oppose the project.","zh":"黨內改革派開始反對該項目。"},{"en":"Reformists are people who want to change a system gradually rather than preserve it completely.","zh":"Reformists 是希望逐步改變制度，而不是完全維持原狀的人。"},{"en":"Reformists in a school may argue for fairer rules instead of removing all rules.","zh":"學校中的改革派可能主張更公平規則，而不是取消所有規則。"},{"en":"If reformists gain influence, old policies may be reviewed or replaced.","zh":"如果改革派影響力增加，舊政策可能被重新檢視或取代。"},{"en":"This word describes people who support change from within a system.","zh":"這個詞描述支持在制度內改變的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"neither popular nor economical","meaning":"既不受歡迎也不合乎經濟效益","examples":[{"en":"The reformists believed that the dam was neither popular nor economical.","zh":"改革派認為該水壩既不受歡迎也不合乎經濟效益。"},{"en":"Neither popular nor economical means not liked by people and not financially sensible.","zh":"Neither popular nor economical 指既不受人喜歡，也不在財政上合理。"},{"en":"A school trip that students dislike and families cannot afford is neither popular nor economical.","zh":"如果學生不喜歡，而家庭又負擔不起，學校旅行就是既不受歡迎也不合乎經濟效益。"},{"en":"If a project costs too much and lacks support, politicians may abandon it.","zh":"如果項目成本太高又缺乏支持，政治人物可能放棄它。"},{"en":"This phrase gives two negative judgments at once.","zh":"這個片語一次給出兩個負面評價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"generate electricity","meaning":"發電","examples":[{"en":"Other methods could generate electricity more cheaply.","zh":"其他方法可以更便宜地發電。"},{"en":"To generate electricity means to produce electrical power.","zh":"To generate electricity 指產生電力。"},{"en":"Solar panels can generate electricity when sunlight hits their cells.","zh":"陽光照射太陽能電池時，太陽能板可以發電。"},{"en":"If a method generates electricity cheaply, it may be preferred over more expensive projects.","zh":"如果某方法能便宜發電，它可能比更昂貴工程更受青睞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes producing usable electric power.","zh":"這個片語描述產生可用電力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"burn coal","meaning":"燃燒煤炭","examples":[{"en":"The reformists considered generating electricity by burning coal.","zh":"改革派考慮透過燃燒煤炭來發電。"},{"en":"To burn coal means to use coal as fuel, usually to produce heat or electricity.","zh":"To burn coal 指使用煤炭作燃料，通常用來產生熱能或電力。"},{"en":"A power station may burn coal to run turbines and supply a city.","zh":"發電站可能燃燒煤炭來推動渦輪機並為城市供電。"},{"en":"If a country burns coal heavily, air pollution and carbon emissions may rise.","zh":"如果一個國家大量燃燒煤炭，空氣污染和碳排放可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a traditional but polluting energy method.","zh":"這個片語描述傳統但污染性的能源方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"use nuclear power","meaning":"使用核能","examples":[{"en":"Nuclear power was presented as another source of electricity.","zh":"核能被提出作為另一種電力來源。"},{"en":"To use nuclear power means to produce energy from nuclear reactions in a power station.","zh":"To use nuclear power 指在發電站利用核反應產生能源。"},{"en":"Some countries use nuclear power to generate large amounts of electricity with low direct carbon emissions.","zh":"一些國家使用核能，以低直接碳排放產生大量電力。"},{"en":"If nuclear power is used, safety, waste, and public trust become important issues.","zh":"如果使用核能，安全、廢料和公眾信任會成為重要議題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one possible energy source.","zh":"這個片語描述一種可能能源來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hardliners","meaning":"強硬派","examples":[{"en":"Party hardliners continued to defend the dam.","zh":"黨內強硬派繼續維護水壩。"},{"en":"Hardliners are people who strongly defend strict traditional positions and resist compromise.","zh":"Hardliners 是堅決維護嚴格傳統立場並拒絕妥協的人。"},{"en":"School hardliners may insist on punishment even when counselling would help more.","zh":"學校中的強硬派可能堅持懲罰，即使輔導更有幫助。"},{"en":"If hardliners control a decision, reform becomes difficult.","zh":"如果強硬派控制決策，改革就會困難。"},{"en":"This word describes people who take an uncompromising position.","zh":"這個詞描述採取不妥協立場的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"defend Stalinist ideas","meaning":"維護史太林主義思想","examples":[{"en":"The hardliners defended Stalinist ideas about large dams.","zh":"強硬派維護關於大型水壩的史太林主義思想。"},{"en":"To defend Stalinist ideas means to support political beliefs linked with central control, heavy industry, and grand state projects.","zh":"To defend Stalinist ideas 指支持與中央控制、重工業和大型國家工程有關的政治信念。"},{"en":"A politician may defend old ideas if they see them as symbols of national strength.","zh":"如果政治人物把舊思想視為國家力量象徵，他可能維護它們。"},{"en":"If leaders defend outdated ideology, they may ignore practical and environmental concerns.","zh":"如果領導者維護過時意識形態，他們可能忽視實際和環境關注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes support for a specific old political tradition.","zh":"這個片語描述支持一種特定舊政治傳統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"large dams","meaning":"大型水壩","examples":[{"en":"Large dams were treated as symbols of industrial progress.","zh":"大型水壩被視為工業進步的象徵。"},{"en":"Large dams are major structures built across rivers to store water, control flow, or generate electricity.","zh":"Large dams 是橫跨河流興建、用於儲水、控制水流或發電的大型結構。"},{"en":"A large dam may provide power and irrigation for many towns.","zh":"大型水壩可能為許多城鎮提供電力和灌溉。"},{"en":"If a large dam floods valleys, it can also destroy homes and ecosystems.","zh":"如果大型水壩淹沒山谷，它也可能摧毀住宅和生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes big river-control projects with both benefits and risks.","zh":"這個片語描述大型河流控制工程，兼具好處和風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"symbols of progress","meaning":"進步的象徵","examples":[{"en":"Supporters regarded major engineering projects as symbols of progress.","zh":"支持者把大型工程項目視為進步的象徵。"},{"en":"Symbols of progress are things that people believe represent modernisation, development, or improvement.","zh":"Symbols of progress 是人們認為代表現代化、發展或改善的事物。"},{"en":"A new railway may be seen as a symbol of progress in a remote town.","zh":"新鐵路可能被偏遠城鎮視為進步的象徵。"},{"en":"If a project becomes a symbol of progress, criticism of it may be treated as backward-looking.","zh":"如果某項目成為進步象徵，對它的批評可能被視為落後。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what an object or project is made to represent.","zh":"這個片語描述物件或項目被賦予的代表意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"environmental issues","meaning":"環境議題","examples":[{"en":"Environmental issues exposed weaknesses in Communist governments.","zh":"環境議題暴露出共產政府的弱點。"},{"en":"Environmental issues are problems involving nature, pollution, resources, climate, or public health.","zh":"Environmental issues 是涉及自然、污染、資源、氣候或公共健康的問題。"},{"en":"A school may discuss environmental issues such as plastic waste and air pollution.","zh":"學校可能討論塑膠廢物和空氣污染等環境議題。"},{"en":"If governments ignore environmental issues, public trust may decline.","zh":"如果政府忽視環境議題，公眾信任可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase covers problems affecting the natural world and human communities.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋影響自然世界和人類社區的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"weak point of","meaning":"……的弱點","examples":[{"en":"Environmental protection was a weak point of Eastern European communism.","zh":"環境保護是東歐共產主義的弱點。"},{"en":"A weak point of something is an area where it is vulnerable or performs badly.","zh":"Weak point of something 是某事物脆弱或表現差的方面。"},{"en":"Pronunciation may be a weak point of a student who reads well but rarely speaks.","zh":"對閱讀好但很少說話的學生來說，發音可能是弱點。"},{"en":"If a system has a weak point, opponents may focus their criticism there.","zh":"如果制度有弱點，反對者可能集中批評該處。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a weakness inside a larger system.","zh":"這個片語指出較大系統內部的弱處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Eastern European communism","meaning":"東歐共產主義","examples":[{"en":"Environmental opposition grew during the final years of Eastern European communism.","zh":"在東歐共產主義最後幾年，環境反對力量增加。"},{"en":"Eastern European communism refers to Communist political systems in Eastern Europe during the Cold War period.","zh":"Eastern European communism 指冷戰時期東歐的共產政治制度。"},{"en":"History students may study Eastern European communism to understand state control and opposition movements.","zh":"歷史學生可能研究東歐共產主義，以理解國家控制和反對運動。"},{"en":"If environmental campaigns challenged these regimes, green politics could become political resistance.","zh":"如果環保運動挑戰這些政權，綠色政治就可能變成政治反抗。"},{"en":"This phrase names a regional political system.","zh":"這個片語命名一種地區政治制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in its final years","meaning":"在其最後幾年","examples":[{"en":"The political system faced growing opposition in its final years.","zh":"該政治制度在其最後幾年面對日益增加的反對。"},{"en":"In its final years means during the last period before something ended.","zh":"In its final years 指某事結束前的最後時期。"},{"en":"In its final years, an old school building may need frequent repairs.","zh":"在其最後幾年，舊校舍可能需要頻繁維修。"},{"en":"If a regime faces pressure in its final years, small protests may become historically important.","zh":"如果政權在最後幾年面對壓力，小型抗議可能變得具歷史重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the closing stage of an organisation or system.","zh":"這個片語描述組織或制度的結束階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"with the support of","meaning":"在……支持下","examples":[{"en":"Environmental groups were founded with the support of youth organisations.","zh":"環保組織在青年組織支持下成立。"},{"en":"With the support of someone means helped, encouraged, or backed by them.","zh":"With the support of someone 指在某人的幫助、鼓勵或支持下。"},{"en":"A student club may succeed with the support of teachers and parents.","zh":"學生社團可能在老師和家長支持下成功。"},{"en":"If a campaign has organisational support, it can reach more people.","zh":"如果運動有組織支持，它可以接觸更多人。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who helped an action happen.","zh":"這個片語指出誰幫助行動發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Young Communist Leagues","meaning":"青年共產主義聯盟","examples":[{"en":"The Young Communist Leagues supported several environmental groups.","zh":"青年共產主義聯盟支持了幾個環保組織。"},{"en":"Young Communist Leagues were youth organisations linked with Communist parties.","zh":"Young Communist Leagues 是與共產黨有關的青年組織。"},{"en":"Young Communist Leagues may organise study activities, public service, or youth campaigns.","zh":"青年共產主義聯盟可能組織學習活動、公共服務或青年運動。"},{"en":"If such groups support environmental work, officials may first see it as politically harmless.","zh":"如果這類組織支持環保工作，官員起初可能視之為政治上無害。"},{"en":"This phrase names youth organisations within a Communist political context.","zh":"這個片語命名共產政治背景下的青年組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a host of","meaning":"大量的……","examples":[{"en":"A host of environmental groups were founded during the 1970s.","zh":"大量環保組織在1970年代成立。"},{"en":"A host of something means a large number of them.","zh":"A host of something 指大量某事物。"},{"en":"A host of students joined the charity walk after the school assembly.","zh":"學校早會後，大量學生參加慈善步行。"},{"en":"If a host of groups appears, a social concern may be spreading quickly.","zh":"如果大量團體出現，某種社會關注可能正在快速擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises quantity and variety.","zh":"這個片語強調數量和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"environmental groups","meaning":"環保組織","examples":[{"en":"Many environmental groups later became politically active.","zh":"許多環保組織後來變得政治活躍。"},{"en":"Environmental groups are organisations that work to protect nature and reduce pollution.","zh":"Environmental groups 是致力保護自然和減少污染的組織。"},{"en":"Environmental groups may organise clean-up days, petitions, or public talks.","zh":"環保組織可能組織清潔日、請願或公開講座。"},{"en":"If environmental groups challenge government projects, they may become political actors.","zh":"如果環保組織挑戰政府工程，它們可能成為政治行動者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised groups focused on environmental protection.","zh":"這個片語描述專注環境保護的有組織團體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"harmless product of","meaning":"……的無害產物","examples":[{"en":"Officials saw the groups as a harmless product of youthful idealism.","zh":"官員把這些團體視為青年理想主義的無害產物。"},{"en":"A harmless product of something is a result that seems safe and not threatening.","zh":"Harmless product of something 是看似安全且不具威脅的結果。"},{"en":"A school may see students’ posters as a harmless product of excitement before sports day.","zh":"學校可能把學生海報視為運動日前興奮情緒的無害產物。"},{"en":"If leaders underestimate a movement as harmless, they may miss its political power.","zh":"如果領導者低估運動，視之為無害，他們可能錯過其政治力量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a result judged as innocent or low-risk.","zh":"這個片語描述被判斷為天真或低風險的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"youthful idealism","meaning":"青年理想主義","examples":[{"en":"Officials underestimated the political power of youthful idealism.","zh":"官員低估了青年理想主義的政治力量。"},{"en":"Youthful idealism is the strong belief among young people that society can be fairer or better.","zh":"Youthful idealism 是年輕人強烈相信社會可以更公平或更美好的信念。"},{"en":"Youthful idealism may lead students to volunteer, protest, or start community projects.","zh":"青年理想主義可能令學生做義工、抗議或開展社區項目。"},{"en":"If idealism is joined with organisation, it can become a force for change.","zh":"如果理想主義加上組織能力，它可以成為改變力量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hopeful values often associated with young people.","zh":"這個片語描述常與年輕人相關的希望價值觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Boy Scouts","meaning":"童軍","examples":[{"en":"Some groups developed from Boy Scout organisations.","zh":"一些團體由童軍組織發展而來。"},{"en":"Boy Scouts are youth groups that teach outdoor skills, teamwork, service, and discipline.","zh":"Boy Scouts 是教授戶外技能、團隊合作、服務和紀律的青年團體。"},{"en":"Boy Scouts may learn camping, first aid, map reading, and community service.","zh":"童軍可能學習露營、急救、看地圖和社區服務。"},{"en":"If young people learn teamwork early, they may later organise campaigns more effectively.","zh":"如果年輕人早年學會團隊合作，他們之後可能更有效組織運動。"},{"en":"This phrase names a youth movement, not just boys who walk in nature.","zh":"這個片語命名青年運動，而不是只指在自然中行走的男孩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"natural history societies","meaning":"博物學會","examples":[{"en":"Natural history societies helped encourage environmental interest.","zh":"博物學會幫助鼓勵人們對環境產生興趣。"},{"en":"Natural history societies are groups that study plants, animals, rocks, landscapes, and local nature.","zh":"Natural history societies 是研究植物、動物、岩石、景觀和本地自然的團體。"},{"en":"A natural history society may organise bird walks and talks about local forests.","zh":"博物學會可能組織觀鳥步行和本地森林講座。"},{"en":"If people learn about nature closely, they may become more willing to protect it.","zh":"如果人們深入了解自然，他們可能更願意保護它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes community groups interested in the natural world.","zh":"這個片語描述關注自然世界的社區團體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"green idealism","meaning":"綠色理想主義","examples":[{"en":"Green idealism gradually became connected with political resistance.","zh":"綠色理想主義逐漸與政治反抗連接起來。"},{"en":"Green idealism is the belief that protecting nature should guide public life and decisions.","zh":"Green idealism 是相信保護自然應指導公共生活和決策的信念。"},{"en":"Students show green idealism when they push their school to reduce waste.","zh":"學生推動學校減少廢物時，就是展現綠色理想主義。"},{"en":"If green idealism challenges official projects, it can become politically powerful.","zh":"如果綠色理想主義挑戰官方項目，它可以變得具有政治力量。"},{"en":"This phrase links environmental values with hope for change.","zh":"這個片語把環境價值與改變的希望連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"steadily become","meaning":"逐漸成為","examples":[{"en":"Environmentalism steadily became a focus of opposition.","zh":"環保主義逐漸成為反對力量的焦點。"},{"en":"To steadily become something means to gradually turn into it over time.","zh":"To steadily become something 指隨時間逐步變成某事物。"},{"en":"A shy student may steadily become more confident through regular speaking practice.","zh":"害羞學生可能透過定期口語練習逐漸變得更有信心。"},{"en":"If a small issue steadily becomes larger, more people begin to notice it.","zh":"如果小問題逐漸變大，更多人開始注意它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow but continuous development.","zh":"這個片語描述緩慢但持續的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"focal point for","meaning":"……的焦點","examples":[{"en":"Green politics became a focal point for political opposition.","zh":"綠色政治成為政治反對力量的焦點。"},{"en":"A focal point for something is the main place, issue, or idea around which attention gathers.","zh":"Focal point for something 是注意力聚集的主要地方、議題或想法。"},{"en":"A school library can become a focal point for reading activities.","zh":"學校圖書館可以成為閱讀活動的焦點。"},{"en":"If one issue becomes a focal point, different groups may unite around it.","zh":"如果某議題成為焦點，不同團體可能圍繞它聯合起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the centre of attention or action.","zh":"這個片語描述注意力或行動的中心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"political opposition","meaning":"政治反對力量","examples":[{"en":"Environmental campaigns provided a form of political opposition.","zh":"環保運動提供了一種政治反對力量。"},{"en":"Political opposition is organised disagreement with a government, party, or political system.","zh":"Political opposition 是對政府、政黨或政治制度的有組織反對。"},{"en":"Citizens may express political opposition through speeches, petitions, elections, or protests.","zh":"市民可能透過演講、請願、選舉或示威表達政治反對。"},{"en":"If direct criticism is dangerous, opposition may appear through environmental campaigns.","zh":"如果直接批評很危險，反對力量可能透過環保運動出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes resistance in the political sphere.","zh":"這個片語描述政治領域中的抵抗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"human-rights movement","meaning":"人權運動","examples":[{"en":"Charter 77 was a human-rights movement in Czechoslovakia.","zh":"Charter 77 是捷克斯洛伐克的一場人權運動。"},{"en":"A human-rights movement is an organised effort to protect basic freedoms and dignity.","zh":"Human-rights movement 是保護基本自由和尊嚴的有組織努力。"},{"en":"A human-rights movement may defend free speech, fair trials, and protection from abuse.","zh":"人權運動可能捍衛言論自由、公平審訊和免受虐待的保障。"},{"en":"If a movement links human rights with environmental issues, its concerns become broader.","zh":"如果運動把人權與環境議題連接起來，其關注就變得更廣泛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes activism focused on fundamental rights.","zh":"這個片語描述專注基本權利的行動主義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take up environmentalism","meaning":"開始支持環保主義","examples":[{"en":"The Charter 77 movement took up environmentalism.","zh":"Charter 77 運動開始支持環保主義。"},{"en":"To take up environmentalism means to begin supporting environmental protection as an important cause.","zh":"To take up environmentalism 指開始支持環境保護作為重要理念。"},{"en":"A student council may take up environmentalism by reducing plastic use at school.","zh":"學生會可能透過減少學校塑膠使用來開始支持環保主義。"},{"en":"If a human-rights group takes up environmentalism, it treats pollution as a public concern.","zh":"如果人權團體開始支持環保主義，它就把污染視為公共關注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adopting an environmental cause.","zh":"這個片語描述採納環保理念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"green-minded people","meaning":"重視環保的人","examples":[{"en":"Green-minded people in Poland and Estonia joined an international organisation.","zh":"波蘭和愛沙尼亞重視環保的人加入了一個國際組織。"},{"en":"Green-minded people are people who care strongly about environmental protection.","zh":"Green-minded people 是非常關心環境保護的人。"},{"en":"Green-minded students may bring reusable lunch boxes and organise recycling.","zh":"重視環保的學生可能帶可重用飯盒並組織回收。"},{"en":"If green-minded people connect across borders, environmental campaigns can become international.","zh":"如果重視環保的人跨國連結，環保運動可以變成國際運動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people with environmental values.","zh":"這個片語描述有環保價值觀的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Friends of the Earth International","meaning":"國際地球之友","examples":[{"en":"Environmentalists joined Friends of the Earth International.","zh":"環保人士加入國際地球之友。"},{"en":"Friends of the Earth International is a global network of environmental organisations.","zh":"Friends of the Earth International 是全球環保組織網絡。"},{"en":"A local environmental group may join Friends of the Earth International to share campaigns and information.","zh":"本地環保團體可能加入國際地球之友，以分享運動和資訊。"},{"en":"If activists join an international network, their local issue may receive wider support.","zh":"如果活動人士加入國際網絡，他們的本地議題可能獲得更廣泛支持。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific international environmental organisation.","zh":"這個片語命名一個特定國際環保組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"protest against air pollution","meaning":"抗議空氣污染","examples":[{"en":"Activists organised campaigns to protest against air pollution.","zh":"活動人士組織運動抗議空氣污染。"},{"en":"To protest against air pollution means to publicly oppose dirty air and demand action.","zh":"To protest against air pollution 指公開反對骯髒空氣並要求行動。"},{"en":"Residents may protest against air pollution if factories release smoke near homes.","zh":"如果工廠在住宅附近排煙，居民可能抗議空氣污染。"},{"en":"If protests grow, governments may introduce cleaner transport or stricter factory rules.","zh":"如果抗議增加，政府可能引入更清潔交通或更嚴格工廠規則。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public action against polluted air.","zh":"這個片語描述針對空氣污染的公開行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"resistance group","meaning":"反抗組織","examples":[{"en":"Bulgarian environmentalists built a resistance group called Ecoglasnost.","zh":"保加利亞環保人士建立了一個名為 Ecoglasnost 的反抗組織。"},{"en":"A resistance group is an organised group that opposes authority, injustice, or a harmful policy.","zh":"Resistance group 是反對權威、不公義或有害政策的有組織團體。"},{"en":"Residents may form a resistance group to fight a dangerous waste project.","zh":"居民可能組成反抗組織，反對危險廢物項目。"},{"en":"If a resistance group gains members, it can put pressure on officials.","zh":"如果反抗組織獲得成員，它可以向官員施壓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised opposition, often under difficult conditions.","zh":"這個片語描述有組織反對，通常是在困難條件下。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Ecoglasnost","meaning":"Ecoglasnost 環保組織","examples":[{"en":"Ecoglasnost organised large environmental protests in Bulgaria.","zh":"Ecoglasnost 環保組織在保加利亞組織大型環保抗議。"},{"en":"Ecoglasnost was a Bulgarian environmental resistance group.","zh":"Ecoglasnost 是保加利亞一個環保反抗組織。"},{"en":"A history class may study Ecoglasnost as an example of environmental activism becoming political.","zh":"歷史課可能研究 Ecoglasnost，作為環保行動主義變成政治力量的例子。"},{"en":"If a group organises large rallies, it can become a visible challenge to authority.","zh":"如果團體組織大型集會，它可以成為對權威的明顯挑戰。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific environmental organisation.","zh":"這個片語命名一個特定環保組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"hold huge rallies","meaning":"舉行大型集會","examples":[{"en":"The group held huge rallies in 1989.","zh":"該組織在1989年舉行大型集會。"},{"en":"To hold huge rallies means to organise very large public gatherings for a cause.","zh":"To hold huge rallies 指為某理念組織非常大型的公開集會。"},{"en":"Students may hold a rally to demand safer roads near their school.","zh":"學生可能舉行集會，要求學校附近道路更安全。"},{"en":"If rallies are huge, the issue becomes difficult for authorities to ignore.","zh":"如果集會規模很大，當局就難以忽視該議題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large-scale public mobilisation.","zh":"這個片語描述大規模公眾動員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"potent symbols of","meaning":"……的強烈象徵","examples":[{"en":"Large water-engineering projects were potent symbols of the old political system.","zh":"大型水利工程項目是舊政治制度的強烈象徵。"},{"en":"Potent symbols of something are powerful signs that strongly represent an idea, system, or feeling.","zh":"Potent symbols of something 是強烈代表某想法、制度或感受的有力符號。"},{"en":"A closed factory may become a potent symbol of economic decline in a town.","zh":"關閉的工廠可能成為城鎮經濟衰落的強烈象徵。"},{"en":"If a dam symbolises state power, opposing it can carry political meaning.","zh":"如果水壩象徵國家權力，反對它就可能帶有政治意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes symbols with strong emotional or political force.","zh":"這個片語描述具有強烈情緒或政治力量的象徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"water-engineering projects","meaning":"水利工程項目","examples":[{"en":"Large water-engineering projects were associated with Stalinism.","zh":"大型水利工程項目與史太林主義有關。"},{"en":"Water-engineering projects are large works that control, redirect, store, or use water.","zh":"Water-engineering projects 是控制、改道、儲存或使用水的大型工程。"},{"en":"Dams, canals, reservoirs, and flood barriers are water-engineering projects.","zh":"水壩、運河、水庫和防洪牆都是水利工程項目。"},{"en":"If such projects ignore local ecology, they can create serious environmental damage.","zh":"如果這些工程忽視本地生態，它們可以造成嚴重環境破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes engineering works built around water systems.","zh":"這個片語描述圍繞水系統興建的工程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"old Stalinism","meaning":"舊式史太林主義","examples":[{"en":"The dams were viewed as symbols of old Stalinism.","zh":"這些水壩被視為舊式史太林主義的象徵。"},{"en":"Old Stalinism refers to an older style of Communist rule associated with central control, heavy industry, and grand state projects.","zh":"Old Stalinism 指與中央控制、重工業和大型國家工程相關的舊式共產統治風格。"},{"en":"Critics may use “old Stalinism” to criticise rigid political thinking and state power.","zh":"批評者可能用「舊式史太林主義」批評僵化政治思維和國家權力。"},{"en":"If a project is linked with old Stalinism, it may seem authoritarian rather than modern.","zh":"如果某項目與舊式史太林主義有關，它可能顯得威權而非現代。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an outdated political style.","zh":"這個片語描述過時的政治風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words and phrases from the list.","zh":"學生使用列表中的字詞和片語完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill in missing parts of a shortened version of the passage.","zh":"To complete the summary 指填補文章簡短版本中缺失的部分。"},{"en":"In reading exams, students should read the whole summary before choosing answers.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生應先閱讀整個摘要，再選答案。"},{"en":"If the summary changes the wording, students must match meaning rather than exact phrases.","zh":"如果摘要改變措辭，學生必須配對意思，而不是只找完全相同片語。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction for gap-filling tasks.","zh":"這個片語是填空題常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"using the list of","meaning":"使用……列表","examples":[{"en":"The summary must be completed using the list of words provided.","zh":"摘要必須使用所提供的詞語列表完成。"},{"en":"Using the list of something means choosing from the given set of options.","zh":"Using the list of something 指從給定的一組選項中選擇。"},{"en":"Students may answer a matching task using the list of names beside the passage.","zh":"學生可能使用文章旁邊的人名列表回答配對題。"},{"en":"If answers must come from a list, students should not invent their own words.","zh":"如果答案必須來自列表，學生不應自創詞語。"},{"en":"This phrase tells learners where the possible answers come from.","zh":"這個片語告訴學習者可能答案來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"discuss something with","meaning":"與……討論某事","examples":[{"en":"Vargha visited the area to discuss development plans with local officials.","zh":"Vargha 到訪該地區，與地方官員討論發展計劃。"},{"en":"To discuss something with someone means to talk about it and exchange information or opinions.","zh":"To discuss something with someone 指與某人談論某事並交換資料或意見。"},{"en":"A student may discuss subject choices with a teacher before making a decision.","zh":"學生作決定前，可能與老師討論選科。"},{"en":"If people discuss a plan early, problems may be noticed before work begins.","zh":"如果人們早期討論計劃，問題可能在工程開始前被注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two-way communication about a topic.","zh":"這個片語描述關於某主題的雙向溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"constructing a small park","meaning":"興建小型公園","examples":[{"en":"The original discussion concerned constructing a small park.","zh":"最初討論涉及興建小型公園。"},{"en":"Constructing a small park means building a limited public green space.","zh":"Constructing a small park 指建造有限規模的公共綠色空間。"},{"en":"A community may support constructing a small park so children have somewhere safe to play.","zh":"社區可能支持興建小型公園，讓孩子有安全地方玩耍。"},{"en":"If a small park is planned near historic remains, planners must protect the site carefully.","zh":"如果小型公園計劃建於歷史遺跡附近，規劃者必須小心保護該地點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a modest local building project.","zh":"這個片語描述小規模本地建設項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be swallowed up by","meaning":"被……吞沒；被……淹沒","examples":[{"en":"The tree-lined river bend was to be swallowed up by the dam.","zh":"兩旁種滿樹木的河灣將被水壩吞沒。"},{"en":"To be swallowed up by something means to disappear because something larger covers or absorbs it.","zh":"To be swallowed up by something 指因被更大的事物覆蓋或吸收而消失。"},{"en":"A small shop may be swallowed up by a large shopping mall project.","zh":"小店可能被大型商場項目吞沒。"},{"en":"If a valley is swallowed up by a reservoir, its roads and fields may vanish under water.","zh":"如果山谷被水庫淹沒，其道路和田野可能消失在水下。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests being completely overtaken or covered.","zh":"這個片語暗示被完全吞併或覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"colossal dam","meaning":"巨型水壩","examples":[{"en":"The river bend was threatened by a colossal dam.","zh":"該河灣受到巨型水壩威脅。"},{"en":"A colossal dam is an extremely large dam.","zh":"Colossal dam 是極其大型的水壩。"},{"en":"A colossal dam may hold back enough water to create a huge reservoir.","zh":"巨型水壩可能阻擋足夠水量，形成巨大水庫。"},{"en":"If a dam is colossal, its environmental and social effects may also be very large.","zh":"如果水壩規模巨大，其環境和社會影響也可能非常大。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the enormous scale of the structure.","zh":"這個片語強調結構的龐大規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"severe impact on","meaning":"對……造成嚴重影響","examples":[{"en":"The project was expected to have a severe impact on the ecosystem.","zh":"該項目預計會對生態系統造成嚴重影響。"},{"en":"A severe impact on something is a serious and damaging effect on it.","zh":"Severe impact on something 是對某事造成嚴重而有害的影響。"},{"en":"Long roadworks can have a severe impact on small shops if customers stop visiting.","zh":"如果顧客停止到訪，長期道路工程可以對小店造成嚴重影響。"},{"en":"If a river project damages wetlands and water reserves, its impact is severe.","zh":"如果河流工程破壞濕地和地下水，其影響就是嚴重的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong negative consequences.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈負面後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"combined public-works project","meaning":"聯合公共工程項目","examples":[{"en":"The dam formed part of a combined public-works project.","zh":"該水壩構成聯合公共工程項目的一部分。"},{"en":"A combined public-works project is a large government construction scheme with several linked purposes.","zh":"Combined public-works project 是有幾個相關目的的大型政府建設計劃。"},{"en":"A city may launch a combined public-works project to improve drainage, roads, and public spaces together.","zh":"城市可能推出聯合公共工程項目，同時改善排水、道路和公共空間。"},{"en":"If many aims are combined, one project may affect transport, farming, and the environment at once.","zh":"如果許多目標被結合，一項工程可能同時影響交通、農業和環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a joined-up state construction programme.","zh":"這個片語描述整合式國家建設計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"public-works project","meaning":"公共工程項目","examples":[{"en":"The project involved dams, irrigation and improved navigation.","zh":"該項目涉及水壩、灌溉和改善航運。"},{"en":"A public-works project is a government-funded construction project for public infrastructure.","zh":"Public-works project 是由政府資助、用於公共基建的建設項目。"},{"en":"Bridges, roads, reservoirs, and drainage systems are public-works projects.","zh":"橋樑、道路、水庫和排水系統都是公共工程項目。"},{"en":"If a public-works project is large, it may require public consultation and environmental study.","zh":"如果公共工程項目規模大，它可能需要公眾諮詢和環境研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes infrastructure built for public use or national development.","zh":"這個片語描述為公共使用或國家發展而建的基建。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"establish an organisation","meaning":"成立組織","examples":[{"en":"The campaigners established the Danube Circle.","zh":"運動人士成立了多瑙河圈。"},{"en":"To establish an organisation means to formally create a group for a purpose.","zh":"To establish an organisation 指為某目的正式創立團體。"},{"en":"Parents may establish an organisation to support children with special learning needs.","zh":"家長可能成立組織，支援有特殊學習需要的兒童。"},{"en":"If an organisation is established, members can coordinate meetings, publicity, and action.","zh":"如果組織成立，成員可以協調會議、宣傳和行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes founding a structured group.","zh":"這個片語描述創立有結構的團體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"demonstrate people’s autonomy","meaning":"展示人民的自主權","examples":[{"en":"The group tried to demonstrate people’s autonomy in a democracy.","zh":"該組織嘗試展示民主制度中人民的自主權。"},{"en":"To demonstrate people’s autonomy means to show that citizens can think, decide, and act for themselves.","zh":"To demonstrate people’s autonomy 指顯示市民能自己思考、決定和行動。"},{"en":"Students demonstrate autonomy when they organise a reading club without waiting for teachers.","zh":"學生不等老師安排而自行組織閱讀會時，就是展示自主。"},{"en":"If people sign petitions and hold meetings, they show that public life is not only controlled from above.","zh":"如果人們簽署請願和舉行會議，他們顯示公共生活不只是由上而下控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes showing independent civic action.","zh":"這個片語描述展示獨立公民行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"Hungarian edition","meaning":"匈牙利版本","examples":[{"en":"Vargha became editor of the Hungarian edition of Scientific American.","zh":"Vargha 成為《科學美國人》匈牙利版本的編輯。"},{"en":"A Hungarian edition is a version of a publication prepared for Hungarian readers.","zh":"Hungarian edition 是為匈牙利讀者準備的出版物版本。"},{"en":"A magazine may publish a Hungarian edition with translated articles and local notes.","zh":"雜誌可能出版匈牙利版本，包含翻譯文章和本地註解。"},{"en":"If a scientific magazine has local editions, more readers can access research in their own language.","zh":"如果科學雜誌有本地版本，更多讀者能用自己的語言接觸研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a language-specific version.","zh":"這個片語描述特定語言版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be discharged from a position","meaning":"被解除職務","examples":[{"en":"An editor may be discharged from a position for political reasons.","zh":"編輯可能因政治原因被解除職務。"},{"en":"To be discharged from a position means to be removed from a job or duty.","zh":"To be discharged from a position 指被免除工作或職責。"},{"en":"A coach may be discharged from a position after repeated complaints from parents.","zh":"教練可能因家長反覆投訴而被解除職務。"},{"en":"If someone is discharged for speaking out, the action may be seen as punishment.","zh":"如果某人因發聲而被解除職務，該行動可能被視為懲罰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal removal from a role.","zh":"這個片語描述正式被移除職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reformist politicians","meaning":"改革派政治人物","examples":[{"en":"Reformist politicians opposed the dam on economic grounds.","zh":"改革派政治人物基於經濟理由反對水壩。"},{"en":"Reformist politicians are political figures who support changes to improve the existing system.","zh":"Reformist politicians 是支持改變現有制度以改善它的政治人物。"},{"en":"Reformist politicians may propose fairer rules rather than defend old practices.","zh":"改革派政治人物可能提出更公平規則，而不是維護舊做法。"},{"en":"If reformists see a project as wasteful, they may oppose it even from inside the government.","zh":"如果改革派認為項目浪費，他們即使在政府內部也可能反對它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes politicians who favour change.","zh":"這個片語描述支持改革的政治人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"political establishment","meaning":"政治建制","examples":[{"en":"The political establishment originally supported the project.","zh":"政治建制最初支持該項目。"},{"en":"The political establishment is the powerful group of leaders and institutions that control politics.","zh":"Political establishment 是控制政治的有權勢領導層和機構。"},{"en":"A reform movement may challenge the political establishment when official leaders ignore public needs.","zh":"當官方領袖忽視公眾需要，改革運動可能挑戰政治建制。"},{"en":"If the establishment supports a project, officials and media may defend it strongly.","zh":"如果建制支持某項目，官員和傳媒可能強力維護它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the ruling political order.","zh":"這個片語指掌權的政治秩序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be in collision over","meaning":"因……而發生衝突","examples":[{"en":"The authorities and environmentalists were in collision over the dam.","zh":"當局和環保人士因水壩而發生衝突。"},{"en":"To be in collision over something means to be in serious conflict about it.","zh":"To be in collision over something 指因某事出現嚴重衝突。"},{"en":"Parents and school managers may be in collision over a new uniform rule.","zh":"家長和學校管理層可能因新校服規則而發生衝突。"},{"en":"If two groups have opposite aims, negotiation may become difficult.","zh":"如果兩個群體目標相反，談判可能變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong disagreement, not a minor difference.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈分歧，而不是小差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"favourable impact","meaning":"正面影響","examples":[{"en":"Supporters claimed that the project would have a favourable impact on navigation.","zh":"支持者聲稱該項目會對航運有正面影響。"},{"en":"A favourable impact is a positive or helpful effect.","zh":"Favourable impact 是正面或有幫助的效果。"},{"en":"A new bus route may have a favourable impact on students who live far from school.","zh":"新巴士路線可能對住得離學校遠的學生有正面影響。"},{"en":"If a project improves transport safely, it may have a favourable impact on trade.","zh":"如果項目安全地改善交通，它可能對貿易有正面影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a good result or advantage.","zh":"這個片語描述好結果或優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be separated from","meaning":"與……分開","examples":[{"en":"Political protest could not easily be separated from environmental activism.","zh":"政治抗議不能輕易與環境行動主義分開。"},{"en":"To be separated from something means to be clearly divided from it.","zh":"To be separated from something 指與某事清楚分開。"},{"en":"In school life, study habits cannot be fully separated from sleep and health.","zh":"在學校生活中，學習習慣不能完全與睡眠和健康分開。"},{"en":"If environmental issues challenge state power, ecology and politics become linked.","zh":"如果環境議題挑戰國家權力，生態和政治就會連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two things are closely connected.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩件事密切相關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be passed by","meaning":"獲……通過","examples":[{"en":"A proposal may be passed by the government despite public opposition.","zh":"一項建議可能在公眾反對下仍獲政府通過。"},{"en":"To be passed by a government means to be officially approved or accepted by it.","zh":"To be passed by a government 指由政府正式批准或接受。"},{"en":"A new school rule may be passed by the board after several meetings.","zh":"新校規可能在幾次會議後獲校董會通過。"},{"en":"If a proposal is passed despite opposition, public anger may continue.","zh":"如果建議在反對下仍獲通過，公眾憤怒可能繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal approval by an authority.","zh":"這個片語描述由權威作出正式批准。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與文章資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否與文章資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information means to match what the text says.","zh":"To agree with the information 指與文本所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the passage says the dam was secret, a statement saying it was openly discussed does not agree.","zh":"如果文章說水壩是秘密策劃，而陳述說它被公開討論，就不一致。"},{"en":"If a statement agrees, students should be able to find clear support in the text.","zh":"如果陳述一致，學生應能在文本中找到清楚支持。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in True/False/Not Given reading tasks.","zh":"這個片語用於 True/False/Not Given 閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文章資料相反","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相反。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"To contradict the information 指說出與文本相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the text says the group opposed the dam, a statement saying it supported the dam contradicts it.","zh":"如果文本說該組織反對水壩，而陳述說它支持水壩，就與資料相反。"},{"en":"When information is contradicted, the answer is usually false.","zh":"當資料被相反陳述否定，答案通常是 false。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct disagreement with the passage.","zh":"這個片語描述與文章直接不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students select “NOT GIVEN” when there is no relevant information.","zh":"當文中沒有相關資料時，學生選擇 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not tell us whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"There is no information on this 指文章沒有告訴我們該陳述是真還是假。"},{"en":"If a text describes a protest but not the protesters’ ages, there is no information on their ages.","zh":"如果文本描述示威但沒有說示威者年齡，文中就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from outside knowledge when the text gives no evidence.","zh":"當文本沒有證據時，學生不應用外部知識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the answer cannot be proven from the passage.","zh":"這個片語表示答案不能從文章中證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"predict that","meaning":"預測","examples":[{"en":"Vargha predicted that the dam would damage the environment.","zh":"Vargha 預測水壩會破壞環境。"},{"en":"To predict that something will happen means to say it is likely before it occurs.","zh":"To predict that something will happen 指在某事發生前說它很可能出現。"},{"en":"A teacher may predict that students will find a question difficult after seeing the vocabulary.","zh":"老師看到詞彙後，可能預測學生會覺得題目困難。"},{"en":"If scientists predict environmental damage, planners should examine the risk carefully.","zh":"如果科學家預測環境破壞，規劃者應仔細研究風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a forecast or warning.","zh":"這個片語描述作出預測或警告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"wreck the natural environment","meaning":"嚴重破壞自然環境","examples":[{"en":"The proposed dam could wreck the natural environment.","zh":"擬建水壩可能嚴重破壞自然環境。"},{"en":"To wreck the natural environment means to seriously damage land, water, plants, and animals.","zh":"To wreck the natural environment 指嚴重損害土地、水、植物和動物。"},{"en":"Illegal dumping can wreck the natural environment around a village.","zh":"非法傾倒廢物可以嚴重破壞村莊周圍的自然環境。"},{"en":"If wetlands and water reserves are destroyed, the natural environment may not recover easily.","zh":"如果濕地和地下水儲備被破壞，自然環境可能不容易復原。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severe harm to nature.","zh":"這個片語描述對自然的嚴重傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be managed by","meaning":"由……管理","examples":[{"en":"The project was managed by several state organisations.","zh":"該項目由幾個國家組織管理。"},{"en":"To be managed by someone means to be controlled, organised, or directed by them.","zh":"To be managed by someone 指由某人控制、組織或指導。"},{"en":"A school trip may be managed by teachers and parent volunteers.","zh":"學校旅行可能由老師和家長義工管理。"},{"en":"If a project is managed by state organisations, government priorities may shape its decisions.","zh":"如果項目由國家組織管理，政府優先事項可能塑造其決策。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who controls an activity or project.","zh":"這個片語指出誰控制某活動或項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"unauthorised group","meaning":"未經批准的組織","examples":[{"en":"The Danube Circle operated as an unauthorised group.","zh":"多瑙河圈作為未經批准的組織運作。"},{"en":"An unauthorised group is a group that has not received official permission to exist or act.","zh":"Unauthorised group 是沒有獲得官方許可而存在或行動的團體。"},{"en":"Students may form an unauthorised group chat if the school does not approve it.","zh":"如果學校不批准，學生可能成立未經批准的群組聊天。"},{"en":"If a group is unauthorised under a strict regime, members may face punishment.","zh":"如果團體在嚴格政權下未經批准，成員可能面對懲罰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lack of official approval.","zh":"這個片語描述缺乏官方批准。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"oppose the dam","meaning":"反對興建水壩","examples":[{"en":"The organisation was formed to oppose the dam.","zh":"該組織成立是為了反對興建水壩。"},{"en":"To oppose the dam means to disagree with and campaign against its construction.","zh":"To oppose the dam 指不同意並發起運動反對其興建。"},{"en":"Villagers may oppose a dam if it will flood their homes.","zh":"如果水壩會淹沒家園，村民可能反對興建水壩。"},{"en":"If people oppose a project strongly, they may write articles, sign petitions, and hold meetings.","zh":"如果人們強烈反對某項目，他們可能寫文章、簽署請願和舉行會議。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active resistance to a dam project.","zh":"這個片語描述對水壩項目的積極抵抗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be accepted as","meaning":"被接受為","examples":[{"en":"The authorities did not accept Vargha as an independent editor.","zh":"當局不接受 Vargha 作為獨立編輯。"},{"en":"To be accepted as something means to be recognised or treated in that role or identity.","zh":"To be accepted as something 指被認可或視作某種角色或身份。"},{"en":"A new student may be accepted as a team leader after showing responsibility.","zh":"新學生展現責任感後，可能被接受為隊長。"},{"en":"If a critic is not accepted as independent, their work may be dismissed as political.","zh":"如果批評者不被接受為獨立人士，其工作可能被視為政治性而遭否定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognition by others.","zh":"這個片語描述被他人承認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"embrace environmental ideas","meaning":"接受並支持環保理念","examples":[{"en":"The Charter 77 movement embraced environmental ideas.","zh":"Charter 77 運動接受並支持環保理念。"},{"en":"To embrace environmental ideas means to accept and support beliefs about protecting nature.","zh":"To embrace environmental ideas 指接受並支持關於保護自然的信念。"},{"en":"A school may embrace environmental ideas by reducing waste and saving energy.","zh":"學校可能透過減少廢物和節省能源，接受並支持環保理念。"},{"en":"If a human-rights group embraces environmental ideas, it may connect pollution with citizens’ rights.","zh":"如果人權團體接受環保理念，它可能把污染與市民權利連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active acceptance of green values.","zh":"這個片語描述積極接受綠色價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for the final question.","zh":"學生為最後一題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option that matches the passage.","zh":"To choose the correct letter 指選擇與文章相符的答案選項。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice question, students choose the correct letter after comparing all options.","zh":"在選擇題中，學生比較所有選項後選出正確字母。"},{"en":"If two options seem similar, students should return to the exact wording in the text.","zh":"如果兩個選項看起來相似，學生應回到文本的準確措辭。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"main purpose of","meaning":"……的主要目的","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the main purpose of the Nagymaros Dam.","zh":"題目問 Nagymaros 水壩的主要目的。"},{"en":"The main purpose of something is the most important reason it exists or is planned.","zh":"Main purpose of something 是某事存在或被計劃的最重要原因。"},{"en":"The main purpose of homework should be practice, not punishment.","zh":"功課的主要目的應是練習，而不是懲罰。"},{"en":"If a project has several aims, students must identify the most central one.","zh":"如果項目有幾個目標，學生必須識別最核心的一個。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the primary aim rather than minor benefits.","zh":"這個片語著重主要目的，而不是次要好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be related to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The proposed development was related to energy and transportation.","zh":"擬議發展與能源和交通有關。"},{"en":"To be related to something means to have a connection with it.","zh":"To be related to something 指與某事有連繫。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be related to sleep, diet, and stress.","zh":"學生疲倦可能與睡眠、飲食和壓力有關。"},{"en":"If a dam project is related to energy and transport, it may involve both electricity and shipping.","zh":"如果水壩項目與能源和交通有關，它可能涉及發電和航運。"},{"en":"This phrase shows connection, not always direct cause.","zh":"這個片語顯示關係，而不一定是直接原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"develop a source of electric power","meaning":"開發電力來源","examples":[{"en":"The dam was intended to develop a source of electric power.","zh":"該水壩旨在開發電力來源。"},{"en":"To develop a source of electric power means to create or use a way to produce electricity.","zh":"To develop a source of electric power 指創造或使用一種發電方法。"},{"en":"A village may develop a source of electric power by installing solar panels or a small wind turbine.","zh":"村莊可能透過安裝太陽能板或小型風力渦輪機來開發電力來源。"},{"en":"If a country needs more electricity, it may develop new power sources.","zh":"如果國家需要更多電力，它可能開發新電源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating electricity supply.","zh":"這個片語描述創造電力供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"irrigation and navigation","meaning":"灌溉和航運","examples":[{"en":"The project aimed to improve irrigation and navigation.","zh":"該項目旨在改善灌溉和航運。"},{"en":"Irrigation and navigation mean supplying farmland with water and improving travel by boat or ship.","zh":"Irrigation and navigation 指向農田供水，以及改善船隻航行。"},{"en":"A river project may support irrigation for farms and navigation for cargo boats.","zh":"河流工程可能支持農田灌溉和貨船航運。"},{"en":"If both irrigation and navigation improve, farming and trade may benefit.","zh":"如果灌溉和航運都改善，農業和貿易可能受益。"},{"en":"This phrase combines agricultural water use with water transport.","zh":"這個片語結合農業用水和水上交通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"connect the Black Sea and the Danube","meaning":"連接黑海與多瑙河","examples":[{"en":"The wider plan would improve shipping between the Black Sea and the Danube.","zh":"更廣泛計劃會改善黑海與多瑙河之間的航運。"},{"en":"To connect the Black Sea and the Danube means to create or improve a water route linking them.","zh":"To connect the Black Sea and the Danube 指建立或改善連接黑海與多瑙河的水路。"},{"en":"A canal can connect two waterways so ships can travel farther inland.","zh":"運河可以連接兩條水道，讓船隻駛往更遠內陸。"},{"en":"If the Black Sea and the Danube are better connected, trade routes may expand.","zh":"如果黑海與多瑙河連接得更好，貿易路線可能擴展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a transport link between a sea and a river system.","zh":"這個片語描述海洋與河流系統之間的交通連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"develop a beauty spot","meaning":"發展風景名勝","examples":[{"en":"The original park proposal aimed to develop a local beauty spot.","zh":"最初的公園建議旨在發展本地風景名勝。"},{"en":"To develop a beauty spot means to build facilities or attractions in a scenic place.","zh":"To develop a beauty spot 指在風景優美的地方建設設施或景點。"},{"en":"A council may develop a beauty spot by adding paths, signs, and picnic areas.","zh":"議會可能透過增設步道、指示牌和野餐區來發展風景名勝。"},{"en":"If development is careful, visitors can enjoy the place without damaging it.","zh":"如果發展謹慎，遊客可以享受該地方而不破壞它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improving a scenic area for public use.","zh":"這個片語描述改善風景區以供公眾使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 136 - The Nagymaros Dam.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 137":[{"front":"the discovery of","meaning":"……的發現","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes the discovery of Uranus by Sir William Herschel.","zh":"文章描述威廉・赫歇爾爵士對天王星的發現。"},{"en":"The discovery of something means the act of finding it for the first time.","zh":"the discovery of 某物，指首次找到或發現它這件事。"},{"en":"A student may feel excited about the discovery of a new shortcut to school.","zh":"學生可能因發現一條上學新捷徑而感到興奮。"},{"en":"The discovery of a mistake in a bill can lead to a refund.","zh":"發現帳單中的錯誤可以導致退款。"},{"en":"The phrase usually points to the moment when something unknown becomes known.","zh":"這個短語通常指未知事物變成已知的一刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Uranus","meaning":"天王星","examples":[{"en":"Uranus was discovered by Sir William Herschel in 1781.","zh":"天王星由威廉・赫歇爾爵士於1781年發現。"},{"en":"Uranus is a planet in the solar system beyond Saturn.","zh":"Uranus 是太陽系中位於土星之外的一顆行星。"},{"en":"Students may learn about Uranus when studying the order of the planets in science class.","zh":"學生在科學課學習行星次序時，可能會學到天王星。"},{"en":"Because Uranus is very far from Earth, it cannot be seen clearly without proper equipment.","zh":"因為天王星距離地球很遠，沒有適當設備就不能清楚看見。"},{"en":"The word names a specific planet, not a general type of star.","zh":"這個詞是一顆特定行星的名稱，而不是一般恆星類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"put forward a theory","meaning":"提出理論","examples":[{"en":"Someone once put forward an attractive but unlikely theory.","zh":"曾有人提出一個吸引但不大可能的理論。"},{"en":"To put forward a theory means to suggest an explanation for people to consider.","zh":"put forward a theory 指提出一個解釋供人考慮。"},{"en":"A student may put forward a theory about why plants in one classroom grow faster than others.","zh":"學生可能提出理論，解釋為何某課室的植物比其他課室長得快。"},{"en":"A theory needs evidence, or people may find it interesting but unconvincing.","zh":"理論需要證據，否則人們可能覺得它有趣但欠說服力。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when someone proposes an idea, not when the idea has already been proven.","zh":"這個短語用於某人提出想法時，而不是該想法已被證明時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"attractive though unlikely","meaning":"吸引但不大可能的","examples":[{"en":"The idea was an attractive though unlikely theory.","zh":"這個想法是一個吸引但不大可能的理論。"},{"en":"Attractive though unlikely means appealing or interesting, but not very probable.","zh":"attractive though unlikely 指有吸引力或有趣，但可能性不高。"},{"en":"The idea of finishing all homework in ten minutes is attractive though unlikely.","zh":"十分鐘內完成所有功課這個想法吸引但不大可能。"},{"en":"Some explanations sound pleasant because they are simple, but they may not match the evidence.","zh":"有些解釋因為簡單而聽起來吸引，但未必符合證據。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts emotional appeal with low probability.","zh":"這個短語對比情感吸引力與低可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"throughout the Earth’s annual revolution","meaning":"在地球每年公轉期間","examples":[{"en":"Throughout the Earth’s annual revolution around the sun, one point in space is hidden.","zh":"在地球每年繞太陽公轉期間，太空中有一點被隱藏。"},{"en":"Throughout the Earth’s annual revolution means during the whole year-long movement of Earth around the sun.","zh":"throughout the Earth’s annual revolution 指在地球圍繞太陽一整年運行期間。"},{"en":"Throughout a school year, a student’s progress can be measured by tests, homework and classwork.","zh":"在整個學年期間，學生進步可以透過測驗、功課和課堂表現衡量。"},{"en":"If something remains true throughout a whole cycle, it continues from beginning to end.","zh":"如果某事在整個循環中都成立，它就由開始到結束一直持續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something happening during an entire repeated period.","zh":"這個短語描述某事在整個重複周期中發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"annual revolution around the sun","meaning":"繞太陽的年度公轉","examples":[{"en":"The Earth’s annual revolution around the sun hides one part of its orbit.","zh":"地球繞太陽的年度公轉遮住其軌道的一部分。"},{"en":"Annual revolution around the sun means one complete yearly movement of a planet around the sun.","zh":"annual revolution around the sun 指行星每年圍繞太陽完成一次運行。"},{"en":"In science class, students learn that Earth’s annual revolution around the sun takes about one year.","zh":"在科學課中，學生學到地球繞太陽的年度公轉約需一年。"},{"en":"This movement helps explain seasons and the changing position of stars in the night sky.","zh":"這種運動幫助解釋季節和夜空中星星位置的變化。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to orbital movement, not political revolution.","zh":"這個短語指軌道運行，而不是政治革命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one point in space","meaning":"太空中的一點","examples":[{"en":"There is one point in space that is always hidden from our eyes.","zh":"太空中有一點總是從我們眼前隱藏。"},{"en":"One point in space means one particular position in the universe.","zh":"one point in space 指宇宙中的一個特定位置。"},{"en":"A telescope may be aimed at one point in space to observe a distant star.","zh":"望遠鏡可能指向太空中的一點，以觀察遙遠恆星。"},{"en":"If that point is blocked by a bright object, scientists may not be able to study it directly.","zh":"如果該點被明亮物體遮擋，科學家可能無法直接研究它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a location in space, not a physical dot on paper.","zh":"這個短語描述太空位置，而不是紙上的實體圓點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hidden from our eyes","meaning":"從我們眼前隱藏","examples":[{"en":"The opposite part of the Earth’s orbit is hidden from our eyes.","zh":"地球軌道的相反部分從我們眼前隱藏。"},{"en":"Hidden from our eyes means unable to be seen by us.","zh":"hidden from our eyes 指我們看不見。"},{"en":"A small sign may be hidden from our eyes if a large bus stops in front of it.","zh":"如果一輛大型巴士停在小標誌前，標誌可能從我們眼前隱藏。"},{"en":"When something is hidden, people may need tools or a different position to see it.","zh":"當某物被隱藏，人們可能需要工具或不同位置才能看見它。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on blocked sight.","zh":"這個短語重點在視線被遮擋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the opposite part of","meaning":"……的相反部分","examples":[{"en":"The hidden point is the opposite part of the Earth’s orbit.","zh":"隱藏點是地球軌道的相反部分。"},{"en":"The opposite part of something is the part on the other side from a given position.","zh":"opposite part of 某物，指相對於某位置另一邊的部分。"},{"en":"If the library is at one end of the corridor, the music room may be at the opposite part of it.","zh":"如果圖書館在走廊一端，音樂室可能在其相反部分。"},{"en":"Knowing opposite positions helps people understand layout and direction.","zh":"知道相反位置幫助人理解布局和方向。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a position directly or broadly across from another.","zh":"這個短語描述與另一位置直接或大致相對的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the Earth’s orbit","meaning":"地球軌道","examples":[{"en":"The point lies on the opposite part of the Earth’s orbit.","zh":"該點位於地球軌道的相反部分。"},{"en":"The Earth’s orbit is the path Earth follows as it moves around the sun.","zh":"the Earth’s orbit 是地球圍繞太陽運行時所跟隨的路徑。"},{"en":"Students often draw the Earth’s orbit as an oval around the sun in science lessons.","zh":"學生在科學課中常把地球軌道畫成圍繞太陽的橢圓。"},{"en":"Understanding the Earth’s orbit helps explain why Earth’s position changes during the year.","zh":"理解地球軌道有助解釋地球位置為何一年中會改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to Earth’s path in space.","zh":"這個短語指地球在太空中的路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hidden by the sun","meaning":"被太陽遮住","examples":[{"en":"This point is always hidden by the sun.","zh":"這一點總是被太陽遮住。"},{"en":"Hidden by the sun means blocked from view because the sun is in the way or too bright.","zh":"hidden by the sun 指因太陽在中間或太亮而看不見。"},{"en":"A faint star may be hidden by the sun during the day.","zh":"白天時，微弱星星可能被太陽遮住。"},{"en":"Bright sunlight can make nearby objects in the sky impossible to see.","zh":"強烈陽光可以令天空中附近物體無法看見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visibility being blocked by the sun’s position or brightness.","zh":"這個短語描述可見性被太陽位置或亮度阻擋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"essentially similar to","meaning":"本質上與……相似","examples":[{"en":"The theory imagined another planet essentially similar to our own.","zh":"該理論想像另一顆行星本質上與我們自己的地球相似。"},{"en":"Essentially similar to something means basically the same in important features.","zh":"essentially similar to 某物，指在重要特徵上基本相同。"},{"en":"Two schools may be essentially similar to each other if they have the same subjects, timetable and rules.","zh":"如果兩間學校有相同科目、時間表和規則，它們本質上可能相似。"},{"en":"Small differences may exist, but the main nature is alike.","zh":"小差異可能存在，但主要性質相似。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on basic similarity rather than exact sameness.","zh":"這個短語重點在基本相似，而不是完全相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"our own","meaning":"我們自己的；我們的地球","examples":[{"en":"The hidden world was imagined to be similar to our own.","zh":"那個隱藏世界被想像為與我們自己的地球相似。"},{"en":"Our own means the one that belongs to us or is familiar to us.","zh":"our own 指屬於我們或我們熟悉的那個。"},{"en":"Students may compare another school system with our own to understand the differences.","zh":"學生可能把另一種學校制度與我們自己的制度比較，以理解差異。"},{"en":"People often judge new places by comparing them with their own home or community.","zh":"人們常透過與自己的家或社區比較來判斷新地方。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to something connected with the speaker or group.","zh":"這個短語指回與說話者或群體相關的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"always invisible","meaning":"永遠看不見的","examples":[{"en":"The imagined planet would be always invisible from Earth.","zh":"這顆想像中的行星從地球上會永遠看不見。"},{"en":"Always invisible means impossible to see at all times.","zh":"always invisible 指任何時候都不能被看見。"},{"en":"A password is always invisible on the screen if it appears only as dots.","zh":"如果密碼只顯示為圓點，它在螢幕上就是永遠看不見的。"},{"en":"If something is always invisible, people need indirect evidence to prove it exists.","zh":"如果某物永遠看不見，人們需要間接證據來證明它存在。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses continuous invisibility, not just temporary hiding.","zh":"這個短語強調持續不可見，而不是暫時隱藏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"space probe","meaning":"太空探測器","examples":[{"en":"A space probe could send back evidence of such a world.","zh":"太空探測器可以傳回這樣一個世界的證據。"},{"en":"A space probe is an unmanned spacecraft sent to collect information in space.","zh":"space probe 是被派往太空收集資料的無人太空船。"},{"en":"Scientists may send a space probe to take pictures of a distant planet.","zh":"科學家可能派太空探測器拍攝遙遠行星。"},{"en":"Space probes help humans study places that are too far or dangerous to visit.","zh":"太空探測器幫助人類研究太遠或太危險而不能親自到訪的地方。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a machine used for space exploration.","zh":"這個短語指用於太空探索的機器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"send back evidence","meaning":"傳回證據","examples":[{"en":"A space probe might send back evidence that such a world existed.","zh":"太空探測器可能傳回證據，證明這樣一個世界存在。"},{"en":"To send back evidence means to transmit information or proof from a distant place.","zh":"send back evidence 指從遠方傳送資訊或證據回來。"},{"en":"A robot in a collapsed building may send back evidence that someone is trapped inside.","zh":"倒塌大樓中的機械人可能傳回證據，顯示有人被困在內。"},{"en":"Evidence sent back from a probe can change what scientists believe.","zh":"從探測器傳回的證據可以改變科學家的看法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes returning proof to observers elsewhere.","zh":"這個短語描述把證據傳回給別處的觀察者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"such a world","meaning":"這樣一個世界","examples":[{"en":"The discovery of such a world would cause great excitement.","zh":"發現這樣一個世界會引起極大興奮。"},{"en":"Such a world means a world of the kind just described.","zh":"such a world 指剛描述的那種世界。"},{"en":"If scientists found a planet with oceans and air, such a world would attract huge interest.","zh":"如果科學家找到有海洋和空氣的行星，這樣一個世界會吸引巨大興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase avoids repeating a long description again.","zh":"這個短語避免再次重複長描述。"},{"en":"It points back to an imagined or previously mentioned world.","zh":"它指回想像中或之前提及的世界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cause a sensation","meaning":"引起轟動","examples":[{"en":"Herschel’s discovery of Uranus caused a sensation in 1781.","zh":"赫歇爾發現天王星於1781年引起轟動。"},{"en":"To cause a sensation means to create great excitement, surprise or public attention.","zh":"cause a sensation 指引起極大興奮、驚訝或公眾關注。"},{"en":"A student’s invention may cause a sensation if it solves a problem everyone faces.","zh":"如果學生的發明解決人人面對的問題，可能引起轟動。"},{"en":"New discoveries cause a sensation when they change what people thought was possible.","zh":"當新發現改變人們以為可能的事情，就會引起轟動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong public reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈公眾反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"no more sensation than","meaning":"不會比……更轟動","examples":[{"en":"Such a discovery would cause no more sensation than Herschel’s discovery did.","zh":"這樣的發現不會比赫歇爾的發現更轟動。"},{"en":"No more sensation than means not more excitement or shock than another event caused.","zh":"no more sensation than 指不會比另一事件引起更多興奮或震驚。"},{"en":"A new school rule caused no more sensation than last year’s timetable change did.","zh":"新校規引起的轟動不會比去年的時間表改動更大。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the level of public reaction between two events.","zh":"這個短語比較兩件事的公眾反應程度。"},{"en":"It suggests that the earlier event was already extremely surprising.","zh":"它暗示較早事件已經非常令人驚訝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Sir William Herschel","meaning":"威廉・赫歇爾爵士","examples":[{"en":"Sir William Herschel discovered Uranus in 1781.","zh":"威廉・赫歇爾爵士於1781年發現天王星。"},{"en":"Sir William Herschel was an astronomer known for discovering Uranus.","zh":"Sir William Herschel 是一位以發現天王星聞名的天文學家。"},{"en":"Students may meet his name in science lessons about the history of astronomy.","zh":"學生在關於天文學歷史的科學課中可能見到他的名字。"},{"en":"His discovery mattered because it expanded the known solar system.","zh":"他的發現重要，因為它擴大了人類已知的太陽系。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific historical scientist.","zh":"這個短語是一位特定歷史科學家的名字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"extraordinary man","meaning":"非凡人物","examples":[{"en":"Herschel was an extraordinary man with wide-ranging talents.","zh":"赫歇爾是一位有廣泛才能的非凡人物。"},{"en":"An extraordinary man is a person who is unusually impressive or remarkable.","zh":"extraordinary man 是異常令人敬佩或出色的人。"},{"en":"A teacher who can inspire weak students, organise projects and write books may be called extraordinary.","zh":"如果老師能激勵弱學生、組織項目並寫書，可能被稱為非凡人物。"},{"en":"Extraordinary people often stand out because their achievements go beyond ordinary expectations.","zh":"非凡人物常因成就超出一般期望而突出。"},{"en":"The phrase praises someone as unusually gifted or important.","zh":"這個短語稱讚某人異常有才華或重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cover so vast a field of work","meaning":"涉獵如此廣闊的工作領域","examples":[{"en":"No other astronomer had covered so vast a field of work.","zh":"沒有其他天文學家曾涉獵如此廣闊的工作領域。"},{"en":"To cover so vast a field of work means to study or work across an extremely wide range of topics.","zh":"cover so vast a field of work 指研究或工作範圍極其廣泛。"},{"en":"A journalist covers a vast field of work if she reports on politics, health, education and technology.","zh":"如果記者報道政治、健康、教育和科技，她就涉獵廣闊的工作領域。"},{"en":"Wide work requires energy, curiosity and the ability to learn many things.","zh":"廣泛工作需要精力、好奇心和學習多種事物的能力。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses breadth of achievement.","zh":"這個短語強調成就的廣度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"career deserves study","meaning":"事業生涯值得研究","examples":[{"en":"Herschel’s career deserves study because of his unusual achievements.","zh":"赫歇爾的事業生涯因其不尋常成就而值得研究。"},{"en":"If a career deserves study, it is important enough to examine carefully.","zh":"如果一段事業生涯 deserves study，意思是它重要到值得仔細研究。"},{"en":"A teacher’s career may deserve study if her methods changed how many students learned.","zh":"如果一位老師的方法改變了許多學生學習方式，她的事業生涯可能值得研究。"},{"en":"Studying a remarkable career helps people understand how success developed over time.","zh":"研究非凡事業生涯幫助人理解成功如何隨時間發展。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that someone’s work is historically or educationally valuable.","zh":"這個短語暗示某人的工作具有歷史或教育價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be born in","meaning":"出生於……","examples":[{"en":"Herschel was born in Hanover in Germany in 1738.","zh":"赫歇爾於1738年出生於德國漢諾威。"},{"en":"To be born in a place means to begin life there as a baby.","zh":"be born in 某地，指作為嬰兒在那裏開始生命。"},{"en":"A student may be born in Hong Kong but later move to Canada.","zh":"學生可能出生於香港，但之後搬到加拿大。"},{"en":"Where someone is born can shape early language, culture and opportunities.","zh":"某人出生地可以塑造早期語言、文化和機會。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a person’s birthplace.","zh":"這個短語給出某人的出生地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"leave the army","meaning":"離開軍隊","examples":[{"en":"Herschel left the German army in 1757.","zh":"赫歇爾於1757年離開德國軍隊。"},{"en":"To leave the army means to stop serving as a soldier.","zh":"leave the army 指停止服役，不再當士兵。"},{"en":"A person may leave the army and later train as a teacher or engineer.","zh":"一個人可能離開軍隊後接受教師或工程師訓練。"},{"en":"Leaving the army can change someone’s career path completely.","zh":"離開軍隊可以完全改變某人的事業路向。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ending military service.","zh":"這個短語描述結束軍事服役。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"arrive in England","meaning":"抵達英格蘭","examples":[{"en":"Herschel arrived in England with no money but great musical ability.","zh":"赫歇爾抵達英格蘭時沒有錢，但有卓越音樂才能。"},{"en":"To arrive in England means to reach England after travelling there.","zh":"arrive in England 指經過旅程後到達英格蘭。"},{"en":"A student may arrive in England for university and need time to understand local accents.","zh":"學生可能抵達英格蘭讀大學，並需要時間理解本地口音。"},{"en":"Arriving in a new country can be difficult without money, contacts or secure work.","zh":"沒有金錢、人脈或穩定工作時，到達新國家可能很困難。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the start of someone’s life or journey in England.","zh":"這個短語標誌某人在英格蘭生活或旅程的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"with no money but","meaning":"沒有錢，但有……","examples":[{"en":"He arrived in England with no money but exceptional musical ability.","zh":"他抵達英格蘭時沒有錢，但有出眾音樂才能。"},{"en":"With no money but something means lacking money but possessing another valuable quality or skill.","zh":"with no money but 某物，指沒有錢，但擁有另一種有價值的品質或技能。"},{"en":"A young chef may start a business with no money but strong cooking skills and determination.","zh":"年輕廚師可能沒有錢，但憑強烹飪技巧和決心創業。"},{"en":"Talent can open doors, but lack of money still makes life difficult.","zh":"才能可以打開機會之門，但缺錢仍會令生活困難。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts financial poverty with another strength.","zh":"這個短語對比金錢匱乏與另一項強項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"exceptional musical ability","meaning":"出眾的音樂才能","examples":[{"en":"Herschel had exceptional musical ability.","zh":"赫歇爾有出眾的音樂才能。"},{"en":"Exceptional musical ability means unusually strong skill in playing, understanding or creating music.","zh":"exceptional musical ability 指在演奏、理解或創作音樂方面有異常強的能力。"},{"en":"A child with exceptional musical ability may learn difficult piano pieces very quickly.","zh":"有出眾音樂才能的孩子可能很快學會困難鋼琴曲。"},{"en":"Such ability can lead to professional work if it is supported by training and practice.","zh":"如果有訓練和練習支持，這種才能可以帶來專業工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes talent far above ordinary level.","zh":"這個短語描述遠高於一般水平的才能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"play the violin and oboe","meaning":"拉小提琴和吹雙簧管","examples":[{"en":"Herschel played the violin and oboe professionally.","zh":"赫歇爾專業地拉小提琴和吹雙簧管。"},{"en":"To play the violin and oboe means to perform music using these two instruments.","zh":"play the violin and oboe 指使用這兩種樂器演奏音樂。"},{"en":"A music student may learn to play the violin and oboe for an orchestra exam.","zh":"音樂學生可能為管弦樂考試學習拉小提琴和吹雙簧管。"},{"en":"Learning two instruments requires time, practice and strong listening skills.","zh":"學兩種樂器需要時間、練習和強聆聽能力。"},{"en":"The phrase names specific musical abilities.","zh":"這個短語指出具體音樂能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at one time","meaning":"曾經","examples":[{"en":"At one time, he was organist in the Octagon Chapel.","zh":"他曾經是八角教堂的管風琴師。"},{"en":"At one time means during a particular earlier period.","zh":"at one time 指在較早某段時間。"},{"en":"At one time, the old classroom was used as a library.","zh":"舊課室曾經被用作圖書館。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something was true before, though it may not be true now.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事以前是真的，但現在未必如此。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing past roles or situations.","zh":"它適合描述過去角色或情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"organist","meaning":"管風琴師","examples":[{"en":"Herschel worked as an organist in Bath.","zh":"赫歇爾在巴斯任職管風琴師。"},{"en":"An organist is a musician who plays the organ, often in a church or chapel.","zh":"organist 是演奏管風琴的音樂人，常在教堂或小教堂工作。"},{"en":"A church may hire an organist to play music during services and weddings.","zh":"教堂可能聘請管風琴師在崇拜和婚禮中演奏音樂。"},{"en":"Organists need strong keyboard skills and the ability to follow singers or choirs.","zh":"管風琴師需要強鍵盤技巧，並能配合歌手或合唱團。"},{"en":"The word names a specific musical profession.","zh":"這個詞指出一種特定音樂職業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Octagon Chapel","meaning":"八角教堂","examples":[{"en":"Herschel was once organist in the Octagon Chapel.","zh":"赫歇爾曾是八角教堂的管風琴師。"},{"en":"Octagon Chapel was a chapel where Herschel worked as a musician.","zh":"Octagon Chapel 是赫歇爾曾以音樂人身份工作的教堂。"},{"en":"A chapel is a smaller place of worship than many large churches.","zh":"chapel 是比許多大型教堂較小的禮拜場所。"},{"en":"Working in such a chapel gave Herschel a professional musical role before his astronomy career.","zh":"在這樣的教堂工作，讓赫歇爾在天文事業前有專業音樂職位。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific historical location.","zh":"這個短語指出一個特定歷史地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"active mind","meaning":"活躍的頭腦","examples":[{"en":"Herschel had an active mind and read widely.","zh":"赫歇爾有活躍的頭腦，並廣泛閱讀。"},{"en":"An active mind is a mind that is curious, alert and eager to learn.","zh":"active mind 是好奇、敏銳並渴望學習的頭腦。"},{"en":"A student with an active mind asks questions even after the lesson ends.","zh":"有活躍頭腦的學生即使下課後仍會提問。"},{"en":"An active mind can lead people to explore new subjects and change direction in life.","zh":"活躍頭腦可以令人探索新科目並改變人生方向。"},{"en":"The phrase praises mental energy and curiosity.","zh":"這個短語稱讚思想活力和好奇心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"deep inside","meaning":"內心深處","examples":[{"en":"Deep inside, he knew that music was not his destiny.","zh":"內心深處，他知道音樂不是他的命運。"},{"en":"Deep inside means in one’s true private feelings or inner thoughts.","zh":"deep inside 指在一個人真正私密的感受或內心想法中。"},{"en":"A student may smile in class, but deep inside she may know she is worried about the exam.","zh":"學生可能在課堂上微笑，但內心深處知道自己擔心考試。"},{"en":"People sometimes hide outer confidence while feeling uncertain inside.","zh":"人們有時外表自信，內心卻感到不確定。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a person’s inner truth.","zh":"這個短語指出一個人的內在真實感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be conscious that","meaning":"意識到","examples":[{"en":"He was conscious that music was not his destiny.","zh":"他意識到音樂不是他的命運。"},{"en":"To be conscious that something is true means to be aware of it.","zh":"be conscious that 某事為真，指意識到它。"},{"en":"A student may be conscious that she needs more practice before the speaking exam.","zh":"學生可能意識到自己在口試前需要更多練習。"},{"en":"Awareness of a problem can push someone to make a different choice.","zh":"意識到問題可以推動某人作出不同選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase describes clear inner awareness.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚的內在覺察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not one’s destiny","meaning":"不是某人的命運","examples":[{"en":"Herschel felt that music was not his destiny.","zh":"赫歇爾覺得音樂不是他的命運。"},{"en":"If something is not one’s destiny, it does not feel like the final path or purpose of one’s life.","zh":"如果某事 not one’s destiny，意思是它不像是某人人生最終道路或目的。"},{"en":"A student may enjoy drawing but feel that art is not her destiny as a career.","zh":"學生可能喜歡畫畫，但覺得藝術不是她作為職業的命運。"},{"en":"Realising this can lead people to explore a new field.","zh":"意識到這一點可以令人探索新領域。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a deeper sense of life direction.","zh":"這個短語暗示更深層的人生方向感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"read widely in","meaning":"廣泛閱讀……","examples":[{"en":"He read widely in science and the arts.","zh":"他廣泛閱讀科學與藝術。"},{"en":"To read widely in a subject means to read many different books or materials about it.","zh":"read widely in 某科目，指閱讀許多關於它的不同書籍或材料。"},{"en":"A student who reads widely in history may understand events from several viewpoints.","zh":"廣泛閱讀歷史的學生可能從多個角度理解事件。"},{"en":"Reading widely builds background knowledge and helps people connect ideas.","zh":"廣泛閱讀建立背景知識，並幫助人連接想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad and serious reading.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛而認真的閱讀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"science and the arts","meaning":"科學與藝術","examples":[{"en":"Herschel read widely in science and the arts.","zh":"赫歇爾廣泛閱讀科學與藝術。"},{"en":"Science and the arts means fields such as scientific study, music, literature and visual creativity.","zh":"science and the arts 指科學研究、音樂、文學和視覺創作等領域。"},{"en":"A school with strong science and the arts gives students both experiments and creative expression.","zh":"一所重視科學與藝術的學校，會給學生實驗和創意表達。"},{"en":"Studying both areas can make a person more flexible and imaginative.","zh":"同時研究兩個領域可以令人更靈活和有想像力。"},{"en":"The phrase joins analytical and creative fields together.","zh":"這個短語把分析性和創造性領域結合起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not until…did…","meaning":"直到……才……","examples":[{"en":"Not until 1772 did Herschel come across a book on astronomy.","zh":"直到1772年，赫歇爾才偶然發現一本關於天文學的書。"},{"en":"Not until…did… is an inverted structure used to stress that something happened only after a certain time.","zh":"not until…did… 是倒裝結構，用來強調某事只在某時間之後才發生。"},{"en":"Not until the teacher explained the diagram did the class understand the process.","zh":"直到老師解釋圖表，全班才理解該過程。"},{"en":"This structure makes the delay sound more important or dramatic.","zh":"這個結構令延遲聽起來更重要或更具戲劇性。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and common in careful writing.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常見於嚴謹寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"come across","meaning":"偶然發現","examples":[{"en":"Herschel came across a book on astronomy in 1772.","zh":"赫歇爾於1772年偶然發現一本關於天文學的書。"},{"en":"To come across something means to find it by chance.","zh":"come across 某物，指偶然找到它。"},{"en":"A student may come across a useful article while searching online for homework.","zh":"學生做功課上網搜尋時，可能偶然發現一篇有用文章。"},{"en":"Chance discoveries can sometimes change a person’s interests or plans.","zh":"偶然發現有時可以改變一個人的興趣或計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase describes accidental finding, not planned searching.","zh":"這個短語描述意外找到，而不是有計劃搜尋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a book on astronomy","meaning":"一本關於天文學的書","examples":[{"en":"A book on astronomy changed the direction of Herschel’s life.","zh":"一本關於天文學的書改變了赫歇爾的人生方向。"},{"en":"A book on astronomy is a book about stars, planets and the universe.","zh":"book on astronomy 是關於恆星、行星和宇宙的書。"},{"en":"A student may borrow a book on astronomy after seeing a bright planet in the night sky.","zh":"學生在夜空看見明亮行星後，可能借一本關於天文學的書。"},{"en":"Reading one powerful book can open a new subject and inspire years of study.","zh":"閱讀一本有力量的書可以打開新科目，並啟發多年研究。"},{"en":"The phrase names reading material about the science of space.","zh":"這個短語指出關於太空科學的閱讀材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"by the standards of the time","meaning":"以當時標準來說","examples":[{"en":"At 34, Herschel was middle-aged by the standards of the time.","zh":"以當時標準來說，34歲的赫歇爾已屬中年。"},{"en":"By the standards of the time means judged according to what was normal in that historical period.","zh":"by the standards of the time 指按照該歷史時期的正常標準來判斷。"},{"en":"By the standards of the time, a journey of several days by horse was considered ordinary.","zh":"以當時標準來說，騎馬幾天的旅程被視為普通。"},{"en":"Standards change, so the same age or behaviour may be viewed differently today.","zh":"標準會改變，所以同一年齡或行為今天可能被不同看待。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds readers to judge something in its historical context.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者在歷史背景中判斷某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"without hesitation","meaning":"毫不猶豫","examples":[{"en":"Herschel embarked on his new career without hesitation.","zh":"赫歇爾毫不猶豫地開始新的事業。"},{"en":"Without hesitation means immediately and confidently, without delay or doubt.","zh":"without hesitation 指立即且有信心地行動，沒有拖延或懷疑。"},{"en":"A student may answer without hesitation if she knows the topic very well.","zh":"如果學生非常熟悉題目，她可能毫不猶豫地回答。"},{"en":"People act without hesitation when they feel sure about the next step.","zh":"當人們確定下一步時，就會毫不猶豫地行動。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses quick and confident action.","zh":"這個短語強調快速而有信心的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"embark on","meaning":"開始從事","examples":[{"en":"He embarked on a new career in astronomy.","zh":"他開始從事天文學新事業。"},{"en":"To embark on something means to begin a new activity, journey or project.","zh":"embark on 某事，指開始新的活動、旅程或項目。"},{"en":"A graduate may embark on a teaching career after years of tutoring younger students.","zh":"畢業生可能在多年輔導低年級學生後，開始從事教學事業。"},{"en":"Starting something new often requires planning, courage and patience.","zh":"開始新事物通常需要計劃、勇氣和耐性。"},{"en":"The phrase is slightly formal and often used for major beginnings.","zh":"這個短語稍正式，常用於重大開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"finance something by","meaning":"透過……資助某事","examples":[{"en":"Herschel financed his astronomical work by his professional work as a musician.","zh":"赫歇爾透過作為音樂家的專業工作資助自己的天文工作。"},{"en":"To finance something by an activity means to pay for it using money earned from that activity.","zh":"finance something by 某活動，指用從該活動賺來的錢支付某事。"},{"en":"A student may finance her study trip by working part-time at a café.","zh":"學生可能透過在咖啡店兼職資助自己的遊學團。"},{"en":"If a project has no outside funding, people may need another job to support it.","zh":"如果項目沒有外部資金，人們可能需要另一份工作來支持它。"},{"en":"The phrase links a source of money with what it pays for.","zh":"這個短語把金錢來源與其支付對象連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"professional work","meaning":"專業工作","examples":[{"en":"His professional work as a musician paid for his scientific ambitions.","zh":"他作為音樂家的專業工作支付了他的科學抱負。"},{"en":"Professional work is paid work done with skill, training or recognised expertise.","zh":"professional work 是以技能、訓練或公認專長完成的有薪工作。"},{"en":"A nurse’s professional work includes patient care, record keeping and communication with doctors.","zh":"護士的專業工作包括照顧病人、記錄資料和與醫生溝通。"},{"en":"Professional work can provide income and also build discipline.","zh":"專業工作可以提供收入，也可以建立紀律。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to serious paid work, not a casual hobby.","zh":"這個短語指認真的有薪工作，而不是隨意興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"master the art of","meaning":"掌握……的技藝","examples":[{"en":"He spent years mastering the art of telescope construction.","zh":"他花了多年掌握望遠鏡製造的技藝。"},{"en":"To master the art of something means to become highly skilled at doing it.","zh":"master the art of 某事，指在做該事方面變得非常熟練。"},{"en":"A baker may spend years mastering the art of making soft bread.","zh":"麵包師可能花多年掌握製作鬆軟麵包的技藝。"},{"en":"Mastery usually comes from repeated practice, mistakes and improvement.","zh":"精通通常來自反覆練習、犯錯和改進。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests deep skill, not basic familiarity.","zh":"這個短語暗示深厚技巧，而不是基本熟悉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"telescope construction","meaning":"望遠鏡製造","examples":[{"en":"Herschel became highly skilled in telescope construction.","zh":"赫歇爾在望遠鏡製造方面變得非常熟練。"},{"en":"Telescope construction is the process of designing and building telescopes.","zh":"telescope construction 是設計和建造望遠鏡的過程。"},{"en":"A science club may learn basic telescope construction by assembling lenses and tubes.","zh":"科學學會可能透過組裝鏡片和管筒學習基本望遠鏡製造。"},{"en":"Better telescope construction allows observers to see fainter and more distant objects.","zh":"更好的望遠鏡製造讓觀測者看見更微弱和更遙遠的物體。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the craft and technical work of making telescopes.","zh":"這個短語指製作望遠鏡的工藝和技術工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"by present-day standards","meaning":"以現今標準來說","examples":[{"en":"Even by present-day standards, his instruments were excellent.","zh":"即使以現今標準來說，他的儀器也很出色。"},{"en":"By present-day standards means judged according to today’s level of knowledge, technology or expectation.","zh":"by present-day standards 指按照今天的知識、科技或期望水平來判斷。"},{"en":"By present-day standards, an old computer may seem slow but still impressive for its time.","zh":"以現今標準來說，舊電腦可能顯得慢，但以其時代來說仍令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"The phrase helps compare past achievements with modern expectations.","zh":"這個短語幫助把過去成就與現代期望比較。"},{"en":"It can show that something remains impressive even now.","zh":"它可以顯示某物即使今天仍令人敬佩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"instruments","meaning":"儀器","examples":[{"en":"Herschel’s instruments were comparable with the best.","zh":"赫歇爾的儀器可與最好的媲美。"},{"en":"Instruments are tools or devices used for a particular task, especially scientific or musical work.","zh":"instruments 是用於特定任務的工具或裝置，尤其是科學或音樂工作。"},{"en":"A laboratory needs instruments such as microscopes, scales and thermometers.","zh":"實驗室需要顯微鏡、天平和溫度計等儀器。"},{"en":"Good instruments allow people to measure, observe or perform more accurately.","zh":"良好儀器讓人更準確地量度、觀察或演奏。"},{"en":"The word refers to specialised tools, not just ordinary objects.","zh":"這個詞指專門工具，而不只是普通物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"comparable with the best","meaning":"可與最好的媲美","examples":[{"en":"His telescopes were comparable with the best instruments.","zh":"他的望遠鏡可與最好的儀器媲美。"},{"en":"Comparable with the best means almost as good as the highest-quality examples.","zh":"comparable with the best 指幾乎與最高質素的例子一樣好。"},{"en":"A small school’s debate team may be comparable with the best teams in the city.","zh":"一間小學校的辯論隊可能可與全城最好的隊伍媲美。"},{"en":"When something is comparable with the best, it can compete at a very high level.","zh":"當某物可與最好的媲美，它就能在很高水平競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase praises quality by comparing it with top standards.","zh":"這個短語透過與最高標準比較來稱讚質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"serious observation","meaning":"認真觀測","examples":[{"en":"Serious observation began in 1774.","zh":"認真觀測始於1774年。"},{"en":"Serious observation means careful, systematic watching or recording, especially for study.","zh":"serious observation 指仔細、有系統地觀看或記錄，尤其是為了研究。"},{"en":"A science student begins serious observation when she records plant growth every day.","zh":"科學學生每天記錄植物生長時，就開始認真觀察。"},{"en":"Careful observation can reveal patterns that casual looking would miss.","zh":"仔細觀測可以揭示隨便觀看會錯過的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes disciplined watching, not simple curiosity.","zh":"這個短語描述有紀律的觀察，而不是單純好奇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"set oneself the task of","meaning":"給自己定下……任務","examples":[{"en":"Herschel set himself the task of reviewing the heavens.","zh":"赫歇爾給自己定下巡察天空的任務。"},{"en":"To set oneself the task of doing something means to decide personally to take on that work.","zh":"set oneself the task of doing something 指個人決定承擔該工作。"},{"en":"A student may set herself the task of reading one English article every day.","zh":"學生可能給自己定下每天讀一篇英文文章的任務。"},{"en":"Self-set tasks require discipline because no one else may be forcing the person to do them.","zh":"自我設定的任務需要紀律，因為未必有人逼自己完成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes choosing a demanding goal for oneself.","zh":"這個短語描述為自己選擇一個具挑戰性的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"astonishing task","meaning":"驚人的任務","examples":[{"en":"Reviewing the heavens was an astonishing task.","zh":"巡察天空是一項驚人的任務。"},{"en":"An astonishing task is a task so large, difficult or impressive that it causes surprise.","zh":"astonishing task 是龐大、困難或令人佩服到使人驚訝的任務。"},{"en":"Cleaning an entire school after a flood would be an astonishing task for a small team.","zh":"水浸後由小團隊清理整間學校會是一項驚人的任務。"},{"en":"Such tasks require unusual effort and persistence.","zh":"這類任務需要非一般努力和毅力。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses how remarkable the task is.","zh":"這個短語強調任務多麼非凡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"reviewing the heavens","meaning":"巡察天空","examples":[{"en":"Herschel called his project reviewing the heavens.","zh":"赫歇爾稱他的項目為巡察天空。"},{"en":"Reviewing the heavens means systematically observing the sky and recording what is seen.","zh":"reviewing the heavens 指有系統地觀察天空並記錄所見。"},{"en":"An astronomy club may begin reviewing the heavens by mapping stars visible from the school roof.","zh":"天文學會可能透過繪製學校天台可見星星來開始巡察天空。"},{"en":"A full review takes patience because the sky is vast and changes with time.","zh":"完整巡察需要耐性，因為天空廣闊並會隨時間變化。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a grand name to careful sky observation.","zh":"這個短語給仔細天空觀測一個宏大的名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in other words","meaning":"換言之","examples":[{"en":"In other words, he pointed his telescope at every accessible part of the sky.","zh":"換言之，他把望遠鏡指向每個可觀測的天空部分。"},{"en":"In other words introduces a simpler or clearer way to say the same idea.","zh":"in other words 引出同一想法更簡單或更清楚的說法。"},{"en":"The test checks inference; in other words, students must read between the lines.","zh":"這項測驗考推斷；換言之，學生必須讀懂字裏行間。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain a difficult statement without changing its meaning.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋困難陳述，而不改變其意思。"},{"en":"It is useful when restating an idea for clarity.","zh":"它適合用於為清晰而重述想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"point one’s telescope to","meaning":"將望遠鏡指向……","examples":[{"en":"He pointed his telescope to every accessible part of the sky.","zh":"他將望遠鏡指向每個可觀測的天空部分。"},{"en":"To point one’s telescope to something means to aim the telescope in that direction.","zh":"point one’s telescope to 某物，指把望遠鏡瞄準該方向。"},{"en":"A student may point her telescope to the moon during a school astronomy night.","zh":"學校天文夜中，學生可能將望遠鏡指向月球。"},{"en":"Aiming carefully is important because a small shift can change what appears in the view.","zh":"仔細瞄準很重要，因為小小移動就會改變視野中的物體。"},{"en":"The phrase describes directing an observing instrument.","zh":"這個短語描述指向觀測儀器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"accessible part of the sky","meaning":"可觀測的天空部分","examples":[{"en":"Herschel observed every accessible part of the sky.","zh":"赫歇爾觀察每個可觀測的天空部分。"},{"en":"An accessible part of the sky is a part that can be seen or reached by observation from a given place.","zh":"accessible part of the sky 是從某地可以看見或觀測到的天空部分。"},{"en":"From a city balcony, only a small accessible part of the sky may be visible.","zh":"從城市露台上，可能只有一小部分天空可觀測。"},{"en":"Buildings, weather and daylight can limit what parts of the sky are accessible.","zh":"建築、天氣和日光都可以限制哪些天空部分可被觀測。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the portion that can actually be observed.","zh":"這個短語指實際可以觀察的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"record what one saw","meaning":"記錄所見","examples":[{"en":"Herschel carefully recorded what he saw.","zh":"赫歇爾仔細記錄所見。"},{"en":"To record what one saw means to write down or otherwise save observations.","zh":"record what one saw 指寫下或以其他方式保存觀察結果。"},{"en":"A student records what she saw in a science experiment so she can compare results later.","zh":"學生記錄自己在科學實驗中的所見，以便之後比較結果。"},{"en":"Without records, important details may be forgotten or misremembered.","zh":"沒有記錄，重要細節可能被忘記或記錯。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses careful documentation of observation.","zh":"這個短語強調仔細記錄觀察內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the first review","meaning":"第一次巡察","examples":[{"en":"The first review of the heavens was made in 1775.","zh":"第一次天空巡察於1775年進行。"},{"en":"The first review means the first systematic examination of something.","zh":"first review 指對某事進行的第一次有系統檢查。"},{"en":"A teacher’s first review of students’ essays may focus on structure before grammar.","zh":"老師第一次審閱學生文章時，可能先集中結構再看文法。"},{"en":"A first review creates a starting record for later comparison.","zh":"第一次巡察或檢查會建立起點記錄，以便之後比較。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the earliest organised check or survey.","zh":"這個短語指最早的一次有組織檢查或調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the most momentous","meaning":"最重要的；最具歷史意義的","examples":[{"en":"The second review was the most momentous.","zh":"第二次巡察是最重要的。"},{"en":"The most momentous means the most important because it has great consequences.","zh":"most momentous 指因有重大後果而最重要。"},{"en":"A school’s decision to open free evening classes may be its most momentous change in years.","zh":"學校開設免費晚間課程的決定，可能是多年來最具歷史意義的改變。"},{"en":"Momentous events are remembered because they alter what happens next.","zh":"重大事件會被記住，因為它們改變之後發生的事情。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses historical importance, not just size.","zh":"這個短語強調歷史重要性，而不只是規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"during the latter part of","meaning":"在……的後半部分","examples":[{"en":"Uranus was discovered during the latter part of the second review.","zh":"天王星是在第二次巡察的後半部分被發現的。"},{"en":"During the latter part of something means in the later section or near the end of it.","zh":"during the latter part of 某事，指在其較後部分或接近尾聲時。"},{"en":"During the latter part of the lesson, students practised exam questions.","zh":"在課堂後半部分，學生練習考試題目。"},{"en":"This phrase helps locate an event within a longer period.","zh":"這個短語幫助把事件定位於較長時段之內。"},{"en":"It means not at the beginning, but closer to the end.","zh":"它的意思不是在開始，而是較接近結尾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"royal grant","meaning":"皇家補助金","examples":[{"en":"Herschel was supported by a royal grant after his discovery.","zh":"赫歇爾在發現後得到皇家補助金支持。"},{"en":"A royal grant is money or support given by a king, queen or royal authority.","zh":"royal grant 是由國王、女王或皇家權威給予的金錢或支持。"},{"en":"An artist might receive a grant that allows her to work without another job.","zh":"藝術家可能獲得補助金，使她不用做另一份工作也能創作。"},{"en":"Financial support can give researchers time to focus fully on their work.","zh":"財政支持可以給研究人員時間全心專注於工作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to official support from royalty.","zh":"這個短語指來自王室的官方支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in recognition of","meaning":"為表揚……","examples":[{"en":"The grant was given in recognition of his work.","zh":"該補助金是為表揚他的工作而給予的。"},{"en":"In recognition of something means as an official or public acknowledgement of its value.","zh":"in recognition of 某事，指作為對其價值的官方或公開承認。"},{"en":"A school may give a prize in recognition of a student’s service to classmates.","zh":"學校可能頒獎以表揚學生對同學的服務。"},{"en":"Recognition can encourage people by showing that their effort is valued.","zh":"表揚可以透過顯示努力受到重視來鼓勵人。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why an honour, reward or support is given.","zh":"這個短語解釋榮譽、獎勵或支持為何被給予。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"devote oneself entirely to","meaning":"全心投入……","examples":[{"en":"Herschel was able to devote himself entirely to astronomy.","zh":"赫歇爾得以全心投入天文學。"},{"en":"To devote oneself entirely to something means to give all one’s time and energy to it.","zh":"devote oneself entirely to 某事，指把所有時間和精力投放於它。"},{"en":"A student may devote herself entirely to exam preparation during the final month.","zh":"學生可能在最後一個月全心投入備考。"},{"en":"Full devotion is easier when financial pressure or other duties are reduced.","zh":"當經濟壓力或其他職責減少，全心投入會較容易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes complete commitment.","zh":"這個短語描述完全投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"final achievements","meaning":"最後成就","examples":[{"en":"His final achievements ranged across many areas of astronomy.","zh":"他的最後成就橫跨天文學許多領域。"},{"en":"Final achievements are the major accomplishments someone reaches by the later stage of a career or life.","zh":"final achievements 是某人在事業或人生較後階段達到的重要成就。"},{"en":"A teacher’s final achievements may include textbooks, trained students and a stronger school programme.","zh":"老師的最後成就可能包括教材、培訓出的學生和更強的學校課程。"},{"en":"Looking at final achievements helps people judge the full impact of a life’s work.","zh":"查看最後成就幫助人評估畢生工作的整體影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to later or overall accomplishments.","zh":"這個短語指較後期或整體成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"spread from…to…","meaning":"從……延伸至……","examples":[{"en":"His achievements spread from the sun and moon to remote galaxies.","zh":"他的成就從太陽和月球延伸至遙遠星系。"},{"en":"Spread from A to B means extend across a wide range, beginning with one area and reaching another.","zh":"spread from A to B 指由一個範圍開始，延伸到另一個範圍。"},{"en":"A school project may spread from recycling paper to reducing food waste.","zh":"學校項目可能由回收紙張延伸至減少食物浪費。"},{"en":"When work spreads across many areas, it shows broad influence.","zh":"當工作延伸至許多範疇，它顯示廣泛影響。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights range and expansion.","zh":"這個短語突出範圍和擴展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"remote galaxies","meaning":"遙遠星系","examples":[{"en":"Herschel discovered hundreds of remote galaxies.","zh":"赫歇爾發現數百個遙遠星系。"},{"en":"Remote galaxies are very distant systems of stars far beyond our own galaxy.","zh":"remote galaxies 是遠在我們銀河系以外的恆星系統。"},{"en":"Students may see pictures of remote galaxies taken by powerful telescopes.","zh":"學生可能看到由強大望遠鏡拍攝的遙遠星系照片。"},{"en":"Because remote galaxies are extremely far away, their light can take millions of years to reach us.","zh":"因為遙遠星系極遠，它們的光可能要數百萬年才到達我們。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to distant star systems in space.","zh":"這個短語指太空中的遙遠恆星系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"papers flooded from his pen","meaning":"文章源源不絕地出自他的筆下","examples":[{"en":"Papers flooded from Herschel’s pen until his death.","zh":"直到去世，文章都源源不絕地出自赫歇爾的筆下。"},{"en":"Papers flooded from his pen means he wrote and produced many papers continuously.","zh":"papers flooded from his pen 指他連續寫出和發表大量文章。"},{"en":"A hardworking researcher may produce articles so regularly that papers seem to flood from her pen.","zh":"勤奮研究人員可能定期產出文章，令人覺得作品源源不絕地出自她筆下。"},{"en":"The image suggests great productivity and constant writing.","zh":"這個意象暗示極高產量和持續寫作。"},{"en":"The phrase is figurative, not about actual water or ink flooding.","zh":"這個短語是比喻，不是真的有水或墨水氾濫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the Royal Society","meaning":"皇家學會","examples":[{"en":"Herschel sent a paper to the Royal Society in 1781.","zh":"赫歇爾於1781年向皇家學會提交一篇論文。"},{"en":"The Royal Society is a famous scientific organisation in Britain.","zh":"the Royal Society 是英國著名科學組織。"},{"en":"A scientist may send research to a learned society so other experts can read it.","zh":"科學家可能向學術團體提交研究，讓其他專家閱讀。"},{"en":"Sharing findings with such organisations helps new discoveries become known.","zh":"與這類組織分享發現，幫助新發現被人知道。"},{"en":"The phrase names an important institution in scientific history.","zh":"這個短語指出科學史上一個重要機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"entitled","meaning":"題為","examples":[{"en":"He sent a paper entitled An Account of a Comet.","zh":"他提交了一篇題為《一顆彗星的記述》的論文。"},{"en":"Entitled means having the title named after it.","zh":"entitled 指有某個標題。"},{"en":"A student may submit an essay entitled “The Future of Public Transport.”","zh":"學生可能提交一篇題為《公共交通的未來》的文章。"},{"en":"A clear title helps readers know what a piece of writing is about.","zh":"清楚標題幫助讀者知道文章內容。"},{"en":"The word is used to introduce the name of a book, article or paper.","zh":"這個詞用來引出書、文章或論文的名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"An Account of a Comet","meaning":"《一顆彗星的記述》","examples":[{"en":"Herschel’s paper was entitled An Account of a Comet.","zh":"赫歇爾的論文題為《一顆彗星的記述》。"},{"en":"An Account of a Comet was the title of Herschel’s paper about the object he first thought was a comet.","zh":"An Account of a Comet 是赫歇爾關於他最初以為是彗星的物體的論文標題。"},{"en":"A scientific paper title often tells readers what observation or discovery it reports.","zh":"科學論文標題常告訴讀者它報告甚麼觀察或發現。"},{"en":"If the title is cautious, it may show that the writer is not yet ready to make a bold claim.","zh":"如果標題謹慎，可能顯示作者尚未準備作出大膽聲稱。"},{"en":"The phrase is a specific title, not a general expression.","zh":"這個短語是一個特定標題，而不是一般表達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in his own words","meaning":"用他自己的話來說","examples":[{"en":"The passage then gives the discovery in Herschel’s own words.","zh":"文章接着用赫歇爾自己的話描述這項發現。"},{"en":"In his own words means using the exact or personal way he expressed the idea.","zh":"in his own words 指使用他確切或個人的表達方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask a student to explain a poem in his own words.","zh":"老師可能要求學生用自己的話解釋詩歌。"},{"en":"Using someone’s own words can make a report feel more direct and authentic.","zh":"使用某人自己的話可以令報告更直接和真實。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on personal expression rather than a summary by others.","zh":"這個短語重點在個人表達，而不是他人的摘要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"examine the small stars","meaning":"觀察細小星體","examples":[{"en":"Herschel was examining the small stars near H Geminorum.","zh":"赫歇爾正在觀察雙子座 H 星附近的細小星體。"},{"en":"To examine the small stars means to look carefully at faint or small-looking stars through observation.","zh":"examine the small stars 指透過觀測仔細查看微弱或看似細小的星體。"},{"en":"A student using a telescope may examine small stars beside the moon.","zh":"使用望遠鏡的學生可能觀察月球旁的細小星體。"},{"en":"Careful examination can reveal that one object is not like the others.","zh":"仔細觀察可以揭示某個物體與其他不同。"},{"en":"The phrase describes detailed astronomical observation.","zh":"這個短語描述詳細天文觀測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the neighbourhood of","meaning":"在……附近","examples":[{"en":"He examined stars in the neighbourhood of H Geminorum.","zh":"他觀察雙子座 H 星附近的星體。"},{"en":"In the neighbourhood of means near or around a particular place or object.","zh":"in the neighbourhood of 指在某地方或物體附近或周圍。"},{"en":"A student may look for a café in the neighbourhood of the university.","zh":"學生可能在大學附近尋找咖啡店。"},{"en":"Searching near a known place helps narrow down a large area.","zh":"在已知地方附近搜尋，有助縮小大範圍。"},{"en":"The phrase describes approximate closeness.","zh":"這個短語描述大約接近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"H Geminorum","meaning":"雙子座 H 星","examples":[{"en":"Herschel observed stars near H Geminorum.","zh":"赫歇爾觀察雙子座 H 星附近的星體。"},{"en":"H Geminorum is the name of a star used as a reference point in the passage.","zh":"H Geminorum 是文章中用作參考點的一顆星的名稱。"},{"en":"Astronomers often use named stars to describe where another object appears in the sky.","zh":"天文學家常使用有名稱的星體來描述另一物體在天空中的位置。"},{"en":"A reference star helps observers compare size, brightness or position.","zh":"參考星幫助觀測者比較大小、亮度或位置。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific astronomical object.","zh":"這個短語指出一個特定天體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"perceive one","meaning":"察覺到一個","examples":[{"en":"Herschel perceived one star that appeared larger than the rest.","zh":"赫歇爾察覺到一顆看起來比其餘更大的星。"},{"en":"To perceive one means to notice or become aware of one particular object.","zh":"perceive one 指注意到或意識到一個特定物體。"},{"en":"A teacher may perceive one student looking confused while others seem confident.","zh":"老師可能察覺到一名學生看起來困惑，而其他人似乎有信心。"},{"en":"Careful perception helps people notice details that others overlook.","zh":"仔細察覺幫助人注意到其他人忽略的細節。"},{"en":"The phrase describes noticing one item among many.","zh":"這個短語描述在許多事物中注意到其中一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"visibly larger than","meaning":"明顯比……大","examples":[{"en":"One object appeared visibly larger than the rest.","zh":"一個物體看起來明顯比其餘更大。"},{"en":"Visibly larger than means clearly bigger in appearance than something else.","zh":"visibly larger than 指外觀上清楚比另一物更大。"},{"en":"One suitcase may be visibly larger than the others at the airport check-in counter.","zh":"在機場登記櫃檯，一個行李箱可能明顯比其他更大。"},{"en":"A visible difference in size can make observers look more carefully.","zh":"可見的大小差異可以令觀測者更仔細查看。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a size difference that can be seen.","zh":"這個短語描述看得見的大小差別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be struck with","meaning":"被……震撼","examples":[{"en":"Herschel was struck with the object’s uncommon magnitude.","zh":"赫歇爾被該物體非尋常的大小震撼。"},{"en":"To be struck with something means to be strongly impressed or surprised by it.","zh":"be struck with 某事，指被它強烈打動或驚訝。"},{"en":"A visitor may be struck with the silence inside a large library.","zh":"訪客可能被大型圖書館內的寧靜震撼。"},{"en":"Strong impressions often make people stop and pay closer attention.","zh":"強烈印象常令人停下來並更仔細注意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a sudden feeling of being impressed.","zh":"這個短語描述突然被打動的感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"uncommon magnitude","meaning":"非尋常的大小","examples":[{"en":"The object had uncommon magnitude compared with nearby stars.","zh":"與附近星體相比，該物體有非尋常的大小。"},{"en":"Uncommon magnitude means an unusual size, brightness or importance, depending on context.","zh":"uncommon magnitude 視乎語境可指不尋常的大小、亮度或重要性。"},{"en":"A problem of uncommon magnitude may require help from the whole school, not just one teacher.","zh":"非尋常規模的問題可能需要全校協助，而不只是一位老師。"},{"en":"When something is unusually large or striking, people naturally investigate it further.","zh":"當某事異常大或突出，人們自然會進一步調查。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the scale is not ordinary.","zh":"這個短語強調規模並不普通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"compare it to","meaning":"將它與……比較","examples":[{"en":"He compared the object to H Geminorum.","zh":"他將該物體與雙子座 H 星比較。"},{"en":"To compare it to something means to examine similarities or differences between the two.","zh":"compare it to 某物，指檢視兩者之間的相似或差異。"},{"en":"A student may compare one essay to another to see which has clearer examples.","zh":"學生可能將一篇文章與另一篇比較，以看哪一篇例子更清楚。"},{"en":"Comparison helps people judge size, quality, position or importance.","zh":"比較幫助人判斷大小、質素、位置或重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using one thing as a reference for another.","zh":"這個短語描述用一物作另一物的參考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"suspect it to be","meaning":"懷疑它是……","examples":[{"en":"Herschel suspected the object to be a comet.","zh":"赫歇爾懷疑該物體是一顆彗星。"},{"en":"To suspect it to be something means to think it may be that thing without being certain.","zh":"suspect it to be 某物，指認為它可能是該物，但未能確定。"},{"en":"A teacher may suspect a student’s answer to be copied if it is exactly the same as another one.","zh":"如果學生答案與另一人完全相同，老師可能懷疑它是抄襲的。"},{"en":"Suspicion needs further evidence before it becomes a conclusion.","zh":"懷疑需要進一步證據，才會成為結論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a cautious guess.","zh":"這個短語描述謹慎推測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hallmark of","meaning":"……的標誌","examples":[{"en":"Herschel’s care was the hallmark of a great observer.","zh":"赫歇爾的謹慎是偉大觀測者的標誌。"},{"en":"A hallmark of something is a clear sign or typical feature of it.","zh":"hallmark of 某事，是它的清楚標誌或典型特徵。"},{"en":"Clear explanations are a hallmark of a good teacher.","zh":"清楚解釋是好老師的標誌。"},{"en":"When a quality appears repeatedly, it can become the feature people recognise most.","zh":"當某種品質反覆出現，它可以成為人們最認得的特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a defining sign of excellence or character.","zh":"這個短語指出卓越或性格的定義性標誌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"great observer","meaning":"偉大的觀測者","examples":[{"en":"Herschel was a great observer because he was careful.","zh":"赫歇爾是一位偉大觀測者，因為他很謹慎。"},{"en":"A great observer is someone who notices details accurately and records them carefully.","zh":"great observer 是能準確注意細節並仔細記錄的人。"},{"en":"A doctor must be a good observer to notice small changes in a patient’s condition.","zh":"醫生必須善於觀察，才能注意到病人狀況的細微變化。"},{"en":"Careful observation can prevent wrong conclusions.","zh":"仔細觀察可以防止錯誤結論。"},{"en":"The phrase praises skill in noticing and interpreting what is seen.","zh":"這個短語稱讚注意和解讀所見的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be prepared to","meaning":"準備好去……","examples":[{"en":"He was not prepared to jump to conclusions.","zh":"他並不準備草率下結論。"},{"en":"To be prepared to do something means to be ready or willing to do it.","zh":"be prepared to do something 指準備好或願意做某事。"},{"en":"A student should be prepared to explain her answer if the teacher asks why.","zh":"如果老師問原因，學生應準備好解釋自己的答案。"},{"en":"Being prepared often means having enough confidence, evidence or materials.","zh":"準備好通常意味著有足夠信心、證據或材料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes readiness or willingness.","zh":"這個短語描述準備程度或意願。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"jump to conclusions","meaning":"草率下結論","examples":[{"en":"Herschel was not prepared to jump to conclusions.","zh":"赫歇爾不準備草率下結論。"},{"en":"To jump to conclusions means to decide something too quickly without enough evidence.","zh":"jump to conclusions 指在沒有足夠證據下太快作出判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher should not jump to conclusions when a student is late once.","zh":"當學生只遲到一次，老師不應草率下結論。"},{"en":"Quick judgement can be unfair if important facts are still missing.","zh":"如果重要事實仍缺失，快速判斷可能不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against careless or premature decisions.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要粗心或過早作決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"to be fair","meaning":"公平地說","examples":[{"en":"To be fair, the discovery of a new planet was unexpected.","zh":"公平地說，發現一顆新行星是意料之外的事。"},{"en":"To be fair means to make a balanced point before judging someone or something.","zh":"to be fair 指在判斷某人或某事前提出平衡觀點。"},{"en":"To be fair, the student made mistakes, but the question was also badly worded.","zh":"公平地說，學生犯了錯，但題目本身也寫得不好。"},{"en":"This phrase helps soften criticism by acknowledging another side.","zh":"這個短語透過承認另一面來軟化批評。"},{"en":"It is used when the speaker wants to be reasonable.","zh":"它用於說話者想顯得合理時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the last thought in anybody’s mind","meaning":"誰也沒想到的事","examples":[{"en":"The discovery of a new planet was the last thought in anybody’s mind.","zh":"發現一顆新行星是誰也沒想到的事。"},{"en":"The last thought in anybody’s mind means something nobody expected or considered likely.","zh":"the last thought in anybody’s mind 指沒有人預期或認為可能的事。"},{"en":"During a sunny morning, a sudden flood was the last thought in anybody’s mind.","zh":"在陽光明媚的早上，突然水浸是誰也沒想到的事。"},{"en":"When something is completely unexpected, people may fail to prepare for it.","zh":"當某事完全出乎意料，人們可能沒有準備。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses extreme surprise.","zh":"這個短語強調極度意外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"further observation","meaning":"進一步觀測","examples":[{"en":"Further observation revealed two curious facts.","zh":"進一步觀測揭示了兩個奇怪事實。"},{"en":"Further observation means additional careful watching or study after the first look.","zh":"further observation 指第一次觀看後的額外仔細觀察或研究。"},{"en":"A doctor may need further observation before deciding whether a patient can leave hospital.","zh":"醫生可能需要進一步觀察，才決定病人是否可以出院。"},{"en":"More observation can confirm, correct or deepen an early impression.","zh":"更多觀察可以確認、修正或深化早期印象。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continuing to examine something.","zh":"這個短語描述繼續檢視某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"besides Herschel","meaning":"除了赫歇爾之外","examples":[{"en":"Other astronomers besides Herschel observed the object.","zh":"除了赫歇爾之外，其他天文學家也觀察了該物體。"},{"en":"Besides Herschel means in addition to Herschel.","zh":"besides Herschel 指除了赫歇爾之外。"},{"en":"Besides the class teacher, the school counsellor also spoke to the student.","zh":"除了班主任之外，學校輔導員也與該學生談話。"},{"en":"Mentioning others besides one person shows that more than one observer was involved.","zh":"提到除某人以外的人，顯示涉及不止一名觀察者。"},{"en":"The phrase adds extra people to the statement.","zh":"這個短語為陳述加入額外人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"reveal curious facts","meaning":"揭示奇怪事實","examples":[{"en":"The observations revealed two curious facts.","zh":"觀測揭示了兩個奇怪事實。"},{"en":"To reveal curious facts means to show unusual or interesting pieces of information.","zh":"reveal curious facts 指顯示不尋常或有趣的資訊。"},{"en":"A survey may reveal curious facts about how students actually revise at home.","zh":"調查可能揭示學生在家實際如何溫習的奇怪事實。"},{"en":"Curious facts can lead researchers to ask new questions.","zh":"奇怪事實可以令研究人員提出新問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes discovery of surprising details.","zh":"這個短語描述發現令人驚訝的細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"remarkably sharp disc","meaning":"異常清晰的圓盤","examples":[{"en":"The object showed a remarkably sharp disc.","zh":"該物體顯示出異常清晰的圓盤。"},{"en":"A remarkably sharp disc is a very clear round shape seen through observation.","zh":"remarkably sharp disc 是透過觀察看見的非常清楚圓形。"},{"en":"Through a good telescope, the moon may show a remarkably sharp edge.","zh":"透過好望遠鏡，月球可能顯示出異常清晰的邊緣。"},{"en":"A clear disc can suggest that the object is not an ordinary point-like star.","zh":"清楚圓盤可能暗示該物體不是普通點狀恆星。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strikingly clear circular appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述非常清晰的圓形外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"furthermore","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"Furthermore, the object was moving very slowly.","zh":"此外，該物體移動得非常緩慢。"},{"en":"Furthermore means in addition, and it adds another point to support the idea.","zh":"furthermore 指此外，並加入另一點來支持想法。"},{"en":"The school library is quiet; furthermore, it has many useful reference books.","zh":"學校圖書館很安靜；此外，它有許多有用參考書。"},{"en":"This word helps writers build an argument by adding evidence.","zh":"這個字幫助寫作者透過加入證據建立論點。"},{"en":"It is more formal than “also.”","zh":"它比 “also” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"move so slowly that","meaning":"移動得如此緩慢以致……","examples":[{"en":"The object was moving so slowly that it seemed far from the sun.","zh":"該物體移動得如此緩慢，以致它似乎距離太陽很遠。"},{"en":"Move so slowly that means move at such a low speed that a certain result or conclusion follows.","zh":"move so slowly that 指移動速度低到導致某結果或結論。"},{"en":"The bus moved so slowly that students started worrying they would be late.","zh":"巴士移動得如此緩慢，以致學生開始擔心會遲到。"},{"en":"Very slow movement can suggest distance, delay or difficulty.","zh":"非常緩慢的移動可以暗示距離、延誤或困難。"},{"en":"The phrase links the degree of slowness with its effect.","zh":"這個短語把緩慢程度與其效果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a great distance from","meaning":"距離……很遠","examples":[{"en":"The object was thought to be a great distance from the sun.","zh":"人們認為該物體距離太陽很遠。"},{"en":"A great distance from something means very far away from it.","zh":"a great distance from 某物，指離它非常遠。"},{"en":"A student living a great distance from school may need to wake up very early.","zh":"住得離學校很遠的學生可能需要很早起床。"},{"en":"Greater distance can make travel, observation or communication more difficult.","zh":"距離較遠可以令旅行、觀測或溝通更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses considerable separation.","zh":"這個短語強調相隔很遠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"normally visible","meaning":"通常可見","examples":[{"en":"Comets are normally visible only near the sun.","zh":"彗星通常只在太陽附近可見。"},{"en":"Normally visible means usually able to be seen under typical conditions.","zh":"normally visible 指在一般情況下通常能看見。"},{"en":"The school sign is normally visible from the main road unless a bus blocks it.","zh":"學校招牌通常可從主幹道看見，除非被巴士擋住。"},{"en":"If something appears where it is not normally visible, observers may question what it is.","zh":"如果某物出現在通常不可見的位置，觀察者可能會質疑它是甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes usual visibility.","zh":"這個短語描述通常可見性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"immediate vicinity of","meaning":"……的鄰近範圍","examples":[{"en":"Comets are usually visible only in the immediate vicinity of the sun.","zh":"彗星通常只在太陽的鄰近範圍內可見。"},{"en":"The immediate vicinity of something means the area very close around it.","zh":"immediate vicinity of 某物，指非常接近它的周圍區域。"},{"en":"Students should stay in the immediate vicinity of the meeting point during a school trip.","zh":"學生在學校旅行中應留在集合點的鄰近範圍內。"},{"en":"If something is outside the immediate vicinity, it is not right next to the reference point.","zh":"如果某物在鄰近範圍之外，它就不是緊貼參考點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes close surrounding area.","zh":"這個短語描述接近的周圍範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as its orbit came to be worked out","meaning":"隨着其軌道被計算出來","examples":[{"en":"As its orbit came to be worked out, the truth became clear.","zh":"隨着其軌道被計算出來，真相變得清楚。"},{"en":"As its orbit came to be worked out means while scientists gradually calculated its path around the sun.","zh":"as its orbit came to be worked out 指當科學家逐步計算出它圍繞太陽的路徑時。"},{"en":"As a student’s mistakes came to be analysed, the cause of her weak grammar became clear.","zh":"隨着學生錯誤被分析，她文法薄弱的原因變得清楚。"},{"en":"Working out details can turn uncertainty into understanding.","zh":"計算或理清細節可以把不確定變成理解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes clarity developing as calculations progress.","zh":"這個短語描述隨着計算推進而逐漸清楚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the truth dawned that","meaning":"人們開始明白","examples":[{"en":"The truth dawned that the object was a new planet.","zh":"人們開始明白該物體是一顆新行星。"},{"en":"The truth dawned that means people gradually began to realise the truth.","zh":"the truth dawned that 指人們逐漸開始意識到真相。"},{"en":"After checking the timetable twice, the truth dawned that the students had missed the train.","zh":"查了兩次時間表後，人們開始明白學生已錯過火車。"},{"en":"A realisation may come slowly when evidence builds up step by step.","zh":"當證據一步步累積，理解可能慢慢出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a moment of gradual understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸明白的一刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"far beyond Saturn’s realm","meaning":"遠在土星範圍之外","examples":[{"en":"The new planet lay far beyond Saturn’s realm.","zh":"這顆新行星遠在土星範圍之外。"},{"en":"Far beyond Saturn’s realm means much farther from the sun than Saturn’s known region.","zh":"far beyond Saturn’s realm 指距離太陽遠遠超過土星已知區域。"},{"en":"In a school analogy, a classroom far beyond the sports hall would be well past the area students expected.","zh":"用學校比喻，遠在體育館之外的課室，就是超出學生預期範圍很遠。"},{"en":"Finding something beyond the known boundary can change people’s understanding of a whole system.","zh":"發現超出已知邊界的東西，可以改變人們對整個系統的理解。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses great distance past an expected limit.","zh":"這個短語強調遠遠超過預期限度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reviewer of the heavens","meaning":"天空巡察者","examples":[{"en":"Herschel became known as the reviewer of the heavens.","zh":"赫歇爾被稱為天空巡察者。"},{"en":"Reviewer of the heavens means someone who systematically surveys and examines the sky.","zh":"reviewer of the heavens 指有系統地巡察和檢視天空的人。"},{"en":"A teacher who checks every student’s essay carefully might be called a reviewer of student writing.","zh":"仔細檢查每位學生文章的老師，可以被比作學生寫作巡察者。"},{"en":"The title suggests patience, discipline and wide observation.","zh":"這個稱號暗示耐性、紀律和廣泛觀察。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a poetic name to someone who studies the sky thoroughly.","zh":"這個短語給徹底研究天空的人一個詩意名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"stumble across","meaning":"偶然發現","examples":[{"en":"Herschel had stumbled across an unprecedented prize.","zh":"赫歇爾偶然發現了一項前所未有的重大發現。"},{"en":"To stumble across something means to find it by chance, often unexpectedly.","zh":"stumble across 某物，指偶然且常是意外地找到它。"},{"en":"A student may stumble across a useful old textbook while cleaning a shelf.","zh":"學生清理書架時可能偶然發現一本有用舊課本。"},{"en":"Accidental discoveries can become important if someone is careful enough to notice them.","zh":"如果某人足夠細心去注意，偶然發現可以變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unexpected discovery rather than planned searching.","zh":"這個短語描述意外發現，而不是有計劃搜尋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"unprecedented prize","meaning":"前所未有的重大發現","examples":[{"en":"The discovery of Uranus was an unprecedented prize.","zh":"發現天王星是一項前所未有的重大發現。"},{"en":"An unprecedented prize is a discovery or achievement never seen before and extremely valuable.","zh":"unprecedented prize 是前所未見且極有價值的發現或成就。"},{"en":"A student finding a lost historical letter in a school archive would be an unprecedented prize for researchers.","zh":"學生在學校檔案中找到失落的歷史信件，對研究人員來說會是前所未有的重大發現。"},{"en":"Such a prize matters because it changes what people know or can study.","zh":"這種發現重要，因為它改變人們知道或能研究的內容。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both novelty and importance.","zh":"這個短語同時強調新穎性和重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"want to call it","meaning":"想將它命名為","examples":[{"en":"Herschel wanted to call the planet georgium sidus.","zh":"赫歇爾想將這顆行星命名為 georgium sidus。"},{"en":"To want to call it something means to wish to give it that name.","zh":"want to call it 某名稱，指想給它那個名字。"},{"en":"A child may want to call a new puppy “Star” because it has a white mark.","zh":"孩子可能因新小狗有白色斑點，而想將牠命名為 “Star”。"},{"en":"Names can show honour, affection or the way someone understands a discovery.","zh":"名稱可以顯示敬意、喜愛或某人如何理解一項發現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a naming preference.","zh":"這個短語描述命名偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"georgium sidus","meaning":"喬治之星","examples":[{"en":"Herschel wanted to name Uranus georgium sidus.","zh":"赫歇爾想把天王星命名為 georgium sidus。"},{"en":"Georgium sidus was Herschel’s proposed name for Uranus in honour of King George III.","zh":"georgium sidus 是赫歇爾為向喬治三世致敬而提出的天王星名稱。"},{"en":"Scientists sometimes propose names that reflect patrons, places or mythological figures.","zh":"科學家有時提出反映贊助人、地方或神話人物的名稱。"},{"en":"A proposed name may not become the final accepted name.","zh":"建議名稱未必會成為最終接受的名稱。"},{"en":"The phrase is a historical name suggestion for Uranus.","zh":"這個短語是天王星的一個歷史建議名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in honour of","meaning":"為向……致敬","examples":[{"en":"He chose the name in honour of King George III.","zh":"他選擇這個名稱是為向喬治三世致敬。"},{"en":"In honour of someone means as a way to show respect, thanks or admiration for that person.","zh":"in honour of 某人，指作為表達尊重、感謝或敬佩的方式。"},{"en":"A school may name a library in honour of a teacher who served for forty years.","zh":"學校可能把圖書館命名，以向服務四十年的老師致敬。"},{"en":"Naming something after a person can preserve their memory.","zh":"以某人命名可以保存其記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the respectful reason behind an action.","zh":"這個短語解釋某行動背後的敬意原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"royal patron","meaning":"皇家贊助人","examples":[{"en":"King George III was Herschel’s royal patron.","zh":"喬治三世是赫歇爾的皇家贊助人。"},{"en":"A royal patron is a king, queen or royal figure who supports a person, project or institution.","zh":"royal patron 是支持某人、項目或機構的國王、女王或王室人物。"},{"en":"An artist with a powerful patron may receive money, status and protection.","zh":"有強大贊助人的藝術家可能獲得金錢、地位和保護。"},{"en":"Patronage can allow talented people to continue work that might otherwise be too expensive.","zh":"贊助可以讓有才華的人繼續本來可能太昂貴的工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes support from royalty.","zh":"這個短語描述來自王室的支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"for a time","meaning":"有一段時間","examples":[{"en":"For a time, the planet was called Herschel.","zh":"有一段時間，這顆行星被稱為 Herschel。"},{"en":"For a time means for a limited period, but not permanently.","zh":"for a time 指在有限一段期間內，但不是永久。"},{"en":"For a time, the school hall was used as a temporary classroom.","zh":"有一段時間，學校禮堂被用作臨時課室。"},{"en":"Temporary arrangements may later be replaced by a final decision.","zh":"臨時安排之後可能被最終決定取代。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something true only during a particular period.","zh":"這個短語描述某事只在特定時期成立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"its discoverer","meaning":"其發現者","examples":[{"en":"The planet was once called Herschel in honour of its discoverer.","zh":"這顆行星曾為向其發現者致敬而被稱為 Herschel。"},{"en":"Its discoverer means the person who first found or identified it.","zh":"its discoverer 指最先找到或識別它的人。"},{"en":"A new plant species may be named after its discoverer.","zh":"新植物物種可能以其發現者命名。"},{"en":"Naming something after its discoverer gives public recognition to that person’s work.","zh":"以發現者命名能公開表揚該人的工作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the person responsible for the original discovery.","zh":"這個短語指負責最初發現的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"first proposed by","meaning":"最初由……提出","examples":[{"en":"The name Uranus was first proposed by Johann Elert Bode.","zh":"Uranus 這個名稱最初由 Johann Elert Bode 提出。"},{"en":"First proposed by someone means first suggested by that person.","zh":"first proposed by 某人，指最初由該人建議。"},{"en":"A new school house name may be first proposed by a student council member.","zh":"新校社名稱可能最初由學生會成員提出。"},{"en":"A proposal can influence later decisions even if others must approve it.","zh":"即使仍需他人批准，建議也可以影響後來決定。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the first person to suggest an idea.","zh":"這個短語指出最先提出想法的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in use by","meaning":"到……時已被使用","examples":[{"en":"The name Uranus was in use by the late 19th century.","zh":"Uranus 這個名稱到19世紀後期時已被使用。"},{"en":"In use by a time means already being used when that time arrived.","zh":"in use by 某時間，指到該時間時已經被使用。"},{"en":"The new school email system was in use by September.","zh":"新學校電郵系統到九月時已被使用。"},{"en":"A name or tool may take time to become widely accepted and used.","zh":"一個名稱或工具可能需要時間才變得廣泛被接受和使用。"},{"en":"The phrase connects adoption with a particular time.","zh":"這個短語把採用與特定時間連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the late 19th century","meaning":"19世紀後期","examples":[{"en":"The name Uranus was in use by the late 19th century.","zh":"Uranus 這個名稱到19世紀後期時已被使用。"},{"en":"The late 19th century means the later part of the 1800s.","zh":"the late 19th century 指1800年代的較後部分。"},{"en":"Many technologies developed rapidly in the late 19th century.","zh":"許多科技在19世紀後期快速發展。"},{"en":"Referring to this period helps readers place events in historical order.","zh":"提到這個時期幫助讀者把事件放入歷史次序。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a broad time period, not an exact year.","zh":"這個短語給出大概時段，而不是精確年份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"giant in structure","meaning":"結構上屬巨行星","examples":[{"en":"Uranus is a giant in structure, though not as large as Jupiter or Saturn.","zh":"天王星結構上屬巨行星，雖然不如木星或土星大。"},{"en":"Giant in structure means belonging to the giant-planet type because of its composition and form.","zh":"giant in structure 指因其組成和形態而屬於巨行星類型。"},{"en":"A building may be small in height but complex in structure if it has many hidden systems.","zh":"一座建築可能高度不大，但如果有許多隱藏系統，結構上可以很複雜。"},{"en":"Structure can describe what something is made of, not only how big it looks.","zh":"結構可以描述某物由甚麼構成，而不只是外觀看起來多大。"},{"en":"The phrase separates physical type from simple size.","zh":"這個短語把物理類型與單純大小分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not so much in size","meaning":"在大小方面則未必如此","examples":[{"en":"Uranus is a giant in structure, but not so much in size.","zh":"天王星在結構上屬巨行星，但在大小方面則未必如此。"},{"en":"Not so much in size means not especially large when size alone is considered.","zh":"not so much in size 指只看大小時並不特別大。"},{"en":"A school may be strong in reputation, but not so much in size.","zh":"一所學校可能在聲譽上很強，但在規模方面則未必如此。"},{"en":"This phrase separates one quality from another in a comparison.","zh":"這個短語在比較中把一種品質與另一種品質分開。"},{"en":"It means the description is true in one respect but less true in another.","zh":"它表示描述在某方面成立，但在另一方面較不成立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"diameter","meaning":"直徑","examples":[{"en":"The diameter of Uranus is smaller than those of Jupiter and Saturn.","zh":"天王星的直徑比木星和土星小。"},{"en":"Diameter is the distance across a circle or sphere through its centre.","zh":"diameter 是穿過圓形或球體中心的橫向距離。"},{"en":"A student measures the diameter of a round table by measuring from one side through the middle to the other side.","zh":"學生量度圓桌直徑時，會由一邊經中心量到另一邊。"},{"en":"Diameter helps compare the sizes of round objects such as planets, balls and wheels.","zh":"直徑幫助比較行星、球和車輪等圓形物體的大小。"},{"en":"The word refers to width through the centre.","zh":"這個詞指穿過中心的寬度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"compare unfavourably with","meaning":"與……相比較遜色","examples":[{"en":"Uranus’s diameter compares unfavourably with that of Jupiter and Saturn.","zh":"天王星的直徑與木星和土星相比較遜色。"},{"en":"To compare unfavourably with something means to seem worse, smaller or less impressive when compared with it.","zh":"compare unfavourably with 某物，指與它比較時顯得較差、較小或較不令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"A small library may compare unfavourably with a new city library that has more books and computers.","zh":"小圖書館與有更多書和電腦的新城市圖書館相比，可能較遜色。"},{"en":"Unfavourable comparison can make a real strength look weak beside something much larger.","zh":"不利比較可以令真正強項在更大事物旁顯得弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a negative comparison.","zh":"這個短語描述負面比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"terrestrial scale","meaning":"地球尺度","examples":[{"en":"On the terrestrial scale, Uranus is still colossal.","zh":"以地球尺度來看，天王星仍然巨大。"},{"en":"Terrestrial scale means the scale of Earth or ordinary Earth-based measurements.","zh":"terrestrial scale 指地球或普通地球量度的尺度。"},{"en":"A mountain may seem small beside a planet, but on the terrestrial scale it is huge.","zh":"山脈與行星相比可能顯得小，但以地球尺度來看非常巨大。"},{"en":"Changing the scale of comparison can change how large something seems.","zh":"改變比較尺度可以改變某物看起來有多大。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to judging size by Earthly standards.","zh":"這個短語指以地球標準判斷大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"colossal","meaning":"巨大的","examples":[{"en":"Uranus is still colossal when compared with Earth.","zh":"與地球相比，天王星仍然巨大。"},{"en":"Colossal means extremely large.","zh":"colossal 指極其巨大。"},{"en":"A stadium may look colossal to a child entering it for the first time.","zh":"孩子第一次進入體育場時，可能覺得它巨大無比。"},{"en":"Something colossal can be difficult to measure, move or fully imagine.","zh":"巨大的東西可能難以量度、移動或完全想像。"},{"en":"The word strongly emphasises huge size.","zh":"這個詞強烈強調龐大尺寸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"atmosphere","meaning":"大氣層","examples":[{"en":"Uranus’s atmosphere consists largely of hydrogen and helium.","zh":"天王星的大氣層主要由氫和氦組成。"},{"en":"An atmosphere is the layer of gases surrounding a planet.","zh":"atmosphere 是圍繞行星的氣體層。"},{"en":"Earth’s atmosphere contains the air people breathe.","zh":"地球大氣層包含人們呼吸的空氣。"},{"en":"A planet’s atmosphere affects its temperature, colour and weather.","zh":"行星的大氣層影響其溫度、顏色和天氣。"},{"en":"The word refers to surrounding gases, not mood in this context.","zh":"在這個語境中，這個詞指周圍氣體，而不是氣氛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"consist largely of","meaning":"主要由……組成","examples":[{"en":"The atmosphere consists largely of hydrogen and helium.","zh":"大氣層主要由氫和氦組成。"},{"en":"To consist largely of something means to be made mostly of it.","zh":"consist largely of 某物，指主要由它構成。"},{"en":"A school lunch may consist largely of rice and vegetables.","zh":"學校午餐可能主要由米飯和蔬菜組成。"},{"en":"Knowing what something consists of helps people understand its nature and behaviour.","zh":"知道某物由甚麼組成，幫助人理解其性質和行為。"},{"en":"The phrase describes main composition.","zh":"這個短語描述主要成分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hydrogen and helium","meaning":"氫和氦","examples":[{"en":"Uranus’s atmosphere contains hydrogen and helium.","zh":"天王星的大氣層含有氫和氦。"},{"en":"Hydrogen and helium are light chemical elements commonly found in giant planets and stars.","zh":"hydrogen and helium 是常見於巨行星和恆星中的輕化學元素。"},{"en":"Students may meet hydrogen and helium when learning the periodic table.","zh":"學生學習元素週期表時可能遇到氫和氦。"},{"en":"The presence of these gases helps scientists understand what a planet is made of.","zh":"這些氣體的存在幫助科學家理解行星由甚麼構成。"},{"en":"The phrase names two specific elements.","zh":"這個短語指出兩種特定元素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"with a trace of","meaning":"帶有微量……","examples":[{"en":"The atmosphere contains hydrogen and helium, with a trace of methane.","zh":"大氣層含有氫和氦，並帶有微量甲烷。"},{"en":"With a trace of something means with a very small amount of it.","zh":"with a trace of 某物，指帶有非常少量的它。"},{"en":"A soup may taste of chicken with a trace of ginger.","zh":"湯可能有雞味，並帶有微量薑味。"},{"en":"Even a tiny amount of a substance can affect smell, colour or flavour.","zh":"即使很少量物質，也可以影響氣味、顏色或味道。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small but noticeable quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述少量但可察覺的分量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"methane","meaning":"甲烷","examples":[{"en":"A trace of methane gives Uranus part of its colour.","zh":"微量甲烷給予天王星部分顏色。"},{"en":"Methane is a gas that can be found in some planetary atmospheres and natural gas.","zh":"methane 是可在某些行星大氣層和天然氣中找到的氣體。"},{"en":"Students may learn that methane is released by farms, landfills and some energy systems.","zh":"學生可能學到農場、堆填區和某些能源系統會釋放甲烷。"},{"en":"In a planet’s atmosphere, methane can affect the colour seen through telescopes.","zh":"在行星大氣層中，甲烷可以影響透過望遠鏡看到的顏色。"},{"en":"The word names a specific chemical gas.","zh":"這個詞指出一種特定化學氣體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"through a telescope","meaning":"透過望遠鏡","examples":[{"en":"Through a telescope, Uranus appears as a small bluish-green disc.","zh":"透過望遠鏡，天王星呈現為一個細小藍綠色圓盤。"},{"en":"Through a telescope means when seen using a telescope.","zh":"through a telescope 指使用望遠鏡觀看時。"},{"en":"Through a telescope, students may see the moon’s craters more clearly.","zh":"透過望遠鏡，學生可能更清楚看見月球環形山。"},{"en":"Telescopes make distant objects easier to observe by collecting more light.","zh":"望遠鏡透過收集更多光線，令遙遠物體更容易觀察。"},{"en":"The phrase describes observation using an optical instrument.","zh":"這個短語描述使用光學儀器觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"appear as","meaning":"呈現為","examples":[{"en":"The planet appears as a small bluish-green disc.","zh":"該行星呈現為一個細小藍綠色圓盤。"},{"en":"To appear as something means to look like that thing to an observer.","zh":"appear as 某物，指在觀察者眼中看起來像該物。"},{"en":"From far away, a large building may appear as a tiny block on the horizon.","zh":"從遠處看，大樓可能在地平線上呈現為一小塊。"},{"en":"Appearance can depend on distance, light and the tool used to observe it.","zh":"外觀可以取決於距離、光線和觀測工具。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how something looks, not necessarily what it truly is.","zh":"這個短語描述某物看起來如何，而不一定是真正本質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bluish-green disc","meaning":"藍綠色圓盤","examples":[{"en":"Uranus appears as a bluish-green disc through a telescope.","zh":"天王星透過望遠鏡呈現為藍綠色圓盤。"},{"en":"A bluish-green disc is a round shape with a colour between blue and green.","zh":"bluish-green disc 是帶有藍與綠之間顏色的圓形。"},{"en":"A planet may look like a small coloured disc when seen through a telescope.","zh":"行星透過望遠鏡觀察時，可能看起來像小小彩色圓盤。"},{"en":"Colour can give clues about gases in a planet’s atmosphere.","zh":"顏色可以提供行星大氣層中氣體的線索。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the visual appearance of Uranus.","zh":"這個短語描述天王星的視覺外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"faint green periphery","meaning":"淡綠色邊緣","examples":[{"en":"The planet has a faint green periphery.","zh":"該行星有淡綠色邊緣。"},{"en":"A faint green periphery is a pale green outer edge or border.","zh":"faint green periphery 是淡淡綠色的外邊或邊界。"},{"en":"A lamp may create a faint green periphery around a glass decoration.","zh":"燈光可能在玻璃擺設周圍形成淡綠色邊緣。"},{"en":"The edge of an object can show colours that are less clear than the centre.","zh":"物體邊緣可以顯示比中心較不清晰的顏色。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a subtle colour around the outside.","zh":"這個短語描述外圍的細微顏色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"record the occultation of","meaning":"記錄……的掩星現象","examples":[{"en":"James L. Elliot was recording the occultation of a star behind Uranus.","zh":"James L. Elliot 正在記錄一顆星在天王星後方的掩星現象。"},{"en":"To record the occultation of something means to observe and save details of one object being hidden by another.","zh":"record the occultation of 某物，指觀察並保存一個天體被另一個天體遮蔽的細節。"},{"en":"An astronomy club may record the occultation of a star by timing when it disappears behind the moon.","zh":"天文學會可能透過計時星星何時在月球後消失，記錄其掩星現象。"},{"en":"Such records can reveal rings, atmospheres or other hidden features.","zh":"這類記錄可以揭示環、大氣層或其他隱藏特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful documentation of an astronomical hiding event.","zh":"這個短語描述對天文遮蔽事件的仔細記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"occultation","meaning":"掩星；掩蔽","examples":[{"en":"Occultation occurs when one astronomical object hides another from view.","zh":"當一個天體遮擋另一個天體使其看不見時，就會發生掩星現象。"},{"en":"Occultation is an event in which one object passes in front of another and blocks it.","zh":"occultation 是一個物體從另一物體前方經過並遮擋它的事件。"},{"en":"Students may observe an occultation when the moon covers a distant star.","zh":"當月球遮住遙遠恆星時，學生可能觀察到掩星現象。"},{"en":"Measuring an occultation can help scientists discover details that are hard to see directly.","zh":"量度掩星現象可以幫助科學家發現難以直接看見的細節。"},{"en":"The word refers to an astronomical blocking event.","zh":"這個詞指天文遮蔽事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"behind the planet","meaning":"在行星後方","examples":[{"en":"The star passed behind the planet during the occultation.","zh":"在掩星期間，該星從行星後方經過。"},{"en":"Behind the planet means on the far side of the planet from the observer.","zh":"behind the planet 指在相對於觀察者而言行星的另一邊。"},{"en":"A bus stop may be behind the school building, so visitors cannot see it from the gate.","zh":"巴士站可能在學校大樓後方，所以訪客從校門看不見。"},{"en":"When something passes behind a larger object, it may disappear from view.","zh":"當某物經過較大物體後方，它可能從視野中消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes position relative to the planet and observer.","zh":"這個短語描述相對於行星和觀察者的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"discover the presence of","meaning":"發現……的存在","examples":[{"en":"Elliot discovered the presence of five rings around Uranus.","zh":"Elliot 發現天王星周圍存在五個環。"},{"en":"To discover the presence of something means to find evidence that it exists there.","zh":"discover the presence of 某物，指找到證據顯示它存在於該處。"},{"en":"A doctor may discover the presence of an infection after reading test results.","zh":"醫生閱讀檢測結果後，可能發現感染的存在。"},{"en":"Detecting something’s presence can change how people understand a problem or object.","zh":"偵測到某物存在，可以改變人們對問題或物體的理解。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on finding that something exists.","zh":"這個短語重點在發現某物存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rings encircling","meaning":"環繞……的環","examples":[{"en":"Uranus has rings encircling its equator.","zh":"天王星有環繞其赤道的環。"},{"en":"Rings encircling something are circular bands going around it.","zh":"rings encircling 某物，是圍繞它的圓形帶狀物。"},{"en":"A toy planet may have plastic rings encircling its middle.","zh":"玩具行星可能有塑膠環環繞其中部。"},{"en":"Rings can show the structure and movement of material around a planet.","zh":"環可以顯示行星周圍物質的結構和運動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bands surrounding an object.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞物體的帶狀環。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"equator","meaning":"赤道","examples":[{"en":"The rings encircle the equator of Uranus.","zh":"這些環環繞天王星的赤道。"},{"en":"An equator is an imaginary line around the middle of a planet or moon.","zh":"equator 是圍繞行星或衛星中部的想像線。"},{"en":"Earth’s equator divides the planet into northern and southern halves.","zh":"地球赤道把地球分成北半球和南半球。"},{"en":"Objects near a planet’s equator may move in a different plane from those near its poles.","zh":"接近行星赤道的物體，可能在與兩極附近物體不同的平面中運動。"},{"en":"The word refers to the middle line around a round body.","zh":"這個詞指圓形天體周圍的中線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"exploratory flight","meaning":"探測飛行","examples":[{"en":"More rings were discovered during the exploratory flight of Voyager 2.","zh":"更多環是在旅行者2號的探測飛行期間被發現的。"},{"en":"An exploratory flight is a journey made to investigate and gather information.","zh":"exploratory flight 是為調查和收集資料而進行的飛行旅程。"},{"en":"A drone may make an exploratory flight over a flooded area before rescuers enter.","zh":"救援人員進入前，無人機可能在水浸地區上空進行探測飛行。"},{"en":"Exploration flights can reveal details that cannot be seen clearly from far away.","zh":"探測飛行可以揭示從遠處無法清楚看見的細節。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a flight for discovery and investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述為發現和調查而進行的飛行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Voyager 2","meaning":"旅行者2號","examples":[{"en":"Voyager 2 discovered additional rings and moons around Uranus.","zh":"旅行者2號發現天王星周圍更多環和衛星。"},{"en":"Voyager 2 was an unmanned spacecraft sent to study planets in the outer solar system.","zh":"Voyager 2 是被派往研究外太陽系行星的無人太空船。"},{"en":"Students may learn about Voyager 2 as an example of long-distance space exploration.","zh":"學生可能把旅行者2號作為長距離太空探索例子來學習。"},{"en":"Its observations helped scientists learn more about planets too distant for easy direct study.","zh":"它的觀測幫助科學家更多了解太遙遠而難以直接研究的行星。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific space mission.","zh":"這個短語指出一項特定太空任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in addition to","meaning":"除……之外","examples":[{"en":"In addition to its rings, Uranus has satellites.","zh":"除了它的環之外，天王星也有衛星。"},{"en":"In addition to means as well as or besides something already mentioned.","zh":"in addition to 指除了已提及的某事之外，也包括其他。"},{"en":"In addition to homework, students may need to prepare a short presentation.","zh":"除了功課之外，學生可能還需要準備短簡報。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another item without removing the first one.","zh":"這個短語加入另一項，而不移除第一項。"},{"en":"It is useful when listing more than one feature.","zh":"它適合用於列出多於一個特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"satellites","meaning":"衛星","examples":[{"en":"Uranus has 15 satellites, also called moons.","zh":"天王星有15顆衛星，也稱為月亮。"},{"en":"Satellites are objects that orbit a planet; natural satellites are also called moons.","zh":"satellites 是圍繞行星運行的物體；天然衛星也稱為 moons。"},{"en":"Earth has one natural satellite, the Moon.","zh":"地球有一顆天然衛星，就是月球。"},{"en":"Satellites help scientists understand gravity, formation history and planetary systems.","zh":"衛星幫助科學家理解重力、形成歷史和行星系統。"},{"en":"The word can refer to natural moons or artificial objects, depending on context.","zh":"視乎語境，這個詞可指天然月球或人造物體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"revolve about","meaning":"圍繞……運行","examples":[{"en":"The satellites revolve about the equator of Uranus.","zh":"這些衛星圍繞天王星赤道運行。"},{"en":"To revolve about something means to move around it in a circular or orbital path.","zh":"revolve about 某物，指沿圓形或軌道路徑圍繞它移動。"},{"en":"The moon revolves about Earth as Earth moves around the sun.","zh":"月球圍繞地球運行，而地球圍繞太陽運行。"},{"en":"Objects that revolve about a planet are held by gravity.","zh":"圍繞行星運行的物體受重力牽引。"},{"en":"The phrase describes orbital movement around a central body.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞中心天體的軌道運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"move with the planet","meaning":"與行星一起移動","examples":[{"en":"The moons move with the planet in an east–west direction.","zh":"這些衛星與行星一起沿東西方向移動。"},{"en":"To move with the planet means to travel together with it as part of the same system.","zh":"move with the planet 指作為同一系統的一部分與行星一起移動。"},{"en":"A suitcase on a moving bus moves with the bus until someone takes it off.","zh":"放在行駛巴士上的行李會與巴士一起移動，直到有人把它拿下。"},{"en":"Objects connected by gravity often move together through space.","zh":"受重力連繫的物體常在太空中一起移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shared movement with a larger body.","zh":"這個短語描述與較大天體共同移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"east–west direction","meaning":"東西方向","examples":[{"en":"The moons move in an east–west direction.","zh":"這些衛星沿東西方向移動。"},{"en":"East–west direction means along a line from east to west or west to east.","zh":"east–west direction 指沿東至西或西至東的方向線。"},{"en":"A train line may run in an east–west direction across a city.","zh":"一條鐵路線可能沿東西方向橫跨城市。"},{"en":"Direction labels help people describe movement clearly.","zh":"方向標籤幫助人清楚描述移動。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the broad orientation of movement.","zh":"這個短語給出移動的大致方位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the two largest moons","meaning":"兩個最大的衛星","examples":[{"en":"The two largest moons of Uranus are Titania and Oberon.","zh":"天王星兩個最大的衛星是天衛三和天衛四。"},{"en":"The two largest moons means the two biggest natural satellites orbiting a planet.","zh":"the two largest moons 指圍繞行星運行的兩顆最大天然衛星。"},{"en":"A science chart may list the two largest moons first because they are easiest to compare.","zh":"科學圖表可能先列出兩個最大的衛星，因為它們最容易比較。"},{"en":"Larger moons may be easier to observe than smaller ones.","zh":"較大的衛星可能比小衛星更容易觀測。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies size ranking among moons.","zh":"這個短語指出衛星中的大小排名。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Titania and Oberon","meaning":"天衛三和天衛四","examples":[{"en":"Titania and Oberon were discovered by Herschel in 1787.","zh":"天衛三和天衛四由赫歇爾於1787年發現。"},{"en":"Titania and Oberon are two large moons of Uranus.","zh":"Titania and Oberon 是天王星的兩顆大型衛星。"},{"en":"Students may remember Titania and Oberon as names connected with literature and astronomy.","zh":"學生可能把天衛三和天衛四記作與文學和天文學相關的名稱。"},{"en":"Naming moons helps scientists discuss them clearly instead of using only numbers.","zh":"為衛星命名幫助科學家清楚討論它們，而不只使用數字。"},{"en":"The phrase names two specific satellites.","zh":"這個短語指出兩顆特定衛星。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the next two","meaning":"接下來兩個","examples":[{"en":"The next two moons, Umbriel and Ariel, were found in 1851.","zh":"接下來兩個衛星，即天衛二和天衛一，於1851年被發現。"},{"en":"The next two means the following two items in a sequence or ranking.","zh":"the next two 指順序或排名中接下來的兩項。"},{"en":"After checking the first two answers, the teacher looked at the next two.","zh":"檢查頭兩個答案後，老師看接下來兩個。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise information in order.","zh":"這個短語幫助按次序組織資訊。"},{"en":"It refers to two things that come after the ones already mentioned.","zh":"它指已提及事物之後的兩項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Umbriel and Ariel","meaning":"天衛二和天衛一","examples":[{"en":"Umbriel and Ariel were found by William Lassell.","zh":"天衛二和天衛一由 William Lassell 發現。"},{"en":"Umbriel and Ariel are two moons of Uranus.","zh":"Umbriel and Ariel 是天王星的兩顆衛星。"},{"en":"An astronomy table may list Umbriel and Ariel with their discovery dates.","zh":"天文表格可能列出天衛二和天衛一及其發現日期。"},{"en":"Learning moon names helps students follow descriptions of a planet’s satellite system.","zh":"學習衛星名稱幫助學生理解行星衛星系統的描述。"},{"en":"The phrase names two specific Uranian moons.","zh":"這個短語指出兩顆特定天王星衛星。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be found by","meaning":"由……發現","examples":[{"en":"Umbriel and Ariel were found by the British astronomer William Lassell.","zh":"天衛二和天衛一由英國天文學家 William Lassell 發現。"},{"en":"To be found by someone means to be discovered or identified by that person.","zh":"be found by 某人，指由該人發現或識別。"},{"en":"A missing school file may be found by a cleaner after classes end.","zh":"遺失的學校文件可能在放學後由清潔工發現。"},{"en":"In science, saying who found something gives credit for the discovery.","zh":"在科學中，說明某物由誰發現，是給予發現功勞。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the discoverer.","zh":"這個短語指出發現者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"British astronomer","meaning":"英國天文學家","examples":[{"en":"William Lassell was a British astronomer.","zh":"William Lassell 是一位英國天文學家。"},{"en":"A British astronomer is a scientist from Britain who studies stars, planets and space.","zh":"British astronomer 是來自英國、研究恆星、行星和太空的科學家。"},{"en":"A British astronomer may work at a university, observatory or space research centre.","zh":"英國天文學家可能在大學、天文台或太空研究中心工作。"},{"en":"Nationality can help readers place a scientist in historical and cultural context.","zh":"國籍可以幫助讀者把科學家放入歷史和文化背景中理解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both profession and nationality.","zh":"這個短語同時描述職業和國籍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"innermost moon","meaning":"最內側的衛星","examples":[{"en":"Miranda was once thought to be the innermost moon of Uranus.","zh":"天衛五曾被認為是天王星最內側的衛星。"},{"en":"The innermost moon is the moon orbiting closest to a planet.","zh":"innermost moon 是軌道最接近行星的衛星。"},{"en":"In a model solar system, the innermost planet is the one closest to the sun.","zh":"在太陽系模型中，最內側行星是最接近太陽的那顆。"},{"en":"Being innermost describes position, not size or importance.","zh":"最內側描述位置，而不是大小或重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the object nearest to the centre.","zh":"這個短語指出最接近中心的物體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Miranda","meaning":"天衛五","examples":[{"en":"Miranda was discovered in 1948 by Gerard Peter Kuiper.","zh":"天衛五於1948年由 Gerard Peter Kuiper 發現。"},{"en":"Miranda is one of the moons of Uranus.","zh":"Miranda 是天王星的其中一顆衛星。"},{"en":"Students may learn Miranda’s name when studying Uranus’s satellite system.","zh":"學生研究天王星衛星系統時，可能學到 Miranda 這個名稱。"},{"en":"Discovering a moon adds detail to scientists’ understanding of a planet.","zh":"發現衛星會為科學家對行星的理解加入細節。"},{"en":"The word names a specific natural satellite.","zh":"這個詞指出一顆特定天然衛星。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"American astronomer","meaning":"美國天文學家","examples":[{"en":"Gerard Peter Kuiper was an American astronomer.","zh":"Gerard Peter Kuiper 是一位美國天文學家。"},{"en":"An American astronomer is a scientist connected with the United States who studies space.","zh":"American astronomer 是與美國相關、研究太空的科學家。"},{"en":"An American astronomer may use telescopes, spacecraft data and computer models.","zh":"美國天文學家可能使用望遠鏡、太空船資料和電腦模型。"},{"en":"Mentioning a scientist’s background helps readers identify who made a discovery.","zh":"提及科學家的背景幫助讀者辨認誰作出發現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes nationality and scientific profession.","zh":"這個短語描述國籍和科學職業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"pass in front of","meaning":"從……前方經過","examples":[{"en":"Occultation occurs when one object passes in front of another.","zh":"當一個物體從另一個物體前方經過時，就會發生掩蔽。"},{"en":"To pass in front of something means to move across the space between it and the observer.","zh":"pass in front of 某物，指從它與觀察者之間的空間移過。"},{"en":"A student may pass in front of the projector and block the screen for a moment.","zh":"學生可能從投影機前方經過，短暫遮住螢幕。"},{"en":"When one object passes in front of another, it can hide all or part of it.","zh":"當一個物體從另一個前方經過，它可以遮住其全部或部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement across someone’s line of sight.","zh":"這個短語描述穿過某人視線的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"hide something from view","meaning":"遮擋某物使其看不見","examples":[{"en":"One astronomical object may hide another from view.","zh":"一個天體可能遮擋另一個天體使其看不見。"},{"en":"To hide something from view means to block it so people cannot see it.","zh":"hide something from view 指遮住某物，使人無法看見。"},{"en":"A tall student may hide the whiteboard from view if he stands in front of it.","zh":"如果高個學生站在白板前，可能遮擋白板使其看不見。"},{"en":"When something is hidden from view, observers may need to move or wait.","zh":"當某物被遮住，觀察者可能需要移動或等待。"},{"en":"The phrase describes blocked visibility.","zh":"這個短語描述視線被阻擋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"come between","meaning":"來到……之間","examples":[{"en":"The moon may come between an observer and a star.","zh":"月球可能來到觀測者和星星之間。"},{"en":"To come between two things means to move into the space separating them.","zh":"come between 兩物，指移入分隔它們的空間。"},{"en":"A bus may come between a pedestrian and the shop sign, blocking the view.","zh":"巴士可能來到行人和商店招牌之間，擋住視線。"},{"en":"When an object comes between two others, it may interrupt sight, movement or communication.","zh":"當物體來到另外兩者之間，它可能阻斷視線、移動或溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an object entering the middle position.","zh":"這個短語描述物體進入中間位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"observer","meaning":"觀測者","examples":[{"en":"An occultation can occur when the moon comes between an observer and a star.","zh":"當月球來到觀測者和星星之間時，可能發生掩星現象。"},{"en":"An observer is a person who watches or studies something carefully.","zh":"observer 是仔細觀看或研究某事的人。"},{"en":"In a science lesson, one student may act as an observer and record what happens.","zh":"在科學課中，一名學生可能擔任觀察者並記錄發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Careful observers notice details that casual viewers may miss.","zh":"仔細觀察者會注意到隨便觀看的人可能錯過的細節。"},{"en":"The word refers to someone who watches, often for study or evidence.","zh":"這個詞指觀看的人，常為了研究或證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"unmanned spacecraft","meaning":"無人太空船","examples":[{"en":"Voyager 2 was an unmanned spacecraft.","zh":"旅行者2號是一艘無人太空船。"},{"en":"An unmanned spacecraft is a spacecraft that travels without humans on board.","zh":"unmanned spacecraft 是沒有載人飛行的太空船。"},{"en":"Scientists send unmanned spacecraft to places too distant or dangerous for astronauts.","zh":"科學家把無人太空船送往太遙遠或太危險而不適合太空人的地方。"},{"en":"Such spacecraft can collect pictures and data while being controlled from Earth.","zh":"這類太空船可以在地球控制下收集圖片和資料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a robotic space vehicle.","zh":"這個短語描述機械人式太空飛行器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be sent on a voyage past","meaning":"被派往飛越……的旅程","examples":[{"en":"Voyager 2 was sent on a voyage past several planets.","zh":"旅行者2號被派往飛越幾顆行星的旅程。"},{"en":"To be sent on a voyage past something means to be launched or dispatched to travel by and observe it.","zh":"be sent on a voyage past 某物，指被發射或派出，從其旁邊經過並觀察它。"},{"en":"A research boat may be sent on a voyage past several islands to collect water samples.","zh":"研究船可能被派往經過幾個島嶼的旅程，以收集水樣。"},{"en":"Passing close to an object allows scientists to gather clearer information.","zh":"靠近經過物體能讓科學家收集更清楚資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a planned exploratory journey.","zh":"這個短語描述有計劃的探索旅程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"send back information about","meaning":"傳回關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"Voyager 2 sent back information about the planets to scientists on Earth.","zh":"旅行者2號向地球上的科學家傳回關於行星的資料。"},{"en":"To send back information about something means to transmit data or observations from a distant place.","zh":"send back information about 某事，指從遠方傳送數據或觀察結果。"},{"en":"A rescue drone may send back information about blocked roads after a storm.","zh":"救援無人機可能在風暴後傳回關於道路受阻的資料。"},{"en":"Information sent back from a remote location helps people make decisions without being there.","zh":"從遠方傳回的資料幫助人們不用親身到場也能作決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes returning useful data to observers elsewhere.","zh":"這個短語描述把有用數據傳回別處的觀察者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"scientists on Earth","meaning":"地球上的科學家","examples":[{"en":"The spacecraft sent information back to scientists on Earth.","zh":"太空船把資料傳回地球上的科學家。"},{"en":"Scientists on Earth are researchers working from Earth rather than travelling with the spacecraft.","zh":"scientists on Earth 是在地球工作，而不是隨太空船旅行的研究人員。"},{"en":"Scientists on Earth may analyse images sent by a space probe.","zh":"地球上的科學家可能分析太空探測器傳回的影像。"},{"en":"Remote missions depend on these scientists to interpret the data received.","zh":"遙距任務依靠這些科學家解讀收到的數據。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts Earth-based researchers with objects or machines in space.","zh":"這個短語把地球研究人員與太空中的物體或機器作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"complete the table below","meaning":"完成下表","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to complete the table below with dates.","zh":"考生需要用日期完成下表。"},{"en":"To complete the table below means to fill in missing information in the table that follows.","zh":"complete the table below 指填寫下方表格中的缺失資訊。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may complete the table below by finding names, dates or places in the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能透過在文章中尋找姓名、日期或地方來完成下表。"},{"en":"Checking headings helps students know what kind of answer each blank needs.","zh":"查看標題幫助學生知道每個空格需要哪類答案。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"write a date for","meaning":"為……寫上一個日期","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should write a date for each answer.","zh":"考生應為每個答案寫上一個日期。"},{"en":"To write a date for something means to give the year, day or time required by the question.","zh":"write a date for 某項，指給出題目要求的年份、日子或時間。"},{"en":"A student may write a date for each event in a history timeline.","zh":"學生可能為歷史時間線中的每件事寫上一個日期。"},{"en":"If the question asks for a date, writing a name instead will be wrong.","zh":"如果題目要求日期，寫姓名就會錯。"},{"en":"The phrase tells candidates the required answer type.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生所需答案類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"on your answer sheet","meaning":"在答題紙上","examples":[{"en":"Answers should be written on your answer sheet.","zh":"答案應寫在答題紙上。"},{"en":"On your answer sheet means in the official place where exam answers must be recorded.","zh":"on your answer sheet 指在考試答案必須記錄的官方位置。"},{"en":"A student may know the answer, but she loses marks if she does not write it on her answer sheet.","zh":"學生可能知道答案，但如果沒有寫在答題紙上，就會失分。"},{"en":"Exam instructions matter because answers in the wrong place may not be marked.","zh":"考試指示重要，因為寫錯位置的答案可能不被評改。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where candidates must put their answers.","zh":"這個短語指出考生必須把答案放在哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"began investigating astronomy","meaning":"開始研究天文學","examples":[{"en":"Herschel began investigating astronomy after reading a book on the subject.","zh":"赫歇爾閱讀一本關於該科目的書後，開始研究天文學。"},{"en":"To begin investigating astronomy means to start studying and observing stars, planets and space seriously.","zh":"begin investigating astronomy 指開始認真研究和觀察恆星、行星與太空。"},{"en":"A student may begin investigating astronomy after joining a school stargazing club.","zh":"學生加入學校觀星學會後，可能開始研究天文學。"},{"en":"One interesting book or lesson can lead someone to explore a new subject deeply.","zh":"一本有趣的書或一堂課可以引導某人深入探索新科目。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the start of serious study in astronomy.","zh":"這個短語描述認真學習天文學的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"discovery of the planet","meaning":"……行星的發現","examples":[{"en":"The table asks about the discovery of the planet Uranus.","zh":"表格問到天王星這顆行星的發現。"},{"en":"Discovery of the planet means the event in which the planet was first identified.","zh":"discovery of the planet 指該行星首次被識別的事件。"},{"en":"A science timeline may include the discovery of a planet, its rings and its moons.","zh":"科學時間線可能包括一顆行星、其環和其衛星的發現。"},{"en":"Such discoveries change textbooks because they add new objects to known space.","zh":"這類發現會改變教科書，因為它們為已知太空加入新物體。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on when and by whom a planet was found.","zh":"這個短語重點在行星何時及由誰發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"first discovery of","meaning":"首次發現……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the first discovery of Uranus’s rings.","zh":"題目問天王星環的首次發現。"},{"en":"The first discovery of something means the earliest time it was found or identified.","zh":"first discovery of 某物，指它最早被找到或識別的時間。"},{"en":"A museum label may describe the first discovery of an ancient coin in a village field.","zh":"博物館標籤可能描述古錢幣在村莊田地中的首次發現。"},{"en":"First discoveries are important because later research often builds on them.","zh":"首次發現重要，因為後來研究常以它為基礎。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the beginning of known evidence.","zh":"這個短語指出已知證據的開端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the last ten moons","meaning":"最後十個衛星","examples":[{"en":"The last ten moons of Uranus were discovered by Voyager 2.","zh":"天王星最後十個衛星由旅行者2號發現。"},{"en":"The last ten moons means the final group of ten moons mentioned in a sequence or list.","zh":"the last ten moons 指序列或列表中最後一組十個衛星。"},{"en":"A teacher may check the last ten answers on a student’s worksheet separately.","zh":"老師可能另外檢查學生工作紙上的最後十個答案。"},{"en":"Grouping items this way helps readers follow a long list of discoveries.","zh":"這樣分組幫助讀者理解長發現列表。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a particular final set of ten moons.","zh":"這個短語指特定的最後十個衛星。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"agree with the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether statements agree with the views of the writer.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與作者的觀點一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the views of someone means to match that person’s opinions or attitude.","zh":"agree with the views of 某人，指與該人的意見或態度相符。"},{"en":"In a reading test, a statement may agree with the writer’s view even if the same words are not used.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，即使用詞不同，陳述也可能與作者觀點一致。"},{"en":"Students must look for opinion, not only factual detail.","zh":"學生必須尋找觀點，而不只是事實細節。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in YES/NO/NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 YES/NO/NOT GIVEN 題型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A “No” answer contradicts the views of the writer.","zh":"“No” 答案與作者的觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of that person’s opinion.","zh":"contradict the views of 某人，指說出與該人意見相反的內容。"},{"en":"If a writer praises a policy, a statement saying the writer dislikes it contradicts the writer’s views.","zh":"如果作者稱讚一項政策，而陳述說作者不喜歡它，就是與作者觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be based on the passage, not on the student’s own opinion.","zh":"矛盾必須基於文章，而不是學生自己的意見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes disagreement with a stated or implied viewpoint.","zh":"這個短語描述與明示或暗示觀點不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"The answer is not given if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"如果無法判斷作者怎樣想，答案就是沒有提及。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to know or decide.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資訊知道或決定。"},{"en":"If a timetable does not mention room numbers, it is impossible to say which room the class uses.","zh":"如果時間表沒有提及課室號碼，就無法判斷該課使用哪間房。"},{"en":"In exams, students should not guess when the passage gives no evidence.","zh":"在考試中，當文章沒有證據，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a situation where judgement cannot be made.","zh":"這個短語描述無法作出判斷的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"multi-talented","meaning":"多才多藝的","examples":[{"en":"Herschel was multi-talented because he worked in both music and astronomy.","zh":"赫歇爾多才多藝，因為他同時從事音樂和天文學。"},{"en":"Multi-talented means having strong ability in several different areas.","zh":"multi-talented 指在幾個不同領域都有強能力。"},{"en":"A student who writes well, plays piano and leads a sports team is multi-talented.","zh":"會寫作、彈鋼琴並帶領運動隊的學生是多才多藝的。"},{"en":"Having many talents can open unexpected career paths.","zh":"擁有多種才能可以打開意想不到的事業道路。"},{"en":"The word praises broad ability rather than one narrow skill.","zh":"這個詞稱讚廣泛能力，而不是一項狹窄技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"improbable that","meaning":"不大可能","examples":[{"en":"It is improbable that a planet is hidden behind the sun.","zh":"一顆行星隱藏在太陽後面是不大可能的。"},{"en":"Improbable that means unlikely that something is true or will happen.","zh":"improbable that 指某事不大可能是真的或發生。"},{"en":"It is improbable that a student will get full marks without reading the question carefully.","zh":"學生不仔細讀題就取得滿分是不大可能的。"},{"en":"Improbable ideas may still be discussed, but they need strong evidence.","zh":"不大可能的想法仍可被討論，但需要強證據。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses low likelihood.","zh":"這個短語表達低可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"hidden behind the sun","meaning":"隱藏在太陽後面","examples":[{"en":"The theory imagined a planet hidden behind the sun.","zh":"該理論想像一顆行星隱藏在太陽後面。"},{"en":"Hidden behind the sun means blocked from our view because the sun lies between us and the object.","zh":"hidden behind the sun 指因太陽位於我們與該物體之間而被遮住。"},{"en":"A small bird may be hidden behind a tree, so students cannot see it from the classroom.","zh":"小鳥可能藏在樹後，所以學生從課室看不見它。"},{"en":"If something is hidden behind a bright object, direct observation becomes difficult.","zh":"如果某物藏在明亮物體後面，直接觀察會變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an object concealed by position.","zh":"這個短語描述因位置而被遮蔽的物體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"know immediately that","meaning":"立即知道","examples":[{"en":"Herschel did not know immediately that he had found a planet.","zh":"赫歇爾並沒有立即知道自己發現了一顆行星。"},{"en":"To know immediately that something is true means to realise it at once without delay.","zh":"know immediately that 某事為真，指沒有延遲地立刻意識到。"},{"en":"A teacher may not know immediately that a student is struggling if the student stays quiet.","zh":"如果學生保持沉默，老師未必立即知道她有困難。"},{"en":"Some truths only become clear after more evidence is collected.","zh":"有些真相只有在收集更多證據後才變得清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes instant understanding, often in a negative sentence.","zh":"這個短語描述即時理解，常用於否定句。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"collaborate with","meaning":"與……合作","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Herschel collaborated with other astronomers.","zh":"題目問赫歇爾是否與其他天文學家合作。"},{"en":"To collaborate with someone means to work together with that person on a shared task.","zh":"collaborate with 某人，指與該人共同完成共同任務。"},{"en":"Students collaborate with classmates when they prepare a group presentation.","zh":"學生準備小組匯報時，會與同學合作。"},{"en":"Collaboration can combine different skills and produce better results.","zh":"合作可以結合不同技能並產生更好結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cooperative work.","zh":"這個短語描述協作工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"of his time","meaning":"他那個時代的","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to other astronomers of his time.","zh":"該陳述指他那個時代的其他天文學家。"},{"en":"Of his time means living or working during the same historical period as him.","zh":"of his time 指與他生活或工作於同一歷史時期。"},{"en":"A writer of her time may reflect the social values common in that period.","zh":"一位屬於她那個時代的作家，可能反映當時常見社會價值。"},{"en":"Comparing someone with people of his time is fairer than judging only by modern standards.","zh":"將某人與他那個時代的人比較，比只用現代標準判斷更公平。"},{"en":"The phrase places a person within a historical context.","zh":"這個短語把人放入歷史背景中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"newly discovered object","meaning":"新發現的物體","examples":[{"en":"The newly discovered object was first suspected to be a comet.","zh":"這個新發現的物體最初被懷疑是一顆彗星。"},{"en":"A newly discovered object is something that has only recently been found or identified.","zh":"newly discovered object 是剛近期被找到或識別的東西。"},{"en":"A newly discovered fossil may need careful study before scientists name it.","zh":"新發現的化石可能需要仔細研究，科學家才為它命名。"},{"en":"Early guesses about new discoveries can change after more evidence appears.","zh":"關於新發現的早期猜測，可能在更多證據出現後改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something recently found.","zh":"這個短語描述剛被發現的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be considered to be","meaning":"被認為是……","examples":[{"en":"The object was considered to be too far from the sun to be a comet.","zh":"該物體被認為距離太陽太遠，不可能是彗星。"},{"en":"To be considered to be something means to be regarded or judged as that thing.","zh":"be considered to be 某事，指被視為或判斷為該事。"},{"en":"A student may be considered to be ready for the exam after several strong practice results.","zh":"學生在幾次練習成績強後，可能被認為已準備好考試。"},{"en":"Judgement may change when new evidence is found.","zh":"當新證據出現，判斷可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how people assess or classify something.","zh":"這個短語描述人們如何評估或分類某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"too far from","meaning":"距離……太遠","examples":[{"en":"The object seemed too far from the sun to be a normal comet.","zh":"該物體似乎距離太陽太遠，不像正常彗星。"},{"en":"Too far from something means at a distance beyond what is expected or suitable.","zh":"too far from 某物，指距離超出預期或合適範圍。"},{"en":"A student living too far from school may need to take two buses every morning.","zh":"住得離學校太遠的學生可能每天早上要乘兩程巴士。"},{"en":"Distance can make an explanation unlikely if it does not match normal patterns.","zh":"如果距離不符合正常模式，就會令某解釋不大可能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes excessive distance.","zh":"這個短語描述距離過遠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"most important find","meaning":"最重要發現","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether the discovery was the most important find of three centuries.","zh":"題目問這項發現是否為三個世紀以來最重要發現。"},{"en":"The most important find means the discovery with the greatest value or impact.","zh":"most important find 指具有最大價值或影響的發現。"},{"en":"A lost medical record may be the most important find in a hospital investigation.","zh":"遺失的醫療記錄可能是醫院調查中最重要發現。"},{"en":"Important finds can change understanding, policy or future research.","zh":"重要發現可以改變理解、政策或未來研究。"},{"en":"The phrase ranks a discovery above others in significance.","zh":"這個短語把某項發現按重要性排在其他發現之上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the last three hundred years","meaning":"過去三百年","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to the most important find of the last three hundred years.","zh":"該陳述指過去三百年中最重要的發現。"},{"en":"The last three hundred years means the most recent period of three centuries.","zh":"the last three hundred years 指最近三個世紀的時期。"},{"en":"A historian may study changes in education over the last three hundred years.","zh":"歷史學家可能研究過去三百年的教育變化。"},{"en":"A long time span helps show whether an event is unusually important.","zh":"長時間跨度幫助顯示某事件是否異常重要。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a broad historical comparison period.","zh":"這個短語給出廣闊歷史比較時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete each of the following statements","meaning":"完成以下每項陳述","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete each of the following statements with a name.","zh":"考生用一個名字完成以下每項陳述。"},{"en":"To complete each of the following statements means to fill the blank in every sentence listed below.","zh":"complete each of the following statements 指填寫下方每句句子的空格。"},{"en":"In a reading task, students may complete each statement by choosing a word from the passage.","zh":"在閱讀題中，學生可能透過從文章選詞來完成每項陳述。"},{"en":"They must check grammar and meaning before writing the answer.","zh":"他們寫答案前必須檢查文法和意思。"},{"en":"The phrase is an exam instruction for sentence completion.","zh":"這個短語是句子填空的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"with a name from","meaning":"用來自……的名字","examples":[{"en":"The answers should be names from the Reading Passage.","zh":"答案應是來自閱讀文章的名字。"},{"en":"With a name from the passage means using a person’s or object’s name that appears in the text.","zh":"with a name from the passage 指使用文本中出現的人名或物名。"},{"en":"If a question asks for a name from the passage, students should not invent one.","zh":"如果題目要求用文章中的名字，學生不應自創一個。"},{"en":"Looking for capital letters can help candidates locate possible names.","zh":"尋找大寫字母可以幫助考生定位可能的名字。"},{"en":"The phrase tells students the source and type of answer required.","zh":"這個短語告訴學生答案來源和類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the suggested names for","meaning":"為……建議的名稱","examples":[{"en":"The suggested names for the new planet changed over time.","zh":"為新行星建議的名稱隨時間改變。"},{"en":"The suggested names for something are the names people propose before one is finally chosen.","zh":"suggested names for 某物，是人們在最終選定前提出的名稱。"},{"en":"A class may list suggested names for a new school magazine.","zh":"一班學生可能列出為新校刊建議的名稱。"},{"en":"Suggested names can change as different people offer opinions.","zh":"隨着不同人提出意見，建議名稱可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to possible names, not necessarily the final name.","zh":"這個短語指可能名稱，不一定是最終名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"begin with","meaning":"以……開始","examples":[{"en":"The suggested names for the planet began with georgium sidus.","zh":"為這顆行星建議的名稱以 georgium sidus 開始。"},{"en":"To begin with something means to start with that first item or stage.","zh":"begin with 某事，指以該第一項或階段開始。"},{"en":"A lesson may begin with a short quiz before moving to new grammar.","zh":"一堂課可能以短測開始，然後進入新文法。"},{"en":"The first item can set the direction for what follows.","zh":"第一項可以設定之後的方向。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the starting point of a sequence.","zh":"這個短語指出序列的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"followed by","meaning":"接着是","examples":[{"en":"The first suggested name was followed by another temporary name.","zh":"第一個建議名稱之後接着是另一個臨時名稱。"},{"en":"Followed by means coming after something in time, order or sequence.","zh":"followed by 指在時間、次序或序列上接在某事之後。"},{"en":"The school assembly was followed by a class discussion.","zh":"學校早會之後接着是班級討論。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show the order in which events or items appear.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示事件或項目出現的次序。"},{"en":"It means one thing comes next after another.","zh":"它的意思是一件事接在另一件事後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"settle on","meaning":"最終選定","examples":[{"en":"Astronomers finally settled on the name Uranus.","zh":"天文學家最終選定 Uranus 這個名稱。"},{"en":"To settle on something means to decide on it after considering other options.","zh":"settle on 某物，指考慮其他選項後決定採用它。"},{"en":"A class may settle on Friday as the best day for a picnic.","zh":"一班學生可能最終選定星期五作為野餐最佳日子。"},{"en":"People settle on a choice when discussion ends and one option is accepted.","zh":"當討論結束並接受一個選項，人們就作出最終決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reaching a final decision.","zh":"這個短語描述達成最後決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"first five rings","meaning":"最初五個環","examples":[{"en":"The first five rings around Uranus were discovered in 1977.","zh":"天王星周圍最初五個環於1977年被發現。"},{"en":"The first five rings means the earliest group of five rings discovered or listed.","zh":"first five rings 指最早被發現或列出的五個環。"},{"en":"A science worksheet may ask students to identify the first five elements in the periodic table.","zh":"科學工作紙可能要求學生辨認元素週期表中最初五個元素。"},{"en":"Numbering discoveries helps readers follow the order of findings.","zh":"為發現編號幫助讀者理解發現次序。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an initial set of five rings.","zh":"這個短語指最初一組五個環。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"around Uranus","meaning":"圍繞天王星","examples":[{"en":"Several rings were discovered around Uranus.","zh":"幾個環被發現圍繞天王星。"},{"en":"Around Uranus means surrounding or orbiting the planet Uranus.","zh":"around Uranus 指包圍或繞着天王星運行。"},{"en":"A diagram may show moons and rings around Uranus to explain its system.","zh":"圖表可能顯示圍繞天王星的衛星和環，以解釋其系統。"},{"en":"Objects around a planet can reveal how gravity shapes movement in space.","zh":"行星周圍的物體可以揭示重力如何塑造太空中的運動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes position in relation to Uranus.","zh":"這個短語描述相對於天王星的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"closest to the surface of","meaning":"最接近……表面的","examples":[{"en":"Miranda was once believed to be the moon closest to the surface of Uranus.","zh":"天衛五曾被認為是最接近天王星表面的衛星。"},{"en":"Closest to the surface of something means nearest to its outer layer or body.","zh":"closest to the surface of 某物，指最接近其外層或本體。"},{"en":"The classroom closest to the entrance is usually easiest for visitors to find.","zh":"最接近入口的課室通常最容易讓訪客找到。"},{"en":"Being closest may matter because distance affects visibility, travel time or orbit.","zh":"最接近可能很重要，因為距離影響可見性、旅行時間或軌道。"},{"en":"The phrase compares position by nearness.","zh":"這個短語透過接近程度比較位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be believed to be","meaning":"被認為是","examples":[{"en":"Miranda was believed to be the innermost moon before 1986.","zh":"在1986年前，天衛五被認為是最內側的衛星。"},{"en":"To be believed to be something means people thought it was that thing, though it might later prove different.","zh":"be believed to be 某事，指人們以為它是那樣，雖然之後可能證明不同。"},{"en":"A student may be believed to be absent until the teacher sees her in the library.","zh":"老師在圖書館看見學生前，可能以為她缺席。"},{"en":"Beliefs can change when new information becomes available.","zh":"當新資訊出現，信念可以改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what people accepted as true at a certain time.","zh":"這個短語描述人們在某時接受為真的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 137 - The Discovery of Uranus.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 138":[{"front":"beyond the Blue Line","meaning":"藍線以外","examples":[{"en":"The passage explores journeys beyond the Blue Line into the Pacific.","zh":"篇章探討進入太平洋藍線以外的航程。"},{"en":"Beyond the Blue Line means past a known boundary into less familiar waters.","zh":"藍線以外，是指越過已知界線，進入較陌生的水域。"},{"en":"Early sailors who went beyond the Blue Line entered a world full of uncertainty.","zh":"早期航海者前往藍線以外時，進入了一個充滿不確定的世界。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests exploration, risk and movement into the unknown.","zh":"這個短語暗示探索、風險和走向未知。"},{"en":"It can be used figuratively for going beyond familiar limits.","zh":"它也可比喻超越熟悉的界限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the thrill of","meaning":"……的刺激感","examples":[{"en":"Much of the thrill of distant travel rests on difference.","zh":"遠行的大部分刺激感建基於差異。"},{"en":"The thrill of something is the excitement or strong pleasure it gives.","zh":"某事的刺激感，是它帶來的興奮或強烈愉悅。"},{"en":"The thrill of sailing across open water comes partly from danger and discovery.","zh":"橫越開放水域的刺激感部分來自危險和發現。"},{"en":"Travellers often seek the thrill of seeing places unlike home.","zh":"旅人常尋求看見與家鄉不同地方的刺激感。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on emotional excitement.","zh":"這個短語聚焦情感上的興奮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"venture to","meaning":"冒險前往……","examples":[{"en":"Explorers ventured to the far side of the world.","zh":"探險者冒險前往世界的另一端。"},{"en":"To venture to a place means to go there despite risk or uncertainty.","zh":"冒險前往某地，是指即使有風險或不確定仍前往。"},{"en":"The sailors ventured to islands that no one in their community had seen before.","zh":"航海者冒險前往社群中無人見過的島嶼。"},{"en":"People venture to unknown places when curiosity is stronger than fear.","zh":"當好奇心勝過恐懼，人們便會冒險前往未知地方。"},{"en":"This verb suggests courage and risk-taking.","zh":"這個動詞暗示勇氣和冒險精神。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the far side of the world","meaning":"世界的另一端","examples":[{"en":"Cook travelled to the far side of the world.","zh":"Cook 航行到世界的另一端。"},{"en":"The far side of the world means a very distant place, far from one’s home or known world.","zh":"世界的另一端，是指離自己的家或已知世界非常遙遠的地方。"},{"en":"For Europeans in the eighteenth century, many Pacific islands seemed like the far side of the world.","zh":"對十八世紀歐洲人而言，許多太平洋島嶼像是世界的另一端。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises distance and unfamiliarity.","zh":"這個短語強調距離和陌生感。"},{"en":"It is often used to make travel sound dramatic.","zh":"它常用來令旅程聽起來更具戲劇性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rest on","meaning":"取決於；建基於","examples":[{"en":"The thrill of travel rests on the romance of difference.","zh":"旅行的刺激感建基於差異帶來的浪漫感。"},{"en":"To rest on something means to depend on it as a foundation.","zh":"建基於某事，是指依靠它作為基礎。"},{"en":"The argument rests on the idea that early sailors were highly skilled.","zh":"這個論點建基於早期航海者技術高超這個想法。"},{"en":"A theory may rest on one important piece of evidence.","zh":"一個理論可能建基於一項重要證據。"},{"en":"This phrase means something is built upon another idea or condition.","zh":"這個短語表示某事建立在另一想法或條件之上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the romance of difference","meaning":"差異帶來的浪漫感","examples":[{"en":"The romance of difference makes distant travel exciting.","zh":"差異帶來的浪漫感令遠行變得刺激。"},{"en":"The romance of difference is the attractive feeling created by encountering unfamiliar people, places and customs.","zh":"差異帶來的浪漫感，是遇見陌生人物、地方和習俗所產生的吸引感。"},{"en":"For explorers, the romance of difference lay in hearing new languages and seeing new landscapes.","zh":"對探險者而言，差異的浪漫感在於聽見新語言和看見新景觀。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that unfamiliarity can feel beautiful and exciting.","zh":"這個短語暗示陌生感可以美麗而令人興奮。"},{"en":"It links travel with imagination and desire.","zh":"它把旅行與想像和渴望連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"feel a certain sympathy for","meaning":"對……有幾分同情","examples":[{"en":"One may feel a certain sympathy for Captain James Cook.","zh":"人們可能對 James Cook 船長有幾分同情。"},{"en":"To feel a certain sympathy for someone means to partly understand or feel sorry for them.","zh":"對某人有幾分同情，是指部分理解他或為他感到可惜。"},{"en":"Readers may feel a certain sympathy for Cook when he expected difference but found familiarity.","zh":"當 Cook 期待差異卻發現熟悉感時，讀者可能對他有幾分同情。"},{"en":"The phrase is mild and does not suggest complete agreement.","zh":"這個短語語氣溫和，不表示完全認同。"},{"en":"It expresses limited understanding or pity.","zh":"它表達有限度的理解或憐憫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on the day that","meaning":"在……那一天","examples":[{"en":"Cook was surprised on the day that he reached Hawaii.","zh":"Cook 在抵達夏威夷那一天感到驚訝。"},{"en":"On the day that means at the time when a particular event happened.","zh":"在某事那一天，是指某特定事件發生的時候。"},{"en":"On the day that the sailors reached land, they saw canoes approaching.","zh":"航海者抵達陸地那一天，他們看見獨木舟靠近。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a reaction with a specific date or event.","zh":"這個短語把反應與特定日期或事件連接起來。"},{"en":"It is useful for organising narrative time.","zh":"它適合用來整理敘事時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"third expedition to","meaning":"第三次前往……的遠征","examples":[{"en":"Cook was on his third expedition to the Pacific.","zh":"Cook 正在第三次前往太平洋的遠征中。"},{"en":"A third expedition to a place is the third organised journey made there for exploration or research.","zh":"第三次前往某地的遠征，是第三次有組織地前往該地作探索或研究。"},{"en":"The scientist’s third expedition to the island focused on ancient pottery.","zh":"這位科學家第三次前往該島的遠征聚焦古代陶器。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests repeated exploration over time.","zh":"這個短語暗示一段時間內反覆探索。"},{"en":"It identifies both sequence and destination.","zh":"它同時指出次序和目的地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"British navigator","meaning":"英國航海家","examples":[{"en":"Captain James Cook was a British navigator.","zh":"James Cook 船長是一位英國航海家。"},{"en":"A British navigator is a person from Britain skilled in planning and directing sea journeys.","zh":"英國航海家是來自英國、擅長規劃和指揮海上航程的人。"},{"en":"A navigator must understand maps, winds, currents and direction.","zh":"航海家必須理解地圖、風向、洋流和方向。"},{"en":"Cook is remembered as a British navigator because of his Pacific voyages.","zh":"Cook 因其太平洋航行而被記為英國航海家。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies nationality and seafaring role.","zh":"這個短語指出國籍和航海角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"scores of islands","meaning":"數十個島嶼","examples":[{"en":"Cook had explored scores of islands across the Pacific.","zh":"Cook 曾探索太平洋上數十個島嶼。"},{"en":"Scores of islands means many islands, usually dozens of them.","zh":"數十個島嶼，是指很多島嶼，通常是幾十個。"},{"en":"The voyagers passed scores of islands during their journey eastward.","zh":"航海者在向東航行期間經過數十個島嶼。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a sense of large number without an exact figure.","zh":"這個短語在不給精確數字下表達數量龐大。"},{"en":"It is stronger than saying several islands.","zh":"它比說幾個島嶼更強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"across the breadth of","meaning":"橫跨……的廣闊範圍","examples":[{"en":"He explored islands across the breadth of the sea.","zh":"他探索了橫跨海洋廣闊範圍的島嶼。"},{"en":"Across the breadth of something means across its full width or wide extent.","zh":"橫跨某物的廣闊範圍，是指橫越其完整寬度或廣泛區域。"},{"en":"The expedition collected data across the breadth of the ocean.","zh":"遠征隊在橫跨海洋的廣闊範圍收集數據。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses wide geographical coverage.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛地理覆蓋。"},{"en":"It suggests travel from one side of a large area to another.","zh":"它暗示由大區域一側移動到另一側。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lush New Zealand","meaning":"草木茂盛的新西蘭","examples":[{"en":"Cook travelled from lush New Zealand to Easter Island.","zh":"Cook 從草木茂盛的新西蘭航行到復活節島。"},{"en":"Lush New Zealand means New Zealand described as green, fertile and full of vegetation.","zh":"草木茂盛的新西蘭，是把新西蘭描述為翠綠、肥沃且植被豐富。"},{"en":"Lush forests and wet valleys made the island look rich in plant life.","zh":"茂密森林和潮濕山谷令島嶼看起來植物生命豐富。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts green landscapes with barren or lonely places.","zh":"這個短語把綠色景觀與荒涼或孤寂地方作對比。"},{"en":"It uses natural scenery to create atmosphere.","zh":"它利用自然景色營造氣氛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lonely wastes of","meaning":"荒涼偏僻之地","examples":[{"en":"Cook explored the lonely wastes of Easter Island.","zh":"Cook 探索復活節島的荒涼偏僻之地。"},{"en":"Lonely wastes are empty, remote and desolate places.","zh":"荒涼偏僻之地，是空曠、遙遠而荒蕪的地方。"},{"en":"To sailors, an isolated island could seem like lonely wastes after weeks at sea.","zh":"對航海者而言，經過數星期海上航行後，孤島可能像荒涼偏僻之地。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a sense of isolation and barrenness.","zh":"這個短語營造孤立和荒蕪感。"},{"en":"It is more poetic than simply saying remote land.","zh":"它比單純說偏遠土地更具文學色彩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"latest voyage","meaning":"最近一次航行","examples":[{"en":"His latest voyage took him far north.","zh":"他最近一次航行把他帶到很北方。"},{"en":"Latest voyage means the most recent sea journey.","zh":"最近一次航行，是指最近的海上旅程。"},{"en":"The captain’s latest voyage revealed several unknown islands.","zh":"船長最近一次航行揭示了幾個未知島嶼。"},{"en":"This phrase places the journey in a sequence of earlier travels.","zh":"這個短語把旅程放在一連串早前旅行之中。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing explorers with many expeditions.","zh":"它適合描述有多次遠征的探險者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"take someone thousands of miles","meaning":"帶某人航行數千英里","examples":[{"en":"The voyage took Cook thousands of miles north.","zh":"這次航行帶 Cook 向北航行數千英里。"},{"en":"To take someone thousands of miles means to carry or lead them over a very long distance.","zh":"帶某人數千英里，是指帶領或運送某人越過極長距離。"},{"en":"The canoe voyage took the sailors thousands of miles across open sea.","zh":"獨木舟航程帶航海者橫越開放海域數千英里。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the scale of a journey.","zh":"這個短語強調旅程規模。"},{"en":"It can describe travel by ship, plane or overland route.","zh":"它可以描述船、飛機或陸路旅程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"archipelago","meaning":"群島","examples":[{"en":"Cook reached an archipelago that was extremely remote.","zh":"Cook 抵達一個極其偏遠的群島。"},{"en":"An archipelago is a group or chain of islands.","zh":"群島是一組或一連串島嶼。"},{"en":"The sailors moved slowly through the archipelago, stopping at several small islands.","zh":"航海者慢慢穿越群島，停靠幾個小島。"},{"en":"Archipelagoes can help migration because islands provide stepping stones.","zh":"群島能幫助遷徙，因為島嶼提供跳板。"},{"en":"This word refers to island groups, not one single island.","zh":"這個詞指島嶼群，而不是單一島嶼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"so remote that","meaning":"偏遠得……","examples":[{"en":"The archipelago was so remote that even Tahitians knew nothing about it.","zh":"該群島偏遠得連塔希提人也對它一無所知。"},{"en":"So remote that means distant enough to cause a particular result.","zh":"偏遠得，是指遙遠到造成某個結果。"},{"en":"The island was so remote that no trading ship visited it for years.","zh":"該島偏遠得多年沒有商船到訪。"},{"en":"This structure connects degree with consequence.","zh":"這個結構把程度與後果連接起來。"},{"en":"It highlights extreme isolation.","zh":"它突出極端孤立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"old Polynesians","meaning":"老一輩波利尼西亞人","examples":[{"en":"Even the old Polynesians on Tahiti knew nothing about the islands.","zh":"甚至塔希提島上的老一輩波利尼西亞人也對那些島嶼一無所知。"},{"en":"Old Polynesians means elderly Polynesian people with long memories and traditional knowledge.","zh":"老一輩波利尼西亞人，是指擁有長久記憶和傳統知識的年長波利尼西亞人。"},{"en":"Old Polynesians might preserve stories about voyages and ancestors.","zh":"老一輩波利尼西亞人可能保存有關航行和祖先的故事。"},{"en":"If even old people knew nothing of the islands, the place must have seemed extremely remote.","zh":"如果連老人也不知道那些島嶼，那地方一定顯得極其偏遠。"},{"en":"This phrase points to experienced members of Polynesian society.","zh":"這個短語指波利尼西亞社會中經驗豐富的成員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"come paddling out","meaning":"划槳出來","examples":[{"en":"The natives came paddling out in their canoes.","zh":"當地人乘着獨木舟划槳出來。"},{"en":"To come paddling out means to move out across water by using paddles.","zh":"划槳出來，是指用槳划水而向外移動。"},{"en":"Islanders came paddling out to meet the approaching ship.","zh":"島民划槳出來迎接接近的船隻。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a vivid image of canoes moving from shore.","zh":"這個短語生動描繪獨木舟由岸邊駛出的畫面。"},{"en":"It describes movement by human-powered boats.","zh":"它描述以人力划動的船隻移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in their canoes","meaning":"乘坐他們的獨木舟","examples":[{"en":"The Hawaiians came out in their canoes.","zh":"夏威夷人乘坐他們的獨木舟出來。"},{"en":"In their canoes means travelling by small traditional boats.","zh":"乘坐他們的獨木舟，是指乘坐小型傳統船隻前進。"},{"en":"The villagers crossed the lagoon in their canoes.","zh":"村民乘坐獨木舟橫過潟湖。"},{"en":"Canoes were essential for fishing, travel and exploration.","zh":"獨木舟對捕魚、旅行和探索非常重要。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the means of movement.","zh":"這個短語指出移動工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"greet someone in","meaning":"以……向某人打招呼","examples":[{"en":"The natives greeted Cook in a familiar tongue.","zh":"當地人以熟悉的語言向 Cook 打招呼。"},{"en":"To greet someone in a language means to welcome or speak to them using that language.","zh":"以某語言向某人打招呼，是指用該語言歡迎或與某人說話。"},{"en":"The islanders greeted the visitors in words the sailors understood.","zh":"島民用航海者聽得懂的話向訪客打招呼。"},{"en":"A familiar greeting can surprise travellers in a distant place.","zh":"在遙遠地方聽到熟悉問候，會令旅人驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase links welcome with language.","zh":"這個短語把歡迎與語言連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a familiar tongue","meaning":"熟悉的語言","examples":[{"en":"Cook heard a familiar tongue in Hawaii.","zh":"Cook 在夏威夷聽到一種熟悉的語言。"},{"en":"A familiar tongue is a language or way of speaking that one recognises.","zh":"熟悉的語言，是某人認得的語言或說話方式。"},{"en":"After months abroad, hearing a familiar tongue can feel comforting.","zh":"在外地數月後，聽見熟悉語言會令人感到安慰。"},{"en":"Cook was surprised because the language sounded like ones he had heard elsewhere.","zh":"Cook 感到驚訝，因為該語言聽起來像他在其他地方聽過的語言。"},{"en":"This phrase is a literary way to say familiar language.","zh":"這個短語是 familiar language 的文學說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"virtually every","meaning":"幾乎每一個……","examples":[{"en":"Cook had heard the language on virtually every inhabited island.","zh":"Cook 在幾乎每一個有人居住的島嶼上都聽過這種語言。"},{"en":"Virtually every means almost every, with very few exceptions.","zh":"幾乎每一個，是指差不多每一個，只有極少例外。"},{"en":"The same style of pottery appeared on virtually every site the team studied.","zh":"研究團隊研究的幾乎每一個遺址都出現相同陶器風格。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a pattern that is nearly universal.","zh":"這個短語強調幾乎普遍的模式。"},{"en":"It is slightly less absolute than every.","zh":"它比 every 稍微不那麼絕對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mote of inhabited land","meaning":"有人居住的小島點","examples":[{"en":"Cook heard the language on every mote of inhabited land he had visited.","zh":"Cook 在他到訪過的每一個有人居住的小島點都聽過這種語言。"},{"en":"A mote of inhabited land means a tiny piece of land where people live.","zh":"有人居住的小島點，是指有人生活的一小片土地。"},{"en":"Even a small island village can be described poetically as a mote of inhabited land.","zh":"即使一個小島村落，也可以較文學地稱為有人居住的小島點。"},{"en":"The phrase makes the islands sound tiny in the vast ocean.","zh":"這個短語令島嶼在浩瀚海洋中顯得很細小。"},{"en":"It is literary and descriptive.","zh":"它具有文學和描寫色彩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"marvel at","meaning":"對……感到驚奇","examples":[{"en":"Cook marvelled at the ubiquity of Pacific language and culture.","zh":"Cook 對太平洋語言和文化無處不在感到驚奇。"},{"en":"To marvel at something means to feel great wonder or amazement at it.","zh":"對某事感到驚奇，是指因它而感到很大驚訝或讚嘆。"},{"en":"Archaeologists marvelled at how far the pottery style had spread.","zh":"考古學家對陶器風格傳播得如此遙遠感到驚奇。"},{"en":"People marvel when something seems surprising, impressive or difficult to explain.","zh":"當某事令人意外、印象深刻或難以解釋，人們會感到驚奇。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses strong admiration and surprise.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈讚嘆和驚訝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ubiquity of","meaning":"……無處不在","examples":[{"en":"Cook wondered about the ubiquity of this Pacific language.","zh":"Cook 思索這種太平洋語言為何無處不在。"},{"en":"The ubiquity of something means the fact that it appears everywhere or in many places.","zh":"某事無處不在，是指它出現在各處或許多地方。"},{"en":"The ubiquity of similar words across islands suggested a shared history.","zh":"相似詞語在各島無處不在，暗示共同歷史。"},{"en":"Ubiquity can be surprising when places are separated by huge distances.","zh":"當地方被巨大距離分隔，無處不在的現象會令人驚訝。"},{"en":"This word describes widespread presence.","zh":"這個詞描述廣泛存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Pacific language and culture","meaning":"太平洋語言和文化","examples":[{"en":"Cook noticed the spread of Pacific language and culture.","zh":"Cook 注意到太平洋語言和文化的傳播。"},{"en":"Pacific language and culture refers to the related languages, customs and practices found across Pacific islands.","zh":"太平洋語言和文化，是指太平洋島嶼上相關的語言、習俗和做法。"},{"en":"Similar words and rituals showed links in Pacific language and culture.","zh":"相似詞語和儀式顯示太平洋語言和文化之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"The spread of culture raised questions about ancient migration.","zh":"文化傳播引發有關古代遷徙的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase connects speech, customs and identity.","zh":"這個短語連接語言、習俗和身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"wonder in one’s journal","meaning":"在日記中思索","examples":[{"en":"Cook wondered in his journal how the nation had spread so far.","zh":"Cook 在日記中思索這個民族如何傳播得如此遙遠。"},{"en":"To wonder in one’s journal means to record a question or reflection in a diary or log.","zh":"在日記中思索，是指在日記或航海日誌中記錄問題或反思。"},{"en":"The explorer wondered in his journal whether the islands had been settled from the west.","zh":"探險者在日記中思索這些島嶼是否由西方移民定居。"},{"en":"Journals preserve thoughts that later become important evidence.","zh":"日記保存思想，後來可能成為重要證據。"},{"en":"This phrase links private reflection with written record.","zh":"這個短語把私人思考與書面紀錄連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"account for","meaning":"解釋","examples":[{"en":"Cook asked how people could account for this nation’s spread.","zh":"Cook 問人們如何解釋這個民族的傳播。"},{"en":"To account for something means to explain why it happened.","zh":"解釋某事，是指說明它為何發生。"},{"en":"Scientists tried to account for the spread of similar pottery across distant islands.","zh":"科學家嘗試解釋相似陶器如何散佈到遙遠島嶼。"},{"en":"A good explanation must account for both language and archaeology.","zh":"好解釋必須同時解釋語言和考古證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in analytical writing.","zh":"這個短語常見於分析寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"spread itself so far over","meaning":"在……如此廣泛地擴散","examples":[{"en":"The nation had spread itself so far over the vast ocean.","zh":"這個民族已在浩瀚海洋上如此廣泛地擴散。"},{"en":"To spread itself so far over an area means to expand across a very wide space.","zh":"在某範圍如此廣泛地擴散，是指擴展到非常廣闊的空間。"},{"en":"The culture spread itself so far over the Pacific that Cook found related languages everywhere.","zh":"這種文化在太平洋上如此廣泛地擴散，以致 Cook 到處聽見相關語言。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises extraordinary geographical reach.","zh":"這個短語強調非凡的地理範圍。"},{"en":"It is often used when expansion seems difficult to explain.","zh":"它常用於擴展難以解釋的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"vast ocean","meaning":"浩瀚海洋","examples":[{"en":"The Polynesians spread across a vast ocean.","zh":"波利尼西亞人在浩瀚海洋中擴散。"},{"en":"A vast ocean is an extremely large area of sea.","zh":"浩瀚海洋是極其廣大的海域。"},{"en":"Crossing a vast ocean without modern instruments required great skill.","zh":"在沒有現代儀器下橫越浩瀚海洋，需要高超技術。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights distance, danger and isolation.","zh":"這個短語突出距離、危險和孤立。"},{"en":"It makes the achievement of early sailors seem more impressive.","zh":"它令早期航海者的成就顯得更了不起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"flow from","meaning":"由……引申而來","examples":[{"en":"Several questions flow from Cook’s observation.","zh":"幾個問題由 Cook 的觀察引申而來。"},{"en":"To flow from something means to arise naturally from it.","zh":"由某事引申而來，是指自然從它產生。"},{"en":"Many research questions flow from the discovery of the cemetery.","zh":"許多研究問題由墓地的發現引申而來。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one idea leads to others.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個想法帶出其他想法。"},{"en":"It is useful for explaining logical development.","zh":"它適合解釋邏輯發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"tantalize inquiring minds","meaning":"令好奇的頭腦着迷","examples":[{"en":"The question has tantalized inquiring minds for centuries.","zh":"這個問題數個世紀以來令好奇求知的人着迷。"},{"en":"To tantalize inquiring minds means to attract curious people by being fascinating but hard to solve.","zh":"令好奇的頭腦着迷，是指因問題迷人卻難解而吸引好奇者。"},{"en":"The mystery of how the sailors navigated has tantalized scholars for generations.","zh":"航海者如何導航的謎團數代以來令學者着迷。"},{"en":"A tantalizing question invites investigation but does not give easy answers.","zh":"耐人尋味的問題會引發研究，但不會給出容易答案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intellectual fascination.","zh":"這個短語描述智性上的迷戀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"inquiring minds","meaning":"好奇求知的人","examples":[{"en":"Inquiring minds have long wondered about Pacific migration.","zh":"好奇求知的人長久以來都思索太平洋遷徙問題。"},{"en":"Inquiring minds are curious people who want to understand and investigate.","zh":"好奇求知的人，是想理解和調查事情的好奇者。"},{"en":"Inquiring minds ask why similar cultures appeared on distant islands.","zh":"好奇求知的人會問為何相似文化出現在遙遠島嶼上。"},{"en":"The phrase often refers to scholars, explorers or thoughtful readers.","zh":"這個短語常指學者、探險者或有思想的讀者。"},{"en":"It stresses curiosity and the desire for knowledge.","zh":"它強調好奇心和求知欲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"for centuries","meaning":"數個世紀以來","examples":[{"en":"The mystery has interested scholars for centuries.","zh":"這個謎團數個世紀以來一直令學者感興趣。"},{"en":"For centuries means for hundreds of years.","zh":"數個世紀以來，是指持續數百年。"},{"en":"The origins of Polynesian migration have been debated for centuries.","zh":"波利尼西亞遷徙的起源數個世紀以來一直被討論。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a question has a long history.","zh":"這個短語顯示某問題有悠久歷史。"},{"en":"It gives a strong sense of time depth.","zh":"它給人強烈時間深度感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"amazing seafarers","meaning":"了不起的航海者","examples":[{"en":"Researchers asked who these amazing seafarers were.","zh":"研究人員追問這些了不起的航海者是誰。"},{"en":"Amazing seafarers are sailors whose skill, courage or achievements seem extraordinary.","zh":"了不起的航海者，是技能、勇氣或成就非凡的水手。"},{"en":"The Lapita were amazing seafarers because they crossed open ocean in canoes.","zh":"拉皮塔人是了不起的航海者，因為他們乘獨木舟橫越開放海洋。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses admiration for maritime ability.","zh":"這個短語表達對航海能力的讚嘆。"},{"en":"It highlights both navigation and bravery.","zh":"它同時突出導航和勇氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"start more than 3,000 years ago","meaning":"始於三千多年前","examples":[{"en":"The migration started more than 3,000 years ago.","zh":"這次遷徙始於三千多年前。"},{"en":"To start more than 3,000 years ago means to begin earlier than three millennia before now.","zh":"始於三千多年前，是指開始於距今超過三千年以前。"},{"en":"The settlement of many Pacific islands started more than 3,000 years ago.","zh":"許多太平洋島嶼的定居始於三千多年前。"},{"en":"This phrase places the event in deep history.","zh":"這個短語把事件放在久遠歷史中。"},{"en":"It shows that the migration was ancient.","zh":"它顯示遷徙十分古老。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Neolithic people","meaning":"新石器時代的人","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita were a Neolithic people with simple canoes.","zh":"拉皮塔人是擁有簡單獨木舟的新石器時代人群。"},{"en":"Neolithic people were people from the later Stone Age, often associated with farming and stone tools.","zh":"新石器時代的人，是石器時代後期的人，通常與農耕和石器工具相關。"},{"en":"A Neolithic people might grow crops, keep animals and use polished stone tools.","zh":"新石器時代的人可能種植作物、飼養動物並使用磨製石器。"},{"en":"The phrase places the Lapita in a prehistoric technological period.","zh":"這個短語把拉皮塔人放在史前技術時期中。"},{"en":"It contrasts ancient societies with modern ones.","zh":"它把古代社會與現代社會作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"navigation gear","meaning":"導航設備","examples":[{"en":"The early sailors had no modern navigation gear.","zh":"早期航海者沒有現代導航設備。"},{"en":"Navigation gear is equipment used to find direction and position while travelling.","zh":"導航設備是旅行時用來尋找方向和位置的工具。"},{"en":"Compasses, maps and GPS devices are navigation gear.","zh":"指南針、地圖和 GPS 裝置都是導航設備。"},{"en":"The Lapita’s achievement is impressive because they lacked modern navigation gear.","zh":"拉皮塔人的成就令人印象深刻，因為他們缺乏現代導航設備。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to tools for finding one’s way.","zh":"這個短語指尋路工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"manage to","meaning":"設法做到","examples":[{"en":"They managed to find and colonize distant islands.","zh":"他們設法找到並殖民遙遠島嶼。"},{"en":"To manage to do something means to succeed in doing it despite difficulty.","zh":"設法做到某事，是指儘管困難仍成功做到。"},{"en":"The sailors managed to cross the open sea without modern instruments.","zh":"航海者在沒有現代儀器下設法橫越開放海域。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests effort and achievement.","zh":"這個短語暗示努力和成就。"},{"en":"It is often used when success was not easy.","zh":"它常用於成功並不容易的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"let alone","meaning":"更不用說","examples":[{"en":"They found, let alone colonized, far-flung islands.","zh":"他們找到了遙遠分散的小島，更不用說還在島上定居。"},{"en":"Let alone means not to mention something even more difficult or surprising.","zh":"更不用說，是指還未提到更困難或更令人驚訝的事。"},{"en":"It was hard to find the islands, let alone settle families there.","zh":"找到那些島已經很難，更不用說還要讓家庭在那裡定居。"},{"en":"This phrase strengthens a comparison by adding a greater challenge.","zh":"這個短語透過加入更大挑戰來加強比較。"},{"en":"It often follows a negative or difficult idea.","zh":"它常接在否定或困難想法之後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"colonize islands","meaning":"殖民島嶼；在島上定居","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita colonized many islands across the Pacific.","zh":"拉皮塔人在太平洋上許多島嶼定居。"},{"en":"To colonize islands means to settle on them and establish communities there.","zh":"在島上定居，是指在島上落腳並建立社群。"},{"en":"Early voyagers colonized islands by bringing families, plants and animals.","zh":"早期航海者透過帶同家庭、植物和動物在島上定居。"},{"en":"Colonizing an island requires more than arrival; people must survive and reproduce there.","zh":"在島上定居不只是抵達；人們必須在那裡生存和繁衍。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to establishing settlement.","zh":"這個短語指建立聚落。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"far-flung island specks","meaning":"遙遠分散的小島","examples":[{"en":"The ocean contains hundreds of far-flung island specks.","zh":"海洋中有數以百計遙遠分散的小島。"},{"en":"Far-flung island specks are tiny islands scattered across great distances.","zh":"遙遠分散的小島，是散落在巨大距離中的細小島嶼。"},{"en":"From a ship, distant islands may seem like small specks on the horizon.","zh":"從船上看，遠方島嶼可能像地平線上的小點。"},{"en":"The phrase makes the Pacific seem huge and the islands very small.","zh":"這個短語令太平洋顯得巨大，而島嶼顯得很細小。"},{"en":"It emphasises the difficulty of finding land.","zh":"它強調尋找陸地的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"scattered across","meaning":"散佈於……","examples":[{"en":"The islands were scattered across a huge ocean.","zh":"這些島嶼散佈於巨大海洋之中。"},{"en":"Scattered across means spread out irregularly over an area.","zh":"散佈於某地，是指不規則地分布在某個範圍內。"},{"en":"Small villages were scattered across the mountains.","zh":"小村落散佈於山區。"},{"en":"Islands scattered across the sea are harder to find and connect.","zh":"散佈於海上的島嶼較難尋找和連接。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wide and uneven distribution.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛而不均勻的分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"span nearly a third of","meaning":"橫跨接近……三分之一","examples":[{"en":"The Pacific spans nearly a third of the globe.","zh":"太平洋橫跨接近地球三分之一。"},{"en":"To span nearly a third of something means to stretch across almost one third of it.","zh":"橫跨接近某物三分之一，是指延展接近其三分之一的範圍。"},{"en":"A desert might span nearly a third of a region.","zh":"沙漠可能橫跨某地區接近三分之一。"},{"en":"This phrase shows enormous scale.","zh":"這個短語顯示巨大規模。"},{"en":"It helps readers understand the size of the Pacific challenge.","zh":"它幫助讀者理解太平洋挑戰的大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the globe","meaning":"地球","examples":[{"en":"The Pacific covers nearly a third of the globe.","zh":"太平洋覆蓋接近地球三分之一。"},{"en":"The globe means the Earth.","zh":"地球即我們生活的星球。"},{"en":"Ocean currents move heat around the globe.","zh":"洋流把熱量帶到地球各處。"},{"en":"This word often gives a global perspective.","zh":"這個詞常帶出全球視角。"},{"en":"It is more formal or descriptive than simply saying the world.","zh":"它比簡單說 world 較正式或具描寫性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"answers have been slow in coming","meaning":"答案遲遲未出現","examples":[{"en":"Answers to these questions have been slow in coming.","zh":"這些問題的答案遲遲未出現。"},{"en":"Answers have been slow in coming means people have taken a long time to find explanations.","zh":"答案遲遲未出現，是指人們花了很長時間仍未找到解釋。"},{"en":"Scientific answers were slow in coming because the evidence was buried and rare.","zh":"科學答案遲遲未出現，因為證據被埋藏且十分稀少。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests delay and difficulty.","zh":"這個短語暗示延遲和困難。"},{"en":"It is often used for long-standing mysteries.","zh":"它常用於長期未解之謎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"startling archaeological find","meaning":"令人震驚的考古發現","examples":[{"en":"A startling archaeological find was made on Éfaté.","zh":"Éfaté 島上出現一項令人震驚的考古發現。"},{"en":"A startling archaeological find is a surprising discovery of ancient remains or artefacts.","zh":"令人震驚的考古發現，是令人驚訝的古代遺存或文物發現。"},{"en":"The cemetery was a startling archaeological find because it revealed early voyagers.","zh":"該墓地是令人震驚的考古發現，因為它揭示早期航海者。"},{"en":"Such discoveries can change what researchers believe about the past.","zh":"這類發現可以改變研究人員對過去的看法。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses surprise and historical importance.","zh":"這個短語強調驚訝和歷史重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"reveal","meaning":"揭示","examples":[{"en":"The find revealed an ancient seafaring people.","zh":"這項發現揭示了一個古代航海民族。"},{"en":"To reveal something means to show or make it known.","zh":"揭示，是指顯示或使某事被知道。"},{"en":"The pottery revealed links between distant islands.","zh":"陶器揭示遙遠島嶼之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"Archaeology can reveal histories that were never written down.","zh":"考古可以揭示從未被寫下來的歷史。"},{"en":"This verb is common when discoveries provide new knowledge.","zh":"這個動詞常用於發現提供新知識時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ancient seafaring people","meaning":"古代航海民族","examples":[{"en":"The discovery revealed an ancient seafaring people.","zh":"這項發現揭示了一個古代航海民族。"},{"en":"An ancient seafaring people is an old culture or group skilled in sea travel.","zh":"古代航海民族，是擅長海上旅行的古老文化或群體。"},{"en":"The Lapita were an ancient seafaring people who crossed open water.","zh":"拉皮塔人是橫越開放水域的古代航海民族。"},{"en":"Such people depended on boats, winds and knowledge of the sea.","zh":"這類民族依賴船隻、風和海洋知識。"},{"en":"This phrase combines age with maritime skill.","zh":"這個短語結合古老年代與航海能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"distant ancestors","meaning":"遠祖","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita were distant ancestors of today’s Polynesians.","zh":"拉皮塔人是今日波利尼西亞人的遠祖。"},{"en":"Distant ancestors are people from far back in a family or cultural line.","zh":"遠祖是家族或文化血脈中很久以前的人。"},{"en":"Archaeologists study distant ancestors to understand modern populations.","zh":"考古學家研究遠祖，以理解現代人口。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a long historical connection.","zh":"這個短語暗示長遠歷史聯繫。"},{"en":"It links ancient people with present-day descendants.","zh":"它把古代人與今日後裔連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take one’s first steps into","meaning":"踏出通往……的第一步","examples":[{"en":"The early voyagers took their first steps into the unknown.","zh":"早期航海者踏出通往未知世界的第一步。"},{"en":"To take one’s first steps into something means to begin entering or exploring it.","zh":"踏出通往某事的第一步，是指開始進入或探索它。"},{"en":"A child takes her first steps into science by asking simple questions.","zh":"孩子透過提出簡單問題，踏出通往科學的第一步。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a beginning sound important and brave.","zh":"這個短語令開始顯得重要而勇敢。"},{"en":"It is often used for new fields or unknown territory.","zh":"它常用於新領域或未知領土。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the unknown","meaning":"未知世界","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita took their first steps into the unknown.","zh":"拉皮塔人踏出進入未知世界的第一步。"},{"en":"The unknown is something not yet known, understood or explored.","zh":"未知世界是尚未被知道、理解或探索的事物。"},{"en":"Sailing beyond visible land meant entering the unknown.","zh":"駛離可見陸地，意味着進入未知世界。"},{"en":"The phrase carries a sense of risk and discovery.","zh":"這個短語帶有風險和發現的感覺。"},{"en":"It can refer to places, futures or ideas.","zh":"它可以指地方、未來或想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"open a window into","meaning":"讓人了解……","examples":[{"en":"The discoveries opened a window into the world of early voyagers.","zh":"這些發現讓人了解早期航海者的世界。"},{"en":"To open a window into something means to give people a chance to understand it.","zh":"讓人了解某事，是指給人機會理解它。"},{"en":"Ancient bones opened a window into the lives of the first settlers.","zh":"古代骨骸讓人了解最早定居者的生活。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests partial but valuable insight.","zh":"這個短語暗示部分但有價值的見解。"},{"en":"It is common in history and archaeology writing.","zh":"它常見於歷史和考古寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"shadowy world","meaning":"模糊神秘的世界","examples":[{"en":"The discoveries revealed the shadowy world of early voyagers.","zh":"這些發現揭示了早期航海者模糊神秘的世界。"},{"en":"A shadowy world is a world that is unclear, mysterious or poorly understood.","zh":"模糊神秘的世界，是不清楚、神秘或鮮為理解的世界。"},{"en":"Before the excavation, the Lapita’s world remained shadowy to researchers.","zh":"在發掘前，拉皮塔人的世界對研究人員而言仍然模糊神秘。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests limited evidence and mystery.","zh":"這個短語暗示證據有限和神秘感。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing poorly known history.","zh":"它適合描述認識不足的歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"early voyagers","meaning":"早期航海者","examples":[{"en":"The site gives clues about early voyagers in the Pacific.","zh":"該遺址提供有關太平洋早期航海者的線索。"},{"en":"Early voyagers were people who travelled by sea in ancient times.","zh":"早期航海者是古代乘海路旅行的人。"},{"en":"Early voyagers needed knowledge of winds, stars and ocean signs.","zh":"早期航海者需要風、星象和海洋跡象的知識。"},{"en":"Their journeys helped settle distant islands.","zh":"他們的旅程幫助人們在遙遠島嶼定居。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to ancient sea travellers.","zh":"這個短語指古代海上旅人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"first- or second-generation site","meaning":"第一代或第二代遺址","examples":[{"en":"The site may be a first- or second-generation settlement.","zh":"該遺址可能是第一代或第二代定居點。"},{"en":"A first- or second-generation site is a place settled by the original migrants or their children.","zh":"第一代或第二代遺址，是由最初移民或其子女定居的地方。"},{"en":"Such a site can reveal early stages of island colonisation.","zh":"這類遺址能揭示島嶼殖民的早期階段。"},{"en":"Archaeologists value these sites because they are close to the beginning of settlement.","zh":"考古學家重視這些遺址，因為它們接近定居開始時期。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how early a settlement may be.","zh":"這個短語描述定居點可能有多早。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"contain the graves of","meaning":"包含……的墳墓","examples":[{"en":"The site contained the graves of some early Pacific explorers.","zh":"該遺址包含一些早期太平洋探險者的墳墓。"},{"en":"To contain the graves of people means to include burial places where they were buried.","zh":"包含某人的墳墓，是指包括他們被埋葬的地方。"},{"en":"The cemetery contained the graves of several ancient sailors.","zh":"該墓地包含幾名古代航海者的墳墓。"},{"en":"Graves can provide bones, objects and clues about identity.","zh":"墳墓可以提供骨骸、物件和身份線索。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a site with human remains.","zh":"這個短語把遺址與人類遺骸連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Pacific’s first explorers","meaning":"太平洋最早期的探險者","examples":[{"en":"The graves belonged to some of the Pacific’s first explorers.","zh":"這些墳墓屬於一些太平洋最早期的探險者。"},{"en":"The Pacific’s first explorers were among the earliest people to travel into and settle the Pacific islands.","zh":"太平洋最早期的探險者，是最早進入並定居太平洋島嶼的人之一。"},{"en":"Their voyages opened routes across the ocean.","zh":"他們的航行開闢了橫越海洋的路線。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the Lapita a heroic historical role.","zh":"這個短語賦予拉皮塔人英雄式歷史角色。"},{"en":"It emphasises priority and exploration.","zh":"它強調先驅地位和探索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"professor of archaeology","meaning":"考古學教授","examples":[{"en":"Spriggs is a professor of archaeology.","zh":"Spriggs 是考古學教授。"},{"en":"A professor of archaeology is a senior academic who studies ancient human remains and artefacts.","zh":"考古學教授是研究古代人類遺存和文物的高級學者。"},{"en":"A professor of archaeology may lead excavations and train students.","zh":"考古學教授可能帶領發掘並培訓學生。"},{"en":"The title suggests specialist authority.","zh":"這個職銜暗示專門權威。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies an academic role.","zh":"這個短語指出學術角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"co-leader of","meaning":"共同領隊","examples":[{"en":"Spriggs was co-leader of an international team.","zh":"Spriggs 是一支國際團隊的共同領隊。"},{"en":"A co-leader of a team is one of the people sharing leadership responsibility.","zh":"共同領隊，是共同承擔領導責任的人之一。"},{"en":"Two archaeologists were co-leaders of the excavation.","zh":"兩名考古學家是這次發掘的共同領隊。"},{"en":"Co-leadership often occurs in large research projects.","zh":"大型研究項目常出現共同領導。"},{"en":"This phrase shows shared authority.","zh":"這個短語顯示共同權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"international team","meaning":"國際團隊","examples":[{"en":"An international team excavated the site.","zh":"一支國際團隊發掘了該遺址。"},{"en":"An international team is a group of people from different countries working together.","zh":"國際團隊是由來自不同國家的人共同工作組成的小組。"},{"en":"The international team included archaeologists, scientists and local workers.","zh":"這支國際團隊包括考古學家、科學家和本地工人。"},{"en":"Such teams combine different skills and perspectives.","zh":"這類團隊結合不同技能和觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights cross-border cooperation.","zh":"這個短語突出跨國合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"excavate the site","meaning":"發掘遺址","examples":[{"en":"Researchers were excavating the site on Éfaté.","zh":"研究人員正在發掘 Éfaté 島上的遺址。"},{"en":"To excavate a site means to dig carefully in order to uncover archaeological evidence.","zh":"發掘遺址，是指仔細挖掘以揭示考古證據。"},{"en":"Archaeologists excavated the site layer by layer.","zh":"考古學家逐層發掘該遺址。"},{"en":"Excavation must be careful because evidence can be damaged easily.","zh":"發掘必須小心，因為證據容易受損。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal archaeological digging.","zh":"這個短語指正式考古挖掘。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"come to light","meaning":"被發現；曝光","examples":[{"en":"The cemetery came to light only by luck.","zh":"該墓地只是偶然被發現。"},{"en":"To come to light means to be discovered or become known.","zh":"被發現或曝光，是指被揭露或變得為人所知。"},{"en":"New evidence came to light during the excavation.","zh":"發掘期間有新證據被發現。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests that something was hidden before.","zh":"這個短語常暗示某物之前被隱藏。"},{"en":"It is common in history, research and investigations.","zh":"它常見於歷史、研究和調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"by luck","meaning":"偶然地","examples":[{"en":"The burial ground was discovered only by luck.","zh":"該墓地只是偶然地被發現。"},{"en":"By luck means by chance rather than by planning.","zh":"偶然地，是指靠機會而非計劃。"},{"en":"The worker found the ancient grave by luck while digging soil.","zh":"工人挖土時偶然發現古墓。"},{"en":"Many discoveries begin by luck but require careful study afterward.","zh":"許多發現始於偶然，但之後需要仔細研究。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses accident or chance.","zh":"這個短語強調意外或機緣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"backhoe operator","meaning":"反鏟挖泥機操作員","examples":[{"en":"A backhoe operator accidentally opened a grave.","zh":"一名反鏟挖泥機操作員意外挖開一座墳墓。"},{"en":"A backhoe operator is a person who drives and controls a digging machine.","zh":"反鏟挖泥機操作員，是駕駛和操控挖掘機器的人。"},{"en":"The backhoe operator was removing topsoil when the bones appeared.","zh":"該操作員移除表土時，骨骸出現了。"},{"en":"Construction workers sometimes uncover archaeological remains by accident.","zh":"建築工人有時會意外發現考古遺存。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the machine operator.","zh":"這個短語指出機器操作人員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"dig up topsoil","meaning":"挖起表土","examples":[{"en":"The operator was digging up topsoil on the plantation.","zh":"操作員正在種植園挖起表土。"},{"en":"To dig up topsoil means to remove the upper layer of soil.","zh":"挖起表土，是指移除泥土最上層。"},{"en":"Farmers may dig up topsoil before planting or construction.","zh":"農民可能在種植或建設前挖起表土。"},{"en":"Archaeological remains can lie just beneath topsoil.","zh":"考古遺存可能就在表土之下。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical ground removal.","zh":"這個短語描述實際移除地面泥土。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"on the grounds of","meaning":"在……的範圍內","examples":[{"en":"The grave was found on the grounds of a coconut plantation.","zh":"這座墳墓在一個椰子種植園範圍內被發現。"},{"en":"On the grounds of a place means within the land area belonging to it.","zh":"在某地的範圍內，是指位於屬於該地的土地內。"},{"en":"The artefacts were found on the grounds of an old school.","zh":"文物在一所舊學校範圍內被發現。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the location within a property.","zh":"這個短語給出物業內的位置。"},{"en":"It is common in formal descriptions of sites.","zh":"它常見於正式遺址描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"derelict coconut plantation","meaning":"廢棄椰子種植園","examples":[{"en":"The site was located on a derelict coconut plantation.","zh":"該遺址位於一個廢棄椰子種植園。"},{"en":"A derelict coconut plantation is an abandoned or neglected area where coconut trees were once grown.","zh":"廢棄椰子種植園，是曾種植椰子樹但現已荒廢或被忽視的地區。"},{"en":"The derelict plantation had become overgrown before the discovery.","zh":"該廢棄種植園在發現前已雜草叢生。"},{"en":"Such land may hide archaeological remains beneath the surface.","zh":"這類土地可能在地表下藏有考古遺存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both former use and current neglect.","zh":"這個短語同時描述過去用途和現時荒廢狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"scrape open","meaning":"刮開；挖開","examples":[{"en":"The machine scraped open a grave.","zh":"機器刮開了一座墳墓。"},{"en":"To scrape open something means to expose it by scraping away material from the surface.","zh":"刮開某物，是指刮走表面材料而使它暴露出來。"},{"en":"The blade scraped open the soil and revealed bones.","zh":"刀片刮開泥土，露出骨骸。"},{"en":"This action may be accidental and damaging.","zh":"這個動作可能是意外且具破壞性的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rough exposure by a tool or machine.","zh":"這個短語描述工具或機器造成的粗略暴露。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"burial ground","meaning":"墓地","examples":[{"en":"The grave was part of an ancient burial ground.","zh":"這座墳墓是古代墓地的一部分。"},{"en":"A burial ground is a place where people are buried.","zh":"墓地是埋葬人們的地方。"},{"en":"Archaeologists found pottery and bones in the burial ground.","zh":"考古學家在墓地中發現陶器和骨骸。"},{"en":"Burial grounds can reveal beliefs, diet and migration patterns.","zh":"墓地能揭示信仰、飲食和遷徙模式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a cemetery or grave area.","zh":"這個短語指墓園或墳墓區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"harbor the bones of","meaning":"藏有……的骨骸","examples":[{"en":"The cemetery harbors the bones of the Lapita.","zh":"該墓地藏有拉皮塔人的骨骸。"},{"en":"To harbor the bones of someone means to contain or preserve their remains.","zh":"藏有某人的骨骸，是指包含或保存他們的遺骸。"},{"en":"The burial ground harbored the bones of early settlers.","zh":"該墓地藏有早期定居者的骨骸。"},{"en":"This phrase is more literary than simply saying contains.","zh":"這個短語比 simply contains 更具文學色彩。"},{"en":"It suggests hidden preservation over time.","zh":"它暗示長時間隱藏保存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ancient people","meaning":"古代民族","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists call this ancient people the Lapita.","zh":"考古學家稱這個古代民族為拉皮塔人。"},{"en":"An ancient people is a group or culture from the distant past.","zh":"古代民族是來自遙遠過去的群體或文化。"},{"en":"The ancient people left pottery but very few written records.","zh":"這個古代民族留下陶器，但幾乎沒有文字紀錄。"},{"en":"Archaeologists study ancient peoples through bones, tools and settlements.","zh":"考古學家透過骨骸、工具和聚落研究古代民族。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a historical population.","zh":"這個短語指歷史人口群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"derive from","meaning":"源自","examples":[{"en":"The label derives from a beach in New Caledonia.","zh":"這個名稱源自新喀里多尼亞的一個海灘。"},{"en":"To derive from something means to come from it as a source or origin.","zh":"源自某事，是指來自它作為來源或起源。"},{"en":"The name of the culture derives from the place where its pottery was first identified.","zh":"這種文化的名稱源自其陶器首次被識別的地方。"},{"en":"Many academic labels derive from discovery sites.","zh":"許多學術名稱都源自發現地點。"},{"en":"This phrase explains origin.","zh":"這個短語解釋起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"landmark cache","meaning":"具里程碑意義的一批藏品","examples":[{"en":"A landmark cache of Lapita pottery was found in the 1950s.","zh":"二十世紀五十年代發現了一批具里程碑意義的拉皮塔陶器藏品。"},{"en":"A landmark cache is an important group of objects discovered together.","zh":"具里程碑意義的一批藏品，是一起被發現的重要物件群。"},{"en":"The cache of pottery became a landmark because it helped define the culture.","zh":"這批陶器成為里程碑，因為它有助界定該文化。"},{"en":"Such a discovery can guide later research for decades.","zh":"這類發現可以指導之後數十年的研究。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses importance and collected objects.","zh":"這個短語強調重要性和成批物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pottery","meaning":"陶器","examples":[{"en":"Lapita pottery helped archaeologists identify the culture.","zh":"拉皮塔陶器幫助考古學家識別該文化。"},{"en":"Pottery means objects made from fired clay, such as pots, bowls and jars.","zh":"陶器是由燒製黏土製成的物件，例如鍋、碗和罐。"},{"en":"Distinctive pottery patterns can reveal cultural connections.","zh":"獨特陶器紋樣可以揭示文化聯繫。"},{"en":"Archaeologists often use pottery to date and compare sites.","zh":"考古學家常用陶器為遺址斷代和比較。"},{"en":"This word refers to ceramic artefacts.","zh":"這個詞指陶瓷文物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"daring blue-water adventurers","meaning":"勇敢的遠洋冒險者","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita were daring blue-water adventurers.","zh":"拉皮塔人是勇敢的遠洋冒險者。"},{"en":"Daring blue-water adventurers are brave people who travel across deep open ocean.","zh":"勇敢的遠洋冒險者，是橫越深遠開放海洋的勇敢人物。"},{"en":"The Lapita were daring because they sailed far beyond sight of land.","zh":"拉皮塔人十分勇敢，因為他們航行到看不見陸地的遠方。"},{"en":"Blue-water travel is riskier than coastal sailing.","zh":"遠洋航行比沿岸航行更有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights courage and oceanic exploration.","zh":"這個短語突出勇氣和海洋探索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rove the sea","meaning":"在海上遊歷","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita roved the sea as explorers and pioneers.","zh":"拉皮塔人作為探險者和先驅者在海上遊歷。"},{"en":"To rove the sea means to travel widely across it.","zh":"在海上遊歷，是指在海上廣泛旅行。"},{"en":"Ancient sailors roved the sea searching for islands and resources.","zh":"古代航海者在海上遊歷，尋找島嶼和資源。"},{"en":"The verb suggests movement over a broad area.","zh":"這個動詞暗示在廣大範圍內移動。"},{"en":"It is more literary than simply saying travelled.","zh":"它比 simply travelled 更有文學色彩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not just…but also…","meaning":"不只是……也是……","examples":[{"en":"They roved the sea not just as explorers but also as pioneers.","zh":"他們在海上遊歷，不只是探險者，也是先驅者。"},{"en":"Not just A but also B means both A and B are true, with B adding emphasis.","zh":"不只是 A，也是 B，是指 A 和 B 都成立，而 B 增加強調。"},{"en":"The Lapita were not just sailors but also settlers.","zh":"拉皮塔人不只是水手，也是定居者。"},{"en":"This structure expands the role being described.","zh":"這個結構擴展正在描述的角色。"},{"en":"It is useful for showing two connected qualities.","zh":"它適合顯示兩種相關特質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pioneers","meaning":"先驅者","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita were pioneers who built new lives on islands.","zh":"拉皮塔人是在島上建立新生活的先驅者。"},{"en":"Pioneers are people who are among the first to explore, settle or develop a place or idea.","zh":"先驅者是最早探索、定居或發展某地或某想法的人。"},{"en":"The first families on a remote island were pioneers.","zh":"偏遠島嶼上的第一批家庭是先驅者。"},{"en":"Pioneers often face uncertainty and danger.","zh":"先驅者常面對不確定和危險。"},{"en":"This word suggests courage and first steps.","zh":"這個詞暗示勇氣和第一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bring along","meaning":"隨身帶同","examples":[{"en":"The voyagers brought along families, animals and tools.","zh":"航海者隨身帶同家庭、動物和工具。"},{"en":"To bring along something means to take it with you when travelling.","zh":"隨身帶同某物，是指旅行時把它帶在身邊。"},{"en":"The settlers brought along seeds and cooking pots.","zh":"定居者隨身帶同種子和煮食鍋。"},{"en":"What people bring along shows what they need to survive.","zh":"人們帶同甚麼，顯示他們生存需要甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes carrying items or people on a journey.","zh":"這個短語描述旅程中攜帶物品或人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"build new lives","meaning":"建立新生活","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita brought what they needed to build new lives.","zh":"拉皮塔人帶來建立新生活所需的一切。"},{"en":"To build new lives means to create a new way of living in a new place.","zh":"建立新生活，是指在新地方創造新的生活方式。"},{"en":"Families built new lives on islands by planting crops and raising animals.","zh":"家庭透過種植作物和飼養動物在島上建立新生活。"},{"en":"This phrase goes beyond travel and suggests permanent settlement.","zh":"這個短語超越旅行，暗示永久定居。"},{"en":"It focuses on adaptation and survival.","zh":"它聚焦適應和生存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"livestock","meaning":"牲畜","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita travelled with their families and livestock.","zh":"拉皮塔人帶同家人和牲畜旅行。"},{"en":"Livestock are farm animals kept for food, work or other resources.","zh":"牲畜是為食物、勞動或其他資源而飼養的農場動物。"},{"en":"Pigs, chickens and cattle can be livestock.","zh":"豬、雞和牛都可以是牲畜。"},{"en":"Bringing livestock helped settlers survive on new islands.","zh":"帶同牲畜有助定居者在新島上生存。"},{"en":"This word refers to domesticated animals.","zh":"這個詞指馴養動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"taro seedlings","meaning":"芋頭幼苗","examples":[{"en":"The voyagers carried taro seedlings to new islands.","zh":"航海者把芋頭幼苗帶到新島嶼。"},{"en":"Taro seedlings are young taro plants that can be planted and grown for food.","zh":"芋頭幼苗是可以種植並長成食物的年幼芋頭植物。"},{"en":"Settlers carried taro seedlings because taro was an important crop.","zh":"定居者帶同芋頭幼苗，因為芋頭是重要作物。"},{"en":"Seedlings made it possible to reproduce familiar food sources in new places.","zh":"幼苗令人們能在新地方重建熟悉食物來源。"},{"en":"This phrase links migration with agriculture.","zh":"這個短語把遷徙與農業連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stone tools","meaning":"石器工具","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita brought stone tools with them.","zh":"拉皮塔人隨身帶同石器工具。"},{"en":"Stone tools are tools made from stone, often used for cutting, scraping or building.","zh":"石器工具是由石頭製成的工具，常用於切割、刮削或建造。"},{"en":"Early settlers used stone tools to clear land and make objects.","zh":"早期定居者使用石器工具清理土地和製作物件。"},{"en":"Stone tools are important archaeological evidence.","zh":"石器工具是重要考古證據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to prehistoric technology.","zh":"這個短語指史前技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"within the span of","meaning":"在……期間內","examples":[{"en":"Within the span of a few centuries, the Lapita expanded far eastward.","zh":"在幾個世紀期間內，拉皮塔人向東大幅擴展。"},{"en":"Within the span of a period means during that length of time.","zh":"在某段期間內，是指在該時間長度之中。"},{"en":"Within the span of two generations, the settlement reached several islands.","zh":"在兩代人期間內，定居點擴展到幾個島嶼。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a time frame for change.","zh":"這個短語給出變化的時間框架。"},{"en":"It often makes rapid development clearer.","zh":"它常令快速發展更清晰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stretch the boundaries of","meaning":"擴展……的邊界","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita stretched the boundaries of their world.","zh":"拉皮塔人擴展了他們世界的邊界。"},{"en":"To stretch the boundaries of something means to expand its limits.","zh":"擴展某事的邊界，是指擴大其限制。"},{"en":"Each voyage stretched the boundaries of what the sailors knew.","zh":"每次航行都擴展了航海者所知的邊界。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to geography, knowledge or ability.","zh":"這個短語可以指地理、知識或能力。"},{"en":"It suggests pushing beyond previous limits.","zh":"它暗示突破過去限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"jungle-clad volcanoes","meaning":"被叢林覆蓋的火山","examples":[{"en":"Their world stretched from jungle-clad volcanoes to coral islands.","zh":"他們的世界從被叢林覆蓋的火山延伸到珊瑚島。"},{"en":"Jungle-clad volcanoes are volcanoes covered with dense tropical forest.","zh":"被叢林覆蓋的火山，是覆蓋着茂密熱帶森林的火山。"},{"en":"The sailors saw jungle-clad volcanoes rising above the sea.","zh":"航海者看見被叢林覆蓋的火山從海面升起。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a vivid image of green volcanic islands.","zh":"這個短語營造翠綠火山島的生動畫面。"},{"en":"It contrasts high forested islands with low coral islands.","zh":"它把高聳森林島與低矮珊瑚島作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"coral outliers","meaning":"偏遠珊瑚島","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita reached lonely coral outliers in the Pacific.","zh":"拉皮塔人抵達太平洋中孤立的偏遠珊瑚島。"},{"en":"Coral outliers are remote coral islands lying away from main island groups.","zh":"偏遠珊瑚島，是遠離主要島群的珊瑚島。"},{"en":"A coral outlier may be small, low and difficult to see from far away.","zh":"偏遠珊瑚島可能細小、低矮，從遠處難以看見。"},{"en":"Such islands were challenging targets for ancient sailors.","zh":"這類島嶼對古代航海者而言是具挑戰的目標。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses remoteness and coral geography.","zh":"這個短語強調偏遠和珊瑚地貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"eastward in the Pacific","meaning":"向太平洋東面","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita expanded eastward in the Pacific.","zh":"拉皮塔人向太平洋東面擴展。"},{"en":"Eastward in the Pacific means moving toward the eastern part of the Pacific Ocean.","zh":"向太平洋東面，是指朝太平洋東部移動。"},{"en":"The migration continued eastward in the Pacific over several generations.","zh":"這次遷徙在幾代人中繼續向太平洋東面發展。"},{"en":"Direction matters because winds and currents affected travel.","zh":"方向很重要，因為風和洋流影響航行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the direction of expansion.","zh":"這個短語描述擴展方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"along the way","meaning":"沿途","examples":[{"en":"Along the way, they explored many unknown islands.","zh":"沿途，他們探索了許多未知島嶼。"},{"en":"Along the way means during the journey or process.","zh":"沿途，是指在旅程或過程中。"},{"en":"The sailors found new resources along the way.","zh":"航海者沿途發現新資源。"},{"en":"This phrase connects events to a continuing journey.","zh":"這個短語把事件與持續旅程連接起來。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing stages of travel.","zh":"它適合描述旅行階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"discover and colonize","meaning":"發現並殖民","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita discovered and colonized many tropical islands.","zh":"拉皮塔人發現並殖民許多熱帶島嶼。"},{"en":"To discover and colonize means to find new places and then establish communities there.","zh":"發現並殖民，是指找到新地方，然後在那裡建立社群。"},{"en":"Finding an island was only the first step; colonizing it required long-term survival.","zh":"找到島嶼只是第一步；在島上定居需要長期生存。"},{"en":"This phrase combines exploration with settlement.","zh":"這個短語結合探索與定居。"},{"en":"It shows that the Lapita did more than travel.","zh":"它顯示拉皮塔人不只是旅行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tropical islands","meaning":"熱帶島嶼","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita settled on tropical islands across the Pacific.","zh":"拉皮塔人在太平洋各地熱帶島嶼上定居。"},{"en":"Tropical islands are islands in warm regions near the equator.","zh":"熱帶島嶼是位於赤道附近溫暖地區的島嶼。"},{"en":"Tropical islands often have warm seas, rich vegetation and coral reefs.","zh":"熱帶島嶼通常有溫暖海水、茂盛植被和珊瑚礁。"},{"en":"Settling tropical islands required knowledge of crops, fishing and water sources.","zh":"定居熱帶島嶼需要農作物、捕魚和水源知識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes climate and geography.","zh":"這個短語描述氣候和地理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"never before seen by human eyes","meaning":"從未被人類看見過的","examples":[{"en":"They found islands never before seen by human eyes.","zh":"他們發現了從未被人類看見過的島嶼。"},{"en":"Never before seen by human eyes means no person had ever looked at them before.","zh":"從未被人類看見過，是指以前從沒有任何人見過。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the discovery a dramatic and historic feeling.","zh":"這個短語令發現帶有戲劇性和歷史感。"},{"en":"It suggests the islands were completely unknown to humans.","zh":"它暗示那些島嶼對人類而言完全未知。"},{"en":"This expression emphasises first discovery.","zh":"這個表達強調首次發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"their descendants","meaning":"他們的後裔","examples":[{"en":"Their descendants later became famous Polynesian navigators.","zh":"他們的後裔後來成為著名波利尼西亞航海家。"},{"en":"Descendants are people who come from earlier ancestors.","zh":"後裔是來自早期祖先的人。"},{"en":"The descendants of the Lapita carried related languages across the Pacific.","zh":"拉皮塔人的後裔把相關語言帶到太平洋各地。"},{"en":"This phrase links past populations with later generations.","zh":"這個短語把過去人口與後來世代連接起來。"},{"en":"It is common in history and genealogy.","zh":"它常見於歷史和家族譜系。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"great Polynesian navigators","meaning":"偉大的波利尼西亞航海家","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita’s descendants became great Polynesian navigators.","zh":"拉皮塔人的後裔成為偉大的波利尼西亞航海家。"},{"en":"Great Polynesian navigators were highly skilled sailors from Polynesian cultures.","zh":"偉大的波利尼西亞航海家，是來自波利尼西亞文化、技術高超的水手。"},{"en":"They could travel between distant islands using natural signs.","zh":"他們能利用自然跡象在遙遠島嶼之間航行。"},{"en":"This phrase shows admiration for their navigation ability.","zh":"這個短語表達對其導航能力的讚賞。"},{"en":"It connects later Polynesian success with earlier Lapita foundations.","zh":"它把後來波利尼西亞人的成功與早期拉皮塔基礎連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tend to think of","meaning":"往往會想到","examples":[{"en":"We tend to think of the Tahitians and Hawaiians as great navigators.","zh":"我們往往會想到塔希提人和夏威夷人是偉大航海家。"},{"en":"To tend to think of something in a way means usually or naturally imagine it that way.","zh":"往往會以某方式想到某事，是指通常或自然地那樣想像它。"},{"en":"Many people tend to think of explorers as men on large ships.","zh":"許多人往往會想到探險者是乘大型船隻的男性。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a common assumption.","zh":"這個短語引入常見假設。"},{"en":"It is useful before correcting or broadening an idea.","zh":"它適合用於修正或擴闊想法之前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the New Zealand Maori","meaning":"新西蘭毛利人","examples":[{"en":"The New Zealand Maori were descendants of early Pacific voyagers.","zh":"新西蘭毛利人是早期太平洋航海者的後裔。"},{"en":"The New Zealand Maori are the Indigenous Polynesian people of New Zealand.","zh":"新西蘭毛利人是新西蘭的波利尼西亞原住民族。"},{"en":"Maori traditions preserve stories of ancestral voyages.","zh":"毛利傳統保存祖先航行的故事。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a major Polynesian culture.","zh":"這個短語指出一個主要波利尼西亞文化。"},{"en":"It connects New Zealand history with wider Pacific migration.","zh":"它把新西蘭歷史與更廣泛太平洋遷徙連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"erect statues","meaning":"豎立雕像","examples":[{"en":"The people of Easter Island erected famous statues.","zh":"復活節島人民豎立了著名雕像。"},{"en":"To erect statues means to build or raise large sculpted figures.","zh":"豎立雕像，是指建造或立起大型雕刻人物。"},{"en":"A community may erect statues to honour ancestors or leaders.","zh":"社區可能豎立雕像以紀念祖先或領袖。"},{"en":"Easter Island’s statues show cultural achievement and organisation.","zh":"復活節島雕像顯示文化成就和組織能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes constructing standing monuments.","zh":"這個短語描述建造直立紀念物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lay the foundation","meaning":"奠定基礎","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita laid the foundation for later Polynesian cultures.","zh":"拉皮塔人為後來的波利尼西亞文化奠定基礎。"},{"en":"To lay the foundation means to create the base for future development.","zh":"奠定基礎，是指為未來發展建立根基。"},{"en":"Early settlement laid the foundation for later island societies.","zh":"早期定居為後來島嶼社會奠定基礎。"},{"en":"Foundations can be cultural, linguistic or technological.","zh":"基礎可以是文化、語言或技術上的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important beginning.","zh":"這個短語描述重要開端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"bequeath to","meaning":"留傳給……","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita bequeathed language, customs and culture to the islands.","zh":"拉皮塔人把語言、習俗和文化留傳給這些島嶼。"},{"en":"To bequeath something to someone means to pass it on to later people or places.","zh":"把某物留傳給某人，是指把它傳給後來的人或地方。"},{"en":"Ancestors bequeathed navigation knowledge to their descendants.","zh":"祖先把導航知識留傳給後裔。"},{"en":"This verb is often used for inheritance beyond money.","zh":"這個動詞常用於金錢以外的繼承。"},{"en":"It suggests a lasting legacy.","zh":"它暗示持久遺產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"customs and cultures","meaning":"習俗和文化","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita passed on customs and cultures to their descendants.","zh":"拉皮塔人把習俗和文化傳給他們的後裔。"},{"en":"Customs and cultures are shared practices, beliefs, values and ways of life.","zh":"習俗和文化是共同做法、信仰、價值觀和生活方式。"},{"en":"Island customs and cultures may include language, ceremony, food and navigation.","zh":"島嶼習俗和文化可能包括語言、儀式、食物和導航。"},{"en":"These traditions help communities preserve identity.","zh":"這些傳統幫助社群保存身份。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to inherited social life.","zh":"這個短語指承傳下來的社會生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"carry around","meaning":"傳播到……各處","examples":[{"en":"Their descendants carried these cultures around the Pacific.","zh":"他們的後裔把這些文化傳播到太平洋各處。"},{"en":"To carry something around a region means to spread or take it to many places there.","zh":"把某物傳播到某地各處，是指把它帶到該地許多地方。"},{"en":"Migrants carried stories and tools around the islands.","zh":"移民把故事和工具帶到各島各處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cultural movement through travel.","zh":"這個短語描述文化透過旅行移動。"},{"en":"It suggests active transmission.","zh":"它暗示主動傳承。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"leave a glorious legacy","meaning":"留下輝煌遺產","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita left a glorious legacy in the Pacific.","zh":"拉皮塔人在太平洋留下輝煌遺產。"},{"en":"To leave a glorious legacy means to leave behind an impressive and lasting influence.","zh":"留下輝煌遺產，是指留下令人讚嘆且持久的影響。"},{"en":"Early navigators left a legacy of language, settlement and sailing knowledge.","zh":"早期航海者留下語言、定居和航海知識的遺產。"},{"en":"A legacy can continue long after the original people disappear.","zh":"遺產可以在原來的人消失後很久仍延續。"},{"en":"This phrase praises historical impact.","zh":"這個短語讚揚歷史影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"precious few clues","meaning":"極少珍貴線索","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita left precious few clues about themselves.","zh":"拉皮塔人留下關於自己的極少珍貴線索。"},{"en":"Precious few clues means very few clues, and the few available are valuable.","zh":"極少珍貴線索，是指線索非常少，而少數現存線索又很有價值。"},{"en":"Researchers had precious few clues before the cemetery was found.","zh":"在墓地被發現前，研究人員只有極少珍貴線索。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses scarcity and importance.","zh":"這個短語強調稀少和重要性。"},{"en":"It is useful when evidence is limited.","zh":"它適合用於證據有限的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"intriguing clue","meaning":"耐人尋味的線索","examples":[{"en":"An intriguing clue comes from tests on teeth.","zh":"一個耐人尋味的線索來自對牙齒的測試。"},{"en":"An intriguing clue is a piece of evidence that is interesting and makes people want to know more.","zh":"耐人尋味的線索，是有趣並令人想知道更多的證據。"},{"en":"The isotope result was an intriguing clue about childhood origins.","zh":"同位素結果是關於童年來源的耐人尋味線索。"},{"en":"Such clues may not answer everything, but they guide research.","zh":"這些線索未必回答一切，但能引導研究。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests curiosity and partial discovery.","zh":"這個短語暗示好奇和部分發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"chemical tests on","meaning":"對……進行化學測試","examples":[{"en":"Chemical tests on teeth can reveal where people grew up.","zh":"對牙齒進行化學測試可以揭示人們在哪裡長大。"},{"en":"Chemical tests on something are scientific analyses of its chemical composition.","zh":"對某物進行化學測試，是科學分析其化學成分。"},{"en":"Chemical tests on bones can show information about diet.","zh":"對骨骼進行化學測試可以顯示飲食資料。"},{"en":"Such tests help archaeologists study ancient people without written records.","zh":"這類測試幫助考古學家研究沒有文字紀錄的古人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes laboratory analysis.","zh":"這個短語描述實驗室分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"skeletons","meaning":"骨骼","examples":[{"en":"Researchers tested the teeth of several skeletons.","zh":"研究人員測試了幾具骨骼的牙齒。"},{"en":"Skeletons are the bones of human or animal bodies.","zh":"骨骼是人類或動物身體的骨頭。"},{"en":"Ancient skeletons can reveal age, health and migration history.","zh":"古代骨骼可以揭示年齡、健康和遷徙歷史。"},{"en":"Archaeologists handle skeletons carefully because they are fragile evidence.","zh":"考古學家小心處理骨骼，因為它們是脆弱證據。"},{"en":"This word refers to preserved bone remains.","zh":"這個詞指保存下來的骨骸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"consume as a child","meaning":"兒時攝取","examples":[{"en":"The food and water you consume as a child leave traces in your teeth.","zh":"你兒時攝取的食物和水會在牙齒中留下痕跡。"},{"en":"To consume as a child means to eat or drink during childhood.","zh":"兒時攝取，是指在童年期間吃或喝。"},{"en":"Minerals consumed as a child can become part of forming teeth.","zh":"兒時攝取的礦物質可以成為形成中牙齒的一部分。"},{"en":"Childhood diet can therefore leave long-term chemical evidence.","zh":"因此童年飲食可以留下長期化學證據。"},{"en":"This phrase links early life with later scientific analysis.","zh":"這個短語把早年生活與後來科學分析連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deposit elements in","meaning":"把元素沉積在……","examples":[{"en":"Food and water deposit elements in adult teeth.","zh":"食物和水會把元素沉積在恆齒中。"},{"en":"To deposit elements in something means to leave chemical substances there over time.","zh":"把元素沉積在某物中，是指隨時間把化學物質留在那裡。"},{"en":"Drinking water can deposit minerals in forming teeth.","zh":"飲用水可以把礦物質沉積在形成中的牙齒裡。"},{"en":"These deposits can later be studied by scientists.","zh":"這些沉積物日後可以被科學家研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes chemical traces being laid down.","zh":"這個短語描述化學痕跡被留下。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"still-forming adult teeth","meaning":"仍在形成中的恆齒","examples":[{"en":"Elements are deposited in still-forming adult teeth.","zh":"元素會沉積在仍在形成中的恆齒裡。"},{"en":"Still-forming adult teeth are permanent teeth that are not yet fully developed.","zh":"仍在形成中的恆齒，是尚未完全發育的永久牙齒。"},{"en":"A child’s still-forming adult teeth can record chemical signals from food and water.","zh":"兒童仍在形成中的恆齒可以記錄食物和水中的化學訊號。"},{"en":"This makes teeth useful for studying childhood origins.","zh":"這令牙齒有助研究童年來源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to developing permanent teeth.","zh":"這個短語指正在發育的永久牙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"isotope signatures","meaning":"同位素特徵","examples":[{"en":"Isotope signatures can reveal a person’s geographical roots.","zh":"同位素特徵可以揭示一個人的地理根源。"},{"en":"Isotope signatures are chemical patterns that can indicate where someone lived or what they consumed.","zh":"同位素特徵是可顯示某人曾住在哪裡或攝取甚麼的化學模式。"},{"en":"Different islands may leave different isotope signatures in teeth.","zh":"不同島嶼可能在牙齒中留下不同同位素特徵。"},{"en":"Scientists compare these signatures to possible places of origin.","zh":"科學家把這些特徵與可能的原居地比較。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to chemical identity markers.","zh":"這個短語指化學身份標記。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"vary subtly from place to place","meaning":"因地而有細微差異","examples":[{"en":"Isotope signatures vary subtly from place to place.","zh":"同位素特徵會因地而有細微差異。"},{"en":"To vary subtly means to differ slightly but meaningfully.","zh":"有細微差異，是指略有不同但仍具意義。"},{"en":"The mineral content of water can vary subtly from island to island.","zh":"水中礦物含量可能因島而有細微差異。"},{"en":"Small differences can still help identify broad origins.","zh":"小差異仍可幫助識別大致來源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fine geographical variation.","zh":"這個短語描述細微地理差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"reveal your roots","meaning":"揭示你的根源","examples":[{"en":"Tests on teeth can reveal your roots.","zh":"對牙齒的測試可以揭示你的根源。"},{"en":"To reveal your roots means to show where you or your ancestors came from.","zh":"揭示你的根源，是指顯示你或你的祖先來自哪裡。"},{"en":"Chemical evidence in teeth may reveal a person’s childhood roots.","zh":"牙齒中的化學證據可能揭示一個人的童年根源。"},{"en":"Roots can refer to family, culture or geography.","zh":"根源可以指家庭、文化或地理來源。"},{"en":"This phrase connects identity with origin.","zh":"這個短語把身份與來源連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"eastern roots","meaning":"東部根源","examples":[{"en":"Isotope tests may reveal a person’s eastern roots.","zh":"同位素測試可能揭示一個人的東部根源。"},{"en":"Eastern roots are origins or connections in an eastern region.","zh":"東部根源，是指在東方地區的來源或聯繫。"},{"en":"The analysis suggested that some individuals had eastern roots rather than local ones.","zh":"分析顯示有些人可能有東部根源，而非本地來源。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a broad direction of origin.","zh":"這個短語給出大致來源方向。"},{"en":"It does not necessarily identify an exact island.","zh":"它不一定指出確切島嶼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"isotope analysis","meaning":"同位素分析","examples":[{"en":"Isotope analysis showed that some Lapita were not born on Éfaté.","zh":"同位素分析顯示，有些拉皮塔人並非出生於 Éfaté 島。"},{"en":"Isotope analysis is the scientific study of isotope patterns in materials such as teeth or bones.","zh":"同位素分析是對牙齒或骨骼等材料中的同位素模式進行科學研究。"},{"en":"Archaeologists used isotope analysis to study where ancient people grew up.","zh":"考古學家使用同位素分析研究古人在哪裡長大。"},{"en":"The method can suggest origins even when written records do not exist.","zh":"即使沒有文字紀錄，這種方法也能暗示來源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a scientific technique.","zh":"這個短語指一種科學技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"spend one’s childhood","meaning":"度過童年","examples":[{"en":"Several Lapita did not spend their childhoods on Éfaté.","zh":"幾名拉皮塔人並非在 Éfaté 島度過童年。"},{"en":"To spend one’s childhood somewhere means to live there as a child.","zh":"在某地度過童年，是指兒時生活在那裡。"},{"en":"A person who spent childhood near the sea may know boats from an early age.","zh":"在海邊度過童年的人可能自小熟悉船隻。"},{"en":"Childhood location can leave chemical traces in teeth.","zh":"童年所在地可以在牙齒中留下化學痕跡。"},{"en":"This phrase connects early life with place.","zh":"這個短語把早年生活與地方連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pinpoint","meaning":"精確指出","examples":[{"en":"Isotopes cannot pinpoint their precise island of origin.","zh":"同位素無法精確指出他們確切的原居島嶼。"},{"en":"To pinpoint something means to identify it exactly.","zh":"精確指出某事，是指準確識別它。"},{"en":"The evidence can suggest a region but cannot pinpoint the village.","zh":"證據可以暗示一個地區，但不能精確指出村落。"},{"en":"Pinpointing origin requires very precise data.","zh":"精確指出來源需要非常精準的數據。"},{"en":"This verb stresses exactness.","zh":"這個動詞強調準確性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"precise island of origin","meaning":"確切的原居島嶼","examples":[{"en":"The analysis could not identify the precise island of origin.","zh":"分析無法識別確切的原居島嶼。"},{"en":"A precise island of origin is the exact island where a person came from or was born.","zh":"確切的原居島嶼，是一個人來自或出生的準確島嶼。"},{"en":"Researchers knew the person was not local but not the precise island of origin.","zh":"研究人員知道此人不是本地人，但不知道確切原居島嶼。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the limit of scientific evidence.","zh":"這個短語突出科學證據的限制。"},{"en":"It asks for exact geographical source.","zh":"它要求準確地理來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"this much is clear","meaning":"這一點很清楚","examples":[{"en":"This much is clear: some Lapita came from elsewhere.","zh":"這一點很清楚：有些拉皮塔人來自其他地方。"},{"en":"This much is clear means this particular point is certain, even if other details are not.","zh":"這一點很清楚，是指即使其他細節不明，這個特定重點是確定的。"},{"en":"The exact route is unknown, but this much is clear: the sailors travelled far.","zh":"確切路線未知，但這一點很清楚：航海者走得很遠。"},{"en":"This phrase separates certainty from uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語把確定性與不確定性分開。"},{"en":"It is useful in cautious academic explanation.","zh":"它適合用於謹慎的學術解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at some point in one’s life","meaning":"在人生某個階段","examples":[{"en":"At some point in their lives, they left their birth villages.","zh":"在人生某個階段，他們離開了出生村落。"},{"en":"At some point in one’s life means at an unspecified time during one’s lifetime.","zh":"在人生某個階段，是指一生中某個未明確指出的時間。"},{"en":"At some point in his life, the sailor moved to another island.","zh":"在人生某個階段，這名水手搬到另一個島。"},{"en":"This phrase allows uncertainty about exact timing.","zh":"這個短語容許對準確時間的不確定。"},{"en":"It is useful when evidence shows change but not the exact date.","zh":"當證據顯示有變化但沒有確切日期時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"villages of their birth","meaning":"他們出生的村落","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita left the villages of their birth.","zh":"拉皮塔人離開了他們出生的村落。"},{"en":"Villages of their birth are the villages where they were born.","zh":"他們出生的村落，是他們出生所在的村落。"},{"en":"Leaving the village of one’s birth may mean leaving family, land and memories.","zh":"離開出生村落可能意味着離開家庭、土地和記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than birthplace village.","zh":"這個短語比 birthplace village 更正式。"},{"en":"It highlights emotional and geographical origin.","zh":"它突出情感和地理來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make a voyage by","meaning":"乘……航行","examples":[{"en":"They made a voyage by seagoing canoe.","zh":"他們乘遠洋獨木舟航行。"},{"en":"To make a voyage by something means to travel using that form of transport.","zh":"乘某物航行，是指使用該交通工具旅行。"},{"en":"The settlers made a voyage by canoe across open water.","zh":"定居者乘獨木舟橫越開放水域。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies how the journey was made.","zh":"這個短語指出旅程如何完成。"},{"en":"It is often used for sea travel.","zh":"它常用於海上旅行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"seagoing canoe","meaning":"遠洋獨木舟","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita travelled by seagoing canoe.","zh":"拉皮塔人乘遠洋獨木舟旅行。"},{"en":"A seagoing canoe is a canoe capable of travelling on the open sea.","zh":"遠洋獨木舟是能在開放海域航行的獨木舟。"},{"en":"A seagoing canoe must be stable enough for waves and long distances.","zh":"遠洋獨木舟必須足夠穩定，以應付海浪和長距離。"},{"en":"Such canoes made island colonisation possible.","zh":"這類獨木舟令島嶼定居成為可能。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to ocean-capable traditional boats.","zh":"這個短語指具遠洋能力的傳統船隻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"never to return","meaning":"一去不返","examples":[{"en":"They left their home villages, never to return.","zh":"他們離開家鄉村落，一去不返。"},{"en":"Never to return means they did not come back again.","zh":"一去不返，是指他們再也沒有回來。"},{"en":"Some migrants left the island, never to return.","zh":"有些移民離開島嶼後一去不返。"},{"en":"The phrase adds finality and emotional weight.","zh":"這個短語增加終結感和情感重量。"},{"en":"It suggests a permanent departure.","zh":"它暗示永久離開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"DNA teased from","meaning":"從……提取出的 DNA","examples":[{"en":"DNA teased from ancient bones may answer old questions.","zh":"從古代骨骸提取出的 DNA 可能回答老問題。"},{"en":"DNA teased from something means DNA carefully extracted from it.","zh":"從某物提取出的 DNA，是指小心從其中取得的 DNA。"},{"en":"Scientists teased DNA from a tiny piece of ancient tooth.","zh":"科學家從一小塊古代牙齒中提取 DNA。"},{"en":"The verb suggests careful and difficult extraction.","zh":"這個動詞暗示提取過程仔細且困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes delicate scientific recovery.","zh":"這個短語描述精細的科學回收。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ancient bones","meaning":"古代骨骸","examples":[{"en":"DNA from ancient bones may reveal the Lapita’s origins.","zh":"來自古代骨骸的 DNA 可能揭示拉皮塔人的起源。"},{"en":"Ancient bones are old skeletal remains from people or animals of the past.","zh":"古代骨骸是過去人類或動物的古老骨骼遺存。"},{"en":"Ancient bones can preserve DNA, diet evidence and disease clues.","zh":"古代骨骸可以保存 DNA、飲食證據和疾病線索。"},{"en":"Researchers handle ancient bones carefully to avoid contamination.","zh":"研究人員小心處理古代骨骸，以避免污染。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to old biological remains.","zh":"這個短語指古老生物遺存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"puzzling questions","meaning":"令人困惑的問題","examples":[{"en":"DNA may help answer puzzling questions in Pacific anthropology.","zh":"DNA 可能幫助回答太平洋人類學中令人困惑的問題。"},{"en":"Puzzling questions are difficult questions that are confusing or hard to solve.","zh":"令人困惑的問題，是令人迷惑或難以解決的困難問題。"},{"en":"The origin of the Lapita remains a puzzling question.","zh":"拉皮塔人的起源仍是令人困惑的問題。"},{"en":"Such questions require evidence from many fields.","zh":"這類問題需要來自多個領域的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses mystery and difficulty.","zh":"這個短語強調神秘和困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Pacific anthropology","meaning":"太平洋人類學","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita are important in Pacific anthropology.","zh":"拉皮塔人在太平洋人類學中十分重要。"},{"en":"Pacific anthropology is the study of human societies, cultures and origins in the Pacific region.","zh":"太平洋人類學是研究太平洋地區人類社會、文化和起源的學科。"},{"en":"Pacific anthropology examines migration, language, settlement and identity.","zh":"太平洋人類學研究遷徙、語言、定居和身份。"},{"en":"The Lapita matter because they shaped later island cultures.","zh":"拉皮塔人重要，因為他們塑造了後來島嶼文化。"},{"en":"This phrase names an academic field.","zh":"這個短語命名一個學術領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"spring from one source","meaning":"源自單一來源","examples":[{"en":"Researchers ask whether Pacific islanders sprang from one source.","zh":"研究人員追問太平洋島民是否源自單一來源。"},{"en":"To spring from one source means to originate from a single place or group.","zh":"源自單一來源，是指起源於一個地方或群體。"},{"en":"A language family may spring from one source before spreading widely.","zh":"一個語系可能源自單一來源，然後廣泛傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about common origin.","zh":"這個短語詢問共同起源。"},{"en":"It is more vivid than simply saying come from.","zh":"它比 simply come from 更生動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"outward migration","meaning":"向外遷徙","examples":[{"en":"There may have been one outward migration from Asia.","zh":"可能曾有一次從亞洲向外遷徙。"},{"en":"Outward migration is movement away from a starting region to other places.","zh":"向外遷徙，是由起點地區移往其他地方。"},{"en":"Outward migration from Asia may have carried people into the Pacific.","zh":"從亞洲向外遷徙可能把人們帶入太平洋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes expansion away from an origin.","zh":"這個短語描述從起源地向外擴展。"},{"en":"It is common in population-history discussions.","zh":"它常見於人口歷史討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a single point in Asia","meaning":"亞洲的單一地點","examples":[{"en":"Some scholars suggest migration from a single point in Asia.","zh":"有些學者提出遷徙源自亞洲的單一地點。"},{"en":"A single point in Asia means one specific place or region in Asia.","zh":"亞洲的單一地點，是亞洲某個特定地方或地區。"},{"en":"The theory proposes that the islanders began from a single point in Asia.","zh":"這個理論提出島民起源於亞洲的一個單一地點。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts one origin with several origins.","zh":"這個短語把單一起源與多個起源作對比。"},{"en":"It highlights a simple migration model.","zh":"它突出簡單的遷徙模型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"different points","meaning":"不同地點","examples":[{"en":"Migration may have started from several different points.","zh":"遷徙可能從幾個不同地點開始。"},{"en":"Different points means several separate places or origins.","zh":"不同地點，是指幾個分開的地方或起源。"},{"en":"Islanders may have migrated from different points across Asia.","zh":"島民可能從亞洲各個不同地點遷徙而來。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a more complex pattern.","zh":"這個短語暗示更複雜的模式。"},{"en":"It contrasts with a single origin.","zh":"它與單一起源形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"represent the best opportunity","meaning":"代表最佳機會","examples":[{"en":"The site represents the best opportunity to study the Lapita.","zh":"該遺址代表研究拉皮塔人的最佳機會。"},{"en":"To represent the best opportunity means to offer the strongest chance to achieve something.","zh":"代表最佳機會，是指提供最有力的機會去達成某事。"},{"en":"The cemetery represents the best opportunity to learn about early Pacific settlers.","zh":"該墓地代表了解早期太平洋定居者的最佳機會。"},{"en":"Rare evidence becomes valuable when few other sites exist.","zh":"當其他遺址很少，稀有證據就變得寶貴。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights exceptional research value.","zh":"這個短語突出非凡研究價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"find out","meaning":"查明","examples":[{"en":"Researchers hope to find out who the Lapita were.","zh":"研究人員希望查明拉皮塔人是誰。"},{"en":"To find out means to discover information.","zh":"查明，是指發現資訊。"},{"en":"DNA may help scientists find out where ancient people came from.","zh":"DNA 可能幫助科學家查明古人來自哪裡。"},{"en":"This phrase is common and simple.","zh":"這個短語常見而簡單。"},{"en":"It focuses on learning something previously unknown.","zh":"它聚焦得知先前未知的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"closest descendants","meaning":"最接近的後裔","examples":[{"en":"DNA may reveal who the Lapita’s closest descendants are today.","zh":"DNA 可能揭示今日誰是拉皮塔人最接近的後裔。"},{"en":"Closest descendants are present-day people most directly related to an ancient group.","zh":"最接近的後裔，是與古代群體關係最直接的現代人。"},{"en":"Genetic tests may identify the closest descendants of early settlers.","zh":"基因測試可能識別早期定居者最接近的後裔。"},{"en":"This phrase connects ancient DNA with modern populations.","zh":"這個短語把古代 DNA 與現代人口連接起來。"},{"en":"It refers to biological or cultural relationship.","zh":"它指生物或文化關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stubborn question","meaning":"難以解答的問題","examples":[{"en":"One stubborn question remains unanswered.","zh":"一個難以解答的問題仍未有答案。"},{"en":"A stubborn question is a difficult question that resists easy answers.","zh":"難以解答的問題，是抗拒簡單答案的困難問題。"},{"en":"How the Lapita sailed so far remains a stubborn question.","zh":"拉皮塔人如何航行那麼遠，仍是一個難以解答的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that evidence has not yet solved the mystery.","zh":"這個短語暗示證據尚未解開謎團。"},{"en":"It personifies the question as hard to move.","zh":"它把問題擬人化為難以推動的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have yet to provide","meaning":"尚未提供","examples":[{"en":"Archaeology has yet to provide clear answers.","zh":"考古學尚未提供清楚答案。"},{"en":"To have yet to provide something means to not have provided it so far.","zh":"尚未提供某物，是指到目前為止仍未提供。"},{"en":"DNA studies have yet to provide the final answer.","zh":"DNA 研究尚未提供最終答案。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the answer may come later.","zh":"這個短語暗示答案日後可能出現。"},{"en":"It is useful for cautious academic writing.","zh":"它適合用於謹慎學術寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ancient equivalent of","meaning":"古代相當於……的成就","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita achieved the ancient equivalent of a moon landing.","zh":"拉皮塔人達成了古代相當於登月的成就。"},{"en":"The ancient equivalent of something means a past achievement comparable to a modern one.","zh":"古代相當於某事的成就，是可與現代某事相比的古代成就。"},{"en":"Crossing the open Pacific was the ancient equivalent of a major space mission.","zh":"橫越開放太平洋是古代相當於重大太空任務的成就。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers grasp the scale of an ancient achievement.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者理解古代成就的規模。"},{"en":"It uses modern comparison to explain historical difficulty.","zh":"它用現代比較解釋歷史困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"moon landing","meaning":"登月","examples":[{"en":"Their long voyages were compared to a moon landing.","zh":"他們的長途航行被比作登月。"},{"en":"A moon landing is the act of landing a spacecraft on the moon.","zh":"登月是太空船降落在月球上的行動。"},{"en":"Calling Lapita voyages a moon landing shows how extraordinary they were.","zh":"把拉皮塔航程稱為登月，顯示它們多麼非凡。"},{"en":"The comparison stresses risk, technology and courage.","zh":"這個比較強調風險、技術和勇氣。"},{"en":"This phrase is used as a metaphor for a remarkable achievement.","zh":"這個短語被用作非凡成就的比喻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"many times over","meaning":"多次地","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita achieved this feat many times over.","zh":"拉皮塔人多次達成這項壯舉。"},{"en":"Many times over means repeatedly, not just once.","zh":"多次地，是指反覆發生，而不只是一次。"},{"en":"The sailors crossed dangerous seas many times over.","zh":"航海者多次橫越危險海域。"},{"en":"This phrase intensifies the achievement.","zh":"這個短語加強成就感。"},{"en":"It shows repetition of a difficult action.","zh":"它顯示困難行動被重複完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rigging","meaning":"船索裝置；帆具","examples":[{"en":"No one has found their canoes or any rigging.","zh":"沒有人找到他們的獨木舟或任何帆具。"},{"en":"Rigging is the system of ropes, sails and equipment used to control a boat’s sails.","zh":"船索裝置或帆具，是用來控制船帆的繩索、帆和設備系統。"},{"en":"Canoe rigging would show how the Lapita handled wind.","zh":"獨木舟帆具會顯示拉皮塔人如何利用風。"},{"en":"Without rigging evidence, sailing methods remain uncertain.","zh":"沒有帆具證據，航行方法仍不確定。"},{"en":"This word refers to sailing equipment.","zh":"這個詞指航行設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reveal how","meaning":"揭示如何……","examples":[{"en":"The rigging could reveal how the canoes were sailed.","zh":"帆具可以揭示獨木舟如何航行。"},{"en":"To reveal how something happened means to show the method or process behind it.","zh":"揭示某事如何發生，是指顯示其背後方法或過程。"},{"en":"Tool marks may reveal how ancient boats were built.","zh":"工具痕跡可能揭示古船如何建造。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces explanation of technique.","zh":"這個短語引入技術解釋。"},{"en":"It is common in scientific and historical writing.","zh":"它常見於科學和歷史寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"oral histories and traditions","meaning":"口述歷史和傳統","examples":[{"en":"Later oral histories and traditions offer few insights.","zh":"後來的口述歷史和傳統提供很少見解。"},{"en":"Oral histories and traditions are stories and knowledge passed down by speech rather than writing.","zh":"口述歷史和傳統，是透過說話而非文字流傳下來的故事和知識。"},{"en":"Islanders may preserve migration stories through oral histories and traditions.","zh":"島民可能透過口述歷史和傳統保存遷徙故事。"},{"en":"Such sources are valuable but may not answer technical questions.","zh":"這類來源有價值，但未必能回答技術問題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to spoken cultural memory.","zh":"這個短語指口頭文化記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"later Polynesians","meaning":"後來的波利尼西亞人","examples":[{"en":"Later Polynesians preserved few clues about Lapita canoe technology.","zh":"後來的波利尼西亞人保存了很少關於拉皮塔獨木舟技術的線索。"},{"en":"Later Polynesians are Polynesian peoples who came after the Lapita period.","zh":"後來的波利尼西亞人，是拉皮塔時期之後的波利尼西亞人群。"},{"en":"Later Polynesians inherited some cultural traditions from earlier voyagers.","zh":"後來的波利尼西亞人繼承了早期航海者的一些文化傳統。"},{"en":"The phrase distinguishes descendants from the original Lapita people.","zh":"這個短語把後裔與原本拉皮塔人區分開。"},{"en":"It places evidence in a later historical stage.","zh":"它把證據放在較後歷史階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"offer insights","meaning":"提供見解","examples":[{"en":"The traditions do not offer insights into Lapita sailing methods.","zh":"這些傳統沒有提供關於拉皮塔航行方法的見解。"},{"en":"To offer insights means to provide useful understanding.","zh":"提供見解，是指提供有用理解。"},{"en":"Bones may offer insights into diet and migration.","zh":"骨骼可能提供飲食和遷徙方面的見解。"},{"en":"Some evidence offers insights into culture but not technology.","zh":"有些證據提供文化見解，但不提供技術見解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes informative value.","zh":"這個短語描述資訊價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"all we can say for certain","meaning":"我們唯一可以肯定地說的是","examples":[{"en":"All we can say for certain is that the Lapita had ocean-going canoes.","zh":"我們唯一可以肯定地說的是，拉皮塔人有遠洋獨木舟。"},{"en":"All we can say for certain means this is the only point we know definitely.","zh":"我們唯一可以肯定地說的是，表示這是我們確切知道的唯一重點。"},{"en":"All we can say for certain is that they reached the island by sea.","zh":"我們唯一可以肯定地說的是，他們經海路抵達該島。"},{"en":"This phrase separates evidence from speculation.","zh":"這個短語把證據與推測分開。"},{"en":"It is useful when knowledge is limited.","zh":"當知識有限時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"capable of ocean voyages","meaning":"能夠進行遠洋航行","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita had canoes capable of ocean voyages.","zh":"拉皮塔人有能夠進行遠洋航行的獨木舟。"},{"en":"Capable of ocean voyages means able to travel safely across open sea.","zh":"能夠進行遠洋航行，是指可以安全橫越開放海域。"},{"en":"A boat capable of ocean voyages must handle waves, wind and distance.","zh":"能遠洋航行的船必須應付海浪、風和距離。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses technical ability.","zh":"這個短語強調技術能力。"},{"en":"It distinguishes ocean travel from short coastal trips.","zh":"它把遠洋旅行與短途沿岸航行區分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have the ability to","meaning":"有能力去……","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita had the ability to sail their canoes.","zh":"拉皮塔人有能力駕駛他們的獨木舟。"},{"en":"To have the ability to do something means to be able to do it.","zh":"有能力做某事，是指能夠做到。"},{"en":"Skilled sailors had the ability to read winds and waves.","zh":"熟練水手有能力解讀風和浪。"},{"en":"Ability may come from training, experience or inherited knowledge.","zh":"能力可能來自培訓、經驗或承傳知識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes capacity.","zh":"這個短語描述能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"sailing skills","meaning":"航海技術","examples":[{"en":"Their sailing skills were developed over thousands of years.","zh":"他們的航海技術經數千年發展而成。"},{"en":"Sailing skills are abilities needed to control boats and navigate at sea.","zh":"航海技術是控制船隻和海上導航所需的能力。"},{"en":"Sailing skills include reading winds, setting sails and recognising signs of land.","zh":"航海技術包括解讀風向、調整船帆和辨認陸地跡象。"},{"en":"These skills helped ancient people cross open water.","zh":"這些技能幫助古人橫越開放水域。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical maritime expertise.","zh":"這個短語指實用海事專長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"pass down","meaning":"傳承下來","examples":[{"en":"Sailing skills were passed down by earlier mariners.","zh":"航海技術由早期航海者傳承下來。"},{"en":"To pass down knowledge means to transmit it to later generations.","zh":"把知識傳承下來，是指把它傳給後來世代。"},{"en":"Parents passed down navigation stories to their children.","zh":"父母把導航故事傳承給孩子。"},{"en":"Skills passed down orally may leave few physical traces.","zh":"口頭傳承的技能可能留下很少實物痕跡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cultural inheritance.","zh":"這個短語描述文化承傳。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"earlier mariners","meaning":"早期航海者","examples":[{"en":"Earlier mariners developed Pacific sailing skills.","zh":"早期航海者發展出太平洋航海技術。"},{"en":"Earlier mariners are sailors who lived and travelled before the group being discussed.","zh":"早期航海者，是在所討論群體之前生活和航行的水手。"},{"en":"Earlier mariners learned to cross short distances between visible islands.","zh":"早期航海者學會在可見島嶼之間橫越短距離。"},{"en":"Their knowledge formed the basis for later long voyages.","zh":"他們的知識形成後來長途航行的基礎。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to previous generations of sailors.","zh":"這個短語指較早世代的水手。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"work one’s way through","meaning":"一路穿越……","examples":[{"en":"Earlier mariners worked their way through western Pacific archipelagoes.","zh":"早期航海者一路穿越西太平洋群島。"},{"en":"To work one’s way through somewhere means to move gradually through it with effort.","zh":"一路穿越某地，是指努力地逐步通過該地。"},{"en":"The sailors worked their way through a chain of islands before reaching open ocean.","zh":"航海者一路穿越一連串島嶼，然後抵達開放海洋。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests slow, step-by-step progress.","zh":"這個短語暗示緩慢、一步步的進展。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing difficult routes.","zh":"它適合描述困難路線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"archipelagoes","meaning":"群島","examples":[{"en":"Mariners travelled through the archipelagoes of the western Pacific.","zh":"航海者穿越西太平洋的群島。"},{"en":"Archipelagoes are groups or chains of islands.","zh":"群島是一組或一連串島嶼。"},{"en":"The western Pacific contains many archipelagoes that could guide early sailors.","zh":"西太平洋有許多群島，可以引導早期航海者。"},{"en":"Island chains can make travel easier by providing visible destinations.","zh":"島鏈提供可見目的地，使旅行較容易。"},{"en":"This word is the plural of archipelago.","zh":"這個詞是 archipelago 的複數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"short crossings","meaning":"短距離渡海","examples":[{"en":"They made short crossings to islands within sight.","zh":"他們短距離渡海前往看得見的島嶼。"},{"en":"Short crossings are brief journeys across water from one land area to another.","zh":"短距離渡海，是由一片陸地橫越水域到另一片陸地的短旅程。"},{"en":"Early sailors practised navigation through short crossings between nearby islands.","zh":"早期航海者透過附近島嶼之間的短距離渡海練習導航。"},{"en":"Such crossings are less risky than open-ocean voyages.","zh":"這類渡海比遠洋航行風險較低。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited sea journeys.","zh":"這個短語描述有限的海上旅程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"within sight of","meaning":"在……看得見的範圍內","examples":[{"en":"They sailed to islands within sight of each other.","zh":"他們航行到彼此看得見的島嶼。"},{"en":"Within sight of means close enough to be seen.","zh":"在某物看得見的範圍內，是指距離近到可以看見。"},{"en":"The next island was within sight of the beach.","zh":"下一個島在海灘看得見的範圍內。"},{"en":"Sailing within sight of land is safer than sailing into empty horizons.","zh":"在看得見陸地範圍內航行，比駛向空曠地平線更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible distance.","zh":"這個短語描述可視距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the real adventure","meaning":"真正的冒險","examples":[{"en":"The real adventure began near the end of the Solomons chain.","zh":"真正的冒險在接近所羅門群島鏈盡頭時開始。"},{"en":"The real adventure means the truly difficult, exciting or dangerous part.","zh":"真正的冒險，是指真正困難、刺激或危險的部分。"},{"en":"The real adventure began when the sailors left the last visible island behind.","zh":"當航海者把最後一座可見島嶼拋在身後，真正的冒險便開始。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a turning point in a story.","zh":"這個短語標示故事轉折點。"},{"en":"It heightens the sense of risk.","zh":"它加強風險感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"near the end of","meaning":"接近……的盡頭","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita neared the end of the Solomons chain.","zh":"拉皮塔人接近所羅門群島鏈的盡頭。"},{"en":"Near the end of something means close to its final part.","zh":"接近某物的盡頭，是指靠近其最後部分。"},{"en":"The crew rested near the end of the island chain.","zh":"船員在接近島鏈盡頭處休息。"},{"en":"This phrase gives position within a sequence or route.","zh":"這個短語給出在次序或路線中的位置。"},{"en":"It often prepares for a transition.","zh":"它常為轉變作準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the Solomons chain","meaning":"所羅門群島鏈","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita reached the end of the Solomons chain.","zh":"拉皮塔人抵達所羅門群島鏈的盡頭。"},{"en":"The Solomons chain is a chain of islands in the western Pacific.","zh":"所羅門群島鏈是西太平洋的一連串島嶼。"},{"en":"The end of the Solomons chain marked a point where visible islands became fewer.","zh":"所羅門群島鏈的盡頭標誌着可見島嶼變少的地方。"},{"en":"This place is important because beyond it lay more open water.","zh":"這個地方很重要，因為再往外就是更開放的水域。"},{"en":"This phrase names a geographical island chain.","zh":"這個短語命名一條地理島鏈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the edge of the world","meaning":"世界的邊緣","examples":[{"en":"For the Lapita, this was the edge of the world.","zh":"對拉皮塔人而言，這就是世界的邊緣。"},{"en":"The edge of the world means the farthest known boundary of one’s world.","zh":"世界的邊緣，是某人所知世界的最遠界線。"},{"en":"To ancient sailors, the last island may have felt like the edge of the world.","zh":"對古代航海者而言，最後一座島可能感覺像世界的邊緣。"},{"en":"This phrase is imaginative, not literal.","zh":"這個短語是想像式說法，不是字面意思。"},{"en":"It shows how unknown the open ocean seemed.","zh":"它顯示開放海洋看起來多麼未知。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"nearest landfall","meaning":"最近的陸地","examples":[{"en":"The nearest landfall was almost 230 miles away.","zh":"最近的陸地相距接近 230 英里。"},{"en":"Nearest landfall means the closest place where sailors could reach land.","zh":"最近的陸地，是航海者可以抵達的最近陸地。"},{"en":"After leaving the island chain, the nearest landfall lay far beyond sight.","zh":"離開島鏈後，最近的陸地遠在視線之外。"},{"en":"This phrase measures the distance to safety or destination.","zh":"這個短語量度到安全地點或目的地的距離。"},{"en":"It is common in sea travel contexts.","zh":"它常見於海上旅行語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"out of sight of land","meaning":"看不見陸地","examples":[{"en":"The sailors were out of sight of land for many miles.","zh":"航海者有許多英里都看不見陸地。"},{"en":"Out of sight of land means too far away to see any land.","zh":"看不見陸地，是指距離陸地太遠而無法看見。"},{"en":"Once the canoe was out of sight of land, navigation became more dangerous.","zh":"一旦獨木舟駛到看不見陸地，導航就變得更危險。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a major step into open-ocean travel.","zh":"這個短語顯示進入遠洋航行的一大步。"},{"en":"It suggests isolation and risk.","zh":"它暗示孤立和風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"empty horizons on every side","meaning":"四周都是空曠的地平線","examples":[{"en":"The sailors faced empty horizons on every side.","zh":"航海者面對四周都是空曠的地平線。"},{"en":"Empty horizons on every side means there was only sea and sky in all directions.","zh":"四周都是空曠的地平線，是指所有方向都只有海和天空。"},{"en":"The crew saw empty horizons on every side after leaving the last island.","zh":"船員離開最後一座島後，看見四周都是空曠的地平線。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a feeling of loneliness and uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語營造孤寂和不確定感。"},{"en":"It emphasises the difficulty of navigation.","zh":"它強調導航的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"thrust into","meaning":"向……推進","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita’s thrust into the Pacific was eastward.","zh":"拉皮塔人向太平洋推進的方向是向東。"},{"en":"A thrust into somewhere is a strong movement or expansion into that area.","zh":"向某地推進，是強力移動或擴展進入該地區。"},{"en":"The explorers’ thrust into open water marked a new stage of migration.","zh":"探險者向開放水域推進，標誌遷徙新階段。"},{"en":"This noun suggests energy and determination.","zh":"這個名詞暗示力量和決心。"},{"en":"It is often used for bold expansion.","zh":"它常用於大膽擴展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"eastward","meaning":"向東","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita’s movement into the Pacific was eastward.","zh":"拉皮塔人進入太平洋的移動方向是向東。"},{"en":"Eastward means toward the east.","zh":"向東，是指朝東方。"},{"en":"The canoes sailed eastward into open water.","zh":"獨木舟向東駛入開放水域。"},{"en":"Direction mattered because the trade winds usually blew against them.","zh":"方向很重要，因為信風通常迎面吹來。"},{"en":"This word describes movement direction.","zh":"這個詞描述移動方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"prevailing trade winds","meaning":"盛行信風","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita sailed against the prevailing trade winds.","zh":"拉皮塔人逆着盛行信風航行。"},{"en":"Prevailing trade winds are the usual steady winds that blow in tropical ocean regions.","zh":"盛行信風是在熱帶海洋地區通常穩定吹動的風。"},{"en":"These winds strongly affected ancient sailing routes.","zh":"這些風強烈影響古代航行路線。"},{"en":"Sailing against prevailing trade winds required skill or favourable conditions.","zh":"逆着盛行信風航行需要技巧或有利條件。"},{"en":"This phrase combines normal wind direction with navigation.","zh":"這個短語把正常風向與導航連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"nagging headwinds","meaning":"持續迎面吹來的逆風","examples":[{"en":"Nagging headwinds may have helped the Lapita return home.","zh":"持續迎面吹來的逆風可能幫助拉皮塔人回家。"},{"en":"Nagging headwinds are persistent winds blowing against the direction of travel.","zh":"持續迎面吹來的逆風，是不斷朝旅行相反方向吹來的風。"},{"en":"Headwinds slowed the canoe but could help it return if the sailors turned back.","zh":"逆風會減慢獨木舟，但如果航海者掉頭，它可以幫助回程。"},{"en":"The word nagging suggests constant irritation or pressure.","zh":"“nagging” 暗示持續的煩擾或壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficult but useful wind conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述困難但有用的風況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the key to","meaning":"……的關鍵","examples":[{"en":"Those headwinds may have been the key to their success.","zh":"那些逆風可能是他們成功的關鍵。"},{"en":"The key to something is the most important factor that makes it possible.","zh":"某事的關鍵，是令它成為可能的最重要因素。"},{"en":"Knowing the winds was the key to safe exploration.","zh":"了解風向是安全探索的關鍵。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main explanation.","zh":"這個短語指出主要解釋。"},{"en":"It is common in analytical writing.","zh":"它常見於分析寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"sail out into the unknown","meaning":"駛向未知海域","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita could sail out into the unknown for days.","zh":"拉皮塔人可以連續數天駛向未知海域。"},{"en":"To sail out into the unknown means to leave familiar waters and enter unexplored areas.","zh":"駛向未知海域，是指離開熟悉水域，進入未探索區域。"},{"en":"The crew sailed out into the unknown beyond the last visible island.","zh":"船員駛離最後一座可見島嶼，進入未知海域。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses courage and uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語強調勇氣和不確定。"},{"en":"It is often used for exploration narratives.","zh":"它常用於探險敘事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reconnoiter","meaning":"偵察；探察","examples":[{"en":"The sailors could reconnoiter before turning back.","zh":"航海者可以在掉頭前先偵察。"},{"en":"To reconnoiter means to explore or inspect an area to gain information.","zh":"偵察或探察，是指探索或檢視某區域以取得資訊。"},{"en":"The canoe crew reconnoitered the sea for signs of land.","zh":"獨木舟船員探察海面，尋找陸地跡象。"},{"en":"Reconnoitering allows travellers to test conditions before committing fully.","zh":"偵察讓旅行者在完全投入前測試情況。"},{"en":"This verb is formal and often linked with exploration or military scouting.","zh":"這個動詞較正式，常與探索或軍事偵察相關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"secure in the knowledge that","meaning":"因知道……而安心","examples":[{"en":"They sailed out secure in the knowledge that the winds could bring them home.","zh":"他們因知道風可以把他們帶回家而安心地駛出。"},{"en":"Secure in the knowledge that means feeling confident because one knows a reassuring fact.","zh":"因知道某事而安心，是指因掌握令人放心的事實而有信心。"},{"en":"The sailors explored secure in the knowledge that trade winds could help their return.","zh":"航海者因知道信風能幫助回程而安心探索。"},{"en":"This phrase combines confidence with information.","zh":"這個短語結合信心與資訊。"},{"en":"It explains why a risky action felt manageable.","zh":"它解釋為何高風險行動感覺可應付。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"turn about","meaning":"掉頭","examples":[{"en":"If they found nothing, they could turn about.","zh":"如果他們沒有發現任何東西，就可以掉頭。"},{"en":"To turn about means to turn around and go back in the opposite direction.","zh":"掉頭，是指轉身或轉向，朝相反方向返回。"},{"en":"The canoe could turn about when the crew saw no sign of land.","zh":"當船員看不見陸地跡象，獨木舟可以掉頭。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests changing direction at sea.","zh":"這個短語暗示在海上改變方向。"},{"en":"It is useful for navigation contexts.","zh":"它適合導航語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"catch a swift ride home","meaning":"乘風快速回家","examples":[{"en":"The sailors could catch a swift ride home on the trade winds.","zh":"航海者可以乘着信風快速回家。"},{"en":"To catch a swift ride home means to return quickly by using a favourable force or transport.","zh":"乘風快速回家，是指利用有利力量或交通快速返回。"},{"en":"By turning west, the sailors could catch a swift ride home with the wind behind them.","zh":"透過轉向西方，航海者可以順着背後的風快速回家。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and vivid.","zh":"這個短語語氣較口語而生動。"},{"en":"It suggests that the return journey could be much easier.","zh":"它暗示回程可以容易得多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"make the whole thing work","meaning":"令整件事行得通","examples":[{"en":"The trade winds made the whole thing work.","zh":"信風令整件事行得通。"},{"en":"To make the whole thing work means to make the entire plan or system possible.","zh":"令整件事行得通，是指令整個計劃或系統成為可能。"},{"en":"The return winds made the exploration strategy work.","zh":"回程風令探索策略行得通。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what allowed success.","zh":"這個短語指出成功所依靠的因素。"},{"en":"It is conversational but useful for explanation.","zh":"它較口語，但適合解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"skilled seafarers","meaning":"技術高超的航海者","examples":[{"en":"Skilled seafarers could detect clues to land.","zh":"技術高超的航海者能察覺通往陸地的線索。"},{"en":"Skilled seafarers are experienced sailors who understand the sea well.","zh":"技術高超的航海者，是經驗豐富並熟悉海洋的水手。"},{"en":"Skilled seafarers notice birds, clouds and floating plants.","zh":"技術高超的航海者會注意海鳥、雲和漂浮植物。"},{"en":"Their knowledge can turn tiny signs into useful navigation clues.","zh":"他們的知識能把微小跡象變成有用導航線索。"},{"en":"This phrase praises practical sea expertise.","zh":"這個短語讚揚實用海上專長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"abundant leads to follow","meaning":"大量可追尋的線索","examples":[{"en":"Seafarers found abundant leads to follow to land.","zh":"航海者找到大量可追尋的通往陸地線索。"},{"en":"Abundant leads to follow are many clues that can guide someone toward a goal.","zh":"大量可追尋的線索，是許多可以引導某人朝目標前進的提示。"},{"en":"Birds and floating twigs provided abundant leads to follow.","zh":"鳥和漂浮樹枝提供大量可追尋的線索。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the sea offered information to skilled observers.","zh":"這個短語暗示海洋向熟練觀察者提供資訊。"},{"en":"It connects evidence with direction.","zh":"它把證據與方向連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"seabirds and turtles","meaning":"海鳥和海龜","examples":[{"en":"Seabirds and turtles could guide sailors towards land.","zh":"海鳥和海龜可以引導航海者前往陸地。"},{"en":"Seabirds and turtles are marine animals that may indicate nearby land or reefs.","zh":"海鳥和海龜是可能顯示附近有陸地或礁石的海洋動物。"},{"en":"Sailors watched seabirds and turtles because their behaviour could reveal direction.","zh":"航海者觀察海鳥和海龜，因為牠們的行為可以揭示方向。"},{"en":"Natural signs helped navigation before modern instruments.","zh":"在沒有現代儀器前，自然跡象幫助導航。"},{"en":"This phrase lists living clues at sea.","zh":"這個短語列出海上的生物線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"carried out to sea by the tides","meaning":"被潮水帶出海","examples":[{"en":"Coconuts and twigs were carried out to sea by the tides.","zh":"椰子和小樹枝被潮水帶出海。"},{"en":"Carried out to sea by the tides means moved from land into the ocean by tidal water.","zh":"被潮水帶出海，是指被潮汐水流從陸地帶到海洋。"},{"en":"Leaves carried out to sea by the tides may signal that land is nearby.","zh":"被潮水帶出海的葉子可能顯示附近有陸地。"},{"en":"Floating objects can guide sailors if they know how to read them.","zh":"如果航海者懂得解讀，漂浮物可以指引方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes tidal transport.","zh":"這個短語描述潮汐運送。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"pileup of clouds","meaning":"雲層堆積","examples":[{"en":"The afternoon pileup of clouds could suggest an island nearby.","zh":"下午的雲層堆積可能暗示附近有島嶼。"},{"en":"A pileup of clouds is a thick gathering or build-up of clouds.","zh":"雲層堆積是雲厚厚聚集或積聚。"},{"en":"Clouds may pile up over an island because warm air rises above land.","zh":"雲可能在島上方堆積，因為暖空氣在陸地上升。"},{"en":"Sailors could use cloud patterns as signs of land.","zh":"航海者可以利用雲形作為陸地跡象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visual clue in the sky.","zh":"這個短語描述天空中的視覺線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"on the horizon","meaning":"在地平線上","examples":[{"en":"Clouds on the horizon could indicate land.","zh":"地平線上的雲可能顯示有陸地。"},{"en":"On the horizon means at the distant line where the sky seems to meet the sea or land.","zh":"在地平線上，是指在天空似乎與海或地面相接的遠方線上。"},{"en":"The sailors saw a dark shape on the horizon.","zh":"航海者在地平線上看見一個深色形狀。"},{"en":"Signs on the horizon can be important during ocean navigation.","zh":"地平線上的跡象在海洋導航中很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distant visibility.","zh":"這個短語描述遠方可見之處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"betoken","meaning":"預示；顯示","examples":[{"en":"A pileup of clouds may betoken an island in the distance.","zh":"雲層堆積可能預示遠處有島嶼。"},{"en":"To betoken something means to be a sign of it.","zh":"預示某事，是指成為該事的跡象。"},{"en":"Smoke on the horizon may betoken human settlement nearby.","zh":"地平線上的煙可能顯示附近有人類聚落。"},{"en":"This word is formal and literary.","zh":"這個詞較正式且具文學色彩。"},{"en":"It means indicate or signal.","zh":"它的意思是 indicate 或 signal。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in the distance","meaning":"在遠處","examples":[{"en":"An island may lie in the distance.","zh":"一座島可能位於遠處。"},{"en":"In the distance means far away but possibly visible.","zh":"在遠處，是指離得很遠但可能看得見。"},{"en":"The sailors saw clouds in the distance and changed course.","zh":"航海者看見遠處有雲，便改變航向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes far-off location.","zh":"這個短語描述遠方位置。"},{"en":"It often creates a sense of discovery.","zh":"它常營造發現感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"presuppose","meaning":"預先假定","examples":[{"en":"This explanation presupposes one essential detail.","zh":"這個解釋預先假定一個關鍵細節。"},{"en":"To presuppose something means to assume it is true before making an argument.","zh":"預先假定某事，是指在提出論點前假設它為真。"},{"en":"The theory presupposes that the sailors could control their canoes well.","zh":"這個理論預先假定航海者能很好控制獨木舟。"},{"en":"A presupposition may be reasonable but still unproven.","zh":"預設可能合理，但仍未被證明。"},{"en":"This verb is common in academic analysis.","zh":"這個動詞常見於學術分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"essential detail","meaning":"關鍵細節","examples":[{"en":"The theory depends on one essential detail.","zh":"這個理論取決於一個關鍵細節。"},{"en":"An essential detail is a key piece of information that is necessary for an explanation.","zh":"關鍵細節是解釋中必要的重要資訊。"},{"en":"Whether the canoes could tack is an essential detail.","zh":"獨木舟能否迎風斜駛是一個關鍵細節。"},{"en":"Without essential details, a theory may remain uncertain.","zh":"沒有關鍵細節，理論可能仍不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies crucial information.","zh":"這個短語指出重要資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"master the advanced art of","meaning":"掌握……的高階技巧","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita may have mastered the advanced art of tacking.","zh":"拉皮塔人可能已掌握迎風斜駛的高階技巧。"},{"en":"To master the advanced art of something means to become highly skilled at a difficult technique.","zh":"掌握某事的高階技巧，是指精通一項困難技術。"},{"en":"Skilled sailors mastered the advanced art of reading winds.","zh":"熟練水手掌握了判讀風向的高階技巧。"},{"en":"The phrase makes the skill sound complex and impressive.","zh":"這個短語令技能聽起來複雜而令人佩服。"},{"en":"It emphasises expertise gained through practice.","zh":"它強調透過練習獲得的專長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"tacking into the wind","meaning":"迎風斜駛","examples":[{"en":"Tacking into the wind would have helped sailors travel eastward.","zh":"迎風斜駛會幫助航海者向東航行。"},{"en":"Tacking into the wind is a sailing technique that allows a boat to move against the wind by zigzagging.","zh":"迎風斜駛是一種讓船透過之字形航行逆風前進的航海技巧。"},{"en":"A canoe that could tack into the wind would be easier to sail eastward.","zh":"能迎風斜駛的獨木舟較容易向東航行。"},{"en":"This technique is important when the wind blows from the direction sailors want to go.","zh":"當風從航海者想前往的方向吹來，這項技術很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an advanced sailing method.","zh":"這個短語指高階航海方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no proof that","meaning":"沒有證據顯示","examples":[{"en":"There is no proof that the Lapita could tack into the wind.","zh":"沒有證據顯示拉皮塔人能迎風斜駛。"},{"en":"No proof that something is true means there is no clear evidence supporting it.","zh":"沒有證據顯示某事為真，是指沒有清楚證據支持它。"},{"en":"There is no proof that the canoe had a particular sail design.","zh":"沒有證據顯示該獨木舟有某種特定船帆設計。"},{"en":"The phrase does not mean the idea is impossible.","zh":"這個短語不代表想法不可能。"},{"en":"It simply marks a lack of evidence.","zh":"它只是標示缺乏證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"assumption","meaning":"假設","examples":[{"en":"The theory is based on an assumption about their canoes.","zh":"這個理論建基於關於他們獨木舟的假設。"},{"en":"An assumption is something believed to be true without definite proof.","zh":"假設是在沒有確切證據下被認為真實的事。"},{"en":"The reconstruction rested on the assumption that the canoes had sails.","zh":"重建模型建基於獨木舟有帆的假設。"},{"en":"Assumptions help build theories but must be tested.","zh":"假設幫助建立理論，但必須被測試。"},{"en":"This word refers to an unproven starting point.","zh":"這個詞指未被證明的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"re-create early voyages","meaning":"重現早期航行","examples":[{"en":"People have built canoes to re-create early voyages.","zh":"人們建造獨木舟以重現早期航行。"},{"en":"To re-create early voyages means to repeat or simulate ancient journeys.","zh":"重現早期航行，是指重複或模擬古代旅程。"},{"en":"Researchers re-created early voyages to test canoe performance.","zh":"研究人員重現早期航行，以測試獨木舟性能。"},{"en":"Re-creation helps test whether a theory is practical.","zh":"重現有助測試理論是否實際可行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes experimental reconstruction.","zh":"這個短語描述實驗性重建。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"based on that assumption","meaning":"基於那個假設","examples":[{"en":"The canoe reconstructions were based on that assumption.","zh":"這些獨木舟重建模型基於那個假設。"},{"en":"Based on that assumption means built or argued from that belief.","zh":"基於那個假設，是指以該信念作為建立或論證基礎。"},{"en":"The sailing experiment was based on the assumption that the canoe could tack.","zh":"航行實驗基於獨木舟能迎風斜駛的假設。"},{"en":"If the assumption is wrong, the conclusion may be weaker.","zh":"如果假設錯誤，結論可能較弱。"},{"en":"This phrase connects evidence or models with their starting belief.","zh":"這個短語把證據或模型與其起始信念連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"how they were rigged","meaning":"它們如何裝配帆索","examples":[{"en":"No one knows how Lapita canoes were rigged.","zh":"沒有人知道拉皮塔獨木舟如何裝配帆索。"},{"en":"How they were rigged means how their sails, ropes and equipment were arranged.","zh":"它們如何裝配帆索，是指船帆、繩索和設備如何安排。"},{"en":"Canoe rigging affects whether a boat can sail against the wind.","zh":"獨木舟帆索裝配會影響船能否逆風航行。"},{"en":"Without physical remains, researchers can only infer the rigging.","zh":"沒有實物遺存，研究人員只能推斷帆索裝配。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about sailing design.","zh":"這個短語詢問航行設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"however they did it","meaning":"無論他們如何做到","examples":[{"en":"However they did it, the Lapita spread across the Pacific.","zh":"無論他們如何做到，拉皮塔人都已散佈於太平洋。"},{"en":"However they did it means no matter what exact method they used.","zh":"無論他們如何做到，是指不論他們使用甚麼確切方法。"},{"en":"However they crossed the sea, their achievement remains remarkable.","zh":"無論他們如何橫越海洋，他們的成就仍令人驚嘆。"},{"en":"This phrase admits uncertainty while stressing the result.","zh":"這個短語承認不確定，同時強調結果。"},{"en":"It is useful when the outcome is clear but the method is not.","zh":"當結果清楚但方法不明時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"call it quits","meaning":"停止；到此為止","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita spread far across the Pacific and then called it quits.","zh":"拉皮塔人廣泛散佈於太平洋，然後便停止了。"},{"en":"To call it quits means to stop doing something.","zh":"停止或到此為止，是指不再繼續做某事。"},{"en":"After reaching many islands, the sailors may have called it quits and settled down.","zh":"抵達許多島嶼後，航海者可能決定到此為止並安頓下來。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and conversational.","zh":"這個短語較口語。"},{"en":"It suggests choosing not to continue farther.","zh":"它暗示選擇不再繼續前進。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"for reasons known only to them","meaning":"原因只有他們自己知道","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita stopped for reasons known only to them.","zh":"拉皮塔人停下來的原因只有他們自己知道。"},{"en":"For reasons known only to them means nobody else knows exactly why they did it.","zh":"原因只有他們自己知道，是指其他人不知道他們確切為何這樣做。"},{"en":"The settlers left the island for reasons known only to them.","zh":"定居者離開該島的原因只有他們自己知道。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights historical uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語突出歷史不確定性。"},{"en":"It suggests motives are lost to time.","zh":"它暗示動機已隨時間消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"ahead lay","meaning":"前方是……","examples":[{"en":"Ahead lay the vast emptiness of the central Pacific.","zh":"前方是中太平洋的浩瀚空曠。"},{"en":"Ahead lay means in front of them there was.","zh":"前方是，是指在他們前面有某物。"},{"en":"Ahead lay open water with no visible islands.","zh":"前方是沒有可見島嶼的開放水域。"},{"en":"This phrase is literary and dramatic.","zh":"這個短語具文學和戲劇色彩。"},{"en":"It often introduces a major challenge.","zh":"它常引入重大挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"vast emptiness","meaning":"浩瀚空曠","examples":[{"en":"The central Pacific was a vast emptiness.","zh":"中太平洋是一片浩瀚空曠。"},{"en":"Vast emptiness means an enormous open space with little or nothing visible.","zh":"浩瀚空曠，是指巨大而幾乎沒有可見物的開放空間。"},{"en":"Sailors faced vast emptiness when no land appeared for days.","zh":"當數日看不見陸地，航海者面對浩瀚空曠。"},{"en":"The phrase creates loneliness and danger.","zh":"這個短語營造孤獨和危險感。"},{"en":"It emphasises the scale of open ocean.","zh":"它強調開放海洋的規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"central Pacific","meaning":"中太平洋","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita did not move far into the central Pacific.","zh":"拉皮塔人沒有深入中太平洋太遠。"},{"en":"The central Pacific is the middle region of the Pacific Ocean.","zh":"中太平洋是太平洋中部區域。"},{"en":"The central Pacific contains vast distances between islands.","zh":"中太平洋的島嶼之間距離極大。"},{"en":"Travel there required long open-water voyages.","zh":"在那裡旅行需要長途開放水域航行。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a broad ocean region.","zh":"這個短語指出一個廣闊海洋區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"too thinly stretched","meaning":"人手過於分散","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita may have been too thinly stretched to venture farther.","zh":"拉皮塔人可能人手過於分散，無法冒險走得更遠。"},{"en":"Too thinly stretched means spread over too wide an area with too few people or resources.","zh":"人手過於分散，是指人或資源分布範圍太廣而數量不足。"},{"en":"A small team covering many islands may become too thinly stretched.","zh":"一支小隊負責許多島嶼，可能變得人手過於分散。"},{"en":"When people are thinly stretched, further expansion becomes difficult.","zh":"當人手過於分散，進一步擴展便變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes overextension.","zh":"這個短語描述過度擴張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"venture farther","meaning":"冒險走得更遠","examples":[{"en":"They may have lacked the numbers to venture farther.","zh":"他們可能缺乏人數去冒險走得更遠。"},{"en":"To venture farther means to go further into unknown or risky territory.","zh":"冒險走得更遠，是指進一步進入未知或有風險的地方。"},{"en":"The sailors did not venture farther once supplies became low.","zh":"物資變少後，航海者沒有冒險走得更遠。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests risk beyond the current boundary.","zh":"這個短語暗示超越當前邊界的風險。"},{"en":"It is often used for exploration.","zh":"它常用於探索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"number more than","meaning":"數量超過","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita probably never numbered more than a few thousand.","zh":"拉皮塔人的數量可能從未超過幾千人。"},{"en":"To number more than means to have a population or total greater than a certain amount.","zh":"數量超過，是指人口或總數高於某數量。"},{"en":"The settlement may not have numbered more than a few hundred people.","zh":"該定居點人數可能不超過幾百人。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for population size.","zh":"這個短語用於人口規模。"},{"en":"It often appears in historical estimates.","zh":"它常出現在歷史估算中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"in total","meaning":"總共","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita probably numbered only a few thousand in total.","zh":"拉皮塔人總共可能只有幾千人。"},{"en":"In total means altogether, counting everything or everyone.","zh":"總共，是指把所有東西或所有人加起來。"},{"en":"The expedition included twenty people in total.","zh":"遠征隊總共有二十人。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a complete count.","zh":"這個短語給出完整數量。"},{"en":"It is used to avoid counting separate parts individually.","zh":"它用來避免逐項分開計算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"rapid migration eastward","meaning":"快速向東遷徙","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita encountered hundreds of islands during their rapid migration eastward.","zh":"拉皮塔人在快速向東遷徙期間遇到數以百計島嶼。"},{"en":"Rapid migration eastward means quick movement of people toward the east.","zh":"快速向東遷徙，是人群快速朝東方移動。"},{"en":"Their rapid migration eastward carried families across many island groups.","zh":"他們快速向東遷徙，把家庭帶過許多島群。"},{"en":"This phrase combines speed and direction.","zh":"這個短語結合速度和方向。"},{"en":"It describes a major population movement.","zh":"它描述重大人口移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"encounter hundreds of","meaning":"遇到數以百計的……","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita encountered hundreds of islands.","zh":"拉皮塔人遇到數以百計的島嶼。"},{"en":"To encounter hundreds of something means to come across many of them.","zh":"遇到數以百計的某物，是指碰見大量該事物。"},{"en":"Sailors encountered hundreds of reefs and small islands along the way.","zh":"航海者沿途遇到數以百計的礁石和小島。"},{"en":"This phrase shows repeated discovery.","zh":"這個短語顯示反覆發現。"},{"en":"It suggests the Pacific offered many stopping points.","zh":"它暗示太平洋提供許多停靠點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"supplied with","meaning":"擁有；獲得","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita were supplied with an abundance of islands.","zh":"拉皮塔人獲得大量島嶼作為資源。"},{"en":"To be supplied with something means to have or be provided with it.","zh":"擁有或獲得某物，是指有某物或被提供某物。"},{"en":"The route was supplied with many islands where settlers could stop.","zh":"這條路線擁有許多可讓定居者停靠的島嶼。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests availability of resources or opportunities.","zh":"這個短語暗示資源或機會可取得。"},{"en":"It can be literal or figurative.","zh":"它可以按字面或比喻理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"embarrassment of riches","meaning":"過多的豐富資源","examples":[{"en":"The islands offered an embarrassment of riches.","zh":"這些島嶼提供過多的豐富資源。"},{"en":"An embarrassment of riches means so many good options or resources that choosing becomes difficult.","zh":"過多的豐富資源，是指好選擇或資源多到令人難以選擇。"},{"en":"The settlers found an embarrassment of riches in fertile islands and marine resources.","zh":"定居者在肥沃島嶼和海洋資源中找到過多的豐富資源。"},{"en":"This phrase is positive but slightly humorous.","zh":"這個短語意思正面，但略帶幽默。"},{"en":"It suggests abundance beyond need.","zh":"它暗示豐富程度超過需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"settle down","meaning":"安頓下來","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita could settle down on the islands they found.","zh":"拉皮塔人可以在他們發現的島嶼上安頓下來。"},{"en":"To settle down means to stop moving and begin living permanently in a place.","zh":"安頓下來，是指停止移動並開始在某地永久生活。"},{"en":"After years of travel, the families settled down on a fertile island.","zh":"多年旅行後，這些家庭在肥沃島嶼上安頓下來。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts movement with stability.","zh":"這個短語對比移動與穩定。"},{"en":"It is common in migration stories.","zh":"它常見於遷徙故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"Earth’s last Edens","meaning":"地球最後的伊甸園","examples":[{"en":"The islands were described as Earth’s last Edens.","zh":"這些島嶼被描述為地球最後的伊甸園。"},{"en":"Earth’s last Edens means some of the last untouched, beautiful and fertile places on Earth.","zh":"地球最後的伊甸園，是地球上最後一些未受破壞、美麗而肥沃的地方。"},{"en":"To settlers, empty tropical islands may have seemed like Earth’s last Edens.","zh":"對定居者而言，空無人煙的熱帶島嶼可能像地球最後的伊甸園。"},{"en":"The phrase evokes paradise and abundance.","zh":"這個短語喚起天堂和豐饒意象。"},{"en":"It is poetic and idealised.","zh":"它具詩意並帶理想化色彩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"give all the credit to","meaning":"把所有功勞歸於……","examples":[{"en":"Anderson does not give all the credit to human skill and daring.","zh":"Anderson 沒有把所有功勞歸於人類技巧和膽識。"},{"en":"To give all the credit to something means to say it deserves all the praise for success.","zh":"把所有功勞歸於某事，是指說它應得所有成功讚賞。"},{"en":"The researcher did not give all the credit to sailing skill alone.","zh":"研究人員沒有把所有功勞只歸於航海技術。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces another factor in the explanation.","zh":"這個短語引入解釋中的另一因素。"},{"en":"It is useful when success has multiple causes.","zh":"當成功有多個原因時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"human skill and daring","meaning":"人類技巧和膽識","examples":[{"en":"Human skill and daring may not fully explain the migration.","zh":"人類技巧和膽識未必能完全解釋這次遷徙。"},{"en":"Human skill and daring means people’s technical ability and courage.","zh":"人類技巧和膽識，是人的技術能力和勇氣。"},{"en":"The voyages required human skill and daring, but climate may also have helped.","zh":"這些航行需要人類技巧和膽識，但氣候可能也有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase recognises achievement while leaving room for other causes.","zh":"這個短語承認成就，同時容許其他原因。"},{"en":"It combines competence with bravery.","zh":"它結合能力與勇氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"invoke the winds of change","meaning":"引用變化之風作解釋","examples":[{"en":"Anderson invokes the winds of change to explain the migration.","zh":"Anderson 引用變化之風來解釋這次遷徙。"},{"en":"To invoke the winds of change means to refer to changing winds or broader change as an explanation.","zh":"引用變化之風作解釋，是指以風向變化或更廣泛變化作為解釋。"},{"en":"The researcher invoked the winds of change when discussing El Niño.","zh":"研究人員討論厄爾尼諾時引用變化之風。"},{"en":"The phrase is partly literal and partly metaphorical.","zh":"這個短語部分按字面理解，部分具比喻意味。"},{"en":"It connects climate shifts with historical movement.","zh":"它把氣候轉變與歷史移動連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"climate disruption","meaning":"氣候擾動","examples":[{"en":"El Niño is a climate disruption that affects the Pacific.","zh":"厄爾尼諾是影響太平洋的氣候擾動。"},{"en":"Climate disruption is a disturbance in normal climate patterns.","zh":"氣候擾動是正常氣候模式受到干擾。"},{"en":"El Niño can create climate disruption by changing winds and ocean temperatures.","zh":"厄爾尼諾可透過改變風向和海水溫度造成氣候擾動。"},{"en":"Such disruptions can affect travel, rainfall and food supplies.","zh":"這類擾動會影響旅行、降雨和食物供應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes abnormal climate disturbance.","zh":"這個短語描述異常氣候干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"scatter the first settlers","meaning":"使最早的定居者分散","examples":[{"en":"El Niño may have helped scatter the first settlers across the ocean.","zh":"厄爾尼諾可能幫助使最早的定居者分散到海洋各處。"},{"en":"To scatter settlers means to spread them over a wide area.","zh":"使定居者分散，是指把他們散佈到廣大地區。"},{"en":"Strong winds may have scattered voyagers across distant islands.","zh":"強風可能把航海者分散到遙遠島嶼。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests movement that may be partly accidental.","zh":"這個短語暗示移動可能部分是意外的。"},{"en":"It connects climate with human dispersal.","zh":"它把氣候與人類分散連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"to the ends of the ocean","meaning":"到海洋盡頭","examples":[{"en":"Settlers may have been scattered to the ends of the ocean.","zh":"定居者可能被分散到海洋盡頭。"},{"en":"To the ends of the ocean means to the most distant parts of the sea.","zh":"到海洋盡頭，是指到海洋最遙遠的部分。"},{"en":"The phrase makes the voyages sound extremely far-reaching.","zh":"這個短語令航程聽起來極其遙遠。"},{"en":"It is poetic rather than precise.","zh":"它是詩意說法，而非精確位置。"},{"en":"It emphasises vast distance.","zh":"它強調巨大距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"climate data obtained from","meaning":"從……取得的氣候數據","examples":[{"en":"Climate data obtained from corals supports the theory.","zh":"從珊瑚取得的氣候數據支持這個理論。"},{"en":"Climate data obtained from something is climate information collected from that source.","zh":"從某物取得的氣候數據，是從該來源收集到的氣候資訊。"},{"en":"Climate data obtained from lake sediments can reveal past rainfall patterns.","zh":"從湖床沉積物取得的氣候數據可以揭示過去降雨模式。"},{"en":"Scientists use natural archives to reconstruct old climates.","zh":"科學家使用自然檔案重建古氣候。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the evidence source.","zh":"這個短語指出證據來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"slow-growing corals","meaning":"生長緩慢的珊瑚","examples":[{"en":"Slow-growing corals preserve evidence of past climate events.","zh":"生長緩慢的珊瑚保存過去氣候事件的證據。"},{"en":"Slow-growing corals are corals that increase in size gradually over long periods.","zh":"生長緩慢的珊瑚，是長時間逐漸增大的珊瑚。"},{"en":"Their growth layers can record changes in ocean conditions.","zh":"它們的生長層可以記錄海洋環境變化。"},{"en":"Scientists study slow-growing corals like natural climate archives.","zh":"科學家把生長緩慢的珊瑚當作自然氣候檔案研究。"},{"en":"This phrase connects marine biology with climate history.","zh":"這個短語把海洋生物學與氣候歷史連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"lake-bed sediments","meaning":"湖床沉積物","examples":[{"en":"Lake-bed sediments can provide climate data.","zh":"湖床沉積物可以提供氣候數據。"},{"en":"Lake-bed sediments are layers of mud, sand and organic material at the bottom of lakes.","zh":"湖床沉積物是湖底的淤泥、沙和有機物層。"},{"en":"These sediments can preserve pollen, minerals and other climate clues.","zh":"這些沉積物可以保存花粉、礦物和其他氣候線索。"},{"en":"Scientists read sediment layers to understand past environments.","zh":"科學家閱讀沉積層以理解過去環境。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to natural deposits under lake water.","zh":"這個短語指湖水下方的自然沉積物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"point to","meaning":"指向；顯示","examples":[{"en":"The data point to frequent El Niño events.","zh":"數據顯示厄爾尼諾現象頻繁出現。"},{"en":"To point to something means to indicate or suggest it.","zh":"指向某事，是指顯示或暗示它。"},{"en":"The pottery evidence points to contact between islands.","zh":"陶器證據顯示島嶼之間有接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when evidence supports a conclusion.","zh":"當證據支持某結論時，這個短語很常見。"},{"en":"It does not always mean absolute proof.","zh":"它不一定代表絕對證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a series of","meaning":"一連串","examples":[{"en":"The data point to a series of unusual climate events.","zh":"數據顯示一連串不尋常氣候事件。"},{"en":"A series of something is several events or items happening one after another.","zh":"一連串某事，是幾個事件或項目一個接一個發生。"},{"en":"A series of storms damaged the island over several weeks.","zh":"一連串風暴在數星期內破壞了該島。"},{"en":"This phrase shows repeated occurrence.","zh":"這個短語顯示反覆出現。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing linked events.","zh":"它適合描述相連事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"unusually frequent","meaning":"異常頻繁的","examples":[{"en":"Unusually frequent El Niño events occurred during the Lapita expansion.","zh":"拉皮塔人擴張期間，厄爾尼諾現象異常頻繁。"},{"en":"Unusually frequent means happening more often than normal.","zh":"異常頻繁，是指比正常更常發生。"},{"en":"Unusually frequent storms can change travel routes.","zh":"異常頻繁的風暴可以改變旅行路線。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a pattern that stands out from the ordinary.","zh":"這個短語暗示某模式不同尋常。"},{"en":"It is often used in climate analysis.","zh":"它常用於氣候分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"El Niño events","meaning":"厄爾尼諾現象","examples":[{"en":"El Niño events may have affected ancient Pacific voyages.","zh":"厄爾尼諾現象可能影響古代太平洋航行。"},{"en":"El Niño events are climate events involving unusual warming in parts of the Pacific Ocean.","zh":"厄爾尼諾現象是太平洋部分海域異常變暖的氣候事件。"},{"en":"These events can change winds, rainfall and ocean conditions.","zh":"這些現象會改變風向、降雨和海洋狀況。"},{"en":"Ancient sailors may have benefited from wind changes during El Niño events.","zh":"古代航海者可能受惠於厄爾尼諾期間的風向變化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to repeated episodes of El Niño.","zh":"這個短語指厄爾尼諾的反覆事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"around the time of","meaning":"大約在……時期","examples":[{"en":"These events occurred around the time of the Lapita expansion.","zh":"這些事件大約發生在拉皮塔人擴張時期。"},{"en":"Around the time of something means during approximately the same period.","zh":"大約在某時期，是指約在同一時段。"},{"en":"The climate shift happened around the time of the migration.","zh":"氣候轉變大約發生在遷徙時期。"},{"en":"This phrase gives approximate timing.","zh":"這個短語給出約略時間。"},{"en":"It does not mean the exact same date.","zh":"它不代表完全相同日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the Lapita expansion","meaning":"拉皮塔人的擴張","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita expansion may have been helped by climate events.","zh":"拉皮塔人的擴張可能受到氣候事件幫助。"},{"en":"The Lapita expansion was the spread of Lapita people and culture across Pacific islands.","zh":"拉皮塔人的擴張，是拉皮塔人和文化在太平洋島嶼間的傳播。"},{"en":"The expansion involved travel, settlement and movement of plants and animals.","zh":"這次擴張涉及旅行、定居以及植物和動物的移動。"},{"en":"Climate events may have influenced the speed and direction of expansion.","zh":"氣候事件可能影響擴張速度和方向。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major prehistoric migration.","zh":"這個短語命名一次重要史前遷徙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"second wave of","meaning":"第二波","examples":[{"en":"A second wave of pioneer navigators travelled farther east.","zh":"第二波先驅航海者向更東方航行。"},{"en":"A second wave of people means a later group following an earlier one.","zh":"第二波人群，是跟隨早前一批之後的較後群體。"},{"en":"A second wave of settlers reached more distant islands.","zh":"第二波定居者抵達更遙遠島嶼。"},{"en":"This phrase shows stages of movement over time.","zh":"這個短語顯示移動隨時間分階段發生。"},{"en":"It often appears in migration history.","zh":"它常出現在遷徙歷史中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"pioneer navigators","meaning":"先驅航海者","examples":[{"en":"Pioneer navigators made voyages to remote Pacific islands.","zh":"先驅航海者航行到偏遠太平洋島嶼。"},{"en":"Pioneer navigators are among the first sailors to find routes to new places.","zh":"先驅航海者是最早找到通往新地方路線的水手之一。"},{"en":"These navigators opened paths that later travellers could follow.","zh":"這些航海者開闢了後來旅人可跟隨的路徑。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises both first discovery and navigation skill.","zh":"這個短語同時強調首次發現和導航技巧。"},{"en":"It describes early route-finders.","zh":"它描述早期開路者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"remotest corners","meaning":"最偏遠的角落","examples":[{"en":"The voyagers reached the remotest corners of the Pacific.","zh":"航海者抵達太平洋最偏遠的角落。"},{"en":"Remotest corners are the most distant and isolated parts of a region.","zh":"最偏遠的角落，是某地區最遙遠和孤立的部分。"},{"en":"Easter Island is often imagined as one of the remotest corners of the Pacific.","zh":"復活節島常被想像為太平洋最偏遠角落之一。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises extreme distance.","zh":"這個短語強調極端距離。"},{"en":"It is more vivid than remote places.","zh":"它比 remote places 更生動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"reverse the regular flow of","meaning":"逆轉……的正常流向","examples":[{"en":"El Niño can reverse the regular flow of the trade winds.","zh":"厄爾尼諾可以逆轉信風的正常流向。"},{"en":"To reverse the regular flow of something means to make it move in the opposite direction from normal.","zh":"逆轉某物的正常流向，是指令它朝與平常相反的方向移動。"},{"en":"A climate event may reverse the regular flow of winds for weeks.","zh":"氣候事件可能連續數星期逆轉風的正常流向。"},{"en":"Such reversal could help sailors travel in an otherwise difficult direction.","zh":"這種逆轉可幫助航海者朝原本困難的方向前進。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major change in normal movement.","zh":"這個短語描述正常移動的重大改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"weeks at a time","meaning":"一次持續數星期","examples":[{"en":"The winds could change for weeks at a time.","zh":"風向可能一次持續數星期地改變。"},{"en":"Weeks at a time means for periods lasting several weeks each.","zh":"一次持續數星期，是指每次持續幾星期。"},{"en":"During El Niño, unusual winds may persist for weeks at a time.","zh":"在厄爾尼諾期間，異常風向可能一次持續數星期。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses duration and repetition.","zh":"這個短語強調持續時間和重複性。"},{"en":"It suggests the change lasted long enough to matter.","zh":"它暗示變化持續得足以產生影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"super El Niño events","meaning":"超級厄爾尼諾現象","examples":[{"en":"Super El Niño events may have helped ancient voyagers.","zh":"超級厄爾尼諾現象可能幫助古代航海者。"},{"en":"Super El Niño events are unusually strong El Niño events.","zh":"超級厄爾尼諾現象是異常強烈的厄爾尼諾事件。"},{"en":"Such events may reverse winds more powerfully or for longer periods.","zh":"這些事件可能更強烈或更長時間地逆轉風向。"},{"en":"Ancient sailors could have been carried farther east during super El Niño events.","zh":"古代航海者可能在超級厄爾尼諾期間被帶往更東方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extreme climate episodes.","zh":"這個短語描述極端氣候事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"speed ancient mariners","meaning":"加速古代航海者前進","examples":[{"en":"These events might have sped ancient mariners eastward.","zh":"這些事件可能加速古代航海者向東前進。"},{"en":"To speed ancient mariners means to help ancient sailors move faster.","zh":"加速古代航海者前進，是指幫助古代水手更快移動。"},{"en":"Reversed winds could speed mariners toward distant islands.","zh":"逆轉風向可以加速航海者前往遙遠島嶼。"},{"en":"This phrase links climate with faster travel.","zh":"這個短語把氣候與更快旅行連接起來。"},{"en":"It suggests the winds acted like a natural engine.","zh":"它暗示風像自然引擎一樣發揮作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"long, unplanned voyages","meaning":"漫長而非計劃中的航行","examples":[{"en":"Climate events could have caused long, unplanned voyages.","zh":"氣候事件可能造成漫長而非計劃中的航行。"},{"en":"Long, unplanned voyages are lengthy journeys that were not intended in advance.","zh":"漫長而非計劃中的航行，是事前沒有打算進行的長途旅程。"},{"en":"Strong winds may push a canoe into a long, unplanned voyage.","zh":"強風可能把獨木舟推入一場漫長而非計劃中的航行。"},{"en":"Such voyages could accidentally lead to new island discoveries.","zh":"這類航行可能意外帶來新島嶼發現。"},{"en":"This phrase combines distance with accident.","zh":"這個短語結合距離與偶然。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be key to","meaning":"對……至關重要","examples":[{"en":"El Niño may have been key to launching Polynesians eastward.","zh":"厄爾尼諾可能對把波利尼西亞人送往東方至關重要。"},{"en":"To be key to something means to be very important for causing or enabling it.","zh":"對某事至關重要，是指對造成或促成它非常重要。"},{"en":"Wind changes may have been key to crossing open ocean.","zh":"風向變化可能對橫越開放海洋至關重要。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a crucial factor.","zh":"這個短語指出關鍵因素。"},{"en":"It is stronger than saying related to.","zh":"它比 saying related to 更強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"launch someone across","meaning":"把某人送越……","examples":[{"en":"Winds may have launched Polynesians across open water.","zh":"風可能把波利尼西亞人送越開放水域。"},{"en":"To launch someone across a space means to send or propel them across it.","zh":"把某人送越某空間，是指把他們送過或推過它。"},{"en":"Strong winds launched the canoe across the wide gap.","zh":"強風把獨木舟送越廣闊空隙。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the movement sound forceful and sudden.","zh":"這個短語令移動聽起來有力量且突然。"},{"en":"It can be literal or metaphorical.","zh":"它可按字面或比喻理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"wide expanse of open water","meaning":"廣闊無邊的開放水域","examples":[{"en":"The voyagers crossed a wide expanse of open water.","zh":"航海者橫越一大片廣闊無邊的開放水域。"},{"en":"A wide expanse of open water is a large uninterrupted area of sea.","zh":"廣闊無邊的開放水域，是一大片沒有陸地間斷的海面。"},{"en":"Crossing a wide expanse of open water required confidence and supplies.","zh":"橫越廣闊開放水域需要信心和物資。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises distance without land.","zh":"這個短語強調沒有陸地的距離。"},{"en":"It creates a sense of exposure and risk.","zh":"它營造暴露和風險感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"cross that gap","meaning":"越過那段空隙","examples":[{"en":"Once they crossed that gap, they could island-hop.","zh":"一旦他們越過那段空隙，就可以跳島航行。"},{"en":"To cross that gap means to travel across the empty space between land areas.","zh":"越過那段空隙，是指橫越陸地之間的空白空間。"},{"en":"After crossing the gap, the sailors reached islands closer together.","zh":"越過空隙後，航海者抵達彼此較接近的島嶼。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a major barrier in a route.","zh":"這個短語標示路線中的重大障礙。"},{"en":"It shows that one difficult crossing changed what became possible.","zh":"它顯示一段困難橫渡如何改變之後的可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"island-hop throughout","meaning":"在各島之間跳島航行","examples":[{"en":"Sailors could island-hop throughout the region.","zh":"航海者可以在該區各島之間跳島航行。"},{"en":"To island-hop throughout a region means to travel from island to island across it.","zh":"在某區跳島航行，是指由一個島到另一個島旅行。"},{"en":"After reaching one island group, navigators could island-hop farther east.","zh":"抵達一個島群後，航海家可以繼續向東跳島航行。"},{"en":"Island-hopping reduces risk because each island becomes a stepping stone.","zh":"跳島航行降低風險，因為每個島都成為踏腳石。"},{"en":"This phrase describes staged island travel.","zh":"這個短語描述分階段島嶼旅行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"downwind to","meaning":"順風前往……","examples":[{"en":"From the Marquesas, it is mostly downwind to Hawaii.","zh":"從馬克薩斯群島前往夏威夷大多是順風。"},{"en":"Downwind to a place means travelling in the same direction as the wind blows.","zh":"順風前往某地，是指沿着風所吹的方向前進。"},{"en":"Sailing downwind to an island is usually easier than sailing against the wind.","zh":"順風前往一座島通常比逆風航行更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a favourable sailing direction.","zh":"這個短語描述有利的航行方向。"},{"en":"It links geography with wind patterns.","zh":"它把地理與風向模式連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"lie in the opposite direction","meaning":"位於相反方向","examples":[{"en":"Easter Island lies in the opposite direction.","zh":"復活節島位於相反方向。"},{"en":"To lie in the opposite direction means to be located the other way from a reference point or route.","zh":"位於相反方向，是指位於相對於參照點或路線的另一方向。"},{"en":"Hawaii lies downwind, but Easter Island lies in the opposite direction.","zh":"夏威夷在順風方向，但復活節島位於相反方向。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare possible routes.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較可能路線。"},{"en":"It describes geographical orientation.","zh":"它描述地理方位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"upwind","meaning":"逆風方向","examples":[{"en":"Easter Island is normally upwind.","zh":"復活節島通常位於逆風方向。"},{"en":"Upwind means in the direction from which the wind is blowing.","zh":"逆風方向，是指風從那個方向吹來。"},{"en":"Sailing upwind is harder because the wind comes from ahead.","zh":"逆風航行較難，因為風從前方吹來。"},{"en":"A destination upwind may require tacking or unusual wind conditions.","zh":"位於逆風方向的目的地可能需要迎風斜駛或異常風況。"},{"en":"This word describes a difficult sailing direction.","zh":"這個詞描述困難的航行方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"period of frequent activity","meaning":"活動頻繁的時期","examples":[{"en":"The voyage occurred during a period of frequent El Niño activity.","zh":"這次航行發生在厄爾尼諾活動頻繁的時期。"},{"en":"A period of frequent activity is a time when something happens often.","zh":"活動頻繁的時期，是某事經常發生的時間。"},{"en":"The sailors travelled during a period of frequent climate disruption.","zh":"航海者在氣候擾動頻繁的時期旅行。"},{"en":"This phrase connects timing with repeated events.","zh":"這個短語把時間與反覆事件連接起來。"},{"en":"It helps explain why unusual voyages may have occurred.","zh":"它有助解釋為何不尋常航行可能發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"complete the summary with","meaning":"用……完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the summary with the list of words.","zh":"考生用詞語列表完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary with words means to fill gaps using the given options.","zh":"用字詞完成摘要，是指使用提供的選項填補空格。"},{"en":"Students complete the summary with words that match the passage.","zh":"學生用符合篇章的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"},{"en":"It tests understanding of main ideas and details.","zh":"它測試對主旨和細節的理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"question arising from","meaning":"由……引起的問題","examples":[{"en":"The question arising from Cook’s expedition fascinated researchers.","zh":"由 Cook 遠征引起的問題令研究人員着迷。"},{"en":"A question arising from something is a question caused or suggested by it.","zh":"由某事引起的問題，是由該事造成或引出的問題。"},{"en":"A question arising from the discovery was where the people came from.","zh":"由這項發現引起的問題是這些人來自哪裡。"},{"en":"This phrase links an observation with later research.","zh":"這個短語把觀察與後來研究連接起來。"},{"en":"It is common in academic discussion.","zh":"它常見於學術討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be derived from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"Several other questions were derived from Cook’s original question.","zh":"其他幾個問題源自 Cook 最初的問題。"},{"en":"To be derived from something means to come from it as a source.","zh":"源自某事，是指以它為來源而來。"},{"en":"Later research topics were derived from the first mystery.","zh":"後來的研究題目源自最初謎團。"},{"en":"This phrase shows intellectual origin.","zh":"這個短語顯示思想來源。"},{"en":"It is common in formal writing.","zh":"它常見於正式寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"fascinate researchers","meaning":"令研究人員着迷","examples":[{"en":"The question has fascinated researchers for a long time.","zh":"這個問題長久以來令研究人員着迷。"},{"en":"To fascinate researchers means to attract their deep interest and curiosity.","zh":"令研究人員着迷，是指吸引他們深厚興趣和好奇心。"},{"en":"The spread of Pacific culture fascinated researchers because it was hard to explain.","zh":"太平洋文化的傳播令研究人員着迷，因為它難以解釋。"},{"en":"Fascinating questions often drive long-term investigation.","zh":"令人着迷的問題常推動長期研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong academic interest.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈學術興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"valuable information about","meaning":"關於……的寶貴資料","examples":[{"en":"The find provided valuable information about early seafarers.","zh":"這項發現提供關於早期航海者的寶貴資料。"},{"en":"Valuable information about something is useful knowledge that helps understanding.","zh":"關於某事的寶貴資料，是有助理解的有用知識。"},{"en":"DNA can provide valuable information about migration history.","zh":"DNA 可以提供關於遷徙歷史的寶貴資料。"},{"en":"Such information matters when other evidence is scarce.","zh":"當其他證據稀少，這類資料很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights usefulness of evidence.","zh":"這個短語突出證據的有用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"excavation site","meaning":"發掘現場","examples":[{"en":"Researchers studied the excavation site on Éfaté.","zh":"研究人員研究 Éfaté 島上的發掘現場。"},{"en":"An excavation site is a place where archaeologists are digging and studying remains.","zh":"發掘現場是考古學家正在挖掘和研究遺存的地方。"},{"en":"The excavation site contained graves, pottery and bones.","zh":"該發掘現場包含墳墓、陶器和骨骸。"},{"en":"Site records help researchers preserve context.","zh":"現場記錄幫助研究人員保存背景資料。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an active archaeological location.","zh":"這個短語指正在進行考古工作的地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"be uncovered","meaning":"被發現；被挖出","examples":[{"en":"A grave containing Lapita bones was uncovered.","zh":"一座藏有拉皮塔人骨骸的墳墓被發現。"},{"en":"To be uncovered means to be found or exposed after being hidden.","zh":"被發現或被挖出，是指在被隱藏後被找到或暴露。"},{"en":"Pottery fragments were uncovered beneath the topsoil.","zh":"陶器碎片在表土下被挖出。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in archaeology and investigation.","zh":"這個短語常見於考古和調查。"},{"en":"It suggests discovery after concealment.","zh":"它暗示隱藏後被發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"various studies","meaning":"各種研究","examples":[{"en":"Various studies were conducted on the Lapita remains.","zh":"對拉皮塔遺骸進行了各種研究。"},{"en":"Various studies means several different types of research.","zh":"各種研究，是指幾種不同類型的研究。"},{"en":"Various studies included isotope tests, DNA analysis and archaeological comparison.","zh":"各種研究包括同位素測試、DNA 分析和考古比較。"},{"en":"Using various studies gives a fuller picture.","zh":"使用多種研究方法能提供更完整圖像。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses multiple methods.","zh":"這個短語強調多種方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"conduct studies","meaning":"進行研究","examples":[{"en":"Researchers conducted studies to investigate the ancient Lapita.","zh":"研究人員進行研究以調查古代拉皮塔人。"},{"en":"To conduct studies means to carry out research carefully and systematically.","zh":"進行研究，是指仔細而有系統地執行研究。"},{"en":"Scientists conducted studies on teeth to learn about childhood origins.","zh":"科學家對牙齒進行研究，以了解童年來源。"},{"en":"Conducting studies helps turn discoveries into evidence-based conclusions.","zh":"進行研究幫助把發現轉化為基於證據的結論。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic writing.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"investigate","meaning":"調查；研究","examples":[{"en":"The studies investigated the ancient Lapita and their descendants.","zh":"這些研究調查古代拉皮塔人及其後裔。"},{"en":"To investigate means to examine carefully in order to find out the truth.","zh":"調查或研究，是指仔細檢視以查明真相。"},{"en":"Archaeologists investigated how the cemetery was used.","zh":"考古學家研究該墓地如何被使用。"},{"en":"Investigation requires evidence, methods and careful interpretation.","zh":"調查需要證據、方法和謹慎解讀。"},{"en":"This verb is used in research and inquiry.","zh":"這個動詞用於研究和查詢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"spread so far across","meaning":"如此廣泛地擴散至……","examples":[{"en":"Researchers asked how the Lapita spread so far across the ocean.","zh":"研究人員問拉皮塔人如何如此廣泛地擴散至海洋各處。"},{"en":"To spread so far across an area means to expand over a very large distance within it.","zh":"如此廣泛地擴散至某範圍，是指在其中擴展到非常遙遠距離。"},{"en":"The culture spread so far across the Pacific that similar pottery appeared on many islands.","zh":"這種文化如此廣泛地擴散至太平洋，以致許多島嶼都有相似陶器。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises surprising reach.","zh":"這個短語強調令人意外的範圍。"},{"en":"It is often used when distance is hard to explain.","zh":"當距離難以解釋時，它常被使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"all that is certain is that","meaning":"唯一肯定的是","examples":[{"en":"All that is certain is that they were skilled canoeists.","zh":"唯一肯定的是，他們是熟練的獨木舟航行者。"},{"en":"All that is certain is that means the only definite conclusion is this.","zh":"唯一肯定的是，表示唯一確定的結論是這一點。"},{"en":"All that is certain is that the sailors crossed open water.","zh":"唯一肯定的是，航海者橫越了開放水域。"},{"en":"This phrase limits claims to what evidence supports.","zh":"這個短語把說法限制在證據支持的範圍內。"},{"en":"It is useful when many details remain unknown.","zh":"當許多細節仍未知時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"skilled canoeists","meaning":"熟練的獨木舟航行者","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita were skilled canoeists.","zh":"拉皮塔人是熟練的獨木舟航行者。"},{"en":"Skilled canoeists are people highly capable of travelling and navigating by canoe.","zh":"熟練的獨木舟航行者，是非常擅長乘獨木舟航行和導航的人。"},{"en":"Skilled canoeists can control boats in waves and changing winds.","zh":"熟練獨木舟航行者能在海浪和變化風向中控制船隻。"},{"en":"Their ability helped them explore islands far from home.","zh":"他們的能力幫助他們探索遠離家園的島嶼。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on canoe-handling expertise.","zh":"這個短語聚焦獨木舟操控專長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"take full advantage of","meaning":"充分利用","examples":[{"en":"The sailors may have taken full advantage of the trade winds.","zh":"航海者可能充分利用信風。"},{"en":"To take full advantage of something means to use it as effectively as possible.","zh":"充分利用某物，是指盡可能有效地使用它。"},{"en":"Ancient sailors took full advantage of favourable winds to travel farther.","zh":"古代航海者充分利用有利風向，航行得更遠。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests skillful use of an opportunity.","zh":"這個短語暗示熟練地利用機會。"},{"en":"It is stronger than simply use.","zh":"它比 simply use 更強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"chemical tests indicate that","meaning":"化學測試顯示","examples":[{"en":"Chemical tests indicate that some Lapita came from elsewhere.","zh":"化學測試顯示，有些拉皮塔人來自其他地方。"},{"en":"Chemical tests indicate that means laboratory results suggest a conclusion.","zh":"化學測試顯示，是指實驗室結果暗示某結論。"},{"en":"Chemical tests indicate that the person did not grow up on the island.","zh":"化學測試顯示，該人並非在島上長大。"},{"en":"This phrase presents scientific evidence cautiously.","zh":"這個短語謹慎呈現科學證據。"},{"en":"It does not always mean absolute proof.","zh":"它不一定代表絕對證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"vary from childhood to adulthood","meaning":"從童年到成年有所變化","examples":[{"en":"The option discusses whether elements vary from childhood to adulthood.","zh":"該選項討論元素是否從童年到成年有所變化。"},{"en":"To vary from childhood to adulthood means to change between early life and adult life.","zh":"從童年到成年有所變化，是指在早年生活和成年生活之間改變。"},{"en":"Diet may vary from childhood to adulthood if a person moves islands.","zh":"如果一個人搬到另一個島，飲食可能從童年到成年有所變化。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts two life stages.","zh":"這個短語對比兩個人生階段。"},{"en":"It is useful in questions about biological evidence.","zh":"它適合用於關於生物證據的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"remain the same","meaning":"保持不變","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether isotope signatures remain the same in different places.","zh":"該選項問同位素特徵在不同地方是否保持不變。"},{"en":"To remain the same means not to change.","zh":"保持不變，是指沒有改變。"},{"en":"Isotope signatures do not remain the same everywhere.","zh":"同位素特徵並非在各處都保持不變。"},{"en":"If they remained the same, they could not help identify origins.","zh":"如果它們保持不變，就不能幫助識別來源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lack of change.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"conceal one’s origin","meaning":"隱藏某人的出身地","examples":[{"en":"Chemical signatures cannot fully conceal one’s origin.","zh":"化學特徵不能完全隱藏某人的出身地。"},{"en":"To conceal one’s origin means to hide where someone came from.","zh":"隱藏某人的出身地，是指掩蓋某人來自哪裡。"},{"en":"Teeth may reveal origins that a person’s burial place conceals.","zh":"牙齒可能揭示被埋葬地點隱藏的來源。"},{"en":"Chemical evidence can make hidden movement visible.","zh":"化學證據可以令隱藏的移動變得可見。"},{"en":"This phrase links identity with hidden background.","zh":"這個短語把身份與隱藏背景連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"exactly locate","meaning":"精確定位","examples":[{"en":"Isotope analysis cannot exactly locate their birth island.","zh":"同位素分析不能精確定位他們的出生島嶼。"},{"en":"To exactly locate something means to identify its precise position or place.","zh":"精確定位某物，是指識別其準確位置或地點。"},{"en":"The data can suggest a region but cannot exactly locate the village.","zh":"數據可以暗示一個地區，但不能精確定位村落。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses precision.","zh":"這個短語強調準確性。"},{"en":"It is often used when evidence has limits.","zh":"它常用於證據有限的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"birth island","meaning":"出生島嶼","examples":[{"en":"The analysis cannot identify a person’s exact birth island.","zh":"分析不能識別一個人的確切出生島嶼。"},{"en":"Birth island means the island where a person was born.","zh":"出生島嶼是指一個人出生的島。"},{"en":"A sailor’s burial island may differ from his birth island.","zh":"水手的埋葬島嶼可能不同於他的出生島嶼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in migration studies.","zh":"這個短語適合用於遷徙研究。"},{"en":"It connects personal origin with geography.","zh":"它把個人來源與地理連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"crossing stretches of sea","meaning":"橫越一片片海域","examples":[{"en":"The Lapita reached new places by crossing stretches of sea.","zh":"拉皮塔人透過橫越一片片海域抵達新地方。"},{"en":"Crossing stretches of sea means travelling across sections of ocean between land areas.","zh":"橫越一片片海域，是指橫越陸地之間的海洋區段。"},{"en":"The sailors crossed stretches of sea from one island group to another.","zh":"航海者從一個島群到另一個島群，橫越一片片海域。"},{"en":"This phrase breaks a long journey into parts.","zh":"這個短語把長途旅程分成部分。"},{"en":"It describes repeated sea crossings.","zh":"它描述反覆海上橫渡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"find answers about","meaning":"找到關於……的答案","examples":[{"en":"DNA may help researchers find answers about the islanders.","zh":"DNA 可能幫助研究人員找到關於島民的答案。"},{"en":"To find answers about something means to discover explanations or information concerning it.","zh":"找到關於某事的答案，是指發現有關它的解釋或資訊。"},{"en":"Archaeologists hope to find answers about ancient migration routes.","zh":"考古學家希望找到關於古代遷徙路線的答案。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses the goal of research.","zh":"這個短語表達研究目標。"},{"en":"It is common in science and history writing.","zh":"它常見於科學和歷史寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"leave more questions for","meaning":"留下更多問題給……","examples":[{"en":"The discovery may leave more questions for anthropologists to answer.","zh":"這項發現可能留下更多問題給人類學家解答。"},{"en":"To leave more questions for someone means to create further uncertainties they must investigate.","zh":"留下更多問題給某人，是指造成更多他們必須研究的不確定。"},{"en":"The DNA result answered one issue but left more questions for researchers.","zh":"DNA 結果回答了一個問題，但留下更多問題給研究人員。"},{"en":"Discoveries often solve one mystery while creating another.","zh":"發現常解決一個謎團，同時產生另一個。"},{"en":"This phrase shows research is unfinished.","zh":"這個短語顯示研究尚未完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"ancestors of","meaning":"……的祖先","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the ancestors of the Lapita.","zh":"題目問有關拉皮塔人的祖先。"},{"en":"Ancestors of a group are the earlier people from whom they descended.","zh":"某群體的祖先，是他們所源自的較早人群。"},{"en":"Researchers debated the ancestors of the Pacific islanders.","zh":"研究人員討論太平洋島民的祖先。"},{"en":"This phrase concerns origin and descent.","zh":"這個短語關乎起源和血脈。"},{"en":"It is common in anthropology and history.","zh":"它常見於人類學和歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"accessible to view","meaning":"看得見的","examples":[{"en":"Some islands were accessible to view from nearby land.","zh":"有些島嶼可從附近陸地看見。"},{"en":"Accessible to view means able to be seen from a particular place.","zh":"看得見的，是指能從某個地方被看見。"},{"en":"An island within sight of shore is accessible to view.","zh":"在岸邊視線範圍內的島嶼是看得見的。"},{"en":"Visible islands made early navigation easier.","zh":"可見島嶼令早期導航較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what can be seen.","zh":"這個短語聚焦可見性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"fully explore","meaning":"充分探索","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether sailors fully explored the horizons.","zh":"該選項問航海者是否充分探索地平線。"},{"en":"To fully explore something means to examine it as completely as possible.","zh":"充分探索某事，是指盡可能完整地檢視它。"},{"en":"The sailors could not fully explore every horizon because supplies were limited.","zh":"航海者無法充分探索每個地平線，因為物資有限。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests thorough investigation.","zh":"這個短語暗示徹底調查。"},{"en":"It is stronger than simply look at.","zh":"它比 simply look at 更強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"once out exploring the sea","meaning":"一旦出海探索","examples":[{"en":"Once out exploring the sea, sailors followed clues to land.","zh":"一旦出海探索，航海者便跟隨通往陸地的線索。"},{"en":"Once out exploring the sea means after sailors had left land and begun searching at sea.","zh":"一旦出海探索，是指航海者離開陸地並開始在海上尋找之後。"},{"en":"Once out exploring the sea, they watched birds and clouds carefully.","zh":"一旦出海探索，他們便仔細觀察鳥和雲。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the stage after departure.","zh":"這個短語標示出發後的階段。"},{"en":"It connects exploration with observation.","zh":"它把探索與觀察連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"unsuitable for sailing","meaning":"不適合航行","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether the winds were unsuitable for sailing.","zh":"該選項問風是否不適合航行。"},{"en":"Unsuitable for sailing means not favourable or safe for moving a boat.","zh":"不適合航行，是指不利於或不安全地移動船隻。"},{"en":"Strong headwinds may be unsuitable for sailing eastward.","zh":"強烈逆風可能不適合向東航行。"},{"en":"Whether winds are suitable depends on direction and boat design.","zh":"風是否合適取決於方向和船隻設計。"},{"en":"This phrase describes poor sailing conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述不良航行條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"overshoot one’s home port","meaning":"駛過自己的母港","examples":[{"en":"A sailor might overshoot his home port in poor conditions.","zh":"在惡劣情況下，水手可能駛過自己的母港。"},{"en":"To overshoot one’s home port means to sail past it by mistake.","zh":"駛過自己的母港，是指錯誤地航行越過它。"},{"en":"Bad weather could make a canoe overshoot its home island.","zh":"惡劣天氣可能令獨木舟駛過自己的家島。"},{"en":"Overshooting is dangerous because the sailor may lose the safe return point.","zh":"駛過目的地很危險，因為水手可能失去安全返回點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes going too far beyond a destination.","zh":"這個短語描述越過目的地太遠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"sail off into eternity","meaning":"永遠駛離；一去不返","examples":[{"en":"The option imagines sailors sailing off into eternity.","zh":"該選項想像航海者永遠駛離。"},{"en":"To sail off into eternity means to disappear forever at sea.","zh":"永遠駛離，是指在海上一去不返、永遠消失。"},{"en":"Without return winds, sailors might have feared sailing off into eternity.","zh":"沒有回程風，航海者可能害怕一去不返。"},{"en":"This phrase is dramatic and not literal.","zh":"這個短語具有戲劇性，並非字面意思。"},{"en":"It suggests endless loss beyond the horizon.","zh":"它暗示在地平線外無盡迷失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"sail in one direction","meaning":"朝一個方向航行","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that sailors would sail in one direction.","zh":"該選項指出航海者會朝一個方向航行。"},{"en":"To sail in one direction means to continue moving the same way without turning.","zh":"朝一個方向航行，是指一直朝同一方向移動而不轉向。"},{"en":"The sailors did not simply sail in one direction forever; they could turn back.","zh":"航海者並非只是永遠朝一個方向航行；他們可以掉頭。"},{"en":"Directional control mattered for exploration and return.","zh":"方向控制對探索和回程很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes steady movement along one course.","zh":"這個短語描述沿同一路線穩定移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所提供資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether statements agree with the information given.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與所提供資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"與所提供資料一致，是指符合篇章所說內容。"},{"en":"A statement agrees with the passage only if the text clearly supports it.","zh":"只有文本清楚支持某陳述，它才與篇章一致。"},{"en":"Students should avoid using outside knowledge for this task.","zh":"學生應避免在這類題目使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the information in the passage.","zh":"陳述可能與篇章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"與資料相矛盾，是指說出與文本內容相反的東西。"},{"en":"If the passage says the reason is unknown, giving a definite reason contradicts the information.","zh":"如果篇章說原因未知，給出確定原因就是與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for FALSE answers.","zh":"這個短語用於 FALSE 答案。"},{"en":"It requires clear conflict with the text.","zh":"它需要與文本有清楚衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果沒有這方面的資料，考生寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not provide enough evidence to decide.","zh":"沒有這方面的資料，是指篇章沒有提供足夠證據作判斷。"},{"en":"If the text never mentions a detail, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文本從未提到某細節，就沒有這方面的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not infer too much from silence.","zh":"學生不應從沉默中過度推論。"},{"en":"This phrase corresponds to NOT GIVEN.","zh":"這個短語對應 NOT GIVEN。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"canoe in the prevailing wind","meaning":"在盛行風中划獨木舟","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether the Lapita could canoe in the prevailing wind.","zh":"該陳述問拉皮塔人能否在盛行風中划獨木舟。"},{"en":"To canoe in the prevailing wind means to travel by canoe under the usual wind conditions.","zh":"在盛行風中划獨木舟，是指在通常風況下乘獨木舟航行。"},{"en":"The Lapita may have used prevailing winds to return home.","zh":"拉皮塔人可能利用盛行風回家。"},{"en":"This phrase connects canoe travel with normal wind direction.","zh":"這個短語把獨木舟航行與正常風向連接起來。"},{"en":"It is used in a reading-question context.","zh":"它用於閱讀題語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"find one’s way back","meaning":"找路回去","examples":[{"en":"The trade winds may have helped sailors find their way back.","zh":"信風可能幫助航海者找路回去。"},{"en":"To find one’s way back means to return successfully to the starting place.","zh":"找路回去，是指成功返回起點。"},{"en":"Sailors used wind and stars to find their way back to home islands.","zh":"航海者利用風和星星找路回到家島。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on navigation and return.","zh":"這個短語聚焦導航和回程。"},{"en":"It is important in exploration because leaving is only half the challenge.","zh":"它在探索中很重要，因為離開只是一半挑戰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"stop sailing farther","meaning":"停止繼續遠航","examples":[{"en":"The reason why the Lapita stopped sailing farther is still unknown.","zh":"拉皮塔人停止繼續遠航的原因仍然未知。"},{"en":"To stop sailing farther means to choose or cease to continue travelling beyond a point.","zh":"停止繼續遠航，是指選擇不再或停止越過某點繼續航行。"},{"en":"The settlers may have stopped sailing farther because they found enough islands.","zh":"定居者可能因找到足夠島嶼而停止繼續遠航。"},{"en":"The exact reason remains uncertain.","zh":"確切原因仍不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the end of expansion.","zh":"這個短語描述擴張的終止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"the majority of","meaning":"大多數","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether the majority of the Lapita lived in Fiji.","zh":"題目問大多數拉皮塔人是否住在斐濟。"},{"en":"The majority of a group means more than half of it.","zh":"大多數某群體，是指超過一半。"},{"en":"The majority of the crew stayed on the island while a few explored.","zh":"大多數船員留在島上，少數人去探索。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for comparing numbers within a group.","zh":"這個短語用於比較群體內數量。"},{"en":"It requires evidence about proportion.","zh":"它需要比例方面的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"take advantage of El Niño","meaning":"利用厄爾尼諾現象","examples":[{"en":"Navigators may have taken advantage of El Niño during later voyages.","zh":"航海家可能在後來航行中利用厄爾尼諾現象。"},{"en":"To take advantage of El Niño means to use its unusual wind or climate effects for travel.","zh":"利用厄爾尼諾現象，是指使用其異常風向或氣候影響來旅行。"},{"en":"Sailors could take advantage of El Niño if it reversed normal trade winds.","zh":"如果厄爾尼諾逆轉正常信風，水手可以利用它。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests using a natural event as an opportunity.","zh":"這個短語暗示把自然事件作為機會。"},{"en":"It connects climate knowledge with navigation.","zh":"它把氣候知識與導航連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":26},{"front":"further voyages","meaning":"進一步航行","examples":[{"en":"El Niño may have helped navigators during their further voyages.","zh":"厄爾尼諾可能在航海者進一步航行期間幫助他們。"},{"en":"Further voyages are later or additional journeys beyond earlier ones.","zh":"進一步航行，是早期旅程之後的後續或額外航程。"},{"en":"After the first settlement, further voyages carried people to more remote islands.","zh":"首次定居後，進一步航行把人們帶到更偏遠島嶼。"},{"en":"This phrase shows continuation of exploration.","zh":"這個短語顯示探索延續。"},{"en":"It can refer to journeys made after an initial stage.","zh":"它可以指初步階段後的航程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 138 - Beyond the blue line.pdf","sourcePage":26}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 139":[{"front":"dinosaurs’ footprints and extinction","meaning":"恐龍足跡與滅絕","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines dinosaurs’ footprints and the events connected with their rise and extinction.","zh":"文章探討恐龍足跡，以及與牠們崛起和滅絕有關的事件。"},{"en":"Dinosaurs’ footprints and extinction refer to fossil tracks and the disappearance of dinosaurs from Earth.","zh":"dinosaurs’ footprints and extinction 指恐龍化石足跡，以及恐龍從地球上消失。"},{"en":"A museum lesson may use dinosaurs’ footprints and extinction to teach students how fossils reveal the past.","zh":"博物館課堂可能使用恐龍足跡與滅絕來教學生化石如何揭示過去。"},{"en":"Footprints can show where dinosaurs walked, while extinction evidence helps explain why they disappeared.","zh":"足跡可以顯示恐龍曾在哪裡行走，而滅絕證據有助解釋牠們為何消失。"},{"en":"This phrase connects physical fossil evidence with a major event in Earth’s history.","zh":"這個短語把實體化石證據與地球歷史上的重大事件連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be killed by an asteroid","meaning":"被小行星撞擊所滅絕","examples":[{"en":"The dinosaurs are widely believed to have been killed by an asteroid.","zh":"人們普遍相信恐龍是被小行星撞擊所滅絕。"},{"en":"To be killed by an asteroid means to die or become extinct because a large space rock hits Earth.","zh":"be killed by an asteroid 指因大型太空岩石撞擊地球而死亡或滅絕。"},{"en":"A science documentary may explain how animals could be killed by an asteroid impact.","zh":"科學紀錄片可能解釋動物如何被小行星撞擊所滅絕。"},{"en":"If an asteroid hits with enough force, dust, fire and climate change can kill many species.","zh":"如果小行星撞擊威力足夠大，塵埃、火災和氣候變化可以殺死許多物種。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to a catastrophic event rather than an ordinary death.","zh":"這個短語通常指災難性事件，而不是普通死亡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"when the dust had fallen","meaning":"當塵埃落定後","examples":[{"en":"When the dust had fallen, the great reptiles had also disappeared.","zh":"當塵埃落定後，巨型爬蟲類動物也已消失。"},{"en":"When the dust had fallen means after the chaos, smoke, or confusion had settled.","zh":"when the dust had fallen 指混亂、煙塵或困惑平息之後。"},{"en":"After a heated school debate, when the dust had fallen, everyone could see which plan was practical.","zh":"一場激烈校內辯論後，當塵埃落定，大家才看清哪個計劃實際可行。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the real result becomes clear only after a dramatic event is over.","zh":"這個短語暗示真正結果要到戲劇性事件結束後才變得清楚。"},{"en":"It can be literal, after actual dust settles, or figurative, after a crisis ends.","zh":"它可以是字面意思，即真正塵埃落下；也可以是比喻，指危機結束後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the great reptiles","meaning":"巨型爬蟲類動物","examples":[{"en":"The great reptiles disappeared after a catastrophic impact.","zh":"這些巨型爬蟲類動物在災難性撞擊後消失。"},{"en":"The great reptiles refers to large ancient reptiles, especially dinosaurs.","zh":"the great reptiles 指大型古代爬蟲類動物，尤其是恐龍。"},{"en":"Children often imagine the great reptiles as enormous animals walking through ancient forests.","zh":"孩子常想像巨型爬蟲類動物在古代森林中行走。"},{"en":"These reptiles disappeared when environmental conditions changed too severely for them to survive.","zh":"當環境條件變得過於嚴峻，這些爬蟲類動物便無法生存而消失。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds grand and historical, not like ordinary modern lizards.","zh":"這個短語聽起來宏大而帶歷史感，不像普通現代蜥蜴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a nice, if ironic, symmetry","meaning":"一種巧妙但帶諷刺意味的對稱","examples":[{"en":"There is a nice, if ironic, symmetry between the dinosaurs’ rise and fall.","zh":"恐龍的崛起與衰落之間有一種巧妙但帶諷刺意味的對稱。"},{"en":"A nice, if ironic, symmetry means a neat parallel that is also surprising or slightly bitter.","zh":"a nice, if ironic, symmetry 指一種整齊的相似關係，但同時令人意外或略帶苦澀。"},{"en":"It is a nice, if ironic, symmetry when a noisy student later becomes a silence-loving librarian.","zh":"如果一名吵鬧學生後來成為熱愛安靜的圖書館員，那就是一種巧妙但帶諷刺意味的對稱。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when two events match each other in an unexpected way.","zh":"當兩件事以意想不到的方式互相呼應時，可以使用這個短語。"},{"en":"In this passage, the irony is that impacts may explain both dinosaur dominance and disappearance.","zh":"在文章中，諷刺之處是撞擊可能同時解釋恐龍的主宰和消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a similar impact","meaning":"類似的撞擊","examples":[{"en":"A similar impact may have contributed to the dinosaurs’ rise.","zh":"類似的撞擊可能促成恐龍的崛起。"},{"en":"A similar impact means another event of the same kind, such as another asteroid strike.","zh":"a similar impact 指同類型的另一個事件，例如另一次小行星撞擊。"},{"en":"If one school failed after poor planning, a similar impact might happen to another school using the same plan.","zh":"如果一間學校因規劃差而失敗，另一間採用同一計劃的學校也可能受到類似影響。"},{"en":"Similar impacts can produce similar results when the conditions are alike.","zh":"當條件相似，類似影響可以產生相似結果。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one event with another that works in a related way.","zh":"這個短語把一個事件與另一個運作方式相關的事件作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"bring about","meaning":"導致；引起","examples":[{"en":"An asteroid strike may have brought about a major ecological change.","zh":"小行星撞擊可能導致重大生態變化。"},{"en":"To bring about something means to cause it to happen.","zh":"bring about something 指導致某事發生。"},{"en":"A new head teacher may bring about changes in school rules and routines.","zh":"新校長可能引起校規和常規上的改變。"},{"en":"Large events can bring about sudden change because they disturb existing systems.","zh":"大事件可以導致突然變化，因為它們擾亂現有系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining causes and results.","zh":"解釋原因和結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the dinosaurs’ rise","meaning":"恐龍的崛起","examples":[{"en":"The researchers propose a new explanation for the dinosaurs’ rise.","zh":"研究者提出一個解釋恐龍崛起的新說法。"},{"en":"The dinosaurs’ rise means the process by which dinosaurs became more successful and dominant.","zh":"the dinosaurs’ rise 指恐龍變得更成功和更具主導地位的過程。"},{"en":"A history lesson may compare the rise of dinosaurs with the rise of human civilisations.","zh":"歷史課可能把恐龍的崛起與人類文明的興起作比較。"},{"en":"Their rise may have happened when other animal groups weakened or disappeared.","zh":"當其他動物群體變弱或消失時，恐龍可能因此崛起。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing power, spread, and importance over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間增加的力量、分布和重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the thesis proposed by","meaning":"由……提出的論點","examples":[{"en":"The thesis proposed by Paul Olsen links dinosaur dominance to an asteroid strike.","zh":"Paul Olsen 提出的論點把恐龍主導地位與小行星撞擊連起來。"},{"en":"The thesis proposed by someone means the main argument or explanation that person puts forward.","zh":"thesis proposed by someone 指某人提出的主要論點或解釋。"},{"en":"The thesis proposed by a student in an essay should be clear in the introduction.","zh":"學生在文章中提出的論點應在引言中清楚表明。"},{"en":"A strong thesis helps readers understand what evidence will be used to support it.","zh":"有力論點幫助讀者理解將用甚麼證據支持它。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic writing and research discussion.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術寫作和研究討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fossil record","meaning":"化石記錄","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs first appeared in the fossil record about 230 million years ago.","zh":"恐龍最早在約二億三千萬年前出現在化石記錄中。"},{"en":"The fossil record is the evidence of past life preserved in rocks.","zh":"fossil record 指保存在岩石中的古代生命證據。"},{"en":"Museums use the fossil record to show how animals and plants changed over time.","zh":"博物館使用化石記錄來展示動植物如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"If a species appears in the fossil record, scientists know it existed in the past.","zh":"如果一個物種出現在化石記錄中，科學家便知道它過去曾存在。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to preserved evidence, not a written human record.","zh":"這個短語指保存下來的證據，而不是人類書寫記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the Triassic period","meaning":"三疊紀","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs first appeared during the Triassic period.","zh":"恐龍最早出現在三疊紀。"},{"en":"The Triassic period is a geological period before the Jurassic, when early dinosaurs appeared.","zh":"Triassic period 指侏羅紀之前的一個地質時期，早期恐龍在此時出現。"},{"en":"A science textbook may place the Triassic period on a timeline of Earth history.","zh":"科學教科書可能把三疊紀放在地球歷史時間線上。"},{"en":"Studying this period helps explain what animals lived before dinosaurs became dominant.","zh":"研究這個時期有助解釋恐龍成為主宰前有哪些動物生活。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific ancient time period.","zh":"這個短語指一個特定古代時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"share the Earth with","meaning":"與……共同生活在地球上","examples":[{"en":"Early dinosaurs shared the Earth with many other reptiles.","zh":"早期恐龍與許多其他爬蟲類動物共同生活在地球上。"},{"en":"To share the Earth with other animals means to live on the planet at the same time as them.","zh":"share the Earth with other animals 指與其他動物在同一時期生活於地球上。"},{"en":"Humans share the Earth with birds, insects, fish and countless other species.","zh":"人類與鳥類、昆蟲、魚類和無數其他物種共同生活在地球上。"},{"en":"Species that share an environment may compete for food, space and safety.","zh":"共同生活於同一環境的物種可能競爭食物、空間和安全。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses coexistence rather than dominance.","zh":"這個短語強調共存，而不是支配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"other sorts of reptile","meaning":"其他種類的爬蟲類動物","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs initially lived alongside many other sorts of reptile.","zh":"恐龍最初與許多其他種類的爬蟲類動物一起生活。"},{"en":"Other sorts of reptile means other kinds of cold-blooded vertebrate animals, such as ancient crocodile-like creatures.","zh":"other sorts of reptile 指其他種類的冷血脊椎動物，例如古代類鱷動物。"},{"en":"A zoo may display different sorts of reptile, including snakes, turtles and lizards.","zh":"動物園可能展示不同種類的爬蟲類動物，包括蛇、龜和蜥蜴。"},{"en":"Comparing different reptiles helps students see that dinosaurs were only one group among many.","zh":"比較不同爬蟲類動物有助學生看見恐龍只是眾多群體之一。"},{"en":"This phrase means other reptile types, not other dinosaurs only.","zh":"這個短語指其他爬蟲類型，而不只是其他恐龍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the subsequent Jurassic","meaning":"隨後的侏羅紀","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs became dominant during the subsequent Jurassic period.","zh":"恐龍在隨後的侏羅紀成為主宰。"},{"en":"The subsequent Jurassic means the Jurassic period that came after the Triassic.","zh":"subsequent Jurassic 指三疊紀之後的侏羅紀。"},{"en":"In a history lesson, students may study one event and then the subsequent period that followed it.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生可能先研究一件事件，再研究其後的時期。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show sequence in geological time.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示地質時間的先後次序。"},{"en":"It means the later Jurassic period, not the earlier Triassic period.","zh":"它指較後的侏羅紀，而不是較早的三疊紀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"overrun the planet","meaning":"遍佈並支配地球","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs eventually overran the planet.","zh":"恐龍最終遍佈並支配地球。"},{"en":"To overrun the planet means to spread widely and become dominant across Earth.","zh":"overrun the planet 指在地球上廣泛擴散並成為主導。"},{"en":"A weed can overrun a garden if no one removes it.","zh":"如果沒有人清除，雜草可以遍佈並佔據花園。"},{"en":"A species may overrun an area when competitors disappear and food is available.","zh":"當競爭者消失且食物充足，物種可能迅速佔據一個地區。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests rapid spread and strong control.","zh":"這個短語暗示快速擴散和強勢控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"turn into the monsters depicted in","meaning":"變成……中描繪的巨獸","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs turned into the enormous creatures depicted in popular films.","zh":"恐龍變成流行電影中描繪的巨大生物。"},{"en":"To turn into the monsters depicted in something means to develop into the huge frightening creatures shown there.","zh":"turn into the monsters depicted in something 指發展成某作品中展示的巨大可怕生物。"},{"en":"A small business story can turn into the dramatic struggle depicted in a documentary.","zh":"一個小企業故事可以變成紀錄片中描繪的戲劇性掙扎。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts an earlier modest form with a later dramatic image.","zh":"這個短語把早期較普通的形式與後來戲劇化形象作對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing how something becomes like its famous representation.","zh":"描述某物如何變得像著名呈現方式時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be depicted in","meaning":"在……中被描繪","examples":[{"en":"Huge dinosaurs are depicted in the film Jurassic Park.","zh":"巨型恐龍在電影《侏羅紀公園》中被描繪。"},{"en":"To be depicted in something means to be shown or represented in a picture, film, book or story.","zh":"be depicted in something 指在圖片、電影、書或故事中被展示或呈現。"},{"en":"City life is often depicted in films as busy, fast and stressful.","zh":"城市生活常在電影中被描繪成忙碌、快速和壓力大。"},{"en":"How something is depicted can shape what people believe about it.","zh":"某物如何被描繪可以塑造人們對它的看法。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on representation, not direct reality.","zh":"這個短語集中於呈現方式，而不是直接現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"appear on screen","meaning":"出現在銀幕上","examples":[{"en":"Many dinosaurs that appeared on screen actually lived during the Cretaceous period.","zh":"許多出現在銀幕上的恐龍其實生活在白堊紀。"},{"en":"To appear on screen means to be shown in a film, television programme or video.","zh":"appear on screen 指在電影、電視節目或影片中出現。"},{"en":"A famous actor may appear on screen for only five minutes but still impress viewers.","zh":"著名演員可能只在銀幕上出現五分鐘，仍令觀眾印象深刻。"},{"en":"Creatures that appear on screen may not always match historical or scientific accuracy.","zh":"出現在銀幕上的生物未必總是符合歷史或科學準確性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to visual appearance in moving images.","zh":"這個短語指在動態影像中的視覺出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the still more recent Cretaceous period","meaning":"更為晚近的白堊紀","examples":[{"en":"Some famous dinosaurs came from the still more recent Cretaceous period.","zh":"一些著名恐龍來自更為晚近的白堊紀。"},{"en":"The still more recent Cretaceous period means the Cretaceous, which came after the Jurassic.","zh":"still more recent Cretaceous period 指在侏羅紀之後的白堊紀。"},{"en":"A timeline helps students see that the Cretaceous period was later than the Jurassic.","zh":"時間線幫助學生看見白堊紀比侏羅紀更晚。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to compare several ancient periods in order.","zh":"這個短語用於按次序比較幾個古代時期。"},{"en":"It stresses that the period is more recent, even though it is still ancient.","zh":"它強調該時期較晚近，即使它仍然非常古老。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be the first to suggest","meaning":"最先提出……","examples":[{"en":"Olsen’s team was not the first to suggest a link with an asteroid strike.","zh":"Olsen 的團隊並非最先提出與小行星撞擊有關的人。"},{"en":"To be the first to suggest something means to be the earliest person or group to propose an idea.","zh":"be the first to suggest something 指最早提出某個想法的人或群體。"},{"en":"A student may be the first to suggest using a shared calendar for group work.","zh":"學生可能最先提出用共享日曆做小組工作。"},{"en":"Being first matters because later researchers may build on the original idea.","zh":"最先提出很重要，因為後來研究者可能在原想法上發展。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the earliest proposal, not necessarily the final proof.","zh":"這個短語指出最早建議，而不一定是最終證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"inherit the Earth","meaning":"成為地球的主宰","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs may have inherited the Earth after competing reptiles disappeared.","zh":"競爭性的爬蟲類動物消失後，恐龍可能成為地球的主宰。"},{"en":"To inherit the Earth means to become the main group living on and dominating the planet.","zh":"inherit the Earth 指成為地球上主要生活並支配的群體。"},{"en":"In a classroom, a quiet group may inherit responsibility after louder students leave the project.","zh":"在課室中，較安靜的小組可能在吵鬧學生退出專題後接手責任。"},{"en":"A species can inherit an environment when its competitors are removed.","zh":"當競爭者被移除，一個物種可以接管某環境。"},{"en":"This phrase is figurative and suggests taking over after others decline.","zh":"這個短語是比喻用法，暗示在其他群體衰落後接管。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as the result of","meaning":"由於……；作為……的結果","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs may have become dominant as the result of an asteroid strike.","zh":"恐龍可能由於小行星撞擊而成為主宰。"},{"en":"As the result of means because of or caused by something.","zh":"as the result of 指由於某事或由某事造成。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may improve as the result of regular speaking practice.","zh":"學生的信心可能由於定期口語練習而提高。"},{"en":"When one event causes a later change, we can describe the change as the result of it.","zh":"當一件事造成後來變化，我們可以說該變化是它的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly shows cause and effect.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"asteroid strike","meaning":"小行星撞擊","examples":[{"en":"An asteroid strike may have transformed the Earth’s ecosystems.","zh":"小行星撞擊可能改變了地球的生態系統。"},{"en":"An asteroid strike is an event in which a large space rock hits a planet or moon.","zh":"asteroid strike 指大型太空岩石撞擊行星或月球的事件。"},{"en":"A science teacher may use a video to show how an asteroid strike creates a crater.","zh":"科學老師可能用影片展示小行星撞擊如何形成隕石坑。"},{"en":"A powerful strike can change climate, destroy habitats and trigger extinctions.","zh":"強烈撞擊可以改變氣候、摧毀棲息地並引發滅絕。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sudden impact from space.","zh":"這個短語描述來自太空的突然撞擊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"show that","meaning":"證明","examples":[{"en":"The researchers were the first to show that the takeover happened rapidly.","zh":"研究者是最先證明接管過程迅速發生的人。"},{"en":"To show that means to provide evidence proving or strongly suggesting something.","zh":"show that 指提供證據證明或強烈顯示某事。"},{"en":"Exam results may show that students need more reading practice.","zh":"考試結果可能證明學生需要更多閱讀練習。"},{"en":"Evidence shows a point when it makes the explanation more convincing.","zh":"當證據令解釋更具說服力，它就能證明某一點。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what evidence demonstrates.","zh":"這個短語引出證據所證明的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the takeover","meaning":"取得主導地位","examples":[{"en":"The dinosaurs’ takeover of the planet happened extremely quickly.","zh":"恐龍取得地球主導地位的過程發生得極快。"},{"en":"The takeover means the process of gaining control or becoming dominant.","zh":"takeover 指取得控制權或成為主導的過程。"},{"en":"A new manager’s takeover of a team may change routines within a week.","zh":"新經理接管團隊後，可能在一星期內改變常規。"},{"en":"In nature, a takeover can happen when one group expands after rivals disappear.","zh":"在自然界中，當競爭者消失，一個群體擴張時，就可能出現接管。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a shift in power or control.","zh":"這個短語暗示權力或控制地位的轉移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in a geological eyeblink","meaning":"在地質時間上的一瞬間","examples":[{"en":"The takeover occurred in a geological eyeblink.","zh":"這次接管在地質時間上的一瞬間發生。"},{"en":"In a geological eyeblink means extremely quickly when measured against Earth’s long history.","zh":"in a geological eyeblink 指按地球漫長歷史來看極快發生。"},{"en":"A mountain forming over a few million years may still be fast in a geological eyeblink.","zh":"一座山在幾百萬年間形成，從地質角度看仍可能像一瞬間。"},{"en":"The phrase helps readers understand speed on a geological timescale.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者理解地質時間尺度上的速度。"},{"en":"It does not mean literally one blink; it means very short compared with deep time.","zh":"它不是指字面眨眼，而是指與深時相比非常短。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"dinosaur skeletons","meaning":"恐龍骨骼化石","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaur skeletons are much rarer than footprints.","zh":"恐龍骨骼化石比足跡罕見得多。"},{"en":"Dinosaur skeletons are fossilised bones from dinosaurs.","zh":"dinosaur skeletons 指恐龍留下的化石化骨骼。"},{"en":"A museum may display dinosaur skeletons to show the size and shape of ancient animals.","zh":"博物館可能展示恐龍骨骼化石，以顯示古代動物的大小和形態。"},{"en":"Skeletons are rare because bones must be buried and preserved under special conditions.","zh":"骨骼很罕見，因為骨頭必須在特殊條件下被掩埋並保存。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to body fossils, not trace fossils like footprints.","zh":"這個短語指身體化石，而不是足跡這類遺跡化石。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"surprisingly abundant","meaning":"出乎意料地豐富","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaur footprints are surprisingly abundant.","zh":"恐龍足跡出乎意料地豐富。"},{"en":"Surprisingly abundant means much more common or plentiful than people expect.","zh":"surprisingly abundant 指比人們預期更常見或更多。"},{"en":"In a small town, free study spaces may be surprisingly abundant if libraries and community centres stay open late.","zh":"在小鎮中，如果圖書館和社區中心開得很晚，免費自修空間可能出乎意料地多。"},{"en":"Something seems surprising when people expect it to be rare but find many examples.","zh":"當人們預期某物罕見卻發現很多例子，它就令人意外。"},{"en":"This phrase combines quantity with unexpectedness.","zh":"這個短語結合了數量多和出乎意料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as good an indication of...as","meaning":"與……同樣能反映……","examples":[{"en":"The prints are as good an indication of body size as the skeletons themselves.","zh":"這些足跡與骨骼本身同樣能反映體型。"},{"en":"As good an indication of A as B means equally useful for showing or estimating A.","zh":"as good an indication of A as B 指在顯示或估計 A 方面與 B 同樣有用。"},{"en":"A student’s daily homework may be as good an indication of effort as one final test.","zh":"學生每天的功課與一次期末考同樣能反映努力程度。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two types of evidence and says both can show the same thing well.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種證據，並指出兩者都能很好地顯示同一事情。"},{"en":"It is useful when defending evidence that may seem indirect.","zh":"當要維護看似間接的證據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the sizes of the beasts","meaning":"巨獸的體型","examples":[{"en":"Footprints provide evidence of the sizes of the beasts that made them.","zh":"足跡提供留下它們的巨獸體型的證據。"},{"en":"The sizes of the beasts means how large the animals were.","zh":"sizes of the beasts 指動物有多大。"},{"en":"A zoo guide may compare footprints to help children imagine the sizes of the animals.","zh":"動物園導賞員可能比較足跡，幫助孩子想像動物體型。"},{"en":"Larger footprints often suggest larger bodies, though scientists still need careful analysis.","zh":"較大的足跡通常暗示較大的身體，但科學家仍需要仔細分析。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds dramatic and refers to the body size of large animals.","zh":"這個短語語氣較戲劇化，指大型動物的身體大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"concentrate on","meaning":"集中研究……","examples":[{"en":"The researchers concentrated on footprints rather than bones.","zh":"研究者集中研究足跡，而不是骨骼。"},{"en":"To concentrate on something means to focus attention and effort on it.","zh":"concentrate on something 指把注意力和努力集中於某事。"},{"en":"A student may concentrate on grammar before improving essay style.","zh":"學生可能先集中研究文法，再改善作文風格。"},{"en":"Researchers concentrate on one type of evidence when it offers clearer or more plentiful data.","zh":"當某類證據更清楚或更豐富，研究者會集中研究它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes focused study or effort.","zh":"這個短語描述集中學習或努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the prints in question","meaning":"所討論的足跡","examples":[{"en":"The prints in question were discovered in eastern North America.","zh":"所討論的足跡是在北美洲東部發現的。"},{"en":"The prints in question means the particular footprints being discussed.","zh":"prints in question 指正在討論的特定足跡。"},{"en":"In a police report, the car in question is the specific car connected with the incident.","zh":"在警方報告中，the car in question 指與事件有關的那輛特定車。"},{"en":"This phrase helps narrow attention to the exact item under discussion.","zh":"這個短語幫助把注意力收窄到正在討論的確切事物。"},{"en":"It is formal and often used when clarifying reference.","zh":"它較正式，常用於澄清指代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"eastern North America","meaning":"北美洲東部","examples":[{"en":"The researchers examined sites across eastern North America.","zh":"研究者檢視了北美洲東部各地點。"},{"en":"Eastern North America refers to the eastern part of the North American continent.","zh":"eastern North America 指北美洲大陸的東部。"},{"en":"A travel guide may describe forests, cities and coastlines in eastern North America.","zh":"旅遊指南可能描述北美洲東部的森林、城市和海岸線。"},{"en":"In geological studies, a region matters because rocks and fossils are not evenly distributed.","zh":"在地質研究中，地區很重要，因為岩石和化石分布並不平均。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a broad geographical area.","zh":"這個短語指出一個廣闊地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be full of","meaning":"充滿……","examples":[{"en":"The region was full of ancient rift valleys.","zh":"該地區充滿古代裂谷。"},{"en":"To be full of something means to contain many examples of it.","zh":"be full of something 指包含很多某物。"},{"en":"A school noticeboard may be full of club announcements before term begins.","zh":"開學前，學校告示板可能充滿學會通知。"},{"en":"When an area is full of valleys or lakes, it gives scientists many places to study.","zh":"當一個地區充滿山谷或湖泊，科學家就有許多地方可研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes abundance in a place.","zh":"這個短語描述某地有大量某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rift valleys","meaning":"裂谷","examples":[{"en":"Ancient rift valleys contained numerous lakes.","zh":"古代裂谷包含許多湖泊。"},{"en":"Rift valleys are long low areas formed when the Earth’s crust pulls apart.","zh":"rift valleys 指地殼拉裂時形成的長形低地。"},{"en":"A geography teacher may use East Africa to explain how rift valleys form.","zh":"地理老師可能用東非例子解釋裂谷如何形成。"},{"en":"Rift valleys can hold lakes, rivers and sediments that preserve geological evidence.","zh":"裂谷可以容納湖泊、河流和沉積物，保存地質證據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a landform created by movement in the Earth’s crust.","zh":"這個短語指由地殼運動形成的地貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"similar to those in","meaning":"與……的相似","examples":[{"en":"The ancient valleys were similar to those in East Africa today.","zh":"這些古代山谷與今日東非的山谷相似。"},{"en":"Similar to those in means like the examples found in another place or group.","zh":"similar to those in 指與另一地方或群體中的例子相似。"},{"en":"The school rules are similar to those in many international schools.","zh":"這些校規與許多國際學校的校規相似。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers understand an unfamiliar thing by comparing it with a familiar example.","zh":"這個短語透過與熟悉例子比較，幫助讀者理解陌生事物。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing resemblance across places or times.","zh":"描述跨地方或跨時代的相似時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"grow and shrink","meaning":"擴大和縮小","examples":[{"en":"The lakes grew and shrank at regular intervals.","zh":"這些湖泊定期擴大和縮小。"},{"en":"To grow and shrink means to become larger and then smaller over time.","zh":"grow and shrink 指隨時間變大再變小。"},{"en":"A child’s interest in a hobby may grow and shrink during the school year.","zh":"孩子對興趣活動的熱情可能在學年中增加和減少。"},{"en":"Lakes can grow after wet periods and shrink during dry periods.","zh":"湖泊可以在潮濕時期擴大，在乾旱時期縮小。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated change in size.","zh":"這個短語描述大小上的反覆變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at regular intervals","meaning":"定期；每隔固定時間","examples":[{"en":"The lakes changed in size at regular intervals.","zh":"這些湖泊每隔固定時間改變大小。"},{"en":"At regular intervals means happening after equal or predictable periods of time.","zh":"at regular intervals 指在相等或可預測的時間間隔後發生。"},{"en":"A teacher may give short quizzes at regular intervals to check progress.","zh":"老師可能定期進行小測，以檢查進展。"},{"en":"Regular intervals make patterns easier to measure and predict.","zh":"固定間隔令模式更容易量度和預測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated timing, not random timing.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆的時間安排，而不是隨機時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"climatic changes","meaning":"氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"Climatic changes caused the lakes to expand and contract.","zh":"氣候變化導致湖泊擴張和收縮。"},{"en":"Climatic changes are long-term changes in temperature, rainfall or weather patterns.","zh":"climatic changes 指氣溫、降雨或天氣模式的長期變化。"},{"en":"Farmers notice climatic changes when planting seasons become wetter or drier than before.","zh":"當種植季節比以前更濕或更乾，農民會注意到氣候變化。"},{"en":"Climate changes can affect lakes, crops, animals and human settlements.","zh":"氣候變化可以影響湖泊、農作物、動物和人類聚居地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad environmental change, not one day’s weather.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛環境變化，而不是某一天的天氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"periodic shifts in","meaning":"……的周期性變化","examples":[{"en":"Periodic shifts in the Earth’s orbit affected the climate.","zh":"地球軌道的周期性變化影響了氣候。"},{"en":"Periodic shifts in something are repeated changes that happen at intervals.","zh":"periodic shifts in something 指每隔一段時間反覆出現的變化。"},{"en":"Periodic shifts in school enrolment may occur when families move into a new district.","zh":"當家庭搬入新地區，學校收生可能出現周期性變化。"},{"en":"Repeated shifts can create long-term patterns that scientists can measure.","zh":"反覆變化可以形成科學家能量度的長期模式。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses regular or recurring change.","zh":"這個短語強調定期或反覆出現的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the Earth’s orbit","meaning":"地球軌道","examples":[{"en":"Changes in the Earth’s orbit can influence long-term climate patterns.","zh":"地球軌道的變化可以影響長期氣候模式。"},{"en":"The Earth’s orbit is the path Earth follows as it moves around the Sun.","zh":"Earth’s orbit 指地球繞太陽運行的路徑。"},{"en":"A science teacher may use a diagram to show the Earth’s orbit and seasons.","zh":"科學老師可能用圖表展示地球軌道和季節。"},{"en":"Small orbital changes can affect how much sunlight reaches different parts of the planet.","zh":"微小軌道變化可以影響到達地球不同地區的陽光量。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to astronomy and climate science.","zh":"這個短語屬於天文學和氣候科學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be responsible for","meaning":"是造成……的原因","examples":[{"en":"A similar astronomical phenomenon is responsible for modern ice ages.","zh":"類似的天文現象是造成現代冰河時期的原因。"},{"en":"To be responsible for something means to be the cause of it.","zh":"be responsible for something 指是造成某事的原因。"},{"en":"Poor sleep may be responsible for a student’s lack of concentration.","zh":"睡眠不足可能是造成學生缺乏專注力的原因。"},{"en":"Identifying what is responsible for a problem helps people choose the right solution.","zh":"找出造成問題的原因，有助人選擇正確解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase explains cause, not moral blame only.","zh":"這個短語解釋原因，不只是道德責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"modern ice ages","meaning":"現代冰河時期","examples":[{"en":"Orbital changes are associated with modern ice ages.","zh":"軌道變化與現代冰河時期有關。"},{"en":"Modern ice ages are recent geological periods when large ice sheets expanded over parts of Earth.","zh":"modern ice ages 指較近期的地質寒冷時期，當時大型冰蓋擴展到地球部分地區。"},{"en":"Students may learn about modern ice ages when studying climate change over thousands of years.","zh":"學生研究數千年氣候變化時，可能學到現代冰河時期。"},{"en":"Ice ages can reshape landscapes by moving glaciers across land.","zh":"冰河時期可以透過冰川在陸地上移動而重塑地貌。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to cold geological periods, not a single snowy winter.","zh":"這個短語指寒冷地質時期，而不是一次下雪的冬天。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"combined with","meaning":"結合……","examples":[{"en":"Orbital regularity, combined with magnetic evidence, allows precise dating.","zh":"軌道規律結合磁性證據，可以讓年代測定更精確。"},{"en":"Combined with means used together with another thing.","zh":"combined with 指與另一事物一起使用。"},{"en":"Regular revision, combined with feedback, helps students improve writing faster.","zh":"定期溫習結合回饋，可以幫助學生更快改善寫作。"},{"en":"Two types of evidence can be stronger together than either one alone.","zh":"兩類證據結合起來可能比單獨使用任何一類更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor supports or strengthens another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個因素支持或加強另一個因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"reversals in the Earth’s magnetic field","meaning":"地球磁場逆轉","examples":[{"en":"Scientists can detect reversals in the Earth’s magnetic field in ancient rocks.","zh":"科學家可以在古代岩石中探測到地球磁場逆轉。"},{"en":"Reversals in the Earth’s magnetic field are changes in which magnetic north and south switch places.","zh":"reversals in the Earth’s magnetic field 指磁北和磁南互換位置的變化。"},{"en":"A geography lesson may use magnetic reversals to explain how rocks can be dated.","zh":"地理課可能用磁場逆轉來解釋岩石如何被定年。"},{"en":"These reversals leave evidence in minerals as rocks form.","zh":"這些逆轉會在岩石形成時把證據留在礦物中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major change in Earth’s magnetism.","zh":"這個短語描述地球磁性上的重大變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be detectable in","meaning":"可在……中探測到","examples":[{"en":"Magnetic-field reversals are detectable in tiny mineral grains.","zh":"磁場逆轉可在微小礦物顆粒中探測到。"},{"en":"To be detectable in something means to be able to be found or measured there.","zh":"be detectable in something 指能在某物中被發現或量度。"},{"en":"A small amount of sugar may be detectable in a drink even if it does not taste very sweet.","zh":"即使飲品味道不太甜，少量糖分也可能在其中被探測到。"},{"en":"Detectable evidence helps scientists identify changes that cannot be seen directly.","zh":"可探測證據幫助科學家識別不能直接看見的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether something can be found by testing.","zh":"這個短語集中於某物是否可透過測試被發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"tiny grains of","meaning":"微小顆粒的……","examples":[{"en":"The evidence is preserved in tiny grains of magnetic minerals.","zh":"證據保存在微小顆粒的磁性礦物中。"},{"en":"Tiny grains of something are very small particles of that material.","zh":"tiny grains of something 指某種物質的非常細小顆粒。"},{"en":"Tiny grains of sand can get inside shoes after a beach trip.","zh":"沙灘旅行後，微小沙粒可能進入鞋內。"},{"en":"Small grains can preserve important evidence because they form and settle within rocks.","zh":"小顆粒可以保存重要證據，因為它們在岩石中形成和沉積。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very small pieces of a substance.","zh":"這個短語描述某物質的非常細小部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"magnetic minerals","meaning":"磁性礦物","examples":[{"en":"Certain magnetic minerals preserve evidence of past magnetic changes.","zh":"某些磁性礦物保存了過去磁場變化的證據。"},{"en":"Magnetic minerals are minerals that respond to or record magnetism.","zh":"magnetic minerals 指會對磁力作出反應或記錄磁性的礦物。"},{"en":"Scientists study magnetic minerals in rocks to understand ancient Earth conditions.","zh":"科學家研究岩石中的磁性礦物，以了解古代地球條件。"},{"en":"These minerals can lock in the direction of Earth’s magnetic field when they form.","zh":"這些礦物形成時可以鎖定地球磁場方向。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to natural materials useful in geological dating.","zh":"這個短語指對地質定年有用的天然材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be dated to within","meaning":"可把年代確定至誤差不超過……","examples":[{"en":"The rocks can be dated to within a few thousand years.","zh":"這些岩石的年代可確定至誤差不超過數千年。"},{"en":"To be dated to within a period means to have an estimated age with that margin of error.","zh":"be dated to within a period 指估計年代的誤差範圍不超過該時間。"},{"en":"An old document may be dated to within ten years if its paper and ink are tested.","zh":"如果測試紙張和墨水，舊文件年代可能可確定至誤差不超過十年。"},{"en":"More precise dating helps scientists compare events in the correct order.","zh":"更精確的定年幫助科學家按正確次序比較事件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how accurate an age estimate is.","zh":"這個短語描述年代估計有多準確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as a bonus","meaning":"額外的好處是","examples":[{"en":"As a bonus, the lake-edge sediments preserved animal tracks.","zh":"額外的好處是，湖邊沉積物保存了動物足跡。"},{"en":"As a bonus means as an extra advantage in addition to the main benefit.","zh":"as a bonus 指作為主要好處以外的額外優點。"},{"en":"A library card lets students borrow books; as a bonus, it may also give access to online journals.","zh":"圖書證讓學生借書；額外好處是，它也可能提供網上期刊權限。"},{"en":"Bonus benefits are not always expected, but they make the situation better.","zh":"額外好處不一定預期得到，但會令情況更好。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an additional positive point.","zh":"這個短語引出額外的正面之處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"squishy lake-edge sediments","meaning":"柔軟的湖邊沉積物","examples":[{"en":"Squishy lake-edge sediments recorded the footprints of passing animals.","zh":"柔軟的湖邊沉積物記錄了經過動物的足跡。"},{"en":"Squishy lake-edge sediments are soft wet layers of mud or sand near a lake shore.","zh":"squishy lake-edge sediments 指湖岸附近柔軟潮濕的泥或沙層。"},{"en":"Children can see a similar effect when wet mud records shoe prints after rain.","zh":"孩子在雨後濕泥記錄鞋印時，可以看到類似效果。"},{"en":"Soft sediment preserves tracks because feet press shapes into it before it hardens.","zh":"柔軟沉積物能保存足跡，因為腳在它變硬前壓出形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why footprints could be recorded so clearly.","zh":"這個短語解釋足跡為何能被清楚記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"record the tracks of","meaning":"記錄……的足跡","examples":[{"en":"Soft sediment can record the tracks of passing animals.","zh":"柔軟沉積物可以記錄經過動物的足跡。"},{"en":"To record the tracks of animals means to preserve marks left by their feet.","zh":"record the tracks of animals 指保存牠們腳留下的痕跡。"},{"en":"Wet sand on a beach can record the tracks of dogs, birds and children.","zh":"沙灘上的濕沙可以記錄狗、鳥和孩子的足跡。"},{"en":"Tracks are recorded when a surface is soft enough to hold the shape.","zh":"當表面足夠柔軟能保留形狀時，足跡就會被記錄下來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical evidence left by movement.","zh":"這個短語描述移動留下的實體證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"passing animals","meaning":"經過的動物","examples":[{"en":"The sediment preserved tracks left by passing animals.","zh":"沉積物保存了經過動物留下的足跡。"},{"en":"Passing animals are animals that move through an area without necessarily staying there.","zh":"passing animals 指移動穿過某地，但不一定停留在那裡的動物。"},{"en":"A muddy path may show marks from passing dogs, cats or birds.","zh":"泥濘小路可能顯示經過的狗、貓或鳥留下的痕跡。"},{"en":"Passing animals can leave evidence even if no bones remain behind.","zh":"即使沒有骨骼留下，經過的動物仍可留下證據。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on animals moving through a place.","zh":"這個短語集中於動物穿越某地的動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"divide the labour between themselves","meaning":"在彼此之間分工","examples":[{"en":"The researchers divided the labour between themselves.","zh":"研究者在彼此之間分工。"},{"en":"To divide the labour between themselves means to share different parts of the work among team members.","zh":"divide the labour between themselves 指把工作不同部分分配給團隊成員。"},{"en":"In a group project, students may divide the labour so one researches and another writes.","zh":"在小組專題中，學生可能分工，一人研究，另一人寫作。"},{"en":"Dividing labour helps large tasks finish faster and more carefully.","zh":"分工有助大型任務更快、更仔細完成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised teamwork.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的團隊合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"study tracks at 80 sites","meaning":"在八十個地點研究足跡","examples":[{"en":"The team studied fossil tracks at 80 different sites.","zh":"團隊在八十個不同地點研究化石足跡。"},{"en":"To study tracks at 80 sites means to examine footprints in many separate locations.","zh":"study tracks at 80 sites 指在許多不同位置檢查足跡。"},{"en":"A research team may study water quality at 80 sites to compare different neighbourhoods.","zh":"研究團隊可能在八十個地點研究水質，以比較不同社區。"},{"en":"Studying many sites gives stronger evidence than looking at one place only.","zh":"研究多個地點比只看一個地方提供更有力證據。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the scale and spread of the investigation.","zh":"這個短語強調調查的規模和分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"so-called ichnotaxa","meaning":"所謂的遺跡分類群","examples":[{"en":"The researchers examined 18 so-called ichnotaxa.","zh":"研究者檢視了十八個所謂的遺跡分類群。"},{"en":"So-called ichnotaxa means categories known by this technical name, based on trace fossils such as footprints.","zh":"so-called ichnotaxa 指以這個技術名稱稱呼、基於足跡等遺跡化石的分類。"},{"en":"A teacher may say “so-called learning styles” when using a term carefully or cautiously.","zh":"老師謹慎使用某術語時，可能說「所謂的學習風格」。"},{"en":"The phrase so-called often introduces a term that may be technical, debated or unfamiliar.","zh":"so-called 這個短語常引出技術性、有爭議或陌生的名稱。"},{"en":"Here, it prepares readers for a scientific classification word.","zh":"在這裡，它讓讀者準備好理解一個科學分類詞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ichnotaxa","meaning":"遺跡分類群","examples":[{"en":"Ichnotaxa are categories based on recognisable fossil footprints.","zh":"遺跡分類群是基於可辨認化石足跡的分類。"},{"en":"Ichnotaxa are scientific groups based on trace fossils rather than body fossils.","zh":"ichnotaxa 指基於遺跡化石而非身體化石的科學分類群。"},{"en":"A footprint type may be given an ichnotaxon even when the exact animal is unknown.","zh":"即使確切動物未知，一種足跡類型也可能被歸入一個遺跡分類群。"},{"en":"These categories help scientists compare tracks across different sites.","zh":"這些分類幫助科學家比較不同地點的足跡。"},{"en":"This word is useful when fossils show behaviour or movement rather than bones.","zh":"當化石顯示行為或移動而不是骨骼時，這個字很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"recognisable types of footprint","meaning":"可辨認的足跡類型","examples":[{"en":"Ichnotaxa are recognisable types of footprint.","zh":"遺跡分類群是可辨認的足跡類型。"},{"en":"Recognisable types of footprint are track shapes that can be identified and grouped.","zh":"recognisable types of footprint 指可以被識別和分組的足跡形狀。"},{"en":"A beach may show recognisable types of footprint from dogs, birds and shoes.","zh":"沙灘可能顯示狗、鳥和鞋留下的可辨認足跡類型。"},{"en":"Scientists group footprints when their shapes are consistent enough to compare.","zh":"當足跡形狀足夠一致可作比較，科學家便會把它們分組。"},{"en":"This phrase describes footprints that have clear features.","zh":"這個短語描述具有清楚特徵的足跡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be matched precisely with","meaning":"與……作精確配對","examples":[{"en":"A footprint cannot always be matched precisely with the species that made it.","zh":"足跡不一定總能與留下它的物種作精確配對。"},{"en":"To be matched precisely with something means to be linked exactly to it.","zh":"be matched precisely with something 指與某物準確地連繫起來。"},{"en":"A lost key may not be matched precisely with its owner if many students have similar keys.","zh":"如果很多學生有相似鎖匙，遺失的鎖匙未必能與主人精確配對。"},{"en":"Precise matching is difficult when evidence is incomplete or several possibilities look similar.","zh":"當證據不完整或幾種可能性很相似時，精確配對很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exact identification.","zh":"這個短語描述準確識別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the species of animal","meaning":"動物物種","examples":[{"en":"The precise species of animal cannot always be identified from a print.","zh":"不一定總能從足跡辨認出確切的動物物種。"},{"en":"The species of animal means the exact biological kind of animal.","zh":"species of animal 指生物學上精確的動物種類。"},{"en":"A biologist may identify the species of animal from hair, feathers or footprints.","zh":"生物學家可能從毛髮、羽毛或足跡辨認動物物種。"},{"en":"Identifying species is harder when only partial evidence remains.","zh":"當只剩部分證據時，辨認物種更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to exact classification, not just a general animal group.","zh":"這個短語指精確分類，而不只是大致動物群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a general sort of animal","meaning":"大致的動物類別","examples":[{"en":"A footprint can often be linked to a general sort of animal.","zh":"足跡通常可以連繫到大致的動物類別。"},{"en":"A general sort of animal means a broad animal group rather than an exact species.","zh":"general sort of animal 指廣泛動物群，而不是確切物種。"},{"en":"A large paw print may show that a dog-like animal passed by, even if the exact breed is unknown.","zh":"大爪印可能顯示有類犬動物經過，即使確切品種未知。"},{"en":"General identification is useful when precise evidence is not available.","zh":"當沒有精確證據時，大致識別仍然有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes approximate classification.","zh":"這個短語描述近似分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"act as an indicator of","meaning":"作為……的指標","examples":[{"en":"Footprints act as an indicator of the fate of an animal group.","zh":"足跡作為某動物群命運的指標。"},{"en":"To act as an indicator of something means to provide a sign or clue about it.","zh":"act as an indicator of something 指提供關於某事的跡象或線索。"},{"en":"Falling attendance can act as an indicator of student dissatisfaction.","zh":"出席率下降可以作為學生不滿的指標。"},{"en":"Indicators help people notice changes that may not be directly visible.","zh":"指標幫助人注意到未必能直接看見的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence that points to a larger pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述指向更大模式的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the fate of","meaning":"……的命運","examples":[{"en":"The fossil evidence reveals the fate of several reptile groups.","zh":"化石證據揭示了幾個爬蟲類群體的命運。"},{"en":"The fate of something means what eventually happened to it.","zh":"fate of something 指某物最終發生了甚麼事。"},{"en":"A report may explain the fate of a closed school building after students moved away.","zh":"報告可能解釋學生搬走後一座停用校舍的命運。"},{"en":"Fossils reveal fate by showing which groups survived, declined or disappeared.","zh":"化石透過顯示哪些群體存活、衰落或消失來揭示命運。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing final outcomes.","zh":"討論最終結果時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"even when","meaning":"即使在……的情況下","examples":[{"en":"Footprints provide evidence even when no bones survive.","zh":"即使沒有骨骼保存下來，足跡仍提供證據。"},{"en":"Even when means despite the fact that something happens or is true.","zh":"even when 指即使某事發生或屬實。"},{"en":"A student may keep studying even when the topic feels difficult.","zh":"即使題目感覺困難，學生仍可能繼續學習。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one fact remains true under a challenging condition.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事在困難條件下仍然成立。"},{"en":"It is useful for emphasising persistence or contrast.","zh":"它適合用於強調持續性或對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tell the story","meaning":"說明事情的經過","examples":[{"en":"Fossil footprints can tell the story when skeletons are absent.","zh":"當骨骼不存在時，化石足跡可以說明事情的經過。"},{"en":"To tell the story means to explain what happened through evidence or details.","zh":"tell the story 指透過證據或細節解釋發生了甚麼事。"},{"en":"A messy classroom can tell the story of a rushed group project.","zh":"凌亂的課室可以說明匆忙小組專題的經過。"},{"en":"Evidence tells the story when it helps people reconstruct events.","zh":"當證據幫助人重建事件，它就能說明事情經過。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal or figurative, and it often means “reveal the history.”","zh":"這個短語可以是字面或比喻，常指「揭示歷史」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"disappear before the end of","meaning":"在……結束前消失","examples":[{"en":"Five types of footprint disappear before the end of the Triassic.","zh":"五種足跡類型在三疊紀結束前消失。"},{"en":"To disappear before the end of a period means to stop appearing before that period finishes.","zh":"disappear before the end of a period 指在某時期完結前停止出現。"},{"en":"A bus route may disappear before the end of the year if few passengers use it.","zh":"如果乘客很少，一條巴士路線可能在年底前消失。"},{"en":"In fossils, disappearance can suggest that the animals making those marks died out or moved away.","zh":"在化石中，消失可能暗示留下那些痕跡的動物滅絕或遷走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes loss before a time boundary.","zh":"這個短語描述在時間界線之前消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"march confidently across the boundary","meaning":"明顯跨越年代分界繼續存在","examples":[{"en":"Four footprint types march confidently across the boundary into the Jurassic.","zh":"四種足跡類型明顯跨越分界進入侏羅紀並繼續存在。"},{"en":"To march confidently across the boundary means to continue clearly from one period into the next.","zh":"march confidently across the boundary 指清楚地從一個時期延續到下一個時期。"},{"en":"A family tradition may march confidently across generations when children still practise it.","zh":"如果孩子仍繼續實踐家庭傳統，該傳統就能明顯跨越世代延續。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests strong survival rather than weak or uncertain continuation.","zh":"這個短語暗示強力存續，而不是薄弱或不確定的延續。"},{"en":"In geology, it means the evidence continues past a major time boundary.","zh":"在地質學中，它指證據跨越重大時間分界後仍持續出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the Triassic–Jurassic boundary","meaning":"三疊紀與侏羅紀分界","examples":[{"en":"Major biological changes occurred at the Triassic–Jurassic boundary.","zh":"重大生物變化發生在三疊紀與侏羅紀分界。"},{"en":"The Triassic–Jurassic boundary is the geological dividing line between the Triassic and Jurassic periods.","zh":"Triassic–Jurassic boundary 指三疊紀與侏羅紀之間的地質分界線。"},{"en":"A science chart may mark the Triassic–Jurassic boundary with a line on a timeline.","zh":"科學圖表可能在時間線上用一條線標示三疊紀與侏羅紀分界。"},{"en":"Boundaries matter because fossils before and after them can show major change.","zh":"分界很重要，因為其前後的化石可以顯示重大變化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a time boundary, not a physical wall.","zh":"這個短語指時間分界，而不是實體牆。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"vanish at the boundary","meaning":"在分界處消失","examples":[{"en":"Several footprint types vanish at the geological boundary.","zh":"幾種足跡類型在地質分界處消失。"},{"en":"To vanish at the boundary means to disappear exactly around a dividing point in time or space.","zh":"vanish at the boundary 指正正在時間或空間分界點附近消失。"},{"en":"A shop brand may vanish at the boundary between old and new ownership.","zh":"一個店舖品牌可能在新舊業權交接處消失。"},{"en":"If fossils vanish at a boundary, scientists may suspect a sudden environmental change.","zh":"如果化石在分界處消失，科學家可能懷疑突然環境變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes abrupt disappearance at a key dividing line.","zh":"這個短語描述在關鍵分界線上的突然消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"only just splutter across","meaning":"勉強跨過分界後便消失","examples":[{"en":"Some groups only just splutter across the boundary before disappearing.","zh":"有些群體勉強跨過分界後便消失。"},{"en":"To only just splutter across means to survive briefly and weakly past a boundary.","zh":"only just splutter across 指僅僅、微弱地跨過某分界後短暫存續。"},{"en":"A struggling club may only just splutter into the next school year before closing.","zh":"一個苦苦支撐的學會可能勉強撐到下一學年後便結束。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests continuation, but only with difficulty and for a short time.","zh":"這個短語暗示有延續，但困難且時間短。"},{"en":"It contrasts weak survival with strong continuation.","zh":"它把微弱存活與強力延續作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"appear from nowhere","meaning":"突然出現","examples":[{"en":"Three new types of footprint appear from nowhere.","zh":"三種新的足跡類型突然出現。"},{"en":"To appear from nowhere means to appear suddenly without an obvious earlier source.","zh":"appear from nowhere 指在沒有明顯早期來源下突然出現。"},{"en":"A new fashion may appear from nowhere on social media and become popular quickly.","zh":"新潮流可能在社交媒體上突然出現並迅速流行。"},{"en":"Sudden appearance can make researchers ask what changed just before it happened.","zh":"突然出現會令研究者追問之前發生了甚麼變化。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests surprise and lack of visible origin.","zh":"這個短語暗示驚訝和缺乏可見起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"almost as soon as","meaning":"幾乎就在……開始時","examples":[{"en":"New footprint types appeared almost as soon as the Jurassic began.","zh":"新足跡類型幾乎就在侏羅紀開始時出現。"},{"en":"Almost as soon as means very shortly after something happened.","zh":"almost as soon as 指某事發生後不久。"},{"en":"The students started asking questions almost as soon as the new topic was introduced.","zh":"新題目一介紹，學生幾乎立即開始提問。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a very quick sequence of events.","zh":"這個短語強調事件之間非常快速的先後關係。"},{"en":"It suggests that little time passed between the first event and the second.","zh":"它暗示第一件事和第二件事之間幾乎沒有時間間隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the boundary itself is suggestive","meaning":"分界本身頗具啟示性","examples":[{"en":"The boundary itself is suggestive of a sudden catastrophic event.","zh":"分界本身頗具啟示性，暗示一次突然災難事件。"},{"en":"The boundary itself is suggestive means the dividing line provides clues even before other evidence is considered.","zh":"boundary itself is suggestive 指即使未考慮其他證據，分界線本身也提供線索。"},{"en":"A sudden drop in attendance itself is suggestive of a problem in the school timetable.","zh":"出席率突然下降本身就暗示學校時間表可能有問題。"},{"en":"Something is suggestive when it points toward a possible explanation.","zh":"當某物指向一個可能解釋，它就是具啟示性的。"},{"en":"This phrase means the evidence hints at something but may not prove it alone.","zh":"這個短語表示證據有所暗示，但單靠它未必能證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"geological indication","meaning":"地質跡象","examples":[{"en":"An iridium layer provided the first geological indication of the impact.","zh":"一層銥提供了撞擊的第一個地質跡象。"},{"en":"A geological indication is a clue in rocks or Earth materials that suggests a past event.","zh":"geological indication 指岩石或地球物質中暗示過去事件的線索。"},{"en":"Cracked layers in rock may be a geological indication of past earthquakes.","zh":"岩石中的裂層可能是過去地震的地質跡象。"},{"en":"Such indications help scientists reconstruct events that happened millions of years ago.","zh":"這類跡象幫助科學家重建數百萬年前的事件。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to evidence preserved in Earth’s structure.","zh":"這個短語指保存在地球結構中的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an unusually high level of","meaning":"異常高水平的……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists discovered an unusually high level of iridium in the rocks.","zh":"科學家在岩石中發現異常高水平的銥。"},{"en":"An unusually high level of something means an amount much greater than normal.","zh":"an unusually high level of something 指某物數量遠高於正常水平。"},{"en":"An unusually high level of noise outside a school may suggest roadworks nearby.","zh":"學校外異常高水平的噪音可能暗示附近有道路工程。"},{"en":"When a level is unusually high, scientists often look for a special cause.","zh":"當某水平異常偏高，科學家通常會尋找特殊原因。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a measurement with what is normally expected.","zh":"這個短語把測量值與正常預期作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"iridium","meaning":"銥","examples":[{"en":"Iridium is rare at the Earth’s surface but common in meteorites.","zh":"銥在地球表面很罕見，但在隕石中常見。"},{"en":"Iridium is a heavy metal element that can help scientists identify possible asteroid impacts.","zh":"iridium 是一種重金屬元素，可以幫助科學家識別可能的小行星撞擊。"},{"en":"A chemistry teacher may mention iridium when teaching rare metallic elements.","zh":"化學老師教授稀有金屬元素時可能提到銥。"},{"en":"High iridium levels in rocks can suggest material from space reached Earth.","zh":"岩石中高水平的銥可能暗示來自太空的物質到達地球。"},{"en":"This word names a specific element, not a general mineral.","zh":"這個字指一種特定元素，而不是一般礦物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at the end of the Cretaceous","meaning":"在白堊紀末期","examples":[{"en":"The dinosaurs disappeared at the end of the Cretaceous.","zh":"恐龍在白堊紀末期消失。"},{"en":"At the end of the Cretaceous means during the final part of the Cretaceous period.","zh":"at the end of the Cretaceous 指在白堊紀最後階段。"},{"en":"A timeline may show a major extinction at the end of the Cretaceous.","zh":"時間線可能顯示白堊紀末期發生一次重大滅絕。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event at a specific point in geological time.","zh":"這個短語把事件放在地質時間中的特定位置。"},{"en":"It is often used when discussing dinosaur extinction.","zh":"討論恐龍滅絕時常使用它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"disappear from the fossil record","meaning":"從化石記錄中消失","examples":[{"en":"Many large reptiles disappear from the fossil record at this boundary.","zh":"許多大型爬蟲類動物在這個分界處從化石記錄中消失。"},{"en":"To disappear from the fossil record means to stop appearing in preserved fossil evidence.","zh":"disappear from the fossil record 指停止出現在保存下來的化石證據中。"},{"en":"If a shell type disappears from the fossil record, scientists may ask whether the animal died out.","zh":"如果一種貝殼類型從化石記錄中消失，科學家可能問該動物是否滅絕。"},{"en":"Fossil disappearance can suggest extinction, migration or gaps in preservation.","zh":"化石中的消失可能暗示滅絕、遷移或保存缺口。"},{"en":"This phrase describes absence from geological evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述在地質證據中的缺席。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be normally rare at","meaning":"在……通常很罕見","examples":[{"en":"Iridium is normally rare at the Earth’s surface.","zh":"銥在地球表面通常很罕見。"},{"en":"To be normally rare at a place means to be uncommon there under ordinary conditions.","zh":"be normally rare at a place 指在普通情況下於某地不常見。"},{"en":"Snow is normally rare at sea level in many tropical cities.","zh":"在許多熱帶城市，海平面地區通常很少下雪。"},{"en":"If something normally rare appears in large amounts, scientists may suspect an unusual event.","zh":"如果通常罕見的東西大量出現，科學家可能懷疑有異常事件。"},{"en":"This phrase compares ordinary scarcity with unusual abundance.","zh":"這個短語把平常稀少與異常豐富作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be more abundant in","meaning":"在……中更豐富","examples":[{"en":"Iridium is more abundant in meteorites than at the Earth’s surface.","zh":"銥在隕石中比在地球表面更豐富。"},{"en":"To be more abundant in something means to exist there in larger amounts.","zh":"be more abundant in something 指在某物中以較大數量存在。"},{"en":"Calcium is more abundant in milk than in many soft drinks.","zh":"鈣在牛奶中比在許多汽水中更豐富。"},{"en":"If an element is more abundant in meteorites, high levels on Earth may suggest space material.","zh":"如果某元素在隕石中較豐富，地球上的高含量可能暗示太空物質。"},{"en":"This phrase compares quantities in different places or materials.","zh":"這個短語比較不同地方或物質中的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"begin to believe","meaning":"開始相信","examples":[{"en":"Researchers began to believe the impact theory after examining the evidence.","zh":"研究者檢視證據後開始相信撞擊理論。"},{"en":"To begin to believe something means to start accepting it as likely or true.","zh":"begin to believe something 指開始接受某事可能屬實。"},{"en":"A teacher may begin to believe a student is struggling after seeing repeated mistakes.","zh":"老師看到反覆錯誤後，可能開始相信學生遇到困難。"},{"en":"People begin to believe a theory when evidence starts to fit together.","zh":"當證據開始互相吻合，人們會開始相信某理論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gradual change in opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述觀點逐漸改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the impact theory","meaning":"撞擊理論","examples":[{"en":"The impact theory proposes that an asteroid caused mass extinction.","zh":"撞擊理論提出小行星造成大規模滅絕。"},{"en":"The impact theory is the idea that a major asteroid or comet strike caused huge biological change.","zh":"impact theory 指大型小行星或彗星撞擊造成重大生物變化的想法。"},{"en":"Students may learn the impact theory when studying why dinosaurs disappeared.","zh":"學生研究恐龍為何消失時，可能學到撞擊理論。"},{"en":"The theory gained support when scientists found unusual chemical evidence in rocks.","zh":"當科學家在岩石中發現異常化學證據時，該理論得到支持。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an explanation based on a catastrophic collision.","zh":"這個短語指基於災難性碰撞的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"look for other anomalies","meaning":"尋找其他異常現象","examples":[{"en":"Scientists started to look for other geological anomalies.","zh":"科學家開始尋找其他地質異常現象。"},{"en":"To look for other anomalies means to search for more unusual signs or patterns.","zh":"look for other anomalies 指搜尋更多不尋常跡象或模式。"},{"en":"A doctor may look for other anomalies if one test result seems strange.","zh":"如果一項測試結果很奇怪，醫生可能尋找其他異常。"},{"en":"Finding more anomalies can strengthen a theory or reveal a new problem.","zh":"找到更多異常現象可以加強理論或揭示新問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes searching for evidence that does not fit the normal pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述尋找不符合正常模式的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"turn up","meaning":"被發現；出現","examples":[{"en":"Another important anomaly turned up above the boundary layer.","zh":"另一個重要異常現象在分界層之上被發現。"},{"en":"To turn up means to appear, be found, or be discovered.","zh":"turn up 指出現、被找到或被發現。"},{"en":"A lost worksheet may turn up under a pile of books.","zh":"遺失的工作紙可能在一堆書下面出現。"},{"en":"Evidence often turns up after researchers check a wider area carefully.","zh":"研究者仔細檢查更大範圍後，證據常會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and suggests discovery.","zh":"這個短語較口語，暗示發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a surprising abundance of","meaning":"數量異常豐富的……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists found a surprising abundance of fern spores.","zh":"科學家發現數量異常豐富的蕨類孢子。"},{"en":"A surprising abundance of something means an unexpectedly large amount of it.","zh":"surprising abundance of something 指某物數量大得出乎意料。"},{"en":"A teacher may find a surprising abundance of good essays after a difficult assignment.","zh":"老師可能在一項困難作業後發現意外大量好文章。"},{"en":"Unexpected abundance can be a clue that something unusual happened.","zh":"意外豐富的數量可以成為發生異常事件的線索。"},{"en":"This phrase combines large quantity with surprise.","zh":"這個短語結合了大量和驚訝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fern spores","meaning":"蕨類孢子","examples":[{"en":"Fern spores became unusually abundant after the impact.","zh":"撞擊後，蕨類孢子變得異常豐富。"},{"en":"Fern spores are tiny reproductive cells produced by ferns.","zh":"fern spores 指蕨類植物產生的微小繁殖細胞。"},{"en":"A biology teacher may compare fern spores with seeds to explain plant reproduction.","zh":"生物老師可能把蕨類孢子與種子比較，以解釋植物繁殖。"},{"en":"Spores can spread quickly when open land becomes available after disturbance.","zh":"當干擾後出現空地，孢子可以快速擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to tiny plant reproductive structures, not pollen from flowers.","zh":"這個短語指微小植物繁殖結構，而不是花粉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"just above the boundary layer","meaning":"就在分界層之上","examples":[{"en":"The fern spores were found just above the boundary layer.","zh":"蕨類孢子就在分界層之上被發現。"},{"en":"Just above the boundary layer means immediately higher than a specific geological dividing layer.","zh":"just above the boundary layer 指緊接在某地質分界層上方。"},{"en":"A note placed just above a table line may belong to the next section, not the previous one.","zh":"放在表格線上方的註釋可能屬於下一部分，而不是上一部分。"},{"en":"Position matters because layers above and below a boundary represent different times.","zh":"位置很重要，因為分界上下的層代表不同時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exact location in layered material.","zh":"這個短語描述分層物質中的精確位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"boundary layer","meaning":"地質分界層","examples":[{"en":"The boundary layer marks a major geological transition.","zh":"地質分界層標示重大地質轉變。"},{"en":"A boundary layer is a layer of rock or sediment marking a division between time periods or events.","zh":"boundary layer 指標示時期或事件分界的岩石或沉積層。"},{"en":"A geology teacher may use a boundary layer to show where one period ends and another begins.","zh":"地質老師可能用分界層顯示一個時期在哪裡結束，另一個時期在哪裡開始。"},{"en":"Boundary layers can preserve evidence of sudden environmental change.","zh":"分界層可以保存突然環境變化的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a physical layer with time significance.","zh":"這個短語指具有時間意義的實體層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be known as","meaning":"被稱為……","examples":[{"en":"The sudden increase in fern spores is known as a fern spike.","zh":"蕨類孢子的突然增加被稱為蕨類孢子激增。"},{"en":"To be known as something means to have a particular name.","zh":"be known as something 指有某個名稱。"},{"en":"Hong Kong is known as a busy international city.","zh":"香港被稱為繁忙的國際城市。"},{"en":"Scientific terms help researchers describe a pattern quickly and precisely.","zh":"科學術語幫助研究者快速而準確地描述模式。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the name people use for something.","zh":"這個短語引出人們用來稱呼某事的名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fern spike","meaning":"蕨類孢子激增","examples":[{"en":"A fern spike indicates that ferns spread rapidly after a disaster.","zh":"蕨類孢子激增顯示災難後蕨類快速擴散。"},{"en":"A fern spike is a sudden large increase in fern spores in the fossil record.","zh":"fern spike 指化石記錄中蕨類孢子突然大量增加。"},{"en":"A biology class may use a fern spike to explain how plants return after disturbance.","zh":"生物課可能用蕨類孢子激增來解釋植物如何在干擾後回復。"},{"en":"Fern spikes occur because ferns can quickly colonise damaged or cleared land.","zh":"蕨類孢子激增會出現，是因為蕨類能迅速佔據受破壞或被清空的土地。"},{"en":"This phrase is a scientific clue that vegetation was disrupted.","zh":"這個短語是植被曾受擾亂的科學線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"match the theory nicely","meaning":"與該理論十分吻合","examples":[{"en":"The fern-spore evidence matched the asteroid-impact theory nicely.","zh":"蕨類孢子證據與小行星撞擊理論十分吻合。"},{"en":"To match the theory nicely means to fit a theory well and support it clearly.","zh":"match the theory nicely 指與某理論配合得很好並清楚支持它。"},{"en":"A student’s survey results may match her argument nicely if the answers support her claim.","zh":"如果調查答案支持學生的主張，她的調查結果就與論點十分吻合。"},{"en":"Evidence that matches a theory makes the theory more convincing.","zh":"與理論吻合的證據會令理論更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a good fit between evidence and explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述證據與解釋之間的良好配合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"opportunists","meaning":"機會型物種","examples":[{"en":"Many modern ferns are opportunists that thrive in disturbed environments.","zh":"許多現代蕨類是能在受干擾環境中繁盛的機會型物種。"},{"en":"Opportunists are organisms or people that take advantage of sudden opportunities.","zh":"opportunists 指能利用突然機會的生物或人。"},{"en":"In business, opportunists may open food stalls quickly when a new school opens nearby.","zh":"在商業中，當附近新學校開幕，機會型商人可能迅速開小食店。"},{"en":"In nature, opportunists grow fast when competitors are removed.","zh":"在自然界中，當競爭者被移除，機會型物種會快速生長。"},{"en":"This word can be neutral in ecology but negative when describing selfish behaviour.","zh":"這個字在生態學中可以是中性，但形容自私行為時可能帶負面意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"compete against","meaning":"與……競爭","examples":[{"en":"Ferns often cannot compete successfully against leafy plants.","zh":"蕨類常無法成功與有葉植物競爭。"},{"en":"To compete against something means to try to succeed while another group is trying to use the same resources.","zh":"compete against something 指在另一群體也試圖使用同一資源時努力取得成功。"},{"en":"Small shops compete against supermarkets by offering personal service.","zh":"小店透過提供個人化服務與超級市場競爭。"},{"en":"Competition becomes harder when another group grows faster or uses resources better.","zh":"當另一群體生長更快或更善用資源，競爭會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rivalry for space, food, customers or success.","zh":"這個短語描述為空間、食物、顧客或成功而競爭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"plants with leaves","meaning":"有葉植物","examples":[{"en":"Ferns may struggle to compete against larger plants with leaves.","zh":"蕨類可能難以與較大型有葉植物競爭。"},{"en":"Plants with leaves are plants that have broad structures for capturing sunlight.","zh":"plants with leaves 指具有寬大結構以吸收陽光的植物。"},{"en":"In a garden, plants with large leaves may shade smaller plants beneath them.","zh":"在花園中，葉片大的植物可能遮住下方較小植物。"},{"en":"Leafy plants can outcompete ferns if they block light and take space.","zh":"如果有葉植物遮擋光線並佔據空間，它們可以勝過蕨類。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to ordinary leafy plants rather than spores or bare stems.","zh":"這個短語指普通有葉植物，而不是孢子或裸莖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a piece of land is cleared","meaning":"一片土地被清空","examples":[{"en":"Ferns spread quickly when a piece of land is cleared.","zh":"當一片土地被清空，蕨類會迅速擴散。"},{"en":"When a piece of land is cleared, existing plants, trees or cover are removed from it.","zh":"a piece of land is cleared 指某地原有植物、樹木或覆蓋物被移除。"},{"en":"After a construction site is cleared, weeds may appear before new buildings are finished.","zh":"建築地盤被清空後，新建築完成前可能先長出雜草。"},{"en":"Cleared land gives fast-growing plants open space and sunlight.","zh":"被清空的土地給快速生長植物提供開放空間和陽光。"},{"en":"This phrase describes land after vegetation or objects have been removed.","zh":"這個短語描述植被或物件被移除後的土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"volcanic eruption","meaning":"火山爆發","examples":[{"en":"A volcanic eruption can remove existing plant cover.","zh":"火山爆發可以移除原有植物覆蓋。"},{"en":"A volcanic eruption is an event in which lava, ash or gases burst from a volcano.","zh":"volcanic eruption 指熔岩、火山灰或氣體從火山噴出的事件。"},{"en":"A geography class may watch footage of a volcanic eruption to understand natural hazards.","zh":"地理課可能觀看火山爆發片段，以理解自然災害。"},{"en":"Eruptions can bury forests, change soil and create new land surfaces.","zh":"火山爆發可以掩埋森林、改變泥土並形成新地表。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a powerful geological event.","zh":"這個短語描述強大的地質事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be the first to set up shop","meaning":"最先在某地落地生根","examples":[{"en":"Ferns are often the first plants to set up shop on cleared land.","zh":"蕨類常是最先在被清空土地上落地生根的植物。"},{"en":"To be the first to set up shop means to be the first to arrive, settle and start growing or operating.","zh":"be the first to set up shop 指最先到達、定居並開始生長或營運。"},{"en":"A coffee stall may be the first to set up shop near a new station.","zh":"咖啡小店可能最先在新車站附近開業。"},{"en":"First arrivals can benefit because there is less competition for space.","zh":"最先到達者可以受益，因為空間競爭較少。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and suggests quickly occupying a new opportunity.","zh":"這個短語較口語，暗示迅速佔據新機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"asteroid strike","meaning":"小行星撞擊","examples":[{"en":"An asteroid strike could destroy vegetation over a vast area.","zh":"小行星撞擊可以摧毀廣大地區的植被。"},{"en":"An asteroid strike is a collision between Earth and a large rocky object from space.","zh":"asteroid strike 指地球與來自太空的大型岩石物體相撞。"},{"en":"A classroom model may show how an asteroid strike throws dust into the air.","zh":"課堂模型可能展示小行星撞擊如何把塵埃拋入空中。"},{"en":"A large strike can destroy plants, darken skies and disrupt food chains.","zh":"大型撞擊可以摧毀植物、令天空變暗並打亂食物鏈。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sudden external event with planet-wide effects.","zh":"這個短語描述突然的外來事件，並可能產生全球性影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"scour the Earth of","meaning":"把地球大部分的……清除","examples":[{"en":"The impact may have scoured much of the Earth of its plant cover.","zh":"這次撞擊可能把地球大部分地區的植物覆蓋清除。"},{"en":"To scour the Earth of something means to remove it harshly or completely from a large area.","zh":"scour the Earth of something 指猛烈或徹底地從大範圍清除某物。"},{"en":"A powerful storm can scour a beach of loose sand and small plants.","zh":"強烈風暴可以把沙灘上的鬆散沙粒和小植物清走。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests violent clearing, not gentle cleaning.","zh":"這個短語暗示猛烈清除，而不是溫和清潔。"},{"en":"It is used when a force strips something away over a wide area.","zh":"當某種力量在廣大地區剝走某物時，可以使用它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"vegetable cover","meaning":"植被","examples":[{"en":"The asteroid may have destroyed much of the Earth’s vegetable cover.","zh":"小行星可能摧毀了地球大部分植被。"},{"en":"Vegetable cover means plant life covering the ground, such as forests, grasses and ferns.","zh":"vegetable cover 指覆蓋地面的植物生命，例如森林、草和蕨類。"},{"en":"Farmers protect vegetable cover on hillsides to reduce soil erosion.","zh":"農民保護山坡植被，以減少水土流失。"},{"en":"When plant cover disappears, soil, animals and climate can all be affected.","zh":"當植被消失，泥土、動物和氣候都可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to vegetation, not vegetables for eating.","zh":"這個短語指植物覆蓋，而不是用來食用的蔬菜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"provide a paradise for","meaning":"為……提供理想環境","examples":[{"en":"The cleared land provided a paradise for ferns.","zh":"被清空的土地為蕨類提供理想環境。"},{"en":"To provide a paradise for something means to create ideal conditions for it to thrive.","zh":"provide a paradise for something 指為某物創造理想的繁盛條件。"},{"en":"A quiet library can provide a paradise for students who need to revise.","zh":"安靜圖書館可以為需要溫習的學生提供理想環境。"},{"en":"Open land with little competition can help ferns spread rapidly.","zh":"競爭少的空地可以幫助蕨類快速擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a positive image to describe a perfect environment.","zh":"這個短語用正面意象描述完美環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a good indication that","meaning":"……的有力跡象","examples":[{"en":"A fern spike is a good indication that a catastrophe occurred.","zh":"蕨類孢子激增是災難曾發生的有力跡象。"},{"en":"A good indication that something happened is strong evidence or a clear sign of it.","zh":"good indication that something happened 指某事發生的強證據或清楚跡象。"},{"en":"Empty shelves can be a good indication that a product is very popular.","zh":"空貨架可以是某產品很受歡迎的有力跡象。"},{"en":"An indication helps people infer something that they did not directly witness.","zh":"跡象幫助人推斷自己沒有直接看見的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence that points toward a conclusion.","zh":"這個短語描述指向結論的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"something terrible has happened","meaning":"發生了可怕的事情","examples":[{"en":"A sudden fern spike suggests that something terrible has happened.","zh":"蕨類孢子突然激增暗示發生了可怕的事情。"},{"en":"Something terrible has happened means a serious and damaging event has occurred.","zh":"something terrible has happened 指發生了嚴重而有破壞性的事件。"},{"en":"If a classroom is suddenly empty and damaged, people may fear that something terrible has happened.","zh":"如果課室突然空無一人且被破壞，人們可能擔心發生了可怕的事情。"},{"en":"Sudden changes in evidence can suggest a major disaster in the past.","zh":"證據突然變化可以暗示過去發生了重大災難。"},{"en":"This phrase is broad and emotional, often used before the exact cause is known.","zh":"這個短語較廣泛且帶情感色彩，常在確切原因未知前使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"appear at the end of","meaning":"在……末期出現","examples":[{"en":"An iridium anomaly and a fern spike appear at the end of the Triassic.","zh":"銥異常和蕨類孢子激增在三疊紀末期出現。"},{"en":"To appear at the end of a period means to be found or happen during its final part.","zh":"appear at the end of a period 指在某時期最後部分被發現或發生。"},{"en":"Important review questions often appear at the end of a textbook chapter.","zh":"重要複習問題常在教科書章節末尾出現。"},{"en":"Location near the end of a period can help scientists connect evidence with a major transition.","zh":"位於某時期末期可以幫助科學家把證據與重大轉變連起來。"},{"en":"This phrase marks timing or position near a conclusion.","zh":"這個短語標示接近結束時的時間或位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"account for","meaning":"解釋；說明……的原因","examples":[{"en":"The catastrophe accounts for the disappearance of several footprint types.","zh":"這場災難解釋了幾種足跡類型消失的原因。"},{"en":"To account for something means to explain why it happened.","zh":"account for something 指解釋某事為何發生。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask what accounts for a sudden drop in test scores.","zh":"老師可能問甚麼原因解釋測驗分數突然下降。"},{"en":"A strong explanation accounts for both the cause and the observed result.","zh":"有力解釋會同時說明原因和所觀察到的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining evidence or changes.","zh":"解釋證據或變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"disappearing ichnotaxa","meaning":"消失的遺跡分類群","examples":[{"en":"The disappearing ichnotaxa represented animals that did not survive.","zh":"消失的遺跡分類群代表未能存活的動物。"},{"en":"Disappearing ichnotaxa are footprint categories that stop appearing in the fossil record.","zh":"disappearing ichnotaxa 指在化石記錄中停止出現的足跡分類。"},{"en":"A scientist may study disappearing track types to learn which animals vanished.","zh":"科學家可能研究消失的足跡類型，以了解哪些動物消失。"},{"en":"When ichnotaxa disappear suddenly, the animals that made them may have died out.","zh":"當遺跡分類群突然消失，留下它們的動物可能已滅絕。"},{"en":"This phrase connects missing footprints with possible extinction.","zh":"這個短語把缺失的足跡與可能的滅絕連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"survive the holocaust","meaning":"在大災難中存活","examples":[{"en":"Many reptile groups did not survive the ecological holocaust.","zh":"許多爬蟲類群體未能在這場生態大災難中存活。"},{"en":"To survive the holocaust means to remain alive through a huge disaster or destruction.","zh":"survive the holocaust 指在巨大災難或破壞中仍然存活。"},{"en":"Some trees may survive a wildfire while smaller plants disappear.","zh":"有些樹可能在山火中存活，而較小植物消失。"},{"en":"Survival depends on whether a species can find food, shelter and suitable conditions after disaster.","zh":"存活取決於一個物種在災後能否找到食物、庇護和合適條件。"},{"en":"This phrase is very strong and describes survival through extreme destruction.","zh":"這個短語語氣非常強烈，描述在極端破壞中存活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"how rapidly","meaning":"……的速度有多快","examples":[{"en":"The researchers were surprised by how rapidly new dinosaur types appeared.","zh":"研究者對新恐龍類型出現的速度有多快感到驚訝。"},{"en":"How rapidly means how quickly something happens.","zh":"how rapidly 指某事發生得有多快。"},{"en":"A teacher may be surprised by how rapidly a student improves after daily practice.","zh":"老師可能對學生每天練習後進步速度有多快感到驚訝。"},{"en":"Rapid change attracts attention because it may need a special explanation.","zh":"快速變化會吸引注意，因為它可能需要特殊解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about the speed of change.","zh":"這個短語詢問變化速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a mere 10,000 years after","meaning":"僅在……一萬年後","examples":[{"en":"Eubrontes appeared a mere 10,000 years after the iridium anomaly.","zh":"巨型真雷龍足跡類型僅在銥異常一萬年後出現。"},{"en":"A mere 10,000 years after means only 10,000 years later, which is short in geological time.","zh":"a mere 10,000 years after 指僅在一萬年後，在地質時間中算很短。"},{"en":"A city changing within a mere ten years may seem surprisingly fast to residents.","zh":"一座城市僅在十年內改變，對居民來說可能出奇地快。"},{"en":"The word mere makes the time period sound smaller than expected.","zh":"mere 這個字令該時間聽起來比預期更短。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the event happened unusually soon after another event.","zh":"這個短語強調事件在另一事件後異常迅速發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Eubrontes giganteus","meaning":"巨型真雷龍足跡類型","examples":[{"en":"Eubrontes giganteus left very large footprints in early Jurassic rocks.","zh":"巨型真雷龍足跡類型在早期侏羅紀岩石中留下非常大的足跡。"},{"en":"Eubrontes giganteus is a name given to a large fossil footprint type, not necessarily the exact animal species.","zh":"Eubrontes giganteus 是給大型化石足跡類型的名稱，不一定是確切動物物種。"},{"en":"A museum label may use Eubrontes giganteus to identify a trackway made by a large dinosaur.","zh":"博物館標籤可能用 Eubrontes giganteus 來識別大型恐龍留下的足跡列。"},{"en":"Large tracks of this type help scientists estimate the size of the animal that made them.","zh":"這類大型足跡幫助科學家估計留下足跡的動物體型。"},{"en":"This term belongs to fossil footprint classification.","zh":"這個術語屬於化石足跡分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be made by","meaning":"由……留下","examples":[{"en":"The Eubrontes prints were made by large theropods.","zh":"巨型真雷龍足跡由大型獸腳類恐龍留下。"},{"en":"To be made by something means to be created or left by that thing.","zh":"be made by something 指由某物創造或留下。"},{"en":"Muddy footprints in a hallway may be made by students coming in after rain.","zh":"走廊中的泥腳印可能由雨後進入的學生留下。"},{"en":"Identifying what made a mark helps people understand the event behind it.","zh":"識別痕跡由甚麼造成，有助人理解背後事件。"},{"en":"This phrase links evidence with its source.","zh":"這個短語把證據與其來源連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"theropods","meaning":"獸腳類恐龍","examples":[{"en":"Theropods were a major group of meat-eating dinosaurs.","zh":"獸腳類恐龍是肉食恐龍中的一個主要群體。"},{"en":"Theropods are a group of mostly two-legged dinosaurs, many of which were predators.","zh":"theropods 指一群多數以兩足行走的恐龍，其中許多是捕食者。"},{"en":"A child may learn about theropods when studying Tyrannosaurus in a dinosaur book.","zh":"孩子閱讀恐龍書研究暴龍時，可能學到獸腳類恐龍。"},{"en":"Their footprints can show movement, size and possible hunting behaviour.","zh":"牠們的足跡可以顯示移動、體型和可能的捕獵行為。"},{"en":"This word refers to a dinosaur group, not one single species.","zh":"這個字指一個恐龍群體，而不是單一物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"go on to produce","meaning":"後來演化出……","examples":[{"en":"The theropod group went on to produce enormous predators.","zh":"獸腳類恐龍群體後來演化出巨大捕食者。"},{"en":"To go on to produce something means later to develop or create it.","zh":"go on to produce something 指後來發展或產生某物。"},{"en":"A small school club may go on to produce successful artists years later.","zh":"一個小型學校學會多年後可能培養出成功藝術家。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an early group or process led to later results.","zh":"這個短語顯示早期群體或過程導致後來結果。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing development over time.","zh":"描述隨時間發展時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"such nightmares as","meaning":"像……這樣的可怕巨獸","examples":[{"en":"The group produced such nightmares as Allosaurus and Tyrannosaurus.","zh":"這個群體產生了像異特龍和暴龍這樣的可怕巨獸。"},{"en":"Such nightmares as means frightening examples such as the ones named.","zh":"such nightmares as 指像所列舉例子那樣令人害怕的事物。"},{"en":"A teacher might jokingly describe exam mistakes such nightmares as missing names and blank pages.","zh":"老師可能開玩笑地把漏寫名字和交白卷等考試錯誤稱為可怕例子。"},{"en":"This phrase uses dramatic language to make examples sound fearsome.","zh":"這個短語使用戲劇化語言，使例子聽起來可怕。"},{"en":"It is colourful and informal, not neutral scientific wording.","zh":"它色彩鮮明且較口語，不是中性科學用語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be 20% bigger than","meaning":"比……大百分之二十","examples":[{"en":"The Eubrontes track was 20% bigger than earlier theropod tracks.","zh":"巨型真雷龍足跡比早期獸腳類恐龍足跡大百分之二十。"},{"en":"To be 20% bigger than something means to be one fifth larger than it.","zh":"be 20% bigger than something 指比某物大五分之一。"},{"en":"A classroom that is 20% bigger than another can hold more desks and students.","zh":"一間比另一間大百分之二十的課室可以容納更多書桌和學生。"},{"en":"A percentage comparison makes size differences clearer and more precise.","zh":"百分比比較令大小差異更清楚、更精確。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a measured comparison, not just a vague impression.","zh":"這個短語給出量化比較，而不只是模糊印象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rapid increase in size","meaning":"體型迅速增大","examples":[{"en":"The researchers sought to explain the rapid increase in dinosaur size.","zh":"研究者試圖解釋恐龍體型迅速增大。"},{"en":"A rapid increase in size means something becomes larger quickly.","zh":"rapid increase in size 指某物快速變大。"},{"en":"A child’s feet may show a rapid increase in size during a growth spurt.","zh":"孩子在發育高峰期腳部大小可能迅速增加。"},{"en":"Rapid growth often needs an explanation because it may reflect a major change in conditions.","zh":"快速增長通常需要解釋，因為它可能反映條件重大改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fast physical enlargement.","zh":"這個短語描述身體大小快速增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a phenomenon called","meaning":"一種稱為……的現象","examples":[{"en":"The increase may have resulted from a phenomenon called ecological release.","zh":"這種增大可能源於一種稱為生態釋放的現象。"},{"en":"A phenomenon called something means an event or process known by that name.","zh":"phenomenon called something 指以某名稱為人所知的事件或過程。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain a phenomenon called evaporation when water disappears from a cup.","zh":"老師可能在杯中水消失時解釋一種稱為蒸發的現象。"},{"en":"Naming a phenomenon helps students remember and discuss the pattern.","zh":"為現象命名幫助學生記住和討論該模式。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a technical term by giving its name.","zh":"這個短語透過給出名稱來引入技術術語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ecological release","meaning":"生態釋放","examples":[{"en":"Ecological release can occur when competing species disappear.","zh":"當競爭物種消失時，生態釋放可能發生。"},{"en":"Ecological release is when a species expands or changes after competitors or predators are removed.","zh":"ecological release 指競爭者或捕食者被移除後，某物種擴張或改變。"},{"en":"On an island with few predators, a small animal may grow larger or become more common.","zh":"在捕食者少的島上，小動物可能長得更大或變得更常見。"},{"en":"When pressure from competitors falls, a species may use more space and resources.","zh":"當競爭壓力下降，物種可能使用更多空間和資源。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why animals may flourish after rivals vanish.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何競爭者消失後，動物可能蓬勃發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be seen today when","meaning":"現今可在……的情況下見到","examples":[{"en":"Ecological release is seen today when reptiles reach isolated islands.","zh":"當爬蟲類到達孤立島嶼時，現今可見生態釋放。"},{"en":"To be seen today when something happens means the same pattern can still be observed in modern situations.","zh":"be seen today when something happens 指相同模式仍可在現代情況中被觀察到。"},{"en":"Similar classroom behaviour is seen today when students feel rules are unclear.","zh":"當學生覺得規則不清楚時，現今也可見相似課室行為。"},{"en":"Modern examples help people understand ancient processes more easily.","zh":"現代例子幫助人更容易理解古代過程。"},{"en":"This phrase links past explanation with present-day observation.","zh":"這個短語把過去解釋與現今觀察連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tend to be","meaning":"往往是……","examples":[{"en":"Modern reptiles tend to be relatively small creatures.","zh":"現代爬蟲類往往是相對較小的生物。"},{"en":"Tend to be means usually or generally are.","zh":"tend to be 指通常或一般是。"},{"en":"Younger students tend to be nervous before their first speech.","zh":"年幼學生第一次演講前往往會緊張。"},{"en":"A tendency describes a common pattern, not an absolute rule.","zh":"趨勢描述常見模式，而不是絕對規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for cautious generalisation.","zh":"作出謹慎概括時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"face no competitors","meaning":"沒有面對競爭者","examples":[{"en":"Some island reptiles grow larger when they face no competitors.","zh":"有些島上爬蟲類在沒有競爭者時會長得更大。"},{"en":"To face no competitors means to have no other groups competing for the same resources.","zh":"face no competitors 指沒有其他群體競爭同一資源。"},{"en":"A small shop may grow quickly if it faces no competitors in a new neighbourhood.","zh":"如果新社區中沒有競爭者，小店可能迅速成長。"},{"en":"Without competitors, a species can use more food, space and opportunities.","zh":"沒有競爭者時，一個物種可以使用更多食物、空間和機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a situation with little or no competition.","zh":"這個短語描述競爭很少或沒有競爭的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the most spectacular example","meaning":"最引人注目的例子","examples":[{"en":"The Komodo dragon is one of the most spectacular examples.","zh":"科莫多巨蜥是最引人注目的例子之一。"},{"en":"The most spectacular example means the most impressive or striking case.","zh":"most spectacular example 指最令人印象深刻或最突出的個案。"},{"en":"A teacher may call a student’s dramatic improvement the most spectacular example of practice paying off.","zh":"老師可能把學生戲劇性的進步稱為練習帶來成果的最引人注目的例子。"},{"en":"Spectacular examples are memorable because they clearly show the point.","zh":"引人注目的例子令人難忘，因為它們清楚顯示重點。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a particularly impressive illustration.","zh":"這個短語突出特別令人印象深刻的例證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the Indonesian island of Komodo","meaning":"印尼科莫多島","examples":[{"en":"Very large lizards live on the Indonesian island of Komodo.","zh":"非常大的蜥蜴生活在印尼科莫多島。"},{"en":"The Indonesian island of Komodo is an island in Indonesia known for Komodo dragons.","zh":"Indonesian island of Komodo 指印尼一個以科莫多巨蜥聞名的島嶼。"},{"en":"A geography lesson may mention the Indonesian island of Komodo when discussing island ecosystems.","zh":"地理課討論島嶼生態系統時，可能提到印尼科莫多島。"},{"en":"Islands can produce unusual animal sizes because their ecological conditions are special.","zh":"島嶼可以產生不尋常的動物體型，因為其生態條件特殊。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific place, not just any island.","zh":"這個短語指特定地方，而不是任何島嶼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"local lizards","meaning":"本地蜥蜴","examples":[{"en":"The local lizards have evolved unusually large bodies.","zh":"本地蜥蜴已演化出異常巨大的身體。"},{"en":"Local lizards are lizards native to or living in a particular area.","zh":"local lizards 指原生於或生活在某特定地區的蜥蜴。"},{"en":"Tourists may see local lizards sunning themselves on rocks near a village.","zh":"遊客可能看到本地蜥蜴在村莊附近的岩石上曬太陽。"},{"en":"Local animals can develop unusual features when their environment is isolated.","zh":"當環境孤立，本地動物可能發展出不尋常特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to lizards from that place, not imported animals.","zh":"這個短語指該地的蜥蜴，而不是外來動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be referred to as dragons","meaning":"被稱為巨龍","examples":[{"en":"The enormous lizards are often referred to as dragons.","zh":"這些巨型蜥蜴常被稱為巨龍。"},{"en":"To be referred to as something means to be called by that name or description.","zh":"be referred to as something 指被稱為某個名稱或描述。"},{"en":"A strict teacher may jokingly be referred to as a “dragon” by nervous students.","zh":"緊張學生可能開玩笑地把嚴格老師稱為「巨龍」。"},{"en":"Names often reflect how people imagine or feel about something.","zh":"名稱常反映人們如何想像或感受某事物。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what people call someone or something.","zh":"這個短語引出人們如何稱呼某人或某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in other words","meaning":"換句話說","examples":[{"en":"In other words, dinosaurs flourished after their competitors disappeared.","zh":"換句話說，恐龍在競爭者消失後蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"In other words introduces the same idea expressed more simply or clearly.","zh":"in other words 用來以更簡單或更清楚方式表達同一想法。"},{"en":"The bus is unreliable; in other words, students cannot count on it every morning.","zh":"巴士不可靠；換句話說，學生不能每天早上依靠它。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to clarify an explanation for readers.","zh":"作者使用這個短語來為讀者澄清解釋。"},{"en":"It helps restate a difficult point in easier language.","zh":"它幫助用較容易語言重述困難重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"flourish","meaning":"蓬勃發展","examples":[{"en":"The dinosaurs could flourish after rival animal groups were eliminated.","zh":"競爭動物群體被淘汰後，恐龍能夠蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"To flourish means to grow, succeed or develop very well.","zh":"flourish 指生長、成功或發展得非常好。"},{"en":"A student may flourish in a smaller class where teachers can give more attention.","zh":"學生在較小班級中可能蓬勃發展，因為老師能給更多關注。"},{"en":"Species flourish when food, space and conditions support their growth.","zh":"當食物、空間和條件支持增長，物種會蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"This word describes strong success or healthy development.","zh":"這個字描述強勢成功或健康發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"competition had been knocked out","meaning":"競爭者已被淘汰","examples":[{"en":"Dinosaurs expanded rapidly after the competition had been knocked out.","zh":"競爭者被淘汰後，恐龍迅速擴張。"},{"en":"Competition had been knocked out means rival groups had been removed or defeated.","zh":"competition had been knocked out 指競爭群體已被移除或擊敗。"},{"en":"A small café may grow quickly after nearby competitors close down.","zh":"附近競爭者關門後，小咖啡店可能迅速成長。"},{"en":"When competition disappears, remaining groups can access more resources.","zh":"當競爭消失，剩餘群體可以取得更多資源。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and suggests competitors were eliminated.","zh":"這個短語較口語，暗示競爭者被消除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"leave the question of","meaning":"留下……這個問題","examples":[{"en":"The theory leaves the question of where the impact occurred.","zh":"這個理論留下撞擊發生地點這個問題。"},{"en":"To leave the question of something means to leave that issue unanswered or unresolved.","zh":"leave the question of something 指讓某議題仍未有答案或未解決。"},{"en":"A school report may explain falling grades but leave the question of student stress unanswered.","zh":"學校報告可能解釋成績下降，但留下學生壓力這個問題。"},{"en":"A theory can solve one problem while leaving another question open.","zh":"一個理論可以解決一個問題，同時留下另一個問題。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a remaining uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語引出仍存在的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the Earth’s crust","meaning":"地殼","examples":[{"en":"No obvious crater of the correct age has been found in the Earth’s crust.","zh":"地殼中尚未發現年代正確的明顯隕石坑。"},{"en":"The Earth’s crust is the outer solid layer of the planet.","zh":"Earth’s crust 指地球最外層的固體部分。"},{"en":"A geography lesson may compare the Earth’s crust with the mantle beneath it.","zh":"地理課可能把地殼與其下方的地幔作比較。"},{"en":"Craters, mountains and faults can be preserved or changed within the crust.","zh":"隕石坑、山脈和斷層可以在地殼中被保存或改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the hard outer part of Earth.","zh":"這個短語指地球堅硬的外層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"may have been overlooked","meaning":"可能已被忽略","examples":[{"en":"The ancient impact crater may have been overlooked.","zh":"古代撞擊坑可能已被忽略。"},{"en":"May have been overlooked means may not have been noticed or recognised.","zh":"may have been overlooked 指可能未被注意或辨認出來。"},{"en":"A teacher’s helpful comment may have been overlooked in a long email.","zh":"老師有用的評論可能在長電郵中被忽略。"},{"en":"Evidence can be overlooked when it is buried, damaged or not expected.","zh":"當證據被掩埋、受損或出乎意料，它可能被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible missed discovery.","zh":"這個短語描述可能錯過的發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be eroded and buried","meaning":"被侵蝕和掩埋","examples":[{"en":"Old craters are often eroded and buried.","zh":"古老隕石坑常被侵蝕和掩埋。"},{"en":"To be eroded and buried means to be worn away and then covered by rock, soil or sediment.","zh":"be eroded and buried 指被磨蝕，然後被岩石、泥土或沉積物覆蓋。"},{"en":"An old road may be eroded by rain and buried under mud.","zh":"舊路可能被雨水侵蝕，並被泥土掩埋。"},{"en":"Erosion and burial can make ancient features hard to recognise.","zh":"侵蝕和掩埋可以令古代特徵難以辨認。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how physical evidence disappears from view.","zh":"這個短語描述實體證據如何從視線中消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"not always easy to find","meaning":"並非總是容易找到","examples":[{"en":"Ancient impact craters are not always easy to find.","zh":"古代撞擊坑並非總是容易找到。"},{"en":"Not always easy to find means sometimes difficult to locate or identify.","zh":"not always easy to find 指有時難以定位或識別。"},{"en":"A small error in an essay is not always easy to find after reading it many times.","zh":"作文中的小錯誤讀了很多次後，並非總是容易找到。"},{"en":"Things become hard to find when they are hidden, damaged or mixed with similar objects.","zh":"當東西被隱藏、受損或與相似物混在一起，就會難以找到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical difficulty, not impossibility.","zh":"這個短語描述實際困難，而不是不可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"alternatively","meaning":"另一種可能是","examples":[{"en":"Alternatively, the crater may have disappeared completely.","zh":"另一種可能是，隕石坑可能已完全消失。"},{"en":"Alternatively means another possible explanation or choice is being introduced.","zh":"alternatively 指引入另一個可能解釋或選擇。"},{"en":"We can take the bus; alternatively, we can walk if the weather is good.","zh":"我們可以乘巴士；另一種可能是，如果天氣好就步行。"},{"en":"Writers use this word when offering a different possibility.","zh":"作者提出不同可能性時會使用這個字。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise alternative explanations.","zh":"這個短語有助組織替代解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"may have vanished","meaning":"可能已經消失","examples":[{"en":"The impact site may have vanished because of crustal recycling.","zh":"撞擊地點可能因地殼循環而已經消失。"},{"en":"May have vanished means may have disappeared completely.","zh":"may have vanished 指可能已完全消失。"},{"en":"A missing file may have vanished after the computer was reset.","zh":"電腦重設後，遺失檔案可能已經消失。"},{"en":"Evidence may vanish when natural processes destroy or cover it.","zh":"當自然過程摧毀或覆蓋證據時，證據可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes possible disappearance.","zh":"這個短語描述可能的消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"continental crust","meaning":"大陸地殼","examples":[{"en":"The continental crust is relatively permanent.","zh":"大陸地殼相對永久。"},{"en":"Continental crust is the thick part of Earth’s crust that forms the continents.","zh":"continental crust 指形成大陸的較厚地殼部分。"},{"en":"A geography teacher may compare continental crust with oceanic crust.","zh":"地理老師可能把大陸地殼與海洋地殼作比較。"},{"en":"Continental crust preserves old rocks because it is not recycled as quickly as the ocean floor.","zh":"大陸地殼保存古老岩石，因為它不像海床那樣快速被循環更新。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the crust beneath landmasses.","zh":"這個短語指陸地大塊下方的地殼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"more or less permanent","meaning":"大致上永久存在","examples":[{"en":"The continental crust is more or less permanent.","zh":"大陸地殼大致上永久存在。"},{"en":"More or less permanent means almost permanent, though not absolutely unchanging.","zh":"more or less permanent 指幾乎永久，但並非絕對不變。"},{"en":"A school building may be more or less permanent, unlike temporary classroom tents.","zh":"校舍可能大致上永久存在，不像臨時課室帳篷。"},{"en":"This phrase allows a small exception while making a broad point.","zh":"這個短語容許小例外，同時作出大致說法。"},{"en":"It means stable for a very long time, not literally forever.","zh":"它指長時間穩定，而不是字面永遠不變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"ocean floor","meaning":"海床","examples":[{"en":"The ocean floor is continuously renewed by geological activity.","zh":"海床不斷因地質活動而更新。"},{"en":"The ocean floor is the solid surface beneath the oceans.","zh":"ocean floor 指海洋下方的固體表面。"},{"en":"A map of the ocean floor may show ridges, trenches and underwater mountains.","zh":"海床地圖可能顯示洋脊、海溝和海底山脈。"},{"en":"New ocean floor forms in some places while old floor is destroyed elsewhere.","zh":"新海床在某些地方形成，而舊海床在其他地方被摧毀。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the seabed on a geological scale.","zh":"這個短語指地質尺度上的海底。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be constantly recycled","meaning":"不斷被循環更新","examples":[{"en":"The ocean floor is constantly recycled by tectonic processes.","zh":"海床不斷被地殼構造過程循環更新。"},{"en":"To be constantly recycled means to be repeatedly created, destroyed and replaced.","zh":"be constantly recycled 指反覆被創造、摧毀和取代。"},{"en":"Plastic bottles can be constantly recycled only if collection systems work well.","zh":"只有回收系統運作良好，膠樽才可不斷被循環再用。"},{"en":"Oceanic crust is recycled when it forms at ridges and sinks at trenches.","zh":"海洋地殼在洋脊形成並在海溝下沉時被循環更新。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated renewal rather than simple reuse.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆更新，而不是簡單再用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"tectonic processes","meaning":"地殼構造過程","examples":[{"en":"Tectonic processes continually create and destroy oceanic crust.","zh":"地殼構造過程不斷創造和摧毀海洋地殼。"},{"en":"Tectonic processes are movements and changes involving Earth’s crustal plates.","zh":"tectonic processes 指涉及地殼板塊的移動和變化。"},{"en":"Earthquakes and mountain building are connected with tectonic processes.","zh":"地震和造山作用與地殼構造過程有關。"},{"en":"These processes can move continents, recycle ocean floor and destroy old craters.","zh":"這些過程可以移動大陸、更新海床並摧毀古老隕石坑。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to large-scale geological movement.","zh":"這個短語指大規模地質運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"bring about continental drift","meaning":"引起大陸漂移","examples":[{"en":"Tectonic processes bring about continental drift.","zh":"地殼構造過程引起大陸漂移。"},{"en":"To bring about continental drift means to cause continents to move slowly over geological time.","zh":"bring about continental drift 指造成大陸在地質時間中緩慢移動。"},{"en":"A geography model may show how plate movement brings about continental drift.","zh":"地理模型可能展示板塊運動如何引起大陸漂移。"},{"en":"Continental drift happens because tectonic plates move beneath and around the continents.","zh":"大陸漂移發生，是因為板塊在大陸下方和周圍移動。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with the movement of continents.","zh":"這個短語把原因與大陸移動連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"continental drift","meaning":"大陸漂移","examples":[{"en":"Continental drift results from the movement of tectonic plates.","zh":"大陸漂移源自板塊移動。"},{"en":"Continental drift is the slow movement of continents across Earth’s surface over millions of years.","zh":"continental drift 指大陸在數百萬年間於地球表面緩慢移動。"},{"en":"Students may study continental drift to understand why South America and Africa look like matching pieces.","zh":"學生可能研究大陸漂移，以理解為何南美洲和非洲看起來像可拼合的兩塊。"},{"en":"Drift changes oceans, climates and the positions of landmasses.","zh":"漂移改變海洋、氣候和陸塊位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very slow geological movement.","zh":"這個短語描述非常緩慢的地質移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be swallowed up","meaning":"被吞沒","examples":[{"en":"An ocean crater may have been swallowed up by crustal movement.","zh":"海洋隕石坑可能已被地殼運動吞沒。"},{"en":"To be swallowed up means to be absorbed, covered or destroyed so that it disappears.","zh":"be swallowed up 指被吸收、覆蓋或摧毀，以致消失。"},{"en":"A small village may be swallowed up by a growing city.","zh":"小村莊可能被不斷擴張的城市吞沒。"},{"en":"Geological movement can swallow up evidence by carrying old crust beneath the surface.","zh":"地質運動可以把舊地殼帶入地表以下，從而吞沒證據。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests complete disappearance into something larger.","zh":"這個短語暗示完全消失於更大事物之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"by now","meaning":"到現在為止","examples":[{"en":"A crater in ancient oceanic crust would have disappeared by now.","zh":"古代海洋地殼中的隕石坑到現在為止應已消失。"},{"en":"By now means by the present time or by this point.","zh":"by now 指到現在或到目前這一點為止。"},{"en":"If the bus left early, it should be at the station by now.","zh":"如果巴士早已開出，它現在應該已到車站。"},{"en":"This phrase compares what should have happened with the time that has passed.","zh":"這個短語把應已發生的事與已過去的時間作比較。"},{"en":"It is useful when making an expectation about the present.","zh":"對現在情況作出預期時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a third possibility","meaning":"第三種可能性","examples":[{"en":"A third possibility is that the correct crater has been misdated.","zh":"第三種可能性是正確的隕石坑年代被錯誤測定。"},{"en":"A third possibility means another possible explanation after two have already been considered.","zh":"a third possibility 指在已有兩種可能解釋後提出的另一種可能。"},{"en":"If a student is absent, one possibility is illness, another is transport trouble, and a third possibility is a family emergency.","zh":"如果學生缺席，一種可能是生病，另一種是交通問題，第三種可能是家庭緊急情況。"},{"en":"Offering several possibilities helps readers see that the answer is uncertain.","zh":"提出幾種可能性幫助讀者看見答案仍不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase organises alternative explanations.","zh":"這個短語用來組織替代解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be known but misdated","meaning":"已被發現但年代測定錯誤","examples":[{"en":"The impact crater may already be known but misdated.","zh":"該撞擊坑可能已被發現，但年代測定錯誤。"},{"en":"To be known but misdated means to have been discovered, but assigned the wrong age.","zh":"be known but misdated 指已被發現，但被判定為錯誤年代。"},{"en":"A historical photograph may be known but misdated if the year written on it is wrong.","zh":"如果歷史照片上寫的年份錯了，它可能已被發現但年代標錯。"},{"en":"Misdating can hide connections between evidence and events.","zh":"年代錯誤可以隱藏證據與事件之間的關聯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an object that is identified but placed in the wrong time.","zh":"這個短語描述已被識別但被放在錯誤時間中的物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be thought to be","meaning":"被認為是……","examples":[{"en":"The Manicouagan structure is thought to be 214 million years old.","zh":"Manicouagan 結構被認為已有二億一千四百萬年歷史。"},{"en":"To be thought to be something means people believe or estimate that it is so.","zh":"be thought to be something 指人們相信或估計某事如此。"},{"en":"An old temple is thought to be over 500 years old.","zh":"一座古廟被認為已有五百多年歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase shows belief or estimation, not absolute certainty.","zh":"這個短語顯示信念或估計，而不是絕對確定。"},{"en":"It is common in scientific and historical writing.","zh":"它常見於科學和歷史寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"some 100 kilometres across","meaning":"直徑約一百公里","examples":[{"en":"The crater is some 100 kilometres across.","zh":"該隕石坑直徑約一百公里。"},{"en":"Some 100 kilometres across means approximately 100 kilometres wide from one side to the other.","zh":"some 100 kilometres across 指從一邊到另一邊約一百公里寬。"},{"en":"A storm system some 100 kilometres across can affect several towns at once.","zh":"一個直徑約一百公里的風暴系統可以同時影響幾個城鎮。"},{"en":"The word some here means about, not an unknown group of things.","zh":"這裡的 some 意思是「約」，不是不明數量的一些東西。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate size.","zh":"這個短語給出近似大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the largest of between three and five craters","meaning":"三至五個隕石坑中最大的一個","examples":[{"en":"Manicouagan may be the largest of several related craters.","zh":"Manicouagan 可能是幾個相關隕石坑中最大的一個。"},{"en":"The largest of between three and five craters means the biggest crater among a small group of three to five.","zh":"largest of between three and five craters 指三至五個隕石坑小群體中最大的一個。"},{"en":"In a school garden, one pond may be the largest of three small ponds.","zh":"在學校花園中，一個池塘可能是三個小池塘中最大的一個。"},{"en":"Comparing size helps scientists decide which impact feature was most important.","zh":"比較大小幫助科學家判斷哪個撞擊特徵最重要。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies one item as the biggest within a limited group.","zh":"這個短語指出某項目是有限群體中最大的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"form within a few hours of each other","meaning":"在相隔數小時內形成","examples":[{"en":"The craters may have formed within a few hours of each other.","zh":"這些隕石坑可能在相隔數小時內形成。"},{"en":"To form within a few hours of each other means to be created almost at the same time.","zh":"form within a few hours of each other 指幾乎在同一時間形成。"},{"en":"Several complaints may arrive within a few hours of each other after a school app fails.","zh":"學校應用程式故障後，幾宗投訴可能在相隔數小時內到達。"},{"en":"Close timing can suggest that events shared the same cause.","zh":"時間接近可以暗示事件有共同原因。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses near-simultaneous occurrence.","zh":"這個短語強調幾乎同時發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"lumps of a disintegrated comet","meaning":"一顆解體彗星的碎塊","examples":[{"en":"The craters may have been made by lumps of a disintegrated comet.","zh":"這些隕石坑可能由一顆解體彗星的碎塊造成。"},{"en":"Lumps of a disintegrated comet are broken pieces of a comet that has fallen apart.","zh":"lumps of a disintegrated comet 指已解體彗星的破碎部分。"},{"en":"A cracked biscuit can break into lumps, just as a comet can break into fragments.","zh":"一塊裂開的餅乾可以碎成幾塊，就像彗星可以碎成碎片。"},{"en":"If several pieces hit Earth, they may create several craters close in time.","zh":"如果幾塊碎片撞擊地球，它們可能在接近時間形成幾個隕石坑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fragments from a comet that broke apart.","zh":"這個短語描述來自解體彗星的碎片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"hit the Earth one by one","meaning":"逐一撞擊地球","examples":[{"en":"The comet fragments may have hit the Earth one by one.","zh":"彗星碎片可能逐一撞擊地球。"},{"en":"To hit the Earth one by one means to strike the planet separately in sequence.","zh":"hit the Earth one by one 指按次序分別撞擊地球。"},{"en":"Raindrops hit a window one by one before the rain becomes heavy.","zh":"雨滴在大雨前會逐一打在窗上。"},{"en":"Separate impacts can create several craters rather than one single crater.","zh":"分開撞擊可以形成幾個隕石坑，而不是單一隕石坑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated impacts in order.","zh":"這個短語描述按次序反覆撞擊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"perceptible effect on","meaning":"對……產生可察覺的影響","examples":[{"en":"Such a major impact should have had a perceptible effect on the world.","zh":"如此重大的撞擊應對世界產生可察覺的影響。"},{"en":"A perceptible effect on something is an effect that can be noticed or measured.","zh":"perceptible effect on something 指可被注意或量度的影響。"},{"en":"A new bus route may have a perceptible effect on traffic near a school.","zh":"新巴士路線可能對學校附近交通產生可察覺影響。"},{"en":"If an event is large enough, its effects should leave visible or measurable signs.","zh":"如果事件足夠大，其影響應留下可見或可量度跡象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an impact that is not hidden or trivial.","zh":"這個短語描述並非隱藏或微不足道的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"record an event","meaning":"記錄某事件","examples":[{"en":"Rocks of the correct age should record such a major event.","zh":"年代正確的岩石應記錄如此重大的事件。"},{"en":"To record an event means to preserve evidence that the event happened.","zh":"record an event 指保存某事件曾發生的證據。"},{"en":"A school logbook may record an event such as a fire drill or special visit.","zh":"學校日誌可能記錄消防演習或特別探訪等事件。"},{"en":"Rocks can record events through chemicals, fossils, layers or damage patterns.","zh":"岩石可以透過化學物質、化石、層理或破壞模式記錄事件。"},{"en":"This phrase means to preserve information, not necessarily to write it down.","zh":"這個短語意思是保存資訊，不一定是寫下來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"it is possible that","meaning":"有可能……","examples":[{"en":"It is possible that the Manicouagan crater has been dated incorrectly.","zh":"有可能 Manicouagan 隕石坑的年代被錯誤測定。"},{"en":"It is possible that means something may be true, though it is not certain.","zh":"it is possible that 指某事可能是真的，但未確定。"},{"en":"It is possible that a student missed the message because the email went to spam.","zh":"有可能學生錯過訊息，因為電郵進入垃圾郵件夾。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a cautious explanation or hypothesis.","zh":"這個短語引出謹慎解釋或假設。"},{"en":"It is useful when evidence is not strong enough for certainty.","zh":"當證據不足以確定時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the next thing to check","meaning":"下一項要查證的事情","examples":[{"en":"The crater’s age will be the next thing to check.","zh":"該隕石坑的年代將是下一項要查證的事情。"},{"en":"The next thing to check means the next detail or question that should be examined.","zh":"next thing to check 指下一個應檢查的細節或問題。"},{"en":"If a computer will not connect to the internet, the next thing to check is the Wi-Fi password.","zh":"如果電腦連不上網，下一項要查證的事情是 Wi-Fi 密碼。"},{"en":"Researchers identify the next thing to check when one uncertainty blocks progress.","zh":"當一個不確定因素阻礙進展，研究者會找出下一項要查證的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the next practical step in investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述調查中的下一個實際步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agree with the views of","meaning":"與作者觀點一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether each statement agrees with the writer’s views.","zh":"考生判斷每項陳述是否與作者觀點一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the views of someone means to match what that person thinks or argues.","zh":"agree with the views of someone 指與某人的想法或論點相符。"},{"en":"In a reading test, a statement agrees with the writer only if the passage clearly supports it.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，只有篇章清楚支持某陳述，它才與作者觀點一致。"},{"en":"Students should use textual evidence rather than personal opinion.","zh":"學生應使用文本證據，而不是個人意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in Yes, No, Not Given questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 Yes, No, Not Given 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與作者觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the writer’s views.","zh":"一項陳述可能與作者觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what that person believes or argues.","zh":"contradict the views of someone 指說出與某人信念或論點相反的意思。"},{"en":"A statement contradicts the writer if the passage clearly says the opposite.","zh":"如果篇章清楚說出相反內容，該陳述就與作者觀點矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be based on evidence, not assumption.","zh":"矛盾必須基於證據，而不是假設。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear conflict with an opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述與某觀點的清楚衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Write “NOT GIVEN” when it is impossible to determine the writer’s view.","zh":"當無法判斷作者觀點時，寫 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資料作出判斷。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions a crater’s size, it is impossible to say how wide it is.","zh":"如果篇章從未提到隕石坑大小，就無法判斷它有多寬。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when the text gives no evidence.","zh":"當文本沒有證據時，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase explains uncertainty caused by missing information.","zh":"這個短語解釋因資料缺失造成的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lead to the dinosaurs’ rise","meaning":"導致恐龍崛起","examples":[{"en":"An asteroid strike may have led to the dinosaurs’ rise.","zh":"小行星撞擊可能導致恐龍崛起。"},{"en":"To lead to the dinosaurs’ rise means to cause dinosaurs to become more dominant and widespread.","zh":"lead to the dinosaurs’ rise 指造成恐龍變得更具主導地位並更廣泛分布。"},{"en":"A school policy may lead to better attendance if it solves transport problems.","zh":"如果學校政策解決交通問題，它可能導致出席率改善。"},{"en":"One event can lead to a major change when it removes old obstacles.","zh":"當一件事移除舊障礙，它可以導致重大變化。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with dinosaur dominance.","zh":"這個短語把原因與恐龍主導地位連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"exaggerate the size of","meaning":"誇大……的體型","examples":[{"en":"Popular films may exaggerate the size of some animals.","zh":"流行電影可能誇大某些動物的體型。"},{"en":"To exaggerate the size of something means to make it seem larger than it really is.","zh":"exaggerate the size of something 指令某物看起來比實際更大。"},{"en":"An advertisement may exaggerate the size of a burger to attract customers.","zh":"廣告可能誇大漢堡包大小來吸引顧客。"},{"en":"Exaggeration can create excitement but may reduce accuracy.","zh":"誇大可以製造刺激感，但可能降低準確性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making size appear unrealistically large.","zh":"這個短語描述把大小呈現得不切實際地大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"provide adequate evidence","meaning":"提供足夠證據","examples":[{"en":"Footprints can provide adequate evidence about dinosaur size.","zh":"足跡可以提供關於恐龍體型的足夠證據。"},{"en":"To provide adequate evidence means to give enough proof to support a conclusion.","zh":"provide adequate evidence 指提供足以支持結論的證據。"},{"en":"A student provides adequate evidence when an essay uses clear examples from the text.","zh":"學生在作文中使用文本清楚例子時，就是提供足夠證據。"},{"en":"Adequate evidence may be enough for one question, even if it does not answer everything.","zh":"足夠證據可能足以回答一個問題，即使不能回答所有問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence that is sufficient for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述對某目的而言足夠的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"more useful than","meaning":"比……更有用","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether footprints were more useful than magnetic evidence.","zh":"題目問足跡是否比磁性證據更有用。"},{"en":"More useful than means better or more helpful for a particular purpose.","zh":"more useful than 指對某特定目的較好或較有幫助。"},{"en":"A timetable may be more useful than a long email when students need quick information.","zh":"當學生需要快速資訊，時間表可能比長電郵更有用。"},{"en":"Usefulness depends on the question people are trying to answer.","zh":"有用程度取決於人們試圖回答甚麼問題。"},{"en":"This phrase compares practical value.","zh":"這個短語比較實際價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"date geological material","meaning":"測定地質物質的年代","examples":[{"en":"Magnetic evidence helps scientists date geological material.","zh":"磁性證據幫助科學家測定地質物質的年代。"},{"en":"To date geological material means to estimate the age of rocks, sediments or fossils.","zh":"date geological material 指估計岩石、沉積物或化石的年代。"},{"en":"Scientists may date volcanic ash to learn when an eruption happened.","zh":"科學家可能測定火山灰年代，以了解火山爆發何時發生。"},{"en":"Dating material helps researchers place events in the correct order.","zh":"測定物質年代幫助研究者把事件放在正確次序中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finding the age of Earth materials.","zh":"這個短語描述找出地球物質年齡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"to within a few thousand years","meaning":"誤差在數千年以內","examples":[{"en":"The rocks can be dated to within a few thousand years.","zh":"這些岩石可以被測定至誤差在數千年以內。"},{"en":"To within a few thousand years means with an error range no larger than several thousand years.","zh":"to within a few thousand years 指誤差範圍不超過數千年。"},{"en":"An ancient settlement may be dated to within a few decades if records are good.","zh":"如果記錄良好，古代聚落可能被定年至誤差數十年以內。"},{"en":"Smaller error ranges make historical or geological comparisons more precise.","zh":"較小誤差範圍令歷史或地質比較更精確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accuracy in dating.","zh":"這個短語描述定年準確度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"provide exact information about","meaning":"提供有關……的確切資料","examples":[{"en":"Footprints do not always provide exact information about species.","zh":"足跡不一定總能提供有關物種的確切資料。"},{"en":"To provide exact information about something means to give precise details about it.","zh":"provide exact information about something 指提供關於某事的精確細節。"},{"en":"A receipt can provide exact information about the price and date of a purchase.","zh":"收據可以提供有關購買價格和日期的確切資料。"},{"en":"Some evidence gives useful clues without providing exact details.","zh":"有些證據提供有用線索，但不提供精確細節。"},{"en":"This phrase separates precise information from general indication.","zh":"這個短語把精確資料與一般指標分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the Earth’s surface","meaning":"地球表面","examples":[{"en":"Iridium is uncommon at the Earth’s surface.","zh":"銥在地球表面並不常見。"},{"en":"The Earth’s surface is the outer visible layer of the planet, including land and ocean floor.","zh":"Earth’s surface 指地球外部可見層，包括陸地和海床。"},{"en":"Mountains, rivers, cities and deserts all exist on the Earth’s surface.","zh":"山脈、河流、城市和沙漠都存在於地球表面。"},{"en":"Materials rare at the surface may become important clues when found in unusual amounts.","zh":"在地表罕見的物質若以異常數量被發現，可能成為重要線索。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the outside of Earth, not its deep interior.","zh":"這個短語指地球外部，而不是深層內部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the following summary","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the following summary using words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the following summary means to fill the blanks in a short version of the text.","zh":"complete the following summary 指填補文本簡短版本中的空格。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete a summary by choosing exact words from the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過從文章選擇原字來完成摘要。"},{"en":"Summary completion checks whether students understand main ideas and key details.","zh":"摘要填充題檢查學生是否理解主要思想和關鍵細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個詞","examples":[{"en":"Each summary answer must contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個摘要答案必須不多於兩個詞。"},{"en":"No more than two words means one or two words only, not three or more.","zh":"no more than two words 指只可用一個或兩個詞，不能三個或以上。"},{"en":"If the answer is “ancient rocks,” it follows the rule, but “the ancient rocks” does not.","zh":"如果答案是 “ancient rocks”，就符合規則；但 “the ancient rocks” 不符合。"},{"en":"Word limits matter because extra words can make an answer wrong.","zh":"字數限制很重要，因為多寫字可能令答案錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"apply a phenomenon to explain","meaning":"運用一種現象來解釋","examples":[{"en":"The researchers applied a biological phenomenon to explain the increase in size.","zh":"研究者運用一種生物現象來解釋體型增大。"},{"en":"To apply a phenomenon to explain something means to use a known process as an explanation.","zh":"apply a phenomenon to explain something 指用已知過程作為某事的解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may apply the idea of habit formation to explain why daily revision works.","zh":"老師可能運用習慣形成這個概念來解釋每日溫習為何有效。"},{"en":"Applying a known pattern helps make an unusual event easier to understand.","zh":"運用已知模式有助令人更容易理解不尋常事件。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a general process with a specific case.","zh":"這個短語把一般過程與具體個案連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be similar to what happens","meaning":"與現今發生的情況相似","examples":[{"en":"The ancient process may be similar to what happens on islands today.","zh":"古代過程可能與現今島嶼上發生的情況相似。"},{"en":"To be similar to what happens means to resemble a process or event seen elsewhere.","zh":"be similar to what happens 指與其他地方所見的過程或事件相似。"},{"en":"A child’s classroom behaviour may be similar to what happens at home when routines change.","zh":"當常規改變時，孩子在課室的行為可能與家中發生的情況相似。"},{"en":"Comparing similar processes helps people understand unfamiliar situations.","zh":"比較相似過程幫助人理解陌生情況。"},{"en":"This phrase links one case with another comparable case.","zh":"這個短語把一個個案與另一個可比較個案連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"indigenous lizards","meaning":"本土蜥蜴","examples":[{"en":"Indigenous lizards on Komodo have developed unusually large bodies.","zh":"科莫多島上的本土蜥蜴已發展出異常巨大的身體。"},{"en":"Indigenous lizards are lizards native to a particular place.","zh":"indigenous lizards 指原生於某特定地方的蜥蜴。"},{"en":"A nature guide may explain how indigenous lizards differ from introduced species.","zh":"自然導賞員可能解釋本土蜥蜴如何不同於外來物種。"},{"en":"Native animals can evolve special features when they live in isolated environments.","zh":"本土動物生活在孤立環境中時，可以演化出特殊特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to local original species, not animals brought from elsewhere.","zh":"這個短語指當地原生物種，而不是從其他地方帶來的動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"refer to something as","meaning":"把……稱為……","examples":[{"en":"People refer to the giant Komodo lizards as dragons.","zh":"人們把巨型科莫多蜥蜴稱為巨龍。"},{"en":"To refer to something as something else means to call or describe it by that name.","zh":"refer to something as something else 指以某名稱稱呼或描述某物。"},{"en":"Students may refer to a difficult exam as a nightmare.","zh":"學生可能把困難考試稱為噩夢。"},{"en":"Names can show how people feel about an object, animal or event.","zh":"名稱可以顯示人們對物件、動物或事件的感受。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the label people use.","zh":"這個短語引出人們使用的標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"traces of an old impact","meaning":"古代撞擊的痕跡","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have not found clear traces of the ancient impact.","zh":"科學家尚未找到古代撞擊的清楚痕跡。"},{"en":"Traces of an old impact are remaining signs that a collision happened long ago.","zh":"traces of an old impact 指很久以前碰撞發生後留下的跡象。"},{"en":"A cracked wall may contain traces of an old earthquake.","zh":"裂開的牆可能包含古代地震的痕跡。"},{"en":"Traces can be hard to find if erosion and burial have changed the surface.","zh":"如果侵蝕和掩埋已改變地表，痕跡可能難以找到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes leftover evidence from a past collision.","zh":"這個短語描述過去碰撞留下的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"overlook the evidence","meaning":"忽略證據","examples":[{"en":"Researchers may simply have overlooked the evidence.","zh":"研究者可能只是忽略了證據。"},{"en":"To overlook the evidence means to fail to notice or properly consider it.","zh":"overlook the evidence 指未能注意或適當考慮證據。"},{"en":"A student may overlook evidence in a passage if they read too quickly.","zh":"如果學生讀得太快，可能忽略文章中的證據。"},{"en":"Evidence is easily overlooked when people already expect a different answer.","zh":"當人們已預期另一個答案，證據很容易被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase describes missing information that could matter.","zh":"這個短語描述錯過可能重要的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be difficult to spot","meaning":"難以察覺","examples":[{"en":"Old craters can be difficult to spot after erosion and burial.","zh":"古老隕石坑經侵蝕和掩埋後可能難以察覺。"},{"en":"To be difficult to spot means to be hard to see, notice or identify.","zh":"be difficult to spot 指難以看見、注意或識別。"},{"en":"A small spelling mistake can be difficult to spot in a long essay.","zh":"長作文中的小串字錯誤可能難以察覺。"},{"en":"Things become difficult to spot when they are hidden or look like their surroundings.","zh":"當東西被隱藏或看起來像周圍環境，就會難以察覺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual or practical difficulty in detection.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺上或實際偵測上的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"vanish because of","meaning":"因……而消失","examples":[{"en":"An ocean crater may vanish because of tectonic activity.","zh":"海洋隕石坑可能因地殼構造活動而消失。"},{"en":"To vanish because of something means to disappear as a result of that cause.","zh":"vanish because of something 指由於某原因而消失。"},{"en":"Chalk writing may vanish because of rain.","zh":"粉筆字可能因下雨而消失。"},{"en":"Evidence can vanish because of natural processes that destroy or cover it.","zh":"證據可能因摧毀或覆蓋它的自然過程而消失。"},{"en":"This phrase links disappearance with its cause.","zh":"這個短語把消失與其原因連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"crustal movement","meaning":"地殼運動","examples":[{"en":"Crustal movement continually reshapes the Earth’s surface.","zh":"地殼運動不斷重塑地球表面。"},{"en":"Crustal movement is the movement of the Earth’s outer solid layer.","zh":"crustal movement 指地球外層固體部分的移動。"},{"en":"Earthquakes can result from sudden crustal movement along faults.","zh":"地震可以由斷層上突然的地殼運動造成。"},{"en":"Over long periods, crustal movement can lift mountains or destroy ocean floor.","zh":"長時間下，地殼運動可以抬升山脈或摧毀海床。"},{"en":"This phrase describes geological movement in the Earth’s crust.","zh":"這個短語描述地殼中的地質運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be swallowed by","meaning":"被……吞沒","examples":[{"en":"An oceanic crater may be swallowed by tectonic processes.","zh":"海洋隕石坑可能被地殼構造過程吞沒。"},{"en":"To be swallowed by something means to be taken in, covered or destroyed by it.","zh":"be swallowed by something 指被某物吸收、覆蓋或摧毀。"},{"en":"A small path may be swallowed by weeds if no one clears it.","zh":"如果沒有人清理，小路可能被雜草吞沒。"},{"en":"Geological features can be swallowed by crustal movement over millions of years.","zh":"地質特徵可以在數百萬年間被地殼運動吞沒。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests disappearing into a larger process or object.","zh":"這個短語暗示消失於較大過程或物體之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be misdated","meaning":"年代被錯誤測定","examples":[{"en":"Some known craters may have been misdated.","zh":"有些已知隕石坑的年代可能被錯誤測定。"},{"en":"To be misdated means to be given the wrong age or date.","zh":"be misdated 指被給予錯誤年代或日期。"},{"en":"A historical letter may be misdated if the writer wrote the wrong year.","zh":"如果作者寫錯年份，歷史信件可能年代被標錯。"},{"en":"Misdated evidence can make scientists connect it to the wrong event.","zh":"年代錯誤的證據可以令科學家把它連到錯誤事件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an error in dating, not an error in location.","zh":"這個短語描述定年錯誤，而不是位置錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 139 - The Dinosaurs Footprints and Extinction.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 140":[{"front":"Digital Diet","meaning":"數碼節能方案","examples":[{"en":"A digital diet involves reducing the energy and environmental costs of computing.","zh":"數碼節能方案涉及減少運算的能源和環境成本。"},{"en":"A digital diet is a plan to use digital devices, websites and online services in a less wasteful way.","zh":"數碼節能方案是指以較不浪費的方式使用數碼裝置、網站和網上服務。"},{"en":"A school can start a digital diet by switching off unused computers after lessons.","zh":"學校可以在課後關掉不用的電腦，開始實行數碼節能方案。"},{"en":"A digital diet can lower electricity bills and reduce carbon emissions from technology use.","zh":"數碼節能方案可以降低電費，並減少科技使用帶來的碳排放。"},{"en":"This phrase is about making digital life cleaner, not about avoiding technology completely.","zh":"這個短語關於令數碼生活更環保，而不是完全避免科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"telecommuting","meaning":"遙距工作","examples":[{"en":"Telecommuting can reduce the need for employees to travel to an office.","zh":"遙距工作可以減少員工前往辦公室的需要。"},{"en":"Telecommuting means working from home or another location by using digital communication tools.","zh":"telecommuting 指透過數碼通訊工具在家中或其他地點工作。"},{"en":"An office worker may use telecommuting twice a week instead of taking the train to work.","zh":"辦公室員工可能每星期遙距工作兩天，而不是乘火車上班。"},{"en":"Telecommuting can save travel time, reduce traffic and lower fuel use.","zh":"遙距工作可以節省通勤時間、減少交通流量並降低燃料使用。"},{"en":"It works best when employees have reliable Internet and clear communication with their teams.","zh":"當員工有穩定網絡並與團隊清楚溝通時，遙距工作最有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Internet shopping","meaning":"網上購物","examples":[{"en":"Internet shopping may save some of the energy used by traditional retailing.","zh":"網上購物可能節省傳統零售所使用的部分能源。"},{"en":"Internet shopping means buying goods or services through websites or apps.","zh":"Internet shopping 指透過網站或應用程式購買商品或服務。"},{"en":"A family may use Internet shopping to order groceries instead of driving to several shops.","zh":"家庭可能使用網上購物訂購雜貨，而不是駕車到幾間商店。"},{"en":"Internet shopping can reduce some travel, but delivery and packaging still use resources.","zh":"網上購物可以減少部分交通，但送貨和包裝仍會使用資源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to online buying rather than visiting a physical shop.","zh":"這個短語指網上購買，而不是親身到實體店。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"online meetings","meaning":"網上會議","examples":[{"en":"Online meetings can replace some business trips and face-to-face gatherings.","zh":"網上會議可以取代部分商務旅程和面對面聚會。"},{"en":"Online meetings are meetings held through video calls or digital communication platforms.","zh":"online meetings 指透過視像通話或數碼通訊平台舉行的會議。"},{"en":"A teacher may hold online meetings with parents who cannot come to school.","zh":"老師可能與不能到校的家長舉行網上會議。"},{"en":"Online meetings can save travel time and reduce transport-related emissions.","zh":"網上會議可以節省交通時間，並減少與交通相關的排放。"},{"en":"They are useful for discussion, but some sensitive conversations may still work better in person.","zh":"它們適合討論，但有些敏感對話仍可能較適合親身進行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"save energy","meaning":"節省能源","examples":[{"en":"Digital services may save energy compared with some in-person alternatives.","zh":"與某些親身進行的替代方式相比，數碼服務可能節省能源。"},{"en":"To save energy means to use less electricity, fuel or power.","zh":"save energy 指使用較少電力、燃料或能量。"},{"en":"A household can save energy by turning off lights in empty rooms.","zh":"家庭可以透過關掉空房間的燈來節省能源。"},{"en":"Saving energy can lower bills and reduce pollution from power generation.","zh":"節省能源可以降低賬單，並減少發電造成的污染。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when an action reduces the amount of energy needed.","zh":"當某行動減少所需能源量時，就會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Online meetings may use less energy compared with international business travel.","zh":"與國際商務旅行相比，網上會議可能使用較少能源。"},{"en":"Compared with means when one thing is considered beside another thing.","zh":"compared with 指把一件事與另一件事放在一起考慮。"},{"en":"Compared with taking a taxi, walking to school costs nothing and gives exercise.","zh":"與乘的士相比，步行上學不用花錢，還能運動。"},{"en":"Comparisons help people judge which option is cheaper, cleaner or more practical.","zh":"比較幫助人判斷哪個選項較便宜、較環保或較實際。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing contrast between two choices.","zh":"這個短語適合用來顯示兩個選擇之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in-person alternatives","meaning":"親身進行的替代方式","examples":[{"en":"Video conferences can replace some in-person alternatives.","zh":"視像會議可以取代某些親身進行的替代方式。"},{"en":"In-person alternatives are options that require people to meet physically in the same place.","zh":"in-person alternatives 指需要人們親身在同一地方見面的選項。"},{"en":"An online parent meeting can replace the in-person alternative of travelling to school.","zh":"網上家長會可以取代親身前往學校這種替代方式。"},{"en":"Replacing in-person alternatives may save time, transport costs and emissions.","zh":"取代親身方式可能節省時間、交通費和排放。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts physical attendance with digital participation.","zh":"這個短語把親身出席與數碼參與作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as the digital age moves on","meaning":"隨着數碼時代發展","examples":[{"en":"As the digital age moves on, its environmental impact is becoming clearer.","zh":"隨着數碼時代發展，其環境影響變得更清楚。"},{"en":"As the digital age moves on means as modern digital technology continues to develop over time.","zh":"as the digital age moves on 指隨着現代數碼科技隨時間繼續發展。"},{"en":"As the digital age moves on, students use more cloud storage, video lessons and online tests.","zh":"隨着數碼時代發展，學生使用更多雲端儲存、視像課堂和網上測驗。"},{"en":"More digital activity can create new convenience but also higher electricity demand.","zh":"更多數碼活動可以帶來新便利，但也會提高用電需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a continuing technological period, not one single invention.","zh":"這個短語描述一個持續的科技時代，而不是單一發明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"green reputation","meaning":"環保形象","examples":[{"en":"The technology industry once enjoyed a strong green reputation.","zh":"科技業曾經享有強烈的環保形象。"},{"en":"A green reputation is the public image of being environmentally friendly.","zh":"green reputation 指被公眾視為環保的形象。"},{"en":"A restaurant gains a green reputation when it reduces plastic waste and saves water.","zh":"餐廳減少塑膠廢物並節約用水時，會建立環保形象。"},{"en":"If a company uses too much electricity, its green reputation may weaken.","zh":"如果公司用電太多，其環保形象可能削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how environmentally responsible people think an organisation is.","zh":"這個短語描述人們認為某組織有多環保負責。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"turn a lot browner","meaning":"變得沒有那麼環保","examples":[{"en":"The digital industry’s green reputation is turning a lot browner.","zh":"數碼行業的環保形象正變得沒有那麼環保。"},{"en":"To turn a lot browner means to become much less environmentally friendly in public perception.","zh":"turn a lot browner 指在公眾觀感中變得遠沒有那麼環保。"},{"en":"A “green” delivery service may turn browner if it uses many polluting vans.","zh":"如果「綠色」送貨服務使用大量污染貨車，它的形象可能變得不那麼環保。"},{"en":"A reputation turns browner when hidden energy use or emissions become visible.","zh":"當隱藏能源使用或排放變得可見，形象就會變得較不環保。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the idea of “green” with a less clean reality.","zh":"這個短語把「綠色」形象與較不潔淨的現實作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"e-mailing","meaning":"使用電郵","examples":[{"en":"E-mailing requires electricity to power computers, networks and servers.","zh":"使用電郵需要電力來供應電腦、網絡和伺服器。"},{"en":"E-mailing means sending and receiving messages electronically through the Internet.","zh":"e-mailing 指透過互聯網以電子方式收發訊息。"},{"en":"Office workers may spend hours e-mailing clients, colleagues and suppliers every day.","zh":"辦公室員工每天可能花數小時使用電郵聯絡客戶、同事和供應商。"},{"en":"E-mailing saves paper and postage, but it still depends on electricity and data centres.","zh":"使用電郵節省紙張和郵費，但仍依賴電力和數據中心。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to digital communication by e-mail.","zh":"這個短語指透過電郵進行數碼溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"number crunching","meaning":"大量數據運算","examples":[{"en":"Number crunching can require substantial computing power.","zh":"大量數據運算可能需要相當大的運算能力。"},{"en":"Number crunching means processing large amounts of numerical data.","zh":"number crunching 指處理大量數字數據。"},{"en":"A school may use number crunching to analyse exam results across different classes.","zh":"學校可能使用大量數據運算來分析不同班級的考試成績。"},{"en":"Heavy number crunching can make computers work harder and use more electricity.","zh":"大量數據運算可以令電腦運作更繁重並使用更多電力。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for data analysis, statistics and financial calculations.","zh":"這個短語常用於數據分析、統計和財務計算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"web searches","meaning":"網頁搜尋","examples":[{"en":"Billions of web searches consume a significant amount of electricity.","zh":"數以十億計的網頁搜尋消耗相當多電力。"},{"en":"Web searches are searches for information on the Internet using a search engine.","zh":"web searches 指使用搜尋引擎在互聯網上尋找資料。"},{"en":"A student does web searches to find articles for a science project.","zh":"學生進行網頁搜尋，為科學項目尋找文章。"},{"en":"Each search seems tiny, but millions of searches together require servers and power.","zh":"每次搜尋看似微小，但數以百萬計搜尋合起來需要伺服器和電力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordinary online searching that still has an energy cost.","zh":"這個短語描述普通網上搜尋，但它仍有能源成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"consume as much as","meaning":"消耗多達……","examples":[{"en":"Digital activities can consume as much electricity as some industries.","zh":"數碼活動可以消耗多達某些行業的電力。"},{"en":"To consume as much as something means to use an equal or similar amount.","zh":"consume as much as something 指使用相等或相近的數量。"},{"en":"A large air conditioner may consume as much electricity as several smaller fans.","zh":"一部大型冷氣機可能消耗多達幾部小風扇的電力。"},{"en":"This comparison can surprise people because small daily actions add up.","zh":"這種比較可能令人驚訝，因為小型日常行動會累積起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing that one thing uses more resources than expected.","zh":"這個短語適合顯示某事使用的資源比預期更多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"kilowatt-hours","meaning":"千瓦小時；度電","examples":[{"en":"Electricity use is often measured in kilowatt-hours.","zh":"電力使用量常以千瓦小時量度。"},{"en":"Kilowatt-hours are units used to measure how much electrical energy is used over time.","zh":"kilowatt-hours 是用來量度一段時間內使用了多少電能的單位。"},{"en":"A household electricity bill shows how many kilowatt-hours the family used in a month.","zh":"家庭電費單會顯示該家庭一個月用了多少度電。"},{"en":"More kilowatt-hours usually mean higher electricity costs and greater energy demand.","zh":"千瓦小時越多，通常代表電費越高和能源需求越大。"},{"en":"This phrase is a standard way to talk about electricity consumption.","zh":"這個短語是談論用電量的標準方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the nation’s electricity","meaning":"全國用電量","examples":[{"en":"Computing accounted for a measurable share of the nation’s electricity use.","zh":"運算佔全國用電量中可量度的一部分。"},{"en":"The nation’s electricity means all the electricity used in a country.","zh":"the nation’s electricity 指一個國家使用的所有電力。"},{"en":"Factories, homes, schools and transport systems all use part of the nation’s electricity.","zh":"工廠、家庭、學校和交通系統都使用全國用電量的一部分。"},{"en":"If computing uses more of the nation’s electricity, energy planning becomes more important.","zh":"如果運算使用更多全國用電量，能源規劃就變得更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to electricity consumption at country level.","zh":"這個短語指國家層面的電力消耗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"half of which","meaning":"其中一半","examples":[{"en":"The country uses large amounts of electricity, half of which may come from coal.","zh":"該國使用大量電力，其中一半可能來自燃煤。"},{"en":"Half of which means fifty per cent of the thing just mentioned.","zh":"half of which 指剛提到事物的百分之五十。"},{"en":"The school bought 100 tablets, half of which were used in science lessons.","zh":"學校購買了 100 部平板電腦，其中一半用於科學課。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an amount with extra information about one half of it.","zh":"這個短語把某個數量與其中一半的額外資料連接起來。"},{"en":"It is useful in formal writing when adding detail after a comma.","zh":"它適合在正式寫作中於逗號後加入細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"come from coal","meaning":"來自燃煤","examples":[{"en":"A large proportion of electricity still comes from coal.","zh":"很大比例的電力仍來自燃煤。"},{"en":"To come from coal means to be generated by burning coal for energy.","zh":"come from coal 指透過燃燒煤炭產生能源而發電。"},{"en":"A city’s electricity may come from coal if its power plants burn coal to produce power.","zh":"如果城市的發電廠燃燒煤炭發電，其電力就可能來自燃煤。"},{"en":"Electricity from coal can create large amounts of carbon dioxide.","zh":"來自燃煤的電力可以造成大量二氧化碳。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies coal as the energy source behind the electricity.","zh":"這個短語指出煤炭是電力背後的能源來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"eat up energy","meaning":"大量消耗能源","examples":[{"en":"The world’s computers eat up enormous quantities of energy.","zh":"全球電腦大量消耗能源。"},{"en":"To eat up energy means to use a large amount of energy quickly or continuously.","zh":"eat up energy 指快速或持續使用大量能源。"},{"en":"Old air conditioners can eat up energy during a hot summer.","zh":"舊冷氣機在炎熱夏天可以大量消耗能源。"},{"en":"Devices that eat up energy increase electricity bills and environmental pressure.","zh":"大量耗能的裝置會增加電費和環境壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and suggests wasteful or heavy consumption.","zh":"這個短語較口語，暗示浪費或高消耗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"double by","meaning":"到……時增加一倍","examples":[{"en":"Computer energy consumption was expected to double by 2010.","zh":"電腦能源消耗預計到 2010 年時增加一倍。"},{"en":"To double by a time means to become twice as large before or at that time.","zh":"double by a time 指在某時間前或到某時間時變成兩倍。"},{"en":"A school’s online storage needs may double by next year if every class uploads videos.","zh":"如果每班都上載影片，學校的網上儲存需求可能到明年增加一倍。"},{"en":"When energy use doubles, costs and emissions can rise sharply.","zh":"當能源使用增加一倍，成本和排放可能急升。"},{"en":"This phrase links growth with a deadline or future point.","zh":"這個短語把增長與期限或未來時間點連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"if present trends continue","meaning":"如果目前趨勢持續","examples":[{"en":"Energy use will rise sharply if present trends continue.","zh":"如果目前趨勢持續，能源使用將急劇上升。"},{"en":"If present trends continue means if current patterns keep going in the same direction.","zh":"if present trends continue 指如果目前模式繼續朝同一方向發展。"},{"en":"If present trends continue, more students will submit homework through online platforms.","zh":"如果目前趨勢持續，更多學生會透過網上平台交功課。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when making predictions based on existing data.","zh":"這個短語常用於根據現有數據作預測。"},{"en":"It warns that today’s pattern can create tomorrow’s problem.","zh":"它提醒今天的模式可以造成明天的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"According to Jonathan Koomey, computer energy use was rising rapidly.","zh":"根據 Jonathan Koomey，電腦能源使用正在快速上升。"},{"en":"According to means based on what a person, source or report says.","zh":"according to 指根據某人、來源或報告所說。"},{"en":"According to the school notice, the library will close early on Friday.","zh":"根據學校通告，圖書館星期五會提早關閉。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to show where information comes from.","zh":"作者使用這個短語來顯示資訊來源。"},{"en":"This phrase should be followed by a clear source, not just a vague claim.","zh":"這個短語後面應有清楚來源，而不是模糊說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"staff scientist","meaning":"研究機構科學家","examples":[{"en":"Jonathan Koomey worked as a staff scientist at a national laboratory.","zh":"Jonathan Koomey 在一所國家實驗室擔任研究機構科學家。"},{"en":"A staff scientist is a scientist employed by an organisation to conduct research as part of its regular team.","zh":"staff scientist 指受某機構聘用、作為固定團隊成員進行研究的科學家。"},{"en":"A hospital may hire a staff scientist to study patient data and improve treatment methods.","zh":"醫院可能聘請研究機構科學家來研究病人數據並改善治療方法。"},{"en":"Staff scientists provide expert knowledge and long-term research support.","zh":"研究機構科學家提供專業知識和長期研究支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a professional research role inside an institution.","zh":"這個短語描述機構內的專業研究職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory","meaning":"勞倫斯伯克利國家實驗室","examples":[{"en":"Research on computing energy use was conducted at Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory.","zh":"有關運算能源使用的研究在勞倫斯伯克利國家實驗室進行。"},{"en":"Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory is a major research laboratory in the United States.","zh":"Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory 是美國一所重要研究實驗室。"},{"en":"A scientist working at Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory may study energy, climate or computing.","zh":"在勞倫斯伯克利國家實驗室工作的科學家可能研究能源、氣候或運算。"},{"en":"Research from national laboratories can influence public policy and industry practice.","zh":"國家實驗室的研究可以影響公共政策和行業做法。"},{"en":"This phrase names the institution connected with the research.","zh":"這個短語命名與研究相關的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, companies have both financial and environmental reasons to save energy.","zh":"因此，公司有財務和環保兩方面的理由去節省能源。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what has just been described.","zh":"as a result 指因為剛描述的事情。"},{"en":"The classroom lights were left on all night; as a result, the electricity bill increased.","zh":"課室燈整晚沒有關；因此，電費增加了。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with its consequence.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"},{"en":"It helps readers follow the logic from one sentence to the next.","zh":"它幫助讀者跟上句子之間的邏輯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"power bill","meaning":"電費開支","examples":[{"en":"The power bill for running a computer may exceed its purchase price.","zh":"運行電腦的電費開支可能超過其購買價格。"},{"en":"A power bill is the amount of money paid for electricity use.","zh":"power bill 指為用電而支付的金額。"},{"en":"A family’s power bill may rise if several air conditioners run every night.","zh":"如果幾部冷氣機每晚運作，家庭電費開支可能上升。"},{"en":"High power bills encourage people and companies to use energy more carefully.","zh":"高電費會鼓勵人和公司更謹慎地使用能源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to electricity cost, not the price of the device itself.","zh":"這個短語指電力成本，而不是裝置本身的價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"run a computer","meaning":"運行電腦","examples":[{"en":"Electricity is required to run a computer throughout its working life.","zh":"電腦在整個工作壽命中都需要電力來運行。"},{"en":"To run a computer means to power it and keep it operating.","zh":"run a computer 指為電腦供電並使其運作。"},{"en":"A school needs electricity to run computers in the library every day.","zh":"學校每天需要電力來運行圖書館的電腦。"},{"en":"Running a computer for long hours increases energy use and heat.","zh":"長時間運行電腦會增加能源使用和熱量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the power needed to make a computer work.","zh":"這個短語描述使電腦運作所需的電力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"over its lifetime","meaning":"在其整個使用期內","examples":[{"en":"A computer may consume a great deal of energy over its lifetime.","zh":"電腦在其整個使用期內可能消耗大量能源。"},{"en":"Over its lifetime means during the whole period that something is used or exists.","zh":"over its lifetime 指在某物被使用或存在的整個期間。"},{"en":"A washing machine may cost more in electricity over its lifetime than at purchase.","zh":"洗衣機在整個使用期內的電費可能比購買價更高。"},{"en":"Looking at lifetime cost helps buyers see hidden long-term expenses.","zh":"查看整個使用期成本有助買家看見隱藏的長期開支。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on total use, not only the first day or first year.","zh":"這個短語著重總使用量，而不只是第一天或第一年。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"surpass the cost of","meaning":"超過……的成本","examples":[{"en":"The lifetime electricity bill may surpass the cost of buying the machine.","zh":"整個使用期的電費可能超過購買該機器的成本。"},{"en":"To surpass the cost of something means to become greater than that cost.","zh":"surpass the cost of something 指變得高於某成本。"},{"en":"Repairing an old printer may surpass the cost of buying a new one.","zh":"維修舊打印機的費用可能超過購買新打印機的成本。"},{"en":"If running costs surpass the purchase price, efficiency becomes very important.","zh":"如果運行成本超過購買價，能源效益就變得非常重要。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two costs and shows one is higher.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種成本，並顯示其中一種較高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the first place","meaning":"最初；本來","examples":[{"en":"Electricity may eventually cost more than buying the computer in the first place.","zh":"電力最終可能比最初購買電腦花費更多。"},{"en":"In the first place means originally or at the beginning.","zh":"in the first place 指最初或一開始。"},{"en":"A student may regret joining a course if they did not need it in the first place.","zh":"如果學生本來不需要某課程，之後可能後悔報讀。"},{"en":"This phrase often looks back to the original decision or starting point.","zh":"這個短語常回顧最初決定或起點。"},{"en":"It helps compare what happened later with what was true at the start.","zh":"它幫助比較後來發生的事與開始時的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a business reason to","meaning":"做……的商業理由","examples":[{"en":"Rising electricity bills give companies a business reason to improve efficiency.","zh":"上升的電費給公司改善效率的商業理由。"},{"en":"A business reason to do something is a practical financial or commercial motive for doing it.","zh":"business reason to do something 指做某事的實際財務或商業動機。"},{"en":"A shop has a business reason to reduce waste if waste disposal becomes expensive.","zh":"如果處理廢物變得昂貴，商店就有減少浪費的商業理由。"},{"en":"Companies act faster when saving energy also saves money.","zh":"當節省能源同時節省金錢，公司會更快行動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the motive is not only moral but also commercial.","zh":"這個短語顯示動機不只是道德上的，也是商業上的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cut energy costs","meaning":"削減能源成本","examples":[{"en":"Technology companies are seeking ways to cut energy costs.","zh":"科技公司正在尋找方法削減能源成本。"},{"en":"To cut energy costs means to reduce the amount of money spent on electricity or fuel.","zh":"cut energy costs 指減少花在電力或燃料上的金錢。"},{"en":"A school can cut energy costs by using LED lights and switching off unused projectors.","zh":"學校可以透過使用 LED 燈和關掉不用的投影機來削減能源成本。"},{"en":"Cutting energy costs can make a business more profitable and environmentally responsible.","zh":"削減能源成本可以令企業更有利潤，也更有環保責任。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on reducing spending linked to energy use.","zh":"這個短語著重減少與能源使用相關的開支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"以及；同時","examples":[{"en":"Energy efficiency provides an economic benefit as well as an environmental one.","zh":"能源效益提供經濟好處，也提供環境好處。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to another thing.","zh":"as well as 指除了另一事物之外，也包括某事。"},{"en":"A good bicycle route saves money as well as improving health.","zh":"良好單車路線節省金錢，同時改善健康。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two benefits or features exist together.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩種好處或特色同時存在。"},{"en":"It is useful when one action has more than one positive result.","zh":"當一個行動有多於一個正面結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"environmental reason","meaning":"環保理由","examples":[{"en":"Reducing energy use is both a business and an environmental objective.","zh":"減少能源使用既是商業目標，也是環保目標。"},{"en":"An environmental reason is a reason connected with protecting nature or reducing harm to the planet.","zh":"environmental reason 指與保護自然或減少對地球傷害有關的理由。"},{"en":"A family may stop using plastic bags for an environmental reason.","zh":"家庭可能基於環保理由停止使用膠袋。"},{"en":"Environmental reasons become stronger when pollution, waste or emissions are clearly reduced.","zh":"當污染、廢物或排放明顯減少，環保理由就更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why an action is good for the natural world.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何某行動對自然世界有益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"one of the biggest energy sinks","meaning":"最大能源消耗項目之一","examples":[{"en":"Cooling equipment is one of the biggest energy sinks in a data centre.","zh":"冷卻設備是數據中心最大能源消耗項目之一。"},{"en":"One of the biggest energy sinks means one of the main things that uses a lot of energy.","zh":"one of the biggest energy sinks 指其中一個大量消耗能源的主要項目。"},{"en":"In a shopping mall, air conditioning may be one of the biggest energy sinks.","zh":"在商場中，冷氣可能是最大能源消耗項目之一。"},{"en":"Energy sinks raise costs because they use power continuously or heavily.","zh":"能源消耗項目因持續或大量用電而提高成本。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where much of the energy is being consumed.","zh":"這個短語指出大量能源被消耗在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not from…but from…","meaning":"不是來自……而是來自……","examples":[{"en":"Much of the energy use comes not from computers but from cooling systems.","zh":"很多能源使用不是來自電腦，而是來自冷卻系統。"},{"en":"Not from A but from B means the real source is B, not A.","zh":"not from A but from B 指真正來源是 B，而不是 A。"},{"en":"The delay came not from poor planning but from a sudden train breakdown.","zh":"延誤不是來自規劃差，而是來自突然的火車故障。"},{"en":"This structure corrects a possible misunderstanding about the cause.","zh":"這個結構糾正對原因的可能誤解。"},{"en":"It is useful when the obvious answer is not the true answer.","zh":"當表面答案不是真正答案時，這個結構很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"computers themselves","meaning":"電腦本身","examples":[{"en":"The computers themselves are not the only source of energy consumption.","zh":"電腦本身並不是能源消耗的唯一來源。"},{"en":"Computers themselves means the actual computer machines, not the surrounding equipment or systems.","zh":"computers themselves 指實際的電腦機器，而不是周邊設備或系統。"},{"en":"In a computer room, the computers themselves use power, but lights and cooling also use power.","zh":"在電腦室中，電腦本身用電，但燈光和冷卻也用電。"},{"en":"Focusing only on computers themselves may ignore hidden energy costs.","zh":"只集中於電腦本身可能忽略隱藏能源成本。"},{"en":"This phrase separates the machines from everything that supports them.","zh":"這個短語把機器與支援它們的一切分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"air conditioning","meaning":"冷氣系統","examples":[{"en":"Air conditioning is needed to prevent servers from becoming too hot.","zh":"需要冷氣系統來防止伺服器變得太熱。"},{"en":"Air conditioning is a system that cools and controls the temperature of indoor air.","zh":"air conditioning 指冷卻並控制室內空氣溫度的系統。"},{"en":"A classroom uses air conditioning during summer so students can study comfortably.","zh":"課室在夏天使用冷氣系統，讓學生舒適地學習。"},{"en":"Air conditioning can protect machines and people, but it also consumes electricity.","zh":"冷氣系統可以保護機器和人，但也會消耗電力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to cooling equipment used inside buildings.","zh":"這個短語指建築物內使用的冷卻設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"keep something from overheating","meaning":"防止……過熱","examples":[{"en":"Cooling systems keep computer servers from overheating.","zh":"冷卻系統防止電腦伺服器過熱。"},{"en":"To keep something from overheating means to stop it from becoming dangerously hot.","zh":"keep something from overheating 指阻止某物變得危險地熱。"},{"en":"A laptop stand with a fan can keep a computer from overheating during video editing.","zh":"有風扇的手提電腦架可以在剪片時防止電腦過熱。"},{"en":"If equipment overheats, it may slow down, shut off or become damaged.","zh":"如果設備過熱，可能變慢、關機或受損。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the protective purpose of cooling.","zh":"這個短語解釋冷卻的保護用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"for every kilowatt-hour","meaning":"每使用一千瓦小時","examples":[{"en":"For every kilowatt-hour used for computing, another may be used for cooling.","zh":"每使用一千瓦小時進行運算，可能另需一千瓦小時用於冷卻。"},{"en":"For every kilowatt-hour means each time one unit of electrical energy is used.","zh":"for every kilowatt-hour 指每使用一個電能單位。"},{"en":"For every kilowatt-hour used by classroom computers, extra energy may be used by air conditioning.","zh":"課室電腦每使用一度電，冷氣可能也使用額外能源。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare energy used for one purpose with energy used for another.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較某用途和另一用途的能源使用。"},{"en":"It often appears in calculations and efficiency discussions.","zh":"它常出現在計算和效率討論中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be required to cool","meaning":"需要用來冷卻……","examples":[{"en":"Additional electricity is required to cool the server equipment.","zh":"需要額外電力來冷卻伺服器設備。"},{"en":"To be required to cool something means to be needed in order to reduce its temperature.","zh":"be required to cool something 指需要某物來降低其溫度。"},{"en":"Extra fans may be required to cool a crowded classroom on a hot day.","zh":"炎熱日子裡，擠迫課室可能需要額外風扇來冷卻。"},{"en":"More heat usually means more energy is required to cool the space.","zh":"熱量越多，通常需要更多能源來冷卻空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes energy needed for temperature control.","zh":"這個短語描述溫度控制所需的能源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"furnace-like","meaning":"像火爐般灼熱的","examples":[{"en":"Rows of operating servers can become furnace-like without effective cooling.","zh":"如果沒有有效冷卻，一排排運作中的伺服器可以變得像火爐般灼熱。"},{"en":"Furnace-like means extremely hot, like a furnace or oven.","zh":"furnace-like 指極熱，像火爐或焗爐一樣。"},{"en":"A closed car can feel furnace-like after sitting in the sun for hours.","zh":"汽車在陽光下停放數小時後，車內可能像火爐般灼熱。"},{"en":"Furnace-like conditions can damage equipment and make rooms unsafe to work in.","zh":"像火爐般灼熱的環境可以損壞設備，並令房間不適合工作。"},{"en":"This word describes intense, uncomfortable heat.","zh":"這個詞描述強烈、令人不舒服的熱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"racks of servers","meaning":"一排排伺服器機架","examples":[{"en":"Large data centres contain extensive racks of servers.","zh":"大型數據中心有大量一排排伺服器機架。"},{"en":"Racks of servers are rows or frames holding many server computers together.","zh":"racks of servers 指放置許多伺服器電腦的排架或框架。"},{"en":"A university data room may have racks of servers storing research files and student records.","zh":"大學數據室可能有一排排伺服器機架，儲存研究文件和學生紀錄。"},{"en":"More racks of servers usually mean more computing power and more cooling needs.","zh":"更多伺服器機架通常代表更多運算能力和更多冷卻需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical arrangement of servers in data centres.","zh":"這個短語描述數據中心中伺服器的實體排列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Internet giant","meaning":"互聯網巨企","examples":[{"en":"Google is an Internet giant with enormous computing requirements.","zh":"Google 是一家有巨大運算需求的互聯網巨企。"},{"en":"An Internet giant is a very large and powerful company that provides online services.","zh":"Internet giant 指提供網上服務、規模和影響力都很大的公司。"},{"en":"An Internet giant may run search engines, cloud storage, video platforms or online shops.","zh":"互聯網巨企可能經營搜尋引擎、雲端儲存、影片平台或網店。"},{"en":"Internet giants need huge data centres because millions of people use their services daily.","zh":"互聯網巨企需要巨大數據中心，因為每天有數以百萬計的人使用其服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes scale and influence in the online world.","zh":"這個短語描述網上世界中的規模和影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"this reality has driven efforts","meaning":"這種現實促使人們採取行動","examples":[{"en":"High energy use has driven efforts to develop cleaner power sources.","zh":"高能源使用促使人們努力開發更潔淨的能源來源。"},{"en":"This reality has driven efforts means this situation has pushed people to take action.","zh":"this reality has driven efforts 指這種情況推動人們採取行動。"},{"en":"Rising school electricity bills have driven efforts to install LED lights.","zh":"學校電費上升促使人們努力安裝 LED 燈。"},{"en":"When a problem becomes expensive or visible, it often drives efforts to find solutions.","zh":"當問題變得昂貴或明顯，就常會促使人們努力尋找解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase links a real problem with action taken in response.","zh":"這個短語把真實問題與回應行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"installation of","meaning":"……的安裝","examples":[{"en":"The company invested in the installation of a large solar array.","zh":"該公司投資安裝大型太陽能板陣列。"},{"en":"The installation of something means putting equipment in place so it can be used.","zh":"installation of something 指把設備安置好，使其可以使用。"},{"en":"The installation of new classroom projectors took place during the summer holiday.","zh":"新課室投影機的安裝在暑假期間進行。"},{"en":"Installation can require money at first, but it may reduce costs later.","zh":"安裝起初可能需要金錢，但之後可能降低成本。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to setting up equipment, not merely buying it.","zh":"這個短語指設置設備，而不只是購買設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"solar array","meaning":"太陽能板陣列","examples":[{"en":"A solar array can provide part of a building’s electricity needs.","zh":"太陽能板陣列可以提供建築物部分用電需求。"},{"en":"A solar array is a group of solar panels arranged together to generate electricity.","zh":"solar array 指一組排列在一起、用來發電的太陽能板。"},{"en":"A school roof may hold a solar array that powers lights in the library.","zh":"學校屋頂可能有太陽能板陣列，為圖書館燈光供電。"},{"en":"Solar arrays reduce reliance on electricity from fossil fuels when sunlight is available.","zh":"當有陽光時，太陽能板陣列能減少對化石燃料電力的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a collection of solar panels, not one small panel alone.","zh":"這個短語指一組太陽能板，而不是單一小型板。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"provide 30 per cent of","meaning":"提供百分之三十的……","examples":[{"en":"The installation can provide 30 per cent of peak power demand.","zh":"該裝置可以提供用電高峰需求的百分之三十。"},{"en":"To provide 30 per cent of something means to supply nearly one third of the total amount needed.","zh":"provide 30 per cent of something 指供應所需總量中接近三分之一。"},{"en":"A school solar system may provide 30 per cent of daytime electricity use.","zh":"學校太陽能系統可能提供日間用電量的百分之三十。"},{"en":"Supplying 30 per cent can still make a big difference when total demand is high.","zh":"當總需求很高，供應百分之三十仍能帶來很大差異。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a precise share of supply.","zh":"這個短語給出精確的供應比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"peak power needs","meaning":"用電高峰需求","examples":[{"en":"The solar system helps meet the headquarters’ peak power needs.","zh":"太陽能系統有助滿足總部的用電高峰需求。"},{"en":"Peak power needs are the highest levels of electricity demand during the busiest or most energy-intensive times.","zh":"peak power needs 指在最繁忙或最耗能時段的最高用電需求。"},{"en":"A shopping mall’s peak power needs may occur on hot weekend afternoons.","zh":"商場的用電高峰需求可能出現在炎熱週末下午。"},{"en":"Meeting peak power needs is difficult because demand rises suddenly and strongly.","zh":"滿足用電高峰需求很困難，因為需求會突然大幅上升。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to maximum electricity demand, not average use.","zh":"這個短語指最高用電需求，而不是平均用電量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"headquarters","meaning":"總部","examples":[{"en":"The company installed renewable-energy technology at its headquarters.","zh":"該公司在總部安裝可再生能源技術。"},{"en":"Headquarters is the main office or central base of an organisation.","zh":"headquarters 指組織的主要辦公室或中央基地。"},{"en":"A charity’s headquarters may coordinate branches in different districts.","zh":"慈善機構總部可能協調不同地區的分部。"},{"en":"Decisions made at headquarters can affect offices, shops or workers everywhere.","zh":"總部作出的決定可以影響各地辦公室、店舖或員工。"},{"en":"This word refers to the central place from which an organisation is managed.","zh":"這個詞指組織被管理的中央地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"increased purchases of","meaning":"增加購買……","examples":[{"en":"The company also made increased purchases of renewable energy.","zh":"該公司也增加購買可再生能源。"},{"en":"Increased purchases of something means buying more of it than before.","zh":"increased purchases of something 指比以前購買更多某物。"},{"en":"A school made increased purchases of recycled paper after changing its environmental policy.","zh":"學校改變環保政策後，增加購買再造紙。"},{"en":"Increased purchases can support suppliers and show a stronger commitment to a product.","zh":"增加購買可以支持供應商，並顯示對產品更強承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth in buying activity.","zh":"這個短語描述購買活動增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"renewable energy","meaning":"可再生能源","examples":[{"en":"Renewable energy includes solar, wind and geothermal power.","zh":"可再生能源包括太陽能、風能和地熱能。"},{"en":"Renewable energy comes from sources that can naturally replenish, such as sunlight, wind and heat from the Earth.","zh":"renewable energy 來自可自然補充的來源，例如陽光、風和地球熱能。"},{"en":"A school may use renewable energy by installing solar panels on its roof.","zh":"學校可能透過在屋頂安裝太陽能板來使用可再生能源。"},{"en":"Using renewable energy can reduce dependence on coal, oil and gas.","zh":"使用可再生能源可以減少對煤、石油和天然氣的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts cleaner energy sources with fossil fuels.","zh":"這個短語把較潔淨能源與化石燃料作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"deliver web pages within seconds","meaning":"在數秒內提供網頁","examples":[{"en":"Search companies must deliver web pages within seconds.","zh":"搜尋公司必須在數秒內提供網頁。"},{"en":"To deliver web pages within seconds means to show online results very quickly after a user requests them.","zh":"deliver web pages within seconds 指在用戶要求後非常快速地顯示網上結果。"},{"en":"Students expect search engines to deliver web pages within seconds when they look up homework information.","zh":"學生查找功課資料時，期望搜尋引擎在數秒內提供網頁。"},{"en":"Fast delivery requires powerful servers, networks and energy.","zh":"快速提供服務需要強大伺服器、網絡和能源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the speed expected from modern online services.","zh":"這個短語描述現代網上服務被期望達到的速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"maintain hundreds of thousands of","meaning":"維持數以十萬計的……","examples":[{"en":"Google must maintain hundreds of thousands of computer servers.","zh":"Google 必須維持數以十萬計的電腦伺服器。"},{"en":"To maintain hundreds of thousands of something means to keep an extremely large number working properly.","zh":"maintain hundreds of thousands of something 指保持極大量事物正常運作。"},{"en":"A transport authority may maintain hundreds of thousands of street lights across a city.","zh":"交通部門可能維持城市中數以十萬計的街燈。"},{"en":"Maintaining so many machines requires staff, electricity, space and repairs.","zh":"維持如此多機器需要員工、電力、空間和維修。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses both scale and ongoing responsibility.","zh":"這個短語強調規模和持續責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"computer servers","meaning":"電腦伺服器","examples":[{"en":"Computer servers process and deliver information across the Internet.","zh":"電腦伺服器在互聯網上處理並傳送資訊。"},{"en":"Computer servers are powerful computers that store, process and send data to other computers.","zh":"computer servers 指儲存、處理並向其他電腦傳送數據的強大電腦。"},{"en":"A school server may store student files and allow teachers to access them.","zh":"學校伺服器可能儲存學生文件，並讓老師存取。"},{"en":"More online users create more work for computer servers.","zh":"更多網上用戶會為電腦伺服器創造更多工作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to machines that support websites, apps and digital services.","zh":"這個短語指支援網站、應用程式和數碼服務的機器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cavernous buildings","meaning":"巨大空曠的建築物","examples":[{"en":"Large server farms are housed in cavernous buildings.","zh":"大型伺服器場設於巨大空曠的建築物內。"},{"en":"Cavernous buildings are very large, open buildings that feel like caves because of their size.","zh":"cavernous buildings 指非常大型、開闊，因尺寸而像洞穴的建築物。"},{"en":"A huge warehouse with high ceilings may feel like a cavernous building.","zh":"高樓底的大型倉庫可能感覺像巨大空曠的建築物。"},{"en":"Data centres need cavernous buildings because they contain many servers and cooling systems.","zh":"數據中心需要巨大空曠的建築物，因為內有許多伺服器和冷卻系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a building that is vast and spacious inside.","zh":"這個短語描述內部廣闊寬敞的建築物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"server energy efficiency","meaning":"伺服器能源效益","examples":[{"en":"Server energy efficiency is a major concern for Internet companies.","zh":"伺服器能源效益是互聯網公司的重大關注。"},{"en":"Server energy efficiency means how much useful computing work servers produce for the electricity they use.","zh":"server energy efficiency 指伺服器每使用電力能產生多少有用運算工作。"},{"en":"A company improves server energy efficiency when the same website traffic uses less power.","zh":"當同樣網站流量使用較少電力，公司就改善了伺服器能源效益。"},{"en":"Better efficiency lowers operating costs and reduces emissions.","zh":"更高效益降低營運成本並減少排放。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on making server work less wasteful.","zh":"這個短語著重令伺服器工作較少浪費。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"actively work to","meaning":"積極致力於……","examples":[{"en":"Technology companies are actively working to reduce electricity consumption.","zh":"科技公司正積極致力於減少用電量。"},{"en":"To actively work to do something means to make direct and ongoing efforts to achieve it.","zh":"actively work to do something 指直接而持續地努力達成某事。"},{"en":"A school may actively work to reduce bullying by training teachers and educating students.","zh":"學校可能透過培訓老師和教育學生，積極致力於減少欺凌。"},{"en":"Active work suggests real action, not only public promises.","zh":"積極工作暗示真正行動，而不只是公開承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase shows deliberate effort toward a goal.","zh":"這個短語顯示朝目標作出的有意努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"maximise the efficiency of","meaning":"將……的效率提升至最高","examples":[{"en":"Google is working to maximise the efficiency of its data centres.","zh":"Google 正努力將其數據中心的效率提升至最高。"},{"en":"To maximise the efficiency of something means to make it work as well as possible with the least waste.","zh":"maximise the efficiency of something 指令某物以最少浪費盡可能有效運作。"},{"en":"A restaurant may maximise the efficiency of its kitchen by organising ingredients clearly.","zh":"餐廳可能透過清楚整理食材來將廚房效率提升至最高。"},{"en":"Maximising efficiency can reduce cost, time, energy and mistakes.","zh":"將效率最大化可以減少成本、時間、能源和錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improving performance to the highest practical level.","zh":"這個短語描述把表現提升至實際可行的最高水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"data centres","meaning":"數據中心","examples":[{"en":"Data centres contain the computing equipment needed to provide online services.","zh":"數據中心包含提供網上服務所需的運算設備。"},{"en":"Data centres are buildings or facilities that house servers, storage systems and networking equipment.","zh":"data centres 指放置伺服器、儲存系統和網絡設備的建築物或設施。"},{"en":"A bank may use data centres to store customer records and process online transactions.","zh":"銀行可能使用數據中心儲存客戶紀錄並處理網上交易。"},{"en":"Data centres need electricity, cooling and security to operate safely.","zh":"數據中心需要電力、冷卻和保安才能安全運作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the physical backbone of many digital services.","zh":"這個短語指許多數碼服務的實體骨幹。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"account for most of","meaning":"佔……的大部分","examples":[{"en":"Data centres account for most of the energy the company consumes.","zh":"數據中心佔公司能源消耗的大部分。"},{"en":"To account for most of something means to make up the largest share of it.","zh":"account for most of something 指構成某事物的最大比例。"},{"en":"Heating may account for most of a family’s winter electricity bill.","zh":"暖氣可能佔家庭冬季電費的大部分。"},{"en":"If one activity accounts for most energy use, improving it can create large savings.","zh":"如果一項活動佔大部分能源使用，改善它可以帶來大量節省。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to show the main source or share.","zh":"這個短語用來顯示主要來源或比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"worldwide","meaning":"在全球","examples":[{"en":"Large technology firms operate data centres worldwide.","zh":"大型科技公司在全球營運數據中心。"},{"en":"Worldwide means in many countries or across the whole world.","zh":"worldwide 指在許多國家或全世界範圍內。"},{"en":"A popular learning app may be used by students worldwide.","zh":"受歡迎的學習應用程式可能被全球學生使用。"},{"en":"Worldwide operations require planning across different time zones, climates and laws.","zh":"全球營運需要跨越不同時區、氣候和法律進行規劃。"},{"en":"This word stresses global reach.","zh":"這個詞強調全球範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"funnel profits into","meaning":"將利潤投放於……","examples":[{"en":"Google planned to funnel some of its profits into renewable-energy research.","zh":"Google 計劃將部分利潤投放於可再生能源研究。"},{"en":"To funnel profits into something means to direct money earned from business toward that activity.","zh":"funnel profits into something 指把業務賺到的錢引導投放到某活動。"},{"en":"A school book fair may funnel profits into buying new library books.","zh":"學校書展可能將利潤投放於購買新圖書館書籍。"},{"en":"Companies funnel profits into research when they want long-term benefits.","zh":"公司想獲得長期好處時，會將利潤投放於研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes channelling money into a chosen purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述把金錢導向選定用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a new effort","meaning":"新計劃；新行動","examples":[{"en":"The company launched a new effort to make clean energy more affordable.","zh":"該公司推出一項新計劃，使潔淨能源更可負擔。"},{"en":"A new effort is a fresh attempt or organised action to achieve a goal.","zh":"new effort 指為達成目標而作出的新嘗試或有組織行動。"},{"en":"A school may launch a new effort to reduce food waste in the canteen.","zh":"學校可能推出新行動，減少飯堂食物浪費。"},{"en":"New efforts often begin when older methods are not enough.","zh":"當舊方法不足夠時，新計劃常會開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a planned push to solve a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述為解決問題而作出的有計劃推動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be dubbed","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"The renewable-energy programme was dubbed RE<C.","zh":"該可再生能源計劃被稱為 RE<C。"},{"en":"To be dubbed something means to be given a particular name or label.","zh":"be dubbed something 指被賦予某個名稱或標籤。"},{"en":"A school recycling project may be dubbed “Green Friday”.","zh":"學校回收計劃可能被稱為 “Green Friday”。"},{"en":"A memorable name can make a programme easier to recognise and discuss.","zh":"易記名稱可以令計劃更容易被識別和討論。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when naming projects, people or ideas.","zh":"這個短語常用於命名項目、人物或想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"renewable energy cheaper than coal","meaning":"比煤炭更便宜的可再生能源","examples":[{"en":"The project aimed to make renewable energy cheaper than coal.","zh":"該項目旨在令可再生能源比煤炭更便宜。"},{"en":"Renewable energy cheaper than coal means clean energy costs less to produce or buy than coal-based energy.","zh":"renewable energy cheaper than coal 指潔淨能源的生產或購買成本低於燃煤能源。"},{"en":"If solar power becomes cheaper than coal, households may switch to cleaner electricity faster.","zh":"如果太陽能變得比煤炭更便宜，家庭可能更快轉用潔淨電力。"},{"en":"Lower renewable-energy prices can reduce pollution by making clean choices financially attractive.","zh":"較低的可再生能源價格可以透過令潔淨選擇在財務上更吸引而減少污染。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a cost comparison between clean energy and fossil fuel.","zh":"這個短語顯示潔淨能源與化石燃料之間的成本比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sources such as","meaning":"……等來源","examples":[{"en":"The project supported energy sources such as solar and wind power.","zh":"該項目支持太陽能和風能等能源來源。"},{"en":"Sources such as means examples of the type being discussed.","zh":"sources such as 指所討論類別中的例子。"},{"en":"Students can learn from online sources such as videos, articles and practice exercises.","zh":"學生可以從影片、文章和練習等網上來源學習。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples without claiming the list is complete.","zh":"這個短語引入例子，但不表示列表完整。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving representative examples.","zh":"當給出代表性例子時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"solar-thermal energy","meaning":"太陽熱能","examples":[{"en":"Solar-thermal energy uses sunlight to produce heat and electricity.","zh":"太陽熱能利用陽光產生熱和電力。"},{"en":"Solar-thermal energy is energy captured from the sun’s heat rather than directly from light alone.","zh":"solar-thermal energy 指從太陽熱力而不只是光本身取得的能源。"},{"en":"A building may use solar-thermal energy to heat water for showers.","zh":"建築物可能使用太陽熱能為淋浴熱水加熱。"},{"en":"Using solar heat can reduce the need for gas or electric water heating.","zh":"使用太陽熱可以減少對煤氣或電熱水的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to heat-based solar technology.","zh":"這個短語指以熱力為基礎的太陽能技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"high-altitude wind","meaning":"高空風能","examples":[{"en":"High-altitude wind may provide a powerful source of renewable energy.","zh":"高空風能可能提供強大的可再生能源來源。"},{"en":"High-altitude wind is wind found high above the ground, where it may be stronger or steadier.","zh":"high-altitude wind 指地面高處的風，可能更強或更穩定。"},{"en":"Engineers may study high-altitude wind to see whether flying turbines could generate electricity.","zh":"工程師可能研究高空風能，以了解飛行式渦輪能否發電。"},{"en":"Stronger winds can produce more power if technology can capture them safely.","zh":"如果技術能安全捕捉更強的風，就可以產生更多電力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to wind energy above normal tower height.","zh":"這個短語指高於普通塔架高度的風能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"geothermal energy","meaning":"地熱能","examples":[{"en":"Geothermal energy uses heat from beneath the Earth’s surface.","zh":"地熱能利用地球表面下方的熱力。"},{"en":"Geothermal energy is energy produced from natural heat inside the Earth.","zh":"geothermal energy 指由地球內部天然熱力產生的能源。"},{"en":"A town near volcanic activity may use geothermal energy to heat buildings.","zh":"火山活動附近的城鎮可能使用地熱能為建築物供暖。"},{"en":"Geothermal systems can provide steady power because underground heat is available day and night.","zh":"地熱系統可以提供穩定電力，因為地下熱力日夜都存在。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to energy from Earth’s internal heat.","zh":"這個短語指來自地球內部熱力的能源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"within years, not decades","meaning":"在數年而非數十年內","examples":[{"en":"The company hoped to achieve its goal within years, not decades.","zh":"該公司希望在數年而非數十年內達成目標。"},{"en":"Within years, not decades means in a few years rather than after many tens of years.","zh":"within years, not decades 指在幾年內，而不是在許多個十年之後。"},{"en":"A school may hope to improve its exam results within years, not decades.","zh":"學校可能希望在數年而非數十年內改善考試成績。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses urgency and ambition.","zh":"這個短語強調迫切性和抱負。"},{"en":"It contrasts a near-term goal with a very long wait.","zh":"它把短期目標與非常漫長的等待作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the meantime","meaning":"與此同時","examples":[{"en":"In the meantime, the computing industry is using practical methods to save energy.","zh":"與此同時，運算行業正使用實際方法來節省能源。"},{"en":"In the meantime means during the period before something else happens.","zh":"in the meantime 指在另一件事發生之前的期間。"},{"en":"The new library will open next year; in the meantime, students can use the study room.","zh":"新圖書館明年開放；與此同時，學生可以使用自修室。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a temporary action while people wait for a bigger solution.","zh":"這個短語引入等待較大解決方案期間的臨時行動。"},{"en":"It connects the present with a future goal.","zh":"它把現在與未來目標連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the industry as a whole","meaning":"整個行業","examples":[{"en":"The industry as a whole has introduced several energy-saving measures.","zh":"整個行業已引入幾項節能措施。"},{"en":"The industry as a whole means the entire industry, not just one company.","zh":"the industry as a whole 指整個行業，而不只是某一家公司。"},{"en":"The restaurant industry as a whole changed after more customers started ordering delivery.","zh":"當更多顧客開始叫外賣，整個餐飲業都改變了。"},{"en":"When an industry as a whole changes, suppliers, workers and customers may all be affected.","zh":"當整個行業改變，供應商、員工和顧客都可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase looks at the broad sector rather than individual cases.","zh":"這個短語看的是廣泛行業，而不是個別個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"employ a few tricks","meaning":"採用一些技巧","examples":[{"en":"Technology companies have employed a few tricks to save electricity.","zh":"科技公司採用一些技巧來節省電力。"},{"en":"To employ a few tricks means to use several clever methods to achieve a result.","zh":"employ a few tricks 指使用幾種聰明方法來達成結果。"},{"en":"A teacher may employ a few tricks, such as games and timers, to keep students focused.","zh":"老師可能採用一些技巧，例如遊戲和計時器，令學生保持專注。"},{"en":"Small tricks can produce large savings when applied across many machines.","zh":"當小技巧應用於大量機器，就能產生大量節省。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests practical, clever techniques rather than major inventions only.","zh":"這個短語暗示實用而聰明的技巧，而不只是重大發明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"save watts","meaning":"節省電力","examples":[{"en":"Small design changes can save watts across millions of machines.","zh":"小型設計改變可以在數以百萬計機器中節省電力。"},{"en":"To save watts means to reduce the amount of electrical power being used.","zh":"save watts 指減少正在使用的電功率。"},{"en":"A laptop screen that dims automatically can save watts during long lessons.","zh":"手提電腦屏幕自動變暗可以在長課堂中節省電力。"},{"en":"Saving a few watts per device matters when thousands of devices are running.","zh":"每部裝置節省幾瓦，在數千部裝置同時運作時就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes small reductions in power use.","zh":"這個短語描述用電功率的小幅減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cut down on","meaning":"減少……","examples":[{"en":"Engineers are trying to cut down on unnecessary energy transformations.","zh":"工程師正嘗試減少不必要的能源轉換。"},{"en":"To cut down on something means to reduce the amount or frequency of it.","zh":"cut down on something 指減少某事物的數量或頻率。"},{"en":"A family can cut down on takeaway meals to save money and reduce packaging waste.","zh":"家庭可以減少外賣餐，以節省金錢並減少包裝廢物。"},{"en":"Cutting down on wasteful steps usually makes a system cheaper and cleaner.","zh":"減少浪費步驟通常令系統更便宜、更潔淨。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing something that is excessive or unnecessary.","zh":"這個短語描述減少過多或不必要的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"undergo transformations","meaning":"經歷多次轉換","examples":[{"en":"Electricity may undergo several transformations before reaching the correct voltage.","zh":"電力在達到正確電壓前可能經歷多次轉換。"},{"en":"To undergo transformations means to go through changes in form, state or condition.","zh":"undergo transformations 指經歷形式、狀態或情況上的改變。"},{"en":"A school building may undergo transformations when classrooms become computer labs.","zh":"當課室變成電腦室，學校建築可能經歷轉變。"},{"en":"Each transformation can create energy loss if the process is inefficient.","zh":"如果過程低效，每次轉換都可能造成能源損失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a series of changes something experiences.","zh":"這個短語描述某物所經歷的一系列變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"operating voltage","meaning":"操作電壓","examples":[{"en":"Computer equipment requires electricity at the correct operating voltage.","zh":"電腦設備需要正確操作電壓的電力。"},{"en":"Operating voltage is the voltage level needed for a device to work safely and properly.","zh":"operating voltage 指裝置安全和正常運作所需的電壓水平。"},{"en":"A phone charger provides the operating voltage that a mobile phone battery needs.","zh":"手機充電器提供手機電池所需的操作電壓。"},{"en":"If the operating voltage is wrong, equipment may fail or become damaged.","zh":"如果操作電壓錯誤，設備可能故障或受損。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the electrical level required during normal operation.","zh":"這個短語指正常運作期間所需的電力水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rearrange the stacks of servers","meaning":"重新排列伺服器機架","examples":[{"en":"Engineers can rearrange the stacks of servers to improve cooling.","zh":"工程師可以重新排列伺服器機架以改善冷卻。"},{"en":"To rearrange the stacks of servers means to change how groups of servers are positioned.","zh":"rearrange the stacks of servers 指改變多組伺服器的擺放方式。"},{"en":"A data-centre team may rearrange server stacks so hot air flows away more easily.","zh":"數據中心團隊可能重新排列伺服器機架，使熱空氣更容易流走。"},{"en":"Better arrangement can reduce cooling needs and save electricity.","zh":"更好的排列可以減少冷卻需求並節省電力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing physical layout to improve performance.","zh":"這個短語描述改變實體佈局以改善表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cooling mechanics","meaning":"冷卻系統的運作方式","examples":[{"en":"Changes to cooling mechanics can reduce data-centre energy use.","zh":"改變冷卻系統的運作方式可以減少數據中心能源使用。"},{"en":"Cooling mechanics means the way a cooling system works, moves air and removes heat.","zh":"cooling mechanics 指冷卻系統如何運作、移動空氣和移除熱量。"},{"en":"A classroom’s cooling mechanics improve when fans push cool air evenly around the room.","zh":"當風扇把冷空氣均勻推送到課室各處，課室冷卻運作方式就改善了。"},{"en":"Better cooling mechanics can prevent overheating while using less power.","zh":"更好的冷卻運作可以防止過熱，同時使用較少電力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how cooling actually functions.","zh":"這個短語著重冷卻實際如何運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"use software to create","meaning":"使用軟件建立……","examples":[{"en":"Companies use software to create several virtual computers on one machine.","zh":"公司使用軟件在一部機器上建立幾部虛擬電腦。"},{"en":"To use software to create something means to make it through programs rather than physical construction.","zh":"use software to create something 指透過程式而不是實體建造來製作某物。"},{"en":"A teacher may use software to create online quizzes for students.","zh":"老師可能使用軟件為學生建立網上測驗。"},{"en":"Software can create virtual tools without needing extra physical machines.","zh":"軟件可以建立虛擬工具，而不需要額外實體機器。"},{"en":"This phrase describes building or organising something digitally.","zh":"這個短語描述以數碼方式建立或組織某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"virtual computers","meaning":"虛擬電腦","examples":[{"en":"Virtual computers allow one physical machine to perform several roles.","zh":"虛擬電腦讓一部實體機器執行多個角色。"},{"en":"Virtual computers are software-based computers that behave like separate machines inside one physical computer.","zh":"virtual computers 指以軟件建立、在一部實體電腦內像獨立機器般運作的電腦。"},{"en":"A school server may run several virtual computers for different departments.","zh":"學校伺服器可能為不同部門運行幾部虛擬電腦。"},{"en":"Virtual computers reduce the need for many separate physical machines.","zh":"虛擬電腦減少對多部獨立實體機器的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to computer systems created by software rather than hardware alone.","zh":"這個短語指由軟件而不只是硬件建立的電腦系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Companies can create virtual machines rather than deploy several physical computers.","zh":"公司可以建立虛擬機器，而不是部署多部實體電腦。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of; it shows a clear choice between two options.","zh":"rather than 指「而不是」，顯示兩個選項之間的清楚選擇。"},{"en":"A student may revise for twenty minutes daily rather than study all night before the exam.","zh":"學生可以每天溫習二十分鐘，而不是考試前通宵溫習。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one option is preferred over another.","zh":"當一個選項比另一個更可取時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It helps show contrast between a chosen action and an avoided action.","zh":"它幫助顯示被選行動與被避免行動之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"deploy several real ones","meaning":"部署多部實體電腦","examples":[{"en":"Virtualisation reduces the need to deploy several real computers.","zh":"虛擬化技術減少部署多部實體電腦的需要。"},{"en":"To deploy several real ones means to put several physical machines into use.","zh":"deploy several real ones 指把多部實體機器投入使用。"},{"en":"A small office may use one powerful server instead of deploying several real computers.","zh":"小型辦公室可能使用一部強大伺服器，而不是部署多部實體電腦。"},{"en":"Fewer physical machines can mean lower purchase costs, less space and less electricity use.","zh":"較少實體機器可以代表較低購買成本、較少空間和較少用電。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts physical deployment with virtual alternatives.","zh":"這個短語把實體部署與虛擬替代方案作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"virtualisation","meaning":"虛擬化技術","examples":[{"en":"Virtualisation allows computing resources to be shared more efficiently.","zh":"虛擬化技術讓運算資源能更有效率地共享。"},{"en":"Virtualisation is a technology that lets one physical computer act like several separate computers.","zh":"virtualisation 指讓一部實體電腦像幾部獨立電腦般運作的技術。"},{"en":"A company may use virtualisation to run several business systems on one server.","zh":"公司可能使用虛擬化技術，在一部伺服器上運行幾個業務系統。"},{"en":"Virtualisation saves energy because fewer physical machines are needed.","zh":"虛擬化技術節省能源，因為需要較少實體機器。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using software to divide and share computing power.","zh":"這個短語描述使用軟件分配和共享運算能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"allow a company to","meaning":"使公司能夠……","examples":[{"en":"Virtualisation allowed Hewlett-Packard to consolidate its data centres.","zh":"虛擬化技術使 Hewlett-Packard 能夠整合其數據中心。"},{"en":"To allow a company to do something means to make it possible for the company to do it.","zh":"allow a company to do something 指使公司能夠做某事。"},{"en":"Online payment tools allow a small shop to sell products outside its neighbourhood.","zh":"網上支付工具使小店能夠向社區以外銷售產品。"},{"en":"New technology can allow a company to reduce costs or change its operations.","zh":"新科技可以使公司能夠降低成本或改變營運。"},{"en":"This phrase links a tool or condition with what it enables.","zh":"這個短語把工具或條件與它所促成的事情連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"consolidate data centres","meaning":"整合數據中心","examples":[{"en":"The company consolidated dozens of data centres into a much smaller number.","zh":"該公司把數十個數據中心整合成少得多的數目。"},{"en":"To consolidate data centres means to combine many data centres into fewer, larger or more efficient ones.","zh":"consolidate data centres 指把許多數據中心合併成較少、較大或較有效率的數據中心。"},{"en":"A university may consolidate data centres from several departments into one shared facility.","zh":"大學可能把幾個部門的數據中心整合成一個共享設施。"},{"en":"Consolidation can reduce duplication, save energy and simplify management.","zh":"整合可以減少重複、節省能源並簡化管理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes combining separate facilities into a smaller number.","zh":"這個短語描述把分散設施合併成較少數目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"spread throughout the world","meaning":"分布於世界各地","examples":[{"en":"The original data centres were spread throughout the world.","zh":"原本的數據中心分布於世界各地。"},{"en":"Spread throughout the world means located or distributed in many countries or regions.","zh":"spread throughout the world 指位於或分布在許多國家或地區。"},{"en":"A charity may have offices spread throughout the world to support local communities.","zh":"慈善機構可能有分布於世界各地的辦公室，以支援本地社區。"},{"en":"When facilities are spread widely, communication and management can become more complex.","zh":"當設施分布廣泛，溝通和管理可能變得更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes global distribution.","zh":"這個短語描述全球分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"backup data centres","meaning":"後備數據中心","examples":[{"en":"The company maintained several backup data centres for emergencies.","zh":"該公司維持幾個後備數據中心以應付緊急情況。"},{"en":"Backup data centres are extra facilities kept ready in case main data centres fail.","zh":"backup data centres 指為主要數據中心故障時備用的額外設施。"},{"en":"A bank may use backup data centres so online services continue during a power failure.","zh":"銀行可能使用後備數據中心，使網上服務在停電時仍能繼續。"},{"en":"Backup systems improve reliability but also require space, equipment and energy.","zh":"後備系統提升可靠性，但也需要空間、設備和能源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to reserve data facilities for protection.","zh":"這個短語指用作保護的備用數據設施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"social and environmental responsibility","meaning":"社會及環境責任","examples":[{"en":"The executive was responsible for the firm’s social and environmental policies.","zh":"該高層負責公司的社會及環境政策。"},{"en":"Social and environmental responsibility means acting in ways that protect people, communities and the natural environment.","zh":"social and environmental responsibility 指以保護人、社區和自然環境的方式行事。"},{"en":"A company shows social and environmental responsibility by treating workers fairly and reducing waste.","zh":"公司公平對待員工並減少廢物，就是展示社會及環境責任。"},{"en":"Responsible policies can improve public trust and reduce harm.","zh":"負責任政策可以提升公眾信任並減少傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase joins concern for society with concern for the planet.","zh":"這個短語把對社會的關注與對地球的關注連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tackle the energy issue","meaning":"處理能源問題","examples":[{"en":"The technology industry is also tackling the energy issue at chip level.","zh":"科技行業也正在晶片層面處理能源問題。"},{"en":"To tackle the energy issue means to deal directly with the problem of energy use.","zh":"tackle the energy issue 指直接處理能源使用問題。"},{"en":"A school may tackle the energy issue by measuring electricity use in each classroom.","zh":"學校可能透過量度每間課室的用電量來處理能源問題。"},{"en":"Tackling the issue requires action, not just recognising that a problem exists.","zh":"處理問題需要行動，而不只是承認問題存在。"},{"en":"This phrase describes actively trying to solve an energy problem.","zh":"這個短語描述積極嘗試解決能源問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at the computer-chip level","meaning":"在電腦晶片層面","examples":[{"en":"Energy efficiency can be improved at the computer-chip level.","zh":"能源效益可以在電腦晶片層面改善。"},{"en":"At the computer-chip level means by changing the design or operation of the small chips inside computers.","zh":"at the computer-chip level 指透過改變電腦內部小型晶片的設計或運作來做事。"},{"en":"Engineers may save power at the computer-chip level before changing the whole machine.","zh":"工程師可能先在電腦晶片層面節電，再改變整部機器。"},{"en":"Improvements at chip level can affect millions of devices at once.","zh":"晶片層面的改善可以一次影響數以百萬計裝置。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the smallest hardware components, not the whole building.","zh":"這個短語著重最小型硬件組件，而不是整座建築物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"with every doubling of","meaning":"每當……增加一倍","examples":[{"en":"With every doubling of processing power came a rise in electricity use.","zh":"每當運算能力增加一倍，用電量便上升。"},{"en":"With every doubling of something means each time that thing becomes twice as large.","zh":"with every doubling of something 指每次某事物變成兩倍。"},{"en":"With every doubling of class size, teachers may find it harder to give individual feedback.","zh":"每當班級人數增加一倍，老師可能更難給予個別回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two changes happen together repeatedly.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩種變化反覆同時發生。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing a repeated relationship between growth and consequence.","zh":"它適合描述增長與後果之間的重複關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"processing power","meaning":"運算能力","examples":[{"en":"Modern computers provide far greater processing power than earlier machines.","zh":"現代電腦提供比早期機器大得多的運算能力。"},{"en":"Processing power is a computer’s ability to perform calculations and handle tasks quickly.","zh":"processing power 指電腦快速進行計算和處理任務的能力。"},{"en":"Video editing needs more processing power than simple word processing.","zh":"影片剪輯比簡單文字處理需要更多運算能力。"},{"en":"Greater processing power can improve speed, but it may also increase energy demand.","zh":"更高運算能力可以提升速度，但也可能增加能源需求。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to computational strength.","zh":"這個短語指計算能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"power consumption","meaning":"耗電量","examples":[{"en":"Increased processing power was traditionally linked to increased power consumption.","zh":"運算能力增加傳統上與耗電量增加相關。"},{"en":"Power consumption is the amount of electricity a device or system uses.","zh":"power consumption 指裝置或系統使用的電量。"},{"en":"A refrigerator with low power consumption costs less to run each month.","zh":"低耗電量雪櫃每月運作成本較低。"},{"en":"High power consumption raises bills and may require more cooling.","zh":"高耗電量會提高電費，並可能需要更多冷卻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes electricity use, not the price of the device.","zh":"這個短語描述用電量，而不是裝置價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"chipmakers","meaning":"晶片製造商","examples":[{"en":"Chipmakers are developing processors that use less electricity.","zh":"晶片製造商正在開發耗電較少的處理器。"},{"en":"Chipmakers are companies or engineers that design or manufacture computer chips.","zh":"chipmakers 指設計或製造電腦晶片的公司或工程師。"},{"en":"Chipmakers compete to create faster phone processors with longer battery life.","zh":"晶片製造商競爭創造更快、電池續航更長的手機處理器。"},{"en":"Better chip design can reduce energy use across computers, phones and servers.","zh":"更好的晶片設計可以減少電腦、手機和伺服器的能源使用。"},{"en":"This word refers to the people or firms behind computer-chip production.","zh":"這個詞指電腦晶片生產背後的人或公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"shift to","meaning":"轉用；轉向","examples":[{"en":"Major chipmakers have shifted to multicore technology.","zh":"主要晶片製造商已轉用多核心技術。"},{"en":"To shift to something means to move from one method, system or focus to another.","zh":"shift to something 指從一種方法、系統或重點轉向另一種。"},{"en":"A school may shift to online notices instead of printed circulars.","zh":"學校可能轉用網上通告，而不是紙本通告。"},{"en":"A shift often happens when the old method becomes less effective or too costly.","zh":"當舊方法變得較不有效或太昂貴，轉變常會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear change in direction.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚方向改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"so-called multicore technology","meaning":"所謂多核心技術","examples":[{"en":"So-called multicore technology places several processors on one circuit.","zh":"所謂多核心技術把幾個處理器放在一個電路上。"},{"en":"So-called multicore technology refers to the technology commonly named “multicore”.","zh":"so-called multicore technology 指通常被稱為「多核心」的技術。"},{"en":"A computer using so-called multicore technology can divide tasks between several processing cores.","zh":"使用所謂多核心技術的電腦可以把任務分配到幾個處理核心。"},{"en":"Multicore design can improve efficiency because work is shared rather than pushed through one core.","zh":"多核心設計可以提高效率，因為工作被分擔，而不是全部推到一個核心。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a technical term while signalling what it is called.","zh":"這個短語引入技術名稱，同時指出它的稱呼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pack multiple processors into","meaning":"將多個處理器置於……內","examples":[{"en":"Multicore chips pack multiple processors into a single circuit.","zh":"多核心晶片將多個處理器置於單一電路內。"},{"en":"To pack multiple processors into something means to fit several processing units inside one structure.","zh":"pack multiple processors into something 指把幾個處理單元放入一個結構內。"},{"en":"Phone designers pack multiple processors into small chips to handle apps, cameras and games.","zh":"手機設計師把多個處理器置於小型晶片內，以處理應用程式、相機和遊戲。"},{"en":"Packing more processors together can improve performance without simply raising speed.","zh":"把更多處理器放在一起可以改善效能，而不只是提高速度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes placing many computing parts into a compact space.","zh":"這個短語描述把多個運算部件放入緊湊空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a single circuit","meaning":"單一電路","examples":[{"en":"Several processing cores can be integrated into a single circuit.","zh":"幾個處理核心可以整合到單一電路中。"},{"en":"A single circuit is one connected electronic pathway or chip structure.","zh":"single circuit 指一個連接的電子路徑或晶片結構。"},{"en":"A small calculator may contain a single circuit that controls its basic functions.","zh":"小型計算機可能包含控制基本功能的單一電路。"},{"en":"Combining parts into a single circuit can reduce space and improve efficiency.","zh":"把部件結合到單一電路可以減少空間並提高效率。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to one unified electronic unit.","zh":"這個短語指一個統一電子單元。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rather than separating them","meaning":"而不是把它們分開","examples":[{"en":"Multicore technology combines processors rather than separating them.","zh":"多核心技術結合處理器，而不是把它們分開。"},{"en":"Rather than separating them means instead of keeping them apart.","zh":"rather than separating them 指不是把它們分開，而是採取另一做法。"},{"en":"A school may teach science and technology together rather than separating them into unrelated lessons.","zh":"學校可能把科學和科技一起教授，而不是把它們分成無關課堂。"},{"en":"Combining related parts can reduce waste and improve coordination.","zh":"結合相關部分可以減少浪費並改善協調。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the contrast between joining and separating clear.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示結合與分開之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"move away from","meaning":"不再採用；摒棄","examples":[{"en":"Chip designers moved away from a narrow focus on clock speed.","zh":"晶片設計師不再單純集中於時鐘速度。"},{"en":"To move away from something means to stop depending on it or stop treating it as central.","zh":"move away from something 指不再依賴某事，或不再把它視為核心。"},{"en":"A school may move away from memorisation and focus more on problem-solving.","zh":"學校可能不再採用死記硬背，而更重視解難。"},{"en":"People move away from old methods when those methods no longer solve the problem well.","zh":"當舊方法不再有效解決問題，人們就會摒棄它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift in approach or priority.","zh":"這個短語描述方法或優先事項的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a linear focus on","meaning":"單純集中於……","examples":[{"en":"The industry moved away from a linear focus on megahertz and gigahertz.","zh":"行業不再單純集中於兆赫和吉赫。"},{"en":"A linear focus on something means concentrating on one simple measure as if progress only moves in that direction.","zh":"linear focus on something 指只集中於一個簡單指標，像進步只朝那方向發生。"},{"en":"A school should avoid a linear focus on test scores if it also values creativity and confidence.","zh":"如果學校也重視創意和信心，就應避免單純集中於考試分數。"},{"en":"A narrow focus can hide other important measures of improvement.","zh":"狹窄焦點可能隱藏其他重要改善指標。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that one-dimensional thinking is too limited.","zh":"這個短語暗示單一維度思考太有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"megahertz and gigahertz","meaning":"兆赫和吉赫","examples":[{"en":"Megahertz and gigahertz are units used to describe processor speed.","zh":"兆赫和吉赫是用來描述處理器速度的單位。"},{"en":"Megahertz and gigahertz measure frequency, often used to describe how fast a processor’s clock runs.","zh":"megahertz and gigahertz 量度頻率，常用來描述處理器時鐘運行有多快。"},{"en":"A computer label may list gigahertz to show the speed of its processor.","zh":"電腦標籤可能列出吉赫數，以顯示處理器速度。"},{"en":"Higher gigahertz can mean faster operation, but it is not the only measure of performance.","zh":"較高吉赫可能代表較快運作，但不是唯一效能指標。"},{"en":"This phrase names technical units linked to computer speed.","zh":"這個短語命名與電腦速度相關的技術單位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"throttle down microprocessors","meaning":"降低微處理器的運行速度","examples":[{"en":"Engineers throttled down microprocessors to reduce power consumption.","zh":"工程師降低微處理器的運行速度，以減少耗電量。"},{"en":"To throttle down microprocessors means to slow processors down so they use less power.","zh":"throttle down microprocessors 指降低處理器速度，使其用電較少。"},{"en":"A laptop may throttle down its processor when the battery is low.","zh":"手提電腦在電量低時可能降低處理器運行速度。"},{"en":"Slowing a processor can reduce heat and extend battery life.","zh":"減慢處理器可以減少熱量並延長電池續航。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limiting processor speed for efficiency or protection.","zh":"這個短語描述為效率或保護而限制處理器速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"energy savings","meaning":"節能效果","examples":[{"en":"Multicore technology produced substantial energy savings.","zh":"多核心技術產生相當大的節能效果。"},{"en":"Energy savings are reductions in the amount of energy used.","zh":"energy savings 指能源使用量的減少。"},{"en":"A school’s energy savings may grow after lights are replaced with LEDs.","zh":"學校把燈換成 LED 後，節能效果可能增加。"},{"en":"Energy savings lower bills and reduce environmental impact.","zh":"節能效果降低賬單並減少環境影響。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to saved energy, not saved money only.","zh":"這個短語指節省的能源，而不只是節省的金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pretty substantial","meaning":"相當可觀","examples":[{"en":"The reduction in electricity consumption was pretty substantial.","zh":"用電量的減少相當可觀。"},{"en":"Pretty substantial means quite large or important.","zh":"pretty substantial 指相當大或相當重要。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement is pretty substantial if their mark rises from 50 to 75.","zh":"如果學生分數由 50 分升到 75 分，進步就相當可觀。"},{"en":"A substantial reduction in energy use can make a noticeable difference to costs.","zh":"能源使用量大幅減少可以對成本產生明顯差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is mildly informal but still clear in meaning.","zh":"這個短語略帶口語，但意思仍清楚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"shrink circuits","meaning":"縮小電路","examples":[{"en":"Chipmakers continue to shrink circuits to extremely small dimensions.","zh":"晶片製造商繼續把電路縮小至極細尺寸。"},{"en":"To shrink circuits means to make electronic circuits physically smaller.","zh":"shrink circuits 指令電子電路在實體上變得更小。"},{"en":"Phone makers shrink circuits so more functions can fit inside a thinner device.","zh":"手機製造商縮小電路，使更多功能能放進更薄裝置。"},{"en":"Smaller circuits can reduce power use and increase portability.","zh":"較小電路可以減少用電並提高便攜性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes miniaturisation in electronics.","zh":"這個短語描述電子學中的微型化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"on the nanoscale","meaning":"在納米尺度上","examples":[{"en":"Modern computer circuits are manufactured on the nanoscale.","zh":"現代電腦電路在納米尺度上製造。"},{"en":"On the nanoscale means at extremely tiny sizes measured in nanometres.","zh":"on the nanoscale 指在以納米量度的極微小尺寸上。"},{"en":"Scientists study materials on the nanoscale when ordinary microscopes are not enough.","zh":"當普通顯微鏡不足夠時，科學家會在納米尺度上研究材料。"},{"en":"Nanoscale design allows many components to fit into very small chips.","zh":"納米尺度設計讓許多組件能放入非常小的晶片。"},{"en":"This phrase describes work at a size far smaller than everyday objects.","zh":"這個短語描述遠小於日常物件的尺寸層面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"need less electricity to","meaning":"需要較少電力去……","examples":[{"en":"A smaller chip needs less electricity to deliver the same performance.","zh":"較小晶片需要較少電力去提供相同效能。"},{"en":"To need less electricity to do something means to require a smaller amount of power for the same task.","zh":"need less electricity to do something 指完成同一任務所需電力較少。"},{"en":"An LED bulb needs less electricity to light a room than an old bulb.","zh":"LED 燈泡比舊燈泡需要較少電力去照亮房間。"},{"en":"Devices that need less electricity can lower bills and battery use.","zh":"需要較少電力的裝置可以降低電費和電池使用。"},{"en":"This phrase links efficiency with reduced power demand.","zh":"這個短語把效率與較低電力需求連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"deliver the same performance","meaning":"提供相同效能","examples":[{"en":"Improved chips can deliver the same performance while using less power.","zh":"改良晶片可以在使用較少電力時提供相同效能。"},{"en":"To deliver the same performance means to produce the same level of speed, quality or output.","zh":"deliver the same performance 指產生相同水平的速度、質素或輸出。"},{"en":"A smaller air conditioner may deliver the same performance as an older large model if it is efficient.","zh":"如果效率高，較小冷氣機可能提供與舊大型型號相同效能。"},{"en":"Keeping performance the same while using less energy is a key efficiency goal.","zh":"在使用較少能源時保持相同效能，是能源效益的重要目標。"},{"en":"This phrase compares output while another factor changes.","zh":"這個短語在另一因素改變時比較輸出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"personal computers","meaning":"個人電腦","examples":[{"en":"More personal computers are expected to meet energy-efficiency standards.","zh":"預期更多個人電腦會符合能源效益標準。"},{"en":"Personal computers are computers designed for individual users at home, school or work.","zh":"personal computers 指為家庭、學校或工作中的個別使用者設計的電腦。"},{"en":"A student may use a personal computer for essays, online classes and research.","zh":"學生可能使用個人電腦寫文章、上網課和做資料搜集。"},{"en":"Efficient personal computers reduce electricity use across millions of households.","zh":"高效個人電腦可以減少數以百萬計家庭的用電。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to individual-use computers rather than large servers.","zh":"這個短語指個人使用的電腦，而不是大型伺服器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"meet efficiency standards","meaning":"符合能源效益標準","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers are designing computers that meet efficiency standards.","zh":"製造商正在設計符合能源效益標準的電腦。"},{"en":"To meet efficiency standards means to satisfy official or recognised rules about energy performance.","zh":"meet efficiency standards 指滿足關於能源表現的官方或公認規則。"},{"en":"A refrigerator must meet efficiency standards before receiving an energy label.","zh":"雪櫃在取得能源標籤前，必須符合能源效益標準。"},{"en":"Meeting standards helps buyers compare products more easily.","zh":"符合標準幫助買家更容易比較產品。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a product reaches an accepted level of efficiency.","zh":"這個短語顯示產品達到被接受的效率水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Energy Star compliance","meaning":"符合「能源之星」標準","examples":[{"en":"Energy Star compliance requires computers to meet limits on electricity use.","zh":"符合「能源之星」標準要求電腦達到用電限制。"},{"en":"Energy Star compliance means meeting the energy-efficiency requirements of the Energy Star programme.","zh":"Energy Star compliance 指符合「能源之星」計劃的能源效益要求。"},{"en":"A school may choose computers with Energy Star compliance to reduce electricity bills.","zh":"學校可能選擇符合「能源之星」標準的電腦，以減少電費。"},{"en":"Compliance gives buyers confidence that the product meets recognised energy standards.","zh":"符合標準讓買家相信產品達到公認能源標準。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to satisfying a specific efficiency certification.","zh":"這個短語指滿足特定能源效益認證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"mandate that","meaning":"規定","examples":[{"en":"The standard mandates that a desktop computer consume no more than 65 watts.","zh":"該標準規定桌面電腦耗電不得超過 65 瓦。"},{"en":"To mandate that something happen means to officially require it.","zh":"mandate that something happen 指正式要求某事發生。"},{"en":"School rules may mandate that students wear safety glasses in the laboratory.","zh":"學校規則可能規定學生在實驗室戴安全眼鏡。"},{"en":"A mandate creates a rule that manufacturers or users must follow.","zh":"規定會建立製造商或使用者必須遵守的規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often appears in laws, standards and policies.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常出現在法律、標準和政策中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"desktop computer","meaning":"桌面電腦","examples":[{"en":"A desktop computer must meet specific electricity-consumption limits.","zh":"桌面電腦必須符合特定耗電限制。"},{"en":"A desktop computer is a computer designed to stay on a desk rather than be carried around.","zh":"desktop computer 指設計放在桌上而不是隨身攜帶的電腦。"},{"en":"A school office may use a desktop computer for printing, records and e-mail.","zh":"學校辦公室可能使用桌面電腦列印、處理紀錄和收發電郵。"},{"en":"Desktop computers often use more power than small laptops.","zh":"桌面電腦通常比小型手提電腦耗電更多。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a fixed personal computer with separate or built-in parts.","zh":"這個短語指固定式個人電腦，可有分開或內置部件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"consume no more than","meaning":"耗電不超過……","examples":[{"en":"The standard requires a desktop to consume no more than 65 watts.","zh":"該標準要求桌面電腦耗電不超過 65 瓦。"},{"en":"To consume no more than an amount means to use that amount or less.","zh":"consume no more than an amount 指使用該數量或更少。"},{"en":"A small fan may consume no more than 30 watts on its lowest setting.","zh":"小風扇在最低設定下可能耗電不超過 30 瓦。"},{"en":"Limits on energy use help manufacturers design more efficient products.","zh":"能源使用限制幫助製造商設計更高效產品。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a maximum amount that must not be exceeded.","zh":"這個短語設定不得超出的最高數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the federal government","meaning":"聯邦政府","examples":[{"en":"The federal government may introduce stricter purchasing requirements.","zh":"聯邦政府可能引入更嚴格的採購要求。"},{"en":"The federal government is the national-level government in a federal political system.","zh":"federal government 指聯邦政治制度中的國家層面政府。"},{"en":"The federal government may set standards for government offices across the country.","zh":"聯邦政府可能為全國政府辦公室制定標準。"},{"en":"When the federal government changes buying rules, large suppliers may adjust their products.","zh":"當聯邦政府改變採購規則，大型供應商可能調整其產品。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to central national authority, not local government.","zh":"這個短語指中央國家權力，而不是地方政府。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"agencies such as","meaning":"……等機構","examples":[{"en":"Government agencies such as NASA may adopt environmental standards.","zh":"NASA 等政府機構可能採用環境標準。"},{"en":"Agencies such as means organisations like the examples that follow.","zh":"agencies such as 指像後面例子那樣的機構。"},{"en":"Public agencies such as hospitals and schools may need clear emergency plans.","zh":"醫院和學校等公共機構可能需要清楚應急計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples without listing every possible organisation.","zh":"這個短語引入例子，而不列出所有可能機構。"},{"en":"It helps readers understand the type of agency being discussed.","zh":"它幫助讀者理解正在討論的機構類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Department of Defense","meaning":"國防部","examples":[{"en":"The Department of Defense purchases large quantities of computer equipment.","zh":"國防部購買大量電腦設備。"},{"en":"The Department of Defense is the government department responsible for national military affairs in the United States.","zh":"Department of Defense 指美國負責國家軍事事務的政府部門。"},{"en":"A large department like the Department of Defense can influence suppliers through its purchasing choices.","zh":"像國防部這樣的大型部門可以透過採購選擇影響供應商。"},{"en":"If it requires efficient computers, manufacturers may produce more efficient models.","zh":"如果它要求高效電腦，製造商可能生產更多高效型號。"},{"en":"This phrase names a major government buyer of technology.","zh":"這個短語命名一個主要政府科技買家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"require all purchases to meet","meaning":"要求所有採購符合……","examples":[{"en":"Government agencies may require all computer purchases to meet an environmental standard.","zh":"政府機構可能要求所有電腦採購符合環境標準。"},{"en":"To require all purchases to meet a standard means every item bought must satisfy that rule.","zh":"require all purchases to meet a standard 指每項購買物品都必須滿足該規則。"},{"en":"A school may require all furniture purchases to meet safety standards.","zh":"學校可能要求所有家具採購符合安全標準。"},{"en":"Such requirements push suppliers to improve product quality and compliance.","zh":"這類要求推動供應商改善產品質素和合規程度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rule applied to every purchase.","zh":"這個短語描述適用於每項採購的規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"environmental assessment standard","meaning":"環境評估標準","examples":[{"en":"An environmental assessment standard helps buyers compare electronic products.","zh":"環境評估標準幫助買家比較電子產品。"},{"en":"An environmental assessment standard is a set of criteria used to judge a product’s environmental impact.","zh":"environmental assessment standard 指用來判斷產品環境影響的一套準則。"},{"en":"A school may use an environmental assessment standard before buying new computers.","zh":"學校購買新電腦前，可能使用環境評估標準。"},{"en":"Standards make comparison easier because products are judged by the same rules.","zh":"標準使比較更容易，因為產品按同一規則評估。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a formal way of measuring environmental performance.","zh":"這個短語指量度環境表現的正式方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Electronic Product Environmental Assessment Tool","meaning":"電子產品環境評估工具","examples":[{"en":"The Electronic Product Environmental Assessment Tool evaluates the environmental impact of electronic equipment.","zh":"電子產品環境評估工具評估電子設備的環境影響。"},{"en":"The Electronic Product Environmental Assessment Tool is a system for rating electronic products by environmental criteria.","zh":"Electronic Product Environmental Assessment Tool 是按環境準則評級電子產品的系統。"},{"en":"A government office may use this tool when choosing greener computers.","zh":"政府辦公室選擇較環保電腦時，可能使用這個工具。"},{"en":"Such tools help large buyers reward manufacturers that design cleaner products.","zh":"這類工具幫助大型買家獎勵設計較潔淨產品的製造商。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific assessment tool for electronics.","zh":"這個短語命名電子產品的特定評估工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"form an initiative","meaning":"成立一項倡議","examples":[{"en":"Google, Intel and other companies formed an energy-saving initiative.","zh":"Google、Intel 和其他公司成立一項節能倡議。"},{"en":"To form an initiative means to create an organised plan or campaign for a specific goal.","zh":"form an initiative 指為特定目標建立有組織的計劃或運動。"},{"en":"Several schools may form an initiative to reduce lunch-box waste.","zh":"幾間學校可能成立一項倡議，以減少飯盒廢物。"},{"en":"Initiatives bring different people or organisations together around one problem.","zh":"倡議把不同人士或組織聚集到同一問題上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes starting a coordinated action.","zh":"這個短語描述開始一項協同行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Climate Savers Computing Initiative","meaning":"氣候拯救者電腦計劃","examples":[{"en":"The Climate Savers Computing Initiative aimed to reduce computer power use.","zh":"氣候拯救者電腦計劃旨在減少電腦用電。"},{"en":"The Climate Savers Computing Initiative was a programme focused on making computing more energy-efficient.","zh":"Climate Savers Computing Initiative 是一項著重令運算更具能源效益的計劃。"},{"en":"A company joining the initiative might choose computers with better power-management features.","zh":"加入該計劃的公司可能選擇有更好電源管理功能的電腦。"},{"en":"Such initiatives can create industry-wide pressure to reduce electricity waste.","zh":"這類倡議可以創造全行業壓力，減少電力浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase names a campaign linking computing with climate protection.","zh":"這個短語命名一項把運算與氣候保護連繫起來的運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cut power consumption by","meaning":"將耗電量削減……","examples":[{"en":"The initiative aimed to cut computer power consumption by 50 per cent.","zh":"該倡議旨在將電腦耗電量削減百分之五十。"},{"en":"To cut power consumption by an amount means to reduce electricity use by that amount.","zh":"cut power consumption by an amount 指把用電量減少該數量。"},{"en":"A school may cut power consumption by 20 per cent after replacing old lights.","zh":"學校更換舊燈後，可能將耗電量削減百分之二十。"},{"en":"Cutting consumption by half can greatly reduce bills and emissions.","zh":"將耗電量減半可以大幅減少賬單和排放。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a measured reduction in energy use.","zh":"這個短語給出可量度的能源使用減幅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sleep modes","meaning":"睡眠模式","examples":[{"en":"Sleep modes reduce the power used by an inactive computer.","zh":"睡眠模式減少閒置電腦所使用的電力。"},{"en":"Sleep modes are low-power settings that keep a computer ready while using less electricity.","zh":"sleep modes 指讓電腦保持可快速使用但耗電較少的低功耗設定。"},{"en":"A laptop enters sleep mode when a student closes the lid during lunch.","zh":"學生午飯時合上手提電腦，電腦會進入睡眠模式。"},{"en":"Sleep modes save energy because the machine is not fully active.","zh":"睡眠模式節省能源，因為機器沒有完全活躍運作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to automatic or manual low-power computer states.","zh":"這個短語指自動或手動的低功耗電腦狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"power-management tools","meaning":"電源管理工具","examples":[{"en":"Most operating systems include built-in power-management tools.","zh":"大多數作業系統包括內置電源管理工具。"},{"en":"Power-management tools are settings or programs that control how much electricity a device uses.","zh":"power-management tools 指控制裝置使用多少電力的設定或程式。"},{"en":"A laptop’s power-management tools may dim the screen after five minutes of inactivity.","zh":"手提電腦的電源管理工具可能在閒置五分鐘後調暗屏幕。"},{"en":"These tools reduce waste by lowering power when full performance is not needed.","zh":"這些工具在不需要完整效能時降低功耗，從而減少浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to software features for saving electricity.","zh":"這個短語指用來節省電力的軟件功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be built into","meaning":"內置於……","examples":[{"en":"Energy-saving settings are built into most modern operating systems.","zh":"節能設定內置於大多數現代作業系統。"},{"en":"To be built into something means to be included as a normal part of it.","zh":"be built into something 指作為某物的正常部分被包括在內。"},{"en":"Spell-checking is built into many writing apps.","zh":"拼字檢查內置於許多寫作應用程式。"},{"en":"Built-in features are easier to use because people do not need to install extra tools.","zh":"內置功能較容易使用，因為人們不需要安裝額外工具。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something already included inside a system.","zh":"這個短語描述已經包含在系統內的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"operating systems","meaning":"作業系統","examples":[{"en":"Operating systems control a computer’s basic functions and settings.","zh":"作業系統控制電腦的基本功能和設定。"},{"en":"Operating systems are the main software that allows computers, phones or tablets to run programs.","zh":"operating systems 指讓電腦、手機或平板運行程式的主要軟件。"},{"en":"A phone’s operating system controls apps, storage, security and battery settings.","zh":"手機作業系統控制應用程式、儲存、安全和電池設定。"},{"en":"Better operating systems can help devices save energy automatically.","zh":"更好的作業系統可以幫助裝置自動節省能源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the software foundation of a digital device.","zh":"這個短語指數碼裝置的軟件基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"offer savings today","meaning":"現時即可節省能源","examples":[{"en":"Built-in power settings can offer immediate energy savings.","zh":"內置電源設定可以現時即可節省能源。"},{"en":"To offer savings today means to provide reductions in cost or energy use right now.","zh":"offer savings today 指現在就能減少成本或能源使用。"},{"en":"Switching off unused classroom lights can offer savings today, not years later.","zh":"關掉不用的課室燈可以現時即刻節省能源，而不是多年後才見效。"},{"en":"Immediate savings are attractive because they do not require waiting for new technology.","zh":"即時節省很吸引，因為不需要等待新科技。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a benefit available at once.","zh":"這個短語突出立即可得到的好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have settings enabled","meaning":"已啟用設定","examples":[{"en":"Most computers do not have their energy-saving settings enabled.","zh":"大多數電腦沒有啟用其節能設定。"},{"en":"To have settings enabled means the settings are switched on and active.","zh":"have settings enabled 指設定已被打開並處於啟用狀態。"},{"en":"A phone has location settings enabled when apps can use its location.","zh":"當應用程式可以使用手機位置時，手機就是已啟用定位設定。"},{"en":"If energy-saving settings are not enabled, the computer may waste power while idle.","zh":"如果節能設定未啟用，電腦在閒置時可能浪費電力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes whether a feature is turned on.","zh":"這個短語描述某功能是否已開啟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"properly activated","meaning":"正確啟用","examples":[{"en":"Properly activated power settings can substantially reduce electricity use.","zh":"正確啟用的電源設定可以大幅減少用電。"},{"en":"Properly activated means correctly turned on and set up so the feature works as intended.","zh":"properly activated 指正確開啟並設定，使功能按預期運作。"},{"en":"A security alarm only protects a classroom if it is properly activated before leaving.","zh":"保安警鐘只有在離開前正確啟用，才能保護課室。"},{"en":"If energy-saving tools are properly activated, computers can sleep or power down automatically.","zh":"如果節能工具正確啟用，電腦可以自動睡眠或關機。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses correct setup, not just having the feature available.","zh":"這個短語強調正確設定，而不只是有該功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"prevent a computer from causing","meaning":"防止電腦造成……","examples":[{"en":"Energy-saving tools can prevent a computer from causing unnecessary emissions.","zh":"節能工具可以防止電腦造成不必要排放。"},{"en":"To prevent a computer from causing something means to stop its operation from producing that problem.","zh":"prevent a computer from causing something 指阻止電腦運作產生某問題。"},{"en":"Sleep mode can prevent a computer from causing wasted electricity overnight.","zh":"睡眠模式可以防止電腦在夜間造成電力浪費。"},{"en":"Reducing power use prevents extra emissions when electricity comes from fossil fuels.","zh":"當電力來自化石燃料，減少用電可以防止額外排放。"},{"en":"This phrase links computer settings with avoiding negative effects.","zh":"這個短語把電腦設定與避免負面影響連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"carbon-dioxide emissions","meaning":"二氧化碳排放","examples":[{"en":"Electricity generation can produce large carbon-dioxide emissions.","zh":"發電可以產生大量二氧化碳排放。"},{"en":"Carbon-dioxide emissions are releases of carbon dioxide gas into the atmosphere.","zh":"carbon-dioxide emissions 指二氧化碳氣體被釋放到大氣中。"},{"en":"Cars, power plants and factories can all produce carbon-dioxide emissions.","zh":"汽車、發電廠和工廠都可以產生二氧化碳排放。"},{"en":"High emissions contribute to climate change by increasing greenhouse gases.","zh":"高排放透過增加溫室氣體而加劇氣候變化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to one major type of climate-related pollution.","zh":"這個短語指一種主要與氣候相關的污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"power plants","meaning":"發電廠","examples":[{"en":"Power plants produce electricity for computers and data centres.","zh":"發電廠為電腦和數據中心生產電力。"},{"en":"Power plants are facilities that generate electricity from sources such as coal, gas, wind, water or sunlight.","zh":"power plants 指由煤、天然氣、風、水或陽光等來源發電的設施。"},{"en":"A city depends on power plants to keep hospitals, schools and homes running.","zh":"城市依賴發電廠來維持醫院、學校和家庭運作。"},{"en":"If power plants burn fossil fuels, electricity use can create emissions.","zh":"如果發電廠燃燒化石燃料，用電就會造成排放。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the places where electricity is generated.","zh":"這個短語指生產電力的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"power down","meaning":"關機","examples":[{"en":"Users can power down a computer when it is not needed.","zh":"使用者可以在不需要電腦時關機。"},{"en":"To power down means to switch off or reduce power to a device.","zh":"power down 指關掉裝置或降低供電。"},{"en":"A teacher may power down the classroom projector after the lesson ends.","zh":"老師可能在課堂結束後關掉課室投影機。"},{"en":"Powering down unused machines saves electricity and reduces heat.","zh":"關掉不用的機器可以節省電力並減少熱量。"},{"en":"This phrase is more technical than simply saying “turn off”.","zh":"這個短語比單純說 “turn off” 更有技術感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unplug the computer","meaning":"拔除電腦電源","examples":[{"en":"To use no electricity at all, users must unplug the computer.","zh":"若要完全不使用電力，使用者必須拔除電腦電源。"},{"en":"To unplug the computer means to remove its power plug from the electrical socket.","zh":"unplug the computer 指把電腦電源插頭從插座拔出。"},{"en":"A family may unplug the computer before a long holiday.","zh":"家庭可能在長假期前拔除電腦電源。"},{"en":"Unplugging prevents standby power use because the machine is completely disconnected.","zh":"拔掉電源可防止待機耗電，因為機器完全斷開電力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physically cutting off the power supply.","zh":"這個短語描述實際切斷電源供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"use zero power","meaning":"完全不耗電","examples":[{"en":"A fully unplugged computer uses zero power.","zh":"完全拔掉電源的電腦完全不耗電。"},{"en":"To use zero power means to consume no electricity at all.","zh":"use zero power 指完全不消耗電力。"},{"en":"A lamp uses zero power when it is unplugged from the wall.","zh":"燈從牆上插座拔掉時，就完全不耗電。"},{"en":"Devices in standby mode may still use electricity, so they do not use zero power.","zh":"待機模式的裝置可能仍用電，所以並非完全不耗電。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete absence of power consumption.","zh":"這個短語描述完全沒有電力消耗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be not an option","meaning":"並非可行選擇","examples":[{"en":"Completely shutting down a machine is not always an option.","zh":"完全關閉機器並非總是可行選擇。"},{"en":"If something is not an option, it is not possible or not suitable in that situation.","zh":"if something is not an option 指某事在該情況下不可能或不合適。"},{"en":"Turning off hospital computers completely is not an option if patient monitoring depends on them.","zh":"如果病人監測依賴醫院電腦，完全關閉它們就不是可行選擇。"},{"en":"When shutdown is not an option, sleep mode may be a better compromise.","zh":"當關機不是可行選擇，睡眠模式可能是較好的折衷方案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a choice that cannot realistically be used.","zh":"這個短語描述現實上不能使用的選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"environmentally friendly use","meaning":"環保用途","examples":[{"en":"Climate research may be an environmentally friendly use of spare computing capacity.","zh":"氣候研究可能是閒置運算能力的一種環保用途。"},{"en":"An environmentally friendly use is a way of using something that helps or harms the environment less.","zh":"environmentally friendly use 指以有助環境或較少傷害環境的方式使用某物。"},{"en":"Using old tablets for school reading can be an environmentally friendly use if it prevents waste.","zh":"如果舊平板用於學校閱讀並避免浪費，就是一種環保用途。"},{"en":"Computing power becomes more responsible when it supports useful research instead of sitting idle.","zh":"當運算能力支持有用研究而不是閒置時，就更負責任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using a resource in a greener way.","zh":"這個短語描述以較環保方式使用資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"wasted computing cycles","meaning":"被浪費的運算週期","examples":[{"en":"Idle machines contain wasted computing cycles that could support research.","zh":"閒置機器包含可支援研究的被浪費運算週期。"},{"en":"Wasted computing cycles are unused processing capacity that could have been used for useful work.","zh":"wasted computing cycles 指本可用於有用工作的未用處理能力。"},{"en":"A classroom computer left idle all day has wasted computing cycles.","zh":"整天閒置的課室電腦有被浪費的運算週期。"},{"en":"Using idle processing power for research can turn waste into value.","zh":"把閒置處理能力用於研究，可以把浪費轉化為價值。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to unused computer work capacity.","zh":"這個短語指未被使用的電腦工作能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"model climate change","meaning":"模擬氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"Distributed computers can help scientists model climate change.","zh":"分散式電腦可以幫助科學家模擬氣候變化。"},{"en":"To model climate change means to use computer calculations to simulate how the climate may change.","zh":"model climate change 指使用電腦計算模擬氣候可能如何改變。"},{"en":"Scientists model climate change to understand future rainfall, temperature and sea levels.","zh":"科學家模擬氣候變化，以理解未來降雨、溫度和海平面。"},{"en":"Better models can help governments plan for floods, droughts and heatwaves.","zh":"更好的模型可以幫助政府規劃洪水、乾旱和熱浪應對。"},{"en":"This phrase describes scientific prediction through computer simulation.","zh":"這個短語描述透過電腦模擬進行科學預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"offer an opportunity to","meaning":"提供機會去……","examples":[{"en":"ClimatePrediction.net offers users an opportunity to support climate research.","zh":"ClimatePrediction.net 為使用者提供機會去支持氣候研究。"},{"en":"To offer an opportunity to do something means to give people a chance to do it.","zh":"offer an opportunity to do something 指給人做某事的機會。"},{"en":"A school club may offer students an opportunity to volunteer in the community.","zh":"學校學會可能為學生提供機會去社區做義工。"},{"en":"Opportunities matter because they turn interest into action.","zh":"機會很重要，因為它把興趣轉化為行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes opening a chance for participation.","zh":"這個短語描述開放參與的機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"predict the consequences of","meaning":"預測……的後果","examples":[{"en":"Computer models help predict the consequences of coal burning.","zh":"電腦模型幫助預測燃煤的後果。"},{"en":"To predict the consequences of something means to estimate what will happen because of it.","zh":"predict the consequences of something 指估計某事會造成甚麼結果。"},{"en":"A doctor may predict the consequences of poor sleep on a student’s concentration.","zh":"醫生可能預測睡眠不足對學生專注力的後果。"},{"en":"Prediction helps people act earlier before harm becomes worse.","zh":"預測幫助人們在傷害惡化前更早行動。"},{"en":"This phrase links an action with its future effects.","zh":"這個短語把行動與其未來影響連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"coal burning","meaning":"燃煤","examples":[{"en":"Coal burning releases large quantities of carbon dioxide.","zh":"燃煤釋放大量二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Coal burning means using coal as fuel, usually to produce heat or electricity.","zh":"coal burning 指使用煤作燃料，通常用來產生熱或電力。"},{"en":"A power plant uses coal burning when it burns coal to generate electricity.","zh":"發電廠燃燒煤炭發電時，就是使用燃煤。"},{"en":"Coal burning contributes to air pollution and greenhouse-gas emissions.","zh":"燃煤會造成空氣污染和溫室氣體排放。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to one of the most carbon-intensive energy practices.","zh":"這個短語指最碳密集的能源做法之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a free tool","meaning":"免費工具","examples":[{"en":"CO2 Stats is a free tool for estimating website-related emissions.","zh":"CO2 Stats 是估算網站相關排放量的免費工具。"},{"en":"A free tool is a program, app or resource that people can use without paying.","zh":"free tool 指人們可以不付費使用的程式、應用程式或資源。"},{"en":"A student may use a free tool to check grammar before submitting an essay.","zh":"學生可能使用免費工具在提交文章前檢查文法。"},{"en":"Free tools can spread quickly because cost is not a barrier.","zh":"免費工具可以快速普及，因為成本不是障礙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a useful resource available at no charge.","zh":"這個短語描述免費可用的有用資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be embedded into","meaning":"嵌入……","examples":[{"en":"The tool can be embedded into almost any website.","zh":"該工具可以嵌入幾乎任何網站。"},{"en":"To be embedded into something means to be placed inside it as part of its structure or operation.","zh":"be embedded into something 指被放入某物內，成為其結構或運作的一部分。"},{"en":"A video can be embedded into a school webpage so students can watch it there.","zh":"影片可以嵌入學校網頁，讓學生在那裡觀看。"},{"en":"Embedded tools are convenient because users do not need to leave the page.","zh":"嵌入式工具很方便，因為使用者不用離開頁面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inserting a feature into a larger digital space.","zh":"這個短語描述把功能插入較大的數碼空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"calculate emissions","meaning":"計算排放量","examples":[{"en":"The program calculates emissions associated with website use.","zh":"該程式計算與網站使用相關的排放量。"},{"en":"To calculate emissions means to estimate or work out the amount of pollution released.","zh":"calculate emissions 指估算或計算釋放出的污染量。"},{"en":"A travel app may calculate emissions from a flight or train journey.","zh":"旅遊應用程式可能計算航班或火車旅程的排放量。"},{"en":"Calculating emissions helps people compare choices and reduce their impact.","zh":"計算排放量幫助人們比較選擇並減少影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes measuring pollution in numerical terms.","zh":"這個短語描述以數字方式量度污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be associated with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Every website has energy use associated with its operation.","zh":"每個網站都有與其運作有關的能源使用。"},{"en":"To be associated with something means to be connected with it.","zh":"be associated with something 指與某事物有連繫。"},{"en":"Stress is often associated with poor sleep and lack of exercise.","zh":"壓力常與睡眠差和缺乏運動有關。"},{"en":"When energy use is associated with a website, visiting the site has an environmental cost.","zh":"當能源使用與網站有關，瀏覽該網站就有環境成本。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a connection between two things.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩件事之間的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be based on an assumption","meaning":"以某項假設為基礎","examples":[{"en":"The estimate is based on an assumption about power consumption.","zh":"該估算以一項關於耗電量的假設為基礎。"},{"en":"To be based on an assumption means to depend on an idea that is accepted as true for calculation or reasoning.","zh":"be based on an assumption 指依賴某個被當作真實的想法來計算或推理。"},{"en":"A school budget may be based on an assumption that student numbers will not change.","zh":"學校預算可能以學生人數不會改變這項假設為基礎。"},{"en":"If the assumption is wrong, the final estimate may also be wrong.","zh":"如果假設錯誤，最終估算也可能錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a calculation may not be exact.","zh":"這個短語提醒計算未必完全精確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"power consumed by","meaning":"由……消耗的電力","examples":[{"en":"The calculation includes power consumed by the computer, network and server.","zh":"計算包括由電腦、網絡和伺服器消耗的電力。"},{"en":"Power consumed by something means the electricity used by that device or system.","zh":"power consumed by something 指由某裝置或系統使用的電力。"},{"en":"A smart meter can show the power consumed by an air conditioner in one hour.","zh":"智能電錶可以顯示冷氣機一小時消耗的電力。"},{"en":"Knowing power consumption helps users find where energy is being wasted.","zh":"了解耗電量幫助使用者找出能源在哪裡被浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies which part is using electricity.","zh":"這個短語指出哪一部分正在用電。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"personal computer, network and server","meaning":"個人電腦、網絡和伺服器","examples":[{"en":"Website use involves a personal computer, network and server.","zh":"網站使用涉及個人電腦、網絡和伺服器。"},{"en":"A personal computer, network and server are the connected parts that let a user access a website.","zh":"personal computer, network and server 指讓使用者存取網站的互相連接部分。"},{"en":"When a student opens an online article, the personal computer, network and server all use energy.","zh":"當學生打開網上文章，個人電腦、網絡和伺服器都會使用能源。"},{"en":"Digital actions seem simple, but several systems work together behind them.","zh":"數碼行動看似簡單，但背後有幾個系統共同運作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the chain of technology behind Internet use.","zh":"這個短語顯示互聯網使用背後的科技鏈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be emitted every second","meaning":"每秒被排放","examples":[{"en":"A small quantity of carbon dioxide is emitted every second of use.","zh":"每使用一秒，都有少量二氧化碳被排放。"},{"en":"To be emitted every second means to be released continuously once each second or throughout every second.","zh":"be emitted every second 指每秒或每一秒期間持續被釋放。"},{"en":"A running car may emit exhaust gases every second its engine is on.","zh":"汽車引擎運作時，可能每秒排放廢氣。"},{"en":"Small emissions every second can become large when many users are online for hours.","zh":"每秒的小量排放在許多使用者長時間上網時可以變得很大。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses continuous release over time.","zh":"這個短語強調隨時間持續釋放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"carbon footprint","meaning":"碳足跡","examples":[{"en":"A website’s carbon footprint reflects the energy used to deliver it.","zh":"網站的碳足跡反映提供該網站所使用的能源。"},{"en":"A carbon footprint is the total greenhouse-gas impact caused by an activity, product or organisation.","zh":"carbon footprint 指某活動、產品或組織造成的總溫室氣體影響。"},{"en":"A family can reduce its carbon footprint by using public transport and saving electricity.","zh":"家庭可以透過使用公共交通和節省電力來減少碳足跡。"},{"en":"Digital services have carbon footprints because servers and networks use power.","zh":"數碼服務有碳足跡，因為伺服器和網絡使用電力。"},{"en":"This phrase measures environmental impact in terms of emissions.","zh":"這個短語以排放量來量度環境影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"roughly equivalent to","meaning":"大致相等於","examples":[{"en":"The typical carbon footprint is roughly equivalent to the breathing of 1.5 people.","zh":"典型碳足跡大致相等於 1.5 個人的呼吸量。"},{"en":"Roughly equivalent to means approximately equal to something else.","zh":"roughly equivalent to 指大約等於另一事物。"},{"en":"Walking one kilometre is roughly equivalent to ten or fifteen minutes for many people.","zh":"對許多人來說，步行一公里大致相等於十至十五分鐘。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain unfamiliar numbers by comparing them with familiar things.","zh":"這個短語透過熟悉事物比較，幫助解釋陌生數字。"},{"en":"It shows an approximate comparison, not an exact match.","zh":"它顯示近似比較，而不是精確相等。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"co-create a tool","meaning":"共同開發工具","examples":[{"en":"Alexander Wissner-Gross helped co-create the web-based emissions tool.","zh":"Alexander Wissner-Gross 幫助共同開發該網上排放工具。"},{"en":"To co-create a tool means to help design or build it together with others.","zh":"co-create a tool 指與其他人一起幫助設計或建立工具。"},{"en":"A teacher and students may co-create a tool for tracking homework deadlines.","zh":"老師和學生可能共同開發工具來追蹤功課期限。"},{"en":"Co-creation combines different skills and ideas into one product.","zh":"共同創作把不同技能和想法結合成一個產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shared creation, not individual invention alone.","zh":"這個短語描述共同創造，而不只是個人發明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"match the people with","meaning":"將人物與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match the listed people with their opinions or actions.","zh":"學生將列出的人物與其觀點或行動配對。"},{"en":"To match the people with something means to connect each person to the correct idea, action or description.","zh":"match the people with something 指把每個人物連接到正確想法、行動或描述。"},{"en":"In a reading task, students may match scientists with their discoveries.","zh":"在閱讀題中，學生可能把科學家與其發現配對。"},{"en":"This task checks whether students can locate who said or did what.","zh":"這類題目檢查學生能否找出誰說了或做了甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a person-information matching activity.","zh":"這個短語描述人物與資料的配對活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"opinions or deeds","meaning":"觀點或行動","examples":[{"en":"The task asks about both opinions and deeds mentioned in the passage.","zh":"題目問文章中提到的觀點或行動。"},{"en":"Opinions or deeds means what people think or what they actually do.","zh":"opinions or deeds 指人們的想法或他們實際做的事。"},{"en":"A history question may ask students to separate a leader’s opinions from his deeds.","zh":"歷史題可能要求學生區分領袖的觀點與行動。"},{"en":"Deeds can show whether a person acted according to their stated opinions.","zh":"行動可以顯示一個人是否按其聲稱的觀點行事。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both beliefs and actions.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋信念和行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"use any letter more than once","meaning":"可重複使用任何字母","examples":[{"en":"The same letter may be used more than once in the matching task.","zh":"在配對題中，同一字母可使用多於一次。"},{"en":"To use any letter more than once means an answer option can be repeated.","zh":"use any letter more than once 指答案選項可以重複使用。"},{"en":"In a paragraph-matching question, paragraph C may answer two separate items.","zh":"在段落配對題中，C 段可能回答兩個不同項目。"},{"en":"This instruction prevents students from forcing every answer to be different.","zh":"這項指示防止學生硬要每個答案都不同。"},{"en":"It is important to follow the instruction rather than assume a one-to-one match.","zh":"重要的是按指示作答，而不是假設一對一配對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"identify ways to optimise","meaning":"找出優化……的方法","examples":[{"en":"The executive identified ways to optimise energy use across the company.","zh":"該高層找出優化整間公司能源使用的方法。"},{"en":"To identify ways to optimise something means to find methods for making it work as efficiently as possible.","zh":"identify ways to optimise something 指找出令某事盡可能高效運作的方法。"},{"en":"A school may identify ways to optimise classroom space before admitting more students.","zh":"學校在取錄更多學生前，可能找出優化課室空間的方法。"},{"en":"Optimising energy use can reduce waste without reducing service quality.","zh":"優化能源使用可以減少浪費，而不降低服務質素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finding practical improvement methods.","zh":"這個短語描述尋找實際改善方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"major parts of a company","meaning":"公司主要部分","examples":[{"en":"Data centres form a major part of an Internet company’s operations.","zh":"數據中心構成互聯網公司營運的主要部分。"},{"en":"Major parts of a company are the important sections, systems or activities that keep the business running.","zh":"major parts of a company 指維持企業運作的重要部門、系統或活動。"},{"en":"In a delivery company, drivers and route-planning systems are major parts of the company.","zh":"在送貨公司中，司機和路線規劃系統都是公司的主要部分。"},{"en":"If a major part fails, the whole organisation may be affected.","zh":"如果主要部分失效，整個組織都可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to central business components, not small side details.","zh":"這個短語指核心業務組件，而不是小細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"describe a major innovation","meaning":"描述一項重大創新","examples":[{"en":"The speaker described a major innovation in computer-chip technology.","zh":"說話者描述了一項電腦晶片技術的重大創新。"},{"en":"To describe a major innovation means to explain an important new development.","zh":"describe a major innovation 指解釋一項重要的新發展。"},{"en":"A teacher may describe a major innovation in medicine to show how vaccines changed public health.","zh":"老師可能描述醫學上的重大創新，展示疫苗如何改變公共健康。"},{"en":"Major innovations can alter costs, habits and whole industries.","zh":"重大創新可以改變成本、習慣和整個行業。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on explaining a significant new idea or technology.","zh":"這個短語著重解釋重要的新想法或技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a small but important component","meaning":"細小但重要的組件","examples":[{"en":"A computer chip is a small but important component of a computer.","zh":"電腦晶片是電腦中細小但重要的組件。"},{"en":"A small but important component is a tiny part that plays a key role in a larger system.","zh":"small but important component 指在較大系統中發揮關鍵作用的細小部分。"},{"en":"A battery is a small but important component of a wireless mouse.","zh":"電池是無線滑鼠中細小但重要的組件。"},{"en":"If a small but important component fails, the whole device may stop working.","zh":"如果細小但重要的組件故障，整個裝置可能停止運作。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds students that size does not always show importance.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生，大小不一定代表重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"aim to develop","meaning":"旨在研發……","examples":[{"en":"The company aimed to develop affordable alternative energy sources.","zh":"該公司旨在研發可負擔的替代能源。"},{"en":"To aim to develop something means to plan and work toward creating or improving it.","zh":"aim to develop something 指計劃並努力創造或改善某事物。"},{"en":"A school may aim to develop students’ speaking confidence through weekly practice.","zh":"學校可能旨在透過每週練習培養學生的說話信心。"},{"en":"Development takes time because ideas must be tested and improved.","zh":"研發需要時間，因為想法必須被測試和改良。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear goal for future progress.","zh":"這個短語描述未來進步的清晰目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"alternative energy sources","meaning":"替代能源","examples":[{"en":"Solar, wind and geothermal power are alternative energy sources.","zh":"太陽能、風能和地熱能都是替代能源。"},{"en":"Alternative energy sources are energy sources used instead of traditional fossil fuels such as coal and oil.","zh":"alternative energy sources 指用來取代煤和石油等傳統化石燃料的能源來源。"},{"en":"A town may study alternative energy sources before building a new power system.","zh":"城鎮建立新供電系統前，可能研究替代能源。"},{"en":"Alternative sources can reduce pollution if they replace high-carbon fuels.","zh":"如果替代能源取代高碳燃料，就可以減少污染。"},{"en":"This phrase describes non-traditional or cleaner energy options.","zh":"這個短語描述非傳統或較潔淨的能源選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in the near future","meaning":"在不久將來","examples":[{"en":"The company hoped to lower renewable-energy costs in the near future.","zh":"該公司希望在不久將來降低可再生能源成本。"},{"en":"In the near future means soon, but not immediately today.","zh":"in the near future 指很快，但不是今天立即發生。"},{"en":"A school may introduce digital textbooks in the near future.","zh":"學校可能在不久將來引入電子課本。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a change is expected fairly soon.","zh":"當預期變化會較快發生時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It is less exact than giving a specific date.","zh":"它比給出具體日期較不精確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"estimate that","meaning":"估計","examples":[{"en":"The scientist estimated that computer energy consumption would rise sharply.","zh":"該科學家估計電腦能源消耗會急劇上升。"},{"en":"To estimate that means to make a careful guess based on available information.","zh":"estimate that 指根據現有資料作出謹慎推測。"},{"en":"A teacher may estimate that half the class needs more practice after checking homework.","zh":"老師檢查功課後，可能估計半班需要更多練習。"},{"en":"Estimates are useful when exact numbers are not yet available.","zh":"當精確數字尚未可得，估計很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an informed prediction, not a random guess.","zh":"這個短語引入有根據的預測，而不是隨意猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"an astonishing amount of","meaning":"驚人的……數量","examples":[{"en":"Computers were expected to consume an astonishing amount of energy.","zh":"電腦預計會消耗驚人的能源量。"},{"en":"An astonishing amount of something means a surprisingly large quantity.","zh":"astonishing amount of something 指令人驚訝的大量某物。"},{"en":"A busy restaurant may throw away an astonishing amount of food each night.","zh":"繁忙餐廳每晚可能丟棄驚人的食物量。"},{"en":"Astonishing amounts often make people realise a problem is bigger than expected.","zh":"驚人數量常令人意識到問題比預期更大。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses surprise at the size of a quantity.","zh":"這個短語強調對數量大小的驚訝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"current trends","meaning":"現時趨勢","examples":[{"en":"The prediction assumed that current trends would continue.","zh":"該預測假設現時趨勢會持續。"},{"en":"Current trends are the patterns or directions that are happening now.","zh":"current trends 指目前正在發生的模式或方向。"},{"en":"Current trends in education include more online lessons and digital homework.","zh":"教育中的現時趨勢包括更多網課和電子功課。"},{"en":"Predictions based on current trends may change if behaviour or technology changes.","zh":"以現時趨勢為基礎的預測，如果行為或科技改變，也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to present patterns used to think about the future.","zh":"這個短語指用來思考未來的當前模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a powerful technique","meaning":"強而有效的技術","examples":[{"en":"Virtualisation is a powerful technique for consolidating computer resources.","zh":"虛擬化技術是整合電腦資源的強而有效的技術。"},{"en":"A powerful technique is a method that produces strong results.","zh":"powerful technique 指能產生強大效果的方法。"},{"en":"Spaced repetition is a powerful technique for remembering vocabulary.","zh":"間隔重複是記憶詞彙的強而有效技巧。"},{"en":"A powerful technique can save time, reduce waste or improve performance.","zh":"強而有效的技術可以節省時間、減少浪費或改善表現。"},{"en":"This phrase praises the effectiveness of a method.","zh":"這個短語讚揚方法的有效性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"computing resources","meaning":"運算資源","examples":[{"en":"Virtualisation allows computing resources to be used more efficiently.","zh":"虛擬化技術讓運算資源能更有效地被使用。"},{"en":"Computing resources are the processing power, memory, storage and network capacity available for digital tasks.","zh":"computing resources 指可用於數碼任務的處理能力、記憶體、儲存和網絡容量。"},{"en":"A school’s computing resources may include laptops, servers and cloud storage.","zh":"學校的運算資源可能包括手提電腦、伺服器和雲端儲存。"},{"en":"Better use of computing resources can reduce the need to buy extra machines.","zh":"更好使用運算資源可以減少購買額外機器的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the digital capacity available for work.","zh":"這個短語指可用於工作的數碼能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"fail to activate","meaning":"未能啟用","examples":[{"en":"Most computer users fail to activate built-in energy-saving tools.","zh":"大多數電腦使用者未能啟用內置節能工具。"},{"en":"To fail to activate something means not to switch it on or make it work.","zh":"fail to activate something 指沒有開啟或啟動某功能。"},{"en":"A student may fail to activate spelling check before submitting an essay.","zh":"學生提交文章前可能未能啟用拼字檢查。"},{"en":"If users fail to activate power tools, computers may waste electricity unnecessarily.","zh":"如果使用者未能啟用電源工具，電腦可能不必要地浪費電力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes missing an important setup step.","zh":"這個短語描述錯過重要設定步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"built-in power-management tools","meaning":"內置電源管理工具","examples":[{"en":"Built-in power-management tools can reduce unnecessary electricity use.","zh":"內置電源管理工具可以減少不必要用電。"},{"en":"Built-in power-management tools are energy-saving features already included in a computer system.","zh":"built-in power-management tools 指已包含在電腦系統中的節能功能。"},{"en":"A laptop may have built-in power-management tools that dim the screen and sleep automatically.","zh":"手提電腦可能有內置電源管理工具，自動調暗屏幕並進入睡眠。"},{"en":"These tools help users save energy without buying extra software.","zh":"這些工具幫助使用者不用購買額外軟件也能節省能源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to included settings for controlling power use.","zh":"這個短語指用來控制電力使用的內置設定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"符合文中資料","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷每個陳述是否符合文章。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the text says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文本所說內容一致。"},{"en":"If the passage says servers need cooling, a statement saying the same thing agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說伺服器需要冷卻，而陳述說同一件事，就是符合文中資料。"},{"en":"Students should choose TRUE only when the text clearly supports the statement.","zh":"只有當文本清楚支持陳述時，學生才應選 TRUE。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE, FALSE and NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE、FALSE 和 NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文中資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the information given in the passage.","zh":"陳述可能與文章所給資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說法與文章內容相反。"},{"en":"If the text says computers use more energy but the statement says they use none, it contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文本說電腦使用更多能源，但陳述說完全不用能源，就是與文中資料矛盾。"},{"en":"Students choose FALSE when there is clear disagreement with the passage.","zh":"當與文章有明確不一致時，學生選 FALSE。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct conflict with the source text.","zh":"這個短語描述與來源文本直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"The response is used when there is no information on this point.","zh":"當文中沒有關於這一點的資料時，使用這個回答。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有說明該陳述是真還是假。"},{"en":"If a passage discusses Google but never mentions Apple, there is no information on Apple’s actions.","zh":"如果文章討論 Google 但從未提到 Apple，就沒有 Apple 行動的相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from outside knowledge when the text is silent.","zh":"當文本沒有提及時，學生不應根據外部知識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase explains when NOT GIVEN is appropriate.","zh":"這個短語解釋何時適合選 NOT GIVEN。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"an amount comparable to","meaning":"與……相若的數量","examples":[{"en":"Server cooling requires an amount of energy comparable to computing itself.","zh":"伺服器冷卻需要與運算本身相若的能源量。"},{"en":"An amount comparable to something means a quantity that is similar in size.","zh":"amount comparable to something 指大小相近的數量。"},{"en":"A family’s heating bill may be comparable to its grocery bill in winter.","zh":"家庭冬季取暖費可能與雜貨費相若。"},{"en":"Comparability helps readers understand scale by relating two quantities.","zh":"可比較性透過連繫兩個數量，幫助讀者理解規模。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two amounts are surprisingly close.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個數量驚人地接近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"have a severe impact on","meaning":"對……有嚴重影響","examples":[{"en":"The number of active servers may have a severe impact on energy demand.","zh":"活躍伺服器的數量可能對能源需求有嚴重影響。"},{"en":"To have a severe impact on something means to affect it very strongly and often negatively.","zh":"have a severe impact on something 指非常強烈且通常負面地影響某事。"},{"en":"A long transport strike can have a severe impact on students getting to school.","zh":"長時間交通罷工可以對學生上學有嚴重影響。"},{"en":"More active servers can sharply increase electricity and cooling needs.","zh":"更多活躍伺服器可以急劇增加電力和冷卻需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong effect that may create serious problems.","zh":"這個短語描述可能造成嚴重問題的強烈影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"Internet connection speeds","meaning":"互聯網連接速度","examples":[{"en":"Large server networks help maintain fast Internet connection speeds.","zh":"大型伺服器網絡有助維持快速互聯網連接速度。"},{"en":"Internet connection speeds describe how quickly data moves between a user’s device and the Internet.","zh":"Internet connection speeds 描述數據在使用者裝置和互聯網之間移動有多快。"},{"en":"Slow Internet connection speeds can make online lessons freeze or disconnect.","zh":"緩慢互聯網連接速度可以令網課畫面停頓或斷線。"},{"en":"Higher speeds require strong networks, servers and sometimes more energy.","zh":"更高速度需要強大網絡、伺服器，有時也需要更多能源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the speed of online access.","zh":"這個短語指上網速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"companies from other fields","meaning":"其他行業的公司","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to companies from other fields joining the initiative.","zh":"該陳述提到其他行業的公司加入倡議。"},{"en":"Companies from other fields are businesses that operate outside the main industry being discussed.","zh":"companies from other fields 指在所討論主要行業以外營運的企業。"},{"en":"A food company and a bank are companies from other fields if the topic is computing.","zh":"如果主題是運算，食品公司和銀行就是其他行業的公司。"},{"en":"When companies from other fields join an initiative, the issue may be wider than one industry.","zh":"當其他行業公司加入倡議，該議題可能不只涉及單一行業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organisations outside the original sector.","zh":"這個短語描述原本行業以外的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a collaborative effort","meaning":"協作行動","examples":[{"en":"Several technology companies joined a collaborative effort to save energy.","zh":"幾間科技公司加入一項節能協作行動。"},{"en":"A collaborative effort is a project or action done by several people or organisations working together.","zh":"collaborative effort 指由幾個人或組織共同合作完成的項目或行動。"},{"en":"Schools in the same district may start a collaborative effort to reduce food waste.","zh":"同一區的學校可能開始一項協作行動，以減少食物浪費。"},{"en":"Collaboration can share costs, knowledge and responsibility.","zh":"協作可以分擔成本、知識和責任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes teamwork toward a shared goal.","zh":"這個短語描述朝共同目標進行的團隊合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"government action","meaning":"政府行動","examples":[{"en":"Government action may encourage the purchase of efficient computers.","zh":"政府行動可能鼓勵購買高效電腦。"},{"en":"Government action means steps taken by public authorities to influence behaviour or solve problems.","zh":"government action 指公共當局為影響行為或解決問題而採取的措施。"},{"en":"Government action can include laws, subsidies, purchasing rules or public campaigns.","zh":"政府行動可以包括法律、補貼、採購規則或公共宣傳。"},{"en":"When government action changes buying standards, companies may adjust their products.","zh":"當政府行動改變購買標準，公司可能調整產品。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to official action by the state.","zh":"這個短語指國家或政府的官方行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be expected to help","meaning":"預期有助於……","examples":[{"en":"Stricter purchasing rules are expected to help save energy.","zh":"更嚴格採購規則預期有助於節省能源。"},{"en":"To be expected to help means people believe something will probably improve the situation.","zh":"be expected to help 指人們相信某事可能改善情況。"},{"en":"Extra reading practice is expected to help students improve vocabulary.","zh":"額外閱讀練習預期有助於學生改善詞彙量。"},{"en":"Expected benefits are predictions, so they should later be checked against real results.","zh":"預期好處是預測，因此之後應與實際結果核對。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a likely positive effect.","zh":"這個短語描述可能的正面效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"in the near future","meaning":"在不久將來","examples":[{"en":"New government requirements may be introduced in the near future.","zh":"新政府要求可能在不久將來推出。"},{"en":"In the near future means soon, but without giving an exact date.","zh":"in the near future 指很快，但沒有給出確切日期。"},{"en":"The school may update its computer rooms in the near future.","zh":"學校可能在不久將來更新電腦室。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a change is likely to happen fairly soon.","zh":"當某變化很可能較快發生時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It suggests something is approaching, but not necessarily immediately.","zh":"它暗示某事即將到來，但不一定立即發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"efforts to save energy","meaning":"節省能源的工作","examples":[{"en":"Efforts to save energy have reached the computer-chip level.","zh":"節省能源的工作已達到電腦晶片層面。"},{"en":"Efforts to save energy are actions taken to reduce electricity or fuel use.","zh":"efforts to save energy 指為減少電力或燃料使用而採取的行動。"},{"en":"A family’s efforts to save energy may include using fans instead of air conditioning.","zh":"家庭節省能源的工作可能包括使用風扇而不是冷氣。"},{"en":"Energy-saving efforts become stronger when they target both machines and user habits.","zh":"當節能工作同時針對機器和使用者習慣，效果會更強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical attempts to reduce energy consumption.","zh":"這個短語描述減少能源消耗的實際嘗試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"rise together","meaning":"一同上升","examples":[{"en":"Processing power and power consumption had risen together.","zh":"運算能力和耗電量曾一同上升。"},{"en":"To rise together means to increase at the same time.","zh":"rise together 指同時增加。"},{"en":"In summer, electricity use and air-conditioning demand often rise together.","zh":"夏天時，用電量和冷氣需求常一同上升。"},{"en":"When two things rise together, improving one may affect the other.","zh":"當兩件事一同上升，改善其中一項可能影響另一項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes linked increases.","zh":"這個短語描述互相關連的增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"switch to multicore technology","meaning":"轉用多核心技術","examples":[{"en":"Chipmakers switched to multicore technology to improve efficiency.","zh":"晶片製造商轉用多核心技術以改善效率。"},{"en":"To switch to multicore technology means to change from older chip designs to chips with several processing cores.","zh":"switch to multicore technology 指從舊晶片設計轉到有多個處理核心的晶片。"},{"en":"A computer brand may switch to multicore technology so laptops can run faster without using too much power.","zh":"電腦品牌可能轉用多核心技術，使手提電腦更快運行而不使用太多電力。"},{"en":"The switch can improve performance while reducing energy waste.","zh":"這種轉變可以改善效能，同時減少能源浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a technological shift in processor design.","zh":"這個短語描述處理器設計上的科技轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"integrate several processors","meaning":"整合多個處理器","examples":[{"en":"Multicore chips integrate several processors into one circuit.","zh":"多核心晶片把多個處理器整合到一個電路中。"},{"en":"To integrate several processors means to combine multiple processing units into one system.","zh":"integrate several processors 指把多個處理單元結合到一個系統中。"},{"en":"Engineers may integrate several processors so a device can handle many tasks at once.","zh":"工程師可能整合多個處理器，使裝置能同時處理多項任務。"},{"en":"Integration can save space and improve coordination between parts.","zh":"整合可以節省空間並改善部件之間的協調。"},{"en":"This phrase describes combining separate computing units.","zh":"這個短語描述結合分開的運算單元。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"achieve significant energy savings","meaning":"達到顯著節能效果","examples":[{"en":"The new chip design achieved significant energy savings.","zh":"新晶片設計達到顯著節能效果。"},{"en":"To achieve significant energy savings means to reduce energy use by an important and noticeable amount.","zh":"achieve significant energy savings 指把能源使用減少到重要而明顯的程度。"},{"en":"A school achieved significant energy savings after replacing old air conditioners.","zh":"學校更換舊冷氣機後達到顯著節能效果。"},{"en":"Significant savings can lower costs and reduce emissions at the same time.","zh":"顯著節能可以同時降低成本和減少排放。"},{"en":"This phrase describes successful and meaningful energy reduction.","zh":"這個短語描述成功而有意義的能源減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"continue to shrink circuits","meaning":"繼續縮小電路","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers continue to shrink circuits at the nanoscale.","zh":"製造商繼續在納米尺度上縮小電路。"},{"en":"To continue to shrink circuits means to keep making electronic circuits smaller and smaller.","zh":"continue to shrink circuits 指持續把電子電路做得越來越小。"},{"en":"Phone makers continue to shrink circuits so devices can become thinner and more powerful.","zh":"手機製造商繼續縮小電路，使裝置更薄且更強大。"},{"en":"Smaller circuits may need less electricity and allow more features in limited space.","zh":"較小電路可能需要較少電力，並在有限空間內容納更多功能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an ongoing trend in chip manufacturing.","zh":"這個短語描述晶片製造中的持續趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"maintain the same performance","meaning":"維持相同效能","examples":[{"en":"Smaller chips use less energy while maintaining the same performance.","zh":"較小晶片使用較少能源，同時維持相同效能。"},{"en":"To maintain the same performance means to keep the same level of speed, quality or output.","zh":"maintain the same performance 指保持相同水平的速度、質素或輸出。"},{"en":"A new laptop may maintain the same performance while using less battery power.","zh":"新手提電腦可能在使用較少電池電力時維持相同效能。"},{"en":"Maintaining performance while reducing energy use is a sign of better efficiency.","zh":"在減少能源使用時維持效能，是更高效率的標誌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes keeping results steady even when resources are reduced.","zh":"這個短語描述即使資源減少仍保持結果穩定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words taken from the passage.","zh":"學生使用取自文章的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill in missing words so the shortened version of the text makes sense.","zh":"complete the summary 指填入缺失字詞，使文本的簡短版本意思完整。"},{"en":"A student should read the whole summary before choosing words from the passage.","zh":"學生選擇文章字詞前，應先閱讀整段摘要。"},{"en":"Grammar and meaning around each gap help students decide the correct answer.","zh":"每個空格周圍的文法和意思幫助學生判斷正確答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in reading tests.","zh":"這個短語是閱讀測驗中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個詞","examples":[{"en":"Each summary answer must contain no more than three words.","zh":"每個摘要答案必須包含不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must be one, two or three words only.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案只能是一個、兩個或三個詞。"},{"en":"If the limit is no more than three words, “carbon dioxide emissions” is acceptable.","zh":"如果限制是不多於三個詞，“carbon dioxide emissions” 是可以的。"},{"en":"Writing four words can lose marks even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫四個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word-limit rule for exam answers.","zh":"這個短語為考試答案給出嚴格字數限制規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 140 - Digital diet.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 141":[{"front":"the history of the guitar","meaning":"結他的歷史","examples":[{"en":"The passage traces the history of the guitar from ancient stringed instruments to modern electric models.","zh":"文章追溯結他的歷史，由古代弦樂器到現代電結他型號。"},{"en":"The history of the guitar is the story of how the instrument developed in name, shape, sound, and technology over time.","zh":"the history of the guitar 指這種樂器在名稱、外形、聲音和技術上如何隨時間發展的故事。"},{"en":"A music teacher may explain the history of the guitar before students compare acoustic and electric models.","zh":"音樂老師可能先解釋結他的歷史，再讓學生比較木結他和電結他型號。"},{"en":"Understanding the history of the guitar helps learners see why today’s instrument has its familiar shape and strings.","zh":"理解結他的歷史有助學習者明白為何今日樂器有熟悉的外形和弦線。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the instrument’s long development, not just famous modern guitarists.","zh":"這個短語指樂器的長期發展，而不只是著名現代結他手。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be brought into English","meaning":"被引入英語","examples":[{"en":"The word “guitar” was brought into English from Spanish.","zh":"“guitar” 這個詞由西班牙語被引入英語。"},{"en":"When a word is brought into English, it enters English from another language.","zh":"當一個詞 be brought into English，它就是由另一種語言進入英語。"},{"en":"The word “karaoke” was brought into English from Japanese.","zh":"“karaoke” 這個詞由日語被引入英語。"},{"en":"Words are often brought into English when people borrow new objects, foods, ideas, or cultural practices.","zh":"當人們借用新物件、食物、想法或文化做法時，詞語常會被引入英語。"},{"en":"The phrase describes language borrowing, not physically carrying an object into England.","zh":"這個短語描述語言借用，而不是把物件實際帶入英國。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as an adaptation of","meaning":"作為……的改寫形式","examples":[{"en":"The English word developed as an adaptation of the Spanish word “guitarra”.","zh":"這個英語詞作為西班牙語 “guitarra” 的改寫形式發展而來。"},{"en":"As an adaptation of means as a changed version of something earlier.","zh":"as an adaptation of 指作為某個較早事物的改動版本。"},{"en":"A film may be made as an adaptation of a famous novel.","zh":"電影可以作為著名小說的改編版本被製作。"},{"en":"When a word moves between languages, its spelling or pronunciation may change as an adaptation of the original form.","zh":"當詞語在語言之間移動，其串法或發音可能作為原本形式的改寫而改變。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something is based on an earlier model but not exactly identical.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事物建基於早期版本，但並非完全相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in turn","meaning":"繼而；反過來","examples":[{"en":"The Spanish word was, in turn, derived from Greek.","zh":"這個西班牙語詞繼而源自希臘語。"},{"en":"In turn means as the next step in a chain of events or relationships.","zh":"in turn 指作為一連串事件或關係中的下一步。"},{"en":"A student learns from a teacher and, in turn, teaches the same skill to a younger brother.","zh":"學生向老師學習，繼而把同一技能教給弟弟。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show that one source came from an earlier source before it influenced something else.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示一個來源先來自更早來源，之後再影響其他事物。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining a sequence of influence.","zh":"它適合用於解釋影響的連鎖次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be derived from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"The word “guitarra” was derived from the Greek word “kithara”.","zh":"“guitarra” 這個詞源自希臘語 “kithara”。"},{"en":"To be derived from something means to come from it as an origin or source.","zh":"be derived from something 指以某事物作為起源或來源。"},{"en":"Many English scientific words are derived from Latin or Greek.","zh":"許多英語科學詞彙源自拉丁語或希臘語。"},{"en":"If a word is derived from another language, its modern form may still keep traces of the older word.","zh":"如果一個詞源自另一種語言，其現代形式可能仍保留舊詞痕跡。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used when tracing origins.","zh":"這個短語常用於追溯起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"trace the roots of","meaning":"追溯……的根源","examples":[{"en":"Researchers can trace the roots of the word through several languages.","zh":"研究人員可以透過幾種語言追溯這個詞的根源。"},{"en":"To trace the roots of something means to follow its origin back through history.","zh":"trace the roots of something 指沿歷史追尋某事物的起源。"},{"en":"A historian may trace the roots of a festival through old records and village stories.","zh":"歷史學家可能透過舊紀錄和村落故事追溯節日的根源。"},{"en":"Tracing roots helps explain why a modern word, custom, or object has its present form.","zh":"追溯根源有助解釋為何現代詞語、習俗或物件有現今形式。"},{"en":"The phrase is about finding origins, not growing plant roots.","zh":"這個短語關於尋找起源，而不是植物根部生長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"further back","meaning":"追溯至更早時期","examples":[{"en":"The roots of the word can be traced further back into linguistic history.","zh":"這個詞的根源可以追溯至語言演變史中更早時期。"},{"en":"Further back means to an earlier point in time or history.","zh":"further back 指回到時間或歷史中較早的點。"},{"en":"A family may trace its records further back after finding an old birth certificate.","zh":"家庭找到舊出生證明後，可能把家族紀錄追溯至更早時期。"},{"en":"Looking further back can reveal older influences that are not obvious at first.","zh":"向更早時期追溯，可以揭示一開始不明顯的更古老影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes going earlier in time, not moving physically backwards.","zh":"這個短語描述回到更早時間，而不是身體向後移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"linguistic history","meaning":"語言演變史","examples":[{"en":"The word has a long and complex linguistic history.","zh":"這個詞有悠長而複雜的語言演變史。"},{"en":"Linguistic history is the history of how a word, language, or sound changes over time.","zh":"linguistic history 指詞語、語言或聲音如何隨時間改變的歷史。"},{"en":"The linguistic history of “tea” shows how trade helped spread words across countries.","zh":"“tea” 的語言演變史顯示貿易如何幫助詞語跨國傳播。"},{"en":"Studying linguistic history can explain why similar words appear in different languages.","zh":"研究語言演變史可以解釋為何相似詞語出現在不同語言中。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to language development, not political history.","zh":"這個短語指語言發展，而不是政治歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a combination of","meaning":"……的組合","examples":[{"en":"The original term may have been a combination of two linguistic roots.","zh":"原本詞語可能是兩個語言詞根的組合。"},{"en":"A combination of things means two or more things joined together.","zh":"a combination of things 指兩個或以上事物結合在一起。"},{"en":"A good study plan is often a combination of reading, practice, and review.","zh":"好的學習計劃通常是閱讀、練習和複習的組合。"},{"en":"When two word roots combine, they can create a new word with a blended meaning.","zh":"當兩個詞根結合，它們可以創造出具有混合意思的新詞。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the result comes from more than one part.","zh":"這個短語強調結果來自多於一個部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Indo-European stem","meaning":"印歐語詞幹","examples":[{"en":"The word may contain an Indo-European stem meaning music.","zh":"這個詞可能包含一個意指音樂的印歐語詞幹。"},{"en":"An Indo-European stem is an ancient word part from the language family that includes English, Greek, Latin, and many others.","zh":"Indo-European stem 指來自印歐語系的古老詞語部分；英語、希臘語、拉丁語和許多語言都屬於該語系。"},{"en":"A linguistics class may study an Indo-European stem to explain related words in different languages.","zh":"語言學課可能研究印歐語詞幹，以解釋不同語言中的相關詞語。"},{"en":"Ancient stems can survive in modern words even after spelling and pronunciation change.","zh":"即使串法和發音改變，古老詞幹仍可以保存在現代詞語中。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a historical language root, not a plant stem.","zh":"這個短語指歷史語言詞根，而不是植物莖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"meaning music","meaning":"意指音樂","examples":[{"en":"The stem “guit-” is said to have a meaning connected with music.","zh":"據說 “guit-” 這個詞幹有與音樂相關的意思。"},{"en":"Meaning music means carrying an idea related to music, sound, or musical performance.","zh":"meaning music 指帶有與音樂、聲音或音樂表演相關的意思。"},{"en":"A word root meaning music may appear in the names of instruments or songs.","zh":"意指音樂的詞根可能出現在樂器或歌曲名稱中。"},{"en":"If a root carries a musical meaning, it can help explain why similar instrument names share that root.","zh":"如果詞根帶有音樂意思，它可以幫助解釋為何相似樂器名稱共享該詞根。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the sense attached to a word part.","zh":"這個短語解釋詞語部分所承載的意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"linguistic root","meaning":"語言詞根","examples":[{"en":"The element “-tar” is a linguistic root meaning string or chord.","zh":"“-tar” 這個元素是一個意指弦線或和弦的語言詞根。"},{"en":"A linguistic root is a basic word part from which other words develop.","zh":"linguistic root 指其他詞語由其發展而來的基本詞語部分。"},{"en":"In English, a root such as “port” can relate to carrying, as in “transport”.","zh":"在英語中，像 “port” 這樣的詞根可與 carrying 有關，例如 “transport”。"},{"en":"Knowing a root helps students guess meanings of unfamiliar related words.","zh":"認識詞根有助學生猜測陌生相關詞語的意思。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the basic origin inside a word.","zh":"這個短語指詞語內部的基本來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"chord or string","meaning":"和弦或弦線","examples":[{"en":"The root “-tar” may mean chord or string.","zh":"“-tar” 這個詞根可能意指和弦或弦線。"},{"en":"Chord or string refers either to a group of musical notes played together or to the stretched line on an instrument.","zh":"chord or string 指一起彈奏的一組音，或樂器上被拉緊的弦線。"},{"en":"A guitarist presses a string to change the note and may play several notes together as a chord.","zh":"結他手按住弦線改變音高，也可能把幾個音一起彈成和弦。"},{"en":"If a word root means string, it naturally fits the name of a stringed instrument.","zh":"如果詞根意指弦線，它自然適合用於弦樂器名稱。"},{"en":"The phrase links musical sound with the physical strings that produce it.","zh":"這個短語把音樂聲音與產生聲音的實體弦線連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be common to","meaning":"為多種……所共有","examples":[{"en":"The root “-tar” is common to a number of languages.","zh":"“-tar” 這個詞根為多種語言所共有。"},{"en":"To be common to several things means to be shared by them.","zh":"be common to several things 指被它們共同擁有。"},{"en":"Respect for elders is common to many cultures, though it is shown in different ways.","zh":"尊重長者為許多文化所共有，雖然表現方式不同。"},{"en":"If a word root is common to many languages, it may come from an older shared source.","zh":"如果一個詞根為多種語言所共有，它可能來自更古老的共同來源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something shared, not something ordinary only.","zh":"這個短語描述共同擁有，而不只是普通常見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a number of languages","meaning":"多種語言","examples":[{"en":"The same linguistic root appears in a number of languages.","zh":"同一個語言詞根出現在多種語言中。"},{"en":"A number of languages means several languages, without giving an exact number.","zh":"a number of languages 指幾種語言，但沒有給出確實數量。"},{"en":"The word for “mother” sounds similar in a number of languages.","zh":"“mother” 一詞在多種語言中聽起來相似。"},{"en":"When a root appears in several languages, linguists may investigate a shared history.","zh":"當一個詞根出現在幾種語言中，語言學家可能研究共同歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a general plural quantity.","zh":"這個短語提供概括的複數數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be found in","meaning":"可在……中找到","examples":[{"en":"The root “-tar” can also be found in the word “sitar”.","zh":"“-tar” 這個詞根也可在 “sitar” 一詞中找到。"},{"en":"To be found in something means to exist or appear inside it.","zh":"be found in something 指存在或出現在某物之中。"},{"en":"The sound “photo” can be found in words like “photograph” and “photosynthesis”.","zh":"“photo” 這個音可以在 “photograph” 和 “photosynthesis” 等詞中找到。"},{"en":"Finding the same root in several words can show a connection in meaning or history.","zh":"在幾個詞中找到同一詞根，可以顯示意思或歷史上的關係。"},{"en":"The phrase describes presence inside a word, place, or object.","zh":"這個短語描述存在於詞語、地方或物件之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sitar","meaning":"西塔琴","examples":[{"en":"The sitar is another stringed musical instrument.","zh":"西塔琴是另一種弦樂器。"},{"en":"A sitar is a long-necked stringed instrument associated especially with Indian classical music.","zh":"sitar 指一種長頸弦樂器，尤其與印度古典音樂有關。"},{"en":"A music student may compare the sound of a sitar with that of a guitar.","zh":"音樂學生可能比較西塔琴和結他的聲音。"},{"en":"Because the sitar has strings, its name helps illustrate roots connected with stringed instruments.","zh":"因為西塔琴有弦，其名稱有助說明與弦樂器相關的詞根。"},{"en":"The word names a specific instrument, not a general word for all guitars.","zh":"這個詞命名一種特定樂器，而不是所有結他的通稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stringed musical instrument","meaning":"弦樂器","examples":[{"en":"Both the guitar and the sitar are stringed musical instruments.","zh":"結他和西塔琴都是弦樂器。"},{"en":"A stringed musical instrument is an instrument that makes sound through vibrating strings.","zh":"stringed musical instrument 指透過弦線震動發聲的樂器。"},{"en":"Violins, guitars, harps, and sitars are stringed musical instruments.","zh":"小提琴、結他、豎琴和西塔琴都是弦樂器。"},{"en":"If the strings are plucked, bowed, or struck, they vibrate and produce musical notes.","zh":"當弦線被撥、拉或敲擊，它們會震動並產生音符。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how the instrument produces sound.","zh":"這個短語描述樂器如何發聲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"spelling and pronunciation","meaning":"拼寫和發音","examples":[{"en":"The spelling and pronunciation of the word differ between languages.","zh":"這個詞的拼寫和發音因語言而有所不同。"},{"en":"Spelling and pronunciation are how a word is written and how it is spoken.","zh":"spelling and pronunciation 指一個詞如何書寫以及如何讀出。"},{"en":"English learners often notice that spelling and pronunciation do not always match.","zh":"英語學習者常注意到拼寫和發音不一定相符。"},{"en":"When a word enters a new language, its spelling and pronunciation may change to fit local habits.","zh":"當詞語進入新語言，其拼寫和發音可能會改變以配合本地習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both written form and sound.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋書面形式和聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"differ between languages","meaning":"因語言而有所不同","examples":[{"en":"The word for guitar differs between languages.","zh":"表示結他的詞語因語言而有所不同。"},{"en":"To differ between languages means to have different forms, sounds, or uses in different languages.","zh":"differ between languages 指在不同語言中有不同形式、聲音或用法。"},{"en":"The word for “school” differs between languages, even when the idea is similar.","zh":"表示「學校」的詞語因語言而有所不同，即使概念相似。"},{"en":"Differences between languages can make translation difficult but also reveal history.","zh":"語言之間的差異可以令翻譯困難，但也能揭示歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase describes variation across languages.","zh":"這個短語描述跨語言差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"key elements","meaning":"關鍵元素","examples":[{"en":"The key elements of the word have survived throughout history.","zh":"這個詞的關鍵元素貫穿歷史保存了下來。"},{"en":"Key elements are the most important parts of something.","zh":"key elements 指某事物中最重要的部分。"},{"en":"In an essay, the key elements are a clear answer, evidence, and explanation.","zh":"在作文中，關鍵元素包括清楚答案、證據和解釋。"},{"en":"If key elements survive, a word or design can change while still remaining recognisable.","zh":"如果關鍵元素保存下來，詞語或設計即使改變仍可被認出。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the parts that matter most.","zh":"這個短語指出最重要的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be present in","meaning":"存在於……之中","examples":[{"en":"Similar roots have been present in most words for guitar.","zh":"相似詞根存在於大多數表示結他的詞語之中。"},{"en":"To be present in something means to exist or appear inside it.","zh":"be present in something 指存在或出現在某物之中。"},{"en":"A clear topic sentence should be present in every good paragraph.","zh":"每個好段落中都應存在清楚主題句。"},{"en":"If a root is present in many related words, it can suggest a shared origin.","zh":"如果詞根存在於許多相關詞語中，它可能暗示共同起源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something existing within a larger thing.","zh":"這個短語描述某物存在於較大事物之內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"throughout history","meaning":"貫穿歷史；歷來","examples":[{"en":"The main elements of the word have remained present throughout history.","zh":"這個詞的主要元素貫穿歷史一直存在。"},{"en":"Throughout history means across a long period of the past up to later times.","zh":"throughout history 指跨越漫長過去並延續至後來時期。"},{"en":"Throughout history, people have used music for celebration, mourning, and storytelling.","zh":"歷來，人們使用音樂來慶祝、哀悼和講故事。"},{"en":"If an idea survives throughout history, it has lasted through many social and cultural changes.","zh":"如果一個想法貫穿歷史存活下來，它就經歷了許多社會和文化變化。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises long-term continuity.","zh":"這個短語強調長期延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"gain popularity as","meaning":"作為……而普及","examples":[{"en":"The guitar gained much of its popularity as a musical instrument in the modern era.","zh":"結他在現代作為樂器獲得大部分普及度。"},{"en":"To gain popularity as something means to become widely liked or used in that role.","zh":"gain popularity as something 指以某種角色變得廣受喜愛或使用。"},{"en":"Online tutoring gained popularity as a flexible way to learn after school.","zh":"網上補習作為放學後彈性學習方式而普及。"},{"en":"An object gains popularity when people find it useful, enjoyable, or fashionable.","zh":"當人們覺得某物有用、有趣或時尚，它就會變得普及。"},{"en":"The phrase describes becoming more accepted in a particular function.","zh":"這個短語描述在特定功能上變得更被接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"modern era","meaning":"現代","examples":[{"en":"The guitar became especially popular during the modern era.","zh":"結他在現代變得特別受歡迎。"},{"en":"The modern era means the recent historical period, especially compared with ancient or medieval times.","zh":"modern era 指較近期的歷史時期，尤其相對於古代或中世紀。"},{"en":"In the modern era, smartphones have changed how students study and communicate.","zh":"在現代，智能電話改變了學生學習和溝通的方式。"},{"en":"New technology and mass media often make cultural objects spread faster in the modern era.","zh":"新科技和大眾媒體常令文化物件在現代傳播得更快。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts recent history with earlier periods.","zh":"這個短語把近期歷史與較早時期作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"guitar-like instruments","meaning":"類似結他的樂器","examples":[{"en":"Guitar-like instruments existed thousands of years before the modern guitar.","zh":"類似結他的樂器早在現代結他出現數千年前已存在。"},{"en":"Guitar-like instruments are instruments that resemble guitars in shape, strings, or playing method.","zh":"guitar-like instruments 指在外形、弦線或演奏方式上類似結他的樂器。"},{"en":"A child may call a small lute a guitar-like instrument if it has strings and a body.","zh":"如果小魯特琴有弦和琴身，孩子可能稱它為類似結他的樂器。"},{"en":"Such instruments show that the idea of plucked strings is much older than the modern guitar.","zh":"這類樂器顯示撥弦概念比現代結他古老得多。"},{"en":"The phrase means similar to a guitar, not exactly a guitar.","zh":"這個短語指類似結他，而不是完全等同結他。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be in existence","meaning":"已經存在","examples":[{"en":"Guitar-like instruments have been in existence for more than 5,000 years.","zh":"類似結他的樂器已經存在超過五千年。"},{"en":"To be in existence means to exist or be present in the world.","zh":"be in existence 指存在於世界上。"},{"en":"Some school traditions have been in existence for over a century.","zh":"一些學校傳統已經存在超過一個世紀。"},{"en":"If something has been in existence for thousands of years, it has survived many cultural changes.","zh":"如果某物已存在數千年，它就經歷了許多文化變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continued existence over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間持續存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"numerous cultures","meaning":"眾多文化","examples":[{"en":"Similar stringed instruments appeared in numerous cultures.","zh":"相似弦樂器出現在眾多文化中。"},{"en":"Numerous cultures means many different societies or cultural groups.","zh":"numerous cultures 指許多不同社會或文化群體。"},{"en":"Rice dishes appear in numerous cultures, though each place cooks them differently.","zh":"米飯菜式出現在眾多文化中，雖然每個地方煮法不同。"},{"en":"When similar objects appear in many cultures, they may answer a common human need.","zh":"當相似物件出現在許多文化中，它們可能回應了共同的人類需要。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises wide cultural variety.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛文化多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"throughout the world","meaning":"遍及世界","examples":[{"en":"Guitar-like instruments were played throughout the world.","zh":"類似結他的樂器在世界各地被演奏。"},{"en":"Throughout the world means in many places across the whole world.","zh":"throughout the world 指在全世界許多地方。"},{"en":"English songs are listened to throughout the world through streaming platforms.","zh":"英文歌曲透過串流平台在世界各地被聆聽。"},{"en":"When an instrument spreads throughout the world, different cultures may adapt it in their own ways.","zh":"當樂器遍及世界，不同文化可能以自己的方式改造它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes global spread.","zh":"這個短語描述全球傳播。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the modern eye and ear","meaning":"現代人的視覺和聽覺","examples":[{"en":"The earliest instruments that the modern eye and ear would recognise appeared centuries ago.","zh":"現代人的視覺和聽覺會認得出的最早樂器在數百年前出現。"},{"en":"The modern eye and ear means what people today would see and hear as familiar.","zh":"the modern eye and ear 指今日人們會視為和聽為熟悉的感覺。"},{"en":"A very old building may still look like a school to the modern eye if it has classrooms and desks.","zh":"如果一座很舊的建築有課室和書桌，現代人視覺上仍可能認出它像學校。"},{"en":"If an instrument is recognisable to modern eyes and ears, it shares important features with today’s version.","zh":"如果樂器能被現代人的視覺和聽覺認出，它就與今日版本共享重要特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to modern perception through sight and sound.","zh":"這個短語指透過視覺和聽覺作出的現代感知。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"recognise something as","meaning":"將……辨認為……","examples":[{"en":"Modern listeners would recognise these instruments as acoustic guitars.","zh":"現代聽眾會將這些樂器辨認為木結他。"},{"en":"To recognise something as something else means to identify it as belonging to that type.","zh":"recognise something as something else 指把某物辨認為屬於某類。"},{"en":"A student may recognise a formal letter as a complaint if it asks for a refund politely.","zh":"如果一封正式信禮貌地要求退款，學生可能將它辨認為投訴信。"},{"en":"People recognise an object when it has enough familiar features.","zh":"當物件有足夠熟悉特徵，人們就能認出它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes identification based on known signs.","zh":"這個短語描述根據已知跡象作出辨認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"normal acoustic guitar","meaning":"一般木結他","examples":[{"en":"The earliest recognisable examples resemble a normal acoustic guitar.","zh":"最早可辨認的例子像一般木結他。"},{"en":"A normal acoustic guitar is a standard non-electric guitar that produces sound through its hollow wooden body.","zh":"normal acoustic guitar 指標準非電結他，透過中空木製琴身發聲。"},{"en":"A beginner often starts with a normal acoustic guitar before buying an electric one.","zh":"初學者常先用一般木結他，再買電結他。"},{"en":"Acoustic guitars can be played without an amplifier because the body helps project sound.","zh":"木結他不用擴音器也能演奏，因為琴身幫助傳出聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts a familiar wooden guitar with electric or unusual models.","zh":"這個短語把熟悉的木製結他與電結他或不尋常型號作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"date from","meaning":"始於；可追溯至","examples":[{"en":"The earliest recognisable acoustic guitars date from about 500 years ago.","zh":"最早可辨認的木結他可追溯至約五百年前。"},{"en":"To date from a time means to come from or have existed since that time.","zh":"date from a time 指來自或自某時期起已存在。"},{"en":"This school building dates from the 1950s, so it needs careful maintenance.","zh":"這座校舍始於1950年代，所以需要仔細保養。"},{"en":"Dating an object helps historians place it in the correct period.","zh":"為物件定年幫助歷史學家把它放在正確時期。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to describe historical origin or age.","zh":"這個短語用於描述歷史起源或年代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"about 500 years ago","meaning":"約五百年前","examples":[{"en":"Recognisable acoustic guitars appeared about 500 years ago.","zh":"可辨認的木結他大約在五百年前出現。"},{"en":"About 500 years ago means approximately five centuries before the present.","zh":"about 500 years ago 指距今大約五個世紀。"},{"en":"A castle built about 500 years ago may still show how people defended towns in the past.","zh":"約五百年前建成的城堡可能仍顯示昔日人們如何防衛城鎮。"},{"en":"When an instrument form lasts for centuries, it has likely met musicians’ needs well.","zh":"當一種樂器形式延續數百年，它很可能很好地滿足了音樂人需要。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate historical time.","zh":"這個短語提供大約歷史時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"prior to this time","meaning":"在此之前","examples":[{"en":"Prior to this time, many other kinds of stringed instruments were used.","zh":"在此之前，許多其他種類的弦樂器被使用。"},{"en":"Prior to this time means before the period being discussed.","zh":"prior to this time 指在所討論時期之前。"},{"en":"Prior to the exam, students should check the question format and time limit.","zh":"在考試之前，學生應檢查題型和時間限制。"},{"en":"The phrase helps separate earlier developments from later ones.","zh":"這個短語幫助把較早發展與較後發展分開。"},{"en":"It is more formal than “before this”.","zh":"它比 before this 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be in use","meaning":"被使用","examples":[{"en":"Stringed instruments were in use throughout the ancient world.","zh":"弦樂器在整個古代世界被使用。"},{"en":"To be in use means to be used by people at that time.","zh":"be in use 指在當時被人使用。"},{"en":"Old textbooks may still be in use if schools cannot afford new copies.","zh":"如果學校買不起新書，舊教科書可能仍被使用。"},{"en":"If an object remains in use for a long time, it usually serves a practical purpose.","zh":"如果物件長時間仍被使用，它通常有實際用途。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active use, not merely existence.","zh":"這個短語描述被實際使用，而不只是存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be known primarily from","meaning":"主要透過……為人所知","examples":[{"en":"Many early instruments are known primarily from visual depictions.","zh":"許多早期樂器主要透過圖像記錄為人所知。"},{"en":"To be known primarily from something means that most knowledge about it comes from that source.","zh":"be known primarily from something 指關於某事的大部分知識來自該來源。"},{"en":"Some ancient dances are known primarily from paintings and written descriptions.","zh":"一些古代舞蹈主要透過畫作和文字描述為人所知。"},{"en":"If physical objects do not survive, pictures may become the main evidence.","zh":"如果實物沒有保存下來，圖像可能成為主要證據。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the main source of our knowledge.","zh":"這個短語顯示我們知識的主要來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"visual depictions","meaning":"視覺描繪；圖像記錄","examples":[{"en":"Paintings and carvings provide visual depictions of early instruments.","zh":"繪畫和雕刻提供早期樂器的視覺描繪。"},{"en":"Visual depictions are pictures, carvings, drawings, or other images showing what something looked like.","zh":"visual depictions 指顯示某物外貌的圖畫、雕刻、繪圖或其他圖像。"},{"en":"A museum poster may use visual depictions to show how ancient clothing was worn.","zh":"博物館海報可能用圖像記錄展示古代衣服如何穿著。"},{"en":"Visual evidence helps historians study objects that no longer physically exist.","zh":"視覺證據幫助歷史學家研究已不再實際存在的物件。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to image-based records.","zh":"這個短語指以圖像為基礎的紀錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"continued existence","meaning":"持續保存至今","examples":[{"en":"Few of the earliest instruments have survived in continued existence.","zh":"最早期樂器中很少能持續保存至今。"},{"en":"Continued existence means remaining present or surviving over time.","zh":"continued existence 指隨時間仍然存在或存活下來。"},{"en":"The continued existence of an old school tradition depends on students still practising it.","zh":"舊學校傳統能否持續存在，取決於學生是否仍實踐它。"},{"en":"Fragile objects may not survive in continued existence unless they are carefully protected.","zh":"易碎物件若不被仔細保護，可能無法持續保存至今。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses survival across time.","zh":"這個短語強調跨時間保存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"music written for","meaning":"為……創作的音樂","examples":[{"en":"Little music written for these early instruments still survives.","zh":"為這些早期樂器創作的音樂很少仍保存下來。"},{"en":"Music written for an instrument means music composed especially to be played on that instrument.","zh":"music written for an instrument 指特別為某樂器演奏而創作的音樂。"},{"en":"A piano teacher may choose music written for beginners so students can practise comfortably.","zh":"鋼琴老師可能選擇為初學者創作的音樂，讓學生能舒適練習。"},{"en":"If written music does not survive, historians know less about how an instrument sounded.","zh":"如果書面樂譜沒有保存下來，歷史學家對樂器聲音的了解就較少。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a piece of music with its intended instrument.","zh":"這個短語把音樂作品與其預定樂器連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the majority of","meaning":"大部分","examples":[{"en":"The majority of the depictions show relatively simple instruments.","zh":"大部分圖像記錄顯示相對簡單的樂器。"},{"en":"The majority of something means more than half or most of it.","zh":"the majority of something 指超過一半或大多數。"},{"en":"The majority of students in the class chose the speaking course.","zh":"班中大部分學生選擇了口語課程。"},{"en":"If the majority of evidence points one way, researchers may treat that pattern as important.","zh":"如果大部分證據指向同一方向，研究人員可能把該模式視為重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the larger part of a group.","zh":"這個短語描述一個群體中較大部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"simple stringed instruments","meaning":"簡單弦樂器","examples":[{"en":"Many ancient pictures show simple stringed instruments.","zh":"許多古代圖畫顯示簡單弦樂器。"},{"en":"Simple stringed instruments are basic musical instruments that produce sound with strings and have few complex parts.","zh":"simple stringed instruments 指透過弦線發聲且複雜部件較少的基本樂器。"},{"en":"A child’s toy harp is a simple stringed instrument because it has strings but little mechanism.","zh":"孩子的玩具豎琴是簡單弦樂器，因為它有弦但機械結構很少。"},{"en":"Early instruments were often simpler because makers had fewer tools and materials.","zh":"早期樂器通常較簡單，因為製作者有較少工具和材料。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts basic instruments with more developed modern ones.","zh":"這個短語把基本樂器與較發達現代樂器作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lack some of the parts","meaning":"缺少部分……","examples":[{"en":"Early instruments often lacked some of the parts found on modern guitars.","zh":"早期樂器常缺少現代結他上的部分部件。"},{"en":"To lack some of the parts means to be missing certain pieces that another object has.","zh":"lack some of the parts 指缺少另一物件所具有的某些部件。"},{"en":"A cheap school bag may lack some of the parts found on hiking backpacks, such as chest straps.","zh":"便宜書包可能缺少行山背囊上的部分部件，例如胸帶。"},{"en":"Missing parts can make an older object work differently from its modern version.","zh":"缺少部件可以令舊物件與現代版本運作方式不同。"},{"en":"The phrase describes incomplete similarity, not total absence.","zh":"這個短語描述相似但不完整，而不是完全沒有。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"define a modern guitar","meaning":"界定現代結他","examples":[{"en":"Certain structural parts help define a modern guitar.","zh":"某些結構部件有助界定現代結他。"},{"en":"To define a modern guitar means to identify the features that make it recognisable as a modern guitar.","zh":"define a modern guitar 指指出令它可被辨認為現代結他的特徵。"},{"en":"The shape, strings, neck, and sound hole can help define a normal acoustic guitar.","zh":"外形、弦線、琴頸和音孔可以幫助界定一般木結他。"},{"en":"If an old instrument lacks these features, people may not classify it as a guitar.","zh":"如果舊樂器缺少這些特徵，人們可能不會把它分類為結他。"},{"en":"The phrase is about essential identifying features.","zh":"這個短語關於必要辨認特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have more in common with","meaning":"與……有更多共通點","examples":[{"en":"Some early instruments have more in common with the lute than the guitar.","zh":"有些早期樂器與魯特琴比與結他有更多共通點。"},{"en":"To have more in common with something means to share more features with it than with another thing.","zh":"have more in common with something 指與某物共享的特徵比與另一物更多。"},{"en":"A tablet has more in common with a laptop than with a paper notebook.","zh":"平板電腦與手提電腦比與紙本筆記簿有更多共通點。"},{"en":"Shared features help people decide which category an object belongs to.","zh":"共同特徵幫助人判斷物件屬於哪一類。"},{"en":"The phrase is used for comparison based on similarity.","zh":"這個短語用於基於相似性的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the lute","meaning":"魯特琴","examples":[{"en":"Several ancient instruments resembled the lute more closely than the guitar.","zh":"幾種古代樂器比起結他更接近魯特琴。"},{"en":"The lute is an old stringed instrument with a rounded body and a neck, often played by plucking.","zh":"lute 指一種古老弦樂器，有圓形琴身和琴頸，通常以撥弦方式演奏。"},{"en":"A museum may display a lute beside early guitars to show differences in instrument design.","zh":"博物館可能把魯特琴放在早期結他旁邊，以展示樂器設計差異。"},{"en":"Because some early instruments look like lutes, historians must be careful when classifying them.","zh":"因為一些早期樂器看起來像魯特琴，歷史學家分類時必須小心。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific historical stringed instrument.","zh":"這個短語命名一種特定歷史弦樂器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"some uncertainty about","meaning":"對……存在一些不確定性","examples":[{"en":"There is some uncertainty about the date of the first six-string guitar.","zh":"對第一把六弦結他的日期存在一些不確定性。"},{"en":"Some uncertainty about something means people are not completely sure about it.","zh":"some uncertainty about something 指人們對某事不完全肯定。"},{"en":"There is some uncertainty about the exact date when the old school hall was built.","zh":"對舊學校禮堂確實建成年份存在一些不確定性。"},{"en":"Uncertainty often remains when records are missing or objects are difficult to verify.","zh":"當紀錄缺失或物件難以驗證，不確定性常會存在。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests doubt, but not total ignorance.","zh":"這個短語暗示有疑問，但不是完全不知道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"exact date","meaning":"確實日期","examples":[{"en":"No one knows the exact date when the first six-string guitar was produced.","zh":"沒有人知道第一把六弦結他製成的確實日期。"},{"en":"An exact date is the precise day, month, or year when something happened.","zh":"exact date 指某事發生的精確日子、月份或年份。"},{"en":"A historian may know the exact date of a battle but not the exact number of people present.","zh":"歷史學家可能知道一場戰役的確實日期，但不知道在場確實人數。"},{"en":"Without documents, exact dates are often harder to prove than general periods.","zh":"沒有文件時，確實日期通常比大概時期更難證明。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses precision in time.","zh":"這個短語強調時間上的精確性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"earliest six-string guitar","meaning":"最早的六弦結他","examples":[{"en":"The earliest six-string guitar may have appeared in the eighteenth century.","zh":"最早的六弦結他可能出現在十八世紀。"},{"en":"The earliest six-string guitar means the first known guitar with six strings.","zh":"earliest six-string guitar 指已知第一把有六條弦的結他。"},{"en":"A museum label may identify an instrument as the earliest six-string guitar in its collection.","zh":"博物館標籤可能把某樂器標示為其收藏中最早的六弦結他。"},{"en":"Finding the earliest example helps historians understand when the modern guitar form began.","zh":"找到最早例子有助歷史學家理解現代結他形式何時開始。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a historical first, not simply an old guitar.","zh":"這個短語指歷史上的最早例子，而不只是舊結他。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"still in existence","meaning":"仍然存在","examples":[{"en":"The oldest known six-string guitar is still in existence.","zh":"已知最古老的六弦結他仍然存在。"},{"en":"Still in existence means something continues to exist today.","zh":"still in existence 指某物至今仍然存在。"},{"en":"Some handwritten letters from a century ago are still in existence in family archives.","zh":"一百年前的一些手寫信仍然存在於家族檔案中。"},{"en":"If an old instrument is still in existence, researchers can examine it directly.","zh":"如果舊樂器仍然存在，研究人員可以直接檢視它。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses survival up to the present.","zh":"這個短語強調一直保存至今。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be dated 1779","meaning":"標示製於 1779 年","examples":[{"en":"The guitar made by Gaetano Vinaccia is dated 1779.","zh":"Gaetano Vinaccia 製作的結他標示製於 1779 年。"},{"en":"To be dated 1779 means to be marked, identified, or judged as coming from the year 1779.","zh":"be dated 1779 指被標示、辨認或判定為來自1779年。"},{"en":"A letter dated 1920 was written or officially marked in that year.","zh":"一封 dated 1920 的信，是在該年書寫或正式標註的。"},{"en":"A date on an object can help historians place it in the correct period.","zh":"物件上的日期可以幫助歷史學家把它放在正確時期。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to historical dating, not romantic dating.","zh":"這個短語指歷史定年，不是戀愛約會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"authenticity","meaning":"真偽；真實性","examples":[{"en":"The authenticity of some early guitars is uncertain.","zh":"一些早期結他的真偽並不確定。"},{"en":"Authenticity means whether something is real, original, or genuinely what it claims to be.","zh":"authenticity 指某物是否真實、原裝或確實如它所聲稱。"},{"en":"A museum checks the authenticity of a painting before displaying it as a famous artist’s work.","zh":"博物館在把畫作展示為名家作品前，會檢查其真偽。"},{"en":"If authenticity is uncertain, historians may hesitate to use the object as strong evidence.","zh":"如果真偽不確定，歷史學家可能不願把該物件用作強證據。"},{"en":"The word is about genuineness, not quality alone.","zh":"這個詞關於真實性，而不只是質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be alleged to have been made","meaning":"據稱製於……","examples":[{"en":"Some guitars are alleged to have been made before 1790.","zh":"有些結他據稱製於1790年前。"},{"en":"To be alleged to have been made means people claim it was made at that time, but it is not fully proven.","zh":"be alleged to have been made 指有人聲稱某物製於某時，但尚未完全證明。"},{"en":"A vase alleged to have been made in the Ming dynasty still needs expert testing.","zh":"據稱製於明代的花瓶仍需要專家檢測。"},{"en":"Alleged dates can be wrong if sellers exaggerate an object’s age.","zh":"如果賣家誇大物件年代，據稱日期可能錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase signals a claim that requires verification.","zh":"這個短語表示需要驗證的聲稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"prior to 1790","meaning":"1790 年之前","examples":[{"en":"Several instruments were claimed to have been made prior to 1790.","zh":"幾件樂器被聲稱製於 1790 年之前。"},{"en":"Prior to 1790 means before the year 1790.","zh":"prior to 1790 指在1790年之前。"},{"en":"A building constructed prior to 1900 may need special protection as a heritage site.","zh":"建於1900年之前的建築可能需要作為文物地點特別保護。"},{"en":"If an instrument truly dates prior to 1790, it may be important evidence in guitar history.","zh":"如果樂器確實可追溯至1790年前，它可能是結他史中的重要證據。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a formal time boundary.","zh":"這個短語給出正式時間界線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be suspect","meaning":"令人懷疑","examples":[{"en":"The authenticity of many supposed early guitars is suspect.","zh":"許多所謂早期結他的真偽令人懷疑。"},{"en":"To be suspect means to be doubtful or not fully trusted.","zh":"be suspect 指令人存疑或不完全可信。"},{"en":"A student’s excuse may be suspect if it changes every time the teacher asks.","zh":"如果學生的藉口每次老師詢問都不同，它可能令人懷疑。"},{"en":"Evidence becomes suspect when it cannot be verified or when experts find inconsistencies.","zh":"當證據無法驗證或專家發現不一致，它就變得令人懷疑。"},{"en":"The phrase means questionable, not definitely false.","zh":"這個短語意思是值得質疑，不是一定虛假。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"discover fakes","meaning":"發現贗品","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have discovered many fake historical guitars.","zh":"研究人員已發現許多歷史結他贗品。"},{"en":"To discover fakes means to find objects that are not genuine although they were presented as real.","zh":"discover fakes 指找到被說成真品但其實不真實的物件。"},{"en":"A museum may discover fakes after testing the paint and materials of old artworks.","zh":"博物館檢測舊畫作的顏料和材料後，可能發現贗品。"},{"en":"Discovering fakes can change what historians believe about an object’s age.","zh":"發現贗品可以改變歷史學家對物件年代的看法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes uncovering false or forged items.","zh":"這個短語描述揭發虛假或偽造物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"date to this era","meaning":"可追溯至這個時期","examples":[{"en":"Many discovered fakes date to the same historical era.","zh":"許多被發現的贗品可追溯至同一歷史時期。"},{"en":"To date to this era means to belong to or come from that period of history.","zh":"date to this era 指屬於或來自該歷史時期。"},{"en":"A coin may date to the Roman era if its design and metal match that period.","zh":"如果硬幣的設計和金屬符合羅馬時期，它可能可追溯至羅馬時代。"},{"en":"Dating an object to an era helps researchers compare it with other objects from the same time.","zh":"把物件定年至某時期，有助研究人員與同時期其他物件比較。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an object with a historical period.","zh":"這個短語把物件與歷史時期連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"early nineteenth century","meaning":"十九世紀初","examples":[{"en":"The modern six-string guitar developed during the early nineteenth century.","zh":"現代六弦結他在十九世紀初發展起來。"},{"en":"The early nineteenth century means the first part of the 1800s.","zh":"early nineteenth century 指1800年代的早期部分。"},{"en":"A history class may study the early nineteenth century to understand industrial change.","zh":"歷史課可能研究十九世紀初，以理解工業變化。"},{"en":"If a musical instrument took shape in this period, later makers may have followed its design.","zh":"如果樂器在這時期成形，後來製作者可能跟隨其設計。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a broad historical time, not an exact year.","zh":"這個短語提供廣泛歷史時間，而不是確切年份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be generally accepted as","meaning":"普遍被視為","examples":[{"en":"The early nineteenth century is generally accepted as a key period in guitar history.","zh":"十九世紀初普遍被視為結他史中的關鍵時期。"},{"en":"To be generally accepted as something means most experts or people agree to regard it in that way.","zh":"be generally accepted as something 指大多數專家或人們同意以某方式看待它。"},{"en":"Shakespeare is generally accepted as one of the most important writers in English.","zh":"Shakespeare 普遍被視為英語中最重要作家之一。"},{"en":"General acceptance grows when evidence from many sources points to the same conclusion.","zh":"當多個來源的證據指向同一結論，普遍接受度就會增加。"},{"en":"The phrase shows broad agreement, not absolute certainty.","zh":"這個短語顯示廣泛同意，而不是絕對確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"time period during which","meaning":"……發生的時期","examples":[{"en":"This was the time period during which guitars developed their modern form.","zh":"這是結他發展出現代形式的時期。"},{"en":"Time period during which means the span of time when something happened.","zh":"time period during which 指某事發生的一段時間。"},{"en":"The summer holiday is the time period during which many students revise for entrance exams.","zh":"暑假是許多學生準備入學試的時期。"},{"en":"Naming the period helps readers understand when a change took place.","zh":"指出時期幫助讀者理解變化何時發生。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an event with its historical timeframe.","zh":"這個短語把事件與其歷史時間框架連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take on a modern shape","meaning":"逐漸形成現代外形","examples":[{"en":"Six-string guitars began taking on their modern shape.","zh":"六弦結他開始逐漸形成現代外形。"},{"en":"To take on a modern shape means to gradually develop the form recognised today.","zh":"take on a modern shape 指逐步發展出今日可辨認的形式。"},{"en":"A small town may take on a modern shape when new roads, schools, and shops are built.","zh":"當新道路、學校和商店建成，小鎮可能逐漸形成現代外貌。"},{"en":"Objects often take on a familiar shape after makers improve them over many years.","zh":"物件常在製作者多年改良後逐漸形成熟悉外形。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual development in form.","zh":"這個短語描述外形上的逐步發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"shape and dimensions","meaning":"外形和尺寸","examples":[{"en":"The guitar’s basic shape and dimensions have remained relatively stable.","zh":"結他的基本外形和尺寸一直相對穩定。"},{"en":"Shape and dimensions are the form of an object and its measurements, such as length, width, and depth.","zh":"shape and dimensions 指物件的形式以及長度、闊度和深度等量度。"},{"en":"A desk’s shape and dimensions determine whether it fits inside a classroom.","zh":"書桌的外形和尺寸決定它是否適合放入課室。"},{"en":"If an instrument’s dimensions remain stable, players and makers can develop standard techniques.","zh":"如果樂器尺寸保持穩定，演奏者和製作者可以發展標準技巧。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to physical form and size.","zh":"這個短語指實體形式和大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for nearly two hundred years","meaning":"接近二百年來","examples":[{"en":"Guitar makers have produced modern acoustic guitars for nearly two hundred years.","zh":"接近二百年來，結他製造師一直製作現代木結他。"},{"en":"For nearly two hundred years means for almost two centuries.","zh":"for nearly two hundred years 指差不多兩個世紀。"},{"en":"A family business may serve the same neighbourhood for nearly two hundred years.","zh":"家族企業可能接近二百年來服務同一社區。"},{"en":"If a design lasts that long, it has probably proved useful and popular.","zh":"如果設計能持續那麼久，它很可能已證明有用並受歡迎。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises a very long duration.","zh":"這個短語強調非常長的持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"luthiers","meaning":"弦樂器製琴師；結他製琴師","examples":[{"en":"Luthiers specialise in constructing and repairing stringed instruments.","zh":"弦樂器製琴師專門製作和維修弦樂器。"},{"en":"Luthiers are skilled craftspeople who make or repair stringed instruments such as guitars, violins, and lutes.","zh":"luthiers 指製作或維修結他、小提琴和魯特琴等弦樂器的熟練工匠。"},{"en":"A guitarist may take a damaged instrument to a luthier instead of a normal repair shop.","zh":"結他手可能把損壞樂器帶給製琴師，而不是普通維修店。"},{"en":"Because small changes affect sound, luthiers need careful hands and musical understanding.","zh":"因為細小改變會影響聲音，製琴師需要細心雙手和音樂理解。"},{"en":"The word names a specialist instrument maker or repairer.","zh":"這個詞命名專門製作或維修樂器的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"guitar makers","meaning":"結他製造師","examples":[{"en":"Luthiers are skilled guitar makers.","zh":"製琴師是熟練的結他製造師。"},{"en":"Guitar makers are people who build, design, or repair guitars.","zh":"guitar makers 指製作、設計或維修結他的人。"},{"en":"A guitar maker may choose different wood to change the sound of an acoustic guitar.","zh":"結他製造師可能選用不同木材來改變木結他的聲音。"},{"en":"Skilled makers influence how comfortable an instrument feels and how rich it sounds.","zh":"熟練製作者會影響樂器手感是否舒適以及聲音是否豐富。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to craftspeople, not factory machines alone.","zh":"這個短語指工匠，而不只是工廠機器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"produce versions of","meaning":"製作不同版本的……","examples":[{"en":"Guitar makers have produced many versions of the modern acoustic guitar.","zh":"結他製造師製作了許多不同版本的現代木結他。"},{"en":"To produce versions of something means to make different forms or models of the same basic thing.","zh":"produce versions of something 指製作同一基本事物的不同形式或型號。"},{"en":"A phone company may produce several versions of the same model with different storage sizes.","zh":"手機公司可能製作同一型號的幾個版本，提供不同儲存容量。"},{"en":"Different versions allow users to choose what fits their needs and budget.","zh":"不同版本讓使用者選擇符合需要和預算的產品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating variations, not completely unrelated products.","zh":"這個短語描述製作變化版本，而不是完全無關產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"modern acoustic guitar","meaning":"現代木結他","examples":[{"en":"The modern acoustic guitar developed largely in the nineteenth century.","zh":"現代木結他大致在十九世紀發展起來。"},{"en":"A modern acoustic guitar is a non-electric guitar with a familiar body shape and strings, producing sound naturally through its body.","zh":"modern acoustic guitar 指一種非電結他，有熟悉琴身和弦線，透過琴身自然發聲。"},{"en":"A singer may use a modern acoustic guitar for a small café performance.","zh":"歌手可能在小咖啡店演出時使用現代木結他。"},{"en":"Its design became stable because it balanced sound, comfort, and playability.","zh":"它的設計變得穩定，因為它平衡了聲音、舒適度和可演奏性。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the present-day wooden guitar form.","zh":"這個短語指今日木製結他的形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"electric guitar","meaning":"電結他","examples":[{"en":"The electric guitar was not developed until the twentieth century.","zh":"電結他直到二十世紀才被研發出來。"},{"en":"An electric guitar is a guitar that uses electronic pickups and an amplifier to produce a louder sound.","zh":"electric guitar 指使用電子拾音器和擴音器產生較大聲音的結他。"},{"en":"A rock band usually uses an electric guitar because it can cut through drums and bass.","zh":"搖滾樂隊通常使用電結他，因為它能在鼓和低音中突出。"},{"en":"Electric guitars changed popular music by allowing stronger volume and new tones.","zh":"電結他透過更大音量和新音色改變了流行音樂。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a guitar powered by electronics, not just any loud guitar.","zh":"這個短語指由電子設備發聲的結他，而不只是任何大聲結他。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not developed until","meaning":"直到……才被研發","examples":[{"en":"The first electric guitar was not developed until the early twentieth century.","zh":"第一把電結他直到二十世紀初才被研發。"},{"en":"Not developed until means something did not appear or become created before that time.","zh":"not developed until 指某事物在該時間之前尚未出現或被創造。"},{"en":"Many students do not develop strong writing skills until they receive regular feedback.","zh":"許多學生直到收到定期回饋後才發展出強寫作能力。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights that a development happened later than people might expect.","zh":"這個短語強調某發展比人們可能預期的更晚發生。"},{"en":"It is useful when stressing delay in history or progress.","zh":"它適合用於強調歷史或進展中的延遲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"early twentieth century","meaning":"二十世紀初","examples":[{"en":"Electric guitar technology emerged in the early twentieth century.","zh":"電結他技術在二十世紀初出現。"},{"en":"The early twentieth century means the first part of the 1900s.","zh":"early twentieth century 指1900年代的早期部分。"},{"en":"A history class may study the early twentieth century to understand radio, cinema, and new machines.","zh":"歷史課可能研究二十世紀初，以理解收音機、電影和新機器。"},{"en":"New technology from this period changed music, communication, and daily life.","zh":"這一時期的新科技改變了音樂、溝通和日常生活。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a broad historical period, not an exact year.","zh":"這個短語提供廣泛歷史時期，而不是確切年份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"receive a patent for","meaning":"取得……的專利","examples":[{"en":"George Beauchamp received a patent for an electric guitar in 1936.","zh":"George Beauchamp 在1936年取得電結他的專利。"},{"en":"To receive a patent for something means to be given legal protection for an invention.","zh":"receive a patent for something 指某項發明獲得法律保護。"},{"en":"An engineer may receive a patent for a safer bicycle brake design.","zh":"工程師可能取得更安全單車煞車設計的專利。"},{"en":"Patents help inventors protect their ideas and control commercial use.","zh":"專利幫助發明者保護想法並控制商業使用。"},{"en":"The phrase is about legal recognition of invention.","zh":"這個短語關於發明的法律認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the first patent","meaning":"首項專利","examples":[{"en":"Beauchamp received the first patent for an electric guitar.","zh":"Beauchamp 取得電結他的首項專利。"},{"en":"The first patent is the earliest official legal protection granted for an invention of that kind.","zh":"first patent 指某類發明最早獲批的正式法律保護。"},{"en":"A company may advertise that it holds the first patent for a new medical device.","zh":"公司可能宣傳自己持有某新醫療裝置的首項專利。"},{"en":"The first patent can mark an important moment in a technology’s history.","zh":"首項專利可以標示某項技術史上的重要時刻。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on legal priority, not necessarily the first object ever made.","zh":"這個短語重點是法律上的優先，而不一定是最早實物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"go on to","meaning":"繼而；後來","examples":[{"en":"Beauchamp went on to co-found the company Rickenbacker.","zh":"Beauchamp 後來共同創立 Rickenbacker 公司。"},{"en":"To go on to do something means to later do it after an earlier event or achievement.","zh":"go on to do something 指在較早事件或成就之後，後來做某事。"},{"en":"A student may win a local speech contest and go on to represent the school abroad.","zh":"學生可能先贏得本地演講比賽，繼而代表學校到海外比賽。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the next important step in a person’s story.","zh":"這個短語顯示人物故事中的下一個重要步驟。"},{"en":"It links earlier success with later action.","zh":"它把早前成功與後來行動連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"co-found","meaning":"共同創立","examples":[{"en":"George Beauchamp helped co-found Rickenbacker.","zh":"George Beauchamp 協助共同創立 Rickenbacker。"},{"en":"To co-found a company means to start it together with one or more other people.","zh":"co-found a company 指與一位或多位其他人共同創辦公司。"},{"en":"Two friends may co-found a tutoring centre after teaching students for several years.","zh":"兩位朋友教學生多年後，可能共同創立補習中心。"},{"en":"Co-founders usually share responsibility for the early direction of a business.","zh":"共同創辦人通常共同負責企業早期方向。"},{"en":"The word means founding together, not joining after the company already exists.","zh":"這個詞指一起創辦，而不是公司成立後才加入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"originally known as","meaning":"原名為","examples":[{"en":"Rickenbacker was originally known as the Electro String Instrument Company.","zh":"Rickenbacker 原名為 Electro String Instrument Company。"},{"en":"Originally known as means first called by a particular name before later being renamed.","zh":"originally known as 指在後來改名之前最初以某名稱為人所知。"},{"en":"A school may be originally known as a village college before it becomes a university.","zh":"學校在成為大學前可能原名為村鎮學院。"},{"en":"Old names can show a company’s early purpose or identity.","zh":"舊名稱可以顯示公司早期目的或身份。"},{"en":"The phrase explains an earlier name.","zh":"這個短語解釋較早名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"begin producing","meaning":"開始生產","examples":[{"en":"Rickenbacker began producing electric guitars in the late 1930s.","zh":"Rickenbacker 在1930年代後期開始生產電結他。"},{"en":"To begin producing something means to start making it for use or sale.","zh":"begin producing something 指開始製造某物供使用或銷售。"},{"en":"A bakery may begin producing gluten-free bread after many customers ask for it.","zh":"麵包店可能在許多顧客要求後開始生產無麩質麵包。"},{"en":"Once a company begins production, the product can reach more users.","zh":"一旦公司開始生產，產品就能接觸更多使用者。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the start of manufacturing.","zh":"這個短語標示製造的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in the late 1930s","meaning":"在 1930 年代後期","examples":[{"en":"The company began production in the late 1930s.","zh":"該公司在1930年代後期開始生產。"},{"en":"In the late 1930s means during the final years of the 1930s, roughly 1937 to 1939.","zh":"in the late 1930s 指1930年代的最後幾年，大約1937至1939年。"},{"en":"A film made in the late 1930s may show clothing and technology from before the Second World War.","zh":"在1930年代後期製作的電影可能展示二戰前的衣着和科技。"},{"en":"Giving a decade period helps place events even when the exact year is less important.","zh":"給出年代時期有助定位事件，即使確切年份較不重要。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate historical timeframe.","zh":"這個短語提供大約歷史時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"receive most of its fame","meaning":"獲得大部分知名度","examples":[{"en":"Rickenbacker received most of its fame during the 1960s.","zh":"Rickenbacker 在1960年代獲得大部分知名度。"},{"en":"To receive most of its fame means to become best known or most widely recognised during that period.","zh":"receive most of its fame 指在某時期變得最知名或最廣受認識。"},{"en":"A singer may receive most of her fame after one song becomes a global hit.","zh":"歌手可能在一首歌成為全球熱門後獲得大部分知名度。"},{"en":"Fame can grow when famous users, media, or cultural trends bring attention to a product.","zh":"當著名使用者、媒體或文化潮流帶來關注，名氣可以增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the period when recognition was strongest.","zh":"這個短語描述知名度最強的時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the Beatles’ debut performance","meaning":"披頭四的首次演出","examples":[{"en":"John Lennon used a Rickenbacker guitar during the Beatles’ debut television performance.","zh":"John Lennon 在披頭四首次電視演出中使用 Rickenbacker 結他。"},{"en":"The Beatles’ debut performance means the band’s first public performance in a particular setting, such as television.","zh":"the Beatles’ debut performance 指該樂隊在特定場合，例如電視上的首次公開演出。"},{"en":"A singer’s debut performance on a school stage may become an important memory.","zh":"歌手在學校舞台上的首次演出可能成為重要回憶。"},{"en":"When a famous musician uses an instrument in a debut performance, the instrument can gain attention.","zh":"當著名音樂人在首次演出中使用某樂器，該樂器可以得到關注。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a first appearance, not the whole career.","zh":"這個短語指首次亮相，而不是整個職業生涯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"use something for a performance","meaning":"使用……作演出","examples":[{"en":"John Lennon used a Rickenbacker guitar for an important performance.","zh":"John Lennon 使用 Rickenbacker 結他作一場重要演出。"},{"en":"To use something for a performance means to choose and play or wear it during a show.","zh":"use something for a performance 指在演出中選用並使用或穿戴某物。"},{"en":"A violinist may use her best instrument for a school concert.","zh":"小提琴手可能使用自己最好的樂器作學校音樂會演出。"},{"en":"The equipment used in a performance can affect sound, confidence, and audience memory.","zh":"演出中使用的設備可以影響聲音、信心和觀眾記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an item with a specific public event.","zh":"這個短語把物件與特定公開活動連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"of his own","meaning":"屬於他自己的","examples":[{"en":"George Harrison later bought a Rickenbacker guitar of his own.","zh":"George Harrison 後來買了一把屬於他自己的 Rickenbacker 結他。"},{"en":"Of his own means belonging personally to him, not borrowed or shared.","zh":"of his own 指由他個人擁有，而不是借用或共享。"},{"en":"A student may borrow a laptop at first and later buy one of her own.","zh":"學生一開始可能借用手提電腦，後來買一部屬於自己的。"},{"en":"Owning something of one’s own gives more control over how and when it is used.","zh":"擁有屬於自己的東西，令人更能控制何時和如何使用。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises personal possession.","zh":"這個短語強調個人擁有。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"one of its earliest","meaning":"其中最早期的……之一","examples":[{"en":"The company gave Harrison one of its earliest 12-string electric guitars.","zh":"該公司送給 Harrison 其中一把最早期的十二弦電結他。"},{"en":"One of its earliest means among the first examples produced by that company or group.","zh":"one of its earliest 指屬於該公司或群體最早製作的例子之一。"},{"en":"A museum may display one of a brand’s earliest mobile phones.","zh":"博物館可能展示某品牌其中一部最早期的手機。"},{"en":"Early examples can be historically important because they show how a design began.","zh":"早期例子可能有歷史重要性，因為它們顯示設計如何開始。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies something as part of the first generation.","zh":"這個短語指出某物屬於第一代例子之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"12-string electric guitar","meaning":"十二弦電結他","examples":[{"en":"George Harrison received an early 12-string electric guitar.","zh":"George Harrison 收到一把早期十二弦電結他。"},{"en":"A 12-string electric guitar is an electric guitar with twelve strings, often producing a fuller, ringing sound.","zh":"12-string electric guitar 指有十二條弦的電結他，通常產生更飽滿、響亮的聲音。"},{"en":"A guitarist may use a 12-string electric guitar when a song needs a bright and rich texture.","zh":"當歌曲需要明亮而豐富的質感，結他手可能使用十二弦電結他。"},{"en":"Extra strings can make the sound thicker, but they may also make the instrument harder to tune.","zh":"額外弦線可以令聲音更厚，但也可能令樂器較難調音。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific type of electric guitar.","zh":"這個短語命名一種特定類型的電結他。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bass guitar","meaning":"低音結他","examples":[{"en":"Paul McCartney used a Rickenbacker bass guitar.","zh":"Paul McCartney 使用 Rickenbacker 低音結他。"},{"en":"A bass guitar is a lower-pitched guitar that usually provides the deep rhythmic foundation in a band.","zh":"bass guitar 指音高較低的結他，通常在樂隊中提供深沉節奏基礎。"},{"en":"In a school band, the bass guitar often plays notes that connect the drums with the chords.","zh":"在學校樂隊中，低音結他常彈奏連接鼓和和弦的音。"},{"en":"Without bass, music may sound thinner and less grounded.","zh":"沒有低音，音樂可能聽起來較薄弱和不穩固。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the low-range guitar, not an ordinary six-string lead guitar.","zh":"這個短語指低音域結他，而不是普通六弦主音結他。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"for recording","meaning":"用於錄音","examples":[{"en":"Paul McCartney used the instrument for recording music.","zh":"Paul McCartney 使用該樂器錄製音樂。"},{"en":"For recording means for making a permanent audio or video version of a performance.","zh":"for recording 指用於製作演出或聲音的永久音訊或影片版本。"},{"en":"A singer may use a quieter room for recording a clean vocal track.","zh":"歌手可能使用較安靜房間來錄製清晰人聲。"},{"en":"Instruments chosen for recording affect the sound that listeners hear later.","zh":"錄音時選用的樂器會影響聽眾之後聽到的聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase describes studio or recorded use, not necessarily live performance.","zh":"這個短語描述錄音室或錄製用途，不一定是現場演出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"throughout their career","meaning":"貫穿他們的職業生涯","examples":[{"en":"The Beatles used Rickenbacker guitars throughout their career.","zh":"披頭四在整個職業生涯中使用 Rickenbacker 結他。"},{"en":"Throughout their career means during the whole or most of the period when they worked professionally.","zh":"throughout their career 指在他們專業工作期間的全部或大部分時間。"},{"en":"A teacher may use the same teaching notebook throughout her career because it contains valuable examples.","zh":"老師可能因一本教學筆記有寶貴例子，而在整個職業生涯中使用它。"},{"en":"If musicians use a brand throughout their career, fans may strongly associate the brand with them.","zh":"如果音樂人在整個職業生涯中使用某品牌，歌迷可能強烈把該品牌與他們聯繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses long-term professional use.","zh":"這個短語強調長期職業使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make something highly popular","meaning":"令……廣受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The Beatles made Rickenbacker guitars highly popular.","zh":"披頭四令 Rickenbacker 結他廣受歡迎。"},{"en":"To make something highly popular means to cause many people to like, buy, or use it.","zh":"make something highly popular 指令許多人喜歡、購買或使用某物。"},{"en":"A celebrity can make a small local café highly popular by posting about it online.","zh":"名人在網上發文可以令一間本地小咖啡店廣受歡迎。"},{"en":"When admired people use a product, fans may want the same thing.","zh":"當受人仰慕的人使用某產品，粉絲可能也想要同樣東西。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating strong public popularity.","zh":"這個短語描述創造強烈大眾人氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"among other musicians","meaning":"在其他音樂人之中","examples":[{"en":"The guitars became popular among other musicians of the era.","zh":"這些結他在那個年代的其他音樂人之中變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"Among other musicians means within the group of musicians apart from the people already mentioned.","zh":"among other musicians 指在已提及人物以外的音樂人群體之中。"},{"en":"A new singing technique may spread among other musicians after one famous performer uses it.","zh":"一位著名表演者使用新唱法後，它可能在其他音樂人之中傳開。"},{"en":"Popularity among professionals can make a product more respected and widely copied.","zh":"在專業人士之中受歡迎，可以令產品更受尊重並被廣泛模仿。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to influence inside a wider professional group.","zh":"這個短語指在更廣泛專業群體中的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"of the era","meaning":"那個年代的","examples":[{"en":"Many musicians of the era copied the Beatles’ choice of instruments.","zh":"那個年代的許多音樂人模仿披頭四的樂器選擇。"},{"en":"Of the era means belonging to or typical of that historical period.","zh":"of the era 指屬於或代表某一歷史時期。"},{"en":"Clothes of the era can help viewers recognise when a film is set.","zh":"那個年代的衣服可以幫助觀眾辨認電影背景時間。"},{"en":"When an object becomes fashionable in one era, it may later symbolise that period.","zh":"當物件在某一時代變得流行，它日後可能象徵該時期。"},{"en":"The phrase links people or things to a particular time.","zh":"這個短語把人物或事物與特定時間連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"electric guitar pioneers","meaning":"電結他先驅","examples":[{"en":"Fender and Gibson were early electric guitar pioneers.","zh":"Fender 和 Gibson 是早期電結他先驅。"},{"en":"Electric guitar pioneers are people or companies that helped create and develop electric guitars at an early stage.","zh":"electric guitar pioneers 指在早期幫助創造和發展電結他的人或公司。"},{"en":"A technology company can be a pioneer if it introduces a product before the market is ready.","zh":"如果科技公司在市場準備好之前推出產品，它可以成為先驅。"},{"en":"Pioneers influence later designs because others build on their early work.","zh":"先驅會影響後來設計，因為其他人會在其早期工作上發展。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights early leadership and innovation.","zh":"這個短語突出早期領導和創新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"develop models","meaning":"研發型號","examples":[{"en":"Both companies developed influential electric guitar models.","zh":"兩家公司都研發了有影響力的電結他型號。"},{"en":"To develop models means to design and create particular versions of a product.","zh":"develop models 指設計和創造某產品的特定版本。"},{"en":"A car company may develop models for families, delivery drivers, and sports drivers.","zh":"汽車公司可能為家庭、送貨司機和跑車司機研發不同型號。"},{"en":"When a model becomes successful, later products may copy its features.","zh":"當某型號成功，後來產品可能模仿其特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase describes product design and creation.","zh":"這個短語描述產品設計和創造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Fender Telecaster","meaning":"Fender Telecaster 結他","examples":[{"en":"The Fender Telecaster was introduced in the early 1950s.","zh":"Fender Telecaster 在1950年代初推出。"},{"en":"The Fender Telecaster is a famous solid-body electric guitar model made by Fender.","zh":"Fender Telecaster 指 Fender 製造的著名實心琴身電結他型號。"},{"en":"A guitarist may choose a Telecaster for its bright sound and simple design.","zh":"結他手可能因其明亮聲音和簡潔設計而選擇 Telecaster。"},{"en":"Because it appeared early and became popular, it influenced many later electric guitars.","zh":"因為它早期出現並變得受歡迎，它影響了許多後來電結他。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific guitar model.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定結他型號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"debut","meaning":"首次推出；面世","examples":[{"en":"The Fender Stratocaster debuted in 1954.","zh":"Fender Stratocaster 在1954年首次推出。"},{"en":"To debut means to appear or be introduced publicly for the first time.","zh":"debut 指首次公開出現或推出。"},{"en":"A student band may debut at the school music festival.","zh":"學生樂隊可能在學校音樂節首次演出。"},{"en":"A successful debut can quickly attract attention from customers, critics, or audiences.","zh":"成功首演或首次推出可以迅速吸引顧客、評論者或觀眾注意。"},{"en":"The word marks a first public appearance.","zh":"這個詞標示首次公開亮相。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Fender Stratocaster","meaning":"Fender Stratocaster 結他","examples":[{"en":"The Fender Stratocaster became one of the best-known electric guitar designs.","zh":"Fender Stratocaster 成為最知名的電結他設計之一。"},{"en":"The Fender Stratocaster is a famous electric guitar model known for its contoured body and versatile sound.","zh":"Fender Stratocaster 指著名電結他型號，以流線琴身和多變聲音聞名。"},{"en":"A guitarist may choose a Stratocaster for blues, rock, or pop performances.","zh":"結他手可能為藍調、搖滾或流行音樂演出選擇 Stratocaster。"},{"en":"Its popularity helped make its shape familiar even to people who do not play guitar.","zh":"它的受歡迎程度令即使不彈結他的人也熟悉其外形。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific influential guitar model.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定而具影響力的結他型號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"begin selling","meaning":"開始出售","examples":[{"en":"Gibson began selling the Gibson Les Paul in 1952.","zh":"Gibson 在1952年開始出售 Gibson Les Paul。"},{"en":"To begin selling something means to start offering it to customers for purchase.","zh":"begin selling something 指開始向顧客提供某物購買。"},{"en":"A school shop may begin selling healthier snacks after parents complain about junk food.","zh":"家長投訴垃圾食物後，學校小食部可能開始出售較健康小食。"},{"en":"Once a product begins selling, real users can test whether the design works well.","zh":"一旦產品開始出售，真正使用者就可以測試設計是否好用。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the start of commercial availability.","zh":"這個短語標示商業供應的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be based partially on","meaning":"部分建基於……","examples":[{"en":"The Gibson Les Paul was based partially on assistance from Les Paul.","zh":"Gibson Les Paul 部分建基於來自 Les Paul 的協助。"},{"en":"To be based partially on something means to be developed using that thing as one of several influences.","zh":"be based partially on something 指以某事作為幾個影響因素之一來發展。"},{"en":"A school policy may be based partially on student feedback and partially on teacher experience.","zh":"學校政策可能部分建基於學生回饋，部分建基於教師經驗。"},{"en":"Partial influence means something helped shape the result but was not the only factor.","zh":"部分影響代表某事幫助塑造結果，但不是唯一因素。"},{"en":"The phrase signals a shared or mixed source.","zh":"這個短語表示來源是共同或混合的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"assistance from","meaning":"來自……的協助","examples":[{"en":"The company developed the model with assistance from Les Paul.","zh":"該公司在 Les Paul 的協助下研發該型號。"},{"en":"Assistance from someone means help, advice, or support given by that person.","zh":"assistance from someone 指某人提供的幫助、建議或支援。"},{"en":"A student may complete a science project with assistance from a teacher.","zh":"學生可能在老師協助下完成科學專題。"},{"en":"Expert assistance can improve a product by adding practical knowledge.","zh":"專家協助可以透過加入實用知識來改善產品。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who helped.","zh":"這個短語指出誰提供了幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"jazz musician","meaning":"爵士樂手","examples":[{"en":"Les Paul was a well-known jazz musician.","zh":"Les Paul 是一位著名爵士樂手。"},{"en":"A jazz musician is a person who performs or creates jazz music.","zh":"jazz musician 指演奏或創作爵士音樂的人。"},{"en":"A jazz musician may improvise new melodies during a live performance.","zh":"爵士樂手可能在現場演出中即興創作新旋律。"},{"en":"Musicians with practical playing experience can offer valuable ideas for instrument design.","zh":"有實際演奏經驗的音樂人可以為樂器設計提供寶貴想法。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies someone by musical style and profession.","zh":"這個短語以音樂風格和職業辨認某人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"guitar innovator","meaning":"結他創新者","examples":[{"en":"Les Paul was both a musician and a guitar innovator.","zh":"Les Paul 既是音樂人，也是結他創新者。"},{"en":"A guitar innovator is someone who introduces new ideas, designs, or techniques related to the guitar.","zh":"guitar innovator 指在結他方面引入新想法、設計或技術的人。"},{"en":"A guitar innovator may create a new pickup, body shape, or recording method.","zh":"結他創新者可能創造新拾音器、琴身外形或錄音方法。"},{"en":"Innovators change what later musicians can play and how instruments are made.","zh":"創新者會改變後來音樂人能演奏甚麼，以及樂器如何製作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creative influence, not just skill at playing.","zh":"這個短語描述創造性影響，而不只是演奏技巧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"present-day guitars","meaning":"現今的結他","examples":[{"en":"Many present-day electric guitars follow designs developed in the 1950s.","zh":"許多現今的電結他沿用1950年代發展出的設計。"},{"en":"Present-day guitars are guitars made, sold, or used in the current period.","zh":"present-day guitars 指現時製造、出售或使用的結他。"},{"en":"Present-day guitars may look modern but still use ideas from older models.","zh":"現今的結他可能外觀看似現代，但仍使用舊型號的想法。"},{"en":"If current designs follow older ones, it shows those earlier designs were successful.","zh":"如果現有設計沿用舊設計，就顯示早期設計很成功。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts today’s instruments with historical versions.","zh":"這個短語把今日樂器與歷史版本作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"solid-body electric guitar","meaning":"實心琴身電結他","examples":[{"en":"A solid-body electric guitar has a solid rather than hollow body.","zh":"實心琴身電結他有實心而非中空琴身。"},{"en":"A solid-body electric guitar is an electric guitar whose body is made from solid material instead of a resonating hollow box.","zh":"solid-body electric guitar 指琴身由實心材料製成，而不是共鳴中空箱體的電結他。"},{"en":"Many rock guitarists use solid-body electric guitars because they work well with amplifiers.","zh":"許多搖滾結他手使用實心琴身電結他，因為它們配合擴音器表現良好。"},{"en":"A solid body can reduce feedback and allow louder performance.","zh":"實心琴身可以減少回授噪音，並容許更大聲演出。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the physical construction of a type of electric guitar.","zh":"這個短語描述一種電結他的實體結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be based largely on","meaning":"很大程度上建基於","examples":[{"en":"Modern electric guitars are based largely on several early designs.","zh":"現代電結他很大程度上建基於幾種早期設計。"},{"en":"To be based largely on something means to depend mainly on it as a model or source.","zh":"be based largely on something 指主要以某物作為模型或來源。"},{"en":"A new school handbook may be based largely on last year’s rules with small updates.","zh":"新學校手冊可能很大程度上建基於去年的規則，只作小更新。"},{"en":"If many products are based on old designs, those designs continue to influence the market.","zh":"如果許多產品建基於舊設計，那些設計仍繼續影響市場。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the main foundation of something.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事物的主要基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"early electric guitar designs","meaning":"早期電結他設計","examples":[{"en":"Three early electric guitar designs continue to influence manufacturers.","zh":"三種早期電結他設計繼續影響製造商。"},{"en":"Early electric guitar designs are the first important forms or models of electric guitars.","zh":"early electric guitar designs 指電結他最早期的重要形式或型號。"},{"en":"A guitar museum may display early electric guitar designs beside modern instruments.","zh":"結他博物館可能把早期電結他設計與現代樂器並列展示。"},{"en":"Early designs can become standards if later makers keep copying their successful features.","zh":"如果後來製作者繼續複製成功特徵，早期設計可以成為標準。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to influential design beginnings.","zh":"這個短語指有影響力的設計起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an enormous number of","meaning":"數量極多的","examples":[{"en":"An enormous number of individuals have influenced guitar history.","zh":"數量極多的人影響了結他歷史。"},{"en":"An enormous number of means a very large number of people or things.","zh":"an enormous number of 指非常大量的人或事物。"},{"en":"An enormous number of students use online videos to practise pronunciation.","zh":"數量極多的學生使用網上影片練習發音。"},{"en":"When many people contribute to a field, its history becomes richer and more complex.","zh":"當許多人為一個領域作出貢獻，其歷史就變得更豐富和複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly emphasises quantity.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make one’s mark on","meaning":"對……留下深遠影響","examples":[{"en":"Many musicians and designers have made their mark on the guitar.","zh":"許多音樂人和設計師對結他留下深遠影響。"},{"en":"To make one’s mark on something means to have a noticeable and lasting influence on it.","zh":"make one’s mark on something 指對某事留下明顯而持久的影響。"},{"en":"A teacher can make her mark on a school by creating a strong reading programme.","zh":"老師可以透過建立強大閱讀計劃，對學校留下深遠影響。"},{"en":"People make their mark when later generations remember or use their contributions.","zh":"當後代記得或使用某人的貢獻，他就留下了影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes leaving an important impact.","zh":"這個短語描述留下重要影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the way in which","meaning":"……的方式","examples":[{"en":"Individuals changed the way in which guitars were built and played.","zh":"一些人改變了結他被製造和演奏的方式。"},{"en":"The way in which means the manner or method by which something happens.","zh":"the way in which 指某事發生的方法或方式。"},{"en":"A new timetable can change the way in which students organise homework.","zh":"新時間表可以改變學生安排功課的方式。"},{"en":"Changing the way something is done can affect results, habits, and expectations.","zh":"改變做某事的方式可以影響結果、習慣和期望。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a method or process.","zh":"這個短語引入方法或過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be built, played and perceived","meaning":"被製造、演奏和看待","examples":[{"en":"The guitar has changed in how it is built, played, and perceived.","zh":"結他在被製造、演奏和看待的方式上都改變了。"},{"en":"To be built, played and perceived means to be made, used musically, and understood or viewed by people.","zh":"be built, played and perceived 指被製作、被音樂性使用，以及被人理解或看待。"},{"en":"A musical instrument can change when makers redesign it, performers use new techniques, and audiences hear it differently.","zh":"當製作者重新設計樂器、演奏者使用新技巧、觀眾以不同方式聆聽時，樂器就會改變。"},{"en":"These three changes affect both the object and its cultural meaning.","zh":"這三種改變同時影響物件本身和其文化意義。"},{"en":"The phrase covers construction, performance, and public image.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋製造、演出和公眾形象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"particularly well known","meaning":"尤其廣為人知","examples":[{"en":"Some figures in guitar history are particularly well known.","zh":"結他歷史中的一些人物尤其廣為人知。"},{"en":"Particularly well known means especially famous or widely recognised.","zh":"particularly well known 指特別有名或廣受認識。"},{"en":"Some teachers in a school are particularly well known because generations of students remember them.","zh":"學校中有些老師尤其廣為人知，因為幾代學生都記得他們。"},{"en":"Famous figures are easier to remember, but less famous people may also have contributed greatly.","zh":"著名人物較容易被記住，但較不出名的人也可能有巨大貢獻。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a higher level of public recognition.","zh":"這個短語突出較高程度的公眾認知。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the majority of","meaning":"大多數","examples":[{"en":"The majority of guitar innovators remain unknown to modern fans.","zh":"大多數結他創新者仍不為現代歌迷所知。"},{"en":"The majority of means most or more than half of a group.","zh":"the majority of 指一個群體中的大多數或超過一半。"},{"en":"The majority of students prefer examples that are clear rather than beautiful but confusing.","zh":"大多數學生較喜歡清楚例句，而不是漂亮但令人困惑的句子。"},{"en":"When most contributors are unknown, history may overfocus on a few famous names.","zh":"當大多數貢獻者不為人知，歷史可能過度集中於少數名人。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the larger part of a group.","zh":"這個短語指出群體中較大部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"virtually invisible to","meaning":"幾乎不為……所知","examples":[{"en":"Many early guitar makers are virtually invisible to modern guitar fans.","zh":"許多早期結他製造師幾乎不為現代結他迷所知。"},{"en":"Virtually invisible to someone means almost completely unknown or unnoticed by that person or group.","zh":"virtually invisible to someone 指幾乎完全不被某人或某群體知道或注意。"},{"en":"The cleaning staff may be virtually invisible to students until classrooms are not cleaned.","zh":"清潔員工可能幾乎不為學生注意，直到課室沒有被清潔。"},{"en":"Important contributors can become invisible if records focus only on famous performers.","zh":"如果紀錄只集中於著名表演者，重要貢獻者可能變得隱形。"},{"en":"The phrase means socially or historically unseen, not literally transparent.","zh":"這個短語指社會或歷史上看不見，而不是字面透明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"modern guitar fans","meaning":"現代結他迷","examples":[{"en":"Modern guitar fans may know little about early instrument makers.","zh":"現代結他迷可能對早期樂器製作者所知甚少。"},{"en":"Modern guitar fans are people today who enjoy, follow, or collect guitars and guitar music.","zh":"modern guitar fans 指今日喜歡、追隨或收藏結他和結他音樂的人。"},{"en":"A modern guitar fan may know famous rock players but not the craftspeople who shaped the instrument.","zh":"現代結他迷可能認識著名搖滾樂手，但不認識塑造樂器的工匠。"},{"en":"Fan culture can focus on recent stars and forget earlier technical contributors.","zh":"粉絲文化可以集中於近期明星，而忘記早期技術貢獻者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes present-day enthusiasts.","zh":"這個短語描述現今愛好者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"look at the entire history of","meaning":"審視……的完整歷史","examples":[{"en":"Readers should look at the entire history of the guitar.","zh":"讀者應審視結他的完整歷史。"},{"en":"To look at the entire history of something means to consider its full development from beginning to present.","zh":"look at the entire history of something 指考慮某事由開始至現今的完整發展。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to look at the entire history of a city before judging one modern problem.","zh":"老師可能要求學生先審視一座城市的完整歷史，再判斷一個現代問題。"},{"en":"A full historical view prevents people from focusing only on recent events.","zh":"完整歷史視角可以防止人只集中於近期事件。"},{"en":"The phrase encourages a broad perspective.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵廣闊視角。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rather than just","meaning":"而不只是","examples":[{"en":"The passage considers the whole history rather than just electric guitars.","zh":"文章考慮整段歷史，而不只是電結他。"},{"en":"Rather than just means instead of focusing only on one limited part.","zh":"rather than just 指不是只集中於某個有限部分。"},{"en":"Students should study grammar in real writing rather than just memorising rules.","zh":"學生應在真實寫作中學文法，而不只是背規則。"},{"en":"The phrase broadens attention beyond a narrow focus.","zh":"這個短語把注意力從狹窄焦點擴闊。"},{"en":"It is useful when correcting an oversimplified view.","zh":"它適合用於修正過分簡化的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"recent developments","meaning":"近期發展","examples":[{"en":"Recent developments represent only one part of guitar history.","zh":"近期發展只代表結他歷史的一部分。"},{"en":"Recent developments are changes or advances that happened not long ago.","zh":"recent developments 指不久前發生的變化或進展。"},{"en":"Recent developments in online learning include live quizzes and AI feedback tools.","zh":"網上學習的近期發展包括即時測驗和人工智能回饋工具。"},{"en":"Recent changes may attract attention, but older developments may be equally important.","zh":"近期改變可能吸引注意，但較舊發展可能同樣重要。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to newer events in a longer story.","zh":"這個短語指較長故事中的較新事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be largely confined to","meaning":"很大程度上局限於","examples":[{"en":"Modern discussions are often largely confined to electric guitars.","zh":"現代討論常很大程度上局限於電結他。"},{"en":"To be largely confined to something means to be mostly limited to that area or topic.","zh":"be largely confined to something 指大多限於某範圍或主題。"},{"en":"A student’s revision may be largely confined to vocabulary if she ignores writing practice.","zh":"如果學生忽視寫作練習，她的溫習可能很大程度上局限於詞彙。"},{"en":"When discussion is too confined, important wider context may be missed.","zh":"當討論過於局限，重要的更廣闊背景可能被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a narrow focus.","zh":"這個短語描述狹窄焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"see more of","meaning":"看見更多……","examples":[{"en":"A broader historical view allows us to see more of earlier contributions.","zh":"更廣闊的歷史視角讓我們看見更多早期貢獻。"},{"en":"To see more of something means to notice or understand a larger part of it.","zh":"see more of something 指注意到或理解某事更大部分。"},{"en":"Reading several essays lets a teacher see more of a student’s real writing ability.","zh":"閱讀幾篇作文可以讓老師看見學生更多真實寫作能力。"},{"en":"A wider view can reveal people and events that a narrow view hides.","zh":"更廣闊視角可以揭示狹窄視角隱藏的人物和事件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gaining fuller understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述獲得更完整理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"contributions of earlier generations","meaning":"前幾代人的貢獻","examples":[{"en":"Earlier generations made important contributions to guitar development.","zh":"前幾代人對結他發展作出重要貢獻。"},{"en":"Contributions of earlier generations are the useful work, ideas, or achievements of people who came before us.","zh":"contributions of earlier generations 指我們之前的人所作出的有用工作、想法或成就。"},{"en":"A school’s current success may depend on the contributions of earlier generations of teachers.","zh":"學校今日的成功可能依賴前幾代老師的貢獻。"},{"en":"Remembering earlier contributions helps people avoid thinking progress began only recently.","zh":"記住早期貢獻有助人避免以為進步只是最近才開始。"},{"en":"The phrase gives credit to people from the past.","zh":"這個短語把功勞歸給過去的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"choose no more than three words","meaning":"選擇不超過三個字","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should choose no more than three words from the passage.","zh":"考生應從文章中選擇不超過三個字。"},{"en":"Choose no more than three words means the answer must contain one, two, or three words only.","zh":"choose no more than three words 指答案只能包含一個、兩個或三個詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “electric guitar”, it fits because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “electric guitar”，它符合要求，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing four words may lose marks even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫四個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict exam word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格考試字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"for each answer","meaning":"每個答案","examples":[{"en":"Each answer must follow the stated word limit.","zh":"每個答案都必須遵守所述字數限制。"},{"en":"For each answer means for every separate response in the task.","zh":"for each answer 指任務中的每一個獨立答案。"},{"en":"For each answer in a reading test, students should check spelling and word count.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，每個答案都應檢查串法和字數。"},{"en":"The rule applies to every blank, not only the first one.","zh":"這條規則適用於每個空格，而不只是第一個。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds candidates to treat all answers individually.","zh":"這個短語提醒考生逐一處理所有答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"despite differences in","meaning":"儘管……有所不同","examples":[{"en":"Despite differences in spelling and pronunciation, the word has common roots.","zh":"儘管拼寫和發音有所不同，這個詞有共同根源。"},{"en":"Despite differences in means even though there are differences in a particular feature.","zh":"despite differences in 指即使在某方面存在差異。"},{"en":"Despite differences in age, the students worked well together on the project.","zh":"儘管年齡有所不同，學生在項目中合作得很好。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights that one shared fact remains true although differences exist.","zh":"這個短語強調雖然存在差異，但某個共同事實仍成立。"},{"en":"It is useful for showing contrast with a surprising common point.","zh":"它適合用於以令人意外的共同點作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"appear in the word for","meaning":"出現在表示……的詞語中","examples":[{"en":"The roots “guit-” and “-tar” appear in the word for guitar in many languages.","zh":"“guit-” 和 “-tar” 這兩個詞根出現在許多語言中表示結他的詞語中。"},{"en":"To appear in the word for something means to be present as part of that word.","zh":"appear in the word for something 指作為某詞語的一部分存在。"},{"en":"The sound “tele” appears in the word for distant communication, such as “telephone”.","zh":"“tele” 這個音出現在表示遠距離溝通的詞語中，例如 “telephone”。"},{"en":"If a root appears in related words across languages, it may show shared history.","zh":"如果詞根出現在跨語言的相關詞語中，它可能顯示共同歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a word part being visible inside a term.","zh":"這個短語描述詞語部分在術語中可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"approximately","meaning":"大約","examples":[{"en":"Recognisable acoustic guitars have existed for approximately five centuries.","zh":"可辨認的木結他已存在大約五個世紀。"},{"en":"Approximately means about or nearly, not exactly.","zh":"approximately 指大約或接近，不是完全準確。"},{"en":"The bus ride takes approximately thirty minutes when traffic is normal.","zh":"交通正常時，巴士車程大約三十分鐘。"},{"en":"We use approximately when an exact number is unnecessary or unknown.","zh":"當確切數字不必要或未知時，我們使用 approximately。"},{"en":"The word signals an estimate.","zh":"這個詞表示估算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"no one knows","meaning":"沒有人知道","examples":[{"en":"No one knows the exact date of the earliest six-string guitar.","zh":"沒有人知道最早六弦結他的確實日期。"},{"en":"No one knows means the information is not known by anyone, or at least not reliably known.","zh":"no one knows 指沒有人知道該資訊，或至少沒有可靠地知道。"},{"en":"No one knows exactly who first invented the old playground game.","zh":"沒有人確切知道誰最先發明那個舊操場遊戲。"},{"en":"When records are missing, historians may only give a likely period rather than a definite answer.","zh":"當紀錄缺失，歷史學家可能只能給出可能時期，而不是確定答案。"},{"en":"The phrase signals uncertainty or lack of evidence.","zh":"這個短語表示不確定或缺乏證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"change very little","meaning":"變化很少","examples":[{"en":"The basic dimensions of acoustic guitars have changed very little.","zh":"木結他的基本尺寸變化很少。"},{"en":"To change very little means to remain almost the same over time.","zh":"change very little 指隨時間幾乎保持不變。"},{"en":"A school uniform may change very little if students and parents still like the design.","zh":"如果學生和家長仍喜歡校服設計，校服可能變化很少。"},{"en":"If a design works well, makers may have little reason to alter it.","zh":"如果設計效果良好，製作者可能沒有太大理由改動它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stability rather than major development.","zh":"這個短語描述穩定，而不是重大發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be issued","meaning":"被頒發","examples":[{"en":"A patent for an electric guitar was issued in the mid-1930s.","zh":"電結他專利在1930年代中期被頒發。"},{"en":"To be issued means to be officially given, released, or granted.","zh":"be issued 指被正式給予、發布或授予。"},{"en":"A school pass may be issued to students who need to enter the library after class.","zh":"學校通行證可能被頒發給放學後需要進入圖書館的學生。"},{"en":"When a patent is issued, the invention receives formal legal recognition.","zh":"當專利被頒發，該發明就得到正式法律認可。"},{"en":"The phrase often appears in official or legal contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於官方或法律語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"mid-1930s","meaning":"1930 年代中期","examples":[{"en":"The first electric guitar patent was issued in the mid-1930s.","zh":"第一項電結他專利在1930年代中期被頒發。"},{"en":"The mid-1930s means the middle years of the 1930s, roughly 1934 to 1936.","zh":"mid-1930s 指1930年代中間幾年，大約1934至1936年。"},{"en":"A photograph from the mid-1930s may show fashion and technology from before the war.","zh":"1930年代中期的照片可能展示戰前時尚和科技。"},{"en":"Using “mid-” gives an approximate period when the exact year is less important.","zh":"使用 “mid-” 可在確切年份較不重要時提供大概時期。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a historical timeframe within a decade.","zh":"這個短語描述十年中的歷史時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be involved in the development of","meaning":"參與……的研發","examples":[{"en":"Les Paul was involved in the development of the electric guitar.","zh":"Les Paul 參與了電結他的研發。"},{"en":"To be involved in the development of something means to take part in helping it grow, improve, or be created.","zh":"be involved in the development of something 指參與幫助某物成長、改善或創造。"},{"en":"Teachers may be involved in the development of a new school curriculum.","zh":"老師可能參與新學校課程的研發。"},{"en":"People involved in development can influence design, testing, and final use.","zh":"參與研發的人可以影響設計、測試和最終使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active participation in creating or improving something.","zh":"這個短語描述主動參與創造或改善某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"know little about","meaning":"對……所知不多","examples":[{"en":"Many modern guitar fans know little about the instrument’s early history.","zh":"許多現代結他迷對這種樂器的早期歷史所知不多。"},{"en":"To know little about something means to have only limited knowledge of it.","zh":"know little about something 指對某事只有有限知識。"},{"en":"A student may enjoy classical music but know little about how orchestras developed.","zh":"學生可能喜歡古典音樂，但對管弦樂團如何發展所知不多。"},{"en":"When people know little about a history, they may overfocus on recent famous figures.","zh":"當人們對一段歷史所知不多，他們可能過度集中於近期名人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limited understanding, not complete ignorance.","zh":"這個短語描述理解有限，而不是完全無知。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rich history","meaning":"豐富的歷史","examples":[{"en":"The guitar has a rich history extending over thousands of years.","zh":"結他有延續數千年的豐富歷史。"},{"en":"Rich history means a long, varied, and interesting past with many important developments.","zh":"rich history 指悠長、多樣且有趣的過去，包含許多重要發展。"},{"en":"A city with a rich history may have old buildings, festivals, stories, and different communities.","zh":"有豐富歷史的城市可能有舊建築、節日、故事和不同社群。"},{"en":"A rich history gives people more than one angle for understanding the present.","zh":"豐富歷史讓人能從不止一個角度理解現在。"},{"en":"The phrase praises depth and variety in the past.","zh":"這個短語讚揚過去的深度和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the summary with words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill missing words in a shortened version of the text.","zh":"complete the summary 指填補文本簡短版本中的缺漏字詞。"},{"en":"A student should read the whole summary before choosing each answer.","zh":"學生應先讀完整個摘要，再選擇每個答案。"},{"en":"Summary completion tests meaning, grammar, and exact wording.","zh":"摘要填空測試意思、文法和準確用字。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"instruments similar to","meaning":"與……相似的樂器","examples":[{"en":"Instruments similar to the guitar have existed for thousands of years.","zh":"與結他相似的樂器已存在數千年。"},{"en":"Instruments similar to something are instruments that share important features with it.","zh":"instruments similar to something 指與某物共享重要特徵的樂器。"},{"en":"Instruments similar to the violin may have strings, a bow, and a wooden body.","zh":"與小提琴相似的樂器可能有弦、弓和木製琴身。"},{"en":"Similar instruments can show how musical ideas developed before the modern form appeared.","zh":"相似樂器可以顯示音樂概念在現代形式出現前如何發展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes resemblance, not exact identity.","zh":"這個短語描述相似，而不是完全相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"actual physical examples","meaning":"真實的實物例子","examples":[{"en":"Few actual physical examples of the earliest instruments survive.","zh":"最早期樂器中很少有真實的實物例子保存下來。"},{"en":"Actual physical examples are real objects that still exist and can be examined directly.","zh":"actual physical examples 指仍然存在並可被直接檢視的真實物件。"},{"en":"A museum may have actual physical examples of old coins rather than only drawings of them.","zh":"博物館可能有舊硬幣的真實實物例子，而不只是圖畫。"},{"en":"When physical examples survive, researchers can study materials, size, and construction.","zh":"當實物例子保存下來，研究人員可以研究材料、大小和構造。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts real objects with pictures or descriptions.","zh":"這個短語把真實物件與圖片或描述作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Knowledge often comes from pictures rather than surviving instruments.","zh":"知識往往來自圖像，而不是保存下來的樂器。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of, showing a contrast between two sources or choices.","zh":"rather than 指而不是，用來顯示兩個來源或選擇之間的對比。"},{"en":"A student may learn pronunciation from listening rather than reading spelling alone.","zh":"學生可能透過聆聽學習發音，而不是只讀拼寫。"},{"en":"The phrase helps identify what is used instead of another possible thing.","zh":"這個短語幫助指出用甚麼取代另一個可能事物。"},{"en":"It makes the contrast between two options clear.","zh":"它令兩個選項之間的對比清楚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be closer to","meaning":"較接近……","examples":[{"en":"Some early instruments were closer to the lute than the modern guitar.","zh":"一些早期樂器較接近魯特琴，而不是現代結他。"},{"en":"To be closer to something means to be more similar to it than to another thing.","zh":"be closer to something 指比起另一事物更相似於某物。"},{"en":"A short report may be closer to an article than a full academic essay.","zh":"短報告可能較接近文章，而不是完整學術論文。"},{"en":"Similarity helps people decide how to classify an unclear object.","zh":"相似度幫助人們判斷如何分類不清楚的物件。"},{"en":"The phrase compares degree of resemblance.","zh":"這個短語比較相似程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as we know it today","meaning":"正如我們今天所認識的","examples":[{"en":"Early instruments differed from the guitar as we know it today.","zh":"早期樂器不同於我們今天所認識的結他。"},{"en":"As we know it today means in the form familiar to people now.","zh":"as we know it today 指以現今人們熟悉的形式而言。"},{"en":"The school system as we know it today developed over many years.","zh":"我們今天所認識的學校制度經多年發展而來。"},{"en":"Older versions of an object may look different from the modern form we recognise.","zh":"物件的舊版本可能與我們認得出的現代形式不同。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts historical forms with the current familiar form.","zh":"這個短語把歷史形式與現今熟悉形式作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"open to question","meaning":"值得懷疑；尚有疑問","examples":[{"en":"The authenticity of several early guitars is open to question.","zh":"幾把早期結他的真偽尚有疑問。"},{"en":"Open to question means doubtful or not fully certain.","zh":"open to question 指值得懷疑或不完全確定。"},{"en":"The accuracy of a student’s online source is open to question if no author is named.","zh":"如果網上來源沒有作者，學生使用的資料準確性就值得懷疑。"},{"en":"When evidence is weak, a claim remains open to question until it is verified.","zh":"當證據薄弱，聲稱在被驗證前仍有疑問。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that something can reasonably be challenged.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事可以合理地被質疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"before the final decade of","meaning":"在……最後十年之前","examples":[{"en":"Some guitars were supposedly made before the final decade of the eighteenth century.","zh":"有些結他據稱製於十八世紀最後十年之前。"},{"en":"Before the final decade of a century means before the last ten years of that century began.","zh":"before the final decade of a century 指在該世紀最後十年開始之前。"},{"en":"A building made before the final decade of the nineteenth century was built before the 1890s.","zh":"建於十九世紀最後十年之前的建築，就是建於1890年代之前。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a formal historical time limit without naming every year.","zh":"這個短語提供正式歷史時間界線，而不用列出每一年。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing approximate dates.","zh":"它適合用於討論大約日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"eighteenth century","meaning":"十八世紀","examples":[{"en":"The oldest surviving six-string guitars date from the eighteenth century.","zh":"最古老的現存六弦結他可追溯至十八世紀。"},{"en":"The eighteenth century means the years from 1701 to 1800.","zh":"eighteenth century 指1701年至1800年。"},{"en":"A history class may study the eighteenth century to understand trade, science, and political change.","zh":"歷史課可能研究十八世紀，以理解貿易、科學和政治變化。"},{"en":"If an instrument dates from the eighteenth century, it is several hundred years old today.","zh":"如果樂器可追溯至十八世紀，它今日已有數百年歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase names a historical century, not the 1800s.","zh":"這個短語命名一個歷史世紀，不是1800年代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"also known as","meaning":"又稱為","examples":[{"en":"Guitar makers are also known as luthiers.","zh":"結他製造師又稱為 luthiers。"},{"en":"Also known as means having another name or being called by another term.","zh":"also known as 指有另一個名稱或被另一個詞稱呼。"},{"en":"Hong Kong International Airport is also known as Chek Lap Kok Airport.","zh":"香港國際機場又稱為赤鱲角機場。"},{"en":"Giving another name helps readers recognise the same person, place, or job in different texts.","zh":"提供另一名稱有助讀者在不同文本中認出同一人、地點或工作。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an alternative name.","zh":"這個短語引入別名。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"play a major part","meaning":"發揮重要作用","examples":[{"en":"Rickenbacker played a major part in developing the electric guitar.","zh":"Rickenbacker 在電結他發展中發揮重要作用。"},{"en":"To play a major part means to have an important role in making something happen.","zh":"play a major part 指在促成某事發生中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"Parents can play a major part in helping children build reading habits.","zh":"家長可以在幫助孩子建立閱讀習慣方面發揮重要作用。"},{"en":"When a company contributes key designs or technology, it may shape an entire industry.","zh":"當公司貢獻關鍵設計或技術，它可能塑造整個行業。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights an important contribution.","zh":"這個短語突出重要貢獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"take several decades to develop","meaning":"需要數十年發展","examples":[{"en":"The electric guitar took several decades to develop fully.","zh":"電結他需要數十年才發展成熟。"},{"en":"To take several decades to develop means to need many tens of years to reach a mature form.","zh":"take several decades to develop 指需要許多十年才達到成熟形式。"},{"en":"A city’s railway system may take several decades to develop fully.","zh":"一個城市的鐵路系統可能需要數十年才完全發展成熟。"},{"en":"Complex inventions often improve slowly through testing, failure, and redesign.","zh":"複雜發明通常透過測試、失敗和重新設計而慢慢改善。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses long, gradual development.","zh":"這個短語強調漫長而漸進的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in use today","meaning":"現今仍在使用","examples":[{"en":"Many electric guitars in use today follow early Fender and Gibson designs.","zh":"許多現今仍在使用的電結他沿用早期 Fender 和 Gibson 設計。"},{"en":"In use today means currently being used by people.","zh":"in use today 指現時仍被人使用。"},{"en":"Some teaching methods in use today were first developed decades ago.","zh":"一些現今仍在使用的教學方法早在數十年前已發展出來。"},{"en":"If an old design remains in use today, it has continued to meet practical needs.","zh":"如果舊設計現今仍在使用，它就一直能滿足實際需要。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises present-day use.","zh":"這個短語強調今日仍在使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be similar in design to","meaning":"在設計上與……相似","examples":[{"en":"Modern electric guitars are similar in design to models from the 1950s.","zh":"現代電結他在設計上與1950年代型號相似。"},{"en":"To be similar in design to something means to share important design features with it.","zh":"be similar in design to something 指與某物共享重要設計特徵。"},{"en":"A new school desk may be similar in design to an older model but made from lighter materials.","zh":"新學校書桌可能在設計上與舊型號相似，但用較輕材料製成。"},{"en":"When modern products copy older design features, those older models remain influential.","zh":"當現代產品複製舊設計特徵，那些舊型號仍具有影響力。"},{"en":"The phrase compares design, not necessarily age, price, or quality.","zh":"這個短語比較設計，而不一定比較年代、價格或質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 141 - The history of the guitar.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 142":[{"front":"the secret of the yawn","meaning":"打呵欠的奧秘","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines the biological and psychological secrets of yawning.","zh":"文章探討打呵欠在生物和心理方面的奧秘。"},{"en":"The secret of the yawn means the hidden reason why yawning happens and what it may show about the body or mind.","zh":"the secret of the yawn 指打呵欠為何發生，以及它可能反映身體或心理狀態的隱藏原因。"},{"en":"A science lesson about tiredness may explore the secret of the yawn by asking why people yawn before sleep.","zh":"關於疲倦的科學課可能透過詢問人為何睡前打呵欠，來探索打呵欠的奧秘。"},{"en":"Studying yawning can reveal links between breathing, brain activity, attention, and empathy.","zh":"研究打呵欠可以揭示呼吸、大腦活動、專注和同理心之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a familiar daily action has a deeper scientific explanation.","zh":"當熟悉的日常動作有更深科學解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"begin to study","meaning":"開始研究……","examples":[{"en":"The researcher began to study yawning in the 1980s.","zh":"研究人員在1980年代開始研究打呵欠。"},{"en":"To begin to study something means to start examining it carefully or scientifically.","zh":"begin to study something 指開始仔細或科學地研究某事。"},{"en":"A student may begin to study vocabulary by keeping a small notebook of useful phrases.","zh":"學生可能透過記下實用短語的小筆記本開始研究詞彙。"},{"en":"Researchers often begin to study a topic after noticing a strange pattern or unanswered question.","zh":"研究人員常在注意到奇怪模式或未解問題後開始研究某主題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the starting point of learning or research.","zh":"描述學習或研究的起點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"convince someone of the merits of","meaning":"說服某人相信……的價值","examples":[{"en":"It was difficult to convince students of the merits of yawning research.","zh":"要說服學生相信打呵欠研究的價值並不容易。"},{"en":"To convince someone of the merits of something means to persuade them that it is valuable or worthwhile.","zh":"convince someone of the merits of something 指說服某人相信某事有價值或值得做。"},{"en":"A teacher may need to convince students of the merits of reading slowly before they stop rushing.","zh":"老師可能需要說服學生相信慢慢閱讀的價值，他們才會停止急着看完。"},{"en":"If people think a topic is silly, clear evidence is needed to show why it matters.","zh":"如果人們覺得某個主題很傻，就需要清楚證據顯示它為何重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when others doubt the value of an idea.","zh":"當別人懷疑某想法的價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the merits of","meaning":"……的價值；優點","examples":[{"en":"Some students initially doubted the merits of “yawning science”.","zh":"有些學生最初懷疑「打呵欠科學」的價值。"},{"en":"The merits of something are its good points, value, or advantages.","zh":"merits of something 指某事的好處、價值或優點。"},{"en":"Before joining a club, students may consider the merits of spending time on it every week.","zh":"加入學會前，學生可能考慮每週花時間在它上面的價值。"},{"en":"A topic may look unusual, but its merits become clear when it explains real human behaviour.","zh":"一個主題可能看似不尋常，但當它解釋真實人類行為時，其價值就變得清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing whether something is worth attention.","zh":"討論某事是否值得關注時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"yawning science","meaning":"打呵欠研究","examples":[{"en":"Yawning science examines the causes and functions of yawning.","zh":"打呵欠研究探討打呵欠的原因和功能。"},{"en":"Yawning science means scientific research into why people and animals yawn.","zh":"yawning science 指關於人和動物為何打呵欠的科學研究。"},{"en":"A student project on yawning science might compare yawning before sleep and after seeing others yawn.","zh":"關於打呵欠研究的學生專題，可能比較睡前打呵欠和看見別人打呵欠後的反應。"},{"en":"The field may sound funny, but it can reveal how the brain and body work together.","zh":"這個領域聽起來可能有趣，但它可以揭示大腦和身體如何共同運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when everyday behaviour becomes a subject of serious research.","zh":"當日常行為成為嚴肅研究對象時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"appear quirky","meaning":"看似古怪","examples":[{"en":"The decision to study yawning may appear quirky.","zh":"決定研究打呵欠可能看似古怪。"},{"en":"Appear quirky means seem unusual, slightly odd, or unexpected.","zh":"appear quirky 指看起來不尋常、有點奇怪或出乎意料。"},{"en":"A teacher’s habit of starting every lesson with a puzzle may appear quirky at first.","zh":"老師每堂課都用謎題開始，最初可能看似古怪。"},{"en":"Something quirky can still be useful if it leads to serious learning or discovery.","zh":"古怪的東西如果能帶來認真學習或發現，仍然可以有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an idea looks strange but may have real value.","zh":"當一個想法看似奇怪但可能有真正價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a logical extension of","meaning":"……的合理延伸","examples":[{"en":"The study of human yawning was a logical extension of earlier animal research.","zh":"人類打呵欠研究是早期動物研究的合理延伸。"},{"en":"A logical extension of something is a natural next step that follows from earlier work or ideas.","zh":"logical extension of something 指由早期工作或想法自然發展而來的下一步。"},{"en":"After teaching basic grammar, essay writing is a logical extension of sentence practice.","zh":"教完基本文法後，文章寫作是句子練習的合理延伸。"},{"en":"If a researcher has studied animal movement, studying human yawning may reasonably follow.","zh":"如果研究人員曾研究動物動作，研究人類打呵欠就是合理延續。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing that a new project grows naturally from an old one.","zh":"顯示新項目自然源自舊項目時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"developmental neuroscience","meaning":"發展神經科學","examples":[{"en":"The researcher’s earlier work was in developmental neuroscience.","zh":"該研究人員早期的工作屬於發展神經科學。"},{"en":"Developmental neuroscience is the study of how the brain and nervous system develop over time.","zh":"developmental neuroscience 指研究大腦和神經系統如何隨時間發展的學科。"},{"en":"A developmental neuroscience study may examine how babies learn to control movement.","zh":"發展神經科學研究可能檢視嬰兒如何學會控制動作。"},{"en":"This field helps explain why some behaviours appear before birth or early in childhood.","zh":"這個領域幫助解釋為何某些行為在出生前或童年早期出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in scientific discussions of brain development.","zh":"在討論大腦發展的科學語境中，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be reported in","meaning":"在……中發表","examples":[{"en":"The findings were reported in several scientific papers.","zh":"這些發現在幾篇科學論文中發表。"},{"en":"Be reported in means be written about or published in a particular source.","zh":"be reported in 指在某個來源中被寫出、報道或發表。"},{"en":"A school’s exam results may be reported in the local newspaper.","zh":"學校考試成績可能在本地報紙中報道。"},{"en":"When findings are reported in scientific papers, other researchers can examine them.","zh":"當研究結果在科學論文中發表，其他研究人員就可以檢視它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving the source where information appeared.","zh":"說明資料出現在哪個來源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"wing-flapping","meaning":"拍動翅膀","examples":[{"en":"The researcher had previously studied wing-flapping in birds.","zh":"研究人員以前研究過鳥類拍動翅膀。"},{"en":"Wing-flapping is the repeated movement of a bird’s wings up and down.","zh":"wing-flapping 指鳥的翅膀反覆上下拍動。"},{"en":"Young birds practise wing-flapping before they can fly properly.","zh":"幼鳥在能正常飛行前會練習拍動翅膀。"},{"en":"Studying wing-flapping can help scientists understand movement, development, and nervous control.","zh":"研究拍動翅膀可以幫助科學家理解動作、發育和神經控制。"},{"en":"This word is useful when describing bird behaviour.","zh":"描述鳥類行為時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"during development and evolution","meaning":"在發育及演化期間","examples":[{"en":"The paper examined wing-flapping during development and evolution.","zh":"該論文檢視拍動翅膀在發育及演化期間的情況。"},{"en":"During development and evolution means while an individual grows and while a species changes over generations.","zh":"during development and evolution 指在個體成長期間，以及物種跨世代改變期間。"},{"en":"Scientists may study how walking changes during development and evolution.","zh":"科學家可能研究行走在發育及演化期間如何改變。"},{"en":"Looking at both levels helps researchers connect individual growth with long-term biological history.","zh":"同時看兩個層面，幫助研究人員把個體成長與長期生物歷史連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing growth within life and change across generations.","zh":"比較生命中的成長和跨世代變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"neurobehavioural problem","meaning":"神經行為問題","examples":[{"en":"Yawning can be studied as a neurobehavioural problem.","zh":"打呵欠可以作為神經行為問題來研究。"},{"en":"A neurobehavioural problem is a question about how the nervous system produces or controls behaviour.","zh":"neurobehavioural problem 指關於神經系統如何產生或控制行為的問題。"},{"en":"Scientists may treat sleepwalking as a neurobehavioural problem because it involves the brain and action.","zh":"科學家可能把夢遊視為神經行為問題，因為它涉及大腦和行動。"},{"en":"Yawning is not only a visible movement; it may reveal how brain circuits trigger behaviour.","zh":"打呵欠不只是可見動作；它可能揭示大腦迴路如何觸發行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in scientific research on brain and behaviour.","zh":"在關於大腦與行為的科學研究中，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"there is not much difference between","meaning":"……之間沒有太大分別","examples":[{"en":"There is not much difference between the two movements as research problems.","zh":"作為研究問題，這兩種動作之間沒有太大分別。"},{"en":"There is not much difference between two things means they are quite similar in the relevant way.","zh":"there is not much difference between two things 指兩者在相關方面相當相似。"},{"en":"There is not much difference between studying at a library and a quiet classroom if both places help concentration.","zh":"如果圖書館和安靜課室都能幫助專注，在兩者之間學習就沒有太大分別。"},{"en":"The researcher saw yawning and wing-flapping as similar problems because both involve movement and nervous control.","zh":"研究人員把打呵欠和拍動翅膀視為相似問題，因為兩者都涉及動作和神經控制。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when two things look different but share an important feature.","zh":"當兩件事看似不同但有重要共通點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"face- and body-flapping","meaning":"面部及身體擺動","examples":[{"en":"Human yawning involves movements of the face and body.","zh":"人類打呵欠涉及面部和身體的動作。"},{"en":"Face- and body-flapping refers to the visible movements of the face and body during yawning.","zh":"face- and body-flapping 指打呵欠時面部和身體可見的動作。"},{"en":"When someone yawns widely and stretches their shoulders, their face and body both move.","zh":"當某人張大口打呵欠並伸展肩膀時，他的面部和身體都會移動。"},{"en":"These movements make yawning more than a simple opening of the mouth.","zh":"這些動作令打呵欠不只是簡單張口。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing yawning as a whole-body action.","zh":"把打呵欠描述為全身性動作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"human yawners","meaning":"打呵欠的人","examples":[{"en":"Human yawners often stretch parts of the face and body.","zh":"打呵欠的人常伸展面部和身體部分。"},{"en":"Human yawners are people who are yawning.","zh":"human yawners 指正在打呵欠的人。"},{"en":"A sleepy student becomes a human yawner when they open their mouth widely during a long lesson.","zh":"困倦學生在長課堂中張大口時，就成為打呵欠的人。"},{"en":"Human yawners may show visible signs of tiredness, boredom, or social response.","zh":"打呵欠的人可能表現出疲倦、沉悶或社交反應的可見跡象。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when focusing on the person who performs the yawn.","zh":"聚焦執行打呵欠動作的人時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ancient, primitive act","meaning":"古老而原始的動作","examples":[{"en":"Yawning is an ancient, primitive act.","zh":"打呵欠是一種古老而原始的動作。"},{"en":"An ancient, primitive act is a very old basic behaviour that appeared early in evolution.","zh":"ancient, primitive act 指在演化早期已出現的非常古老基本行為。"},{"en":"Blinking is a simple protective movement that feels ancient and automatic.","zh":"眨眼是一種簡單保護動作，感覺古老而自動。"},{"en":"Because yawning appears in many animals and before birth, it may be deeply rooted in biology.","zh":"因為打呵欠出現在許多動物身上並在出生前出現，它可能深深植根於生物本能。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a behaviour older than modern human culture.","zh":"描述比現代人類文化更古老的行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"even before birth","meaning":"甚至在出生前","examples":[{"en":"Humans yawn even before birth.","zh":"人類甚至在出生前已會打呵欠。"},{"en":"Even before birth means before a baby is born, while still inside the mother’s body.","zh":"even before birth 指嬰兒出生前，仍在母體內時。"},{"en":"Babies can respond to sounds even before birth.","zh":"嬰兒甚至在出生前已能對聲音有反應。"},{"en":"If yawning appears before birth, it cannot simply be learned from watching other people.","zh":"如果打呵欠在出生前已出現，它就不可能只是透過觀看他人學來的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing that a behaviour begins very early.","zh":"強調某行為很早開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"open wide","meaning":"張得很大","examples":[{"en":"A fetus may open its mouth wide while yawning in the womb.","zh":"胎兒在子宮內打呵欠時，可能把嘴巴張得很大。"},{"en":"To open wide means to open something, especially the mouth or eyes, very broadly.","zh":"open wide 指把某物，尤其是嘴巴或眼睛，張開得很大。"},{"en":"A dentist may ask a patient to open wide during a check-up.","zh":"牙醫檢查時可能要求病人張大口。"},{"en":"Opening the mouth wide is one of the most visible parts of a yawn.","zh":"把嘴張得很大是打呵欠最明顯的部分之一。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a large physical opening.","zh":"描述大幅張開的身體動作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in the womb","meaning":"在子宮內","examples":[{"en":"Human beings begin to yawn while still in the womb.","zh":"人類在仍然在子宮內時已開始打呵欠。"},{"en":"In the womb means inside the mother’s uterus before birth.","zh":"in the womb 指出生前在母親子宮內。"},{"en":"Doctors can observe a baby’s movement in the womb using medical scans.","zh":"醫生可以使用醫學掃描觀察嬰兒在子宮內的活動。"},{"en":"Behaviours seen in the womb may be part of early biological development.","zh":"在子宮內可見的行為可能屬於早期生物發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing prenatal development.","zh":"討論產前發育時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"unhinge their jaws","meaning":"使下顎脫離關節位置","examples":[{"en":"Some snakes unhinge their jaws when they yawn.","zh":"有些蛇打呵欠時會使下顎脫離關節位置。"},{"en":"To unhinge their jaws means to loosen or open the jaw joint far beyond normal movement.","zh":"unhinge their jaws 指放鬆或張開下顎關節，幅度遠超一般動作。"},{"en":"A snake may appear to unhinge its jaws when it opens its mouth very widely.","zh":"蛇張口很大時，看起來可能像使下顎脫離關節位置。"},{"en":"This movement allows certain animals to make extremely large mouth openings.","zh":"這種動作讓某些動物能把嘴巴張得極大。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing dramatic jaw movement in animals.","zh":"描述動物戲劇性的下顎動作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"one species of penguin","meaning":"一種企鵝","examples":[{"en":"One species of penguin yawns during courtship behaviour.","zh":"一種企鵝在求偶行為期間會打呵欠。"},{"en":"One species of penguin means one particular biological kind of penguin.","zh":"one species of penguin 指某一特定生物種類的企鵝。"},{"en":"One species of bird may sing loudly while another stays mostly silent.","zh":"一種鳥可能大聲鳴唱，而另一種則多數安靜。"},{"en":"Mentioning one species shows that the behaviour is not necessarily shared by all penguins.","zh":"提到一種物種顯示該行為不一定適用於所有企鵝。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a statement applies to one type, not a whole group.","zh":"當說法只適用於某一類而非整個群體時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as part of mating","meaning":"作為交配行為的一部分","examples":[{"en":"The penguin yawns as part of mating.","zh":"這種企鵝打呵欠作為交配行為的一部分。"},{"en":"As part of mating means as one behaviour involved in attracting or choosing a mate.","zh":"as part of mating 指作為吸引或選擇伴侶的一種行為。"},{"en":"Some birds sing, dance, or display feathers as part of mating.","zh":"有些鳥會唱歌、跳舞或展示羽毛作為交配行為的一部分。"},{"en":"A behaviour may look ordinary to humans but play an important role in reproduction.","zh":"某行為在人類看來可能普通，但在繁殖中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when animal behaviour is connected to courtship.","zh":"當動物行為與求偶有關時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"only now are researchers beginning to","meaning":"研究人員直至現在才開始……","examples":[{"en":"Only now are researchers beginning to understand contagious yawning.","zh":"研究人員直至現在才開始理解傳染性打呵欠。"},{"en":"Only now are researchers beginning to means researchers have started to understand something only recently.","zh":"only now are researchers beginning to 指研究人員直到最近才開始理解某事。"},{"en":"Only now are schools beginning to understand how strongly sleep affects learning.","zh":"學校直到現在才開始理解睡眠對學習有多大影響。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that the topic has been unclear for a long time.","zh":"這個短語暗示該主題長時間以來一直不清楚。"},{"en":"This structure is useful when emphasising recent progress after long uncertainty.","zh":"強調長期不確定後的近期進展時，這個結構很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"why we yawn back","meaning":"為何我們會跟着打呵欠","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are investigating why we yawn back after seeing another person yawn.","zh":"科學家正在研究為何我們看見另一個人打呵欠後會跟着打呵欠。"},{"en":"Why we yawn back refers to the reason people yawn after seeing or hearing someone else yawn.","zh":"why we yawn back 指人們看到或聽到別人打呵欠後自己也打呵欠的原因。"},{"en":"A student may yawn back in class after noticing a friend yawn across the room.","zh":"學生在課堂上看見房間另一邊的朋友打呵欠後，可能也跟着打呵欠。"},{"en":"This reaction may reveal something about attention, empathy, or social connection.","zh":"這種反應可能揭示專注、同理心或社交連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing contagious yawning.","zh":"討論傳染性打呵欠時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cognitive neuroscience","meaning":"認知神經科學","examples":[{"en":"Steven Platek is a professor of cognitive neuroscience.","zh":"Steven Platek 是認知神經科學教授。"},{"en":"Cognitive neuroscience is the study of how brain activity supports thinking, feeling, memory, and behaviour.","zh":"cognitive neuroscience 指研究大腦活動如何支持思考、情感、記憶和行為的學科。"},{"en":"A cognitive neuroscience study may scan the brain while people make decisions.","zh":"認知神經科學研究可能在人們作決定時掃描大腦。"},{"en":"This field can connect visible behaviour, such as yawning, with hidden brain processes.","zh":"這個領域可以把打呵欠等可見行為與隱藏大腦過程連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in scientific discussions of mind and brain.","zh":"在關於心智和大腦的科學討論中，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"contagious yawning","meaning":"傳染性打呵欠","examples":[{"en":"Contagious yawning occurs when one person’s yawn triggers another.","zh":"當一個人的呵欠引發另一個人的呵欠時，就出現傳染性打呵欠。"},{"en":"Contagious yawning means yawning that spreads from one person to another.","zh":"contagious yawning 指從一個人傳到另一個人的打呵欠。"},{"en":"A student may start yawning after watching a classmate yawn during a quiet lesson.","zh":"學生在安靜課堂中看見同學打呵欠後，可能開始打呵欠。"},{"en":"The reaction may happen because the viewer is paying attention to another person’s state.","zh":"這種反應可能發生，是因為觀看者留意到另一個人的狀態。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when yawning behaves like a social response.","zh":"當打呵欠像社交反應般出現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be done only by","meaning":"只由……作出","examples":[{"en":"Contagious yawning appears to be done only by humans and other primates.","zh":"傳染性打呵欠看來只由人類和其他靈長類動物作出。"},{"en":"Be done only by means be performed by a limited group and not by others.","zh":"be done only by 指某行為只由有限群體執行，而不是由其他群體執行。"},{"en":"Some school duties are done only by trained staff because they involve safety.","zh":"有些學校職責只由受過訓練的職員執行，因為涉及安全。"},{"en":"If a behaviour is done only by certain species, it may reveal something special about their brains.","zh":"如果某行為只由某些物種作出，它可能揭示牠們大腦的特別之處。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when limiting who can perform an action.","zh":"限定誰能執行某行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"other primates","meaning":"其他靈長類動物","examples":[{"en":"Contagious yawning has been observed in people and other primates.","zh":"傳染性打呵欠在人類和其他靈長類動物身上被觀察到。"},{"en":"Other primates are animals related to humans, such as apes and monkeys.","zh":"other primates 指與人類有親緣關係的動物，例如猿和猴。"},{"en":"Scientists may compare humans with other primates to study social behaviour.","zh":"科學家可能比較人類和其他靈長類動物，以研究社交行為。"},{"en":"Similar behaviour in humans and other primates can suggest shared biological roots.","zh":"人類和其他靈長類動物有相似行為，可能暗示共同生物根源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in discussions of human and animal behaviour.","zh":"討論人類和動物行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"psychological test","meaning":"心理測驗","examples":[{"en":"Platek used a psychological test in his first experiment.","zh":"Platek 在第一項實驗中使用心理測驗。"},{"en":"A psychological test is a tool used to measure thoughts, feelings, personality, ability, or behaviour.","zh":"psychological test 指用來量度思想、感受、性格、能力或行為的工具。"},{"en":"A school counsellor may use a psychological test to understand a student’s anxiety level.","zh":"學校輔導員可能使用心理測驗來了解學生焦慮程度。"},{"en":"In yawning research, such a test can help compare empathy with yawning response.","zh":"在打呵欠研究中，這類測驗可以幫助比較同理心和打呵欠反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when mental or emotional qualities are measured.","zh":"當心理或情緒特質被量度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rank people on","meaning":"按……為人評級","examples":[{"en":"The test ranked people on their level of empathy.","zh":"這項測驗按同理心水平為人評級。"},{"en":"To rank people on something means to place them in order according to that quality or score.","zh":"rank people on something 指根據某種特質或分數把人排序。"},{"en":"A school may rank students on reading speed for research, not for punishment.","zh":"學校可能按閱讀速度為學生評級作研究用途，而不是懲罰。"},{"en":"Ranking people can help researchers compare high and low groups in an experiment.","zh":"為人評級可以幫助研究人員在實驗中比較高低組別。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when participants are sorted by a measured trait.","zh":"當參與者按被量度特質分類時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"empathic feelings","meaning":"同理心感受","examples":[{"en":"The test measured the participants’ empathic feelings.","zh":"這項測驗量度參與者的同理心感受。"},{"en":"Empathic feelings are feelings of understanding or sharing another person’s emotions.","zh":"empathic feelings 指理解或感受到另一個人情緒的感受。"},{"en":"A student may have empathic feelings when a classmate cries after failing a test.","zh":"當同學考試不合格後哭泣，學生可能產生同理心感受。"},{"en":"Strong empathic feelings can make people notice and respond to others’ discomfort.","zh":"強烈同理心感受可以令人注意並回應他人的不適。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing emotional connection.","zh":"討論情感連繫時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"score high on","meaning":"在……方面取得高分","examples":[{"en":"Some participants did not score high on compassion.","zh":"有些參與者在同情心方面沒有取得高分。"},{"en":"To score high on something means to receive a high result in a test or measure of that quality.","zh":"score high on something 指在某項測驗或特質量度中取得高分。"},{"en":"A student may score high on vocabulary but low on listening.","zh":"學生可能在詞彙方面取得高分，但在聆聽方面分數較低。"},{"en":"People who score high on empathy may be more likely to respond to others’ emotions.","zh":"在同理心方面取得高分的人，可能較容易回應他人情緒。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing measured abilities or traits.","zh":"比較被量度的能力或特質時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"compassion","meaning":"同情心；憐憫心","examples":[{"en":"The experiment examined whether compassion was related to yawning.","zh":"實驗檢視同情心是否與打呵欠有關。"},{"en":"Compassion is a caring feeling toward someone who is suffering or in difficulty.","zh":"compassion 指對正在受苦或遇到困難的人產生關懷感。"},{"en":"A student shows compassion when they help a classmate who is upset after losing a competition.","zh":"學生在同學比賽失敗後難過時安慰他，就是表現同情心。"},{"en":"Compassion can lead people to notice others’ pain and offer support.","zh":"同情心可以令人注意到他人的痛苦並提供支援。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing kindness, empathy, and social behaviour.","zh":"討論善意、同理心和社交行為時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"yawn back","meaning":"跟着打呵欠","examples":[{"en":"Participants with lower empathy were less likely to yawn back.","zh":"同理心較低的參與者較少可能跟着打呵欠。"},{"en":"To yawn back means to yawn in response to seeing or hearing another person yawn.","zh":"yawn back 指看到或聽到別人打呵欠後自己也打呵欠。"},{"en":"A child may yawn back after watching a parent yawn on the sofa.","zh":"孩子看見父母在梳化上打呵欠後，可能跟着打呵欠。"},{"en":"If someone does not yawn back, it may suggest the social trigger did not affect them strongly.","zh":"如果某人沒有跟着打呵欠，可能表示社交觸發對他影響不強。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing contagious yawning.","zh":"描述傳染性打呵欠時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"literally have people saying","meaning":"真的有人說……","examples":[{"en":"The researchers literally had people asking why they were watching yawns.","zh":"研究人員真的遇到有人問為何要觀看打呵欠。"},{"en":"Literally have people saying means people actually said something, not just metaphorically.","zh":"literally have people saying 指人們真的說了某話，而不只是比喻。"},{"en":"The lecture was so confusing that the teacher literally had students asking what the topic was.","zh":"那堂課太令人困惑，老師真的遇到學生問主題是甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the reaction really happened in the experiment.","zh":"這個短語強調該反應在實驗中真的發生。"},{"en":"It is useful when a response sounds surprising but is true.","zh":"當某個反應聽起來令人驚訝但是真實時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have no effect","meaning":"沒有作用","examples":[{"en":"The yawning videos had no effect on some participants.","zh":"打呵欠影片對某些參與者沒有作用。"},{"en":"Have no effect means not change or influence someone or something.","zh":"have no effect 指沒有改變或影響某人或某事。"},{"en":"A warning sign may have no effect if students do not read it.","zh":"如果學生不閱讀警告牌，它可能沒有作用。"},{"en":"If the videos had no effect, those participants did not yawn in response.","zh":"如果影片沒有作用，那些參與者就沒有跟着打呵欠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something produces no visible result.","zh":"當某事沒有產生可見結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"second experiment","meaning":"第二項實驗","examples":[{"en":"Platek used brain imaging in his second experiment.","zh":"Platek 在第二項實驗中使用腦部成像。"},{"en":"A second experiment is another study carried out after the first one.","zh":"second experiment 指在第一項之後進行的另一項研究。"},{"en":"If the first classroom activity fails, a teacher may try a second experiment with a different method.","zh":"如果第一個課堂活動失敗，老師可能用不同方法嘗試第二項實驗。"},{"en":"A second experiment can test whether earlier findings appear under new conditions.","zh":"第二項實驗可以測試早期發現在新條件下是否仍然出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research develops step by step.","zh":"當研究逐步發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"put someone in a machine","meaning":"讓某人進入儀器","examples":[{"en":"The researchers put ten students in a brain-imaging machine.","zh":"研究人員讓十名學生進入腦部成像儀器。"},{"en":"To put someone in a machine means to place a person inside a device for testing or scanning.","zh":"put someone in a machine 指把某人放入設備內作測試或掃描。"},{"en":"Doctors may put a patient in a scanning machine to examine an injured knee.","zh":"醫生可能讓病人進入掃描儀器，以檢查受傷膝蓋。"},{"en":"In experiments, placing people in machines allows researchers to collect physical data.","zh":"在實驗中，讓人進入儀器可以讓研究人員收集身體數據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing medical or scientific testing.","zh":"描述醫學或科學測試時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"magnetic resonance imaging machine","meaning":"磁力共振成像儀","examples":[{"en":"The students watched videos inside a magnetic resonance imaging machine.","zh":"學生在磁力共振成像儀內觀看影片。"},{"en":"A magnetic resonance imaging machine is a medical scanner that uses magnets to create images of the inside of the body.","zh":"magnetic resonance imaging machine 指使用磁場製造人體內部影像的醫學掃描儀器。"},{"en":"A hospital may use a magnetic resonance imaging machine to examine the brain after an injury.","zh":"醫院可能使用磁力共振成像儀檢查受傷後的大腦。"},{"en":"In yawning research, the machine can show which brain areas become active.","zh":"在打呵欠研究中，這部儀器可以顯示哪些大腦區域變得活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in medical and neuroscience contexts.","zh":"這個短語適用於醫學和神經科學語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"watch videotapes of","meaning":"觀看……的錄影片段","examples":[{"en":"The students watched videotapes of people yawning.","zh":"學生觀看人們打呵欠的錄影片段。"},{"en":"To watch videotapes of something means to view recorded videos showing that action or subject.","zh":"watch videotapes of something 指觀看顯示某行動或主題的錄影。"},{"en":"Students may watch videotapes of public speeches to learn presentation skills.","zh":"學生可能觀看公開演講的錄影片段，以學習演講技巧。"},{"en":"Watching yawning videos allowed researchers to see whether participants would yawn back.","zh":"觀看打呵欠影片讓研究人員觀察參與者是否會跟着打呵欠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when recorded behaviour is used in an experiment.","zh":"當錄下的行為被用於實驗時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the part of the brain which reacted","meaning":"作出反應的大腦部分","examples":[{"en":"The researchers identified the part of the brain which reacted to the videos.","zh":"研究人員找出對影片作出反應的大腦部分。"},{"en":"The part of the brain which reacted means the brain region that became active during a stimulus.","zh":"the part of the brain which reacted 指在刺激出現時變得活躍的大腦區域。"},{"en":"A scan can show the part of the brain which reacted when a patient heard familiar music.","zh":"掃描可以顯示病人聽到熟悉音樂時作出反應的大腦部分。"},{"en":"Finding the reacting brain area helps connect behaviour with brain function.","zh":"找出反應的大腦區域，有助把行為與大腦功能連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing brain-imaging results.","zh":"描述腦部成像結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"control empathy","meaning":"控制同理心","examples":[{"en":"Scientists believe that this brain region helps control empathy.","zh":"科學家相信這個大腦區域幫助控制同理心。"},{"en":"To control empathy means to help regulate the ability to understand or share another person’s feelings.","zh":"control empathy 指幫助調節理解或感受他人情緒的能力。"},{"en":"Some brain areas help control emotion when people see others in pain.","zh":"當人看見別人痛苦時，某些大腦區域幫助控制情緒。"},{"en":"If a region controls empathy, it may become active when people respond emotionally to others.","zh":"如果某區域控制同理心，它在人們對他人作出情感反應時可能變得活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how the brain supports social feeling.","zh":"討論大腦如何支持社交情感時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"posterior cingulate","meaning":"後扣帶皮層","examples":[{"en":"The posterior cingulate became active during contagious yawning.","zh":"後扣帶皮層在傳染性打呵欠期間變得活躍。"},{"en":"The posterior cingulate is a brain region linked with attention, awareness, and social processing.","zh":"posterior cingulate 指與注意、意識和社交處理有關的大腦區域。"},{"en":"Neuroscientists may observe the posterior cingulate when people think about themselves or others.","zh":"當人思考自己或他人時，神經科學家可能觀察後扣帶皮層。"},{"en":"Its activity during contagious yawning suggests yawning may involve more than simple breathing.","zh":"它在傳染性打呵欠中活躍，暗示打呵欠可能不只是簡單呼吸。"},{"en":"This phrase is technical and useful in brain-imaging research.","zh":"這個短語較技術性，適用於腦部成像研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"middle rear of the brain","meaning":"大腦中後部","examples":[{"en":"The posterior cingulate lies near the middle rear of the brain.","zh":"後扣帶皮層位於大腦中後部附近。"},{"en":"The middle rear of the brain means the central back area inside the brain.","zh":"middle rear of the brain 指大腦內部中央偏後的位置。"},{"en":"A brain diagram can help students locate the middle rear of the brain more easily.","zh":"腦部圖表可以幫助學生更容易找出大腦中後部。"},{"en":"Giving the location helps readers understand where the named brain region sits.","zh":"提供位置有助讀者理解所命名的大腦區域位於哪裏。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining anatomy in simple words.","zh":"用簡單文字解釋解剖位置時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not necessarily","meaning":"不一定","examples":[{"en":"Platek said that frequent yawning did not necessarily mean someone was nicer.","zh":"Platek 說，經常打呵欠不一定代表某人較友善。"},{"en":"Not necessarily means not always or not in every case.","zh":"not necessarily 指不總是或並非每種情況都如此。"},{"en":"A quiet student is not necessarily unhappy; they may simply be concentrating.","zh":"安靜的學生不一定不開心；他可能只是正在專心。"},{"en":"Frequent contagious yawning may suggest empathy, but it does not prove kindness by itself.","zh":"經常出現傳染性打呵欠可能暗示同理心，但不能單獨證明善良。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when avoiding an over-simple conclusion.","zh":"避免過度簡化結論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a good indicator of","meaning":"……的良好指標","examples":[{"en":"Contagious yawning may be a good indicator of a person’s mental state.","zh":"傳染性打呵欠可能是一個人心理狀態的良好指標。"},{"en":"A good indicator of something is a sign that gives useful information about it.","zh":"good indicator of something 指能提供有用資訊的跡象。"},{"en":"Regular homework completion can be a good indicator of a student’s study habits.","zh":"定期完成功課可以是學生學習習慣的良好指標。"},{"en":"If yawning back reflects attention or empathy, it may tell researchers about the mind.","zh":"如果跟着打呵欠反映專注或同理心，它可能告訴研究人員心理狀態。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one visible sign suggests a hidden condition.","zh":"當一個可見跡象暗示隱藏狀況時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"state of mind","meaning":"心理狀態","examples":[{"en":"Yawning may provide information about a person’s state of mind.","zh":"打呵欠可能提供關於一個人心理狀態的資料。"},{"en":"State of mind means a person’s mental or emotional condition at a particular time.","zh":"state of mind 指人在某一時間的心理或情緒狀況。"},{"en":"A student’s state of mind before an exam may affect confidence and performance.","zh":"學生考試前的心理狀態可能影響信心和表現。"},{"en":"Tiredness, stress, attention, and empathy can all be part of someone’s mental state.","zh":"疲倦、壓力、專注和同理心都可以是一個人心理狀態的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing what a person is thinking or feeling.","zh":"討論一個人正在想甚麼或感受甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"empathise with","meaning":"對……產生同理心","examples":[{"en":"Yawning back may show that someone is empathising with another person.","zh":"跟着打呵欠可能顯示某人正對另一個人產生同理心。"},{"en":"To empathise with someone means to understand or share that person’s feelings.","zh":"empathise with someone 指理解或感受到某人的情緒。"},{"en":"A teacher may empathise with a nervous student because they remember feeling the same before exams.","zh":"老師可能對緊張學生產生同理心，因為他記得自己考試前也有相同感受。"},{"en":"When people empathise with others, they may respond to their emotions or body signals.","zh":"當人對他人產生同理心，他們可能回應對方的情緒或身體訊號。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing emotional connection.","zh":"討論情感連繫時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pay attention","meaning":"留心；專注","examples":[{"en":"Contagious yawning may indicate that someone is paying attention.","zh":"傳染性打呵欠可能顯示某人正在留心。"},{"en":"To pay attention means to notice, watch, or listen carefully.","zh":"pay attention 指留意、觀看或仔細聆聽。"},{"en":"A student who pays attention in class can answer questions about the lesson.","zh":"上課專心的學生能回答關於課堂的問題。"},{"en":"If a person notices another person yawning, they must be attending to that person at some level.","zh":"如果一個人注意到另一個人打呵欠，他在某程度上必然留意着對方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing focus and awareness.","zh":"討論專注和意識時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"third experiment","meaning":"第三項實驗","examples":[{"en":"Platek’s third experiment focused on people with brain disorders.","zh":"Platek 的第三項實驗聚焦有腦部疾病的人。"},{"en":"A third experiment is the next study after the first and second experiments.","zh":"third experiment 指第一和第二項實驗之後的下一項研究。"},{"en":"A scientist may run a third experiment to test the same idea with a different group of people.","zh":"科學家可能進行第三項實驗，用不同人群測試同一想法。"},{"en":"Using another experiment helps researchers check whether earlier results are reliable.","zh":"使用另一項實驗幫助研究人員檢查早期結果是否可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a research project has several stages.","zh":"當研究項目有幾個階段時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"brain disorders","meaning":"腦部疾病","examples":[{"en":"The experiment examined yawning in people with brain disorders.","zh":"實驗檢視有腦部疾病人士的打呵欠情況。"},{"en":"Brain disorders are conditions that affect how the brain works.","zh":"brain disorders 指影響大腦如何運作的狀況。"},{"en":"Epilepsy, autism, and some injuries can involve brain disorders or brain-related difficulties.","zh":"癲癇、自閉症和某些創傷可能涉及腦部疾病或腦部相關困難。"},{"en":"Studying brain disorders can reveal which brain systems are needed for normal behaviour.","zh":"研究腦部疾病可以揭示正常行為需要哪些大腦系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in medical and neuroscience contexts.","zh":"這個短語適用於醫學和神經科學語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"such as","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"The study included disorders such as autism and schizophrenia.","zh":"研究包括自閉症和思覺失調等疾病。"},{"en":"Such as means for example.","zh":"such as 指例如。"},{"en":"Students should bring stationery such as pens, pencils, and rulers.","zh":"學生應帶文具，例如原子筆、鉛筆和間尺。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples without claiming the list is complete.","zh":"這個短語引入例子，但不表示清單完整。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving clear examples of a broader category.","zh":"為較廣泛類別提供清楚例子時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"autism","meaning":"自閉症","examples":[{"en":"People with autism may experience difficulty connecting emotionally with others.","zh":"自閉症人士可能較難與他人建立情感聯繫。"},{"en":"Autism is a developmental condition that can affect communication, social interaction, and behaviour.","zh":"autism 指一種發展狀況，可能影響溝通、社交互動和行為。"},{"en":"A child with autism may prefer routine and find sudden changes stressful.","zh":"有自閉症的孩子可能偏好固定規律，並覺得突然改變很有壓力。"},{"en":"Autism affects people differently, so support should match each person’s needs.","zh":"自閉症對每個人影響不同，因此支援應配合個別需要。"},{"en":"This word is useful in discussions of development and social communication.","zh":"這個詞適用於發展和社交溝通討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"schizophrenia","meaning":"思覺失調","examples":[{"en":"Schizophrenia may affect emotional and social connections.","zh":"思覺失調可能影響情感和社交連繫。"},{"en":"Schizophrenia is a serious mental disorder that can affect thinking, perception, emotion, and behaviour.","zh":"schizophrenia 指一種嚴重精神障礙，可能影響思考、感知、情緒和行為。"},{"en":"A person with schizophrenia may need medical treatment, social support, and stable routines.","zh":"思覺失調患者可能需要醫療治療、社會支援和穩定日常規律。"},{"en":"Because it can affect how people interpret reality, it may influence social connection.","zh":"因為它可以影響人如何理解現實，所以可能影響社交連繫。"},{"en":"This word is useful in medical and psychological contexts.","zh":"這個詞適用於醫學和心理學語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have difficulty doing","meaning":"做……有困難","examples":[{"en":"Some patients have difficulty connecting emotionally with others.","zh":"有些病人與他人建立情感聯繫有困難。"},{"en":"To have difficulty doing something means to find that action hard to do.","zh":"have difficulty doing something 指覺得做某事困難。"},{"en":"A beginner may have difficulty understanding fast English speech.","zh":"初學者可能難以理解快速英語說話。"},{"en":"If people have difficulty connecting emotionally, social situations may feel confusing or tiring.","zh":"如果人們難以建立情感聯繫，社交情況可能令人困惑或疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a struggle with an action.","zh":"描述做某事有困難時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"connect emotionally with","meaning":"與……建立情感聯繫","examples":[{"en":"People with certain disorders may struggle to connect emotionally with others.","zh":"有某些疾病的人可能難以與他人建立情感聯繫。"},{"en":"To connect emotionally with someone means to feel understanding, sympathy, or closeness with that person.","zh":"connect emotionally with someone 指與某人產生理解、同情或親近感。"},{"en":"A teacher connects emotionally with students when they notice fear, frustration, or excitement.","zh":"當老師注意到學生的恐懼、挫折或興奮時，就能與學生建立情感聯繫。"},{"en":"Emotional connection can make communication feel safer and more meaningful.","zh":"情感連繫可以令溝通感覺更安全和更有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing relationships and empathy.","zh":"討論關係和同理心時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"one of the few other researchers","meaning":"少數其他研究人員之一","examples":[{"en":"Robert Provine is one of the few other researchers studying yawning.","zh":"Robert Provine 是少數其他研究打呵欠的研究人員之一。"},{"en":"One of the few other researchers means one of a small number of people also working on the same topic.","zh":"one of the few other researchers 指同樣研究某主題的少數人之一。"},{"en":"A teacher may be one of the few other researchers studying how students learn idioms in daily speech.","zh":"老師可能是少數研究學生如何在日常說話中學習成語的研究人員之一。"},{"en":"If only a few researchers study a topic, the field may still be young or unusual.","zh":"如果只有少數研究人員研究某主題，該領域可能仍年輕或不尋常。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a research area has very few specialists.","zh":"當研究領域專家很少時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the basic yawn","meaning":"一般的呵欠","examples":[{"en":"Provine found that the basic yawn lasts about six seconds.","zh":"Provine 發現一般的呵欠持續約六秒。"},{"en":"The basic yawn means the ordinary or typical form of a yawn.","zh":"basic yawn 指普通或典型形式的呵欠。"},{"en":"A basic yawn usually involves opening the mouth widely and taking a deep breath.","zh":"一般的呵欠通常涉及張大口和深吸氣。"},{"en":"Measuring the basic yawn gives researchers a standard pattern to compare with unusual cases.","zh":"量度一般呵欠讓研究人員有標準模式可與異常情況比較。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the normal version of a behaviour.","zh":"描述某行為的正常版本時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"last about six seconds","meaning":"持續約六秒","examples":[{"en":"An average yawn lasts about six seconds.","zh":"一般一次呵欠持續約六秒。"},{"en":"Last about six seconds means continue for roughly six seconds.","zh":"last about six seconds 指持續大約六秒。"},{"en":"A short traffic light countdown may last about six seconds before changing.","zh":"短暫交通燈倒數可能在轉燈前持續約六秒。"},{"en":"Measuring duration helps researchers describe yawning more precisely.","zh":"量度持續時間幫助研究人員更精確描述打呵欠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving an approximate length of time.","zh":"提供大約時間長度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"come in bouts","meaning":"一陣陣出現","examples":[{"en":"Yawns often come in bouts rather than occurring only once.","zh":"呵欠常一陣陣出現，而不是只出現一次。"},{"en":"Come in bouts means happen several times in a short period, with pauses between them.","zh":"come in bouts 指在短時間內多次發生，中間有停頓。"},{"en":"Coughs may come in bouts when someone has a throat infection.","zh":"當某人喉嚨感染時，咳嗽可能一陣陣出現。"},{"en":"If yawns come in bouts, one yawn may be followed by another after a short interval.","zh":"如果呵欠一陣陣出現，一次呵欠後可能隔一小段時間又來一次。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when actions happen in repeated clusters.","zh":"當動作成群重複發生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at an interval of","meaning":"每隔……","examples":[{"en":"Yawns may occur at an interval of about 68 seconds.","zh":"呵欠可能每隔約68秒出現一次。"},{"en":"At an interval of something means with that amount of time between one event and the next.","zh":"at an interval of something 指兩次事件之間相隔某段時間。"},{"en":"Buses may arrive at an interval of ten minutes during busy hours.","zh":"繁忙時段，巴士可能每隔十分鐘到站。"},{"en":"Measuring intervals helps researchers see whether a pattern is regular.","zh":"量度間隔幫助研究人員看出模式是否有規律。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing repeated events separated by time.","zh":"描述相隔一段時間的重複事件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"half-yawn","meaning":"打半個呵欠","examples":[{"en":"Men and women half-yawn with similar frequency.","zh":"男性和女性打半個呵欠的頻率相似。"},{"en":"A half-yawn is an incomplete or smaller yawn that does not fully open the mouth.","zh":"half-yawn 指不完整或較小的呵欠，嘴巴沒有完全張開。"},{"en":"A student trying to stay polite in class may give only a half-yawn.","zh":"學生在課堂上想保持禮貌，可能只打半個呵欠。"},{"en":"Half-yawns can still show tiredness even if they are less obvious than full yawns.","zh":"半個呵欠即使不如完整呵欠明顯，仍可顯示疲倦。"},{"en":"This word is useful when describing a partial version of a yawn.","zh":"描述呵欠的部分版本時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"equally often","meaning":"同樣頻密","examples":[{"en":"Men and women yawn equally often.","zh":"男性和女性打呵欠同樣頻密。"},{"en":"Equally often means with the same frequency.","zh":"equally often 指以相同頻率發生。"},{"en":"Two buses may arrive equally often if each comes every fifteen minutes.","zh":"如果兩條巴士線每十五分鐘一班，它們就同樣頻密。"},{"en":"If two groups yawn equally often, gender alone may not explain the frequency.","zh":"如果兩組人打呵欠同樣頻密，單靠性別可能不能解釋頻率。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing how often actions happen.","zh":"比較行動發生頻率時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be significantly less likely to","meaning":"明顯較少可能……","examples":[{"en":"Men are significantly less likely to cover their mouths.","zh":"男性明顯較少可能掩着嘴巴。"},{"en":"Be significantly less likely to means have a much lower chance of doing something.","zh":"be significantly less likely to 指做某事的可能性低得多。"},{"en":"Students who sleep well may be significantly less likely to fall asleep in class.","zh":"睡得好的學生在課堂上睡着的可能性可能明顯較低。"},{"en":"A large difference between groups can suggest a meaningful behavioural pattern.","zh":"群體之間的大差異可以暗示有意義的行為模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing probabilities in research.","zh":"在研究中比較可能性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cover their mouths","meaning":"掩着嘴巴","examples":[{"en":"Some people cover their mouths while yawning.","zh":"有些人打呵欠時會掩着嘴巴。"},{"en":"To cover their mouths means to place a hand or object over the mouth.","zh":"cover their mouths 指把手或物件放在嘴巴上遮住。"},{"en":"A polite student may cover their mouth when coughing in class.","zh":"有禮貌的學生在課堂咳嗽時可能掩着嘴巴。"},{"en":"People may cover their mouths while yawning because of manners or hygiene.","zh":"人們打呵欠時可能因禮貌或衛生而掩着嘴巴。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing social behaviour around the mouth.","zh":"描述與嘴部有關的社交行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"indicate a complex distinction","meaning":"顯示複雜差異","examples":[{"en":"The behaviour may indicate a complex distinction between the genders.","zh":"這種行為可能顯示男女之間的複雜差異。"},{"en":"To indicate a complex distinction means to suggest a difference that is not simple or easy to explain.","zh":"indicate a complex distinction 指暗示一種不簡單或不易解釋的差異。"},{"en":"Different study habits may indicate a complex distinction between younger and older students.","zh":"不同學習習慣可能顯示年幼學生和年長學生之間的複雜差異。"},{"en":"If men and women cover their mouths differently, social habits may be involved.","zh":"如果男性和女性掩嘴方式不同，可能涉及社交習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when behaviour suggests a deeper difference.","zh":"當行為暗示更深層差異時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"between the genders","meaning":"男女之間","examples":[{"en":"Yawning behaviour may differ between the genders.","zh":"打呵欠行為可能在男女之間有所不同。"},{"en":"Between the genders means comparing males and females.","zh":"between the genders 指比較男性和女性。"},{"en":"A survey may find differences between the genders in preferred sports or hobbies.","zh":"調查可能發現男女之間在喜歡的運動或興趣上有差異。"},{"en":"Differences between genders may reflect biology, culture, habit, or a mixture of these.","zh":"男女之間的差異可能反映生物、文化、習慣或它們的混合。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing male and female behaviour.","zh":"比較男性和女性行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a watched yawner never yawns","meaning":"被人注視時反而不會打呵欠","examples":[{"en":"Provine joked that a watched yawner never yawns.","zh":"Provine 開玩笑說，被人注視時反而不會打呵欠。"},{"en":"A watched yawner never yawns means someone being closely observed may stop doing the very thing researchers want to see.","zh":"a watched yawner never yawns 指被仔細觀察的人可能停止做研究人員想看到的事情。"},{"en":"A shy child may stop singing when adults watch too closely.","zh":"害羞孩子在成人太仔細看着時，可能停止唱歌。"},{"en":"Observation can change behaviour because people become self-conscious.","zh":"觀察可以改變行為，因為人會變得有自我意識。"},{"en":"This humorous phrase is useful when research subjects behave differently under attention.","zh":"當研究對象在被注意時行為不同，這個幽默短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"physical root of yawning","meaning":"打呵欠的生理根源","examples":[{"en":"The physical root of yawning remains uncertain.","zh":"打呵欠的生理根源仍不確定。"},{"en":"The physical root of yawning means the bodily or biological cause behind yawning.","zh":"physical root of yawning 指打呵欠背後的身體或生物原因。"},{"en":"Doctors may look for the physical root of a headache before giving treatment.","zh":"醫生可能先尋找頭痛的生理根源，再給予治療。"},{"en":"If the physical root is unclear, researchers cannot fully explain why yawning occurs.","zh":"如果生理根源不清楚，研究人員就不能完整解釋為何會打呵欠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when asking for the biological cause of a behaviour.","zh":"詢問某行為的生物原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"remain a mystery","meaning":"仍然是謎","examples":[{"en":"The precise biological cause of yawning remains a mystery.","zh":"打呵欠的準確生物原因仍然是謎。"},{"en":"Remain a mystery means still be unknown or unexplained.","zh":"remain a mystery 指仍然未知或未被解釋。"},{"en":"The reason a student suddenly improved may remain a mystery if no one knows about their extra practice.","zh":"如果沒有人知道學生額外練習，他突然進步的原因可能仍然是謎。"},{"en":"A mystery remains when evidence is not enough to give a clear answer.","zh":"當證據不足以給出清楚答案，謎團就仍然存在。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a question has not yet been solved.","zh":"當問題尚未解決時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be coordinated within","meaning":"在……內協調","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers believe yawning is coordinated within the hypothalamus.","zh":"有些研究人員相信打呵欠在下丘腦內被協調。"},{"en":"Be coordinated within means be organised or controlled inside a particular body part or system.","zh":"be coordinated within 指在某個身體部位或系統內被組織或控制。"},{"en":"Breathing is coordinated within brain systems that regulate rhythm and response.","zh":"呼吸在調節節奏和反應的大腦系統內被協調。"},{"en":"If yawning is coordinated within the hypothalamus, that area may help organise the whole action.","zh":"如果打呵欠在下丘腦內協調，該區域可能幫助組織整個動作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining where a biological process is controlled.","zh":"解釋生物過程在哪裏被控制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hypothalamus","meaning":"下丘腦","examples":[{"en":"The hypothalamus may help coordinate yawning and breathing.","zh":"下丘腦可能幫助協調打呵欠和呼吸。"},{"en":"The hypothalamus is a small brain region involved in controlling basic body functions.","zh":"hypothalamus 指大腦中一個參與控制基本身體功能的小區域。"},{"en":"The hypothalamus helps regulate hunger, temperature, sleep, and hormones.","zh":"下丘腦幫助調節飢餓、體溫、睡眠和荷爾蒙。"},{"en":"Because yawning may be linked to breathing and body state, the hypothalamus may be involved.","zh":"因為打呵欠可能與呼吸和身體狀態有關，下丘腦可能參與其中。"},{"en":"This word is useful in neuroscience and physiology.","zh":"這個詞適用於神經科學和生理學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the area that controls","meaning":"控制……的區域","examples":[{"en":"The hypothalamus is an area that also controls breathing.","zh":"下丘腦也是控制呼吸的區域。"},{"en":"The area that controls something is the part responsible for regulating that function.","zh":"area that controls something 指負責調節某功能的部分。"},{"en":"The area that controls balance helps people stand and walk without falling.","zh":"控制平衡的區域幫助人站立和行走而不跌倒。"},{"en":"If a brain area controls a function, damage to it may affect that function.","zh":"如果某大腦區域控制某功能，該區域受損可能影響該功能。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining body systems in simple terms.","zh":"用簡單語言解釋身體系統時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"share properties","meaning":"具有共同特性","examples":[{"en":"Yawning and stretching share several physical properties.","zh":"打呵欠和伸展具有幾項共同身體特性。"},{"en":"To share properties means to have similar features or characteristics.","zh":"share properties 指擁有相似特徵或特性。"},{"en":"Running and cycling share properties because both raise the heart rate and use leg muscles.","zh":"跑步和踩單車具有共同特性，因為兩者都提高心率並使用腿部肌肉。"},{"en":"If yawning and stretching share properties, they may be related body actions.","zh":"如果打呵欠和伸展具有共同特性，它們可能是相關的身體動作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing features of two things.","zh":"比較兩件事的特徵時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be performed together","meaning":"一同進行","examples":[{"en":"Yawning and stretching may be performed together.","zh":"打呵欠和伸展可能一同進行。"},{"en":"Be performed together means be done at the same time or as part of the same action.","zh":"be performed together 指在同一時間或作為同一行動的一部分被做出。"},{"en":"Singing and clapping may be performed together during a school performance.","zh":"在學校表演中，唱歌和拍手可能一同進行。"},{"en":"People often yawn and stretch together when they wake up or feel sleepy.","zh":"人們醒來或感到困倦時，常會一邊打呵欠一邊伸展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when two actions happen as a pair.","zh":"當兩個動作成對發生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"global motor complex","meaning":"全身性運動複合動作","examples":[{"en":"The two movements may form part of a global motor complex.","zh":"這兩種動作可能構成全身性運動複合動作的一部分。"},{"en":"A global motor complex is a coordinated pattern involving movement across many parts of the body.","zh":"global motor complex 指涉及身體多個部分協調活動的動作模式。"},{"en":"A full-body stretch after waking can involve arms, back, face, and breathing together.","zh":"醒來後全身伸展可以同時涉及手臂、背部、面部和呼吸。"},{"en":"If yawning belongs to a motor complex, it is not just a mouth movement.","zh":"如果打呵欠屬於運動複合動作，它就不只是嘴部動作。"},{"en":"This phrase is technical and useful when describing whole-body movement patterns.","zh":"描述全身性動作模式時，這個短語較技術性但有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"co-occur","meaning":"同時出現","examples":[{"en":"Yawning and stretching do not always co-occur.","zh":"打呵欠和伸展並不總是同時出現。"},{"en":"Co-occur means happen at the same time.","zh":"co-occur 指在同一時間發生。"},{"en":"Headache and tiredness may co-occur when a student sleeps too little.","zh":"當學生睡眠不足時，頭痛和疲倦可能同時出現。"},{"en":"If two behaviours co-occur often, researchers may ask whether they are connected.","zh":"如果兩種行為經常同時出現，研究人員可能會問它們是否有關。"},{"en":"This word is useful when describing events that appear together.","zh":"描述一起出現的事件時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not always occur together","meaning":"並非總是同時發生","examples":[{"en":"Yawning and stretching do not always occur together.","zh":"打呵欠和伸展並非總是同時發生。"},{"en":"Not always occur together means two things sometimes happen separately.","zh":"not always occur together 指兩件事有時會分開發生。"},{"en":"Hunger and tiredness do not always occur together; a person can feel one without the other.","zh":"飢餓和疲倦並非總是同時發生；人可以只感到其中一種。"},{"en":"Yawning may happen without stretching, which suggests the two actions are related but not identical.","zh":"打呵欠可能在沒有伸展時發生，這暗示兩個動作相關但不完全相同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when separating two commonly linked events.","zh":"區分兩個常被連在一起的事件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"especially before bedtime","meaning":"尤其在睡前","examples":[{"en":"People may yawn without stretching, especially before bedtime.","zh":"人們可能會打呵欠而不伸展，尤其在睡前。"},{"en":"Especially before bedtime means particularly in the period before going to sleep.","zh":"especially before bedtime 指尤其是在準備睡覺前的一段時間。"},{"en":"Children may become quiet and slow, especially before bedtime.","zh":"孩子可能變得安靜和動作緩慢，尤其在睡前。"},{"en":"Yawning before sleep may reflect tiredness even when no stretching happens.","zh":"睡前打呵欠可能反映疲倦，即使沒有伸展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one situation is a clear example of a broader pattern.","zh":"當某一情況是更廣泛模式的清楚例子時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"chart movement","meaning":"記錄動作變化","examples":[{"en":"The researchers charted movement in the developing fetus.","zh":"研究人員記錄發育中胎兒的動作變化。"},{"en":"To chart movement means to record and track how movement changes over time.","zh":"chart movement 指記錄並追蹤動作如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"A physiotherapist may chart movement in a patient’s arm after injury.","zh":"物理治療師可能記錄病人受傷後手臂的動作變化。"},{"en":"Charting movement helps researchers see patterns that are not obvious from one observation.","zh":"記錄動作變化幫助研究人員看見單次觀察看不出的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when movement is carefully recorded.","zh":"當動作被仔細記錄時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"developing fetus","meaning":"發育中的胎兒","examples":[{"en":"The studies examined movement in the developing fetus.","zh":"研究檢視發育中胎兒的動作。"},{"en":"A developing fetus is an unborn baby growing inside the womb.","zh":"developing fetus 指在子宮內成長的未出生嬰兒。"},{"en":"Doctors monitor a developing fetus to check growth, movement, and health.","zh":"醫生監測發育中的胎兒，以檢查成長、活動和健康。"},{"en":"Studying fetal movement can show when certain behaviours begin before birth.","zh":"研究胎兒動作可以顯示某些行為在出生前何時開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in prenatal development and medical contexts.","zh":"這個短語適用於產前發育和醫學語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"using ultrasound","meaning":"使用超聲波","examples":[{"en":"The researchers observed fetal movements using ultrasound.","zh":"研究人員使用超聲波觀察胎兒動作。"},{"en":"Using ultrasound means using sound-wave imaging to see inside the body.","zh":"using ultrasound 指使用聲波成像來觀察身體內部。"},{"en":"Doctors often check a baby’s position using ultrasound during pregnancy.","zh":"醫生在懷孕期間常使用超聲波檢查嬰兒位置。"},{"en":"Ultrasound allows researchers to observe movement without directly touching the fetus.","zh":"超聲波讓研究人員無需直接接觸胎兒也能觀察動作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining a safe medical imaging method.","zh":"解釋安全醫學成像方法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"observe not just…but…","meaning":"觀察到的不只是……還有……","examples":[{"en":"The researchers observed not just yawning but also stretching.","zh":"研究人員觀察到的不只是打呵欠，還有伸展。"},{"en":"Observe not just A but B means notice or study both things, not only the first one.","zh":"observe not just A but B 指注意或研究兩件事，而不只是第一件。"},{"en":"A teacher should observe not just exam scores but also effort and confidence.","zh":"老師應觀察的不只是考試分數，還有努力和信心。"},{"en":"Looking at more than one behaviour can reveal connections between them.","zh":"觀察多於一種行為可以揭示它們之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"This structure is useful when expanding attention beyond one item.","zh":"把注意力由單一項目擴展出去時，這個結構很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a link between","meaning":"……之間的聯繫","examples":[{"en":"The study found a link between yawning and stretching.","zh":"研究發現打呵欠和伸展之間有聯繫。"},{"en":"A link between two things is a connection or relationship between them.","zh":"link between two things 指兩件事之間的連接或關係。"},{"en":"Researchers may find a link between poor sleep and weak concentration.","zh":"研究人員可能發現睡眠不足和專注力弱之間有聯繫。"},{"en":"A link does not always prove direct cause, but it suggests the two things are related.","zh":"聯繫不一定證明直接因果，但暗示兩者相關。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing relationships in research.","zh":"討論研究中的關係時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as early as","meaning":"早至……","examples":[{"en":"The connection was observed as early as the first prenatal trimester.","zh":"這種聯繫早至妊娠首三個月已被觀察到。"},{"en":"As early as means at an unexpectedly early time.","zh":"as early as 指在令人意外的早期時間。"},{"en":"Some children can recognise letters as early as age three.","zh":"有些孩子早至三歲已能認出字母。"},{"en":"Finding a behaviour as early as pregnancy suggests it begins before learning from society.","zh":"如果某行為早至懷孕期間已出現，就暗示它在從社會學習之前已開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing how early something appears.","zh":"強調某事出現得很早時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"first prenatal trimester","meaning":"妊娠首三個月","examples":[{"en":"Yawning and stretching were linked by the end of the first prenatal trimester.","zh":"到妊娠首三個月結束時，打呵欠和伸展已出現聯繫。"},{"en":"The first prenatal trimester is the first three-month period of pregnancy.","zh":"first prenatal trimester 指懷孕的首三個月。"},{"en":"Doctors often perform early checks during the first prenatal trimester.","zh":"醫生常在妊娠首三個月進行早期檢查。"},{"en":"If a behaviour appears in this period, it belongs to very early development.","zh":"如果某行為在這段時期出現，它就屬於非常早期的發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in medical and developmental contexts.","zh":"這個短語適用於醫學和發展語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"extraordinary demonstration","meaning":"非同尋常的證明","examples":[{"en":"Stroke patients provide an extraordinary demonstration of the connection.","zh":"中風患者提供了這種聯繫的非同尋常證明。"},{"en":"An extraordinary demonstration is an unusually clear or surprising example that shows something.","zh":"extraordinary demonstration 指非常清楚或令人驚訝地展示某事的例子。"},{"en":"A student who improves from failing to top of the class can be an extraordinary demonstration of practice.","zh":"學生由不合格進步到全班第一，可以是練習作用的非同尋常證明。"},{"en":"When paralysed arms move during yawning, the link between systems becomes striking.","zh":"當癱瘓手臂在打呵欠時移動，系統之間的聯繫就變得非常鮮明。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence is especially vivid or unexpected.","zh":"當證據特別生動或出乎意料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"yawn-stretch linkage","meaning":"打呵欠與伸展之間的聯繫","examples":[{"en":"The movement of paralysed patients reveals the yawn-stretch linkage.","zh":"癱瘓患者的動作揭示打呵欠與伸展之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"Yawn-stretch linkage means the connection between yawning and stretching movements.","zh":"yawn-stretch linkage 指打呵欠和伸展動作之間的連接。"},{"en":"A person may yawn and stretch together after waking up, showing this linkage in daily life.","zh":"一個人醒來後可能一邊打呵欠一邊伸展，顯示日常生活中的這種聯繫。"},{"en":"In stroke patients, the linkage may appear when yawning triggers movement in a paralysed arm.","zh":"在中風患者身上，當打呵欠觸發癱瘓手臂活動時，這種聯繫可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a connection between two body actions.","zh":"描述兩種身體動作之間的連接時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be paralysed on one side","meaning":"身體一側癱瘓","examples":[{"en":"Some stroke patients are paralysed on one side of the body.","zh":"有些中風患者身體一側癱瘓。"},{"en":"Be paralysed on one side means lose movement or control on the left or right side of the body.","zh":"be paralysed on one side 指身體左側或右側失去活動或控制能力。"},{"en":"After a serious stroke, a patient may be paralysed on one side and need rehabilitation.","zh":"嚴重中風後，病人可能身體一側癱瘓並需要復康。"},{"en":"One-sided paralysis can affect walking, dressing, eating, and daily independence.","zh":"單側癱瘓可以影響行走、穿衣、進食和日常自理能力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in medical descriptions of stroke effects.","zh":"在醫學上描述中風影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"because of brain damage","meaning":"因腦部受損","examples":[{"en":"The patients became paralysed because of brain damage.","zh":"患者因腦部受損而癱瘓。"},{"en":"Because of brain damage means as a result of injury to the brain.","zh":"because of brain damage 指由大腦受傷造成。"},{"en":"A person may have speech problems because of brain damage after an accident.","zh":"一個人在意外後可能因腦部受損而有說話問題。"},{"en":"Damage to one brain area can affect movement, memory, language, or emotion.","zh":"某個大腦區域受損可以影響活動、記憶、語言或情緒。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the medical cause of a problem.","zh":"解釋問題的醫學原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be caused by a stroke","meaning":"由中風引起","examples":[{"en":"The brain damage was caused by a stroke.","zh":"腦部受損由中風引起。"},{"en":"Be caused by a stroke means result from a sudden interruption of blood supply to the brain.","zh":"be caused by a stroke 指由腦部血液供應突然中斷而造成。"},{"en":"Weakness in one arm may be caused by a stroke and needs urgent medical attention.","zh":"一隻手臂無力可能由中風引起，需要緊急醫療處理。"},{"en":"A stroke can damage brain tissue and affect body movement.","zh":"中風可以損害腦組織並影響身體活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the source of neurological injury.","zh":"解釋神經損傷來源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"prominent neurologist","meaning":"著名神經科醫生","examples":[{"en":"Sir Francis Walshe was a prominent British neurologist.","zh":"Sir Francis Walshe 是著名英國神經科醫生。"},{"en":"A prominent neurologist is a well-known doctor or scientist who studies the nervous system.","zh":"prominent neurologist 指研究神經系統並廣為人知的醫生或科學家。"},{"en":"A prominent neurologist may be invited to speak at hospitals and universities.","zh":"著名神經科醫生可能受邀到醫院和大學演講。"},{"en":"Mentioning a prominent expert makes the observation sound more credible.","zh":"提到著名專家會令觀察結果聽起來更可信。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying an important medical specialist.","zh":"指出重要醫學專家時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hemiplegics","meaning":"偏癱患者","examples":[{"en":"Hemiplegics have paralysis affecting one side of the body.","zh":"偏癱患者身體一側受到癱瘓影響。"},{"en":"Hemiplegics are people who have paralysis on one side of the body.","zh":"hemiplegics 指身體一側癱瘓的人。"},{"en":"A hemiplegic patient may need therapy to practise walking, balance, and arm movement.","zh":"偏癱患者可能需要治療來練習行走、平衡和手臂活動。"},{"en":"Studying hemiplegics can show how brain damage affects movement systems.","zh":"研究偏癱患者可以顯示腦部受損如何影響運動系統。"},{"en":"This word is medical and should be used carefully and respectfully.","zh":"這個詞屬醫學用語，使用時應小心和尊重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be startled and mystified","meaning":"感到驚訝和困惑","examples":[{"en":"The patients were startled and mystified by the movement of their arms.","zh":"患者對自己手臂的動作感到驚訝和困惑。"},{"en":"Be startled and mystified means be surprised and confused because something unexpected happens.","zh":"be startled and mystified 指因意外事情發生而感到驚訝和困惑。"},{"en":"A child may be startled and mystified when a broken toy suddenly starts working again.","zh":"當壞掉的玩具突然又能運作，孩子可能感到驚訝和困惑。"},{"en":"Paralysed patients may feel confused if an arm they cannot control moves during a yawn.","zh":"如果癱瘓患者無法控制的手臂在打呵欠時移動，他可能感到困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an event is both shocking and hard to explain.","zh":"當事件既令人震驚又難以解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"otherwise paralysed arm","meaning":"平時癱瘓的手臂","examples":[{"en":"The patients’ otherwise paralysed arms moved when they yawned.","zh":"患者平時癱瘓的手臂在他們打呵欠時移動。"},{"en":"An otherwise paralysed arm is an arm that is normally paralysed except in this special situation.","zh":"otherwise paralysed arm 指除了這個特殊情況外，通常都是癱瘓的手臂。"},{"en":"A normally silent phone that rings during one emergency could be called otherwise silent.","zh":"平時無聲的電話在一次緊急情況中響起，可說是 otherwise silent。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the surprise that an arm usually unable to move suddenly moves.","zh":"這個短語突出令人驚訝之處：一隻通常不能動的手臂突然移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an exception appears in an otherwise fixed condition.","zh":"當固定狀態中出現例外時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rise and flex automatically","meaning":"自動抬起和屈曲","examples":[{"en":"The paralysed arm may rise and flex automatically during a yawn.","zh":"癱瘓手臂可能在打呵欠期間自動抬起和屈曲。"},{"en":"To rise and flex automatically means to lift and bend without conscious control.","zh":"rise and flex automatically 指不受意識控制地抬起和彎曲。"},{"en":"A person’s knee may jerk automatically when a doctor taps it with a reflex hammer.","zh":"醫生用反射槌敲膝蓋時，人的膝蓋可能自動彈起。"},{"en":"Automatic movement suggests that unconscious neural pathways may still be active.","zh":"自動動作暗示不受意識控制的神經路徑可能仍然活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing involuntary movement.","zh":"描述非自願動作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"what neurologists term","meaning":"神經科醫生稱為……的現象","examples":[{"en":"The movement is what neurologists term an “associated response”.","zh":"這種動作是神經科醫生稱為「聯合反應」的現象。"},{"en":"What neurologists term means what brain and nerve specialists call something.","zh":"what neurologists term 指腦和神經專家如何稱呼某事。"},{"en":"What doctors term inflammation may appear as redness, swelling, heat, and pain.","zh":"醫生稱為 inflammation 的現象，可能表現為紅、腫、熱和痛。"},{"en":"Using the specialist term helps connect the observation to medical knowledge.","zh":"使用專業術語有助把觀察與醫學知識連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing a technical name.","zh":"引入技術名稱時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"associated response","meaning":"聯合反應","examples":[{"en":"An associated response is an involuntary movement linked to another action.","zh":"聯合反應是與另一個動作相連的非自願動作。"},{"en":"An associated response is a movement that appears automatically together with another behaviour.","zh":"associated response 指與另一行為一起自動出現的動作。"},{"en":"A person’s hand may twitch when they sneeze, if the movement is linked involuntarily.","zh":"如果某人的手在打噴嚏時不自主抽動，而這動作與噴嚏相連，就可視為類似反應。"},{"en":"In stroke patients, yawning may trigger movement in a limb that is usually paralysed.","zh":"在中風患者身上，打呵欠可能觸發平時癱瘓的肢體活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one action unexpectedly activates another movement.","zh":"當一個動作意外啟動另一個動作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"apparently activate","meaning":"看來會啟動……","examples":[{"en":"Yawning apparently activates undamaged neural connections.","zh":"打呵欠看來會啟動未受損的神經連接。"},{"en":"Apparently activate means seem to switch on or stimulate something, based on available evidence.","zh":"apparently activate 指根據現有證據看來會開啟或刺激某物。"},{"en":"A familiar song may apparently activate memories from childhood.","zh":"熟悉歌曲看來會啟動童年記憶。"},{"en":"The word apparently shows the writer is cautious rather than completely certain.","zh":"apparently 這個詞顯示作者態度謹慎，而不是完全肯定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence suggests activation but does not prove everything.","zh":"當證據暗示啟動但未能證明一切時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"undamaged connections","meaning":"未受損的連接","examples":[{"en":"The response may depend on undamaged connections in the nervous system.","zh":"這種反應可能依賴神經系統中未受損的連接。"},{"en":"Undamaged connections are nerve pathways or links that have not been harmed.","zh":"undamaged connections 指沒有受傷害的神經路徑或連結。"},{"en":"After an injury, doctors may test whether undamaged connections still allow movement or feeling.","zh":"受傷後，醫生可能測試未受損連接是否仍能容許活動或感覺。"},{"en":"If some connections remain undamaged, the body may still produce certain automatic actions.","zh":"如果某些連接仍未受損，身體可能仍能產生某些自動動作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing what remains functional after injury.","zh":"討論受傷後仍可運作的部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"unconsciously controlled","meaning":"不受意識控制的","examples":[{"en":"The relevant neural connections are unconsciously controlled.","zh":"相關神經連接是不受意識控制的。"},{"en":"Unconsciously controlled means controlled without deliberate thought or awareness.","zh":"unconsciously controlled 指不經刻意思考或意識而被控制。"},{"en":"Breathing is often unconsciously controlled, although people can also control it briefly.","zh":"呼吸通常是不受意識控制的，雖然人也可以短暫控制它。"},{"en":"If a movement is unconsciously controlled, it may happen even when a person does not intend it.","zh":"如果某動作不受意識控制，它可能在人沒有意圖時發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing automatic body processes.","zh":"描述自動身體過程時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"connections between the brain and","meaning":"大腦與……之間的連接","examples":[{"en":"Yawning activates connections between the brain and the spinal motor system.","zh":"打呵欠啟動大腦與脊髓運動系統之間的連接。"},{"en":"Connections between the brain and something are pathways that allow signals to pass between them.","zh":"connections between the brain and something 指讓訊號在大腦和某部分之間傳遞的路徑。"},{"en":"Connections between the brain and muscles help a person move their hands and legs.","zh":"大腦與肌肉之間的連接幫助人移動手腳。"},{"en":"If these pathways are damaged, movement may become weak or impossible.","zh":"如果這些路徑受損，活動可能變弱或變得不可能。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how the nervous system sends signals.","zh":"解釋神經系統如何傳送訊號時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cord motor system","meaning":"脊髓運動系統","examples":[{"en":"The cord motor system helps control movement in the limbs.","zh":"脊髓運動系統幫助控制肢體活動。"},{"en":"The cord motor system refers to motor pathways in the spinal cord that help control movement.","zh":"cord motor system 指脊髓中幫助控制活動的運動路徑。"},{"en":"Doctors may test spinal motor function by checking reflexes in the legs.","zh":"醫生可能透過檢查腿部反射來測試脊髓運動功能。"},{"en":"If the system is activated, muscles may move even without conscious intention.","zh":"如果該系統被啟動，肌肉可能在沒有意識意圖下移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in medical discussions of movement control.","zh":"在關於活動控制的醫學討論中，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"innervate a limb","meaning":"為肢體提供神經支配","examples":[{"en":"The motor system innervates the paralysed limb.","zh":"運動系統為癱瘓肢體提供神經支配。"},{"en":"To innervate a limb means to supply nerves to that arm or leg so it can receive signals.","zh":"innervate a limb 指向手臂或腿提供神經，使其能接收訊號。"},{"en":"Nerves innervate the fingers, allowing them to feel and move.","zh":"神經支配手指，使它們能感覺和活動。"},{"en":"If a limb is not properly innervated, movement and sensation may be affected.","zh":"如果肢體沒有得到正常神經支配，活動和感覺可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is technical and useful in anatomy and neurology.","zh":"這個短語較技術性，適用於解剖學和神經學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"paralysed limb","meaning":"癱瘓肢體","examples":[{"en":"The associated response causes movement in a paralysed limb.","zh":"聯合反應導致癱瘓肢體出現動作。"},{"en":"A paralysed limb is an arm or leg that has lost normal movement control.","zh":"paralysed limb 指失去正常活動控制的手臂或腿。"},{"en":"After a stroke, a patient may need therapy for a paralysed limb.","zh":"中風後，病人可能需要為癱瘓肢體接受治療。"},{"en":"Unexpected movement in a paralysed limb can give doctors clues about remaining nerve pathways.","zh":"癱瘓肢體的意外動作可以給醫生關於剩餘神經路徑的線索。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in medical descriptions of paralysis.","zh":"在醫學上描述癱瘓時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"it is not known whether","meaning":"尚未知道是否……","examples":[{"en":"It is not known whether this response predicts recovery.","zh":"尚未知道這種反應是否能預測康復。"},{"en":"It is not known whether means researchers do not yet know if something is true.","zh":"it is not known whether 指研究人員尚未知道某事是否真實。"},{"en":"It is not known whether a new school policy will improve exam results until data are collected.","zh":"在收集數據之前，尚未知道新學校政策是否會改善考試成績。"},{"en":"This phrase shows uncertainty and avoids claiming more than the evidence supports.","zh":"這個短語顯示不確定性，避免作出超出證據的聲稱。"},{"en":"It is useful in cautious scientific writing.","zh":"它適用於謹慎的科學寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"positive prognosis for recovery","meaning":"康復的正面預後指標","examples":[{"en":"Researchers do not know whether the response is a positive prognosis for recovery.","zh":"研究人員不知道這種反應是否是康復的正面預後指標。"},{"en":"A positive prognosis for recovery is a sign that a patient is likely to improve.","zh":"positive prognosis for recovery 指顯示病人很可能改善的跡象。"},{"en":"A doctor may see improved speech after a stroke as a positive prognosis for recovery.","zh":"醫生可能把中風後說話能力改善視為康復的正面預後指標。"},{"en":"If yawning-related movement predicted recovery, it would be medically important.","zh":"如果與打呵欠相關的動作能預測康復，它就有醫學重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in clinical discussions of future health outcomes.","zh":"在臨床討論未來健康結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be therapeutic for","meaning":"對……有治療作用","examples":[{"en":"It is unclear whether yawning is therapeutic for nerve recovery.","zh":"尚不清楚打呵欠是否對神經康復有治療作用。"},{"en":"Be therapeutic for something means help treat, improve, or support healing in that area.","zh":"be therapeutic for something 指有助治療、改善或支持某方面康復。"},{"en":"Gentle exercise can be therapeutic for some back problems if guided by a professional.","zh":"在專業人士指導下，溫和運動可能對某些背部問題有治療作用。"},{"en":"If yawning were therapeutic for nerves, it might help recovery rather than simply accompany it.","zh":"如果打呵欠對神經有治療作用，它可能幫助康復，而不只是伴隨康復出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing possible treatment effects.","zh":"討論可能的治療效果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reinnervation","meaning":"神經再支配","examples":[{"en":"Scientists do not know whether yawning encourages reinnervation.","zh":"科學家不知道打呵欠是否促進神經再支配。"},{"en":"Reinnervation is the process of nerves reconnecting with muscles or body parts after damage.","zh":"reinnervation 指神經在受損後重新與肌肉或身體部位連接的過程。"},{"en":"After a nerve injury, doctors may look for signs of reinnervation in weak muscles.","zh":"神經受傷後，醫生可能在無力肌肉中尋找神經再支配的跡象。"},{"en":"Reinnervation could help restore movement if new nerve connections become functional.","zh":"如果新神經連接變得可運作，神經再支配可能幫助恢復活動。"},{"en":"This word is technical and useful in neurology and rehabilitation.","zh":"這個詞較技術性，適用於神經學和復康。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"prevention of muscular atrophy","meaning":"預防肌肉萎縮","examples":[{"en":"Yawning may or may not help with the prevention of muscular atrophy.","zh":"打呵欠可能有助或無助於預防肌肉萎縮。"},{"en":"Prevention of muscular atrophy means stopping muscles from wasting or shrinking because they are not used.","zh":"prevention of muscular atrophy 指阻止肌肉因缺乏使用而消耗或縮小。"},{"en":"Physiotherapy can help with the prevention of muscular atrophy after a long hospital stay.","zh":"長期住院後，物理治療可以幫助預防肌肉萎縮。"},{"en":"If a paralysed limb moves occasionally, it might reduce muscle wasting, but this is uncertain here.","zh":"如果癱瘓肢體偶爾活動，可能減少肌肉消耗，但這裏仍不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in rehabilitation and medical contexts.","zh":"這個短語適用於復康和醫學語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"clinical neurology","meaning":"臨床神經學","examples":[{"en":"Clinical neurology provides other surprising examples of yawning.","zh":"臨床神經學提供其他關於打呵欠的驚人例子。"},{"en":"Clinical neurology is the medical study and treatment of disorders of the brain, nerves, and spinal cord.","zh":"clinical neurology 指對大腦、神經和脊髓疾病的醫學研究和治療。"},{"en":"A clinical neurologist may treat patients with stroke, epilepsy, or movement disorders.","zh":"臨床神經科醫生可能治療中風、癲癇或運動障礙患者。"},{"en":"Clinical cases can reveal body functions that laboratory studies alone may miss.","zh":"臨床個案可以揭示單靠實驗室研究可能錯過的身體功能。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when medical practice gives scientific insight.","zh":"當醫療實踐提供科學見解時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"offer other surprises","meaning":"帶來其他令人驚訝的發現","examples":[{"en":"Clinical neurology offers other surprises concerning voluntary movement.","zh":"臨床神經學在自主活動方面帶來其他令人驚訝的發現。"},{"en":"To offer other surprises means to provide additional unexpected examples or discoveries.","zh":"offer other surprises 指提供額外意想不到的例子或發現。"},{"en":"A history lesson may offer other surprises when students learn that old inventions were very advanced.","zh":"當學生知道舊發明其實很先進，歷史課可能帶來其他驚喜。"},{"en":"Neurology can surprise researchers because damaged brains sometimes preserve unexpected abilities.","zh":"神經學會令研究人員驚訝，因為受損大腦有時保留意想不到的能力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a topic produces more unexpected findings.","zh":"當一個主題產生更多意外發現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"locked-in syndrome","meaning":"閉鎖症候群","examples":[{"en":"Some patients with locked-in syndrome can still yawn normally.","zh":"有些閉鎖症候群患者仍能正常打呵欠。"},{"en":"Locked-in syndrome is a condition in which a person is conscious but almost unable to move voluntarily.","zh":"locked-in syndrome 指一個人有意識，但幾乎無法自主活動的狀況。"},{"en":"A patient with locked-in syndrome may communicate only through eye movements.","zh":"閉鎖症候群患者可能只能透過眼球動作溝通。"},{"en":"If such patients can yawn, yawning must depend on brain systems different from ordinary voluntary movement.","zh":"如果這類患者能打呵欠，打呵欠必然依賴不同於一般自主活動的大腦系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in serious neurological discussion.","zh":"這個短語適用於嚴肅神經學討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be almost totally deprived of","meaning":"幾乎完全失去……","examples":[{"en":"These patients are almost totally deprived of voluntary movement.","zh":"這些患者幾乎完全失去自主活動能力。"},{"en":"Be almost totally deprived of something means have nearly none of it.","zh":"be almost totally deprived of something 指幾乎完全沒有某物。"},{"en":"A remote village may be almost totally deprived of public transport if no buses or trains run there.","zh":"如果沒有巴士或火車，偏遠村莊可能幾乎完全失去公共交通。"},{"en":"Patients with almost no voluntary movement may still keep some automatic body functions.","zh":"幾乎沒有自主活動能力的患者，仍可能保留某些自動身體功能。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing extreme lack.","zh":"描述極度缺乏時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ability to move voluntarily","meaning":"自主活動能力","examples":[{"en":"Locked-in patients have very little ability to move voluntarily.","zh":"閉鎖症候群患者的自主活動能力非常有限。"},{"en":"Ability to move voluntarily means the capacity to move the body by conscious choice.","zh":"ability to move voluntarily 指按意識選擇移動身體的能力。"},{"en":"A healthy person uses voluntary movement when they decide to lift a cup.","zh":"健康人士決定拿起杯子時，就是使用自主活動能力。"},{"en":"Losing voluntary movement does not always mean losing all automatic movements.","zh":"失去自主活動不一定代表失去所有自動動作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when distinguishing chosen action from reflexive action.","zh":"區分有意識行動和反射行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"yawn normally","meaning":"正常打呵欠","examples":[{"en":"Some severely paralysed patients can still yawn normally.","zh":"有些嚴重癱瘓患者仍能正常打呵欠。"},{"en":"To yawn normally means to perform an ordinary yawn despite other physical problems.","zh":"yawn normally 指即使有其他身體問題，仍能作出普通呵欠。"},{"en":"A patient may be unable to speak clearly but still breathe and yawn normally.","zh":"病人可能無法清楚說話，但仍能正常呼吸和打呵欠。"},{"en":"Normal yawning in paralysed patients suggests yawning uses deep automatic circuits.","zh":"癱瘓患者能正常打呵欠，暗示打呵欠使用深層自動迴路。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a basic function remains intact.","zh":"當基本功能仍然完整時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"neural circuits","meaning":"神經迴路","examples":[{"en":"Neural circuits for spontaneous yawning are located deep in the brain.","zh":"自發性打呵欠的神經迴路位於大腦深處。"},{"en":"Neural circuits are networks of nerve cells that send signals and control functions.","zh":"neural circuits 指傳送訊號並控制功能的神經細胞網絡。"},{"en":"Neural circuits help the brain control movement, memory, emotion, and breathing.","zh":"神經迴路幫助大腦控制活動、記憶、情緒和呼吸。"},{"en":"If yawning depends on deep neural circuits, it may continue even when voluntary movement is lost.","zh":"如果打呵欠依賴深層神經迴路，即使自主活動喪失，它仍可能繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in neuroscience.","zh":"這個短語適用於神經科學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"spontaneous yawning","meaning":"自發性打呵欠","examples":[{"en":"Spontaneous yawning may be controlled by the brain stem.","zh":"自發性打呵欠可能由腦幹控制。"},{"en":"Spontaneous yawning is yawning that happens naturally without being triggered by seeing someone else yawn.","zh":"spontaneous yawning 指自然發生，而不是由看見別人打呵欠觸發的打呵欠。"},{"en":"A person may experience spontaneous yawning when tired, bored, or waking up.","zh":"一個人疲倦、沉悶或剛醒來時，可能出現自發性打呵欠。"},{"en":"Because it is automatic, spontaneous yawning may be controlled by older brain systems.","zh":"因為它是自動的，自發性打呵欠可能由較古老的大腦系統控制。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting natural yawning with contagious yawning.","zh":"對比自然打呵欠和傳染性打呵欠時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"brain stem","meaning":"腦幹","examples":[{"en":"The neural circuits for yawning may exist in the brain stem.","zh":"打呵欠的神經迴路可能存在於腦幹中。"},{"en":"The brain stem is the lower part of the brain that controls many basic life functions.","zh":"brain stem 指大腦較低部分，控制許多基本生命功能。"},{"en":"The brain stem helps regulate breathing, heartbeat, and alertness.","zh":"腦幹幫助調節呼吸、心跳和警覺。"},{"en":"If yawning circuits are in the brain stem, yawning may remain even in severe brain conditions.","zh":"如果打呵欠迴路在腦幹中，即使在嚴重腦部狀況下，打呵欠仍可能保留。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in neuroscience and medical contexts.","zh":"這個短語適用於神經科學和醫學語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"respiratory centres","meaning":"呼吸中樞","examples":[{"en":"The brain stem contains important respiratory centres.","zh":"腦幹包含重要呼吸中樞。"},{"en":"Respiratory centres are brain areas that help control breathing.","zh":"respiratory centres 指幫助控制呼吸的大腦區域。"},{"en":"Doctors monitor breathing carefully when respiratory centres may be affected by injury.","zh":"當呼吸中樞可能受傷害影響時，醫生會仔細監測呼吸。"},{"en":"Because yawning involves breathing, respiratory centres may be relevant to its control.","zh":"因為打呵欠涉及呼吸，呼吸中樞可能與其控制有關。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in physiology and neurology.","zh":"這個短語適用於生理學和神經學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"vasomotor centres","meaning":"血管運動中樞","examples":[{"en":"Vasomotor centres help regulate the diameter of blood vessels.","zh":"血管運動中樞幫助調節血管直徑。"},{"en":"Vasomotor centres are brain regions that control widening and narrowing of blood vessels.","zh":"vasomotor centres 指控制血管擴張和收縮的大腦區域。"},{"en":"Blood vessels may narrow when the body needs to maintain blood pressure.","zh":"當身體需要維持血壓時，血管可能收縮。"},{"en":"These centres are important because blood flow affects many body functions.","zh":"這些中樞很重要，因為血流影響許多身體功能。"},{"en":"This phrase is technical and useful in physiology.","zh":"這個短語較技術性，適用於生理學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"anencephalic individuals","meaning":"無腦畸形人士","examples":[{"en":"Anencephalic individuals may still be able to yawn.","zh":"無腦畸形人士可能仍然能夠打呵欠。"},{"en":"Anencephalic individuals are people born without major parts of the brain and skull.","zh":"anencephalic individuals 指出生時缺少大腦和頭骨主要部分的人。"},{"en":"Doctors study rare cases of anencephalic individuals to understand which basic functions remain.","zh":"醫生研究無腦畸形人士的罕見個案，以理解哪些基本功能仍然保留。"},{"en":"If such individuals can yawn, yawning may depend on very basic brain structures.","zh":"如果這類人士能打呵欠，打呵欠可能依賴非常基本的大腦結構。"},{"en":"This phrase is medical and should be used with care and respect.","zh":"這個短語屬醫學用語，應小心和尊重地使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"possess only","meaning":"只具有……","examples":[{"en":"Some individuals possess only the most basic parts of the brain.","zh":"有些人只具有大腦最基本的部分。"},{"en":"Possess only means have nothing except the thing mentioned.","zh":"possess only 指除了所提到的東西外沒有其他東西。"},{"en":"A small village school may possess only a few computers for all students.","zh":"小型鄉村學校可能只具有幾部供所有學生使用的電腦。"},{"en":"If a person possesses only basic brain structures but can yawn, yawning may be controlled very deeply.","zh":"如果一個人只具有基本大腦結構但能打呵欠，打呵欠可能由很深層位置控制。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when emphasising extreme limitation.","zh":"強調極大限制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"medulla oblongata","meaning":"延髓","examples":[{"en":"The medulla oblongata controls several essential bodily functions.","zh":"延髓控制幾項重要身體功能。"},{"en":"The medulla oblongata is a lower brain-stem structure involved in vital functions such as breathing and heart rate.","zh":"medulla oblongata 指腦幹較低部位，參與呼吸和心率等重要功能。"},{"en":"Medical students learn about the medulla oblongata when studying basic survival functions.","zh":"醫科學生學習基本生存功能時會學到延髓。"},{"en":"Its role in automatic control helps explain why some basic actions can continue without conscious movement.","zh":"它在自動控制中的角色有助解釋為何某些基本動作可以在沒有自主活動下繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase is technical and useful in neuroscience.","zh":"這個短語較技術性，適用於神經科學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"multiplicity of stimuli","meaning":"多種不同刺激","examples":[{"en":"Contagious yawning can be triggered by a multiplicity of stimuli.","zh":"傳染性打呵欠可以由多種不同刺激觸發。"},{"en":"A multiplicity of stimuli means many different triggers or signals.","zh":"multiplicity of stimuli 指許多不同觸發因素或訊號。"},{"en":"A dog may react to a multiplicity of stimuli, such as sounds, smells, and movement.","zh":"狗可能對多種不同刺激有反應，例如聲音、氣味和動作。"},{"en":"If yawning can be triggered by many stimuli, it may involve several brain systems.","zh":"如果打呵欠可以由許多刺激觸發，它可能涉及多個大腦系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when more than one kind of trigger is involved.","zh":"當涉及多於一種觸發因素時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"by contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"Spontaneous yawning is controlled by lower regions; by contrast, contagious yawning is more complex.","zh":"自發性打呵欠由較低層區域控制；相比之下，傳染性打呵欠更複雜。"},{"en":"By contrast means used to show a clear difference from what was just mentioned.","zh":"by contrast 指用來顯示與剛提到內容的清楚差異。"},{"en":"Some students enjoy silent reading; by contrast, others learn better through discussion.","zh":"有些學生喜歡靜默閱讀；相比之下，另一些學生透過討論學得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers compare two different types of yawning.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者比較兩種不同類型的打呵欠。"},{"en":"It is useful when moving from one idea to an opposite or different idea.","zh":"從一個想法轉到相反或不同想法時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"implicate higher brain regions","meaning":"顯示較高層大腦區域參與其中","examples":[{"en":"Contagious yawning appears to implicate several higher brain regions.","zh":"傳染性打呵欠看來顯示幾個較高層大腦區域參與其中。"},{"en":"To implicate higher brain regions means to suggest that more advanced parts of the brain are involved.","zh":"implicate higher brain regions 指暗示較高階的大腦部分有參與。"},{"en":"A memory task may implicate higher brain regions because it requires attention and meaning.","zh":"記憶任務可能涉及較高層大腦區域，因為它需要注意和理解意義。"},{"en":"If contagious yawning involves empathy, it may need social and cognitive brain systems.","zh":"如果傳染性打呵欠涉及同理心，它可能需要社交和認知大腦系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when brain activity suggests involvement of complex processing areas.","zh":"當大腦活動暗示複雜處理區域參與時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"complete the summary paragraph","meaning":"完成摘要段落","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary paragraph using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的詞語完成摘要段落。"},{"en":"Complete the summary paragraph means fill in missing words in a short paragraph that summarises part of the text.","zh":"complete the summary paragraph 指填寫概括文本部分內容的短段落中的缺漏詞語。"},{"en":"Students should complete the summary paragraph by matching ideas, not by guessing from memory.","zh":"學生應透過配對意思完成摘要段落，而不是憑記憶猜測。"},{"en":"This task checks whether readers understand both meaning and exact wording.","zh":"這項任務檢查讀者是否理解意思和準確用詞。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不超過三個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than three words.","zh":"每個答案應包含不超過三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must use one, two, or three words only.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案只能使用一個、兩個或三個英文詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “posterior cingulate,” it follows the rule because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 posterior cingulate，它符合規則，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing too many words can lose marks even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫太多詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in completion questions.","zh":"這個短語在填空題中很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"an average yawn","meaning":"一般一次呵欠","examples":[{"en":"An average yawn takes approximately six seconds.","zh":"一般一次呵欠大約需時六秒。"},{"en":"An average yawn means a typical or usual yawn, not an unusually short or long one.","zh":"average yawn 指典型或普通的呵欠，而不是異常短或長的呵欠。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to time an average yawn during a simple science activity.","zh":"老師可能在簡單科學活動中要求學生量度一般一次呵欠的時間。"},{"en":"Knowing the average length helps researchers compare normal and unusual yawning.","zh":"知道平均長度有助研究人員比較正常和異常打呵欠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a typical example.","zh":"描述典型例子時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"occur with an interval","meaning":"相隔一段時間出現","examples":[{"en":"Yawns occur with an interval before the next one.","zh":"呵欠會相隔一段時間才出現下一次。"},{"en":"Occur with an interval means happen with a period of time between one event and the next.","zh":"occur with an interval 指兩次事件之間隔着一段時間發生。"},{"en":"Buses occur with an interval of ten minutes during busy hours.","zh":"繁忙時段，巴士每隔十分鐘一班。"},{"en":"If yawns appear at regular intervals, researchers can describe a pattern.","zh":"如果呵欠以固定間隔出現，研究人員就能描述一個模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when repeated events are separated by time.","zh":"當重複事件之間有時間分隔時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"accompanying behaviour","meaning":"伴隨行為","examples":[{"en":"The accompanying behaviour may differ between men and women.","zh":"伴隨行為可能在男女之間有所不同。"},{"en":"Accompanying behaviour is an extra action that happens together with the main behaviour.","zh":"accompanying behaviour 指與主要行為一起發生的額外行動。"},{"en":"Smiling may be an accompanying behaviour when someone greets a friend.","zh":"當某人向朋友打招呼時，微笑可能是伴隨行為。"},{"en":"Covering the mouth can accompany yawning and may reflect manners or habit.","zh":"掩嘴可以伴隨打呵欠，並可能反映禮貌或習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one behaviour comes with another.","zh":"當一種行為伴隨另一種行為出現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"show a distinction","meaning":"顯示差異","examples":[{"en":"Mouth-covering behaviour shows a distinction between the genders.","zh":"掩嘴行為顯示男女之間有差異。"},{"en":"To show a distinction means to reveal a difference between two things or groups.","zh":"show a distinction 指揭示兩件事或兩個群體之間的差異。"},{"en":"Exam results may show a distinction between students who revised daily and those who revised late.","zh":"考試成績可能顯示每天溫習和臨急溫習的學生之間有差異。"},{"en":"If men and women behave differently when yawning, the behaviour may show a social distinction.","zh":"如果男女打呵欠時行為不同，該行為可能顯示社交差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence points to a difference.","zh":"當證據指出差異時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be associated with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The hypothalamus is also associated with breathing.","zh":"下丘腦也與呼吸有關。"},{"en":"Be associated with means be connected to or linked with something.","zh":"be associated with 指與某事有連繫或關聯。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is often associated with low concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足常與課堂專注力低有關。"},{"en":"If a brain area is associated with breathing, it may also be relevant to yawning.","zh":"如果某大腦區域與呼吸有關，它也可能與打呵欠相關。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when two things are related but not necessarily one direct cause.","zh":"當兩件事有關但不一定是直接因果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"before birth","meaning":"出生前","examples":[{"en":"A link between yawning and stretching appears before birth.","zh":"打呵欠和伸展之間的聯繫在出生前已出現。"},{"en":"Before birth means before a baby is born.","zh":"before birth 指嬰兒出生之前。"},{"en":"Doctors can observe some baby movements before birth using scans.","zh":"醫生可以使用掃描在出生前觀察某些嬰兒動作。"},{"en":"If a behaviour appears before birth, it may be part of early biological development.","zh":"如果某行為在出生前出現，它可能屬於早期生物發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing prenatal behaviour.","zh":"討論產前行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"work together automatically","meaning":"自動協同運作","examples":[{"en":"The two movements can work together automatically after brain damage.","zh":"大腦受損後，這兩種動作可以自動協同運作。"},{"en":"To work together automatically means to operate as a linked action without conscious control.","zh":"work together automatically 指在沒有意識控制下作為相連動作運作。"},{"en":"Breathing and swallowing normally work together automatically when people drink.","zh":"人喝水時，呼吸和吞嚥通常會自動協同運作。"},{"en":"After brain damage, some automatic movement links may remain even when voluntary control is weak.","zh":"大腦受損後，即使自主控制變弱，某些自動動作連結仍可能保留。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing unconscious coordination.","zh":"描述不受意識控制的協調時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"brain is damaged","meaning":"大腦受損","examples":[{"en":"Unexpected movement may occur when part of the brain is damaged.","zh":"當大腦部分受損時，可能出現意外動作。"},{"en":"When the brain is damaged means when injury or disease harms brain tissue or function.","zh":"brain is damaged 指受傷或疾病損害腦組織或腦功能。"},{"en":"Speech, memory, or movement can change when the brain is damaged.","zh":"當大腦受損，說話、記憶或活動能力可能改變。"},{"en":"Brain damage can reveal which parts of the brain normally control certain behaviours.","zh":"腦部受損可以揭示大腦哪些部分通常控制某些行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in medical explanations of unusual symptoms.","zh":"在醫學上解釋異常症狀時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"which paragraph contains","meaning":"哪一段包含……","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which paragraph contains each piece of information.","zh":"學生找出哪一段包含每項資料。"},{"en":"Which paragraph contains asks students to find where a detail appears in the passage.","zh":"which paragraph contains 要求學生找出某細節在文章哪裏出現。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students scan the text to decide which paragraph contains a specific fact.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生掃讀文本，以判斷哪一段包含特定事實。"},{"en":"The answer may use different words from the question, so meaning matters more than exact repetition.","zh":"答案可能使用與題目不同的字眼，所以意思比完全重複字詞更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in information-location reading tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於資料定位閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rate of yawning","meaning":"打呵欠的頻率","examples":[{"en":"The rate of yawning shows a regular pattern.","zh":"打呵欠的頻率顯示一種規律模式。"},{"en":"Rate of yawning means how often yawning happens in a period of time.","zh":"rate of yawning 指在一段時間內打呵欠發生的頻密程度。"},{"en":"A researcher may record the rate of yawning during a long lecture.","zh":"研究人員可能記錄長講座期間打呵欠的頻率。"},{"en":"If the rate increases when people are tired, yawning may be linked to body state.","zh":"如果人在疲倦時頻率增加，打呵欠可能與身體狀態有關。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when yawning is measured scientifically.","zh":"當打呵欠被科學量度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"regular pattern","meaning":"規律模式","examples":[{"en":"Yawns sometimes occur according to a regular pattern.","zh":"呵欠有時按照規律模式出現。"},{"en":"A regular pattern is an arrangement or sequence that repeats in a predictable way.","zh":"regular pattern 指以可預測方式重複的安排或次序。"},{"en":"A bus timetable has a regular pattern if buses arrive every ten minutes.","zh":"如果巴士每十分鐘到站，巴士時間表就有規律模式。"},{"en":"If yawns follow a regular pattern, researchers can measure and compare them more easily.","zh":"如果呵欠跟隨規律模式，研究人員就能更容易量度和比較它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when repeated events are organised rather than random.","zh":"當重複事件有組織而非隨機時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"inherent ability","meaning":"與生俱來的能力","examples":[{"en":"Yawning is an inherent ability present before birth.","zh":"打呵欠是在出生前已存在的與生俱來能力。"},{"en":"An inherent ability is a natural capacity that exists without being taught.","zh":"inherent ability 指不需要被教授而自然存在的能力。"},{"en":"A baby’s ability to cry is an inherent ability rather than a learned classroom skill.","zh":"嬰兒哭泣的能力是與生俱來的，而不是課堂學來的技能。"},{"en":"If yawning appears before birth, it may be an inborn biological behaviour.","zh":"如果打呵欠在出生前已出現，它可能是天生生物行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a skill or action seems natural from the beginning.","zh":"當一種技能或行動似乎一開始就自然存在時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"appear in both animals and humans","meaning":"同時出現在動物和人類身上","examples":[{"en":"Yawning appears in both animals and humans.","zh":"打呵欠同時出現在動物和人類身上。"},{"en":"Appear in both animals and humans means be found in non-human animals as well as people.","zh":"appear in both animals and humans 指在非人類動物和人類身上都能找到。"},{"en":"Play behaviour appears in both animals and humans, especially when young individuals learn social skills.","zh":"玩耍行為同時出現在動物和人類身上，尤其當幼年個體學習社交技能時。"},{"en":"A behaviour found in both groups may have deep biological roots.","zh":"同時出現在兩個群體中的行為可能有深層生物根源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing human and animal behaviour.","zh":"比較人類和動物行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"indicate attention or empathy","meaning":"顯示專注或同理心","examples":[{"en":"Yawning back may indicate attention or empathy.","zh":"跟着打呵欠可能顯示專注或同理心。"},{"en":"To indicate attention or empathy means to show that someone is noticing another person or sharing their feelings.","zh":"indicate attention or empathy 指顯示某人留意另一個人或感受到對方情緒。"},{"en":"A student who copies a friend’s worried expression may indicate attention or empathy.","zh":"學生模仿朋友擔心的表情，可能顯示專注或同理心。"},{"en":"Contagious yawning may happen when people are socially aware of each other.","zh":"傳染性打呵欠可能在人們對彼此有社交意識時發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a small behaviour reveals a mental state.","zh":"當小行為揭示心理狀態時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"during communication","meaning":"在溝通期間","examples":[{"en":"Empathic yawning may occur during communication with others.","zh":"具同理心的打呵欠可能在與他人溝通期間發生。"},{"en":"During communication means while people are exchanging signals, words, emotions, or attention.","zh":"during communication 指在人們交換訊號、說話、情緒或注意力時。"},{"en":"During communication, facial expressions can matter as much as words.","zh":"在溝通期間，面部表情可以和文字一樣重要。"},{"en":"Yawning back during communication may show that people are socially connected.","zh":"在溝通期間跟着打呵欠可能顯示人們有社交連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when behaviour happens as people interact.","zh":"當行為在人們互動時發生，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"higher regions of the brain","meaning":"大腦較高層區域","examples":[{"en":"Higher regions of the brain may be involved in contagious yawning.","zh":"大腦較高層區域可能參與傳染性打呵欠。"},{"en":"Higher regions of the brain are areas linked with more complex thinking, awareness, and social processing.","zh":"higher regions of the brain 指與較複雜思考、意識和社交處理有關的大腦區域。"},{"en":"Solving a difficult problem may involve higher regions of the brain.","zh":"解決困難問題可能涉及大腦較高層區域。"},{"en":"If contagious yawning uses higher brain regions, it may involve attention and empathy rather than only reflex.","zh":"如果傳染性打呵欠使用較高層大腦區域，它可能涉及專注和同理心，而不只是反射。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when distinguishing complex brain processes from basic automatic ones.","zh":"區分複雜大腦過程和基本自動過程時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與資料相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements agree with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與文章資料相符。"},{"en":"Agree with the information means match what the text says or supports.","zh":"agree with the information 指符合文本所說或支持的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says yawns last about six seconds, a statement saying the same agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說呵欠持續約六秒，而陳述說同樣內容，它就與資料相符。"},{"en":"Students should compare meaning carefully rather than only matching repeated words.","zh":"學生應仔細比較意思，而不只是配對重複字眼。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章內容相反的意思。"},{"en":"If the passage says men and women yawn equally often, a statement saying only men yawn often contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說男女打呵欠同樣頻密，而陳述說只有男性經常打呵欠，就與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"A contradiction must be clearly shown by the text.","zh":"矛盾必須由文本清楚顯示。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying FALSE answers.","zh":"辨認 FALSE 答案時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Choose “NOT GIVEN” when there is no information on the statement.","zh":"當該陳述沒有相關資料時，選擇 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文章沒有說明該陳述是真還是假。"},{"en":"If the passage discusses yawning but not sleep quality scores, there is no information on that detail.","zh":"如果文章討論打呵欠但沒有談睡眠質素分數，就沒有該細節的相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when the text gives no evidence.","zh":"當文本沒有證據時，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is essential for NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語對 NOT GIVEN 題很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"understand why","meaning":"明白為何……","examples":[{"en":"Several participants did not understand why they were watching yawning videos.","zh":"幾名參與者不明白為何他們要觀看打呵欠影片。"},{"en":"To understand why means to know the reason for something.","zh":"understand why 指知道某事背後的原因。"},{"en":"A student may not understand why an answer is wrong until the teacher explains the grammar rule.","zh":"學生可能直到老師解釋文法規則後，才明白為何答案錯了。"},{"en":"If participants do not understand why they are doing a task, the experiment may feel strange to them.","zh":"如果參與者不明白為何要做某項任務，實驗可能令他們感到奇怪。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone needs the reason behind an action.","zh":"當某人需要知道行動背後原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be asked to watch","meaning":"被要求觀看……","examples":[{"en":"The students were asked to watch people yawning.","zh":"學生被要求觀看人們打呵欠。"},{"en":"Be asked to watch means be instructed or requested to look at something carefully.","zh":"be asked to watch 指被指示或要求仔細觀看某物。"},{"en":"Students may be asked to watch a short video before answering questions.","zh":"學生可能被要求觀看一段短片，然後回答問題。"},{"en":"In an experiment, people are asked to watch material so researchers can observe their reactions.","zh":"在實驗中，人們被要求觀看材料，以便研究人員觀察他們的反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing an assigned viewing task.","zh":"描述被安排的觀看任務時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"indicate a link between","meaning":"顯示……之間有聯繫","examples":[{"en":"The results indicate a link between yawning and empathy.","zh":"結果顯示打呵欠和同理心之間有聯繫。"},{"en":"To indicate a link between two things means to suggest that they are connected.","zh":"indicate a link between two things 指暗示兩件事有關。"},{"en":"Survey results may indicate a link between sleep and concentration.","zh":"調查結果可能顯示睡眠和專注力之間有聯繫。"},{"en":"A link does not always prove direct cause, but it gives researchers a reason to investigate further.","zh":"聯繫不一定證明直接因果，但會給研究人員進一步調查的理由。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing research findings.","zh":"討論研究發現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have a positive impact on","meaning":"對……有正面影響","examples":[{"en":"It is uncertain whether yawning has a positive impact on recovery.","zh":"尚不確定打呵欠是否對康復有正面影響。"},{"en":"To have a positive impact on something means to improve it or help it develop well.","zh":"have a positive impact on something 指改善某事或幫助它良好發展。"},{"en":"Regular exercise can have a positive impact on mood and sleep.","zh":"定期運動可以對情緒和睡眠有正面影響。"},{"en":"If yawning helped nerve recovery, it would have a positive impact on rehabilitation.","zh":"如果打呵欠有助神經康復，它就會對復康有正面影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing possible benefits.","zh":"討論可能好處時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"recovery from brain damage","meaning":"腦部受損後的康復","examples":[{"en":"The researchers could not confirm that yawning improves recovery from brain damage.","zh":"研究人員未能確認打呵欠能改善腦部受損後的康復。"},{"en":"Recovery from brain damage means improvement after the brain has been injured or harmed.","zh":"recovery from brain damage 指大腦受傷或受損後的改善過程。"},{"en":"A patient’s recovery from brain damage may involve speech therapy, physical therapy, and medical care.","zh":"病人腦部受損後的康復可能涉及言語治療、物理治療和醫療照顧。"},{"en":"Recovery can be slow because the brain and nervous system need time to adapt.","zh":"康復可能很慢，因為大腦和神經系統需要時間適應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in medical discussions of rehabilitation.","zh":"在醫學復康討論中，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 142 - The secret of the Yawn.pdf","sourcePage":14}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 143":[{"front":"water filter","meaning":"濾水器","examples":[{"en":"The new water filter can provide safe drinking water without expensive technology.","zh":"這款新濾水器可以在不需要昂貴科技的情況下提供安全食水。"},{"en":"A water filter is a device that removes dirt, germs, or harmful substances from water.","zh":"濾水器是清除水中污垢、細菌或有害物質的裝置。"},{"en":"A family may use a water filter at home if tap water tastes unpleasant or looks cloudy.","zh":"如果自來水味道不好或看起來混濁，家庭可能在家中使用濾水器。"},{"en":"If a water filter works well, people can drink safer water and reduce the risk of illness.","zh":"如果濾水器運作良好，人們可以飲用更安全的水，並減低患病風險。"},{"en":"A water filter is especially useful where clean water is difficult to obtain.","zh":"在難以取得潔淨食水的地方，濾水器尤其有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ingenious invention","meaning":"巧妙的發明","examples":[{"en":"An ingenious invention could improve access to clean water.","zh":"一項巧妙的發明可以改善人們取得潔淨食水的機會。"},{"en":"An ingenious invention is a clever new device or method that solves a problem in a simple or surprising way.","zh":"巧妙的發明是以簡單或令人意想不到的方式解決問題的新裝置或方法。"},{"en":"A pencil with an eraser on the end was once an ingenious invention because it solved two classroom needs at once.","zh":"鉛筆尾端附有橡皮擦曾是一項巧妙的發明，因為它同時解決兩個課堂需要。"},{"en":"If an invention is ingenious, it may use cheap materials to solve a serious problem.","zh":"如果一項發明巧妙，它可能用廉價材料解決嚴重問題。"},{"en":"The phrase praises both creativity and practical usefulness.","zh":"這個短語同時讚賞創意和實用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be set to","meaning":"即將；預計會","examples":[{"en":"The invention is set to bring clean water to developing communities.","zh":"這項發明預計會為發展中社區帶來潔淨食水。"},{"en":"To be set to do something means to be expected or ready to do it soon.","zh":"「be set to」做某事，意思是預計或準備很快做該事。"},{"en":"The school is set to open a new library next month.","zh":"學校即將在下月開放新圖書館。"},{"en":"If a new device is set to reduce costs, many people may benefit once it is introduced.","zh":"如果新裝置預計會降低成本，它推出後許多人可能受惠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something likely to happen in the near future.","zh":"這個短語描述不久將來很可能發生的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"bring clean water to","meaning":"為……帶來潔淨食水","examples":[{"en":"The filter could bring clean water to much of the developing world.","zh":"這款濾水器可以為發展中地區大部分地方帶來潔淨食水。"},{"en":"To bring clean water to a place means to make safe drinking water available there.","zh":"「bring clean water to」某地，意思是令該地能取得安全食水。"},{"en":"A new village well can bring clean water to families who used to walk far for it.","zh":"一口新的村井可以為以前要走很遠取水的家庭帶來潔淨食水。"},{"en":"If clean water reaches a community, fewer children may become sick from dirty water.","zh":"如果潔淨食水到達一個社區，較少孩子可能因污水而生病。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on improving access to safe water.","zh":"這個短語集中於改善安全食水的取得。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the third world","meaning":"第三世界","examples":[{"en":"The invention was designed for communities in the third world.","zh":"這項發明是為第三世界社區設計的。"},{"en":"The third world is an older term often used to refer to poorer developing countries.","zh":"「the third world」是較舊用語，常指較貧困的發展中國家。"},{"en":"Charities may work in third-world communities where schools, clinics, or water systems are limited.","zh":"慈善機構可能在學校、診所或供水系統有限的第三世界社區工作。"},{"en":"If technology is designed for poor communities, it must be cheap, simple, and easy to repair.","zh":"如果科技是為貧困社區設計，它必須便宜、簡單且容易維修。"},{"en":"The phrase is understandable in older texts, though “developing countries” is often preferred today.","zh":"這個短語在舊文本中可理解，但今天通常較常用「發展中國家」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cutting-edge science","meaning":"尖端科學","examples":[{"en":"The filter is based on cutting-edge science.","zh":"這款濾水器建基於尖端科學。"},{"en":"Cutting-edge science is the newest and most advanced scientific knowledge or research.","zh":"尖端科學是最新、最先進的科學知識或研究。"},{"en":"Hospitals may use cutting-edge science to detect disease earlier than before.","zh":"醫院可能使用尖端科學比以往更早發現疾病。"},{"en":"If a simple product is based on cutting-edge science, it can be both advanced and practical.","zh":"如果簡單產品建基於尖端科學，它可以既先進又實用。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests modern knowledge at the front of scientific development.","zh":"這個短語暗示處於科學發展最前沿的現代知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"down-to-earth materials","meaning":"普通實用的材料","examples":[{"en":"The advanced filter is made from extremely down-to-earth materials.","zh":"這款先進濾水器由極其普通實用的材料製成。"},{"en":"Down-to-earth materials are simple, ordinary, and practical materials that are easy to find.","zh":"「down-to-earth materials」是簡單、普通、實用且容易找到的材料。"},{"en":"A school art project may use down-to-earth materials such as cardboard, string, and old newspapers.","zh":"學校美術項目可能使用硬紙板、繩子和舊報紙等普通實用材料。"},{"en":"If a device uses down-to-earth materials, more communities can make it without special supplies.","zh":"如果裝置使用普通實用材料，更多社區就能不靠特殊供應自行製作。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts simple materials with complex or expensive technology.","zh":"這個短語把簡單材料與複雜或昂貴科技作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a handful of","meaning":"一把；一小撮……","examples":[{"en":"The production process requires only a handful of clay.","zh":"製作過程只需要一小撮黏土。"},{"en":"A handful of something means a small amount that can fit in one hand.","zh":"「a handful of」某物，意思是一隻手能握住的小量。"},{"en":"A cook may add a handful of rice to soup to make it thicker.","zh":"廚師可能在湯中加入一把米，令它更濃稠。"},{"en":"If only a handful of material is needed, production becomes cheaper and easier.","zh":"如果只需要一小撮材料，製作就變得更便宜、更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase usually suggests a small, manageable quantity.","zh":"這個短語通常表示小而容易處理的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"coffee grounds","meaning":"咖啡渣","examples":[{"en":"Used coffee grounds can be mixed with clay to make the filter.","zh":"用過的咖啡渣可以與黏土混合，用來製作濾水器。"},{"en":"Coffee grounds are the wet or dry remains of coffee beans after coffee has been made.","zh":"咖啡渣是咖啡沖泡後剩下的濕或乾咖啡豆殘渣。"},{"en":"Some gardeners add coffee grounds to soil to improve compost.","zh":"有些園丁會把咖啡渣加入泥土中改善堆肥。"},{"en":"When coffee grounds burn away during firing, they can leave tiny holes in the clay.","zh":"當咖啡渣在燒製時燃燒消失，它可以在黏土中留下細小孔洞。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a common waste material that can be reused.","zh":"這個短語指可以再利用的常見廢料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cow manure","meaning":"牛糞","examples":[{"en":"Cow manure provides the heat needed to fire the filters.","zh":"牛糞提供燒製濾水器所需的熱力。"},{"en":"Cow manure is waste from cows, often used as fertiliser or fuel when dried.","zh":"牛糞是牛的排泄物，乾燥後常用作肥料或燃料。"},{"en":"Farmers may spread cow manure on fields to improve the soil.","zh":"農民可能把牛糞撒在田地上改善土壤。"},{"en":"If dried cow manure burns well, it can provide heat where wood or gas is expensive.","zh":"如果乾牛糞燃燒效果好，它可以在木材或煤氣昂貴的地方提供熱力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an ordinary farm material with practical uses.","zh":"這個短語描述具有實際用途的普通農場材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the ingredients that","meaning":"用來……的材料","examples":[{"en":"Clay and organic waste are the ingredients that make the filter possible.","zh":"黏土和有機廢料是用來製成這款濾水器的材料。"},{"en":"The ingredients that do something are the materials needed to produce a result.","zh":"「the ingredients that」做某事，是產生某結果所需的材料。"},{"en":"Flour, water, and yeast are the ingredients that make bread rise and form its shape.","zh":"麵粉、水和酵母是用來令麵包發起並形成形狀的材料。"},{"en":"If the right ingredients are cheap and local, the product can be made more widely.","zh":"如果合適材料便宜且本地可得，產品就可以更廣泛地製造。"},{"en":"The phrase explains which materials are responsible for creating something.","zh":"這個短語解釋哪些材料負責創造某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"safe drinking water","meaning":"安全食水","examples":[{"en":"The filters could provide clean, safe drinking water.","zh":"這些濾水器可以提供潔淨、安全食水。"},{"en":"Safe drinking water is water that people can drink without a high risk of illness.","zh":"安全食水是人們飲用後不會有高患病風險的水。"},{"en":"Schools need safe drinking water so students do not have to buy bottled drinks every day.","zh":"學校需要安全食水，學生才不用每天買瓶裝飲品。"},{"en":"If water contains pathogens, it is not safe to drink until it has been treated.","zh":"如果水含有病原體，它在處理前並不安全飲用。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on water that is clean enough for human health.","zh":"這個短語集中於對人體健康足夠潔淨的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"simple new technology","meaning":"簡單的新技術","examples":[{"en":"The simple new technology can be used without specialised equipment.","zh":"這項簡單的新技術可以在沒有專門設備的情況下使用。"},{"en":"Simple new technology is a new method or device that is easy to understand and use.","zh":"「simple new technology」是容易理解和使用的新方法或裝置。"},{"en":"A school may adopt simple new technology, such as an online attendance form, without major training.","zh":"學校可能採用簡單的新技術，例如網上點名表，而不需要大量培訓。"},{"en":"If technology is simple, communities can use it without depending on outside experts.","zh":"如果科技簡單，社區就能在不依賴外來專家的情況下使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes innovation that is practical rather than complicated.","zh":"這個短語描述實用而非複雜的創新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be developed by","meaning":"由……研發","examples":[{"en":"The water filter was developed by an ANU materials scientist.","zh":"這款濾水器由一位 ANU 材料科學家研發。"},{"en":"To be developed by someone means to be designed, created, or improved by that person or group.","zh":"「be developed by」某人，意思是由該人或群體設計、創造或改良。"},{"en":"A new reading app may be developed by teachers who understand students’ needs.","zh":"新閱讀應用程式可能由了解學生需要的老師研發。"},{"en":"If a product is developed by a specialist, it may be based on expert knowledge.","zh":"如果產品由專家研發，它可能建基於專業知識。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who created or improved something.","zh":"這個短語指出誰創造或改良了某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"materials scientist","meaning":"材料科學家","examples":[{"en":"Tony Flynn is a materials scientist at ANU.","zh":"Tony Flynn 是 ANU 的材料科學家。"},{"en":"A materials scientist studies the properties and uses of materials such as metals, plastics, clay, or ceramics.","zh":"材料科學家研究金屬、塑膠、黏土或陶瓷等材料的特性和用途。"},{"en":"A materials scientist may test which material is strongest, cheapest, or safest for a product.","zh":"材料科學家可能測試哪種材料對產品最堅固、最便宜或最安全。"},{"en":"If a filter depends on clay structure, a materials scientist can explain why it works.","zh":"如果濾水器依靠黏土結構，材料科學家可以解釋它為何有效。"},{"en":"The phrase names a scientist who studies what things are made from.","zh":"這個短語指出研究物件由甚麼製成的科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"allow something to be made from","meaning":"讓某物以……製成","examples":[{"en":"The process allows filters to be made from commonly available materials.","zh":"這個過程讓濾水器能以普遍可取得的材料製成。"},{"en":"To allow something to be made from certain materials means to make it possible to produce it using those materials.","zh":"「allow something to be made from」某些材料，意思是使人能用那些材料製造某物。"},{"en":"A simple recipe allows bread to be made from flour, water, yeast, and salt.","zh":"簡單食譜讓麵包可以用麵粉、水、酵母和鹽製成。"},{"en":"If a process uses local materials, people do not need expensive imports.","zh":"如果過程使用本地材料，人們就不需要昂貴進口品。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how a method makes production possible.","zh":"這個短語顯示方法如何令製作成為可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"commonly available materials","meaning":"普遍可取得的材料","examples":[{"en":"The filters are made from commonly available materials.","zh":"這些濾水器由普遍可取得的材料製成。"},{"en":"Commonly available materials are materials that many people can easily find or obtain.","zh":"「commonly available materials」是許多人容易找到或取得的材料。"},{"en":"Cardboard, string, and plastic bottles are commonly available materials for school projects.","zh":"硬紙板、繩子和膠樽是學校專題中普遍可取得的材料。"},{"en":"If a product uses commonly available materials, poor communities can make it more easily.","zh":"如果產品使用普遍可取得的材料，貧困社區可以更容易製作。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights accessibility and low dependence on special supplies.","zh":"這個短語突出可取得性和較少依賴特殊供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fire the filters","meaning":"燒製濾水器","examples":[{"en":"The filters can be fired directly on the ground.","zh":"這些濾水器可以直接在地面上燒製。"},{"en":"To fire the filters means to heat the clay filters strongly so they harden like pottery.","zh":"「fire the filters」意思是強烈加熱黏土濾水器，使其像陶器一樣變硬。"},{"en":"A potter fires bowls in a kiln to make them strong enough for daily use.","zh":"陶藝師在窯中燒製碗，使它們足夠堅硬作日常使用。"},{"en":"If clay is fired properly, it becomes harder and can keep its shape.","zh":"如果黏土被正確燒製，它會變硬並保持形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the heating stage in making ceramic objects.","zh":"這個短語描述製作陶瓷物件中的加熱階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"source of heat","meaning":"熱源","examples":[{"en":"Cow manure is used as the source of heat.","zh":"牛糞被用作熱源。"},{"en":"A source of heat is something that provides the high temperature needed for a process.","zh":"「source of heat」是提供某過程所需高溫的東西。"},{"en":"In a kitchen, a gas stove is a source of heat for cooking.","zh":"在廚房中，煤氣爐是煮食的熱源。"},{"en":"If wood is scarce, people may need another source of heat for firing clay.","zh":"如果木材稀缺，人們可能需要另一種熱源來燒製黏土。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what produces heat.","zh":"這個短語指出甚麼產生熱力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"without the need for","meaning":"無需……","examples":[{"en":"The filters can be produced without the need for a kiln.","zh":"這些濾水器可以在無需陶窯的情況下製作。"},{"en":"Without the need for something means that thing is not required.","zh":"「without the need for」某物，意思是該物不是必需的。"},{"en":"Students can submit homework online without the need for printing.","zh":"學生可以網上交功課，無需列印。"},{"en":"If a method works without expensive equipment, more people can use it.","zh":"如果方法無需昂貴設備也能運作，更多人可以使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that a usual requirement has been removed.","zh":"這個短語強調通常需要的東西已被移除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"potter’s kiln","meaning":"陶窯","examples":[{"en":"The production method does not require a potter’s kiln.","zh":"這種製作方法不需要陶窯。"},{"en":"A potter’s kiln is a special oven used to fire clay objects at high temperatures.","zh":"陶窯是用高溫燒製黏土物件的特殊爐。"},{"en":"A ceramics class may use a potter’s kiln to harden cups, bowls, and tiles.","zh":"陶藝課可能使用陶窯燒硬杯、碗和瓷磚。"},{"en":"If a community has no kiln, ordinary pottery production can be difficult.","zh":"如果社區沒有陶窯，普通陶器製作可能很困難。"},{"en":"The phrase names specialised equipment for making ceramics.","zh":"這個短語指出製作陶瓷的專門設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be tested and shown to","meaning":"經測試並證實能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The filters have been tested and shown to remove dangerous organisms.","zh":"這些濾水器經測試並證實能夠清除危險微生物。"},{"en":"To be tested and shown to do something means experiments have proved that it can do it.","zh":"「be tested and shown to」做某事，意思是實驗已證明它能做到該事。"},{"en":"A medicine must be tested and shown to be safe before doctors use it widely.","zh":"藥物在醫生廣泛使用前，必須經測試並證實安全。"},{"en":"If a filter is tested successfully, people can trust it more.","zh":"如果濾水器成功通過測試，人們會更信任它。"},{"en":"The phrase connects testing with proof of effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語把測試與有效性證明連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"remove common pathogens","meaning":"清除常見病原體","examples":[{"en":"The filters remove common pathogens from drinking water.","zh":"這些濾水器清除飲用水中的常見病原體。"},{"en":"To remove common pathogens means to take out disease-causing organisms often found in water or food.","zh":"「remove common pathogens」意思是清除水或食物中常見的致病微生物。"},{"en":"Boiling water can remove or kill many common pathogens before people drink it.","zh":"飲用前煮沸水可以清除或殺死許多常見病原體。"},{"en":"If pathogens remain in water, people may suffer diarrhoea or other diseases.","zh":"如果病原體留在水中，人們可能患腹瀉或其他疾病。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on making water safer by removing harmful microorganisms.","zh":"這個短語集中於透過清除有害微生物令水更安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pathogens","meaning":"病原體","examples":[{"en":"Pathogens can cause serious disease when they enter drinking water.","zh":"病原體進入飲用水時，可以造成嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"Pathogens are microorganisms, such as bacteria or viruses, that can cause disease.","zh":"病原體是能引起疾病的微生物，例如細菌或病毒。"},{"en":"Doctors wash their hands carefully to avoid spreading pathogens to patients.","zh":"醫生仔細洗手，以避免把病原體傳給病人。"},{"en":"If pathogens get into food or water, many people can become sick quickly.","zh":"如果病原體進入食物或水中，許多人可能很快生病。"},{"en":"The word is a scientific term for disease-causing germs.","zh":"這個詞是致病細菌或微生物的科學用語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"disease-producing organisms","meaning":"致病微生物","examples":[{"en":"Pathogens are disease-producing organisms.","zh":"病原體是致病微生物。"},{"en":"Disease-producing organisms are living things so small that they can cause illness in people, animals, or plants.","zh":"「disease-producing organisms」是細小到可以令人、動物或植物生病的生物。"},{"en":"A dirty kitchen may allow disease-producing organisms to grow on food.","zh":"骯髒廚房可能讓致病微生物在食物上生長。"},{"en":"If water filters block such organisms, the water becomes safer to drink.","zh":"如果濾水器阻隔這些微生物，水就變得更安全可飲用。"},{"en":"The phrase explains pathogens in simpler words.","zh":"這個短語以較簡單字眼解釋病原體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"E. coli","meaning":"大腸桿菌","examples":[{"en":"The filters have been tested against the E. coli bacterium.","zh":"這些濾水器已用大腸桿菌進行測試。"},{"en":"E. coli is a type of bacterium, and some forms can cause serious illness through contaminated food or water.","zh":"大腸桿菌是一種細菌，其中某些類型可透過受污染食物或水造成嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"Health officials may test drinking water for E. coli after flooding.","zh":"水災後，衛生官員可能檢測飲用水是否有大腸桿菌。"},{"en":"If a filter removes E. coli effectively, it can reduce a serious water-safety risk.","zh":"如果濾水器有效清除大腸桿菌，它可以減少嚴重食水安全風險。"},{"en":"The phrase names a bacterium often used to test water contamination.","zh":"這個短語指出常用於測試水污染的細菌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"unlike other devices","meaning":"與其他裝置不同","examples":[{"en":"Unlike other water-filtering devices, these filters are inexpensive.","zh":"與其他濾水裝置不同，這些濾水器成本低廉。"},{"en":"Unlike other devices means different from other devices in an important way.","zh":"「unlike other devices」意思是在重要方面與其他裝置不同。"},{"en":"Unlike other phones, this model can work for three days without charging.","zh":"與其他電話不同，這個型號不用充電也能運作三天。"},{"en":"If a filter is unlike expensive devices, it may be more suitable for poor communities.","zh":"如果濾水器不同於昂貴裝置，它可能更適合貧困社區。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a contrast with similar products.","zh":"這個短語引出與相似產品的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"water-filtering devices","meaning":"濾水裝置","examples":[{"en":"Many water-filtering devices require expensive equipment.","zh":"許多濾水裝置需要昂貴設備。"},{"en":"Water-filtering devices are tools or machines used to clean water before drinking or use.","zh":"濾水裝置是飲用或使用前清潔水的工具或機器。"},{"en":"A camping shop may sell small water-filtering devices for hikers.","zh":"露營店可能售賣給遠足者使用的小型濾水裝置。"},{"en":"If a device needs special parts, it may be difficult to use in remote villages.","zh":"如果裝置需要特殊零件，在偏遠村莊可能難以使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes equipment designed to make water cleaner.","zh":"這個短語描述用來令水更潔淨的設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"simple and inexpensive to make","meaning":"製作簡單而且成本低廉","examples":[{"en":"The filters are simple and inexpensive to make.","zh":"這些濾水器製作簡單而且成本低廉。"},{"en":"Simple and inexpensive to make means easy to produce and not costly.","zh":"「simple and inexpensive to make」意思是容易生產且成本不高。"},{"en":"Paper bookmarks are simple and inexpensive to make for a school reading activity.","zh":"紙書籤對學校閱讀活動而言製作簡單而且成本低廉。"},{"en":"If a health device is cheap and easy to make, more families can access it.","zh":"如果健康裝置便宜又易製作，更多家庭可以取得它。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses practical production, especially for low-resource settings.","zh":"這個短語強調實際生產，尤其適用於資源有限的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"explain and demonstrate","meaning":"解釋和示範","examples":[{"en":"The production method is easy to explain and demonstrate.","zh":"這種製作方法容易解釋和示範。"},{"en":"To explain and demonstrate something means to describe it clearly and show how it is done.","zh":"「explain and demonstrate」某事，意思是清楚說明它並展示如何做。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain and demonstrate how to use a microscope before students try it.","zh":"老師可能在學生嘗試前解釋和示範如何使用顯微鏡。"},{"en":"If a method is easy to demonstrate, local people can learn it quickly.","zh":"如果方法容易示範，本地人可以很快學會。"},{"en":"The phrase combines verbal explanation with practical showing.","zh":"這個短語結合口頭解釋和實際展示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be made by anyone, anywhere","meaning":"任何人在任何地方都能製作","examples":[{"en":"The filters can be made by anyone, anywhere.","zh":"這些濾水器任何人在任何地方都能製作。"},{"en":"To be made by anyone, anywhere means no special expert or special location is needed.","zh":"「be made by anyone, anywhere」意思是不需要專門專家或特殊地點。"},{"en":"A simple paper mask design can be made by anyone, anywhere if the instructions are clear.","zh":"如果指示清楚，簡單紙面具設計任何人在任何地方都能製作。"},{"en":"If a filter can be produced locally, communities do not have to wait for imports.","zh":"如果濾水器可以在本地製作，社區就不用等待進口。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses accessibility and independence.","zh":"這個短語強調可取得性和自主性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"require Western technology","meaning":"需要西方科技","examples":[{"en":"The process does not require any Western technology.","zh":"這個過程不需要任何西方科技。"},{"en":"To require Western technology means to need equipment, methods, or systems imported from wealthy Western countries.","zh":"「require Western technology」意思是需要從富裕西方國家進口的設備、方法或系統。"},{"en":"A village project is easier to maintain if it does not require foreign technology or spare parts.","zh":"如果村莊項目不需要外國科技或零件，就較容易維持。"},{"en":"If a method avoids expensive imported equipment, local people can use it more independently.","zh":"如果方法避免昂貴進口設備，本地人就能更獨立使用。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts local simplicity with imported high-tech systems.","zh":"這個短語把本地簡易方法與進口高科技系統作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"all you need is","meaning":"你所需要的只是……","examples":[{"en":"All you need is clay, cow manure and a match.","zh":"你所需要的只是黏土、牛糞和一根火柴。"},{"en":"All you need is means these are the only necessary things.","zh":"「all you need is」意思是這些就是唯一需要的東西。"},{"en":"To start a simple diary, all you need is a notebook and a pen.","zh":"要開始寫簡單日記，你所需要的只是一本筆記簿和一支筆。"},{"en":"If all you need is cheap local material, more people can try the method.","zh":"如果你所需要的只是廉價本地材料，更多人就能嘗試該方法。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises simplicity and low requirements.","zh":"這個短語強調簡單和低需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"terracotta clay","meaning":"赤陶黏土","examples":[{"en":"Terracotta clay is one of the filter’s main ingredients.","zh":"赤陶黏土是濾水器的主要材料之一。"},{"en":"Terracotta clay is reddish-brown clay commonly used to make pottery, tiles, and plant pots.","zh":"赤陶黏土是常用於製作陶器、瓦片和花盆的紅褐色黏土。"},{"en":"A garden shop may sell terracotta clay pots because they are simple and porous.","zh":"園藝店可能售賣赤陶花盆，因為它們簡單且多孔。"},{"en":"If terracotta clay is fired, it becomes hard but can still contain tiny pores.","zh":"如果赤陶黏土被燒製，它會變硬，但仍可含有細小孔洞。"},{"en":"The phrase names a common pottery material.","zh":"這個短語指出常見陶器材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"production of the filters","meaning":"濾水器的製作","examples":[{"en":"The production of the filters is extremely simple.","zh":"濾水器的製作極其簡單。"},{"en":"Production of the filters means the process of making the filters.","zh":"「production of the filters」意思是製作濾水器的過程。"},{"en":"A community workshop can teach the production of filters step by step.","zh":"社區工作坊可以逐步教授濾水器的製作。"},{"en":"If production is simple, local people can make replacements when old filters break.","zh":"如果製作簡單，本地人可以在舊濾水器損壞時製作替代品。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the full making process, not just one step.","zh":"這個短語指完整製作過程，而不只是其中一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"dry, crushed clay","meaning":"乾燥並壓碎的黏土","examples":[{"en":"The first step is to prepare some dry, crushed clay.","zh":"第一步是準備一些乾燥並壓碎的黏土。"},{"en":"Dry, crushed clay is clay that has been dried and broken into small pieces or powder.","zh":"「dry, crushed clay」是已乾燥並被弄成小碎片或粉末的黏土。"},{"en":"A pottery class may begin by preparing dry, crushed clay before mixing it with water.","zh":"陶藝課可能先準備乾燥壓碎的黏土，再與水混合。"},{"en":"If clay is crushed evenly, it can mix more smoothly with other materials.","zh":"如果黏土被均勻壓碎，它可以更順滑地與其他材料混合。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the prepared form of clay before shaping.","zh":"這個短語描述塑形前黏土的準備形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mix something with","meaning":"把某物與……混合","examples":[{"en":"The clay is mixed with organic material.","zh":"黏土與有機材料混合。"},{"en":"To mix something with another material means to combine them so they become one mixture.","zh":"「mix something with」另一種材料，意思是把兩者結合成一種混合物。"},{"en":"A baker mixes flour with water to make dough.","zh":"麵包師把麵粉與水混合來製作麵糰。"},{"en":"If clay is mixed with organic material, firing can leave tiny pores inside it.","zh":"如果黏土與有機材料混合，燒製後可以在其中留下細小孔洞。"},{"en":"The phrase describes combining materials for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述為某目的結合材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"organic material","meaning":"有機材料","examples":[{"en":"Organic material creates small passages inside the finished filter.","zh":"有機材料在完成的濾水器內形成細小通道。"},{"en":"Organic material is material that comes from living things, such as plants, food waste, or manure.","zh":"有機材料是來自生物的材料，例如植物、食物廢料或糞便。"},{"en":"Leaves and vegetable scraps are organic material often used in compost.","zh":"葉子和蔬菜殘渣是常用於堆肥的有機材料。"},{"en":"When organic material burns away, it can leave spaces inside clay.","zh":"當有機材料燃燒消失，它可以在黏土中留下空隙。"},{"en":"The phrase describes natural matter from living sources.","zh":"這個短語描述來自生命來源的自然物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"used tea leaves","meaning":"用過的茶葉","examples":[{"en":"Used tea leaves can be added to the clay mixture.","zh":"用過的茶葉可以加入黏土混合物中。"},{"en":"Used tea leaves are tea leaves left after tea has been made.","zh":"「used tea leaves」是泡茶後剩下的茶葉。"},{"en":"Some people put used tea leaves into plant soil instead of throwing them away.","zh":"有些人把用過的茶葉放入植物泥土中，而不是丟掉。"},{"en":"If used tea leaves burn away in clay, they may help form pores.","zh":"如果用過的茶葉在黏土中燃燒消失，它們可能幫助形成孔洞。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a common household waste that can be reused.","zh":"這個短語指可再利用的常見家居廢料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rice hulls","meaning":"稻殼","examples":[{"en":"Rice hulls can also be used as organic material.","zh":"稻殼也可以用作有機材料。"},{"en":"Rice hulls are the dry outer coverings of grains of rice.","zh":"稻殼是米粒外面的乾燥外殼。"},{"en":"Farmers may collect rice hulls after rice is processed.","zh":"農民可能在稻米加工後收集稻殼。"},{"en":"If rice hulls are mixed with clay and later burned away, they can leave tiny spaces.","zh":"如果稻殼與黏土混合並之後燃燒消失，它們可以留下細小空隙。"},{"en":"The phrase names an agricultural waste material.","zh":"這個短語指出一種農業廢料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"add enough water to","meaning":"加入足夠的水以……","examples":[{"en":"Add enough water to create a thick mixture.","zh":"加入足夠的水以製成濃稠混合物。"},{"en":"To add enough water to do something means to put in the amount of water needed for that result.","zh":"「add enough water to」做某事，意思是加入達到該結果所需的水量。"},{"en":"A cook adds enough water to flour to make dough that can be shaped.","zh":"廚師在麵粉中加入足夠的水，以製作可塑形的麵糰。"},{"en":"If too little water is added, the mixture may crumble; if too much is added, it may become runny.","zh":"如果水太少，混合物可能碎裂；如果水太多，可能變得太稀。"},{"en":"The phrase links the amount of water with the desired texture.","zh":"這個短語把水量與想要的質感連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"stiff biscuit-like mixture","meaning":"餅乾麵糰般硬實的混合物","examples":[{"en":"The clay and water form a stiff biscuit-like mixture.","zh":"黏土和水形成餅乾麵糰般硬實的混合物。"},{"en":"A stiff biscuit-like mixture is a thick, firm mixture that can hold its shape.","zh":"「stiff biscuit-like mixture」是濃稠、結實並能保持形狀的混合物。"},{"en":"Cookie dough before baking can feel like a stiff biscuit-like mixture.","zh":"烘焙前的曲奇麵糰可能感覺像餅乾麵糰般硬實的混合物。"},{"en":"If the mixture is too soft, it may not form a strong pot shape.","zh":"如果混合物太軟，它可能無法形成堅固陶罐形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase helps describe texture in a familiar way.","zh":"這個短語以熟悉方式幫助描述質感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"form a cylindrical pot","meaning":"製成圓柱形陶罐","examples":[{"en":"The mixture is shaped to form a cylindrical pot.","zh":"混合物被塑形成圓柱形陶罐。"},{"en":"To form a cylindrical pot means to make the material into a round container with straight sides.","zh":"「form a cylindrical pot」意思是把材料製成直邊圓形容器。"},{"en":"In art class, students may roll clay around a tube to form a cylindrical pot.","zh":"在美術課中，學生可能把黏土圍着圓管捲起，以製成圓柱形陶罐。"},{"en":"If the pot shape is regular, water can pass through its walls more evenly.","zh":"如果陶罐形狀規則，水可以更均勻地通過其器壁。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shaping material into a container.","zh":"這個短語描述把材料塑造成容器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cylindrical pot","meaning":"圓柱形陶罐","examples":[{"en":"The filter is produced in the form of a cylindrical pot.","zh":"濾水器以圓柱形陶罐的形式製成。"},{"en":"A cylindrical pot is a container shaped like a cylinder, with a round base and straight sides.","zh":"「cylindrical pot」是形狀像圓柱、有圓形底部和直邊的容器。"},{"en":"A pencil holder is often a small cylindrical pot on a desk.","zh":"筆筒常是書桌上的小型圓柱形容器。"},{"en":"If a filter is shaped like a pot, water can be poured into it and pass through the walls.","zh":"如果濾水器形狀像陶罐，水可以倒入其中並穿過器壁。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the physical shape of the filter.","zh":"這個短語描述濾水器的物理形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have one end closed","meaning":"一端封閉","examples":[{"en":"The cylindrical pot should have one end closed.","zh":"圓柱形陶罐應該一端封閉。"},{"en":"To have one end closed means one side or opening is sealed so liquid cannot pass straight through.","zh":"「have one end closed」意思是一邊或一個開口被封住，使液體不能直接通過。"},{"en":"A bottle has one end closed so it can hold water.","zh":"瓶子一端封閉，因此可以盛水。"},{"en":"If the filter pot had both ends open, water might escape too quickly without filtering properly.","zh":"如果濾水陶罐兩端都開口，水可能太快流走而未能正確過濾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a container shape needed for holding liquid.","zh":"這個短語描述盛載液體所需的容器形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dry it in the sun","meaning":"把它放在陽光下曬乾","examples":[{"en":"The newly formed pot must be dried in the sun.","zh":"新成形的陶罐必須放在陽光下曬乾。"},{"en":"To dry it in the sun means to place it under sunlight so moisture evaporates.","zh":"「dry it in the sun」意思是把它放在陽光下，讓水分蒸發。"},{"en":"People may dry clothes in the sun when they do not have a dryer.","zh":"沒有乾衣機時，人們可能把衣服放在陽光下曬乾。"},{"en":"If the clay pot is not dry enough before firing, it may crack or break.","zh":"如果黏土陶罐在燒製前不夠乾，它可能裂開或破裂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a simple natural drying method.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單自然的乾燥方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"give the best results","meaning":"取得最佳效果","examples":[{"en":"Used coffee grounds have given the best results to date.","zh":"用過的咖啡渣至今取得最佳效果。"},{"en":"To give the best results means to produce the most successful or effective outcome.","zh":"「give the best results」意思是產生最成功或最有效的結果。"},{"en":"A student may find that revising every morning gives the best results for memory.","zh":"學生可能發現每天早上溫習對記憶取得最佳效果。"},{"en":"If one material filters water better than others, researchers may choose it for production.","zh":"如果一種材料比其他材料更好地過濾水，研究人員可能選擇它作生產用途。"},{"en":"The phrase compares different methods or materials by effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語按效果比較不同方法或材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"to date","meaning":"至今","examples":[{"en":"Coffee grounds have produced the best results to date.","zh":"咖啡渣至今產生最佳效果。"},{"en":"To date means up to the present time.","zh":"「to date」意思是截至目前為止。"},{"en":"This is the best test score the class has achieved to date.","zh":"這是全班至今取得的最佳測驗分數。"},{"en":"If a method works best to date, later experiments may still improve on it.","zh":"如果某方法至今效果最好，後來實驗仍可能進一步改善。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the conclusion is based on evidence available so far.","zh":"這個短語顯示結論建基於目前可得證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"surround the pots with","meaning":"用……圍住陶罐","examples":[{"en":"The pots are surrounded with straw before firing.","zh":"燒製前，陶罐被稻草圍住。"},{"en":"To surround the pots with something means to place that material all around the pots.","zh":"「surround the pots with」某物，意思是把該材料放在陶罐四周。"},{"en":"A gardener may surround young plants with straw to protect the soil.","zh":"園丁可能用稻草圍住幼苗以保護泥土。"},{"en":"If straw surrounds the pots, it can help start the fire evenly.","zh":"如果稻草圍住陶罐，它可以幫助均勻地點火。"},{"en":"The phrase describes putting material around an object.","zh":"這個短語描述把材料放在物件周圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"straw","meaning":"稻草；乾草","examples":[{"en":"Straw is used to light the cow manure.","zh":"稻草用來點燃牛糞。"},{"en":"Straw is the dry stalks of grain plants, often used for bedding, packing, or fuel.","zh":"「straw」是穀物植物的乾莖，常用作墊料、包裝或燃料。"},{"en":"Farmers may use straw to cover animal bedding or protect soil.","zh":"農民可能用稻草鋪動物墊料或保護泥土。"},{"en":"If straw catches fire easily, it can help start a larger fuel source burning.","zh":"如果稻草容易着火，它可以幫助點燃較大的燃料來源。"},{"en":"The word refers to a dry plant material, not a drinking straw in this context.","zh":"在這個語境中，這個詞指乾植物材料，而不是飲管。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mound of cow manure","meaning":"一堆牛糞","examples":[{"en":"The pots are placed inside a mound of cow manure.","zh":"陶罐被放在一堆牛糞之內。"},{"en":"A mound of cow manure is a pile or heap of cow dung.","zh":"「mound of cow manure」是一堆或一大堆牛糞。"},{"en":"Farmers may leave a mound of manure near fields before spreading it as fertiliser.","zh":"農民可能把一堆牛糞放在田邊，之後撒作肥料。"},{"en":"If the pots are placed inside the mound, the burning manure can heat them from all sides.","zh":"如果陶罐放在糞堆中，燃燒中的牛糞可以從四周加熱它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the pile used as fuel around the pots.","zh":"這個短語描述用作陶罐周圍燃料的一堆物料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"light the straw","meaning":"點燃稻草","examples":[{"en":"The producer lights the straw to begin the firing process.","zh":"製作者點燃稻草，以開始燒製過程。"},{"en":"To light the straw means to set the dry straw on fire.","zh":"「light the straw」意思是把乾稻草點着。"},{"en":"A camper may light dry twigs before adding larger pieces of wood.","zh":"露營者可能先點燃乾樹枝，再加入較大的木塊。"},{"en":"If the straw burns first, it can ignite the cow manure around the pots.","zh":"如果稻草先燃燒，它可以點燃陶罐周圍的牛糞。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the first step in starting the fire.","zh":"這個短語描述起火的第一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"top up","meaning":"添加；補充","examples":[{"en":"More manure is used to top up the fire when necessary.","zh":"有需要時會用更多牛糞添加到火中。"},{"en":"To top up something means to add more of it so there is enough.","zh":"「top up」某物，意思是再加入一些，使其足夠。"},{"en":"A student may top up a water bottle before leaving school.","zh":"學生離校前可能把水樽補滿。"},{"en":"If the fire becomes weak, adding more fuel can keep the temperature high.","zh":"如果火勢變弱，添加更多燃料可以保持高溫。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adding extra material to maintain a level or supply.","zh":"這個短語描述加入額外材料以維持水平或供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as required","meaning":"按需要","examples":[{"en":"The burning manure should be topped up as required.","zh":"燃燒中的牛糞應按需要補充。"},{"en":"As required means when and as much as needed.","zh":"「as required」意思是在需要時並按所需程度。"},{"en":"A teacher may give extra worksheets as required when students need more practice.","zh":"當學生需要更多練習時，老師可能按需要給額外工作紙。"},{"en":"If fuel is added as required, the fire can stay hot without wasting material.","zh":"如果燃料按需要添加，火可以保持高溫而不浪費材料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes flexible action according to need.","zh":"這個短語描述按需要靈活行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in less than 60 minutes","meaning":"在少於60分鐘內","examples":[{"en":"The filters can be finished in less than 60 minutes.","zh":"這些濾水器可以在少於60分鐘內完成。"},{"en":"In less than 60 minutes means before one full hour has passed.","zh":"「in less than 60 minutes」意思是在一整小時過去之前。"},{"en":"A simple lunch can be cooked in less than 60 minutes.","zh":"一頓簡單午餐可以在少於60分鐘內煮好。"},{"en":"If production takes under an hour, communities can make many filters quickly.","zh":"如果製作需時少於一小時，社區可以快速製作許多濾水器。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the process is relatively fast.","zh":"這個短語強調過程相對快速。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"finished pot","meaning":"完成的陶罐","examples":[{"en":"The walls of the finished pot must have the correct thickness.","zh":"完成的陶罐器壁必須有正確厚度。"},{"en":"A finished pot is the pot after it has been shaped, dried, and fired.","zh":"「finished pot」是已塑形、曬乾並燒製後的陶罐。"},{"en":"In a pottery class, students paint the finished pot only after it has cooled.","zh":"在陶藝課中，學生只會在完成的陶罐冷卻後上色。"},{"en":"If the finished pot is too thin, it may break; if it is too thick, water may not pass through well.","zh":"如果完成的陶罐太薄，它可能破裂；如果太厚，水可能不能順利通過。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the completed ceramic object.","zh":"這個短語指完成的陶瓷物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"about as thick as","meaning":"厚度大約相等於……","examples":[{"en":"The wall should be about as thick as an adult’s index finger.","zh":"器壁厚度應大約相等於成年人的食指。"},{"en":"About as thick as means approximately the same thickness as something familiar.","zh":"「about as thick as」意思是厚度大約與某個熟悉物件相同。"},{"en":"A slice of bread may be about as thick as a student’s notebook.","zh":"一片麵包可能厚度大約相等於學生筆記本。"},{"en":"If instructions use a familiar comparison, people can judge thickness without special tools.","zh":"如果指示使用熟悉比較，人們不用特殊工具也能判斷厚度。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate measurement through comparison.","zh":"這個短語透過比較提供大約量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"adult’s index finger","meaning":"成年人的食指","examples":[{"en":"The filter wall should be about as thick as an adult’s index finger.","zh":"濾水器器壁厚度應大約相等於成年人的食指。"},{"en":"An adult’s index finger is the pointing finger of a grown person.","zh":"「adult’s index finger」是成年人的指示用手指。"},{"en":"A craft teacher may compare clay thickness with an adult’s index finger to make instructions simple.","zh":"手工老師可能把黏土厚度與成年人的食指比較，使指示簡單。"},{"en":"If the wall is roughly this thickness, the filter may be strong but still porous enough.","zh":"如果器壁大約這個厚度，濾水器可能夠堅固，同時仍有足夠孔隙。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a practical body-based measurement.","zh":"這個短語提供實用的身體量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"properties of cow manure","meaning":"牛糞的特性","examples":[{"en":"The properties of cow manure make it a suitable fuel.","zh":"牛糞的特性使它成為合適燃料。"},{"en":"Properties of cow manure are its features, such as how dry it is and how easily it burns.","zh":"「properties of cow manure」是牛糞的特徵，例如乾燥程度和燃燒容易程度。"},{"en":"A science class may study the properties of paper, metal, and clay by testing them.","zh":"科學課可能透過測試紙、金屬和黏土來研究它們的特性。"},{"en":"If a material burns quickly and reaches high heat, its properties make it useful as fuel.","zh":"如果材料燃燒快速並達到高溫，其特性使它可作燃料。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the qualities that explain how a material behaves.","zh":"這個短語指解釋材料如何表現的性質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be vital","meaning":"至關重要","examples":[{"en":"The heating properties of the manure are vital to the process.","zh":"牛糞的加熱特性對該過程至關重要。"},{"en":"To be vital means to be extremely important or necessary.","zh":"「be vital」意思是極其重要或必不可少。"},{"en":"Clean hands are vital in a hospital because they prevent infection.","zh":"在醫院，乾淨雙手至關重要，因為它們防止感染。"},{"en":"If cow manure cannot produce enough heat, the filter may not be fired properly.","zh":"如果牛糞不能產生足夠熱力，濾水器可能無法正確燒製。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something the process cannot succeed without.","zh":"這個短語描述過程成功不可缺少的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"reach a temperature of","meaning":"達到……的溫度","examples":[{"en":"The manure can reach a temperature of 700 degrees.","zh":"牛糞可以達到700度的溫度。"},{"en":"To reach a temperature of a certain number means to heat up to that level.","zh":"「reach a temperature of」某數字，意思是加熱至該水平。"},{"en":"An oven may reach a temperature of 200 degrees before bread is baked.","zh":"焗爐可能在烘焙麵包前達到200度的溫度。"},{"en":"If the fuel reaches a high enough temperature, clay can harden properly.","zh":"如果燃料達到足夠高溫，黏土可以正確變硬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a measured level of heat.","zh":"這個短語描述可量度的熱力水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in half an hour","meaning":"在半小時內","examples":[{"en":"The fuel can reach 700 degrees in half an hour.","zh":"燃料可以在半小時內達到700度。"},{"en":"In half an hour means within thirty minutes.","zh":"「in half an hour」意思是在三十分鐘內。"},{"en":"A student may finish a short grammar exercise in half an hour.","zh":"學生可能在半小時內完成短文法練習。"},{"en":"If fuel heats up quickly, the whole production process becomes faster.","zh":"如果燃料升溫很快，整個製作過程就變得更快。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a short time frame.","zh":"這個短語提供短時間範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"after another 20 to 30 minutes","meaning":"再過20至30分鐘後","examples":[{"en":"The temperature may reach 950 degrees after another 20 to 30 minutes.","zh":"再過20至30分鐘後，溫度可能達到950度。"},{"en":"After another 20 to 30 minutes means after an additional period of about twenty to thirty minutes.","zh":"「after another 20 to 30 minutes」意思是再額外經過約二十至三十分鐘後。"},{"en":"Soup may become softer after another 20 to 30 minutes of cooking.","zh":"湯再煮20至30分鐘後，材料可能變得更軟。"},{"en":"If the temperature continues rising, the clay may fire more completely.","zh":"如果溫度繼續上升，黏土可能燒製得更完全。"},{"en":"The phrase adds an extra time period after an earlier stage.","zh":"這個短語在早前階段之後加入額外時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make a good fuel","meaning":"是良好的燃料","examples":[{"en":"Dry cow manure makes a good fuel for firing clay.","zh":"乾牛糞是燒製黏土的良好燃料。"},{"en":"To make a good fuel means to work well as something that burns and produces heat.","zh":"「make a good fuel」意思是適合作為燃燒並產生熱力的材料。"},{"en":"Dry wood makes a good fuel for a campfire because it catches fire easily.","zh":"乾木材是營火的良好燃料，因為它容易着火。"},{"en":"If a fuel burns hot and quickly, it can be useful for heating or firing.","zh":"如果燃料燃燒得熱而快，它可用於加熱或燒製。"},{"en":"The phrase judges how suitable a material is for producing heat.","zh":"這個短語判斷材料是否適合產生熱力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be high in organic material","meaning":"含有大量有機物質","examples":[{"en":"Cow manure is very high in organic material.","zh":"牛糞含有大量有機物質。"},{"en":"To be high in organic material means to contain a large amount of matter from living things.","zh":"「be high in organic material」意思是含有大量來自生物的物質。"},{"en":"Compost is high in organic material because it contains leaves, food scraps, and plant matter.","zh":"堆肥含有大量有機物質，因為它包含葉子、食物殘渣和植物材料。"},{"en":"If manure contains much organic material, it can burn and release heat when dry.","zh":"如果糞便含有很多有機物質，乾燥後可以燃燒並釋放熱力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the composition of a material.","zh":"這個短語描述材料的組成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"burn readily and quickly","meaning":"容易而且迅速燃燒","examples":[{"en":"The dry manure burns readily and quickly.","zh":"乾牛糞容易而且迅速燃燒。"},{"en":"To burn readily and quickly means to catch fire easily and burn fast.","zh":"「burn readily and quickly」意思是容易着火並快速燃燒。"},{"en":"Dry leaves burn readily and quickly, so people should keep them away from flames.","zh":"乾葉容易而且迅速燃燒，所以人們應使它們遠離火焰。"},{"en":"If a fuel burns easily, it can start the firing process without complicated equipment.","zh":"如果燃料容易燃燒，它可以在沒有複雜設備下開始燒製過程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes easy and rapid combustion.","zh":"這個短語描述容易且快速的燃燒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"exactly as found in the field","meaning":"按在田野發現時的原狀使用","examples":[{"en":"The manure is best used exactly as found in the field.","zh":"牛糞最好按在田野發現時的原狀使用。"},{"en":"Exactly as found in the field means in its natural collected state, without extra processing.","zh":"「exactly as found in the field」意思是以自然收集時的狀態使用，不作額外加工。"},{"en":"A science teacher may ask students to observe a leaf exactly as found in the field before cutting it.","zh":"科學老師可能要求學生在剪開葉子前，先按田野發現時的原狀觀察它。"},{"en":"If a material works without processing, preparation time and labour are reduced.","zh":"如果材料不用加工也能運作，準備時間和勞力都會減少。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses using something in its original condition.","zh":"這個短語強調以原本狀態使用某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"break it up","meaning":"把它弄碎","examples":[{"en":"There is no need to break the dry manure up.","zh":"沒有需要把乾牛糞弄碎。"},{"en":"To break it up means to separate something into smaller pieces.","zh":"「break it up」意思是把某物分成較小塊。"},{"en":"A cook may break up chocolate before melting it.","zh":"廚師可能在融化朱古力前把它弄碎。"},{"en":"If manure burns well without being broken up, the process becomes simpler.","zh":"如果牛糞不用弄碎也能燃燒良好，過程就變得更簡單。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physically dividing a material.","zh":"這個短語描述把材料物理分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"process it further","meaning":"進一步加工","examples":[{"en":"The manure does not need to be processed any further.","zh":"牛糞不需要進一步加工。"},{"en":"To process it further means to treat, prepare, or change it more before use.","zh":"「process it further」意思是在使用前再處理、準備或改變它。"},{"en":"Washed fruit can be eaten without processing it further.","zh":"洗淨的水果可以不用進一步加工便食用。"},{"en":"If a material needs no further processing, people can use it quickly and cheaply.","zh":"如果材料不需要進一步加工，人們可以快速而廉價地使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extra preparation that may or may not be necessary.","zh":"這個短語描述可能需要或不需要的額外準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"expensive item","meaning":"昂貴的設備","examples":[{"en":"A potter’s kiln is an expensive item.","zh":"陶窯是一件昂貴的設備。"},{"en":"An expensive item is something that costs a lot of money to buy.","zh":"「expensive item」是購買成本很高的物件。"},{"en":"A laptop can be an expensive item for a family with a limited budget.","zh":"對預算有限的家庭而言，手提電腦可能是昂貴物品。"},{"en":"If production depends on expensive items, poor communities may not be able to copy it.","zh":"如果生產依賴昂貴設備，貧困社區可能無法複製該方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a costly object or piece of equipment.","zh":"這個短語描述成本高的物件或設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take up to","meaning":"最多需要","examples":[{"en":"A kiln can take up to five hours to reach the required temperature.","zh":"陶窯最多需要五小時才能達到所需溫度。"},{"en":"To take up to a certain time means it may need as long as that time, though sometimes less.","zh":"「take up to」某時間，意思是最多可能需要該段時間，但有時較少。"},{"en":"A bus journey can take up to an hour during rush hour.","zh":"繁忙時間巴士車程最多可能需要一小時。"},{"en":"If heating takes up to five hours, production becomes slower and more fuel is needed.","zh":"如果加熱最多需要五小時，製作會變慢並需要更多燃料。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the maximum possible time needed.","zh":"這個短語提供所需時間上限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get up to 800 degrees","meaning":"升至800度","examples":[{"en":"A traditional kiln may take several hours to get up to 800 degrees.","zh":"傳統陶窯可能需要數小時升至800度。"},{"en":"To get up to 800 degrees means to heat until the temperature reaches 800 degrees.","zh":"「get up to 800 degrees」意思是加熱至溫度達到800度。"},{"en":"An oven must get up to the right temperature before some bread can bake properly.","zh":"有些麵包要正確烘焙，焗爐必須先升至合適溫度。"},{"en":"If equipment heats slowly, workers must wait before the firing process can begin.","zh":"如果設備升溫慢，工人在燒製過程開始前必須等待。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rising to a high temperature.","zh":"這個短語描述升至高溫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"expensive or scarce fuel","meaning":"昂貴或稀缺的燃料","examples":[{"en":"A kiln may require expensive or scarce fuel.","zh":"陶窯可能需要昂貴或稀缺的燃料。"},{"en":"Expensive or scarce fuel is fuel that costs a lot or is difficult to find.","zh":"「expensive or scarce fuel」是成本高或難以找到的燃料。"},{"en":"In remote villages, gas or dry wood may be expensive or scarce fuel.","zh":"在偏遠村莊，煤氣或乾木材可能是昂貴或稀缺燃料。"},{"en":"If fuel is costly or rare, a community cannot depend on it for everyday production.","zh":"如果燃料昂貴或稀少，社區就不能依賴它作日常生產。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why low-cost local fuel matters.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何低成本本地燃料重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"gas or wood","meaning":"煤氣或木材","examples":[{"en":"Traditional kilns are commonly heated with gas or wood.","zh":"傳統陶窯通常以煤氣或木材加熱。"},{"en":"Gas or wood are common fuels used to produce heat for cooking, heating, or firing.","zh":"「gas or wood」是用於煮食、取暖或燒製的常見燃料。"},{"en":"A restaurant may cook with gas, while a campsite may use wood for a fire.","zh":"餐廳可能用煤氣煮食，而露營地可能用木材生火。"},{"en":"If gas or wood is scarce, firing clay becomes expensive or difficult.","zh":"如果煤氣或木材稀缺，燒製黏土會變得昂貴或困難。"},{"en":"The phrase names two ordinary fuel sources.","zh":"這個短語指出兩種普通燃料來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"experience to operate","meaning":"操作……所需的經驗","examples":[{"en":"A potter needs experience to operate a kiln safely.","zh":"陶藝師需要操作陶窯所需的經驗，才能安全使用它。"},{"en":"Experience to operate something means practical skill learned from using it before.","zh":"「experience to operate」某物，意思是從以前使用中學到的實際技能。"},{"en":"A driver needs experience to operate a large bus safely in heavy traffic.","zh":"司機需要操作大型巴士所需的經驗，才能在繁忙交通中安全駕駛。"},{"en":"If equipment requires experience, beginners may make mistakes or cause danger.","zh":"如果設備需要經驗才能操作，初學者可能犯錯或造成危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the practical knowledge needed to use a machine.","zh":"這個短語描述使用機器所需的實用知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"insulation","meaning":"隔熱物料；隔熱設備","examples":[{"en":"A traditional kiln normally requires effective insulation.","zh":"傳統陶窯通常需要有效隔熱物料。"},{"en":"Insulation is material or design that keeps heat from escaping or entering too quickly.","zh":"「insulation」是防止熱力太快散失或進入的材料或設計。"},{"en":"Homes use insulation in walls and roofs to stay warm in winter and cool in summer.","zh":"房屋在牆壁和屋頂使用隔熱物料，以在冬天保暖、夏天保持涼快。"},{"en":"If a kiln lacks insulation, it may waste fuel and fail to reach high temperatures.","zh":"如果陶窯缺乏隔熱設備，它可能浪費燃料並無法達到高溫。"},{"en":"The word describes protection against heat transfer.","zh":"這個詞描述防止熱力傳遞的保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"nothing other than","meaning":"除了……之外甚麼也不需要","examples":[{"en":"The new process requires nothing other than manure and a match.","zh":"這個新過程除了牛糞和火柴之外甚麼也不需要。"},{"en":"Nothing other than means only that thing and nothing else.","zh":"「nothing other than」意思是只需要該物，其他一概不需要。"},{"en":"To start the game, children need nothing other than a ball and some open space.","zh":"要開始遊戲，孩子除了球和一些空地之外甚麼也不需要。"},{"en":"If a method requires nothing other than local fuel, it is easier to copy widely.","zh":"如果方法除了本地燃料之外甚麼也不需要，它就更容易廣泛複製。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly emphasises simplicity.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調簡單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pile of cow manure","meaning":"一堆牛糞","examples":[{"en":"The filters can be fired using only a pile of cow manure.","zh":"這些濾水器只用一堆牛糞便可燒製。"},{"en":"A pile of cow manure is a heap of cow dung gathered together.","zh":"「pile of cow manure」是一堆聚集起來的牛糞。"},{"en":"A farmer may collect a pile of manure before using it as fertiliser.","zh":"農民可能先收集一堆牛糞，再用作肥料。"},{"en":"If the pile burns hot enough, it can replace a kiln for this simple process.","zh":"如果糞堆燃燒得足夠熱，它可以在這種簡單過程中取代陶窯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the basic fuel arrangement.","zh":"這個短語描述基本燃料安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"restrictions apply","meaning":"限制適用","examples":[{"en":"None of the restrictions associated with kilns apply to this method.","zh":"與陶窯相關的限制都不適用於這種方法。"},{"en":"When restrictions apply, certain limits or rules affect what people can do.","zh":"當「restrictions apply」時，某些限制或規則會影響人們能做甚麼。"},{"en":"In a library, age restrictions may apply to borrowing certain materials.","zh":"在圖書館，某些材料的借閱可能有年齡限制適用。"},{"en":"If kiln restrictions do not apply, people need less money, fuel, and specialist skill.","zh":"如果陶窯限制不適用，人們就需要較少金錢、燃料和專門技能。"},{"en":"The phrase explains whether limits are relevant to a situation.","zh":"這個短語解釋限制是否與某情況相關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"freely available across","meaning":"在……各地都可免費取得","examples":[{"en":"Cow dung is freely available across much of the developing world.","zh":"牛糞在發展中地區大部分地方都可免費取得。"},{"en":"Freely available across an area means easy to obtain in many places there, often without payment.","zh":"「freely available across」某地，意思是在該地許多地方容易取得，通常不用付款。"},{"en":"Public drinking water is freely available across many city parks.","zh":"公共飲用水在許多城市公園各處都可免費取得。"},{"en":"If a material is freely available, communities can use it without high supply costs.","zh":"如果材料可免費取得，社區就能不用高供應成本而使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses wide and easy access.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛而容易取得。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"developing world","meaning":"發展中地區","examples":[{"en":"The filter was designed for use throughout the developing world.","zh":"這款濾水器是為在整個發展中地區使用而設計的。"},{"en":"The developing world refers to countries or regions with lower income levels and less developed infrastructure.","zh":"「developing world」指收入水平較低、基礎設施較不完善的國家或地區。"},{"en":"Many health projects in the developing world focus on water, sanitation, education, and clinics.","zh":"發展中地區的許多健康項目集中於食水、衛生、教育和診所。"},{"en":"If technology is built for the developing world, it should be affordable and easy to maintain.","zh":"如果科技是為發展中地區而設，它應該負擔得起並容易維護。"},{"en":"The phrase describes places still developing economically and socially.","zh":"這個短語描述經濟和社會仍在發展的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"natural fuel factory","meaning":"天然燃料製造者","examples":[{"en":"Mr Flynn describes a cow as a natural fuel factory.","zh":"Flynn 先生把牛形容為天然燃料製造者。"},{"en":"A natural fuel factory is a humorous way to say that an animal naturally produces material that can be used as fuel.","zh":"「natural fuel factory」是一種幽默說法，意思是動物自然產生可作燃料的材料。"},{"en":"A farmer may joke that cows are natural fuel factories when dried dung is used for cooking fires.","zh":"當乾牛糞用作煮食燃料時，農民可能開玩笑說牛是天然燃料製造者。"},{"en":"If manure can replace wood or gas, cattle become a source of useful energy.","zh":"如果糞便能取代木材或煤氣，牛隻就成為有用能源來源。"},{"en":"The phrase is metaphorical but points to a practical fuel source.","zh":"這個短語是比喻，但指向實際燃料來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"my understanding is that","meaning":"據我理解","examples":[{"en":"My understanding is that cow dung burns similarly in different regions.","zh":"據我理解，牛糞在不同地區燃燒方式相似。"},{"en":"My understanding is that means “as far as I know” or “based on what I believe”.","zh":"「my understanding is that」意思是「據我所知」或「根據我的理解」。"},{"en":"My understanding is that the school will announce the exam timetable next week.","zh":"據我理解，學校下星期會公布考試時間表。"},{"en":"If someone is not completely certain, this phrase makes the statement sound careful.","zh":"如果某人並非百分百肯定，這個短語會令說法顯得謹慎。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a cautious personal understanding.","zh":"這個短語引入謹慎的個人理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pretty much the same","meaning":"差不多一樣","examples":[{"en":"Cow dung should be pretty much the same wherever it is found.","zh":"無論在哪裏找到，牛糞應該差不多一樣。"},{"en":"Pretty much the same means almost the same, with no important difference.","zh":"「pretty much the same」意思是幾乎一樣，沒有重要差別。"},{"en":"The two worksheets are pretty much the same, except for a few examples.","zh":"兩份工作紙差不多一樣，只是有幾個例子不同。"},{"en":"If the fuel is similar everywhere, the method can work in many regions.","zh":"如果燃料在各地都相似，該方法就能在許多地區運作。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and means “nearly identical”.","zh":"這個短語較口語，意思是「幾乎相同」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"wherever you find it","meaning":"無論在哪裏找到它","examples":[{"en":"The fuel should work similarly wherever you find it.","zh":"無論在哪裏找到它，這種燃料應該以相似方式運作。"},{"en":"Wherever you find it means in any place where it is found.","zh":"「wherever you find it」意思是在任何找到它的地方。"},{"en":"Clean sand has similar basic features wherever you find it, though quality may vary.","zh":"無論在哪裏找到，乾淨沙的基本特徵相似，雖然質素可能不同。"},{"en":"If cow dung works wherever it is found, the filter process is easier to transfer.","zh":"如果牛糞無論在哪裏找到都能運作，濾水器製作過程就更容易轉移。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that location should not make a major difference.","zh":"這個短語強調地點不應造成重大差別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"domestic uses","meaning":"家居用途","examples":[{"en":"Manure has long been used as a fuel for domestic uses.","zh":"糞便長久以來被用作家居用途的燃料。"},{"en":"Domestic uses are uses inside the home or for ordinary household needs.","zh":"「domestic uses」是在家中或普通家庭需要上的用途。"},{"en":"Gas has domestic uses such as cooking, heating water, and warming rooms.","zh":"煤氣有煮食、加熱水和暖房等家居用途。"},{"en":"If a fuel is already used at home, people may accept it more easily for simple production.","zh":"如果燃料已在家中使用，人們可能更容易接受它用於簡單生產。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts household use with industrial use.","zh":"這個短語把家庭用途與工業用途作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not a new idea","meaning":"並非新概念","examples":[{"en":"Using manure as a fuel is not a new idea.","zh":"使用糞便作燃料並非新概念。"},{"en":"Not a new idea means the idea has existed or been used before.","zh":"「not a new idea」意思是該想法以前已存在或被使用過。"},{"en":"Online learning was not a new idea before it became common during school closures.","zh":"網上學習在停課期間普及之前，並非新概念。"},{"en":"If an idea is old, a new invention may still use it in a clever new way.","zh":"如果想法很舊，新發明仍可能以巧妙新方式使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase rejects the claim that something is completely original.","zh":"這個短語否定某事完全原創的說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"porosity of clay","meaning":"黏土的多孔性","examples":[{"en":"Potters have understood the porosity of clay for many years.","zh":"陶藝師多年來已了解黏土的多孔性。"},{"en":"Porosity of clay means the presence of tiny holes or spaces inside clay.","zh":"「porosity of clay」意思是黏土內有細小孔洞或空隙。"},{"en":"A porous flowerpot lets some air and water move through its walls.","zh":"多孔花盆讓一些空氣和水穿過其器壁。"},{"en":"If clay has the right porosity, water can pass through while larger particles are blocked.","zh":"如果黏土有合適多孔性，水可以通過，而較大微粒會被阻隔。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a key physical property of clay.","zh":"這個短語描述黏土的一項關鍵物理特性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ceramics lecturer","meaning":"陶瓷學講師","examples":[{"en":"Mr Flynn was formerly a ceramics lecturer.","zh":"Flynn 先生以前是陶瓷學講師。"},{"en":"A ceramics lecturer is a teacher at a college or university who teaches the making and science of clay objects.","zh":"「ceramics lecturer」是在學院或大學教授黏土物件製作和科學的老師。"},{"en":"A ceramics lecturer may show students how firing temperature changes clay.","zh":"陶瓷學講師可能向學生示範燒製溫度如何改變黏土。"},{"en":"If someone has taught ceramics, they may understand clay properties very well.","zh":"如果有人教過陶瓷學，他可能非常了解黏土特性。"},{"en":"The phrase names an academic teacher in pottery and ceramic materials.","zh":"這個短語指出陶藝和陶瓷材料方面的學術教師。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be well aware of","meaning":"十分了解……","examples":[{"en":"As a former lecturer, he was well aware of clay’s properties.","zh":"作為前講師，他十分了解黏土的特性。"},{"en":"To be well aware of something means to know it clearly and fully.","zh":"「be well aware of」某事，意思是清楚而充分知道它。"},{"en":"Experienced teachers are well aware of the mistakes students often make.","zh":"經驗豐富的老師十分了解學生常犯的錯誤。"},{"en":"If a scientist is well aware of a material’s weakness, they may turn it into an advantage.","zh":"如果科學家十分了解材料弱點，他可能把它轉化為優勢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong awareness, not vague knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈認知，而不是模糊知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rather than viewing","meaning":"與其把……視為……","examples":[{"en":"Rather than viewing porosity as a problem, he used it as an advantage.","zh":"與其把多孔性視為問題，他把它用作優勢。"},{"en":"Rather than viewing something in one way means instead of seeing it that way.","zh":"「rather than viewing」某事為某物，意思是不是以那種方式看待它。"},{"en":"Rather than viewing mistakes as failure, students can use them as clues for improvement.","zh":"與其把錯誤視為失敗，學生可以把它們用作改善線索。"},{"en":"If a weakness is viewed differently, it may become part of the solution.","zh":"如果弱點被以不同方式看待，它可能成為解決方案的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a contrast between two ways of thinking.","zh":"這個短語引出兩種思考方式之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"porous nature","meaning":"多孔性質","examples":[{"en":"The filter depends on the porous nature of fired clay.","zh":"這款濾水器依靠燒製黏土的多孔性質。"},{"en":"Porous nature means the quality of having many tiny holes that allow liquid or air to pass through.","zh":"「porous nature」意思是具有許多細小孔洞，讓液體或空氣通過的特性。"},{"en":"A sponge has a porous nature because it absorbs water through many tiny spaces.","zh":"海綿具有多孔性質，因為它透過許多細小空隙吸水。"},{"en":"If fired clay is porous, it can let water pass slowly while blocking larger organisms.","zh":"如果燒製黏土多孔，它可以讓水慢慢通過，同時阻隔較大微生物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a material’s hole-filled structure.","zh":"這個短語描述材料充滿孔洞的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"after all","meaning":"畢竟","examples":[{"en":"After all, ordinary pots are normally expected to hold water.","zh":"畢竟，普通陶罐通常被期望能盛水。"},{"en":"After all introduces a reason that supports or explains what was just said.","zh":"「after all」引出支持或解釋剛才說法的理由。"},{"en":"Bring an umbrella; after all, the weather report says it may rain.","zh":"帶傘吧；畢竟，天氣報告說可能下雨。"},{"en":"If clay pots usually hold water, using porous clay as a filter seems unusual at first.","zh":"如果黏土陶罐通常用來盛水，把多孔黏土用作濾水器起初似乎不尋常。"},{"en":"The phrase often means “when you think about it”.","zh":"這個短語常表示「仔細想想」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hold water","meaning":"盛水；不漏水","examples":[{"en":"A normal cooking pot must be able to hold water.","zh":"普通煮食鍋必須能夠盛水。"},{"en":"To hold water literally means to contain water without leaking.","zh":"「hold water」字面意思是盛載水而不漏出。"},{"en":"A cracked cup cannot hold water because liquid runs out through the crack.","zh":"裂開的杯不能盛水，因為液體會從裂縫流出。"},{"en":"If ordinary pots must hold water, potters usually try to reduce porosity.","zh":"如果普通陶罐必須盛水，陶藝師通常會嘗試減少多孔性。"},{"en":"The phrase here refers to physical ability to contain liquid.","zh":"這個短語在這裡指物理上盛載液體的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"capitalise on","meaning":"充分利用……","examples":[{"en":"The filters capitalise on the porous nature of clay.","zh":"這些濾水器充分利用黏土的多孔性質。"},{"en":"To capitalise on something means to use it to gain an advantage.","zh":"「capitalise on」某事，意思是利用它取得優勢。"},{"en":"A student may capitalise on strong vocabulary by writing more precise essays.","zh":"學生可能充分利用強大詞彙，寫出更精準的作文。"},{"en":"If a material’s weakness is useful in another context, designers can turn it into a strength.","zh":"如果材料的弱點在另一語境中有用，設計者可以把它變成優勢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making good use of an existing feature.","zh":"這個短語描述善用現有特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"commercial ceramic filters","meaning":"商用陶瓷濾水器","examples":[{"en":"Other commercial ceramic filters are already available.","zh":"其他商用陶瓷濾水器已經可買到。"},{"en":"Commercial ceramic filters are clay-based water filters made and sold by companies.","zh":"「commercial ceramic filters」是由公司製造和銷售的陶瓷濾水器。"},{"en":"A shop may sell commercial ceramic filters for households that want cleaner water.","zh":"商店可能售賣商用陶瓷濾水器給想要更潔淨食水的家庭。"},{"en":"If commercial filters are too expensive, poor families may need a cheaper local alternative.","zh":"如果商用濾水器太昂貴，貧困家庭可能需要較便宜的本地替代品。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts market products with homemade or community-made filters.","zh":"這個短語把市場產品與自製或社區製濾水器作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"even if available","meaning":"即使可以買到","examples":[{"en":"Even if available locally, commercial filters may be too expensive.","zh":"即使本地可以買到，商用濾水器也可能太昂貴。"},{"en":"Even if available means although something can be obtained.","zh":"「even if available」意思是雖然某物可以取得。"},{"en":"Even if a tutor is available, some families may not be able to afford lessons.","zh":"即使可以找到補習老師，有些家庭也可能負擔不起課程。"},{"en":"If a product exists but costs too much, availability alone does not solve the problem.","zh":"如果產品存在但價格太高，單是可以取得並不能解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a contrast between access and practical usefulness.","zh":"這個短語引出取得與實際可用性之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"prices starting at","meaning":"價格由……起","examples":[{"en":"Commercial filters have prices starting at five US dollars each.","zh":"商用濾水器價格由每個五美元起。"},{"en":"Prices starting at a certain amount means the lowest price begins at that amount.","zh":"「prices starting at」某金額，意思是最低價格由該金額開始。"},{"en":"A café may advertise lunch sets with prices starting at 50 dollars.","zh":"咖啡店可能宣傳午餐套餐價格由50元起。"},{"en":"If the starting price is already high for poor families, the product remains unaffordable.","zh":"如果起始價格對貧困家庭來說已經很高，產品仍然負擔不起。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the minimum cost, not necessarily the average cost.","zh":"這個短語提供最低成本，而不一定是平均成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"outside the budgets of","meaning":"超出……的預算","examples":[{"en":"Commercial filters are outside the budgets of many families.","zh":"商用濾水器超出許多家庭的預算。"},{"en":"Outside the budgets of someone means too expensive for them to afford.","zh":"「outside the budgets of」某人，意思是對他們來說太昂貴，負擔不起。"},{"en":"A new laptop may be outside the budget of a student who works part-time.","zh":"新手提電腦可能超出兼職學生的預算。"},{"en":"If a health product costs too much, people may go without it even when they need it.","zh":"如果健康產品太貴，人們即使需要也可能不用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something financially out of reach.","zh":"這個短語描述財政上負擔不起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"filtration process","meaning":"過濾過程","examples":[{"en":"The filtration process is simple but effective.","zh":"過濾過程簡單但有效。"},{"en":"A filtration process is the method by which water or liquid passes through a material to remove unwanted substances.","zh":"「filtration process」是水或液體穿過材料以清除不需要物質的方法。"},{"en":"A coffee machine uses a filtration process when water passes through ground coffee and paper.","zh":"咖啡機中水穿過咖啡粉和濾紙時，就是使用過濾過程。"},{"en":"If the filtration process blocks pathogens, the water becomes safer to drink.","zh":"如果過濾過程阻隔病原體，水就變得更安全可飲用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how filtering happens.","zh":"這個短語描述過濾如何發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"basic principle","meaning":"基本原理","examples":[{"en":"The basic principle is that water can pass through tiny passages.","zh":"基本原理是水可以通過細小通道。"},{"en":"A basic principle is the main simple idea that explains how something works.","zh":"「basic principle」是解釋某事如何運作的主要簡單想法。"},{"en":"The basic principle of saving money is spending less than you earn.","zh":"儲錢的基本原理是花費少於收入。"},{"en":"If students understand the basic principle, they can remember the details more easily.","zh":"如果學生理解基本原理，就更容易記住細節。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the core idea behind a process.","zh":"這個短語指出過程背後的核心想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"passages through the filter","meaning":"穿過濾水器的通道","examples":[{"en":"There are narrow passages through the filter’s walls.","zh":"濾水器器壁中有狹窄通道。"},{"en":"Passages through the filter are tiny routes that allow water to move from one side to the other.","zh":"「passages through the filter」是讓水從一邊移到另一邊的細小路徑。"},{"en":"A sponge has small passages through which water can move.","zh":"海綿有讓水通過的小通道。"},{"en":"If the passages are the right size, water passes through but many germs cannot.","zh":"如果通道大小合適，水能通過，但許多細菌不能通過。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the small internal paths in a filter.","zh":"這個短語描述濾水器內部的小路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"wide enough for","meaning":"闊度足以讓……","examples":[{"en":"The passages are wide enough for water droplets to pass through.","zh":"這些通道闊度足以讓水滴通過。"},{"en":"Wide enough for something means having enough space for that thing to fit or move through.","zh":"「wide enough for」某物，意思是有足夠空間讓該物放入或通過。"},{"en":"A doorway must be wide enough for a wheelchair to pass through.","zh":"門口必須闊度足以讓輪椅通過。"},{"en":"If filter passages are wide enough for water but not germs, filtration can work.","zh":"如果濾水器通道闊度足以讓水通過但不讓細菌通過，過濾就能運作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sufficient width for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述為某目的而有足夠寬度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"water droplets","meaning":"水滴","examples":[{"en":"Water droplets move slowly through the clay walls.","zh":"水滴慢慢穿過黏土器壁。"},{"en":"Water droplets are tiny drops of water.","zh":"「water droplets」是細小的水珠。"},{"en":"After rain, water droplets may remain on leaves and windows.","zh":"下雨後，水滴可能留在葉子和窗戶上。"},{"en":"If droplets pass slowly through clay, the filter has time to block larger organisms.","zh":"如果水滴慢慢穿過黏土，濾水器就有時間阻隔較大微生物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes small individual drops of water.","zh":"這個短語描述單一細小水珠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pass through","meaning":"穿過；通過","examples":[{"en":"Clean water can pass through the filter’s small openings.","zh":"潔淨水可以穿過濾水器的小開口。"},{"en":"To pass through something means to move from one side of it to the other.","zh":"「pass through」某物，意思是從它的一邊移到另一邊。"},{"en":"Light can pass through clear glass but not through a thick wall.","zh":"光可以穿過透明玻璃，但不能穿過厚牆。"},{"en":"If water can pass through clay while germs cannot, the filter separates them.","zh":"如果水可以穿過黏土而細菌不能，濾水器就把它們分開。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement through an opening or material.","zh":"這個短語描述穿過開口或材料的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"too narrow for","meaning":"太狹窄而不能讓……","examples":[{"en":"The passages are too narrow for most pathogens to pass through.","zh":"這些通道太狹窄，不能讓大多數病原體通過。"},{"en":"Too narrow for something means not wide enough for that thing to enter or move through.","zh":"「too narrow for」某物，意思是不夠闊讓該物進入或通過。"},{"en":"A gap under a door may be too narrow for a large envelope.","zh":"門底縫隙可能太窄，不能讓大型信封通過。"},{"en":"If passages are too narrow for germs, they become trapped instead of entering the clean water.","zh":"如果通道太窄，病菌不能通過，它們就會被困住而不進入潔淨水。"},{"en":"The phrase explains blocking by small size.","zh":"這個短語解釋透過細小尺寸阻隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deadly bacterium","meaning":"致命細菌","examples":[{"en":"E. coli can be a deadly bacterium.","zh":"大腸桿菌可以是致命細菌。"},{"en":"A deadly bacterium is a bacterium that can cause severe illness or death.","zh":"「deadly bacterium」是可以造成嚴重疾病或死亡的細菌。"},{"en":"Hospitals take deadly bacteria seriously because they can spread to vulnerable patients.","zh":"醫院嚴肅處理致命細菌，因為它們可以傳播給脆弱病人。"},{"en":"If drinking water contains deadly bacteria, treatment is urgently needed.","zh":"如果飲用水含有致命細菌，就急需處理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a dangerous disease-causing bacterium.","zh":"這個短語描述危險的致病細菌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"remove 96.4 to 99.8 per cent of","meaning":"清除百分之96.4至99.8的……","examples":[{"en":"The filters remove 96.4 to 99.8 per cent of E. coli.","zh":"這些濾水器清除百分之96.4至99.8的大腸桿菌。"},{"en":"To remove 96.4 to 99.8 per cent of something means to take away almost all of it.","zh":"「remove 96.4 to 99.8 per cent of」某物，意思是清除幾乎全部該物。"},{"en":"A good air purifier may remove a high percentage of dust from a small room.","zh":"好空氣清新機可能從小房間中清除高比例灰塵。"},{"en":"If a filter removes nearly all bacteria, the remaining amount may be low enough to be safe.","zh":"如果濾水器清除幾乎所有細菌，剩餘量可能低到安全水平。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a precise measure of effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語提供有效性的精確量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"well within safe levels","meaning":"遠低於危險水平","examples":[{"en":"The amount of bacteria remaining is well within safe levels.","zh":"剩餘細菌量遠低於危險水平。"},{"en":"Well within safe levels means clearly below the amount considered dangerous.","zh":"「well within safe levels」意思是明顯低於被視為危險的數量。"},{"en":"A swimming pool’s chlorine level should stay within safe levels for children.","zh":"游泳池的氯含量應保持在兒童安全水平內。"},{"en":"If bacteria are well within safe levels, the water is much less likely to cause disease.","zh":"如果細菌量遠低於危險水平，水造成疾病的可能性就低得多。"},{"en":"The phrase reassures readers that the remaining amount is acceptable.","zh":"這個短語讓讀者放心，剩餘數量是可接受的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"filter a litre of water","meaning":"過濾一公升水","examples":[{"en":"One filter takes about two hours to filter a litre of water.","zh":"一個濾水器大約需要兩小時過濾一公升水。"},{"en":"To filter a litre of water means to clean one litre of water by passing it through a filter.","zh":"「filter a litre of water」意思是讓一公升水通過濾水器以清潔它。"},{"en":"A camper may filter a litre of water before cooking dinner.","zh":"露營者可能在煮晚餐前過濾一公升水。"},{"en":"If filtering one litre takes two hours, families must plan water use ahead of time.","zh":"如果過濾一公升水需要兩小時，家庭就必須提前規劃用水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both the amount of water and the filtering action.","zh":"這個短語同時描述水量和過濾動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"burn away after firing","meaning":"燒製後燃燒消失","examples":[{"en":"The organic material burns away after firing.","zh":"有機材料在燒製後燃燒消失。"},{"en":"To burn away after firing means to disappear because it is burned during the heating process.","zh":"「burn away after firing」意思是在加熱過程中因燃燒而消失。"},{"en":"Paper placed in a hot fire will burn away and leave ash.","zh":"紙張放入烈火中會燃燒消失並留下灰。"},{"en":"If organic material burns away inside clay, empty spaces are left behind.","zh":"如果有機材料在黏土內燃燒消失，就會留下空隙。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how pores form in the fired filter.","zh":"這個短語解釋燒製後濾水器孔洞如何形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"produce the structure","meaning":"形成所需結構","examples":[{"en":"Burning the organic material helps produce the filter’s porous structure.","zh":"燃燒有機材料有助形成濾水器的多孔結構。"},{"en":"To produce the structure means to create the physical arrangement or form of something.","zh":"「produce the structure」意思是形成某物的物理排列或形態。"},{"en":"Steel beams help produce the structure of a strong building.","zh":"鋼樑有助形成堅固建築物的結構。"},{"en":"If burning leaves tiny spaces, it creates the structure needed for filtration.","zh":"如果燃燒留下細小空隙，它就形成過濾所需結構。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how the form of an object is made.","zh":"這個短語集中於物件形態如何形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"become trapped","meaning":"被困住","examples":[{"en":"Pathogens become trapped inside the narrow passages.","zh":"病原體被困在狹窄通道內。"},{"en":"To become trapped means to be caught and unable to move through or escape.","zh":"「become trapped」意思是被困住，無法通過或逃出。"},{"en":"A coin may become trapped under a heavy cupboard.","zh":"硬幣可能被困在沉重櫃子底下。"},{"en":"If pathogens become trapped in the filter, they cannot pass into the clean water.","zh":"如果病原體被困在濾水器中，它們就不能進入潔淨水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being blocked and held in place.","zh":"這個短語描述被阻隔並留在原處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"overcome potential problems","meaning":"克服潛在問題","examples":[{"en":"The addition of organic material overcomes potential problems with fine clay.","zh":"加入有機材料克服了較細密黏土的潛在問題。"},{"en":"To overcome potential problems means to solve difficulties that could happen.","zh":"「overcome potential problems」意思是解決可能發生的困難。"},{"en":"A teacher may overcome potential problems in a school trip by preparing backup transport.","zh":"老師可能透過準備後備交通來克服學校旅行的潛在問題。"},{"en":"If fine clay blocks water flow, adding organic material can create pores and solve the issue.","zh":"如果細密黏土阻礙水流，加入有機材料可以形成孔洞並解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preventing or solving likely difficulties.","zh":"這個短語描述預防或解決可能出現的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"finer clays","meaning":"較細密的黏土","examples":[{"en":"Finer clays may prevent water from flowing through the filter.","zh":"較細密的黏土可能阻止水流過濾水器。"},{"en":"Finer clays are clays made of very small particles packed closely together.","zh":"「finer clays」是由非常細小顆粒緊密排列組成的黏土。"},{"en":"A potter may use finer clay for smooth bowls because it gives a clean surface.","zh":"陶藝師可能用較細密黏土製作光滑碗，因為它表面較乾淨。"},{"en":"If clay particles are too fine, the spaces between them may be too small for water flow.","zh":"如果黏土顆粒太細，顆粒之間的空隙可能太小，不能讓水流動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes clay texture and particle size.","zh":"這個短語描述黏土質地和顆粒大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"let water through","meaning":"讓水通過","examples":[{"en":"Clay that is too fine may not let water through.","zh":"太細密的黏土可能不讓水通過。"},{"en":"To let water through means to allow water to pass from one side to another.","zh":"「let water through」意思是容許水從一邊通過到另一邊。"},{"en":"A good umbrella should not let water through during heavy rain.","zh":"好雨傘在大雨中不應讓水通過。"},{"en":"If filter walls do not let water through, the device cannot work as a filter.","zh":"如果濾水器器壁不讓水通過，裝置就不能作為濾水器運作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes allowing water to pass.","zh":"這個短語描述容許水通過。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cracks are halted","meaning":"裂縫受到阻止","examples":[{"en":"The porous structure means that cracks are soon halted.","zh":"多孔結構意味着裂縫很快受到阻止。"},{"en":"If cracks are halted, they stop spreading further through the material.","zh":"如果「cracks are halted」，意思是裂縫停止在材料中繼續延伸。"},{"en":"A small tear in fabric may be halted by sewing a patch over it.","zh":"布料上的小裂口可以透過縫上一塊補丁而被阻止擴大。"},{"en":"If pores interrupt a crack, the pot may be less likely to split completely.","zh":"如果孔洞中斷裂縫，陶罐可能較不容易完全裂開。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stopping damage from spreading.","zh":"這個短語描述阻止損害擴散。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"universally available","meaning":"全球各地都可取得","examples":[{"en":"Organic materials are universally available.","zh":"有機材料在全球各地都可取得。"},{"en":"Universally available means available almost everywhere or to almost everyone.","zh":"「universally available」意思是幾乎所有地方或幾乎所有人都能取得。"},{"en":"Sunlight is universally available in many outdoor learning activities, though weather varies.","zh":"在許多戶外學習活動中，陽光大致上各地可得，雖然天氣不同。"},{"en":"If materials are universally available, the method can be used in many communities.","zh":"如果材料全球各地都可取得，該方法就能在許多社區使用。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses very broad availability.","zh":"這個短語強調非常廣泛的可取得性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be born out of","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"The invention was born out of a World Vision project.","zh":"這項發明源自一個世界宣明會項目。"},{"en":"To be born out of something means to develop as a result of it.","zh":"「be born out of」某事，意思是因它而發展出來。"},{"en":"A school recycling club may be born out of students’ concern about waste.","zh":"學校回收學會可能源自學生對浪費的關注。"},{"en":"If a project reveals a local problem, a useful invention may grow from that need.","zh":"如果項目揭示本地問題，有用發明可能從該需要中產生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an origin or source.","zh":"這個短語描述起源或來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"World Vision project","meaning":"世界宣明會項目","examples":[{"en":"The original research formed part of a World Vision project.","zh":"最初研究是世界宣明會項目的一部分。"},{"en":"A World Vision project is a charity project organised by World Vision to support communities in need.","zh":"「World Vision project」是由世界宣明會組織、支援有需要社區的慈善項目。"},{"en":"A World Vision project may focus on clean water, child health, education, or local livelihoods.","zh":"世界宣明會項目可能集中於潔淨食水、兒童健康、教育或本地生計。"},{"en":"If a charity project works with local people, it can produce solutions that match local materials.","zh":"如果慈善項目與本地人合作，它可以產生配合本地材料的解決方案。"},{"en":"The phrase names the development project behind the research.","zh":"這個短語指出該研究背後的發展項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Manatuto community","meaning":"東帝汶 Manatuto 社區","examples":[{"en":"The project involved the Manatuto community in East Timor.","zh":"該項目涉及東帝汶 Manatuto 社區。"},{"en":"The Manatuto community refers to people living in the Manatuto area of East Timor.","zh":"「Manatuto community」指居住在東帝汶 Manatuto 地區的人。"},{"en":"A community project may train local residents to make and repair useful products.","zh":"社區項目可能訓練本地居民製作和維修有用產品。"},{"en":"If the Manatuto community can manufacture filters locally, families may gain safer water and income.","zh":"如果 Manatuto 社區能在本地製造濾水器，家庭可能獲得更安全食水和收入。"},{"en":"The phrase names the local community involved in the project.","zh":"這個短語指出參與該項目的本地社區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"East Timor","meaning":"東帝汶","examples":[{"en":"The first ceramic filters were developed in East Timor.","zh":"首批陶瓷濾水器在東帝汶研發。"},{"en":"East Timor is a country in Southeast Asia also known as Timor-Leste.","zh":"「East Timor」是東南亞一個國家，也稱 Timor-Leste。"},{"en":"A development project in East Timor may focus on water, health, or local employment.","zh":"東帝汶的發展項目可能集中於食水、健康或本地就業。"},{"en":"If a method works in East Timor using local materials, it may inspire use in other places.","zh":"如果方法能使用東帝汶本地材料運作，它可能啟發其他地方使用。"},{"en":"The phrase names the country where the early filter work took place.","zh":"這個短語指出早期濾水器工作發生的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"charity","meaning":"慈善機構","examples":[{"en":"The charity wanted to support a small local industry.","zh":"該慈善機構想支持一個本地小型產業。"},{"en":"A charity is an organisation that helps people, communities, animals, or causes without aiming mainly for profit.","zh":"慈善機構是幫助人、社區、動物或公益目的，而不主要追求利潤的組織。"},{"en":"A charity may provide food, medical help, education, or emergency support.","zh":"慈善機構可能提供食物、醫療幫助、教育或緊急支援。"},{"en":"If a charity supports local production, the community may gain both useful goods and jobs.","zh":"如果慈善機構支持本地生產，社區可能同時獲得有用產品和工作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an organisation working for public benefit.","zh":"這個短語指為公共利益工作的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"help set up","meaning":"協助成立","examples":[{"en":"World Vision wanted to help set up a local manufacturing industry.","zh":"世界宣明會想協助成立本地製造產業。"},{"en":"To help set up something means to assist in starting or establishing it.","zh":"「help set up」某事，意思是協助開始或建立它。"},{"en":"Teachers may help set up a reading club by finding books and inviting students.","zh":"老師可能透過找書和邀請學生來協助成立閱讀學會。"},{"en":"If a charity helps set up an industry, local people may continue it after the project ends.","zh":"如果慈善機構協助成立產業，項目結束後本地人可能繼續營運。"},{"en":"The phrase describes support during the beginning stage.","zh":"這個短語描述在起始階段提供支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"small industry","meaning":"小型產業","examples":[{"en":"The project aimed to create a small industry in the community.","zh":"該項目旨在社區中創造一個小型產業。"},{"en":"A small industry is a local business activity that produces goods or services on a limited scale.","zh":"「small industry」是在有限規模上生產貨品或服務的本地商業活動。"},{"en":"A village may build a small industry around making soap, baskets, or food products.","zh":"村莊可能圍繞製作肥皂、籃子或食品建立小型產業。"},{"en":"If a small industry succeeds, it can create jobs and meet local needs.","zh":"如果小型產業成功，它可以創造工作並滿足本地需要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes local production that is modest but economically useful.","zh":"這個短語描述規模不大但具經濟用途的本地生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"manufacture water filters","meaning":"製造濾水器","examples":[{"en":"The community planned to manufacture water filters locally.","zh":"該社區計劃在本地製造濾水器。"},{"en":"To manufacture water filters means to make water filters in an organised production process.","zh":"「manufacture water filters」意思是以有組織的生產過程製作濾水器。"},{"en":"A local workshop may manufacture water filters using clay and simple tools.","zh":"本地工作坊可能使用黏土和簡單工具製造濾水器。"},{"en":"If a community manufactures filters itself, it can reduce dependence on imported products.","zh":"如果社區自己製造濾水器，它可以減少對進口產品的依賴。"},{"en":"The phrase describes producing filters for use or sale.","zh":"這個短語描述為使用或銷售而生產濾水器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"initial research","meaning":"初步研究","examples":[{"en":"Initial research found that the local clay was too fine.","zh":"初步研究發現本地黏土太細密。"},{"en":"Initial research is the first stage of study done to understand a problem or test an idea.","zh":"「initial research」是為理解問題或測試想法而進行的第一階段研究。"},{"en":"Initial research for a school project may involve interviews and basic reading.","zh":"學校專題的初步研究可能包括訪問和基本閱讀。"},{"en":"If initial research finds a problem, the design may need to change.","zh":"如果初步研究發現問題，設計可能需要改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes early investigation before a final solution.","zh":"這個短語描述最終解決方案前的早期調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"local clay","meaning":"本地黏土","examples":[{"en":"The local clay did not initially produce an effective filter.","zh":"本地黏土最初未能製成有效濾水器。"},{"en":"Local clay is clay found in the nearby area rather than imported from elsewhere.","zh":"「local clay」是在附近地區找到，而不是從別處進口的黏土。"},{"en":"Potters often use local clay because it is cheaper and easier to obtain.","zh":"陶藝師常使用本地黏土，因為它較便宜和容易取得。"},{"en":"If local clay is too fine, water may not flow through the filter properly.","zh":"如果本地黏土太細密，水可能無法正確流過濾水器。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises using materials available in the community.","zh":"這個短語強調使用社區可取得的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be too fine","meaning":"太細密","examples":[{"en":"The clay was too fine to allow enough water through.","zh":"黏土太細密，不能讓足夠的水通過。"},{"en":"To be too fine means to have particles that are too small or tightly packed for the purpose.","zh":"「be too fine」意思是顆粒太小或排列太緊密，不適合該目的。"},{"en":"Flour that is too fine may create a texture different from coarse flour.","zh":"太細的麵粉可能產生與粗麵粉不同的質感。"},{"en":"If clay is too fine, the spaces between particles may be too narrow for water flow.","zh":"如果黏土太細密，顆粒之間的空隙可能太窄，不能讓水流動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a material being too smooth or dense for the intended use.","zh":"這個短語描述材料對預定用途而言太幼滑或太密實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be solved by the addition of","meaning":"透過加入……解決","examples":[{"en":"The problem was solved by the addition of organic material.","zh":"該問題透過加入有機材料解決。"},{"en":"To be solved by the addition of something means the problem is fixed because that thing is added.","zh":"「be solved by the addition of」某物，意思是因加入該物而解決問題。"},{"en":"A soup that tastes flat may be improved by the addition of a little salt.","zh":"味道淡的湯可能透過加入少量鹽而改善。"},{"en":"If organic material creates pores in fine clay, the water-flow problem can be solved.","zh":"如果有機材料在細密黏土中形成孔洞，水流問題就可以解決。"},{"en":"The phrase links the solution directly to adding a material.","zh":"這個短語把解決方法直接連到加入材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"working ceramic filter","meaning":"能正常運作的陶瓷濾水器","examples":[{"en":"The researchers successfully produced a working ceramic filter.","zh":"研究人員成功製成能正常運作的陶瓷濾水器。"},{"en":"A working ceramic filter is a clay-based filter that actually functions as intended.","zh":"「working ceramic filter」是實際能按預期運作的陶瓷濾水器。"},{"en":"A school science project is successful when students build a working model, not just a drawing.","zh":"學校科學專題在學生製成可運作模型，而不只是畫圖時才算成功。"},{"en":"If the ceramic filter lets water through and blocks pathogens, it is working properly.","zh":"如果陶瓷濾水器讓水通過並阻隔病原體，它就是正常運作。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the filter is functional, not just experimental.","zh":"這個短語強調濾水器具功能，而不只是實驗品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"overcome a problem","meaning":"克服問題","examples":[{"en":"The team overcame the problems involved in producing the filter.","zh":"團隊克服了製作濾水器涉及的問題。"},{"en":"To overcome a problem means to find a way to deal with it successfully.","zh":"「overcome a problem」意思是找到方法成功處理問題。"},{"en":"A student may overcome a pronunciation problem by practising with recordings every day.","zh":"學生可能透過每天跟錄音練習來克服發音問題。"},{"en":"If researchers solve the clay problem, the filter can finally work.","zh":"如果研究人員解決黏土問題，濾水器最終可以運作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes defeating a difficulty through effort or a solution.","zh":"這個短語描述透過努力或方案戰勝困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"kiln-based solution","meaning":"以窯爐為基礎的方案","examples":[{"en":"The original solution was kiln-based.","zh":"最初方案是以窯爐為基礎的。"},{"en":"A kiln-based solution is a method that depends on using a kiln.","zh":"「kiln-based solution」是依賴使用窯爐的方法。"},{"en":"A ceramics class often uses a kiln-based solution for hardening student pottery.","zh":"陶藝課通常使用以窯爐為基礎的方案來燒硬學生陶器。"},{"en":"If a solution depends on a kiln, it may not work in communities without such equipment.","zh":"如果方案依賴窯爐，它可能不適用於沒有該設備的社區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a method built around kiln use.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞窯爐使用而建立的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be particular to","meaning":"只適用於……","examples":[{"en":"The original method was particular to the community’s materials.","zh":"原本方法只適用於該社區的材料。"},{"en":"To be particular to something means to be specific to it and not easily shared by others.","zh":"「be particular to」某事，意思是只針對它，並不容易被其他地方共用。"},{"en":"A school rule may be particular to one campus because its building layout is unusual.","zh":"某校規可能只適用於一個校園，因為其建築布局很特別。"},{"en":"If a method depends on one community’s special clay, it may not work elsewhere.","zh":"如果方法依賴某社區的特殊黏土，它可能不適用於其他地方。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something limited to a specific situation.","zh":"這個短語描述只限於特定情況的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be applied elsewhere","meaning":"應用於其他地方","examples":[{"en":"The original production method could not easily be applied elsewhere.","zh":"原本生產方法不容易應用於其他地方。"},{"en":"To be applied elsewhere means to be used in another place or situation.","zh":"「be applied elsewhere」意思是在另一個地方或情況中使用。"},{"en":"A teaching method used in one class may be applied elsewhere if students have similar needs.","zh":"如果學生需要相似，一班使用的教學方法可能應用於其他地方。"},{"en":"If a process requires local conditions that others lack, it is hard to apply elsewhere.","zh":"如果過程需要其他地方沒有的本地條件，就難以應用於其他地方。"},{"en":"The phrase describes transferring a method to a new context.","zh":"這個短語描述把方法轉移到新語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"manure firing","meaning":"以牛糞燒製","examples":[{"en":"Manure firing removed the need for an expensive kiln.","zh":"以牛糞燒製消除了對昂貴陶窯的需要。"},{"en":"Manure firing is the process of using burning manure to fire clay objects.","zh":"「manure firing」是使用燃燒中的糞便燒製黏土物件的過程。"},{"en":"A village pottery project may use manure firing when wood and gas are too costly.","zh":"當木材和煤氣太昂貴時，村莊陶器項目可能使用牛糞燒製。"},{"en":"If manure firing reaches high enough temperatures, it can replace kiln firing for simple filters.","zh":"如果牛糞燒製達到足夠高溫，它可以為簡單濾水器取代窯爐燒製。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a low-technology firing method.","zh":"這個短語描述低科技燒製方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"no requirement for","meaning":"無需……","examples":[{"en":"The new process has no requirement for a kiln.","zh":"這個新過程無需陶窯。"},{"en":"No requirement for something means that thing is not needed.","zh":"「no requirement for」某物，意思是不需要該物。"},{"en":"An online form may have no requirement for printing or posting documents.","zh":"網上表格可能無需列印或郵寄文件。"},{"en":"If there is no requirement for a kiln, communities save money and training time.","zh":"如果無需陶窯，社區就節省金錢和培訓時間。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly states that a usual tool or condition is unnecessary.","zh":"這個短語清楚說明通常的工具或條件並非必要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"zero-technology approach","meaning":"零科技方案","examples":[{"en":"Manure firing created a zero-technology approach.","zh":"以牛糞燒製創造了一種零科技方案。"},{"en":"A zero-technology approach is a method that uses almost no modern machines or advanced equipment.","zh":"「zero-technology approach」是幾乎不使用現代機器或先進設備的方法。"},{"en":"Teaching outdoors with stones and sticks can be a zero-technology approach to basic counting.","zh":"用石頭和木枝在戶外教基本數數，可以是零科技教學方法。"},{"en":"If a water filter method uses no complex technology, it can be taught in remote areas.","zh":"如果濾水器方法不使用複雜科技，它可以在偏遠地區教授。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses extreme simplicity and independence from machines.","zh":"這個短語強調極度簡單和不依賴機器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be available anywhere","meaning":"可在任何地方使用","examples":[{"en":"The zero-technology approach can be made available anywhere.","zh":"這種零科技方案可在任何地方使用。"},{"en":"To be available anywhere means to be usable or obtainable in any place.","zh":"「be available anywhere」意思是在任何地方都能使用或取得。"},{"en":"A phone app with offline notes can be available anywhere, even without internet.","zh":"有離線筆記的手機應用程式可在任何地方使用，即使沒有網絡。"},{"en":"If a method depends only on common materials, it can spread to many places.","zh":"如果方法只依賴常見材料，它就能傳到許多地方。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises wide practical access.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛實際可及性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"all the components","meaning":"所有組成材料","examples":[{"en":"All the components needed for the filter are widely available.","zh":"濾水器所需的所有組成材料都廣泛可取得。"},{"en":"All the components means every part or material needed to make something.","zh":"「all the components」意思是製作某物所需的每一個部分或材料。"},{"en":"A computer will not work properly unless all the components are connected.","zh":"除非所有組件都連接好，電腦不會正常運作。"},{"en":"If all the components are local and cheap, production becomes much easier.","zh":"如果所有組成材料都是本地且便宜，生產就容易得多。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the complete set of required parts.","zh":"這個短語指所需部分的完整組合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"widely available","meaning":"廣泛可取得","examples":[{"en":"The materials are widely available throughout developing countries.","zh":"這些材料在發展中國家各地廣泛可取得。"},{"en":"Widely available means easy to find or obtain in many places.","zh":"「widely available」意思是在許多地方容易找到或取得。"},{"en":"Rice is widely available in many Asian communities.","zh":"米在許多亞洲社區廣泛可取得。"},{"en":"If materials are widely available, transport and supply costs are lower.","zh":"如果材料廣泛可取得，運輸和供應成本會較低。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad access, not rarity.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛可接觸，而不是稀有。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"there is no reason why","meaning":"沒有理由……不能……","examples":[{"en":"There is no reason why the method could not be used elsewhere.","zh":"沒有理由這種方法不能在其他地方使用。"},{"en":"There is no reason why means there seems to be nothing stopping something from happening.","zh":"「there is no reason why」意思是似乎沒有東西阻止某事發生。"},{"en":"There is no reason why students cannot improve if they practise regularly and get feedback.","zh":"如果學生定期練習並得到回饋，沒有理由不能進步。"},{"en":"If all materials are common, there is no clear barrier to using the method in other places.","zh":"如果所有材料都常見，就沒有明顯障礙阻止該方法在其他地方使用。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses confidence that something should be possible.","zh":"這個短語表達對某事應該可行的信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be applied throughout","meaning":"在……各地應用","examples":[{"en":"The technology could be applied throughout the developing world.","zh":"這項技術可以在整個發展中地區應用。"},{"en":"To be applied throughout an area means to be used across the whole area or in many places within it.","zh":"「be applied throughout」某地，意思是在整個地區或其中許多地方使用。"},{"en":"A successful reading programme may be applied throughout a school district.","zh":"成功閱讀計劃可能在整個校區應用。"},{"en":"If a method is simple and cheap, it can be applied in many communities.","zh":"如果方法簡單且便宜，它可以在許多社區應用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad use across a region.","zh":"這個短語描述在某區域廣泛使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have no plans to patent","meaning":"無意為……申請專利","examples":[{"en":"Mr Flynn has no plans to patent his idea.","zh":"Flynn 先生無意為他的意念申請專利。"},{"en":"To have no plans to patent something means not to intend to claim legal ownership over the invention.","zh":"「have no plans to patent」某物，意思是不打算對該發明主張法律擁有權。"},{"en":"A teacher may share a worksheet freely and have no plans to copyright it for sale.","zh":"老師可能免費分享工作紙，並無意為出售而申請版權。"},{"en":"If an inventor does not patent an idea, others may copy and use it more easily.","zh":"如果發明者不為意念申請專利，其他人可能更容易複製和使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a deliberate choice not to restrict use legally.","zh":"這個短語顯示刻意不在法律上限制使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"patent an idea","meaning":"為意念申請專利","examples":[{"en":"He deliberately chose not to patent the filter design.","zh":"他刻意選擇不為濾水器設計申請專利。"},{"en":"To patent an idea means to get legal protection that gives the inventor rights over it.","zh":"「patent an idea」意思是取得法律保護，讓發明者擁有其權利。"},{"en":"A company may patent an idea before selling a new medical device.","zh":"公司可能在銷售新醫療裝置前為意念申請專利。"},{"en":"If an idea is patented, other people may need permission to use it commercially.","zh":"如果意念已申請專利，其他人可能需要許可才能商業使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes legally protecting an invention or design.","zh":"這個短語描述在法律上保護發明或設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"legal obstacles","meaning":"法律障礙","examples":[{"en":"There will be no legal obstacles to communities adopting the design.","zh":"社區採用該設計將不會有法律障礙。"},{"en":"Legal obstacles are laws, rights, or official rules that make an action difficult or impossible.","zh":"「legal obstacles」是令行動困難或不可能的法律、權利或官方規則。"},{"en":"A school may face legal obstacles if it wants to use copyrighted material without permission.","zh":"如果學校想未經許可使用受版權保護材料，可能面對法律障礙。"},{"en":"If no patent blocks the design, communities can copy it freely.","zh":"如果沒有專利阻擋該設計，社區就可以自由複製它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes legal barriers to action.","zh":"這個短語描述行動上的法律阻礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be adopted in","meaning":"在……被採用","examples":[{"en":"The design can be adopted in any community that needs it.","zh":"這個設計可以在任何需要它的社區被採用。"},{"en":"To be adopted in a place means to be accepted and used there.","zh":"「be adopted in」某地，意思是在那裡被接受和使用。"},{"en":"A new teaching method may be adopted in several schools after successful trials.","zh":"新教學方法成功試行後，可能在幾所學校被採用。"},{"en":"If a filter design is cheap and effective, villages may begin using it quickly.","zh":"如果濾水器設計便宜且有效，村莊可能很快開始使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a method becoming accepted in a setting.","zh":"這個短語描述方法在某環境中被接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have a right to","meaning":"有權獲得……","examples":[{"en":"Everyone has a right to clean water.","zh":"每個人都有權獲得潔淨食水。"},{"en":"To have a right to something means to deserve it morally, legally, or socially.","zh":"「have a right to」某物，意思是在道德、法律或社會上應該得到它。"},{"en":"Children have a right to basic education and safety.","zh":"孩子有權獲得基本教育和安全。"},{"en":"If people have a right to clean water, technology should help them access it affordably.","zh":"如果人們有權獲得潔淨食水，科技應幫助他們以可負擔方式取得。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something people should be allowed or able to have.","zh":"這個短語描述人們應被允許或能夠擁有的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have the potential to","meaning":"有潛力去……","examples":[{"en":"The filters have the potential to improve millions of lives.","zh":"這些濾水器有潛力改善數百萬人的生活。"},{"en":"To have the potential to do something means to be able to do it in the future if used well.","zh":"「have the potential to」做某事，意思是如果運用得好，將來有能力做到它。"},{"en":"A shy student may have the potential to become a strong speaker with practice.","zh":"害羞學生經過練習後，可能有潛力成為出色演講者。"},{"en":"If a cheap filter spreads widely, it could reduce water-borne disease for many families.","zh":"如果廉價濾水器廣泛傳播，它可以為許多家庭減少水源性疾病。"},{"en":"The phrase describes future possibility, not guaranteed success.","zh":"這個短語描述未來可能性，而不是保證成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"enable someone to","meaning":"使某人能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The filters could enable people to drink water safely.","zh":"這些濾水器可以使人們能夠安全飲水。"},{"en":"To enable someone to do something means to make it possible for them to do it.","zh":"「enable someone to」做某事，意思是使某人有可能做到該事。"},{"en":"Online lessons enable students in remote areas to learn from specialist teachers.","zh":"網上課程使偏遠地區學生能夠向專科老師學習。"},{"en":"If a filter removes pathogens, it enables families to use local water more safely.","zh":"如果濾水器清除病原體，它就使家庭能夠更安全地使用本地水。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a tool or action with new ability.","zh":"這個短語把工具或行動與新能力連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"drink water safely","meaning":"安全地飲用食水","examples":[{"en":"The invention could enable anyone to drink water safely.","zh":"這項發明可以使任何人安全地飲用食水。"},{"en":"To drink water safely means to drink water without a high risk of infection or illness.","zh":"「drink water safely」意思是在沒有高感染或患病風險下飲水。"},{"en":"Hikers use water treatment tablets so they can drink stream water safely.","zh":"遠足者使用淨水片，讓他們可以安全飲用溪水。"},{"en":"If water contains dangerous bacteria, people cannot drink it safely until it is filtered or boiled.","zh":"如果水含有危險細菌，人們在過濾或煮沸前不能安全飲用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes safe human consumption of water.","zh":"這個短語描述人類安全飲用水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"complete the flow chart","meaning":"完成流程圖","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the flow chart using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的詞語完成流程圖。"},{"en":"To complete the flow chart means to fill in missing steps in a process diagram.","zh":"「complete the flow chart」意思是填寫流程圖中缺失的步驟。"},{"en":"In a science lesson, students may complete a flow chart showing how rain forms.","zh":"在科學課中，學生可能完成顯示雨如何形成的流程圖。"},{"en":"If a flow chart is completed correctly, the order of steps becomes clear.","zh":"如果流程圖正確完成，步驟次序就變得清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction for process information.","zh":"這個短語是關於過程資料的常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個詞","examples":[{"en":"Each answer must contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案必須包含不多於兩個詞。"},{"en":"No more than two words means one or two words only, not three or more.","zh":"「no more than two words」意思是只可一個或兩個詞，不可三個或更多。"},{"en":"If the answer is “cow manure”, it fits a two-word limit.","zh":"如果答案是 “cow manure”，它符合兩詞限制。"},{"en":"If students write extra words, the answer may be marked wrong even when the idea is correct.","zh":"如果學生寫多了詞，即使意思正確，答案也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語在考試指示中給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"guide to making","meaning":"……的製作指南","examples":[{"en":"The flow chart provides a guide to making water filters.","zh":"流程圖提供濾水器的製作指南。"},{"en":"A guide to making something is a set of instructions that explains how to produce it.","zh":"「guide to making」某物，是解釋如何製作它的一套指示。"},{"en":"A cooking book gives a guide to making soup, bread, and simple meals.","zh":"食譜書提供製作湯、麵包和簡單餐點的指南。"},{"en":"If a guide is clear, people can follow the steps without expert help.","zh":"如果指南清楚，人們不用專家幫助也能跟隨步驟。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical instructions for production.","zh":"這個短語描述製作某物的實用指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"combine A and B","meaning":"把A和B混合","examples":[{"en":"The first step is to combine clay and organic material.","zh":"第一步是把黏土和有機材料混合。"},{"en":"To combine A and B means to put two things together so they form a mixture or work as one.","zh":"「combine A and B」意思是把兩物放在一起，使它們形成混合物或共同運作。"},{"en":"A student can combine pictures and short notes to make revision easier.","zh":"學生可以把圖片和簡短筆記混合使用，使溫習更容易。"},{"en":"If clay and organic material are combined, the final filter can become porous after firing.","zh":"如果黏土和有機材料混合，最終濾水器在燒製後可以變得多孔。"},{"en":"The phrase describes joining two elements for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述為某目的結合兩個元素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"sufficient water","meaning":"足夠的水","examples":[{"en":"The producer adds sufficient water to make a thick mixture.","zh":"製作者加入足夠的水來製成濃稠混合物。"},{"en":"Sufficient water means enough water for the intended purpose.","zh":"「sufficient water」意思是達到預定目的所需的足夠水量。"},{"en":"A plant needs sufficient water to grow, but too much water can damage its roots.","zh":"植物需要足夠的水生長，但太多水可能損害根部。"},{"en":"If the clay mixture lacks sufficient water, it may be too dry to shape.","zh":"如果黏土混合物缺乏足夠水分，它可能太乾而不能塑形。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an adequate amount, not too little.","zh":"這個短語描述足夠的量，而不是太少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"create a thick mixture","meaning":"製成濃稠混合物","examples":[{"en":"The ingredients are combined to create a thick mixture.","zh":"這些材料被混合以製成濃稠混合物。"},{"en":"To create a thick mixture means to make a dense mixture that is not watery or runny.","zh":"「create a thick mixture」意思是製成濃密、不稀水的混合物。"},{"en":"A cook adds flour to sauce to create a thick mixture.","zh":"廚師在醬汁中加入麵粉來製成濃稠混合物。"},{"en":"If the mixture is thick enough, it can be shaped into a pot.","zh":"如果混合物足夠濃稠，它就可以被塑形成陶罐。"},{"en":"The phrase describes achieving the right texture for shaping.","zh":"這個短語描述達到適合塑形的質感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"shape the mixture","meaning":"將混合物塑形","examples":[{"en":"The producer shapes the mixture into a cylinder.","zh":"製作者將混合物塑形成圓柱體。"},{"en":"To shape the mixture means to press or form it into a particular shape.","zh":"「shape the mixture」意思是把混合物壓成或製成特定形狀。"},{"en":"Children shape clay into animals during an art lesson.","zh":"孩子在美術課中把黏土塑形成動物。"},{"en":"If the mixture is shaped evenly, the finished filter may work more consistently.","zh":"如果混合物塑形均勻，完成的濾水器可能運作更穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes turning soft material into a planned form.","zh":"這個短語描述把柔軟材料變成計劃形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"pack straw around","meaning":"把稻草塞在……周圍","examples":[{"en":"Straw is packed around the clay cylinders.","zh":"稻草被塞在黏土圓柱體周圍。"},{"en":"To pack straw around something means to place straw tightly around it.","zh":"「pack straw around」某物，意思是把稻草緊密放在它周圍。"},{"en":"Farmers may pack straw around young plants to protect them from cold.","zh":"農民可能把稻草塞在幼苗周圍，以保護它們免受寒冷。"},{"en":"If straw is packed around the clay, it can help the fire start close to the filters.","zh":"如果稻草塞在黏土周圍，它可以幫助火在濾水器附近開始燃燒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes surrounding an object with straw.","zh":"這個短語描述用稻草圍住物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"clay cylinders","meaning":"黏土圓柱體","examples":[{"en":"The clay cylinders are surrounded with straw before firing.","zh":"黏土圓柱體在燒製前被稻草圍住。"},{"en":"Clay cylinders are tube-like or pot-like clay shapes with circular sides.","zh":"「clay cylinders」是像管狀或陶罐狀、有圓形側面的黏土形狀。"},{"en":"Students may make clay cylinders in pottery class before turning them into cups.","zh":"學生在陶藝課中可能先製作黏土圓柱體，再把它們變成杯。"},{"en":"If clay cylinders are dried and fired, they can become hard ceramic objects.","zh":"如果黏土圓柱體被曬乾和燒製，它們可以變成堅硬陶瓷物件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the shaped clay pieces before they become finished filters.","zh":"這個短語描述成為完成濾水器前已塑形的黏土件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be used as fuel for firing","meaning":"被用作燒製燃料","examples":[{"en":"Cow manure is used as fuel for firing the filters.","zh":"牛糞被用作燒製濾水器的燃料。"},{"en":"To be used as fuel for firing means to be burned to provide heat for hardening clay.","zh":"「be used as fuel for firing」意思是被燃燒以提供硬化黏土所需熱力。"},{"en":"Wood is often used as fuel for firing traditional pottery.","zh":"木材常被用作燒製傳統陶器的燃料。"},{"en":"If cow manure is used as fuel, communities may avoid buying gas or wood.","zh":"如果牛糞被用作燃料，社區可能避免購買煤氣或木材。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the material burned during the ceramic heating process.","zh":"這個短語描述陶瓷加熱過程中被燃燒的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"maximum temperature","meaning":"最高溫度","examples":[{"en":"The fuel can reach a maximum temperature of about 950 degrees.","zh":"燃料可以達到約950度的最高溫度。"},{"en":"Maximum temperature is the highest temperature reached or allowed.","zh":"「maximum temperature」是達到或容許的最高溫度。"},{"en":"A classroom thermometer may record the maximum temperature during a hot afternoon.","zh":"課室溫度計可能記錄炎熱下午的最高溫度。"},{"en":"If the fuel reaches a high maximum temperature, it can fire clay effectively.","zh":"如果燃料達到高最高溫度，它可以有效燒製黏土。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the upper heat level.","zh":"這個短語描述熱度上限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be baked in under","meaning":"在少於……內燒製完成","examples":[{"en":"The filters can be baked in under an hour.","zh":"這些濾水器可以在少於一小時內燒製完成。"},{"en":"To be baked in under a certain time means to be heated and finished before that time has passed.","zh":"「be baked in under」某時間，意思是在該時間過去前被加熱並完成。"},{"en":"Small biscuits can be baked in under twenty minutes.","zh":"小餅乾可以在少於二十分鐘內焗好。"},{"en":"If filters can be baked in under an hour, production is faster than kiln firing.","zh":"如果濾水器可在少於一小時內燒製完成，生產就比窯燒更快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes quick completion by heating.","zh":"這個短語描述透過加熱快速完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與文章資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否與文章一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information means to match what the text says.","zh":"「agree with the information」意思是符合文本所說。"},{"en":"In a reading exercise, students must check exact evidence before marking an answer true.","zh":"在閱讀練習中，學生標示答案為真之前必須檢查準確證據。"},{"en":"If a statement adds a detail not found in the passage, it may not agree with the information.","zh":"如果陳述加入文章沒有的細節，它可能不與資料一致。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds students to rely on the text.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生依靠文本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文章資料相反","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相反。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"「contradict the information」意思是說出與文章內容相反的東西。"},{"en":"If the passage says the method is cheap, saying it is expensive contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說方法便宜，說它昂貴就與資料相反。"},{"en":"When a statement contradicts the text, the answer should not be TRUE.","zh":"當陳述與文本相反，答案就不應是 TRUE。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a direct conflict with the passage.","zh":"這個短語描述與文章直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students write “NOT GIVEN” when there is no relevant information.","zh":"當文中沒有相關資料時，學生寫 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not tell us about that point.","zh":"「there is no information on this」意思是文章沒有告訴我們該點。"},{"en":"If an article never mentions the inventor’s favourite food, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文章從未提及發明家最喜歡的食物，文中就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"When no evidence is given, students should not guess from common sense.","zh":"當沒有證據時，學生不應憑常識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when a statement cannot be checked from the text.","zh":"這個短語用於陳述無法從文本核實的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reach 950 degrees","meaning":"達到950度","examples":[{"en":"The manure can eventually reach a temperature of 950 degrees.","zh":"牛糞最終可以達到950度。"},{"en":"To reach 950 degrees means to heat up until the temperature is 950 degrees.","zh":"「reach 950 degrees」意思是加熱至溫度為950度。"},{"en":"A kiln may need to reach a very high temperature before clay becomes hard.","zh":"陶窯可能需要達到很高溫度，黏土才會變硬。"},{"en":"If cow manure reaches 950 degrees, it can provide enough heat for firing filters.","zh":"如果牛糞達到950度，它可以提供足夠熱力來燒製濾水器。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reaching a specific high heat level.","zh":"這個短語描述達到特定高溫水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"initially be found to be unsuitable","meaning":"最初被發現並不合適","examples":[{"en":"The local clay was initially found to be unsuitable on its own.","zh":"本地黏土最初被發現單獨使用並不合適。"},{"en":"To initially be found to be unsuitable means early tests showed it did not work well for the purpose.","zh":"「initially be found to be unsuitable」意思是早期測試顯示它不適合該目的。"},{"en":"A classroom may initially be found unsuitable for exams if it is too noisy.","zh":"如果課室太嘈吵，它最初可能被發現不適合作考試場地。"},{"en":"If a material fails early tests, researchers may add something to improve it.","zh":"如果材料未能通過早期測試，研究人員可能加入某物來改善它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an early negative finding.","zh":"這個短語描述早期負面發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"twice as effective as","meaning":"效果是……的兩倍","examples":[{"en":"The statement claims that coffee grounds are twice as effective as other materials.","zh":"該陳述聲稱咖啡渣的效果是其他材料的兩倍。"},{"en":"Twice as effective as means producing double the useful result compared with something else.","zh":"「twice as effective as」意思是相比另一物，產生兩倍有用效果。"},{"en":"A study method may be twice as effective as another if students remember twice as many words.","zh":"如果學生記得兩倍詞語，一種學習方法的效果可能是另一種的兩倍。"},{"en":"If one material is twice as effective, researchers may prefer it for production.","zh":"如果一種材料效果是兩倍，研究人員可能較喜歡用它來生產。"},{"en":"The phrase makes a strong numerical comparison of effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語對效果作強烈數字比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"difficult bacterium to combat","meaning":"難以對付的細菌","examples":[{"en":"Some bacteria are particularly difficult to combat.","zh":"有些細菌特別難以對付。"},{"en":"A difficult bacterium to combat is a bacterium that is hard to remove, kill, or control.","zh":"「difficult bacterium to combat」是難以清除、殺死或控制的細菌。"},{"en":"Hospitals worry about bacteria that are difficult to combat because they may resist treatment.","zh":"醫院擔心難以對付的細菌，因為它們可能抗拒治療。"},{"en":"If a filter removes a hard-to-combat bacterium, it may be especially useful.","zh":"如果濾水器能清除難以對付的細菌，它可能特別有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a microorganism that is hard to fight.","zh":"這個短語描述難以處理的微生物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"thickness of the wall","meaning":"器壁厚度","examples":[{"en":"The thickness of the wall affects the filter’s performance.","zh":"器壁厚度影響濾水器的表現。"},{"en":"Thickness of the wall means how thick the side of the pot or filter is.","zh":"「thickness of the wall」意思是陶罐或濾水器側壁有多厚。"},{"en":"A paper cup with greater wall thickness may keep drinks warm longer.","zh":"器壁較厚的紙杯可能讓飲品保溫更久。"},{"en":"If the filter wall is too thick, water may pass too slowly; if too thin, it may break.","zh":"如果濾水器器壁太厚，水可能通過太慢；如果太薄，可能破裂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an important physical measurement.","zh":"這個短語描述重要的物理量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"let pathogens pass","meaning":"讓病原體通過","examples":[{"en":"A successful filter must not let pathogens pass through it.","zh":"成功的濾水器不能讓病原體通過。"},{"en":"To let pathogens pass means to allow disease-causing organisms to move through.","zh":"「let pathogens pass」意思是容許致病微生物通過。"},{"en":"A broken mask may let dust or germs pass if it has large gaps.","zh":"如果口罩有大縫隙，可能讓灰塵或細菌通過。"},{"en":"If a water filter lets pathogens pass, the water may still cause illness.","zh":"如果濾水器讓病原體通過，水仍可能造成疾病。"},{"en":"The phrase describes failure to block harmful microorganisms.","zh":"這個短語描述未能阻隔有害微生物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"vary according to","meaning":"按……而有所不同","examples":[{"en":"The wall thickness does not vary according to the fuel temperature.","zh":"器壁厚度不會按燃料溫度而有所不同。"},{"en":"To vary according to something means to change depending on it.","zh":"「vary according to」某事，意思是取決於它而改變。"},{"en":"Homework time may vary according to the student’s age and workload.","zh":"功課時間可能按學生年齡和工作量而有所不同。"},{"en":"If filter thickness varied with temperature, producers would need to adjust measurements each time.","zh":"如果濾水器厚度隨溫度而變，製作者每次都需要調整量度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes change based on a condition.","zh":"這個短語描述基於條件而改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the same thickness as","meaning":"與……厚度相同","examples":[{"en":"The wall should be approximately the same thickness as an adult’s forefinger.","zh":"器壁應大約與成年人的食指厚度相同。"},{"en":"The same thickness as means having about equal width from one side to the other.","zh":"「the same thickness as」意思是由一邊到另一邊的厚度大約相等。"},{"en":"A slice of cake may be cut the same thickness as a phone.","zh":"一片蛋糕可能切成與電話厚度相同。"},{"en":"If a filter wall matches a familiar thickness, local makers can judge it without measuring tools.","zh":"如果濾水器器壁配合熟悉厚度，本地製作者不用量度工具也能判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase compares thickness with something known.","zh":"這個短語把厚度與已知物件比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"adult’s forefinger","meaning":"成年人的食指","examples":[{"en":"The passage compares the wall thickness with an adult’s forefinger.","zh":"文章把器壁厚度與成年人的食指比較。"},{"en":"An adult’s forefinger is the index finger of a grown person.","zh":"「adult’s forefinger」是成年人的食指。"},{"en":"A craft instruction may use an adult’s forefinger as a rough guide for thickness.","zh":"手工指示可能用成年人的食指作為厚度粗略參考。"},{"en":"If the wall is about this thick, the filter may balance strength and water flow.","zh":"如果器壁大約這麼厚，濾水器可能在強度與水流之間取得平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase provides a simple, body-based measurement.","zh":"這個短語提供簡單的身體量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be mentioned by","meaning":"由……提及","examples":[{"en":"The correct wall thickness is mentioned by Mr Flynn.","zh":"正確器壁厚度由 Flynn 先生提及。"},{"en":"To be mentioned by someone means to be stated or referred to by that person.","zh":"「be mentioned by」某人，意思是由該人說出或提到。"},{"en":"A homework deadline mentioned by the teacher should be written down carefully.","zh":"老師提及的功課限期應仔細記下。"},{"en":"If a detail is mentioned by the inventor, it may be important for the process.","zh":"如果細節由發明者提及，它可能對過程很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who gave the information.","zh":"這個短語指出誰提供資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"statement about the charity","meaning":"關於該慈善機構的陳述","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which statement about the charity is accurate.","zh":"問題問哪項關於該慈善機構的陳述是準確的。"},{"en":"A statement about the charity is a sentence giving information or an opinion about the charity.","zh":"「statement about the charity」是提供關於該慈善機構資料或意見的句子。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students check whether a statement about an organisation matches the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生檢查關於機構的陳述是否符合文章。"},{"en":"If the passage says the charity supported local industry, another claim must be checked against that fact.","zh":"如果文章說慈善機構支持本地產業，另一說法就必須與該事實核對。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an exam statement focused on the charity.","zh":"這個短語指以該慈善機構為焦點的考試陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"fail to find suitable materials","meaning":"未能找到合適材料","examples":[{"en":"The project did not completely fail to find suitable materials.","zh":"該項目並沒有完全未能找到合適材料。"},{"en":"To fail to find suitable materials means to be unable to locate materials that work for the purpose.","zh":"「fail to find suitable materials」意思是無法找到適合該目的的材料。"},{"en":"A student may fail to find suitable materials for a model bridge if only weak paper is available.","zh":"如果只有脆弱紙張可用，學生可能未能找到製作模型橋的合適材料。"},{"en":"If local clay alone is unsuitable, adding organic material may still solve the problem.","zh":"如果本地黏土單獨使用不合適，加入有機材料仍可能解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an unsuccessful search for workable materials.","zh":"這個短語描述尋找可用材料不成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"manufacture for sale worldwide","meaning":"製造並在全球出售","examples":[{"en":"The original kiln-based filter was not manufactured for sale worldwide.","zh":"原本以窯爐為基礎的濾水器並沒有被製造並在全球出售。"},{"en":"To manufacture for sale worldwide means to produce goods so they can be sold across the world.","zh":"「manufacture for sale worldwide」意思是生產貨品，使它們可在全球出售。"},{"en":"A phone company may manufacture a new model for sale worldwide after testing it locally.","zh":"電話公司本地測試新型號後，可能製造並在全球出售。"},{"en":"If a filter is only a local project, it may not be produced for global commercial sale.","zh":"如果濾水器只是本地項目，它可能不是為全球商業銷售而生產。"},{"en":"The phrase describes large-scale international production and selling.","zh":"這個短語描述大規模國際生產和銷售。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"establish a local industry","meaning":"建立本地產業","examples":[{"en":"The charity intended to help establish a local water-filter industry.","zh":"該慈善機構打算協助建立本地濾水器產業。"},{"en":"To establish a local industry means to create a business activity in a community or region.","zh":"「establish a local industry」意思是在社區或地區中創造商業生產活動。"},{"en":"A village may establish a local industry by training residents to make handmade products.","zh":"村莊可能透過訓練居民製作手工產品來建立本地產業。"},{"en":"If a local industry grows, people can earn income without leaving the community.","zh":"如果本地產業增長，人們不用離開社區也能賺取收入。"},{"en":"The phrase describes building production and jobs locally.","zh":"這個短語描述在本地建立生產和工作機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"deliberately not patent","meaning":"刻意不申請專利","examples":[{"en":"Mr Flynn is deliberately not patenting the filter design.","zh":"Flynn 先生刻意不為濾水器設計申請專利。"},{"en":"To deliberately not patent something means to intentionally avoid claiming legal ownership over it.","zh":"「deliberately not patent」某物，意思是有意避免對它主張法律擁有權。"},{"en":"A teacher may deliberately not copyright materials so other teachers can use them freely.","zh":"老師可能刻意不為教材申請版權，使其他老師可自由使用。"},{"en":"If an inventor avoids patenting a life-saving design, communities can copy it without paying fees.","zh":"如果發明者避免為救命設計申請專利，社區就可以不用付費而複製。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the choice is intentional.","zh":"這個短語強調該選擇是有意識的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be used freely","meaning":"可自由使用","examples":[{"en":"The design can be used freely by communities around the world.","zh":"這個設計可由世界各地社區自由使用。"},{"en":"To be used freely means to be used without payment, permission barriers, or legal restrictions.","zh":"「be used freely」意思是可在沒有付款、許可障礙或法律限制下使用。"},{"en":"Open educational materials can be used freely by teachers and students.","zh":"開放教育材料可由老師和學生自由使用。"},{"en":"If a filter design can be used freely, poor communities can adopt it more easily.","zh":"如果濾水器設計可自由使用，貧困社區就更容易採用它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unrestricted practical use.","zh":"這個短語描述不受限制的實際使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"around the world","meaning":"世界各地","examples":[{"en":"The inventor hopes the design will be adopted around the world.","zh":"發明者希望這個設計會在世界各地被採用。"},{"en":"Around the world means in many countries or places across the globe.","zh":"「around the world」意思是在全球許多國家或地方。"},{"en":"Students around the world use the internet to learn languages.","zh":"世界各地學生使用互聯網學習語言。"},{"en":"If a design spreads around the world, it can help many different communities.","zh":"如果設計傳播到世界各地，它可以幫助許多不同社區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes global reach.","zh":"這個短語描述全球範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"sufficiently refined","meaning":"足夠完善","examples":[{"en":"The technology is simple but sufficiently refined to filter water safely.","zh":"這項技術簡單，但足夠完善，可以安全過濾食水。"},{"en":"Sufficiently refined means developed or improved enough to work well for its purpose.","zh":"「sufficiently refined」意思是已發展或改善到足以有效達成目的。"},{"en":"A lesson plan may be simple but sufficiently refined to help students practise clearly.","zh":"課堂計劃可以簡單但足夠完善，幫助學生清楚練習。"},{"en":"If a design is refined enough, it can be safe even without complex equipment.","zh":"如果設計足夠完善，即使沒有複雜設備也可以安全。"},{"en":"The phrase balances simplicity with effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語平衡簡單與有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"prevent someone from doing something","meaning":"阻止某人做某事","examples":[{"en":"No legal obstacles should prevent communities from using the design.","zh":"不應有法律障礙阻止社區使用這個設計。"},{"en":"To prevent someone from doing something means to stop them from doing it.","zh":"「prevent someone from doing something」意思是阻止某人做某事。"},{"en":"Heavy rain may prevent students from playing football after school.","zh":"大雨可能阻止學生放學後踢足球。"},{"en":"If patents prevent communities from copying a filter, the invention may help fewer people.","zh":"如果專利阻止社區複製濾水器，該發明可能幫助較少人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something blocking an action.","zh":"這個短語描述某物阻礙一項行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be adopted widely","meaning":"被廣泛採用","examples":[{"en":"The design has the potential to be adopted widely.","zh":"這個設計有潛力被廣泛採用。"},{"en":"To be adopted widely means to be accepted and used by many people or places.","zh":"「be adopted widely」意思是被許多人或地方接受和使用。"},{"en":"A useful school app may be adopted widely if it is free and easy to use.","zh":"如果一款有用的學校應用程式免費又易用，它可能被廣泛採用。"},{"en":"If a water-filter design is cheap, effective, and unrestricted, it may spread quickly.","zh":"如果濾水器設計便宜、有效且不受限制，它可能快速傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad acceptance and use.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛接受和使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 143 - Water Filter.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 144":[{"front":"science-fiction film","meaning":"科幻電影","examples":[{"en":"Metropolis is an influential science-fiction film.","zh":"《大都會》是一部具影響力的科幻電影。"},{"en":"A science-fiction film is a movie that imagines future technology, space travel, robots, or changed societies.","zh":"科幻電影是想像未來科技、太空旅行、機械人或改變了的社會的電影。"},{"en":"Students may watch a science-fiction film to discuss how technology could affect human life.","zh":"學生可能觀看科幻電影，討論科技如何影響人類生活。"},{"en":"If a film shows robots replacing workers, it uses imagined technology to explore real fears.","zh":"如果電影展示機械人取代工人，它就是用想像科技探索真實恐懼。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a film genre based on scientific imagination, not ordinary realism.","zh":"這個短語指以科學想像為基礎的電影類型，而不是普通寫實電影。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"steadily become fact","meaning":"逐漸成為現實","examples":[{"en":"Some ideas from the film are steadily becoming fact.","zh":"電影中的一些構想正逐漸成為現實。"},{"en":"To steadily become fact means to change gradually from imagination or prediction into reality.","zh":"“Steadily become fact” 指由想像或預測逐步變成現實。"},{"en":"Video calls once sounded futuristic, but they steadily became fact as phones improved.","zh":"視像通話曾聽起來很未來，但隨着手機改善，它逐漸成為現實。"},{"en":"If a science-fiction idea appears in real life step by step, people may say it is becoming fact.","zh":"如果科幻構想一步步出現在現實生活中，人們可能說它正在成為現實。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow movement from fiction to reality.","zh":"這個短語描述由虛構慢慢走向現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"German director","meaning":"德國導演","examples":[{"en":"Fritz Lang was a highly influential German director.","zh":"Fritz Lang 是一位極具影響力的德國導演。"},{"en":"A German director is a film director from Germany or strongly associated with German cinema.","zh":"德國導演是來自德國或與德國電影緊密相關的電影導演。"},{"en":"A German director may use expressionist lighting, unusual sets, or serious social themes.","zh":"德國導演可能使用表現主義燈光、奇特佈景或嚴肅社會主題。"},{"en":"If a director’s films influence later filmmakers, their nationality becomes part of film history.","zh":"如果導演的電影影響後來電影人，其國籍就成為電影史的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies both a person’s creative role and cultural background.","zh":"這個短語同時指出一個人的創作角色和文化背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"first glimpse of","meaning":"初次看到……","examples":[{"en":"Lang’s first glimpse of the United States inspired the film.","zh":"Lang 初次看到美國，啟發了這部電影。"},{"en":"A first glimpse of something is the first brief look at it.","zh":"初次看到某物，指第一次短暫看見它。"},{"en":"A traveller’s first glimpse of a new city from the train window can be unforgettable.","zh":"旅客從火車窗初次看到新城市，可能令人難忘。"},{"en":"If a first glimpse is powerful, it may shape a person’s memory or imagination.","zh":"如果初次看到的畫面很有力量，它可能塑造一個人的記憶或想像。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an early visual impression, often before deeper knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述早期視覺印象，通常在深入了解之前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"night-time view","meaning":"夜景","examples":[{"en":"He saw a striking night-time view of the New York skyline.","zh":"他看見紐約天際線令人印象深刻的夜景。"},{"en":"A night-time view is the appearance of a place after dark, often with lights.","zh":"夜景是某地入黑後的樣貌，通常帶有燈光。"},{"en":"A family may enjoy the night-time view of a harbour from a high hotel room.","zh":"家庭可能從高層酒店房間欣賞海港夜景。"},{"en":"If city lights shine across tall buildings, the night-time view can feel dramatic.","zh":"如果城市燈光照亮高樓，夜景可以感覺富戲劇性。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on what a place looks like at night.","zh":"這個短語強調某地在夜晚的樣貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"New York skyline","meaning":"紐約天際線","examples":[{"en":"The New York skyline made a powerful impression on Lang.","zh":"紐約天際線給 Lang 留下強烈印象。"},{"en":"The New York skyline is the outline of New York’s tall buildings seen against the sky.","zh":"紐約天際線是紐約高樓映在天空背景下形成的輪廓。"},{"en":"Tourists often photograph the New York skyline from a ferry or bridge.","zh":"遊客常從渡輪或橋上拍攝紐約天際線。"},{"en":"If a skyline is full of skyscrapers, it can suggest modern power and ambition.","zh":"如果天際線充滿摩天大廈，它可以暗示現代力量和抱負。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the city’s recognisable shape formed by buildings.","zh":"這個短語指由建築形成的城市可辨認輪廓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"from the deck of","meaning":"從……的甲板上","examples":[{"en":"He viewed the city from the deck of an ocean liner.","zh":"他從遠洋客輪的甲板上觀看這座城市。"},{"en":"From the deck of a ship means from the flat open area on the ship where people can stand.","zh":"從船的甲板上，指從船上人們可以站立的平坦開放區域觀看。"},{"en":"Passengers may watch the harbour from the deck of a ferry.","zh":"乘客可能從渡輪甲板上觀看海港。"},{"en":"If someone sees a city from a ship’s deck, the skyline may appear slowly from the water.","zh":"如果某人從船甲板看城市，天際線可能從水面慢慢出現。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the viewing position on a vessel.","zh":"這個短語給出船上的觀看位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ocean liner","meaning":"遠洋客輪","examples":[{"en":"Lang arrived in the United States on an ocean liner.","zh":"Lang 乘遠洋客輪抵達美國。"},{"en":"An ocean liner is a large passenger ship designed to travel long distances across the sea.","zh":"遠洋客輪是設計用來跨海長途航行的大型客船。"},{"en":"Before air travel became common, many migrants crossed the Atlantic by ocean liner.","zh":"在航空旅行普及前，許多移民乘遠洋客輪橫渡大西洋。"},{"en":"If a director arrives by ocean liner, the first sight of a harbour city can feel cinematic.","zh":"如果導演乘遠洋客輪抵達，初見海港城市可以很有電影感。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a large ship for long sea journeys, not a small boat.","zh":"這個短語指長途海上旅程用的大型船隻，而不是小船。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"later recall","meaning":"後來回想","examples":[{"en":"Lang later recalled the moment as the inspiration for Metropolis.","zh":"Lang 後來回想那一刻是《大都會》的靈感來源。"},{"en":"To later recall something means to remember and describe it after some time has passed.","zh":"“Later recall” 某事指一段時間後記起並描述它。"},{"en":"A student may later recall a teacher’s advice when facing a difficult decision.","zh":"學生面對困難決定時，可能後來回想起老師的建議。"},{"en":"If an experience becomes important, people may recall it years later as a turning point.","zh":"如果一段經歷變得重要，人們多年後可能把它回想為轉捩點。"},{"en":"The phrase connects memory with later reflection.","zh":"這個短語把記憶與後來反思連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"direct inspiration for","meaning":"……的直接靈感來源","examples":[{"en":"The New York skyline was the direct inspiration for the film.","zh":"紐約天際線是這部電影的直接靈感來源。"},{"en":"A direct inspiration for something is the clear source that gives someone the idea to create it.","zh":"某事的直接靈感來源，是給人創作構想的清楚來源。"},{"en":"A teacher’s story may be the direct inspiration for a student’s essay.","zh":"老師的故事可能是學生作文的直接靈感來源。"},{"en":"If a city view inspires a film’s design, the real place becomes part of the film’s origin.","zh":"如果城市景觀啟發電影設計，真實地方就成為電影起源的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the immediate creative source.","zh":"這個短語指出直接的創作來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"innovative and influential","meaning":"創新而具影響力","examples":[{"en":"Metropolis remains an innovative and influential science-fiction film.","zh":"《大都會》仍是一部創新而具影響力的科幻電影。"},{"en":"Innovative and influential means new in ideas and powerful in shaping later work.","zh":"創新而具影響力指想法新穎，並有力量塑造後來作品。"},{"en":"A teaching app can be innovative and influential if many schools copy its methods.","zh":"如果許多學校模仿某教學應用程式的方法，它就可以創新而具影響力。"},{"en":"If a film invents new visual techniques, later directors may learn from it.","zh":"如果電影發明新視覺技術，後來導演可能向它學習。"},{"en":"The phrase praises both originality and long-term effect.","zh":"這個短語同時讚揚原創性和長期影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ever made","meaning":"歷來製作的","examples":[{"en":"It is one of the most influential science-fiction films ever made.","zh":"它是歷來製作的最具影響力科幻電影之一。"},{"en":"Ever made means created at any time in history up to now.","zh":"“Ever made” 指直到現在為止歷史上任何時候創作出來的。"},{"en":"Some people call it one of the best school films ever made because it still feels relevant.","zh":"有些人稱它為歷來製作的最佳校園電影之一，因為它仍然貼近現實。"},{"en":"If a work is among the greatest ever made, it is being compared with all past examples.","zh":"如果作品屬於歷來最佳之一，它就是與所有過去例子比較。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a very broad historical comparison.","zh":"這個短語給出非常廣闊的歷史比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"bleak vision of","meaning":"對……的悲觀想像","examples":[{"en":"Metropolis presents a bleak vision of the future.","zh":"《大都會》呈現對未來的悲觀想像。"},{"en":"A bleak vision of something is a dark, pessimistic or frightening picture of it.","zh":"對某事的悲觀想像，是對它黑暗、悲觀或可怕的描繪。"},{"en":"A novel may offer a bleak vision of school life if students are treated like exam machines.","zh":"如果小說把學生描寫成考試機器，它可能呈現對校園生活的悲觀想像。"},{"en":"If a future world is unequal and cruel, the vision is not hopeful.","zh":"如果未來世界不平等且殘酷，這種想像就不是充滿希望。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a negative imagined picture.","zh":"這個短語描述負面的想像畫面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the early twenty-first century","meaning":"21世紀初","examples":[{"en":"The film imagines life in the early twenty-first century.","zh":"這部電影想像21世紀初的生活。"},{"en":"The early twenty-first century means the first decades of the 2000s.","zh":"21世紀初指2000年代最初幾十年。"},{"en":"Smartphones and social media became central to daily life in the early twenty-first century.","zh":"智能手機和社交媒體在21世紀初成為日常生活核心。"},{"en":"If an old film imagined this period, viewers today can compare prediction with reality.","zh":"如果舊電影想像這個時期，今日觀眾可以比較預測與現實。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a time setting near the beginning of the 2000s.","zh":"這個短語給出2000年代初期的時間背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at once both…and…","meaning":"同時既……又……","examples":[{"en":"The future city is at once both chilling and exhilarating.","zh":"這座未來城市同時既令人不寒而慄又令人振奮。"},{"en":"At once both A and B means two different qualities are present at the same time.","zh":"“At once both A and B” 指兩種不同特質同時存在。"},{"en":"A final exam can be at once both frightening and exciting for a hardworking student.","zh":"對努力學生來說，期末考試可以同時既可怕又令人興奮。"},{"en":"If a city looks beautiful but cruel, the viewer may feel admiration and fear together.","zh":"如果城市看起來美麗但殘酷，觀眾可能同時感到欣賞和恐懼。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a strong double feeling or double quality.","zh":"這個短語突出強烈的雙重感受或雙重特質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"chilling and exhilarating","meaning":"令人不寒而慄又振奮","examples":[{"en":"The film’s vision of the future is chilling and exhilarating.","zh":"這部電影對未來的想像令人不寒而慄又振奮。"},{"en":"Chilling and exhilarating means frightening but also exciting and energising.","zh":"令人不寒而慄又振奮，指令人害怕，但同時令人興奮和充滿力量。"},{"en":"A roller coaster can be chilling and exhilarating when it drops suddenly from a great height.","zh":"過山車從高處突然下墜時，可以令人不寒而慄又振奮。"},{"en":"If a future city feels dangerous yet visually amazing, it can create both fear and thrill.","zh":"如果未來城市感覺危險卻視覺上驚人，就能同時造成恐懼和刺激。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a mixed emotional reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述混合的情緒反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"spectacular city of the future","meaning":"壯觀的未來城市","examples":[{"en":"The film presents a spectacular city of the future.","zh":"這部電影呈現一座壯觀的未來城市。"},{"en":"A spectacular city of the future is an imagined future city that looks impressive, advanced and dramatic.","zh":"壯觀的未來城市是想像中的未來城市，看起來令人印象深刻、先進而富戲劇性。"},{"en":"A game may show a spectacular city of the future with flying trains and glowing towers.","zh":"遊戲可能展示有飛行列車和發光高塔的壯觀未來城市。"},{"en":"If a city looks spectacular, viewers may admire it even while fearing its social problems.","zh":"如果城市看起來壯觀，觀眾即使害怕其社會問題，也可能欣賞它。"},{"en":"The phrase combines futuristic setting with visual greatness.","zh":"這個短語結合未來背景與視覺宏偉感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"technological marvel","meaning":"科技奇觀","examples":[{"en":"Metropolis is depicted as a technological marvel.","zh":"《大都會》被描繪成科技奇觀。"},{"en":"A technological marvel is something so advanced or impressive that people admire its technology.","zh":"科技奇觀是非常先進或令人印象深刻、使人讚嘆其科技的事物。"},{"en":"A modern hospital robot may be seen as a technological marvel if it performs delicate surgery.","zh":"如果現代醫院機械人能進行精細手術，它可能被視為科技奇觀。"},{"en":"If a city has airships, elevated trains and huge towers, it may appear technologically amazing.","zh":"如果一座城市有飛船、高架列車和巨塔，它可能顯得科技上驚人。"},{"en":"The phrase praises impressive technical achievement.","zh":"這個短語讚揚令人印象深刻的技術成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"high-rise buildings","meaning":"高樓大廈","examples":[{"en":"The city contains enormous high-rise buildings.","zh":"這座城市有巨大的高樓大廈。"},{"en":"High-rise buildings are very tall buildings with many floors.","zh":"高樓大廈是有很多樓層的非常高的建築物。"},{"en":"Office workers may travel by lift every morning in high-rise buildings.","zh":"辦公室員工每天早上可能在高樓大廈中乘升降機。"},{"en":"If a city has many high-rise buildings, its skyline can look dense and modern.","zh":"如果城市有許多高樓大廈，其天際線可以顯得密集而現代。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to tall urban architecture.","zh":"這個短語指高大的城市建築。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be connected by","meaning":"由……連接","examples":[{"en":"The high-rise buildings are connected by elevated railways.","zh":"這些高樓大廈由高架鐵路連接。"},{"en":"To be connected by something means to be linked through a road, bridge, railway or system.","zh":"“Be connected by” 某物指透過道路、橋樑、鐵路或系統連接起來。"},{"en":"Two school buildings may be connected by a covered walkway.","zh":"兩座校舍可能由有蓋通道連接。"},{"en":"If buildings are connected by railways, people can move between them without using streets below.","zh":"如果建築物由鐵路連接，人們就能不使用下方街道而往返其間。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the link between separate places.","zh":"這個短語解釋分離地方之間的連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"elevated railways","meaning":"高架鐵路","examples":[{"en":"Elevated railways connect the buildings above the city.","zh":"高架鐵路在城市上方連接建築物。"},{"en":"Elevated railways are train lines built above ground level on raised structures.","zh":"高架鐵路是建在地面以上、由高架結構支撐的鐵路線。"},{"en":"Some cities use elevated railways to reduce traffic on crowded streets.","zh":"有些城市使用高架鐵路來減少擁擠街道上的交通。"},{"en":"If trains run above the roads, the city can feel layered and futuristic.","zh":"如果列車在道路上方行駛，城市可以感覺有層次而具未來感。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to rail transport raised above ordinary street level.","zh":"這個短語指高於普通街道水平的鐵路交通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"airships","meaning":"飛船","examples":[{"en":"Airships move through the skies above Metropolis.","zh":"飛船在《大都會》上空移動。"},{"en":"Airships are large aircraft that float in the air, usually using gas-filled bodies.","zh":"飛船是在空中漂浮的大型航空器，通常使用充氣船體。"},{"en":"An old postcard may show airships above a city as a symbol of future travel.","zh":"舊明信片可能展示城市上空的飛船，作為未來交通的象徵。"},{"en":"If airships fill the sky, the film world feels advanced and unusual.","zh":"如果天空充滿飛船，電影世界就感覺先進而奇特。"},{"en":"The word refers to lighter-than-air flying vehicles.","zh":"這個詞指比空氣輕的飛行器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"extreme inequality","meaning":"極端不平等","examples":[{"en":"The city is characterised by extreme inequality.","zh":"這座城市以極端不平等為特徵。"},{"en":"Extreme inequality is a very large gap between rich and poor or powerful and powerless groups.","zh":"極端不平等是富人與窮人、掌權者與無權者之間非常大的差距。"},{"en":"A town has extreme inequality if some families live in luxury while others cannot afford food.","zh":"如果一些家庭過着奢華生活，而另一些買不起食物，一個城鎮就有極端不平等。"},{"en":"If inequality becomes extreme, social tension and anger may increase.","zh":"如果不平等變得極端，社會緊張和憤怒可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a serious imbalance in society.","zh":"這個短語描述社會中的嚴重失衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"social division","meaning":"社會分化","examples":[{"en":"The film depicts a world of inequality and social division.","zh":"這部電影描繪一個充滿不平等和社會分化的世界。"},{"en":"Social division is separation between groups in society because of wealth, class, race, work or power.","zh":"社會分化是社會群體因財富、階級、種族、工作或權力而分隔。"},{"en":"A school can show social division if rich and poor students never mix.","zh":"如果富裕學生和貧窮學生從不混在一起，學校就可能出現社會分化。"},{"en":"If social division deepens, people may stop seeing one another as part of the same community.","zh":"如果社會分化加深，人們可能不再把彼此視為同一社區的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a divided society, not just individual disagreement.","zh":"這個短語描述分裂的社會，而不只是個人分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"live below ground","meaning":"住在地底","examples":[{"en":"The workers are forced to live below ground.","zh":"工人被迫住在地底。"},{"en":"To live below ground means to live under the surface of the earth, often in hidden or restricted spaces.","zh":"住在地底指住在地面以下，通常在隱藏或受限制的空間中。"},{"en":"In some stories, poor citizens live below ground while the wealthy enjoy sunlight above.","zh":"在一些故事中，貧窮市民住在地底，而富人享受上方陽光。"},{"en":"If workers live underground, the setting suggests isolation and lower social status.","zh":"如果工人住在地下，這個背景暗示隔離和較低社會地位。"},{"en":"The phrase can be literal, but it also often symbolises oppression.","zh":"這個短語可以是字面意思，但也常象徵壓迫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"exist as machines","meaning":"像機器一樣生存","examples":[{"en":"The workers exist as machines rather than as individuals.","zh":"工人像機器一樣生存，而不是作為個體存在。"},{"en":"To exist as machines means to live or work in a way that removes personal feeling, choice and identity.","zh":"像機器一樣生存，指以失去個人感受、選擇和身份的方式生活或工作。"},{"en":"Students may feel like machines if they only repeat exam drills without understanding.","zh":"如果學生只重複考試操練而不理解，他們可能感覺自己像機器。"},{"en":"If workers are treated only for output, their humanity is ignored.","zh":"如果工人只因產量被看待，他們的人性就被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises systems that reduce people to functions.","zh":"這個短語批評把人簡化成功能的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"endless routine","meaning":"無休止的例行工作","examples":[{"en":"The workers are trapped in an endless routine.","zh":"工人被困在無休止的例行工作中。"},{"en":"An endless routine is a repeated pattern of tasks that seems never to stop.","zh":"無休止的例行工作，是看似永不停止的重複任務模式。"},{"en":"A student may feel trapped in an endless routine of school, homework and sleep.","zh":"學生可能覺得自己被困在上學、功課和睡覺的無休止例行中。"},{"en":"If work has no change, rest or purpose, routine can become mentally exhausting.","zh":"如果工作沒有變化、休息或目的，例行工作可以令人精神疲憊。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests repetition, boredom and lack of escape.","zh":"這個短語暗示重複、沉悶和無法逃離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mind-numbing shifts","meaning":"令人麻木的輪班","examples":[{"en":"The workers endure mind-numbing 10-hour shifts.","zh":"工人忍受令人麻木的十小時輪班。"},{"en":"Mind-numbing shifts are long work periods so dull and repetitive that they make people feel mentally empty.","zh":"令人麻木的輪班，是長時間、沉悶又重複，令人感到精神空洞的工作時段。"},{"en":"A cashier may find a twelve-hour shift mind-numbing if every customer asks the same question.","zh":"如果每位顧客都問同一問題，收銀員可能覺得十二小時輪班令人麻木。"},{"en":"If workers repeat one motion for hours, concentration and dignity may suffer.","zh":"如果工人數小時重複同一動作，專注力和尊嚴都可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase combines long working time with mental exhaustion.","zh":"這個短語結合長工時和精神疲憊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"city’s elite","meaning":"城市精英階層","examples":[{"en":"The city’s elite live in luxury above ground.","zh":"城市精英階層在地面上過着奢華生活。"},{"en":"A city’s elite are the small group of people with the most wealth, power or status in that city.","zh":"城市精英階層是城市中擁有最多財富、權力或地位的小群體。"},{"en":"The city’s elite may attend private clubs while ordinary workers struggle with rent.","zh":"城市精英階層可能出入私人會所，而普通工人為租金掙扎。"},{"en":"If the elite live separately from workers, social division becomes visible.","zh":"如果精英與工人分開生活，社會分化就變得可見。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the privileged top group in urban society.","zh":"這個短語指城市社會中享有特權的頂層群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"lead lives of luxury","meaning":"過着奢華生活","examples":[{"en":"The elite lead lives of luxury high above the workers.","zh":"精英在工人上方高處過着奢華生活。"},{"en":"To lead lives of luxury means to live with great comfort, wealth and expensive pleasures.","zh":"過着奢華生活指生活非常舒適、富有，並享受昂貴娛樂。"},{"en":"Some celebrities lead lives of luxury with private cars, large homes and personal staff.","zh":"一些名人擁有私家車、大宅和私人員工，過着奢華生活。"},{"en":"If one group lives in luxury while another suffers, inequality becomes obvious.","zh":"如果一個群體過奢華生活，而另一群體受苦，不平等就很明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a wealthy lifestyle far beyond basic needs.","zh":"這個短語描述遠超基本需要的富裕生活方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"high above","meaning":"在高高的上方","examples":[{"en":"The wealthy live high above the underground workers.","zh":"富人住在地下工人高高的上方。"},{"en":"High above means far higher in physical position, often suggesting power or distance.","zh":"“High above” 指在實際位置上高出很多，常暗示權力或距離。"},{"en":"A manager in a glass office high above the factory floor may seem separated from workers.","zh":"坐在工廠樓層高高上方玻璃辦公室中的經理，可能顯得與工人分離。"},{"en":"If rich people live high above poor workers, the vertical space symbolises social hierarchy.","zh":"如果富人住在窮工人高高上方，垂直空間就象徵社會階級。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe both height and social separation.","zh":"這個短語可以描述高度，也可以描述社會分隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"preside over","meaning":"統領；掌管……","examples":[{"en":"John Fredersen presides over the entire city.","zh":"John Fredersen 掌管整座城市。"},{"en":"To preside over something means to control, direct or formally lead it from a position of authority.","zh":"“Preside over” 某事指從權威位置控制、指揮或正式領導它。"},{"en":"A principal may preside over a school assembly from the stage.","zh":"校長可能在台上主持學校早會。"},{"en":"If one person presides over a whole city, the society appears highly centralised.","zh":"如果一個人掌管整座城市，該社會就顯得高度中央集權。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests authority, supervision and power.","zh":"這個短語暗示權威、監督和權力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Master of Metropolis","meaning":"大都會的主人","examples":[{"en":"John Fredersen is known as the Master of Metropolis.","zh":"John Fredersen 被稱為大都會的主人。"},{"en":"The Master of Metropolis means the person who controls or dominates the city of Metropolis.","zh":"大都會的主人指控制或支配大都會這座城市的人。"},{"en":"In a story, a company owner may become the master of a town if everyone depends on his factory.","zh":"在故事中，如果人人依賴某工廠，公司老闆可能成為城鎮主人。"},{"en":"If one man controls work, housing and machines, his power is almost absolute.","zh":"如果一個人控制工作、住房和機器，其權力就幾乎是絕對的。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a ruler-like title to an industrial leader.","zh":"這個短語給工業領袖一個像統治者的稱號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sole satisfaction","meaning":"唯一的滿足感","examples":[{"en":"His sole satisfaction appears to come from exercising power.","zh":"他唯一的滿足感似乎來自行使權力。"},{"en":"Sole satisfaction means the only thing that gives someone pleasure or fulfilment.","zh":"唯一的滿足感指唯一給某人快樂或成就感的事物。"},{"en":"A student whose sole satisfaction is winning may forget to enjoy learning.","zh":"如果學生唯一的滿足感是勝利，他可能忘記享受學習。"},{"en":"If a leader’s only pleasure is control, relationships and compassion may disappear.","zh":"如果領袖唯一樂趣是控制，關係和同情心可能消失。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a narrow and possibly unhealthy source of happiness.","zh":"這個短語強調狹窄且可能不健康的快樂來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lie in","meaning":"在於……","examples":[{"en":"Fredersen’s satisfaction seems to lie in the exercise of power.","zh":"Fredersen 的滿足感似乎在於權力的行使。"},{"en":"To lie in something means to be found in or depend on that thing.","zh":"“Lie in” 某事指存在於或取決於該事。"},{"en":"The value of a good teacher lies in patience, clarity and care.","zh":"好老師的價值在於耐性、清晰和關懷。"},{"en":"If someone’s happiness lies in power, losing control may frighten them deeply.","zh":"如果某人的快樂在於權力，失去控制可能令他深感恐懼。"},{"en":"The phrase explains where the real source of something is.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事真正來源在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"exercise of power","meaning":"權力的行使","examples":[{"en":"Fredersen takes pleasure in the exercise of power.","zh":"Fredersen 從權力的行使中得到快樂。"},{"en":"The exercise of power means the use of authority to control people, decisions or systems.","zh":"權力的行使指使用權威去控制人、決定或系統。"},{"en":"A head teacher’s exercise of power can be fair if rules are explained clearly.","zh":"如果校長清楚解釋規則，權力的行使可以是公平的。"},{"en":"If power is exercised only for control, people below may feel oppressed.","zh":"如果權力只為控制而行使，下層人士可能感到受壓迫。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on power being used, not just possessed.","zh":"這個短語強調權力被使用，而不只是被擁有。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"graphic depiction of","meaning":"對……的鮮明描繪","examples":[{"en":"Lang’s graphic depiction of the future is highly memorable.","zh":"Lang 對未來的鮮明描繪非常令人難忘。"},{"en":"A graphic depiction of something is a vivid and detailed visual presentation of it.","zh":"對某事的鮮明描繪，是對它作出生動而詳細的視覺呈現。"},{"en":"A poster may give a graphic depiction of pollution by showing fish trapped in plastic.","zh":"海報可能透過展示魚被困在塑膠中，對污染作出鮮明描繪。"},{"en":"If a film depicts machines and workers vividly, viewers remember the warning more clearly.","zh":"如果電影生動描繪機器和工人，觀眾就更清楚記得警告。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong visual representation.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈視覺呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be conceived in","meaning":"以……構想","examples":[{"en":"The future city is conceived in almost completely abstract terms.","zh":"這座未來城市幾乎完全以抽象方式構想。"},{"en":"To be conceived in a certain way means to be imagined, designed or understood in that way.","zh":"“Be conceived in” 某方式指以該方式想像、設計或理解。"},{"en":"A school project may be conceived in practical terms if the goal is to solve a real problem.","zh":"如果學校項目目標是解決真實問題，它可能以實用角度構想。"},{"en":"If machines are conceived abstractly, their exact function matters less than their symbolic meaning.","zh":"如果機器以抽象方式構想，其確實功能就不及象徵意義重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the way an idea is formed.","zh":"這個短語描述想法形成的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"abstract terms","meaning":"抽象方式","examples":[{"en":"Lang presents the machines in abstract terms.","zh":"Lang 以抽象方式呈現機器。"},{"en":"Abstract terms are general or symbolic ideas rather than concrete details.","zh":"抽象方式是使用一般或象徵性想法，而不是具體細節。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain freedom in abstract terms before giving real-life examples.","zh":"老師可能先以抽象方式解釋自由，再給出現實例子。"},{"en":"If machines are shown in abstract terms, they may represent industry rather than specific devices.","zh":"如果機器以抽象方式呈現，它們可能代表工業，而不是特定設備。"},{"en":"The phrase points to symbolic meaning more than practical detail.","zh":"這個短語指向象徵意義多於實際細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"function of","meaning":"……的功能","examples":[{"en":"The function of each individual machine is never explained.","zh":"每部個別機器的功能從未被解釋。"},{"en":"The function of something is the job, purpose or role it serves.","zh":"某物的功能是它所執行的工作、目的或角色。"},{"en":"The function of a school bell is to signal when lessons begin or end.","zh":"學校鐘聲的功能是提示課堂開始或結束。"},{"en":"If a machine’s function is unclear, viewers focus more on its appearance and meaning.","zh":"如果機器功能不清楚，觀眾會更集中於其外觀和意義。"},{"en":"The phrase asks what something is for.","zh":"這個短語詢問某物用來做甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be left undefined","meaning":"未有明確說明","examples":[{"en":"The purpose of the individual machines is left undefined.","zh":"個別機器的用途未有明確說明。"},{"en":"To be left undefined means not to be clearly explained or fixed.","zh":"“Be left undefined” 指沒有被清楚解釋或固定下來。"},{"en":"If homework instructions are left undefined, students may not know what to submit.","zh":"如果功課指示未有明確說明，學生可能不知道要交甚麼。"},{"en":"When a film leaves machines undefined, they can work as symbols rather than realistic tools.","zh":"當電影沒有明確說明機器，它們就可以作為象徵，而不是寫實工具。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deliberate or accidental lack of clear meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述有意或無意缺乏清楚意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"instead","meaning":"反而","examples":[{"en":"Instead, the machines symbolise industry as a whole.","zh":"反而，這些機器象徵整個工業體系。"},{"en":"Instead means in place of what has just been mentioned or expected.","zh":"“Instead” 指取代剛提到或預期的事物。"},{"en":"The student did not copy the answer; instead, she explained it in her own words.","zh":"這名學生沒有抄答案；反而，她用自己的話解釋。"},{"en":"If a film does not explain a machine’s function, it may use the machine symbolically instead.","zh":"如果電影不解釋機器功能，它可能反而象徵性地使用機器。"},{"en":"The word signals a replacement or contrast.","zh":"這個詞表示替代或對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a mass of","meaning":"大量的……","examples":[{"en":"The machinery appears as a mass of dials, levers and gauges.","zh":"機械看起來像大量儀表盤、控制桿和量表組成的東西。"},{"en":"A mass of something means a large, crowded and sometimes confusing amount of it.","zh":"“A mass of” 某物指大量、密集且有時令人混亂的東西。"},{"en":"A teacher may face a mass of forms before the start of a school trip.","zh":"學校旅行開始前，老師可能面對大量表格。"},{"en":"If a machine is shown as a mass of controls, it can look overwhelming and inhuman.","zh":"如果機器被呈現為大量控制裝置，它可以顯得壓倒性且不人性化。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests quantity and visual density.","zh":"這個短語暗示數量和視覺密度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"dials, levers and gauges","meaning":"儀表盤、控制桿和量表","examples":[{"en":"The machines contain countless dials, levers and gauges.","zh":"這些機器有無數儀表盤、控制桿和量表。"},{"en":"Dials, levers and gauges are control and measuring parts found on machines.","zh":"儀表盤、控制桿和量表是機器上的控制和量度部件。"},{"en":"An old aircraft cockpit may be full of dials, levers and gauges.","zh":"舊式飛機駕駛艙可能滿是儀表盤、控制桿和量表。"},{"en":"If workers must watch many controls at once, their job may become exhausting.","zh":"如果工人必須同時監察許多控制裝置，工作可能變得令人疲憊。"},{"en":"The phrase creates an image of complicated machinery.","zh":"這個短語營造複雜機械的畫面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"symbolically stand for","meaning":"象徵……","examples":[{"en":"The machinery symbolically stands for all industry.","zh":"機械象徵整個工業。"},{"en":"To symbolically stand for something means to represent a larger idea rather than only itself.","zh":"“Symbolically stand for” 某事指代表一個更大的想法，而不只是它本身。"},{"en":"A school uniform may symbolically stand for discipline and belonging.","zh":"校服可以象徵紀律和歸屬感。"},{"en":"If one machine stands for all industry, it becomes a visual shorthand for a whole system.","zh":"如果一部機器象徵整個工業，它就成為整個系統的視覺簡寫。"},{"en":"The phrase explains symbolic representation.","zh":"這個短語解釋象徵性代表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"industry as a whole","meaning":"整個工業體系","examples":[{"en":"The machines represent industry as a whole.","zh":"這些機器代表整個工業體系。"},{"en":"Industry as a whole means the entire system of factories, production, machines, workers and business.","zh":"整個工業體系指工廠、生產、機器、工人和商業的完整系統。"},{"en":"When people discuss pollution from industry as a whole, they are not blaming one factory only.","zh":"當人們討論整個工業體系造成的污染時，他們不是只責怪一間工廠。"},{"en":"If machines represent industry as a whole, they symbolise a complete economic system.","zh":"如果機器代表整個工業體系，它們就象徵完整經濟系統。"},{"en":"The phrase looks at the full system rather than one part.","zh":"這個短語看的是整個系統，而不是單一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"slave-like extensions of","meaning":"像奴隸般成為……的延伸","examples":[{"en":"The workers become slave-like extensions of the equipment.","zh":"工人像奴隸般成為設備的延伸。"},{"en":"Slave-like extensions of something are people treated as if they exist only to serve or continue a machine or system.","zh":"像奴隸般成為某物的延伸，指人被當成只是為服務或延續機器或系統而存在。"},{"en":"Workers may feel like extensions of computers if they only enter data all day without judgement.","zh":"如果工人整天只輸入數據而不能判斷，可能覺得自己像電腦的延伸。"},{"en":"If people lose choice and individuality at work, the system becomes dehumanising.","zh":"如果人在工作中失去選擇和個體性，系統就變得去人性化。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly criticises work that reduces humans to tools.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評把人簡化成工具的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"operate the equipment","meaning":"操作設備","examples":[{"en":"The workers must operate the equipment for long hours.","zh":"工人必須長時間操作設備。"},{"en":"To operate the equipment means to control or use machines, tools or devices.","zh":"操作設備指控制或使用機器、工具或裝置。"},{"en":"A nurse must learn to operate the equipment before using it with patients.","zh":"護士在為病人使用設備前，必須學會操作它。"},{"en":"If workers operate heavy machines without rest, mistakes and injuries may increase.","zh":"如果工人不休息地操作重型機器，錯誤和受傷可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical control of machinery.","zh":"這個短語描述對機械的實際控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"emphasise this idea","meaning":"強調這個想法","examples":[{"en":"Lang emphasises this idea in the shift-change sequence.","zh":"Lang 在換班場面中強調這個想法。"},{"en":"To emphasise this idea means to make the idea clearer, stronger or more noticeable.","zh":"強調這個想法，指令這個想法更清楚、更有力或更明顯。"},{"en":"A teacher may emphasise an idea by repeating it and giving a simple example.","zh":"老師可能透過重複並給出簡單例子來強調一個想法。"},{"en":"If a film shows workers moving like machines, it strengthens the idea that they have lost individuality.","zh":"如果電影展示工人像機器般移動，它就加強他們失去個體性的想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a point more forceful.","zh":"這個短語描述使觀點更有力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"shift-change sequence","meaning":"換班場面","examples":[{"en":"The shift-change sequence shows workers moving in identical groups.","zh":"換班場面展示工人以一模一樣的群組移動。"},{"en":"A shift-change sequence is a scene showing one group of workers finishing work and another group beginning.","zh":"換班場面是展示一組工人下班、另一組工人開始工作的場景。"},{"en":"In a hospital, a shift change happens when night nurses hand duties to day nurses.","zh":"在醫院中，夜班護士把職責交給日班護士時，就是換班。"},{"en":"If a film shows shift change mechanically, it can make workers look like replaceable parts.","zh":"如果電影以機械化方式展示換班，就可以令工人看似可替換零件。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a scene organised around changing work shifts.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞工作輪班交替而組織的場面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at the start of","meaning":"在……開始時","examples":[{"en":"The sequence appears at the start of the film.","zh":"這個場面出現在電影開始時。"},{"en":"At the start of something means at the beginning of it.","zh":"“At the start of” 某事指在它的開端。"},{"en":"At the start of a lesson, a teacher may review yesterday’s vocabulary.","zh":"在課堂開始時，老師可能重溫昨天的詞彙。"},{"en":"If a powerful image appears at the start of a film, it shapes the viewer’s expectations.","zh":"如果有力影像出現在電影開始時，它會塑造觀眾期待。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the opening point of an event or text.","zh":"這個短語指出事件或文本的開端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"zombie-like","meaning":"像喪屍般的","examples":[{"en":"The workers move in zombie-like ranks.","zh":"工人以像喪屍般的隊列移動。"},{"en":"Zombie-like means moving or behaving without energy, thought or individuality.","zh":"像喪屍般的，指移動或行為沒有活力、思想或個體性。"},{"en":"Students may walk zombie-like into class after staying up all night.","zh":"學生通宵不睡後，可能像喪屍般走進課室。"},{"en":"If workers look zombie-like, the film suggests they have been drained by the system.","zh":"如果工人看起來像喪屍，電影就暗示他們被體制耗盡。"},{"en":"The word creates an image of lifeless human movement.","zh":"這個詞營造沒有生命力的人類動作畫面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"geometric ranks","meaning":"幾何形狀的整齊隊列","examples":[{"en":"The workers walk in rigid geometric ranks.","zh":"工人以僵硬的幾何形狀整齊隊列行走。"},{"en":"Geometric ranks are arranged rows or groups that look mathematically ordered and regular.","zh":"幾何形狀的整齊隊列，是看起來數學化、有規律地排列的行列或群組。"},{"en":"Soldiers may stand in geometric ranks during a parade.","zh":"士兵在閱兵時可能站成幾何形狀的整齊隊列。"},{"en":"If workers move in perfect rows, they appear controlled rather than free.","zh":"如果工人以完美行列移動，他們就顯得受控制而非自由。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests order, discipline and loss of individuality.","zh":"這個短語暗示秩序、紀律和個體性的喪失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be dressed in","meaning":"穿着……","examples":[{"en":"The workers are dressed in identical dark overalls.","zh":"工人穿着一模一樣的深色工人服。"},{"en":"To be dressed in something means to be wearing those clothes.","zh":"“Be dressed in” 某衣物指穿着那些衣服。"},{"en":"Students may be dressed in school uniforms for a formal ceremony.","zh":"學生可能在正式典禮中穿着校服。"},{"en":"If everyone is dressed in identical clothing, personal difference becomes less visible.","zh":"如果人人穿着相同衣物，個人差異就變得較不明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what people are wearing.","zh":"這個短語描述人們身上穿甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dark overalls","meaning":"深色工人服","examples":[{"en":"All the workers wear the same dark overalls.","zh":"所有工人都穿着相同深色工人服。"},{"en":"Dark overalls are plain protective work clothes, usually covering the body and often worn in factories.","zh":"深色工人服是普通保護性工作服，通常包裹身體，常在工廠穿着。"},{"en":"A mechanic may wear dark overalls to keep oil and dust off normal clothes.","zh":"技工可能穿深色工人服，以防油污和灰塵弄髒普通衣服。"},{"en":"If all workers wear the same overalls, the group may look uniform and impersonal.","zh":"如果所有工人穿相同工人服，群體可能看起來一致而缺乏個性。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests practical labour clothing and visual sameness.","zh":"這個短語暗示實用勞動服裝和視覺上的相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"exhibit the same","meaning":"表現出同樣的……","examples":[{"en":"The workers all exhibit the same bowed posture.","zh":"工人全都表現出同樣低垂的姿勢。"},{"en":"To exhibit the same feature means to show an identical quality, behaviour or appearance.","zh":"“Exhibit the same” 特徵指顯示相同的特質、行為或外貌。"},{"en":"Several tired students may exhibit the same slow walk after a long exam.","zh":"幾名疲倦學生在長時間考試後，可能表現出同樣緩慢步伐。"},{"en":"If all workers exhibit the same posture, the film removes their individuality.","zh":"如果所有工人表現出同樣姿勢，電影就抹去他們的個體性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated visible similarity.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆出現的可見相似性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bowed head","meaning":"低垂的頭","examples":[{"en":"Each worker walks with a bowed head.","zh":"每名工人都低垂着頭行走。"},{"en":"A bowed head is a head lowered forward, often suggesting tiredness, shame, obedience or sadness.","zh":"低垂的頭是向前低下的頭，常暗示疲倦、羞愧、服從或悲傷。"},{"en":"A student may sit with a bowed head after receiving disappointing results.","zh":"學生收到令人失望的成績後，可能低垂着頭坐着。"},{"en":"If workers walk with bowed heads, they look defeated rather than energetic.","zh":"如果工人低垂着頭行走，他們看起來像被擊敗，而不是有活力。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a physical sign of emotional or social pressure.","zh":"這個短語給出情緒或社會壓力的身體表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dead-eyed stare","meaning":"呆滯無神的凝視","examples":[{"en":"The workers have the same dead-eyed stare.","zh":"工人有同樣呆滯無神的凝視。"},{"en":"A dead-eyed stare is a blank look with little emotion, energy or awareness.","zh":"呆滯無神的凝視是缺少情感、活力或意識的空洞眼神。"},{"en":"After a sleepless night, a student may answer questions with a dead-eyed stare.","zh":"通宵不睡後，學生回答問題時可能帶着呆滯無神的凝視。"},{"en":"If workers stare without expression, viewers may feel that the system has emptied them emotionally.","zh":"如果工人毫無表情地凝視，觀眾可能感到體制已把他們情感掏空。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lifeless, exhausted-looking eyes.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有生命力、看似疲憊的眼神。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"extraordinary fantasy sequence","meaning":"非凡的幻想場面","examples":[{"en":"The film contains an extraordinary fantasy sequence.","zh":"這部電影包含一個非凡的幻想場面。"},{"en":"An extraordinary fantasy sequence is an unusual and imaginative scene that departs from ordinary realism.","zh":"非凡的幻想場面，是不尋常且富想像力、偏離普通寫實的場景。"},{"en":"A film may use a fantasy sequence to show a child’s fear as a giant shadow.","zh":"電影可能使用幻想場面，把孩子的恐懼呈現為巨大陰影。"},{"en":"If a scene turns a machine into a monster, it expresses emotion through fantasy.","zh":"如果場景把機器變成怪物，它就是透過幻想表達情感。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a remarkable imaginative scene within a film.","zh":"這個短語指電影中令人印象深刻的想像場景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be transformed into","meaning":"被變成……","examples":[{"en":"A machine is transformed into a huge statue.","zh":"一部機器被變成一座巨大雕像。"},{"en":"To be transformed into something means to change completely into a different form.","zh":"“Be transformed into” 某物指完全變成另一種形態。"},{"en":"An old factory may be transformed into an art museum.","zh":"舊工廠可能被變成藝術博物館。"},{"en":"If a machine is transformed into a statue, the film shifts from realism to symbolism.","zh":"如果機器被變成雕像，電影就由寫實轉向象徵。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a major change in form or meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述形態或意義上的重大改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"open-jawed statue","meaning":"張開大口的雕像","examples":[{"en":"The machine becomes a huge open-jawed statue.","zh":"這部機器變成一座張開大口的巨大雕像。"},{"en":"An open-jawed statue is a statue with its mouth wide open, often looking threatening or hungry.","zh":"張開大口的雕像，是嘴巴大開、常看似威脅人或飢餓的雕像。"},{"en":"A temple gate sculpture with an open jaw may look as if it is guarding the entrance.","zh":"寺廟入口張口雕塑可能看起來像在守護入口。"},{"en":"If a machine becomes open-jawed, it can appear to devour the workers.","zh":"如果機器變成張開大口的形態，它可以看似吞噬工人。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a frightening image of a mouth-like structure.","zh":"這個短語營造像嘴巴一樣的可怕結構畫面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"swallow someone up","meaning":"吞噬某人","examples":[{"en":"The enormous machine appears to swallow the workers up.","zh":"這部巨大機器看似吞噬工人。"},{"en":"To swallow someone up means to consume, absorb or completely take them into a larger force or system.","zh":"吞噬某人指消耗、吸收或完全把某人納入更大力量或系統中。"},{"en":"A busy office can swallow a new worker up if no one helps them adjust.","zh":"如果沒有人幫新員工適應，繁忙辦公室可能把他吞噬。"},{"en":"If a machine seems to swallow workers, the film suggests industry consumes human life.","zh":"如果機器看似吞噬工人，電影就暗示工業消耗人類生命。"},{"en":"The phrase can be literal, but often means being overwhelmed by something huge.","zh":"這個短語可以是字面意思，但常指被巨大事物壓倒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"on one level","meaning":"從一個層面來看","examples":[{"en":"On one level, the machines provide services for the elite.","zh":"從一個層面來看，機器為精英提供服務。"},{"en":"On one level means from one way of understanding a situation, though there may be deeper meanings.","zh":"“On one level” 指從理解情況的一種方式來看，雖然可能有更深意思。"},{"en":"On one level, homework is practice; on another level, it teaches discipline.","zh":"從一個層面來看，功課是練習；從另一層面來看，它教紀律。"},{"en":"If a film works on one level as entertainment, it may also work as social criticism.","zh":"如果電影在一個層面上是娛樂，它也可能在另一層面上是社會批評。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces one layer of interpretation.","zh":"這個短語引出一層詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"exploited workers","meaning":"受剝削的工人","examples":[{"en":"The exploited workers produce wealth for the ruling class.","zh":"受剝削的工人為統治階級創造財富。"},{"en":"Exploited workers are workers used unfairly so others can gain profit or power.","zh":"受剝削的工人是被不公平利用、使他人獲利或掌權的工人。"},{"en":"Workers who receive very low pay for dangerous jobs may be exploited workers.","zh":"做危險工作但薪金極低的工人，可能是受剝削的工人。"},{"en":"If workers create wealth but cannot share its benefits, exploitation becomes clear.","zh":"如果工人創造財富卻無法分享利益，剝削就很清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unfair treatment in labour relations.","zh":"這個短語描述勞資關係中的不公平對待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"provide wealth and services","meaning":"提供財富和服務","examples":[{"en":"The workers provide wealth and services for the elite.","zh":"工人為精英提供財富和服務。"},{"en":"To provide wealth and services means to produce money, comfort, labour or benefits for others.","zh":"提供財富和服務指為他人生產金錢、舒適、勞動或利益。"},{"en":"Hotel staff provide services for guests by cleaning rooms, cooking food and answering questions.","zh":"酒店員工透過清潔房間、煮食和回答問題為客人提供服務。"},{"en":"If one group provides everything while another enjoys the benefits, inequality may deepen.","zh":"如果一個群體提供一切，而另一群體享受利益，不平等可能加深。"},{"en":"The phrase shows what labour supplies to those in power.","zh":"這個短語顯示勞動向掌權者供應甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"allow someone to","meaning":"讓某人能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The workers’ labour allows the elite to live in luxury.","zh":"工人的勞動讓精英能夠過奢華生活。"},{"en":"To allow someone to do something means to make it possible for them to do it.","zh":"“Allow someone to” 做某事指使某人能夠做該事。"},{"en":"A scholarship can allow a student to study abroad.","zh":"獎學金可以讓學生能夠出國留學。"},{"en":"If workers’ labour allows others to enjoy comfort, the connection between classes becomes clear.","zh":"如果工人的勞動讓其他人享受舒適，階級之間的關係就變得清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase links one person’s action with another person’s opportunity.","zh":"這個短語把一個人的行動與另一個人的機會連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lives of leisure","meaning":"悠閒享樂的生活","examples":[{"en":"The wealthy enjoy lives of leisure above the city.","zh":"富人在城市上方享受悠閒享樂的生活。"},{"en":"Lives of leisure are lives with much free time, comfort and little need to work.","zh":"悠閒享樂的生活，是有大量自由時間、舒適感和很少需要工作的生活。"},{"en":"Retired people with enough savings may enjoy lives of leisure filled with travel and hobbies.","zh":"有足夠儲蓄的退休人士可能享受充滿旅遊和興趣的悠閒生活。"},{"en":"If one class lives in leisure while another works underground, the contrast is severe.","zh":"如果一個階級悠閒生活，而另一個階級在地下工作，對比就很強烈。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a privileged lifestyle free from hard labour.","zh":"這個短語描述免於艱苦勞動的特權生活方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"on a more profound level","meaning":"在更深層次上","examples":[{"en":"On a more profound level, the industrial system exists to preserve itself.","zh":"在更深層次上，工業體系存在是為了保存自身。"},{"en":"On a more profound level means at a deeper and more serious level of meaning.","zh":"“On a more profound level” 指在更深入、更嚴肅的意義層面上。"},{"en":"On a more profound level, a school rule about punctuality may teach respect for others’ time.","zh":"在更深層次上，關於準時的校規可能教人尊重他人時間。"},{"en":"If a film’s machines do more than serve people, they may represent a system protecting itself.","zh":"如果電影中的機器不只是服務人，它們可能代表保護自身的體制。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a deeper interpretation.","zh":"這個短語引出更深層詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"demented industry","meaning":"瘋狂的工業體系","examples":[{"en":"The film presents an image of demented industry.","zh":"這部電影呈現一幅瘋狂工業體系的影像。"},{"en":"Demented industry means an industrial system that seems mad, uncontrolled or violently irrational.","zh":"瘋狂的工業體系，指看似瘋癲、失控或暴力非理性的工業系統。"},{"en":"A factory that values output more than human safety may look like demented industry in a social critique.","zh":"如果工廠重視產量多於人身安全，它在社會批評中可能像瘋狂工業體系。"},{"en":"If machines consume workers only to keep running, the system appears insane.","zh":"如果機器吞噬工人只是為了繼續運轉，這個系統就顯得瘋狂。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly criticises industry as destructive and unreasonable.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評工業具破壞性且不合理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"serve itself","meaning":"為自身服務","examples":[{"en":"The purpose of the industrial system is simply to serve itself.","zh":"工業體系的目的只是為自身服務。"},{"en":"To serve itself means to exist mainly to continue and benefit the system, not people outside it.","zh":"為自身服務指主要為延續和有利於系統本身而存在，而不是服務外部的人。"},{"en":"A committee may seem to serve itself if it holds meetings only to create more meetings.","zh":"如果委員會開會只是為了製造更多會議，它可能看似為自身服務。"},{"en":"If a company protects profits while ignoring workers, it may appear to serve itself.","zh":"如果公司保護利潤卻忽視工人，它可能顯得為自身服務。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises self-preserving systems.","zh":"這個短語批評自我保存的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"continuance of the system","meaning":"體制的延續","examples":[{"en":"Power and the continuance of the system are all that matter.","zh":"權力和體制的延續才是唯一重要的事。"},{"en":"The continuance of the system means the system keeps existing and operating.","zh":"體制的延續指該體制繼續存在和運作。"},{"en":"A school may focus too much on the continuance of old rules even when students need change.","zh":"即使學生需要改變，學校也可能過分關注舊規則的延續。"},{"en":"If maintaining a system matters more than people’s welfare, the system becomes oppressive.","zh":"如果維持體制比人的福祉更重要，該體制就變得壓迫。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses survival of an organisation or structure over other values.","zh":"這個短語強調組織或結構的存續高於其他價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"from one shift to the next","meaning":"從一個輪班到下一個","examples":[{"en":"The system continues unchanged from one shift to the next.","zh":"這個體制從一個輪班到下一個都不變地持續。"},{"en":"From one shift to the next means from one work period to the following one.","zh":"從一個輪班到下一個，指從一個工作時段到接下來的工作時段。"},{"en":"In a hospital, patient notes are passed from one shift to the next.","zh":"在醫院中，病人紀錄會從一個輪班交到下一個輪班。"},{"en":"If nothing changes between shifts, workers may feel trapped in endless repetition.","zh":"如果輪班之間沒有任何改變，工人可能感到被困在無盡重複中。"},{"en":"The phrase shows continuity across repeated work cycles.","zh":"這個短語顯示反覆工作周期中的延續性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"all that counts","meaning":"唯一重要的事","examples":[{"en":"Power and control are all that count in Metropolis.","zh":"在《大都會》中，權力和控制是唯一重要的事。"},{"en":"All that counts means the only thing that is considered important.","zh":"“All that counts” 指唯一被視為重要的事。"},{"en":"In a bad classroom, test scores may seem like all that counts.","zh":"在差劣課室中，考試分數可能看似唯一重要的事。"},{"en":"If profit is all that counts, worker welfare and fairness may be ignored.","zh":"如果利潤是唯一重要的事，工人福祉和公平可能被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase reveals a narrow value system.","zh":"這個短語揭示狹隘的價值系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"consume people and their labour","meaning":"消耗人力及其勞動","examples":[{"en":"The city consumes people and their labour.","zh":"這座城市消耗人力及其勞動。"},{"en":"To consume people and their labour means to use up human energy, time and work for the system’s benefit.","zh":"消耗人力及其勞動，指為系統利益耗盡人的精力、時間和工作。"},{"en":"A company may consume workers’ labour if it demands long hours without fair pay.","zh":"如果公司要求長工時卻不給公平薪酬，它可能消耗工人的勞動。"},{"en":"If a city runs by exhausting workers, it turns human lives into fuel for production.","zh":"如果城市靠耗盡工人來運行，它就把人類生命變成生產燃料。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly criticises exploitative systems.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評剝削性系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in the process","meaning":"在過程中","examples":[{"en":"In the process, the city becomes like a living creature.","zh":"在過程中，這座城市變得像一個生物。"},{"en":"In the process means while this is happening or as a result of these actions.","zh":"“In the process” 指當這件事正在發生時，或作為這些行動的結果。"},{"en":"A student may revise hard and, in the process, discover a real interest in history.","zh":"學生可能努力溫習，而在過程中發現自己真正對歷史有興趣。"},{"en":"If a system consumes labour, in the process it may seem to become alive and hungry.","zh":"如果體制消耗勞動，在過程中它可能看似變得有生命而飢餓。"},{"en":"The phrase links an action with something that happens during or because of it.","zh":"這個短語把行動與其期間或因其而發生的事連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"perverse parody of","meaning":"對……的扭曲模仿","examples":[{"en":"The city becomes a perverse parody of a living being.","zh":"這座城市成為對生命體的扭曲模仿。"},{"en":"A perverse parody of something is a twisted and disturbing imitation of it.","zh":"對某物的扭曲模仿，是對它扭曲而令人不安的仿製。"},{"en":"A school that pretends to care but only measures grades can become a perverse parody of education.","zh":"如果學校假裝關心教育卻只量度成績，它可以成為對教育的扭曲模仿。"},{"en":"If a city acts like a creature but feeds on workers, the imitation of life is frightening.","zh":"如果城市像生物般運作卻以工人為食，這種生命模仿就很可怕。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a dark, distorted version of something meaningful.","zh":"這個短語描述某種有意義事物的黑暗、扭曲版本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"living being","meaning":"生物；生命體","examples":[{"en":"The industrial city is presented as a living being.","zh":"這座工業城市被呈現為一個生命體。"},{"en":"A living being is an organism or creature that is alive.","zh":"生物或生命體是有生命的有機體或生物。"},{"en":"A tree, a dog and a human are living beings because they grow and respond to their environment.","zh":"樹、狗和人都是生命體，因為它們會生長並回應環境。"},{"en":"If a city is described as a living being, it is being imagined as if it can breathe, hunger or act.","zh":"如果城市被描述為生命體，它就是被想像成能呼吸、飢餓或行動。"},{"en":"The phrase gives life-like qualities to something.","zh":"這個短語賦予某物類似生命的特質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"it is enlightening to","meaning":"將……聯繫起來很有啟發性","examples":[{"en":"It is enlightening to relate the film to the modern global economy.","zh":"將這部電影與現代全球經濟聯繫起來很有啟發性。"},{"en":"It is enlightening to do something means doing it helps people understand something more clearly.","zh":"“It is enlightening to” 做某事指這樣做有助人更清楚理解某事。"},{"en":"It is enlightening to compare two schools when discussing why some students learn faster.","zh":"討論為何一些學生學得較快時，比較兩間學校很有啟發性。"},{"en":"If an old film explains modern problems, the comparison can teach viewers something new.","zh":"如果舊電影能解釋現代問題，這種比較可以教會觀眾新東西。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a useful way of gaining insight.","zh":"這個短語引出獲得洞見的有用方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"relate something to","meaning":"將某事與……聯繫起來","examples":[{"en":"The writer relates Metropolis to the modern global economy.","zh":"作者將《大都會》與現代全球經濟聯繫起來。"},{"en":"To relate something to another thing means to connect them in meaning or explanation.","zh":"“Relate something to” 另一事指在意義或解釋上把它們連接起來。"},{"en":"A teacher may relate a novel to students’ daily lives to make it easier to understand.","zh":"老師可能把小說與學生日常生活聯繫起來，使它更容易理解。"},{"en":"If a film about industry is related to global business, its message becomes contemporary.","zh":"如果關於工業的電影被聯繫到全球商業，其訊息就變得貼近當代。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a meaningful connection.","zh":"這個短語描述建立有意義的連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"modern global economy","meaning":"現代全球經濟","examples":[{"en":"The film can be compared with the modern global economy.","zh":"這部電影可以與現代全球經濟比較。"},{"en":"The modern global economy is the present worldwide system of trade, production, finance and business.","zh":"現代全球經濟是當今世界範圍內的貿易、生產、金融和商業系統。"},{"en":"A phone may be designed in one country, assembled in another and sold worldwide in the modern global economy.","zh":"在現代全球經濟中，手機可能在一國設計、在另一國組裝，並在全球銷售。"},{"en":"If companies move factories for lower costs, workers in many countries can be affected.","zh":"如果公司為降低成本而搬遷工廠，許多國家的工人都可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes today’s interconnected economic system.","zh":"這個短語描述今日相互連接的經濟系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"multinational corporations","meaning":"跨國企業","examples":[{"en":"Multinational corporations often move production between countries.","zh":"跨國企業常把生產在不同國家之間轉移。"},{"en":"Multinational corporations are large companies that operate in more than one country.","zh":"跨國企業是在多於一個國家營運的大型公司。"},{"en":"A multinational corporation may design products in Europe and manufacture them in Asia.","zh":"跨國企業可能在歐洲設計產品，在亞洲製造產品。"},{"en":"If such companies chase cheaper labour, local workers may lose jobs.","zh":"如果這些公司追求更廉價勞工，本地工人可能失去工作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to powerful businesses working across national borders.","zh":"這個短語指跨越國界運作的強大企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"routinely close factories","meaning":"經常關閉工廠","examples":[{"en":"Some corporations routinely close factories in one region.","zh":"一些企業經常關閉某一地區的工廠。"},{"en":"To routinely close factories means to shut down factories regularly as part of normal business practice.","zh":"經常關閉工廠，指把關閉工廠當作正常商業做法反覆進行。"},{"en":"A company may routinely close factories when production becomes cheaper elsewhere.","zh":"當其他地方生產成本較低，公司可能經常關閉工廠。"},{"en":"If factories close often, workers and local communities face uncertainty.","zh":"如果工廠經常關閉，工人和本地社區就面對不穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests repeated closures, not a rare emergency decision.","zh":"這個短語暗示反覆關閉，而不是罕見緊急決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in one continent","meaning":"在一個洲份","examples":[{"en":"A company may close factories in one continent and reopen them elsewhere.","zh":"公司可能在一個洲份關閉工廠，並在其他地方重開。"},{"en":"In one continent means in one of the world’s large land regions, such as Europe, Asia or Africa.","zh":"在一個洲份，指在世界大型陸地區域之一，例如歐洲、亞洲或非洲。"},{"en":"A business may sell products in one continent while manufacturing them in another.","zh":"企業可能在一個洲份銷售產品，卻在另一洲份製造。"},{"en":"If factories move from one continent to another, global workers compete under different conditions.","zh":"如果工廠從一個洲份搬到另一個，全球工人就在不同條件下競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a large geographical scale.","zh":"這個短語給出大型地理尺度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"take advantage of","meaning":"利用……","examples":[{"en":"Some corporations move abroad to take advantage of cheap labour.","zh":"一些企業搬到海外以利用廉價勞工。"},{"en":"To take advantage of something means to use an opportunity or situation for benefit.","zh":"“Take advantage of” 某事指利用機會或情況獲益。"},{"en":"Students may take advantage of free library resources before exams.","zh":"學生可能在考試前利用免費圖書館資源。"},{"en":"If companies take advantage of low wages, profits may rise while workers benefit little.","zh":"如果公司利用低工資，利潤可能上升，而工人受益很少。"},{"en":"The phrase can be neutral, but it may sound negative when people are being used unfairly.","zh":"這個短語可以是中性，但當人被不公平利用時可帶負面意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cheap labour","meaning":"廉價勞工","examples":[{"en":"Companies may relocate factories to obtain cheap labour.","zh":"公司可能搬遷工廠以取得廉價勞工。"},{"en":"Cheap labour means workers who can be hired for low wages.","zh":"廉價勞工指可以用低工資聘用的工人。"},{"en":"A factory may move to a poorer region because cheap labour lowers production costs.","zh":"工廠可能搬到較貧窮地區，因為廉價勞工降低生產成本。"},{"en":"If businesses depend on cheap labour, workers may struggle to earn a decent living.","zh":"如果企業依賴廉價勞工，工人可能難以賺取體面生活。"},{"en":"The phrase often raises questions about fairness and exploitation.","zh":"這個短語常引發關於公平和剝削的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"increased efficiency and profits","meaning":"提高效率和利潤","examples":[{"en":"Corporations often pursue increased efficiency and profits.","zh":"企業常追求提高效率和利潤。"},{"en":"Increased efficiency and profits mean producing more with fewer resources and earning more money.","zh":"提高效率和利潤，指用較少資源生產更多，並賺取更多金錢。"},{"en":"A delivery company may use better software to increase efficiency and profits.","zh":"速遞公司可能使用更好軟件來提高效率和利潤。"},{"en":"If efficiency and profit become the only goals, worker welfare may be ignored.","zh":"如果效率和利潤成為唯一目標，員工福祉可能被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase describes common business aims.","zh":"這個短語描述常見商業目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have little to do with","meaning":"與……關係不大","examples":[{"en":"Corporate goals may have little to do with employee welfare.","zh":"企業目標可能與員工福祉關係不大。"},{"en":"To have little to do with something means to be only weakly connected or not mainly concerned with it.","zh":"“Have little to do with” 某事指與它只有很弱連繫，或主要不關心它。"},{"en":"A student’s bad mood may have little to do with school if the real problem is lack of sleep.","zh":"如果真正問題是睡眠不足，學生心情差可能與學校關係不大。"},{"en":"If a company focuses only on profit, staff wellbeing may not influence decisions much.","zh":"如果公司只集中利潤，員工福祉可能對決定影響不大。"},{"en":"The phrase separates one issue from another.","zh":"這個短語把一個議題與另一個分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"welfare of employees","meaning":"員工福祉","examples":[{"en":"The corporations show little concern for the welfare of employees.","zh":"這些企業很少關心員工福祉。"},{"en":"Welfare of employees means workers’ health, safety, pay, dignity and general wellbeing.","zh":"員工福祉指工人的健康、安全、薪酬、尊嚴和整體身心狀況。"},{"en":"A good employer protects the welfare of employees by offering fair hours and safe workplaces.","zh":"好僱主透過提供公平工時和安全工作場所來保護員工福祉。"},{"en":"If employee welfare is ignored, productivity may rise temporarily but trust will fall.","zh":"如果員工福祉被忽視，生產力可能暫時上升，但信任會下降。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how workers are treated.","zh":"這個短語強調工人如何被對待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the majority of","meaning":"大多數……","examples":[{"en":"The majority of employees receive few benefits from corporate growth.","zh":"大多數員工從企業增長中得到很少好處。"},{"en":"The majority of a group means more than half of that group.","zh":"大多數某群體，指該群體中超過一半的人。"},{"en":"The majority of students may prefer a later start time if they sleep too little.","zh":"如果學生睡得太少，大多數學生可能較喜歡較遲開始上課。"},{"en":"If the majority of workers gain little from growth, wealth is not being shared widely.","zh":"如果大多數工人從增長中得益很少，財富就沒有被廣泛分享。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the larger part of a group.","zh":"這個短語描述群體中較大部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"population at large","meaning":"廣大市民","examples":[{"en":"Corporate decisions can affect the population at large.","zh":"企業決定可以影響廣大市民。"},{"en":"The population at large means the general public, not just a small group.","zh":"廣大市民指一般公眾，而不只是小群體。"},{"en":"A new public transport policy can affect the population at large if most people use buses and trains.","zh":"如果大多數人使用巴士和火車，新公共交通政策就可以影響廣大市民。"},{"en":"If corporations close factories, the effects may reach families, shops and local services.","zh":"如果企業關閉工廠，影響可能波及家庭、商店和本地服務。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to society broadly.","zh":"這個短語廣泛指整個社會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sustain the momentum of","meaning":"維持……的勢頭","examples":[{"en":"Corporations aim to sustain the momentum of their own growth.","zh":"企業旨在維持自身增長的勢頭。"},{"en":"To sustain the momentum of something means to keep its progress, speed or success going.","zh":"維持某事的勢頭，指保持其進展、速度或成功。"},{"en":"A student may sustain the momentum of revision by studying a little every day.","zh":"學生可以透過每天學習一點來維持溫習勢頭。"},{"en":"If a company keeps expanding, it may make decisions mainly to maintain growth.","zh":"如果公司持續擴張，它可能主要為維持增長而作決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes keeping a process moving forward.","zh":"這個短語描述保持過程向前推進。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"corporate growth","meaning":"企業增長","examples":[{"en":"Their main priority is continued corporate growth.","zh":"他們的主要優先事項是持續企業增長。"},{"en":"Corporate growth means a company becomes larger, earns more, or expands its business.","zh":"企業增長指公司變得更大、賺得更多或擴展業務。"},{"en":"A company may achieve corporate growth by opening new shops in different cities.","zh":"公司可能透過在不同城市開新店實現企業增長。"},{"en":"If corporate growth benefits only shareholders, workers may feel ignored.","zh":"如果企業增長只惠及股東，工人可能覺得被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase describes expansion at company level.","zh":"這個短語描述公司層面的擴張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"monetary rewards","meaning":"金錢回報","examples":[{"en":"The system increases monetary rewards for a small elite.","zh":"這個體制增加了少數精英的金錢回報。"},{"en":"Monetary rewards are financial benefits such as salary, bonuses, profit or dividends.","zh":"金錢回報是薪金、花紅、利潤或股息等財務利益。"},{"en":"Sales staff may receive monetary rewards when they exceed monthly targets.","zh":"銷售員超過每月目標時，可能獲得金錢回報。"},{"en":"If monetary rewards go mainly to managers, ordinary workers may not share in success.","zh":"如果金錢回報主要流向管理層，普通工人可能無法分享成功。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on money-based benefits.","zh":"這個短語強調以金錢為基礎的利益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a tiny elite","meaning":"極少數精英","examples":[{"en":"A tiny elite receives most of the financial benefits.","zh":"極少數精英獲得大部分財務利益。"},{"en":"A tiny elite is a very small group of people with great wealth, power or advantage.","zh":"極少數精英是擁有巨大財富、權力或優勢的非常小群體。"},{"en":"In some companies, a tiny elite makes decisions that affect thousands of workers.","zh":"在一些公司中，極少數精英作出的決定影響數千名工人。"},{"en":"If only a tiny elite benefits, inequality can become sharper.","zh":"如果只有極少數精英受益，不平等可能變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises concentration of benefits at the top.","zh":"這個短語批評利益集中在頂層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"executives and shareholders","meaning":"高級行政人員和股東","examples":[{"en":"The elite consists mainly of executives and shareholders.","zh":"精英主要由高級行政人員和股東組成。"},{"en":"Executives and shareholders are senior managers and people who own shares in a company.","zh":"高級行政人員和股東，是公司的高層管理者和持有公司股份的人。"},{"en":"Executives run the company, while shareholders may profit when the company earns more.","zh":"高級行政人員營運公司，而股東可能在公司賺更多時獲利。"},{"en":"If decisions benefit executives and shareholders first, workers may receive little protection.","zh":"如果決定首先惠及高級行政人員和股東，工人可能得到很少保障。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies powerful corporate groups.","zh":"這個短語指出有權勢的企業群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the essence of","meaning":"……的典型化身","examples":[{"en":"Fredersen is the essence of the powerful company boss.","zh":"Fredersen 是強大企業老闆的典型化身。"},{"en":"The essence of something is its most important or typical quality.","zh":"某事的典型化身，是它最重要或最典型的特質。"},{"en":"Patience is the essence of good teaching because students need time to understand.","zh":"耐性是良好教學的核心，因為學生需要時間理解。"},{"en":"If a character shows control, wealth and cold authority, he may embody the essence of corporate power.","zh":"如果角色展現控制、財富和冷酷權威，他可能體現企業權力的本質。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the central nature of something.","zh":"這個短語指向某事的核心本質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"big company boss","meaning":"大企業老闆","examples":[{"en":"Fredersen resembles a powerful big company boss.","zh":"Fredersen 像一位有權勢的大企業老闆。"},{"en":"A big company boss is a senior leader who controls a large corporation.","zh":"大企業老闆是控制大型企業的高層領袖。"},{"en":"A big company boss may make decisions about factories, wages and international expansion.","zh":"大企業老闆可能決定工廠、工資和國際擴張。"},{"en":"If one boss controls too much, employees may have little voice.","zh":"如果一位老闆控制太多，員工可能很少有發言權。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to powerful corporate leadership.","zh":"這個短語指有權勢的企業領導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"feel perfectly at home","meaning":"感到非常自在","examples":[{"en":"A corporate leader would feel perfectly at home in Fredersen’s office.","zh":"企業領袖會在 Fredersen 的辦公室感到非常自在。"},{"en":"To feel perfectly at home means to feel completely comfortable and familiar in a place or situation.","zh":"“Feel perfectly at home” 指在某地方或情況中感到完全舒適和熟悉。"},{"en":"A student who loves books may feel perfectly at home in a quiet library.","zh":"喜愛書本的學生可能在安靜圖書館感到非常自在。"},{"en":"If an office represents power and control, a powerful executive may feel comfortable there.","zh":"如果辦公室代表權力和控制，有權勢的高管可能在那裡感到舒服。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strong sense of belonging or ease.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈歸屬感或自在感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"skyscraper office","meaning":"摩天大廈辦公室","examples":[{"en":"Fredersen works in an enormous skyscraper office.","zh":"Fredersen 在一間巨大的摩天大廈辦公室工作。"},{"en":"A skyscraper office is an office located in a very tall city building.","zh":"摩天大廈辦公室是位於非常高城市建築中的辦公室。"},{"en":"A company director in a skyscraper office may look down over the city streets below.","zh":"摩天大廈辦公室中的公司董事可能俯視下方城市街道。"},{"en":"If power is shown from a high office, the height symbolises distance from ordinary workers.","zh":"如果權力從高處辦公室呈現，高度就象徵與普通工人的距離。"},{"en":"The phrase links corporate authority with vertical urban space.","zh":"這個短語把企業權威與垂直城市空間連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"panoramic view of","meaning":"……的全景","examples":[{"en":"His office offers a panoramic view of the city.","zh":"他的辦公室提供城市全景。"},{"en":"A panoramic view of a place is a wide, sweeping view that shows a large area.","zh":"某地的全景，是展示大範圍的寬闊視野。"},{"en":"A hilltop restaurant may offer a panoramic view of the harbour.","zh":"山頂餐廳可能提供海港全景。"},{"en":"If a boss has a panoramic view of the city, the image can suggest control from above.","zh":"如果老闆擁有城市全景，畫面可以暗示由上而下的控制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broad visual perspective.","zh":"這個短語描述廣闊視覺角度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"there is never any mention of","meaning":"從未提及……","examples":[{"en":"There is never any mention of government in the film.","zh":"這部電影從未提及政府。"},{"en":"There is never any mention of something means the topic is not referred to at all.","zh":"“There is never any mention of” 某事指該題目完全沒有被提到。"},{"en":"In the school report, there is never any mention of how students feel.","zh":"在學校報告中，從未提及學生感受。"},{"en":"If government is never mentioned, the film may suggest that corporate power has replaced it.","zh":"如果政府從未被提及，電影可能暗示企業權力已取代政府。"},{"en":"The phrase draws attention to a meaningful absence.","zh":"這個短語把注意力引向有意義的缺席。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"by implication","meaning":"言下之意","examples":[{"en":"By implication, government has become obsolete.","zh":"言下之意，政府已變得過時。"},{"en":"By implication means suggested indirectly, even if not stated openly.","zh":"“By implication” 指間接暗示，即使沒有公開說出。"},{"en":"If a teacher praises only exam scores, by implication creativity may seem less important.","zh":"如果老師只稱讚考試分數，言下之意創意可能較不重要。"},{"en":"If a film shows no government, viewers may infer that public authority has disappeared.","zh":"如果電影沒有展示政府，觀眾可能推斷公共權威已消失。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an unstated but logical meaning.","zh":"這個短語引出未明說但合乎邏輯的意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"become obsolete","meaning":"變得過時","examples":[{"en":"The concept of government appears to have become obsolete.","zh":"政府這個概念看似已變得過時。"},{"en":"To become obsolete means to become outdated, unnecessary or no longer useful.","zh":"變得過時指變得落後、不必要或不再有用。"},{"en":"Some old phone chargers become obsolete when new devices use different ports.","zh":"當新裝置使用不同接口，一些舊手機充電器就會變得過時。"},{"en":"If government is obsolete in a story, private power may have taken over its role.","zh":"如果故事中的政府過時，私人權力可能已接管其角色。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being replaced by newer conditions or systems.","zh":"這個短語描述被較新條件或系統取代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"supreme industrialist","meaning":"至高無上的工業巨頭","examples":[{"en":"Fredersen is the city’s supreme industrialist.","zh":"Fredersen 是這座城市至高無上的工業巨頭。"},{"en":"A supreme industrialist is the most powerful business leader in an industrial system.","zh":"至高無上的工業巨頭，是工業體系中最有權力的商業領袖。"},{"en":"In a company town, one supreme industrialist may control factories, housing and wages.","zh":"在公司城鎮中，一名至高無上的工業巨頭可能控制工廠、住房和工資。"},{"en":"If an industrialist has supreme power, workers may have little protection from decisions above them.","zh":"如果工業家擁有至高權力，工人對上層決定可能幾乎沒有保障。"},{"en":"The phrase presents business authority as almost ruler-like.","zh":"這個短語把商業權威呈現得近乎統治者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"magician-scientist","meaning":"魔法師兼科學家","examples":[{"en":"Rotwang is portrayed as a magician-scientist.","zh":"Rotwang 被描繪為魔法師兼科學家。"},{"en":"A magician-scientist is a character who combines mysterious magic-like power with scientific invention.","zh":"魔法師兼科學家，是結合神秘魔法般力量與科學發明的角色。"},{"en":"A story may include a magician-scientist who builds robots in a dark laboratory.","zh":"故事可能有一位魔法師兼科學家，在黑暗實驗室中製造機械人。"},{"en":"If science is shown with magic-like danger, technology can feel strange and threatening.","zh":"如果科學以魔法般危險呈現，科技就可能感覺奇怪而具威脅。"},{"en":"The phrase blends fantasy and science in one figure.","zh":"這個短語把幻想和科學融合在一個人物中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cohort","meaning":"同夥；伙伴","examples":[{"en":"Rotwang is Fredersen’s magician-scientist cohort.","zh":"Rotwang 是 Fredersen 的魔法師兼科學家同夥。"},{"en":"A cohort is an associate, companion or partner in a shared activity, often with a slightly secretive tone.","zh":"同夥或伙伴，是共同活動中的助手、同伴或合作人，常略帶秘密意味。"},{"en":"A dishonest manager and his cohort may plan how to hide company losses.","zh":"不誠實經理和其同夥可能計劃如何隱藏公司虧損。"},{"en":"If a scientist is a ruler’s cohort, technology may serve power rather than society.","zh":"如果科學家是統治者同夥，科技可能服務權力而不是社會。"},{"en":"The word suggests partnership, sometimes in questionable actions.","zh":"這個詞暗示合作關係，有時涉及可疑行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"so far, so good","meaning":"到目前為止一切尚好","examples":[{"en":"So far, so good: the film’s visual symbolism is extremely effective.","zh":"到目前為止一切尚好：這部電影的視覺象徵極其有效。"},{"en":"So far, so good means things are acceptable or successful up to this point.","zh":"“So far, so good” 指事情到目前為止可以接受或成功。"},{"en":"A student may say “so far, so good” after finishing the first two sections of an exam calmly.","zh":"學生平靜完成考試前兩部分後，可能說「到目前為止一切尚好」。"},{"en":"If the early parts of a film work well, criticism may begin only when the story weakens later.","zh":"如果電影早段運作良好，批評可能只在後來故事變弱時開始。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a temporary positive judgement.","zh":"這個短語給出暫時正面判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"speak for themselves","meaning":"不言自明","examples":[{"en":"The film’s images are powerful enough to speak for themselves.","zh":"這部電影的影像有足夠力量，不言自明。"},{"en":"If images speak for themselves, they are clear and strong without needing much explanation.","zh":"如果影像不言自明，它們就是清楚而有力，不需要太多解釋。"},{"en":"A photograph of a flooded classroom may speak for itself about poor building maintenance.","zh":"水浸課室的照片本身可能足以說明建築維修差。"},{"en":"If visual evidence is obvious, extra commentary may be unnecessary.","zh":"如果視覺證據很明顯，額外評論可能不必要。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that the meaning is self-evident.","zh":"這個短語暗示意思本身已很清楚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"impeccable","meaning":"無可挑剔的","examples":[{"en":"The visual imagery is impeccable in its symbolism.","zh":"視覺意象在象徵手法上無可挑剔。"},{"en":"Impeccable means extremely good, faultless or without obvious mistakes.","zh":"“Impeccable” 指極好、無瑕或沒有明顯錯誤。"},{"en":"A student may give an impeccable presentation if the speech is clear, organised and confident.","zh":"如果學生演講清晰、有組織又自信，就可能作出無可挑剔的匯報。"},{"en":"If symbolism is impeccable, every image supports the meaning precisely.","zh":"如果象徵手法無可挑剔，每個影像都精準支持意思。"},{"en":"The word expresses very strong praise.","zh":"這個詞表達非常強烈的讚賞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"symbolism and cynicism","meaning":"象徵手法和犬儒態度","examples":[{"en":"The film is powerful in both its symbolism and its cynicism.","zh":"這部電影在象徵手法和犬儒態度上都很有力量。"},{"en":"Symbolism and cynicism mean meaningful visual representation together with a dark, distrustful view of human systems.","zh":"象徵手法和犬儒態度，指有意義的視覺代表，加上對人類系統的黑暗、不信任看法。"},{"en":"A cartoon showing politicians as puppets may use symbolism and cynicism at the same time.","zh":"把政客畫成木偶的漫畫，可能同時使用象徵手法和犬儒態度。"},{"en":"If a film uses machines to represent industry and shows power as cruel, both elements are present.","zh":"如果電影用機器代表工業，並把權力展示為殘酷，兩種元素就同時存在。"},{"en":"The phrase combines artistic meaning with critical distrust.","zh":"這個短語結合藝術意義與批判性不信任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sentimental storyline","meaning":"感傷的故事情節","examples":[{"en":"The writer criticises the film’s sentimental storyline.","zh":"作者批評這部電影感傷的故事情節。"},{"en":"A sentimental storyline is a plot that relies heavily on emotion, love or simple moral feeling.","zh":"感傷的故事情節，是高度依賴情感、愛或簡單道德感的情節。"},{"en":"A drama may have a sentimental storyline if every problem is solved by one tearful speech.","zh":"如果劇集每個問題都由一場流淚演說解決，它可能有感傷的故事情節。"},{"en":"If a serious social conflict ends through love alone, some viewers may find the story too soft.","zh":"如果嚴重社會衝突只靠愛解決，有些觀眾可能覺得故事太軟弱。"},{"en":"The phrase can be critical when emotion replaces realistic complexity.","zh":"當情感取代現實複雜性時，這個短語可以帶批評意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"instantly fall in love with","meaning":"立即愛上……","examples":[{"en":"Freder instantly falls in love with Maria.","zh":"Freder 立即愛上 Maria。"},{"en":"To instantly fall in love with someone means to feel romantic love immediately after meeting or seeing them.","zh":"立即愛上某人，指在遇見或看見某人後立刻產生愛情。"},{"en":"In a fairy tale, a prince may instantly fall in love with a stranger at a dance.","zh":"在童話中，王子可能在舞會上立即愛上一名陌生人。"},{"en":"If a character falls in love too quickly, the story may feel unrealistic or sentimental.","zh":"如果角色太快墮入愛河，故事可能顯得不現實或感傷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sudden romantic attraction.","zh":"這個短語描述突然的浪漫吸引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"visionary","meaning":"有遠見的人","examples":[{"en":"Maria is portrayed as a visionary leader.","zh":"Maria 被描繪為有遠見的領袖。"},{"en":"A visionary is someone who imagines a better future and inspires others with that vision.","zh":"有遠見的人，是能想像更好未來並以該願景啟發他人的人。"},{"en":"A school principal can be visionary if she sees how technology and care can improve learning.","zh":"如果校長看見科技和關懷如何改善學習，她就可以是有遠見的人。"},{"en":"If a leader gives people hope, followers may trust them even during hardship.","zh":"如果領袖給人希望，追隨者即使在困境中也可能信任他們。"},{"en":"The word suggests future-facing imagination and leadership.","zh":"這個詞暗示面向未來的想像力和領導力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"underground movement","meaning":"地下運動","examples":[{"en":"Maria leads an underground movement among the workers.","zh":"Maria 在工人之中領導一場地下運動。"},{"en":"An underground movement is a secret or unofficial group working for social or political change.","zh":"地下運動是為社會或政治改變而秘密或非正式運作的群體。"},{"en":"Students in a story may form an underground movement to oppose unfair school rules.","zh":"故事中的學生可能組成地下運動，反對不公平校規。"},{"en":"If open protest is dangerous, people may organise underground instead.","zh":"如果公開抗議危險，人們可能改為地下組織。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests hidden resistance or organised belief.","zh":"這個短語暗示隱藏的抵抗或有組織信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pseudo-religious movement","meaning":"類宗教地下運動","examples":[{"en":"Maria leads an underground pseudo-religious movement.","zh":"Maria 領導一場類宗教地下運動。"},{"en":"A pseudo-religious movement is a movement that looks or sounds religious without being a formal religion.","zh":"類宗教運動是看起來或聽起來像宗教，但不是正式宗教的運動。"},{"en":"A leader may use candles, chants and moral language to create a pseudo-religious atmosphere.","zh":"領袖可能使用蠟燭、吟唱和道德語言，營造類宗教氣氛。"},{"en":"If workers gather around prophecy and faith-like language, the movement may feel religious in style.","zh":"如果工人圍繞預言和類似信仰的語言聚集，運動在形式上可能像宗教。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests imitation of religious form.","zh":"這個短語暗示對宗教形式的模仿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"preach that","meaning":"宣揚……","examples":[{"en":"Maria preaches that the workers should wait peacefully.","zh":"Maria 宣揚工人應和平等待。"},{"en":"To preach that something is true means to teach or urge it strongly, often with moral or religious force.","zh":"“Preach that” 某事為真指強烈教導或敦促它，常帶道德或宗教力量。"},{"en":"A coach may preach that teamwork matters more than individual glory.","zh":"教練可能宣揚團隊合作比個人榮耀更重要。"},{"en":"If a leader preaches patience, followers may delay direct action.","zh":"如果領袖宣揚忍耐，追隨者可能推遲直接行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated moral teaching or persuasion.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆的道德教導或說服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rebel","meaning":"反抗","examples":[{"en":"Maria tells the workers not to rebel against the system.","zh":"Maria 告訴工人不要反抗體制。"},{"en":"To rebel means to resist or fight against authority, rules or a system.","zh":"反抗指抵抗或對抗權威、規則或體制。"},{"en":"Students may rebel against unfair rules if they feel no one listens to them.","zh":"如果學生覺得沒有人聽他們說話，可能反抗不公平規則。"},{"en":"If workers rebel, the existing order may be threatened.","zh":"如果工人反抗，現有秩序可能受到威脅。"},{"en":"The word describes active resistance, not quiet disagreement.","zh":"這個詞描述積極抵抗，而不是安靜不同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"await the arrival of","meaning":"等待……的到來","examples":[{"en":"The workers are encouraged to await the arrival of a mediator.","zh":"工人被鼓勵等待調解者的到來。"},{"en":"To await the arrival of someone means to wait for that person to come.","zh":"“Await the arrival of” 某人指等待該人到來。"},{"en":"A family may await the arrival of a doctor when a child is seriously ill.","zh":"孩子重病時，家庭可能等待醫生的到來。"},{"en":"If workers wait for a mediator, they may avoid taking action themselves.","zh":"如果工人等待調解者，他們可能避免自己採取行動。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests expectation and delay.","zh":"這個短語暗示期待和延遲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mediator between","meaning":"……之間的調解者","examples":[{"en":"Freder becomes the mediator between capital and labour.","zh":"Freder 成為資本與勞工之間的調解者。"},{"en":"A mediator between two sides is someone who helps them communicate and reach agreement.","zh":"兩方之間的調解者，是幫助他們溝通和達成共識的人。"},{"en":"A teacher may act as a mediator between two students after an argument.","zh":"兩名學生爭吵後，老師可能充當他們之間的調解者。"},{"en":"If workers and bosses cannot trust each other, a mediator may reduce conflict.","zh":"如果工人和老闆不能互相信任，調解者可能減少衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a person placed between opposing groups.","zh":"這個短語描述位於對立群體之間的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"capital and labour","meaning":"資本與勞工","examples":[{"en":"The film attempts to reconcile capital and labour.","zh":"這部電影嘗試調和資本與勞工。"},{"en":"Capital and labour refer to business owners or money on one side, and workers on the other.","zh":"資本與勞工指一方是企業擁有人或資金，另一方是工人。"},{"en":"In a factory dispute, capital may want lower costs while labour wants fair wages.","zh":"在工廠糾紛中，資本可能想降低成本，而勞工想要公平工資。"},{"en":"If capital and labour are in conflict, production and social peace may both suffer.","zh":"如果資本與勞工衝突，生產和社會和平都可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the two sides of industrial relations.","zh":"這個短語描述工業關係中的兩方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be embodied by","meaning":"由……體現","examples":[{"en":"The idea of the heart is embodied by Freder’s love.","zh":"心的理念由 Freder 的愛體現。"},{"en":"To be embodied by something means to be represented or made visible through it.","zh":"“Be embodied by” 某事指透過它被代表或變得可見。"},{"en":"A school’s values may be embodied by a teacher who treats every student fairly.","zh":"學校價值觀可能由公平對待每名學生的老師體現。"},{"en":"If an abstract idea is embodied in a character, viewers understand it through action and emotion.","zh":"如果抽象想法體現在角色身上，觀眾就透過行動和情感理解它。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an idea with a concrete form.","zh":"這個短語把想法與具體形式連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"write the screenplay","meaning":"編寫劇本","examples":[{"en":"Lang wrote the screenplay with Thea von Harbou.","zh":"Lang 與 Thea von Harbou 編寫劇本。"},{"en":"To write the screenplay means to create the script for a film, including scenes, dialogue and action.","zh":"編寫劇本指創作電影的文字腳本，包括場景、對白和動作。"},{"en":"A film student may write the screenplay before actors are chosen.","zh":"電影學生可能在選角前先編寫劇本。"},{"en":"If the screenplay is weak, even strong images may not fully save the story.","zh":"如果劇本薄弱，即使影像強烈也未必能完全拯救故事。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to writing the film’s written plan.","zh":"這個短語指撰寫電影的文字計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in collaboration with","meaning":"與……合作","examples":[{"en":"Lang wrote the screenplay in collaboration with his then-wife.","zh":"Lang 與他當時的妻子合作編寫劇本。"},{"en":"In collaboration with someone means working together with that person.","zh":"“In collaboration with” 某人指與該人一起工作。"},{"en":"A teacher may design a lesson in collaboration with the school librarian.","zh":"老師可能與學校圖書館主任合作設計課堂。"},{"en":"If a film is written in collaboration, its ideas may come from more than one mind.","zh":"如果電影是合作編寫，其想法可能來自多於一個人。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises joint work.","zh":"這個短語強調共同工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"then-wife","meaning":"當時的妻子","examples":[{"en":"Thea von Harbou was Lang’s then-wife.","zh":"Thea von Harbou 是 Lang 當時的妻子。"},{"en":"Then-wife means the woman who was someone’s wife at that time, though not necessarily later.","zh":"當時的妻子，指某人在那個時候的妻子，但之後未必仍是。"},{"en":"A writer may thank his then-wife in an old book published before their divorce.","zh":"作家可能在離婚前出版的舊書中感謝他當時的妻子。"},{"en":"If a text says then-wife, it signals a relationship that belonged to that period.","zh":"如果文本說當時的妻子，就是提示該關係屬於那個時期。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when marital status changed later.","zh":"這個短語在婚姻狀況後來改變時很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"flee from","meaning":"逃離……","examples":[{"en":"Lang fled from the Nazis in 1933.","zh":"Lang 在1933年逃離納粹。"},{"en":"To flee from someone or something means to escape because of danger or fear.","zh":"逃離某人或某事指因危險或恐懼而逃走。"},{"en":"Families may flee from a burning building when the fire alarm sounds.","zh":"火警鐘響起時，家庭可能逃離燃燒中的建築物。"},{"en":"If artists flee from a regime, they may continue their work in another country.","zh":"如果藝術家逃離某政權，他們可能在另一國繼續工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes urgent escape from threat.","zh":"這個短語描述因威脅而急切逃走。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"continue a successful career","meaning":"延續成功的事業","examples":[{"en":"Lang continued a successful career in Hollywood.","zh":"Lang 在荷里活延續成功的事業。"},{"en":"To continue a successful career means to keep achieving professional success after a change or move.","zh":"延續成功的事業，指在變化或遷移後仍保持專業成功。"},{"en":"A teacher may continue a successful career after moving to a new school.","zh":"老師轉到新學校後，可能延續成功的教學生涯。"},{"en":"If a director leaves one country but keeps making important films, the career continues strongly.","zh":"如果導演離開一個國家但繼續拍重要電影，其事業就強勢延續。"},{"en":"The phrase shows professional success lasting beyond a disruption.","zh":"這個短語顯示專業成功在干擾後仍然持續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"under the Hitler regime","meaning":"在希特拉政權下","examples":[{"en":"Von Harbou continued making films under the Hitler regime.","zh":"Von Harbou 在希特拉政權下繼續拍電影。"},{"en":"Under the Hitler regime means during the period when Hitler and the Nazi government controlled Germany.","zh":"在希特拉政權下，指希特拉和納粹政府控制德國的時期。"},{"en":"Artists working under an oppressive regime may face pressure to follow official ideas.","zh":"在壓迫性政權下工作的藝術家，可能面對遵從官方思想的壓力。"},{"en":"If someone continued working under that regime, later readers may judge the choice politically or morally.","zh":"如果某人在該政權下繼續工作，後來讀者可能從政治或道德角度評價這個選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase places an action within a specific authoritarian historical context.","zh":"這個短語把行動放在特定威權歷史背景中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"constant tension","meaning":"持續的張力","examples":[{"en":"There is a constant tension between the script and the imagery.","zh":"劇本與影像之間存在持續的張力。"},{"en":"Constant tension is continuing conflict or disagreement between two elements.","zh":"持續的張力，是兩個元素之間不斷的衝突或不一致。"},{"en":"In group projects, there may be constant tension between speed and quality.","zh":"在小組項目中，速度和質素之間可能有持續張力。"},{"en":"If a film’s images are harsh but its story is sentimental, the two parts pull in different directions.","zh":"如果電影影像尖銳但故事感傷，兩部分就朝不同方向拉扯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an ongoing unresolved conflict.","zh":"這個短語描述持續而未解決的衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"too-tidy platitudes","meaning":"過分簡化而陳腔濫調的說法","examples":[{"en":"The writer criticises the script’s too-tidy platitudes.","zh":"作者批評劇本中過分簡化而陳腔濫調的說法。"},{"en":"Too-tidy platitudes are overly simple moral statements that make complex problems seem easy.","zh":"過分簡化而陳腔濫調的說法，是把複雜問題說得很容易的過度簡單道德陳述。"},{"en":"Saying “just be kind” may be a too-tidy platitude if a school has deep bullying problems.","zh":"如果學校有深層欺凌問題，只說「友善一點」可能是過分簡化的陳腔濫調。"},{"en":"If a film solves class conflict with a neat slogan, the answer may feel unrealistic.","zh":"如果電影用整齊口號解決階級衝突，答案可能感覺不現實。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises simple comforting ideas that avoid real complexity.","zh":"這個短語批評避開真實複雜性的簡單安慰性想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"uncompromisingly caustic","meaning":"毫不妥協而尖銳的","examples":[{"en":"Lang’s imagery is uncompromisingly caustic.","zh":"Lang 的影像毫不妥協而尖銳。"},{"en":"Uncompromisingly caustic means sharply critical without softening the attack.","zh":"毫不妥協而尖銳，指批評非常尖銳，沒有把攻擊語氣軟化。"},{"en":"A cartoon may be uncompromisingly caustic if it shows greed as a monster eating the poor.","zh":"如果漫畫把貪婪畫成吞食窮人的怪物，它可能毫不妥協而尖銳。"},{"en":"If images expose cruelty directly, viewers cannot easily ignore the criticism.","zh":"如果影像直接揭露殘酷，觀眾就難以忽視批評。"},{"en":"The phrase describes harsh, fearless social criticism.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴厲而無畏的社會批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"caustic vigour","meaning":"尖銳有力的風格","examples":[{"en":"The imagery possesses an uncompromisingly caustic vigour.","zh":"這些影像具有毫不妥協而尖銳有力的風格。"},{"en":"Caustic vigour is sharp, energetic critical force.","zh":"尖銳有力的風格，是尖銳、充滿能量的批判力量。"},{"en":"A speech has caustic vigour if it attacks injustice with anger, clarity and power.","zh":"如果演講以憤怒、清晰和力量攻擊不公義，它就有尖銳有力的風格。"},{"en":"If a film’s images are visually forceful and socially biting, they have caustic vigour.","zh":"如果電影影像在視覺上有力且在社會批評上辛辣，它們就有尖銳力量。"},{"en":"The phrase praises strong criticism, not gentle beauty.","zh":"這個短語讚揚強烈批評，而不是溫和美感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"visual imagery","meaning":"視覺意象","examples":[{"en":"Lang’s visual imagery is more powerful than the film’s message.","zh":"Lang 的視覺意象比電影訊息更有力量。"},{"en":"Visual imagery means pictures, symbols and visual details used to create meaning.","zh":"視覺意象指用來創造意義的圖像、符號和視覺細節。"},{"en":"A poster’s visual imagery may show a cracked earth to warn about drought.","zh":"海報的視覺意象可能展示龜裂大地，以警告乾旱。"},{"en":"If visual imagery is powerful, viewers may remember images more than dialogue.","zh":"如果視覺意象有力，觀眾可能記住影像多於對白。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on meaning created through sight.","zh":"這個短語強調透過視覺創造的意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"to my mind","meaning":"在我看來","examples":[{"en":"To my mind, the workers need their own political consciousness.","zh":"在我看來，工人需要自己的政治意識。"},{"en":"To my mind means in my opinion or as I see it.","zh":"“To my mind” 指在我看來或按我的理解。"},{"en":"To my mind, students learn vocabulary better when examples show real situations.","zh":"在我看來，例子展示真實情況時，學生學詞彙會更好。"},{"en":"If a writer uses this phrase, they are clearly giving a personal judgement.","zh":"如果作者使用這個短語，就是清楚表達個人判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an opinion while sounding thoughtful.","zh":"這個短語引出意見，同時聽起來較審慎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"not so much…as…","meaning":"與其說……不如說……","examples":[{"en":"It is not so much love as political awareness that the workers require.","zh":"工人需要的與其說是愛，不如說是政治意識。"},{"en":"Not so much A as B means the real point is B rather than A.","zh":"“Not so much A as B” 指真正重點是 B，而不是 A。"},{"en":"The problem is not so much laziness as poor time management.","zh":"問題與其說是懶惰，不如說是時間管理差。"},{"en":"If workers need awareness more than romance, the writer rejects the film’s simple solution.","zh":"如果工人需要意識多於浪漫愛情，作者就是拒絕電影的簡單解方。"},{"en":"The phrase corrects a mistaken focus by replacing it with a better one.","zh":"這個短語透過替換成更好焦點來糾正錯誤重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"mediate between","meaning":"在……之間調解","examples":[{"en":"The heart is supposed to mediate between the head and the hands.","zh":"心被認為應在頭腦與雙手之間調解。"},{"en":"To mediate between two sides means to help them communicate and find balance or agreement.","zh":"在兩方之間調解，指幫助它們溝通並尋找平衡或共識。"},{"en":"A parent may mediate between two siblings who are fighting over a shared room.","zh":"父母可能在兩個為共用房間爭吵的兄弟姊妹之間調解。"},{"en":"If one group plans and another group works, a mediator may try to connect decision and labour.","zh":"如果一個群體計劃，另一個群體工作，調解者可能嘗試連接決策與勞動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes acting between opposing or separate sides.","zh":"這個短語描述在對立或分離的兩方之間行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"develop political consciousness","meaning":"培養政治意識","examples":[{"en":"The workers need to develop their own political consciousness.","zh":"工人需要培養自己的政治意識。"},{"en":"To develop political consciousness means to become aware of power, rights, systems and collective interests.","zh":"培養政治意識，指變得意識到權力、權利、制度和集體利益。"},{"en":"Students may develop political consciousness when they learn how laws affect housing and wages.","zh":"當學生學習法律如何影響住房和工資時，可能培養政治意識。"},{"en":"If workers understand why they are exploited, they can organise more effectively.","zh":"如果工人理解自己為何被剝削，就能更有效組織起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growing awareness of social and political power.","zh":"這個短語描述對社會和政治權力的意識增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"act accordingly","meaning":"採取相應行動","examples":[{"en":"People should understand the system and act accordingly.","zh":"人們應理解體制並採取相應行動。"},{"en":"To act accordingly means to behave in a way that fits what one knows or what the situation requires.","zh":"採取相應行動，指根據自己所知或情況所需來行動。"},{"en":"If a student knows an exam is tomorrow, they should act accordingly and revise tonight.","zh":"如果學生知道明天有考試，就應採取相應行動，今晚溫習。"},{"en":"If citizens understand how companies influence them, they can make choices that match that understanding.","zh":"如果市民理解公司如何影響自己，就能作出符合該理解的選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase links knowledge with appropriate action.","zh":"這個短語把知識與適當行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"through the ballot box","meaning":"透過投票箱；透過選舉","examples":[{"en":"Citizens can exercise power through the ballot box.","zh":"市民可以透過投票箱行使權力。"},{"en":"Through the ballot box means by voting in elections.","zh":"透過投票箱指透過在選舉中投票。"},{"en":"Residents may express disagreement with local policies through the ballot box.","zh":"居民可能透過投票箱表達對本地政策的不滿。"},{"en":"If people vote, they can influence who makes laws and public decisions.","zh":"如果人們投票，就能影響誰制定法律和公共決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes democratic political action.","zh":"這個短語描述民主政治行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"buying power","meaning":"購買力","examples":[{"en":"Consumers can influence corporations through their buying power.","zh":"消費者可以透過購買力影響企業。"},{"en":"Buying power is the ability of consumers to affect companies through what they choose to buy or not buy.","zh":"購買力是消費者透過選擇買或不買甚麼來影響公司的能力。"},{"en":"If shoppers stop buying wasteful packaging, their buying power can pressure companies to change.","zh":"如果購物者停止購買浪費包裝，其購買力可以迫使公司改變。"},{"en":"When many people choose ethical products, businesses may adjust their practices.","zh":"當許多人選擇道德產品，企業可能調整做法。"},{"en":"The phrase treats spending decisions as a form of influence.","zh":"這個短語把消費決定視為一種影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sceptical resistance to","meaning":"對……抱懷疑態度並加以抵抗","examples":[{"en":"The writer encourages sceptical resistance to materialistic fantasies.","zh":"作者鼓勵人們對物質主義幻想抱懷疑態度並加以抵抗。"},{"en":"Sceptical resistance to something means questioning it carefully and refusing to accept it too easily.","zh":"對某事抱懷疑態度並加以抵抗，指仔細質疑它，並拒絕輕易接受。"},{"en":"Students need sceptical resistance to online rumours before sharing them.","zh":"學生分享網上謠言前，需要對它們抱懷疑態度並加以抵抗。"},{"en":"If advertising promises happiness through products, sceptical resistance can protect consumers.","zh":"如果廣告承諾產品帶來幸福，懷疑式抵抗可以保護消費者。"},{"en":"The phrase combines doubt with active refusal.","zh":"這個短語結合懷疑和主動拒絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"materialistic fantasies","meaning":"物質主義幻想","examples":[{"en":"Advertising often promotes materialistic fantasies.","zh":"廣告常宣傳物質主義幻想。"},{"en":"Materialistic fantasies are dreams or images suggesting that possessions and wealth will bring happiness or status.","zh":"物質主義幻想，是暗示財物和財富會帶來幸福或地位的夢想或形象。"},{"en":"A luxury car advert may sell the materialistic fantasy of success and admiration.","zh":"豪華汽車廣告可能販賣成功和受人羨慕的物質主義幻想。"},{"en":"If people believe such fantasies, they may buy things they do not need.","zh":"如果人們相信這些幻想，可能購買自己不需要的東西。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises consumer dreams built around money and objects.","zh":"這個短語批評圍繞金錢和物件建立的消費夢想。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"all the same","meaning":"儘管如此","examples":[{"en":"All the same, the film remains highly relevant today.","zh":"儘管如此，這部電影今天仍高度相關。"},{"en":"All the same means despite what has just been said, the following point is still true.","zh":"“All the same” 指儘管剛才所說為真，接下來的觀點仍然成立。"},{"en":"The essay has grammar mistakes; all the same, its argument is strong.","zh":"這篇文章有文法錯誤；儘管如此，其論點很有力。"},{"en":"If a film has weaknesses but still matters, this phrase introduces the balancing judgement.","zh":"如果電影有弱點但仍然重要，這個短語就引出平衡判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase signals concession followed by a positive or contrasting point.","zh":"這個短語表示讓步後接正面或對比觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"accurate representation of","meaning":"對……的準確呈現","examples":[{"en":"The film is an accurate representation of modern industrial relations.","zh":"這部電影是對現代工業關係的準確呈現。"},{"en":"An accurate representation of something shows it truthfully or closely matches reality.","zh":"對某事的準確呈現，指真實展示它或與現實非常接近。"},{"en":"A school survey gives an accurate representation of students’ views only if many students answer honestly.","zh":"只有許多學生誠實作答，學校調查才能準確呈現學生意見。"},{"en":"If a film shows real patterns of power and labour, it may represent society accurately.","zh":"如果電影展示真實的權力和勞動模式，它就可能準確呈現社會。"},{"en":"The phrase praises truthfulness or closeness to reality.","zh":"這個短語讚揚真實性或與現實接近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"industrial and social relations","meaning":"工業和社會關係","examples":[{"en":"Metropolis explores industrial and social relations.","zh":"《大都會》探索工業和社會關係。"},{"en":"Industrial and social relations are the connections between work, business, class, power and society.","zh":"工業和社會關係，是工作、商業、階級、權力和社會之間的連繫。"},{"en":"A factory town shows industrial and social relations when wages affect housing, schools and family life.","zh":"當工資影響住房、學校和家庭生活，工廠城鎮就展示工業和社會關係。"},{"en":"If bosses and workers live separate lives, both workplace and social relations are divided.","zh":"如果老闆和工人過着分離生活，工作關係和社會關係都被分化。"},{"en":"The phrase links economic production with social structure.","zh":"這個短語把經濟生產與社會結構連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"at any time since","meaning":"自……以來的任何時候","examples":[{"en":"The film is more relevant now than at any time since its release.","zh":"這部電影現在比自上映以來任何時候都更相關。"},{"en":"At any time since means during any point in the period after a past event.","zh":"“At any time since” 指在某過去事件之後的任何時間點。"},{"en":"The school’s safety rules matter more now than at any time since the accident.","zh":"自那次意外以來，學校安全規則現在比任何時候都更重要。"},{"en":"If a film becomes more relevant decades later, later society may resemble its warnings.","zh":"如果電影數十年後變得更相關，後來社會可能像它的警告。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the present with all moments after a past point.","zh":"這個短語把現在與某過去時間點之後的所有時刻比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"original release","meaning":"最初上映","examples":[{"en":"Metropolis remains influential long after its original release.","zh":"《大都會》在最初上映很久之後仍具影響力。"},{"en":"Original release means the first time a film, book or product was made available to the public.","zh":"最初上映指電影、書籍或產品第一次向公眾推出。"},{"en":"A film may become popular again many years after its original release.","zh":"一部電影可能在最初上映多年後再次流行。"},{"en":"If a movie is still discussed after its first showing, its influence has lasted.","zh":"如果電影在首次放映後仍被討論，其影響力就是持久的。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the first public appearance of a work.","zh":"這個短語指出作品第一次公開面世。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"potent movie symbol","meaning":"強而有力的電影象徵","examples":[{"en":"Fredersen remains a potent movie symbol of corporate power.","zh":"Fredersen 仍是企業權力的強而有力電影象徵。"},{"en":"A potent movie symbol is a film image or character that strongly represents a larger idea.","zh":"強而有力的電影象徵，是強烈代表較大想法的電影影像或角色。"},{"en":"A lonely child in a war film can become a potent movie symbol of innocence lost.","zh":"戰爭電影中的孤獨孩子可以成為失去純真的強而有力電影象徵。"},{"en":"If Fredersen symbolises corporate power, viewers can connect one character with a whole system.","zh":"如果 Fredersen 象徵企業權力，觀眾就能把一個角色與整個系統連接。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a powerful symbol created by cinema.","zh":"這個短語描述由電影創造的有力象徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a handful of","meaning":"少數幾個……","examples":[{"en":"A handful of corporate leaders control enormous resources.","zh":"少數幾個企業領袖控制龐大資源。"},{"en":"A handful of people or things means a small number of them.","zh":"“A handful of” 人或物指少數幾個。"},{"en":"A handful of students may stay after class to ask extra questions.","zh":"少數幾名學生可能下課後留下問額外問題。"},{"en":"If a handful of leaders control great wealth, power is concentrated.","zh":"如果少數領袖控制巨大財富，權力就是集中化。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a small group, often surprisingly powerful or important.","zh":"這個短語暗示一個小群體，常令人意外地有權力或重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"elusive corporate figureheads","meaning":"難以捉摸的企業領袖","examples":[{"en":"Fredersen represents elusive corporate figureheads.","zh":"Fredersen 代表難以捉摸的企業領袖。"},{"en":"Elusive corporate figureheads are powerful company leaders who are hard for ordinary people to see, question or hold responsible.","zh":"難以捉摸的企業領袖，是普通人難以見到、質問或追究責任的有權勢公司領袖。"},{"en":"Customers may complain about a company but never know who its real corporate figureheads are.","zh":"顧客可能投訴一間公司，卻永遠不知道真正企業領袖是誰。"},{"en":"If leaders are elusive, responsibility can feel distant and hidden.","zh":"如果領袖難以捉摸，責任就會感覺遙遠而隱藏。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises powerful business figures who remain out of reach.","zh":"這個短語批評遙不可及的有權勢商業人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"increasingly treat","meaning":"日益將……視為","examples":[{"en":"Some corporations increasingly treat the world as a single market.","zh":"一些企業日益將世界視為單一市場。"},{"en":"To increasingly treat something in a certain way means to do so more and more over time.","zh":"日益以某方式看待某事，指隨時間越來越這樣做。"},{"en":"Schools increasingly treat digital skills as essential for every subject.","zh":"學校日益將數碼技能視為每科都必需的能力。"},{"en":"If companies increasingly see the world as one market, local differences may be ignored.","zh":"如果公司日益把世界看成單一市場，本地差異可能被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a growing pattern in behaviour or attitude.","zh":"這個短語描述行為或態度中日益增長的模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"global village","meaning":"地球村","examples":[{"en":"The world is increasingly treated as a global village.","zh":"世界日益被視為地球村。"},{"en":"A global village is the idea that the world feels closely connected through travel, trade and communication.","zh":"地球村是指世界透過旅遊、貿易和通訊而感覺緊密相連的想法。"},{"en":"Social media can make distant countries feel like part of the same global village.","zh":"社交媒體可以令遙遠國家感覺像同一地球村的一部分。"},{"en":"If companies treat the world as one village, they may sell the same products across many cultures.","zh":"如果公司把世界視為一個村落，它們可能在多種文化中銷售同一產品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes worldwide connection, sometimes with loss of local difference.","zh":"這個短語描述全球連繫，有時也伴隨本地差異流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"agree with the claims of","meaning":"與作者的主張一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether statements agree with the claims of the writer.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與作者的主張一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the claims of the writer means to match what the writer argues or believes.","zh":"與作者的主張一致，指符合作者所論證或相信的內容。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students should look for evidence before deciding whether a statement agrees with the writer.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先尋找證據，再判斷陳述是否與作者一致。"},{"en":"If a statement changes the writer’s meaning, it does not agree with the claim.","zh":"如果陳述改變作者意思，它就不符合該主張。"},{"en":"The phrase is used for questions about the writer’s views.","zh":"這個短語用於關於作者觀點的題目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與作者觀點矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A “No” response means that the statement contradicts the writer’s views.","zh":"“No” 回應表示該陳述與作者觀點矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what that person thinks or argues.","zh":"與某人觀點矛盾，指說出與該人想法或論點相反的內容。"},{"en":"If a teacher says revision is necessary, a statement saying revision is useless contradicts her view.","zh":"如果老師說溫習是必要的，而陳述說溫習無用，就與她的觀點矛盾。"},{"en":"In reading tests, contradiction must be based on the passage, not personal opinion.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，矛盾必須基於文章，而不是個人意見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct conflict with an expressed view.","zh":"這個短語描述與已表達觀點的直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"The answer is not given if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"如果無法判斷作者想法，答案就是 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"無法判斷指沒有足夠資料作決定。"},{"en":"If a passage mentions a director but not his favourite colour, it is impossible to say what it is.","zh":"如果文章提到一位導演但沒有提及他最喜歡的顏色，就無法判斷是甚麼。"},{"en":"Students should choose NOT GIVEN when the passage gives no clear support or contradiction.","zh":"當文章沒有清楚支持或矛盾時，學生應選 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"The phrase warns students not to guess beyond the text.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生不要超出文本猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"inspiration for the film","meaning":"電影的靈感來源","examples":[{"en":"The New York skyline provided the inspiration for the film.","zh":"紐約天際線提供了這部電影的靈感來源。"},{"en":"Inspiration for the film means the idea, image or experience that helped create the movie.","zh":"電影的靈感來源，是幫助創造電影的想法、影像或經歷。"},{"en":"A childhood memory may provide the inspiration for a student’s short film.","zh":"童年回憶可能成為學生短片的靈感來源。"},{"en":"If a skyline inspires a film, its shapes may appear in the film’s visual design.","zh":"如果天際線啟發電影，其形狀可能出現在電影視覺設計中。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the creative source behind a movie.","zh":"這個短語指出電影背後的創作來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"come from","meaning":"來自……","examples":[{"en":"The inspiration for Metropolis came from Lang’s visit to the United States.","zh":"《大都會》的靈感來自 Lang 到訪美國。"},{"en":"To come from something means to originate in or be caused by that source.","zh":"“Come from” 某事指源於或由該來源造成。"},{"en":"A student’s interest in science may come from a visit to a space museum.","zh":"學生對科學的興趣可能來自參觀太空博物館。"},{"en":"If an idea comes from travel, the new place has shaped the creator’s imagination.","zh":"如果想法來自旅行，新地方就塑造了創作者想像。"},{"en":"The phrase explains origin or source.","zh":"這個短語解釋起源或來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"以……為原型","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether Fredersen was based on a real industrialist.","zh":"題目問 Fredersen 是否以真實工業家為原型。"},{"en":"To be based on something or someone means to be created using it as a model or source.","zh":"“Be based on” 某物或某人指以它作為模型或來源來創作。"},{"en":"A film character may be based on a teacher the writer knew at school.","zh":"電影角色可能以作者在學校認識的老師為原型。"},{"en":"If a character is based on a real person, viewers may look for similarities.","zh":"如果角色以真人為原型，觀眾可能尋找相似之處。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the source model behind a creation.","zh":"這個短語顯示創作背後的來源模型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"industrialist","meaning":"工業家","examples":[{"en":"Fredersen is portrayed as a powerful industrialist.","zh":"Fredersen 被描繪為一位有權勢的工業家。"},{"en":"An industrialist is a person who owns, manages or strongly influences large industries or factories.","zh":"工業家是擁有、管理或強烈影響大型工業或工廠的人。"},{"en":"A nineteenth-century industrialist might build textile mills and employ thousands of workers.","zh":"十九世紀工業家可能建立紡織廠並僱用數千名工人。"},{"en":"If an industrialist controls jobs and production, they may also influence politics and society.","zh":"如果工業家控制工作和生產，他也可能影響政治和社會。"},{"en":"The word refers to a powerful figure in industry.","zh":"這個詞指工業中的有權勢人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"opening of the film","meaning":"電影開場","examples":[{"en":"The opening of the film shows workers changing shifts.","zh":"電影開場展示工人換班。"},{"en":"The opening of the film means the first scene or first part of the movie.","zh":"電影開場指電影的第一場或第一部分。"},{"en":"The opening of a film can introduce its mood, setting and main conflict.","zh":"電影開場可以介紹氣氛、背景和主要衝突。"},{"en":"If workers appear in the opening, the film immediately stresses labour and control.","zh":"如果工人在開場出現，電影就立即強調勞動和控制。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the beginning section of a movie.","zh":"這個短語指電影開始部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"move energetically","meaning":"精力充沛地移動","examples":[{"en":"The workers do not move energetically in the opening sequence.","zh":"工人在開場段落中並沒有精力充沛地移動。"},{"en":"To move energetically means to move with strength, life and active force.","zh":"精力充沛地移動，指以力量、生命力和活躍感移動。"},{"en":"Children may move energetically during a sports lesson after sitting all morning.","zh":"孩子坐了一整個早上後，可能在體育課中精力充沛地移動。"},{"en":"If workers do not move energetically, they may look tired, controlled or lifeless.","zh":"如果工人沒有精力充沛地移動，他們可能看起來疲倦、受控制或無生命力。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts active movement with slow or exhausted movement.","zh":"這個短語把活躍動作與緩慢或疲憊動作作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"choose to remain","meaning":"選擇留下","examples":[{"en":"Von Harbou chose to remain in Germany.","zh":"Von Harbou 選擇留在德國。"},{"en":"To choose to remain means to decide to stay rather than leave.","zh":"選擇留下指決定留在原處而不是離開。"},{"en":"A student may choose to remain at school after class to finish a project.","zh":"學生可能選擇放學後留在學校完成項目。"},{"en":"If someone chooses to remain under a dangerous regime, the decision may be controversial.","zh":"如果某人選擇留在危險政權下，這決定可能具爭議。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses deliberate staying.","zh":"這個短語強調有意識地留下。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete the summary below","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to complete the summary below with words from the passage.","zh":"考生需要用文章中的詞語完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"Complete the summary below means fill in missing words in the short summary printed after the instruction.","zh":"“Complete the summary below” 指填寫指示下方短摘要中的缺漏字詞。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole summary first to understand its grammar and logic.","zh":"學生應先閱讀整段摘要，以理解其文法和邏輯。"},{"en":"If the answer must come from the passage, students should avoid using their own words.","zh":"如果答案必須來自文章，學生應避免使用自己的字詞。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案應包含不多於兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must use two words or fewer.","zh":"“No more than two words” 指答案必須使用兩個字或更少。"},{"en":"If the answer is “cheap labour,” it fits the two-word limit.","zh":"如果答案是 “cheap labour”，它符合兩詞限制。"},{"en":"Students may lose marks if they write three words when only two are allowed.","zh":"如果只准兩個詞而學生寫三個詞，可能會失分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict exam word limit.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格考試字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"depict a world of","meaning":"描繪一個充滿……的世界","examples":[{"en":"The director depicts a world of inequality and social division.","zh":"導演描繪一個充滿不平等和社會分化的世界。"},{"en":"To depict a world of something means to show an imagined or represented society full of that quality.","zh":"描繪一個充滿某事的世界，指展示一個充滿該特質的想像或被呈現的社會。"},{"en":"A novel may depict a world of fear where people cannot speak freely.","zh":"小說可能描繪一個充滿恐懼、人們不能自由說話的世界。"},{"en":"If a film depicts a divided world, viewers understand the social conflict quickly.","zh":"如果電影描繪分裂世界，觀眾很快理解社會衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how a creator presents a whole society or setting.","zh":"這個短語描述創作者如何呈現整個社會或背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"mindless masses","meaning":"缺乏自主思想的大眾","examples":[{"en":"The workers are presented as mindless masses.","zh":"工人被呈現為缺乏自主思想的大眾。"},{"en":"Mindless masses are large groups shown as having no independent thought or individuality.","zh":"缺乏自主思想的大眾，是被呈現為沒有獨立思想或個體性的大群體。"},{"en":"A bad school system may treat students as mindless masses if it ignores their different needs.","zh":"如果差劣學校制度忽視學生不同需要，就可能把學生當成缺乏自主思想的大眾。"},{"en":"If people move and think as one controlled group, they appear dehumanised.","zh":"如果人們像受控制群體一樣行動和思考，就顯得被去人性化。"},{"en":"The phrase is strongly critical and suggests loss of personal agency.","zh":"這個短語批評性很強，暗示個人能動性喪失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be treated as","meaning":"被當作……","examples":[{"en":"The underground workers are treated as machines.","zh":"地下工人被當作機器。"},{"en":"To be treated as something means to be dealt with as if one were that thing.","zh":"“Be treated as” 某物指被以彷彿自己是該物的方式對待。"},{"en":"Students should not be treated as numbers in a school report.","zh":"學生不應在學校報告中被當作數字。"},{"en":"If workers are treated as machines, their feelings and rights may be ignored.","zh":"如果工人被當作機器，其感受和權利可能被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how someone is regarded or handled.","zh":"這個短語描述某人被如何看待或處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"control the entire city","meaning":"控制整座城市","examples":[{"en":"Fredersen controls the entire city from his office.","zh":"Fredersen 從辦公室控制整座城市。"},{"en":"To control the entire city means to have power over all major systems, decisions and people in it.","zh":"控制整座城市，指掌握其中所有主要系統、決定和人。"},{"en":"In a dystopian story, one company may control the entire city’s transport, housing and jobs.","zh":"在反烏托邦故事中，一間公司可能控制整座城市的交通、住房和工作。"},{"en":"If one person controls a whole city, ordinary citizens may have little freedom.","zh":"如果一個人控制整座城市，普通市民可能幾乎沒有自由。"},{"en":"The phrase shows total or near-total authority.","zh":"這個短語顯示完全或近乎完全的權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"present something in abstract terms","meaning":"以抽象方式呈現某事物","examples":[{"en":"Lang presents the machines in abstract terms.","zh":"Lang 以抽象方式呈現機器。"},{"en":"To present something in abstract terms means to show it as a symbol or idea rather than through practical details.","zh":"以抽象方式呈現某事物，指把它作為象徵或想法展示，而不是透過實際細節。"},{"en":"A teacher may present justice in abstract terms before discussing real court cases.","zh":"老師可能先以抽象方式呈現公義，再討論真實法庭案例。"},{"en":"If machines are presented abstractly, they can represent all industry rather than specific tools.","zh":"如果機器被抽象呈現，它們可以代表整個工業，而不是特定工具。"},{"en":"The phrase explains a symbolic style of presentation.","zh":"這個短語解釋象徵式呈現風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"remain undefined","meaning":"仍未有明確說明","examples":[{"en":"The function of each machine remains undefined.","zh":"每部機器的功能仍未有明確說明。"},{"en":"To remain undefined means to continue without a clear explanation or fixed meaning.","zh":"仍未有明確說明，指繼續沒有清楚解釋或固定意思。"},{"en":"If group roles remain undefined, students may not know who should write or present.","zh":"如果小組角色仍未明確說明，學生可能不知道誰該寫作或匯報。"},{"en":"If machine functions remain undefined, viewers focus on what the machines symbolise.","zh":"如果機器功能仍未清楚說明，觀眾就集中於機器象徵甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes continuing lack of clarity.","zh":"這個短語描述持續缺乏清晰度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be concerned with","meaning":"關注……","examples":[{"en":"Multinational corporations are concerned with efficiency and profits.","zh":"跨國企業關注效率和利潤。"},{"en":"To be concerned with something means to focus on it or regard it as important.","zh":"“Be concerned with” 某事指集中於它或把它視為重要。"},{"en":"A hospital is concerned with patient safety as well as medical results.","zh":"醫院關注病人安全，也關注醫療結果。"},{"en":"If companies are mainly concerned with profit, worker welfare may become secondary.","zh":"如果公司主要關注利潤，員工福祉可能變成次要。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what a person or organisation cares about.","zh":"這個短語指出人或組織關心甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"increasing efficiency","meaning":"提高效率","examples":[{"en":"Many corporations focus on increasing efficiency.","zh":"許多企業集中於提高效率。"},{"en":"Increasing efficiency means making work faster, cheaper or less wasteful.","zh":"提高效率指令工作更快、更便宜或更少浪費。"},{"en":"A school office may increase efficiency by using online forms instead of paper forms.","zh":"學校辦公室可以透過使用網上表格而不是紙本表格來提高效率。"},{"en":"If efficiency increases but staff are overworked, the improvement may have human costs.","zh":"如果效率提高但員工過勞，改善可能有人性代價。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common goal in business and management.","zh":"這個短語描述商業和管理中的常見目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"first sentence indicates","meaning":"第一句顯示","examples":[{"en":"The first sentence indicates the writer’s mixed feelings about the future.","zh":"第一句顯示作者對未來的矛盾感受。"},{"en":"If a sentence indicates something, it shows or suggests it.","zh":"如果一句話顯示某事，它就是展示或暗示該事。"},{"en":"The first sentence of an essay can indicate whether the writer is worried, hopeful or critical.","zh":"文章第一句可以顯示作者是擔心、希望還是批判。"},{"en":"If the opening sentence contains both fear and excitement, it indicates a complex attitude.","zh":"如果開首句同時包含恐懼和興奮，它就顯示複雜態度。"},{"en":"The phrase asks students to infer meaning from the beginning of a text.","zh":"這個短語要求學生從文本開頭推斷意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"fear about technology","meaning":"對科技的恐懼","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to the writer’s fear about technology.","zh":"該選項提到作者對科技的恐懼。"},{"en":"Fear about technology is anxiety that machines, systems or inventions may harm people or society.","zh":"對科技的恐懼，是擔心機器、系統或發明可能傷害人或社會。"},{"en":"Parents may have fear about technology if children spend too much time online.","zh":"如果孩子花太多時間上網，家長可能有對科技的恐懼。"},{"en":"If a film shows machines consuming workers, it can create fear about industrial progress.","zh":"如果電影展示機器吞噬工人，就可以造成對工業進步的恐懼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes emotional worry about technological change.","zh":"這個短語描述對科技變化的情緒性憂慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contradictory feelings","meaning":"矛盾的感受","examples":[{"en":"The film creates contradictory feelings towards the future.","zh":"這部電影造成對未來的矛盾感受。"},{"en":"Contradictory feelings are emotions that oppose each other, such as fear and excitement.","zh":"矛盾的感受，是彼此相反的情緒，例如恐懼和興奮。"},{"en":"A student may have contradictory feelings before graduation, feeling happy but also nervous.","zh":"學生畢業前可能有矛盾感受，既高興又緊張。"},{"en":"If a future city looks beautiful and cruel, viewers may feel both attraction and horror.","zh":"如果未來城市看起來美麗又殘酷，觀眾可能同時感到吸引和恐懼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mixed emotions that do not fit neatly together.","zh":"這個短語描述無法整齊配合的混合情緒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"successful management of","meaning":"對……的成功管理","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to the elite’s successful management of the workers.","zh":"該選項提到精英對工人的成功管理。"},{"en":"Successful management of a group means controlling or organising that group effectively.","zh":"對某群體的成功管理，指有效控制或組織該群體。"},{"en":"A teacher’s successful management of a noisy class requires clear rules and calm authority.","zh":"老師對嘈雜班級的成功管理，需要清楚規則和冷靜權威。"},{"en":"If workers obey perfectly, the elite may appear to manage them successfully, though unfairly.","zh":"如果工人完全服從，精英可能看似成功管理他們，雖然不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase can be neutral, but in this context it may imply control over people.","zh":"這個短語可以是中性，但在此語境中可能暗示對人的控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"individual machines","meaning":"個別機器","examples":[{"en":"The function of the individual machines is never defined.","zh":"個別機器的功能從未被界定。"},{"en":"Individual machines are separate specific machines, not machinery as a whole.","zh":"個別機器是分開的特定機器，而不是整體機械。"},{"en":"In a factory tour, students may learn what individual machines do at each stage.","zh":"在工廠參觀中，學生可能學到每階段個別機器的作用。"},{"en":"If individual machines are not explained, the film treats them as symbols rather than tools.","zh":"如果個別機器沒有被解釋，電影就是把它們當成象徵而不是工具。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on each machine separately.","zh":"這個短語強調逐一看每部機器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"present the theme symbolically","meaning":"以象徵方式呈現主題","examples":[{"en":"Lang presents the film’s industrial theme symbolically.","zh":"Lang 以象徵方式呈現電影的工業主題。"},{"en":"To present a theme symbolically means to express an idea through images, actions or objects rather than direct explanation.","zh":"以象徵方式呈現主題，指透過影像、動作或物件表達想法，而不是直接解釋。"},{"en":"A film may present loneliness symbolically by showing one chair in a large empty room.","zh":"電影可能透過在巨大空房中展示一張椅子，象徵性呈現孤獨。"},{"en":"If machines stand for industry, the film communicates its theme visually.","zh":"如果機器代表工業，電影就是以視覺方式傳達主題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes indirect artistic communication.","zh":"這個短語描述間接的藝術溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be important to exploit","meaning":"值得加以剝削","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that workers are important to exploit.","zh":"該選項暗示工人值得加以剝削。"},{"en":"To be important to exploit means to be valuable because someone can use it unfairly for gain.","zh":"值得加以剝削，指某事物因能被人不公平利用以獲益而有價值。"},{"en":"A company may see cheap land as important to exploit if it only cares about profit.","zh":"如果公司只關心利潤，可能把廉價土地視為值得加以剝削。"},{"en":"If workers are treated as resources to exploit, their rights and dignity are ignored.","zh":"如果工人被當成可剝削資源，其權利和尊嚴就被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase is morally negative because exploitation involves unfair use.","zh":"這個短語帶道德上的負面意味，因為剝削涉及不公平利用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"difficult to understand","meaning":"難以理解","examples":[{"en":"The fantasy sequence may initially be difficult to understand.","zh":"這個幻想場面起初可能難以理解。"},{"en":"Difficult to understand means not easy to make sense of at first.","zh":"難以理解指一開始不容易明白。"},{"en":"A poem may be difficult to understand until the teacher explains its symbols.","zh":"一首詩可能在老師解釋其象徵前難以理解。"},{"en":"If a scene is symbolic, viewers may need time to connect the images with the meaning.","zh":"如果場景具象徵性，觀眾可能需要時間把影像與意思連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes temporary confusion or complexity.","zh":"這個短語描述暫時困惑或複雜性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"focus of the movie","meaning":"電影的重點","examples":[{"en":"The machines are not the only focus of the movie.","zh":"機器不是這部電影唯一的重點。"},{"en":"The focus of the movie is the main subject, idea or area of attention in the film.","zh":"電影的重點，是電影中的主要題材、想法或注意力所在。"},{"en":"In a sports film, the focus may be friendship rather than winning.","zh":"在體育電影中，重點可能是友誼，而不是勝利。"},{"en":"If machines are important but workers also matter, the film has more than one focus.","zh":"如果機器重要但工人也重要，電影就有多於一個重點。"},{"en":"The phrase helps identify what the film is really about.","zh":"這個短語幫助識別電影真正關於甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"writer’s purpose","meaning":"作者的目的","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the writer’s purpose in the fifth paragraph.","zh":"題目問作者在第五段中的目的。"},{"en":"A writer’s purpose is the reason the writer includes a paragraph, example or argument.","zh":"作者的目的，是作者加入某段、例子或論點的原因。"},{"en":"A writer may include statistics to prove that a problem is serious.","zh":"作者可能加入統計數字，以證明問題嚴重。"},{"en":"If a paragraph compares film with reality, its purpose may be to show relevance.","zh":"如果一段把電影與現實比較，其目的可能是顯示相關性。"},{"en":"The phrase asks why the writer wrote something, not only what it says.","zh":"這個短語問作者為何寫某事，而不只是它說了甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"profit-oriented goal","meaning":"以利潤為本的目標","examples":[{"en":"The corporations have a strongly profit-oriented goal.","zh":"這些企業有強烈以利潤為本的目標。"},{"en":"A profit-oriented goal is an aim focused mainly on making money.","zh":"以利潤為本的目標，是主要集中於賺錢的目標。"},{"en":"A school canteen with a profit-oriented goal may sell popular snacks rather than healthy meals.","zh":"如果學校飯堂有以利潤為本的目標，可能售賣受歡迎零食而非健康餐。"},{"en":"If companies pursue profit above all else, worker welfare may become less important.","zh":"如果公司把利潤置於一切之上，員工福祉可能變得較不重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a business aim centred on financial gain.","zh":"這個短語描述以財務收益為中心的商業目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"compare the movie with reality","meaning":"將電影與現實比較","examples":[{"en":"The writer compares the movie with reality in the global economy.","zh":"作者將電影與全球經濟中的現實比較。"},{"en":"To compare the movie with reality means to examine similarities between the film and real life.","zh":"將電影與現實比較，指檢視電影與真實生活之間的相似之處。"},{"en":"Students may compare a school drama with reality to see whether it shows teenage life accurately.","zh":"學生可能把校園劇與現實比較，看它是否準確呈現青少年生活。"},{"en":"If a film’s imagined world resembles modern corporations, the comparison makes the film relevant.","zh":"如果電影想像世界類似現代企業，這種比較就令電影變得相關。"},{"en":"The phrase describes linking fiction with actual conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述把虛構與實際情況連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"explore the difference between","meaning":"探討……之間的分別","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to exploring the difference between fantasy and reality.","zh":"該選項提到探討幻想與現實之間的分別。"},{"en":"To explore the difference between two things means to examine how they are not the same.","zh":"探討兩者之間的分別，指檢視它們如何不同。"},{"en":"A teacher may explore the difference between spoken English and formal writing.","zh":"老師可能探討口語英語與正式寫作之間的分別。"},{"en":"If a paragraph compares film and global business, it may show similarities rather than differences.","zh":"如果一段比較電影和全球商業，它可能顯示相似，而不是分別。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful comparison of contrast.","zh":"這個短語描述對差異的仔細比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"shed light on","meaning":"闡明……；使人了解……","examples":[{"en":"The paragraph sheds light on the behaviour of multinational corporations.","zh":"這一段闡明跨國企業的行為。"},{"en":"To shed light on something means to make it easier to understand.","zh":"“Shed light on” 某事指使它更容易理解。"},{"en":"A survey can shed light on why students feel stressed before exams.","zh":"調查可以使人了解為何學生考試前感到壓力。"},{"en":"If a film comparison explains corporate behaviour, it helps readers see the pattern clearly.","zh":"如果電影比較解釋企業行為，它就幫助讀者清楚看見模式。"},{"en":"The phrase means to clarify or explain.","zh":"這個短語指澄清或解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"underdeveloped industries","meaning":"發展不足的工業","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to industries that remain underdeveloped.","zh":"該選項提到仍然發展不足的工業。"},{"en":"Underdeveloped industries are industries that have not yet grown, modernised or become fully productive.","zh":"發展不足的工業，是尚未增長、現代化或充分具生產力的工業。"},{"en":"A country may have underdeveloped industries if factories lack technology and trained workers.","zh":"如果工廠缺乏科技和受訓工人，一個國家可能有發展不足的工業。"},{"en":"If industries remain underdeveloped, jobs and wages may be limited.","zh":"如果工業仍發展不足，就業和工資可能受限制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weak or incomplete industrial development.","zh":"這個短語描述薄弱或不完整的工業發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"writer’s opinion about","meaning":"作者對……的看法","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for the writer’s opinion about the movie.","zh":"題目問作者對這部電影的看法。"},{"en":"The writer’s opinion about something is the attitude, judgement or belief the writer expresses.","zh":"作者對某事的看法，是作者表達的態度、判斷或信念。"},{"en":"Students can identify the writer’s opinion by noticing praise, criticism and contrast words.","zh":"學生可以透過留意讚賞、批評和對比詞來識別作者看法。"},{"en":"If the writer praises the images but criticises the story, the opinion is mixed.","zh":"如果作者讚賞影像但批評故事，其看法就是混合的。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for evaluation rather than simple fact.","zh":"這個短語要求評價，而不是簡單事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"poor use of symbolism","meaning":"象徵手法運用欠佳","examples":[{"en":"The writer does not accuse the film of a poor use of symbolism.","zh":"作者並沒有指責這部電影象徵手法運用欠佳。"},{"en":"Poor use of symbolism means using symbols weakly, confusingly or ineffectively.","zh":"象徵手法運用欠佳，指符號使用得薄弱、混亂或無效。"},{"en":"A film has poor use of symbolism if a repeated object never connects clearly to the theme.","zh":"如果電影中反覆出現的物件從未清楚連接主題，它就象徵手法運用欠佳。"},{"en":"If the writer calls the symbolism impeccable, they are not criticising that part.","zh":"如果作者稱象徵手法無可挑剔，就不是在批評該部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ineffective symbolic technique.","zh":"這個短語描述無效的象徵技巧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in all aspects","meaning":"在所有方面","examples":[{"en":"The writer does not consider the film perfect in all aspects.","zh":"作者不認為這部電影在所有方面都完美。"},{"en":"In all aspects means in every part, area or respect.","zh":"在所有方面指在每個部分、範疇或角度。"},{"en":"A student may be strong in vocabulary but not perfect in all aspects of writing.","zh":"學生可能詞彙強，但在寫作所有方面都完美。"},{"en":"If a film has excellent images but a weak plot, it is not perfect in all aspects.","zh":"如果電影影像出色但情節薄弱，它就不是在所有方面都完美。"},{"en":"The phrase describes total completeness across all areas.","zh":"這個短語描述跨所有範疇的完全性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"good but could be better","meaning":"很好但仍可改善","examples":[{"en":"The writer considers the film good but believes it could be better.","zh":"作者認為這部電影很好，但相信它仍可改善。"},{"en":"Good but could be better means already successful in some ways but still having weaknesses.","zh":"很好但仍可改善，指在某些方面已成功，但仍有弱點。"},{"en":"A student’s essay may be good but could be better if examples are added.","zh":"如果加入例子，學生文章可能很好但仍可改善。"},{"en":"If a film has powerful images but a sentimental story, praise and criticism can both be fair.","zh":"如果電影有強大影像但故事感傷，讚賞和批評都可以公平。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses balanced evaluation rather than total approval or rejection.","zh":"這個短語表達平衡評價，而不是完全認同或否定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 144 - Movie of Metropolis.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 145":[{"front":"pollution in the bay","meaning":"海灣污染","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines the causes and effects of pollution in Florida Bay.","zh":"文章探討佛羅里達灣污染的成因和影響。"},{"en":"Pollution in the bay means harmful substances or changes that damage the water, plants, and animals in a bay.","zh":"pollution in the bay 指損害海灣水質、植物和動物的有害物質或變化。"},{"en":"A town may worry about pollution in the bay if dirty water flows from streets into the sea.","zh":"如果骯髒雨水從街道流入海中，小鎮可能擔心海灣污染。"},{"en":"Pollution in the bay can kill marine plants, reduce fish numbers, and harm tourism.","zh":"海灣污染可以殺死海洋植物、減少魚類數量並損害旅遊業。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a coastal water area is being damaged by human activity.","zh":"這個片語用於描述沿海水域被人類活動破壞的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pour water into","meaning":"把水注入……","examples":[{"en":"Pouring freshwater into the sea may alter the bay’s ecology.","zh":"把淡水注入海中可能改變海灣生態。"},{"en":"To pour water into a place means to send or let water flow into it.","zh":"pour water into a place 指把水送入或讓水流入某地方。"},{"en":"Workers may pour water into a dry pond to save the fish inside.","zh":"工人可能把水注入乾涸池塘，以拯救裡面的魚。"},{"en":"If too much water is poured into a small area, it can change the balance of salt, nutrients, or temperature.","zh":"如果太多水被注入小範圍地區，它可能改變鹽分、養分或溫度平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding water, often deliberately or through a planned system.","zh":"這個片語描述加水，通常是有意或透過計劃系統進行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sound harmless enough","meaning":"聽起來似乎無害","examples":[{"en":"Pouring water into the sea sounds harmless enough.","zh":"把水注入海中聽起來似乎無害。"},{"en":"To sound harmless enough means to seem safe or not dangerous at first.","zh":"sound harmless enough 指起初聽起來安全或沒有危險。"},{"en":"Letting children watch one short video sounds harmless enough, but it may become a daily habit.","zh":"讓孩子看一條短影片聽起來似乎無害，但可能變成每日習慣。"},{"en":"A simple change can sound harmless enough until people examine its hidden effects.","zh":"一個簡單改變聽起來似乎無害，直到人們檢視其隱藏影響。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces a situation that seems safe but may actually cause problems.","zh":"這個片語常引入看似安全但實際可能造成問題的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a large and shallow section of","meaning":"……一個大而水淺的區域","examples":[{"en":"Florida Bay is a large and shallow section of the Gulf of Mexico.","zh":"佛羅里達灣是墨西哥灣一個大而水淺的區域。"},{"en":"A large and shallow section of water is a wide area where the water is not very deep.","zh":"large and shallow section of water 指一片廣闊但水不深的水域。"},{"en":"Children may play safely in a large and shallow section of a swimming pool.","zh":"孩子可能在泳池一個大而水淺的區域安全玩耍。"},{"en":"Shallow water can be easily affected by heat, pollution, and changes in freshwater flow.","zh":"淺水區容易受熱力、污染和淡水流量變化影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the size and depth of part of a larger water body.","zh":"這個片語描述較大水體中某部分的大小和深度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lie between","meaning":"位於……之間","examples":[{"en":"Florida Bay lies between the Everglades and the Florida Keys.","zh":"佛羅里達灣位於大沼澤地和佛羅里達礁島群之間。"},{"en":"To lie between two places means to be located in the space separating them.","zh":"lie between two places 指位於兩個地方之間的空間。"},{"en":"A small park may lie between a school and a housing estate.","zh":"小公園可能位於學校和屋苑之間。"},{"en":"If a bay lies between wetlands and islands, changes in either area may affect it.","zh":"如果海灣位於濕地和島嶼之間，任一地區的變化都可能影響它。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a place’s position by using two reference points.","zh":"這個片語用兩個參照點說明位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the southern end of","meaning":"……的南端","examples":[{"en":"The bay lies near the southern end of the Everglades.","zh":"該海灣位於大沼澤地南端附近。"},{"en":"The southern end of a place is the part closest to the south.","zh":"southern end of a place 指某地方最接近南方的部分。"},{"en":"The school gate is at the southern end of the campus.","zh":"學校大門位於校園南端。"},{"en":"If a river reaches the southern end of a wetland, water from the north may eventually flow there.","zh":"如果河流到達濕地南端，北方的水最終可能流到那裡。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe position within a larger area.","zh":"這個片語幫助描述較大地區內的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"prove highly controversial","meaning":"引起極大爭議","examples":[{"en":"The proposal is proving highly controversial.","zh":"這項建議正引起極大爭議。"},{"en":"To prove highly controversial means to cause strong disagreement among people.","zh":"prove highly controversial 指引起人們強烈分歧。"},{"en":"A new school rule banning phones may prove highly controversial among students and parents.","zh":"禁止手機的新校規可能在學生和家長之間引起極大爭議。"},{"en":"If experts disagree about a plan’s effects, the plan can quickly become controversial.","zh":"如果專家對計劃影響意見不一，該計劃很快會變得具爭議性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an issue that many people argue about.","zh":"這個片語描述許多人爭論的議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be divided over whether","meaning":"對是否……意見分歧","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are divided over whether the extra water will help the bay.","zh":"研究人員對額外水量是否有助海灣意見分歧。"},{"en":"To be divided over whether something is true means people disagree about it.","zh":"be divided over whether something is true 指人們對某事是否屬實有不同意見。"},{"en":"Parents may be divided over whether homework should be reduced.","zh":"家長可能對是否應減少功課意見分歧。"},{"en":"If evidence points in different directions, experts may be divided over what action to take.","zh":"如果證據指向不同方向，專家可能對應採取甚麼行動意見分歧。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disagreement about a yes-or-no question.","zh":"這個片語描述對是非問題的分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"help or hinder","meaning":"有助還是妨礙","examples":[{"en":"Scientists disagree about whether freshwater will help or hinder marine life.","zh":"科學家對淡水會有助還是妨礙海洋生物意見不一。"},{"en":"To help or hinder something means either to support it or make it more difficult.","zh":"help or hinder something 指支持某事或令某事更困難。"},{"en":"New technology can help or hinder learning, depending on how students use it.","zh":"新科技可以有助學習，也可以妨礙學習，視乎學生如何使用。"},{"en":"If freshwater brings nutrients into the sea, it may help some plants but hinder corals.","zh":"如果淡水把養分帶入海中，它可能有助某些植物，但妨礙珊瑚。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an action may have positive or negative effects.","zh":"這個片語適用於某行動可能有正面或負面影響的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what is at risk is","meaning":"面臨風險的是……","examples":[{"en":"What is at risk is the future of the bay’s seagrass beds.","zh":"面臨風險的是該海灣海草床的未來。"},{"en":"What is at risk is introduces the thing that may be harmed or lost.","zh":"what is at risk is 用來引出可能受損或失去的事物。"},{"en":"If a library closes, what is at risk is children’s easy access to books.","zh":"如果圖書館關閉，面臨風險的是孩子容易接觸書本的機會。"},{"en":"When pollution increases, what is at risk may be the whole food chain.","zh":"當污染增加，面臨風險的可能是整條食物鏈。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the main thing in danger.","zh":"這個片語突出主要受威脅的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"extensive beds of seagrasses","meaning":"大片海草床","examples":[{"en":"Florida Bay contains extensive beds of seagrasses.","zh":"佛羅里達灣有大片海草床。"},{"en":"Extensive beds of seagrasses are large areas of the sea floor covered with seagrass.","zh":"extensive beds of seagrasses 指海床上被海草覆蓋的大面積區域。"},{"en":"Divers may see extensive beds of seagrasses in shallow coastal water.","zh":"潛水者可能在淺海沿岸水域看到大片海草床。"},{"en":"If seagrass beds die, young fish and shellfish lose shelter.","zh":"如果海草床死亡，幼魚和貝類會失去庇護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes widespread underwater plant habitats.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛的水下植物棲息地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"muddy floor","meaning":"泥濘海床","examples":[{"en":"The seagrasses grow on the bay’s muddy floor.","zh":"海草生長在海灣的泥濘海床上。"},{"en":"A muddy floor is a soft wet bottom surface covered with mud.","zh":"muddy floor 指被泥覆蓋的柔軟濕底部表面。"},{"en":"After heavy rain, a playground may have a muddy floor that is hard to walk on.","zh":"大雨後，操場可能有泥濘地面，令人難以行走。"},{"en":"In a bay, a muddy floor can hold nutrients and support plant growth.","zh":"在海灣中，泥濘海床可以保存養分並支持植物生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the soft bottom of a water area.","zh":"這個片語描述水域的柔軟底部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"act as nurseries for","meaning":"作為……的育幼場","examples":[{"en":"The seagrass beds act as nurseries for young marine animals.","zh":"海草床作為年幼海洋動物的育幼場。"},{"en":"To act as nurseries for animals means to provide a safe place where young animals can grow.","zh":"act as nurseries for animals 指提供安全地方讓幼小動物成長。"},{"en":"A quiet mangrove forest can act as a nursery for young fish.","zh":"安靜的紅樹林可以作為幼魚的育幼場。"},{"en":"If nursery habitats disappear, fewer young animals may survive to adulthood.","zh":"如果育幼棲息地消失，能存活至成年的幼小動物可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place that protects early life.","zh":"這個片語描述保護早期生命的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"larvae","meaning":"幼體","examples":[{"en":"The seagrasses provide shelter for the larvae of shrimps and fish.","zh":"海草為蝦和魚的幼體提供庇護。"},{"en":"Larvae are very young forms of some animals before they become adults.","zh":"larvae 是某些動物長成成體前的幼年形態。"},{"en":"Mosquito larvae live in water before becoming flying mosquitoes.","zh":"蚊子的幼體在變成會飛的蚊子前生活在水中。"},{"en":"If larvae lose safe shelter, many may be eaten before they grow.","zh":"如果幼體失去安全庇護，許多可能在長大前被吃掉。"},{"en":"This word describes an early stage in an animal’s life cycle.","zh":"這個詞描述動物生命周期中的早期階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"shrimps and lobsters","meaning":"蝦和龍蝦","examples":[{"en":"The bay supports the larvae of shrimps and lobsters.","zh":"該海灣支持蝦和龍蝦的幼體。"},{"en":"Shrimps and lobsters are shellfish that live in the sea and are important for food and fishing.","zh":"shrimps and lobsters 是生活在海中、對食物和捕魚重要的甲殼類動物。"},{"en":"Restaurants may buy shrimps and lobsters from local fishermen.","zh":"餐廳可能向本地漁民購買蝦和龍蝦。"},{"en":"If young shrimps and lobsters lose habitat, fishing businesses may suffer later.","zh":"如果幼小蝦和龍蝦失去棲息地，捕魚業日後可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to valuable marine animals.","zh":"這個片語指有價值的海洋動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sport and commercial-fishing species","meaning":"遊釣及商業捕撈物種","examples":[{"en":"Many fish in the bay are important species for sport and commercial fishing.","zh":"海灣中許多魚類是遊釣及商業捕撈的重要物種。"},{"en":"Sport and commercial-fishing species are fish caught for recreation or for sale.","zh":"sport and commercial-fishing species 是供娛樂捕魚或出售捕撈的魚類。"},{"en":"Tourists may pay for sport fishing trips, while fishing companies catch fish commercially.","zh":"遊客可能付費參加遊釣旅程，而漁業公司則作商業捕撈。"},{"en":"If these species decline, both leisure activities and businesses lose income.","zh":"如果這些物種減少，休閒活動和企業收入都會受損。"},{"en":"This phrase links marine life with recreation and the economy.","zh":"這個片語把海洋生物與娛樂和經濟連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"also in danger","meaning":"也面臨危險","examples":[{"en":"The coral reefs of the Florida Keys are also in danger.","zh":"佛羅里達礁島群的珊瑚礁也面臨危險。"},{"en":"Also in danger means facing risk in addition to another thing already mentioned.","zh":"also in danger 指除了已提及的另一事物外，也面對風險。"},{"en":"If a school loses funding, after-school clubs are also in danger.","zh":"如果學校失去資助，課後活動也面臨危險。"},{"en":"When one part of an ecosystem suffers, nearby habitats may also be threatened.","zh":"當生態系統某部分受害，附近棲息地也可能受威脅。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another item to the list of things at risk.","zh":"這個片語把另一個有風險的事物加入列表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an impressive range of","meaning":"一大片令人印象深刻的……","examples":[{"en":"The Florida Keys contain an impressive range of coral reefs.","zh":"佛羅里達礁島群擁有一大片令人印象深刻的珊瑚礁。"},{"en":"An impressive range of something means a large and varied collection of it.","zh":"an impressive range of something 指大量且多樣化的某類事物。"},{"en":"A library may offer an impressive range of books for different ages and interests.","zh":"圖書館可能提供一系列令人印象深刻、適合不同年齡和興趣的書籍。"},{"en":"If an area has an impressive range of habitats, it can support many species.","zh":"如果一個地區有令人印象深刻的多種棲息地，它可以支持許多物種。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights both variety and richness.","zh":"這個片語突出多樣性和豐富程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"coral reefs","meaning":"珊瑚礁","examples":[{"en":"The coral reefs support hundreds of animal species.","zh":"珊瑚礁支持數百種動物。"},{"en":"Coral reefs are underwater structures built by tiny coral animals and used as habitats by many sea creatures.","zh":"coral reefs 是由微小珊瑚動物建立的水下結構，並被許多海洋生物用作棲息地。"},{"en":"Divers visit coral reefs to see colourful fish, corals, and turtles.","zh":"潛水者到珊瑚礁觀看色彩繽紛的魚、珊瑚和海龜。"},{"en":"If coral reefs die, many animals lose food and shelter.","zh":"如果珊瑚礁死亡，許多動物會失去食物和庇護。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to rich but fragile marine ecosystems.","zh":"這個片語指豐富但脆弱的海洋生態系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"run the length of","meaning":"沿……全長延伸","examples":[{"en":"The reefs run the length of the Florida Keys.","zh":"這些珊瑚礁沿佛羅里達礁島群全長延伸。"},{"en":"To run the length of a place means to extend along it from one end to the other.","zh":"run the length of a place 指沿某地由一端延伸到另一端。"},{"en":"A bicycle path may run the length of a river.","zh":"單車徑可能沿河流全長延伸。"},{"en":"If reefs run along a chain of islands, they protect and support a wide coastal area.","zh":"如果珊瑚礁沿島鏈延伸，它們會保護並支持廣闊沿海地區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something extending along a long area.","zh":"這個片語描述某物沿長形區域延伸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the third-largest barrier reef","meaning":"全球第三大堡礁","examples":[{"en":"The Florida Keys form the third-largest barrier reef in the world.","zh":"佛羅里達礁島群構成全球第三大堡礁。"},{"en":"The third-largest barrier reef means a reef system that ranks third in size among barrier reefs globally.","zh":"third-largest barrier reef 指在全球堡礁中按大小排名第三的礁系。"},{"en":"A city may have the third-largest port in a country if only two ports are bigger.","zh":"如果一個國家只有兩個港口較大，某城市可能有全國第三大港口。"},{"en":"If a reef is one of the world’s largest, its decline has global importance.","zh":"如果珊瑚礁是世界最大之一，其衰退就具有全球重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase shows size ranking.","zh":"這個片語顯示大小排名。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"coral cover","meaning":"珊瑚覆蓋率","examples":[{"en":"Coral cover has fallen sharply since the 1980s.","zh":"自1980年代以來，珊瑚覆蓋率急劇下降。"},{"en":"Coral cover is the amount or percentage of sea floor covered by living coral.","zh":"coral cover 是海床被活珊瑚覆蓋的數量或百分比。"},{"en":"Scientists measure coral cover to check whether a reef is healthy.","zh":"科學家量度珊瑚覆蓋率，以檢查珊瑚礁是否健康。"},{"en":"If coral cover falls, fewer animals can depend on the reef for shelter.","zh":"如果珊瑚覆蓋率下降，能依賴珊瑚礁作庇護的動物會減少。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to describe reef condition.","zh":"這個片語用來描述珊瑚礁狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"drop by","meaning":"下降……","examples":[{"en":"Coral cover has dropped by 40 percent.","zh":"珊瑚覆蓋率已下降40%。"},{"en":"To drop by an amount means to decrease by that amount.","zh":"drop by an amount 指按某數量下降。"},{"en":"A shop’s income may drop by 20 percent after roadworks block the entrance.","zh":"如果道路工程堵塞入口，店舖收入可能下降20%。"},{"en":"If coral cover drops by a large percentage, the ecosystem may be seriously weakened.","zh":"如果珊瑚覆蓋率大幅下降，生態系統可能嚴重削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to describe measurable decreases.","zh":"這個片語用於描述可量度的減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a third of the species","meaning":"三分之一的物種","examples":[{"en":"A third of the coral species have disappeared.","zh":"三分之一的珊瑚物種已經消失。"},{"en":"A third of the species means one out of every three species in a group.","zh":"a third of the species 指一組物種中每三種有一種。"},{"en":"If a third of the trees in a park die, visitors will notice the change.","zh":"如果公園三分之一的樹木死亡，遊人會注意到變化。"},{"en":"When a third of species disappear, biodiversity is seriously reduced.","zh":"當三分之一物種消失，生物多樣性會嚴重下降。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a large proportion of a biological group.","zh":"這個片語表示生物群體中的一大比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have gone","meaning":"已經消失","examples":[{"en":"Many of the coral species have gone since the 1980s.","zh":"自1980年代以來，許多珊瑚物種已經消失。"},{"en":"Have gone means have disappeared or are no longer present.","zh":"have gone 指已經消失或不再存在。"},{"en":"The old shops have gone, and new cafés have replaced them.","zh":"舊店舖已經消失，新的咖啡店取代了它們。"},{"en":"If species have gone from a reef, the ecosystem has already changed.","zh":"如果物種已從珊瑚礁消失，生態系統已經改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes loss over time.","zh":"這個片語描述隨時間流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have a damaging effect on","meaning":"對……造成破壞性影響","examples":[{"en":"The decline of coral has had a damaging effect on marine animals.","zh":"珊瑚衰退對海洋動物造成破壞性影響。"},{"en":"To have a damaging effect on something means to harm it or make it worse.","zh":"have a damaging effect on something 指傷害某事或令它變差。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can have a damaging effect on memory and mood.","zh":"睡眠不足可以對記憶和心情造成破壞性影響。"},{"en":"If pollution damages coral, it can also harm animals that depend on coral.","zh":"如果污染破壞珊瑚，它也會傷害依賴珊瑚的動物。"},{"en":"This phrase links a problem with its harmful result.","zh":"這個片語把問題與其有害結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"depend on the reef","meaning":"依賴珊瑚礁","examples":[{"en":"Crabs, turtles and fish depend on the reef for survival.","zh":"蟹、海龜和魚類依賴珊瑚礁生存。"},{"en":"To depend on the reef means to need the reef for food, shelter, breeding, or protection.","zh":"depend on the reef 指需要珊瑚礁提供食物、庇護、繁殖地或保護。"},{"en":"A child may depend on a school bus to get to class on time.","zh":"孩子可能依賴校巴準時上課。"},{"en":"If animals depend on the reef, damage to the reef affects their survival.","zh":"如果動物依賴珊瑚礁，珊瑚礁受損就會影響牠們生存。"},{"en":"This phrase shows reliance on a habitat.","zh":"這個片語顯示對棲息地的依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ecological change","meaning":"生態變化","examples":[{"en":"Scientists disagree about what is causing the ecological change.","zh":"科學家對是甚麼造成生態變化意見不一。"},{"en":"Ecological change means a change in the relationships among plants, animals, water, soil, and the environment.","zh":"ecological change 指植物、動物、水、土壤和環境之間關係的變化。"},{"en":"A new road through a forest may cause ecological change by disturbing wildlife routes.","zh":"穿過森林的新道路可能透過干擾野生動物路線造成生態變化。"},{"en":"If one species disappears, the whole ecosystem may change in unexpected ways.","zh":"如果一個物種消失，整個生態系統可能以意想不到的方式改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes change in an ecosystem.","zh":"這個片語描述生態系統中的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a matter of much debate","meaning":"爭議很大的問題","examples":[{"en":"The cause of the damage is a matter of much debate.","zh":"破壞的成因是一個爭議很大的問題。"},{"en":"A matter of much debate is an issue that many people argue about because the answer is unclear.","zh":"matter of much debate 是因答案不清楚而被許多人爭論的議題。"},{"en":"Whether homework should be compulsory is a matter of much debate in some schools.","zh":"功課是否應強制，在一些學校是爭議很大的問題。"},{"en":"If evidence is incomplete, the cause of a problem may remain debated for years.","zh":"如果證據不完整，問題成因可能多年來仍有爭議。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strongly disputed question.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈爭議的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"of no small consequence","meaning":"影響重大；絕非小事","examples":[{"en":"The answer to this question is of no small consequence.","zh":"這個問題的答案影響重大。"},{"en":"Of no small consequence means very important and likely to have serious effects.","zh":"of no small consequence 指非常重要，並可能帶來嚴重影響。"},{"en":"Choosing the right hospital for surgery is of no small consequence.","zh":"為手術選擇合適醫院絕非小事。"},{"en":"If a decision affects money, health, and the environment, it is not a minor matter.","zh":"如果決定影響金錢、健康和環境，它就不是小事。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that something matters greatly.","zh":"這個片語強調某事非常重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"devote money to","meaning":"撥款用於……","examples":[{"en":"The government plans to devote billions of dollars to restoring the Everglades.","zh":"政府計劃撥款數十億美元用於修復大沼澤地。"},{"en":"To devote money to something means to set aside or spend money for that purpose.","zh":"devote money to something 指為某目的預留或花費金錢。"},{"en":"A school may devote money to hiring reading tutors.","zh":"學校可能撥款用於聘請閱讀導師。"},{"en":"If the government devotes money to restoration, taxpayers expect real improvement.","zh":"如果政府撥款用於修復，納稅人會期望真正改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes funding a particular goal.","zh":"這個片語描述資助特定目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"over the next 30 years","meaning":"在未來三十年","examples":[{"en":"The restoration work will continue over the next 30 years.","zh":"修復工作將在未來三十年持續。"},{"en":"Over the next 30 years means during the coming three decades.","zh":"over the next 30 years 指在未來三個十年期間。"},{"en":"A city may build new rail lines over the next 30 years.","zh":"一個城市可能在未來三十年建造新鐵路線。"},{"en":"If a project lasts this long, its effects may be slow and difficult to measure.","zh":"如果項目持續這麼久，其效果可能緩慢且難以量度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a long future period.","zh":"這個片語描述很長的未來時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"revitalise the Everglades","meaning":"恢復大沼澤地的生態活力","examples":[{"en":"The government plans to revitalise the Everglades.","zh":"政府計劃恢復大沼澤地的生態活力。"},{"en":"To revitalise the Everglades means to restore the health and activity of this wetland ecosystem.","zh":"revitalise the Everglades 指恢復這個濕地生態系統的健康和活力。"},{"en":"A town may revitalise an old park by cleaning ponds and planting trees.","zh":"小鎮可能透過清理池塘和種樹令舊公園恢復活力。"},{"en":"If water flows return, the Everglades may support more wildlife again.","zh":"如果水流恢復，大沼澤地可能再次支持更多野生動物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bringing a damaged natural area back to life.","zh":"這個片語描述令受損自然地區重新恢復生命力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"seasonal freshwater flows","meaning":"季節性淡水流量","examples":[{"en":"The project will restore seasonal freshwater flows.","zh":"該項目將恢復季節性淡水流量。"},{"en":"Seasonal freshwater flows are natural movements of fresh water that change with wet and dry seasons.","zh":"seasonal freshwater flows 是隨雨季和旱季變化的自然淡水流動。"},{"en":"A river may have stronger freshwater flows during the rainy season.","zh":"河流在雨季可能有較強的淡水流量。"},{"en":"If seasonal flows are blocked, wetlands may become too dry or too salty.","zh":"如果季節性水流被阻擋，濕地可能變得太乾或太鹹。"},{"en":"This phrase describes natural water movement linked to seasons.","zh":"這個片語描述與季節相關的自然水流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be restored in order to","meaning":"為了……而恢復","examples":[{"en":"Freshwater flows will be restored in order to improve the region’s health.","zh":"淡水流量將為了改善該區健康而恢復。"},{"en":"To be restored in order to do something means to be brought back for a specific purpose.","zh":"be restored in order to do something 指為特定目的而恢復。"},{"en":"A closed playground may be restored in order to give children a safe place to play.","zh":"關閉的遊樂場可能為了給孩子安全玩耍空間而被修復。"},{"en":"If a natural flow is restored, the aim is often to repair ecological balance.","zh":"如果自然水流被恢復，目的通常是修復生態平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase connects restoration with purpose.","zh":"這個片語把恢復與目的連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"improve the region’s health","meaning":"改善該區的生態狀況","examples":[{"en":"The project is intended to improve the ecological health of the region.","zh":"該項目旨在改善該區的生態狀況。"},{"en":"To improve the region’s health means to make the environment, water, plants, and animals in an area healthier.","zh":"improve the region’s health 指令某地區的環境、水、植物和動物更健康。"},{"en":"A city may improve a region’s health by reducing waste and cleaning rivers.","zh":"城市可以透過減少廢物和清理河流改善地區健康。"},{"en":"If pollution falls, wildlife may recover and the region’s health may improve.","zh":"如果污染下降，野生動物可能恢復，該區生態狀況可能改善。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to environmental health rather than human health only.","zh":"這個片語可以指環境健康，而不只是人類健康。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"run off into","meaning":"流入……","examples":[{"en":"The restored freshwater will eventually run off into the bay.","zh":"恢復的淡水最終會流入海灣。"},{"en":"To run off into a place means for water to flow over land or through channels into that place.","zh":"run off into a place 指水從陸地表面或渠道流入某地。"},{"en":"Rainwater can run off into drains after a storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，雨水可以流入排水渠。"},{"en":"If fertilised water runs off into the sea, it may carry nutrients with it.","zh":"如果含肥料的水流入海中，它可能帶同養分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes water moving from one area into another.","zh":"這個片語描述水從一個地區流入另一地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"marine ecologist","meaning":"海洋生態學家","examples":[{"en":"Joseph Zieman is a marine ecologist at the University of Virginia.","zh":"Joseph Zieman 是維珍尼亞大學的海洋生態學家。"},{"en":"A marine ecologist is a scientist who studies relationships among sea organisms and their environment.","zh":"marine ecologist 是研究海洋生物與其環境之間關係的科學家。"},{"en":"A marine ecologist may study coral reefs, seagrass beds, fish, and water quality.","zh":"海洋生態學家可能研究珊瑚礁、海草床、魚類和水質。"},{"en":"If a bay changes suddenly, marine ecologists investigate possible causes.","zh":"如果海灣突然改變，海洋生態學家會調查可能原因。"},{"en":"This phrase names a scientist specialising in marine ecosystems.","zh":"這個片語指專門研究海洋生態系統的科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a lack of fresh water","meaning":"缺乏淡水","examples":[{"en":"Zieman believes that a lack of fresh water is the bay’s main problem.","zh":"Zieman 相信缺乏淡水是該海灣的主要問題。"},{"en":"A lack of fresh water means there is not enough non-salty water available.","zh":"lack of fresh water 指可用的非鹹水不足。"},{"en":"A village may suffer from a lack of fresh water during a drought.","zh":"村莊在乾旱期間可能因缺乏淡水而受苦。"},{"en":"If a bay receives too little fresh water, its salinity may rise.","zh":"如果海灣接收太少淡水，其鹽度可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shortage of freshwater.","zh":"這個片語描述淡水短缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the blame lies with","meaning":"問題在於；責任歸咎於……","examples":[{"en":"He argues that the blame lies with decades of drainage.","zh":"他認為責任歸咎於數十年的排水工程。"},{"en":"The blame lies with something means that thing is responsible for the problem.","zh":"the blame lies with something 指問題由某事造成或責任在於某事。"},{"en":"If students fail because instructions were unclear, the blame may lie with poor communication.","zh":"如果學生因指示不清而失敗，問題可能在於溝通不善。"},{"en":"When people identify where the blame lies, they can decide what to fix.","zh":"當人們找出責任所在，就能決定應修正甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the main cause or responsibility.","zh":"這個片語指出主要原因或責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a century of drainage","meaning":"一個世紀的排水工程","examples":[{"en":"A century of drainage has changed the flow of water into the bay.","zh":"一個世紀的排水工程改變了流入海灣的水流。"},{"en":"A century of drainage means about one hundred years of removing or redirecting water from land.","zh":"century of drainage 指約一百年把水從土地移走或改道。"},{"en":"A century of drainage can turn wetlands into farms but damage natural water systems.","zh":"一個世紀的排水工程可以把濕地變成農田，但損害自然水系統。"},{"en":"If drainage lasts for many decades, restoring natural flow may be difficult.","zh":"如果排水持續許多十年，恢復自然水流可能很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-term human control of water.","zh":"這個片語描述人類長期控制水流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be aimed at","meaning":"旨在……","examples":[{"en":"The drainage programme was aimed at creating farmland.","zh":"這項排水計劃旨在創造農地。"},{"en":"To be aimed at something means to be designed to achieve that goal.","zh":"be aimed at something 指為達成某目標而設計。"},{"en":"A school campaign may be aimed at reducing bullying.","zh":"學校宣傳活動可能旨在減少欺凌。"},{"en":"If a project is aimed at farming, it may ignore ecological effects.","zh":"如果項目旨在農業，它可能忽視生態影響。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose behind an action.","zh":"這個片語解釋行動背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"turn the marshes into","meaning":"把沼澤地變成……","examples":[{"en":"Engineers tried to turn the marshes into farmland and development sites.","zh":"工程師試圖把沼澤地變成農地和發展用地。"},{"en":"To turn the marshes into something means to change wetland areas into a different type of land use.","zh":"turn the marshes into something 指把濕地改造成另一種土地用途。"},{"en":"Developers may try to turn old factories into flats.","zh":"發展商可能試圖把舊工廠變成住宅。"},{"en":"If marshes are turned into farms, wildlife may lose habitat.","zh":"如果沼澤地被變成農田，野生動物可能失去棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes conversion from one land type to another.","zh":"這個片語描述從一種土地類型轉為另一種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"marshes","meaning":"沼澤地","examples":[{"en":"Large areas of marshes were drained for agriculture.","zh":"大片沼澤地被排水用於農業。"},{"en":"Marshes are wetland areas with soft wet ground and many water-loving plants.","zh":"marshes 是有柔軟濕地面和許多喜水植物的濕地。"},{"en":"Birds, frogs, and insects often live in marshes.","zh":"鳥類、青蛙和昆蟲常生活在沼澤地。"},{"en":"If marshes are drained, they may lose wildlife and their ability to hold water.","zh":"如果沼澤地被排水，它們可能失去野生動物和蓄水能力。"},{"en":"This word refers to a type of wetland habitat.","zh":"這個詞指一種濕地棲息地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"farmland and areas for development","meaning":"農地和發展用地","examples":[{"en":"The marshes were converted into farmland and areas for development.","zh":"沼澤地被改造成農地和發展用地。"},{"en":"Farmland and areas for development are land used for farming or future buildings, roads, and businesses.","zh":"farmland and areas for development 指用於耕作或未來建築、道路和商業的土地。"},{"en":"A city may divide land into farmland and areas for development when planning growth.","zh":"城市規劃增長時，可能把土地劃分為農地和發展用地。"},{"en":"If wetlands are converted into development land, natural habitats may shrink.","zh":"如果濕地被改造成發展用地，自然棲息地可能縮小。"},{"en":"This phrase describes human land use.","zh":"這個片語描述人類土地用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cause the flow to dwindle","meaning":"令水流逐漸減少","examples":[{"en":"Drainage caused the flow of freshwater into the bay to dwindle.","zh":"排水工程令流入海灣的淡水流量逐漸減少。"},{"en":"To cause the flow to dwindle means to make the amount of water gradually decrease.","zh":"cause the flow to dwindle 指令水量逐步下降。"},{"en":"A blocked pipe can cause the flow of water to dwindle in a building.","zh":"堵塞水管可以令建築物水流逐漸減少。"},{"en":"If canals divert water away, the natural flow to a bay may shrink over time.","zh":"如果運河把水引走，流向海灣的自然水流可能隨時間縮小。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gradual reduction in water movement.","zh":"這個片語描述水流逐漸減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dwindle","meaning":"逐漸減少","examples":[{"en":"The supply of freshwater has dwindled over time.","zh":"淡水供應隨時間逐漸減少。"},{"en":"To dwindle means to become smaller or less little by little.","zh":"dwindle 指一點一點變小或變少。"},{"en":"A family’s savings may dwindle if expenses keep rising.","zh":"如果開支不斷上升，家庭儲蓄可能逐漸減少。"},{"en":"If water supply dwindles, plants and animals may struggle to survive.","zh":"如果水源逐漸減少，植物和動物可能難以生存。"},{"en":"This word describes gradual decrease.","zh":"這個詞描述逐步下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"overall, more saline","meaning":"整體含鹽量更高","examples":[{"en":"The reduction in freshwater has made the bay, overall, more saline.","zh":"淡水減少令該海灣整體含鹽量更高。"},{"en":"Overall, more saline means generally saltier when the whole area is considered.","zh":"overall, more saline 指從整體來看鹽分更高。"},{"en":"A soup becomes more saline if too much salt is added.","zh":"如果加入太多鹽，湯會變得更鹹。"},{"en":"If less freshwater enters a bay, seawater may make the bay saltier overall.","zh":"如果較少淡水流入海灣，海水可能令海灣整體更鹹。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a general rise in saltiness.","zh":"這個片語描述鹽度整體上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"kill the seagrasses","meaning":"殺死海草","examples":[{"en":"Zieman argues that the increased salinity kills the seagrasses.","zh":"Zieman 認為鹽度增加會殺死海草。"},{"en":"To kill the seagrasses means to cause these underwater plants to die.","zh":"kill the seagrasses 指令這些水下植物死亡。"},{"en":"Dirty water can kill plants in a pond if it blocks light and adds harmful chemicals.","zh":"如果污水遮擋光線並加入有害化學物，可能殺死池塘植物。"},{"en":"If salinity rises beyond what plants can tolerate, seagrasses may die.","zh":"如果鹽度升至植物無法承受，海草可能死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes damage to underwater vegetation.","zh":"這個片語描述對水下植物的破壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as these rot","meaning":"當這些海草腐爛時","examples":[{"en":"As the dead seagrasses rot, they release nutrients.","zh":"當死去的海草腐爛時，它們釋放養分。"},{"en":"As these rot means while these dead plants or materials decay.","zh":"as these rot 指當這些死去植物或物質分解時。"},{"en":"As fallen leaves rot, they return nutrients to the soil.","zh":"當落葉腐爛時，它們把養分還給土壤。"},{"en":"If dead seagrasses rot in water, they can change water chemistry.","zh":"如果死海草在水中腐爛，它們可以改變水的化學狀況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what happens during decay.","zh":"這個片語描述腐化過程中發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"nutrients are released","meaning":"營養物被釋放","examples":[{"en":"Nutrients are released into the water as the plants decay.","zh":"當植物分解時，營養物被釋放到水中。"},{"en":"Nutrients are released means substances that feed living things are let out into the environment.","zh":"nutrients are released 指餵養生物的物質被釋放到環境中。"},{"en":"Compost releases nutrients into soil as kitchen waste breaks down.","zh":"當廚餘分解時，堆肥會把營養物釋放到土壤中。"},{"en":"If too many nutrients are released into water, algae may grow too quickly.","zh":"如果太多營養物被釋放到水中，藻類可能生長過快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a natural or pollution-related transfer of food substances.","zh":"這個片語描述食物性物質自然或因污染而轉移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"feed microscopic plants and animals","meaning":"為微小動植物提供養分","examples":[{"en":"The released nutrients feed microscopic plants and animals.","zh":"被釋放的營養物為微小動植物提供養分。"},{"en":"To feed microscopic plants and animals means to provide nutrients that allow tiny organisms to grow.","zh":"feed microscopic plants and animals 指提供養分，讓微小生物生長。"},{"en":"Fertiliser in a pond can feed tiny algae and make the water green.","zh":"池塘中的肥料可以為微小藻類提供養分，令水變綠。"},{"en":"If too many tiny organisms are fed by nutrients, blooms may form.","zh":"如果太多微小生物得到養分，可能形成大量繁殖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how nutrients support very small life forms.","zh":"這個片語描述養分如何支持極細小生命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"microscopic plants and animals","meaning":"微小動植物","examples":[{"en":"Microscopic plants and animals can multiply rapidly in nutrient-rich water.","zh":"微小動植物可以在養分豐富的水中快速繁殖。"},{"en":"Microscopic plants and animals are tiny living things that are too small to see clearly without a microscope.","zh":"microscopic plants and animals 是沒有顯微鏡便難以看清的微小生物。"},{"en":"Pond water may contain microscopic plants and animals even when it looks clear.","zh":"即使池水看起來清澈，裡面也可能含有微小動植物。"},{"en":"If nutrients increase, these tiny organisms may grow in huge numbers.","zh":"如果養分增加，這些微小生物可能大量生長。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to very small aquatic life.","zh":"這個片語指非常細小的水生生命。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"crystal-clear waters","meaning":"清澈透明的水域","examples":[{"en":"The bay was once known for its crystal-clear waters.","zh":"該海灣曾以清澈透明的水域聞名。"},{"en":"Crystal-clear waters are waters that are extremely clear and easy to see through.","zh":"crystal-clear waters 是非常清澈、容易看穿的水域。"},{"en":"Tourists enjoy swimming in crystal-clear waters where they can see fish below.","zh":"遊客喜歡在清澈透明的水域游泳，因為可看見下面的魚。"},{"en":"If pollution increases, crystal-clear waters may become cloudy and unattractive.","zh":"如果污染增加，清澈透明的水域可能變得混濁且不吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very clean-looking water.","zh":"這個片語描述看起來非常乾淨的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"resemble pea soup","meaning":"像濃湯般混濁","examples":[{"en":"The bay’s water sometimes resembles pea soup.","zh":"該海灣的水有時像濃湯般混濁。"},{"en":"To resemble pea soup means to look thick, green, and cloudy rather than clear.","zh":"resemble pea soup 指看起來濃稠、發綠而混濁，而不是清澈。"},{"en":"After algae grows too much, a pond may resemble pea soup.","zh":"當藻類過度生長後，池塘可能像濃湯般混濁。"},{"en":"If water resembles pea soup, sunlight may not reach underwater plants.","zh":"如果水像濃湯般混濁，陽光可能無法到達水下植物。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a vivid image of polluted, cloudy water.","zh":"這個片語用生動圖像描述受污染而混濁的水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in a vicious circle","meaning":"形成惡性循環","examples":[{"en":"The ecological damage continues in a vicious circle.","zh":"生態破壞形成惡性循環並持續下去。"},{"en":"In a vicious circle means one bad result causes another bad result, which then makes the first problem worse.","zh":"in a vicious circle 指一個壞結果造成另一個壞結果，而後者又令最初問題惡化。"},{"en":"A tired student may sleep late because of unfinished homework, then become too tired to finish the next day’s work.","zh":"疲倦學生可能因未完成功課而夜睡，然後太疲倦而無法完成翌日功課。"},{"en":"If dead seagrass feeds plankton and plankton blocks sunlight, more seagrass dies.","zh":"如果死海草餵養浮游生物，而浮游生物遮擋陽光，就會有更多海草死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a harmful cycle that reinforces itself.","zh":"這個片語描述會自我強化的有害循環。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"turbid blooms","meaning":"令水體混濁的浮游生物大量繁殖","examples":[{"en":"Turbid blooms prevent sunlight from reaching the seagrasses.","zh":"令水體混濁的浮游生物大量繁殖會阻止陽光到達海草。"},{"en":"Turbid blooms are cloudy masses of tiny organisms growing in water.","zh":"turbid blooms 是水中微小生物大量生長而形成的混濁團塊。"},{"en":"A lake may develop turbid blooms after fertiliser washes into it.","zh":"肥料被沖入湖中後，湖泊可能出現令水體混濁的浮游生物大量繁殖。"},{"en":"If turbid blooms block light, underwater plants cannot photosynthesise properly.","zh":"如果混濁藻華遮擋光線，水下植物就不能正常進行光合作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cloudy biological growth in water.","zh":"這個片語描述水中混濁的生物大量生長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"block out sunlight","meaning":"遮擋陽光","examples":[{"en":"Plankton blooms block out sunlight.","zh":"浮游生物大量繁殖會遮擋陽光。"},{"en":"To block out sunlight means to stop sunlight from passing through.","zh":"block out sunlight 指阻止陽光穿過。"},{"en":"Tall buildings can block out sunlight from small flats.","zh":"高樓可以遮擋小單位的陽光。"},{"en":"If cloudy water blocks out sunlight, plants below the surface may die.","zh":"如果混濁水體遮擋陽光，水面下的植物可能死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preventing light from reaching something.","zh":"這個片語描述阻止光線到達某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cause more seagrasses to die","meaning":"令更多海草死亡","examples":[{"en":"Reduced sunlight causes more seagrasses to die.","zh":"陽光減少令更多海草死亡。"},{"en":"To cause more seagrasses to die means to increase the death of these underwater plants.","zh":"cause more seagrasses to die 指增加這些水下植物的死亡。"},{"en":"If curtains block light from a houseplant, they may cause the plant to weaken.","zh":"如果窗簾遮擋室內植物的光線，可能令植物變弱。"},{"en":"When cloudy water reduces sunlight, seagrasses cannot make enough food.","zh":"當混濁水體減少陽光，海草無法製造足夠食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a direct ecological result of low light.","zh":"這個片語描述低光照帶來的直接生態結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"yet more turbidity","meaning":"更嚴重的水體混濁","examples":[{"en":"More dying seagrass leads to yet more turbidity.","zh":"更多死亡海草會導致更嚴重的水體混濁。"},{"en":"Yet more turbidity means an even greater level of cloudiness in the water.","zh":"yet more turbidity 指水中混濁程度進一步增加。"},{"en":"If construction dust keeps entering a stream, it may cause yet more turbidity.","zh":"如果建築塵土不斷流入溪流，可能造成更嚴重的水體混濁。"},{"en":"When dying plants feed more blooms, the water becomes increasingly cloudy.","zh":"當死亡植物餵養更多浮游生物，水會變得越來越混濁。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an already bad condition becomes worse.","zh":"這個片語顯示已經惡劣的情況變得更差。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tolerate much higher levels of","meaning":"承受高得多的……水平","examples":[{"en":"Lapointe believes that seagrasses can tolerate much higher levels of salinity.","zh":"Lapointe 相信海草能承受高得多的鹽度水平。"},{"en":"To tolerate much higher levels of something means to survive or function even when that thing is present in larger amounts.","zh":"tolerate much higher levels of something 指即使某事物含量較高，仍能生存或正常運作。"},{"en":"Some students can tolerate much higher levels of noise than others when studying.","zh":"有些學生溫習時能承受比其他人高得多的噪音水平。"},{"en":"If seagrasses tolerate high salt levels, salinity may not be the main cause of their death.","zh":"如果海草能承受高鹽度，鹽度可能不是其死亡主因。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong resistance to a condition.","zh":"這個片語描述對某條件有強抵抗力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"levels of salinity","meaning":"鹽度水平","examples":[{"en":"The bay’s levels of salinity may not be high enough to kill seagrasses.","zh":"該海灣的鹽度水平可能未高到足以殺死海草。"},{"en":"Levels of salinity are measurements of how salty water is.","zh":"levels of salinity 是水有多鹹的量度。"},{"en":"Aquarium owners check salinity levels before adding marine fish.","zh":"水族箱主人在加入海魚前會檢查鹽度水平。"},{"en":"If salinity levels rise too much, some plants and animals cannot survive.","zh":"如果鹽度水平升得太高，一些植物和動物無法生存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the amount of salt in water.","zh":"這個片語描述水中的鹽分含量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"furthermore","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"Furthermore, Lapointe points to evidence from an earlier experiment.","zh":"此外，Lapointe 指出來自較早實驗的證據。"},{"en":"Furthermore means in addition to what has just been said.","zh":"furthermore 指除了剛才所說之外。"},{"en":"The library is quiet; furthermore, it stays open after school.","zh":"圖書館很安靜；此外，它放學後仍開放。"},{"en":"Writers use furthermore to add another reason or piece of evidence.","zh":"作者使用 furthermore 來加入另一個理由或證據。"},{"en":"This word helps build an argument step by step.","zh":"這個詞幫助一步步建立論證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be increased experimentally","meaning":"以實驗方式增加","examples":[{"en":"Freshwater flows were increased experimentally during the 1990s.","zh":"淡水流量在1990年代以實驗方式增加。"},{"en":"To be increased experimentally means to be raised as part of a controlled test or study.","zh":"be increased experimentally 指作為受控測試或研究的一部分而被提高。"},{"en":"A teacher may increase homework experimentally for one month to see whether practice improves results.","zh":"老師可能以實驗方式增加一個月功課，以觀察練習是否改善成績。"},{"en":"If water flow is increased experimentally, researchers can observe the ecological response.","zh":"如果水流以實驗方式增加，研究人員可以觀察生態反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a planned test, not a permanent change.","zh":"這個片語描述計劃中的測試，而不是永久改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"The increased freshwater led to massive plankton blooms.","zh":"增加的淡水導致浮游生物大量繁殖。"},{"en":"To lead to something means to cause it to happen.","zh":"lead to something 指造成某事發生。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can lead to weaker concentration the next day.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致翌日專注力較弱。"},{"en":"If nutrient-rich water enters a bay, it may lead to rapid algae growth.","zh":"如果富含養分的水流入海灣，可能導致藻類快速生長。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with a result.","zh":"這個片語把原因與結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"massive plankton blooms","meaning":"浮游生物大量繁殖","examples":[{"en":"The experiment resulted in massive plankton blooms.","zh":"該實驗導致浮游生物大量繁殖。"},{"en":"Massive plankton blooms are very large increases in tiny floating organisms in water.","zh":"massive plankton blooms 是水中漂浮微生物數量大幅增加。"},{"en":"A lake may suffer massive plankton blooms after fertiliser runoff enters it.","zh":"肥料徑流進入湖泊後，湖泊可能出現浮游生物大量繁殖。"},{"en":"If blooms become massive, they can make water cloudy and block sunlight.","zh":"如果大量繁殖變得嚴重，會令水混濁並遮擋陽光。"},{"en":"This phrase describes explosive growth of plankton.","zh":"這個片語描述浮游生物爆發式增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"run off from","meaning":"從……流出","examples":[{"en":"Freshwater ran off from heavily fertilised farmland.","zh":"淡水從重度施肥的農地流出。"},{"en":"To run off from a place means for water to flow away from it, often carrying substances with it.","zh":"run off from a place 指水從某地方流走，常帶走其他物質。"},{"en":"Rainwater may run off from a road and carry oil into drains.","zh":"雨水可能從道路流出，並把油污帶入排水渠。"},{"en":"If water runs off from farmland, it can carry fertiliser into rivers.","zh":"如果水從農田流出，它可以把肥料帶入河流。"},{"en":"This phrase describes water leaving a surface or area.","zh":"這個片語描述水離開某表面或地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"well-fertilised farmland","meaning":"施用大量肥料的農地","examples":[{"en":"Water from well-fertilised farmland carried nitrogen into the bay.","zh":"來自施用大量肥料農地的水把氮帶入海灣。"},{"en":"Well-fertilised farmland is farmland that has received a large or effective amount of fertiliser.","zh":"well-fertilised farmland 是施用了大量或有效肥料的農地。"},{"en":"Well-fertilised farmland may produce more crops but also create polluted runoff.","zh":"施用大量肥料的農地可能產出更多農作物，但也造成污染徑流。"},{"en":"If rain washes fertiliser away, nearby water may receive too many nutrients.","zh":"如果雨水把肥料沖走，附近水域可能接收過多養分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes farmland treated with fertiliser.","zh":"這個片語描述使用肥料處理的農地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cause a fivefold rise in","meaning":"令……增加至五倍","examples":[{"en":"Farm runoff caused a fivefold rise in nitrogen levels.","zh":"農田徑流令氮含量增加至五倍。"},{"en":"To cause a fivefold rise in something means to make it increase to five times its previous level.","zh":"cause a fivefold rise in something 指令某物增加至原來水平的五倍。"},{"en":"A viral video may cause a fivefold rise in visits to a small shop’s website.","zh":"爆紅影片可能令小店網站瀏覽量增加至五倍。"},{"en":"If nitrogen levels rise fivefold, the water chemistry changes dramatically.","zh":"如果氮含量增加至五倍，水的化學狀況會大幅改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very large measurable increase.","zh":"這個片語描述非常大的可量度增幅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"nitrogen levels","meaning":"氮含量","examples":[{"en":"Nitrogen levels rose sharply after the freshwater flow increased.","zh":"淡水流量增加後，氮含量急劇上升。"},{"en":"Nitrogen levels are the amounts of nitrogen compounds in water, soil, or air.","zh":"nitrogen levels 是水、土壤或空氣中氮化合物的含量。"},{"en":"Farmers may test soil nitrogen levels before adding fertiliser.","zh":"農民可能在施肥前測試土壤氮含量。"},{"en":"If nitrogen levels in water become too high, algae may grow too fast.","zh":"如果水中氮含量過高，藻類可能生長過快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a measurable nutrient level.","zh":"這個片語描述可量度的養分水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be like pouring fuel on a fire","meaning":"猶如火上加油","examples":[{"en":"Adding nitrogen-rich water was like pouring fuel on a fire.","zh":"加入富含氮的水猶如火上加油。"},{"en":"To be like pouring fuel on a fire means to make an already bad problem much worse.","zh":"be like pouring fuel on a fire 指令已經糟糕的問題變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"Shouting during an argument is like pouring fuel on a fire.","zh":"在爭吵中大聲叫喊猶如火上加油。"},{"en":"If algae are already growing, adding nutrients can make the bloom explode.","zh":"如果藻類已在生長，加入養分可以令藻華爆發。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strong image of making trouble worse.","zh":"這個片語用強烈圖像描述令麻煩惡化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"mass mortality of","meaning":"……大量死亡","examples":[{"en":"The plankton bloom caused mass mortality of seagrasses.","zh":"浮游生物大量繁殖導致海草大量死亡。"},{"en":"Mass mortality of something means a large number of living things die at the same time or in a short period.","zh":"mass mortality of something 指大量生物在同一時間或短期內死亡。"},{"en":"Extreme heat can cause mass mortality of fish in shallow ponds.","zh":"極端高溫可以導致淺池魚類大量死亡。"},{"en":"If seagrass dies in large quantities, the animals depending on it lose shelter.","zh":"如果海草大量死亡，依賴它的動物會失去庇護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large-scale death.","zh":"這個片語描述大規模死亡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"increased turbidity","meaning":"水體混濁度增加","examples":[{"en":"The plankton caused increased turbidity in the water.","zh":"浮游生物令水體混濁度增加。"},{"en":"Increased turbidity means the water has become more cloudy and less clear.","zh":"increased turbidity 指水變得更混濁、不再清澈。"},{"en":"Building work near a river can cause increased turbidity after rain.","zh":"河流附近的建築工程在下雨後可以造成水體混濁度增加。"},{"en":"If turbidity increases, sunlight cannot pass through the water easily.","zh":"如果混濁度增加，陽光不能容易穿過水體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes worsening water clarity.","zh":"這個片語描述水質清澈度惡化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"thrive only in waters where","meaning":"只在……的水域中茁壯生長","examples":[{"en":"Corals thrive only in waters where nutrient levels are low.","zh":"珊瑚只在養分含量低的水域中茁壯生長。"},{"en":"To thrive only in waters where a condition exists means to grow well only under that water condition.","zh":"thrive only in waters where a condition exists 指只在具備某水質條件時才能良好生長。"},{"en":"Some aquarium fish thrive only in waters where the temperature is carefully controlled.","zh":"一些水族箱魚只在溫度受仔細控制的水中茁壯生長。"},{"en":"If corals need low nutrients, polluted water may stop them from growing.","zh":"如果珊瑚需要低養分水域，受污染的水可能阻止其生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strict environmental requirement.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴格的環境要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"nutrient levels","meaning":"養分含量","examples":[{"en":"High nutrient levels can damage coral reefs.","zh":"高養分含量可以破壞珊瑚礁。"},{"en":"Nutrient levels are the amounts of substances such as nitrogen and phosphorus that feed plants and tiny organisms.","zh":"nutrient levels 是氮和磷等餵養植物及微小生物的物質含量。"},{"en":"Gardeners check nutrient levels in soil before planting vegetables.","zh":"園丁在種菜前會檢查土壤養分含量。"},{"en":"If nutrient levels in seawater rise too much, algae may grow and harm corals.","zh":"如果海水養分含量升得太高，藻類可能生長並傷害珊瑚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the amount of growth-supporting substances.","zh":"這個片語描述支持生長物質的含量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"do more damage to","meaning":"對……造成更大破壞","examples":[{"en":"Nitrogen-rich freshwater may do more damage to the reef.","zh":"富含氮的淡水可能對珊瑚礁造成更大破壞。"},{"en":"To do more damage to something means to harm it more seriously or further.","zh":"do more damage to something 指對某物造成更嚴重或進一步傷害。"},{"en":"Ignoring a small leak can do more damage to a house over time.","zh":"忽視小漏水會隨時間對房屋造成更大破壞。"},{"en":"If a solution brings extra pollution, it may do more damage than the original problem.","zh":"如果解決方案帶來額外污染，它造成的破壞可能比原問題更大。"},{"en":"This phrase compares or emphasises harmful effects.","zh":"這個片語比較或強調有害影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a plausible theory","meaning":"合理的理論","examples":[{"en":"Lapointe’s explanation is a plausible theory.","zh":"Lapointe 的解釋是一個合理的理論。"},{"en":"A plausible theory is an explanation that seems reasonable based on available evidence.","zh":"plausible theory 是根據現有證據看來合理的解釋。"},{"en":"If a student’s bus was delayed during heavy rain, lateness has a plausible explanation.","zh":"如果學生在大雨期間因巴士延誤而遲到，這是一個合理解釋。"},{"en":"A plausible theory still needs testing before it is accepted as true.","zh":"合理理論在被接受為真前仍需要測試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an idea that is believable but not yet proven.","zh":"這個片語描述可信但尚未證實的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"water flowing off crops","meaning":"從農作物田地流出的水","examples":[{"en":"Water flowing off crops can carry fertilisers into the bay.","zh":"從農作物田地流出的水可以把肥料帶入海灣。"},{"en":"Water flowing off crops is runoff that moves from farm fields into nearby drains, rivers, or seas.","zh":"water flowing off crops 是從農田流入附近排水渠、河流或海洋的徑流。"},{"en":"After rain, water flowing off vegetable fields may carry soil and chemicals away.","zh":"下雨後，從菜田流出的水可能帶走泥土和化學物。"},{"en":"If crop runoff contains fertiliser, it can add nutrients to natural waters.","zh":"如果農田徑流含有肥料，它可以把養分加入自然水域。"},{"en":"This phrase describes farm water moving into the wider environment.","zh":"這個片語描述農田水流入更大環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"heavily fertilised farmland","meaning":"重度施肥的農地","examples":[{"en":"Heavily fertilised farmland lies on the northern edge of the Everglades.","zh":"重度施肥的農地位於大沼澤地北緣。"},{"en":"Heavily fertilised farmland is farmland treated with large amounts of fertiliser.","zh":"heavily fertilised farmland 是施用了大量肥料的農地。"},{"en":"Heavily fertilised farmland may produce strong crops but also polluted runoff.","zh":"重度施肥的農地可能產出強壯作物，但也造成受污染徑流。"},{"en":"If rain washes fertiliser into rivers, nearby water quality may fall.","zh":"如果雨水把肥料沖入河流，附近水質可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes farmland with a high level of fertiliser use.","zh":"這個片語描述肥料使用量高的農地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on the northern edge of","meaning":"位於……的北緣","examples":[{"en":"The farmland is located on the northern edge of the Everglades.","zh":"該農地位於大沼澤地北緣。"},{"en":"On the northern edge of a place means along its north side or boundary.","zh":"on the northern edge of a place 指沿某地北側或北部邊界。"},{"en":"A housing estate may be built on the northern edge of a town.","zh":"屋苑可能建在城鎮北緣。"},{"en":"If farms sit on the edge of a wetland, runoff may enter the wetland system.","zh":"如果農田位於濕地邊緣，徑流可能進入濕地系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a position at the north boundary of an area.","zh":"這個片語描述位於某區北部邊界的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be rich in nitrogen","meaning":"含有大量氮","examples":[{"en":"Water from the farmland is rich in nitrogen.","zh":"來自農地的水含有大量氮。"},{"en":"To be rich in nitrogen means to contain a high amount of nitrogen compounds.","zh":"be rich in nitrogen 指含有高量氮化合物。"},{"en":"Compost can be rich in nitrogen and help plants grow.","zh":"堆肥可以含有大量氮，並幫助植物生長。"},{"en":"If water is rich in nitrogen, algae may multiply quickly.","zh":"如果水含有大量氮，藻類可能快速繁殖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a high concentration of a nutrient.","zh":"這個片語描述某種養分濃度高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"end up in","meaning":"最終流入……","examples":[{"en":"Much of the nitrogen eventually ends up in the bay.","zh":"大部分氮最終流入海灣。"},{"en":"To end up in a place means to finally arrive there, often after moving through other places.","zh":"end up in a place 指最終到達某地方，常是在經過其他地方後。"},{"en":"Plastic thrown on the street may end up in the sea after heavy rain.","zh":"街上丟棄的塑膠可能在大雨後最終流入海中。"},{"en":"If chemicals end up in water, they can affect plants and animals.","zh":"如果化學物最終進入水中，它們可能影響植物和動物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the final destination of something.","zh":"這個片語描述某物的最終去處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be convinced that","meaning":"深信","examples":[{"en":"Kruczynski is convinced that farmland nitrogen is not the chief problem.","zh":"Kruczynski 深信農田氮並非主要問題。"},{"en":"To be convinced that something is true means to strongly believe it after considering evidence.","zh":"be convinced that something is true 指考慮證據後強烈相信某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may be convinced that a student can improve after seeing steady effort.","zh":"老師看到學生穩定努力後，可能深信他能進步。"},{"en":"If a scientist is convinced by evidence, they may support one explanation over another.","zh":"如果科學家被證據說服，可能支持其中一個解釋而非另一個。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong belief.","zh":"這個片語表示強烈信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the chief problem","meaning":"主要問題","examples":[{"en":"Nitrogen from farmland may not be the chief problem.","zh":"來自農地的氮可能不是主要問題。"},{"en":"The chief problem is the main or most important problem.","zh":"chief problem 是最主要或最重要的問題。"},{"en":"In a noisy classroom, the chief problem may be unclear rules rather than bad students.","zh":"在嘈吵課室中，主要問題可能是規則不清，而不是學生壞。"},{"en":"If people identify the chief problem wrongly, their solution may fail.","zh":"如果人們錯誤識別主要問題，解決方案可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the main cause of trouble.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於麻煩的主要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"well away from","meaning":"遠離……","examples":[{"en":"Some dying coral reefs are well away from farmland pollution.","zh":"一些正在死亡的珊瑚礁遠離農地污染。"},{"en":"Well away from means far from something, not close to it.","zh":"well away from 指遠離某物，而不是靠近它。"},{"en":"A school playground should be well away from busy traffic.","zh":"學校操場應遠離繁忙交通。"},{"en":"If damaged reefs are far from farmland, farmland pollution may not explain all the damage.","zh":"如果受損珊瑚礁遠離農地，農地污染可能不能解釋所有破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses distance from a possible cause or danger.","zh":"這個片語強調與可能原因或危險的距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"nitrogen pollution","meaning":"氮污染","examples":[{"en":"Some reefs unaffected by nitrogen pollution are also dying.","zh":"一些未受氮污染影響的珊瑚礁也正在死亡。"},{"en":"Nitrogen pollution is pollution caused by too much nitrogen entering water, soil, or air.","zh":"nitrogen pollution 是過多氮進入水、土壤或空氣造成的污染。"},{"en":"Fertiliser runoff can create nitrogen pollution in rivers and lakes.","zh":"肥料徑流可以在河流和湖泊造成氮污染。"},{"en":"If nitrogen pollution increases, algae may grow too fast and reduce oxygen.","zh":"如果氮污染增加，藻類可能過快生長並減少氧氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pollution from excess nutrients.","zh":"這個片語描述來自過量養分的污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"curiously","meaning":"奇怪的是","examples":[{"en":"Curiously, a few coral reefs are thriving.","zh":"奇怪的是，少數珊瑚礁正在茁壯生長。"},{"en":"Curiously means strangely or surprisingly, especially when something does not fit the expected pattern.","zh":"curiously 指奇怪地或令人意外地，特別是某事不符合預期模式時。"},{"en":"Curiously, the quiet student gave the most confident presentation.","zh":"奇怪的是，那名安靜學生作出了最有信心的匯報。"},{"en":"If some reefs thrive while nearby reefs die, the pattern needs closer study.","zh":"如果一些珊瑚礁茁壯生長，而附近珊瑚礁死亡，這種模式需要更仔細研究。"},{"en":"This word introduces an unexpected observation.","zh":"這個詞引入出乎意料的觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"local sewage discharges","meaning":"當地污水排放","examples":[{"en":"Local sewage discharges may contribute to the pollution.","zh":"當地污水排放可能導致污染。"},{"en":"Local sewage discharges are releases of wastewater from homes, toilets, or treatment systems nearby.","zh":"local sewage discharges 是附近家庭、廁所或處理系統排出的污水。"},{"en":"A beach may close if local sewage discharges make the water unsafe.","zh":"如果當地污水排放令水質不安全，海灘可能關閉。"},{"en":"If sewage enters the sea, it can add nutrients and harmful bacteria.","zh":"如果污水進入海中，它可以增加養分和有害細菌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pollution from human waste systems.","zh":"這個片語描述來自人類污水系統的污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"thousands of cesspits","meaning":"數以千計的化糞池","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of cesspits are located along the Florida Keys.","zh":"佛羅里達礁島群沿線有數以千計的化糞池。"},{"en":"Thousands of cesspits means a very large number of underground pits used to collect sewage.","zh":"thousands of cesspits 指大量用來收集污水的地下坑池。"},{"en":"Old villages may rely on cesspits instead of modern sewerage systems.","zh":"舊村落可能依賴化糞池，而不是現代污水處理系統。"},{"en":"If many cesspits leak, nearby groundwater and seawater may become polluted.","zh":"如果許多化糞池滲漏，附近地下水和海水可能受污染。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a large possible sewage source.","zh":"這個片語指出一個巨大的可能污水來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be part of the problem","meaning":"是問題的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Sewage from cesspits may be part of the problem.","zh":"來自化糞池的污水可能是問題的一部分。"},{"en":"To be part of the problem means to contribute to a bad situation, even if it is not the only cause.","zh":"be part of the problem 指對壞情況有貢獻，即使不是唯一原因。"},{"en":"If students are tired, long homework may be part of the problem.","zh":"如果學生疲倦，長時間功課可能是問題的一部分。"},{"en":"If both farms and sewage add nutrients, each may worsen pollution.","zh":"如果農田和污水都增加養分，兩者都可能加劇污染。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies one contributing factor.","zh":"這個片語指出其中一個促成因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"claims and counterclaims","meaning":"各方相反的主張","examples":[{"en":"Claims and counterclaims make the outcome difficult to predict.","zh":"各方相反的主張令結果難以預測。"},{"en":"Claims and counterclaims are arguments and opposing arguments made by different sides.","zh":"claims and counterclaims 是不同方面提出的論點和相反論點。"},{"en":"In a school debate, one team gives claims and the other gives counterclaims.","zh":"在學校辯論中，一隊提出主張，另一隊提出反駁主張。"},{"en":"If experts offer opposite explanations, decisions become harder.","zh":"如果專家提出相反解釋，決策會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a dispute with competing arguments.","zh":"這個片語描述有互相競爭論點的爭議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the impact of","meaning":"……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Scientists cannot confidently predict the impact of the restoration plan.","zh":"科學家無法有信心地預測修復計劃的影響。"},{"en":"The impact of something is the effect or influence it has.","zh":"impact of something 是某事帶來的效果或影響。"},{"en":"A teacher may study the impact of smaller classes on students’ writing.","zh":"老師可能研究小班教學對學生寫作的影響。"},{"en":"If a plan affects water quality, wildlife, and tourism, its impact is complex.","zh":"如果計劃影響水質、野生動物和旅遊，其影響就很複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase asks what results something will produce.","zh":"這個片語詢問某事會產生甚麼結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"difficult to predict","meaning":"難以預測","examples":[{"en":"The effects of the project are difficult to predict.","zh":"該項目的效果難以預測。"},{"en":"Difficult to predict means hard to know in advance.","zh":"difficult to predict 指事先難以知道。"},{"en":"The weather can be difficult to predict during a typhoon season.","zh":"颱風季期間，天氣可能難以預測。"},{"en":"If many factors interact, the final result becomes uncertain.","zh":"如果許多因素互相作用，最終結果會變得不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uncertainty about the future.","zh":"這個片語描述對未來的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"benefit from","meaning":"從……受益","examples":[{"en":"The bay may benefit from the restoration of freshwater flows.","zh":"該海灣可能從恢復淡水流量中受益。"},{"en":"To benefit from something means to gain help, improvement, or advantage from it.","zh":"benefit from something 指從某事得到幫助、改善或好處。"},{"en":"Students benefit from clear examples when learning new vocabulary.","zh":"學生學習新詞彙時會從清晰例子中受益。"},{"en":"If natural water flows return, plants and animals may recover.","zh":"如果自然水流恢復，植物和動物可能復原。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving a positive effect.","zh":"這個片語描述得到正面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make matters much worse","meaning":"令情況惡化很多","examples":[{"en":"If nitrogen is the problem, the project could make matters much worse.","zh":"如果氮是問題所在，該項目可能令情況惡化很多。"},{"en":"To make matters much worse means to turn a bad situation into a far more serious one.","zh":"make matters much worse 指把壞情況變成嚴重得多的情況。"},{"en":"Ignoring a small illness can make matters much worse if it spreads.","zh":"如果小病擴散，忽視它可能令情況惡化很多。"},{"en":"If a solution adds more pollution, it may worsen the original problem.","zh":"如果解決方案增加更多污染，它可能令原本問題惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that action may have harmful consequences.","zh":"這個片語警告行動可能有害後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the second hypothesis","meaning":"第二個假說","examples":[{"en":"The second hypothesis concerns nitrogen pollution.","zh":"第二個假說關乎氮污染。"},{"en":"The second hypothesis is the second possible explanation being discussed.","zh":"second hypothesis 是正在討論的第二個可能解釋。"},{"en":"In a science lesson, the first hypothesis may involve heat, while the second hypothesis involves light.","zh":"在科學課中，第一個假說可能涉及熱力，第二個假說涉及光線。"},{"en":"If the second hypothesis is correct, the solution must address a different cause.","zh":"如果第二個假說正確，解決方案就必須處理不同原因。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise competing explanations.","zh":"這個片語幫助組織互相競爭的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"prove correct","meaning":"證實正確","examples":[{"en":"If the hypothesis proves correct, nitrogen will need to be removed.","zh":"如果該假說證實正確，就需要去除氮。"},{"en":"To prove correct means to turn out to be true after evidence is checked.","zh":"prove correct 指在證據被檢查後證明為真。"},{"en":"If a doctor’s first diagnosis proves correct, treatment can begin quickly.","zh":"如果醫生最初診斷證實正確，治療就能迅速開始。"},{"en":"If a theory proves correct, policy should follow its evidence.","zh":"如果理論證實正確，政策應跟隨其證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes confirmation after uncertainty.","zh":"這個片語描述不確定後得到證實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"remove nitrogen from","meaning":"從……去除氮","examples":[{"en":"The authorities may need to remove nitrogen from farmland runoff.","zh":"當局可能需要從農田徑流中去除氮。"},{"en":"To remove nitrogen from something means to take nitrogen compounds out of it.","zh":"remove nitrogen from something 指把氮化合物從某物中移除。"},{"en":"A filter may remove harmful chemicals from drinking water.","zh":"過濾器可能從飲用水中去除有害化學物。"},{"en":"If nitrogen is removed from runoff before it reaches the bay, algae growth may be reduced.","zh":"如果徑流到達海灣前已去除氮，藻類生長可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cleaning water by taking out excess nutrients.","zh":"這個片語描述透過移除過量養分來淨化水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"neither will be easy","meaning":"兩者都不容易","examples":[{"en":"Removing nitrogen from farmland and sewage will not be easy.","zh":"從農田和污水中去除氮，兩者都不容易。"},{"en":"Neither will be easy means both tasks will be difficult.","zh":"neither will be easy 指兩項任務都困難。"},{"en":"Reducing school stress and improving exam results are both important, but neither will be easy.","zh":"減少學校壓力和提高考試成績都很重要，但兩者都不容易。"},{"en":"If two pollution sources must be fixed, both may require time and money.","zh":"如果兩個污染來源都必須處理，兩者可能都需要時間和金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses difficulty on both sides.","zh":"這個片語強調兩方面都有困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"man-made wetlands","meaning":"人工濕地","examples":[{"en":"Man-made wetlands are being built near the bay.","zh":"人工濕地正在海灣附近興建。"},{"en":"Man-made wetlands are artificial wetland areas designed by people to clean water or support wildlife.","zh":"man-made wetlands 是人類設計、用來淨化水或支持野生動物的人工濕地區域。"},{"en":"A city may build man-made wetlands to filter storm water before it enters a river.","zh":"城市可能建造人工濕地，在雨水流入河流前過濾它。"},{"en":"If wetlands trap nutrients, they can reduce some kinds of pollution.","zh":"如果濕地能截留養分，它們可以減少某些污染。"},{"en":"This phrase describes human-created wetland systems.","zh":"這個片語描述人造濕地系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"currently being built","meaning":"目前正在興建","examples":[{"en":"The wetlands are currently being built to reduce pollution.","zh":"這些濕地目前正在興建，以減少污染。"},{"en":"Currently being built means under construction now.","zh":"currently being built 指現在正在施工。"},{"en":"A new library is currently being built beside the school.","zh":"新圖書館目前正在學校旁邊興建。"},{"en":"If a system is still being built, its full effects cannot yet be measured.","zh":"如果系統仍在興建，其完整效果尚不能量度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something in progress at the present time.","zh":"這個片語描述目前正在進行中的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reduce phosphate runoff","meaning":"減少磷酸鹽徑流","examples":[{"en":"The wetlands are designed to reduce phosphate runoff.","zh":"這些濕地旨在減少磷酸鹽徑流。"},{"en":"To reduce phosphate runoff means to lower the amount of phosphate carried away by flowing water.","zh":"reduce phosphate runoff 指降低被水流帶走的磷酸鹽量。"},{"en":"Farms can reduce fertiliser runoff by planting grass strips beside fields.","zh":"農場可以透過在田邊種草帶來減少肥料徑流。"},{"en":"If phosphate runoff decreases, algae growth may become easier to control.","zh":"如果磷酸鹽徑流減少，藻類生長可能較易控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cutting nutrient pollution from moving water.","zh":"這個片語描述減少流動水中的養分污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fertiliser runoff","meaning":"肥料徑流","examples":[{"en":"Fertiliser runoff carries nutrients into the bay.","zh":"肥料徑流把養分帶入海灣。"},{"en":"Fertiliser runoff is water that washes fertiliser from farms, gardens, or lawns into nearby water bodies.","zh":"fertiliser runoff 是把農場、花園或草坪上的肥料沖入附近水體的水流。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can create fertiliser runoff from a golf course.","zh":"大雨可以造成高爾夫球場的肥料徑流。"},{"en":"If fertiliser runoff reaches a river, it can feed algae and reduce water quality.","zh":"如果肥料徑流到達河流，它可以餵養藻類並降低水質。"},{"en":"This phrase describes nutrient pollution from land.","zh":"這個片語描述來自陸地的養分污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"algal culture","meaning":"藻類培養物","examples":[{"en":"An algal culture might help remove nitrogen from the water.","zh":"藻類培養物可能有助從水中去除氮。"},{"en":"An algal culture is a controlled growth of algae used for study or treatment.","zh":"algal culture 是受控生長、用於研究或處理的藻類。"},{"en":"Scientists may grow an algal culture in a tank to test how algae absorb nutrients.","zh":"科學家可能在水槽中培養藻類，以測試藻類如何吸收養分。"},{"en":"If algae take up nitrogen, an algal culture could help clean polluted water.","zh":"如果藻類吸收氮，藻類培養物可以幫助淨化受污染水體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes algae grown deliberately for a purpose.","zh":"這個片語描述為特定目的而有意培養的藻類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a contained algal bloom","meaning":"受控藻華","examples":[{"en":"The proposed system would use a contained algal bloom.","zh":"建議系統會使用受控藻華。"},{"en":"A contained algal bloom is algae growth kept within a controlled area so it does not spread freely.","zh":"contained algal bloom 是被限制在受控區域內、不自由擴散的藻類大量生長。"},{"en":"A laboratory tank can hold a contained algal bloom for water-treatment experiments.","zh":"實驗室水槽可以容納受控藻華，用於水處理實驗。"},{"en":"If the bloom is contained, algae can absorb nutrients without clouding the whole bay.","zh":"如果藻華受控，藻類可以吸收養分而不令整個海灣混濁。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled use of algae.","zh":"這個片語描述對藻類的受控使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deal with discharges from","meaning":"處理來自……的排放","examples":[{"en":"The wetlands would need to deal with discharges from farmland.","zh":"這些濕地需要處理來自農地的排放。"},{"en":"To deal with discharges from a place means to handle or treat waste water flowing out of it.","zh":"deal with discharges from a place 指處理或淨化從某地流出的廢水。"},{"en":"A factory must deal with discharges from its machines before water enters a river.","zh":"工廠必須在水進入河流前處理來自機器的排放。"},{"en":"If wetlands cannot treat farm discharges, nutrients may still reach the bay.","zh":"如果濕地不能處理農田排放，養分仍可能到達海灣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes managing waste or polluted water.","zh":"這個片語描述管理廢水或受污染水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be costly","meaning":"成本高昂","examples":[{"en":"Adding an algal culture to the wetlands would be costly.","zh":"在濕地加入藻類培養物成本高昂。"},{"en":"To be costly means to require a lot of money.","zh":"be costly 指需要很多金錢。"},{"en":"Replacing all school computers at once would be costly.","zh":"一次過更換所有學校電腦會成本高昂。"},{"en":"If a solution is costly, governments must decide whether the benefits justify the price.","zh":"如果解決方案成本高昂，政府必須決定其好處是否值得。"},{"en":"This phrase describes high financial cost.","zh":"這個片語描述高昂財政成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the replacement of…with…","meaning":"以……取代……","examples":[{"en":"The replacement of cesspits with proper sewerage would be expensive.","zh":"以完善污水處理系統取代化糞池會十分昂貴。"},{"en":"The replacement of A with B means taking away A and using B instead.","zh":"replacement of A with B 指移除 A，改用 B。"},{"en":"The replacement of old desks with adjustable ones can make classrooms more comfortable.","zh":"以可調校書桌取代舊書桌可以令課室更舒適。"},{"en":"If cesspits are replaced with sewerage, sewage pollution may be reduced.","zh":"如果以污水處理系統取代化糞池，污水污染可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change from an old system to a new one.","zh":"這個片語描述由舊系統轉為新系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"proper sewerage","meaning":"完善的污水處理系統","examples":[{"en":"The Florida Keys need proper sewerage to reduce sewage pollution.","zh":"佛羅里達礁島群需要完善的污水處理系統來減少污水污染。"},{"en":"Proper sewerage is a safe and organised system for collecting and treating sewage.","zh":"proper sewerage 是安全而有組織地收集和處理污水的系統。"},{"en":"A growing town needs proper sewerage so waste does not leak into wells or rivers.","zh":"成長中的小鎮需要完善污水處理系統，避免廢物流入水井或河流。"},{"en":"If proper sewerage is absent, human waste may pollute nearby water.","zh":"如果缺乏完善污水處理系統，人類廢物可能污染附近水域。"},{"en":"This phrase describes modern sewage infrastructure.","zh":"這個片語描述現代污水基建。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"one estimate puts the cost at","meaning":"一項估算認為成本為……","examples":[{"en":"One estimate puts the cost of the work at $650 million.","zh":"一項估算認為工程成本為6.5億美元。"},{"en":"One estimate puts the cost at a figure means one calculation says the work will cost that amount.","zh":"one estimate puts the cost at a figure 指一項計算認為工程將花費該金額。"},{"en":"One estimate puts the cost of renovating the school hall at two million dollars.","zh":"一項估算認為翻新學校禮堂成本為二百萬美元。"},{"en":"If estimates are high, officials may delay or redesign the project.","zh":"如果估算成本很高，官員可能延遲或重新設計項目。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a calculated cost.","zh":"這個片語引入計算得出的成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"either way","meaning":"無論如何","examples":[{"en":"Either way, the proposed protective zone will not stop the pollution.","zh":"無論如何，擬議保護區都不能阻止污染。"},{"en":"Either way means whichever of the two possibilities is true.","zh":"either way 指兩種可能性中無論哪一種為真。"},{"en":"You can take the bus or walk; either way, you should arrive before class starts.","zh":"你可以乘巴士或步行；無論如何，你應該在上課前到達。"},{"en":"If both explanations lead to the same practical problem, the conclusion applies either way.","zh":"如果兩種解釋都導向同一實際問題，結論無論如何都適用。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the result is the same under different possibilities.","zh":"這個片語顯示在不同可能性下結果相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be designated as","meaning":"被劃為……","examples":[{"en":"A large area of sea will be designated as a protective zone.","zh":"一大片海域將被劃為保護區。"},{"en":"To be designated as something means to be officially named or assigned that role.","zh":"be designated as something 指被官方命名或指定為某角色。"},{"en":"A building may be designated as a heritage site.","zh":"建築物可能被劃為文物地點。"},{"en":"If an area is designated as protected, rules may limit what people can do there.","zh":"如果某地被劃為受保護區域，規則可能限制人們在那裡做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official classification.","zh":"這個片語描述官方分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"protective zone","meaning":"保護區","examples":[{"en":"The government plans to establish a protective zone around the reef.","zh":"政府計劃在珊瑚礁周圍設立保護區。"},{"en":"A protective zone is an area where special rules are used to protect nature, people, or property.","zh":"protective zone 是用特殊規則保護自然、人或財產的區域。"},{"en":"A school may create a protective zone near the gate where cars cannot stop.","zh":"學校可能在校門附近設立車輛不能停靠的保護區。"},{"en":"If a reef lies inside a protective zone, fishing or boating may be restricted.","zh":"如果珊瑚礁位於保護區內，捕魚或划船可能受限制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an area set aside for protection.","zh":"這個片語描述為保護而劃出的區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"deputy secretary of commerce","meaning":"商務部副部長","examples":[{"en":"The protective zone will be announced by the deputy secretary of commerce.","zh":"保護區將由商務部副部長宣布。"},{"en":"A deputy secretary of commerce is a senior government official working under the commerce secretary.","zh":"deputy secretary of commerce 是在商務部長之下工作的高級政府官員。"},{"en":"A deputy secretary may announce policies related to business, trade, or economic activity.","zh":"副部長可能宣布與商業、貿易或經濟活動有關的政策。"},{"en":"If a senior official announces a zone, the plan has formal government support.","zh":"如果高級官員宣布某區域，該計劃具有正式政府支持。"},{"en":"This phrase names a government position.","zh":"這個片語指出一個政府職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"do nothing to","meaning":"對……毫無幫助","examples":[{"en":"The designation will do nothing to stop pollution entering the reef.","zh":"這項劃定對阻止污染進入珊瑚礁毫無幫助。"},{"en":"To do nothing to solve a problem means to have no useful effect on it.","zh":"do nothing to solve a problem 指對解決問題沒有任何有用效果。"},{"en":"Buying a new notebook will do nothing to improve grades if a student never studies.","zh":"如果學生從不溫習，買新筆記簿對提高成績毫無幫助。"},{"en":"If a protective zone does not stop dirty water, it cannot solve water pollution.","zh":"如果保護區不能阻止污水，它就不能解決水污染。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that an action is ineffective for a specific problem.","zh":"這個片語強調某行動對特定問題無效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"protect the reef from","meaning":"保護珊瑚礁免受……","examples":[{"en":"The protective zone cannot protect the reef from water pollution.","zh":"保護區不能保護珊瑚礁免受水污染。"},{"en":"To protect the reef from something means to keep the reef safe from that danger.","zh":"protect the reef from something 指令珊瑚礁免受該危險傷害。"},{"en":"Rules may protect children from unsafe traffic near school.","zh":"規則可以保護兒童免受學校附近危險交通傷害。"},{"en":"If pollution flows through water, a boundary on a map may not protect the reef.","zh":"如果污染透過水流移動，地圖上的邊界未必能保護珊瑚礁。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preventing harm to a reef.","zh":"這個片語描述防止珊瑚礁受害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a more fundamental flaw","meaning":"更根本的缺陷","examples":[{"en":"Some critics believe that the plans contain a more fundamental flaw.","zh":"一些批評者認為這些計劃包含更根本的缺陷。"},{"en":"A more fundamental flaw is a deeper problem in the basic idea or design.","zh":"more fundamental flaw 是基本想法或設計中的深層問題。"},{"en":"A lesson plan may have a fundamental flaw if students cannot understand the instructions.","zh":"如果學生不能理解指示，課堂計劃可能有根本缺陷。"},{"en":"If the original goal is wrong, small improvements cannot fix the plan.","zh":"如果原本目標錯誤，小修小補無法修正計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a serious underlying weakness.","zh":"這個片語指出嚴重的根本弱點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"return something to","meaning":"把某物恢復至……","examples":[{"en":"The restoration plan aims to return the bay to an earlier condition.","zh":"修復計劃旨在把海灣恢復至較早狀態。"},{"en":"To return something to a condition means to bring it back to that state.","zh":"return something to a condition 指把某物帶回某種狀態。"},{"en":"A cleaner may return a classroom to order after a messy activity.","zh":"清潔工可能在混亂活動後把課室恢復整齊。"},{"en":"If people return a wetland to a former condition, they try to restore old water patterns.","zh":"如果人們把濕地恢復至以前狀態，就是嘗試恢復舊水流模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes restoration to a previous state.","zh":"這個片語描述恢復至以前狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a Utopian ideal","meaning":"烏托邦式的理想狀態","examples":[{"en":"The plan may be based on a Utopian ideal of the natural bay.","zh":"該計劃可能建基於自然海灣的烏托邦式理想狀態。"},{"en":"A Utopian ideal is an imagined perfect state that may be unrealistic.","zh":"Utopian ideal 是想像中完美但可能不切實際的狀態。"},{"en":"A school with no exams, no stress, and perfect motivation is a Utopian ideal.","zh":"沒有考試、沒有壓力、動機完美的學校是一種烏托邦式理想。"},{"en":"If restoration is based on an unrealistic ideal, the plan may ignore natural change.","zh":"如果修復建基於不現實理想，計劃可能忽視自然變化。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a goal may be too perfect to be practical.","zh":"這個片語提醒某目標可能過於完美而不實際。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"before humans wrought damage","meaning":"在人類造成破壞之前","examples":[{"en":"Some people want to restore the bay to its condition before humans wrought damage.","zh":"一些人希望把海灣恢復至人類造成破壞之前的狀態。"},{"en":"Before humans wrought damage means before people caused serious harm to the environment.","zh":"before humans wrought damage 指在人類對環境造成嚴重傷害之前。"},{"en":"A forest may never return fully to its state before humans wrought damage through logging.","zh":"森林可能永遠無法完全回到人類砍伐造成破壞之前的狀態。"},{"en":"If no one knows the original condition clearly, restoration goals become uncertain.","zh":"如果沒有人清楚知道原本狀態，修復目標就變得不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts a damaged present with an imagined earlier natural state.","zh":"這個片語把受損現在與想像中的早期自然狀態作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"wrought damage","meaning":"造成破壞","examples":[{"en":"Canal construction wrought considerable damage on the bay.","zh":"運河建設對海灣造成相當大破壞。"},{"en":"To wrought damage means to cause serious harm, especially through an action or process.","zh":"wrought damage 指透過某行動或過程造成嚴重傷害。"},{"en":"A poorly planned road can wrought damage on a quiet neighbourhood.","zh":"規劃不善的道路可以對安靜社區造成破壞。"},{"en":"If engineering works change water flow, they may damage wetlands for decades.","zh":"如果工程改變水流，可能對濕地造成數十年破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and describes serious harm caused by human action.","zh":"這個片語較正式，描述人類行動造成的嚴重傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cut the largest canals","meaning":"開鑿最大的運河","examples":[{"en":"Engineers cut the largest canals in the Everglades during the 1950s.","zh":"工程師在1950年代於大沼澤地開鑿最大的運河。"},{"en":"To cut canals means to dig artificial waterways through land.","zh":"cut canals 指在土地中挖掘人工水道。"},{"en":"Workers may cut a canal to move water away from farmland.","zh":"工人可能開鑿運河，把水從農地引走。"},{"en":"If engineers cut large canals through wetlands, natural water flow may change.","zh":"如果工程師在濕地中開鑿大型運河，自然水流可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes constructing man-made waterways.","zh":"這個片語描述建造人工水道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take most of the water away","meaning":"把大部分水引走","examples":[{"en":"The canals took most of the water away from the bay.","zh":"這些運河把大部分水從海灣引走。"},{"en":"To take most of the water away means to divert or remove a large part of the water supply.","zh":"take most of the water away 指把大部分水供應改道或移走。"},{"en":"A broken pipe may take most of the water away from a garden pond.","zh":"破裂水管可能把花園池塘的大部分水引走。"},{"en":"If canals remove too much water, wetlands can dry out and become saltier.","zh":"如果運河移走太多水，濕地可能乾涸並變得更鹹。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major reduction in water reaching a place.","zh":"這個片語描述到達某地的水大幅減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be more like an estuary","meaning":"更像河口","examples":[{"en":"Kruczynski suspects that the original bay was more like an estuary.","zh":"Kruczynski 懷疑原本的海灣更像河口。"},{"en":"To be more like an estuary means to have conditions similar to a river mouth where fresh water mixes with seawater.","zh":"be more like an estuary 指具有類似河口的條件，即淡水與海水混合。"},{"en":"A coastal lake may be more like an estuary if river water enters it daily.","zh":"如果河水每天流入，沿海湖泊可能更像河口。"},{"en":"If the bay was naturally mixed and changeable, restoring only clear seawater may be unrealistic.","zh":"如果海灣本來就是混合而變動的，只恢復清澈海水可能不現實。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a place with an estuary-like environment.","zh":"這個片語把某地與河口式環境比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"estuary","meaning":"河口","examples":[{"en":"An estuary contains a mixture of fresh water and seawater.","zh":"河口含有淡水和海水的混合物。"},{"en":"An estuary is the area where a river meets the sea.","zh":"estuary 是河流與海洋相遇的地方。"},{"en":"Birds and young fish often use an estuary because food is plentiful there.","zh":"鳥類和幼魚常使用河口，因為那裡食物充足。"},{"en":"If an estuary receives too much pollution from upstream, coastal waters may suffer.","zh":"如果河口從上游接收太多污染，沿海水域可能受害。"},{"en":"This word describes a mixed freshwater-and-saltwater habitat.","zh":"這個詞描述淡水與鹹水混合的棲息地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"wish to re-create","meaning":"希望重現……","examples":[{"en":"Many people wish to re-create a particular version of the bay.","zh":"許多人希望重現該海灣的某個特定版本。"},{"en":"To wish to re-create something means to want to bring back or copy an earlier form of it.","zh":"wish to re-create something 指希望恢復或複製某物較早的形式。"},{"en":"A school may wish to re-create an old reading corner that students loved.","zh":"學校可能希望重現學生喜愛的舊閱讀角。"},{"en":"If people re-create the wrong version of nature, restoration may not match reality.","zh":"如果人們重現錯誤版本的自然，修復可能不符合現實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a desire to rebuild or reproduce something from the past.","zh":"這個片語描述希望重建或再現過去的某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a changing phase in","meaning":"……中一個變動階段","examples":[{"en":"The clear-water bay may have been only a changing phase in its history.","zh":"清澈水域的海灣可能只是其歷史中一個變動階段。"},{"en":"A changing phase in something is one temporary stage in a longer process.","zh":"changing phase in something 指較長過程中的一個暫時階段。"},{"en":"Teenage rebellion may be a changing phase in a child’s development.","zh":"青少年反叛可能是孩子發展中的一個變動階段。"},{"en":"If clear water was only one phase, it may not represent the bay’s permanent natural state.","zh":"如果清澈水域只是其中一個階段，它未必代表海灣永久自然狀態。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a stage that changes over time.","zh":"這個片語描述會隨時間改變的階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"do not merely…but…as well","meaning":"不僅……也……","examples":[{"en":"The arguments do not merely involve ecological risks but economic ones as well.","zh":"這些爭論不僅涉及生態風險，也涉及經濟風險。"},{"en":"Do not merely A but B as well means not only A, but also B.","zh":"do not merely A but B as well 指不只是 A，也包括 B。"},{"en":"The problem does not merely affect students’ marks but their confidence as well.","zh":"這個問題不僅影響學生分數，也影響他們的信心。"},{"en":"If a plan affects both nature and income, debate becomes more serious.","zh":"如果計劃同時影響自然和收入，爭議會變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"This structure adds a second important point.","zh":"這個結構加入第二個重要點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"threaten to create","meaning":"可能造成……","examples":[{"en":"The restoration plan may threaten to create economic problems.","zh":"修復計劃可能造成經濟問題。"},{"en":"To threaten to create something means to risk causing a serious problem.","zh":"threaten to create something 指有造成嚴重問題的風險。"},{"en":"A new road closure may threaten to create traffic jams near schools.","zh":"新道路封閉可能造成學校附近交通擠塞。"},{"en":"If a restoration plan harms tourism, it may create economic trouble.","zh":"如果修復計劃損害旅遊業，它可能造成經濟麻煩。"},{"en":"This phrase warns about a possible negative result.","zh":"這個片語警告可能出現負面結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"economic problems as well","meaning":"也造成經濟問題","examples":[{"en":"The dispute could create economic problems as well.","zh":"這場爭議也可能造成經濟問題。"},{"en":"Economic problems as well means financial or business difficulties in addition to other problems.","zh":"economic problems as well 指除了其他問題外，還有財政或商業困難。"},{"en":"A flood can cause health problems and economic problems as well.","zh":"水災可以造成健康問題，也造成經濟問題。"},{"en":"If coral reefs decline, tourism businesses may lose customers.","zh":"如果珊瑚礁衰退，旅遊企業可能失去顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase adds money-related consequences to the discussion.","zh":"這個片語把金錢相關後果加入討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"depend on tourism","meaning":"依賴旅遊業","examples":[{"en":"The economy of the Florida Keys depends heavily on tourism.","zh":"佛羅里達礁島群的經濟高度依賴旅遊業。"},{"en":"To depend on tourism means to rely on visitors’ spending for jobs and income.","zh":"depend on tourism 指依靠遊客消費提供工作和收入。"},{"en":"A small island may depend on tourism if most shops serve visitors.","zh":"如果大多數商店服務遊客，小島可能依賴旅遊業。"},{"en":"If tourists stop coming, hotels, restaurants, and boat operators may suffer.","zh":"如果遊客停止到訪，酒店、餐廳和船隻營運者可能受苦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes economic reliance on visitors.","zh":"這個片語描述經濟上依靠遊客。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"local tourist industry","meaning":"本地旅遊業","examples":[{"en":"The local tourist industry earns billions of dollars each year.","zh":"本地旅遊業每年賺取數十億美元。"},{"en":"The local tourist industry includes businesses that serve visitors in an area.","zh":"local tourist industry 包括某地區服務遊客的企業。"},{"en":"Hotels, restaurants, tour guides, boat trips, and souvenir shops are part of the local tourist industry.","zh":"酒店、餐廳、導遊、船遊和紀念品店都是本地旅遊業的一部分。"},{"en":"If pollution damages natural attractions, the tourist industry may lose income.","zh":"如果污染破壞自然景點，旅遊業可能失去收入。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to tourism businesses in a particular place.","zh":"這個片語指特定地方的旅遊企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"annual turnover","meaning":"年營業額","examples":[{"en":"The tourist industry has an annual turnover of $2.5 billion.","zh":"該旅遊業年營業額達25億美元。"},{"en":"Annual turnover is the total amount of money a business or industry receives in one year.","zh":"annual turnover 是企業或行業一年內收到的總金額。"},{"en":"A small café may have an annual turnover of one million dollars.","zh":"小咖啡店年營業額可能有一百萬美元。"},{"en":"If an industry has high annual turnover, damage to it can affect many workers.","zh":"如果某行業年營業額很高，對它的破壞會影響許多工人。"},{"en":"This phrase measures yearly business income.","zh":"這個片語量度年度商業收入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"fishing-boat trips","meaning":"乘船釣魚活動","examples":[{"en":"Visitors come to the area for fishing-boat trips.","zh":"遊客來到該區參加乘船釣魚活動。"},{"en":"Fishing-boat trips are tourist or leisure journeys by boat to catch fish.","zh":"fishing-boat trips 是乘船出海捕魚的旅遊或休閒行程。"},{"en":"A family may book a fishing-boat trip during a seaside holiday.","zh":"家庭可能在海邊假期預訂乘船釣魚活動。"},{"en":"If fish numbers decline, fishing-boat trips may become less attractive.","zh":"如果魚類數量下降，乘船釣魚活動可能變得較不吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a tourism activity linked to fishing.","zh":"這個片語描述與釣魚相關的旅遊活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"manatee watching","meaning":"觀賞海牛","examples":[{"en":"Manatee watching attracts tourists to the Florida Keys.","zh":"觀賞海牛吸引遊客到佛羅里達礁島群。"},{"en":"Manatee watching is the activity of observing manatees in their natural habitat.","zh":"manatee watching 是在海牛自然棲息地觀察海牛的活動。"},{"en":"Tourists may join a quiet boat tour for manatee watching.","zh":"遊客可能參加安靜的船遊來觀賞海牛。"},{"en":"If water pollution harms manatees, this tourist activity may decline.","zh":"如果水污染傷害海牛，這項旅遊活動可能衰退。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wildlife-based tourism.","zh":"這個片語描述以野生動物為基礎的旅遊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"scuba diving and snorkelling","meaning":"水肺潛水及浮潛","examples":[{"en":"Visitors enjoy scuba diving and snorkelling around the reefs.","zh":"遊客喜歡在珊瑚礁周圍水肺潛水及浮潛。"},{"en":"Scuba diving and snorkelling are activities that allow people to explore underwater life.","zh":"scuba diving and snorkelling 是讓人探索水下生命的活動。"},{"en":"Beginners may start with snorkelling before trying scuba diving.","zh":"初學者可能先嘗試浮潛，再試水肺潛水。"},{"en":"If reefs lose colour and fish, diving tourism may decline.","zh":"如果珊瑚礁失去色彩和魚類，潛水旅遊可能衰退。"},{"en":"This phrase describes popular marine recreation.","zh":"這個片語描述受歡迎的海洋休閒活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"exotically coloured corals","meaning":"色彩奇異的珊瑚","examples":[{"en":"Tourists come to view the exotically coloured corals.","zh":"遊客前來觀看色彩奇異的珊瑚。"},{"en":"Exotically coloured corals are corals with unusual, bright, or striking colours.","zh":"exotically coloured corals 是顏色不尋常、鮮艷或奪目的珊瑚。"},{"en":"A diver may photograph exotically coloured corals during a reef tour.","zh":"潛水者可能在珊瑚礁旅程中拍攝色彩奇異的珊瑚。"},{"en":"If pollution kills colourful corals, reefs become less attractive to visitors.","zh":"如果污染殺死色彩繽紛的珊瑚，珊瑚礁對遊客會較不吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visually impressive coral.","zh":"這個片語描述視覺上令人印象深刻的珊瑚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make the problems worse","meaning":"令問題惡化","examples":[{"en":"The restoration plan could make the problems in the bay worse.","zh":"修復計劃可能令海灣問題惡化。"},{"en":"To make the problems worse means to increase the harm or difficulty already present.","zh":"make the problems worse 指增加已存在的傷害或困難。"},{"en":"Giving more homework to exhausted students may make the problem worse.","zh":"給疲憊學生更多功課可能令問題惡化。"},{"en":"If a plan adds nutrients to polluted water, it may worsen the ecological damage.","zh":"如果計劃向受污染水體加入養分，可能加劇生態破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a solution may backfire.","zh":"這個片語警告解決方案可能適得其反。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"prove a very expensive mistake","meaning":"最終成為代價高昂的錯誤","examples":[{"en":"A failed restoration project could prove a very expensive mistake.","zh":"失敗的修復項目可能最終成為代價高昂的錯誤。"},{"en":"To prove a very expensive mistake means to turn out to be a costly failure.","zh":"prove a very expensive mistake 指最終變成花費巨大而失敗的錯誤。"},{"en":"Buying software that no one uses can prove a very expensive mistake for a school.","zh":"購買沒有人使用的軟件，對學校而言可能最終成為代價高昂的錯誤。"},{"en":"If a restoration project damages both ecology and tourism, the cost is not only financial.","zh":"如果修復項目同時損害生態和旅遊，代價就不只是金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decision that later looks wrong and costly.","zh":"這個片語描述日後看來錯誤且昂貴的決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"which paragraph contains","meaning":"哪一段包含……","examples":[{"en":"Candidates identify which paragraph contains the required information.","zh":"考生識別哪一段包含所需資料。"},{"en":"Which paragraph contains asks students to find the paragraph where certain information appears.","zh":"which paragraph contains 要求學生找出某資料出現在哪一段。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may scan for the paragraph that contains a date or example.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能掃讀找出包含日期或例子的段落。"},{"en":"If a question asks which paragraph contains an idea, the wording may not be exactly the same.","zh":"如果題目問哪一段包含某想法，用字未必完全相同。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in information-matching tasks.","zh":"這個片語常見於資訊配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"contain information about","meaning":"包含關於……的資料","examples":[{"en":"The paragraph contains information about changes in coral cover.","zh":"該段包含關於珊瑚覆蓋率變化的資料。"},{"en":"To contain information about something means to include details on that topic.","zh":"contain information about something 指包括關於某主題的細節。"},{"en":"A school notice may contain information about exam dates and room numbers.","zh":"學校通告可能包含關於考試日期和課室編號的資料。"},{"en":"If a paragraph contains information about coral decline, it may include statistics or examples.","zh":"如果段落包含關於珊瑚衰退的資料，它可能包括統計或例子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where relevant details are found.","zh":"這個片語描述相關細節在哪裡找到。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be more resistant to","meaning":"對……有更強抵抗力","examples":[{"en":"Seagrass may be more resistant to salinity than expected.","zh":"海草可能比預期對鹽度有更強抵抗力。"},{"en":"To be more resistant to something means to be better able to survive or withstand it.","zh":"be more resistant to something 指更能生存或承受某事。"},{"en":"Some phone cases are more resistant to water than ordinary cases.","zh":"有些手機殼比普通手機殼更防水。"},{"en":"If seagrass is resistant to salt, salinity may not explain its death.","zh":"如果海草耐鹽，鹽度可能不能解釋其死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stronger ability to endure a harmful condition.","zh":"這個片語描述更強承受有害條件的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"than expected","meaning":"比預期","examples":[{"en":"The plants may tolerate more salt than expected.","zh":"這些植物可能能承受比預期更多的鹽分。"},{"en":"Than expected means more, less, better, or worse than people thought would happen.","zh":"than expected 指比人們原先認為的更多、更少、更好或更差。"},{"en":"The test was easier than expected, so students finished early.","zh":"測驗比預期容易，所以學生提早完成。"},{"en":"If a plant survives better than expected, scientists may revise their theory.","zh":"如果植物比預期更能生存，科學家可能修正理論。"},{"en":"This phrase compares reality with prediction.","zh":"這個片語把現實與預測比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the importance of identifying","meaning":"找出……的重要性","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains the importance of identifying the cause of the problem.","zh":"文章解釋找出問題成因的重要性。"},{"en":"The importance of identifying something means why it matters to find or recognise it correctly.","zh":"importance of identifying something 指正確找出或識別某事為何重要。"},{"en":"Doctors know the importance of identifying the real cause of pain before treatment.","zh":"醫生明白在治療前找出痛楚真正原因的重要性。"},{"en":"If the wrong cause is identified, money may be spent on the wrong solution.","zh":"如果成因被錯誤識別，金錢可能花在錯誤解決方案上。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses why accurate diagnosis matters.","zh":"這個片語強調準確診斷為何重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"cause of the controversy","meaning":"爭議的成因","examples":[{"en":"Researchers disagree about the cause of the controversy.","zh":"研究人員對爭議的成因意見不一。"},{"en":"The cause of the controversy is the reason people are arguing about an issue.","zh":"cause of the controversy 是人們爭論某議題的原因。"},{"en":"The cause of a school controversy may be an unclear new rule.","zh":"學校爭議的成因可能是一條不清楚的新規則。"},{"en":"If scientists interpret evidence differently, disagreement can grow.","zh":"如果科學家對證據有不同詮釋，分歧可能擴大。"},{"en":"This phrase asks why a dispute began or continues.","zh":"這個片語詢問爭議為何開始或持續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"expensive proposals","meaning":"昂貴的建議方案","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes expensive proposals for removing nitrogen.","zh":"文章描述用於去除氮的昂貴建議方案。"},{"en":"Expensive proposals are suggested plans that would cost a lot of money.","zh":"expensive proposals 是成本很高的建議計劃。"},{"en":"Building a new sports hall and theatre would be an expensive proposal for a small school.","zh":"對小學校而言，建造新體育館和劇院會是昂貴建議方案。"},{"en":"If a proposal is expensive, decision-makers must ask whether it will truly work.","zh":"如果方案昂貴，決策者必須問它是否真正有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes costly suggested solutions.","zh":"這個片語描述成本高昂的建議解決方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"solve the nitrogen problem","meaning":"解決氮污染問題","examples":[{"en":"Several costly measures may be needed to solve the nitrogen problem.","zh":"可能需要幾項昂貴措施來解決氮污染問題。"},{"en":"To solve the nitrogen problem means to reduce excess nitrogen to a safe or acceptable level.","zh":"solve the nitrogen problem 指把過量氮減至安全或可接受水平。"},{"en":"A farm may solve a nitrogen problem by using less fertiliser and planting buffer strips.","zh":"農場可能透過減少施肥和種植緩衝草帶來解決氮污染問題。"},{"en":"If nitrogen is not reduced, algal blooms may continue.","zh":"如果氮沒有減少，藻華可能持續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fixing pollution caused by too much nitrogen.","zh":"這個片語描述處理過量氮造成的污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"statistics showing","meaning":"顯示……的統計數字","examples":[{"en":"The paragraph contains statistics showing a decline in coral health.","zh":"該段包含顯示珊瑚健康下降的統計數字。"},{"en":"Statistics showing something are numbers that demonstrate a pattern or change.","zh":"statistics showing something 是展示某模式或變化的數字。"},{"en":"A report may include statistics showing that fewer students walk to school.","zh":"報告可能包括顯示較少學生步行上學的統計數字。"},{"en":"If statistics show decline, the problem is measurable rather than just a feeling.","zh":"如果統計數字顯示下降，問題就是可量度的，而不只是感覺。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces numerical evidence.","zh":"這個片語引入數字證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"ecological changes","meaning":"生態變化","examples":[{"en":"The statistics show major ecological changes in the reef.","zh":"統計數字顯示珊瑚礁出現重大生態變化。"},{"en":"Ecological changes are changes in living things and their relationships with the environment.","zh":"ecological changes 是生物及其與環境關係上的變化。"},{"en":"Fewer birds and more insects in a park may show ecological changes.","zh":"公園中鳥類減少而昆蟲增加，可能顯示生態變化。"},{"en":"If coral species disappear, the reef ecosystem has changed deeply.","zh":"如果珊瑚物種消失，珊瑚礁生態系統已深刻改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changes in natural systems.","zh":"這個片語描述自然系統中的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"match the people with","meaning":"把人物與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match the people with their opinions or deeds.","zh":"考生把人物與他們的意見或行動配對。"},{"en":"To match the people with something means to connect each person to the correct idea, action, or statement.","zh":"match the people with something 指把每個人物連接到正確想法、行動或陳述。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may match scientists with the theories they support.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能把科學家與其支持的理論配對。"},{"en":"If names and opinions are similar, careful reading is needed.","zh":"如果姓名和意見相似，就需要仔細閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in matching questions.","zh":"這個片語常見於配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"opinions or deeds","meaning":"意見或行動","examples":[{"en":"The task compares the scientists’ opinions or deeds.","zh":"任務比較科學家的意見或行動。"},{"en":"Opinions or deeds means what people think or what they have done.","zh":"opinions or deeds 指人們的想法或他們做過的事。"},{"en":"A history question may ask students to match leaders with their opinions or deeds.","zh":"歷史題可能要求學生把領袖與其意見或行動配對。"},{"en":"If one scientist argues and another carries out research, both opinions and deeds matter.","zh":"如果一位科學家提出論點，另一位進行研究，意見和行動都重要。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both beliefs and actions.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋信念和行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"appropriate letters","meaning":"適當字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the appropriate letters in the answer boxes.","zh":"考生在答案框中寫上適當字母。"},{"en":"Appropriate letters are the correct letter choices that match the answers.","zh":"appropriate letters 是與答案相符的正確字母選項。"},{"en":"If the answer is scientist B, students must write the appropriate letter, not the full name.","zh":"如果答案是科學家 B，學生必須寫適當字母，而不是全名。"},{"en":"Writing the wrong letter can lose marks even if the idea is understood.","zh":"即使理解意思，寫錯字母也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds students to follow the test format.","zh":"這個片語提醒學生遵守考試格式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"drainage system","meaning":"排水系統","examples":[{"en":"The Everglades drainage system reduced freshwater flow.","zh":"大沼澤地排水系統減少了淡水流量。"},{"en":"A drainage system is a network of canals, pipes, or channels that removes water from land.","zh":"drainage system 是由運河、管道或渠道組成、把水從土地排走的網絡。"},{"en":"A school needs a drainage system to stop the playground from flooding.","zh":"學校需要排水系統，以防操場水浸。"},{"en":"If a drainage system removes too much water, wetlands may dry out.","zh":"如果排水系統移走太多水，濕地可能乾涸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes infrastructure for moving water away.","zh":"這個片語描述把水移走的基建。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"increase the bay’s salinity","meaning":"提高海灣鹽度","examples":[{"en":"Reduced freshwater flow may increase the bay’s salinity.","zh":"淡水流量減少可能提高海灣鹽度。"},{"en":"To increase the bay’s salinity means to make the bay’s water saltier.","zh":"increase the bay’s salinity 指令海灣水變得更鹹。"},{"en":"If less rain enters a pond near the sea, its salinity may rise.","zh":"如果較少雨水進入海邊池塘，其鹽度可能上升。"},{"en":"Higher salinity can affect plants and animals that need a certain salt balance.","zh":"較高鹽度會影響需要特定鹽分平衡的植物和動物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rise in salt content.","zh":"這個片語描述含鹽量上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"restore water with high nitrogen levels","meaning":"恢復含高氮量的水流","examples":[{"en":"Restoring water with high nitrogen levels may damage the reef.","zh":"恢復含高氮量的水流可能破壞珊瑚礁。"},{"en":"To restore water with high nitrogen levels means to bring back water flow that contains a lot of nitrogen.","zh":"restore water with high nitrogen levels 指恢復含有大量氮的水流。"},{"en":"A city should not restore river flow if the water is still full of pollutants.","zh":"如果水仍充滿污染物，城市不應恢復河流流量。"},{"en":"If restored water carries nitrogen, it may feed algae instead of helping the ecosystem.","zh":"如果恢復的水流帶有氮，它可能餵養藻類，而不是幫助生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that restored flow may also carry pollution.","zh":"這個片語警告恢復水流也可能帶來污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"further ecological damage","meaning":"進一步生態破壞","examples":[{"en":"Nitrogen-rich water could cause further ecological damage.","zh":"富含氮的水可能造成進一步生態破壞。"},{"en":"Further ecological damage means additional harm to plants, animals, and natural systems.","zh":"further ecological damage 指對植物、動物和自然系統造成額外傷害。"},{"en":"Cutting more trees after a landslide may cause further ecological damage.","zh":"山泥傾瀉後再砍更多樹，可能造成進一步生態破壞。"},{"en":"If polluted water enters a fragile reef, the damage may continue or worsen.","zh":"如果受污染水進入脆弱珊瑚礁，破壞可能繼續或惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extra harm after damage has already begun.","zh":"這個片語描述破壞已開始後的額外傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be caused by nearby farmland","meaning":"由附近農地造成","examples":[{"en":"High nitrogen levels may be caused by nearby farmland.","zh":"高氮含量可能由附近農地造成。"},{"en":"To be caused by nearby farmland means to result from farming activity close to the affected area.","zh":"be caused by nearby farmland 指由受影響地區附近的農業活動造成。"},{"en":"A river’s muddy water may be caused by nearby farmland after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，河水混濁可能由附近農地造成。"},{"en":"If fertiliser washes from fields into water, farmland can become a pollution source.","zh":"如果肥料從田地沖入水中，農地就可能成為污染來源。"},{"en":"This phrase links an environmental problem to local agriculture.","zh":"這個片語把環境問題與本地農業連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"One scientist blames sewage discharges rather than farmland nutrients.","zh":"一位科學家責怪污水排放，而不是農地養分。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of, and it clearly contrasts two possible causes or choices.","zh":"rather than 指「而不是」，清楚對比兩個可能原因或選擇。"},{"en":"A student may need sleep rather than another cup of coffee.","zh":"學生可能需要睡眠，而不是再喝一杯咖啡。"},{"en":"If sewage is the problem rather than farmland, the solution must target waste systems.","zh":"如果問題是污水而不是農地，解決方案就必須針對廢水系統。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate the real cause from another possible cause.","zh":"這個片語幫助把真正原因與另一個可能原因分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"increase nitrogen levels","meaning":"提高氮含量","examples":[{"en":"Sewage discharges may increase nitrogen levels in the bay.","zh":"污水排放可能提高海灣中的氮含量。"},{"en":"To increase nitrogen levels means to raise the amount of nitrogen compounds present.","zh":"increase nitrogen levels 指提高氮化合物的含量。"},{"en":"Adding too much fertiliser can increase nitrogen levels in soil.","zh":"加入太多肥料可以提高土壤氮含量。"},{"en":"If nitrogen levels rise in water, algae may grow rapidly.","zh":"如果水中氮含量上升，藻類可能快速生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding or raising a nutrient concentration.","zh":"這個片語描述增加或提高養分濃度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所提供資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether each statement agrees with the information given.","zh":"考生判斷每項陳述是否與所提供資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指符合文章所說內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says coral cover fell, a statement saying it declined agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說珊瑚覆蓋率下降，陳述說它減少就是與資料一致。"},{"en":"If a statement changes the meaning, it does not agree even if some words look similar.","zh":"如果陳述改變意思，即使某些字眼看似相似，也不一致。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in TRUE, FALSE, and NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個片語用於 TRUE、FALSE 和 NOT GIVEN 題型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement is false if it contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"如果陳述與文章資料相矛盾，就是錯誤。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文本相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the text says the project is controversial, saying everyone agrees contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文本說該項目有爭議，說所有人都同意就是與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should mark a statement false when it directly conflicts with the passage.","zh":"當陳述與文章直接衝突時，學生應標示為錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clear disagreement with the text.","zh":"這個片語描述與文本明確不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write NOT GIVEN if there is no information on the statement.","zh":"如果文中沒有關於該陳述的資料，考生寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not say enough to decide whether it is true or false.","zh":"no information on this 指文章沒有提供足夠資料判斷真假。"},{"en":"If an article never mentions cost, there is no information on whether the project is cheap.","zh":"如果文章從未提及成本，就沒有資料判斷項目是否便宜。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when the passage gives no evidence.","zh":"當文章沒有證據時，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase explains when to choose NOT GIVEN.","zh":"這個片語解釋何時選擇 NOT GIVEN。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"everyone agrees that","meaning":"所有人都同意……","examples":[{"en":"The statement claims that everyone agrees the action is harmless.","zh":"該陳述聲稱所有人都同意該行動無害。"},{"en":"Everyone agrees that means all people share the same opinion.","zh":"everyone agrees that 指所有人都有相同意見。"},{"en":"Everyone agrees that students need clear instructions before an exam.","zh":"所有人都同意學生考試前需要清楚指示。"},{"en":"If scientists are divided, it is wrong to say everyone agrees.","zh":"如果科學家意見分歧，說所有人都同意就是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete agreement, so it should be used carefully.","zh":"這個片語描述完全一致，因此應謹慎使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"flow off different types of crops","meaning":"從不同農作物田地流出","examples":[{"en":"Nitrogen can enter the bay in water flowing off crops.","zh":"氮可以透過從農作物田地流出的水進入海灣。"},{"en":"To flow off different types of crops means for water to run away from various farm fields.","zh":"flow off different types of crops 指水從不同農田流走。"},{"en":"Rainwater may flow off vegetable crops, fruit fields, and grassland after a storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，雨水可能從菜田、果園和草地流出。"},{"en":"If the water carries fertiliser, different crops can all contribute to nutrient pollution.","zh":"如果水帶有肥料，不同農作物都可能造成養分污染。"},{"en":"This phrase describes runoff from agricultural land.","zh":"這個片語描述來自農地的徑流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"regardless of","meaning":"不論；不管","examples":[{"en":"The project may not succeed regardless of the pollution’s cause.","zh":"不論污染成因為何，該項目都可能不會成功。"},{"en":"Regardless of means without being affected by a particular factor.","zh":"regardless of 指不受某特定因素影響。"},{"en":"Students must arrive on time regardless of the weather.","zh":"不論天氣如何，學生都必須準時到達。"},{"en":"If a plan fails regardless of the cause, deeper design problems may exist.","zh":"如果計劃不論原因為何都會失敗，可能存在更深層設計問題。"},{"en":"This phrase means the result stays the same despite different conditions.","zh":"這個片語表示即使條件不同，結果仍相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be effective regardless of","meaning":"無論……也能有效","examples":[{"en":"The restoration project cannot be effective regardless of the cause.","zh":"修復項目不能無論成因如何都有效。"},{"en":"To be effective regardless of something means to work well no matter what that factor is.","zh":"be effective regardless of something 指不管某因素如何都能有效運作。"},{"en":"A good study plan should be effective regardless of whether the test is easy or difficult.","zh":"好溫習計劃應無論測驗容易或困難都有效。"},{"en":"If a pollution solution works only for one cause, it is not effective regardless of cause.","zh":"如果污染解決方案只針對一種成因有效，它就不是無論成因如何都有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes success under different conditions.","zh":"這個片語描述在不同條件下都成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"no one can recall","meaning":"沒有人記得","examples":[{"en":"No one can recall exactly what the bay was like before the 1950s.","zh":"沒有人記得1950年代前該海灣究竟是怎樣。"},{"en":"No one can recall means nobody can remember clearly.","zh":"no one can recall 指沒有人能清楚記得。"},{"en":"No one can recall who first suggested the school tradition.","zh":"沒有人記得是誰最先提出學校傳統。"},{"en":"If no one can remember the original condition, restoration goals become uncertain.","zh":"如果沒有人記得原本狀態，修復目標就變得不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lack of reliable memory.","zh":"這個片語描述缺乏可靠記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"make a fundamental contribution to","meaning":"對……作出重要貢獻","examples":[{"en":"Tourism makes a fundamental contribution to the local economy.","zh":"旅遊業對本地經濟作出重要貢獻。"},{"en":"To make a fundamental contribution to something means to play a basic and very important role in supporting it.","zh":"make a fundamental contribution to something 指在支持某事方面發揮基本而非常重要的作用。"},{"en":"Teachers make a fundamental contribution to children’s development.","zh":"老師對兒童發展作出重要貢獻。"},{"en":"If tourism supports many jobs, losing visitors can hurt the whole area.","zh":"如果旅遊業支持許多工作，失去遊客會傷害整個地區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an essential contribution.","zh":"這個片語描述不可或缺的貢獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the economy of the area","meaning":"該區經濟","examples":[{"en":"Tourism is essential to the economy of the Florida Keys area.","zh":"旅遊業對佛羅里達礁島群該區經濟至關重要。"},{"en":"The economy of the area means the jobs, businesses, income, and spending in that place.","zh":"economy of the area 指某地方的工作、企業、收入和消費。"},{"en":"A factory closure can damage the economy of a small town.","zh":"工廠關閉可以損害小鎮經濟。"},{"en":"If reefs attract tourists, their health becomes important to the area’s economy.","zh":"如果珊瑚礁吸引遊客，其健康就對該區經濟重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the financial life of a region.","zh":"這個片語描述一個地區的財政生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 145 - Pollution! In the Bay.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 146":[{"front":"find our way","meaning":"尋找方向；找到路","examples":[{"en":"Humans use several methods to find their way through unfamiliar places.","zh":"人類使用幾種方法在陌生地方尋找方向。"},{"en":"To find our way means to discover the correct route or direction to a place.","zh":"find our way 指找出前往某地的正確路線或方向。"},{"en":"A student may use signs in a new school building to find her way to the library.","zh":"學生在新校舍中可能利用指示牌找到去圖書館的路。"},{"en":"If people cannot find their way, they may waste time, feel anxious, or arrive late.","zh":"如果人們找不到路，可能會浪費時間、感到焦慮或遲到。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when someone is trying to move through a place successfully.","zh":"這個短語用於某人嘗試成功穿過某地方時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"follow the directions","meaning":"按照指示","examples":[{"en":"You can follow the directions given by the car’s computer.","zh":"你可以按照汽車電腦給出的指示。"},{"en":"To follow the directions means to do what the instructions tell you to do.","zh":"follow the directions 指按照指示所說去做。"},{"en":"A visitor can follow the directions on a hospital sign to reach the correct ward.","zh":"訪客可以按照醫院指示牌到達正確病房。"},{"en":"If you ignore the directions, you may turn into the wrong street or miss the building.","zh":"如果你忽視指示，可能會轉入錯誤街道或錯過大樓。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses obeying a route or set of instructions step by step.","zh":"這個短語強調一步一步遵從路線或指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"reach your destination","meaning":"到達目的地","examples":[{"en":"The navigation system helps you reach your destination without error.","zh":"導航系統幫助你準確無誤地到達目的地。"},{"en":"To reach your destination means to arrive at the place you intended to go.","zh":"reach your destination 指到達你原本打算前往的地方。"},{"en":"A bus app can help students reach their destination by showing where to get off.","zh":"巴士應用程式可以透過顯示在哪裏下車，幫助學生到達目的地。"},{"en":"Clear signs reduce confusion and help travellers arrive at the right place.","zh":"清楚標誌減少混亂，並幫助旅客到達正確地方。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the successful end point of a journey.","zh":"這個短語重點在旅程成功的終點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"without error","meaning":"準確無誤地","examples":[{"en":"The driver reached the destination without error.","zh":"司機準確無誤地到達目的地。"},{"en":"Without error means with no mistake or incorrect step.","zh":"without error 指沒有任何錯誤或不正確步驟。"},{"en":"A student fills in an answer sheet without error when every answer is written in the right box.","zh":"當每個答案都寫在正確格子中，學生就是準確無誤地填寫答題紙。"},{"en":"Careful checking helps people complete important tasks without error.","zh":"仔細檢查幫助人準確無誤地完成重要任務。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses accuracy and correctness.","zh":"這個短語強調準確和正確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Global Positioning System","meaning":"全球定位系統","examples":[{"en":"The Global Positioning System can guide drivers through unfamiliar areas.","zh":"全球定位系統可以引導司機穿過陌生地區。"},{"en":"The Global Positioning System is a satellite-based system that helps people know their location.","zh":"Global Positioning System 是以衞星為基礎、幫助人知道自己位置的系統。"},{"en":"A delivery driver may use the Global Positioning System to find a customer’s building.","zh":"送貨司機可能使用全球定位系統尋找顧客的大樓。"},{"en":"If GPS data is wrong, the driver may be guided to the wrong road.","zh":"如果 GPS 資料錯誤，司機可能被引導到錯誤道路。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the technology commonly called GPS.","zh":"這個短語指通常稱為 GPS 的科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"direct someone to","meaning":"引導某人前往……","examples":[{"en":"GPS can direct you to within a few yards of your goal.","zh":"GPS 可以引導你到距離目標只有幾碼的位置。"},{"en":"To direct someone to a place means to guide them towards that place.","zh":"direct someone to 某地，指引導某人前往該地方。"},{"en":"A receptionist can direct visitors to the meeting room on the third floor.","zh":"接待員可以引導訪客前往三樓會議室。"},{"en":"Good directions prevent people from wandering around and asking several times.","zh":"良好指示可以防止人四處亂走和反覆詢問。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when someone or something gives route guidance.","zh":"這個短語用於某人或某物提供路線引導時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"within a few yards of","meaning":"距離……只有幾碼","examples":[{"en":"The system can guide you to within a few yards of the building.","zh":"該系統可以引導你到距離大樓只有幾碼的位置。"},{"en":"Within a few yards of something means very close to it, only a short distance away.","zh":"within a few yards of 某物，指非常接近它，只相隔很短距離。"},{"en":"A taxi may drop a passenger within a few yards of the school gate.","zh":"的士可能把乘客放下在距離校門只有幾碼的位置。"},{"en":"Being this close usually makes it easy to see the final destination.","zh":"距離這麼近通常容易看見最終目的地。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate but very short distance.","zh":"這個短語給出大約但非常短的距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"satellite service","meaning":"衞星服務","examples":[{"en":"The satellite service depends on accurate digital maps.","zh":"衞星服務依賴準確的電子地圖。"},{"en":"A satellite service is a system that uses satellites to provide information or communication.","zh":"satellite service 是使用衞星提供資訊或通訊的系統。"},{"en":"Weather apps may use a satellite service to show storms moving across a region.","zh":"天氣應用程式可能使用衞星服務顯示風暴如何穿過地區。"},{"en":"If the satellite signal is weak, navigation information may become less reliable.","zh":"如果衞星訊號弱，導航資訊可能變得較不可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes support provided from satellites above Earth.","zh":"這個短語描述由地球上空衞星提供的支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"digital maps","meaning":"電子地圖","examples":[{"en":"GPS devices use digital maps to calculate routes.","zh":"GPS 裝置使用電子地圖計算路線。"},{"en":"Digital maps are electronic maps stored and displayed on phones, computers, or navigation devices.","zh":"digital maps 是儲存在手機、電腦或導航裝置並顯示出來的電子地圖。"},{"en":"A student can use digital maps to check how long it takes to walk to a new café.","zh":"學生可以使用電子地圖查看步行到新咖啡店需時多久。"},{"en":"Digital maps must be updated when new roads, buildings, or exits appear.","zh":"當新道路、大樓或出口出現，電子地圖必須更新。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to map information in electronic form.","zh":"這個短語指電子形式的地圖資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"become slightly outdated","meaning":"變得稍為過時","examples":[{"en":"Digital maps can become slightly outdated as roads change.","zh":"隨着道路改變，電子地圖可能變得稍為過時。"},{"en":"To become slightly outdated means to become a little old or no longer fully accurate.","zh":"become slightly outdated 指變得有點舊或不再完全準確。"},{"en":"A school website may become slightly outdated if it still shows last year’s timetable.","zh":"如果學校網站仍顯示去年的時間表，它可能變得稍為過時。"},{"en":"Even a small change can confuse users if the information is not updated.","zh":"如果資訊沒有更新，即使小改動也可以令使用者困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a minor but real loss of accuracy.","zh":"這個短語暗示輕微但真實的準確性下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"become lost","meaning":"迷路","examples":[{"en":"A driver may become lost if the map is inaccurate.","zh":"如果地圖不準確，司機可能迷路。"},{"en":"To become lost means to no longer know where you are or which way to go.","zh":"become lost 指不再知道自己在哪裏或應往哪個方向走。"},{"en":"A child may become lost in a large shopping mall if she walks away from her parents.","zh":"如果孩子在大型商場離開父母，她可能迷路。"},{"en":"Poor signs, wrong maps, or unfamiliar streets can cause people to lose their way.","zh":"差劣標誌、錯誤地圖或陌生街道都可以令人迷路。"},{"en":"The phrase describes confusion about location or direction.","zh":"這個短語描述對位置或方向感到困惑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rely on","meaning":"依靠……","examples":[{"en":"Without GPS, people must rely on their natural navigation skills.","zh":"沒有 GPS，人們必須依靠自然導航技能。"},{"en":"To rely on something means to depend on it for help or success.","zh":"rely on 某物，指依靠它來獲得幫助或成功。"},{"en":"A student may rely on a timetable to know when each lesson begins.","zh":"學生可能依靠時間表知道每堂課何時開始。"},{"en":"If people rely on only one tool, they may struggle when that tool fails.","zh":"如果人們只依靠一種工具，當該工具失效時可能會吃力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dependence on a person, skill, or resource.","zh":"這個短語描述對人、技能或資源的依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ancient human skill","meaning":"古老的人類技能","examples":[{"en":"Navigating through physical space is an ancient human skill.","zh":"在實體空間中辨認方向是一項古老的人類技能。"},{"en":"An ancient human skill is an ability people have used since very early human history.","zh":"ancient human skill 是人類自很早歷史以來一直使用的能力。"},{"en":"Finding food, returning home, and recognising safe paths were ancient human skills.","zh":"尋找食物、回家和辨認安全路線都是古老的人類技能。"},{"en":"Such skills developed because survival depended on movement through the environment.","zh":"這些技能之所以發展，是因為生存取決於在環境中移動。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a modern ability with very old human experience.","zh":"這個短語把現代能力與非常古老的人類經驗連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"navigate in three-dimensional space","meaning":"在三維空間中辨認方向","examples":[{"en":"Humans can navigate in three-dimensional space without electronic devices.","zh":"人類不用電子裝置也能在三維空間中辨認方向。"},{"en":"To navigate in three-dimensional space means to find one’s way through places with height, depth, distance, and direction.","zh":"navigate in three-dimensional space 指在有高度、深度、距離和方向的地方找到路。"},{"en":"A student navigates in three-dimensional space when she moves through staircases, corridors, and floors in a new building.","zh":"學生在新大樓中穿過樓梯、走廊和樓層時，就是在三維空間中辨認方向。"},{"en":"This skill helps people avoid obstacles and understand where objects are around them.","zh":"這項技能幫助人避開障礙物，並理解周圍物件的位置。"},{"en":"The phrase describes real-world movement, not flat map reading only.","zh":"這個短語描述真實世界中的移動，而不只是讀平面地圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"biological positioning system","meaning":"生物定位系統","examples":[{"en":"The human brain contains a flexible biological positioning system.","zh":"人腦包含一個靈活的生物定位系統。"},{"en":"A biological positioning system is the body’s natural way of working out where it is and where it is going.","zh":"biological positioning system 是身體自然判斷自己在哪裏和正往哪裏去的方法。"},{"en":"A child uses this system when she remembers how to walk from the classroom to the playground.","zh":"孩子記得如何由課室走到操場時，就在使用這個系統。"},{"en":"Because the system learns from experience, familiar places become easier to navigate.","zh":"因為這個系統能從經驗中學習，熟悉地方會較容易辨認方向。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the brain’s navigation ability with technological positioning systems.","zh":"這個短語把大腦的導航能力與科技定位系統作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have an important advantage over","meaning":"相比……具有重要優勢","examples":[{"en":"Human navigation has an important advantage over GPS.","zh":"人類導航相比 GPS 具有重要優勢。"},{"en":"To have an important advantage over something means to be better than it in a significant way.","zh":"have an important advantage over 某物，指在重要方面比它更好。"},{"en":"A paper notebook has an important advantage over a phone when the battery is dead.","zh":"當手機沒電時，紙本筆記相比手機具有重要優勢。"},{"en":"If one method still works when another fails, that advantage becomes clear.","zh":"如果一種方法在另一種失效時仍然有效，其優勢就變得清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to compare strengths between two things.","zh":"這個短語用於比較兩者之間的強項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"go awry","meaning":"出錯；偏離正軌","examples":[{"en":"The whole system does not go awry when one source of information fails.","zh":"當一個資訊來源失效，整個系統不會出錯。"},{"en":"To go awry means to go wrong or stop working as planned.","zh":"go awry 指出錯或不再按計劃運作。"},{"en":"A school trip can go awry if the bus arrives late and the museum booking is missed.","zh":"如果巴士遲到而錯過博物館預約，學校旅行可能出錯。"},{"en":"If a plan depends on only one piece of information, one mistake can make everything go wrong.","zh":"如果計劃只依賴一項資訊，一個錯誤就可以令一切出問題。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that something has moved away from the intended path.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事偏離原本路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"guidance system","meaning":"導航系統","examples":[{"en":"The human guidance system processes information in several ways.","zh":"人類導航系統以幾種方式處理資訊。"},{"en":"A guidance system is a method or set of processes that helps someone move in the right direction.","zh":"guidance system 是幫助某人朝正確方向移動的方法或一組程序。"},{"en":"Airport signs form a guidance system that helps passengers find gates and exits.","zh":"機場標誌形成導航系統，幫助乘客找到登機閘口和出口。"},{"en":"A good guidance system reduces confusion by giving clear cues at important points.","zh":"良好導航系統透過在重要位置提供清楚線索來減少混亂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes support for direction and movement.","zh":"這個短語描述對方向和移動的支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"work in various ways","meaning":"以多種方式運作","examples":[{"en":"Biological navigation works in various ways.","zh":"生物導航以多種方式運作。"},{"en":"To work in various ways means to operate through several different methods.","zh":"work in various ways 指透過幾種不同方法運作。"},{"en":"Students learn vocabulary in various ways, such as reading, speaking, and using flashcards.","zh":"學生以多種方式學詞彙，例如閱讀、說話和使用詞卡。"},{"en":"If one method fails, having other methods can make the whole system more reliable.","zh":"如果一種方法失敗，擁有其他方法可以令整個系統更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses variety in how something functions.","zh":"這個短語強調某事如何運作的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ask questions of","meaning":"向……詢問","examples":[{"en":"You can ask questions of people on the pavement.","zh":"你可以向行人路上的人詢問。"},{"en":"To ask questions of someone means to ask that person for information or help.","zh":"ask questions of 某人，指向該人詢問資訊或求助。"},{"en":"A tourist may ask questions of station staff when she cannot find the correct platform.","zh":"當旅客找不到正確月台，可能向車站職員詢問。"},{"en":"Asking questions can save time when signs or maps are unclear.","zh":"當標誌或地圖不清楚，提問可以節省時間。"},{"en":"The phrase is slightly formal and means asking people directly.","zh":"這個短語稍正式，意思是直接向人發問。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"look familiar","meaning":"看起來熟悉","examples":[{"en":"You may follow a street that looks familiar.","zh":"你可能沿着一條看起來熟悉的街道走。"},{"en":"To look familiar means to seem like something you have seen or experienced before.","zh":"look familiar 指看起來像你以前見過或經歷過的東西。"},{"en":"A shopfront may look familiar because you passed it earlier in the day.","zh":"店舖門面可能看起來熟悉，因為你當天較早時經過它。"},{"en":"Familiar sights help people feel more confident about where they are.","zh":"熟悉景象幫助人對自己所在位置更有信心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recognition based on memory.","zh":"這個短語描述基於記憶的辨認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"navigational rubric","meaning":"導航準則","examples":[{"en":"A navigational rubric can help someone maintain a general direction.","zh":"導航準則可以幫助某人維持大致方向。"},{"en":"A navigational rubric is a simple rule or guideline used to help someone navigate.","zh":"navigational rubric 是用來幫助某人導航的簡單規則或指引。"},{"en":"A hiker may use the rubric “keep the river on your right” to avoid turning the wrong way.","zh":"行山者可能使用「讓河一直在右邊」這條準則，以避免走錯方向。"},{"en":"Such rules reduce memory load because they do not require every street name.","zh":"這些規則減少記憶負擔，因為不需要記住每條街名。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a guiding rule for movement.","zh":"這個短語描述移動時的指導規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"keep something on your left","meaning":"讓……一直在左邊","examples":[{"en":"You can keep the river on your left while walking south.","zh":"你向南走時，可以讓河流一直在左邊。"},{"en":"To keep something on your left means to make sure it stays on the left side as you move.","zh":"keep something on your left 指在移動時確保某物一直留在左邊。"},{"en":"A visitor may keep the school fence on her left until she reaches the main gate.","zh":"訪客可能讓學校圍欄一直在左邊，直到到達正門。"},{"en":"This method helps people maintain direction without reading every street sign.","zh":"這種方法幫助人不必讀每個路牌也能維持方向。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a simple spatial rule for navigation.","zh":"這個短語給出簡單的空間導航規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"eventually cross","meaning":"最終橫過","examples":[{"en":"If you continue east, you will eventually cross the main road.","zh":"如果你繼續向東走，最終會橫過主幹道。"},{"en":"To eventually cross something means to reach and go across it after some time.","zh":"eventually cross 某物，指一段時間後到達並穿過它。"},{"en":"If students walk straight down the corridor, they will eventually cross the school hall entrance.","zh":"如果學生沿走廊一直走，最終會經過學校禮堂入口。"},{"en":"Continuing in a general direction can lead travellers to a major landmark.","zh":"持續朝大致方向前進，可以帶旅客到達主要地標。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a result that happens later, not immediately.","zh":"這個短語暗示結果較後發生，而不是即時發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"flexible and capable of learning","meaning":"靈活並有學習能力","examples":[{"en":"The human positioning system is flexible and capable of learning.","zh":"人類定位系統靈活並有學習能力。"},{"en":"Flexible and capable of learning means able to adjust and improve through experience.","zh":"flexible and capable of learning 指能夠透過經驗調整和改善。"},{"en":"A new student becomes more capable of finding classrooms after walking around the school for a week.","zh":"新學生在學校走了一星期後，會更懂得找到課室。"},{"en":"Learning makes navigation easier because familiar signs and paths become meaningful.","zh":"學習令導航更容易，因為熟悉標誌和路線變得有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a system that can change instead of following one fixed rule.","zh":"這個短語描述能改變的系統，而不是只跟隨固定規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"know the way from A to B","meaning":"知道由 A 前往 B 的路線","examples":[{"en":"She knows the way from the station to the museum.","zh":"她知道由車站前往博物館的路線。"},{"en":"To know the way from A to B means to know the route between two places.","zh":"know the way from A to B 指知道兩個地方之間的路線。"},{"en":"A student may know the way from home to school but not from school to the hospital.","zh":"學生可能知道由家到學校的路，但不知道由學校到醫院的路。"},{"en":"Knowing one route does not always mean knowing the whole area.","zh":"知道一條路線不一定代表熟悉整個地區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes route knowledge between a starting point and an end point.","zh":"這個短語描述起點和終點之間的路線知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"figure out how to","meaning":"想出如何……","examples":[{"en":"People can often figure out how to reach a new destination.","zh":"人們常能想出如何到達新的目的地。"},{"en":"To figure out how to do something means to think and find a way to do it.","zh":"figure out how to do something 指思考並找出做某事的方法。"},{"en":"A student may figure out how to solve a grammar problem by comparing examples.","zh":"學生可能透過比較例子，想出如何解決文法問題。"},{"en":"People figure things out when they use clues, memory, and reasoning together.","zh":"人們使用線索、記憶和推理時，就能想出方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes solving a practical problem by thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述透過思考解決實際問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"complex cognitive system","meaning":"複雜的認知系統","examples":[{"en":"Navigation depends on a complex cognitive system.","zh":"導航依賴複雜的認知系統。"},{"en":"A complex cognitive system is a mental system involving thinking, memory, attention, and decision-making.","zh":"complex cognitive system 是涉及思考、記憶、注意力和決策的心理系統。"},{"en":"Reading a difficult article uses a complex cognitive system because students must remember, compare, and infer.","zh":"閱讀困難文章會使用複雜認知系統，因為學生必須記憶、比較和推斷。"},{"en":"Navigation feels simple, but the brain must process many kinds of information at once.","zh":"導航感覺簡單，但大腦必須同時處理多種資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a complicated mental process.","zh":"這個短語描述複雜的心理過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"really work","meaning":"真正運作","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are investigating how human navigation really works.","zh":"研究人員正在調查人類導航真正如何運作。"},{"en":"How something really works means how it actually operates beneath the surface.","zh":"how something really works 指某事在表面之下實際如何運作。"},{"en":"A teacher may study how memory really works to design better revision lessons.","zh":"老師可能研究記憶真正如何運作，以設計更好溫習課。"},{"en":"Understanding the real process helps people improve training and avoid wrong assumptions.","zh":"理解真正過程幫助人改善訓練並避免錯誤假設。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for the true mechanism, not just the appearance.","zh":"這個短語問真正機制，而不只是表面情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"look at several strategies","meaning":"研究多種策略","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are looking at several strategies used in navigation.","zh":"研究人員正在研究導航中使用的多種策略。"},{"en":"To look at several strategies means to study or consider more than one method.","zh":"look at several strategies 指研究或考慮多於一種方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may look at several strategies before helping students improve spelling.","zh":"老師可能在幫助學生改善串字前研究多種策略。"},{"en":"Comparing methods helps people see which one works best in each situation.","zh":"比較方法幫助人看出哪一種在不同情況中最有效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes examining different possible approaches.","zh":"這個短語描述審視不同可行方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"orient oneself in space","meaning":"在空間中辨認方向","examples":[{"en":"People use landmarks to orient themselves in space.","zh":"人們使用地標在空間中辨認方向。"},{"en":"To orient oneself in space means to work out where one is and which direction one is facing or moving.","zh":"orient oneself in space 指判斷自己在哪裏，以及正面向或移向哪個方向。"},{"en":"A new student may orient herself in school by remembering the office, playground, and main gate.","zh":"新學生可能透過記住校務處、操場和正門，在學校中辨認方向。"},{"en":"If people cannot orient themselves, they may know the destination but not how to move towards it.","zh":"如果人們不能辨認方向，他們可能知道目的地，卻不知道如何前往。"},{"en":"The phrase describes finding one’s position and direction.","zh":"這個短語描述找出自己的位置和方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"navigational strategies","meaning":"導航策略","examples":[{"en":"Humans combine several navigational strategies when travelling.","zh":"人類旅行時會結合幾種導航策略。"},{"en":"Navigational strategies are methods people use to find routes and avoid getting lost.","zh":"navigational strategies 是人們用來找路和避免迷路的方法。"},{"en":"A tourist may use a map, street signs, and advice from locals as different navigational strategies.","zh":"旅客可能使用地圖、街道標誌和本地人建議作為不同導航策略。"},{"en":"Using several strategies can make travel safer when one method fails.","zh":"使用幾種策略可以在一種方法失效時令旅程更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to planned or learned ways of finding direction.","zh":"這個短語指有計劃或習得的辨認方向方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"guidance","meaning":"引導式導航","examples":[{"en":"Guidance uses a visible landmark near the destination.","zh":"引導式導航使用目的地附近的可見地標。"},{"en":"Guidance is a navigation method that directs someone towards a visible target or landmark.","zh":"guidance 是引導某人朝可見目標或地標前進的導航方法。"},{"en":"A child may find the school office by walking towards the tall clock tower beside it.","zh":"孩子可能透過朝旁邊的高鐘樓走，找到校務處。"},{"en":"Guidance works best when the landmark can be seen clearly from a distance.","zh":"當地標從遠處清楚可見時，引導式導航最有效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes navigation by following something visible.","zh":"這個短語描述透過跟隨可見物而導航。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"path integration","meaning":"路徑整合","examples":[{"en":"Path integration involves keeping track of one’s movements.","zh":"路徑整合涉及記錄自身移動。"},{"en":"Path integration is a navigation method in which the brain estimates position by adding up movement and direction.","zh":"path integration 是大腦透過累加移動和方向來估計位置的導航方法。"},{"en":"A hiker may use path integration by remembering that she walked north for ten minutes and then east.","zh":"行山者可能記得自己向北走十分鐘再向東走，以使用路徑整合。"},{"en":"If movement is recorded wrongly, the estimated position may become inaccurate.","zh":"如果移動被錯誤記錄，估計位置可能變得不準確。"},{"en":"The phrase describes navigation based on one’s own movement rather than landmarks alone.","zh":"這個短語描述基於自身移動而非只靠地標的導航。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"route following","meaning":"按路線導航","examples":[{"en":"Route following uses a detailed sequence of landmarks and directions.","zh":"按路線導航使用一連串詳細地標和方向。"},{"en":"Route following means travelling by following a step-by-step set of route instructions.","zh":"route following 指按照逐步路線指示前進。"},{"en":"A visitor follows a route when she turns left at the bank and then right after the bridge.","zh":"訪客在銀行左轉，然後過橋後右轉，就是在按路線導航。"},{"en":"This method is useful, but one missed step can make the traveller confused.","zh":"這種方法有用，但漏掉一步就可以令旅客困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes navigation through ordered instructions.","zh":"這個短語描述透過有次序指示導航。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"combinations thereof","meaning":"以上方法的不同組合","examples":[{"en":"People may use all three methods or combinations thereof.","zh":"人們可能使用三種方法全部，或以上方法的不同組合。"},{"en":"Combinations thereof means mixtures of the things just mentioned.","zh":"combinations thereof 指剛提及事物的不同混合。"},{"en":"A student may revise using notes, past papers, or combinations thereof.","zh":"學生可能使用筆記、歷屆試題，或以上方法的不同組合來溫習。"},{"en":"Combining methods can help when one method alone is not enough.","zh":"當單一方法不足，組合方法可以幫忙。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and refers back to items already listed.","zh":"這個短語較正式，指回已列出的項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"navigational skills","meaning":"導航技能","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are learning more about human navigational skills.","zh":"科學家正更多了解人類導航技能。"},{"en":"Navigational skills are abilities used to find routes, recognise places, and avoid getting lost.","zh":"navigational skills 是用來找路、辨認地方和避免迷路的能力。"},{"en":"A delivery worker needs strong navigational skills to move around a city quickly.","zh":"送貨員需要強導航技能，才能快速在城市中移動。"},{"en":"These skills improve when people practise reading signs, remembering routes, and using landmarks.","zh":"當人們練習閱讀標誌、記住路線和使用地標，這些技能會改善。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical abilities for finding one’s way.","zh":"這個短語指尋路的實用能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"make the case that","meaning":"提出理據說明","examples":[{"en":"Researchers make the case that navigation supports other mental abilities.","zh":"研究人員提出理據說明導航支援其他心理能力。"},{"en":"To make the case that something is true means to present reasons and evidence for it.","zh":"make the case that 某事為真，指提出理由和證據支持它。"},{"en":"A student can make the case that longer library hours would help exam preparation.","zh":"學生可以提出理據說明延長圖書館開放時間有助備考。"},{"en":"Strong evidence makes an argument more convincing and harder to dismiss.","zh":"強證據令論點更有說服力，也更難被駁回。"},{"en":"The phrase describes building a reasoned argument.","zh":"這個短語描述建立有理據的論證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"underlie our powers of","meaning":"是我們……能力的基礎","examples":[{"en":"Navigational ability may underlie our powers of memory and reasoning.","zh":"導航能力可能是我們記憶和推理能力的基礎。"},{"en":"To underlie our powers of something means to form the hidden basis of those abilities.","zh":"underlie our powers of 某事，指形成那些能力的隱藏基礎。"},{"en":"Basic vocabulary may underlie a student’s power to read difficult articles.","zh":"基本詞彙可能是學生閱讀困難文章能力的基礎。"},{"en":"If one ability underlies another, improving the first may support the second.","zh":"如果一種能力是另一種能力的基礎，改善前者可能支援後者。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a deeper foundation behind visible skills.","zh":"這個短語指出可見技能背後的深層基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"logical thinking","meaning":"邏輯思維","examples":[{"en":"Spatial navigation may be connected with logical thinking.","zh":"空間導航可能與邏輯思維有關。"},{"en":"Logical thinking is the ability to reason clearly and connect ideas in a sensible order.","zh":"logical thinking 是清楚推理並以合理次序連接想法的能力。"},{"en":"A student uses logical thinking when she checks why one answer follows from the evidence.","zh":"學生查核為何某答案由證據推出時，就是在使用邏輯思維。"},{"en":"Logical thinking helps people solve problems without relying only on guesses or feelings.","zh":"邏輯思維幫助人解決問題，而不只依靠猜測或感覺。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to clear, step-by-step reasoning.","zh":"這個短語指清楚、逐步的推理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"arrive in a place","meaning":"到達某個地方","examples":[{"en":"Imagine that you have arrived in a place you have never visited.","zh":"想像你到達一個從未去過的地方。"},{"en":"To arrive in a place means to reach that place after travelling there.","zh":"arrive in a place 指經過旅程後到達某個地方。"},{"en":"A student may feel nervous when she arrives in a new city for university.","zh":"學生到達新城市讀大學時，可能感到緊張。"},{"en":"After arriving, people often need to work out where to go next.","zh":"到達後，人們通常需要弄清下一步去哪裏。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the beginning of a new location experience.","zh":"這個短語標誌新地方經驗的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get off the train","meaning":"下火車","examples":[{"en":"You get off the train at Grand Central Terminal.","zh":"你在 Grand Central Terminal 下火車。"},{"en":"To get off the train means to leave the train after it stops.","zh":"get off the train 指火車停下後離開車廂。"},{"en":"Commuters get off the train when it reaches their station.","zh":"通勤者在火車到達自己的車站時下火車。"},{"en":"If passengers get off at the wrong stop, they may need to wait for another train.","zh":"如果乘客在錯誤車站下車，可能需要等另一班火車。"},{"en":"The phrase describes leaving a train, not boarding it.","zh":"這個短語描述離開火車，而不是登上火車。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have a few hours to explore","meaning":"有數小時遊覽","examples":[{"en":"You have a few hours to explore Manhattan.","zh":"你有數小時遊覽曼哈頓。"},{"en":"To have a few hours to explore means to have a limited amount of time to look around a place.","zh":"have a few hours to explore 指有有限時間四處看看某地方。"},{"en":"A visitor may have a few hours to explore a museum before meeting friends for dinner.","zh":"訪客可能在與朋友晚飯前有數小時遊覽博物館。"},{"en":"Limited time makes people choose only the most interesting or convenient places.","zh":"時間有限會令人只選最有趣或最方便的地方。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests short but free time for discovery.","zh":"這個短語暗示短暫但自由的探索時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"return for your ride home","meaning":"回去乘車返家","examples":[{"en":"You must return to the station for your ride home.","zh":"你必須回到車站乘車返家。"},{"en":"To return for your ride home means to go back to the place where your transport home will leave.","zh":"return for your ride home 指回到送你回家的交通工具出發地點。"},{"en":"A student on a school trip must return to the coach before it leaves for home.","zh":"參加學校旅行的學生必須在旅遊巴開車前回去乘車返家。"},{"en":"If you return late, you may miss your transport and need another plan.","zh":"如果你回去遲了，可能錯過交通工具並需要另一個安排。"},{"en":"The phrase connects going back with catching transport home.","zh":"這個短語把回程與乘交通工具返家連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"head uptown","meaning":"向市區北面前進","examples":[{"en":"You head uptown to visit Central Park.","zh":"你向市區北面前進去參觀中央公園。"},{"en":"To head uptown means to go towards the northern or upper part of a city, especially in Manhattan.","zh":"head uptown 指前往城市北部或較上方地區，尤其在曼哈頓。"},{"en":"A tourist may head uptown after lunch to see museums and parks.","zh":"旅客午飯後可能向市區北面前進去看博物館和公園。"},{"en":"Knowing whether to go uptown or downtown helps travellers choose the right train direction.","zh":"知道應往 uptown 還是 downtown，有助旅客選對列車方向。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a city direction rather than a precise address.","zh":"這個短語給出城市方向，而不是精確地址。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"popular spots","meaning":"熱門地點","examples":[{"en":"Visitors often explore popular spots in Manhattan.","zh":"訪客常遊覽曼哈頓的熱門地點。"},{"en":"Popular spots are places many people like to visit.","zh":"popular spots 是許多人喜歡到訪的地方。"},{"en":"A city’s popular spots may include markets, parks, museums, and famous streets.","zh":"一座城市的熱門地點可能包括街市、公園、博物館和著名街道。"},{"en":"Popular spots can become crowded because tourists and locals both go there.","zh":"熱門地點可能變得擠迫，因為旅客和本地人都會去。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to well-liked locations.","zh":"這個短語指受歡迎的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have been told about","meaning":"曾聽別人介紹過","examples":[{"en":"You visit several attractions that you have been told about.","zh":"你參觀幾個曾聽別人介紹過的景點。"},{"en":"To have been told about something means someone has previously given you information about it.","zh":"have been told about 某事，指以前有人給你關於它的資訊。"},{"en":"A student may visit a café she has been told about by her classmates.","zh":"學生可能去同學曾介紹過的咖啡店。"},{"en":"Recommendations can influence where people choose to go.","zh":"推薦可以影響人們選擇去哪裏。"},{"en":"The phrase connects present action with earlier information from others.","zh":"這個短語把現在行動與較早從他人得來的資訊連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"meander in and out of","meaning":"悠閒地進出……","examples":[{"en":"You meander in and out of shops along the way.","zh":"你沿途悠閒地進出商店。"},{"en":"To meander in and out of places means to move slowly and casually between them without a strict plan.","zh":"meander in and out of 地方，指沒有嚴格計劃地慢慢而隨意在它們之間移動。"},{"en":"Friends may meander in and out of small shops during a relaxed weekend walk.","zh":"朋友可能在輕鬆的週末散步中悠閒地進出小店。"},{"en":"This kind of movement can make people lose track of direction or time.","zh":"這種移動可能令人失去方向感或時間感。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests wandering pleasantly rather than moving directly.","zh":"這個短語暗示愉快地閒逛，而不是直接前往。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"along the way","meaning":"沿途","examples":[{"en":"You stop at several shops along the way.","zh":"你沿途在幾間商店停下。"},{"en":"Along the way means during the journey or while moving towards a destination.","zh":"along the way 指在旅程中或前往目的地期間。"},{"en":"Students may buy snacks along the way to the cinema.","zh":"學生可能在去戲院沿途買零食。"},{"en":"Things noticed along the way can become useful landmarks later.","zh":"沿途注意到的東西之後可以成為有用地標。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to events or places encountered during travel.","zh":"這個短語指旅途中遇到的事件或地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get back to","meaning":"返回……","examples":[{"en":"You suddenly realise that it is time to get back to the station.","zh":"你突然意識到是時候返回車站。"},{"en":"To get back to a place means to return to it.","zh":"get back to 某地，指回到該地方。"},{"en":"A child must get back to the classroom before the next lesson starts.","zh":"孩子必須在下一堂課開始前返回課室。"},{"en":"If people wander too far, getting back may become harder than expected.","zh":"如果人們走得太遠，返回可能比預期困難。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on returning to an earlier place.","zh":"這個短語重點在回到早前的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ask passersby for help","meaning":"向途人求助","examples":[{"en":"Tourists often ask passersby for help when they are lost.","zh":"旅客迷路時常向途人求助。"},{"en":"To ask passersby for help means to ask people walking nearby for information or assistance.","zh":"ask passersby for help 指向附近走過的人詢問資訊或求助。"},{"en":"A visitor may ask passersby for help if her phone battery dies in an unfamiliar district.","zh":"如果訪客在陌生地區手機沒電，可能向途人求助。"},{"en":"Helpful passersby can give local knowledge that maps may not show clearly.","zh":"樂於助人的途人可以提供地圖未必清楚顯示的本地知識。"},{"en":"The phrase describes seeking help from strangers in public places.","zh":"這個短語描述在公共地方向陌生人尋求幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"most likely","meaning":"很可能","examples":[{"en":"Most likely, different people will give different types of directions.","zh":"很可能，不同的人會給出不同類型的指示。"},{"en":"Most likely means probably or very probably.","zh":"most likely 指大概或很可能。"},{"en":"If a student has not revised at all, she will most likely find the test difficult.","zh":"如果學生完全沒有溫習，她很可能覺得測驗困難。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when something is expected but not completely certain.","zh":"這個短語用於某事被預期會發生，但並非完全確定時。"},{"en":"It gives a careful prediction rather than an absolute statement.","zh":"它給出謹慎預測，而不是絕對陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in many different forms","meaning":"以多種不同形式","examples":[{"en":"Directions may be given in many different forms.","zh":"指示可能以多種不同形式給出。"},{"en":"In many different forms means in several different types or styles.","zh":"in many different forms 指以幾種不同類型或風格。"},{"en":"Feedback can come in many different forms, such as written comments, scores, or face-to-face advice.","zh":"回饋可以以多種不同形式出現，例如書面評語、分數或面對面建議。"},{"en":"Different forms help different people because not everyone understands information the same way.","zh":"不同形式能幫助不同人，因為不是每個人都以相同方式理解資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses variety in presentation.","zh":"這個短語強調呈現方式的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"orient oneself by","meaning":"以……辨認方向","examples":[{"en":"Some people orient themselves by a prominent landmark.","zh":"有些人以顯眼地標辨認方向。"},{"en":"To orient oneself by something means to use it to understand one’s position or direction.","zh":"orient oneself by 某物，指使用它來理解自己的位置或方向。"},{"en":"A student may orient herself by the school clock tower when moving around campus.","zh":"學生在校園中移動時，可能以學校鐘樓辨認方向。"},{"en":"A clear landmark helps people decide which way to walk next.","zh":"清楚地標幫助人決定下一步往哪邊走。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using a reference point for direction.","zh":"這個短語描述使用參考點來辨認方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"prominent landmark","meaning":"顯眼的地標","examples":[{"en":"A prominent landmark can be seen from a long distance.","zh":"顯眼的地標可以從遠距離看見。"},{"en":"A prominent landmark is a noticeable building, object, or place that helps people recognise an area.","zh":"prominent landmark 是幫助人辨認地區的明顯建築、物件或地方。"},{"en":"A tall church, clock tower, or bright sign can be a prominent landmark.","zh":"高教堂、鐘樓或明亮招牌都可以是顯眼地標。"},{"en":"Prominent landmarks help travellers stay oriented when streets look similar.","zh":"當街道看起來相似，顯眼地標幫助旅客保持方向感。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a highly visible point of reference.","zh":"這個短語指非常容易看見的參考點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"gesture southward","meaning":"向南方示意","examples":[{"en":"The passerby gestures southward towards the building.","zh":"途人向南方那座大樓示意。"},{"en":"To gesture southward means to point or move one’s hand towards the south.","zh":"gesture southward 指用手指向或移向南方。"},{"en":"A teacher may gesture towards the library when a new student asks where to go.","zh":"當新學生問去哪裏，老師可能向圖書館方向示意。"},{"en":"Gestures help when spoken directions are short or when people do not know street names.","zh":"當口頭指示很短或人們不知道街名，手勢會有幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical direction-giving.","zh":"這個短語描述用身體動作給方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"head for","meaning":"朝……前進","examples":[{"en":"Head for the tall building near the station.","zh":"朝車站附近的高樓前進。"},{"en":"To head for a place means to move towards it.","zh":"head for 某地，指朝它移動。"},{"en":"After school, students may head for the bus stop before it becomes crowded.","zh":"放學後，學生可能在巴士站變擠迫前朝那裏前進。"},{"en":"Choosing a visible target makes it easier to keep moving in the right direction.","zh":"選擇可見目標令保持正確方向前進更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a simple instruction to go towards something.","zh":"這個短語給出朝某物前進的簡單指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"right below","meaning":"就在……下方","examples":[{"en":"The station is right below the MetLife Building.","zh":"車站就在 MetLife Building 下方。"},{"en":"Right below means directly underneath or very close underneath something.","zh":"right below 指正正在某物下面或非常接近其下方。"},{"en":"The café is right below the language centre, so students can meet there after class.","zh":"咖啡店就在語言中心下方，所以學生下課後可以在那裏見面。"},{"en":"Knowing what is above a place can help people find what is below it.","zh":"知道某地方上面是甚麼，可以幫助人找到下面的地方。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a precise vertical location.","zh":"這個短語給出精確的垂直位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"navigational approach","meaning":"導航方法","examples":[{"en":"Neurologists call this navigational approach guidance.","zh":"神經學家稱這種導航方法為引導式導航。"},{"en":"A navigational approach is a method used to find direction or reach a place.","zh":"navigational approach 是用來辨認方向或到達某地的方法。"},{"en":"Using a landmark, following street signs, and retracing steps are different navigational approaches.","zh":"使用地標、跟隨路牌和原路折返都是不同導航方法。"},{"en":"Different approaches work better in different environments.","zh":"不同方法在不同環境中更有效。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a way of solving a navigation problem.","zh":"這個短語指解決導航問題的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"visible from a distance","meaning":"從遠處可看見","examples":[{"en":"The tower is visible from a distance.","zh":"那座塔從遠處可看見。"},{"en":"Visible from a distance means able to be seen even when you are not close to it.","zh":"visible from a distance 指即使不接近也能看見。"},{"en":"A bright school sign may be visible from a distance across the street.","zh":"明亮的學校招牌可能從街對面遠處可看見。"},{"en":"Objects that are visible from far away can guide travellers through unfamiliar areas.","zh":"從遠處可看見的物件可以引導旅客穿過陌生地區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something easy to see before you reach it.","zh":"這個短語描述到達前已容易看見的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"serve as the marker for","meaning":"作為……的標記","examples":[{"en":"A landmark serves as the marker for the destination.","zh":"地標作為目的地的標記。"},{"en":"To serve as the marker for something means to act as the sign that identifies or indicates it.","zh":"serve as the marker for 某物，指作為辨認或指出它的標誌。"},{"en":"A red door may serve as the marker for the entrance to a small clinic.","zh":"紅色門可能作為小診所入口的標記。"},{"en":"Markers help people recognise a place quickly and avoid passing it by.","zh":"標記幫助人快速認出地方並避免錯過。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a visible clue that points to something.","zh":"這個短語描述指向某物的可見線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"one’s destination","meaning":"某人的目的地","examples":[{"en":"A visible building can indicate one’s destination.","zh":"可見的大樓可以指出某人的目的地。"},{"en":"One’s destination is the place a person intends to reach.","zh":"one’s destination 是某人打算到達的地方。"},{"en":"A hospital may be the destination for a patient taking a taxi to an appointment.","zh":"病人乘的士去覆診時，醫院可能就是他的目的地。"},{"en":"Knowing the destination clearly helps travellers choose the right route.","zh":"清楚知道目的地幫助旅客選擇正確路線。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the goal of a journey.","zh":"這個短語指旅程目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"city dweller","meaning":"城市居民","examples":[{"en":"A city dweller may give directions by referring to familiar places.","zh":"城市居民可能透過提到熟悉地方來給指示。"},{"en":"A city dweller is someone who lives in a city.","zh":"city dweller 是住在城市的人。"},{"en":"A city dweller may know shortcuts through stations, shopping centres, and side streets.","zh":"城市居民可能知道穿過車站、商場和小街的捷徑。"},{"en":"People who live in a city often use local landmarks instead of official map language.","zh":"住在城市的人常使用本地地標，而不是正式地圖語言。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a person whose daily life is based in an urban area.","zh":"這個短語描述日常生活以城市為基地的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"remember passing","meaning":"記得曾經經過","examples":[{"en":"Try to remember the places that you passed earlier.","zh":"嘗試記得你早前曾經經過的地方。"},{"en":"To remember passing a place means to recall seeing or going by it before.","zh":"remember passing 某地，指回想起以前見過或經過它。"},{"en":"A student may remember passing the school office and use it to find the exit.","zh":"學生可能記得曾經經過校務處，並用它來找出口。"},{"en":"Remembered places can help travellers retrace their route when they feel lost.","zh":"記得曾經經過的地方可以幫助旅客迷路時沿路折返。"},{"en":"The phrase connects memory with previous movement.","zh":"這個短語把記憶與先前移動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"point someone towards","meaning":"指引某人前往……","examples":[{"en":"The directions point you towards the last place you remember.","zh":"指示會指引你前往你記得的最後一個地方。"},{"en":"To point someone towards a place means to guide that person in its direction.","zh":"point someone towards 某地，指引導該人朝該方向前進。"},{"en":"A security guard may point a visitor towards the lift after checking her appointment.","zh":"保安檢查訪客預約後，可能指引她前往電梯。"},{"en":"Directions that point people towards familiar places reduce uncertainty.","zh":"指引人前往熟悉地方的方向，可以減少不確定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes giving directional help.","zh":"這個短語描述提供方向上的幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"aim for","meaning":"以……為前進目標","examples":[{"en":"You aim for the most recent landmark that you recall.","zh":"你以你記得的最近地標為前進目標。"},{"en":"To aim for a place means to move towards it as your target.","zh":"aim for 某地，指把它作為目標並朝它前進。"},{"en":"A runner may aim for the school gate when finishing a long practice route.","zh":"跑手完成長距離練習路線時，可能以校門為前進目標。"},{"en":"Choosing a target helps people keep moving in a clear direction.","zh":"選擇目標幫助人保持清楚方向前進。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when a place becomes a practical goal.","zh":"這個短語用於某地方成為實際目標時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"notable place","meaning":"顯著地點","examples":[{"en":"A church or public building can serve as a notable place.","zh":"教堂或公共建築可以作為顯著地點。"},{"en":"A notable place is a location that is easy to notice or remember.","zh":"notable place 是容易注意或記住的位置。"},{"en":"A bright library entrance can be a notable place for students meeting after school.","zh":"明亮的圖書館入口可以成為學生放學後見面的顯著地點。"},{"en":"Notable places are useful because people can use them as reference points.","zh":"顯著地點有用，因為人們可以把它們作為參考點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a place that stands out.","zh":"這個短語描述突出的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"and so on","meaning":"如此類推","examples":[{"en":"You move from one familiar landmark to the next, and so on.","zh":"你由一個熟悉地標移到下一個，如此類推。"},{"en":"And so on means the same pattern continues with more similar things.","zh":"and so on 指同一模式繼續，包括更多相似事物。"},{"en":"A student may revise vocabulary, grammar, sentence structure, and so on.","zh":"學生可能溫習詞彙、文法、句子結構，如此類推。"},{"en":"The phrase avoids listing every example when the pattern is already clear.","zh":"當模式已清楚，這個短語可避免列出每個例子。"},{"en":"It means “and other similar things after that.”","zh":"它的意思是「以及之後其他相似事物」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"retrace your path","meaning":"沿原路折返","examples":[{"en":"You can retrace your path by returning to previously visited places.","zh":"你可以透過回到之前到過的地方沿原路折返。"},{"en":"To retrace your path means to go back along the same route you used earlier.","zh":"retrace your path 指沿着早前走過的同一路線回去。"},{"en":"A student who leaves her umbrella in the canteen may retrace her path to find it.","zh":"如果學生把雨傘留在飯堂，可能沿原路折返回去尋找。"},{"en":"Retracing helps when you are unsure which new direction to take.","zh":"當你不確定應走哪個新方向，沿路折返會有幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase describes returning step by step along a known route.","zh":"這個短語描述沿已知路線一步步返回。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"add together","meaning":"把……加在一起","examples":[{"en":"The brain adds together the separate stages of a journey.","zh":"大腦把旅程的不同階段加在一起。"},{"en":"To add together means to combine separate parts into one total or overall result.","zh":"add together 指把分開部分結合成一個總數或整體結果。"},{"en":"A student adds together bus fare and lunch money to know how much cash she needs.","zh":"學生把巴士費和午餐錢加在一起，以知道需要多少現金。"},{"en":"In navigation, adding movements together helps the brain estimate current position.","zh":"在導航中，把移動加在一起幫助大腦估計目前位置。"},{"en":"The phrase describes combining parts to form a whole.","zh":"這個短語描述把部分合成整體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"individual legs of a trek","meaning":"行程的各個路段","examples":[{"en":"The brain records the individual legs of a trek.","zh":"大腦記錄行程的各個路段。"},{"en":"Individual legs of a trek are the separate parts or stages of a journey.","zh":"individual legs of a trek 是旅程中分開的部分或階段。"},{"en":"A hike may have one leg from the bus stop to the hill, and another leg from the hill to the village.","zh":"一次行山可能有一段由巴士站到山上，另一段由山上到村莊。"},{"en":"Remembering each leg helps travellers understand how far and in what direction they have moved.","zh":"記住每個路段幫助旅客理解自己走了多遠和朝甚麼方向走。"},{"en":"The phrase breaks a journey into smaller route sections.","zh":"這個短語把旅程分成較小路段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cumulative progress report","meaning":"累積進度記錄","examples":[{"en":"The brain creates a cumulative progress report from your movements.","zh":"大腦從你的移動中建立累積進度記錄。"},{"en":"A cumulative progress report is an overall record built by adding each stage of progress.","zh":"cumulative progress report 是透過加入每個進展階段而建立的整體記錄。"},{"en":"A teacher’s grade book can act as a cumulative progress report for a student’s writing over a term.","zh":"老師的成績簿可以作為學生一學期寫作的累積進度記錄。"},{"en":"In navigation, each movement updates the brain’s estimate of where the body is.","zh":"在導航中，每次移動都會更新大腦對身體位置的估計。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a running total of progress.","zh":"這個短語描述進度的持續累加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rely primarily on","meaning":"主要依賴……","examples":[{"en":"Many animals rely primarily on path integration.","zh":"許多動物主要依賴路徑整合。"},{"en":"To rely primarily on something means to depend mainly on it, even if other methods may also help.","zh":"rely primarily on 某事，指主要依靠它，即使其他方法也可能有幫助。"},{"en":"A student may rely primarily on past papers when preparing for an exam.","zh":"學生備考時可能主要依賴歷屆試題。"},{"en":"If the main method is weak, the whole task becomes harder.","zh":"如果主要方法薄弱，整項任務會變得更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the chief source of support.","zh":"這個短語指出主要支援來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"get around","meaning":"四處活動；往來各處","examples":[{"en":"Animals use path integration to get around.","zh":"動物使用路徑整合四處活動。"},{"en":"To get around means to move from place to place, especially within an area.","zh":"get around 指在不同地方之間移動，尤其是在某區域內。"},{"en":"A new student uses a campus map to get around during the first week of school.","zh":"新學生在開學第一週使用校園地圖四處走動。"},{"en":"If people cannot get around easily, school, work, and shopping become difficult.","zh":"如果人們不能容易往來各處，上學、工作和購物都會變困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical movement through an environment.","zh":"這個短語描述在環境中的實際移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"desert ants","meaning":"沙漠螞蟻","examples":[{"en":"Desert ants can navigate across large areas without landmarks.","zh":"沙漠螞蟻可以在沒有地標的大片地區中辨認方向。"},{"en":"Desert ants are ants that live in dry desert environments and can travel away from their nests to forage.","zh":"desert ants 是生活在乾燥沙漠環境中，並會離巢覓食的螞蟻。"},{"en":"A desert ant may leave its nest to search for food on bare ground where there are few visual clues.","zh":"沙漠螞蟻可能離開巢穴，在幾乎沒有視覺線索的裸地上找食物。"},{"en":"Because deserts have few landmarks, these ants need strong internal navigation methods.","zh":"因為沙漠地標很少，這些螞蟻需要強大的內在導航方法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to insects used as examples of natural navigation.","zh":"這個短語指被用作自然導航例子的昆蟲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the genus Cataglyphis","meaning":"Cataglyphis 屬","examples":[{"en":"Desert ants of the genus Cataglyphis use an internal navigation system.","zh":"Cataglyphis 屬的沙漠螞蟻使用內在導航系統。"},{"en":"The genus Cataglyphis is a biological group of desert ants known for strong navigation ability.","zh":"genus Cataglyphis 是一類以強導航能力聞名的沙漠螞蟻生物分類。"},{"en":"Scientists study Cataglyphis ants because they travel far from their nests and return accurately.","zh":"科學家研究 Cataglyphis 螞蟻，因為牠們離巢很遠仍能準確返回。"},{"en":"Studying one genus helps researchers compare similar animals within a clear biological group.","zh":"研究一個屬幫助研究人員在清楚生物群組中比較相似動物。"},{"en":"The phrase names a scientific classification, not one individual ant.","zh":"這個短語指出科學分類，而不是單一螞蟻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"return from foraging","meaning":"覓食後返回","examples":[{"en":"The ants use path integration to return from foraging.","zh":"螞蟻使用路徑整合在覓食後返回。"},{"en":"To return from foraging means to come back after searching for food.","zh":"return from foraging 指尋找食物後回來。"},{"en":"Bees return from foraging when they fly back to the hive after finding nectar.","zh":"蜜蜂找到花蜜後飛回蜂巢，就是覓食後返回。"},{"en":"Animals need reliable navigation because food searches can take them far from home.","zh":"動物需要可靠導航，因為尋找食物可能令牠們離家很遠。"},{"en":"The phrase connects food-seeking with the journey back.","zh":"這個短語把覓食與回程連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as far as 100 yards away","meaning":"遠至一百碼以外","examples":[{"en":"The ants may forage as far as 100 yards away from the nest.","zh":"螞蟻可能在離巢遠至一百碼以外覓食。"},{"en":"As far as 100 yards away means at a distance of up to 100 yards.","zh":"as far as 100 yards away 指距離最遠可達一百碼。"},{"en":"A student may park as far as 100 yards away from school when nearby spaces are full.","zh":"當附近車位滿了，學生可能把車停在離學校遠至一百碼以外。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the distance can be surprisingly long.","zh":"這個短語顯示距離可以令人意外地長。"},{"en":"It gives an upper limit for how far something may be.","zh":"它給出某事可能到達多遠的上限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"note the general direction","meaning":"記住大致方向","examples":[{"en":"The ants note the general direction from which they came.","zh":"螞蟻記住自己來時的大致方向。"},{"en":"To note the general direction means to remember the broad direction, not every small detail.","zh":"note the general direction 指記住大方向，而不是每個小細節。"},{"en":"A hiker may note the general direction of the car park before walking into the woods.","zh":"行山者走入樹林前，可能記住停車場的大致方向。"},{"en":"Remembering a broad direction can help when there are few signs or landmarks.","zh":"當標誌或地標很少，記住大方向可以幫忙。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on overall orientation.","zh":"這個短語重點在整體方向感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"retrace their steps","meaning":"原路折返","examples":[{"en":"The ants retrace their steps towards the nest.","zh":"螞蟻朝巢穴原路折返。"},{"en":"To retrace one’s steps means to go back along the route one has already taken.","zh":"retrace one’s steps 指沿自己已走過的路線返回。"},{"en":"A student who loses her keys may retrace her steps from the classroom to the canteen.","zh":"遺失鎖匙的學生可能由課室到飯堂原路折返。"},{"en":"Retracing steps helps people return to a known point when they are uncertain.","zh":"原路折返幫助人在不確定時回到已知地點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes going back through a previous path.","zh":"這個短語描述沿先前路徑返回。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the polarisation of sunlight","meaning":"陽光的偏振現象","examples":[{"en":"The ants use the polarisation of sunlight to orient themselves.","zh":"螞蟻使用陽光的偏振現象來辨認方向。"},{"en":"The polarisation of sunlight is a pattern in sunlight that some animals can use for direction.","zh":"polarisation of sunlight 是陽光中的一種模式，有些動物可用它辨認方向。"},{"en":"Humans may not notice this pattern, but certain insects can use it like a compass.","zh":"人類未必注意到這種模式，但某些昆蟲可以像指南針一樣使用它。"},{"en":"This helps ants navigate even when the sun is not clearly visible.","zh":"這幫助螞蟻即使在太陽不清楚可見時也能導航。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a natural light cue used in orientation.","zh":"這個短語指用於辨認方向的自然光線線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"orient themselves","meaning":"辨認自身方向","examples":[{"en":"The ants use sunlight to orient themselves under cloudy skies.","zh":"螞蟻在多雲天空下使用陽光辨認自身方向。"},{"en":"To orient themselves means to work out their position or direction.","zh":"orient themselves 指判斷自己的位置或方向。"},{"en":"Students orient themselves in a new building by checking signs and remembering exits.","zh":"學生透過查看標誌和記住出口，在新大樓中辨認自身方向。"},{"en":"Without orientation, people or animals may move in the wrong direction.","zh":"沒有方向感，人或動物可能朝錯誤方向移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes finding direction before or during movement.","zh":"這個短語描述在移動前或移動期間找出方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"overcast skies","meaning":"陰天","examples":[{"en":"The ants can navigate even under overcast skies.","zh":"螞蟻即使在陰天也能導航。"},{"en":"Overcast skies are skies covered with clouds, with little direct sunlight visible.","zh":"overcast skies 是被雲覆蓋、幾乎看不到直接陽光的天空。"},{"en":"A sports day may feel cooler under overcast skies than under bright sun.","zh":"在陰天下運動會可能比在烈日下較涼快。"},{"en":"Cloudy conditions can make navigation harder if an animal relies on the sun.","zh":"如果動物依賴太陽，多雲情況可能令導航更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes cloudy weather conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述多雲天氣狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be faithful to","meaning":"忠實遵循……","examples":[{"en":"The ants remain faithful to their inner homing vector.","zh":"螞蟻忠實遵循牠們的內在歸巢向量。"},{"en":"To be faithful to something means to keep following it or staying loyal to it.","zh":"be faithful to 某事，指持續跟隨或忠於它。"},{"en":"A student may be faithful to a revision timetable even when friends invite her out.","zh":"即使朋友邀請外出，學生也可能忠實遵循溫習時間表。"},{"en":"Remaining faithful to a plan can help people avoid changing direction too easily.","zh":"忠實遵循計劃可以幫助人避免太容易改變方向。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests steady loyalty or continued obedience.","zh":"這個短語暗示穩定忠誠或持續服從。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"inner homing vector","meaning":"內在歸巢向量","examples":[{"en":"An inner homing vector guides the ants towards their nest.","zh":"內在歸巢向量引導螞蟻朝巢穴前進。"},{"en":"An inner homing vector is an internal sense of direction and distance back home.","zh":"inner homing vector 是返回家或巢穴的內在方向和距離感。"},{"en":"A person may have a rough inner sense of how to return to the hotel after walking around a city.","zh":"一個人在城市中走動後，可能有大概知道如何回酒店的內在感覺。"},{"en":"If this internal guide is wrong, the traveller may continue confidently in the wrong direction.","zh":"如果這個內在指引錯誤，旅客可能自信地朝錯誤方向繼續走。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an internal navigation signal.","zh":"這個短語描述內在導航訊號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pick something up","meaning":"拿起某物","examples":[{"en":"A scientist may pick an ant up and move it elsewhere.","zh":"科學家可能拿起一隻螞蟻並把它移到別處。"},{"en":"To pick something up means to lift it from a surface with the hand or another tool.","zh":"pick something up 指用手或工具把某物從表面提起。"},{"en":"A teacher may pick up a dropped pencil and return it to a student.","zh":"老師可能撿起掉下的鉛筆並還給學生。"},{"en":"Picking something up changes its position and may interrupt what it was doing.","zh":"拿起某物會改變其位置，並可能打斷它正在做的事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lifting an object or small living thing.","zh":"這個短語描述提起物件或小生物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a totally different spot","meaning":"完全不同的地點","examples":[{"en":"The ant may be placed in a totally different spot.","zh":"螞蟻可能被放在完全不同的地點。"},{"en":"A totally different spot is a place completely unlike or separate from the original place.","zh":"totally different spot 是與原本地方完全不同或分開的位置。"},{"en":"A teacher may move a noisy student to a totally different spot in the classroom.","zh":"老師可能把吵鬧學生移到課室中完全不同的位置。"},{"en":"Changing someone’s location can make old directions or assumptions useless.","zh":"改變某人的位置可以令舊方向或假設失效。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a complete change of position.","zh":"這個短語強調位置完全改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stubbornly proceed","meaning":"固執地繼續前進","examples":[{"en":"The displaced ant stubbornly proceeds in its original direction.","zh":"被移走的螞蟻固執地沿原來方向繼續前進。"},{"en":"To stubbornly proceed means to continue moving or acting in the same way despite evidence or difficulty.","zh":"stubbornly proceed 指即使有證據或困難，仍以同一方式繼續移動或行動。"},{"en":"A student may stubbornly proceed with a wrong answer even after the teacher gives a hint.","zh":"即使老師給出提示，學生可能仍固執地繼續使用錯誤答案。"},{"en":"Stubborn continuation can be useful if the plan is right, but harmful if the situation has changed.","zh":"如果計劃正確，固執地繼續可能有用；但如果情況已改變，則可能有害。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests determined but possibly mistaken persistence.","zh":"這個短語暗示堅持但可能錯誤的持續行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"originally determined direction","meaning":"原先確定的方向","examples":[{"en":"The insect continues in the originally determined direction.","zh":"昆蟲繼續沿原先確定的方向前進。"},{"en":"The originally determined direction is the direction worked out at the beginning.","zh":"originally determined direction 是一開始判斷出的方向。"},{"en":"A runner may continue in the originally determined direction even after missing a sign.","zh":"跑手即使錯過標誌，也可能繼續沿原先確定的方向前進。"},{"en":"If the starting calculation is wrong, following the original direction can lead away from the goal.","zh":"如果起初計算錯誤，跟隨原來方向可能會離目標越來越遠。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an earlier chosen direction.","zh":"這個短語指較早選定的方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"realise that","meaning":"意識到","examples":[{"en":"The ant eventually realises that it has not reached the nest.","zh":"螞蟻最終意識到自己沒有到達巢穴。"},{"en":"To realise that something is true means to become aware of it.","zh":"realise that 某事為真，指開始意識到它。"},{"en":"A student may realise that she is in the wrong classroom when she sees unfamiliar classmates.","zh":"學生看到不熟悉的同學時，可能意識到自己在錯誤課室。"},{"en":"Realising a mistake is the first step towards correcting it.","zh":"意識到錯誤是改正它的第一步。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a moment of understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述理解的一刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"successively larger loops","meaning":"逐次擴大的環形路線","examples":[{"en":"The ant walks in successively larger loops while searching.","zh":"螞蟻搜尋時走出逐次擴大的環形路線。"},{"en":"Successively larger loops are circular paths that become bigger one after another.","zh":"successively larger loops 是一個接一個變大的圓形路徑。"},{"en":"A person looking for a lost key may search in successively larger circles around the desk.","zh":"尋找遺失鎖匙的人可能圍着書桌以逐次擴大的圓圈搜尋。"},{"en":"Expanding the search area increases the chance of finding a missed target.","zh":"擴大搜尋範圍會增加找到錯過目標的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a repeated pattern that grows in size.","zh":"這個短語描述尺寸逐漸增大的重複模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"find its way home","meaning":"找到回家的路","examples":[{"en":"The ant searches in loops to find its way home.","zh":"螞蟻以環形路線搜尋，以找到回家的路。"},{"en":"To find its way home means to discover the route back to where it lives or started.","zh":"find its way home 指找出回到住處或起點的路線。"},{"en":"A child lost in a park may use familiar trees and paths to find her way home.","zh":"在公園迷路的孩子可能使用熟悉樹木和小路找到回家的路。"},{"en":"Animals need this ability because food searches often take them away from safety.","zh":"動物需要這種能力，因為覓食常令牠們離開安全地方。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on returning to a familiar home place.","zh":"這個短語重點在回到熟悉的家或起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"whether...or...","meaning":"無論……還是……","examples":[{"en":"Whether returning to an anthill or a station, an animal must track its movement.","zh":"無論是返回蟻丘還是車站，動物都必須追蹤自己的移動。"},{"en":"Whether A or B means the statement is true in both situations.","zh":"whether A or B 指陳述在兩種情況中都成立。"},{"en":"Whether studying at home or in the library, students need quiet time to concentrate.","zh":"無論在家還是在圖書館溫習，學生都需要安靜時間集中精神。"},{"en":"This structure shows that different cases share the same requirement or result.","zh":"這個結構顯示不同情況共享同一要求或結果。"},{"en":"The phrase helps compare two possibilities under one idea.","zh":"這個短語幫助在同一想法下比較兩種可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"keep track of","meaning":"記錄；掌握……","examples":[{"en":"Animals must keep track of their own movements.","zh":"動物必須記錄自己的移動。"},{"en":"To keep track of something means to monitor, remember, or record it as it changes.","zh":"keep track of 某事，指隨着它改變而監察、記住或記錄它。"},{"en":"A student may keep track of homework deadlines in a planner.","zh":"學生可能在手帳中記錄功課限期。"},{"en":"If people do not keep track of their spending, they may run out of money unexpectedly.","zh":"如果人們不掌握自己的開支，可能會意外地用完錢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes staying aware of ongoing information.","zh":"這個短語描述持續掌握資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"one’s own movements","meaning":"自身的移動","examples":[{"en":"Path integration requires an awareness of one’s own movements.","zh":"路徑整合需要對自身移動有意識。"},{"en":"One’s own movements are the actions and changes in position made by one’s body.","zh":"one’s own movements 是自己身體所作出的動作和位置變化。"},{"en":"A dancer must be aware of her own movements to avoid hitting other performers.","zh":"舞者必須意識到自身的移動，以免撞到其他表演者。"},{"en":"Knowing how far and in what direction you moved helps you estimate where you are.","zh":"知道自己移動了多遠和朝甚麼方向，有助估計自己在哪裏。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on self-motion rather than outside landmarks.","zh":"這個短語重點在自我移動，而不是外部地標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"individual segments","meaning":"各個路段","examples":[{"en":"The traveller must remember which individual segments have been completed.","zh":"旅客必須記住哪些各個路段已完成。"},{"en":"Individual segments are separate parts of a route, task, or process.","zh":"individual segments 是路線、任務或過程中的分開部分。"},{"en":"A student writing an essay may divide it into individual segments such as introduction, examples, and conclusion.","zh":"學生寫文章時可能把它分成引言、例子和結論等各個部分。"},{"en":"Remembering each segment helps people know what has already been done and what remains.","zh":"記住每個部分幫助人知道已完成甚麼和還剩甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase breaks a larger whole into smaller parts.","zh":"這個短語把較大整體分成較小部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"gather data from","meaning":"從……收集資料","examples":[{"en":"The brain gathers data from the surrounding environment.","zh":"大腦從周圍環境收集資料。"},{"en":"To gather data from something means to collect information from that source.","zh":"gather data from 某物，指從該來源收集資訊。"},{"en":"A teacher may gather data from quizzes, homework, and class discussion.","zh":"老師可能從小測、功課和課堂討論中收集資料。"},{"en":"More sources of data can help people make better decisions.","zh":"更多資料來源可以幫助人作出更好決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes collecting useful information for understanding or action.","zh":"這個短語描述為理解或行動收集有用資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sights, sounds and smells","meaning":"景象、聲音和氣味","examples":[{"en":"The brain uses sights, sounds and smells during navigation.","zh":"大腦在導航期間使用景象、聲音和氣味。"},{"en":"Sights, sounds and smells are visual, auditory, and scent-based information from the environment.","zh":"sights, sounds and smells 是來自環境的視覺、聽覺和氣味資訊。"},{"en":"A student may recognise the canteen by the smell of food, the sound of chairs, and the sight of lunch queues.","zh":"學生可能透過食物氣味、椅子聲和午餐隊伍景象認出飯堂。"},{"en":"These sensory clues help people remember places more clearly.","zh":"這些感官線索幫助人更清楚記住地方。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to different senses working together.","zh":"這個短語指不同感官一起運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"muscle contractions","meaning":"肌肉收縮","examples":[{"en":"Muscle contractions provide information about bodily movement.","zh":"肌肉收縮提供關於身體移動的資訊。"},{"en":"Muscle contractions are the tightening actions of muscles when the body moves.","zh":"muscle contractions 是身體移動時肌肉收緊的動作。"},{"en":"When a student climbs stairs, muscle contractions in her legs help move her upward.","zh":"當學生上樓梯，腿部肌肉收縮幫助她向上移動。"},{"en":"The body can use these internal signals to estimate effort, distance, and direction.","zh":"身體可以使用這些內部訊號估計用力、距離和方向。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to physical movement signals from muscles.","zh":"這個短語指來自肌肉的身體移動訊號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a sense of time passing","meaning":"對時間流逝的感覺","examples":[{"en":"A sense of time passing helps the brain estimate distance.","zh":"對時間流逝的感覺幫助大腦估計距離。"},{"en":"A sense of time passing is the feeling of how much time has gone by.","zh":"sense of time passing 是對已過去多少時間的感覺。"},{"en":"A walker may think she has gone far because she feels she has been walking for twenty minutes.","zh":"行人可能因感覺已走了二十分鐘，而認為自己走了很遠。"},{"en":"Time cues help estimate distance when exact signs or maps are unavailable.","zh":"當沒有精確標誌或地圖，時間線索幫助估計距離。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an internal awareness of duration.","zh":"這個短語描述對持續時間的內在意識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"determine which way","meaning":"判斷……方向","examples":[{"en":"Sensory information helps determine which way the body has moved.","zh":"感官資訊幫助判斷身體朝哪個方向移動。"},{"en":"To determine which way means to work out the direction of movement or action.","zh":"determine which way 指判斷移動或行動的方向。"},{"en":"A cyclist may determine which way to turn by checking road signs and traffic flow.","zh":"單車手可能透過查看路牌和車流判斷應往哪邊轉。"},{"en":"Without enough information, people may choose the wrong direction.","zh":"沒有足夠資訊，人們可能選錯方向。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deciding or identifying direction.","zh":"這個短語描述決定或辨認方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"church spire","meaning":"教堂尖頂","examples":[{"en":"A church spire may serve as a memorable landmark.","zh":"教堂尖頂可以作為容易記住的地標。"},{"en":"A church spire is the tall pointed top of a church building.","zh":"church spire 是教堂建築上高而尖的頂部。"},{"en":"A traveller may use a church spire to recognise the centre of an old town.","zh":"旅客可能使用教堂尖頂認出舊城鎮中心。"},{"en":"Tall structures help navigation because they can be seen over smaller buildings.","zh":"高大結構有助導航，因為它們可在較小建築物上方被看見。"},{"en":"The phrase names a visible architectural feature.","zh":"這個短語指出一種可見建築特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sizzling sausages","meaning":"滋滋作響的香腸","examples":[{"en":"The smell of sizzling sausages may help someone recognise a location.","zh":"滋滋作響的香腸氣味可能幫助某人認出一個位置。"},{"en":"Sizzling sausages are sausages making a sharp frying sound as they cook.","zh":"sizzling sausages 是烹煮時發出尖細煎炸聲的香腸。"},{"en":"A student may recognise the school fair by the smell and sound of sizzling sausages.","zh":"學生可能透過滋滋作響的香腸聲和氣味認出學校嘉年華。"},{"en":"Strong food smells can become memory clues for places.","zh":"強烈食物氣味可以成為地方記憶線索。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a vivid example of sound and smell guiding memory.","zh":"這個短語給出聲音和氣味引導記憶的生動例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"vendor’s grill","meaning":"小販的烤架","examples":[{"en":"The smell from a vendor’s grill can become a navigational clue.","zh":"小販烤架傳出的氣味可以成為導航線索。"},{"en":"A vendor’s grill is a cooking surface used by a street seller to cook food.","zh":"vendor’s grill 是街頭小販用來烹調食物的烹煮表面。"},{"en":"A night-market visitor may remember a corner because of the smoke from a vendor’s grill.","zh":"夜市訪客可能因小販烤架的煙而記住某個街角。"},{"en":"Smells from food stalls can help people recognise where they have been.","zh":"食物攤檔的氣味可以幫助人認出自己曾到過哪裏。"},{"en":"The phrase connects street food with sensory navigation.","zh":"這個短語把街頭食物與感官導航連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"open courtyard","meaning":"開放式庭院","examples":[{"en":"An open courtyard may mark an important point in a journey.","zh":"開放式庭院可以標記旅程中的重要位置。"},{"en":"An open courtyard is an uncovered open space surrounded partly or fully by buildings.","zh":"open courtyard 是由建築部分或完全圍繞、沒有上蓋的開放空間。"},{"en":"Students may meet in an open courtyard between lessons because it is easy to find.","zh":"學生可能在課堂之間於開放式庭院見面，因為它容易找到。"},{"en":"Open spaces can serve as landmarks because they look different from narrow corridors or streets.","zh":"開放空間可以作為地標，因為它們看起來不同於狹窄走廊或街道。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a visible public or semi-public space.","zh":"這個短語描述可見的公共或半公共空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"snapshots of","meaning":"……的片段印象","examples":[{"en":"Memorable landmarks act as snapshots of different stages of a journey.","zh":"容易記住的地標就像旅程不同階段的片段印象。"},{"en":"Snapshots of something are brief mental images or records of particular moments.","zh":"snapshots of 某事，是特定時刻的簡短心理影像或記錄。"},{"en":"A student may keep snapshots of a school trip in her mind, such as the bus, beach, and museum.","zh":"學生可能在腦中保留學校旅行的片段印象，例如巴士、沙灘和博物館。"},{"en":"These snapshots help people remember the order of events or places.","zh":"這些片段印象幫助人記住事件或地點次序。"},{"en":"The phrase compares memory to quick photographs.","zh":"這個短語把記憶比作快速照片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"memorable junctures","meaning":"容易記住的關鍵節點","examples":[{"en":"Landmarks represent memorable junctures during a journey.","zh":"地標代表旅程中容易記住的關鍵節點。"},{"en":"Memorable junctures are important points in a route or process that are easy to remember.","zh":"memorable junctures 是路線或過程中容易記住的重要位置。"},{"en":"A bright mural at a turning can be a memorable juncture on the way to school.","zh":"轉角處的鮮明壁畫可以是上學路上容易記住的關鍵節點。"},{"en":"Remembering such points helps travellers divide a route into manageable sections.","zh":"記住這些位置幫助旅客把路線分成容易處理的部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes key moments or places that stand out.","zh":"這個短語描述突出的關鍵時刻或地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in addition to","meaning":"除……之外","examples":[{"en":"In addition to guidance, people use path integration and route following.","zh":"除了引導式導航外，人們也使用路徑整合和按路線導航。"},{"en":"In addition to means as well as, or besides something already mentioned.","zh":"in addition to 指除了已提到的某事之外，也包括其他。"},{"en":"In addition to textbooks, students can learn English through films and conversations.","zh":"除了教科書外，學生也可以透過電影和對話學英文。"},{"en":"The phrase adds extra information without replacing the first item.","zh":"這個短語加入額外資訊，而不是取代第一項。"},{"en":"It is useful when listing more than one method or factor.","zh":"它適合用於列出多於一種方法或因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"approach someone for help","meaning":"上前向某人求助","examples":[{"en":"A visitor may approach an office worker for help.","zh":"訪客可能上前向辦公室職員求助。"},{"en":"To approach someone for help means to go to that person and ask for assistance.","zh":"approach someone for help 指走向某人並請求協助。"},{"en":"A student may approach a librarian for help finding a reference book.","zh":"學生可能上前向圖書館員求助，以尋找參考書。"},{"en":"People often approach someone nearby when maps or signs are not enough.","zh":"當地圖或標誌不足，人們常向附近的人求助。"},{"en":"The phrase describes taking the first step to ask for support.","zh":"這個短語描述主動尋求支援的第一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"street corner","meaning":"街角","examples":[{"en":"You may ask for directions at a busy street corner.","zh":"你可能在繁忙街角問路。"},{"en":"A street corner is the place where two streets meet.","zh":"street corner 是兩條街道相交的地方。"},{"en":"Friends may agree to meet at the street corner outside a cinema.","zh":"朋友可能約在戲院外街角見面。"},{"en":"Street corners are useful for directions because they are clear turning points.","zh":"街角對指路有用，因為它們是清楚轉向點。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a common urban location.","zh":"這個短語指常見城市位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"walk straight down","meaning":"沿……一直向前行","examples":[{"en":"Walk straight down Fifth Avenue towards 47th Street.","zh":"沿 Fifth Avenue 一直向前行，朝 47th Street 前進。"},{"en":"To walk straight down a street means to continue forward along it without turning.","zh":"walk straight down 某街，指沿着它一直向前走，不轉彎。"},{"en":"A student may walk straight down the corridor until she sees the science lab.","zh":"學生可能沿走廊一直向前行，直到看見科學實驗室。"},{"en":"This instruction is easy to follow because it requires no decision at each corner.","zh":"這項指示容易跟隨，因為每個街角都不需要作決定。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a direct route instruction.","zh":"這個短語給出直接路線指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"turn left on","meaning":"在……左轉","examples":[{"en":"Turn left on 47th Street.","zh":"在 47th Street 左轉。"},{"en":"To turn left on a street means to change direction left when you reach that street.","zh":"turn left on 某街，指到達該街時向左改變方向。"},{"en":"A visitor may turn left on the road beside the library to reach the playground.","zh":"訪客可能在圖書館旁邊的道路左轉，到達操場。"},{"en":"Missing the correct left turn can send a traveller away from the route.","zh":"錯過正確左轉位可以令旅客偏離路線。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a specific turning instruction.","zh":"這個短語給出具體轉向指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"turn right on","meaning":"在……右轉","examples":[{"en":"Turn right on Park Avenue.","zh":"在 Park Avenue 右轉。"},{"en":"To turn right on a street means to change direction right when you reach that street.","zh":"turn right on 某街，指到達該街時向右改變方向。"},{"en":"A driver may turn right on the main road after passing the petrol station.","zh":"司機經過油站後可能在主幹道右轉。"},{"en":"Correct right turns help travellers follow a planned route accurately.","zh":"正確右轉幫助旅客準確跟隨計劃路線。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common route-following instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見的按路線導航指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"go through","meaning":"穿過……","examples":[{"en":"Go through the walkway under the building.","zh":"穿過大樓下方的通道。"},{"en":"To go through a place means to enter one side and come out the other side.","zh":"go through 某地方，指從一邊進入並從另一邊出來。"},{"en":"Students may go through the covered passage to reach the sports hall during rain.","zh":"下雨時，學生可能穿過有蓋通道到達體育館。"},{"en":"Going through a shortcut can save time but may confuse people if signs are poor.","zh":"穿過捷徑可以節省時間，但如果標誌差，可能令人困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes passing inside or across a space.","zh":"這個短語描述在某空間內部或之中穿過。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"intermediate points","meaning":"中途地點","examples":[{"en":"Route following uses directions for reaching intermediate points.","zh":"按路線導航使用到達中途地點的指示。"},{"en":"Intermediate points are places between the starting point and final destination.","zh":"intermediate points 是起點和最終目的地之間的地方。"},{"en":"On the way to a museum, a café and a bridge may be intermediate points.","zh":"前往博物館途中，咖啡店和橋可能是中途地點。"},{"en":"Remembering these points helps travellers check whether they are still on the right route.","zh":"記住這些地點幫助旅客檢查自己是否仍在正確路線上。"},{"en":"The phrase describes middle stages in a journey.","zh":"這個短語描述旅程中的中間階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"more precise than","meaning":"比……更精確","examples":[{"en":"Route following is more precise than general guidance.","zh":"按路線導航比一般引導更精確。"},{"en":"More precise than means more exact or detailed than something else.","zh":"more precise than 指比另一事物更準確或更詳細。"},{"en":"“Turn left at the bank” is more precise than “go that way.”","zh":"「在銀行左轉」比「往那邊走」更精確。"},{"en":"Precise directions reduce guessing and help people avoid wrong turns.","zh":"精確指示減少猜測，並幫助人避免轉錯彎。"},{"en":"The phrase compares levels of accuracy.","zh":"這個短語比較準確程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"forget the details","meaning":"忘記細節","examples":[{"en":"You may become lost if you forget the details of the route.","zh":"如果你忘記路線細節，可能會迷路。"},{"en":"To forget the details means to fail to remember the small but important parts.","zh":"forget the details 指未能記住細小但重要的部分。"},{"en":"A student may forget the details of a science experiment and mix the steps wrongly.","zh":"學生可能忘記科學實驗細節，並把步驟混錯。"},{"en":"Missing small details can make an otherwise good plan fail.","zh":"漏掉小細節可以令本來好的計劃失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that accuracy depends on remembering specifics.","zh":"這個短語提醒人準確性取決於記住具體內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take a wrong turn","meaning":"轉錯彎","examples":[{"en":"A traveller may take a wrong turn at an unfamiliar junction.","zh":"旅客可能在陌生路口轉錯彎。"},{"en":"To take a wrong turn means to turn onto the wrong road or path.","zh":"take a wrong turn 指轉入錯誤道路或小路。"},{"en":"A driver may take a wrong turn if two exits look almost the same.","zh":"如果兩個出口看起來幾乎一樣，司機可能轉錯彎。"},{"en":"One wrong turn can add time, create confusion, or lead someone away from the destination.","zh":"一次轉錯彎可以增加時間、造成混亂或令人遠離目的地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a navigation mistake.","zh":"這個短語描述導航錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the only way to recover","meaning":"唯一的補救方法","examples":[{"en":"The only way to recover may be to return to a familiar landmark.","zh":"唯一的補救方法可能是回到熟悉地標。"},{"en":"The only way to recover means the only method to correct a mistake or regain control.","zh":"the only way to recover 指改正錯誤或重新掌控情況的唯一方法。"},{"en":"If a student loses her essay file, the only way to recover may be to use an older backup.","zh":"如果學生遺失文章檔案，唯一補救方法可能是使用較舊備份。"},{"en":"When a route goes wrong, returning to something familiar can restore confidence.","zh":"當路線出錯，回到熟悉事物可以恢復信心。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the single practical solution left.","zh":"這個短語指出剩下的唯一實際解決方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"backtrack","meaning":"原路折返","examples":[{"en":"If you take a wrong turn, you may need to backtrack.","zh":"如果你轉錯彎，可能需要原路折返。"},{"en":"To backtrack means to go back along the way you came.","zh":"backtrack 指沿着來路返回。"},{"en":"A shopper may backtrack through the mall to find a shop she passed earlier.","zh":"購物者可能在商場中原路折返，以找到早前經過的商店。"},{"en":"Backtracking can cost time, but it helps people return to a known route.","zh":"原路折返可能花時間，但它幫助人回到已知路線。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reversing direction after a mistake.","zh":"這個短語描述出錯後反方向返回。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"familiar spot","meaning":"熟悉的地點","examples":[{"en":"You should backtrack until you reach a familiar spot.","zh":"你應原路折返，直到到達熟悉的地點。"},{"en":"A familiar spot is a place you recognise because you have seen or visited it before.","zh":"familiar spot 是你因曾見過或到過而認得的地方。"},{"en":"A student may wait at a familiar spot outside the school gate to meet her parents.","zh":"學生可能在校門外熟悉的地點等父母。"},{"en":"Familiar spots reduce anxiety because they help people rebuild their route.","zh":"熟悉地點減少焦慮，因為它們幫助人重新建立路線。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a recognised location.","zh":"這個短語指被認出的地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reference landmark","meaning":"參考地標","examples":[{"en":"A reference landmark indicates the general position of a destination.","zh":"參考地標指出目的地的大致位置。"},{"en":"A reference landmark is a place or object used to judge where another place is.","zh":"reference landmark 是用來判斷另一地方位置的地點或物件。"},{"en":"A tall library building can be a reference landmark for finding nearby classrooms.","zh":"高大的圖書館大樓可以作為尋找附近課室的參考地標。"},{"en":"Reference landmarks help people understand location even without exact street names.","zh":"參考地標幫助人即使沒有精確街名也能理解位置。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a landmark used for comparison and orientation.","zh":"這個短語描述用於比較和辨認方向的地標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"challenge the brain","meaning":"對大腦構成考驗","examples":[{"en":"Detailed route following can challenge the brain.","zh":"詳細按路線導航可以對大腦構成考驗。"},{"en":"To challenge the brain means to make the brain work hard to process or remember information.","zh":"challenge the brain 指令大腦努力處理或記住資訊。"},{"en":"A difficult puzzle can challenge the brain because it requires memory and logic.","zh":"困難謎題可以對大腦構成考驗，因為它需要記憶和邏輯。"},{"en":"Too many detailed directions can overload attention and cause mistakes.","zh":"太多詳細指示可以使注意力過載並造成錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mental difficulty or demand.","zh":"這個短語描述心理困難或要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"keep something in your head","meaning":"把……記在腦中","examples":[{"en":"You must keep several landmarks and directions in your head.","zh":"你必須把幾個地標和方向記在腦中。"},{"en":"To keep something in your head means to remember it without writing it down.","zh":"keep something in your head 指不用寫下來而記住它。"},{"en":"A waiter may keep several table orders in his head during a busy lunch.","zh":"侍應在繁忙午餐時段可能把幾張枱的訂單記在腦中。"},{"en":"If too much information must be remembered, mistakes become more likely.","zh":"如果要記住太多資訊，錯誤會更可能發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes relying on memory.","zh":"這個短語描述依靠記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the most detailed method","meaning":"最詳細的方法","examples":[{"en":"Route following is the most detailed navigation method.","zh":"按路線導航是最詳細的導航方法。"},{"en":"The most detailed method is the method that gives the greatest number of specific steps or pieces of information.","zh":"most detailed method 是提供最多具體步驟或資訊的方法。"},{"en":"A recipe with exact temperatures, times, and amounts is the most detailed method for baking a cake.","zh":"列出精確溫度、時間和分量的食譜，是烘焙蛋糕最詳細的方法。"},{"en":"Detailed methods can be accurate, but they may be harder to remember.","zh":"詳細方法可以準確，但可能較難記住。"},{"en":"The phrase compares how much information a method includes.","zh":"這個短語比較方法包含多少資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"most reliable","meaning":"最可靠的","examples":[{"en":"A detailed route is often the most reliable form of navigation.","zh":"詳細路線通常是最可靠的導航形式。"},{"en":"Most reliable means most likely to work correctly and consistently.","zh":"most reliable 指最有可能正確且穩定運作。"},{"en":"A timetable from the school office is usually more reliable than a rumour from classmates.","zh":"由校務處發出的時間表通常比同學間的傳聞更可靠。"},{"en":"Reliable methods reduce risk because people can depend on them.","zh":"可靠方法減少風險，因為人們可以依靠它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the option people can trust most.","zh":"這個短語描述最值得信任的選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be undone by","meaning":"因……而失效","examples":[{"en":"A good route can be undone by a simple memory lapse.","zh":"一條好路線可以因一次簡單短暫失憶而失效。"},{"en":"To be undone by something means to fail because of that problem.","zh":"be undone by 某事，指因該問題而失敗。"},{"en":"A strong essay can be undone by careless grammar mistakes in the final paragraph.","zh":"一篇強文章可能因最後一段粗心文法錯誤而失色。"},{"en":"One small error can ruin a plan if the plan depends on exact steps.","zh":"如果計劃依賴精確步驟，一個小錯誤可以毀掉計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how a weakness can cancel a strength.","zh":"這個短語顯示弱點如何抵消優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"routine memory lapses","meaning":"日常的短暫失憶","examples":[{"en":"Routine memory lapses can make a person miss a turning.","zh":"日常的短暫失憶可以令一個人錯過轉彎位。"},{"en":"Routine memory lapses are ordinary moments when someone briefly forgets something.","zh":"routine memory lapses 是某人短暫忘記事情的普通時刻。"},{"en":"A student may have a routine memory lapse and forget where she put her notebook.","zh":"學生可能有日常短暫失憶，忘記把筆記本放在哪裏。"},{"en":"Small memory failures can cause larger problems when timing or directions matter.","zh":"當時間或方向重要，小記憶失誤可以造成較大問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes common, everyday forgetfulness.","zh":"這個短語描述常見日常健忘。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cognitive memory","meaning":"認知記憶","examples":[{"en":"Path integration places less pressure on cognitive memory.","zh":"路徑整合對認知記憶造成較少壓力。"},{"en":"Cognitive memory is the mental ability to store, process, and recall information.","zh":"cognitive memory 是儲存、處理和回想資訊的心理能力。"},{"en":"A student uses cognitive memory when remembering vocabulary and applying it in a sentence.","zh":"學生記住詞彙並在句子中應用時，就在使用認知記憶。"},{"en":"When instructions are too detailed, cognitive memory may become overloaded.","zh":"當指示太詳細，認知記憶可能過載。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to memory used in thinking and decision-making.","zh":"這個短語指思考和決策中使用的記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be less burdened","meaning":"負擔較輕","examples":[{"en":"Memory is less burdened when only general directions are required.","zh":"當只需要大致方向時，記憶負擔較輕。"},{"en":"To be less burdened means to have less pressure, load, or difficulty.","zh":"be less burdened 指承受較少壓力、負荷或困難。"},{"en":"Students are less burdened when homework instructions are clear and short.","zh":"當功課指示清楚而簡短，學生負擔較輕。"},{"en":"Reducing unnecessary detail makes a task easier to manage.","zh":"減少不必要細節令任務較容易處理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a lighter mental or practical load.","zh":"這個短語描述較輕的心理或實際負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"deal with only","meaning":"只需處理……","examples":[{"en":"The brain has to deal with only a few general instructions.","zh":"大腦只需處理少量概括指示。"},{"en":"To deal with only something means to handle just that limited amount or type of information.","zh":"deal with only 某事，指只處理有限數量或類型的資訊。"},{"en":"A cashier may deal with only card payments if the shop stops accepting cash.","zh":"如果商店停止收現金，收銀員可能只需處理信用卡付款。"},{"en":"Fewer items to handle can reduce mistakes and stress.","zh":"要處理的項目較少，可以減少錯誤和壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a limited task or reduced load.","zh":"這個短語強調任務有限或負荷減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"general instructions","meaning":"概括指示","examples":[{"en":"Path integration uses a small number of general instructions.","zh":"路徑整合使用少量概括指示。"},{"en":"General instructions are broad directions that do not include every small detail.","zh":"general instructions 是不包含每個小細節的大方向指示。"},{"en":"“Keep walking towards the river” is a general instruction, while “turn left at the bank” is more detailed.","zh":"「一直朝河走」是概括指示，而「在銀行左轉」則更詳細。"},{"en":"General instructions are easier to remember but may be less exact.","zh":"概括指示較容易記住，但可能較不精確。"},{"en":"The phrase describes simple guidance rather than a full step-by-step route.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單引導，而不是完整逐步路線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rely fundamentally on","meaning":"從根本上依賴……","examples":[{"en":"Path integration relies fundamentally on a sense of bodily direction.","zh":"路徑整合從根本上依賴身體方向感。"},{"en":"To rely fundamentally on something means to depend on it as the basic foundation.","zh":"rely fundamentally on 某事，指把它作為基本基礎來依靠。"},{"en":"Reading comprehension relies fundamentally on understanding vocabulary and sentence structure.","zh":"閱讀理解從根本上依賴理解詞彙和句子結構。"},{"en":"If the foundation is weak, the whole skill becomes less reliable.","zh":"如果基礎薄弱，整項技能會變得較不可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the core thing a process depends on.","zh":"這個短語指出某過程依賴的核心事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"general direction of movement","meaning":"移動的大致方向","examples":[{"en":"The brain tracks the body’s general direction of movement.","zh":"大腦追蹤身體移動的大致方向。"},{"en":"General direction of movement means the broad way the body is moving, such as north, south, left, or forward.","zh":"general direction of movement 指身體移動的大方向，例如北、南、左或向前。"},{"en":"A hiker may remember the general direction of movement even if she forgets each tree or rock.","zh":"行山者即使忘記每棵樹或石頭，也可能記得移動的大致方向。"},{"en":"Knowing broad direction helps people estimate where they may be after walking.","zh":"知道大方向幫助人估計走路後可能在哪裏。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on overall movement rather than exact steps.","zh":"這個短語重點在整體移動，而不是精確步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have access to","meaning":"可以取得……","examples":[{"en":"We always have access to information about our own movement.","zh":"我們總是可以取得關於自身移動的資訊。"},{"en":"To have access to something means to be able to use, reach, or obtain it.","zh":"have access to 某物，指能夠使用、接觸或取得它。"},{"en":"Students have access to online dictionaries when the school allows phones for learning.","zh":"當學校容許用手機學習，學生可以取得網上字典。"},{"en":"Access to useful information makes problem-solving easier.","zh":"可以取得有用資訊會令解難更容易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes availability.","zh":"這個短語描述可取得性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"sensory inputs","meaning":"感官輸入","examples":[{"en":"The brain combines several sensory inputs during navigation.","zh":"大腦在導航期間結合幾種感官輸入。"},{"en":"Sensory inputs are pieces of information received through the senses, such as sight, sound, smell, and body movement.","zh":"sensory inputs 是透過感官接收的資訊，例如視覺、聲音、氣味和身體移動。"},{"en":"A driver uses sensory inputs from mirrors, engine sounds, and road signs.","zh":"司機使用來自倒後鏡、引擎聲和路牌的感官輸入。"},{"en":"Combining different inputs helps the brain make a more accurate judgement.","zh":"結合不同輸入幫助大腦作出更準確判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to information entering the brain through the body’s senses.","zh":"這個短語指透過身體感官進入大腦的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"nevertheless","meaning":"儘管如此","examples":[{"en":"Nevertheless, people often give detailed route-following directions.","zh":"儘管如此，人們常給出詳細的按路線導航指示。"},{"en":"Nevertheless means despite what has just been said.","zh":"nevertheless 指儘管剛才說了某事，情況仍然如此。"},{"en":"The exam is difficult; nevertheless, students can improve with steady practice.","zh":"考試很難；儘管如此，學生可以透過穩定練習進步。"},{"en":"The word introduces a contrast that does not cancel the previous point.","zh":"這個字引出對比，但不取消前一點。"},{"en":"It is useful when the next idea is surprising after the first idea.","zh":"當下一個想法在第一個想法之後顯得意外時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in part because","meaning":"部分原因是","examples":[{"en":"People prefer detailed directions in part because cities are complex.","zh":"人們偏好詳細指示，部分原因是城市複雜。"},{"en":"In part because means partly because, but not only because.","zh":"in part because 指部分原因是，但不是唯一原因。"},{"en":"Students may like group work in part because it makes difficult tasks feel less lonely.","zh":"學生可能喜歡小組工作，部分原因是它令困難任務感覺不那麼孤單。"},{"en":"The phrase shows one reason among several possible reasons.","zh":"這個短語顯示幾個可能原因中的一個。"},{"en":"It gives a careful explanation rather than a single complete cause.","zh":"它給出謹慎解釋，而不是單一完整原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"man-made surroundings","meaning":"人造環境","examples":[{"en":"General directional advice may fail in complex, man-made surroundings.","zh":"在複雜人造環境中，一般方向建議可能失效。"},{"en":"Man-made surroundings are environments created or heavily shaped by people, such as cities, malls, or stations.","zh":"man-made surroundings 是由人創造或大幅塑造的環境，例如城市、商場或車站。"},{"en":"A shopping centre is a man-made surrounding with corridors, shops, escalators, and exits.","zh":"商場是人造環境，有走廊、商店、扶手電梯和出口。"},{"en":"These surroundings can confuse travellers because many parts look similar.","zh":"這些環境可以令旅客困惑，因為許多部分看起來相似。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts built environments with natural landscapes.","zh":"這個短語把建成環境與自然景觀作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rely on your memory","meaning":"依靠記憶","examples":[{"en":"On a later visit, you may rely on your memory to get around.","zh":"之後再到訪時，你可能依靠記憶四處走動。"},{"en":"To rely on your memory means to depend on what you remember rather than on outside help.","zh":"rely on your memory 指依靠自己記得的東西，而不是外部幫助。"},{"en":"A student may rely on her memory to find the exam room after visiting it once.","zh":"學生去過一次考試室後，可能依靠記憶找到它。"},{"en":"Memory becomes more useful when a place has been visited several times.","zh":"當地方去過幾次，記憶會變得更有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using remembered information for guidance.","zh":"這個短語描述使用記住的資訊作引導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in various combinations","meaning":"以不同組合","examples":[{"en":"People use the three navigation methods in various combinations.","zh":"人們以不同組合使用三種導航方法。"},{"en":"In various combinations means mixed together in different ways.","zh":"in various combinations 指以不同方式混合在一起。"},{"en":"Students may study with notes, videos, past papers, or these tools in various combinations.","zh":"學生可能用筆記、影片、歷屆試題，或以不同組合使用這些工具來學習。"},{"en":"Combining methods allows people to adjust to different needs and situations.","zh":"組合方法讓人能因應不同需要和情況作調整。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses flexible mixing.","zh":"這個短語強調靈活混合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"deliver concrete directions","meaning":"提供具體方向","examples":[{"en":"The different navigation systems deliver concrete directions.","zh":"不同導航系統提供具體方向。"},{"en":"To deliver concrete directions means to provide clear, practical instructions about where to go.","zh":"deliver concrete directions 指提供清楚、實用的前往指示。"},{"en":"A receptionist delivers concrete directions when she says, “Take the lift to the third floor, then turn right.”","zh":"接待員說「乘電梯到三樓，然後右轉」時，就是提供具體方向。"},{"en":"Concrete directions reduce guessing because they tell people what to do next.","zh":"具體方向減少猜測，因為它們告訴人下一步做甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes useful, specific guidance.","zh":"這個短語描述有用而具體的引導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"an image of the real world","meaning":"現實世界的影像","examples":[{"en":"A cognitive map may appear to be an image of the real world.","zh":"認知地圖可能看似現實世界的影像。"},{"en":"An image of the real world is a mental or visual representation of actual places and objects.","zh":"image of the real world 是對實際地方和物件的心理或視覺呈現。"},{"en":"A child may draw an image of the real world by showing her home, school, and park on paper.","zh":"孩子可能在紙上畫出家、學校和公園，形成現實世界的影像。"},{"en":"Such images help people think about places even when they are not physically there.","zh":"這些影像幫助人即使不在現場也能思考地方。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a representation, not the real place itself.","zh":"這個短語描述一種呈現，而不是實際地方本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a kind of road map","meaning":"一種道路地圖","examples":[{"en":"Some people imagine a kind of road map in the brain.","zh":"有些人想像大腦中有一種道路地圖。"},{"en":"A kind of road map means something like a map that shows routes and places.","zh":"a kind of road map 指像顯示路線和地方的地圖一樣的東西。"},{"en":"A student may imagine a kind of road map from the bus stop to the school library.","zh":"學生可能想像由巴士站到學校圖書館的一種道路地圖。"},{"en":"This image helps explain navigation, but the brain may not store places exactly like a paper map.","zh":"這個影像有助解釋導航，但大腦未必像紙本地圖那樣精確儲存地方。"},{"en":"The phrase is a comparison used to simplify a mental process.","zh":"這個短語是用來簡化心理過程的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"symbols for","meaning":"代表……的符號","examples":[{"en":"A conventional map uses symbols for stations and buildings.","zh":"傳統地圖使用代表車站和建築物的符號。"},{"en":"Symbols for something are marks or pictures that represent it.","zh":"symbols for 某物，是代表它的標記或圖像。"},{"en":"A school map may use a small book symbol for the library.","zh":"學校地圖可能使用小書本符號代表圖書館。"},{"en":"Symbols save space and make maps easier to read quickly.","zh":"符號節省空間，並令地圖更容易快速閱讀。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to visual signs that stand for real things.","zh":"這個短語指代表真實事物的視覺標誌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the portion of memory that","meaning":"負責……的記憶部分","examples":[{"en":"The cognitive map is the portion of memory that controls navigation.","zh":"認知地圖是負責控制導航的記憶部分。"},{"en":"The portion of memory that does something is the part of memory responsible for that function.","zh":"portion of memory that 做某事，是負責該功能的記憶部分。"},{"en":"A student may use the portion of memory that stores vocabulary when writing an essay.","zh":"學生寫文章時，可能使用負責儲存詞彙的記憶部分。"},{"en":"Different memory functions help people remember places, words, faces, and routines.","zh":"不同記憶功能幫助人記住地方、詞語、面孔和日常程序。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a specific part of memory by its job.","zh":"這個短語透過功能指出記憶的特定部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"control navigation","meaning":"控制導航","examples":[{"en":"Part of human memory helps control navigation.","zh":"人類記憶的一部分幫助控制導航。"},{"en":"To control navigation means to manage how someone finds direction and moves through space.","zh":"control navigation 指管理某人如何辨認方向並在空間中移動。"},{"en":"A map app controls navigation by choosing routes and warning drivers about turns.","zh":"地圖應用程式透過選擇路線和提醒司機轉彎來控制導航。"},{"en":"In the brain, memory helps control navigation by storing landmarks and movement patterns.","zh":"在大腦中，記憶透過儲存地標和移動模式來幫助控制導航。"},{"en":"The phrase describes managing the process of wayfinding.","zh":"這個短語描述管理尋路過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"cognitive map","meaning":"認知地圖","examples":[{"en":"A cognitive map represents spatial relationships in the mind.","zh":"認知地圖在腦中呈現空間關係。"},{"en":"A cognitive map is a mental representation of places and how they relate to one another.","zh":"cognitive map 是對地方及其相互關係的心理呈現。"},{"en":"A student may have a cognitive map of her school, knowing where the hall, canteen, and classrooms are.","zh":"學生可能有學校的認知地圖，知道禮堂、飯堂和課室在哪裏。"},{"en":"Cognitive maps help people travel without checking a physical map every minute.","zh":"認知地圖幫助人不必每分鐘查看實體地圖也能行走。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to mental knowledge of space.","zh":"這個短語指對空間的心理知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"map metaphor","meaning":"地圖比喻","examples":[{"en":"The map metaphor provides a convenient explanation of spatial memory.","zh":"地圖比喻為空間記憶提供方便解釋。"},{"en":"A map metaphor is a comparison that explains memory as if it were a map.","zh":"map metaphor 是把記憶解釋成像地圖一樣的比較。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a filing-cabinet metaphor to explain how notes are organised.","zh":"老師可能使用文件櫃比喻來解釋筆記如何組織。"},{"en":"Metaphors make difficult ideas easier to understand, but they may not be perfectly accurate.","zh":"比喻令困難想法更容易理解，但未必完全準確。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a helpful comparison, not a literal fact.","zh":"這個短語描述有幫助的比較，而不是字面事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"obviously seductive","meaning":"顯然很有吸引力","examples":[{"en":"The map metaphor is obviously seductive because it seems easy to understand.","zh":"地圖比喻顯然很有吸引力，因為它似乎容易理解。"},{"en":"Obviously seductive means clearly attractive or tempting, especially because it feels simple.","zh":"obviously seductive 指明顯吸引人或誘人，尤其因為它感覺簡單。"},{"en":"A quick study trick may be obviously seductive if it promises high marks with little effort.","zh":"如果快速學習技巧承諾少努力得高分，它可能顯然很有吸引力。"},{"en":"Attractive explanations can be misleading when they hide complexity.","zh":"有吸引力的解釋若隱藏複雜性，可能會誤導。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that something appealing may not be fully accurate.","zh":"這個短語提醒人，吸引人的東西未必完全準確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"present geographic information","meaning":"呈現地理資料","examples":[{"en":"Maps present geographic information in a visual form.","zh":"地圖以視覺形式呈現地理資料。"},{"en":"To present geographic information means to show facts about places, distances, and locations.","zh":"present geographic information 指展示關於地方、距離和位置的事實。"},{"en":"A school map presents geographic information by showing classrooms, exits, and playgrounds.","zh":"學校地圖透過顯示課室、出口和操場來呈現地理資料。"},{"en":"Visual information helps people compare locations quickly.","zh":"視覺資訊幫助人快速比較位置。"},{"en":"The phrase describes showing place-based data clearly.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚展示地點相關資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"convenient visual inspection","meaning":"方便的視覺查閱","examples":[{"en":"A map allows geographic information to be examined through convenient visual inspection.","zh":"地圖讓人透過方便的視覺查閱檢視地理資料。"},{"en":"Convenient visual inspection means easy checking by looking at something.","zh":"convenient visual inspection 指透過觀看輕鬆查核某物。"},{"en":"A timetable on a classroom wall allows convenient visual inspection of lesson times.","zh":"課室牆上的時間表讓人方便地以視覺查閱課堂時間。"},{"en":"When information can be checked visually, people do not need to remember every detail.","zh":"當資訊可以用視覺方式查核，人們不需要記住每個細節。"},{"en":"The phrase describes quick and easy looking-based checking.","zh":"這個短語描述快速而方便的觀看式查核。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be developed before writing","meaning":"在文字出現前已被發展","examples":[{"en":"In many cultures, maps were developed before writing.","zh":"在許多文化中，地圖在文字出現前已被發展。"},{"en":"To be developed before writing means to appear or be created earlier than written language.","zh":"be developed before writing 指比書面語言更早出現或被創造。"},{"en":"A community may use drawings of rivers and paths before it develops a written record system.","zh":"社群可能在發展文字記錄系統前，先使用河流和小路圖。"},{"en":"Practical needs, such as travel and hunting, can lead to maps before formal writing exists.","zh":"旅行和狩獵等實際需要，可以在正式文字存在前促成地圖出現。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the historical order of two inventions.","zh":"這個短語比較兩項發明的歷史先後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"almost every society","meaning":"幾乎每個社會","examples":[{"en":"Maps are used in almost every society today.","zh":"今天幾乎每個社會都使用地圖。"},{"en":"Almost every society means nearly all communities or organised human groups.","zh":"almost every society 指幾乎所有社群或有組織的人類群體。"},{"en":"Almost every society needs some way to show roads, land, or important buildings.","zh":"幾乎每個社會都需要某種方式顯示道路、土地或重要建築。"},{"en":"A practice found in nearly all societies may reflect a common human need.","zh":"幾乎所有社會都有的做法，可能反映共同人類需要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses very wide use across cultures.","zh":"這個短語強調跨文化的廣泛使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"derive from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"Maps may derive from a universal form of spatial thinking.","zh":"地圖可能源自一種普遍的空間思維形式。"},{"en":"To derive from something means to come from it or have it as an origin.","zh":"derive from 某物，指來自它或以它為起源。"},{"en":"Many English words derive from Latin or French.","zh":"許多英文詞源自拉丁語或法語。"},{"en":"Knowing where something derives from can explain why it has its present form.","zh":"知道某物源自哪裏，可以解釋它為何有現在形式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes origin or source.","zh":"這個短語描述起源或來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a universal way","meaning":"一種普遍方式","examples":[{"en":"Spatial memory may follow a universal way of organising information.","zh":"空間記憶可能遵循一種普遍方式來組織資訊。"},{"en":"A universal way is a method or pattern shared widely by people across cultures.","zh":"universal way 是跨文化廣泛共享的方法或模式。"},{"en":"Using left and right to describe direction may be a fairly universal way of organising space.","zh":"使用左和右描述方向，可能是相當普遍的空間組織方式。"},{"en":"If a way is universal, it suggests a common human pattern rather than one local habit.","zh":"如果某方式是普遍的，它暗示共同人類模式，而不是單一本地習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something broadly shared.","zh":"這個短語描述被廣泛共享的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"spatial-memory networks","meaning":"空間記憶網絡","examples":[{"en":"Spatial-memory networks help humans understand physical relationships.","zh":"空間記憶網絡幫助人類理解實體關係。"},{"en":"Spatial-memory networks are connected brain systems that store and process information about places and space.","zh":"spatial-memory networks 是儲存和處理地方與空間資訊的相連大腦系統。"},{"en":"A student uses spatial-memory networks when remembering where classrooms are in relation to the hall.","zh":"學生記得課室與禮堂的位置關係時，就是在使用空間記憶網絡。"},{"en":"These networks help people move around without seeing the whole route at once.","zh":"這些網絡幫助人即使不能一次看見整條路線，也能四處移動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to brain systems for place-based memory.","zh":"這個短語指處理地點記憶的大腦系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be wired","meaning":"以特定方式連接","examples":[{"en":"Human spatial-memory networks may be wired in similar ways.","zh":"人類空間記憶網絡可能以相似方式連接。"},{"en":"To be wired in a certain way means to be connected or organised in that way, especially in the brain.","zh":"be wired in 某方式，指以該方式連接或組織，尤其是在大腦中。"},{"en":"Some people seem wired to notice sounds quickly, while others notice visual details first.","zh":"有些人似乎天生較快注意聲音，而另一些則先注意視覺細節。"},{"en":"How a system is wired affects how it processes information.","zh":"系統如何連接會影響它如何處理資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes internal organisation or connection.","zh":"這個短語描述內部組織或連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the notion of","meaning":"……這個觀念","examples":[{"en":"The notion of a literal map in the brain may be misleading.","zh":"大腦中有實際地圖這個觀念可能令人誤解。"},{"en":"The notion of something is the idea or belief about it.","zh":"notion of 某事，是關於它的想法或信念。"},{"en":"The notion of learning only by memorising is too narrow for modern education.","zh":"只靠背誦學習這個觀念對現代教育來說太狹窄。"},{"en":"Some notions are attractive because they are simple, but they may hide complexity.","zh":"有些觀念因為簡單而吸引，但可能隱藏複雜性。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an idea for discussion or criticism.","zh":"這個短語引出要討論或批評的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"literal map","meaning":"實際存在的地圖","examples":[{"en":"The brain probably does not contain a literal map of the surroundings.","zh":"大腦很可能不包含周圍環境的實際地圖。"},{"en":"A literal map is an actual map, not just a comparison or metaphor.","zh":"literal map 是真正的地圖，而不只是比較或比喻。"},{"en":"A paper map on a classroom wall is a literal map, but a student’s memory of the school is not.","zh":"課室牆上的紙本地圖是實際地圖，但學生對學校的記憶不是。"},{"en":"Confusing a metaphor with a literal map can lead to wrong assumptions about the brain.","zh":"把比喻與實際地圖混淆，可能導致對大腦的錯誤假設。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that something is real and map-like, not symbolic.","zh":"這個短語強調某物是真實且像地圖的，而不是象徵性的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be misleading","meaning":"可能令人誤解","examples":[{"en":"Describing spatial memory as a real map may be misleading.","zh":"把空間記憶描述為真正地圖可能令人誤解。"},{"en":"To be misleading means to give people a wrong idea or make them misunderstand.","zh":"be misleading 指給人錯誤想法或令人誤會。"},{"en":"A sign can be misleading if it points left but the entrance is actually on the right.","zh":"如果標誌指向左邊，但入口其實在右邊，它可能令人誤解。"},{"en":"Misleading explanations can feel simple while hiding important differences.","zh":"誤導性解釋可能感覺簡單，卻隱藏重要差異。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that something may guide people towards a false conclusion.","zh":"這個短語提醒某事可能把人導向錯誤結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a growing body of research","meaning":"日益增加的大量研究","examples":[{"en":"A growing body of research challenges the literal-map theory.","zh":"日益增加的大量研究挑戰實際地圖理論。"},{"en":"A growing body of research means an increasing amount of studies and evidence.","zh":"growing body of research 指越來越多研究和證據。"},{"en":"A growing body of research shows that sleep affects learning and memory.","zh":"日益增加的大量研究顯示睡眠影響學習和記憶。"},{"en":"When more studies point in the same direction, an old idea may need revision.","zh":"當更多研究指向同一方向，舊想法可能需要修訂。"},{"en":"The phrase describes accumulating academic evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸累積的學術證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"imply that","meaning":"顯示；意味著","examples":[{"en":"Recent studies imply that the cognitive map is mainly a metaphor.","zh":"近期研究顯示認知地圖主要是一種比喻。"},{"en":"To imply that something is true means to suggest it without saying it directly or absolutely.","zh":"imply that 某事為真，指不直接或絕對地說出，而是暗示它。"},{"en":"A student’s repeated lateness may imply that the bus route is unreliable.","zh":"學生反覆遲到可能意味著巴士路線不可靠。"},{"en":"Evidence can imply a conclusion before it fully proves it.","zh":"證據在完全證明某結論前，已可以暗示它。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests meaning based on clues.","zh":"這個短語描述基於線索的意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"mostly a metaphor","meaning":"主要是一種比喻","examples":[{"en":"The cognitive map is probably mostly a metaphor.","zh":"認知地圖很可能主要是一種比喻。"},{"en":"Mostly a metaphor means mainly a comparison used to explain something, not a literal description.","zh":"mostly a metaphor 指主要是用來解釋某事的比較，而不是字面描述。"},{"en":"Calling the classroom a “second home” is mostly a metaphor, not a claim that students live there.","zh":"把課室稱為「第二個家」主要是一種比喻，不是說學生住在那裏。"},{"en":"Metaphors can help understanding, but they may oversimplify complex processes.","zh":"比喻可以幫助理解，但可能過度簡化複雜過程。"},{"en":"The phrase warns readers not to take a comparison too literally.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者不要把比較理解得太字面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"hierarchical structure","meaning":"階層式結構","examples":[{"en":"Spatial memory may have a hierarchical structure of relationships.","zh":"空間記憶可能具有關係的階層式結構。"},{"en":"A hierarchical structure is an arrangement with larger levels above smaller levels.","zh":"hierarchical structure 是較大層級在上、較小層級在下的安排。"},{"en":"A school timetable has a hierarchy: term, week, day, and lesson.","zh":"學校時間表有階層：學期、星期、日子和課堂。"},{"en":"Hierarchical organisation helps people manage complex information by grouping it.","zh":"階層式組織透過分組幫助人管理複雜資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes layered structure.","zh":"這個短語描述分層結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"relationships between places","meaning":"地點之間的關係","examples":[{"en":"The brain may store relationships between places rather than exact maps.","zh":"大腦可能儲存地點之間的關係，而不是精確地圖。"},{"en":"Relationships between places are the ways locations connect, such as distance, direction, or order.","zh":"relationships between places 是位置如何連接，例如距離、方向或次序。"},{"en":"A student may remember that the library is beside the hall and below the staff room.","zh":"學生可能記得圖書館在禮堂旁邊，並在教員室下方。"},{"en":"Knowing relationships between places can guide movement even without a perfect map.","zh":"知道地點之間的關係，即使沒有完美地圖也能引導移動。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on connections, not isolated locations.","zh":"這個短語重點在連繫，而不是孤立位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"envision the large scale","meaning":"想像整體大範圍","examples":[{"en":"You first envision the large scale and general direction.","zh":"你首先想像整體大範圍和大致方向。"},{"en":"To envision the large scale means to imagine the broad overall layout before focusing on details.","zh":"envision the large scale 指先想像廣闊整體布局，再集中於細節。"},{"en":"Before writing an essay, a student may envision the large scale by deciding the main argument and sections.","zh":"寫文章前，學生可能透過決定主要論點和段落來想像大範圍結構。"},{"en":"Seeing the big picture helps people avoid getting trapped in small details too early.","zh":"看見整體圖像幫助人避免太早被小細節困住。"},{"en":"The phrase describes thinking about the overall structure first.","zh":"這個短語描述先思考整體結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"visualise the general direction","meaning":"想像大致方向","examples":[{"en":"You visualise the general direction of the station.","zh":"你想像車站的大致方向。"},{"en":"To visualise the general direction means to form a mental image of the broad way to go.","zh":"visualise the general direction 指在腦中形成應往哪個大方向走的影像。"},{"en":"A visitor may visualise the general direction of the hotel before checking the exact street.","zh":"訪客可能在查精確街道前，先想像酒店的大致方向。"},{"en":"Visualising direction helps people begin moving even before all details are clear.","zh":"想像方向幫助人即使細節未清楚，也能開始移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes imagining a broad route in the mind.","zh":"這個短語描述在腦中想像大致路線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"within that system","meaning":"在該系統之內","examples":[{"en":"Within that system, you recall a more detailed route.","zh":"在該系統之內，你回想起一條更詳細路線。"},{"en":"Within that system means inside or as part of the larger structure just mentioned.","zh":"within that system 指在剛提到的較大結構內或作為其中一部分。"},{"en":"A school has a timetable system; within that system, each class has its own lesson plan.","zh":"學校有時間表制度；在該系統之內，每班有自己的課堂計劃。"},{"en":"Larger structures help organise smaller details.","zh":"較大結構幫助組織較小細節。"},{"en":"The phrase links a detail to a broader framework.","zh":"這個短語把細節連到更廣框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"imagine the route to","meaning":"想像前往……的路線","examples":[{"en":"You imagine the route to the last place you remember.","zh":"你想像前往你記得的最後一個地方的路線。"},{"en":"To imagine the route to a place means to picture in your mind how to get there.","zh":"imagine the route to 某地，指在腦中想像如何到達那裏。"},{"en":"A student may imagine the route to the exam room before leaving home.","zh":"學生可能在離家前想像前往考試室的路線。"},{"en":"Imagining a route can help reduce anxiety and guide first steps.","zh":"想像路線可以幫助減少焦慮並引導第一步。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mental planning before or during movement.","zh":"這個短語描述移動前或移動期間的心理規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"nearby surroundings","meaning":"附近環境","examples":[{"en":"You then examine your nearby surroundings.","zh":"然後你查看附近環境。"},{"en":"Nearby surroundings are the places, objects, and signs close to where you are.","zh":"nearby surroundings 是靠近你所在位置的地方、物件和標誌。"},{"en":"A visitor may check nearby surroundings for a bus stop, street sign, or shop name.","zh":"訪客可能查看附近環境中有沒有巴士站、街牌或店名。"},{"en":"Looking carefully at what is nearby can help connect memory with the real environment.","zh":"仔細查看附近事物可以幫助把記憶與真實環境連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the immediate area around someone.","zh":"這個短語指某人周圍的即時範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"pick out","meaning":"辨認出；挑出","examples":[{"en":"You pick out a recognisable shopfront or street corner.","zh":"你辨認出一個容易辨認的店舖門面或街角。"},{"en":"To pick out something means to identify or select it from among other things.","zh":"pick out 某物，指從其他事物中辨認或選出它。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to pick out the main verb in a long sentence.","zh":"老師可能要求學生在長句中挑出主要動詞。"},{"en":"Picking out a familiar feature helps people make sense of a confusing scene.","zh":"辨認出熟悉特徵幫助人理解令人困惑的場景。"},{"en":"The phrase describes noticing and choosing something specific.","zh":"這個短語描述注意並選出具體事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"recognisable shopfront","meaning":"容易辨認的店舖門面","examples":[{"en":"A recognisable shopfront can guide you towards a familiar location.","zh":"容易辨認的店舖門面可以引導你前往熟悉位置。"},{"en":"A recognisable shopfront is the front of a shop that is easy to identify.","zh":"recognisable shopfront 是容易辨認的店舖正面。"},{"en":"A bright bakery window may be a recognisable shopfront on the way to school.","zh":"明亮的麵包店櫥窗可能是上學路上容易辨認的店舖門面。"},{"en":"Recognisable features help travellers know they are near a remembered place.","zh":"容易辨認的特徵幫助旅客知道自己接近記得的地方。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a visible and memorable shop exterior.","zh":"這個短語描述可見且容易記住的店舖外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"send someone towards","meaning":"引導某人前往……","examples":[{"en":"A local landmark can send you towards the place you remember.","zh":"本地地標可以引導你前往你記得的地方。"},{"en":"To send someone towards a place means to guide or lead them in that direction.","zh":"send someone towards 某地，指引導或帶領某人朝該方向前進。"},{"en":"A school sign can send visitors towards the main office.","zh":"學校標誌可以引導訪客前往校務處。"},{"en":"Clear cues can direct people without needing a long explanation.","zh":"清楚線索可以不用長篇解釋也引導人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something acting as a guide.","zh":"這個短語描述某物起引導作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"nested scheme","meaning":"嵌套式架構","examples":[{"en":"Spatial information may be arranged in a hierarchical, nested scheme.","zh":"空間資訊可能被安排成階層式、嵌套式架構。"},{"en":"A nested scheme is an arrangement in which smaller parts sit inside larger parts.","zh":"nested scheme 是較小部分置於較大部分之內的安排。"},{"en":"A school timetable can be nested: lessons inside days, days inside weeks, and weeks inside terms.","zh":"學校時間表可以是嵌套式：課堂在日子內，日子在星期內，星期在學期內。"},{"en":"Nesting helps people manage complex information by grouping related details together.","zh":"嵌套幫助人透過把相關細節分組來管理複雜資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a layered structure of information.","zh":"這個短語描述資訊的分層結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"positions and distances","meaning":"位置和距離","examples":[{"en":"The brain stores relative positions and distances between places.","zh":"大腦儲存地點之間的相對位置和距離。"},{"en":"Positions and distances are where places are and how far apart they are.","zh":"positions and distances 是地方在哪裏以及彼此相隔多遠。"},{"en":"A student may remember the canteen’s position beside the hall and its distance from the classroom.","zh":"學生可能記得飯堂的位置在禮堂旁邊，以及它與課室的距離。"},{"en":"Knowing positions and distances helps people choose a practical route.","zh":"知道位置和距離幫助人選擇實際路線。"},{"en":"The phrase describes basic spatial information.","zh":"這個短語描述基本空間資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be relative","meaning":"是相對的","examples":[{"en":"In a cognitive map, positions and distances may be relative.","zh":"在認知地圖中，位置和距離可能是相對的。"},{"en":"To be relative means to depend on comparison with something else rather than on exact measurement.","zh":"be relative 指取決於與其他事物比較，而不是精確量度。"},{"en":"A student may know the library is closer than the sports hall, even if she does not know the exact distance.","zh":"學生可能知道圖書館比體育館近，即使不知道精確距離。"},{"en":"Relative information is useful, but it may not match a precise scale.","zh":"相對資訊有用，但未必符合精確比例。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts approximate relationship with exact measurement.","zh":"這個短語對比近似關係與精確量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in contrast with","meaning":"與……形成對比","examples":[{"en":"A cognitive map is relative, in contrast with a geometrically precise road map.","zh":"認知地圖是相對的，與幾何上精確的道路地圖形成對比。"},{"en":"In contrast with means compared with something different or opposite.","zh":"in contrast with 指與不同或相反的事物相比。"},{"en":"A spoken explanation may be flexible, in contrast with a printed timetable.","zh":"口頭解釋可能較靈活，與印刷時間表形成對比。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a clear difference between two things.","zh":"這個短語突出兩件事之間的清楚差異。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing how one idea differs from another.","zh":"它適合用來顯示一個想法如何不同於另一個。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"geometrically precise scale","meaning":"幾何上精確的比例","examples":[{"en":"A road map displays locations on a geometrically precise scale.","zh":"道路地圖以幾何上精確的比例顯示位置。"},{"en":"A geometrically precise scale shows distances and positions according to exact mathematical proportions.","zh":"geometrically precise scale 是按精確數學比例顯示距離和位置。"},{"en":"An architect’s drawing needs a precise scale so builders know the true size of each room.","zh":"建築師圖則需要精確比例，讓建築工人知道每個房間的真實尺寸。"},{"en":"Precise scale helps maps show where places are in relation to one another accurately.","zh":"精確比例幫助地圖準確顯示地方之間的位置關係。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to exact measured representation.","zh":"這個短語指精確量度的呈現方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"match each statement with","meaning":"把每項陳述與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match each statement with the correct navigation method.","zh":"考生把每項陳述與正確導航方法配對。"},{"en":"To match each statement with something means to connect every sentence to the correct option.","zh":"match each statement with 某物，指把每句句子連到正確選項。"},{"en":"In a reading task, students may match each statement with the person who said it.","zh":"在閱讀題中，學生可能把每項陳述與說出該話的人配對。"},{"en":"Matching requires evidence from the text, not guessing from keywords alone.","zh":"配對需要文本證據，而不是只靠關鍵字猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語描述常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"navigation method","meaning":"導航方法","examples":[{"en":"The questions compare three different navigation methods.","zh":"題目比較三種不同導航方法。"},{"en":"A navigation method is a way of finding direction or reaching a destination.","zh":"navigation method 是辨認方向或到達目的地的方法。"},{"en":"Using landmarks, following GPS, and asking people are all navigation methods.","zh":"使用地標、跟隨 GPS 和問人都是導航方法。"},{"en":"Different methods work better depending on the place and available information.","zh":"不同方法是否更有效，取決於地方和可用資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a practical way of finding one’s route.","zh":"這個短語指實際尋找路線的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"appropriate letters","meaning":"適當的字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the appropriate letters in the answer boxes.","zh":"考生在答案框中寫上適當字母。"},{"en":"Appropriate letters are the correct option labels chosen from the list.","zh":"appropriate letters 是從列表中選出的正確選項標籤。"},{"en":"A student should write the appropriate letters only after matching each statement carefully.","zh":"學生應在仔細配對每項陳述後才寫上適當字母。"},{"en":"Writing the wrong letter can make an otherwise understood answer incorrect.","zh":"寫錯字母可以令本來理解了的答案變錯。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to answer choices in letter form.","zh":"這個短語指以字母形式呈現的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"use any letter more than once","meaning":"同一字母可使用多於一次","examples":[{"en":"Candidates may use any letter more than once.","zh":"考生可以使用任何字母多於一次。"},{"en":"To use any letter more than once means the same option can be chosen for several answers.","zh":"use any letter more than once 指同一選項可以用於幾個答案。"},{"en":"In a matching task, one paragraph may match two statements, so its letter is used twice.","zh":"在配對題中，一段可能配對兩項陳述，所以其字母會用兩次。"},{"en":"This instruction prevents students from wrongly assuming each option can appear only once.","zh":"這項指示防止學生錯誤假設每個選項只能出現一次。"},{"en":"The phrase gives permission to repeat answer choices.","zh":"這個短語容許重複使用答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"starting point","meaning":"起點","examples":[{"en":"The ant records a general direction from its starting point.","zh":"螞蟻從起點記錄大致方向。"},{"en":"A starting point is the place where a journey, process, or activity begins.","zh":"starting point 是旅程、過程或活動開始的地方。"},{"en":"The school gate may be the starting point for a class walking tour.","zh":"校門可能是一班學生步行導賞的起點。"},{"en":"Knowing the starting point helps people measure how far they have travelled.","zh":"知道起點幫助人量度自己走了多遠。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the beginning location or stage.","zh":"這個短語指出開始位置或階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"use a combination of","meaning":"使用……的組合","examples":[{"en":"Route following uses a combination of landmarks and directions.","zh":"按路線導航使用地標和方向的組合。"},{"en":"To use a combination of things means to use them together.","zh":"use a combination of 事物，指把它們一起使用。"},{"en":"A student may use a combination of notes, recordings, and practice questions to revise.","zh":"學生可能使用筆記、錄音和練習題的組合來溫習。"},{"en":"Combining different tools can make a method stronger than using one tool alone.","zh":"結合不同工具可以令方法比單用一種工具更強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mixing two or more elements.","zh":"這個短語描述混合兩種或以上元素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"reach the destination","meaning":"到達目的地","examples":[{"en":"Detailed directions help the traveller reach the destination.","zh":"詳細指示幫助旅客到達目的地。"},{"en":"To reach the destination means to arrive at the intended final place.","zh":"reach the destination 指到達預定的最終地方。"},{"en":"A patient follows hospital signs to reach the destination, such as the eye clinic.","zh":"病人跟隨醫院標誌到達目的地，例如眼科診所。"},{"en":"Clear directions reduce the chance of arriving at the wrong building.","zh":"清楚指示減少到達錯誤大樓的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on successful arrival.","zh":"這個短語重點在成功到達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"near the destination","meaning":"在目的地附近","examples":[{"en":"Guidance uses a prominent building near the destination.","zh":"引導式導航使用目的地附近的顯眼建築。"},{"en":"Near the destination means close to the place someone wants to reach.","zh":"near the destination 指接近某人想到達的地方。"},{"en":"A taxi driver may look for a hotel sign near the destination to confirm the correct street.","zh":"的士司機可能尋找目的地附近的酒店招牌，以確認正確街道。"},{"en":"Landmarks near the final point help travellers complete the last part of a journey.","zh":"最終地點附近的地標幫助旅客完成旅程最後一段。"},{"en":"The phrase describes closeness to the intended end point.","zh":"這個短語描述接近預定終點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"for orientation","meaning":"用作辨認方向","examples":[{"en":"A prominent building can be used for orientation.","zh":"顯眼建築可以用作辨認方向。"},{"en":"For orientation means for understanding position and direction.","zh":"for orientation 指為了理解位置和方向。"},{"en":"A map at a shopping mall entrance is useful for orientation before visitors start walking.","zh":"商場入口的地圖在訪客開始走之前，有助辨認方向。"},{"en":"Orientation helps people decide where they are and where to go next.","zh":"方向辨認幫助人決定自己在哪裏和下一步去哪裏。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the purpose of helping someone find direction.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助某人尋找方向的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"require retracing","meaning":"需要原路折返","examples":[{"en":"A wrong turn may require retracing the route.","zh":"轉錯彎可能需要原路折返。"},{"en":"To require retracing means to make it necessary to go back along the route already taken.","zh":"require retracing 指令沿已走路線返回變得必要。"},{"en":"If a student enters the wrong corridor, she may need to retrace her route to the lift.","zh":"如果學生進入錯誤走廊，她可能需要沿原路折返回電梯。"},{"en":"Retracing becomes necessary when moving forward would lead further away from the goal.","zh":"當繼續向前會更遠離目標，原路折返就變得必要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a situation where going back is needed.","zh":"這個短語描述需要回頭的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a known place","meaning":"已知地點","examples":[{"en":"The traveller backtracks until reaching a known place.","zh":"旅客原路折返，直到到達已知地點。"},{"en":"A known place is a location that someone recognises or understands.","zh":"known place 是某人認得或理解的位置。"},{"en":"A child may return to a known place like the school gate when she cannot find her classroom.","zh":"當孩子找不到課室時，可能回到校門這類已知地點。"},{"en":"Known places help people restart navigation from a safe reference point.","zh":"已知地點幫助人從安全參考點重新開始導航。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a familiar and reliable location.","zh":"這個短語指熟悉且可靠的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"reference point","meaning":"參考點","examples":[{"en":"A previously passed place can serve as a reference point.","zh":"之前經過的地方可以作為參考點。"},{"en":"A reference point is a known place or object used to judge position or direction.","zh":"reference point 是用來判斷位置或方向的已知地方或物件。"},{"en":"A student may use the main staircase as a reference point when finding classrooms.","zh":"學生尋找課室時，可能使用主樓梯作為參考點。"},{"en":"Reference points reduce confusion because they give people something stable to compare with.","zh":"參考點減少混亂，因為它給人穩定事物作比較。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an anchor for orientation.","zh":"這個短語描述方向辨認的定位依據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the next stage","meaning":"下一階段","examples":[{"en":"The remembered landmark guides the traveller to the next stage.","zh":"記得的地標引導旅客前往下一階段。"},{"en":"The next stage is the following part of a journey, plan, or process.","zh":"next stage 是旅程、計劃或過程中的下一部分。"},{"en":"After finishing the introduction, a student moves to the next stage of writing: explaining examples.","zh":"完成引言後，學生進入寫作下一階段：解釋例子。"},{"en":"Breaking a task into stages makes it easier to know what to do next.","zh":"把任務分成階段，讓人更容易知道下一步做甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the next step after the current one.","zh":"這個短語指當前之後的下一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"respond if","meaning":"在……情況下作出反應","examples":[{"en":"The question asks how the ant responds if it is moved.","zh":"題目問如果螞蟻被移動，牠會如何作出反應。"},{"en":"To respond if something happens means to react in that situation.","zh":"respond if 某事發生，指在該情況中作出反應。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask how students should respond if a fire alarm rings.","zh":"老師可能問如果火警鐘響，學生應如何作出反應。"},{"en":"Thinking about responses before a problem happens can make action faster and safer.","zh":"在問題發生前思考反應，可以令行動更快和更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase links a reaction to a condition.","zh":"這個短語把反應與條件連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"adjust its orientation sensors","meaning":"調整其方向感應系統","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that the ant adjusts its orientation sensors.","zh":"選項暗示螞蟻會調整其方向感應系統。"},{"en":"To adjust its orientation sensors means to change the system it uses to sense direction.","zh":"adjust its orientation sensors 指改變它用來感知方向的系統。"},{"en":"A phone may adjust its compass sensor when the user moves it in a figure-eight pattern.","zh":"當使用者以八字形移動手機時，手機可能調整其指南針感應器。"},{"en":"If a navigation sensor is adjusted correctly, direction readings may become more accurate.","zh":"如果導航感應器調整正確，方向讀數可能變得更準確。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing a direction-sensing system.","zh":"這個短語描述改變方向感應系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"release a scent","meaning":"釋放氣味","examples":[{"en":"Some insects release a scent to communicate with others.","zh":"有些昆蟲釋放氣味來與其他同類溝通。"},{"en":"To release a scent means to give off a smell into the air or environment.","zh":"release a scent 指把氣味散發到空氣或環境中。"},{"en":"A flower releases a scent that attracts bees.","zh":"花朵釋放氣味吸引蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Animals may use scents to mark paths, warn others, or find mates.","zh":"動物可能使用氣味標記路線、警告其他同類或尋找伴侶。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sending smell-based signals.","zh":"這個短語描述發出以氣味為基礎的訊號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"seek help from","meaning":"向……求助","examples":[{"en":"The option asks whether the ant seeks help from other ants.","zh":"選項問螞蟻是否向其他螞蟻求助。"},{"en":"To seek help from someone means to try to get assistance from that person.","zh":"seek help from 某人，指嘗試從該人取得協助。"},{"en":"A student may seek help from a teacher when she cannot understand a question.","zh":"學生不明白問題時，可能向老師求助。"},{"en":"Seeking help early can prevent a small problem from becoming serious.","zh":"及早求助可以防止小問題變嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase describes actively looking for support.","zh":"這個短語描述主動尋求支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"continue moving","meaning":"繼續移動","examples":[{"en":"The displaced ant continues moving in the original direction.","zh":"被移走的螞蟻繼續沿原來方向移動。"},{"en":"To continue moving means to keep going without stopping.","zh":"continue moving 指不停下來並繼續前進。"},{"en":"A runner may continue moving slowly after feeling tired so she can finish the race.","zh":"跑手疲倦後可能仍慢慢繼續移動，以完成比賽。"},{"en":"Continuing in one direction can be useful if the route is correct, but risky if conditions have changed.","zh":"如果路線正確，繼續朝同一方向可能有用；但如果情況已改變，就有風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ongoing motion.","zh":"這個短語描述持續移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"become completely lost","meaning":"完全迷失方向","examples":[{"en":"The ant does not immediately become completely lost.","zh":"螞蟻不會立即完全迷失方向。"},{"en":"To become completely lost means to have no idea where to go or how to return.","zh":"become completely lost 指完全不知道該往哪裏走或如何返回。"},{"en":"A tourist may become completely lost if her phone dies and she cannot recognise any street.","zh":"如果旅客手機沒電又認不出任何街道，可能完全迷失方向。"},{"en":"Complete loss of direction can cause panic and lead to poor decisions.","zh":"完全失去方向感可以造成恐慌並導致差決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes total confusion about location or route.","zh":"這個短語描述對位置或路線的完全困惑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a statement about","meaning":"有關……的陳述","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which statement about cognitive maps is true.","zh":"題目問哪一句有關認知地圖的陳述是正確的。"},{"en":"A statement about something is a sentence that gives information or an opinion on that topic.","zh":"statement about 某事，是提供該主題資訊或意見的句子。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to choose the correct statement about photosynthesis.","zh":"老師可能要求學生選出有關光合作用的正確陳述。"},{"en":"In reading tests, each statement must be checked against the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，每項陳述都必須與文章核對。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the topic of a claim.","zh":"這個短語引出主張的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"obvious difference between","meaning":"……之間的明顯差別","examples":[{"en":"There is an obvious difference between a cognitive map and a paper map.","zh":"認知地圖和紙本地圖之間有明顯差別。"},{"en":"An obvious difference between two things is a clear way in which they are not the same.","zh":"obvious difference between 兩物，是它們不相同的清楚之處。"},{"en":"There is an obvious difference between reading a recipe and actually cooking the dish.","zh":"閱讀食譜和真正烹調菜式之間有明顯差別。"},{"en":"Noticing obvious differences helps students avoid false comparisons.","zh":"注意明顯差別幫助學生避免錯誤比較。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a clear contrast.","zh":"這個短語突出清楚對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"exist in our heads","meaning":"存在於我們腦中","examples":[{"en":"A cognitive map exists as part of the brain’s memory system.","zh":"認知地圖作為大腦記憶系統的一部分存在。"},{"en":"To exist in our heads means to exist as an idea, memory, or mental image rather than a physical object.","zh":"exist in our heads 指作為想法、記憶或心理影像存在，而不是實體物件。"},{"en":"A student’s plan for an essay may exist in her head before she writes it down.","zh":"學生的文章計劃可能在寫下來之前已存在於腦中。"},{"en":"Mental information can guide action even when it cannot be seen directly.","zh":"心理資訊即使不能直接看見，也可以引導行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something stored in the mind.","zh":"這個短語描述儲存在頭腦中的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be always correct","meaning":"總是準確","examples":[{"en":"A person’s internal representation is not always correct.","zh":"一個人的內在呈現並不總是準確。"},{"en":"To be always correct means to be accurate every time without exception.","zh":"be always correct 指每一次都準確，沒有例外。"},{"en":"A student’s memory of a timetable is not always correct, so she should check the notice.","zh":"學生對時間表的記憶不一定總是準確，所以應查看通知。"},{"en":"Human memory can be useful but still contain errors.","zh":"人類記憶可以有用，但仍可能包含錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used in negative sentences to warn against overconfidence.","zh":"這個短語常用於否定句，以提醒人不要過度自信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"exist only in","meaning":"只存在於……","examples":[{"en":"Spatial-memory systems do not exist only in certain cultures.","zh":"空間記憶系統並非只存在於某些文化中。"},{"en":"To exist only in a place or group means to be found there and nowhere else.","zh":"exist only in 某地方或群體，指只在那裏存在，其他地方沒有。"},{"en":"Good manners do not exist only in rich families; they can be taught anywhere.","zh":"良好禮貌並非只存在於富裕家庭；它可以在任何地方被教導。"},{"en":"If something does not exist only in one culture, it may reflect a broader human pattern.","zh":"如果某事不只存在於一種文化，它可能反映更廣泛的人類模式。"},{"en":"The phrase limits where something is found, often in a negative statement.","zh":"這個短語限制某物出現的位置，常用於否定句。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"be managed by","meaning":"由……管理","examples":[{"en":"Navigation is managed by memory systems in the brain.","zh":"導航由大腦中的記憶系統管理。"},{"en":"To be managed by something means to be controlled, organised, or handled by it.","zh":"be managed by 某物，指由它控制、組織或處理。"},{"en":"A school library is managed by librarians who organise books and borrowing rules.","zh":"學校圖書館由圖書館員管理，他們整理書籍和借閱規則。"},{"en":"Good management helps a complex system work smoothly.","zh":"良好管理幫助複雜系統順利運作。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who or what controls a process.","zh":"這個短語指出誰或甚麼控制某過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"wayfinding","meaning":"尋路","examples":[{"en":"Wayfinding involves selecting and combining different navigation methods.","zh":"尋路涉及選擇並結合不同導航方法。"},{"en":"Wayfinding is the process of working out how to travel through an environment to reach a place.","zh":"wayfinding 是判斷如何穿過環境到達某地的過程。"},{"en":"Clear signs in a hospital improve wayfinding for patients and visitors.","zh":"醫院中清楚標誌可以改善病人和訪客尋路。"},{"en":"Poor wayfinding can make people late, anxious, or dependent on staff for help.","zh":"差劣尋路設計可以令人遲到、焦慮或依賴職員幫助。"},{"en":"The word refers to practical route-finding in real spaces.","zh":"這個字指在真實空間中的實際尋路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"correctly reflect","meaning":"正確反映","examples":[{"en":"The description should correctly reflect the function of a cognitive map.","zh":"描述應正確反映認知地圖的功能。"},{"en":"To correctly reflect something means to show or represent it accurately.","zh":"correctly reflect 某事，指準確顯示或呈現它。"},{"en":"A report should correctly reflect what students said in the survey.","zh":"報告應正確反映學生在調查中所說的內容。"},{"en":"If a summary does not reflect the source correctly, readers may misunderstand the main point.","zh":"如果摘要沒有正確反映來源，讀者可能誤解主旨。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses accurate representation.","zh":"這個短語強調準確呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"on a large scale","meaning":"從大範圍角度","examples":[{"en":"The traveller first visualises a general route on a large scale.","zh":"旅客先從大範圍角度想像大致路線。"},{"en":"On a large scale means from a broad overall view rather than in small detail.","zh":"on a large scale 指從廣闊整體角度，而不是小細節層面。"},{"en":"A city planner thinks on a large scale before deciding where small streets should go.","zh":"城市規劃師先從大範圍角度思考，再決定小街應放在哪裏。"},{"en":"Large-scale thinking helps people understand the whole area before focusing on one corner.","zh":"大範圍思考幫助人先理解整個地區，再集中於一個角落。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broad level of thinking or action.","zh":"這個短語描述廣闊層面的思考或行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"reproduce exact details","meaning":"重現確切細節","examples":[{"en":"A cognitive map does not necessarily reproduce exact details.","zh":"認知地圖不一定重現確切細節。"},{"en":"To reproduce exact details means to copy or represent every small detail accurately.","zh":"reproduce exact details 指準確複製或呈現每個小細節。"},{"en":"A student may remember the main idea of a lesson but not reproduce exact details from the teacher’s words.","zh":"學生可能記得課堂主旨，但不能重現老師用詞的確切細節。"},{"en":"Human memory often stores useful patterns rather than perfect copies.","zh":"人類記憶通常儲存有用模式，而不是完美複本。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses precise reproduction of information.","zh":"這個短語強調精確重現資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"play a more important role","meaning":"發揮更重要作用","examples":[{"en":"Observation may play an important role during the final stage of navigation.","zh":"觀察可能在導航最後階段發揮重要作用。"},{"en":"To play a more important role means to become more significant than before or than other factors.","zh":"play a more important role 指比以前或其他因素變得更重要。"},{"en":"In a speaking exam, confidence may play a more important role after students already know the content.","zh":"在口試中，當學生已知道內容，信心可能發揮更重要作用。"},{"en":"Different factors become more important at different stages of a task.","zh":"不同因素會在任務不同階段變得更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes relative importance.","zh":"這個短語描述相對重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料一致","examples":[{"en":"A true statement agrees with the information given in the passage.","zh":"正確陳述與文章所給資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the text states.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文本所陳述內容相符。"},{"en":"If a passage says the station is below a building, the same statement agrees with the information given.","zh":"如果文章說車站在大樓下方，相同陳述就與所給資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should check the passage rather than rely on outside knowledge.","zh":"學生應查核文章，而不是依靠外部知識。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個短語用於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章中的資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文本內容相反的事情。"},{"en":"If the passage says ants continue in the same direction, a statement saying they immediately turn back contradicts it.","zh":"如果文章說螞蟻繼續朝同一方向走，而陳述說牠們立即折返，就是與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction is different from missing information.","zh":"矛盾不同於資料缺失。"},{"en":"The phrase helps students identify FALSE answers.","zh":"這個短語幫助學生辨認 FALSE 答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"Write “NOT GIVEN” if there is no information on the statement.","zh":"如果文中沒有該陳述的資料，就寫 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the passage does not say anything about that point.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文章沒有說明該點。"},{"en":"If the text never mentions the driver’s age, a statement about age has no information in the passage.","zh":"如果文本從未提到司機年齡，關於年齡的陳述就沒有文章資料支持。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when the passage is silent.","zh":"當文章沒有說明時，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a NOT GIVEN situation.","zh":"這個短語指出 NOT GIVEN 的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"biological navigation","meaning":"生物導航","examples":[{"en":"Biological navigation is flexible and capable of learning.","zh":"生物導航靈活並有學習能力。"},{"en":"Biological navigation is the natural ability of living things to find direction and move through space.","zh":"biological navigation 是生物尋找方向並在空間中移動的自然能力。"},{"en":"Birds, ants, and humans all use forms of biological navigation.","zh":"鳥類、螞蟻和人類都使用某些形式的生物導航。"},{"en":"This ability can combine body signals, memory, landmarks, and sensory information.","zh":"這種能力可以結合身體訊號、記憶、地標和感官資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to navigation based on living systems rather than machines.","zh":"這個短語指基於生命系統而非機器的導航。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"receive a helpful answer","meaning":"得到有幫助的回答","examples":[{"en":"You may receive useful directions when you ask a passerby.","zh":"當你問途人時，可能得到有用指示。"},{"en":"To receive a helpful answer means to get a reply that gives useful information or solves a problem.","zh":"receive a helpful answer 指得到提供有用資訊或解決問題的回覆。"},{"en":"A student may receive a helpful answer when she asks a librarian how to find a book.","zh":"學生向圖書館員詢問如何找書時，可能得到有幫助的回答。"},{"en":"Helpful answers reduce confusion and help people act with more confidence.","zh":"有幫助的回答減少困惑，並幫助人更有信心行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a useful response to a question.","zh":"這個短語描述對問題的有用回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"collect comprehensive sensory information","meaning":"收集全面的感官資料","examples":[{"en":"The brain collects comprehensive sensory information during a journey.","zh":"大腦在旅程中收集全面的感官資料。"},{"en":"To collect comprehensive sensory information means to gather a wide range of details from the senses.","zh":"collect comprehensive sensory information 指從感官收集廣泛細節。"},{"en":"A driver collects sensory information from road signs, mirrors, engine sounds, and surrounding traffic.","zh":"司機從路牌、倒後鏡、引擎聲和周圍交通收集感官資料。"},{"en":"The more complete the sensory information is, the better the brain can judge location and direction.","zh":"感官資訊越完整，大腦越能判斷位置和方向。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad information gathering through the senses.","zh":"這個短語描述透過感官進行廣泛資訊收集。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"along the way","meaning":"沿途","examples":[{"en":"Travellers notice sights, sounds and smells along the way.","zh":"旅客沿途注意到景象、聲音和氣味。"},{"en":"Along the way means during the journey from one place to another.","zh":"along the way 指由一地到另一地的旅程期間。"},{"en":"A student may buy breakfast along the way to school.","zh":"學生可能在上學沿途買早餐。"},{"en":"Things noticed along the way can later help someone remember the route.","zh":"沿途注意到的東西之後可以幫助某人記住路線。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what happens or appears during travel.","zh":"這個短語指旅途中發生或出現的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"require more mental effort","meaning":"需要較多腦力","examples":[{"en":"Detailed route following may require more mental effort than path integration.","zh":"詳細按路線導航可能比路徑整合需要較多腦力。"},{"en":"To require more mental effort means to need more attention, memory, or thinking.","zh":"require more mental effort 指需要更多注意力、記憶或思考。"},{"en":"Solving a word problem may require more mental effort than copying a sentence.","zh":"解文字題可能比抄句子需要較多腦力。"},{"en":"Tasks with many steps often feel harder because the brain must hold more information.","zh":"步驟多的任務常感覺較難，因為大腦必須保存更多資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a higher thinking load.","zh":"這個短語描述較高思考負荷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"familiar surroundings","meaning":"熟悉的環境","examples":[{"en":"People can navigate more easily in familiar surroundings.","zh":"人們在熟悉的環境中可以更容易導航。"},{"en":"Familiar surroundings are places and features a person already knows well.","zh":"familiar surroundings 是某人已經熟知的地方和特徵。"},{"en":"A student moves confidently in familiar surroundings like her own school corridor.","zh":"學生在自己的學校走廊等熟悉環境中會自信地移動。"},{"en":"Familiarity reduces the need to check signs or ask for help.","zh":"熟悉感減少查看標誌或求助的需要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an environment that is already known.","zh":"這個短語描述已知的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"exact map of your location","meaning":"所在位置的精確地圖","examples":[{"en":"The brain does not necessarily produce an exact map of your location.","zh":"大腦不一定產生你所在位置的精確地圖。"},{"en":"An exact map of your location is a precise representation of where you are and what surrounds you.","zh":"exact map of your location 是準確呈現你在哪裏和周圍有甚麼的地圖。"},{"en":"A phone map may show an exact map of your location with nearby roads and buildings.","zh":"手機地圖可能顯示你所在位置的精確地圖，包括附近道路和建築。"},{"en":"Human memory often gives a useful sense of place, but not a perfect map.","zh":"人類記憶通常提供有用位置感，但不是完美地圖。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts precise map-like information with approximate mental knowledge.","zh":"這個短語把精確地圖式資訊與近似心理知識作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"automatically emerge","meaning":"自動浮現","examples":[{"en":"A complete mental map does not automatically emerge in the mind.","zh":"完整心理地圖不會在腦中自動浮現。"},{"en":"To automatically emerge means to appear by itself without deliberate effort.","zh":"automatically emerge 指無須刻意努力而自行出現。"},{"en":"Fluency does not automatically emerge after one English lesson.","zh":"流利能力不會在一堂英文課後自動浮現。"},{"en":"Complex skills usually develop through repeated use, feedback, and memory.","zh":"複雜技能通常透過反覆使用、回饋和記憶發展。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that something does not simply appear on its own.","zh":"這個短語提醒人某事不會自行簡單出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 146 - Finding our way.pdf","sourcePage":22}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 147":[{"front":"Rainwater Harvesting","meaning":"雨水收集","examples":[{"en":"Rainwater harvesting can improve water security in drought-stricken communities.","zh":"雨水收集可以改善受旱災打擊社區的用水安全。"},{"en":"Rainwater harvesting means collecting and storing rainwater for later use.","zh":"雨水收集是指收集並儲存雨水以供日後使用。"},{"en":"A village may use rainwater harvesting to provide water during dry months.","zh":"村落可以使用雨水收集在乾旱月份供水。"},{"en":"This method is especially useful where wells often dry up.","zh":"這種方法在水井經常乾涸的地方尤其有用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a practical water-management system.","zh":"這個短語指一種實用的水資源管理系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"suffer a prolonged drought","meaning":"遭受長期乾旱","examples":[{"en":"Southern Sri Lanka suffered a prolonged drought for two years.","zh":"斯里蘭卡南部遭受了兩年長期乾旱。"},{"en":"To suffer a prolonged drought means to experience a long period with very little rain.","zh":"遭受長期乾旱，是指經歷一段長時間雨量極少的時期。"},{"en":"Farmers may suffer a prolonged drought when crops fail season after season.","zh":"當農作物一季接一季失收，農民可能遭受長期乾旱。"},{"en":"A prolonged drought can damage food supplies, health and income.","zh":"長期乾旱會破壞糧食供應、健康和收入。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses both hardship and duration.","zh":"這個短語同時強調困苦和持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be described by locals as","meaning":"被本地居民形容為","examples":[{"en":"The drought was described by locals as the worst in 50 years.","zh":"這場乾旱被本地居民形容為五十年來最嚴重的一次。"},{"en":"To be described by locals as something means local people used those words to explain it.","zh":"被本地居民形容為某事，是指當地人用那些說法來描述它。"},{"en":"The storm was described by locals as the most frightening one they had seen.","zh":"這場風暴被本地居民形容為他們見過最可怕的一次。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the view of people who experienced the event directly.","zh":"這個短語顯示直接經歷事件的人如何看待它。"},{"en":"It is useful when reporting community testimony.","zh":"它適合用於報道社區證言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the worst in 50 years","meaning":"五十年來最嚴重的","examples":[{"en":"Residents described it as the worst drought in 50 years.","zh":"居民形容它是五十年來最嚴重的乾旱。"},{"en":"The worst in 50 years means more severe than anything similar during the last five decades.","zh":"五十年來最嚴重的，是指比過去五十年任何同類事件更嚴重。"},{"en":"A flood described as the worst in 50 years would be unusually destructive.","zh":"被形容為五十年來最嚴重的水災，通常破壞力異常大。"},{"en":"This phrase uses time comparison to show seriousness.","zh":"這個短語用時間比較顯示嚴重程度。"},{"en":"It is often used in news and reports.","zh":"它常見於新聞和報告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a successful crop","meaning":"成功收成；理想收成","examples":[{"en":"Some areas did not produce a successful crop for several seasons.","zh":"有些地區連續幾季都沒有理想收成。"},{"en":"A successful crop is a good harvest that grows well enough to be useful or profitable.","zh":"成功收成是農作物生長良好，足以食用或帶來收入的收成。"},{"en":"Farmers need enough rain to produce a successful crop.","zh":"農民需要足夠雨水才可取得理想收成。"},{"en":"Without a successful crop, families may lose food and income.","zh":"沒有成功收成，家庭可能失去食物和收入。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to farming results.","zh":"這個短語指農業成果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"consecutive seasons","meaning":"連續多個農耕季節","examples":[{"en":"Farmers experienced crop failure for four or five consecutive seasons.","zh":"農民連續四五個農耕季節都經歷農作物失收。"},{"en":"Consecutive seasons are seasons that happen one after another without interruption.","zh":"連續多個季節，是指一個接一個發生，中間沒有中斷。"},{"en":"A team that wins three consecutive seasons has won three seasons in a row.","zh":"一支球隊連續三季勝出，就是一連三季勝出。"},{"en":"Consecutive crop failures create serious pressure because there is no recovery period.","zh":"連續失收會造成嚴重壓力，因為沒有恢復期。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses continuity.","zh":"這個短語強調連續性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dangerously low levels","meaning":"危險的低水平","examples":[{"en":"Water in local wells dropped to dangerously low levels.","zh":"本地水井的水位降至危險的低水平。"},{"en":"Dangerously low levels are levels so low that they may cause harm or crisis.","zh":"危險的低水平，是低到可能造成傷害或危機的水平。"},{"en":"A reservoir at dangerously low levels may force water restrictions.","zh":"水庫處於危險低水平時，可能迫使政府限制用水。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests urgent risk, not just mild shortage.","zh":"這個短語暗示緊急風險，而不只是輕微短缺。"},{"en":"It is often used for water, blood sugar, oxygen or money.","zh":"它常用於水位、血糖、氧氣或金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"increasingly malnourished","meaning":"日益營養不良","examples":[{"en":"Children became increasingly malnourished during the drought.","zh":"乾旱期間，兒童日益營養不良。"},{"en":"Increasingly malnourished means becoming more seriously underfed over time.","zh":"日益營養不良，是指隨時間變得越來越嚴重地缺乏營養。"},{"en":"Children may become increasingly malnourished when food prices rise and crops fail.","zh":"當食物價格上升而農作物失收，兒童可能日益營養不良。"},{"en":"Malnutrition affects growth, learning and health.","zh":"營養不良會影響成長、學習和健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes worsening nutritional condition.","zh":"這個短語描述營養狀況惡化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"school attendance fell","meaning":"學校出席率下降","examples":[{"en":"School attendance fell because children spent more time fetching water.","zh":"學校出席率下降，因為兒童花更多時間取水。"},{"en":"School attendance fell means fewer students went to school regularly.","zh":"學校出席率下降，是指較少學生定期上學。"},{"en":"Attendance may fall when children need to work or help at home.","zh":"當兒童需要工作或在家幫忙，出席率可能下降。"},{"en":"Water shortages can indirectly harm education.","zh":"缺水會間接損害教育。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decline in student presence.","zh":"這個短語描述學生出席情況下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"an estimated 1.6 million people","meaning":"估計一百六十萬人","examples":[{"en":"An estimated 1.6 million people were affected by the drought.","zh":"估計一百六十萬人受到乾旱影響。"},{"en":"An estimated number is an approximate figure, not an exact count.","zh":"估計數字是約略數字，而不是精確計算。"},{"en":"An estimated 10,000 residents left the flooded district.","zh":"估計一萬名居民離開受水災影響地區。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when exact figures are unavailable.","zh":"當沒有精確數據時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It gives scale while showing uncertainty.","zh":"它顯示規模，同時保留不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be affected by","meaning":"受……影響","examples":[{"en":"Millions of people were affected by severe water shortages.","zh":"數百萬人受嚴重缺水影響。"},{"en":"To be affected by something means to experience its influence or harm.","zh":"受某事影響，是指經歷它帶來的影響或傷害。"},{"en":"Farmers are affected by drought when their crops fail.","zh":"當農作物失收，農民便受乾旱影響。"},{"en":"People can be affected directly or indirectly.","zh":"人們可以直接或間接受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reports about disasters and social problems.","zh":"這個短語常見於災害和社會問題報告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"drought-stricken areas","meaning":"受旱災打擊的地區","examples":[{"en":"Muthukandiya is located in one of Sri Lanka’s drought-stricken areas.","zh":"Muthukandiya 位於斯里蘭卡其中一個受旱災打擊的地區。"},{"en":"Drought-stricken areas are places badly affected by long periods without enough rain.","zh":"受旱災打擊的地區，是長時間雨水不足並受嚴重影響的地方。"},{"en":"Drought-stricken areas often suffer crop failure and water shortages.","zh":"這些地區常出現農作物失收和缺水。"},{"en":"These areas may need emergency water supplies or long-term water systems.","zh":"這些地區可能需要緊急供水或長期水利系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes places hit by drought.","zh":"這個短語描述受乾旱打擊的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the dry zone","meaning":"乾旱地帶","examples":[{"en":"Much of southern Sri Lanka lies within the country’s dry zone.","zh":"斯里蘭卡南部大部分位於該國乾旱地帶。"},{"en":"The dry zone is an area that receives relatively little rainfall.","zh":"乾旱地帶是降雨量相對較少的地區。"},{"en":"Farming in the dry zone is difficult without reliable water storage.","zh":"沒有可靠儲水，在乾旱地帶耕作很困難。"},{"en":"People in the dry zone often depend heavily on seasonal rain.","zh":"乾旱地帶的人常高度依賴季節性降雨。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a climatic region.","zh":"這個短語描述氣候區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"half the country’s population","meaning":"全國一半人口","examples":[{"en":"About half of Sri Lanka’s population lives in the dry zone.","zh":"斯里蘭卡約一半人口住在乾旱地帶。"},{"en":"Half the country’s population means around fifty percent of all people in the country.","zh":"全國一半人口，是指該國所有人口約百分之五十。"},{"en":"If half the country’s population depends on one river, water planning becomes crucial.","zh":"如果全國一半人口依賴一條河，水資源規劃就非常重要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a problem affects a very large group.","zh":"這個短語顯示問題影響非常龐大的人群。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing national scale.","zh":"它適合描述全國規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"vary greatly from year to year","meaning":"每年變化很大","examples":[{"en":"Rainfall in the area varies greatly from year to year.","zh":"該地區雨量每年變化很大。"},{"en":"To vary greatly from year to year means to change a lot each year.","zh":"每年變化很大，是指每一年都大幅改變。"},{"en":"Farm income may vary greatly from year to year when rainfall is unreliable.","zh":"當雨量不穩定，農場收入可能每年變化很大。"},{"en":"Large yearly variation makes planning difficult.","zh":"年度變化大會令規劃困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unpredictability over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間的不穩定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"extreme dry spells","meaning":"極端乾旱期","examples":[{"en":"The region often experiences extreme dry spells between monsoons.","zh":"該地區在兩次季候雨之間常經歷極端乾旱期。"},{"en":"Extreme dry spells are very severe periods with little or no rain.","zh":"極端乾旱期是雨量極少或完全無雨的嚴重時期。"},{"en":"Extreme dry spells can empty wells and damage crops.","zh":"極端乾旱期會令水井乾涸並損害農作物。"},{"en":"They are especially harmful when communities lack stored water.","zh":"當社區缺乏儲水，這些時期尤其有害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intense short- or medium-term dryness.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈的短期或中期乾旱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in between monsoons","meaning":"在兩次季候雨之間","examples":[{"en":"Long dry spells can occur in between monsoons.","zh":"長時間乾旱可能在兩次季候雨之間出現。"},{"en":"In between monsoons means during the period between two rainy monsoon seasons.","zh":"在兩次季候雨之間，是指兩個季候雨雨季之間的時期。"},{"en":"Farmers may store water in between monsoons to survive dry months.","zh":"農民可能在兩次季候雨之間儲水，以度過乾旱月份。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a seasonal time frame.","zh":"這個短語給出季節性時間框架。"},{"en":"It is common in discussions of South Asian climate.","zh":"它常見於南亞氣候討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"much worse than usual","meaning":"比平常嚴重得多","examples":[{"en":"This drought was much worse than the region usually experienced.","zh":"這次乾旱比該地區平常經歷的嚴重得多。"},{"en":"Much worse than usual means far more severe than normal.","zh":"比平常嚴重得多，是指遠比正常情況嚴重。"},{"en":"This year’s flu season was much worse than usual.","zh":"今年流感季節比平常嚴重得多。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the event exceeded ordinary hardship.","zh":"這個短語顯示事件超出一般困難。"},{"en":"It often introduces a reason for urgent action.","zh":"它常引出緊急行動的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"despite some rain","meaning":"儘管有一些降雨","examples":[{"en":"Despite some rain in November, many wells remained unusable.","zh":"儘管十一月有一些降雨，許多水井仍不能使用。"},{"en":"Despite some rain means although rain did fall, it was not enough to solve the problem.","zh":"儘管有一些降雨，是指雖然下了雨，但不足以解決問題。"},{"en":"Despite some rain, the reservoir stayed nearly empty.","zh":"儘管有一些降雨，水庫仍幾乎空了。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts limited improvement with continuing difficulty.","zh":"這個短語對比有限改善與持續困難。"},{"en":"It warns that light rain may not end a drought.","zh":"它提醒少量降雨未必能結束乾旱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tube wells","meaning":"管井","examples":[{"en":"Only half of the district’s tube wells were in working order.","zh":"該區只有一半管井運作正常。"},{"en":"Tube wells are narrow wells made by drilling into underground water sources.","zh":"管井是透過鑽入地下水源而建成的狹窄水井。"},{"en":"A village may use tube wells when surface water is unreliable.","zh":"當地表水不可靠，村落可能使用管井。"},{"en":"Tube wells require maintenance to keep water flowing safely.","zh":"管井需要保養，才能安全持續供水。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a groundwater-supply structure.","zh":"這個短語指地下水供應設施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be in working order","meaning":"運作正常","examples":[{"en":"Only about half of the tube wells were in working order.","zh":"只有約一半管井運作正常。"},{"en":"To be in working order means to function properly.","zh":"運作正常，是指能正常發揮功能。"},{"en":"A pump is in working order if it can still bring water to the surface.","zh":"如果水泵仍能把水抽到地面，它就是運作正常。"},{"en":"Equipment that is not in working order may be useless during a crisis.","zh":"在危機中，不能正常運作的設備可能毫無用處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical functionality.","zh":"這個短語描述實際功能狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"devastate supplies of","meaning":"嚴重破壞……的供應","examples":[{"en":"The drought devastated supplies of rice and freshwater fish.","zh":"乾旱嚴重破壞稻米和淡水魚的供應。"},{"en":"To devastate supplies of something means to severely reduce or destroy its availability.","zh":"嚴重破壞某物供應，是指大幅減少或摧毀其可取得性。"},{"en":"A storm can devastate supplies of vegetables by damaging farms.","zh":"風暴可以透過破壞農場而嚴重破壞蔬菜供應。"},{"en":"When food supplies are devastated, diets and income suffer.","zh":"當食物供應受嚴重破壞，飲食和收入都會受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severe damage to availability.","zh":"這個短語描述可供應量受到嚴重打擊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"freshwater fish","meaning":"淡水魚","examples":[{"en":"Freshwater fish form part of the staple diet in inland villages.","zh":"淡水魚是內陸村落主食的一部分。"},{"en":"Freshwater fish are fish that live in rivers, lakes or ponds rather than the sea.","zh":"淡水魚是生活在河流、湖泊或池塘，而不是海洋中的魚。"},{"en":"Tilapia from a village pond is an example of freshwater fish.","zh":"村塘中的羅非魚就是淡水魚例子。"},{"en":"Freshwater fish can be an important source of protein.","zh":"淡水魚可以是重要蛋白質來源。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts river and lake fish with marine fish.","zh":"這個短語把河湖魚與海魚作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"staple diet","meaning":"主食","examples":[{"en":"Rice and freshwater fish are the staple diet of many inland villagers.","zh":"稻米和淡水魚是許多內陸村民的主食。"},{"en":"A staple diet is the main food people eat regularly.","zh":"主食是人們經常食用的主要食物。"},{"en":"Bread may be part of the staple diet in some countries.","zh":"在一些國家，麵包可能是主食的一部分。"},{"en":"When a staple diet is disrupted, nutrition can quickly worsen.","zh":"當主食供應受干擾，營養狀況會很快惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to everyday basic food.","zh":"這個短語指日常基本食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"inland villages","meaning":"內陸村落","examples":[{"en":"Many inland villages depend on local rice and fish supplies.","zh":"許多內陸村落依賴本地稻米和魚類供應。"},{"en":"Inland villages are villages away from the coast or sea.","zh":"內陸村落是遠離海岸或海洋的村落。"},{"en":"Inland villages may rely on wells, ponds and rainfall for water.","zh":"內陸村落可能依賴水井、池塘和降雨供水。"},{"en":"They may be more vulnerable when local water sources fail.","zh":"當本地水源失效時，它們可能更脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rural settlements away from the coast.","zh":"這個短語描述遠離海岸的農村聚落。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"close down","meaning":"停業；關閉","examples":[{"en":"Many local industries closed down during the drought.","zh":"乾旱期間，許多本地工業停業。"},{"en":"To close down means to stop operating, usually because of serious difficulty.","zh":"停業或關閉，是指停止運作，通常因遇到嚴重困難。"},{"en":"A small factory may close down if it has no water or electricity.","zh":"如果沒有水或電，小工廠可能停業。"},{"en":"When local industries close down, villagers lose jobs.","zh":"當本地工業停業，村民會失去工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes business or institutional shutdown.","zh":"這個短語描述企業或機構停止運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"head for the towns","meaning":"前往城鎮","examples":[{"en":"Villagers headed for the towns in search of employment.","zh":"村民前往城鎮尋找工作。"},{"en":"To head for the towns means to go towards urban areas.","zh":"前往城鎮，是指朝城市或市鎮地區移動。"},{"en":"Young people may head for the towns when farming income falls.","zh":"當農業收入下降，年輕人可能前往城鎮。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests migration caused by need.","zh":"這個短語常暗示因需要而遷移。"},{"en":"It shows movement from rural areas to towns.","zh":"它顯示由農村向城鎮移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in search of work","meaning":"尋找工作","examples":[{"en":"Many residents left their villages in search of work.","zh":"許多居民離開村落尋找工作。"},{"en":"In search of work means trying to find employment.","zh":"尋找工作，是指嘗試找到就業機會。"},{"en":"A farmer may move to the city in search of work after crops fail.","zh":"農作物失收後，農民可能搬到城市尋找工作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the purpose of migration.","zh":"這個短語顯示遷移目的。"},{"en":"It is common in descriptions of economic hardship.","zh":"它常見於經濟困難的描述中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"government resettlement scheme","meaning":"政府重新安置計劃","examples":[{"en":"The villagers arrived through a government resettlement scheme.","zh":"村民透過政府重新安置計劃來到該地。"},{"en":"A government resettlement scheme is an official programme that moves people to a new area.","zh":"政府重新安置計劃，是政府把人搬到新地區的官方方案。"},{"en":"Families may join a resettlement scheme after losing land or homes.","zh":"家庭失去土地或房屋後，可能參加重新安置計劃。"},{"en":"Such schemes often provide land, housing or basic services.","zh":"這類計劃通常提供土地、住房或基本服務。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised relocation by the government.","zh":"這個短語指由政府組織的遷置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be given six acres of land","meaning":"獲分配六英畝土地","examples":[{"en":"Each resettled family was given six acres of land.","zh":"每個重新安置家庭獲分配六英畝土地。"},{"en":"To be given six acres of land means to receive that amount of land for use or ownership.","zh":"獲分配六英畝土地，是指獲得該面積土地作使用或擁有。"},{"en":"A farming family may be given land but still need water and tools.","zh":"農戶可能獲分配土地，但仍需要水和工具。"},{"en":"Land alone may not support a family without irrigation.","zh":"沒有灌溉，單靠土地未必能養活家庭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes land allocation.","zh":"這個短語描述土地分配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"irrigation system","meaning":"灌溉系統","examples":[{"en":"The families received land without an irrigation system.","zh":"這些家庭獲得土地，但沒有灌溉系統。"},{"en":"An irrigation system supplies water to crops through channels, pumps or pipes.","zh":"灌溉系統透過水渠、水泵或水管為農作物供水。"},{"en":"A farm with an irrigation system can grow crops even when rain is limited.","zh":"有灌溉系統的農場即使雨量有限也能種植作物。"},{"en":"Without irrigation, farming depends heavily on rainfall.","zh":"沒有灌溉，農業便高度依賴降雨。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to water supply for agriculture.","zh":"這個短語指農業供水系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"crop production","meaning":"農作物生產","examples":[{"en":"Local crop production depends entirely on rainfall.","zh":"本地農作物生產完全依賴降雨。"},{"en":"Crop production means the growing and harvesting of plants for food or income.","zh":"農作物生產，是指種植和收割用作食物或收入的植物。"},{"en":"Rice crop production falls when fields do not receive enough water.","zh":"當田地沒有足夠水分，稻米生產會下降。"},{"en":"Reliable water improves crop production and food security.","zh":"可靠水源能改善農作物生產和糧食安全。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to agricultural output.","zh":"這個短語指農業產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rely entirely on rainfall","meaning":"完全依賴降雨","examples":[{"en":"Farming in the village relies entirely on rainfall.","zh":"村中的耕作完全依賴降雨。"},{"en":"To rely entirely on rainfall means to depend only on rain for water.","zh":"完全依賴降雨，是指只依靠雨水供水。"},{"en":"Farmers who rely entirely on rainfall are vulnerable to dry spells.","zh":"完全依賴降雨的農民容易受乾旱期影響。"},{"en":"Rain-fed farming becomes risky when rainfall varies greatly.","zh":"當雨量變化很大，雨養農業便變得有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase shows complete dependence on weather.","zh":"這個短語顯示對天氣的完全依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be insufficient to support","meaning":"不足以維持……","examples":[{"en":"Crop production is insufficient to support most village families.","zh":"農作物生產不足以維持大多數村落家庭。"},{"en":"To be insufficient to support means not enough to maintain people’s basic needs.","zh":"不足以維持，是指不足夠滿足人們基本需要。"},{"en":"A small income may be insufficient to support a large family.","zh":"微薄收入可能不足以維持一個大家庭。"},{"en":"Insufficient production can force people to seek extra work.","zh":"生產不足會迫使人們尋找額外工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shortage relative to need.","zh":"這個短語描述相對於需要的不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"village economy","meaning":"村落經濟","examples":[{"en":"The village economy depends partly on seasonal labour.","zh":"村落經濟部分依賴季節性勞動。"},{"en":"A village economy is the system of work, income and exchange within a village.","zh":"村落經濟是村內工作、收入和交換的系統。"},{"en":"Farming, small shops and day labour can all support a village economy.","zh":"耕作、小店和日薪勞動都可以支持村落經濟。"},{"en":"When drought hits farming, the village economy becomes weaker.","zh":"當乾旱打擊農業，村落經濟會變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to local economic life.","zh":"這個短語指本地經濟生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"day labourers","meaning":"散工；日薪勞工","examples":[{"en":"Many villagers work as day labourers on nearby plantations.","zh":"許多村民在附近種植園做散工。"},{"en":"Day labourers are workers paid by the day rather than with a regular salary.","zh":"散工或日薪勞工，是按日支薪而非領固定薪金的工人。"},{"en":"Day labourers may pick crops when plantations need extra workers.","zh":"當種植園需要額外人手，散工可能負責採摘作物。"},{"en":"Their income is often insecure because work may not be available every day.","zh":"他們收入通常不穩定，因為未必每天都有工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes temporary daily-paid workers.","zh":"這個短語描述臨時按日支薪工人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sugar-cane plantations","meaning":"甘蔗種植園","examples":[{"en":"Villagers often find work on nearby sugar-cane plantations.","zh":"村民常在附近甘蔗種植園找到工作。"},{"en":"Sugar-cane plantations are large farms where sugar cane is grown.","zh":"甘蔗種植園是種植甘蔗的大型農場。"},{"en":"Workers on sugar-cane plantations may cut, carry and process cane.","zh":"甘蔗種植園工人可能砍甘蔗、搬運和處理甘蔗。"},{"en":"Plantations can provide seasonal jobs for nearby villagers.","zh":"種植園可以為附近村民提供季節性工作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to large-scale sugar-cane farms.","zh":"這個短語指大規模甘蔗農場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be dug to provide","meaning":"被挖掘以提供……","examples":[{"en":"Three wells were dug to provide water for domestic use.","zh":"三口水井被挖掘以提供家居用水。"},{"en":"To be dug to provide something means to be excavated in order to supply it.","zh":"被挖掘以提供某物，是指被開挖以供應該物。"},{"en":"A new well was dug to provide drinking water for the school.","zh":"一口新井被挖掘以為學校提供飲用水。"},{"en":"This phrase links construction with purpose.","zh":"這個短語把建設與目的連接起來。"},{"en":"It is often used for wells, channels and pits.","zh":"它常用於水井、水渠和坑洞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"domestic water","meaning":"家居用水","examples":[{"en":"The wells provide domestic water for drinking, washing and cooking.","zh":"這些水井提供飲用、洗滌和煮食用的家居用水。"},{"en":"Domestic water is water used in households for everyday needs.","zh":"家居用水是家庭日常需要所用的水。"},{"en":"Families need domestic water for cooking rice and washing clothes.","zh":"家庭需要家居用水來煮飯和洗衣。"},{"en":"Safe domestic water improves health and hygiene.","zh":"安全家居用水能改善健康和衛生。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to household use, not farming water.","zh":"這個短語指家庭用途，而不是農業用水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"run dry","meaning":"乾涸","examples":[{"en":"The village wells run dry for much of the year.","zh":"村中的水井一年大部分時間都乾涸。"},{"en":"To run dry means to have no water left.","zh":"乾涸，是指沒有水剩下。"},{"en":"A pond may run dry during a long drought.","zh":"長期乾旱期間，池塘可能乾涸。"},{"en":"When wells run dry, people must walk further to collect water.","zh":"當水井乾涸，人們必須走更遠路取水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes water sources becoming empty.","zh":"這個短語描述水源變空。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"spend several hours doing something","meaning":"花數小時做某事","examples":[{"en":"Women and children may spend several hours fetching water.","zh":"婦女和兒童可能花數小時取水。"},{"en":"To spend several hours doing something means to use a few hours on that activity.","zh":"花數小時做某事，是指用幾個小時進行該活動。"},{"en":"Students may spend several hours preparing for an oral presentation.","zh":"學生可能花數小時準備口頭報告。"},{"en":"Long time spent fetching water reduces time for school and work.","zh":"長時間取水會減少上學和工作的時間。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a heavy time burden.","zh":"這個短語突出沉重時間負擔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"walk up to three miles","meaning":"步行長達三英里","examples":[{"en":"Some villagers walk up to three miles to collect water.","zh":"有些村民步行長達三英里去取水。"},{"en":"To walk up to three miles means to walk as far as three miles, though sometimes less.","zh":"步行長達三英里，是指最遠走三英里，有時可能較短。"},{"en":"Children may walk up to three miles to reach the nearest school.","zh":"兒童可能步行長達三英里到最近的學校。"},{"en":"Long walking distances make daily water collection exhausting.","zh":"長距離步行令每日取水十分疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a maximum distance.","zh":"這個短語給出最遠距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fetch water","meaning":"取水","examples":[{"en":"Women and children regularly fetch water from distant wells.","zh":"婦女和兒童定期從遠處水井取水。"},{"en":"To fetch water means to go and collect water, then bring it back.","zh":"取水，是指去收集水並把它帶回來。"},{"en":"A child may fetch water from a public tap before breakfast.","zh":"兒童可能在早餐前從公共水龍頭取水。"},{"en":"Fetching water becomes burdensome when the source is far away.","zh":"當水源很遠，取水會變成沉重負擔。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a daily survival task.","zh":"這個短語描述日常生存工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"drinking, washing and cooking","meaning":"飲用、洗滌和煮食","examples":[{"en":"The collected water is used for drinking, washing and cooking.","zh":"收集回來的水用於飲用、洗滌和煮食。"},{"en":"Drinking, washing and cooking are basic household uses of water.","zh":"飲用、洗滌和煮食是水的基本家庭用途。"},{"en":"Clean water is needed for drinking, washing and cooking every day.","zh":"每天都需要清潔水來飲用、洗滌和煮食。"},{"en":"If water is scarce, all three daily activities become difficult.","zh":"如果缺水，這三項日常活動都會變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase lists essential domestic needs.","zh":"這個短語列出基本家居需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"discuss water problems with","meaning":"與……討論水資源問題","examples":[{"en":"Local communities discussed their water problems with Practical Action South Asia.","zh":"本地社區與 Practical Action South Asia 討論他們的水資源問題。"},{"en":"To discuss problems with someone means to talk with them in order to understand or solve the problems.","zh":"與某人討論問題，是指和他們交談，以理解或解決問題。"},{"en":"Villagers discussed water problems with engineers before choosing a system.","zh":"村民在選擇系統前與工程師討論水資源問題。"},{"en":"Discussion allows local voices to shape the project.","zh":"討論讓本地聲音塑造項目。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests consultation and cooperation.","zh":"這個短語暗示諮詢和合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"what followed was","meaning":"隨後出現的是","examples":[{"en":"What followed was a community-based drought-mitigation initiative.","zh":"隨後出現的是一項以社區為本的旱災紓緩計劃。"},{"en":"What followed was means the next thing that happened was.","zh":"隨後出現的是，指接下來發生的事情是。"},{"en":"The villagers met the engineers; what followed was a plan for water storage.","zh":"村民與工程師會面；隨後出現的是儲水計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the result of earlier action.","zh":"這個短語引入較早行動的結果。"},{"en":"It is useful for narrative development.","zh":"它適合用於敘事推進。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"drought-mitigation initiative","meaning":"旱災紓緩計劃","examples":[{"en":"The organisation developed a drought-mitigation initiative based on rainwater collection.","zh":"該組織制定了一項以雨水收集為基礎的旱災紓緩計劃。"},{"en":"A drought-mitigation initiative is a planned project to reduce the harm caused by drought.","zh":"旱災紓緩計劃，是一項旨在減少乾旱傷害的規劃項目。"},{"en":"Building storage tanks can be part of a drought-mitigation initiative.","zh":"建造儲水缸可以是旱災紓緩計劃的一部分。"},{"en":"Mitigation does not remove drought, but it reduces its impact.","zh":"紓緩不會消除乾旱，但會減少其影響。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised drought-response action.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的抗旱行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"以……為基礎","examples":[{"en":"The initiative was based on low-cost rainwater-harvesting technology.","zh":"該計劃以低成本雨水收集技術為基礎。"},{"en":"To be based on something means to use it as the main foundation or idea.","zh":"以某事為基礎，是指把它作為主要根基或想法。"},{"en":"The lesson was based on real examples from students’ writing.","zh":"這堂課以學生寫作中的真實例子為基礎。"},{"en":"A project based on local technology is often easier to maintain.","zh":"以本地技術為基礎的項目通常較容易維護。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the foundation of a plan.","zh":"這個短語顯示計劃的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"low-cost technology","meaning":"低成本技術","examples":[{"en":"The project used low-cost technology that local people could maintain.","zh":"該項目使用本地居民能維護的低成本技術。"},{"en":"Low-cost technology is technology that does not require much money to build or use.","zh":"低成本技術，是建造或使用時不需要太多金錢的技術。"},{"en":"A simple water filter can be low-cost technology for a village.","zh":"簡單濾水器可以是村落的低成本技術。"},{"en":"Low cost matters when families have limited income.","zh":"當家庭收入有限，低成本非常重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes affordable practical tools.","zh":"這個短語描述可負擔的實用工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be already used in","meaning":"已在……使用","examples":[{"en":"The technology was already used in Sri Lanka and elsewhere in the region.","zh":"該技術已在斯里蘭卡及區內其他地方使用。"},{"en":"To be already used in a place means people there had used it before the current project.","zh":"已在某地使用，是指該地人們在目前項目之前已使用它。"},{"en":"Solar pumps were already used in nearby villages before the new scheme began.","zh":"新計劃開始前，太陽能水泵已在附近村落使用。"},{"en":"Existing use can make a technology seem more reliable.","zh":"既有使用情況可以令技術看起來更可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase shows prior adoption.","zh":"這個短語顯示早前已被採用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"collect and store rainwater","meaning":"收集和儲存雨水","examples":[{"en":"The system uses tanks to collect and store rainwater.","zh":"該系統使用水缸收集和儲存雨水。"},{"en":"To collect and store rainwater means to gather rain and keep it for later use.","zh":"收集和儲存雨水，是指收集雨水並保留作日後使用。"},{"en":"A roof tank can collect and store rainwater during the wet season.","zh":"屋頂水缸可以在雨季收集和儲存雨水。"},{"en":"Stored rainwater helps households during dry months.","zh":"儲存雨水能在乾旱月份幫助家庭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main function of rainwater harvesting.","zh":"這個短語描述雨水收集的主要功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be channelled by","meaning":"由……引流","examples":[{"en":"Rainwater is channelled by gutters and pipes into storage tanks.","zh":"雨水由排水槽和水管引流入儲水缸。"},{"en":"To be channelled by something means to be directed through it.","zh":"由某物引流，是指被引導通過該物。"},{"en":"Water from the roof is channelled by pipes into a barrel.","zh":"屋頂雨水由水管引流入水桶。"},{"en":"Channels guide water so it does not simply run away.","zh":"引流設施引導水流，使它不會白白流走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled movement of water.","zh":"這個短語描述水的受控移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"gutters and pipes","meaning":"排水槽和水管","examples":[{"en":"Gutters and pipes carry water from roofs to storage tanks.","zh":"排水槽和水管把水從屋頂帶到儲水缸。"},{"en":"Gutters and pipes are channels and tubes that guide water.","zh":"排水槽和水管是引導水流的渠道和管道。"},{"en":"A house needs clean gutters and pipes to collect rainwater properly.","zh":"房屋需要乾淨的排水槽和水管，才能妥善收集雨水。"},{"en":"Blocked gutters can stop water from reaching the tank.","zh":"堵塞的排水槽會阻止水流到水缸。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to basic water-collection equipment.","zh":"這個短語指基本集水設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"run off the roofs","meaning":"從屋頂流下","examples":[{"en":"The system collects rainwater as it runs off the roofs of houses.","zh":"該系統收集從房屋屋頂流下的雨水。"},{"en":"To run off the roofs means to flow down from roof surfaces.","zh":"從屋頂流下，是指從屋頂表面向下流動。"},{"en":"Rainwater runs off the roof into the gutter during a storm.","zh":"暴雨期間，雨水從屋頂流入排水槽。"},{"en":"Roof runoff can be wasted unless it is collected.","zh":"屋頂徑流如果不被收集，就會被浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes natural water flow from roofs.","zh":"這個短語描述雨水從屋頂自然流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"indigenous tradition","meaning":"本土傳統","examples":[{"en":"Sri Lanka has an indigenous tradition of rainwater harvesting.","zh":"斯里蘭卡有雨水收集的本土傳統。"},{"en":"An indigenous tradition is a local practice that developed within a place over time.","zh":"本土傳統是在某地長時間發展出來的本地做法。"},{"en":"Traditional tank irrigation may be part of an indigenous tradition.","zh":"傳統水缸灌溉可能是本土傳統的一部分。"},{"en":"Such traditions often reflect local climate and knowledge.","zh":"這類傳統通常反映本地氣候和知識。"},{"en":"This phrase values local historical practice.","zh":"這個短語重視本地歷史做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"go back to","meaning":"追溯至……","examples":[{"en":"The country’s irrigation tradition goes back to the third century BC.","zh":"該國的灌溉傳統可追溯至公元前三世紀。"},{"en":"To go back to a time means to have existed since that time.","zh":"追溯至某時，是指自該時期起已存在。"},{"en":"This village festival goes back to the nineteenth century.","zh":"這個村落節日可追溯至十九世紀。"},{"en":"The phrase shows historical depth.","zh":"這個短語顯示歷史深度。"},{"en":"It is useful for explaining long traditions.","zh":"它適合解釋悠久傳統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the third century BC","meaning":"公元前三世紀","examples":[{"en":"Rainwater-management systems existed as early as the third century BC.","zh":"雨水管理系統早在公元前三世紀已存在。"},{"en":"The third century BC means the period from 300 BC to 201 BC.","zh":"公元前三世紀是指公元前 300 年至公元前 201 年。"},{"en":"A structure from the third century BC is more than two thousand years old.","zh":"來自公元前三世紀的結構已有二千多年歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an ancient historical date.","zh":"這個短語給出古代歷史日期。"},{"en":"It shows that the practice has a long history.","zh":"它顯示這種做法歷史悠久。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"policy-makers","meaning":"政策制定者","examples":[{"en":"Policy-makers had often overlooked small-scale rainwater technology.","zh":"政策制定者常忽視小規模雨水技術。"},{"en":"Policy-makers are people who create rules, plans or public policies.","zh":"政策制定者是制定規則、計劃或公共政策的人。"},{"en":"Policy-makers decide whether to fund schools, roads or water systems.","zh":"政策制定者決定是否資助學校、道路或供水系統。"},{"en":"Their choices affect how resources are distributed.","zh":"他們的選擇影響資源如何分配。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to decision-makers in government or organisations.","zh":"這個短語指政府或組織中的決策者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"overlook the value of","meaning":"忽視……的價值","examples":[{"en":"Officials had overlooked the value of traditional water-harvesting systems.","zh":"官員曾忽視傳統集水系統的價值。"},{"en":"To overlook the value of something means to fail to notice how useful or important it is.","zh":"忽視某事的價值，是指未能注意它有多有用或重要。"},{"en":"Schools may overlook the value of quiet reading time.","zh":"學校可能忽視安靜閱讀時間的價值。"},{"en":"Valuable local knowledge is sometimes ignored because it seems old-fashioned.","zh":"有價值的本地知識有時因看似老舊而被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase describes underestimating importance.","zh":"這個短語描述低估重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take an interest in","meaning":"對……產生興趣","examples":[{"en":"Officials have only recently taken an interest in household-level structures.","zh":"官員只是近來才對家庭層面的設施產生興趣。"},{"en":"To take an interest in something means to begin paying attention to it.","zh":"對某事產生興趣，是指開始留意它。"},{"en":"Students may take an interest in science after doing a simple experiment.","zh":"學生做過簡單實驗後，可能對科學產生興趣。"},{"en":"Interest often leads to research, funding or action.","zh":"興趣通常會帶來研究、資金或行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growing attention.","zh":"這個短語描述關注增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"household-level structures","meaning":"家庭層面的設施","examples":[{"en":"Household-level structures allow individual families to store water.","zh":"家庭層面的設施讓個別家庭儲水。"},{"en":"Household-level structures are facilities built for use by single households.","zh":"家庭層面的設施是供單一家庭使用的設施。"},{"en":"A rainwater tank beside a house is a household-level structure.","zh":"房屋旁的雨水缸就是家庭層面的設施。"},{"en":"Such structures give families more control over water supply.","zh":"這類設施讓家庭更能掌控供水。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts family-scale systems with large public schemes.","zh":"這個短語把家庭規模系統與大型公共計劃作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"top-down approach","meaning":"由上而下的方法","examples":[{"en":"Earlier government programmes often followed a top-down approach.","zh":"早期政府計劃常採用由上而下的方法。"},{"en":"A top-down approach is planned by authorities with limited local participation.","zh":"由上而下的方法，是由權力機構規劃，而本地參與有限。"},{"en":"A top-down water project may install equipment without consulting villagers.","zh":"由上而下的水利項目可能不諮詢村民便安裝設備。"},{"en":"Such approaches can fail if users do not understand or support them.","zh":"如果使用者不理解或不支持，這類方法可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with community-based planning.","zh":"這個短語與以社區為本的規劃形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in their conception and application","meaning":"在構思和實施方面","examples":[{"en":"Some programmes were top-down in both their conception and application.","zh":"有些計劃在構思和實施方面都是由上而下的。"},{"en":"In their conception and application means in both the planning stage and the way they were carried out.","zh":"在構思和實施方面，是指在規劃階段和實際執行方式上。"},{"en":"A policy may fail in conception and application if it is poorly designed and badly implemented.","zh":"如果政策設計差且執行差，它在構思和實施方面都可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase covers idea and practice together.","zh":"這個短語同時涵蓋想法和實踐。"},{"en":"It is useful for evaluating programmes.","zh":"它適合用於評估計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"install tanks free of charge","meaning":"免費安裝水缸","examples":[{"en":"Some programmes installed storage tanks free of charge.","zh":"有些計劃免費安裝儲水缸。"},{"en":"To install tanks free of charge means to set up tanks without asking users to pay.","zh":"免費安裝水缸，是指設置水缸而不要求使用者付款。"},{"en":"A charity may install water filters free of charge for poor households.","zh":"慈善機構可能為貧困家庭免費安裝濾水器。"},{"en":"Free installation helps access but may not ensure maintenance.","zh":"免費安裝有助取得設備，但未必確保保養。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unpaid provision of equipment.","zh":"這個短語描述免費提供設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"provide training in","meaning":"提供……方面的培訓","examples":[{"en":"The programmes did not always provide training in maintenance skills.","zh":"這些計劃並不總是提供保養技能方面的培訓。"},{"en":"To provide training in something means to teach people how to do it.","zh":"提供某方面的培訓，是指教人們如何做該事。"},{"en":"A project may provide training in repairing pumps.","zh":"項目可能提供維修水泵方面的培訓。"},{"en":"Training helps users keep systems working after experts leave.","zh":"培訓幫助使用者在專家離開後保持系統運作。"},{"en":"This phrase connects education with practical ability.","zh":"這個短語把教育與實用能力連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"skills needed to","meaning":"做……所需的技能","examples":[{"en":"Residents need the skills required to build and maintain the tanks.","zh":"居民需要建造和保養水缸所需的技能。"},{"en":"Skills needed to do something are the abilities required for that task.","zh":"做某事所需的技能，是完成該任務必需的能力。"},{"en":"The skills needed to repair a tank include mixing cement and checking leaks.","zh":"修理水缸所需的技能包括攪拌水泥和檢查滲漏。"},{"en":"Without the needed skills, a project may not last.","zh":"沒有所需技能，項目可能不能持久。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical capability.","zh":"這個短語聚焦實際能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"maintain something properly","meaning":"妥善保養……","examples":[{"en":"Users must know how to maintain storage tanks properly.","zh":"使用者必須知道如何妥善保養儲水缸。"},{"en":"To maintain something properly means to keep it clean, safe and working well.","zh":"妥善保養某物，是指保持它清潔、安全並運作良好。"},{"en":"Families must maintain gutters properly so rainwater can enter the tank.","zh":"家庭必須妥善保養排水槽，使雨水能流入水缸。"},{"en":"Proper maintenance prevents breakdowns and contamination.","zh":"妥善保養能防止故障和污染。"},{"en":"This phrase describes responsible care of equipment.","zh":"這個短語描述對設備的負責任照顧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"deliberately take a different approach","meaning":"刻意採取不同方法","examples":[{"en":"Practical Action deliberately took a different approach from earlier programmes.","zh":"Practical Action 刻意採取與早期計劃不同的方法。"},{"en":"To deliberately take a different approach means to intentionally choose another method.","zh":"刻意採取不同方法，是指有意選擇另一種方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may deliberately take a different approach after students fail to understand the first explanation.","zh":"學生未能理解第一個解釋後，老師可能刻意採取不同方法。"},{"en":"This phrase shows purposeful change, not accident.","zh":"這個短語顯示有目的改變，而不是偶然。"},{"en":"It often suggests learning from past weaknesses.","zh":"它常暗示從過去弱點中學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"build up a local skills base","meaning":"建立本地技術基礎","examples":[{"en":"The project aimed to build up a local skills base.","zh":"該項目旨在建立本地技術基礎。"},{"en":"To build up a local skills base means to develop useful abilities within the community.","zh":"建立本地技術基礎，是指在社區內發展有用技能。"},{"en":"Training local masons builds up a skills base for future water projects.","zh":"培訓本地泥水匠能為未來水利項目建立技術基礎。"},{"en":"Local skills reduce dependence on outside experts.","zh":"本地技能減少對外來專家的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes capacity building.","zh":"這個短語描述能力建設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"builders and users","meaning":"建造者和使用者","examples":[{"en":"Both builders and users received training through the project.","zh":"建造者和使用者都透過該項目接受培訓。"},{"en":"Builders and users are the people who construct the system and the people who operate it.","zh":"建造者和使用者，是建造系統的人和操作系統的人。"},{"en":"A tank project needs trained builders and informed users.","zh":"水缸項目需要受訓建造者和了解情況的使用者。"},{"en":"Training both groups improves quality and long-term maintenance.","zh":"同時培訓兩組人能改善質素和長期保養。"},{"en":"This phrase includes both makers and owners.","zh":"這個短語包括製作者和擁有者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"create structures and systems","meaning":"建立架構和制度","examples":[{"en":"The organisation helped create structures and systems for local management.","zh":"該組織幫助建立本地管理的架構和制度。"},{"en":"To create structures and systems means to set up organisations, rules and procedures.","zh":"建立架構和制度，是指設立組織、規則和程序。"},{"en":"A village may create systems for collecting maintenance money.","zh":"村落可能建立收取保養費的制度。"},{"en":"Systems help projects continue after the first installation.","zh":"制度幫助項目在最初安裝後繼續運作。"},{"en":"This phrase goes beyond physical construction.","zh":"這個短語超越實體建設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"manage their own schemes","meaning":"管理自己的計劃","examples":[{"en":"Communities were trained to manage their own rainwater-harvesting schemes.","zh":"社區接受培訓，以管理自己的雨水收集計劃。"},{"en":"To manage their own schemes means to organise and run the projects themselves.","zh":"管理自己的計劃，是指自行組織和運作項目。"},{"en":"A village committee may manage its own water scheme after training.","zh":"村委員會受訓後可能管理自己的供水計劃。"},{"en":"Local management can make projects more sustainable.","zh":"本地管理可以令項目更可持續。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses community ownership.","zh":"這個短語強調社區擁有權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be involved throughout","meaning":"全程參與","examples":[{"en":"The community of Muthukandiya was involved throughout the project.","zh":"Muthukandiya 社區全程參與該項目。"},{"en":"To be involved throughout means to participate from beginning to end.","zh":"全程參與，是指由開始到結束都參與。"},{"en":"Parents were involved throughout the school improvement plan.","zh":"家長全程參與學校改善計劃。"},{"en":"Continuous involvement helps people understand and support decisions.","zh":"持續參與幫助人們理解並支持決策。"},{"en":"This phrase describes full participation.","zh":"這個短語描述完整參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"analyse their water problems","meaning":"分析他們的水資源問題","examples":[{"en":"Villagers met to analyse their water problems.","zh":"村民開會分析他們的水資源問題。"},{"en":"To analyse water problems means to examine their causes, effects and possible solutions.","zh":"分析水資源問題，是指檢視其成因、影響和可能解決方法。"},{"en":"A community may analyse water problems by mapping dry wells and walking distances.","zh":"社區可以透過標示乾涸水井和步行距離來分析水問題。"},{"en":"Analysis helps avoid choosing the wrong solution.","zh":"分析有助避免選錯方案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful problem diagnosis.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細診斷問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"develop a mitigation plan","meaning":"制定紓緩計劃","examples":[{"en":"The community developed a mitigation plan for future droughts.","zh":"社區為未來乾旱制定紓緩計劃。"},{"en":"To develop a mitigation plan means to create a plan to reduce future harm.","zh":"制定紓緩計劃，是指創建減少未來傷害的方案。"},{"en":"A town may develop a flood-mitigation plan before the rainy season.","zh":"城鎮可能在雨季前制定防洪紓緩計劃。"},{"en":"Such plans prepare communities before disaster becomes severe.","zh":"這類計劃讓社區在災害變嚴重前作準備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planning for risk reduction.","zh":"這個短語描述風險減低規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"select the technology","meaning":"選擇技術","examples":[{"en":"Villagers helped select the rainwater-harvesting technology.","zh":"村民幫助選擇雨水收集技術。"},{"en":"To select the technology means to choose the technical method or equipment.","zh":"選擇技術，是指選定技術方法或設備。"},{"en":"A school may select solar technology after comparing costs and maintenance needs.","zh":"學校可能在比較成本和保養需要後選擇太陽能技術。"},{"en":"Local users should help select technology because they know local conditions.","zh":"本地使用者應協助選擇技術，因為他們了解本地情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choosing a practical solution.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇實用方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"local masons","meaning":"本地泥水匠","examples":[{"en":"Two local masons were trained to construct household tanks.","zh":"兩名本地泥水匠接受培訓以建造家庭水缸。"},{"en":"Local masons are skilled builders from the community who work with brick, stone or cement.","zh":"本地泥水匠是來自社區、使用磚、石或水泥工作的熟練建造工人。"},{"en":"Local masons can repair tanks quickly because they live nearby.","zh":"本地泥水匠住在附近，因此能迅速修理水缸。"},{"en":"Training local masons keeps knowledge inside the village.","zh":"培訓本地泥水匠能把知識留在村內。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to community-based construction workers.","zh":"這個短語指以社區為本的建造工人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"receive on-the-job training","meaning":"接受在職培訓","examples":[{"en":"The masons received several days of on-the-job training.","zh":"泥水匠接受了數天在職培訓。"},{"en":"To receive on-the-job training means to learn while doing the actual work.","zh":"接受在職培訓，是指在實際工作中學習。"},{"en":"A new mechanic may receive on-the-job training in a repair shop.","zh":"新機械師可能在維修店接受在職培訓。"},{"en":"This kind of training is practical because learners practise real tasks.","zh":"這種培訓很實用，因為學員練習真實任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes workplace-based learning.","zh":"這個短語描述以工作場所為基礎的學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"household storage tanks","meaning":"家庭儲水缸","examples":[{"en":"The project installed 5,000-litre household storage tanks.","zh":"該項目安裝了 5,000 公升家庭儲水缸。"},{"en":"Household storage tanks are water tanks used by individual families.","zh":"家庭儲水缸是個別家庭使用的儲水缸。"},{"en":"A household storage tank can collect roof rainwater during the wet season.","zh":"家庭儲水缸可以在雨季收集屋頂雨水。"},{"en":"Larger tanks provide more protection during long dry periods.","zh":"較大水缸在長期乾旱期間提供更多保障。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to family-level water storage.","zh":"這個短語指家庭層面的儲水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"surface tanks","meaning":"地面儲水缸","examples":[{"en":"Some families installed surface tanks made from ferrocement.","zh":"有些家庭安裝由鋼絲網水泥製成的地面儲水缸。"},{"en":"Surface tanks are storage tanks built above ground level.","zh":"地面儲水缸是建在地面以上的儲水缸。"},{"en":"A surface tank beside a house is easier to inspect than an underground tank.","zh":"房屋旁的地面水缸比地下水缸更容易檢查。"},{"en":"Surface tanks may be cheaper or easier to build in some locations.","zh":"在某些地方，地面水缸可能較便宜或較容易建造。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts above-ground tanks with buried tanks.","zh":"這個短語把地上水缸與埋地水缸作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ferrocement","meaning":"鋼絲網水泥","examples":[{"en":"Ferrocement was used to construct strong surface tanks.","zh":"鋼絲網水泥被用來建造堅固的地面水缸。"},{"en":"Ferrocement is a material made with cement mortar reinforced by wire mesh.","zh":"鋼絲網水泥是由水泥砂漿和鋼絲網加固而成的材料。"},{"en":"Builders may use ferrocement to make thin but strong water tanks.","zh":"建造者可能使用鋼絲網水泥製作薄而堅固的水缸。"},{"en":"It is useful where low-cost durable construction is needed.","zh":"在需要低成本耐用建設的地方，它很有用。"},{"en":"This word refers to a specific construction material.","zh":"這個詞指一種特定建築材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"underground tanks","meaning":"地下儲水缸","examples":[{"en":"Other households chose underground tanks made from brick.","zh":"其他家庭選擇由磚建成的地下儲水缸。"},{"en":"Underground tanks are storage tanks built below the surface of the ground.","zh":"地下儲水缸是建在地面以下的儲水缸。"},{"en":"An underground tank may keep water cooler and save space.","zh":"地下水缸可能保持水較涼並節省空間。"},{"en":"Underground tanks can be harder to inspect than surface tanks.","zh":"地下水缸可能比地面水缸較難檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes buried water-storage structures.","zh":"這個短語描述埋於地下的儲水設施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be made from brick","meaning":"由磚建成","examples":[{"en":"The underground storage tanks were made from brick.","zh":"地下儲水缸由磚建成。"},{"en":"To be made from brick means to be constructed using bricks as the main material.","zh":"由磚建成，是指使用磚作為主要材料建造。"},{"en":"A small well cover may be made from brick and cement.","zh":"小型井蓋可能由磚和水泥建成。"},{"en":"Brick structures can be strong if built and sealed properly.","zh":"如果建造和密封得當，磚結構可以很堅固。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies construction material.","zh":"這個短語指出建築材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"including tank, pipes, gutters and filters","meaning":"包括水缸、水管、排水槽和濾器","examples":[{"en":"Each system included a tank, pipes, gutters and filters.","zh":"每個系統包括水缸、水管、排水槽和濾器。"},{"en":"Including these parts means the system contained all these components.","zh":"包括這些部分，是指系統包含所有這些組件。"},{"en":"A full rainwater system may include a roof, gutters, pipes, a filter and a tank.","zh":"完整雨水系統可能包括屋頂、排水槽、水管、濾器和水缸。"},{"en":"Filters help keep stored water cleaner.","zh":"濾器有助保持儲水較潔淨。"},{"en":"This phrase lists the essential equipment in the system.","zh":"這個短語列出系統中的必要設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be equivalent to","meaning":"相等於……","examples":[{"en":"The cost was equivalent to a month’s income for an average family.","zh":"成本相等於普通家庭一個月收入。"},{"en":"To be equivalent to something means to be equal in value, amount or effect.","zh":"相等於某物，是指在價值、數量或效果上等同。"},{"en":"The repair cost was equivalent to two weeks’ wages.","zh":"維修費相等於兩星期工資。"},{"en":"Equivalence helps readers understand the real burden of a cost.","zh":"等量比較幫助讀者理解成本的真實負擔。"},{"en":"This phrase explains scale through comparison.","zh":"這個短語透過比較解釋規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a month’s income","meaning":"一個月收入","examples":[{"en":"The complete system cost about a month’s income for a village household.","zh":"完整系統成本約等於一個村落家庭一個月收入。"},{"en":"A month’s income is the amount of money a household earns in one month.","zh":"一個月收入是家庭在一個月內賺取的金額。"},{"en":"A repair costing a month’s income is expensive for a poor family.","zh":"對貧困家庭而言，花費一個月收入的維修十分昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show affordability.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示負擔能力。"},{"en":"It connects price with ordinary household earnings.","zh":"它把價格與普通家庭收入連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"just over half the cost","meaning":"略多於一半成本","examples":[{"en":"The community provided just over half the cost of each system.","zh":"社區提供每套系統略多於一半成本。"},{"en":"Just over half the cost means slightly more than 50 percent of the total cost.","zh":"略多於一半成本，是指總成本稍多於百分之五十。"},{"en":"Parents paid just over half the cost of the school trip.","zh":"家長支付學校旅行略多於一半成本。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate share.","zh":"這個短語給出約略比例。"},{"en":"It shows that the community made a substantial contribution.","zh":"它顯示社區作出相當大貢獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the form of","meaning":"以……形式","examples":[{"en":"Families contributed in the form of materials and unskilled labour.","zh":"家庭以材料和非技術勞力形式作出貢獻。"},{"en":"In the form of something means through that type or method.","zh":"以某種形式，是指透過該類型或方法。"},{"en":"Students may contribute in the form of posters, speeches and research.","zh":"學生可以海報、演講和研究形式作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Contributions do not always have to be cash.","zh":"貢獻不一定必須是現金。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the type of contribution.","zh":"這個短語指出貢獻類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"unskilled labour","meaning":"非技術勞力","examples":[{"en":"Villagers contributed materials and unskilled labour to the project.","zh":"村民向項目貢獻材料和非技術勞力。"},{"en":"Unskilled labour is physical work that does not require specialised training.","zh":"非技術勞力是不需要專門培訓的體力工作。"},{"en":"Carrying sand or digging soil may count as unskilled labour.","zh":"搬沙或挖泥可以算作非技術勞力。"},{"en":"Unskilled labour can still be valuable in community projects.","zh":"在社區項目中，非技術勞力仍然很有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts general labour with technical work.","zh":"這個短語把一般勞動與技術工作作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"contribute the rest","meaning":"提供餘下部分","examples":[{"en":"Practical Action South Asia contributed the rest of the cost.","zh":"Practical Action South Asia 提供餘下成本。"},{"en":"To contribute the rest means to provide the remaining amount.","zh":"提供餘下部分，是指提供剩餘金額。"},{"en":"The school paid half the fee, and a charity contributed the rest.","zh":"學校支付一半費用，慈善機構提供餘下部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shared funding.","zh":"這個短語描述共同資助。"},{"en":"It shows how a total cost is completed.","zh":"它顯示總成本如何被補足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"skilled labour","meaning":"技術勞工","examples":[{"en":"The organisation paid for materials, transport and skilled labour.","zh":"該組織支付材料、運輸和技術勞工費用。"},{"en":"Skilled labour is work requiring training, experience or technical ability.","zh":"技術勞工是需要培訓、經驗或技術能力的工作。"},{"en":"Building a waterproof storage tank requires skilled labour.","zh":"建造防水儲水缸需要技術勞工。"},{"en":"Skilled labour usually costs more because it needs expertise.","zh":"技術勞工通常成本較高，因為需要專業知識。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts trained work with unskilled labour.","zh":"這個短語把受訓工作與非技術勞力作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"learn how to use and maintain","meaning":"學習如何使用和保養","examples":[{"en":"Households learned how to use and maintain the tanks.","zh":"家庭學習如何使用和保養水缸。"},{"en":"To learn how to use and maintain something means to know how to operate and care for it.","zh":"學習如何使用和保養某物，是指知道如何操作和照顧它。"},{"en":"Families learned how to clean filters and check pipes.","zh":"家庭學會如何清潔濾器和檢查水管。"},{"en":"Training users prevents equipment from failing through misuse.","zh":"培訓使用者可防止設備因誤用而失效。"},{"en":"This phrase links use with long-term care.","zh":"這個短語把使用與長期照顧連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"keep water supplies clean","meaning":"保持供水潔淨","examples":[{"en":"The community was trained to keep domestic water supplies clean.","zh":"社區接受培訓，以保持家居供水潔淨。"},{"en":"To keep water supplies clean means to prevent stored or collected water from becoming contaminated.","zh":"保持供水潔淨，是指防止儲存或收集的水受到污染。"},{"en":"Covering tanks helps keep water supplies clean.","zh":"蓋好水缸有助保持供水潔淨。"},{"en":"Clean water reduces illness such as diarrhoea.","zh":"清潔食水能減少肚瀉等疾病。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on hygiene and safety.","zh":"這個短語聚焦衛生和安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be set up to run","meaning":"成立以管理……","examples":[{"en":"A village society was set up to run the project.","zh":"一個村落協會被成立以管理該項目。"},{"en":"To be set up to run something means to be established in order to manage it.","zh":"成立以管理某事，是指建立一個機構來負責它。"},{"en":"A committee was set up to run the school garden.","zh":"一個委員會被成立以管理學校花園。"},{"en":"Local organisations help projects continue after outside support ends.","zh":"本地組織幫助項目在外來支援結束後繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating a management body.","zh":"這個短語描述建立管理機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rainwater-harvesting society","meaning":"雨水收集協會","examples":[{"en":"The village rainwater-harvesting society coordinated the local scheme.","zh":"村落雨水收集協會協調本地計劃。"},{"en":"A rainwater-harvesting society is a local group organised to manage rainwater collection.","zh":"雨水收集協會是管理雨水收集的本地組織。"},{"en":"The society may collect fees, arrange repairs and monitor water quality.","zh":"協會可能收費、安排維修和監察水質。"},{"en":"Such groups support community ownership.","zh":"這類組織支持社區擁有權。"},{"en":"This phrase names a local water-management organisation.","zh":"這個短語命名本地水資源管理組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"to date","meaning":"至今","examples":[{"en":"To date, dozens of families have installed storage tanks.","zh":"至今，已有數十個家庭安裝儲水缸。"},{"en":"To date means up to the present time.","zh":"至今，是指直到目前為止。"},{"en":"To date, the school has trained fifty student volunteers.","zh":"至今，學校已培訓五十名學生義工。"},{"en":"This phrase reports progress so far.","zh":"這個短語報告目前進展。"},{"en":"It suggests that more may happen later.","zh":"它暗示日後可能還會有更多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in and around","meaning":"在……及其周邊","examples":[{"en":"Families in and around Muthukandiya have benefited from the project.","zh":"Muthukandiya 及其周邊的家庭已受惠於該項目。"},{"en":"In and around a place means inside that place and in nearby areas.","zh":"在某地及其周邊，是指在該地內以及附近地區。"},{"en":"People in and around the town used the new clinic.","zh":"城鎮及其周邊的人使用新診所。"},{"en":"This phrase broadens the area slightly beyond one location.","zh":"這個短語把範圍略微擴展到一個地方之外。"},{"en":"It is useful when benefits spread to neighbouring communities.","zh":"當好處擴散到鄰近社區時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"evaluations show clearly that","meaning":"評估清楚顯示","examples":[{"en":"Evaluations show clearly that storage tanks improve household water supplies.","zh":"評估清楚顯示，儲水缸改善家庭供水。"},{"en":"Evaluations show clearly that means assessments provide strong evidence for a conclusion.","zh":"評估清楚顯示，是指評估為某結論提供有力證據。"},{"en":"Evaluations show clearly that extra reading improves vocabulary.","zh":"評估清楚顯示，額外閱讀能改善詞彙。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the result is not just an opinion.","zh":"這個短語暗示結果不只是意見。"},{"en":"It is useful in reports and project reviews.","zh":"它適合用於報告和項目檢討。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"considerably more water","meaning":"多得多的水","examples":[{"en":"Households with tanks have considerably more water for domestic needs.","zh":"有水缸的家庭有多得多的水供家居需要。"},{"en":"Considerably more water means much more water, not just a little more.","zh":"多得多的水，是指水量大幅增加，而不只是多一點。"},{"en":"A family with a new tank may have considerably more water during dry months.","zh":"有新水缸的家庭在乾旱月份可能有多得多的水。"},{"en":"More water can reduce walking time and improve hygiene.","zh":"更多水能減少步行時間並改善衛生。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a large increase.","zh":"這個短語強調大幅增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rely entirely on","meaning":"完全依賴……","examples":[{"en":"Some households still rely entirely on wells and ponds.","zh":"有些家庭仍完全依賴水井和池塘。"},{"en":"To rely entirely on something means to depend only on it.","zh":"完全依賴某物，是指只依靠它。"},{"en":"A village that relies entirely on one well is vulnerable if that well fails.","zh":"完全依賴一口井的村落，如果那口井失效便很脆弱。"},{"en":"Complete reliance on one source can be risky.","zh":"完全依賴單一來源可能有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase shows total dependence.","zh":"這個短語顯示完全依靠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"during the driest months","meaning":"在最乾旱的月份","examples":[{"en":"The tanks are particularly valuable during the driest months.","zh":"水缸在最乾旱的月份尤其有價值。"},{"en":"During the driest months means in the months with the least rainfall.","zh":"在最乾旱的月份，是指雨量最少的月份。"},{"en":"Stored water is most important during the driest months of the year.","zh":"儲存水在一年中最乾旱的月份最重要。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the period of greatest need.","zh":"這個短語指出需求最大的時期。"},{"en":"It is common in drought and water-supply discussions.","zh":"它常見於乾旱和供水討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"up to twice as much water","meaning":"多達兩倍的水","examples":[{"en":"Households with tanks may have up to twice as much water available.","zh":"有水缸的家庭可用水量可能多達兩倍。"},{"en":"Up to twice as much water means as much as double the amount, though possibly less.","zh":"多達兩倍的水，是指最多可達原來兩倍，但也可能較少。"},{"en":"A larger tank may provide up to twice as much water as a smaller one.","zh":"較大水缸可能提供比小水缸多達兩倍的水。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a maximum possible increase.","zh":"這個短語給出最大可能增幅。"},{"en":"It suggests a substantial improvement.","zh":"它暗示大幅改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take full advantage of","meaning":"充分利用……","examples":[{"en":"Nandawathie took full advantage of the opportunities created by the project.","zh":"Nandawathie 充分利用該項目創造的機會。"},{"en":"To take full advantage of something means to use an opportunity as much as possible.","zh":"充分利用某事，是指盡可能使用某個機會。"},{"en":"A student may take full advantage of free tutoring by attending every session.","zh":"學生可以透過出席每節課充分利用免費補習。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active and effective use.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動且有效使用。"},{"en":"It often describes someone who makes the most of a chance.","zh":"它常描述某人善用機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"opportunities brought by","meaning":"由……帶來的機會","examples":[{"en":"Rainwater harvesting brought new economic opportunities to her family.","zh":"雨水收集為她的家庭帶來新的經濟機會。"},{"en":"Opportunities brought by something are chances created as a result of it.","zh":"由某事帶來的機會，是因它而產生的可能性。"},{"en":"A new road may bring business opportunities to a village.","zh":"新道路可能為村落帶來商業機會。"},{"en":"Better water supply can create opportunities for farming and small trade.","zh":"更好供水可以創造農業和小買賣機會。"},{"en":"This phrase links improvement with new possibilities.","zh":"這個短語把改善與新可能性連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a better water supply","meaning":"更完善的供水","examples":[{"en":"A better water supply enabled her to grow vegetables.","zh":"更完善的供水使她能夠種植蔬菜。"},{"en":"A better water supply means more reliable, cleaner or more convenient access to water.","zh":"更完善的供水，是指更可靠、更潔淨或更方便取得水。"},{"en":"A better water supply can allow families to plant crops near home.","zh":"更完善的供水可以讓家庭在家附近種植作物。"},{"en":"Improved supply affects health, work and education.","zh":"供水改善會影響健康、工作和教育。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improvement in access to water.","zh":"這個短語描述取水條件改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"close at hand","meaning":"就在附近；隨手可得","examples":[{"en":"The family now has a reliable water supply close at hand.","zh":"這個家庭現在有可靠供水就在附近。"},{"en":"Close at hand means nearby and easy to reach.","zh":"就在附近或隨手可得，是指距離近且容易取得。"},{"en":"A water tap close at hand saves a family hours of walking.","zh":"附近有水龍頭可以為家庭節省數小時步行時間。"},{"en":"When water is close at hand, daily life becomes safer and easier.","zh":"當水源隨手可得，日常生活會更安全和容易。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses convenience and proximity.","zh":"這個短語強調方便和接近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"begin by doing something","meaning":"先從做某事開始","examples":[{"en":"She began by growing a few vegetables beside her home.","zh":"她先從在家旁種幾種蔬菜開始。"},{"en":"To begin by doing something means to start with that first action.","zh":"先從做某事開始，是指以該第一步行動開始。"},{"en":"A student may begin by learning ten useful phrases each day.","zh":"學生可以先從每天學十個實用短語開始。"},{"en":"Small beginnings can lead to larger changes.","zh":"小開始可以帶來更大改變。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the first step in a process.","zh":"這個短語引入過程中的第一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"income from selling","meaning":"銷售……所得的收入","examples":[{"en":"The income from selling vegetables helped her start a business.","zh":"銷售蔬菜所得的收入幫助她創業。"},{"en":"Income from selling something is money earned by selling it.","zh":"銷售某物所得的收入，是售賣它賺到的金錢。"},{"en":"Income from selling eggs can help a family pay school fees.","zh":"銷售雞蛋所得收入可以幫助家庭支付學費。"},{"en":"Small sales can create capital for bigger activities.","zh":"小額銷售可以為更大活動創造資金。"},{"en":"This phrase links trade with earnings.","zh":"這個短語把買賣與收入連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"open a small shop","meaning":"開設小店","examples":[{"en":"She used her additional income to open a small shop.","zh":"她用額外收入開設小店。"},{"en":"To open a small shop means to start a small retail business.","zh":"開設小店，是指開始經營小型零售生意。"},{"en":"A villager may open a small shop selling vegetables, tea and basic goods.","zh":"村民可能開設售賣蔬菜、茶和基本用品的小店。"},{"en":"A small shop can add income beyond farming.","zh":"小店可以在農業以外增加收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes starting a local business.","zh":"這個短語描述開始本地小生意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"on her doorstep","meaning":"就在家門前","examples":[{"en":"She opened a small shop on her doorstep.","zh":"她就在家門前開設小店。"},{"en":"On her doorstep means very close to her home, literally or figuratively.","zh":"就在家門前，是指非常靠近她的家，可按字面或比喻理解。"},{"en":"A woman may sell vegetables on her doorstep to neighbours.","zh":"一名婦女可能就在家門前向鄰居賣蔬菜。"},{"en":"Having work on the doorstep saves travel time.","zh":"工作就在家門前可以節省交通時間。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses closeness to home.","zh":"這個短語強調靠近住所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"increase earnings still further","meaning":"令收入進一步增加","examples":[{"en":"The shop increased her earnings still further.","zh":"小店令她的收入進一步增加。"},{"en":"To increase earnings still further means to raise income even more.","zh":"令收入進一步增加，是指讓收入再提高。"},{"en":"After selling vegetables, opening a shop increased the family’s earnings still further.","zh":"售賣蔬菜後，開店令家庭收入進一步增加。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a second stage of improvement.","zh":"這個短語顯示第二階段改善。"},{"en":"It often follows an earlier income gain.","zh":"它常接在早前收入增長之後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"enable someone to apply for","meaning":"使某人能夠申請……","examples":[{"en":"Her improved income enabled her to apply for a loan.","zh":"她改善了的收入使她能夠申請貸款。"},{"en":"To enable someone to apply for something means to make it possible for them to request it.","zh":"使某人能夠申請某物，是指令他們有可能提出申請。"},{"en":"A stable salary may enable a worker to apply for housing assistance.","zh":"穩定薪金可能使工人能夠申請住房援助。"},{"en":"Better income can improve access to financial services.","zh":"更好收入可以改善取得金融服務的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase connects ability with changed circumstances.","zh":"這個短語把能力與情況改變連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"apply for a loan","meaning":"申請貸款","examples":[{"en":"She applied for a loan to install solar power.","zh":"她申請貸款以安裝太陽能系統。"},{"en":"To apply for a loan means to request borrowed money from a lender.","zh":"申請貸款，是指向貸款人要求借款。"},{"en":"A farmer may apply for a loan to buy seeds or equipment.","zh":"農民可能申請貸款購買種子或設備。"},{"en":"Loan applications usually require proof of income or repayment ability.","zh":"貸款申請通常需要收入證明或還款能力證明。"},{"en":"This phrase describes requesting financial support.","zh":"這個短語描述要求財務支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"install solar power","meaning":"安裝太陽能系統","examples":[{"en":"The loan enabled her to install solar power in her house.","zh":"這筆貸款使她能在家中安裝太陽能系統。"},{"en":"To install solar power means to set up equipment that uses sunlight to generate electricity.","zh":"安裝太陽能系統，是指設置使用陽光發電的設備。"},{"en":"A family may install solar power to light the home at night.","zh":"家庭可能安裝太陽能系統以在夜間照明。"},{"en":"Solar power can reduce dependence on unreliable electricity supplies.","zh":"太陽能可以減少對不穩定電力供應的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to setting up a renewable-energy system.","zh":"這個短語指設置可再生能源系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"think of doing something","meaning":"考慮做某事","examples":[{"en":"She is now thinking of building another storage tank.","zh":"她現在正考慮建造另一個儲水缸。"},{"en":"To think of doing something means to consider doing it.","zh":"考慮做某事，是指思考是否去做它。"},{"en":"A student may think of joining a debate club to improve speaking.","zh":"學生可能考慮加入辯論學會來改善說話能力。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a possible future plan.","zh":"這個短語暗示可能的未來計劃。"},{"en":"It does not mean the action has already happened.","zh":"它不表示行動已經發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"feel safer","meaning":"感到更安全","examples":[{"en":"She feels safer because she no longer fetches water at isolated times.","zh":"她感到更安全，因為她不再需要在偏僻時段取水。"},{"en":"To feel safer means to feel less exposed to danger or fear.","zh":"感到更安全，是指較少感到暴露於危險或恐懼。"},{"en":"A child may feel safer walking to school with friends.","zh":"孩子和朋友一起上學時可能感到更安全。"},{"en":"Better water access can improve women’s safety.","zh":"更好取水條件可以改善婦女安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional and physical security.","zh":"這個短語描述情感和身體安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"no longer have to","meaning":"不再需要……","examples":[{"en":"She no longer has to walk to the village well before dawn.","zh":"她不再需要在黎明前步行到村中水井。"},{"en":"No longer have to means do not need to do something anymore.","zh":"不再需要做某事，是指現在已沒有必要做它。"},{"en":"With a nearby tap, children no longer have to fetch water far away.","zh":"有了附近水龍頭，兒童不再需要到遠處取水。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights relief from a previous burden.","zh":"這個短語突出從過去負擔中解脫。"},{"en":"It contrasts past necessity with present improvement.","zh":"它對比過去需要與現在改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"early morning or late evening","meaning":"清晨或晚上較夜時","examples":[{"en":"Fetching water in the early morning or late evening made her feel unsafe.","zh":"在清晨或晚上較夜時取水令她感到不安全。"},{"en":"Early morning or late evening means very early or quite late in the day.","zh":"清晨或晚上較夜時，是指一天中很早或相當晚的時間。"},{"en":"Walking alone in the early morning or late evening may feel risky.","zh":"清晨或晚上較夜時獨自行走可能令人覺得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests times when fewer people are around.","zh":"這個短語常暗示周圍人較少的時段。"},{"en":"It helps explain safety concerns.","zh":"它有助解釋安全憂慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"complain of diarrhoea","meaning":"訴說患有肚瀉","examples":[{"en":"Her children no longer complain so often of diarrhoea.","zh":"她的孩子不再那麼常訴說患有肚瀉。"},{"en":"To complain of diarrhoea means to say that one is suffering from diarrhoea.","zh":"訴說患有肚瀉，是指說自己正受肚瀉困擾。"},{"en":"Children may complain of diarrhoea after drinking unsafe water.","zh":"兒童飲用不安全水後可能訴說患有肚瀉。"},{"en":"Fewer complaints can suggest better water quality or hygiene.","zh":"投訴減少可能顯示水質或衛生改善。"},{"en":"This phrase reports a health symptom.","zh":"這個短語報告健康症狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have more time for","meaning":"有更多時間做……","examples":[{"en":"Her daughter now has more time for schoolwork.","zh":"她的女兒現在有更多時間做功課。"},{"en":"To have more time for something means to have extra time available for it.","zh":"有更多時間做某事，是指有額外時間可用於該事。"},{"en":"Children have more time for study when they no longer spend hours fetching water.","zh":"當兒童不再花數小時取水，他們有更多時間學習。"},{"en":"Time saved from daily chores can improve education.","zh":"從日常雜務中節省時間可以改善教育。"},{"en":"This phrase connects reduced burden with opportunity.","zh":"這個短語把負擔減少與機會連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in the short term","meaning":"短期而言","examples":[{"en":"In the short term, the project has clearly been successful.","zh":"短期而言，該項目明顯成功。"},{"en":"In the short term means over a relatively near or immediate period.","zh":"短期而言，是指在相對接近或即時的時期內。"},{"en":"In the short term, free water tanks can quickly reduce walking time.","zh":"短期而言，免費水缸能迅速減少步行時間。"},{"en":"Short-term success does not always guarantee long-term sustainability.","zh":"短期成功不一定保證長期可持續。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts immediate results with future outcomes.","zh":"這個短語對比即時結果與未來結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"on a small scale","meaning":"以小規模形式","examples":[{"en":"The initiative has succeeded on a small scale.","zh":"該計劃已以小規模形式成功。"},{"en":"On a small scale means involving a limited number of people or places.","zh":"以小規模形式，是指涉及有限人數或地點。"},{"en":"A pilot project may succeed on a small scale before expanding.","zh":"試驗項目可能先以小規模形式成功，再擴展。"},{"en":"Small-scale success is useful but may not prove that large-scale expansion is easy.","zh":"小規模成功有用，但未必證明大規模擴展容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited scope.","zh":"這個短語描述有限範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the challenge lies in","meaning":"挑戰在於……","examples":[{"en":"The challenge lies in expanding the project sustainably.","zh":"挑戰在於以可持續方式擴展項目。"},{"en":"The challenge lies in something means that is the main difficult part.","zh":"挑戰在於某事，是指那就是主要困難部分。"},{"en":"The challenge lies in keeping students motivated after the first week.","zh":"挑戰在於第一星期後仍讓學生保持動力。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where the real problem is.","zh":"這個短語指出真正問題所在。"},{"en":"It is useful for analysis and evaluation.","zh":"它適合用於分析和評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make initiatives sustainable","meaning":"令計劃可持續","examples":[{"en":"Organisers need to make local water initiatives sustainable.","zh":"組織者需要令本地水資源計劃可持續。"},{"en":"To make initiatives sustainable means to ensure projects can continue without failing quickly.","zh":"令計劃可持續，是指確保項目能持續，而不會很快失敗。"},{"en":"Training villagers and creating funds can make water initiatives sustainable.","zh":"培訓村民和建立基金可以令水資源計劃可持續。"},{"en":"Sustainability requires skills, money and local management.","zh":"可持續性需要技能、金錢和本地管理。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on long-term survival of projects.","zh":"這個短語聚焦項目的長期存續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"expand their coverage","meaning":"擴大覆蓋範圍","examples":[{"en":"The project must expand its coverage to reach more villages.","zh":"該項目必須擴大覆蓋範圍，以惠及更多村落。"},{"en":"To expand coverage means to include more people, places or services.","zh":"擴大覆蓋範圍，是指包括更多人、地方或服務。"},{"en":"A health campaign may expand its coverage from one town to the whole district.","zh":"健康宣傳活動可能由一個城鎮擴大至整個地區。"},{"en":"Expansion requires more money, workers and organisation.","zh":"擴展需要更多金錢、人手和組織。"},{"en":"This phrase describes widening reach.","zh":"這個短語描述擴大影響範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at a purely technical level","meaning":"純粹從技術層面來說","examples":[{"en":"At a purely technical level, the system is sustainable.","zh":"純粹從技術層面來說，該系統是可持續的。"},{"en":"At a purely technical level means considering only the technology, not money or organisation.","zh":"純粹從技術層面來說，是指只考慮技術，而不考慮金錢或組織。"},{"en":"A machine may work well at a technical level but fail because no one can afford repairs.","zh":"一部機器在技術層面可能運作良好，但因無人負擔維修而失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase separates technical feasibility from social or financial issues.","zh":"這個短語把技術可行性與社會或財務問題分開。"},{"en":"It is useful for careful evaluation.","zh":"它適合用於謹慎評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"evidently sustainable","meaning":"明顯可持續的","examples":[{"en":"Rainwater harvesting is evidently sustainable from a technical perspective.","zh":"從技術角度看，雨水收集明顯可持續。"},{"en":"Evidently sustainable means clearly able to continue or be maintained.","zh":"明顯可持續，是指明顯能夠持續或被維持。"},{"en":"A simple hand pump may be evidently sustainable if locals can repair it easily.","zh":"如果本地人容易修理，簡單手泵可能明顯可持續。"},{"en":"The word evidently suggests the evidence is fairly clear.","zh":"“evidently” 暗示證據相當清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clear sustainability in one respect.","zh":"這個短語描述某方面清楚的可持續性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"skills required to","meaning":"做……所需的技能","examples":[{"en":"The skills required to build the tanks can be learned fairly easily.","zh":"建造水缸所需的技能可以相當容易學會。"},{"en":"Skills required to do something are abilities needed for that task.","zh":"做某事所需的技能，是完成該任務需要的能力。"},{"en":"The skills required to clean filters can be taught in one workshop.","zh":"清潔濾器所需的技能可以在一次工作坊中教授。"},{"en":"If required skills are simple, projects can spread more easily.","zh":"如果所需技能簡單，項目便較容易擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies necessary abilities.","zh":"這個短語指出必要能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be taught fairly easily","meaning":"相當容易教授","examples":[{"en":"Basic construction and maintenance skills can be taught fairly easily.","zh":"基本建造和保養技能可以相當容易教授。"},{"en":"To be taught fairly easily means people can learn it without extreme difficulty.","zh":"相當容易教授，是指人們可以不太困難地學會。"},{"en":"Simple tank-cleaning methods can be taught fairly easily to households.","zh":"簡單水缸清潔方法可以相當容易教給家庭。"},{"en":"Easy training helps communities become independent.","zh":"容易培訓有助社區變得獨立。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests practical transferability.","zh":"這個短語暗示技能容易傳授。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be shared by","meaning":"可由……傳授","examples":[{"en":"The trained masons can share their skills with other workers.","zh":"受訓泥水匠可以把技能傳授給其他工人。"},{"en":"To be shared by someone means to be passed on or made available by that person.","zh":"可由某人傳授，是指由該人傳遞或提供給別人。"},{"en":"Repair knowledge can be shared by trained villagers.","zh":"維修知識可由受訓村民傳授。"},{"en":"Shared skills help projects spread without constant outside help.","zh":"技能分享能幫助項目在不斷依賴外援下擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes knowledge transfer.","zh":"這個短語描述知識轉移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"find work with","meaning":"在……找到工作","examples":[{"en":"The masons are now finding work with other development agencies.","zh":"泥水匠現在正在其他發展援助機構找到工作。"},{"en":"To find work with an organisation means to get jobs or paid tasks from it.","zh":"在某組織找到工作，是指從該組織得到工作或有薪任務。"},{"en":"A trained technician may find work with a local water charity.","zh":"受訓技術員可能在本地水務慈善機構找到工作。"},{"en":"Training can create employment beyond the original project.","zh":"培訓可以在原項目以外創造就業。"},{"en":"This phrase links new skills with job opportunities.","zh":"這個短語把新技能與工作機會連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"development agencies","meaning":"發展援助機構","examples":[{"en":"Development agencies have employed the trained masons on other projects.","zh":"發展援助機構已在其他項目中聘用受訓泥水匠。"},{"en":"Development agencies are organisations that support social and economic improvement projects.","zh":"發展援助機構是支持社會和經濟改善項目的組織。"},{"en":"A development agency may fund water, health or education programmes.","zh":"發展援助機構可能資助水務、健康或教育計劃。"},{"en":"These agencies often work with poor or rural communities.","zh":"這些機構常與貧困或農村社區合作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organisations involved in development work.","zh":"這個短語指參與發展工作的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"non-structural elements","meaning":"非硬件元素","examples":[{"en":"The non-structural elements of the project present greater difficulties.","zh":"該項目的非硬件元素帶來更大困難。"},{"en":"Non-structural elements are parts not involving physical buildings or equipment.","zh":"非硬件元素是不涉及實體建築或設備的部分。"},{"en":"Funding rules and community organisation are non-structural elements.","zh":"資金規則和社區組織都是非硬件元素。"},{"en":"These elements can be harder than construction because they depend on behaviour.","zh":"這些元素可能比建造更難，因為它們取決於行為。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts social systems with hardware.","zh":"這個短語把社會制度與硬件作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"financial and organisational aspects","meaning":"財政及組織層面","examples":[{"en":"The financial and organisational aspects present a bigger challenge.","zh":"財政及組織層面構成更大挑戰。"},{"en":"Financial and organisational aspects are the money-related and management-related parts of a project.","zh":"財政及組織層面，是項目中與金錢和管理相關的部分。"},{"en":"A water scheme needs both funds and a committee to manage repairs.","zh":"供水計劃既需要資金，也需要委員會管理維修。"},{"en":"Good technology can fail if finance and organisation are weak.","zh":"如果財政和組織薄弱，好技術也會失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to non-technical project conditions.","zh":"這個短語指非技術性的項目條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"present a bigger challenge","meaning":"構成更大挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Community financing may present a bigger challenge than construction.","zh":"社區融資可能比建設構成更大挑戰。"},{"en":"To present a bigger challenge means to be more difficult than something else.","zh":"構成更大挑戰，是指比其他事情更困難。"},{"en":"Keeping volunteers active may present a bigger challenge than recruiting them.","zh":"讓義工持續投入可能比招募他們構成更大挑戰。"},{"en":"Some problems are harder because they require long-term cooperation.","zh":"有些問題更難，因為需要長期合作。"},{"en":"This phrase compares difficulty levels.","zh":"這個短語比較困難程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"revolving fund","meaning":"循環基金","examples":[{"en":"A revolving fund was created to finance maintenance and new tanks.","zh":"一個循環基金被建立，以資助保養和新水缸。"},{"en":"A revolving fund is a pool of money that is reused as people contribute or repay money.","zh":"循環基金是一筆會在人們供款或還款後重複使用的資金。"},{"en":"A village may use a revolving fund to pay for repairs and future installations.","zh":"村落可能使用循環基金支付維修和未來安裝費用。"},{"en":"Such funds can support projects over time if people contribute regularly.","zh":"如果人們定期供款，這類基金可長期支持項目。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a continuing community finance system.","zh":"這個短語指持續性的社區財務系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"households that had already benefited","meaning":"已經受惠的家庭","examples":[{"en":"Households that had already benefited were asked to contribute monthly.","zh":"已經受惠的家庭被要求每月供款。"},{"en":"Households that had already benefited are families that had already received help or advantages from the project.","zh":"已經受惠的家庭，是已從項目得到幫助或好處的家庭。"},{"en":"Families with installed tanks may be asked to support future households.","zh":"已安裝水缸的家庭可能被要求支持未來家庭。"},{"en":"This arrangement spreads benefits through community contribution.","zh":"這種安排透過社區供款擴散好處。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies earlier beneficiaries.","zh":"這個短語指出較早受益者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"contribute a small monthly amount","meaning":"每月小額供款","examples":[{"en":"Each household agreed to contribute a small monthly amount.","zh":"每個家庭同意每月小額供款。"},{"en":"To contribute a small monthly amount means to pay a little money every month.","zh":"每月小額供款，是指每個月支付少量金錢。"},{"en":"Families may contribute a small monthly amount to repair the village pump.","zh":"家庭可能每月小額供款，用來修理村中水泵。"},{"en":"Small regular payments can build a useful fund over time.","zh":"定期小額付款可以隨時間建立有用基金。"},{"en":"This phrase describes affordable ongoing contribution.","zh":"這個短語描述可負擔的持續供款。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"pay for maintenance and repairs","meaning":"支付保養及維修費用","examples":[{"en":"The fund was intended to pay for maintenance and repairs.","zh":"該基金旨在支付保養及維修費用。"},{"en":"To pay for maintenance and repairs means to cover the cost of keeping equipment working and fixing damage.","zh":"支付保養及維修費用，是指承擔保持設備運作和修復損壞的成本。"},{"en":"A community fund can pay for maintenance and repairs of water tanks.","zh":"社區基金可以支付水缸的保養及維修費用。"},{"en":"Without repair money, even good systems may stop working.","zh":"沒有維修資金，即使好系統也可能停止運作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on long-term upkeep costs.","zh":"這個短語聚焦長期維護成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"prove difficult to","meaning":"證明難以……","examples":[{"en":"It proved difficult to persuade households to contribute regularly.","zh":"事實證明，說服家庭定期供款很困難。"},{"en":"Prove difficult to means turn out to be hard to do.","zh":"證明難以做某事，是指結果顯示它很難做到。"},{"en":"It proved difficult to keep the committee active after the first year.","zh":"事實證明，第一年後保持委員會活躍很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests difficulty discovered through experience.","zh":"這個短語暗示困難是從經驗中發現的。"},{"en":"It is often used in project evaluation.","zh":"它常用於項目評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"recover costs from","meaning":"從……收回成本","examples":[{"en":"Recovering costs from non-income-generating projects is difficult.","zh":"從不產生收入的項目收回成本很困難。"},{"en":"To recover costs from something means to get back money spent on it.","zh":"從某事收回成本，是指取回花在它上面的金錢。"},{"en":"A charity may struggle to recover costs from a free health programme.","zh":"慈善機構可能難以從免費健康計劃收回成本。"},{"en":"Cost recovery is easier when a project creates direct income.","zh":"當項目直接產生收入，收回成本較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes financial repayment or reimbursement.","zh":"這個短語描述財務回收或補償。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"interventions","meaning":"干預措施；支援項目","examples":[{"en":"Community-development interventions do not always generate direct income.","zh":"社區發展干預措施並不總是直接產生收入。"},{"en":"Interventions are planned actions designed to improve a problem situation.","zh":"干預措施是為改善問題情況而設計的有計劃行動。"},{"en":"A nutrition programme can be an intervention for malnourished children.","zh":"營養計劃可以是針對營養不良兒童的干預措施。"},{"en":"Some interventions improve health or safety without earning money.","zh":"有些干預措施改善健康或安全，但不賺錢。"},{"en":"This word is common in development and policy contexts.","zh":"這個詞常見於發展和政策語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"generate income directly","meaning":"直接產生收入","examples":[{"en":"The water project does not generate income directly for every household.","zh":"該供水項目並不為每個家庭直接產生收入。"},{"en":"To generate income directly means to produce money in a clear and immediate way.","zh":"直接產生收入，是指以清楚和即時方式帶來金錢。"},{"en":"A vegetable garden may generate income directly if the family sells the produce.","zh":"如果家庭出售農產品，菜園可能直接產生收入。"},{"en":"Clean water may bring benefits even if it does not create cash for everyone.","zh":"清潔用水即使不為每個人創造現金，也可能帶來好處。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts direct earnings with indirect benefits.","zh":"這個短語對比直接收入與間接好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a difficult proposition","meaning":"困難的做法；棘手問題","examples":[{"en":"Recovering costs from such projects is a difficult proposition.","zh":"從這類項目收回成本是一個困難的做法。"},{"en":"A difficult proposition is an idea or task that is hard to carry out successfully.","zh":"困難的做法或棘手問題，是難以成功執行的想法或任務。"},{"en":"Asking poor households to pay regular fees can be a difficult proposition.","zh":"要求貧困家庭定期繳費可能是棘手問題。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests practical difficulty, not impossibility.","zh":"這個短語暗示實際困難，而不是不可能。"},{"en":"It is often used in formal analysis.","zh":"它常用於正式分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be overcome if","meaning":"如果……便可克服","examples":[{"en":"The problem may be overcome if the scheme is clearly explained.","zh":"如果清楚解釋該計劃，問題便可克服。"},{"en":"To be overcome if something happens means the difficulty can be solved under that condition.","zh":"如果某事發生便可克服，是指困難在該條件下可以被解決。"},{"en":"Fear of payment may be overcome if families understand how the fund works.","zh":"如果家庭明白基金如何運作，對付款的恐懼便可克服。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a possible solution.","zh":"這個短語引入可能解決方法。"},{"en":"It links condition with success.","zh":"它把條件與成功連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"explain something more fully","meaning":"更詳細地解釋……","examples":[{"en":"Organisers should explain the funding system more fully.","zh":"組織者應更詳細地解釋資金制度。"},{"en":"To explain something more fully means to give more complete details about it.","zh":"更詳細地解釋某事，是指提供更完整細節。"},{"en":"Teachers should explain homework rules more fully if students misunderstand them.","zh":"如果學生誤解功課規則，老師應更詳細解釋。"},{"en":"Fuller explanation can increase trust and cooperation.","zh":"更完整解釋能增加信任和合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clearer communication.","zh":"這個短語描述更清晰溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"at the outset","meaning":"一開始","examples":[{"en":"The revolving-fund concept should be explained at the outset.","zh":"循環基金概念應一開始便解釋。"},{"en":"At the outset means at the beginning.","zh":"一開始，是指在開始時。"},{"en":"Project rules should be explained at the outset to avoid later confusion.","zh":"項目規則應一開始便解釋，以避免日後混亂。"},{"en":"Early explanation helps people know what they are agreeing to.","zh":"早期解釋幫助人們知道自己同意甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the timing of an action.","zh":"這個短語指出行動時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"demonstration project","meaning":"示範計劃","examples":[{"en":"The Muthukandiya initiative was planned as a demonstration project.","zh":"Muthukandiya 計劃被規劃為示範計劃。"},{"en":"A demonstration project is a project designed to show that an idea can work.","zh":"示範計劃是用來顯示某個想法可行的項目。"},{"en":"A village may run a demonstration project before expanding a water system elsewhere.","zh":"村落可能先推行示範計劃，再把供水系統擴展到其他地方。"},{"en":"Demonstration projects help other communities learn from results.","zh":"示範計劃幫助其他社區從結果中學習。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a model project.","zh":"這個短語指模型項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"community-based drought mitigation","meaning":"以社區為本的旱災紓緩","examples":[{"en":"The project demonstrated community-based drought mitigation.","zh":"該項目展示了以社區為本的旱災紓緩。"},{"en":"Community-based drought mitigation means reducing drought harm through local participation and management.","zh":"以社區為本的旱災紓緩，是透過本地參與和管理減少旱災傷害。"},{"en":"Villagers building and maintaining tanks is community-based drought mitigation.","zh":"村民建造並保養水缸，就是以社區為本的旱災紓緩。"},{"en":"Community involvement can make solutions more suitable and sustainable.","zh":"社區參與可以令方案更合適和可持續。"},{"en":"This phrase combines local action with drought protection.","zh":"這個短語結合本地行動與抗旱保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be feasible","meaning":"可行","examples":[{"en":"The project showed that local rainwater harvesting was feasible.","zh":"該項目顯示本地雨水收集是可行的。"},{"en":"To be feasible means to be possible and practical.","zh":"可行，是指有可能而且實際可做。"},{"en":"A larger tank may be feasible if materials and trained workers are available.","zh":"如果有材料和受訓工人，較大型水缸可能可行。"},{"en":"Feasibility depends on cost, skills and local conditions.","zh":"可行性取決於成本、技能和本地條件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical possibility.","zh":"這個短語描述實際可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"use the same approach","meaning":"採用相同方法","examples":[{"en":"Several other organisations have begun projects using the same approach.","zh":"其他幾個組織已開始採用相同方法推行項目。"},{"en":"To use the same approach means to apply the same method or strategy.","zh":"採用相同方法，是指應用同一方法或策略。"},{"en":"Another village may use the same approach to train local builders first.","zh":"另一村落可能採用相同方法，先培訓本地建造者。"},{"en":"Reusing a successful approach can help spread good practice.","zh":"重用成功方法可以幫助良好做法擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes copying or adapting a method.","zh":"這個短語描述複製或調整方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"introduce larger tanks","meaning":"引入更大型水缸","examples":[{"en":"The feasibility of introducing larger tanks is being investigated.","zh":"引入更大型水缸的可行性正在研究中。"},{"en":"To introduce larger tanks means to start using storage tanks with greater capacity.","zh":"引入更大型水缸，是指開始使用容量更大的儲水缸。"},{"en":"Larger tanks may provide more water during longer dry periods.","zh":"較大型水缸可能在更長乾旱期提供更多水。"},{"en":"However, they may cost more and require stronger construction.","zh":"然而，它們可能成本更高，也需要更堅固建造。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible technical upgrade.","zh":"這個短語描述可能的技術升級。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be investigated","meaning":"正在研究","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are investigating whether larger tanks would be practical.","zh":"研究人員正在研究較大型水缸是否實用。"},{"en":"To be investigated means to be studied or examined carefully.","zh":"正在研究，是指被仔細研究或檢視。"},{"en":"The cause of water contamination should be investigated quickly.","zh":"食水污染原因應迅速研究。"},{"en":"Investigation helps people make decisions based on evidence.","zh":"研究幫助人們根據證據作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal study or inquiry.","zh":"這個短語描述正式研究或調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a lot of effort and patience","meaning":"大量努力和耐性","examples":[{"en":"Sustainable community projects require a lot of effort and patience.","zh":"可持續社區項目需要大量努力和耐性。"},{"en":"A lot of effort and patience means much hard work and willingness to wait.","zh":"大量努力和耐性，是指很多辛勤工作和願意等待。"},{"en":"Training villagers and building trust require a lot of effort and patience.","zh":"培訓村民和建立信任需要大量努力和耐性。"},{"en":"Community change is slow because people need time to learn and agree.","zh":"社區改變很慢，因為人們需要時間學習和達成共識。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses persistence.","zh":"這個短語強調堅持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"generate interest","meaning":"引起興趣","examples":[{"en":"Project organisers must generate interest among local residents.","zh":"項目組織者必須在本地居民中引起興趣。"},{"en":"To generate interest means to create attention, curiosity or willingness to participate.","zh":"引起興趣，是指創造注意、好奇或參與意願。"},{"en":"A demonstration tank may generate interest in rainwater harvesting.","zh":"示範水缸可能引起人們對雨水收集的興趣。"},{"en":"Interest is necessary before people contribute time or money.","zh":"在人們貢獻時間或金錢之前，興趣是必要的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes building local support.","zh":"這個短語描述建立本地支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"develop the skills","meaning":"培養技能","examples":[{"en":"Communities need time to develop the necessary technical skills.","zh":"社區需要時間培養必要技術技能。"},{"en":"To develop the skills means to build abilities through learning and practice.","zh":"培養技能，是指透過學習和練習建立能力。"},{"en":"Local workers need practice to develop the skills for tank construction.","zh":"本地工人需要練習，以培養建造水缸的技能。"},{"en":"Skills develop gradually, not instantly.","zh":"技能是逐步培養的，不是立即出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes training over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間進行的培訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"organise management structures","meaning":"組織管理架構","examples":[{"en":"Successful projects require well-organised management structures.","zh":"成功項目需要組織良好的管理架構。"},{"en":"To organise management structures means to set up clear groups, roles and rules for running a project.","zh":"組織管理架構，是指設立清晰小組、角色和規則來運作項目。"},{"en":"A village may organise a committee to manage water fees and repairs.","zh":"村落可能組織委員會管理水費和維修。"},{"en":"Clear structures prevent confusion and conflict.","zh":"清晰架構能防止混亂和衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on project governance.","zh":"這個短語聚焦項目治理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"implement sustainable projects","meaning":"推行可持續項目","examples":[{"en":"Communities need support to implement sustainable projects.","zh":"社區需要支援去推行可持續項目。"},{"en":"To implement sustainable projects means to put long-lasting, practical projects into action.","zh":"推行可持續項目，是指把持久而實用的項目付諸實行。"},{"en":"A village may implement a sustainable project by building tanks and training users.","zh":"村落可以透過建造水缸和培訓使用者推行可持續項目。"},{"en":"Implementation turns plans into real changes.","zh":"推行把計劃變成真實改變。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical execution.","zh":"這個短語聚焦實際執行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"it will probably be some time before","meaning":"可能還需要一段時間才……","examples":[{"en":"It will probably be some time before the technology spreads widely.","zh":"這項技術可能還需要一段時間才會廣泛普及。"},{"en":"It will probably be some time before something happens means it is likely to take a while.","zh":"可能還需要一段時間才發生某事，是指它很可能需要一些時間。"},{"en":"It will probably be some time before every village has storage tanks.","zh":"可能還需要一段時間，每個村落才都有儲水缸。"},{"en":"This phrase manages expectations about slow change.","zh":"這個短語調整人們對緩慢改變的期望。"},{"en":"It suggests delay without saying something is impossible.","zh":"它暗示延遲，而不是說不可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"spread rapidly and spontaneously","meaning":"迅速而自發地普及","examples":[{"en":"The technology is unlikely to spread rapidly and spontaneously.","zh":"這項技術不太可能迅速而自發地普及。"},{"en":"To spread rapidly and spontaneously means to become common quickly without much outside support.","zh":"迅速而自發地普及，是指在很少外來支援下快速變得常見。"},{"en":"A new farming method may not spread spontaneously if it requires training.","zh":"如果新農法需要培訓，就未必會自發普及。"},{"en":"Some technologies need organisation before they can expand.","zh":"有些技術需要組織安排才可擴展。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts natural diffusion with supported expansion.","zh":"這個短語對比自然擴散與受支援擴展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"across the district’s villages","meaning":"遍及區內各村落","examples":[{"en":"The aim is eventually to spread the system across the district’s villages.","zh":"目標是最終把系統推廣至區內各村落。"},{"en":"Across the district’s villages means throughout the villages in that district.","zh":"遍及區內各村落，是指覆蓋該區的所有或許多村落。"},{"en":"A water project may expand across the district’s villages over several years.","zh":"供水項目可能在數年間擴展至區內各村落。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wider geographical coverage.","zh":"這個短語描述更廣闊地理覆蓋。"},{"en":"It shows an aim beyond one community.","zh":"它顯示目標超越單一社區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"external support","meaning":"外來支援","examples":[{"en":"Many communities will initially require external support.","zh":"許多社區起初需要外來支援。"},{"en":"External support is help from outside the community, such as money, training or expertise.","zh":"外來支援是來自社區外的幫助，例如金錢、培訓或專業知識。"},{"en":"A village may need external support to buy materials for its first tanks.","zh":"村落可能需要外來支援來購買第一批水缸材料。"},{"en":"Outside help can start a project, but local skills help sustain it.","zh":"外援可以啟動項目，但本地技能有助維持它。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts outside assistance with local resources.","zh":"這個短語把外部協助與本地資源作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no more than three words and/or a number","meaning":"不多於三個詞及／或一個數字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer must contain no more than three words and/or a number.","zh":"每個答案必須包含不多於三個詞及／或一個數字。"},{"en":"No more than three words and/or a number means the answer may include up to three words plus a number if needed.","zh":"不多於三個詞及／或一個數字，是指答案最多可包含三個詞，並可按需要加入數字。"},{"en":"“six acres” is acceptable because it contains a number and one word.","zh":"“six acres” 可以接受，因為它包含一個數字和一個詞。"},{"en":"Students must follow the word limit exactly in reading tests.","zh":"學生在閱讀測驗中必須嚴格遵守字數限制。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"main source of livelihood","meaning":"主要生計來源","examples":[{"en":"Day labour is the main source of livelihood for many village families.","zh":"日薪勞動是許多村落家庭的主要生計來源。"},{"en":"A main source of livelihood is the primary way people earn money or obtain what they need to live.","zh":"主要生計來源，是人們賺錢或取得生活所需的主要方式。"},{"en":"Fishing may be the main source of livelihood in a coastal village.","zh":"捕魚可能是沿海村落的主要生計來源。"},{"en":"If the main livelihood fails, families become vulnerable.","zh":"如果主要生計失效，家庭會變得脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to basic economic survival.","zh":"這個短語指基本經濟生存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"local people","meaning":"本地居民","examples":[{"en":"The question asks how local people earn their living.","zh":"題目問本地居民如何謀生。"},{"en":"Local people are residents who live in the area being discussed.","zh":"本地居民是住在所討論地區的人。"},{"en":"Local people often understand water problems better than outside visitors.","zh":"本地居民通常比外來者更了解水資源問題。"},{"en":"Their knowledge is important for community projects.","zh":"他們的知識對社區項目很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people from the place itself.","zh":"這個短語指該地本身的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"earn extra money","meaning":"賺取額外收入","examples":[{"en":"Villagers work on plantations to earn extra money.","zh":"村民在種植園工作以賺取額外收入。"},{"en":"To earn extra money means to make additional income beyond one’s main income.","zh":"賺取額外收入，是指在主要收入以外賺取更多金錢。"},{"en":"A student may tutor younger pupils to earn extra money.","zh":"學生可能輔導低年級學生以賺取額外收入。"},{"en":"Extra income helps families cope with poor harvests.","zh":"額外收入幫助家庭應對收成差的情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes supplementary earnings.","zh":"這個短語描述補充收入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"daily household use","meaning":"日常家居用途","examples":[{"en":"The wells were dug to supply water for daily household use.","zh":"這些水井被挖掘以供應日常家居用途的水。"},{"en":"Daily household use means ordinary family needs every day.","zh":"日常家居用途，是指家庭每天的普通需要。"},{"en":"Water for daily household use includes cooking, drinking and washing.","zh":"日常家居用水包括煮食、飲用和洗滌。"},{"en":"A reliable supply reduces the burden of household chores.","zh":"可靠供應能減輕家務負擔。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to routine domestic needs.","zh":"這個短語指日常家庭需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"planning begin","meaning":"規劃開始","examples":[{"en":"The question asks when planning for the mitigation project began.","zh":"題目問紓緩項目的規劃何時開始。"},{"en":"Planning begin means the point at which preparation or organisation started.","zh":"規劃開始，是指準備或組織工作開始的時間點。"},{"en":"Planning began after villagers discussed water problems with the organisation.","zh":"規劃在村民與組織討論水問題後開始。"},{"en":"Knowing when planning began helps students follow the sequence of events.","zh":"知道規劃何時開始，有助學生理解事件次序。"},{"en":"This phrase is mainly used in question wording.","zh":"這個短語主要用於題目措辭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"collect rainwater from","meaning":"從……收集雨水","examples":[{"en":"Gutters and pipes collect rainwater from house roofs.","zh":"排水槽和水管從房屋屋頂收集雨水。"},{"en":"To collect rainwater from somewhere means to gather water falling or flowing from that surface.","zh":"從某處收集雨水，是指收集落在或流經該表面的水。"},{"en":"A tank can collect rainwater from a school roof.","zh":"水缸可以從學校屋頂收集雨水。"},{"en":"Roof collection is useful because roofs provide a clean catchment surface.","zh":"屋頂收集有用，因為屋頂提供較潔淨的集水面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the source of collected rainwater.","zh":"這個短語描述收集雨水的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"obtain more water","meaning":"取得更多水","examples":[{"en":"Storage tanks enable families to obtain more water.","zh":"儲水缸使家庭能取得更多水。"},{"en":"To obtain more water means to get a larger amount of water.","zh":"取得更多水，是指得到更大量的水。"},{"en":"Families obtain more water when rain is stored instead of lost.","zh":"當雨水被儲存而不是流失，家庭便能取得更多水。"},{"en":"More water improves hygiene, cooking and small-scale gardening.","zh":"更多水能改善衛生、煮食和小規模種植。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increased access.","zh":"這個短語描述取得途徑增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"domestic needs","meaning":"家居需要","examples":[{"en":"Stored rainwater is used to meet domestic needs.","zh":"儲存雨水用來滿足家居需要。"},{"en":"Domestic needs are everyday household requirements.","zh":"家居需要是日常家庭需求。"},{"en":"Cooking, washing and drinking are domestic needs.","zh":"煮食、洗滌和飲用都是家居需要。"},{"en":"Water projects often begin by meeting domestic needs before agricultural needs.","zh":"供水項目通常先滿足家居需要，再處理農業需要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to family-level necessities.","zh":"這個短語指家庭層面的必需品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"rely only on","meaning":"只依賴……","examples":[{"en":"Some families rely only on wells and ponds for water.","zh":"有些家庭只依賴水井和池塘取水。"},{"en":"To rely only on something means to depend on it and nothing else.","zh":"只依賴某物，是指依靠它而沒有其他選擇。"},{"en":"A family relying only on one pond is vulnerable in a drought.","zh":"只依賴一個池塘的家庭在乾旱時很脆弱。"},{"en":"Adding rainwater tanks reduces dependence on one source.","zh":"增加雨水缸能減少對單一來源的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses limited alternatives.","zh":"這個短語強調替代選擇有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"符合文中資料","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否符合篇章。"},{"en":"Agree with the information given means match what the text says.","zh":"符合文中資料，是指與文本所說內容相符。"},{"en":"A statement agrees with the passage only if the passage clearly supports it.","zh":"只有當篇章清楚支持某陳述，它才符合文中資料。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge for this task.","zh":"學生不應在這類題目使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文中資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the information in the passage.","zh":"陳述可能與篇章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"與資料相矛盾，是指說出與文本內容相反的東西。"},{"en":"If the passage says tanks improved water supply, saying they worsened it contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說水缸改善供水，說它們令供水惡化就是與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction requires clear evidence in the text.","zh":"矛盾需要文本中有清楚證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in reading-test instructions.","zh":"這個短語用於閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"This response is used when the passage gives no relevant information.","zh":"當篇章沒有提供相關資料時，使用這個回應。"},{"en":"No information on this means the text does not say enough to decide.","zh":"文中沒有相關資料，是指文本沒有足夠內容作判斷。"},{"en":"If the passage does not mention local government funding, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果篇章沒有提及地方政府資助，文中就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when information is missing.","zh":"資料缺失時，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase corresponds to NOT GIVEN.","zh":"這個短語對應 NOT GIVEN。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"government initiatives","meaning":"政府措施","examples":[{"en":"Government initiatives had often failed to provide enough training.","zh":"政府措施常未能提供足夠培訓。"},{"en":"Government initiatives are official projects or actions started by the government.","zh":"政府措施是由政府啟動的官方項目或行動。"},{"en":"A government initiative may provide wells, tanks or farming support.","zh":"政府措施可能提供水井、水缸或農業支援。"},{"en":"Initiatives can fail if they ignore training and maintenance.","zh":"如果忽視培訓和保養，措施可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to public-sector programmes.","zh":"這個短語指公共部門計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"at least partly unsuccessful","meaning":"至少部分不成功","examples":[{"en":"Some earlier programmes were at least partly unsuccessful.","zh":"有些早期計劃至少部分不成功。"},{"en":"At least partly unsuccessful means not completely successful, even if some parts worked.","zh":"至少部分不成功，是指不是完全成功，即使有些部分有效。"},{"en":"A training scheme may be partly unsuccessful if people attend but do not use the skills.","zh":"如果人們出席培訓卻沒有使用技能，培訓計劃可能部分不成功。"},{"en":"This phrase allows a balanced judgement.","zh":"這個短語容許平衡判斷。"},{"en":"It does not mean total failure.","zh":"它不代表完全失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"construct parts of","meaning":"建造……的部分","examples":[{"en":"The masons were trained to construct parts of the storage system.","zh":"泥水匠受訓建造儲水系統的部分。"},{"en":"To construct parts of something means to build some components of it.","zh":"建造某物的部分，是指建造其中一些組件。"},{"en":"Workers may construct parts of a tank, such as the base and walls.","zh":"工人可能建造水缸的部分，例如底座和牆身。"},{"en":"Training on parts of a system can still create valuable local expertise.","zh":"即使只培訓系統部分，也能建立有價值的本地專業知識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes partial construction responsibility.","zh":"這個短語描述部分建造責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"share the cost","meaning":"分擔成本","examples":[{"en":"The community and Practical Action shared the cost of each system.","zh":"社區和 Practical Action 分擔每套系統的成本。"},{"en":"To share the cost means two or more parties each pay part of the total.","zh":"分擔成本，是指兩方或多方各自支付總成本的一部分。"},{"en":"Parents and the school may share the cost of a trip.","zh":"家長和學校可能分擔旅行成本。"},{"en":"Cost-sharing can increase local commitment.","zh":"分擔成本可以增加本地投入感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes divided financial responsibility.","zh":"這個短語描述分攤財務責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"local government","meaning":"地方政府","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether the local government contributed financially.","zh":"題目問地方政府是否作出財政貢獻。"},{"en":"Local government is the authority responsible for a district, town or community area.","zh":"地方政府是負責地區、城鎮或社區範圍的行政機關。"},{"en":"Local government may manage roads, water systems and public health services.","zh":"地方政府可能管理道路、水務系統和公共健康服務。"},{"en":"Its financial role must be supported by the passage before students answer YES.","zh":"學生要答 YES，篇章必須支持其財政角色。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to government at local level.","zh":"這個短語指本地層級政府。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"amount and quality of water","meaning":"水量和水質","examples":[{"en":"The tanks improve both the amount and quality of domestic water.","zh":"水缸同時改善家居用水的水量和水質。"},{"en":"Amount and quality of water means how much water there is and how clean or safe it is.","zh":"水量和水質，是指水有多少，以及它有多潔淨或安全。"},{"en":"A project may increase the amount of water but still need filters to improve quality.","zh":"項目可能增加水量，但仍需要濾器改善水質。"},{"en":"Both quantity and quality matter for health.","zh":"水量和水質對健康都很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase combines supply volume with safety.","zh":"這個短語結合供應量與安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"take a job in","meaning":"在……任職","examples":[{"en":"The widow did not have to take a job in the scheme.","zh":"這位寡婦不需要在該計劃中任職。"},{"en":"To take a job in something means to accept paid work within that project or organisation.","zh":"在某項目中任職，是指接受該項目或組織內的有薪工作。"},{"en":"A villager may take a job in a water project as a maintenance worker.","zh":"村民可能在供水項目中擔任維修工人。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used when discussing employment options.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論就業選擇。"},{"en":"It describes formal or semi-formal work participation.","zh":"它描述正式或半正式工作參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"send someone to school","meaning":"供某人上學","examples":[{"en":"Improved water access gave her daughter more time for schoolwork.","zh":"改善取水條件讓她的女兒有更多時間做功課。"},{"en":"To send someone to school means to ensure they attend school and receive education.","zh":"供某人上學，是指確保他們上學並接受教育。"},{"en":"Better household income can help parents send children to school.","zh":"更好的家庭收入可以幫助父母供孩子上學。"},{"en":"Water access supports schooling by reducing time spent fetching water.","zh":"取水條件改善透過減少取水時間來支持上學。"},{"en":"This phrase connects family resources with education.","zh":"這個短語把家庭資源與教育連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contribute to maintenance costs","meaning":"分擔保養費用","examples":[{"en":"Households were asked to contribute to maintenance costs.","zh":"家庭被要求分擔保養費用。"},{"en":"To contribute to maintenance costs means to pay part of the money needed for upkeep and repairs.","zh":"分擔保養費用，是指支付維護和維修所需金錢的一部分。"},{"en":"Families may contribute to maintenance costs through a monthly fund.","zh":"家庭可以透過每月基金分擔保養費用。"},{"en":"Regular contributions help keep water systems working.","zh":"定期供款幫助保持供水系統運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shared responsibility for future repairs.","zh":"這個短語描述共同承擔未來維修責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"training two masons at once","meaning":"同時培訓兩名泥水匠","examples":[{"en":"The question compares training two masons at once with training only one.","zh":"題目比較同時培訓兩名泥水匠與只培訓一名泥水匠。"},{"en":"Training two masons at once means teaching two local builders during the same training period.","zh":"同時培訓兩名泥水匠，是指在同一培訓期教授兩名本地建造工人。"},{"en":"Training two masons at once may help them support and check each other’s work.","zh":"同時培訓兩名泥水匠可能幫助他們互相支援和檢查工作。"},{"en":"Having two trained workers reduces dependence on a single person.","zh":"有兩名受訓工人能減少對單一人士的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes simultaneous skills training.","zh":"這個短語描述同步技能培訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 147 - Rainwater Harvesting.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 148":[{"front":"children’s compliance and noncompliance","meaning":"兒童的服從與不服從","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines children’s compliance and noncompliance in different situations.","zh":"文章探討兒童在不同情況下的服從與不服從。"},{"en":"Children’s compliance and noncompliance refer to whether children follow instructions or refuse to do so.","zh":"children’s compliance and noncompliance 指兒童是否遵從指示或拒絕遵從。"},{"en":"A teacher may observe children’s compliance and noncompliance during group activities.","zh":"老師可能在小組活動中觀察兒童的服從與不服從。"},{"en":"Clear rules can increase compliance, while confusing instructions may lead to noncompliance.","zh":"清楚規則可以增加服從，而含糊指示可能導致不服從。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how children respond to adults’ requests.","zh":"討論兒童如何回應成人要求時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"socialisation","meaning":"社會化","examples":[{"en":"Many scientists believe that socialisation is a long process.","zh":"許多科學家相信社會化是一個漫長過程。"},{"en":"Socialisation is the process by which children learn the rules, values, and behaviours of society.","zh":"socialisation 指兒童學習社會規則、價值觀和行為方式的過程。"},{"en":"Children experience socialisation when they learn to share toys and wait their turn.","zh":"孩子學習分享玩具和輪候時，就是在經歷社會化。"},{"en":"Family, school, and friends all shape socialisation over many years.","zh":"家庭、學校和朋友多年來都會塑造社會化。"},{"en":"This word is used when discussing how people learn to live with others.","zh":"討論人如何學會與他人共同生活時，可以使用這個字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a long process","meaning":"漫長的過程","examples":[{"en":"Socialisation is generally considered a long process.","zh":"社會化通常被視為一個漫長的過程。"},{"en":"A long process is something that takes a lot of time and happens in many stages.","zh":"a long process 指需要很多時間並分多個階段發生的事情。"},{"en":"Learning a new language is a long process, not something completed in one week.","zh":"學習一種新語言是一個漫長的過程，不是一星期就能完成的事。"},{"en":"If a process is long, people need patience and repeated practice.","zh":"如果一個過程漫長，人們需要耐性和反覆練習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual development rather than quick change.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步發展，而不是快速改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"its starting point","meaning":"它的起點","examples":[{"en":"Compliance may be the starting point of socialisation.","zh":"服從可能是社會化的起點。"},{"en":"Its starting point means the first stage or beginning of a process.","zh":"its starting point 指某過程的第一階段或開始。"},{"en":"A child’s first school day may be the starting point of a new friendship.","zh":"孩子第一天上學可能是一段新友誼的起點。"},{"en":"Once the starting point is clear, people can understand how later development happens.","zh":"一旦起點清楚，人們就能理解後來發展如何發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when identifying where something begins.","zh":"當指出某事從哪裡開始時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"promote compliance","meaning":"促進服從行為","examples":[{"en":"Parents and researchers often seek to promote compliance in children.","zh":"父母和研究者常尋求促進兒童的服從行為。"},{"en":"To promote compliance means to encourage people to follow rules or requests.","zh":"promote compliance 指鼓勵人遵守規則或要求。"},{"en":"Teachers promote compliance by giving clear instructions and praising cooperation.","zh":"老師透過給予清楚指示和讚賞合作來促進服從行為。"},{"en":"Consistent routines can promote compliance because children know what to expect.","zh":"穩定常規可以促進服從，因為孩子知道會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in parenting, education, and behaviour research.","zh":"這個短語常用於育兒、教育和行為研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be a priority","meaning":"是優先事項","examples":[{"en":"Promoting compliance in young children is considered a priority.","zh":"促進幼兒服從行為被視為優先事項。"},{"en":"To be a priority means to be more important than many other tasks or concerns.","zh":"be a priority 指比許多其他任務或關注更重要。"},{"en":"Safety is a priority when children go on a school trip.","zh":"孩子參加學校旅行時，安全是優先事項。"},{"en":"When something is a priority, adults spend time and effort dealing with it first.","zh":"當某事是優先事項，成人會先花時間和精力處理它。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when ranking importance.","zh":"當排列重要性時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"motivationally distinct forms","meaning":"動機上有所不同的形式","examples":[{"en":"The study examined motivationally distinct forms of child compliance.","zh":"研究檢視兒童服從行為中動機上有所不同的形式。"},{"en":"Motivationally distinct forms are types of behaviour driven by different reasons or motives.","zh":"motivationally distinct forms 指由不同原因或動機推動的行為類型。"},{"en":"Two students may both do homework, but one is motivated by interest and the other by fear.","zh":"兩個學生都可能做功課，但一個出於興趣，另一個出於恐懼。"},{"en":"Looking at motivation helps researchers understand whether obedience is willing or forced.","zh":"研究動機有助研究者理解服從是自願還是被迫。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the same behaviour may come from different inner reasons.","zh":"當同一行為可能來自不同內在原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"child compliance","meaning":"兒童服從行為","examples":[{"en":"Researchers observed different forms of child compliance.","zh":"研究者觀察了不同形式的兒童服從行為。"},{"en":"Child compliance means a child’s willingness to follow an adult’s instruction or rule.","zh":"child compliance 指兒童願意遵從成人指示或規則。"},{"en":"A child shows compliance when she puts away toys after being asked.","zh":"孩子被要求後把玩具收好，就是表現出服從行為。"},{"en":"Compliance may increase when instructions are clear and the child feels respected.","zh":"當指示清楚而孩子感到被尊重時，服從行為可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes obedient behaviour in children.","zh":"這個短語描述兒童的順從行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mutually positive affect","meaning":"雙方的正面情感","examples":[{"en":"Mother-child mutually positive affect was associated with committed compliance.","zh":"母子雙方的正面情感與主動而投入的服從有關。"},{"en":"Mutually positive affect means both people show warm, happy, or friendly feelings toward each other.","zh":"mutually positive affect 指雙方都向彼此表現溫暖、快樂或友好的情感。"},{"en":"A parent and child share positive affect when they smile, laugh, and cooperate during homework.","zh":"父母和孩子在做功課時微笑、笑着合作，就是分享正面情感。"},{"en":"Positive emotional exchange can make children more willing to follow instructions.","zh":"正面情感交流可以令兒童更願意遵從指示。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a two-way emotional connection, not one person’s mood only.","zh":"這個短語描述雙向情感連繫，而不只是單方面情緒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"maternal control","meaning":"母親的管教","examples":[{"en":"The researchers observed maternal control in several situations.","zh":"研究者在幾種情況中觀察母親的管教。"},{"en":"Maternal control means the way a mother guides, limits, or directs a child’s behaviour.","zh":"maternal control 指母親引導、限制或指揮孩子行為的方式。"},{"en":"Maternal control may appear when a mother tells a child not to touch a hot stove.","zh":"母親叫孩子不要碰熱爐時，就是一種母親的管教。"},{"en":"Firm but warm control can help children understand boundaries.","zh":"堅定但溫暖的管教可以幫助孩子理解界線。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in research about parenting and discipline.","zh":"這個短語用於關於育兒和紀律的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"control contexts","meaning":"管教情境","examples":[{"en":"Maternal behaviour was observed in three different control contexts.","zh":"研究者在三種不同管教情境中觀察母親行為。"},{"en":"Control contexts are situations in which an adult tries to guide or limit a child’s behaviour.","zh":"control contexts 指成人嘗試引導或限制兒童行為的情況。"},{"en":"Meal time, play time, and clean-up time can be different control contexts.","zh":"用餐時間、遊戲時間和收拾時間可以是不同管教情境。"},{"en":"Children may respond differently depending on the type of control context.","zh":"兒童可能因管教情境不同而有不同反應。"},{"en":"This phrase helps researchers compare behaviour across situations.","zh":"這個短語幫助研究者比較不同情況下的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"mother-child dyads","meaning":"母子配對","examples":[{"en":"The study involved 103 mother-child dyads.","zh":"該研究涉及103對母子配對。"},{"en":"Mother-child dyads are pairs consisting of one mother and one child.","zh":"mother-child dyads 指由一位母親和一名孩子組成的配對。"},{"en":"A researcher may film mother-child dyads while they play together.","zh":"研究者可能拍攝母子配對一起玩耍的情況。"},{"en":"Studying dyads helps researchers see how two people influence each other.","zh":"研究配對有助研究者看見兩個人如何互相影響。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to paired participants in family research.","zh":"這個短語指家庭研究中的配對參與者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be examined as correlates of","meaning":"被研究為與……相關的因素","examples":[{"en":"Several behaviours were examined as correlates of internalization.","zh":"幾種行為被研究為與內化相關的因素。"},{"en":"To be examined as correlates of something means to be studied as factors linked with it.","zh":"be examined as correlates of something 指被研究為與某事相關的因素。"},{"en":"Sleep habits may be examined as correlates of school performance.","zh":"睡眠習慣可能被研究為與學業表現相關的因素。"},{"en":"If two things are correlated, they appear together, but one may not directly cause the other.","zh":"如果兩件事相關，它們會一起出現，但其中一方未必直接造成另一方。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research when studying relationships between variables.","zh":"研究變項之間關係時，這個短語很常見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"internalization","meaning":"內化；將規範內化","examples":[{"en":"The study assessed children’s internalization of parental rules.","zh":"該研究評估兒童對父母規則的內化。"},{"en":"Internalization is the process of accepting rules or values so that they guide behaviour from within.","zh":"internalization 指接受規則或價值觀，使它們從內在引導行為的過程。"},{"en":"A child shows internalization when he tells the truth even when no adult is watching.","zh":"孩子即使沒有成人看着也說真話，就是表現出內化。"},{"en":"Internalization develops when rules become part of a child’s own thinking.","zh":"當規則成為孩子自己思考的一部分時，內化就會發展。"},{"en":"This word describes deeper learning than simple obedience.","zh":"這個字描述比單純服從更深層的學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be assessed using","meaning":"透過……評估","examples":[{"en":"Internalization was assessed using observation and maternal ratings.","zh":"內化是透過觀察和母親評分來評估的。"},{"en":"To be assessed using something means to be measured or judged with that method.","zh":"be assessed using something 指用某方法量度或判斷某事。"},{"en":"Speaking ability may be assessed using interviews and recorded tasks.","zh":"說話能力可能透過面試和錄音任務來評估。"},{"en":"Using more than one method can give a fuller picture of a child’s behaviour.","zh":"使用多於一種方法可以更全面了解兒童行為。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how researchers measure something.","zh":"這個短語解釋研究者如何量度某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"prohibited temptations","meaning":"被禁止接觸的誘惑物","examples":[{"en":"The children were observed while alone with prohibited temptations.","zh":"兒童單獨面對被禁止接觸的誘惑物時受到觀察。"},{"en":"Prohibited temptations are attractive objects or activities that a child has been told not to touch or do.","zh":"prohibited temptations 指吸引人但孩子被告知不能碰或不能做的物件或活動。"},{"en":"A plate of sweets can become a prohibited temptation if a child is told to wait until dinner.","zh":"如果孩子被告知要等到晚飯後，一碟糖果就可能成為被禁止的誘惑物。"},{"en":"Such temptations test whether children follow rules without adult supervision.","zh":"這類誘惑物測試兒童在沒有成人監督下是否遵守規則。"},{"en":"This phrase combines desire with a clear ban.","zh":"這個短語結合慾望和明確禁令。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"maternal ratings","meaning":"母親評分","examples":[{"en":"The study also used maternal ratings of the children’s behaviour.","zh":"該研究也使用母親對兒童行為的評分。"},{"en":"Maternal ratings are mothers’ scores or judgements about their children’s behaviour.","zh":"maternal ratings 指母親對孩子行為作出的分數或判斷。"},{"en":"A mother may rate how often her child follows instructions at home.","zh":"母親可能評分孩子在家中多常遵從指示。"},{"en":"Ratings can add useful information, but they may reflect a parent’s personal view.","zh":"評分可以加入有用資訊，但也可能反映家長個人看法。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to behaviour evaluation provided by mothers.","zh":"這個短語指由母親提供的行為評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"one form of compliance","meaning":"一種服從形式","examples":[{"en":"The researchers placed particular emphasis on one form of compliance.","zh":"研究者特別強調一種服從形式。"},{"en":"One form of compliance means one type or pattern of obedient behaviour.","zh":"one form of compliance 指服從行為的一種類型或模式。"},{"en":"A child may obey quietly, willingly, or only after repeated warnings; each is a different form.","zh":"孩子可能安靜服從、自願服從，或在多次警告後才服從；每種都是不同形式。"},{"en":"Studying one form closely helps researchers understand what kind of obedience matters most.","zh":"仔細研究一種形式有助研究者理解哪種服從最重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when compliance is divided into categories.","zh":"當服從被分成不同類別時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"committed compliance","meaning":"主動而投入的服從","examples":[{"en":"Committed compliance occurs when a child willingly accepts a parent’s request.","zh":"當孩子自願接受父母要求時，就會出現主動而投入的服從。"},{"en":"Committed compliance means obedience that is willing, wholehearted, and not merely forced.","zh":"committed compliance 指自願、全心投入，而不只是被迫的服從。"},{"en":"A child shows committed compliance when he cleans up toys without arguing after a gentle reminder.","zh":"孩子在溫和提醒後不爭辯地收拾玩具，就是表現出主動而投入的服從。"},{"en":"This kind of compliance may show that the child has begun to accept the rule internally.","zh":"這種服從可能顯示孩子已開始內在接受規則。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts willing obedience with reluctant obedience.","zh":"這個短語把自願服從與勉強服從作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"appear committed wholeheartedly to","meaning":"看來全心全意投入於……","examples":[{"en":"The child appeared committed wholeheartedly to the maternal agenda.","zh":"孩子看來全心全意投入於母親的要求和安排。"},{"en":"To appear committed wholeheartedly to something means to seem fully willing and emotionally invested in it.","zh":"appear committed wholeheartedly to something 指看起來完全自願且情感上投入某事。"},{"en":"A student appears committed wholeheartedly to a project when she works carefully without reminders.","zh":"學生無需提醒也仔細完成專題時，就看來全心投入於該項目。"},{"en":"Wholehearted commitment makes behaviour look self-motivated rather than forced.","zh":"全心投入令行為看起來是自我推動，而不是被迫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible, sincere involvement.","zh":"這個短語描述可見而真誠的投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"maternal agenda","meaning":"母親的要求和安排","examples":[{"en":"The child willingly accepted the mother’s instructions and expectations.","zh":"孩子自願接受母親的指示和期望。"},{"en":"A maternal agenda is the mother’s set of requests, goals, or expectations for the child.","zh":"maternal agenda 指母親對孩子的一組要求、目標或期望。"},{"en":"A mother’s agenda may include finishing homework, eating dinner, and going to bed on time.","zh":"母親的安排可能包括完成功課、吃晚飯和準時睡覺。"},{"en":"Children comply more easily when the agenda is clear and reasonable.","zh":"當要求清楚而合理時，孩子較容易服從。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what the mother wants the child to do.","zh":"這個短語描述母親希望孩子做的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be eager to endorse","meaning":"樂意支持並接受","examples":[{"en":"The child was eager to endorse and accept the mother’s request.","zh":"孩子樂意支持並接受母親的要求。"},{"en":"To be eager to endorse something means to be willing and enthusiastic about supporting it.","zh":"be eager to endorse something 指願意且熱心支持某事。"},{"en":"A student may be eager to endorse a class rule if it makes games fairer.","zh":"如果班規令遊戲更公平，學生可能樂意支持該規則。"},{"en":"Children are more likely to endorse a request when they understand its purpose.","zh":"當孩子理解要求的目的，他們較可能支持它。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active agreement, not silent obedience.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動同意，而不是沉默服從。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a predictor of","meaning":"……的預測因素","examples":[{"en":"Positive mother-child emotion was a predictor of committed compliance.","zh":"母子之間的正面情感是主動而投入的服從的預測因素。"},{"en":"A predictor of something is a factor that helps forecast whether something will happen.","zh":"predictor of something 指有助預測某事是否會發生的因素。"},{"en":"Regular practice is often a predictor of better exam performance.","zh":"定期練習常是更好考試表現的預測因素。"},{"en":"If one behaviour predicts another, researchers can use it to understand future outcomes.","zh":"如果一種行為能預測另一種行為，研究者可用它理解未來結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research and statistics.","zh":"這個短語常見於研究和統計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a concomitant of","meaning":"……的伴隨因素","examples":[{"en":"Positive affect was also a concomitant of committed compliance.","zh":"正面情感也是主動而投入的服從的伴隨因素。"},{"en":"A concomitant of something is something that happens together with it or is closely associated with it.","zh":"concomitant of something 指與某事同時出現或密切相關的事物。"},{"en":"Tiredness is often a concomitant of long working hours.","zh":"疲倦常是長工時的伴隨因素。"},{"en":"If two things are concomitants, they appear together but may not directly cause each other.","zh":"如果兩件事是伴隨因素，它們會一起出現，但未必直接互相造成。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and common in academic writing.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常見於學術寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"share positive affect","meaning":"分享正面情感","examples":[{"en":"Some children regularly shared positive affect with their mothers.","zh":"有些兒童經常與母親分享正面情感。"},{"en":"To share positive affect means to exchange warm, happy, or friendly emotions.","zh":"share positive affect 指交流溫暖、快樂或友善的情緒。"},{"en":"A child and parent share positive affect when they laugh together while cooking.","zh":"孩子和父母一起煮食時笑起來，就是分享正面情感。"},{"en":"Sharing positive emotion can make later instructions feel less threatening.","zh":"分享正面情緒可以令之後的指示感覺較不具威脅。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on emotional connection between people.","zh":"這個短語集中於人與人之間的情感連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"show a high level of","meaning":"表現出高水平的……","examples":[{"en":"These children showed a high level of committed compliance.","zh":"這些兒童表現出高水平的主動而投入的服從。"},{"en":"To show a high level of something means to display a large amount or strong degree of it.","zh":"show a high level of something 指表現出大量或強烈程度的某事。"},{"en":"A student may show a high level of concentration during silent reading.","zh":"學生在安靜閱讀時可能表現出高水平的專注。"},{"en":"High levels of compliance may appear when routines and relationships are stable.","zh":"當常規和關係穩定時，可能出現高水平服從。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing degree or intensity.","zh":"描述程度或強度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be more internalized","meaning":"更能將規範內化","examples":[{"en":"Children who complied willingly were also more internalized.","zh":"自願服從的兒童也更能將規範內化。"},{"en":"To be more internalized means that rules or values have become more part of a child’s own thinking.","zh":"be more internalized 指規則或價值觀更成為孩子自己思考的一部分。"},{"en":"A child is more internalized when he returns a lost wallet without being told.","zh":"孩子在沒有人要求下歸還失物，便顯示更能內化規範。"},{"en":"Internalized rules guide behaviour even when adults are not watching.","zh":"已內化的規則會在成人沒有看着時仍引導行為。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests deeper moral learning rather than surface obedience.","zh":"這個短語暗示更深層的道德學習，而不是表面服從。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"differences and similarities between","meaning":"……之間的異同","examples":[{"en":"The study explored differences and similarities between two demand contexts.","zh":"該研究探討兩種要求情境之間的異同。"},{"en":"Differences and similarities between two things are the ways they are unlike and alike.","zh":"differences and similarities between two things 指兩者不同和相同之處。"},{"en":"Students may compare differences and similarities between online and face-to-face lessons.","zh":"學生可能比較網課與面授課之間的異同。"},{"en":"Looking at both helps people avoid one-sided judgement.","zh":"同時看差異和相似之處有助避免片面判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in comparison writing and research.","zh":"這個短語適合用於比較寫作和研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"comply with requests","meaning":"遵從要求","examples":[{"en":"Children may find it easier to comply with some requests than others.","zh":"兒童可能覺得遵從某些要求比另一些要求容易。"},{"en":"To comply with requests means to do what someone asks.","zh":"comply with requests 指按別人的要求去做。"},{"en":"A child may comply with a request to choose a book but resist a request to stop playing.","zh":"孩子可能遵從選書的要求，但抗拒停止遊戲的要求。"},{"en":"Requests are easier to follow when they are clear and reasonable.","zh":"當要求清楚而合理時，較容易遵從。"},{"en":"This phrase describes following instructions rather than making independent choices.","zh":"這個短語描述遵從指示，而不是獨立選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"comply with prohibitions","meaning":"遵守禁令","examples":[{"en":"The study also examined how children complied with prohibitions.","zh":"該研究也檢視兒童如何遵守禁令。"},{"en":"To comply with prohibitions means to obey rules that tell someone not to do something.","zh":"comply with prohibitions 指遵守叫人不要做某事的規則。"},{"en":"A child complies with a prohibition when he does not touch a fragile vase after being told not to.","zh":"孩子被告知不要碰易碎花瓶後沒有碰，就是遵守禁令。"},{"en":"Prohibitions may be easier to understand when adults explain the danger behind them.","zh":"當成人解釋禁令背後的危險時，禁令可能較容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on obeying “Don’t” rules.","zh":"這個短語集中於遵守「不要做」的規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"demand contexts","meaning":"要求情境","examples":[{"en":"Researchers compared “Do” and “Don’t” demand contexts.","zh":"研究者比較「做」和「不要做」兩種要求情境。"},{"en":"Demand contexts are situations in which an adult asks a child either to do something or not to do something.","zh":"demand contexts 指成人要求兒童做某事或不要做某事的情況。"},{"en":"“Put on your shoes” and “Don’t touch the oven” are different demand contexts.","zh":"「穿鞋」和「不要碰焗爐」是不同要求情境。"},{"en":"Children may react differently to action requests and stopping requests.","zh":"兒童對行動要求和停止要求可能反應不同。"},{"en":"This phrase helps researchers classify types of adult demands.","zh":"這個短語幫助研究者分類成人要求的種類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"appear more challenging to","meaning":"對……似乎更具挑戰性","examples":[{"en":"Maternal “Do” requests appeared more challenging to toddlers.","zh":"母親的「做」要求對幼兒似乎更具挑戰性。"},{"en":"To appear more challenging to someone means to seem harder for that person to handle.","zh":"appear more challenging to someone 指對某人來說看似較難應付。"},{"en":"Long writing tasks may appear more challenging to young learners than short answers.","zh":"對年幼學習者來說，長篇寫作任務可能比短答更具挑戰性。"},{"en":"A task may seem challenging when it requires effort, attention, or self-control.","zh":"當任務需要努力、注意力或自制力時，就可能看似具挑戰性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes perceived difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述感受到的難度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"toddlers","meaning":"幼兒","examples":[{"en":"Young toddlers may react differently to requests and prohibitions.","zh":"年幼幼兒對要求和禁令可能有不同反應。"},{"en":"Toddlers are very young children, usually around one to three years old, who are learning to walk and talk.","zh":"toddlers 指非常年幼的兒童，通常約一至三歲，正在學走路和說話。"},{"en":"Toddlers may say “no” often because they are learning independence.","zh":"幼兒可能常說「不」，因為他們正在學習獨立。"},{"en":"Their behaviour can change quickly because their language and self-control are still developing.","zh":"他們的行為可以快速改變，因為語言和自制力仍在發展。"},{"en":"This word refers to children older than babies but younger than preschoolers.","zh":"這個字指比嬰兒大但比學前兒童小的孩子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"individual coherence of behaviour","meaning":"個人行為的一致性","examples":[{"en":"The study found some individual coherence of behaviour across situations.","zh":"該研究發現跨情境存在某種個人行為一致性。"},{"en":"Individual coherence of behaviour means a person shows a similar pattern of behaviour in different situations.","zh":"individual coherence of behaviour 指一個人在不同情境中表現出相似行為模式。"},{"en":"A child who is patient at home and at school shows some behavioural coherence.","zh":"一個孩子在家和在學校都很有耐性，就顯示某種行為一致性。"},{"en":"Coherent behaviour across settings suggests a stable personal pattern.","zh":"跨場景一致的行為暗示穩定的個人模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when behaviour is consistent rather than random.","zh":"當行為一致而非隨機時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"across both contexts","meaning":"在兩種情境中","examples":[{"en":"Some behavioural patterns remained consistent across both contexts.","zh":"有些行為模式在兩種情境中保持一致。"},{"en":"Across both contexts means in both of the two situations being compared.","zh":"across both contexts 指在被比較的兩種情況中。"},{"en":"A student may stay polite across both contexts, at home and at school.","zh":"學生在家和在學校兩種情境中都可能保持有禮。"},{"en":"If behaviour appears across both contexts, it may be part of the child’s usual style.","zh":"如果行為在兩種情境中都出現，它可能是孩子一貫風格的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing two settings.","zh":"比較兩種場景時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the implication of","meaning":"……的含意","examples":[{"en":"The article discusses the implication of committed compliance.","zh":"文章討論主動而投入的服從的含意。"},{"en":"The implication of something is the meaning, result, or possible consequence it suggests.","zh":"implication of something 指某事暗示的意義、結果或可能後果。"},{"en":"A teacher may discuss the implication of poor attendance for exam results.","zh":"老師可能討論出席率差對考試成績的含意。"},{"en":"Understanding implications helps readers see why a finding matters.","zh":"理解含意幫助讀者看見研究結果為何重要。"},{"en":"This phrase asks what a fact may mean beyond itself.","zh":"這個短語詢問一個事實本身以外可能代表甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"emerging internalized regulators","meaning":"逐漸形成的內化調節機制","examples":[{"en":"Committed compliance may support emerging internalized regulators of conduct.","zh":"主動而投入的服從可能支持逐漸形成的內化行為調節機制。"},{"en":"Emerging internalized regulators are developing inner controls that guide behaviour without outside pressure.","zh":"emerging internalized regulators 指正在發展、能在沒有外在壓力下引導行為的內在控制機制。"},{"en":"A child who stops himself from hitting a classmate may be using an emerging internal regulator.","zh":"孩子阻止自己打同學，可能正在使用逐漸形成的內化調節機制。"},{"en":"These regulators grow as children practise self-control and accept rules.","zh":"這些調節機制會隨着孩子練習自制和接受規則而成長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes early moral and behavioural self-management.","zh":"這個短語描述早期道德和行為自我管理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"regulators of conduct","meaning":"行為調節機制","examples":[{"en":"Children gradually develop internal regulators of conduct.","zh":"兒童逐漸發展內在行為調節機制。"},{"en":"Regulators of conduct are inner controls that help people decide how to behave.","zh":"regulators of conduct 指幫助人決定如何行為的內在控制。"},{"en":"A child’s conscience can become a regulator of conduct when no adult is nearby.","zh":"當沒有成人在旁時，孩子的良心可以成為行為調節機制。"},{"en":"Strong conduct regulators reduce the need for constant punishment or reminders.","zh":"強的行為調節機制可以減少持續懲罰或提醒的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mechanisms that guide behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述引導行為的機制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"find it difficult to recognise","meaning":"覺得難以辨認","examples":[{"en":"Some parents found it difficult to recognise compliance.","zh":"有些父母覺得難以辨認服從行為。"},{"en":"To find it difficult to recognise something means to have trouble noticing or identifying it.","zh":"find it difficult to recognise something 指難以注意到或識別某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may find it difficult to recognise anxiety in a quiet student.","zh":"老師可能覺得難以辨認安靜學生的焦慮。"},{"en":"If adults miss good behaviour, they may fail to praise it.","zh":"如果成人錯過良好行為，就可能未能讚賞它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficulty in noticing something clearly.","zh":"這個短語描述難以清楚注意某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"overlook noncompliance","meaning":"忽略不服從行為","examples":[{"en":"Some parents even overlooked their children’s noncompliance.","zh":"有些父母甚至忽略孩子的不服從行為。"},{"en":"To overlook noncompliance means to fail to notice or respond when a child does not obey.","zh":"overlook noncompliance 指沒有注意或回應孩子不服從。"},{"en":"A parent may overlook noncompliance if a child refuses quietly rather than angrily.","zh":"如果孩子安靜地拒絕而不是發脾氣，父母可能忽略不服從行為。"},{"en":"Overlooking disobedience can make rules seem less important.","zh":"忽略不服從可能令規則看似不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes missed or ignored refusal.","zh":"這個短語描述被錯過或忽視的拒絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"despite receiving","meaning":"儘管接受了……","examples":[{"en":"Despite receiving a good education, children do not always obey their parents.","zh":"儘管接受了良好教育，兒童並不總是服從父母。"},{"en":"Despite receiving something means although someone has received it.","zh":"despite receiving something 指雖然某人接受了某物。"},{"en":"Despite receiving clear instructions, a student may still misunderstand the task.","zh":"儘管接受了清楚指示，學生仍可能誤解任務。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast between what we expect and what actually happens.","zh":"這個短語引出預期與實際發生之事的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when a result is surprising.","zh":"當結果令人意外時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"obey their parents","meaning":"服從父母","examples":[{"en":"Well-educated children may still sometimes disobey rather than obey their parents.","zh":"受過良好教育的兒童有時仍可能不服從，而不是服從父母。"},{"en":"To obey their parents means to follow what their parents ask or tell them to do.","zh":"obey their parents 指遵從父母要求或指示。"},{"en":"A child obeys parents when he turns off the television after being asked.","zh":"孩子被要求後關掉電視，就是服從父母。"},{"en":"Children may obey more easily when rules are consistent and explained calmly.","zh":"當規則一致並被平靜解釋時，孩子可能較容易服從。"},{"en":"This phrase describes following parental authority.","zh":"這個短語描述遵從父母權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"especially boys at certain ages","meaning":"尤其是某些年齡的男孩","examples":[{"en":"Noncompliance may be particularly common among boys at certain ages.","zh":"不服從行為可能在某些年齡的男孩中尤其常見。"},{"en":"Especially boys at certain ages means boys in some age groups may show the behaviour more often.","zh":"especially boys at certain ages 指某些年齡組的男孩可能更常表現出該行為。"},{"en":"Teachers may notice that some boys at certain ages test rules more openly.","zh":"老師可能注意到某些年齡的男孩更公開試探規則。"},{"en":"Age matters because children’s self-control and independence change as they develop.","zh":"年齡很重要，因為兒童的自制力和獨立性會隨發展而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a specific group within children.","zh":"這個短語指出兒童中的特定群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be considered acceptable","meaning":"被視為可以接受","examples":[{"en":"A certain level of noncompliance was considered acceptable.","zh":"某程度的不服從被視為可以接受。"},{"en":"To be considered acceptable means to be judged as allowed, normal, or not too serious.","zh":"be considered acceptable 指被判斷為可容許、正常或不太嚴重。"},{"en":"A small amount of noise may be considered acceptable during group work.","zh":"小組活動中少量噪音可能被視為可以接受。"},{"en":"Behaviour is more likely to be accepted when it is mild and temporary.","zh":"當行為輕微且短暫時，較可能被接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a judgement about what is tolerable.","zh":"這個短語描述對甚麼可容忍的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"respond patiently","meaning":"耐心回應","examples":[{"en":"Some parents responded patiently to disobedient behaviour.","zh":"有些父母耐心回應不聽話的行為。"},{"en":"To respond patiently means to react calmly without anger or rushing.","zh":"respond patiently 指冷靜回應，不發怒也不急躁。"},{"en":"A teacher responds patiently when a child refuses to write and needs time to explain why.","zh":"當孩子拒絕寫字並需要時間解釋原因時，老師耐心回應。"},{"en":"Patient responses can reduce conflict and help children calm down.","zh":"耐心回應可以減少衝突並幫助孩子冷靜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gentle reaction to difficult behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述對困難行為的溫和反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not necessarily wrong","meaning":"未必是錯的","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers argue that noncompliance is not necessarily wrong.","zh":"有些研究者認為不服從未必是錯的。"},{"en":"Not necessarily wrong means not always bad or unacceptable.","zh":"not necessarily wrong 指不一定是壞事或不可接受。"},{"en":"A child asking “why” is not necessarily wrong; it may show curiosity.","zh":"孩子問「為甚麼」未必是錯的；這可能顯示好奇心。"},{"en":"Some refusal can help children learn independence and negotiation.","zh":"某些拒絕可以幫助兒童學習獨立和協商。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against judging a behaviour too quickly.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要太快判斷某種行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"determine the effects of","meaning":"確定……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The researchers wanted to determine the effects of different disciplinary techniques.","zh":"研究者想確定不同管教技巧的影響。"},{"en":"To determine the effects of something means to find out what results it produces.","zh":"determine the effects of something 指找出某事產生甚麼結果。"},{"en":"A school may study the effects of later start times on student attention.","zh":"學校可能研究較遲上課時間對學生專注力的影響。"},{"en":"Researchers need evidence before saying one method works better than another.","zh":"研究者需要證據，才可說一種方法比另一種更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when evaluating causes and results.","zh":"評估原因和結果時，這個短語很常見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"parental disciplinary techniques","meaning":"父母管教技巧","examples":[{"en":"The study compared several parental disciplinary techniques.","zh":"該研究比較了幾種父母管教技巧。"},{"en":"Parental disciplinary techniques are methods parents use to correct or guide children’s behaviour.","zh":"parental disciplinary techniques 指父母用來糾正或引導兒童行為的方法。"},{"en":"Explaining rules, giving warnings, and removing privileges are disciplinary techniques.","zh":"解釋規則、給予警告和取消特權都是管教技巧。"},{"en":"Different techniques can lead to different emotional and behavioural responses.","zh":"不同技巧可以帶來不同情緒和行為反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing how parents handle misbehaviour.","zh":"討論父母如何處理不當行為時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be trained to observe","meaning":"接受訓練去觀察","examples":[{"en":"Mothers were trained to observe emotional incidents involving their children.","zh":"母親接受訓練去觀察涉及自己孩子的情緒事件。"},{"en":"To be trained to observe means to be taught how to watch and record something carefully.","zh":"be trained to observe 指被教導如何仔細觀看和記錄某事。"},{"en":"Student teachers may be trained to observe classroom behaviour before teaching alone.","zh":"見習老師可能先接受訓練去觀察課室行為，然後才獨自教學。"},{"en":"Training improves observation because people learn what details to notice.","zh":"訓練能改善觀察，因為人們學會注意哪些細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning a systematic way to watch.","zh":"這個短語描述學習一套有系統的觀察方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"emotional incidents","meaning":"情緒事件","examples":[{"en":"The mothers recorded emotional incidents involving their toddlers.","zh":"母親記錄涉及幼兒的情緒事件。"},{"en":"Emotional incidents are events that involve strong feelings such as anger, fear, joy, or sadness.","zh":"emotional incidents 指涉及憤怒、恐懼、快樂或悲傷等強烈情感的事件。"},{"en":"A child crying after losing a toy is an emotional incident at home.","zh":"孩子失去玩具後哭起來，就是家中的情緒事件。"},{"en":"Recording emotional incidents helps researchers understand how children and parents react.","zh":"記錄情緒事件有助研究者了解兒童和父母如何反應。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to feeling-related events, not ordinary routines only.","zh":"這個短語指與情感有關的事件，而不只是普通日常。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"toddler-aged children","meaning":"幼兒年齡的兒童","examples":[{"en":"The study focused on mothers and their toddler-aged children.","zh":"該研究集中於母親和她們幼兒年齡的兒童。"},{"en":"Toddler-aged children are children at the stage when they are beginning to walk, talk, and test independence.","zh":"toddler-aged children 指處於開始走路、說話和試探獨立階段的兒童。"},{"en":"Toddler-aged children often need simple rules and repeated reminders.","zh":"幼兒年齡的兒童通常需要簡單規則和反覆提醒。"},{"en":"This age group may show quick changes in language, emotion, and self-control.","zh":"這個年齡組在語言、情緒和自制方面可能快速改變。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a young developmental stage.","zh":"這個短語指出一個年幼發展階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"disciplinary encounters","meaning":"管教事件","examples":[{"en":"Reports of disciplinary encounters were analysed by the researchers.","zh":"研究者分析了管教事件的報告。"},{"en":"Disciplinary encounters are moments when an adult corrects, warns, or guides a child’s behaviour.","zh":"disciplinary encounters 指成人糾正、警告或引導兒童行為的時刻。"},{"en":"A parent asking a child to stop hitting a sibling is a disciplinary encounter.","zh":"父母要求孩子停止打兄弟姊妹，就是管教事件。"},{"en":"These encounters can affect whether a child feels ashamed, angry, or cooperative.","zh":"這些事件可以影響孩子感到羞愧、憤怒或合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes real interactions around discipline.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞管教的真實互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be analysed in terms of","meaning":"按照……來分析","examples":[{"en":"The reports were analysed in terms of discipline type and child response.","zh":"這些報告按照管教方式和兒童反應來分析。"},{"en":"To be analysed in terms of something means to be studied by focusing on that aspect.","zh":"be analysed in terms of something 指集中於某方面來研究。"},{"en":"Exam results may be analysed in terms of gender, school type, and study time.","zh":"考試成績可能按照性別、學校類型和學習時間來分析。"},{"en":"Choosing clear categories helps researchers compare cases more fairly.","zh":"選擇清楚類別有助研究者更公平地比較個案。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the basis of analysis.","zh":"這個短語解釋分析的依據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"types of discipline","meaning":"管教方式","examples":[{"en":"The study compared several types of discipline used by mothers.","zh":"該研究比較了母親使用的幾種管教方式。"},{"en":"Types of discipline are different methods adults use to guide or correct behaviour.","zh":"types of discipline 指成人用來引導或糾正行為的不同方法。"},{"en":"Reasoning, warnings, time-out, and loss of privileges are types of discipline.","zh":"說理、警告、暫停活動和失去特權都是管教方式。"},{"en":"Different discipline types may teach children different lessons.","zh":"不同管教方式可能教會孩子不同教訓。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when comparing parenting or classroom management methods.","zh":"比較育兒或課室管理方法時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"reasoning","meaning":"說理","examples":[{"en":"Reasoning alone was not always effective in securing compliance.","zh":"單靠說理並不總能有效促使服從。"},{"en":"Reasoning means explaining why a rule or request makes sense.","zh":"reasoning 指解釋為何某規則或要求合理。"},{"en":"A parent uses reasoning when saying, “You need a coat because it is cold outside.”","zh":"父母說「外面很冷，所以你需要外套」時，就是在說理。"},{"en":"Reasoning can help children understand rules, but it may not work when emotions are high.","zh":"說理可以幫助孩子理解規則，但情緒高漲時未必有效。"},{"en":"This word refers to explanation based on logic.","zh":"這個字指基於邏輯的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"verbal prohibition","meaning":"口頭禁止","examples":[{"en":"Verbal prohibition was one of the disciplinary techniques examined.","zh":"口頭禁止是被檢視的管教技巧之一。"},{"en":"Verbal prohibition means using words to tell someone not to do something.","zh":"verbal prohibition 指用說話告訴某人不要做某事。"},{"en":"A parent uses verbal prohibition when saying, “Do not run near the road.”","zh":"父母說「不要在馬路旁跑」時，就是使用口頭禁止。"},{"en":"Verbal prohibition works best when the warning is clear and immediate.","zh":"當警告清楚而即時，口頭禁止效果最好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a spoken “Don’t” instruction.","zh":"這個短語描述口頭的「不要做」指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"physical coercion","meaning":"身體強制","examples":[{"en":"Physical coercion was somewhat effective in gaining compliance.","zh":"身體強制在促成服從方面有一定效果。"},{"en":"Physical coercion means using physical force or restraint to make someone obey.","zh":"physical coercion 指使用身體力量或限制來令某人服從。"},{"en":"Holding a child’s hand to stop him from touching a hot pan is a mild form of physical control.","zh":"握住孩子的手阻止他碰熱鍋，是一種輕微的身體控制。"},{"en":"Coercion may create quick compliance, but it can also cause fear or resistance.","zh":"強制可能帶來快速服從，但也可能造成恐懼或抗拒。"},{"en":"This phrase should be used carefully because it involves force.","zh":"這個短語涉及力量，應小心使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"love withdrawal","meaning":"撤回關愛","examples":[{"en":"Love withdrawal was particularly effective when combined with other techniques.","zh":"撤回關愛與其他技巧結合使用時特別有效。"},{"en":"Love withdrawal means showing reduced affection or emotional warmth after a child misbehaves.","zh":"love withdrawal 指孩子行為不當後，成人表現出減少關愛或情感溫暖。"},{"en":"A parent may withdraw warmth by becoming distant after a child lies.","zh":"孩子說謊後，父母可能變得疏離，這就是撤回關愛。"},{"en":"This technique may gain obedience because children want to restore emotional closeness.","zh":"這種技巧可能促成服從，因為孩子想恢復情感親密。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an emotional form of discipline.","zh":"這個短語描述一種情感性管教方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"combinations thereof","meaning":"上述方法的不同組合","examples":[{"en":"The researchers also studied combinations thereof.","zh":"研究者也研究了上述方法的不同組合。"},{"en":"Combinations thereof means different mixtures of the methods or things just mentioned.","zh":"combinations thereof 指剛才提到的方法或事物的不同混合。"},{"en":"A teacher may use praise, reminders, or combinations thereof during class.","zh":"老師可能在課堂中使用讚賞、提醒或上述方法的不同組合。"},{"en":"Studying combinations helps researchers see whether methods work better together.","zh":"研究組合有助研究者了解方法一起使用時是否更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and refers back to items already listed.","zh":"這個短語較正式，指回已列出的項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"children’s responses","meaning":"兒童的反應","examples":[{"en":"The study classified children’s responses to discipline.","zh":"該研究分類兒童對管教的反應。"},{"en":"Children’s responses are the ways children react to adults’ actions or instructions.","zh":"children’s responses 指兒童對成人行動或指示的反應方式。"},{"en":"A child may respond to discipline with obedience, tears, avoidance, or negotiation.","zh":"孩子可能以服從、哭泣、逃避或協商來回應管教。"},{"en":"Responses can show whether a technique calms a child or creates resistance.","zh":"反應可以顯示某技巧是令孩子冷靜還是造成抗拒。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe behaviour after adult intervention.","zh":"這個短語幫助描述成人介入後的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"avoidance","meaning":"逃避行為","examples":[{"en":"Avoidance was one possible response to parental discipline.","zh":"逃避行為是對父母管教的一種可能反應。"},{"en":"Avoidance means trying to escape, ignore, or stay away from an unpleasant situation.","zh":"avoidance 指嘗試逃離、忽視或遠離不愉快情況。"},{"en":"A child shows avoidance when he hides under the table instead of answering a parent.","zh":"孩子躲到桌下而不回答父母時，就是表現出逃避行為。"},{"en":"Avoidance may reduce conflict briefly but leave the problem unresolved.","zh":"逃避可能短暫減少衝突，但問題仍未解決。"},{"en":"This word describes moving away from pressure rather than facing it directly.","zh":"這個字描述遠離壓力，而不是直接面對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"type of misdeed","meaning":"過失類型","examples":[{"en":"The child’s response sometimes depended on the type of misdeed.","zh":"孩子的反應有時取決於過失類型。"},{"en":"Type of misdeed means the kind of wrong action a child has done.","zh":"type of misdeed 指孩子所做錯事的種類。"},{"en":"Breaking a toy and hurting a classmate are different types of misdeed.","zh":"弄壞玩具和傷害同學是不同過失類型。"},{"en":"Parents may respond differently depending on whether harm was accidental or deliberate.","zh":"父母可能根據傷害是意外還是故意而作出不同回應。"},{"en":"This phrase helps classify children’s misbehaviour.","zh":"這個短語幫助分類兒童的不當行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"harm to people","meaning":"對他人造成傷害","examples":[{"en":"Some misdeeds involved harm to people.","zh":"有些過失涉及對他人造成傷害。"},{"en":"Harm to people means injury, pain, fear, or upset caused to other people.","zh":"harm to people 指對他人造成受傷、痛苦、恐懼或不安。"},{"en":"Pushing a classmate can cause harm to people, even if the child says it was a joke.","zh":"推同學可能對他人造成傷害，即使孩子說那只是玩笑。"},{"en":"Behaviour involving harm to people is often treated more seriously than a small mess.","zh":"涉及傷害他人的行為通常比弄亂東西更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on damage done to persons rather than objects.","zh":"這個短語集中於對人而不是物件造成的損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"harm to property","meaning":"對財物造成損害","examples":[{"en":"The study also examined acts involving harm to property.","zh":"該研究也檢視涉及對財物造成損害的行為。"},{"en":"Harm to property means damage done to objects, buildings, or belongings.","zh":"harm to property 指對物件、建築物或個人物品造成損害。"},{"en":"Drawing on a wall or breaking a toy can be harm to property.","zh":"在牆上塗鴉或弄壞玩具都可以是對財物造成損害。"},{"en":"Property damage may lead parents to teach responsibility and repair.","zh":"財物損害可能令父母教導責任和修復。"},{"en":"This phrase separates damage to things from harm to people.","zh":"這個短語把對物件的損害與對人的傷害分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lapses of self-control","meaning":"一時失去自制力","examples":[{"en":"Some incidents were classified as lapses of self-control.","zh":"有些事件被分類為一時失去自制力。"},{"en":"Lapses of self-control are moments when someone briefly fails to control their behaviour or emotion.","zh":"lapses of self-control 指某人短暫未能控制行為或情緒的時刻。"},{"en":"A child grabbing sweets before dinner may show a lapse of self-control.","zh":"孩子晚飯前搶糖果，可能顯示一時失去自制力。"},{"en":"Tiredness, hunger, or strong emotion can lead to lapses of self-control.","zh":"疲倦、飢餓或強烈情緒可以導致一時失去自制力。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a temporary failure rather than a fixed character problem.","zh":"這個短語暗示暫時失控，而不是固定性格問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"results indicated that","meaning":"結果顯示","examples":[{"en":"The results indicated that some disciplinary combinations were more effective.","zh":"結果顯示某些管教組合更有效。"},{"en":"Results indicated that means the findings showed or suggested a conclusion.","zh":"results indicated that 指研究結果顯示或暗示某個結論。"},{"en":"The test results indicated that students needed more listening practice.","zh":"測驗結果顯示學生需要更多聆聽練習。"},{"en":"Researchers use this phrase when evidence points toward a pattern.","zh":"當證據指向某種模式時，研究者會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what data seem to show.","zh":"這個短語引出數據似乎顯示的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be effective in securing","meaning":"能有效促使……","examples":[{"en":"Love withdrawal was effective in securing children’s compliance.","zh":"撤回關愛能有效促使兒童服從。"},{"en":"To be effective in securing something means to successfully achieve or obtain it.","zh":"be effective in securing something 指成功達成或取得某事。"},{"en":"Clear reminders may be effective in securing students’ attention before a lesson.","zh":"清楚提醒可能能有效促使學生在上課前集中注意力。"},{"en":"A method is effective when it produces the desired response.","zh":"當方法產生預期反應，它就是有效的。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in research.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"regardless of","meaning":"不論；無論","examples":[{"en":"The technique worked regardless of which other method accompanied it.","zh":"不論伴隨哪種其他方法，這種技巧都有效。"},{"en":"Regardless of means no matter what or despite something.","zh":"regardless of 指不論甚麼或儘管某事。"},{"en":"Students must submit homework on time regardless of whether they find it difficult.","zh":"無論學生覺得功課困難與否，都必須準時提交。"},{"en":"If a result appears regardless of conditions, it may be quite strong.","zh":"如果某結果在不同條件下都出現，它可能相當有力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something remains true in different situations.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事在不同情況下仍成立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be combined with","meaning":"與……結合使用","examples":[{"en":"Love withdrawal was often combined with another disciplinary technique.","zh":"撤回關愛常與另一種管教技巧結合使用。"},{"en":"To be combined with something means to be used together with it.","zh":"be combined with something 指與某物一起使用。"},{"en":"Reading practice can be combined with vocabulary games.","zh":"閱讀練習可以與詞彙遊戲結合使用。"},{"en":"Combining methods can strengthen an effect or change how children respond.","zh":"結合方法可以加強效果或改變兒童反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using two things together.","zh":"這個短語描述把兩樣東西一起使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"avoidant responses","meaning":"逃避式反應","examples":[{"en":"Avoidant responses were more likely after love withdrawal.","zh":"撤回關愛後較可能出現逃避式反應。"},{"en":"Avoidant responses are reactions in which a child avoids, withdraws, or escapes from the situation.","zh":"avoidant responses 指孩子逃避、退縮或離開情境的反應。"},{"en":"A child may give an avoidant response by looking away and refusing to talk.","zh":"孩子望向別處並拒絕說話，可能就是逃避式反應。"},{"en":"Emotional pressure can lead to avoidance rather than open discussion.","zh":"情感壓力可能導致逃避，而不是開放討論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a defensive reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述防衛性反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"emotional reunification","meaning":"與父母重新建立情感連繫","examples":[{"en":"Emotional reunification with the parent often followed love withdrawal.","zh":"撤回關愛後常出現與父母重新建立情感連繫。"},{"en":"Emotional reunification means restoring warmth, closeness, or connection after emotional distance.","zh":"emotional reunification 指在情感距離後恢復溫暖、親近或連繫。"},{"en":"A parent and child may experience reunification when they hug after an argument.","zh":"父母和孩子爭吵後擁抱時，可能經歷情感重新連繫。"},{"en":"Reunification can reduce distress because the relationship feels safe again.","zh":"重新連繫可以減少不安，因為關係再次感覺安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repairing emotional connection.","zh":"這個短語描述修復情感連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be more likely to follow","meaning":"較可能在……之後出現","examples":[{"en":"Avoidance was more likely to follow love withdrawal than other techniques.","zh":"逃避較可能在撤回關愛之後出現，而不是在其他技巧之後。"},{"en":"To be more likely to follow something means to happen more often after it.","zh":"be more likely to follow something 指較常在某事之後發生。"},{"en":"A quiet mood may be more likely to follow a difficult argument than a happy game.","zh":"困難爭吵後較可能出現安靜情緒，而不是快樂遊戲後。"},{"en":"If one response follows a method often, researchers may see a pattern.","zh":"如果一種反應常跟隨某方法出現，研究者可能看到模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what tends to happen afterwards.","zh":"這個短語描述之後往往會發生甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"somewhat less effective","meaning":"效果稍遜","examples":[{"en":"Physical coercion was somewhat less effective than love withdrawal.","zh":"身體強制比撤回關愛效果稍遜。"},{"en":"Somewhat less effective means a little or moderately less successful.","zh":"somewhat less effective 指成功程度稍低或中等程度較低。"},{"en":"Email reminders may be somewhat less effective than face-to-face reminders for young children.","zh":"對幼兒來說，電郵提醒可能比面對面提醒效果稍遜。"},{"en":"A method can still work while being less effective than another method.","zh":"一種方法可以仍然有效，但比另一種方法稍遜。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a careful comparison, not a complete rejection.","zh":"這個短語作出謹慎比較，而不是完全否定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be ineffective unless","meaning":"除非……，否則無效","examples":[{"en":"Reasoning was ineffective unless it was combined with physical coercion.","zh":"除非說理與身體強制結合使用，否則無效。"},{"en":"To be ineffective unless something happens means not to work except under that condition.","zh":"be ineffective unless something happens 指除非某條件成立，否則不起作用。"},{"en":"A study plan may be ineffective unless the student follows it regularly.","zh":"除非學生定期跟從，否則學習計劃可能無效。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a method depends on another condition to succeed.","zh":"這個短語顯示一種方法需要另一條件才會成功。"},{"en":"It is useful for explaining limits.","zh":"它適合用來解釋限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"express noncompliance directly","meaning":"直接表達不服從","examples":[{"en":"Younger children sometimes express noncompliance directly.","zh":"年幼兒童有時會直接表達不服從。"},{"en":"To express noncompliance directly means to refuse openly and clearly.","zh":"express noncompliance directly 指公開而清楚地拒絕服從。"},{"en":"A young child may express noncompliance directly by saying, “No, I won’t.”","zh":"年幼孩子可能說「不，我不要」來直接表達不服從。"},{"en":"Direct refusal is common when children have not yet learned negotiation skills.","zh":"當兒童尚未學會協商技巧時，直接拒絕很常見。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts open refusal with indirect resistance.","zh":"這個短語把公開拒絕與間接抗拒作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as they grow older","meaning":"隨着他們長大","examples":[{"en":"Children may change their behaviour as they grow older.","zh":"隨着兒童長大，他們的行為可能改變。"},{"en":"As they grow older means while they become older and develop.","zh":"as they grow older 指當他們年齡增長並發展時。"},{"en":"Children often become better at explaining feelings as they grow older.","zh":"隨着孩子長大，他們通常更善於解釋感受。"},{"en":"Age brings changes in language, self-control, and social understanding.","zh":"年齡帶來語言、自制力和社交理解的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes development over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sophisticated approaches","meaning":"較複雜成熟的方法","examples":[{"en":"Older children may use more sophisticated approaches to resist requests.","zh":"年長兒童可能使用較複雜成熟的方法來抗拒要求。"},{"en":"Sophisticated approaches are more complex, thoughtful, or skilful methods.","zh":"sophisticated approaches 指較複雜、有思考或有技巧的方法。"},{"en":"Instead of saying “no,” an older child may explain reasons or suggest a compromise.","zh":"年長孩子可能不說「不」，而是解釋原因或提出折衷。"},{"en":"More sophisticated resistance can appear as negotiation rather than open defiance.","zh":"較成熟的抗拒可能以協商而不是公開反抗出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes behaviour that is more developed and strategic.","zh":"這個短語描述較發展成熟和有策略的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"become more skilful at","meaning":"變得更擅長","examples":[{"en":"Children become more skilful at negotiating as they grow older.","zh":"兒童隨着長大變得更擅長協商。"},{"en":"To become more skilful at something means to improve one’s ability to do it.","zh":"become more skilful at something 指做某事的能力有所提高。"},{"en":"Students become more skilful at writing when they receive clear feedback.","zh":"學生收到清楚回饋時，寫作會變得更擅長。"},{"en":"Practice and maturity help children express disagreement more effectively.","zh":"練習和成熟幫助兒童更有效地表達不同意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual improvement in a skill.","zh":"這個短語描述技能上的逐步進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"negotiate","meaning":"協商；討價還價","examples":[{"en":"Older children may negotiate instead of refusing immediately.","zh":"年長兒童可能會協商，而不是立即拒絕。"},{"en":"To negotiate means to discuss an issue in order to reach an agreement.","zh":"negotiate 指討論一個問題，以達成協議。"},{"en":"A child may negotiate by asking to finish a game before starting homework.","zh":"孩子可能要求先完成遊戲再開始功課，這就是協商。"},{"en":"Negotiation can reduce conflict because both sides explain what they want.","zh":"協商可以減少衝突，因為雙方都解釋自己想要甚麼。"},{"en":"This verb describes discussion, not simple obedience or refusal.","zh":"這個動詞描述討論，而不是單純服從或拒絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"give reasons for refusing","meaning":"提出拒絕的理由","examples":[{"en":"Children may learn to give reasons for refusing a request.","zh":"兒童可能學會提出拒絕要求的理由。"},{"en":"To give reasons for refusing means to explain why one does not want to obey or agree.","zh":"give reasons for refusing 指解釋為何不想服從或同意。"},{"en":"A child may say, “I cannot clean now because my homework is due tonight.”","zh":"孩子可能說：「我現在不能清潔，因為今晚要交功課。」"},{"en":"Giving reasons can make refusal sound more thoughtful and less defiant.","zh":"提出理由可以令拒絕聽起來更有思考，而較少反抗意味。"},{"en":"This phrase describes explained disagreement.","zh":"這個短語描述有解釋的不同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rather than directly opposing","meaning":"而不是直接反抗","examples":[{"en":"They may negotiate rather than directly opposing their parents.","zh":"他們可能會協商，而不是直接反抗父母。"},{"en":"Rather than directly opposing means instead of openly resisting or fighting against someone.","zh":"rather than directly opposing 指而不是公開抗拒或反對某人。"},{"en":"A student may ask for extra time rather than directly opposing a teacher’s deadline.","zh":"學生可能要求延長時間，而不是直接反抗老師的限期。"},{"en":"This approach can reduce conflict because disagreement becomes discussion.","zh":"這種方法可以減少衝突，因為不同意變成討論。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly contrasts negotiation with direct resistance.","zh":"這個短語清楚對比協商與直接抗拒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"reflect development","meaning":"反映成長發展","examples":[{"en":"Noncompliance can sometimes reflect healthy development.","zh":"不服從有時可以反映健康成長發展。"},{"en":"To reflect development means to show that a person is growing or changing in ability.","zh":"reflect development 指顯示一個人在能力上成長或改變。"},{"en":"A child asking for reasons may reflect development in thinking skills.","zh":"孩子要求理由可能反映思考能力的發展。"},{"en":"Some disagreement can show growing independence rather than simple bad behaviour.","zh":"某些不同意可以顯示獨立性增長，而不只是壞行為。"},{"en":"This phrase helps interpret behaviour as part of growth.","zh":"這個短語幫助把行為理解為成長的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"benefit children","meaning":"對兒童有益","examples":[{"en":"Learning to negotiate may benefit children in some ways.","zh":"學習協商在某些方面可能對兒童有益。"},{"en":"To benefit children means to help children or support their development.","zh":"benefit children 指幫助兒童或支持其發展。"},{"en":"Reading aloud can benefit children by improving vocabulary and attention.","zh":"朗讀可以透過改善詞彙和專注力而對兒童有益。"},{"en":"A skill benefits children when it helps them handle school, family, or friendships better.","zh":"當一項技能幫助兒童更好處理學校、家庭或友情，它就對兒童有益。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on positive effects for children.","zh":"這個短語集中於對兒童的正面影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hold different views","meaning":"持有不同看法","examples":[{"en":"Experts have held different views about childhood noncompliance.","zh":"專家對兒童不服從持有不同看法。"},{"en":"To hold different views means to have different opinions or beliefs.","zh":"hold different views 指有不同意見或信念。"},{"en":"Parents and teachers may hold different views about how much homework children need.","zh":"父母和老師可能對孩子需要多少功課持有不同看法。"},{"en":"Different views often appear when evidence is complex or values differ.","zh":"當證據複雜或價值觀不同，常會出現不同看法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disagreement in opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述意見上的分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in recent years","meaning":"近年來","examples":[{"en":"In recent years, experts have debated how much compliance children need.","zh":"近年來，專家一直討論兒童需要多少服從。"},{"en":"In recent years means during the last few years or the modern period.","zh":"in recent years 指在過去幾年或近代時期。"},{"en":"In recent years, many schools have paid more attention to children’s mental health.","zh":"近年來，許多學校更重視兒童心理健康。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a fairly new trend or discussion.","zh":"這個短語引出較新的趨勢或討論。"},{"en":"It helps contrast current thinking with older views.","zh":"它幫助把當前想法與較舊觀點作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"instil compliance in","meaning":"向……灌輸服從觀念","examples":[{"en":"Some experts have tried to instil compliance in children.","zh":"有些專家曾嘗試向兒童灌輸服從觀念。"},{"en":"To instil compliance in children means to gradually teach them to follow rules and instructions.","zh":"instil compliance in children 指逐步教導兒童遵守規則和指示。"},{"en":"Parents may instil compliance by using routines and consistent expectations.","zh":"父母可能透過常規和一致期望向孩子灌輸服從觀念。"},{"en":"Repeated guidance can make obedience feel normal over time.","zh":"反覆引導可以隨時間令服從感覺正常。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests slowly building a habit or attitude.","zh":"這個短語暗示慢慢建立習慣或態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"daily activities","meaning":"日常活動","examples":[{"en":"A child’s daily activities should follow a predictable order.","zh":"兒童的日常活動應按可預測次序進行。"},{"en":"Daily activities are the things people do regularly each day.","zh":"daily activities 指人們每天定期做的事情。"},{"en":"Brushing teeth, eating breakfast, and going to school are daily activities for many children.","zh":"刷牙、吃早餐和上學是許多孩子的日常活動。"},{"en":"When daily activities are predictable, children may feel calmer and more cooperative.","zh":"當日常活動可預測時，兒童可能感到更平靜、更合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordinary routines.","zh":"這個短語描述普通常規。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"occur in the same order","meaning":"按相同次序進行","examples":[{"en":"Wallace Friesen argued that activities should occur in the same order each day.","zh":"Wallace Friesen 認為活動每天應按相同次序進行。"},{"en":"To occur in the same order means to happen in the same sequence every time.","zh":"occur in the same order 指每次都按相同順序發生。"},{"en":"A bedtime routine may occur in the same order: bath, story, then sleep.","zh":"睡前程序可能按相同次序進行：洗澡、講故事，然後睡覺。"},{"en":"Repeated order helps children predict what comes next.","zh":"反覆的次序幫助兒童預測接下來會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stable sequencing.","zh":"這個短語描述穩定順序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as much as possible","meaning":"盡可能","examples":[{"en":"A child’s routine should remain consistent as much as possible.","zh":"兒童的常規應盡可能保持一致。"},{"en":"As much as possible means to the greatest practical degree.","zh":"as much as possible 指在實際可行範圍內最大程度地。"},{"en":"Students should revise as much as possible before an important exam, without losing sleep.","zh":"學生應在不犧牲睡眠下，盡可能在重要考試前溫習。"},{"en":"This phrase allows for effort while recognising that perfect consistency may be impossible.","zh":"這個短語容許努力，同時承認完美一致可能不可能。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving realistic advice.","zh":"給出務實建議時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"defiant children","meaning":"反叛的兒童","examples":[{"en":"A regular routine may be particularly helpful for defiant children.","zh":"固定常規可能對反叛的兒童特別有幫助。"},{"en":"Defiant children are children who often resist rules, instructions, or adult authority.","zh":"defiant children 指常抗拒規則、指示或成人權威的兒童。"},{"en":"A defiant child may refuse to put on shoes even when the family is late.","zh":"反叛的孩子即使家人快遲到，也可能拒絕穿鞋。"},{"en":"Predictable routines can reduce defiance because fewer requests feel sudden.","zh":"可預測常規可以減少反抗，因為較少要求感覺突然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes children who openly challenge adults.","zh":"這個短語描述公開挑戰成人的兒童。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ultimately the most important","meaning":"最終是最重要的","examples":[{"en":"Developing a routine may ultimately be the most important strategy.","zh":"建立固定程序最終可能是最重要的策略。"},{"en":"Ultimately the most important means finally or in the long run the most important.","zh":"ultimately the most important 指最終或長遠來說最重要。"},{"en":"For language learning, daily practice may ultimately be the most important habit.","zh":"對語言學習來說，每日練習最終可能是最重要的習慣。"},{"en":"Something may seem simple but become most important because it affects many later actions.","zh":"某事可能看似簡單，但因影響許多後續行動而變得最重要。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the final main priority.","zh":"這個短語突出最終的主要優先事項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"develop a routine","meaning":"建立固定程序","examples":[{"en":"Parents can develop a routine that helps a child know what to expect.","zh":"父母可以建立固定程序，幫助孩子知道會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"To develop a routine means to create a regular pattern of activities.","zh":"develop a routine 指建立一套固定活動模式。"},{"en":"A family may develop a routine of dinner, homework, reading, and bedtime.","zh":"家庭可能建立晚飯、功課、閱讀和睡覺的固定程序。"},{"en":"Routines reduce arguments because children know the order of events.","zh":"固定程序減少爭吵，因為孩子知道事情的次序。"},{"en":"This phrase describes building a predictable daily structure.","zh":"這個短語描述建立可預測的日常結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"know what to expect","meaning":"知道會發生甚麼","examples":[{"en":"A regular routine helps children know what to expect.","zh":"固定常規幫助兒童知道會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"To know what to expect means to understand what will probably happen next.","zh":"know what to expect 指明白接下來大概會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"A timetable helps students know what to expect during the school day.","zh":"時間表幫助學生知道上學日會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Children feel safer when they can predict meals, homework, and bedtime.","zh":"當孩子能預測用餐、功課和睡覺時間，他們會感到更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes confidence created by predictability.","zh":"這個短語描述可預測性帶來的信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"increase the chances that","meaning":"增加……的機會","examples":[{"en":"A predictable schedule increases the chances that a child will comply.","zh":"可預測時間表增加孩子服從的機會。"},{"en":"To increase the chances that something happens means to make it more likely.","zh":"increase the chances that something happens 指令某事更可能發生。"},{"en":"Clear revision notes increase the chances that students will remember key points.","zh":"清楚溫習筆記增加學生記住重點的機會。"},{"en":"Predictability can increase compliance because children are not surprised by requests.","zh":"可預測性可以增加服從，因為孩子不會對要求感到突然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes raising probability, not guaranteeing a result.","zh":"這個短語描述提高可能性，而不是保證結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"comply with chores","meaning":"按要求做家務","examples":[{"en":"Children may be more willing to comply with chores when they follow a routine.","zh":"當孩子跟隨固定程序時，可能更願意按要求做家務。"},{"en":"To comply with chores means to do household tasks when asked or expected.","zh":"comply with chores 指在被要求或被期望時完成家務。"},{"en":"A child complies with chores when she puts laundry away after dinner.","zh":"孩子晚飯後收好洗好的衣服，就是按要求做家務。"},{"en":"Routine can make chores feel normal rather than like sudden punishment.","zh":"固定程序可以令家務感覺正常，而不是突如其來的懲罰。"},{"en":"This phrase connects obedience with everyday home tasks.","zh":"這個短語把服從與日常家庭任務連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"homework requests","meaning":"做功課的要求","examples":[{"en":"A regular schedule can reduce resistance to homework requests.","zh":"固定時間表可以減少對做功課要求的抗拒。"},{"en":"Homework requests are instructions or reminders asking a child to do schoolwork at home.","zh":"homework requests 指要求或提醒孩子在家做學校功課的指示。"},{"en":"A parent makes a homework request when saying, “Please start your maths now.”","zh":"父母說「請現在開始做數學」時，就是提出做功課的要求。"},{"en":"Children may resist homework requests less when homework time is predictable.","zh":"當做功課時間可預測，孩子可能較少抗拒做功課要求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes requests connected with study at home.","zh":"這個短語描述與在家學習有關的要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hygiene requests","meaning":"個人衞生要求","examples":[{"en":"Children may also respond better to routine hygiene requests.","zh":"兒童也可能對固定的個人衞生要求反應更好。"},{"en":"Hygiene requests are instructions about cleanliness, such as washing hands or brushing teeth.","zh":"hygiene requests 指關於清潔的指示，例如洗手或刷牙。"},{"en":"A parent gives a hygiene request when asking a child to wash before dinner.","zh":"父母要求孩子晚飯前洗手，就是提出個人衞生要求。"},{"en":"Regular hygiene routines can reduce arguments because the request becomes expected.","zh":"固定衞生常規可以減少爭吵，因為要求變得可預期。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to health and cleanliness-related instructions.","zh":"這個短語指與健康和清潔有關的指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"undesirable activities","meaning":"不喜歡的活動","examples":[{"en":"Children often resist undesirable activities.","zh":"兒童常抗拒不喜歡的活動。"},{"en":"Undesirable activities are tasks that people do not want to do or do not enjoy.","zh":"undesirable activities 指人們不想做或不享受的任務。"},{"en":"For many children, tidying a room is an undesirable activity.","zh":"對許多孩子來說，整理房間是不喜歡的活動。"},{"en":"Undesirable tasks cause less conflict when they are short, predictable, and followed by something pleasant.","zh":"當不喜歡的任務短、可預測，並接着有愉快活動，衝突會較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes activities that feel unpleasant or unwanted.","zh":"這個短語描述令人不快或不想做的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at suitable times","meaning":"在合適時間","examples":[{"en":"Unpopular tasks should occur at suitable times during the day.","zh":"不受歡迎的任務應在一天中的合適時間進行。"},{"en":"At suitable times means at moments that are appropriate or practical.","zh":"at suitable times 指在合適或實際可行的時刻。"},{"en":"Parents may ask children to do homework at a suitable time, not when they are exhausted.","zh":"父母可能在合適時間要求孩子做功課，而不是在孩子筋疲力盡時。"},{"en":"Timing matters because children comply better when they are not hungry or tired.","zh":"時間安排很重要，因為孩子不餓不累時較容易服從。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on choosing the right moment.","zh":"這個短語集中於選擇正確時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"become habits","meaning":"變成習慣","examples":[{"en":"Repeated activities eventually become habits.","zh":"重複的活動最終會變成習慣。"},{"en":"To become habits means to turn into regular behaviours people do almost automatically.","zh":"become habits 指變成幾乎自動進行的常規行為。"},{"en":"Brushing teeth before bed becomes a habit when children do it every night.","zh":"當孩子每晚睡前刷牙，刷牙就會變成習慣。"},{"en":"Repetition helps actions feel normal and require less effort.","zh":"重複幫助行動變得正常，並需要較少努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how repeated behaviour becomes automatic.","zh":"這個短語描述重複行為如何變得自動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be carried out without question","meaning":"不加抗拒地完成","examples":[{"en":"Established habits may be carried out without question.","zh":"已建立的習慣可能會不加抗拒地完成。"},{"en":"To be carried out without question means to be done without arguing or hesitation.","zh":"be carried out without question 指沒有爭辯或猶豫地完成。"},{"en":"In a good routine, packing a school bag may be carried out without question.","zh":"在良好常規中，收拾書包可能會不加抗拒地完成。"},{"en":"Habits reduce resistance because the action no longer feels negotiable.","zh":"習慣減少抗拒，因為行動不再感覺可以討價還價。"},{"en":"This phrase describes automatic cooperation.","zh":"這個短語描述自動合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"develop routines for","meaning":"為……建立固定程序","examples":[{"en":"Most adults have developed routines for everyday tasks.","zh":"大多數成年人已為日常任務建立固定程序。"},{"en":"To develop routines for something means to create regular ways of doing it.","zh":"develop routines for something 指為某事建立固定做法。"},{"en":"A student may develop routines for revision, exercise, and sleep.","zh":"學生可能為溫習、運動和睡眠建立固定程序。"},{"en":"Routines save mental energy because people do not need to decide every step again.","zh":"固定程序節省心理能量，因為人們不用每一步重新決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organising repeated tasks.","zh":"這個短語描述組織反覆任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"know what to expect","meaning":"知道可以預期甚麼","examples":[{"en":"A personal routine helps people know what to expect each day.","zh":"個人常規幫助人知道每天可以預期甚麼。"},{"en":"To know what to expect means to understand the likely order or outcome of events.","zh":"know what to expect 指理解事情可能的次序或結果。"},{"en":"A child knows what to expect when bedtime always follows reading.","zh":"當睡前閱讀後總是睡覺，孩子就知道可以預期甚麼。"},{"en":"Predictability can reduce anxiety because fewer events feel sudden.","zh":"可預測性能減少焦慮，因為較少事情感覺突然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the comfort of knowing what comes next.","zh":"這個短語描述知道接下來會發生甚麼所帶來的安心感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"without realising it","meaning":"在沒有察覺的情況下","examples":[{"en":"Many parents already use compliance strategies without realising it.","zh":"許多父母已在沒有察覺的情況下使用服從策略。"},{"en":"Without realising it means without being aware that one is doing something.","zh":"without realising it 指沒有意識到自己正在做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may encourage confidence without realising it by smiling at shy students.","zh":"老師可能透過向害羞學生微笑，在沒有察覺下鼓勵自信。"},{"en":"People often use useful strategies naturally before they learn their official names.","zh":"人們常在學到正式名稱前，自然使用有用策略。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unconscious or unnoticed action.","zh":"這個短語描述無意識或未被注意的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"become very upset","meaning":"變得非常不安","examples":[{"en":"Children can become very upset when routines are unexpectedly changed.","zh":"當常規突然改變時，兒童可能變得非常不安。"},{"en":"To become very upset means to feel strongly sad, angry, worried, or distressed.","zh":"become very upset 指感到強烈悲傷、憤怒、擔心或困擾。"},{"en":"A toddler may become very upset if bedtime happens without the usual story.","zh":"如果睡前沒有平常的故事，幼兒可能變得非常不安。"},{"en":"Sudden changes can upset children because they lose predictability.","zh":"突然改變會令兒童不安，因為他們失去可預測性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong emotional reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈情緒反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"daily expectations","meaning":"每日預期事項","examples":[{"en":"Daily expectations should form part of a regular routine.","zh":"每日預期事項應成為固定常規的一部分。"},{"en":"Daily expectations are things people are expected to do each day.","zh":"daily expectations 指人們每天被期望做的事情。"},{"en":"A child’s daily expectations may include brushing teeth, packing a bag, and doing homework.","zh":"孩子的每日預期事項可能包括刷牙、收拾書包和做功課。"},{"en":"Clear expectations reduce conflict because children know what adults want.","zh":"清楚期望可以減少衝突，因為孩子知道成人想要甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes everyday responsibilities or expected actions.","zh":"這個短語描述日常責任或預期行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be made part of","meaning":"被納入……之中","examples":[{"en":"Necessary activities should be made part of the child’s routine.","zh":"必要活動應被納入兒童的常規之中。"},{"en":"To be made part of something means to be included in it regularly.","zh":"be made part of something 指被定期包括在某事之中。"},{"en":"Reading can be made part of bedtime if parents do it every night.","zh":"如果父母每晚都做，閱讀可以被納入睡前程序。"},{"en":"When a task becomes part of a routine, children resist it less.","zh":"當任務成為常規的一部分，孩子較少抗拒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding something into a regular pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述把某事加入固定模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"plan to do","meaning":"計劃去做","examples":[{"en":"Children think about what they plan to do each day.","zh":"兒童會思考自己每天計劃去做甚麼。"},{"en":"To plan to do something means to decide in advance that one will do it.","zh":"plan to do something 指事先決定將會做某事。"},{"en":"A child may plan to play football after finishing homework.","zh":"孩子可能計劃完成功課後去踢足球。"},{"en":"If adults suddenly interrupt a child’s plan, refusal may happen.","zh":"如果成人突然打斷孩子的計劃，可能會出現拒絕。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intended future action.","zh":"這個短語描述預定的未來行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"expect to be able to","meaning":"預期自己能夠","examples":[{"en":"Children expect to be able to do what they want.","zh":"兒童預期自己能夠做想做的事。"},{"en":"To expect to be able to do something means to believe one will have the chance or permission to do it.","zh":"expect to be able to do something 指相信自己會有機會或許可做某事。"},{"en":"A child may expect to be able to watch cartoons after dinner.","zh":"孩子可能預期自己晚飯後能夠看卡通片。"},{"en":"When expectations are suddenly blocked, children may become upset or defiant.","zh":"當期望突然受阻，兒童可能變得不安或反抗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes anticipated freedom or opportunity.","zh":"這個短語描述預期中的自由或機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"automatic refusal","meaning":"自動拒絕反應","examples":[{"en":"An unexpected request can result in automatic refusal.","zh":"突然出現的要求可以導致自動拒絕反應。"},{"en":"Automatic refusal is an immediate “no” response given without much thought.","zh":"automatic refusal 指沒有太多思考便立即說「不」的反應。"},{"en":"A child may show automatic refusal when asked to stop a game suddenly.","zh":"當孩子突然被要求停止遊戲，可能表現出自動拒絕。"},{"en":"Sudden requests can trigger refusal because children feel interrupted.","zh":"突如其來的要求可以引發拒絕，因為孩子感到被打斷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quick resistance rather than carefully reasoned disagreement.","zh":"這個短語描述快速抗拒，而不是經仔細思考的不同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"defiant behaviour","meaning":"反抗行為","examples":[{"en":"Sudden changes may trigger defiant behaviour.","zh":"突然改變可能引發反抗行為。"},{"en":"Defiant behaviour is open resistance to rules, requests, or authority.","zh":"defiant behaviour 指公開抗拒規則、要求或權威。"},{"en":"A child shows defiant behaviour when he shouts “I won’t!” and refuses to move.","zh":"孩子大叫「我不要！」並拒絕移動，就是表現反抗行為。"},{"en":"Defiance may increase when children feel controlled, tired, or surprised.","zh":"當孩子感到被控制、疲倦或意外時，反抗可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active opposition, not quiet hesitation.","zh":"這個短語描述主動反對，而不是安靜猶豫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ensure that","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"A consistent routine ensures that important activities are completed.","zh":"一致的常規確保重要活動完成。"},{"en":"To ensure that something happens means to make certain it happens.","zh":"ensure that something happens 指確保某事發生。"},{"en":"A checklist can ensure that students bring all materials to class.","zh":"清單可以確保學生帶齊所有上課材料。"},{"en":"Parents use routines to ensure that homework, meals, and sleep happen on time.","zh":"父母使用常規來確保功課、用餐和睡眠準時進行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a result more certain.","zh":"這個短語描述令結果更確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in the same general order","meaning":"按大致相同的次序","examples":[{"en":"The activities should be completed in the same general order each day.","zh":"這些活動每天應按大致相同的次序完成。"},{"en":"In the same general order means in roughly the same sequence, even if small details change.","zh":"in the same general order 指大致按相同順序，即使小細節會改變。"},{"en":"A child may wash, read, and sleep in the same general order every night.","zh":"孩子可能每晚按洗澡、閱讀、睡覺的大致相同次序進行。"},{"en":"General order gives predictability without requiring perfect sameness.","zh":"大致次序提供可預測性，但不要求完全一樣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes flexible but stable sequencing.","zh":"這個短語描述靈活但穩定的順序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"enjoyable activities","meaning":"令人享受的活動","examples":[{"en":"Enjoyable activities can be used to motivate children.","zh":"令人享受的活動可以用來推動兒童。"},{"en":"Enjoyable activities are things children like doing and find pleasant.","zh":"enjoyable activities 指孩子喜歡做並覺得愉快的事情。"},{"en":"Playing a game, drawing, or visiting a park can be enjoyable activities.","zh":"玩遊戲、畫畫或去公園都可以是令人享受的活動。"},{"en":"Enjoyable activities can encourage children to finish less pleasant tasks first.","zh":"令人享受的活動可以鼓勵孩子先完成較不愉快的任務。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to activities that feel rewarding.","zh":"這個短語指感覺有回報的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"frequently resist","meaning":"經常抗拒","examples":[{"en":"Some children frequently resist chores or homework.","zh":"有些兒童經常抗拒家務或功課。"},{"en":"To frequently resist something means to oppose it often.","zh":"frequently resist something 指經常反對或拒絕某事。"},{"en":"A child may frequently resist bedtime if the routine changes every night.","zh":"如果睡前程序每晚改變，孩子可能經常抗拒睡覺。"},{"en":"Frequent resistance can become a pattern if adults respond inconsistently.","zh":"如果成人回應不一致，頻繁抗拒可能變成模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated opposition, not one unusual refusal.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆反對，而不是一次不尋常拒絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"positive reinforcement","meaning":"正面強化","examples":[{"en":"An enjoyable activity can work as positive reinforcement.","zh":"令人享受的活動可以作為正面強化。"},{"en":"Positive reinforcement means adding something pleasant after a behaviour to encourage it to happen again.","zh":"positive reinforcement 指在某行為後加入愉快事物，以鼓勵該行為再次發生。"},{"en":"Praise after a child shares toys can be positive reinforcement.","zh":"孩子分享玩具後得到讚賞，就是正面強化。"},{"en":"Reinforcement works because children connect the behaviour with a good result.","zh":"強化有效，是因為孩子把行為與好結果連起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in behaviour learning and parenting.","zh":"這個短語常見於行為學習和育兒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"comply with a request","meaning":"遵從要求","examples":[{"en":"The child receives positive reinforcement after complying with a request.","zh":"孩子在遵從要求後獲得正面強化。"},{"en":"To comply with a request means to do what someone has asked.","zh":"comply with a request 指按照別人的要求去做。"},{"en":"A child complies with a request when he washes his hands after being told.","zh":"孩子被要求後洗手，就是遵從要求。"},{"en":"Reinforcement after compliance can make the behaviour more likely next time.","zh":"服從後得到強化，可以令下次更可能出現該行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes following a specific instruction.","zh":"這個短語描述遵從具體指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"arrange the day so that","meaning":"安排一天的活動，使……","examples":[{"en":"Parents can arrange the day so that less popular tasks come first.","zh":"父母可以安排一天的活動，使較不受歡迎的任務先進行。"},{"en":"To arrange the day so that something happens means to plan the order of daily activities for a purpose.","zh":"arrange the day so that something happens 指為某目的規劃每日活動次序。"},{"en":"A parent may arrange the day so that homework happens before television.","zh":"父母可能安排一天，使功課在看電視前完成。"},{"en":"Good arrangement can reduce arguments by making the order predictable.","zh":"良好安排可以透過令次序可預測而減少爭吵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes purposeful scheduling.","zh":"這個短語描述有目的的時間安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"occur immediately before","meaning":"緊接在……之前發生","examples":[{"en":"A resisted activity can occur immediately before a preferred one.","zh":"受抗拒的活動可以緊接在喜愛的活動之前發生。"},{"en":"To occur immediately before something means to happen right before it.","zh":"occur immediately before something 指正正在某事之前發生。"},{"en":"Homework may occur immediately before playtime in a child’s routine.","zh":"在孩子常規中，功課可能緊接在遊戲時間之前發生。"},{"en":"Placing an unpopular task before a pleasant one can increase motivation.","zh":"把不受歡迎任務放在愉快活動前，可以增加動力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes close sequence in time.","zh":"這個短語描述時間上的緊密次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"highly preferred activities","meaning":"非常喜愛的活動","examples":[{"en":"Children are motivated by highly preferred activities.","zh":"兒童會受到非常喜愛的活動推動。"},{"en":"Highly preferred activities are activities children strongly like or choose often.","zh":"highly preferred activities 指兒童非常喜歡或經常選擇的活動。"},{"en":"For one child, drawing may be a highly preferred activity after homework.","zh":"對一個孩子來說，畫畫可能是功課後非常喜愛的活動。"},{"en":"Preferred activities can motivate effort because children want to reach them.","zh":"喜愛的活動可以推動努力，因為孩子想進入那些活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong personal preference.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈個人偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reduce defiant behaviour","meaning":"減少反抗行為","examples":[{"en":"A well-planned schedule can reduce defiant behaviour.","zh":"規劃良好的時間表可以減少反抗行為。"},{"en":"To reduce defiant behaviour means to make open resistance less frequent or less intense.","zh":"reduce defiant behaviour 指令公開抗拒變得較少或較不強烈。"},{"en":"A clear bedtime routine can reduce defiant behaviour at night.","zh":"清楚睡前常規可以減少夜晚的反抗行為。"},{"en":"Defiance often decreases when children know what is expected and what comes next.","zh":"當孩子知道被期望甚麼和接下來會發生甚麼，反抗常會減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lowering opposition to rules.","zh":"這個短語描述降低對規則的反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"motivate someone to perform","meaning":"推動某人完成……","examples":[{"en":"A preferred activity may motivate the child to perform an undesirable task.","zh":"喜愛的活動可能推動孩子完成不喜歡的任務。"},{"en":"To motivate someone to perform a task means to give them a reason to do it.","zh":"motivate someone to perform a task 指給某人理由去完成某任務。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a class game to motivate students to finish reading quietly.","zh":"老師可能使用班級遊戲來推動學生安靜完成閱讀。"},{"en":"Motivation increases when the task is followed by something rewarding.","zh":"當任務之後有獎勵，動力會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what encourages action.","zh":"這個短語解釋甚麼鼓勵行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be presented as though","meaning":"被表達得好像……","examples":[{"en":"The arrangement should not be presented as though it were a punishment or bribe.","zh":"這個安排不應被表達得好像是懲罰或賄賂。"},{"en":"To be presented as though something were true means to be described in a way that makes it seem true.","zh":"be presented as though something were true 指被描述得令某事看起來是真的。"},{"en":"A study task should not be presented as though it were a threat.","zh":"學習任務不應被表達得好像是一種威脅。"},{"en":"How adults word an arrangement can change how children feel about it.","zh":"成人如何措辭表達安排，可以改變兒童對它的感受。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the impression created by explanation.","zh":"這個短語集中於解釋方式造成的印象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be allowed only if","meaning":"只有在……情況下才獲准","examples":[{"en":"The preferred activity should not appear to be allowed only if the child obeys.","zh":"喜愛的活動不應看似只有在孩子服從時才獲准。"},{"en":"Be allowed only if means be permitted under one condition and not otherwise.","zh":"be allowed only if 指只在某條件下被允許，否則不允許。"},{"en":"A child may feel controlled if playtime is allowed only if every task is perfect.","zh":"如果只有每項任務都完美才可玩，孩子可能感到被控制。"},{"en":"Conditional permission can feel like a bribe or threat if worded badly.","zh":"如果措辭不好，條件式許可可能感覺像賄賂或威脅。"},{"en":"This phrase describes permission tied to a requirement.","zh":"這個短語描述與要求掛鈎的許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"complete the non-preferred activity","meaning":"完成不喜歡的活動","examples":[{"en":"The child must complete the non-preferred activity first.","zh":"孩子必須先完成不喜歡的活動。"},{"en":"To complete the non-preferred activity means to finish the task the child does not especially like.","zh":"complete the non-preferred activity 指完成孩子不太喜歡的任務。"},{"en":"A child may complete tidying the room before watching a cartoon.","zh":"孩子可能先完成整理房間，再看卡通片。"},{"en":"Completing a disliked task first can make the later enjoyable activity feel earned.","zh":"先完成不喜歡的任務，可以令之後的愉快活動感覺像是應得的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finishing an unpopular task.","zh":"這個短語描述完成不受歡迎的任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"word the request","meaning":"措辭表達要求","examples":[{"en":"Parents should word the request carefully and positively.","zh":"父母應小心而正面地措辭表達要求。"},{"en":"To word the request means to choose the exact words used when asking someone to do something.","zh":"word the request 指選擇提出要求時使用的具體字句。"},{"en":"A parent may word a request as “Please put your shoes by the door” rather than “Stop being messy.”","zh":"父母可能把要求措辭為「請把鞋放在門邊」，而不是「別再那麼亂」。"},{"en":"Careful wording can reduce defensiveness and increase cooperation.","zh":"小心措辭可以減少防衛心並增加合作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how a request is expressed.","zh":"這個短語集中於要求如何被表達。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"move on to","meaning":"繼續進行","examples":[{"en":"The child can move on to the preferred activity after finishing the task.","zh":"孩子完成任務後，可以繼續進行喜愛的活動。"},{"en":"To move on to something means to continue to the next activity or stage.","zh":"move on to something 指繼續進入下一個活動或階段。"},{"en":"After completing reading practice, students can move on to a vocabulary game.","zh":"完成閱讀練習後，學生可以繼續進行詞彙遊戲。"},{"en":"Moving on feels smoother when the order of activities is clear.","zh":"當活動次序清楚，過渡會更順暢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transition from one task to another.","zh":"這個短語描述從一項任務轉到另一項任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as soon as","meaning":"一……便……","examples":[{"en":"As soon as the child finishes cleaning, the game can begin.","zh":"孩子一完成清潔，遊戲便可以開始。"},{"en":"As soon as means immediately after something happens.","zh":"as soon as 指某事發生後立即。"},{"en":"As soon as students finish the quiz, they may check their answers.","zh":"學生一完成小測，便可以核對答案。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the timing clear and can motivate children to finish.","zh":"這個短語令時間清楚，並可以推動兒童完成任務。"},{"en":"It links one action directly to the next.","zh":"它把一個行動直接連接到下一個行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"praise is the best way to","meaning":"讚賞是……的最佳方法","examples":[{"en":"Paul Edith insisted that praise is the best way to encourage compliance.","zh":"Paul Edith 堅持認為讚賞是鼓勵服從的最佳方法。"},{"en":"Praise is the best way to do something means praise is considered the most effective method for that purpose.","zh":"praise is the best way to do something 指讚賞被視為達成某目的最有效的方法。"},{"en":"Some teachers believe praise is the best way to encourage shy students to speak.","zh":"有些老師相信讚賞是鼓勵害羞學生說話的最佳方法。"},{"en":"Praise can work because children often repeat behaviour that receives warm attention.","zh":"讚賞可以有效，因為兒童常重複得到溫暖關注的行為。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly recommends praise as a method.","zh":"這個短語強烈建議把讚賞作為方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"encourage someone to comply","meaning":"鼓勵某人服從","examples":[{"en":"Praise can encourage children to comply with requests.","zh":"讚賞可以鼓勵兒童遵從要求。"},{"en":"To encourage someone to comply means to make them more willing to follow a request or rule.","zh":"encourage someone to comply 指令某人更願意遵從要求或規則。"},{"en":"A teacher may encourage students to comply by thanking them for lining up quietly.","zh":"老師可能透過感謝學生安靜排隊來鼓勵他們服從。"},{"en":"Encouragement works better when it makes the child feel capable rather than controlled.","zh":"當鼓勵令孩子感到有能力，而不是被控制，效果更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing willingness to obey.","zh":"這個短語描述增加服從意願。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"familiar advice","meaning":"常見的建議","examples":[{"en":"The suggestion that parents should praise children is familiar advice.","zh":"父母應讚賞兒童這個建議是常見的建議。"},{"en":"Familiar advice is guidance that people have heard many times before.","zh":"familiar advice 指人們已聽過很多次的指引。"},{"en":"“Sleep early before an exam” is familiar advice for students.","zh":"「考試前早點睡」是給學生的常見建議。"},{"en":"Familiar advice may still be useful if people apply it properly.","zh":"如果人們正確應用，常見建議仍可能有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes advice that is common rather than new.","zh":"這個短語描述常見而非新穎的建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"praise a child’s behaviour","meaning":"讚賞兒童的行為","examples":[{"en":"Parents should praise a child’s appropriate behaviour.","zh":"父母應讚賞兒童合適的行為。"},{"en":"To praise a child’s behaviour means to give positive attention to what the child did well.","zh":"praise a child’s behaviour 指對孩子做得好的行動給予正面關注。"},{"en":"A parent may praise a child’s behaviour by saying, “Thank you for sharing your toys.”","zh":"父母可能說「謝謝你分享玩具」來讚賞孩子的行為。"},{"en":"Praising behaviour helps children know exactly what to repeat.","zh":"讚賞行為幫助孩子清楚知道要重複甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the action, not just the child’s personality.","zh":"這個短語集中於行動，而不只是孩子的性格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be more likely to repeat","meaning":"較可能重複","examples":[{"en":"A praised child is more likely to repeat the behaviour.","zh":"受到讚賞的孩子較可能重複該行為。"},{"en":"To be more likely to repeat something means to have a greater chance of doing it again.","zh":"be more likely to repeat something 指更有機會再次做某事。"},{"en":"A student who is praised for neat notes may be more likely to keep writing carefully.","zh":"因筆記整齊而受讚賞的學生，可能較會繼續仔細書寫。"},{"en":"Positive attention can make a behaviour feel rewarding.","zh":"正面關注可以令某行為感覺有回報。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how reinforcement affects future behaviour.","zh":"這個短語解釋強化如何影響未來行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be essential when","meaning":"在……時不可或缺","examples":[{"en":"Praise is essential when working with defiant children.","zh":"與反叛兒童相處時，讚賞不可或缺。"},{"en":"To be essential when doing something means to be necessary in that situation.","zh":"be essential when doing something 指在某情況下是必要的。"},{"en":"Patience is essential when teaching a young child to read.","zh":"教年幼孩子閱讀時，耐心不可或缺。"},{"en":"Something is essential when progress is difficult without it.","zh":"當沒有某事就難以進展，它就是不可或缺的。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a necessary condition.","zh":"這個短語突出必要條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"positive attention","meaning":"正面關注","examples":[{"en":"Praise gives a child positive attention.","zh":"讚賞給孩子正面關注。"},{"en":"Positive attention is warm, approving attention given to good behaviour.","zh":"positive attention 指對良好行為給予溫暖、認同的注意。"},{"en":"A teacher gives positive attention when she smiles and says, “Good listening.”","zh":"老師微笑並說「你很用心聽」，就是給予正面關注。"},{"en":"Children may repeat behaviours that bring positive attention from adults.","zh":"兒童可能重複能帶來成人正面關注的行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attention that encourages rather than criticises.","zh":"這個短語描述鼓勵而非批評的關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be delivered in a way that","meaning":"以能夠……的方式表達","examples":[{"en":"Praise must be delivered in a way that encourages independence.","zh":"讚賞必須以能夠鼓勵獨立的方式表達。"},{"en":"To be delivered in a way that does something means to be expressed so that it has that effect.","zh":"be delivered in a way that does something 指以能產生某效果的方式表達。"},{"en":"Feedback should be delivered in a way that helps students improve rather than feel ashamed.","zh":"回饋應以幫助學生改善而不是感到羞愧的方式表達。"},{"en":"The same message can have different effects depending on how it is delivered.","zh":"同一訊息會因表達方式不同而有不同效果。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on manner and effect.","zh":"這個短語集中於方式和效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"without prompting","meaning":"無需提示","examples":[{"en":"The goal is for the child to repeat the behaviour without prompting.","zh":"目標是讓孩子無需提示也重複該行為。"},{"en":"Without prompting means without being reminded, asked, or guided by someone else.","zh":"without prompting 指沒有別人提醒、要求或引導。"},{"en":"A child brushes her teeth without prompting when she does it before anyone reminds her.","zh":"孩子在沒有人提醒前自己刷牙，就是無需提示。"},{"en":"Behaviour is more independent when it happens without adult reminders.","zh":"當行為在沒有成人提醒下發生，就更具獨立性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes self-initiated action.","zh":"這個短語描述自發行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"考生為每條題目選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option marked by the right letter.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選出以正確字母標示的答案選項。"},{"en":"In reading exams, students should check whether the answer requires a letter or a word.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生應檢查答案要求填字母還是單字。"},{"en":"Copying the wrong letter can lose marks even when the idea is correct.","zh":"即使想法正確，抄錯字母也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in multiple-choice instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於多項選擇題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"receive a good education","meaning":"接受良好教育","examples":[{"en":"Children who receive a good education may still disobey instructions.","zh":"接受良好教育的兒童仍可能不服從指示。"},{"en":"To receive a good education means to get strong teaching, guidance, and learning opportunities.","zh":"receive a good education 指得到良好教學、引導和學習機會。"},{"en":"A child may receive a good education at a school with caring teachers and useful resources.","zh":"孩子可能在有關愛老師和有用資源的學校接受良好教育。"},{"en":"Education can shape behaviour, but it does not guarantee perfect obedience.","zh":"教育可以塑造行為，但不保證完全服從。"},{"en":"This phrase describes educational quality, not automatic character formation.","zh":"這個短語描述教育質素，而不是自動形成品格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"disobey parents’ instructions","meaning":"不服從父母的指示","examples":[{"en":"Some children occasionally disobey their parents’ instructions.","zh":"有些兒童偶爾不服從父母的指示。"},{"en":"To disobey parents’ instructions means to refuse or fail to do what parents tell them.","zh":"disobey parents’ instructions 指拒絕或未能做到父母要求的事。"},{"en":"A child disobeys instructions when he keeps playing after being told to stop.","zh":"孩子被叫停後仍繼續玩，就是不服從指示。"},{"en":"Disobedience may happen because children are tired, upset, or testing limits.","zh":"不服從可能因孩子疲倦、不安或試探界限而發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes not following parental direction.","zh":"這個短語描述不遵從父母指導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"when dealing with","meaning":"在處理……時","examples":[{"en":"Parents need to be observant when dealing with compliance and noncompliance.","zh":"父母在處理服從與不服從時需要善於觀察。"},{"en":"When dealing with something means when handling or responding to that issue.","zh":"when dealing with something 指在處理或回應該問題時。"},{"en":"Teachers need patience when dealing with nervous students.","zh":"老師在處理緊張學生時需要耐性。"},{"en":"The approach adults use can affect whether a problem gets better or worse.","zh":"成人使用的方法可以影響問題變好或變壞。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the situation in which a skill is needed.","zh":"這個短語引出需要某種技能的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"recognise compliant behaviour","meaning":"辨認服從行為","examples":[{"en":"Parents should be able to recognise compliant behaviour.","zh":"父母應能夠辨認服從行為。"},{"en":"To recognise compliant behaviour means to notice when a child is following instructions appropriately.","zh":"recognise compliant behaviour 指注意到孩子正在適當地遵從指示。"},{"en":"A parent recognises compliance when a child quietly begins homework after being asked once.","zh":"孩子被要求一次後安靜開始做功課，父母就辨認到服從行為。"},{"en":"Recognising good behaviour helps adults praise it before problems appear.","zh":"辨認良好行為幫助成人在問題出現前讚賞它。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on noticing obedience clearly.","zh":"這個短語集中於清楚注意到服從。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ask teachers for help","meaning":"向老師求助","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that parents should ask teachers for help.","zh":"該選項暗示父母應向老師求助。"},{"en":"To ask teachers for help means to seek advice or support from teachers.","zh":"ask teachers for help 指向老師尋求建議或支援。"},{"en":"Parents may ask teachers for help if a child refuses homework every night.","zh":"如果孩子每晚拒絕做功課，父母可能向老師求助。"},{"en":"Teachers can share what works in class and what behaviour they have observed.","zh":"老師可以分享課堂中有效的方法和自己觀察到的行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes turning to school staff for guidance.","zh":"這個短語描述向學校人員尋求指導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"pretend not to notice","meaning":"假裝沒有注意到","examples":[{"en":"Some parents may pretend not to notice difficult behaviour.","zh":"有些父母可能假裝沒有注意到困難行為。"},{"en":"To pretend not to notice means to act as if one has not seen something.","zh":"pretend not to notice 指表現得好像沒有看見某事。"},{"en":"A parent may pretend not to notice a minor complaint to avoid a bigger argument.","zh":"父母可能假裝沒有注意到輕微抱怨，以避免更大爭吵。"},{"en":"Ignoring behaviour deliberately can sometimes calm a situation, but it can also allow problems to continue.","zh":"有意忽視行為有時能令情況冷靜，但也可能讓問題持續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intentional non-response.","zh":"這個短語描述有意不回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據","examples":[{"en":"According to Henry Porter, noncompliance may have developmental benefits.","zh":"根據 Henry Porter，不服從可能有發展上的好處。"},{"en":"According to someone means based on what that person says or writes.","zh":"according to someone 指根據某人所說或所寫。"},{"en":"According to the teacher, students should revise vocabulary every day.","zh":"根據老師所說，學生應每天溫習詞彙。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the source of an idea.","zh":"這個短語指出某想法的來源。"},{"en":"It is useful when reporting another person’s view.","zh":"報告他人觀點時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be entirely harmful","meaning":"完全有害","examples":[{"en":"Noncompliance is not necessarily entirely harmful.","zh":"不服從不一定完全有害。"},{"en":"To be entirely harmful means to be completely damaging with no positive side.","zh":"be entirely harmful 指完全造成損害，沒有正面一面。"},{"en":"A child’s disagreement is not entirely harmful if it teaches respectful negotiation.","zh":"如果孩子的不同意教會尊重地協商，就不完全有害。"},{"en":"Some behaviours can have both risks and developmental value.","zh":"有些行為可以同時有風險和發展價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when rejecting an overly negative judgement.","zh":"否定過分負面的判斷時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"have positive effects","meaning":"產生正面影響","examples":[{"en":"Learning to negotiate may have positive effects on a child’s development.","zh":"學習協商可能對兒童發展產生正面影響。"},{"en":"To have positive effects means to produce helpful or beneficial results.","zh":"have positive effects 指產生有幫助或有益的結果。"},{"en":"Regular reading can have positive effects on vocabulary and concentration.","zh":"定期閱讀可以對詞彙和專注力產生正面影響。"},{"en":"Positive effects may appear slowly through repeated practice.","zh":"正面影響可能透過反覆練習慢慢出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes good consequences.","zh":"這個短語描述好的後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"require medical assistance","meaning":"需要醫療協助","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not suggest that ordinary noncompliance requires medical assistance.","zh":"文章沒有暗示普通不服從需要醫療協助。"},{"en":"To require medical assistance means to need help from a doctor or health professional.","zh":"require medical assistance 指需要醫生或醫療專業人士幫助。"},{"en":"A child with a serious injury requires medical assistance immediately.","zh":"嚴重受傷的孩子需要立即醫療協助。"},{"en":"Ordinary disagreement is different from a medical problem.","zh":"普通不同意與醫療問題不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a need for professional healthcare support.","zh":"這個短語描述需要專業醫療支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be treated by a specialist","meaning":"由專家處理","examples":[{"en":"Serious behavioural difficulties may sometimes be treated by a specialist.","zh":"嚴重行為困難有時可能由專家處理。"},{"en":"To be treated by a specialist means to receive help from a professional with expert training.","zh":"be treated by a specialist 指接受受過專門訓練的專業人士幫助。"},{"en":"A child with severe speech delay may be treated by a speech therapist.","zh":"有嚴重語言遲緩的孩子可能由言語治療師處理。"},{"en":"Specialist treatment is usually needed when ordinary support is not enough.","zh":"當普通支援不足時，通常需要專家治療。"},{"en":"This phrase describes professional intervention.","zh":"這個短語描述專業介入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"when children are growing up","meaning":"當兒童逐漸長大時","examples":[{"en":"Children adopt different communication strategies when they are growing up.","zh":"當兒童逐漸長大時，他們會採用不同溝通策略。"},{"en":"When children are growing up means during the period when they are developing physically, emotionally, and socially.","zh":"when children are growing up 指在兒童身體、情感和社交上發展的時期。"},{"en":"When children are growing up, they gradually learn how to explain feelings more clearly.","zh":"當兒童逐漸長大時，他們慢慢學會更清楚解釋感受。"},{"en":"Growing up changes how children talk to parents, teachers, and friends.","zh":"成長會改變兒童與父母、老師和朋友說話的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the developmental period of childhood.","zh":"這個短語描述童年的發展時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"become skilful at negotiating","meaning":"變得善於協商","examples":[{"en":"Older children often become skilful at negotiating with adults.","zh":"年長兒童通常變得善於與成人協商。"},{"en":"To become skilful at negotiating means to get better at discussing and reaching agreement.","zh":"become skilful at negotiating 指變得更善於討論和達成協議。"},{"en":"A child becomes skilful at negotiating when she suggests finishing homework after dinner and explains why.","zh":"孩子提出晚飯後完成功課並解釋原因，就是變得善於協商。"},{"en":"Negotiation skills improve as children learn language, reasons, and compromise.","zh":"隨着兒童學會語言、理由和折衷，協商技巧會改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social and communication development.","zh":"這個短語描述社交和溝通發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"deceive rather than disobey","meaning":"欺騙而不是違抗","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that children learn to deceive rather than disobey.","zh":"該選項暗示兒童學會欺騙而不是違抗。"},{"en":"Deceive rather than disobey means tricking someone instead of openly refusing.","zh":"deceive rather than disobey 指欺騙某人，而不是公開拒絕。"},{"en":"A child may deceive rather than disobey by pretending homework is finished.","zh":"孩子可能假裝功課已完成，這就是欺騙而不是違抗。"},{"en":"Deception can hide conflict, while direct disobedience shows it openly.","zh":"欺騙可以隱藏衝突，而直接違抗則公開顯示衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts lying with open refusal.","zh":"這個短語把說謊與公開拒絕作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"tend to keep silent","meaning":"傾向保持沉默","examples":[{"en":"Some children may tend to keep silent rather than argue.","zh":"有些兒童可能傾向保持沉默，而不是爭辯。"},{"en":"To tend to keep silent means to usually avoid speaking in a situation.","zh":"tend to keep silent 指在某情況中通常避免說話。"},{"en":"A shy student may tend to keep silent when asked to explain a mistake.","zh":"害羞學生被要求解釋錯誤時，可能傾向保持沉默。"},{"en":"Silence may hide disagreement rather than show true agreement.","zh":"沉默可能隱藏不同意，而不是表示真正同意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common habit of not speaking.","zh":"這個短語描述不說話的常見習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"response to parental instructions","meaning":"對父母指示的反應","examples":[{"en":"Children’s responses to parental instructions can change with age.","zh":"兒童對父母指示的反應可以隨年齡改變。"},{"en":"A response to parental instructions is the way a child reacts when a parent gives directions.","zh":"response to parental instructions 指孩子在父母給出指示後的反應方式。"},{"en":"A child may respond by obeying, refusing, asking questions, or negotiating.","zh":"孩子可能透過服從、拒絕、提問或協商作出反應。"},{"en":"Age affects responses because children’s language and self-control develop over time.","zh":"年齡影響反應，因為兒童語言和自制力會隨時間發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes behaviour after parents give instructions.","zh":"這個短語描述父母給指示後的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be associated with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Direct refusal is more closely associated with younger children.","zh":"直接拒絕與較年幼兒童關係更密切。"},{"en":"To be associated with something means to be linked or connected with it.","zh":"be associated with something 指與某事相連或有關。"},{"en":"Regular reading is often associated with stronger vocabulary.","zh":"定期閱讀常與較強詞彙量有關。"},{"en":"Association does not always prove cause, but it shows a relationship.","zh":"相關不一定證明因果，但顯示有關係。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research findings.","zh":"這個短語常見於研究結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"prefer to refuse directly","meaning":"較喜歡直接拒絕","examples":[{"en":"Younger children may prefer to refuse directly.","zh":"年幼兒童可能較喜歡直接拒絕。"},{"en":"To prefer to refuse directly means to choose open refusal instead of indirect resistance.","zh":"prefer to refuse directly 指選擇公開拒絕，而不是間接抗拒。"},{"en":"A toddler may prefer to refuse directly by saying “No!” loudly.","zh":"幼兒可能大聲說「不！」來直接拒絕。"},{"en":"Direct refusal may happen when children lack the words to negotiate.","zh":"當兒童缺乏協商用語時，可能會直接拒絕。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple and open form of noncompliance.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單而公開的不服從形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"refuse to answer","meaning":"拒絕回答","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that older children refuse to answer.","zh":"該選項暗示年長兒童拒絕回答。"},{"en":"To refuse to answer means to choose not to reply to a question or request.","zh":"refuse to answer 指選擇不回應問題或要求。"},{"en":"A child may refuse to answer when angry or embarrassed.","zh":"孩子憤怒或尷尬時，可能拒絕回答。"},{"en":"Refusing to answer can make adults unsure whether the child disagrees or feels upset.","zh":"拒絕回答會令成人不確定孩子是不同意還是不安。"},{"en":"This phrase describes silence as a form of resistance.","zh":"這個短語描述以沉默作為抗拒形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"remain silent","meaning":"保持沉默","examples":[{"en":"Some children may remain silent when they disagree.","zh":"有些兒童不同意時可能保持沉默。"},{"en":"To remain silent means to continue not speaking.","zh":"remain silent 指繼續不說話。"},{"en":"A student may remain silent in a meeting even if he dislikes the plan.","zh":"學生即使不喜歡計劃，也可能在會議中保持沉默。"},{"en":"Silence can hide disagreement, fear, or confusion.","zh":"沉默可以隱藏不同意、恐懼或困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continued quietness rather than active speech.","zh":"這個短語描述持續安靜，而不是主動說話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"list of statements","meaning":"陳述列表","examples":[{"en":"The task provides a list of statements about four researchers.","zh":"該任務提供關於四位研究者的陳述列表。"},{"en":"A list of statements is a set of sentences that students must match, judge, or analyse.","zh":"list of statements 指一組需要學生配對、判斷或分析的句子。"},{"en":"In reading tests, a list of statements may summarise different people’s opinions.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，陳述列表可能概述不同人的意見。"},{"en":"Students should read each statement carefully before matching it with evidence.","zh":"學生在把每項陳述與證據配對前，應仔細閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"match each person with","meaning":"將每個人物與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match each person with the correct statement.","zh":"學生將每個人物與正確陳述配對。"},{"en":"To match each person with something means to connect every person to the right option.","zh":"match each person with something 指把每個人物連接到正確選項。"},{"en":"In a reading task, students may match each researcher with a finding.","zh":"在閱讀題中，學生可能把每位研究者與某個發現配對。"},{"en":"Matching requires evidence from the text, not memory or guessing.","zh":"配對需要文本證據，而不是記憶或猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common exam task.","zh":"這個短語描述常見考試任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"of all ages","meaning":"所有年齡的","examples":[{"en":"The statement refers to children of all ages.","zh":"該陳述指所有年齡的兒童。"},{"en":"Of all ages means including every age group.","zh":"of all ages 指包括每個年齡組。"},{"en":"A library programme may welcome children of all ages.","zh":"圖書館活動可能歡迎所有年齡的兒童。"},{"en":"If a claim applies to children of all ages, it should fit toddlers and teenagers alike.","zh":"如果一個說法適用於所有年齡的兒童，它應同時適合幼兒和青少年。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broad age range.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛年齡範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"express noncompliance indirectly","meaning":"間接表達不服從","examples":[{"en":"Older children may express noncompliance indirectly through negotiation.","zh":"年長兒童可能透過協商間接表達不服從。"},{"en":"To express noncompliance indirectly means to resist without openly saying “no.”","zh":"express noncompliance indirectly 指不公開說「不」而抗拒。"},{"en":"A child may ask for extra time instead of refusing a task directly.","zh":"孩子可能要求更多時間，而不是直接拒絕任務。"},{"en":"Indirect resistance can look like bargaining, delay, or questioning.","zh":"間接抗拒可能看起來像討價還價、拖延或提問。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts subtle refusal with open defiance.","zh":"這個短語把含蓄拒絕與公開反抗作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contrary behaviour","meaning":"反抗行為","examples":[{"en":"Contrary behaviour may indicate noncompliance.","zh":"反抗行為可能顯示不服從。"},{"en":"Contrary behaviour is behaviour that goes against what someone has been asked to do.","zh":"contrary behaviour 指與被要求做的事相反的行為。"},{"en":"A child shows contrary behaviour when told to sit down but keeps running.","zh":"孩子被要求坐下卻繼續跑，就是表現出反抗行為。"},{"en":"Such behaviour may show refusal, frustration, or a desire for control.","zh":"這類行為可能顯示拒絕、挫折或想控制情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes behaviour that opposes instructions.","zh":"這個短語描述違背指示的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"arrange enjoyable activities","meaning":"安排令人享受的活動","examples":[{"en":"Parents can arrange enjoyable activities after resisted tasks.","zh":"父母可以在受抗拒的任務後安排令人享受的活動。"},{"en":"To arrange enjoyable activities means to plan pleasant tasks or rewards at suitable times.","zh":"arrange enjoyable activities 指在合適時間安排愉快任務或獎勵。"},{"en":"A parent may arrange a short game after homework is finished.","zh":"父母可能在功課完成後安排一個短遊戲。"},{"en":"Enjoyable activities can make less pleasant duties easier to start.","zh":"令人享受的活動可以令較不愉快的責任更容易開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using scheduling to support cooperation.","zh":"這個短語描述使用時間安排來支持合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"follow frequently resisted activities","meaning":"緊接在經常受抗拒的活動之後","examples":[{"en":"Preferred activities should follow frequently resisted activities.","zh":"喜愛的活動應緊接在經常受抗拒的活動之後。"},{"en":"To follow frequently resisted activities means to happen after tasks children often oppose.","zh":"follow frequently resisted activities 指在兒童常抗拒的任務之後發生。"},{"en":"Playtime may follow a frequently resisted chore like cleaning the desk.","zh":"遊戲時間可能緊接在清理書桌這類常被抗拒的家務後。"},{"en":"This order can motivate children because a pleasant activity comes next.","zh":"這種次序可以推動兒童，因為愉快活動會接着出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a planned sequence for behaviour management.","zh":"這個短語描述行為管理中的計劃次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"use praise to encourage","meaning":"運用讚賞來鼓勵","examples":[{"en":"Paul Edith advised parents to use praise to encourage compliance.","zh":"Paul Edith 建議父母運用讚賞來鼓勵服從。"},{"en":"To use praise to encourage something means to give positive feedback so the behaviour happens again.","zh":"use praise to encourage something 指給予正面回饋，使該行為再次發生。"},{"en":"A teacher may use praise to encourage quiet reading.","zh":"老師可能運用讚賞來鼓勵安靜閱讀。"},{"en":"Praise works best when it names the exact behaviour being encouraged.","zh":"當讚賞指出正在被鼓勵的具體行為時，效果最好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes praise as a behaviour-building tool.","zh":"這個短語描述把讚賞作為建立行為的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"at an early age","meaning":"在年幼時","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to taking children to school at an early age.","zh":"該選項提到在年幼時帶孩子上學。"},{"en":"At an early age means when someone is still young.","zh":"at an early age 指某人仍年幼時。"},{"en":"Children who hear stories at an early age may develop stronger vocabulary.","zh":"在年幼時聽故事的兒童可能發展出較強詞彙量。"},{"en":"Early experiences can shape habits because young children learn quickly.","zh":"早期經驗可以塑造習慣，因為年幼兒童學習得很快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something happening in childhood or early development.","zh":"這個短語描述某事在童年或早期發展中發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"agree with the claims of","meaning":"與……的主張一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether statements agree with the claims of the writer.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與作者的主張一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the claims of someone means to match what that person argues or says.","zh":"agree with the claims of someone 指與某人的論點或說法相符。"},{"en":"In reading exams, a statement agrees with the writer only if the text clearly supports it.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，只有文本清楚支持某陳述，它才與作者一致。"},{"en":"Students should use evidence, not personal opinion, to judge agreement.","zh":"學生應使用證據，而不是個人意見，判斷是否一致。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in Yes, No, Not Given tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於 Yes, No, Not Given 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A “NO” answer means that the statement contradicts the writer’s views.","zh":"“NO” 答案表示該陳述與作者的觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what that person thinks.","zh":"contradict the views of someone 指說出與某人想法相反的內容。"},{"en":"A statement contradicts the writer if the passage clearly says the opposite.","zh":"如果篇章清楚說出相反意思，該陳述就與作者觀點矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be based on text evidence, not assumption.","zh":"矛盾必須基於文本證據，而不是假設。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear conflict with an opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述與某觀點的清楚衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Students choose “NOT GIVEN” if it is impossible to determine the writer’s view.","zh":"如果無法判斷作者觀點，學生選擇 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資料作決定。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions a child’s age, it is impossible to say how old the child is.","zh":"如果篇章從未提到孩子年齡，就無法判斷孩子幾歲。"},{"en":"Students should not guess when the text gives no evidence.","zh":"當文本沒有證據時，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase explains uncertainty caused by missing information.","zh":"這個短語解釋因資料缺失造成的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"manage relationships with peers","meaning":"處理與同輩的關係","examples":[{"en":"Older children may gradually learn to manage relationships with peers.","zh":"年長兒童可能逐漸學會處理與同輩的關係。"},{"en":"To manage relationships with peers means to handle friendships and conflicts with people of a similar age.","zh":"manage relationships with peers 指處理與相近年齡者的友誼和衝突。"},{"en":"A child manages peer relationships when she shares materials and solves arguments calmly.","zh":"孩子分享材料並冷靜解決爭吵時，就是在處理同輩關係。"},{"en":"Negotiation helps children maintain friendships without giving in every time.","zh":"協商幫助兒童維持友情，而不需要每次都讓步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social skills with classmates or friends.","zh":"這個短語描述與同學或朋友相處的社交技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"have never tried to","meaning":"從未嘗試去","examples":[{"en":"The statement claims that experts have never tried to instil compliance.","zh":"該陳述聲稱專家從未嘗試向兒童灌輸服從觀念。"},{"en":"Have never tried to means have not made any attempt to do something.","zh":"have never tried to 指從未作出任何嘗試去做某事。"},{"en":"A student who has never tried to revise with flashcards cannot know whether they help.","zh":"從未嘗試用詞卡溫習的學生，不能知道它們是否有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a strong negative claim about past action.","zh":"這個短語對過去行動作出強烈否定說法。"},{"en":"It is often tested carefully in reading questions because “never” is absolute.","zh":"它常在閱讀題中被仔細測試，因為 “never” 是絕對字眼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"deny the importance of","meaning":"否認……的重要性","examples":[{"en":"Paul Edith did not deny the importance of effective praise.","zh":"Paul Edith 沒有否認有效讚賞的重要性。"},{"en":"To deny the importance of something means to say it is not important.","zh":"deny the importance of something 指說某事不重要。"},{"en":"A teacher may not deny the importance of grammar, even if she values creativity too.","zh":"老師即使也重視創意，也未必否認文法的重要性。"},{"en":"People may disagree about methods without rejecting the value behind them.","zh":"人們可以不同意方法，而不否定背後價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes refusing to accept that something matters.","zh":"這個短語描述拒絕承認某事重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in an encouraging way","meaning":"以鼓勵性的方式","examples":[{"en":"Praise should be delivered in an encouraging way.","zh":"讚賞應以鼓勵性的方式表達。"},{"en":"In an encouraging way means in a manner that gives confidence, hope, or motivation.","zh":"in an encouraging way 指以給人信心、希望或動力的方式。"},{"en":"A teacher gives feedback in an encouraging way when she says what to improve and what was done well.","zh":"老師指出需要改善之處和做得好的地方時，就是以鼓勵性的方式給回饋。"},{"en":"Encouraging language helps children feel capable rather than ashamed.","zh":"鼓勵性語言幫助孩子感到有能力，而不是羞愧。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a positive and supportive manner.","zh":"這個短語描述正面而支持性的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 148 - Compliance Or Noncompliance For Children.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 149":[{"front":"photovoltaics on the rooftop","meaning":"天台光伏發電系統","examples":[{"en":"Photovoltaics on the rooftop can provide clean electricity for a family home.","zh":"天台光伏發電系統可以為家庭住宅提供清潔電力。"},{"en":"Photovoltaics on the rooftop means solar panels installed on a roof to turn sunlight into electricity.","zh":"Photovoltaics on the rooftop 指安裝在屋頂上，把陽光轉化為電力的太陽能板。"},{"en":"A family may install photovoltaics on the rooftop to reduce its monthly electricity bill.","zh":"家庭可能安裝天台光伏發電系統，以減少每月電費。"},{"en":"If the roof receives strong sunlight, photovoltaics on the rooftop can produce useful daytime power.","zh":"如果屋頂接收強烈陽光，天台光伏發電系統可以產生有用的日間電力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rooftop electricity system, not ordinary roof decoration.","zh":"這個片語描述屋頂發電系統，而不是普通屋頂裝飾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a natural choice for","meaning":"……的自然選擇","examples":[{"en":"Solar power may be a natural choice for powering the family home.","zh":"太陽能可能是為家庭住宅供電的自然選擇。"},{"en":"A natural choice for something is an option that seems suitable, obvious, or sensible.","zh":"A natural choice for something 指看起來合適、明顯或合理的選擇。"},{"en":"A library is a natural choice for students who need a quiet place to study.","zh":"對需要安靜地方溫習的學生來說，圖書館是自然選擇。"},{"en":"If a house has a sunny roof, solar panels become a natural choice for reducing electricity bills.","zh":"如果房屋有陽光充足的屋頂，太陽能板就成為減少電費的自然選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the option fits the situation well.","zh":"這個片語暗示該選項十分配合情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"power the family home","meaning":"為家庭住宅供電","examples":[{"en":"Rooftop solar panels can help power the family home.","zh":"天台太陽能板可以幫助為家庭住宅供電。"},{"en":"To power the family home means to provide electricity for household needs.","zh":"To power the family home 指為家庭日常需要提供電力。"},{"en":"A home battery can power the family home during a short power cut.","zh":"家用電池可以在短暫停電期間為家庭住宅供電。"},{"en":"If solar panels produce enough electricity, they can run lights, appliances, and air-conditioning.","zh":"如果太陽能板產生足夠電力，它們可以運行照明、電器和空調。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on supplying energy for daily home life.","zh":"這個片語著重為日常家居生活供應能源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"過去","examples":[{"en":"In the past, homeowners had few choices about their electricity supply.","zh":"過去，業主對自己的電力供應選擇不多。"},{"en":"In the past means in earlier times, before the present situation.","zh":"In the past 指較早時期，在現況之前。"},{"en":"In the past, students had to search paper dictionaries instead of using apps.","zh":"過去，學生要查紙本字典，而不是使用應用程式。"},{"en":"If technology changes, choices that were impossible in the past may become normal today.","zh":"如果科技改變，過去不可能的選擇今天可能變得正常。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts earlier conditions with the present.","zh":"這個片語把以前的情況與現在作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"urban homeowners","meaning":"城市業主","examples":[{"en":"Urban homeowners are increasingly installing solar-energy systems.","zh":"城市業主正越來越多地安裝太陽能系統。"},{"en":"Urban homeowners are people who own homes in towns or cities.","zh":"Urban homeowners 是在城鎮或城市擁有住宅的人。"},{"en":"Urban homeowners may worry about electricity bills because flats and houses use many appliances.","zh":"城市業主可能擔心電費，因為單位和房屋使用很多電器。"},{"en":"If city roofs are used well, urban homeowners can help generate cleaner electricity locally.","zh":"如果城市屋頂被善用，城市業主可以幫助在本地產生更清潔電力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to property owners in city areas, not rural farmers.","zh":"這個片語指城市地區的物業擁有人，而不是鄉郊農民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have little choice in","meaning":"在……方面選擇不多","examples":[{"en":"Homeowners once had little choice in how electricity was supplied.","zh":"業主過去在電力如何供應方面選擇不多。"},{"en":"To have little choice in something means to have very few options or little control over it.","zh":"To have little choice in something 指在某事上選項很少或控制權很少。"},{"en":"Students may have little choice in their timetable if the school sets all lessons.","zh":"如果學校安排所有課堂，學生在時間表方面可能選擇不多。"},{"en":"If a family depends only on the grid, it has little choice in where its electricity comes from.","zh":"如果家庭只依賴電網，它在電力來源方面就選擇不多。"},{"en":"This phrase shows limited freedom to decide.","zh":"這個片語顯示決定自由有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the way electricity is supplied","meaning":"電力供應方式","examples":[{"en":"Consumers can now influence the way electricity is supplied to their homes.","zh":"消費者現在可以影響電力供應到其住宅的方式。"},{"en":"The way electricity is supplied means how power reaches users and where that power comes from.","zh":"The way electricity is supplied 指電力如何到達用戶，以及電力來自哪裡。"},{"en":"A building may change the way electricity is supplied by adding solar panels and batteries.","zh":"大廈可以透過加入太陽能板和電池來改變電力供應方式。"},{"en":"If more homes generate power, the supply system becomes less one-directional.","zh":"如果更多住宅發電，供應系統就不再那麼單向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the method and source of electricity delivery.","zh":"這個片語描述電力輸送的方法和來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be supplied to","meaning":"被供應到……","examples":[{"en":"Electricity is supplied to homes through the grid network.","zh":"電力透過電網被供應到住宅。"},{"en":"To be supplied to someone means to be provided or delivered to them.","zh":"To be supplied to someone 指被提供或輸送給某人。"},{"en":"Clean water is supplied to schools through underground pipes.","zh":"清潔食水透過地下水管被供應到學校。"},{"en":"If electricity is supplied to homes reliably, families can cook, study, and work safely.","zh":"如果電力可靠地供應到住宅，家庭便可以安全煮食、學習和工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes delivery of a resource to users.","zh":"這個片語描述資源被輸送給使用者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a rapidly increasing number of","meaning":"數量迅速增加的……","examples":[{"en":"A rapidly increasing number of households are choosing solar energy.","zh":"數量迅速增加的家庭正在選擇太陽能。"},{"en":"A rapidly increasing number of something means the number is growing quickly.","zh":"A rapidly increasing number of something 指某事物的數量正在快速增長。"},{"en":"A rapidly increasing number of students are using online videos to review lessons.","zh":"數量迅速增加的學生正在使用網上影片複習課堂。"},{"en":"If solar prices fall, a rapidly increasing number of families may install rooftop panels.","zh":"如果太陽能價格下降，數量迅速增加的家庭可能安裝天台太陽能板。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises fast growth in quantity.","zh":"這個片語強調數量快速增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"households worldwide","meaning":"全球家庭","examples":[{"en":"Households worldwide are adopting rooftop solar systems.","zh":"全球家庭正在採用天台太陽能系統。"},{"en":"Households worldwide means families or homes in many countries around the world.","zh":"Households worldwide 指世界許多國家的家庭或住宅。"},{"en":"Households worldwide use electricity for lighting, cooking, cooling, and communication.","zh":"全球家庭使用電力照明、煮食、降溫和通訊。"},{"en":"If energy prices rise, households worldwide may look for cheaper power options.","zh":"如果能源價格上升，全球家庭可能尋找更便宜的電力選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes homes across many regions, not one local community.","zh":"這個片語描述跨越許多地區的家庭，而不是單一本地社區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"choose the solar-energy option","meaning":"選擇太陽能方案","examples":[{"en":"More homeowners are choosing the solar-energy option.","zh":"越來越多業主正在選擇太陽能方案。"},{"en":"To choose the solar-energy option means to select solar power instead of relying only on conventional electricity.","zh":"To choose the solar-energy option 指選擇太陽能，而不是只依賴傳統電力。"},{"en":"A family may choose the solar-energy option after comparing long-term electricity bills.","zh":"家庭比較長期電費後，可能選擇太陽能方案。"},{"en":"If government support lowers installation costs, more people may choose solar.","zh":"如果政府支援降低安裝成本，更多人可能選擇太陽能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decision to use solar power.","zh":"這個片語描述使用太陽能的決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"solar energy","meaning":"太陽能","examples":[{"en":"Solar energy is produced by converting sunlight into electricity.","zh":"太陽能透過把陽光轉化成電力而產生。"},{"en":"Solar energy is energy from the sun that can be used for heat or electricity.","zh":"Solar energy 是來自太陽、可用於供熱或發電的能源。"},{"en":"A school may use solar energy to power lights in a classroom block.","zh":"學校可能使用太陽能為課室大樓照明供電。"},{"en":"If sunlight is strong and frequent, solar energy can reduce dependence on fossil fuels.","zh":"如果陽光強而頻密，太陽能可以減少對化石燃料的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to energy from sunlight, not energy from the moon or wind.","zh":"這個片語指來自陽光的能源，而不是來自月亮或風的能源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the conversion of sunlight into energy","meaning":"把陽光轉化成能源","examples":[{"en":"Photovoltaics enable the conversion of sunlight into usable energy.","zh":"光伏技術使把陽光轉化成可用能源成為可能。"},{"en":"The conversion of sunlight into energy means changing sunlight into electricity or heat that people can use.","zh":"The conversion of sunlight into energy 指把陽光轉變成人們可使用的電力或熱能。"},{"en":"A solar calculator works through the conversion of sunlight into energy.","zh":"太陽能計算機透過把陽光轉化成能源來運作。"},{"en":"If this conversion becomes cheaper, more homes can produce their own power.","zh":"如果這種轉化變得更便宜，更多住宅就能自己發電。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change from natural light into practical energy.","zh":"這個片語描述由自然光轉變成實用能源的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be made possible through","meaning":"透過……得以實現","examples":[{"en":"Solar electricity is made possible through the use of photovoltaic panels.","zh":"太陽能電力透過使用光伏板得以實現。"},{"en":"To be made possible through something means to become achievable because of that thing.","zh":"To be made possible through something 指因某事物而變得可以實現。"},{"en":"Online lessons are made possible through video platforms and stable internet.","zh":"網上課堂透過視像平台和穩定網絡得以實現。"},{"en":"If a new tool reduces cost, a difficult project may become possible.","zh":"如果新工具降低成本，困難項目可能變得可行。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the means that allows something to happen.","zh":"這個片語解釋使某事發生的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the use of photovoltaics","meaning":"光伏技術的使用","examples":[{"en":"The use of photovoltaics has increased in residential areas.","zh":"光伏技術的使用在住宅區有所增加。"},{"en":"The use of photovoltaics means using solar-cell technology to produce electricity from light.","zh":"The use of photovoltaics 指使用太陽能電池技術把光轉化成電力。"},{"en":"A village clinic may benefit from the use of photovoltaics if the grid is unreliable.","zh":"如果電網不可靠，鄉村診所可能受惠於光伏技術的使用。"},{"en":"If more buildings use photovoltaics, less electricity may need to come from fossil fuels.","zh":"如果更多建築物使用光伏技術，較少電力需要來自化石燃料。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on applying solar technology in real settings.","zh":"這個片語著重在實際環境中應用太陽能技術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"photovoltaic panels","meaning":"光伏板；太陽能板","examples":[{"en":"Photovoltaic panels convert sunlight directly into electricity.","zh":"光伏板把陽光直接轉化成電力。"},{"en":"Photovoltaic panels are solar panels made of cells that generate electricity when light hits them.","zh":"Photovoltaic panels 是由太陽能電池組成、受光照時發電的太陽能板。"},{"en":"A school roof may hold photovoltaic panels to power fans and lights.","zh":"學校屋頂可能裝有光伏板，為風扇和照明供電。"},{"en":"If panels are shaded by trees, they may produce less electricity.","zh":"如果光伏板被樹蔭遮擋，它們可能產生較少電力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the physical panels used in solar electricity systems.","zh":"這個片語指太陽能發電系統中使用的實體板。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fit onto the roof","meaning":"安裝在屋頂上","examples":[{"en":"Photovoltaic panels can be fitted onto the roof of a house.","zh":"光伏板可以安裝在房屋屋頂上。"},{"en":"To fit onto the roof means to install or place something securely on the top of a building.","zh":"To fit onto the roof 指把某物穩固地安裝或放置在建築物頂部。"},{"en":"A technician may fit a satellite dish onto the roof if the signal is better there.","zh":"如果屋頂訊號較好，技術員可能把衛星碟安裝在屋頂上。"},{"en":"If panels are fitted correctly, they can stay safe during wind and rain.","zh":"如果太陽能板安裝正確，它們可以在風雨中保持安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical installation on a roof.","zh":"這個片語描述在屋頂上的實體安裝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"photovoltaics-powered home","meaning":"光伏供電住宅","examples":[{"en":"A photovoltaics-powered home remains connected to the electricity grid.","zh":"光伏供電住宅仍然連接到電網。"},{"en":"A photovoltaics-powered home is a house that receives part or all of its electricity from solar panels.","zh":"Photovoltaics-powered home 是部分或全部電力來自太陽能板的住宅。"},{"en":"A family living in a photovoltaics-powered home may use solar electricity during sunny hours.","zh":"住在光伏供電住宅的家庭，可能在陽光充足時使用太陽能電力。"},{"en":"If solar output is low at night, the home may still draw power from the grid.","zh":"如果夜間太陽能輸出低，住宅仍可能從電網取電。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a home supported by solar power, not one cut off from all other electricity.","zh":"這個片語描述由太陽能支援的住宅，而不是完全切斷其他電力來源的住宅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"remain connected to","meaning":"繼續連接到……","examples":[{"en":"The solar-powered home remains connected to the power lines.","zh":"太陽能供電住宅繼續連接到電力線。"},{"en":"To remain connected to something means to continue being linked to it.","zh":"To remain connected to something 指繼續與某物保持連接。"},{"en":"A laptop remains connected to Wi-Fi if the signal is stable.","zh":"如果訊號穩定，手提電腦會繼續連接到 Wi-Fi。"},{"en":"If a solar home remains connected to the grid, it can still receive electricity at night.","zh":"如果太陽能住宅繼續連接到電網，它夜間仍可以取得電力。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the connection continues.","zh":"這個片語強調連接持續存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"power lines","meaning":"電力線","examples":[{"en":"The house can receive electricity through the power lines at night.","zh":"該住宅夜間可以透過電力線接收電力。"},{"en":"Power lines are cables that carry electricity from the grid to buildings.","zh":"Power lines 是把電力從電網輸送到建築物的電纜。"},{"en":"After a storm, broken power lines may cause homes to lose electricity.","zh":"暴風雨後，斷裂的電力線可能令住宅停電。"},{"en":"If a solar home stays connected to power lines, it has a backup supply.","zh":"如果太陽能住宅仍連接電力線，它就有後備供電。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to electricity-carrying cables, not telephone wires.","zh":"這個片語指輸送電力的電纜，而不是電話線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"no storage is required on-site","meaning":"現場毋須設置儲電設備","examples":[{"en":"No battery storage is required on-site in this type of system.","zh":"這類系統現場毋須設置電池儲電設備。"},{"en":"No storage is required on-site means electricity does not need to be stored at the house itself.","zh":"No storage is required on-site 指電力不需要儲存在住宅本身。"},{"en":"A small shop may use the grid as backup, so no large battery is needed on-site.","zh":"小店可能使用電網作後備，因此現場不需要大型電池。"},{"en":"If unused power goes to the grid, the home does not need expensive local storage.","zh":"如果未用電力輸送到電網，住宅就不需要昂貴的本地儲電設備。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why some solar homes do not require batteries.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何一些太陽能住宅不需要電池。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on-site storage","meaning":"現場儲電","examples":[{"en":"The grid removes the need for on-site storage.","zh":"電網消除了現場儲電的需要。"},{"en":"On-site storage means storing energy or materials at the place where they are used.","zh":"On-site storage 指在使用地點儲存能源或物料。"},{"en":"A restaurant may need on-site storage for frozen food and cleaning supplies.","zh":"餐廳可能需要現場儲存冷凍食物和清潔用品。"},{"en":"If a home has no battery, it has little on-site storage for solar electricity.","zh":"如果住宅沒有電池，它就幾乎沒有太陽能電力的現場儲存。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to storage at the actual location, not at a distant facility.","zh":"這個片語指在實際地點儲存，而不是在遠處設施儲存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a box of electronics","meaning":"一組電子設備","examples":[{"en":"The system requires a box of electronics called an inverter.","zh":"該系統需要一組名為逆變器的電子設備。"},{"en":"A box of electronics is a device containing electronic parts that control or convert electricity.","zh":"A box of electronics 是包含電子部件、用來控制或轉換電力的裝置。"},{"en":"A router is a small box of electronics that connects a home to the internet.","zh":"路由器是一組小型電子設備，把住宅連接到互聯網。"},{"en":"If the electronics fail, the solar system may stop sending usable power to the home.","zh":"如果電子設備故障，太陽能系統可能停止向住宅輸送可用電力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a compact technical device, not an ordinary storage box.","zh":"這個片語描述小型技術裝置，而不是普通儲物箱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"inverter","meaning":"逆變器","examples":[{"en":"The inverter connects the photovoltaic system to the electricity grid.","zh":"逆變器把光伏系統連接到電網。"},{"en":"An inverter is a device that changes solar electricity into a form that homes and grids can use.","zh":"Inverter 是把太陽能電力轉換成住宅和電網可用形式的裝置。"},{"en":"A technician may check the inverter if the solar panels are producing power but the house is not using it.","zh":"如果太陽能板正在發電但住宅不能使用，技術員可能檢查逆變器。"},{"en":"If the inverter fails, electricity from the panels may not be usable.","zh":"如果逆變器故障，太陽能板產生的電力可能無法使用。"},{"en":"This word names a key electronic part of a solar-power system.","zh":"這個詞命名太陽能發電系統中的關鍵電子部件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"provide the interface between","meaning":"提供……之間的介面","examples":[{"en":"The inverter provides the interface between the solar panels and the grid.","zh":"逆變器提供太陽能板與電網之間的介面。"},{"en":"To provide the interface between two things means to act as the connection that lets them work together.","zh":"To provide the interface between two things 指作為連接，使兩者能共同運作。"},{"en":"A phone app can provide the interface between a customer and a delivery service.","zh":"手機應用程式可以提供顧客與外賣服務之間的介面。"},{"en":"If the interface is poor, two systems may not communicate properly.","zh":"如果介面差，兩個系統可能不能正常溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a link that allows interaction.","zh":"這個片語描述讓互動得以發生的連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"grid network","meaning":"電網","examples":[{"en":"Excess solar power can be fed into the grid network.","zh":"剩餘太陽能電力可以輸送到電網。"},{"en":"The grid network is the connected system of power lines and stations that delivers electricity.","zh":"Grid network 是由電力線和電站連接而成、輸送電力的系統。"},{"en":"A city depends on the grid network to supply homes, shops, schools, and hospitals.","zh":"城市依靠電網為住宅、商店、學校和醫院供電。"},{"en":"If many homes send power into the grid, the network must manage two-way flows.","zh":"如果許多住宅把電力送入電網，該網絡就必須管理雙向電流。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the wider electricity system.","zh":"這個片語指較廣泛的電力系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"illustrate the system","meaning":"說明該系統","examples":[{"en":"The diagram illustrates how the rooftop photovoltaic system works.","zh":"圖表說明天台光伏發電系統如何運作。"},{"en":"To illustrate the system means to show or explain how the system operates, often with a picture.","zh":"To illustrate the system 指展示或解釋該系統如何運作，常以圖片輔助。"},{"en":"A teacher may draw arrows to illustrate how water moves through a plant.","zh":"老師可能畫箭嘴說明水如何在植物中流動。"},{"en":"If a diagram illustrates a system clearly, students can follow the direction of flow.","zh":"如果圖表清楚說明系統，學生就能跟隨流動方向。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a visual explains a process.","zh":"這個片語用於視覺圖像解釋過程時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"during the day","meaning":"在日間","examples":[{"en":"During the day, the solar panels may produce more electricity than the home needs.","zh":"在日間，太陽能板可能產生多於住宅所需的電力。"},{"en":"During the day means in the hours when there is daylight.","zh":"During the day 指有日光的時段。"},{"en":"Shops often use more lighting and air-conditioning during the day.","zh":"商店在日間通常使用更多照明和空調。"},{"en":"If panels produce power during the day, the electricity can match daytime work and cooling needs.","zh":"如果太陽能板在日間發電，電力可以配合日間工作和降溫需要。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts daylight hours with night-time.","zh":"這個片語把日光時段與夜間作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"excess power","meaning":"剩餘電力","examples":[{"en":"Excess power from the solar array is sent to the grid.","zh":"來自太陽能板陣列的剩餘電力被送到電網。"},{"en":"Excess power is electricity produced beyond what is immediately needed.","zh":"Excess power 是超出即時需要而產生的電力。"},{"en":"A school may have excess power on sunny weekends when classrooms are empty.","zh":"陽光充足的週末課室空置時，學校可能有剩餘電力。"},{"en":"If excess power is not stored or exported, it may be wasted.","zh":"如果剩餘電力沒有被儲存或輸出，它可能被浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes surplus electricity.","zh":"這個片語描述多出的電力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"solar array","meaning":"太陽能板陣列","examples":[{"en":"A solar array consists of several connected photovoltaic panels.","zh":"太陽能板陣列由幾塊連接起來的光伏板組成。"},{"en":"A solar array is a group of solar panels working together as one system.","zh":"Solar array 是一組共同作為一個系統運作的太陽能板。"},{"en":"A factory roof may hold a large solar array to reduce daytime electricity costs.","zh":"工廠屋頂可能設有大型太陽能板陣列，以減少日間電費。"},{"en":"If one panel in the array is shaded, the system’s output may fall.","zh":"如果陣列中一塊板被遮蔭，系統輸出可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a set of panels, not just one panel.","zh":"這個片語指一組太陽能板，而不只是一塊板。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be fed back to the grid","meaning":"被輸送回電網","examples":[{"en":"Unused electricity is fed back to the grid.","zh":"未使用的電力被輸送回電網。"},{"en":"To be fed back to the grid means to be sent from a building into the electricity network.","zh":"To be fed back to the grid 指從建築物送回電力網絡。"},{"en":"A home with solar panels may feed power back to the grid on a sunny afternoon.","zh":"有太陽能板的住宅可能在陽光充足的下午把電力輸送回電網。"},{"en":"If power is fed back to the grid, other users may be able to use it.","zh":"如果電力被輸送回電網，其他用戶可能可以使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reverse flow from the home to the wider network.","zh":"這個片語描述從住宅流向更大網絡的反向流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"daytime power","meaning":"日間用電","examples":[{"en":"Factories and offices often require large amounts of daytime power.","zh":"工廠和辦公室通常需要大量日間用電。"},{"en":"Daytime power is electricity used or produced during the hours of daylight.","zh":"Daytime power 是在日光時段使用或產生的電力。"},{"en":"A school needs daytime power for computers, fans, projectors, and kitchen equipment.","zh":"學校需要日間用電來運行電腦、風扇、投影機和廚房設備。"},{"en":"If solar panels produce daytime power, they may match business electricity use well.","zh":"如果太陽能板產生日間電力，它們可能很配合商業用電。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to electricity demand or supply during the day.","zh":"這個片語指日間的電力需求或供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"flow the opposite way","meaning":"朝相反方向流動","examples":[{"en":"At night, electricity flows the opposite way from the grid to the home.","zh":"夜間，電力從電網流向住宅，朝相反方向流動。"},{"en":"To flow the opposite way means to move in the reverse direction.","zh":"To flow the opposite way 指朝相反方向移動。"},{"en":"Traffic may flow the opposite way in the evening when commuters return home.","zh":"傍晚通勤者回家時，交通可能朝相反方向流動。"},{"en":"If solar power flows to the grid by day, grid power may flow back to the home at night.","zh":"如果太陽能電力日間流向電網，夜間電網電力可能流回住宅。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reversal in direction.","zh":"這個片語描述方向的逆轉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"effectively provide storage","meaning":"實際上提供儲電功能","examples":[{"en":"The grid network effectively provides storage for unused solar power.","zh":"電網實際上為未使用的太陽能電力提供儲電功能。"},{"en":"To effectively provide storage means to serve the same practical purpose as storage, even if no battery is used.","zh":"To effectively provide storage 指即使沒有使用電池，也發揮與儲存相同的實際作用。"},{"en":"A library effectively provides storage for books that families cannot keep at home.","zh":"圖書館實際上為家庭不能存放在家中的書提供儲存功能。"},{"en":"If extra solar power is exported and later balanced by grid electricity, the grid works like storage.","zh":"如果額外太陽能被輸出，之後再由電網電力平衡，電網就像儲電一樣運作。"},{"en":"This phrase means something performs the function of storage in practice.","zh":"這個片語意思是某物在實際上發揮儲存功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"demand for electricity","meaning":"電力需求","examples":[{"en":"Solar energy is especially useful when demand for electricity peaks during daylight hours.","zh":"當電力需求在日光時段達到高峰時，太陽能特別有用。"},{"en":"Demand for electricity means how much electricity people need or use.","zh":"Demand for electricity 指人們需要或使用多少電力。"},{"en":"Demand for electricity rises when many households turn on air-conditioners in hot weather.","zh":"炎熱天氣中，許多家庭開空調時，電力需求會上升。"},{"en":"If demand is high during sunny hours, solar power can help meet it directly.","zh":"如果需求在陽光充足時段很高，太陽能可以直接幫助滿足需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the level of electricity need.","zh":"這個片語描述電力需要的水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be well matched to","meaning":"與……十分配合","examples":[{"en":"Electricity demand is well matched to the hours when the sun shines.","zh":"電力需求與有陽光的時段十分配合。"},{"en":"To be well matched to something means to fit it closely or work well with it.","zh":"To be well matched to something 指與某事十分吻合或配合良好。"},{"en":"A quiet library is well matched to students who need focused revision.","zh":"安靜圖書館與需要專心溫習的學生十分配合。"},{"en":"If solar output matches daytime demand, less energy may be wasted.","zh":"如果太陽能輸出配合日間需求，較少能源可能被浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a good fit between two things.","zh":"這個片語描述兩件事之間的良好配合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"when the sun shines","meaning":"有陽光時","examples":[{"en":"Solar panels generate electricity when the sun shines.","zh":"有陽光時，太陽能板會發電。"},{"en":"When the sun shines means during periods with direct or useful sunlight.","zh":"When the sun shines 指有直接或有用陽光的時段。"},{"en":"Children often prefer outdoor games when the sun shines after several rainy days.","zh":"連續多天落雨後，有陽光時孩子通常更喜歡戶外遊戲。"},{"en":"If a place has long sunny days, solar panels can produce more electricity.","zh":"如果一個地方日照時間長，太陽能板可以產生更多電力。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the condition needed for solar generation.","zh":"這個片語標示太陽能發電所需的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be especially valuable","meaning":"特別有價值","examples":[{"en":"Solar power is especially valuable where daytime demand is high.","zh":"在日間需求高的地方，太陽能特別有價值。"},{"en":"To be especially valuable means to be particularly useful or important in a certain situation.","zh":"To be especially valuable 指在某情況中特別有用或重要。"},{"en":"A quiet study room is especially valuable during exam season.","zh":"在考試季，安靜自修室特別有價值。"},{"en":"If electricity demand peaks on hot sunny afternoons, solar power becomes especially valuable.","zh":"如果電力需求在炎熱晴朗下午達到高峰，太陽能就變得特別有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights unusually high usefulness.","zh":"這個片語突顯異常高的用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"air-conditioning loads","meaning":"空調用電負荷","examples":[{"en":"Air-conditioning loads are high in offices during hot weather.","zh":"炎熱天氣中，辦公室的空調用電負荷很高。"},{"en":"Air-conditioning loads are the amount of electricity needed to run cooling systems.","zh":"Air-conditioning loads 是運行冷氣系統所需的電力量。"},{"en":"A shopping mall has heavy air-conditioning loads on a humid summer afternoon.","zh":"在潮濕夏日下午，商場有很高空調用電負荷。"},{"en":"If cooling demand rises, electricity use and costs may increase sharply.","zh":"如果冷卻需求上升，用電量和成本可能急劇增加。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to energy demand created by air-conditioning.","zh":"這個片語指由空調造成的能源需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"offices and factories","meaning":"辦公室及工廠","examples":[{"en":"Offices and factories often consume more electricity during the day.","zh":"辦公室及工廠通常在日間消耗更多電力。"},{"en":"Offices and factories are workplaces where people do administrative, commercial, or industrial work.","zh":"Offices and factories 是人們從事行政、商業或工業工作的工作場所。"},{"en":"Offices use computers and lighting, while factories may run machines and cooling systems.","zh":"辦公室使用電腦和照明，而工廠可能運行機器和冷卻系統。"},{"en":"If offices and factories use solar power during work hours, they may reduce daytime grid demand.","zh":"如果辦公室及工廠在工作時間使用太陽能，它們可能減少日間電網需求。"},{"en":"This phrase groups major daytime electricity users.","zh":"這個片語把主要日間用電者歸為一類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"heating loads","meaning":"暖氣用電負荷","examples":[{"en":"Heating loads for homes are relatively small in some warm regions.","zh":"在一些溫暖地區，住宅的暖氣用電負荷相對較小。"},{"en":"Heating loads are the amount of energy needed to warm buildings.","zh":"Heating loads 是為建築物供暖所需的能源量。"},{"en":"A flat in a cold city may have high heating loads in winter.","zh":"寒冷城市中的單位在冬天可能有很高暖氣用電負荷。"},{"en":"If heating loads are low, homes may need less electricity or gas for warmth.","zh":"如果暖氣負荷低，住宅可能較少需要電力或燃氣取暖。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to energy demand created by heating.","zh":"這個片語指由供暖造成的能源需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the first systematic exploration of","meaning":"對……的首次系統性研究","examples":[{"en":"The first systematic exploration of residential photovoltaics began in the United States.","zh":"對住宅光伏發電系統的首次系統性研究始於美國。"},{"en":"The first systematic exploration of something means the first organised and careful study of it.","zh":"The first systematic exploration of something 指對某事進行的首次有組織、仔細研究。"},{"en":"A school may begin the first systematic exploration of why students arrive late.","zh":"學校可能開始首次系統性研究學生遲到的原因。"},{"en":"If a new technology is explored systematically, researchers can compare results fairly.","zh":"如果新科技被有系統地研究，研究人員可以公平比較結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes structured research rather than casual trial.","zh":"這個片語描述有結構的研究，而不是隨意試驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"residential photovoltaics","meaning":"住宅光伏發電系統","examples":[{"en":"Researchers studied the performance of residential photovoltaics in different climates.","zh":"研究人員研究住宅光伏發電系統在不同氣候中的表現。"},{"en":"Residential photovoltaics are solar-electric systems installed on or near homes.","zh":"Residential photovoltaics 是安裝在住宅上或住宅附近的太陽能發電系統。"},{"en":"A housing estate may use residential photovoltaics to lower electricity costs for residents.","zh":"屋苑可能使用住宅光伏發電系統，以降低居民電費。"},{"en":"If residential photovoltaics spread widely, household electricity can become cleaner.","zh":"如果住宅光伏發電系統廣泛普及，家庭用電可以變得更清潔。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to solar power for homes, not large solar farms.","zh":"這個片語指住宅用太陽能，而不是大型太陽能農場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"during the 1970s","meaning":"在二十世紀七十年代","examples":[{"en":"The American research programme began during the 1970s.","zh":"美國研究計劃在二十世紀七十年代開始。"},{"en":"During the 1970s means in the years from 1970 to 1979.","zh":"During the 1970s 指1970年至1979年間。"},{"en":"Many schools changed their teaching materials during the 1970s.","zh":"許多學校在二十世紀七十年代改變教材。"},{"en":"If a project began during the 1970s, it started before today’s cheaper solar technology existed.","zh":"如果項目在二十世紀七十年代開始，它早於今天較便宜的太陽能技術。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a decade as a time period.","zh":"這個片語以十年為時間範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a well-conceived programme","meaning":"構思周詳的計劃","examples":[{"en":"A well-conceived programme tested different residential solar designs.","zh":"一個構思周詳的計劃測試了不同住宅太陽能設計。"},{"en":"A well-conceived programme is a carefully planned project with clear aims and methods.","zh":"A well-conceived programme 是有清晰目標和方法、經仔細規劃的項目。"},{"en":"A well-conceived school reading programme gives students books, time, and feedback.","zh":"構思周詳的學校閱讀計劃會給學生書籍、時間和回饋。"},{"en":"If a programme is well conceived, it is more likely to produce useful results.","zh":"如果計劃構思周詳，它更可能產生有用結果。"},{"en":"This phrase praises the planning behind a project.","zh":"這個片語稱讚項目背後的規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the siting of","meaning":"……的選址","examples":[{"en":"The programme began with the siting of experimental stations across the country.","zh":"該計劃由全國各地實驗站的選址開始。"},{"en":"The siting of something means choosing where it should be located.","zh":"The siting of something 指選擇某物應位於哪裡。"},{"en":"The siting of a new school must consider transport, safety, and nearby families.","zh":"新學校的選址必須考慮交通、安全和附近家庭。"},{"en":"If test stations are sited in different climates, researchers can compare performance fairly.","zh":"如果測試站設於不同氣候區，研究人員可以公平比較表現。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on location decisions.","zh":"這個片語著重位置決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"residential experimental stations","meaning":"住宅實驗站","examples":[{"en":"Residential experimental stations were built in several climatic zones.","zh":"住宅實驗站建於幾個氣候區。"},{"en":"Residential experimental stations are test sites designed to study home-based systems.","zh":"Residential experimental stations 是用來研究家居系統的測試場地。"},{"en":"A university may build an experimental house to test energy-saving walls and windows.","zh":"大學可能建造一間實驗房屋，測試節能牆壁和窗戶。"},{"en":"If stations copy real homes, results can be more useful for future housing.","zh":"如果實驗站模仿真實住宅，結果對未來房屋會更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research sites that imitate or study homes.","zh":"這個片語描述模擬或研究住宅的研究場地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"selected locations","meaning":"選定地點","examples":[{"en":"The stations were placed at selected locations around the country.","zh":"這些實驗站設於全國各地的選定地點。"},{"en":"Selected locations are places chosen for a particular purpose.","zh":"Selected locations 是為特定目的而選出的地方。"},{"en":"A school trip may stop at selected locations that show local history clearly.","zh":"學校旅行可能在能清楚展示本地歷史的選定地點停留。"},{"en":"If researchers choose selected locations carefully, the test results become more meaningful.","zh":"如果研究人員仔細選擇地點，測試結果會更有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase means the places were chosen deliberately, not randomly.","zh":"這個片語意思是地點被刻意選出，而不是隨機挑選。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"represent different climatic zones","meaning":"代表不同氣候區","examples":[{"en":"The experimental sites represented different climatic zones.","zh":"這些實驗場地代表不同氣候區。"},{"en":"To represent different climatic zones means to include places with different weather patterns.","zh":"To represent different climatic zones 指包括有不同天氣模式的地方。"},{"en":"A national farming study may choose farms that represent dry, wet, hot, and cool regions.","zh":"全國農業研究可能選擇代表乾燥、潮濕、炎熱和涼爽地區的農場。"},{"en":"If test sites represent different climates, researchers can see where a system works best.","zh":"如果測試場地代表不同氣候，研究人員可以看見系統在哪裡最有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using varied locations to reflect wider conditions.","zh":"這個片語描述使用多樣地點來反映更廣泛條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"climatic zones","meaning":"氣候區","examples":[{"en":"Solar systems were tested in a range of climatic zones.","zh":"太陽能系統在一系列氣候區中接受測試。"},{"en":"Climatic zones are areas grouped by similar weather, temperature, rainfall, and sunlight patterns.","zh":"Climatic zones 是按相似天氣、溫度、降雨和日照模式分組的地區。"},{"en":"A country may have coastal, desert, mountain, and tropical climatic zones.","zh":"一個國家可能有沿海、沙漠、山區和熱帶氣候區。"},{"en":"If solar panels are tested in several climatic zones, their performance can be compared more accurately.","zh":"如果太陽能板在幾個氣候區測試，其表現可以更準確比較。"},{"en":"This phrase classifies regions by climate.","zh":"這個片語按氣候分類地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dummy houses","meaning":"模擬房屋","examples":[{"en":"The experimental stations contained several dummy houses.","zh":"實驗站包含幾間模擬房屋。"},{"en":"Dummy houses are artificial or test houses built to simulate real homes.","zh":"Dummy houses 是為模擬真實住宅而建的人造或測試房屋。"},{"en":"Engineers may use dummy houses to test insulation before building real housing estates.","zh":"工程師可能使用模擬房屋來測試隔熱，然後才建造真實屋苑。"},{"en":"If dummy houses imitate family homes, researchers can test systems safely and repeatedly.","zh":"如果模擬房屋仿照家庭住宅，研究人員可以安全而反覆地測試系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes experimental houses, not homes with real families.","zh":"這個片語描述實驗房屋，而不是有真實家庭居住的住宅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"solar-energy system design","meaning":"太陽能系統設計","examples":[{"en":"Each dummy house used a different solar-energy system design.","zh":"每間模擬房屋使用不同的太陽能系統設計。"},{"en":"Solar-energy system design means the planned arrangement of panels, wiring, controls, and related equipment.","zh":"Solar-energy system design 指太陽能板、電線、控制裝置和相關設備的規劃安排。"},{"en":"A school may compare two system designs before choosing one for its roof.","zh":"學校在為屋頂選擇系統前，可能比較兩種系統設計。"},{"en":"If the design is poor, even good panels may produce less useful electricity.","zh":"如果設計差，即使太陽能板良好，也可能產生較少可用電力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to how the whole solar system is planned.","zh":"這個片語指整個太陽能系統如何被規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"within nearby communities","meaning":"在附近社區內","examples":[{"en":"Homes within nearby communities were monitored during the experiment.","zh":"實驗期間，附近社區內的住宅受到監察。"},{"en":"Within nearby communities means in the neighbourhoods or towns close to the test site.","zh":"Within nearby communities 指在接近測試場地的社區或城鎮中。"},{"en":"A clinic may study health habits within nearby communities before planning services.","zh":"診所可能在計劃服務前研究附近社區內的健康習慣。"},{"en":"If nearby homes are monitored, researchers can compare real use with experimental results.","zh":"如果附近住宅受到監察，研究人員可以把真實使用與實驗結果比較。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people or places close to the research area.","zh":"這個片語描述接近研究區域的人或地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be monitored to see how well","meaning":"受到監察以了解……的配合程度","examples":[{"en":"Household electricity use was monitored to see how well it matched solar generation.","zh":"家庭用電受到監察，以了解它與太陽能發電的配合程度。"},{"en":"To be monitored to see how well something works means to be observed and measured to judge performance.","zh":"To be monitored to see how well something works 指被觀察和量度，以判斷表現。"},{"en":"A teacher may monitor a student’s reading speed to see how well a new method works.","zh":"老師可能監察學生閱讀速度，以了解新方法有多有效。"},{"en":"If energy use is monitored, researchers can identify times of shortage or surplus.","zh":"如果能源使用受到監察，研究人員可以識別短缺或過剩的時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful checking for performance.","zh":"這個片語描述為評估表現而仔細檢查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"energy use","meaning":"能源使用量","examples":[{"en":"The researchers compared household energy use with solar output.","zh":"研究人員比較家庭能源使用量與太陽能輸出。"},{"en":"Energy use means the amount and pattern of electricity or fuel consumed.","zh":"Energy use 指電力或燃料的消耗量和使用模式。"},{"en":"A family can reduce energy use by switching off lights and using efficient appliances.","zh":"家庭可以透過關燈和使用高效電器來減少能源使用量。"},{"en":"If energy use is high at night, solar panels alone may not meet all needs.","zh":"如果夜間能源使用量高，單靠太陽能板可能不能滿足所有需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how much energy people actually consume.","zh":"這個片語描述人們實際消耗多少能源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"match the energy generated","meaning":"與所產生的能源配合","examples":[{"en":"The study examined whether household demand matched the energy generated by solar roofs.","zh":"研究考察家庭需求是否與太陽能屋頂所產生的能源配合。"},{"en":"To match the energy generated means to use electricity at a level that fits the amount produced.","zh":"To match the energy generated 指用電水平配合所產生的電量。"},{"en":"A school may schedule laundry or charging during sunny hours to match solar output.","zh":"學校可能安排洗衣或充電在陽光充足時進行，以配合太陽能輸出。"},{"en":"If demand does not match generation, electricity may need to be stored or imported.","zh":"如果需求不配合發電量，電力可能需要被儲存或從外部輸入。"},{"en":"This phrase compares energy use with energy production.","zh":"這個片語比較能源使用與能源生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dummy roofs","meaning":"模擬屋頂","examples":[{"en":"The dummy roofs generated electricity under controlled conditions.","zh":"模擬屋頂在受控條件下發電。"},{"en":"Dummy roofs are artificial test roofs built to examine how systems perform.","zh":"Dummy roofs 是為檢查系統表現而建的人造測試屋頂。"},{"en":"Engineers may use dummy roofs to test whether panels survive heavy rain.","zh":"工程師可能使用模擬屋頂測試太陽能板能否承受大雨。"},{"en":"If dummy roofs are built at different angles, researchers can compare sunlight capture.","zh":"如果模擬屋頂以不同角度建造，研究人員可以比較陽光捕捉效果。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to experimental roof structures.","zh":"這個片語指實驗用屋頂結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a change in government priorities","meaning":"政府優先事項的改變","examples":[{"en":"A change in government priorities brought the American programme to an end.","zh":"政府優先事項的改變令美國計劃告終。"},{"en":"A change in government priorities means leaders decide to focus money and attention on different goals.","zh":"A change in government priorities 指領導者決定把金錢和注意力集中在不同目標上。"},{"en":"A school project may stop after a change in management priorities.","zh":"管理層優先事項改變後，學校項目可能停止。"},{"en":"If energy research is no longer a priority, funding may be reduced or cancelled.","zh":"如果能源研究不再是優先事項，資金可能被減少或取消。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how political focus can affect programmes.","zh":"這個片語解釋政治焦點如何影響計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"halt a programme","meaning":"中止一項計劃","examples":[{"en":"The government halted the photovoltaic research programme in the early 1980s.","zh":"政府在1980年代初中止了光伏研究計劃。"},{"en":"To halt a programme means to stop it, usually before it has fully finished.","zh":"To halt a programme 指停止一項計劃，通常是在它完全完成之前。"},{"en":"A school may halt an exchange programme if travel becomes unsafe.","zh":"如果旅行變得不安全，學校可能中止交流計劃。"},{"en":"If funding disappears, a research programme may be halted suddenly.","zh":"如果資金消失，研究計劃可能突然被中止。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an official stop to an organised project.","zh":"這個片語描述有組織項目的正式停止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the US effort","meaning":"美國所作的推動工作","examples":[{"en":"The US effort to promote residential photovoltaics declined in the early 1980s.","zh":"美國推動住宅光伏發電系統的工作在1980年代初減弱。"},{"en":"The US effort means the work, funding, and policies carried out by the United States.","zh":"The US effort 指美國所進行的工作、資金投入和政策。"},{"en":"A national effort to improve reading may include teacher training and library funding.","zh":"改善閱讀的全國性工作可能包括教師培訓和圖書館資助。"},{"en":"If a country’s effort weakens, other countries may take the lead.","zh":"如果一個國家的推動工作減弱，其他國家可能取得領先。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised action by a country.","zh":"這個片語指一個國家有組織的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"drop away","meaning":"逐漸減弱；停止","examples":[{"en":"As the US effort dropped away, Japan expanded its own research.","zh":"隨着美國的推動工作逐漸減弱，日本擴展自己的研究。"},{"en":"To drop away means to gradually become weaker, smaller, or less active.","zh":"To drop away 指逐漸變弱、變少或變得不活躍。"},{"en":"Student interest may drop away if a course becomes too repetitive.","zh":"如果課程變得太重複，學生興趣可能逐漸減弱。"},{"en":"If government support drops away, companies may slow investment.","zh":"如果政府支援逐漸減弱，公司可能放慢投資。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual decline rather than sudden disappearance.","zh":"這個片語描述逐步衰退，而不是突然消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"come to the fore","meaning":"變得突出；受到重視","examples":[{"en":"The Japanese Sunshine Project came to the fore after the US programme ended.","zh":"美國計劃結束後，日本陽光計劃變得突出。"},{"en":"To come to the fore means to become important, noticeable, or leading.","zh":"To come to the fore 指變得重要、顯眼或領先。"},{"en":"During a crisis, good communication skills often come to the fore.","zh":"危機期間，良好溝通技巧通常會變得突出。"},{"en":"If one country reduces research, another country’s project may come to the fore.","zh":"如果一個國家減少研究，另一個國家的項目可能受到重視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming prominent.","zh":"這個片語描述變得顯著。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"residential test station","meaning":"住宅測試站","examples":[{"en":"Japan installed a large residential test station on Rokko Island.","zh":"日本在六甲島安裝了一個大型住宅測試站。"},{"en":"A residential test station is a research site that tests systems designed for homes.","zh":"Residential test station 是測試住宅用系統的研究場地。"},{"en":"Engineers may build a residential test station to compare different insulation materials.","zh":"工程師可能建造住宅測試站，比較不同隔熱材料。"},{"en":"If a test station simulates daily home use, results can guide real housing policies.","zh":"如果測試站模擬日常家居使用，結果可以指導真實房屋政策。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a controlled home-like research facility.","zh":"這個片語描述受控、像住宅的研究設施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be installed on","meaning":"被安裝在……","examples":[{"en":"A photovoltaic test station was installed on Rokko Island.","zh":"一個光伏測試站被安裝在六甲島。"},{"en":"To be installed on a place means to be set up or fixed there for use.","zh":"To be installed on a place 指被設置或固定在某處以供使用。"},{"en":"Security cameras may be installed on the school entrance.","zh":"保安攝像機可能被安裝在學校入口。"},{"en":"If solar equipment is installed on an island, researchers can test it in local conditions.","zh":"如果太陽能設備被安裝在島上，研究人員可以在當地條件下測試它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes placing equipment in a specific location.","zh":"這個片語描述把設備放置於特定位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"consist of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"The installation consists of eighteen simulated homes.","zh":"該設施由十八間模擬住宅組成。"},{"en":"To consist of something means to be made up of those parts.","zh":"To consist of something 指由那些部分構成。"},{"en":"A simple lunch may consist of rice, vegetables, and soup.","zh":"簡單午餐可能由米飯、蔬菜和湯組成。"},{"en":"If a test station consists of many simulated homes, researchers can test several designs at once.","zh":"如果測試站由許多模擬住宅組成，研究人員可以同時測試幾種設計。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what something contains.","zh":"這個片語解釋某物包含甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be equipped with","meaning":"配備有……","examples":[{"en":"Each dummy home was equipped with its own photovoltaic system.","zh":"每間模擬住宅都配備有自己的光伏系統。"},{"en":"To be equipped with something means to have the tools or devices needed for a purpose.","zh":"To be equipped with something 指擁有某目的所需的工具或裝置。"},{"en":"A classroom equipped with projectors and speakers can support multimedia lessons.","zh":"配備投影機和揚聲器的課室可以支持多媒體課堂。"},{"en":"If each house is equipped with solar panels, researchers can compare individual performance.","zh":"如果每間房屋都配備太陽能板，研究人員可以比較個別表現。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something has been provided with useful equipment.","zh":"這個片語顯示某物已獲提供有用設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"kilowatt photovoltaic system","meaning":"千瓦級光伏系統","examples":[{"en":"Each test home had a two-to-five-kilowatt photovoltaic system.","zh":"每間測試住宅都有一個二至五千瓦的光伏系統。"},{"en":"A kilowatt photovoltaic system is a solar-power system measured by its electricity-generating capacity in kilowatts.","zh":"Kilowatt photovoltaic system 是以千瓦量度發電能力的太陽能發電系統。"},{"en":"A small home may need a smaller kilowatt system than a large house with many appliances.","zh":"小型住宅可能比有很多電器的大屋需要較小的千瓦級系統。"},{"en":"If the system size is too small, it may not cover household electricity demand.","zh":"如果系統容量太小，它可能不能覆蓋家庭用電需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the capacity of a solar-electric system.","zh":"這個片語描述太陽能發電系統的容量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"simulated homes","meaning":"模擬住宅","examples":[{"en":"Some simulated homes contained electrical appliances.","zh":"一些模擬住宅包含電器。"},{"en":"Simulated homes are artificial homes built to imitate real household conditions.","zh":"Simulated homes 是為模仿真實家庭條件而建的人造住宅。"},{"en":"Engineers may use simulated homes to test how appliances affect energy use.","zh":"工程師可能使用模擬住宅測試電器如何影響能源使用。"},{"en":"If simulated homes behave like real homes, experiments become more practical.","zh":"如果模擬住宅像真實住宅般運作，實驗就更實用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to test homes, not occupied family houses.","zh":"這個片語指測試用住宅，而不是有人居住的家庭住宅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"electrical appliances","meaning":"電器","examples":[{"en":"The test houses contained electrical appliances such as refrigerators.","zh":"測試房屋包含雪櫃等電器。"},{"en":"Electrical appliances are devices that use electricity to perform household tasks.","zh":"Electrical appliances 是使用電力完成家務或日常任務的裝置。"},{"en":"Kettles, washing machines, fans, and televisions are electrical appliances.","zh":"電熱水壺、洗衣機、風扇和電視都是電器。"},{"en":"If many appliances run at the same time, household electricity demand rises.","zh":"如果許多電器同時運作，家庭用電需求會上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes everyday devices powered by electricity.","zh":"這個片語描述由電力驅動的日常裝置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"air-conditioning units","meaning":"空調設備","examples":[{"en":"The appliances included television sets, refrigerators and air-conditioning units.","zh":"電器包括電視機、雪櫃和空調設備。"},{"en":"Air-conditioning units are machines that cool indoor air.","zh":"Air-conditioning units 是冷卻室內空氣的機器。"},{"en":"A classroom may need air-conditioning units during a hot and humid summer.","zh":"在炎熱潮濕的夏天，課室可能需要空調設備。"},{"en":"If many air-conditioning units run at once, electricity demand can rise sharply.","zh":"如果許多空調設備同時運行，電力需求可能急劇上升。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to cooling machines, not ventilation alone.","zh":"這個片語指冷卻機器，而不只是通風。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"switch on and off","meaning":"開啟和關閉","examples":[{"en":"The appliances switched on and off automatically.","zh":"電器自動開啟和關閉。"},{"en":"To switch on and off means to start and stop operating.","zh":"To switch on and off 指開始和停止運作。"},{"en":"A classroom fan may switch on and off according to the timer.","zh":"課室風扇可能按計時器開啟和關閉。"},{"en":"If appliances switch on together, household electricity demand may suddenly rise.","zh":"如果電器同時開啟，家庭用電需求可能突然上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled starting and stopping.","zh":"這個片語描述受控的啟動和停止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"under computer control","meaning":"由電腦控制","examples":[{"en":"The electrical appliances operated under computer control.","zh":"電器由電腦控制運作。"},{"en":"Under computer control means controlled automatically by a computer system.","zh":"Under computer control 指由電腦系統自動控制。"},{"en":"A school’s lights may operate under computer control to save energy after lessons.","zh":"學校照明可能由電腦控制，在課後節省能源。"},{"en":"If appliances are controlled by computer, researchers can repeat the same test conditions.","zh":"如果電器由電腦控制，研究人員可以重複相同測試條件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes automated control rather than human switching.","zh":"這個片語描述自動控制，而不是人手開關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"provide a lavish lifestyle for","meaning":"為……提供奢華生活","examples":[{"en":"The appliances appeared to provide a lavish lifestyle for the imaginary residents.","zh":"這些電器似乎為想像中的住戶提供奢華生活。"},{"en":"To provide a lavish lifestyle for someone means to give them a very comfortable and luxurious way of living.","zh":"To provide a lavish lifestyle for someone 指給某人非常舒適和豪華的生活方式。"},{"en":"A hotel with private pools and personal service provides a lavish lifestyle for guests.","zh":"有私人泳池和個人服務的酒店為客人提供奢華生活。"},{"en":"If a test home runs many appliances, it can simulate high electricity use.","zh":"如果測試住宅運行許多電器，它可以模擬高用電量。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests luxury and comfort beyond basic needs.","zh":"這個片語暗示超越基本需要的奢侈和舒適。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"non-existent occupants","meaning":"根本不存在的住戶","examples":[{"en":"The simulated houses had appliances but no real occupants.","zh":"模擬房屋有電器，但沒有真實住戶。"},{"en":"Non-existent occupants are imaginary residents who do not actually live in the building.","zh":"Non-existent occupants 是實際上沒有住在建築物中的想像住戶。"},{"en":"A model flat may be designed for non-existent occupants to show how furniture could fit.","zh":"示範單位可能為根本不存在的住戶設計，以展示家具如何擺放。"},{"en":"If houses have no real occupants, computers must simulate daily use patterns.","zh":"如果房屋沒有真實住戶，電腦就必須模擬日常使用模式。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights that the residents are not real people.","zh":"這個片語突顯住戶不是真實的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"simulate household loads","meaning":"模擬家庭用電負荷","examples":[{"en":"Electronic equipment simulated household electricity loads.","zh":"電子設備模擬家庭用電負荷。"},{"en":"To simulate household loads means to imitate the electricity demand of a real home.","zh":"To simulate household loads 指模仿真實住宅的電力需求。"},{"en":"Engineers may simulate household loads by turning appliances on at typical family times.","zh":"工程師可能在典型家庭時間開啟電器，以模擬家庭用電負荷。"},{"en":"If loads are simulated accurately, test results can predict real household performance.","zh":"如果負荷被準確模擬，測試結果可以預測真實家庭表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes imitating home electricity use for research.","zh":"這個片語描述為研究而模仿家庭用電。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"household loads","meaning":"家庭用電負荷","examples":[{"en":"Researchers tested how different household loads affected the system.","zh":"研究人員測試不同家庭用電負荷如何影響系統。"},{"en":"Household loads are the electricity demands created by appliances and activities in a home.","zh":"Household loads 是由家中電器和活動造成的電力需求。"},{"en":"Cooking, laundry, air-conditioning, and lighting all add to household loads.","zh":"煮食、洗衣、空調和照明都會增加家庭用電負荷。"},{"en":"If household loads peak at night, daytime solar power may not cover them directly.","zh":"如果家庭用電負荷在夜間達到高峰，日間太陽能未必能直接覆蓋它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how much electricity a home needs at different times.","zh":"這個片語描述住宅在不同時間需要多少電力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"allow something to be explored systematically","meaning":"使……得以有系統地研究","examples":[{"en":"The station allowed photovoltaic systems to be explored systematically.","zh":"該測試站使光伏系統得以有系統地研究。"},{"en":"To allow something to be explored systematically means to make careful, organised study possible.","zh":"To allow something to be explored systematically 指使仔細而有組織的研究成為可能。"},{"en":"A school database allows attendance problems to be explored systematically.","zh":"學校資料庫使出席問題得以有系統地研究。"},{"en":"If conditions are controlled, researchers can study one factor at a time.","zh":"如果條件受控，研究人員可以一次研究一個因素。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making structured investigation possible.","zh":"這個片語描述使結構化調查成為可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"well-controlled test conditions","meaning":"控制良好的測試條件","examples":[{"en":"The systems were examined under well-controlled test conditions.","zh":"這些系統在控制良好的測試條件下接受檢查。"},{"en":"Well-controlled test conditions are conditions carefully managed so results can be trusted.","zh":"Well-controlled test conditions 是被仔細管理、令結果可信的條件。"},{"en":"A science class uses well-controlled conditions when only one variable is changed.","zh":"科學課只改變一個變項時，就是使用控制良好的條件。"},{"en":"If test conditions are controlled, researchers can identify what caused the result.","zh":"如果測試條件受控，研究人員可以識別是甚麼造成結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful experimental control.","zh":"這個片語描述仔細的實驗控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"insurmountable problems","meaning":"無法克服的問題","examples":[{"en":"The researchers identified no insurmountable problems.","zh":"研究人員沒有發現無法克服的問題。"},{"en":"Insurmountable problems are problems so difficult that they cannot be overcome.","zh":"Insurmountable problems 是困難到不能被克服的問題。"},{"en":"A lack of money can feel like an insurmountable problem for a small community project.","zh":"對小型社區項目來說，缺乏資金可能感覺像無法克服的問題。"},{"en":"If no insurmountable problems appear, a technology may be ready for wider testing.","zh":"如果沒有出現無法克服的問題，技術可能已準備好進行更廣泛測試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes obstacles that would stop progress completely.","zh":"這個片語描述會完全阻止進展的障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"experience gained from","meaning":"從……取得的經驗","examples":[{"en":"Japan used the experience gained from the test station to plan a national campaign.","zh":"日本利用從測試站取得的經驗來規劃全國推廣計劃。"},{"en":"Experience gained from something means practical knowledge learned through doing or testing it.","zh":"Experience gained from something 指透過做某事或測試某事而學到的實用知識。"},{"en":"A teacher may use experience gained from one class to improve the next lesson.","zh":"老師可能利用從一班取得的經驗來改善下一堂課。"},{"en":"If engineers learn from a test site, they can avoid mistakes in real installations.","zh":"如果工程師從測試場地學習，他們可以在真實安裝中避免錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes useful lessons collected from practice.","zh":"這個片語描述從實踐中收集到的有用教訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"massive residential campaign","meaning":"大型住宅光伏推廣計劃","examples":[{"en":"Japan launched a massive residential photovoltaics campaign.","zh":"日本推出大型住宅光伏推廣計劃。"},{"en":"A massive residential campaign is a large organised effort aimed at many homes.","zh":"Massive residential campaign 是針對大量住宅的大型有組織行動。"},{"en":"A city may run a massive residential campaign to replace old lights with efficient ones.","zh":"城市可能推行大型住宅計劃，把舊燈換成高效燈。"},{"en":"If a campaign reaches many households, it can change the market quickly.","zh":"如果推廣計劃接觸許多家庭，它可以快速改變市場。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large-scale action focused on homes.","zh":"這個片語描述集中於住宅的大規模行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"meanwhile","meaning":"與此同時","examples":[{"en":"Meanwhile, Germany began its own rooftop solar programme.","zh":"與此同時，德國開始自己的天台太陽能計劃。"},{"en":"Meanwhile means at the same time or during the same period.","zh":"Meanwhile 指同時或在同一時期。"},{"en":"The teacher checked homework; meanwhile, the students read quietly.","zh":"老師檢查功課；與此同時，學生安靜閱讀。"},{"en":"If one country expands solar research while another does the same, both developments happen meanwhile.","zh":"如果一個國家擴展太陽能研究，而另一個國家也這樣做，兩項發展就是同時發生。"},{"en":"This word connects two events happening in parallel.","zh":"這個詞連接兩件並行發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"1,000-roof programme","meaning":"「一千屋頂計劃」","examples":[{"en":"Germany launched a 1,000-roof programme in 1990.","zh":"德國在1990年推出「一千屋頂計劃」。"},{"en":"A 1,000-roof programme is a scheme to install solar systems on about one thousand roofs.","zh":"1,000-roof programme 是在約一千個屋頂上安裝太陽能系統的計劃。"},{"en":"A town may begin with a 100-roof project before expanding to more homes.","zh":"城鎮可能先從一百屋頂項目開始，再擴展到更多住宅。"},{"en":"If many roofs are included, researchers can see how the technology works in real communities.","zh":"如果包括許多屋頂，研究人員可以看見技術在真實社區中如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase names a rooftop-solar installation campaign.","zh":"這個片語命名一項天台太陽能安裝推廣計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be aimed at doing something","meaning":"旨在做某事","examples":[{"en":"The programme was aimed at installing photovoltaics on private homes.","zh":"該計劃旨在把光伏系統安裝在私人住宅上。"},{"en":"To be aimed at doing something means to be designed with that goal in mind.","zh":"To be aimed at doing something 指以該目標為設計目的。"},{"en":"A reading club may be aimed at helping shy students speak more confidently.","zh":"閱讀會可能旨在幫助害羞學生更有信心地說話。"},{"en":"If a policy is aimed at cutting emissions, its success should be measured by emissions reduction.","zh":"如果政策旨在減少排放，其成功應以排放減幅衡量。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly states the purpose of an action or plan.","zh":"這個片語清楚說明行動或計劃的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"install photovoltaics on","meaning":"在……上安裝光伏系統","examples":[{"en":"The programme installed photovoltaics on the roofs of private homes.","zh":"該計劃在私人住宅屋頂上安裝光伏系統。"},{"en":"To install photovoltaics on a building means to put solar-electric equipment there for use.","zh":"To install photovoltaics on a building 指在建築物上安裝可使用的太陽能發電設備。"},{"en":"A school may install photovoltaics on its sports hall roof.","zh":"學校可能在體育館屋頂上安裝光伏系統。"},{"en":"If panels are installed on a sunny roof, the building can generate its own electricity.","zh":"如果太陽能板安裝在陽光充足的屋頂上，建築物可以自己發電。"},{"en":"This phrase describes placing solar-power equipment on a surface.","zh":"這個片語描述把太陽能發電設備安放在某表面上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"private homes","meaning":"私人住宅","examples":[{"en":"The German programme initially targeted one thousand private homes.","zh":"德國計劃最初以一千間私人住宅為目標。"},{"en":"Private homes are houses or flats owned or lived in by individual families rather than public institutions.","zh":"Private homes 是由個別家庭擁有或居住的房屋或單位，而不是公共機構。"},{"en":"Energy-saving advice often needs to be simple enough for private homes to follow.","zh":"節能建議通常需要簡單到私人住宅能夠實行。"},{"en":"If private homes adopt solar power, household emissions may fall.","zh":"如果私人住宅採用太陽能，家庭排放可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to ordinary residences, not offices or factories.","zh":"這個片語指普通住宅，而不是辦公室或工廠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"federal and regional government subsidies","meaning":"聯邦及地區政府補貼","examples":[{"en":"Federal and regional government subsidies covered most of the installation cost.","zh":"聯邦及地區政府補貼承擔了大部分安裝成本。"},{"en":"Federal and regional government subsidies are financial support from national and local authorities.","zh":"Federal and regional government subsidies 是來自國家和地方政府的財政支援。"},{"en":"A family may install solar panels sooner if subsidies lower the upfront cost.","zh":"如果補貼降低前期成本，家庭可能更早安裝太陽能板。"},{"en":"If subsidies cover much of the price, more households can afford new technology.","zh":"如果補貼承擔大部分價格，更多家庭可以負擔新科技。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public funding from different levels of government.","zh":"這個片語描述來自不同政府層級的公共資金。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be involved","meaning":"涉及其中","examples":[{"en":"Large government subsidies were involved in the programme.","zh":"大量政府補貼涉及該計劃。"},{"en":"To be involved means to be included or play a part in something.","zh":"To be involved 指被包括在某事中或在其中發揮作用。"},{"en":"Several teachers may be involved in planning a school open day.","zh":"幾位老師可能參與策劃學校開放日。"},{"en":"If public money is involved, officials usually monitor how it is spent.","zh":"如果涉及公共資金，官員通常會監察其使用方式。"},{"en":"This phrase shows participation or inclusion.","zh":"這個片語顯示參與或包含其中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"account for","meaning":"佔……","examples":[{"en":"The subsidies accounted for around 70% of the total system cost.","zh":"補貼佔系統總成本約70%。"},{"en":"To account for an amount means to make up that amount or proportion.","zh":"To account for an amount 指構成該數量或比例。"},{"en":"Transport may account for a large part of a student’s monthly spending.","zh":"交通費可能佔學生每月開支很大部分。"},{"en":"If subsidies account for most of the cost, the buyer pays much less.","zh":"如果補貼佔大部分成本，買家就支付少得多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the share one part takes in a total.","zh":"這個片語描述某部分在總數中所佔比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"total system costs","meaning":"系統總成本","examples":[{"en":"Government assistance covered most of the total system costs.","zh":"政府援助承擔了大部分系統總成本。"},{"en":"Total system costs are all the expenses needed to buy, install, and connect a system.","zh":"Total system costs 是購買、安裝和連接一個系統所需的全部開支。"},{"en":"When buying a computer system, total costs include hardware, software, setup, and support.","zh":"購買電腦系統時，總成本包括硬件、軟件、設置和支援。"},{"en":"If hidden costs are ignored, the system may be more expensive than expected.","zh":"如果隱藏成本被忽略，系統可能比預期更昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the full cost, not just the panels.","zh":"這個片語指完整成本，而不只是太陽能板成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"prove immensely popular","meaning":"證明極受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The rooftop programme proved immensely popular.","zh":"天台計劃證明極受歡迎。"},{"en":"To prove immensely popular means to turn out to be extremely well liked or strongly demanded.","zh":"To prove immensely popular 指結果顯示極受喜愛或需求很強。"},{"en":"A free weekend bus service may prove immensely popular with elderly residents.","zh":"免費週末巴士服務可能證明極受長者歡迎。"},{"en":"If a programme proves popular, organisers may need to expand it.","zh":"如果計劃證明受歡迎，主辦方可能需要擴展它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes popularity shown by real response.","zh":"這個片語描述由實際反應顯示出的受歡迎程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"force the extension of","meaning":"迫使……擴展","examples":[{"en":"High demand forced the extension of the programme.","zh":"高需求迫使該計劃擴展。"},{"en":"To force the extension of something means to make it necessary to expand or continue it.","zh":"To force the extension of something 指令擴展或延續某事變得必要。"},{"en":"Extra student demand may force the extension of a popular after-school class.","zh":"額外學生需求可能迫使受歡迎的課後班擴展。"},{"en":"If too many households apply, a solar scheme may need more funding and places.","zh":"如果太多家庭申請，太陽能計劃可能需要更多資金和名額。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that pressure creates expansion.","zh":"這個片語顯示壓力造成擴展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be extended to","meaning":"擴展至……","examples":[{"en":"The scheme was extended to more than two thousand homes.","zh":"該計劃擴展至超過二千間住宅。"},{"en":"To be extended to someone or somewhere means to be expanded so they are included.","zh":"To be extended to someone or somewhere 指被擴大以包括他們或該地方。"},{"en":"A lunch subsidy may be extended to more students if family incomes fall.","zh":"如果家庭收入下降，午餐津貼可能擴展至更多學生。"},{"en":"If a pilot scheme works well, it may be extended to other districts.","zh":"如果試驗計劃成效良好，它可能擴展至其他地區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes widening coverage.","zh":"這個片語描述擴大覆蓋範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be scattered across","meaning":"分布在……各地","examples":[{"en":"The participating homes were scattered across Germany.","zh":"參與住宅分布在德國各地。"},{"en":"To be scattered across a place means to be spread out in many different locations.","zh":"To be scattered across a place 指分散在許多不同地點。"},{"en":"Small clinics may be scattered across rural areas so residents can reach basic care.","zh":"小診所可能分布在鄉郊各地，讓居民能取得基本醫療。"},{"en":"If test homes are scattered across a country, results reflect more varied conditions.","zh":"如果測試住宅分布全國各地，結果能反映更多不同條件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wide distribution, not one cluster.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛分布，而不是集中一處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stimulate other countries to","meaning":"促使其他國家……","examples":[{"en":"Germany’s success stimulated other European countries to launch similar schemes.","zh":"德國的成功促使其他歐洲國家推出類似計劃。"},{"en":"To stimulate other countries to act means to encourage or prompt them to do something.","zh":"To stimulate other countries to act 指鼓勵或促使其他國家做某事。"},{"en":"One school’s success can stimulate other schools to try the same reading programme.","zh":"一間學校的成功可以促使其他學校嘗試同一閱讀計劃。"},{"en":"If a solar scheme works well, neighbouring countries may copy the idea.","zh":"如果太陽能計劃成效良好，鄰近國家可能仿效該想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one example encouraging wider action.","zh":"這個片語描述一個例子鼓勵更廣泛行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"launch similar programmes","meaning":"推出類似計劃","examples":[{"en":"Several European countries launched similar photovoltaic programmes.","zh":"幾個歐洲國家推出類似光伏計劃。"},{"en":"To launch similar programmes means to start projects that resemble an earlier one.","zh":"To launch similar programmes 指開始與早前計劃相似的項目。"},{"en":"After one library starts a reading club, other libraries may launch similar programmes.","zh":"一間圖書館開設閱讀會後，其他圖書館可能推出類似計劃。"},{"en":"If a model works in one country, similar programmes may spread quickly.","zh":"如果某模式在一個國家有效，類似計劃可能迅速傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase describes starting comparable organised actions.","zh":"這個片語描述開始可比較的有組織行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"one-million-roof programme","meaning":"「一百萬屋頂計劃」","examples":[{"en":"Japan later developed a one-million-roof programme.","zh":"日本後來發展出「一百萬屋頂計劃」。"},{"en":"A one-million-roof programme is a very large scheme to put solar systems on one million roofs.","zh":"One-million-roof programme 是在一百萬個屋頂上安裝太陽能系統的大型計劃。"},{"en":"A city may begin with a small pilot before aiming for a million homes.","zh":"城市可能先從小型試驗開始，再以一百萬間住宅為目標。"},{"en":"If such a programme succeeds, it can transform an entire industry.","zh":"如果這類計劃成功，它可以改變整個產業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an extremely ambitious rooftop-solar campaign.","zh":"這個片語描述極具雄心的天台太陽能推廣計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be prompted by","meaning":"由……促成","examples":[{"en":"The Japanese campaign was prompted by earlier testing and Germany’s success.","zh":"日本推廣計劃由早前測試和德國成功經驗促成。"},{"en":"To be prompted by something means to be caused or encouraged by it.","zh":"To be prompted by something 指由某事造成或鼓勵而發生。"},{"en":"A school may start a breakfast club prompted by concerns about hungry students.","zh":"學校可能因擔心學生捱餓而開設早餐會。"},{"en":"If another country’s programme succeeds, it may prompt similar action elsewhere.","zh":"如果另一國計劃成功，它可能促成其他地方採取類似行動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what triggered a decision.","zh":"這個片語顯示是甚麼觸發決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"test site","meaning":"測試場地","examples":[{"en":"The Rokko Island test site provided valuable practical experience.","zh":"六甲島測試場地提供了寶貴實務經驗。"},{"en":"A test site is a place where equipment, systems, or ideas are tried out.","zh":"Test site 是測試設備、系統或想法的地方。"},{"en":"A school playground may be used as a test site for new safety surfaces.","zh":"學校操場可能被用作新安全地面的測試場地。"},{"en":"If a test site gives reliable results, the design can be improved before wider use.","zh":"如果測試場地提供可靠結果，設計可以在更廣泛使用前得到改善。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a location used for experimentation.","zh":"這個片語指用於實驗的地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"initially quoted aims","meaning":"最初公布的目標","examples":[{"en":"The organisation’s initially quoted aims were highly ambitious.","zh":"該組織最初公布的目標非常雄心勃勃。"},{"en":"Initially quoted aims are goals first publicly stated or announced.","zh":"Initially quoted aims 是最初公開說明或公布的目標。"},{"en":"A school’s initially quoted aim may be to help every student read one book a month.","zh":"學校最初公布的目標可能是幫助每位學生每月讀一本書。"},{"en":"If initial aims are too ambitious, the programme may begin on a smaller scale.","zh":"如果初始目標太雄心勃勃，計劃可能以較小規模開始。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the first announced targets.","zh":"這個片語指最初公布的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have homes equipped with","meaning":"讓住宅配備……","examples":[{"en":"Japan aimed to have tens of thousands of homes equipped with photovoltaics.","zh":"日本目標是讓數以萬計住宅配備光伏系統。"},{"en":"To have homes equipped with something means to arrange for homes to be fitted with that equipment.","zh":"To have homes equipped with something 指安排住宅安裝某設備。"},{"en":"A housing project may have homes equipped with smoke alarms and energy-saving lights.","zh":"住宅項目可能讓住宅配備煙霧警報器和節能燈。"},{"en":"If many homes are equipped with solar panels, electricity generation becomes more distributed.","zh":"如果許多住宅配備太陽能板，發電就變得更分散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving homes a particular system or device.","zh":"這個片語描述為住宅提供某系統或裝置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"on the way to","meaning":"邁向……的過程中","examples":[{"en":"The initial target was a step on the way to one million solar homes.","zh":"最初目標是邁向一百萬太陽能住宅過程中的一步。"},{"en":"On the way to something means moving toward a larger goal.","zh":"On the way to something 指正朝着較大目標前進。"},{"en":"Passing a small test can be a step on the way to exam confidence.","zh":"通過小測可以是邁向考試信心過程中的一步。"},{"en":"If a programme starts with a few thousand homes, it may still be on the way to a much bigger target.","zh":"如果計劃由數千間住宅開始，它仍可能是在邁向更大目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes progress toward a destination or aim.","zh":"這個片語描述朝目的地或目標前進。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make a modest start","meaning":"以小規模起步","examples":[{"en":"The programme made a modest start in 1994.","zh":"該計劃在1994年以小規模起步。"},{"en":"To make a modest start means to begin on a small or limited scale.","zh":"To make a modest start 指以小型或有限規模開始。"},{"en":"A student may make a modest start by learning ten new words a day.","zh":"學生可能透過每天學十個新詞以小規模起步。"},{"en":"If a project starts modestly, it can test methods before expanding.","zh":"如果項目以小規模開始，它可以在擴展前測試方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small beginning, not failure.","zh":"這個片語描述小型開始，而不是失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"government subsidy","meaning":"政府補貼","examples":[{"en":"Each early installation received a government subsidy.","zh":"每個早期安裝項目都獲得政府補貼。"},{"en":"A government subsidy is money given by the government to reduce the cost of something.","zh":"Government subsidy 是政府提供、用來降低某物成本的金錢。"},{"en":"A family may buy an electric appliance sooner if a government subsidy lowers the price.","zh":"如果政府補貼降低價格，家庭可能更早購買電器。"},{"en":"If subsidies are generous, new technology can reach ordinary households faster.","zh":"如果補貼慷慨，新科技可以更快進入普通家庭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public financial support.","zh":"這個片語描述公共財政支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cover half the cost","meaning":"承擔一半成本","examples":[{"en":"The government subsidy covered half the installation cost.","zh":"政府補貼承擔了一半安裝成本。"},{"en":"To cover half the cost means to pay 50% of the total price.","zh":"To cover half the cost 指支付總價格的50%。"},{"en":"A school may cover half the cost of a study trip for low-income students.","zh":"學校可能為低收入學生承擔一半遊學費用。"},{"en":"If the government covers half the cost, families need less money upfront.","zh":"如果政府承擔一半成本，家庭前期需要的金錢就較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sharing a payment equally with another payer.","zh":"這個片語描述與另一付款方平均分擔費用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"suburban developments","meaning":"市郊新發展區","examples":[{"en":"Entire new suburban developments adopted photovoltaic systems.","zh":"整個市郊新發展區採用了光伏系統。"},{"en":"Suburban developments are new housing areas built outside or around a city centre.","zh":"Suburban developments 是在市中心外圍或周邊建造的新住宅區。"},{"en":"A suburban development may include houses, small parks, schools, and shops.","zh":"市郊新發展區可能包括房屋、小公園、學校和商店。"},{"en":"If new suburbs include solar systems from the start, installation can be planned more cheaply.","zh":"如果新市郊從一開始就加入太陽能系統，安裝可以更便宜地規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to newly built residential areas near cities.","zh":"這個片語指靠近城市的新建住宅區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"entire new developments","meaning":"整個新發展項目","examples":[{"en":"Entire new housing developments began using solar power.","zh":"整個新住宅發展項目開始使用太陽能。"},{"en":"Entire new developments means complete new building projects, not just a few individual units.","zh":"Entire new developments 指完整的新建築項目，而不是少數個別單位。"},{"en":"An entire new development may include several streets of homes built at the same time.","zh":"整個新發展項目可能包括同時建造的幾條街住宅。"},{"en":"If a whole development uses the same energy system, planning and maintenance may be easier.","zh":"如果整個發展項目使用同一能源系統，規劃和維修可能更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the full scale of a new project.","zh":"這個片語強調新項目的完整規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"good news for","meaning":"對……是好消息","examples":[{"en":"The growth of solar power is good news for the photovoltaic industry.","zh":"太陽能增長對光伏產業是好消息。"},{"en":"Good news for someone means something that is likely to benefit them.","zh":"Good news for someone 指可能令某人或某群體受益的事情。"},{"en":"More students joining a reading club is good news for the school library.","zh":"更多學生加入閱讀會對學校圖書館是好消息。"},{"en":"If solar demand rises, manufacturers and installers may gain more business.","zh":"如果太陽能需求上升，製造商和安裝商可能獲得更多生意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a positive development for a group.","zh":"這個片語描述對某群體有利的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be concerned with the environment","meaning":"關注環境","examples":[{"en":"The development also benefits everyone concerned with the environment.","zh":"這項發展也使所有關注環境的人受益。"},{"en":"To be concerned with the environment means to care about protecting nature and reducing pollution.","zh":"To be concerned with the environment 指關心保護自然和減少污染。"},{"en":"Students concerned with the environment may bring reusable bottles to school.","zh":"關注環境的學生可能帶可重用水樽回校。"},{"en":"If people care about cleaner air, they may support renewable energy.","zh":"如果人們關心更清潔空氣，他們可能支持可再生能源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes environmental concern and responsibility.","zh":"這個片語描述環境關注和責任感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the photovoltaic industry","meaning":"光伏產業","examples":[{"en":"Large residential programmes helped expand the photovoltaic industry.","zh":"大型住宅計劃幫助擴大光伏產業。"},{"en":"The photovoltaic industry includes companies that make, sell, install, and maintain solar-electric systems.","zh":"Photovoltaic industry 包括製造、銷售、安裝和維修太陽能發電系統的公司。"},{"en":"Jobs in the photovoltaic industry may include engineering, sales, roof installation, and system repair.","zh":"光伏產業中的工作可能包括工程、銷售、屋頂安裝和系統維修。"},{"en":"If demand grows, the industry can lower costs through larger production.","zh":"如果需求增長，該產業可以透過更大規模生產降低成本。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the business sector around solar-electric technology.","zh":"這個片語指圍繞太陽能發電技術的商業界別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the use of fossil fuels","meaning":"化石燃料的使用","examples":[{"en":"The use of fossil fuels causes both financial and environmental costs.","zh":"化石燃料的使用造成金錢和環境成本。"},{"en":"The use of fossil fuels means burning coal, oil, or gas for energy.","zh":"The use of fossil fuels 指燃燒煤、石油或天然氣來取得能源。"},{"en":"A city that relies on petrol buses depends heavily on fossil fuels.","zh":"依賴汽油巴士的城市嚴重依賴化石燃料。"},{"en":"If fossil fuels are burned, greenhouse gases and air pollution may increase.","zh":"如果燃燒化石燃料，溫室氣體和空氣污染可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes energy use based on ancient underground fuels.","zh":"這個片語描述基於地下古老燃料的能源使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"generate electricity","meaning":"發電","examples":[{"en":"Coal, oil and gas are commonly burnt to generate electricity.","zh":"煤、石油和天然氣通常被燃燒來發電。"},{"en":"To generate electricity means to produce electrical power.","zh":"To generate electricity 指產生電力。"},{"en":"A wind turbine can generate electricity when strong wind turns its blades.","zh":"當強風吹動葉片，風力渦輪機可以發電。"},{"en":"If a power station generates electricity from coal, it may also release pollution.","zh":"如果發電站用煤發電，它也可能釋放污染。"},{"en":"This phrase describes producing usable electrical energy.","zh":"這個片語描述產生可用電能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be costly in financial terms","meaning":"在金錢方面代價高昂","examples":[{"en":"Fossil-fuel electricity can be costly in financial terms.","zh":"化石燃料電力在金錢方面可能代價高昂。"},{"en":"To be costly in financial terms means to require a lot of money.","zh":"To be costly in financial terms 指需要很多金錢。"},{"en":"Repairing an old lift can be costly in financial terms for a small building.","zh":"對小型大廈來說，維修舊升降機在金錢方面可能代價高昂。"},{"en":"If fuel prices rise, electricity from fossil fuels may become more expensive.","zh":"如果燃料價格上升，來自化石燃料的電力可能變得更昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on money cost, not environmental cost.","zh":"這個片語著重金錢成本，而不是環境成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in terms of environmental damage","meaning":"就環境破壞而言","examples":[{"en":"Fossil fuels are also costly in terms of environmental damage.","zh":"就環境破壞而言，化石燃料代價也很高。"},{"en":"In terms of environmental damage means when considering harm to nature, air, water, or climate.","zh":"In terms of environmental damage 指從對自然、空氣、水或氣候的傷害來看。"},{"en":"A plastic bag may seem cheap, but it can be costly in terms of waste.","zh":"膠袋看似便宜，但就廢物而言可能代價高昂。"},{"en":"If a fuel pollutes the air, its environmental cost is higher than its price suggests.","zh":"如果一種燃料污染空氣，其環境成本比價格顯示的更高。"},{"en":"This phrase shifts the focus from money to environmental harm.","zh":"這個片語把焦點從金錢轉向環境傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"environmental damage","meaning":"環境破壞","examples":[{"en":"The burning of fossil fuels causes serious environmental damage.","zh":"燃燒化石燃料造成嚴重環境破壞。"},{"en":"Environmental damage is harm done to air, water, land, wildlife, or climate.","zh":"Environmental damage 是對空氣、水、土地、野生動物或氣候造成的傷害。"},{"en":"Dumping rubbish into rivers causes environmental damage that affects fish and people.","zh":"把垃圾倒入河流會造成影響魚類和人類的環境破壞。"},{"en":"If electricity production damages the environment, society pays costs beyond the electricity bill.","zh":"如果發電破壞環境，社會付出的成本就不只電費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harm to the natural world.","zh":"這個片語描述對自然世界的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"gases produced by","meaning":"由……產生的氣體","examples":[{"en":"Gases produced by burning fossil fuels contribute to climate change.","zh":"由燃燒化石燃料產生的氣體加劇氣候變化。"},{"en":"Gases produced by something are gases released as a result of that process.","zh":"Gases produced by something 是由某過程釋放出來的氣體。"},{"en":"Smoke and gases produced by a kitchen fire can make a room unsafe.","zh":"由廚房火災產生的煙和氣體會令房間不安全。"},{"en":"If gases produced by power stations trap heat, they worsen the greenhouse effect.","zh":"如果由發電站產生的氣體困住熱量，它們會加劇溫室效應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emissions created by an activity.","zh":"這個片語描述由某活動產生的排放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the burning of fossil fuels","meaning":"燃燒化石燃料","examples":[{"en":"The burning of fossil fuels releases greenhouse gases.","zh":"燃燒化石燃料會釋放溫室氣體。"},{"en":"The burning of fossil fuels means using coal, oil, or gas as fuel by setting it alight or combusting it.","zh":"The burning of fossil fuels 指透過點燃或燃燒煤、石油或天然氣來使用它們作燃料。"},{"en":"A power station may burn coal to produce electricity for a city.","zh":"發電站可能燃燒煤為城市發電。"},{"en":"If fossil fuels are burned in large amounts, carbon emissions increase.","zh":"如果大量燃燒化石燃料，碳排放會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process behind much conventional energy production.","zh":"這個片語描述許多傳統能源生產背後的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a major contributor to","meaning":"……的主要成因","examples":[{"en":"Electricity generation is a major contributor to the greenhouse effect.","zh":"發電是溫室效應的主要成因之一。"},{"en":"A major contributor to something is an important cause or source of it.","zh":"A major contributor to something 是某事的重要原因或來源。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can be a major contributor to weak concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以是課堂專注力差的主要成因。"},{"en":"If power stations release many emissions, they contribute heavily to climate change.","zh":"如果發電站釋放大量排放，它們就大大加劇氣候變化。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a significant cause.","zh":"這個片語指出重要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the greenhouse effect","meaning":"溫室效應","examples":[{"en":"Carbon emissions intensify the greenhouse effect.","zh":"碳排放加劇溫室效應。"},{"en":"The greenhouse effect is the process by which gases trap heat in the atmosphere.","zh":"Greenhouse effect 是氣體把熱量困在大氣中的過程。"},{"en":"A real greenhouse stays warm because glass traps heat inside.","zh":"真正的溫室保持溫暖，是因為玻璃把熱量困在裏面。"},{"en":"If greenhouse gases increase, more heat may remain around the earth.","zh":"如果溫室氣體增加，更多熱量可能留在地球周圍。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why some emissions warm the planet.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何某些排放令地球升溫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"deal with this problem","meaning":"處理這個問題","examples":[{"en":"Governments are setting emissions targets to deal with this problem.","zh":"政府正在設定排放目標以處理這個問題。"},{"en":"To deal with this problem means to take action to manage, reduce, or solve it.","zh":"To deal with this problem 指採取行動管理、減少或解決問題。"},{"en":"A school may deal with lateness by changing bus arrangements and warning students earlier.","zh":"學校可能透過改變校巴安排和提前提醒學生來處理遲到問題。"},{"en":"If emissions cause warming, governments may deal with the problem through rules and incentives.","zh":"如果排放造成暖化，政府可能透過規例和誘因處理這個問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical action against a difficulty.","zh":"這個片語描述針對困難的實際行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"propose stringent targets","meaning":"提出嚴格目標","examples":[{"en":"Many governments are proposing stringent emissions targets.","zh":"許多政府正在提出嚴格排放目標。"},{"en":"To propose stringent targets means to suggest strict goals that are difficult to meet.","zh":"To propose stringent targets 指提出嚴格且難以達成的目標。"},{"en":"A school may propose stringent attendance targets to reduce lateness.","zh":"學校可能提出嚴格出席目標，以減少遲到。"},{"en":"If targets are stringent, companies may need major changes to meet them.","zh":"如果目標嚴格，公司可能需要重大改變才能達成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes putting forward tough measurable goals.","zh":"這個片語描述提出艱難而可量度的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stringent targets","meaning":"嚴格目標","examples":[{"en":"Stringent targets may limit the amount of greenhouse gas released.","zh":"嚴格目標可能限制溫室氣體釋放量。"},{"en":"Stringent targets are strict goals with little room for failure or delay.","zh":"Stringent targets 是嚴格目標，幾乎沒有失敗或拖延空間。"},{"en":"A hospital may set stringent hygiene targets to reduce infections.","zh":"醫院可能設定嚴格衛生目標，以減少感染。"},{"en":"If targets are stringent, weak or symbolic action will not be enough.","zh":"如果目標嚴格，薄弱或象徵式行動是不足夠的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes demanding standards.","zh":"這個片語描述要求高的標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"greenhouse-gas emissions","meaning":"溫室氣體排放","examples":[{"en":"Governments are trying to reduce greenhouse-gas emissions.","zh":"政府正嘗試減少溫室氣體排放。"},{"en":"Greenhouse-gas emissions are gases released into the air that trap heat in the atmosphere.","zh":"Greenhouse-gas emissions 是釋放到空氣中並把熱量困在大氣中的氣體。"},{"en":"Cars, power stations, and factories can all produce greenhouse-gas emissions.","zh":"汽車、發電站和工廠都可以產生溫室氣體排放。"},{"en":"If emissions fall, climate risks may be reduced over time.","zh":"如果排放下降，氣候風險可能隨時間減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pollution linked with global warming.","zh":"這個片語描述與全球暖化相關的污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the amount permitted","meaning":"獲准排放的數量","examples":[{"en":"New rules may restrict the amount of emissions permitted.","zh":"新規則可能限制獲准排放的數量。"},{"en":"The amount permitted is the quantity that rules allow.","zh":"The amount permitted 是規則所容許的數量。"},{"en":"A school rule may limit the amount of time permitted for phone use during lunch.","zh":"校規可能限制午膳期間獲准使用手機的時間。"},{"en":"If the permitted amount of pollution falls, factories must reduce emissions.","zh":"如果獲准污染量下降，工廠就必須減少排放。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an official limit.","zh":"這個片語描述官方限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"all sources of emissions","meaning":"所有排放來源","examples":[{"en":"All sources of greenhouse-gas emissions may receive greater scrutiny.","zh":"所有溫室氣體排放來源可能受到更嚴格審查。"},{"en":"All sources of emissions means every activity, sector, or place that releases gases.","zh":"All sources of emissions 指每一項釋放氣體的活動、行業或地方。"},{"en":"A city may examine transport, buildings, and waste as sources of emissions.","zh":"城市可能檢視交通、建築和廢物作為排放來源。"},{"en":"If every source is checked, hidden causes of pollution become easier to find.","zh":"如果每個來源都被檢查，隱藏污染原因就更容易找出。"},{"en":"This phrase includes both large and small emitters.","zh":"這個片語包括大型和小型排放者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"residential electricity use","meaning":"住宅用電","examples":[{"en":"Residential electricity use contributes to overall energy demand.","zh":"住宅用電會增加整體能源需求。"},{"en":"Residential electricity use means the electricity consumed by homes.","zh":"Residential electricity use 指住宅消耗的電力。"},{"en":"Cooking, cooling, lighting, and charging devices all add to residential electricity use.","zh":"煮食、降溫、照明和為裝置充電都會增加住宅用電。"},{"en":"If homes become more efficient, residential electricity use can fall.","zh":"如果住宅變得更節能，住宅用電可以下降。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on household electricity consumption.","zh":"這個片語著重家庭電力消耗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"receive closer attention","meaning":"得到更密切關注","examples":[{"en":"Household electricity consumption will receive closer attention in the future.","zh":"家庭電力消耗未來會得到更密切關注。"},{"en":"To receive closer attention means to be examined more carefully than before.","zh":"To receive closer attention 指比以前被更仔細檢視。"},{"en":"A student’s spelling may receive closer attention if it keeps affecting exam marks.","zh":"如果拼字一直影響考試分數，學生的拼字可能得到更密切關注。"},{"en":"If homes contribute to emissions, governments may monitor household energy use more carefully.","zh":"如果住宅造成排放，政府可能更仔細監察家庭能源使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increased scrutiny.","zh":"這個片語描述更高程度的審查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"it is likely that","meaning":"很可能","examples":[{"en":"It is likely that governments will introduce stricter building regulations.","zh":"政府很可能會引入更嚴格的建築規例。"},{"en":"It is likely that means there is a strong possibility that something will happen.","zh":"It is likely that 指某事發生的可能性很高。"},{"en":"It is likely that students who practise daily will improve faster.","zh":"每天練習的學生很可能進步更快。"},{"en":"If energy targets become stricter, it is likely that building rules will change.","zh":"如果能源目標變得更嚴格，建築規則很可能會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses probability, not certainty.","zh":"這個片語表達可能性，而不是確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"building codes","meaning":"建築規例","examples":[{"en":"Future building codes may require homes to use energy-saving technology.","zh":"未來建築規例可能要求住宅使用節能科技。"},{"en":"Building codes are official rules about how buildings must be designed and constructed.","zh":"Building codes 是關於建築物必須如何設計和建造的官方規則。"},{"en":"Building codes may require fire exits, safe wiring, and strong materials.","zh":"建築規例可能要求走火通道、安全電線和堅固材料。"},{"en":"If building codes include solar requirements, new homes must plan for energy production.","zh":"如果建築規例包括太陽能要求，新住宅就必須規劃能源生產。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to legal construction standards.","zh":"這個片語指法定建築標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"attempt to constrain","meaning":"試圖限制……","examples":[{"en":"The regulations may attempt to constrain the energy demands of new housing.","zh":"規例可能試圖限制新建住宅的能源需求。"},{"en":"To attempt to constrain something means to try to limit or control it.","zh":"To attempt to constrain something 指嘗試限制或控制某事。"},{"en":"A school may attempt to constrain phone use by collecting phones before class.","zh":"學校可能透過課前收集手機來試圖限制手機使用。"},{"en":"If new homes use too much energy, rules may try to reduce that demand.","zh":"如果新住宅使用太多能源，規則可能嘗試降低該需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an effort to place limits on something.","zh":"這個片語描述對某事設限的努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"energy demands","meaning":"能源需求","examples":[{"en":"Better insulation and solar panels can reduce a home’s energy demands.","zh":"更好隔熱和太陽能板可以減少住宅能源需求。"},{"en":"Energy demands are the amount of energy required by a building, system, or activity.","zh":"Energy demands 是建築物、系統或活動所需的能源量。"},{"en":"A restaurant has high energy demands because it cooks, cools food, and runs lights for long hours.","zh":"餐廳能源需求高，因為它煮食、冷藏食物並長時間開燈。"},{"en":"If energy demands fall, bills and emissions may fall too.","zh":"如果能源需求下降，帳單和排放也可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how much energy is needed.","zh":"這個片語描述需要多少能源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"new housing","meaning":"新建住宅","examples":[{"en":"New housing may be required to meet strict energy standards.","zh":"新建住宅可能被要求符合嚴格能源標準。"},{"en":"New housing means newly built homes or residential developments.","zh":"New housing 指新建成的住宅或住宅發展項目。"},{"en":"A city may require new housing to include better insulation and safer wiring.","zh":"城市可能要求新建住宅包括更好隔熱和更安全電線。"},{"en":"If new housing is designed efficiently, residents can save energy for many years.","zh":"如果新建住宅設計節能，居民可以多年節省能源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to future or recently built homes.","zh":"這個片語指未來或最近建成的住宅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"photovoltaics or the equivalent","meaning":"光伏系統或同等技術","examples":[{"en":"Building codes may require photovoltaics or an equivalent technology.","zh":"建築規例可能要求光伏系統或同等技術。"},{"en":"Photovoltaics or the equivalent means solar panels or another technology that provides a similar energy-saving function.","zh":"Photovoltaics or the equivalent 指太陽能板或另一種提供相似節能功能的技術。"},{"en":"A school may use solar panels or an equivalent system, such as a shared renewable-energy supply.","zh":"學校可能使用太陽能板或同等系統，例如共享可再生能源供應。"},{"en":"If one technology is unsuitable, an equivalent option may still meet the rule.","zh":"如果某技術不合適，同等選項仍可能符合規則。"},{"en":"This phrase allows similar alternatives, not only one exact system.","zh":"這個片語容許相似替代方案，而不只是一種精確系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be stipulated","meaning":"被明文規定","examples":[{"en":"The use of energy-saving systems may be stipulated by building regulations.","zh":"節能系統的使用可能被建築規例明文規定。"},{"en":"To be stipulated means to be clearly required by a rule, contract, or official document.","zh":"To be stipulated 指被規則、合約或官方文件清楚要求。"},{"en":"A rental contract may stipulate that tenants cannot smoke indoors.","zh":"租約可能明文規定租客不能在室內吸煙。"},{"en":"If solar systems are stipulated in building codes, developers must include them.","zh":"如果太陽能系統在建築規例中被明文規定，發展商就必須包括它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a requirement stated formally.","zh":"這個片語描述正式寫明的要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lessen demands on","meaning":"減輕對……的需求","examples":[{"en":"Rooftop solar panels can lessen demands on the electricity grid.","zh":"天台太陽能板可以減輕對電網的需求。"},{"en":"To lessen demands on something means to reduce the pressure or amount of use placed on it.","zh":"To lessen demands on something 指減少某系統承受的壓力或使用量。"},{"en":"More buses can lessen demands on crowded train lines.","zh":"更多巴士可以減輕對擁擠鐵路線的需求。"},{"en":"If homes generate electricity themselves, the grid may need to supply less power at peak times.","zh":"如果住宅自己發電，電網在高峰時段需要供應的電力可能較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing pressure on a system.","zh":"這個片語描述減少系統壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"hence reduce","meaning":"從而減少","examples":[{"en":"Lower grid demand may hence reduce fossil-fuel emissions.","zh":"較低電網需求可能從而減少化石燃料排放。"},{"en":"Hence reduce means therefore make something smaller or lower.","zh":"Hence reduce 指因此令某事變少或降低。"},{"en":"Better sleep may improve concentration and hence reduce careless mistakes.","zh":"更好睡眠可能改善專注力，從而減少粗心錯誤。"},{"en":"If solar power replaces coal electricity, emissions may fall as a result.","zh":"如果太陽能取代煤電，排放可能因此下降。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with a reduction.","zh":"這個片語把原因與減少連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"fossil-fuel emissions","meaning":"化石燃料排放","examples":[{"en":"Solar electricity can reduce fossil-fuel emissions.","zh":"太陽能電力可以減少化石燃料排放。"},{"en":"Fossil-fuel emissions are gases and pollution released when coal, oil, or gas is burned.","zh":"Fossil-fuel emissions 是燃燒煤、石油或天然氣時釋放的氣體和污染物。"},{"en":"Petrol cars produce fossil-fuel emissions when their engines run.","zh":"汽油車引擎運行時會產生化石燃料排放。"},{"en":"If renewable energy replaces fossil fuels, these emissions can decrease.","zh":"如果可再生能源取代化石燃料，這些排放可以減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pollution from burning ancient fuels.","zh":"這個片語描述燃燒古老燃料產生的污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"approvals for building renovations","meaning":"樓宇翻新工程審批","examples":[{"en":"Approvals for building renovations may depend on energy-saving improvements.","zh":"樓宇翻新工程審批可能取決於節能改善。"},{"en":"Approvals for building renovations are official permissions to repair, change, or upgrade a building.","zh":"Approvals for building renovations 是維修、改動或升級建築物所需的官方許可。"},{"en":"A flat owner may need approval before changing windows or external walls.","zh":"單位業主更換窗戶或外牆前可能需要審批。"},{"en":"If approval depends on energy measures, owners may install insulation or solar panels.","zh":"如果審批取決於節能措施，業主可能安裝隔熱或太陽能板。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to official permission for building work.","zh":"這個片語指建築工程的官方許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be conditional upon","meaning":"以……為條件","examples":[{"en":"Planning approval may be conditional upon installing energy-saving equipment.","zh":"規劃審批可能以安裝節能設備為條件。"},{"en":"To be conditional upon something means to depend on that requirement being met.","zh":"To be conditional upon something 指取決於是否滿足該要求。"},{"en":"A scholarship may be conditional upon maintaining good attendance.","zh":"獎學金可能以保持良好出席率為條件。"},{"en":"If renovation approval is conditional upon solar installation, owners must install it first.","zh":"如果翻新審批以安裝太陽能為條件，業主必須先安裝它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a condition that must be satisfied.","zh":"這個片語描述必須滿足的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take energy-saving measures","meaning":"採取節能措施","examples":[{"en":"Householders may be required to take energy-saving measures.","zh":"住戶可能被要求採取節能措施。"},{"en":"To take energy-saving measures means to act in ways that reduce energy use.","zh":"To take energy-saving measures 指採取行動減少能源使用。"},{"en":"A family may take energy-saving measures by using LED lights and efficient appliances.","zh":"家庭可能透過使用LED燈和高效電器採取節能措施。"},{"en":"If many homes save energy, demand on the grid may fall.","zh":"如果許多住宅節能，電網需求可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical steps to use less energy.","zh":"這個片語描述減少能源使用的實際步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"everyone would benefit","meaning":"人人都會受益","examples":[{"en":"Everyone would benefit from cleaner and more efficient housing.","zh":"人人都會從更清潔、更高效的住宅中受益。"},{"en":"Everyone would benefit means all people would gain some advantage.","zh":"Everyone would benefit 指所有人都會得到某些好處。"},{"en":"Everyone would benefit if public transport became cheaper and more reliable.","zh":"如果公共交通變得更便宜和更可靠，人人都會受益。"},{"en":"If homes use less energy, residents save money and society reduces pollution.","zh":"如果住宅使用較少能源，居民節省金錢，社會也減少污染。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a result that helps many groups.","zh":"這個片語描述有助許多群體的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"initial cost","meaning":"初期成本","examples":[{"en":"Installing a photovoltaic system involves an initial cost.","zh":"安裝光伏系統涉及初期成本。"},{"en":"Initial cost is the money paid at the beginning before later savings or benefits appear.","zh":"Initial cost 是在後來節省或好處出現前，最初支付的金錢。"},{"en":"Buying a reusable water bottle has an initial cost, but it may save money later.","zh":"購買可重用水樽有初期成本，但之後可能省錢。"},{"en":"If the initial cost is high, families may need subsidies or loans.","zh":"如果初期成本高，家庭可能需要補貼或貸款。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to upfront payment.","zh":"這個片語指前期付款。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"attach a system to the rooftop","meaning":"把系統安裝到天台","examples":[{"en":"A professional installer can attach the solar system to the rooftop.","zh":"專業安裝人員可以把太陽能系統安裝到天台。"},{"en":"To attach a system to the rooftop means to fix equipment securely on the roof.","zh":"To attach a system to the rooftop 指把設備穩固固定在屋頂上。"},{"en":"Workers may attach safety rails to a rooftop before repair work begins.","zh":"維修工作開始前，工人可能把安全欄杆安裝到天台。"},{"en":"If the system is not attached properly, strong wind may damage it.","zh":"如果系統沒有妥善安裝，強風可能損壞它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes secure physical installation.","zh":"這個片語描述穩固的實體安裝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"householder’s outlay","meaning":"住戶支出","examples":[{"en":"The householder’s outlay may be recovered through lower electricity bills.","zh":"住戶支出可能透過較低電費收回。"},{"en":"A householder’s outlay is the money a resident or homeowner spends at the start.","zh":"Householder’s outlay 是居民或業主最初花出的金錢。"},{"en":"A family’s outlay on a new fridge may be partly recovered through lower energy bills.","zh":"家庭購買新雪櫃的支出，可能部分透過較低能源帳單收回。"},{"en":"If savings are large enough, the initial outlay can be paid back over time.","zh":"如果節省金額足夠大，初期支出可以隨時間回本。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the money paid by the household.","zh":"這個片語著重家庭支付的金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be compensated by","meaning":"由……補償","examples":[{"en":"The initial cost is eventually compensated by energy savings.","zh":"初期成本最終由能源節省補償。"},{"en":"To be compensated by something means to be balanced or made worthwhile by it.","zh":"To be compensated by something 指由某好處抵消或令某事變得值得。"},{"en":"A long journey may be compensated by a cheaper rent and a better home.","zh":"漫長通勤可能由較便宜租金和較好住宅補償。"},{"en":"If solar panels save money each month, the high starting cost becomes easier to accept.","zh":"如果太陽能板每月省錢，高昂前期成本就較容易接受。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how one disadvantage is balanced by a benefit.","zh":"這個片語顯示一個缺點如何由一項好處抵消。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"savings on energy bills","meaning":"節省能源開支","examples":[{"en":"Photovoltaic systems can produce substantial savings on energy bills.","zh":"光伏系統可以大幅節省能源開支。"},{"en":"Savings on energy bills are reductions in the money paid for electricity, gas, or other energy.","zh":"Savings on energy bills 是電力、燃氣或其他能源費用的減少。"},{"en":"A family may get savings on energy bills by using efficient lights and better insulation.","zh":"家庭可以透過使用高效燈具和更好隔熱來節省能源開支。"},{"en":"If solar panels generate free daytime power, monthly bills may fall.","zh":"如果太陽能板產生免費日間電力，每月帳單可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes money saved through lower energy use or production.","zh":"這個片語描述透過降低能源使用或自行發電而省下的金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in addition","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"In addition, solar power benefits the wider environment.","zh":"此外，太陽能有利於更廣泛的環境。"},{"en":"In addition means furthermore or as another point.","zh":"In addition 指除此之外，或作為另一點。"},{"en":"The new library is quiet; in addition, it opens late for students.","zh":"新圖書館很安靜；此外，它為學生開放至較晚時間。"},{"en":"If solar panels save money, and in addition reduce pollution, they offer more than one benefit.","zh":"如果太陽能板省錢，此外又減少污染，它們就提供多於一項好處。"},{"en":"This phrase adds an extra idea.","zh":"這個片語加入額外想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"stand to gain from","meaning":"可望從……中得益","examples":[{"en":"Everyone stands to gain from cleaner forms of electricity.","zh":"人人都可望從更清潔的電力形式中得益。"},{"en":"To stand to gain from something means to be likely to benefit from it.","zh":"To stand to gain from something 指很可能從某事中受益。"},{"en":"Students stand to gain from clearer feedback because they know how to improve.","zh":"學生可望從更清晰的回饋中得益，因為他們知道如何改進。"},{"en":"If air becomes cleaner, children, elderly people, and workers all benefit.","zh":"如果空氣變得更清潔，兒童、長者和工人都會受益。"},{"en":"This phrase shows who is likely to receive an advantage.","zh":"這個片語顯示誰很可能得到好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"benign environmental impact","meaning":"對環境較為友善的影響","examples":[{"en":"Solar energy has a more benign environmental impact than fossil fuels.","zh":"太陽能比化石燃料對環境有較為友善的影響。"},{"en":"A benign environmental impact is an effect on nature that is mild, low-risk, or less harmful.","zh":"Benign environmental impact 是對自然較溫和、風險較低或較少傷害的影響。"},{"en":"A reusable bottle has a more benign environmental impact than many disposable plastic bottles.","zh":"可重用水樽比許多即棄膠樽對環境有較友善的影響。"},{"en":"If an energy source releases little pollution, its environmental impact is more benign.","zh":"如果能源來源釋放很少污染，其環境影響就較為友善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gentler effect on the environment.","zh":"這個片語描述對環境較溫和的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"which paragraph contains","meaning":"哪一段包含……","examples":[{"en":"Candidates identify which paragraph contains each piece of information.","zh":"考生識別哪一段包含每項資料。"},{"en":"Which paragraph contains means which section of the passage includes the required idea.","zh":"Which paragraph contains 指文章哪一部分包含所需意思。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may need to find which paragraph contains a historical example.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能需要找出哪一段包含歷史例子。"},{"en":"If two paragraphs mention solar power, students should choose the one with the exact detail.","zh":"如果兩段都提到太陽能，學生應選擇有準確細節的一段。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in paragraph-matching tasks.","zh":"這個片語常見於段落配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the following information","meaning":"以下資料","examples":[{"en":"The task asks candidates to locate the following information in the passage.","zh":"任務要求考生在文章中找出以下資料。"},{"en":"The following information means the details listed after the instruction.","zh":"The following information 指指示後列出的細節。"},{"en":"Students should read the following information carefully before scanning the text.","zh":"學生應先仔細閱讀以下資料，再掃讀文章。"},{"en":"If the information is paraphrased, students must match meaning rather than exact words.","zh":"如果資料被改寫，學生必須配對意思，而不是只找完全相同字眼。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the items candidates must find.","zh":"這個片語引出考生必須尋找的項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"use any letter more than once","meaning":"可多次使用任何字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates may use any paragraph letter more than once.","zh":"考生可多次使用任何段落字母。"},{"en":"To use any letter more than once means the same answer option can be repeated.","zh":"To use any letter more than once 指同一答案選項可以重複使用。"},{"en":"In a matching task, one paragraph may answer two different questions.","zh":"在配對題中，同一段可能回答兩條不同問題。"},{"en":"If students assume each letter can be used only once, they may choose wrong answers.","zh":"如果學生假設每個字母只可用一次，他們可能選錯答案。"},{"en":"This instruction tells candidates that repeated answers are allowed.","zh":"這個指示告訴考生可以重複使用答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"electricity use is greater during the day","meaning":"日間用電量較高","examples":[{"en":"In some countries, electricity use is greater during the day than at night.","zh":"在一些國家，日間用電量比夜間較高。"},{"en":"Electricity use is greater during the day means more power is consumed in daylight hours.","zh":"Electricity use is greater during the day 指日光時段消耗更多電力。"},{"en":"Offices, schools, and shops can make daytime electricity use higher than night-time use.","zh":"辦公室、學校和商店可以令日間用電量高於夜間。"},{"en":"If daytime use is high, solar power may match demand well.","zh":"如果日間用電量高，太陽能可能很配合需求。"},{"en":"This phrase compares electricity consumption at different times.","zh":"這個片語比較不同時段的電力消耗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a detailed description of","meaning":"對……的詳細描述","examples":[{"en":"The passage gives a detailed description of the Japanese solar experiment.","zh":"文章對日本太陽能實驗作出詳細描述。"},{"en":"A detailed description of something explains its parts, steps, and features clearly.","zh":"A detailed description of something 清楚解釋某事的部分、步驟和特徵。"},{"en":"A teacher may give a detailed description of how to answer a summary question.","zh":"老師可能詳細描述如何回答摘要題。"},{"en":"If a description is detailed, readers can picture how the system works.","zh":"如果描述詳細，讀者可以想像系統如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an explanation with many useful details.","zh":"這個片語描述包含許多有用細節的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lead to nationwide promotion","meaning":"促成全國推廣","examples":[{"en":"The successful experiment led to photovoltaics being promoted throughout the country.","zh":"成功實驗促成光伏系統在全國推廣。"},{"en":"To lead to nationwide promotion means to cause something to be encouraged across the whole country.","zh":"To lead to nationwide promotion 指促使某事在全國範圍內被鼓勵採用。"},{"en":"A successful reading trial may lead to nationwide promotion of the same school programme.","zh":"成功的閱讀試驗可能促成同一學校計劃全國推廣。"},{"en":"If a test proves a technology works, governments may promote it more widely.","zh":"如果測試證明某技術有效，政府可能更廣泛推廣它。"},{"en":"This phrase links a successful trial with national expansion.","zh":"這個片語把成功試驗與全國擴展連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"conventional means of generating electricity","meaning":"傳統發電方式","examples":[{"en":"Burning fossil fuels is a conventional means of generating electricity.","zh":"燃燒化石燃料是傳統發電方式。"},{"en":"A conventional means of generating electricity is a traditional or widely used method of producing power.","zh":"Conventional means of generating electricity 是傳統或廣泛使用的發電方法。"},{"en":"Coal-fired power stations are a conventional means of generating electricity in many regions.","zh":"燃煤發電站在許多地區都是傳統發電方式。"},{"en":"If conventional methods pollute heavily, cleaner alternatives become more attractive.","zh":"如果傳統方法造成嚴重污染，更清潔替代方案就更有吸引力。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts older standard methods with newer energy options.","zh":"這個片語把舊有標準方法與較新能源選項作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"negative effects of","meaning":"……的負面影響","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes the negative effects of fossil-fuel electricity.","zh":"文章描述化石燃料電力的負面影響。"},{"en":"Negative effects of something are the harmful results it causes.","zh":"Negative effects of something 是某事造成的有害結果。"},{"en":"Poor sleep has negative effects on memory, patience, and concentration.","zh":"睡眠不足對記憶、耐性和專注力有負面影響。"},{"en":"If fossil-fuel electricity produces emissions, its negative effects extend beyond electricity bills.","zh":"如果化石燃料電力產生排放，其負面影響就超出電費本身。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on damage or disadvantages.","zh":"這個片語著重傷害或缺點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"an explanation of the system","meaning":"對該系統的解釋","examples":[{"en":"One paragraph provides an explanation of the photovoltaic system.","zh":"其中一段提供對該光伏系統的解釋。"},{"en":"An explanation of the system tells readers how the parts work together.","zh":"An explanation of the system 告訴讀者各部分如何共同運作。"},{"en":"A diagram can give an explanation of a water-filter system by showing pipes and filters.","zh":"圖表可以透過展示水管和濾芯來解釋濾水系統。"},{"en":"If students understand the system, they can answer process questions more accurately.","zh":"如果學生理解系統，他們可以更準確回答流程題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a clear account of how something operates.","zh":"這個片語指清楚說明某物如何運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"long-term benefits","meaning":"長遠好處","examples":[{"en":"Lower bills and reduced emissions are long-term benefits of photovoltaics.","zh":"較低帳單和減少排放是光伏系統的長遠好處。"},{"en":"Long-term benefits are advantages that continue or appear over a long period.","zh":"Long-term benefits 是持續很久或長時間後出現的好處。"},{"en":"Regular exercise has long-term benefits for health, mood, and energy.","zh":"定期運動對健康、心情和精力有長遠好處。"},{"en":"If solar panels last for many years, savings can build up over time.","zh":"如果太陽能板可使用多年，節省可以隨時間累積。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lasting advantages, not quick rewards only.","zh":"這個片語描述持久優勢，而不只是即時回報。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a large campaign","meaning":"大型推廣計劃","examples":[{"en":"Japan launched a large campaign to install rooftop photovoltaics.","zh":"日本推出大型推廣計劃，以安裝天台光伏系統。"},{"en":"A large campaign is a big organised effort to persuade, support, or change behaviour.","zh":"Large campaign 是大規模、有組織地說服、支援或改變行為的行動。"},{"en":"A city may run a large campaign to encourage recycling in every district.","zh":"城市可能推行大型推廣計劃，鼓勵每區回收。"},{"en":"If a campaign is large, it needs funding, publicity, and public participation.","zh":"如果推廣計劃規模大，它需要資金、宣傳和公眾參與。"},{"en":"This phrase describes action on a wide scale.","zh":"這個片語描述大範圍行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be inspired by","meaning":"受到……啟發","examples":[{"en":"The Japanese programme was partly inspired by Germany’s successful example.","zh":"日本計劃部分受到德國成功例子的啟發。"},{"en":"To be inspired by something means to get an idea, motivation, or model from it.","zh":"To be inspired by something 指從某事中得到想法、動力或模式。"},{"en":"A student may be inspired by a senior’s success and start studying earlier.","zh":"學生可能受到師兄師姐成功啟發，開始更早溫習。"},{"en":"If one solar scheme succeeds, another country may use it as a model.","zh":"如果一個太陽能計劃成功，另一國可能把它作為模式。"},{"en":"This phrase shows where an idea or motivation comes from.","zh":"這個片語顯示想法或動力來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a successful example","meaning":"成功例子","examples":[{"en":"Germany’s rooftop scheme provided a successful example for other countries.","zh":"德國天台計劃為其他國家提供成功例子。"},{"en":"A successful example is a case that works well and can guide others.","zh":"Successful example 是運作良好並能指導其他人的個案。"},{"en":"A school with strong reading results can be a successful example for other schools.","zh":"閱讀成績好的學校可以成為其他學校的成功例子。"},{"en":"If one country proves a policy works, others may adapt it to their own needs.","zh":"如果一個國家證明政策有效，其他國家可能按自身需要改用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a model worth learning from.","zh":"這個片語描述值得學習的模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether each statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"考生判斷每項陳述是否與文章資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information means to match what the passage says.","zh":"To agree with the information 指與文章所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the passage says subsidies covered half the cost, a statement saying the same thing agrees with it.","zh":"如果文章說補貼承擔一半成本，陳述說同一件事就與資料一致。"},{"en":"If a statement changes the meaning, it does not agree even if some words are similar.","zh":"如果陳述改變意思，即使有些字相似，也不一致。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in True/False/Not Given tasks.","zh":"這個片語常見於True/False/Not Given題型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"To contradict the information 指說出與文章所說相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the text says the homes were uninhabited, a statement saying families lived there contradicts it.","zh":"如果文本說住宅無人居住，而陳述說有家庭住在那裡，它就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"When a statement contradicts the text, the answer should be false.","zh":"當陳述與文本矛盾，答案應是false。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct conflict with the source.","zh":"這個片語描述與來源直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"“Not Given” means that the passage provides no information on the point.","zh":"“Not Given” 指文章沒有提供關於該點的資料。"},{"en":"No information on this means the text does not tell us whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"No information on this 指文本沒有告訴我們該陳述是真或假。"},{"en":"If a passage names a programme but not its exact budget, there is no information on the budget.","zh":"如果文章提到一項計劃但沒有說明精確預算，預算方面就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when the passage provides no information.","zh":"當文章沒有相關資料時，學生不應使用外部知識作答。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the answer cannot be proved from the text.","zh":"這個片語表示答案不能從文本中證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be used to store electricity","meaning":"被用來儲存電力","examples":[{"en":"The grid, rather than the photovoltaic panels, is used to balance electricity supply.","zh":"電網而不是光伏板，被用來平衡電力供應。"},{"en":"To be used to store electricity means to keep electrical energy for later use.","zh":"To be used to store electricity 指保存電能供日後使用。"},{"en":"A home battery can be used to store electricity generated during the day.","zh":"家用電池可以被用來儲存日間產生的電力。"},{"en":"If electricity is stored, it can be used when sunlight is not available.","zh":"如果電力被儲存，它可以在沒有陽光時使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes saving power for later, not simply producing it.","zh":"這個片語描述保存電力供日後使用，而不只是產生電力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"provide continuous support for","meaning":"持續支持……","examples":[{"en":"A government may provide continuous support for residential solar power.","zh":"政府可能持續支持住宅太陽能。"},{"en":"To provide continuous support for something means to keep helping it over time.","zh":"To provide continuous support for something 指隨時間持續幫助某事。"},{"en":"A school provides continuous support for weak readers through weekly practice and feedback.","zh":"學校透過每週練習和回饋，持續支持閱讀能力弱的學生。"},{"en":"If support continues, households may feel safer investing in solar systems.","zh":"如果支援持續，家庭可能更放心投資太陽能系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing help rather than one-time assistance.","zh":"這個片語描述持續幫助，而不是一次性援助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"solar-powered house","meaning":"太陽能供電住宅","examples":[{"en":"The test station included simulated solar-powered houses.","zh":"測試站包括模擬太陽能供電住宅。"},{"en":"A solar-powered house is a home that uses solar energy for some or all of its electricity.","zh":"Solar-powered house 是使用太陽能供應部分或全部電力的住宅。"},{"en":"A solar-powered house may run lights and appliances from rooftop panels on sunny days.","zh":"太陽能供電住宅在晴天可能由天台太陽能板運行照明和電器。"},{"en":"If the panels produce too little power, the house may still need grid electricity.","zh":"如果太陽能板產生太少電力，住宅可能仍需要電網電力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the energy source of a home.","zh":"這個片語描述住宅的能源來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be uninhabited","meaning":"無人居住","examples":[{"en":"The dummy homes were uninhabited because they were experimental structures.","zh":"模擬住宅無人居住，因為它們是實驗結構。"},{"en":"To be uninhabited means to have no people living there.","zh":"To be uninhabited 指沒有人居住。"},{"en":"An old village may be uninhabited after residents move to the city.","zh":"居民搬到城市後，舊村莊可能無人居住。"},{"en":"If test houses are uninhabited, researchers must simulate human electricity use.","zh":"如果測試住宅無人居住，研究人員必須模擬人類用電。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place without residents.","zh":"這個片語描述沒有居民的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"provide half the money required","meaning":"提供所需款項的一半","examples":[{"en":"The government provided half the money required for early installations.","zh":"政府為早期安裝提供所需款項的一半。"},{"en":"To provide half the money required means to pay 50% of the amount needed.","zh":"To provide half the money required 指支付所需金額的50%。"},{"en":"Parents may provide half the money required for a school trip, while the school pays the rest.","zh":"家長可能提供學校旅行所需款項的一半，而學校支付餘下部分。"},{"en":"If the government pays half, the household’s financial burden becomes smaller.","zh":"如果政府支付一半，家庭財政負擔就變小。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sharing the required cost equally.","zh":"這個片語描述平均分擔所需成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"with regard to","meaning":"關於；在……方面","examples":[{"en":"The statement concerns national targets with regard to greenhouse gases.","zh":"該陳述關於溫室氣體方面的國家目標。"},{"en":"With regard to means about or concerning a particular subject.","zh":"With regard to 指關於某特定主題。"},{"en":"With regard to homework, students want clearer deadlines and shorter tasks.","zh":"關於功課，學生希望有更清晰截止日期和較短任務。"},{"en":"If a law changes with regard to emissions, companies may need new equipment.","zh":"如果法律在排放方面改變，公司可能需要新設備。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the topic being discussed.","zh":"這個片語引出正在討論的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"strict emissions goals","meaning":"嚴格排放目標","examples":[{"en":"Some governments have introduced strict emissions goals.","zh":"一些政府已引入嚴格排放目標。"},{"en":"Strict emissions goals are firm targets for reducing the amount of pollution released.","zh":"Strict emissions goals 是減少污染物釋放量的堅定目標。"},{"en":"A factory may need new filters to meet strict emissions goals.","zh":"工廠可能需要新過濾器來符合嚴格排放目標。"},{"en":"If goals are strict, old equipment may no longer be acceptable.","zh":"如果目標嚴格，舊設備可能不再可接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes demanding pollution-reduction targets.","zh":"這個片語描述高要求的減排目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the major source of","meaning":"……的主要來源","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether household electricity is the major source of greenhouse gases.","zh":"該陳述詢問家庭用電是否是溫室氣體的主要來源。"},{"en":"The major source of something is the largest or most important origin of it.","zh":"The major source of something 是某事物最大或最重要的來源。"},{"en":"In a classroom, noise from group work may be the major source of distraction.","zh":"在課室中，小組活動的噪音可能是分心的主要來源。"},{"en":"If one sector is the major source of emissions, policies may focus there first.","zh":"如果某行業是排放的主要來源，政策可能先集中於該處。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main origin of a problem or supply.","zh":"這個片語指出問題或供應的主要來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be included in the design of","meaning":"被納入……的設計","examples":[{"en":"Energy-saving measures may be included in the design of new homes.","zh":"節能措施可能被納入新住宅的設計。"},{"en":"To be included in the design of something means to be planned as part of it from the beginning.","zh":"To be included in the design of something 指從一開始就被規劃為其中一部分。"},{"en":"Ramps should be included in the design of public buildings so wheelchair users can enter easily.","zh":"斜道應被納入公共建築設計，讓輪椅使用者容易進入。"},{"en":"If solar panels are included in the design, installation may be cheaper and neater.","zh":"如果太陽能板被納入設計，安裝可能更便宜和更整齊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planning a feature into a project.","zh":"這個片語描述把某特徵規劃進項目之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"improvements to buildings","meaning":"樓宇改善工程","examples":[{"en":"Future regulations may affect both new homes and improvements to buildings.","zh":"未來規例可能影響新住宅和樓宇改善工程。"},{"en":"Improvements to buildings are changes that make buildings safer, more efficient, or more useful.","zh":"Improvements to buildings 是令建築物更安全、更高效或更有用的改動。"},{"en":"Adding insulation, repairing windows, and upgrading wiring are improvements to buildings.","zh":"加裝隔熱、維修窗戶和升級電線都是樓宇改善工程。"},{"en":"If building improvements save energy, residents may pay lower bills.","zh":"如果樓宇改善工程節省能源，居民可能支付較低帳單。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to upgrading existing buildings, not building new ones only.","zh":"這個片語指升級現有建築物，而不只是建造新建築。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 149 - Photovoltaics on the rooftop.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 150":[{"front":"the persuaders","meaning":"說服大眾的人","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines how professional persuaders influence consumers.","zh":"文章探討專業說服者如何影響消費者。"},{"en":"The persuaders are people or organisations that try to change what others think, feel, or buy.","zh":"說服大眾的人是指試圖改變別人想法、感受或購買行為的人或機構。"},{"en":"Advertisers, salespeople, politicians and influencers can all act as persuaders.","zh":"廣告商、銷售員、政治人物和網紅都可以充當說服大眾的人。"},{"en":"Persuaders use words, images, emotions and social pressure to shape people’s decisions.","zh":"說服者利用文字、影像、情緒和社會壓力來塑造人們的決定。"},{"en":"Good readers should notice what persuaders are trying to make them believe or do.","zh":"優秀讀者應留意說服者正試圖令人相信甚麼或做甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have long lived in an age where","meaning":"長久以來一直生活在……的時代","examples":[{"en":"We have long lived in an age where persuasive messages surround us.","zh":"我們長久以來一直生活在充滿說服性訊息的時代。"},{"en":"To have long lived in an age where something happens means that this situation has existed for many years.","zh":"have long lived in an age where something happens 指某種情況已經存在很多年。"},{"en":"We have long lived in an age where students use phones for learning, shopping and entertainment.","zh":"我們長久以來一直生活在學生用手機學習、購物和娛樂的時代。"},{"en":"If people have long lived in an age where advertising is everywhere, they may stop noticing it.","zh":"如果人們長久以來一直生活在廣告無處不在的時代，他們可能不再察覺廣告。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a long-lasting modern condition, not a sudden change.","zh":"這個短語描述長期存在的現代狀況，而不是突然變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"powerful images","meaning":"具強大感染力的影像","examples":[{"en":"Advertisers use powerful images to attract attention.","zh":"廣告商使用具強大感染力的影像來吸引注意。"},{"en":"Powerful images are pictures that strongly affect people’s feelings, memory or imagination.","zh":"powerful images 指強烈影響人們感受、記憶或想像的圖片。"},{"en":"A charity may use powerful images of homeless families to make viewers care.","zh":"慈善機構可能使用無家者家庭的強烈影像，令人關心。"},{"en":"Powerful images can make a message easier to remember than plain words.","zh":"具強大感染力的影像可以令訊息比普通文字更易被記住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes images with emotional or persuasive force.","zh":"這個短語描述具有情感或說服力量的影像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"catchy soundbites","meaning":"朗朗上口的簡短口號","examples":[{"en":"Politicians often rely on catchy soundbites.","zh":"政治人物常依賴朗朗上口的簡短口號。"},{"en":"Catchy soundbites are short, memorable phrases designed to be repeated easily.","zh":"catchy soundbites 指設計得短小、易記、容易重複的句子。"},{"en":"A school campaign may use a catchy soundbite like “Read more, dream more.”","zh":"學校活動可能使用 “Read more, dream more.” 這類朗朗上口的簡短口號。"},{"en":"Catchy soundbites help messages spread quickly because people can remember and quote them.","zh":"朗朗上口的口號幫助訊息快速傳播，因為人們能記住並引用它們。"},{"en":"This phrase often refers to slogans that are simple, attractive and easy to repeat.","zh":"這個短語常指簡單、吸引、容易重複的標語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"too-good-to-miss offers","meaning":"看似不容錯過的優惠","examples":[{"en":"Shoppers are frequently presented with too-good-to-miss offers.","zh":"購物者經常看到看似不容錯過的優惠。"},{"en":"Too-good-to-miss offers are deals that seem so attractive that customers feel they should not refuse them.","zh":"too-good-to-miss offers 指看起來非常吸引，以致顧客覺得不應拒絕的優惠。"},{"en":"A shop may advertise a “buy one, get one free” deal as a too-good-to-miss offer.","zh":"商店可能把「買一送一」宣傳成看似不容錯過的優惠。"},{"en":"Such offers can make people buy quickly before thinking carefully about whether they need the product.","zh":"這類優惠可以令人未仔細思考是否需要產品前就快速購買。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests urgency and temptation.","zh":"這個短語常暗示迫切感和誘惑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"bombard someone from every quarter","meaning":"從四方八面轟炸某人","examples":[{"en":"Advertising messages bombard us from every quarter.","zh":"廣告訊息從四方八面轟炸我們。"},{"en":"To bombard someone from every quarter means to attack or overwhelm them with messages from many directions.","zh":"bombard someone from every quarter 指訊息從許多方向攻向或壓倒某人。"},{"en":"Students may feel bombarded from every quarter when teachers, parents and apps all remind them to study.","zh":"當老師、家長和應用程式都提醒學生溫習，學生可能感到被四方八面轟炸。"},{"en":"When messages bombard people from every quarter, they may feel tired or pressured.","zh":"當訊息從四方八面轟炸人們，他們可能感到疲累或有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated pressure coming from many sources at once.","zh":"這個短語描述來自多個來源的反覆壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be at work","meaning":"正在發揮作用","examples":[{"en":"All around us, professional persuaders are at work.","zh":"在我們四周，專業說服者正在發揮作用。"},{"en":"To be at work means to be actively operating or influencing a situation.","zh":"be at work 指正在積極運作或影響某情況。"},{"en":"In a busy shop, marketing is at work when music, signs and discounts guide customers.","zh":"在繁忙商店中，音樂、標誌和折扣引導顧客時，市場推廣正在發揮作用。"},{"en":"Hidden forces can be at work even when people do not notice them.","zh":"即使人們沒有注意到，隱藏力量也可能正在發揮作用。"},{"en":"This phrase often means something is quietly producing an effect.","zh":"這個短語常表示某事正悄悄產生效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"unsubtle methods","meaning":"不含蓄的手法","examples":[{"en":"Some persuaders use obvious and unsubtle methods.","zh":"有些說服者使用明顯而不含蓄的手法。"},{"en":"Unsubtle methods are direct, obvious methods that do not hide their purpose.","zh":"unsubtle methods 指直接、明顯、不隱藏目的的方法。"},{"en":"A shop assistant uses an unsubtle method if he repeatedly says, “Buy this now.”","zh":"如果店員反覆說「現在買這個」，就是使用不含蓄的手法。"},{"en":"Unsubtle methods may attract attention, but they can also annoy people.","zh":"不含蓄的手法可能吸引注意，但也可能令人反感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes persuasion that is not delicate or hidden.","zh":"這個短語描述不細膩、不隱藏的說服方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"plant a kiss on","meaning":"親吻……","examples":[{"en":"A political candidate may plant a kiss on a baby’s head for publicity.","zh":"政治候選人可能為了宣傳而親吻嬰兒的頭。"},{"en":"To plant a kiss on someone means to kiss them deliberately, often in a visible or dramatic way.","zh":"plant a kiss on someone 指有意地親吻某人，通常是明顯或帶戲劇性的方式。"},{"en":"A grandmother may plant a kiss on a child’s forehead before school.","zh":"祖母可能在孩子上學前親吻他的額頭。"},{"en":"In public life, planting a kiss on someone can be used to create a warm image.","zh":"在公共生活中，親吻某人可以用來塑造溫暖形象。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds more deliberate than simply “kiss”.","zh":"這個短語比單純的 “kiss” 聽起來更刻意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"wannabe political leader","meaning":"想要上位的政治領袖","examples":[{"en":"A wannabe political leader may carefully manage their public image.","zh":"想要上位的政治領袖可能會仔細管理自己的公眾形象。"},{"en":"A wannabe political leader is someone who wants to become a political leader but has not yet achieved that status.","zh":"wannabe political leader 指想成為政治領袖但尚未達到該地位的人。"},{"en":"A wannabe political leader may attend every community event to become more visible.","zh":"想要上位的政治人物可能參加每個社區活動，以提高曝光。"},{"en":"Wanting power can make such a person copy the behaviour of successful politicians.","zh":"對權力的渴望可能令這類人模仿成功政治人物的行為。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound slightly critical because “wannabe” suggests ambition without achievement.","zh":"這個短語可能帶一點批評意味，因為 “wannabe” 暗示有野心但未有成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"liquidation sale","meaning":"清貨大減價","examples":[{"en":"The shop advertised a liquidation sale for more than a year.","zh":"該店宣傳清貨大減價超過一年。"},{"en":"A liquidation sale is a sale where a business sells off goods, often because it is closing or clearing stock.","zh":"liquidation sale 指企業售清貨品的減價活動，通常因結業或清理存貨。"},{"en":"A furniture shop may hold a liquidation sale before moving out of a mall.","zh":"家具店搬離商場前可能舉行清貨大減價。"},{"en":"Liquidation sales attract buyers because people expect unusually low prices.","zh":"清貨大減價吸引買家，因為人們預期價格特別低。"},{"en":"This phrase can also be used as a marketing trick if the shop is not really closing.","zh":"如果商店不是真的結業，這個短語也可能成為市場推廣花招。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"close down","meaning":"結業；停業","examples":[{"en":"The shop claimed that it was closing down.","zh":"該店聲稱快要結業。"},{"en":"To close down means to stop operating permanently or for a long period.","zh":"close down 指永久或長期停止營運。"},{"en":"A small café may close down if rent rises and customers decrease.","zh":"如果租金上升而顧客減少，小咖啡店可能結業。"},{"en":"When a business closes down, workers may lose jobs and customers must go elsewhere.","zh":"當企業結業，員工可能失業，顧客亦要到別處消費。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than “close for the day”.","zh":"這個短語比「當天關門」意思更強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"know what they are about","meaning":"很清楚自己在做甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Professional advertisers know exactly what they are about.","zh":"專業廣告人很清楚自己在做甚麼。"},{"en":"To know what one is about means to understand one’s purpose, method and goal clearly.","zh":"know what one is about 指清楚理解自己的目的、方法和目標。"},{"en":"A good teacher knows what she is about when every activity supports the lesson aim.","zh":"如果每項活動都支援課堂目標，好老師就是很清楚自己在做甚麼。"},{"en":"People who know what they are about act confidently because they understand what they want to achieve.","zh":"很清楚自己在做甚麼的人行動有信心，因為他們明白自己想達成甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests competence, focus and clear intention.","zh":"這個短語暗示能力、專注和清晰意圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"highly capable","meaning":"能力很高的","examples":[{"en":"The most successful persuaders are highly capable.","zh":"最成功的說服者能力很高。"},{"en":"Highly capable means very skilled and able to do something well.","zh":"highly capable 指很有技巧，能把某事做好。"},{"en":"A highly capable nurse can stay calm, organise tasks and comfort patients.","zh":"能力很高的護士能保持冷靜、安排工作並安慰病人。"},{"en":"Highly capable people often make difficult work look simple because they have strong skills.","zh":"能力很高的人常把困難工作做得看似簡單，因為他們技巧強。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to praise ability and effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語用來讚揚能力和成效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be they … or …","meaning":"無論是……還是……","examples":[{"en":"Be they politicians or advertisers, persuaders use similar techniques.","zh":"無論是政治人物還是廣告人，說服者都使用相似技巧。"},{"en":"Be they A or B means whether they are A or B.","zh":"be they A or B 指無論他們是 A 還是 B。"},{"en":"Be they teachers or parents, adults should explain rules clearly to children.","zh":"無論是老師還是家長，成年人都應向孩子清楚解釋規則。"},{"en":"This structure groups different people together because the same point applies to all of them.","zh":"這個結構把不同人歸在一起，因為同一論點適用於所有人。"},{"en":"It is a formal way to say “whether they are…or…”.","zh":"這是 “whether they are…or…” 的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"supermarket chains","meaning":"連鎖超級市場","examples":[{"en":"Large supermarket chains invest heavily in marketing.","zh":"大型連鎖超級市場在市場推廣上投入大量資金。"},{"en":"Supermarket chains are groups of supermarkets with the same name and owner.","zh":"supermarket chains 指同名且同一擁有者的一組超級市場。"},{"en":"A supermarket chain may have branches in many districts of the same city.","zh":"連鎖超級市場可能在同一城市多個地區都有分店。"},{"en":"Large chains can collect customer data and design promotions across many stores.","zh":"大型連鎖店可以收集顧客數據，並在多間分店設計促銷。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to linked shops, not one independent grocery store.","zh":"這個短語指互相關連的店舖，而不是單一獨立雜貨店。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"know exactly what to do","meaning":"很清楚應該怎樣做","examples":[{"en":"Advertisers know exactly what to do to influence consumers.","zh":"廣告商很清楚應該怎樣做才能影響消費者。"},{"en":"To know exactly what to do means to understand the correct action clearly.","zh":"know exactly what to do 指清楚知道正確行動是甚麼。"},{"en":"An experienced doctor knows exactly what to do when a patient shows warning signs.","zh":"有經驗的醫生在病人出現警號時，很清楚應該怎樣做。"},{"en":"People who know exactly what to do can act quickly and confidently.","zh":"很清楚應該怎樣做的人能快速而有信心地行動。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests certainty, experience and control.","zh":"這個短語暗示確定、經驗和掌控。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sell someone an idea","meaning":"向某人推銷一個概念","examples":[{"en":"Political campaigns try to sell voters an idea or image.","zh":"政治宣傳活動試圖向選民推銷一個概念或形象。"},{"en":"To sell someone an idea means to persuade them to accept or support that idea.","zh":"sell someone an idea 指說服某人接受或支持某想法。"},{"en":"A student may try to sell classmates an idea for a charity project.","zh":"學生可能嘗試向同學推銷一個慈善項目的概念。"},{"en":"People sell ideas by showing benefits, reducing doubts and creating excitement.","zh":"人們透過展示好處、減少疑慮和創造興奮感來推銷想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is about persuasion, not only selling a physical product.","zh":"這個短語關於說服，不只是售賣實體產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"when it comes to","meaning":"說到……；在……方面","examples":[{"en":"When it comes to persuasion, large companies have a major advantage.","zh":"說到說服，大公司有重大優勢。"},{"en":"When it comes to something means when discussing or dealing with that subject.","zh":"when it comes to something 指在討論或處理某主題時。"},{"en":"When it comes to exams, regular practice is more useful than panic revision.","zh":"說到考試，定期練習比恐慌式溫習更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows the discussion to one particular topic.","zh":"這個短語把討論收窄到某個特定主題。"},{"en":"It is often used before giving an opinion or comparison about a specific area.","zh":"它常用於就某個特定範疇提出意見或比較前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rule supreme","meaning":"佔據絕對優勢","examples":[{"en":"The largest persuaders rule supreme in the advertising world.","zh":"最大型說服者在廣告世界中佔據絕對優勢。"},{"en":"To rule supreme means to dominate completely or have the greatest power in an area.","zh":"rule supreme 指在某範疇完全主導或擁有最大力量。"},{"en":"In a small town, one popular bakery may rule supreme because everyone buys bread there.","zh":"在小鎮中，一間受歡迎麵包店可能佔據絕對優勢，因為人人都在那裡買麵包。"},{"en":"A company can rule supreme when it has more money, data and influence than competitors.","zh":"當公司比競爭者有更多資金、數據和影響力，就可能佔據絕對優勢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clear dominance.","zh":"這個短語描述明顯主導地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"employ skilled image-makers","meaning":"聘用專業形象設計師","examples":[{"en":"Political parties employ skilled image-makers.","zh":"政黨聘用專業形象設計師。"},{"en":"To employ skilled image-makers means to hire experts who shape how a person or organisation appears to the public.","zh":"employ skilled image-makers 指聘請專家塑造某人或組織在公眾眼中的形象。"},{"en":"A celebrity may employ skilled image-makers before launching a new album.","zh":"名人推出新專輯前可能聘用專業形象設計師。"},{"en":"Image-makers can choose clothes, photos, speeches and events to create a desired impression.","zh":"形象設計師可以選擇服裝、照片、演講和活動來營造理想印象。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that public image is often professionally managed.","zh":"這個短語顯示公眾形象常由專業人士管理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"psychological tricks","meaning":"心理技巧","examples":[{"en":"Advertisers use psychological tricks to influence buyers.","zh":"廣告商使用心理技巧來影響買家。"},{"en":"Psychological tricks are methods that use how people think or feel to change their behaviour.","zh":"psychological tricks 指利用人們如何思考或感受來改變行為的方法。"},{"en":"A shop uses a psychological trick when it prices an item at $99 instead of $100.","zh":"商店把商品定價為 99 元而不是 100 元時，就是使用心理技巧。"},{"en":"These tricks work because people do not always make decisions logically.","zh":"這些技巧有效，因為人們不總是理性地作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests hidden techniques that affect the mind.","zh":"這個短語暗示影響心理的隱藏手法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"guarantee that","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Marketing techniques cannot guarantee that every customer will buy.","zh":"市場推廣技巧不能確保每位顧客都會購買。"},{"en":"To guarantee that something will happen means to make certain that it will happen.","zh":"guarantee that something will happen 指確保某事一定會發生。"},{"en":"A high mark in one quiz does not guarantee that a student will do well in the final exam.","zh":"一次小測高分不會確保學生在期末考試中表現好。"},{"en":"Advertising can increase interest, but it cannot guarantee a sale every time.","zh":"廣告可以增加興趣，但不能每次都確保成交。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing certainty or lack of certainty.","zh":"這個短語用於討論確定或不確定時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the most cautious among us","meaning":"我們當中最謹慎的人","examples":[{"en":"Even the most cautious among us can be influenced.","zh":"即使我們當中最謹慎的人也可能受到影響。"},{"en":"The most cautious among us means the people in our group who are most careful and least easily fooled.","zh":"the most cautious among us 指我們群體中最小心、最不容易受騙的人。"},{"en":"Even the most cautious among us may click on a fake email if it looks official.","zh":"即使我們當中最謹慎的人，如果假電郵看起來正式，也可能點擊。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that careful people are not completely safe from influence.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者，小心的人也不會完全免受影響。"},{"en":"It is often used to show that a problem affects everyone.","zh":"它常用來顯示某問題影響所有人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be open to manipulation","meaning":"容易受到操控","examples":[{"en":"Consumers may be more open to manipulation than they realise.","zh":"消費者可能比自己意識到的更容易受到操控。"},{"en":"To be open to manipulation means to be vulnerable to being controlled or influenced unfairly.","zh":"be open to manipulation 指容易被不公平地控制或影響。"},{"en":"Tired shoppers may be open to manipulation when bright signs promise huge savings.","zh":"疲倦購物者看到鮮明標誌承諾大減價時，可能容易受到操控。"},{"en":"People become easier to manipulate when they are rushed, emotional or lacking information.","zh":"當人們匆忙、情緒化或缺乏資訊時，就更容易被操控。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that influence may happen without full awareness.","zh":"這個短語提醒影響可能在未完全察覺下發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"spend more time than intended","meaning":"花費比原定更多時間","examples":[{"en":"Shoppers often spend more time in supermarkets than intended.","zh":"購物者常在超級市場花費比原定更多時間。"},{"en":"To spend more time than intended means to stay longer than originally planned.","zh":"spend more time than intended 指停留時間比原本計劃更長。"},{"en":"A student may spend more time than intended on social media before starting homework.","zh":"學生開始做功課前可能在社交媒體上花費比原定更多時間。"},{"en":"If a shop is pleasant and easy to browse, customers may stay longer than planned.","zh":"如果商店舒適又容易瀏覽，顧客可能停留得比原定更久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gap between a plan and actual behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述計劃與實際行為之間的差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"end up with","meaning":"最終得到；結果買了","examples":[{"en":"Customers often end up with products they had not planned to buy.","zh":"顧客常結果買了原本沒有計劃購買的產品。"},{"en":"To end up with something means to finally have it, often unexpectedly.","zh":"end up with something 指最終擁有某物，常常是出乎意料地。"},{"en":"A family may go shopping for milk and end up with snacks, magazines and toys.","zh":"一家人可能原本去買牛奶，結果買了零食、雜誌和玩具。"},{"en":"Clever store design can make shoppers end up with more items than they expected.","zh":"聰明店舖設計可以令購物者最終買到比預期更多貨品。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests an unplanned result.","zh":"這個短語常暗示非計劃中的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"realise we wanted","meaning":"意識到自己想要","examples":[{"en":"We sometimes buy products that we did not realise we wanted.","zh":"我們有時會購買自己原本沒有意識到想要的產品。"},{"en":"To realise we wanted something means to become aware that we desire it.","zh":"realise we wanted something 指開始意識到自己渴望某物。"},{"en":"A student may not realise they wanted a quiet study lamp until they see one on sale.","zh":"學生可能直到看到安靜讀書燈特價，才意識到自己想要它。"},{"en":"Advertising can make people notice desires they had not thought about before.","zh":"廣告可以令人注意到以前沒有想過的慾望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming aware of a hidden or newly created want.","zh":"這個短語描述意識到隱藏或新產生的需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"right from the start","meaning":"從一開始","examples":[{"en":"Right from the start, supermarkets have used advanced marketing methods.","zh":"從一開始，超級市場就使用先進市場推廣方法。"},{"en":"Right from the start means from the very beginning.","zh":"right from the start 指從最初一刻開始。"},{"en":"A good teacher explains expectations right from the start of the course.","zh":"好老師從課程一開始就解釋要求。"},{"en":"If a business uses data right from the start, its planning may become more precise.","zh":"如果企業從一開始就使用數據，規劃可能更精準。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that something began immediately, not later.","zh":"這個短語強調某事是立即開始，而不是後來才開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ahead of the game","meaning":"領先一步","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets have long been ahead of the game in consumer psychology.","zh":"超級市場長期在消費者心理方面領先一步。"},{"en":"To be ahead of the game means to be more advanced or better prepared than others.","zh":"be ahead of the game 指比其他人更先進或準備更充分。"},{"en":"A student is ahead of the game if they revise every week instead of waiting until the exam.","zh":"如果學生每星期溫習而不是等到考試前，就領先一步。"},{"en":"Businesses stay ahead of the game by understanding customers before competitors do.","zh":"企業透過比競爭者更早理解顧客來保持領先。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an advantage gained through preparation or intelligence.","zh":"這個短語暗示透過準備或智慧取得優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"introduce shopping baskets","meaning":"引入購物籃","examples":[{"en":"Sainsbury introduced shopping baskets into its stores.","zh":"Sainsbury 在店內引入購物籃。"},{"en":"To introduce shopping baskets means to start providing baskets for customers to carry goods.","zh":"introduce shopping baskets 指開始提供購物籃，讓顧客攜帶貨品。"},{"en":"A small bookstore may introduce shopping baskets so readers can carry several books easily.","zh":"小型書店可能引入購物籃，讓讀者容易攜帶多本書。"},{"en":"Baskets can encourage customers to pick up more items because carrying becomes easier.","zh":"購物籃可以鼓勵顧客拿起更多貨品，因為攜帶變得更方便。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding a simple tool that changes shopping behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述加入一種改變購物行為的簡單工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a stroke of marketing genius","meaning":"市場推廣上的天才之舉","examples":[{"en":"The shopping basket was a stroke of marketing genius.","zh":"購物籃是市場推廣上的天才之舉。"},{"en":"A stroke of marketing genius is a very clever marketing idea that produces strong results.","zh":"stroke of marketing genius 指非常聰明、能產生強大效果的市場推廣想法。"},{"en":"Offering free samples near the entrance can be a stroke of marketing genius if it makes shoppers buy more.","zh":"如果入口附近提供免費試食能令顧客買更多，就可以是市場推廣上的天才之舉。"},{"en":"Simple ideas can become marketing genius when they quietly change customer behaviour.","zh":"當簡單想法悄悄改變顧客行為，就可以成為市場推廣天才之舉。"},{"en":"This phrase praises a clever commercial move.","zh":"這個短語讚揚聰明的商業行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"browse","meaning":"隨意瀏覽貨品","examples":[{"en":"Shopping baskets encouraged customers to browse for longer.","zh":"購物籃鼓勵顧客更長時間隨意瀏覽貨品。"},{"en":"To browse means to look casually at goods, websites or books without a fixed plan.","zh":"browse 指沒有固定計劃地隨意看看商品、網站或書籍。"},{"en":"A student may browse in a bookstore before choosing a novel.","zh":"學生可能在書店隨意瀏覽，然後選一本小說。"},{"en":"Browsing can lead to unplanned purchases because people notice things they did not seek.","zh":"隨意瀏覽可能導致非計劃購買，因為人們會注意到原本沒有尋找的東西。"},{"en":"This word describes relaxed looking rather than urgent searching.","zh":"這個詞描述輕鬆觀看，而不是急切搜尋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pick up items","meaning":"拿起；選購貨品","examples":[{"en":"Customers could pick up items while walking through the store.","zh":"顧客可以在店內行走時拿起貨品。"},{"en":"To pick up items means to take goods from shelves, often while shopping.","zh":"pick up items 指從貨架拿取商品，通常是在購物時。"},{"en":"A parent may pick up items for dinner on the way home from work.","zh":"家長下班回家途中可能選購晚餐所需貨品。"},{"en":"If baskets make it easy to pick up items, customers may buy more than planned.","zh":"如果購物籃令拿取貨品變得容易，顧客可能買得比計劃更多。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean choosing goods, not just lifting objects.","zh":"這個短語可以指選購貨品，而不只是舉起物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"previously ignored","meaning":"以前忽略的","examples":[{"en":"Shoppers began buying items they had previously ignored.","zh":"購物者開始購買以前忽略的貨品。"},{"en":"Previously ignored means not noticed or considered before.","zh":"previously ignored 指以前沒有注意或考慮的。"},{"en":"A student may discover a useful grammar book that they had previously ignored on the shelf.","zh":"學生可能發現架上一本文法書很有用，而那本書以前被他忽略了。"},{"en":"Better display can make customers notice products they previously ignored.","zh":"更好的陳列可以令顧客注意到以前忽略的產品。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that attention has changed over time.","zh":"這個短語顯示注意力隨時間改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"soon after came","meaning":"不久之後便出現……","examples":[{"en":"Soon after came the introduction of shopping trolleys.","zh":"不久之後便出現購物車的引入。"},{"en":"Soon after came something means that another development happened shortly afterwards.","zh":"soon after came something 指另一項發展在不久之後發生。"},{"en":"The school first introduced online homework; soon after came digital report cards.","zh":"學校先引入網上功課；不久之後便出現電子成績表。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to show a sequence of related changes.","zh":"這個短語常用來顯示一連串相關變化。"},{"en":"It sounds slightly formal and places the new development after an earlier one.","zh":"它語氣稍正式，並把新發展放在較早事件之後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"attract more traffic","meaning":"吸引更多交通流量","examples":[{"en":"New roads often attract more traffic.","zh":"新道路常吸引更多交通流量。"},{"en":"To attract more traffic means to bring in more vehicles, visitors or users.","zh":"attract more traffic 指帶來更多車輛、訪客或使用者。"},{"en":"A new shopping mall may attract more traffic to a quiet neighbourhood.","zh":"新商場可能為安靜社區吸引更多人流和車流。"},{"en":"More capacity can sometimes create more demand instead of reducing pressure.","zh":"更多容量有時會創造更多需求，而不是減少壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe roads, websites, shops or events.","zh":"這個短語可以描述道路、網站、店舖或活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the same applies to","meaning":"同樣道理適用於……","examples":[{"en":"The same principle applies to the amount of space in a trolley.","zh":"同樣道理適用於購物車的容量。"},{"en":"The same applies to something means the same idea is also true for that thing.","zh":"the same applies to something 指同一想法也適用於某事物。"},{"en":"Students need rest before exams; the same applies to teachers during busy marking periods.","zh":"學生考試前需要休息；同樣道理適用於繁忙改卷期的老師。"},{"en":"This phrase connects one example to another by showing they follow the same logic.","zh":"這個短語透過顯示兩者遵循同一邏輯，把一個例子連接到另一個例子。"},{"en":"It is useful when extending an argument.","zh":"當要延伸論點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"trolley space","meaning":"購物車容量","examples":[{"en":"More trolley space can encourage customers to buy more.","zh":"更多購物車容量可以鼓勵顧客買更多。"},{"en":"Trolley space is the amount of room available inside a shopping trolley.","zh":"trolley space 指購物車內可用的空間大小。"},{"en":"A parent may choose a larger trolley space when buying groceries for the whole week.","zh":"家長為全星期購買雜貨時，可能選擇容量較大的購物車。"},{"en":"If the trolley looks empty, shoppers may feel they have not bought enough yet.","zh":"如果購物車看起來空空如也，購物者可能覺得自己還未買夠。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to carrying capacity inside a shopping cart.","zh":"這個短語指購物車內部的承載容量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"relationship marketing","meaning":"關係營銷","examples":[{"en":"Relationship marketing aims to develop long-term customer loyalty.","zh":"關係營銷旨在培養長期顧客忠誠度。"},{"en":"Relationship marketing is marketing that focuses on building continuing relationships with customers.","zh":"relationship marketing 指著重與顧客建立持續關係的市場推廣。"},{"en":"A coffee shop uses relationship marketing when it remembers regular customers’ favourite drinks.","zh":"咖啡店記得常客最喜歡的飲品時，就是使用關係營銷。"},{"en":"Strong relationships can make customers return even when prices are slightly higher.","zh":"強關係可以令顧客即使價格稍高仍然回來。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on loyalty, not just one-time sales.","zh":"這個短語著重忠誠度，而不只是一次性銷售。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"aisles are laid out","meaning":"通道被安排佈局","examples":[{"en":"Supermarket aisles are laid out to maximise profits.","zh":"超級市場通道被安排佈局，以將利潤最大化。"},{"en":"When aisles are laid out, the shop arranges its walkways and shelves in a planned way.","zh":"aisles are laid out 指店舖以有計劃方式安排通道和貨架。"},{"en":"A bookstore may lay out aisles so bestsellers are easy to find.","zh":"書店可能安排通道，使暢銷書容易被找到。"},{"en":"Aisle layout affects what customers see, where they walk and how long they stay.","zh":"通道佈局影響顧客看見甚麼、走到哪裡和停留多久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planned store arrangement.","zh":"這個短語描述有計劃的店舖安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"maximise profits","meaning":"將利潤最大化","examples":[{"en":"Stores arrange products carefully to maximise profits.","zh":"商店仔細安排產品，以將利潤最大化。"},{"en":"To maximise profits means to make the greatest possible amount of money after costs.","zh":"maximise profits 指在扣除成本後賺取盡可能多的金錢。"},{"en":"A restaurant may maximise profits by reducing food waste and selling popular dishes.","zh":"餐廳可能透過減少食物浪費和銷售受歡迎菜式來將利潤最大化。"},{"en":"Businesses often change prices, displays and services to maximise profits.","zh":"企業常改變價格、陳列和服務來將利潤最大化。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on increasing financial gain as much as possible.","zh":"這個短語著重盡可能增加財務收益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pander to","meaning":"迎合……","examples":[{"en":"Stores pander to consumers’ desire for convenience.","zh":"商店迎合消費者對便利的渴望。"},{"en":"To pander to someone’s desire means to satisfy it, often in a way that encourages weakness or easy choices.","zh":"pander to someone’s desire 指滿足某人的渴望，常帶有鼓勵弱點或容易選擇的意味。"},{"en":"A snack shop may pander to students’ love of sugar by placing sweets near the counter.","zh":"小食店可能把糖果放在收銀處附近，迎合學生對甜食的喜愛。"},{"en":"Businesses pander to customers when they make buying easier, faster or more tempting.","zh":"企業令購買更容易、更快或更誘人時，就是在迎合顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound slightly critical because it suggests calculated pleasing.","zh":"這個短語可帶一點批評意味，因為它暗示有計算地討好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"money-rich, time-poor lifestyle","meaning":"有錢但缺乏時間的生活模式","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets cater for a money-rich, time-poor lifestyle.","zh":"超級市場迎合有錢但缺乏時間的生活模式。"},{"en":"A money-rich, time-poor lifestyle describes people who have money to spend but little free time.","zh":"money-rich, time-poor lifestyle 指人們有錢消費，但空閒時間很少的生活模式。"},{"en":"Busy office workers may choose ready meals because they live a money-rich, time-poor lifestyle.","zh":"繁忙辦公室員工可能選擇即食餐，因為他們過着有錢但缺乏時間的生活。"},{"en":"This lifestyle creates demand for convenience, delivery and prepared food.","zh":"這種生活模式創造對便利、送貨和預製食品的需求。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why people may pay more to save time.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何人們可能願意付更多錢來節省時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"low-turnover products","meaning":"銷量較低的產品","examples":[{"en":"Low-turnover products are often placed at the back of a shop.","zh":"銷量較低的產品常被放在店舖後方。"},{"en":"Low-turnover products are items that sell slowly or are bought less frequently.","zh":"low-turnover products 指銷售較慢或較少被購買的商品。"},{"en":"Expensive kitchen machines may be low-turnover products because customers do not buy them often.","zh":"昂貴廚房機器可能是銷量較低的產品，因為顧客不常購買。"},{"en":"Shops may place low-turnover products farther inside so customers pass other goods first.","zh":"商店可能把低銷量產品放得更深入，讓顧客先經過其他貨品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes products with slower sales movement.","zh":"這個短語描述銷售流動較慢的產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"electrical goods","meaning":"電器產品","examples":[{"en":"Clothes and electrical goods may be stocked away from the entrance.","zh":"衣服和電器產品可能被放在遠離入口的位置。"},{"en":"Electrical goods are products that use electricity, such as kettles, fans, phones or televisions.","zh":"electrical goods 指使用電力的產品，例如電熱水壺、風扇、手機或電視。"},{"en":"A family may compare prices before buying electrical goods because they can be expensive.","zh":"家庭購買電器產品前可能比較價格，因為它們可以很昂貴。"},{"en":"Shops may place electrical goods deep inside so customers walk past many displays.","zh":"商店可能把電器產品放在店內深處，讓顧客經過許多陳列。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to electronic or electric household products.","zh":"這個短語指電子或電動家居產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be stocked at the back","meaning":"被放在店舖後方","examples":[{"en":"Low-turnover items are stocked at the back of the store.","zh":"銷量較低的貨品被放在店舖後方。"},{"en":"To be stocked at the back means to be placed for sale in the rear part of a shop.","zh":"be stocked at the back 指被放在店舖後部供出售。"},{"en":"A supermarket may stock large bags of rice at the back so customers walk through several aisles.","zh":"超級市場可能把大袋米放在後方，讓顧客走過幾條通道。"},{"en":"Items stocked at the back can increase customer exposure to other products.","zh":"被放在後方的貨品可以增加顧客接觸其他產品的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a deliberate product-location strategy.","zh":"這個短語描述刻意的商品位置策略。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"high-turnover items","meaning":"銷量高的貨品","examples":[{"en":"High-turnover items are usually easier to access.","zh":"銷量高的貨品通常較容易取得。"},{"en":"High-turnover items are products that sell quickly and are replaced often.","zh":"high-turnover items 指銷售快、經常補貨的產品。"},{"en":"Bread, milk and eggs are high-turnover items in many supermarkets.","zh":"麵包、牛奶和雞蛋是許多超級市場中的高銷量貨品。"},{"en":"Shops make high-turnover items easy to find because many customers need them.","zh":"商店讓高銷量貨品容易找到，因為很多顧客需要它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes products with fast sales movement.","zh":"這個短語描述銷售流動快速的產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"command positions at the front","meaning":"佔據前方的顯眼位置","examples":[{"en":"Popular products command positions at the front of the store.","zh":"受歡迎產品佔據店舖前方的顯眼位置。"},{"en":"To command positions at the front means to occupy important, visible places near the entrance.","zh":"command positions at the front 指佔據入口附近重要而顯眼的位置。"},{"en":"New phones may command positions at the front of an electronics shop.","zh":"新手機可能佔據電子產品店前方的顯眼位置。"},{"en":"Products at the front receive more attention because customers see them immediately.","zh":"位於前方的產品會得到更多注意，因為顧客立即看見它們。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that strong-selling items earn the best display space.","zh":"這個短語暗示暢銷商品取得最佳陳列空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"work hard to stall someone","meaning":"設法拖延某人","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets work hard to stall customers inside the store.","zh":"超級市場設法拖延顧客在店內逗留。"},{"en":"To stall someone means to delay them or make them stay longer.","zh":"stall someone 指拖延某人或令他們停留更久。"},{"en":"A salesperson may stall a customer by offering a free demonstration.","zh":"銷售員可能透過提供免費示範來拖延顧客。"},{"en":"If shoppers are stalled inside a store, they have more time to notice extra products.","zh":"如果購物者被拖延在店內，他們就有更多時間注意額外產品。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest a deliberate attempt to slow people down.","zh":"這個短語可以暗示有意令人慢下來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the more …, the more …","meaning":"越……，便越……","examples":[{"en":"The more time customers spend in a shop, the more they tend to buy.","zh":"顧客在店內花越多時間，通常便買得越多。"},{"en":"The more…, the more… shows that one thing increases as another thing increases.","zh":"the more…, the more… 顯示一件事隨另一件事增加而增加。"},{"en":"The more students read, the more vocabulary they usually learn.","zh":"學生讀得越多，通常便學到越多詞彙。"},{"en":"This structure is useful for explaining a relationship between two changes.","zh":"這個結構適合解釋兩種變化之間的關係。"},{"en":"It often shows a cause-and-effect pattern.","zh":"它常顯示因果模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"great efforts are made to","meaning":"人們投入很大努力去……","examples":[{"en":"Great efforts are made to create a pleasant shopping environment.","zh":"人們投入很大努力去營造舒適購物環境。"},{"en":"Great efforts are made to do something means people work very hard to achieve it.","zh":"great efforts are made to do something 指人們非常努力去達成某事。"},{"en":"Great efforts are made to keep hospitals clean because infection is dangerous.","zh":"人們投入很大努力保持醫院清潔，因為感染很危險。"},{"en":"When great efforts are made, the result is usually planned rather than accidental.","zh":"當人們投入很大努力，結果通常是有計劃的，而不是偶然的。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses serious preparation and work.","zh":"這個短語強調認真準備和工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make the environment pleasant","meaning":"令環境舒適","examples":[{"en":"Stores use lighting and music to make the environment pleasant.","zh":"商店使用燈光和音樂來令環境舒適。"},{"en":"To make the environment pleasant means to make a place comfortable, attractive or enjoyable.","zh":"make the environment pleasant 指令地方舒適、吸引或令人愉快。"},{"en":"A teacher can make the classroom environment pleasant by keeping it tidy and welcoming.","zh":"老師可以透過保持課室整潔和親切來令課室環境舒適。"},{"en":"Pleasant environments encourage people to stay longer and feel more relaxed.","zh":"舒適環境鼓勵人們停留更久並感到更放鬆。"},{"en":"This phrase is about improving the feeling of a place.","zh":"這個短語關於改善一個地方的感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pipe air around","meaning":"把空氣輸送到各處","examples":[{"en":"Some supermarkets pipe air from the bakery around the store.","zh":"有些超級市場把麵包店的空氣輸送到店內各處。"},{"en":"To pipe air around means to move air through pipes or vents to different parts of a building.","zh":"pipe air around 指透過管道或通風口把空氣送到建築物不同部分。"},{"en":"A hotel may pipe warm air around rooms during winter.","zh":"酒店可能在冬天把暖空氣輸送到各房間。"},{"en":"Piping bakery air around a store can spread a pleasant smell and influence shoppers.","zh":"把麵包店空氣輸送到店內各處，可以散播宜人香味並影響購物者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled movement of air.","zh":"這個短語描述受控制的空氣流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in-store bakery","meaning":"店內麵包店","examples":[{"en":"The smell from an in-store bakery can encourage spending.","zh":"店內麵包店的氣味可以鼓勵消費。"},{"en":"An in-store bakery is a bakery located inside a supermarket or shop.","zh":"in-store bakery 指位於超級市場或商店內的麵包店。"},{"en":"Customers may smell fresh bread from an in-store bakery while walking through the aisles.","zh":"顧客在通道行走時，可能聞到店內麵包店的新鮮麵包香。"},{"en":"The smell can make people feel hungry and buy more food.","zh":"這種氣味可以令人感到肚餓並購買更多食物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a bakery used as both a service and a marketing tool.","zh":"這個短語指同時作為服務和市場工具的麵包店。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fake aromas","meaning":"人造香氣","examples":[{"en":"Some retailers use fake aromas to influence shoppers.","zh":"有些零售商使用人造香氣來影響購物者。"},{"en":"Fake aromas are artificial smells added to create a certain mood or reaction.","zh":"fake aromas 指加入的人造氣味，用來營造某種情緒或反應。"},{"en":"A shop may use a fake coffee aroma even if no coffee is being made there.","zh":"即使店內沒有沖咖啡，商店也可能使用人造咖啡香。"},{"en":"Fake aromas can make customers feel hungry, relaxed or interested in a product.","zh":"人造香氣可以令顧客感到飢餓、放鬆或對產品有興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that smell can be deliberately manufactured.","zh":"這個短語暗示氣味可以被刻意製造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"evocative sense","meaning":"容易喚起回憶的感官","examples":[{"en":"Smell is an especially evocative sense.","zh":"嗅覺是一種特別容易喚起回憶的感官。"},{"en":"An evocative sense is a sense that strongly brings back memories, feelings or images.","zh":"evocative sense 指能強烈喚起記憶、感受或畫面的感官。"},{"en":"The smell of school lunches may be evocative because it reminds adults of childhood.","zh":"學校午餐的氣味可能容易喚起回憶，因為它令成年人想起童年。"},{"en":"Smell can quickly evoke hunger, comfort, home or special occasions.","zh":"氣味可以快速喚起飢餓、舒適、家的感覺或特別場合。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why scent is powerful in persuasion.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何香味在說服中有力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"subliminal sense","meaning":"潛意識層面的感官","examples":[{"en":"Smell can influence behaviour at a subliminal level.","zh":"嗅覺可以在潛意識層面影響行為。"},{"en":"A subliminal sense affects people below their conscious awareness.","zh":"subliminal sense 指在意識察覺以下影響人的感官。"},{"en":"Background music in a shop may influence shoppers at a subliminal level without them noticing.","zh":"商店中的背景音樂可能在潛意識層面影響購物者，而他們沒有察覺。"},{"en":"Subliminal effects are powerful because people may not realise they are being influenced.","zh":"潛意識效果有力量，因為人們可能沒有意識到自己被影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes influence that happens beneath conscious thought.","zh":"這個短語描述在有意識思考以下發生的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be effective in increasing","meaning":"有效增加……","examples":[{"en":"Pleasant smells can be effective in increasing consumer spending.","zh":"宜人香味可以有效增加消費者開支。"},{"en":"To be effective in increasing something means to successfully make it grow or rise.","zh":"be effective in increasing something 指成功令某事增加或上升。"},{"en":"Clear reminders can be effective in increasing students’ homework submission rates.","zh":"清楚提醒可以有效增加學生交功課率。"},{"en":"A method is effective if it produces the intended increase.","zh":"如果一種方法產生預期增加，它就是有效的。"},{"en":"This phrase links a strategy with measurable growth.","zh":"這個短語把策略與可量度增長連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fragrance half the premises","meaning":"為一半場所增添香氣","examples":[{"en":"A casino fragranced half the premises during an experiment.","zh":"一間賭場在實驗期間為一半場所增添香氣。"},{"en":"To fragrance half the premises means to add scent to one half of a building or business area.","zh":"fragrance half the premises 指為建築物或營業區的一半加入香味。"},{"en":"A hotel might fragrance half the lobby to test whether guests feel more relaxed there.","zh":"酒店可能為一半大堂增添香氣，以測試客人是否更放鬆。"},{"en":"Fragrancing only part of a place allows researchers to compare scented and unscented areas.","zh":"只為部分地方加香，可以讓研究者比較有香氣和無香氣區域。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deliberately adding smell to a physical space.","zh":"這個短語描述刻意為實體空間加入氣味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"profit soar","meaning":"利潤急升","examples":[{"en":"Profit soared in the aroma-filled areas.","zh":"在充滿香氣的區域，利潤急升。"},{"en":"When profit soars, it rises very quickly and strongly.","zh":"profit soar 指利潤快速而大幅上升。"},{"en":"A bakery’s profit may soar after a famous food blogger recommends it.","zh":"著名美食博客推薦後，麵包店利潤可能急升。"},{"en":"Profit can soar when more customers buy or when each customer spends more.","zh":"當更多顧客購買，或每位顧客花費更多，利潤可以急升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sharp increase in earnings.","zh":"這個短語描述收益急劇增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"aroma-filled areas","meaning":"充滿香氣的區域","examples":[{"en":"Customers spent more money in aroma-filled areas.","zh":"顧客在充滿香氣的區域花更多錢。"},{"en":"Aroma-filled areas are places where a noticeable pleasant smell has been added or is present.","zh":"aroma-filled areas 指加入或存在明顯宜人香味的地方。"},{"en":"A shopping mall may create aroma-filled areas near cafés and bakeries.","zh":"商場可能在咖啡店和麵包店附近創造充滿香氣的區域。"},{"en":"Pleasant smells can make people stay longer and spend more.","zh":"宜人香味可以令人停留更久並花費更多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes spaces where scent is part of the atmosphere.","zh":"這個短語描述香氣成為氣氛一部分的空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"from the supermarkets’ perspective","meaning":"從超級市場的角度來看","examples":[{"en":"From the supermarkets’ perspective, loyalty cards are highly successful.","zh":"從超級市場的角度來看，顧客積分卡非常成功。"},{"en":"From someone’s perspective means from their point of view or according to their interests.","zh":"from someone’s perspective 指從某人的觀點或利益角度來看。"},{"en":"From a student’s perspective, homework is stressful; from a teacher’s perspective, it shows progress.","zh":"從學生角度看，功課有壓力；從老師角度看，功課顯示進步。"},{"en":"Different perspectives can lead to different judgments about the same practice.","zh":"不同角度可以令同一做法得到不同判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers to ask whose interests are being considered.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者要問正在考慮誰的利益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"loyalty card","meaning":"顧客積分卡","examples":[{"en":"A loyalty card records information about a customer’s purchases.","zh":"顧客積分卡記錄顧客購買資料。"},{"en":"A loyalty card is a card or account that gives rewards to regular customers.","zh":"loyalty card 指向常客提供獎賞的卡或帳戶。"},{"en":"A supermarket loyalty card may give points whenever a shopper buys groceries.","zh":"超級市場顧客積分卡可能在購物者購買雜貨時給予積分。"},{"en":"Loyalty cards encourage repeat shopping while also collecting useful customer data.","zh":"顧客積分卡鼓勵重複購物，同時收集有用顧客數據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a reward system linked to customer behaviour.","zh":"這個短語指與顧客行為相關的獎賞制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"punters","meaning":"顧客；消費者","examples":[{"en":"Punters may believe that loyalty cards simply reward regular shopping.","zh":"顧客可能相信積分卡只是獎勵經常購物。"},{"en":"Punters are ordinary customers, buyers or members of the public.","zh":"punters 指普通顧客、買家或大眾。"},{"en":"A café may offer discounts to punters who visit every morning.","zh":"咖啡店可能向每天早上到訪的顧客提供折扣。"},{"en":"Businesses study punters because their habits reveal what sells well.","zh":"企業研究消費者，因為他們的習慣揭示甚麼賣得好。"},{"en":"This word is informal and often means everyday customers.","zh":"這個詞較口語，常指日常顧客。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be rewarded for","meaning":"因……而獲得獎勵","examples":[{"en":"Customers assume that they are rewarded for their fidelity.","zh":"顧客以為自己因忠誠而獲得獎勵。"},{"en":"To be rewarded for something means to receive a benefit because of that behaviour or quality.","zh":"be rewarded for something 指因某行為或特質而獲得好處。"},{"en":"Students may be rewarded for perfect attendance with a certificate.","zh":"學生可能因全勤而獲頒證書獎勵。"},{"en":"Rewards encourage people to repeat the behaviour that earns them benefits.","zh":"獎勵鼓勵人們重複能帶來好處的行為。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a prize or benefit with its reason.","zh":"這個短語把獎品或好處與其原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fidelity","meaning":"忠誠度","examples":[{"en":"Loyalty schemes appear to reward shoppers for their fidelity.","zh":"忠誠計劃看似獎勵購物者的忠誠度。"},{"en":"Fidelity means loyalty or faithfulness to a person, group, shop or belief.","zh":"fidelity 指對某人、群體、商店或信念的忠誠。"},{"en":"A customer shows fidelity to a café if they return there every week.","zh":"如果顧客每星期都回到同一間咖啡店，就是展示忠誠度。"},{"en":"Businesses reward fidelity because loyal customers provide steady income.","zh":"企業獎勵忠誠度，因為忠實顧客提供穩定收入。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than “loyalty”.","zh":"這個詞比 “loyalty” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"all the while","meaning":"在整個過程中；與此同時","examples":[{"en":"All the while, the store is collecting valuable consumer data.","zh":"與此同時，商店正在收集有價值的消費者數據。"},{"en":"All the while means during the whole time that something else is happening.","zh":"all the while 指在另一件事發生的整個期間。"},{"en":"A child may play a game, and all the while the app is collecting information.","zh":"孩子可能正在玩遊戲，而在整個過程中，應用程式正在收集資料。"},{"en":"This phrase often reveals a hidden process happening in the background.","zh":"這個短語常揭示背景中正在發生的隱藏過程。"},{"en":"It can show that one thing is happening while people focus on another.","zh":"它可以顯示人們專注於一件事時，另一件事也在發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"trade information about","meaning":"以……交換有關資料","examples":[{"en":"Customers trade information about their shopping habits for rewards.","zh":"顧客以自己的購物習慣資料換取獎賞。"},{"en":"To trade information about something means to give data in exchange for a benefit.","zh":"trade information about something 指交出有關某事的資料，以換取好處。"},{"en":"A user may trade information about their fitness habits for a free app service.","zh":"用戶可能以自己的健身習慣資料換取免費應用程式服務。"},{"en":"This exchange can benefit companies because personal data helps them target customers.","zh":"這種交換可以令公司受惠，因為個人數據幫助它們針對顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that information can become a kind of currency.","zh":"這個短語顯示資料可以成為一種貨幣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"shopping habits","meaning":"購物習慣","examples":[{"en":"Loyalty cards reveal detailed shopping habits.","zh":"顧客積分卡揭示詳細購物習慣。"},{"en":"Shopping habits are the regular patterns in what, when and how people buy things.","zh":"shopping habits 指人們購買甚麼、何時購買和如何購買的固定模式。"},{"en":"A family’s shopping habits may show that they buy fresh food every weekend.","zh":"一個家庭的購物習慣可能顯示他們每週末購買新鮮食物。"},{"en":"Shops study shopping habits to decide prices, promotions and product placement.","zh":"商店研究購物習慣，以決定價格、促銷和產品擺放。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to repeated buying behaviour, not one purchase only.","zh":"這個短語指重複購買行為，而不是單次購買。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"stick to","meaning":"一直光顧；堅持選擇","examples":[{"en":"Loyal customers often stick to the same shops.","zh":"忠實顧客常一直光顧同一批商店。"},{"en":"To stick to something means to continue using or choosing it.","zh":"stick to something 指繼續使用或選擇某事物。"},{"en":"A student may stick to one revision timetable because it works well.","zh":"學生可能堅持使用一個溫習時間表，因為它有效。"},{"en":"Customers stick to familiar shops when they trust the prices, staff and products.","zh":"顧客信任價格、員工和產品時，就會一直光顧熟悉商店。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests loyalty or consistency.","zh":"這個短語暗示忠誠或一致性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"essential commodities","meaning":"生活必需品","examples":[{"en":"Customers may pay more for essential commodities at familiar shops.","zh":"顧客可能在熟悉商店為生活必需品支付更高價格。"},{"en":"Essential commodities are basic goods that people need in daily life.","zh":"essential commodities 指人們日常生活所需的基本商品。"},{"en":"Rice, milk, cooking oil and toilet paper are essential commodities for many families.","zh":"米、牛奶、食油和廁紙是許多家庭的生活必需品。"},{"en":"People may accept higher prices for essential commodities if the shop is convenient.","zh":"如果商店方便，人們可能接受生活必需品價格較高。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to necessary goods, not luxury products.","zh":"這個短語指必要商品，而不是奢侈品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"account for","meaning":"佔；構成","examples":[{"en":"A small group of customers may account for most of a company’s profit.","zh":"一小群顧客可能佔公司大部分利潤。"},{"en":"To account for something means to make up or represent a particular part of it.","zh":"account for something 指佔某事物的一部分或構成某比例。"},{"en":"In a class, late homework may account for most of a student’s lost marks.","zh":"在一班中，遲交功課可能佔學生失分的大部分。"},{"en":"If a few customers account for most profit, a company will treat them very carefully.","zh":"如果少數顧客佔大部分利潤，公司會非常小心對待他們。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used with percentages, proportions and causes.","zh":"這個短語常與百分比、比例和原因一起使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"identify elite shoppers","meaning":"辨認高價值顧客","examples":[{"en":"Reward cards can help supermarkets identify elite shoppers.","zh":"獎賞卡可以幫助超級市場辨認高價值顧客。"},{"en":"To identify elite shoppers means to find the customers who spend the most or bring the most profit.","zh":"identify elite shoppers 指找出花費最多或帶來最多利潤的顧客。"},{"en":"An airline may identify elite travellers by tracking who flies most often.","zh":"航空公司可能透過追蹤誰最常飛行來辨認高價值旅客。"},{"en":"Once a company identifies elite shoppers, it can send them special offers.","zh":"公司辨認高價值顧客後，就可以向他們發送特別優惠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sorting customers by value to the business.","zh":"這個短語描述按企業價值分類顧客。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"better accommodate","meaning":"更切合……的需要","examples":[{"en":"Stores may use customer data to better accommodate profitable shoppers.","zh":"商店可能使用顧客數據來更切合高利潤購物者的需要。"},{"en":"To better accommodate someone means to serve their needs more effectively.","zh":"better accommodate someone 指更有效地服務某人的需要。"},{"en":"A school may adjust lesson times to better accommodate working parents.","zh":"學校可能調整上課時間，以更切合在職家長的需要。"},{"en":"Businesses use data to better accommodate customers by offering what they are likely to buy.","zh":"企業透過提供顧客可能購買的東西，利用數據更切合顧客需要。"},{"en":"This phrase means adapting service to fit people more closely.","zh":"這個短語指調整服務以更貼合人們。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"individual consumers","meaning":"個別消費者","examples":[{"en":"Advertising can be tailored to individual consumers.","zh":"廣告可以為個別消費者度身訂造。"},{"en":"Individual consumers are separate customers with their own needs, habits and preferences.","zh":"individual consumers 指有自己需要、習慣和偏好的個別顧客。"},{"en":"A music app may recommend songs to individual consumers based on listening history.","zh":"音樂應用程式可能根據聆聽紀錄向個別消費者推薦歌曲。"},{"en":"Treating consumers individually can make advertising feel more personal and persuasive.","zh":"個別化對待消費者可以令廣告感覺更個人化、更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts one customer with a broad general audience.","zh":"這個短語把單一顧客與廣泛大眾作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"futuristic thriller","meaning":"未來科幻驚慄片","examples":[{"en":"Minority Report is a futuristic thriller featuring personalised advertising.","zh":"《未來報告》是一部以個人化廣告為特色的未來科幻驚慄片。"},{"en":"A futuristic thriller is an exciting story set in the future, often involving danger, technology or crime.","zh":"futuristic thriller 指設定在未來、通常涉及危險、科技或犯罪的刺激故事。"},{"en":"A film about robots controlling a city could be a futuristic thriller.","zh":"關於機械人控制城市的電影可以是未來科幻驚慄片。"},{"en":"Such stories often warn how future technology might affect ordinary life.","zh":"這類故事常警告未來科技可能如何影響日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase combines a future setting with suspense.","zh":"這個短語結合未來背景和懸疑感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be bombarded with","meaning":"被大量……轟炸","examples":[{"en":"The character is bombarded with personalised advertisements.","zh":"角色被大量個人化廣告轟炸。"},{"en":"To be bombarded with something means to receive too much of it from many directions.","zh":"be bombarded with something 指從許多方向收到太多某事物。"},{"en":"Students may be bombarded with messages from group chats before a school event.","zh":"學校活動前，學生可能被群組聊天訊息大量轟炸。"},{"en":"When people are bombarded with adverts, they may feel overwhelmed or manipulated.","zh":"當人們被大量廣告轟炸，可能感到不勝負荷或被操控。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests repeated and excessive exposure.","zh":"這個短語暗示反覆而過量的接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"interactive personalised adverts","meaning":"互動式個人化廣告","examples":[{"en":"Technology may allow retailers to display interactive personalised adverts.","zh":"科技可能讓零售商展示互動式個人化廣告。"},{"en":"Interactive personalised adverts are advertisements that respond to individual consumers and invite some kind of interaction.","zh":"interactive personalised adverts 指回應個別消費者並邀請某種互動的廣告。"},{"en":"A shopping screen may show a personalised advert when it recognises a customer’s loyalty account.","zh":"當購物屏幕識別顧客的會員帳戶時，可能顯示個人化廣告。"},{"en":"These adverts can feel more powerful because they seem to speak directly to one person.","zh":"這些廣告可能更有力量，因為它們像直接對某個人說話。"},{"en":"This phrase describes advertising shaped by data and user response.","zh":"這個短語描述由數據和用戶反應塑造的廣告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sound far-fetched","meaning":"聽起來難以置信","examples":[{"en":"The idea may sound far-fetched, but similar technology already exists.","zh":"這個想法可能聽起來難以置信，但類似科技已經存在。"},{"en":"To sound far-fetched means to seem unlikely, unrealistic or hard to believe.","zh":"sound far-fetched 指看似不大可能、不現實或難以相信。"},{"en":"A plan to finish a year’s work in one weekend sounds far-fetched.","zh":"在一個週末完成一整年工作的計劃聽起來難以置信。"},{"en":"New technology can sound far-fetched before people see it working in real life.","zh":"新科技在人們看見它實際運作前，可能聽起來難以置信。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an idea that feels unbelievable at first.","zh":"這個短語描述一開始令人覺得不可信的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"data-gathering revolution","meaning":"數據收集革命","examples":[{"en":"The data-gathering revolution has transformed modern retailing.","zh":"數據收集革命改變了現代零售業。"},{"en":"A data-gathering revolution is a major change in how much information is collected and used.","zh":"data-gathering revolution 指收集和使用資訊的數量和方式出現重大變化。"},{"en":"Fitness watches created a data-gathering revolution in how people track health habits.","zh":"健身手錶在追蹤健康習慣方面造成數據收集革命。"},{"en":"When companies gather more data, they can target customers more precisely.","zh":"當公司收集更多數據，它們可以更精準地針對顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large shift driven by information collection.","zh":"這個短語描述由資訊收集推動的大轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"see the introduction of","meaning":"見證……的引入","examples":[{"en":"Recent years have seen the introduction of electronic product tracking.","zh":"近年見證了電子產品追蹤的引入。"},{"en":"To see the introduction of something means that something new has appeared or begun during that period.","zh":"see the introduction of something 指某時期出現或開始某種新事物。"},{"en":"The school year saw the introduction of online homework submission.","zh":"這個學年見證了網上交功課的引入。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to describe new developments in a period of time.","zh":"這個短語常用來描述某段時間內的新發展。"},{"en":"It makes time sound like a witness to change.","zh":"它把時間寫得像變化的見證者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"radio-frequency identification","meaning":"無線射頻識別技術","examples":[{"en":"Radio-frequency identification allows products to be electronically tracked.","zh":"無線射頻識別技術讓產品能被電子追蹤。"},{"en":"Radio-frequency identification is a technology that uses radio signals to identify and track tagged objects.","zh":"radio-frequency identification 指使用無線電訊號識別和追蹤已標記物件的技術。"},{"en":"A library may use radio-frequency identification to track borrowed books.","zh":"圖書館可能使用無線射頻識別技術追蹤借出的書。"},{"en":"RFID can make stock control faster because products can be scanned automatically.","zh":"RFID 可以令庫存控制更快，因為產品可被自動掃描。"},{"en":"This phrase is often shortened to RFID.","zh":"這個短語常縮寫為 RFID。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"electronically tag products","meaning":"以電子方式標記產品","examples":[{"en":"Retailers can electronically tag products with RFID technology.","zh":"零售商可以用 RFID 技術以電子方式標記產品。"},{"en":"To electronically tag products means to attach digital identifiers so items can be tracked or scanned.","zh":"electronically tag products 指附上電子識別標籤，使商品可被追蹤或掃描。"},{"en":"A warehouse may electronically tag products to know where each box is stored.","zh":"倉庫可能以電子方式標記產品，以知道每個箱子存放在哪裡。"},{"en":"Electronic tags help businesses follow goods from shelves to checkout and beyond.","zh":"電子標籤幫助企業從貨架到收銀，甚至之後追蹤貨品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding digital tracking to physical products.","zh":"這個短語描述為實體產品加入數碼追蹤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"follow products into people’s homes","meaning":"追蹤產品進入顧客家中","examples":[{"en":"RFID may allow retailers to follow products into people’s homes.","zh":"RFID 可能讓零售商追蹤產品進入顧客家中。"},{"en":"To follow products into people’s homes means to track goods even after customers have bought them and taken them home.","zh":"follow products into people’s homes 指即使顧客購買並把商品帶回家後，仍追蹤貨品。"},{"en":"A smart fridge might follow products into a home by recording what food is inside.","zh":"智能雪櫃可能透過記錄內有甚麼食物，追蹤產品進入家庭。"},{"en":"This kind of tracking can raise privacy concerns because shopping data continues beyond the store.","zh":"這種追蹤可能引起私隱憂慮，因為購物數據延續到店外。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extended product tracking after purchase.","zh":"這個短語描述購買後延伸的產品追蹤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"no matter how savvy","meaning":"無論多麼精明","examples":[{"en":"No matter how savvy consumers think they are, advertising can still influence them.","zh":"無論消費者認為自己多麼精明，廣告仍可以影響他們。"},{"en":"No matter how savvy means even if someone is very clever, experienced or hard to fool.","zh":"no matter how savvy 指即使某人非常聰明、有經驗或不易受騙。"},{"en":"No matter how savvy online users are, they should still check suspicious links.","zh":"無論網上用戶多麼精明，仍應檢查可疑連結。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that skill or awareness does not remove all risk.","zh":"這個短語顯示技巧或意識不能消除所有風險。"},{"en":"It is often used to warn confident people not to be overconfident.","zh":"它常用來提醒有信心的人不要過分自信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"marketing ploys","meaning":"市場推廣花招","examples":[{"en":"Consumers are becoming more aware of marketing ploys.","zh":"消費者越來越意識到市場推廣花招。"},{"en":"Marketing ploys are clever tricks or strategies used to persuade people to buy.","zh":"marketing ploys 指用來說服人購買的聰明手法或策略。"},{"en":"A “limited time only” sign can be a marketing ploy if the sale returns every week.","zh":"如果優惠每星期都回來，“limited time only” 標誌可能是市場推廣花招。"},{"en":"Marketing ploys work by creating urgency, curiosity or emotional pressure.","zh":"市場推廣花招透過製造迫切感、好奇心或情感壓力來發揮作用。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests that the tactic is calculated.","zh":"這個短語常暗示策略是經過計算的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the advertising industry","meaning":"廣告業","examples":[{"en":"The advertising industry invests heavily in psychological research.","zh":"廣告業在心理研究上投入大量資金。"},{"en":"The advertising industry is the business sector that creates and sells promotional messages.","zh":"advertising industry 指創作和銷售宣傳訊息的商業行業。"},{"en":"Designers, copywriters, media planners and data analysts may work in the advertising industry.","zh":"設計師、文案、媒體策劃和數據分析師都可能在廣告業工作。"},{"en":"The industry studies consumers so adverts can become more persuasive.","zh":"廣告業研究消費者，使廣告變得更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to advertising as a whole business field.","zh":"這個短語指作為整個商業範疇的廣告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"still wins","meaning":"仍然勝出","examples":[{"en":"Despite consumer awareness, the advertising industry still wins.","zh":"儘管消費者有意識，廣告業仍然勝出。"},{"en":"Still wins means continues to succeed even though there are obstacles or opposition.","zh":"still wins 指即使有障礙或反對，仍繼續成功。"},{"en":"A strong team still wins even when the weather is bad and the match is difficult.","zh":"強隊即使天氣差、比賽困難，仍然勝出。"},{"en":"Advertising still wins when people know the tricks but buy the products anyway.","zh":"當人們知道廣告花招但仍購買產品，廣告仍然勝出。"},{"en":"This phrase shows success despite resistance.","zh":"這個短語顯示在阻力下仍取得成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"focus on what products do","meaning":"集中說明產品的功能","examples":[{"en":"Some adverts focus on what products do.","zh":"有些廣告集中說明產品的功能。"},{"en":"To focus on what products do means to emphasise their functions and practical effects.","zh":"focus on what products do 指強調產品的功能和實際效果。"},{"en":"A vacuum-cleaner advert may focus on what the product does by showing how it removes dust.","zh":"吸塵機廣告可能透過展示如何清除灰塵來集中說明產品功能。"},{"en":"Functional adverts appeal to customers who want clear practical benefits.","zh":"功能型廣告吸引想要清楚實際好處的顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts practical information with emotional appeal.","zh":"這個短語把實用資訊與情感吸引作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"how products make us feel","meaning":"產品令我們有何感受","examples":[{"en":"Other adverts focus on how products make us feel.","zh":"其他廣告集中於產品令我們有何感受。"},{"en":"How products make us feel refers to the emotions, identity or mood linked to using them.","zh":"how products make us feel 指使用產品時連繫到的情緒、身份或心情。"},{"en":"A perfume advert may focus on how the product makes people feel confident and attractive.","zh":"香水廣告可能集中於產品如何令人感到自信和有吸引力。"},{"en":"Emotional advertising works when feelings matter more than technical details.","zh":"當感受比技術細節更重要，情感廣告就會有效。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why ads often sell a feeling, not just an object.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何廣告常售賣感覺，而不只是物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"以……為基礎","examples":[{"en":"Consumer attitudes may be based on logic or emotion.","zh":"消費者態度可能以邏輯或情緒為基礎。"},{"en":"To be based on something means to be built from or supported by it.","zh":"be based on something 指由某事建立或支持。"},{"en":"A school rule should be based on student safety, not convenience alone.","zh":"學校規則應以學生安全為基礎，而不只是方便。"},{"en":"If a decision is based on emotion, facts may have less influence.","zh":"如果決定以情緒為基礎，事實的影響可能較小。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the foundation of an idea, action or judgement.","zh":"這個短語指出想法、行動或判斷的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cognitive foundations","meaning":"認知基礎","examples":[{"en":"Some attitudes are based on cognitive foundations.","zh":"有些態度以認知基礎建立。"},{"en":"Cognitive foundations are the thinking, knowledge and reasoning behind a belief or attitude.","zh":"cognitive foundations 指信念或態度背後的思考、知識和推理。"},{"en":"A student’s opinion on recycling may have cognitive foundations if it is based on facts about waste.","zh":"如果學生對回收的看法以廢物事實為基礎，就有認知基礎。"},{"en":"Cognitive foundations make persuasion more logical because they involve information and analysis.","zh":"認知基礎令說服更合乎邏輯，因為它涉及資訊和分析。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts thought-based reasons with emotion-based reasons.","zh":"這個短語把思想基礎的理由與情感基礎的理由作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"logical reasoning","meaning":"邏輯推理","examples":[{"en":"Informative adverts appeal to logical reasoning.","zh":"資訊型廣告訴諸邏輯推理。"},{"en":"Logical reasoning is thinking that follows evidence, facts and clear steps.","zh":"logical reasoning 指遵循證據、事實和清晰步驟的思考。"},{"en":"A student uses logical reasoning when they compare prices before buying a laptop.","zh":"學生購買手提電腦前比較價格時，就是使用邏輯推理。"},{"en":"Advertisers use logical reasoning when they explain how a product saves money or time.","zh":"廣告商解釋產品如何節省金錢或時間時，就是使用邏輯推理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes decision-making based on thought rather than feeling alone.","zh":"這個短語描述基於思考而不只是感覺的決策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"informative appeals","meaning":"資訊型宣傳手法","examples":[{"en":"Advertisers use informative appeals for highly functional products.","zh":"廣告商為高度實用的產品使用資訊型宣傳手法。"},{"en":"Informative appeals are advertising methods that persuade by giving facts, details or explanations.","zh":"informative appeals 指透過提供事實、細節或解釋來說服的廣告方法。"},{"en":"A washing-machine advert may use informative appeals by listing water use, capacity and warranty.","zh":"洗衣機廣告可能透過列出用水量、容量和保養期來使用資訊型宣傳手法。"},{"en":"These appeals work best when customers want practical information before buying.","zh":"當顧客購買前想要實用資訊，這類手法最有效。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts fact-based persuasion with emotional persuasion.","zh":"這個短語把事實型說服與情感型說服作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"emotional appeal","meaning":"情感吸引力","examples":[{"en":"Some practical products have little emotional appeal.","zh":"有些實用產品情感吸引力很低。"},{"en":"Emotional appeal is the power to attract people through feelings rather than facts alone.","zh":"emotional appeal 指透過感受而不只是事實吸引人的力量。"},{"en":"A charity advert has emotional appeal if it makes viewers feel sympathy and responsibility.","zh":"如果慈善廣告令人感到同情和責任，它就有情感吸引力。"},{"en":"Products with strong emotional appeal can seem desirable even when people do not need them.","zh":"情感吸引力強的產品即使人們不需要，也可能看起來令人想要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes persuasion through feeling.","zh":"這個短語描述透過感情進行說服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"high functionality","meaning":"高實用性","examples":[{"en":"Bleach has high functionality but limited emotional appeal.","zh":"漂白水有高實用性，但情感吸引力有限。"},{"en":"High functionality means a product is very useful and performs a clear practical job.","zh":"high functionality 指產品非常有用，並執行清楚的實際功能。"},{"en":"A calculator has high functionality because it helps students solve sums quickly.","zh":"計算機有高實用性，因為它幫助學生快速計算。"},{"en":"Highly functional products may be bought because they work, not because they feel exciting.","zh":"高實用性產品可能因為有效而被購買，而不是因為令人興奮。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical usefulness.","zh":"這個短語著重實際用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be based on affect","meaning":"以情感為基礎","examples":[{"en":"Some purchasing decisions are based on affect rather than logic.","zh":"有些購買決定以情感而非邏輯為基礎。"},{"en":"To be based on affect means to be driven by feelings, moods or emotions.","zh":"be based on affect 指由感受、心情或情緒推動。"},{"en":"A teenager may choose shoes based on affect because they feel stylish and confident in them.","zh":"青少年可能以情感為基礎選鞋，因為穿上它們覺得時尚和自信。"},{"en":"When decisions are based on affect, emotional response can outweigh practical facts.","zh":"當決定以情感為基礎，情緒反應可以凌駕實際事實。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in psychology and consumer behaviour.","zh":"這個短語常用於心理學和消費者行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tap into our feelings","meaning":"利用我們的感受","examples":[{"en":"Advertising teams try to tap into our feelings.","zh":"廣告團隊試圖利用我們的感受。"},{"en":"To tap into our feelings means to use or connect with our emotions.","zh":"tap into our feelings 指利用或連接我們的情緒。"},{"en":"A graduation speech may tap into students’ feelings by mentioning shared memories.","zh":"畢業演講可能透過提到共同回憶來觸動學生感受。"},{"en":"Ads tap into feelings when they link products with love, fear, pride or belonging.","zh":"當廣告把產品與愛、恐懼、自豪或歸屬感連繫起來，就是在利用感受。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests using emotions as a source of influence.","zh":"這個短語暗示把情緒作為影響來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"emotional responses","meaning":"情緒反應","examples":[{"en":"Emotional responses can dominate purchasing decisions.","zh":"情緒反應可以主導購買決定。"},{"en":"Emotional responses are feelings people experience after seeing, hearing or thinking about something.","zh":"emotional responses 指人們看見、聽見或想到某事後產生的感受。"},{"en":"A sad charity video may create emotional responses such as sympathy and guilt.","zh":"悲傷的慈善影片可能產生同情和內疚等情緒反應。"},{"en":"Strong emotional responses can make people act before they think carefully.","zh":"強烈情緒反應可以令人在仔細思考前行動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to feelings that influence behaviour.","zh":"這個短語指影響行為的感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"dominate over cognition","meaning":"凌駕於理性認知","examples":[{"en":"Emotional reactions may dominate over cognition.","zh":"情緒反應可能凌駕於理性認知。"},{"en":"To dominate over cognition means to have more influence than logical thought.","zh":"dominate over cognition 指比邏輯思考有更大影響力。"},{"en":"Fear can dominate over cognition when people make quick decisions during an emergency.","zh":"緊急情況下，人們快速作決定時，恐懼可能凌駕於理性認知。"},{"en":"In advertising, feelings may dominate over cognition if the image is powerful enough.","zh":"在廣告中，如果影像足夠強烈，感覺可能凌駕於理性認知。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotion defeating careful reasoning.","zh":"這個短語描述情緒壓倒仔細推理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"play on our need to","meaning":"利用我們對……的需要","examples":[{"en":"Advertisers play on our need to feel safe and accepted.","zh":"廣告商利用我們對安全感和被接納的需要。"},{"en":"To play on our need to do something means to use that need to influence us.","zh":"play on our need to do something 指利用我們的某種需要來影響我們。"},{"en":"A security advert may play on our need to protect our family.","zh":"保安廣告可能利用我們保護家庭的需要。"},{"en":"Advertisers use this technique because basic human needs can be very persuasive.","zh":"廣告商使用這種技巧，因為基本人類需要非常有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests emotional manipulation.","zh":"這個短語常暗示情感操控。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"need to be safe","meaning":"對安全感的需要","examples":[{"en":"Insurance advertisements appeal to our need to be safe.","zh":"保險廣告訴諸我們對安全感的需要。"},{"en":"The need to be safe is the human desire for protection from danger, loss or harm.","zh":"need to be safe 指人類希望免受危險、損失或傷害的保護需求。"},{"en":"Parents may buy a car seat because of their need to keep children safe.","zh":"父母可能因想保障孩子安全而購買兒童汽車座椅。"},{"en":"Products that promise protection can feel attractive when people worry about risk.","zh":"當人們擔心風險，承諾保護的產品可能感覺吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a basic emotional need.","zh":"這個短語描述基本情感需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"need to belong","meaning":"歸屬感的需要","examples":[{"en":"Fashion advertising often appeals to the need to belong.","zh":"時裝廣告常訴諸歸屬感的需要。"},{"en":"The need to belong is the desire to feel accepted as part of a group.","zh":"need to belong 指希望感到自己被接納並屬於某群體。"},{"en":"A teenager may buy certain trainers because classmates wear the same brand.","zh":"青少年可能因同學穿同一品牌而購買某款運動鞋。"},{"en":"Advertising uses belonging when it suggests a product will help people fit in.","zh":"當廣告暗示產品能幫助人融入群體，就是在利用歸屬感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a social and emotional need.","zh":"這個短語描述社交和情感需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"feel part of a group","meaning":"感到自己屬於某個群體","examples":[{"en":"Fashion adverts can make customers feel part of a group.","zh":"時裝廣告可以令顧客感到自己屬於某個群體。"},{"en":"To feel part of a group means to feel included, accepted and connected with others.","zh":"feel part of a group 指感到被包括、被接納並與他人連繫。"},{"en":"A school team jacket can make students feel part of a group.","zh":"學校隊服外套可以令學生感到自己屬於某個群體。"},{"en":"People may buy brands that help them feel they belong to a certain lifestyle.","zh":"人們可能購買能令自己覺得屬於某種生活方式的品牌。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why identity can influence buying.","zh":"這個短語解釋身份認同為何能影響購買。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"self-esteem","meaning":"自尊","examples":[{"en":"Aspirational advertising often appeals to consumers’ self-esteem.","zh":"激發上進心的廣告常訴諸消費者的自尊。"},{"en":"Self-esteem is the way people value and feel about themselves.","zh":"self-esteem 指人們如何評價和感受自己。"},{"en":"A student’s self-esteem may improve when teachers praise real progress.","zh":"當老師稱讚真實進步，學生自尊可能提升。"},{"en":"Advertising appeals to self-esteem when it suggests a product makes people better, admired or successful.","zh":"當廣告暗示產品令人更好、更受欣賞或更成功，就是訴諸自尊。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to personal confidence and sense of worth.","zh":"這個短語指個人信心和自我價值感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"aspirational adverts","meaning":"激發上進心的廣告","examples":[{"en":"Aspirational adverts connect products with success and status.","zh":"激發上進心的廣告把產品與成功和地位連繫起來。"},{"en":"Aspirational adverts are advertisements that make people desire a better, richer or more successful life.","zh":"aspirational adverts 指令人渴望更好、更富裕或更成功生活的廣告。"},{"en":"A watch advert may show confident executives to create an aspirational image.","zh":"手錶廣告可能展示自信高管，以創造令人嚮往的形象。"},{"en":"These adverts work by making a product seem linked to the person people want to become.","zh":"這類廣告透過令產品似乎與人們想成為的形象相連而發揮作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes advertising based on ambition and ideal identity.","zh":"這個短語描述以抱負和理想身份為基礎的廣告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at a premium","meaning":"非常寶貴；供不應求","examples":[{"en":"Time and advertising space are often at a premium.","zh":"時間和廣告空間通常非常寶貴。"},{"en":"At a premium means scarce, valuable or difficult to obtain.","zh":"at a premium 指稀缺、有價值或難以取得。"},{"en":"During exam season, quiet study seats in the library are at a premium.","zh":"考試季節期間，圖書館安靜自修座位供不應求。"},{"en":"When something is at a premium, people compete for it or use it very carefully.","zh":"當某物非常寶貴，人們會競爭取得或非常小心使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited resources with high value.","zh":"這個短語描述有限但高價值的資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a quick way of meeting needs","meaning":"快速滿足需要的方法","examples":[{"en":"Celebrities offer a quick way of meeting several emotional needs.","zh":"名人提供一種快速滿足多種情感需要的方法。"},{"en":"A quick way of meeting needs is a fast method for satisfying what people want or feel they lack.","zh":"quick way of meeting needs 指快速滿足人們想要或覺得缺乏之物的方法。"},{"en":"A school app can be a quick way of meeting parents’ need for updates.","zh":"學校應用程式可以快速滿足家長對最新資訊的需要。"},{"en":"Celebrities meet emotional needs by offering familiarity, success and trust in one image.","zh":"名人透過一個形象提供熟悉感、成功感和信任感，以滿足情感需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an efficient shortcut to satisfying needs.","zh":"這個短語描述有效率地滿足需要的捷徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"epitomise success","meaning":"是成功的典範","examples":[{"en":"A famous celebrity may epitomise success.","zh":"著名名人可能是成功的典範。"},{"en":"To epitomise success means to be a perfect or typical example of success.","zh":"epitomise success 指成為成功的完美或典型例子。"},{"en":"A student who rose from failure to university admission may epitomise hard work and success.","zh":"一名由失敗走到大學取錄的學生，可能是努力和成功的典範。"},{"en":"Advertisers use people who epitomise success to make products seem linked to achievement.","zh":"廣告商使用成功典範人物，令產品看似與成就相連。"},{"en":"This phrase describes someone or something that strongly represents an idea.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈代表某概念的人或物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"seem familiar","meaning":"看起來熟悉","examples":[{"en":"Celebrities seem familiar to many consumers.","zh":"名人對許多消費者來說看起來熟悉。"},{"en":"To seem familiar means to feel known or recognisable, even without real personal contact.","zh":"seem familiar 指感覺像認識或認得，即使沒有真正個人接觸。"},{"en":"A news presenter may seem familiar because viewers see them every evening.","zh":"新聞主播可能看起來熟悉，因為觀眾每晚都看見他。"},{"en":"Familiarity can create trust, even if people do not actually know the person.","zh":"熟悉感可以創造信任，即使人們其實不認識該人。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why famous faces can influence buyers.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何名人面孔能影響買家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make the product seem safe","meaning":"令產品看來可靠","examples":[{"en":"A familiar celebrity can make the product seem safe.","zh":"熟悉的名人可以令產品看來可靠。"},{"en":"To make the product seem safe means to make buyers feel the product is trustworthy or low-risk.","zh":"make the product seem safe 指令買家覺得產品可信或風險低。"},{"en":"A doctor in an advert may make a health product seem safe.","zh":"廣告中的醫生可能令健康產品看來可靠。"},{"en":"Familiar faces reduce doubt because customers transfer trust from the person to the product.","zh":"熟悉面孔減少疑慮，因為顧客把對人的信任轉移到產品上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how advertising lowers fear or hesitation.","zh":"這個短語描述廣告如何降低恐懼或猶豫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"advertising campaign","meaning":"廣告宣傳活動","examples":[{"en":"The survey examined 4,000 advertising campaigns.","zh":"該調查研究了 4,000 個廣告宣傳活動。"},{"en":"An advertising campaign is a planned set of adverts used to promote a product, idea or brand.","zh":"advertising campaign 指用來推廣產品、想法或品牌的一系列有計劃廣告。"},{"en":"A school may run an advertising campaign to encourage students to join a reading programme.","zh":"學校可能舉行廣告宣傳活動，鼓勵學生參加閱讀計劃。"},{"en":"Campaigns combine images, slogans and media channels to reach many people.","zh":"宣傳活動結合影像、口號和媒體渠道，以接觸許多人。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a coordinated advertising effort, not one single advert.","zh":"這個短語指協調一致的廣告努力，而不是單一廣告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"more effective than","meaning":"比……更有效","examples":[{"en":"Advertisements with celebrities were more effective than those without.","zh":"有名人的廣告比沒有名人的廣告更有效。"},{"en":"More effective than means better at producing the desired result.","zh":"more effective than 指在產生理想結果方面更好。"},{"en":"Daily vocabulary practice is more effective than memorising a long list once.","zh":"每日詞彙練習比一次過背長清單更有效。"},{"en":"An advert is more effective if it makes people remember and act.","zh":"如果廣告令人記住並採取行動，它就更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how well two methods work.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種方法運作得有多好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"stimulate a rapid response","meaning":"刺激快速反應","examples":[{"en":"Humour can stimulate a rapid emotional response.","zh":"幽默可以刺激快速情緒反應。"},{"en":"To stimulate a rapid response means to quickly cause a reaction.","zh":"stimulate a rapid response 指快速引起反應。"},{"en":"A loud alarm can stimulate a rapid response from students during a fire drill.","zh":"響亮警鐘可以在消防演習中刺激學生快速反應。"},{"en":"Funny adverts work quickly because laughter appears before careful analysis.","zh":"搞笑廣告很快奏效，因為笑聲在仔細分析前出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that triggers an immediate reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述觸發即時反應的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be remembered for longer","meaning":"被記得更久","examples":[{"en":"Funny advertisements are often remembered for longer.","zh":"搞笑廣告通常被記得更久。"},{"en":"To be remembered for longer means to stay in people’s memory for more time.","zh":"be remembered for longer 指在人的記憶中停留更長時間。"},{"en":"A teacher’s funny example may be remembered for longer than a dry definition.","zh":"老師的搞笑例子可能比乾巴巴的定義被記得更久。"},{"en":"Humour, surprise and emotion help messages remain in memory.","zh":"幽默、驚喜和情緒幫助訊息留在記憶中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lasting memorability.","zh":"這個短語描述持久記憶度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"straight adverts","meaning":"正經直接的廣告","examples":[{"en":"Humorous adverts may be more memorable than straight adverts.","zh":"幽默廣告可能比正經直接的廣告更令人記得。"},{"en":"Straight adverts are direct advertisements that give information without jokes or dramatic tricks.","zh":"straight adverts 指不使用笑話或戲劇手法、直接提供資訊的廣告。"},{"en":"A straight advert for medicine may simply explain the symptoms it treats.","zh":"藥物的正經直接廣告可能只是解釋它治療的症狀。"},{"en":"Straight adverts can be clear, but they may not stay in memory as well as funny ones.","zh":"正經直接的廣告可以清晰，但可能不如搞笑廣告令人記得。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts plain advertising with more creative styles.","zh":"這個短語把平實廣告與更具創意的風格作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"combine humour with","meaning":"將幽默與……結合","examples":[{"en":"Some campaigns combine humour with sexual imagery.","zh":"有些宣傳活動將幽默與性暗示影像結合。"},{"en":"To combine humour with something means to use humour together with another element.","zh":"combine humour with something 指把幽默與另一元素一起使用。"},{"en":"A teacher may combine humour with real examples to make grammar easier to remember.","zh":"老師可能將幽默與真實例子結合，使文法更易記。"},{"en":"Combining two appeals can make a message more noticeable.","zh":"結合兩種吸引力可以令訊息更顯眼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mixing two persuasive tools.","zh":"這個短語描述混合兩種說服工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sexual imagery","meaning":"性暗示影像","examples":[{"en":"Sexual imagery is sometimes used to attract attention.","zh":"性暗示影像有時被用來吸引注意。"},{"en":"Sexual imagery means pictures or suggestions linked to sexual attraction.","zh":"sexual imagery 指與性吸引力相關的圖片或暗示。"},{"en":"A perfume advert may use sexual imagery to make the product seem desirable.","zh":"香水廣告可能使用性暗示影像，使產品看似令人渴望。"},{"en":"Such imagery can attract attention quickly, but it may also offend some viewers.","zh":"這類影像可以快速吸引注意，但也可能冒犯一些觀眾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual persuasion using desire or attractiveness.","zh":"這個短語描述利用慾望或吸引力的視覺說服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be on to a winner","meaning":"很可能會成功","examples":[{"en":"An advertiser who combines several strong appeals may be on to a winner.","zh":"廣告人若結合幾種強大吸引力，很可能會成功。"},{"en":"To be on to a winner means to have found an idea or method that is likely to succeed.","zh":"be on to a winner 指找到很可能成功的想法或方法。"},{"en":"A café may be on to a winner if its lunch set is cheap, tasty and fast.","zh":"如果咖啡店午餐套餐便宜、美味又快捷，它很可能會成功。"},{"en":"When several strengths work together, success becomes more likely.","zh":"當幾個優勢共同發揮作用，成功就更有可能。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses confidence that a strategy will work.","zh":"這個短語表達對策略會奏效的信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"slice-of-life adverts","meaning":"生活片段式廣告","examples":[{"en":"Slice-of-life adverts present familiar everyday situations.","zh":"生活片段式廣告呈現熟悉的日常情況。"},{"en":"Slice-of-life adverts are advertisements that show ordinary scenes from daily life.","zh":"slice-of-life adverts 指展示日常生活普通場景的廣告。"},{"en":"A detergent advert showing a family doing laundry is a slice-of-life advert.","zh":"展示家庭洗衣的洗衣劑廣告就是生活片段式廣告。"},{"en":"These adverts work because viewers recognise the situation and imagine themselves in it.","zh":"這類廣告有效，因為觀眾認得該情境並想像自己身處其中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes advertising based on everyday realism.","zh":"這個短語描述以日常真實感為基礎的廣告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tried-and-tested method","meaning":"經過反覆驗證的方法","examples":[{"en":"Slice-of-life advertising is a tried-and-tested method.","zh":"生活片段式廣告是經過反覆驗證的方法。"},{"en":"A tried-and-tested method is a method that has been used many times and shown to work.","zh":"tried-and-tested method 指已被多次使用並證實有效的方法。"},{"en":"Practising past papers is a tried-and-tested method for preparing for exams.","zh":"練習歷屆試題是準備考試的經過反覆驗證的方法。"},{"en":"Businesses trust tried-and-tested methods because the risk feels lower.","zh":"企業信任經驗證方法，因為風險感覺較低。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a proven approach, not a new experiment.","zh":"這個短語描述已證實的方法，而不是新實驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"paint a picture of","meaning":"描繪……的景象","examples":[{"en":"The advert paints a picture of an attractive lifestyle.","zh":"廣告描繪一種吸引人的生活方式。"},{"en":"To paint a picture of something means to describe or show it clearly and vividly.","zh":"paint a picture of something 指清楚而生動地描述或展示某事。"},{"en":"A travel brochure paints a picture of quiet beaches and relaxed mornings.","zh":"旅遊小冊子描繪寧靜海灘和悠閒早晨的景象。"},{"en":"Advertising paints pictures so people can imagine a life connected with the product.","zh":"廣告描繪畫面，使人想像與產品相關的生活。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe visual or verbal description.","zh":"這個短語可以描述視覺或文字描寫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"still feel familiar","meaning":"仍然令人感到熟悉","examples":[{"en":"The idealised lifestyle must still feel familiar to the audience.","zh":"這種理想化生活方式仍必須令觀眾感到熟悉。"},{"en":"To still feel familiar means to remain recognisable and easy to relate to.","zh":"still feel familiar 指仍然容易認出和產生共鳴。"},{"en":"A new school app should still feel familiar if it uses simple buttons and clear labels.","zh":"如果新學校應用程式使用簡單按鈕和清楚標籤，就仍然令人感到熟悉。"},{"en":"If an advert feels too distant, viewers may not connect it with their own lives.","zh":"如果廣告感覺太遙遠，觀眾可能無法把它與自己生活連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the need to balance idealisation with realism.","zh":"這個短語顯示需要在理想化與真實感之間取得平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"self-image","meaning":"自我形象","examples":[{"en":"A consumer’s self-image can affect their response to a brand.","zh":"消費者的自我形象可以影響他們對品牌的反應。"},{"en":"Self-image is the way people see and imagine themselves.","zh":"self-image 指人們如何看待和想像自己。"},{"en":"A student with a sporty self-image may prefer trainers over formal shoes.","zh":"有運動型自我形象的學生可能偏好運動鞋而不是正式皮鞋。"},{"en":"Brands influence people when they match how customers want to see themselves.","zh":"當品牌配合顧客想如何看待自己，就能影響人們。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to personal identity in one’s own mind.","zh":"這個短語指人心中的個人身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tally with","meaning":"與……一致","examples":[{"en":"An advert is stronger when the brand tallies with the consumer’s self-image.","zh":"當品牌與消費者自我形象一致，廣告就更有力。"},{"en":"To tally with something means to match or agree with it.","zh":"tally with something 指與某事相配或一致。"},{"en":"A student’s subject choices should tally with their interests and future plans.","zh":"學生選科應與興趣和未來計劃一致。"},{"en":"Advertising works better when the product image tallies with what buyers want to be.","zh":"當產品形象與買家想成為的人一致，廣告就更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a close fit between two things.","zh":"這個短語描述兩件事之間的貼合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the brand being advertised","meaning":"正在宣傳的品牌","examples":[{"en":"Consumers respond more strongly when they identify with the brand being advertised.","zh":"當消費者認同正在宣傳的品牌，他們反應更強。"},{"en":"The brand being advertised is the product name or company identity promoted in an advert.","zh":"brand being advertised 指廣告中被推廣的產品名稱或公司身份。"},{"en":"A sports advert works better if young athletes identify with the brand being advertised.","zh":"如果年輕運動員認同正在宣傳的品牌，運動廣告會更有效。"},{"en":"People respond when a brand seems to fit their values, lifestyle or dreams.","zh":"當品牌似乎符合人們的價值、生活方式或夢想，他們就會有反應。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the specific brand currently promoted.","zh":"這個短語指目前正在推廣的特定品牌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"behaviourist theories","meaning":"行為主義理論","examples":[{"en":"Advertisers sometimes apply behaviourist theories to marketing.","zh":"廣告商有時把行為主義理論應用於市場推廣。"},{"en":"Behaviourist theories explain behaviour by focusing on stimulus, response, reward and habit.","zh":"behaviourist theories 透過刺激、反應、獎賞和習慣來解釋行為。"},{"en":"A teacher uses behaviourist ideas when stickers reward children for reading daily.","zh":"老師用貼紙獎勵孩子每日閱讀時，就是使用行為主義想法。"},{"en":"Advertisers use these theories by linking products with pleasant sights, sounds or rewards.","zh":"廣告商透過把產品與愉快影像、聲音或獎賞連繫起來使用這些理論。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to psychological theories about learned behaviour.","zh":"這個短語指關於學習行為的心理學理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sensory information","meaning":"感官資料","examples":[{"en":"Advertising supplies consumers with sensory information.","zh":"廣告向消費者提供感官資料。"},{"en":"Sensory information is information received through sight, sound, smell, taste or touch.","zh":"sensory information 指透過視覺、聽覺、嗅覺、味覺或觸覺接收的資訊。"},{"en":"A bakery gives sensory information through the smell of bread and the sight of cakes.","zh":"麵包店透過麵包香和蛋糕外觀提供感官資料。"},{"en":"The more senses a product engages, the more real it may feel to customers.","zh":"產品調動越多感官，對顧客來說可能感覺越真實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information entering through the senses.","zh":"這個短語描述透過感官進入的資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"receive from an object","meaning":"從物件接收到","examples":[{"en":"The more sensory information we receive from an object, the better we know it.","zh":"我們從物件接收到越多感官資料，就越了解它。"},{"en":"To receive information from an object means to gain details about it through seeing, touching, smelling or using it.","zh":"receive information from an object 指透過看、觸摸、嗅聞或使用它來取得細節。"},{"en":"A shopper receives information from a jacket by feeling its fabric and checking its weight.","zh":"購物者透過觸摸外套布料和檢查重量，從外套接收資訊。"},{"en":"More information helps people judge quality, usefulness and comfort.","zh":"更多資訊幫助人們判斷質素、用途和舒適度。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how direct experience builds familiarity.","zh":"這個短語解釋直接經驗如何建立熟悉感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cause salivation","meaning":"引起唾液分泌","examples":[{"en":"An effective chocolate advert may cause salivation.","zh":"有效朱古力廣告可能引起唾液分泌。"},{"en":"To cause salivation means to make the mouth produce saliva, often because food looks or smells attractive.","zh":"cause salivation 指令口腔產生唾液，常因食物看起來或聞起來吸引。"},{"en":"The smell of fresh noodles may cause salivation before lunch.","zh":"午飯前新鮮麵條的氣味可能引起唾液分泌。"},{"en":"Food adverts use close-up images to make viewers imagine taste and hunger.","zh":"食物廣告使用特寫影像，使觀眾想像味道和飢餓感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical response to food-related stimulation.","zh":"這個短語描述對食物相關刺激的身體反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"no wonder","meaning":"難怪","examples":[{"en":"No wonder advertising has been compared to a nervous system.","zh":"難怪廣告被比作神經系統。"},{"en":"No wonder means it is not surprising.","zh":"no wonder 指並不令人驚訝。"},{"en":"No wonder the student is tired; he studied until 2 a.m.","zh":"難怪這名學生疲倦；他溫習到凌晨兩點。"},{"en":"This phrase links an explanation with a result that now seems understandable.","zh":"這個短語把解釋與現在變得可理解的結果連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is used when the reason makes the situation obvious.","zh":"當原因令情況變得明顯時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be dubbed","meaning":"被稱為……","examples":[{"en":"Advertisements have been dubbed the nervous system of business.","zh":"廣告被稱為商業的神經系統。"},{"en":"To be dubbed something means to be given a particular name or description.","zh":"be dubbed something 指被賦予某個名稱或描述。"},{"en":"A hardworking student may be dubbed the class organiser by classmates.","zh":"勤奮學生可能被同學稱為班級組織者。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when a label captures an important quality.","zh":"當一個標籤抓住重要特質時，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It is often used in journalism and commentary.","zh":"它常用於新聞和評論中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"nervous system of the business world","meaning":"商業世界的神經系統","examples":[{"en":"Advertising has been called the nervous system of the business world.","zh":"廣告被稱為商業世界的神經系統。"},{"en":"The nervous system of the business world is a metaphor suggesting that advertising carries signals through commerce.","zh":"nervous system of the business world 是比喻，表示廣告在商業中傳送訊號。"},{"en":"In a company, emails may act like a nervous system by sending information quickly between teams.","zh":"在公司中，電郵可以像神經系統般在團隊之間快速傳送資訊。"},{"en":"Advertising connects businesses and consumers by transmitting messages, desires and responses.","zh":"廣告透過傳送訊息、慾望和反應，把企業與消費者連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase presents advertising as a communication network for business.","zh":"這個短語把廣告呈現為商業的溝通網絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"make a sale","meaning":"成功推銷","examples":[{"en":"Most people could make a sale if they strongly believed in the product.","zh":"如果大多數人真心相信產品，他們都可能成功推銷。"},{"en":"To make a sale means to successfully persuade someone to buy something.","zh":"make a sale 指成功說服某人購買某物。"},{"en":"A student helping at a charity fair may make a sale by explaining why the cookies support a good cause.","zh":"學生在慈善市集幫忙時，可能透過解釋曲奇支持好目的而成功推銷。"},{"en":"Sales happen more easily when the seller sounds honest and confident.","zh":"當銷售者聽起來誠實又有信心，銷售更容易成功。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to completing a successful selling action.","zh":"這個短語指完成成功銷售行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"truly believe in","meaning":"真心相信……","examples":[{"en":"Salespeople are more convincing when they truly believe in a product.","zh":"銷售員真心相信產品時更有說服力。"},{"en":"To truly believe in something means to genuinely trust its value or importance.","zh":"truly believe in something 指真誠相信某事的價值或重要性。"},{"en":"A teacher speaks more powerfully when she truly believes in helping weaker students.","zh":"老師真心相信幫助較弱學生時，說話會更有力量。"},{"en":"Genuine belief makes persuasion feel more honest and less forced.","zh":"真誠信念令說服感覺更誠實、較不勉強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sincere confidence, not pretending.","zh":"這個短語描述真誠信心，而不是假裝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be in a different league","meaning":"屬於完全不同的層次","examples":[{"en":"Professional salespeople are in a different league from ordinary sellers.","zh":"專業銷售員與普通賣家屬於完全不同的層次。"},{"en":"To be in a different league means to be much better or at a much higher level.","zh":"be in a different league 指好得多或處於高得多的水平。"},{"en":"A trained athlete is in a different league from someone who only jogs once a month.","zh":"受訓運動員與每月只慢跑一次的人屬於完全不同的層次。"},{"en":"People in a different league often have skills that beginners cannot easily copy.","zh":"屬於不同層次的人通常有初學者難以輕易模仿的技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a strong comparison in ability.","zh":"這個短語對能力作強烈比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"suitable customers","meaning":"合適的顧客","examples":[{"en":"Good salespeople match products with suitable customers.","zh":"優秀銷售員把產品與合適的顧客配對。"},{"en":"Suitable customers are people whose needs, budget or situation fit a product or service.","zh":"suitable customers 指需要、預算或情況與產品或服務相配的人。"},{"en":"A piano teacher looks for suitable customers who want regular lessons and have time to practise.","zh":"鋼琴老師尋找想定期上課且有時間練習的合適顧客。"},{"en":"Matching products with suitable customers reduces waste and increases satisfaction.","zh":"把產品配對給合適顧客可以減少浪費並提高滿意度。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on fit between buyer and product.","zh":"這個短語著重買家與產品之間的配合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"at the right time","meaning":"在適當時候","examples":[{"en":"The best salespeople approach customers at the right time.","zh":"最好的銷售員在適當時候接觸顧客。"},{"en":"At the right time means when the moment is most suitable.","zh":"at the right time 指在最合適的時刻。"},{"en":"A teacher gives feedback at the right time when students can still improve their drafts.","zh":"當學生仍可改善草稿時，老師在適當時候給予回饋。"},{"en":"Good timing can make advice feel helpful instead of annoying.","zh":"良好時機可以令建議感覺有幫助，而不是令人厭煩。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises timing as part of success.","zh":"這個短語強調時機是成功的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"basic psychological techniques","meaning":"基本心理技巧","examples":[{"en":"Professional sellers use basic psychological techniques.","zh":"專業銷售員使用基本心理技巧。"},{"en":"Basic psychological techniques are simple methods that influence how people think, feel or decide.","zh":"basic psychological techniques 指影響人們如何思考、感受或決定的簡單方法。"},{"en":"A teacher uses a basic psychological technique when she praises effort to encourage more practice.","zh":"老師稱讚努力以鼓勵更多練習時，就是使用基本心理技巧。"},{"en":"Salespeople use such techniques to build trust, reduce doubt and increase desire.","zh":"銷售員使用這些技巧來建立信任、減少疑慮和增加慾望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes simple mind-based strategies.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單的心理策略。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"stripped to its simplest level","meaning":"簡化到最基本層面","examples":[{"en":"Stripped to its simplest level, selling involves increasing perceived need.","zh":"簡化到最基本層面，銷售涉及增加被感知的需要。"},{"en":"Stripped to its simplest level means reduced to the most basic idea.","zh":"stripped to its simplest level 指把某事簡化到最基本概念。"},{"en":"Stripped to its simplest level, revision means practising what you cannot yet do well.","zh":"簡化到最基本層面，溫習就是練習自己尚未做好的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase removes extra details so the core meaning becomes clear.","zh":"這個短語去除額外細節，使核心意思清楚。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining a complex process in plain terms.","zh":"當用簡單語言解釋複雜過程時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"heighten someone’s perception of","meaning":"加強某人對……的感覺","examples":[{"en":"Sellers heighten the buyer’s perception of how much a product is needed.","zh":"銷售員加強買家對產品有多需要的感覺。"},{"en":"To heighten someone’s perception of something means to make them feel or notice it more strongly.","zh":"heighten someone’s perception of something 指令某人更強烈地感到或注意到某事。"},{"en":"A health poster can heighten people’s perception of the danger of smoking.","zh":"健康海報可以加強人們對吸煙危險的感覺。"},{"en":"Salespeople heighten perceived need by showing problems customers may not have considered.","zh":"銷售員透過指出顧客可能未考慮的問題來加強被感知需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing awareness or concern.","zh":"這個短語描述增加意識或關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"product or service","meaning":"產品或服務","examples":[{"en":"The seller must show why the product or service is valuable.","zh":"銷售員必須展示產品或服務為何有價值。"},{"en":"A product or service is something sold to customers, either a physical item or an action provided for them.","zh":"product or service 指售予顧客的東西，可以是實體物品或為他們提供的行動。"},{"en":"A phone is a product, while phone repair is a service.","zh":"手機是產品，而手機維修是服務。"},{"en":"Customers buy products or services when they believe these things solve a problem.","zh":"當顧客相信產品或服務能解決問題，他們就會購買。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both goods and helpful work.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋商品和有用工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"certain requirements","meaning":"某些要求","examples":[{"en":"Buyers normally have certain requirements when choosing a product.","zh":"買家選擇產品時通常有某些要求。"},{"en":"Certain requirements are specific needs or conditions that must be met.","zh":"certain requirements 指必須滿足的具體需要或條件。"},{"en":"A student buying a laptop may have certain requirements, such as long battery life and low weight.","zh":"學生購買手提電腦時可能有某些要求，例如電池續航長和重量輕。"},{"en":"If a product fails to meet key requirements, the buyer may reject it.","zh":"如果產品不能滿足關鍵要求，買家可能拒絕它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to important conditions in a decision.","zh":"這個短語指決策中的重要條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"judge the suitability of","meaning":"判斷……是否合適","examples":[{"en":"Customers judge the suitability of a product against their needs.","zh":"顧客根據自己的需要判斷產品是否合適。"},{"en":"To judge the suitability of something means to decide whether it fits a purpose or situation.","zh":"judge the suitability of something 指判斷某物是否符合目的或情況。"},{"en":"A teacher judges the suitability of a book by checking its language level and topic.","zh":"老師透過檢查語言程度和題材來判斷一本書是否合適。"},{"en":"Customers judge suitability by comparing price, function, size and comfort.","zh":"顧客透過比較價格、功能、尺寸和舒適度來判斷合適程度。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on deciding whether something is appropriate.","zh":"這個短語著重判斷某物是否適當。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"tease out","meaning":"逐步探問出","examples":[{"en":"A skilled salesperson teases out the buyer’s real priorities.","zh":"熟練銷售員逐步探問出買家的真正優先事項。"},{"en":"To tease out information means to gradually discover it by asking careful questions.","zh":"tease out information 指透過仔細提問逐漸發現資料。"},{"en":"A teacher may tease out a shy student’s opinion by asking simple follow-up questions.","zh":"老師可能透過簡單追問逐步探問出害羞學生的意見。"},{"en":"Salespeople tease out needs because customers may not state them clearly at first.","zh":"銷售員逐步探問需要，因為顧客起初未必清楚說出來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gentle, gradual discovery.","zh":"這個短語描述溫和而逐步的發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"meet these requirements","meaning":"滿足這些要求","examples":[{"en":"The salesperson explains how the product can meet these requirements.","zh":"銷售員解釋產品如何滿足這些要求。"},{"en":"To meet these requirements means to satisfy the stated needs or conditions.","zh":"meet these requirements 指滿足已說明的需要或條件。"},{"en":"A course meets students’ requirements if it fits their level, schedule and goals.","zh":"如果課程符合學生程度、時間表和目標，就滿足學生要求。"},{"en":"Customers are more likely to buy when they see how a product meets their requirements.","zh":"當顧客看見產品如何滿足自己的要求，就更可能購買。"},{"en":"This phrase describes matching needs successfully.","zh":"這個短語描述成功配合需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"human nature","meaning":"人性","examples":[{"en":"It is human nature to prefer speaking to listening.","zh":"較喜歡說話而不是聆聽是人性。"},{"en":"Human nature means the basic tendencies or behaviours common to many people.","zh":"human nature 指許多人共有的基本傾向或行為。"},{"en":"It is human nature to feel nervous before an important test or interview.","zh":"重要測驗或面試前感到緊張是人性。"},{"en":"Salespeople use human nature when they let customers talk about themselves.","zh":"銷售員讓顧客談論自己時，就是利用人性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what people often naturally do or feel.","zh":"這個短語描述人們常自然會做或感到的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"prefer to speak rather than listen","meaning":"較喜歡說話而不是聆聽","examples":[{"en":"Many people prefer to speak rather than listen.","zh":"許多人較喜歡說話而不是聆聽。"},{"en":"To prefer to speak rather than listen means to enjoy talking more than hearing others.","zh":"prefer to speak rather than listen 指比起聆聽別人，更喜歡自己說話。"},{"en":"In group work, one student may prefer to speak rather than listen to classmates’ ideas.","zh":"在小組工作中，一名學生可能較喜歡說話，而不是聆聽同學想法。"},{"en":"When everyone wants to speak, communication can become weaker.","zh":"當人人都想說話，溝通可能變得較弱。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts talking with listening.","zh":"這個短語把說話與聆聽作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"pander to this","meaning":"迎合這一點","examples":[{"en":"Good salespeople pander to the customer’s desire to speak.","zh":"優秀銷售員迎合顧客想說話的慾望。"},{"en":"To pander to this means to satisfy or exploit the desire just mentioned.","zh":"pander to this 指滿足或利用剛提到的慾望。"},{"en":"A teacher may pander to students’ love of games by turning revision into a quiz.","zh":"老師可能把溫習變成問答遊戲，迎合學生喜歡遊戲這一點。"},{"en":"Salespeople pander to talkative customers because it helps them gather information.","zh":"銷售員迎合健談顧客，因為這有助收集資料。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to an earlier desire or weakness.","zh":"這個短語指回前文的慾望或弱點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ask someone about their needs","meaning":"詢問某人的需要","examples":[{"en":"Salespeople ask customers about their needs.","zh":"銷售員詢問顧客的需要。"},{"en":"To ask someone about their needs means to question them about what they want, lack or must solve.","zh":"ask someone about their needs 指詢問某人想要甚麼、缺少甚麼或必須解決甚麼。"},{"en":"A doctor asks patients about their needs before suggesting treatment.","zh":"醫生建議治療前會詢問病人的需要。"},{"en":"Asking about needs helps avoid offering the wrong solution.","zh":"詢問需要有助避免提供錯誤解決方案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first step in understanding a customer or client.","zh":"這個短語描述理解顧客或客戶的第一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"work with someone to","meaning":"與某人合作去……","examples":[{"en":"A salesperson may offer to work with the buyer to achieve an objective.","zh":"銷售員可能提出與買家合作去達成目標。"},{"en":"To work with someone to do something means to cooperate with them to reach a goal.","zh":"work with someone to do something 指與某人合作以達到目標。"},{"en":"A teacher works with a student to improve weak grammar areas.","zh":"老師與學生合作去改善薄弱文法範疇。"},{"en":"Working with someone makes the process feel like cooperation rather than pressure.","zh":"與某人合作會令過程感覺像合作，而不是壓迫。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests partnership and shared effort.","zh":"這個短語暗示伙伴關係和共同努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"achieve their objectives","meaning":"達成他們的目標","examples":[{"en":"Buyers want products that help them achieve their objectives.","zh":"買家想要能幫助他們達成目標的產品。"},{"en":"To achieve their objectives means to reach the goals they want to accomplish.","zh":"achieve their objectives 指達到他們想完成的目標。"},{"en":"Students choose revision tools that help them achieve their objectives in exams.","zh":"學生選擇能幫助他們在考試中達成目標的溫習工具。"},{"en":"Products become attractive when buyers see how they help solve a goal-related problem.","zh":"當買家看見產品如何幫助解決與目標相關的問題，產品就變得吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on reaching planned aims.","zh":"這個短語著重達到計劃目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, the customer feels listened to.","zh":"因此，顧客感到自己被聆聽。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what has just happened or been explained.","zh":"as a result 指因為剛發生或剛解釋的事。"},{"en":"The teacher gave clear examples; as a result, the class understood the grammar.","zh":"老師給出清楚例子；因此，全班理解了文法。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with its effect.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"},{"en":"It helps readers follow the logical consequence of an action.","zh":"它幫助讀者跟上行動帶來的邏輯結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"receive a consultation","meaning":"接受諮詢服務","examples":[{"en":"The buyer feels that they are receiving a consultation.","zh":"買家感覺自己正在接受諮詢服務。"},{"en":"To receive a consultation means to get personalised advice from someone with knowledge.","zh":"receive a consultation 指從有知識的人那裡得到個人化建議。"},{"en":"A patient receives a consultation when a doctor asks questions and explains treatment options.","zh":"醫生提問並解釋治療選項時，病人就是接受諮詢服務。"},{"en":"Sales can feel softer when customers believe they are receiving advice, not pressure.","zh":"當顧客相信自己得到的是建議而不是壓力，銷售會感覺較柔和。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a guided discussion about needs and solutions.","zh":"這個短語描述關於需要和解決方案的引導式討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"sales pitch","meaning":"推銷說辭","examples":[{"en":"A consultation feels less aggressive than a sales pitch.","zh":"諮詢服務感覺比推銷說辭較不具攻擊性。"},{"en":"A sales pitch is a prepared attempt to persuade someone to buy something.","zh":"sales pitch 指預先準備好、試圖說服某人購買的說法。"},{"en":"A phone salesperson may give a sales pitch about a new internet plan.","zh":"電話銷售員可能就新的上網計劃作推銷說辭。"},{"en":"A strong sales pitch highlights benefits and tries to overcome doubts.","zh":"強力推銷說辭會突出好處並試圖克服疑慮。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound negative if the persuasion feels too pushy.","zh":"如果說服感覺太進取，這個短語可能帶負面意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"present a demeanour","meaning":"表現出某種態度","examples":[{"en":"The salesperson presents a confident demeanour.","zh":"銷售員表現出自信的態度。"},{"en":"To present a demeanour means to show a particular outward attitude or manner.","zh":"present a demeanour 指展示某種外在態度或舉止。"},{"en":"A teacher presents a calm demeanour during an emergency so students do not panic.","zh":"老師在緊急情況中表現出冷靜態度，使學生不會恐慌。"},{"en":"A confident demeanour can make customers feel the seller knows what they are doing.","zh":"自信態度可以令顧客覺得銷售員清楚自己在做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible behaviour and attitude.","zh":"這個短語描述可見行為和態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"take it for granted that","meaning":"理所當然地認為","examples":[{"en":"The salesperson takes it for granted that the sale will be made.","zh":"銷售員理所當然地認為交易會成功。"},{"en":"To take it for granted that something will happen means to assume it is certain.","zh":"take it for granted that something will happen 指假定某事一定會發生。"},{"en":"A student should not take it for granted that good handwriting will make a weak answer correct.","zh":"學生不應理所當然地認為字體漂亮就會令弱答案變正確。"},{"en":"Salespeople may act as if the purchase is already certain to guide customers forward.","zh":"銷售員可能表現得像購買已經確定，以引導顧客向前。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an assumption treated as obvious.","zh":"這個短語描述把假設視為理所當然。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"build up a level of rapport","meaning":"逐步建立融洽關係","examples":[{"en":"Salespeople build up a level of rapport with potential buyers.","zh":"銷售員與潛在買家逐步建立融洽關係。"},{"en":"To build up a level of rapport means to gradually create a friendly and trusting relationship.","zh":"build up a level of rapport 指逐漸建立友好和信任的關係。"},{"en":"A tutor builds rapport with a student by remembering their goals and worries.","zh":"導師透過記得學生的目標和憂慮來建立融洽關係。"},{"en":"Rapport makes conversations feel safer and more natural.","zh":"融洽關係令對話感覺更安全和自然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trust growing through repeated small interactions.","zh":"這個短語描述信任透過反覆小互動逐漸增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"ask questions about","meaning":"詢問有關……的問題","examples":[{"en":"They ask questions about the customer’s family and lifestyle.","zh":"他們詢問有關顧客家庭和生活方式的問題。"},{"en":"To ask questions about something means to request information on that topic.","zh":"ask questions about something 指要求提供某主題的資訊。"},{"en":"A doctor asks questions about sleep, diet and exercise before giving advice.","zh":"醫生給建議前會詢問有關睡眠、飲食和運動的問題。"},{"en":"Good questions reveal needs that people may not explain directly.","zh":"好問題能揭示人們未必直接說出的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information-gathering through conversation.","zh":"這個短語描述透過對話收集資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"double benefit","meaning":"雙重好處","examples":[{"en":"Friendly conversation offers a double benefit to the salesperson.","zh":"友善對話為銷售員提供雙重好處。"},{"en":"A double benefit is two advantages gained from one action.","zh":"double benefit 指一個行動帶來兩個好處。"},{"en":"Walking to school gives a double benefit: exercise and saving transport money.","zh":"步行上學有雙重好處：運動和節省交通費。"},{"en":"Friendly chat helps the salesperson seem likeable and collect useful information.","zh":"友善聊天幫助銷售員顯得討人喜歡，並收集有用資料。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights two useful results from the same thing.","zh":"這個短語突出同一事情帶來兩個有用結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"make someone likeable","meaning":"令某人討人喜歡","examples":[{"en":"Personal conversation can make the salesperson more likeable.","zh":"私人對話可以令銷售員更討人喜歡。"},{"en":"To make someone likeable means to make others feel that the person is pleasant and easy to trust.","zh":"make someone likeable 指令別人覺得某人親切、容易信任。"},{"en":"A teacher becomes more likeable when she listens carefully and remembers students’ names.","zh":"老師細心聆聽並記得學生名字時，會變得更討人喜歡。"},{"en":"Likeable people can persuade more easily because others feel comfortable with them.","zh":"討人喜歡的人較容易說服別人，因為他人覺得與他們相處舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improving someone’s social appeal.","zh":"這個短語描述提升某人的社交吸引力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"furnish someone with information","meaning":"向某人提供資料","examples":[{"en":"The conversation furnishes the salesperson with useful information.","zh":"對話向銷售員提供有用資料。"},{"en":"To furnish someone with information means to provide them with useful details.","zh":"furnish someone with information 指向某人提供有用細節。"},{"en":"A school survey furnishes teachers with information about students’ learning difficulties.","zh":"學校調查向老師提供有關學生學習困難的資料。"},{"en":"Salespeople use information from conversations to choose the most persuasive product features.","zh":"銷售員利用對話中的資料來選擇最具說服力的產品特色。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and means “provide someone with information”.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是「向某人提供資料」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"client’s wants","meaning":"客戶的需要","examples":[{"en":"Questions reveal more about the client’s wants.","zh":"問題揭示更多客戶的需要。"},{"en":"A client’s wants are the things a customer hopes to get, experience or avoid.","zh":"client’s wants 指顧客希望得到、經歷或避免的事情。"},{"en":"A travel agent asks about a client’s wants before recommending a holiday package.","zh":"旅行社職員推薦假期套票前，會詢問客戶的需要。"},{"en":"Understanding wants helps sellers match products with real desires.","zh":"理解需要幫助銷售者把產品配對到真實慾望。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what the customer personally values.","zh":"這個短語著重顧客個人重視甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"as far as possible","meaning":"盡可能","examples":[{"en":"Effective salespeople adapt as far as possible to each customer.","zh":"有效銷售員盡可能適應每位顧客。"},{"en":"As far as possible means to the greatest degree that is practical or realistic.","zh":"as far as possible 指在實際或現實可行範圍內達到最大程度。"},{"en":"A teacher helps each student as far as possible, even when the class is large.","zh":"即使班級很大，老師也會盡可能幫助每位學生。"},{"en":"Businesses adapt as far as possible when customers have different needs.","zh":"當顧客有不同需要，企業會盡可能作出調整。"},{"en":"This phrase recognises effort while admitting there may be limits.","zh":"這個短語承認努力，同時承認可能有界限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"match their style to","meaning":"使自己的風格配合……","examples":[{"en":"Salespeople match their style to the buyer’s personality.","zh":"銷售員使自己的風格配合買家的性格。"},{"en":"To match one’s style to someone means to adjust behaviour so it fits that person.","zh":"match one’s style to someone 指調整行為，使其適合某人。"},{"en":"A tutor may match her teaching style to a student who learns best through examples.","zh":"導師可能使教學風格配合最能透過例子學習的學生。"},{"en":"Matching style can make communication feel more natural and comfortable.","zh":"配合風格可以令溝通感覺更自然和舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adapting one’s manner to another person.","zh":"這個短語描述把自己的方式調整至配合另一個人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"come across","meaning":"給人某種印象","examples":[{"en":"The seller observes how the buyer comes across.","zh":"銷售員觀察買家給人甚麼印象。"},{"en":"To come across in a certain way means to give a particular impression to others.","zh":"come across in a certain way 指給別人某種印象。"},{"en":"A student may come across as confident if they speak clearly and calmly.","zh":"如果學生說話清楚而冷靜，可能給人自信的印象。"},{"en":"How someone comes across affects how others respond to them.","zh":"一個人給人的印象會影響別人如何回應他。"},{"en":"This phrase describes outward impression, not necessarily true personality.","zh":"這個短語描述外在印象，而不一定是真實性格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"crack jokes","meaning":"說笑話","examples":[{"en":"If the buyer cracks jokes, the seller may do the same.","zh":"如果買家說笑話，銷售員可能也這樣做。"},{"en":"To crack jokes means to tell jokes or make funny comments.","zh":"crack jokes 指講笑話或作出有趣評論。"},{"en":"A teacher may crack jokes to help nervous students relax before a test.","zh":"老師可能在測驗前說笑話，幫助緊張學生放鬆。"},{"en":"Humour can build rapport when it fits the situation and does not offend anyone.","zh":"當幽默適合情境且不冒犯任何人，它可以建立融洽關係。"},{"en":"This phrase describes casual joking in conversation.","zh":"這個短語描述對話中的輕鬆說笑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"respond in kind","meaning":"以同樣方式回應","examples":[{"en":"When a buyer jokes, a salesperson may respond in kind.","zh":"當買家說笑，銷售員可能以同樣方式回應。"},{"en":"To respond in kind means to reply in the same manner or style.","zh":"respond in kind 指以相同方式或風格回應。"},{"en":"If a friend sends a kind message, you may respond in kind with warm words.","zh":"如果朋友發來友善訊息，你可能以溫暖說話作同樣回應。"},{"en":"Salespeople respond in kind to make the buyer feel understood and matched.","zh":"銷售員以同樣方式回應，使買家感到被理解和配合。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mirroring the tone or behaviour of another person.","zh":"這個短語描述模仿另一人的語氣或行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be interested in the feel of","meaning":"對……的感覺更感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Some customers are more interested in the feel of a product.","zh":"有些顧客對產品的觸感更感興趣。"},{"en":"To be interested in the feel of something means to care about how it feels when touched or used.","zh":"be interested in the feel of something 指重視某物被觸摸或使用時的感覺。"},{"en":"A shopper buying a sweater may be interested in the feel of the fabric.","zh":"購買毛衣的購物者可能對布料觸感更感興趣。"},{"en":"Some buyers choose products based on comfort rather than technical features.","zh":"有些買家根據舒適感而不是技術特色選擇產品。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on touch, comfort and sensory experience.","zh":"這個短語著重觸覺、舒適度和感官經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"集中於……","examples":[{"en":"The salesperson focuses on whatever matters most to the buyer.","zh":"銷售員集中於買家最重視的任何事情。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give attention to it above other things.","zh":"focus on something 指比其他事情更注意某事。"},{"en":"A student should focus on weak grammar areas before an exam.","zh":"學生考試前應集中於薄弱文法範疇。"},{"en":"Salespeople focus on customer priorities so their advice feels relevant.","zh":"銷售員集中於顧客優先事項，使建議感覺相關。"},{"en":"This phrase describes directing attention to the most important point.","zh":"這個短語描述把注意力放在最重要之處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"at its most extreme","meaning":"在最極端的情況下","examples":[{"en":"At its most extreme, adaptation may involve copying body language.","zh":"在最極端的情況下，適應可能涉及模仿身體語言。"},{"en":"At its most extreme means in the strongest or most intense form.","zh":"at its most extreme 指在最強烈或最激烈的形式下。"},{"en":"At its most extreme, exam stress can stop students sleeping properly.","zh":"在最極端的情況下，考試壓力可以令學生無法正常睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the far end of a range of behaviour.","zh":"這個短語顯示某種行為範圍的最遠端。"},{"en":"It often introduces an example that is more dramatic than usual.","zh":"它常引入比平常更戲劇化的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"appear empathetic","meaning":"表現得有同理心","examples":[{"en":"A salesperson may try to appear empathetic.","zh":"銷售員可能嘗試表現得有同理心。"},{"en":"To appear empathetic means to seem understanding and sensitive to another person’s feelings.","zh":"appear empathetic 指看起來理解並關心他人的感受。"},{"en":"A doctor appears empathetic when she listens carefully before giving advice.","zh":"醫生在給建議前細心聆聽時，就顯得有同理心。"},{"en":"In sales, appearing empathetic can make customers feel safe and respected.","zh":"在銷售中，表現得有同理心可以令顧客感到安全和受尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the impression of empathy, whether fully genuine or not.","zh":"這個短語著重同理心的印象，不論是否完全真誠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"mirror body language","meaning":"模仿身體語言","examples":[{"en":"Some sellers attempt to mirror the buyer’s body language.","zh":"有些銷售員嘗試模仿買家的身體語言。"},{"en":"To mirror body language means to copy someone’s posture, gestures or movements subtly.","zh":"mirror body language 指細微地模仿某人的姿勢、手勢或動作。"},{"en":"A friendly interviewer may mirror body language by leaning forward when the candidate does.","zh":"友善面試官可能在求職者向前傾時也向前傾，來模仿身體語言。"},{"en":"Mirroring can create comfort because people feel the other person is similar to them.","zh":"模仿可以創造舒適感，因為人們覺得對方與自己相似。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical imitation used to build rapport.","zh":"這個短語描述用來建立融洽關係的身體模仿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"whatever method is used","meaning":"無論採用哪種方法","examples":[{"en":"Whatever method is used, the final aim is to make the sale.","zh":"無論採用哪種方法，最終目的都是完成銷售。"},{"en":"Whatever method is used means no matter which method is chosen.","zh":"whatever method is used 指不論選擇哪種方法。"},{"en":"Whatever method is used for revision, students still need to practise regularly.","zh":"無論採用哪種溫習方法，學生仍需要定期練習。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that different methods may lead toward the same goal.","zh":"這個短語顯示不同方法可能朝向同一目標。"},{"en":"It is useful when method varies but purpose remains fixed.","zh":"當方法不同但目的不變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"work towards one aim","meaning":"朝着同一目標努力","examples":[{"en":"All salespeople work towards one aim.","zh":"所有銷售員都朝着同一目標努力。"},{"en":"To work towards one aim means to direct effort toward a single goal.","zh":"work towards one aim 指把努力集中於單一目標。"},{"en":"A class works towards one aim when everyone prepares for the school performance together.","zh":"當全班一起準備學校演出，就是朝着同一目標努力。"},{"en":"Shared aims help people coordinate their actions.","zh":"共同目標幫助人們協調行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes focused effort toward a clear target.","zh":"這個短語描述朝清晰目標集中努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"close the deal","meaning":"完成交易","examples":[{"en":"The salesperson’s main objective is to close the deal.","zh":"銷售員的主要目標是完成交易。"},{"en":"To close the deal means to complete an agreement or sale successfully.","zh":"close the deal 指成功完成協議或銷售。"},{"en":"A real-estate agent closes the deal when the buyer signs the purchase contract.","zh":"當買家簽署購買合約，地產代理就完成交易。"},{"en":"Salespeople use closing techniques to move customers from interest to commitment.","zh":"銷售員使用成交技巧，把顧客由有興趣推向作出承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the final step of turning discussion into agreement.","zh":"這個短語描述把討論變成協議的最後一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"closing signals","meaning":"成交訊號","examples":[{"en":"Salespeople look for closing signals from potential clients.","zh":"銷售員尋找潛在客戶的成交訊號。"},{"en":"Closing signals are signs that a customer may be ready to buy or agree.","zh":"closing signals 指顧客可能準備購買或同意的跡象。"},{"en":"A customer asking about delivery dates may be giving a closing signal.","zh":"顧客詢問送貨日期可能是在給出成交訊號。"},{"en":"Salespeople watch for these signals so they know when to ask for commitment.","zh":"銷售員留意這些訊號，以知道何時要求承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes clues near the end of a sale.","zh":"這個短語描述銷售接近結尾時的線索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"through their dealings with","meaning":"在與……往來的過程中","examples":[{"en":"Sellers look for clues through their dealings with customers.","zh":"銷售者在與顧客往來的過程中尋找線索。"},{"en":"Through their dealings with someone means during their interactions or business contact with them.","zh":"through their dealings with someone 指在與某人的互動或商業接觸期間。"},{"en":"A teacher learns about students’ strengths through her dealings with them in class.","zh":"老師在課堂與學生往來的過程中了解他們的強項。"},{"en":"Repeated dealings reveal habits, preferences and concerns.","zh":"反覆往來會揭示習慣、偏好和憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes learning from ongoing contact.","zh":"這個短語描述從持續接觸中學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"potential clients","meaning":"潛在客戶","examples":[{"en":"Salespeople watch potential clients for signs of interest.","zh":"銷售員觀察潛在客戶是否有興趣。"},{"en":"Potential clients are people who may become customers but have not yet bought anything.","zh":"potential clients 指可能成為顧客但尚未購買的人。"},{"en":"A tutor may speak with potential clients who are considering English lessons.","zh":"導師可能與正在考慮英文課的潛在客戶交談。"},{"en":"Businesses pay attention to potential clients because they may become future income.","zh":"企業重視潛在客戶，因為他們可能成為未來收入來源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to possible future customers.","zh":"這個短語指可能的未來顧客。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"assume success","meaning":"假定會成功","examples":[{"en":"The closing process works by assuming success.","zh":"成交過程透過假定會成功來運作。"},{"en":"To assume success means to behave as if the desired result will happen.","zh":"assume success 指表現得像理想結果將會發生。"},{"en":"A teacher assumes success when she says, “When you finish this essay, we will improve the conclusion.”","zh":"老師說「當你完成這篇文章後，我們會改善結論」時，就是假定會成功。"},{"en":"In sales, assuming success can guide the buyer toward agreement without asking directly.","zh":"在銷售中，假定會成功可以不直接發問而引導買家同意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes confidence used as a persuasive strategy.","zh":"這個短語描述把信心作為說服策略。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"invite a negative response","meaning":"引來否定回答","examples":[{"en":"A direct question may invite a negative response.","zh":"直接問題可能引來否定回答。"},{"en":"To invite a negative response means to make it easy or likely for someone to say no.","zh":"invite a negative response 指令某人容易或很可能說不。"},{"en":"Asking “Do you want to cancel?” may invite a negative response in customer service.","zh":"在客戶服務中問「你想取消嗎？」可能引來否定回答。"},{"en":"Salespeople avoid questions that give customers an easy chance to refuse.","zh":"銷售員避免讓顧客容易拒絕的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wording that encourages rejection.","zh":"這個短語描述鼓勵拒絕的措辭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"effectively done","meaning":"實際上已經完成","examples":[{"en":"The salesperson behaves as though the deal is effectively done.","zh":"銷售員表現得像交易實際上已經完成。"},{"en":"Effectively done means practically completed, even if not formally finished.","zh":"effectively done 指實際上已完成，即使形式上尚未完全結束。"},{"en":"If all group members agree on the plan, the project decision is effectively done.","zh":"如果所有組員都同意計劃，項目決定實際上已經完成。"},{"en":"Acting as if something is effectively done can push people toward final confirmation.","zh":"表現得像某事實際上已完成，可以推動人們作最後確認。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a situation that is almost settled in practice.","zh":"這個短語描述實際上幾乎已定的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"convenient delivery date","meaning":"方便的送貨日期","examples":[{"en":"Asking for a convenient delivery date assumes that the purchase will happen.","zh":"詢問方便的送貨日期是假定購買會發生。"},{"en":"A convenient delivery date is a delivery time that suits the customer’s schedule.","zh":"convenient delivery date 指符合顧客時間表的送貨日期。"},{"en":"A furniture shop may ask which Saturday would be a convenient delivery date.","zh":"家具店可能詢問哪個星期六是方便的送貨日期。"},{"en":"Asking about delivery can move the buyer’s mind from “whether to buy” to “when to receive it”.","zh":"詢問送貨可以把買家的思考由「是否購買」轉到「何時收貨」。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical date for receiving goods.","zh":"這個短語描述收貨的合適日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"respond accordingly","meaning":"作出相應回應","examples":[{"en":"Customers often respond accordingly when a sale is treated as certain.","zh":"當銷售被視為已確定，顧客常作出相應回應。"},{"en":"To respond accordingly means to react in a way that fits the situation.","zh":"respond accordingly 指以符合情況的方式作反應。"},{"en":"If a fire alarm rings, students should respond accordingly by leaving the classroom calmly.","zh":"如果火警鐘響起，學生應冷靜離開課室作出相應回應。"},{"en":"When sellers act as if a purchase is agreed, some customers may respond by choosing details.","zh":"當銷售員表現得像購買已同意，有些顧客可能回應並選擇細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a response shaped by the situation presented.","zh":"這個短語描述由所呈現情況塑造的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"prove such a pushover","meaning":"證明自己如此容易被說服","examples":[{"en":"The buyer may later wonder why they proved such a pushover.","zh":"買家之後可能疑惑為何自己證明如此容易被說服。"},{"en":"To prove such a pushover means to turn out to be very easy to persuade or defeat.","zh":"prove such a pushover 指結果顯示自己很容易被說服或擊敗。"},{"en":"A student may feel like a pushover if they agree to do all the group work.","zh":"如果學生同意做所有小組工作，可能覺得自己很容易被人利用。"},{"en":"People become pushovers when they find it hard to say no under pressure.","zh":"當人們在壓力下難以拒絕，就容易變成被說服的人。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and slightly critical.","zh":"這個短語較口語，並帶一點批評意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生為每條問題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the option marked by the right letter.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選出由正確字母標示的選項。"},{"en":"In multiple-choice questions, students must decide whether A, B, C or D is correct.","zh":"在多項選擇題中，學生必須判斷 A、B、C 或 D 哪個正確。"},{"en":"Choosing the wrong letter loses marks even if the student understands the idea.","zh":"即使學生理解意思，選錯字母也會失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"according to the paragraph","meaning":"根據該段","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the purpose described according to the paragraph.","zh":"題目問根據該段所描述的目的。"},{"en":"According to the paragraph means based only on the information in that paragraph.","zh":"according to the paragraph 指只根據該段資料。"},{"en":"According to the paragraph, students should not use outside knowledge to answer.","zh":"根據該段，學生不應使用外部知識作答。"},{"en":"This phrase tells students to locate evidence in a specific part of the text.","zh":"這個短語告訴學生在文本特定部分找證據。"},{"en":"It limits the answer to what the paragraph actually says.","zh":"它把答案限制在該段實際所說內容內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"supermarket’s purpose","meaning":"超級市場的目的","examples":[{"en":"The question focuses on the supermarket’s purpose in introducing baskets.","zh":"題目集中於超級市場引入購物籃的目的。"},{"en":"A supermarket’s purpose is the reason why the supermarket does something.","zh":"supermarket’s purpose 指超級市場做某事的原因。"},{"en":"A supermarket’s purpose in placing milk at the back may be to make customers pass more products.","zh":"超級市場把牛奶放在後方的目的，可能是讓顧客經過更多產品。"},{"en":"Understanding purpose helps readers see the business strategy behind a simple action.","zh":"理解目的幫助讀者看見簡單行動背後的商業策略。"},{"en":"This phrase asks why a supermarket chose a particular method.","zh":"這個短語詢問超級市場為何選擇某方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"introduce baskets","meaning":"引入購物籃","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets introduced baskets to change customer behaviour.","zh":"超級市場引入購物籃以改變顧客行為。"},{"en":"To introduce baskets means to start providing baskets for shoppers to carry goods.","zh":"introduce baskets 指開始提供購物籃讓購物者攜帶貨品。"},{"en":"A pharmacy may introduce baskets so customers can carry medicine, tissues and toiletries easily.","zh":"藥房可能引入購物籃，讓顧客容易攜帶藥物、紙巾和洗漱用品。"},{"en":"Baskets make small extra purchases easier because shoppers do not need to hold everything by hand.","zh":"購物籃令小額額外購買更容易，因為購物者不用手拿所有東西。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a store tool added for customer behaviour and convenience.","zh":"這個短語描述為顧客行為和方便而加入的店舖工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"convenient shopping environment","meaning":"方便的購物環境","examples":[{"en":"A convenient shopping environment can improve the customer experience.","zh":"方便的購物環境可以改善顧客體驗。"},{"en":"A convenient shopping environment is a store setting that makes buying easy, quick and comfortable.","zh":"convenient shopping environment 指令購買變得容易、快速和舒適的店舖環境。"},{"en":"Clear signs, wide aisles and helpful baskets create a convenient shopping environment.","zh":"清楚標誌、寬闊通道和有用購物籃能營造方便的購物環境。"},{"en":"Convenience can make customers stay longer and return more often.","zh":"便利可以令顧客停留更久並更常回來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shop designed around ease of use.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞易用性設計的商店。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"spend more time shopping","meaning":"花更多時間購物","examples":[{"en":"Some store designs make customers spend more time shopping.","zh":"有些店舖設計令顧客花更多時間購物。"},{"en":"To spend more time shopping means to stay longer while choosing or buying goods.","zh":"spend more time shopping 指在選購或購買商品時停留更久。"},{"en":"A mall with comfortable seats and cafés may make families spend more time shopping.","zh":"有舒適座位和咖啡店的商場可能令家庭花更多時間購物。"},{"en":"The longer customers shop, the more chances they have to notice extra products.","zh":"顧客購物時間越長，注意到額外產品的機會就越多。"},{"en":"This phrase links time in the shop with possible spending.","zh":"這個短語把店內時間與可能消費連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"reduce congestion","meaning":"減少擠塞","examples":[{"en":"Wider aisles can help reduce congestion.","zh":"較寬通道可以幫助減少擠塞。"},{"en":"To reduce congestion means to make a crowded place or route less blocked.","zh":"reduce congestion 指令擁擠地方或路線較少堵塞。"},{"en":"Extra buses can reduce congestion outside a school at dismissal time.","zh":"放學時增加巴士可以減少校外擠塞。"},{"en":"Less congestion helps people move more comfortably and safely.","zh":"較少擠塞有助人們更舒適和安全地移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for traffic, crowds and narrow spaces.","zh":"這個短語用於交通、人群和狹窄空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"carry a large number of items","meaning":"攜帶大量貨品","examples":[{"en":"A trolley allows shoppers to carry a large number of items.","zh":"購物車讓購物者攜帶大量貨品。"},{"en":"To carry a large number of items means to hold or transport many goods at once.","zh":"carry a large number of items 指一次過拿着或運送很多貨品。"},{"en":"A delivery bag helps a courier carry a large number of items to different homes.","zh":"外賣保溫袋幫助送貨員攜帶大量貨品到不同住戶。"},{"en":"When shoppers can carry more, they may buy more.","zh":"當購物者能攜帶更多，就可能購買更多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes capacity and ease of transport.","zh":"這個短語描述容量和運送便利。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"possess a quality","meaning":"具備某種特質","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what quality the best salespeople possess.","zh":"題目問最好的銷售員具備甚麼特質。"},{"en":"To possess a quality means to have a particular characteristic or ability.","zh":"possess a quality 指擁有某種特徵或能力。"},{"en":"A good nurse must possess patience, kindness and attention to detail.","zh":"好護士必須具備耐性、善良和注重細節。"},{"en":"People with useful qualities often perform better in demanding jobs.","zh":"具備有用特質的人通常在要求高的工作中表現更好。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and means “have a quality”.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是「有某種特質」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the right product","meaning":"合適的產品","examples":[{"en":"A good salesperson offers the right product to the right customer.","zh":"好銷售員向合適顧客提供合適產品。"},{"en":"The right product is the product that best fits a customer’s needs, budget and situation.","zh":"right product 指最符合顧客需要、預算和情況的產品。"},{"en":"A student needs the right product when choosing a laptop for schoolwork, not gaming.","zh":"學生選擇用於學業而非遊戲的手提電腦時，需要合適產品。"},{"en":"Offering the right product builds trust because the customer feels understood.","zh":"提供合適產品可以建立信任，因為顧客感到被理解。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses suitability, not simply price.","zh":"這個短語強調合適性，而不只是價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"demonstrate professional knowledge","meaning":"展示專業知識","examples":[{"en":"Salespeople should demonstrate professional knowledge of their products.","zh":"銷售員應展示對產品的專業知識。"},{"en":"To demonstrate professional knowledge means to show expert understanding in a clear way.","zh":"demonstrate professional knowledge 指以清楚方式展示專業理解。"},{"en":"A pharmacist demonstrates professional knowledge when explaining how to take medicine safely.","zh":"藥劑師解釋如何安全服藥時，就是展示專業知識。"},{"en":"Customers trust sellers more when they can answer detailed questions accurately.","zh":"當銷售員能準確回答詳細問題，顧客更信任他們。"},{"en":"This phrase connects expertise with visible explanation.","zh":"這個短語把專業能力與可見解釋連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"persuade customers to buy","meaning":"說服顧客購買","examples":[{"en":"Strong sales techniques can persuade customers to buy.","zh":"強銷售技巧可以說服顧客購買。"},{"en":"To persuade customers to buy means to convince them to make a purchase.","zh":"persuade customers to buy 指說服顧客作出購買。"},{"en":"A clear demonstration may persuade customers to buy a kitchen appliance.","zh":"清楚示範可能說服顧客購買廚房電器。"},{"en":"Customers are persuaded when they believe the product solves their problem.","zh":"當顧客相信產品能解決問題，就會被說服。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the goal of sales communication.","zh":"這個短語描述銷售溝通的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"at length","meaning":"詳細地；長篇地","examples":[{"en":"Salespeople should not always talk at length to customers.","zh":"銷售員不應總是長篇地對顧客說話。"},{"en":"At length means for a long time or in great detail.","zh":"at length 指長時間地或非常詳細地。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain a difficult grammar point at length before practice begins.","zh":"老師可能在練習開始前詳細解釋一個困難文法點。"},{"en":"Talking at length can be useful, but it may also bore listeners if they need a simple answer.","zh":"長篇解釋可以有用，但如果聽眾只需要簡單答案，也可能令人厭煩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extended speech or explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述延長的說話或解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"define their needs","meaning":"界定他們的需要","examples":[{"en":"Good questions help buyers define their needs.","zh":"好問題幫助買家界定他們的需要。"},{"en":"To define their needs means to identify clearly what they require or want.","zh":"define their needs 指清楚識別他們需要或想要甚麼。"},{"en":"A student defines their needs before choosing whether to join grammar, speaking or writing lessons.","zh":"學生在選擇文法、口語或寫作課前，會界定自己的需要。"},{"en":"Clear needs make it easier to choose suitable products or services.","zh":"清楚需要令選擇合適產品或服務更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes turning vague wants into specific requirements.","zh":"這個短語描述把模糊慾望變成具體要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"choose suitable products","meaning":"選擇合適產品","examples":[{"en":"A consultation can help buyers choose suitable products.","zh":"諮詢可以幫助買家選擇合適產品。"},{"en":"To choose suitable products means to select items that fit one’s needs, budget and situation.","zh":"choose suitable products 指選擇符合需要、預算和情況的物品。"},{"en":"A pharmacist helps customers choose suitable products for a mild cough.","zh":"藥劑師幫助顧客為輕微咳嗽選擇合適產品。"},{"en":"Suitable products reduce waste because customers are less likely to regret buying them.","zh":"合適產品可以減少浪費，因為顧客較不容易後悔購買。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on matching products to real needs.","zh":"這個短語著重把產品配對到真實需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"interpersonal skills","meaning":"人際溝通技巧","examples":[{"en":"Successful salespeople need strong interpersonal skills.","zh":"成功銷售員需要強大人際溝通技巧。"},{"en":"Interpersonal skills are the abilities needed to communicate and build relationships with people.","zh":"interpersonal skills 指與人溝通和建立關係所需的能力。"},{"en":"A nurse needs interpersonal skills to comfort patients and speak with families.","zh":"護士需要人際溝通技巧來安慰病人並與家屬交談。"},{"en":"Good interpersonal skills help people listen, respond and avoid conflict.","zh":"良好人際技巧幫助人聆聽、回應和避免衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people skills, not technical knowledge alone.","zh":"這個短語指待人技巧，而不只是技術知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"contain the following information","meaning":"包含以下資料","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which paragraph contains the following information.","zh":"學生辨認哪一段包含以下資料。"},{"en":"To contain the following information means to include the details listed in the question.","zh":"contain the following information 指包括題目列出的細節。"},{"en":"In a reading test, one paragraph may contain the following information about customer loyalty.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，某一段可能包含以下關於顧客忠誠度的資料。"},{"en":"Students must locate meaning, not simply match the same words.","zh":"學生必須尋找意思，而不只是配對相同字詞。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in paragraph-matching tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於段落配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"use any letter more than once","meaning":"每個字母可使用多於一次","examples":[{"en":"Students may use any paragraph letter more than once.","zh":"學生可以使用任何段落字母多於一次。"},{"en":"To use any letter more than once means the same answer option can be chosen repeatedly.","zh":"use any letter more than once 指同一答案選項可以重複選擇。"},{"en":"In a matching task, paragraph B may answer two different questions.","zh":"在配對題中，B 段可能回答兩個不同問題。"},{"en":"This instruction prevents students from wrongly assuming each letter is used only once.","zh":"這項指示防止學生錯誤以為每個字母只能用一次。"},{"en":"It is important for exam strategy.","zh":"它對考試策略很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"keep consumers in the store longer","meaning":"令消費者在店內逗留更久","examples":[{"en":"Supermarkets use several methods to keep consumers in the store longer.","zh":"超級市場使用幾種方法令消費者在店內逗留更久。"},{"en":"To keep consumers in the store longer means to make shoppers stay inside for more time.","zh":"keep consumers in the store longer 指令購物者在店內停留更多時間。"},{"en":"Comfortable lighting, slow music and product samples can keep consumers in the store longer.","zh":"舒適燈光、慢音樂和試食可以令消費者在店內逗留更久。"},{"en":"The longer shoppers stay, the more products they may notice and buy.","zh":"購物者停留越久，就可能注意和購買越多產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a retail strategy to increase spending.","zh":"這個短語描述增加消費的零售策略。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"build a close relationship with","meaning":"與……建立密切關係","examples":[{"en":"Salespeople try to build a close relationship with buyers.","zh":"銷售員嘗試與買家建立密切關係。"},{"en":"To build a close relationship with someone means to develop trust and familiarity over time.","zh":"build a close relationship with someone 指隨時間建立信任和熟悉感。"},{"en":"A tutor builds a close relationship with students by understanding their goals and worries.","zh":"導師透過理解學生目標和憂慮，與學生建立密切關係。"},{"en":"Close relationships make people more willing to listen and cooperate.","zh":"密切關係令人更願意聆聽和合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual relationship-building.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步建立關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"make a lasting impression","meaning":"留下持久印象","examples":[{"en":"Humorous advertisements can make a lasting impression.","zh":"幽默廣告可以留下持久印象。"},{"en":"To make a lasting impression means to be remembered for a long time.","zh":"make a lasting impression 指令人長時間記得。"},{"en":"A teacher’s kind words can make a lasting impression on a nervous student.","zh":"老師善意的說話可以在緊張學生心中留下持久印象。"},{"en":"Humour, surprise and emotion help messages stay in memory.","zh":"幽默、驚喜和情緒幫助訊息留在記憶中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong and long-term influence on memory.","zh":"這個短語描述對記憶的強烈和長期影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"secure an order","meaning":"成功取得訂單","examples":[{"en":"Salespeople use closing techniques to secure an order.","zh":"銷售員使用成交技巧來成功取得訂單。"},{"en":"To secure an order means to successfully get a customer to place an order.","zh":"secure an order 指成功令顧客下訂單。"},{"en":"A printer company secures an order when a school agrees to buy new machines.","zh":"當學校同意購買新機器，打印機公司就成功取得訂單。"},{"en":"Sales techniques aim to turn interest into a confirmed purchase.","zh":"銷售技巧旨在把興趣轉化成確認購買。"},{"en":"This phrase describes winning a business commitment.","zh":"這個短語描述取得商業承諾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"generate different profits","meaning":"帶來不同利潤","examples":[{"en":"Different customer groups generate different levels of profit.","zh":"不同顧客群帶來不同水平的利潤。"},{"en":"To generate different profits means to produce different amounts of financial gain.","zh":"generate different profits 指產生不同金額的財務收益。"},{"en":"A café may find that office workers generate more profit than occasional tourists.","zh":"咖啡店可能發現上班族比偶爾到訪的遊客帶來更多利潤。"},{"en":"Businesses study this difference so they can focus on more valuable customer groups.","zh":"企業研究這種差異，以便集中於更有價值的顧客群。"},{"en":"This phrase links customer groups with financial results.","zh":"這個短語把顧客群與財務結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"complete the notes below","meaning":"完成以下筆記","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the notes using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成以下筆記。"},{"en":"To complete the notes below means to fill missing words in the notes that follow.","zh":"complete the notes below 指填寫下方筆記中的缺失字詞。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole note section before choosing answers.","zh":"學生選答案前應閱讀整個筆記部分。"},{"en":"The grammar around each gap helps show what kind of word is needed.","zh":"每個空格周圍的文法有助顯示需要哪類詞。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common reading-exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案應包含不多於兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must be one or two words only.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案只能是一個或兩個詞。"},{"en":"If the limit is no more than two words, “loyalty cards” is acceptable.","zh":"如果限制是不多於兩個詞，“loyalty cards” 是可以的。"},{"en":"Writing three words can lose marks even if the meaning is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫三個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict answer-length rule.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格答案長度規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"accommodate the increasing volume of","meaning":"容納日益增加的……數量","examples":[{"en":"Larger trolleys accommodate the increasing volume of shopping.","zh":"較大型購物車容納日益增加的購物量。"},{"en":"To accommodate the increasing volume of something means to provide enough space or capacity for a growing amount.","zh":"accommodate the increasing volume of something 指提供足夠空間或容量來應付日益增加的數量。"},{"en":"A school may build more classrooms to accommodate the increasing volume of students.","zh":"學校可能興建更多課室，以容納日益增加的學生人數。"},{"en":"Larger capacity can encourage people to put more items inside.","zh":"更大容量可以鼓勵人們放入更多物品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adjusting to growth in quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述為數量增長作調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"width of the aisles","meaning":"通道的闊度","examples":[{"en":"The width of the aisles is designed to influence shopping behaviour.","zh":"通道的闊度被設計來影響購物行為。"},{"en":"The width of the aisles is how wide the walking spaces between shelves are.","zh":"width of the aisles 指貨架之間行走空間有多寬。"},{"en":"A supermarket with wider aisles lets families push trolleys more comfortably.","zh":"通道較寬的超級市場讓家庭更舒適地推購物車。"},{"en":"Aisle width affects speed, comfort and how easily customers stop to look at products.","zh":"通道闊度影響速度、舒適度，以及顧客停下看產品的容易程度。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a physical design feature of a store.","zh":"這個短語指店舖的實體設計特色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be designed to maximise","meaning":"旨在將……最大化","examples":[{"en":"The store layout is designed to maximise profit.","zh":"店舖佈局旨在將利潤最大化。"},{"en":"To be designed to maximise something means to be planned in a way that increases it as much as possible.","zh":"be designed to maximise something 指以盡可能增加某事為目標而設計。"},{"en":"A timetable may be designed to maximise students’ study time before exams.","zh":"時間表可能旨在將學生考試前的溫習時間最大化。"},{"en":"Store layouts maximise profit by guiding customers past products they may buy.","zh":"店舖佈局透過引導顧客經過可能購買的產品來將利潤最大化。"},{"en":"This phrase links design with a clear goal of increase.","zh":"這個短語把設計與明確增加目標連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"research has shown that","meaning":"研究顯示","examples":[{"en":"Research has shown that pleasant aromas can increase spending.","zh":"研究顯示，宜人香氣可以增加消費。"},{"en":"Research has shown that means studies or evidence have demonstrated a finding.","zh":"research has shown that 指研究或證據已證明某項發現。"},{"en":"Research has shown that regular sleep helps students learn more effectively.","zh":"研究顯示，規律睡眠有助學生更有效學習。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a statement sound evidence-based rather than personal.","zh":"這個短語令說法聽起來有證據支持，而不是個人看法。"},{"en":"It is often used before reporting scientific or survey results.","zh":"它常用於報告科學或調查結果前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"encourage people to buy","meaning":"鼓勵人們購買","examples":[{"en":"Pleasant smells may encourage people to buy more.","zh":"宜人香味可能鼓勵人們購買更多。"},{"en":"To encourage people to buy means to make them more willing to purchase something.","zh":"encourage people to buy 指令人更願意購買某物。"},{"en":"Free samples can encourage people to buy food they had not planned to try.","zh":"免費試食可以鼓勵人們購買原本沒有打算嘗試的食物。"},{"en":"Encouragement works by reducing hesitation or increasing desire.","zh":"鼓勵透過減少猶豫或增加慾望發揮作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a soft push toward purchasing.","zh":"這個短語描述推動購買的溫和力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"in addition to","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"In addition to music, supermarkets use loyalty schemes.","zh":"除了音樂之外，超級市場還使用忠誠計劃。"},{"en":"In addition to means as well as something already mentioned.","zh":"in addition to 指除了已提到的某事之外，也包括另一事。"},{"en":"In addition to homework, students need regular reading practice.","zh":"除了功課之外，學生需要定期閱讀練習。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another item or method to the discussion.","zh":"這個短語為討論加入另一項目或方法。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing that several factors work together.","zh":"當要顯示幾個因素共同作用時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"create a comfortable environment","meaning":"營造舒適環境","examples":[{"en":"Retailers try to create a comfortable environment.","zh":"零售商嘗試營造舒適環境。"},{"en":"To create a comfortable environment means to make a place pleasant and easy to stay in.","zh":"create a comfortable environment 指令地方舒適、令人願意停留。"},{"en":"A library creates a comfortable environment with quiet rooms, good lighting and clean desks.","zh":"圖書館透過安靜房間、良好燈光和乾淨書桌營造舒適環境。"},{"en":"Comfortable environments make people stay longer and feel more positive.","zh":"舒適環境令人停留更久並感覺更正面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shaping a place to affect people’s mood.","zh":"這個短語描述塑造地方以影響人的心情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"regular customers","meaning":"經常光顧的顧客","examples":[{"en":"Loyalty cards are designed to reward regular customers.","zh":"顧客積分卡旨在獎勵經常光顧的顧客。"},{"en":"Regular customers are people who buy from the same business repeatedly.","zh":"regular customers 指反覆在同一企業購買的人。"},{"en":"A café may know regular customers by name because they visit every morning.","zh":"咖啡店可能認得經常光顧的顧客名字，因為他們每天早上到訪。"},{"en":"Businesses reward regular customers because they provide stable income.","zh":"企業獎勵常客，因為他們提供穩定收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeat buyers, not one-time visitors.","zh":"這個短語描述重複購買者，而不是一次性訪客。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"clothing advertisements","meaning":"服裝廣告","examples":[{"en":"Clothing advertisements often appeal to the need for belonging.","zh":"服裝廣告常訴諸歸屬感的需要。"},{"en":"Clothing advertisements are adverts that promote clothes, fashion brands or styles.","zh":"clothing advertisements 指推廣衣服、時裝品牌或風格的廣告。"},{"en":"A clothing advertisement may show a group of confident friends wearing the same brand.","zh":"服裝廣告可能展示一群自信朋友穿着同一品牌。"},{"en":"These adverts can suggest that buying certain clothes helps people fit in.","zh":"這些廣告可以暗示購買某些衣服有助人融入群體。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to fashion-related promotional messages.","zh":"這個短語指與時裝相關的宣傳訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"appeal to buyers’ desire","meaning":"迎合買家的渴望","examples":[{"en":"Fashion campaigns appeal to buyers’ desire to fit in.","zh":"時裝宣傳活動迎合買家想融入群體的渴望。"},{"en":"To appeal to buyers’ desire means to attract customers by connecting with something they want.","zh":"appeal to buyers’ desire 指透過連接顧客想要的東西來吸引他們。"},{"en":"A phone advert may appeal to buyers’ desire for status and convenience.","zh":"手機廣告可能迎合買家對地位和方便的渴望。"},{"en":"Advertising works better when it understands what buyers already want emotionally.","zh":"當廣告理解買家已有的情感慾望，效果會更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes persuasion through customer desire.","zh":"這個短語描述透過顧客慾望進行說服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"feature celebrities","meaning":"以名人作招徠","examples":[{"en":"Advertisements that feature celebrities may be more effective.","zh":"以名人作招徠的廣告可能更有效。"},{"en":"To feature celebrities means to include famous people as an important part of the advert.","zh":"feature celebrities 指把名人作為廣告的重要部分。"},{"en":"A sports drink advert may feature celebrities from the football world.","zh":"運動飲品廣告可能以足球界名人作招徠。"},{"en":"Celebrities attract attention and can transfer their image to the product.","zh":"名人吸引注意，並可以把他們的形象轉移到產品上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using fame as a marketing tool.","zh":"這個短語描述把名氣作為市場推廣工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 150 - The Persuaders.pdf","sourcePage":23}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 151":[{"front":"origin of species","meaning":"物種起源","examples":[{"en":"Darwin devoted much of his life to studying the origin of species.","zh":"Darwin 把一生中很多時間用於研究物種起源。"},{"en":"The origin of species means how different kinds of living things first appeared and developed.","zh":"origin of species 指不同種類生物最初如何出現和發展。"},{"en":"A biology lesson on the origin of species may explain why birds on different islands have different beaks.","zh":"關於物種起源的生物課，可能解釋為何不同島嶼上的鳥有不同鳥喙。"},{"en":"Studying the origin of species helps scientists understand how life changes over long periods.","zh":"研究物種起源幫助科學家理解生命如何在漫長時期中改變。"},{"en":"The phrase is about evolutionary beginnings, not the birthplace of one individual animal.","zh":"這個短語關於演化上的起源，而不是某隻動物個體的出生地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"continent formation","meaning":"大陸形成","examples":[{"en":"Continental movement has played an important role in continent formation.","zh":"大陸移動在大陸形成中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"Continent formation is the process by which large landmasses form, join, split, and change over time.","zh":"continent formation 指大型陸塊隨時間形成、連接、分裂和改變的過程。"},{"en":"A geography teacher may use maps to show continent formation from ancient supercontinents to modern continents.","zh":"地理老師可能用地圖展示由古代超大陸到現今大洲的大陸形成過程。"},{"en":"When tectonic plates move, they can help create, break, or reshape continents.","zh":"當構造板塊移動，它們可以幫助形成、分裂或重塑大陸。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to long-term geological change, not the creation of countries.","zh":"這個短語指長期地質變化，而不是國家的建立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the fact that","meaning":"……這個事實","examples":[{"en":"The fact that the continents were once joined has major biological implications.","zh":"大陸曾經連接在一起這個事實有重大的生物學含義。"},{"en":"The fact that introduces something true or accepted as important evidence.","zh":"the fact that 用來引入被視為真實或重要證據的事情。"},{"en":"The fact that a student improved after regular practice shows the method may be useful.","zh":"學生在定期練習後進步這個事實，顯示該方法可能有用。"},{"en":"When a fact changes how we explain a problem, it becomes central to the argument.","zh":"當一個事實改變我們解釋問題的方式，它就成為論點核心。"},{"en":"The phrase presents a statement as a key piece of information.","zh":"這個短語把某陳述呈現為關鍵資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Pangean supercontinent","meaning":"盤古超級大陸","examples":[{"en":"All the present continents were once part of a Pangean supercontinent.","zh":"所有現今大洲曾經都是盤古超級大陸的一部分。"},{"en":"A Pangean supercontinent is the ancient huge landmass called Pangea that once joined the continents together.","zh":"Pangean supercontinent 指名為 Pangea 的古代巨大陸塊，曾把各大洲連接起來。"},{"en":"In geography class, students may imagine the Pangean supercontinent as a giant jigsaw before the pieces drifted apart.","zh":"在地理課中，學生可把盤古超級大陸想像成在各塊漂離前的一塊巨大拼圖。"},{"en":"When the supercontinent broke up, plants and animals were carried to different future continents.","zh":"當超級大陸分裂，動植物被帶到日後不同大洲。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an ancient connected landmass, not a modern political region.","zh":"這個短語描述古代相連陸塊，而不是現代政治地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Panthalassa Ocean","meaning":"泛大洋","examples":[{"en":"The Panthalassa Ocean once surrounded the ancient supercontinent.","zh":"泛大洋曾經包圍古代超級大陸。"},{"en":"The Panthalassa Ocean was the vast ancient ocean around Pangea.","zh":"Panthalassa Ocean 指包圍盤古大陸的巨大古代海洋。"},{"en":"A map of ancient Earth may show Panthalassa covering most of the planet’s surface.","zh":"古代地球地圖可能顯示泛大洋覆蓋地球表面大部分。"},{"en":"Because Pangea was surrounded by this ocean, ocean barriers affected how species could spread.","zh":"因為盤古大陸被這個海洋包圍，海洋屏障影響物種如何擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase names an ancient ocean, not a present-day sea.","zh":"這個短語命名一個古代海洋，而不是現今海域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Tethys Ocean","meaning":"特提斯洋","examples":[{"en":"The Tethys Ocean once separated major ancient landmasses.","zh":"特提斯洋曾經分隔主要古代陸塊。"},{"en":"The Tethys Ocean was an ancient ocean lying between important prehistoric continents.","zh":"Tethys Ocean 指位於重要史前大陸之間的古代海洋。"},{"en":"A geology diagram may show the Tethys Ocean between northern and southern landmasses.","zh":"地質圖可能顯示特提斯洋位於北方和南方陸塊之間。"},{"en":"As this ocean opened and later closed, it helped shape species distribution and mountain formation.","zh":"隨着這個海洋張開並後來閉合，它幫助塑造物種分布和山脈形成。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a vanished ancient ocean with geological importance.","zh":"這個短語指一個已消失但具地質重要性的古代海洋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have profound implications for","meaning":"對……有深遠影響","examples":[{"en":"Continental movement has profound implications for the evolution of life.","zh":"大陸移動對生命演化有深遠影響。"},{"en":"To have profound implications for something means to have deep and important effects on it.","zh":"have profound implications for something 指對某事有深刻而重要的影響。"},{"en":"A new public transport system can have profound implications for where families choose to live.","zh":"新公共交通系統可以對家庭選擇住在哪裏有深遠影響。"},{"en":"If continents move, species may become isolated, mixed, or forced to adapt.","zh":"如果大陸移動，物種可能被隔離、混合或被迫適應。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that one fact changes the way we understand a major issue.","zh":"這個短語表示某事實會改變我們理解重大議題的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"multicellular life","meaning":"多細胞生命","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the evolution of multicellular life on Earth.","zh":"文章討論地球上多細胞生命的演化。"},{"en":"Multicellular life refers to living things made of many cells, such as animals, plants, and fungi.","zh":"multicellular life 指由許多細胞組成的生物，例如動物、植物和真菌。"},{"en":"A jellyfish is multicellular life because its body contains many specialised cells.","zh":"水母是多細胞生命，因為牠的身體包含許多專門化細胞。"},{"en":"Multicellular life allowed organisms to develop larger bodies and more complex functions.","zh":"多細胞生命使生物能發展出較大身體和更複雜功能。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts with single-celled life, such as bacteria.","zh":"這個短語與細菌等單細胞生命形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"scientific considerations","meaning":"科學上的考慮因素","examples":[{"en":"These scientific considerations were unknown in the nineteenth century.","zh":"這些科學上的考慮因素在十九世紀並不為人所知。"},{"en":"Scientific considerations are facts, principles, or questions that must be considered in scientific thinking.","zh":"scientific considerations 指科學思考中必須考慮的事實、原則或問題。"},{"en":"When planning a vaccine study, safety and sample size are important scientific considerations.","zh":"規劃疫苗研究時，安全性和樣本大小都是重要科學考慮因素。"},{"en":"If scientists lack key information, their conclusions may be impressive but incomplete.","zh":"如果科學家缺乏關鍵資訊，他們的結論可能了不起但不完整。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to scientific factors that affect judgement.","zh":"這個短語指影響判斷的科學因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be unknown to","meaning":"不為……所知","examples":[{"en":"The ancient arrangement of the continents was unknown to early scientists.","zh":"古代大陸排列不為早期科學家所知。"},{"en":"To be unknown to someone means that person or group does not know about it.","zh":"be unknown to someone 指某人或某群體不知道某事。"},{"en":"The exact cause of a student’s anxiety may be unknown to the teacher at first.","zh":"學生焦慮的確切原因最初可能不為老師所知。"},{"en":"When information is unknown, people may make careful guesses based on available evidence.","zh":"當資訊未知，人們可能根據現有證據作謹慎推測。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a lack of knowledge, not active rejection.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏知識，而不是主動否定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"scientific deductions","meaning":"科學推論","examples":[{"en":"Darwin and Wallace made remarkable scientific deductions.","zh":"Darwin 和 Wallace 作出了了不起的科學推論。"},{"en":"Scientific deductions are conclusions reached by reasoning from evidence.","zh":"scientific deductions 指根據證據推理得出的結論。"},{"en":"A doctor may make scientific deductions from symptoms, test results, and medical history.","zh":"醫生可能根據症狀、檢查結果和病歷作出科學推論。"},{"en":"Good deductions help scientists explain facts even before all modern tools are available.","zh":"良好推論幫助科學家在所有現代工具出現前解釋事實。"},{"en":"The phrase means evidence-based reasoning, not random guessing.","zh":"這個短語指以證據為基礎的推理，而不是隨機猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"even more remarkable","meaning":"更加了不起","examples":[{"en":"The lack of modern geological knowledge makes their conclusions even more remarkable.","zh":"缺乏現代地質知識令他們的結論更加了不起。"},{"en":"Even more remarkable means more impressive than it already seemed.","zh":"even more remarkable 指比原本已經看似令人佩服的情況更令人佩服。"},{"en":"A student’s high score is even more remarkable if she studied while caring for a sick parent.","zh":"如果學生一邊照顧生病父母一邊溫習仍取得高分，成績就更加了不起。"},{"en":"When people succeed despite serious limits, their achievement seems greater.","zh":"當人在嚴重限制下仍成功，其成就會顯得更大。"},{"en":"The phrase adds extra emphasis to an already impressive fact.","zh":"這個短語對已令人印象深刻的事實作額外強調。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"independently of each other","meaning":"各自獨立地","examples":[{"en":"Darwin and Wallace developed similar ideas independently of each other.","zh":"Darwin 和 Wallace 各自獨立地發展出相似想法。"},{"en":"Independently of each other means two people do something separately without copying or knowing the other’s work.","zh":"independently of each other 指兩人分開做某事，沒有抄襲或知道對方工作。"},{"en":"Two students may solve the same maths problem independently of each other using different methods.","zh":"兩名學生可能用不同方法各自獨立地解出同一道數學題。"},{"en":"If researchers reach the same idea separately, the idea may seem stronger.","zh":"如果研究人員分別得出同一想法，該想法可能顯得更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses separate discovery.","zh":"這個短語強調獨立發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"young contemporary","meaning":"年輕的同時代學者","examples":[{"en":"Alfred Russel Wallace was a young contemporary of Charles Darwin.","zh":"Alfred Russel Wallace 是 Charles Darwin 年輕的同時代學者。"},{"en":"A young contemporary is a younger person living and working in the same period as someone else.","zh":"young contemporary 指與某人生活和工作於同一時期、但較年輕的人。"},{"en":"A young contemporary of a famous writer may share the same historical pressures but begin later.","zh":"著名作家的年輕同時代人可能面對同一歷史壓力，但起步較遲。"},{"en":"Being contemporaries means two thinkers can respond to similar questions of their age.","zh":"同時代代表兩位思想家可以回應同一時代的相似問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes age and time relationship, not friendship.","zh":"這個短語描述年齡和時代關係，而不是友誼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reach the conclusion that","meaning":"得出……的結論","examples":[{"en":"Both scientists reached the conclusion that species evolved naturally.","zh":"兩位科學家都得出物種自然演化的結論。"},{"en":"To reach the conclusion that means to decide something after thinking about evidence.","zh":"reach the conclusion that 指在思考證據後判斷某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may reach the conclusion that students need more practice after marking several weak essays.","zh":"老師批改幾篇弱作文後，可能得出學生需要更多練習的結論。"},{"en":"When evidence points in one direction, researchers may finally form a conclusion.","zh":"當證據指向同一方向，研究人員可能最終形成結論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reasoned judgement, not an instant opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述有推理的判斷，而不是即時意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"evolve by natural selection","meaning":"透過自然選擇演化","examples":[{"en":"Darwin and Wallace argued that species evolve by natural selection.","zh":"Darwin 和 Wallace 主張物種透過自然選擇演化。"},{"en":"To evolve by natural selection means to change over generations because better-adapted individuals survive and reproduce more.","zh":"evolve by natural selection 指較適應環境的個體更能生存和繁殖，令物種經多代改變。"},{"en":"In a dry environment, plants that need less water may survive better and pass on their traits.","zh":"在乾燥環境中，需要較少水分的植物可能更容易存活並傳下特徵。"},{"en":"Over many generations, small survival advantages can change a whole population.","zh":"經過許多代，小小生存優勢可以改變整個種群。"},{"en":"The phrase explains a mechanism of evolution.","zh":"這個短語解釋演化的一種機制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"natural selection","meaning":"自然選擇","examples":[{"en":"Natural selection favours organisms that are better adapted to their environment.","zh":"自然選擇有利於更適應環境的生物。"},{"en":"Natural selection is the process in which useful traits become more common because they help survival or reproduction.","zh":"natural selection 指有用特徵因有助生存或繁殖而變得更常見的過程。"},{"en":"Dark-coloured insects may survive better on dark tree bark because birds see them less easily.","zh":"深色昆蟲在深色樹皮上可能較容易存活，因為鳥較難看見牠們。"},{"en":"If a trait helps an organism survive, it may be passed to more offspring.","zh":"如果某特徵幫助生物生存，它可能傳給更多後代。"},{"en":"The phrase means nature “selects” through survival, not through conscious choice.","zh":"這個短語指自然透過生存來「選擇」，不是有意識選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"write of one’s own inspiration","meaning":"寫述自己的靈感來源","examples":[{"en":"Wallace later wrote of his own inspiration in his autobiography.","zh":"Wallace 後來在自傳中寫述自己的靈感來源。"},{"en":"To write of one’s own inspiration means to describe the idea or moment that motivated one’s thinking.","zh":"write of one’s own inspiration 指描述激發自己想法的理念或時刻。"},{"en":"An artist may write of her own inspiration after seeing an ordinary street in a new way.","zh":"藝術家可能在以新角度看見普通街道後，寫述自己的靈感來源。"},{"en":"Explaining inspiration helps readers understand how an important idea began.","zh":"解釋靈感來源幫助讀者理解重要想法如何開始。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and means writing about the source of one’s idea.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是書寫自己想法的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on the whole","meaning":"整體而言","examples":[{"en":"Wallace concluded that, on the whole, the best-fitted organisms survived.","zh":"Wallace 總結指，整體而言，最適應環境的生物存活下來。"},{"en":"On the whole means generally or when considering everything together.","zh":"on the whole 指一般來說或整體考慮後。"},{"en":"On the whole, the class improved, although a few students still struggled with grammar.","zh":"整體而言，全班有進步，雖然少數學生仍在文法上有困難。"},{"en":"The phrase allows small exceptions while giving a general judgement.","zh":"這個短語在作一般判斷時容許少量例外。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing an overall pattern.","zh":"它適合用於描述整體模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the best fitted","meaning":"最適應環境的個體","examples":[{"en":"In difficult conditions, the best fitted were more likely to survive.","zh":"在困難環境中，最適應環境的個體較可能存活。"},{"en":"The best fitted are the individuals best suited to their environment.","zh":"the best fitted 指最適合其環境的個體。"},{"en":"In a cold classroom, students with warm coats are best fitted to stay comfortable.","zh":"在寒冷課室中，穿暖外套的學生最適合保持舒適。"},{"en":"In nature, better fit can mean finding food, avoiding predators, or resisting disease.","zh":"在自然界中，更適應可以指找到食物、避開捕食者或抵抗疾病。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to suitability, not moral superiority.","zh":"這個短語指適應程度，而不是道德上較優越。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"escape the effects of disease","meaning":"逃過疾病的影響","examples":[{"en":"The healthiest individuals were more likely to escape the effects of disease.","zh":"最健康的個體較可能逃過疾病的影響。"},{"en":"To escape the effects of disease means to avoid being seriously harmed by illness.","zh":"escape the effects of disease 指避免受到疾病嚴重傷害。"},{"en":"A vaccinated child may escape the worst effects of flu even if classmates become sick.","zh":"接種疫苗的孩子即使同學患病，也可能逃過流感最嚴重的影響。"},{"en":"Strong health can help organisms survive when disease spreads through a population.","zh":"當疾病在種群中傳播，強健健康可以幫助生物存活。"},{"en":"The phrase means avoiding damage, not literally running away from disease.","zh":"這個短語指避免傷害，而不是字面上逃離疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the strongest, the swiftest or the most cunning","meaning":"最強壯、最快或最狡猾的個體","examples":[{"en":"Predators favoured the strongest, the swiftest or the most cunning animals.","zh":"捕食者有利於最強壯、最快或最狡猾的動物。"},{"en":"The strongest, the swiftest or the most cunning means those with power, speed, or cleverness that helps survival.","zh":"the strongest, the swiftest or the most cunning 指具有力量、速度或智慧並有助生存的個體。"},{"en":"In a race, the swiftest runner may win; in a debate, the most cunning speaker may win support.","zh":"在賽跑中，最快的跑手可能勝出；在辯論中，最機敏的講者可能贏得支持。"},{"en":"Different environments reward different strengths, so survival is not based on one trait only.","zh":"不同環境會獎賞不同優勢，所以生存不只取決於單一特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase lists several possible survival advantages.","zh":"這個短語列出幾種可能的生存優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in times of famine","meaning":"在饑荒時期","examples":[{"en":"In times of famine, the most effective hunters were more likely to survive.","zh":"在饑荒時期，最有效率的獵食者較可能存活。"},{"en":"In times of famine means during periods when there is a severe shortage of food.","zh":"in times of famine 指在食物嚴重短缺的時期。"},{"en":"In times of famine, families may have to store grain carefully and share food fairly.","zh":"在饑荒時期，家庭可能要小心儲存穀物並公平分配食物。"},{"en":"Food shortage increases competition, so individuals with useful survival skills may do better.","zh":"食物短缺會增加競爭，因此有用生存技能的個體可能表現較好。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a crisis caused by lack of food.","zh":"這個短語描述由缺乏食物造成的危機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it suddenly flashed on me that","meaning":"我突然想到……","examples":[{"en":"It suddenly flashed on Wallace that natural selection could improve a species.","zh":"Wallace 突然想到自然選擇可以改善物種。"},{"en":"It suddenly flashed on me that means I suddenly understood or realised something.","zh":"it suddenly flashed on me that 指我突然明白或意識到某事。"},{"en":"It suddenly flashed on me that I had left my homework on the bus.","zh":"我突然想到自己把功課留在巴士上。"},{"en":"A sudden realisation can change how a person understands a problem.","zh":"突然的領悟可以改變一個人理解問題的方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a quick moment of insight.","zh":"這個短語描述快速出現的洞見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"self-acting process","meaning":"自行運作的過程","examples":[{"en":"Wallace described natural selection as a self-acting process.","zh":"Wallace 把自然選擇描述為自行運作的過程。"},{"en":"A self-acting process is a process that operates by itself without someone directing it.","zh":"self-acting process 指在沒有人指揮下自行運作的過程。"},{"en":"A thermostat is part of a self-acting process because it turns heating on and off automatically.","zh":"恆溫器屬於自行運作過程的一部分，因為它會自動開關暖氣。"},{"en":"Natural selection works without a planner because survival and reproduction produce the result.","zh":"自然選擇不需要計劃者，因為生存和繁殖會產生結果。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses automatic operation.","zh":"這個短語強調自動運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"improve the race","meaning":"改善整個物種","examples":[{"en":"He believed that the process would gradually improve the race.","zh":"他相信這個過程會逐漸改善整個物種。"},{"en":"In this context, improve the race means make a species or population better adapted over generations.","zh":"在此語境中，improve the race 指令一個物種或種群經多代變得更適應環境。"},{"en":"A farmer might improve a crop variety by saving seeds from the strongest plants each year.","zh":"農夫可能每年保留最強壯植物的種子，以改善作物品種。"},{"en":"If weaker individuals reproduce less, useful traits may become more common over time.","zh":"如果較弱個體繁殖較少，有用特徵可能隨時間變得更常見。"},{"en":"The phrase reflects old wording and should be understood carefully in its historical context.","zh":"這個短語反映舊時用語，應在歷史語境中小心理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in every generation","meaning":"在每一代中","examples":[{"en":"Natural selection operates in every generation.","zh":"自然選擇在每一代中運作。"},{"en":"In every generation means in each new group of offspring over time.","zh":"in every generation 指在每一批新後代中。"},{"en":"In every generation, families pass down stories, habits, and sometimes property.","zh":"在每一代中，家庭會傳下故事、習慣，有時也傳下財產。"},{"en":"If selection happens repeatedly, small changes can build up across many generations.","zh":"如果選擇反覆發生，小變化可以在許多代中累積。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses repeated occurrence over time.","zh":"這個短語強調隨時間重複出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"inferior individuals","meaning":"較弱勢的個體","examples":[{"en":"Inferior individuals were less likely to survive and reproduce.","zh":"較弱勢的個體較不可能存活和繁殖。"},{"en":"Inferior individuals means individuals less well adapted to the conditions being discussed.","zh":"inferior individuals 指在所討論環境中較不適應的個體。"},{"en":"In a drought, plants that need too much water may be inferior individuals in that environment.","zh":"在乾旱中，需要太多水的植物在該環境下可能是較弱勢個體。"},{"en":"If such individuals leave fewer offspring, their traits may become less common.","zh":"如果這類個體留下較少後代，其特徵可能變得較少見。"},{"en":"The phrase is comparative and scientific here, not a moral insult.","zh":"這個短語在此屬比較和科學用法，不是道德侮辱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be killed off","meaning":"被淘汰；被消滅","examples":[{"en":"Poorly adapted organisms may eventually be killed off.","zh":"適應不良的生物最終可能被淘汰。"},{"en":"To be killed off means to die out or be eliminated completely from a group or place.","zh":"be killed off 指從某群體或地方完全死亡或被消除。"},{"en":"A weak plant species may be killed off in a garden if stronger weeds take all the sunlight.","zh":"如果較強雜草奪走所有陽光，花園中的弱勢植物物種可能被淘汰。"},{"en":"Harsh conditions can remove individuals that cannot survive them.","zh":"嚴酷環境可以淘汰無法存活的個體。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds final and describes elimination, not temporary weakness.","zh":"這個短語聽起來很徹底，描述消除，而不是暫時弱勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"superior individuals","meaning":"較優勢的個體","examples":[{"en":"Superior individuals were more likely to remain and reproduce.","zh":"較優勢的個體較可能留下並繁殖。"},{"en":"Superior individuals are those better adapted to the conditions around them.","zh":"superior individuals 指更適應周圍條件的個體。"},{"en":"In a cold climate, animals with thicker fur may be superior individuals for survival.","zh":"在寒冷氣候中，毛較厚的動物在生存上可能是較優勢個體。"},{"en":"If better-adapted individuals reproduce more, their traits may spread.","zh":"如果較適應的個體繁殖更多，其特徵可能擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase means biologically better suited, not morally better.","zh":"這個短語指生物上更適合，而不是道德上更好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the fittest survive","meaning":"適者生存","examples":[{"en":"The principle that the fittest survive became central to evolutionary theory.","zh":"適者生存這一原則成為演化理論的核心。"},{"en":"The fittest survive means the organisms best adapted to their environment are most likely to live and reproduce.","zh":"the fittest survive 指最適應環境的生物最可能存活和繁殖。"},{"en":"In a polluted river, fish that tolerate dirty water may survive better than others.","zh":"在受污染河流中，能忍受污水的魚可能比其他魚更容易存活。"},{"en":"Survival advantages can change a population when they are passed to offspring.","zh":"當生存優勢傳給後代，它們可以改變種群。"},{"en":"The phrase is about environmental fit, not physical strength alone.","zh":"這個短語關於環境適應，而不只是體力強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be influenced by","meaning":"受……影響","examples":[{"en":"Darwin and Wallace were influenced by the work of Thomas Malthus.","zh":"Darwin 和 Wallace 受 Thomas Malthus 的著作影響。"},{"en":"To be influenced by something means to have one’s ideas, actions, or decisions shaped by it.","zh":"be influenced by something 指想法、行動或決定受到某事塑造。"},{"en":"A student may be influenced by a good teacher and decide to study science.","zh":"學生可能受好老師影響而決定讀科學。"},{"en":"Reading another thinker’s work can give researchers a new way to interpret evidence.","zh":"閱讀另一位思想家的著作可以給研究人員新的證據詮釋方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes impact on thinking or behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述對思考或行為的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"essays on population","meaning":"關於人口的論文","examples":[{"en":"Malthus’s essays on population influenced evolutionary thinking.","zh":"Malthus 關於人口的論文影響了演化思想。"},{"en":"Essays on population are written works discussing human numbers, growth, resources, and survival.","zh":"essays on population 指討論人口數量、增長、資源和生存的文章。"},{"en":"A social studies class may read essays on population to understand housing pressure.","zh":"社會科課堂可能閱讀關於人口的論文，以理解住屋壓力。"},{"en":"Ideas about population growth can influence how people think about competition for food.","zh":"關於人口增長的想法可以影響人們如何理解食物競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase names writing focused on population issues.","zh":"這個短語命名以人口議題為焦點的文章。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Principles of Population","meaning":"《人口原理》","examples":[{"en":"Both naturalists had read Malthus’s Principles of Population.","zh":"兩位博物學家都讀過 Malthus 的《人口原理》。"},{"en":"Principles of Population refers to Malthus’s work about population growth and limited resources.","zh":"Principles of Population 指 Malthus 關於人口增長和有限資源的著作。"},{"en":"A history teacher may mention Principles of Population when explaining nineteenth-century social thought.","zh":"歷史老師解釋十九世紀社會思想時，可能提到《人口原理》。"},{"en":"The book helped Darwin and Wallace think about competition and survival in nature.","zh":"這本書幫助 Darwin 和 Wallace 思考自然界中的競爭和生存。"},{"en":"The phrase is a title, so it should be treated as a specific work.","zh":"這個短語是書名，因此應視為特定著作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the direct result of","meaning":"……的直接結果","examples":[{"en":"Their conclusions were the direct result of years of observation.","zh":"他們的結論是多年觀察的直接結果。"},{"en":"The direct result of something means caused clearly and immediately by it.","zh":"direct result of something 指明顯而直接由某事造成。"},{"en":"A student’s fluency may be the direct result of daily speaking practice.","zh":"學生的流利度可能是每日口語練習的直接結果。"},{"en":"Long observation can lead directly to stronger scientific conclusions.","zh":"長期觀察可以直接帶來更有力的科學結論。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a clear cause-and-effect relationship.","zh":"這個短語指出清楚因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"personal observation","meaning":"親身觀察","examples":[{"en":"The theory developed partly through personal observation of wildlife.","zh":"該理論部分透過對野生動物的親身觀察而發展。"},{"en":"Personal observation is knowledge gained by directly seeing or studying something oneself.","zh":"personal observation 指親自直接看見或研究某事而獲得的知識。"},{"en":"A teacher’s personal observation of a student’s habits may reveal why homework is late.","zh":"老師對學生習慣的親身觀察，可能揭示為何功課遲交。"},{"en":"Direct observation can provide details that books or reports may miss.","zh":"直接觀察可以提供書本或報告可能看漏的細節。"},{"en":"The phrase means seeing evidence personally, not hearing it second-hand.","zh":"這個短語指親自看見證據，而不是間接聽來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"widely separated geographic locations","meaning":"相距遙遠的地理位置","examples":[{"en":"The two scientists worked in widely separated geographic locations.","zh":"兩位科學家在相距遙遠的地理位置工作。"},{"en":"Widely separated geographic locations are places far apart from each other on Earth.","zh":"widely separated geographic locations 指地球上彼此相距很遠的地方。"},{"en":"Two researchers working in Hong Kong and Brazil are in widely separated geographic locations.","zh":"分別在香港和巴西工作的兩位研究人員處於相距遙遠的地理位置。"},{"en":"If people far apart reach similar conclusions, the evidence may be especially persuasive.","zh":"如果相距很遠的人得出相似結論，證據可能特別有說服力。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises great physical distance.","zh":"這個短語強調實體距離很遠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the voyage of the Beagle","meaning":"「小獵犬號」航程","examples":[{"en":"Darwin made important observations during the voyage of the Beagle.","zh":"Darwin 在「小獵犬號」航程中作出重要觀察。"},{"en":"The voyage of the Beagle was Darwin’s scientific journey on the ship HMS Beagle.","zh":"the voyage of the Beagle 指 Darwin 乘坐 HMS Beagle 進行的科學旅程。"},{"en":"A history lesson may describe the voyage of the Beagle as a turning point in Darwin’s thinking.","zh":"歷史課可能把「小獵犬號」航程描述為 Darwin 思想的轉捩點。"},{"en":"Travel exposed Darwin to animals and plants that challenged fixed ideas about species.","zh":"旅行令 Darwin 接觸到挑戰物種固定觀念的動植物。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific scientific journey.","zh":"這個短語命名一次特定科學旅程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Galapagos Islands","meaning":"加拉帕戈斯群島","examples":[{"en":"Darwin studied unusual animals on the Galapagos Islands.","zh":"Darwin 在加拉帕戈斯群島研究不尋常動物。"},{"en":"The Galapagos Islands are islands in the Pacific famous for distinctive wildlife and evolutionary studies.","zh":"Galapagos Islands 指太平洋中以獨特野生動物和演化研究聞名的群島。"},{"en":"Students often learn about Galapagos finches when studying adaptation.","zh":"學生學習適應時，常認識加拉帕戈斯雀鳥。"},{"en":"Isolation on islands can allow species to develop unusual features.","zh":"島嶼隔離可以讓物種發展出不尋常特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase names a key location in the history of evolutionary science.","zh":"這個短語命名演化科學史上的關鍵地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the East Pacific","meaning":"東太平洋","examples":[{"en":"The Galapagos Islands lie in the East Pacific.","zh":"加拉帕戈斯群島位於東太平洋。"},{"en":"The East Pacific is the eastern part of the Pacific Ocean, near the Americas.","zh":"the East Pacific 指太平洋東部，接近美洲。"},{"en":"A geography map may show island chains in the East Pacific near South America.","zh":"地理地圖可能顯示南美洲附近東太平洋的島鏈。"},{"en":"Location in the ocean affects climate, isolation, and species movement.","zh":"位於海洋中的位置會影響氣候、隔離和物種移動。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a broad geographical position.","zh":"這個短語提供廣泛地理位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"years of travel","meaning":"多年的旅程","examples":[{"en":"Wallace developed his ideas during years of travel.","zh":"Wallace 在多年的旅程中發展出自己的想法。"},{"en":"Years of travel means a long period spent moving through different places.","zh":"years of travel 指長時間在不同地方旅行。"},{"en":"A photographer may develop a strong eye for detail after years of travel.","zh":"攝影師經過多年旅程後，可能培養出敏銳的細節眼光。"},{"en":"Long travel can expose a researcher to many examples that reshape their thinking.","zh":"長期旅行可以讓研究人員接觸許多例子，重塑其思考。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses long experience gained through movement.","zh":"這個短語強調透過移動獲得的長期經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Amazon Basin","meaning":"亞馬遜盆地","examples":[{"en":"Wallace conducted biological research in the Amazon Basin.","zh":"Wallace 在亞馬遜盆地進行生物研究。"},{"en":"The Amazon Basin is the huge region drained by the Amazon River and its tributaries.","zh":"Amazon Basin 指由亞馬遜河及其支流流經的廣大地區。"},{"en":"A scientist studying rainforest insects may work in the Amazon Basin for months.","zh":"研究雨林昆蟲的科學家可能在亞馬遜盆地工作數月。"},{"en":"Because the region is rich in species, it offers important evidence for biology.","zh":"因為該地區物種豐富，它為生物學提供重要證據。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major South American ecological region.","zh":"這個短語命名南美洲一個主要生態地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Indonesian-Australian Archipelago","meaning":"印度尼西亞—澳洲群島","examples":[{"en":"Wallace studied wildlife throughout the Indonesian-Australian Archipelago.","zh":"Wallace 在整個印度尼西亞—澳洲群島研究野生動物。"},{"en":"The Indonesian-Australian Archipelago is the island region between Southeast Asia and Australia.","zh":"Indonesian-Australian Archipelago 指東南亞與澳洲之間的群島地區。"},{"en":"A map of this archipelago shows many islands with different animal communities.","zh":"這個群島的地圖顯示許多島嶼有不同動物群落。"},{"en":"Island chains can reveal how species spread, separate, and evolve.","zh":"島鏈可以揭示物種如何擴散、分離和演化。"},{"en":"The phrase names a biologically important island region.","zh":"這個短語命名一個生物學上重要的島嶼地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"document one’s ideas","meaning":"記錄自己的想法","examples":[{"en":"Darwin had been documenting his ideas for many years.","zh":"Darwin 多年來一直記錄自己的想法。"},{"en":"To document one’s ideas means to write them down carefully so they can be developed or shared later.","zh":"document one’s ideas 指仔細寫下想法，以便日後發展或分享。"},{"en":"A student may document her essay ideas in a notebook before writing the final draft.","zh":"學生可能在寫最終稿前，把作文想法記錄在筆記簿中。"},{"en":"Careful documentation prevents important thoughts from being forgotten or misrepresented.","zh":"仔細記錄可以防止重要想法被遺忘或錯誤呈現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recording ideas systematically.","zh":"這個短語描述有系統地記錄想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"receive a paper on","meaning":"收到一篇關於……的論文","examples":[{"en":"Darwin received a paper on natural selection from Wallace.","zh":"Darwin 收到 Wallace 一篇關於自然選擇的論文。"},{"en":"To receive a paper on a topic means to be given an academic written work about that topic.","zh":"receive a paper on a topic 指收到一篇關於該主題的學術文章。"},{"en":"A professor may receive a paper on climate policy from a graduate student.","zh":"教授可能收到研究生一篇關於氣候政策的論文。"},{"en":"Receiving new research can force a scholar to respond, compare, or publish.","zh":"收到新研究可以迫使學者回應、比較或發表。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in academic contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the selfsame subject","meaning":"完全相同的主題","examples":[{"en":"Wallace’s paper dealt with the selfsame subject as Darwin’s research.","zh":"Wallace 的論文處理與 Darwin 研究完全相同的主題。"},{"en":"The selfsame subject means exactly the same topic.","zh":"the selfsame subject 指完全相同的題目。"},{"en":"Two students may unknowingly choose the selfsame subject for their history projects.","zh":"兩名學生可能在不知情下為歷史專題選了完全相同的主題。"},{"en":"If two researchers study the same subject separately, priority becomes important.","zh":"如果兩位研究人員分別研究同一主題，優先發表權就變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and emphasises exact sameness.","zh":"這個短語較正式，強調完全相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ask for someone’s opinion","meaning":"徵詢某人的意見","examples":[{"en":"Wallace asked for Darwin’s opinion on his paper.","zh":"Wallace 徵詢 Darwin 對其論文的意見。"},{"en":"To ask for someone’s opinion means to request that person’s view, advice, or judgement.","zh":"ask for someone’s opinion 指請求某人提供看法、建議或判斷。"},{"en":"A student may ask for a teacher’s opinion before submitting a scholarship essay.","zh":"學生提交獎學金作文前，可能徵詢老師意見。"},{"en":"Asking an expert can help improve work before it is shared publicly.","zh":"請教專家可以在公開分享前改善作品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes seeking advice, not demanding agreement.","zh":"這個短語描述尋求建議，而不是要求同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"help in getting something published","meaning":"協助把……發表","examples":[{"en":"Wallace requested Darwin’s help in getting the paper published.","zh":"Wallace 請求 Darwin 協助把論文發表。"},{"en":"Help in getting something published means assistance with making written work publicly available.","zh":"help in getting something published 指協助讓書面作品公開發表。"},{"en":"A young researcher may ask a supervisor for help in getting an article published.","zh":"年輕研究人員可能請導師協助把文章發表。"},{"en":"Publication support can involve editing, recommendation, or contact with a journal.","zh":"發表支援可以包括編輯、推薦或聯絡期刊。"},{"en":"The phrase is about the process of bringing work to readers.","zh":"這個短語關於把作品帶到讀者面前的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"press someone to","meaning":"催促某人去……","examples":[{"en":"Darwin’s friends pressed him to present his conclusions.","zh":"Darwin 的朋友催促他發表自己的結論。"},{"en":"To press someone to do something means to strongly urge or push that person to act.","zh":"press someone to do something 指強烈敦促或推動某人行動。"},{"en":"A teacher may press a talented student to enter a writing competition.","zh":"老師可能催促有天分的學生參加寫作比賽。"},{"en":"Pressure from trusted people can make someone act sooner than planned.","zh":"可信任人士的壓力可以令人比原計劃更早行動。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests strong encouragement, not physical pushing.","zh":"這個短語暗示強烈鼓勵，而不是身體推撞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"present one’s conclusions","meaning":"發表自己的結論","examples":[{"en":"Darwin was encouraged to present his conclusions publicly.","zh":"Darwin 被鼓勵公開發表自己的結論。"},{"en":"To present one’s conclusions means to explain the final results of one’s reasoning or research.","zh":"present one’s conclusions 指解釋自己推理或研究的最終結果。"},{"en":"A student may present her conclusions at the end of a science project.","zh":"學生可能在科學專題結尾發表自己的結論。"},{"en":"Public presentation allows others to examine, question, and build on the findings.","zh":"公開發表讓其他人檢視、提問並在發現上繼續發展。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in academic and formal discussion.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術和正式討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lose priority to","meaning":"把優先發表權讓給……","examples":[{"en":"His friends feared that Darwin might lose priority to another naturalist.","zh":"他的朋友擔心 Darwin 可能把優先發表權讓給另一位博物學家。"},{"en":"To lose priority to someone means to lose the right to be recognised as the first to make a discovery or claim.","zh":"lose priority to someone 指失去被承認為首先作出發現或主張的權利。"},{"en":"A researcher may lose priority if another team publishes the same result first.","zh":"如果另一團隊先發表相同結果，研究人員可能失去優先權。"},{"en":"In science, timing matters because early publication can establish credit.","zh":"在科學中，時間很重要，因為早發表可以確立功勞。"},{"en":"The phrase is about first recognition, not importance in general.","zh":"這個短語關於首先獲認可，而不是一般重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"unknown naturalist","meaning":"名不見經傳的博物學家","examples":[{"en":"Wallace was still a relatively unknown naturalist at the time.","zh":"Wallace 當時仍是一位相對名不見經傳的博物學家。"},{"en":"An unknown naturalist is a scientist who studies nature but has not yet become famous.","zh":"unknown naturalist 指研究自然但尚未成名的科學家。"},{"en":"An unknown naturalist may collect valuable field data long before receiving public attention.","zh":"名不見經傳的博物學家可能早在受到公眾注意前已收集寶貴野外數據。"},{"en":"A lack of fame does not mean a scientist’s work is unimportant.","zh":"缺乏名氣不代表科學家的工作不重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reputation, not ability.","zh":"這個短語描述聲譽，而不是能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"preside over","meaning":"主持……","examples":[{"en":"Lyell and Hooker presided over the historic scientific meeting.","zh":"Lyell 和 Hooker 主持了那場歷史性科學會議。"},{"en":"To preside over a meeting means to lead, chair, or formally manage it.","zh":"preside over a meeting 指領導、主持或正式管理會議。"},{"en":"A principal may preside over a staff meeting about school policy.","zh":"校長可能主持關於學校政策的教職員會議。"},{"en":"Someone presiding over a meeting controls order, speakers, and procedure.","zh":"主持會議的人控制秩序、發言者和程序。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests official leadership during an event.","zh":"這個短語暗示活動中的正式領導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hastily called meeting","meaning":"倉促召開的會議","examples":[{"en":"The scientists arranged a hastily called meeting in London.","zh":"科學家在倫敦安排了一場倉促召開的會議。"},{"en":"A hastily called meeting is a meeting arranged quickly because action is urgent.","zh":"hastily called meeting 指因行動緊急而快速安排的會議。"},{"en":"A school may hold a hastily called meeting after a serious safety incident.","zh":"發生嚴重安全事件後，學校可能舉行倉促召開的會議。"},{"en":"Such meetings happen when waiting too long could create problems.","zh":"當等待太久可能造成問題，這類會議就會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses urgency and limited preparation time.","zh":"這個短語強調緊急和準備時間有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"historic meeting","meaning":"歷史性會議","examples":[{"en":"The event later became recognised as a historic meeting.","zh":"該事件後來被視為一場歷史性會議。"},{"en":"A historic meeting is a meeting later seen as important in history.","zh":"historic meeting 指後來被認為在歷史上重要的會議。"},{"en":"A peace agreement may begin with a historic meeting between leaders.","zh":"和平協議可能由領袖之間的歷史性會議開始。"},{"en":"A meeting becomes historic when its decisions change a field or society.","zh":"當會議決定改變一個領域或社會，它就成為歷史性會議。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long-term significance, not just an old meeting.","zh":"這個短語描述長期重要性，而不只是舊會議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Linnean Society","meaning":"林奈學會","examples":[{"en":"The theory was presented at a meeting of the Linnean Society.","zh":"該理論在林奈學會的一場會議上發表。"},{"en":"The Linnean Society is a learned society connected with natural history and biological science.","zh":"Linnean Society 是與自然史和生物科學有關的學術學會。"},{"en":"A scientist may present new research to a society such as the Linnean Society.","zh":"科學家可能向林奈學會這類學會發表新研究。"},{"en":"Presenting work to a respected society gives it a formal scientific audience.","zh":"向受尊重學會發表作品，能為其提供正式科學聽眾。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific scientific institution.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定科學機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"distinguished members","meaning":"傑出的會員","examples":[{"en":"The explanation was presented to the society’s distinguished members.","zh":"這個解釋被呈現給該學會的傑出會員。"},{"en":"Distinguished members are respected or important members of a group.","zh":"distinguished members 指某群體中受尊重或重要的會員。"},{"en":"A university may invite distinguished members of the community to a prize ceremony.","zh":"大學可能邀請社區傑出成員參加頒獎典禮。"},{"en":"Presenting to distinguished members can make a scientific claim more visible.","zh":"向傑出會員發表可以令科學主張更受注意。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises status and respect.","zh":"這個短語強調地位和尊重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"independently and unknown to one another","meaning":"各自獨立而互不知情地","examples":[{"en":"The two scientists had worked independently and unknown to one another.","zh":"兩位科學家曾各自獨立而互不知情地工作。"},{"en":"Independently and unknown to one another means separately, without either person knowing the other was doing similar work.","zh":"independently and unknown to one another 指各自分開，且彼此不知道對方正在做相似工作。"},{"en":"Two students may independently and unknowingly write essays on the same unusual topic.","zh":"兩名學生可能各自獨立而互不知情地寫同一個不尋常題目。"},{"en":"Separate discovery can show that the evidence strongly points toward the same idea.","zh":"分別發現可以顯示證據強烈指向同一想法。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both independence and lack of awareness.","zh":"這個短語同時強調獨立和不知情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"conceive the same theory","meaning":"構想出相同理論","examples":[{"en":"Darwin and Wallace conceived the same theory independently.","zh":"Darwin 和 Wallace 各自構想出相同理論。"},{"en":"To conceive the same theory means to form the same explanatory idea.","zh":"conceive the same theory 指形成相同的解釋性想法。"},{"en":"Two doctors may conceive the same theory about a patient’s illness after seeing the same symptoms.","zh":"兩位醫生看見相同症狀後，可能構想出相同病因理論。"},{"en":"If different people form the same theory separately, the evidence behind it may be strong.","zh":"如果不同人分別形成同一理論，其背後證據可能很強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating an idea in the mind.","zh":"這個短語描述在腦海中創造想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ingenious theory","meaning":"極具創意的理論","examples":[{"en":"Natural selection was regarded as a highly ingenious theory.","zh":"自然選擇被視為一套極具創意的理論。"},{"en":"An ingenious theory is a clever and original explanation of something difficult.","zh":"ingenious theory 指對困難事情作出聰明而原創的解釋。"},{"en":"A student may offer an ingenious theory to explain why a machine keeps failing.","zh":"學生可能提出一個極具創意的理論來解釋機器為何不斷故障。"},{"en":"A good theory can connect many separate observations under one explanation.","zh":"好理論可以把許多分散觀察連結在一個解釋之下。"},{"en":"The phrase praises intelligence and creativity.","zh":"這個短語讚揚智慧和創意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"anomalous distribution of species","meaning":"物種的異常分布","examples":[{"en":"Both scientists noticed the anomalous distribution of species.","zh":"兩位科學家都注意到物種的異常分布。"},{"en":"Anomalous distribution of species means species are found in places that seem unusual or difficult to explain.","zh":"anomalous distribution of species 指物種出現在看似不尋常或難以解釋的地方。"},{"en":"If two related animals live on distant islands but not on nearby land, their distribution may seem anomalous.","zh":"如果兩種相關動物生活在遙遠島嶼上，卻不在附近陸地上，其分布可能顯得異常。"},{"en":"Unusual distribution patterns can lead scientists to ask how species moved or separated.","zh":"異常分布模式可以引導科學家追問物種如何移動或分離。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a puzzling geographical pattern of life.","zh":"這個短語描述令人困惑的生命地理模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in particular regions","meaning":"在特定地區","examples":[{"en":"Some related species appeared only in particular regions.","zh":"一些相關物種只出現在特定地區。"},{"en":"In particular regions means in specific areas, not everywhere.","zh":"in particular regions 指在特定區域，而不是到處都有。"},{"en":"Certain food traditions exist only in particular regions of a country.","zh":"某些飲食傳統只存在於一個國家的特定地區。"},{"en":"If a species lives only in a particular region, that region may reveal something about its history.","zh":"如果物種只生活在特定地區，該地區可能揭示其歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase narrows attention to specific places.","zh":"這個短語把注意力收窄至具體地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"evolutionary significance","meaning":"演化上的重要性","examples":[{"en":"The distribution of species had profound evolutionary significance.","zh":"物種分布有深遠的演化上的重要性。"},{"en":"Evolutionary significance means importance for understanding how life changes over time.","zh":"evolutionary significance 指對理解生命如何隨時間改變具有重要意義。"},{"en":"A fossil with features between two groups may have evolutionary significance.","zh":"具有兩個類群之間特徵的化石可能有演化上的重要性。"},{"en":"Species distribution can show how isolation, adaptation, and descent shaped life.","zh":"物種分布可以顯示隔離、適應和血緣如何塑造生命。"},{"en":"The phrase marks something as important to evolutionary explanation.","zh":"這個短語表示某事對演化解釋很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"subsequently","meaning":"其後","examples":[{"en":"Subsequently, Darwin concentrated almost entirely on writing and research.","zh":"其後，Darwin 幾乎完全專注於寫作和研究。"},{"en":"Subsequently means afterwards or later.","zh":"subsequently 指之後或後來。"},{"en":"A student failed the first mock exam and subsequently changed her study method.","zh":"學生第一次模擬考失敗，其後改變了學習方法。"},{"en":"The word helps show the order of events.","zh":"這個詞幫助顯示事件順序。"},{"en":"It is more formal than “later”.","zh":"它比 later 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"spend the rest of one’s days","meaning":"度過餘生","examples":[{"en":"Darwin spent the rest of his days studying the origin of species.","zh":"Darwin 度過餘生研究物種起源。"},{"en":"To spend the rest of one’s days doing something means to devote the remaining part of one’s life to it.","zh":"spend the rest of one’s days doing something 指把餘下人生用於某事。"},{"en":"After retirement, a teacher may spend the rest of her days writing books for students.","zh":"退休後，老師可能度過餘生為學生寫書。"},{"en":"A lifelong project can shape how a person uses all later years.","zh":"終身項目可以塑造一個人如何使用之後所有年份。"},{"en":"The phrase is literary and refers to the rest of one’s life.","zh":"這個短語較文學化，指餘下人生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"almost total seclusion","meaning":"幾乎完全隱居","examples":[{"en":"Darwin worked in almost total seclusion.","zh":"Darwin 幾乎完全隱居地工作。"},{"en":"Almost total seclusion means being nearly completely away from public life or frequent social contact.","zh":"almost total seclusion 指幾乎完全遠離公共生活或頻繁社交接觸。"},{"en":"A writer may finish a difficult book in almost total seclusion to avoid distractions.","zh":"作家可能在幾乎完全隱居中完成一本困難著作，以避開干擾。"},{"en":"Seclusion can allow deep concentration, but it may also reduce social exchange.","zh":"隱居可以讓人深度專注，但也可能減少社交交流。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a very private and isolated way of living or working.","zh":"這個短語描述非常私人而孤立的生活或工作方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"Darwin focused on evolution; in contrast, Wallace studied biogeography.","zh":"Darwin 專注於演化；相比之下，Wallace 研究生物地理學。"},{"en":"In contrast means by comparison, showing a clear difference.","zh":"in contrast 指相比之下，用來顯示清楚差異。"},{"en":"Some students prefer quiet study; in contrast, others learn better in discussion groups.","zh":"有些學生喜歡安靜溫習；相比之下，另一些人在討論小組中學得更好。"},{"en":"The phrase helps compare two people, ideas, or situations.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較兩個人、想法或情況。"},{"en":"It signals that the next point is different from the previous one.","zh":"它表示下一點與前一點不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"apply oneself to","meaning":"專心投入於……","examples":[{"en":"Wallace applied himself to the study of biogeography.","zh":"Wallace 專心投入於生物地理學研究。"},{"en":"To apply oneself to something means to work hard and seriously at it.","zh":"apply oneself to something 指努力而認真地從事某事。"},{"en":"A student who applies herself to grammar practice may improve quickly.","zh":"專心投入文法練習的學生可能很快進步。"},{"en":"Serious effort over time can turn interest into expertise.","zh":"長期認真努力可以把興趣變成專業能力。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses dedication and concentration.","zh":"這個短語強調投入和專注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"biogeography","meaning":"生物地理學","examples":[{"en":"Biogeography examines where species live and why they occur there.","zh":"生物地理學研究物種生活在哪裏以及為何出現在那裏。"},{"en":"Biogeography is the study of the geographical distribution of living things.","zh":"biogeography 指研究生物地理分布的學科。"},{"en":"A biogeography lesson may ask why certain animals live only on islands.","zh":"生物地理學課可能問為何某些動物只生活在島嶼上。"},{"en":"The field connects biology with geography, climate, evolution, and geology.","zh":"這個領域把生物學與地理、氣候、演化和地質連起來。"},{"en":"The word names a scientific field about life and place.","zh":"這個詞命名一門關於生命與地方的科學領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pattern and distribution of species","meaning":"物種的分布模式","examples":[{"en":"Wallace studied the pattern and distribution of species.","zh":"Wallace 研究物種的分布模式。"},{"en":"The pattern and distribution of species means where species occur and what regular arrangements can be seen.","zh":"pattern and distribution of species 指物種出現在哪裏，以及可見的規律排列。"},{"en":"A map of birds in a city can show their pattern and distribution across parks and streets.","zh":"城市鳥類地圖可以顯示牠們在公園和街道中的分布模式。"},{"en":"If species form clear patterns, scientists can look for causes such as climate or barriers.","zh":"如果物種形成清晰模式，科學家可以尋找氣候或屏障等原因。"},{"en":"The phrase links location with repeated biological arrangement.","zh":"這個短語把位置與反覆出現的生物排列連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"result in the publication of","meaning":"促成……出版","examples":[{"en":"His research resulted in the publication of a major scientific work.","zh":"他的研究促成一部重要科學著作出版。"},{"en":"To result in the publication of something means to lead to that work being printed or released.","zh":"result in the publication of something 指導致某作品被印刷或發表。"},{"en":"Years of interviews may result in the publication of a book about local history.","zh":"多年的訪問可能促成一本關於本地歷史的書出版。"},{"en":"When research is organised and completed, it can become a publishable work.","zh":"當研究被整理並完成，它可以成為可出版作品。"},{"en":"The phrase connects earlier work with a final publication.","zh":"這個短語把早前工作與最終出版物連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"massive two-volume work","meaning":"大型兩卷本著作","examples":[{"en":"Wallace published a massive two-volume work on animal distribution.","zh":"Wallace 出版了一部關於動物分布的大型兩卷本著作。"},{"en":"A massive two-volume work is a very large book published in two separate volumes.","zh":"massive two-volume work 指分成兩卷出版的非常大型書籍。"},{"en":"A university library may keep a massive two-volume dictionary on a reference shelf.","zh":"大學圖書館可能在參考書架上收藏大型兩卷本字典。"},{"en":"Large works often gather years of research into an organised form.","zh":"大型著作通常把多年研究整理成有系統形式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both size and structure of a publication.","zh":"這個短語同時描述出版物的大小和結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"gentle and modest","meaning":"溫和而謙遜","examples":[{"en":"Wallace was described as a gentle and modest man.","zh":"Wallace 被描述為一位溫和而謙遜的人。"},{"en":"Gentle and modest means kind in manner and not boastful about one’s abilities.","zh":"gentle and modest 指待人溫和，且不炫耀自己的能力。"},{"en":"A gentle and modest teacher corrects mistakes without making students feel ashamed.","zh":"溫和而謙遜的老師會糾正錯誤，而不令學生感到羞恥。"},{"en":"Modesty can make a person respected because success is not used to look down on others.","zh":"謙遜可以令人受尊重，因為成功不被用來貶低他人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes character and social behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述性格和社交行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"persistent and quietly courageous","meaning":"堅毅而低調勇敢","examples":[{"en":"He was also persistent and quietly courageous.","zh":"他也堅毅而低調勇敢。"},{"en":"Persistent and quietly courageous means continuing despite difficulty without making a show of bravery.","zh":"persistent and quietly courageous 指在困難中繼續堅持，但不高調展示勇氣。"},{"en":"A student who keeps practising after repeated failure is persistent and quietly courageous.","zh":"反覆失敗後仍繼續練習的學生，就是堅毅而低調勇敢。"},{"en":"Quiet courage often appears in steady effort rather than dramatic gestures.","zh":"低調勇氣常出現在穩定努力中，而不是戲劇性姿態。"},{"en":"The phrase praises calm endurance.","zh":"這個短語讚揚平靜的堅持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"arduous climates and terrains","meaning":"艱苦的氣候和地形","examples":[{"en":"Wallace spent years working in arduous climates and terrains.","zh":"Wallace 多年在艱苦的氣候和地形中工作。"},{"en":"Arduous climates and terrains are difficult weather conditions and landscapes that make work hard.","zh":"arduous climates and terrains 指令工作困難的天氣條件和地貌。"},{"en":"Researchers in deserts face arduous climates and terrains because of heat, sand, and distance.","zh":"沙漠研究人員因高溫、沙地和距離而面對艱苦的氣候和地形。"},{"en":"Harsh environments can make fieldwork dangerous, slow, and physically exhausting.","zh":"嚴酷環境可以令野外工作危險、緩慢且體力負擔大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes difficult natural working conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述困難的自然工作條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the Malay Archipelago","meaning":"馬來群島","examples":[{"en":"Wallace carried out extensive fieldwork in the Malay Archipelago.","zh":"Wallace 在馬來群島進行廣泛野外考察。"},{"en":"The Malay Archipelago is a large island region in Southeast Asia.","zh":"Malay Archipelago 指東南亞的大型島嶼地區。"},{"en":"A map of the Malay Archipelago includes many islands between mainland Asia and Australia.","zh":"馬來群島地圖包括亞洲大陸和澳洲之間許多島嶼。"},{"en":"Its island geography makes it important for studying species separation and distribution.","zh":"其島嶼地理令它對研究物種分隔和分布很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase names a key region in Wallace’s research.","zh":"這個短語命名 Wallace 研究中的關鍵地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"patient and detailed observations","meaning":"耐心而仔細的觀察","examples":[{"en":"He made patient and detailed observations of animals.","zh":"他對動物作出耐心而仔細的觀察。"},{"en":"Patient and detailed observations are careful notes made slowly and accurately over time.","zh":"patient and detailed observations 指經過時間慢慢而準確記下的仔細觀察。"},{"en":"A teacher may make patient and detailed observations before judging why a child struggles to read.","zh":"老師在判斷孩子為何閱讀困難前，可能作出耐心而仔細的觀察。"},{"en":"Careful observation can reveal patterns that quick inspection misses.","zh":"仔細觀察可以揭示快速檢查看不到的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses time, care, and accuracy.","zh":"這個短語強調時間、用心和準確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"zoological observations","meaning":"動物學觀察","examples":[{"en":"Wallace’s zoological observations helped establish biogeography.","zh":"Wallace 的動物學觀察幫助建立生物地理學。"},{"en":"Zoological observations are careful studies or notes about animals.","zh":"zoological observations 指關於動物的仔細研究或記錄。"},{"en":"A zoo keeper’s zoological observations may record how animals eat, move, and socialise.","zh":"動物園管理員的動物學觀察可能記錄動物如何進食、移動和社交。"},{"en":"Animal observations can help scientists understand behaviour, distribution, and evolution.","zh":"動物觀察可以幫助科學家理解行為、分布和演化。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to observation in animal science.","zh":"這個短語指動物科學中的觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"collect a huge number of specimens","meaning":"收集大量標本","examples":[{"en":"Wallace collected a huge number of specimens for museums.","zh":"Wallace 為博物館收集大量標本。"},{"en":"To collect a huge number of specimens means to gather many animal, plant, or fossil samples for study.","zh":"collect a huge number of specimens 指收集許多動物、植物或化石樣本作研究。"},{"en":"A biology class may collect leaf specimens to compare shapes and colours.","zh":"生物課可能收集葉子標本，以比較形狀和顏色。"},{"en":"Large collections allow scientists to compare variation across places and species.","zh":"大量收藏讓科學家比較不同地點和物種之間的變異。"},{"en":"The phrase describes large-scale scientific collecting.","zh":"這個短語描述大規模科學採集。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"museums and collectors","meaning":"博物館和收藏家","examples":[{"en":"Wallace sold specimens to museums and collectors.","zh":"Wallace 把標本賣給博物館和收藏家。"},{"en":"Museums and collectors are institutions and individuals that preserve, study, or display objects.","zh":"museums and collectors 指保存、研究或展示物件的機構和個人。"},{"en":"A fossil hunter may sell rare shells to museums and collectors.","zh":"化石獵人可能把稀有貝殼賣給博物館和收藏家。"},{"en":"Collections can support research when specimens are labelled and stored carefully.","zh":"當標本被仔細標記和保存，收藏可以支持研究。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to both public institutions and private buyers.","zh":"這個短語同時指公共機構和私人買家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make a living","meaning":"維持生計","examples":[{"en":"He made a living by collecting and selling biological specimens.","zh":"他靠收集和售賣生物標本維持生計。"},{"en":"To make a living means to earn enough money to support oneself.","zh":"make a living 指賺取足夠金錢來養活自己。"},{"en":"A musician may make a living by teaching lessons and performing at events.","zh":"音樂人可能透過教課和活動表演維持生計。"},{"en":"People often combine several activities to earn a stable income.","zh":"人們常結合幾種活動來賺取穩定收入。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on earning income, not becoming rich.","zh":"這個短語重點是賺取收入，而不是致富。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a distinct faunal boundary","meaning":"明顯的動物群分界線","examples":[{"en":"Wallace identified a distinct faunal boundary in Southeast Asia.","zh":"Wallace 在東南亞識別出一條明顯的動物群分界線。"},{"en":"A distinct faunal boundary is a clear dividing line between different animal regions.","zh":"distinct faunal boundary 指不同動物區之間清楚的分界線。"},{"en":"A river may act as a faunal boundary if animals on one side differ sharply from those on the other.","zh":"如果河流兩岸動物明顯不同，該河可能成為動物群分界線。"},{"en":"Such boundaries help scientists understand barriers, history, and species movement.","zh":"這類分界線幫助科學家理解屏障、歷史和物種移動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to animal distribution, not political borders.","zh":"這個短語指動物分布，而不是政治邊界。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Wallace’s Line","meaning":"華萊士線","examples":[{"en":"Wallace’s Line separates two major animal regions.","zh":"華萊士線分隔兩個主要動物地理區。"},{"en":"Wallace’s Line is a biogeographical boundary between Asian and Australian animal groups.","zh":"Wallace’s Line 指亞洲和澳洲動物群之間的生物地理分界線。"},{"en":"A student may study Wallace’s Line to understand why nearby islands can have very different animals.","zh":"學生可能研究華萊士線，以理解為何鄰近島嶼可以有非常不同的動物。"},{"en":"The line exists because deep history and barriers shaped species distribution.","zh":"這條線存在，是因為深層歷史和屏障塑造了物種分布。"},{"en":"The phrase names one of the most famous boundaries in biogeography.","zh":"這個短語命名生物地理學中最著名的分界線之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Asian realm","meaning":"亞洲動物地理區","examples":[{"en":"Animals west of the line mainly belong to an Asian realm.","zh":"分界線以西的動物主要屬於亞洲動物地理區。"},{"en":"An Asian realm is a biological region whose animals are mainly related to Asian species.","zh":"Asian realm 指動物主要與亞洲物種有關的生物區域。"},{"en":"Tigers, monkeys, and many Asian birds are examples of animals associated with the Asian realm.","zh":"老虎、猴子和許多亞洲鳥類都是與亞洲動物地理區相關的動物例子。"},{"en":"If an island’s animals resemble Asian species, scientists may place it in the Asian realm.","zh":"如果某島動物像亞洲物種，科學家可能把它歸入亞洲動物地理區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a faunal region, not a political area.","zh":"這個短語描述動物群地理區，而不是政治區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Australian realm","meaning":"澳洲動物地理區","examples":[{"en":"Animals east of the line mainly belong to an Australian realm.","zh":"分界線以東的動物主要屬於澳洲動物地理區。"},{"en":"An Australian realm is a biological region whose animals are mainly related to Australian species.","zh":"Australian realm 指動物主要與澳洲物種有關的生物區域。"},{"en":"Marsupials are often associated with the Australian realm.","zh":"有袋類動物常與澳洲動物地理區有關。"},{"en":"If island animals resemble Australian species more than Asian species, the island may belong to this realm.","zh":"如果島嶼動物比起亞洲物種更像澳洲物種，該島可能屬於這個動物地理區。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an animal-distribution region, not only modern Australia.","zh":"這個短語指動物分布區域，而不只是現代澳洲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in essence","meaning":"本質上；簡單來說","examples":[{"en":"In essence, Wallace’s discovery raised a difficult geographical question.","zh":"本質上，Wallace 的發現提出了一個困難地理問題。"},{"en":"In essence means in the most basic or central meaning.","zh":"in essence 指在最基本或最核心的意思上。"},{"en":"In essence, a good essay answers the question clearly and supports its answer.","zh":"簡單來說，一篇好作文要清楚回答問題並支持答案。"},{"en":"The phrase helps summarise a complex idea simply.","zh":"這個短語幫助把複雜想法簡單概括。"},{"en":"It often introduces the core point after details.","zh":"它常在細節之後引入核心重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pose a difficult question","meaning":"提出一個難題","examples":[{"en":"The boundary posed a difficult question about the history of species.","zh":"這條分界線提出了一個關於物種歷史的難題。"},{"en":"To pose a difficult question means to create or raise a problem that is hard to answer.","zh":"pose a difficult question 指造成或提出一個難以回答的問題。"},{"en":"A sudden drop in exam results may pose a difficult question for school leaders.","zh":"考試成績突然下降可能給學校領導提出一個難題。"},{"en":"Difficult questions push researchers to look for better evidence and explanations.","zh":"難題推動研究人員尋找更好證據和解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase is about raising a challenge, not asking casually.","zh":"這個短語關於提出挑戰，而不是隨便提問。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have a clear affinity with","meaning":"與……有明顯親緣關係","examples":[{"en":"Some animals have a clear affinity with species from another hemisphere.","zh":"有些動物與另一半球的物種有明顯親緣關係。"},{"en":"To have a clear affinity with something means to show a strong natural relationship or similarity to it.","zh":"have a clear affinity with something 指與某物顯示強烈自然關係或相似性。"},{"en":"A local dialect may have a clear affinity with a neighbouring region’s speech.","zh":"本地方言可能與鄰近地區的說話有明顯關係。"},{"en":"If animals resemble species from far away, scientists may ask how that relationship developed.","zh":"如果動物像遠方物種，科學家可能追問這種關係如何形成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes obvious connection or closeness.","zh":"這個短語描述明顯聯繫或親近性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Northern Hemisphere","meaning":"北半球","examples":[{"en":"Many Asian species originated in the Northern Hemisphere.","zh":"許多亞洲物種起源於北半球。"},{"en":"The Northern Hemisphere is the half of Earth north of the equator.","zh":"Northern Hemisphere 指赤道以北的地球半球。"},{"en":"Europe, North America, and most of Asia lie in the Northern Hemisphere.","zh":"歐洲、北美洲和亞洲大部分都位於北半球。"},{"en":"Hemisphere location can affect climate, migration, and species history.","zh":"半球位置可以影響氣候、遷徙和物種歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a broad global position.","zh":"這個短語提供廣泛全球位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Southern Hemisphere counterparts","meaning":"南半球的同類物種","examples":[{"en":"They met their Southern Hemisphere counterparts near Wallace’s Line.","zh":"牠們在華萊士線附近遇上南半球的同類物種。"},{"en":"Southern Hemisphere counterparts are similar or related species found in the southern half of Earth.","zh":"Southern Hemisphere counterparts 指地球南半球中相似或相關的物種。"},{"en":"A northern bird species may have Southern Hemisphere counterparts that fill similar ecological roles.","zh":"某種北方鳥類可能有在南半球扮演相似生態角色的同類物種。"},{"en":"When counterparts meet, scientists can compare their origins and differences.","zh":"當同類物種相遇，科學家可以比較其起源和差異。"},{"en":"The phrase means matching forms from the Southern Hemisphere.","zh":"這個短語指來自南半球的相應形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"distinct demarcation zone","meaning":"明顯的分界帶","examples":[{"en":"Wallace’s Line forms a distinct demarcation zone.","zh":"華萊士線形成一個明顯的分界帶。"},{"en":"A distinct demarcation zone is a clear area or line marking separation between two regions.","zh":"distinct demarcation zone 指標示兩個區域分隔的清楚地帶或界線。"},{"en":"A river can form a distinct demarcation zone between two neighbourhoods.","zh":"河流可以在兩個社區之間形成明顯分界帶。"},{"en":"Clear zones help people see where one pattern ends and another begins.","zh":"清楚分界有助人看見一種模式在哪裏結束，另一種在哪裏開始。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises a visible or meaningful division.","zh":"這個短語強調可見或有意義的分隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be uncertain about","meaning":"對……不確定","examples":[{"en":"Wallace was uncertain about how to classify the island of Celebes.","zh":"Wallace 對如何分類西里伯斯島不確定。"},{"en":"To be uncertain about something means not to be sure about it.","zh":"be uncertain about something 指對某事不肯定。"},{"en":"A student may be uncertain about which university course to choose.","zh":"學生可能對選哪個大學課程不確定。"},{"en":"Uncertainty often appears when evidence points in more than one direction.","zh":"當證據指向多於一個方向，不確定常會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lack of confidence in a judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述對判斷缺乏信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Celebes","meaning":"西里伯斯島；蘇拉威西島","examples":[{"en":"Celebes is now more commonly known as Sulawesi.","zh":"Celebes 現在更常被稱為 Sulawesi。"},{"en":"Celebes is an older name for the island now called Sulawesi in Indonesia.","zh":"Celebes 是印度尼西亞今日稱為 Sulawesi 的島嶼的舊名。"},{"en":"A history map may use Celebes, while a modern map usually uses Sulawesi.","zh":"歷史地圖可能使用 Celebes，而現代地圖通常使用 Sulawesi。"},{"en":"Knowing older place names helps readers understand historical scientific writing.","zh":"了解舊地名有助讀者理解歷史科學寫作。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific island with an older English name.","zh":"這個短語命名一個有舊英文名稱的特定島嶼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"curiously shaped","meaning":"形狀奇特的","examples":[{"en":"Celebes is a curiously shaped island.","zh":"西里伯斯島是一個形狀奇特的島嶼。"},{"en":"Curiously shaped means having an unusual or interesting shape.","zh":"curiously shaped 指形狀不尋常或有趣。"},{"en":"A curiously shaped building may attract tourists because it looks unlike the others nearby.","zh":"形狀奇特的建築可能因看起來不像附近其他建築而吸引遊客。"},{"en":"Unusual shape can affect geography, travel routes, and how people describe a place.","zh":"不尋常形狀可以影響地理、交通路線和人們如何描述某地。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests the shape invites attention or curiosity.","zh":"這個短語暗示形狀引人注意或好奇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"midway between","meaning":"位於……兩者之間","examples":[{"en":"The island lies midway between the two faunal regions.","zh":"該島位於兩個動物地理區之間的中間位置。"},{"en":"Midway between means in the middle position between two places or things.","zh":"midway between 指位於兩個地方或事物之間的中間位置。"},{"en":"A café midway between school and home is a convenient meeting place.","zh":"位於學校和家之間的咖啡店是方便的會面地點。"},{"en":"A place in the middle of two regions may show mixed features from both sides.","zh":"位於兩個區域之間的地方可能顯示兩邊混合特徵。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a central position between two points.","zh":"這個短語描述兩點之間的中央位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"assign flora and fauna to","meaning":"將動植物歸入……","examples":[{"en":"Wallace initially assigned its flora and fauna to the Australian region.","zh":"Wallace 最初將其動植物歸入澳洲地區。"},{"en":"To assign flora and fauna to a region means to classify its plants and animals as belonging to that region.","zh":"assign flora and fauna to a region 指把某地動植物分類為屬於該區域。"},{"en":"A biologist may assign a wetland’s birds and plants to a coastal ecosystem category.","zh":"生物學家可能把濕地的鳥類和植物歸入沿海生態系統類別。"},{"en":"Classification helps researchers compare places and understand biological origins.","zh":"分類幫助研究人員比較地點並理解生物起源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes scientific grouping.","zh":"這個短語描述科學分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"flora and fauna","meaning":"動植物群","examples":[{"en":"The island’s flora and fauna were difficult to classify.","zh":"該島的動植物群很難分類。"},{"en":"Flora and fauna means the plants and animals of a place.","zh":"flora and fauna 指某地的植物和動物。"},{"en":"A nature reserve protects local flora and fauna such as trees, birds, insects, and mammals.","zh":"自然保護區保護樹木、鳥類、昆蟲和哺乳動物等本地動植物群。"},{"en":"If an island has mixed flora and fauna, its geological history may be complex.","zh":"如果島嶼有混合動植物群，其地質歷史可能很複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and refers to living things in a region.","zh":"這個短語較正式，指某地區的生物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"transfer something to","meaning":"將……轉移至；改歸入","examples":[{"en":"Wallace later transferred the island to the Asian side of the line.","zh":"Wallace 後來將該島改歸入分界線的亞洲一側。"},{"en":"To transfer something to a category or place means to move it from one group or position to another.","zh":"transfer something to a category or place 指把某物從一個群組或位置移到另一個。"},{"en":"A teacher may transfer a student to another class if the level is more suitable.","zh":"如果程度更合適，老師可能把學生轉到另一班。"},{"en":"New evidence can make researchers change how they classify something.","zh":"新證據可以令研究人員改變某物的分類方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving or reassigning.","zh":"這個短語描述移動或重新歸類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the reason for his dilemma","meaning":"他陷入兩難的原因","examples":[{"en":"Modern geology explains the reason for his dilemma.","zh":"現代地質學解釋了他陷入兩難的原因。"},{"en":"The reason for his dilemma means the cause of his difficult choice or uncertainty.","zh":"reason for his dilemma 指他面對困難選擇或不確定的原因。"},{"en":"A teacher may understand the reason for a student’s dilemma after learning she has two exams on the same day.","zh":"老師知道學生同日有兩場考試後，可能理解她陷入兩難的原因。"},{"en":"When evidence supports two different options, a dilemma becomes hard to resolve.","zh":"當證據支持兩個不同選項，兩難就難以解決。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why someone was unsure.","zh":"這個短語解釋某人為何不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"natural history","meaning":"自然歷史","examples":[{"en":"East and West Celebes once had separate natural histories.","zh":"東西西里伯斯曾經有分開的自然歷史。"},{"en":"Natural history is the history of plants, animals, rocks, environments, and their development in nature.","zh":"natural history 指植物、動物、岩石、環境及其在自然中發展的歷史。"},{"en":"A museum of natural history may display fossils, insects, shells, and animal skeletons.","zh":"自然歷史博物館可能展示化石、昆蟲、貝殼和動物骨架。"},{"en":"If two regions have different natural histories, their species may have different origins.","zh":"如果兩個地區有不同自然歷史，其物種可能有不同起源。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to nature’s past, not human political history.","zh":"這個短語指自然的過去，而不是人類政治歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lie on opposite sides of","meaning":"位於……的兩側","examples":[{"en":"The two regions once lay on opposite sides of the Tethys Ocean.","zh":"這兩個地區曾經位於特提斯洋的兩側。"},{"en":"To lie on opposite sides of something means to be positioned on the two different sides of it.","zh":"lie on opposite sides of something 指位於某物的兩個不同側面。"},{"en":"Two schools may lie on opposite sides of a busy road.","zh":"兩所學校可能位於一條繁忙道路的兩側。"},{"en":"If land areas lie on opposite sides of an ocean, their species may evolve separately.","zh":"如果陸地位於海洋兩側，其物種可能分開演化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical position across a barrier.","zh":"這個短語描述隔着屏障的實體位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"collide with","meaning":"與……碰撞","examples":[{"en":"The two ancient islands did not collide with each other until much later.","zh":"這兩個古代島嶼直到很久之後才彼此碰撞。"},{"en":"To collide with something means to crash into it or come into forceful contact with it.","zh":"collide with something 指撞上某物或與它發生強力接觸。"},{"en":"Two cyclists may collide with each other if neither brakes at a corner.","zh":"如果兩名單車手在轉角都不煞車，他們可能互相碰撞。"},{"en":"When landmasses collide, their plants and animals may come into contact.","zh":"當陸塊碰撞，其動植物可能開始接觸。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong contact after movement.","zh":"這個短語描述移動後的強烈接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"categorise","meaning":"分類","examples":[{"en":"Wallace’s Line categorises flora and fauna according to their origins.","zh":"華萊士線根據動植物起源把它們分類。"},{"en":"To categorise means to put things into groups based on shared features.","zh":"categorise 指根據共同特徵把事物分組。"},{"en":"A teacher may categorise vocabulary into verbs, nouns, and adjectives.","zh":"老師可能把詞彙分類為動詞、名詞和形容詞。"},{"en":"Categorising information makes complex patterns easier to understand.","zh":"分類資訊令複雜模式更容易理解。"},{"en":"The word describes grouping, not judging value.","zh":"這個詞描述分組，而不是判斷價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Laurasia-derived flora and fauna","meaning":"源自勞亞古陸的動植物","examples":[{"en":"The Asian species were largely Laurasia-derived flora and fauna.","zh":"亞洲物種大多是源自勞亞古陸的動植物。"},{"en":"Laurasia-derived flora and fauna are plants and animals whose origins trace back to Laurasia.","zh":"Laurasia-derived flora and fauna 指起源可追溯至勞亞古陸的植物和動物。"},{"en":"A biology map may show Laurasia-derived animals spreading through northern landmasses.","zh":"生物地圖可能顯示源自勞亞古陸的動物穿過北方陸塊擴散。"},{"en":"If species come from Laurasia, their present distribution may reflect ancient northern land connections.","zh":"如果物種源自勞亞古陸，其現今分布可能反映古代北方陸地連接。"},{"en":"The phrase describes origin, not current political location.","zh":"這個短語描述起源，而不是現今政治位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Gondwana-derived flora and fauna","meaning":"源自岡瓦納古陸的動植物","examples":[{"en":"The Australian species were largely Gondwana-derived flora and fauna.","zh":"澳洲物種大多是源自岡瓦納古陸的動植物。"},{"en":"Gondwana-derived flora and fauna are plants and animals whose origins trace back to Gondwana.","zh":"Gondwana-derived flora and fauna 指起源可追溯至岡瓦納古陸的植物和動物。"},{"en":"A scientist may identify Gondwana-derived species by comparing fossils, DNA, and distribution.","zh":"科學家可能透過比較化石、DNA 和分布來識別源自岡瓦納的物種。"},{"en":"If related species live in Australia, South America, and Africa, Gondwana may help explain the link.","zh":"如果相關物種生活在澳洲、南美洲和非洲，岡瓦納古陸可能幫助解釋這種聯繫。"},{"en":"The phrase connects modern species with an ancient southern landmass.","zh":"這個短語把現代物種與古代南方陸塊連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"evolve on opposite shores","meaning":"在相對兩岸演化","examples":[{"en":"The two groups evolved on opposite shores of the Tethys Ocean.","zh":"這兩個群體在特提斯洋相對兩岸演化。"},{"en":"To evolve on opposite shores means to develop separately on two sides of a sea or ocean.","zh":"evolve on opposite shores 指在海洋或海域兩側分開發展。"},{"en":"Two fishing villages on opposite shores may develop different traditions over generations.","zh":"位於相對兩岸的兩個漁村，可能經幾代發展出不同傳統。"},{"en":"Separation by water can lead populations to adapt in different ways.","zh":"被水域分隔可以令種群以不同方式適應。"},{"en":"The phrase connects geography with separate development.","zh":"這個短語把地理與分開發展連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"closure of the Tethys Ocean","meaning":"特提斯洋的閉合","examples":[{"en":"The closure of the Tethys Ocean continues to shape the region.","zh":"特提斯洋的閉合繼續塑造該地區。"},{"en":"The closure of the Tethys Ocean means the ancient ocean gradually narrowed and disappeared as landmasses moved together.","zh":"closure of the Tethys Ocean 指古代海洋隨陸塊互相靠近而逐漸收窄並消失。"},{"en":"A geology class may use this closure to explain mountains and complex island regions.","zh":"地質課可能用這個閉合過程解釋山脈和複雜島嶼地區。"},{"en":"When an ocean closes, continents collide and species from different regions may meet.","zh":"當海洋閉合，大陸會碰撞，來自不同地區的物種可能相遇。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a long geological process, not a sudden event.","zh":"這個短語描述漫長地質過程，而不是突然事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be manifested by","meaning":"透過……表現出來","examples":[{"en":"The ancient geological process is manifested by continuing continental collisions.","zh":"這個古代地質過程透過持續的大陸碰撞表現出來。"},{"en":"To be manifested by something means to be shown or expressed through it.","zh":"be manifested by something 指透過某事顯示或表現出來。"},{"en":"A student’s anxiety may be manifested by silence, late homework, and poor sleep.","zh":"學生的焦慮可能透過沉默、遲交功課和睡眠差表現出來。"},{"en":"Hidden processes often become visible through their effects.","zh":"隱藏過程常透過其效果變得可見。"},{"en":"The phrase means “shown through”, not simply caused by.","zh":"這個短語意思是「透過……顯示」，不只是「由……造成」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ongoing collision","meaning":"持續進行的碰撞","examples":[{"en":"The ongoing collision of tectonic regions continues today.","zh":"構造區域之間持續進行的碰撞至今仍在繼續。"},{"en":"An ongoing collision is a collision that is still happening over time.","zh":"ongoing collision 指仍隨時間發生的碰撞。"},{"en":"Two companies may face an ongoing collision of interests if both want the same market.","zh":"如果兩家公司都想爭取同一市場，它們可能面對持續進行的利益碰撞。"},{"en":"In geology, collision can continue for millions of years and shape mountains or islands.","zh":"在地質學中，碰撞可以持續數百萬年並塑造山脈或島嶼。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the process has not finished.","zh":"這個短語強調過程尚未結束。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"continuing closure","meaning":"持續閉合","examples":[{"en":"The Mediterranean Sea reflects the continuing closure of the ancient ocean.","zh":"地中海反映古代海洋的持續閉合。"},{"en":"Continuing closure means an ocean or gap is still gradually narrowing.","zh":"continuing closure 指海洋或間隙仍在逐漸收窄。"},{"en":"A slowly closing gap between two teams in a competition shows continuing closure in scores.","zh":"比賽中兩隊分差慢慢收窄，顯示分數上的持續閉合。"},{"en":"In geology, continuing closure can create pressure, earthquakes, and mountain building.","zh":"在地質學中，持續閉合可以造成壓力、地震和造山作用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a process still moving toward closing.","zh":"這個短語描述仍在朝閉合方向進行的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a remnant of","meaning":"……的遺留部分","examples":[{"en":"The Mediterranean Sea is a remnant of the Western Tethys Ocean.","zh":"地中海是西特提斯洋的遺留部分。"},{"en":"A remnant of something is a remaining part of something that was once larger.","zh":"remnant of something 指曾經較大事物留下來的一部分。"},{"en":"An old city wall may be a remnant of a much larger defensive system.","zh":"舊城牆可能是一套更大型防禦系統的遺留部分。"},{"en":"Remnants help researchers reconstruct what existed in the past.","zh":"遺留部分幫助研究人員重建過去存在的事物。"},{"en":"The phrase points to what is left after change or destruction.","zh":"這個短語指出改變或破壞後留下的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"quote at length from","meaning":"大量引用……","examples":[{"en":"Wegener quoted at length from Wallace’s work.","zh":"Wegener 大量引用 Wallace 的著作。"},{"en":"To quote at length from a work means to include a long passage from it.","zh":"quote at length from a work 指引用該作品中的長段文字。"},{"en":"A student should not quote at length from a book unless the exact wording is necessary.","zh":"除非原文措辭必要，學生不應大量引用一本書。"},{"en":"Long quotations can show respect for a source but may also interrupt the writer’s own explanation.","zh":"長引文可以顯示對來源的重視，但也可能打斷作者自己的解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to using an extended direct quotation.","zh":"這個短語指使用較長直接引文。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"according to someone’s reading","meaning":"按照某人的理解","examples":[{"en":"According to Wegener’s reading, Wallace’s evidence supported continental movement.","zh":"按照 Wegener 的理解，Wallace 的證據支持大陸移動。"},{"en":"According to someone’s reading means according to that person’s interpretation of the evidence or text.","zh":"according to someone’s reading 指按照某人對證據或文本的詮釋。"},{"en":"According to the teacher’s reading, the poem is about memory rather than love.","zh":"按照老師的理解，這首詩是關於記憶，而不是愛情。"},{"en":"Different readings can lead to different conclusions from the same material.","zh":"不同理解可以從同一材料導向不同結論。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses interpretation, not necessarily final truth.","zh":"這個短語強調詮釋，不一定是最終真理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"clear divisions","meaning":"明顯分類","examples":[{"en":"Wallace identified three clear divisions among Australian animals.","zh":"Wallace 在澳洲動物中識別出三個明顯分類。"},{"en":"Clear divisions are obvious separations between groups or categories.","zh":"clear divisions 指群組或類別之間明顯的分隔。"},{"en":"A teacher may see clear divisions between beginner, intermediate, and advanced students.","zh":"老師可能看見初級、中級和高級學生之間的明顯分別。"},{"en":"Clear divisions make classification easier and reveal patterns.","zh":"明顯分類令分類更容易，並揭示模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes obvious boundaries or group differences.","zh":"這個短語描述明顯界線或群體差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"support a theory","meaning":"支持一套理論","examples":[{"en":"The animal distributions supported Wegener’s theory.","zh":"動物分布支持 Wegener 的理論。"},{"en":"To support a theory means to provide evidence that makes the theory more believable.","zh":"support a theory 指提供證據，使該理論更可信。"},{"en":"A student’s survey results may support her theory that homework stress affects sleep.","zh":"學生的調查結果可能支持她關於功課壓力影響睡眠的理論。"},{"en":"Strong evidence can support a theory even if some questions remain.","zh":"即使仍有一些問題，強證據也可以支持一套理論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence strengthening an explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述證據加強解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"continental displacement","meaning":"大陸位移","examples":[{"en":"Wegener used biological evidence to support continental displacement.","zh":"Wegener 使用生物證據支持大陸位移。"},{"en":"Continental displacement means the movement of continents from earlier positions to new positions.","zh":"continental displacement 指大陸由早前位置移動到新位置。"},{"en":"A classroom model may show continental displacement by sliding paper continents across a map.","zh":"課室模型可能透過在地圖上滑動紙大陸來展示大陸位移。"},{"en":"If continents move, species once close together may later be separated by oceans.","zh":"如果大陸移動，曾經接近的物種後來可能被海洋隔開。"},{"en":"The phrase is another way to discuss continental movement.","zh":"這個短語是討論大陸移動的另一種說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"long established in","meaning":"長期存在於……","examples":[{"en":"Some animal groups had long been established in southwestern Australia.","zh":"一些動物群早已長期存在於澳洲西南部。"},{"en":"To be long established in a place means to have existed there for a very long time.","zh":"be long established in a place 指在某地已存在很長時間。"},{"en":"A family business may be long established in a neighbourhood after operating there for decades.","zh":"家族企業在某社區經營數十年後，可能長期存在於該區。"},{"en":"Long-established species can reveal old biological connections.","zh":"長期存在的物種可以揭示古老生物聯繫。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses deep history in a place.","zh":"這個短語強調在某地有深厚歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"southwestern Australia","meaning":"澳洲西南部","examples":[{"en":"Wallace examined animals long established in southwestern Australia.","zh":"Wallace 檢視了長期存在於澳洲西南部的動物。"},{"en":"Southwestern Australia is the southwest part of the Australian continent.","zh":"southwestern Australia 指澳洲大陸的西南部。"},{"en":"A map can show southwestern Australia as a region with distinctive plants and animals.","zh":"地圖可以顯示澳洲西南部是有獨特動植物的地區。"},{"en":"Studying a specific region helps scientists compare local species with those elsewhere.","zh":"研究特定地區幫助科學家把本地物種與其他地方物種比較。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a precise geographical area.","zh":"這個短語提供精確地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have no affinity with","meaning":"與……沒有親緣關係","examples":[{"en":"Some Australian animals had no affinity with species in Asia.","zh":"一些澳洲動物與亞洲物種沒有親緣關係。"},{"en":"To have no affinity with something means to show no close natural relationship or similarity to it.","zh":"have no affinity with something 指與某物沒有密切自然關係或相似性。"},{"en":"A local dialect may have no affinity with a neighbouring language if they developed separately.","zh":"如果本地方言與鄰近語言分開發展，它可能與該語言沒有親緣關係。"},{"en":"Lack of affinity can suggest different origins or long isolation.","zh":"缺乏親緣關係可能暗示不同起源或長期隔離。"},{"en":"The phrase describes absence of close connection.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有密切聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"marsupials","meaning":"有袋類動物","examples":[{"en":"Many Australian mammals are marsupials.","zh":"許多澳洲哺乳動物是有袋類動物。"},{"en":"Marsupials are mammals whose young are usually born very undeveloped and continue growing in a pouch.","zh":"marsupials 指幼體通常出生時非常未成熟，並在育兒袋中繼續成長的哺乳動物。"},{"en":"Kangaroos and koalas are well-known marsupials.","zh":"袋鼠和樹熊是著名有袋類動物。"},{"en":"Marsupials are important in biogeography because many are strongly associated with Australia.","zh":"有袋類動物在生物地理學中重要，因為許多與澳洲強烈相關。"},{"en":"The word names a major group of mammals.","zh":"這個詞命名哺乳動物的一大類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"monotremes","meaning":"單孔類動物","examples":[{"en":"Monotremes are mammals that lay eggs.","zh":"單孔類動物是會下蛋的哺乳動物。"},{"en":"Monotremes are unusual mammals that reproduce by laying eggs instead of giving birth to live young.","zh":"monotremes 指透過下蛋而不是生出活幼體繁殖的不尋常哺乳動物。"},{"en":"The platypus is a famous monotreme.","zh":"鴨嘴獸是著名單孔類動物。"},{"en":"Because monotremes are rare and ancient, they interest scientists studying mammal evolution.","zh":"因為單孔類動物稀有而古老，牠們令研究哺乳動物演化的科學家感興趣。"},{"en":"The word names a small group of egg-laying mammals.","zh":"這個詞命名一小類會下蛋的哺乳動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be clearly related to","meaning":"與……明顯有關","examples":[{"en":"Australian marsupials are clearly related to species in other regions.","zh":"澳洲有袋類動物與其他地區的物種明顯有關。"},{"en":"To be clearly related to something means to show an obvious biological or historical connection with it.","zh":"be clearly related to something 指與某物有明顯生物或歷史聯繫。"},{"en":"Two languages may be clearly related if they share many basic words and grammar patterns.","zh":"如果兩種語言共享許多基本詞彙和文法模式，它們可能明顯有關。"},{"en":"Clear relationship helps researchers trace ancestry and movement.","zh":"清楚關係幫助研究人員追溯祖先和移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visible or evidence-supported connection.","zh":"這個短語描述可見或有證據支持的聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the Moluccas","meaning":"馬魯古群島","examples":[{"en":"Wallace compared Australian animals with those in the Moluccas.","zh":"Wallace 把澳洲動物與馬魯古群島的動物比較。"},{"en":"The Moluccas are a group of islands in eastern Indonesia.","zh":"the Moluccas 指印度尼西亞東部的一組島嶼。"},{"en":"A geography map may label the Moluccas as the Maluku Islands.","zh":"地理地圖可能把 Moluccas 標示為 Maluku Islands。"},{"en":"Island groups like the Moluccas are important for comparing Asian and Australian fauna.","zh":"像馬魯古群島這樣的島群，對比較亞洲和澳洲動物群很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific island region.","zh":"這個短語命名特定島嶼地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Pacific islands","meaning":"太平洋島嶼","examples":[{"en":"Related animal groups were also found on various Pacific islands.","zh":"相關動物群也在不同太平洋島嶼上被發現。"},{"en":"Pacific islands are islands located in the Pacific Ocean.","zh":"Pacific islands 指位於太平洋中的島嶼。"},{"en":"Many Pacific islands have unique birds, plants, and marine life.","zh":"許多太平洋島嶼有獨特鳥類、植物和海洋生物。"},{"en":"Island isolation can lead species to evolve differently from mainland relatives.","zh":"島嶼隔離可以令物種與大陸近親以不同方式演化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broad group of oceanic islands.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛的海洋島嶼群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"none are found in","meaning":"……之中完全找不到","examples":[{"en":"None of these animal groups are found in neighbouring Indonesia.","zh":"這些動物群在鄰近的印度尼西亞之中完全找不到。"},{"en":"None are found in a place means no examples exist or have been recorded there.","zh":"none are found in a place 指沒有任何例子存在或被記錄於該地。"},{"en":"None of the missing library books were found in the classroom.","zh":"遺失的圖書在課室中完全找不到。"},{"en":"Absence from a nearby region can be as important as presence in a distant one.","zh":"在附近地區缺席，可以與在遙遠地區出現同樣重要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses complete absence.","zh":"這個短語強調完全沒有。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"from this and related data","meaning":"根據這些及相關數據","examples":[{"en":"From this and related data, Wegener rejected the accepted explanation.","zh":"根據這些及相關數據，Wegener 否定了被接受的解釋。"},{"en":"From this and related data means using this evidence together with other connected information.","zh":"from this and related data 指使用這項證據以及其他相關資訊。"},{"en":"From exam scores and related data, a school may decide which skills need more teaching.","zh":"根據考試分數及相關數據，學校可能決定哪些技能需要更多教學。"},{"en":"Combining related evidence can make a conclusion stronger than using one fact alone.","zh":"結合相關證據可以令結論比單用一個事實更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces reasoning based on multiple pieces of data.","zh":"這個短語引入基於多項數據的推理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"broadly accepted theory","meaning":"當時廣泛接受的理論","examples":[{"en":"The land-bridge explanation was a broadly accepted theory at the time.","zh":"陸橋解釋是當時廣泛接受的理論。"},{"en":"A broadly accepted theory is an explanation supported or believed by many people in a field.","zh":"broadly accepted theory 指在某領域中被許多人支持或相信的解釋。"},{"en":"A teaching method may become broadly accepted after many schools report success with it.","zh":"當許多學校報告成功後，一種教學方法可能變成廣泛接受的理論。"},{"en":"Even a widely accepted theory can be challenged by new evidence.","zh":"即使廣泛接受的理論也可以被新證據挑戰。"},{"en":"The phrase describes popularity or acceptance, not guaranteed truth.","zh":"這個短語描述受歡迎或被接受，而不是保證真實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"land-bridge theory","meaning":"陸橋理論","examples":[{"en":"The land-bridge theory proposed that species crossed vanished land connections.","zh":"陸橋理論提出物種曾橫越已消失的陸地連接。"},{"en":"The land-bridge theory was the idea that continents or islands were once connected by land bridges that later disappeared.","zh":"land-bridge theory 指大陸或島嶼曾由後來消失的陸橋連接的想法。"},{"en":"A scientist might use a land-bridge theory to explain how animals reached an island without flying.","zh":"科學家可能用陸橋理論解釋動物如何在不飛行下到達島嶼。"},{"en":"If evidence fits continental drift better, the land-bridge explanation becomes weaker.","zh":"如果證據更符合大陸漂移，陸橋解釋就變得較弱。"},{"en":"The phrase names an older explanation for species distribution.","zh":"這個短語命名一種解釋物種分布的舊理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"account for","meaning":"解釋……","examples":[{"en":"Wegener believed the land-bridge theory could not account for the evidence.","zh":"Wegener 認為陸橋理論不能解釋這些證據。"},{"en":"To account for something means to explain it satisfactorily.","zh":"account for something 指令人滿意地解釋某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask a student to account for the sudden improvement in her writing.","zh":"老師可能要求學生解釋寫作突然進步的原因。"},{"en":"If a theory cannot explain important evidence, scientists may look for a better one.","zh":"如果理論不能解釋重要證據，科學家可能尋找更好理論。"},{"en":"The phrase means explain, not count money here.","zh":"這個短語在此解作解釋，不是計算金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"distribution of animals","meaning":"動物分布","examples":[{"en":"Continental drift offered a better explanation for the distribution of animals.","zh":"大陸漂移為動物分布提供了更好解釋。"},{"en":"Distribution of animals means where different animals are found across regions.","zh":"distribution of animals 指不同動物在各地區出現的位置。"},{"en":"A map of bird sightings can show the distribution of animals in a city.","zh":"鳥類目擊地圖可以顯示城市中的動物分布。"},{"en":"Animal distribution can reveal barriers, climate limits, and ancient history.","zh":"動物分布可以揭示屏障、氣候限制和古代歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on location patterns of animal life.","zh":"這個短語重點是動物生命的位置模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"continental drift","meaning":"大陸漂移","examples":[{"en":"Continental drift explains why related species occur on distant continents.","zh":"大陸漂移解釋為何相關物種出現在遙遠大洲上。"},{"en":"Continental drift is the slow movement of continents over geological time.","zh":"continental drift 指大陸在地質時間中緩慢移動。"},{"en":"A geography teacher may show how South America and Africa once fitted together to explain continental drift.","zh":"地理老師可能展示南美洲和非洲曾如何吻合，以解釋大陸漂移。"},{"en":"If continents separate, related species may end up far apart.","zh":"如果大陸分離，相關物種可能最終相距很遠。"},{"en":"The phrase explains large-scale movement of landmasses.","zh":"這個短語解釋大陸塊的大規模移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"dismiss a theory","meaning":"否定一套理論","examples":[{"en":"Wegener dismissed the land-bridge theory.","zh":"Wegener 否定了陸橋理論。"},{"en":"To dismiss a theory means to reject it as unconvincing or inadequate.","zh":"dismiss a theory 指因其不能令人信服或不足夠而拒絕接受。"},{"en":"A doctor may dismiss an early diagnosis after new test results prove it wrong.","zh":"新檢查結果證明早期診斷錯誤後，醫生可能否定該診斷。"},{"en":"Scientists dismiss a theory when it fails to account for important evidence.","zh":"當理論不能解釋重要證據，科學家會否定它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rejecting an explanation, not merely ignoring it.","zh":"這個短語描述拒絕一種解釋，而不只是忽視它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in preference to","meaning":"寧取……而捨棄……","examples":[{"en":"He dismissed the older theory in preference to continental drift.","zh":"他捨棄較舊理論，寧取大陸漂移。"},{"en":"In preference to means choosing one thing rather than another because it seems better.","zh":"in preference to 指選擇某物而不是另一物，因為它似乎較好。"},{"en":"A student may use examples in preference to abstract claims when writing an essay.","zh":"學生寫作文時可能寧用例子，而不用抽象聲稱。"},{"en":"If one explanation fits the evidence better, researchers may choose it over an older one.","zh":"如果一個解釋更符合證據，研究人員可能選它而放棄較舊解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly shows a choice between alternatives.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示在不同選項之間作選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"migrate across","meaning":"橫越……遷徙","examples":[{"en":"The rejected theory proposed that species migrated across land bridges.","zh":"被否定的理論提出物種曾橫越陸橋遷徙。"},{"en":"To migrate across something means to move from one side to another, often over a large area.","zh":"migrate across something 指從一邊移動到另一邊，通常跨越大範圍。"},{"en":"Birds may migrate across oceans during seasonal travel.","zh":"鳥類在季節性遷徙中可能橫越海洋。"},{"en":"Migration across land connections can explain movement without requiring flight or rafting.","zh":"橫越陸地連接遷徙，可以在不需飛行或漂流下解釋移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement through or over a region.","zh":"這個短語描述穿越或跨越某地區的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"now-submerged","meaning":"現已沉沒的","examples":[{"en":"The supposed land bridges are now-submerged.","zh":"假設中的陸橋現已沉沒。"},{"en":"Now-submerged means currently underwater, though formerly above water.","zh":"now-submerged 指現在在水下，雖然以前在水面以上。"},{"en":"An old road may be now-submerged after a valley is flooded to build a reservoir.","zh":"山谷被淹沒用作建水庫後，舊道路可能現已沉沒。"},{"en":"If a land bridge is now submerged, direct evidence may be difficult to see today.","zh":"如果陸橋現已沉沒，今日可能難以看到直接證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a past land feature now below water.","zh":"這個短語描述如今位於水下的昔日陸地特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"intercontinental land bridges","meaning":"洲際陸橋","examples":[{"en":"Scientists once proposed the existence of intercontinental land bridges.","zh":"科學家曾提出洲際陸橋的存在。"},{"en":"Intercontinental land bridges are land connections between continents.","zh":"intercontinental land bridges 指大洲之間的陸地連接。"},{"en":"A land bridge between two continents would allow animals to move without crossing deep ocean.","zh":"兩個大洲之間的陸橋會讓動物不用橫越深海也能移動。"},{"en":"The idea was used to explain similar species on distant lands before plate tectonics was accepted.","zh":"在板塊構造被接受前，這個想法曾用來解釋遙遠陸地上的相似物種。"},{"en":"The phrase names a proposed land connection across continents.","zh":"這個短語命名跨越大洲的假設陸地連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"leading geologist","meaning":"領先的地質學家","examples":[{"en":"Eduard Suess was one of Europe’s leading geologists.","zh":"Eduard Suess 是歐洲領先的地質學家之一。"},{"en":"A leading geologist is a highly respected expert in the study of Earth’s rocks and structure.","zh":"leading geologist 指研究地球岩石和結構的高度受尊重專家。"},{"en":"A leading geologist may advise governments on earthquake risk or land use.","zh":"領先地質學家可能就地震風險或土地使用向政府提供建議。"},{"en":"Experts can strongly influence what theories are accepted in their time.","zh":"專家可以強烈影響其時代接受哪些理論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes status within a scientific field.","zh":"這個短語描述科學領域中的地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rigid Earth","meaning":"堅硬的地球","examples":[{"en":"Suess believed that the rigid Earth contracted as it cooled.","zh":"Suess 相信堅硬的地球在冷卻時會收縮。"},{"en":"Rigid Earth means the idea that Earth’s outer structure was fixed, hard, and not made of moving plates.","zh":"rigid Earth 指地球外部結構固定、堅硬，並非由移動板塊組成的想法。"},{"en":"A rigid object bends less easily than a flexible one.","zh":"堅硬物體比有彈性的物體更不容易彎曲。"},{"en":"If Earth were rigid, scientists would explain mountains and oceans differently from modern plate tectonics.","zh":"如果地球是堅硬固定的，科學家會用不同於現代板塊構造的方式解釋山脈和海洋。"},{"en":"The phrase reflects an older geological view.","zh":"這個短語反映較舊的地質觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"upper crust","meaning":"地殼上層","examples":[{"en":"He argued that the Earth’s upper crust shrank and folded.","zh":"他主張地殼上層會收縮和摺曲。"},{"en":"The upper crust is the outermost solid layer of Earth’s crust.","zh":"upper crust 指地殼最外層的固體岩石層。"},{"en":"A geology class may compare the upper crust to the thin skin of an apple.","zh":"地質課可能把地殼上層比作蘋果的薄皮。"},{"en":"Changes in the crust can create mountains, faults, and basins.","zh":"地殼變化可以形成山脈、斷層和盆地。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to Earth’s outer rocky layer.","zh":"這個短語指地球外部岩石層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"shrink and wrinkle","meaning":"收縮和起皺","examples":[{"en":"Suess believed that the crust would shrink and wrinkle as it cooled.","zh":"Suess 相信地殼在冷卻時會收縮和起皺。"},{"en":"To shrink and wrinkle means to become smaller and form folds or lines.","zh":"shrink and wrinkle 指變小並形成摺痕或皺紋。"},{"en":"An apple skin may shrink and wrinkle as the fruit dries out.","zh":"當蘋果變乾，果皮可能收縮和起皺。"},{"en":"Suess used this idea to explain folded landforms on a cooling Earth.","zh":"Suess 用這個想法解釋冷卻地球上的摺曲地形。"},{"en":"The phrase describes contraction and folding.","zh":"這個短語描述收縮和摺皺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"withering skin","meaning":"乾皺的果皮","examples":[{"en":"He compared the Earth’s crust to the withering skin of an apple.","zh":"他把地殼比作蘋果乾皺的果皮。"},{"en":"Withering skin is skin or peel that is drying, shrinking, and wrinkling.","zh":"withering skin 指正在乾燥、收縮和起皺的皮或果皮。"},{"en":"A forgotten orange may develop withering skin after weeks on a table.","zh":"被忘在桌上幾星期的橙可能出現乾皺果皮。"},{"en":"The image helps explain how an old theory imagined Earth’s crust folding.","zh":"這個圖像幫助解釋舊理論如何想像地殼摺曲。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a visual metaphor for shrinkage.","zh":"這個短語用視覺比喻表達收縮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"aging apple","meaning":"老化的蘋果","examples":[{"en":"The old theory compared the Earth with an aging apple.","zh":"舊理論把地球比作老化的蘋果。"},{"en":"An aging apple is an apple becoming old, dry, soft, or wrinkled.","zh":"aging apple 指變老、乾燥、變軟或起皺的蘋果。"},{"en":"A teacher may use an aging apple to show how skin wrinkles as it dries.","zh":"老師可能用老化的蘋果展示果皮如何在乾燥時起皺。"},{"en":"The metaphor helped explain a shrinking Earth theory before plate tectonics.","zh":"在板塊構造前，這個比喻幫助解釋地球收縮理論。"},{"en":"The phrase is used as an analogy, not literal geology.","zh":"這個短語用作類比，不是字面地質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"once-contiguous plateaus","meaning":"曾經相連的高原","examples":[{"en":"Suess believed that oceans filled the gaps between once-contiguous plateaus.","zh":"Suess 相信海洋填滿了曾經相連的高原之間的空隙。"},{"en":"Once-contiguous plateaus are high flat land areas that were formerly connected.","zh":"once-contiguous plateaus 指以前曾連接的高平坦陸地。"},{"en":"Two fields now separated by a road may once have been contiguous farmland.","zh":"現在被道路分隔的兩塊田，可能曾經是相連農地。"},{"en":"If plateaus were once connected, their separation needs a geological explanation.","zh":"如果高原曾經相連，其分離需要地質解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formerly joined land surfaces.","zh":"這個短語描述以前相連的陸地表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"dynamic Earth","meaning":"不斷活動的地球","examples":[{"en":"Modern geology shows that we live on a dynamic Earth.","zh":"現代地質學顯示我們生活在一個不斷活動的地球上。"},{"en":"A dynamic Earth is an Earth that is constantly changing through plate movement, earthquakes, volcanoes, and erosion.","zh":"dynamic Earth 指透過板塊移動、地震、火山和侵蝕不斷改變的地球。"},{"en":"A geography lesson on a dynamic Earth may show how mountains rise and coastlines change.","zh":"關於不斷活動地球的地理課，可能展示山脈如何升起和海岸線如何改變。"},{"en":"Because Earth is dynamic, continents are not fixed forever.","zh":"因為地球不斷活動，大陸不是永遠固定的。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts with the idea of a rigid, unmoving Earth.","zh":"這個短語與堅硬不動地球的想法形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"shifting tectonic plates","meaning":"移動中的構造板塊","examples":[{"en":"The Earth’s surface consists of shifting tectonic plates.","zh":"地球表面由移動中的構造板塊組成。"},{"en":"Shifting tectonic plates are large pieces of Earth’s outer shell that slowly move.","zh":"shifting tectonic plates 指地球外殼中緩慢移動的大型板塊。"},{"en":"Earthquakes often happen near the edges of shifting tectonic plates.","zh":"地震常發生在移動中的構造板塊邊緣附近。"},{"en":"Plate movement can create mountains, ocean trenches, and continental drift.","zh":"板塊移動可以形成山脈、海溝和大陸漂移。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the moving structure of Earth’s surface.","zh":"這個短語描述地球表面的移動結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"colliding and separating plates","meaning":"不斷碰撞和分離的板塊","examples":[{"en":"Continents move because tectonic plates are constantly colliding and separating.","zh":"大陸會移動，因為構造板塊不斷碰撞和分離。"},{"en":"Colliding and separating plates are tectonic plates that crash together or move apart.","zh":"colliding and separating plates 指互相碰撞或分開移動的構造板塊。"},{"en":"A classroom model can show colliding plates with two books pushed together.","zh":"課室模型可以用兩本書推在一起來展示碰撞板塊。"},{"en":"When plates collide or separate, they can reshape continents and oceans.","zh":"當板塊碰撞或分離，它們可以重塑大陸和海洋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the main movements behind plate tectonics.","zh":"這個短語描述板塊構造背後的主要運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the main debate in the field","meaning":"該領域的主要爭論","examples":[{"en":"The main debate in the field of biogeography has now shifted.","zh":"生物地理學領域的主要爭論如今已經轉移。"},{"en":"The main debate in the field is the most important argument among specialists in that subject.","zh":"main debate in the field 指該學科專家之間最重要的爭論。"},{"en":"The main debate in education may concern whether exams or coursework measure learning better.","zh":"教育領域的主要爭論可能關於考試還是課程作業更能量度學習。"},{"en":"When new evidence appears, a field’s central debate can change.","zh":"當新證據出現，一個領域的核心爭論可以改變。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the key disagreement in an academic area.","zh":"這個短語指出學術領域中的關鍵分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"shift from…to…","meaning":"從……轉移至……","examples":[{"en":"The scientific debate shifted from continental movement to species distribution.","zh":"科學爭論從大陸移動轉移至物種分布。"},{"en":"To shift from A to B means to move focus, attention, or direction from one thing to another.","zh":"shift from A to B 指把焦點、注意力或方向由 A 移到 B。"},{"en":"A student may shift from memorising words to practising full sentences.","zh":"學生可能從背單詞轉移至練習完整句子。"},{"en":"A shift in focus can happen when an old question is mostly settled.","zh":"當舊問題大致解決，焦點轉移就可能出現。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly shows a change of focus.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示焦點改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"dispersalism","meaning":"擴散論","examples":[{"en":"Dispersalism emphasises the movement of species into new areas.","zh":"擴散論強調物種移動到新地區。"},{"en":"Dispersalism is the view that species distributions are often explained by organisms spreading to new places.","zh":"dispersalism 指認為物種分布常可由生物擴散到新地方來解釋的觀點。"},{"en":"A bird reaching an island by flying would support a dispersalist explanation.","zh":"鳥類透過飛行到達島嶼，會支持擴散論解釋。"},{"en":"If species can cross barriers, their current locations may result from movement rather than land separation.","zh":"如果物種能跨越屏障，其現今位置可能源自移動，而不是陸地分隔。"},{"en":"The term contrasts with vicarianism.","zh":"這個術語與隔離分化論形成對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"vicarianism","meaning":"隔離分化論","examples":[{"en":"Vicarianism emphasises the separation of populations by natural barriers.","zh":"隔離分化論強調自然屏障對種群的分隔。"},{"en":"Vicarianism is the view that species distribution is often explained by populations being split by barriers such as seas or mountains.","zh":"vicarianism 指認為物種分布常由海洋或山脈等屏障分隔種群來解釋的觀點。"},{"en":"A lake forming between two populations may create a vicarian pattern.","zh":"湖泊在兩個種群之間形成，可能創造隔離分化模式。"},{"en":"When separated groups evolve independently, new species may develop.","zh":"當分隔群體獨立演化，新物種可能形成。"},{"en":"The term focuses on isolation rather than active movement.","zh":"這個術語重點是隔離，而不是主動移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"versus","meaning":"與……對立；對……","examples":[{"en":"The modern debate concerns dispersalism versus vicarianism.","zh":"現代爭論關於擴散論與隔離分化論的對立。"},{"en":"Versus means against or compared with, especially between two competing ideas or sides.","zh":"versus 指對抗或比較，尤其用於兩個競爭想法或陣營之間。"},{"en":"A class debate may discuss online learning versus classroom learning.","zh":"班級辯論可能討論網上學習對課室學習。"},{"en":"Using versus highlights contrast or conflict between options.","zh":"使用 versus 會突出選項之間的對比或衝突。"},{"en":"The word is common in debates, sports, and comparisons.","zh":"這個詞常見於辯論、運動和比較中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unrestricted radiation of species","meaning":"物種不受限制地擴散","examples":[{"en":"Dispersalism involves the unrestricted radiation of species.","zh":"擴散論涉及物種不受限制地擴散。"},{"en":"Unrestricted radiation of species means species spreading widely into many areas without strong barriers limiting them.","zh":"unrestricted radiation of species 指物種在沒有強大屏障限制下廣泛擴散到許多地區。"},{"en":"A plant with wind-blown seeds may spread rapidly across open land if no barriers stop it.","zh":"如果沒有屏障阻止，種子隨風傳播的植物可能迅速擴散過開闊土地。"},{"en":"Wide radiation can make species histories harder to trace.","zh":"廣泛擴散可以令物種歷史更難追溯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad biological spread.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛的生物擴散。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"on the one hand…on the other","meaning":"一方面……另一方面……","examples":[{"en":"The debate concerns dispersal on the one hand and isolation on the other.","zh":"這場爭論一方面關於擴散，另一方面關於隔離。"},{"en":"On the one hand…on the other introduces two contrasting sides of an issue.","zh":"on the one hand…on the other 用來引入一個議題的兩個相對方面。"},{"en":"On the one hand, online learning is flexible; on the other, students may feel isolated.","zh":"一方面，網上學習很靈活；另一方面，學生可能感到孤立。"},{"en":"The structure helps writers present balanced comparison.","zh":"這個結構幫助作者作平衡比較。"},{"en":"It is useful when both sides have reasonable points.","zh":"當雙方都有合理觀點時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"short-term phenomenon","meaning":"短期現象","examples":[{"en":"Species dispersal is often a short-term phenomenon.","zh":"物種擴散通常是短期現象。"},{"en":"A short-term phenomenon is something that happens over a relatively brief period.","zh":"short-term phenomenon 指在相對短時間內發生的事情。"},{"en":"A sudden increase in mask sales during a flu outbreak may be a short-term phenomenon.","zh":"流感爆發期間口罩銷量突然增加，可能是短期現象。"},{"en":"Short-term events can still have long-term consequences if they change where species live.","zh":"如果短期事件改變物種生活地點，它仍可以有長期後果。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts brief events with slow geological processes.","zh":"這個短語把短暫事件與緩慢地質過程作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"daily or seasonal migration","meaning":"每日或季節性遷徙","examples":[{"en":"Dispersal may involve daily or seasonal migration.","zh":"擴散可能涉及每日或季節性遷徙。"},{"en":"Daily or seasonal migration is movement that happens every day or during particular seasons.","zh":"daily or seasonal migration 指每天或在特定季節發生的移動。"},{"en":"Birds may make seasonal migration to warmer places before winter.","zh":"鳥類可能在冬天前進行季節性遷徙到較暖地方。"},{"en":"Repeated movement can expand a species’ range if some individuals settle elsewhere.","zh":"如果一些個體在別處定居，反覆移動可以擴大物種分布範圍。"},{"en":"The phrase describes regular movement patterns.","zh":"這個短語描述規律移動模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"natural environment","meaning":"自然環境","examples":[{"en":"A species generally spreads to the limits of its natural environment.","zh":"一個物種通常會擴散至其自然環境的界限。"},{"en":"Natural environment means the surrounding conditions in nature where a species can live.","zh":"natural environment 指物種能夠生活的自然周圍條件。"},{"en":"A fish’s natural environment may include clean water, suitable temperature, and enough food.","zh":"魚的自然環境可能包括乾淨水、合適溫度和足夠食物。"},{"en":"When the environment becomes unsuitable, a species may stop spreading or decline.","zh":"當環境變得不合適，物種可能停止擴散或下降。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to natural living conditions, not human-made office settings.","zh":"這個短語指自然生活條件，而不是人造辦公環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"an extensive and continuous landmass","meaning":"廣闊而連續的陸地","examples":[{"en":"Species can spread widely across an extensive and continuous landmass.","zh":"物種可以在廣闊而連續的陸地上廣泛擴散。"},{"en":"An extensive and continuous landmass is a large unbroken area of land.","zh":"extensive and continuous landmass 指大片不間斷的陸地。"},{"en":"A desert animal may spread across a continuous landmass if the climate suits it.","zh":"如果氣候合適，沙漠動物可能在連續陸地上擴散。"},{"en":"Without oceans or mountains blocking movement, species can travel farther.","zh":"沒有海洋或山脈阻擋移動時，物種可以走得更遠。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both size and lack of breaks.","zh":"這個短語同時強調面積大和沒有中斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"vicarian evolution","meaning":"隔離演化","examples":[{"en":"Vicarian evolution occurs when populations become geographically separated.","zh":"當種群在地理上被分隔，隔離演化就會發生。"},{"en":"Vicarian evolution is evolution that happens after populations are split by barriers.","zh":"vicarian evolution 指種群被屏障分隔後發生的演化。"},{"en":"If a river separates one insect population into two, each side may evolve differently.","zh":"如果河流把一個昆蟲種群分成兩邊，每一邊可能以不同方式演化。"},{"en":"Long isolation can create new species from one original population.","zh":"長期隔離可以由一個原始種群形成新物種。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on evolution through separation.","zh":"這個短語重點是透過分隔產生的演化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"depend upon","meaning":"取決於……","examples":[{"en":"Vicarian evolution depends upon the isolation of populations.","zh":"隔離演化取決於種群隔離。"},{"en":"To depend upon something means to rely on it as a necessary condition.","zh":"depend upon something 指依賴某事作為必要條件。"},{"en":"A student’s progress may depend upon regular practice and useful feedback.","zh":"學生進步可能取決於定期練習和有用回饋。"},{"en":"If isolation does not occur, vicarian evolution cannot happen in the same way.","zh":"如果隔離沒有發生，隔離演化就不能以同樣方式出現。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one thing requires another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一件事需要另一件事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"separation and isolation","meaning":"分離和隔絕","examples":[{"en":"Natural barriers cause the separation and isolation of species.","zh":"天然屏障造成物種的分離和隔絕。"},{"en":"Separation and isolation mean groups are split apart and kept from mixing.","zh":"separation and isolation 指群體被分開並被阻止混合。"},{"en":"A damaged bridge can create separation and isolation between two villages.","zh":"損壞的橋樑可以造成兩條村之間的分離和隔絕。"},{"en":"In biology, isolation can stop populations from breeding with each other.","zh":"在生物學中，隔離可以阻止種群彼此繁殖。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being divided and cut off.","zh":"這個短語描述被分開和切斷聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a variety of species","meaning":"多種物種","examples":[{"en":"Geographical barriers may divide a variety of species.","zh":"地理屏障可能分隔多種物種。"},{"en":"A variety of species means several different kinds of species.","zh":"a variety of species 指幾種不同物種。"},{"en":"A pond can support a variety of species, including fish, insects, frogs, and plants.","zh":"池塘可以支持多種物種，包括魚、昆蟲、青蛙和植物。"},{"en":"If a barrier forms, many different species may be affected at the same time.","zh":"如果屏障形成，許多不同物種可能同時受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses diversity, not just one type.","zh":"這個短語強調多樣性，而不只是單一類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"within the confines of","meaning":"在……的範圍內","examples":[{"en":"Populations may evolve within the confines of natural barriers.","zh":"種群可能在天然屏障的範圍內演化。"},{"en":"Within the confines of something means inside the limits or boundaries of it.","zh":"within the confines of something 指在某物的限制或邊界之內。"},{"en":"Students must finish the essay within the confines of the word limit.","zh":"學生必須在字數限制範圍內完成作文。"},{"en":"If populations stay within barriers, they may develop separately from outside groups.","zh":"如果種群留在屏障之內，它們可能與外部群體分開發展。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses restriction by boundaries.","zh":"這個短語強調受邊界限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"natural barriers","meaning":"天然屏障","examples":[{"en":"Islands, lakes and seas can act as natural barriers.","zh":"島嶼、湖泊和海洋可以充當天然屏障。"},{"en":"Natural barriers are features of nature that block movement or separate groups.","zh":"natural barriers 指阻擋移動或分隔群體的自然特徵。"},{"en":"Mountains can be natural barriers between villages and affect travel routes.","zh":"山脈可以成為村落之間的天然屏障，並影響交通路線。"},{"en":"In evolution, barriers can prevent populations from mixing and lead to difference.","zh":"在演化中，屏障可以阻止種群混合並導致差異。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to physical features, not human-made walls.","zh":"這個短語指自然地貌，而不是人造牆。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in the form of","meaning":"以……的形式","examples":[{"en":"Natural barriers may appear in the form of islands or shallow seas.","zh":"天然屏障可能以島嶼或淺海的形式出現。"},{"en":"In the form of means appearing as or taking the shape of something.","zh":"in the form of 指以某種樣貌、形式或形態出現。"},{"en":"Help may come in the form of money, advice, or extra lessons.","zh":"幫助可能以金錢、建議或額外課堂的形式出現。"},{"en":"Barriers can take many forms, so scientists must identify what actually limits movement.","zh":"屏障可以有許多形式，所以科學家必須辨認真正限制移動的是甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the specific type or shape of something.","zh":"這個短語引入某事的具體類型或形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"shallow seas","meaning":"淺海","examples":[{"en":"Shallow seas may isolate populations for long periods.","zh":"淺海可能長時間隔離種群。"},{"en":"Shallow seas are areas of sea where the water is not very deep.","zh":"shallow seas 指水不太深的海域。"},{"en":"Fishing boats may work in shallow seas near the coast.","zh":"漁船可能在海岸附近的淺海作業。"},{"en":"Even shallow water can act as a barrier for animals that cannot cross it.","zh":"即使水不深，對不能穿越的動物而言也可以成為屏障。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a marine feature that can affect movement.","zh":"這個短語描述可以影響移動的海洋地貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"topographical features","meaning":"地形特徵","examples":[{"en":"Islands and lakes are important topographical features.","zh":"島嶼和湖泊是重要地形特徵。"},{"en":"Topographical features are physical features of land or landscape, such as mountains, valleys, islands, and lakes.","zh":"topographical features 指土地或地景的實體特徵，例如山脈、山谷、島嶼和湖泊。"},{"en":"A map shows topographical features so hikers can understand the terrain.","zh":"地圖顯示地形特徵，讓遠足者理解地勢。"},{"en":"Such features can shape travel, settlement, and species distribution.","zh":"這類特徵可以塑造交通、聚居和物種分布。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to physical geography.","zh":"這個短語指實體地理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"take a long time to develop","meaning":"需要很長時間形成","examples":[{"en":"Major topographical features take a long time to develop.","zh":"主要地形特徵需要很長時間形成。"},{"en":"To take a long time to develop means to form gradually over an extended period.","zh":"take a long time to develop 指在長時間中逐漸形成。"},{"en":"A student’s writing style may take a long time to develop through reading and practice.","zh":"學生的寫作風格可能需要透過閱讀和練習長時間形成。"},{"en":"Geological features often need millions of years to form.","zh":"地質特徵通常需要數百萬年形成。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses slow development rather than sudden change.","zh":"這個短語強調緩慢發展，而不是突然改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"use the information in the passage","meaning":"使用文章中的資料","examples":[{"en":"Students use the information in the passage to match people with ideas.","zh":"學生使用文章中的資料，把人物與想法配對。"},{"en":"To use the information in the passage means to base answers only on what the text says.","zh":"use the information in the passage 指只根據文本所說內容作答。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should use the passage rather than outside knowledge.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應使用文章資料，而不是外部知識。"},{"en":"This prevents guessing and keeps answers tied to evidence.","zh":"這可以防止猜測，並令答案緊扣證據。"},{"en":"The phrase is an exam instruction about source-based answering.","zh":"這個短語是關於根據來源作答的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"opinions or deeds","meaning":"觀點或行為","examples":[{"en":"The task asks students to match people with their opinions or deeds.","zh":"該任務要求學生把人物與其觀點或行為配對。"},{"en":"Opinions or deeds means what people thought or what they did.","zh":"opinions or deeds 指人們的想法或所做的事。"},{"en":"A history worksheet may ask students to match leaders with their opinions or deeds.","zh":"歷史工作紙可能要求學生把領袖與其觀點或行為配對。"},{"en":"Separating belief from action helps readers understand a person’s role clearly.","zh":"區分信念和行動幫助讀者清楚理解一個人的角色。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both ideas and actions.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋想法和行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"appropriate letters","meaning":"適當的字母","examples":[{"en":"Students write the appropriate letters in the answer boxes.","zh":"學生在答案格中寫上適當的字母。"},{"en":"Appropriate letters are the correct letter choices that match the answer options.","zh":"appropriate letters 指與答案選項相符的正確字母。"},{"en":"If option D matches the statement, D is the appropriate letter.","zh":"如果選項 D 符合陳述，D 就是適當的字母。"},{"en":"Writing the right letter matters because the examiner marks the code, not a long explanation.","zh":"寫對字母很重要，因為考官評的是代號，不是長解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to correct answer labels.","zh":"這個短語指正確答案標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"urge someone to publish","meaning":"催促某人發表……","examples":[{"en":"Darwin’s friends urged him to publish his scientific findings.","zh":"Darwin 的朋友催促他發表科學研究結果。"},{"en":"To urge someone to publish means to strongly encourage that person to make their work public.","zh":"urge someone to publish 指強烈鼓勵某人公開其作品。"},{"en":"A supervisor may urge a student to publish a strong research paper.","zh":"導師可能催促學生發表一篇有力研究論文。"},{"en":"Urging can happen when delay might cause someone to lose credit or opportunity.","zh":"當延誤可能令某人失去功勞或機會時，催促可能出現。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests serious encouragement to release written work.","zh":"這個短語暗示認真鼓勵發表書面作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"scientific findings","meaning":"科學研究結果","examples":[{"en":"The researchers wanted Darwin to present his scientific findings.","zh":"研究人員希望 Darwin 發表他的科學研究結果。"},{"en":"Scientific findings are results or conclusions discovered through scientific study.","zh":"scientific findings 指透過科學研究發現的結果或結論。"},{"en":"A lab report should clearly state the scientific findings of an experiment.","zh":"實驗報告應清楚列出實驗的科學研究結果。"},{"en":"Findings become stronger when they are supported by repeated evidence.","zh":"當發現有反覆證據支持，它們會變得更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to what research has discovered.","zh":"這個短語指研究所發現的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"physical features of the Earth’s crust","meaning":"地殼的物理特徵","examples":[{"en":"Suess described the physical features of the Earth’s crust.","zh":"Suess 描述了地殼的物理特徵。"},{"en":"Physical features of the Earth’s crust are visible or measurable structures of Earth’s outer rocky layer.","zh":"physical features of the Earth’s crust 指地球外部岩石層中可見或可量度的結構。"},{"en":"Mountains, faults, valleys, and plateaus are physical features of the crust.","zh":"山脈、斷層、山谷和高原都是地殼的物理特徵。"},{"en":"Explaining these features helps geologists understand how Earth has changed.","zh":"解釋這些特徵幫助地質學家理解地球如何改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to Earth’s physical structure, not its climate.","zh":"這個短語指地球物理結構，而不是氣候。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"believe in continental drift","meaning":"相信大陸漂移學說","examples":[{"en":"Wegener believed in continental drift.","zh":"Wegener 相信大陸漂移學說。"},{"en":"To believe in continental drift means to accept that continents move slowly over geological time.","zh":"believe in continental drift 指接受大陸會在地質時間中緩慢移動。"},{"en":"A student may believe in continental drift after seeing matching fossils and coastlines.","zh":"學生看見相符化石和海岸線後，可能相信大陸漂移學說。"},{"en":"Acceptance of the idea changed how scientists explained species distribution.","zh":"接受這個想法改變了科學家解釋物種分布的方式。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to support for a scientific theory.","zh":"這個短語指支持一套科學理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reject the land-bridge theory","meaning":"否定陸橋理論","examples":[{"en":"Wegener rejected the land-bridge theory as an explanation.","zh":"Wegener 否定陸橋理論作為解釋。"},{"en":"To reject the land-bridge theory means to decide that vanished land bridges do not adequately explain the evidence.","zh":"reject the land-bridge theory 指認為已消失陸橋不能充分解釋證據。"},{"en":"A researcher may reject an old theory when new data fit a better model.","zh":"當新數據更符合較好模型，研究人員可能否定舊理論。"},{"en":"Rejection often happens when an explanation becomes too weak or complicated.","zh":"當一種解釋變得太弱或太複雜，否定常會發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes refusing to accept a specific scientific explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述拒絕接受某個特定科學解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"publish work on","meaning":"發表關於……的著作","examples":[{"en":"Wallace published work on the distribution of animals.","zh":"Wallace 發表了關於動物分布的著作。"},{"en":"To publish work on a topic means to release research or writing about that subject.","zh":"publish work on a topic 指發表關於某主題的研究或寫作。"},{"en":"A teacher may publish work on how students learn grammar through examples.","zh":"老師可能發表關於學生如何透過例句學習文法的著作。"},{"en":"Publishing work allows other people to read, question, and use the findings.","zh":"發表作品讓其他人閱讀、提問和使用研究發現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making research public.","zh":"這個短語描述把研究公開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"different regions","meaning":"不同地區","examples":[{"en":"Biogeographers compare animal populations in different regions.","zh":"生物地理學家比較不同地區的動物種群。"},{"en":"Different regions are separate areas or parts of the world.","zh":"different regions 指世界上分開的區域或地區。"},{"en":"Students may compare weather in different regions of the same country.","zh":"學生可能比較同一國家不同地區的天氣。"},{"en":"Comparing regions can reveal patterns that one place alone cannot show.","zh":"比較地區可以揭示單一地方無法顯示的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on geographical difference.","zh":"這個短語重點是地理差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"argue that species evolve","meaning":"主張物種會演化","examples":[{"en":"Darwin and Wallace argued that species evolve through natural selection.","zh":"Darwin 和 Wallace 主張物種會透過自然選擇演化。"},{"en":"To argue that species evolve means to present reasons for believing species change over time.","zh":"argue that species evolve 指提出理由支持物種會隨時間改變。"},{"en":"A biology student may argue that species evolve by using fossil and DNA evidence.","zh":"生物學生可能用化石和 DNA 證據主張物種會演化。"},{"en":"Strong arguments connect observations with a clear mechanism.","zh":"有力論證會把觀察與清楚機制連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a scientific claim about change in life.","zh":"這個短語描述提出關於生命變化的科學主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"which paragraph contains","meaning":"哪一段包含……","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which paragraph contains each piece of information.","zh":"學生辨認哪一段包含每項資料。"},{"en":"Which paragraph contains means which section of the passage includes the required information.","zh":"which paragraph contains 指文章中哪一段包括所需資訊。"},{"en":"In a reading exam, students may underline keywords to find which paragraph contains the answer.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生可能劃下關鍵詞，以找出哪一段包含答案。"},{"en":"This task tests locating information, not writing personal opinions.","zh":"這項任務測試定位資訊，而不是寫個人意見。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction in paragraph-matching questions.","zh":"這個短語是段落配對題中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"best-adapted animals","meaning":"最適應環境的動物","examples":[{"en":"The best-adapted animals were more likely to survive.","zh":"最適應環境的動物較可能存活。"},{"en":"Best-adapted animals are animals whose traits suit their environment especially well.","zh":"best-adapted animals 指特徵特別適合其環境的動物。"},{"en":"In snowy areas, white-furred animals may be better adapted because predators see them less easily.","zh":"在雪地中，白毛動物可能較適應，因為捕食者較難看見牠們。"},{"en":"Good adaptation can increase survival and reproduction.","zh":"良好適應可以提高存活和繁殖機會。"},{"en":"The phrase means best suited to conditions, not strongest in every way.","zh":"這個短語意思是最適合環境，而不是每方面都最強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a boundary between","meaning":"……之間的界線","examples":[{"en":"Wallace discovered a boundary between Asian and Australian fauna.","zh":"Wallace 發現亞洲及澳洲動物群之間的界線。"},{"en":"A boundary between two things is a dividing line or zone separating them.","zh":"boundary between two things 指分隔兩者的界線或地帶。"},{"en":"A river may form a boundary between two districts.","zh":"河流可能形成兩個地區之間的界線。"},{"en":"Boundaries help show where one pattern ends and another begins.","zh":"界線幫助顯示一種模式在哪裏結束，另一種在哪裏開始。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe physical, biological, or social divisions.","zh":"這個短語可以描述實體、生物或社會分隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"Asian and Australian fauna","meaning":"亞洲及澳洲動物群","examples":[{"en":"Wallace’s Line separates Asian and Australian fauna.","zh":"華萊士線分隔亞洲及澳洲動物群。"},{"en":"Asian and Australian fauna means the animal life associated with Asian and Australian regions.","zh":"Asian and Australian fauna 指與亞洲和澳洲地區有關的動物生命。"},{"en":"Monkeys are common in Asian fauna, while many marsupials are linked to Australian fauna.","zh":"猴子常見於亞洲動物群，而許多有袋類動物與澳洲動物群相關。"},{"en":"Sharp differences between faunas can reveal ancient barriers and histories.","zh":"動物群之間的明顯差異可以揭示古代屏障和歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to animal groups, not plants.","zh":"這個短語指動物群，而不是植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"links exist between","meaning":"……之間存在聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Links exist between animals in Australia and Africa.","zh":"澳洲和非洲的動物之間存在聯繫。"},{"en":"Links exist between things means there are connections or relationships between them.","zh":"links exist between things 指事物之間有連接或關係。"},{"en":"Links exist between sleep and concentration because tired students often learn less effectively.","zh":"睡眠和專注力之間存在聯繫，因為疲倦學生通常學得較不有效。"},{"en":"When links exist between distant species, scientists may look for shared ancestry.","zh":"當遙遠物種之間存在聯繫，科學家可能尋找共同祖先。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence of connection.","zh":"這個短語描述有關聯的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the following summary","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the following summary using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the following summary means to fill gaps in the short text below the instruction.","zh":"complete the following summary 指填補指示下方短文中的空格。"},{"en":"Students should check grammar before choosing each word for the summary.","zh":"學生應在為摘要選每個詞前檢查文法。"},{"en":"This task tests whether the reader understands key ideas and exact wording.","zh":"這項任務測試讀者是否理解重點和準確用字。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不超過兩個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案應包含不超過兩個字。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must use one or two words only.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案只能使用一個或兩個詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “natural selection,” it fits because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 “natural selection”，它符合要求，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing three words may lose marks even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫三個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word-limit rule.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格字數限制規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Wegener supported continental drift rather than the land-bridge theory.","zh":"Wegener 支持大陸漂移，而不是陸橋理論。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of, showing that one option is chosen over another.","zh":"rather than 指而不是，顯示選擇一個選項而非另一個。"},{"en":"A student should revise weak grammar rather than simply rereading easy notes.","zh":"學生應溫習薄弱文法，而不是只重讀容易筆記。"},{"en":"The phrase helps separate the preferred explanation from the rejected one.","zh":"這個短語幫助把較受支持的解釋與被否定的解釋分開。"},{"en":"It is useful for making contrasts clear.","zh":"它適合用於清楚表達對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"unusual distribution of species","meaning":"物種的異常分布","examples":[{"en":"Continental movement helps explain the unusual distribution of species.","zh":"大陸移動有助解釋物種的異常分布。"},{"en":"Unusual distribution of species means species appear in places that are surprising or hard to explain.","zh":"unusual distribution of species 指物種出現在令人驚訝或難以解釋的地方。"},{"en":"If similar animals live on distant continents but not in between, their distribution may be unusual.","zh":"如果相似動物生活在遙遠大洲，卻不在中間地區，其分布可能異常。"},{"en":"Unusual patterns can lead scientists to consider ancient land movement.","zh":"異常模式可以引導科學家考慮古代陸地移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a puzzling pattern of where life is found.","zh":"這個短語描述生命出現位置上的謎樣模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"rejected theory","meaning":"被否定的理論","examples":[{"en":"The rejected theory proposed the existence of vanished land bridges.","zh":"被否定的理論提出已消失陸橋的存在。"},{"en":"A rejected theory is an explanation that has been dismissed because evidence does not support it well enough.","zh":"rejected theory 指因證據不足以支持而被否定的解釋。"},{"en":"A doctor may abandon a rejected theory about symptoms after lab results point elsewhere.","zh":"化驗結果指向其他方向後，醫生可能放棄關於症狀的被否定理論。"},{"en":"Theories can be rejected when better explanations appear.","zh":"當更好解釋出現，理論可以被否定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an idea no longer accepted in the argument.","zh":"這個短語描述在論證中不再被接受的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in constant motion","meaning":"不斷移動","examples":[{"en":"Tectonic plates are in constant motion.","zh":"構造板塊不斷移動。"},{"en":"In constant motion means always moving, even if the movement is slow.","zh":"in constant motion 指一直在移動，即使速度很慢。"},{"en":"A crowded station is in constant motion as people arrive, leave, and change platforms.","zh":"擁擠車站因人們到達、離開和轉月台而不斷移動。"},{"en":"Because plates keep moving, continents and oceans slowly change over time.","zh":"因為板塊持續移動，大陸和海洋會隨時間慢慢改變。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses continuous movement.","zh":"這個短語強調連續運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"central debate","meaning":"核心爭論","examples":[{"en":"The central debate in biogeography now concerns two different processes.","zh":"生物地理學中的核心爭論現在關於兩個不同過程。"},{"en":"A central debate is the main disagreement or question in a field.","zh":"central debate 指某領域中的主要分歧或問題。"},{"en":"A central debate in schools may be how much homework students should receive.","zh":"學校中的核心爭論可能是學生應有多少功課。"},{"en":"Central debates guide what researchers study and argue about.","zh":"核心爭論引導研究人員研究和爭論甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the core issue under discussion.","zh":"這個短語指出討論中的核心議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"shift to two concepts","meaning":"轉向兩個概念","examples":[{"en":"The debate has shifted to two concepts concerning species distribution.","zh":"這場爭論已轉向關於物種分布的兩個概念。"},{"en":"To shift to two concepts means to move the focus of discussion onto two main ideas.","zh":"shift to two concepts 指把討論焦點移到兩個主要想法上。"},{"en":"A writing lesson may shift to two concepts: clarity and evidence.","zh":"寫作課可能轉向兩個概念：清晰度和證據。"},{"en":"When a debate shifts, old questions may be replaced by more precise ones.","zh":"當爭論轉移，舊問題可能被更精確問題取代。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change in intellectual focus.","zh":"這個短語描述思想焦點的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 151 - Origin of Species & Continent Formation.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 152":[{"front":"roller-coaster pioneers","meaning":"過山車先驅","examples":[{"en":"Early roller-coaster pioneers could not have imagined today’s technology.","zh":"早期過山車先驅不可能想像今天的科技。"},{"en":"Roller-coaster pioneers were the early inventors, designers, and builders who helped create the first roller coasters.","zh":"roller-coaster pioneers 指幫助創造最早期過山車的早期發明者、設計師和建造者。"},{"en":"The roller-coaster pioneers had to work with simple materials such as wood, ice, wheels, and basic tracks.","zh":"過山車先驅必須使用木材、冰、輪子和基本軌道等簡單材料。"},{"en":"Because these pioneers experimented with new ride designs, later engineers could build faster and safer coasters.","zh":"因為這些先驅嘗試新的機動遊戲設計，後來的工程師才能建造更快和更安全的過山車。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the early people who started an important development.","zh":"討論開創某項重要發展的早期人物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"technological advancements","meaning":"科技進步","examples":[{"en":"Technological advancements have transformed roller-coaster design.","zh":"科技進步已改變過山車設計。"},{"en":"Technological advancements are improvements in machines, tools, materials, or scientific methods.","zh":"technological advancements 指機器、工具、材料或科學方法上的改良。"},{"en":"Smartphones became more powerful because of technological advancements in batteries, screens, and chips.","zh":"智能手機因電池、螢幕和晶片方面的科技進步而變得更強大。"},{"en":"In roller coasters, better brakes, wheels, and computer controls can create safer thrills.","zh":"在過山車中，更好的煞車、車輪和電腦控制可以創造更安全的刺激感。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing progress caused by new technology.","zh":"描述由新科技帶來的進展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be made to create","meaning":"為創造……而作出的","examples":[{"en":"Many advancements have been made to create modern roller coasters.","zh":"許多進步都是為創造現代過山車而作出的。"},{"en":"Be made to create something means be developed or produced for the purpose of making something possible.","zh":"be made to create something 指為了使某物成為可能而被發展或製造出來。"},{"en":"New safety rules were made to create a safer school environment.","zh":"新安全規則是為創造更安全的學校環境而制定的。"},{"en":"Stronger tracks were made to create rides that could go faster without becoming too dangerous.","zh":"更堅固的軌道是為創造可以更快但不會太危險的機動遊戲而製造的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the purpose behind improvements.","zh":"解釋改良背後的目的時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tallest and fastest","meaning":"最高及最快的","examples":[{"en":"Kingda Ka was described as the tallest and fastest roller coaster in the world.","zh":"Kingda Ka 被描述為世界上最高及最快的過山車。"},{"en":"Tallest and fastest means having the greatest height and the highest speed compared with others.","zh":"tallest and fastest 指與其他相比高度最高、速度最快。"},{"en":"A city may advertise its new tower as the tallest and fastest-built project in the region.","zh":"城市可能宣傳新塔樓為區內最高及建造速度最快的項目。"},{"en":"A ride described as the tallest and fastest attracts people who want extreme excitement.","zh":"被描述為最高及最快的機動遊戲會吸引追求極端刺激的人。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing record-breaking machines or structures.","zh":"比較破紀錄的機器或建築時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"launch passengers from zero to","meaning":"把乘客由零加速至……","examples":[{"en":"The ride launches passengers from zero to 128 miles per hour.","zh":"這項機動遊戲把乘客由零加速至每小時128英里。"},{"en":"To launch passengers from zero to a speed means to accelerate riders from a complete stop to that speed very quickly.","zh":"launch passengers from zero to a speed 指把乘客由完全靜止迅速加速到某速度。"},{"en":"A sports car can launch from zero to high speed in only a few seconds.","zh":"跑車可以在短短幾秒內由零加速至高速。"},{"en":"A sudden launch creates strong force because the body changes speed so quickly.","zh":"突然加速會產生強大力量，因為身體速度變化非常快。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing rapid acceleration.","zh":"描述快速加速時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"miles per hour","meaning":"每小時英里","examples":[{"en":"The roller coaster reaches 128 miles per hour in only a few seconds.","zh":"過山車在短短幾秒內達到每小時128英里。"},{"en":"Miles per hour is a unit used to measure speed, especially in Britain and the United States.","zh":"miles per hour 是量度速度的單位，尤其常見於英國和美國。"},{"en":"A car travelling at 60 miles per hour covers 60 miles in one hour.","zh":"以每小時60英里行駛的汽車，一小時行走60英里。"},{"en":"The higher the miles per hour, the faster the vehicle or ride is moving.","zh":"每小時英里數越高，車輛或機動遊戲移動得越快。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting speed.","zh":"報告速度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"take over four seconds to","meaning":"需要超過四秒才……","examples":[{"en":"Most sports cars take over four seconds to reach 60 miles per hour.","zh":"大多數跑車需要超過四秒才達到每小時60英里。"},{"en":"Take over four seconds to do something means need more than four seconds to complete that action.","zh":"take over four seconds to do something 指需要多於四秒才完成某行動。"},{"en":"Some computers take over four seconds to open a large file.","zh":"有些電腦需要超過四秒才開啟大型檔案。"},{"en":"If a ride reaches high speed faster than a sports car, the launch feels especially powerful.","zh":"如果機動遊戲比跑車更快達到高速，發射感會特別強烈。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing how long different actions take.","zh":"比較不同動作所需時間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"heave riders skyward","meaning":"把乘客猛力推向高空","examples":[{"en":"The roller coaster heaves its riders skyward at a steep angle.","zh":"過山車以陡峭角度把乘客猛力推向高空。"},{"en":"To heave riders skyward means to push or lift passengers upward with great force.","zh":"heave riders skyward 指以強大力量把乘客向上推或抬高。"},{"en":"A powerful lift can heave riders skyward so suddenly that they feel pressed into their seats.","zh":"強力提升可以突然把乘客推向高空，使他們感到被壓進座位。"},{"en":"The word heave suggests a heavy, forceful upward movement rather than a gentle climb.","zh":"heave 這個詞暗示沉重而有力的向上動作，而不是溫和爬升。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing dramatic upward motion.","zh":"描述戲劇性的向上移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"at a 90-degree angle","meaning":"以90度角","examples":[{"en":"The train rises at a 90-degree angle.","zh":"列車以90度角上升。"},{"en":"At a 90-degree angle means vertically or at a right angle to the ground.","zh":"at a 90-degree angle 指垂直，或與地面成直角。"},{"en":"A wall usually stands at a 90-degree angle to the floor.","zh":"牆壁通常與地板成90度角。"},{"en":"When a coaster climbs at a 90-degree angle, riders feel as if they are going straight up.","zh":"當過山車以90度角爬升，乘客會感覺像是垂直向上。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing exact position or slope.","zh":"描述準確位置或斜度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"straight up","meaning":"垂直向上","examples":[{"en":"The roller coaster carries its passengers straight up.","zh":"過山車把乘客垂直向上帶起。"},{"en":"Straight up means directly upward, without leaning much to the side.","zh":"straight up 指直接向上，沒有明顯向旁邊傾斜。"},{"en":"A lift moves straight up from the ground floor to the tenth floor.","zh":"升降機由地下垂直向上移動到十樓。"},{"en":"Going straight up can feel more frightening than climbing a gentle slope.","zh":"垂直向上移動可能比爬平緩斜坡更令人害怕。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing vertical movement.","zh":"描述垂直移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"reach a height of","meaning":"達到……的高度","examples":[{"en":"The train reaches a height of 456 feet.","zh":"列車達到456英尺的高度。"},{"en":"To reach a height of something means to rise to that measured level above the ground.","zh":"reach a height of something 指上升到離地某個量度高度。"},{"en":"A building may reach a height of 300 metres after construction is finished.","zh":"建築完成後可能達到300米的高度。"},{"en":"The higher a coaster reaches, the more energy it can gain before falling.","zh":"過山車升得越高，在下落前可獲得的能量就越多。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving exact height.","zh":"提供準確高度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"above the ground","meaning":"離地","examples":[{"en":"The highest point is more than 400 feet above the ground.","zh":"最高點離地超過400英尺。"},{"en":"Above the ground means higher than the surface of the earth or floor.","zh":"above the ground 指高於地面或地板表面。"},{"en":"A balcony on the tenth floor is far above the ground.","zh":"十樓的露台離地很高。"},{"en":"The farther riders are above the ground, the more dramatic the drop may feel.","zh":"乘客離地越遠，下降時可能感覺越戲劇化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing height or position.","zh":"描述高度或位置時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"before dropping","meaning":"在急降之前","examples":[{"en":"The train climbs steeply before dropping more than 400 feet.","zh":"列車在急降超過400英尺之前陡峭爬升。"},{"en":"Before dropping means before falling or descending quickly.","zh":"before dropping 指在下墜或快速下降之前。"},{"en":"A lift may pause for a moment before dropping to a lower floor in a safety test.","zh":"升降機在安全測試中下降到較低樓層之前，可能會暫停一刻。"},{"en":"In a roller coaster, the slow climb before dropping builds tension for riders.","zh":"在過山車中，急降之前的緩慢爬升會為乘客建立緊張感。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing what happens just before a fall.","zh":"描述下落前發生的事情時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"with that said","meaning":"話雖如此","examples":[{"en":"With that said, roller coasters are about more than speed and height.","zh":"話雖如此，過山車不只關乎速度和高度。"},{"en":"With that said means although the previous point is true, another point also needs attention.","zh":"with that said 指雖然前面的觀點是真的，但另一點也需要注意。"},{"en":"The exam is difficult; with that said, students can improve with regular practice.","zh":"考試很難；話雖如此，學生可以透過定期練習進步。"},{"en":"This phrase helps shift from one idea to a balancing idea.","zh":"這個短語幫助由一個想法轉到一個平衡想法。"},{"en":"It is useful when you want to add a qualification after a strong statement.","zh":"當你想在強烈說法後加入保留或補充時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be about more than","meaning":"不只關乎……","examples":[{"en":"Roller coasters are about more than just speed and height.","zh":"過山車不只關乎速度和高度。"},{"en":"Be about more than something means involve other important things besides that one thing.","zh":"be about more than something 指除了某事以外，還涉及其他重要事情。"},{"en":"Good teaching is about more than giving correct answers.","zh":"好教學不只關乎給出正確答案。"},{"en":"A successful ride needs design, safety, rhythm, surprise, and comfort as well as speed.","zh":"成功的機動遊戲除了速度，也需要設計、安全、節奏、驚喜和舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when rejecting an overly narrow view.","zh":"拒絕過於狹窄的看法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"creativity of the designers","meaning":"設計師的創意","examples":[{"en":"The creativity of the designers makes each ride distinctive.","zh":"設計師的創意令每項機動遊戲各具特色。"},{"en":"The creativity of the designers means the original ideas and imagination used by the people who design something.","zh":"creativity of the designers 指設計某物的人所使用的原創想法和想像力。"},{"en":"The creativity of the designers can turn a small classroom into an exciting learning space.","zh":"設計師的創意可以把小課室變成令人興奮的學習空間。"},{"en":"Creative design helps roller coasters feel different even when they use similar tracks and technology.","zh":"創意設計令過山車即使用相似軌道和科技，也能感覺不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how human imagination shapes a product.","zh":"解釋人類想像力如何塑造產品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"build roller coasters","meaning":"建造過山車","examples":[{"en":"Engineers and designers work together to build roller coasters.","zh":"工程師和設計師合作建造過山車。"},{"en":"To build roller coasters means to design, construct, and assemble rides with tracks, cars, supports, and safety systems.","zh":"build roller coasters 指設計、建造和組裝包含軌道、車卡、支架和安全系統的機動遊戲。"},{"en":"A company needs engineers, welders, electricians, and safety experts to build roller coasters.","zh":"公司需要工程師、焊接工、電工和安全專家來建造過山車。"},{"en":"Building roller coasters is difficult because the ride must be exciting and safe at the same time.","zh":"建造過山車很困難，因為機動遊戲必須同時刺激又安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the construction of amusement rides.","zh":"討論遊樂設施建設時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have its own unique way of","meaning":"有其獨特的……方式","examples":[{"en":"Each coaster has its own unique way of creating excitement.","zh":"每座過山車都有其獨特的製造刺激方式。"},{"en":"Have its own unique way of doing something means do something in a special style that is different from others.","zh":"have its own unique way of doing something 指以不同於其他事物的特別風格做某事。"},{"en":"Every teacher has their own unique way of explaining difficult grammar.","zh":"每位老師都有其獨特的解釋困難文法方式。"},{"en":"A coaster may create excitement through speed, height, darkness, sharp turns, or sudden drops.","zh":"過山車可能透過速度、高度、黑暗、急彎或突然下墜製造刺激。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing different methods or styles.","zh":"比較不同方法或風格時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"produce intense thrills","meaning":"帶來強烈刺激感","examples":[{"en":"Modern rides produce intense thrills while controlling risk.","zh":"現代機動遊戲在控制風險的同時帶來強烈刺激感。"},{"en":"To produce intense thrills means to create very strong feelings of excitement, fear, and enjoyment.","zh":"produce intense thrills 指製造非常強烈的興奮、恐懼和享受感。"},{"en":"A horror film can produce intense thrills without putting viewers in real danger.","zh":"恐怖電影可以帶來強烈刺激感，而不讓觀眾真正處於危險中。"},{"en":"Roller coasters produce thrills through speed and drops, but safety systems reduce actual risk.","zh":"過山車透過速度和下墜帶來刺激，但安全系統降低實際風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when entertainment feels exciting but controlled.","zh":"當娛樂令人興奮但受控制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"with less risk than","meaning":"風險比……低","examples":[{"en":"A roller-coaster ride may involve less risk than an average car journey.","zh":"一次過山車旅程的風險可能比一般汽車旅程低。"},{"en":"With less risk than something means being safer or less likely to cause harm than that thing.","zh":"with less risk than something 指比某事更安全或較不可能造成傷害。"},{"en":"Cycling in a protected lane may involve less risk than cycling beside heavy traffic.","zh":"在受保護單車徑踩單車，風險可能比在繁忙交通旁踩單車低。"},{"en":"Safety checks can make a frightening ride less risky than it looks.","zh":"安全檢查可以令看似可怕的機動遊戲風險較低。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing danger levels.","zh":"比較危險程度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"average car ride","meaning":"一般汽車旅程","examples":[{"en":"The writer compares roller-coaster safety with the average car ride.","zh":"作者把過山車安全性與一般汽車旅程作比較。"},{"en":"An average car ride is a normal journey by car, not an unusual or extreme one.","zh":"average car ride 指普通汽車旅程，而不是特殊或極端旅程。"},{"en":"A short trip to school is an average car ride for many families.","zh":"對許多家庭來說，短途上學是一段一般汽車旅程。"},{"en":"Comparing a roller coaster with an average car ride helps readers judge risk more realistically.","zh":"把過山車與一般汽車旅程比較，有助讀者更實際地判斷風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when referring to ordinary travel by car.","zh":"指普通汽車出行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"evolve drastically","meaning":"經歷巨大演變","examples":[{"en":"Roller coasters have evolved drastically over the centuries.","zh":"過山車幾個世紀以來經歷巨大演變。"},{"en":"To evolve drastically means to change very greatly over time.","zh":"evolve drastically 指隨時間發生非常巨大的改變。"},{"en":"Mobile phones have evolved drastically from simple calling devices into powerful computers.","zh":"手提電話由簡單通話工具變成強大電腦，經歷巨大演變。"},{"en":"Roller coasters changed from ice slides into complex steel rides because design and technology improved.","zh":"過山車由冰滑梯變成複雜鋼鐵機動遊戲，是因為設計和科技改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing major long-term change.","zh":"描述重大長期變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"over the years","meaning":"多年來","examples":[{"en":"The design of roller coasters has changed greatly over the years.","zh":"多年來，過山車設計發生了很大變化。"},{"en":"Over the years means during a long period of time.","zh":"over the years 指在很長一段時間內。"},{"en":"Over the years, a shy student can become a confident speaker through practice.","zh":"多年來，害羞學生可以透過練習變成自信演講者。"},{"en":"Small improvements made over the years can lead to a very different final result.","zh":"多年來作出的小改良，可以帶來非常不同的最終結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing gradual change.","zh":"描述漸進變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"primitive beginnings","meaning":"原始起源","examples":[{"en":"Roller coasters had primitive beginnings as ice slides.","zh":"過山車的原始起源是冰滑梯。"},{"en":"Primitive beginnings are simple, early, and undeveloped starting points.","zh":"primitive beginnings 指簡單、早期且尚未成熟的起點。"},{"en":"Many modern computers had primitive beginnings as large machines used only by experts.","zh":"許多現代電腦的原始起源是只有專家使用的大型機器。"},{"en":"A simple beginning can later develop into something complex and impressive.","zh":"簡單起點可以後來發展成複雜而令人印象深刻的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing how advanced things started simply.","zh":"描述先進事物如何由簡單起點開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Russian ice slides","meaning":"俄羅斯冰滑梯","examples":[{"en":"Russian ice slides were direct ancestors of modern roller coasters.","zh":"俄羅斯冰滑梯是現代過山車的直接前身。"},{"en":"Russian ice slides were early amusement structures made of icy slopes used for fast downhill rides.","zh":"Russian ice slides 指由冰斜坡構成、用於高速下滑的早期娛樂設施。"},{"en":"People in cold climates could enjoy Russian ice slides because natural ice made sliding possible.","zh":"寒冷氣候中的人可以享受俄羅斯冰滑梯，因為天然冰使滑行成為可能。"},{"en":"These slides mattered because they introduced the basic idea of climbing high and rushing down.","zh":"這些滑梯重要，因為它們引入了爬高再高速下滑的基本概念。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the historical origin of roller coasters.","zh":"解釋過山車歷史起源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"metal monsters","meaning":"鋼鐵巨獸","examples":[{"en":"The largest modern roller coasters are sometimes described as metal monsters.","zh":"最大型的現代過山車有時被描述為鋼鐵巨獸。"},{"en":"Metal monsters is a vivid phrase for huge, powerful-looking machines made mainly of metal.","zh":"metal monsters 是生動說法，指主要由金屬製成、巨大而有力量感的機器。"},{"en":"A giant crane on a construction site may look like a metal monster to a child.","zh":"對孩子來說，建築地盤上的巨型吊機可能像鋼鐵巨獸。"},{"en":"Calling a roller coaster a metal monster makes it sound massive, exciting, and a little frightening.","zh":"把過山車稱為鋼鐵巨獸，令它聽起來龐大、刺激且有點可怕。"},{"en":"This phrase is metaphorical and useful for dramatic description.","zh":"這個短語是比喻性，適合戲劇化描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"structural elements","meaning":"結構元素","examples":[{"en":"Roller coasters combine creative design with structural elements.","zh":"過山車結合創意設計和結構元素。"},{"en":"Structural elements are the physical parts that support and form a building, ride, or machine.","zh":"structural elements 指支撐和構成建築、機動遊戲或機器的實體部分。"},{"en":"Beams, columns, tracks, and supports are structural elements in a roller coaster.","zh":"橫樑、柱、軌道和支架都是過山車的結構元素。"},{"en":"If structural elements are weak, even a creative design cannot be safe.","zh":"如果結構元素薄弱，即使設計有創意也不能安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how something is physically built.","zh":"討論某物如何實體建造時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"purest forms of architecture","meaning":"最純粹的建築形式之一","examples":[{"en":"The writer considers roller coasters one of the purest forms of architecture.","zh":"作者認為過山車是最純粹的建築形式之一。"},{"en":"Purest forms of architecture means examples of building design that show structure and purpose very clearly.","zh":"purest forms of architecture 指非常清楚展示結構和用途的建築設計例子。"},{"en":"A bridge can be seen as a pure form of architecture because every support has a clear function.","zh":"橋樑可以被視為純粹建築形式，因為每個支撐都有清楚功能。"},{"en":"Roller coasters reveal their structure openly instead of hiding it behind walls.","zh":"過山車公開展示其結構，而不是把它藏在牆後。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing design that is both functional and beautiful.","zh":"討論兼具功能和美感的設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at first glance","meaning":"乍看之下","examples":[{"en":"At first glance, a roller coaster resembles a passenger train.","zh":"乍看之下，過山車像客運列車。"},{"en":"At first glance means when something is first seen or considered quickly.","zh":"at first glance 指最初看見或快速考慮某事時。"},{"en":"At first glance, the two essays look similar, but one has much stronger evidence.","zh":"乍看之下，兩篇文章很相似，但其中一篇證據強得多。"},{"en":"First impressions can be useful, but they may miss important differences.","zh":"第一印象可以有用，但可能錯過重要差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when appearance changes after closer examination.","zh":"當外觀在仔細檢視後改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"something like","meaning":"有點像……","examples":[{"en":"A roller coaster is something like a passenger train.","zh":"過山車有點像客運列車。"},{"en":"Something like means similar to, but not exactly the same as.","zh":"something like 指相似，但並不完全一樣。"},{"en":"A tablet is something like a small computer, but it is easier to carry.","zh":"平板電腦有點像小型電腦，但較容易攜帶。"},{"en":"A roller coaster looks like a train because it has connected cars on tracks, but it works differently.","zh":"過山車看起來像火車，因為它有在軌道上的相連車卡，但運作方式不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when making an approximate comparison.","zh":"作近似比較時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"consist of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"A roller coaster consists of a series of connected cars.","zh":"過山車由一連串相連車卡組成。"},{"en":"Consist of means be made up of particular parts.","zh":"consist of 指由特定部分組成。"},{"en":"A simple lunch may consist of rice, vegetables, and fish.","zh":"簡單午餐可能由米飯、蔬菜和魚組成。"},{"en":"If a ride consists of connected cars, all passengers move along the track together.","zh":"如果機動遊戲由相連車卡組成，所有乘客會一起沿軌道移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing what something is made from.","zh":"描述某物由甚麼構成時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a series of connected cars","meaning":"一連串相連車卡","examples":[{"en":"The ride contains a series of connected cars that move together.","zh":"這項機動遊戲包含一連串相連並一起移動的車卡。"},{"en":"A series of connected cars means several carriages joined together in order.","zh":"a series of connected cars 指幾節按順序連接起來的車廂或車卡。"},{"en":"A train has a series of connected cars so many passengers can travel at once.","zh":"火車有一連串相連車卡，因此許多乘客可以同時出行。"},{"en":"Connected cars help the roller coaster move as one train around the track.","zh":"相連車卡幫助過山車作為一列車沿軌道移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing linked vehicle sections.","zh":"描述相連車輛部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"move on tracks","meaning":"在軌道上行駛","examples":[{"en":"The cars move on tracks throughout the ride.","zh":"車卡在整個機動遊戲過程中都在軌道上行駛。"},{"en":"To move on tracks means to travel along fixed metal rails or guided paths.","zh":"move on tracks 指沿固定金屬路軌或導向路徑行駛。"},{"en":"Trams move on tracks through busy city streets.","zh":"電車在繁忙城市街道上沿軌道行駛。"},{"en":"Tracks control the direction of the cars and keep the ride predictable.","zh":"軌道控制車卡方向，並令機動遊戲走向可預測。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing rail-based movement.","zh":"描述以軌道為基礎的移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"unlike a passenger train","meaning":"與客運列車不同","examples":[{"en":"Unlike a passenger train, a roller coaster has no engine of its own.","zh":"與客運列車不同，過山車本身沒有引擎。"},{"en":"Unlike a passenger train means different from a train that carries passengers normally.","zh":"unlike a passenger train 指不同於一般載客列車。"},{"en":"Unlike a bus, a tram must follow fixed tracks.","zh":"與巴士不同，電車必須跟隨固定軌道。"},{"en":"The contrast helps readers see that roller coasters may look like trains but move differently.","zh":"這個對比幫助讀者看出過山車可能像火車，但移動方式不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing a clear difference from something familiar.","zh":"顯示與熟悉事物的清楚差異時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"power source of its own","meaning":"本身的動力來源","examples":[{"en":"The train has no power source of its own for most of the ride.","zh":"列車在大部分運行過程中沒有本身的動力來源。"},{"en":"A power source of its own is an engine, motor, battery, or system that provides energy independently.","zh":"power source of its own 指能獨立提供能量的引擎、馬達、電池或系統。"},{"en":"A bicycle has no power source of its own unless it is electric.","zh":"單車本身沒有動力來源，除非它是電動單車。"},{"en":"Because a coaster usually lacks its own engine, gravity and momentum do most of the work.","zh":"因為過山車通常沒有自己的引擎，重力和動量負責大部分運動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining where movement energy comes from.","zh":"解釋移動能量從何而來時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be moved by gravity and momentum","meaning":"由重力和動量推動","examples":[{"en":"The train is moved mainly by gravity and momentum.","zh":"列車主要由重力和動量推動。"},{"en":"Be moved by gravity and momentum means be carried forward by falling force and built-up motion.","zh":"be moved by gravity and momentum 指由下墜力量和累積運動帶動向前。"},{"en":"A skateboarder rolling downhill is moved by gravity and momentum.","zh":"滑板手下坡滑行時，就是由重力和動量推動。"},{"en":"Once a coaster has climbed high enough, gravity pulls it down and momentum carries it onward.","zh":"一旦過山車爬得夠高，重力把它拉下來，動量則帶它繼續前進。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining motion without an engine.","zh":"解釋沒有引擎的運動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"gravity and momentum","meaning":"重力和動量","examples":[{"en":"Gravity and momentum carry the train around the track.","zh":"重力和動量帶動列車沿軌道行駛。"},{"en":"Gravity is the force pulling things downward, and momentum is the motion an object keeps after moving.","zh":"gravity 是把物件向下拉的力量，而 momentum 是物件移動後保持的運動。"},{"en":"A ball rolling down a hill uses gravity and momentum to continue moving.","zh":"球沿山坡滾下時，利用重力和動量繼續移動。"},{"en":"Roller coasters rely on these forces after the first lift or launch.","zh":"過山車在第一次提升或發射後依靠這些力量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining basic physical forces in rides.","zh":"解釋機動遊戲中的基本物理力量時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"build up momentum","meaning":"累積動量","examples":[{"en":"The train must first build up momentum.","zh":"列車必須先累積動量。"},{"en":"To build up momentum means to gain speed and moving force gradually.","zh":"build up momentum 指逐漸獲得速度和運動力量。"},{"en":"A cyclist builds up momentum while riding down a slope.","zh":"單車手下坡時會累積動量。"},{"en":"Once momentum builds up, the train can continue through hills and turns without an engine.","zh":"一旦動量累積起來，列車就能不用引擎繼續穿過山坡和彎道。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing how movement becomes stronger.","zh":"描述運動如何變強時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"get the train to the top","meaning":"把列車送上頂部","examples":[{"en":"The lifting system gets the train to the top of the first hill.","zh":"提升系統把列車送上第一個山坡的頂部。"},{"en":"To get the train to the top means to move the train upward until it reaches the highest point.","zh":"get the train to the top 指把列車向上移動，直到它到達最高點。"},{"en":"A ski lift gets skiers to the top of a mountain before they come down.","zh":"滑雪吊椅把滑雪者送上山頂，然後他們滑下來。"},{"en":"Getting the train to the top gives it the height needed for the first drop.","zh":"把列車送上頂部，能給它第一次下墜所需的高度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the purpose of a lifting system.","zh":"解釋提升系統的目的時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"powerful launch","meaning":"強力發射","examples":[{"en":"Some modern coasters begin with a powerful launch.","zh":"有些現代過山車以強力發射開始。"},{"en":"A powerful launch is a sudden strong push that starts a ride or vehicle moving quickly.","zh":"powerful launch 指突然強力推動，使機動遊戲或車輛快速開始移動。"},{"en":"A rocket needs a powerful launch to leave the ground.","zh":"火箭需要強力發射才能離開地面。"},{"en":"A powerful launch can replace the slow climb used in older roller coasters.","zh":"強力發射可以取代舊式過山車使用的緩慢爬升。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a forceful start.","zh":"描述有力開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"traditional lifting mechanism","meaning":"傳統提升機制","examples":[{"en":"A long chain forms the traditional lifting mechanism.","zh":"一條長鏈構成傳統提升機制。"},{"en":"A traditional lifting mechanism is an older standard system used to pull a roller-coaster train uphill.","zh":"traditional lifting mechanism 指用來把過山車列車拉上坡的較舊標準系統。"},{"en":"Many classic coasters use a chain as their traditional lifting mechanism.","zh":"許多經典過山車使用鏈條作為傳統提升機制。"},{"en":"This mechanism gives the train enough height before gravity takes over.","zh":"這個機制在重力接手之前，給列車足夠高度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how older roller coasters begin their rides.","zh":"解釋舊式過山車如何開始運行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a long length of chain","meaning":"一條長鏈","examples":[{"en":"The system uses a long length of chain beneath the track.","zh":"這個系統使用軌道下方的一條長鏈。"},{"en":"A long length of chain is a long continuous piece made of linked metal parts.","zh":"long length of chain 指由相連金屬部分組成的一條長而連續的鏈。"},{"en":"A bicycle uses a chain to transfer power from the pedals to the wheel.","zh":"單車使用鏈條把腳踏的力量傳到車輪。"},{"en":"In a roller coaster, the chain pulls the cars slowly up the first hill.","zh":"在過山車中，鏈條把車卡慢慢拉上第一個山坡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a mechanical part.","zh":"描述機械部件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"run up the hill","meaning":"沿斜坡向上運行","examples":[{"en":"The chain runs up the hill under the track.","zh":"鏈條在軌道下方沿斜坡向上運行。"},{"en":"To run up the hill means to extend or move upward along a slope.","zh":"run up the hill 指沿斜坡向上延伸或移動。"},{"en":"A cable car line runs up the hill to carry passengers to the viewpoint.","zh":"纜車線沿斜坡向上運行，把乘客送到觀景點。"},{"en":"When the chain runs up the hill, it can pull the coaster train upward.","zh":"當鏈條沿斜坡向上運行，它就能把過山車列車向上拉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing direction along a slope.","zh":"描述沿斜坡的方向時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"under the track","meaning":"在軌道下方","examples":[{"en":"The lifting chain is positioned under the track.","zh":"提升鏈條位於軌道下方。"},{"en":"Under the track means below the rails or path on which the cars move.","zh":"under the track 指在車卡行駛的路軌或路徑下面。"},{"en":"Wires may be hidden under the floor so people do not trip over them.","zh":"電線可能藏在地板下方，以免人絆倒。"},{"en":"Placing the chain under the track lets it pull the train without blocking the riders’ view.","zh":"把鏈條放在軌道下方，讓它能拉動列車而不阻擋乘客視線。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing location in a machine or structure.","zh":"描述機器或結構中的位置時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be fastened in a loop","meaning":"被連接成環狀","examples":[{"en":"The chain is fastened in a continuous loop.","zh":"鏈條被連接成一個連續環狀。"},{"en":"Be fastened in a loop means be joined to form a closed circle or oval shape.","zh":"be fastened in a loop 指被接合成封閉圓形或橢圓形。"},{"en":"A belt on a machine is fastened in a loop so it can keep moving around wheels.","zh":"機器上的皮帶被連接成環狀，因此能不停繞着輪子移動。"},{"en":"A looped chain can move continuously and pull each train up the hill.","zh":"環狀鏈條可以持續移動，並把每列車拉上山坡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing circular mechanical movement.","zh":"描述循環機械運動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be wound around","meaning":"纏繞在……上","examples":[{"en":"The chain is wound around gears at both ends of the hill.","zh":"鏈條纏繞在山坡兩端的齒輪上。"},{"en":"Be wound around means be wrapped or looped around something.","zh":"be wound around 指被繞在或纏在某物上。"},{"en":"A rope may be wound around a pole to hold a tent in place.","zh":"繩子可能纏繞在柱上，以固定帳篷。"},{"en":"When a chain is wound around gears, the gears can move it smoothly.","zh":"當鏈條纏繞在齒輪上，齒輪就能順暢帶動它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing how flexible parts fit around wheels or gears.","zh":"描述可彎曲部件如何繞着輪子或齒輪時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"gear at the top","meaning":"位於頂部的齒輪","examples":[{"en":"One gear is located at the top of the hill.","zh":"一個齒輪位於山坡頂部。"},{"en":"A gear at the top is a toothed wheel placed at the upper end of a mechanism.","zh":"gear at the top 指放在機械裝置上端的有齒輪子。"},{"en":"A bicycle has gears that help control how force is transferred to the wheel.","zh":"單車有齒輪，幫助控制力量如何傳到車輪。"},{"en":"The top gear helps guide the chain over the summit of the lift hill.","zh":"頂部齒輪幫助引導鏈條越過提升坡的最高點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the position of mechanical parts.","zh":"描述機械零件位置時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bottom of the hill","meaning":"斜坡底部","examples":[{"en":"A second gear is positioned at the bottom of the hill.","zh":"第二個齒輪位於斜坡底部。"},{"en":"The bottom of the hill is the lowest part of a slope.","zh":"bottom of the hill 指斜坡最低的位置。"},{"en":"A bus stop may be located at the bottom of the hill so passengers do not have to climb far.","zh":"巴士站可能設在斜坡底部，讓乘客不必爬太遠。"},{"en":"The lower gear starts the chain moving upward from the base of the lift hill.","zh":"較低的齒輪從提升坡底部開始帶動鏈條向上。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing position on a slope.","zh":"描述斜坡上的位置時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be turned by","meaning":"由……帶動","examples":[{"en":"The lower gear is turned by a simple motor.","zh":"較低的齒輪由簡單馬達帶動。"},{"en":"Be turned by something means be rotated or made to move around by that thing.","zh":"be turned by something 指由某物使其旋轉或轉動。"},{"en":"A fan blade is turned by an electric motor.","zh":"風扇葉片由電動馬達帶動。"},{"en":"When the gear is turned by the motor, the chain begins to move.","zh":"當齒輪由馬達帶動，鏈條就開始移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining what powers a moving part.","zh":"解釋甚麼為活動部件提供動力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"simple motor","meaning":"簡單馬達","examples":[{"en":"A simple motor powers the chain mechanism.","zh":"一個簡單馬達為鏈條機制提供動力。"},{"en":"A simple motor is a basic machine that turns electrical energy into movement.","zh":"simple motor 指把電能轉化為運動的基本機器。"},{"en":"A toy car may use a simple motor to turn its wheels.","zh":"玩具車可能使用簡單馬達來轉動車輪。"},{"en":"In the lift system, the motor moves the chain so the train can climb.","zh":"在提升系統中，馬達帶動鏈條，使列車可以爬升。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing basic mechanical power.","zh":"描述基本機械動力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"chain loop","meaning":"鏈條環","examples":[{"en":"The motor continuously turns the chain loop.","zh":"馬達持續轉動鏈條環。"},{"en":"A chain loop is a chain joined into a closed moving circle.","zh":"chain loop 指被接成封閉移動圓環的鏈條。"},{"en":"A bicycle chain forms a loop around the front and back gears.","zh":"單車鏈條在前後齒輪周圍形成一個環。"},{"en":"A chain loop can keep moving in one direction and carry force around a system.","zh":"鏈條環可以持續朝一個方向移動，並在系統中傳遞力量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining chain-driven machines.","zh":"解釋鏈條驅動機器時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"continually move up","meaning":"持續向上移動","examples":[{"en":"The chain continually moves up the hill.","zh":"鏈條持續向斜坡上方移動。"},{"en":"Continually move up means keep moving upward without stopping for long.","zh":"continually move up 指不停或不長時間停止地向上移動。"},{"en":"A queue may continually move up when staff serve customers quickly.","zh":"如果職員快速服務顧客，隊伍可能持續向前移動。"},{"en":"The chain must keep moving upward so it can pull each coaster train to the summit.","zh":"鏈條必須持續向上移動，才能把每列過山車拉到最高點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing repeated or continuous upward motion.","zh":"描述重複或連續向上運動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"conveyor belt","meaning":"輸送帶","examples":[{"en":"The moving chain functions like a long conveyor belt.","zh":"移動中的鏈條像一條長輸送帶般運作。"},{"en":"A conveyor belt is a moving belt used to carry objects from one place to another.","zh":"conveyor belt 指用來把物件從一處運到另一處的移動帶。"},{"en":"Supermarket checkouts use conveyor belts to move groceries toward the cashier.","zh":"超級市場收銀處使用輸送帶把貨品送到收銀員面前。"},{"en":"The chain works like a conveyor belt because it carries pulling force up the hill.","zh":"鏈條像輸送帶一樣運作，因為它把拉力帶上斜坡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining continuous mechanical movement.","zh":"解釋連續機械運動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"grip onto","meaning":"緊扣住……","examples":[{"en":"The coaster cars grip onto the chain during the climb.","zh":"過山車車卡在爬升期間緊扣住鏈條。"},{"en":"To grip onto something means to hold it tightly so that it does not slip away.","zh":"grip onto something 指緊緊抓住某物，使它不會滑走。"},{"en":"A child may grip onto a handrail when climbing steep stairs.","zh":"孩子爬陡樓梯時可能緊握扶手。"},{"en":"The cars must grip onto the chain so they can be pulled safely upward.","zh":"車卡必須緊扣住鏈條，才能被安全地向上拉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a firm mechanical or physical hold.","zh":"描述堅固機械連接或身體抓握時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"chain dogs","meaning":"鏈鈎","examples":[{"en":"Chain dogs connect the train to the lifting chain.","zh":"鏈鈎把列車連接到提升鏈條。"},{"en":"Chain dogs are hooks or catches under coaster cars that attach to the lift chain.","zh":"chain dogs 指過山車車卡下方扣住提升鏈條的鈎或扣件。"},{"en":"A latch on a gate works a little like a chain dog because it catches and holds onto something.","zh":"閘門上的門閂有點像鏈鈎，因為它會扣住並固定某物。"},{"en":"Without chain dogs, the moving chain could not pull the train up the hill securely.","zh":"沒有鏈鈎，移動中的鏈條就不能穩固地把列車拉上山坡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining a specific roller-coaster part.","zh":"解釋特定過山車部件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sturdy hinged hooks","meaning":"堅固的鉸接式鈎","examples":[{"en":"Chain dogs are sturdy hinged hooks beneath the cars.","zh":"鏈鈎是車卡下方堅固的鉸接式鈎。"},{"en":"Sturdy hinged hooks are strong hooks attached with joints that allow them to move.","zh":"sturdy hinged hooks 指有活動接頭、可以移動的堅固鈎件。"},{"en":"A folding gate may use sturdy hinges so it can open and close safely.","zh":"摺閘可能使用堅固鉸鏈，使它能安全開關。"},{"en":"Strong hinged hooks can catch the chain firmly while still releasing at the right moment.","zh":"堅固的鉸接式鈎可以牢牢扣住鏈條，同時在正確時刻鬆開。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing durable moving parts.","zh":"描述耐用活動部件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"roll to the bottom","meaning":"滑行至底部","examples":[{"en":"The train rolls to the bottom of the first hill.","zh":"列車滑行至第一個山坡的底部。"},{"en":"To roll to the bottom means to move downward on wheels until reaching the lowest point.","zh":"roll to the bottom 指靠輪子向下移動，直到到達最低點。"},{"en":"A ball may roll to the bottom of a driveway if the ground slopes downward.","zh":"如果車道向下傾斜，球可能滾到車道底部。"},{"en":"Once the train reaches the bottom, it is ready to catch onto the lift chain.","zh":"一旦列車到達底部，它就準備扣住提升鏈條。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing movement down a slope.","zh":"描述沿斜坡向下移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"catch onto","meaning":"扣住……","examples":[{"en":"The hooks catch onto the moving chain links.","zh":"鈎子扣住移動中的鏈環。"},{"en":"To catch onto something means to hook, grip, or attach to it.","zh":"catch onto something 指鈎住、抓住或連接到某物。"},{"en":"A jacket may catch onto a door handle when someone walks past.","zh":"外套經過門柄時可能勾住門柄。"},{"en":"The hooks must catch onto the chain before the train can be pulled upward.","zh":"鈎子必須先扣住鏈條，列車才能被向上拉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing attachment after contact.","zh":"描述接觸後連接時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"chain links","meaning":"鏈環","examples":[{"en":"The chain dogs attach themselves to the chain links.","zh":"鏈鈎會扣住鏈環。"},{"en":"Chain links are the individual metal loops that make up a chain.","zh":"chain links 指組成鏈條的一個個金屬環。"},{"en":"A necklace chain is made of many small chain links.","zh":"頸鏈由許多小鏈環組成。"},{"en":"The hooks can pull the train because they catch individual links in the moving chain.","zh":"鈎子能拉動列車，是因為它們扣住移動鏈條中的個別鏈環。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the parts of a chain.","zh":"描述鏈條組成部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be hooked","meaning":"被鈎住","examples":[{"en":"Once the chain dog is hooked, the train begins to climb.","zh":"一旦鏈鈎被鈎住，列車就開始爬升。"},{"en":"Be hooked means be caught or attached by a hook.","zh":"be hooked 指被鈎子扣住或連接。"},{"en":"A bag may be hooked onto a bicycle handle for a short ride.","zh":"袋子可能被鈎在單車手把上作短途騎行。"},{"en":"Once the coaster hook catches the chain, the train can be pulled uphill.","zh":"一旦過山車鈎扣住鏈條，列車就能被拉上坡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a secure connection.","zh":"描述穩固連接時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pull the train to the top","meaning":"把列車拉上頂部","examples":[{"en":"The chain pulls the train to the top of the hill.","zh":"鏈條把列車拉上山坡頂部。"},{"en":"To pull the train to the top means to drag or lift the train upward until it reaches the summit.","zh":"pull the train to the top 指把列車向上拖或拉，直到它到達最高點。"},{"en":"A tow rope pulls skiers to the top of a small slope.","zh":"拖索把滑雪者拉上小斜坡頂部。"},{"en":"Pulling the train to the top gives the coaster the height needed for the first descent.","zh":"把列車拉上頂部，給過山車第一次下降所需的高度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the lift phase of a roller coaster.","zh":"描述過山車提升階段時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at the summit","meaning":"在最高點","examples":[{"en":"At the summit, the train is released from the chain.","zh":"在最高點，列車會從鏈條鬆開。"},{"en":"At the summit means at the highest point of a hill, mountain, or track.","zh":"at the summit 指在山、斜坡或軌道的最高點。"},{"en":"Hikers may rest at the summit after a long climb.","zh":"行山人士長時間攀登後可能在最高點休息。"},{"en":"On a roller coaster, reaching the summit usually comes just before the main drop.","zh":"在過山車上，到達最高點通常緊接主要下墜之前。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the top point of a climb.","zh":"描述爬升頂點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be released","meaning":"被鬆開","examples":[{"en":"The chain dog is released when the train reaches the summit.","zh":"當列車到達最高點時，鏈鈎被鬆開。"},{"en":"Be released means be let go or no longer held.","zh":"be released 指被放開或不再被固定。"},{"en":"A seat belt buckle is released when the passenger presses the button.","zh":"乘客按下按鈕時，安全帶扣會被鬆開。"},{"en":"Once the train is released from the chain, gravity begins to pull it downward.","zh":"一旦列車從鏈條鬆開，重力就開始把它向下拉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something stops being attached or controlled.","zh":"當某物停止被連接或控制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"start its descent","meaning":"開始下降","examples":[{"en":"The train starts its descent down the first hill.","zh":"列車開始沿第一個山坡下降。"},{"en":"To start its descent means to begin moving downward.","zh":"start its descent 指開始向下移動。"},{"en":"An aircraft starts its descent when it begins to fly lower before landing.","zh":"飛機降落前開始飛低，就是開始下降。"},{"en":"The first descent gives riders speed and excitement for the rest of the ride.","zh":"第一次下降為乘客帶來速度和刺激，推動餘下旅程。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the beginning of a downward movement.","zh":"描述向下移動的開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"long, fascinating history","meaning":"悠久而有趣的歷史","examples":[{"en":"Roller coasters have a long, fascinating history.","zh":"過山車有悠久而有趣的歷史。"},{"en":"A long, fascinating history is a history that lasts many years and contains interesting developments.","zh":"long, fascinating history 指持續多年並包含有趣發展的歷史。"},{"en":"The history of public transport has a long, fascinating history of horses, trams, buses, and trains.","zh":"公共交通有悠久而有趣的歷史，包括馬車、電車、巴士和火車。"},{"en":"Learning the history of roller coasters shows how simple slides became modern thrill rides.","zh":"學習過山車歷史可以顯示簡單滑梯如何變成現代刺激機動遊戲。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing an interesting historical topic.","zh":"引入有趣歷史主題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"direct ancestors of","meaning":"……的直接前身","examples":[{"en":"Russian ice slides were the direct ancestors of roller coasters.","zh":"俄羅斯冰滑梯是過山車的直接前身。"},{"en":"Direct ancestors of something are earlier forms from which the later thing developed.","zh":"direct ancestors of something 指後來事物由其發展而來的較早形式。"},{"en":"Early handwritten newsletters were direct ancestors of modern newspapers.","zh":"早期手寫通訊是現代報紙的直接前身。"},{"en":"Calling ice slides the direct ancestors of roller coasters shows a clear line of development.","zh":"把冰滑梯稱為過山車的直接前身，顯示清楚的發展線索。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when tracing origins.","zh":"追溯起源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"monumental ice slides","meaning":"巨型冰滑梯","examples":[{"en":"Monumental ice slides were popular in early modern Russia.","zh":"巨型冰滑梯在近代早期俄羅斯很受歡迎。"},{"en":"Monumental ice slides were very large and impressive ice-covered sliding structures.","zh":"monumental ice slides 指非常大型、令人印象深刻並覆蓋冰面的滑梯結構。"},{"en":"A monumental staircase in a museum is huge enough to impress visitors immediately.","zh":"博物館中的巨型樓梯大得足以立刻令訪客印象深刻。"},{"en":"Large ice slides attracted crowds because they looked grand and offered exciting speed.","zh":"大型冰滑梯吸引群眾，因為它們看起來宏偉並提供刺激速度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing something large, historic, and impressive.","zh":"描述大型、具歷史感且令人印象深刻的事物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"long, steep wooden slides","meaning":"又長又陡的木滑梯","examples":[{"en":"The earliest rides used long, steep wooden slides.","zh":"最早期的機動遊戲使用又長又陡的木滑梯。"},{"en":"Long, steep wooden slides are extended wooden slopes that drop sharply downward.","zh":"long, steep wooden slides 指又長並急速向下傾斜的木製滑坡。"},{"en":"A playground slide that is very high and sharply angled may feel steep to young children.","zh":"對幼童來說，非常高且角度大的遊樂場滑梯可能感覺很陡。"},{"en":"The steepness helped early riders gain speed as they slid down.","zh":"陡峭程度幫助早期乘客在滑下時獲得速度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the shape of early amusement rides.","zh":"描述早期娛樂設施形狀時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be covered in ice","meaning":"覆蓋着冰","examples":[{"en":"The wooden slides were covered in ice.","zh":"木滑梯覆蓋着冰。"},{"en":"Be covered in ice means have ice spread over the surface.","zh":"be covered in ice 指表面被冰覆蓋。"},{"en":"A car windscreen may be covered in ice on a very cold morning.","zh":"在非常寒冷的早上，汽車擋風玻璃可能覆蓋着冰。"},{"en":"Ice makes a surface slippery, so riders can slide down quickly.","zh":"冰令表面變滑，所以乘客可以快速滑下。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing frozen surfaces.","zh":"描述結冰表面時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as high as","meaning":"高達……","examples":[{"en":"Some Russian slides were as high as 70 feet.","zh":"有些俄羅斯滑梯高達70英尺。"},{"en":"As high as means reaching a surprisingly high maximum amount or level.","zh":"as high as 指達到令人驚訝的高位或最高數量。"},{"en":"In summer, the temperature in some cities can rise as high as 40 degrees Celsius.","zh":"夏天某些城市氣溫可高達攝氏40度。"},{"en":"Saying a slide was as high as 70 feet helps readers understand why it felt thrilling.","zh":"說滑梯高達70英尺，有助讀者理解它為何刺激。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving an impressive maximum figure.","zh":"提供令人印象深刻的最高數字時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"shoot down the slope","meaning":"高速滑下斜坡","examples":[{"en":"Riders shot down the slope at high speed.","zh":"乘客高速滑下斜坡。"},{"en":"To shoot down the slope means to move very quickly down an inclined surface.","zh":"shoot down the slope 指非常快速地沿斜面向下移動。"},{"en":"A child on a sled may shoot down a snowy hill after a strong push.","zh":"坐在雪橇上的孩子被用力一推後，可能高速滑下雪坡。"},{"en":"A steep icy slope causes riders to move faster and feel more excitement.","zh":"陡峭結冰斜坡會令乘客移動更快，感到更刺激。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing sudden fast downward movement.","zh":"描述突然快速向下移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sleds made out of wood","meaning":"木製雪橇","examples":[{"en":"Some riders used sleds made out of wood.","zh":"有些乘客使用木製雪橇。"},{"en":"Sleds made out of wood are sliding vehicles built from wooden materials.","zh":"sleds made out of wood 指由木材製成的滑行工具。"},{"en":"Children in snowy areas may use wooden sleds to slide down small hills.","zh":"下雪地區的孩子可能使用木製雪橇滑下小山坡。"},{"en":"Wood was a practical early material because it was available and easy to shape.","zh":"木材是實用的早期材料，因為它容易取得並易於塑形。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing what an object is made from.","zh":"描述物件由甚麼製成時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"blocks of ice","meaning":"冰塊","examples":[{"en":"Other riders travelled on solid blocks of ice.","zh":"其他乘客坐在實心冰塊上滑行。"},{"en":"Blocks of ice are large solid pieces of frozen water.","zh":"blocks of ice 指大型固體冰塊。"},{"en":"Restaurants may keep fish fresh by placing it on blocks of ice.","zh":"餐廳可能把魚放在冰塊上保持新鮮。"},{"en":"Ice blocks could slide smoothly on icy surfaces, making them useful for early rides.","zh":"冰塊可以在結冰表面順暢滑行，因此對早期機動遊戲有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing simple frozen objects.","zh":"描述簡單冰凍物件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"crash-land in","meaning":"猛然着地於……","examples":[{"en":"The riders would crash-land in a pile of sand.","zh":"乘客會猛然着地於一堆沙中。"},{"en":"To crash-land in something means to land suddenly and roughly in that place.","zh":"crash-land in something 指突然並猛烈地降落在某處。"},{"en":"A child jumping from a sofa may crash-land in a pile of cushions.","zh":"孩子從梳化跳下時，可能猛然落在一堆墊子上。"},{"en":"A sand pile softened the rough landing after riders came down quickly.","zh":"沙堆在乘客高速滑下後，緩和粗暴着地。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing an uncontrolled or forceful landing.","zh":"描述失控或強力着地時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sand pile","meaning":"沙堆","examples":[{"en":"A sand pile helped stop the sleds safely.","zh":"沙堆幫助雪橇安全停下。"},{"en":"A sand pile is a heap of sand placed in one area.","zh":"sand pile 指堆在一處的一堆沙。"},{"en":"Construction workers may leave a sand pile beside a building site.","zh":"建築工人可能把沙堆放在工地旁。"},{"en":"In early rides, a sand pile slowed riders down and reduced the danger of stopping suddenly.","zh":"在早期機動遊戲中，沙堆令乘客減速，降低突然停下的危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a simple safety feature.","zh":"描述簡單安全設施時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"coaster historians","meaning":"過山車歷史學家","examples":[{"en":"Coaster historians disagree about the development of early rides.","zh":"過山車歷史學家對早期機動遊戲的發展意見不一。"},{"en":"Coaster historians are people who study the history of roller coasters.","zh":"coaster historians 指研究過山車歷史的人。"},{"en":"A coaster historian may collect old maps, tickets, photographs, and engineering records.","zh":"過山車歷史學家可能收集舊地圖、門票、照片和工程紀錄。"},{"en":"Historians may disagree when evidence from the early period is incomplete.","zh":"當早期證據不完整時，歷史學家可能意見分歧。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing experts on roller-coaster history.","zh":"討論過山車歷史專家時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"diverge on","meaning":"對……意見分歧","examples":[{"en":"Historians diverge on how ice slides developed into roller coasters.","zh":"歷史學家對冰滑梯如何發展成過山車意見分歧。"},{"en":"To diverge on something means to have different opinions about it.","zh":"diverge on something 指對某事有不同意見。"},{"en":"Teachers may diverge on whether homework should be given every day.","zh":"老師可能對是否應每天給功課意見分歧。"},{"en":"People often diverge when evidence is unclear or can be interpreted in several ways.","zh":"當證據不清楚或可有多種解讀，人們常會意見分歧。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing disagreement among experts.","zh":"描述專家之間的分歧時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"exact evolution of","meaning":"……的確切演變","examples":[{"en":"The exact evolution of ice slides remains debated.","zh":"冰滑梯的確切演變仍有爭議。"},{"en":"The exact evolution of something means the precise way it changed step by step over time.","zh":"exact evolution of something 指某物隨時間逐步變化的準確過程。"},{"en":"Researchers may not know the exact evolution of a local festival if early records are missing.","zh":"如果早期紀錄缺失，研究人員可能不知道某本地節日的確切演變。"},{"en":"When evidence is incomplete, the exact path of development can remain uncertain.","zh":"當證據不完整，發展的確切路徑可能仍不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing historical or biological change in detail.","zh":"詳細討論歷史或生物變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rolling carts","meaning":"滾輪車","examples":[{"en":"Ice slides eventually developed into rides using rolling carts.","zh":"冰滑梯最終發展成使用滾輪車的機動遊戲。"},{"en":"Rolling carts are small wheeled vehicles that move along a surface or track.","zh":"rolling carts 指沿表面或軌道移動的小型有輪車輛。"},{"en":"A warehouse may use rolling carts to move heavy boxes.","zh":"倉庫可能使用滾輪車搬運重箱。"},{"en":"Adding rolling carts changed ice-slide rides into something closer to modern roller coasters.","zh":"加入滾輪車令冰滑梯遊戲變得更接近現代過山車。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing early wheeled vehicles.","zh":"描述早期有輪車輛時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"most widespread account","meaning":"最廣泛流傳的說法","examples":[{"en":"The most widespread account credits French entrepreneurs with the change.","zh":"最廣泛流傳的說法把這項改變歸功於法國企業家。"},{"en":"The most widespread account is the version of a story that is most commonly accepted or repeated.","zh":"most widespread account 指最常被接受或重複的故事版本。"},{"en":"The most widespread account of a school tradition may come from older teachers.","zh":"關於學校傳統最廣泛流傳的說法可能來自年長老師。"},{"en":"A widespread account may be popular even if historians still debate the details.","zh":"廣泛流傳的說法可能很流行，即使歷史學家仍在爭論細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one explanation is common but not necessarily final.","zh":"當一個解釋常見但未必是最終定論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"entrepreneurial Frenchmen","meaning":"有企業家精神的法國人","examples":[{"en":"Entrepreneurial Frenchmen brought the ice-slide idea to France.","zh":"有企業家精神的法國人把冰滑梯構思帶到法國。"},{"en":"Entrepreneurial Frenchmen were French people with business energy and a willingness to try new commercial ideas.","zh":"entrepreneurial Frenchmen 指具有商業活力並願意嘗試新商業構思的法國人。"},{"en":"Entrepreneurial shop owners may turn a simple local snack into a successful brand.","zh":"有企業家精神的店主可能把簡單本地小食變成成功品牌。"},{"en":"These Frenchmen saw an entertainment idea and tried to adapt it for a new market.","zh":"這些法國人看到一個娛樂構思，並嘗試把它改造成適合新市場的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing people who combine invention with business ambition.","zh":"描述結合創新和商業野心的人時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"import an idea to","meaning":"把構思引入……","examples":[{"en":"French businessmen imported the Russian idea to France.","zh":"法國商人把俄羅斯構思引入法國。"},{"en":"To import an idea to a place means to bring a concept from one country or setting into another.","zh":"import an idea to a place 指把一個概念從一個國家或環境帶到另一個地方。"},{"en":"A school may import an idea from another education system and adapt it for local students.","zh":"學校可能從另一個教育制度引入構思，並為本地學生作調整。"},{"en":"Imported ideas often need changes because local conditions are different.","zh":"引入的構思常需要改變，因為本地條件不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how concepts spread across places.","zh":"討論概念如何跨地方傳播時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"warmer climate","meaning":"較溫暖的氣候","examples":[{"en":"The warmer climate of France caused practical difficulties.","zh":"法國較溫暖的氣候造成實際困難。"},{"en":"Warmer climate means weather conditions that are generally hotter than another place.","zh":"warmer climate 指整體天氣比另一地方較熱。"},{"en":"A warmer climate can make outdoor ice activities difficult to maintain.","zh":"較溫暖的氣候會令戶外冰上活動難以維持。"},{"en":"Because France was warmer than Russia, ice slides melted more easily.","zh":"因為法國比俄羅斯溫暖，冰滑梯較容易融化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when weather affects design or lifestyle.","zh":"當天氣影響設計或生活方式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tend to melt","meaning":"往往會融化","examples":[{"en":"The French climate tended to melt the ice.","zh":"法國氣候往往會令冰融化。"},{"en":"Tend to melt means usually become liquid because of heat.","zh":"tend to melt 指通常因熱力而變成液體。"},{"en":"Ice cream tends to melt quickly if it is left in the sun.","zh":"如果雪糕放在陽光下，往往會很快融化。"},{"en":"Because the ice melted too easily, designers needed a different surface.","zh":"因為冰太容易融化，設計師需要不同表面。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a repeated natural tendency.","zh":"描述反覆出現的自然傾向時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"waxed slides","meaning":"塗蠟滑梯","examples":[{"en":"The French began building waxed slides instead of ice-covered ones.","zh":"法國人開始建造塗蠟滑梯，而不是覆冰滑梯。"},{"en":"Waxed slides are slides coated with wax to make the surface smooth and slippery.","zh":"waxed slides 指表面塗上蠟以變得順滑和易滑的滑梯。"},{"en":"A drawer may slide more easily if its runners are waxed.","zh":"如果抽屜路軌塗蠟，抽屜可能更容易滑動。"},{"en":"Wax replaced ice because it could create a slippery surface in a warmer climate.","zh":"蠟取代冰，因為它能在較暖氣候中製造滑面。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how a design was adapted.","zh":"解釋設計如何被改造時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"add wheels to","meaning":"為……加上輪子","examples":[{"en":"Designers eventually added wheels to the sleds.","zh":"設計師最終為雪橇加上輪子。"},{"en":"To add wheels to something means to attach wheels so it can roll instead of only slide.","zh":"add wheels to something 指加裝輪子，使某物能滾動而不只是滑行。"},{"en":"A suitcase becomes easier to move when manufacturers add wheels to it.","zh":"製造商為行李箱加上輪子後，行李箱就更容易移動。"},{"en":"Adding wheels allowed rides to work even when ice was not available.","zh":"加上輪子令機動遊戲即使沒有冰也能運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining a practical design improvement.","zh":"解釋實用設計改良時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be attached to the track","meaning":"被固定在軌道上","examples":[{"en":"The train was attached securely to the track.","zh":"列車被安全固定在軌道上。"},{"en":"Be attached to the track means be connected to the rails so that the vehicle stays in place.","zh":"be attached to the track 指被連接到路軌，使車輛保持在位置上。"},{"en":"A toy train works better when it is properly attached to its track.","zh":"玩具火車正確固定在軌道上時，運作會更好。"},{"en":"Secure attachment reduces the chance of the cars leaving the track during turns.","zh":"穩固連接減少車卡在轉彎時離開軌道的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing ride safety and control.","zh":"討論機動遊戲安全和控制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"train axle","meaning":"列車車軸","examples":[{"en":"The train axle fitted into a groove in the track.","zh":"列車車軸嵌入軌道中的凹槽。"},{"en":"A train axle is a rod or bar that connects wheels and helps them turn together.","zh":"train axle 指連接車輪並幫助它們一起轉動的杆或軸。"},{"en":"A bicycle wheel also turns around an axle.","zh":"單車車輪也圍繞車軸轉動。"},{"en":"If the axle fits into a groove, the car can stay aligned with the track.","zh":"如果車軸嵌入凹槽，車卡就能與軌道保持對齊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing vehicle mechanics.","zh":"描述車輛機械結構時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fit into","meaning":"嵌入……","examples":[{"en":"The axle fitted into a carved groove.","zh":"車軸嵌入刻出的凹槽。"},{"en":"To fit into something means to match its shape or size and go inside it properly.","zh":"fit into something 指形狀或大小合適，能正確進入某物之中。"},{"en":"A key must fit into a lock before it can turn.","zh":"鎖匙必須能插入鎖孔，才能轉動。"},{"en":"If the axle fits into the groove, the train is guided along the track.","zh":"如果車軸嵌入凹槽，列車就會被引導沿軌道前進。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing how parts match physically.","zh":"描述零件如何實體配合時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"carved groove","meaning":"刻出的槽","examples":[{"en":"A carved groove helped keep the train on course.","zh":"刻出的槽幫助列車保持在路線上。"},{"en":"A carved groove is a narrow channel cut into a surface.","zh":"carved groove 指在表面刻出的狹窄溝槽。"},{"en":"A wooden cutting board may have a carved groove to collect liquid.","zh":"木砧板可能有刻出的槽，用來收集液體。"},{"en":"In early coasters, grooves helped guide wheels or axles along the correct path.","zh":"在早期過山車中，槽幫助引導車輪或車軸沿正確路徑行駛。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a shaped guiding channel.","zh":"描述成形的導向溝槽時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"expand on an idea","meaning":"進一步發展某個構思","examples":[{"en":"French designers continued to expand on the original idea.","zh":"法國設計師繼續進一步發展原來的構思。"},{"en":"To expand on an idea means to develop it further by adding details, improvements, or new features.","zh":"expand on an idea 指透過加入細節、改良或新特徵進一步發展想法。"},{"en":"A student can expand on an essay idea by adding examples and explanation.","zh":"學生可以透過加入例子和解釋來進一步發展文章想法。"},{"en":"Designers expanded the basic ice-slide concept by adding wheels, tracks, and turns.","zh":"設計師透過加入輪子、軌道和彎道，進一步發展冰滑梯的基本概念。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a simple idea becomes more developed.","zh":"當簡單想法變得更成熟時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"complex track layouts","meaning":"複雜的軌道佈局","examples":[{"en":"Later rides featured more complex track layouts.","zh":"後來的機動遊戲有更複雜的軌道佈局。"},{"en":"Complex track layouts are track designs with more parts, directions, turns, and changes in height.","zh":"complex track layouts 指包含更多部分、方向、彎道和高度變化的軌道設計。"},{"en":"A model train set can have a complex layout with bridges, tunnels, and crossings.","zh":"模型火車組可以有包含橋、隧道和交叉位的複雜佈局。"},{"en":"More complex layouts make rides feel less predictable and more exciting.","zh":"更複雜的佈局令機動遊戲較難預測，也更刺激。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing design complexity.","zh":"描述設計複雜性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"multiple cars","meaning":"多節車卡","examples":[{"en":"Some early roller coasters used multiple cars.","zh":"有些早期過山車使用多節車卡。"},{"en":"Multiple cars means more than one connected carriage or vehicle section.","zh":"multiple cars 指多於一節相連車廂或車輛部分。"},{"en":"A train uses multiple cars so many passengers can ride together.","zh":"火車使用多節車卡，讓許多乘客一起乘搭。"},{"en":"Using multiple cars allows more riders to experience the coaster at the same time.","zh":"使用多節車卡讓更多乘客可以同時體驗過山車。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a vehicle made of several sections.","zh":"描述由幾個部分組成的車輛時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"twists and turns","meaning":"迂迴曲折；急彎","examples":[{"en":"The tracks included all sorts of twists and turns.","zh":"軌道包括各種迂迴曲折和急彎。"},{"en":"Twists and turns are curved, changing, or unexpected movements in a route or story.","zh":"twists and turns 指路線或故事中彎曲、變化或意想不到的發展。"},{"en":"A mountain road with many twists and turns can make drivers slow down.","zh":"有很多急彎的山路會令司機減速。"},{"en":"In roller coasters, twists and turns create surprise and make the ride more exciting.","zh":"在過山車中，迂迴曲折和急彎製造驚喜，使旅程更刺激。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for both physical routes and complicated stories.","zh":"這個短語可用於實體路線，也可用於複雜故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in comparison to","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"In comparison to the first European coaster, America’s first coaster is disputed.","zh":"與第一座歐洲過山車相比，美國第一座過山車有爭議。"},{"en":"In comparison to means when compared with another thing.","zh":"in comparison to 指與另一事物相比。"},{"en":"In comparison to city schools, village schools may have smaller classes.","zh":"與城市學校相比，鄉村學校班級可能較小。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers understand one thing by placing it beside another.","zh":"這個短語透過把一件事放在另一件事旁邊，幫助讀者理解它。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing similarities or differences.","zh":"顯示相似或差異時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"even greater debate over","meaning":"對……有更大爭議","examples":[{"en":"There is an even greater debate over America’s first true roller coaster.","zh":"對美國第一座真正的過山車有更大爭議。"},{"en":"An even greater debate over something means stronger disagreement about it than about another issue.","zh":"even greater debate over something 指對某事的分歧比另一議題更強。"},{"en":"There may be debate over school uniforms, but an even greater debate over phone bans.","zh":"人們可能對校服有爭議，但對手機禁令有更大爭議。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that historians disagree especially strongly about this point.","zh":"這個短語暗示歷史學家對這一點尤其意見不一。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing levels of controversy.","zh":"比較爭議程度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"first true coaster","meaning":"第一座真正的過山車","examples":[{"en":"Historians disagree about which ride was America’s first true coaster.","zh":"歷史學家對哪項機動遊戲是美國第一座真正的過山車意見不一。"},{"en":"The first true coaster means the earliest ride that can properly be called a roller coaster.","zh":"first true coaster 指最早可以被恰當稱為過山車的機動遊戲。"},{"en":"Experts may debate the first true example of a technology when earlier versions were incomplete.","zh":"當早期版本尚不完整，專家可能爭論某科技的第一個真正例子。"},{"en":"A ride may be early, but historians may ask whether it had enough features to count as a true coaster.","zh":"一項機動遊戲可能很早出現，但歷史學家會問它是否具備足夠特徵，可算真正過山車。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when defining the real beginning of something.","zh":"定義某事真正開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be considered by many to be","meaning":"被許多人視為","examples":[{"en":"The railway was considered by many to be a remarkable early coaster.","zh":"這條鐵路被許多人視為一座非凡的早期過山車。"},{"en":"Be considered by many to be means many people regard something in a particular way.","zh":"be considered by many to be 指許多人以某種方式看待某事。"},{"en":"The school library is considered by many to be the heart of the campus.","zh":"學校圖書館被許多人視為校園的核心。"},{"en":"When many historians accept a view, it becomes influential even if not everyone agrees.","zh":"當許多歷史學家接受某觀點，即使不是人人同意，它也變得有影響力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting a common opinion.","zh":"報告普遍看法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be located in","meaning":"位於……","examples":[{"en":"The railway was located in Pennsylvania’s Lehigh Valley.","zh":"這條鐵路位於賓夕凡尼亞州的 Lehigh Valley。"},{"en":"Be located in means be found or situated in a particular place.","zh":"be located in 指位於或坐落於某一地方。"},{"en":"The school is located in a quiet area near the park.","zh":"學校位於公園附近一個安靜區域。"},{"en":"Giving the location helps readers connect the historical event to a real place.","zh":"提供位置有助讀者把歷史事件連接到真實地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stating where something is.","zh":"說明某物在哪裏時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be originally used to","meaning":"最初用來……","examples":[{"en":"The railway was originally used to transport coal.","zh":"這條鐵路最初用來運送煤炭。"},{"en":"Be originally used to do something means its first purpose was to do that action.","zh":"be originally used to do something 指最初用途是做某事。"},{"en":"An old factory may have been originally used to make textiles.","zh":"舊工廠最初可能用來製造紡織品。"},{"en":"A railway built for coal later became an attraction when people found it exciting.","zh":"為煤炭而建的鐵路後來因人們覺得刺激而變成景點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing how an object’s purpose changed.","zh":"顯示物件用途如何改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"transport coal","meaning":"運送煤炭","examples":[{"en":"The railway transported coal between two mountains.","zh":"這條鐵路在兩座山之間運送煤炭。"},{"en":"To transport coal means to carry coal from one place to another.","zh":"transport coal 指把煤炭從一個地方運到另一個地方。"},{"en":"Trucks may transport coal from a mine to a power station.","zh":"貨車可能把煤炭從礦場運送到發電站。"},{"en":"A railway was useful for coal because heavy loads are easier to move on tracks.","zh":"鐵路對煤炭運輸有用，因為重物在軌道上較容易移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing mining and transport.","zh":"討論採礦和運輸時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"mining entrepreneur","meaning":"採礦企業家","examples":[{"en":"Josiah White was a mining entrepreneur.","zh":"Josiah White 是一名採礦企業家。"},{"en":"A mining entrepreneur is a businessperson who starts or runs businesses connected with mining.","zh":"mining entrepreneur 指創辦或經營採礦相關業務的商人。"},{"en":"A mining entrepreneur may invest in equipment, workers, railways, and land.","zh":"採礦企業家可能投資設備、工人、鐵路和土地。"},{"en":"Because mining required transport, such entrepreneurs often developed rail systems too.","zh":"因為採礦需要運輸，這類企業家也常發展鐵路系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing businesspeople in the mining industry.","zh":"描述採礦業商人時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have the idea of","meaning":"想到……的構思","examples":[{"en":"He had the idea of turning the railway into a thrill ride.","zh":"他想到把鐵路改造成刺激機動遊戲的構思。"},{"en":"To have the idea of doing something means to think of a possible plan or new use.","zh":"have the idea of doing something 指想到一個可能計劃或新用途。"},{"en":"A teacher may have the idea of turning vocabulary revision into a game.","zh":"老師可能想到把詞彙溫習變成遊戲的構思。"},{"en":"A new idea can change an ordinary tool into something more valuable.","zh":"新想法可以把普通工具變成更有價值的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing someone’s creative plan.","zh":"引入某人的創意計劃時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"turn something into","meaning":"把某物改造成……","examples":[{"en":"The railway was turned into a part-time attraction.","zh":"這條鐵路被改造成非全日運作的景點。"},{"en":"To turn something into something else means to change its purpose, form, or use.","zh":"turn something into something else 指改變某物的用途、形式或功能。"},{"en":"A family can turn an empty room into a study area.","zh":"家庭可以把空房改造成書房。"},{"en":"The coal railway became an attraction because people used it for excitement instead of transport.","zh":"這條煤炭鐵路成為景點，因為人們用它尋求刺激而不是運輸。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing transformation.","zh":"描述轉變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"part-time thrill ride","meaning":"非全日運作的刺激機動遊戲","examples":[{"en":"The coal railway became a part-time thrill ride.","zh":"這條煤炭鐵路變成非全日運作的刺激機動遊戲。"},{"en":"A part-time thrill ride is an attraction used for excitement only at certain times, not as its main full-time purpose.","zh":"part-time thrill ride 指只在某些時候用作刺激娛樂、而非全職主要用途的景點。"},{"en":"A school hall may become a part-time cinema on Friday evenings.","zh":"學校禮堂可能在星期五晚上變成非全日運作的電影院。"},{"en":"The railway still had practical origins, but it was sometimes used to entertain passengers.","zh":"這條鐵路仍有實用起源，但有時被用來娛樂乘客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something has a secondary entertainment role.","zh":"當某物有次要娛樂角色時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"immediate popularity","meaning":"迅即大受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The attraction gained immediate popularity.","zh":"這個景點迅即大受歡迎。"},{"en":"Immediate popularity means becoming popular very quickly after appearing.","zh":"immediate popularity 指出現後很快變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"A new snack may gain immediate popularity if students love its taste and price.","zh":"如果學生喜歡新零食的味道和價錢，它可能迅即大受歡迎。"},{"en":"The thrill ride became popular quickly because it offered an unusual experience.","zh":"這項刺激機動遊戲很快受歡迎，因為它提供不尋常體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when success happens soon after launch.","zh":"當成功在推出後很快發生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"strictly a passenger train","meaning":"完全改作客運列車","examples":[{"en":"It soon became strictly a passenger train.","zh":"它很快完全改作客運列車。"},{"en":"Strictly a passenger train means used only for carrying passengers, not for goods or another purpose.","zh":"strictly a passenger train 指只用來載客，而不是運貨或作其他用途。"},{"en":"A vehicle that once carried both cargo and people may later become strictly a passenger service.","zh":"一輛曾同時載貨和載人的車輛，後來可能完全改作客運服務。"},{"en":"Once the ride became popular, its entertainment use replaced its coal-transport role.","zh":"一旦這項機動遊戲受歡迎，其娛樂用途就取代了運煤角色。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a purpose becomes exclusive.","zh":"當用途變得單一時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"steam engine","meaning":"蒸汽機車","examples":[{"en":"A steam engine hauled passengers up the mountain.","zh":"蒸汽機車把乘客拖運上山。"},{"en":"A steam engine is an engine powered by steam, often used in older trains.","zh":"steam engine 指由蒸汽驅動的引擎，常用於舊式火車。"},{"en":"Museums sometimes display steam engines to show early transport technology.","zh":"博物館有時展示蒸汽機車，以呈現早期交通科技。"},{"en":"The steam engine supplied the power needed to pull passengers uphill.","zh":"蒸汽機車提供把乘客拉上山所需的力量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing older railway systems.","zh":"討論舊式鐵路系統時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"haul passengers to","meaning":"把乘客拖運到……","examples":[{"en":"The engine hauled passengers to the top of the mountain.","zh":"引擎把乘客拖運到山頂。"},{"en":"To haul passengers to a place means to pull or carry them there with force.","zh":"haul passengers to a place 指用力量把乘客拉或運送到某處。"},{"en":"A cable car hauls passengers to a hilltop station.","zh":"纜車把乘客拖運到山頂站。"},{"en":"Hauling passengers upward required power before gravity could bring them down.","zh":"在重力把乘客帶下來之前，把乘客向上拖運需要動力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing heavy or uphill transport.","zh":"描述重型或上坡運輸時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"coast back down","meaning":"靠慣性滑行下山","examples":[{"en":"Passengers coasted back down the mountain.","zh":"乘客靠慣性滑行下山。"},{"en":"To coast back down means to move downward smoothly using gravity rather than engine power.","zh":"coast back down 指不用引擎動力，而靠重力順暢向下移動。"},{"en":"A cyclist may coast back down a hill without pedalling.","zh":"單車手可能不用踩踏，靠慣性滑行下山。"},{"en":"Coasting down created the thrilling part of the early railway ride.","zh":"滑行下山創造了早期鐵路遊樂設施的刺激部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing movement powered by slope and momentum.","zh":"描述由斜坡和動量推動的運動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be rumoured to reach","meaning":"據傳達到……","examples":[{"en":"The train was rumoured to reach 100 miles per hour.","zh":"據傳這列車達到每小時100英里。"},{"en":"Be rumoured to reach means people said it reached that level, but the claim may not be proven.","zh":"be rumoured to reach 指有人說它達到某水平，但該說法未必已被證實。"},{"en":"A new phone may be rumoured to reach record battery life before official tests are released.","zh":"新手機在官方測試發布前，可能據傳達到破紀錄電池續航。"},{"en":"Rumours can make an attraction sound more exciting even when evidence is uncertain.","zh":"傳聞可以令景點聽起來更刺激，即使證據不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting an unconfirmed claim.","zh":"報告未經證實的說法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"switchback railroad","meaning":"折返式鐵路","examples":[{"en":"The attraction became known as a switchback railroad.","zh":"這個景點被稱為折返式鐵路。"},{"en":"A switchback railroad is a railway with a track design that changes direction, often on a slope.","zh":"switchback railroad 指使用會改變方向的軌道設計，通常位於斜坡上的鐵路。"},{"en":"Mountain railways may use switchbacks to climb steep land more safely.","zh":"山區鐵路可能使用折返路線，以更安全地爬升陡峭地形。"},{"en":"In early coasters, switchback designs allowed cars to move downhill in a controlled route.","zh":"在早期過山車中，折返式設計讓車卡沿受控路線下坡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing early roller-coaster track design.","zh":"討論早期過山車軌道設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"switchback track","meaning":"折返軌道","examples":[{"en":"A switchback track allowed the cars to reverse direction.","zh":"折返軌道讓車卡能改變方向。"},{"en":"A switchback track is a track layout that makes vehicles change direction, often back and forth.","zh":"switchback track 指令車輛改變方向、常來回折返的軌道佈局。"},{"en":"A hiking path may use switchbacks so walkers can climb a steep hill gradually.","zh":"行山路徑可能使用折返路線，讓行山者逐步爬上陡坡。"},{"en":"Switchback tracks helped early coaster cars travel safely on limited space.","zh":"折返軌道幫助早期過山車車卡在有限空間中安全行駛。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a zigzag or reversing route.","zh":"描述之字形或折返路線時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"allow riders to","meaning":"讓乘客能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The track allowed riders to coast downhill backwards.","zh":"軌道讓乘客能夠向後滑行下山。"},{"en":"Allow riders to means make it possible for passengers to do something.","zh":"allow riders to 指使乘客能夠做某事。"},{"en":"A safety bar allows riders to enjoy the ride without standing up accidentally.","zh":"安全桿讓乘客能享受機動遊戲，而不會意外站起來。"},{"en":"The track design allowed passengers to experience a new kind of movement.","zh":"軌道設計讓乘客體驗一種新的移動方式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing what a design enables.","zh":"描述設計使甚麼成為可能時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"feature a dead end","meaning":"設有盡頭路段","examples":[{"en":"The track featured a dead end at the summit.","zh":"軌道在最高點設有盡頭路段。"},{"en":"To feature a dead end means to include a track or road that stops and does not continue forward.","zh":"feature a dead end 指包含一段停止並不能繼續向前的軌道或道路。"},{"en":"A playground maze may feature a dead end to make the game harder.","zh":"遊樂場迷宮可能設有盡頭，以增加遊戲難度。"},{"en":"A dead end forced the train to stop and then move back in the opposite direction.","zh":"盡頭路段迫使列車停下，然後向相反方向移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a route design.","zh":"描述路線設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"dead end","meaning":"盡頭；死路","examples":[{"en":"The engine stopped at a dead end near the top.","zh":"引擎在接近頂部的一處盡頭停下。"},{"en":"A dead end is a road, path, or track that stops and does not lead onward.","zh":"dead end 指停止並不能繼續通往前方的道路、路徑或軌道。"},{"en":"A driver may need to turn around after entering a dead end street.","zh":"司機進入死路後可能需要掉頭。"},{"en":"In a switchback railway, a dead end helps create the change of direction.","zh":"在折返式鐵路中，盡頭有助創造方向改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing blocked or ending routes.","zh":"描述被阻斷或終止的路線時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"detach its cars","meaning":"解開所拖行的車卡","examples":[{"en":"The steam engine would detach its cars at the top.","zh":"蒸汽機車會在頂部解開所拖行的車卡。"},{"en":"To detach its cars means to disconnect the carriages from the engine or main vehicle.","zh":"detach its cars 指把車卡從引擎或主車輛分離。"},{"en":"A train crew may detach damaged cars before continuing a journey.","zh":"火車人員可能在繼續旅程前解開受損車卡。"},{"en":"Once the cars were detached, they could coast down by themselves.","zh":"一旦車卡被解開，它們就能自行滑行下山。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing separation of connected vehicle parts.","zh":"描述相連車輛部分分離時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"coast down backwards","meaning":"向後滑行下山","examples":[{"en":"The passenger cars then coasted down backwards.","zh":"乘客車卡隨後向後滑行下山。"},{"en":"To coast down backwards means to move downhill in reverse direction using gravity.","zh":"coast down backwards 指靠重力以向後方向下坡移動。"},{"en":"A toy car on a slope may coast down backwards if it is facing the wrong way.","zh":"如果玩具車方向相反，它可能在斜坡上向後滑下。"},{"en":"Moving backward downhill made the early ride feel unusual and exciting.","zh":"向後下坡移動令早期機動遊戲感覺不尋常又刺激。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing backward movement without engine power.","zh":"描述沒有引擎動力的向後移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"go through changes","meaning":"經歷變化","examples":[{"en":"The railway went through several track and name changes.","zh":"這條鐵路經歷了幾次軌道和名稱變化。"},{"en":"To go through changes means to experience changes over time.","zh":"go through changes 指隨時間經歷改變。"},{"en":"A school may go through changes when it gets a new principal and timetable.","zh":"學校在有新校長和新時間表時，可能經歷變化。"},{"en":"Attractions change names or designs when owners improve them or respond to visitors.","zh":"當擁有人改善景點或回應遊客時，景點會改名或改設計。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something develops through several stages.","zh":"當某物經歷幾個階段發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"minor track changes","meaning":"輕微軌道改動","examples":[{"en":"The railway underwent a few minor track changes.","zh":"這條鐵路經歷了幾次輕微軌道改動。"},{"en":"Minor track changes are small adjustments to the path, shape, or arrangement of rails.","zh":"minor track changes 指對路軌路線、形狀或安排作出小調整。"},{"en":"A train station may make minor track changes to improve safety.","zh":"火車站可能作出輕微軌道改動以改善安全。"},{"en":"Small changes can improve the ride without replacing the whole system.","zh":"小改動可以改善機動遊戲，而不必替換整個系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when changes are limited rather than major.","zh":"當變化有限而非重大時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"manage to last","meaning":"成功維持","examples":[{"en":"The attraction managed to last for more than a century.","zh":"這個景點成功維持超過一個世紀。"},{"en":"Manage to last means succeed in continuing for a long time despite difficulty.","zh":"manage to last 指即使有困難，仍成功持續很長時間。"},{"en":"A small family shop may manage to last for decades by serving loyal customers well.","zh":"小型家庭店可能透過好好服務忠實顧客，成功維持數十年。"},{"en":"If an attraction lasts a century, it has survived changing tastes and technology.","zh":"如果景點能維持一個世紀，它就經歷了品味和科技變化仍然存活。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when survival over time is impressive.","zh":"當長期存續令人印象深刻時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"over 100 years","meaning":"超過一百年","examples":[{"en":"The railway remained in operation for over 100 years.","zh":"這條鐵路運作超過一百年。"},{"en":"Over 100 years means more than one century.","zh":"over 100 years 指多於一個世紀。"},{"en":"Some schools have served their communities for over 100 years.","zh":"有些學校服務社區超過一百年。"},{"en":"A ride operating for over 100 years has historical and cultural importance.","zh":"運作超過一百年的機動遊戲具有歷史和文化重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing a very long duration.","zh":"強調非常長時間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"coaster craze","meaning":"過山車熱潮","examples":[{"en":"The roller-coaster craze was beginning to spread across America.","zh":"過山車熱潮開始在美國各地蔓延。"},{"en":"A coaster craze is a period when many people become very excited about roller coasters.","zh":"coaster craze 指很多人突然對過山車非常興奮的一段時期。"},{"en":"A city may experience a food-truck craze when many people start visiting them every weekend.","zh":"當很多人每週末開始光顧美食車，城市可能出現美食車熱潮。"},{"en":"A craze spreads when popularity grows quickly and more businesses copy the idea.","zh":"當受歡迎程度快速上升，更多商家模仿這個構思，熱潮就會蔓延。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a sudden fashion or enthusiasm.","zh":"描述突然流行或熱情時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"start to build","meaning":"開始增加；逐漸形成","examples":[{"en":"Public enthusiasm for roller coasters started to build.","zh":"公眾對過山車的熱情開始增加。"},{"en":"Start to build means begin to increase gradually.","zh":"start to build 指開始逐漸增加。"},{"en":"Excitement may start to build before a school concert begins.","zh":"學校音樂會開始前，興奮感可能逐漸形成。"},{"en":"As more people heard about the ride, interest slowly became stronger.","zh":"隨着更多人聽說這項機動遊戲，興趣慢慢變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when emotions, support, or pressure grow over time.","zh":"當情緒、支持或壓力隨時間增長時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"creation of","meaning":"……的創建","examples":[{"en":"The creation of the Switch Back Railway attracted national attention.","zh":"Switch Back Railway 的創建吸引了全國關注。"},{"en":"Creation of something means the making or invention of it.","zh":"creation of something 指製造或發明某物。"},{"en":"The creation of a new library can change how a community studies and meets.","zh":"新圖書館的創建可以改變社區學習和聚會的方式。"},{"en":"When a new attraction is created, it can influence later designs.","zh":"當一個新景點被創建，它可以影響後來設計。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the beginning of a new thing.","zh":"討論新事物的開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"give something national attention","meaning":"令……受到全國關注","examples":[{"en":"The new railway gave roller coasters national attention.","zh":"這條新鐵路令過山車受到全國關注。"},{"en":"To give something national attention means to make people across the country notice it.","zh":"give something national attention 指令全國各地的人注意到某事。"},{"en":"A student invention may give a school national attention if it wins a major prize.","zh":"如果學生發明贏得重要獎項，可能令學校受到全國關注。"},{"en":"National attention can make an idea spread quickly to other regions.","zh":"全國關注可以令一個構思迅速傳播到其他地區。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something becomes known beyond a local area.","zh":"當某事變得不只在本地知名時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"pop up all over","meaning":"在各地湧現","examples":[{"en":"Switchback railways began popping up all over the country.","zh":"折返式鐵路開始在全國各地湧現。"},{"en":"To pop up all over means to appear suddenly in many places.","zh":"pop up all over 指突然在很多地方出現。"},{"en":"Bubble-tea shops may pop up all over a city when they become fashionable.","zh":"當珍珠奶茶變得流行，珍珠奶茶店可能在城市各地湧現。"},{"en":"When a ride becomes popular, similar attractions may appear quickly everywhere.","zh":"當一項機動遊戲受歡迎，類似景點可能迅速到處出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and useful for describing rapid spread.","zh":"這個短語較口語，適合描述快速擴散。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"all over the country","meaning":"全國各地","examples":[{"en":"Similar attractions were built all over the country.","zh":"類似景點在全國各地建造起來。"},{"en":"All over the country means in many places across the whole nation.","zh":"all over the country 指遍及整個國家的許多地方。"},{"en":"Students all over the country may take the same public exam.","zh":"全國各地的學生可能參加同一個公開考試。"},{"en":"If an idea spreads all over the country, it is no longer just local.","zh":"如果一個構思傳遍全國各地，它就不再只是本地現象。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing wide national spread.","zh":"描述全國範圍的廣泛傳播時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"puzzle the modern-day thrill seeker","meaning":"令現代追求刺激的人感到不解","examples":[{"en":"The popularity of these gentle rides may puzzle modern-day thrill seekers.","zh":"這些溫和機動遊戲的受歡迎程度可能令現代追求刺激的人感到不解。"},{"en":"To puzzle the modern-day thrill seeker means to confuse people today who enjoy extreme excitement.","zh":"puzzle the modern-day thrill seeker 指令今天喜歡極端刺激的人感到困惑。"},{"en":"A slow old film may puzzle modern viewers who are used to fast editing.","zh":"慢節奏舊電影可能令習慣快剪接的現代觀眾感到不解。"},{"en":"Early coasters seem mild today, so modern thrill seekers may wonder why people waited so long for them.","zh":"早期過山車今天看來很溫和，所以現代追求刺激的人可能想不通為何人們等這麼久。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when old tastes seem strange to modern people.","zh":"當舊時品味對現代人來說顯得奇怪時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"modern-day thrill seeker","meaning":"現代追求刺激的人","examples":[{"en":"A modern-day thrill seeker may find early rides rather mild.","zh":"現代追求刺激的人可能覺得早期機動遊戲相當溫和。"},{"en":"A modern-day thrill seeker is a person today who enjoys exciting, frightening, or extreme experiences.","zh":"modern-day thrill seeker 指今天喜歡刺激、驚險或極端經驗的人。"},{"en":"A modern-day thrill seeker may enjoy skydiving, bungee jumping, or very fast rides.","zh":"現代追求刺激的人可能喜歡跳傘、笨豬跳或非常快的機動遊戲。"},{"en":"Such people may expect stronger excitement than old amusement rides could provide.","zh":"這類人可能期待比舊式遊樂設施更強烈的刺激。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing people who actively look for excitement.","zh":"描述主動尋求刺激的人時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"mild ride","meaning":"刺激程度較低的機動遊戲","examples":[{"en":"The first switchback railways offered a relatively mild ride.","zh":"最早期的折返式鐵路提供相對溫和的機動遊戲體驗。"},{"en":"A mild ride is an amusement ride that is not very fast, frightening, or intense.","zh":"mild ride 指速度不太快、不太可怕或不太強烈的機動遊戲。"},{"en":"A slow Ferris wheel may be a mild ride suitable for young children.","zh":"慢速摩天輪可能是適合幼童的溫和機動遊戲。"},{"en":"Mild rides can still be popular if they feel new, safe, or fun.","zh":"如果溫和機動遊戲感覺新鮮、安全或有趣，仍可以受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing gentle attractions with extreme ones.","zh":"比較溫和景點與極端景點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in comparison to","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"The early ride was mild in comparison to modern roller coasters.","zh":"與現代過山車相比，早期機動遊戲較溫和。"},{"en":"In comparison to means when compared with another thing.","zh":"in comparison to 指與另一事物相比。"},{"en":"In comparison to a smartphone, an old mobile phone had very few functions.","zh":"與智能手機相比，舊式手提電話功能很少。"},{"en":"Early rides seem gentle because modern coasters are much faster and taller.","zh":"早期機動遊戲看似溫和，因為現代過山車快得多也高得多。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when judging one thing beside another.","zh":"把一事物放在另一事物旁邊判斷時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"pay a nickel","meaning":"支付五美仙","examples":[{"en":"Guests paid a nickel to experience the ride.","zh":"遊客支付五美仙來體驗這項機動遊戲。"},{"en":"To pay a nickel means to pay five cents in old American currency.","zh":"pay a nickel 指支付美國舊幣制中的五美仙。"},{"en":"A child in the past might pay a nickel for a small sweet or newspaper.","zh":"過去孩子可能支付五美仙買一粒糖或一份報紙。"},{"en":"The low price made early rides accessible to many visitors.","zh":"低票價令早期機動遊戲較容易讓許多遊客參與。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing historical prices in America.","zh":"討論美國歷史價格時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"wait in line","meaning":"排隊等候","examples":[{"en":"Visitors sometimes waited in line for several hours.","zh":"遊客有時排隊等候數小時。"},{"en":"To wait in line means to stand or sit in a queue until it is your turn.","zh":"wait in line 指排隊站着或坐着等候輪到自己。"},{"en":"Students wait in line outside the classroom before an exam.","zh":"學生考試前在課室外排隊等候。"},{"en":"Long lines show that a ride or service is very popular.","zh":"長隊顯示機動遊戲或服務非常受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in American English; British English often says queue.","zh":"這個短語常見於美式英語；英式英語常說 queue。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"up to five hours","meaning":"長達五小時","examples":[{"en":"Some guests waited for up to five hours.","zh":"有些遊客等候長達五小時。"},{"en":"Up to five hours means as long as five hours, but not more than that.","zh":"up to five hours 指最長五小時，但不超過這個時間。"},{"en":"Patients may wait up to five hours in a busy emergency room.","zh":"在繁忙急症室，病人可能等候長達五小時。"},{"en":"Waiting this long shows how strongly people wanted to try the ride.","zh":"等這麼久顯示人們非常想嘗試這項機動遊戲。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving a maximum time.","zh":"提供最長時間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"side-by-side tracks","meaning":"並排軌道","examples":[{"en":"The attraction consisted of a pair of side-by-side tracks.","zh":"這個景點由一對並排軌道組成。"},{"en":"Side-by-side tracks are two tracks placed next to each other.","zh":"side-by-side tracks 指兩條放在彼此旁邊的軌道。"},{"en":"Two railway platforms may have side-by-side tracks for trains going in opposite directions.","zh":"兩個火車月台可能有並排軌道，供相反方向列車行駛。"},{"en":"Side-by-side tracks allowed early coaster cars to move in a simple organised layout.","zh":"並排軌道讓早期過山車車卡以簡單而有秩序的佈局移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing parallel structures.","zh":"描述平行結構時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"gradual hills","meaning":"平緩斜坡","examples":[{"en":"The tracks contained gradual hills rather than steep drops.","zh":"軌道包含平緩斜坡，而不是陡峭急降。"},{"en":"Gradual hills are slopes that rise or fall gently, not suddenly.","zh":"gradual hills 指緩慢上升或下降的坡，而不是突然變陡。"},{"en":"A road with gradual hills is easier for cyclists than a very steep road.","zh":"有平緩斜坡的道路比非常陡的道路更適合單車手。"},{"en":"Gradual hills made early rides less intense than modern coasters with sharp drops.","zh":"平緩斜坡令早期機動遊戲比有急降的現代過山車刺激度低。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing gentle changes in height.","zh":"描述高度上的溫和變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"top speed","meaning":"最高速度","examples":[{"en":"The vehicles reached a top speed of six miles per hour.","zh":"車輛達到每小時六英里的最高速度。"},{"en":"Top speed means the highest speed a vehicle or machine can reach.","zh":"top speed 指車輛或機器能達到的最高速度。"},{"en":"A small electric scooter may have a top speed of 25 kilometres per hour.","zh":"小型電動滑板車的最高速度可能是每小時25公里。"},{"en":"A low top speed makes a ride feel gentler and safer.","zh":"低最高速度令機動遊戲感覺更溫和和安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing how fast machines can go.","zh":"比較機器能跑多快時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"regardless","meaning":"儘管如此","examples":[{"en":"Regardless, the rides became extremely popular.","zh":"儘管如此，這些機動遊戲變得極受歡迎。"},{"en":"Regardless means despite what was just mentioned.","zh":"regardless 指儘管剛才提到的情況如此。"},{"en":"The lesson was difficult; regardless, students stayed focused until the end.","zh":"課堂很困難；儘管如此，學生仍專注到最後。"},{"en":"Even though the early rides were slow, people still found them exciting.","zh":"即使早期機動遊戲速度很慢，人們仍覺得它們刺激。"},{"en":"This word is useful when the result happens despite a possible objection.","zh":"當結果在有可能阻礙的情況下仍然發生時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"spark someone to","meaning":"激發某人去……","examples":[{"en":"Their popularity sparked designers to create better rides.","zh":"它們的受歡迎程度激發設計師創造更好的機動遊戲。"},{"en":"To spark someone to do something means to inspire or trigger them to act.","zh":"spark someone to do something 指啟發或觸發某人採取行動。"},{"en":"A teacher’s praise can spark a student to write more confidently.","zh":"老師的稱讚可以激發學生更自信地寫作。"},{"en":"Public enthusiasm for early coasters encouraged designers to improve the technology.","zh":"公眾對早期過山車的熱情鼓勵設計師改善科技。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one event motivates action.","zh":"當一件事推動行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bigger and better","meaning":"更大而且更好","examples":[{"en":"Designers began developing coasters that were bigger and better.","zh":"設計師開始發展更大而且更好的過山車。"},{"en":"Bigger and better means larger, more impressive, or improved in quality.","zh":"bigger and better 指更大型、更令人印象深刻或質素更高。"},{"en":"A school fair may become bigger and better each year as more students join.","zh":"隨着更多學生參與，學校嘉年華可能一年比一年更大更好。"},{"en":"Competition can push companies to create products that are bigger and better.","zh":"競爭可以推動公司創造更大而且更好的產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing improvement and expansion together.","zh":"同時描述改善和擴展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"best decades in","meaning":"……最鼎盛的數十年","examples":[{"en":"The 1910s and 1920s were among the best decades in roller-coaster history.","zh":"1910年代和1920年代是過山車歷史中最鼎盛的數十年之一。"},{"en":"Best decades in something means one of the most successful or important ten-year periods in that area.","zh":"best decades in something 指某領域中最成功或最重要的十年時期之一。"},{"en":"The 1990s may be seen as one of the best decades in a singer’s career.","zh":"1990年代可能被視為某歌手事業中最鼎盛的十年之一。"},{"en":"A decade becomes important when many successful designs, ideas, or achievements appear.","zh":"當許多成功設計、想法或成就出現，一個十年就會變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a peak period in history.","zh":"描述歷史高峰期時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"new wave of technology","meaning":"新一輪科技發展","examples":[{"en":"A new wave of technology transformed coaster design.","zh":"新一輪科技發展改變了過山車設計。"},{"en":"A new wave of technology means a group of new technical developments arriving around the same time.","zh":"new wave of technology 指一批新技術發展在相近時期出現。"},{"en":"A new wave of technology in classrooms may include tablets, online platforms, and AI tools.","zh":"課室中新一輪科技發展可能包括平板、網上平台和人工智能工具。"},{"en":"When several innovations appear together, they can change an industry quickly.","zh":"當幾項創新同時出現，它們可以迅速改變一個行業。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when technological change comes in a powerful period.","zh":"當科技變化以強大時期出現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"up-stop wheels","meaning":"防脫軌輪","examples":[{"en":"Up-stop wheels helped keep the train attached to the track.","zh":"防脫軌輪幫助列車保持連接在軌道上。"},{"en":"Up-stop wheels are safety wheels that stop coaster cars from lifting off the rails.","zh":"up-stop wheels 指阻止過山車車卡離開路軌的安全車輪。"},{"en":"A safety clip on a climbing rope works in a similar way by preventing dangerous separation.","zh":"攀石繩上的安全扣以類似方式運作，防止危險分離。"},{"en":"Up-stop wheels allowed designers to create steeper drops and stronger forces safely.","zh":"防脫軌輪讓設計師能安全創造更陡下墜和更強力量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining a key roller-coaster safety invention.","zh":"解釋重要過山車安全發明時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"arrangement that","meaning":"……的裝置","examples":[{"en":"The wheels formed an arrangement that resisted powerful forces.","zh":"這些車輪形成一種能抵抗強大力量的裝置。"},{"en":"Arrangement that means a design or positioning of parts that does a particular job.","zh":"arrangement that 指能完成某特定功能的部件設計或位置安排。"},{"en":"A classroom may use an arrangement that lets students discuss in small groups.","zh":"課室可能使用一種讓學生小組討論的佈置。"},{"en":"The wheel arrangement kept the train secure when gravity tried to pull it away from the track.","zh":"這種車輪裝置在重力試圖把列車拉離軌道時，仍令列車保持穩固。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing how parts are organised for a purpose.","zh":"描述部件如何為某目的被組織時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"keep something attached to","meaning":"使某物保持連接在……","examples":[{"en":"The system kept the coaster’s wheels attached to its tracks.","zh":"這個系統使過山車車輪保持連接在軌道上。"},{"en":"To keep something attached to something else means to prevent it from separating.","zh":"keep something attached to something else 指防止某物與另一物分離。"},{"en":"A strong clip keeps a name badge attached to a shirt.","zh":"堅固夾子使名牌保持扣在襯衫上。"},{"en":"Keeping the wheels attached to the track made sharper turns and drops safer.","zh":"讓車輪保持連接在軌道上，使更急的轉彎和下墜更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing secure connection.","zh":"描述穩固連接時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"resist gravitational forces","meaning":"抵抗強大重力","examples":[{"en":"The wheels resisted high gravitational forces.","zh":"車輪抵抗強大重力。"},{"en":"To resist gravitational forces means to stay secure even when strong forces pull or push the train.","zh":"resist gravitational forces 指即使強大力量拉動或推動列車，仍保持穩固。"},{"en":"A safety harness must resist strong forces during a sudden stop.","zh":"安全帶必須在突然停下時抵抗強大力量。"},{"en":"Roller-coaster wheels must resist forces that could otherwise lift the train from the track.","zh":"過山車車輪必須抵抗可能把列車抬離軌道的力量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing safety under powerful motion.","zh":"討論高速運動中的安全時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"open up a realm of possibilities","meaning":"開拓廣闊的可能性","examples":[{"en":"The invention opened up a realm of new design possibilities.","zh":"這項發明開拓了廣闊的新設計可能性。"},{"en":"To open up a realm of possibilities means to make many new options or ideas possible.","zh":"open up a realm of possibilities 指令許多新選項或想法成為可能。"},{"en":"Online learning opened up a realm of possibilities for students who live far from schools.","zh":"網上學習為住得離學校很遠的學生開拓廣闊可能性。"},{"en":"Once trains could stay attached to the track, designers could safely try more daring layouts.","zh":"一旦列車能保持連接在軌道上，設計師就能安全嘗試更大膽的佈局。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one innovation creates many future options.","zh":"當一項創新創造許多未來選項時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a realm of possibilities","meaning":"廣闊的可能性","examples":[{"en":"New safety technology created a realm of possibilities.","zh":"新安全科技創造了廣闊的可能性。"},{"en":"A realm of possibilities means a wide range of new things that could happen or be created.","zh":"realm of possibilities 指許多可能發生或被創造的新事物。"},{"en":"Learning a new language opens a realm of possibilities for travel, work, and friendship.","zh":"學習新語言為旅行、工作和友誼打開廣闊可能性。"},{"en":"Better safety systems allowed coaster designers to imagine designs that were impossible before.","zh":"更好的安全系統讓過山車設計師想像以前不可能的設計。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a large set of opportunities.","zh":"描述大量機會時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"never been seen before","meaning":"前所未見","examples":[{"en":"Designers created track features that had never been seen before.","zh":"設計師創造了前所未見的軌道特徵。"},{"en":"Never been seen before means completely new or not previously known to people.","zh":"never been seen before 指完全新穎或以前不為人所知。"},{"en":"A school science fair may display an invention that has never been seen before in the community.","zh":"學校科學展可能展示社區前所未見的發明。"},{"en":"New safety technology allowed designers to create features earlier builders could not attempt.","zh":"新安全科技讓設計師創造早期建造者不能嘗試的特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing innovation or novelty.","zh":"描述創新或新奇事物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"North America alone","meaning":"單是北美洲","examples":[{"en":"North America alone had around 1,500 roller coasters.","zh":"單是北美洲就有約1,500座過山車。"},{"en":"North America alone means only North America, without counting other regions.","zh":"North America alone 指只計北美洲，不包括其他地區。"},{"en":"One city alone may have more restaurants than several nearby towns combined.","zh":"單是一個城市的餐廳數量，可能比附近幾個小鎮加起來還多。"},{"en":"Saying North America alone had 1,500 coasters shows how large the craze became.","zh":"說單是北美洲就有1,500座過山車，顯示熱潮變得多麼龐大。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when emphasising that a figure is already impressive before adding other places.","zh":"當一個數字在未加上其他地方前已很驚人時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rise rapidly","meaning":"迅速上升","examples":[{"en":"The number of amusement rides was rising rapidly.","zh":"遊樂設施數量正在迅速上升。"},{"en":"Rise rapidly means increase quickly in number, level, or amount.","zh":"rise rapidly 指數量、水平或程度快速增加。"},{"en":"Food prices may rise rapidly after a poor harvest.","zh":"收成差後，食物價格可能迅速上升。"},{"en":"Rapid growth in rides showed that amusement parks were expanding quickly.","zh":"遊樂設施快速增長顯示遊樂場正在迅速擴展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing fast increase.","zh":"描述快速增加時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the Great Depression","meaning":"經濟大蕭條","examples":[{"en":"The Great Depression severely damaged the amusement industry.","zh":"經濟大蕭條嚴重損害遊樂業。"},{"en":"The Great Depression was a major economic crisis in the 1930s that caused unemployment and business failure.","zh":"the Great Depression 指1930年代重大經濟危機，造成失業和企業倒閉。"},{"en":"During the Great Depression, many families had little money for entertainment.","zh":"在經濟大蕭條期間，許多家庭沒有太多錢用於娛樂。"},{"en":"Amusement parks suffered because people could not afford leisure activities.","zh":"遊樂場受到打擊，因為人們負擔不起休閒活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing economic history.","zh":"討論經濟歷史時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"deal a crushing blow to","meaning":"對……造成沉重打擊","examples":[{"en":"The Great Depression dealt a crushing blow to amusement parks.","zh":"經濟大蕭條對遊樂場造成沉重打擊。"},{"en":"To deal a crushing blow to something means to damage it very seriously.","zh":"deal a crushing blow to something 指嚴重損害某事。"},{"en":"Losing its main customer may deal a crushing blow to a small business.","zh":"失去主要客戶可能對小企業造成沉重打擊。"},{"en":"Economic crisis reduced visitors and money, so amusement parks struggled to survive.","zh":"經濟危機減少遊客和收入，因此遊樂場難以生存。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing severe damage.","zh":"描述嚴重損害時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"amusement parks","meaning":"遊樂場","examples":[{"en":"Amusement parks suffered badly during the economic crisis.","zh":"遊樂場在經濟危機期間受到嚴重影響。"},{"en":"Amusement parks are places with rides, games, shows, and attractions for entertainment.","zh":"amusement parks 指有機動遊戲、遊戲攤位、表演和景點的娛樂場所。"},{"en":"Families may visit amusement parks during holidays to ride coasters and play games.","zh":"家庭可能在假期到遊樂場乘搭過山車和玩遊戲。"},{"en":"Amusement parks depend on visitors having money and time for leisure.","zh":"遊樂場依賴遊客有金錢和時間進行休閒活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing leisure and entertainment businesses.","zh":"討論休閒和娛樂業務時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"as bad as it was","meaning":"儘管情況如此惡劣","examples":[{"en":"As bad as the Depression was, park owners remained hopeful.","zh":"儘管經濟大蕭條情況如此惡劣，遊樂場擁有人仍保持希望。"},{"en":"As bad as it was means although the situation was very bad.","zh":"as bad as it was 指雖然情況非常差。"},{"en":"As bad as the storm was, the school managed to reopen the next day.","zh":"儘管暴風雨情況如此惡劣，學校仍成功在第二天重開。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast between a serious problem and a hopeful response.","zh":"這個短語引出嚴重問題與有希望回應之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when something positive remains despite difficulty.","zh":"當困難中仍有正面情況時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"optimistic outlook for","meaning":"對……抱有樂觀展望","examples":[{"en":"Amusement parks had an optimistic outlook for the future.","zh":"遊樂場對未來抱有樂觀展望。"},{"en":"An optimistic outlook for something means a hopeful view about what will happen later.","zh":"optimistic outlook for something 指對日後會發生的事情有希望的看法。"},{"en":"A student may have an optimistic outlook for exams after weeks of steady revision.","zh":"學生經過數星期穩定溫習後，可能對考試抱有樂觀展望。"},{"en":"Hopeful owners may continue investing even after difficult years.","zh":"有希望的業主即使經歷困難年份，也可能繼續投資。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing positive expectations.","zh":"描述正面期望時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"feel the effects of","meaning":"感受到……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Roller coasters soon felt the effects of World War II.","zh":"過山車很快感受到第二次世界大戰的影響。"},{"en":"To feel the effects of something means to be affected by it.","zh":"feel the effects of something 指受到某事影響。"},{"en":"Families may feel the effects of rising food prices at the supermarket.","zh":"家庭可能在超級市場感受到食物價格上升的影響。"},{"en":"War affected amusement parks because materials, money, and public attention shifted elsewhere.","zh":"戰爭影響遊樂場，因為材料、金錢和公眾注意力轉移到其他地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a large event affects people or industries.","zh":"當大型事件影響人或行業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"World War II","meaning":"第二次世界大戰","examples":[{"en":"World War II led to the closure of many amusement rides.","zh":"第二次世界大戰導致許多遊樂設施關閉。"},{"en":"World War II was a major global war fought from 1939 to 1945.","zh":"World War II 指1939年至1945年間爆發的重大世界戰爭。"},{"en":"During World War II, many industries had to focus on military needs.","zh":"在第二次世界大戰期間，許多行業必須專注軍事需要。"},{"en":"Entertainment businesses suffered because resources and people were drawn into the war effort.","zh":"娛樂業受損，因為資源和人力被投入戰爭。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing twentieth-century history.","zh":"討論二十世紀歷史時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be forced into neglect","meaning":"被迫陷入乏人理會的狀態","examples":[{"en":"Roller coasters were forced into a period of neglect.","zh":"過山車被迫陷入一段乏人理會的時期。"},{"en":"Be forced into neglect means be pushed into a situation where something is ignored or not maintained.","zh":"be forced into neglect 指被迫進入被忽視或缺乏維護的狀態。"},{"en":"An old library may be forced into neglect if the town cuts its funding.","zh":"如果城鎮削減資金，舊圖書館可能被迫陷入乏人理會的狀態。"},{"en":"During wartime, amusement rides were not a priority, so many were left unused or poorly maintained.","zh":"戰時遊樂設施不是優先事項，因此許多被閒置或維護不足。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when outside events cause abandonment.","zh":"當外部事件造成棄置時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"shadow of neglect","meaning":"被忽視的陰影","examples":[{"en":"The industry entered a shadow of neglect during the war.","zh":"該行業在戰爭期間進入被忽視的陰影。"},{"en":"Shadow of neglect means a period or condition in which something is overlooked, forgotten, or poorly cared for.","zh":"shadow of neglect 指某事被忽略、遺忘或照顧不足的一段時期或狀態。"},{"en":"A historic building may fall under a shadow of neglect if no one repairs it for years.","zh":"如果多年沒有人維修，歷史建築可能落入被忽視的陰影。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that the industry did not disappear completely, but it lost attention and care.","zh":"這個短語暗示該行業沒有完全消失，但失去了關注和照顧。"},{"en":"This phrase is metaphorical and useful for describing decline.","zh":"這個短語是比喻性，適合描述衰落。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"nearly all","meaning":"幾乎全部","examples":[{"en":"Nearly all of America’s roller coasters were shut down.","zh":"美國幾乎全部過山車都被關閉。"},{"en":"Nearly all means almost every one, but not necessarily 100 percent.","zh":"nearly all 指幾乎每一個，但不一定百分之百。"},{"en":"Nearly all students submitted the assignment before the deadline.","zh":"幾乎全部學生都在截止日期前提交功課。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the shutdown was widespread and severe.","zh":"這個短語顯示關閉情況廣泛而嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a very large majority.","zh":"描述非常大多數時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be shut down","meaning":"被關閉","examples":[{"en":"Most roller coasters were shut down during the war.","zh":"大多數過山車在戰爭期間被關閉。"},{"en":"Be shut down means be closed or stopped from operating.","zh":"be shut down 指被關閉或停止運作。"},{"en":"A shop may be shut down if it cannot pay rent.","zh":"如果商店付不起租金，可能被關閉。"},{"en":"When rides are shut down, they stop earning money and may fall into disrepair.","zh":"當機動遊戲被關閉，它們停止賺錢，並可能逐漸失修。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when businesses, machines, or services stop operating.","zh":"當企業、機器或服務停止運作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"to this very day","meaning":"直到今天","examples":[{"en":"To this very day, coaster numbers remain below their earlier peak.","zh":"直到今天，過山車數量仍低於早期高峰。"},{"en":"To this very day means even now, after a long time has passed.","zh":"to this very day 指即使過了很久，直到現在仍然如此。"},{"en":"To this very day, some families still follow traditions started by their grandparents.","zh":"直到今天，有些家庭仍遵循祖父母開始的傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the effect of a past event continues into the present.","zh":"這個短語強調過去事件的影響延續到現在。"},{"en":"It is useful when a historical consequence has lasted a long time.","zh":"當歷史後果持續很久時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a tiny fraction of","meaning":"……的一小部分","examples":[{"en":"Today’s total is only a tiny fraction of the 1920s figure.","zh":"今天的總數只是1920年代數字的一小部分。"},{"en":"A tiny fraction of something means a very small part of it.","zh":"tiny fraction of something 指某物中非常小的一部分。"},{"en":"A small school library may own only a tiny fraction of the books in a city library.","zh":"小型學校圖書館可能只擁有城市圖書館藏書的一小部分。"},{"en":"Saying the number is a tiny fraction shows how sharply it has fallen.","zh":"說數字只是一小部分，顯示它大幅下降。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing a small amount with a much larger one.","zh":"把小數量與大得多的數量比較時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"traditional lifting mechanism","meaning":"傳統過山車提升機制","examples":[{"en":"The questions describe the traditional roller-coaster lifting mechanism.","zh":"題目描述傳統過山車提升機制。"},{"en":"A traditional lifting mechanism is the older chain-based system that pulls coaster trains uphill.","zh":"traditional lifting mechanism 指較舊的鏈條式系統，用來把過山車列車拉上坡。"},{"en":"Many classic roller coasters still use a traditional lifting mechanism before the first drop.","zh":"許多經典過山車在第一次下墜前仍使用傳統提升機制。"},{"en":"The mechanism is needed because the train must first gain height before gravity can move it.","zh":"這個機制是必要的，因為列車必須先取得高度，重力才能推動它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing how a coaster begins its ride.","zh":"描述過山車如何開始運行時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個詞","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案應包含不多於兩個詞。"},{"en":"No more than two words means the answer must use one or two words only.","zh":"no more than two words 指答案只能使用一個或兩個英文詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “chain loop,” it follows the rule because it has two words.","zh":"如果答案是 chain loop，它符合規則，因為有兩個詞。"},{"en":"Writing three words may lose marks even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫三個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"This instruction is common in reading completion tasks.","zh":"這項指示常見於閱讀填空題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"and/or a number","meaning":"及／或一個數字","examples":[{"en":"An answer may contain words, a number, or both.","zh":"答案可以包含文字、一個數字，或兩者兼有。"},{"en":"And/or a number means the answer may include words, a number, or a combination of the two.","zh":"and/or a number 指答案可以包含文字、數字，或文字和數字的組合。"},{"en":"“456 feet” follows an and/or a number rule because it includes a number and a word.","zh":"456 feet 符合 and/or a number 規則，因為它包含一個數字和一個詞。"},{"en":"Students must check the instruction before deciding how much to write.","zh":"學生在決定寫多少之前，必須查看指示。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in exam instructions about answer length.","zh":"這個短語適用於關於答案長度的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"long line for climbing uphill","meaning":"用於爬坡的長鏈","examples":[{"en":"A long chain pulls the roller-coaster train uphill.","zh":"一條長鏈把過山車列車拉上坡。"},{"en":"A long line for climbing uphill refers to a long chain or similar part used to move something up a slope.","zh":"long line for climbing uphill 指用來把某物沿斜坡向上移動的長鏈或類似部件。"},{"en":"A ski lift uses a long cable to help people travel uphill.","zh":"滑雪吊索使用長鋼索幫助人們上坡。"},{"en":"Without this long pulling part, the train could not reach the top of the first hill.","zh":"沒有這個長拉動部件，列車就不能到達第一個山坡頂部。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a lifting system in simple words.","zh":"用簡單語言描述提升系統時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"climb uphill","meaning":"向斜坡上行","examples":[{"en":"The lifting mechanism enables the train to climb uphill.","zh":"提升機制使列車能夠向斜坡上行。"},{"en":"To climb uphill means to move upward along a slope.","zh":"climb uphill 指沿斜坡向上移動。"},{"en":"A cyclist must work harder to climb uphill than to ride on flat ground.","zh":"單車手上坡比在平路騎行需要更努力。"},{"en":"The train climbs uphill so it can later descend using gravity.","zh":"列車向斜坡上行，之後就能靠重力下降。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing upward movement on a slope.","zh":"描述在斜坡上向上移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be firmly connected to","meaning":"牢固連接至……","examples":[{"en":"The chain is firmly connected to form a loop.","zh":"鏈條被牢固連接成一個環。"},{"en":"Be firmly connected to means be joined tightly and securely to something.","zh":"be firmly connected to 指緊密而安全地連接到某物。"},{"en":"A safety rope must be firmly connected to a climber’s harness.","zh":"安全繩必須牢固連接到攀登者的安全帶。"},{"en":"A firmly connected chain can move continuously without breaking apart.","zh":"牢固連接的鏈條可以持續移動而不會斷開。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing strong attachment.","zh":"描述強力連接時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"on top and underneath","meaning":"在頂部及下方","examples":[{"en":"Gears are positioned on top of and underneath the hill.","zh":"齒輪位於山坡頂部及下方。"},{"en":"On top and underneath means at the upper part and below something.","zh":"on top and underneath 指在某物上方和下方。"},{"en":"A bunk bed has one mattress on top and another underneath.","zh":"雙層床有一張床墊在上方，另一張在下方。"},{"en":"Gears placed at both positions help the chain move around the lift hill.","zh":"放在兩個位置的齒輪幫助鏈條繞着提升坡移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining two opposite locations.","zh":"解釋兩個相反位置時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"provide power","meaning":"提供動力","examples":[{"en":"A motor provides power for the lifting chain.","zh":"馬達為提升鏈條提供動力。"},{"en":"To provide power means to supply the energy needed to make something work.","zh":"provide power 指供應某物運作所需的能量。"},{"en":"A battery provides power for a remote control.","zh":"電池為遙控器提供動力。"},{"en":"The motor provides power so the chain can pull the heavy train uphill.","zh":"馬達提供動力，使鏈條可以把沉重列車拉上坡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how a machine operates.","zh":"解釋機器如何運作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的詞語完成摘要。"},{"en":"Complete the summary means fill in missing words in a short version of the text.","zh":"complete the summary 指填寫文本簡短版本中的缺漏詞語。"},{"en":"Students should complete the summary by finding the same idea in the reading passage.","zh":"學生應透過在閱讀篇章中找到相同意思來完成摘要。"},{"en":"Summary completion tests understanding, not just word matching.","zh":"摘要填空測試理解，而不只是字詞配對。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"earliest roller coasters","meaning":"最早期的過山車","examples":[{"en":"The earliest roller coasters may have originated in Russia.","zh":"最早期的過山車可能起源於俄羅斯。"},{"en":"Earliest roller coasters means the first or oldest forms of rides that later developed into roller coasters.","zh":"earliest roller coasters 指後來發展成過山車的最初或最古老機動遊戲形式。"},{"en":"The earliest computers were much larger and slower than modern laptops.","zh":"最早期的電腦比現代手提電腦大得多且慢得多。"},{"en":"Studying the earliest roller coasters helps explain how today’s rides evolved.","zh":"研究最早期的過山車有助解釋今天的機動遊戲如何演變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the beginning of a technology or attraction.","zh":"討論科技或景點的開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"originate in","meaning":"起源於……","examples":[{"en":"The first ice-slide rides may have originated in Russia.","zh":"最早的冰滑梯機動遊戲可能起源於俄羅斯。"},{"en":"To originate in a place means to begin or come from that place.","zh":"originate in a place 指開始於或來自某地方。"},{"en":"Many popular foods originated in one region before spreading worldwide.","zh":"許多受歡迎食物起源於某一地區，然後傳遍世界。"},{"en":"If roller coasters originated in ice slides, their history began with cold-weather entertainment.","zh":"如果過山車起源於冰滑梯，其歷史就始於寒冷天氣中的娛樂。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when tracing where something started.","zh":"追溯某物從哪裏開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"wooden slides","meaning":"木滑梯","examples":[{"en":"The original rides consisted of wooden slides.","zh":"原始機動遊戲由木滑梯組成。"},{"en":"Wooden slides are slides made mainly from wood.","zh":"wooden slides 指主要由木材製成的滑梯。"},{"en":"Older playgrounds often had wooden slides before metal and plastic became common.","zh":"在金屬和塑膠普及前，舊式遊樂場常有木滑梯。"},{"en":"Wood was used because early builders could shape it into long sloping structures.","zh":"木材被使用，是因為早期建造者可以把它塑造成長斜坡結構。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the material of early rides.","zh":"描述早期機動遊戲的材料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be modified into","meaning":"被改造成……","examples":[{"en":"The French slides were modified into waxed surfaces.","zh":"法國滑梯被改造成塗蠟表面。"},{"en":"Be modified into something means be changed into a new form or design.","zh":"be modified into something 指被改變成新的形式或設計。"},{"en":"A classroom can be modified into a small performance space by moving desks aside.","zh":"課室可以透過移開桌子被改造成小型表演空間。"},{"en":"The slides were modified because ice did not work well in warmer France.","zh":"滑梯被改造，是因為冰在較溫暖的法國不太適用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing practical adaptation.","zh":"描述實用改造時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"melt the ice","meaning":"令冰融化","examples":[{"en":"The warmer French climate would melt the ice.","zh":"較溫暖的法國氣候會令冰融化。"},{"en":"To melt the ice means to make frozen water turn into liquid water.","zh":"melt the ice 指令結冰的水變成液態水。"},{"en":"Warm sunlight can melt the ice on a car windscreen.","zh":"溫暖陽光可以令汽車擋風玻璃上的冰融化。"},{"en":"If the ice melted, the slide would no longer work properly.","zh":"如果冰融化，滑梯就不能正常運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when heat changes a frozen surface.","zh":"當熱力改變冰凍表面時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"add wheels to the sleds","meaning":"為雪橇加上輪子","examples":[{"en":"French designers later added wheels to the sleds.","zh":"法國設計師後來為雪橇加上輪子。"},{"en":"To add wheels to the sleds means to attach wheels so the sleds could roll on a track or surface.","zh":"add wheels to the sleds 指加裝輪子，使雪橇能在軌道或表面上滾動。"},{"en":"Adding wheels to a suitcase makes it easier to pull through an airport.","zh":"為行李箱加上輪子，令它更容易在機場拖行。"},{"en":"Wheels allowed the ride to work without depending on ice.","zh":"輪子令機動遊戲不再依賴冰也能運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining an important design change.","zh":"解釋重要設計改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"appear in Pennsylvania","meaning":"在賓夕凡尼亞州出現","examples":[{"en":"America’s first coaster was said to appear in Pennsylvania.","zh":"據說美國第一座過山車在賓夕凡尼亞州出現。"},{"en":"Appear in Pennsylvania means be found, built, or first seen in that American state.","zh":"appear in Pennsylvania 指在美國賓夕凡尼亞州被發現、建造或首次出現。"},{"en":"A new museum may appear in a city after years of planning.","zh":"新博物館可能在多年規劃後在城市中出現。"},{"en":"Locating the coaster in Pennsylvania connects the history to a specific mining region.","zh":"把過山車定位於賓夕凡尼亞州，將這段歷史連接到特定採礦地區。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when saying where something first emerged.","zh":"說明某物最初在哪裏出現時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be designed to transport","meaning":"被設計用來運送……","examples":[{"en":"The railway was designed to transport coal.","zh":"這條鐵路被設計用來運送煤炭。"},{"en":"Be designed to transport something means be built for the purpose of carrying it from one place to another.","zh":"be designed to transport something 指為了把某物從一處運到另一處而建造。"},{"en":"School buses are designed to transport students safely.","zh":"校巴被設計用來安全運送學生。"},{"en":"The railway’s original purpose was practical before it became a thrill ride.","zh":"這條鐵路在成為刺激機動遊戲前，原本用途是實用的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining an object’s intended function.","zh":"解釋物件原定功能時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"between two mountains","meaning":"在兩座山之間","examples":[{"en":"The railway transported coal between two mountains.","zh":"這條鐵路在兩座山之間運送煤炭。"},{"en":"Between two mountains means in the space or route connecting one mountain and another.","zh":"between two mountains 指在連接一座山和另一座山的空間或路線中。"},{"en":"A village may sit between two mountains and be difficult to reach by road.","zh":"村莊可能位於兩座山之間，公路難以到達。"},{"en":"A railway between two mountains was useful for moving heavy coal across rough land.","zh":"兩座山之間的鐵路對穿越崎嶇地形運送重煤很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing location or route.","zh":"描述位置或路線時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"convert something into","meaning":"把某物改造成……","examples":[{"en":"Josiah White converted the railway into a thrill ride.","zh":"Josiah White 把鐵路改造成刺激機動遊戲。"},{"en":"To convert something into something else means to change its use, form, or purpose.","zh":"convert something into something else 指改變某物的用途、形式或目的。"},{"en":"A family can convert a spare bedroom into a study room.","zh":"家庭可以把空置睡房改造成書房。"},{"en":"The railway’s purpose changed from transporting coal to entertaining passengers.","zh":"這條鐵路的用途由運煤改為娛樂乘客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing transformation.","zh":"描述轉變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"downhill backwards","meaning":"向後下坡","examples":[{"en":"The switchback track allowed the cars to travel downhill backwards.","zh":"折返軌道讓車卡能夠向後下坡。"},{"en":"Downhill backwards means moving down a slope while facing or moving in the reverse direction.","zh":"downhill backwards 指以相反方向面向或移動着下坡。"},{"en":"A toy car may roll downhill backwards if it starts facing uphill.","zh":"如果玩具車一開始面向上坡，它可能向後滾下斜坡。"},{"en":"Travelling backward downhill made the early ride feel unusual and exciting.","zh":"向後下坡令早期機動遊戲感覺不尋常又刺激。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing direction and movement on a slope.","zh":"描述斜坡上的方向和移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與文章資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements agree with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與文章資料一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the information means match what the text says.","zh":"agree with the information 指符合文本所說內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says the ride was in Pennsylvania, a statement saying the same agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說該機動遊戲在賓夕凡尼亞州，而陳述說同樣內容，它就與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should check meaning carefully instead of matching only repeated words.","zh":"學生應仔細檢查意思，而不是只配對重複字眼。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE, FALSE, NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文章資料相反","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相反。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章所述相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the text says the coaster was slow and a statement says it was extremely fast, the statement contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文本說過山車很慢，而陳述說它極快，該陳述就與資料相反。"},{"en":"A contradiction must be clear from the passage, not from outside knowledge.","zh":"矛盾必須清楚來自文章，而不是外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase helps students identify FALSE answers.","zh":"這個短語幫助學生辨認 FALSE 答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students select “NOT GIVEN” when the passage provides no relevant information.","zh":"當文章沒有提供相關資料時，學生選 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the text does not say whether the idea is true or false.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文本沒有說明該想法是真還是假。"},{"en":"If a passage describes a ride but never mentions ticket sales by month, there is no information on that.","zh":"如果文章描述一項機動遊戲，但從未提到每月門票銷售，就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from background knowledge when the text is silent.","zh":"當文本沒有提及時，學生不應根據背景知識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is essential for NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語對 NOT GIVEN 題很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"most exciting roller coaster","meaning":"最刺激的過山車","examples":[{"en":"The statement describes a New Jersey ride as the world’s most exciting roller coaster.","zh":"這個陳述把新澤西州的一項機動遊戲描述為世界上最刺激的過山車。"},{"en":"The most exciting roller coaster means the coaster believed to give the strongest thrill or enjoyment.","zh":"most exciting roller coaster 指被認為帶來最強刺激或享受的過山車。"},{"en":"A theme park may advertise a new ride as its most exciting roller coaster to attract visitors.","zh":"主題公園可能把新機動遊戲宣傳為園內最刺激的過山車，以吸引遊客。"},{"en":"Such a claim is often subjective unless the passage gives clear evidence for it.","zh":"除非文章提供清楚證據，這類說法通常帶主觀性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when judging whether a statement overstates what the text says.","zh":"判斷陳述是否誇大文本內容時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"further innovations","meaning":"進一步創新","examples":[{"en":"The French introduced further innovations to the original ice slide.","zh":"法國人對原始冰滑梯引入進一步創新。"},{"en":"Further innovations are additional new ideas or improvements after the first invention.","zh":"further innovations 指第一項發明後加入的額外新想法或改良。"},{"en":"A phone company may introduce further innovations after releasing its first model.","zh":"手機公司推出第一款型號後，可能引入進一步創新。"},{"en":"Adding waxed surfaces, wheels, and better tracks helped the ride develop beyond the original slide.","zh":"加入塗蠟表面、輪子和更好軌道，幫助機動遊戲超越原始滑梯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when improvements continue after an initial idea.","zh":"當初步想法之後繼續改良時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"including both A and B","meaning":"包括A和B","examples":[{"en":"The developments included both wheeled cars and improved tracks.","zh":"這些發展包括有輪車卡和改善後的軌道。"},{"en":"Including both A and B means containing two named things, not just one of them.","zh":"including both A and B 指包含兩個被點名的事物，而不只是其中一個。"},{"en":"A good revision plan should include both grammar practice and reading practice.","zh":"好的溫習計劃應包括文法練習和閱讀練習。"},{"en":"Mentioning both features helps students see that the improvement had more than one part.","zh":"提到兩個特徵有助學生看出改良不只包含一個部分。"},{"en":"This structure is useful when two items are equally relevant.","zh":"當兩項內容同樣相關時，這個結構很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 152 - Roller coaster.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 153":[{"front":"be inspired by","meaning":"受……啟發","examples":[{"en":"Many modern inventions are inspired by systems found in nature.","zh":"許多現代發明受大自然中系統的啟發。"},{"en":"Be inspired by means get an idea from something and use it to create or improve another thing.","zh":"be inspired by 指從某事物獲得想法，並用來創造或改善另一事物。"},{"en":"A student’s story may be inspired by a childhood memory.","zh":"學生的故事可能受童年回憶啟發。"},{"en":"If engineers are inspired by birds, they may design machines that fly more smoothly.","zh":"如果工程師受鳥類啟發，他們可能設計出飛得更流暢的機器。"},{"en":"The phrase shows where an idea comes from.","zh":"這個片語顯示一個想法來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mimic Mother Nature","meaning":"模仿大自然","examples":[{"en":"Designers mimic Mother Nature to create more efficient products.","zh":"設計師模仿大自然，以創造更高效的產品。"},{"en":"Mimic Mother Nature means copy patterns, shapes, or systems found in the natural world.","zh":"mimic Mother Nature 指模仿自然界中的模式、形狀或系統。"},{"en":"A shoe designer may mimic Mother Nature by copying the grip of animal feet.","zh":"鞋履設計師可能透過模仿動物腳掌的抓地力來模仿大自然。"},{"en":"If humans mimic nature well, products may use less energy and create less waste.","zh":"如果人類能有效模仿大自然，產品可能使用較少能源並產生較少廢物。"},{"en":"The phrase treats nature as a teacher for design.","zh":"這個片語把大自然視為設計上的老師。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"around the globe","meaning":"世界各地","examples":[{"en":"Researchers around the globe are studying biomimicry.","zh":"世界各地的研究人員正在研究仿生學。"},{"en":"Around the globe means in many countries or different parts of the world.","zh":"around the globe 指在許多國家或世界不同地方。"},{"en":"Students around the globe use the internet to learn languages.","zh":"世界各地的學生使用互聯網學習語言。"},{"en":"If scientists around the globe study the same problem, ideas can spread more quickly.","zh":"如果世界各地的科學家研究同一問題，想法就能更快傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses worldwide reach.","zh":"這個片語強調全球範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"endeavour to","meaning":"努力去……","examples":[{"en":"Researchers endeavour to create efficient and environmentally friendly technologies.","zh":"研究人員努力去創造高效而環保的科技。"},{"en":"Endeavour to means try hard to do something, especially something difficult or important.","zh":"endeavour to 指努力做某事，尤其是困難或重要的事情。"},{"en":"A school may endeavour to help every student read confidently.","zh":"學校可能努力去幫助每位學生有信心地閱讀。"},{"en":"If a task requires research, time, and patience, people must endeavour to complete it properly.","zh":"如果任務需要研究、時間和耐性，人們就必須努力去妥善完成。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds formal and stresses serious effort.","zh":"這個片語較正式，強調認真努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"create new technologies","meaning":"創造新科技","examples":[{"en":"Scientists use natural models to create new technologies.","zh":"科學家利用自然界模型來創造新科技。"},{"en":"Create new technologies means develop new tools, machines, systems, or methods.","zh":"create new technologies 指研發新的工具、機器、系統或方法。"},{"en":"Engineers create new technologies when they design safer batteries or better medical devices.","zh":"工程師設計更安全電池或更好醫療設備時，就是在創造新科技。"},{"en":"If scientists study nature carefully, they may create technologies that waste less energy.","zh":"如果科學家仔細研究大自然，可能創造出較少浪費能源的科技。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on invention and practical application.","zh":"這個片語集中於發明和實際應用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"honour the tenets of life","meaning":"遵從生命的基本原則","examples":[{"en":"Biomimetic technologies aim to honour the tenets of life.","zh":"仿生科技旨在遵從生命的基本原則。"},{"en":"Honour the tenets of life means respect the basic principles by which natural systems work.","zh":"honour the tenets of life 指尊重自然系統運作的基本原則。"},{"en":"A school garden honours the tenets of life when it reuses compost and avoids waste.","zh":"學校花園重用堆肥並避免浪費時，就是遵從生命的基本原則。"},{"en":"If a factory copies nature’s low-waste systems, it may operate more sustainably.","zh":"如果工廠模仿大自然低廢物系統，就可能更可持續地運作。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests respect for nature’s rules, not just copying its appearance.","zh":"這個片語暗示尊重大自然的規則，而不只是模仿外形。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tenets of life","meaning":"生命的基本原則","examples":[{"en":"The tenets of life include efficiency and minimal waste.","zh":"生命的基本原則包括效率和最低限度的浪費。"},{"en":"Tenets of life are the basic principles that living systems tend to follow.","zh":"tenets of life 指生命系統傾向遵循的基本原則。"},{"en":"In nature, one tenet of life is that waste from one organism can become food for another.","zh":"在大自然中，生命的一項基本原則是某生物的廢物可以成為另一生物的食物。"},{"en":"If designers follow these tenets, they may create products that use fewer resources.","zh":"如果設計師遵循這些原則，可能創造出使用較少資源的產品。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to nature’s guiding rules.","zh":"這個片語指大自然的指導規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"highly efficient","meaning":"高效率的","examples":[{"en":"Natural systems are often highly efficient.","zh":"自然系統通常十分高效率。"},{"en":"Highly efficient means able to achieve a result with little waste of energy, time, or materials.","zh":"highly efficient 指能以很少能源、時間或材料浪費達到結果。"},{"en":"A highly efficient washing machine uses less water and electricity.","zh":"高效率洗衣機使用較少水和電。"},{"en":"If a system is highly efficient, it can do more work with fewer resources.","zh":"如果一個系統高效率，它就能用較少資源完成更多工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong performance with low waste.","zh":"這個片語描述低浪費下的高表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"environmentally friendly","meaning":"環保的","examples":[{"en":"Many biomimetic products are environmentally friendly.","zh":"許多仿生產品都是環保的。"},{"en":"Environmentally friendly means causing little harm to nature, air, water, land, or living things.","zh":"environmentally friendly 指對大自然、空氣、水、土地或生物造成較少傷害。"},{"en":"A reusable bottle is more environmentally friendly than a disposable plastic bottle.","zh":"可重用水樽比即棄膠樽更環保。"},{"en":"If a product uses fewer toxins and less energy, it is usually more environmentally friendly.","zh":"如果產品使用較少毒素和能源，通常就更環保。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lower environmental damage.","zh":"這個片語描述較低環境損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"biomimicry","meaning":"仿生學","examples":[{"en":"Biomimicry involves learning from and imitating nature.","zh":"仿生學涉及向大自然學習並模仿大自然。"},{"en":"Biomimicry is the practice of studying nature’s designs and using them to solve human problems.","zh":"biomimicry 指研究大自然的設計，並用來解決人類問題的做法。"},{"en":"A building designer may use biomimicry by copying termite mounds to improve cooling.","zh":"建築設計師可能透過模仿白蟻丘來改善降溫，這就是仿生學。"},{"en":"If biomimicry works well, technology can become more efficient and less wasteful.","zh":"如果仿生學運作良好，科技可以變得更高效且較少浪費。"},{"en":"The word combines biology, design, and innovation.","zh":"這個詞結合生物學、設計和創新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"not a new concept","meaning":"並非新概念","examples":[{"en":"Biomimicry is not a new concept.","zh":"仿生學並非新概念。"},{"en":"Not a new concept means the idea has existed for a long time, even if it has become popular recently.","zh":"not a new concept 指某想法已存在很久，即使它最近才流行。"},{"en":"Online learning feels modern, but distance education is not a new concept.","zh":"網上學習感覺現代，但遙距教育並非新概念。"},{"en":"If people have copied nature for centuries, biomimicry is an old idea with new tools.","zh":"如果人類數百年來都在模仿大自然，仿生學就是一個有新工具的舊想法。"},{"en":"The phrase corrects the mistaken belief that something is completely recent.","zh":"這個片語糾正某事完全新近才出現的錯誤想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"look to nature to","meaning":"從大自然尋找方法去……","examples":[{"en":"Leonardo da Vinci looked to nature to design flying machines.","zh":"Leonardo da Vinci 從大自然尋找方法去設計飛行器。"},{"en":"Look to nature to means study natural systems in order to find ideas or solutions.","zh":"look to nature to 指研究自然系統，以尋找想法或解決方案。"},{"en":"Engineers may look to nature to design quieter fans or stronger materials.","zh":"工程師可能從大自然尋找方法去設計更安靜的風扇或更堅固的材料。"},{"en":"If humans face a design problem, nature may already offer a tested model.","zh":"如果人類面對設計問題，大自然可能已提供經過考驗的模型。"},{"en":"The phrase shows nature being used as a source of guidance.","zh":"這個片語顯示大自然被用作指導來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"flying machines","meaning":"飛行器","examples":[{"en":"Leonardo da Vinci studied birds while designing flying machines.","zh":"Leonardo da Vinci 在設計飛行器時研究鳥類。"},{"en":"Flying machines are devices designed to move through the air.","zh":"flying machines 指設計用來在空中移動的裝置。"},{"en":"Early inventors imagined flying machines long before modern aircraft existed.","zh":"早期發明家在現代飛機出現很久以前已想像飛行器。"},{"en":"If a flying machine copies bird wings, it may use natural ideas about lift and movement.","zh":"如果飛行器模仿鳥翼，它可能使用關於升力和移動的自然想法。"},{"en":"The phrase can refer to early aircraft designs or imagined machines.","zh":"這個片語可指早期飛機設計或想像中的機器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pharmaceutical companies","meaning":"製藥公司","examples":[{"en":"Pharmaceutical companies have long copied useful substances found in plants.","zh":"製藥公司長久以來都模仿植物中有用的物質。"},{"en":"Pharmaceutical companies are businesses that research, make, and sell medicines.","zh":"pharmaceutical companies 指研究、製造和銷售藥物的企業。"},{"en":"Pharmaceutical companies may test plant chemicals to see whether they can become safe drugs.","zh":"製藥公司可能測試植物化學物，以判斷它們能否成為安全藥物。"},{"en":"If a plant compound treats illness, companies may try to reproduce it in controlled form.","zh":"如果某植物化合物能治病，公司可能嘗試以受控形式重製它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the medicine industry.","zh":"這個片語指醫藥產業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"mimic plant compounds","meaning":"模仿植物化合物","examples":[{"en":"Some pharmaceutical companies mimic plant compounds in medicines.","zh":"有些製藥公司在藥物中模仿植物化合物。"},{"en":"Mimic plant compounds means copy the chemical structure or effect of substances found in plants.","zh":"mimic plant compounds 指模仿植物中物質的化學結構或作用。"},{"en":"Scientists may mimic plant compounds when a natural substance reduces pain or infection.","zh":"當天然物質能減痛或減少感染時，科學家可能模仿植物化合物。"},{"en":"If a compound is useful but rare, copying it can make treatment more widely available.","zh":"如果某化合物有用但稀有，模仿它可以令治療更廣泛可得。"},{"en":"The phrase describes chemical imitation for practical use.","zh":"這個片語描述為實際用途而進行的化學模仿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"plant compounds","meaning":"植物化合物","examples":[{"en":"Many drugs are based on useful plant compounds.","zh":"許多藥物以有用的植物化合物為基礎。"},{"en":"Plant compounds are chemical substances naturally produced by plants.","zh":"plant compounds 指植物自然產生的化學物質。"},{"en":"Caffeine and menthol are familiar plant compounds found in everyday products.","zh":"咖啡因和薄荷醇是日常產品中常見的植物化合物。"},{"en":"If a plant compound affects the body, researchers may study it for medical use.","zh":"如果植物化合物會影響身體，研究人員可能研究其醫療用途。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to chemicals from plants.","zh":"這個片語指來自植物的化學物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"synthetic drugs","meaning":"合成藥物","examples":[{"en":"Plant compounds are sometimes reproduced in synthetic drugs.","zh":"植物化合物有時會在合成藥物中被重製。"},{"en":"Synthetic drugs are medicines made by chemical processes rather than taken directly from nature.","zh":"synthetic drugs 指透過化學過程製成，而不是直接從大自然取得的藥物。"},{"en":"A synthetic drug may copy the effect of a natural pain-relieving compound.","zh":"合成藥物可能模仿天然止痛化合物的作用。"},{"en":"If natural materials are limited, synthetic drugs can provide a more stable supply.","zh":"如果天然材料有限，合成藥物可以提供更穩定的供應。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts laboratory-made medicine with natural sources.","zh":"這個片語把實驗室製成的藥物與天然來源作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a greater need for","meaning":"對……有更大需求","examples":[{"en":"There is a greater need for low-energy manufacturing processes.","zh":"人們對低能源生產過程有更大需求。"},{"en":"A greater need for something means it has become more necessary than before.","zh":"a greater need for something 指某事物比以前更有必要。"},{"en":"There is a greater need for mental health support when students face heavy pressure.","zh":"當學生面對沉重壓力，對心理健康支援就有更大需求。"},{"en":"If energy prices rise, factories may feel a greater need for efficient production.","zh":"如果能源價格上升，工廠可能感到對高效生產有更大需求。"},{"en":"The phrase shows increasing necessity.","zh":"這個片語顯示必要性增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"manufacturing processes","meaning":"生產過程","examples":[{"en":"Biomimicry can improve manufacturing processes.","zh":"仿生學可以改善生產過程。"},{"en":"Manufacturing processes are the steps used to make products in factories or workshops.","zh":"manufacturing processes 指在工廠或工作坊製造產品所用的步驟。"},{"en":"A bakery’s manufacturing process includes mixing, baking, cooling, and packaging.","zh":"麵包店的生產過程包括攪拌、烘焙、冷卻和包裝。"},{"en":"If manufacturing processes use less heat and fewer chemicals, they may become safer and greener.","zh":"如果生產過程使用較少熱力和化學物，就可能變得更安全和更環保。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how goods are produced.","zh":"這個片語描述貨品如何被製造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"use a minimum of","meaning":"使用最少量的……","examples":[{"en":"Sustainable products should use a minimum of energy and materials.","zh":"可持續產品應使用最少量的能源和材料。"},{"en":"Use a minimum of means use the smallest possible amount.","zh":"use a minimum of 指使用盡可能少的數量。"},{"en":"A good travel bag uses a minimum of space but still holds essential items.","zh":"好的旅行袋使用最少量空間，但仍能裝下必需品。"},{"en":"If factories use a minimum of resources, costs and pollution may fall.","zh":"如果工廠使用最少資源，成本和污染可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses efficiency and avoiding waste.","zh":"這個片語強調效率和避免浪費。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"energy, materials and toxins","meaning":"能源、物料和有毒物質","examples":[{"en":"New manufacturing methods should minimise energy, materials and toxins.","zh":"新生產方法應盡量減少能源、物料和有毒物質。"},{"en":"Energy, materials and toxins are resources used and harmful substances produced or involved in making things.","zh":"energy, materials and toxins 指製造物品時使用的資源，以及產生或涉及的有害物質。"},{"en":"A cleaner factory design may reduce energy, materials and toxins at the same time.","zh":"較清潔的工廠設計可能同時減少能源、物料和有毒物質。"},{"en":"If production needs fewer materials and releases fewer toxins, it is safer for workers and the environment.","zh":"如果生產需要較少材料並釋放較少毒素，對工人和環境都較安全。"},{"en":"The phrase groups three key concerns in sustainable manufacturing.","zh":"這個片語集合可持續生產中的三個關鍵關注點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what’s more","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"What’s more, modern computers allow designers to copy complex natural shapes.","zh":"此外，現代電腦讓設計師能模仿複雜的自然形狀。"},{"en":"What’s more means in addition, and it introduces another important point.","zh":"what’s more 指此外，並引出另一個重要點。"},{"en":"The library is quiet; what’s more, it stays open until late during exam season.","zh":"圖書館很安靜；此外，它在考試季節開放至很晚。"},{"en":"If a product saves energy and is cheaper to make, what’s more, companies may adopt it quickly.","zh":"如果產品節省能源且製造較便宜，此外，公司可能很快採用它。"},{"en":"The phrase adds extra support to an argument.","zh":"這個片語為論點加入額外支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"technological advancements","meaning":"科技進步","examples":[{"en":"Technological advancements have made biomimetic design easier.","zh":"科技進步令仿生設計更容易。"},{"en":"Technological advancements are improvements in tools, machines, software, or scientific methods.","zh":"technological advancements 指工具、機器、軟件或科學方法上的改進。"},{"en":"Technological advancements allow doctors to detect some diseases earlier than before.","zh":"科技進步讓醫生比以前更早偵測某些疾病。"},{"en":"If computer modelling improves, designers can test complex shapes before making them.","zh":"如果電腦模擬改善，設計師就能在製造前測試複雜形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes progress in technology.","zh":"這個片語描述科技上的進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"newfound spirit of innovation","meaning":"新興的創新精神","examples":[{"en":"A newfound spirit of innovation is encouraging designers to study nature.","zh":"新興的創新精神正在鼓勵設計師研究大自然。"},{"en":"A newfound spirit of innovation means a recently developed enthusiasm for creating new ideas and solutions.","zh":"newfound spirit of innovation 指近期形成的、對創造新想法和解決方案的熱情。"},{"en":"A school may show a newfound spirit of innovation after teachers begin trying new lesson formats.","zh":"當老師開始嘗試新課堂形式後，學校可能展現新興的創新精神。"},{"en":"If businesses feel pressure to reduce waste, they may become more willing to experiment.","zh":"如果企業感到減少浪費的壓力，可能更願意實驗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fresh creative energy.","zh":"這個片語描述新鮮的創造能量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"myriad ways to","meaning":"無數種……的方法","examples":[{"en":"There are myriad ways to imitate nature’s most effective designs.","zh":"有無數種方法可以模仿大自然最有效的設計。"},{"en":"Myriad ways to means a very large number of ways to do something.","zh":"myriad ways to 指做某事有非常大量的方法。"},{"en":"There are myriad ways to practise English, from reading signs to recording your own voice.","zh":"練習英語有無數種方法，從閱讀標誌到錄下自己的聲音。"},{"en":"If nature offers many models, designers have many possible paths for innovation.","zh":"如果大自然提供許多模型，設計師就有許多可能的創新路徑。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses abundance and variety.","zh":"這個片語強調數量豐富和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Mother Nature’s best assets","meaning":"大自然最出色的特點","examples":[{"en":"Designers try to mimic Mother Nature’s best assets.","zh":"設計師嘗試模仿大自然最出色的特點。"},{"en":"Mother Nature’s best assets are the most useful strengths, patterns, or systems found in nature.","zh":"Mother Nature’s best assets 指自然界中最有用的強項、模式或系統。"},{"en":"A designer may see a spider web’s strength as one of Mother Nature’s best assets.","zh":"設計師可能把蜘蛛網的強度視為大自然最出色的特點之一。"},{"en":"If humans copy nature’s best assets carefully, they may build stronger and lighter products.","zh":"如果人類仔細模仿大自然最好的特點，就可能製造更堅固而更輕的產品。"},{"en":"The phrase praises the valuable features of the natural world.","zh":"這個片語讚賞自然界有價值的特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a perfect storm","meaning":"多種有利因素同時出現的局面","examples":[{"en":"Several favourable developments have created a perfect storm for biomimicry.","zh":"幾項有利發展為仿生學創造了多種有利因素同時出現的局面。"},{"en":"A perfect storm is a situation where several factors combine to create a powerful result.","zh":"a perfect storm 指幾個因素結合並產生強大結果的情況。"},{"en":"Cheap internet, smartphones, and online payment created a perfect storm for food delivery apps.","zh":"便宜互聯網、智能手機和網上付款，為外賣應用程式創造了多種因素同時出現的局面。"},{"en":"If environmental pressure, computer power, and design interest all increase together, biomimicry can grow quickly.","zh":"如果環境壓力、電腦運算能力和設計興趣同時增加，仿生學就能快速發展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes many forces coming together at once.","zh":"這個片語描述多股力量同時結合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"happen right now","meaning":"現正發生","examples":[{"en":"A major change in biomimetic design is happening right now.","zh":"仿生設計中的重大變化現正發生。"},{"en":"Happen right now means be taking place at this present moment or in the current period.","zh":"happen right now 指在此刻或目前這段時期正在發生。"},{"en":"A school renovation may be happening right now, so some classrooms are closed.","zh":"學校翻新工程可能現正發生，所以部分課室關閉。"},{"en":"If change is happening right now, people can observe it instead of only predicting it.","zh":"如果變化現正發生，人們就可以觀察它，而不只是預測它。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses immediacy.","zh":"這個片語強調即時性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"inventor and CEO","meaning":"發明家兼行政總裁","examples":[{"en":"Jay Harman is an inventor and CEO of PAX Scientific.","zh":"Jay Harman 是 PAX Scientific 的發明家兼行政總裁。"},{"en":"An inventor and CEO is someone who creates new products and also leads a company.","zh":"inventor and CEO 指創造新產品，同時領導公司的人。"},{"en":"An inventor and CEO may design a device in the lab and then decide how to sell it.","zh":"發明家兼行政總裁可能在實驗室設計裝置，然後決定如何銷售。"},{"en":"If a CEO is also an inventor, the company’s business strategy may be closely linked to technology.","zh":"如果行政總裁同時是發明家，公司的商業策略可能與科技密切相關。"},{"en":"The phrase combines creative and executive roles.","zh":"這個片語結合創造和管理角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"design fans, mixers and pumps","meaning":"設計風扇、攪拌器和泵","examples":[{"en":"The company designs fans, mixers and pumps based on natural patterns.","zh":"該公司根據自然模式設計風扇、攪拌器和泵。"},{"en":"Design fans, mixers and pumps means create machines that move air, mix substances, or move liquids.","zh":"design fans, mixers and pumps 指創造移動空氣、混合物質或輸送液體的機器。"},{"en":"An engineering firm may design fans, mixers and pumps for factories, kitchens, or water systems.","zh":"工程公司可能為工廠、廚房或水系統設計風扇、攪拌器和泵。"},{"en":"If these machines copy natural flow patterns, they may use less energy.","zh":"如果這些機器模仿自然流動模式，可能使用較少能源。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to designing practical industrial equipment.","zh":"這個片語指設計實用工業設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"achieve maximum efficiency","meaning":"達至最高效率","examples":[{"en":"The equipment is designed to achieve maximum efficiency.","zh":"這些設備被設計成能達至最高效率。"},{"en":"Achieve maximum efficiency means reach the highest possible level of useful output with the least waste.","zh":"achieve maximum efficiency 指以最少浪費達到最高可能的有用產出。"},{"en":"A bus route can achieve maximum efficiency if it carries many passengers without long delays.","zh":"如果巴士路線能載大量乘客而沒有長時間延誤，就能達至最高效率。"},{"en":"If a pump moves more water with less power, it is closer to maximum efficiency.","zh":"如果泵用較少電力輸送更多水，就更接近最高效率。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the best possible use of resources.","zh":"這個片語強調資源的最佳使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"imitate the natural flow of","meaning":"模仿……的自然流動方式","examples":[{"en":"The machines imitate the natural flow of fluids.","zh":"這些機器模仿流體的自然流動方式。"},{"en":"Imitate the natural flow of means copy the way liquids or gases move in nature.","zh":"imitate the natural flow of 指模仿液體或氣體在大自然中的移動方式。"},{"en":"A ventilation system may imitate the natural flow of air through caves.","zh":"通風系統可能模仿空氣穿過洞穴的自然流動方式。"},{"en":"If machines copy smoother natural flow, they may reduce noise and energy loss.","zh":"如果機器模仿更順暢的自然流動，就可能減少噪音和能源損失。"},{"en":"The phrase connects movement in nature with human design.","zh":"這個片語把自然界的移動與人類設計連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"natural flow of fluids","meaning":"流體的自然流動","examples":[{"en":"PAX Scientific studies the natural flow of fluids.","zh":"PAX Scientific 研究流體的自然流動。"},{"en":"Natural flow of fluids means the way liquids or gases move without artificial forcing.","zh":"natural flow of fluids 指液體或氣體在沒有人工強迫下的移動方式。"},{"en":"Water swirling down a drain shows a natural flow of fluid.","zh":"水旋轉流入去水渠，顯示了流體的自然流動。"},{"en":"If engineers understand natural fluid flow, they can design quieter and more efficient pumps.","zh":"如果工程師理解自然流體流動，就能設計更安靜、更高效的泵。"},{"en":"The phrase belongs to fluid movement and design.","zh":"這個片語屬於流體移動和設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"shapes in nature","meaning":"自然界中的形狀","examples":[{"en":"Shapes in nature often appear simple once they are understood.","zh":"自然界中的形狀一旦被理解，往往看似簡單。"},{"en":"Shapes in nature are forms found in living things, water, wind, rocks, shells, or plants.","zh":"shapes in nature 指在生物、水、風、岩石、貝殼或植物中找到的形態。"},{"en":"Spirals in shells and branching patterns in trees are common shapes in nature.","zh":"貝殼中的螺旋和樹木中的分枝模式，是自然界中常見的形狀。"},{"en":"If designers study natural shapes, they may discover efficient structures.","zh":"如果設計師研究自然形狀，可能發現高效結構。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to visible natural forms.","zh":"這個片語指可見的自然形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"once you understand them","meaning":"一旦你理解它們","examples":[{"en":"Natural patterns seem simple once you understand them.","zh":"自然模式一旦你理解它們，就會顯得簡單。"},{"en":"Once you understand them means after you have learned how they work.","zh":"once you understand them 指在你學會它們如何運作之後。"},{"en":"Grammar rules feel less frightening once you understand them through examples.","zh":"文法規則一旦你透過例子理解它們，就不會那麼可怕。"},{"en":"If a natural pattern is understood, designers can adapt it more confidently.","zh":"如果自然模式被理解，設計師就能更有信心地改造它。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that difficulty can disappear after explanation.","zh":"這個片語顯示困難可以在解釋後消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"geometries at play","meaning":"當中發揮作用的幾何結構","examples":[{"en":"Researchers must understand the geometries at play in natural systems.","zh":"研究人員必須理解自然系統中發揮作用的幾何結構。"},{"en":"Geometries at play are the shapes, patterns, and spatial relationships that are actively influencing how something works.","zh":"geometries at play 指正在影響某事物運作的形狀、模式和空間關係。"},{"en":"A football coach studies the spacing at play between players during an attack.","zh":"足球教練會研究進攻時球員之間發揮作用的站位。"},{"en":"If engineers understand the geometries at play in a shell, they may copy its strength.","zh":"如果工程師理解貝殼中發揮作用的幾何結構，就可能模仿其強度。"},{"en":"The phrase points to hidden structure behind visible form.","zh":"這個片語指出可見形態背後的隱藏結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"adapt natural geometries","meaning":"改造自然界的幾何結構","examples":[{"en":"Designers adapt natural geometries for industrial products.","zh":"設計師為工業產品改造自然界的幾何結構。"},{"en":"Adapt natural geometries means change natural shapes or patterns so they can be used in human designs.","zh":"adapt natural geometries 指改變自然形狀或模式，使其能用於人類設計。"},{"en":"An architect may adapt honeycomb geometry to design a strong lightweight roof.","zh":"建築師可能改造蜂巢幾何結構，以設計堅固輕巧的屋頂。"},{"en":"If natural geometry is copied too literally, it may not fit industrial needs.","zh":"如果自然幾何被過於字面地複製，可能不符合工業需要。"},{"en":"The phrase means modify nature’s patterns, not simply trace them.","zh":"這個片語指改造大自然模式，而不只是照着描繪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a complex process","meaning":"複雜過程","examples":[{"en":"Turning a natural form into a product is a complex process.","zh":"把自然形態變成產品是一個複雜過程。"},{"en":"A complex process is a task with many connected steps, decisions, and difficulties.","zh":"a complex process 指包含許多互相關連步驟、決定和困難的任務。"},{"en":"Applying to university can be a complex process because students need forms, documents, and deadlines.","zh":"申請大學可能是一個複雜過程，因為學生需要表格、文件和截止日期。"},{"en":"If a design must copy nature and fit factory production, the process becomes complicated.","zh":"如果設計既要模仿自然，又要符合工廠生產，過程就會變得複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that the task is not simple.","zh":"這個片語提醒任務並不簡單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"computer power","meaning":"電腦運算能力","examples":[{"en":"Modern computer power allows researchers to model natural shapes.","zh":"現代電腦運算能力讓研究人員能模擬自然形狀。"},{"en":"Computer power means the ability of computers to process data, run calculations, and create models.","zh":"computer power 指電腦處理數據、運行計算和建立模型的能力。"},{"en":"Weather forecasts need computer power because millions of measurements must be processed.","zh":"天氣預報需要電腦運算能力，因為數以百萬計的測量必須被處理。"},{"en":"If computer power increases, scientists can test more designs before building them.","zh":"如果電腦運算能力增加，科學家就能在建造前測試更多設計。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to computing strength and speed.","zh":"這個片語指電腦計算強度和速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"manufacturing capability","meaning":"生產能力","examples":[{"en":"Companies now have the manufacturing capability to produce complex forms.","zh":"公司現在有生產能力製造複雜形態。"},{"en":"Manufacturing capability is the ability to make a product using available machines, materials, and skills.","zh":"manufacturing capability 指使用現有機器、材料和技術製造產品的能力。"},{"en":"A small workshop may lack the manufacturing capability to produce thousands of identical parts.","zh":"小工作坊可能缺乏生產數千個相同零件的能力。"},{"en":"If a factory gains better machines, it can make shapes that were impossible before.","zh":"如果工廠獲得更好的機器，就能製造以前不可能的形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what production systems can actually do.","zh":"這個片語描述生產系統實際能做到甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"produce these types of shapes","meaning":"製造這類形狀","examples":[{"en":"Modern machinery can produce these types of shapes accurately.","zh":"現代機器能準確製造這類形狀。"},{"en":"Produce these types of shapes means manufacture forms with similar complexity or structure.","zh":"produce these types of shapes 指製造具有相似複雜度或結構的形態。"},{"en":"A 3D printer can produce these types of shapes more easily than traditional cutting tools.","zh":"3D打印機比傳統切割工具更容易製造這類形狀。"},{"en":"If factories can produce complex natural shapes, biomimetic designs become more practical.","zh":"如果工廠能製造複雜自然形狀，仿生設計就更實用。"},{"en":"The phrase links design possibility with manufacturing.","zh":"這個片語把設計可能性與製造連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"capture nature’s efficiencies","meaning":"採用大自然的高效機制","examples":[{"en":"Industries could save energy by capturing nature’s efficiencies.","zh":"工業界可以透過採用大自然的高效機制來節省能源。"},{"en":"Capture nature’s efficiencies means successfully use the low-waste, high-performance methods found in nature.","zh":"capture nature’s efficiencies 指成功使用大自然中低浪費、高表現的方法。"},{"en":"A building may capture nature’s efficiencies by using natural airflow instead of constant air conditioning.","zh":"建築物可以透過使用自然通風而不是持續冷氣來採用大自然的高效機制。"},{"en":"If industries copy efficient natural systems, they may reduce costs and pollution.","zh":"如果工業界模仿高效自然系統，可能降低成本和污染。"},{"en":"The phrase means learning from how nature saves energy and materials.","zh":"這個片語指學習大自然如何節省能源和材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"across the board","meaning":"全面地；在所有方面","examples":[{"en":"Energy use could be reduced across the board.","zh":"能源使用可以全面減少。"},{"en":"Across the board means in every area or for all parts of a system.","zh":"across the board 指在每個範疇或系統所有部分中。"},{"en":"A school may improve safety across the board by checking classrooms, playgrounds, and buses.","zh":"學校可以透過檢查課室、操場和校巴，全面改善安全。"},{"en":"If all departments reduce electricity use, savings happen across the board.","zh":"如果所有部門都減少用電，節省就會在所有方面出現。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses broad, not limited, change.","zh":"這個片語強調廣泛而非有限的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"decrease dependency on fuel","meaning":"減少對燃料的依賴","examples":[{"en":"Biomimicry could decrease dependency on fuel.","zh":"仿生學可以減少對燃料的依賴。"},{"en":"Decrease dependency on fuel means reduce the need to use fuel for energy.","zh":"decrease dependency on fuel 指減少使用燃料獲取能源的需要。"},{"en":"Better public transport can decrease dependency on private car fuel.","zh":"更好的公共交通可以減少對私家車燃料的依賴。"},{"en":"If machines become more efficient, factories need less fuel to produce the same output.","zh":"如果機器變得更高效，工廠就需要較少燃料來產生同樣產出。"},{"en":"The phrase links efficiency with lower fuel use.","zh":"這個片語把效率與較低燃料使用連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"by at least 50 percent","meaning":"至少百分之五十","examples":[{"en":"Fuel dependency could fall by at least 50 percent.","zh":"對燃料的依賴可以下降至少百分之五十。"},{"en":"By at least 50 percent means by half or more.","zh":"by at least 50 percent 指下降或改變一半或以上。"},{"en":"A shop may cut plastic bag use by at least 50 percent after charging for bags.","zh":"商店收取膠袋費後，膠袋使用量可能減少至少百分之五十。"},{"en":"If energy demand falls by at least 50 percent, the savings are substantial.","zh":"如果能源需求下降至少百分之五十，節省量就很可觀。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a minimum size of change.","zh":"這個片語給出變化的最低幅度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"tools and methodology","meaning":"工具和方法","examples":[{"en":"Researchers already possess useful tools and methodology.","zh":"研究人員已擁有有用的工具和方法。"},{"en":"Tools and methodology means the equipment, techniques, and systematic methods used to study or solve a problem.","zh":"tools and methodology 指用來研究或解決問題的設備、技術和系統方法。"},{"en":"A teacher needs both teaching tools and methodology to help weak students improve.","zh":"老師需要教學工具和方法，才能幫助能力較弱的學生進步。"},{"en":"If researchers have good tools and methodology, they can test ideas more reliably.","zh":"如果研究人員有良好工具和方法，就能更可靠地測試想法。"},{"en":"The phrase combines practical instruments with organised methods.","zh":"這個片語結合實用工具和有組織的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"reduce energy consumption","meaning":"減少能源消耗","examples":[{"en":"Biomimetic technologies can reduce energy consumption significantly.","zh":"仿生科技可以大幅減少能源消耗。"},{"en":"Reduce energy consumption means use less electricity, fuel, or power.","zh":"reduce energy consumption 指使用較少電力、燃料或能源。"},{"en":"Turning off lights after class can reduce energy consumption in a school.","zh":"課後關燈可以減少學校能源消耗。"},{"en":"If machines move air or water more efficiently, they reduce energy use and operating costs.","zh":"如果機器更有效地移動空氣或水，就能減少能源使用和營運成本。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on lowering energy demand.","zh":"這個片語集中於降低能源需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"between 30 and 40 percent","meaning":"百分之三十至四十之間","examples":[{"en":"Current methods may reduce energy use by between 30 and 40 percent.","zh":"現行方法可能把能源使用減少百分之三十至四十之間。"},{"en":"Between 30 and 40 percent means more than 30 percent but less than 40 percent.","zh":"between 30 and 40 percent 指超過百分之三十但低於百分之四十。"},{"en":"A sale offering between 30 and 40 percent off can make expensive items more affordable.","zh":"提供百分之三十至四十折扣的減價，可以令昂貴物品較可負擔。"},{"en":"If energy use falls by this amount, the improvement is large enough to matter.","zh":"如果能源使用下降這個幅度，改善就大到值得重視。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate numerical range.","zh":"這個片語給出大約的數字範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mainstream companies","meaning":"主流企業","examples":[{"en":"Mainstream companies have begun investing in biomimicry.","zh":"主流企業已開始投資仿生學。"},{"en":"Mainstream companies are ordinary large or well-known businesses, not only small experimental firms.","zh":"mainstream companies 指普通大型或知名企業，而不只是小型實驗公司。"},{"en":"When mainstream companies adopt online payment, customers quickly treat it as normal.","zh":"當主流企業採用網上付款，顧客很快就會視之為正常。"},{"en":"If mainstream companies invest in biomimicry, the idea has moved beyond specialist research.","zh":"如果主流企業投資仿生學，這個概念就已超越專門研究。"},{"en":"The phrase signals broad business acceptance.","zh":"這個片語標示廣泛商業接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"equate biomimicry with","meaning":"將仿生學與……相提並論","examples":[{"en":"Companies increasingly equate biomimicry with commercial success.","zh":"公司越來越將仿生學與商業成功相提並論。"},{"en":"Equate biomimicry with something means treat biomimicry as closely connected with that result.","zh":"equate biomimicry with something 指把仿生學視為與某結果密切相關。"},{"en":"Some schools equate good grades with success, although education is broader than exams.","zh":"有些學校把好成績與成功相提並論，雖然教育比考試更廣闊。"},{"en":"If companies see biomimicry as profitable, they may invest in it more seriously.","zh":"如果公司把仿生學視為有利可圖，就可能更認真投資。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that two ideas are being linked strongly.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩個概念被緊密連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the bottom line","meaning":"盈利底線；最終利潤","examples":[{"en":"Mainstream companies now recognise that biomimicry can improve the bottom line.","zh":"主流企業現在認識到仿生學可以改善盈利底線。"},{"en":"The bottom line means a company’s final profit or financial result.","zh":"the bottom line 指公司的最終利潤或財務結果。"},{"en":"A shop improves the bottom line if it reduces waste and sells more products.","zh":"如果商店減少浪費並賣出更多產品，就能改善最終利潤。"},{"en":"If biomimicry lowers energy costs, it can make a business more profitable.","zh":"如果仿生學降低能源成本，就能令企業更有利可圖。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in business discussions.","zh":"這個片語常見於商業討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"introduce a prototype car","meaning":"推出汽車原型","examples":[{"en":"DaimlerChrysler introduced a prototype car inspired by a fish.","zh":"DaimlerChrysler 推出了一款受魚啟發的汽車原型。"},{"en":"Introduce a prototype car means present an early test version of a new car design.","zh":"introduce a prototype car 指展示新汽車設計的早期測試版本。"},{"en":"A car company may introduce a prototype car at an exhibition before mass production begins.","zh":"汽車公司可能在展覽中推出汽車原型，然後才開始大量生產。"},{"en":"If a prototype performs well, engineers may develop it into a real product.","zh":"如果原型表現良好，工程師可能把它發展成真正產品。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to showing an experimental vehicle.","zh":"這個片語指展示實驗性車輛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"prototype car","meaning":"汽車原型","examples":[{"en":"The prototype car was designed to be both strong and light.","zh":"該汽車原型被設計成既堅固又輕巧。"},{"en":"A prototype car is an early model built to test a new vehicle idea.","zh":"prototype car 指為測試新車概念而製作的早期模型。"},{"en":"Engineers may drive a prototype car on test tracks before selling the final version.","zh":"工程師可能在測試賽道駕駛汽車原型，然後才出售最終版本。"},{"en":"If a prototype car reveals design problems, the company can fix them before production.","zh":"如果汽車原型揭示設計問題，公司可以在生產前修正。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a trial version, not a normal showroom car.","zh":"這個片語描述試驗版本，而不是普通展廳汽車。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be modelled on","meaning":"以……為設計藍本","examples":[{"en":"The car was modelled on a coral reef fish.","zh":"這款汽車以一種珊瑚礁魚類為設計藍本。"},{"en":"Be modelled on means be designed by copying or adapting the form of something else.","zh":"be modelled on 指透過模仿或改造另一事物的形式來設計。"},{"en":"A school library may be modelled on a café to make reading feel relaxed.","zh":"學校圖書館可能以咖啡店為設計藍本，令閱讀感覺更放鬆。"},{"en":"If a vehicle is modelled on a fish, its shape may copy how the fish moves through water.","zh":"如果車輛以魚為設計藍本，其形狀可能模仿魚如何在水中移動。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the design source.","zh":"這個片語指出設計來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"coral reef fish","meaning":"珊瑚礁魚類","examples":[{"en":"The boxfish is a type of coral reef fish.","zh":"箱魨是一種珊瑚礁魚類。"},{"en":"Coral reef fish are fish that live around coral reefs.","zh":"coral reef fish 指生活在珊瑚礁周圍的魚類。"},{"en":"Divers often see colourful coral reef fish swimming among corals.","zh":"潛水員常看見色彩鮮艷的珊瑚礁魚類在珊瑚間游動。"},{"en":"If a coral reef fish moves efficiently in water, designers may study its shape.","zh":"如果珊瑚礁魚類在水中移動高效，設計師可能研究其形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase names fish from a reef habitat.","zh":"這個片語指出來自珊瑚礁棲息地的魚類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"despite its boxy body","meaning":"儘管它的身體呈方盒形","examples":[{"en":"Despite its boxy body, the fish moves efficiently through water.","zh":"儘管它的身體呈方盒形，這種魚仍能高效地在水中移動。"},{"en":"Despite its boxy body means although its body looks square and not streamlined.","zh":"despite its boxy body 指雖然它的身體看起來方正而不像流線型。"},{"en":"Despite its small size, a tablet can perform many tasks once done on a computer.","zh":"儘管平板電腦體積小，它也能完成許多以前由電腦做的工作。"},{"en":"If a box-shaped fish moves efficiently, its appearance challenges common assumptions.","zh":"如果方盒形魚能高效移動，其外形就挑戰常見假設。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces contrast between appearance and performance.","zh":"這個片語引出外觀與表現之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cube-shaped body","meaning":"立方體形的身體","examples":[{"en":"The boxfish has a distinctive cube-shaped body.","zh":"箱魨有獨特的立方體形身體。"},{"en":"A cube-shaped body is a body shaped roughly like a box or cube.","zh":"cube-shaped body 指大致像盒子或立方體的身體。"},{"en":"A toy robot may have a cube-shaped body that makes it look simple and solid.","zh":"玩具機械人可能有立方體形身體，使它看起來簡單而堅固。"},{"en":"If a fish has a cube-shaped body but moves well, shape alone does not tell the whole story.","zh":"如果魚有立方體形身體但移動良好，形狀本身不能說明全部情況。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a square, box-like physical form.","zh":"這個片語描述方正、盒子般的身體形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"defy a long-held standard","meaning":"違反長久以來的標準","examples":[{"en":"The car’s shape defied a long-held aerodynamic standard.","zh":"這款汽車的形狀違反了長久以來的空氣動力學標準。"},{"en":"Defy a long-held standard means challenge or go against a rule people have believed for a long time.","zh":"defy a long-held standard 指挑戰或違反人們長期相信的規則。"},{"en":"A student may defy a long-held standard by proving that a simple design works better than a complex one.","zh":"學生可能透過證明簡單設計比複雜設計更好，違反長久以來的標準。"},{"en":"If new evidence contradicts an old design rule, engineers may rethink their assumptions.","zh":"如果新證據與舊設計規則矛盾，工程師可能重新思考假設。"},{"en":"The phrase describes breaking an established belief.","zh":"這個片語描述打破既有信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"aerodynamic standard","meaning":"空氣動力學標準","examples":[{"en":"The raindrop shape had long been considered an aerodynamic standard.","zh":"水滴形長久以來被視為空氣動力學標準。"},{"en":"An aerodynamic standard is a widely accepted idea about what shape moves efficiently through air.","zh":"aerodynamic standard 指關於甚麼形狀能高效穿過空氣的廣泛接受概念。"},{"en":"Racing cyclists follow aerodynamic standards when they lower their bodies to reduce drag.","zh":"賽車單車手壓低身體減少阻力時，就是遵循空氣動力學標準。"},{"en":"If a boxy shape works well, it may challenge existing aerodynamic standards.","zh":"如果方盒形狀表現良好，就可能挑戰現有空氣動力學標準。"},{"en":"The phrase belongs to design involving air movement.","zh":"這個片語屬於涉及空氣流動的設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"automotive design","meaning":"汽車設計","examples":[{"en":"The boxfish challenged traditional assumptions in automotive design.","zh":"箱魨挑戰了汽車設計中的傳統假設。"},{"en":"Automotive design is the design of cars and other motor vehicles.","zh":"automotive design 指汽車和其他機動車輛的設計。"},{"en":"Automotive design includes shape, safety, weight, comfort, and fuel efficiency.","zh":"汽車設計包括外形、安全、重量、舒適度和燃油效率。"},{"en":"If natural models influence car shape, automotive design may become more experimental.","zh":"如果自然模型影響汽車外形，汽車設計可能變得更具實驗性。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to vehicle design as a professional field.","zh":"這個片語指作為專業領域的車輛設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"raindrop shape","meaning":"水滴形","examples":[{"en":"Many vehicle designers favour a smooth raindrop shape.","zh":"許多車輛設計師偏好平滑的水滴形。"},{"en":"A raindrop shape is a rounded form that tapers smoothly at one end.","zh":"raindrop shape 指一端平滑收窄的圓潤形狀。"},{"en":"A helmet may use a raindrop shape to reduce air resistance.","zh":"頭盔可能使用水滴形來減少空氣阻力。"},{"en":"If designers assume raindrop shapes are always best, they may ignore other efficient forms.","zh":"如果設計師假設水滴形永遠最好，就可能忽視其他高效形態。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common streamlined form.","zh":"這個片語描述常見的流線型形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"streamlined boxfish","meaning":"流線型箱魨","examples":[{"en":"The streamlined boxfish inspired a highly efficient car body.","zh":"流線型箱魨啟發了一個高效率車身。"},{"en":"A streamlined boxfish is a boxfish whose body helps it move smoothly through water despite its boxy form.","zh":"streamlined boxfish 指即使身體呈方盒形，仍能順暢在水中移動的箱魨。"},{"en":"A designer may study a streamlined boxfish to learn how corners and curves work together.","zh":"設計師可能研究流線型箱魨，以了解角位和曲線如何配合。"},{"en":"If a boxfish can move with low resistance, its shape may be useful for vehicle design.","zh":"如果箱魨能以低阻力移動，其形狀可能對車輛設計有用。"},{"en":"The phrase joins an unexpected body shape with efficient movement.","zh":"這個片語把意想不到的身體形狀與高效移動連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prove to be","meaning":"證明是","examples":[{"en":"The unusual shape proved to be aerodynamically ideal.","zh":"這個不尋常形狀證明在空氣動力學上十分理想。"},{"en":"Prove to be means turn out to have a particular quality after testing or experience.","zh":"prove to be 指經測試或經驗後顯示具有某種特質。"},{"en":"A quiet student may prove to be an excellent team leader during a project.","zh":"安靜學生可能在項目中證明是出色的小組領袖。"},{"en":"If a strange design performs well in tests, it may prove to be better than expected.","zh":"如果奇怪設計在測試中表現良好，它可能證明比預期更好。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a result that becomes clear later.","zh":"這個片語顯示後來變得清楚的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"aerodynamically ideal","meaning":"在空氣動力學上十分理想","examples":[{"en":"The boxfish’s shape proved to be aerodynamically ideal.","zh":"箱魨的形狀證明在空氣動力學上十分理想。"},{"en":"Aerodynamically ideal means shaped in a way that moves through air with very little resistance.","zh":"aerodynamically ideal 指形狀能以很少阻力穿過空氣。"},{"en":"A racing car must be aerodynamically efficient so it can move faster with less drag.","zh":"賽車必須在空氣動力學上高效，才能以較少阻力更快前進。"},{"en":"If a shape reduces air resistance, it can improve fuel efficiency and speed.","zh":"如果形狀減少空氣阻力，就能改善燃油效率和速度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an excellent shape for moving through air.","zh":"這個片語描述非常適合穿過空氣的形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"unique construction","meaning":"獨特結構","examples":[{"en":"The unique construction of the fish’s skin inspired the car’s frame.","zh":"魚皮的獨特結構啟發了汽車框架。"},{"en":"Unique construction means a special way something is built or arranged.","zh":"unique construction 指某物被建造或安排的特殊方式。"},{"en":"A bridge’s unique construction may allow it to carry heavy traffic without many pillars.","zh":"橋樑的獨特結構可能令它不需要很多支柱也能承載繁忙交通。"},{"en":"If a fish’s skin is built in a special way, engineers may copy its strength and lightness.","zh":"如果魚皮以特殊方式構成，工程師可能模仿其強度和輕巧。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on unusual structure.","zh":"這個片語集中於不尋常結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"numerous hexagonal plates","meaning":"大量六角形板塊","examples":[{"en":"The fish’s skin contains numerous hexagonal plates.","zh":"這種魚的皮膚含有大量六角形板塊。"},{"en":"Numerous hexagonal plates are many six-sided flat pieces arranged together.","zh":"numerous hexagonal plates 指許多六邊形的平板塊排列在一起。"},{"en":"A honeycomb contains numerous hexagonal cells that use space efficiently.","zh":"蜂巢含有大量六角形小格，能高效利用空間。"},{"en":"If plates are hexagonal, they can fit together closely with little wasted space.","zh":"如果板塊是六角形，它們就能緊密拼合，幾乎不浪費空間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a repeated six-sided structure.","zh":"這個片語描述重複的六邊形結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"bony plates","meaning":"骨質板塊","examples":[{"en":"The boxfish is protected by strong bony plates.","zh":"箱魨受到堅固的骨質板塊保護。"},{"en":"Bony plates are hard protective pieces made of bone-like material.","zh":"bony plates 指由類似骨骼材料構成的堅硬保護片。"},{"en":"Some animals have bony plates that act like natural armour.","zh":"有些動物有骨質板塊，像天然盔甲一樣。"},{"en":"If bony plates are strong but light, they can inspire protective product design.","zh":"如果骨質板塊堅固但輕巧，就能啟發保護性產品設計。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a hard biological shield.","zh":"這個片語指堅硬的生物保護盾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"provide a perfect model for","meaning":"為……提供理想模型","examples":[{"en":"The fish provided a perfect model for lightweight vehicle design.","zh":"這種魚為輕量化車輛設計提供了理想模型。"},{"en":"Provide a perfect model for means offer an excellent example that others can copy or adapt.","zh":"provide a perfect model for 指提供一個極佳例子，讓其他人模仿或改造。"},{"en":"A well-run library can provide a perfect model for organising a study room.","zh":"運作良好的圖書館可以為整理自修室提供理想模型。"},{"en":"If an animal combines strength and lightness, it can guide engineers facing the same challenge.","zh":"如果動物結合強度和輕巧，就能指導面對同樣挑戰的工程師。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one thing serves as an ideal example.","zh":"這個片語顯示某物作為理想例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"maximum strength","meaning":"最大強度","examples":[{"en":"The designers wanted the car to have maximum strength.","zh":"設計師希望汽車具有最大強度。"},{"en":"Maximum strength means the greatest possible ability to resist pressure, force, or damage.","zh":"maximum strength 指抵抗壓力、力量或損壞的最大能力。"},{"en":"A bridge needs maximum strength when it carries heavy trucks every day.","zh":"橋樑每天承載重型貨車時，需要最大強度。"},{"en":"If a structure has maximum strength with little material, it is both safe and efficient.","zh":"如果結構用少量材料達到最大強度，它就既安全又高效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the highest level of durability.","zh":"這個片語描述最高耐用度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"minimal weight","meaning":"最低重量","examples":[{"en":"The car combined maximum strength with minimal weight.","zh":"這款汽車結合最大強度和最低重量。"},{"en":"Minimal weight means the lowest possible weight while still keeping the needed function.","zh":"minimal weight 指在仍保持所需功能下的最低可能重量。"},{"en":"A hiking backpack should have minimal weight so walkers do not tire quickly.","zh":"遠足背包應有最低重量，這樣行山者才不會很快疲倦。"},{"en":"If a vehicle has minimal weight, it may use less fuel to move.","zh":"如果車輛重量最低，移動時可能使用較少燃料。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses lightness without losing usefulness.","zh":"這個片語強調輕巧而不失功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"flock to","meaning":"蜂擁而至；紛紛尋求……","examples":[{"en":"Companies and communities are flocking to biomimicry experts.","zh":"公司和社區正紛紛尋求仿生學專家。"},{"en":"Flock to means go to someone or something in large numbers.","zh":"flock to 指大量前往某人或某事物那裡。"},{"en":"Students may flock to a popular teacher before exams for revision advice.","zh":"考試前，學生可能蜂擁到受歡迎老師那裡尋求溫習建議。"},{"en":"If a new idea seems profitable and sustainable, companies may flock to experts who understand it.","zh":"如果新概念看似有利可圖又可持續，公司可能紛紛尋求理解它的專家。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests strong and widespread interest.","zh":"這個片語暗示強烈而廣泛的興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"landmark book","meaning":"具里程碑意義的著作","examples":[{"en":"Janine Benyus wrote a landmark book about biomimicry.","zh":"Janine Benyus 寫了一本關於仿生學的具里程碑意義著作。"},{"en":"A landmark book is an important book that changes how people understand a subject.","zh":"landmark book 指一本改變人們如何理解某主題的重要著作。"},{"en":"A landmark textbook may introduce a teaching method that schools later adopt widely.","zh":"具里程碑意義的教科書可能介紹一種後來被學校廣泛採用的教學方法。"},{"en":"If a book inspires companies and scientists, it may become influential beyond academic circles.","zh":"如果一本書啟發公司和科學家，它的影響力可能超越學術圈。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses major importance.","zh":"這個片語強調重大重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be inspired by nature","meaning":"受大自然啟發","examples":[{"en":"Her book explores innovation inspired by nature.","zh":"她的書探討受大自然啟發的創新。"},{"en":"Be inspired by nature means get ideas from plants, animals, ecosystems, or natural processes.","zh":"be inspired by nature 指從植物、動物、生態系統或自然過程中獲得想法。"},{"en":"A building can be inspired by nature if its cooling system copies termite mounds.","zh":"如果建築物的冷卻系統模仿白蟻丘，它就是受大自然啟發。"},{"en":"If a design is inspired by nature, it may solve problems in a low-waste way.","zh":"如果設計受大自然啟發，可能以低浪費方式解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase connects creativity with natural models.","zh":"這個片語把創意與自然模型連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cofounder","meaning":"共同創辦人","examples":[{"en":"Janine Benyus is a cofounder of the Biomimicry Guild.","zh":"Janine Benyus 是仿生學協會的共同創辦人。"},{"en":"A cofounder is one of the people who start an organisation, company, or project together.","zh":"cofounder 指共同創立組織、公司或項目的人之一。"},{"en":"A student club may have two cofounders who share planning and leadership duties.","zh":"學生學會可能有兩位共同創辦人，共同負責計劃和領導。"},{"en":"If someone is a cofounder, they helped create the organisation from the beginning.","zh":"如果某人是共同創辦人，他就是從一開始協助建立該組織。"},{"en":"The word shows shared founding responsibility.","zh":"這個詞顯示共同創立責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Biomimicry Guild","meaning":"仿生學協會","examples":[{"en":"The Biomimicry Guild connects scientists with commercial designers.","zh":"仿生學協會把科學家與商業設計師連接起來。"},{"en":"The Biomimicry Guild is an organisation that helps people apply nature-inspired ideas to design and business.","zh":"Biomimicry Guild 是一個幫助人們把受自然啟發的想法應用於設計和商業的組織。"},{"en":"A design team may contact the Biomimicry Guild when it wants to learn from animal movement or plant surfaces.","zh":"當設計團隊想向動物移動或植物表面學習時，可能聯絡仿生學協會。"},{"en":"If scientists and designers are connected, natural research can become practical products more easily.","zh":"如果科學家和設計師被連接起來，自然研究就更容易變成實用產品。"},{"en":"The phrase names an organisation focused on biomimicry.","zh":"這個片語指一個專注於仿生學的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"seat someone at the table with","meaning":"讓某人與……共同參與討論","examples":[{"en":"The organisation seats biologists at the table with company designers.","zh":"該組織讓生物學家與公司設計師共同參與討論。"},{"en":"Seat someone at the table with means include someone in important discussions with another group.","zh":"seat someone at the table with 指讓某人與另一群體一起參與重要討論。"},{"en":"A school may seat students at the table with teachers when discussing new rules.","zh":"學校討論新規則時，可能讓學生與老師共同參與討論。"},{"en":"If biologists join designers early, nature’s lessons can shape products from the start.","zh":"如果生物學家早期加入設計師，大自然的啟示就能從一開始塑造產品。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests real participation, not just later advice.","zh":"這個片語暗示真正參與，而不只是後來提供意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"researchers and designers","meaning":"研究人員和設計師","examples":[{"en":"Biologists collaborate with researchers and designers.","zh":"生物學家與研究人員和設計師合作。"},{"en":"Researchers and designers are people who study problems and people who create practical solutions or products.","zh":"researchers and designers 指研究問題的人，以及創造實際解決方案或產品的人。"},{"en":"Researchers and designers may work together to make school furniture more comfortable.","zh":"研究人員和設計師可能合作，使學校家具更舒適。"},{"en":"If researchers understand nature and designers understand users, their cooperation can produce better products.","zh":"如果研究人員理解大自然，而設計師理解用戶，他們的合作可以產生更好產品。"},{"en":"The phrase joins scientific study with creative application.","zh":"這個片語把科學研究與創意應用連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"their objective is to","meaning":"他們的目標是","examples":[{"en":"Their objective is to match industrial challenges with natural solutions.","zh":"他們的目標是把工業挑戰與自然解決方法配對。"},{"en":"Their objective is to means their goal or purpose is to do something.","zh":"their objective is to 指他們的目標或目的在於做某事。"},{"en":"A school recycling club’s objective is to reduce waste and teach students better habits.","zh":"學校回收學會的目標是減少廢物並教學生更好習慣。"},{"en":"If a project’s objective is clear, people can judge whether it succeeds.","zh":"如果項目目標清楚，人們就能判斷它是否成功。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a planned aim.","zh":"這個片語引出計劃好的目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"marry industrial problems with","meaning":"將工業問題與……結合","examples":[{"en":"The guild marries industrial problems with natural solutions.","zh":"該協會將工業問題與自然解決方法結合。"},{"en":"Marry industrial problems with means connect factory or business challenges with suitable ideas from another source.","zh":"marry industrial problems with 指把工廠或商業挑戰與另一來源中的合適想法連接起來。"},{"en":"A teacher may marry grammar problems with real-life speaking tasks to make lessons useful.","zh":"老師可能將文法問題與真實口語任務結合，使課堂更有用。"},{"en":"If a company has a cooling problem and nature offers a low-energy model, the two can be matched.","zh":"如果公司有冷卻問題，而大自然提供低能源模型，兩者就可以被配對。"},{"en":"The phrase means combine two things so they solve each other.","zh":"這個片語指把兩件事結合起來，讓它們互相解決問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"natural solutions","meaning":"自然界的解決方法","examples":[{"en":"Nature can provide elegant solutions to industrial problems.","zh":"大自然可以為工業問題提供優雅的自然解決方法。"},{"en":"Natural solutions are answers or methods found in nature that can help solve human problems.","zh":"natural solutions 指在大自然中找到、能幫助解決人類問題的答案或方法。"},{"en":"Planting trees is a natural solution to reducing heat in a school playground.","zh":"種樹是減低學校操場熱力的一種自然解決方法。"},{"en":"If natural solutions use fewer chemicals, they may be safer and cheaper over time.","zh":"如果自然解決方法使用較少化學物，長遠可能更安全和更便宜。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to problem-solving ideas from nature.","zh":"這個片語指來自大自然的解難想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ultimately transcend","meaning":"最終超越……","examples":[{"en":"Benyus hopes companies will ultimately transcend simple product design.","zh":"Benyus 希望公司最終超越簡單產品設計。"},{"en":"Ultimately transcend means eventually go beyond a limit or basic level.","zh":"ultimately transcend 指最終超越某個限制或基本層面。"},{"en":"A language course may ultimately transcend exam training and help students communicate confidently.","zh":"語言課程可能最終超越考試訓練，幫助學生有信心地溝通。"},{"en":"If biomimicry goes beyond product shape, it can influence whole business systems.","zh":"如果仿生學超越產品外形，就能影響整個商業系統。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving to a deeper or higher level.","zh":"這個片語描述進入更深或更高層次。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"mere product design","meaning":"單純的產品設計","examples":[{"en":"Biomimicry involves more than mere product design.","zh":"仿生學涉及的範圍超過單純的產品設計。"},{"en":"Mere product design means only designing individual products, without changing wider systems.","zh":"mere product design 指只是設計個別產品，而沒有改變更大系統。"},{"en":"A school improvement plan should be more than mere decoration of classrooms.","zh":"學校改善計劃不應只是單純裝飾課室。"},{"en":"If a company only copies a shell shape, it remains at product design rather than system change.","zh":"如果公司只是模仿貝殼形狀，它就停留在產品設計，而不是系統改變。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests something is too limited if it stops there.","zh":"這個片語暗示如果只停在這一步，就太有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"embrace nature","meaning":"接納大自然的原則","examples":[{"en":"Companies may eventually embrace nature at every level of operation.","zh":"公司最終可能在每個營運層面接納大自然的原則。"},{"en":"Embrace nature means accept and apply nature’s principles seriously.","zh":"embrace nature 指認真接受並應用大自然的原則。"},{"en":"A school may embrace nature by creating outdoor classrooms and reducing waste.","zh":"學校可能透過建立戶外課室和減少浪費來接納大自然的原則。"},{"en":"If businesses embrace nature, they may rethink materials, energy, transport, and waste.","zh":"如果企業接納大自然的原則，就可能重新思考材料、能源、運輸和廢物。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests active acceptance, not casual admiration.","zh":"這個片語暗示主動接受，而不是隨便欣賞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on a holistic level","meaning":"從整體層面","examples":[{"en":"Benyus wants industries to imitate nature on a more holistic level.","zh":"Benyus 希望工業界從更整體的層面模仿大自然。"},{"en":"On a holistic level means considering the whole system, not just separate parts.","zh":"on a holistic level 指考慮整個系統，而不只是分開的部分。"},{"en":"A doctor treats health on a holistic level when they consider sleep, diet, stress, and exercise together.","zh":"醫生同時考慮睡眠、飲食、壓力和運動時，就是從整體層面治療健康。"},{"en":"If industries imitate ecosystems as whole networks, they go beyond copying single shapes.","zh":"如果工業界把生態系統作為整個網絡來模仿，就超越了複製單一形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses whole-system thinking.","zh":"這個片語強調整體系統思維。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"break something into three tiers","meaning":"將某事分成三個層次","examples":[{"en":"Benyus breaks biomimicry into three tiers.","zh":"Benyus 將仿生學分成三個層次。"},{"en":"Break something into three tiers means divide it into three levels or categories.","zh":"break something into three tiers 指把某事分成三個層級或類別。"},{"en":"A teacher may break essay marking into three tiers: content, organisation, and language.","zh":"老師可能將文章評分分成三個層次：內容、組織和語言。"},{"en":"If a topic is complex, dividing it into tiers makes it easier to explain.","zh":"如果主題複雜，把它分成層次會更容易解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes structured classification.","zh":"這個片語描述有結構的分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"three tiers","meaning":"三個層次","examples":[{"en":"The framework consists of three tiers of biomimicry.","zh":"這個框架由仿生學的三個層次組成。"},{"en":"Three tiers are three levels arranged from basic to more advanced or complex.","zh":"three tiers 指由基本到較進階或複雜排列的三個層級。"},{"en":"A school award system may have three tiers: bronze, silver, and gold.","zh":"學校獎勵制度可能有三個層次：銅、銀和金。"},{"en":"If biomimicry has three tiers, learners can understand it step by step.","zh":"如果仿生學有三個層次，學習者就能一步步理解它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a layered structure.","zh":"這個片語描述分層結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on a basic level","meaning":"在基本層面","examples":[{"en":"On a basic level, designers imitate natural shapes.","zh":"在基本層面，設計師模仿自然形狀。"},{"en":"On a basic level means at the simplest or first stage of understanding.","zh":"on a basic level 指在最簡單或最初的理解階段。"},{"en":"On a basic level, good writing needs clear ideas and correct sentences.","zh":"在基本層面，好寫作需要清楚想法和正確句子。"},{"en":"If designers begin by copying shapes, deeper system changes may come later.","zh":"如果設計師先從模仿形狀開始，更深層的系統改變可能之後才出現。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the simplest layer of an idea.","zh":"這個片語引出一個想法的最簡單層面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"albeit complicated","meaning":"雖然複雜","examples":[{"en":"The first level is basic, albeit complicated in practice.","zh":"第一個層次是基本的，雖然實際操作上很複雜。"},{"en":"Albeit complicated means although it is complicated.","zh":"albeit complicated 指雖然它很複雜。"},{"en":"The school plan is simple in theory, albeit complicated when teachers try to timetable it.","zh":"學校計劃在理論上簡單，雖然老師排時間表時很複雜。"},{"en":"If a design idea is basic but difficult to manufacture, it is basic only in concept.","zh":"如果設計概念基本但難以製造，它只是概念上基本。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a contrast in a formal way.","zh":"這個片語以較正式方式引出對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"precise and efficient shapes","meaning":"精確而高效的形狀","examples":[{"en":"Industry can imitate nature’s precise and efficient shapes.","zh":"工業界可以模仿大自然精確而高效的形狀。"},{"en":"Precise and efficient shapes are forms that are accurately structured and perform well with little waste.","zh":"precise and efficient shapes 指結構準確且以少浪費發揮良好功能的形態。"},{"en":"A well-designed spoon has a precise and efficient shape for holding food comfortably.","zh":"設計良好的湯匙有精確而高效的形狀，能舒服地盛載食物。"},{"en":"If natural shapes use material carefully, copying them can improve product design.","zh":"如果自然形狀仔細使用材料，模仿它們可以改善產品設計。"},{"en":"The phrase links accuracy with practical performance.","zh":"這個片語把準確性與實際表現連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"structures and geometries","meaning":"結構和幾何形態","examples":[{"en":"Natural structures and geometries often inspire products.","zh":"自然結構和幾何形態常啟發產品。"},{"en":"Structures and geometries are the arrangements, shapes, and patterns that make something work.","zh":"structures and geometries 指令某物運作的安排、形狀和模式。"},{"en":"Architects study structures and geometries when designing roofs, bridges, and towers.","zh":"建築師設計屋頂、橋樑和塔時會研究結構和幾何形態。"},{"en":"If a natural structure is strong and light, it can guide human engineering.","zh":"如果自然結構堅固又輕巧，它就能指導人類工程。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to both physical build and mathematical form.","zh":"這個片語同時指物理構造和數學形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"microstructure of","meaning":"……的微觀結構","examples":[{"en":"The microstructure of the lotus leaf keeps its surface clean.","zh":"荷葉的微觀結構使其表面保持清潔。"},{"en":"The microstructure of something is its extremely small surface or internal structure.","zh":"microstructure of something 指某物極細小的表面或內部結構。"},{"en":"Scientists study the microstructure of fabric to make clothes more breathable.","zh":"科學家研究布料的微觀結構，以製造更透氣的衣服。"},{"en":"If a surface has tiny bumps, its microstructure may affect how water behaves on it.","zh":"如果表面有微小凸起，其微觀結構可能影響水在上面的行為。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on very small design details.","zh":"這個片語集中於非常細小的設計細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lotus leaf","meaning":"荷葉","examples":[{"en":"The surface of a lotus leaf naturally repels water and dirt.","zh":"荷葉表面自然排斥水和污垢。"},{"en":"A lotus leaf is the broad leaf of the lotus plant, often known for staying clean in muddy water.","zh":"lotus leaf 指荷花植物寬大的葉子，常以在泥水中保持清潔聞名。"},{"en":"Students may observe a lotus leaf to see how water droplets roll off it.","zh":"學生可能觀察荷葉，看看水珠如何從上面滾走。"},{"en":"If a surface behaves like a lotus leaf, it may clean itself when rain falls.","zh":"如果表面像荷葉一樣運作，下雨時可能自行清潔。"},{"en":"The phrase names a natural model for self-cleaning surfaces.","zh":"這個片語指出自潔表面的自然模型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cause raindrops to bead","meaning":"令雨水凝成水珠","examples":[{"en":"The leaf’s microstructure causes raindrops to bead.","zh":"葉子的微觀結構令雨水凝成水珠。"},{"en":"Cause raindrops to bead means make rainwater gather into small round drops instead of spreading flat.","zh":"cause raindrops to bead 指令雨水聚成小圓滴，而不是平鋪開。"},{"en":"Wax on a car can cause raindrops to bead on the surface.","zh":"汽車蠟可以令雨水在車身表面凝成水珠。"},{"en":"If water beads on a surface, it can roll away and carry dirt with it.","zh":"如果水在表面凝成水珠，就能滾走並帶走污垢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes water forming droplets.","zh":"這個片語描述水形成水滴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"run off immediately","meaning":"立即流走","examples":[{"en":"Water droplets run off immediately from the lotus leaf.","zh":"水滴會立即從荷葉上流走。"},{"en":"Run off immediately means flow or roll away at once.","zh":"run off immediately 指立刻流走或滾走。"},{"en":"Rain may run off immediately from a new waterproof jacket.","zh":"雨水可能會立即從新的防水外套上流走。"},{"en":"If water runs off quickly, the surface stays drier and cleaner.","zh":"如果水快速流走，表面就保持較乾和較乾淨。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fast removal of liquid from a surface.","zh":"這個片語描述液體快速離開表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"thereby cleaning and drying","meaning":"從而清潔和弄乾","examples":[{"en":"The droplets roll away, thereby cleaning and drying the surface.","zh":"水滴滾走，從而清潔和弄乾表面。"},{"en":"Thereby cleaning and drying means producing the result of making something clean and dry.","zh":"thereby cleaning and drying 指產生令某物變乾淨和乾爽的結果。"},{"en":"A window coating may make rainwater roll off, thereby cleaning the glass naturally.","zh":"窗戶塗層可能令雨水滾走，從而自然清潔玻璃。"},{"en":"If water carries dust away as it leaves, the surface becomes cleaner without scrubbing.","zh":"如果水離開時帶走灰塵，表面就無需刷洗也變乾淨。"},{"en":"The phrase links an action with its result.","zh":"這個片語把行動與結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"exploit a discovery","meaning":"利用一項發現","examples":[{"en":"A British paint company exploited this discovery commercially.","zh":"一間英國油漆公司把這項發現商業化利用。"},{"en":"Exploit a discovery means use a new finding for practical, commercial, or strategic benefit.","zh":"exploit a discovery 指為實際、商業或策略利益使用一項新發現。"},{"en":"A school may exploit a research discovery by changing how it teaches reading.","zh":"學校可能透過改變閱讀教學方式來利用一項研究發現。"},{"en":"If a company turns a scientific finding into a product, it is exploiting the discovery commercially.","zh":"如果公司把科學發現變成產品，就是在商業上利用該發現。"},{"en":"The phrase can be neutral, but it often suggests active use for gain.","zh":"這個片語可以是中性，但常暗示為利益而主動使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a line of building paints","meaning":"一系列建築塗料","examples":[{"en":"The company developed a line of building paints inspired by lotus leaves.","zh":"該公司開發了一系列受荷葉啟發的建築塗料。"},{"en":"A line of building paints is a series of related paint products used on buildings.","zh":"a line of building paints 指一系列用於建築物的相關油漆產品。"},{"en":"A hardware shop may sell a line of outdoor paints for walls, doors, and fences.","zh":"五金店可能出售一系列戶外塗料，用於牆壁、門和圍欄。"},{"en":"If the paints copy lotus leaves, rain may help keep painted surfaces clean.","zh":"如果塗料模仿荷葉，雨水可能幫助保持塗面清潔。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a product range.","zh":"這個片語描述產品系列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"layered structure","meaning":"分層結構","examples":[{"en":"The layered structure of a butterfly wing creates colour.","zh":"蝴蝶翅膀的分層結構產生顏色。"},{"en":"Layered structure means a form built from several thin layers arranged on top of one another.","zh":"layered structure 指由幾層薄層上下排列而成的形態。"},{"en":"A layered cake has a simple layered structure of cake, cream, and fruit.","zh":"分層蛋糕有蛋糕、忌廉和水果組成的簡單分層結構。"},{"en":"If tiny layers interact with light, they can create colour without pigment.","zh":"如果微小層次與光線互動，就能不用色素也產生顏色。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on stacked arrangement.","zh":"這個片語集中於堆疊排列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"butterfly wing","meaning":"蝴蝶翅膀","examples":[{"en":"A butterfly wing can produce colour without coloured pigments.","zh":"蝴蝶翅膀可以在沒有彩色色素下產生顏色。"},{"en":"A butterfly wing is the delicate wing of a butterfly, often covered with tiny scales.","zh":"butterfly wing 指蝴蝶薄而精細的翅膀，通常覆蓋着微小鱗片。"},{"en":"Under a microscope, a butterfly wing may show structures invisible to the naked eye.","zh":"在顯微鏡下，蝴蝶翅膀可能顯示肉眼看不見的結構。"},{"en":"If its wing structure changes how light reflects, colour can appear without dye.","zh":"如果翅膀結構改變光線反射方式，就能不用染料也出現顏色。"},{"en":"The phrase names a natural example of structural colour.","zh":"這個片語指出結構色的自然例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"peacock plume","meaning":"孔雀羽毛","examples":[{"en":"A peacock plume creates colour by refracting light.","zh":"孔雀羽毛透過折射光線產生顏色。"},{"en":"A peacock plume is a long colourful feather from a peacock’s tail display.","zh":"peacock plume 指孔雀尾部展示用的長而鮮艷的羽毛。"},{"en":"A museum may use a peacock plume to explain how structure can create bright colour.","zh":"博物館可能用孔雀羽毛解釋結構如何產生明亮色彩。"},{"en":"If light bends through tiny structures in the plume, different colours can appear.","zh":"如果光線穿過羽毛中的微小結構而彎曲，就會出現不同顏色。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a natural object famous for shimmering colour.","zh":"這個片語指以閃亮顏色聞名的自然物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"iridescent colour","meaning":"彩虹般變色的色彩","examples":[{"en":"The layered structure creates an iridescent colour.","zh":"分層結構產生彩虹般變色的色彩。"},{"en":"Iridescent colour changes or shines differently depending on the angle of light.","zh":"iridescent colour 指會隨光線角度改變或閃耀不同顏色的色彩。"},{"en":"Soap bubbles show iridescent colour when they reflect purple, green, and blue.","zh":"肥皂泡反射紫色、綠色和藍色時，會顯示彩虹般變色的色彩。"},{"en":"If cosmetics copy iridescent colour, the product may look different under different lighting.","zh":"如果化妝品模仿這種色彩，產品在不同光線下可能看起來不同。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shimmering, colour-shifting effects.","zh":"這個片語描述閃亮而會變色的效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"refract light","meaning":"折射光線","examples":[{"en":"The tiny layers refract light to produce colour.","zh":"微小層次折射光線以產生顏色。"},{"en":"Refract light means bend light as it passes through or between materials.","zh":"refract light 指光線穿過或進入不同材料時發生彎曲。"},{"en":"A glass prism refracts light and separates it into different colours.","zh":"玻璃棱鏡會折射光線，並把光分成不同顏色。"},{"en":"If a surface refracts light in different ways, it can create shimmering colour.","zh":"如果表面以不同方式折射光線，就能產生閃爍色彩。"},{"en":"The phrase belongs to how light changes direction.","zh":"這個片語屬於光線如何改變方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be mimicked by","meaning":"被……模仿","examples":[{"en":"The optical effect is being mimicked by cosmetics companies.","zh":"這種光學效果正被化妝品公司模仿。"},{"en":"Be mimicked by means be copied or imitated by someone or something.","zh":"be mimicked by 指被某人或某物模仿。"},{"en":"A popular teaching method may be mimicked by other schools.","zh":"受歡迎的教學方法可能被其他學校模仿。"},{"en":"If a natural effect is useful, companies may copy it in commercial products.","zh":"如果自然效果有用，公司可能在商業產品中模仿它。"},{"en":"The phrase shows who is copying the model.","zh":"這個片語顯示誰在模仿該模型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cosmetics giant","meaning":"化妝品巨擘","examples":[{"en":"L’Oréal is a global cosmetics giant.","zh":"L’Oréal 是全球化妝品巨擘。"},{"en":"A cosmetics giant is a very large and powerful company in the beauty products industry.","zh":"cosmetics giant 指美容產品行業中非常大型且有影響力的公司。"},{"en":"A cosmetics giant may sell skincare, makeup, shampoo, and perfume around the world.","zh":"化妝品巨擘可能在世界各地銷售護膚品、化妝品、洗髮水和香水。"},{"en":"If a cosmetics giant adopts biomimicry, the idea can reach millions of consumers.","zh":"如果化妝品巨擘採用仿生學，這個想法可以接觸數以百萬計消費者。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses company size and market influence.","zh":"這個片語強調公司規模和市場影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"soon-to-be-released","meaning":"即將推出的","examples":[{"en":"The company developed a soon-to-be-released range of cosmetics.","zh":"該公司開發了一系列即將推出的化妝品。"},{"en":"Soon-to-be-released means planned to become available soon.","zh":"soon-to-be-released 指計劃很快可供使用或購買。"},{"en":"Students may be excited about a soon-to-be-released game after watching its trailer.","zh":"學生看完預告片後，可能對即將推出的遊戲感到興奮。"},{"en":"If a product is soon-to-be-released, marketing may begin before customers can buy it.","zh":"如果產品即將推出，市場推廣可能在顧客能購買前已開始。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something close to launch.","zh":"這個片語描述接近推出的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a line of eye shadow","meaning":"一系列眼影","examples":[{"en":"The company planned a line of eye shadow inspired by natural colours.","zh":"該公司計劃推出一系列受自然色彩啟發的眼影。"},{"en":"A line of eye shadow is a series of related eye-makeup products.","zh":"a line of eye shadow 指一系列相關的眼部化妝產品。"},{"en":"A cosmetics shop may sell a line of eye shadow in earth tones, bright colours, and shimmer finishes.","zh":"化妝品店可能出售一系列大地色、鮮色和閃亮效果的眼影。"},{"en":"If eye shadow copies butterfly wings, it may create colour through light effects.","zh":"如果眼影模仿蝴蝶翅膀，可能透過光學效果產生色彩。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a product range for eye makeup.","zh":"這個片語描述眼妝產品系列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lipstick and nail varnish","meaning":"唇膏和指甲油","examples":[{"en":"The product range included lipstick and nail varnish.","zh":"該產品系列包括唇膏和指甲油。"},{"en":"Lipstick and nail varnish are cosmetics used to colour lips and nails.","zh":"lipstick and nail varnish 指用來為嘴唇和指甲上色的化妝品。"},{"en":"A makeup bag may contain lipstick and nail varnish for formal events.","zh":"化妝袋中可能有唇膏和指甲油，用於正式場合。"},{"en":"If these products copy natural light effects, they may appear to change colour in different angles.","zh":"如果這些產品模仿自然光學效果，它們可能在不同角度下看似變色。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to common beauty products.","zh":"這個片語指常見美容產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the next level of","meaning":"……的下一個層次","examples":[{"en":"The next level of biomimicry imitates natural processes.","zh":"仿生學的下一個層次是模仿自然過程。"},{"en":"The next level of means a more advanced stage than the previous one.","zh":"the next level of 指比前一階段更進階的層次。"},{"en":"After learning basic grammar, the next level of writing is using ideas clearly in paragraphs.","zh":"學會基本文法後，寫作的下一個層次是在段落中清楚使用想法。"},{"en":"If designers move beyond shapes to processes, their work becomes deeper.","zh":"如果設計師從形狀進一步到過程，其工作就變得更深入。"},{"en":"The phrase shows progression from one stage to another.","zh":"這個片語顯示從一個階段進展到另一個階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"imitate natural processes","meaning":"模仿自然過程","examples":[{"en":"Scientists imitate natural processes as well as physical shapes.","zh":"科學家模仿自然過程以及實體形狀。"},{"en":"Imitate natural processes means copy the way living systems make, clean, move, repair, or recycle things.","zh":"imitate natural processes 指模仿生命系統製造、清潔、移動、修復或循環再用物質的方式。"},{"en":"A factory may imitate natural processes by turning waste from one step into material for another.","zh":"工廠可能透過把一個步驟的廢物變成另一個步驟的材料來模仿自然過程。"},{"en":"If engineers copy how shells form in water, they may avoid toxic industrial methods.","zh":"如果工程師模仿貝殼如何在水中形成，就可能避免有毒工業方法。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on copying how nature works, not only how it looks.","zh":"這個片語集中於模仿大自然如何運作，而不只是外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"biochemical recipes","meaning":"生化「配方」","examples":[{"en":"Organisms provide biochemical recipes for useful materials.","zh":"生物為有用材料提供生化「配方」。"},{"en":"Biochemical recipes are natural chemical instructions used by living things to make materials.","zh":"biochemical recipes 指生物用來製造材料的天然化學指令。"},{"en":"A spider’s body follows a biochemical recipe when it makes silk.","zh":"蜘蛛製造蛛絲時，其身體遵循一種生化配方。"},{"en":"If scientists understand a biochemical recipe, they may produce strong materials without harsh chemicals.","zh":"如果科學家理解一種生化配方，就可能不用強烈化學物也能生產堅固材料。"},{"en":"The phrase uses “recipe” to describe natural chemical processes.","zh":"這個片語用「配方」描述天然化學過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"nasal glands of seabirds","meaning":"海鳥的鼻腺","examples":[{"en":"Engineers are studying the nasal glands of seabirds.","zh":"工程師正在研究海鳥的鼻腺。"},{"en":"Nasal glands of seabirds are organs near seabirds’ noses that help remove excess salt.","zh":"nasal glands of seabirds 指海鳥鼻子附近、幫助排出多餘鹽分的器官。"},{"en":"Biology students may study seabird nasal glands to learn how animals survive drinking salty water.","zh":"生物學生可能研究海鳥鼻腺，以了解動物如何靠飲用鹹水生存。"},{"en":"If engineers understand these glands, they may improve methods for removing salt from seawater.","zh":"如果工程師理解這些腺體，就可能改善從海水中除鹽的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase names a natural system useful for desalination ideas.","zh":"這個片語指出對海水化淡有用的自然系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"solve the problem of","meaning":"解決……的問題","examples":[{"en":"Seabird biology may help solve the problem of desalination.","zh":"海鳥生物學可能有助解決海水化淡的問題。"},{"en":"Solve the problem of means find an effective answer to a difficulty.","zh":"solve the problem of 指找到有效答案來處理困難。"},{"en":"A school may solve the problem of late homework by using clearer deadlines and reminders.","zh":"學校可能透過更清楚截止日期和提醒，解決遲交功課的問題。"},{"en":"If nature already removes salt efficiently, engineers can learn from that system.","zh":"如果大自然已能高效除鹽，工程師就能向該系統學習。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a difficulty with a possible solution.","zh":"這個片語把困難與可能解決方法連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"desalination","meaning":"海水化淡","examples":[{"en":"Desalination removes salt from seawater.","zh":"海水化淡會從海水中去除鹽分。"},{"en":"Desalination is the process of taking salt out of seawater to make it usable.","zh":"desalination 指從海水中取出鹽分，使其可供使用的過程。"},{"en":"Dry cities may depend on desalination when rivers and reservoirs cannot supply enough water.","zh":"當河流和水塘不能供應足夠水，乾旱城市可能依賴海水化淡。"},{"en":"If desalination becomes cheaper, coastal communities may gain a more reliable water source.","zh":"如果海水化淡變得更便宜，沿海社區可能獲得更可靠水源。"},{"en":"The word refers to turning salty water into usable water.","zh":"這個詞指把鹹水變成可用水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the abalone’s ability to","meaning":"鮑魚……的能力","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have studied the abalone’s ability to build a strong shell.","zh":"研究人員研究了鮑魚建造堅固外殼的能力。"},{"en":"The abalone’s ability to means the special capacity an abalone has to do something.","zh":"the abalone’s ability to 指鮑魚做某事的特殊能力。"},{"en":"Scientists may study a gecko’s ability to climb walls to design better adhesives.","zh":"科學家可能研究壁虎爬牆的能力，以設計更好的黏合劑。"},{"en":"If abalone shells are strong but made in gentle conditions, they can inspire greener manufacturing.","zh":"如果鮑魚殼堅固但在溫和條件下形成，就能啟發更環保的生產。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on a useful natural skill.","zh":"這個片語集中於有用的自然技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"self-assemble its shell","meaning":"自行組合形成外殼","examples":[{"en":"The abalone can self-assemble its shell in water.","zh":"鮑魚能在水中自行組合形成外殼。"},{"en":"Self-assemble its shell means build its shell through natural processes without external factory-like force.","zh":"self-assemble its shell 指透過自然過程建立外殼，而不需要外部工廠式力量。"},{"en":"Some materials may self-assemble when their tiny parts naturally arrange themselves into a structure.","zh":"有些材料的小粒子自然排列成結構時，就可能自行組合。"},{"en":"If scientists copy self-assembly, they may make strong materials with less heat and pressure.","zh":"如果科學家模仿自組裝，就可能用較少熱力和壓力製造堅固材料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a natural building process.","zh":"這個片語描述自然建造過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"incredibly durable","meaning":"極其耐用的","examples":[{"en":"The abalone produces an incredibly durable shell.","zh":"鮑魚製造出極其耐用的外殼。"},{"en":"Incredibly durable means extremely strong and able to last despite pressure or damage.","zh":"incredibly durable 指極其堅固，並能在壓力或損害下持久使用。"},{"en":"A good school bag should be incredibly durable if students carry heavy books every day.","zh":"如果學生每天背重書包，好的書包應該極其耐用。"},{"en":"If a natural shell is incredibly durable, engineers may study its structure for new materials.","zh":"如果天然外殼極其耐用，工程師可能研究其結構來開發新材料。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses exceptional toughness.","zh":"這個片語強調非凡韌性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"using local ingredients","meaning":"使用本地材料","examples":[{"en":"The shell is created in water using local ingredients.","zh":"外殼在水中使用本地材料形成。"},{"en":"Using local ingredients means making something with materials found nearby.","zh":"using local ingredients 指使用附近找到的材料製作某物。"},{"en":"A restaurant using local ingredients may buy vegetables from nearby farms.","zh":"使用本地材料的餐廳可能向附近農場購買蔬菜。"},{"en":"If production uses local materials, transport costs and environmental impact may fall.","zh":"如果生產使用本地材料，運輸成本和環境影響可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase connects making with nearby resources.","zh":"這個片語把製作與附近資源連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"inspire an alternative to","meaning":"啟發……的替代方法","examples":[{"en":"The process inspired an alternative to toxic manufacturing.","zh":"這個過程啟發了有毒生產的替代方法。"},{"en":"Inspire an alternative to means give people an idea for replacing one method with another.","zh":"inspire an alternative to 指給人一個想法，以另一方法取代原有方法。"},{"en":"Online banking inspired an alternative to waiting in long bank queues.","zh":"網上銀行啟發了排長隊到銀行辦事的替代方法。"},{"en":"If nature makes strong materials without toxins, industry may find a cleaner method.","zh":"如果大自然不用毒素也能製造堅固材料，工業界可能找到更清潔方法。"},{"en":"The phrase connects inspiration with replacement.","zh":"這個片語把啟發與取代連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"conventional manufacturing method","meaning":"傳統生產方法","examples":[{"en":"The new process could replace a conventional manufacturing method.","zh":"這個新過程可以取代傳統生產方法。"},{"en":"A conventional manufacturing method is a traditional or commonly used way of making products.","zh":"conventional manufacturing method 指製造產品的傳統或常用方法。"},{"en":"A factory may use a conventional manufacturing method because workers already know it well.","zh":"工廠可能使用傳統生產方法，因為工人已很熟悉。"},{"en":"If conventional methods use toxic chemicals, cleaner alternatives become attractive.","zh":"如果傳統方法使用有毒化學物，更清潔的替代方法就變得吸引。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts established production with new methods.","zh":"這個片語把既有生產方式與新方法作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"often toxic","meaning":"往往有毒的","examples":[{"en":"Conventional industrial processes are often toxic.","zh":"傳統工業過程往往有毒。"},{"en":"Often toxic means frequently involving poisonous or harmful substances.","zh":"often toxic 指經常涉及有毒或有害物質。"},{"en":"Some old cleaning products were often toxic and dangerous if used without ventilation.","zh":"有些舊清潔產品往往有毒，如果不通風使用會很危險。"},{"en":"If a process is toxic, it can harm workers, water, air, or soil.","zh":"如果過程有毒，就可能傷害工人、水、空氣或土壤。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that harm is common, not rare.","zh":"這個片語提醒傷害常見，而不是罕見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"heat, beat and treat","meaning":"加熱、敲打和處理的生產方式","examples":[{"en":"Some conventional manufacturing relies on a “heat, beat and treat” method.","zh":"有些傳統生產依賴「加熱、敲打和處理」的方法。"},{"en":"Heat, beat and treat refers to industrial methods that use high heat, force, and chemical treatment.","zh":"heat, beat and treat 指使用高熱、力量和化學處理的工業方法。"},{"en":"Making metal parts may involve heating the material, pressing it into shape, and treating the surface.","zh":"製作金屬零件可能涉及加熱材料、壓成形狀和處理表面。"},{"en":"If manufacturing depends on high heat and chemicals, it may use more energy and create more pollution.","zh":"如果生產依賴高熱和化學物，就可能使用更多能源並造成更多污染。"},{"en":"The phrase summarises a harsh industrial approach.","zh":"這個片語概括一種強力而粗暴的工業方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"deal with harmful bacteria","meaning":"應付有害細菌","examples":[{"en":"Researchers study how organisms deal with harmful bacteria.","zh":"研究人員研究生物如何應付有害細菌。"},{"en":"Deal with harmful bacteria means control, avoid, kill, or reduce dangerous bacteria.","zh":"deal with harmful bacteria 指控制、避免、殺死或減少危險細菌。"},{"en":"Hospitals deal with harmful bacteria by cleaning surfaces and washing hands carefully.","zh":"醫院透過清潔表面和仔細洗手來應付有害細菌。"},{"en":"If seaweed can stop bacteria naturally, its method may inspire safer coatings.","zh":"如果海藻能自然阻止細菌，其方法可能啟發更安全塗層。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on managing biological threats.","zh":"這個片語集中於處理生物威脅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be instructive","meaning":"具啟發性的","examples":[{"en":"Natural methods of controlling bacteria can be instructive.","zh":"控制細菌的自然方法可以具啟發性。"},{"en":"Be instructive means teach people something useful or help them understand a method.","zh":"be instructive 指教人有用東西或幫助人理解方法。"},{"en":"A student’s mistake can be instructive if the teacher explains why it happened.","zh":"如果老師解釋錯誤如何發生，學生的錯誤可以具啟發性。"},{"en":"If nature solves a problem cleanly, studying it can guide human design.","zh":"如果大自然乾淨地解決問題，研究它可以指導人類設計。"},{"en":"The phrase means useful as a lesson.","zh":"這個片語指作為教訓有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"teem with microbes","meaning":"充滿微生物","examples":[{"en":"The seaweed lives in water that teems with microbes.","zh":"這種海藻生活在充滿微生物的水中。"},{"en":"Teem with microbes means be full of tiny living organisms such as bacteria.","zh":"teem with microbes 指充滿細菌等微小生物。"},{"en":"A damp kitchen sponge can teem with microbes if it is not cleaned regularly.","zh":"如果不定期清潔，潮濕廚房海綿可以充滿微生物。"},{"en":"If seawater teems with microbes, seaweed needs a way to stay clean.","zh":"如果海水充滿微生物，海藻就需要方法保持清潔。"},{"en":"The phrase describes very high biological abundance.","zh":"這個片語描述極高的生物數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"figure out how","meaning":"弄清楚如何……","examples":[{"en":"Researchers tried to figure out how the seaweed stayed clean.","zh":"研究人員嘗試弄清楚海藻如何保持清潔。"},{"en":"Figure out how means discover or understand the method by which something happens.","zh":"figure out how 指發現或理解某事發生的方法。"},{"en":"A student may figure out how to solve a maths problem after seeing one clear example.","zh":"學生看過一個清楚例子後，可能弄清楚如何解數學題。"},{"en":"If scientists figure out how an organism resists bacteria, they can copy the method.","zh":"如果科學家弄清楚生物如何抵抗細菌，就能模仿該方法。"},{"en":"The phrase means work out the process.","zh":"這個片語指找出過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"keep free of","meaning":"避免受到……影響","examples":[{"en":"The seaweed keeps free of harmful bacterial colonies.","zh":"這種海藻避免受到有害細菌群落影響。"},{"en":"Keep free of means remain without something unwanted or harmful.","zh":"keep free of 指保持沒有某種不想要或有害的東西。"},{"en":"A school kitchen must keep food free of dirt and insects.","zh":"學校廚房必須保持食物沒有污垢和昆蟲。"},{"en":"If seaweed keeps free of bacteria without poison, its strategy may be useful to humans.","zh":"如果海藻不用毒物也能避免細菌，其策略可能對人類有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes staying clean or unaffected.","zh":"這個片語描述保持清潔或不受影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bacterial colonies","meaning":"細菌群落","examples":[{"en":"Biofilms are dense bacterial colonies.","zh":"生物膜是密集的細菌群落。"},{"en":"Bacterial colonies are groups of bacteria growing together.","zh":"bacterial colonies 指一起生長的細菌群體。"},{"en":"Bacterial colonies can form on unwashed dishes, teeth, or damp surfaces.","zh":"細菌群落可以在未洗的碗碟、牙齒或潮濕表面形成。"},{"en":"If bacteria gather into colonies, they may become harder to remove.","zh":"如果細菌聚集成群落，就可能更難清除。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised groups of bacteria.","zh":"這個片語描述有組織的細菌群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be called biofilms","meaning":"被稱為生物膜","examples":[{"en":"These bacterial colonies are called biofilms.","zh":"這些細菌群落被稱為生物膜。"},{"en":"Be called biofilms means be known by the scientific name biofilms.","zh":"be called biofilms 指以 biofilms 這個科學名稱為人所知。"},{"en":"The sticky layer on teeth can be called plaque, a kind of biofilm.","zh":"牙齒上的黏性層可被稱為牙菌斑，是一種生物膜。"},{"en":"If bacteria stick together on a surface, scientists may call the structure a biofilm.","zh":"如果細菌黏在表面並聚集，科學家可能稱該結構為生物膜。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a technical name.","zh":"這個片語引入技術名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cause plaque","meaning":"導致牙菌斑","examples":[{"en":"Biofilms can cause plaque on teeth.","zh":"生物膜可以導致牙齒上的牙菌斑。"},{"en":"Cause plaque means lead to a sticky layer of bacteria forming on teeth.","zh":"cause plaque 指導致牙齒上形成黏性的細菌層。"},{"en":"Poor brushing habits can cause plaque to build up near the gums.","zh":"刷牙習慣差可能導致牙肉附近積聚牙菌斑。"},{"en":"If plaque is not removed, it can lead to bad breath and tooth problems.","zh":"如果牙菌斑沒有被清除，可能導致口臭和牙齒問題。"},{"en":"The phrase connects bacterial growth with dental health.","zh":"這個片語把細菌生長與牙齒健康連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"clog up","meaning":"堵塞","examples":[{"en":"Bacterial growth can clog up a bathroom drain.","zh":"細菌生長可以堵塞浴室去水渠。"},{"en":"Clog up means block a passage so that water, air, or movement cannot flow easily.","zh":"clog up 指堵住通道，使水、空氣或移動不能順暢流通。"},{"en":"Hair can clog up a shower drain if it is not removed.","zh":"如果不清除頭髮，它可以堵塞淋浴去水渠。"},{"en":"If bacteria and dirt build up inside a pipe, water may drain more slowly.","zh":"如果細菌和污垢在水管內積聚，水可能排得更慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes blockage.","zh":"這個片語描述阻塞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bathroom drain","meaning":"浴室去水渠","examples":[{"en":"Biofilms sometimes form inside a bathroom drain.","zh":"生物膜有時在浴室去水渠內形成。"},{"en":"A bathroom drain is the pipe or opening that carries water away from a sink, bath, or shower.","zh":"bathroom drain 指把洗手盆、浴缸或淋浴間的水排走的水管或開口。"},{"en":"A bathroom drain may smell bad if hair, soap, and bacteria collect inside it.","zh":"如果頭髮、肥皂和細菌積聚在內，浴室去水渠可能發出臭味。"},{"en":"If microbes grow inside the drain, they can form sticky layers that are hard to clean.","zh":"如果微生物在去水渠內生長，就能形成難清潔的黏性層。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a common household water outlet.","zh":"這個片語指常見的家居排水口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"determine that","meaning":"確定","examples":[{"en":"The researchers determined that the seaweed uses natural chemicals.","zh":"研究人員確定這種海藻使用天然化學物。"},{"en":"Determine that means discover or conclude something after investigation.","zh":"determine that 指經調查後發現或得出結論。"},{"en":"A doctor may determine that a fever is caused by an infection after tests.","zh":"醫生可能在檢查後確定發燒由感染引起。"},{"en":"If researchers determine the cause of an effect, they can explain the process more clearly.","zh":"如果研究人員確定某效果的原因，就能更清楚解釋過程。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a research finding.","zh":"這個片語引出研究發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"natural chemicals","meaning":"天然化學物","examples":[{"en":"The seaweed produces natural chemicals called furanones.","zh":"這種海藻產生名為呋喃酮的天然化學物。"},{"en":"Natural chemicals are chemical substances made by living things or found in nature.","zh":"natural chemicals 指由生物製造或存在於自然界的化學物質。"},{"en":"Plants produce natural chemicals that attract insects or defend against being eaten.","zh":"植物產生天然化學物來吸引昆蟲或防止被吃掉。"},{"en":"If a natural chemical blocks bacteria, it may inspire safer cleaning products.","zh":"如果天然化學物能阻止細菌，就可能啟發更安全清潔產品。"},{"en":"The phrase does not mean automatically safe; it means naturally occurring.","zh":"這個片語不代表自動安全，而是指自然存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"furanones","meaning":"呋喃酮","examples":[{"en":"Furanones interfere with communication between bacteria.","zh":"呋喃酮會干擾細菌之間的溝通。"},{"en":"Furanones are natural chemical compounds that can affect how bacteria signal to one another.","zh":"furanones 指能影響細菌如何互相發訊號的天然化學化合物。"},{"en":"Scientists may study furanones to design surfaces that resist bacterial build-up.","zh":"科學家可能研究呋喃酮，以設計抗細菌積聚的表面。"},{"en":"If furanones stop bacteria from organising, they may prevent harmful colonies from forming.","zh":"如果呋喃酮阻止細菌組織起來，就可能防止有害群落形成。"},{"en":"The word names a chemical group with anti-biofilm potential.","zh":"這個詞指出一類具抗生物膜潛力的化學物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"jam a signalling system","meaning":"干擾訊號系統","examples":[{"en":"Furanones jam the bacteria’s signalling system.","zh":"呋喃酮會干擾細菌的訊號系統。"},{"en":"Jam a signalling system means block or disrupt the way messages are sent.","zh":"jam a signalling system 指阻塞或擾亂訊息傳遞方式。"},{"en":"Poor Wi-Fi can jam communication between a computer and an online classroom.","zh":"差劣 Wi-Fi 可以干擾電腦與網上課室之間的溝通。"},{"en":"If bacteria cannot exchange signals, they may fail to gather into colonies.","zh":"如果細菌不能交換訊號，就可能無法聚集成群落。"},{"en":"The phrase describes interference with communication.","zh":"這個片語描述對溝通的干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"cell-to-cell signalling","meaning":"細胞之間的訊號傳遞","examples":[{"en":"Bacteria rely on cell-to-cell signalling to organise themselves.","zh":"細菌依賴細胞之間的訊號傳遞來組織自己。"},{"en":"Cell-to-cell signalling is communication between individual cells.","zh":"cell-to-cell signalling 指個別細胞之間的溝通。"},{"en":"Human body cells use cell-to-cell signalling to coordinate growth and repair.","zh":"人體細胞使用細胞之間的訊號傳遞來協調生長和修復。"},{"en":"If bacterial signalling is blocked, bacteria may not know when to gather together.","zh":"如果細菌訊號被阻斷，細菌可能不知道何時聚集。"},{"en":"The phrase describes communication at the cellular level.","zh":"這個片語描述細胞層面的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"allow bacteria to communicate","meaning":"讓細菌互相溝通","examples":[{"en":"The signalling system allows bacteria to communicate.","zh":"這個訊號系統讓細菌互相溝通。"},{"en":"Allow bacteria to communicate means make it possible for bacteria to send signals to one another.","zh":"allow bacteria to communicate 指使細菌能互相發送訊號。"},{"en":"A classroom discussion platform allows students to communicate after lessons.","zh":"課堂討論平台讓學生在課後互相溝通。"},{"en":"If bacteria communicate successfully, they can coordinate group behaviour.","zh":"如果細菌成功溝通，就能協調群體行為。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what a signalling system does.","zh":"這個片語解釋訊號系統的功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"gather together","meaning":"聚集在一起","examples":[{"en":"Bacteria communicate before they gather together in colonies.","zh":"細菌在聚集成群落之前會互相溝通。"},{"en":"Gather together means come together into a group.","zh":"gather together 指聚成一個群體。"},{"en":"Students gather together in the hall before the school assembly begins.","zh":"學生在早會開始前聚集在禮堂。"},{"en":"If bacteria gather together on a surface, they may form a biofilm.","zh":"如果細菌在表面聚集在一起，就可能形成生物膜。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement from separate individuals to a group.","zh":"這個片語描述從分散個體變成群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the most sophisticated application","meaning":"最先進的應用","examples":[{"en":"The third level is the most sophisticated application of biomimicry.","zh":"第三個層次是仿生學最先進的應用。"},{"en":"The most sophisticated application means the most advanced, complex, and developed use of an idea.","zh":"the most sophisticated application 指一個概念最先進、複雜和成熟的用途。"},{"en":"A school’s most sophisticated use of technology may combine data, feedback, and personalised learning.","zh":"學校對科技最先進的應用可能結合數據、回饋和個人化學習。"},{"en":"If biomimicry changes whole industrial systems, it is more advanced than copying one shape.","zh":"如果仿生學改變整個工業系統，就比模仿單一形狀更進階。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the highest level of application.","zh":"這個片語標示最高應用層次。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"According to Benyus, companies should operate like organisms.","zh":"根據 Benyus 的說法，公司應該像生物一樣運作。"},{"en":"According to means based on what a person, source, or evidence says.","zh":"according to 指根據某人、某來源或某證據所說。"},{"en":"According to the timetable, the last bus leaves at ten thirty.","zh":"根據時間表，尾班巴士十點半開出。"},{"en":"If a statement begins with according to, the writer is showing where the idea comes from.","zh":"如果一句話以 according to 開頭，作者就是顯示想法來自哪裡。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of information.","zh":"這個片語指出資訊來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"see oneself as","meaning":"將自己視為……","examples":[{"en":"A company can see itself as an organism in an ecosystem.","zh":"公司可以將自己視為生態系統中的生物。"},{"en":"See oneself as means understand or imagine one’s identity in a particular way.","zh":"see oneself as 指以某種方式理解或想像自己的身份。"},{"en":"A teacher may see herself as a guide rather than a source of answers only.","zh":"老師可能將自己視為引導者，而不只是答案來源。"},{"en":"If a company sees itself as part of an ecosystem, it may care more about relationships and waste flows.","zh":"如果公司將自己視為生態系統的一部分，就可能更重視關係和廢物流動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes self-identity or self-perception.","zh":"這個片語描述自我身份或自我看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"economic ecosystem","meaning":"經濟生態系統","examples":[{"en":"Companies operate within a complex economic ecosystem.","zh":"公司在複雜的經濟生態系統內運作。"},{"en":"An economic ecosystem is a network of businesses, customers, suppliers, workers, and resources that affect one another.","zh":"economic ecosystem 指互相影響的企業、顧客、供應商、工人和資源網絡。"},{"en":"A local market is an economic ecosystem where shops, delivery workers, customers, and suppliers depend on each other.","zh":"本地街市是一個經濟生態系統，商店、送貨員、顧客和供應商互相依賴。"},{"en":"If one part of the ecosystem fails, other businesses may also be affected.","zh":"如果生態系統中某一部分失效，其他企業也可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase applies ecological thinking to business.","zh":"這個片語把生態思維應用於商業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make thrifty use of","meaning":"節約使用……","examples":[{"en":"An efficient company makes thrifty use of limited resources.","zh":"高效公司會節約使用有限資源。"},{"en":"Make thrifty use of means use something carefully and economically, without waste.","zh":"make thrifty use of 指小心而節省地使用某物，不浪費。"},{"en":"A family makes thrifty use of leftovers when it turns them into lunch the next day.","zh":"家庭把剩菜變成第二天午餐時，就是節約使用剩餘食物。"},{"en":"If companies use resources thriftily, they lower costs and reduce waste.","zh":"如果公司節約使用資源，就能降低成本和減少浪費。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses careful and economical use.","zh":"這個片語強調小心和節省的使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"limited resources","meaning":"有限資源","examples":[{"en":"Natural ecosystems make effective use of limited resources.","zh":"自然生態系統有效使用有限資源。"},{"en":"Limited resources are supplies such as time, money, energy, materials, or water that are not unlimited.","zh":"limited resources 指時間、金錢、能源、材料或水等並非無限的供應。"},{"en":"A school with limited resources must choose carefully how to spend its budget.","zh":"資源有限的學校必須小心選擇如何使用預算。"},{"en":"If resources are limited, waste becomes more costly.","zh":"如果資源有限，浪費就變得更昂貴。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses scarcity and careful use.","zh":"這個片語強調稀缺和謹慎使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"symbiotic relationships","meaning":"共生關係","examples":[{"en":"Industries can create symbiotic relationships with one another.","zh":"工業企業可以彼此建立共生關係。"},{"en":"Symbiotic relationships are relationships in which different parties live or work together and benefit from each other.","zh":"symbiotic relationships 指不同一方共同生活或合作，並從彼此身上受益的關係。"},{"en":"A school and a library can have a symbiotic relationship if students use the library and the library gains visitors.","zh":"如果學生使用圖書館，而圖書館獲得訪客，學校和圖書館就可以有共生關係。"},{"en":"If one factory’s waste becomes another factory’s raw material, both sides benefit.","zh":"如果一間工廠的廢物成為另一間工廠的原材料，雙方都受益。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mutual support.","zh":"這個片語描述互相支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"boardroom approach","meaning":"董事會層面的管理方式","examples":[{"en":"This boardroom approach treats companies as parts of an ecosystem.","zh":"這種董事會層面的管理方式把公司視為生態系統的一部分。"},{"en":"A boardroom approach is a way of thinking used in high-level company decision-making.","zh":"boardroom approach 指用於公司高層決策的思考方式。"},{"en":"A boardroom approach to sustainability may ask how waste, suppliers, and profits connect.","zh":"董事會層面的可持續管理方式可能會問廢物、供應商和利潤如何連接。"},{"en":"If executives think like ecologists, they may redesign whole business systems.","zh":"如果高層管理人員像生態學家般思考，可能重新設計整個商業系統。"},{"en":"The phrase brings ecological ideas into corporate management.","zh":"這個片語把生態想法帶入企業管理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"at this level","meaning":"在這個層次","examples":[{"en":"At this level, industries examine their complete systems of production.","zh":"在這個層次，工業界檢視其完整生產系統。"},{"en":"At this level means at this stage or degree of complexity.","zh":"at this level 指在這個階段或複雜程度。"},{"en":"At this level, students should not only know words but also use them in writing.","zh":"在這個層次，學生不應只知道詞語，還要能在寫作中使用它們。"},{"en":"If biomimicry reaches this level, companies study whole systems rather than single products.","zh":"如果仿生學達到這個層次，公司就會研究整個系統，而不是單一產品。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a particular stage in a framework.","zh":"這個片語標示框架中的某一階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"any given company","meaning":"任何一間特定公司","examples":[{"en":"Any given company can be imagined as part of a natural ecosystem.","zh":"任何一間特定公司都可以被想像成自然生態系統的一部分。"},{"en":"Any given company means any particular company chosen as an example.","zh":"any given company 指任何被選作例子的特定公司。"},{"en":"Any given school has its own timetable, students, teachers, and problems.","zh":"任何一間特定學校都有自己的時間表、學生、老師和問題。"},{"en":"If any given company depends on suppliers and customers, it is not isolated.","zh":"如果任何一間公司都依賴供應商和顧客，它就不是孤立的。"},{"en":"The phrase means “whichever company we choose to look at”.","zh":"這個片語意思是「我們選來看的任何一間公司」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"collection of industries","meaning":"一組工業企業","examples":[{"en":"A collection of industries can operate like a forest ecosystem.","zh":"一組工業企業可以像森林生態系統一樣運作。"},{"en":"A collection of industries is a group of different businesses or industrial sectors working in related ways.","zh":"collection of industries 指一組以相關方式運作的不同企業或工業部門。"},{"en":"A port area may contain a collection of industries such as shipping, storage, food processing, and repair.","zh":"港口地區可能包含航運、倉儲、食品加工和維修等一組工業企業。"},{"en":"If industries exchange materials and energy, they may function like connected organisms.","zh":"如果工業企業交換材料和能源，就可能像相連的生物般運作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a group, not a single company.","zh":"這個片語描述一個群體，而不是單一公司。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"food web","meaning":"食物網","examples":[{"en":"An industrial network can be designed like a natural food web.","zh":"工業網絡可以被設計成像自然食物網一樣。"},{"en":"A food web is a network of feeding relationships in which energy and materials pass between organisms.","zh":"food web 指能量和物質在生物之間傳遞的覓食關係網絡。"},{"en":"In a pond food web, algae feed small animals, and small animals feed fish.","zh":"在池塘食物網中，藻類餵養小動物，小動物再餵養魚。"},{"en":"If factories imitate a food web, one company’s waste can feed another process.","zh":"如果工廠模仿食物網，一間公司的廢物可以供應另一個過程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes connected flows of resources.","zh":"這個片語描述資源流動的連接網絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"manufacturing inputs and outputs","meaning":"生產投入和產出","examples":[{"en":"A company’s food web consists of manufacturing inputs and outputs.","zh":"公司的食物網由生產投入和產出組成。"},{"en":"Manufacturing inputs and outputs are the materials, energy, and resources entering production and the products or waste leaving it.","zh":"manufacturing inputs and outputs 指進入生產的材料、能源和資源，以及離開生產的產品或廢物。"},{"en":"A bakery’s inputs include flour and electricity, while its outputs include bread and food waste.","zh":"麵包店的投入包括麵粉和電力，而產出包括麵包和食物廢料。"},{"en":"If companies track inputs and outputs, they can find waste that another business may use.","zh":"如果公司追蹤投入和產出，就能找到另一企業可使用的廢物。"},{"en":"The phrase helps analyse production as a system.","zh":"這個片語幫助把生產分析為一個系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"waste products","meaning":"廢料","examples":[{"en":"Waste products from one factory may be useful to another.","zh":"一間工廠的廢料可能對另一間工廠有用。"},{"en":"Waste products are unwanted materials left over after a process.","zh":"waste products 指某過程後剩下的不需要材料。"},{"en":"Vegetable peels are waste products in a kitchen, but they can become compost.","zh":"菜皮是廚房中的廢料，但可以變成堆肥。"},{"en":"If waste products are reused, less material goes to landfill.","zh":"如果廢料被重用，送到堆填區的材料就較少。"},{"en":"The phrase does not always mean useless rubbish.","zh":"這個片語不一定指無用垃圾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"manufacturing process","meaning":"生產工序","examples":[{"en":"One manufacturing process can supply materials to another.","zh":"一個生產工序可以為另一個工序供應材料。"},{"en":"A manufacturing process is a series of steps used to make a product.","zh":"manufacturing process 指用來製造產品的一連串步驟。"},{"en":"The manufacturing process for bread includes mixing, rising, baking, and cooling.","zh":"麵包的生產工序包括攪拌、發酵、烘焙和冷卻。"},{"en":"If one process creates useful leftovers, another process can use them as materials.","zh":"如果一個工序產生有用剩餘物，另一個工序可以把它們用作材料。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on production steps.","zh":"這個片語集中於生產步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be used as an ingredient","meaning":"被用作原料","examples":[{"en":"Industrial waste can be used as an ingredient in another process.","zh":"工業廢料可以被用作另一個過程中的原料。"},{"en":"Be used as an ingredient means be included as a material in making something else.","zh":"be used as an ingredient 指被包括作為製作另一事物的材料。"},{"en":"Leftover rice can be used as an ingredient in fried rice.","zh":"剩飯可以被用作炒飯的原料。"},{"en":"If waste gas becomes an ingredient in plastic, pollution may be turned into value.","zh":"如果廢氣成為塑膠原料，污染可能被轉化為價值。"},{"en":"The phrase shows one material becoming part of a new product.","zh":"這個片語顯示一種材料成為新產品的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"industrial activity","meaning":"工業活動","examples":[{"en":"One company’s waste may support another industrial activity.","zh":"一間公司的廢料可能支持另一項工業活動。"},{"en":"Industrial activity means work related to manufacturing, processing, production, or heavy business operations.","zh":"industrial activity 指與製造、加工、生產或大型商業運作有關的工作。"},{"en":"A port city may have industrial activity such as ship repair, storage, and food processing.","zh":"港口城市可能有修船、倉儲和食品加工等工業活動。"},{"en":"If industrial activity is planned poorly, it may create pollution and waste.","zh":"如果工業活動規劃不善，可能產生污染和廢物。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to production-related economic activity.","zh":"這個片語指與生產相關的經濟活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"biodegradable plastic","meaning":"可生物降解塑膠","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have developed a biodegradable plastic from waste gas.","zh":"科學家已從廢氣開發出可生物降解塑膠。"},{"en":"Biodegradable plastic is plastic that can be broken down by living organisms under suitable conditions.","zh":"biodegradable plastic 指能在合適條件下被生物分解的塑膠。"},{"en":"A café may use biodegradable plastic cups to reduce long-lasting waste.","zh":"咖啡店可能使用可生物降解塑膠杯，以減少長期廢物。"},{"en":"If biodegradable plastic breaks down properly, it may cause less lasting pollution than ordinary plastic.","zh":"如果可生物降解塑膠能適當分解，它可能比普通塑膠造成較少持久污染。"},{"en":"The phrase describes plastic designed to decompose.","zh":"這個片語描述設計來分解的塑膠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be synthesised from","meaning":"由……合成","examples":[{"en":"The plastic is synthesised from carbon dioxide and limonene.","zh":"這種塑膠由二氧化碳和檸檬烯合成。"},{"en":"Be synthesised from means be chemically made from particular starting materials.","zh":"be synthesised from 指由特定起始材料經化學方法製成。"},{"en":"Some medicines are synthesised from simple chemicals in a laboratory.","zh":"有些藥物在實驗室中由簡單化學物合成。"},{"en":"If plastic is synthesised from waste gas, a pollutant can become a useful material.","zh":"如果塑膠由廢氣合成，污染物就能變成有用材料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes chemical production from source ingredients.","zh":"這個片語描述由來源原料進行化學生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"carbon dioxide","meaning":"二氧化碳","examples":[{"en":"A cement factory can supply waste carbon dioxide for plastic production.","zh":"水泥廠可以供應廢棄二氧化碳作塑膠生產。"},{"en":"Carbon dioxide is a gas produced by breathing, burning fuel, and many industrial processes.","zh":"carbon dioxide 指由呼吸、燃燒燃料和許多工業過程產生的氣體。"},{"en":"Plants use carbon dioxide during photosynthesis to make food.","zh":"植物在光合作用中使用二氧化碳來製造食物。"},{"en":"If factories capture carbon dioxide instead of releasing it, emissions may be reduced.","zh":"如果工廠收集二氧化碳而不是排放它，排放量可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major greenhouse gas.","zh":"這個片語指出一種主要溫室氣體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"limonene","meaning":"檸檬烯","examples":[{"en":"Limonene is an important component of citrus oil.","zh":"檸檬烯是柑橘油的重要成分。"},{"en":"Limonene is a natural chemical found in citrus fruit peels, often giving a lemon-like smell.","zh":"limonene 指存在於柑橘果皮中的天然化學物，常帶有檸檬般氣味。"},{"en":"Cleaning products may contain limonene because it has a fresh citrus scent.","zh":"清潔產品可能含有檸檬烯，因為它有清新的柑橘香味。"},{"en":"If limonene can be used in plastics, fruit waste may become a useful chemical source.","zh":"如果檸檬烯可用於塑膠，水果廢料可能變成有用化學來源。"},{"en":"The word names a plant-based compound.","zh":"這個詞指植物來源化合物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a major component in","meaning":"……的主要成分","examples":[{"en":"Limonene is a major component in the oil from citrus rind.","zh":"檸檬烯是柑橘果皮油中的主要成分。"},{"en":"A major component in something is one of its main parts or ingredients.","zh":"a major component in something 指某物中的主要部分或原料之一。"},{"en":"Water is a major component in soup, even if vegetables and meat give it flavour.","zh":"水是湯的主要成分，即使蔬菜和肉類帶來味道。"},{"en":"If limonene is a major component of citrus oil, citrus peel can be a useful source.","zh":"如果檸檬烯是柑橘油的主要成分，柑橘皮就可以是有用來源。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies an important part of a mixture.","zh":"這個片語指出混合物中的重要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be extracted from","meaning":"從……提取","examples":[{"en":"The oil is extracted from citrus rind.","zh":"這種油從柑橘果皮中提取。"},{"en":"Be extracted from means be removed or obtained from a source material.","zh":"be extracted from 指從來源材料中取出或獲得。"},{"en":"Olive oil is extracted from olives by pressing them.","zh":"橄欖油透過壓榨橄欖提取。"},{"en":"If useful chemicals are extracted from waste fruit peels, waste can become valuable.","zh":"如果有用化學物從廢棄果皮中提取，廢物就能變得有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes obtaining something from a source.","zh":"這個片語描述從來源取得某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"citrus rind","meaning":"柑橘果皮","examples":[{"en":"Limonene can be obtained from citrus rind.","zh":"檸檬烯可以從柑橘果皮中取得。"},{"en":"Citrus rind is the outer peel of fruits such as oranges, lemons, and limes.","zh":"citrus rind 指橙、檸檬和青檸等水果的外層果皮。"},{"en":"A cook may grate citrus rind into a cake to add a fresh smell.","zh":"廚師可能把柑橘果皮磨碎加入蛋糕，以增加清新氣味。"},{"en":"If citrus rind is reused, food waste can become a source of useful chemicals.","zh":"如果柑橘果皮被重用，食物廢料就能成為有用化學物的來源。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the outer skin of citrus fruit.","zh":"這個片語指柑橘水果的外皮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"work with","meaning":"與……合作","examples":[{"en":"The chemist is working with a cement factory.","zh":"這位化學家正與一間水泥廠合作。"},{"en":"Work with means cooperate with another person, group, or organisation.","zh":"work with 指與另一個人、群體或組織合作。"},{"en":"A teacher may work with parents to support a student who lacks confidence.","zh":"老師可能與家長合作，支援缺乏信心的學生。"},{"en":"If scientists work with factories, research ideas can be tested in real industrial settings.","zh":"如果科學家與工廠合作，研究想法就能在真實工業環境中測試。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses collaboration.","zh":"這個片語強調合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"cement factory","meaning":"水泥廠","examples":[{"en":"A cement factory produces carbon dioxide as waste.","zh":"水泥廠產生二氧化碳作為廢氣。"},{"en":"A cement factory is a factory that makes cement for construction.","zh":"cement factory 指製造建築用水泥的工廠。"},{"en":"A cement factory may supply materials used to build roads, bridges, and buildings.","zh":"水泥廠可能供應用於建造道路、橋樑和建築物的材料。"},{"en":"If a cement factory releases waste gas, capturing it could reduce pollution.","zh":"如果水泥廠排放廢氣，收集它可以減少污染。"},{"en":"The phrase names an industrial site linked to construction materials.","zh":"這個片語指出與建築材料有關的工業地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"trap waste carbon dioxide","meaning":"收集廢棄二氧化碳","examples":[{"en":"The project aims to trap waste carbon dioxide from the factory.","zh":"該項目旨在從工廠收集廢棄二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Trap waste carbon dioxide means capture carbon dioxide before it escapes into the air.","zh":"trap waste carbon dioxide 指在二氧化碳逃逸到空氣前把它收集起來。"},{"en":"A factory may trap waste gas and store it instead of releasing it through a chimney.","zh":"工廠可能收集廢氣並儲存，而不是透過煙囪排放。"},{"en":"If waste carbon dioxide is trapped, it can sometimes be reused in another product.","zh":"如果廢棄二氧化碳被收集，有時可以在另一產品中重用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes capturing a pollutant.","zh":"這個片語描述捕集污染物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"use it as an ingredient","meaning":"將它用作原料","examples":[{"en":"The captured gas can be used as an ingredient in plastic.","zh":"捕集到的氣體可以被用作塑膠中的原料。"},{"en":"Use it as an ingredient means include it as one material in making a new product.","zh":"use it as an ingredient 指把它作為製造新產品的一種材料。"},{"en":"A cook can use leftover vegetables as an ingredient in soup.","zh":"廚師可以將剩餘蔬菜用作湯的原料。"},{"en":"If captured carbon dioxide becomes an ingredient, waste is turned into a resource.","zh":"如果捕集到的二氧化碳成為原料，廢物就被轉化成資源。"},{"en":"The phrase shows reuse in production.","zh":"這個片語顯示生產中的重用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"global network","meaning":"全球網絡","examples":[{"en":"ZERI is a global network of scientists and entrepreneurs.","zh":"ZERI 是一個由科學家和企業家組成的全球網絡。"},{"en":"A global network is a connected group of people or organisations spread across the world.","zh":"global network 指分布於世界各地、互相連接的人或組織群體。"},{"en":"A global network of schools may share lesson materials and student projects online.","zh":"全球學校網絡可能在網上分享教材和學生項目。"},{"en":"If experts form a global network, successful ideas can travel quickly between countries.","zh":"如果專家組成全球網絡，成功想法就能快速在國家之間傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses worldwide connection.","zh":"這個片語強調全球連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"scientists, entrepreneurs and educators","meaning":"科學家、企業家和教育工作者","examples":[{"en":"The organisation connects scientists, entrepreneurs and educators.","zh":"該組織連接科學家、企業家和教育工作者。"},{"en":"Scientists, entrepreneurs and educators are researchers, business builders, and teaching professionals.","zh":"scientists, entrepreneurs and educators 指研究人員、創業者和教學專業人士。"},{"en":"A sustainability project may need scientists, entrepreneurs and educators to develop ideas, fund them, and teach communities.","zh":"可持續項目可能需要科學家、企業家和教育工作者來發展想法、提供資金並教育社區。"},{"en":"If these groups cooperate, research can become practical and widely understood.","zh":"如果這些群體合作，研究就能變得實用並被廣泛理解。"},{"en":"The phrase brings together knowledge, business, and education.","zh":"這個片語集合知識、商業和教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"initiate a project","meaning":"開展項目","examples":[{"en":"ZERI has initiated several eco-industrial projects.","zh":"ZERI 已開展幾個生態工業項目。"},{"en":"Initiate a project means formally start or launch a planned activity.","zh":"initiate a project 指正式開始或推出一項有計劃的活動。"},{"en":"A school may initiate a recycling project after students notice too much plastic waste.","zh":"學生注意到太多塑膠廢物後，學校可能開展回收項目。"},{"en":"If an organisation initiates a project, it usually provides direction, people, or resources.","zh":"如果組織開展項目，通常會提供方向、人手或資源。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on beginning an organised effort.","zh":"這個片語集中於開始有組織的努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"eco-industrial projects","meaning":"生態工業項目","examples":[{"en":"Eco-industrial projects turn waste into useful raw materials.","zh":"生態工業項目把廢物轉化為有用原材料。"},{"en":"Eco-industrial projects are industrial plans designed to reduce waste and imitate ecological cycles.","zh":"eco-industrial projects 指旨在減少廢物並模仿生態循環的工業計劃。"},{"en":"An eco-industrial project may connect a brewery, bakery, and mushroom farm through shared waste materials.","zh":"生態工業項目可能透過共享廢料，把釀酒廠、麵包店和蘑菇農場連接起來。"},{"en":"If industries reuse one another’s waste, pollution and raw-material costs can fall.","zh":"如果工業企業重用彼此的廢物，污染和原材料成本可以下降。"},{"en":"The phrase combines ecology with industrial production.","zh":"這個片語結合生態與工業生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"attempt to find ways to","meaning":"嘗試尋找方法去……","examples":[{"en":"The projects attempt to find ways to reuse all waste.","zh":"這些項目嘗試尋找方法去重用所有廢物。"},{"en":"Attempt to find ways to means try to discover practical methods for doing something.","zh":"attempt to find ways to 指嘗試發現做某事的實用方法。"},{"en":"Teachers may attempt to find ways to help quiet students speak more confidently.","zh":"老師可能嘗試尋找方法去幫助安靜學生更有信心地說話。"},{"en":"If waste is difficult to reuse, projects may need experiments and partnerships.","zh":"如果廢物難以重用，項目可能需要實驗和合作夥伴。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses effort toward practical solutions.","zh":"這個片語強調朝實際解決方案努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reuse all waste","meaning":"重用所有廢料","examples":[{"en":"ZERI aims to reuse all waste as raw materials.","zh":"ZERI 旨在把所有廢料作為原材料重用。"},{"en":"Reuse all waste means find a new purpose for every leftover material instead of throwing it away.","zh":"reuse all waste 指為每種剩餘材料找到新用途，而不是丟棄。"},{"en":"A kitchen may reuse food waste as compost for a school garden.","zh":"廚房可能把廚餘作為學校花園的堆肥重用。"},{"en":"If all waste is reused, factories reduce pollution and buy fewer new materials.","zh":"如果所有廢料都被重用，工廠就減少污染並購買較少新材料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a zero-waste goal.","zh":"這個片語描述零廢物目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"raw materials","meaning":"原材料","examples":[{"en":"One industry’s waste can become another industry’s raw materials.","zh":"一個工業的廢料可以成為另一個工業的原材料。"},{"en":"Raw materials are basic materials used to make products.","zh":"raw materials 指用來製造產品的基本材料。"},{"en":"Flour is a raw material for bread, and cotton is a raw material for shirts.","zh":"麵粉是麵包的原材料，棉花是恤衫的原材料。"},{"en":"If waste becomes raw material, the economy becomes more circular.","zh":"如果廢物變成原材料，經濟就變得更循環。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the starting materials of production.","zh":"這個片語指生產的起始材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a growing number of projects","meaning":"越來越多的項目","examples":[{"en":"A growing number of projects are applying ZERI principles.","zh":"越來越多的項目正在應用 ZERI 原則。"},{"en":"A growing number of projects means more and more projects over time.","zh":"a growing number of projects 指隨時間有越來越多項目。"},{"en":"A growing number of schools are using tablets for homework and reading.","zh":"越來越多學校使用平板電腦做功課和閱讀。"},{"en":"If more projects adopt the same principles, the idea is spreading.","zh":"如果更多項目採用同一原則，這個想法正在擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase describes increasing adoption.","zh":"這個片語描述採用數量增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"apply ZERI principles","meaning":"應用 ZERI 原則","examples":[{"en":"The Canadian project applies ZERI principles to brewing waste.","zh":"這個加拿大項目把 ZERI 原則應用於釀酒廢料。"},{"en":"Apply ZERI principles means use the idea that waste from one process should become useful material for another.","zh":"apply ZERI principles 指使用一個過程的廢物應成為另一過程有用材料的理念。"},{"en":"A school can apply similar principles by turning food waste into garden compost.","zh":"學校可以透過把廚餘變成花園堆肥來應用類似原則。"},{"en":"If a brewery’s leftover grain feeds another business, ZERI thinking is being used.","zh":"如果釀酒廠剩餘穀物供應另一企業，就是在使用 ZERI 思維。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a practical project with zero-waste principles.","zh":"這個片語把實際項目與零廢物原則連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"spent grains","meaning":"釀酒後剩餘的穀物","examples":[{"en":"The brewery reuses spent grains from beer production.","zh":"釀酒廠重用啤酒生產中釀酒後剩餘的穀物。"},{"en":"Spent grains are leftover grains after brewing has removed what is needed for beer.","zh":"spent grains 指釀酒提取所需成分後剩下的穀物。"},{"en":"A bakery may use spent grains from a brewery to add flavour and fibre to bread.","zh":"麵包店可能使用釀酒廠的剩餘穀物，為麵包增加味道和纖維。"},{"en":"If spent grains are thrown away, useful nutrients are wasted.","zh":"如果釀酒後剩餘的穀物被丟棄，有用養分就被浪費。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a brewing by-product.","zh":"這個片語指釀酒副產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a by-product of","meaning":"……的副產品","examples":[{"en":"Spent grain is a by-product of the beer-making process.","zh":"剩餘穀物是啤酒釀製過程的副產品。"},{"en":"A by-product of something is a secondary material or result produced during a main process.","zh":"a by-product of something 指主要過程中產生的次要材料或結果。"},{"en":"Heat can be a by-product of running large computer servers.","zh":"熱力可以是大型電腦伺服器運作的副產品。"},{"en":"If by-products are reused, companies can reduce waste and sometimes earn extra income.","zh":"如果副產品被重用，公司可以減少廢物，有時還能增加收入。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something produced indirectly.","zh":"這個片語描述間接產生的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"beer-making process","meaning":"啤酒釀製過程","examples":[{"en":"The beer-making process produces large quantities of spent grain.","zh":"啤酒釀製過程產生大量剩餘穀物。"},{"en":"The beer-making process is the series of steps used to produce beer from ingredients such as grain, water, and yeast.","zh":"beer-making process 指用穀物、水和酵母等原料製造啤酒的一連串步驟。"},{"en":"A brewery tour may show visitors the beer-making process from grain to bottle.","zh":"釀酒廠導賞可能向訪客展示從穀物到瓶裝的啤酒釀製過程。"},{"en":"If the process creates leftover grain, that waste can be redirected to food production.","zh":"如果該過程產生剩餘穀物，該廢料可以轉用於食品生產。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to brewing steps.","zh":"這個片語指釀酒步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"make bread and grow mushrooms","meaning":"製作麵包和種植蘑菇","examples":[{"en":"The project uses spent grain to make bread and grow mushrooms.","zh":"該項目使用剩餘穀物製作麵包和種植蘑菇。"},{"en":"Make bread and grow mushrooms means turn leftover grain into food products or mushroom-growing material.","zh":"make bread and grow mushrooms 指把剩餘穀物轉化為食品或蘑菇種植材料。"},{"en":"A community kitchen might use brewery waste to make bread and grow mushrooms for local markets.","zh":"社區廚房可能使用釀酒廢料，為本地市場製作麵包和種植蘑菇。"},{"en":"If one waste material supports two food uses, less of it goes to landfill.","zh":"如果一種廢料支持兩種食物用途，送往堆填區的廢料就更少。"},{"en":"The phrase shows practical reuse of agricultural waste.","zh":"這個片語顯示農業廢料的實際重用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"continue to adopt","meaning":"繼續採用……","examples":[{"en":"Industries continue to adopt models found in nature.","zh":"工業界繼續採用大自然中的模式。"},{"en":"Continue to adopt means keep choosing and using something over time.","zh":"continue to adopt 指隨時間繼續選擇和使用某事物。"},{"en":"Schools continue to adopt online tools when they help students learn more clearly.","zh":"當網上工具幫助學生更清楚學習時，學校會繼續採用它們。"},{"en":"If nature-inspired designs save money, companies may keep using them.","zh":"如果受自然啟發的設計節省金錢，公司可能會繼續使用。"},{"en":"The phrase shows ongoing acceptance.","zh":"這個片語顯示持續接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"nature’s models","meaning":"大自然的模式","examples":[{"en":"Nature’s models can guide complete production systems.","zh":"大自然的模式可以指導完整生產系統。"},{"en":"Nature’s models are examples from natural organisms, processes, or ecosystems that humans can learn from.","zh":"nature’s models 指人類可以學習的自然生物、過程或生態系統例子。"},{"en":"A bird’s wing is one of nature’s models for flight.","zh":"鳥翼是大自然中關於飛行的其中一個模式。"},{"en":"If companies follow nature’s models, waste can become food for another process.","zh":"如果公司遵循大自然的模式，廢物就可以成為另一過程的食物。"},{"en":"The phrase treats nature as a source of practical examples.","zh":"這個片語把大自然視為實際例子的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"entire manufacturing processes","meaning":"整套生產過程","examples":[{"en":"Entire manufacturing processes could eventually operate locally.","zh":"整套生產過程最終可以在本地運作。"},{"en":"Entire manufacturing processes are complete production systems from raw materials to finished products.","zh":"entire manufacturing processes 指從原材料到成品的完整生產系統。"},{"en":"A company may redesign its entire manufacturing process to reduce waste at every step.","zh":"公司可能重新設計整套生產過程，以在每個步驟減少浪費。"},{"en":"If the whole process operates locally, transport needs and supply delays may fall.","zh":"如果整個過程在本地運作，運輸需求和供應延誤可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the full production chain.","zh":"這個片語集中於完整生產鏈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"operate locally","meaning":"在本地運作","examples":[{"en":"Future factories may operate locally with nearby materials.","zh":"未來工廠可能使用附近材料在本地運作。"},{"en":"Operate locally means work within a local area using nearby resources, workers, or markets.","zh":"operate locally 指在本地區域內使用附近資源、工人或市場運作。"},{"en":"A bakery operates locally when it buys flour nearby and sells bread to the neighbourhood.","zh":"麵包店在附近購買麵粉並把麵包賣給社區時，就是在本地運作。"},{"en":"If production operates locally, communities may reduce transport costs and emissions.","zh":"如果生產在本地運作，社區可能減少運輸成本和排放。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses local production and local supply.","zh":"這個片語強調本地生產和本地供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"local ingredients","meaning":"本地原料","examples":[{"en":"Biomimetic factories can rely on local ingredients.","zh":"仿生工廠可以依賴本地原料。"},{"en":"Local ingredients are materials found or produced near the place where they are used.","zh":"local ingredients 指在使用地附近找到或生產的材料。"},{"en":"A school canteen may use local ingredients from nearby farms.","zh":"學校飯堂可能使用附近農場的本地原料。"},{"en":"If factories use local ingredients, they may reduce transport and support local economies.","zh":"如果工廠使用本地原料，可能減少運輸並支持本地經濟。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to nearby materials used in production or cooking.","zh":"這個片語指生產或烹飪中使用的附近材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"liquefied beach sand","meaning":"液化的沙灘沙粒","examples":[{"en":"Some factories use liquefied beach sand to manufacture glass.","zh":"有些工廠使用液化的沙灘沙粒來製造玻璃。"},{"en":"Liquefied beach sand is sand that has been melted into a liquid-like state by high heat.","zh":"liquefied beach sand 指被高熱熔化成近似液體狀態的沙。"},{"en":"Glassmakers heat sand until it melts before shaping it into bottles or windows.","zh":"玻璃製造商先把沙加熱至熔化，再塑造成瓶子或窗戶。"},{"en":"If sand is liquefied, it can be formed into clear and hard glass products.","zh":"如果沙被液化，就可以形成透明而堅硬的玻璃產品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sand transformed by heat.","zh":"這個片語描述被熱力轉化的沙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"make windshields","meaning":"製造擋風玻璃","examples":[{"en":"Liquefied sand can be used to make windshields.","zh":"液化沙可以用來製造擋風玻璃。"},{"en":"Make windshields means produce the front glass screens used in vehicles.","zh":"make windshields 指製造車輛前方使用的玻璃屏。"},{"en":"A car factory needs strong clear glass to make windshields safely.","zh":"汽車工廠需要堅固透明玻璃來安全製造擋風玻璃。"},{"en":"If a windshield is made well, it protects drivers while allowing them to see the road.","zh":"如果擋風玻璃製作良好，就能保護司機，同時讓他們看見道路。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to manufacturing vehicle glass.","zh":"這個片語指製造車用玻璃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"embrace biomimicry","meaning":"接納仿生學","examples":[{"en":"More scientists and engineers are beginning to embrace biomimicry.","zh":"越來越多科學家和工程師開始接納仿生學。"},{"en":"Embrace biomimicry means accept and actively use nature-inspired design principles.","zh":"embrace biomimicry 指接受並主動使用受自然啟發的設計原則。"},{"en":"A design school may embrace biomimicry by asking students to study plants and animals before designing products.","zh":"設計學校可能要求學生先研究植物和動物再設計產品，從而接納仿生學。"},{"en":"If engineers embrace biomimicry, they may create cleaner and more efficient systems.","zh":"如果工程師接納仿生學，就可能創造更清潔和更高效的系統。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests serious acceptance, not just curiosity.","zh":"這個片語暗示認真接受，而不只是好奇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"natural organisms","meaning":"自然生物","examples":[{"en":"Natural organisms provide models for sustainable technology.","zh":"自然生物為可持續科技提供模型。"},{"en":"Natural organisms are living things found in nature, such as plants, animals, fungi, and microbes.","zh":"natural organisms 指自然界中的生物，例如植物、動物、真菌和微生物。"},{"en":"A biology class may study natural organisms in a pond to understand food webs.","zh":"生物課可能研究池塘中的自然生物，以理解食物網。"},{"en":"If natural organisms solve problems efficiently, designers can learn from their structures and processes.","zh":"如果自然生物高效解決問題，設計師可以向其結構和過程學習。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to living examples from nature.","zh":"這個片語指來自大自然的生命例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"come to be regarded as","meaning":"逐漸被視為……","examples":[{"en":"Natural organisms may come to be regarded as mentors.","zh":"自然生物可能逐漸被視為導師。"},{"en":"Come to be regarded as means gradually begin to be seen or treated in a particular way.","zh":"come to be regarded as 指逐漸開始被看作或對待為某種身份。"},{"en":"A quiet student may come to be regarded as a leader after helping classmates consistently.","zh":"安靜學生如果持續幫助同學，可能逐漸被視為領袖。"},{"en":"If engineers repeatedly learn from organisms, nature may gradually be seen as a teacher.","zh":"如果工程師反覆向生物學習，大自然可能逐漸被視為老師。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change in how something is viewed.","zh":"這個片語描述看法上的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be regarded as mentors","meaning":"被視為導師","examples":[{"en":"Scientists may regard natural organisms as mentors.","zh":"科學家可能把自然生物視為導師。"},{"en":"Be regarded as mentors means be seen as teachers or guides.","zh":"be regarded as mentors 指被視為老師或引導者。"},{"en":"Older students may be regarded as mentors when they help younger students adjust to school.","zh":"當高年級學生幫助低年級學生適應學校時，他們可能被視為導師。"},{"en":"If organisms teach engineers better design, they are treated like mentors.","zh":"如果生物教會工程師更好的設計，牠們就被當作導師。"},{"en":"The phrase gives nature an educational role.","zh":"這個片語賦予大自然教育角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be deemed masterful","meaning":"被視為極高明的","examples":[{"en":"Natural processes may be deemed masterful by engineers.","zh":"自然過程可能被工程師視為極高明。"},{"en":"Be deemed masterful means be judged to be extremely skilful, effective, or impressive.","zh":"be deemed masterful 指被判斷為極有技巧、高效或令人讚嘆。"},{"en":"A simple lesson can be deemed masterful if every student finally understands a difficult idea.","zh":"如果簡單一課令每位學生終於明白困難概念，它可以被視為極高明。"},{"en":"If nature creates strong materials without waste, engineers may admire the process deeply.","zh":"如果大自然不浪費也能創造堅固材料，工程師可能深深佩服該過程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes high praise and expert judgement.","zh":"這個片語描述高度讚賞和專家判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"gain popularity","meaning":"日益受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Switchback railways quickly gained popularity in America.","zh":"折返式鐵路很快在美國日益受歡迎。"},{"en":"Gain popularity means become more liked, used, or accepted by many people.","zh":"gain popularity 指變得更受很多人喜愛、使用或接受。"},{"en":"A new study app may gain popularity if students find it simple and useful.","zh":"如果學生覺得新的學習應用程式簡單又有用，它可能日益受歡迎。"},{"en":"If an idea solves a real problem, it can gain popularity very quickly.","zh":"如果一個想法解決真實問題，就可以很快受歡迎。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rising public interest or acceptance.","zh":"這個片語描述公眾興趣或接受度上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"diminish the importance of","meaning":"削弱……的重要性","examples":[{"en":"The economic crisis diminished the importance of amusement parks.","zh":"經濟危機削弱了遊樂園的重要性。"},{"en":"Diminish the importance of means make something seem less important or less central.","zh":"diminish the importance of 指令某事看起來較不重要或不再居於核心位置。"},{"en":"Online maps diminished the importance of paper street directories.","zh":"網上地圖削弱了紙本街道指南的重要性。"},{"en":"If people have less money, entertainment businesses may become less important than daily necessities.","zh":"如果人們金錢較少，娛樂業可能變得不如日常必需品重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a reduction in perceived importance.","zh":"這個片語描述被認為重要的程度下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"worldwide","meaning":"在全球範圍內","examples":[{"en":"The final statement refers to the importance of American roller coasters worldwide.","zh":"最後一句陳述提到美國過山車在全球範圍內的重要性。"},{"en":"Worldwide means across the whole world or in many countries.","zh":"worldwide 指遍及全世界或許多國家。"},{"en":"A song can become popular worldwide if people share it online in many languages.","zh":"如果人們用多種語言在網上分享，一首歌可以在全球範圍內流行。"},{"en":"If a technology spreads worldwide, it affects markets and habits far beyond its place of origin.","zh":"如果一項科技在全球範圍內擴散，它就會影響遠超其起源地的市場和習慣。"},{"en":"The word stresses global reach.","zh":"這個詞強調全球影響範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 153 - Inspired by Mimicking Mother Nature.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 154":[{"front":"memory and age","meaning":"記憶與年齡","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines how memory and other mental abilities change with age.","zh":"文章探討記憶和其他心智能力如何隨年齡改變。"},{"en":"Memory and age refers to the relationship between getting older and changes in remembering, thinking, and learning.","zh":"「memory and age」指年紀增長與記憶、思考和學習變化之間的關係。"},{"en":"A student may interview grandparents to learn how memory and age affect daily routines.","zh":"學生可能訪問祖父母，了解記憶與年齡如何影響日常習慣。"},{"en":"If memory changes with age, people may use notes, calendars, or repeated practice to help themselves.","zh":"如果記憶隨年齡改變，人們可能使用筆記、日曆或重複練習來幫助自己。"},{"en":"The phrase does not mean all memory disappears with age; different kinds of memory may change differently.","zh":"這個短語並不表示所有記憶都會隨年齡消失；不同種類的記憶可能有不同變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ongoing maturation process","meaning":"持續的成熟過程","examples":[{"en":"Aging is part of an ongoing maturation process.","zh":"老化是持續成熟過程的一部分。"},{"en":"An ongoing maturation process is a continuing process of growth, development, and change.","zh":"「ongoing maturation process」是持續成長、發展和改變的過程。"},{"en":"A child’s language ability develops through an ongoing maturation process, not in one sudden step.","zh":"孩子的語言能力是透過持續成熟過程發展，而不是一步突然完成。"},{"en":"If maturation continues over time, the body and mind keep adapting at different stages of life.","zh":"如果成熟過程持續進行，身體和心智會在人生不同階段繼續適應。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests ageing is a natural process, not just decline.","zh":"這個短語暗示老化是自然過程，而不只是衰退。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"go through","meaning":"經歷","examples":[{"en":"All our organs go through a process of maturation and aging.","zh":"我們所有器官都會經歷成熟和老化的過程。"},{"en":"To go through a process means to experience it from beginning to end or over time.","zh":"「go through」一個過程，意思是由開始到結束或在一段時間內經歷它。"},{"en":"Students go through a period of adjustment when they move to a new school.","zh":"學生轉到新學校時，會經歷一段適應期。"},{"en":"If people go through stress for too long, their sleep and mood may be affected.","zh":"如果人們長時間經歷壓力，睡眠和心情可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase often describes changes, difficulties, or stages that someone or something experiences.","zh":"這個短語常描述某人或某物經歷的變化、困難或階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in a sense","meaning":"在某程度上","examples":[{"en":"In a sense, aging reflects the condition of both body and mind.","zh":"在某程度上，老化反映身體和心智的狀態。"},{"en":"In a sense means from one point of view, although the statement may not be completely true in every way.","zh":"「in a sense」意思是從某一角度來看，雖然該說法未必在所有方面完全成立。"},{"en":"In a sense, exams measure preparation as much as intelligence.","zh":"在某程度上，考試衡量準備程度，也衡量智力。"},{"en":"If a person exercises and keeps learning, ageing may reflect both physical and mental habits.","zh":"如果一個人運動並持續學習，老化可能反映身體和心智習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when making a careful, qualified statement.","zh":"這個短語適合用於謹慎、有保留的說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be keyed to","meaning":"取決於；與……密切相關","examples":[{"en":"Aging is keyed to the level of vigor of the body.","zh":"老化取決於身體的活力水平。"},{"en":"To be keyed to something means to be closely connected with or dependent on it.","zh":"「be keyed to」某事，意思是與它密切相關或取決於它。"},{"en":"A revision plan should be keyed to the student’s exam date and weak topics.","zh":"溫習計劃應與學生的考試日期和薄弱題目密切相關。"},{"en":"If mental energy is keyed to physical health, poor sleep may make thinking slower.","zh":"如果腦力與身體健康密切相關，睡眠不足可能令思考變慢。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that one thing is strongly linked to another factor.","zh":"這個短語顯示一件事與另一因素有強烈關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"level of vigor","meaning":"活力水平","examples":[{"en":"The aging process is related to the body’s level of vigor.","zh":"老化過程與身體的活力水平有關。"},{"en":"Level of vigor means the amount of physical energy, strength, and liveliness someone has.","zh":"「level of vigor」意思是某人擁有的體力、力量和活躍程度。"},{"en":"A person’s level of vigor may improve after regular exercise and better sleep.","zh":"一個人定期運動並改善睡眠後，活力水平可能提升。"},{"en":"If the body’s vigor decreases, daily tasks may feel more tiring.","zh":"如果身體活力下降，日常任務可能變得更疲累。"},{"en":"The phrase describes general physical vitality rather than one single skill.","zh":"這個短語描述整體身體生命力，而不是單一技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"continuous interaction between","meaning":"……之間的持續互動","examples":[{"en":"Aging involves a continuous interaction between physical and mental activity.","zh":"老化涉及身體活動與腦力活動之間的持續互動。"},{"en":"A continuous interaction between two things means they keep affecting each other over time.","zh":"「continuous interaction between」兩件事，意思是它們隨時間不斷互相影響。"},{"en":"There is a continuous interaction between a teacher’s feedback and a student’s improvement.","zh":"老師回饋與學生進步之間存在持續互動。"},{"en":"If physical activity affects mood and mood affects activity, the two form an ongoing cycle.","zh":"如果身體活動影響心情，而心情又影響活動，兩者就形成持續循環。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a two-way relationship, not a one-way cause.","zh":"這個短語描述雙向關係，而不是單向原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"levels of body activity","meaning":"身體活動水平","examples":[{"en":"Levels of body activity may affect mental aging.","zh":"身體活動水平可能影響心智老化。"},{"en":"Levels of body activity are the amounts of movement, exercise, and physical effort in daily life.","zh":"「levels of body activity」是日常生活中的移動、運動和體力活動量。"},{"en":"A person with high body activity may walk, garden, climb stairs, and exercise regularly.","zh":"身體活動水平高的人可能經常步行、園藝、爬樓梯和運動。"},{"en":"If body activity is very low, energy, sleep, and mood may gradually decline.","zh":"如果身體活動水平很低，精力、睡眠和心情可能逐漸下降。"},{"en":"The phrase measures how physically active a person is.","zh":"這個短語衡量一個人身體活動有多活躍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"levels of mental activity","meaning":"腦力活動水平","examples":[{"en":"Mental activity may influence how the brain ages.","zh":"腦力活動可能影響大腦如何老化。"},{"en":"Levels of mental activity are the amounts of thinking, learning, problem-solving, and concentration a person uses.","zh":"「levels of mental activity」是一個人使用思考、學習、解難和專注的程度。"},{"en":"Reading, playing chess, learning languages, and solving puzzles can raise mental activity.","zh":"閱讀、下棋、學語言和解謎可以提高腦力活動水平。"},{"en":"If people keep using their minds, the brain may adapt and stay more flexible.","zh":"如果人們持續使用心智，大腦可能適應並保持更有彈性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how actively the mind is being used.","zh":"這個短語描述心智被使用得有多活躍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"academic title","meaning":"學術職銜","examples":[{"en":"Scheibel’s academic title reflects his work across several fields.","zh":"Scheibel 的學術職銜反映他橫跨幾個領域的工作。"},{"en":"An academic title is an official university position or rank, such as professor or lecturer.","zh":"「academic title」是大學中的正式職位或級別，例如教授或講師。"},{"en":"A professor’s academic title may show their department and area of expertise.","zh":"教授的學術職銜可能顯示其學系和專業範疇。"},{"en":"If someone has titles in several fields, their research may connect different subjects.","zh":"如果某人在幾個領域都有職銜，其研究可能連接不同科目。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a person’s formal role in education or research.","zh":"這個短語指出人在教育或研究中的正式角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"far-flung domains","meaning":"以往相距甚遠的領域","examples":[{"en":"Once far-flung domains now contribute to brain research.","zh":"以往相距甚遠的領域現在也為腦部研究作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Far-flung domains are fields or areas that once seemed distant, separate, or unrelated.","zh":"「far-flung domains」是曾經看似遙遠、分離或不相關的領域。"},{"en":"Art, computing, and medicine may seem far-flung, but they can work together in medical design.","zh":"藝術、電腦和醫學可能看似相距甚遠，但它們可以在醫療設計中合作。"},{"en":"If distant fields begin to connect, researchers may solve problems in new ways.","zh":"如果遙遠領域開始連接，研究人員可能以新方式解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights subjects that used to feel far apart.","zh":"這個短語突出以往感覺分隔很遠的學科。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"converge on","meaning":"匯聚於；共同研究……","examples":[{"en":"Several academic fields now converge on the study of the mind and brain.","zh":"幾個學術領域現在匯聚於心智與大腦研究。"},{"en":"To converge on something means to come together and focus on the same point or subject.","zh":"「converge on」某事，意思是聚集起來並集中於同一點或題目。"},{"en":"Teachers, parents, and counsellors may converge on one plan to help a struggling student.","zh":"老師、家長和輔導員可能共同制定一個計劃來幫助有困難的學生。"},{"en":"If many fields converge on a problem, the solution may become richer and more complete.","zh":"如果許多領域共同研究一個問題，解決方案可能更豐富和完整。"},{"en":"The phrase describes different paths coming together toward one focus.","zh":"這個短語描述不同路徑朝同一焦點匯合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"professor of anatomy","meaning":"解剖學教授","examples":[{"en":"Scheibel is a professor of anatomy and several related subjects.","zh":"Scheibel 是解剖學及幾個相關科目的教授。"},{"en":"A professor of anatomy is a university scholar who teaches and studies the structure of the body.","zh":"「professor of anatomy」是在大學教授和研究身體結構的學者。"},{"en":"Medical students learn from professors of anatomy when studying organs, nerves, and muscles.","zh":"醫科學生研究器官、神經和肌肉時，會向解剖學教授學習。"},{"en":"If a brain researcher understands anatomy, they can connect mental functions with physical structures.","zh":"如果腦研究者理解解剖學，他可以把心智能力與身體結構連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase names an academic expert in body structure.","zh":"這個短語指出身體結構方面的學術專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cell biology","meaning":"細胞生物學","examples":[{"en":"Cell biology contributes to the study of the brain.","zh":"細胞生物學有助腦部研究。"},{"en":"Cell biology is the study of cells, their structures, and how they work.","zh":"「cell biology」是研究細胞、其結構以及如何運作的學科。"},{"en":"Students study cell biology when learning about cell membranes, nuclei, and energy production.","zh":"學生學習細胞膜、細胞核和能量生產時，就是在學細胞生物學。"},{"en":"If scientists understand cells, they can better understand how brain tissue changes with age.","zh":"如果科學家理解細胞，他們可以更了解腦組織如何隨年齡改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a biological field focused on life’s basic units.","zh":"這個短語描述專注於生命基本單位的生物學領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"psychiatry","meaning":"精神醫學","examples":[{"en":"Scheibel’s work includes psychiatry and behavioral sciences.","zh":"Scheibel 的工作包括精神醫學和行為科學。"},{"en":"Psychiatry is the medical field that studies and treats mental illness.","zh":"「psychiatry」是研究和治療精神疾病的醫學領域。"},{"en":"A person with serious depression may see a doctor trained in psychiatry.","zh":"有嚴重抑鬱的人可能會看受過精神醫學訓練的醫生。"},{"en":"If brain changes affect mood and memory, psychiatry can help connect biology with behaviour.","zh":"如果腦部變化影響心情和記憶，精神醫學可以幫助連接生物學與行為。"},{"en":"The phrase names a medical field concerned with mental health.","zh":"這個短語指出關注心理健康的醫學領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"behavioral sciences","meaning":"行為科學","examples":[{"en":"Behavioral sciences examine human and animal behaviour.","zh":"行為科學研究人類和動物行為。"},{"en":"Behavioral sciences are fields that study how people and animals act, learn, and respond.","zh":"「behavioral sciences」是研究人和動物如何行動、學習和反應的領域。"},{"en":"Psychology and sociology are often part of the behavioral sciences.","zh":"心理學和社會學常屬於行為科學。"},{"en":"If researchers study behaviour, they can see how memory affects real choices and habits.","zh":"如果研究人員研究行為，他們可以看到記憶如何影響真實選擇和習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes scientific study of actions and responses.","zh":"這個短語描述對行動和反應的科學研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Brain Research Institute","meaning":"腦科學研究所","examples":[{"en":"Scheibel directs the university’s Brain Research Institute.","zh":"Scheibel 主持該大學的腦科學研究所。"},{"en":"A Brain Research Institute is a centre where scientists study the brain, mind, and nervous system.","zh":"「Brain Research Institute」是科學家研究大腦、心智和神經系統的中心。"},{"en":"A university brain institute may use imaging machines, lab tests, and memory experiments.","zh":"大學腦研究所可能使用影像機器、實驗室測試和記憶實驗。"},{"en":"If researchers work in one institute, they can share equipment and ideas more easily.","zh":"如果研究人員在同一研究所工作，他們可以更容易共享設備和想法。"},{"en":"The phrase names an organised research centre focused on the brain.","zh":"這個短語指出專注於大腦的有組織研究中心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"experimental evidence","meaning":"實驗證據","examples":[{"en":"Experimental evidence once appeared to support common beliefs about aging.","zh":"實驗證據曾似乎支持關於老化的普遍看法。"},{"en":"Experimental evidence is information gathered from controlled tests or experiments.","zh":"「experimental evidence」是從受控制測試或實驗中收集到的資料。"},{"en":"A science teacher asks students to use experimental evidence before making conclusions.","zh":"科學老師要求學生在下結論前使用實驗證據。"},{"en":"If experimental evidence changes, old beliefs may need to be revised.","zh":"如果實驗證據改變，舊信念可能需要修正。"},{"en":"The phrase describes proof based on testing rather than opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述基於測試而不是意見的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"back up","meaning":"支持；證實","examples":[{"en":"Experimental evidence backed up popular assumptions about mental decline.","zh":"實驗證據支持了關於心智能力衰退的普遍假設。"},{"en":"To back up an idea means to support it with evidence or reasons.","zh":"「back up」一個想法，意思是用證據或理由支持它。"},{"en":"A student should back up an essay argument with examples from the text.","zh":"學生應用文本例子支持作文論點。"},{"en":"If data back up a claim, people are more likely to believe it.","zh":"如果數據支持某主張，人們更可能相信它。"},{"en":"The phrase means “support”, not “move backwards” in this context.","zh":"在這個語境中，這個短語意思是「支持」，不是「向後移動」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"popular assumptions","meaning":"普遍假設","examples":[{"en":"Popular assumptions suggested that the aging mind inevitably deteriorated.","zh":"普遍假設認為老化中的心智必然退化。"},{"en":"Popular assumptions are beliefs many people accept without always checking the evidence.","zh":"「popular assumptions」是許多人接受但未必檢查證據的信念。"},{"en":"A popular assumption is that older people cannot learn technology, but many do learn well.","zh":"一個普遍假設是長者不能學科技，但其實很多人學得很好。"},{"en":"If research challenges popular assumptions, society may need to change its views.","zh":"如果研究挑戰普遍假設，社會可能需要改變看法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes common beliefs that may or may not be true.","zh":"這個短語描述常見但未必真實的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"undergo decay","meaning":"經歷衰退","examples":[{"en":"The aging mind was believed to undergo decay.","zh":"人們曾相信老化中的心智會經歷衰退。"},{"en":"To undergo decay means to experience gradual weakening, decline, or breakdown.","zh":"「undergo decay」意思是經歷逐漸變弱、下降或分解。"},{"en":"A building may undergo decay if it is left empty and unrepaired for years.","zh":"如果建築物多年空置又不維修，它可能經歷衰敗。"},{"en":"If a skill is never practised, it may decline over time.","zh":"如果技能從不練習，它可能隨時間衰退。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a slow process of deterioration.","zh":"這個短語暗示緩慢退化過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"analogous to","meaning":"與……相似","examples":[{"en":"Mental decline was thought to be analogous to physical decline.","zh":"心智能力衰退曾被認為與身體衰退相似。"},{"en":"Analogous to means similar to something in an important way.","zh":"「analogous to」意思是在重要方面與某事相似。"},{"en":"Forgetting an old password is analogous to losing a key because both block access.","zh":"忘記舊密碼與遺失鎖匙相似，因為兩者都阻止進入。"},{"en":"If mental ageing is treated as analogous to body ageing, people may expect both to decline together.","zh":"如果心智老化被視為與身體老化相似，人們可能預期兩者一起衰退。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a comparison based on similarity.","zh":"這個短語引入基於相似性的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"aging body","meaning":"老化中的身體","examples":[{"en":"The aging mind was compared with the aging body.","zh":"老化中的心智被拿來與老化中的身體比較。"},{"en":"An aging body is a body that changes over time as a person grows older.","zh":"「aging body」是隨人年紀增長而改變的身體。"},{"en":"An aging body may need more rest after heavy exercise.","zh":"老化中的身體在劇烈運動後可能需要更多休息。"},{"en":"If the body ages, muscles, joints, and energy levels may change.","zh":"如果身體老化，肌肉、關節和能量水平可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical ageing, not mental ageing.","zh":"這個短語描述身體老化，而不是心智老化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"consistently outperform","meaning":"持續表現勝過……","examples":[{"en":"Younger animals consistently outperform older ones on memory tests.","zh":"較年輕動物在記憶測試中持續表現勝過較年長動物。"},{"en":"To consistently outperform others means to do better than them again and again.","zh":"「consistently outperform」別人，意思是一次又一次表現比他們好。"},{"en":"A student who studies every week may consistently outperform classmates who revise only before tests.","zh":"每星期溫習的學生可能持續表現勝過只在測驗前溫習的同學。"},{"en":"If one group consistently performs better, researchers look for the reason behind the pattern.","zh":"如果一組人持續表現較好，研究人員會尋找該模式背後的原因。"},{"en":"The phrase shows repeated superior performance, not one lucky result.","zh":"這個短語顯示重複的優越表現，而不是一次幸運結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"older colleagues","meaning":"較年長的同類","examples":[{"en":"Younger animals performed better than their older colleagues.","zh":"較年輕動物表現比較年長的同類好。"},{"en":"Older colleagues means older members of the same group, workplace, or category.","zh":"「older colleagues」指同一群體、工作場所或類別中較年長的成員。"},{"en":"A new teacher may learn classroom routines from older colleagues.","zh":"新老師可能向較年長同事學習課室日常安排。"},{"en":"If younger workers learn quickly but older colleagues have experience, both groups bring strengths.","zh":"如果年輕員工學得快而年長同事有經驗，兩組都有優勢。"},{"en":"The phrase compares people or animals within the same group.","zh":"這個短語比較同一群體中的人或動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"memory tests","meaning":"記憶測試","examples":[{"en":"Researchers compared animals of different ages on memory tests.","zh":"研究人員以記憶測試比較不同年齡的動物。"},{"en":"Memory tests are tasks designed to measure how well someone or something can remember information.","zh":"「memory tests」是設計來量度某人或某物記得資料能力的任務。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a short memory test to see whether students remember new vocabulary.","zh":"老師可能用短記憶測試查看學生是否記得新詞彙。"},{"en":"If older and younger groups get different scores, researchers may study why memory changes.","zh":"如果年長和年輕組別得分不同，研究人員可能研究為何記憶改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes tests focused on remembering.","zh":"這個短語描述專注於記憶的測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mental functions","meaning":"心智能力","examples":[{"en":"Psychologists believed that memory and other mental functions declined with age.","zh":"心理學家曾相信記憶和其他心智能力會隨年齡下降。"},{"en":"Mental functions are abilities of the mind, such as memory, attention, reasoning, and problem-solving.","zh":"「mental functions」是心智能力，例如記憶、注意力、推理和解難。"},{"en":"Sleep affects mental functions because tired students find it harder to focus and remember.","zh":"睡眠影響心智能力，因為疲倦學生較難專注和記憶。"},{"en":"If mental functions stay active through learning, people may cope better with ageing.","zh":"如果心智能力透過學習保持活躍，人們可能更能應對老化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what the mind does, not just what the brain physically is.","zh":"這個短語描述心智做甚麼，而不只是大腦的物理狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"deteriorate over time","meaning":"隨時間退化","examples":[{"en":"Some mental functions appear to deteriorate over time.","zh":"有些心智能力似乎會隨時間退化。"},{"en":"To deteriorate over time means to gradually become worse as time passes.","zh":"「deteriorate over time」意思是隨時間逐漸變差。"},{"en":"A bicycle left outside in the rain may deteriorate over time.","zh":"單車長期放在雨中，可能隨時間變壞。"},{"en":"If a skill is not used, it may slowly weaken.","zh":"如果技能不被使用，它可能慢慢變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual decline, not sudden collapse.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸下降，而不是突然崩潰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"inevitable organic changes","meaning":"無可避免的生理變化","examples":[{"en":"Mental decline was blamed on inevitable organic changes in the brain.","zh":"心智能力衰退曾被歸咎於大腦中無可避免的生理變化。"},{"en":"Inevitable organic changes are unavoidable physical or biological changes in the body.","zh":"「inevitable organic changes」是身體中無法避免的物理或生物變化。"},{"en":"Hair turning grey is an organic change that often happens with age.","zh":"頭髮變白是常隨年齡出現的生理變化。"},{"en":"If brain changes are considered inevitable, people may wrongly assume nothing can help.","zh":"如果腦部變化被視為無可避免，人們可能錯誤地以為沒有方法幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase describes biological changes that seem natural and unavoidable.","zh":"這個短語描述看似自然且不可避免的生物變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"neurons die off","meaning":"神經元逐漸死亡","examples":[{"en":"Researchers once believed that mental ability declined as neurons died off.","zh":"研究人員曾相信心智能力因神經元逐漸死亡而下降。"},{"en":"When neurons die off, nerve cells in the brain or nervous system gradually disappear or stop functioning.","zh":"當「neurons die off」時，大腦或神經系統中的神經細胞逐漸消失或停止運作。"},{"en":"A science lesson may explain that neurons send signals through the brain and body.","zh":"科學課可能解釋神經元在大腦和身體中傳送訊號。"},{"en":"If many neurons die, brain communication may become weaker.","zh":"如果很多神經元死亡，腦部溝通可能變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes loss of nerve cells over time.","zh":"這個短語描述神經細胞隨時間流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mental decline","meaning":"心智能力衰退","examples":[{"en":"Mental decline after young adulthood once appeared inevitable.","zh":"成年初期後的心智能力衰退曾看似無可避免。"},{"en":"Mental decline means a decrease in abilities such as memory, reasoning, attention, or learning.","zh":"「mental decline」意思是記憶、推理、注意力或學習等能力下降。"},{"en":"A person may worry about mental decline if they forget appointments more often than before.","zh":"如果一個人比以前更常忘記約會，他可能擔心心智能力衰退。"},{"en":"If decline is caused partly by inactivity, learning and stimulation may help slow it.","zh":"如果衰退部分由不活躍造成，學習和刺激可能有助減慢它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reduction in mental ability, not ordinary tiredness.","zh":"這個短語描述心智能力減少，而不是普通疲倦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"young adulthood","meaning":"成年初期","examples":[{"en":"Researchers once expected mental decline after young adulthood.","zh":"研究人員曾預期成年初期後會出現心智能力衰退。"},{"en":"Young adulthood is the early adult period, often after adolescence and before middle age.","zh":"「young adulthood」是成年早期，通常在青春期之後、中年之前。"},{"en":"Many people make major education, career, and relationship decisions during young adulthood.","zh":"許多人在成年初期作出重大的教育、事業和關係決定。"},{"en":"If researchers use young adulthood as a comparison point, they may study what changes later.","zh":"如果研究人員把成年初期作比較點，他們可能研究之後有甚麼改變。"},{"en":"The phrase names an early stage of adult life.","zh":"這個短語指出成年人生早期階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"appear inevitable","meaning":"看來無可避免","examples":[{"en":"Loss of mental ability once appeared inevitable.","zh":"心智能力喪失曾看來無可避免。"},{"en":"To appear inevitable means to seem impossible to avoid.","zh":"「appear inevitable」意思是看起來無法避免。"},{"en":"If a student never revises, failure may appear inevitable before the exam.","zh":"如果學生從不溫習，考試前失敗可能看來無可避免。"},{"en":"When new evidence appears, something that once seemed unavoidable may become preventable.","zh":"當新證據出現，曾看似不可避免的事可能變得可預防。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how a situation seems, not always what is truly certain.","zh":"這個短語描述情況看起來如何，而不一定是真正必然。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be equipped with","meaning":"配備","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are now equipped with advanced brain-imaging techniques.","zh":"研究人員現在配備先進腦部影像技術。"},{"en":"To be equipped with something means to have the tools, skills, or resources needed for a task.","zh":"「be equipped with」某物，意思是擁有完成任務所需的工具、技能或資源。"},{"en":"A classroom equipped with projectors and tablets can support interactive lessons.","zh":"配備投影機和平板電腦的課室可以支援互動課堂。"},{"en":"If scientists are equipped with better tools, they can observe the brain more accurately.","zh":"如果科學家配備更好工具，他們可以更準確觀察大腦。"},{"en":"The phrase describes having what is necessary to do a job.","zh":"這個短語描述擁有做某事所需的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"imaging techniques","meaning":"影像技術","examples":[{"en":"Imaging techniques allow researchers to observe the working brain.","zh":"影像技術讓研究人員觀察運作中的大腦。"},{"en":"Imaging techniques are methods that create pictures of the inside of the body or brain.","zh":"「imaging techniques」是產生身體或大腦內部影像的方法。"},{"en":"Hospitals use imaging techniques to see bones, organs, or blood flow without surgery.","zh":"醫院使用影像技術，在不用手術的情況下看骨骼、器官或血流。"},{"en":"If imaging techniques improve, doctors and scientists can detect hidden changes earlier.","zh":"如果影像技術改善，醫生和科學家可以更早發現隱藏變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes technology for seeing internal structures or activity.","zh":"這個短語描述觀看內部結構或活動的科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"capture the brain in action","meaning":"捕捉腦部運作情況","examples":[{"en":"Modern imaging techniques capture the brain in action.","zh":"現代影像技術能捕捉腦部運作情況。"},{"en":"To capture the brain in action means to record what the brain is doing while a person performs a task.","zh":"「capture the brain in action」意思是在某人執行任務時記錄大腦正在做甚麼。"},{"en":"A scanner can capture the brain in action while someone reads, remembers, or makes decisions.","zh":"掃描儀可以在人閱讀、記憶或作決定時捕捉腦部運作情況。"},{"en":"If scientists see the brain in action, they can compare how different age groups solve problems.","zh":"如果科學家看到腦部運作，他們可以比較不同年齡組如何解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes observing active brain processes, not just brain shape.","zh":"這個短語描述觀察活躍的腦部過程，而不只是腦的形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"measure the flow of blood","meaning":"測量血流","examples":[{"en":"Rapoport measured the flow of blood in the participants’ brains.","zh":"Rapoport 測量參加者腦中的血流。"},{"en":"To measure the flow of blood means to record how much blood moves through a body part.","zh":"「measure the flow of blood」意思是記錄有多少血液流經身體某部分。"},{"en":"Doctors may measure blood flow to check whether the heart or brain is receiving enough oxygen.","zh":"醫生可能測量血流，以檢查心臟或大腦是否獲得足夠氧氣。"},{"en":"If blood flow increases in one brain area, that area may be more active during a task.","zh":"如果某腦區血流增加，該區在任務期間可能更活躍。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a way to study physical activity inside the body.","zh":"這個短語描述研究身體內部活動的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"go through a task","meaning":"進行一項任務","examples":[{"en":"Participants went through a task involving photographs of faces.","zh":"參加者進行一項涉及人臉照片的任務。"},{"en":"To go through a task means to complete the steps of an activity or test.","zh":"「go through a task」意思是完成一項活動或測試的步驟。"},{"en":"Students may go through a listening task before discussing the answers.","zh":"學生可能先進行聆聽任務，再討論答案。"},{"en":"If participants go through the same task, researchers can compare their performance fairly.","zh":"如果參加者進行同一任務，研究人員可以公平比較他們的表現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes carrying out a structured activity.","zh":"這個短語描述執行有結構的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"match photos of faces","meaning":"配對人臉照片","examples":[{"en":"The participants had to match photos of faces.","zh":"參加者必須配對人臉照片。"},{"en":"To match photos of faces means to identify which face pictures show the same person or belong together.","zh":"「match photos of faces」意思是辨認哪些人臉照片顯示同一人或應配在一起。"},{"en":"A security officer may match a passport photo with the traveller’s face.","zh":"保安人員可能把護照照片與旅客面孔配對。"},{"en":"If a person can match faces quickly, their visual memory may be working well.","zh":"如果一個人能快速配對人臉，其視覺記憶可能運作良好。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a recognition task using face pictures.","zh":"這個短語描述使用人臉圖片的辨認任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"blood flow","meaning":"血流","examples":[{"en":"Blood flow can reflect activity within the brain.","zh":"血流可以反映腦內活動。"},{"en":"Blood flow is the movement of blood through blood vessels in the body.","zh":"「blood flow」是血液在身體血管中流動。"},{"en":"Exercise increases blood flow to muscles because they need more oxygen.","zh":"運動會增加流向肌肉的血流，因為肌肉需要更多氧氣。"},{"en":"If a brain area needs more energy, blood flow to that area may increase.","zh":"如果某腦區需要更多能量，流向該區的血流可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes circulation of blood, often linked with activity.","zh":"這個短語描述血液循環，常與活動有關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reflect neuronal activity","meaning":"反映神經元活動","examples":[{"en":"Blood flow reflects neuronal activity.","zh":"血流反映神經元活動。"},{"en":"To reflect neuronal activity means to show where nerve cells are active.","zh":"「reflect neuronal activity」意思是顯示神經細胞在哪裡活躍。"},{"en":"Brain scans may reflect neuronal activity when someone solves a maths problem.","zh":"當某人解數學題時，腦掃描可能反映神經元活動。"},{"en":"If blood flow rises in one brain area, researchers may infer that neurons there are working harder.","zh":"如果某腦區血流上升，研究人員可能推斷該處神經元工作較多。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a physical signal with brain-cell activity.","zh":"這個短語把物理訊號與腦細胞活動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"networks of neurons","meaning":"神經元網絡","examples":[{"en":"Different age groups may use different networks of neurons.","zh":"不同年齡組可能使用不同神經元網絡。"},{"en":"Networks of neurons are groups of nerve cells that work together to perform tasks.","zh":"「networks of neurons」是一起工作以執行任務的一組神經細胞。"},{"en":"When students learn a new skill, networks of neurons strengthen through practice.","zh":"當學生學習新技能時，神經元網絡會透過練習變強。"},{"en":"If one network becomes less efficient, the brain may use another network to help.","zh":"如果一個網絡變得較低效，大腦可能使用另一網絡來幫忙。"},{"en":"The phrase describes connected brain cells working as a system.","zh":"這個短語描述連接起來作為系統運作的腦細胞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be used by","meaning":"被……使用","examples":[{"en":"Different neural networks were used by older and younger subjects.","zh":"不同神經網絡被年長和年輕受試者使用。"},{"en":"To be used by someone means to be employed or relied on by that person or group.","zh":"「be used by」某人，意思是由該人或群體使用或依靠。"},{"en":"A study app may be used by students who want extra grammar practice.","zh":"想額外練習文法的學生可能使用學習應用程式。"},{"en":"If different strategies are used by different groups, the same result may be reached in different ways.","zh":"如果不同群體使用不同策略，同一結果可能以不同方式達到。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who uses a tool, method, or system.","zh":"這個短語指出誰使用工具、方法或系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reaction times","meaning":"反應時間","examples":[{"en":"Older and younger subjects sometimes had the same reaction times.","zh":"年長和年輕受試者有時有相同反應時間。"},{"en":"Reaction times are the amounts of time people take to respond to something.","zh":"「reaction times」是人們對某事作出反應所需的時間。"},{"en":"A driver’s reaction time matters when a child suddenly runs across the road.","zh":"當小孩突然衝出馬路時，司機的反應時間很重要。"},{"en":"If two groups have the same reaction times, they may perform equally fast even with different strategies.","zh":"如果兩組有相同反應時間，即使用不同策略，也可能表現一樣快。"},{"en":"The phrase measures speed of response.","zh":"這個短語量度反應速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"significantly different","meaning":"明顯不同","examples":[{"en":"The neural networks used by the two groups were significantly different.","zh":"兩組使用的神經網絡明顯不同。"},{"en":"Significantly different means clearly and importantly different, not just slightly different.","zh":"「significantly different」意思是清楚且重要地不同，而不只是稍有不同。"},{"en":"Two classes may have significantly different results if one receives extra practice for months.","zh":"如果一班接受數月額外練習，兩班成績可能明顯不同。"},{"en":"If brain patterns are significantly different, researchers may investigate how each group completes the task.","zh":"如果腦部模式明顯不同，研究人員可能調查每組如何完成任務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a meaningful difference.","zh":"這個短語描述有意義的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"internal strategies","meaning":"內在策略","examples":[{"en":"Older subjects used different internal strategies.","zh":"年長受試者使用不同內在策略。"},{"en":"Internal strategies are mental methods people use inside their minds to complete a task.","zh":"「internal strategies」是人們在腦中使用來完成任務的心理方法。"},{"en":"A student may use internal strategies such as grouping words or visualising pictures to remember vocabulary.","zh":"學生可能使用把詞語分組或想像圖像等內在策略來記詞。"},{"en":"If people use better mental strategies, they may perform well despite slower reaction speed.","zh":"如果人們使用更好的心理策略，即使反應較慢，也可能表現良好。"},{"en":"The phrase describes hidden thinking methods, not visible actions.","zh":"這個短語描述隱藏的思考方法，而不是可見行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"accomplish the same result","meaning":"達到相同結果","examples":[{"en":"Both groups could accomplish the same result.","zh":"兩組都能達到相同結果。"},{"en":"To accomplish the same result means to reach the same outcome, even if the method is different.","zh":"「accomplish the same result」意思是達到相同成果，即使方法不同。"},{"en":"Two students may accomplish the same result in maths using different steps.","zh":"兩名學生可能用不同步驟在數學中達到相同結果。"},{"en":"If older adults use different brain networks but answer correctly, the final outcome is still the same.","zh":"如果年長成人使用不同腦網絡但答案正確，最終結果仍相同。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the outcome rather than the method.","zh":"這個短語集中於結果，而不是方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"同時","examples":[{"en":"The two groups completed the task at the same time.","zh":"兩組同時完成任務。"},{"en":"At the same time means during the same moment or within the same amount of time.","zh":"「at the same time」意思是在同一時刻或用相同時間。"},{"en":"Two classmates may finish a race at the same time.","zh":"兩名同學可能同時完成賽跑。"},{"en":"If older and younger participants finish at the same time, speed alone may not show effort.","zh":"如果年長和年輕參加者同時完成，速度本身未必顯示努力程度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes simultaneous timing or equal completion time.","zh":"這個短語描述同時發生或相同完成時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"require greater effort","meaning":"需要更大努力","examples":[{"en":"The task may have required greater effort from the older subjects.","zh":"該任務對年長受試者可能需要更大努力。"},{"en":"To require greater effort means to need more energy, attention, or work to complete.","zh":"「require greater effort」意思是需要更多精力、注意力或工作才能完成。"},{"en":"Reading a difficult article requires greater effort than reading a simple story.","zh":"閱讀困難文章比閱讀簡單故事需要更大努力。"},{"en":"If a task requires more effort, people may perform well but feel more tired afterward.","zh":"如果任務需要更多努力，人們可能表現良好，但之後更疲倦。"},{"en":"The phrase explains hidden difficulty behind similar results.","zh":"這個短語解釋相似結果背後的隱藏困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"on the part of","meaning":"對……而言；由……作出","examples":[{"en":"The task may have demanded greater effort on the part of older subjects.","zh":"該任務可能需要年長受試者作出更大努力。"},{"en":"On the part of someone means done, felt, or shown by that person or group.","zh":"「on the part of」某人，意思是由該人或群體作出、感到或表現出。"},{"en":"Success in group work requires patience on the part of every student.","zh":"小組合作成功需要每位學生都付出耐心。"},{"en":"If more effort is needed on the part of older adults, the result may look equal but feel harder.","zh":"如果年長成人需要作出更多努力，結果可能看似相同但感覺更難。"},{"en":"The phrase points to who provides the action, feeling, or effort.","zh":"這個短語指出誰提供行動、感受或努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"originally involved in","meaning":"原本參與……","examples":[{"en":"Some neurons originally involved in the task may no longer have been used.","zh":"一些原本參與該任務的神經元可能已不再被使用。"},{"en":"Originally involved in something means first or initially taking part in it.","zh":"「originally involved in」某事，意思是最初或原本參與其中。"},{"en":"A student originally involved in a project may leave when the topic changes.","zh":"原本參與項目的學生可能在題目改變時離開。"},{"en":"If brain cells originally involved in a task become less active, other cells may help.","zh":"如果原本參與任務的腦細胞變得較不活躍，其他細胞可能幫忙。"},{"en":"The phrase describes participation at an earlier stage.","zh":"這個短語描述較早階段的參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be taken over by","meaning":"被……接替","examples":[{"en":"The work of certain neurons may have been taken over by other neurons.","zh":"某些神經元的工作可能已被其他神經元接替。"},{"en":"To be taken over by someone or something means to be replaced or controlled by them.","zh":"「be taken over by」某人或某物，意思是被他們取代或控制。"},{"en":"If a teacher is absent, the class may be taken over by another teacher.","zh":"如果老師缺席，課堂可能由另一位老師接替。"},{"en":"If one brain network becomes weaker, another network may take over part of the job.","zh":"如果一個腦網絡變弱，另一個網絡可能接手部分工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one person, group, or system assuming another’s role.","zh":"這個短語描述一個人、群體或系統承擔另一方角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"create different networks","meaning":"建立不同網絡","examples":[{"en":"The brain may create different networks to complete the same task.","zh":"大腦可能建立不同網絡來完成同一任務。"},{"en":"To create different networks means to form alternative systems of connected parts.","zh":"「create different networks」意思是形成由互相連接部分組成的替代系統。"},{"en":"A school may create different support networks for academic help, counselling, and career advice.","zh":"學校可能建立不同支援網絡，提供學業幫助、輔導和職業建議。"},{"en":"If the brain creates new routes, it may compensate for weakened older routes.","zh":"如果大腦建立新路線，它可能彌補較弱的舊路線。"},{"en":"The phrase shows adaptation through new connections.","zh":"這個短語顯示透過新連接作出適應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fast and accurate typists","meaning":"快速而準確的打字員","examples":[{"en":"Salthouse studied groups of fast and accurate typists.","zh":"Salthouse 研究了幾組快速而準確的打字員。"},{"en":"Fast and accurate typists are people who can type quickly while making few mistakes.","zh":"「fast and accurate typists」是能快速打字且錯誤很少的人。"},{"en":"Office workers who type reports all day often become fast and accurate typists.","zh":"整天打報告的辦公室員工常成為快速而準確的打字員。"},{"en":"If typists are both fast and accurate, researchers can compare skill rather than simple ability.","zh":"如果打字員既快又準，研究人員可以比較技巧，而不只是基本能力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes high performance in typing speed and correctness.","zh":"這個短語描述打字速度和準確度上的高表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"of college age","meaning":"大學年齡的","examples":[{"en":"One group of typists was of college age.","zh":"其中一組打字員是大學年齡的。"},{"en":"Of college age means around the age when people usually attend college or university.","zh":"「of college age」意思是大約在人們通常上大學的年齡。"},{"en":"Students of college age are often in their late teens or early twenties.","zh":"大學年齡的學生通常是十幾歲末或二十出頭。"},{"en":"If one research group is of college age, it may be compared with older adults.","zh":"如果一個研究組是大學年齡的，它可以與較年長成人比較。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an age range, not necessarily actual college enrolment.","zh":"這個短語描述年齡範圍，而不一定表示實際就讀大學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"reaction time","meaning":"反應速度","examples":[{"en":"Reaction time is generally faster in younger people.","zh":"年輕人的反應速度通常較快。"},{"en":"Reaction time is the time needed to respond after seeing, hearing, or feeling something.","zh":"「reaction time」是看到、聽到或感覺到某事後作出反應所需的時間。"},{"en":"In a driving test, reaction time matters when a traffic light changes suddenly.","zh":"在駕駛考試中，交通燈突然轉變時反應速度很重要。"},{"en":"If reaction time slows with age, people may use experience to compensate.","zh":"如果反應速度隨年齡變慢，人們可能用經驗來彌補。"},{"en":"The phrase measures how quickly someone responds.","zh":"這個短語量度某人反應有多快。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"grow less nimble with age","meaning":"隨年齡增長變得不靈活","examples":[{"en":"Most people’s fingers grow less nimble with age.","zh":"大多數人的手指會隨年齡增長變得較不靈活。"},{"en":"To grow less nimble with age means to become less quick and flexible as one gets older.","zh":"「grow less nimble with age」意思是隨年紀增長變得較不快速和靈活。"},{"en":"An older pianist may practise daily because fingers can grow less nimble with age.","zh":"年長鋼琴家可能每天練習，因為手指會隨年齡增長變得不靈活。"},{"en":"If fingers become less nimble, typing or buttoning a shirt may take more care.","zh":"如果手指變得不靈活，打字或扣襯衫鈕扣可能需要更小心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a gradual loss of physical quickness and flexibility.","zh":"這個短語描述身體敏捷和靈活性逐漸下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tap right along","meaning":"流暢快速地打字","examples":[{"en":"The younger typists were expected to tap right along.","zh":"人們預期較年輕打字員會流暢快速地打字。"},{"en":"To tap right along means to type or press keys smoothly and quickly without stopping.","zh":"「tap right along」意思是順暢快速地打字或按鍵而不停頓。"},{"en":"A student who knows the keyboard well can tap right along during a timed typing test.","zh":"熟悉鍵盤的學生在限時打字測試中可以流暢快速地打字。"},{"en":"If someone taps right along, their fingers move easily and confidently.","zh":"如果某人 tap right along，他的手指移動得容易而自信。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests fluent, continuous typing.","zh":"這個短語暗示流暢、連續的打字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fumble","meaning":"笨拙地操作；手忙腳亂","examples":[{"en":"Older typists might have been expected to fumble at the keyboard.","zh":"人們本可能預期較年長打字員在鍵盤上手忙腳亂。"},{"en":"To fumble means to handle something awkwardly, slowly, or with mistakes.","zh":"「fumble」意思是笨拙、緩慢或錯誤地操作某物。"},{"en":"A nervous student may fumble with notes before giving a speech.","zh":"緊張學生演講前可能手忙腳亂地整理筆記。"},{"en":"If someone fumbles at the keyboard, typing speed and accuracy may fall.","zh":"如果某人在鍵盤上笨拙操作，打字速度和準確度可能下降。"},{"en":"The word describes clumsy handling, often under pressure or difficulty.","zh":"這個詞描述笨拙處理，常出現在有壓力或困難時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"type 60 words a minute","meaning":"每分鐘打六十個字","examples":[{"en":"Both groups typed 60 words a minute.","zh":"兩組每分鐘打六十個字。"},{"en":"To type 60 words a minute means to produce sixty words of text in one minute.","zh":"「type 60 words a minute」意思是在一分鐘內打出六十個字。"},{"en":"A receptionist may need to type 60 words a minute to handle office work efficiently.","zh":"接待員可能需要每分鐘打六十個字，才能有效處理辦公室工作。"},{"en":"If older and younger typists type at the same speed, strategy may explain the result.","zh":"如果年長和年輕打字員以相同速度打字，策略可能解釋該結果。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a clear measure of typing speed.","zh":"這個短語提供清楚的打字速度量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"it turned out","meaning":"結果發現","examples":[{"en":"It turned out that the older typists used more efficient strategies.","zh":"結果發現，較年長打字員使用更有效率的策略。"},{"en":"It turned out means the result or truth was discovered later.","zh":"「it turned out」意思是結果或真相後來被發現。"},{"en":"It turned out that the quiet student had practised the presentation for weeks.","zh":"結果發現，那位安靜學生已為匯報練習數星期。"},{"en":"If research produces an unexpected result, “it turned out” introduces the discovery.","zh":"如果研究產生意外結果，“it turned out” 會引出該發現。"},{"en":"The phrase often signals that reality was different from expectation.","zh":"這個短語常表示現實與預期不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cunning little strategies","meaning":"巧妙的小策略","examples":[{"en":"The older typists used cunning little strategies.","zh":"較年長打字員使用巧妙的小策略。"},{"en":"Cunning little strategies are clever small methods used to solve a problem efficiently.","zh":"「cunning little strategies」是用來有效解決問題的聰明小方法。"},{"en":"A student may use cunning little strategies, such as grouping difficult words by sound.","zh":"學生可能使用巧妙的小策略，例如按聲音把難詞分組。"},{"en":"If physical speed declines, clever strategies can save time and reduce effort.","zh":"如果身體速度下降，聰明策略可以節省時間和減少努力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes small but smart ways to work better.","zh":"這個短語描述細小但聰明的改善方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"far more efficient than","meaning":"比……有效率得多","examples":[{"en":"The older typists were far more efficient than expected.","zh":"較年長打字員比預期有效率得多。"},{"en":"Far more efficient than means much better at using time, effort, or movement than another person or expectation.","zh":"「far more efficient than」意思是在使用時間、努力或動作方面遠比另一人或預期更好。"},{"en":"A well-planned bus route is far more efficient than several separate car journeys.","zh":"規劃良好的巴士路線比幾趟私家車行程有效率得多。"},{"en":"If someone uses fewer movements to get the same result, they are more efficient.","zh":"如果某人用較少動作達到相同結果，他就更有效率。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a strong difference in efficiency.","zh":"這個短語顯示效率上的強烈差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"younger counterparts","meaning":"較年輕的同類","examples":[{"en":"The older typists used fewer movements than their younger counterparts.","zh":"較年長打字員比他們較年輕的同類使用更少動作。"},{"en":"Younger counterparts are younger people who have the same role or are being compared in the same task.","zh":"「younger counterparts」是擔任相同角色或在同一任務中被比較的較年輕人士。"},{"en":"Older teachers may use different classroom strategies from their younger counterparts.","zh":"較年長老師可能使用與較年輕同事不同的課堂策略。"},{"en":"If older adults perform like younger counterparts, experience may be helping them.","zh":"如果年長成人表現像較年輕同類一樣，經驗可能正在幫助他們。"},{"en":"The phrase compares younger and older people in similar positions.","zh":"這個短語比較處於相似位置的年輕和年長人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make fewer finger movements","meaning":"減少手指動作","examples":[{"en":"The older typists made fewer finger movements.","zh":"較年長打字員減少了手指動作。"},{"en":"To make fewer finger movements means to move the fingers less often while doing a task.","zh":"「make fewer finger movements」意思是在做任務時較少移動手指。"},{"en":"Skilled pianists may make fewer finger movements because their hands know the pattern well.","zh":"熟練鋼琴家可能減少手指動作，因為雙手熟悉模式。"},{"en":"If typists make fewer unnecessary movements, they can save small amounts of time.","zh":"如果打字員減少不必要動作，他們可以節省少量時間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes efficiency in hand or finger action.","zh":"這個短語描述手部或手指動作上的效率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a fraction of a second","meaning":"極短的一瞬間","examples":[{"en":"Each saved movement preserved a fraction of a second.","zh":"每個節省下來的動作都保留了極短的一瞬間。"},{"en":"A fraction of a second is a very tiny amount of time, less than one full second.","zh":"「a fraction of a second」是非常短的時間，少於一整秒。"},{"en":"In a race, a fraction of a second can decide who wins.","zh":"在比賽中，極短的一瞬間可以決定誰勝出。"},{"en":"If many tiny time savings add up, a person can finish a task just as quickly as someone faster.","zh":"如果許多微小時間節省加起來，一個人可以像速度較快的人一樣快完成任務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an extremely short moment.","zh":"這個短語描述極短時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"here and there","meaning":"在各個細微之處","examples":[{"en":"The typists saved small amounts of time here and there.","zh":"打字員在各個細微之處節省少量時間。"},{"en":"Here and there means in several small places or moments, not all at once.","zh":"「here and there」意思是在幾個細小地方或時刻，而不是一次過。"},{"en":"A student can improve an essay by fixing unclear words here and there.","zh":"學生可以透過在各處修改不清楚字詞來改善作文。"},{"en":"If small savings happen here and there, the total effect can become noticeable.","zh":"如果小節省在各處出現，總效果可以變得明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes scattered small changes or amounts.","zh":"這個短語描述分散的小改變或數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"read ahead","meaning":"預先閱讀後面的文字","examples":[{"en":"The older typists read ahead in the text.","zh":"較年長打字員會預先閱讀後面的文字。"},{"en":"To read ahead means to look at upcoming words or information before reaching them in the task.","zh":"「read ahead」意思是在任務中到達之前先看即將出現的字詞或資料。"},{"en":"A good speaker may read ahead in notes to prepare for the next point.","zh":"好演講者可能預先閱讀筆記中的下一點。"},{"en":"If typists read ahead, they can plan finger movements before the words arrive.","zh":"如果打字員預先閱讀後面的文字，他們可以在字詞到來前規劃手指動作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preparing for what comes next.","zh":"這個短語描述為接下來的內容作準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be reshaped to","meaning":"被重新塑造成……","examples":[{"en":"Neural networks may be reshaped to compensate for physical losses.","zh":"神經網絡可能被重新塑造成用以彌補身體能力喪失。"},{"en":"To be reshaped to do something means to be changed in form or organisation for a purpose.","zh":"「be reshaped to」做某事，意思是為某目的而在形式或組織上被改變。"},{"en":"A timetable may be reshaped to give students more revision time before exams.","zh":"時間表可能被重新安排，以給學生更多考前溫習時間。"},{"en":"If the brain reshapes its networks, it may find new ways to perform old tasks.","zh":"如果大腦重塑其網絡，它可能找到執行舊任務的新方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adaptation through structural or organisational change.","zh":"這個短語描述透過結構或組織改變來適應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"compensate for","meaning":"彌補","examples":[{"en":"The brain can compensate for losses in motor skills.","zh":"大腦可以彌補動作技能衰退。"},{"en":"To compensate for something means to make up for a weakness, loss, or problem.","zh":"「compensate for」某事，意思是彌補弱點、損失或問題。"},{"en":"A student with weak spelling may compensate for it by proofreading carefully.","zh":"串字較弱的學生可能透過仔細校對來彌補。"},{"en":"If fingers move more slowly, better planning can compensate for the loss of speed.","zh":"如果手指移動較慢，更好的規劃可以彌補速度損失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes balancing out a disadvantage.","zh":"這個短語描述抵消不利因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"losses in motor skills","meaning":"動作技能衰退","examples":[{"en":"The brain may adapt to losses in motor skills.","zh":"大腦可能適應動作技能衰退。"},{"en":"Losses in motor skills are declines in the ability to control movement, such as typing, walking, or grasping.","zh":"「losses in motor skills」是控制動作能力下降，例如打字、步行或抓握。"},{"en":"After an injury, a patient may experience losses in motor skills and need therapy.","zh":"受傷後，病人可能經歷動作技能衰退並需要治療。"},{"en":"If motor skills decline, people may use tools, practice, or strategies to remain independent.","zh":"如果動作技能下降，人們可能使用工具、練習或策略來保持獨立。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reduced physical control of movement.","zh":"這個短語描述身體動作控制能力減弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"age changes","meaning":"年齡帶來的變化","examples":[{"en":"Experience can help people adapt to age changes.","zh":"經驗可以幫助人們適應年齡帶來的變化。"},{"en":"Age changes are physical, mental, or social changes that happen as people grow older.","zh":"「age changes」是人隨年紀增長而出現的身體、心智或社會變化。"},{"en":"A person may adapt to age changes by exercising more gently and using reminders.","zh":"一個人可能透過較溫和運動和使用提醒來適應年齡變化。"},{"en":"If people understand age changes, they may plan healthier routines earlier.","zh":"如果人們理解年齡帶來的變化，他們可能更早規劃健康習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changes linked with getting older.","zh":"這個短語描述與變老相關的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be kept in isolation","meaning":"被隔離飼養","examples":[{"en":"A rat’s brain may shrink when it is kept in isolation.","zh":"老鼠被隔離飼養時，腦部可能萎縮。"},{"en":"To be kept in isolation means to be separated from others and from normal social contact.","zh":"「be kept in isolation」意思是與其他個體和正常社交接觸分開。"},{"en":"A sick student may be kept in isolation to prevent spreading an infection.","zh":"生病學生可能被隔離，以防傳播感染。"},{"en":"If animals are kept alone without stimulation, their brains and behaviour may change.","zh":"如果動物被單獨飼養且沒有刺激，其大腦和行為可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being separated, often for safety or experiment.","zh":"這個短語描述被分隔，常出於安全或實驗目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"without playmates","meaning":"沒有玩伴","examples":[{"en":"The rat was kept without playmates or objects to explore.","zh":"該老鼠被飼養時沒有玩伴，也沒有可探索物件。"},{"en":"Without playmates means having no companions to play or interact with.","zh":"「without playmates」意思是沒有可一起玩耍或互動的同伴。"},{"en":"A child without playmates during a holiday may feel lonely and bored.","zh":"假期中沒有玩伴的孩子可能感到孤獨和沉悶。"},{"en":"If young animals lack playmates, they may have fewer chances to learn social behaviour.","zh":"如果年幼動物沒有玩伴，它們可能較少機會學習社交行為。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights absence of social interaction.","zh":"這個短語突出缺乏社交互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"interact with","meaning":"與……互動","examples":[{"en":"Animals need objects and companions to interact with.","zh":"動物需要可互動的物件和同伴。"},{"en":"To interact with someone or something means to communicate, play, respond, or have contact with them.","zh":"「interact with」某人或某物，意思是與他們溝通、玩耍、回應或接觸。"},{"en":"Students interact with classmates during group discussions.","zh":"學生在小組討論中與同學互動。"},{"en":"If people interact with stimulating environments, they may learn and remember more.","zh":"如果人們與具刺激性的環境互動，他們可能學得和記得更多。"},{"en":"The phrase describes two-way contact or activity.","zh":"這個短語描述雙向接觸或活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the brain shrinks","meaning":"腦部萎縮","examples":[{"en":"An isolated rat’s brain may shrink.","zh":"被隔離飼養的老鼠腦部可能萎縮。"},{"en":"The brain shrinks means the brain becomes smaller in size or volume.","zh":"「the brain shrinks」意思是大腦在大小或體積上變小。"},{"en":"Doctors may monitor whether the brain shrinks in certain diseases or after severe inactivity.","zh":"醫生可能監測某些疾病或嚴重不活動後腦部是否萎縮。"},{"en":"If the brain receives too little stimulation, some brain structures may become less developed.","zh":"如果大腦接受太少刺激，某些腦結構可能發展較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a physical reduction in brain tissue or size.","zh":"這個短語描述腦組織或大小的物理減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"put an animal with","meaning":"把動物與……放在一起","examples":[{"en":"Researchers put the rat with several other rats.","zh":"研究人員把該老鼠與幾隻其他老鼠放在一起。"},{"en":"To put an animal with others means to place it in the same environment as them.","zh":"「put an animal with」其他個體，意思是把它放在同一環境中。"},{"en":"A vet may put a nervous dog with calm dogs to help it feel safer.","zh":"獸醫可能把緊張的狗與冷靜的狗放在一起，幫助牠感到更安全。"},{"en":"If an isolated animal is placed with companions, it gains social stimulation.","zh":"如果被隔離動物與同伴放在一起，它會得到社交刺激。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing an animal’s environment by adding company.","zh":"這個短語描述透過加入同伴來改變動物環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"an assortment of","meaning":"各式各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"The cage contained an assortment of wheels, ladders and toys.","zh":"籠中有各式各樣的輪子、梯子和玩具。"},{"en":"An assortment of things is a mixed collection of different kinds of items.","zh":"「an assortment of」物件，是不同種類物品的混合集合。"},{"en":"A classroom cupboard may contain an assortment of markers, scissors, tape, and paper.","zh":"課室櫃中可能有各式各樣的箱頭筆、剪刀、膠紙和紙張。"},{"en":"If animals receive an assortment of objects, they have more chances to explore and learn.","zh":"如果動物得到各式各樣的物件，牠們有更多機會探索和學習。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises variety within a collection.","zh":"這個短語強調集合中的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"significant differences","meaning":"顯著差異","examples":[{"en":"Researchers observed significant differences in the rat’s brain.","zh":"研究人員在老鼠腦中觀察到顯著差異。"},{"en":"Significant differences are differences large or important enough to matter.","zh":"「significant differences」是大到或重要到值得注意的差異。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice significant differences between essays written before and after feedback.","zh":"老師可能注意到回饋前後作文之間有顯著差異。"},{"en":"If two environments produce significant brain differences, surroundings clearly matter.","zh":"如果兩種環境造成顯著腦部差異，周圍環境顯然重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes meaningful differences, not tiny random changes.","zh":"這個短語描述有意義的差異，而不是微小隨機變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"integrative biology","meaning":"綜合生物學","examples":[{"en":"Diamond was a professor of integrative biology.","zh":"Diamond 是綜合生物學教授。"},{"en":"Integrative biology is a field that connects different levels of biology, from cells to whole organisms and environments.","zh":"「integrative biology」是連接生物學不同層次的領域，由細胞到整個生物和環境。"},{"en":"A course in integrative biology may link genetics, behaviour, anatomy, and ecology.","zh":"綜合生物學課程可能連接遺傳、行為、解剖和生態。"},{"en":"If researchers integrate several biological areas, they can understand living systems more completely.","zh":"如果研究人員整合幾個生物範疇，他們可以更完整理解生命系統。"},{"en":"The phrase describes biology that brings different parts together.","zh":"這個短語描述把不同部分結合起來的生物學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"proliferating dendrites","meaning":"不斷增生的樹突","examples":[{"en":"Proliferating dendrites first appeared in particular brain areas.","zh":"不斷增生的樹突首先出現在特定腦區。"},{"en":"Proliferating dendrites are growing branch-like extensions of neurons that help receive signals.","zh":"「proliferating dendrites」是不斷生長、像樹枝一樣幫助接收訊號的神經元延伸部分。"},{"en":"A biology diagram may show dendrites like branches coming out of a nerve cell.","zh":"生物圖可能把樹突畫成由神經細胞伸出的樹枝。"},{"en":"If dendrites increase, neurons may make more connections with other neurons.","zh":"如果樹突增加，神經元可能與其他神經元建立更多連接。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growth in the brain’s communication structures.","zh":"這個短語描述大腦溝通結構的增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"visual association areas","meaning":"視覺聯合區","examples":[{"en":"Dendrites first appeared in the visual association areas.","zh":"樹突首先出現在視覺聯合區。"},{"en":"Visual association areas are brain regions that help interpret and connect visual information.","zh":"「visual association areas」是幫助解讀和連接視覺資料的腦區。"},{"en":"When a person recognises a familiar face, visual association areas may help link the image with memory.","zh":"當人辨認熟悉面孔時，視覺聯合區可能幫助把影像與記憶連繫起來。"},{"en":"If these areas are stimulated by a rich environment, visual processing may become more connected.","zh":"如果這些區域受到豐富環境刺激，視覺處理可能變得更有連接。"},{"en":"The phrase names brain areas involved in making sense of what we see.","zh":"這個短語指出參與理解所見事物的腦區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"enriched environment","meaning":"豐富刺激的環境","examples":[{"en":"The rats’ brains developed in an enriched environment.","zh":"老鼠的腦部在豐富刺激的環境中發展。"},{"en":"An enriched environment is a setting with social contact, objects, variety, and stimulation.","zh":"「enriched environment」是有社交接觸、物件、多樣性和刺激的環境。"},{"en":"A child’s enriched learning environment may include books, games, music, and conversation.","zh":"孩子的豐富學習環境可能包括書本、遊戲、音樂和對話。"},{"en":"If animals live in an enriched environment, their brains may develop more connections.","zh":"如果動物生活在豐富刺激的環境中，牠們的大腦可能發展出更多連接。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts a stimulating environment with an empty or isolated one.","zh":"這個短語把刺激性環境與空洞或隔離環境作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cerebral cortex","meaning":"大腦皮層","examples":[{"en":"The whole cerebral cortex expanded after a month.","zh":"一個月後，整個大腦皮層擴大了。"},{"en":"The cerebral cortex is the outer layer of the brain involved in thinking, sensing, memory, and control.","zh":"「cerebral cortex」是大腦外層，參與思考、感覺、記憶和控制。"},{"en":"A neuroscience lesson may compare the cerebral cortex to a command centre for complex tasks.","zh":"神經科學課可能把大腦皮層比作複雜任務的指揮中心。"},{"en":"If the cortex changes after stimulation, experience may physically affect the brain.","zh":"如果皮層在刺激後改變，經驗可能會在身體上影響大腦。"},{"en":"The phrase names a major brain structure.","zh":"這個短語指出主要腦部結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"expand","meaning":"擴大；增長","examples":[{"en":"The cerebral cortex expanded in the enriched environment.","zh":"大腦皮層在豐富刺激的環境中增長。"},{"en":"To expand means to become larger or wider.","zh":"「expand」意思是變得更大或更廣。"},{"en":"A school may expand its library when more students begin to read regularly.","zh":"當更多學生開始定期閱讀，學校可能擴大圖書館。"},{"en":"If a brain area expands after stimulation, the environment may be affecting its structure.","zh":"如果某腦區在刺激後擴大，環境可能正在影響其結構。"},{"en":"The word describes growth in size, range, or capacity.","zh":"這個詞描述大小、範圍或能力上的增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"blood supply","meaning":"血液供應","examples":[{"en":"The brain’s blood supply also increased.","zh":"大腦的血液供應也增加。"},{"en":"Blood supply is the amount of blood delivered to a body part.","zh":"「blood supply」是輸送到身體某部分的血液量。"},{"en":"Exercise improves blood supply to muscles because they need oxygen and nutrients.","zh":"運動改善肌肉血液供應，因為肌肉需要氧氣和養分。"},{"en":"If blood supply to the brain improves, brain cells may receive more support.","zh":"如果流向大腦的血液供應改善，腦細胞可能得到更多支持。"},{"en":"The phrase describes delivery of blood to tissue.","zh":"這個短語描述血液輸送到組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"get bored","meaning":"感到沉悶","examples":[{"en":"Even animals in an enriched environment can get bored.","zh":"即使在豐富刺激環境中的動物也會感到沉悶。"},{"en":"To get bored means to become uninterested because there is not enough variety or challenge.","zh":"「get bored」意思是因缺乏變化或挑戰而變得不感興趣。"},{"en":"Students may get bored if every lesson uses the same worksheet format.","zh":"如果每堂課都用同一款工作紙，學生可能感到沉悶。"},{"en":"If toys never change, animals may stop exploring them.","zh":"如果玩具從不改變，動物可能停止探索它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes loss of interest after repeated exposure.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆接觸後失去興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"unless the toys are varied","meaning":"除非玩具有變化","examples":[{"en":"The rats became bored unless the toys were varied.","zh":"除非玩具有變化，否則老鼠會感到沉悶。"},{"en":"Unless the toys are varied means if the toys are not changed or made different.","zh":"「unless the toys are varied」意思是如果玩具沒有被改變或變得不同。"},{"en":"Children may lose interest in a play corner unless the toys are varied occasionally.","zh":"除非玩具偶爾有變化，孩子可能對遊戲角失去興趣。"},{"en":"If stimulation stays the same, learning and curiosity may drop.","zh":"如果刺激一直相同，學習和好奇心可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that variety is needed to prevent boredom.","zh":"這個短語顯示需要變化來防止沉悶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"need stimulation","meaning":"需要刺激","examples":[{"en":"Animals and humans both need stimulation.","zh":"動物和人類都需要刺激。"},{"en":"To need stimulation means to need activity, variety, challenge, or contact that keeps the mind active.","zh":"「need stimulation」意思是需要能保持心智活躍的活動、變化、挑戰或接觸。"},{"en":"Young children need stimulation through play, conversation, music, and movement.","zh":"幼兒需要透過遊戲、對話、音樂和活動得到刺激。"},{"en":"If people receive too little stimulation, they may become bored and mentally inactive.","zh":"如果人們得到太少刺激，他們可能變得沉悶和心智不活躍。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why rich environments can support learning.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何豐富環境能支持學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"profoundly important","meaning":"極為重要的","examples":[{"en":"Memory is one of our most profoundly important mental functions.","zh":"記憶是我們最極為重要的心智能力之一。"},{"en":"Profoundly important means deeply and extremely important.","zh":"「profoundly important」意思是深刻而極其重要。"},{"en":"Sleep is profoundly important for students because it affects memory, mood, and concentration.","zh":"睡眠對學生極為重要，因為它影響記憶、心情和專注。"},{"en":"If something is profoundly important, losing it can affect many parts of life.","zh":"如果某物極為重要，失去它會影響生活許多方面。"},{"en":"The phrase gives strong emphasis to importance.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be notorious for","meaning":"以……而聞名；出了名會……","examples":[{"en":"Memory is notorious for its failure with age.","zh":"記憶出了名會隨年齡增長而衰退。"},{"en":"To be notorious for something means to be well known for something bad or problematic.","zh":"「be notorious for」某事，意思是因不好的或有問題的事情而廣為人知。"},{"en":"That bus route is notorious for delays during rush hour.","zh":"那條巴士線在繁忙時間以延誤聞名。"},{"en":"If memory is notorious for decline, people may fear ordinary forgetfulness too much.","zh":"如果記憶以衰退聞名，人們可能過分害怕普通健忘。"},{"en":"The phrase usually carries a negative meaning.","zh":"這個短語通常帶負面意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"failure with age","meaning":"隨年齡增長而衰退","examples":[{"en":"Memory is often associated with failure as people age.","zh":"記憶常被聯想到隨年齡增長而衰退。"},{"en":"Failure with age means decline or reduced performance as a person grows older.","zh":"「failure with age」意思是隨着人變老而衰退或表現下降。"},{"en":"People may worry about eyesight failure with age when reading small print becomes harder.","zh":"當閱讀細字變得更難，人們可能擔心視力隨年齡增長而衰退。"},{"en":"If memory failure with age is not universal, researchers must separate normal lapses from serious decline.","zh":"如果記憶隨年齡衰退並非普遍，研究人員必須區分正常小失誤和嚴重下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes worsening ability linked with ageing.","zh":"這個短語描述與老化相關的能力變差。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"spend money to","meaning":"花錢去……","examples":[{"en":"The foundation spent millions of dollars to study memory loss.","zh":"該基金會花了數百萬美元去研究記憶力衰退。"},{"en":"To spend money to do something means to use money for that purpose.","zh":"「spend money to」做某事，意思是為該目的使用金錢。"},{"en":"A school may spend money to improve the library and buy new books.","zh":"學校可能花錢改善圖書館並購買新書。"},{"en":"If a problem is important, organisations may spend large sums to research it.","zh":"如果問題重要，機構可能花大筆金錢去研究它。"},{"en":"The phrase links money with a goal or action.","zh":"這個短語把金錢與目標或行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"set up a consortium","meaning":"成立聯盟","examples":[{"en":"The foundation set up a consortium of leading medical centers.","zh":"該基金會成立了一個由頂尖醫療中心組成的聯盟。"},{"en":"To set up a consortium means to create a group of organisations that work together on a shared project.","zh":"「set up a consortium」意思是建立一組共同處理同一項目的機構。"},{"en":"Several schools may set up a consortium to share teachers for rare subjects.","zh":"幾所學校可能成立聯盟，共享冷門科目的老師。"},{"en":"If research is too large for one centre, a consortium can combine resources and expertise.","zh":"如果研究對單一中心來說太龐大，聯盟可以結合資源和專業知識。"},{"en":"The phrase describes forming a cooperative research or work group.","zh":"這個短語描述成立合作研究或工作團體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"consortium of","meaning":"……的聯盟","examples":[{"en":"A consortium of research centers studied memory and aging.","zh":"一個由研究中心組成的聯盟研究記憶與老化。"},{"en":"A consortium of organisations is a group that cooperates on a common task.","zh":"「consortium of」機構，是合作完成共同任務的一組機構。"},{"en":"A consortium of hospitals may share patient data to study a disease.","zh":"醫院聯盟可能共享病人數據來研究疾病。"},{"en":"If different centres join a consortium, the research can include more people and better equipment.","zh":"如果不同中心加入聯盟，研究可以包括更多人和更好設備。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a formal partnership.","zh":"這個短語描述正式合作關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"leading medical centers","meaning":"頂尖醫療中心","examples":[{"en":"Leading medical centers participated in the research.","zh":"頂尖醫療中心參與了該研究。"},{"en":"Leading medical centers are major hospitals or research institutions known for high-quality medical work.","zh":"「leading medical centers」是以高質素醫療工作聞名的大型醫院或研究機構。"},{"en":"Patients with rare diseases may be referred to leading medical centers for specialist care.","zh":"患有罕見病的病人可能被轉介到頂尖醫療中心接受專科護理。"},{"en":"If leading centres join a study, the research may gain stronger expertise and credibility.","zh":"如果頂尖中心加入研究，研究可能獲得更強專業知識和可信度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes top medical institutions.","zh":"這個短語描述頂級醫療機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"measure memory loss","meaning":"測量記憶力衰退","examples":[{"en":"Researchers used several methods to measure memory loss.","zh":"研究人員使用幾種方法測量記憶力衰退。"},{"en":"To measure memory loss means to assess how much remembering ability has declined.","zh":"「measure memory loss」意思是評估記憶能力下降了多少。"},{"en":"Doctors may measure memory loss by asking patients to recall words or events.","zh":"醫生可能透過要求病人回想詞語或事件來測量記憶力衰退。"},{"en":"If memory loss is measured carefully, normal ageing can be separated from disease.","zh":"如果記憶衰退被仔細測量，正常老化可以與疾病區分開來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes testing the degree of memory decline.","zh":"這個短語描述測試記憶下降程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"brain imaging technology","meaning":"腦部影像技術","examples":[{"en":"The study used brain imaging technology.","zh":"該研究使用腦部影像技術。"},{"en":"Brain imaging technology is equipment and methods used to create images of brain structure or activity.","zh":"「brain imaging technology」是用來產生腦部結構或活動影像的設備和方法。"},{"en":"Hospitals use brain imaging technology to check strokes, tumours, or injuries.","zh":"醫院使用腦部影像技術檢查中風、腫瘤或受傷。"},{"en":"If researchers use brain imaging, they can see which areas are active during memory tasks.","zh":"如果研究人員使用腦部影像，他們可以看到記憶任務期間哪些區域活躍。"},{"en":"The phrase describes modern tools for observing the brain.","zh":"這個短語描述觀察大腦的現代工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"neurochemical experiments","meaning":"神經化學實驗","examples":[{"en":"Researchers conducted neurochemical experiments.","zh":"研究人員進行了神經化學實驗。"},{"en":"Neurochemical experiments are tests about chemicals involved in the brain and nervous system.","zh":"「neurochemical experiments」是關於大腦和神經系統中化學物質的測試。"},{"en":"A lab may study how a chemical messenger affects learning in animals.","zh":"實驗室可能研究某種化學信使如何影響動物學習。"},{"en":"If brain chemicals change with age, memory and mood may also change.","zh":"如果腦部化學物質隨年齡改變，記憶和心情也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes experiments connecting chemistry with brain function.","zh":"這個短語描述把化學與腦功能連繫起來的實驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cognitive and psychological tests","meaning":"認知和心理測試","examples":[{"en":"The consortium used cognitive and psychological tests.","zh":"該聯盟使用認知和心理測試。"},{"en":"Cognitive and psychological tests measure thinking, memory, attention, emotion, or behaviour.","zh":"「cognitive and psychological tests」量度思考、記憶、注意力、情緒或行為。"},{"en":"A psychologist may use such tests to understand why a student struggles with learning.","zh":"心理學家可能使用這類測試了解學生為何學習有困難。"},{"en":"If test results are compared across ages, researchers can study mental change over time.","zh":"如果不同年齡的測試結果被比較，研究人員可以研究心智隨時間改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formal tests of mind and behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述心智和行為的正式測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fairly clear","meaning":"頗為清楚","examples":[{"en":"One conclusion about memory is already fairly clear.","zh":"關於記憶的一個結論已經頗為清楚。"},{"en":"Fairly clear means reasonably easy to understand or strongly suggested, though not perfectly certain.","zh":"「fairly clear」意思是相當容易理解或有強烈暗示，但未必完全肯定。"},{"en":"After several practice tests, it was fairly clear which grammar points the class needed to review.","zh":"幾次練習測驗後，班級需要重溫哪些文法點已頗為清楚。"},{"en":"If evidence points in the same direction, a conclusion becomes clearer.","zh":"如果證據都指向同一方向，結論就變得更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase shows cautious confidence.","zh":"這個短語顯示謹慎的信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"aspects of memory","meaning":"記憶的不同方面","examples":[{"en":"Many aspects of memory do not depend entirely on age.","zh":"記憶的許多方面並不完全取決於年齡。"},{"en":"Aspects of memory are different parts or types of remembering.","zh":"「aspects of memory」是記憶的不同部分或種類。"},{"en":"Remembering names, facts, experiences, and skills are different aspects of memory.","zh":"記住名字、事實、經歷和技能都是記憶的不同方面。"},{"en":"If one aspect declines but another remains strong, memory is more complex than people assume.","zh":"如果一方面下降但另一方面仍強，記憶就比人們想像複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase helps divide memory into smaller parts for study.","zh":"這個短語有助把記憶分成較小部分來研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a function of age","meaning":"由年齡決定的結果","examples":[{"en":"Some aspects of memory are not a function of age.","zh":"記憶的某些方面並不是由年齡決定的結果。"},{"en":"A function of age means something that depends on or is caused by age.","zh":"「a function of age」意思是取決於年齡或由年齡造成的事。"},{"en":"A child’s height is partly a function of age, nutrition, and genetics.","zh":"孩子的身高部分取決於年齡、營養和遺傳。"},{"en":"If memory performance depends more on education than age, age is not the main factor.","zh":"如果記憶表現更取決於教育而不是年齡，年齡就不是主要因素。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a result linked to age as a determining factor.","zh":"這個短語描述與年齡作為決定因素有關的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"more than one form","meaning":"多於一種形式","examples":[{"en":"Memory exists in more than one form.","zh":"記憶存在多於一種形式。"},{"en":"More than one form means there are several types, not just a single kind.","zh":"「more than one form」意思是不只一種，而是有幾種類型。"},{"en":"Learning happens in more than one form: reading, listening, practice, and discussion all matter.","zh":"學習有多於一種形式：閱讀、聆聽、練習和討論都重要。"},{"en":"If memory has several forms, one type may weaken while another remains stable.","zh":"如果記憶有幾種形式，一種類型可能變弱而另一種保持穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises variety within a category.","zh":"這個短語強調某類別內的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"semantic memory","meaning":"語義記憶","examples":[{"en":"Semantic memory stores factual knowledge.","zh":"語義記憶儲存事實性知識。"},{"en":"Semantic memory is memory for facts, meanings, concepts, and general knowledge.","zh":"「semantic memory」是關於事實、意思、概念和一般知識的記憶。"},{"en":"Knowing that Paris is the capital of France is part of semantic memory.","zh":"知道巴黎是法國首都，是語義記憶的一部分。"},{"en":"If information is repeated and learned well, it may become part of semantic memory.","zh":"如果資料被重複並學得很熟，它可能成為語義記憶的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes knowledge without needing to remember when it was learned.","zh":"這個短語描述不需要記得何時學會的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"factual knowledge","meaning":"事實性知識","examples":[{"en":"Facts and general knowledge form part of semantic memory.","zh":"事實和一般知識構成語義記憶的一部分。"},{"en":"Factual knowledge is information that can be stated as facts, such as dates, names, rules, or definitions.","zh":"「factual knowledge」是可以作為事實陳述的資料，例如日期、姓名、規則或定義。"},{"en":"A student needs factual knowledge before writing a good history essay.","zh":"學生需要事實性知識，才能寫出好的歷史作文。"},{"en":"If facts are reviewed often, they may stay in memory for years.","zh":"如果事實經常被重溫，它們可能在記憶中保留多年。"},{"en":"The phrase describes knowledge of what is true or known.","zh":"這個短語描述關於真實或已知內容的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"Episodic memory, on the other hand, stores events and experiences.","zh":"另一方面，情節記憶儲存事件和經歷。"},{"en":"On the other hand introduces a contrast or a different side of the discussion.","zh":"「on the other hand」引出對比或討論中的另一面。"},{"en":"Online learning is flexible; on the other hand, it can feel lonely for some students.","zh":"網上學習很有彈性；另一方面，對一些學生來說可能感到孤單。"},{"en":"If semantic memory stores facts, episodic memory, on the other hand, stores personal events.","zh":"如果語義記憶儲存事實，另一方面，情節記憶儲存個人事件。"},{"en":"The phrase helps compare two ideas clearly.","zh":"這個短語幫助清楚比較兩個想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"episodic memory","meaning":"情節記憶","examples":[{"en":"Episodic memory contains events situated in time and space.","zh":"情節記憶包含發生於時間和空間中的事件。"},{"en":"Episodic memory is memory of personal events and experiences linked to when and where they happened.","zh":"「episodic memory」是關於個人事件和經歷的記憶，並與事情何時何地發生有關。"},{"en":"Remembering your first day at school is an example of episodic memory.","zh":"記得自己第一天上學是情節記憶的一個例子。"},{"en":"If an event is emotional or vivid, episodic memory may store it more strongly.","zh":"如果事件情緒強烈或鮮明，情節記憶可能把它儲存得更強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes memory of experiences, not just facts.","zh":"這個短語描述經歷記憶，而不只是事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"event memory","meaning":"事件記憶","examples":[{"en":"Episodic memory is also known as event memory.","zh":"情節記憶也稱為事件記憶。"},{"en":"Event memory is memory of things that happened at particular times and places.","zh":"「event memory」是對在特定時間和地點發生的事情的記憶。"},{"en":"A person’s memory of a birthday party is event memory.","zh":"一個人對生日派對的記憶就是事件記憶。"},{"en":"If an event has strong sounds, faces, and emotions, it may be easier to remember.","zh":"如果事件有強烈聲音、面孔和情緒，它可能更容易被記住。"},{"en":"The phrase is a simpler name for episodic memory.","zh":"這個短語是情節記憶的較簡單名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"occurrences in time and space","meaning":"發生於特定時間和空間的事件","examples":[{"en":"Episodic memory records occurrences in time and space.","zh":"情節記憶記錄發生於特定時間和空間的事件。"},{"en":"Occurrences in time and space are events connected to a particular when and where.","zh":"「occurrences in time and space」是與特定時間和地點相連的事件。"},{"en":"A graduation ceremony is an occurrence in time and space because it happened on a certain day in a certain place.","zh":"畢業典禮是發生於特定時間和空間的事件，因為它在某日某地發生。"},{"en":"If a memory includes the setting and moment, it is more like an event memory than a fact.","zh":"如果記憶包含場景和時刻，它更像事件記憶，而不是事實。"},{"en":"The phrase describes events located in context.","zh":"這個短語描述位於情境中的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be triggered by","meaning":"由……觸發","examples":[{"en":"Episodic memories may be triggered by contextual cues.","zh":"情節記憶可能由情境線索觸發。"},{"en":"To be triggered by something means to be caused or activated by it.","zh":"「be triggered by」某事，意思是由它引起或啟動。"},{"en":"A song may trigger memories of a school trip.","zh":"一首歌可能觸發對學校旅行的記憶。"},{"en":"If a smell reminds someone of home, the smell has triggered a memory.","zh":"如果某種氣味令某人想起家，那氣味就觸發了記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something starting a response or memory.","zh":"這個短語描述某物啟動反應或記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cues from the context","meaning":"情境線索","examples":[{"en":"Events may be recalled through cues from the context.","zh":"事件可能透過情境線索被回想起來。"},{"en":"Cues from the context are clues in the surroundings or situation that help people remember.","zh":"「cues from the context」是環境或情況中幫助人記憶的提示。"},{"en":"Seeing an old classroom may give a student cues from the context and bring back memories.","zh":"看見舊課室可能給學生情境線索，並喚起記憶。"},{"en":"If a person returns to the place where something happened, memory may become easier.","zh":"如果一個人回到事情發生的地方，記憶可能變得較容易。"},{"en":"The phrase describes hints that come from the situation around an event.","zh":"這個短語描述來自事件周圍情境的提示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be reminded of","meaning":"被提醒想起……","examples":[{"en":"People often do not need to be reminded of major historical events.","zh":"人們通常不需要被提醒想起重大歷史事件。"},{"en":"To be reminded of something means to be made to remember it.","zh":"「be reminded of」某事，意思是被某物令自己記起它。"},{"en":"A photo may remind a student of a school picnic.","zh":"一張照片可能令學生想起學校野餐。"},{"en":"If an event is vivid, people may remember it without needing reminders.","zh":"如果事件很鮮明，人們可能不需要提醒就記得它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something bringing a memory back.","zh":"這個短語描述某物把記憶帶回來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"circumstances surrounding","meaning":"圍繞……的情況","examples":[{"en":"People may remember the circumstances surrounding major news.","zh":"人們可能記得圍繞重大新聞的情況。"},{"en":"Circumstances surrounding something are the conditions, details, and events around it.","zh":"「circumstances surrounding」某事，是圍繞它的條件、細節和事件。"},{"en":"A student may remember the circumstances surrounding the day exam results were released.","zh":"學生可能記得考試成績公布那天周圍的情況。"},{"en":"If news is shocking, people may remember where they were and who told them.","zh":"如果新聞令人震驚，人們可能記得自己當時在哪裡和誰告訴他。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the background details around an event.","zh":"這個短語描述事件周圍的背景細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be assassinated","meaning":"被刺殺","examples":[{"en":"Many people remember hearing that JFK had been assassinated.","zh":"許多人記得聽到 JFK 被刺殺的消息。"},{"en":"To be assassinated means to be murdered for political or public reasons.","zh":"「be assassinated」意思是因政治或公共原因被謀殺。"},{"en":"A history lesson may discuss leaders who were assassinated during periods of unrest.","zh":"歷史課可能討論在動盪時期被刺殺的領袖。"},{"en":"If a public figure is assassinated, the event can shock an entire country.","zh":"如果公眾人物被刺殺，事件可以震驚整個國家。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a targeted killing, usually of an important person.","zh":"這個短語描述有目標的殺害，通常對象是重要人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be etched into","meaning":"深深刻在……","examples":[{"en":"A vivid event can be etched into episodic memory.","zh":"鮮明事件可以深深刻在情節記憶中。"},{"en":"To be etched into memory means to be remembered very strongly and clearly.","zh":"「be etched into」記憶，意思是被非常強烈和清楚地記住。"},{"en":"A first performance on stage may be etched into a student’s memory for years.","zh":"第一次上台表演可能多年來深深刻在學生記憶中。"},{"en":"If an event is emotional or shocking, it may stay in memory more vividly.","zh":"如果事件情緒強烈或令人震驚，它可能更鮮明地留在記憶中。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a memory is deeply carved into the mind.","zh":"這個短語暗示記憶深深刻在腦海中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"less vivid item","meaning":"不太鮮明的事情","examples":[{"en":"People often forget less vivid items from daily life.","zh":"人們常忘記日常生活中不太鮮明的事情。"},{"en":"A less vivid item is something ordinary, faint, or not very memorable.","zh":"「less vivid item」是普通、模糊或不太令人記住的事情。"},{"en":"A person may forget what they ate last Tuesday because it was a less vivid item.","zh":"一個人可能忘記上星期二吃了甚麼，因為那是不太鮮明的事情。"},{"en":"If an event is not emotional or unusual, it may be harder to remember later.","zh":"如果事件不情緒化或不尋常，之後可能更難記得。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts ordinary details with striking memories.","zh":"這個短語把普通細節與鮮明記憶作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"blame something on","meaning":"把某事歸咎於……","examples":[{"en":"People may blame ordinary forgetfulness on aging memory.","zh":"人們可能把普通健忘歸咎於老化中的記憶力。"},{"en":"To blame something on a cause means to say that the cause is responsible for it.","zh":"「blame something on」某原因，意思是說該原因要對某事負責。"},{"en":"A student may blame a low mark on lack of sleep, but poor preparation may also matter.","zh":"學生可能把低分歸咎於睡眠不足，但準備不足也可能重要。"},{"en":"If people blame every mistake on age, they may ignore stress, distraction, or poor organisation.","zh":"如果人們把每個錯誤都歸咎於年齡，他們可能忽略壓力、分心或組織欠佳。"},{"en":"The phrase describes assigning responsibility for a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述把問題責任歸於某原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"aging memory","meaning":"老化中的記憶力","examples":[{"en":"Minor lapses are often blamed on an aging memory.","zh":"小失誤常被歸咎於老化中的記憶力。"},{"en":"Aging memory is memory that changes or seems weaker as a person grows older.","zh":"「aging memory」是隨人變老而改變或看似變弱的記憶。"},{"en":"An older adult may worry about aging memory when they misplace keys more often.","zh":"長者更常放錯鎖匙時，可能擔心老化中的記憶力。"},{"en":"If small lapses are caused by stress rather than age, the problem may be manageable.","zh":"如果小失誤由壓力而非年齡造成，問題可能可以處理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes memory in the context of getting older.","zh":"這個短語描述變老背景下的記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"begin to decline","meaning":"開始衰退","examples":[{"en":"Episodic memory begins to decline for many people in their 50s.","zh":"對許多人來說，情節記憶在五十多歲開始衰退。"},{"en":"To begin to decline means to start becoming weaker, lower, or less effective.","zh":"「begin to decline」意思是開始變弱、變低或較低效。"},{"en":"A student’s concentration may begin to decline after several hours without a break.","zh":"學生連續數小時不休息後，專注力可能開始下降。"},{"en":"If a skill begins to decline, early practice and support may slow the change.","zh":"如果技能開始衰退，早期練習和支援可能減慢變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the start of a downward trend.","zh":"這個短語描述下降趨勢的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at any age","meaning":"在任何年齡","examples":[{"en":"Episodic memory is never perfect at any age.","zh":"情節記憶在任何年齡都從不完美。"},{"en":"At any age means no matter how old a person is.","zh":"「at any age」意思是不論一個人多大年紀。"},{"en":"People can learn new words at any age if they practise regularly.","zh":"人們在任何年齡都可以學新詞，只要定期練習。"},{"en":"If memory is imperfect at any age, forgetting small details is not always a sign of ageing.","zh":"如果記憶在任何年齡都不完美，忘記小細節不一定是老化跡象。"},{"en":"The phrase applies a statement to all stages of life.","zh":"這個短語把說法應用於人生所有階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"begin as an event","meaning":"由一件事件開始","examples":[{"en":"Every memory begins as an event.","zh":"每段記憶都由一件事件開始。"},{"en":"To begin as an event means to start from something that actually happened.","zh":"「begin as an event」意思是由實際發生的事情開始。"},{"en":"A friendship memory may begin as an event, such as the first day two students met.","zh":"友誼記憶可能由一件事件開始，例如兩名學生第一次見面的日子。"},{"en":"If an event is repeated or reviewed, it may later become general knowledge.","zh":"如果事件被重複或重溫，它之後可能變成一般知識。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how experience can become memory.","zh":"這個短語顯示經驗如何變成記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"through repetition","meaning":"透過重複","examples":[{"en":"Through repetition, some memories become permanent knowledge.","zh":"透過重複，有些記憶變成永久知識。"},{"en":"Through repetition means by doing, hearing, or reviewing something many times.","zh":"「through repetition」意思是透過多次做、聽到或重溫某事。"},{"en":"Students remember irregular verbs through repetition and practice.","zh":"學生透過重複和練習記住不規則動詞。"},{"en":"If information is repeated often, it is more likely to stay in long-term memory.","zh":"如果資料經常重複，它更可能留在長期記憶中。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning by repeated exposure.","zh":"這個短語描述透過反覆接觸來學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"leave behind a residue of","meaning":"留下……的痕跡","examples":[{"en":"Repeated events leave behind a residue of knowledge.","zh":"重複事件留下知識的痕跡。"},{"en":"To leave behind a residue of something means to leave a remaining trace after the original experience has passed.","zh":"「leave behind a residue of」某物，意思是在原本經歷過去後留下殘餘痕跡。"},{"en":"A childhood trip may leave behind a residue of language, smells, and place names.","zh":"童年旅行可能留下語言、氣味和地名的痕跡。"},{"en":"If lessons are repeated for years, they may leave lasting knowledge even after details fade.","zh":"如果課程多年重複，即使細節淡去，它們也可能留下持久知識。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what remains after experience.","zh":"這個短語描述經歷之後留下的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"residue of knowledge","meaning":"知識的留存","examples":[{"en":"Semantic memory is a residue of repeated experience.","zh":"語義記憶是重複經驗留下的知識留存。"},{"en":"A residue of knowledge is what remains in the mind after repeated learning or experience.","zh":"「residue of knowledge」是反覆學習或經驗後留在腦中的東西。"},{"en":"After years of using English, a student keeps a residue of grammar rules even if they forget the lessons.","zh":"多年使用英語後，即使忘記課堂，學生仍保留文法規則的知識留存。"},{"en":"If practice is repeated enough, knowledge may remain after the original context is forgotten.","zh":"如果練習足夠重複，原本情境被忘記後知識仍可能留下。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lasting knowledge left by experience.","zh":"這個短語描述經驗留下的持久知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on a specific day","meaning":"在某個特定日子","examples":[{"en":"A person first learns each fact on a specific day.","zh":"一個人最初在某個特定日子學會每個事實。"},{"en":"On a specific day means on one particular date or occasion.","zh":"「on a specific day」意思是在某一個特定日期或場合。"},{"en":"A student may learn the word “photosynthesis” on a specific day in biology class.","zh":"學生可能在生物課某個特定日子學到 “photosynthesis” 這個詞。"},{"en":"If the fact is repeated later, the learner may forget the exact day but remember the content.","zh":"如果該事實後來被重複，學習者可能忘記確切日子，但記得內容。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a particular time, not a general period.","zh":"這個短語指特定時間，而不是一般時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"go over information","meaning":"重溫資料","examples":[{"en":"People remember information better when they go over it repeatedly.","zh":"當人們反覆重溫資料，他們會記得更好。"},{"en":"To go over information means to review or study it again.","zh":"「go over information」意思是再次複習或學習資料。"},{"en":"Students should go over vocabulary before a dictation.","zh":"學生應在默書前重溫詞彙。"},{"en":"If information is reviewed many times, it becomes easier to recall later.","zh":"如果資料被多次重溫，之後會更容易回想。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated review for learning.","zh":"這個短語描述為學習而反覆複習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"permanent part of","meaning":"……的永久部分","examples":[{"en":"Repeated information can become a permanent part of one’s knowledge.","zh":"重複的資料可以成為某人知識的永久部分。"},{"en":"A permanent part of something is a lasting element that remains there for a long time.","zh":"「permanent part of」某物，是長時間留在其中的持久元素。"},{"en":"Basic multiplication becomes a permanent part of a student’s knowledge after years of use.","zh":"經過多年使用，基本乘法會成為學生知識的永久部分。"},{"en":"If knowledge is practised often, it may stay even when the original lesson is forgotten.","zh":"如果知識經常練習，即使原本課堂被忘記，它仍可能留下。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that becomes lasting and stable.","zh":"這個短語描述某物變得持久和穩定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"knowledge base","meaning":"知識基礎","examples":[{"en":"Repeated facts become part of a person’s knowledge base.","zh":"重複的事實會成為一個人知識基礎的一部分。"},{"en":"A knowledge base is the collection of facts, ideas, and skills a person or system can use.","zh":"「knowledge base」是一個人或系統可使用的事實、想法和技能集合。"},{"en":"Reading widely builds a student’s knowledge base for writing essays.","zh":"廣泛閱讀可以建立學生寫作文的知識基礎。"},{"en":"If your knowledge base is strong, new information is easier to understand and remember.","zh":"如果你的知識基礎強，新資料會更容易理解和記住。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stored knowledge that supports future learning.","zh":"這個短語描述支持未來學習的儲存知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"remember the content, not the context","meaning":"記得內容而非背景","examples":[{"en":"People often remember the content, not the context in which they learned it.","zh":"人們常記得內容，而不是學會它的背景。"},{"en":"To remember the content, not the context means to know the information but forget when or where it was learned.","zh":"「remember the content, not the context」意思是知道資料，但忘記何時或在哪裡學到。"},{"en":"A student may know a grammar rule but not remember which teacher first explained it.","zh":"學生可能知道一條文法規則，但不記得哪位老師最先解釋。"},{"en":"If repeated learning turns an event into knowledge, the original setting may fade.","zh":"如果重複學習把事件變成知識，原本情境可能淡去。"},{"en":"The phrase separates what was learned from the situation of learning.","zh":"這個短語把所學內容與學習情境分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"language knowledge","meaning":"語言知識","examples":[{"en":"Language knowledge is largely a long-term residue of learning.","zh":"語言知識很大程度上是學習的長期留存。"},{"en":"Language knowledge is what a person knows about vocabulary, grammar, pronunciation, and meaning.","zh":"「language knowledge」是一個人對詞彙、文法、發音和意思的認識。"},{"en":"A student’s language knowledge grows through reading, listening, speaking, and writing.","zh":"學生的語言知識透過閱讀、聆聽、說話和寫作增長。"},{"en":"If language is practised often, knowledge remains even when individual lessons are forgotten.","zh":"如果語言經常練習，即使個別課堂被忘記，知識仍會留下。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stored understanding of a language.","zh":"這個短語描述對語言的儲存理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"knowledge of the world","meaning":"對世界的認識","examples":[{"en":"Our knowledge of the world forms part of semantic memory.","zh":"我們對世界的認識構成語義記憶的一部分。"},{"en":"Knowledge of the world is general understanding of people, places, facts, events, and how things work.","zh":"「knowledge of the world」是對人、地方、事實、事件和事物運作方式的一般理解。"},{"en":"Reading news and books can expand a student’s knowledge of the world.","zh":"閱讀新聞和書籍可以擴闊學生對世界的認識。"},{"en":"If people know more about the world, they can connect new information to existing ideas.","zh":"如果人們對世界認識更多，他們可以把新資料與現有想法連繫起來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad general knowledge beyond personal memories.","zh":"這個短語描述超越個人記憶的廣泛一般知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"semipermanent residue","meaning":"半永久性的留存","examples":[{"en":"Some knowledge remains as a semipermanent residue.","zh":"有些知識以半永久性留存的形式保留下來。"},{"en":"A semipermanent residue is something that stays for a long time but may not last forever.","zh":"「semipermanent residue」是長時間留下但未必永遠存在的東西。"},{"en":"After years of French lessons, a learner may keep a semipermanent residue of basic phrases.","zh":"經過多年法文課後，學習者可能保留基本短語的半永久性留存。"},{"en":"If knowledge is used rarely, it may remain faintly rather than disappear completely.","zh":"如果知識很少使用，它可能模糊地留下，而不是完全消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lasting but not perfectly permanent memory.","zh":"這個短語描述持久但並非完全永久的記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"probe the longevity of","meaning":"探究……能維持多久","examples":[{"en":"Bahrick probed the longevity of knowledge.","zh":"Bahrick 探究知識能維持多久。"},{"en":"To probe the longevity of something means to investigate how long it lasts.","zh":"「probe the longevity of」某物，意思是調查它能持續多長時間。"},{"en":"Researchers may probe the longevity of vaccine protection by following patients for years.","zh":"研究人員可能透過多年跟進病人來探究疫苗保護能維持多久。"},{"en":"If knowledge stays for decades, learning has a longer effect than expected.","zh":"如果知識可保留數十年，學習的影響就比預期更長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a careful study of duration.","zh":"這個短語描述對持續時間的仔細研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"longevity of knowledge","meaning":"知識的持久性","examples":[{"en":"The study examined the longevity of knowledge.","zh":"該研究探討知識的持久性。"},{"en":"Longevity of knowledge means how long knowledge remains in memory.","zh":"「longevity of knowledge」意思是知識在記憶中保留多久。"},{"en":"A teacher may wonder about the longevity of knowledge after students finish a course.","zh":"學生完成課程後，老師可能想知道知識的持久性。"},{"en":"If knowledge is practised for years, its longevity may be much greater.","zh":"如果知識被多年練習，其持久性可能大得多。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how durable learning is.","zh":"這個短語集中於學習有多耐久。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"high school graduates","meaning":"中學畢業生","examples":[{"en":"Bahrick tested 1,000 high school graduates.","zh":"Bahrick 測試了1,000名中學畢業生。"},{"en":"High school graduates are people who have completed secondary school.","zh":"「high school graduates」是完成中學教育的人。"},{"en":"High school graduates may enter university, start work, or take vocational training.","zh":"中學畢業生可能入讀大學、開始工作或接受職業培訓。"},{"en":"If researchers test graduates years later, they can study how much school knowledge remains.","zh":"如果研究人員多年後測試畢業生，他們可以研究學校知識留下多少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes people after finishing high school.","zh":"這個短語描述完成中學後的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"recall their algebra","meaning":"回想起所學的代數","examples":[{"en":"The participants were tested on how well they could recall their algebra.","zh":"參加者接受測試，看他們能多好地回想起所學的代數。"},{"en":"To recall their algebra means to remember the algebra they had learned before.","zh":"「recall their algebra」意思是記起他們以前學過的代數。"},{"en":"Adults may struggle to recall algebra if they have not used it since school.","zh":"如果成年人自離校後沒有用過代數，他們可能難以回想起來。"},{"en":"If learners studied algebra for many years, they may recall more of it later.","zh":"如果學習者學了很多年代數，他們之後可能回想起更多內容。"},{"en":"The phrase describes remembering a learned school subject.","zh":"這個短語描述記起學過的學校科目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as recently as","meaning":"最近至……","examples":[{"en":"Some participants had studied algebra as recently as one month earlier.","zh":"有些參加者最近至一個月前才學過代數。"},{"en":"As recently as means only as little time ago as the stated period.","zh":"「as recently as」意思是最近到所述時間之前而已。"},{"en":"A student may have revised the topic as recently as yesterday.","zh":"學生可能最近至昨天才溫習過該題目。"},{"en":"If someone studied a subject recently, they may remember more details.","zh":"如果某人最近學過某科，他可能記得更多細節。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that something happened not long ago.","zh":"這個短語強調某事發生在不久之前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as long as 50 years earlier","meaning":"早至五十年前","examples":[{"en":"Others had studied algebra as long as 50 years earlier.","zh":"其他人早至五十年前已學過代數。"},{"en":"As long as 50 years earlier means as far back as fifty years before the testing time.","zh":"「as long as 50 years earlier」意思是早到測試時間之前五十年。"},{"en":"Some adults may remember songs they learned as long as forty years earlier.","zh":"有些成年人可能記得早至四十年前學過的歌曲。"},{"en":"If knowledge lasts that long, early learning can have a very durable effect.","zh":"如果知識能維持那麼久，早期學習可以有很持久的影響。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises a surprisingly long time gap.","zh":"這個短語強調令人驚訝的長時間距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"determine how long","meaning":"確定……有多久","examples":[{"en":"The researcher determined how long each person had studied algebra.","zh":"研究人員確定每個人學習代數有多久。"},{"en":"To determine how long means to find out the length of time.","zh":"「determine how long」意思是查明時間長度。"},{"en":"A teacher may determine how long students spend on homework each night.","zh":"老師可能確定學生每晚花多久做功課。"},{"en":"If researchers know how long someone studied, they can compare study duration with memory.","zh":"如果研究人員知道某人學習了多久，他們可以比較學習時長與記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase describes measuring or finding duration.","zh":"這個短語描述量度或查明持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"over the course of adulthood","meaning":"在整個成年期","examples":[{"en":"He measured how much algebra was used over the course of adulthood.","zh":"他測量在整個成年期使用了多少代數。"},{"en":"Over the course of adulthood means throughout the years of adult life.","zh":"「over the course of adulthood」意思是在成年生活的多年期間。"},{"en":"People may change jobs several times over the course of adulthood.","zh":"人們在整個成年期可能多次轉工。"},{"en":"If a skill is used often during adulthood, it may stay stronger in memory.","zh":"如果技能在成年期經常使用，它可能在記憶中保持較強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something happening across adult years.","zh":"這個短語描述某事跨越成年年月發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a person’s grasp of","meaning":"某人對……的掌握","examples":[{"en":"A person’s grasp of algebra did not depend mainly on age.","zh":"一個人對代數的掌握並不主要取決於年齡。"},{"en":"A person’s grasp of something is how well they understand or can use it.","zh":"「a person’s grasp of」某事，是他理解或使用它的程度。"},{"en":"A student’s grasp of grammar improves when they can explain rules and use them in writing.","zh":"當學生能解釋規則並在寫作中使用，對文法的掌握就會改善。"},{"en":"If someone’s grasp of a subject is strong, they can solve problems even years later.","zh":"如果某人對某科掌握強，即使多年後仍能解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes understanding and practical command.","zh":"這個短語描述理解和實際掌控。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"at the time of testing","meaning":"在測試時","examples":[{"en":"Participants’ knowledge was assessed at the time of testing.","zh":"參加者的知識在測試時被評估。"},{"en":"At the time of testing means when the test was being carried out.","zh":"「at the time of testing」意思是在測試進行時。"},{"en":"A student’s mood at the time of testing can affect concentration.","zh":"學生在測試時的心情可以影響專注力。"},{"en":"If researchers record age and performance at the time of testing, comparisons become clearer.","zh":"如果研究人員在測試時記錄年齡和表現，比較會更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the exact moment of measurement.","zh":"這個短語指出量度的確切時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"depend on how long ago","meaning":"取決於多久以前……","examples":[{"en":"Knowledge did not depend on how long ago the course had been taken.","zh":"知識並不取決於課程是在多久以前修讀。"},{"en":"To depend on how long ago something happened means to be affected by the amount of time since it happened.","zh":"「depend on how long ago」某事發生，意思是受該事發生至今的時間長度影響。"},{"en":"A password memory may depend on how long ago someone last used it.","zh":"記得密碼可能取決於某人上次使用它是在多久以前。"},{"en":"If knowledge does not depend on time since learning, other factors may be more important.","zh":"如果知識不取決於學習距今多久，其他因素可能更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an outcome with distance in time.","zh":"這個短語把結果與時間距離連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"determining factor","meaning":"決定因素","examples":[{"en":"The duration of instruction was the determining factor.","zh":"教學持續時間是決定因素。"},{"en":"A determining factor is the thing that most strongly decides the result.","zh":"「determining factor」是最強烈決定結果的因素。"},{"en":"For exam success, regular practice may be the determining factor rather than natural talent.","zh":"對考試成功而言，定期練習可能是決定因素，而不是天分。"},{"en":"If study duration predicts long-term memory, age may not be the key factor.","zh":"如果學習時長能預測長期記憶，年齡就未必是關鍵因素。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the most important cause or influence.","zh":"這個短語描述最重要的原因或影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"duration of instruction","meaning":"教學持續時間","examples":[{"en":"The duration of instruction strongly affected long-term memory.","zh":"教學持續時間強烈影響長期記憶。"},{"en":"Duration of instruction means the length of time a person receives teaching or training.","zh":"「duration of instruction」意思是某人接受教學或訓練的時間長度。"},{"en":"A language course lasting two years has a longer duration of instruction than a weekend workshop.","zh":"兩年語言課程的教學持續時間比週末工作坊長。"},{"en":"If instruction lasts longer, students have more chances to repeat and use the material.","zh":"如果教學持續較久，學生有更多機會重複和使用材料。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how long teaching continues.","zh":"這個短語集中於教學延續多久。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"within two or three years","meaning":"在兩三年內","examples":[{"en":"Many participants forgot most of the material within two or three years.","zh":"許多參加者在兩三年內忘記了大部分材料。"},{"en":"Within two or three years means before two or three years have passed.","zh":"「within two or three years」意思是在兩年或三年過去之前。"},{"en":"A student may forget a rarely used formula within two or three years after graduation.","zh":"學生畢業後可能在兩三年內忘記很少使用的公式。"},{"en":"If material is not practised, forgetting can happen within a relatively short period.","zh":"如果材料沒有練習，遺忘可以在相對短時間內發生。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a time limit for something happening.","zh":"這個短語設定某事發生的時間限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"spread out over","meaning":"分散於……期間","examples":[{"en":"The Spanish courses were spread out over a couple of years.","zh":"西班牙語課程分散於兩年左右期間。"},{"en":"To be spread out over a period means to be arranged across that whole period, not crowded into one short time.","zh":"「spread out over」一段時間，意思是安排在整段時間內，而不是擠在很短時間。"},{"en":"Revision is easier when homework is spread out over several weeks.","zh":"如果功課分散於幾星期，溫習會較容易。"},{"en":"If language learning is spread out over years, repetition may strengthen memory.","zh":"如果語言學習分散於多年，重複可能加強記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase describes distribution across time.","zh":"這個短語描述在時間上的分佈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a couple of years","meaning":"兩年左右","examples":[{"en":"Some participants studied Spanish over a couple of years.","zh":"有些參加者在兩年左右期間學習西班牙語。"},{"en":"A couple of years means about two years.","zh":"「a couple of years」意思是大約兩年。"},{"en":"A student may spend a couple of years preparing for a difficult language exam.","zh":"學生可能花兩年左右準備困難的語言考試。"},{"en":"If learning lasts a couple of years, there is more time for practice and review.","zh":"如果學習持續兩年左右，就有更多時間練習和重溫。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate, informal time period.","zh":"這個短語提供近似而較口語的時間長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"decades later","meaning":"數十年後","examples":[{"en":"Some learners recalled much of the vocabulary decades later.","zh":"有些學習者數十年後仍回想起很多詞彙。"},{"en":"Decades later means many tens of years after an event.","zh":"「decades later」意思是在某事件後很多個十年。"},{"en":"Decades later, former classmates may still remember their favourite teacher’s advice.","zh":"數十年後，舊同學可能仍記得最喜歡老師的建議。"},{"en":"If vocabulary is remembered decades later, the original learning was very durable.","zh":"如果詞彙數十年後仍被記得，原本學習非常持久。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises a very long time after something happened.","zh":"這個短語強調某事發生後非常長的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"retain only a trace","meaning":"只保留一點痕跡","examples":[{"en":"Those who took one course retained only a trace of the language.","zh":"只修讀一個課程的人，只保留了該語言的一點痕跡。"},{"en":"To retain only a trace means to keep only a very small amount or faint memory.","zh":"「retain only a trace」意思是只保留非常少量或模糊記憶。"},{"en":"A student may retain only a trace of a subject studied briefly many years ago.","zh":"學生可能對多年前短暫學過的科目只保留一點痕跡。"},{"en":"If learning is short and rarely used, little may remain later.","zh":"如果學習時間短又很少使用，之後可能只剩很少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes very weak remaining memory.","zh":"這個短語描述非常薄弱的殘餘記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"long-term residue of knowledge","meaning":"長期留存的知識","examples":[{"en":"Well-learned material can leave a long-term residue of knowledge.","zh":"學得很熟的材料可以留下長期留存的知識。"},{"en":"A long-term residue of knowledge is knowledge that remains for many years after learning.","zh":"「long-term residue of knowledge」是學習後多年仍保留的知識。"},{"en":"A person may keep a long-term residue of school French even after forgetting many lessons.","zh":"一個人即使忘記很多課堂，也可能保留學校法文的長期知識。"},{"en":"If a subject is practised repeatedly, it may leave knowledge that lasts into adulthood.","zh":"如果某科被反覆練習，它可能留下持續到成年的知識。"},{"en":"The phrase describes durable learning that remains over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間仍保留的持久學習成果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"remain stable over the decades","meaning":"數十年間保持穩定","examples":[{"en":"Some knowledge remains stable over the decades.","zh":"有些知識在數十年間保持穩定。"},{"en":"To remain stable over the decades means to stay mostly unchanged for many tens of years.","zh":"「remain stable over the decades」意思是在數十年間大致保持不變。"},{"en":"A person’s basic reading ability may remain stable over the decades if used daily.","zh":"如果每天使用，一個人的基本閱讀能力可能數十年間保持穩定。"},{"en":"If knowledge remains stable, age alone may not be causing major loss.","zh":"如果知識保持穩定，年齡本身未必造成重大喪失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long-lasting consistency.","zh":"這個短語描述長期一致性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"independent of","meaning":"不受……影響","examples":[{"en":"The retained knowledge was independent of the person’s age.","zh":"保留下來的知識不受該人年齡影響。"},{"en":"Independent of something means not controlled or strongly affected by it.","zh":"「independent of」某事，意思是不受它控制或強烈影響。"},{"en":"A student’s kindness should be valued independent of exam results.","zh":"學生的善良應在不受考試成績影響下被重視。"},{"en":"If memory depends on study duration independent of age, older learners may still remember well.","zh":"如果記憶取決於學習時長而不受年齡影響，年長學習者仍可能記得很好。"},{"en":"The phrase separates one factor from another.","zh":"這個短語把一個因素與另一因素分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"serious deficit","meaning":"嚴重缺損","examples":[{"en":"No serious deficit appeared until later life.","zh":"直到較後人生階段才出現嚴重缺損。"},{"en":"A serious deficit is a major weakness, shortage, or loss in ability.","zh":"「serious deficit」是能力上的重大弱點、不足或喪失。"},{"en":"A child with a serious reading deficit may need extra support at school.","zh":"有嚴重閱讀缺損的孩子可能在學校需要額外支援。"},{"en":"If no serious deficit appears early, normal ageing may not explain every small memory lapse.","zh":"如果早期沒有嚴重缺損，正常老化未必能解釋每個小記憶失誤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an important lack or impairment.","zh":"這個短語描述重要不足或受損。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"degenerative processes of aging","meaning":"老化的退化過程","examples":[{"en":"Later deficits may result from the degenerative processes of aging.","zh":"較後期缺損可能源於老化的退化過程。"},{"en":"Degenerative processes of aging are biological changes that gradually damage or weaken body systems over time.","zh":"「degenerative processes of aging」是隨時間逐漸損害或削弱身體系統的生物變化。"},{"en":"Joint pain in later life may result partly from degenerative processes of aging.","zh":"晚年關節痛可能部分來自老化的退化過程。"},{"en":"If degeneration affects the brain, memory and movement may become harder.","zh":"如果退化影響大腦，記憶和動作可能變得更難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual biological decline linked with ageing.","zh":"這個短語描述與老化相關的逐漸生物衰退。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"cognitive loss","meaning":"認知能力喪失","examples":[{"en":"The decline may be biological rather than a purely cognitive loss.","zh":"這種衰退可能是生物性的，而不是純粹認知能力喪失。"},{"en":"Cognitive loss is a decline in mental abilities such as memory, attention, reasoning, or learning.","zh":"「cognitive loss」是記憶、注意力、推理或學習等心智能力下降。"},{"en":"A patient may be tested for cognitive loss if they often forget familiar tasks.","zh":"如果病人常忘記熟悉任務，可能接受認知能力喪失測試。"},{"en":"If memory problems come from disease, the cause may be biological as well as mental.","zh":"如果記憶問題來自疾病，成因可能既是生物性也是心智性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes loss in thinking ability.","zh":"這個短語描述思考能力的喪失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"metamemory","meaning":"後設記憶","examples":[{"en":"Metamemory is knowledge about how one’s own memory works.","zh":"後設記憶是關於自己記憶如何運作的知識。"},{"en":"Metamemory means awareness of one’s memory strengths, weaknesses, and strategies.","zh":"「metamemory」意思是對自己記憶強項、弱點和策略的認識。"},{"en":"A student uses metamemory when they know they must write new words down or they will forget them.","zh":"當學生知道自己必須寫下新詞，否則會忘記時，他就在使用後設記憶。"},{"en":"If people understand their own memory, they can choose better study methods.","zh":"如果人們理解自己的記憶，他們可以選擇更好的學習方法。"},{"en":"The word describes thinking about one’s own memory.","zh":"這個詞描述思考自己的記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"byproduct of","meaning":"……的副產品","examples":[{"en":"Metamemory may be a byproduct of going to school.","zh":"後設記憶可能是上學的副產品。"},{"en":"A byproduct of something is an extra result that happens because of it, even if it was not the main aim.","zh":"「byproduct of」某事，是因它而出現的額外結果，即使那不是主要目標。"},{"en":"Confidence can be a byproduct of practising public speaking regularly.","zh":"自信可以是定期練習公開演說的副產品。"},{"en":"If schooling teaches children how they learn, better metamemory may develop alongside subject knowledge.","zh":"如果學校教育教孩子他們如何學習，更好的後設記憶可能與學科知識一起發展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an additional result of a process.","zh":"這個短語描述某過程的附帶結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"mental development","meaning":"心智發展","examples":[{"en":"Mental development is especially rapid during childhood.","zh":"心智發展在童年期間尤其快速。"},{"en":"Mental development is the growth of thinking, memory, language, attention, and problem-solving abilities.","zh":"「mental development」是思考、記憶、語言、注意力和解難能力的成長。"},{"en":"Reading with children supports mental development by building language and imagination.","zh":"與孩子一起閱讀透過建立語言和想像力支持心智發展。"},{"en":"If children receive rich stimulation, their mental development may progress more strongly.","zh":"如果孩子得到豐富刺激，其心智發展可能更強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growth of the mind.","zh":"這個短語描述心智成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"question-and-answer process","meaning":"問答過程","examples":[{"en":"The question-and-answer process helps children learn.","zh":"問答過程幫助孩子學習。"},{"en":"A question-and-answer process is learning through asking questions and giving responses.","zh":"「question-and-answer process」是透過提問和回答來學習。"},{"en":"Teachers use a question-and-answer process to check whether students understand a passage.","zh":"老師使用問答過程檢查學生是否理解篇章。"},{"en":"If children answer questions, they practise recalling and organising information.","zh":"如果孩子回答問題，他們會練習回想和組織資料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes interactive learning.","zh":"這個短語描述互動式學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"exam-taking","meaning":"應考","examples":[{"en":"Exam-taking can teach children how their memory works.","zh":"應考可以教孩子了解自己的記憶如何運作。"},{"en":"Exam-taking is the act or experience of sitting tests or examinations.","zh":"「exam-taking」是參加測驗或考試的行為或經驗。"},{"en":"Regular exam-taking may show students which subjects they remember easily and which need revision.","zh":"定期應考可能讓學生看到哪些科目容易記得，哪些需要溫習。"},{"en":"If exams require recall under pressure, students learn about their memory limits.","zh":"如果考試要求在壓力下回想資料，學生會了解自己的記憶限制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the testing experience itself.","zh":"這個短語描述考試經驗本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a broad range of studies","meaning":"廣泛的研究","examples":[{"en":"A broad range of studies examined people over 60.","zh":"廣泛的研究考察了六十歲以上人士。"},{"en":"A broad range of studies means many different kinds of research studies.","zh":"「a broad range of studies」意思是許多不同種類的研究。"},{"en":"A broad range of studies may include surveys, experiments, interviews, and medical tests.","zh":"廣泛的研究可能包括問卷、實驗、訪問和醫療測試。"},{"en":"If many studies point to the same pattern, the conclusion becomes stronger.","zh":"如果許多研究指向同一模式，結論會變得更強。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises variety and quantity of research.","zh":"這個短語強調研究的多樣性和數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the better educated a person is","meaning":"一個人教育程度越高","examples":[{"en":"The better educated a person is, the better they may perform.","zh":"一個人教育程度越高，他們可能表現越好。"},{"en":"The better educated a person is means the more education or training that person has received.","zh":"「the better educated a person is」意思是一個人接受的教育或培訓越多。"},{"en":"The better educated a patient is about medicine, the more carefully they may follow instructions.","zh":"病人對藥物的教育程度越高，越可能小心遵從指示。"},{"en":"If education improves test performance, schooling may build useful mental strategies.","zh":"如果教育改善測試表現，學校教育可能建立有用心智策略。"},{"en":"The phrase sets up a comparison: more education may lead to better results.","zh":"這個短語建立比較：教育越多，結果可能越好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be more likely to","meaning":"更有可能……","examples":[{"en":"Better-educated people are more likely to perform well on tests.","zh":"教育程度較高的人更有可能在測試中表現良好。"},{"en":"To be more likely to do something means to have a higher chance of doing it.","zh":"「be more likely to」做某事，意思是做該事的機會較高。"},{"en":"Students who revise regularly are more likely to remember key examples.","zh":"定期溫習的學生更有可能記住重要例子。"},{"en":"If people receive more education, they may be more likely to use effective memory strategies.","zh":"如果人們接受更多教育，他們可能更有可能使用有效記憶策略。"},{"en":"The phrase describes greater probability, not certainty.","zh":"這個短語描述較高可能性，而不是肯定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"perform better in life","meaning":"在生活中表現較好","examples":[{"en":"Education is associated with performing better in life.","zh":"教育與在生活中表現較好有關。"},{"en":"To perform better in life means to manage work, learning, decisions, and daily challenges more successfully.","zh":"「perform better in life」意思是更成功地處理工作、學習、決定和日常挑戰。"},{"en":"Good reading skills can help people perform better in life because they understand information more easily.","zh":"良好閱讀能力可以幫助人在生活中表現較好，因為他們較容易理解資料。"},{"en":"If education builds confidence and problem-solving, it may support better life outcomes.","zh":"如果教育建立自信和解難能力，它可能支持更好人生結果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad success beyond one test.","zh":"這個短語描述超越單一測驗的廣泛成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"psychological tests","meaning":"心理測試","examples":[{"en":"Better-educated adults often perform well on psychological tests.","zh":"教育程度較高的成年人通常在心理測試中表現良好。"},{"en":"Psychological tests are formal tasks used to measure mental abilities, emotions, or behaviour.","zh":"「psychological tests」是用來量度心智能力、情緒或行為的正式任務。"},{"en":"A psychologist may use psychological tests to assess attention or memory problems.","zh":"心理學家可能使用心理測試評估注意力或記憶問題。"},{"en":"If education affects test-taking strategies, scores on psychological tests may differ.","zh":"如果教育影響應試策略，心理測試分數可能不同。"},{"en":"The phrase describes tests used in psychology.","zh":"這個短語描述心理學中使用的測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"adult novice chess players","meaning":"成年初學棋手","examples":[{"en":"Researchers studied adult novice chess players.","zh":"研究人員研究了成年初學棋手。"},{"en":"Adult novice chess players are grown-up beginners who are new to chess.","zh":"「adult novice chess players」是剛開始學棋的成年初學者。"},{"en":"An adult novice chess player may know how the pieces move but lack advanced strategies.","zh":"成年初學棋手可能知道棋子如何移動，但缺乏高階策略。"},{"en":"If adults are beginners, they may rely on general memory rather than chess expertise.","zh":"如果成年人是初學者，他們可能依靠一般記憶，而不是棋藝專長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes age and skill level together.","zh":"這個短語同時描述年齡和技能水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"child experts","meaning":"兒童專家","examples":[{"en":"The adults were compared with child experts at chess.","zh":"成年人與兒童棋藝專家作比較。"},{"en":"Child experts are children who are highly skilled in a particular activity or subject.","zh":"「child experts」是在某活動或科目中特別熟練的孩子。"},{"en":"A child expert in music may play difficult pieces better than many adults.","zh":"兒童音樂專家可能演奏困難樂曲，比很多成年人更好。"},{"en":"If children have specialised knowledge, they may outperform adults in that specific area.","zh":"如果孩子有專門知識，他們可能在該特定範疇勝過成年人。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts young age with high expertise.","zh":"這個短語把年幼與高度專長作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"random series of numbers","meaning":"隨機數字序列","examples":[{"en":"The participants tried to remember a random series of numbers.","zh":"參加者試圖記住隨機數字序列。"},{"en":"A random series of numbers is a sequence of numbers with no obvious pattern.","zh":"「random series of numbers」是沒有明顯模式的一串數字。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to remember a random series of numbers to test short-term memory.","zh":"老師可能要求學生記住隨機數字序列來測試短期記憶。"},{"en":"If numbers have no pattern, they are harder to organise and recall.","zh":"如果數字沒有模式，它們較難組織和回想。"},{"en":"The phrase describes information that is difficult to remember because it lacks structure.","zh":"這個短語描述因缺乏結構而難記的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"as expected","meaning":"正如預期","examples":[{"en":"As expected, the adults remembered the numbers better.","zh":"正如預期，成年人更好地記住數字。"},{"en":"As expected means the result was what people thought would happen.","zh":"「as expected」意思是結果與人們原先認為會發生的相同。"},{"en":"As expected, students who practised every day performed better in the oral test.","zh":"正如預期，每天練習的學生在口試中表現較好。"},{"en":"If a result matches earlier predictions, writers can use this phrase to introduce it.","zh":"如果結果符合早前預測，作者可以用這個短語引出它。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the result is not surprising.","zh":"這個短語表示結果並不令人意外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"outscore","meaning":"得分高於……","examples":[{"en":"The adults outscored the children on the number task.","zh":"成年人在數字任務中得分高於兒童。"},{"en":"To outscore someone means to get a higher score than them.","zh":"「outscore」某人，意思是分數比他更高。"},{"en":"A student may outscore classmates in vocabulary if they read every day.","zh":"如果學生每天閱讀，他可能在詞彙方面得分高於同學。"},{"en":"If adults outscore children on random numbers, their general memory may be stronger in that task.","zh":"如果成年人在隨機數字任務中得分高於兒童，他們在該任務中的一般記憶可能較強。"},{"en":"The word describes scoring better in a comparison.","zh":"這個詞描述在比較中得分較高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"patterns of chess pieces","meaning":"棋子排列模式","examples":[{"en":"The children remembered patterns of chess pieces more effectively.","zh":"兒童更有效地記住棋子排列模式。"},{"en":"Patterns of chess pieces are arrangements of pieces on a chessboard.","zh":"「patterns of chess pieces」是棋盤上棋子的排列方式。"},{"en":"A chess coach may show students common patterns of pieces from famous games.","zh":"棋藝教練可能向學生展示名局中的常見棋子排列模式。"},{"en":"If a player understands chess patterns, they can remember board positions more easily.","zh":"如果棋手理解棋局模式，他們可以更容易記住棋盤位置。"},{"en":"The phrase describes meaningful arrangements within chess.","zh":"這個短語描述棋中的有意義排列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be arranged on","meaning":"被排列在……上","examples":[{"en":"The chess pieces were arranged on a board.","zh":"棋子被排列在棋盤上。"},{"en":"To be arranged on something means to be placed in a particular order or pattern on its surface.","zh":"「be arranged on」某物，意思是按特定次序或模式放在其表面上。"},{"en":"Books may be arranged on a shelf by subject or author.","zh":"書本可能按科目或作者排列在書架上。"},{"en":"If items are arranged meaningfully, they are easier to remember.","zh":"如果物件被有意義地排列，它們會更容易記住。"},{"en":"The phrase describes placement and organisation on a surface.","zh":"這個短語描述在表面上的放置和組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"better organized","meaning":"組織得更好","examples":[{"en":"The children’s chess knowledge was better organized.","zh":"兒童的棋藝知識組織得更好。"},{"en":"Better organized means arranged more clearly and usefully in the mind or in a system.","zh":"「better organized」意思是在腦中或系統中安排得更清楚和更有用。"},{"en":"A student’s notes become better organized when headings, examples, and summaries are added.","zh":"加入標題、例子和摘要後，學生的筆記會組織得更好。"},{"en":"If knowledge is well organised, new information can fit into it more easily.","zh":"如果知識組織良好，新資料可以更容易放進去。"},{"en":"The phrase describes clearer structure.","zh":"這個短語描述更清楚的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"existing knowledge","meaning":"現有知識","examples":[{"en":"Existing knowledge can support new memory.","zh":"現有知識可以支持新記憶。"},{"en":"Existing knowledge is information a person already knows before learning something new.","zh":"「existing knowledge」是一個人在學新東西前已知道的資料。"},{"en":"A student who knows basic biology can learn genetics more easily because of existing knowledge.","zh":"已懂基本生物的學生可以因現有知識而更容易學遺傳學。"},{"en":"If new facts connect to old knowledge, they are easier to understand and remember.","zh":"如果新事實連接到舊知識，它們更容易理解和記住。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the knowledge already in the mind.","zh":"這個短語描述腦中已存在的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"serve as a framework for","meaning":"作為……的框架","examples":[{"en":"The children’s chess knowledge served as a framework for new memory.","zh":"兒童的棋藝知識作為新記憶的框架。"},{"en":"To serve as a framework for something means to provide a structure that helps organise it.","zh":"「serve as a framework for」某事，意思是提供幫助組織它的結構。"},{"en":"An essay outline can serve as a framework for a student’s argument.","zh":"作文大綱可以作為學生論點的框架。"},{"en":"If existing knowledge provides a framework, new details become easier to place and recall.","zh":"如果現有知識提供框架，新細節會更容易安放和回想。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a structure that supports learning or thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述支持學習或思考的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"specialized knowledge","meaning":"專門知識","examples":[{"en":"Specialized knowledge can improve over time.","zh":"專門知識可以隨時間提升。"},{"en":"Specialized knowledge is deep knowledge about a particular field, skill, or occupation.","zh":"「specialized knowledge」是關於特定領域、技能或職業的深入知識。"},{"en":"A nurse has specialized knowledge about patient care and medical routines.","zh":"護士有關於病人護理和醫療程序的專門知識。"},{"en":"If people work in one field for years, their specialized knowledge may grow even as they age.","zh":"如果人們多年在一個領域工作，他們的專門知識可能即使年長仍會增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes expert knowledge in a specific area.","zh":"這個短語描述特定範疇的專家知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"mental resource","meaning":"心智資源","examples":[{"en":"Specialized knowledge is a valuable mental resource.","zh":"專門知識是一種有價值的心智資源。"},{"en":"A mental resource is a thinking tool or store of knowledge that helps a person solve problems.","zh":"「mental resource」是幫助人解決問題的思考工具或知識儲備。"},{"en":"A student’s vocabulary is a mental resource when writing essays.","zh":"學生寫作文時，詞彙就是一種心智資源。"},{"en":"If someone has strong mental resources, new tasks may become easier to handle.","zh":"如果某人有強大心智資源，新任務可能較容易處理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes useful knowledge or skill stored in the mind.","zh":"這個短語描述腦中有用的知識或技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"improve with time","meaning":"隨時間提升","examples":[{"en":"Some forms of knowledge improve with time.","zh":"有些形式的知識會隨時間提升。"},{"en":"To improve with time means to become better as years or experience increase.","zh":"「improve with time」意思是隨年月或經驗增加而變得更好。"},{"en":"A teacher’s explanations may improve with time after many years of classroom practice.","zh":"經過多年課堂實踐，老師的解釋可能隨時間提升。"},{"en":"If knowledge is used often, experience can make it deeper and better organised.","zh":"如果知識經常使用，經驗可以令它更深入和組織更好。"},{"en":"The phrase describes positive change over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間而來的正面變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"crystallized intelligence","meaning":"晶體智力","examples":[{"en":"Crystallized intelligence can remain strong into old age.","zh":"晶體智力可以到老年仍保持強。"},{"en":"Crystallized intelligence is knowledge and skill built from learning, experience, vocabulary, and facts.","zh":"「crystallized intelligence」是由學習、經驗、詞彙和事實建立的知識和技能。"},{"en":"A retired doctor may still have strong crystallized intelligence about diagnosis and patient care.","zh":"退休醫生可能仍有關於診斷和病人護理的強大晶體智力。"},{"en":"If people keep using their knowledge, this intelligence may remain stable for many years.","zh":"如果人們持續使用知識，這種智力可能多年保持穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts learned knowledge with quick problem-solving speed.","zh":"這個短語把習得知識與快速解難速度作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"one’s occupation","meaning":"某人的職業","examples":[{"en":"Knowledge about one’s occupation may remain stable for decades.","zh":"關於某人職業的知識可能數十年間保持穩定。"},{"en":"One’s occupation is the job or type of work a person does.","zh":"「one’s occupation」是一個人從事的工作或職業種類。"},{"en":"A chef’s occupation requires knowledge of food, timing, hygiene, and taste.","zh":"廚師的職業需要食物、時間掌握、衛生和味道方面的知識。"},{"en":"If people work in the same occupation for years, specialised knowledge may become very strong.","zh":"如果人們多年從事同一職業，專門知識可能變得很強。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a person’s work or profession.","zh":"這個短語指一個人的工作或專業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"decline at all","meaning":"完全沒有下降","examples":[{"en":"Occupational knowledge may not decline at all until late life.","zh":"職業知識直到晚年可能完全沒有下降。"},{"en":"To not decline at all means not to decrease or weaken in any noticeable way.","zh":"「not decline at all」意思是沒有任何明顯減少或變弱。"},{"en":"A person’s reading habit may not decline at all after retirement if they keep reading daily.","zh":"如果一個人退休後仍每天閱讀，閱讀習慣可能完全沒有下降。"},{"en":"If knowledge is used constantly, age may not reduce it for a long time.","zh":"如果知識不斷被使用，年齡可能長時間不會削弱它。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises no decline, not just slow decline.","zh":"這個短語強調沒有下降，而不只是下降慢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"disease or dementia","meaning":"疾病或認知障礙症","examples":[{"en":"Specialized knowledge may remain strong without disease or dementia.","zh":"在沒有疾病或認知障礙症的情況下，專門知識可能保持強大。"},{"en":"Disease or dementia means illness or serious decline in brain function that affects memory and thinking.","zh":"「disease or dementia」指疾病或影響記憶和思考的嚴重腦功能衰退。"},{"en":"A doctor checks for dementia when memory problems interfere with daily life.","zh":"當記憶問題干擾日常生活，醫生會檢查是否有認知障礙症。"},{"en":"If no disease or dementia is present, some kinds of knowledge may remain stable in old age.","zh":"如果沒有疾病或認知障礙症，有些知識到老年仍可能保持穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes medical conditions that can affect cognition.","zh":"這個短語描述可影響認知的醫療狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"remain even longer","meaning":"維持更長時間","examples":[{"en":"Crystallized intelligence may remain even longer in healthy adults.","zh":"晶體智力在健康成人身上可能維持更長時間。"},{"en":"To remain even longer means to continue existing for more time than expected or than another thing.","zh":"「remain even longer」意思是比預期或比另一事物存在更久。"},{"en":"A useful study habit may remain even longer if it becomes part of daily routine.","zh":"如果有用學習習慣成為日常生活一部分，它可能維持更長時間。"},{"en":"If knowledge is well organised, it may last beyond other mental abilities.","zh":"如果知識組織良好，它可能比其他心智能力維持更久。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises extended duration.","zh":"這個短語強調延長的持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be organized by","meaning":"透過……整理","examples":[{"en":"Special knowledge is often organized by a process called chunking.","zh":"專門知識常透過稱為組塊化的過程整理。"},{"en":"To be organized by something means to be arranged through that method or process.","zh":"「be organized by」某事，意思是透過該方法或過程安排。"},{"en":"A student’s notes may be organized by topic, date, or question type.","zh":"學生筆記可以透過題目、日期或題型整理。"},{"en":"If knowledge is organised by patterns, it becomes easier to remember and use.","zh":"如果知識透過模式整理，它會更容易記住和使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the method used to structure information.","zh":"這個短語描述用來組織資料的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"chunking","meaning":"組塊化","examples":[{"en":"Chunking combines related procedures into larger units.","zh":"組塊化把相關程序合併成較大單位。"},{"en":"Chunking is a memory strategy that groups small pieces of information into larger, meaningful units.","zh":"「chunking」是一種記憶策略，把小資訊組成較大而有意義的單位。"},{"en":"A student may remember a phone number by chunking it into groups of three or four digits.","zh":"學生可能透過把電話號碼分成三或四個數字一組來記憶。"},{"en":"If information is chunked, the brain has fewer separate items to hold.","zh":"如果資料被組塊化，大腦需要保持的獨立項目就較少。"},{"en":"The word describes grouping for easier memory.","zh":"這個詞描述為更容易記憶而分組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"merge into","meaning":"合併成……","examples":[{"en":"The mind may merge two procedures into a single command.","zh":"心智可能把兩個程序合併成單一指令。"},{"en":"To merge into something means to combine and become one larger unit.","zh":"「merge into」某物，意思是結合並變成一個較大單位。"},{"en":"Two small classes may merge into one group if there are not enough students.","zh":"如果學生人數不足，兩個小班可能合併成一組。"},{"en":"If repeated actions merge into one mental command, experts can work faster.","zh":"如果重複動作合併成一個心理指令，專家可以工作更快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes separate parts joining together.","zh":"這個短語描述分開的部分結合起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"single command","meaning":"單一指令","examples":[{"en":"Two repeated procedures can become a single mental command.","zh":"兩個重複程序可以變成單一心理指令。"},{"en":"A single command is one instruction that controls or represents several smaller actions.","zh":"「single command」是一項控制或代表幾個較小動作的指示。"},{"en":"A computer shortcut can act as a single command for copying and saving work.","zh":"電腦快捷鍵可以作為複製和儲存工作的單一指令。"},{"en":"If the brain turns many small steps into one command, skilled action becomes faster.","zh":"如果大腦把許多小步驟變成一個指令，熟練動作會更快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes simplification of several actions into one instruction.","zh":"這個短語描述把幾個動作簡化成一項指令。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"apply yourself to","meaning":"專心投入……","examples":[{"en":"You build expertise when you apply yourself to a specific interest.","zh":"當你專心投入某個特定興趣時，你會建立專長。"},{"en":"To apply yourself to something means to work hard and concentrate seriously on it.","zh":"「apply yourself to」某事，意思是努力並認真集中於它。"},{"en":"A student who applies herself to writing will practise, revise, and learn from feedback.","zh":"專心投入寫作的學生會練習、修改並從回饋中學習。"},{"en":"If people apply themselves to one field for years, they develop specialised knowledge.","zh":"如果人們多年專心投入一個領域，他們會發展專門知識。"},{"en":"The phrase describes focused effort over time.","zh":"這個短語描述長時間的集中努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"match each description with","meaning":"將每項描述與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match each description with the correct level of biomimicry.","zh":"考生將每項描述與正確仿生層次配對。"},{"en":"To match each description with something means to connect every description to the correct answer or category.","zh":"「match each description with」某物，意思是把每項描述連接到正確答案或類別。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may match each description with the paragraph that contains the information.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能將每項描述與包含該資料的段落配對。"},{"en":"If candidates match descriptions carefully, they must understand both meaning and evidence.","zh":"如果考生仔細配對描述，他們必須理解意思和證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common matching task in exams.","zh":"這個短語描述考試中的常見配對任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the correct level of","meaning":"……的正確層次","examples":[{"en":"Each example belongs to the correct level of biomimicry.","zh":"每個例子屬於仿生的正確層次。"},{"en":"The correct level of something is the proper stage, category, or degree it belongs to.","zh":"「the correct level of」某事，是它所屬的適當階段、類別或程度。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to choose the correct level of difficulty for their reading book.","zh":"老師可能要求學生為閱讀書選擇正確難度層次。"},{"en":"If an example is placed at the wrong level, the classification becomes inaccurate.","zh":"如果例子放在錯誤層次，分類就會不準確。"},{"en":"The phrase describes accurate categorisation by level.","zh":"這個短語描述按層次作準確分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"appropriate letter","meaning":"適當字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the appropriate letter in each box.","zh":"考生在每個方格中寫上適當字母。"},{"en":"The appropriate letter is the option letter that correctly matches the answer.","zh":"「appropriate letter」是與答案正確配對的選項字母。"},{"en":"In a multiple-choice question, students must write the appropriate letter clearly.","zh":"在多項選擇題中，學生必須清楚寫上適當字母。"},{"en":"If the idea is right but the letter is wrong, the answer may still lose marks.","zh":"如果意思正確但字母錯誤，答案仍可能失分。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the correct exam option symbol.","zh":"這個短語指正確的考試選項符號。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"precise and efficient shapes","meaning":"精確而高效的形狀","examples":[{"en":"The first level mimics nature’s precise and efficient shapes.","zh":"第一層次模仿大自然精確而高效的形狀。"},{"en":"Precise and efficient shapes are forms that are exact, well-designed, and use little wasted material or energy.","zh":"「precise and efficient shapes」是準確、設計良好，並少浪費材料或能量的形態。"},{"en":"A bicycle helmet may copy precise and efficient natural shapes to stay strong but light.","zh":"單車頭盔可能模仿精確而高效的自然形狀，以保持堅固但輕巧。"},{"en":"If a shape is efficient, it can perform well without unnecessary weight or complexity.","zh":"如果形狀高效，它可以在沒有不必要重量或複雜度下表現良好。"},{"en":"The phrase describes design inspired by effective natural forms.","zh":"這個短語描述受有效自然形態啟發的設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"imitate biochemical recipes","meaning":"模仿生化配方","examples":[{"en":"The second level imitates natural processes and biochemical recipes.","zh":"第二層次模仿自然過程和生化配方。"},{"en":"To imitate biochemical recipes means to copy the chemical processes living things use to make materials.","zh":"「imitate biochemical recipes」意思是模仿生物用來製造材料的化學過程。"},{"en":"Scientists may imitate biochemical recipes when designing glues inspired by shellfish.","zh":"科學家設計受貝類啟發的膠水時，可能模仿生化配方。"},{"en":"If industry copies nature’s chemistry, it may produce materials with less heat or waste.","zh":"如果工業模仿自然化學，它可能以較少熱力或廢物生產材料。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning from biological chemistry.","zh":"這個短語描述向生物化學學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"create symbiotic relationships","meaning":"建立共生關係","examples":[{"en":"The third level creates symbiotic relationships between industries.","zh":"第三層次在產業之間建立共生關係。"},{"en":"To create symbiotic relationships means to build partnerships in which different sides benefit from one another.","zh":"「create symbiotic relationships」意思是建立不同方面互相受益的合作關係。"},{"en":"A school and a library can create a symbiotic relationship by sharing space and reading programmes.","zh":"學校和圖書館可以透過共享空間和閱讀計劃建立共生關係。"},{"en":"If one factory’s waste becomes another factory’s resource, both can benefit.","zh":"如果一間工廠的廢物變成另一間工廠的資源，雙方都可以受益。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mutually helpful connections.","zh":"這個短語描述互惠互助的連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"synthesised plastic","meaning":"合成塑膠","examples":[{"en":"A synthesised plastic can incorporate waste carbon dioxide.","zh":"合成塑膠可以納入廢棄二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Synthesised plastic is plastic made through chemical production rather than taken directly from nature.","zh":"「synthesised plastic」是透過化學生產製成，而不是直接取自自然的塑膠。"},{"en":"A lab may create a synthesised plastic for packaging or medical devices.","zh":"實驗室可能為包裝或醫療裝置創造合成塑膠。"},{"en":"If a synthesised plastic uses waste gas, manufacturing may become less wasteful.","zh":"如果合成塑膠使用廢氣，製造過程可能變得較少浪費。"},{"en":"The phrase describes man-made plastic produced by chemical methods.","zh":"這個短語描述由化學方法製造的人造塑膠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"recycle a waste gas","meaning":"循環再用廢氣","examples":[{"en":"The manufacturing process can recycle a waste gas.","zh":"製造過程可以循環再用廢氣。"},{"en":"To recycle a waste gas means to capture a gas that would be discarded and use it again.","zh":"「recycle a waste gas」意思是捕捉本會被棄置的氣體並再次使用。"},{"en":"A factory may recycle waste gas instead of releasing all of it into the air.","zh":"工廠可能循環再用廢氣，而不是把它全部排放到空氣中。"},{"en":"If waste gas becomes a raw material, pollution and production costs may both fall.","zh":"如果廢氣變成原材料，污染和生產成本可能都下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes turning unwanted gas into a useful resource.","zh":"這個短語描述把不需要的氣體變成有用資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"produce a range of","meaning":"生產一系列……","examples":[{"en":"Cosmetics companies produce a range of iridescent products.","zh":"化妝品公司生產一系列閃彩產品。"},{"en":"To produce a range of products means to make several different types of products.","zh":"「produce a range of」產品，意思是製造幾種不同種類的產品。"},{"en":"A bakery may produce a range of breads, cakes, and biscuits.","zh":"麵包店可能生產一系列麵包、蛋糕和餅乾。"},{"en":"If customers have different needs, companies may produce a wider range of choices.","zh":"如果顧客有不同需要，公司可能生產更廣泛的選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises variety in production.","zh":"這個短語強調生產中的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"iridescent cosmetics","meaning":"閃彩化妝品","examples":[{"en":"Natural optical structures have inspired iridescent cosmetics.","zh":"自然光學結構啟發了閃彩化妝品。"},{"en":"Iridescent cosmetics are makeup products that appear to change colour or shine with rainbow-like effects.","zh":"「iridescent cosmetics」是看似會變色或呈現彩虹般光澤的化妝品。"},{"en":"A teenager may choose iridescent cosmetics for a festival because they reflect light brightly.","zh":"青少年可能在節日選擇閃彩化妝品，因為它們會明亮反光。"},{"en":"If designers copy natural colour structures, cosmetics can shine without ordinary pigments alone.","zh":"如果設計者模仿自然顏色結構，化妝品可以不只靠普通色素而閃亮。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shimmering makeup inspired by light effects.","zh":"這個短語描述受光學效果啟發的閃亮化妝品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"take inspiration from nature","meaning":"從大自然取得靈感","examples":[{"en":"Researchers take inspiration from nature to solve technical problems.","zh":"研究人員從大自然取得靈感來解決技術問題。"},{"en":"To take inspiration from nature means to learn design ideas from plants, animals, or natural systems.","zh":"「take inspiration from nature」意思是從植物、動物或自然系統學習設計想法。"},{"en":"Engineers may take inspiration from birds when designing lighter aircraft wings.","zh":"工程師設計更輕的機翼時，可能從鳥類取得靈感。"},{"en":"If nature has solved a problem through evolution, designers may copy the principle.","zh":"如果大自然透過演化解決了某問題，設計者可能模仿其原理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using nature as a source of ideas.","zh":"這個短語描述把大自然作為想法來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"remove excess salt","meaning":"去除多餘鹽分","examples":[{"en":"Desalination systems remove excess salt from water.","zh":"海水淡化系統從水中去除多餘鹽分。"},{"en":"To remove excess salt means to take out too much salt from a substance, especially water.","zh":"「remove excess salt」意思是從物質，尤其是水中取出過多鹽分。"},{"en":"A water filter may remove excess salt before seawater can be used for drinking.","zh":"海水可作飲用前，濾水器可能去除多餘鹽分。"},{"en":"If excess salt remains in water, people cannot drink it safely.","zh":"如果水中仍有過多鹽分，人們就不能安全飲用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reducing salt to a usable level.","zh":"這個短語描述把鹽分減至可用水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"become part of","meaning":"成為……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"A manufacturing company can become part of an economic ecosystem.","zh":"製造公司可以成為經濟生態系統的一部分。"},{"en":"To become part of something means to join it or be included in it.","zh":"「become part of」某物，意思是加入它或被包含在其中。"},{"en":"A new student becomes part of the class when classmates include them in activities.","zh":"當同學把新學生包括在活動中，他就成為班級的一部分。"},{"en":"If a company becomes part of a network, it can exchange resources with others.","zh":"如果公司成為網絡的一部分，它可以與其他公司交換資源。"},{"en":"The phrase describes joining a larger system.","zh":"這個短語描述加入較大系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"prevent bacterial growth","meaning":"防止細菌生長","examples":[{"en":"Natural chemicals from seaweed can prevent bacterial growth.","zh":"來自海藻的天然化學物可以防止細菌生長。"},{"en":"To prevent bacterial growth means to stop bacteria from multiplying.","zh":"「prevent bacterial growth」意思是阻止細菌繁殖。"},{"en":"Refrigeration can prevent bacterial growth in fresh food for a limited time.","zh":"冷藏可以在有限時間內防止新鮮食物中的細菌生長。"},{"en":"If bacteria cannot grow, food, medicine, or surfaces may stay safer for longer.","zh":"如果細菌不能生長，食物、藥物或表面可能保持更安全更久。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stopping harmful microorganisms from increasing.","zh":"這個短語描述阻止有害微生物增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether each statement agrees with the information given.","zh":"考生判斷每項陳述是否與所給資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"「agree with the information given」意思是符合篇章所說。"},{"en":"In a reading exam, an answer agrees with the text only when the evidence is clearly stated.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，只有證據清楚寫出，答案才與文本一致。"},{"en":"If a statement adds something not mentioned, it may not agree with the information.","zh":"如果陳述加入未提及內容，它可能不與資料一致。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds candidates to use the passage, not outside knowledge.","zh":"這個短語提醒考生使用篇章，而不是外部知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to state the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"「contradict the information」意思是陳述與篇章所說相反的內容。"},{"en":"If a passage says biomimicry is not new, saying it is completely new contradicts the information.","zh":"如果篇章說仿生學並非新事物，說它完全新就與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"When a statement contradicts the text, candidates should not mark it as true.","zh":"當陳述與文本矛盾時，考生不應把它標為真。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a direct conflict with the source.","zh":"這個短語描述與來源直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"The answer is not given if there is no information on this.","zh":"如果沒有這方面的資料，答案就是 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the passage does not tell us whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"「no information on this」意思是篇章沒有告訴我們陳述是真還是假。"},{"en":"If a text never mentions the price of a product, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文本從未提及產品價格，就沒有這方面的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from common sense when the passage gives no evidence.","zh":"當篇章沒有證據時，學生不應憑常識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase is used for NOT GIVEN answers in reading tasks.","zh":"這個短語用於閱讀題中的 NOT GIVEN 答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"completely new concept","meaning":"全新的概念","examples":[{"en":"Biomimicry is not a completely new concept.","zh":"仿生學並不是全新的概念。"},{"en":"A completely new concept is an idea that has never existed or been used before.","zh":"「completely new concept」是從未存在或從未被使用過的想法。"},{"en":"Online learning was not a completely new concept before schools used it widely.","zh":"在學校廣泛使用網上學習之前，它並不是全新的概念。"},{"en":"If people have copied nature for centuries, biomimicry cannot be described as entirely new.","zh":"如果人們數百年來一直模仿自然，仿生學就不能被描述為完全新。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses absolute novelty.","zh":"這個短語強調絕對的新穎性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"emerge only recently","meaning":"只在最近才出現","examples":[{"en":"The practice did not emerge only recently.","zh":"這種做法並不是只在最近才出現。"},{"en":"To emerge only recently means to appear or become known only in the near past.","zh":"「emerge only recently」意思是只在不久前才出現或被人知道。"},{"en":"Online shopping did not emerge only recently, but it became much more common later.","zh":"網上購物並不是只在最近才出現，但後來變得普及很多。"},{"en":"If an idea has old examples, it did not begin only in modern times.","zh":"如果一個想法有舊例子，它就不是只在現代才開始。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on when something first appeared.","zh":"這個短語集中於某事最初何時出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the first designer to","meaning":"首位……的設計師","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Leonardo was the first designer to mimic nature.","zh":"該陳述問 Leonardo 是否是首位模仿自然的設計師。"},{"en":"The first designer to do something is the earliest known person to use that design approach.","zh":"「the first designer to」做某事，指最早已知使用該設計方法的人。"},{"en":"A history question may ask who was the first designer to use steel in a certain building style.","zh":"歷史題可能問誰是首位在某建築風格中使用鋼材的設計師。"},{"en":"If earlier examples exist, someone later cannot be called the first designer.","zh":"如果有更早例子，較後的人就不能被稱為首位設計師。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies priority in design history.","zh":"這個短語指出設計歷史中的先後地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"involve more than","meaning":"不只涉及……","examples":[{"en":"Biomimicry involves more than simply copying natural shapes.","zh":"仿生學不只涉及單純模仿自然形狀。"},{"en":"To involve more than something means to include additional or deeper elements beyond it.","zh":"「involve more than」某事，意思是包括超出它的額外或更深入元素。"},{"en":"Good writing involves more than correct grammar; it also needs ideas and structure.","zh":"好寫作不只涉及正確文法；它也需要想法和結構。"},{"en":"If biomimicry studies processes and systems, it is broader than surface imitation.","zh":"如果仿生學研究過程和系統，它就比表面模仿更廣。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show that an idea is more complex than it first seems.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示想法比最初看來更複雜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"simply copy shapes","meaning":"單純模仿形狀","examples":[{"en":"Advanced biomimicry does not simply copy shapes from nature.","zh":"高階仿生學並不單純模仿自然形狀。"},{"en":"To simply copy shapes means to imitate only the outside form without copying deeper function or process.","zh":"「simply copy shapes」意思是只模仿外在形態，而不模仿更深層功能或過程。"},{"en":"A student who simply copies a model essay may miss how the argument works.","zh":"只單純抄襲範文的學生可能錯過論點如何運作。"},{"en":"If designers only copy appearance, they may not gain the real efficiency of natural systems.","zh":"如果設計者只模仿外觀，他們可能得不到自然系統真正的效率。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts surface imitation with deeper understanding.","zh":"這個短語把表面模仿與深層理解作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"current findings","meaning":"目前研究結果","examples":[{"en":"Current findings suggest substantial reductions in energy use.","zh":"目前研究結果顯示能源使用可大幅減少。"},{"en":"Current findings are the latest results or conclusions from research.","zh":"「current findings」是研究中的最新結果或結論。"},{"en":"Current findings from a school survey may show that students need more quiet study space.","zh":"學校調查的目前結果可能顯示學生需要更多安靜學習空間。"},{"en":"If current findings are strong, they may influence design, policy, or future research.","zh":"如果目前研究結果有力，它們可能影響設計、政策或未來研究。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to evidence available at the present time.","zh":"這個短語指目前可得的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"up to 40 percent","meaning":"高達百分之四十","examples":[{"en":"Existing methods can reduce energy consumption by up to 40 percent.","zh":"現有方法可以將能源消耗減少高達百分之四十。"},{"en":"Up to 40 percent means the maximum amount can be 40 percent, though it may be less.","zh":"「up to 40 percent」意思是最高可達百分之四十，但也可能較少。"},{"en":"A shop sale offering up to 40 percent off does not mean every item is reduced by 40 percent.","zh":"商店減價高達四折，並不表示每件貨品都減價四成。"},{"en":"If energy use falls by up to 40 percent, the saving can be substantial.","zh":"如果能源使用減少高達百分之四十，節省可以很可觀。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an upper limit, not a guaranteed exact figure.","zh":"這個短語提供上限，而不是保證的準確數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"best-selling product","meaning":"暢銷產品","examples":[{"en":"The statement describes the prototype car as a best-selling product.","zh":"該陳述把原型車描述為暢銷產品。"},{"en":"A best-selling product is a product that sells in very large numbers compared with others.","zh":"「best-selling product」是相比其他產品銷量非常高的產品。"},{"en":"A phone may become a best-selling product if it is reliable, affordable, and well advertised.","zh":"如果電話可靠、價格合理且宣傳良好，它可能成為暢銷產品。"},{"en":"If a prototype has not yet been sold widely, it cannot truly be a best-selling product.","zh":"如果原型尚未廣泛銷售，它就不能真正成為暢銷產品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes commercial success in sales.","zh":"這個短語描述銷售上的商業成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"seek solutions beyond","meaning":"在……以外尋找解決方法","examples":[{"en":"Some companies seek solutions beyond their own industries.","zh":"有些公司在自己所屬行業以外尋找解決方法。"},{"en":"To seek solutions beyond something means to look outside the usual area for answers.","zh":"「seek solutions beyond」某範圍，意思是在通常範圍外尋找答案。"},{"en":"A teacher may seek solutions beyond textbooks by using games, interviews, and real examples.","zh":"老師可能在課本以外尋找解決方法，例如使用遊戲、訪問和真實例子。"},{"en":"If companies look beyond their own field, they may find ideas from nature or other industries.","zh":"如果公司跳出自己領域尋找，它們可能從自然或其他行業找到想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes searching outside familiar boundaries.","zh":"這個短語描述在熟悉邊界以外搜尋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"one’s own industry","meaning":"自己所屬的行業","examples":[{"en":"Companies can learn from specialists outside their own industry.","zh":"公司可以向自己所屬行業以外的專家學習。"},{"en":"One’s own industry is the business field or sector in which a person or company works.","zh":"「one’s own industry」是個人或公司工作的商業領域或部門。"},{"en":"A restaurant belongs to the food industry, while a hospital belongs to the healthcare industry.","zh":"餐廳屬於飲食業，而醫院屬於醫療行業。"},{"en":"If a company learns from another industry, it may solve old problems in fresh ways.","zh":"如果公司向另一行業學習，它可能以新方式解決舊問題。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a company’s usual professional field.","zh":"這個短語指出公司通常所屬的專業領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"apply the microstructure of","meaning":"將……的微觀結構應用於……","examples":[{"en":"The paint company applied the microstructure of the lotus leaf to its products.","zh":"油漆公司將蓮葉的微觀結構應用於其產品。"},{"en":"To apply the microstructure of something means to use its tiny surface design or pattern in another product.","zh":"「apply the microstructure of」某物，意思是把其微小表面設計或模式用於另一產品。"},{"en":"Engineers may apply the microstructure of shark skin to surfaces that reduce drag.","zh":"工程師可能將鯊魚皮的微觀結構應用於減少阻力的表面。"},{"en":"If a product copies a useful natural surface, it may gain the same practical function.","zh":"如果產品模仿有用的自然表面，它可能獲得相同實際功能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using microscopic natural design in technology.","zh":"這個短語描述在科技中使用微觀自然設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"increase production","meaning":"提高產量","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether the brewery increased production.","zh":"該陳述問啤酒廠是否提高產量。"},{"en":"To increase production means to make more goods or output than before.","zh":"「increase production」意思是製造比以前更多貨品或產出。"},{"en":"A bakery may increase production before a festival because customers buy more bread and cakes.","zh":"麵包店可能在節日前提高產量，因為顧客購買更多麵包和蛋糕。"},{"en":"If demand rises, a factory may add workers or machines to produce more.","zh":"如果需求上升，工廠可能增加工人或機器來生產更多。"},{"en":"The phrase describes raising the amount being made.","zh":"這個短語描述提高製造量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 154 - Memory and Age.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 156":[{"front":"Art in Iron and Steel","meaning":"鋼鐵中的藝術","examples":[{"en":"Art in iron and steel shows how engineering structures can possess artistic value.","zh":"鋼鐵中的藝術顯示工程結構如何可以具有藝術價值。"},{"en":"Art in iron and steel means artistic beauty found in bridges, factories, machines and other metal structures.","zh":"鋼鐵中的藝術指在橋樑、工廠、機器和其他金屬結構中發現的藝術美。"},{"en":"A photographer may see art in iron and steel when sunlight falls across a railway bridge.","zh":"當陽光照在鐵路橋上，攝影師可能看見鋼鐵中的藝術。"},{"en":"If people look carefully at engineering forms, they may notice rhythm, balance and beauty.","zh":"如果人們仔細觀察工程形態，可能會注意到節奏、平衡和美感。"},{"en":"The phrase challenges the idea that metal structures are only practical and never artistic.","zh":"這個短語挑戰金屬結構只具實用性、從不具藝術性的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"works of engineering and technology","meaning":"工程及科技作品","examples":[{"en":"Works of engineering and technology can inspire artists and photographers.","zh":"工程及科技作品可以啟發藝術家和攝影師。"},{"en":"Works of engineering and technology are human-made structures, machines or systems created through technical skill.","zh":"工程及科技作品是透過技術能力創造出來的人造結構、機器或系統。"},{"en":"Bridges, dams, railway stations and skyscrapers are works of engineering and technology.","zh":"橋樑、水壩、火車站和摩天大廈都是工程及科技作品。"},{"en":"If such works are large or beautifully designed, they can become artistic subjects.","zh":"如果這些作品規模巨大或設計優美，就可以成為藝術題材。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical creations that may also carry visual and cultural value.","zh":"這個短語指實用創造物，也可能具有視覺和文化價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be viewed as the antithesis of","meaning":"被視為與……完全對立","examples":[{"en":"Engineering is sometimes viewed as the antithesis of art and humanity.","zh":"工程有時被視為與藝術和人性完全對立。"},{"en":"To be viewed as the antithesis of something means to be seen as its complete opposite.","zh":"“Be viewed as the antithesis of” 某事指被看成與它完全相反。"},{"en":"A strict exam system may be viewed as the antithesis of creativity if it leaves no room for imagination.","zh":"如果嚴格考試制度完全沒有想像空間，它可能被視為與創意完全對立。"},{"en":"If technology is seen only as cold and mechanical, people may view it as opposed to art.","zh":"如果科技只被看成冰冷機械，人們可能把它視為與藝術相反。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a strong contrast, often based on public perception.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈對比，常基於公眾觀感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"art and humanity","meaning":"藝術與人性","examples":[{"en":"Some critics believe that industrial technology conflicts with art and humanity.","zh":"有些批評者認為工業科技與藝術和人性衝突。"},{"en":"Art and humanity refer to creativity, feeling, dignity and the human side of culture.","zh":"藝術與人性指創造力、情感、尊嚴和文化中人性化的一面。"},{"en":"A school values art and humanity when it teaches music, literature and empathy, not only science.","zh":"如果學校不只教科學，也教音樂、文學和同理心，就是重視藝術與人性。"},{"en":"If a workplace treats people like machines, critics may say it lacks humanity.","zh":"如果工作場所把人當成機器，批評者可能說它缺乏人性。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts human creativity and feeling with cold efficiency.","zh":"這個短語把人類創意和情感與冰冷效率作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the connotations of","meaning":"……所帶有的含意","examples":[{"en":"The connotations of assembly lines are not always positive.","zh":"生產線所帶有的含意並不總是正面的。"},{"en":"The connotations of a word or image are the feelings and associations it suggests beyond its literal meaning.","zh":"一個詞或影像所帶有的含意，是它在字面意思以外暗示的感覺和聯想。"},{"en":"The word “home” has warm connotations of safety, family and belonging.","zh":"“Home” 這個詞帶有安全、家庭和歸屬感的溫暖含意。"},{"en":"If assembly lines suggest boredom and pressure, their connotations can be negative.","zh":"如果生產線令人聯想到沉悶和壓力，其含意就可以是負面的。"},{"en":"The phrase helps discuss implied meanings rather than direct definitions.","zh":"這個短語幫助討論隱含意思，而不是直接定義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"assembly lines","meaning":"生產線","examples":[{"en":"Assembly lines are often associated with repetitive industrial work.","zh":"生產線常與重複的工業工作聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Assembly lines are factory systems in which products move from worker to worker for different tasks.","zh":"生產線是工廠系統，產品會由一名工人移到另一名工人，以完成不同工序。"},{"en":"A toy factory may use assembly lines so each worker adds one part before the toy moves on.","zh":"玩具工廠可能使用生產線，讓每名工人在玩具移走前加入一個零件。"},{"en":"Assembly lines can increase efficiency, but they may also make work feel repetitive.","zh":"生產線可以提高效率，但也可能令工作感覺重複。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests mass production and standardised labour.","zh":"這個短語常暗示大量生產和標準化勞動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"positive values","meaning":"正面價值","examples":[{"en":"Technological creations may contain important positive values.","zh":"科技創造物可能包含重要正面價值。"},{"en":"Positive values are good qualities or meanings, such as usefulness, creativity, courage or public benefit.","zh":"正面價值是良好特質或意義，例如實用性、創意、勇氣或公共利益。"},{"en":"A public library has positive values because it supports learning and community life.","zh":"公共圖書館具有正面價值，因為它支持學習和社區生活。"},{"en":"If a bridge connects neighbourhoods safely, it has social as well as technical value.","zh":"如果一座橋安全連接社區，它就同時具有社會和技術價值。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show that technology can be meaningful, not merely mechanical.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示科技可以有意義，而不只是機械化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"creations of the mind","meaning":"心智創造的成果","examples":[{"en":"Bridges and machines are creations of the human mind.","zh":"橋樑和機器是人類心智創造的成果。"},{"en":"Creations of the mind are things designed or imagined through human thought and intelligence.","zh":"心智創造的成果，是透過人類思想和智慧設計或想像出來的事物。"},{"en":"A poem, a computer programme and a bridge can all be creations of the mind.","zh":"詩、電腦程式和橋樑都可以是心智創造的成果。"},{"en":"If people recognise machines as mental creations, they may see imagination behind engineering.","zh":"如果人們把機器視為心智成果，就可能看見工程背後的想像力。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises human thought behind physical objects.","zh":"這個短語強調實體物件背後的人類思想。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"human industry","meaning":"人類的勤勞與創造力","examples":[{"en":"Major engineering projects demonstrate human industry and imagination.","zh":"重大工程項目展現人類的勤勞與想像力。"},{"en":"Human industry means human hard work, skill and organised effort.","zh":"人類的勤勞與創造力指人類的努力、技術和有組織行動。"},{"en":"A community garden shows human industry when neighbours plan, dig, plant and maintain it together.","zh":"當鄰居一起規劃、挖土、種植和維護社區花園時，它就展現人類勤勞。"},{"en":"If a dam takes years to build, it reflects long-term human industry.","zh":"如果水壩需要多年建成，它就反映長期的人類勤勞。"},{"en":"The phrase praises effort as well as creativity.","zh":"這個短語既讚揚努力，也讚揚創意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be overwhelmed by","meaning":"被……蓋過","examples":[{"en":"The benefits of technology can be overwhelmed by negative public images.","zh":"科技的好處可能被負面公眾形象蓋過。"},{"en":"To be overwhelmed by something means to be covered, weakened or made less noticeable by it.","zh":"“Be overwhelmed by” 某事指被它覆蓋、削弱或變得不明顯。"},{"en":"A student’s good ideas may be overwhelmed by messy handwriting in an exam essay.","zh":"學生的好想法可能在考試作文中被凌亂字跡蓋過。"},{"en":"If people only see factory pollution, the positive side of engineering may be hidden.","zh":"如果人們只看見工廠污染，工程的正面一面可能被隱藏。"},{"en":"The phrase shows one force becoming stronger than another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一種力量壓過另一種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"associated negative images","meaning":"相關的負面形象","examples":[{"en":"Industrial work has many associated negative images.","zh":"工業工作有許多相關的負面形象。"},{"en":"Associated negative images are unfavourable pictures or ideas linked with something in people’s minds.","zh":"相關的負面形象，是在人們心中與某事連繫的不利畫面或想法。"},{"en":"Long queues have associated negative images of wasted time and frustration.","zh":"長隊帶有浪費時間和沮喪的相關負面形象。"},{"en":"If factories are linked with smoke and dull labour, their associated images can harm public opinion.","zh":"如果工廠與煙霧和沉悶勞動相連，其相關形象可損害公眾觀感。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to mental associations, not necessarily the full reality.","zh":"這個短語指心理聯想，不一定是完整現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"repetitive and stressful jobs","meaning":"重複而壓力大的工作","examples":[{"en":"Assembly-line work is often linked to repetitive and stressful jobs.","zh":"生產線工作常與重複而壓力大的工作相連。"},{"en":"Repetitive and stressful jobs involve doing the same tasks again and again under pressure.","zh":"重複而壓力大的工作，是在壓力下反覆做相同任務。"},{"en":"A cashier may find work repetitive and stressful during a long holiday rush.","zh":"收銀員在漫長假日購物高峰期間，可能覺得工作重複而壓力大。"},{"en":"If workers repeat one movement all day, they may feel bored, tired or treated like machines.","zh":"如果工人整天重複同一動作，他們可能感到沉悶、疲倦或被當成機器。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both sameness and pressure at work.","zh":"這個短語同時描述工作中的重複性和壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"threatened jobs","meaning":"受威脅的職位","examples":[{"en":"Automation can create fears about threatened jobs.","zh":"自動化可以令人擔心職位受威脅。"},{"en":"Threatened jobs are jobs that may disappear or be reduced because of change.","zh":"受威脅的職位，是因變化而可能消失或減少的工作。"},{"en":"Shop workers may worry about threatened jobs when self-checkout machines spread.","zh":"當自助付款機普及，店員可能擔心職位受威脅。"},{"en":"If new machines replace human tasks, workers may fear unemployment.","zh":"如果新機器取代人類任務，工人可能害怕失業。"},{"en":"The phrase usually appears when technology or economic change creates job insecurity.","zh":"這個短語通常出現在科技或經濟變化造成工作不穩時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fuel the arguments of","meaning":"為……的論點提供理據","examples":[{"en":"Images of poor working conditions fuel the arguments of critics.","zh":"惡劣工作環境的影像為批評者的論點提供理據。"},{"en":"To fuel the arguments of someone means to provide evidence or emotion that makes their claims stronger.","zh":"“Fuel the arguments of” 某人指提供證據或情緒，使其主張更有力。"},{"en":"A failed school policy may fuel the arguments of parents who already wanted reform.","zh":"失敗的校政可能為本來已要求改革的家長論點提供理據。"},{"en":"If photos show unsafe factories, they can strengthen criticism of industrial systems.","zh":"如果照片顯示工廠不安全，就能加強對工業體系的批評。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests adding energy to an existing debate.","zh":"這個短語暗示為既有辯論增加力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"critics of technology","meaning":"科技批評者","examples":[{"en":"Critics of technology often focus on its effects on workers.","zh":"科技批評者常集中於科技對工人的影響。"},{"en":"Critics of technology are people who question or oppose certain uses of modern tools, machines or systems.","zh":"科技批評者是質疑或反對某些現代工具、機器或系統用途的人。"},{"en":"Some critics of technology worry that children spend too much time on screens.","zh":"一些科技批評者擔心孩子花太多時間看螢幕。"},{"en":"If technology harms privacy or jobs, critics may demand stricter rules.","zh":"如果科技損害私隱或職位，批評者可能要求更嚴格規則。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people who challenge technological progress or its consequences.","zh":"這個短語指挑戰科技進步或其後果的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"even as","meaning":"即使同時","examples":[{"en":"Some people criticise technology even as they benefit from it.","zh":"有些人批評科技，即使同時從中受益。"},{"en":"Even as means at the same time as, often showing contrast or irony.","zh":"“Even as” 指在同一時間，常顯示對比或諷刺。"},{"en":"A student may complain about online homework even as it helps them submit work quickly.","zh":"學生可能抱怨網上功課，即使它同時幫助他快速交功課。"},{"en":"If people use the Internet to attack modern technology, their actions contain irony.","zh":"如果人們使用互聯網攻擊現代科技，他們的行為就帶有諷刺。"},{"en":"The phrase shows two things happening together in a surprising way.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩件事以令人意外的方式同時發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"drive powerful cars","meaning":"駕駛高性能汽車","examples":[{"en":"Some critics drive powerful cars while opposing industrial development.","zh":"有些批評者一邊反對工業發展，一邊駕駛高性能汽車。"},{"en":"To drive powerful cars means to use cars with strong engines and high performance.","zh":"駕駛高性能汽車指使用引擎強、性能高的汽車。"},{"en":"A businessperson may drive a powerful car because they enjoy speed and status.","zh":"商人可能因喜歡速度和地位感而駕駛高性能汽車。"},{"en":"If someone attacks industry but enjoys high-performance machines, others may see contradiction.","zh":"如果某人批評工業卻享受高性能機器，其他人可能看見矛盾。"},{"en":"The phrase can suggest comfort with technology in daily life.","zh":"這個短語可以暗示日常生活中對科技的依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"use the Internet to protest","meaning":"使用互聯網抗議","examples":[{"en":"Campaigners may use the Internet to protest against modern technology.","zh":"活動人士可能使用互聯網抗議現代科技。"},{"en":"To use the Internet to protest means to spread criticism or organise opposition online.","zh":"使用互聯網抗議指在網上傳播批評或組織反對行動。"},{"en":"Students may use the Internet to protest against a school rule by sharing petitions.","zh":"學生可能透過分享請願書，使用互聯網抗議校規。"},{"en":"If people protest technology through websites, they rely on the very system they criticise.","zh":"如果人們透過網站抗議科技，他們就依賴自己批評的系統。"},{"en":"The phrase can reveal irony between message and method.","zh":"這個短語可以揭示訊息與方法之間的諷刺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"artless aspects of","meaning":"……缺乏藝術性的方面","examples":[{"en":"Critics object to what they see as the artless aspects of industrial life.","zh":"批評者反對他們所看見的工業生活中缺乏藝術性的方面。"},{"en":"Artless aspects of something are parts that seem plain, ugly, mechanical or lacking beauty.","zh":"某事缺乏藝術性的方面，是看似平板、醜陋、機械化或缺乏美感的部分。"},{"en":"A shopping mall may have artless aspects if every floor looks identical and lifeless.","zh":"如果商場每層都看起來一模一樣且沒有生氣，它可能有缺乏藝術性的方面。"},{"en":"If factory work feels purely repetitive, people may see it as lacking artistic or human value.","zh":"如果工廠工作感覺純粹重複，人們可能認為它缺乏藝術或人性價值。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises something for seeming without creativity or grace.","zh":"這個短語批評某事看似缺乏創意或優雅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"dehumanising aspects of","meaning":"……使人失去人性的方面","examples":[{"en":"Repetitive work may reveal the dehumanising aspects of industrial production.","zh":"重複工作可能揭示工業生產使人失去人性的方面。"},{"en":"Dehumanising aspects of something are parts that make people feel less valued as human beings.","zh":"某事使人失去人性的方面，是令人成為人這一點不被重視的部分。"},{"en":"A workplace has dehumanising aspects if staff are treated only as numbers.","zh":"如果員工只被當成數字，工作場所就有使人失去人性的方面。"},{"en":"If workers cannot rest, speak or use judgement, the job may feel dehumanising.","zh":"如果工人不能休息、說話或運用判斷，工作可能令人感到被去人性化。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on loss of dignity and individuality.","zh":"這個短語強調尊嚴和個體性的喪失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"industrialised society","meaning":"工業化社會","examples":[{"en":"Technology plays a central role in an industrialised society.","zh":"科技在工業化社會中扮演核心角色。"},{"en":"An industrialised society is a society whose economy depends heavily on factories, machines and large-scale production.","zh":"工業化社會是經濟高度依賴工廠、機器和大規模生產的社會。"},{"en":"In an industrialised society, many goods are made by machines rather than by hand.","zh":"在工業化社會中，許多貨品由機器而不是人手製造。"},{"en":"If a society industrialises, work, cities and transport systems often change rapidly.","zh":"如果一個社會工業化，工作、城市和交通系統往往快速改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a society shaped by industry.","zh":"這個短語描述由工業塑造的社會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"digitised society","meaning":"數碼化社會","examples":[{"en":"Computers are essential to a highly digitised society.","zh":"電腦對高度數碼化社會至關重要。"},{"en":"A digitised society is a society where information, work and services are handled through digital systems.","zh":"數碼化社會是資訊、工作和服務透過數碼系統處理的社會。"},{"en":"Online banking, electronic health records and e-learning are signs of a digitised society.","zh":"網上銀行、電子健康紀錄和電子學習都是數碼化社會的標誌。"},{"en":"If a society becomes digitised, people need digital skills to study, work and access services.","zh":"如果社會變得數碼化，人們就需要數碼技能來學習、工作和使用服務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes modern life shaped by computers and data.","zh":"這個短語描述由電腦和數據塑造的現代生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"與此同時","examples":[{"en":"At the same time, many engineering structures are admired as works of art.","zh":"與此同時，許多工程結構被視為藝術作品而受到欣賞。"},{"en":"At the same time means while another fact is also true.","zh":"“At the same time” 指另一個事實也同時成立。"},{"en":"A phone can be useful for learning; at the same time, it can distract students.","zh":"手機可以有助學習；與此同時，它也可以分散學生注意力。"},{"en":"If technology has negative images but also artistic beauty, both views can exist together.","zh":"如果科技有負面形象但也有藝術美，兩種看法可以同時存在。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a balancing or contrasting point.","zh":"這個短語引出平衡或對比觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"landmark megastructures","meaning":"地標式巨型建築","examples":[{"en":"Landmark megastructures can become symbols of entire cities.","zh":"地標式巨型建築可以成為整座城市的象徵。"},{"en":"Landmark megastructures are very large built structures that are widely recognised and strongly associated with a place.","zh":"地標式巨型建築是廣為人知、並與某地緊密相連的超大型人造結構。"},{"en":"A famous bridge or tower can become a landmark megastructure for tourists and residents.","zh":"著名橋樑或塔樓可以成為遊客和居民心中的地標式巨型建築。"},{"en":"If a megastructure is visually striking, it may shape a city’s identity.","zh":"如果巨型建築在視覺上突出，它可能塑造城市身份。"},{"en":"The phrase combines huge scale with symbolic importance.","zh":"這個短語結合巨大規模和象徵重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Brooklyn Bridge","meaning":"布魯克林大橋","examples":[{"en":"The Brooklyn Bridge is both an engineering achievement and a city landmark.","zh":"布魯克林大橋既是工程成就，也是城市地標。"},{"en":"The Brooklyn Bridge is a famous bridge in New York that connects Brooklyn and Manhattan.","zh":"布魯克林大橋是紐約著名橋樑，連接布魯克林和曼哈頓。"},{"en":"Tourists may walk across the Brooklyn Bridge to see the skyline and river.","zh":"遊客可能步行橫過布魯克林大橋，欣賞天際線和河景。"},{"en":"Because it is both useful and beautiful, the bridge is admired beyond its transport function.","zh":"因為它既實用又美麗，這座橋在交通功能以外也受到欣賞。"},{"en":"The phrase names a structure that represents art, engineering and urban identity.","zh":"這個短語指出一座代表藝術、工程和城市身份的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Golden Gate Bridge","meaning":"金門大橋","examples":[{"en":"The Golden Gate Bridge has come to embody the spirit of San Francisco.","zh":"金門大橋逐漸成為三藩市精神的象徵。"},{"en":"The Golden Gate Bridge is a famous suspension bridge strongly associated with San Francisco.","zh":"金門大橋是一座著名懸索橋，與三藩市緊密相連。"},{"en":"Visitors often photograph the Golden Gate Bridge because its shape and colour are instantly recognisable.","zh":"遊客常拍攝金門大橋，因為其形狀和顏色令人一眼認出。"},{"en":"If a bridge becomes a city symbol, it can represent local pride and memory.","zh":"如果橋樑成為城市象徵，它就能代表本地自豪和記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase names an engineering structure with iconic cultural value.","zh":"這個短語指出一座具有標誌性文化價值的工程結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"almost universally hailed as","meaning":"幾乎普遍被譽為","examples":[{"en":"Some bridges are almost universally hailed as majestic achievements.","zh":"有些橋樑幾乎普遍被譽為宏偉成就。"},{"en":"To be almost universally hailed as something means to be praised by nearly everyone in that way.","zh":"“Be almost universally hailed as” 某物指幾乎所有人都以該方式讚揚它。"},{"en":"A life-saving medical discovery may be almost universally hailed as a breakthrough.","zh":"拯救生命的醫學發現可能幾乎普遍被譽為突破。"},{"en":"If a bridge is admired by engineers, artists and tourists alike, praise is very widespread.","zh":"如果一座橋同時受工程師、藝術家和遊客欣賞，讚譽就非常廣泛。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses broad approval, though not necessarily absolute agreement.","zh":"這個短語表達廣泛認同，但不一定是絕對一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"majestic human achievements","meaning":"宏偉的人類成就","examples":[{"en":"Large bridges are often celebrated as majestic human achievements.","zh":"大型橋樑常被讚頌為宏偉的人類成就。"},{"en":"Majestic human achievements are impressive accomplishments that show human skill, courage and vision.","zh":"宏偉的人類成就是展現人類技術、勇氣和遠見的驚人成就。"},{"en":"A hospital built after years of community effort can be seen as a human achievement.","zh":"一間經多年社區努力建成的醫院，可以被視為人類成就。"},{"en":"If a structure is majestic, it inspires awe through scale, beauty or difficulty.","zh":"如果一個結構宏偉，它會透過規模、美感或難度令人敬畏。"},{"en":"The phrase praises both the object and the people who made it possible.","zh":"這個短語既讚揚物件，也讚揚使它成真的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"engineering monuments","meaning":"工程紀念建築","examples":[{"en":"Famous bridges can function as great engineering monuments.","zh":"著名橋樑可以作為偉大的工程紀念建築。"},{"en":"Engineering monuments are structures that stand as lasting examples of major engineering achievement.","zh":"工程紀念建築是作為重大工程成就持久例子的結構。"},{"en":"A historic railway station can be an engineering monument if it changed transport in a city.","zh":"如果一座歷史火車站改變了城市交通，它可以是工程紀念建築。"},{"en":"If a monument is still admired decades later, it has meaning beyond its original function.","zh":"如果紀念建築數十年後仍受欣賞，它就有超越原本功能的意義。"},{"en":"The phrase treats engineering works as objects of memory and respect.","zh":"這個短語把工程作品視為記憶和尊重的對象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"come to embody","meaning":"逐漸成為……的象徵","examples":[{"en":"A major structure may come to embody the spirit of a city.","zh":"重大建築可能逐漸成為一座城市精神的象徵。"},{"en":"To come to embody something means gradually to become a clear symbol of it.","zh":"“Come to embody” 某事指逐漸成為它的清楚象徵。"},{"en":"A school song may come to embody students’ shared memories after many years.","zh":"多年後，校歌可能逐漸成為學生共同回憶的象徵。"},{"en":"If a bridge appears in postcards, films and local celebrations, it can embody city identity.","zh":"如果橋樑出現在明信片、電影和本地慶典中，它就能體現城市身份。"},{"en":"The phrase shows symbolic meaning developing over time.","zh":"這個短語顯示象徵意義隨時間形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the spirit of a city","meaning":"城市精神","examples":[{"en":"Landmark architecture can express the spirit of a city.","zh":"地標建築可以表達城市精神。"},{"en":"The spirit of a city means the character, energy, history and identity people associate with that city.","zh":"城市精神指人們與該城市聯繫起來的性格、活力、歷史和身份。"},{"en":"Street markets, old buildings and public transport can all show the spirit of a city.","zh":"街市、舊建築和公共交通都可以展現城市精神。"},{"en":"If a bridge represents freedom, ambition or resilience, it may express a city’s spirit.","zh":"如果一座橋代表自由、抱負或堅韌，它就可能表達城市精神。"},{"en":"The phrase turns a place’s identity into something people can feel.","zh":"這個短語把地方身份變成可感受到的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"respective cities","meaning":"各自所屬的城市","examples":[{"en":"The bridges became iconic symbols of their respective cities.","zh":"這些橋樑成為各自所屬城市的標誌性象徵。"},{"en":"Respective cities means the particular cities that each bridge belongs to or represents.","zh":"各自所屬的城市，指每座橋所屬或代表的特定城市。"},{"en":"Two students returned to their respective classrooms after the joint assembly.","zh":"聯合早會後，兩名學生返回各自的課室。"},{"en":"If two landmarks represent their respective cities, each one is linked to a different place.","zh":"如果兩個地標代表各自城市，每一個都與不同地方相連。"},{"en":"The phrase matches each item with its own corresponding city.","zh":"這個短語把每一項與其對應城市配對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the relationship between","meaning":"……之間的關係","examples":[{"en":"The relationship between art and engineering is complex.","zh":"藝術與工程之間的關係很複雜。"},{"en":"The relationship between two things means how they are connected or affect each other.","zh":"兩件事之間的關係，指它們如何相連或互相影響。"},{"en":"The relationship between sleep and learning is important because tired students remember less.","zh":"睡眠與學習之間的關係很重要，因為疲倦學生記得較少。"},{"en":"If art and engineering influence each other, their relationship is not simply opposite.","zh":"如果藝術和工程互相影響，它們之間的關係就不只是對立。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a connection that may need explanation.","zh":"這個短語引出可能需要解釋的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"seldom easy or consistent","meaning":"很少是簡單或一致的","examples":[{"en":"The relationship between technology and art has seldom been easy or consistent.","zh":"科技與藝術之間的關係很少是簡單或一致的。"},{"en":"Seldom easy or consistent means rarely simple, smooth or the same in every case.","zh":"“Seldom easy or consistent” 指很少簡單、順利或在每個情況中一樣。"},{"en":"The relationship between parents and teenagers is seldom easy or consistent during exam years.","zh":"在考試年份，父母與青少年之間的關係很少是簡單或一致的。"},{"en":"If people sometimes admire technology and sometimes fear it, the relationship is complicated.","zh":"如果人們有時欣賞科技，有時害怕科技，這種關係就是複雜的。"},{"en":"The phrase prepares readers for mixed evidence and changing attitudes.","zh":"這個短語讓讀者準備面對混合證據和變化態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a cog in the wheel","meaning":"大機器中的小齒輪","examples":[{"en":"An industrial worker may appear to be only a cog in the wheel.","zh":"工業工人可能看起來只是大機器中的小齒輪。"},{"en":"A cog in the wheel is a small part of a large system, often with little individual power.","zh":"大機器中的小齒輪，是龐大系統中的小部分，通常缺乏個人力量。"},{"en":"A clerk may feel like a cog in the wheel if they repeat one task all day without being heard.","zh":"如果文員整天重複一項任務又沒人聽其意見，可能覺得自己只是小齒輪。"},{"en":"If workers are treated as replaceable parts, they may feel dehumanised.","zh":"如果工人被當成可替換零件，他們可能感到被去人性化。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests loss of individuality inside a large organisation.","zh":"這個短語暗示在大型組織中失去個體性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the wheel of industry","meaning":"工業體系","examples":[{"en":"Workers were sometimes treated as replaceable parts in the wheel of industry.","zh":"工人有時被視為工業體系中可替換的零件。"},{"en":"The wheel of industry is a metaphor for the large system of factories, production and business.","zh":"工業體系是一個比喻，指工廠、生產和商業組成的大系統。"},{"en":"A delivery worker may feel trapped in the wheel of industry during peak shopping seasons.","zh":"送貨員在購物旺季可能覺得自己被困在工業體系中。"},{"en":"If the system values output more than people, workers can feel like mechanical parts.","zh":"如果系統重視產出多於人，工人就會感到自己像機械零件。"},{"en":"The phrase presents industry as a huge moving machine.","zh":"這個短語把工業呈現為巨大運轉機器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reveal the beauty of","meaning":"展現……的美感","examples":[{"en":"Photography can reveal the beauty of ordinary industrial work.","zh":"攝影可以展現普通工業工作的美感。"},{"en":"To reveal the beauty of something means to show that it has beauty people may not have noticed.","zh":"“Reveal the beauty of” 某事指顯示它具有別人未必注意到的美。"},{"en":"A photo of a wet street at night can reveal the beauty of an ordinary neighbourhood.","zh":"夜晚濕街道的照片可以展現普通社區的美感。"},{"en":"If an artist frames machines carefully, viewers may notice pattern and elegance.","zh":"如果藝術家仔細構圖機器，觀眾可能注意到圖案和優雅。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests making hidden beauty visible.","zh":"這個短語暗示把隱藏美感變得可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"line and composition","meaning":"線條與構圖","examples":[{"en":"The photographer found beauty in the image’s line and composition.","zh":"攝影師在影像的線條與構圖中找到美感。"},{"en":"Line and composition refer to the shapes, directions and arrangement of elements in an artwork or photograph.","zh":"線條與構圖指藝術品或照片中形狀、方向和元素安排。"},{"en":"A drawing can look balanced when its line and composition guide the viewer’s eye.","zh":"當線條與構圖引導觀者視線，圖畫可以看起來平衡。"},{"en":"If factory pipes and beams create strong lines, they may become visually beautiful.","zh":"如果工廠管道和樑柱形成強烈線條，它們可能變得有視覺美。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how an image is organised.","zh":"這個短語強調影像如何被組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"use a wrench","meaning":"使用扳手","examples":[{"en":"The photograph showed a worker using a wrench.","zh":"這張照片顯示一名工人正在使用扳手。"},{"en":"To use a wrench means to operate a metal tool for gripping and turning nuts or bolts.","zh":"使用扳手指操作一種金屬工具，用來夾緊並轉動螺母或螺栓。"},{"en":"A mechanic may use a wrench to loosen a car wheel.","zh":"技工可能使用扳手鬆開汽車車輪。"},{"en":"If a worker uses a wrench all day, the photograph may show both labour and skill.","zh":"如果工人整天使用扳手，照片可能同時顯示勞動和技術。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a practical action with a hand tool.","zh":"這個短語描述使用手工具的實際動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"turn a bolt","meaning":"扭動螺栓","examples":[{"en":"The worker used a wrench to turn a bolt.","zh":"工人使用扳手扭動螺栓。"},{"en":"To turn a bolt means to rotate a metal fastener so it tightens or loosens.","zh":"扭動螺栓指旋轉金屬固定件，使它收緊或鬆開。"},{"en":"A caretaker may turn a bolt to fix a loose school gate.","zh":"管理員可能扭動螺栓來修好鬆脫的校門。"},{"en":"If a bolt is not turned tightly enough, a structure may become unsafe.","zh":"如果螺栓沒有扭緊，結構可能變得不安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small action that can matter in construction or repair.","zh":"這個短語描述在建造或維修中可能重要的小動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"enormous industrial plant","meaning":"巨型工業廠房","examples":[{"en":"The enormous industrial plant became an artistic subject.","zh":"巨型工業廠房成為藝術題材。"},{"en":"An enormous industrial plant is a very large factory or production site.","zh":"巨型工業廠房是非常大型的工廠或生產場地。"},{"en":"A city may have an enormous industrial plant that employs thousands of workers.","zh":"城市可能有一座僱用數千名工人的巨型工業廠房。"},{"en":"If a plant is huge and visually complex, artists may treat it as a dramatic subject.","zh":"如果廠房巨大且視覺上複雜，藝術家可能把它視為富戲劇性的題材。"},{"en":"The phrase combines scale with industrial function.","zh":"這個短語結合規模和工業功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the River Rouge plant","meaning":"River Rouge 工廠","examples":[{"en":"The River Rouge plant was one of the world’s largest car factories.","zh":"River Rouge 工廠曾是世界最大汽車工廠之一。"},{"en":"The River Rouge plant was a major industrial factory complex associated with car production.","zh":"River Rouge 工廠是與汽車生產相關的重大工業廠房群。"},{"en":"An artist visiting the River Rouge plant might see smoke, steel, workers and machinery together.","zh":"到訪 River Rouge 工廠的藝術家可能同時看見煙、鋼鐵、工人和機器。"},{"en":"Because of its scale, the plant could represent modern industry itself.","zh":"由於其規模，這座工廠可以代表現代工業本身。"},{"en":"The phrase names a famous factory that attracted artistic attention.","zh":"這個短語指出一座吸引藝術關注的著名工廠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"open to produce","meaning":"開幕以生產……","examples":[{"en":"The factory opened in 1927 to produce the Model A.","zh":"這間工廠於1927年開幕以生產 Model A。"},{"en":"To open to produce something means to begin operating with the purpose of making that product.","zh":"“Open to produce” 某物指開始營運，目的是製造該產品。"},{"en":"A bakery may open to produce bread for nearby schools and restaurants.","zh":"麵包店可能開幕以為附近學校和餐廳生產麵包。"},{"en":"If a factory opens for a specific product, its machines and workers are organised around that goal.","zh":"如果工廠為特定產品而開幕，其機器和工人都圍繞該目標組織。"},{"en":"The phrase links the start of operation with production purpose.","zh":"這個短語把開始營運與生產目的連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be chosen to photograph","meaning":"獲選拍攝……","examples":[{"en":"Charles Sheeler was chosen to photograph the new factory.","zh":"Charles Sheeler 獲選拍攝這座新工廠。"},{"en":"To be chosen to photograph something means to be selected to take photographs of it.","zh":"“Be chosen to photograph” 某物指被選中為它拍照。"},{"en":"A student may be chosen to photograph Sports Day because they take clear pictures.","zh":"學生可能因照片清晰而獲選拍攝運動會。"},{"en":"If an artist is chosen for a major project, their vision is trusted.","zh":"如果藝術家獲選參與重大項目，其視覺眼光就是受到信任。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being selected for a photographic task.","zh":"這個短語描述被選中執行攝影任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the world’s largest car factory","meaning":"全球最大的汽車工廠","examples":[{"en":"The world’s largest car factory captured Sheeler’s imagination.","zh":"全球最大的汽車工廠激發了 Sheeler 的想像力。"},{"en":"The world’s largest car factory means the biggest factory for making cars at that time or in that context.","zh":"全球最大的汽車工廠指當時或該語境中最大的汽車製造工廠。"},{"en":"A documentary might show the world’s largest car factory to explain mass production.","zh":"紀錄片可能展示全球最大的汽車工廠，以解釋大量生產。"},{"en":"If a factory is the largest in the world, its size alone can impress artists and engineers.","zh":"如果工廠是全球最大，其規模本身已能令藝術家和工程師印象深刻。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises exceptional industrial scale.","zh":"這個短語強調非凡工業規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"capture someone’s imagination","meaning":"激發某人的想像力","examples":[{"en":"The scale of the factory captured the artist’s imagination.","zh":"工廠的規模激發了這位藝術家的想像力。"},{"en":"To capture someone’s imagination means to excite their interest and make them think creatively.","zh":"“Capture someone’s imagination” 指激起某人的興趣，並令他創意地思考。"},{"en":"A science museum can capture children’s imagination by letting them touch machines and models.","zh":"科學博物館可以透過讓孩子觸摸機器和模型來激發他們的想像力。"},{"en":"If a building captures an artist’s imagination, it may become the subject of drawings or photographs.","zh":"如果建築物激發藝術家的想像力，它可能成為素描或照片的題材。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong creative fascination.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈的創作迷戀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the most thrilling subject","meaning":"最令人興奮的題材","examples":[{"en":"Sheeler described the factory as the most thrilling subject he had photographed.","zh":"Sheeler 形容這座工廠是他拍攝過最令人興奮的題材。"},{"en":"The most thrilling subject is the most exciting thing a person has chosen to study, paint or photograph.","zh":"最令人興奮的題材，是某人選擇研究、繪畫或拍攝過最刺激的東西。"},{"en":"A wildlife photographer may call a rare bird the most thrilling subject of the year.","zh":"野生動物攝影師可能把罕見雀鳥稱為本年最令人興奮的題材。"},{"en":"If a factory becomes thrilling to an artist, industrial space is being treated as art.","zh":"如果工廠對藝術家來說變得令人興奮，工業空間就被視為藝術。"},{"en":"The phrase shows intense excitement about a subject.","zh":"這個短語顯示對題材的強烈興奮感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"work with a subject","meaning":"以某題材進行創作","examples":[{"en":"The photographer enjoyed working with industrial subjects.","zh":"這位攝影師喜歡以工業題材進行創作。"},{"en":"To work with a subject means to use it as the focus of artistic, academic or creative work.","zh":"“Work with a subject” 指把某題材作為藝術、學術或創意工作的焦點。"},{"en":"A student may enjoy working with family history as a subject for a school project.","zh":"學生可能喜歡以家庭歷史作為學校項目的題材。"},{"en":"If an artist works with factories, they study their shapes, light and meaning.","zh":"如果藝術家以工廠為題材創作，他們會研究其形狀、光線和意義。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sustained creative engagement with a topic.","zh":"這個短語描述與某題目持續的創作投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"compose oil paintings","meaning":"創作油畫","examples":[{"en":"Sheeler also composed oil paintings of the factory.","zh":"Sheeler 也創作了這座工廠的油畫。"},{"en":"To compose oil paintings means to create paintings using oil paint, with careful arrangement of visual elements.","zh":"創作油畫指使用油彩繪畫，並仔細安排視覺元素。"},{"en":"An artist may compose oil paintings of city streets after making sketches on site.","zh":"藝術家可能在現場素描後，創作城市街道油畫。"},{"en":"If a painter composes a factory scene, they decide how lines, colour and space should work together.","zh":"如果畫家創作工廠場景，就要決定線條、顏色和空間如何配合。"},{"en":"The phrase treats painting as deliberate visual construction.","zh":"這個短語把繪畫視為有意識的視覺建構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"give a work a title","meaning":"為作品命名","examples":[{"en":"The artist gave his factory paintings ambitious titles.","zh":"這位藝術家為其工廠畫作命名，名稱氣勢宏大。"},{"en":"To give a work a title means to name a painting, book, photo or other creation.","zh":"為作品命名指為畫作、書、照片或其他創作取名字。"},{"en":"A student may give a poem a title after deciding its main feeling.","zh":"學生可能在決定詩的主要情感後為詩命名。"},{"en":"If an artist gives a factory painting a grand title, viewers may take the subject more seriously.","zh":"如果藝術家為工廠畫作取宏大標題，觀眾可能更認真看待該題材。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how naming can shape interpretation.","zh":"這個短語顯示命名如何塑造詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"American Landscape","meaning":"《美國風景》","examples":[{"en":"American Landscape presents an industrial plant as part of the national landscape.","zh":"《美國風景》把工業廠房呈現為國家景觀的一部分。"},{"en":"American Landscape is a title that frames industry as part of America’s visual and cultural identity.","zh":"《美國風景》這個標題把工業框定為美國視覺和文化身份的一部分。"},{"en":"A painting called “City Morning” may make ordinary buildings feel like a shared urban scene.","zh":"一幅名為《城市早晨》的畫，可能令普通建築感覺像共同的城市景象。"},{"en":"If a factory is called a landscape, viewers may see it as belonging to the country’s scenery.","zh":"如果工廠被稱為風景，觀眾可能把它看成屬於國家景色的一部分。"},{"en":"The title suggests that modern industry can become part of national art.","zh":"這個標題暗示現代工業可以成為國家藝術的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Classic Landscape","meaning":"《古典風景》","examples":[{"en":"The title Classic Landscape treats the factory as a traditional artistic subject.","zh":"《古典風景》這個標題把工廠視為傳統藝術題材。"},{"en":"Classic Landscape is a title that gives an industrial scene the dignity of traditional landscape art.","zh":"《古典風景》這個標題把工業場景提升至傳統風景藝術的尊嚴。"},{"en":"A modern railway station may look more artistic when framed as a classic landscape.","zh":"如果現代火車站被框定為古典風景，它可能看起來更有藝術性。"},{"en":"If a factory is given such a title, the artist invites viewers to see beauty in it.","zh":"如果工廠被賦予這樣的標題，藝術家就是邀請觀眾看見其中美感。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that industry can join older artistic traditions.","zh":"這個短語暗示工業可以加入較古老的藝術傳統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"long before","meaning":"早在……之前","examples":[{"en":"Long before Sheeler, artists had recognised beauty in engineering.","zh":"早在 Sheeler 之前，藝術家已認識到工程中的美。"},{"en":"Long before means a great deal earlier than a later person, event or period.","zh":"“Long before” 指比後來的人、事件或時期早很多。"},{"en":"Long before smartphones, people used paper maps to find their way.","zh":"早在智能手機之前，人們使用紙本地圖尋路。"},{"en":"If artists admired engineering long before modern factories, the link between art and technology is not new.","zh":"如果藝術家早在現代工廠之前已欣賞工程，藝術與科技的連繫就不是新事物。"},{"en":"The phrase pushes the reader back to an earlier historical point.","zh":"這個短語把讀者帶回更早的歷史時間點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"see beauty and humanity in","meaning":"從……看見美感與人性","examples":[{"en":"Some artists saw beauty and humanity in industrial structures.","zh":"有些藝術家從工業結構中看見美感與人性。"},{"en":"To see beauty and humanity in something means to recognise aesthetic and human value in it.","zh":"從某物看見美感與人性，指在其中認出審美和人的價值。"},{"en":"A photographer may see beauty and humanity in a crowded market through people’s faces and movements.","zh":"攝影師可能透過人們的臉和動作，從擁擠街市中看見美感與人性。"},{"en":"If artists see humanity in machinery, they notice the labour and imagination behind it.","zh":"如果藝術家在機械中看見人性，就會注意到其背後的勞動和想像力。"},{"en":"The phrase challenges cold or purely functional interpretations.","zh":"這個短語挑戰冰冷或純功能性的詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"no more evident than in","meaning":"在……中表現得最明顯","examples":[{"en":"The artistic value of engineering is no more evident than in Coalbrookdale.","zh":"工程的藝術價值在 Coalbrookdale 中表現得最明顯。"},{"en":"No more evident than in a place means that something is especially clear there.","zh":"“No more evident than in” 某地指某事在那裡尤其清楚。"},{"en":"The value of teamwork is no more evident than in a hospital emergency room.","zh":"團隊合作的價值在醫院急症室中表現得最明顯。"},{"en":"If engineering beauty is clearest at Coalbrookdale, that place becomes a powerful example.","zh":"如果工程美在 Coalbrookdale 最清楚，該地就成為有力例子。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the strongest illustration of an idea.","zh":"這個短語突出某想法最強的例證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Coalbrookdale","meaning":"Coalbrookdale（地名）","examples":[{"en":"Coalbrookdale played an important role in the Industrial Revolution.","zh":"Coalbrookdale 在工業革命中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"Coalbrookdale is a historic place in England closely associated with iron production and early industry.","zh":"Coalbrookdale 是英格蘭一個歷史地點，與煉鐵和早期工業密切相關。"},{"en":"A museum visitor may study Coalbrookdale to understand how iron changed bridges and factories.","zh":"博物館訪客可能研究 Coalbrookdale，以理解鐵如何改變橋樑和工廠。"},{"en":"Because important ironwork developed there, Coalbrookdale became a symbol of industrial progress.","zh":"由於重要鐵工在那裡發展，Coalbrookdale 成為工業進步的象徵。"},{"en":"The word names a place where engineering history and artistic interest meet.","zh":"這個詞指出一個工程歷史與藝術興趣交會的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the Industrial Revolution","meaning":"工業革命","examples":[{"en":"Iron was essential to the Industrial Revolution.","zh":"鐵對工業革命至關重要。"},{"en":"The Industrial Revolution was the period when machine production, factories and new transport transformed society.","zh":"工業革命是機器生產、工廠和新交通改變社會的時期。"},{"en":"Students learn about the Industrial Revolution when studying steam engines, factories and urban growth.","zh":"學生研究蒸汽機、工廠和城市增長時，會學到工業革命。"},{"en":"If iron became easier to use, bridges, machines and railways could develop quickly.","zh":"如果鐵變得更容易使用，橋樑、機器和鐵路就能快速發展。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a major shift from hand production to industrial production.","zh":"這個短語指由手工生產轉向工業生產的重大轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be worked for centuries","meaning":"被加工數百年","examples":[{"en":"Iron had been worked in Coalbrookdale for centuries.","zh":"鐵在 Coalbrookdale 已被加工數百年。"},{"en":"To be worked for centuries means to be mined, shaped or processed there for hundreds of years.","zh":"“Be worked for centuries” 指在那裡被開採、塑形或加工數百年。"},{"en":"Clay had been worked in the village for centuries before the pottery became famous.","zh":"在陶器出名之前，黏土已在村莊被加工數百年。"},{"en":"If a material has been worked for centuries, local people have built long experience around it.","zh":"如果某材料被加工數百年，當地人就圍繞它建立了長久經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a long tradition of skilled labour.","zh":"這個短語顯示熟練勞動的悠久傳統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cast the large ribs","meaning":"鑄造大型拱肋","examples":[{"en":"Abraham Darby III cast the large ribs of the iron bridge.","zh":"Abraham Darby III 鑄造了這座鐵橋的大型拱肋。"},{"en":"To cast the large ribs means to make big curved structural pieces by pouring molten metal into moulds.","zh":"鑄造大型拱肋指把熔化金屬倒入模具，製成大型彎曲結構件。"},{"en":"A factory may cast metal parts for machines by using carefully shaped moulds.","zh":"工廠可能使用精心成形的模具，鑄造機器金屬部件。"},{"en":"If bridge ribs are cast accurately, they can support the structure safely.","zh":"如果橋樑拱肋鑄造準確，就能安全支撐結構。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a technical process used in metal construction.","zh":"這個短語描述金屬建造中的技術過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"on the banks of","meaning":"在……的河岸","examples":[{"en":"The bridge components were made on the banks of the River Severn.","zh":"橋樑部件在塞文河河岸製造。"},{"en":"On the banks of a river means beside or along the land at the edge of the river.","zh":"“On the banks of” 一條河指在河邊或沿着河岸土地。"},{"en":"Families may walk on the banks of a river during weekends.","zh":"家庭週末可能在河岸散步。"},{"en":"If a factory is built on the riverbank, materials can be moved by water more easily.","zh":"如果工廠建在河岸，材料就能更容易經水路運輸。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a location next to a river.","zh":"這個短語給出河邊位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the River Severn","meaning":"塞文河","examples":[{"en":"Iron Bridge spans the River Severn in England.","zh":"鐵橋橫跨英格蘭的塞文河。"},{"en":"The River Severn is a major river in Britain, connected here with the historic Iron Bridge.","zh":"塞文河是英國一條主要河流，在此與歷史性的鐵橋相關。"},{"en":"A bridge across the River Severn can link communities on opposite banks.","zh":"橫跨塞文河的橋可以連接兩岸社區。"},{"en":"If a structure spans a river, it becomes part of both transport and landscape.","zh":"如果結構橫跨河流，它就成為交通和景觀的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase names the river that gives the bridge its setting.","zh":"這個短語指出給予橋樑背景的河流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"form the world’s first iron bridge","meaning":"組成全球首座鐵橋","examples":[{"en":"The cast-iron ribs formed the world’s first iron bridge.","zh":"這些鑄鐵拱肋組成全球首座鐵橋。"},{"en":"To form the world’s first iron bridge means to make up the earliest bridge built mainly from iron.","zh":"“Form the world’s first iron bridge” 指組成最早主要由鐵建成的橋。"},{"en":"Several carefully made parts can form a machine when they are joined correctly.","zh":"幾個精心製造的部件正確接合後，可以組成一部機器。"},{"en":"If these ribs formed the first iron bridge, the structure marked a major technological step.","zh":"如果這些拱肋組成首座鐵橋，該結構就標誌重大科技進步。"},{"en":"The phrase links individual components with a historic whole.","zh":"這個短語把個別部件與歷史性整體連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a dramatic departure from","meaning":"與……截然不同","examples":[{"en":"The iron structure was a dramatic departure from traditional bridge design.","zh":"這座鐵結構與傳統橋樑設計截然不同。"},{"en":"A dramatic departure from something is a major and noticeable break from the old way.","zh":"“A dramatic departure from” 某事是與舊方式重大而明顯的分離。"},{"en":"A school that replaces exams with project learning makes a dramatic departure from traditional assessment.","zh":"如果學校以項目學習取代考試，就是與傳統評核截然不同。"},{"en":"If bridges were usually stone or timber, an iron bridge looked radically new.","zh":"如果橋樑通常是石或木建成，鐵橋看起來就非常新穎。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises strong change rather than small adjustment.","zh":"這個短語強調強烈改變，而不是小調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"classic stone and timber bridges","meaning":"傳統石橋和木橋","examples":[{"en":"Earlier bridges were commonly built from stone and timber.","zh":"早期橋樑通常由石和木建成。"},{"en":"Classic stone and timber bridges are traditional bridges made from rock and wood.","zh":"傳統石橋和木橋是由石材和木材製成的傳統橋樑。"},{"en":"Villages may have old stone and timber bridges that blend into the countryside.","zh":"鄉村可能有融入田野景色的舊石橋和木橋。"},{"en":"If iron replaced these materials, bridge design entered a new age.","zh":"如果鐵取代這些材料，橋樑設計就進入新時代。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts older natural materials with modern metal construction.","zh":"這個短語把較古老的天然材料與現代金屬建造作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dot the countryside","meaning":"散布於鄉郊","examples":[{"en":"Stone and timber bridges once dotted the English countryside.","zh":"石橋和木橋曾散布於英格蘭鄉郊。"},{"en":"To dot the countryside means to appear in many scattered places across rural land.","zh":"“Dot the countryside” 指在鄉郊土地中分散出現在許多地方。"},{"en":"Small farms dot the countryside around the old town.","zh":"小農場散布於古城周邊鄉郊。"},{"en":"If bridges dot the landscape, they become familiar parts of everyday scenery.","zh":"如果橋樑散布於景觀中，它們就成為日常風景的熟悉部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes scattered but repeated presence.","zh":"這個短語描述分散但反覆出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be captured in paintings","meaning":"被描繪於畫作中","examples":[{"en":"Traditional bridges were captured in numerous landscape paintings.","zh":"傳統橋樑被描繪於大量風景畫中。"},{"en":"To be captured in paintings means to be shown or recorded by artists in painted form.","zh":"“Be captured in paintings” 指被藝術家以繪畫形式展示或記錄。"},{"en":"A village festival may be captured in paintings before photographs become common.","zh":"在攝影普及前，村莊節日可能被描繪於畫作中。"},{"en":"If bridges are captured in art, they become part of cultural memory.","zh":"如果橋樑被藝術記錄，它們就成為文化記憶的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visual preservation through painting.","zh":"這個短語描述透過繪畫作視覺保存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"serene landscape paintings","meaning":"寧靜的風景畫","examples":[{"en":"The old bridges appeared in serene landscape paintings.","zh":"舊橋出現在寧靜的風景畫中。"},{"en":"Serene landscape paintings are calm and peaceful pictures of natural or rural scenery.","zh":"寧靜的風景畫是描繪自然或鄉村景色的平靜安詳畫作。"},{"en":"A painting of a quiet lake at sunset can be a serene landscape painting.","zh":"日落時分安靜湖泊的畫可以是寧靜的風景畫。"},{"en":"If a bridge appears in a serene landscape, it feels gentle rather than disruptive.","zh":"如果橋樑出現在寧靜風景中，它感覺溫和而非破壞性。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a peaceful artistic mood.","zh":"這個短語營造平和的藝術氣氛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"metal structure","meaning":"金屬結構","examples":[{"en":"The new metal structure represented a major technological change.","zh":"新金屬結構代表重大科技變化。"},{"en":"A metal structure is a built form made mainly from metal such as iron or steel.","zh":"金屬結構是主要由鐵或鋼等金屬製成的建築形態。"},{"en":"A railway bridge, factory roof or stadium frame can be a metal structure.","zh":"鐵路橋、工廠屋頂或體育館框架都可以是金屬結構。"},{"en":"If a metal structure replaces stone and wood, engineers can build in new ways.","zh":"如果金屬結構取代石和木，工程師就能以新方式建造。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on material and construction.","zh":"這個短語強調材料和建造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"appropriately called","meaning":"被恰當地稱為","examples":[{"en":"The bridge was simply but appropriately called Iron Bridge.","zh":"這座橋簡單但恰當地被稱為 Iron Bridge。"},{"en":"Appropriately called means named in a way that clearly fits its nature or character.","zh":"“Appropriately called” 指名稱清楚符合其本質或特徵。"},{"en":"A quiet reading room may be appropriately called the Peace Corner.","zh":"安靜閱讀室可以被恰當地稱為寧靜角。"},{"en":"If the first iron bridge is named Iron Bridge, the name is simple but suitable.","zh":"如果首座鐵橋被命名為 Iron Bridge，名稱就是簡單但合適。"},{"en":"The phrase judges a name as fitting and sensible.","zh":"這個短語判斷名稱貼切而合理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"span the river","meaning":"橫跨河流","examples":[{"en":"The historic bridge still spans the River Severn.","zh":"這座歷史橋樑仍橫跨塞文河。"},{"en":"To span a river means to stretch across it from one side to the other.","zh":"橫跨河流指從一岸延伸至另一岸。"},{"en":"A footbridge spans a small stream so children can walk to school safely.","zh":"行人橋橫跨小溪，讓孩子安全步行上學。"},{"en":"If a bridge spans a river, it connects places that water would otherwise separate.","zh":"如果橋橫跨河流，它就連接原本被水分隔的地方。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the physical crossing function of a bridge.","zh":"這個短語描述橋樑的實際跨越功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"beckon someone to","meaning":"吸引某人去……","examples":[{"en":"The bridge still beckons tourists to walk across it.","zh":"這座橋仍吸引遊客走過它。"},{"en":"To beckon someone to do something means to attract or invite them to do it.","zh":"“Beckon someone to” 做某事指吸引或邀請某人去做。"},{"en":"A colourful book cover may beckon a child to pick it up.","zh":"彩色書封可能吸引孩子拿起那本書。"},{"en":"If a historic bridge looks beautiful and meaningful, it can draw visitors toward it.","zh":"如果歷史橋樑看起來美麗而有意義，它就能吸引訪客走近。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a quiet but strong invitation.","zh":"這個短語暗示安靜但強烈的邀請。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"gaze upon","meaning":"凝望……","examples":[{"en":"Artists and engineers continue to gaze upon the bridge.","zh":"藝術家和工程師繼續凝望這座橋。"},{"en":"To gaze upon something means to look at it steadily, often with admiration or thought.","zh":"“Gaze upon” 某物指穩定地看着它，通常帶着欣賞或思考。"},{"en":"Visitors may gaze upon a mountain view before taking photographs.","zh":"訪客可能先凝望山景，然後才拍照。"},{"en":"If people gaze upon a bridge, they are not just using it; they are contemplating it.","zh":"如果人們凝望一座橋，他們就不只是使用它，而是在沉思它。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests slow, attentive looking.","zh":"這個短語暗示緩慢而專注的觀看。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as if on a pilgrimage","meaning":"彷彿前往朝聖","examples":[{"en":"Visitors cross Iron Bridge as if on a pilgrimage to a revered place.","zh":"訪客橫過 Iron Bridge 時，彷彿前往一個受敬仰的地方朝聖。"},{"en":"As if on a pilgrimage means as though travelling respectfully to a sacred or deeply meaningful site.","zh":"“As if on a pilgrimage” 指彷彿帶着敬意前往神聖或深具意義的地方。"},{"en":"Former students may return to an old school hall as if on a pilgrimage.","zh":"舊生可能回到舊校禮堂，彷彿前往朝聖。"},{"en":"If engineers visit a bridge this way, they treat it with special respect.","zh":"如果工程師以這種方式參觀橋樑，他們就是特別尊重它。"},{"en":"The phrase gives ordinary travel a solemn and respectful feeling.","zh":"這個短語令普通旅程帶有莊重和敬意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a revered place","meaning":"受敬仰的地方","examples":[{"en":"The historic site is treated as a revered place by many engineers.","zh":"這個歷史地點被許多工程師視為受敬仰的地方。"},{"en":"A revered place is a place deeply respected because of its history, meaning or achievement.","zh":"受敬仰的地方，是因歷史、意義或成就而深受尊重的地方。"},{"en":"A community may treat an old temple or school as a revered place.","zh":"社區可能把舊寺廟或學校視為受敬仰的地方。"},{"en":"If a site is revered, visitors behave with admiration rather than casual indifference.","zh":"如果某地受敬仰，訪客會帶着欣賞而非隨意漠視的態度。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests respect built over time.","zh":"這個短語暗示經時間建立起來的尊重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reflection of the ironwork","meaning":"鐵製結構的倒影","examples":[{"en":"The reflection of the ironwork completes the bridge’s visual form.","zh":"鐵製結構的倒影完成了橋樑的視覺形態。"},{"en":"The reflection of the ironwork is the image of the metal structure mirrored on water or another surface.","zh":"鐵製結構的倒影，是金屬結構在水面或另一表面上的鏡像。"},{"en":"A bridge reflected in a calm river can look twice as complete and balanced.","zh":"橋樑映在平靜河面上，可以看起來更加完整和平衡。"},{"en":"If reflection completes a visual shape, nature and engineering work together in the image.","zh":"如果倒影完成視覺形狀，自然和工程就在影像中合作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how light and water add to architectural beauty.","zh":"這個短語描述光線和水面如何增添建築美。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"complete the semicircular structure","meaning":"完成半圓形結構","examples":[{"en":"The reflection completes the bridge’s semicircular structure.","zh":"倒影完成了橋樑的半圓形結構。"},{"en":"To complete the semicircular structure means to make a half-circle shape appear visually whole.","zh":"完成半圓形結構指令半圓形在視覺上看起來完整。"},{"en":"A rainbow reflected in water may complete a circle-like shape.","zh":"彩虹映在水中時，可能完成近似圓形的形狀。"},{"en":"If a bridge arch and its reflection meet visually, the viewer sees a fuller form.","zh":"如果橋拱和其倒影在視覺上相接，觀者就看見更完整的形態。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how reflection changes what the eye perceives.","zh":"這個短語解釋倒影如何改變眼睛所感知的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a wide-open eye into the future","meaning":"望向未來的張開眼睛","examples":[{"en":"The bridge and its reflection resemble a wide-open eye into the future.","zh":"這座橋及其倒影像一隻望向未來的張開眼睛。"},{"en":"A wide-open eye into the future is a metaphor for a structure that seems to look forward to a new age.","zh":"望向未來的張開眼睛是一個比喻，指某結構看似凝視新時代。"},{"en":"A new science centre may look like an eye into the future for young students.","zh":"新科學中心對年輕學生來說，可能像一隻望向未來的眼睛。"},{"en":"If a bridge suggests future progress, its shape becomes symbolic as well as practical.","zh":"如果橋樑暗示未來進步，其形狀就既實用又有象徵意義。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a poetic image of vision, progress and modernity.","zh":"這個短語給出關於視野、進步和現代性的詩意圖像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"what is now the past","meaning":"如今已成過去的未來","examples":[{"en":"The bridge once represented a future that is now the past.","zh":"這座橋曾代表一個如今已成過去的未來。"},{"en":"What is now the past means something that used to feel modern or future-looking but has become historical.","zh":"如今已成過去的未來，指曾經感覺現代或面向未來，但現在已成歷史的事物。"},{"en":"Early computers once looked futuristic, but they are now part of the past.","zh":"早期電腦曾看起來充滿未來感，但現在已屬過去。"},{"en":"If an old bridge once symbolised progress, it shows how yesterday’s future becomes history.","zh":"如果舊橋曾象徵進步，它就顯示昨日的未來如何變成歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase reflects on changing time and perspective.","zh":"這個短語反思時間和視角的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bucolic depiction","meaning":"田園詩般的描繪","examples":[{"en":"The painting offers a bucolic depiction of the bridge and river.","zh":"這幅畫對橋樑和河流作出田園詩般的描繪。"},{"en":"A bucolic depiction is a peaceful, rural-looking presentation of countryside life or scenery.","zh":"田園詩般的描繪，是對鄉村生活或景色作出平和、田園風的呈現。"},{"en":"A poster of sheep, fields and a quiet path may offer a bucolic depiction of village life.","zh":"一張有羊群、田野和安靜小路的海報，可能對村莊生活作出田園詩般的描繪。"},{"en":"If an iron bridge is shown bucolically, industry is made to feel part of nature.","zh":"如果鐵橋被田園化地描繪，工業就被塑造成自然的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a gentle pastoral mood to a scene.","zh":"這個短語為場景帶來柔和的田園氣氛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pedestrians and horsemen","meaning":"行人與騎馬者","examples":[{"en":"The artist included pedestrians and horsemen crossing the bridge.","zh":"藝術家加入了正在過橋的行人與騎馬者。"},{"en":"Pedestrians and horsemen are people walking and people riding horses.","zh":"行人與騎馬者是步行的人和騎馬的人。"},{"en":"An old town painting may show pedestrians and horsemen sharing a narrow road.","zh":"舊城鎮畫作可能顯示行人與騎馬者共用狹窄道路。"},{"en":"If both groups cross the bridge, the scene shows everyday movement and social life.","zh":"如果兩類人都橫過橋樑，場景就顯示日常流動和社會生活。"},{"en":"The phrase helps place the bridge within human activity.","zh":"這個短語幫助把橋樑放在人類活動之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"woodland trail","meaning":"林間小徑","examples":[{"en":"The bridge appears almost like part of a woodland trail.","zh":"這座橋看起來幾乎像林間小徑的一部分。"},{"en":"A woodland trail is a path through trees or forested land.","zh":"林間小徑是穿過樹木或林地的小路。"},{"en":"Families may follow a woodland trail during a weekend walk.","zh":"家庭可能在週末散步時沿着林間小徑走。"},{"en":"If a bridge seems like part of a woodland trail, it feels natural rather than intrusive.","zh":"如果橋樑看似林間小徑的一部分，它就感覺自然，而不是突兀。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an outdoor rural setting.","zh":"這個短語給出戶外鄉郊背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"well-dressed onlookers","meaning":"衣着講究的旁觀者","examples":[{"en":"A pair of well-dressed onlookers admire the bridge.","zh":"一對衣着講究的旁觀者欣賞這座橋。"},{"en":"Well-dressed onlookers are people wearing smart clothes while watching something.","zh":"衣着講究的旁觀者，是穿着得體、正在觀看某事的人。"},{"en":"Well-dressed onlookers may gather outside a theatre before a formal performance.","zh":"衣着講究的旁觀者可能在正式表演前聚集在劇院外。"},{"en":"If onlookers are carefully dressed, the scene may suggest leisure, status or respect.","zh":"如果旁觀者衣着仔細，場景可能暗示閒暇、地位或敬意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes viewers, not builders or workers.","zh":"這個短語描述觀看者，而不是建造者或工人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"interrupt their stroll","meaning":"中斷散步","examples":[{"en":"The onlookers interrupt their stroll to look at the structure.","zh":"旁觀者中斷散步，觀看這個結構。"},{"en":"To interrupt their stroll means to stop a relaxed walk for a moment.","zh":"中斷散步指暫時停下悠閒步行。"},{"en":"A couple may interrupt their stroll to watch street musicians in a park.","zh":"一對夫婦可能中斷散步，觀看公園中的街頭音樂人。"},{"en":"If people stop walking to look at a bridge, the structure has attracted their attention.","zh":"如果人們停下腳步看橋，該結構就吸引了他們注意。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a brief pause caused by interest.","zh":"這個短語顯示因興趣而出現的短暫停頓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"along the riverbank","meaning":"沿着河岸","examples":[{"en":"The figures walk along the riverbank beside the bridge.","zh":"畫中人物沿着橋旁河岸行走。"},{"en":"Along the riverbank means following the land beside a river.","zh":"沿着河岸指沿着河邊土地前進。"},{"en":"Joggers may run along the riverbank in the early morning.","zh":"跑步者可能在清晨沿着河岸跑步。"},{"en":"If people walk along the riverbank, they experience the bridge as part of the surrounding landscape.","zh":"如果人們沿着河岸走，他們就把橋樑體驗為周邊景觀的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a route beside water.","zh":"這個短語給出水邊路線。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"gently flowing river","meaning":"緩緩流動的河流","examples":[{"en":"The bridge stands above a gently flowing river.","zh":"這座橋矗立在緩緩流動的河流上方。"},{"en":"A gently flowing river is a river moving slowly and calmly.","zh":"緩緩流動的河流是慢慢而平靜流動的河。"},{"en":"A picnic beside a gently flowing river can feel peaceful and relaxing.","zh":"在緩緩流動的河流旁野餐，可以感覺平和放鬆。"},{"en":"If a powerful iron bridge stands above gentle water, the contrast softens the scene.","zh":"如果強大的鐵橋位於柔和水流之上，這種對比會令場景變得柔和。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a calm natural background.","zh":"這個短語營造平靜的自然背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a lone man","meaning":"一名獨行男子","examples":[{"en":"A lone man leads two mules beneath the bridge.","zh":"一名獨行男子牽着兩頭騾子走在橋下。"},{"en":"A lone man is a single man by himself, without companions nearby.","zh":"一名獨行男子是獨自一人、附近沒有同伴的男子。"},{"en":"A lone man waiting at a bus stop may make a photograph feel quiet and still.","zh":"獨自等巴士的男子可能令照片感覺安靜而凝定。"},{"en":"If one figure appears alone in a large landscape, the scene may feel peaceful or lonely.","zh":"如果一個人物獨自出現在大景觀中，場景可能感覺平和或孤寂。"},{"en":"The phrase draws attention to one isolated person.","zh":"這個短語把注意力集中於一名孤立人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lead two mules","meaning":"牽着兩頭騾子","examples":[{"en":"The man leads two mules along the towpath.","zh":"這名男子沿着纖道牽着兩頭騾子。"},{"en":"To lead two mules means to guide two working animals by walking in front of or beside them.","zh":"牽着兩頭騾子指走在兩頭工作動物前面或旁邊，引導牠們前進。"},{"en":"A farmer may lead two mules from a field back to a stable.","zh":"農夫可能把兩頭騾子從田地牽回馬廄。"},{"en":"If animals are being led beside a river, the scene suggests old transport and rural labour.","zh":"如果動物被牽着沿河行走，場景就暗示舊式運輸和鄉郊勞動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a slow practical action involving animals.","zh":"這個短語描述與動物相關的緩慢實際動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"beneath an arch","meaning":"在拱門下面","examples":[{"en":"The animals pass beneath an arch in the bridge.","zh":"這些動物從橋的一個拱門下面經過。"},{"en":"Beneath an arch means under a curved opening in a structure.","zh":"在拱門下面指在結構中彎曲開口的下方。"},{"en":"Children may walk beneath an arch at the entrance of an old school.","zh":"孩子可能從舊校入口的拱門下面走過。"},{"en":"If a path passes beneath an arch, the structure allows movement through it.","zh":"如果小路穿過拱門下方，該結構就容許人穿過它。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a clear spatial position below a curved form.","zh":"這個短語給出彎曲形態下方的清楚空間位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"let the towpath pass through","meaning":"讓纖道穿過","examples":[{"en":"The arch lets the towpath pass through the bridge’s abutment.","zh":"這個拱門讓纖道穿過橋台。"},{"en":"To let the towpath pass through means to allow the riverside path to continue through an opening.","zh":"讓纖道穿過指容許河邊小路經開口繼續延伸。"},{"en":"A tunnel lets pedestrians pass through a busy road safely.","zh":"隧道讓行人安全穿過繁忙道路。"},{"en":"If a bridge design lets a path continue, it fits transport needs on land and water.","zh":"如果橋樑設計讓小路延續，它就配合陸上和水上交通需要。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how engineering solves a practical movement problem.","zh":"這個短語顯示工程如何解決實際通行問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bridge abutment","meaning":"橋台","examples":[{"en":"The arch was built into the bridge abutment.","zh":"這個拱門建於橋台之中。"},{"en":"A bridge abutment is the support structure at the end of a bridge, holding it up and connecting it to land.","zh":"橋台是橋樑末端的支撐結構，用來支撐橋並把它連接到土地。"},{"en":"Engineers inspect bridge abutments to check whether the bridge remains safe.","zh":"工程師檢查橋台，以確認橋樑是否仍然安全。"},{"en":"If an abutment is weak, the bridge may not transfer weight properly to the ground.","zh":"如果橋台脆弱，橋樑可能無法把重量正確傳到地面。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a key supporting part of a bridge.","zh":"這個短語指橋樑的重要支撐部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a single boatman","meaning":"一名船夫","examples":[{"en":"A single boatman paddles across the river.","zh":"一名船夫划船橫過河流。"},{"en":"A single boatman is one person operating a small boat alone.","zh":"一名船夫是獨自操作小船的一個人。"},{"en":"A single boatman may carry visitors across a quiet lake in summer.","zh":"夏天，一名船夫可能載遊客橫過安靜湖泊。"},{"en":"If only one boatman appears in a painting, the river scene may feel calm and simple.","zh":"如果畫中只有一名船夫，河景可能感覺平靜而簡樸。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on one individual within a wider landscape.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於廣闊景觀中的一個人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"paddle across","meaning":"划船橫過","examples":[{"en":"The boatman paddles across the river in a small vessel.","zh":"船夫乘小船划船橫過河流。"},{"en":"To paddle across means to move over water by using a paddle.","zh":"“Paddle across” 指使用槳在水面上橫過。"},{"en":"A camper may paddle across a lake in a small canoe.","zh":"露營者可能乘小獨木舟划過湖泊。"},{"en":"If someone paddles across slowly, the movement can make a scene feel peaceful.","zh":"如果某人慢慢划船橫過，動作可以令場景感覺平和。"},{"en":"The phrase describes crossing water by manual effort.","zh":"這個短語描述透過人力橫過水面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tub boat","meaning":"小型桶狀船","examples":[{"en":"The painting includes a tiny tub boat on the river.","zh":"這幅畫包括河上一艘小型桶狀船。"},{"en":"A tub boat is a small, simple boat once used on canals or rivers, often for carrying goods.","zh":"小型桶狀船是一種曾用於運河或河流的小型簡單船隻，常用來運貨。"},{"en":"A museum may display a tub boat to show how people moved materials before modern transport.","zh":"博物館可能展示小型桶狀船，以說明現代交通前人們如何運送材料。"},{"en":"If a tiny boat appears beside a large bridge, the contrast shows scale.","zh":"如果小船出現在大橋旁邊，對比就顯示規模。"},{"en":"The phrase names a small historical working vessel.","zh":"這個短語指出一種小型歷史工作船。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be in no rush","meaning":"並不趕急","examples":[{"en":"The boatman is in no rush as he crosses the river.","zh":"船夫橫過河流時並不趕急。"},{"en":"To be in no rush means not to hurry because there is enough time or no pressure.","zh":"“Be in no rush” 指不急忙，因為有足夠時間或沒有壓力。"},{"en":"A retired neighbour may be in no rush while walking to the market.","zh":"退休鄰居步行去市場時可能並不趕急。"},{"en":"If a scene shows people in no rush, it can feel calm and unhurried.","zh":"如果場景顯示人們並不趕急，它可以感覺平靜而悠閒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes relaxed timing.","zh":"這個短語描述放鬆的時間感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"towline","meaning":"牽引繩","examples":[{"en":"The bridge design removed the need to carry a towline across the path.","zh":"橋樑設計消除了把牽引繩帶過小路的需要。"},{"en":"A towline is a rope or line used to pull a boat or another object.","zh":"牽引繩是用來拉船或其他物件的繩索。"},{"en":"A small boat may use a towline when it needs to be pulled along a canal.","zh":"小船需要沿運河被拉動時，可能使用牽引繩。"},{"en":"If a bridge blocks a towline, workers may need to lift or carry the rope over obstacles.","zh":"如果橋樑阻擋牽引繩，工人可能需要把繩提起或搬過障礙物。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a practical tool used in transport work.","zh":"這個短語指運輸工作中使用的實用工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a coloured engraving","meaning":"彩色版畫","examples":[{"en":"A coloured engraving of the bridge hangs in the museum.","zh":"一幅橋樑彩色版畫掛在博物館中。"},{"en":"A coloured engraving is a printed image made from an engraved surface and later coloured.","zh":"彩色版畫是由雕刻表面印出並後來上色的圖像。"},{"en":"A museum may display coloured engravings of old city streets before photography existed.","zh":"博物館可能展示攝影出現前舊城市街道的彩色版畫。"},{"en":"If an engraving is coloured, it can make a historical scene more vivid to viewers.","zh":"如果版畫上色，它可以令歷史場景對觀眾更生動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an old form of printed artwork.","zh":"這個短語指一種古老印刷藝術形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"countless contemporary renderings","meaning":"無數同時代的描繪作品","examples":[{"en":"The museum contains countless contemporary renderings of Iron Bridge.","zh":"博物館收藏無數 Iron Bridge 的同時代描繪作品。"},{"en":"Countless contemporary renderings are many artistic depictions made around the same period as the subject.","zh":"無數同時代的描繪作品，是在題材所屬時期前後製作的大量藝術描繪。"},{"en":"A museum may collect contemporary renderings of a new railway station from newspapers and artists.","zh":"博物館可能從報紙和藝術家手中收藏新火車站的同時代描繪作品。"},{"en":"If many artists depicted the bridge at the time, it clearly attracted public imagination.","zh":"如果當時許多藝術家描繪這座橋，它顯然激發了公眾想像。"},{"en":"The phrase shows both quantity and historical closeness.","zh":"這個短語同時顯示數量和歷史接近性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in its full glory","meaning":"展現其最壯麗的一面","examples":[{"en":"The pictures show the bridge in its full glory.","zh":"這些圖畫展現這座橋最壯麗的一面。"},{"en":"In its full glory means shown at its most impressive, complete or beautiful.","zh":"“In its full glory” 指以最令人印象深刻、最完整或最美麗的狀態展示。"},{"en":"A school hall looks in its full glory during graduation, with lights, flowers and music.","zh":"畢業禮時，校禮堂有燈光、鮮花和音樂，展現其最壯麗的一面。"},{"en":"If a bridge is shown in full glory, viewers see it as magnificent rather than ordinary.","zh":"如果橋樑被展現其最壯麗一面，觀眾就會把它看成宏偉而非普通。"},{"en":"The phrase presents something at its best.","zh":"這個短語呈現某物的最佳狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in its context","meaning":"在其周遭環境中","examples":[{"en":"The paintings show the bridge in its natural and social context.","zh":"這些畫作在其自然和社會周遭環境中呈現這座橋。"},{"en":"In its context means shown together with the surroundings, people and conditions that give it meaning.","zh":"“In its context” 指與賦予其意義的環境、人物和條件一起展示。"},{"en":"A museum object is easier to understand in its context, with photos of how it was used.","zh":"如果博物館物件配有使用照片，就更容易在其背景中理解。"},{"en":"If a bridge is shown with river life and walkers, viewers see its role in daily society.","zh":"如果橋樑與河上生活和行人一起呈現，觀眾就能看見它在日常社會中的角色。"},{"en":"The phrase prevents an object from being viewed in isolation.","zh":"這個短語避免物件被孤立觀看。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not as a blight on the landscape","meaning":"並非景觀中的破壞物","examples":[{"en":"The artist showed the bridge not as a blight on the landscape but as its centre.","zh":"藝術家把這座橋呈現為景觀中心，而並非景觀中的破壞物。"},{"en":"Not as a blight on the landscape means not as something ugly that spoils the view.","zh":"並非景觀中的破壞物，指不是破壞景色的醜陋東西。"},{"en":"A well-designed school extension may be seen not as a blight but as a useful part of the campus.","zh":"設計良好的校舍擴建部分可能不被視為破壞物，而是校園有用一部分。"},{"en":"If an industrial structure is placed beautifully in a painting, it can enhance rather than damage the scene.","zh":"如果工業結構在畫中被美麗安置，它可以提升而不是破壞場景。"},{"en":"The phrase rejects the idea that technology necessarily ruins natural beauty.","zh":"這個短語否定科技必然破壞自然美的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at the centre of","meaning":"位於……的中心","examples":[{"en":"The iron structure stands at the centre of the landscape.","zh":"這座鐵結構位於景觀中心。"},{"en":"At the centre of something means in the most important or visually central position.","zh":"“At the centre of” 某事指在最重要或視覺上最中央的位置。"},{"en":"A teacher may place the main question at the centre of a lesson.","zh":"老師可能把主要問題放在課堂中心。"},{"en":"If a bridge is at the centre of a painting, other details seem to depend on it.","zh":"如果橋樑位於畫作中心，其他細節就像依附於它。"},{"en":"The phrase can refer to physical position or importance.","zh":"這個短語可以指實際位置或重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"surrounding area","meaning":"周邊地區","examples":[{"en":"The surrounding area appears to radiate out from the bridge.","zh":"周邊地區看似從橋樑向外延伸。"},{"en":"The surrounding area is the land, buildings or space around a central place or object.","zh":"周邊地區是中心地點或物件周圍的土地、建築或空間。"},{"en":"A school’s surrounding area may include shops, bus stops and housing estates.","zh":"學校周邊地區可能包括商店、巴士站和屋苑。"},{"en":"If the surrounding area is arranged around a bridge, the bridge becomes the visual centre.","zh":"如果周邊地區圍繞橋樑安排，橋樑就成為視覺中心。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what lies around something.","zh":"這個短語描述某物周圍的範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"radiate out from","meaning":"從……向外延伸","examples":[{"en":"The landscape seems to radiate out from the central structure.","zh":"景觀看似從中央結構向外延伸。"},{"en":"To radiate out from something means to spread outward from a central point.","zh":"“Radiate out from” 某物指從中心點向外擴散或延伸。"},{"en":"Roads may radiate out from a town square like spokes from a wheel.","zh":"道路可能像車輪輻條一樣從城鎮廣場向外延伸。"},{"en":"If attention radiates out from a bridge, the whole painting is organised around it.","zh":"如果注意力從橋樑向外延伸，整幅畫就圍繞它組織。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests outward movement from a centre.","zh":"這個短語暗示由中心向外的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pale behind","meaning":"在……背後顯得失色","examples":[{"en":"The surrounding landscape pales behind the bridge.","zh":"周圍景觀在橋樑背後顯得失色。"},{"en":"To pale behind something means to seem less impressive or less noticeable compared with it.","zh":"“Pale behind” 某物指與它相比顯得不那麼出色或不那麼明顯。"},{"en":"A simple speech may pale behind a powerful personal story.","zh":"簡單演講在有力個人故事背後可能顯得失色。"},{"en":"If the bridge is visually dominant, trees and hills may seem weaker in comparison.","zh":"如果橋樑在視覺上佔主導，樹木和山丘相比之下可能較弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being overshadowed by something stronger.","zh":"這個短語描述被更強事物蓋過。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"capture the imagination of","meaning":"激發……的想像力","examples":[{"en":"Railways captured the imagination of nineteenth-century artists.","zh":"鐵路激發了十九世紀藝術家的想像力。"},{"en":"To capture the imagination of people means to strongly interest and excite their creative thoughts.","zh":"“Capture the imagination of” 某些人指強烈吸引並激發他們的創意思考。"},{"en":"Space travel captured the imagination of many children after they watched a rocket launch.","zh":"孩子觀看火箭發射後，太空旅行激發了許多孩子的想像力。"},{"en":"If railways seemed fast and modern, artists naturally wanted to depict them.","zh":"如果鐵路看起來快速而現代，藝術家自然想描繪它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes powerful creative fascination shared by a group.","zh":"這個短語描述一群人共有的強烈創作迷戀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"steam engine","meaning":"蒸汽機車","examples":[{"en":"A steam engine could become an important feature of a landscape painting.","zh":"蒸汽機車可以成為風景畫的重要元素。"},{"en":"A steam engine is a machine powered by steam, often used in early trains and factories.","zh":"蒸汽機車是由蒸汽驅動的機器，常用於早期火車和工廠。"},{"en":"A museum may display a steam engine to show how transport changed in the Industrial Revolution.","zh":"博物館可能展示蒸汽機車，以說明工業革命中交通如何改變。"},{"en":"If a steam engine appears in a landscape, industry becomes part of the scenery.","zh":"如果蒸汽機車出現在風景中，工業就成為景色的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase names a key machine of early industrial technology.","zh":"這個短語指出早期工業科技的關鍵機器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in the distance","meaning":"在遠處","examples":[{"en":"The artist placed the steam engine in the distance.","zh":"藝術家把蒸汽機車放在遠處。"},{"en":"In the distance means far away from the viewer or main foreground.","zh":"“In the distance” 指離觀者或主要前景很遠。"},{"en":"A photograph may show mountains in the distance behind a school playground.","zh":"照片可能顯示學校操場後方遠處的山脈。"},{"en":"If a train appears in the distance, it can suggest movement without dominating the scene.","zh":"如果火車出現在遠處，它可以暗示移動而不主導場景。"},{"en":"The phrase describes far-off visual position.","zh":"這個短語描述遠方的視覺位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as much a part of","meaning":"與……同樣成為一部分","examples":[{"en":"The railway became as much a part of the landscape as the animals.","zh":"鐵路與動物同樣成為景觀的一部分。"},{"en":"As much a part of something as another thing means equally belonging to it.","zh":"“As much a part of” 某事 “as” 另一物，指同樣屬於其中。"},{"en":"Buses are as much a part of city life as shops and schools.","zh":"巴士與商店和學校同樣是城市生活的一部分。"},{"en":"If railways become part of the landscape, technology no longer feels separate from nature.","zh":"如果鐵路成為景觀的一部分，科技就不再感覺與自然分離。"},{"en":"The phrase shows equal inclusion in a wider whole.","zh":"這個短語顯示在較大整體中的同等包含。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a herd of cows","meaning":"一群牛","examples":[{"en":"A herd of cows appears in the foreground of the landscape.","zh":"一群牛出現在風景畫前景。"},{"en":"A herd of cows is a group of cows together.","zh":"一群牛是聚在一起的牛。"},{"en":"A farmer may move a herd of cows from one field to another.","zh":"農夫可能把一群牛從一塊田移到另一塊田。"},{"en":"If cows appear beside a railway, rural life and industry are shown together.","zh":"如果牛群出現在鐵路旁，鄉村生活和工業就被一起呈現。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a natural and agricultural detail.","zh":"這個短語給出自然和農業細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in the foreground","meaning":"在前景","examples":[{"en":"The animals are shown in the foreground of the painting.","zh":"這些動物被畫在畫作前景。"},{"en":"In the foreground means in the front part of an image, closest to the viewer.","zh":"“In the foreground” 指在影像最前面、最接近觀者的部分。"},{"en":"A class photo may show students in the foreground and the school building behind them.","zh":"班相可能把學生放在前景，校舍在後方。"},{"en":"If animals are placed in the foreground, viewers notice rural life first.","zh":"如果動物被放在前景，觀者會先注意到鄉村生活。"},{"en":"The phrase helps describe visual arrangement in art or photography.","zh":"這個短語幫助描述藝術或攝影中的視覺安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"man-made structures","meaning":"人造建築","examples":[{"en":"Claude Monet frequently painted man-made structures.","zh":"Claude Monet 經常畫人造建築。"},{"en":"Man-made structures are buildings, bridges, stations or other forms created by people rather than nature.","zh":"人造建築是由人而非自然創造的建築物、橋樑、車站或其他形態。"},{"en":"Roads, tunnels and apartment blocks are man-made structures in a city.","zh":"道路、隧道和住宅大廈都是城市中的人造建築。"},{"en":"If artists paint man-made structures, they treat human construction as worthy of attention.","zh":"如果藝術家畫人造建築，他們就是把人類建造物視為值得注意。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts built objects with natural features.","zh":"這個短語把建成物與自然特徵作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"railway stations","meaning":"火車站","examples":[{"en":"Railway stations became important subjects for Impressionist painters.","zh":"火車站成為印象派畫家的重要題材。"},{"en":"Railway stations are places where passengers board, leave or change trains.","zh":"火車站是乘客上車、下車或轉車的地方。"},{"en":"A busy railway station can show crowds, steam, movement and modern life.","zh":"繁忙火車站可以展示人群、蒸汽、流動和現代生活。"},{"en":"If painters choose railway stations, they are interested in technology and public space.","zh":"如果畫家選擇火車站，他們就是對科技和公共空間感興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase names a transport setting that can also be artistic.","zh":"這個短語指出一個也可以具藝術性的交通場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cathedrals","meaning":"大教堂","examples":[{"en":"Monet painted cathedrals as well as natural subjects.","zh":"Monet 既畫自然題材，也畫大教堂。"},{"en":"Cathedrals are large and important Christian church buildings, often architecturally impressive.","zh":"大教堂是大型而重要的基督教教堂建築，通常在建築上令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"Tourists may visit cathedrals to admire stained glass, stonework and high ceilings.","zh":"遊客可能參觀大教堂，欣賞彩色玻璃、石工和高高天花。"},{"en":"If an artist paints cathedrals repeatedly, they may be studying light and form as much as religion.","zh":"如果藝術家反覆畫大教堂，他可能研究光線和形態，不只是宗教。"},{"en":"The word refers to grand religious architecture.","zh":"這個詞指宏偉宗教建築。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"以及；同時","examples":[{"en":"The artist painted industrial structures as well as water lilies.","zh":"這位藝術家畫睡蓮，也畫工業結構。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to another thing already mentioned.","zh":"“As well as” 指除了已提及的事物之外，也包括另一事物。"},{"en":"A student needs sleep as well as revision before an important exam.","zh":"學生在重要考試前需要溫習，也需要睡眠。"},{"en":"If Monet painted industry as well as nature, his subjects were broader than people may think.","zh":"如果 Monet 既畫工業也畫自然，其題材就比人們想像更廣。"},{"en":"The phrase adds another item without replacing the first.","zh":"這個短語加入另一項，而不是取代第一項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"portrait painters","meaning":"肖像畫家","examples":[{"en":"Portrait painters also found subjects in engineers and inventors.","zh":"肖像畫家也從工程師和發明家中找到題材。"},{"en":"Portrait painters are artists who paint people, usually focusing on face, character and status.","zh":"肖像畫家是畫人物的藝術家，通常集中於面孔、性格和地位。"},{"en":"A portrait painter may show a scientist holding tools that explain their work.","zh":"肖像畫家可能畫科學家拿着能說明其工作的工具。"},{"en":"If engineers appear in portraits, technology becomes part of personal and cultural identity.","zh":"如果工程師出現在肖像中，科技就成為個人和文化身份的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to artists who specialise in representing people.","zh":"這個短語指專門描繪人物的藝術家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"find subjects in","meaning":"從……找到創作題材","examples":[{"en":"Artists found subjects in engineers, inventors and their creations.","zh":"藝術家從工程師、發明家及其創造物中找到創作題材。"},{"en":"To find subjects in something means to discover material worth painting, photographing or writing about.","zh":"“Find subjects in” 某事指發現值得繪畫、拍攝或寫作的材料。"},{"en":"A writer may find subjects in ordinary bus journeys and family conversations.","zh":"作家可能從普通巴士旅程和家庭對話中找到創作題材。"},{"en":"If artists find subjects in engineering, they see creative value in technical life.","zh":"如果藝術家從工程中找到題材，他們就看見技術生活中的創作價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes discovering artistic material in a source.","zh":"這個短語描述在某來源中發現藝術材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"engineers and inventors","meaning":"工程師與發明家","examples":[{"en":"Engineers and inventors appeared in nineteenth-century portraits.","zh":"工程師與發明家出現在十九世紀肖像畫中。"},{"en":"Engineers and inventors are people who design structures, machines, systems or new devices.","zh":"工程師與發明家是設計結構、機器、系統或新裝置的人。"},{"en":"A museum may display portraits of engineers and inventors who changed transport.","zh":"博物館可能展示改變交通的工程師與發明家的肖像。"},{"en":"If artists paint such figures, they honour technical creativity as part of history.","zh":"如果藝術家描繪這些人物，他們就是把技術創意作為歷史一部分來尊重。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people behind technological change.","zh":"這個短語指科技變革背後的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the American founding fathers","meaning":"美國開國元勳","examples":[{"en":"Christian Schussele painted inventors as well as the American founding fathers.","zh":"Christian Schussele 畫發明家，也畫美國開國元勳。"},{"en":"The American founding fathers were key political leaders involved in the creation of the United States.","zh":"美國開國元勳是參與建立美國的重要政治領袖。"},{"en":"History textbooks often show the American founding fathers in formal portraits.","zh":"歷史教科書常以正式肖像展示美國開國元勳。"},{"en":"If inventors are painted beside founding fathers, technical achievement is given national importance.","zh":"如果發明家與開國元勳並列被畫，技術成就就被賦予國家重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to major historical figures in American nation-building.","zh":"這個短語指美國建國中的重要歷史人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be well established as","meaning":"已確立為……","examples":[{"en":"By the twentieth century, industry was well established as an artistic subject.","zh":"到二十世紀，工業已確立為藝術題材。"},{"en":"To be well established as something means to be widely accepted and recognised in that role.","zh":"“Be well established as” 某物指在該角色中被廣泛接受和認可。"},{"en":"Online learning is now well established as part of many schools’ teaching methods.","zh":"網上學習現在已確立為許多學校教學方法的一部分。"},{"en":"If industry is well established as art, artists no longer need to justify choosing factories as subjects.","zh":"如果工業已確立為藝術，藝術家就不再需要為選擇工廠作題材辯護。"},{"en":"The phrase shows strong acceptance over time.","zh":"這個短語顯示經時間形成的強烈接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"subjects for artists","meaning":"藝術家的創作題材","examples":[{"en":"Engineering and technology became accepted subjects for artists.","zh":"工程和科技成為被接受的藝術家創作題材。"},{"en":"Subjects for artists are people, places, objects or ideas that artists choose to represent.","zh":"藝術家的創作題材，是藝術家選擇呈現的人、地方、物件或想法。"},{"en":"Street markets, family kitchens and railway stations can all become subjects for artists.","zh":"街市、家庭廚房和火車站都可以成為藝術家的創作題材。"},{"en":"If technology becomes a subject for artists, machines can be studied visually and emotionally.","zh":"如果科技成為藝術題材，機器就可以在視覺和情感上被研究。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to material suitable for artistic creation.","zh":"這個短語指適合藝術創作的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"illustrate travel articles","meaning":"為旅遊文章繪畫插圖","examples":[{"en":"Joseph Pennell illustrated many European travel articles.","zh":"Joseph Pennell 為許多歐洲旅遊文章繪畫插圖。"},{"en":"To illustrate travel articles means to create pictures that accompany written pieces about places and journeys.","zh":"為旅遊文章繪畫插圖指為關於地方和旅程的文章創作配圖。"},{"en":"A magazine may hire an artist to illustrate travel articles about old towns.","zh":"雜誌可能聘請藝術家為關於古鎮的旅遊文章繪畫插圖。"},{"en":"If illustrations are vivid, readers can imagine places they have never visited.","zh":"如果插圖生動，讀者就能想像未曾到訪的地方。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visual support for travel writing.","zh":"這個短語描述為旅遊寫作提供視覺支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"early in one’s career","meaning":"在某人職業生涯初期","examples":[{"en":"Early in his career, Pennell drew buildings under construction.","zh":"在職業生涯初期，Pennell 畫正在興建的建築物。"},{"en":"Early in one’s career means near the beginning of someone’s working life.","zh":"在某人職業生涯初期，指在某人工作人生的早期。"},{"en":"Early in her career, a teacher may spend extra time preparing every lesson.","zh":"在職業生涯初期，老師可能花額外時間準備每一課。"},{"en":"If an artist chooses construction sites early in his career, that interest may shape later work.","zh":"如果藝術家在職業生涯初期選擇建築地盤，這種興趣可能塑造後來作品。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a time point in professional development.","zh":"這個短語給出專業發展中的時間點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"under construction","meaning":"正在興建","examples":[{"en":"The buildings were still under construction when Pennell drew them.","zh":"Pennell 畫這些建築時，它們仍在興建中。"},{"en":"Under construction means being built and not yet finished.","zh":"“Under construction” 指正在建造，尚未完成。"},{"en":"A new school hall may be under construction for several months.","zh":"新學校禮堂可能正在興建數個月。"},{"en":"If a bridge is under construction, artists can see the hidden process before completion.","zh":"如果橋樑正在興建，藝術家就能在完成前看見隱藏過程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an unfinished building stage.","zh":"這個短語描述未完成的建築階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be shrouded in scaffolding","meaning":"被棚架包圍","examples":[{"en":"The incomplete buildings were shrouded in scaffolding.","zh":"未完成建築被棚架包圍。"},{"en":"To be shrouded in scaffolding means to be covered or surrounded by temporary metal or wooden construction frames.","zh":"“Be shrouded in scaffolding” 指被臨時金屬或木製建築框架覆蓋或包圍。"},{"en":"An old library may be shrouded in scaffolding during repair work.","zh":"舊圖書館維修期間可能被棚架包圍。"},{"en":"If a building is wrapped in scaffolding, viewers can tell it is still being built or restored.","zh":"如果建築被棚架包住，觀者就知道它仍在興建或修復。"},{"en":"The phrase creates an image of construction surrounding a structure.","zh":"這個短語營造建築被施工結構包圍的畫面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"return to America","meaning":"返回美國","examples":[{"en":"Pennell returned to America late in his life.","zh":"Pennell 在晚年返回美國。"},{"en":"To return to America means to go back to the United States after being elsewhere.","zh":"返回美國指在身處其他地方後回到美國。"},{"en":"A student may return to America after studying abroad for a year.","zh":"學生可能在海外留學一年後返回美國。"},{"en":"If an artist returns home late in life, earlier experiences may influence how they see the country.","zh":"如果藝術家晚年回國，早期經歷可能影響他如何看待國家。"},{"en":"The phrase describes going back to a national home or base.","zh":"這個短語描述回到國家家園或基地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"late in life","meaning":"在晚年","examples":[{"en":"The artist returned to America late in life.","zh":"這位藝術家在晚年返回美國。"},{"en":"Late in life means during someone’s later years, often when they are older.","zh":"在晚年指在一個人生命較後期，通常年紀較大時。"},{"en":"A person may learn painting late in life after retiring.","zh":"一個人可能退休後在晚年學畫。"},{"en":"If someone changes direction late in life, it shows growth does not belong only to youth.","zh":"如果某人在晚年改變方向，就顯示成長不只屬於年輕時。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a time near the later part of a person’s life.","zh":"這個短語給出人生較後段的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"record industrial activities","meaning":"記錄工業活動","examples":[{"en":"Pennell recorded industrial activities during the First World War.","zh":"Pennell 在第一次世界大戰期間記錄工業活動。"},{"en":"To record industrial activities means to document factory work, construction or production through writing, drawing or photography.","zh":"記錄工業活動指透過文字、繪畫或攝影記錄工廠工作、建造或生產。"},{"en":"A photographer may record industrial activities in a shipyard for a history project.","zh":"攝影師可能為歷史項目記錄造船廠的工業活動。"},{"en":"If artists record industry, future generations can see how work was organised.","zh":"如果藝術家記錄工業，後代就能看見工作如何組織。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preserving images of labour and production.","zh":"這個短語描述保存勞動和生產影像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be best known for","meaning":"最廣為人知的是","examples":[{"en":"Pennell is best known for his drawings of major engineering projects.","zh":"Pennell 最廣為人知的是他描繪重大工程項目的畫作。"},{"en":"To be best known for something means to be most famous because of it.","zh":"“Be best known for” 某事指因它而最有名。"},{"en":"A teacher may be best known for making difficult grammar easy to understand.","zh":"老師可能最廣為人知的是把困難文法講得容易明白。"},{"en":"If an artist is best known for bridges, that subject defines their public reputation.","zh":"如果藝術家最以橋樑聞名，該題材就定義了其公眾聲譽。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the main reason someone is remembered.","zh":"這個短語指出某人被記住的主要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"depiction of the Panama Canal","meaning":"對巴拿馬運河的描繪","examples":[{"en":"Pennell produced a famous depiction of the Panama Canal.","zh":"Pennell 創作了一幅著名的巴拿馬運河描繪作品。"},{"en":"A depiction of the Panama Canal is an artistic or written representation of that major waterway.","zh":"對巴拿馬運河的描繪，是對這條重大水道的藝術或文字呈現。"},{"en":"A painting may depict the Panama Canal by showing ships, locks and workers.","zh":"畫作可能透過展示船隻、水閘和工人來描繪巴拿馬運河。"},{"en":"If an engineering project is depicted powerfully, viewers may understand its scale and difficulty.","zh":"如果工程項目被有力描繪，觀眾可能理解其規模和難度。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a representation of a specific engineering work.","zh":"這個短語指對特定工程作品的呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"near completion","meaning":"接近竣工","examples":[{"en":"The Panama Canal was near completion when Pennell depicted it.","zh":"Pennell 描繪巴拿馬運河時，它已接近竣工。"},{"en":"Near completion means almost finished but not completely done.","zh":"接近竣工指幾乎完成，但尚未完全完成。"},{"en":"A new sports centre may be near completion when workers are painting the final walls.","zh":"當工人正在粉刷最後牆身，新體育中心可能接近竣工。"},{"en":"If a project is near completion, viewers can see both the finished form and remaining work.","zh":"如果項目接近竣工，觀者可以同時看見完成形態和剩餘工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the final stage before completion.","zh":"這個短語描述完成前的最後階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"etchings","meaning":"蝕刻版畫","examples":[{"en":"Pennell produced etchings of several unfinished bridges.","zh":"Pennell 創作了幾座未完成橋樑的蝕刻版畫。"},{"en":"Etchings are prints made from designs cut or chemically marked into a metal plate.","zh":"蝕刻版畫是由刻入或以化學方法標記在金屬板上的設計印製而成的版畫。"},{"en":"An art class may study etchings to understand older printmaking techniques.","zh":"美術課可能研究蝕刻版畫，以理解較古老的版畫技術。"},{"en":"If an artist uses etching, lines and shadows can give engineering structures strong texture.","zh":"如果藝術家使用蝕刻，線條和陰影可以令工程結構有強烈質感。"},{"en":"The word refers to a printmaking form, not a simple sketch.","zh":"這個詞指一種版畫形式，而不是簡單素描。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"partially completed bridges","meaning":"部分建成的橋樑","examples":[{"en":"His works showed partially completed bridges.","zh":"他的作品展示部分建成的橋樑。"},{"en":"Partially completed bridges are bridges that have been built in part but are not yet finished.","zh":"部分建成的橋樑是已建成一部分但尚未完成的橋。"},{"en":"Drivers may see partially completed bridges beside highways during long construction projects.","zh":"在漫長建築工程期間，司機可能在高速公路旁看見部分建成的橋樑。"},{"en":"If a bridge is only partly complete, its beams and supports reveal the construction process.","zh":"如果橋只完成部分，其橫樑和支撐就揭示建造過程。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises an unfinished stage of engineering.","zh":"這個短語強調工程未完成階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the Hell Gate Bridge","meaning":"Hell Gate Bridge（橋名）","examples":[{"en":"Pennell depicted the Hell Gate Bridge before it was completed.","zh":"Pennell 在 Hell Gate Bridge 完成前描繪了它。"},{"en":"The Hell Gate Bridge is a major bridge in New York that became a subject of engineering art.","zh":"Hell Gate Bridge 是紐約一座重要橋樑，成為工程藝術題材。"},{"en":"An artist may choose the Hell Gate Bridge because its steel arches create strong visual lines.","zh":"藝術家可能選擇 Hell Gate Bridge，因為其鋼拱形成強烈視覺線條。"},{"en":"If a bridge is drawn before completion, the artwork records both construction and ambition.","zh":"如果橋樑在完成前被畫下，作品就記錄了建造和抱負。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific bridge linked with industrial modernity.","zh":"這個短語指出一座與工業現代性相關的特定橋樑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the Delaware River Bridge","meaning":"Delaware River Bridge（橋名）","examples":[{"en":"The Delaware River Bridge appeared in Pennell’s engineering art.","zh":"Delaware River Bridge 出現在 Pennell 的工程藝術中。"},{"en":"The Delaware River Bridge is a bridge associated here with large-scale engineering and artistic depiction.","zh":"Delaware River Bridge 在此是一座與大型工程和藝術描繪相關的橋樑。"},{"en":"A bridge over a major river may attract artists because it combines structure, water and movement.","zh":"橫跨大河的橋可能吸引藝術家，因為它結合結構、水和流動。"},{"en":"If Pennell depicted it, he treated it as more than a transport route.","zh":"如果 Pennell 描繪它，他就是把它視為不只是交通路線。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific engineering subject in art.","zh":"這個短語指出藝術中的特定工程題材。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be quoted as saying","meaning":"常被引述說","examples":[{"en":"Pennell has often been quoted as saying that great engineering is great art.","zh":"Pennell 常被引述說偉大的工程就是偉大的藝術。"},{"en":"To be quoted as saying something means people repeat words attributed to that person.","zh":"“Be quoted as saying” 某話指人們重複被歸於該人的說法。"},{"en":"A principal may be quoted as saying that reading changes students’ futures.","zh":"校長可能常被引述說閱讀改變學生未來。"},{"en":"If a phrase is often quoted, it becomes closely linked with the speaker’s reputation.","zh":"如果一句話常被引用，它就與說話者聲譽緊密相連。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a reported statement.","zh":"這個短語引出被轉述的說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Great engineering is great art","meaning":"偉大的工程就是偉大的藝術","examples":[{"en":"Pennell believed that great engineering is great art.","zh":"Pennell 相信偉大的工程就是偉大的藝術。"},{"en":"Great engineering is great art means excellent technical design can also possess artistic beauty and emotional power.","zh":"偉大的工程就是偉大的藝術，意思是出色技術設計也可以具有藝術美和情感力量。"},{"en":"A bridge that is safe, elegant and inspiring may prove that engineering can be art.","zh":"一座安全、優雅又鼓舞人心的橋，可能證明工程可以是藝術。"},{"en":"If a structure combines usefulness, scale and beauty, it can be admired like a painting.","zh":"如果結構結合實用性、規模和美感，就可以像畫作一樣被欣賞。"},{"en":"The phrase summarises the argument that technology and art can overlap.","zh":"這個短語總結科技與藝術可以重疊的論點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"express a sentiment","meaning":"表達一種看法","examples":[{"en":"Pennell repeatedly expressed the sentiment that engineering could be beautiful.","zh":"Pennell 反覆表達工程可以美麗這種看法。"},{"en":"To express a sentiment means to state a feeling, attitude or belief.","zh":"“Express a sentiment” 指表達一種感受、態度或信念。"},{"en":"A student may express the sentiment that school should care about mental health, not only grades.","zh":"學生可能表達學校應關心心理健康而不只是成績這種看法。"},{"en":"If an artist says engineering is beautiful, they are expressing a view about value.","zh":"如果藝術家說工程是美麗的，他就是在表達關於價值的看法。"},{"en":"The phrase usually refers to an opinion with emotional force.","zh":"這個短語通常指帶有情感力量的意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"one’s contemporaries","meaning":"某人的同時代人物","examples":[{"en":"Pennell admired the engineers among his contemporaries.","zh":"Pennell 欣賞其同時代人物中的工程師。"},{"en":"One’s contemporaries are people living or working during the same period as that person.","zh":"某人的同時代人物，是與該人在同一時期生活或工作的人。"},{"en":"A young writer may be influenced by their contemporaries in music, film and literature.","zh":"年輕作家可能受音樂、電影和文學界同時代人物影響。"},{"en":"If an artist admires engineers among his contemporaries, he values the creators of his own age.","zh":"如果藝術家欣賞其同時代工程師，他就是重視自己時代的創造者。"},{"en":"The phrase compares people within the same historical moment.","zh":"這個短語比較同一歷史時刻中的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"understand nothing of","meaning":"對……一無所知","examples":[{"en":"Pennell admitted that he understood nothing of engineering.","zh":"Pennell 承認自己對工程一無所知。"},{"en":"To understand nothing of something means to have no real knowledge of it.","zh":"“Understand nothing of” 某事指對它沒有真正知識。"},{"en":"A patient may understand nothing of medical scans but still trust the doctor’s explanation.","zh":"病人可能對醫學掃描一無所知，但仍信任醫生解釋。"},{"en":"If an artist understands little technical detail, they may still respond to visual power.","zh":"如果藝術家不太懂技術細節，仍可以回應視覺力量。"},{"en":"The phrase shows lack of expertise, often with honesty.","zh":"這個短語顯示缺乏專業知識，常帶坦誠意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the greatest architects","meaning":"最偉大的建築師","examples":[{"en":"He described engineers as the greatest architects since the Greeks.","zh":"他把工程師形容為自希臘人以來最偉大的建築師。"},{"en":"The greatest architects are the most important or impressive designers of built structures.","zh":"最偉大的建築師，是最重要或最令人印象深刻的建築結構設計者。"},{"en":"A city may honour its greatest architects by preserving the buildings they designed.","zh":"城市可能透過保存建築師設計的建築，向最偉大的建築師致敬。"},{"en":"If engineers are called great architects, their technical work is being praised as design.","zh":"如果工程師被稱為偉大建築師，其技術工作就是被讚揚為設計。"},{"en":"The phrase elevates engineering to the level of architecture.","zh":"這個短語把工程提升至建築藝術層次。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"pictorial builders","meaning":"具視覺美感的建造者","examples":[{"en":"Pennell regarded engineers as highly pictorial builders.","zh":"Pennell 視工程師為極具視覺美感的建造者。"},{"en":"Pictorial builders are builders whose structures create strong visual images.","zh":"具視覺美感的建造者，是其結構能創造強烈視覺影像的建造者。"},{"en":"A bridge designer may be a pictorial builder if the bridge looks striking in photographs.","zh":"如果橋樑在照片中看起來很突出，橋樑設計者就可以是具視覺美感的建造者。"},{"en":"If engineering shapes are visually powerful, they can attract artists as subjects.","zh":"如果工程形態在視覺上有力，它們就能吸引藝術家作題材。"},{"en":"The phrase links building skill with visual imagination.","zh":"這個短語把建造能力與視覺想像力連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"where some observers saw only utility","meaning":"當一些人只看見實用價值時","examples":[{"en":"Where some observers saw only utility, Pennell also saw beauty.","zh":"當一些觀察者只看見實用價值時，Pennell 也看見美。"},{"en":"Where some observers saw only utility means while some people noticed only practical usefulness.","zh":"“Where some observers saw only utility” 指當一些人只注意到實際用途時。"},{"en":"Some people see only utility in a school timetable, but others see care in how breaks are planned.","zh":"有些人只看見學校時間表的實用價值，但另一些人看見小息安排中的關懷。"},{"en":"If viewers see only function, they may miss form, scale and emotional effect.","zh":"如果觀者只看見功能，就可能錯過形態、規模和情感效果。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts narrow practical judgement with a richer artistic view.","zh":"這個短語把狹窄的實用判斷與更豐富的藝術視角作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"utility","meaning":"實用性","examples":[{"en":"An engineering structure may combine utility with beauty.","zh":"工程結構可以結合實用性與美感。"},{"en":"Utility means practical usefulness.","zh":"實用性指實際用途。"},{"en":"A raincoat has utility because it keeps people dry in bad weather.","zh":"雨衣具有實用性，因為它在壞天氣中令人保持乾爽。"},{"en":"If a bridge has utility, it helps people cross water or valleys safely.","zh":"如果橋樑有實用性，它就幫助人安全橫過水域或山谷。"},{"en":"The word focuses on function rather than decoration.","zh":"這個詞強調功能，而不是裝飾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"beauty in form","meaning":"形式之美","examples":[{"en":"Pennell sometimes found beauty in the form of a structure.","zh":"Pennell 有時在結構的形式中找到美。"},{"en":"Beauty in form means visual appeal found in shape, proportion and structure.","zh":"形式之美指在形狀、比例和結構中找到的視覺吸引力。"},{"en":"A simple chair can have beauty in form if its lines are clean and balanced.","zh":"如果線條乾淨而平衡，一張簡單椅子也可以有形式之美。"},{"en":"If a bridge has elegant curves, people may admire its form even before knowing how it works.","zh":"如果橋樑有優雅曲線，人們在了解其運作前已可能欣賞其形式。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on shape as a source of beauty.","zh":"這個短語強調形態作為美的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"if not in form, then in scale","meaning":"即使不在形式上，也在規模上","examples":[{"en":"He found beauty, if not in form, then at least in scale.","zh":"他即使不在形式上，也至少在規模上找到美。"},{"en":"If not in form, then in scale means that even if shape is not beautiful, size or magnitude may be impressive.","zh":"“If not in form, then in scale” 指即使形狀不美，大小或規模也可能令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"A plain stadium may impress visitors, if not in design, then in scale.","zh":"一座樸素體育館即使不在設計上，也可能在規模上令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"If a dam looks simple but enormous, its greatness may come from scale rather than detail.","zh":"如果水壩看起來簡單但巨大，其偉大可能來自規模而不是細節。"},{"en":"The phrase offers a second way to appreciate something.","zh":"這個短語提供欣賞某物的第二種方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"render a concrete subject","meaning":"描繪具體題材","examples":[{"en":"The artist was not merely rendering a concrete subject.","zh":"這位藝術家不只是描繪具體題材。"},{"en":"To render a concrete subject means to depict a real, physical object or scene in art.","zh":"描繪具體題材指在藝術中呈現真實、實體的物件或場景。"},{"en":"A painter rendering a market stall may carefully show fruit, baskets and people.","zh":"畫家描繪市場攤檔時，可能仔細展示水果、籃子和人。"},{"en":"If an artist only renders the object, they may miss the feeling it creates.","zh":"如果藝術家只描繪物件，就可能錯過它帶來的感覺。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts literal depiction with deeper impression.","zh":"這個短語把字面描繪與更深印象作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"convey an impression","meaning":"傳達印象","examples":[{"en":"Pennell wanted to convey the impression that the structure made on him.","zh":"Pennell 想傳達該結構給他留下的印象。"},{"en":"To convey an impression means to communicate a feeling, effect or response.","zh":"傳達印象指表達一種感覺、效果或反應。"},{"en":"A photograph of an empty classroom can convey an impression of silence and waiting.","zh":"空課室的照片可以傳達寂靜和等待的印象。"},{"en":"If a bridge feels enormous to the artist, the artwork may try to express that feeling.","zh":"如果橋樑令藝術家感到巨大，作品可能嘗試表達那種感覺。"},{"en":"The phrase describes communicating experience, not just copying appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述傳達經驗，而不只是複製外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"make an impression on","meaning":"給……留下印象","examples":[{"en":"Large construction projects made a powerful impression on the artist.","zh":"大型建築工程給這位藝術家留下強烈印象。"},{"en":"To make an impression on someone means to affect their thoughts or feelings strongly enough to be remembered.","zh":"“Make an impression on” 某人指強烈影響其思想或情感，令人記住。"},{"en":"A kind teacher can make a lasting impression on a nervous student.","zh":"仁慈老師可以給緊張學生留下持久印象。"},{"en":"If a construction site impresses an artist, it may become a subject of repeated work.","zh":"如果建築地盤令藝術家印象深刻，它可能成為反覆創作的題材。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a memorable emotional or mental effect.","zh":"這個短語描述令人記得的情感或心理效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the Wonder of Work","meaning":"「勞動的奇蹟」","examples":[{"en":"Pennell called his response to engineering the Wonder of Work.","zh":"Pennell 把自己對工程的反應稱為「勞動的奇蹟」。"},{"en":"The Wonder of Work means a feeling of awe at human labour, skill and construction.","zh":"「勞動的奇蹟」指對人類勞動、技術和建造產生的敬畏感。"},{"en":"A visitor may feel the wonder of work when seeing a huge bridge built piece by piece.","zh":"訪客看見巨大橋樑一塊一塊建成時，可能感到勞動的奇蹟。"},{"en":"If a project requires thousands of hands and years of effort, it can inspire wonder.","zh":"如果一個項目需要數千雙手和多年努力，就可以激發敬畏。"},{"en":"The phrase celebrates labour as something impressive and almost heroic.","zh":"這個短語把勞動讚頌為令人印象深刻、近乎英雄式的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a great construction project","meaning":"大型建築工程","examples":[{"en":"The artist felt a sense of wonder before a great construction project.","zh":"這位藝術家在大型建築工程前感到敬畏。"},{"en":"A great construction project is a large and impressive building or engineering work.","zh":"大型建築工程是大型而令人印象深刻的建築或工程作品。"},{"en":"A new bridge, dam or subway line can be a great construction project.","zh":"新橋、水壩或地鐵線都可以是大型建築工程。"},{"en":"If a project is great in scale and difficulty, it may inspire artists as well as engineers.","zh":"如果工程在規模和難度上巨大，它可能啟發藝術家和工程師。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses size, complexity and ambition.","zh":"這個短語強調規模、複雜性和抱負。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"see engineering as a process","meaning":"將工程視為一個過程","examples":[{"en":"Pennell saw engineering as a process rather than only a finished product.","zh":"Pennell 將工程視為一個過程，而不只是完成品。"},{"en":"To see engineering as a process means to value the planning, labour and construction stages, not just the result.","zh":"將工程視為一個過程，指重視規劃、勞動和建造階段，而不只是結果。"},{"en":"A teacher may see learning as a process rather than only a final exam score.","zh":"老師可能把學習視為一個過程，而不只是最終考試分數。"},{"en":"If engineering is seen as a process, unfinished bridges and scaffolding become meaningful.","zh":"如果工程被視為過程，未完成橋樑和棚架就變得有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase shifts attention from object to effort.","zh":"這個短語把注意力由物件轉向努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be memorialised in","meaning":"在……中得到紀念","examples":[{"en":"The process of construction is memorialised in the finished structure.","zh":"建造過程在完成的結構中得到紀念。"},{"en":"To be memorialised in something means to be preserved or remembered through it.","zh":"“Be memorialised in” 某物指透過它被保存或被記住。"},{"en":"A student’s effort may be memorialised in a graduation photo and certificate.","zh":"學生的努力可能在畢業照片和證書中得到紀念。"},{"en":"If construction work is memorialised in a bridge, the finished object remembers the labour behind it.","zh":"如果建造工作在橋樑中得到紀念，完成品就記住了背後勞動。"},{"en":"The phrase connects memory with a physical object or record.","zh":"這個短語把記憶與實物或記錄連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"completed dam","meaning":"已建成的水壩","examples":[{"en":"A completed dam preserves evidence of the work required to build it.","zh":"已建成的水壩保存了建造它所需工作的證據。"},{"en":"A completed dam is a finished barrier built to hold back or control water.","zh":"已建成的水壩是用來阻擋或控制水流的完成屏障。"},{"en":"Engineers may inspect a completed dam to check whether it can safely handle heavy rain.","zh":"工程師可能檢查已建成的水壩，以確認它能否安全應付大雨。"},{"en":"If a dam is completed, the visible structure hides years of planning and labour.","zh":"如果水壩已建成，可見結構就隱藏了多年規劃和勞動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the finished result of a major engineering process.","zh":"這個短語指重大工程過程的完成結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"skyscraper","meaning":"摩天大廈","examples":[{"en":"A skyscraper can be both a technical and artistic achievement.","zh":"摩天大廈可以同時是技術和藝術成就。"},{"en":"A skyscraper is a very tall building, usually found in a city.","zh":"摩天大廈是非常高的建築物，通常位於城市中。"},{"en":"Office workers may spend every day inside a skyscraper without noticing its engineering.","zh":"辦公室員工可能每天在摩天大廈內工作，卻沒有注意到其工程。"},{"en":"If a skyscraper has elegant form and strong structure, it can be admired as architecture.","zh":"如果摩天大廈有優雅形式和堅固結構，它就可以作為建築受到欣賞。"},{"en":"The word refers to height, urban life and modern construction.","zh":"這個詞指高度、城市生活和現代建造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"great achievement of engineering","meaning":"偉大的工程成就","examples":[{"en":"A major bridge is a great achievement of engineering.","zh":"重大橋樑是偉大的工程成就。"},{"en":"A great achievement of engineering is a technically difficult structure or system successfully created by engineers and workers.","zh":"偉大的工程成就是由工程師和工人成功創造的技術上困難的結構或系統。"},{"en":"A safe subway network can be a great achievement of engineering in a crowded city.","zh":"在擁擠城市中，安全地鐵網絡可以是偉大的工程成就。"},{"en":"If a project solves a hard problem at huge scale, it may deserve this description.","zh":"如果項目以巨大規模解決困難問題，就可能值得這樣描述。"},{"en":"The phrase praises technical success and human effort.","zh":"這個短語讚揚技術成功和人類努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in the aggregate","meaning":"從整體層面來看","examples":[{"en":"Pennell experienced the wonder of work in the aggregate.","zh":"Pennell 從整體層面感受到勞動的奇蹟。"},{"en":"In the aggregate means as a whole, considering all parts together.","zh":"“In the aggregate” 指作為整體，把所有部分一起考慮。"},{"en":"A school’s results may look strong in the aggregate even if a few students need extra help.","zh":"從整體層面來看，學校成績可能很強，即使少數學生需要額外幫助。"},{"en":"If Pennell saw work in the aggregate, he focused on the total project rather than one worker.","zh":"如果 Pennell 從整體看勞動，他就集中於整個工程，而不是個別工人。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an overall view rather than an individual one.","zh":"這個短語給出整體而非個人視角。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"focus on individuals","meaning":"聚焦個人","examples":[{"en":"Lewis Hine focused on the individuals engaged in construction work.","zh":"Lewis Hine 聚焦於參與建築工作的個人。"},{"en":"To focus on individuals means to give attention to particular people rather than a whole system or group.","zh":"聚焦個人指把注意力放在特定人物身上，而不是整個系統或群體。"},{"en":"A teacher may focus on individuals when planning support for students with different needs.","zh":"老師為不同需要學生規劃支援時，可能聚焦個人。"},{"en":"If a photographer focuses on workers, viewers see human courage behind the structure.","zh":"如果攝影師聚焦工人，觀者就看見結構背後的人類勇氣。"},{"en":"The phrase shifts attention from large projects to people.","zh":"這個短語把注意力由大型項目轉向人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"engage in the work","meaning":"參與工作","examples":[{"en":"Hine photographed the workers who engaged in dangerous construction work.","zh":"Hine 拍攝參與危險建築工作的工人。"},{"en":"To engage in the work means to take part in doing it actively.","zh":"“Engage in the work” 指積極參與做該工作。"},{"en":"Volunteers engage in community work when they clean parks or visit elderly residents.","zh":"義工清潔公園或探訪長者時，就是參與社區工作。"},{"en":"If workers engage in dangerous construction, their skill and courage become part of the project.","zh":"如果工人參與危險建築，其技術和勇氣就成為工程的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active participation in a task.","zh":"這個短語描述積極參與任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be trained as","meaning":"受訓成為……","examples":[{"en":"Lewis Hine was trained as a sociologist.","zh":"Lewis Hine 受訓成為社會學家。"},{"en":"To be trained as something means to receive education or preparation for that role.","zh":"“Be trained as” 某身分指接受教育或準備以擔任該角色。"},{"en":"A nurse is trained as a healthcare professional before working with patients.","zh":"護士在照顧病人前，受訓成為醫療專業人員。"},{"en":"If a photographer is trained as a sociologist, they may pay special attention to people and society.","zh":"如果攝影師受訓成為社會學家，他可能特別注意人和社會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes someone’s educational or professional background.","zh":"這個短語描述某人的教育或專業背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be best known as","meaning":"最廣為人知的身分是","examples":[{"en":"Hine became best known as a documentary photographer.","zh":"Hine 最廣為人知的身分是紀實攝影師。"},{"en":"To be best known as something means to be most famous in that role.","zh":"“Be best known as” 某身分指以該角色最有名。"},{"en":"A writer may be best known as a children’s novelist, even if they also wrote essays.","zh":"作家可能最以兒童小說家身分聞名，即使他也寫散文。"},{"en":"If Hine is best known as a documentary photographer, his public identity centres on social images.","zh":"如果 Hine 最以紀實攝影師聞名，他的公眾身份就集中於社會影像。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies someone’s main reputation.","zh":"這個短語指出某人的主要聲譽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"expose the exploitation of","meaning":"揭露對……的剝削","examples":[{"en":"His photographs exposed the exploitation of children.","zh":"他的照片揭露了對兒童的剝削。"},{"en":"To expose the exploitation of someone means to reveal that they are being used unfairly for work, profit or advantage.","zh":"“Expose the exploitation of” 某人指揭示他們在工作、利潤或利益上被不公平利用。"},{"en":"A news report may expose the exploitation of migrant workers in unsafe housing.","zh":"新聞報道可能揭露對住在不安全房屋中移民工人的剝削。"},{"en":"If photographs show children working in factories, they can make hidden injustice visible.","zh":"如果照片顯示兒童在工廠工作，它們就能令隱藏的不公義變得可見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes revealing unfair treatment.","zh":"這個短語描述揭示不公平對待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"document immigrants","meaning":"記錄移民","examples":[{"en":"Hine’s early work documented immigrants arriving in New York.","zh":"Hine 的早期作品記錄了抵達紐約的移民。"},{"en":"To document immigrants means to record their lives, arrival or experiences through photos, writing or film.","zh":"記錄移民指透過照片、文字或影片記錄他們的生活、抵達或經歷。"},{"en":"A community project may document immigrants’ stories so younger generations remember them.","zh":"社區項目可能記錄移民故事，讓年輕一代記住他們。"},{"en":"If artists document immigrants, they can show both hardship and hope.","zh":"如果藝術家記錄移民，就能同時展示艱難和希望。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preserving evidence of migrant experience.","zh":"這個短語描述保存移民經驗的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"pass through Ellis Island","meaning":"經過埃利斯島","examples":[{"en":"Many immigrants passed through Ellis Island.","zh":"許多移民經過埃利斯島。"},{"en":"To pass through Ellis Island means to enter the United States through the historic immigration station in New York Harbor.","zh":"經過埃利斯島指透過紐約港歷史性移民站進入美國。"},{"en":"A family history may begin with a grandparent who passed through Ellis Island.","zh":"一段家族史可能始於一位曾經過埃利斯島的祖父母。"},{"en":"If immigrants passed through this station, their arrival could be officially recorded.","zh":"如果移民經過這個移民站，他們的抵達就可能被官方記錄。"},{"en":"The phrase connects migration with a specific historical gateway.","zh":"這個短語把移民與特定歷史入口連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"living conditions","meaning":"生活環境","examples":[{"en":"Hine documented the living conditions of poor immigrant families.","zh":"Hine 記錄了貧窮移民家庭的生活環境。"},{"en":"Living conditions are the circumstances in which people live, including housing, safety, space and cleanliness.","zh":"生活環境是人們居住的條件，包括住房、安全、空間和清潔程度。"},{"en":"A social worker may visit a flat to check a family’s living conditions.","zh":"社工可能探訪單位，以檢查家庭生活環境。"},{"en":"If living conditions are crowded and unsafe, health and education may suffer.","zh":"如果生活環境擁擠而不安全，健康和教育都可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on daily environment and quality of life.","zh":"這個短語強調日常環境和生活質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"New York tenements","meaning":"紐約廉租住宅","examples":[{"en":"Many immigrant families lived in crowded New York tenements.","zh":"許多移民家庭住在擁擠的紐約廉租住宅中。"},{"en":"New York tenements were low-cost apartment buildings that often housed poor families in crowded conditions.","zh":"紐約廉租住宅是低成本公寓樓，常讓貧窮家庭在擁擠環境中居住。"},{"en":"A photograph of New York tenements may show narrow rooms and many people sharing space.","zh":"紐約廉租住宅的照片可能顯示狹窄房間和許多人共用空間。"},{"en":"If families lived in crowded tenements, their daily life could be difficult and unhealthy.","zh":"如果家庭住在擁擠廉租住宅中，日常生活可能困難且不健康。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to urban housing associated with poverty and immigration.","zh":"這個短語指與貧窮和移民相關的城市住房。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"sweatshops","meaning":"血汗工場","examples":[{"en":"Hine photographed the sweatshops where immigrants worked.","zh":"Hine 拍攝移民工作的血汗工場。"},{"en":"Sweatshops are workplaces where people work long hours for low pay, often in poor conditions.","zh":"血汗工場是人們長時間低薪工作、通常環境惡劣的工作場所。"},{"en":"A clothing factory may be called a sweatshop if workers are underpaid and unsafe.","zh":"如果製衣工廠工人低薪且不安全，它可能被稱為血汗工場。"},{"en":"If sweatshops are exposed, the public may demand labour reform.","zh":"如果血汗工場被揭露，公眾可能要求勞工改革。"},{"en":"The word strongly suggests exploitation and harsh work.","zh":"這個詞強烈暗示剝削和艱苦工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be given the opportunity to","meaning":"獲得機會去……","examples":[{"en":"Hine was given the opportunity to record the construction project.","zh":"Hine 獲得機會去記錄這個建築工程。"},{"en":"To be given the opportunity to do something means to be allowed or invited to do it.","zh":"“Be given the opportunity to” 做某事指被允許或邀請去做。"},{"en":"A student may be given the opportunity to present their project at a school assembly.","zh":"學生可能獲得機會在學校早會上介紹自己的項目。"},{"en":"If an artist is given access to a construction site, they can record moments others never see.","zh":"如果藝術家獲准進入建築地盤，就能記錄其他人看不到的時刻。"},{"en":"The phrase describes receiving a chance to act.","zh":"這個短語描述得到行動機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"record the construction of","meaning":"記錄……的建造過程","examples":[{"en":"He recorded the construction of the Empire State Building.","zh":"他記錄了帝國大廈的建造過程。"},{"en":"To record the construction of something means to document how it was built.","zh":"“Record the construction of” 某物指記錄它如何被建成。"},{"en":"A film crew may record the construction of a new hospital from foundation to opening day.","zh":"攝製隊可能記錄新醫院從地基到開幕日的建造過程。"},{"en":"If construction is recorded, future viewers can see the labour behind the finished building.","zh":"如果建造過程被記錄，未來觀眾就能看見完成建築背後的勞動。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on preserving the building process.","zh":"這個短語強調保存建造過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the Empire State Building","meaning":"帝國大廈","examples":[{"en":"Hine photographed workers constructing the Empire State Building.","zh":"Hine 拍攝建造帝國大廈的工人。"},{"en":"The Empire State Building is a famous skyscraper in New York.","zh":"帝國大廈是紐約著名摩天大廈。"},{"en":"Tourists visit the Empire State Building to see the city from high above.","zh":"遊客參觀帝國大廈，從高處觀看城市。"},{"en":"If photographs show its construction, viewers can appreciate both the building and the workers.","zh":"如果照片展示其建造過程，觀眾就能同時欣賞建築和工人。"},{"en":"The phrase names an iconic modern engineering and architectural structure.","zh":"這個短語指出一座標誌性的現代工程和建築結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"result in striking photographs","meaning":"產生令人印象深刻的照片","examples":[{"en":"The project resulted in striking photographs of construction workers.","zh":"這個項目產生了建築工人令人印象深刻的照片。"},{"en":"To result in striking photographs means to produce images that are visually powerful and memorable.","zh":"“Result in striking photographs” 指產生視覺上有力且令人難忘的影像。"},{"en":"A sports competition may result in striking photographs of effort, joy and defeat.","zh":"體育比賽可能產生努力、喜悅和失敗的令人印象深刻照片。"},{"en":"If a photographer captures workers high above a city, the images can feel dramatic and unforgettable.","zh":"如果攝影師拍到城市高空中的工人，影像可以感覺富戲劇性且難忘。"},{"en":"The phrase links an activity with impressive visual results.","zh":"這個短語把活動與強烈視覺成果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"familiar images","meaning":"為人熟悉的影像","examples":[{"en":"Hine’s photographs have become familiar images of industrial courage.","zh":"Hine 的照片已成為工業勇氣中為人熟悉的影像。"},{"en":"Familiar images are pictures that many people recognise or have seen before.","zh":"為人熟悉的影像，是許多人認得或曾經看過的圖片。"},{"en":"The photo of students raising hands in class is a familiar image of school life.","zh":"學生在課堂舉手的照片，是學校生活中為人熟悉的影像。"},{"en":"If photographs become familiar images, they shape how later generations imagine an event.","zh":"如果照片成為熟悉影像，它們就塑造後代理解某事件的方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes widely recognised visual memory.","zh":"這個短語描述廣為認識的視覺記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"daring and insouciance","meaning":"大膽與從容不迫","examples":[{"en":"The photographs convey both daring and insouciance.","zh":"這些照片傳達大膽與從容不迫。"},{"en":"Daring and insouciance mean bold courage together with relaxed calmness.","zh":"大膽與從容不迫指勇敢膽識加上放鬆冷靜。"},{"en":"A performer walking onto stage with a smile may show daring and insouciance.","zh":"表演者微笑走上舞台時，可能展現大膽與從容不迫。"},{"en":"If workers sit high above the city without visible fear, the image suggests both risk and ease.","zh":"如果工人坐在城市高空卻看不出害怕，影像就暗示風險與輕鬆並存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes brave confidence that looks almost casual.","zh":"這個短語描述看似隨意的勇敢自信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"put one’s life at risk","meaning":"冒生命危險","examples":[{"en":"Hine put his own life at risk to photograph the workers.","zh":"Hine 冒着自己的生命危險去拍攝工人。"},{"en":"To put one’s life at risk means to do something that could cause serious injury or death.","zh":"冒生命危險指做可能造成嚴重受傷或死亡的事情。"},{"en":"Firefighters put their lives at risk when entering a burning building.","zh":"消防員進入燃燒建築時，就是冒生命危險。"},{"en":"If a photographer climbs dangerous heights, the act of taking the picture becomes risky too.","zh":"如果攝影師爬上危險高處，拍照行為本身也變得危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extreme personal danger.","zh":"這個短語描述極端個人危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"capture workers","meaning":"拍攝工人","examples":[{"en":"He risked his safety to capture workers high above the city.","zh":"他冒着安全風險，拍攝城市高空中的工人。"},{"en":"To capture workers means to photograph or record workers in a particular moment or situation.","zh":"拍攝工人指在特定時刻或情況中拍下或記錄工人。"},{"en":"A documentary maker may capture workers preparing food before a restaurant opens.","zh":"紀錄片製作者可能拍攝餐廳開門前準備食物的工人。"},{"en":"If a camera captures workers at dangerous heights, viewers see labour from a new angle.","zh":"如果鏡頭拍攝危險高處的工人，觀眾就從新角度看見勞動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visually recording people at work.","zh":"這個短語描述以視覺方式記錄工作中的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be suspended on cables","meaning":"懸吊在纜索上","examples":[{"en":"Workers were suspended on cables hundreds of feet in the air.","zh":"工人懸吊在數百呎高空的纜索上。"},{"en":"To be suspended on cables means to hang or be supported by strong ropes or metal lines.","zh":"“Be suspended on cables” 指被強繩或金屬線懸掛或支撐。"},{"en":"Window cleaners may be suspended on cables outside tall office buildings.","zh":"清潔窗戶的工人可能懸吊在高層辦公樓外的纜索上。"},{"en":"If workers are suspended high above ground, safety equipment becomes extremely important.","zh":"如果工人懸吊在高空，安全設備就變得極其重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a risky raised position.","zh":"這個短語描述危險的高處位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"hundreds of feet in the air","meaning":"在數百呎高空","examples":[{"en":"The workers performed dangerous tasks hundreds of feet in the air.","zh":"工人在數百呎高空執行危險任務。"},{"en":"Hundreds of feet in the air means very high above the ground.","zh":"在數百呎高空指離地面非常高。"},{"en":"A crane operator may work hundreds of feet in the air on a tall construction site.","zh":"起重機操作員可能在高樓地盤數百呎高空工作。"},{"en":"If people work at such heights, one mistake can be deadly.","zh":"如果人們在這種高度工作，一個錯誤可能致命。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses extreme height and danger.","zh":"這個短語強調極高高度和危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"high girder","meaning":"高處鋼樑","examples":[{"en":"Several workers sat on a high girder to eat lunch.","zh":"幾名工人坐在高處鋼樑上吃午餐。"},{"en":"A high girder is a large horizontal metal beam located high above the ground.","zh":"高處鋼樑是位於離地很高位置的大型水平金屬樑。"},{"en":"Construction workers may stand on a high girder while building a skyscraper frame.","zh":"建築工人搭建摩天大廈框架時，可能站在高處鋼樑上。"},{"en":"If workers sit on a high girder without protection, the scene appears both casual and dangerous.","zh":"如果工人沒有保護地坐在高處鋼樑上，場景看起來既隨意又危險。"},{"en":"The phrase names a structural element at height.","zh":"這個短語指出高處的結構部件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"one of the most striking features","meaning":"最引人注目的特點之一","examples":[{"en":"The absence of safety equipment is one of the most striking features of the photographs.","zh":"缺乏安全設備是這些照片最引人注目的特點之一。"},{"en":"One of the most striking features means one of the most noticeable or memorable parts.","zh":"最引人注目的特點之一，指最明顯或最令人記得的部分之一。"},{"en":"The quietness of the empty school corridor is one of the most striking features of the photo.","zh":"空校園走廊的寧靜，是照片最引人注目的特點之一。"},{"en":"If a feature immediately catches the viewer’s attention, it helps define the image.","zh":"如果一個特點立即吸引觀者注意，它就有助定義影像。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights an especially powerful detail.","zh":"這個短語突出尤其有力的細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the absence of","meaning":"缺乏……","examples":[{"en":"The photographs reveal the absence of modern safety equipment.","zh":"這些照片揭示缺乏現代安全設備。"},{"en":"The absence of something means that it is missing or not present.","zh":"缺乏某物指它不存在或沒有出現。"},{"en":"The absence of clear instructions can make a simple task confusing.","zh":"缺乏清楚指示可以令簡單任務變得混亂。"},{"en":"If the absence of safety gear is obvious, viewers may feel the workers’ danger more strongly.","zh":"如果安全裝備缺乏情況很明顯，觀者可能更強烈感受到工人的危險。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on what is not there.","zh":"這個短語強調不存在的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"safety lines","meaning":"安全繩","examples":[{"en":"The workers did not use safety lines.","zh":"工人沒有使用安全繩。"},{"en":"Safety lines are ropes or cables used to prevent workers from falling.","zh":"安全繩是用來防止工人墜落的繩索或纜索。"},{"en":"Window cleaners on tall buildings usually attach themselves to safety lines.","zh":"高樓外的窗戶清潔工通常把自己扣在安全繩上。"},{"en":"If safety lines are missing, work at height becomes far more dangerous.","zh":"如果缺乏安全繩，高空工作就危險得多。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to protective equipment for risky work.","zh":"這個短語指危險工作中的保護設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"hard hats","meaning":"安全帽","examples":[{"en":"The construction workers were not wearing hard hats.","zh":"建築工人沒有戴安全帽。"},{"en":"Hard hats are strong protective helmets worn on construction sites.","zh":"安全帽是在建築地盤佩戴的堅固保護頭盔。"},{"en":"Visitors to a building site may need hard hats to protect their heads from falling objects.","zh":"到訪建築地盤的人可能需要戴安全帽，以保護頭部免受墜物傷害。"},{"en":"If workers lack hard hats, even small falling tools can cause serious injury.","zh":"如果工人沒有安全帽，即使小工具掉下也可能造成嚴重受傷。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to basic safety equipment.","zh":"這個短語指基本安全設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"evoke a sense of","meaning":"喚起……的感覺","examples":[{"en":"The photographs evoke a sense of the Wonder of Work.","zh":"這些照片喚起「勞動的奇蹟」的感覺。"},{"en":"To evoke a sense of something means to create or bring out a particular feeling.","zh":"“Evoke a sense of” 某事指創造或喚起某種特定感覺。"},{"en":"Old school photos can evoke a sense of childhood and friendship.","zh":"舊校園照片可以喚起童年和友誼的感覺。"},{"en":"If images show workers high above the city, they may evoke awe and admiration.","zh":"如果影像展示城市高空中的工人，它們可能喚起敬畏和欽佩。"},{"en":"The phrase describes emotional response created by art or memory.","zh":"這個短語描述藝術或記憶所創造的情感反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"inspire admiration for","meaning":"激起對……的欽佩","examples":[{"en":"The images inspire admiration for the workers’ bravery and skill.","zh":"這些影像激起人們對工人勇氣與技術的欽佩。"},{"en":"To inspire admiration for someone means to make people respect and appreciate them.","zh":"“Inspire admiration for” 某人指令人尊重和欣賞他們。"},{"en":"A nurse’s calm work during an emergency can inspire admiration from patients’ families.","zh":"護士在緊急情況中的冷靜工作，可以激起病人家屬的欽佩。"},{"en":"If photographs show danger and competence, viewers may admire the workers behind the building.","zh":"如果照片展示危險和能力，觀者可能欽佩建築背後的工人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes respect created by seeing excellence or courage.","zh":"這個短語描述由看見卓越或勇氣而產生的尊重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"bravery and skill","meaning":"勇氣與技術","examples":[{"en":"Great engineering projects depend on workers’ bravery and skill.","zh":"偉大的工程項目依賴工人的勇氣與技術。"},{"en":"Bravery and skill mean courage together with practical ability.","zh":"勇氣與技術指膽量加上實際能力。"},{"en":"Firefighters need bravery and skill when entering a smoke-filled building.","zh":"消防員進入充滿煙霧的建築時，需要勇氣與技術。"},{"en":"If construction workers face height, wind and heavy steel, both courage and technique are necessary.","zh":"如果建築工人面對高空、強風和沉重鋼材，勇氣和技巧都必不可少。"},{"en":"The phrase praises emotional strength and professional competence.","zh":"這個短語讚揚情感力量和專業能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"bring a project to completion","meaning":"令工程竣工","examples":[{"en":"Skilled workers bring a great engineering project to completion.","zh":"熟練工人令偉大工程竣工。"},{"en":"To bring a project to completion means to finish it successfully after planning and work.","zh":"“Bring a project to completion” 指在規劃和工作後成功完成項目。"},{"en":"A student team brings a science project to completion when the model works and the report is submitted.","zh":"當模型運作而報告提交後，學生小組就完成了科學項目。"},{"en":"If workers coordinate well, a difficult construction project can finally be completed safely.","zh":"如果工人協調良好，困難建築工程最終可以安全竣工。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises the effort needed to reach the finished stage.","zh":"這個短語強調到達完成階段所需的努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"which paragraph contains","meaning":"哪一段包含……","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which paragraph contains each piece of information.","zh":"學生識別哪一段包含每項資料。"},{"en":"Which paragraph contains means which section of the passage includes the stated detail.","zh":"“Which paragraph contains” 指文章哪一部分包括所述細節。"},{"en":"In reading tasks, students scan for names, dates and key ideas to find the right paragraph.","zh":"在閱讀題中，學生掃讀姓名、日期和關鍵意思，以找到正確段落。"},{"en":"If one paragraph contains more than one answer, the same letter may be used again.","zh":"如果一段包含超過一個答案，同一字母可能再次使用。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in paragraph-information matching questions.","zh":"這個短語用於段落資料配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the following information","meaning":"以下資料","examples":[{"en":"The task asks students to locate the following information.","zh":"題目要求學生找出以下資料的位置。"},{"en":"The following information means the details listed after the instruction.","zh":"以下資料指指示後列出的細節。"},{"en":"Students should read the following information carefully before scanning the passage.","zh":"學生在掃讀文章前，應仔細閱讀以下資料。"},{"en":"If the information is paraphrased, students must search for meaning, not only exact words.","zh":"如果資料被改寫，學生必須尋找意思，而不只是完全相同的字。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the items that come next.","zh":"這個短語指接下來列出的項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the first connection between","meaning":"……之間最早的聯繫","examples":[{"en":"The question asks where the first connection between art and engineering appears.","zh":"題目問藝術與工程之間最早的聯繫出現在哪裡。"},{"en":"The first connection between two things means the earliest point where they are linked.","zh":"兩件事之間最早的聯繫，指它們最早被連接起來的地方。"},{"en":"A history lesson may ask students to find the first connection between trade and city growth.","zh":"歷史課可能要求學生找出貿易與城市發展之間最早的聯繫。"},{"en":"If a passage traces art and engineering, the first connection may appear in an early example.","zh":"如果文章追溯藝術和工程，最早聯繫可能出現在早期例子中。"},{"en":"The phrase directs students to identify an initial link.","zh":"這個短語引導學生識別初始連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"bring objects and structures together","meaning":"將物件與建築結合","examples":[{"en":"An artwork may bring small objects and built structures together.","zh":"藝術作品可能將小物件與人造建築結合。"},{"en":"To bring objects and structures together means to show them in one scene so they relate visually or meaningfully.","zh":"將物件與建築結合，指把它們展示在同一場景中，使其在視覺或意義上相關。"},{"en":"A photo may bring school desks and a modern building together to show daily learning space.","zh":"照片可能把學校桌椅和現代建築結合，以展示日常學習空間。"},{"en":"If small objects appear beside large structures, the contrast can show scale and human use.","zh":"如果小物件出現在大型結構旁邊，對比可以顯示規模和人的使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes combining different visual elements.","zh":"這個短語描述結合不同視覺元素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"small artistic objects","meaning":"小型藝術物件","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to small artistic objects shown beside larger structures.","zh":"題目指與較大型結構並列展示的小型藝術物件。"},{"en":"Small artistic objects are little items made or arranged for visual or cultural beauty.","zh":"小型藝術物件是為視覺或文化美感而製作或安排的小物品。"},{"en":"A museum display may place small artistic objects beside photographs of buildings.","zh":"博物館展示可能把小型藝術物件放在建築照片旁。"},{"en":"If small objects appear near huge structures, viewers can compare detail and scale.","zh":"如果小物件出現在巨大結構附近，觀者可以比較細節和規模。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts intimate art objects with large engineering works.","zh":"這個短語把親近的小藝術品與大型工程作品作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"built structures","meaning":"人造建築物","examples":[{"en":"Bridges, factories and skyscrapers are examples of built structures.","zh":"橋樑、工廠和摩天大廈都是人造建築物的例子。"},{"en":"Built structures are human-made constructions such as buildings, bridges and towers.","zh":"人造建築物是由人建造的結構，例如建築物、橋樑和塔。"},{"en":"A city’s built structures shape how people move, work and gather.","zh":"城市的人造建築物塑造人們如何移動、工作和聚集。"},{"en":"If artists study built structures, they can explore line, scale and public meaning.","zh":"如果藝術家研究人造建築物，就能探索線條、規模和公共意義。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to constructed objects rather than natural forms.","zh":"這個短語指建造出來的物件，而不是自然形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"working conditions","meaning":"工作環境","examples":[{"en":"Hine recorded the working conditions of industrial labourers.","zh":"Hine 記錄了工業勞工的工作環境。"},{"en":"Working conditions are the environment, safety, hours and treatment people experience at work.","zh":"工作環境是人們在工作中經歷的環境、安全、工時和待遇。"},{"en":"A factory with poor air, long hours and low pay has bad working conditions.","zh":"空氣差、工時長、薪酬低的工廠有惡劣工作環境。"},{"en":"If working conditions are dangerous, photographs can help expose the problem.","zh":"如果工作環境危險，照片可以幫助揭露問題。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on what daily work is actually like.","zh":"這個短語強調日常工作實際情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"record something as an exciting subject","meaning":"將……記錄為令人興奮的題材","examples":[{"en":"Sheeler recorded the factory as an exciting artistic subject.","zh":"Sheeler 將工廠記錄為令人興奮的藝術題材。"},{"en":"To record something as an exciting subject means to present it as worthy of creative attention.","zh":"將某物記錄為令人興奮的題材，指把它呈現為值得創意關注。"},{"en":"A photographer may record a night market as an exciting subject full of light and movement.","zh":"攝影師可能把夜市記錄為充滿光線和動感的令人興奮題材。"},{"en":"If a factory is recorded this way, viewers are invited to see energy rather than dull machinery.","zh":"如果工廠以這種方式被記錄，觀眾就被邀請看見能量，而不是沉悶機械。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how artistic framing can change perception.","zh":"這個短語顯示藝術框架如何改變感知。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"depictions of unfinished projects","meaning":"對未完成工程的描繪","examples":[{"en":"Pennell produced depictions of unfinished engineering projects.","zh":"Pennell 創作了對未完成工程項目的描繪。"},{"en":"Depictions of unfinished projects are images or descriptions showing work before it is complete.","zh":"對未完成工程的描繪，是展示工作尚未完成時的影像或描述。"},{"en":"A school magazine may include depictions of an unfinished library during construction.","zh":"學校雜誌可能刊登正在興建中的未完成圖書館描繪。"},{"en":"If unfinished projects are depicted, viewers can see process, effort and risk.","zh":"如果未完成工程被描繪，觀者就能看見過程、努力和風險。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on construction in progress rather than final results.","zh":"這個短語強調進行中的建造，而不是最終結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"iconic symbols","meaning":"標誌性象徵","examples":[{"en":"Some bridges became iconic symbols of their cities.","zh":"有些橋樑成為其城市的標誌性象徵。"},{"en":"Iconic symbols are widely recognised images or objects that represent a place, idea or group.","zh":"標誌性象徵是廣為人知並代表某地方、想法或群體的形象或物件。"},{"en":"A skyline tower can become an iconic symbol of a modern city.","zh":"天際線塔樓可以成為現代城市的標誌性象徵。"},{"en":"If a bridge appears on postcards and logos, it may become part of local identity.","zh":"如果橋樑出現在明信片和標誌上，它可能成為本地身份的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes objects that stand for something larger than themselves.","zh":"這個短語描述代表比自身更大意義的物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"match the people with","meaning":"將人物與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match the listed people with their opinions or deeds.","zh":"學生將列出的人物與其觀點或行動配對。"},{"en":"To match the people with something means to connect each person to the correct statement, action or idea.","zh":"“Match the people with” 某事指把每個人物連接到正確陳述、行動或想法。"},{"en":"In a history quiz, students may match inventors with their inventions.","zh":"在歷史小測中，學生可能把發明家與其發明配對。"},{"en":"If names appear in different paragraphs, students should track what each person said or did.","zh":"如果姓名出現在不同段落，學生應追蹤每個人說過或做過甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common reading matching task.","zh":"這個短語描述常見閱讀配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"opinions or deeds","meaning":"觀點或行動","examples":[{"en":"The matching task includes both opinions and deeds.","zh":"這道配對題包括觀點或行動。"},{"en":"Opinions or deeds means what people think or say, and what they actually do.","zh":"觀點或行動指人們想甚麼或說甚麼，以及實際做甚麼。"},{"en":"A biography may describe a leader’s opinions or deeds to show their character.","zh":"傳記可能描述領袖的觀點或行動，以顯示其性格。"},{"en":"If a question asks for opinions and deeds, students must distinguish words from actions.","zh":"如果題目問觀點和行動，學生必須區分說話與行為。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both beliefs and behaviour.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋信念和行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"comment that","meaning":"評論說","examples":[{"en":"Pennell commented that engineers were great architects.","zh":"Pennell 評論說工程師是偉大的建築師。"},{"en":"To comment that something is true means to state an opinion or observation about it.","zh":"“Comment that” 某事為真指表達對它的意見或觀察。"},{"en":"A teacher may comment that a student’s essay has strong examples but weak structure.","zh":"老師可能評論說學生文章例子強，但結構弱。"},{"en":"If Pennell comments on engineers, he is expressing a judgement about their creative role.","zh":"如果 Pennell 評論工程師，他就是表達對其創造角色的判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces someone’s stated view.","zh":"這個短語引出某人表達的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"engineering constructions","meaning":"工程建築","examples":[{"en":"Pennell believed that engineering constructions could be beautiful.","zh":"Pennell 相信工程建築可以是美麗的。"},{"en":"Engineering constructions are structures built through engineering skill, such as bridges, dams and towers.","zh":"工程建築是透過工程技術建成的結構，例如橋樑、水壩和塔。"},{"en":"A city may protect old engineering constructions because they show earlier technical achievement.","zh":"城市可能保護舊工程建築，因為它們顯示早期技術成就。"},{"en":"If engineering constructions are visually powerful, artists may treat them as subjects.","zh":"如果工程建築在視覺上有力，藝術家可能把它們視為題材。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to built works created through engineering.","zh":"這個短語指透過工程創造的建成作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"make a romantic depiction","meaning":"作出浪漫化的描繪","examples":[{"en":"Michael Rooker made a romantic depiction of Iron Bridge.","zh":"Michael Rooker 對 Iron Bridge 作出浪漫化的描繪。"},{"en":"To make a romantic depiction means to present something in an idealised, beautiful or emotionally softened way.","zh":"作出浪漫化的描繪，指以理想化、美化或情感柔化的方式呈現某物。"},{"en":"A painter may make a romantic depiction of village life by leaving out poverty and hard labour.","zh":"畫家可能透過省略貧窮和艱苦勞動，對鄉村生活作出浪漫化描繪。"},{"en":"If an iron bridge is shown in a peaceful landscape, industry may seem gentle and poetic.","zh":"如果鐵橋被放在平和風景中，工業可能看起來溫和而詩意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes artistic presentation that beautifies the subject.","zh":"這個短語描述把題材美化的藝術呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"an old bridge","meaning":"古老橋樑","examples":[{"en":"The artist presented the old bridge within a peaceful landscape.","zh":"藝術家把古老橋樑呈現在平和景觀之中。"},{"en":"An old bridge is a bridge built long ago, often carrying historical or cultural meaning.","zh":"古老橋樑是很久以前建成、通常帶有歷史或文化意義的橋。"},{"en":"A village may keep an old bridge because residents see it as part of local memory.","zh":"村莊可能保留古老橋樑，因為居民把它視為本地記憶的一部分。"},{"en":"If an old bridge is still standing, it connects present life with past engineering.","zh":"如果古老橋樑仍然屹立，它就把當下生活與過去工程連接起來。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to age, history and continuity.","zh":"這個短語指年代、歷史和延續性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"artworks demonstrating courage","meaning":"展示勇氣的藝術作品","examples":[{"en":"Hine produced artworks demonstrating the courage of construction workers.","zh":"Hine 創作了展示建築工人勇氣的藝術作品。"},{"en":"Artworks demonstrating courage are images or works that show bravery in action.","zh":"展示勇氣的藝術作品，是顯示行動中勇敢的影像或作品。"},{"en":"A photograph of nurses during a crisis can be an artwork demonstrating courage.","zh":"危機中護士的照片可以是展示勇氣的藝術作品。"},{"en":"If workers are shown high above the city, the artwork makes their danger visible.","zh":"如果工人被呈現在城市高空中，作品就令其危險變得可見。"},{"en":"The phrase connects artistic representation with human bravery.","zh":"這個短語把藝術呈現與人類勇氣連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"workers on site","meaning":"工地上的工人","examples":[{"en":"The photographs show workers on site without modern safety equipment.","zh":"這些照片顯示工地上的工人沒有現代安全設備。"},{"en":"Workers on site are people physically present at a workplace or construction location.","zh":"工地上的工人，是實際身處工作場所或建築地點的人。"},{"en":"Workers on site may need helmets, boots and safety briefings before beginning a task.","zh":"工地上的工人在開始任務前，可能需要頭盔、靴和安全簡報。"},{"en":"If workers are shown on site, viewers see the real conditions of labour.","zh":"如果工人被呈現在工地上，觀者就看見真實勞動環境。"},{"en":"The phrase distinguishes actual workplace presence from office planning.","zh":"這個短語把實際工作現場與辦公室規劃區分開來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"produce portraits involving","meaning":"創作包含……的肖像畫","examples":[{"en":"Schussele produced portraits involving engineers and inventors.","zh":"Schussele 創作包含工程師與發明家的肖像畫。"},{"en":"To produce portraits involving certain people means to create paintings or images that include them.","zh":"創作包含某些人的肖像畫，指創造包括他們的畫作或影像。"},{"en":"A school artist may produce portraits involving teachers, cleaners and students together.","zh":"學校藝術家可能創作包含老師、清潔工和學生的肖像畫。"},{"en":"If portraits include engineers and inventors, technical figures are treated as worthy of honour.","zh":"如果肖像畫包括工程師和發明家，技術人物就被視為值得尊敬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating portrait art with particular subjects.","zh":"這個短語描述以特定人物為題材創作肖像藝術。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"historical figures","meaning":"歷史人物","examples":[{"en":"The artist painted inventors and important historical figures.","zh":"這位藝術家畫發明家和重要歷史人物。"},{"en":"Historical figures are people from the past who are important in history.","zh":"歷史人物是過去在歷史上重要的人。"},{"en":"Students may study historical figures such as leaders, scientists and reformers.","zh":"學生可能研究領袖、科學家和改革者等歷史人物。"},{"en":"If inventors are painted like historical figures, their work is presented as nationally important.","zh":"如果發明家像歷史人物一樣被畫下，其工作就被呈現為具有國家重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people remembered for their role in past events.","zh":"這個短語指因其在過去事件中的角色而被記住的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"ambitious titles","meaning":"氣勢宏大的作品名稱","examples":[{"en":"Sheeler gave his factory paintings ambitious titles.","zh":"Sheeler 給他的工廠畫作氣勢宏大的作品名稱。"},{"en":"Ambitious titles are names that suggest large meaning, seriousness or high artistic purpose.","zh":"氣勢宏大的作品名稱，是暗示重大意義、嚴肅性或高藝術目的的名稱。"},{"en":"A student painting called “The Future of the City” has a more ambitious title than “My Street.”","zh":"一幅學生畫作若名為《城市的未來》，就比《我的街道》有更宏大的標題。"},{"en":"If a factory painting receives a grand title, viewers may interpret it as more than a simple factory scene.","zh":"如果工廠畫作獲得宏大標題，觀者可能把它詮釋為不只是簡單工廠場景。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how titles can raise the status of a work.","zh":"這個短語顯示標題如何提升作品地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的詞語完成摘要。"},{"en":"Complete the summary means fill in missing words in a shortened version of the passage.","zh":"完成摘要指填寫文章簡短版本中的缺漏詞語。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole summary first so they understand its logic.","zh":"學生應先閱讀整段摘要，理解其邏輯。"},{"en":"If the summary follows the passage order, scanning becomes easier.","zh":"如果摘要跟隨文章次序，掃讀就會較容易。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個詞","examples":[{"en":"Each answer must contain no more than three words.","zh":"每個答案必須包含不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must have three words or fewer.","zh":"“No more than three words” 指答案必須有三個詞或更少。"},{"en":"If the answer is “the River Severn,” it fits the three-word limit.","zh":"如果答案是 “the River Severn”，它符合三詞限制。"},{"en":"Extra words can make a correct idea wrong in exam marking.","zh":"額外詞語可以令正確意思在考試評分中變錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word limit for answers.","zh":"這個短語為答案給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"artistic appeal","meaning":"藝術吸引力","examples":[{"en":"Artists began to recognise the artistic appeal of engineering.","zh":"藝術家開始認識工程的藝術吸引力。"},{"en":"Artistic appeal is the visual or emotional attractiveness that makes something interesting to artists.","zh":"藝術吸引力是令某物對藝術家有趣的視覺或情感吸引力。"},{"en":"A crowded market may have artistic appeal because of colour, movement and human stories.","zh":"擁擠街市可能因顏色、流動和人的故事而具有藝術吸引力。"},{"en":"If engineering has artistic appeal, artists may see beauty in bridges and factories.","zh":"如果工程有藝術吸引力，藝術家可能在橋樑和工廠中看見美。"},{"en":"The phrase describes why something attracts artistic attention.","zh":"這個短語描述某物為何吸引藝術關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a good example of","meaning":"……的一個好例子","examples":[{"en":"Iron Bridge is a good example of art and engineering coming together.","zh":"Iron Bridge 是藝術與工程結合的一個好例子。"},{"en":"A good example of something is a clear case that helps explain a wider idea.","zh":"某事的一個好例子，是幫助解釋更大想法的清楚案例。"},{"en":"A school garden is a good example of learning outside the classroom.","zh":"學校花園是課室外學習的一個好例子。"},{"en":"If Iron Bridge combines beauty and function, it explains the link between art and engineering.","zh":"如果 Iron Bridge 結合美感和功能，它就解釋了藝術與工程之間的連繫。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence that supports a point.","zh":"這個短語引出支持觀點的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be built by","meaning":"由……建造","examples":[{"en":"The bridge was built by an innovative ironmaster and engineer.","zh":"這座橋由一位創新的鐵匠大師兼工程師建造。"},{"en":"To be built by someone means that person or group constructed it.","zh":"“Be built by” 某人指由該人或群體建造。"},{"en":"The new library was built by a local construction company.","zh":"新圖書館由本地建築公司建造。"},{"en":"If a bridge is built by an innovative engineer, its design may break with tradition.","zh":"如果橋樑由創新工程師建造，其設計可能突破傳統。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the maker or builder of a structure.","zh":"這個短語指出結構的建造者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be constructed using","meaning":"使用……建造","examples":[{"en":"Earlier bridges were constructed using stone and timber.","zh":"早期橋樑使用石材和木材建造。"},{"en":"To be constructed using something means to be built with those materials or methods.","zh":"“Be constructed using” 某物指使用那些材料或方法建造。"},{"en":"A school stage may be constructed using wood, metal frames and lights.","zh":"學校舞台可能使用木材、金屬框架和燈光建造。"},{"en":"If a bridge is constructed using iron instead of stone, its design possibilities change.","zh":"如果橋樑使用鐵而不是石建造，其設計可能性就改變。"},{"en":"The phrase connects construction with materials.","zh":"這個短語把建造與材料連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"highly significant","meaning":"極為重要","examples":[{"en":"Iron Bridge was highly significant during the Industrial Revolution.","zh":"Iron Bridge 在工業革命期間極為重要。"},{"en":"Highly significant means very important because of its meaning, effect or influence.","zh":"極為重要指因其意義、效果或影響而非常重要。"},{"en":"A small law change can be highly significant if it affects many families.","zh":"如果一項小法律改變影響許多家庭，它可以極為重要。"},{"en":"If Iron Bridge proved iron could be used structurally, its importance went beyond one river crossing.","zh":"如果 Iron Bridge 證明鐵可以用於結構，其重要性就超越一次渡河。"},{"en":"The phrase marks something as historically or practically important.","zh":"這個短語把某事標示為在歷史或實際上重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"stand for centuries","meaning":"屹立數百年","examples":[{"en":"The historic bridge has stood for centuries.","zh":"這座歷史橋樑已屹立數百年。"},{"en":"To stand for centuries means to remain standing for hundreds of years.","zh":"屹立數百年指保持站立狀態達數百年。"},{"en":"An old temple may stand for centuries if it is repaired and protected.","zh":"如果古廟得到修復和保護，可能屹立數百年。"},{"en":"If a bridge stands for centuries, its design and materials have proved durable.","zh":"如果橋樑屹立數百年，其設計和材料就證明了耐久性。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises long survival over time.","zh":"這個短語強調長時間存續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"spectacular paintings and engravings","meaning":"壯觀的畫作和版畫","examples":[{"en":"The museum displays spectacular paintings and engravings of the bridge.","zh":"博物館展示這座橋壯觀的畫作和版畫。"},{"en":"Spectacular paintings and engravings are impressive artworks, including painted images and printed engraved images.","zh":"壯觀的畫作和版畫，是令人印象深刻的藝術作品，包括繪畫影像和雕刻印刷影像。"},{"en":"A museum may use spectacular paintings and engravings to show how people admired a bridge in the past.","zh":"博物館可能使用壯觀的畫作和版畫，展示過去人們如何欣賞一座橋。"},{"en":"If many beautiful images of one structure exist, it probably captured artistic interest.","zh":"如果一個結構有許多美麗圖像，它很可能曾吸引藝術興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes visually striking artworks in more than one medium.","zh":"這個短語描述以多於一種媒介呈現的視覺突出藝術品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be collected and exhibited","meaning":"被收藏及展出","examples":[{"en":"Numerous depictions of Iron Bridge are collected and exhibited locally.","zh":"大量 Iron Bridge 描繪作品在本地被收藏及展出。"},{"en":"To be collected and exhibited means to be gathered and shown publicly, usually in a museum or gallery.","zh":"被收藏及展出指被收集並公開展示，通常在博物館或畫廊中。"},{"en":"Students’ best artworks may be collected and exhibited during the school open day.","zh":"學生最佳作品可能在學校開放日被收藏及展出。"},{"en":"If images of a bridge are collected and exhibited, the community treats them as culturally valuable.","zh":"如果橋樑影像被收藏及展出，社區就是把它們視為有文化價值。"},{"en":"The phrase links preservation with public display.","zh":"這個短語把保存與公開展示連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"local museum","meaning":"本地博物館","examples":[{"en":"A local museum contains many artistic depictions of the bridge.","zh":"本地博物館收藏許多這座橋的藝術描繪作品。"},{"en":"A local museum is a museum in a particular area that preserves objects and stories from that place.","zh":"本地博物館是某地區內保存該地物件和故事的博物館。"},{"en":"A town’s local museum may display old photographs, tools and maps.","zh":"城鎮的本地博物館可能展示舊照片、工具和地圖。"},{"en":"If a local museum collects bridge images, it helps residents understand their heritage.","zh":"如果本地博物館收藏橋樑影像，就幫助居民理解自己的文化遺產。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a community-based place of memory and display.","zh":"這個短語指以社區為本的記憶和展示場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"at the centre of the landscape","meaning":"位於景觀中心","examples":[{"en":"The paintings show the iron structure at the centre of the landscape.","zh":"這些畫作顯示鐵結構位於景觀中心。"},{"en":"At the centre of the landscape means placed in the main visual or symbolic position within the scene.","zh":"位於景觀中心指放在場景中主要的視覺或象徵位置。"},{"en":"A painting may place a village school at the centre of the landscape to show its community importance.","zh":"畫作可能把鄉村學校放在景觀中心，以顯示其社區重要性。"},{"en":"If the bridge is central, the surrounding river, people and hills seem organised around it.","zh":"如果橋樑居於中心，周圍河流、人物和山丘就像圍繞它組織。"},{"en":"The phrase shows both position and importance in an artwork.","zh":"這個短語顯示藝術作品中的位置和重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 156 - Art in Iron and Steel.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 157":[{"front":"mystery on Easter Island","meaning":"復活節島之謎","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines the mystery surrounding Easter Island’s history.","zh":"文章探討圍繞復活節島歷史的謎團。"},{"en":"A mystery on Easter Island is an unanswered question about the island’s past.","zh":"mystery on Easter Island 指關於復活節島過去的未解問題。"},{"en":"Students may discuss the mystery on Easter Island when learning about ancient statues.","zh":"學生學習古代石像時，可能討論復活節島之謎。"},{"en":"If evidence is incomplete, a historical mystery can lead to many competing theories.","zh":"如果證據不完整，歷史謎團可以引出許多互相競爭的理論。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when talking about puzzles in archaeology.","zh":"這個片語適合談論考古學中的謎題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one of the world’s most famous","meaning":"世界上最著名的……之一","examples":[{"en":"Easter Island is one of the world’s most famous archaeological sites.","zh":"復活節島是世界上最著名的考古遺址之一。"},{"en":"One of the world’s most famous means widely known across many countries.","zh":"one of the world’s most famous 指在許多國家廣為人知。"},{"en":"The Great Wall is one of the world’s most famous historic structures.","zh":"長城是世界上最著名的歷史建築之一。"},{"en":"If a place is world-famous, people may recognise it even without visiting it.","zh":"如果一個地方聞名世界，人們即使沒有到訪也可能認得它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows very high international recognition.","zh":"這個片語表示極高的國際知名度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"yet least visited","meaning":"然而遊客極少的","examples":[{"en":"The island is famous yet remains one of the least visited archaeological sites.","zh":"該島很有名，然而仍是遊客極少的考古遺址之一。"},{"en":"Yet least visited means famous, but still visited by very few people.","zh":"yet least visited 指雖然有名，但到訪人數仍然很少。"},{"en":"A museum may be well known yet least visited because it is far from the city.","zh":"一間博物館可能很有名，然而因遠離市區而遊客極少。"},{"en":"If a site is remote, fame does not always bring many visitors.","zh":"如果遺址很偏遠，名氣不一定帶來大量遊客。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a contrast between reputation and actual tourism.","zh":"這個片語形成名聲與實際旅遊情況的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"archaeological site","meaning":"考古遺址","examples":[{"en":"Easter Island is an internationally famous archaeological site.","zh":"復活節島是國際著名的考古遺址。"},{"en":"An archaeological site is a place where remains of past human life are studied.","zh":"archaeological site 是研究過去人類生活遺跡的地方。"},{"en":"An old village with pottery, tools, and graves may become an archaeological site.","zh":"有陶器、工具和墓穴的舊村落可能成為考古遺址。"},{"en":"If a site is protected, researchers can study it without losing evidence.","zh":"如果遺址受到保護，研究人員就能研究它而不失去證據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a place important for understanding history.","zh":"這個片語指對理解歷史重要的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hilly and treeless","meaning":"多山而沒有樹木的","examples":[{"en":"Easter Island is a small, hilly, and now treeless island.","zh":"復活節島是一個細小、多山而現在沒有樹木的島嶼。"},{"en":"Hilly and treeless means having many slopes but few or no trees.","zh":"hilly and treeless 指有許多山坡，但樹木很少或沒有樹木。"},{"en":"A hilly and treeless area may feel exposed to strong wind and sun.","zh":"多山而沒有樹木的地區可能容易暴露於強風和陽光下。"},{"en":"If an island loses its forests, it can become treeless over time.","zh":"如果島嶼失去森林，它隨時間可能變成沒有樹木。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both shape and vegetation.","zh":"這個片語同時描述地形和植被。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"volcanic origin","meaning":"火山形成的；源自火山的","examples":[{"en":"The island is of volcanic origin.","zh":"該島是火山形成的。"},{"en":"Volcanic origin means something was formed by volcanic activity.","zh":"volcanic origin 指某物由火山活動形成。"},{"en":"Many island chains have volcanic origin because lava cooled into land.","zh":"許多島鏈源自火山，因為熔岩冷卻成陸地。"},{"en":"If a place has volcanic origin, its rocks may contain hardened lava.","zh":"如果一個地方源自火山，其岩石可能含有凝固熔岩。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how land was formed.","zh":"這個片語解釋土地如何形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be located in","meaning":"位於……","examples":[{"en":"Easter Island is located in the Pacific Ocean.","zh":"復活節島位於太平洋。"},{"en":"To be located in a place means to be situated there.","zh":"be located in a place 指位於某地方。"},{"en":"The school is located in a quiet residential area.","zh":"這所學校位於安靜的住宅區。"},{"en":"If a hospital is located far away, patients may need longer travel time.","zh":"如果醫院位於很遠的地方，病人可能需要更長交通時間。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the position of a place.","zh":"這個片語說明某地的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"south of the equator","meaning":"赤道以南","examples":[{"en":"The island lies 27 degrees south of the equator.","zh":"該島位於赤道以南27度。"},{"en":"South of the equator means below the imaginary line around the middle of Earth.","zh":"south of the equator 指位於地球中間假想線的南方。"},{"en":"Australia is south of the equator.","zh":"澳洲位於赤道以南。"},{"en":"If a place is south of the equator, its seasons are opposite to many northern countries.","zh":"如果一個地方位於赤道以南，其季節與許多北半球國家相反。"},{"en":"This phrase describes global position.","zh":"這個片語描述全球位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"off the coast of","meaning":"離……海岸","examples":[{"en":"Easter Island lies about 3,600 kilometres off the coast of Chile.","zh":"復活節島位於離智利海岸約3,600公里的地方。"},{"en":"Off the coast of a place means in the sea near, but not on, that land.","zh":"off the coast of a place 指位於某地海岸附近的海上，而不是在陸地上。"},{"en":"A small island may lie off the coast of a larger country.","zh":"小島可能位於離較大國家海岸不遠的地方。"},{"en":"If a site is far off the coast, reaching it can be expensive and difficult.","zh":"如果遺址遠離海岸，到達那裡可能昂貴且困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sea location near land.","zh":"這個片語描述接近陸地的海上位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"remote inhabited island","meaning":"偏遠的有人居住島嶼","examples":[{"en":"It is considered the world’s most remote inhabited island.","zh":"它被視為世界上最偏遠的有人居住島嶼。"},{"en":"A remote inhabited island is an island far from other places but still home to people.","zh":"remote inhabited island 是遠離其他地方但仍有人居住的島嶼。"},{"en":"A remote inhabited island may have limited transport, shops, and medical services.","zh":"偏遠的有人居住島嶼可能交通、商店和醫療服務有限。"},{"en":"If an island is remote, its people may develop distinctive traditions.","zh":"如果島嶼偏遠，其居民可能發展出獨特傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase combines distance with human settlement.","zh":"這個片語結合距離與人類定居。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"technically speaking","meaning":"嚴格來說","examples":[{"en":"Technically speaking, the island is one massive volcano.","zh":"嚴格來說，該島是一座巨型火山。"},{"en":"Technically speaking means according to the strict or scientific definition.","zh":"technically speaking 指根據嚴格或科學定義來說。"},{"en":"Technically speaking, a tomato is a fruit, though people use it like a vegetable.","zh":"嚴格來說，番茄是水果，雖然人們像蔬菜般使用它。"},{"en":"If we speak technically, everyday descriptions may become more precise.","zh":"如果嚴格來說，日常描述可能變得更精確。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a more exact explanation.","zh":"這個片語引入更準確的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a single massive volcano","meaning":"一座巨型火山","examples":[{"en":"Easter Island is technically a single massive volcano.","zh":"嚴格來說，復活節島是一座巨型火山。"},{"en":"A single massive volcano means one very large volcanic structure.","zh":"a single massive volcano 指一個非常龐大的火山結構。"},{"en":"Some islands are actually single massive volcanoes rising from the sea floor.","zh":"有些島嶼其實是從海床升起的一座巨型火山。"},{"en":"If an island is one volcano, its geology is shaped by eruptions and lava.","zh":"如果一個島是一座火山，其地質會受噴發和熔岩塑造。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the island’s physical origin.","zh":"這個片語解釋島嶼的物理起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rise from","meaning":"從……升起","examples":[{"en":"The volcano rises more than ten thousand feet from the ocean floor.","zh":"這座火山從海床升起超過一萬英尺。"},{"en":"To rise from somewhere means to extend upward from that point.","zh":"rise from somewhere 指從某處向上延伸。"},{"en":"A tall tower rises from the centre of the city.","zh":"一座高塔從市中心升起。"},{"en":"If mountains rise from the sea floor, only their tops may appear as islands.","zh":"如果山脈從海床升起，可能只有山頂露出成為島嶼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes upward height from a base.","zh":"這個片語描述由底部向上的高度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ocean floor","meaning":"海床","examples":[{"en":"The island rises from the Pacific Ocean floor.","zh":"該島從太平洋海床升起。"},{"en":"The ocean floor is the ground at the bottom of the sea.","zh":"ocean floor 是海洋底部的地面。"},{"en":"Scientists map the ocean floor to study underwater mountains and trenches.","zh":"科學家繪製海床地圖，以研究水下山脈和海溝。"},{"en":"If a volcano grows from the ocean floor, it may eventually form an island.","zh":"如果火山從海床生長，最終可能形成島嶼。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the seabed.","zh":"這個片語指海底地面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"receive its name from","meaning":"名稱源自……","examples":[{"en":"Easter Island received its best-known name from a Dutch sea captain.","zh":"復活節島最廣為人知的名稱源自一名荷蘭船長。"},{"en":"To receive its name from someone means that person or source gave the name.","zh":"receive its name from someone 指名稱由某人或某來源給予。"},{"en":"A school may receive its name from a respected local educator.","zh":"學校名稱可能源自一位受尊敬的本地教育家。"},{"en":"If a place receives its name from an event, the name preserves part of its history.","zh":"如果地方名稱源自某事件，該名稱會保存部分歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the origin of a name.","zh":"這個片語解釋名稱的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Dutch sea captain","meaning":"荷蘭船長","examples":[{"en":"Jacob Roggeveen was a Dutch sea captain.","zh":"Jacob Roggeveen 是一名荷蘭船長。"},{"en":"A Dutch sea captain is a ship captain from the Netherlands.","zh":"Dutch sea captain 是來自荷蘭的船長。"},{"en":"A sea captain must guide a ship, crew, and voyage safely.","zh":"船長必須安全指揮船隻、船員和航程。"},{"en":"If a captain discovers or records an island, his account may affect its later name.","zh":"如果船長發現或記錄一個島，其記述可能影響後來名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both nationality and occupation.","zh":"這個片語同時指出國籍和職業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the first European to","meaning":"首位……的歐洲人","examples":[{"en":"Roggeveen became the first European to visit the island.","zh":"Roggeveen 成為首位到訪該島的歐洲人。"},{"en":"The first European to do something means the earliest European recorded as doing it.","zh":"the first European to do something 指有記錄中最早做某事的歐洲人。"},{"en":"A sailor may be remembered as the first European to map a remote coast.","zh":"一名水手可能因首位繪製偏遠海岸地圖的歐洲人而被記住。"},{"en":"If someone is first to record a place, later history may use his account.","zh":"如果某人最早記錄一個地方，後來歷史可能使用他的描述。"},{"en":"This phrase marks historical sequence and contact.","zh":"這個片語標示歷史先後和接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Easter Sunday","meaning":"復活節星期日","examples":[{"en":"The captain arrived on Easter Sunday in 1722.","zh":"船長於1722年的復活節星期日抵達。"},{"en":"Easter Sunday is the Christian festival day celebrating the resurrection of Jesus.","zh":"Easter Sunday 是基督教慶祝耶穌復活的節日。"},{"en":"Many families attend church or gather for meals on Easter Sunday.","zh":"許多家庭在復活節星期日上教堂或聚餐。"},{"en":"If an explorer arrived on that day, the date could influence the name he gave.","zh":"如果探險者在那天抵達，日期可能影響他給予的名稱。"},{"en":"This phrase names a religious calendar day.","zh":"這個片語指出一個宗教曆法日子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Norwegian explorer","meaning":"挪威探險家","examples":[{"en":"Thor Heyerdahl was a Norwegian explorer.","zh":"Thor Heyerdahl 是一名挪威探險家。"},{"en":"A Norwegian explorer is a traveller or researcher from Norway who investigates unfamiliar places.","zh":"Norwegian explorer 是來自挪威、研究陌生地方的旅行者或研究者。"},{"en":"An explorer may travel by boat to test a theory about ancient migration.","zh":"探險家可能乘船旅行，以測試古代遷徙理論。"},{"en":"If an explorer becomes famous, his ideas may influence public imagination.","zh":"如果探險家成名，其想法可能影響公眾想像。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies nationality and role.","zh":"這個片語指出國籍和身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"popularize the idea that","meaning":"令……的觀點廣為流傳","examples":[{"en":"Heyerdahl popularized the idea that South Americans first settled the island.","zh":"Heyerdahl 令南美人最早定居該島的觀點廣為流傳。"},{"en":"To popularize an idea means to make many ordinary people know or accept it.","zh":"popularize an idea 指令許多普通人知道或接受某個想法。"},{"en":"A documentary can popularize the idea that sleep affects school performance.","zh":"紀錄片可以令睡眠影響學業表現的觀點廣為流傳。"},{"en":"If a famous writer repeats a theory, it may spread even before being proven.","zh":"如果著名作家重複某理論，它可能在被證實前已流傳。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how an idea becomes widely known.","zh":"這個片語顯示想法如何變得廣為人知。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be originally settled by","meaning":"最初由……定居","examples":[{"en":"He claimed that the island had originally been settled by an advanced society.","zh":"他聲稱該島最初由一個先進社會定居。"},{"en":"To be originally settled by a group means that group first made homes there.","zh":"be originally settled by a group 指某群體最先在那裡建立家園。"},{"en":"A valley may have originally been settled by farming families.","zh":"一個山谷可能最初由農民家庭定居。"},{"en":"If an island was settled by sailors, their language and customs may leave traces.","zh":"如果島嶼由航海者定居，他們的語言和習俗可能留下痕跡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first known human settlement.","zh":"這個片語描述最早已知的人類定居。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"advanced societies","meaning":"先進社會","examples":[{"en":"Heyerdahl believed that advanced South American societies reached the island.","zh":"Heyerdahl 相信先進南美社會曾到達該島。"},{"en":"Advanced societies are communities with developed technology, organisation, art, or knowledge.","zh":"advanced societies 是具有發達科技、組織、藝術或知識的社群。"},{"en":"Ancient cities with writing, farming, and public buildings may be called advanced societies.","zh":"擁有文字、農業和公共建築的古城可被稱為先進社會。"},{"en":"If a society is advanced, it may be able to organise long journeys or large projects.","zh":"如果社會先進，它可能能組織長途旅程或大型工程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes societies with complex development.","zh":"這個片語描述發展複雜的社會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"extensive research","meaning":"廣泛研究","examples":[{"en":"Extensive research later challenged Heyerdahl’s theory.","zh":"後來的廣泛研究挑戰了 Heyerdahl 的理論。"},{"en":"Extensive research means wide, detailed, and careful study.","zh":"extensive research 指廣泛、詳細而仔細的研究。"},{"en":"Doctors need extensive research before recommending a new treatment.","zh":"醫生在建議新治療前需要廣泛研究。"},{"en":"If extensive research contradicts a popular idea, the idea may need revision.","zh":"如果廣泛研究與流行觀點相矛盾，該觀點可能需要修正。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses depth and range of investigation.","zh":"這個片語強調調查的深度和範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"archaeological, ethnographic and linguistic research","meaning":"考古、民族誌及語言學研究","examples":[{"en":"Archaeological, ethnographic, and linguistic research provided strong evidence.","zh":"考古、民族誌及語言學研究提供了有力證據。"},{"en":"This research combines material remains, cultural study, and language evidence.","zh":"這類研究結合物質遺跡、文化研究和語言證據。"},{"en":"Researchers may compare tools, customs, and words to trace a people’s origins.","zh":"研究人員可能比較工具、習俗和詞語，以追溯一個民族的起源。"},{"en":"If different fields point to the same conclusion, the evidence becomes stronger.","zh":"如果不同領域指向同一結論，證據會變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a multi-disciplinary approach.","zh":"這個片語描述跨學科方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"conclusively show that","meaning":"確切顯示","examples":[{"en":"Research conclusively showed that the original hypothesis was inaccurate.","zh":"研究確切顯示原本假說並不準確。"},{"en":"To conclusively show that means to prove something clearly enough to settle the issue.","zh":"conclusively show that 指清楚證明某事，足以解決爭議。"},{"en":"Test results may conclusively show that water is unsafe to drink.","zh":"檢測結果可能確切顯示食水不安全。"},{"en":"If evidence conclusively shows a theory is wrong, scholars must reject it.","zh":"如果證據確切顯示某理論錯誤，學者必須否定它。"},{"en":"This phrase indicates strong proof.","zh":"這個片語表示有力證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hypothesis","meaning":"假說","examples":[{"en":"The evidence did not support Heyerdahl’s hypothesis.","zh":"證據不支持 Heyerdahl 的假說。"},{"en":"A hypothesis is a possible explanation that can be tested with evidence.","zh":"hypothesis 是可以用證據測試的可能解釋。"},{"en":"A student may form a hypothesis before doing a science experiment.","zh":"學生做科學實驗前可能先提出假說。"},{"en":"If evidence does not support a hypothesis, researchers must change their explanation.","zh":"如果證據不支持假說，研究人員必須改變解釋。"},{"en":"This word is common in scientific investigation.","zh":"這個詞常見於科學研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be shown to be inaccurate","meaning":"被證實並不準確","examples":[{"en":"The original settlement theory was shown to be inaccurate.","zh":"原本的定居理論被證實並不準確。"},{"en":"To be shown to be inaccurate means to be proven not correct.","zh":"be shown to be inaccurate 指被證明不正確。"},{"en":"A weather forecast may be shown to be inaccurate when the storm never arrives.","zh":"如果暴風雨沒有來，天氣預報可能被證實並不準確。"},{"en":"If new data disproves an old claim, the claim becomes unreliable.","zh":"如果新數據推翻舊主張，該主張就變得不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence correcting a wrong idea.","zh":"這個片語描述證據糾正錯誤想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it is now recognized that","meaning":"現時普遍認為","examples":[{"en":"It is now recognized that the first inhabitants were Polynesian.","zh":"現時普遍認為最早居民是波利尼西亞人。"},{"en":"It is now recognized that means people now widely accept this as true.","zh":"it is now recognized that 指人們現在廣泛接受某事為真。"},{"en":"It is now recognized that early reading helps later school performance.","zh":"現時普遍認為早期閱讀有助日後學業表現。"},{"en":"If strong evidence accumulates, a new conclusion may become widely accepted.","zh":"如果有力證據累積，新結論可能被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"This phrase presents the current accepted view.","zh":"這個片語呈現目前被接受的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"original inhabitants","meaning":"最早居民","examples":[{"en":"The original inhabitants of Easter Island were of Polynesian origin.","zh":"復活節島的最早居民源自波利尼西亞。"},{"en":"Original inhabitants are the first known people who lived in a place.","zh":"original inhabitants 是已知最早居住在某地的人。"},{"en":"A country’s original inhabitants may have languages and traditions older than later settlers.","zh":"一個國家的最早居民可能擁有比後來定居者更古老的語言和傳統。"},{"en":"If original inhabitants leave evidence, researchers can study migration and culture.","zh":"如果最早居民留下證據，研究人員可以研究遷徙和文化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the earliest residents.","zh":"這個片語指最早的居民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be of Polynesian stock","meaning":"屬波利尼西亞血統","examples":[{"en":"The island’s original inhabitants were of Polynesian stock.","zh":"該島最早居民屬波利尼西亞血統。"},{"en":"To be of Polynesian stock means to come from Polynesian ancestry or origin.","zh":"be of Polynesian stock 指源自波利尼西亞祖先或起源。"},{"en":"People of shared stock may have related languages, customs, and genetic history.","zh":"屬共同血統的人可能有相關語言、習俗和遺傳歷史。"},{"en":"If skeletons show Polynesian stock, settlement theories must reflect that origin.","zh":"如果骨骼顯示波利尼西亞血統，定居理論就必須反映這起源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ancestry.","zh":"這個片語描述祖源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"DNA extracts","meaning":"DNA 提取樣本","examples":[{"en":"DNA extracts from skeletons confirmed the inhabitants’ origins.","zh":"骨骼中的 DNA 提取樣本證實了居民的起源。"},{"en":"DNA extracts are small samples of genetic material taken for analysis.","zh":"DNA extracts 是取出來作分析的小量遺傳物質樣本。"},{"en":"Scientists may use DNA extracts from bones to identify ancient populations.","zh":"科學家可能使用骨骼中的 DNA 提取樣本來識別古代人口。"},{"en":"If DNA extracts match a region, they can support migration theories.","zh":"如果 DNA 提取樣本與某地區吻合，就能支持遷徙理論。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to biological evidence from genetic samples.","zh":"這個片語指來自遺傳樣本的生物證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"confirm a finding","meaning":"證實研究結果","examples":[{"en":"Genetic evidence helped confirm the archaeological findings.","zh":"遺傳證據幫助證實考古研究結果。"},{"en":"To confirm a finding means to support or prove a research result.","zh":"confirm a finding 指支持或證明某項研究結果。"},{"en":"A second test can confirm a finding from the first experiment.","zh":"第二次測試可以證實第一次實驗的發現。"},{"en":"If different evidence confirms the same finding, confidence increases.","zh":"如果不同證據證實同一發現，可信度就會提高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strengthening a conclusion.","zh":"這個片語描述強化結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"most probably","meaning":"很可能","examples":[{"en":"The settlers most probably came from nearby Polynesian islands.","zh":"定居者很可能來自附近的波利尼西亞島嶼。"},{"en":"Most probably means very likely, though not absolutely certain.","zh":"most probably 指很有可能，但並非百分百確定。"},{"en":"If dark clouds gather, it will most probably rain later.","zh":"如果烏雲聚集，稍後很可能會下雨。"},{"en":"Researchers use this phrase when evidence is strong but not final.","zh":"當證據很強但未至最終確定時，研究人員會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses careful confidence.","zh":"這個片語表達謹慎的信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"arrive as early as","meaning":"早於……便抵達","examples":[{"en":"The first settlers may have arrived as early as AD 318.","zh":"第一批定居者可能早於公元318年便抵達。"},{"en":"To arrive as early as a date means to arrive surprisingly early by that time.","zh":"arrive as early as a date 指早到令人意外地在某時間已抵達。"},{"en":"Some students arrive as early as 7 a.m. to revise before school.","zh":"有些學生早於早上七時便到校溫習。"},{"en":"If settlers arrived very early, the island’s human history is longer than expected.","zh":"如果定居者很早抵達，該島的人類歷史就比預期更長。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises early timing.","zh":"這個片語強調時間很早。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"carbon dating","meaning":"碳年代測定","examples":[{"en":"Carbon dating of reeds provided evidence of early settlement.","zh":"蘆葦的碳年代測定提供了早期定居的證據。"},{"en":"Carbon dating is a scientific method used to estimate the age of organic material.","zh":"carbon dating 是用來估算有機物年代的科學方法。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may use carbon dating on wood, bones, or seeds.","zh":"考古學家可能對木材、骨頭或種子使用碳年代測定。"},{"en":"If carbon dating gives an early date, settlement may have begun earlier than expected.","zh":"如果碳年代測定給出很早的日期，定居可能比預期更早開始。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a dating method in archaeology.","zh":"這個片語指考古學中的年代測定方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at the time of their arrival","meaning":"在他們抵達時","examples":[{"en":"At the time of their arrival, much of the island was forested.","zh":"在他們抵達時，島上大部分地區都有森林。"},{"en":"At the time of their arrival means when they first came.","zh":"at the time of their arrival 指他們最初到來的時候。"},{"en":"At the time of students’ arrival, the school hall was already full.","zh":"在學生抵達時，學校禮堂已經坐滿。"},{"en":"If conditions were different at arrival, later changes need explanation.","zh":"如果抵達時情況不同，後來的變化就需要解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase sets the scene at the beginning.","zh":"這個片語交代最初的背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be heavily forested","meaning":"樹木茂密的","examples":[{"en":"Much of Easter Island was once heavily forested.","zh":"復活節島大部分地區曾經樹木茂密。"},{"en":"To be heavily forested means to be covered with many trees.","zh":"be heavily forested 指被大量樹木覆蓋。"},{"en":"A mountain valley may be heavily forested and difficult to cross.","zh":"山谷可能樹木茂密，難以穿越。"},{"en":"If land is heavily forested, people can use wood for houses, boats, or tools.","zh":"如果土地樹木茂密，人們可以使用木材建屋、造船或製作工具。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dense tree cover.","zh":"這個片語描述濃密林木覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be teeming with","meaning":"充滿……","examples":[{"en":"The island was teeming with land birds.","zh":"該島充滿陸鳥。"},{"en":"To be teeming with something means to be full of many living things.","zh":"be teeming with something 指充滿大量生物或人。"},{"en":"A market may be teeming with shoppers before a holiday.","zh":"假期前，市場可能擠滿購物者。"},{"en":"If an island is teeming with birds, food and nesting sites are plentiful.","zh":"如果島上充滿鳥類，食物和築巢地通常很豐富。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests abundance and activity.","zh":"這個片語暗示數量豐富和活動頻繁。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"land birds","meaning":"陸鳥","examples":[{"en":"The island once supported many species of land birds.","zh":"該島曾支援許多陸鳥品種。"},{"en":"Land birds are birds that live mainly on land rather than at sea.","zh":"land birds 是主要生活在陸地而非海上的鳥類。"},{"en":"Sparrows, pigeons, and many forest birds are land birds.","zh":"麻雀、白鴿和許多森林鳥類都是陸鳥。"},{"en":"If land birds lose forests, their nesting places may disappear.","zh":"如果陸鳥失去森林，牠們的築巢地可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts land-based birds with seabirds.","zh":"這個片語把陸地鳥類與海鳥作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"productive breeding site","meaning":"繁殖力高的繁殖地","examples":[{"en":"The island may have been a highly productive breeding site for seabirds.","zh":"該島可能曾是海鳥繁殖力很高的繁殖地。"},{"en":"A productive breeding site is a place where many animals successfully reproduce.","zh":"productive breeding site 是許多動物能成功繁殖的地方。"},{"en":"A quiet wetland can be a productive breeding site for frogs and birds.","zh":"安靜濕地可以是青蛙和鳥類繁殖力高的繁殖地。"},{"en":"If predators arrive, a breeding site may become less productive.","zh":"如果掠食者到來，繁殖地可能變得較不有效。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on successful reproduction.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於成功繁殖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"seabirds","meaning":"海鳥","examples":[{"en":"Large numbers of seabirds once bred on Easter Island.","zh":"大量海鳥曾在復活節島繁殖。"},{"en":"Seabirds are birds that live mainly near or over the sea.","zh":"seabirds 是主要生活在海邊或海上的鳥類。"},{"en":"Gulls and albatrosses are common examples of seabirds.","zh":"海鷗和信天翁是常見海鳥例子。"},{"en":"If seabirds lose safe nesting sites, their numbers can fall quickly.","zh":"如果海鳥失去安全築巢地，其數量可能快速下降。"},{"en":"This word refers to birds closely linked to the ocean.","zh":"這個詞指與海洋密切相關的鳥類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"plentiful food sources","meaning":"豐富的食物來源","examples":[{"en":"Early settlers benefited from plentiful food sources.","zh":"早期定居者受惠於豐富的食物來源。"},{"en":"Plentiful food sources are many available supplies of food.","zh":"plentiful food sources 指大量可取得的食物供應。"},{"en":"A village near rivers and farms may have plentiful food sources.","zh":"靠近河流和農田的村莊可能有豐富食物來源。"},{"en":"If food sources are plentiful, a population can grow more easily.","zh":"如果食物來源豐富，人口更容易增長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes abundance of food.","zh":"這個片語描述食物充足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"human population grew","meaning":"人口增長","examples":[{"en":"The human population grew because food was plentiful.","zh":"由於食物充足，人口增長。"},{"en":"Human population grew means the number of people increased.","zh":"human population grew 指人數增加。"},{"en":"A town’s population may grow when jobs and housing become available.","zh":"當工作和住房增加時，城鎮人口可能增長。"},{"en":"If food and safety improve, more children may survive and population can rise.","zh":"如果食物和安全改善，更多孩子可能存活，人口便會上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes demographic increase.","zh":"這個片語描述人口數量增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"give rise to","meaning":"產生；促成","examples":[{"en":"Population growth gave rise to a rich culture.","zh":"人口增長促成豐富文化。"},{"en":"To give rise to something means to cause it to develop.","zh":"give rise to something 指造成某事發展出來。"},{"en":"New technology can give rise to new jobs and new problems.","zh":"新科技可以產生新工作和新問題。"},{"en":"If communities become larger, they may give rise to more complex traditions.","zh":"如果社群變大，它們可能促成更複雜的傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with a later development.","zh":"這個片語把原因與後來發展連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"religious and artistic culture","meaning":"宗教及藝術文化","examples":[{"en":"The island developed a rich religious and artistic culture.","zh":"該島發展出豐富的宗教及藝術文化。"},{"en":"Religious and artistic culture includes beliefs, rituals, images, music, and creative works.","zh":"religious and artistic culture 包括信仰、儀式、圖像、音樂和創作。"},{"en":"A community’s temples, songs, and carvings can show its religious and artistic culture.","zh":"社群的廟宇、歌曲和雕刻可以展示其宗教及藝術文化。"},{"en":"If a society becomes stable, it may have more time to develop art and ritual.","zh":"如果社會變得穩定，它可能有更多時間發展藝術和儀式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes culture connected with belief and creativity.","zh":"這個片語描述與信仰和創意相關的文化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"most famous features","meaning":"最著名的特色","examples":[{"en":"The moai are the culture’s most famous features.","zh":"摩艾石像是該文化最著名的特色。"},{"en":"Most famous features are the best-known parts or characteristics of something.","zh":"most famous features 是某事物中最廣為人知的部分或特徵。"},{"en":"A city’s skyline may be one of its most famous features.","zh":"一個城市的天際線可能是其最著名特色之一。"},{"en":"If a feature becomes iconic, tourists may associate the whole place with it.","zh":"如果某特色變成標誌性，遊客可能把整個地方與它聯繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what people remember most.","zh":"這個片語指出人們最記得的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"enormous stone statues","meaning":"巨型石像","examples":[{"en":"The moai are enormous stone statues.","zh":"摩艾是巨型石像。"},{"en":"Enormous stone statues are very large figures carved from stone.","zh":"enormous stone statues 是由石頭雕成的非常巨大人物像。"},{"en":"A park may display enormous stone statues at its entrance.","zh":"公園入口可能展示巨型石像。"},{"en":"If statues are enormous, moving them requires many workers or special tools.","zh":"如果石像巨大，搬運它們需要許多工人或特殊工具。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses both size and material.","zh":"這個片語強調大小和材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"moai","meaning":"摩艾石像","examples":[{"en":"Hundreds of moai were created on Easter Island.","zh":"復活節島上創造了數百座摩艾石像。"},{"en":"Moai are the large stone statues made by the people of Easter Island.","zh":"moai 是復活節島居民製作的大型石像。"},{"en":"Visitors often recognise moai by their long faces and heavy bodies.","zh":"遊客常透過長臉和厚重身軀認出摩艾石像。"},{"en":"If moai were moved across the island, their transport required planning and labour.","zh":"如果摩艾石像被運送橫越島嶼，其搬運需要計劃和勞力。"},{"en":"This word names Easter Island’s famous statues.","zh":"這個詞指出復活節島的著名石像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stand upon","meaning":"矗立於……之上","examples":[{"en":"Many moai once stood upon massive stone platforms.","zh":"許多摩艾石像曾矗立於巨型石製平台之上。"},{"en":"To stand upon something means to be positioned on top of it.","zh":"stand upon something 指位於某物上方。"},{"en":"A statue may stand upon a square base in a museum hall.","zh":"雕像可能矗立於博物館大廳的方形底座上。"},{"en":"If a structure stands upon a platform, the platform gives it support and importance.","zh":"如果建築物矗立於平台之上，平台會給它支撐和重要感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical placement.","zh":"這個片語描述實際位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"massive stone platforms","meaning":"巨型石製平台","examples":[{"en":"The statues were placed on massive stone platforms called ahu.","zh":"這些石像被放在稱為 ahu 的巨型石製平台上。"},{"en":"Massive stone platforms are very large raised structures made of stone.","zh":"massive stone platforms 是由石頭製成的大型高起結構。"},{"en":"A temple may have a massive stone platform for ceremonies.","zh":"廟宇可能有巨型石製平台用於儀式。"},{"en":"If statues stand on platforms, viewers may see them as more powerful or sacred.","zh":"如果石像站在平台上，觀看者可能覺得它們更有力量或神聖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large stone bases.","zh":"這個片語描述大型石製底座。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ahu platforms","meaning":"阿胡石台","examples":[{"en":"About 250 ahu platforms remain around the island.","zh":"島上周圍仍保留約250座阿胡石台。"},{"en":"Ahu platforms are the stone platforms on Easter Island that supported moai.","zh":"ahu platforms 是復活節島上支撐摩艾石像的石製平台。"},{"en":"Archaeologists study ahu platforms to understand ceremonies and social organisation.","zh":"考古學家研究阿胡石台，以理解儀式和社會組織。"},{"en":"If many platforms remain, they show how widespread the statue tradition was.","zh":"如果許多平台仍存在，它們顯示石像傳統曾多麼廣泛。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific type of Easter Island structure.","zh":"這個片語指出復活節島的一種特定建築。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be spaced apart","meaning":"相隔……分佈","examples":[{"en":"The platforms were spaced approximately half a mile apart.","zh":"這些平台相隔約半英里分佈。"},{"en":"To be spaced apart means to be placed with distance between each item.","zh":"be spaced apart 指每件物件之間保持距離放置。"},{"en":"Desks may be spaced apart during an exam to prevent cheating.","zh":"考試期間，桌子可能相隔分佈以防作弊。"},{"en":"If platforms are evenly spaced, the arrangement may reflect planning.","zh":"如果平台均勻相隔，這種排列可能反映計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distance between objects.","zh":"這個片語描述物件之間的距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an almost unbroken line","meaning":"幾乎沒有間斷的長線","examples":[{"en":"The platforms formed an almost unbroken line around the island.","zh":"這些平台圍繞島嶼形成幾乎沒有間斷的長線。"},{"en":"An almost unbroken line is a line with very few gaps.","zh":"an almost unbroken line 是幾乎沒有缺口的線。"},{"en":"Shops formed an almost unbroken line along the main street.","zh":"商店沿主街形成幾乎沒有間斷的長線。"},{"en":"If monuments form a line around an island, they may mark territory or sacred space.","zh":"如果紀念物圍繞島嶼成線，它們可能標示領地或神聖空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a nearly continuous arrangement.","zh":"這個片語描述幾乎連續的排列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"around the perimeter of","meaning":"圍繞……的外圍","examples":[{"en":"The ahu platforms extended around the perimeter of the island.","zh":"阿胡石台沿着島嶼外圍延伸。"},{"en":"Around the perimeter of something means along the outer edge of it.","zh":"around the perimeter of something 指沿着某物外邊界。"},{"en":"Trees were planted around the perimeter of the playground.","zh":"樹木被種在操場外圍。"},{"en":"If structures stand around a perimeter, they can define a boundary.","zh":"如果建築物圍繞外圍而立，它們可以界定邊界。"},{"en":"This phrase describes placement along an outside edge.","zh":"這個片語描述沿外緣的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in various stages of completion","meaning":"處於不同完成階段","examples":[{"en":"Many statues remain in various stages of completion.","zh":"許多石像仍處於不同完成階段。"},{"en":"In various stages of completion means some are finished, partly finished, or barely started.","zh":"in various stages of completion 指有些已完成、有些部分完成、有些剛開始。"},{"en":"A classroom may have projects in various stages of completion before the deadline.","zh":"截止日期前，課室裡的專題可能處於不同完成階段。"},{"en":"If objects are unfinished, they can show how work was done step by step.","zh":"如果物件未完成，它們可以顯示工作如何逐步進行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes different levels of progress.","zh":"這個片語描述不同進度水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be scattered around","meaning":"散佈於……","examples":[{"en":"Hundreds of unfinished moai are scattered around the island.","zh":"數百座未完成摩艾石像散佈於島上各處。"},{"en":"To be scattered around means to be spread in different places rather than gathered together.","zh":"be scattered around 指分散在不同地方，而不是集中在一起。"},{"en":"Toys may be scattered around a child’s room after playtime.","zh":"玩耍後，玩具可能散佈於孩子房間各處。"},{"en":"If statues are scattered around an island, researchers must map many locations.","zh":"如果石像散佈於島上，研究人員必須繪製許多地點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uneven spread across an area.","zh":"這個片語描述在某區域中不均勻分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"quarries","meaning":"採石場","examples":[{"en":"Many incomplete statues remain in the island’s quarries.","zh":"許多未完成石像仍留在島上的採石場。"},{"en":"Quarries are places where stone is cut from the ground.","zh":"quarries 是從地下開採石材的地方。"},{"en":"Builders may get marble or granite from quarries.","zh":"建築工人可能從採石場取得大理石或花崗岩。"},{"en":"If unfinished statues remain in quarries, they show where carving began.","zh":"如果未完成石像留在採石場，它們顯示雕刻從哪裡開始。"},{"en":"This word refers to stone-extraction sites.","zh":"這個詞指開採石材的地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"along ancient roads","meaning":"沿着古道","examples":[{"en":"Other statues lie along ancient roads leading to the coast.","zh":"其他石像躺在通往海岸的古道沿線。"},{"en":"Along ancient roads means beside or on old routes used long ago.","zh":"along ancient roads 指在很久以前使用的舊路旁或路上。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may find broken pottery along ancient roads.","zh":"考古學家可能在古道沿線發現破陶器。"},{"en":"If statues lie along roads, they may reveal transport routes.","zh":"如果石像躺在道路沿線，它們可能揭示運輸路線。"},{"en":"This phrase links objects with old pathways.","zh":"這個片語把物件與古老路徑連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be erected","meaning":"被豎立","examples":[{"en":"Completed statues were usually erected in coastal areas.","zh":"完成的石像通常被豎立在沿海地區。"},{"en":"To be erected means to be raised and placed upright.","zh":"be erected 指被升起並直立放置。"},{"en":"A flagpole may be erected in front of a school.","zh":"旗桿可能被豎立在學校前面。"},{"en":"If a statue is erected in public, people can see it as a monument.","zh":"如果雕像被豎立在公共地方，人們可以把它視為紀念物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes setting something upright.","zh":"這個片語描述把某物直立放置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be carved from","meaning":"由……雕刻而成","examples":[{"en":"Nearly all the moai were carved from volcanic stone.","zh":"幾乎所有摩艾石像都是由火山岩雕刻而成。"},{"en":"To be carved from something means to be shaped by cutting that material.","zh":"be carved from something 指透過切削某材料塑造成形。"},{"en":"A wooden mask may be carved from a single block of wood.","zh":"木面具可能由一整塊木頭雕刻而成。"},{"en":"If a statue is carved from hard stone, it requires skill and time.","zh":"如果雕像由堅硬石材雕成，就需要技巧和時間。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the material used for carving.","zh":"這個片語解釋雕刻所用材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tough volcanic stone","meaning":"堅硬的火山岩","examples":[{"en":"The statues were made from the tough stone of Rano Raraku.","zh":"這些石像由 Rano Raraku 的堅硬石材製成。"},{"en":"Tough volcanic stone is hard rock formed from volcanic material.","zh":"tough volcanic stone 是由火山物質形成的堅硬岩石。"},{"en":"Builders may use tough volcanic stone for walls because it lasts long.","zh":"建築工人可能用堅硬火山岩築牆，因為它耐用。"},{"en":"If stone is tough, carving it is difficult but the statue may survive longer.","zh":"如果石材堅硬，雕刻會困難，但石像可能保存更久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong rock from volcanoes.","zh":"這個片語描述來自火山的堅固岩石。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"average statue","meaning":"平均大小的石像","examples":[{"en":"The average statue is over four metres tall.","zh":"平均大小的石像高超過四米。"},{"en":"An average statue means a typical statue when compared with others in the group.","zh":"average statue 指與同組其他石像相比的典型石像。"},{"en":"The average desk in a classroom is lower than an office desk.","zh":"課室中的平均桌子比辦公桌矮。"},{"en":"If the average statue is already large, the biggest examples must be enormous.","zh":"如果平均大小的石像已經很大，最大的例子一定非常巨大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the typical size or value.","zh":"這個片語描述典型大小或數值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"weigh 14 tons","meaning":"重達十四噸","examples":[{"en":"An average moai weighs approximately 14 tons.","zh":"一座平均摩艾石像重約十四噸。"},{"en":"To weigh 14 tons means to have a mass of about 14,000 kilograms.","zh":"weigh 14 tons 指重量約為14,000公斤。"},{"en":"A heavy truck may weigh many tons when fully loaded.","zh":"滿載的重型貨車可能重達許多噸。"},{"en":"If a statue weighs 14 tons, moving it without modern machines is extremely difficult.","zh":"如果石像重達十四噸，沒有現代機器搬動它會極度困難。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a very large weight.","zh":"這個片語給出非常大的重量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"depending upon","meaning":"視乎；取決於","examples":[{"en":"The number of workers needed depended upon the statue’s size.","zh":"所需工人數量視乎石像大小。"},{"en":"Depending upon means being decided or affected by something.","zh":"depending upon 指由某事決定或受某事影響。"},{"en":"The cost of a trip depends upon distance, transport, and hotel prices.","zh":"旅行費用取決於距離、交通和酒店價格。"},{"en":"If a statue is larger, the number of workers needed may increase.","zh":"如果石像較大，所需工人數量可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a condition that changes the result.","zh":"這個片語顯示會改變結果的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"it has been estimated that","meaning":"據估計","examples":[{"en":"It has been estimated that up to 150 people moved each statue.","zh":"據估計，每座石像最多由150人搬動。"},{"en":"It has been estimated that means experts have calculated or guessed based on evidence.","zh":"it has been estimated that 指專家根據證據計算或估算。"},{"en":"It has been estimated that the repair will cost over a million dollars.","zh":"據估計，維修費將超過一百萬美元。"},{"en":"If exact records are missing, researchers may use estimates.","zh":"如果缺乏確切記錄，研究人員可能使用估算。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an evidence-based approximation.","zh":"這個片語引入基於證據的近似數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be needed to drag","meaning":"需要被用來拖動","examples":[{"en":"Large teams were needed to drag the statues across the island.","zh":"需要大型隊伍拖動石像橫越島嶼。"},{"en":"To be needed to drag something means to be required to pull it with force.","zh":"be needed to drag something 指需要某些人或工具用力拉動某物。"},{"en":"Several students may be needed to drag a heavy stage prop safely.","zh":"可能需要幾名學生安全拖動沉重舞台道具。"},{"en":"If an object is huge, many people may be needed to move it.","zh":"如果物件巨大，可能需要許多人搬動它。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the labour required for pulling.","zh":"這個片語解釋拖動所需勞力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"across the countryside","meaning":"橫越郊野","examples":[{"en":"The statues were transported across the countryside.","zh":"這些石像被運送橫越郊野。"},{"en":"Across the countryside means through open rural land.","zh":"across the countryside 指穿越開闊鄉郊土地。"},{"en":"Farmers may drive tractors across the countryside during harvest.","zh":"收成期間，農民可能駕駛拖拉機橫越郊野。"},{"en":"If heavy objects are moved across rough countryside, the journey becomes difficult.","zh":"如果沉重物件被運送橫越崎嶇郊野，旅程會變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement through non-urban land.","zh":"這個片語描述穿越非城市土地的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sledges and rollers","meaning":"雪橇式拖板及滾木","examples":[{"en":"Workers may have used wooden sledges and rollers.","zh":"工人可能使用木製雪橇式拖板及滾木。"},{"en":"Sledges and rollers are tools used to move heavy objects by sliding or rolling them.","zh":"sledges and rollers 是透過滑動或滾動搬運重物的工具。"},{"en":"Movers may use rollers to shift a heavy piano across a floor.","zh":"搬運工可能使用滾輪把沉重鋼琴移過地板。"},{"en":"If ancient workers lacked wheels, sledges and rollers could reduce effort.","zh":"如果古代工人沒有車輪，拖板和滾木可以減少力氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes simple transport equipment.","zh":"這個片語描述簡單運輸設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be made from","meaning":"由……製成","examples":[{"en":"The transport equipment was made from the island’s trees.","zh":"運輸設備由島上的樹木製成。"},{"en":"To be made from something means to be produced using that material.","zh":"be made from something 指使用某材料製造。"},{"en":"Paper is made from wood fibres.","zh":"紙由木纖維製成。"},{"en":"If tools are made from trees, cutting many trees can reduce forest cover.","zh":"如果工具由樹木製成，砍伐許多樹可能減少森林覆蓋。"},{"en":"This phrase explains material origin.","zh":"這個片語解釋材料來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be unable to definitively explain","meaning":"無法確切解釋","examples":[{"en":"Scholars are unable to definitively explain the function of the statues.","zh":"學者無法確切解釋石像的功能。"},{"en":"To be unable to definitively explain means to lack enough evidence for a final answer.","zh":"be unable to definitively explain 指缺乏足夠證據作出最終答案。"},{"en":"Doctors may be unable to definitively explain symptoms after one short appointment.","zh":"醫生在一次短診後可能無法確切解釋症狀。"},{"en":"If records are missing, historians may not reach a certain conclusion.","zh":"如果記錄缺失，歷史學家可能無法得出確定結論。"},{"en":"This phrase shows uncertainty despite study.","zh":"這個片語顯示雖有研究但仍不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"function and use","meaning":"功能和用途","examples":[{"en":"The precise function and use of the moai remain uncertain.","zh":"摩艾石像的確切功能和用途仍不確定。"},{"en":"Function and use means what something was for and how people used it.","zh":"function and use 指某物的目的以及人們如何使用它。"},{"en":"A museum label explains the function and use of an old farming tool.","zh":"博物館標籤會解釋舊農具的功能和用途。"},{"en":"If the function is unclear, researchers must study location, shape, and context.","zh":"如果功能不清楚，研究人員必須研究位置、形狀和背景。"},{"en":"This phrase asks what purpose something served.","zh":"這個片語詢問某物發揮甚麼目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"it is assumed that","meaning":"一般推測","examples":[{"en":"It is assumed that the practice developed from wider Polynesian traditions.","zh":"一般推測這種做法由較廣泛的波利尼西亞傳統發展而來。"},{"en":"It is assumed that means people think something is likely, though it may not be proven fully.","zh":"it is assumed that 指人們認為某事很可能如此，但未必完全證實。"},{"en":"It is assumed that students know basic grammar before joining the course.","zh":"一般假設學生入讀課程前已懂基本文法。"},{"en":"If evidence is indirect, scholars may make cautious assumptions.","zh":"如果證據是間接的，學者可能作出謹慎推測。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a likely but not certain belief.","zh":"這個片語引入可能但不確定的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"derive from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"The practice may have derived from customs found elsewhere in Polynesia.","zh":"這種做法可能源自波利尼西亞其他地方的習俗。"},{"en":"To derive from something means to come from it as a source.","zh":"derive from something 指以某事作為來源。"},{"en":"Many English words derive from Latin or French.","zh":"許多英文詞源自拉丁語或法語。"},{"en":"If a tradition derives from older customs, it may change after moving to a new place.","zh":"如果傳統源自較古老習俗，它移到新地方後可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase explains origin.","zh":"這個片語解釋起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be rooted in","meaning":"根源於……","examples":[{"en":"The statue tradition was rooted in earlier Polynesian practices.","zh":"石像傳統根源於較早的波利尼西亞做法。"},{"en":"To be rooted in something means to be deeply based on it.","zh":"be rooted in something 指深深建基於某事。"},{"en":"A school’s rules may be rooted in respect and safety.","zh":"學校規則可能根源於尊重和安全。"},{"en":"If a custom is rooted in religion, it may carry sacred meaning.","zh":"如果習俗根源於宗教，它可能帶有神聖意義。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a deep origin or foundation.","zh":"這個片語顯示深層起源或基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"evolve in a unique way","meaning":"以獨特方式演變","examples":[{"en":"The tradition evolved in a unique way on Easter Island.","zh":"這種傳統在復活節島以獨特方式演變。"},{"en":"To evolve in a unique way means to develop differently from similar traditions elsewhere.","zh":"evolve in a unique way 指與其他地方相似傳統相比，以不同方式發展。"},{"en":"A local festival may evolve in a unique way after generations of change.","zh":"本地節日經過幾代變化後，可能以獨特方式演變。"},{"en":"If a community is isolated, its culture may develop special features.","zh":"如果社群孤立，其文化可能發展出特殊特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distinctive development over time.","zh":"這個片語描述隨時間而來的獨特發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"archaeological analysis","meaning":"考古分析","examples":[{"en":"Archaeological analysis provides clues about the statues’ purpose.","zh":"考古分析提供關於石像用途的線索。"},{"en":"Archaeological analysis is the study of physical remains to understand past human life.","zh":"archaeological analysis 是研究實體遺跡以理解過去人類生活。"},{"en":"Researchers may use archaeological analysis on bones, tools, buildings, and soil.","zh":"研究人員可能對骨骼、工具、建築和土壤進行考古分析。"},{"en":"If analysis finds patterns in statue placement, it may suggest ritual use.","zh":"如果分析發現石像位置的模式，可能暗示儀式用途。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence-based study of the past.","zh":"這個片語描述基於證據的過去研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"iconographic analysis","meaning":"圖像學分析","examples":[{"en":"Iconographic analysis examines the images and symbols used in the statues.","zh":"圖像學分析檢視石像所使用的圖像和符號。"},{"en":"Iconographic analysis is the study of images, symbols, and their meanings.","zh":"iconographic analysis 是研究圖像、符號及其意義的方法。"},{"en":"Art historians use iconographic analysis to understand religious paintings.","zh":"藝術史學家使用圖像學分析理解宗教畫作。"},{"en":"If a statue has repeated symbols, analysis may reveal shared beliefs.","zh":"如果石像有重複符號，分析可能揭示共同信仰。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on visual meaning.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於視覺意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"statue cult","meaning":"石像崇拜","examples":[{"en":"The statue cult was closely connected with authority and ancestry.","zh":"石像崇拜與權威和祖先密切相關。"},{"en":"A statue cult is a system of religious respect or worship centred on statues.","zh":"statue cult 是以石像為中心的宗教敬奉或崇拜系統。"},{"en":"Ancient communities may build statues for ancestors, gods, or leaders.","zh":"古代社群可能為祖先、神明或領袖建造石像。"},{"en":"If a statue cult grows, statues may become central to ceremonies and power.","zh":"如果石像崇拜發展，石像可能成為儀式和權力的核心。"},{"en":"This phrase links sculpture with belief.","zh":"這個片語把雕塑與信仰連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be based on an ideology of","meaning":"建基於……的思想體系","examples":[{"en":"The cult was based on an ideology of male authority.","zh":"這種崇拜建基於男性權威的思想體系。"},{"en":"To be based on an ideology of something means to rest on a set of beliefs about it.","zh":"be based on an ideology of something 指以一套關於某事的信念為基礎。"},{"en":"A policy may be based on an ideology of individual responsibility.","zh":"政策可能建基於個人責任的思想體系。"},{"en":"If a system is based on authority, power may be concentrated in certain groups.","zh":"如果制度建基於權威，權力可能集中在某些群體手中。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the belief system behind a practice.","zh":"這個片語解釋某做法背後的信念系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lineage-based authority","meaning":"以血統為基礎的權威","examples":[{"en":"The statues represented male, lineage-based authority.","zh":"這些石像代表男性、以血統為基礎的權威。"},{"en":"Lineage-based authority is power that comes from family descent or ancestry.","zh":"lineage-based authority 是來自家族世系或祖先的權力。"},{"en":"In some traditional societies, leadership passes through a family line.","zh":"在一些傳統社會中，領導權透過家族世系傳承。"},{"en":"If authority depends on lineage, ancestors become politically important.","zh":"如果權威取決於血統，祖先在政治上就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase links power with inherited family status.","zh":"這個片語把權力與繼承而來的家族地位連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"incorporate symbolism","meaning":"融入象徵意義","examples":[{"en":"The statue tradition incorporated religious and political symbolism.","zh":"石像傳統融入宗教和政治象徵意義。"},{"en":"To incorporate symbolism means to include signs or images that carry deeper meaning.","zh":"incorporate symbolism 指加入帶有深層意思的符號或圖像。"},{"en":"A school logo may incorporate symbolism through colours and shapes.","zh":"學校標誌可能透過顏色和形狀融入象徵意義。"},{"en":"If art incorporates political symbolism, it can express power without words.","zh":"如果藝術融入政治象徵，它可以不用文字表達權力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding meaningful symbols.","zh":"這個片語描述加入有意義的象徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"anthropomorphic symbolism","meaning":"擬人象徵","examples":[{"en":"The moai use anthropomorphic symbolism by giving human form to sacred power.","zh":"摩艾石像透過把神聖力量賦予人形來使用擬人象徵。"},{"en":"Anthropomorphic symbolism means representing non-human power or ideas in human form.","zh":"anthropomorphic symbolism 指用人類形態表現非人力量或想法。"},{"en":"A cartoon sun with a smiling face uses anthropomorphic symbolism.","zh":"有笑臉的卡通太陽使用擬人象徵。"},{"en":"If sacred power is shown as a human body, people may relate to it more easily.","zh":"如果神聖力量以人體呈現，人們可能更容易理解它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes human-shaped symbolic meaning.","zh":"這個片語描述人形化的象徵意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"symbols of authority and power","meaning":"權威與力量的象徵","examples":[{"en":"The statues were symbols of both authority and power.","zh":"這些石像是權威與力量的象徵。"},{"en":"Symbols of authority and power are objects that represent leadership, control, or status.","zh":"symbols of authority and power 是代表領導、控制或地位的物件。"},{"en":"A crown can be a symbol of authority and power.","zh":"王冠可以是權威與力量的象徵。"},{"en":"If a monument represents rulers, it may strengthen their public image.","zh":"如果紀念物代表統治者，它可能強化他們的公眾形象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes objects that show social dominance.","zh":"這個片語描述顯示社會主導地位的物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not only symbols","meaning":"不只是象徵","examples":[{"en":"To the islanders, the statues were not only symbols.","zh":"對島民而言，這些石像不只是象徵。"},{"en":"Not only symbols means they represented ideas but also had another role.","zh":"not only symbols 指它們代表想法，但也有另一種作用。"},{"en":"A wedding ring is not only a symbol; it can also carry personal memory.","zh":"婚戒不只是象徵，也可以承載個人記憶。"},{"en":"If objects are sacred, people may treat them as powerful, not merely decorative.","zh":"如果物件是神聖的，人們可能把它們視為有力量，而不只是裝飾。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that meaning goes beyond representation.","zh":"這個片語顯示意義超越單純代表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"repositories of sacred spirit","meaning":"神聖力量的載體","examples":[{"en":"The moai were viewed as repositories of sacred spirit.","zh":"摩艾石像被視為神聖力量的載體。"},{"en":"Repositories of sacred spirit are objects believed to hold holy or spiritual power.","zh":"repositories of sacred spirit 是被相信承載神聖或靈性力量的物件。"},{"en":"A sacred relic may be treated as a repository of spiritual meaning.","zh":"聖物可能被視為精神意義的載體。"},{"en":"If people believe an object contains spirit, they may protect it through ritual.","zh":"如果人們相信物件含有靈力，他們可能透過儀式保護它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sacred objects as containers of power.","zh":"這個片語把神聖物件描述為力量容器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ancient Polynesian religions","meaning":"古代波利尼西亞宗教","examples":[{"en":"Sacred objects played an important role in ancient Polynesian religions.","zh":"神聖物件在古代波利尼西亞宗教中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"Ancient Polynesian religions were belief systems practised by early Polynesian peoples.","zh":"ancient Polynesian religions 是早期波利尼西亞民族實踐的信仰系統。"},{"en":"These religions could include ancestors, spirits, sacred places, and ritual objects.","zh":"這些宗教可包括祖先、靈體、聖地和儀式物件。"},{"en":"If statues belonged to such beliefs, their meaning was religious as well as artistic.","zh":"如果石像屬於這類信仰，其意義既是宗教的，也是藝術的。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to older Pacific Island belief systems.","zh":"這個片語指較古老的太平洋島嶼信仰系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"properly fashioned","meaning":"經適當製作的","examples":[{"en":"An object had to be properly fashioned before ritual use.","zh":"物件在儀式使用前必須經適當製作。"},{"en":"Properly fashioned means made in the correct shape, style, or method.","zh":"properly fashioned 指以正確形狀、風格或方法製成。"},{"en":"A ceremony costume must be properly fashioned before it is worn in public.","zh":"儀式服裝在公開穿着前必須適當製作。"},{"en":"If sacred objects are made incorrectly, people may not consider them ritually valid.","zh":"如果神聖物件製作不正確，人們可能不視其為具儀式效力。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses correct preparation.","zh":"這個片語強調正確準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ritually prepared","meaning":"經儀式處理的","examples":[{"en":"The sacred objects were ritually prepared.","zh":"這些神聖物件經儀式處理。"},{"en":"Ritually prepared means made ready through religious or ceremonial actions.","zh":"ritually prepared 指透過宗教或儀式行動準備好。"},{"en":"A temple object may be ritually prepared before an important festival.","zh":"廟宇物件可能在重要節日前經儀式處理。"},{"en":"If an item is ritually prepared, people may treat it as more than ordinary material.","zh":"如果物件經儀式處理，人們可能把它視為不只是普通材料。"},{"en":"This phrase connects preparation with ceremony.","zh":"這個片語把準備與儀式連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be believed to be charged by","meaning":"被認為注入了……","examples":[{"en":"The objects were believed to be charged by a spiritual essence.","zh":"這些物件被認為注入了一種精神力量。"},{"en":"To be believed to be charged by something means people thought it was filled with that power.","zh":"be believed to be charged by something 指人們相信某物充滿那種力量。"},{"en":"A sacred stone may be believed to be charged by ancestral energy.","zh":"神聖石頭可能被認為注入了祖先能量。"},{"en":"If people believe an object is spiritually charged, they may handle it carefully.","zh":"如果人們相信物件被靈力注入，他們可能小心處理它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a belief about spiritual power entering an object.","zh":"這個片語描述靈性力量進入物件的信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"spiritual essence","meaning":"精神力量；靈性能量","examples":[{"en":"The islanders believed that sacred objects contained a spiritual essence.","zh":"島民相信神聖物件含有精神力量。"},{"en":"Spiritual essence means an invisible sacred force or inner spirit.","zh":"spiritual essence 指不可見的神聖力量或內在靈性。"},{"en":"Some communities believe old family objects carry spiritual essence from ancestors.","zh":"一些社群相信舊家庭物件帶有祖先的精神力量。"},{"en":"If an object is thought to contain spiritual essence, it may be used in ritual.","zh":"如果物件被認為含有靈性能量，它可能用於儀式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to non-physical sacred power.","zh":"這個片語指非物質的神聖力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"mana","meaning":"瑪納；神聖靈力","examples":[{"en":"Mana was regarded as a magical spiritual force.","zh":"瑪納被視為一種神奇的精神力量。"},{"en":"Mana is a sacred spiritual power in many Polynesian belief systems.","zh":"mana 是許多波利尼西亞信仰系統中的神聖靈力。"},{"en":"A leader may be believed to possess mana through ancestry or achievement.","zh":"領袖可能被認為透過血統或成就擁有瑪納。"},{"en":"If an object holds mana, people may treat it with respect and fear.","zh":"如果物件含有瑪納，人們可能以尊敬和敬畏態度對待它。"},{"en":"This word names an important Polynesian spiritual concept.","zh":"這個詞指出重要的波利尼西亞靈性概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sanctuaries","meaning":"聖所","examples":[{"en":"The ahu platforms served as sanctuaries for the people.","zh":"阿胡石台為人們發揮聖所的作用。"},{"en":"Sanctuaries are sacred or protected places.","zh":"sanctuaries 是神聖或受保護的地方。"},{"en":"A temple may serve as a sanctuary for prayer and quiet reflection.","zh":"廟宇可作為祈禱和安靜反思的聖所。"},{"en":"If a platform is a sanctuary, people may gather there for ritual purposes.","zh":"如果平台是聖所，人們可能聚集在那裡進行儀式。"},{"en":"This word suggests protection and holiness.","zh":"這個詞暗示保護和神聖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ritually charged objects","meaning":"經儀式注入力量的物件","examples":[{"en":"The moai were ritually charged sacred objects.","zh":"摩艾是經儀式注入力量的神聖物件。"},{"en":"Ritually charged objects are items believed to contain power through ceremony.","zh":"ritually charged objects 是被相信透過儀式含有力量的物件。"},{"en":"A ceremonial mask may be treated as ritually charged after a blessing.","zh":"儀式面具在祝福後可能被視為經儀式注入力量的物件。"},{"en":"If people believe an object is charged, it may not be used casually.","zh":"如果人們相信物件被注入力量，它可能不會被隨便使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sacred objects empowered by ritual.","zh":"這個片語描述透過儀式獲得力量的神聖物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"besides its better-known name","meaning":"除了較廣為人知的名稱外","examples":[{"en":"Besides its better-known name, the island has several ancient names.","zh":"除了較廣為人知的名稱外，該島還有幾個古名。"},{"en":"Besides its better-known name means apart from the name most people recognise.","zh":"besides its better-known name 指除了大多數人認得的名稱之外。"},{"en":"Besides its official name, a city may have an old local nickname.","zh":"除了官方名稱外，一個城市可能有舊本地暱稱。"},{"en":"If a place has several names, each may reveal a different part of its history.","zh":"如果地方有幾個名稱，每個名稱都可能揭示其歷史的不同部分。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces additional names.","zh":"這個片語引入其他名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"also be known as","meaning":"又稱為","examples":[{"en":"Easter Island is also known as Te-Pito-O-Te-Henua.","zh":"復活節島又稱為 Te-Pito-O-Te-Henua。"},{"en":"To also be known as means to have another name.","zh":"also be known as 指另有一個名稱。"},{"en":"New York City is also known as the Big Apple.","zh":"紐約市又稱為大蘋果。"},{"en":"If a place has different names, people from different cultures may use different terms.","zh":"如果一個地方有不同名稱，不同文化的人可能使用不同說法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an alternative name.","zh":"這個片語引入另一個名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the Navel of the World","meaning":"世界的肚臍；世界中心","examples":[{"en":"Te-Pito-O-Te-Henua means “The Navel of the World”.","zh":"Te-Pito-O-Te-Henua 意思是「世界的肚臍」。"},{"en":"The Navel of the World is a symbolic name suggesting a central or sacred place.","zh":"the Navel of the World 是象徵名稱，暗示某地是中心或神聖之處。"},{"en":"A culture may call its homeland the centre of the world to express importance.","zh":"一種文化可能稱自己的家園為世界中心，以表達重要性。"},{"en":"If a name suggests centrality, later writers may build theories around it.","zh":"如果名稱暗示中心地位，後來作家可能圍繞它建立理論。"},{"en":"This phrase carries mythological and symbolic meaning.","zh":"這個片語帶有神話和象徵意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Eyes Looking at Heaven","meaning":"望向天空的眼睛","examples":[{"en":"Mata-Ki-Te-Rani means “Eyes Looking at Heaven”.","zh":"Mata-Ki-Te-Rani 意思是「望向天空的眼睛」。"},{"en":"Eyes Looking at Heaven is a poetic name suggesting upward sight or spiritual attention.","zh":"Eyes Looking at Heaven 是詩意名稱，暗示向上觀看或靈性關注。"},{"en":"A temple name may refer to heaven to show religious meaning.","zh":"廟宇名稱可能提到天空，以顯示宗教意義。"},{"en":"If a place name mentions the sky, some writers may connect it with astronomy.","zh":"如果地名提到天空，一些作家可能把它與天文學連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds symbolic rather than purely geographical.","zh":"這個片語聽起來具象徵意味，而不只是地理名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a host of","meaning":"大量；許多","examples":[{"en":"A host of mythological details has inspired alternative theories.","zh":"大量神話細節啟發了另類理論。"},{"en":"A host of means a large number of something.","zh":"a host of 指大量某事物。"},{"en":"A school fair may include a host of games, food stalls, and performances.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能包括許多遊戲、食物攤位和表演。"},{"en":"If a topic has many details, writers may create many interpretations.","zh":"如果一個主題有許多細節，作家可能創造許多詮釋。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses quantity and variety.","zh":"這個片語強調數量和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"mythological details","meaning":"神話細節","examples":[{"en":"Some writers focus on the island’s mythological details.","zh":"一些作家聚焦於該島的神話細節。"},{"en":"Mythological details are parts of stories, names, or beliefs connected with myths.","zh":"mythological details 是與神話相關的故事、名稱或信仰細節。"},{"en":"A legend about a mountain spirit contains mythological details.","zh":"關於山神的傳說包含神話細節。"},{"en":"If writers focus only on myths, they may ignore archaeological evidence.","zh":"如果作家只聚焦神話，可能忽視考古證據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to story-based symbolic information.","zh":"這個片語指以故事為基礎的象徵資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"mainstream archaeologists","meaning":"主流考古學家","examples":[{"en":"Mainstream archaeologists generally reject the more speculative claims.","zh":"主流考古學家一般拒絕較具猜測性的說法。"},{"en":"Mainstream archaeologists are scholars who follow accepted evidence-based methods in archaeology.","zh":"mainstream archaeologists 是遵循考古學中受認可、以證據為本方法的學者。"},{"en":"Mainstream archaeologists rely on dates, artefacts, bones, and site analysis.","zh":"主流考古學家依靠年代、文物、骨骼和遺址分析。"},{"en":"If a theory lacks evidence, mainstream archaeologists may reject it.","zh":"如果理論缺乏證據，主流考古學家可能否定它。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts established scholarship with fringe claims.","zh":"這個片語把既有學術與邊緣說法作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"point to the possibility that","meaning":"顯示……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"Some writers claim the ancient names point to the possibility of a scientific function.","zh":"一些作家聲稱古名顯示其具有科學功能的可能性。"},{"en":"To point to the possibility that means to suggest that something may be true.","zh":"point to the possibility that 指暗示某事可能是真的。"},{"en":"A student’s repeated mistakes may point to the possibility that the grammar was not understood.","zh":"學生反覆犯錯可能顯示他沒有理解文法的可能性。"},{"en":"If evidence only points to a possibility, it does not prove the claim.","zh":"如果證據只是顯示可能性，它並未證明主張。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses cautious suggestion.","zh":"這個片語表達謹慎暗示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"geodetic marker","meaning":"大地測量標記","examples":[{"en":"The island has been described by some writers as a geodetic marker.","zh":"一些作家把該島描述為大地測量標記。"},{"en":"A geodetic marker is a point used for measuring positions on Earth.","zh":"geodetic marker 是用來測量地球位置的點。"},{"en":"Surveyors may use markers to map land accurately.","zh":"測量員可能使用標記來準確繪製土地。"},{"en":"If a site is claimed to be a geodetic marker, the claim needs strong measurement evidence.","zh":"如果某遺址被聲稱是大地測量標記，該說法需要有力測量證據。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to surveying and mapping.","zh":"這個片語屬於測量和製圖領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"astronomical observatory","meaning":"天文觀測站","examples":[{"en":"Some alternative theories describe the island as an astronomical observatory.","zh":"一些另類理論把該島描述為天文觀測站。"},{"en":"An astronomical observatory is a place used to observe stars, planets, or the sky.","zh":"astronomical observatory 是用來觀察星星、行星或天空的地方。"},{"en":"A school may visit an observatory to look through telescopes.","zh":"學校可能參觀天文觀測站，用望遠鏡觀星。"},{"en":"If ancient buildings align with stars, researchers may consider astronomical use.","zh":"如果古建築與星體排列一致，研究人員可能考慮天文用途。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a site for studying the heavens.","zh":"這個片語描述研究天象的地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"long-forgotten civilization","meaning":"被遺忘已久的文明","examples":[{"en":"The theory refers to a long-forgotten ancient civilization.","zh":"該理論提及一個被遺忘已久的古代文明。"},{"en":"A long-forgotten civilization is a society from the distant past that people no longer remember clearly.","zh":"long-forgotten civilization 是來自遙遠過去、已不被清楚記得的社會。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may uncover ruins from a long-forgotten civilization.","zh":"考古學家可能發掘出被遺忘已久文明的遺跡。"},{"en":"If a civilization is forgotten, stories about it may mix fact with imagination.","zh":"如果文明被遺忘，關於它的故事可能混合事實與想像。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests mystery and lost history.","zh":"這個片語暗示神秘感和失落歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"scientific outpost","meaning":"科學前哨站","examples":[{"en":"One writer suggested that the island was a scientific outpost.","zh":"一名作家提出該島是一個科學前哨站。"},{"en":"A scientific outpost is a distant place used for research or observation.","zh":"scientific outpost 是用於研究或觀察的偏遠地點。"},{"en":"An Antarctic research station can be called a scientific outpost.","zh":"南極研究站可被稱為科學前哨站。"},{"en":"If a remote island were an outpost, people would expect evidence of organised study.","zh":"如果偏遠島嶼是前哨站，人們會期望找到有組織研究的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a remote research base.","zh":"這個片語描述偏遠研究基地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"antediluvian civilization","meaning":"大洪水前的古代文明","examples":[{"en":"The proposed civilization is described as antediluvian.","zh":"該假設文明被描述為大洪水前的文明。"},{"en":"Antediluvian civilization means a civilisation imagined as existing before a great ancient flood.","zh":"antediluvian civilization 指被想像為存在於古代大洪水之前的文明。"},{"en":"Some myths speak of antediluvian worlds destroyed by disaster.","zh":"一些神話談及被災難毀滅的大洪水前世界。"},{"en":"If a theory uses antediluvian claims, historians need strong evidence before accepting it.","zh":"如果理論使用大洪水前文明的說法，歷史學家接受前需要有力證據。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds ancient, speculative, and mythic.","zh":"這個片語聽起來古老、具猜測性和神話色彩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"extreme importance","meaning":"極其重要","examples":[{"en":"The island’s location supposedly had extreme importance.","zh":"該島的位置據稱極其重要。"},{"en":"Extreme importance means very great significance.","zh":"extreme importance 指非常重大的意義。"},{"en":"A hospital’s location has extreme importance during an emergency.","zh":"醫院位置在緊急情況中極其重要。"},{"en":"If a site’s position matters greatly, people may build theories around its location.","zh":"如果遺址位置非常重要，人們可能圍繞其位置建立理論。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses strong importance.","zh":"這個片語強調高度重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"planet-spanning","meaning":"橫跨全球的","examples":[{"en":"The theory proposes a planet-spanning system of sacred sites.","zh":"該理論提出一個橫跨全球的神聖遺址系統。"},{"en":"Planet-spanning means extending across the whole world.","zh":"planet-spanning 指延伸至整個世界。"},{"en":"The Internet is a planet-spanning communication network.","zh":"互聯網是一個橫跨全球的通訊網絡。"},{"en":"If a theory claims a planet-spanning system, it needs evidence from many regions.","zh":"如果理論聲稱有橫跨全球的系統，就需要來自許多地區的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes global scale.","zh":"這個片語描述全球規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"mathematically precise grid","meaning":"數學上精確的網格","examples":[{"en":"The proposed sites formed a mathematically precise grid.","zh":"這些被提出的遺址形成數學上精確的網格。"},{"en":"A mathematically precise grid is a pattern arranged with exact numerical spacing or alignment.","zh":"mathematically precise grid 是以精確數字間距或排列組成的圖案。"},{"en":"City planners may design streets in a grid with equal distances.","zh":"城市規劃師可能設計間距相等的街道網格。"},{"en":"If sites form a precise grid by chance, researchers must test the claim carefully.","zh":"如果遺址偶然形成精確網格，研究人員必須仔細測試該說法。"},{"en":"This phrase combines mathematics with spatial arrangement.","zh":"這個片語結合數學和空間排列。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sacred sites","meaning":"神聖遺址","examples":[{"en":"The theory links Easter Island with other sacred sites around the world.","zh":"該理論把復活節島與世界其他神聖遺址連繫起來。"},{"en":"Sacred sites are places considered holy or spiritually important.","zh":"sacred sites 是被視為神聖或具靈性重要性的地方。"},{"en":"Temples, burial grounds, and pilgrimage routes can be sacred sites.","zh":"廟宇、墓地和朝聖路線都可以是神聖遺址。"},{"en":"If a place is sacred, people may protect it through rituals and rules.","zh":"如果一個地方神聖，人們可能透過儀式和規則保護它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to religiously meaningful places.","zh":"這個片語指具有宗教意義的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"alternative scholars","meaning":"非主流學者","examples":[{"en":"Alternative scholars have proposed non-mainstream explanations.","zh":"非主流學者提出了非主流解釋。"},{"en":"Alternative scholars are writers or researchers outside the accepted academic mainstream.","zh":"alternative scholars 是位於受認可學術主流以外的作家或研究者。"},{"en":"Alternative scholars may ask interesting questions but still need reliable evidence.","zh":"非主流學者可能提出有趣問題，但仍需要可靠證據。"},{"en":"If a theory is non-mainstream, experts examine its methods carefully.","zh":"如果理論屬非主流，專家會仔細檢查其方法。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with mainstream academic researchers.","zh":"這個片語與主流學術研究者作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"extensively study","meaning":"廣泛研究","examples":[{"en":"Some writers have extensively studied the locations of the proposed markers.","zh":"一些作家廣泛研究了被提出標記的位置。"},{"en":"To extensively study something means to examine it in great detail and range.","zh":"extensively study something 指詳細而廣泛地研究某事。"},{"en":"A student may extensively study past papers before a major exam.","zh":"學生可能在大型考試前廣泛研究歷屆試題。"},{"en":"If a topic is studied extensively, many details and patterns may appear.","zh":"如果主題被廣泛研究，許多細節和模式可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep and wide study.","zh":"這個片語描述深入而廣泛的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"possible function","meaning":"可能的功能","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have debated the possible function of ancient structures.","zh":"研究人員一直爭論古代建築的可能功能。"},{"en":"Possible function means what something may have been used for.","zh":"possible function 指某物可能曾用來做甚麼。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may debate the possible function of a strange stone circle.","zh":"考古學家可能爭論奇怪石圈的可能功能。"},{"en":"If an object’s use is unclear, scholars compare it with similar finds.","zh":"如果物件用途不清楚，學者會把它與相似發現比較。"},{"en":"This phrase shows uncertainty about purpose.","zh":"這個片語顯示對用途的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"global network of","meaning":"全球……網絡","examples":[{"en":"The theory proposes a global network of observatories.","zh":"該理論提出一個全球觀測站網絡。"},{"en":"A global network of something means connected examples spread around the world.","zh":"global network of something 指分布世界各地並互相連接的事物。"},{"en":"Universities may form a global network of researchers.","zh":"大學可能組成全球研究人員網絡。"},{"en":"If sites form a global network, there should be clear links between them.","zh":"如果遺址形成全球網絡，它們之間應有清楚連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes worldwide connection.","zh":"這個片語描述世界範圍的連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sophisticated astronomical observatories","meaning":"先進的天文觀測站","examples":[{"en":"The writers imagined a network of sophisticated astronomical observatories.","zh":"這些作家想像有一個先進天文觀測站網絡。"},{"en":"Sophisticated astronomical observatories are advanced places for studying the sky.","zh":"sophisticated astronomical observatories 是用於研究天空的先進場所。"},{"en":"Modern observatories use powerful telescopes and computers.","zh":"現代天文觀測站使用強大望遠鏡和電腦。"},{"en":"If ancient observatories were sophisticated, their builders needed strong astronomical knowledge.","zh":"如果古代觀測站很先進，建造者需要強大的天文知識。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests advanced scientific structures.","zh":"這個片語暗示先進科學建築。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be dedicated to","meaning":"專門用作……","examples":[{"en":"The proposed observatories were supposedly dedicated to predicting disasters.","zh":"這些假設觀測站據稱專門用作預測災難。"},{"en":"To be dedicated to something means to be used mainly for that purpose.","zh":"be dedicated to something 指主要用於某目的。"},{"en":"A hospital wing may be dedicated to children’s care.","zh":"醫院一翼可能專門用作兒童護理。"},{"en":"If a building is dedicated to research, its design should support that work.","zh":"如果建築專門用作研究，其設計應支援那項工作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows main purpose or devotion.","zh":"這個片語顯示主要目的或專注投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"predict and prepare for","meaning":"預測並為……作準備","examples":[{"en":"The network was allegedly used to predict and prepare for future disasters.","zh":"該網絡據稱用來預測並為未來災難作準備。"},{"en":"To predict and prepare for something means to forecast it and get ready for it.","zh":"predict and prepare for something 指預測某事並為其做好準備。"},{"en":"Governments predict and prepare for typhoons by issuing warnings and opening shelters.","zh":"政府透過發出警告和開放庇護中心來預測並為颱風作準備。"},{"en":"If people can predict danger, preparation may reduce damage.","zh":"如果人們能預測危險，準備工作可能減少損害。"},{"en":"This phrase combines warning with action.","zh":"這個片語結合預警和行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cometary impacts","meaning":"彗星撞擊","examples":[{"en":"The theory refers to the danger of future cometary impacts.","zh":"該理論提及未來彗星撞擊的危險。"},{"en":"Cometary impacts are collisions between comets and planets or moons.","zh":"cometary impacts 是彗星與行星或月球之間的撞擊。"},{"en":"Scientists study space rocks to estimate the risk of future impacts.","zh":"科學家研究太空岩石，以估計未來撞擊風險。"},{"en":"If a large comet struck Earth, the damage could be catastrophic.","zh":"如果大型彗星撞擊地球，損害可能是災難性的。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a space-related disaster.","zh":"這個片語指與太空相關的災難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"crustal displacement","meaning":"地殼移位","examples":[{"en":"Some writers predicted disasters involving crustal displacement.","zh":"一些作家預測涉及地殼移位的災難。"},{"en":"Crustal displacement means movement of Earth’s outer layer.","zh":"crustal displacement 指地球外層的移動。"},{"en":"Earthquakes involve movement in parts of the Earth’s crust.","zh":"地震涉及地殼部分的移動。"},{"en":"If crustal displacement were sudden and large, it could cause major destruction.","zh":"如果地殼移位突然且巨大，可能造成重大破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dramatic geological movement.","zh":"這個片語描述劇烈地質移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cataclysms","meaning":"大災難","examples":[{"en":"The observatories were allegedly intended to predict major cataclysms.","zh":"這些觀測站據稱是用來預測重大災難。"},{"en":"Cataclysms are sudden, violent disasters causing great destruction.","zh":"cataclysms 是突然、猛烈並造成巨大破壞的災難。"},{"en":"A huge volcanic eruption can be a cataclysm for nearby communities.","zh":"大型火山爆發可成為附近社群的大災難。"},{"en":"If people fear cataclysms, they may build myths about warning systems.","zh":"如果人們害怕大災難，可能建立關於預警系統的神話。"},{"en":"This word describes extreme disasters.","zh":"這個詞描述極端災難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in the latter years of","meaning":"在……的後期","examples":[{"en":"Various theories appeared in the latter years of the twentieth century.","zh":"各種理論出現在二十世紀後期。"},{"en":"In the latter years of a period means during the later part of it.","zh":"in the latter years of a period 指在某段時期的較後部分。"},{"en":"In the latter years of school, students prepare more seriously for exams.","zh":"在學校生活後期，學生更認真準備考試。"},{"en":"If theories appear late in a century, they reflect the debates of that time.","zh":"如果理論出現在世紀後期，它們反映當時的爭論。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the later stage of a period.","zh":"這個片語標示某時期的後段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"advance a theory","meaning":"提出理論","examples":[{"en":"Several writers advanced theories about Easter Island’s decline.","zh":"幾位作家提出了關於復活節島衰落的理論。"},{"en":"To advance a theory means to propose it publicly or seriously.","zh":"advance a theory 指公開或認真提出一項理論。"},{"en":"A scientist may advance a theory after gathering unusual evidence.","zh":"科學家可能在收集到不尋常證據後提出理論。"},{"en":"If a theory is advanced without enough evidence, others may challenge it.","zh":"如果理論在證據不足下被提出，其他人可能挑戰它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes putting forward an explanation.","zh":"這個片語描述提出解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rapid decline","meaning":"急速衰落","examples":[{"en":"Writers have debated the reasons for the civilization’s rapid decline.","zh":"作家一直爭論該文明急速衰落的原因。"},{"en":"Rapid decline means a fast fall in strength, population, wealth, or condition.","zh":"rapid decline 指力量、人口、財富或狀況快速下降。"},{"en":"A shop may experience rapid decline after a large competitor opens nearby.","zh":"大型競爭者在附近開業後，小店可能急速衰落。"},{"en":"If food becomes scarce, a society’s health and population may decline quickly.","zh":"如果食物變得稀缺，社會健康和人口可能迅速下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sudden weakening.","zh":"這個片語描述突然衰弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"around the time of","meaning":"大約在……的時候","examples":[{"en":"The decline occurred around the time of early European contact.","zh":"衰落大約發生在早期歐洲人接觸的時候。"},{"en":"Around the time of means near the same period as an event.","zh":"around the time of 指接近某事件發生的同一時期。"},{"en":"A child may move house around the time of starting secondary school.","zh":"孩子可能大約在升讀中學的時候搬家。"},{"en":"If two events happen around the same time, researchers may examine possible links.","zh":"如果兩件事大約同時發生，研究人員可能檢視可能關聯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives approximate timing.","zh":"這個片語給出大約時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"initial European contact","meaning":"歐洲人首次接觸","examples":[{"en":"European contact had major consequences for the islanders.","zh":"歐洲人接觸對島民造成重大後果。"},{"en":"Initial European contact means the first period when Europeans met or reached a place.","zh":"initial European contact 指歐洲人首次遇到或到達某地的時期。"},{"en":"Initial contact between travellers and local people can change trade, disease, and power relations.","zh":"旅人與本地人首次接觸可以改變貿易、疾病和權力關係。"},{"en":"If contact brings disease or violence, local societies may suffer greatly.","zh":"如果接觸帶來疾病或暴力，本地社會可能深受其害。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to first encounters with Europeans.","zh":"這個片語指與歐洲人的首次相遇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"principal among","meaning":"其中最主要的是","examples":[{"en":"Principal among the theories was the environmental-collapse explanation.","zh":"其中最主要的是環境崩潰解釋。"},{"en":"Principal among means the most important among several things.","zh":"principal among 指在幾件事之中最重要。"},{"en":"Principal among the school’s concerns was student safety.","zh":"學校最主要的關注是學生安全。"},{"en":"If one theory is principal among many, it receives the most attention.","zh":"如果某理論是眾多理論中最主要的，它會得到最多注意。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the leading item in a group.","zh":"這個片語突出群體中的主要項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"postulate a theory","meaning":"提出一項假說","examples":[{"en":"Jared Diamond postulated a theory of ecological collapse.","zh":"Jared Diamond 提出了一項生態崩潰假說。"},{"en":"To postulate a theory means to propose it as an explanation.","zh":"postulate a theory 指提出某理論作為解釋。"},{"en":"A researcher may postulate a theory before testing it with data.","zh":"研究人員可能先提出假說，再用數據測試。"},{"en":"If a theory is postulated, it still needs evidence and debate.","zh":"如果假說被提出，它仍需要證據和討論。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and common in academic writing.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常見於學術寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"initial colonization","meaning":"最初殖民定居","examples":[{"en":"The theory begins several centuries after the island’s initial colonization.","zh":"該理論始於該島最初殖民定居後數個世紀。"},{"en":"Initial colonization means the first settlement of a place by newcomers.","zh":"initial colonization 指外來者最早在某地定居。"},{"en":"Initial colonization of an island often depends on boats, food, and safe landing places.","zh":"島嶼最初殖民定居通常取決於船隻、食物和安全登陸點。"},{"en":"If colonization succeeds, population and culture may grow over time.","zh":"如果定居成功，人口和文化可能隨時間增長。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the earliest settlement stage.","zh":"這個片語指最早定居階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"resource needs","meaning":"資源需求","examples":[{"en":"The growing population’s resource needs increased over time.","zh":"不斷增長的人口資源需求隨時間增加。"},{"en":"Resource needs are the food, water, wood, land, and materials people require.","zh":"resource needs 是人們所需的食物、水、木材、土地和材料。"},{"en":"A growing school has greater resource needs, such as classrooms and teachers.","zh":"不斷擴大的學校有更大資源需求，例如課室和老師。"},{"en":"If resource needs exceed supply, conflict or shortage may occur.","zh":"如果資源需求超過供應，就可能出現衝突或短缺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes necessary materials for survival or operation.","zh":"這個片語描述生存或運作所需材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"outpace the capacity of","meaning":"超出……的能力","examples":[{"en":"Human demand began to outpace the island’s capacity to recover.","zh":"人類需求開始超出該島恢復的能力。"},{"en":"To outpace the capacity of something means to grow faster than it can handle or renew.","zh":"outpace the capacity of something 指增長速度超過某物能承受或恢復的能力。"},{"en":"A hospital’s patient numbers may outpace its capacity if many staff are absent.","zh":"如果許多員工缺勤，醫院病人數量可能超出其應付能力。"},{"en":"If demand outpaces recovery, natural resources can become depleted.","zh":"如果需求超過恢復速度，自然資源可能被耗盡。"},{"en":"This phrase shows pressure exceeding limits.","zh":"這個片語顯示壓力超越限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"renew itself ecologically","meaning":"在生態上自我恢復","examples":[{"en":"The island could no longer renew itself ecologically.","zh":"該島再也不能在生態上自我恢復。"},{"en":"To renew itself ecologically means for an environment to restore its plants, soil, water, and wildlife naturally.","zh":"renew itself ecologically 指環境自然恢復植物、土壤、水和野生動物。"},{"en":"A forest can renew itself ecologically if young trees grow after old trees fall.","zh":"如果老樹倒下後幼樹生長，森林便能在生態上自我恢復。"},{"en":"If people remove resources faster than nature restores them, renewal fails.","zh":"如果人類取走資源快過自然恢復速度，自我恢復就會失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes natural environmental recovery.","zh":"這個片語描述自然環境恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be entirely cut down","meaning":"被完全砍伐","examples":[{"en":"According to the theory, the forests were entirely cut down.","zh":"根據該理論，森林被完全砍伐。"},{"en":"To be entirely cut down means all trees were felled or removed.","zh":"be entirely cut down 指所有樹木被砍倒或移除。"},{"en":"A hillside may be entirely cut down to make room for construction.","zh":"山坡可能被完全砍伐，以騰出地方建設。"},{"en":"If forests are entirely cut down, soil erosion and wildlife loss may follow.","zh":"如果森林被完全砍伐，土壤侵蝕和野生動物消失可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete deforestation.","zh":"這個片語描述完全砍伐森林。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ground cover","meaning":"地被植物","examples":[{"en":"The island’s rich ground cover gradually disappeared.","zh":"該島豐富的地被植物逐漸消失。"},{"en":"Ground cover is the low vegetation that covers soil.","zh":"ground cover 是覆蓋土壤的低矮植被。"},{"en":"Grass, moss, and small plants can form ground cover in a garden.","zh":"草、苔蘚和小植物可以在花園中形成地被植物。"},{"en":"If ground cover disappears, rain and wind can erode the soil more easily.","zh":"如果地被植物消失，雨水和風更容易侵蝕土壤。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to protective low plant growth.","zh":"這個片語指保護性的低矮植物覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"erode away","meaning":"被侵蝕殆盡","examples":[{"en":"The fertile ground cover eventually eroded away.","zh":"肥沃的地被植物最終被侵蝕殆盡。"},{"en":"To erode away means to be gradually worn away by wind, water, or other forces.","zh":"erode away 指被風、水或其他力量逐漸磨走。"},{"en":"A beach may erode away after repeated storms.","zh":"海灘可能在反覆風暴後被侵蝕殆盡。"},{"en":"If soil erodes away, farming becomes harder.","zh":"如果土壤被侵蝕，耕作會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow loss through natural forces.","zh":"這個片語描述透過自然力量逐漸流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"springs dry up","meaning":"泉水乾涸","examples":[{"en":"The theory states that the island’s springs dried up.","zh":"該理論指出島上的泉水乾涸。"},{"en":"When springs dry up, natural water sources stop flowing.","zh":"springs dry up 指天然水源停止流動。"},{"en":"A village may suffer if its springs dry up during a long drought.","zh":"如果村莊泉水在長期乾旱中乾涸，居民可能受苦。"},{"en":"If water sources disappear, farming and daily life become difficult.","zh":"如果水源消失，耕作和日常生活會變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes loss of natural freshwater.","zh":"這個片語描述天然淡水流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"vast flocks of birds","meaning":"大群鳥類","examples":[{"en":"Vast flocks of seabirds once came to the island.","zh":"大群海鳥曾來到該島。"},{"en":"Vast flocks of birds are very large groups of birds.","zh":"vast flocks of birds 是非常大量聚在一起的鳥群。"},{"en":"Vast flocks of birds may cover the sky during migration season.","zh":"遷徙季節，大群鳥類可能遮蔽天空。"},{"en":"If flocks disappear, people may lose an important food source.","zh":"如果鳥群消失，人們可能失去重要食物來源。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses large numbers of birds together.","zh":"這個片語強調大量鳥類聚集。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"come to roost","meaning":"前來棲息","examples":[{"en":"Birds came to roost and breed on Easter Island.","zh":"鳥類前來復活節島棲息和繁殖。"},{"en":"To come to roost means to arrive at a place to rest or sleep.","zh":"come to roost 指到某地休息或睡覺。"},{"en":"Birds may come to roost in trees near a village at sunset.","zh":"黃昏時，鳥類可能前來村莊附近的樹上棲息。"},{"en":"If birds regularly roost in one place, that place becomes ecologically important.","zh":"如果鳥類定期在某地棲息，該地在生態上就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes birds settling to rest.","zh":"這個片語描述鳥類停留休息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"with no logs to","meaning":"由於沒有木材去……","examples":[{"en":"With no logs to build canoes, offshore fishing became difficult.","zh":"由於沒有木材去建造獨木舟，離岸捕魚變得困難。"},{"en":"With no logs to do something means lacking the wood needed for that purpose.","zh":"with no logs to do something 指缺乏做某事所需木材。"},{"en":"With no paper to print worksheets, a teacher may use the board instead.","zh":"由於沒有紙張去印工作紙，老師可能改用黑板。"},{"en":"If people lack materials, an important activity may become impossible.","zh":"如果人們缺乏材料，重要活動可能變得不可能。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how missing resources limit action.","zh":"這個片語顯示資源不足如何限制行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"build canoes","meaning":"建造獨木舟","examples":[{"en":"Islanders needed timber to build canoes for fishing.","zh":"島民需要木材建造獨木舟捕魚。"},{"en":"To build canoes means to make small narrow boats, often from wood.","zh":"build canoes 指製作細長小船，通常用木材製成。"},{"en":"A coastal community may build canoes for transport and fishing.","zh":"沿海社群可能建造獨木舟用於交通和捕魚。"},{"en":"If trees disappear, people may lose the wood needed for boats.","zh":"如果樹木消失，人們可能失去造船所需木材。"},{"en":"This phrase connects wood, transport, and sea use.","zh":"這個片語連接木材、交通和海洋使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"offshore fishing","meaning":"離岸捕魚","examples":[{"en":"Canoes were essential for offshore fishing.","zh":"獨木舟對離岸捕魚至關重要。"},{"en":"Offshore fishing is fishing in the sea away from the shore.","zh":"offshore fishing 是在離岸較遠海域捕魚。"},{"en":"Fishermen need boats and safety equipment for offshore fishing.","zh":"漁民進行離岸捕魚需要船隻和安全設備。"},{"en":"If people cannot build boats, offshore fishing becomes much harder.","zh":"如果人們不能造船，離岸捕魚會困難得多。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts deep-water fishing with near-shore fishing.","zh":"這個片語把深水捕魚與近岸捕魚作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"depleted food sources","meaning":"被耗盡的食物來源","examples":[{"en":"Bird and wildlife food sources became depleted.","zh":"鳥類和野生動物食物來源被耗盡。"},{"en":"Depleted food sources are food supplies that have been used up or greatly reduced.","zh":"depleted food sources 是已被用盡或大幅減少的食物供應。"},{"en":"A lake’s fish may become depleted after years of overfishing.","zh":"湖中的魚類可能在多年過度捕撈後被耗盡。"},{"en":"If food sources are depleted, people and animals may face hunger.","zh":"如果食物來源被耗盡，人和動物可能面臨飢餓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious food shortage.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重食物短缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"declining crop yields","meaning":"不斷下降的農作物產量","examples":[{"en":"Soil erosion supposedly caused declining crop yields.","zh":"土壤侵蝕據稱導致農作物產量不斷下降。"},{"en":"Declining crop yields are falling amounts of food produced by farmland.","zh":"declining crop yields 是農田生產的食物數量下降。"},{"en":"A farm may face declining crop yields if soil becomes dry and poor.","zh":"如果土壤變乾變貧瘠，農場可能面對農作物產量下降。"},{"en":"If crop yields decline, families may have less food to eat or trade.","zh":"如果農作物產量下降，家庭可食用或交易的食物會減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reduced agricultural output.","zh":"這個片語描述農業產出減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"erosion of fertile soil","meaning":"肥沃土壤流失","examples":[{"en":"The erosion of fertile soil reduced food production.","zh":"肥沃土壤流失減少了食物生產。"},{"en":"Erosion of fertile soil means rich soil is worn away by wind or water.","zh":"erosion of fertile soil 指富有養分的土壤被風或水沖刷流失。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can cause erosion of fertile soil on bare hillsides.","zh":"大雨可以造成裸露山坡的肥沃土壤流失。"},{"en":"If fertile soil erodes away, crops grow less successfully.","zh":"如果肥沃土壤流失，農作物就較難成功生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes loss of productive land.","zh":"這個片語描述具生產力土地的流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"nutritional intake","meaning":"營養攝取量","examples":[{"en":"The population’s nutritional intake fell sharply.","zh":"人口的營養攝取量急劇下降。"},{"en":"Nutritional intake is the amount and quality of food and nutrients people consume.","zh":"nutritional intake 是人們攝取的食物和營養的數量及質素。"},{"en":"A child’s nutritional intake should include enough protein, vitamins, and calories.","zh":"孩子的營養攝取應包括足夠蛋白質、維他命和熱量。"},{"en":"If food sources decline, nutritional intake may fall and health may suffer.","zh":"如果食物來源減少，營養攝取量可能下降，健康可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on diet and nutrients.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於飲食和營養。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"plummet","meaning":"暴跌；急降","examples":[{"en":"Food shortages caused nutritional intake to plummet.","zh":"食物短缺導致營養攝取量暴跌。"},{"en":"To plummet means to fall very quickly and sharply.","zh":"plummet 指非常快速而劇烈地下降。"},{"en":"A shop’s sales may plummet after a food-safety scandal.","zh":"食品安全醜聞後，店舖銷售可能暴跌。"},{"en":"If nutrition plummets, illness and weakness may increase.","zh":"如果營養攝取急降，疾病和虛弱可能增加。"},{"en":"This word describes a sudden steep fall.","zh":"這個詞描述突然大幅下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"famine set in","meaning":"饑荒開始出現","examples":[{"en":"According to the theory, famine eventually set in.","zh":"根據該理論，饑荒最終開始出現。"},{"en":"When famine sets in, severe food shortage begins and spreads.","zh":"famine set in 指嚴重食物短缺開始並擴散。"},{"en":"A long drought can make famine set in across farming villages.","zh":"長期乾旱可以令農村饑荒開始出現。"},{"en":"If famine sets in, people may suffer hunger, disease, and social disorder.","zh":"如果饑荒開始出現，人們可能遭受飢餓、疾病和社會混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the start of a serious food crisis.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重食物危機的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"cannibalism set in","meaning":"食人行為開始出現","examples":[{"en":"Some accounts claim that cannibalism later set in.","zh":"一些記述聲稱食人行為後來開始出現。"},{"en":"When cannibalism sets in, people begin eating human flesh in extreme conditions.","zh":"cannibalism set in 指人在極端情況下開始吃人肉。"},{"en":"Stories of disaster sometimes describe cannibalism setting in after food disappears.","zh":"災難故事有時描述食物消失後食人行為開始出現。"},{"en":"If society reaches such a stage, it suggests severe breakdown and desperation.","zh":"如果社會走到這一步，表示嚴重崩潰和絕望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an extreme and disturbing consequence.","zh":"這個片語描述極端而令人不安的後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"keep society running","meaning":"維持社會運作","examples":[{"en":"Chiefs, officials, and priests helped keep the complex society running.","zh":"酋長、官員和祭司幫助維持複雜社會運作。"},{"en":"To keep society running means to maintain order, services, rules, and daily life.","zh":"keep society running 指維持秩序、服務、規則和日常生活。"},{"en":"Teachers, nurses, drivers, and cleaners help keep a city running.","zh":"老師、護士、司機和清潔工幫助維持城市運作。"},{"en":"If leaders and workers disappear, society may struggle to function.","zh":"如果領袖和工人消失，社會可能難以運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes maintaining normal social operation.","zh":"這個片語描述維持正常社會運行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"resulting chaos","meaning":"隨之而來的混亂","examples":[{"en":"The resulting chaos supposedly caused social breakdown.","zh":"隨之而來的混亂據稱造成社會崩潰。"},{"en":"Resulting chaos is disorder that happens because of earlier events.","zh":"resulting chaos 是由較早事件造成的混亂。"},{"en":"If a school timetable is changed without notice, the resulting chaos may upset students.","zh":"如果學校時間表沒有通知便改變，隨之而來的混亂可能令學生不安。"},{"en":"When food, leadership, and order fail together, chaos can spread quickly.","zh":"當食物、領導和秩序一起失效，混亂可以迅速擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase links disorder to its cause.","zh":"這個片語把混亂與其原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"trigger a collapse","meaning":"引發崩潰","examples":[{"en":"Resource shortages were said to have triggered a social and cultural collapse.","zh":"據說資源短缺引發了社會和文化崩潰。"},{"en":"To trigger a collapse means to cause a system or society to fall apart.","zh":"trigger a collapse 指造成某系統或社會瓦解。"},{"en":"A financial crisis can trigger the collapse of a small business.","zh":"金融危機可以引發小企業倒閉。"},{"en":"If food shortages trigger collapse, people may lose trust in leaders.","zh":"如果食物短缺引發崩潰，人們可能失去對領袖的信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a cause that starts failure.","zh":"這個片語描述開始失敗的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"drop to between","meaning":"下降至……之間","examples":[{"en":"The population reportedly dropped to between one-quarter and one-tenth of its former size.","zh":"據報人口下降至原來規模的四分之一至十分之一之間。"},{"en":"To drop to between two levels means to fall to a range between them.","zh":"drop to between two levels 指下降至兩個水平之間的範圍。"},{"en":"Attendance may drop to between 40 and 50 students during heavy rain.","zh":"大雨期間，出席人數可能下降至40至50人之間。"},{"en":"If population drops sharply, labour, culture, and family life are affected.","zh":"如果人口急跌，勞動力、文化和家庭生活都會受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an estimated range after a fall.","zh":"這個片語給出下降後的估計範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"former number","meaning":"原來的數量","examples":[{"en":"The population became only a fraction of its former number.","zh":"人口變成只佔原來數量的一小部分。"},{"en":"Former number means the amount or population size that existed before.","zh":"former number 指以前存在的數量或人口規模。"},{"en":"A club may have only half its former number of members after fees increase.","zh":"會費增加後，社團會員可能只剩原來數量的一半。"},{"en":"If a population falls below its former number, recovery may take generations.","zh":"如果人口跌破原來數量，恢復可能需要幾代。"},{"en":"This phrase compares present size with past size.","zh":"這個片語比較現在數量與過去數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be toppled","meaning":"被推倒","examples":[{"en":"Many statues were toppled during periods of conflict.","zh":"許多石像在衝突時期被推倒。"},{"en":"To be toppled means to be pushed over or made to fall.","zh":"be toppled 指被推翻或弄倒。"},{"en":"A strong storm can topple trees along a road.","zh":"強烈風暴可以推倒路邊樹木。"},{"en":"If statues are toppled, the act may show political conflict or social change.","zh":"如果石像被推倒，該行為可能顯示政治衝突或社會變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being knocked down from an upright position.","zh":"這個片語描述從直立位置被弄倒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"supposed clan wars","meaning":"據稱發生的部族戰爭","examples":[{"en":"Some writers attribute the damage to supposed clan wars.","zh":"一些作家把破壞歸因於據稱發生的部族戰爭。"},{"en":"Supposed clan wars are wars believed or claimed to have happened between family groups.","zh":"supposed clan wars 是被相信或聲稱在家族群體之間發生的戰爭。"},{"en":"Historians may question supposed wars if evidence is weak.","zh":"如果證據薄弱，歷史學家可能質疑據稱發生的戰爭。"},{"en":"If damage is blamed on clan wars, researchers need proof of conflict.","zh":"如果破壞被歸咎於部族戰爭，研究人員需要衝突證據。"},{"en":"This phrase signals uncertainty about the explanation.","zh":"這個片語表示該解釋帶有不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"faulty notions","meaning":"錯誤觀念","examples":[{"en":"The final paragraph challenges what it calls faulty notions.","zh":"最後一段挑戰它所稱的錯誤觀念。"},{"en":"Faulty notions are mistaken ideas or beliefs.","zh":"faulty notions 是錯誤的想法或信念。"},{"en":"The notion that all quiet students are weak speakers is faulty.","zh":"認為所有安靜學生都不擅長說話，是錯誤觀念。"},{"en":"If faulty notions spread, people may misunderstand history or society.","zh":"如果錯誤觀念傳播，人們可能誤解歷史或社會。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises ideas as wrong.","zh":"這個片語把某些想法批評為錯誤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"racist assumptions","meaning":"種族主義假設","examples":[{"en":"The writer argues that some earlier theories began with racist assumptions.","zh":"作者認為一些早期理論始於種族主義假設。"},{"en":"Racist assumptions are beliefs based on prejudice about race or ethnic groups.","zh":"racist assumptions 是基於對種族或族裔群體偏見的信念。"},{"en":"A racist assumption may claim one group is naturally less intelligent than another.","zh":"種族主義假設可能聲稱某群體天生比另一群體不聰明。"},{"en":"If historical theories start from racism, they can distort evidence.","zh":"如果歷史理論始於種族主義，它們可以扭曲證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes biased and harmful starting beliefs.","zh":"這個片語描述有偏見且有害的起點信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be perpetuated by","meaning":"被……延續散播","examples":[{"en":"The ideas were perpetuated by later writers.","zh":"這些想法被後來作家延續散播。"},{"en":"To be perpetuated by someone means to be kept alive or spread by them.","zh":"be perpetuated by someone 指被某人保留下來或傳播下去。"},{"en":"A false rumour may be perpetuated by people who repeat it online.","zh":"虛假謠言可能被在網上重複它的人延續散播。"},{"en":"If writers keep repeating an error, the mistake can survive for decades.","zh":"如果作家不斷重複錯誤，該錯誤可以延續數十年。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the continued spread of an idea.","zh":"這個片語描述想法持續傳播。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"sufficient understanding","meaning":"足夠的理解","examples":[{"en":"The writer claims that some authors lacked sufficient historical understanding.","zh":"作者聲稱一些作家缺乏足夠歷史理解。"},{"en":"Sufficient understanding means enough knowledge to judge something properly.","zh":"sufficient understanding 指有足夠知識作出恰當判斷。"},{"en":"A student needs sufficient understanding of grammar before editing complex essays.","zh":"學生在修改複雜文章前需要足夠文法理解。"},{"en":"If writers lack understanding, they may reach misleading conclusions.","zh":"如果作家缺乏理解，可能得出誤導性結論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an adequate level of knowledge.","zh":"這個片語描述足夠的知識水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"actual events","meaning":"實際發生的事件","examples":[{"en":"Historical evidence is needed to understand the actual events on the island.","zh":"需要歷史證據才能理解島上實際發生的事件。"},{"en":"Actual events are what really happened, not what people imagine or assume.","zh":"actual events 是真正發生的事情，而不是人們想像或假設的內容。"},{"en":"Police interviews help establish the actual events after an accident.","zh":"意外後，警方訪問有助確定實際發生的事件。"},{"en":"If stories are exaggerated, evidence is needed to recover actual events.","zh":"如果故事被誇大，就需要證據恢復實際事件。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts reality with speculation.","zh":"這個片語把現實與猜測作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the real truth regarding","meaning":"關於……的真正真相","examples":[{"en":"The writer offers a different account of the real truth regarding the decline.","zh":"作者提供了關於衰落真正真相的不同說法。"},{"en":"The real truth regarding something means the actual facts about it.","zh":"the real truth regarding something 指關於某事的實際事實。"},{"en":"A report may reveal the real truth regarding why a project failed.","zh":"報告可能揭示項目失敗的真正真相。"},{"en":"If earlier explanations were biased, the real truth may be different.","zh":"如果早期解釋有偏見，真正真相可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises factual reality over false stories.","zh":"這個片語強調事實現實，而不是虛假故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"tremendous social devastation","meaning":"嚴重的社會破壞","examples":[{"en":"The island suffered tremendous social devastation.","zh":"該島遭受嚴重的社會破壞。"},{"en":"Tremendous social devastation means extremely serious damage to people, families, and society.","zh":"tremendous social devastation 指對人民、家庭和社會造成極嚴重破壞。"},{"en":"War can cause tremendous social devastation by destroying homes and communities.","zh":"戰爭可以透過摧毀家園和社區造成嚴重社會破壞。"},{"en":"If disease and violence remove many people, society may be deeply damaged.","zh":"如果疾病和暴力奪走許多人，社會可能深受破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severe social destruction.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重社會毀壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a direct consequence of","meaning":"……的直接後果","examples":[{"en":"The devastation was described as a direct consequence of European actions.","zh":"這場破壞被描述為歐洲人行為的直接後果。"},{"en":"A direct consequence of something is a result caused clearly by it.","zh":"direct consequence of something 是由某事明確造成的結果。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is a direct consequence of staying up all night.","zh":"通宵不睡的直接後果是睡眠不足。"},{"en":"If violence leads to population loss, the loss can be a direct consequence of that violence.","zh":"如果暴力導致人口流失，這種流失可成為該暴力的直接後果。"},{"en":"This phrase links cause and result strongly.","zh":"這個片語強烈連接原因和結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"inhumane behaviour","meaning":"不人道行為","examples":[{"en":"The passage condemns the inhumane behaviour of some visitors.","zh":"文章譴責一些訪客的不人道行為。"},{"en":"Inhumane behaviour is cruel behaviour that ignores human suffering and dignity.","zh":"inhumane behaviour 是忽視人類痛苦和尊嚴的殘酷行為。"},{"en":"Forcing workers to live in unsafe rooms is inhumane behaviour.","zh":"強迫工人住在不安全房間是不人道行為。"},{"en":"If visitors kidnap or exploit local people, their behaviour is deeply immoral.","zh":"如果訪客綁架或剝削本地人，其行為極不道德。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cruel and unacceptable treatment.","zh":"這個片語描述殘酷且不能接受的對待。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"first European visitors","meaning":"第一批歐洲訪客","examples":[{"en":"The first European visitors had a profound effect on the island.","zh":"第一批歐洲訪客對該島產生深遠影響。"},{"en":"First European visitors are the earliest Europeans recorded as arriving at a place.","zh":"first European visitors 是有記錄中最早到達某地的歐洲人。"},{"en":"First visitors can bring trade, disease, weapons, or new ideas.","zh":"第一批訪客可能帶來貿易、疾病、武器或新想法。"},{"en":"If first contact is violent, its effects may last for generations.","zh":"如果首次接觸充滿暴力，其影響可能持續幾代。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the beginning of European contact.","zh":"這個片語指歐洲人接觸的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"slavers","meaning":"奴隸販子","examples":[{"en":"Slavers kidnapped many islanders and transported them abroad.","zh":"奴隸販子綁架許多島民並把他們運往海外。"},{"en":"Slavers are people who capture, buy, sell, or transport enslaved people.","zh":"slavers 是捕捉、買賣或運送被奴役者的人。"},{"en":"Slavers destroyed families by taking people away from their homes.","zh":"奴隸販子把人從家園帶走，摧毀家庭。"},{"en":"If slavers remove many adults, a community loses labour, knowledge, and family stability.","zh":"如果奴隸販子帶走許多成年人，社群會失去勞動力、知識和家庭穩定。"},{"en":"This word refers to people involved in the slave trade.","zh":"這個詞指參與奴隸貿易的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"introduce smallpox","meaning":"傳入天花","examples":[{"en":"European visitors introduced smallpox and other diseases.","zh":"歐洲訪客傳入天花和其他疾病。"},{"en":"To introduce smallpox means to bring the disease into a population that did not have it before.","zh":"introduce smallpox 指把天花帶入原本沒有該疾病的人群。"},{"en":"Travellers can introduce disease if there is no immunity in the local community.","zh":"如果本地社群沒有免疫力，旅人可能傳入疾病。"},{"en":"If smallpox spreads in an unprotected population, deaths can be devastating.","zh":"如果天花在沒有保護的人口中傳播，死亡可能非常嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disease arriving through contact.","zh":"這個片語描述疾病透過接觸到來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"brutally remove","meaning":"殘酷地帶走","examples":[{"en":"Many native islanders were brutally removed from their homeland.","zh":"許多本地島民被殘酷地從家園帶走。"},{"en":"To brutally remove people means to take them away by force and cruelty.","zh":"brutally remove people 指以暴力和殘酷方式把人帶走。"},{"en":"Soldiers may brutally remove families during violent conflict.","zh":"士兵可能在暴力衝突中殘酷地帶走家庭。"},{"en":"If people are removed from their homeland, culture and family networks can be broken.","zh":"如果人們被從家園帶走，文化和家庭網絡可能被破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes violent forced displacement.","zh":"這個片語描述暴力強迫遷離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"native islanders","meaning":"本地島民","examples":[{"en":"The native islanders suffered violence and disease.","zh":"本地島民遭受暴力和疾病。"},{"en":"Native islanders are the original local people living on an island.","zh":"native islanders 是居住在島上的原本本地人。"},{"en":"Native islanders may have deep knowledge of local weather, food, and sacred places.","zh":"本地島民可能深入了解當地天氣、食物和神聖地點。"},{"en":"If outsiders exploit native islanders, the whole society can be damaged.","zh":"如果外來者剝削本地島民，整個社會都可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the island’s original people.","zh":"這個片語指島上的原住居民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"mainland South America","meaning":"南美洲大陸","examples":[{"en":"Some islanders were taken to mainland South America.","zh":"一些島民被帶到南美洲大陸。"},{"en":"Mainland South America means the main continental landmass of South America, not its islands.","zh":"mainland South America 指南美洲主要大陸部分，而不是其島嶼。"},{"en":"Travellers may fly from islands to mainland South America for work or study.","zh":"旅客可能從島嶼飛往南美洲大陸工作或讀書。"},{"en":"If islanders were taken there by force, they were removed far from home.","zh":"如果島民被強迫帶到那裡，他們就是被遠遠帶離家園。"},{"en":"This phrase distinguishes the continent from nearby islands.","zh":"這個片語把大陸與附近島嶼區分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct heading for each paragraph.","zh":"考生為每一段選出正確標題。"},{"en":"To choose the correct heading means to select the title that best matches a paragraph’s main idea.","zh":"choose the correct heading 指選擇最符合段落主旨的標題。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students should read the whole paragraph before choosing a heading.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先讀完整段，再選標題。"},{"en":"If a heading matches only one detail, it may not be the correct answer.","zh":"如果標題只符合一個細節，它未必是正確答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in paragraph-matching tasks.","zh":"這個片語常見於段落配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"more headings than paragraphs","meaning":"標題數目多於段落數目","examples":[{"en":"The task provides more headings than paragraphs.","zh":"題目提供的標題數目多於段落數目。"},{"en":"More headings than paragraphs means there are extra title options that will not be used.","zh":"more headings than paragraphs 指有額外標題選項不會被使用。"},{"en":"In an exam, extra headings prevent students from matching by simple elimination.","zh":"在考試中，額外標題防止學生只靠簡單排除法配對。"},{"en":"If there are more headings than paragraphs, students must compare meanings carefully.","zh":"如果標題數目多於段落數目，學生必須仔細比較意思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common test design.","zh":"這個片語描述常見測驗設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the famous moai","meaning":"著名的摩艾石像","examples":[{"en":"One heading focuses on the island’s famous moai statues.","zh":"其中一個標題聚焦於該島著名的摩艾石像。"},{"en":"The famous moai are the well-known stone statues of Easter Island.","zh":"famous moai 是復活節島知名的石像。"},{"en":"Tourists often visit the island mainly to see the famous moai.","zh":"遊客常主要為了看著名摩艾石像而到訪該島。"},{"en":"If a paragraph describes statue size, carving, and platforms, the heading may concern the moai.","zh":"如果段落描述石像大小、雕刻和平台，標題可能與摩艾石像有關。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the island’s iconic statues.","zh":"這個片語指該島具標誌性的石像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"serve symbolic purposes","meaning":"發揮象徵作用","examples":[{"en":"The statues served several symbolic and religious purposes.","zh":"這些石像發揮幾種象徵和宗教作用。"},{"en":"To serve symbolic purposes means to represent ideas, beliefs, or power beyond practical use.","zh":"serve symbolic purposes 指代表超越實際用途的想法、信仰或權力。"},{"en":"A national flag serves symbolic purposes by representing a country.","zh":"國旗透過代表國家來發揮象徵作用。"},{"en":"If a statue symbolises ancestors, it may strengthen identity and authority.","zh":"如果石像象徵祖先，它可能強化身份和權威。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaning rather than physical function only.","zh":"這個片語描述意義，而不只是物理功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"scientific applications","meaning":"科學用途","examples":[{"en":"Some theories link ancient sites with scientific applications.","zh":"一些理論把古代遺址與科學用途連繫起來。"},{"en":"Scientific applications are practical uses connected with science, measurement, or observation.","zh":"scientific applications 是與科學、測量或觀察有關的實際用途。"},{"en":"Satellite images have scientific applications in weather forecasting and farming.","zh":"衛星影像在天氣預報和農業中有科學用途。"},{"en":"If a structure has scientific applications, it may have been used to measure time or stars.","zh":"如果建築有科學用途，它可能曾用來量度時間或星體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes science-related uses.","zh":"這個片語描述與科學相關的用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the story of the name","meaning":"名稱的由來","examples":[{"en":"The first paragraph explains the story of the island’s name.","zh":"第一段解釋該島名稱的由來。"},{"en":"The story of the name means how a name was created or came into use.","zh":"the story of the name 指名稱如何產生或開始被使用。"},{"en":"A school may tell new students the story of its name during orientation.","zh":"學校可能在迎新時告訴新生校名的由來。"},{"en":"If a name comes from a special date, that date becomes part of its history.","zh":"如果名稱源自特別日期，該日期就成為其歷史的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to name origin.","zh":"這個片語指名稱來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"rise and prosperity","meaning":"興起與繁榮","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes the early population’s rise and prosperity.","zh":"文章描述早期人口的興起與繁榮。"},{"en":"Rise and prosperity means growth, success, and wealth or abundance.","zh":"rise and prosperity 指成長、成功和財富或豐足。"},{"en":"A town’s rise and prosperity may follow the opening of a major port.","zh":"主要港口開放後，小鎮可能出現興起與繁榮。"},{"en":"If food is plentiful, a population may grow and create a rich culture.","zh":"如果食物充足，人口可能增長並創造豐富文化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a successful early period.","zh":"這個片語描述成功的早期階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the geology of","meaning":"……的地質","examples":[{"en":"One possible heading concerns the geology of Easter Island.","zh":"其中一個可能標題關於復活節島的地質。"},{"en":"The geology of a place means its rocks, landforms, and physical formation.","zh":"geology of a place 指某地的岩石、地貌和物理形成。"},{"en":"A lesson on the geology of Hong Kong may discuss granite and volcanic rocks.","zh":"關於香港地質的課堂可能討論花崗岩和火山岩。"},{"en":"If a place has volcanic geology, its landscape may include craters and lava stone.","zh":"如果地方具有火山地質，其景觀可能包括火山口和熔岩石。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on physical Earth features.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於地球物理特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"origin of a theory","meaning":"某理論的起源","examples":[{"en":"The question includes a heading about the origin of Heyerdahl’s theory.","zh":"題目包括一個關於 Heyerdahl 理論起源的標題。"},{"en":"Origin of a theory means where an explanation first came from.","zh":"origin of a theory 指某解釋最初來自哪裡。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to explain the origin of a theory before judging it.","zh":"老師可能要求學生先解釋理論起源，再作判斷。"},{"en":"If a theory began from limited evidence, later research may challenge it.","zh":"如果理論源自有限證據，後來研究可能挑戰它。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the starting point of an idea.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於想法的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"counterargument to","meaning":"對……的反駁","examples":[{"en":"The final paragraph presents a counterargument to earlier theories.","zh":"最後一段提出對早期理論的反駁。"},{"en":"A counterargument to something is an argument against it.","zh":"counterargument to something 是反對某事的論點。"},{"en":"A student should include a counterargument to show awareness of other views.","zh":"學生應加入反駁，以顯示了解其他觀點。"},{"en":"If a theory is biased, a counterargument can expose its weakness.","zh":"如果理論有偏見，反駁可以揭示其弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces opposition to an idea.","zh":"這個片語引入對某想法的反對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"politically motivated misconceptions","meaning":"受政治動機影響的錯誤觀念","examples":[{"en":"A counterargument may challenge politically motivated misconceptions.","zh":"反駁可能挑戰受政治動機影響的錯誤觀念。"},{"en":"Politically motivated misconceptions are false ideas shaped by political aims or bias.","zh":"politically motivated misconceptions 是受政治目的或偏見塑造的錯誤想法。"},{"en":"A government may spread misconceptions to protect its image.","zh":"政府可能散播錯誤觀念以保護自身形象。"},{"en":"If history is explained through political bias, people may blame the wrong group.","zh":"如果歷史透過政治偏見解釋，人們可能責怪錯誤群體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mistaken beliefs driven by politics.","zh":"這個片語描述由政治推動的錯誤信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"symbols of authority and power","meaning":"權威和力量的象徵","examples":[{"en":"The moai represented authority and power.","zh":"摩艾石像代表權威和力量。"},{"en":"Symbols of authority and power are objects that show leadership, status, or control.","zh":"symbols of authority and power 是顯示領導、地位或控制的物件。"},{"en":"A judge’s robe can be a symbol of authority and power.","zh":"法官袍可以是權威和力量的象徵。"},{"en":"If a statue represents ancestors, it can support social authority.","zh":"如果石像代表祖先，它可以支持社會權威。"},{"en":"This phrase describes objects carrying political or social meaning.","zh":"這個片語描述帶有政治或社會意義的物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"legacy","meaning":"遺產；後世影響","examples":[{"en":"The question includes a possible heading about the explorers’ legacy.","zh":"題目包括一個可能關於探險家後世影響的標題。"},{"en":"Legacy means what someone or something leaves behind for the future.","zh":"legacy 指某人或某事為未來留下的東西。"},{"en":"A teacher’s legacy may be the confidence she gives her students.","zh":"老師的遺產可能是她給予學生的信心。"},{"en":"If explorers record names and stories, their legacy can shape later understanding.","zh":"如果探險家記錄名稱和故事，他們的後世影響可以塑造後來理解。"},{"en":"This word refers to lasting influence.","zh":"這個詞指持久影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所給資料相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the information given.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否與所給資料相符。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指符合文章所說內容。"},{"en":"In reading tests, a statement may use different words but still agree with the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，陳述可能使用不同字眼但仍與文章相符。"},{"en":"If a statement changes the meaning, it does not agree with the information.","zh":"如果陳述改變意思，它就不與資料相符。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個片語常見於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage states.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文章所述相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the text says the island is remote, saying it is easy to reach contradicts it.","zh":"如果文本說該島偏遠，說它容易到達就是與文本相矛盾。"},{"en":"When a statement contradicts the passage, the answer is usually FALSE.","zh":"當陳述與文章相矛盾，答案通常是 FALSE。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct disagreement with the text.","zh":"這個片語描述與文本直接不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students select “NOT GIVEN” when the passage provides no relevant information.","zh":"當文章沒有提供相關資料時，學生選擇 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the text does not tell us the answer.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文本沒有告訴我們答案。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions ticket prices, there is no information on that topic.","zh":"如果文章從未提及票價，就沒有關於該主題的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from outside knowledge when information is missing.","zh":"當資料缺失時，學生不應用外部知識猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the NOT GIVEN option.","zh":"這個片語解釋 NOT GIVEN 選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"first inhabitants","meaning":"最早居民","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the island’s first inhabitants.","zh":"題目問關於該島最早居民的資料。"},{"en":"First inhabitants are the earliest people known to have lived in a place.","zh":"first inhabitants 是已知最早居住在某地的人。"},{"en":"Archaeologists study tools and bones to identify first inhabitants.","zh":"考古學家研究工具和骨骼，以識別最早居民。"},{"en":"If first inhabitants came from another island group, migration shaped the culture.","zh":"如果最早居民來自另一個島群，遷徙便塑造了文化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the earliest residents.","zh":"這個片語指最早的居民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"construction was not finished","meaning":"建造尚未完成","examples":[{"en":"Some moai remained incomplete because their construction was not finished.","zh":"一些摩艾石像仍未完成，因為其建造尚未完成。"},{"en":"Construction was not finished means building or making stopped before completion.","zh":"construction was not finished 指建造或製作在完成前停止。"},{"en":"A classroom model may remain rough because its construction was not finished.","zh":"課室模型可能因建造尚未完成而仍很粗糙。"},{"en":"If construction stops suddenly, unfinished objects can reveal work methods.","zh":"如果建造突然停止，未完成物件可以揭示工作方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes incomplete building or making.","zh":"這個片語描述未完成的建造或製作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be found elsewhere","meaning":"可在其他地方找到","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether moai can be found elsewhere in Polynesia.","zh":"題目問摩艾石像是否可在波利尼西亞其他地方找到。"},{"en":"To be found elsewhere means to exist or appear in another place.","zh":"be found elsewhere 指存在或出現在另一地方。"},{"en":"Similar pottery may be found elsewhere along the coast.","zh":"相似陶器可能可在海岸其他地方找到。"},{"en":"If a tradition is found elsewhere, it may have shared origins.","zh":"如果某傳統在其他地方也可找到，它可能有共同起源。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one location with other locations.","zh":"這個片語比較某地與其他地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"recognize religious functions","meaning":"認定具有宗教功能","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists have recognized religious functions in many ancient structures.","zh":"考古學家已認定許多古代建築具有宗教功能。"},{"en":"To recognize religious functions means to identify that something was used for worship or ritual.","zh":"recognize religious functions 指識別某物曾用於崇拜或儀式。"},{"en":"A stone circle may be recognised as having religious functions if offerings are found nearby.","zh":"如果石圈附近發現祭品，它可能被認定具有宗教功能。"},{"en":"If a building has altars and sacred objects, its religious role becomes clearer.","zh":"如果建築有祭壇和神聖物件，其宗教角色會更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes identifying sacred purpose.","zh":"這個片語描述識別神聖用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"astronomical functions","meaning":"天文功能","examples":[{"en":"Some alternative theories propose astronomical functions for the structures.","zh":"一些另類理論提出這些建築具有天文功能。"},{"en":"Astronomical functions are uses connected with observing or measuring the sky.","zh":"astronomical functions 是與觀察或量度天空有關的用途。"},{"en":"A stone alignment may have astronomical functions if it marks sunrise at solstice.","zh":"如果石列標示冬至或夏至日出，它可能具有天文功能。"},{"en":"If a structure tracks stars, it may help people organise calendars.","zh":"如果建築追蹤星體，它可能幫助人們安排曆法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sky-related purposes.","zh":"這個片語描述與天空相關的用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"extraterrestrial visitors","meaning":"地球以外的訪客","examples":[{"en":"One statement refers to possible extraterrestrial visitors.","zh":"一項陳述提及可能的地球以外訪客。"},{"en":"Extraterrestrial visitors are imagined beings from outside Earth.","zh":"extraterrestrial visitors 是被想像來自地球以外的生物。"},{"en":"Science fiction often describes extraterrestrial visitors arriving by spacecraft.","zh":"科幻小說常描述地球以外的訪客乘太空船抵達。"},{"en":"If a theory mentions aliens, scholars usually demand extraordinary evidence.","zh":"如果理論提到外星人，學者通常要求極強證據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to non-Earth visitors.","zh":"這個片語指非地球訪客。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"depleted natural resources","meaning":"耗盡的自然資源","examples":[{"en":"One theory links the decline to depleted natural resources.","zh":"一項理論把衰落與耗盡的自然資源連繫起來。"},{"en":"Depleted natural resources are resources such as forests, soil, water, or animals that have been used up.","zh":"depleted natural resources 是森林、土壤、水或動物等已被用盡的資源。"},{"en":"Overfishing can create depleted natural resources in coastal areas.","zh":"過度捕魚可以造成沿海地區自然資源耗盡。"},{"en":"If natural resources are depleted, food and construction materials may become scarce.","zh":"如果自然資源被耗盡，食物和建築材料可能變得稀缺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes environmental shortage caused by overuse.","zh":"這個片語描述因過度使用造成的環境短缺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"lead to the fall of","meaning":"導致……衰亡","examples":[{"en":"The theory suggests that resource depletion led to the fall of the civilization.","zh":"該理論指出資源耗盡導致該文明衰亡。"},{"en":"To lead to the fall of something means to cause its collapse or defeat.","zh":"lead to the fall of something 指造成某事物崩潰或失敗。"},{"en":"Poor leadership can lead to the fall of a company.","zh":"領導不善可以導致公司倒閉。"},{"en":"If food, water, and order fail, a society may collapse.","zh":"如果食物、水和秩序失效，社會可能崩潰。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with downfall.","zh":"這個片語把原因與衰亡連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"distorted perspective","meaning":"扭曲的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The writer describes some earlier explanations as based on a distorted perspective.","zh":"作者把一些早期解釋描述為建基於扭曲的觀點。"},{"en":"A distorted perspective is a biased or twisted way of seeing something.","zh":"distorted perspective 是有偏見或被扭曲的看法。"},{"en":"A student may have a distorted perspective if they judge themselves only by one bad mark.","zh":"如果學生只用一次差成績評價自己，他可能有扭曲觀點。"},{"en":"If historians start with prejudice, their interpretation of evidence may be distorted.","zh":"如果歷史學家以偏見開始，他們對證據的詮釋可能被扭曲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unfair or inaccurate viewpoint.","zh":"這個片語描述不公平或不準確的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete the following summary","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the following summary using words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用篇章中的字詞完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the following summary means to fill in missing words in the short text below.","zh":"complete the following summary 指填寫下面摘要中缺少的字詞。"},{"en":"Students should use exact words from the passage if the instruction requires it.","zh":"如果指示要求，學生應使用篇章中的原字。"},{"en":"If the grammar of the answer does not fit, it may be wrong.","zh":"如果答案文法不配合，可能是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading completion tasks.","zh":"這個片語常見於閱讀填充題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不超過三個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer must contain no more than three words.","zh":"每個答案必須不超過三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means one, two, or three words only.","zh":"no more than three words 指只可用一個、兩個或三個英文詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “volcanic stone”, students should not add extra words.","zh":"如果答案是 “volcanic stone”，學生不應加額外詞語。"},{"en":"If a student writes four words, the answer may be marked wrong even if the idea is right.","zh":"如果學生寫四個詞，即使意思正確，也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word limit.","zh":"這個片語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"speculate about","meaning":"推測；猜想","examples":[{"en":"Many writers have speculated about Easter Island’s fall.","zh":"許多作家推測復活節島的衰亡。"},{"en":"To speculate about something means to guess or suggest possibilities without complete proof.","zh":"speculate about something 指在沒有完整證據下猜想或提出可能性。"},{"en":"Students may speculate about why a character left home before reading the ending.","zh":"學生可能在讀到結尾前猜想角色為何離家。"},{"en":"If evidence is limited, speculation can spread quickly.","zh":"如果證據有限，猜測可以快速傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase signals uncertainty.","zh":"這個片語表示不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"around the time of initial contact","meaning":"大約在最初接觸的時期","examples":[{"en":"The decline occurred around the time of initial European contact.","zh":"衰落大約發生在最初歐洲接觸的時期。"},{"en":"Around the time of initial contact means near the period when outsiders first arrived or met locals.","zh":"around the time of initial contact 指大約在外來者首次到達或遇見本地人的時期。"},{"en":"Disease may spread around the time of first contact between separated communities.","zh":"疾病可能在分隔社群首次接觸時期傳播。"},{"en":"If decline begins near first contact, historians examine what visitors brought.","zh":"如果衰落在首次接觸附近開始，歷史學家會研究訪客帶來甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase gives approximate historical timing.","zh":"這個片語給出大約歷史時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"resources were depleted","meaning":"資源被耗盡","examples":[{"en":"Some theories claim that the island’s resources were depleted.","zh":"一些理論聲稱該島資源被耗盡。"},{"en":"Resources were depleted means useful supplies were used up or greatly reduced.","zh":"resources were depleted 指有用供應被用盡或大幅減少。"},{"en":"A town’s water resources may be depleted after months of drought.","zh":"經過數月乾旱後，小鎮水資源可能被耗盡。"},{"en":"If resources are depleted, people may face shortage, conflict, or migration.","zh":"如果資源被耗盡，人們可能面對短缺、衝突或遷移。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious reduction of supplies.","zh":"這個片語描述供應嚴重減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"growing population","meaning":"不斷增長的人口","examples":[{"en":"A growing population can place heavy pressure on limited resources.","zh":"不斷增長的人口會對有限資源造成沉重壓力。"},{"en":"A growing population is a population that is increasing in number.","zh":"growing population 是數量正在增加的人口。"},{"en":"A growing population may require more schools, homes, food, and healthcare.","zh":"不斷增長的人口可能需要更多學校、房屋、食物和醫療。"},{"en":"If population grows faster than resources, shortages may appear.","zh":"如果人口增長快過資源，短缺可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes demographic increase.","zh":"這個片語描述人口增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"erroneous theories","meaning":"錯誤理論","examples":[{"en":"The writer argues that several erroneous theories became widely accepted.","zh":"作者認為幾個錯誤理論變得被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"Erroneous theories are theories that are wrong or based on false assumptions.","zh":"erroneous theories 是錯誤或建基於虛假假設的理論。"},{"en":"A student may reject an erroneous theory after checking the evidence.","zh":"學生查核證據後，可能否定錯誤理論。"},{"en":"If erroneous theories are repeated often, people may mistake them for truth.","zh":"如果錯誤理論被經常重複，人們可能誤以為它們是真相。"},{"en":"This phrase describes incorrect explanations.","zh":"這個片語描述不正確的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"stem from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"The erroneous theories allegedly stemmed from racist assumptions.","zh":"這些錯誤理論據稱源自種族主義假設。"},{"en":"To stem from something means to come from it as a cause or origin.","zh":"stem from something 指以某事作為原因或起源。"},{"en":"A student’s anxiety may stem from fear of public mistakes.","zh":"學生焦慮可能源自害怕公開犯錯。"},{"en":"If a theory stems from prejudice, its conclusions may be unreliable.","zh":"如果理論源自偏見，其結論可能不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the source of an idea or problem.","zh":"這個片語指出想法或問題的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be advanced by","meaning":"由……提出","examples":[{"en":"The assumptions were advanced by several well-known writers.","zh":"這些假設由幾位著名作家提出。"},{"en":"To be advanced by someone means to be proposed or promoted by that person.","zh":"be advanced by someone 指由某人提出或推廣。"},{"en":"A new education idea may be advanced by teachers who see old methods failing.","zh":"當老師看到舊方法失效，可能提出新的教育想法。"},{"en":"If famous writers advance an idea, it can spread quickly.","zh":"如果著名作家提出某想法，它可以快速傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase describes who puts an idea forward.","zh":"這個片語描述誰提出想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"adequate understanding","meaning":"足夠的理解","examples":[{"en":"Interpreting the island’s history requires adequate archaeological understanding.","zh":"詮釋該島歷史需要足夠的考古理解。"},{"en":"Adequate understanding means enough knowledge to judge or explain something properly.","zh":"adequate understanding 指有足夠知識來正確判斷或解釋某事。"},{"en":"Students need adequate understanding of a passage before answering inference questions.","zh":"學生回答推論題前，需要對篇章有足夠理解。"},{"en":"If understanding is inadequate, conclusions may become shallow or wrong.","zh":"如果理解不足，結論可能變得膚淺或錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sufficient knowledge for reliable interpretation.","zh":"這個片語描述可靠詮釋所需的充分知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"comprehend the true nature of","meaning":"理解……的真實本質","examples":[{"en":"Researchers need strong evidence to comprehend the true nature of past events.","zh":"研究人員需要有力證據來理解過去事件的真實本質。"},{"en":"To comprehend the true nature of something means to understand what it really was like.","zh":"comprehend the true nature of something 指理解某事真正是怎樣的。"},{"en":"A doctor must comprehend the true nature of a patient’s pain before choosing treatment.","zh":"醫生在選擇治療前，必須理解病人痛楚的真實本質。"},{"en":"If evidence is biased, people may misunderstand what really happened.","zh":"如果證據有偏見，人們可能誤解真正發生的事。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses deep and accurate understanding.","zh":"這個片語強調深入而準確的理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"social devastation","meaning":"社會破壞","examples":[{"en":"The final paragraph attributes the social devastation to European violence.","zh":"最後一段把社會破壞歸因於歐洲人的暴力。"},{"en":"Social devastation is severe damage to a community’s people, families, institutions, and culture.","zh":"social devastation 是對社群人民、家庭、制度和文化的嚴重破壞。"},{"en":"War can cause social devastation by breaking schools, homes, and public trust.","zh":"戰爭可以透過破壞學校、家園和公共信任造成社會破壞。"},{"en":"If disease and slavery remove many people, social devastation may follow.","zh":"如果疾病和奴役奪走許多人，社會破壞可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes destruction of society, not only buildings.","zh":"這個片語描述社會被破壞，而不只是建築物受損。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be a direct result of","meaning":"是……的直接結果","examples":[{"en":"The devastation was presented as a direct result of inhumane behaviour.","zh":"這場破壞被呈現為不人道行為的直接結果。"},{"en":"To be a direct result of something means to be clearly caused by it.","zh":"be a direct result of something 指明確由某事造成。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be a direct result of sleeping only three hours.","zh":"學生疲倦可能是只睡三小時的直接結果。"},{"en":"If violence causes social collapse, the collapse is not merely accidental.","zh":"如果暴力造成社會崩潰，這種崩潰就不只是偶然。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly links an outcome to its cause.","zh":"這個片語強烈把結果與原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 157 - Mystery in Easter Island.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 158":[{"front":"saving endangered languages","meaning":"拯救瀕危語言","examples":[{"en":"Saving endangered languages requires action from both linguists and local communities.","zh":"拯救瀕危語言需要語言學家和本地社群雙方行動。"},{"en":"Saving endangered languages means protecting languages that may soon stop being spoken.","zh":"saving endangered languages 指保護可能很快不再有人使用的語言。"},{"en":"A village can help save an endangered language by teaching children songs, stories and daily phrases.","zh":"村莊可以透過教孩子歌曲、故事和日常短語來拯救瀕危語言。"},{"en":"If no one records or teaches the language, younger people may grow up unable to speak it.","zh":"如果沒有人記錄或教授該語言，年輕人長大後可能不會說它。"},{"en":"Saving endangered languages is not only academic work; it also depends on families using the language.","zh":"拯救瀕危語言不只是學術工作；也取決於家庭是否使用該語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"seriously rethink one’s priorities","meaning":"認真重新考慮……的優先次序","examples":[{"en":"Linguists may need to seriously rethink their research priorities.","zh":"語言學家可能需要認真重新考慮他們的研究優先次序。"},{"en":"To seriously rethink one’s priorities means to carefully reconsider what should matter most.","zh":"seriously rethink one’s priorities 指仔細重新思考甚麼應該最重要。"},{"en":"A student may seriously rethink her priorities if she spends hours online but has no time to revise.","zh":"如果學生花數小時上網卻沒有時間溫習，她可能要認真重新考慮自己的優先次序。"},{"en":"When a problem becomes urgent, people may need to move it higher on their list of concerns.","zh":"當問題變得緊急，人們可能需要把它放到更重要的位置。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a deep change in focus, not a small adjustment.","zh":"這個短語暗示焦點上的深層改變，而不是小調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lest something happen","meaning":"以免……發生","examples":[{"en":"Urgent action is needed lest thousands of languages disappear.","zh":"必須緊急行動，以免數以千計語言消失。"},{"en":"Lest something happen means in order to prevent that bad thing from happening.","zh":"lest something happen 指為了防止那件壞事發生。"},{"en":"A teacher may call parents early, lest a student’s small problem become serious.","zh":"老師可能及早聯絡家長，以免學生的小問題變得嚴重。"},{"en":"If warning signs are ignored, the unwanted result may happen before people are ready.","zh":"如果忽視警號，不想見到的結果可能在人們準備好前已發生。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and is often used when there is a risk to avoid.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於表示要避免某種風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"go down in history as","meaning":"以……形象載入歷史","examples":[{"en":"Linguistics must not go down in history as a discipline that ignored language loss.","zh":"語言學絕不能以忽視語言流失的學科形象載入歷史。"},{"en":"To go down in history as something means to be remembered by later generations in that way.","zh":"go down in history as 某形象，指被後世以那種方式記住。"},{"en":"A school principal does not want to go down in history as someone who ignored bullying.","zh":"校長不會想以忽視欺凌的人這種形象載入歷史。"},{"en":"People care about this because future judgement can affect reputation long after actions are taken.","zh":"人們重視這一點，因為未來評價可在行動很久後仍影響聲譽。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how history will remember a person, group or institution.","zh":"這個短語重點在歷史會如何記住某人、群體或機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"preside obliviously over","meaning":"渾然不覺地目睹……發生","examples":[{"en":"Scientists should not preside obliviously over the disappearance of their own field of study.","zh":"科學家不應渾然不覺地目睹自己研究領域的消失。"},{"en":"To preside obliviously over something means to be in a position of responsibility while failing to notice or act on a serious problem.","zh":"preside obliviously over 某事，指身處負責位置，卻沒有注意或處理嚴重問題。"},{"en":"A headteacher would be criticised if she presided obliviously over falling reading standards.","zh":"如果校長渾然不覺地目睹閱讀水平下降，她會受到批評。"},{"en":"When leaders ignore a decline, the damage may become harder to reverse.","zh":"當領袖忽視衰退，傷害可能變得更難逆轉。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly criticises passive leadership in the face of loss.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評面對損失時的被動領導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the disappearance of","meaning":"……的消失","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are alarmed by the disappearance of minority languages.","zh":"研究人員對少數族群語言的消失感到震驚。"},{"en":"The disappearance of something means the process or fact of it no longer existing or being seen.","zh":"the disappearance of 某物，指它不再存在或不再被看見的過程或事實。"},{"en":"The disappearance of small shops can change the character of a neighbourhood.","zh":"小店的消失可以改變一個社區的特色。"},{"en":"If a language disappears, stories, names and local knowledge may disappear with it.","zh":"如果語言消失，故事、名稱和本地知識可能隨之消失。"},{"en":"The phrase often points to loss that is gradual but serious.","zh":"這個短語常指出逐漸但嚴重的損失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the field to which one is dedicated","meaning":"某人致力研究的領域","examples":[{"en":"Languages are the very field to which linguistics is dedicated.","zh":"語言正是語言學致力研究的領域。"},{"en":"The field to which one is dedicated is the subject or area someone has chosen to study or serve seriously.","zh":"the field to which one is dedicated 是某人選擇認真研究或服務的學科或範疇。"},{"en":"A doctor’s field may be children’s health if she has dedicated her career to paediatrics.","zh":"如果醫生把職業生涯投放於兒科，她致力的領域可能就是兒童健康。"},{"en":"If a field is disappearing, the people dedicated to it may feel a special responsibility.","zh":"如果一個領域正在消失，致力於該領域的人可能感到特別責任。"},{"en":"The phrase connects personal commitment with a professional area.","zh":"這個短語把個人投入與專業範疇連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"send a shudder through","meaning":"令……震驚","examples":[{"en":"Krauss’s prediction sent a shudder through the discipline of linguistics.","zh":"Krauss 的預測令語言學界震驚。"},{"en":"To send a shudder through a group means to shock or deeply disturb many people in that group.","zh":"send a shudder through 某群體，指令該群體中許多人震驚或深感不安。"},{"en":"News of a school closure can send a shudder through parents and teachers.","zh":"學校停辦的消息可以令家長和老師震驚。"},{"en":"A frightening prediction may make people realise that action is urgent.","zh":"令人害怕的預測可能令人意識到行動迫切。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a strong emotional reaction, not mild surprise.","zh":"這個短語暗示強烈情緒反應，而不是輕微驚訝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the discipline of linguistics","meaning":"語言學這門學科","examples":[{"en":"The discipline of linguistics studies the structure and use of language.","zh":"語言學這門學科研究語言的結構和使用。"},{"en":"The discipline of linguistics is the academic field that examines how languages work.","zh":"the discipline of linguistics 是研究語言如何運作的學術領域。"},{"en":"Students in linguistics may study grammar, sound systems and how children learn speech.","zh":"語言學學生可能研究語法、音系和兒童如何學說話。"},{"en":"Because linguistics studies language, language loss directly affects its research material.","zh":"因為語言學研究語言，語言流失直接影響它的研究材料。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to linguistics as a formal area of study.","zh":"這個短語指作為正式研究範疇的語言學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"make a prediction that","meaning":"預測……","examples":[{"en":"Krauss made a prediction that thousands of languages would disappear.","zh":"Krauss 預測數以千計語言將會消失。"},{"en":"To make a prediction that something will happen means to say what one believes will happen in the future.","zh":"make a prediction that 某事會發生，指說出自己相信未來會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"A teacher may predict that students will improve if they practise writing every week.","zh":"老師可能預測，如果學生每週練習寫作，他們會進步。"},{"en":"Predictions can guide action because they warn people about possible future results.","zh":"預測可以指導行動，因為它提醒人可能出現的未來結果。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a forecast, not a proven fact.","zh":"這個短語引出預測，而不是已證明事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cease to be uttered","meaning":"不再有人說","examples":[{"en":"Many minority languages may cease to be uttered within a century.","zh":"許多少數族群語言可能在一個世紀內不再有人說。"},{"en":"To cease to be uttered means to stop being spoken aloud by anyone.","zh":"cease to be uttered 指不再由任何人口頭說出。"},{"en":"A family word may cease to be uttered if younger relatives never learn it.","zh":"如果年輕親人從未學會，一個家族用語可能不再有人說。"},{"en":"When speakers die and children shift to another language, old words may fall silent.","zh":"當使用者去世而孩子轉用另一種語言，舊詞語可能沉默下來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes spoken disappearance, not just fewer books or records.","zh":"這個短語描述口語上的消失，而不只是書籍或記錄變少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"within a century","meaning":"在一個世紀內","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of languages could disappear within a century.","zh":"數以千計語言可能在一個世紀內消失。"},{"en":"Within a century means before one hundred years have passed.","zh":"within a century 指在一百年過去之前。"},{"en":"A city may change completely within a century as transport, housing and jobs develop.","zh":"隨着交通、住屋和工作發展，一座城市可能在一個世紀內完全改變。"},{"en":"If no young speakers remain, a language can disappear within a century or sooner.","zh":"如果沒有年輕使用者，一種語言可以在一個世紀內甚至更早消失。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a long but limited time frame.","zh":"這個短語給出長但有限的時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"direct a worldwide effort","meaning":"推動全球性的工作","examples":[{"en":"Scientists and community leaders must direct a worldwide effort to preserve languages.","zh":"科學家和社區領袖必須推動全球性的工作來保存語言。"},{"en":"To direct a worldwide effort means to organise and lead action across many countries.","zh":"direct a worldwide effort 指在多個國家組織和領導行動。"},{"en":"Public-health experts may direct a worldwide effort to control a fast-spreading disease.","zh":"公共衞生專家可能推動全球性的工作來控制快速傳播的疾病。"},{"en":"Global problems need coordination because one village or one university cannot solve them alone.","zh":"全球問題需要協調，因為一條村或一所大學不能單獨解決。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests leadership, planning and international cooperation.","zh":"這個短語暗示領導、規劃和國際合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stabilise the decline of","meaning":"穩定……的衰退情況","examples":[{"en":"Local programmes may help stabilise the decline of endangered languages.","zh":"本地計劃可能幫助穩定瀕危語言的衰退情況。"},{"en":"To stabilise the decline of something means to slow or stop its worsening.","zh":"stabilise the decline of 某事，指減慢或停止它惡化。"},{"en":"A school reading scheme may stabilise the decline of students’ vocabulary levels.","zh":"學校閱讀計劃可能穩定學生詞彙水平的下降。"},{"en":"If children begin using a language again, the loss of speakers may become less rapid.","zh":"如果孩子重新開始使用一種語言，使用者流失可能不再那麼快。"},{"en":"The phrase means preventing further collapse, not necessarily full recovery.","zh":"這個短語指防止進一步崩塌，不一定是完全復原。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"local languages","meaning":"地方語言","examples":[{"en":"Globalisation can place local languages under pressure.","zh":"全球化可以令地方語言承受壓力。"},{"en":"Local languages are languages used by particular communities, towns, regions or indigenous groups.","zh":"local languages 是特定社群、城鎮、地區或原住民群體使用的語言。"},{"en":"A small town may use a local language at home even if the national language is used at school.","zh":"即使學校使用國家語言，小鎮居民可能仍在家中使用地方語言。"},{"en":"If children need the dominant language for work, local languages may be used less often.","zh":"如果孩子工作需要主導語言，地方語言可能較少被使用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to community-based languages, not necessarily official languages.","zh":"這個短語指以社群為基礎的語言，不一定是官方語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"linguistic diversity","meaning":"語言多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Language extinction threatens the linguistic diversity of humankind.","zh":"語言滅絕威脅人類的語言多樣性。"},{"en":"Linguistic diversity means the variety of languages, dialects and speech forms in the world.","zh":"linguistic diversity 指世界上語言、方言和說話形式的多樣。"},{"en":"A city with many immigrant communities may have rich linguistic diversity.","zh":"一座有許多移民社群的城市可能有豐富的語言多樣性。"},{"en":"When small languages disappear, the world loses different ways of naming, thinking and storytelling.","zh":"當小語種消失，世界就失去不同命名、思考和講故事的方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes variety in human language.","zh":"這個短語描述人類語言上的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be doomed to extinction","meaning":"注定滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Without intervention, many languages may be doomed to extinction.","zh":"沒有干預的話，許多語言可能注定滅絕。"},{"en":"To be doomed to extinction means to be almost certain to disappear completely.","zh":"be doomed to extinction 指幾乎肯定會完全消失。"},{"en":"A village tradition may be doomed to extinction if no children learn it from elders.","zh":"如果沒有孩子向長者學習，村莊傳統可能注定消失。"},{"en":"When a language has only a few elderly speakers, its future becomes extremely fragile.","zh":"當一種語言只剩少數年長使用者，它的未來就變得極脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a very serious risk unless action is taken.","zh":"這個短語暗示若不行動，風險非常嚴重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an educated guess","meaning":"根據知識作出的推測","examples":[{"en":"Krauss admitted that his prediction was little more than an educated guess.","zh":"Krauss 承認他的預測不過是根據知識作出的推測。"},{"en":"An educated guess is a careful estimate based on knowledge, not random guessing.","zh":"an educated guess 是基於知識的謹慎估計，而不是隨意猜測。"},{"en":"A doctor may make an educated guess about an illness before test results arrive.","zh":"在檢測結果出來前，醫生可能對疾病作出有根據的推測。"},{"en":"Educated guesses can be useful, but they should be updated when better evidence appears.","zh":"有根據的推測可以有用，但當更好證據出現時應更新。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests informed uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語暗示有資訊基礎的不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"respected linguists","meaning":"備受尊重的語言學家","examples":[{"en":"Other respected linguists issued similar warnings.","zh":"其他備受尊重的語言學家發出類似警告。"},{"en":"Respected linguists are language scholars whose work is trusted by others in the field.","zh":"respected linguists 是其研究受到該領域其他人信任的語言學者。"},{"en":"A respected linguist may be invited to advise a school on bilingual education.","zh":"備受尊重的語言學家可能受邀就雙語教育向學校提供建議。"},{"en":"When respected experts agree about a danger, the warning becomes harder to ignore.","zh":"當備受尊重的專家同意某危險存在，警告就更難被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to professional credibility in language study.","zh":"這個短語指語言研究中的專業可信度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sound a similar alarm","meaning":"發出類似警報","examples":[{"en":"Several researchers sounded a similar alarm about language extinction.","zh":"幾名研究人員就語言滅絕發出類似警報。"},{"en":"To sound a similar alarm means to give a warning about the same danger.","zh":"sound a similar alarm 指就同一危險作出警告。"},{"en":"Several teachers may sound a similar alarm if many students stop reading at home.","zh":"如果許多學生停止在家閱讀，幾名老師可能發出類似警報。"},{"en":"Repeated warnings from different people can show that a problem is widespread.","zh":"來自不同人的反覆警告可以顯示問題很廣泛。"},{"en":"The phrase describes warning others before damage becomes worse.","zh":"這個短語描述在傷害惡化前警告他人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"carry out fieldwork on","meaning":"對……進行實地研究","examples":[{"en":"Kenneth Hale carried out fieldwork on several endangered languages.","zh":"Kenneth Hale 對幾種瀕危語言進行實地研究。"},{"en":"To carry out fieldwork on something means to study it directly in the place where it exists.","zh":"carry out fieldwork on 某事，指在它存在的地方直接研究它。"},{"en":"A geography student may carry out fieldwork on river pollution by collecting water samples.","zh":"地理學生可能透過收集水樣對河流污染進行實地研究。"},{"en":"Fieldwork helps researchers learn from real speakers, places and situations.","zh":"實地研究幫助研究人員向真實使用者、地方和情況學習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical research outside the office or classroom.","zh":"這個短語描述辦公室或課室以外的實際研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pass into extinction","meaning":"走向滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Several languages he had studied later passed into extinction.","zh":"他曾研究的幾種語言後來走向滅絕。"},{"en":"To pass into extinction means to disappear completely after a period of decline.","zh":"pass into extinction 指在一段衰退期後完全消失。"},{"en":"A local craft may pass into extinction if no apprentice learns it from older workers.","zh":"如果沒有學徒向年長工匠學習，本地手藝可能走向消失。"},{"en":"When the last speaker dies, a language may pass into extinction unless it has been revived.","zh":"當最後一名使用者去世，語言可能走向滅絕，除非已被復興。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a gradual movement into permanent loss.","zh":"這個短語暗示逐步走向永久損失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a nationwide survey","meaning":"全國性調查","examples":[{"en":"A nationwide survey examined the condition of Aboriginal languages in Australia.","zh":"一項全國性調查研究澳洲原住民語言的狀況。"},{"en":"A nationwide survey is research that collects information from across an entire country.","zh":"nationwide survey 是從整個國家收集資訊的研究。"},{"en":"A nationwide survey of students may ask about sleep, homework and exam stress.","zh":"一項全國性學生調查可能詢問睡眠、功課和考試壓力。"},{"en":"Such a survey can reveal patterns that one town or school cannot show.","zh":"這類調查可以揭示一個城鎮或學校不能顯示的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research with national coverage.","zh":"這個短語描述具有全國涵蓋面的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"surviving Aboriginal languages","meaning":"仍然存在的澳洲原住民語言","examples":[{"en":"Many surviving Aboriginal languages were no longer spoken by every generation.","zh":"許多仍然存在的澳洲原住民語言已不再由每一代人使用。"},{"en":"Surviving Aboriginal languages are Indigenous Australian languages that still exist in some form.","zh":"surviving Aboriginal languages 是仍以某種形式存在的澳洲原住民語言。"},{"en":"A surviving language may be known by elders even if children no longer speak it fluently.","zh":"一種仍存在的語言可能由長者知道，即使孩子已不能流利使用。"},{"en":"If a language is not passed to every generation, its survival becomes uncertain.","zh":"如果語言沒有傳給每一代，它的存續就變得不確定。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on languages that remain, but may still be endangered.","zh":"這個短語重點在仍然存在但可能仍瀕危的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"no longer be used regularly","meaning":"不再經常使用","examples":[{"en":"Some languages are no longer used regularly by younger speakers.","zh":"有些語言不再由年輕使用者經常使用。"},{"en":"To no longer be used regularly means to stop being used often in normal life.","zh":"no longer be used regularly 指不再在日常生活中經常使用。"},{"en":"A family recipe may no longer be used regularly if everyone starts buying takeaway food.","zh":"如果人人開始買外賣，家庭食譜可能不再經常使用。"},{"en":"When a language is not used at home, school or work, speakers may slowly lose fluency.","zh":"當語言不在家中、學校或工作中使用，使用者可能慢慢失去流利程度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reduced everyday use, not necessarily complete disappearance.","zh":"這個短語描述日常使用減少，不一定是完全消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"all age groups","meaning":"所有年齡組別","examples":[{"en":"A healthy language is normally used by people in all age groups.","zh":"健康的語言通常由所有年齡組別的人使用。"},{"en":"All age groups means children, teenagers, adults and elderly people together.","zh":"all age groups 指兒童、青少年、成年人和長者合在一起。"},{"en":"A public park should be safe and useful for all age groups.","zh":"公園應對所有年齡組別安全且有用。"},{"en":"If only old people speak a language, the next generation may not continue it.","zh":"如果只有老人說一種語言，下一代可能不會延續它。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses wide participation across ages.","zh":"這個短語強調跨年齡的廣泛參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"all but","meaning":"除了……之外全部","examples":[{"en":"All but a small number of the languages were seriously endangered.","zh":"除了少數語言之外，所有語言都嚴重瀕危。"},{"en":"All but means everyone or everything except the people or things mentioned.","zh":"all but 指除了所提到的人或事物外，其餘全部。"},{"en":"All but two students submitted the homework on time.","zh":"除了兩名學生外，所有學生都準時交功課。"},{"en":"If all but a few shops close, the street becomes much quieter.","zh":"如果除了少數商店外全部關門，街道會安靜得多。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful for showing that only a small exception remains.","zh":"這個短語適合顯示只剩小例外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Native American languages","meaning":"美洲原住民語言","examples":[{"en":"Many Native American languages are spoken by only small communities.","zh":"許多美洲原住民語言只由小社群使用。"},{"en":"Native American languages are languages traditionally used by Indigenous peoples of North America.","zh":"Native American languages 是北美原住民傳統使用的語言。"},{"en":"A school may offer classes in a Native American language to help young people reconnect with heritage.","zh":"學校可能開設美洲原住民語言課程，幫助年輕人重新連繫文化傳承。"},{"en":"When a community is small, each fluent speaker becomes especially important.","zh":"當社群很小，每位流利使用者都變得特別重要。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to Indigenous languages, not English varieties in America.","zh":"這個短語指原住民語言，而不是美國英語變體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be spoken or remembered","meaning":"仍有人說或記得","examples":[{"en":"Some languages are no longer actively spoken but are still remembered.","zh":"有些語言已不再被積極使用，但仍有人記得。"},{"en":"To be spoken or remembered means to be used in conversation or at least still known by memory.","zh":"be spoken or remembered 指在對話中使用，或至少仍被人記在腦中。"},{"en":"A family dialect may be remembered by grandparents even if grandchildren rarely speak it.","zh":"家族方言可能由祖父母記得，即使孫輩很少說。"},{"en":"Remembered words can help revival work, but memory alone is weaker than daily use.","zh":"被記得的詞語可以幫助復興工作，但單靠記憶弱於日常使用。"},{"en":"The phrase shows different levels of language survival.","zh":"這個短語顯示語言存續的不同程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a congressional panel","meaning":"國會專責小組","examples":[{"en":"Krauss presented evidence to a congressional panel in 1992.","zh":"Krauss 於1992年向國會專責小組提交證據。"},{"en":"A congressional panel is a small group within a congress that examines a particular issue.","zh":"congressional panel 是國會內研究特定議題的小組。"},{"en":"Experts may speak to a congressional panel about education, health or environmental problems.","zh":"專家可能向國會專責小組講解教育、健康或環境問題。"},{"en":"Such panels gather evidence before recommending laws or public action.","zh":"這些小組在建議法律或公共行動前收集證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to an official government discussion group.","zh":"這個短語指官方政府討論小組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"experts in the field","meaning":"該領域的專家","examples":[{"en":"Many experts in the field are deeply concerned about language loss.","zh":"該領域的許多專家對語言流失深感擔憂。"},{"en":"Experts in the field are people with specialist knowledge in a particular area.","zh":"experts in the field 是在某特定範疇中有專門知識的人。"},{"en":"A hospital may ask experts in the field before introducing a new treatment policy.","zh":"醫院在推出新治療政策前，可能諮詢該領域的專家。"},{"en":"When experts in the field agree, their view often carries more weight.","zh":"當該領域專家意見一致，他們的看法通常更有分量。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to knowledgeable specialists, not general observers.","zh":"這個短語指具知識的專家，而不是一般旁觀者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mourn the loss of","meaning":"為失去……感到惋惜","examples":[{"en":"Linguists mourn the loss of rare languages for several reasons.","zh":"語言學家因幾個原因為失去罕見語言感到惋惜。"},{"en":"To mourn the loss of something means to feel sadness because something valuable has disappeared.","zh":"mourn the loss of 某物，指因有價值的東西消失而感到悲傷。"},{"en":"A community may mourn the loss of an old theatre that held many memories.","zh":"一個社區可能為失去承載許多記憶的舊劇院感到惋惜。"},{"en":"People mourn such losses because they cannot easily be replaced.","zh":"人們為這類損失難過，因為它們不容易被取代。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses grief over cultural, personal or social disappearance.","zh":"這個短語表達對文化、個人或社會消失的哀傷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rare languages","meaning":"罕見語言","examples":[{"en":"Rare languages may contain structures found nowhere else.","zh":"罕見語言可能包含在其他地方找不到的結構。"},{"en":"Rare languages are languages spoken by few people or found in only limited communities.","zh":"rare languages 是由少數人使用或只存在於有限社群中的語言。"},{"en":"A rare language may preserve old words for plants, rivers and family relationships.","zh":"罕見語言可能保存植物、河流和家庭關係的古老詞語。"},{"en":"If a rare language disappears, unique grammar and knowledge may disappear with it.","zh":"如果罕見語言消失，獨特語法和知識可能隨之消失。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on languages that are uncommon and often vulnerable.","zh":"這個短語重點在不常見且往往脆弱的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"to start with","meaning":"首先","examples":[{"en":"To start with, endangered languages have considerable scientific value.","zh":"首先，瀕危語言具有相當大的科學價值。"},{"en":"To start with means first, or as the first point in an explanation.","zh":"to start with 指首先，或作為解釋中的第一點。"},{"en":"To start with, a student should read the question before choosing an answer.","zh":"首先，學生應先讀題目再選答案。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise ideas by introducing the first reason or step.","zh":"這個短語透過引出第一個原因或步驟來幫助組織想法。"},{"en":"It is useful when more points will follow.","zh":"當之後還有更多觀點時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"scientific self-interest","meaning":"科學上的自身利益","examples":[{"en":"Scientific self-interest is one reason linguists want to preserve rare languages.","zh":"科學上的自身利益是語言學家想保存罕見語言的一個原因。"},{"en":"Scientific self-interest means researchers want to protect something partly because it benefits their own field of study.","zh":"scientific self-interest 指研究人員想保護某物，部分原因是它有利於自己的研究領域。"},{"en":"A doctor may support patient databases partly from scientific self-interest because they improve future research.","zh":"醫生可能部分基於科學上的自身利益支持病人資料庫，因為它改善未來研究。"},{"en":"This motive is not necessarily selfish; it can also serve wider knowledge.","zh":"這種動機不一定自私；它也可以服務更廣泛知識。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why scholars may care strongly about preserving research material.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何學者可能強烈關心保存研究材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have to do with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Many linguistic questions have to do with the limits of human speech.","zh":"許多語言學問題與人類語言能力的界限有關。"},{"en":"To have to do with something means to be connected with or related to it.","zh":"have to do with 某事，指與它有連繫或相關。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may have to do with poor sleep rather than laziness.","zh":"學生疲倦可能與睡眠差有關，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"Finding what a problem has to do with helps people choose the right solution.","zh":"找出問題與甚麼有關，幫助人選擇正確解決方法。"},{"en":"The phrase is a natural way to show connection.","zh":"這個短語是表示連繫的自然說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the limits of human speech","meaning":"人類語言能力的界限","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are still exploring the limits of human speech.","zh":"研究人員仍在探索人類語言能力的界限。"},{"en":"The limits of human speech are the boundaries of what human languages can sound like or express.","zh":"the limits of human speech 是人類語言能如何發聲或表達的邊界。"},{"en":"Linguists study unusual sounds to understand the limits of human speech.","zh":"語言學家研究不尋常語音，以理解人類語言能力的界限。"},{"en":"Rare languages may show possibilities that common languages do not show.","zh":"罕見語言可能展示常見語言沒有展示的可能性。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to how far human language ability can go.","zh":"這個短語指人類語言能力可以走多遠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"far from fully explored","meaning":"遠未得到充分研究","examples":[{"en":"The range of possible language structures is far from fully explored.","zh":"可能存在的語言結構範圍遠未得到充分研究。"},{"en":"Far from fully explored means not yet studied or understood completely.","zh":"far from fully explored 指尚未被完全研究或理解。"},{"en":"The effects of online learning on young children are far from fully explored.","zh":"網上學習對幼童的影響遠未得到充分研究。"},{"en":"When an area is not fully explored, researchers should avoid making final claims too quickly.","zh":"當某範疇尚未充分研究，研究人員應避免太快作最終結論。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that much more investigation is needed.","zh":"這個短語暗示仍需要更多調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"structural elements","meaning":"結構元素","examples":[{"en":"Researchers compare the structural elements of different languages.","zh":"研究人員比較不同語言的結構元素。"},{"en":"Structural elements are the basic parts that make up the organisation of a language or system.","zh":"structural elements 是構成語言或系統組織方式的基本部分。"},{"en":"In English, word order and verb forms are important structural elements.","zh":"在英語中，語序和動詞形式是重要結構元素。"},{"en":"Comparing structural elements helps linguists see how languages are similar or different.","zh":"比較結構元素幫助語言學家看見語言如何相似或不同。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the building blocks of a system.","zh":"這個短語重點在系統的組成部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"grammar and vocabulary","meaning":"語法和詞彙","examples":[{"en":"Every language has its own system of grammar and vocabulary.","zh":"每種語言都有自己的語法和詞彙系統。"},{"en":"Grammar and vocabulary mean the rules of a language and the words used in it.","zh":"grammar and vocabulary 指一種語言的規則以及其中使用的詞語。"},{"en":"A student needs both grammar and vocabulary to write a clear email.","zh":"學生需要語法和詞彙才能寫清楚電郵。"},{"en":"If vocabulary is missing, ideas are hard to express; if grammar is weak, meaning may be unclear.","zh":"如果缺乏詞彙，想法難以表達；如果語法薄弱，意思可能不清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both structure and word knowledge.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋結構和詞語知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be truly universal","meaning":"真正具有普遍性","examples":[{"en":"Linguists ask whether any grammatical features are truly universal.","zh":"語言學家問是否有任何語法特徵真正具有普遍性。"},{"en":"To be truly universal means to exist or apply everywhere, without important exceptions.","zh":"be truly universal 指在所有地方存在或適用，沒有重要例外。"},{"en":"A school rule is truly universal only if it applies to every student in every class.","zh":"校規只有在適用於每班每名學生時，才是真正普遍。"},{"en":"If one language lacks a feature, that feature cannot be called universal.","zh":"如果有一種語言缺乏某特徵，該特徵就不能稱為普遍。"},{"en":"The phrase tests whether something is genuinely common to all cases.","zh":"這個短語測試某事是否真正共同存在於所有個案中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be hardwired into the brain","meaning":"天生固定在腦內","examples":[{"en":"Some language abilities may be hardwired into the human brain.","zh":"有些語言能力可能天生固定在人腦內。"},{"en":"To be hardwired into the brain means to be built into the mind naturally rather than learned only from experience.","zh":"be hardwired into the brain 指自然內置於頭腦中，而不只是從經驗學來。"},{"en":"Babies may be hardwired to notice human voices before they understand words.","zh":"嬰兒可能天生就會注意人聲，早於理解字詞。"},{"en":"If an ability is hardwired, children may develop it even without formal teaching.","zh":"如果能力是天生固定的，孩子即使沒有正式教學也可能發展它。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests an inborn mental tendency.","zh":"這個短語暗示天生心理傾向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"reconstruct ancient migration patterns","meaning":"重構古代遷徙模式","examples":[{"en":"Scientists use linguistic evidence to reconstruct ancient migration patterns.","zh":"科學家使用語言證據來重構古代遷徙模式。"},{"en":"To reconstruct ancient migration patterns means to work out how people moved in the distant past.","zh":"reconstruct ancient migration patterns 指推斷遠古人群如何移動。"},{"en":"Historians may use old place names to reconstruct how families settled in a region.","zh":"歷史學家可能使用舊地名來重構家族如何定居某地區。"},{"en":"Similar words in distant communities can suggest earlier contact or movement.","zh":"遠距離社群中相似詞語可能暗示早期接觸或遷移。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using evidence to rebuild a picture of past travel.","zh":"這個短語描述用證據重建過去移動圖像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"borrowed words","meaning":"外來借詞","examples":[{"en":"Borrowed words can reveal historical contact between communities.","zh":"外來借詞可以揭示社群之間的歷史接觸。"},{"en":"Borrowed words are words taken from one language and used in another.","zh":"borrowed words 是從一種語言借入並在另一種語言中使用的詞語。"},{"en":"English uses borrowed words such as “piano” from Italian and “café” from French.","zh":"英語使用外來借詞，例如來自意大利語的 “piano” 和來自法語的 “café”。"},{"en":"Borrowed words often appear when people trade, migrate or live near each other.","zh":"當人們貿易、遷移或住得相近，外來借詞常會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase shows how language records contact between cultures.","zh":"這個短語顯示語言如何記錄文化接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"appear in otherwise unrelated languages","meaning":"出現在本來互不相關的語言中","examples":[{"en":"Similar borrowed words may appear in otherwise unrelated languages.","zh":"相似外來借詞可能出現在本來互不相關的語言中。"},{"en":"To appear in otherwise unrelated languages means to be found in languages that are not normally connected by family origin.","zh":"appear in otherwise unrelated languages 指出現在通常沒有語族關係的語言中。"},{"en":"A food word may appear in unrelated languages if many countries trade the same product.","zh":"如果許多國家交易同一產品，某食物詞可能出現在互不相關的語言中。"},{"en":"Shared borrowed words can show contact even when the languages are not historically related.","zh":"共同借詞可以顯示接觸，即使語言在歷史上並不相關。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights similarity caused by borrowing, not shared ancestry.","zh":"這個短語突出由借用造成的相似，而不是共同祖源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"unrelated languages","meaning":"互不相關的語言","examples":[{"en":"Two unrelated languages may still share words through cultural contact.","zh":"兩種互不相關的語言仍可能透過文化接觸共享詞語。"},{"en":"Unrelated languages are languages that do not come from the same language family.","zh":"unrelated languages 是並非來自同一語族的語言。"},{"en":"Chinese and English are unrelated languages, but both use some borrowed international words.","zh":"中文和英文是互不相關的語言，但兩者都使用一些國際借詞。"},{"en":"Contact through trade, religion or migration can create similarities between unrelated languages.","zh":"貿易、宗教或遷移接觸可以在互不相關的語言之間造成相似。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to languages without a common linguistic origin.","zh":"這個短語指沒有共同語言起源的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a wider portfolio of languages","meaning":"更廣泛的語言研究範圍","examples":[{"en":"A wider portfolio of languages gives researchers stronger evidence.","zh":"更廣泛的語言研究範圍給研究人員更強證據。"},{"en":"A wider portfolio of languages means a broader collection of languages included in study or comparison.","zh":"a wider portfolio of languages 指納入研究或比較的語言集合更廣。"},{"en":"A language teacher may use a wider portfolio of examples from English, French and Japanese to explain word order.","zh":"語言老師可能使用來自英語、法語和日語的更廣泛例子來解釋語序。"},{"en":"Studying more languages reduces the risk of drawing conclusions from too few cases.","zh":"研究更多語言可降低從太少個案得出結論的風險。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests broader coverage and stronger comparison.","zh":"這個短語暗示更廣覆蓋和更強比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the more…, the more likely…","meaning":"越……，便越有可能……","examples":[{"en":"The more languages researchers study, the more likely they are to reach accurate conclusions.","zh":"研究人員研究的語言越多，便越有可能得出準確結論。"},{"en":"The more…, the more likely… means that as one thing increases, the chance of another thing also increases.","zh":"the more…, the more likely… 指一件事增加時，另一件事發生的機會也增加。"},{"en":"The more a student reads, the more likely she is to recognise useful vocabulary in exams.","zh":"學生閱讀越多，便越有可能在考試中認出有用詞彙。"},{"en":"More practice usually increases the chance of better performance.","zh":"練習越多，通常表現更好的機會就越高。"},{"en":"The structure shows a clear relationship between increase and probability.","zh":"這個結構顯示增加與可能性之間的清楚關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get the right answers","meaning":"得出正確答案","examples":[{"en":"Studying diverse languages helps scientists get the right answers.","zh":"研究多樣語言幫助科學家得出正確答案。"},{"en":"To get the right answers means to reach correct conclusions or solutions.","zh":"get the right answers 指得出正確結論或解決方法。"},{"en":"A student can get the right answers more often if she checks the question carefully.","zh":"如果學生仔細檢查題目，她更常能得出正確答案。"},{"en":"Better evidence increases the chance of choosing the correct explanation.","zh":"更好的證據會增加選擇正確解釋的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on accuracy, not speed alone.","zh":"這個短語重點在準確，而不只是速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a near-constant buzz about","meaning":"對……持續不斷的熱議","examples":[{"en":"There has been a near-constant buzz about endangered languages in linguistics.","zh":"語言學界一直對瀕危語言有近乎持續不斷的熱議。"},{"en":"A near-constant buzz about something is frequent discussion and attention surrounding it.","zh":"a near-constant buzz about 某事，指圍繞它頻繁討論和關注。"},{"en":"There may be a near-constant buzz about a new exam policy if students keep discussing it.","zh":"如果學生一直討論新考試政策，就可能出現持續不斷的熱議。"},{"en":"Constant discussion can raise awareness, but it does not always lead to action.","zh":"持續討論可以提高意識，但不一定帶來行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ongoing talk and excitement around a topic.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞某題目的持續談論和興奮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"over the past decade","meaning":"在過去十年","examples":[{"en":"Concern about language extinction has grown over the past decade.","zh":"在過去十年，對語言滅絕的關注有所增加。"},{"en":"Over the past decade means during the last ten years.","zh":"over the past decade 指在最近十年期間。"},{"en":"Over the past decade, many schools have used more online learning tools.","zh":"在過去十年，許多學校使用了更多網上學習工具。"},{"en":"Changes over ten years can reveal a clear trend rather than a short-term event.","zh":"十年間的變化可以揭示清楚趨勢，而不是短期事件。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a recent ten-year time frame.","zh":"這個短語給出最近十年的時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"accomplish depressingly little","meaning":"取得的成果少得令人沮喪","examples":[{"en":"Despite widespread concern, the field accomplished depressingly little.","zh":"儘管關注廣泛，該領域取得的成果少得令人沮喪。"},{"en":"To accomplish depressingly little means to achieve very little, in a way that feels disappointing.","zh":"accomplish depressingly little 指取得非常少成果，令人失望。"},{"en":"A committee may accomplish depressingly little if it holds meetings but never changes school policy.","zh":"如果委員會只開會卻從不改變校政，它可能成果少得令人沮喪。"},{"en":"Talk without funding, planning or action can lead to very small results.","zh":"沒有資金、計劃或行動的討論，可能只帶來很少結果。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses frustration at a lack of progress.","zh":"這個短語表達對缺乏進展的沮喪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"an organised response to","meaning":"對……有組織的回應","examples":[{"en":"Experts expected an organised response to the language crisis.","zh":"專家期待對語言危機有組織的回應。"},{"en":"An organised response to a problem is a planned and coordinated set of actions.","zh":"organised response to 問題，指有計劃、協調好的行動。"},{"en":"A school needs an organised response to bullying, not just one angry warning.","zh":"學校需要對欺凌有組織的回應，而不只是一句憤怒警告。"},{"en":"When many people work together with a plan, a crisis is easier to manage.","zh":"當許多人按計劃合作，危機較容易管理。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests structure, cooperation and practical steps.","zh":"這個短語暗示結構、合作和實際步驟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a dire situation","meaning":"極其嚴峻的情況","examples":[{"en":"The rapid disappearance of languages represents a dire situation.","zh":"語言快速消失代表極其嚴峻的情況。"},{"en":"A dire situation is a very serious and worrying situation.","zh":"dire situation 是非常嚴重且令人擔憂的情況。"},{"en":"A hospital faces a dire situation if there are too many patients and too few nurses.","zh":"如果病人太多而護士太少，醫院就面對極其嚴峻的情況。"},{"en":"Dire situations require urgent action because delay can make the damage worse.","zh":"嚴峻情況需要緊急行動，因為延誤會令傷害更嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase signals severity and danger.","zh":"這個短語表示嚴重性和危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make an attempt to determine","meaning":"嘗試判斷","examples":[{"en":"Linguists should make an attempt to determine which languages can be saved.","zh":"語言學家應嘗試判斷哪些語言可以得以挽救。"},{"en":"To make an attempt to determine something means to try to find out or decide it.","zh":"make an attempt to determine 某事，指嘗試查明或決定它。"},{"en":"A teacher may attempt to determine why a class performed poorly before changing lessons.","zh":"老師可能先嘗試判斷為何一班表現差，再改變課堂。"},{"en":"Careful investigation helps people choose where limited resources should go.","zh":"仔細調查幫助人選擇有限資源應投放在哪裏。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a deliberate effort to reach a judgement.","zh":"這個短語暗示有意識地努力作出判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be saved","meaning":"得以挽救","examples":[{"en":"Some endangered languages may still be saved through community action.","zh":"有些瀕危語言仍可能透過社區行動得以挽救。"},{"en":"To be saved means to be rescued from loss, danger or destruction.","zh":"be saved 指從損失、危險或破壞中被救回。"},{"en":"An old theatre may be saved if residents raise money and use it for community events.","zh":"如果居民籌款並用舊劇院舉辦社區活動，它可能得以挽救。"},{"en":"A language can be saved when children learn it and adults use it regularly.","zh":"當孩子學習一種語言，而成年人定期使用它，該語言可以得以挽救。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that danger exists, but recovery is still possible.","zh":"這個短語暗示危險存在，但仍有恢復可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be documented before","meaning":"在……之前被記錄","examples":[{"en":"Languages that cannot be revived should be documented before they disappear.","zh":"不能復興的語言應在消失前被記錄。"},{"en":"To be documented before something happens means to be recorded earlier, while there is still time.","zh":"be documented before 某事發生，指趁仍有時間先被記錄。"},{"en":"Old family recipes should be documented before the grandparents who know them pass away.","zh":"老一輩仍知道的家庭食譜，應在祖父母離世前被記錄。"},{"en":"If information is not recorded in time, it may be lost permanently.","zh":"如果資訊沒有及時記錄，可能會永久失去。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses recording before it is too late.","zh":"這個短語強調在太遲之前記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"no such effort","meaning":"沒有這種工作","examples":[{"en":"At the time, no such effort had been organised across the profession.","zh":"當時，整個專業界別內沒有這種工作被組織起來。"},{"en":"No such effort means that no effort of that kind existed or had been made.","zh":"no such effort 指沒有那種努力存在或曾經作出。"},{"en":"A school may discuss mental health often, but have no such effort to train teachers properly.","zh":"學校可能常討論心理健康，卻沒有這種正式訓練老師的工作。"},{"en":"Without a real effort, concern remains only talk.","zh":"沒有真正努力，關注只會停留在談論。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts expected action with actual absence.","zh":"這個短語把預期行動與實際缺席作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be organised within the profession","meaning":"在專業界別內組織起來","examples":[{"en":"Language preservation had not been properly organised within the profession.","zh":"語言保存工作尚未在專業界別內妥善組織起來。"},{"en":"To be organised within the profession means to be planned and coordinated by people in that field.","zh":"be organised within the profession 指由該領域的人規劃和協調。"},{"en":"Teacher training may be organised within the profession by experienced educators.","zh":"教師培訓可能由有經驗教育工作者在專業界別內組織起來。"},{"en":"When work is organised within a profession, standards and resources can be shared more easily.","zh":"當工作在專業內組織起來，標準和資源較容易共享。"},{"en":"The phrase describes coordination inside a professional community.","zh":"這個短語描述專業社群內部的協調。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"become fashionable enough to","meaning":"變得相當受重視而有人去……","examples":[{"en":"It only recently became fashionable enough to work on endangered languages.","zh":"研究瀕危語言只是近年才變得相當受重視而有人去做。"},{"en":"To become fashionable enough to do something means to become accepted or popular enough for people to take it up.","zh":"become fashionable enough to do something 指變得足夠被接受或受歡迎，令人開始做它。"},{"en":"Recycling became fashionable enough for many schools to set up student recycling teams.","zh":"回收變得相當受重視後，許多學校設立學生回收隊。"},{"en":"When an issue becomes fashionable, funding and attention may become easier to find.","zh":"當一個議題變得受重視，資金和關注可能較容易找到。"},{"en":"The phrase can suggest that people acted late because the topic was not previously valued.","zh":"這個短語可暗示人們行動較遲，因為該題目以前未被重視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"raise money to deal with","meaning":"籌款處理……","examples":[{"en":"Researchers struggled to raise money to deal with language extinction.","zh":"研究人員很難籌款處理語言滅絕問題。"},{"en":"To raise money to deal with a problem means to collect funds so action can be taken.","zh":"raise money to deal with 問題，指籌集資金以便採取行動。"},{"en":"Parents may raise money to deal with a school’s shortage of library books.","zh":"家長可能籌款處理學校圖書館書籍不足問題。"},{"en":"Without funding, even well-planned projects may not begin.","zh":"沒有資金，即使計劃完善的項目也可能無法開始。"},{"en":"The phrase connects fundraising with practical problem-solving.","zh":"這個短語把籌款與實際解難連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be met with blank stares","meaning":"得到茫然的反應","examples":[{"en":"Whalen’s questions about funding were often met with blank stares.","zh":"Whalen 關於資金的問題常得到茫然的反應。"},{"en":"To be met with blank stares means people respond with confusion, silence or no understanding.","zh":"be met with blank stares 指人們以困惑、沉默或不理解回應。"},{"en":"A teacher’s question may be met with blank stares if the class has not understood the topic.","zh":"如果全班未理解題目，老師的問題可能得到茫然反應。"},{"en":"Blank stares can show that people are unprepared or do not see the importance of an issue.","zh":"茫然反應可以顯示人們沒有準備，或看不到議題重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a disappointing lack of response.","zh":"這個短語描述令人失望的缺乏回應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"found an organisation","meaning":"創立機構","examples":[{"en":"Several linguists founded an organisation to support preservation research.","zh":"幾名語言學家創立機構以支持保存研究。"},{"en":"To found an organisation means to create and formally start a group or institution.","zh":"found an organisation 指創建並正式成立一個團體或機構。"},{"en":"Parents may found an organisation to support children with special learning needs.","zh":"家長可能創立機構以支援有特殊學習需要的兒童。"},{"en":"Founding an organisation can turn individual concern into coordinated action.","zh":"創立機構可以把個人關注轉化為協調行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes starting a structured group for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述為某目的建立有結構團體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the Endangered Languages Fund","meaning":"瀕危語言基金","examples":[{"en":"The Endangered Languages Fund provides grants for language research.","zh":"瀕危語言基金為語言研究提供撥款。"},{"en":"The Endangered Languages Fund is an organisation that supports work on languages at risk of disappearing.","zh":"the Endangered Languages Fund 是支持瀕危語言工作的機構。"},{"en":"A researcher may apply to the fund to record stories from the last fluent speakers.","zh":"研究人員可能向該基金申請資助，以記錄最後流利使用者的故事。"},{"en":"Funding can help cover travel, recording equipment and community training.","zh":"資金可以幫助支付旅費、錄音設備和社區培訓。"},{"en":"The phrase names a specific organisation for language preservation.","zh":"這個短語指出一個語言保存的特定機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"collect funds for","meaning":"為……籌集資金","examples":[{"en":"The organisation collected funds for research grants.","zh":"該機構為研究撥款籌集資金。"},{"en":"To collect funds for something means to gather money to support that purpose.","zh":"collect funds for 某事，指籌集金錢以支持該目的。"},{"en":"A school may collect funds for new computers by holding a charity fair.","zh":"學校可能透過舉辦慈善市集為新電腦籌集資金。"},{"en":"Collected funds allow projects to move from ideas to real action.","zh":"籌得的資金讓項目由想法變成實際行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised fundraising for a specific goal.","zh":"這個短語描述為特定目標進行有組織籌款。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"research grants","meaning":"研究撥款","examples":[{"en":"Small research grants can support urgent documentation projects.","zh":"小額研究撥款可以支持緊急記錄項目。"},{"en":"Research grants are sums of money given to fund academic or scientific work.","zh":"research grants 是用來資助學術或科學工作的款項。"},{"en":"A university student may receive a research grant to study local air pollution.","zh":"大學生可能獲得研究撥款來研究本地空氣污染。"},{"en":"Grants make it possible to buy equipment, travel or hire assistants.","zh":"撥款使購買設備、出行或聘請助手成為可能。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to funding for investigation or study.","zh":"這個短語指用於調查或研究的資金。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a similar foundation","meaning":"類似的基金會","examples":[{"en":"A similar foundation was established in England.","zh":"英格蘭成立了一個類似的基金會。"},{"en":"A similar foundation is another organisation created for a related purpose.","zh":"a similar foundation 是為相關目的而創立的另一個組織。"},{"en":"If one city starts a food bank, a similar foundation may later appear in another city.","zh":"如果一座城市開設食物銀行，另一座城市之後可能出現類似基金會。"},{"en":"Similar organisations can spread a successful idea to new places.","zh":"類似機構可以把成功想法傳到新地方。"},{"en":"The phrase compares one organisation with another of the same general type.","zh":"這個短語比較同一大類的兩個組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"raise only a small sum","meaning":"只籌得一小筆款項","examples":[{"en":"The English foundation managed to raise only a small sum of money.","zh":"英格蘭的基金會只籌得一小筆款項。"},{"en":"To raise only a small sum means to collect a limited amount of money, less than hoped.","zh":"raise only a small sum 指只籌到有限金額，少於期望。"},{"en":"A class may raise only a small sum if few parents attend the fundraising event.","zh":"如果少數家長出席籌款活動，一班學生可能只籌得一小筆款項。"},{"en":"Small funding can limit how many people a project can help.","zh":"資金少會限制項目能幫助多少人。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests disappointing financial support.","zh":"這個短語暗示令人失望的財政支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"encouraging signs","meaning":"令人鼓舞的跡象","examples":[{"en":"There are encouraging signs that language preservation is receiving more support.","zh":"有令人鼓舞的跡象顯示語言保存正獲得更多支持。"},{"en":"Encouraging signs are small pieces of evidence showing that a situation may improve.","zh":"encouraging signs 是顯示情況可能改善的小證據。"},{"en":"More students joining a reading club is an encouraging sign for a school library.","zh":"更多學生加入閱讀會，是學校圖書館的令人鼓舞跡象。"},{"en":"Positive signs can help people continue working even when progress is slow.","zh":"正面跡象可以在進展緩慢時幫助人們繼續努力。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests hope, but not complete success yet.","zh":"這個短語暗示希望，但尚未是完全成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"turn a corner","meaning":"渡過難關並開始改善","examples":[{"en":"The field may finally have turned a corner in its response to language loss.","zh":"該領域在回應語言流失方面可能終於渡過難關並開始改善。"},{"en":"To turn a corner means to pass the worst point and begin to improve.","zh":"turn a corner 指越過最差階段並開始改善。"},{"en":"A student may turn a corner after weeks of poor grades when she finally learns how to revise.","zh":"學生在數星期成績差後終於學會如何溫習，可能就渡過難關。"},{"en":"New funding or clear planning can help a struggling project improve.","zh":"新資金或清楚計劃可以幫助困難項目改善。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a positive change after difficulty.","zh":"這個短語暗示困難後的正面轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"issue a second round of grants","meaning":"發放第二輪撥款","examples":[{"en":"The foundation issued a second round of grants for documentation projects.","zh":"基金會為記錄項目發放第二輪撥款。"},{"en":"To issue a second round of grants means to provide another set of funding after the first one.","zh":"issue a second round of grants 指在第一批之後再提供另一批資金。"},{"en":"A school foundation may issue a second round of grants if the first projects are successful.","zh":"如果第一批項目成功，學校基金可能發放第二輪撥款。"},{"en":"Additional funding allows more teams to begin or continue their work.","zh":"額外資金讓更多團隊開始或繼續工作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to repeated financial support.","zh":"這個短語指重複提供財政支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"total more than","meaning":"合共超過","examples":[{"en":"The grants totalled more than two million dollars.","zh":"這些撥款合共超過二百萬美元。"},{"en":"To total more than an amount means to add up to a number higher than that amount.","zh":"total more than 某數額，指加起來高於該數額。"},{"en":"The cost of books and uniforms may total more than a family expected.","zh":"書本和校服費用合共可能超過家庭預期。"},{"en":"When donations total more than the target, a project can expand.","zh":"當捐款合共超過目標，項目可以擴展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the combined amount.","zh":"這個短語描述合計金額。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"multimedia archive","meaning":"多媒體檔案庫","examples":[{"en":"The foundation created a multimedia archive for endangered-language materials.","zh":"基金會為瀕危語言材料建立多媒體檔案庫。"},{"en":"A multimedia archive is a collection that stores materials such as audio, video, text and images.","zh":"multimedia archive 是儲存音頻、影片、文字和圖片等材料的集合。"},{"en":"A school may build a multimedia archive of interviews with older residents.","zh":"學校可能建立訪問年長居民的多媒體檔案庫。"},{"en":"Multimedia records preserve pronunciation, gesture and daily use better than written notes alone.","zh":"多媒體記錄比單靠文字筆記更能保存發音、手勢和日常使用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a digital or physical collection using different media formats.","zh":"這個短語指使用不同媒體格式的數碼或實體收藏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"house recordings and dictionaries","meaning":"收藏錄音和字典","examples":[{"en":"The archive can house recordings, grammars and dictionaries.","zh":"該檔案庫可以收藏錄音、語法書和字典。"},{"en":"To house recordings and dictionaries means to store and preserve them in one place.","zh":"house recordings and dictionaries 指把它們存放並保存在同一地方。"},{"en":"A library website may house recordings of local songs and dictionaries of old words.","zh":"圖書館網站可能收藏本地歌曲錄音和舊詞字典。"},{"en":"Keeping materials together makes them easier for students and researchers to use.","zh":"把材料集中保存，讓學生和研究人員更容易使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised storage of language resources.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織地儲存語言資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"language data","meaning":"語言資料","examples":[{"en":"The archive preserves valuable language data for future study.","zh":"檔案庫保存有價值的語言資料供未來研究。"},{"en":"Language data is information about how a language sounds, works and is used.","zh":"language data 是關於一種語言如何發音、如何運作和如何使用的資訊。"},{"en":"Recordings of conversations, word lists and grammar notes are all language data.","zh":"對話錄音、詞表和語法筆記都是語言資料。"},{"en":"Good data helps researchers analyse patterns and helps communities teach learners.","zh":"良好資料幫助研究人員分析模式，也幫助社群教導學習者。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to evidence about a language.","zh":"這個短語指關於語言的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dispatch field linguists","meaning":"派遣實地語言學家","examples":[{"en":"The foundation dispatched field linguists to document rare languages.","zh":"基金會派遣實地語言學家記錄罕見語言。"},{"en":"To dispatch field linguists means to send language researchers to communities for direct study.","zh":"dispatch field linguists 指派送語言研究人員到社群進行直接研究。"},{"en":"A university may dispatch researchers to a rural area to record local speech.","zh":"大學可能派遣研究人員到鄉村地區記錄本地說話。"},{"en":"Sending specialists quickly matters when speakers are elderly or few in number.","zh":"當使用者年長或數量很少，迅速派遣專家很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organised field research deployment.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織地派出實地研究人員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"document a language","meaning":"記錄一種語言","examples":[{"en":"Researchers travelled to remote communities to document endangered languages.","zh":"研究人員前往偏遠社群記錄瀕危語言。"},{"en":"To document a language means to record its sounds, words, grammar and everyday use.","zh":"document a language 指記錄其聲音、詞語、語法和日常使用。"},{"en":"A linguist may document a language by recording stories and writing a dictionary.","zh":"語言學家可能透過錄下故事和編寫字典來記錄一種語言。"},{"en":"If a language is well documented, future learners can study it even after speakers become fewer.","zh":"如果語言被妥善記錄，即使使用者變少，未來學習者仍可研究它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes systematic recording, not casual note-taking.","zh":"這個短語描述有系統記錄，而不是隨便做筆記。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a hundred or so speakers","meaning":"約一百名使用者","examples":[{"en":"Aweti was spoken by only a hundred or so people.","zh":"Aweti 只有約一百名使用者。"},{"en":"A hundred or so speakers means about one hundred people who can speak a language.","zh":"a hundred or so speakers 指約一百名能說某語言的人。"},{"en":"A village language with a hundred or so speakers may depend on a few families for survival.","zh":"有約一百名使用者的村莊語言，可能依賴少數家庭存續。"},{"en":"When speaker numbers are this low, each death or language shift matters greatly.","zh":"當使用者數量這麼少，每一次死亡或語言轉移都非常重要。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an approximate small number of speakers.","zh":"這個短語給出大約的少量使用者數目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a dozen or so","meaning":"約十二個","examples":[{"en":"The project included a dozen or so additional languages.","zh":"該項目包括約十二種額外語言。"},{"en":"A dozen or so means about twelve, not an exact number.","zh":"a dozen or so 指大約十二個，不是精確數字。"},{"en":"A teacher may choose a dozen or so useful phrases for students to practise first.","zh":"老師可能先選約十二個有用短語給學生練習。"},{"en":"Approximate numbers are useful when the exact count is not central to the point.","zh":"當精確數量不是重點，約數很有用。"},{"en":"The phrase means roughly twelve.","zh":"這個短語意思是大約十二。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be unlikely to survive the century","meaning":"不大可能延續至本世紀末","examples":[{"en":"Some languages are unlikely to survive the century without intervention.","zh":"沒有干預的話，有些語言不大可能延續至本世紀末。"},{"en":"To be unlikely to survive the century means probably not to remain in use until the century ends.","zh":"be unlikely to survive the century 指很可能不能持續使用到本世紀結束。"},{"en":"A small family business may be unlikely to survive the decade if no one wants to take over.","zh":"如果沒有人想接手，小型家族企業可能不大可能延續到這十年結束。"},{"en":"If children stop learning a language, its chance of lasting another hundred years falls sharply.","zh":"如果孩子停止學習某語言，它再延續一百年的機會會大幅下降。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that survival is doubtful without action.","zh":"這個短語警告若不行動，存續很成疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"edge into the arena","meaning":"開始涉足該領域","examples":[{"en":"The Ford Foundation also edged into the arena of language preservation.","zh":"Ford Foundation 也開始涉足語言保存領域。"},{"en":"To edge into the arena means to begin entering a field slowly or cautiously.","zh":"edge into the arena 指慢慢或謹慎地開始進入某領域。"},{"en":"A small charity may edge into the arena of mental-health support by first funding one school project.","zh":"小型慈善機構可能先資助一個學校項目，開始涉足心理健康支援領域。"},{"en":"New organisations often enter cautiously when a field is difficult or unfamiliar.","zh":"當領域困難或不熟悉，新機構通常會謹慎進入。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests gradual involvement rather than sudden leadership.","zh":"這個短語暗示逐步參與，而不是突然領導。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make a contribution to","meaning":"為……作出貢獻","examples":[{"en":"The foundation made a contribution to several community programmes.","zh":"基金會為幾個社區計劃作出貢獻。"},{"en":"To make a contribution to something means to help it by giving money, effort, ideas or support.","zh":"make a contribution to 某事，指透過金錢、努力、想法或支持幫助它。"},{"en":"Parents can contribute to a school festival by preparing food or helping with games.","zh":"家長可以透過準備食物或協助遊戲，為學校嘉年華作出貢獻。"},{"en":"Contributions matter because large projects often need help from many sources.","zh":"貢獻重要，因為大型項目通常需要多方協助。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adding support to a shared goal.","zh":"這個短語描述為共同目標加入支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"help reinvigorate","meaning":"幫助重新振興","examples":[{"en":"New funding helped reinvigorate the master-apprentice programme.","zh":"新資金幫助重新振興師徒制語言計劃。"},{"en":"To help reinvigorate something means to help give it new energy, strength or activity.","zh":"help reinvigorate 某事，指幫助它重新得到活力、力量或活動。"},{"en":"A new coach may help reinvigorate a tired school sports team.","zh":"新教練可能幫助重新振興疲弱的學校運動隊。"},{"en":"Funding, leadership or fresh interest can bring life back to a struggling project.","zh":"資金、領導或新興趣可以令困難項目重新有生氣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes helping something become active again.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助某事再次活躍起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"master-apprentice programme","meaning":"師徒制語言計劃","examples":[{"en":"A master-apprentice programme pairs fluent elders with younger learners.","zh":"師徒制語言計劃把流利長者與年輕學習者配對。"},{"en":"A master-apprentice programme is a learning system where an expert teaches a learner through close practice.","zh":"master-apprentice programme 是專家透過密切練習教授學習者的學習制度。"},{"en":"A craft worker may teach an apprentice by working beside them every day.","zh":"工匠可能每天與學徒一起工作來教導他。"},{"en":"In language learning, this method helps learners hear real speech during shared activities.","zh":"在語言學習中，這種方法幫助學習者在共同活動中聽到真實說話。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning by direct personal transmission.","zh":"這個短語描述透過直接個人傳承來學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be worried about","meaning":"擔心……","examples":[{"en":"Native American communities were worried about the imminent loss of their languages.","zh":"美洲原住民社群擔心自己的語言即將失去。"},{"en":"To be worried about something means to feel anxious because it may cause harm or loss.","zh":"be worried about 某事，指因它可能造成傷害或損失而焦慮。"},{"en":"Parents may be worried about a child’s sleep if she is tired every morning.","zh":"如果孩子每天早上都疲倦，家長可能擔心她的睡眠。"},{"en":"Worry can lead people to seek advice, funding or urgent action.","zh":"擔心可以促使人尋求建議、資金或緊急行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes concern about a possible problem.","zh":"這個短語描述對可能問題的關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"imminent demise","meaning":"即將消亡","examples":[{"en":"The programme addressed the imminent demise of many indigenous languages.","zh":"該計劃處理許多原住民語言即將消亡的問題。"},{"en":"Imminent demise means a death, failure or disappearance that is expected very soon.","zh":"imminent demise 指預期很快出現的死亡、失敗或消失。"},{"en":"A shop facing unpaid rent and no customers may face imminent demise.","zh":"面對未付租金和沒有顧客的商店，可能面臨即將倒閉。"},{"en":"When demise is imminent, delaying action may mean losing the chance to save something.","zh":"當消亡迫在眉睫，拖延行動可能代表失去挽救機會。"},{"en":"The phrase signals urgent and near-term danger.","zh":"這個短語表示迫切且即將發生的危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"indigenous languages","meaning":"原住民語言","examples":[{"en":"California is home to many endangered indigenous languages.","zh":"加州有許多瀕危原住民語言。"},{"en":"Indigenous languages are languages originally used by native peoples of a place.","zh":"indigenous languages 是某地原住民族原本使用的語言。"},{"en":"An indigenous language may contain local names for plants, animals and sacred places.","zh":"原住民語言可能包含植物、動物和神聖地點的本地名稱。"},{"en":"When indigenous languages decline, communities may lose part of their historical identity.","zh":"當原住民語言衰退，社群可能失去部分歷史身份。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to languages tied to original peoples and lands.","zh":"這個短語指與原住民族和土地相連的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fluent speakers","meaning":"流利使用者","examples":[{"en":"Fluent speakers teach younger relatives through shared activities.","zh":"流利使用者透過共同活動教導較年輕親屬。"},{"en":"Fluent speakers are people who can use a language easily, naturally and accurately.","zh":"fluent speakers 是能輕鬆、自然且準確使用某語言的人。"},{"en":"A fluent speaker can tell stories, explain feelings and solve daily problems in the language.","zh":"流利使用者能用該語言講故事、解釋感受和處理日常問題。"},{"en":"If fluent speakers are elderly, communities must record and share their knowledge quickly.","zh":"如果流利使用者年長，社群必須迅速記錄並分享他們的知識。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to real ability in communication, not memorised words only.","zh":"這個短語指真正溝通能力，而不只是背誦字詞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a younger relative","meaning":"較年輕的親屬","examples":[{"en":"An elder may teach the language to a younger relative.","zh":"長者可以把語言教給較年輕的親屬。"},{"en":"A younger relative is a family member from a younger generation, such as a child, niece or grandson.","zh":"younger relative 是較年輕一代的家庭成員，例如孩子、侄女或孫子。"},{"en":"A grandmother may teach a younger relative old songs while cooking together.","zh":"祖母可能在一起煮食時教較年輕親屬舊歌。"},{"en":"Teaching younger relatives helps knowledge stay inside the family and community.","zh":"教導較年輕親屬有助知識留在家庭和社群內。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on family transmission across generations.","zh":"這個短語重點在跨代家庭傳承。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"native tongue","meaning":"母語","examples":[{"en":"The learners practise their native tongue during everyday activities.","zh":"學習者在日常活動中練習自己的母語。"},{"en":"A native tongue is the first or ancestral language of a person or community.","zh":"native tongue 是個人或社群的第一語言或祖傳語言。"},{"en":"A child may speak the national language at school but use her native tongue with grandparents.","zh":"孩子可能在學校說國家語言，但與祖父母用母語。"},{"en":"Using a native tongue at home can keep family stories and identity alive.","zh":"在家中使用母語可以延續家庭故事和身份。"},{"en":"The phrase is another way to say mother tongue or heritage language.","zh":"這個短語是 mother tongue 或 heritage language 的另一種說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"shared activities","meaning":"共同活動","examples":[{"en":"Teachers and learners use the language during hundreds of hours of shared activities.","zh":"老師和學習者在數百小時共同活動中使用該語言。"},{"en":"Shared activities are things people do together, such as cooking, walking, working or playing.","zh":"shared activities 是人們一起做的事情，例如煮食、散步、工作或遊戲。"},{"en":"A child can learn words naturally during shared activities with grandparents.","zh":"孩子可以在與祖父母的共同活動中自然學到詞語。"},{"en":"Learning through activity helps language connect with real actions and objects.","zh":"透過活動學習幫助語言與真實行動和物件連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses doing things together, not only sitting in a classroom.","zh":"這個短語強調一起做事，而不只是坐在課室。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be spread over six months","meaning":"分布在六個月內進行","examples":[{"en":"The lessons are spread over six months.","zh":"課程分布在六個月內進行。"},{"en":"To be spread over six months means to be arranged across a period of half a year.","zh":"be spread over six months 指安排在半年期間進行。"},{"en":"A training course may be spread over six months so workers can practise between sessions.","zh":"培訓課程可能分布在六個月內，讓員工在課堂之間練習。"},{"en":"Spreading lessons over time helps learners review, forget less and build habits.","zh":"把課程分散進行，有助學習者溫習、減少遺忘並建立習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes time distribution, not one intensive day.","zh":"這個短語描述時間分布，而不是一天密集完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"complete the programme","meaning":"完成該計劃","examples":[{"en":"Dozens of teams have completed the programme.","zh":"數十個團隊已完成該計劃。"},{"en":"To complete the programme means to finish all required parts of a planned course or project.","zh":"complete the programme 指完成一個計劃課程或項目的所有要求部分。"},{"en":"A student completes a training programme after attending every session and passing the final task.","zh":"學生出席每節課並通過最後任務後，就完成培訓計劃。"},{"en":"Completion shows that participants stayed involved long enough to receive the full experience.","zh":"完成顯示參與者投入足夠長時間，獲得完整經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reaching the end of a structured programme.","zh":"這個短語描述到達有結構計劃的終點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"transmit some knowledge of","meaning":"傳授部分……知識","examples":[{"en":"The programme transmitted some knowledge of twenty-five languages.","zh":"該計劃傳授了二十五種語言的部分知識。"},{"en":"To transmit some knowledge of something means to pass part of that knowledge from one person to another.","zh":"transmit some knowledge of 某事，指把其中部分知識由一人傳給另一人。"},{"en":"Grandparents can transmit knowledge of family history by telling stories during meals.","zh":"祖父母可以在飯桌上講故事，傳授部分家族歷史知識。"},{"en":"Even partial transmission can keep a language or tradition from disappearing completely.","zh":"即使只是部分傳承，也可以防止語言或傳統完全消失。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on passing knowledge across people or generations.","zh":"這個短語重點在把知識在人與人或世代之間傳下去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be too early to call something","meaning":"現在稱作……仍言之過早","examples":[{"en":"Hinton said it was too early to call the programme language revitalisation.","zh":"Hinton 說，現在稱該計劃為語言復興仍言之過早。"},{"en":"To be too early to call something means there is not enough evidence yet to use that label confidently.","zh":"be too early to call something 指證據仍不足以有信心使用該稱呼。"},{"en":"After one good test, it is too early to call a student fully prepared for the exam.","zh":"一次測驗表現好後，就說學生已完全準備好考試仍言之過早。"},{"en":"People should wait for stronger results before making big claims.","zh":"人們應等到更強結果出現，才作出重大聲稱。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against judging success too soon.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要太早判斷成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"language revitalisation","meaning":"語言復興","examples":[{"en":"Language revitalisation aims to restore everyday community use.","zh":"語言復興旨在恢復社群日常使用。"},{"en":"Language revitalisation means bringing a declining language back into active use.","zh":"language revitalisation 指把正在衰退的語言重新帶回積極使用。"},{"en":"A school can support language revitalisation by teaching children to speak it in daily situations.","zh":"學校可以透過教孩子在日常情境中說該語言來支持語言復興。"},{"en":"Revitalisation is stronger when families, schools and community events all use the language.","zh":"當家庭、學校和社區活動都使用該語言，復興會更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes more than recording a language; it means making it live again.","zh":"這個短語描述的不只是記錄語言；它指令語言重新活起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the death rate of elderly speakers","meaning":"年長語言使用者的死亡率","examples":[{"en":"The death rate of elderly speakers remains a serious concern.","zh":"年長語言使用者的死亡率仍是一項嚴重憂慮。"},{"en":"The death rate of elderly speakers means how quickly older fluent speakers are dying.","zh":"death rate of elderly speakers 指年長流利使用者去世的速度。"},{"en":"A community may worry if its last fluent elders are passing away faster than children learn.","zh":"如果最後一批流利長者離世速度快於孩子學習速度，社群可能擔憂。"},{"en":"High death rates reduce the time available to record stories, pronunciation and grammar.","zh":"高死亡率會減少記錄故事、發音和語法的可用時間。"},{"en":"The phrase connects language survival with the age of its speakers.","zh":"這個短語把語言存續與使用者年齡連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"recruitment rate","meaning":"年輕使用者的加入速度","examples":[{"en":"The recruitment rate of young speakers remains too low.","zh":"年輕使用者的加入速度仍然太低。"},{"en":"Recruitment rate means the speed or number at which new people join a group or activity.","zh":"recruitment rate 指新人加入某群體或活動的速度或數量。"},{"en":"A school club has a low recruitment rate if few new students join each year.","zh":"如果每年很少新學生加入，學校社團的招募率就低。"},{"en":"If new speakers join too slowly, they cannot replace older speakers who pass away.","zh":"如果新使用者加入太慢，就不能取代去世的年長使用者。"},{"en":"The phrase measures how quickly a group is gaining new members.","zh":"這個短語衡量一個群體增加新成員的速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be greater than","meaning":"高於……","examples":[{"en":"The loss of elderly speakers is greater than the recruitment of young learners.","zh":"年長使用者的流失高於年輕學習者的加入。"},{"en":"To be greater than something means to be larger, stronger or more serious than it.","zh":"be greater than 某事，指比它更大、更強或更嚴重。"},{"en":"If the number of students leaving a club is greater than the number joining, the club will shrink.","zh":"如果離開社團的學生人數高於加入人數，社團會縮小。"},{"en":"When loss is greater than replacement, decline continues.","zh":"當流失高於補充，衰退就會持續。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to compare amounts, rates or effects.","zh":"這個短語用來比較數量、速度或影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"prolong the survival of","meaning":"延長……的存續期","examples":[{"en":"The programme may prolong the survival of endangered languages.","zh":"該計劃可能延長瀕危語言的存續期。"},{"en":"To prolong the survival of something means to help it continue existing for longer.","zh":"prolong the survival of 某事，指幫助它存在更久。"},{"en":"A small grant can prolong the survival of a community library until more funding arrives.","zh":"小額撥款可以延長社區圖書館的存續期，直到更多資金到來。"},{"en":"Teaching young learners can give a language more time before it disappears.","zh":"教導年輕學習者可以在語言消失前爭取更多時間。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests extending life, even if full recovery is uncertain.","zh":"這個短語暗示延長生命，即使完全復原仍不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"give someone more time to","meaning":"給某人更多時間去……","examples":[{"en":"Community teaching gives linguists more time to record the language.","zh":"社區教學給語言學家更多時間去記錄該語言。"},{"en":"To give someone more time to do something means to delay pressure so the person can finish important work.","zh":"give someone more time to do something 指延後壓力，讓某人能完成重要工作。"},{"en":"Extra deadline flexibility gives students more time to revise their essays properly.","zh":"額外限期彈性給學生更多時間好好修改文章。"},{"en":"More time can improve quality because people are not forced to rush.","zh":"更多時間可以改善質素，因為人們不必急忙完成。"},{"en":"The phrase connects delay with a useful opportunity.","zh":"這個短語把延緩與有用機會連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"record languages before they vanish","meaning":"在語言消失前加以記錄","examples":[{"en":"Researchers hope to record endangered languages before they vanish.","zh":"研究人員希望在瀕危語言消失前加以記錄。"},{"en":"To record languages before they vanish means to document them before they disappear from use.","zh":"record languages before they vanish 指在語言不再被使用前記錄它們。"},{"en":"A community may record elders telling stories before those memories are lost.","zh":"社區可能在長者記憶失去前記錄他們講故事。"},{"en":"If recording is delayed, pronunciation and natural conversation may be impossible to recover.","zh":"如果記錄被延誤，發音和自然對話可能無法恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses urgent documentation before disappearance.","zh":"這個短語強調在消失前緊急記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fail to catch on","meaning":"未能流行起來","examples":[{"en":"The master-apprentice approach has failed to catch on outside the United States.","zh":"師徒制方法在美國以外未能流行起來。"},{"en":"To fail to catch on means not to become popular or widely used.","zh":"fail to catch on 指沒有變得受歡迎或被廣泛使用。"},{"en":"A new school app may fail to catch on if students find it confusing.","zh":"如果學生覺得新學校應用程式令人困惑，它可能未能流行起來。"},{"en":"Good ideas may spread slowly if communities lack money, training or confidence.","zh":"如果社群缺乏金錢、培訓或信心，好想法也可能傳播緩慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a method that has not gained broad acceptance.","zh":"這個短語描述某方法未獲廣泛接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a drop in the ocean","meaning":"滄海一粟","examples":[{"en":"One small programme is only a drop in the ocean compared with the scale of the crisis.","zh":"與危機規模相比，一個小計劃只是滄海一粟。"},{"en":"A drop in the ocean is a very small amount compared with what is needed.","zh":"a drop in the ocean 指與所需相比非常少的一點。"},{"en":"Donating ten books may feel like a drop in the ocean if a school library needs thousands.","zh":"如果學校圖書館需要數千本書，捐十本可能像滄海一粟。"},{"en":"Small help is still useful, but it may not solve a huge problem alone.","zh":"小幫助仍有用，但單靠它可能不能解決巨大問題。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the gap between effort and need.","zh":"這個短語強調努力與需要之間的差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be reduced to","meaning":"減少至；只剩下","examples":[{"en":"Hundreds of languages have been reduced to only a few elderly speakers.","zh":"數百種語言已減少至只剩少數年長使用者。"},{"en":"To be reduced to something means to decline until only that smaller or weaker state remains.","zh":"be reduced to 某狀態，指衰退到只剩下較小或較弱狀態。"},{"en":"A busy market may be reduced to a few stalls after rents rise sharply.","zh":"租金急升後，繁忙市場可能只剩下幾個攤檔。"},{"en":"When a language is reduced to a few speakers, normal community use is already in danger.","zh":"當語言只剩少數使用者，正常社群使用已經有危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious shrinkage or decline.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重縮小或衰退。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a mere handful of","meaning":"僅僅少數","examples":[{"en":"Some languages are spoken by a mere handful of elders.","zh":"有些語言只由僅僅少數長者使用。"},{"en":"A mere handful of people means only a very small number of people.","zh":"a mere handful of people 指只有非常少數的人。"},{"en":"A school club may continue with a mere handful of students if most members leave.","zh":"如果大多數成員離開，學校社團可能只剩僅僅少數學生。"},{"en":"When only a handful of speakers remain, every speaker’s knowledge becomes precious.","zh":"當只剩少數使用者，每位使用者的知識都變得珍貴。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises how small the number is.","zh":"這個短語強調數量非常少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"elderly speakers","meaning":"年長語言使用者","examples":[{"en":"Many endangered languages depend on a small number of elderly speakers.","zh":"許多瀕危語言依賴少數年長語言使用者。"},{"en":"Elderly speakers are older people who can still speak a language.","zh":"elderly speakers 是仍能說某語言的年長人士。"},{"en":"A community may invite elderly speakers to schools so children can hear natural pronunciation.","zh":"社群可能邀請年長語言使用者到學校，讓孩子聽到自然發音。"},{"en":"If elderly speakers are not recorded, their knowledge may disappear with them.","zh":"如果年長使用者沒有被記錄，他們的知識可能隨他們消失。"},{"en":"The phrase connects language survival with older generations.","zh":"這個短語把語言存續與年長一代連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"According to the Ethnologue, hundreds of languages face imminent extinction.","zh":"根據《民族語》，數百種語言面臨即將滅絕。"},{"en":"According to means based on what a source says.","zh":"according to 指基於某來源所說。"},{"en":"According to the school notice, classes will finish early on Friday.","zh":"根據學校通知，星期五會提早放學。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show where information comes from.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示資訊來自哪裏。"},{"en":"It is useful when reporting evidence rather than personal opinion.","zh":"它適合用於報告證據，而不是個人意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a catalogue of languages","meaning":"語言目錄","examples":[{"en":"The Ethnologue is a catalogue of languages from around the world.","zh":"《民族語》是來自世界各地的語言目錄。"},{"en":"A catalogue of languages is an organised list or database of languages and information about them.","zh":"catalogue of languages 是有組織的語言清單或資料庫，以及相關資訊。"},{"en":"A library catalogue helps students find books; a language catalogue helps researchers find language data.","zh":"圖書館目錄幫助學生找書；語言目錄幫助研究人員找語言資料。"},{"en":"Catalogues make large amounts of information easier to search and compare.","zh":"目錄令大量資訊更容易搜尋和比較。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a structured reference list.","zh":"這個短語指有結構的參考清單。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"come closest to global coverage","meaning":"最接近涵蓋全球","examples":[{"en":"The Ethnologue comes closest to providing global coverage of the world’s languages.","zh":"《民族語》最接近全面涵蓋世界語言。"},{"en":"To come closest to global coverage means to be the nearest available source to covering the whole world.","zh":"come closest to global coverage 指成為現有來源中最接近覆蓋全世界者。"},{"en":"A school database may come closest to full coverage of student attendance if every teacher updates it daily.","zh":"如果每位老師每天更新，學校資料庫可能最接近完整涵蓋學生出席情況。"},{"en":"Even the best source may still have gaps when the subject is very large.","zh":"當題目非常龐大，即使最佳來源也可能有缺口。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad coverage that is strong but not perfect.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛但不完美的覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the vast majority of","meaning":"絕大多數","examples":[{"en":"The vast majority of these languages have not been fully documented.","zh":"這些語言絕大多數尚未得到完整記錄。"},{"en":"The vast majority of something means almost all of it.","zh":"the vast majority of 某事物，指幾乎全部。"},{"en":"The vast majority of students passed the test after extra revision classes.","zh":"額外溫習課後，絕大多數學生通過測驗。"},{"en":"If the vast majority of records are missing, researchers face a serious evidence problem.","zh":"如果絕大多數記錄缺失，研究人員會面對嚴重證據問題。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises a very large proportion.","zh":"這個短語強調非常大的比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"little or no record of","meaning":"幾乎沒有……的記錄","examples":[{"en":"There is little or no record of many endangered languages.","zh":"許多瀕危語言幾乎沒有記錄。"},{"en":"Little or no record of something means very few or zero written, audio or visual records exist.","zh":"little or no record of 某事，指幾乎沒有或完全沒有文字、音頻或影像記錄。"},{"en":"There may be little or no record of old village songs if no one wrote or recorded them.","zh":"如果沒有人寫下或錄下舊村歌，它們可能幾乎沒有記錄。"},{"en":"Without records, future learners may not know how a language sounded or was used.","zh":"沒有記錄，未來學習者可能不知道語言如何發音或使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a serious lack of preserved evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述保存證據嚴重不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"pronunciation and daily use","meaning":"發音及日常使用方式","examples":[{"en":"Documentation should cover pronunciation and daily language use.","zh":"記錄工作應涵蓋發音及日常使用方式。"},{"en":"Pronunciation and daily use mean how words sound and how people use them in ordinary life.","zh":"pronunciation and daily use 指詞語如何發音，以及人們在普通生活中如何使用它們。"},{"en":"A language class should teach pronunciation and daily use, not only spelling lists.","zh":"語言課應教授發音及日常使用方式，而不只是拼寫清單。"},{"en":"If recordings capture daily use, learners can hear natural greetings, jokes and conversations.","zh":"如果錄音捕捉日常使用，學習者可以聽到自然問候、笑話和對話。"},{"en":"The phrase combines sound with real-life communication.","zh":"這個短語結合聲音與真實生活溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be fully documented","meaning":"得到完整記錄","examples":[{"en":"Only a small number of endangered languages have been fully documented.","zh":"只有少數瀕危語言得到完整記錄。"},{"en":"To be fully documented means to be recorded in enough detail, including sound, grammar, vocabulary and use.","zh":"be fully documented 指以足夠細節記錄，包括聲音、語法、詞彙和使用方式。"},{"en":"A family history is fully documented when photos, names, dates and stories are all recorded.","zh":"當照片、姓名、日期和故事都被記錄，家族歷史就得到完整記錄。"},{"en":"Full documentation gives future learners and researchers more than a rough outline.","zh":"完整記錄給未來學習者和研究人員的不只是粗略輪廓。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests complete and careful recording.","zh":"這個短語暗示完整而仔細的記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"all that remains","meaning":"剩下來的一切","examples":[{"en":"Once a language disappears, written records may be all that remains.","zh":"一旦語言消失，文字記錄可能就是剩下來的一切。"},{"en":"All that remains means the only thing left after everything else has gone.","zh":"all that remains 指其他一切消失後唯一留下的東西。"},{"en":"After an old shop closes, a few photographs may be all that remains of it.","zh":"舊店關門後，幾張照片可能就是它剩下來的一切。"},{"en":"If a language is no longer spoken, recordings and notes may become the only evidence.","zh":"如果語言不再有人說，錄音和筆記可能成為唯一證據。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses final traces after loss.","zh":"這個短語強調失去後的最後痕跡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"vanish from active use","meaning":"不再有人實際使用","examples":[{"en":"A language may survive in archives after it vanishes from active use.","zh":"一種語言不再有人實際使用後，仍可能在檔案中保存。"},{"en":"To vanish from active use means to stop being used regularly in real communication.","zh":"vanish from active use 指不再在真實溝通中定期使用。"},{"en":"A word may vanish from active use if young people no longer hear it at home.","zh":"如果年輕人在家中不再聽到某詞，它可能不再有人實際使用。"},{"en":"Archive survival is different from living use in families, schools and communities.","zh":"檔案中的保存不同於家庭、學校和社群中的活用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes disappearance from daily practice.","zh":"這個短語描述從日常實踐中消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a fossil skeleton","meaning":"化石般的骨架","examples":[{"en":"A grammar and dictionary alone may preserve only a fossil skeleton of a language.","zh":"單靠語法書和字典可能只保存語言化石般的骨架。"},{"en":"A fossil skeleton is a metaphor for a lifeless outline that shows structure but not full living use.","zh":"fossil skeleton 是比喻，指顯示結構但沒有完整活用的無生命輪廓。"},{"en":"A school timetable without students’ voices is like a fossil skeleton of school life.","zh":"沒有學生聲音的時間表，就像學校生活化石般的骨架。"},{"en":"Written rules can show a language’s bones, but not its humour, rhythm or everyday warmth.","zh":"書面規則可以顯示語言的骨架，但不能顯示幽默、節奏或日常溫度。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that incomplete records may feel dead and limited.","zh":"這個短語提醒人，不完整記錄可能顯得死板而有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a scattering of features","meaning":"零散的特徵","examples":[{"en":"An incomplete record preserves only a scattering of linguistic features.","zh":"不完整記錄只保存零散的語言特徵。"},{"en":"A scattering of features means a small, disconnected collection of characteristics.","zh":"a scattering of features 指少量、互不連貫的特徵集合。"},{"en":"A student’s notebook may contain a scattering of useful phrases but no clear system.","zh":"學生筆記可能有零散有用短語，但沒有清楚系統。"},{"en":"Scattered details help a little, but they may not show how the whole language works.","zh":"零散細節有少許幫助，但未必顯示整種語言如何運作。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests fragments rather than a complete picture.","zh":"這個短語暗示碎片，而不是完整圖像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be astute enough to","meaning":"足夠敏銳去……","examples":[{"en":"A skilled researcher must be astute enough to record subtle features.","zh":"熟練研究人員必須足夠敏銳去記錄細微特徵。"},{"en":"To be astute enough to do something means to be clever, observant and sensitive enough to notice what matters.","zh":"be astute enough to do something 指足夠聰明、善於觀察並敏感地注意重要之處。"},{"en":"A good teacher is astute enough to notice when a quiet student does not understand.","zh":"好老師足夠敏銳，能注意到安靜學生其實不明白。"},{"en":"If researchers miss subtle details, later learners may never recover them.","zh":"如果研究人員錯過細微細節，後來學習者可能永遠無法恢復它們。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights sharp judgement and careful observation.","zh":"這個短語突出敏銳判斷和仔細觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"capture a feature","meaning":"記錄下某項特徵","examples":[{"en":"Researchers try to capture pronunciation, grammar and conversational style.","zh":"研究人員嘗試記錄發音、語法和對話風格。"},{"en":"To capture a feature means to record or represent an important characteristic accurately.","zh":"capture a feature 指準確記錄或呈現一項重要特徵。"},{"en":"A photographer may capture a child’s smile at the exact moment it appears.","zh":"攝影師可能在孩子笑容出現的一刻捕捉下來。"},{"en":"In language work, recordings can capture tone and rhythm that writing alone misses.","zh":"在語言工作中，錄音可以記錄文字本身漏掉的聲調和節奏。"},{"en":"The phrase means preserving something important before it is lost.","zh":"這個短語指在某事失去前保存其重要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sketch an outline of","meaning":"勾畫……的概況","examples":[{"en":"Documentation may allow linguists to sketch an outline of a lost language.","zh":"記錄資料可能讓語言學家勾畫一種已失語言的概況。"},{"en":"To sketch an outline of something means to give a rough but useful picture of its main parts.","zh":"sketch an outline of 某事，指提供其主要部分的粗略但有用圖像。"},{"en":"A teacher may sketch an outline of an essay before students write the full version.","zh":"老師可能在學生寫完整文章前勾畫文章概況。"},{"en":"An outline helps people understand the basic structure, even if many details are missing.","zh":"概況幫助人理解基本結構，即使許多細節缺失。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests an incomplete but helpful summary.","zh":"這個短語暗示不完整但有幫助的總結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"fix its place on","meaning":"確定其在……上的位置","examples":[{"en":"Linguists may be able to fix a language’s place on the evolutionary tree.","zh":"語言學家可能能確定一種語言在語言演化樹上的位置。"},{"en":"To fix its place on something means to determine exactly where it belongs in a system.","zh":"fix its place on 某系統，指準確判定它在其中屬於哪裏。"},{"en":"A historian may fix a family’s place on a family tree after checking birth records.","zh":"歷史學家查核出生記錄後，可能確定某家庭在族譜上的位置。"},{"en":"Clear evidence helps researchers classify relationships more accurately.","zh":"清楚證據幫助研究人員更準確分類關係。"},{"en":"The phrase describes placing something in the right position within a structure.","zh":"這個短語描述把某物放在結構中的正確位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"evolutionary tree","meaning":"語言演化樹","examples":[{"en":"Related languages can be placed on an evolutionary tree.","zh":"相關語言可以被放在語言演化樹上。"},{"en":"An evolutionary tree is a diagram that shows how languages, species or groups developed from common ancestors.","zh":"evolutionary tree 是顯示語言、物種或群體如何由共同祖先發展而來的圖表。"},{"en":"A biology class may use an evolutionary tree to show how animals are related.","zh":"生物課可能使用演化樹來顯示動物之間的關係。"},{"en":"In linguistics, the tree helps show which languages share older roots.","zh":"在語言學中，這棵樹幫助顯示哪些語言共享更古老根源。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a branching model of historical development.","zh":"這個短語指歷史發展的分支模型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"little more than","meaning":"僅僅；沒有更多","examples":[{"en":"A basic grammar may reveal little more than the structure of a language.","zh":"基本語法書可能僅僅揭示語言結構。"},{"en":"Little more than means only slightly more than, or almost nothing beyond something.","zh":"little more than 指只比某事多一點，或幾乎沒有超出它。"},{"en":"A rushed report may give little more than a list of problems without solutions.","zh":"匆忙報告可能僅僅列出問題，沒有解決方案。"},{"en":"When documentation is thin, it may show form but not real life use.","zh":"當記錄薄弱，它可能顯示形式，但沒有真實生活使用方式。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises limitation.","zh":"這個短語強調限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"start a conversation","meaning":"展開對話","examples":[{"en":"Researchers want to know how speakers naturally started a conversation.","zh":"研究人員想知道使用者自然如何展開對話。"},{"en":"To start a conversation means to begin speaking with someone.","zh":"start a conversation 指開始與某人交談。"},{"en":"A student may start a conversation by asking a classmate about homework.","zh":"學生可能透過問同學功課來展開對話。"},{"en":"Natural openings show politeness, relationship and culture.","zh":"自然開場白顯示禮貌、關係和文化。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how communication begins.","zh":"這個短語重點在溝通如何開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"talk to babies","meaning":"跟嬰兒說話","examples":[{"en":"Everyday recordings may show how adults talked to babies.","zh":"日常錄音可能顯示成年人如何跟嬰兒說話。"},{"en":"To talk to babies means to speak to very young children, often in a gentle or playful way.","zh":"talk to babies 指跟很年幼的孩子說話，常以溫柔或玩樂方式。"},{"en":"Parents may talk to babies while feeding, bathing or putting them to sleep.","zh":"父母可能在餵食、洗澡或哄睡時跟嬰兒說話。"},{"en":"Baby talk can reveal family warmth, rhythm and early language teaching.","zh":"跟嬰兒說話可以揭示家庭溫情、節奏和早期語言教學。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a simple but culturally important form of speech.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單但在文化上重要的說話形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"converse with one another","meaning":"彼此交談","examples":[{"en":"Researchers want to know how husbands and wives conversed with one another.","zh":"研究人員想知道丈夫和妻子如何彼此交談。"},{"en":"To converse with one another means to talk together in a natural exchange.","zh":"converse with one another 指以自然互動方式一起談話。"},{"en":"Friends converse with one another during lunch about school, family and weekend plans.","zh":"朋友午飯時彼此交談，談學校、家庭和週末計劃。"},{"en":"Conversation patterns can show respect, closeness or social roles.","zh":"對話模式可以顯示尊重、親密或社會角色。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mutual speaking, not one person giving a speech.","zh":"這個短語描述互相說話，而不是一個人發表演講。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the first things one wants to learn","meaning":"某人最先想學的內容","examples":[{"en":"Everyday expressions are among the first things learners want to learn.","zh":"日常表達是學習者最先想學的內容之一。"},{"en":"The first things one wants to learn are the earliest and most useful items a learner hopes to know.","zh":"the first things one wants to learn 是學習者最早、最實用地希望知道的內容。"},{"en":"A traveller usually wants to learn greetings, prices and directions first.","zh":"旅客通常最先想學問候語、價格和方向。"},{"en":"Learners begin with practical phrases because they help them communicate immediately.","zh":"學習者從實用短語開始，因為它們能立即幫助溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to early learning priorities.","zh":"這個短語指早期學習優先事項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"revitalise a language","meaning":"復興一種語言","examples":[{"en":"Communities need natural conversational knowledge to revitalise a language.","zh":"社群需要自然對話知識來復興一種語言。"},{"en":"To revitalise a language means to bring it back into active use and community life.","zh":"revitalise a language 指把語言重新帶回積極使用和社群生活。"},{"en":"A school can help revitalise a language by using it in songs, games and morning greetings.","zh":"學校可以透過在歌曲、遊戲和早晨問候中使用它來復興語言。"},{"en":"Revitalisation requires speakers, teaching materials and real reasons to use the language.","zh":"復興需要使用者、教材和使用該語言的真實理由。"},{"en":"The phrase means making a language living again, not merely storing it in books.","zh":"這個短語指令語言重新活起來，而不只是把它存於書中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as yet","meaning":"至今仍然","examples":[{"en":"As yet, there is no established discipline of conservation linguistics.","zh":"至今仍然沒有確立的語言保育學學科。"},{"en":"As yet means up to now or so far.","zh":"as yet 指直到現在或到目前為止。"},{"en":"As yet, the school has not announced the exam timetable.","zh":"至今學校仍未公布考試時間表。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that something may happen later, but has not happened now.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事之後可能發生，但現在尚未發生。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing an incomplete current situation.","zh":"它適合描述目前未完成的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"conservation linguistics","meaning":"語言保育學","examples":[{"en":"Conservation linguistics would focus on preventing language extinction.","zh":"語言保育學會專注於防止語言滅絕。"},{"en":"Conservation linguistics would be a field devoted to protecting, documenting and revitalising endangered languages.","zh":"conservation linguistics 會是致力保護、記錄和復興瀕危語言的領域。"},{"en":"A conservation linguist might work with elders to record stories and teach young speakers.","zh":"語言保育學家可能與長者合作記錄故事並教導年輕使用者。"},{"en":"Such a field could give language protection clearer methods and professional standards.","zh":"這樣的領域可以為語言保護提供更清楚方法和專業標準。"},{"en":"The phrase connects language study with preservation work.","zh":"這個短語把語言研究與保存工作連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as there is for biology","meaning":"正如生物學已有的那樣","examples":[{"en":"Linguistics lacks a conservation discipline like the one that exists in biology.","zh":"語言學缺乏像生物學已有的那種保育學科。"},{"en":"As there is for biology means in the same way that such a field or system exists in biology.","zh":"as there is for biology 指正如生物學中有這樣的領域或制度。"},{"en":"Education may need a clear ethics code, as there is for medicine.","zh":"教育可能需要清楚倫理守則，正如醫學已有的那樣。"},{"en":"The phrase compares one field with another to show what is missing.","zh":"這個短語把一個領域與另一個領域比較，以顯示缺少甚麼。"},{"en":"It helps readers understand the gap by using a familiar model.","zh":"它透過熟悉模型幫助讀者理解缺口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"almost every strategy tried so far","meaning":"至今嘗試過的幾乎每種策略","examples":[{"en":"Almost every strategy tried so far has produced mixed results.","zh":"至今嘗試過的幾乎每種策略都產生好壞參半的結果。"},{"en":"Almost every strategy tried so far means nearly all methods that have been tested up to now.","zh":"almost every strategy tried so far 指到目前為止測試過的幾乎所有方法。"},{"en":"A school may find that almost every revision strategy tried so far helps some students but not others.","zh":"學校可能發現至今嘗試過的幾乎每種溫習策略，都只幫到部分學生。"},{"en":"Mixed results show that one solution may not work everywhere.","zh":"好壞參半的結果顯示單一方案未必到處有效。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests experience with many attempts, but no perfect answer.","zh":"這個短語暗示已試過很多方法，但沒有完美答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"succeed in some places but fail in others","meaning":"在某些地方成功，卻在另一些地方失敗","examples":[{"en":"The same language programme may succeed in some places but fail in others.","zh":"同一語言計劃可能在某些地方成功，卻在另一些地方失敗。"},{"en":"To succeed in some places but fail in others means to work well in certain contexts but not in different ones.","zh":"succeed in some places but fail in others 指在某些情境有效，但在不同情境無效。"},{"en":"A homework policy may succeed in one school but fail in another if students’ home lives differ.","zh":"如果學生家庭生活不同，功課政策可能在一間學校成功，卻在另一間失敗。"},{"en":"Local culture, funding and leadership can change whether a programme works.","zh":"本地文化、資金和領導會改變計劃是否有效。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that solutions need local adaptation.","zh":"這個短語提醒人解決方案需要本地調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"predict with certainty","meaning":"肯定地預測","examples":[{"en":"Researchers cannot predict with certainty which preservation strategy will work.","zh":"研究人員不能肯定地預測哪種保存策略會有效。"},{"en":"To predict with certainty means to know confidently what will happen before it happens.","zh":"predict with certainty 指在事情發生前有信心知道會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"A teacher cannot predict with certainty which student will improve most by the end of the year.","zh":"老師不能肯定地預測哪名學生到年底會進步最多。"},{"en":"Complex situations make certainty difficult because many factors can change the result.","zh":"複雜情況令確定性困難，因為許多因素可以改變結果。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises limits in forecasting.","zh":"這個短語強調預測上的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"set up language nests","meaning":"設立語言巢","examples":[{"en":"Maori speakers set up language nests for preschool children.","zh":"毛利語使用者為學前兒童設立語言巢。"},{"en":"To set up language nests means to create early-childhood spaces where children are surrounded by a heritage language.","zh":"set up language nests 指建立讓幼兒被傳承語言包圍的早期兒童空間。"},{"en":"A community may set up a language nest where elders speak only the local language with children.","zh":"社區可能設立語言巢，讓長者只用本地語言與孩子交流。"},{"en":"Early immersion can help children hear and use a language naturally before school age.","zh":"早期沉浸可以幫助孩子在入學前自然聽和使用語言。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to community-based language learning for very young children.","zh":"這個短語指為幼兒而設、以社區為基礎的語言學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"preschoolers","meaning":"學前兒童","examples":[{"en":"The language nests immersed preschoolers in Maori.","zh":"語言巢讓學前兒童沉浸於毛利語中。"},{"en":"Preschoolers are young children who are not yet old enough for primary school.","zh":"preschoolers 是尚未到小學年齡的幼兒。"},{"en":"Preschoolers often learn language through songs, games, stories and daily routines.","zh":"學前兒童常透過歌曲、遊戲、故事和日常程序學習語言。"},{"en":"Because young children learn sounds quickly, early exposure can be powerful.","zh":"因為幼兒很快學會聲音，早期接觸可以很有力。"},{"en":"The word refers to children before formal schooling begins.","zh":"這個字指正式上學前的兒童。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be immersed in","meaning":"沉浸於……","examples":[{"en":"Children in the programme were immersed in the native language.","zh":"計劃中的孩子沉浸於本族語言之中。"},{"en":"To be immersed in a language means to be surrounded by it and use it often.","zh":"be immersed in 某語言，指被它包圍並經常使用它。"},{"en":"A student living with a host family may be immersed in English every day.","zh":"住在寄宿家庭的學生可能每天沉浸於英語中。"},{"en":"Immersion helps learners hear natural phrases rather than only memorise textbook lists.","zh":"沉浸幫助學習者聽到自然短語，而不只是背課本文字表。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep exposure through real use.","zh":"這個短語描述透過真實使用進行深度接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"native language","meaning":"本族語言","examples":[{"en":"Young children learned through full exposure to their native language.","zh":"幼兒透過完全接觸本族語言來學習。"},{"en":"A native language is the first language or traditional language of a person or community.","zh":"native language 是個人或社群的第一語言或傳統語言。"},{"en":"Children may speak a national language at school and a native language with grandparents.","zh":"孩子可能在學校說國家語言，與祖父母說本族語言。"},{"en":"Losing a native language can weaken family stories and cultural identity.","zh":"失去本族語言可以削弱家庭故事和文化身份。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a language closely tied to origin and belonging.","zh":"這個短語指與來源和歸屬感緊密相連的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"additional language-only classes","meaning":"額外的全母語課堂","examples":[{"en":"Additional Maori-only classes were introduced as the children grew older.","zh":"隨着孩子長大，額外的全毛利語課堂被引入。"},{"en":"Additional language-only classes are extra lessons taught entirely in the target language.","zh":"additional language-only classes 是完全用目標語言教授的額外課堂。"},{"en":"A school may offer additional Spanish-only classes to help learners use Spanish naturally.","zh":"學校可能提供額外全西班牙語課堂，幫助學習者自然使用西班牙語。"},{"en":"Such classes increase practice time and reduce reliance on another language.","zh":"這類課堂增加練習時間，並減少對另一語言的依賴。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extra immersion-based lessons.","zh":"這個短語描述額外的沉浸式課堂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"progress through school","meaning":"隨着升學階段逐步前進","examples":[{"en":"The children continued receiving Maori instruction as they progressed through school.","zh":"隨着孩子在學校階段逐步前進，他們繼續接受毛利語教學。"},{"en":"To progress through school means to move from one school year or level to the next.","zh":"progress through school 指由一個學年或階段升到下一個。"},{"en":"A child progresses through school from kindergarten to primary and then secondary classes.","zh":"孩子從幼稚園到小學，再到中學，就是在升學階段逐步前進。"},{"en":"Continuing language support across years helps prevent early gains from disappearing.","zh":"多年持續語言支援有助防止早期成果消失。"},{"en":"The phrase describes educational movement over time.","zh":"這個短語描述教育階段隨時間推進。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"primary and secondary school","meaning":"小學及中學","examples":[{"en":"Language programmes continued through primary and secondary school.","zh":"語言計劃延續至小學及中學。"},{"en":"Primary and secondary school means the early and later main stages of formal schooling.","zh":"primary and secondary school 指正式學校教育中的早期和後期主要階段。"},{"en":"Students usually learn basic reading in primary school and more advanced subjects in secondary school.","zh":"學生通常在小學學基本閱讀，在中學學較進階科目。"},{"en":"If language teaching continues through both stages, learners get many years of practice.","zh":"如果語言教學延續兩個階段，學習者就有多年練習。"},{"en":"The phrase covers schooling before university.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋大學前的學校教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a similar approach","meaning":"類似方法","examples":[{"en":"A similar approach was introduced in Hawaii.","zh":"夏威夷引入了類似方法。"},{"en":"A similar approach is a method that is much like one already mentioned.","zh":"similar approach 是與已提及方法十分相似的方法。"},{"en":"If one school improves reading through daily story time, another school may try a similar approach.","zh":"如果一間學校透過每日故事時間改善閱讀，另一間學校可能嘗試類似方法。"},{"en":"Using a similar approach can save time because a model already exists.","zh":"使用類似方法可以節省時間，因為已有模型存在。"},{"en":"The phrase compares methods with shared features.","zh":"這個短語比較具有共同特徵的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"with some success","meaning":"取得一定成功","examples":[{"en":"The Hawaiian programme was implemented with some success.","zh":"夏威夷計劃實施後取得一定成功。"},{"en":"With some success means the result was partly successful, though not perfect.","zh":"with some success 指結果部分成功，但並不完美。"},{"en":"A school may introduce a new homework system with some success if late work decreases but stress remains.","zh":"如果遲交功課減少但壓力仍存在，學校的新功課制度可說取得一定成功。"},{"en":"Partial success can still show that a method has value.","zh":"部分成功仍可顯示方法有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a cautious positive judgement.","zh":"這個短語給出謹慎的正面判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"stabilise at","meaning":"穩定在……","examples":[{"en":"The number of native speakers stabilised at around one thousand.","zh":"母語使用者數目穩定在約一千人。"},{"en":"To stabilise at a number means to stop changing much and remain near that level.","zh":"stabilise at 某數字，指停止大幅變動並維持在接近該水平。"},{"en":"A school’s enrolment may stabilise at 800 students after several years of growth.","zh":"學校收生人數在多年增長後，可能穩定在800人。"},{"en":"Stabilising speaker numbers can show that decline has slowed or stopped.","zh":"使用者數量穩定可以顯示衰退已減慢或停止。"},{"en":"The phrase describes becoming steady around a particular amount.","zh":"這個短語描述在某特定數量附近變得穩定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"receive instruction in","meaning":"接受以……進行的教學","examples":[{"en":"Students can receive instruction in Hawaiian throughout their education.","zh":"學生可以在整個教育過程中接受以夏威夷語進行的教學。"},{"en":"To receive instruction in a language means to be taught using that language.","zh":"receive instruction in 某語言，指用該語言接受教學。"},{"en":"Children may receive instruction in English for science and in Cantonese for local history.","zh":"孩子可能用英語學科學，用廣東話學本地歷史。"},{"en":"Learning subjects through a language gives students more practice than one short language lesson.","zh":"透過某語言學科目，比一節短語言課提供更多練習。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the language used for teaching.","zh":"這個短語重點在教學所用的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"all the way through university","meaning":"一直到大學階段","examples":[{"en":"Some learners can now study in Hawaiian all the way through university.","zh":"有些學習者現在可以一直到大學階段都用夏威夷語學習。"},{"en":"All the way through university means continuously until and including university level.","zh":"all the way through university 指一直持續到並包括大學階段。"},{"en":"A student may study in the same language from primary school all the way through university.","zh":"學生可能由小學一直到大學階段都用同一語言學習。"},{"en":"Long-term support helps a language become useful for advanced subjects, not only childhood learning.","zh":"長期支援幫助語言變得可用於高階科目，而不只是兒童學習。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses continuity across the whole education path.","zh":"這個短語強調整條教育路徑上的連續性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"one factor in the demise of","meaning":"……消亡的一項因素","examples":[{"en":"Loss of confidence is one factor in the demise of a language.","zh":"失去信心是語言消亡的一項因素。"},{"en":"One factor in the demise of something is one cause that helps lead to its decline or disappearance.","zh":"one factor in the demise of 某事，是導致它衰退或消失的一個原因。"},{"en":"Lack of young customers may be one factor in the demise of a small shop.","zh":"缺少年輕顧客可能是小店倒閉的一項因素。"},{"en":"A problem usually has several causes, and one factor may combine with others.","zh":"一個問題通常有幾個原因，而一項因素可能與其他因素結合。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies one contributing cause of failure or loss.","zh":"這個短語指出失敗或損失的一個促成原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"collective doubts about","meaning":"對……產生集體疑慮","examples":[{"en":"Speakers may develop collective doubts about the value of their language.","zh":"使用者可能對自己語言的價值產生集體疑慮。"},{"en":"Collective doubts about something are shared uncertainties or lack of confidence among a group.","zh":"collective doubts about 某事，是一個群體共同的不確定或信心不足。"},{"en":"Students may develop collective doubts about a new exam system if teachers cannot explain it clearly.","zh":"如果老師不能清楚解釋新考試制度，學生可能對它產生集體疑慮。"},{"en":"When a whole community doubts a language’s value, fewer people may pass it to children.","zh":"當整個社群懷疑某語言的價值，較少人可能把它傳給孩子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes group-level uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語描述群體層面的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the usefulness of language loyalty","meaning":"忠於本族語言的實際價值","examples":[{"en":"Communities may question the usefulness of remaining loyal to a minority language.","zh":"社群可能質疑忠於少數族群語言的實際價值。"},{"en":"The usefulness of language loyalty means whether continuing to use and support a language brings practical value.","zh":"the usefulness of language loyalty 指繼續使用和支持某語言是否帶來實際價值。"},{"en":"Parents may question language loyalty if a school and workplace reward only the majority language.","zh":"如果學校和職場只獎勵多數族群語言，家長可能質疑語言忠誠的實用性。"},{"en":"If loyalty seems useless, speakers may shift to a more powerful language.","zh":"如果忠誠看似沒有用，使用者可能轉向更有權力的語言。"},{"en":"The phrase connects emotional attachment with practical benefit.","zh":"這個短語把情感依附與實際好處連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"regard one’s language as inferior to","meaning":"視自己的語言為不及……","examples":[{"en":"Some speakers begin to regard their own language as inferior to the majority language.","zh":"有些使用者開始視自己的語言為不及多數族群語言。"},{"en":"To regard one’s language as inferior to another means to think it is less valuable or less useful.","zh":"regard one’s language as inferior to 另一語言，指認為自己的語言較沒有價值或較沒有用。"},{"en":"A child may regard her home dialect as inferior if classmates laugh at it.","zh":"如果同學取笑，孩子可能視自己的家庭方言為不及標準語。"},{"en":"When people feel ashamed of a language, they may stop using it publicly.","zh":"當人們對語言感到羞恥，他們可能停止在公開場合使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a damaging attitude toward one’s own speech.","zh":"這個短語描述對自己語言有害的態度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"majority language","meaning":"多數族群語言","examples":[{"en":"The majority language often dominates education and public life.","zh":"多數族群語言常主導教育和公共生活。"},{"en":"A majority language is the language used by the largest or most powerful group in a society.","zh":"majority language 是社會中最大或最有權力群體使用的語言。"},{"en":"In many places, children use a minority language at home but the majority language at school.","zh":"在許多地方，孩子在家使用少數族群語言，但在學校使用多數族群語言。"},{"en":"If the majority language is needed for jobs, families may use it more often.","zh":"如果工作需要多數族群語言，家庭可能更常使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the socially dominant language.","zh":"這個短語描述社會上佔主導地位的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"stop using something in all situations","meaning":"在所有場合停止使用某物","examples":[{"en":"Speakers may gradually stop using their language in public and at home.","zh":"使用者可能逐漸在公開場合和家中停止使用自己的語言。"},{"en":"To stop using something in all situations means to abandon it everywhere, not only in one setting.","zh":"stop using something in all situations 指在所有地方放棄使用它，而不只是一種場合。"},{"en":"A student may stop using a local dialect in all situations if she feels embarrassed at school and home.","zh":"如果學生在學校和家中都感到尷尬，她可能在所有場合停止使用本地方言。"},{"en":"When use disappears from both private and public life, revival becomes harder.","zh":"當使用從私人和公共生活中都消失，復興會變得更難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes complete withdrawal from use.","zh":"這個短語描述完全停止使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"pick up on an attitude","meaning":"察覺到某種態度","examples":[{"en":"Children quickly pick up on adults’ negative attitudes towards a language.","zh":"孩子很快察覺到成年人對某語言的負面態度。"},{"en":"To pick up on an attitude means to notice it, even if it is not stated directly.","zh":"pick up on an attitude 指即使態度沒有直接說出，也能注意到它。"},{"en":"A child may pick up on a parent’s worry before anyone explains the problem.","zh":"孩子可能在任何人解釋問題前，已察覺到父母的擔憂。"},{"en":"Children learn from tone, jokes and silence as well as direct instruction.","zh":"孩子不只從直接教導中學習，也從語氣、笑話和沉默中學習。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sensing hidden feelings or views.","zh":"這個短語描述感知隱藏感受或看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"dominant language","meaning":"主導語言","examples":[{"en":"Young people may prefer the dominant language for social and economic reasons.","zh":"年輕人可能因社交和經濟原因偏好主導語言。"},{"en":"A dominant language is the language with the most power, use or social advantage in a community.","zh":"dominant language 是在社群中最有權力、使用最多或最有社會優勢的語言。"},{"en":"Students may use the dominant language at school because textbooks and exams are written in it.","zh":"學生可能在學校使用主導語言，因為課本和考試都用它寫成。"},{"en":"When one language dominates, smaller languages may be pushed into the home or lost entirely.","zh":"當一種語言佔主導，較小語言可能被推入家庭或完全流失。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a language with strong social influence.","zh":"這個短語指具有強大社會影響力的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"not notice until","meaning":"直到……才察覺","examples":[{"en":"Parents may not notice the change until their children stop using the language.","zh":"父母可能直到孩子停止使用該語言才察覺變化。"},{"en":"Not notice until means to fail to realise something before a later event makes it clear.","zh":"not notice until 指在較後事件令事情清楚前，未能意識到某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may not notice a student’s stress until the student stops handing in work.","zh":"老師可能直到學生停止交功課，才察覺學生壓力。"},{"en":"Some changes happen slowly, so people recognise them only after the result becomes obvious.","zh":"有些變化發生得很慢，所以人們只在結果明顯後才認出。"},{"en":"The phrase shows delayed awareness.","zh":"這個短語顯示延遲察覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"even at home","meaning":"即使在家中","examples":[{"en":"Some children stop speaking the minority language even at home.","zh":"有些孩子即使在家中也停止說少數族群語言。"},{"en":"Even at home means surprisingly, the situation happens in the private family space too.","zh":"even at home 指令人意外地，情況也發生在私人家庭空間。"},{"en":"A child may use English even at home if all entertainment and homework are in English.","zh":"如果所有娛樂和功課都用英語，孩子即使在家中也可能使用英語。"},{"en":"When a language disappears from the home, everyday transmission becomes very weak.","zh":"當語言從家庭中消失，日常傳承會變得非常弱。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises that the change has reached the most personal setting.","zh":"這個短語強調變化已到達最私人場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"slip into extinction","meaning":"逐漸走向滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Cornish and some Gaelic dialects gradually slipped into extinction.","zh":"康沃爾語和一些蓋爾方言逐漸走向滅絕。"},{"en":"To slip into extinction means to disappear slowly and quietly over time.","zh":"slip into extinction 指隨時間慢慢而安靜地消失。"},{"en":"A local game may slip into extinction if children slowly stop playing it.","zh":"如果孩子慢慢停止玩某本地遊戲，它可能逐漸走向消失。"},{"en":"Gradual loss can be dangerous because people may not feel urgency until it is too late.","zh":"漸進流失很危險，因為人們可能直到太遲才感到迫切。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests quiet decline rather than sudden collapse.","zh":"這個短語暗示安靜衰退，而不是突然崩塌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be rarely used for","meaning":"很少被用於……","examples":[{"en":"A language may have official status but still be rarely used for everyday communication.","zh":"一種語言可能有官方地位，但仍很少被用於日常溝通。"},{"en":"To be rarely used for something means to be used only occasionally for that purpose.","zh":"be rarely used for 某事，指只偶爾被用於該目的。"},{"en":"A school hall may be rarely used for lessons if classes usually stay in classrooms.","zh":"如果課堂通常留在課室，學校禮堂可能很少被用於上課。"},{"en":"Official recognition does not guarantee daily use.","zh":"官方承認不保證日常使用。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the gap between status and practice.","zh":"這個短語突出地位與實踐之間的差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"daily home life","meaning":"家庭日常生活","examples":[{"en":"Irish Gaelic is not widely used in daily home life.","zh":"愛爾蘭蓋爾語並未廣泛用於家庭日常生活。"},{"en":"Daily home life means ordinary activities and conversations that happen at home every day.","zh":"daily home life 指每天在家中發生的普通活動和對話。"},{"en":"Cooking, helping children with homework and chatting after dinner are parts of daily home life.","zh":"煮飯、幫孩子做功課和晚飯後聊天，都是家庭日常生活的一部分。"},{"en":"If a language is absent from daily home life, children may not learn it naturally.","zh":"如果語言缺席於家庭日常生活，孩子可能無法自然學會它。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to everyday family routines.","zh":"這個短語指日常家庭程序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"official language","meaning":"官方語言","examples":[{"en":"A language can be an official language without being widely spoken.","zh":"一種語言可以是官方語言，但未被廣泛使用。"},{"en":"An official language is a language recognised by a government for public use.","zh":"official language 是政府承認可用於公共用途的語言。"},{"en":"Government forms, courts and schools may use an official language.","zh":"政府表格、法庭和學校可能使用官方語言。"},{"en":"Official status can help a language, but it does not automatically make families speak it.","zh":"官方地位可以幫助語言，但不會自動令家庭使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes legal recognition, not necessarily daily popularity.","zh":"這個短語描述法律承認，而不一定是日常流行程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"ultimately","meaning":"歸根究底","examples":[{"en":"Ultimately, linguists believe that multilingualism offers the best solution.","zh":"歸根究底，語言學家相信多語能力提供最佳解決方法。"},{"en":"Ultimately means in the end, after considering everything.","zh":"ultimately 指在考慮一切之後，最終而言。"},{"en":"Ultimately, a student’s progress depends on practice, feedback and consistency.","zh":"歸根究底，學生進步取決於練習、回饋和持續性。"},{"en":"This word introduces the final or most important conclusion.","zh":"這個字引出最後或最重要的結論。"},{"en":"The phrase helps move from details to the main answer.","zh":"這個短語幫助由細節轉向主要答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the answer to","meaning":"……的解決方法","examples":[{"en":"Multilingualism may be the answer to the problem of language extinction.","zh":"多語能力可能是語言滅絕問題的解決方法。"},{"en":"The answer to a problem is the solution or best response to it.","zh":"the answer to 問題，是該問題的解決方案或最佳回應。"},{"en":"More reading practice may be the answer to a student’s weak vocabulary.","zh":"更多閱讀練習可能是學生詞彙薄弱的解決方法。"},{"en":"A good answer must deal with the real cause, not only the visible symptom.","zh":"好解決方法必須處理真正原因，而不只是表面症狀。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a proposed solution.","zh":"這個短語指出一個建議方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"language extinction","meaning":"語言滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Language extinction occurs when no fluent speakers remain.","zh":"當沒有流利使用者留下時，語言滅絕就會發生。"},{"en":"Language extinction means the complete disappearance of a language as a living form of communication.","zh":"language extinction 指一種語言作為活的溝通形式完全消失。"},{"en":"A language may face extinction if children no longer learn it from parents or elders.","zh":"如果孩子不再向父母或長者學習某語言，它可能面臨滅絕。"},{"en":"Extinction can erase songs, jokes, place names and ways of thinking.","zh":"滅絕可以抹去歌曲、笑話、地名和思考方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the final stage of language loss.","zh":"這個短語描述語言流失的最後階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"multilingualism","meaning":"多語能力；多語社會","examples":[{"en":"Multilingualism allows minority and majority languages to coexist.","zh":"多語能力讓少數族群語言和多數族群語言共存。"},{"en":"Multilingualism means the ability or practice of using more than one language.","zh":"multilingualism 指使用多於一種語言的能力或做法。"},{"en":"A child may use Cantonese at home, English at school and Mandarin with relatives.","zh":"孩子可能在家用廣東話，在學校用英語，與親戚用普通話。"},{"en":"When multilingualism is accepted, people do not have to abandon one language to learn another.","zh":"當多語能力被接受，人們不必為學另一種語言而放棄原有語言。"},{"en":"The phrase supports language coexistence rather than replacement.","zh":"這個短語支持語言共存，而不是取代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"people without formal education","meaning":"未受正規教育的人","examples":[{"en":"People without formal education can still learn several languages.","zh":"未受正規教育的人仍可以學習多種語言。"},{"en":"People without formal education are people who have not received structured schooling or certificates.","zh":"people without formal education 是沒有接受有結構學校教育或取得證書的人。"},{"en":"A market seller without formal education may speak several languages because customers use them.","zh":"未受正規教育的市場小販可能因顧客使用不同語言而會說幾種語言。"},{"en":"Daily need can teach language skills even when classroom learning is absent.","zh":"即使沒有課室學習，日常需要也可以教會語言技能。"},{"en":"The phrase separates real ability from school qualifications.","zh":"這個短語把真實能力與學校資歷分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"learn several languages","meaning":"學習多種語言","examples":[{"en":"Children are capable of learning several languages naturally.","zh":"兒童有能力自然學習多種語言。"},{"en":"To learn several languages means to acquire the ability to understand or use more than two languages.","zh":"learn several languages 指獲得理解或使用多於兩種語言的能力。"},{"en":"A child in a multilingual family may learn several languages through grandparents, school and friends.","zh":"多語家庭中的孩子可能透過祖父母、學校和朋友學習多種語言。"},{"en":"Early exposure makes learning easier because children hear patterns repeatedly.","zh":"早期接觸令學習較容易，因為孩子反覆聽到模式。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that multilingual ability is normal and possible.","zh":"這個短語顯示多語能力是正常且可能的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"as long as","meaning":"只要","examples":[{"en":"People can become multilingual as long as they begin learning early.","zh":"只要人們從小開始學習，就可以變成多語使用者。"},{"en":"As long as means provided that, or if this condition is met.","zh":"as long as 指只要，或如果某條件被滿足。"},{"en":"A student can improve quickly as long as she practises a little every day.","zh":"只要學生每天練習一點，她可以很快進步。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the condition needed for a result to happen.","zh":"這個短語引出結果發生所需的條件。"},{"en":"It shows that success depends on a requirement being satisfied.","zh":"它顯示成功取決於某要求是否被滿足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"start as children","meaning":"從小開始","examples":[{"en":"Language learning is often easier when people start as children.","zh":"當人們從小開始時，語言學習通常較容易。"},{"en":"To start as children means to begin doing or learning something while still young.","zh":"start as children 指仍年幼時開始做或學某事。"},{"en":"People who start music as children may find rhythm and listening easier later.","zh":"從小開始學音樂的人，之後可能覺得節奏和聆聽較容易。"},{"en":"Early habits can become natural because children practise them for many years.","zh":"早期習慣可以變得自然，因為孩子會練習很多年。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights the advantage of beginning young.","zh":"這個短語突出年幼開始的優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"indeed","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"Indeed, most people in the world speak more than one language.","zh":"事實上，世界上大多數人說多於一種語言。"},{"en":"Indeed means in fact, and it strengthens or confirms the previous point.","zh":"indeed 指事實上，並加強或確認前一點。"},{"en":"Many students enjoy stories; indeed, some learn grammar best through stories.","zh":"許多學生喜歡故事；事實上，有些人透過故事最能學好文法。"},{"en":"The word is useful when adding evidence that supports an idea.","zh":"這個字適合用來加入支持想法的證據。"},{"en":"It often introduces a stronger or more surprising fact.","zh":"它常引出更強或更令人意外的事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"speak more than one tongue","meaning":"說多於一種語言","examples":[{"en":"Most of the world’s population can speak more than one tongue.","zh":"世界上大多數人口能說多於一種語言。"},{"en":"To speak more than one tongue means to speak more than one language.","zh":"speak more than one tongue 指說多於一種語言。"},{"en":"A shopkeeper in a tourist area may speak more than one tongue to serve different customers.","zh":"旅遊區店主可能會說多於一種語言，以服務不同顧客。"},{"en":"Speaking several languages can help people work, travel and maintain family identity.","zh":"說幾種語言可以幫助人工作、旅行和維持家庭身份。"},{"en":"The phrase is a slightly literary way to describe multilingual ability.","zh":"這個短語是稍具文學感的方式來描述多語能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"distinct languages","meaning":"不同的語言","examples":[{"en":"Many people routinely speak several distinct languages.","zh":"許多人日常會說幾種不同的語言。"},{"en":"Distinct languages are separate languages, not just small variations of the same one.","zh":"distinct languages 是分開的語言，而不只是同一語言的小變體。"},{"en":"A student may speak Cantonese, English and Japanese as distinct languages.","zh":"學生可能會說廣東話、英語和日語這幾種不同語言。"},{"en":"Knowing distinct languages lets people move between different communities and cultures.","zh":"懂得不同語言讓人能在不同社群和文化之間轉換。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses clear difference between languages.","zh":"這個短語強調語言之間的清楚差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a dialect or two","meaning":"一兩種方言","examples":[{"en":"Multilingual speakers may also use a dialect or two.","zh":"多語使用者也可能使用一兩種方言。"},{"en":"A dialect or two means one or two regional or social varieties of a language.","zh":"a dialect or two 指一兩種地區或社會語言變體。"},{"en":"A person may speak standard English and a dialect or two from home or community life.","zh":"一個人可能會說標準英語，也會說家中或社區中的一兩種方言。"},{"en":"Dialects can carry humour, identity and local memory.","zh":"方言可以承載幽默、身份和本地記憶。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an informal sense of having extra speech varieties.","zh":"這個短語以較口語方式表示還有額外語言變體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"have a gut reaction","meaning":"有直覺上的反感","examples":[{"en":"Some people have a gut reaction against hearing unfamiliar languages.","zh":"有些人聽到不熟悉語言時會有直覺上的反感。"},{"en":"To have a gut reaction means to feel an immediate instinctive response before careful thought.","zh":"have a gut reaction 指在仔細思考前有即時本能反應。"},{"en":"A student may have a gut reaction of fear when seeing a very long exam question.","zh":"學生看到很長考題時，可能本能地感到害怕。"},{"en":"Gut reactions can be strong but are not always fair or accurate.","zh":"直覺反應可以很強，但不一定公平或準確。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an instinctive feeling.","zh":"這個短語描述本能感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in front of someone","meaning":"在某人面前","examples":[{"en":"Minority speakers may be criticised for using their language in front of others.","zh":"少數族群語言使用者可能因在他人面前使用自己的語言而被批評。"},{"en":"In front of someone means where that person can see or hear what is happening.","zh":"in front of someone 指在某人能看見或聽見事情發生的地方。"},{"en":"A child may feel embarrassed if corrected in front of classmates.","zh":"如果孩子在同學面前被糾正，可能感到尷尬。"},{"en":"Public criticism can make people avoid using their language openly.","zh":"公開批評可以令人避免公開使用自己的語言。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the presence of others.","zh":"這個短語重點在他人在場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"commit an immoral act","meaning":"做出不道德的行為","examples":[{"en":"Speaking another language should not be treated as though it were an immoral act.","zh":"說另一種語言不應被視為做出不道德的行為。"},{"en":"To commit an immoral act means to do something considered morally wrong.","zh":"commit an immoral act 指做出被認為道德上錯誤的事情。"},{"en":"Lying to take money from a friend is an immoral act.","zh":"向朋友說謊以取走金錢是不道德行為。"},{"en":"Treating language use as immoral can shame speakers and damage cultural identity.","zh":"把語言使用視為不道德，可以令使用者羞愧並損害文化身份。"},{"en":"The phrase describes wrongdoing in a moral sense, not just breaking a rule.","zh":"這個短語描述道德上的錯誤，而不只是違規。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"it is no coincidence that","meaning":"……並非巧合","examples":[{"en":"It is no coincidence that intolerance is common where languages disappear fastest.","zh":"不包容在語言消失最快的地方常見，這並非巧合。"},{"en":"It is no coincidence that means the connection is meaningful, not accidental.","zh":"it is no coincidence that 指兩者的連繫有意義，而不是偶然。"},{"en":"It is no coincidence that tired students often make more careless mistakes.","zh":"疲倦學生常犯更多粗心錯誤，這並非巧合。"},{"en":"When two patterns appear together repeatedly, one may help explain the other.","zh":"當兩種模式反覆一起出現，其中一個可能幫助解釋另一個。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a likely relationship between facts.","zh":"這個短語指出事實之間可能存在關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"disappear the fastest","meaning":"消失得最快","examples":[{"en":"Minority languages disappear the fastest in some largely monolingual societies.","zh":"在一些大致單語的社會中，少數族群語言消失得最快。"},{"en":"To disappear the fastest means to be lost more quickly than others.","zh":"disappear the fastest 指比其他事物更快失去。"},{"en":"Small shops may disappear the fastest in areas where rent rises sharply.","zh":"在租金急升的地區，小店可能消失得最快。"},{"en":"Languages may disappear quickly when speakers feel pressure to use only the dominant language.","zh":"當使用者感到壓力只使用主導語言，語言可能快速消失。"},{"en":"The phrase compares speed of loss.","zh":"這個短語比較流失速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the first step in doing something","meaning":"做某事的第一步","examples":[{"en":"The first step in saving a language is to respect its speakers.","zh":"拯救一種語言的第一步是尊重其使用者。"},{"en":"The first step in doing something is the earliest action needed to begin a process.","zh":"the first step in doing something 是開始某過程所需的最早行動。"},{"en":"The first step in improving writing is to understand the question clearly.","zh":"改善寫作的第一步是清楚理解題目。"},{"en":"A good first step creates the foundation for later success.","zh":"好的第一步會為之後成功建立基礎。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies where practical action should begin.","zh":"這個短語指出實際行動應從哪裏開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"persuade the majority to","meaning":"說服多數族群去……","examples":[{"en":"Communities must persuade the majority to accept linguistic diversity.","zh":"社群必須說服多數族群接受語言多樣性。"},{"en":"To persuade the majority to do something means to convince the larger or more powerful group to accept an idea or action.","zh":"persuade the majority to do something 指說服較大或較有權力群體接受某想法或行動。"},{"en":"Student leaders may persuade the majority to support a recycling scheme.","zh":"學生領袖可能說服大多數人支持回收計劃。"},{"en":"If the majority changes its attitude, minority groups may feel safer using their language.","zh":"如果多數族群改變態度，少數群體可能更安心使用自己的語言。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on changing the views of the larger group.","zh":"這個短語重點在改變較大群體的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"minority communities","meaning":"少數族群社區","examples":[{"en":"Minority communities should be free to maintain their languages.","zh":"少數族群社區應能自由維持自己的語言。"},{"en":"Minority communities are smaller groups within a society that may have their own language, culture or identity.","zh":"minority communities 是社會中較小的群體，可能有自己的語言、文化或身份。"},{"en":"A minority community may run weekend classes to teach children its heritage language.","zh":"少數族群社區可能開辦週末班教孩子傳承語言。"},{"en":"When minority communities are respected, their members feel less pressure to hide their identity.","zh":"當少數族群社區受到尊重，其成員較少感到要隱藏身份。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to groups with less social or numerical power.","zh":"這個短語指社會或人口上權力較少的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"speak with one’s own voice","meaning":"用自己的聲音發言","examples":[{"en":"Minority groups must be allowed to speak with their own voices.","zh":"少數族群必須被容許用自己的聲音發言。"},{"en":"To speak with one’s own voice means to express one’s own identity, experience and language freely.","zh":"speak with one’s own voice 指自由表達自己的身份、經驗和語言。"},{"en":"Students speak with their own voices when they write about their real neighbourhoods and families.","zh":"學生寫自己真實社區和家庭時，就是用自己的聲音發言。"},{"en":"If people cannot speak in their own way, their culture may be represented by outsiders only.","zh":"如果人們不能以自己的方式說話，他們的文化可能只由外人代表。"},{"en":"The phrase means having authentic expression and agency.","zh":"這個短語指真實表達和自主性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct heading for each paragraph.","zh":"考生為每段選出正確標題。"},{"en":"To choose the correct heading means to select the title that best summarises a paragraph.","zh":"choose the correct heading 指選出最能概括段落的標題。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should identify the main idea before choosing a heading.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先辨認主旨，再選標題。"},{"en":"A heading is wrong if it matches only one small detail but misses the main point.","zh":"如果標題只符合一個小細節卻忽略主旨，就是錯誤標題。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard exam instruction for paragraph matching.","zh":"這個短語是段落配對的標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the most suitable heading","meaning":"最合適的標題","examples":[{"en":"The most suitable heading should summarise the paragraph’s main idea.","zh":"最合適的標題應概括段落主旨。"},{"en":"The most suitable heading is the title that fits the overall meaning best.","zh":"the most suitable heading 是最符合整體意思的標題。"},{"en":"A paragraph about causes of stress needs a heading about causes, not just one example.","zh":"關於壓力成因的段落，需要關於成因的標題，而不只是其中一個例子。"},{"en":"Choosing the best heading requires understanding the whole paragraph.","zh":"選最佳標題需要理解整段。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the best match, not a merely possible match.","zh":"這個短語重點在最佳配對，而不只是可能配對。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"consistent documentation","meaning":"持續而有系統的記錄","examples":[{"en":"Consistent documentation is essential when a language is close to extinction.","zh":"當語言接近滅絕時，持續而有系統的記錄至關重要。"},{"en":"Consistent documentation means regular, organised and reliable recording of information.","zh":"consistent documentation 指定期、有組織且可靠地記錄資訊。"},{"en":"A nurse keeps consistent documentation by writing patient symptoms every day.","zh":"護士每天寫下病人症狀，就是保持持續而有系統的記錄。"},{"en":"Without consistent records, later workers may not know what has already been studied.","zh":"沒有持續記錄，後來工作者可能不知道已研究過甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses steady and systematic recording.","zh":"這個短語強調穩定而有系統的記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"an initial recommendation","meaning":"初步建議","examples":[{"en":"Experts reached an initial recommendation for saving dying languages.","zh":"專家就拯救垂危語言達成初步建議。"},{"en":"An initial recommendation is the first suggestion made before a final or fuller plan.","zh":"initial recommendation 是在最終或完整計劃前提出的第一個建議。"},{"en":"A doctor may give an initial recommendation before test results confirm the diagnosis.","zh":"醫生可能在檢測結果確認診斷前給出初步建議。"},{"en":"Early recommendations help people begin action while more evidence is gathered.","zh":"早期建議幫助人在收集更多證據時先開始行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a first-stage suggestion.","zh":"這個短語描述第一階段建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"reach a consensus on","meaning":"就……達成共識","examples":[{"en":"Linguists reached a consensus on the importance of multilingualism.","zh":"語言學家就多語能力的重要性達成共識。"},{"en":"To reach a consensus on something means to come to a shared agreement about it.","zh":"reach a consensus on 某事，指對它形成共同一致意見。"},{"en":"A class may reach a consensus on the best date for a field trip.","zh":"一班學生可能就考察日期達成共識。"},{"en":"Consensus makes action easier because people are no longer arguing about the basic point.","zh":"共識令行動較容易，因為人們不再爭論基本點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes agreement after discussion.","zh":"這個短語描述討論後的同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"positive gains","meaning":"正面進展","examples":[{"en":"New grants and archives represent positive gains for language protection.","zh":"新撥款和檔案庫代表語言保育的正面進展。"},{"en":"Positive gains are helpful improvements or achievements.","zh":"positive gains 是有幫助的改善或成就。"},{"en":"A school may see positive gains when reading scores rise and students borrow more books.","zh":"當閱讀分數上升且學生借更多書，學校可能看到正面進展。"},{"en":"Gains can encourage people to continue a difficult project.","zh":"進展可以鼓勵人們繼續困難項目。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on measurable or meaningful progress.","zh":"這個短語重點在可衡量或有意義的進步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"language protection","meaning":"語言保育","examples":[{"en":"Community teaching programmes can support language protection.","zh":"社區教學計劃可以支持語言保育。"},{"en":"Language protection means efforts to prevent a language from disappearing or being weakened.","zh":"language protection 指防止語言消失或被削弱的努力。"},{"en":"A village may support language protection by using the local language in signs and festivals.","zh":"村莊可能透過在標誌和節日中使用本地語言來支持語言保育。"},{"en":"Protection works best when children hear the language in daily life.","zh":"當孩子在日常生活中聽到該語言，保育效果最好。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to active defence of a language.","zh":"這個短語指對語言的主動保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"minimum requirements","meaning":"最低要求","examples":[{"en":"Natural conversation records may be minimum requirements for successful revitalisation.","zh":"自然對話記錄可能是成功復興的最低要求。"},{"en":"Minimum requirements are the basic things that must be present for something to work.","zh":"minimum requirements 是某事要有效運作必須具備的基本條件。"},{"en":"A computer class has minimum requirements such as working laptops and internet access.","zh":"電腦課的最低要求包括可用手提電腦和網絡連接。"},{"en":"If minimum requirements are missing, even a good plan may fail.","zh":"如果缺少最低要求，即使好計劃也可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what is absolutely necessary.","zh":"這個短語指出絕對必要的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a potential threat to","meaning":"對……的潛在威脅","examples":[{"en":"Negative attitudes are a potential threat to minority languages.","zh":"負面態度是對少數族群語言的潛在威脅。"},{"en":"A potential threat to something is something that could harm it, even if damage has not happened yet.","zh":"potential threat to 某事，是可能傷害它的事物，即使傷害尚未發生。"},{"en":"Rising rent is a potential threat to small local shops.","zh":"租金上升是對本地小店的潛在威脅。"},{"en":"Early warning matters because potential threats can become real damage.","zh":"早期警告重要，因為潛在威脅可以變成真正傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a possible danger.","zh":"這個短語描述可能危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"minority languages","meaning":"少數族群語言","examples":[{"en":"Minority languages need social acceptance as well as documentation.","zh":"少數族群語言需要社會接受，也需要記錄。"},{"en":"Minority languages are languages used by smaller or less powerful groups in a society.","zh":"minority languages 是由社會中較小或較少權力群體使用的語言。"},{"en":"A minority language may be spoken at home but not used in schools or government offices.","zh":"少數族群語言可能在家中使用，但不在學校或政府辦公室使用。"},{"en":"If minority languages are mocked, young people may stop speaking them.","zh":"如果少數族群語言被嘲笑，年輕人可能停止使用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to languages with less social power, not less value.","zh":"這個短語指社會權力較少的語言，而不是價值較低的語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a period when no real effort was made","meaning":"一段沒有實際行動的時期","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes a period when no real coordinated effort was made.","zh":"文章描述一段沒有真正協調行動的時期。"},{"en":"A period when no real effort was made is a time when people talked about a problem but took little practical action.","zh":"a period when no real effort was made 是人們談論問題但幾乎沒有實際行動的時期。"},{"en":"A school may have a period when no real effort is made to improve bullying prevention.","zh":"學校可能有一段沒有實際努力改善欺凌預防的時期。"},{"en":"Such periods can allow problems to become worse quietly.","zh":"這類時期可以讓問題悄悄惡化。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises delay and inaction.","zh":"這個短語批評拖延和不作為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"native-language programmes","meaning":"本族語言課程","examples":[{"en":"New Zealand and Hawaii launched native-language programmes for children.","zh":"新西蘭和夏威夷為兒童推出本族語言課程。"},{"en":"Native-language programmes are organised courses or projects that teach a community’s traditional language.","zh":"native-language programmes 是教授社群傳統語言的有組織課程或項目。"},{"en":"A weekend school may run native-language programmes for children of migrant families.","zh":"週末學校可能為移民家庭兒童開辦本族語言課程。"},{"en":"Such programmes help young learners connect language with identity and family history.","zh":"這類課程幫助年輕學習者把語言與身份和家族歷史連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to planned education in a heritage language.","zh":"這個短語指以傳承語言進行的有計劃教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"lack of confidence","meaning":"缺乏信心","examples":[{"en":"A lack of confidence among speakers can weaken a language.","zh":"使用者缺乏信心可以削弱一種語言。"},{"en":"Lack of confidence means not believing that something is valuable, useful or worth using.","zh":"lack of confidence 指不相信某事有價值、有用或值得使用。"},{"en":"A student may speak less English because of a lack of confidence, even if she knows the words.","zh":"學生可能因缺乏信心而少說英語，即使她知道詞語。"},{"en":"When speakers lose confidence in their language, they may choose a dominant language instead.","zh":"當使用者對自己的語言失去信心，他們可能改用主導語言。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an inner barrier that changes behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述會改變行為的內在障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a negative factor","meaning":"負面因素","examples":[{"en":"Social shame can become a negative factor in language survival.","zh":"社會羞恥感可以成為語言存續中的負面因素。"},{"en":"A negative factor is something that harms a situation or makes success less likely.","zh":"negative factor 是會傷害情況或降低成功可能性的事物。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is a negative factor in exam performance.","zh":"睡眠不足是考試表現中的負面因素。"},{"en":"Negative factors may not destroy something alone, but they can increase risk.","zh":"負面因素未必單獨摧毀某事，但可以增加風險。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies something that works against success.","zh":"這個短語指出阻礙成功的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"practices in developing countries","meaning":"發展中國家的做法","examples":[{"en":"Multilingual practices are common in several developing countries.","zh":"多語做法在幾個發展中國家很常見。"},{"en":"Practices in developing countries are ways of living, learning or working found in countries with developing economies.","zh":"practices in developing countries 是在經濟發展中的國家裏出現的生活、學習或工作方式。"},{"en":"In some developing countries, children naturally use one language at home and another at school.","zh":"在一些發展中國家，孩子自然地在家用一種語言，在學校用另一種語言。"},{"en":"Such practices can show that multilingualism is practical even without rich resources.","zh":"這類做法可以顯示，即使沒有豐富資源，多語能力仍然實際可行。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to real habits or systems in developing societies.","zh":"這個短語指發展中社會的真實習慣或制度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the value of minority languages","meaning":"少數族群語言的價值","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains the scientific value of minority languages.","zh":"文章解釋少數族群語言的科學價值。"},{"en":"The value of minority languages means the cultural, scientific and social importance of languages spoken by smaller groups.","zh":"the value of minority languages 指由較小群體使用的語言在文化、科學和社會上的重要性。"},{"en":"A minority language may preserve medical plant names unknown in the majority language.","zh":"少數族群語言可能保存多數族群語言中沒有的藥用植物名稱。"},{"en":"If people recognise this value, they are more likely to support preservation.","zh":"如果人們認識這種價值，就更可能支持保存。"},{"en":"The phrase challenges the idea that small languages are unimportant.","zh":"這個短語挑戰小語種不重要的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"government participation","meaning":"政府參與","examples":[{"en":"Government participation can strengthen language-preservation programmes.","zh":"政府參與可以加強語言保存計劃。"},{"en":"Government participation means involvement, support or action from public authorities.","zh":"government participation 指公共機關的參與、支持或行動。"},{"en":"A government may participate by funding language classes or recognising local languages in schools.","zh":"政府可以透過資助語言課程或在學校承認本地語言來參與。"},{"en":"Official support can give programmes money, status and long-term stability.","zh":"官方支持可以給計劃帶來金錢、地位和長期穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the role of public institutions.","zh":"這個短語描述公共機構的角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"language preservation","meaning":"語言保存","examples":[{"en":"Funding and education are both important for language preservation.","zh":"資金和教育對語言保存都很重要。"},{"en":"Language preservation means protecting a language so it can be studied, remembered or used in the future.","zh":"language preservation 指保護語言，使它未來仍能被研究、記住或使用。"},{"en":"A community can support language preservation by recording elders and teaching children.","zh":"社區可以透過記錄長者和教導兒童來支持語言保存。"},{"en":"Preservation is stronger when documentation and daily use happen together.","zh":"當記錄和日常使用同時進行，保存工作會更有力。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on preventing language loss.","zh":"這個短語重點在防止語言流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"match people with opinions or deeds","meaning":"把人物與觀點或行動配對","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match each person with the correct opinion or deed.","zh":"考生把每個人物與正確觀點或行動配對。"},{"en":"To match people with opinions or deeds means to connect each named person to what they said or did.","zh":"match people with opinions or deeds 指把每位具名人物與其說法或行動連起來。"},{"en":"In a history task, students may match leaders with reforms they introduced.","zh":"在歷史題中，學生可能把領袖與他們推行的改革配對。"},{"en":"This question type requires careful reading because names and actions may be far apart in the text.","zh":"這類題型需要仔細閱讀，因為名字和行動可能在文本中相距很遠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a reading-test matching task.","zh":"這個短語描述閱讀測驗中的配對任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the appropriate letter","meaning":"適當的字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write the appropriate letter beside each statement.","zh":"考生在每句陳述旁寫上適當的字母。"},{"en":"The appropriate letter is the answer option that correctly matches the statement.","zh":"appropriate letter 是正確配對該陳述的答案選項。"},{"en":"In a matching exercise, students should write the appropriate letter only after checking evidence.","zh":"在配對練習中，學生應在查核證據後才寫上適當字母。"},{"en":"Choosing the wrong letter often means the student matched a detail to the wrong person.","zh":"選錯字母通常代表學生把細節配給錯誤人物。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the correct option label.","zh":"這個短語指正確選項標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"report a conservation practice","meaning":"報道一項保育做法","examples":[{"en":"Grimes reported a successful language-conservation practice in Hawaii.","zh":"Grimes 報道了夏威夷一項成功的語言保育做法。"},{"en":"To report a conservation practice means to describe or present a method used to protect something.","zh":"report a conservation practice 指描述或呈現用來保護某物的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may report a conservation practice after students successfully reduce paper waste.","zh":"學生成功減少紙張浪費後，老師可能報道一項保育做法。"},{"en":"Reporting a practice helps other communities learn what might work.","zh":"報道一種做法幫助其他社群學習甚麼可能有效。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sharing an example of preservation work.","zh":"這個短語描述分享保存工作的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"predict that languages would disappear","meaning":"預測語言將會消失","examples":[{"en":"Krauss predicted that many languages would disappear within a century.","zh":"Krauss 預測許多語言會在一個世紀內消失。"},{"en":"To predict that languages would disappear means to forecast that they would stop being used in the future.","zh":"predict that languages would disappear 指預測它們將來會停止被使用。"},{"en":"A researcher may predict that a dialect will disappear if no children speak it at home.","zh":"如果沒有孩子在家說某方言，研究人員可能預測它將會消失。"},{"en":"Such predictions can warn communities before the loss becomes irreversible.","zh":"這類預測可以在損失變得不可逆轉前警告社群。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a forecast about future language loss.","zh":"這個短語描述關於未來語言流失的預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"personally witness","meaning":"親身見證","examples":[{"en":"Hale personally witnessed several languages dying out.","zh":"Hale 親身見證幾種語言消亡。"},{"en":"To personally witness something means to see or experience it directly oneself.","zh":"personally witness 某事，指自己直接看見或經歷它。"},{"en":"A nurse may personally witness how poor housing affects patients’ health.","zh":"護士可能親身見證惡劣住屋如何影響病人健康。"},{"en":"Direct experience can make a problem feel more urgent than statistics alone.","zh":"直接經驗可以令問題比單靠統計更顯迫切。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses firsthand observation.","zh":"這個短語強調親身觀察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"die out","meaning":"滅絕；消失","examples":[{"en":"Several languages Hale studied later died out.","zh":"Hale 研究過的幾種語言後來消失了。"},{"en":"To die out means to disappear completely because no one continues using or practising it.","zh":"die out 指因沒有人繼續使用或實踐而完全消失。"},{"en":"A local custom may die out if young people no longer learn it.","zh":"如果年輕人不再學習，本地習俗可能消失。"},{"en":"Languages die out when the last fluent speakers pass away or switch languages.","zh":"當最後流利使用者去世或轉用其他語言，語言就會消亡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual disappearance.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"raise funds for","meaning":"為……籌款","examples":[{"en":"Ostler raised funds for language preservation in England.","zh":"Ostler 在英格蘭為語言保存籌款。"},{"en":"To raise funds for something means to collect money to support it.","zh":"raise funds for 某事，指籌集金錢來支持它。"},{"en":"Students may raise funds for a library by selling handmade cards.","zh":"學生可能透過售賣手製卡片為圖書館籌款。"},{"en":"Fundraising can turn concern into practical support for equipment, teachers or travel.","zh":"籌款可以把關注轉化成對設備、老師或旅費的實際支持。"},{"en":"The phrase describes collecting money for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述為某目的籌集金錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"observe that","meaning":"觀察到；指出","examples":[{"en":"Thomason observed that insufficient effort had been made.","zh":"Thomason 指出所作努力不足。"},{"en":"To observe that something is true means to notice it and state it as a comment or finding.","zh":"observe that 某事為真，指注意到它並作為評論或發現說出。"},{"en":"A teacher may observe that students write better after reading clear examples.","zh":"老師可能觀察到學生閱讀清楚例子後寫得更好。"},{"en":"Observations can draw attention to problems that others have ignored.","zh":"觀察可以令人注意到其他人忽視的問題。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a careful remark based on evidence or experience.","zh":"這個短語引出基於證據或經驗的仔細評論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"insufficient effort","meaning":"不足的努力","examples":[{"en":"Researchers criticised the insufficient effort devoted to endangered languages.","zh":"研究人員批評投放於瀕危語言的努力不足。"},{"en":"Insufficient effort means not enough work, time or resources have been used.","zh":"insufficient effort 指投入的工作、時間或資源不夠。"},{"en":"A student may fail because of insufficient effort if she rarely revises or asks questions.","zh":"如果學生很少溫習或提問，她可能因努力不足而失敗。"},{"en":"When effort is insufficient, important goals remain unfinished.","zh":"當努力不足，重要目標會仍未完成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a lack of serious action.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏認真行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the real result of","meaning":"……的實際成果","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the real result of the master-apprentice programme.","zh":"題目問師徒制計劃的實際成果。"},{"en":"The real result of something is what actually happened, not what people hoped or claimed.","zh":"the real result of 某事，是實際發生的結果，而不是人們希望或聲稱的結果。"},{"en":"The real result of a new homework policy may be less stress, not higher grades.","zh":"新功課政策的實際成果可能是壓力減少，而不是成績提高。"},{"en":"Looking at real results helps people judge a programme honestly.","zh":"查看實際成果幫助人誠實評估計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase separates actual outcomes from expectations.","zh":"這個短語把實際結果與期望分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"revive an endangered language","meaning":"復興一種瀕危語言","examples":[{"en":"A single programme may not be enough to fully revive an endangered language.","zh":"單一計劃可能不足以完全復興一種瀕危語言。"},{"en":"To revive an endangered language means to bring a threatened language back into active use.","zh":"revive an endangered language 指把受威脅語言重新帶回積極使用。"},{"en":"A community may revive an endangered language by teaching children and using it in public events.","zh":"社區可以透過教孩子並在公共活動中使用它來復興瀕危語言。"},{"en":"Revival requires more than records; people must want and need to speak the language.","zh":"復興不只需要記錄；人們必須想說並需要說該語言。"},{"en":"The phrase describes restoring life to a language at risk.","zh":"這個短語描述令瀕危語言重新有生命力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"postpone the extinction of","meaning":"延遲……的滅絕","examples":[{"en":"The programme helped postpone the extinction of several languages.","zh":"該計劃幫助延遲幾種語言的滅絕。"},{"en":"To postpone the extinction of something means to delay its complete disappearance.","zh":"postpone the extinction of 某物，指延後其完全消失。"},{"en":"A small grant may postpone the closure of a community centre until new funding arrives.","zh":"小額撥款可能延遲社區中心關閉，直到新資金到來。"},{"en":"Delaying extinction can give people time to record, teach or revive what remains.","zh":"延遲滅絕可以給人時間記錄、教學或復興剩餘內容。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests buying time, not necessarily solving the whole problem.","zh":"這個短語暗示爭取時間，不一定解決整個問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"increase communication between","meaning":"加強……之間的溝通","examples":[{"en":"Shared activities may increase communication between elders and learners.","zh":"共同活動可能加強長者與學習者之間的溝通。"},{"en":"To increase communication between people means to make them talk or exchange information more often.","zh":"increase communication between 人們，指令他們更常交談或交換資訊。"},{"en":"Group projects can increase communication between quiet students and their classmates.","zh":"小組項目可以加強安靜學生與同學之間的溝通。"},{"en":"More communication helps people build trust and share knowledge naturally.","zh":"更多溝通幫助人建立信任並自然分享知識。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strengthening contact through interaction.","zh":"這個短語描述透過互動加強接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"according to the final paragraph","meaning":"根據最後一段","examples":[{"en":"According to the final paragraph, tolerance is essential for language survival.","zh":"根據最後一段，包容對語言存續至關重要。"},{"en":"According to the final paragraph means based on information stated in the last paragraph of the text.","zh":"according to the final paragraph 指基於文本最後一段所述資訊。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should check the final paragraph before answering a question that mentions it.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生回答提到最後一段的問題前，應先查閱最後一段。"},{"en":"The phrase tells readers exactly where the evidence should come from.","zh":"這個短語清楚告訴讀者證據應來自哪裏。"},{"en":"It is an instruction to use a specific part of the passage.","zh":"它是一項使用文章特定部分的指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"majority-language speakers","meaning":"多數族群語言使用者","examples":[{"en":"Majority-language speakers should respect people who use minority languages.","zh":"多數族群語言使用者應尊重使用少數族群語言的人。"},{"en":"Majority-language speakers are people who speak the socially dominant or most widely used language.","zh":"majority-language speakers 是使用社會主導或最廣泛使用語言的人。"},{"en":"In a classroom, majority-language speakers should not laugh at classmates who use another home language.","zh":"在課室中，多數族群語言使用者不應取笑使用另一家庭語言的同學。"},{"en":"Their attitude can make minority speakers feel safe or ashamed.","zh":"他們的態度可以令少數語言使用者感到安全或羞愧。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to speakers of the language with greater social power.","zh":"這個短語指較有社會權力語言的使用者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"show loyalty to","meaning":"表達對……的忠誠","examples":[{"en":"Speakers may show loyalty to a language by using it in daily life.","zh":"使用者可以透過在日常生活中使用一種語言來表達對它的忠誠。"},{"en":"To show loyalty to something means to support it steadily and not abandon it easily.","zh":"show loyalty to 某事，指穩定支持它且不輕易放棄。"},{"en":"A family may show loyalty to its home dialect by speaking it during meals.","zh":"家庭可以透過飯桌上說家庭方言來表達對它的忠誠。"},{"en":"Loyalty becomes visible through repeated choices, not only words of support.","zh":"忠誠透過反覆選擇顯現，而不只是口頭支持。"},{"en":"The phrase describes commitment shown through action.","zh":"這個短語描述透過行動展示承諾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be tolerant of","meaning":"對……包容","examples":[{"en":"Societies need to be more tolerant of minority-language speakers.","zh":"社會需要更包容少數族群語言使用者。"},{"en":"To be tolerant of someone means to accept differences without hostility or unfair treatment.","zh":"be tolerant of 某人，指接受差異而不抱敵意或不公平對待。"},{"en":"A school should be tolerant of students who speak different home languages.","zh":"學校應包容說不同家庭語言的學生。"},{"en":"Tolerance helps people feel safe enough to use their language openly.","zh":"包容幫助人感到安全，能公開使用自己的語言。"},{"en":"The phrase describes respectful acceptance of difference.","zh":"這個短語描述對差異的尊重和接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"minority-language speakers","meaning":"少數族群語言使用者","examples":[{"en":"Minority-language speakers should be free to use their language publicly.","zh":"少數族群語言使用者應能自由公開使用自己的語言。"},{"en":"Minority-language speakers are people who use a language spoken by a smaller or less powerful group.","zh":"minority-language speakers 是使用較小或較少權力群體語言的人。"},{"en":"A minority-language speaker may use one language at home and the majority language at school or work.","zh":"少數族群語言使用者可能在家用一種語言，在學校或工作中用多數族群語言。"},{"en":"If minority-language speakers are mocked, they may stop passing the language to children.","zh":"如果少數族群語言使用者被嘲笑，他們可能停止把語言傳給孩子。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people whose language needs respect and protection, not pity.","zh":"這個短語指語言需要尊重和保護的人，而不是需要憐憫的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 158 - Save Endangered Language.pdf","sourcePage":22}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 159":[{"front":"designed to last","meaning":"設計得經久耐用","examples":[{"en":"Sustainable products should be designed to last for many years.","zh":"可持續產品應設計得經久耐用，可以使用多年。"},{"en":"Designed to last means made strong enough to be useful for a long time.","zh":"設計得經久耐用，是指製造得足夠堅固，可以長時間有用。"},{"en":"A school bag designed to last should survive years of books, rain, and daily use.","zh":"設計得經久耐用的書包應能承受多年書本、雨水和日常使用。"},{"en":"Products designed to last reduce waste because people do not need to replace them quickly.","zh":"設計得經久耐用的產品能減少浪費，因為人們不用很快更換它們。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on durability, not just attractive appearance.","zh":"這個短語聚焦耐用性，而不只是外觀吸引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"throwaway culture","meaning":"即棄文化","examples":[{"en":"Better product design may help change our throwaway culture.","zh":"更好的產品設計可能有助改變我們的即棄文化。"},{"en":"Throwaway culture is a way of living in which people buy, use, and discard things quickly.","zh":"即棄文化是一種人們快速購買、使用和丟棄物品的生活方式。"},{"en":"Buying a cheap phone case every month is part of throwaway culture.","zh":"每個月買一個便宜手機殼，就是即棄文化的一部分。"},{"en":"Throwaway culture creates waste because products are replaced before they are truly worn out.","zh":"即棄文化會製造浪費，因為產品在真正損壞前已被更換。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises habits of quick consumption and quick disposal.","zh":"這個短語批評快速消費和快速棄置的習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cure our throwaway culture","meaning":"改變我們的即棄文化","examples":[{"en":"The writer asks whether better design could cure our throwaway culture.","zh":"作者問更好的設計能否改變我們的即棄文化。"},{"en":"To cure our throwaway culture means to solve or greatly reduce society’s habit of discarding things too easily.","zh":"改變我們的即棄文化，是指解決或大幅減少社會太容易丟棄物品的習慣。"},{"en":"Repairable furniture could help cure our throwaway culture by making people keep it longer.","zh":"可維修家具可以令人們更長時間保留它，從而幫助改變即棄文化。"},{"en":"This culture can be cured only if design, business, and consumer habits all change.","zh":"只有當設計、商業和消費習慣都改變，這種文化才可能被改善。"},{"en":"The phrase treats wasteful consumption like a social illness that needs treatment.","zh":"這個短語把浪費性消費視為需要治療的社會問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"senior lecturer","meaning":"高級講師","examples":[{"en":"Jonathan Chapman is a senior lecturer at the University of Brighton.","zh":"Jonathan Chapman 是 Brighton 大學的高級講師。"},{"en":"A senior lecturer is an experienced university teacher, often with research and teaching responsibilities.","zh":"高級講師是有經驗的大學教師，通常有研究和教學責任。"},{"en":"A senior lecturer may teach courses, supervise students, and publish academic work.","zh":"高級講師可能教授課程、指導學生並發表學術作品。"},{"en":"The title suggests that Chapman has professional authority in design education.","zh":"這個職銜暗示 Chapman 在設計教育方面有專業權威。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an academic position, not a casual public speaker.","zh":"這個短語指學術職位，而不是普通公開演講者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a new breed of","meaning":"新一代的……","examples":[{"en":"Chapman belongs to a new breed of sustainable designers.","zh":"Chapman 屬於新一代可持續設計師。"},{"en":"A new breed of people means a new type or generation with different ideas or methods.","zh":"新一代的人，是指有不同想法或方法的新類型或新世代。"},{"en":"A new breed of teachers uses technology but still keeps human feedback central.","zh":"新一代老師使用科技，但仍把人性化回饋放在核心。"},{"en":"New social problems often create a new breed of professionals to solve them.","zh":"新社會問題常催生新一代專業人士去解決它們。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests fresh thinking within a field.","zh":"這個短語暗示某領域中的新思維。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sustainable designers","meaning":"可持續設計師","examples":[{"en":"Sustainable designers aim to reduce waste and environmental damage.","zh":"可持續設計師旨在減少浪費和環境破壞。"},{"en":"Sustainable designers create products, systems, or services that use resources responsibly.","zh":"可持續設計師創造負責任使用資源的產品、系統或服務。"},{"en":"A sustainable designer may choose recycled materials for a chair.","zh":"可持續設計師可能為椅子選用回收材料。"},{"en":"Their work matters because design decisions affect how long products last and how easily they are repaired.","zh":"他們的工作很重要，因為設計決定會影響產品能用多久以及是否容易維修。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to designers who consider environmental and social impact.","zh":"這個短語指會考慮環境和社會影響的設計師。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be concerned about","meaning":"關注；擔心……","examples":[{"en":"Many designers are concerned about excessive consumer waste.","zh":"許多設計師關注過度消費浪費。"},{"en":"To be concerned about something means to be worried about it because it may cause harm.","zh":"關注或擔心某事，是指因它可能造成傷害而憂慮。"},{"en":"Parents may be concerned about children spending too much time online.","zh":"父母可能擔心孩子花太多時間上網。"},{"en":"Designers become concerned when products are used briefly and then thrown away.","zh":"當產品只被短暫使用就被丟棄，設計師會感到擔心。"},{"en":"This phrase shows serious worry, not casual curiosity.","zh":"這個短語表示認真的憂慮，而不是隨意好奇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"huge waste associated with","meaning":"與……有關的巨大浪費","examples":[{"en":"They are concerned about the huge waste associated with consumer culture.","zh":"他們關注與消費文化有關的巨大浪費。"},{"en":"Huge waste associated with something means large-scale waste connected to or caused by it.","zh":"與某事有關的巨大浪費，是指與它相連或由它造成的大規模浪費。"},{"en":"There is huge waste associated with school lunches when uneaten food is thrown away daily.","zh":"如果學生每天丟掉未吃完的食物，學校午餐就有巨大浪費。"},{"en":"Consumer culture creates waste when people replace useful items simply because newer ones appear.","zh":"當人們只因新產品出現便更換仍可用物品，消費文化就製造浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase links a problem to the system that produces it.","zh":"這個短語把問題與造成它的系統連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Western consumer culture","meaning":"西方消費文化","examples":[{"en":"Western consumer culture encourages people to replace products frequently.","zh":"西方消費文化鼓勵人們頻繁更換產品。"},{"en":"Western consumer culture refers to buying habits in many wealthy Western societies where new products are strongly promoted.","zh":"西方消費文化指許多富裕西方社會中的購買習慣，其中新產品被大力推廣。"},{"en":"In Western consumer culture, advertising often links identity with possessions.","zh":"在西方消費文化中，廣告常把身份與擁有物聯繫起來。"},{"en":"This culture can increase waste because people feel pressure to own the newest version.","zh":"這種文化會增加浪費，因為人們感到有壓力要擁有最新版本。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a social pattern, not every individual person.","zh":"這個短語描述社會模式，而不是每一個個人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"damage to the environment","meaning":"對環境造成的破壞","examples":[{"en":"Consumer waste causes serious damage to the environment.","zh":"消費浪費對環境造成嚴重破壞。"},{"en":"Damage to the environment means harm done to air, water, land, wildlife, or ecosystems.","zh":"對環境造成的破壞，是指對空氣、水、土地、野生動物或生態系統的傷害。"},{"en":"Plastic rubbish can cause damage to the environment when it enters rivers and seas.","zh":"塑膠垃圾進入河流和海洋時，會對環境造成破壞。"},{"en":"Product waste damages the environment because materials, energy, and disposal all have costs.","zh":"產品浪費會破壞環境，因為材料、能源和棄置都有成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harm beyond human convenience.","zh":"這個短語描述超越人類方便的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"aim to create","meaning":"致力創造……","examples":[{"en":"Some designers aim to create objects that people will value for longer.","zh":"有些設計師致力創造人們會更長久珍惜的物品。"},{"en":"To aim to create something means to have the goal of making it.","zh":"致力創造某物，是指以製造它為目標。"},{"en":"A teacher may aim to create lessons that students can actually use outside class.","zh":"老師可能致力創造學生能在課外真正使用的課堂。"},{"en":"Designers aim to create lasting products because short-lived products lead to waste.","zh":"設計師致力創造耐用產品，因為短命產品會導致浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on intention and design purpose.","zh":"這個短語聚焦意圖和設計目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"want to keep","meaning":"想保留","examples":[{"en":"Emotionally meaningful objects are items that people want to keep.","zh":"有情感意義的物品是人們想保留的東西。"},{"en":"Want to keep means feel a desire to continue owning or using something.","zh":"想保留，是指希望繼續擁有或使用某物。"},{"en":"A child may want to keep an old toy because it reminds them of family.","zh":"孩子可能想保留舊玩具，因為它令他想起家人。"},{"en":"People keep meaningful objects longer, so fewer items are thrown away.","zh":"人們會更長時間保留有意義的物品，因此較少東西被丟棄。"},{"en":"This phrase shows emotional attachment, not only practical use.","zh":"這個短語顯示情感依附，而不只是實際用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rather than discard","meaning":"而不是丟棄","examples":[{"en":"Chapman wants people to keep products rather than discard them.","zh":"Chapman 希望人們保留產品，而不是丟棄它們。"},{"en":"Rather than discard means instead of throwing something away.","zh":"而不是丟棄，是指不把某物扔掉，而採取另一做法。"},{"en":"A family may repair a table rather than discard it after one broken leg.","zh":"家庭可能修理一張斷了一隻腳的桌子，而不是丟棄它。"},{"en":"Keeping rather than discarding saves materials and reduces landfill waste.","zh":"保留而不是丟棄可以節省材料並減少堆填區廢物。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly contrasts reuse with disposal.","zh":"這個短語清楚對比再用與棄置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"durable consumer goods","meaning":"耐用消費品","examples":[{"en":"Some designers create more durable consumer goods.","zh":"有些設計師創造更耐用的消費品。"},{"en":"Durable consumer goods are products bought by consumers that are meant to last for a long time.","zh":"耐用消費品是消費者購買並預期能長時間使用的產品。"},{"en":"Washing machines, bicycles, and furniture can be durable consumer goods.","zh":"洗衣機、單車和家具都可以是耐用消費品。"},{"en":"If durable goods are poorly designed, people may still replace them too quickly.","zh":"如果耐用品設計欠佳，人們仍可能太快更換它們。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to long-lasting products used by households.","zh":"這個短語指家庭使用的長壽命產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"designed with recycling in mind","meaning":"設計時考慮到回收需要","examples":[{"en":"Electronic products should be designed with recycling in mind.","zh":"電子產品應在設計時考慮到回收需要。"},{"en":"Designed with recycling in mind means made so that materials can be recovered easily later.","zh":"設計時考慮到回收需要，是指製造時讓材料日後容易被回收。"},{"en":"A phone designed with recycling in mind might use screws instead of permanent glue.","zh":"設計時考慮回收需要的手機，可能使用螺絲而不是永久膠水。"},{"en":"Recycling becomes harder when products cannot be safely taken apart.","zh":"當產品不能安全拆開，回收就會更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase means disposal is considered at the design stage.","zh":"這個短語表示在設計階段已考慮棄置問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"waste entailed in","meaning":"……所涉及的浪費","examples":[{"en":"The waste entailed in short relationships with products is enormous.","zh":"與產品短暫關係所涉及的浪費非常巨大。"},{"en":"Waste entailed in something means waste involved in or caused by that situation.","zh":"某事所涉及的浪費，是指該情況包含或造成的浪費。"},{"en":"The waste entailed in buying new uniforms every term can be heavy for families.","zh":"每學期購買新校服所涉及的浪費，對家庭可能很沉重。"},{"en":"Short product relationships create waste because manufacturing, packaging, and disposal happen repeatedly.","zh":"短暫產品關係會製造浪費，因為製造、包裝和棄置反覆發生。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights hidden waste inside a behaviour.","zh":"這個短語突出某行為中的隱藏浪費。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fleeting relationships with","meaning":"與……的短暫關係","examples":[{"en":"Consumers often have fleeting relationships with their possessions.","zh":"消費者常與自己的物品有短暫關係。"},{"en":"Fleeting relationships with something are short-lived connections that do not last long.","zh":"與某物的短暫關係，是指不會持久的短命連繫。"},{"en":"A person may have a fleeting relationship with a cheap umbrella bought for one rainy day.","zh":"一個人為一天雨天買便宜雨傘，可能與它只有短暫關係。"},{"en":"Fleeting product relationships lead to waste because items are quickly forgotten or replaced.","zh":"短暫產品關係會導致浪費，因為物品很快被遺忘或取代。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weak and temporary attachment.","zh":"這個短語描述薄弱而暫時的依附。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"consumer durables","meaning":"耐用消費品","examples":[{"en":"Consumer durables include appliances, tools and electronic goods.","zh":"耐用消費品包括電器、工具和電子產品。"},{"en":"Consumer durables are products bought for personal use that should last for years.","zh":"耐用消費品是個人使用並應能持續多年的產品。"},{"en":"Refrigerators, drills, laptops, and sofas are consumer durables.","zh":"雪櫃、電鑽、手提電腦和梳化都是耐用消費品。"},{"en":"When consumer durables are thrown away early, the waste of resources is large.","zh":"當耐用消費品被過早丟棄，資源浪費會很大。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts long-lasting goods with disposable products.","zh":"這個短語把長壽命商品與即棄產品作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be colossal","meaning":"極其龐大","examples":[{"en":"The resources wasted through unnecessary consumption can be colossal.","zh":"不必要消費浪費的資源可能極其龐大。"},{"en":"Colossal means extremely large or enormous.","zh":"極其龐大，是指非常大或巨大。"},{"en":"A city festival can produce a colossal amount of rubbish if no recycling system is used.","zh":"如果沒有回收系統，城市節日可以產生極其龐大的垃圾量。"},{"en":"Waste becomes colossal when millions of people repeat the same small habit.","zh":"當數百萬人重複同一個小習慣，浪費就會變得極其龐大。"},{"en":"This word strongly emphasises size.","zh":"這個詞強烈強調規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"domestic power tools","meaning":"家用電動工具","examples":[{"en":"Domestic power tools are a typical example of underused products.","zh":"家用電動工具是使用不足產品的典型例子。"},{"en":"Domestic power tools are electric tools used at home for repairs or DIY projects.","zh":"家用電動工具是在家中維修或做 DIY 項目時使用的電動工具。"},{"en":"An electric drill, sander, or small saw can be a domestic power tool.","zh":"電鑽、打磨機或小型電鋸都可以是家用電動工具。"},{"en":"These tools are often underused because people buy them for one small job.","zh":"這些工具常使用不足，因為人們為一項小工作而購買它們。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to household tools, not industrial machinery.","zh":"這個短語指家庭工具，而不是工業機器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"electric drills","meaning":"電鑽","examples":[{"en":"Electric drills are often purchased but rarely used.","zh":"電鑽常被購買但很少使用。"},{"en":"Electric drills are power tools used to make holes or drive screws.","zh":"電鑽是用來鑽孔或鎖螺絲的電動工具。"},{"en":"A family may buy an electric drill to put up one shelf.","zh":"家庭可能為安裝一塊層板而買電鑽。"},{"en":"If an electric drill is used only once, most of its manufacturing resources are wasted.","zh":"如果電鑽只用一次，其大部分製造資源就被浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase is used as an example of an underused household product.","zh":"這個短語被用作使用不足家居產品的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a typical example of","meaning":"……的典型例子","examples":[{"en":"Power tools are a typical example of consumer waste.","zh":"電動工具是消費浪費的典型例子。"},{"en":"A typical example of something is a clear and common case that shows the idea well.","zh":"某事的典型例子，是清楚且常見、能很好顯示該想法的個案。"},{"en":"A student forgetting homework after poor sleep is a typical example of tiredness affecting memory.","zh":"學生因睡眠不足而忘記功課，是疲倦影響記憶的典型例子。"},{"en":"Typical examples help readers understand abstract arguments through familiar cases.","zh":"典型例子透過熟悉個案幫助讀者理解抽象論點。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an example that represents a wider pattern.","zh":"這個短語引入代表更廣泛模式的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"however much","meaning":"無論有多少……","examples":[{"en":"However much DIY people plan to do, many tools remain unused.","zh":"無論人們計劃做多少 DIY，許多工具仍然被閒置。"},{"en":"However much means no matter how much.","zh":"無論有多少，是指 no matter how much。"},{"en":"However much a student plans to revise, the plan will fail if they never start.","zh":"無論學生計劃溫習多少，如果從不開始，計劃都會失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts intention with reality.","zh":"這個短語對比意圖與現實。"},{"en":"It is useful when a strong plan still does not lead to action.","zh":"當強烈計劃仍沒有帶來行動時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the purchaser","meaning":"購買者","examples":[{"en":"The purchaser may intend to use the tool regularly.","zh":"購買者可能打算定期使用該工具。"},{"en":"The purchaser is the person who buys something.","zh":"購買者是買某物的人。"},{"en":"The purchaser of a washing machine should keep the receipt for warranty service.","zh":"洗衣機購買者應保留收據，以便享用保養服務。"},{"en":"A purchaser may imagine future use more often than the product is actually used.","zh":"購買者想像的未來用途可能比產品實際使用次數多。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than buyer.","zh":"這個詞比 buyer 較正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"plan to do","meaning":"計劃做","examples":[{"en":"Many purchasers plan to do a great deal of DIY.","zh":"許多購買者計劃做大量 DIY。"},{"en":"To plan to do something means to intend or prepare to do it.","zh":"計劃做某事，是指打算或準備去做它。"},{"en":"A student may plan to finish an essay on Saturday morning.","zh":"學生可能計劃星期六早上完成文章。"},{"en":"Planning to do something does not guarantee that it will actually happen.","zh":"計劃做某事並不保證它真正會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intention before action.","zh":"這個短語描述行動前的意圖。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be thrown away","meaning":"被丟棄","examples":[{"en":"Many power tools are eventually thrown away.","zh":"許多電動工具最終被丟棄。"},{"en":"To be thrown away means to be discarded as rubbish or unwanted.","zh":"被丟棄，是指被當成垃圾或不需要的東西扔掉。"},{"en":"Old notebooks may be thrown away at the end of the school year.","zh":"舊筆記簿可能在學年結束時被丟棄。"},{"en":"Useful items being thrown away too early creates unnecessary waste.","zh":"有用物品過早被丟棄，會造成不必要浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on disposal.","zh":"這個短語聚焦棄置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"having been used","meaning":"在僅被使用……之後","examples":[{"en":"Some tools are thrown away having been used for only a few minutes.","zh":"有些工具在僅被使用幾分鐘後便被丟棄。"},{"en":"Having been used means after being used.","zh":"在被使用之後，是指使用過後。"},{"en":"A paper cup may be thrown away having been used for only one drink.","zh":"紙杯可能在只盛過一杯飲品後就被丟棄。"},{"en":"When a product is discarded after little use, its environmental cost seems especially wasteful.","zh":"當產品只使用很少便被棄置，其環境成本顯得特別浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what happened before the main action.","zh":"這個短語描述主要動作之前發生的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on average","meaning":"平均而言","examples":[{"en":"Domestic drills are used for only a few minutes on average.","zh":"家用電鑽平均而言只使用幾分鐘。"},{"en":"On average means when the total is divided across all cases.","zh":"平均而言，是指把總數分配到所有個案後所得情況。"},{"en":"Students in the class read twenty pages a week on average.","zh":"班中學生平均而言每星期閱讀二十頁。"},{"en":"An average can hide differences because some people may use a tool often and others never use it.","zh":"平均數可能掩蓋差異，因為有些人常用工具，有些人從不使用。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a general statistical picture.","zh":"這個短語給出一般統計圖像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"serve conscience time","meaning":"因內疚而暫時被保留","examples":[{"en":"Unused products often serve conscience time before being discarded.","zh":"未使用的產品常在被丟棄前因內疚而暫時被保留。"},{"en":"To serve conscience time means to be kept for a while because the owner feels guilty about throwing it away.","zh":"因內疚而暫時被保留，是指物品因主人對丟棄它感到內疚而被保留一段時間。"},{"en":"A barely used juicer may serve conscience time in a cupboard before someone finally donates it.","zh":"一部幾乎未用的榨汁機可能在櫃中暫時被保留，之後才終於被捐出。"},{"en":"People keep such items because admitting waste feels uncomfortable.","zh":"人們保留這類物品，是因為承認浪費令人不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase describes delay caused by guilt, not real usefulness.","zh":"這個短語描述由內疚造成的延遲，而不是真正有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"gather dust","meaning":"積滿灰塵；被閒置","examples":[{"en":"Unused tools may gather dust on a garage shelf.","zh":"未使用工具可能在車房層架上積滿灰塵。"},{"en":"To gather dust means to remain unused for a long time.","zh":"積滿灰塵，是指長時間未被使用。"},{"en":"Exercise equipment may gather dust at home after the first week of enthusiasm.","zh":"運動器材可能在第一星期熱情過後就在家中被閒置。"},{"en":"Items that gather dust still occupy space and remind people of wasted money.","zh":"被閒置的物品仍佔用空間，並提醒人們浪費了金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being neglected and unused.","zh":"這個短語描述被忽略和不用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be reluctant to admit","meaning":"不願承認","examples":[{"en":"People are reluctant to admit that they have wasted money.","zh":"人們不願承認自己浪費了金錢。"},{"en":"To be reluctant to admit something means to feel unwilling to accept or say it openly.","zh":"不願承認某事，是指不想接受或公開說出它。"},{"en":"A student may be reluctant to admit that they did not understand the lesson.","zh":"學生可能不願承認自己不明白課堂內容。"},{"en":"People avoid admitting waste because it makes them feel foolish or guilty.","zh":"人們避免承認浪費，因為這令他們感到愚蠢或內疚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional resistance to honesty.","zh":"這個短語描述對誠實面對的情感抗拒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"waste their money","meaning":"浪費金錢","examples":[{"en":"Consumers may feel guilty when they realise they have wasted their money.","zh":"消費者意識到自己浪費金錢時可能感到內疚。"},{"en":"To waste their money means to spend money on something useless or unnecessary.","zh":"浪費金錢，是指把錢花在無用或不必要的東西上。"},{"en":"A person may feel they wasted their money after buying a machine they never use.","zh":"一個人買了從不用的機器後，可能覺得自己浪費了金錢。"},{"en":"Wasted money often leads to guilt, especially when the item also creates waste.","zh":"浪費金錢常導致內疚，尤其當該物品也製造浪費時。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on poor spending decisions.","zh":"這個短語聚焦差劣消費決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the end is inevitable","meaning":"最終結果無可避免","examples":[{"en":"For many unwanted products, the end is inevitable.","zh":"對許多不想要的產品而言，最終結果無可避免。"},{"en":"The end is inevitable means the final result is certain to happen.","zh":"最終結果無可避免，是指最後結果肯定會發生。"},{"en":"If a broken chair is never repaired, the end is inevitable: it will be thrown away.","zh":"如果破椅子從不被修理，最終結果無可避免：它會被丟掉。"},{"en":"Inevitable endings happen when no one uses, repairs, or values the object anymore.","zh":"當沒有人再使用、修理或珍視物品，無可避免的結局就會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that disposal is only a matter of time.","zh":"這個短語暗示棄置只是時間問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"landfill sites","meaning":"堆填區","examples":[{"en":"Discarded power tools may remain in landfill sites for thousands of years.","zh":"被丟棄的電動工具可能在堆填區中留存數千年。"},{"en":"Landfill sites are places where rubbish is buried or stored in large quantities.","zh":"堆填區是大量垃圾被埋藏或存放的地方。"},{"en":"A city sends household waste to landfill sites when it cannot be reused or recycled.","zh":"當家居廢物不能再用或回收，城市會把它送到堆填區。"},{"en":"Products that stay in landfill for years create long-term environmental pressure.","zh":"在堆填區長期存在的產品會造成長期環境壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to waste-disposal locations.","zh":"這個短語指廢物處理地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"design and manufacture","meaning":"設計和製造","examples":[{"en":"The design and manufacture of a product require considerable resources.","zh":"產品的設計和製造需要相當多資源。"},{"en":"Design and manufacture mean planning a product and then producing it.","zh":"設計和製造，是指規劃一件產品，然後生產它。"},{"en":"The design and manufacture of a laptop involve engineers, materials, factories, and testing.","zh":"手提電腦的設計和製造涉及工程師、材料、工廠和測試。"},{"en":"If a product is quickly thrown away, the resources used in its design and manufacture are wasted.","zh":"如果產品很快被丟棄，其設計和製造所用資源就被浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both creation and production.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋創造和生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"packaging and transportation","meaning":"包裝和運輸","examples":[{"en":"Packaging and transportation add to a product’s environmental cost.","zh":"包裝和運輸會增加產品的環境成本。"},{"en":"Packaging and transportation mean wrapping a product and moving it from one place to another.","zh":"包裝和運輸，是指包裝產品並把它從一地運到另一地。"},{"en":"A toy shipped overseas may need plastic packaging, boxes, fuel, and delivery vehicles.","zh":"海外運送的玩具可能需要塑膠包裝、紙箱、燃料和送貨車輛。"},{"en":"These stages add environmental cost because they use materials and energy.","zh":"這些階段會增加環境成本，因為它們使用材料和能源。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that impact happens beyond the product itself.","zh":"這個短語顯示影響不只來自產品本身。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"disposal","meaning":"棄置；處理","examples":[{"en":"The environmental cost includes manufacture, use and disposal.","zh":"環境成本包括製造、使用和棄置。"},{"en":"Disposal means getting rid of something after it is no longer wanted or usable.","zh":"棄置是指在某物不再被需要或不能使用後處理掉它。"},{"en":"Safe battery disposal prevents harmful chemicals from entering soil or water.","zh":"安全電池棄置能防止有害化學品進入泥土或水中。"},{"en":"Poor disposal creates pollution even after a product has stopped being useful.","zh":"差劣棄置會在產品停止有用後仍造成污染。"},{"en":"This word refers to the final stage of a product’s life.","zh":"這個詞指產品生命的最後階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"consume many times its own weight in","meaning":"消耗相當於本身重量多倍的……","examples":[{"en":"A power tool may consume many times its own weight in resources.","zh":"電動工具可能消耗相當於本身重量多倍的資源。"},{"en":"To consume many times its own weight in resources means to require far more material or energy than the product itself weighs.","zh":"消耗相當於本身重量多倍的資源，是指需要遠多於產品本身重量的材料或能源。"},{"en":"A small electronic device may use many times its own weight in mined metals, fuel, and packaging.","zh":"小型電子裝置可能使用相當於本身重量多倍的採礦金屬、燃料和包裝。"},{"en":"This hidden resource use makes short-lived products especially wasteful.","zh":"這種隱藏資源使用令短命產品特別浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase reveals the invisible cost behind a physical object.","zh":"這個短語揭示實體物件背後看不見的成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"active lifespan","meaning":"實際使用壽命","examples":[{"en":"Many consumer products have an extremely short active lifespan.","zh":"許多消費品的實際使用壽命極短。"},{"en":"Active lifespan means the period during which a product is actually used.","zh":"實際使用壽命是產品真正被使用的期間。"},{"en":"A party decoration may have an active lifespan of only one evening.","zh":"派對裝飾的實際使用壽命可能只有一個晚上。"},{"en":"A short active lifespan is wasteful when manufacture required large resources.","zh":"當製造需要大量資源，實際使用壽命短就很浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase is different from how long an object physically exists.","zh":"這個短語不同於物件實際存在多久。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"shorter than that of","meaning":"比……更短","examples":[{"en":"The tool’s active lifespan may be shorter than that of a small insect.","zh":"該工具的實際使用壽命可能比一隻小昆蟲更短。"},{"en":"Shorter than that of means lasting less time than the thing being compared.","zh":"比某物更短，是指持續時間少於被比較的事物。"},{"en":"A phone case may last shorter than that of the phone it protects.","zh":"手機殼的壽命可能比它保護的手機更短。"},{"en":"Comparing lifespans can show how wasteful a product’s use really is.","zh":"比較壽命可以顯示產品使用實際上有多浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for direct comparison.","zh":"這個短語用於直接比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"underlying motivation","meaning":"潛在動機","examples":[{"en":"To understand waste, we should examine the underlying motivation of consumers.","zh":"要理解浪費，我們應檢視消費者的潛在動機。"},{"en":"Underlying motivation means the deeper reason behind someone’s behaviour.","zh":"潛在動機是某人行為背後較深層的原因。"},{"en":"A student’s underlying motivation for studying may be fear of failure rather than love of learning.","zh":"學生學習的潛在動機可能是害怕失敗，而不是熱愛學習。"},{"en":"Understanding motivation helps explain why people buy things they hardly use.","zh":"理解動機有助解釋為何人們購買幾乎不用的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase points to hidden causes beneath visible actions.","zh":"這個短語指可見行動下的隱藏原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"look to","meaning":"從……尋找答案","examples":[{"en":"Researchers often look to consumer psychology for an explanation.","zh":"研究人員常從消費心理學尋找解釋。"},{"en":"To look to something means to seek help, answers, or guidance from it.","zh":"從某處尋找答案，是指向它尋求幫助、答案或指引。"},{"en":"A teacher may look to student feedback to improve a course.","zh":"老師可能從學生回饋中尋找改善課程的方法。"},{"en":"Researchers look to psychology because buying decisions often come from emotion as well as need.","zh":"研究人員從心理學尋找答案，因為購買決定常來自情感以及需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes searching for explanation in a particular field.","zh":"這個短語描述在特定範疇尋找解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"give expression to","meaning":"表達……","examples":[{"en":"People use possessions to give expression to their identity.","zh":"人們使用擁有物來表達自己的身份。"},{"en":"To give expression to something means to show or communicate it.","zh":"表達某事，是指展示或傳達它。"},{"en":"A student may give expression to creativity through drawing or music.","zh":"學生可能透過繪畫或音樂表達創意。"},{"en":"People buy certain objects because those objects help express who they want to be.","zh":"人們購買某些物件，是因為那些物件幫助表達他們想成為怎樣的人。"},{"en":"This phrase connects inner identity with outward signs.","zh":"這個短語把內在身份與外在符號連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"who they are","meaning":"他們的身分","examples":[{"en":"Consumers often choose objects that represent who they are.","zh":"消費者常選擇代表他們身分的物品。"},{"en":"Who they are means a person’s identity, values, personality, or social role.","zh":"他們的身分，是指一個人的身份、價值觀、個性或社會角色。"},{"en":"A teenager may choose clothes that show who they are to their friends.","zh":"青少年可能選擇能向朋友展示自己身分的衣服。"},{"en":"Products become meaningful when people feel they reflect identity.","zh":"當人們覺得產品反映身份，產品就變得有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is about self-image, not just personal information.","zh":"這個短語關乎自我形象，而不只是個人資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"feel they belong to","meaning":"感到自己屬於……","examples":[{"en":"Possessions can show what social group people feel they belong to.","zh":"擁有物可以顯示人們感到自己屬於哪個社會群體。"},{"en":"Feel they belong to means feel accepted as part of a group.","zh":"感到自己屬於某群體，是指覺得自己被接納為其中一部分。"},{"en":"A student may feel they belong to a music club after performing with others.","zh":"學生與其他人表演後，可能感到自己屬於音樂學會。"},{"en":"People may buy brands that signal the group they want to belong to.","zh":"人們可能購買能顯示自己想歸屬群體的品牌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social identity and belonging.","zh":"這個短語描述社會身份和歸屬感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mass production","meaning":"大量生產","examples":[{"en":"Mass production has weakened the personal meaning of many objects.","zh":"大量生產削弱了許多物件的個人意義。"},{"en":"Mass production is the making of large numbers of identical products in factories.","zh":"大量生產是在工廠製造大量相同產品。"},{"en":"A factory may use mass production to make thousands of chairs every week.","zh":"工廠可能使用大量生產每星期製造數千張椅子。"},{"en":"Mass production lowers cost but can make objects feel less personal.","zh":"大量生產降低成本，但會令物件感覺較不個人化。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts factory-made sameness with handmade uniqueness.","zh":"這個短語把工廠製造的相同性與手工製作的獨特性作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"symbolism","meaning":"象徵意義","examples":[{"en":"Consumer objects can carry social and personal symbolism.","zh":"消費物品可以帶有社會和個人象徵意義。"},{"en":"Symbolism is the meaning an object carries beyond its practical use.","zh":"象徵意義是物件在實際用途之外承載的意思。"},{"en":"A wedding ring has symbolism because it represents love and commitment.","zh":"結婚戒指有象徵意義，因為它代表愛和承諾。"},{"en":"Products with strong symbolism may be kept longer because they feel meaningful.","zh":"象徵意義強的產品可能被保留更久，因為它們感覺有意義。"},{"en":"This word refers to hidden or added meaning.","zh":"這個詞指隱藏或附加意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lose much of its potency","meaning":"失去大部分影響力","examples":[{"en":"In mass production, an object’s symbolism may lose much of its potency.","zh":"在大量生產中，物件的象徵意義可能失去大部分影響力。"},{"en":"To lose much of its potency means to become much less powerful or meaningful.","zh":"失去大部分影響力，是指變得力量或意義大大減弱。"},{"en":"A phrase repeated too often in advertising may lose much of its potency.","zh":"廣告中被重複太多次的短語可能失去大部分影響力。"},{"en":"When everyone owns the same object, its personal symbolism may become weaker.","zh":"當人人都擁有相同物件，其個人象徵意義可能變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong meaning becoming diluted.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈意義被沖淡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"for most of human history","meaning":"在人類歷史的大部分時期","examples":[{"en":"For most of human history, people owned relatively few objects.","zh":"在人類歷史的大部分時期，人們擁有的物件相對很少。"},{"en":"For most of human history means during the majority of the time humans have existed.","zh":"在人類歷史的大部分時期，是指人類存在以來的大部分時間。"},{"en":"For most of human history, people repaired clothing rather than replacing it quickly.","zh":"在人類歷史的大部分時期，人們會修補衣服，而不是快速更換。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a broad contrast between past and modern life.","zh":"這個短語建立過去生活與現代生活的廣泛對比。"},{"en":"It reminds readers that current consumer habits are historically unusual.","zh":"它提醒讀者，當前消費習慣在歷史上並不尋常。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"intimate relationship with","meaning":"與……有密切關係","examples":[{"en":"People once had a more intimate relationship with their possessions.","zh":"人們曾與自己的物品有更密切的關係。"},{"en":"An intimate relationship with something means a close, personal, and meaningful connection to it.","zh":"與某物有密切關係，是指與它有親近、個人且有意義的連繫。"},{"en":"A musician may have an intimate relationship with a guitar they have played for years.","zh":"音樂人可能與一把用了多年的結他有密切關係。"},{"en":"Such relationships make people repair and protect objects instead of replacing them quickly.","zh":"這類關係令人們修理和保護物件，而不是快速更換。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests emotional closeness.","zh":"這個短語暗示情感上的親近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"treasure an object","meaning":"珍視一件物品","examples":[{"en":"People often kept and treasured objects for many years.","zh":"人們常保留並珍視物件多年。"},{"en":"To treasure an object means to value it deeply and treat it as special.","zh":"珍視一件物品，是指深深重視它並把它視為特別。"},{"en":"A grandmother may treasure a handmade cup given by her grandchild.","zh":"祖母可能珍視孫兒送的手工杯。"},{"en":"Treasured objects are less likely to be thrown away because they carry memories.","zh":"被珍視的物件較不容易被丟棄，因為它們承載記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional value, not market price.","zh":"這個短語描述情感價值，而不是市場價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make the objects themselves","meaning":"親手製作物品","examples":[{"en":"In the past, people often made the objects themselves.","zh":"在過去，人們常親手製作物品。"},{"en":"To make the objects themselves means to create items personally rather than buy factory-made ones.","zh":"親手製作物品，是指自己創造物件，而不是購買工廠製成品。"},{"en":"A family may make shelves themselves instead of buying ready-made furniture.","zh":"家庭可能親手製作層架，而不是購買現成家具。"},{"en":"Handmade objects often feel more meaningful because effort and time are built into them.","zh":"手工物件通常更有意義，因為其中包含努力和時間。"},{"en":"This phrase links personal labour with emotional value.","zh":"這個短語把個人勞動與情感價值連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pass something on","meaning":"把……傳給下一代","examples":[{"en":"Family members frequently passed valued objects on to later generations.","zh":"家庭成員常把珍貴物件傳給後代。"},{"en":"To pass something on means to give it to another person, often after keeping it for some time.","zh":"把某物傳給別人，是指在保留一段時間後把它交給另一人。"},{"en":"Parents may pass a watch on to a child when the child grows older.","zh":"父母可能在孩子長大後把手錶傳給孩子。"},{"en":"Passing objects on keeps memories and family stories alive.","zh":"把物件傳下去能延續記憶和家庭故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transfer across people or generations.","zh":"這個短語描述在人與人或世代之間轉交。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"specialist objects","meaning":"專門製作的物品","examples":[{"en":"People relied on skilled craftspeople for more specialist objects.","zh":"人們依靠熟練工匠製作較專門的物品。"},{"en":"Specialist objects are items that require special skill, knowledge, or tools to make.","zh":"專門製作的物品，是需要特殊技能、知識或工具才能製成的物件。"},{"en":"A violin is a specialist object because it needs expert craftsmanship.","zh":"小提琴是專門製作的物品，因為它需要專業工藝。"},{"en":"People value specialist objects because they know effort and skill went into them.","zh":"人們重視專門物品，因為知道其中包含努力和技術。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts expert-made items with simple everyday objects.","zh":"這個短語把專家製作的物品與簡單日用品作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"rely on","meaning":"依靠……","examples":[{"en":"Local communities relied on expert manufacturers and craftspeople.","zh":"本地社區依靠專業製造者和工匠。"},{"en":"To rely on someone means to depend on them for help, skill, or support.","zh":"依靠某人，是指倚賴他們的幫助、技能或支援。"},{"en":"A school relies on cleaners to keep classrooms safe and usable.","zh":"學校依靠清潔工保持課室安全可用。"},{"en":"Communities relied on craftspeople because many objects could not be mass-produced locally.","zh":"社區依靠工匠，因為許多物品不能在本地大量生產。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dependence.","zh":"這個短語描述倚賴關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"expert manufacturers","meaning":"專業製造者","examples":[{"en":"Expert manufacturers once made objects for people living nearby.","zh":"專業製造者曾為住在附近的人製作物品。"},{"en":"Expert manufacturers are skilled producers who know how to make specialised goods well.","zh":"專業製造者是懂得優良製作專門商品的熟練生產者。"},{"en":"An expert manufacturer of shoes understands materials, comfort, and repair.","zh":"專業製鞋者了解材料、舒適度和維修。"},{"en":"Expert manufacturers can create objects that customers trust and keep longer.","zh":"專業製造者可以創造顧客信任並更長時間保留的物件。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights skill in making products.","zh":"這個短語突出製作產品的技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"live close by","meaning":"住在附近","examples":[{"en":"The manufacturers often lived close by and knew their customers.","zh":"製造者常住在附近並認識他們的顧客。"},{"en":"To live close by means to live nearby.","zh":"住在附近，是指住在不遠處。"},{"en":"A tutor who lives close by can visit students without a long journey.","zh":"住在附近的導師可以不用長途跋涉就探訪學生。"},{"en":"When makers live close by, customers may know them personally and trust their work.","zh":"當製作者住在附近，顧客可能親自認識他們並信任其作品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical nearness.","zh":"這個短語描述實體距離接近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"know someone personally","meaning":"親自認識某人","examples":[{"en":"Customers often knew the maker personally.","zh":"顧客常親自認識製作者。"},{"en":"To know someone personally means to have direct personal contact with them, not only know their name.","zh":"親自認識某人，是指與他有直接個人接觸，而不只是知道其名字。"},{"en":"A student may know the school librarian personally after borrowing books every week.","zh":"學生每星期借書後，可能親自認識學校圖書館員。"},{"en":"Knowing a maker personally can make an object feel more meaningful.","zh":"親自認識製作者會令物件感覺更有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes real human connection.","zh":"這個短語描述真實人際連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"give objects a history","meaning":"賦予物品歷史","examples":[{"en":"Personal production and ownership gave objects a history.","zh":"個人製作和擁有賦予物品歷史。"},{"en":"To give objects a history means to attach stories, memories, and human experiences to them.","zh":"賦予物品歷史，是指把故事、記憶和人的經歷附加到物件上。"},{"en":"A scratched family dining table has a history because many meals and conversations happened around it.","zh":"一張有刮痕的家庭餐桌有歷史，因為許多飯局和談話在它旁邊發生。"},{"en":"Objects with history are harder to discard because they carry personal meaning.","zh":"有歷史的物件較難被丟棄，因為它們承載個人意義。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how things become emotionally valuable.","zh":"這個短語解釋東西如何變得有情感價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a narrative","meaning":"故事；敘事","examples":[{"en":"A well-used possession can develop a personal narrative.","zh":"一件常用物品可以發展出個人故事。"},{"en":"A narrative is a story or sequence of experiences connected with something.","zh":"故事或敘事，是與某物相連的一連串經歷。"},{"en":"An old suitcase may have a narrative of family trips, moves, and farewells.","zh":"舊行李箱可能有家庭旅行、搬遷和告別的故事。"},{"en":"Narratives make objects meaningful because they connect things with memory.","zh":"故事令物件有意義，因為它們把東西與記憶連接起來。"},{"en":"This word means story, not simply written text.","zh":"這個詞指故事，而不只是書面文字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"emotional connection","meaning":"情感聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Handmade and inherited objects often create an emotional connection.","zh":"手工和繼承物件常創造情感聯繫。"},{"en":"An emotional connection is a personal feeling of attachment or meaning.","zh":"情感聯繫是一種個人依附或意義感。"},{"en":"A child may have an emotional connection with a blanket used since birth.","zh":"孩子可能與出生以來使用的毯子有情感聯繫。"},{"en":"Emotional connection makes people keep objects even when they are old or worn.","zh":"情感聯繫令人們即使物件變舊或磨損仍保留它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes feelings that go beyond practical use.","zh":"這個短語描述超越實際用途的感情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cannot match","meaning":"無法相比","examples":[{"en":"Modern mass production cannot match this personal connection.","zh":"現代大量生產無法與這種個人聯繫相比。"},{"en":"Cannot match means cannot equal or be as good as something.","zh":"無法相比，是指不能等同或不及某事。"},{"en":"A printed message cannot match a handwritten letter from a close friend.","zh":"印刷訊息無法與好友親手寫的信相比。"},{"en":"Factory production may be efficient but cannot match the meaning of handmade objects.","zh":"工廠生產可能有效率，但無法與手工物件的意義相比。"},{"en":"This phrase compares quality, strength, or emotional value.","zh":"這個短語比較質素、強度或情感價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"personal connections","meaning":"個人情感聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Personal connections can make people value products more highly.","zh":"個人情感聯繫可以令人們更重視產品。"},{"en":"Personal connections are emotional links between people and objects, places, or other people.","zh":"個人情感聯繫是人與物件、地方或其他人之間的情感連結。"},{"en":"A student may keep an old pen because of personal connections with a favourite teacher.","zh":"學生可能因與喜愛老師的個人情感聯繫而保留舊筆。"},{"en":"These connections reduce waste because people hesitate to discard meaningful things.","zh":"這些聯繫能減少浪費，因為人們不願丟棄有意義的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why some objects survive longer than others.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何有些物件能保存更久。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"consumerist culture","meaning":"消費主義文化","examples":[{"en":"Consumerist culture encourages constant purchasing and replacement.","zh":"消費主義文化鼓勵不斷購買和更換。"},{"en":"Consumerist culture is a social pattern that treats buying things as central to happiness, identity, or success.","zh":"消費主義文化是一種把購物視為快樂、身份或成功核心的社會模式。"},{"en":"In consumerist culture, people may feel they need new clothes every season.","zh":"在消費主義文化中，人們可能覺得每季都需要新衣服。"},{"en":"This culture increases waste when people replace items to feel new or modern.","zh":"當人們為了感覺新鮮或現代而更換物品，這種文化會增加浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises a society built around consumption.","zh":"這個短語批評圍繞消費建立的社會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"idolise novelty","meaning":"崇尚新奇事物","examples":[{"en":"Consumerist culture tends to idolise novelty.","zh":"消費主義文化往往崇尚新奇事物。"},{"en":"To idolise novelty means to admire newness too much.","zh":"崇尚新奇事物，是指過度欣賞新東西。"},{"en":"A shopper may idolise novelty if they always want the latest phone, even when the old one works.","zh":"如果舊手機仍可使用，購物者卻總想要最新款，就是崇尚新奇。"},{"en":"Idolising novelty leads to waste because older products lose appeal before they lose function.","zh":"崇尚新奇會導致浪費，因為舊產品在失去功能前已失去吸引力。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises excessive love of new things.","zh":"這個短語批評對新事物的過度熱愛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"buy happiness","meaning":"用金錢買到快樂","examples":[{"en":"Most people know that they cannot buy happiness.","zh":"大多數人知道自己不能用金錢買到快樂。"},{"en":"To buy happiness means to gain lasting happiness simply by spending money.","zh":"用金錢買到快樂，是指單靠花錢得到持久快樂。"},{"en":"A person may buy expensive shoes but still feel lonely or stressed.","zh":"一個人可能買昂貴鞋子，但仍感孤單或壓力大。"},{"en":"Buying things can create brief excitement, but it may not solve deeper emotional needs.","zh":"購物可以帶來短暫興奮，但未必解決更深層情感需要。"},{"en":"This phrase questions the link between consumption and real satisfaction.","zh":"這個短語質疑消費與真正滿足之間的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the chance to remake ourselves","meaning":"重新塑造自己的機會","examples":[{"en":"New products seem to offer the chance to remake ourselves.","zh":"新產品似乎提供重新塑造自己的機會。"},{"en":"The chance to remake ourselves means the opportunity to feel like a new or improved person.","zh":"重新塑造自己的機會，是指有機會感覺自己成為更新或更好的人。"},{"en":"A new fitness watch may seem to offer the chance to become healthier and more disciplined.","zh":"新健身手錶可能似乎提供變得更健康和更自律的機會。"},{"en":"Advertising often sells products by promising identity change, not just practical use.","zh":"廣告常透過承諾身份轉變來銷售產品，而不只是實際用途。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why new products feel emotionally powerful.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何新產品在情感上有吸引力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"glossy products","meaning":"外表光鮮的產品","examples":[{"en":"Glossy products are designed to appear attractive and desirable.","zh":"外表光鮮的產品被設計成看起來吸引和令人渴望。"},{"en":"Glossy products look shiny, polished, modern, and appealing.","zh":"外表光鮮的產品看起來閃亮、精緻、現代且有吸引力。"},{"en":"A glossy new laptop may attract buyers even if their old computer still works.","zh":"即使舊電腦仍可使用，一部光鮮的新手提電腦仍可能吸引買家。"},{"en":"Glossy appearance can create desire before people think about need or durability.","zh":"光鮮外表會在人們思考需要或耐用性前先製造欲望。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on surface appeal.","zh":"這個短語聚焦表面吸引力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"box-fresh products","meaning":"全新未使用的產品","examples":[{"en":"Consumers are often attracted to box-fresh products.","zh":"消費者常被全新未使用的產品吸引。"},{"en":"Box-fresh products are brand-new items that look unused and newly opened.","zh":"全新未使用的產品，是看起來未被使用、剛開封的新物品。"},{"en":"New trainers feel box-fresh when they come clean and perfect from the shop.","zh":"新運動鞋從店中買來時乾淨完美，感覺全新未使用。"},{"en":"Box-fresh appeal fades quickly once the item is used and becomes ordinary.","zh":"一旦物品被使用並變得普通，全新感的吸引力很快消退。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the attraction of perfect newness.","zh":"這個短語描述完美新鮮感的吸引力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"seem irresistible","meaning":"看來令人無法抗拒","examples":[{"en":"The appeal of a brand-new product may seem irresistible.","zh":"全新產品的吸引力可能看來令人無法抗拒。"},{"en":"Seem irresistible means appear so attractive that it is hard to refuse.","zh":"看來令人無法抗拒，是指顯得非常吸引，令人難以拒絕。"},{"en":"A half-price dessert may seem irresistible to a hungry student.","zh":"對飢餓學生來說，半價甜品可能看來令人無法抗拒。"},{"en":"Products seem irresistible when advertising connects them with beauty, success, or identity.","zh":"當廣告把產品與美貌、成功或身份連接起來，產品就會顯得無法抗拒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong temptation.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈誘惑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"novelty fades","meaning":"新鮮感消退","examples":[{"en":"When the novelty fades, consumers may lose interest.","zh":"當新鮮感消退，消費者可能失去興趣。"},{"en":"Novelty fades means the feeling of newness and excitement gradually disappears.","zh":"新鮮感消退，是指新奇和興奮的感覺逐漸消失。"},{"en":"A new phone case may feel exciting for a week, but the novelty soon fades.","zh":"新手機殼可能令人興奮一星期，但新鮮感很快消退。"},{"en":"When novelty fades, people may look for another new product to feel excited again.","zh":"當新鮮感消退，人們可能尋找另一個新產品來重新感到興奮。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why newness alone does not create lasting value.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何單靠新鮮感不能創造持久價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"renew the excitement","meaning":"重新獲得興奮感","examples":[{"en":"Some consumers renew the excitement by buying another new product.","zh":"有些消費者透過購買另一件新產品重新獲得興奮感。"},{"en":"To renew the excitement means to bring back the feeling of interest, pleasure, or thrill.","zh":"重新獲得興奮感，是指把興趣、愉快或刺激感帶回來。"},{"en":"A student may renew excitement for studying by using a fresh notebook and a clearer plan.","zh":"學生可能透過使用新筆記簿和更清晰計劃重新獲得學習興奮感。"},{"en":"Buying new things can renew excitement briefly, but the feeling may fade again.","zh":"購買新物品能短暫重新帶來興奮，但感覺可能再次消退。"},{"en":"This phrase describes restarting a positive feeling.","zh":"這個短語描述重新啟動正面感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"new stuff","meaning":"新物品","examples":[{"en":"People frequently buy new stuff to replace usable possessions.","zh":"人們經常購買新物品來取代仍可使用的擁有物。"},{"en":"New stuff means new things or products, especially in casual speech.","zh":"新物品是指新的東西或產品，尤其用於日常口語。"},{"en":"A teenager may want new stuff for school even when last year’s bag still works.","zh":"即使去年的書包仍可使用，青少年也可能想要上學新物品。"},{"en":"Buying new stuff too often increases waste and spending.","zh":"太頻繁購買新物品會增加浪費和開支。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds informal and broad.","zh":"這個短語語氣非正式且範圍廣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the schlock of the new","meaning":"對廉價新奇產品的迷戀","examples":[{"en":"Thackara calls the obsession with new products the schlock of the new.","zh":"Thackara 把對新產品的迷戀稱為對廉價新奇產品的迷戀。"},{"en":"The schlock of the new means cheap, shallow excitement about new products just because they are new.","zh":"對廉價新奇產品的迷戀，是指只因產品新就產生的廉價、膚淺興奮。"},{"en":"A shiny gadget that breaks after one month may represent the schlock of the new.","zh":"一件閃亮但一個月後壞掉的小工具，可能代表這種迷戀。"},{"en":"This idea criticises low-quality novelty that replaces lasting value.","zh":"這個概念批評以低質新奇取代持久價值。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds deliberately critical and ironic.","zh":"這個短語語氣刻意批判且帶諷刺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a network for sharing ideas","meaning":"分享意念的網絡","examples":[{"en":"Doors of Perception is a network for sharing ideas about design.","zh":"Doors of Perception 是一個分享設計意念的網絡。"},{"en":"A network for sharing ideas is a group or platform where people exchange knowledge and suggestions.","zh":"分享意念的網絡，是人們交換知識和建議的群體或平台。"},{"en":"Teachers may join a network for sharing ideas about classroom activities.","zh":"老師可能加入分享課堂活動意念的網絡。"},{"en":"Such networks spread innovation because members learn from one another.","zh":"這類網絡能傳播創新，因為成員互相學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised exchange of thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的想法交流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the future of design","meaning":"設計的未來","examples":[{"en":"The organisation explores ideas about the future of design.","zh":"該組織探討有關設計未來的想法。"},{"en":"The future of design means how design may change in coming years.","zh":"設計的未來，是指設計在未來多年可能如何改變。"},{"en":"Students discussing the future of design may talk about recycling, repair, and digital tools.","zh":"討論設計未來的學生可能談到回收、維修和數碼工具。"},{"en":"Thinking about the future of design helps people prepare for environmental and social challenges.","zh":"思考設計的未來有助人們準備環境和社會挑戰。"},{"en":"This phrase looks beyond current products to future possibilities.","zh":"這個短語超越現時產品，望向未來可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"emotionally durable design","meaning":"情感上持久的設計","examples":[{"en":"Chapman promotes the idea of emotionally durable design.","zh":"Chapman 推廣情感上持久的設計這個概念。"},{"en":"Emotionally durable design creates products people keep because they feel attached to them.","zh":"情感上持久的設計，是創造令人因有感情而保留的產品。"},{"en":"A mug with a changing surface that records use may support emotionally durable design.","zh":"一隻會隨使用而改變表面的杯，可能支持情感上持久的設計。"},{"en":"This design reduces waste by making people less eager to replace objects.","zh":"這種設計透過令人較不急於更換物件來減少浪費。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on lasting emotional value, not only physical strength.","zh":"這個短語聚焦持久情感價值，而不只是實體強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"favourite old jeans","meaning":"最喜愛的舊牛仔褲","examples":[{"en":"Favourite old jeans often become more valued through use.","zh":"最喜愛的舊牛仔褲常因使用而變得更受珍惜。"},{"en":"Favourite old jeans are jeans someone likes especially because they feel familiar and personal.","zh":"最喜愛的舊牛仔褲，是某人特別喜歡、因為感覺熟悉和個人化的牛仔褲。"},{"en":"A person may keep favourite old jeans even after buying newer clothes.","zh":"一個人即使買了新衣服，也可能保留最喜愛的舊牛仔褲。"},{"en":"Repeated use can make clothes more comfortable and emotionally meaningful.","zh":"反覆使用會令衣物更舒適並更有情感意義。"},{"en":"This phrase illustrates how wear can increase value.","zh":"這個短語說明磨損如何增加價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have the right feel","meaning":"有合適的質感","examples":[{"en":"Old jeans may not have the right feel until they have been worn repeatedly.","zh":"舊牛仔褲可能要反覆穿着後才有合適的質感。"},{"en":"Have the right feel means feel comfortable, familiar, or suitable in use.","zh":"有合適的質感，是指使用時感覺舒適、熟悉或合適。"},{"en":"A new pen may not have the right feel until a student writes with it for a few days.","zh":"新筆可能要學生用了幾天後才有合適的手感。"},{"en":"Repeated use can give an object the right feel because it adapts to the owner’s habits.","zh":"反覆使用可以令物件有合適質感，因為它適應主人的習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes personal comfort and familiarity.","zh":"這個短語描述個人舒適感和熟悉感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"worn and washed","meaning":"被穿着和清洗","examples":[{"en":"The jeans improve after they have been worn and washed many times.","zh":"牛仔褲在被多次穿着和清洗後變得更好。"},{"en":"Worn and washed means used as clothing and cleaned repeatedly.","zh":"被穿着和清洗，是指作為衣物被使用並反覆清潔。"},{"en":"A cotton shirt becomes softer after being worn and washed many times.","zh":"棉質恤衫在多次穿着和清洗後會變得更柔軟。"},{"en":"Repeated wearing and washing can make some clothes more comfortable.","zh":"反覆穿着和清洗可以令有些衣物更舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how use can improve emotional and physical fit.","zh":"這個短語顯示使用如何改善情感和實體合身感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"share your life story","meaning":"分享你的人生故事","examples":[{"en":"A well-used object can seem to share your life story.","zh":"一件常用物品似乎可以分享你的人生故事。"},{"en":"To share your life story means to carry memories of experiences you have had.","zh":"分享你的人生故事，是指承載你曾經歷過的記憶。"},{"en":"An old backpack may share your life story if it travelled with you through school and university.","zh":"如果舊背包陪你走過中學和大學，它可能分享你的人生故事。"},{"en":"Objects with memories become harder to replace because they feel connected to personal history.","zh":"有記憶的物件較難被取代，因為它們感覺與個人歷史相連。"},{"en":"This phrase gives ordinary objects emotional depth.","zh":"這個短語賦予普通物件情感深度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fake that look","meaning":"仿製那種外觀","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers can fake an aged look, but not the personal history behind it.","zh":"製造商可以仿製老舊外觀，但不能仿製其背後的個人歷史。"},{"en":"To fake that look means to artificially create an appearance that seems old, used, or authentic.","zh":"仿製那種外觀，是指人工製造看似老舊、使用過或真實的外表。"},{"en":"A factory can fake worn jeans by adding faded patches before sale.","zh":"工廠可以在銷售前加入褪色痕跡來仿製磨舊牛仔褲。"},{"en":"A fake aged look may attract buyers, but it cannot create real memories.","zh":"仿舊外觀可能吸引買家，但不能創造真實記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts surface appearance with genuine experience.","zh":"這個短語對比表面外觀與真正經歷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"gradual unfolding of","meaning":"……的逐漸發展","examples":[{"en":"The gradual unfolding of a relationship with an object increases its meaning.","zh":"與物件關係的逐漸發展會增加其意義。"},{"en":"Gradual unfolding of something means slow development over time.","zh":"某事的逐漸發展，是指隨時間慢慢展開。"},{"en":"The gradual unfolding of friendship happens through shared meals, conversations, and trust.","zh":"友誼的逐漸發展發生在共同用餐、談話和信任之中。"},{"en":"A relationship with an object unfolds as people use it in different moments of life.","zh":"當人們在生命不同時刻使用物件，與它的關係便逐漸發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meaning growing slowly rather than appearing instantly.","zh":"這個短語描述意義慢慢增長，而不是瞬間出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"transform our interactions with","meaning":"改變我們與……的互動","examples":[{"en":"Emotional attachment transforms our interactions with everyday objects.","zh":"情感依附改變我們與日常物件的互動。"},{"en":"To transform our interactions with something means to change the way we use, treat, or relate to it.","zh":"改變我們與某物的互動，是指改變我們使用、對待或與它建立關係的方式。"},{"en":"A personal notebook can transform a student’s interaction with study by making planning feel meaningful.","zh":"一本個人筆記簿可以令規劃變得有意義，從而改變學生與學習的互動。"},{"en":"Emotional attachment changes objects from tools into companions of memory.","zh":"情感依附把物件由工具變成記憶的伴侶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a deep change in relationship.","zh":"這個短語描述關係上的深層改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"richer than simple utility","meaning":"超越單純實用價值","examples":[{"en":"A personal connection makes an object richer than simple utility.","zh":"個人聯繫令物件超越單純實用價值。"},{"en":"Richer than simple utility means more meaningful than just being useful.","zh":"超越單純實用價值，是指比只是有用更有意義。"},{"en":"A handmade bowl is richer than simple utility if it reminds someone of their parent.","zh":"如果手工碗令某人想起父母，它就超越單純實用價值。"},{"en":"Emotional value makes people keep objects even after their practical function becomes ordinary.","zh":"情感價值令人們即使在實用功能變得普通後仍保留物件。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts meaning with mere usefulness.","zh":"這個短語對比意義與單純用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"simple utility","meaning":"單純的實用功能","examples":[{"en":"Many products are valued only for their simple utility.","zh":"許多產品只因其單純實用功能而被重視。"},{"en":"Simple utility means basic practical usefulness.","zh":"單純實用功能，是指基本的實際用途。"},{"en":"A plastic spoon may have simple utility because it helps someone eat one meal.","zh":"塑膠匙有單純實用功能，因為它幫助某人吃一餐。"},{"en":"Products valued only for simple utility are easier to replace when a newer one appears.","zh":"只因單純實用功能而被重視的產品，在新產品出現時較容易被取代。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to function without emotional meaning.","zh":"這個短語指沒有情感意義的功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"industrial analyst","meaning":"工業分析師","examples":[{"en":"Walter Stahel is a Swiss industrial analyst.","zh":"Walter Stahel 是一位瑞士工業分析師。"},{"en":"An industrial analyst studies how industries work, use resources, and affect economies or society.","zh":"工業分析師研究行業如何運作、使用資源，以及影響經濟或社會。"},{"en":"An industrial analyst may examine why factories waste materials.","zh":"工業分析師可能研究工廠為何浪費材料。"},{"en":"Analysts help businesses see problems that daily managers may overlook.","zh":"分析師幫助企業看見日常管理者可能忽略的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a professional role in studying industry.","zh":"這個短語指出研究工業的專業角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the teddy-bear factor","meaning":"泰迪熊效應","examples":[{"en":"Stahel uses the teddy-bear factor to explain emotional durability.","zh":"Stahel 使用泰迪熊效應來解釋情感耐久性。"},{"en":"The teddy-bear factor is the emotional reason people keep an object even when it is old or worn.","zh":"泰迪熊效應是人們即使物件變舊或磨損仍保留它的情感原因。"},{"en":"A child keeps a damaged teddy bear because it feels comforting and familiar.","zh":"孩子保留破損泰迪熊，因為它令人感到安慰和熟悉。"},{"en":"The teddy-bear factor protects objects from being replaced purely for practical reasons.","zh":"泰迪熊效應防止物件純粹因實用原因而被取代。"},{"en":"This phrase explains emotional attachment through a simple example.","zh":"這個短語透過簡單例子解釋情感依附。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"no matter how","meaning":"無論多麼……","examples":[{"en":"No matter how old the teddy bear becomes, its owner may keep it.","zh":"無論泰迪熊變得多麼舊，主人仍可能保留它。"},{"en":"No matter how means regardless of how much or how strongly something is true.","zh":"無論多麼，是指不論某事在多大程度上是真實。"},{"en":"No matter how tired a parent is, they may still comfort a crying child.","zh":"無論父母多麼疲倦，仍可能安慰哭泣的孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one condition does not change the result.","zh":"這個短語顯示某條件不會改變結果。"},{"en":"It is useful for expressing strong attachment or determination.","zh":"它適合表達強烈依附或決心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ragged and worn","meaning":"破舊磨損的","examples":[{"en":"A favourite teddy bear may become ragged and worn.","zh":"最喜愛的泰迪熊可能變得破舊磨損。"},{"en":"Ragged and worn means torn, old, and damaged from long use.","zh":"破舊磨損的，是指因長期使用而撕裂、變舊和受損。"},{"en":"A child’s favourite blanket may become ragged and worn after years of washing.","zh":"孩子最喜愛的毯子經多年清洗後可能變得破舊磨損。"},{"en":"Objects can look ragged and worn yet still feel precious to their owners.","zh":"物件可以看起來破舊磨損，但對主人仍然珍貴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical age and damage.","zh":"這個短語描述實體老化和損傷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rush out and buy","meaning":"立即外出購買","examples":[{"en":"People do not rush out and buy a replacement for a treasured object.","zh":"人們不會立即外出購買一件珍貴物品的替代品。"},{"en":"To rush out and buy something means to go and buy it quickly, often without much thought.","zh":"立即外出購買某物，是指快速去買，通常沒有太多思考。"},{"en":"After seeing an advert, a teenager may rush out and buy the newest headphones.","zh":"看見廣告後，青少年可能立即外出購買最新耳機。"},{"en":"Emotional attachment stops people from rushing to replace old objects.","zh":"情感依附會阻止人們急於更換舊物。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests quick and impulsive buying.","zh":"這個短語暗示快速而衝動的購買。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"connect someone to","meaning":"令某人聯繫起……","examples":[{"en":"An old possession can connect someone to their childhood.","zh":"一件舊物可以令某人聯繫起童年。"},{"en":"To connect someone to something means to make them feel linked to it emotionally or personally.","zh":"令某人聯繫起某事，是指讓他們在情感或個人層面與它相連。"},{"en":"A song can connect someone to memories of school friends.","zh":"一首歌可以令某人聯繫起學生時代朋友的記憶。"},{"en":"Objects connected to childhood are often kept because they carry identity and memory.","zh":"與童年相連的物件常被保留，因為它們承載身份和記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an emotional link.","zh":"這個短語描述情感連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"protect something from obsolescence","meaning":"防止……被淘汰","examples":[{"en":"Emotional value can protect a product from obsolescence.","zh":"情感價值可以防止產品被淘汰。"},{"en":"To protect something from obsolescence means to stop it from becoming unwanted simply because it is old or outdated.","zh":"防止某物被淘汰，是指阻止它只因變舊或過時而不再被需要。"},{"en":"A family watch may be protected from obsolescence by memories attached to it.","zh":"家族手錶可能因附着的記憶而被防止淘汰。"},{"en":"Emotional meaning can make people keep an object even when newer versions exist.","zh":"情感意義可以令人即使有新版本也保留物件。"},{"en":"This phrase links attachment with long-term use.","zh":"這個短語把依附與長期使用連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"obsolescence","meaning":"過時；淘汰","examples":[{"en":"Rapid technological change can lead to product obsolescence.","zh":"快速科技變化可能導致產品過時。"},{"en":"Obsolescence is the state of becoming outdated, no longer useful, or no longer wanted.","zh":"過時或淘汰，是變得落後、不再有用或不再被需要的狀態。"},{"en":"Old phone chargers may face obsolescence when new devices use different ports.","zh":"當新裝置使用不同插口，舊手機充電器可能面臨淘汰。"},{"en":"Obsolescence creates waste when products are discarded before they physically break.","zh":"當產品在實體損壞前被丟棄，過時會製造浪費。"},{"en":"This word describes becoming outdated.","zh":"這個詞描述變得落後。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not simply about","meaning":"不單是關於……","examples":[{"en":"Sustainable design is not simply about making stronger products.","zh":"可持續設計不單是關於製造更堅固的產品。"},{"en":"Not simply about means not only concerned with one thing.","zh":"不單是關於，是指不只涉及一件事。"},{"en":"Good teaching is not simply about explaining grammar; it also involves practice and feedback.","zh":"良好教學不單是關於解釋文法，還涉及練習和回饋。"},{"en":"Sustainable design includes systems, culture, repair, energy, and disposal.","zh":"可持續設計包括系統、文化、維修、能源和棄置。"},{"en":"This phrase broadens the discussion beyond one simple idea.","zh":"這個短語把討論擴展到單一簡單想法之外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"durable items","meaning":"耐用物品","examples":[{"en":"Designers aim to create durable items that remain desirable.","zh":"設計師旨在創造仍然令人想要的耐用物品。"},{"en":"Durable items are things made to last and continue working for a long time.","zh":"耐用物品是製造得能長時間持續使用和運作的東西。"},{"en":"A durable backpack can survive daily school use for several years.","zh":"耐用背包可以承受幾年日常上學使用。"},{"en":"Durable items reduce waste because they do not need frequent replacement.","zh":"耐用物品減少浪費，因為它們不需要頻繁更換。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to long-lasting objects.","zh":"這個短語指長壽命物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a matter of","meaning":"是……的問題","examples":[{"en":"Sustainable design is a matter of considering the whole production system.","zh":"可持續設計是考慮整個生產系統的問題。"},{"en":"A matter of something means it depends on or mainly involves that thing.","zh":"是某事的問題，是指它取決於或主要涉及該事。"},{"en":"Good revision is a matter of regular practice, not last-minute panic.","zh":"良好溫習是定期練習的問題，而不是臨急抱佛腳。"},{"en":"Sustainable design depends on many linked choices, from materials to disposal.","zh":"可持續設計取決於許多相連選擇，從材料到棄置。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the key issue involved.","zh":"這個短語指出所涉及的關鍵議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"properly cost the whole process","meaning":"正確計算整個過程的成本","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers should properly cost the whole process of production and disposal.","zh":"製造商應正確計算生產和棄置整個過程的成本。"},{"en":"To properly cost the whole process means to calculate all financial and environmental costs accurately.","zh":"正確計算整個過程的成本，是指準確計算所有財務和環境成本。"},{"en":"A restaurant should properly cost a meal by including ingredients, labour, rent, and waste.","zh":"餐廳應把食材、人工、租金和廢物都包括在內，正確計算一餐成本。"},{"en":"If disposal costs are ignored, products may seem cheaper than they really are.","zh":"如果忽視棄置成本，產品可能看起來比實際更便宜。"},{"en":"This phrase asks businesses to count hidden costs.","zh":"這個短語要求企業計算隱藏成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"whole process of production","meaning":"整個生產過程","examples":[{"en":"The whole process of production has environmental and financial costs.","zh":"整個生產過程都有環境和財務成本。"},{"en":"The whole process of production means every stage involved in making a product.","zh":"整個生產過程，是指製造產品涉及的每一個階段。"},{"en":"Producing a shirt includes growing cotton, dyeing cloth, sewing, packaging, and shipping.","zh":"生產恤衫包括種棉、染布、縫製、包裝和運輸。"},{"en":"Looking at the whole process reveals costs that are invisible at the shop counter.","zh":"觀察整個過程會揭示在店舖櫃檯看不見的成本。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages full-life-cycle thinking.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵全生命周期思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"energy use","meaning":"能源使用","examples":[{"en":"Sustainable design must take energy use into account.","zh":"可持續設計必須把能源使用考慮在內。"},{"en":"Energy use is the amount of electricity, fuel, or power consumed.","zh":"能源使用是消耗的電力、燃料或能量數量。"},{"en":"A washing machine with lower energy use saves electricity every week.","zh":"能源使用較低的洗衣機每星期都能節省電力。"},{"en":"Reducing energy use can lower bills and environmental impact.","zh":"減少能源使用可以降低帳單和環境影響。"},{"en":"This phrase measures how much power a product or system needs.","zh":"這個短語量度產品或系統需要多少能源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"design of systems","meaning":"系統設計","examples":[{"en":"Cooper argues that sustainability involves the design of systems.","zh":"Cooper 認為可持續性涉及系統設計。"},{"en":"Design of systems means planning how many connected parts work together.","zh":"系統設計，是規劃許多相連部分如何一起運作。"},{"en":"A school’s recycling success depends on the design of systems for bins, collection, and student habits.","zh":"學校回收成功取決於垃圾桶、收集和學生習慣的系統設計。"},{"en":"Sustainable products fail if the wider system for repair or recycling does not exist.","zh":"如果沒有更廣泛的維修或回收系統，可持續產品也會失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase moves design beyond single objects.","zh":"這個短語把設計由單一物件推展到更大系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"design of culture","meaning":"文化的重新設計","examples":[{"en":"Sustainable design may require a broader design of culture.","zh":"可持續設計可能需要更廣泛的文化重新設計。"},{"en":"Design of culture means changing shared habits, values, and expectations, not only products.","zh":"文化的重新設計，是改變共同習慣、價值觀和期望，而不只是產品。"},{"en":"A city designs culture when it makes repairing and sharing normal rather than strange.","zh":"當城市令維修和共享變得正常而不奇怪，就是在重新設計文化。"},{"en":"Waste decreases when culture values care, repair, and long use.","zh":"當文化重視愛惜、維修和長期使用，浪費就會減少。"},{"en":"This phrase treats culture itself as something that can be shaped.","zh":"這個短語把文化本身視為可以被塑造的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"surprisingly slow to take off","meaning":"令人意外地遲遲未能普及","examples":[{"en":"Sustainable design has been surprisingly slow to take off.","zh":"可持續設計令人意外地遲遲未能普及。"},{"en":"Surprisingly slow to take off means taking longer than expected to become popular or widely used.","zh":"令人意外地遲遲未能普及，是指比預期花更長時間才流行或廣泛使用。"},{"en":"A useful school app may be slow to take off if teachers are not trained to use it.","zh":"如果老師未受訓使用，一個有用的學校應用程式可能遲遲未普及。"},{"en":"Good ideas can spread slowly when businesses, costs, or habits stand in the way.","zh":"當企業、成本或習慣阻礙，好想法也可能慢慢才傳開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes delayed adoption.","zh":"這個短語描述採用延遲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"looming environmental crises","meaning":"迫近的環境危機","examples":[{"en":"Looming environmental crises are increasing interest in sustainable design.","zh":"迫近的環境危機正在增加人們對可持續設計的興趣。"},{"en":"Looming environmental crises are serious environmental problems that seem likely to happen soon.","zh":"迫近的環境危機，是看似即將發生的嚴重環境問題。"},{"en":"Water shortages and extreme heat can be looming environmental crises for a city.","zh":"缺水和極端高溫可以成為城市迫近的環境危機。"},{"en":"Looming crises push people to act before damage becomes unavoidable.","zh":"迫近危機推動人們在損害變得無可避免前行動。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a sense of approaching danger.","zh":"這個短語營造危險正在接近的感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"resource depletion","meaning":"資源耗竭","examples":[{"en":"Resource depletion is pushing sustainability higher on the agenda.","zh":"資源耗竭正把可持續性推上更高議程。"},{"en":"Resource depletion means natural resources are being used up faster than they can be replaced.","zh":"資源耗竭，是指自然資源被使用得比補充速度更快。"},{"en":"Overfishing can lead to resource depletion in coastal communities.","zh":"過度捕魚會導致沿海社區資源耗竭。"},{"en":"When resources decline, prices may rise and ecosystems may weaken.","zh":"當資源減少，價格可能上升，生態系統可能變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the shrinking supply of useful natural materials.","zh":"這個短語描述有用自然材料供應縮減。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"push something to the top of the agenda","meaning":"將……推至議程首位","examples":[{"en":"Environmental crises are pushing sustainable design to the top of the agenda.","zh":"環境危機正將可持續設計推至議程首位。"},{"en":"To push something to the top of the agenda means to make it one of the most urgent priorities.","zh":"將某事推至議程首位，是指令它成為最緊急優先事項之一。"},{"en":"A rise in student stress may push mental health to the top of a school’s agenda.","zh":"學生壓力上升可能把心理健康推至學校議程首位。"},{"en":"Serious problems move upward on the agenda when people can no longer ignore them.","zh":"當人們不能再忽視嚴重問題，問題就會在議程上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change in priority.","zh":"這個短語描述優先次序的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"agree with","meaning":"同意……","examples":[{"en":"Thackara agrees with Cooper’s concerns about sustainability.","zh":"Thackara 同意 Cooper 對可持續性的憂慮。"},{"en":"To agree with someone means to share the same opinion or accept their point.","zh":"同意某人，是指持有相同看法或接受其觀點。"},{"en":"A student may agree with a teacher that more practice is needed.","zh":"學生可能同意老師認為需要更多練習。"},{"en":"People agree when they see the same problem or solution.","zh":"當人們看見相同問題或方案，他們就會同意。"},{"en":"This phrase shows shared opinion.","zh":"這個短語顯示共同意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"roots of","meaning":"……的根源","examples":[{"en":"Thackara identifies the roots of impending environmental collapse.","zh":"Thackara 指出即將出現的環境崩潰的根源。"},{"en":"The roots of a problem are its deeper causes.","zh":"問題的根源是其較深層原因。"},{"en":"The roots of poor exam performance may include weak habits, anxiety, and lack of feedback.","zh":"考試表現差的根源可能包括習慣薄弱、焦慮和缺乏回饋。"},{"en":"Solving only surface symptoms will not work if the roots remain.","zh":"如果根源仍存在，只解決表面症狀並不會有效。"},{"en":"This phrase points to underlying causes.","zh":"這個短語指潛在成因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"impending environmental collapse","meaning":"即將出現的環境崩潰","examples":[{"en":"Overconsumption may contribute to impending environmental collapse.","zh":"過度消費可能促成即將出現的環境崩潰。"},{"en":"Impending environmental collapse means a serious breakdown of environmental systems that appears to be approaching.","zh":"即將出現的環境崩潰，是看似正在逼近的環境系統嚴重崩潰。"},{"en":"A region facing drought, soil loss, and dying forests may fear impending environmental collapse.","zh":"面對乾旱、土壤流失和森林死亡的地區，可能擔心即將出現的環境崩潰。"},{"en":"Collapse becomes more likely when consumption exceeds what nature can support.","zh":"當消費超過自然能承受的程度，崩潰更可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase warns of severe environmental danger ahead.","zh":"這個短語警告前方有嚴重環境危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be summarised in","meaning":"可概括為……","examples":[{"en":"The problem can be summarised in two words: weight and speed.","zh":"這個問題可概括為兩個詞：重量和速度。"},{"en":"To be summarised in something means to be expressed briefly using a few words or ideas.","zh":"可概括為某物，是指用少數字詞或想法簡短表達。"},{"en":"The school’s problem can be summarised in one word: overcrowding.","zh":"學校的問題可概括為一個詞：過度擠迫。"},{"en":"Summarising helps readers see the core issue quickly.","zh":"概括幫助讀者快速看見核心問題。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a short explanation of a complex problem.","zh":"這個短語引入複雜問題的簡短解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"more than the planet can sustain","meaning":"超過地球能夠承受的程度","examples":[{"en":"Human beings are producing more goods than the planet can sustain.","zh":"人類正在生產超過地球能夠承受的商品。"},{"en":"More than the planet can sustain means beyond what Earth’s resources and ecosystems can support safely.","zh":"超過地球能夠承受的程度，是指超出地球資源和生態系統能安全支持的範圍。"},{"en":"If people fish faster than fish can reproduce, they take more than the sea can sustain.","zh":"如果人們捕魚速度比魚類繁殖更快，就是取用超過海洋能承受的程度。"},{"en":"Overproduction damages the planet when resources cannot recover quickly enough.","zh":"當資源不能足夠快恢復，過度生產會傷害地球。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that consumption has environmental limits.","zh":"這個短語警告消費有環境限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"vast amounts of energy","meaning":"大量能源","examples":[{"en":"Transporting products requires vast amounts of energy.","zh":"運輸產品需要大量能源。"},{"en":"Vast amounts of energy means extremely large quantities of power or fuel.","zh":"大量能源，是極大的電力或燃料數量。"},{"en":"Flying food across the world uses vast amounts of energy.","zh":"把食物空運到世界各地會使用大量能源。"},{"en":"High energy use increases environmental impact, especially when fossil fuels are used.","zh":"高能源使用會增加環境影響，尤其在使用化石燃料時。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the scale of energy consumption.","zh":"這個短語強調能源消耗規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"move more of it around","meaning":"把更多貨物運送到各地","examples":[{"en":"Modern economies move increasing quantities of goods around the world.","zh":"現代經濟把越來越多貨物運送到世界各地。"},{"en":"To move more of it around means to transport larger amounts of goods from place to place.","zh":"把更多貨物運送到各地，是指把更大量商品從一地運到另一地。"},{"en":"Online shopping makes companies move more packages around cities every day.","zh":"網上購物令公司每天在城市中運送更多包裹。"},{"en":"Moving more goods around uses fuel, labour, packaging, and infrastructure.","zh":"運送更多貨物需要燃料、人手、包裝和基建。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the physical movement behind consumption.","zh":"這個短語突出消費背後的實體運輸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ever faster","meaning":"越來越快","examples":[{"en":"Goods are being manufactured and transported ever faster.","zh":"貨物正以越來越快的速度被製造和運輸。"},{"en":"Ever faster means increasingly quickly over time.","zh":"越來越快，是指隨時間變得更快。"},{"en":"Delivery services are becoming ever faster as customers expect same-day arrival.","zh":"隨着顧客期望即日送達，送貨服務正變得越來越快。"},{"en":"Faster production and transport can increase energy use and pressure on workers.","zh":"更快生產和運輸會增加能源使用和員工壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes speed that keeps increasing.","zh":"這個短語描述持續上升的速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the Information Age","meaning":"資訊時代","examples":[{"en":"The Information Age was expected to reduce dependence on physical goods.","zh":"資訊時代曾被預期會減少對實體商品的依賴。"},{"en":"The Information Age is the modern period in which digital information and technology shape life and work.","zh":"資訊時代是數碼資訊和科技塑造生活與工作的現代時期。"},{"en":"Online banking and video calls are common features of the Information Age.","zh":"網上銀行和視像通話是資訊時代的常見特徵。"},{"en":"People once hoped digital technology would reduce material consumption.","zh":"人們曾希望數碼科技會減少物質消耗。"},{"en":"This phrase names an era shaped by information technology.","zh":"這個短語命名由資訊科技塑造的時代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be supposed to lighten","meaning":"理應減輕……的負擔","examples":[{"en":"Digital technology was supposed to lighten modern economies.","zh":"數碼科技理應減輕現代經濟體系的負擔。"},{"en":"Be supposed to lighten something means be expected to reduce its weight, burden, or resource use.","zh":"理應減輕某事的負擔，是指被期望減少其重量、負擔或資源使用。"},{"en":"Online forms were supposed to lighten office paperwork.","zh":"網上表格理應減輕辦公室文書負擔。"},{"en":"A tool may fail to lighten a system if it adds new tasks instead of removing old ones.","zh":"如果工具增加新任務而不是移除舊任務，它可能未能減輕系統負擔。"},{"en":"This phrase compares expectation with reality.","zh":"這個短語比較期望與現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lighten our economies","meaning":"令經濟體系減少物質消耗","examples":[{"en":"The Information Age was expected to lighten our economies.","zh":"資訊時代曾被預期會令我們的經濟體系減少物質消耗。"},{"en":"To lighten our economies means to reduce the material weight and resource use of economic activity.","zh":"令經濟體系減少物質消耗，是指降低經濟活動的物質重量和資源使用。"},{"en":"Sending documents online can lighten an office economy by reducing paper use.","zh":"網上傳送文件可以透過減少用紙令辦公室經濟體系減少物質消耗。"},{"en":"Digital systems do not lighten economies if they also encourage faster buying and delivery.","zh":"如果數碼系統同時鼓勵更快購買和送貨，它們就未能減少物質消耗。"},{"en":"This phrase links economic activity with material consumption.","zh":"這個短語把經濟活動與物質消耗連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"reduce our impact on","meaning":"減少我們對……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Technology was expected to reduce our impact on the environment.","zh":"科技曾被預期會減少我們對環境的影響。"},{"en":"To reduce our impact on something means to lessen the harm or pressure we place on it.","zh":"減少我們對某事的影響，是指減少我們對它造成的傷害或壓力。"},{"en":"Walking to school can reduce our impact on air quality compared with driving.","zh":"與開車相比，步行上學可以減少我們對空氣質素的影響。"},{"en":"Lower impact often comes from using less energy, fewer materials, and better systems.","zh":"較低影響通常來自較少能源、較少材料和更好系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making human activity less damaging.","zh":"這個短語描述令人的活動較少破壞性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the reverse seems to be happening","meaning":"情況似乎正好相反","examples":[{"en":"Instead of reducing consumption, the reverse seems to be happening.","zh":"消費沒有減少，情況似乎正好相反。"},{"en":"The reverse seems to be happening means the opposite result appears to be occurring.","zh":"情況似乎正好相反，是指相反結果看來正在發生。"},{"en":"The app was meant to save time, but the reverse seems to be happening because students check it constantly.","zh":"這個應用程式原本應節省時間，但學生不斷查看它，情況似乎正好相反。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights disappointment when results oppose expectations.","zh":"當結果與期望相反，這個短語突出失望。"},{"en":"It is useful for showing irony or contradiction.","zh":"它適合用來顯示諷刺或矛盾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"add information technology to","meaning":"把資訊科技加入……","examples":[{"en":"Society has added information technology to the industrial system.","zh":"社會已把資訊科技加入工業系統。"},{"en":"To add information technology to something means to introduce digital tools, data, and networks into it.","zh":"把資訊科技加入某事，是指把數碼工具、數據和網絡引入其中。"},{"en":"A school adds information technology to teaching when it uses online platforms and digital records.","zh":"學校使用網上平台和數碼紀錄時，就是把資訊科技加入教學。"},{"en":"Adding technology may speed up an old system without making it more sustainable.","zh":"加入科技可能只是加快舊系統，而未必令它更可持續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes technological layering onto existing systems.","zh":"這個短語描述把科技疊加到現有系統上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"industrial era","meaning":"工業時代","examples":[{"en":"Modern economies still retain many features of the industrial era.","zh":"現代經濟仍保留許多工業時代的特徵。"},{"en":"The industrial era is the period shaped by factories, mass production, machinery, and large-scale material output.","zh":"工業時代是由工廠、大量生產、機器和大規模物質產出塑造的時期。"},{"en":"Assembly lines are a classic feature of the industrial era.","zh":"裝配線是工業時代的典型特徵。"},{"en":"Even digital economies may keep industrial-era habits of producing and moving goods quickly.","zh":"即使數碼經濟也可能保留工業時代快速生產和運送貨物的習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase names a historical mode of production.","zh":"這個短語命名一種歷史生產模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hasten the metabolism of","meaning":"加快……的運作速度","examples":[{"en":"Technology has hastened the developed world’s metabolism.","zh":"科技加快了已發展世界的運作速度。"},{"en":"To hasten the metabolism of an economy means to speed up how quickly it produces, consumes, and moves goods.","zh":"加快經濟體系的運作速度，是指加快其生產、消費和運送商品的速度。"},{"en":"Same-day delivery hastens the metabolism of shopping by making buying and transport faster.","zh":"即日送貨透過令購買和運輸更快，加快購物系統的運作速度。"},{"en":"Faster economic metabolism can increase resource use and waste.","zh":"更快經濟代謝會增加資源使用和浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a body metaphor for economic speed.","zh":"這個短語用身體比喻描述經濟速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"developed world","meaning":"已發展世界","examples":[{"en":"The developed world consumes resources at a rapid rate.","zh":"已發展世界以高速消耗資源。"},{"en":"The developed world refers to wealthy, industrialised countries with advanced infrastructure and high consumption levels.","zh":"已發展世界指擁有先進基建和高消費水平的富裕工業化國家。"},{"en":"Many countries in the developed world use large amounts of energy per person.","zh":"已發展世界中許多國家的人均能源使用量很大。"},{"en":"Consumption patterns in the developed world strongly affect global resource demand.","zh":"已發展世界的消費模式強烈影響全球資源需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes economically advanced regions, not moral superiority.","zh":"這個短語描述經濟先進地區，而不是道德優越。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"once you grasp that","meaning":"一旦你明白這一點","examples":[{"en":"Once you grasp that consumption involves weight and speed, the solution becomes clearer.","zh":"一旦你明白消費涉及重量和速度，解決方法就變得更清晰。"},{"en":"Once you grasp that means after you understand that point clearly.","zh":"一旦你明白這一點，是指在你清楚理解那個重點之後。"},{"en":"Once you grasp that grammar is about patterns, writing becomes less frightening.","zh":"一旦你明白文法關乎模式，寫作就較不令人害怕。"},{"en":"Understanding the key idea can make a complex problem easier to solve.","zh":"理解關鍵想法可以令複雜問題較容易解決。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the moment when explanation becomes clearer.","zh":"這個短語標示解釋變得清楚的一刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hardly rocket science","meaning":"並非甚麼高深學問","examples":[{"en":"The basic principles of reducing waste are hardly rocket science.","zh":"減少浪費的基本原則並非甚麼高深學問。"},{"en":"Hardly rocket science means not very difficult to understand.","zh":"並非甚麼高深學問，是指不太難理解。"},{"en":"Turning off lights when leaving a room is hardly rocket science.","zh":"離開房間時關燈並非甚麼高深學問。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests the problem may be serious, but the basic idea is simple.","zh":"這個短語暗示問題可能嚴重，但基本想法簡單。"},{"en":"It is informal and slightly humorous.","zh":"它語氣非正式並略帶幽默。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"minimise waste","meaning":"將浪費減至最低","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers and consumers should minimise waste.","zh":"製造商和消費者應將浪費減至最低。"},{"en":"To minimise waste means to reduce waste as much as possible.","zh":"將浪費減至最低，是指盡可能減少浪費。"},{"en":"A school can minimise waste by reusing paper and avoiding unnecessary printing.","zh":"學校可以透過重用紙張和避免不必要打印來將浪費減至最低。"},{"en":"Waste is minimised when products are repaired, shared, recycled, or used longer.","zh":"當產品被維修、共享、回收或用得更久，浪費就會被減至最低。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on reducing unnecessary loss.","zh":"這個短語聚焦減少不必要損失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"minimise energy use","meaning":"將能源消耗減至最低","examples":[{"en":"Efficient products can help minimise energy use.","zh":"高效產品可以幫助將能源消耗減至最低。"},{"en":"To minimise energy use means to reduce the amount of power or fuel consumed as much as possible.","zh":"將能源消耗減至最低，是指盡可能減少使用的電力或燃料。"},{"en":"Turning off air conditioning in empty rooms helps minimise energy use.","zh":"在空房間關掉冷氣有助將能源消耗減至最低。"},{"en":"Lower energy use reduces bills and environmental damage.","zh":"較低能源使用能減少帳單和環境破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in sustainable design and daily conservation.","zh":"這個短語常見於可持續設計和日常節約。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"move things around","meaning":"把物品運送到各處","examples":[{"en":"Local production can reduce the need to move things around.","zh":"本地生產可以減少把物品運送到各處的需要。"},{"en":"To move things around means to transport goods from one place to another.","zh":"把物品運送到各處，是指把貨物從一地運到另一地。"},{"en":"A supermarket moves things around when fruit is shipped from farms to stores.","zh":"當水果由農場運到店舖，超市就是把物品運送到各處。"},{"en":"Moving things around uses fuel and packaging, so local supply can reduce impact.","zh":"運送物品需要燃料和包裝，因此本地供應可以減少影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical distribution of goods.","zh":"這個短語描述貨物的實體分配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"use people more","meaning":"更充分運用人力","examples":[{"en":"A sustainable economy may use human skills more effectively.","zh":"可持續經濟可能更有效地運用人類技能。"},{"en":"Use people more means rely more on human skill, care, repair, and services rather than only materials and machines.","zh":"更充分運用人力，是指更多依靠人的技能、照顧、維修和服務，而不只是材料和機器。"},{"en":"A repair café uses people more by valuing local repair skills.","zh":"維修咖啡店透過重視本地維修技能來更充分運用人力。"},{"en":"Using human skills can reduce material waste because products are maintained instead of replaced.","zh":"使用人類技能可以減少材料浪費，因為產品被維護而不是被取代。"},{"en":"This phrase points to labour and knowledge as resources.","zh":"這個短語把勞動和知識視為資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"post-throwaway society","meaning":"後即棄社會","examples":[{"en":"Designers are considering how to create a post-throwaway society.","zh":"設計師正思考如何創造後即棄社會。"},{"en":"A post-throwaway society is a society that has moved beyond habits of quick disposal.","zh":"後即棄社會是已超越快速棄置習慣的社會。"},{"en":"In a post-throwaway society, people repair, share, rent, and recycle more often.","zh":"在後即棄社會中，人們更常維修、共享、租用和回收。"},{"en":"Such a society reduces waste because ownership and use are organised differently.","zh":"這種社會會減少浪費，因為擁有和使用的方式不同。"},{"en":"This phrase imagines a future after throwaway culture.","zh":"這個短語想像即棄文化之後的未來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"change the engine of an aircraft","meaning":"更換飛機引擎","examples":[{"en":"Transforming consumer culture is like changing the engine of an aircraft.","zh":"改變消費文化就像更換飛機引擎。"},{"en":"Changing the engine of an aircraft means replacing a central system while the whole machine depends on it.","zh":"更換飛機引擎，是指替換一個整部機器依賴的核心系統。"},{"en":"Reforming a school during term time can feel like changing the engine of an aircraft.","zh":"在學期中改革學校，可能感覺像更換飛機引擎。"},{"en":"The metaphor shows that changing consumer culture is difficult because society must keep functioning during the change.","zh":"這個比喻顯示改變消費文化很困難，因為社會必須在轉變中繼續運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a risky transformation of a working system.","zh":"這個短語描述對運作中系統作出高風險轉型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in mid-flight","meaning":"在飛行途中","examples":[{"en":"Manzini compares the transition to changing an engine in mid-flight.","zh":"Manzini 把這個轉變比作在飛行途中更換引擎。"},{"en":"In mid-flight means while an aircraft is already flying.","zh":"在飛行途中，是指飛機已經正在飛行時。"},{"en":"Fixing a company’s main computer system during peak season can feel like repairing a plane in mid-flight.","zh":"在旺季修理公司的主要電腦系統，可能感覺像在飛行途中修理飛機。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests change is risky because the system cannot simply stop.","zh":"這個短語暗示轉變有風險，因為系統不能簡單停下來。"},{"en":"It is often used metaphorically for difficult live transitions.","zh":"它常被比喻用於困難的運作中轉型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"even so","meaning":"即使如此","examples":[{"en":"Even so, Manzini believes that large-scale change is possible.","zh":"即使如此，Manzini 相信大規模改變是可能的。"},{"en":"Even so means despite what has just been said.","zh":"即使如此，是指儘管剛才所說成立。"},{"en":"The exam is difficult; even so, regular practice can improve your score.","zh":"考試很難；即使如此，定期練習仍能提高分數。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces hope or contrast after a problem.","zh":"這個短語在問題之後引入希望或對比。"},{"en":"It shows that a difficulty does not completely block the possibility.","zh":"它顯示困難並不完全阻止可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be done","meaning":"可以做到","examples":[{"en":"Changing the consumer system will be difficult, but it can be done.","zh":"改變消費系統會很困難，但可以做到。"},{"en":"Can be done means is possible to achieve.","zh":"可以做到，是指有可能達成。"},{"en":"Learning academic writing is hard, but it can be done with guidance and practice.","zh":"學術寫作很難，但透過指導和練習可以做到。"},{"en":"Difficult tasks become possible when they are broken into smaller steps.","zh":"當困難任務被拆成較小步驟，就會變得可以做到。"},{"en":"This phrase gives realistic encouragement.","zh":"這個短語給出現實的鼓勵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"not alone","meaning":"並非只有他一人","examples":[{"en":"Manzini is not alone in believing that change is possible.","zh":"並非只有 Manzini 一人相信改變是可能的。"},{"en":"Not alone means other people share the same view or situation.","zh":"並非只有一人，是指其他人也有相同看法或情況。"},{"en":"A student struggling with grammar is not alone; many classmates have the same problem.","zh":"文法有困難的學生並非只有他一人；許多同學都有同樣問題。"},{"en":"Knowing you are not alone can make a difficult task feel less discouraging.","zh":"知道自己並非孤身一人，可以令困難任務較不令人沮喪。"},{"en":"This phrase shows shared belief or experience.","zh":"這個短語顯示共同信念或經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a crucial step","meaning":"關鍵一步","examples":[{"en":"A crucial step is to redesign how resources are produced and distributed.","zh":"關鍵一步是重新設計資源如何生產和分配。"},{"en":"A crucial step is an extremely important action in a process.","zh":"關鍵一步是過程中極其重要的行動。"},{"en":"For exam preparation, a crucial step is identifying the student’s weakest question type.","zh":"對考試準備而言，關鍵一步是找出學生最弱的題型。"},{"en":"Missing a crucial step can cause the whole plan to fail.","zh":"錯過關鍵一步會令整個計劃失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a necessary action.","zh":"這個短語突出必要行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"redesign our globalised world","meaning":"重新設計全球化世界","examples":[{"en":"Manzini proposes redesigning our globalised world.","zh":"Manzini 提議重新設計我們的全球化世界。"},{"en":"To redesign our globalised world means to rethink how global systems of production, trade, and consumption work.","zh":"重新設計全球化世界，是重新思考全球生產、貿易和消費系統如何運作。"},{"en":"A designer may redesign supply chains so food travels shorter distances.","zh":"設計師可能重新設計供應鏈，令食物運輸距離更短。"},{"en":"Global systems need redesign when they create waste faster than nature can recover.","zh":"當全球系統製造浪費的速度快過自然恢復速度，就需要重新設計。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing large interconnected systems.","zh":"這個短語描述改變大型互聯系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"multi-local society","meaning":"多地本土化社會","examples":[{"en":"A multi-local society would rely more heavily on local production.","zh":"多地本土化社會會更大程度依賴本地生產。"},{"en":"A multi-local society is a society made of many connected local systems rather than one distant global supply chain.","zh":"多地本土化社會是由許多相連本地系統組成，而不是只靠遙遠全球供應鏈的社會。"},{"en":"In a multi-local society, towns might produce more food, energy, and services nearby.","zh":"在多地本土化社會中，城鎮可能在附近生產更多食物、能源和服務。"},{"en":"Local production reduces transport needs while networks still connect different places.","zh":"本地生產減少運輸需要，同時網絡仍連接不同地方。"},{"en":"This phrase imagines local self-reliance within wider connections.","zh":"這個短語想像在更廣泛連接中的本地自給。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"his vision is that","meaning":"他的構想是……","examples":[{"en":"His vision is that resources should be sourced locally whenever possible.","zh":"他的構想是資源應在可能時從本地採購。"},{"en":"His vision is that means his imagined future or ideal plan is that.","zh":"他的構想是，指他想像中的未來或理想計劃是這樣。"},{"en":"A principal’s vision may be that every student feels safe and confident at school.","zh":"校長的構想可能是每名學生在學校都感到安全和自信。"},{"en":"A vision guides decisions because it shows what future people are trying to build.","zh":"構想能指導決策，因為它顯示人們想建立怎樣的未來。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces someone’s long-term idea.","zh":"這個短語引入某人的長期想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"from food to electricity generation","meaning":"從食物以至電力生產","examples":[{"en":"Local sourcing could apply to everything from food to electricity generation.","zh":"本地採購可適用於從食物以至電力生產的一切。"},{"en":"From food to electricity generation means across a wide range of resources and services.","zh":"從食物以至電力生產，是指橫跨廣泛資源和服務。"},{"en":"A town may localise systems from vegetables to solar power.","zh":"城鎮可以把系統本地化，從蔬菜到太陽能發電。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that local sourcing is not limited to one small product category.","zh":"這個短語顯示本地採購不限於一個小產品類別。"},{"en":"It expresses a broad range from everyday goods to major infrastructure.","zh":"它表達由日用品到主要基建的廣泛範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as far as possible","meaning":"盡可能","examples":[{"en":"Resources should be sourced locally as far as possible.","zh":"資源應盡可能從本地採購。"},{"en":"As far as possible means as much as can reasonably be done.","zh":"盡可能，是指在合理可行範圍內做到最多。"},{"en":"Students should revise in a quiet place as far as possible.","zh":"學生應盡可能在安靜地方溫習。"},{"en":"The phrase recognises that an ideal may not always be fully achievable.","zh":"這個短語承認理想未必總能完全達成。"},{"en":"It suggests practical effort rather than perfection.","zh":"它暗示實際努力，而不是完美。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be sourced locally","meaning":"從本地採購","examples":[{"en":"Food and other resources should be sourced locally.","zh":"食物和其他資源應從本地採購。"},{"en":"To be sourced locally means to be obtained from nearby producers or suppliers.","zh":"從本地採購，是指從附近生產者或供應商取得。"},{"en":"A restaurant may use vegetables sourced locally from farms near the town.","zh":"餐廳可能使用從城鎮附近農場本地採購的蔬菜。"},{"en":"Local sourcing can reduce transport energy and support local businesses.","zh":"本地採購可以減少運輸能源並支持本地企業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where resources come from.","zh":"這個短語描述資源來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be distributed locally","meaning":"在本地分配","examples":[{"en":"Locally produced resources should also be distributed locally.","zh":"本地生產的資源也應在本地分配。"},{"en":"To be distributed locally means to be delivered or shared within the nearby area.","zh":"在本地分配，是指在附近地區內交付或分享。"},{"en":"Bread baked in a local bakery can be distributed locally to schools and shops.","zh":"本地麵包店烘焙的麵包可以在本地分配到學校和商店。"},{"en":"Local distribution reduces long-distance transport and keeps value within the community.","zh":"本地分配減少長途運輸，並把價值留在社區內。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where goods go after being produced.","zh":"這個短語描述貨物生產後去向何處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"local hubs","meaning":"本地樞紐","examples":[{"en":"Local hubs could coordinate the production and distribution of resources.","zh":"本地樞紐可以協調資源生產和分配。"},{"en":"Local hubs are community-based centres that organise activities, services, or resource flows.","zh":"本地樞紐是以社區為基礎、組織活動、服務或資源流動的中心。"},{"en":"A food hub may connect local farmers with schools, shops, and restaurants.","zh":"食物樞紐可能把本地農民與學校、商店和餐廳連接起來。"},{"en":"Hubs make local systems more efficient because they gather people and resources in one place.","zh":"樞紐把人和資源集中在一處，令本地系統更有效率。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised local centres.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的本地中心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be connected to","meaning":"與……連接","examples":[{"en":"Local hubs would be connected to national and global networks.","zh":"本地樞紐會與全國和全球網絡連接。"},{"en":"To be connected to something means to be linked with it physically, digitally, or organisationally.","zh":"與某物連接，是指以實體、數碼或組織方式與它相連。"},{"en":"A local clinic may be connected to a national hospital database.","zh":"本地診所可能與全國醫院資料庫連接。"},{"en":"Local systems need connections so they can share knowledge and resources beyond one area.","zh":"本地系統需要連接，才能在單一地區以外分享知識和資源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes links between different levels of a system.","zh":"這個短語描述系統不同層級之間的連結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"national and global networks","meaning":"全國及全球網絡","examples":[{"en":"Local systems could operate within national and global networks.","zh":"本地系統可以在全國及全球網絡中運作。"},{"en":"National and global networks are connected systems that operate across a country and across the world.","zh":"全國及全球網絡，是在一國內和全球範圍內運作的相連系統。"},{"en":"A local business may sell through national and global networks online.","zh":"本地企業可能透過網上全國及全球網絡銷售。"},{"en":"Such networks allow local producers to share knowledge, standards, and materials more widely.","zh":"這類網絡讓本地生產者更廣泛分享知識、標準和材料。"},{"en":"This phrase combines local action with wider connection.","zh":"這個短語結合本地行動與更廣泛連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"efficient use of materials","meaning":"有效運用物料","examples":[{"en":"Networks could allow the most efficient use of materials.","zh":"網絡可以讓物料得到最有效運用。"},{"en":"Efficient use of materials means using materials carefully with little waste.","zh":"有效運用物料，是指謹慎使用材料並盡量少浪費。"},{"en":"A workshop uses materials efficiently when leftover wood becomes smaller products.","zh":"工坊把剩餘木材做成較小產品時，就是有效運用物料。"},{"en":"Efficient use reduces cost and environmental damage.","zh":"有效運用能降低成本和環境破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on getting the most value from physical resources.","zh":"這個短語聚焦從實體資源取得最大價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"flow of materials","meaning":"物料流動","examples":[{"en":"Designers must consider the flow of materials through the economy.","zh":"設計師必須考慮物料在經濟中的流動。"},{"en":"Flow of materials means how materials move from extraction to production, use, reuse, and disposal.","zh":"物料流動是材料由開採到生產、使用、再用和棄置的移動方式。"},{"en":"A glass bottle’s material flow may include manufacturing, drinking, collection, washing, and reuse.","zh":"玻璃瓶的物料流動可能包括製造、飲用、收集、清洗和再用。"},{"en":"Understanding material flow helps designers reduce waste at each stage.","zh":"理解物料流動有助設計師在每一階段減少浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase treats materials as moving through a system.","zh":"這個短語把材料視為在系統中移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"what will … look like","meaning":"……會是怎樣","examples":[{"en":"The writer asks what post-throwaway consumerism will look like.","zh":"作者問後即棄消費主義會是怎樣。"},{"en":"What will something look like asks what form or character it may have in the future.","zh":"某事會是怎樣，是詢問它未來可能有甚麼形式或特徵。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask what future classrooms will look like in ten years.","zh":"老師可能問十年後未來課室會是怎樣。"},{"en":"This question helps readers imagine practical details, not just abstract ideas.","zh":"這個問題幫助讀者想像實際細節，而不只是抽象想法。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing future change.","zh":"它適合討論未來改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"for a start","meaning":"首先","examples":[{"en":"For a start, consumers will buy more sustainably designed products.","zh":"首先，消費者會購買更多以可持續方式設計的產品。"},{"en":"For a start means as the first point or first example.","zh":"首先，是指作為第一點或第一個例子。"},{"en":"For a start, a student can improve writing by checking subject-verb agreement.","zh":"首先，學生可以透過檢查主謂一致來改善寫作。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the beginning of a longer explanation.","zh":"這個短語引入較長解釋的開端。"},{"en":"It signals that more points will likely follow.","zh":"它表示之後可能還有更多重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"increasingly buy","meaning":"越來越多地購買","examples":[{"en":"Consumers will increasingly buy products with lower environmental costs.","zh":"消費者會越來越多地購買環境成本較低的產品。"},{"en":"Increasingly buy means buy more and more often over time.","zh":"越來越多地購買，是指隨時間更頻繁購買。"},{"en":"Families increasingly buy energy-saving appliances as electricity bills rise.","zh":"隨着電費上升，家庭越來越多地購買節能電器。"},{"en":"Consumer choices change when awareness, prices, and product availability change.","zh":"當意識、價格和產品供應改變，消費選擇也會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a growing purchasing trend.","zh":"這個短語描述增長中的購買趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"sustainably designed products","meaning":"以可持續方式設計的產品","examples":[{"en":"Sustainably designed products should use fewer resources.","zh":"以可持續方式設計的產品應使用較少資源。"},{"en":"Sustainably designed products are made to reduce waste, energy use, pollution, and unnecessary replacement.","zh":"以可持續方式設計的產品，是為減少浪費、能源使用、污染和不必要更換而製造的產品。"},{"en":"A reusable water bottle made from recycled steel can be a sustainably designed product.","zh":"由回收鋼製成的可重用水樽可以是以可持續方式設計的產品。"},{"en":"Such products help when they are durable, repairable, recyclable, and genuinely useful.","zh":"當這類產品耐用、可維修、可回收並真正有用時，它們就能發揮作用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to products designed with long-term environmental impact in mind.","zh":"這個短語指設計時考慮長期環境影響的產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as simple as","meaning":"可以簡單至……","examples":[{"en":"Sustainable consumption might be as simple as changing a light bulb.","zh":"可持續消費可以簡單至更換一個燈泡。"},{"en":"As simple as means something may be no more difficult than a very easy action.","zh":"可以簡單至，是指某事可能不比一個很容易的行動困難。"},{"en":"Saving water can be as simple as turning off the tap while brushing teeth.","zh":"節約用水可以簡單至刷牙時關掉水龍頭。"},{"en":"Simple changes matter when many people repeat them every day.","zh":"當許多人每天重複簡單改變，它們就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase makes an idea feel practical and achievable.","zh":"這個短語令想法感覺實際而可達成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"install energy-saving light bulbs","meaning":"安裝節能燈泡","examples":[{"en":"Households can install energy-saving light bulbs.","zh":"家庭可以安裝節能燈泡。"},{"en":"To install energy-saving light bulbs means to put in bulbs that use less electricity.","zh":"安裝節能燈泡，是指裝上使用較少電力的燈泡。"},{"en":"A family may install energy-saving light bulbs in the kitchen and living room.","zh":"家庭可能在廚房和客廳安裝節能燈泡。"},{"en":"These bulbs reduce energy use and can lower electricity bills over time.","zh":"這些燈泡能減少能源使用，並隨時間降低電費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple household sustainability action.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單家居可持續行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"energy-saving light bulbs","meaning":"節能燈泡","examples":[{"en":"Energy-saving light bulbs consume less electricity.","zh":"節能燈泡消耗較少電力。"},{"en":"Energy-saving light bulbs are bulbs designed to provide light while using less power.","zh":"節能燈泡是設計成使用較少電力也能照明的燈泡。"},{"en":"A school can reduce electricity bills by replacing old bulbs with energy-saving light bulbs.","zh":"學校可以透過用節能燈泡取代舊燈泡來減少電費。"},{"en":"Lower electricity use means fewer resources are needed to produce power.","zh":"較低用電量意味着需要較少資源來生產電力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to efficient lighting products.","zh":"這個短語指高效照明產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"more efficient washing machines","meaning":"效率較高的洗衣機","examples":[{"en":"More efficient washing machines reduce water and energy use.","zh":"效率較高的洗衣機減少用水和能源使用。"},{"en":"More efficient washing machines clean clothes while using fewer resources.","zh":"效率較高的洗衣機能清洗衣物，同時使用較少資源。"},{"en":"A family may choose a more efficient washing machine to save water and electricity.","zh":"家庭可能選擇效率較高的洗衣機來節省水和電。"},{"en":"Efficient machines reduce environmental impact every time they are used.","zh":"高效機器每次使用都能減少環境影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes appliances that do the same job with less waste.","zh":"這個短語描述用較少浪費完成相同工作的電器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"locally produced groceries","meaning":"本地生產的食品雜貨","examples":[{"en":"Consumers may increasingly choose locally produced groceries.","zh":"消費者可能越來越多選擇本地生產的食品雜貨。"},{"en":"Locally produced groceries are food and household items made or grown near where they are sold.","zh":"本地生產的食品雜貨，是在銷售地附近製造或種植的食物和家庭用品。"},{"en":"A market selling nearby vegetables and bread offers locally produced groceries.","zh":"售賣附近蔬菜和麵包的市場提供本地生產食品雜貨。"},{"en":"Local groceries may need less transport and packaging than imported goods.","zh":"本地食品雜貨可能比進口貨需要較少運輸和包裝。"},{"en":"This phrase connects shopping with local supply.","zh":"這個短語把購物與本地供應連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"less packaging","meaning":"較少包裝","examples":[{"en":"Locally produced goods may require less packaging.","zh":"本地生產商品可能需要較少包裝。"},{"en":"Less packaging means fewer boxes, wrappers, plastic layers, or containers are needed.","zh":"較少包裝，是指需要較少盒子、包裝紙、塑膠層或容器。"},{"en":"Apples sold loose at a market use less packaging than apples packed in plastic trays.","zh":"街市散裝出售的蘋果比塑膠盤包裝的蘋果使用較少包裝。"},{"en":"Less packaging reduces rubbish and saves materials.","zh":"較少包裝能減少垃圾並節省材料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple way to reduce waste.","zh":"這個短語描述減少浪費的簡單方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"spend less on material goods","meaning":"減少在物質商品上的開支","examples":[{"en":"In future, people may spend less on material goods.","zh":"將來，人們可能減少在物質商品上的開支。"},{"en":"To spend less on material goods means to use less money buying physical objects.","zh":"減少在物質商品上的開支，是指用較少金錢購買實體物件。"},{"en":"A family may spend less on material goods by borrowing tools instead of buying them.","zh":"家庭可以透過借用工具而不是購買來減少在物質商品上的開支。"},{"en":"Spending less on goods can reduce clutter, waste, and pressure to own more.","zh":"減少購買商品可以減少雜物、浪費和擁有更多的壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts buying objects with other forms of spending.","zh":"這個短語把購買物件與其他消費形式作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"spend more on services","meaning":"增加在服務方面的開支","examples":[{"en":"Consumers may spend more on services rather than possessions.","zh":"消費者可能增加在服務方面的開支，而不是花在擁有物上。"},{"en":"To spend more on services means to pay more for activities, access, repair, sharing, or help instead of owning goods.","zh":"增加在服務方面的開支，是指更多支付活動、使用權、維修、共享或幫助，而不是擁有商品。"},{"en":"A person may spend more on bike repair services than on buying a new bike.","zh":"一個人可能增加單車維修服務開支，而不是買新單車。"},{"en":"Service-based consumption can reduce waste when it replaces unnecessary ownership.","zh":"當服務型消費取代不必要擁有，它可以減少浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a shift from owning things to using services.","zh":"這個短語指出由擁有物品轉向使用服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"instead of buying","meaning":"而不是購買……","examples":[{"en":"Instead of buying a second car, people may join a sharing scheme.","zh":"人們可能加入共享計劃，而不是購買第二輛車。"},{"en":"Instead of buying means choosing another option rather than purchasing something.","zh":"而不是購買，是指選擇另一個方案，而非購買某物。"},{"en":"Instead of buying a drill, neighbours may borrow one from a tool library.","zh":"鄰居可能從工具圖書館借電鑽，而不是購買一把。"},{"en":"Choosing sharing instead of buying reduces storage needs and product waste.","zh":"選擇共享而不是購買，能減少儲存需要和產品浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a clear alternative to ownership.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示擁有以外的替代方案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"buy into","meaning":"加入；參與……","examples":[{"en":"Consumers may buy into a car-sharing network.","zh":"消費者可能加入汽車共享網絡。"},{"en":"To buy into something means to join, support, or accept an idea, system, or scheme.","zh":"加入或參與某事，是指加入、支持或接受一個想法、系統或計劃。"},{"en":"Parents may buy into a school’s reading programme if they believe it helps children.","zh":"如果家長相信學校閱讀計劃有助孩子，他們可能參與其中。"},{"en":"People buy into sharing schemes when they trust that access is reliable.","zh":"當人們相信共享計劃的使用權可靠，就會加入。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean joining a system, not only purchasing a product.","zh":"這個短語可以指加入系統，而不只是購買產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"car-sharing network","meaning":"汽車共享網絡","examples":[{"en":"A car-sharing network reduces the need for private ownership.","zh":"汽車共享網絡減少私人擁有汽車的需要。"},{"en":"A car-sharing network is a system where people use shared cars instead of owning their own.","zh":"汽車共享網絡是人們使用共享汽車，而不是擁有自己汽車的系統。"},{"en":"A city resident may book a car from a car-sharing network for weekend shopping.","zh":"城市居民可能從汽車共享網絡預約汽車作週末購物。"},{"en":"Sharing cars reduces the number of vehicles needed if many people use them at different times.","zh":"如果許多人在不同時間使用汽車，共享汽車能減少所需車輛數量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes access-based transport.","zh":"這個短語描述以使用權為基礎的交通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"rent a whole lot more","meaning":"租用多得多","examples":[{"en":"Future consumers may rent a whole lot more than they do today.","zh":"未來消費者可能比今天租用多得多。"},{"en":"Rent a whole lot more means hire or borrow paid access to many more things instead of buying them.","zh":"租用多得多，是指更多以付費方式借用或取得使用權，而不是購買。"},{"en":"A family may rent camping equipment rather than store it all year.","zh":"家庭可能租用露營裝備，而不是全年存放它。"},{"en":"Renting more can reduce waste when people need an item only occasionally.","zh":"當人們只是偶爾需要物品，增加租用可以減少浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a major shift from ownership to access.","zh":"這個短語暗示由擁有轉向使用權的重大轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"hardly use","meaning":"幾乎不使用","examples":[{"en":"There is little point in owning items that you hardly use.","zh":"擁有幾乎不使用的物品沒有甚麼意義。"},{"en":"Hardly use means use very rarely or almost never.","zh":"幾乎不使用，是指很少使用或幾乎從不使用。"},{"en":"A printer you hardly use may be better shared with neighbours.","zh":"你幾乎不使用的打印機可能更適合與鄰居共享。"},{"en":"Owning things you hardly use wastes money, space, and materials.","zh":"擁有幾乎不用的東西會浪費金錢、空間和材料。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights low actual use.","zh":"這個短語突出實際使用率低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be updated all the time","meaning":"不斷更新","examples":[{"en":"Electronic goods are likely to be updated all the time.","zh":"電子產品很可能不斷更新。"},{"en":"To be updated all the time means to be changed, improved, or replaced very frequently.","zh":"不斷更新，是指非常頻繁地被改變、改良或取代。"},{"en":"Phone software is updated all the time to fix problems or add features.","zh":"手機軟件不斷更新，以修正問題或加入功能。"},{"en":"Constant updates can make older devices seem outdated quickly.","zh":"持續更新會令舊裝置很快顯得過時。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frequent technological change.","zh":"這個短語描述頻繁科技變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"plans already in place","meaning":"已預先安排好的計劃","examples":[{"en":"Products may be sold with disposal plans already in place.","zh":"產品出售時可能已有預先安排好的棄置計劃。"},{"en":"Plans already in place means arrangements have been prepared before they are needed.","zh":"已預先安排好的計劃，是指在需要之前已準備好的安排。"},{"en":"A school trip should have emergency plans already in place before students leave.","zh":"學校旅行在學生出發前應已有預先安排好的緊急計劃。"},{"en":"Disposal planning becomes easier when arrangements exist before products are sold.","zh":"當產品出售前已有安排，棄置規劃會更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes advance preparation.","zh":"這個短語描述事前準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"plans for disposal","meaning":"棄置方案","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers should prepare plans for disposal before selling products.","zh":"製造商應在出售產品前準備棄置方案。"},{"en":"Plans for disposal are arrangements for what happens to a product after use.","zh":"棄置方案是產品使用後如何處理的安排。"},{"en":"A laptop maker may prepare plans for disposal by collecting old devices for recycling.","zh":"手提電腦製造商可能透過回收舊裝置來準備棄置方案。"},{"en":"Disposal plans reduce waste because end-of-life treatment is not left to chance.","zh":"棄置方案能減少浪費，因為產品壽命結束後的處理不會任由偶然決定。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the final stage of product responsibility.","zh":"這個短語聚焦產品責任的最後階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be designed to be recyclable","meaning":"被設計成可回收","examples":[{"en":"Electronic goods should be designed to be recyclable.","zh":"電子產品應被設計成可回收。"},{"en":"Designed to be recyclable means made so that parts and materials can be recovered and reused.","zh":"被設計成可回收，是指製造時讓零件和材料可以被回收和再用。"},{"en":"A recyclable laptop might be easy to open and separate into metal, plastic, and battery parts.","zh":"可回收手提電腦可能容易打開，並分離成金屬、塑膠和電池部分。"},{"en":"Recycling is harder when products are glued together or made from mixed materials.","zh":"當產品被黏在一起或由混合材料製成，回收就較困難。"},{"en":"This phrase connects product design with end-of-life recovery.","zh":"這個短語把產品設計與壽命結束時的回收連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"extra cost","meaning":"額外費用","examples":[{"en":"Recycling arrangements may add an extra cost to the product.","zh":"回收安排可能為產品增加額外費用。"},{"en":"Extra cost means additional money that must be paid beyond the basic price.","zh":"額外費用是基本價格以外必須支付的額外金錢。"},{"en":"Delivery may add an extra cost when furniture is sent to a remote village.","zh":"當家具送到偏遠村莊，送貨可能增加額外費用。"},{"en":"Extra recycling costs may be worthwhile if they prevent future waste.","zh":"如果額外回收費用能防止未來浪費，它可能值得支付。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an added financial charge.","zh":"這個短語描述附加財務收費。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be added to the retail price","meaning":"被加進零售價","examples":[{"en":"The recycling cost could be added to the retail price.","zh":"回收成本可以被加進零售價。"},{"en":"To be added to the retail price means to be included in the final price paid by customers.","zh":"被加進零售價，是指被包括在顧客支付的最終價格中。"},{"en":"A delivery fee may be added to the retail price of a large appliance.","zh":"大型電器的送貨費可能被加進零售價。"},{"en":"Adding recycling costs to the price makes end-of-life treatment part of the purchase.","zh":"把回收成本加進價格，令產品壽命結束後的處理成為購買的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how hidden costs become visible to buyers.","zh":"這個短語解釋隱藏成本如何對買家變得可見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"as prepayment","meaning":"作為預繳費用","examples":[{"en":"The additional recycling fee would be collected as prepayment.","zh":"額外回收費會作為預繳費用收取。"},{"en":"As prepayment means paid in advance before the service or final cost occurs.","zh":"作為預繳費用，是指在服務或最終成本發生前預先支付。"},{"en":"A tenant may pay one month’s rent as prepayment before moving in.","zh":"租客可能在入住前預繳一個月租金。"},{"en":"Recycling prepayment means customers help pay for future disposal at the time of purchase.","zh":"回收預繳費表示顧客在購買時幫助支付未來棄置成本。"},{"en":"This phrase describes paying before the later need arises.","zh":"這個短語描述在日後需要出現前先付款。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"increasingly concerned about","meaning":"越來越關注……","examples":[{"en":"Consumers are increasingly concerned about the environment.","zh":"消費者越來越關注環境。"},{"en":"Increasingly concerned about something means becoming more worried or aware over time.","zh":"越來越關注某事，是指隨時間變得更擔心或更有意識。"},{"en":"Parents are increasingly concerned about children’s screen time.","zh":"父母越來越關注孩子的螢幕時間。"},{"en":"Concern grows when people see more evidence of harm.","zh":"當人們看見更多傷害證據，關注就會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rising public worry.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾憂慮上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"eagerly adopt","meaning":"積極採用","examples":[{"en":"Many large businesses are eagerly adopting sustainable design.","zh":"許多大型企業正積極採用可持續設計。"},{"en":"To eagerly adopt something means to accept and use it with strong interest or enthusiasm.","zh":"積極採用某事，是指以強烈興趣或熱情接受並使用它。"},{"en":"A school may eagerly adopt a new reading programme if students enjoy it.","zh":"如果學生喜歡，學校可能積極採用新的閱讀計劃。"},{"en":"Businesses adopt green design eagerly when customers reward it and competitors follow.","zh":"當顧客支持而競爭者跟隨，企業會積極採用綠色設計。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active, willing acceptance.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動而願意接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"brush up their green credentials","meaning":"改善企業的環保形象","examples":[{"en":"Companies are brushing up their green credentials to attract customers.","zh":"公司正改善企業的環保形象以吸引顧客。"},{"en":"To brush up green credentials means to improve or present a company’s environmental image more attractively.","zh":"改善環保形象，是指更吸引地改善或展示公司的環境表現。"},{"en":"A hotel may brush up its green credentials by reducing plastic bottles and advertising the change.","zh":"酒店可能透過減少塑膠瓶並宣傳這項改變來改善環保形象。"},{"en":"Companies do this because environmentally aware customers may prefer greener brands.","zh":"公司這樣做，是因為有環保意識的顧客可能偏好較綠色品牌。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound slightly critical if the change is more image than substance.","zh":"如果改變只是形象多於實質，這個短語可能略帶批評意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"green credentials","meaning":"環保表現；綠色形象","examples":[{"en":"Businesses advertise their green credentials to environmentally aware consumers.","zh":"企業向有環保意識的消費者宣傳其環保表現。"},{"en":"Green credentials are evidence or claims showing that a company acts in an environmentally responsible way.","zh":"環保表現或綠色形象，是顯示公司以環境負責方式行事的證據或主張。"},{"en":"A company’s green credentials may include renewable energy use and recyclable packaging.","zh":"公司的環保表現可能包括使用可再生能源和可回收包裝。"},{"en":"Strong green credentials can attract customers, but weak claims may be seen as greenwashing.","zh":"強大的綠色形象可以吸引顧客，但薄弱主張可能被視為漂綠。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to environmental reputation and proof.","zh":"這個短語指環境聲譽和證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"please their customers","meaning":"取悅顧客","examples":[{"en":"Companies adopt greener practices to please their customers.","zh":"公司採用更環保做法來取悅顧客。"},{"en":"To please their customers means to satisfy customers or make them approve of the company.","zh":"取悅顧客，是指令顧客滿意或認同公司。"},{"en":"A café may please customers by offering reusable cups and clearer recycling bins.","zh":"咖啡店可以透過提供可重用杯和更清晰回收箱來取悅顧客。"},{"en":"Businesses change when customer expectations affect reputation and sales.","zh":"當顧客期望影響聲譽和銷售，企業就會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase connects company behaviour with customer approval.","zh":"這個短語把公司行為與顧客認可連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"stay one step ahead of","meaning":"領先……一步","examples":[{"en":"Businesses want to stay one step ahead of the competition.","zh":"企業想領先競爭對手一步。"},{"en":"To stay one step ahead of someone means to keep a small but important advantage over them.","zh":"領先某人一步，是指保持小但重要的優勢。"},{"en":"A student may stay one step ahead by reviewing lessons before problems build up.","zh":"學生可以透過在問題累積前複習課堂來領先一步。"},{"en":"Companies invest in sustainable design to appear more modern than rivals.","zh":"公司投資可持續設計，以顯得比對手更現代。"},{"en":"This phrase describes maintaining an advantage.","zh":"這個短語描述保持優勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the competition","meaning":"競爭對手","examples":[{"en":"Sustainable design may give a company an advantage over the competition.","zh":"可持續設計可能令公司比競爭對手更有優勢。"},{"en":"The competition means rival companies or people trying to win the same customers or prize.","zh":"競爭對手是爭取相同顧客或獎項的其他公司或人。"},{"en":"A small shop can beat the competition by offering better service.","zh":"小店可以透過提供更好服務擊敗競爭對手。"},{"en":"Businesses watch the competition because rivals affect price, design, and customer expectations.","zh":"企業留意競爭對手，因為對手影響價格、設計和顧客期望。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to competitors collectively.","zh":"這個短語統稱競爭者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"what does … imply","meaning":"……暗示甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what the expression “conscience time” implies.","zh":"題目問 “conscience time” 這個表達暗示甚麼。"},{"en":"What does something imply means what hidden meaning or suggestion it carries.","zh":"某事暗示甚麼，是指它帶有甚麼隱含意思或提示。"},{"en":"If a teacher says “interesting choice”, students may wonder what the comment implies.","zh":"如果老師說「有趣的選擇」，學生可能會想這句話暗示甚麼。"},{"en":"In reading tests, implication questions ask students to understand meaning beyond the exact words.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，暗示題要求學生理解字面以外的意思。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on suggested meaning.","zh":"這個短語聚焦隱含意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"feel guilty","meaning":"感到內疚","examples":[{"en":"Consumers may feel guilty about wasting money and resources.","zh":"消費者可能因浪費金錢和資源而感到內疚。"},{"en":"To feel guilty means to feel bad because you think you have done something wrong.","zh":"感到內疚，是指因認為自己做錯事而感覺不好。"},{"en":"A student may feel guilty after copying homework from a friend.","zh":"學生抄朋友功課後可能感到內疚。"},{"en":"People feel guilty about unused products because they know money and materials were wasted.","zh":"人們因未使用產品而內疚，因為他們知道金錢和材料被浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moral discomfort.","zh":"這個短語描述道德上的不舒服。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"throw things away easily","meaning":"輕易丟棄物品","examples":[{"en":"Some people feel guilty when they throw things away too easily.","zh":"有些人輕易丟棄物品時會感到內疚。"},{"en":"To throw things away easily means to discard items quickly without much thought or effort to reuse them.","zh":"輕易丟棄物品，是指沒有太多思考或再用努力便快速丟掉物品。"},{"en":"A person throws things away easily if they bin a repairable toaster after one small fault.","zh":"如果一個人因一個小故障就丟掉可維修多士爐，就是輕易丟棄物品。"},{"en":"Easy disposal increases waste because repair and sharing are ignored.","zh":"輕易棄置會增加浪費，因為維修和共享被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises careless discarding.","zh":"這個短語批評粗心丟棄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be unaware of","meaning":"沒有察覺……","examples":[{"en":"Some consumers may be unaware of the environmental cost of a product.","zh":"有些消費者可能沒有察覺產品的環境成本。"},{"en":"To be unaware of something means not to know about it.","zh":"沒有察覺某事，是指不知道它。"},{"en":"A student may be unaware of a deadline if they miss the announcement.","zh":"如果學生錯過通知，可能沒有察覺截止日期。"},{"en":"Consumers may buy more carefully once they become aware of hidden environmental costs.","zh":"一旦消費者意識到隱藏環境成本，可能會更謹慎購買。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lack of knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏認識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"waste problem","meaning":"浪費問題","examples":[{"en":"Sustainable designers are trying to address the waste problem.","zh":"可持續設計師正嘗試處理浪費問題。"},{"en":"The waste problem is the large social and environmental issue caused by producing and discarding too much.","zh":"浪費問題是由過度生產和棄置造成的大型社會及環境議題。"},{"en":"A school faces a waste problem if hundreds of plastic bottles are thrown away daily.","zh":"如果學校每天丟掉數百個膠樽，就面對浪費問題。"},{"en":"Waste problems grow when products are cheap to buy but hard to reuse or recycle.","zh":"當產品便宜易買但難以再用或回收，浪費問題就會擴大。"},{"en":"This phrase names the issue sustainable design tries to solve.","zh":"這個短語命名可持續設計試圖解決的議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"prior to mass production","meaning":"在大量生產出現之前","examples":[{"en":"Prior to mass production, objects often had a personal history.","zh":"在大量生產出現之前，物品常有個人歷史。"},{"en":"Prior to mass production means before goods were made in large numbers by factories.","zh":"在大量生產出現之前，是指商品由工廠大量製造之前。"},{"en":"Prior to mass production, many families repaired or handmade everyday items.","zh":"在大量生產出現之前，許多家庭會修補或親手製作日用品。"},{"en":"Objects made before mass production often felt more personal because people knew their makers.","zh":"大量生產前製作的物件通常更個人化，因為人們認識製作者。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a historical contrast with modern factory production.","zh":"這個短語標示與現代工廠生產的歷史對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"show their character","meaning":"展示自己的個性","examples":[{"en":"People may use possessions to show their character.","zh":"人們可能使用擁有物來展示自己的個性。"},{"en":"To show their character means to reveal personality, values, or taste.","zh":"展示自己的個性，是指顯示人格、價值觀或品味。"},{"en":"A student may show their character through the books and posters in their room.","zh":"學生可能透過房間中的書和海報展示自己的個性。"},{"en":"People choose objects that signal who they are or who they want to be.","zh":"人們選擇能顯示自己是誰或想成為誰的物件。"},{"en":"This phrase links possessions with identity.","zh":"這個短語把擁有物與身份連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"指的是……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what the word “narrative” refers to.","zh":"題目問 “narrative” 一詞指的是甚麼。"},{"en":"Refer to means point to, mean, or be about something.","zh":"指的是，是指指向、表示或關於某事。"},{"en":"In a reading test, “this problem” may refer to wasteful product design.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，“this problem” 可能指的是浪費性的產品設計。"},{"en":"Understanding reference helps students connect words with earlier ideas.","zh":"理解指代有助學生把字詞與前文想法連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in vocabulary and comprehension questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於詞彙和理解題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"relate personally and meaningfully to","meaning":"與……有個人而深刻的聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Old objects may relate personally and meaningfully to their owners.","zh":"舊物件可能與主人有個人而深刻的聯繫。"},{"en":"To relate personally and meaningfully to someone means to connect with their memories, identity, or feelings.","zh":"與某人有個人而深刻的聯繫，是指與其記憶、身份或感受相連。"},{"en":"A graduation pen may relate personally to a student because it marks an important achievement.","zh":"畢業筆可能與學生有個人聯繫，因為它標誌重要成就。"},{"en":"Meaningful connections make objects harder to throw away.","zh":"有意義的連繫令物件較難被丟棄。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional relevance.","zh":"這個短語描述情感上的相關性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"image created by manufacturers","meaning":"製造商塑造的形象","examples":[{"en":"Advertising often promotes an image created by manufacturers.","zh":"廣告常推廣製造商塑造的形象。"},{"en":"An image created by manufacturers is the impression companies design to make a product seem attractive.","zh":"製造商塑造的形象，是公司設計出來令產品顯得吸引的印象。"},{"en":"A phone company may create an image of youth, speed, and success around a new model.","zh":"手機公司可能圍繞新型號塑造青春、速度和成功的形象。"},{"en":"Such images can make people buy products for identity rather than need.","zh":"這類形象會令人為身份而非需要購買產品。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to marketing-created meaning.","zh":"這個短語指由市場推廣創造的意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"without a personal connection","meaning":"缺乏個人情感聯繫時","examples":[{"en":"Without a personal connection, objects are more easily replaced.","zh":"缺乏個人情感聯繫時，物件較容易被取代。"},{"en":"Without a personal connection means lacking emotional meaning or personal memory.","zh":"缺乏個人情感聯繫，是指缺少情感意義或個人記憶。"},{"en":"A plain free pen is easier to lose if it has no personal connection.","zh":"如果一支普通免費筆沒有個人聯繫，就較容易被弄丟。"},{"en":"Products without personal connection are replaced quickly because they feel interchangeable.","zh":"沒有個人聯繫的產品會被快速更換，因為它們感覺可以互相取代。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why emotional value affects durability.","zh":"這個短語解釋情感價值如何影響耐用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"buy new stuff for freshness","meaning":"為了新鮮感而購買新物品","examples":[{"en":"Consumers may buy new products simply for their freshness and novelty.","zh":"消費者可能只是為了新鮮感和新奇而購買新產品。"},{"en":"To buy new stuff for freshness means to purchase items mainly because they feel new and exciting.","zh":"為了新鮮感而購買新物品，是指主要因物品感覺新和刺激而購買。"},{"en":"A person may buy a new notebook for freshness even though the old one has blank pages.","zh":"一個人可能為了新鮮感買新筆記簿，即使舊的仍有空白頁。"},{"en":"Buying for freshness creates waste when useful items are abandoned too early.","zh":"為新鮮感而購買會在有用物品過早被放棄時製造浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises novelty-driven consumption.","zh":"這個短語批評由新奇驅動的消費。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"practical utility","meaning":"實際用途","examples":[{"en":"Products can have emotional value beyond their practical utility.","zh":"產品可以有超越實際用途的情感價值。"},{"en":"Practical utility means basic usefulness in doing a task.","zh":"實際用途是完成任務的基本有用性。"},{"en":"A cup has practical utility because it holds water.","zh":"杯子有實際用途，因為它能盛水。"},{"en":"An object may be kept for memories even after its practical utility becomes small.","zh":"即使物件的實際用途變小，人們仍可能因記憶而保留它。"},{"en":"This phrase separates function from emotional meaning.","zh":"這個短語把功能與情感意義分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"emotional connections","meaning":"情感聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Emotional connections can make people keep products for longer.","zh":"情感聯繫可以令人更長時間保留產品。"},{"en":"Emotional connections are feelings of attachment, memory, or personal meaning linked to something.","zh":"情感聯繫是與某事相關的依附、記憶或個人意義感。"},{"en":"A person may keep an old bicycle because of emotional connections with childhood rides.","zh":"一個人可能因與童年踩單車的情感聯繫而保留舊單車。"},{"en":"These connections reduce replacement because objects feel personally valuable.","zh":"這些聯繫減少更換，因為物件感覺有個人價值。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why some old products remain loved.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何有些舊產品仍被珍愛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"keep objects for longer","meaning":"更長時間保留物品","examples":[{"en":"Good design may encourage people to keep objects for longer.","zh":"良好設計可能鼓勵人們更長時間保留物品。"},{"en":"To keep objects for longer means to continue using or owning them for more time before replacing them.","zh":"更長時間保留物品，是指在更換前繼續使用或擁有它們更久。"},{"en":"A repairable backpack helps students keep it for longer.","zh":"可維修背包幫助學生更長時間保留它。"},{"en":"Keeping objects longer reduces the demand for new materials and manufacturing.","zh":"更長時間保留物品可以減少對新材料和製造的需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a key goal of sustainable design.","zh":"這個短語描述可持續設計的一個關鍵目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words from the list.","zh":"學生使用列表中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"Complete the summary means fill in missing words in a short passage.","zh":"完成摘要，是指填寫短文中缺失的字詞。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students complete the summary by matching ideas to the original text.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生透過把想法與原文配對來完成摘要。"},{"en":"This task checks whether students understand main ideas and key details.","zh":"這項任務檢查學生是否理解主旨和關鍵細節。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"coming problems","meaning":"即將出現的問題","examples":[{"en":"Coming environmental problems are increasing the pressure for change.","zh":"即將出現的環境問題正在增加改變的壓力。"},{"en":"Coming problems are difficulties that are expected to appear soon or in the future.","zh":"即將出現的問題，是預期很快或未來會出現的困難。"},{"en":"A school may prepare for coming problems such as falling enrolment or staff shortages.","zh":"學校可能為學生人數下降或人手短缺等即將出現的問題作準備。"},{"en":"Recognising coming problems early gives people time to plan.","zh":"及早認識即將出現的問題，能給人時間規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase points to future risks.","zh":"這個短語指未來風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"origins of","meaning":"……的起源","examples":[{"en":"Thackara identifies the origins of the environmental crisis.","zh":"Thackara 指出環境危機的起源。"},{"en":"The origins of something are the causes or beginnings of it.","zh":"某事的起源，是它的原因或開始。"},{"en":"A doctor may investigate the origins of a patient’s repeated headaches.","zh":"醫生可能調查病人反覆頭痛的起源。"},{"en":"Understanding origins helps people solve problems at the source.","zh":"理解起源有助人們從源頭解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase asks where a problem began.","zh":"這個短語詢問問題從何開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be assumed to have","meaning":"被假定具有……","examples":[{"en":"Technology was assumed to have a positive environmental effect.","zh":"科技被假定具有正面環境效果。"},{"en":"To be assumed to have something means people believed it had that quality without fully proving it.","zh":"被假定具有某物，是指人們在未完全證明下相信它有該特質。"},{"en":"A quiet student may be assumed to have no questions, even if they are confused.","zh":"安靜學生可能被假定沒有問題，即使他其實困惑。"},{"en":"Assumptions can be wrong when real behaviour differs from expectation.","zh":"當真實行為與期望不同，假設可能錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an accepted belief that may need checking.","zh":"這個短語描述需要檢查的既有信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"positive effect on society","meaning":"對社會的正面影響","examples":[{"en":"Information technology was expected to have a positive effect on society.","zh":"資訊科技曾被預期會對社會有正面影響。"},{"en":"A positive effect on society is a beneficial impact on people, communities, or daily life.","zh":"對社會的正面影響，是對人、社區或日常生活有益的作用。"},{"en":"Public libraries have a positive effect on society by giving people free access to knowledge.","zh":"公共圖書館透過讓人免費取得知識，對社會有正面影響。"},{"en":"Technology has a positive social effect only if it improves lives without creating bigger problems.","zh":"科技只有在改善生活而不製造更大問題時，才有正面社會影響。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to social benefit.","zh":"這個短語指社會好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"accelerate the world’s metabolism","meaning":"加快全球運作和消耗速度","examples":[{"en":"Modern technology may accelerate the world’s economic metabolism.","zh":"現代科技可能加快全球經濟運作和消耗速度。"},{"en":"To accelerate the world’s metabolism means to speed up global production, consumption, transport, and resource use.","zh":"加快全球運作和消耗速度，是指加快全球生產、消費、運輸和資源使用。"},{"en":"Fast online shopping accelerates the world’s metabolism by increasing deliveries and returns.","zh":"快速網購透過增加送貨和退貨，加快全球運作和消耗速度。"},{"en":"Faster economic activity can increase waste if systems are not redesigned.","zh":"如果系統未被重新設計，更快經濟活動會增加浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a body metaphor for global consumption speed.","zh":"這個短語用身體比喻描述全球消費速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"address this","meaning":"處理這個問題","examples":[{"en":"Manzini proposes local production to address this problem.","zh":"Manzini 提出本地生產來處理這個問題。"},{"en":"To address this means to deal with this issue or try to solve it.","zh":"處理這個問題，是指應對這個議題或嘗試解決它。"},{"en":"A teacher may address this by giving extra examples after students look confused.","zh":"老師看見學生困惑後，可能透過提供額外例子處理這個問題。"},{"en":"Problems are addressed effectively when solutions target the real cause.","zh":"當解決方法針對真正原因，問題就能被有效處理。"},{"en":"This phrase points to action taken in response to a problem.","zh":"這個短語指對問題採取行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be located and redeployed locally","meaning":"在本地取得並重新分配","examples":[{"en":"Resources should be located and redeployed locally where possible.","zh":"資源應在可能時於本地取得並重新分配。"},{"en":"To be located and redeployed locally means to be found, used, and reassigned within a local area.","zh":"在本地取得並重新分配，是指在本地區域內找到、使用並重新安排資源。"},{"en":"A community kitchen may locate surplus food nearby and redeploy it to families in need.","zh":"社區廚房可能在附近取得剩餘食物，並重新分配給有需要家庭。"},{"en":"Local redeployment reduces transport and prevents useful resources from being wasted.","zh":"本地重新分配減少運輸，並防止有用資源被浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase combines finding resources and using them again nearby.","zh":"這個短語結合尋找資源和在附近重新使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"agree with the claims of","meaning":"與作者的主張一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether statements agree with the writer’s claims.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與作者的主張一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the claims of someone means match what that person argues or believes.","zh":"與某人的主張一致，是指符合該人論證或相信的內容。"},{"en":"A statement agrees with the writer’s claim if the passage clearly supports it.","zh":"如果篇章清楚支持某陳述，它就與作者主張一致。"},{"en":"Students should not choose YES unless the writer’s view is actually expressed.","zh":"除非作者觀點確實被表達，學生不應選 YES。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading-comprehension questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀理解題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A “NO” answer contradicts the views expressed in the passage.","zh":"“NO” 答案與篇章表達的觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what they believe or state.","zh":"與某人的觀點相矛盾，是指說出與其相信或陳述相反的內容。"},{"en":"If a writer supports repair, saying they favour quick disposal contradicts their view.","zh":"如果作者支持維修，說他支持快速棄置就是與其觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be based on clear evidence from the text.","zh":"矛盾必須基於文本中的清楚證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disagreement with a stated opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述與已表達觀點不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"“NOT GIVEN” means it is impossible to say from the passage.","zh":"“NOT GIVEN” 表示從篇章中無法判斷。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"無法判斷，是指沒有足夠資訊作決定。"},{"en":"If a passage mentions a designer but not their salary, the salary is impossible to say.","zh":"如果篇章提到一位設計師但沒有提及薪金，薪金就無法判斷。"},{"en":"In exams, students should not guess when the text gives no evidence.","zh":"在考試中，當文本沒有證據，學生不應猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase explains when information is not provided.","zh":"這個短語解釋資料未被提供的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"seldom used","meaning":"很少被使用","examples":[{"en":"Many people buy products that are seldom used.","zh":"許多人購買很少被使用的產品。"},{"en":"Seldom used means rarely used or not used very often.","zh":"很少被使用，是指很少使用或不常使用。"},{"en":"A bread maker may be seldom used after the first few weeks.","zh":"麵包機在最初幾星期後可能很少被使用。"},{"en":"Seldom-used products waste space and resources if they cannot be shared or rented.","zh":"如果很少使用的產品不能共享或租用，就會浪費空間和資源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes low frequency of use.","zh":"這個短語描述使用頻率低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"dispose of electronic goods","meaning":"棄置電子產品","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers need responsible ways to dispose of electronic goods.","zh":"製造商需要負責任的方法棄置電子產品。"},{"en":"To dispose of electronic goods means to get rid of electronic products safely after use.","zh":"棄置電子產品，是指在使用後安全處理電子產品。"},{"en":"A family should dispose of old phones through recycling rather than ordinary rubbish.","zh":"家庭應透過回收棄置舊手機，而不是把它們當普通垃圾丟掉。"},{"en":"Responsible disposal prevents batteries and metals from harming the environment.","zh":"負責任棄置能防止電池和金屬傷害環境。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on safe end-of-life treatment for electronics.","zh":"這個短語聚焦電子產品壽命結束時的安全處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"pay extra money","meaning":"支付額外費用","examples":[{"en":"Consumers may pay extra money towards future recycling costs.","zh":"消費者可能為未來回收成本支付額外費用。"},{"en":"To pay extra money means to pay more than the basic price.","zh":"支付額外費用，是指支付基本價格以外的金錢。"},{"en":"A shopper may pay extra money for delivery or extended warranty.","zh":"購物者可能為送貨或延長保養支付額外費用。"},{"en":"Extra money for recycling can fund proper disposal later.","zh":"為回收支付額外費用，可以資助日後妥善棄置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an additional payment.","zh":"這個短語描述附加付款。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"jump on the sustainability bandwagon","meaning":"趕搭可持續發展熱潮","examples":[{"en":"Some businesses have jumped on the sustainability bandwagon.","zh":"有些企業已趕搭可持續發展熱潮。"},{"en":"To jump on the sustainability bandwagon means to join the popular trend of promoting sustainability, sometimes mainly for image.","zh":"趕搭可持續發展熱潮，是指加入推廣可持續性的流行趨勢，有時主要為形象。"},{"en":"A company may jump on the bandwagon by using green slogans without changing its products.","zh":"公司可能只使用綠色口號而不改變產品，這就是趕搭熱潮。"},{"en":"Businesses do this when customers start rewarding environmentally friendly brands.","zh":"當顧客開始支持環保品牌，企業就會這樣做。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound critical of trend-following.","zh":"這個短語可能帶有批評跟風的意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"sustainability bandwagon","meaning":"可持續發展熱潮","examples":[{"en":"Companies may use the sustainability bandwagon for marketing purposes.","zh":"公司可能為市場推廣目的利用可持續發展熱潮。"},{"en":"The sustainability bandwagon is the popular movement of companies presenting themselves as sustainable.","zh":"可持續發展熱潮，是公司把自己呈現為可持續的流行趨勢。"},{"en":"A brand joins the sustainability bandwagon when it advertises eco-friendly packaging loudly.","zh":"品牌大力宣傳環保包裝時，就是加入可持續發展熱潮。"},{"en":"The bandwagon can encourage real change, but it can also invite shallow claims.","zh":"這股熱潮可以鼓勵真正改變，但也可能帶來膚淺主張。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to sustainability as a trend companies may follow.","zh":"這個短語指公司可能追隨的可持續趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"spend less on repairs","meaning":"減少維修開支","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether companies will spend less on repairs in future.","zh":"題目問公司將來是否會減少維修開支。"},{"en":"To spend less on repairs means to use less money fixing broken or worn products.","zh":"減少維修開支，是指用較少金錢修理損壞或磨損產品。"},{"en":"A family spends less on repairs if they replace a cheap kettle instead of fixing it.","zh":"如果家庭不修理便宜水壺而直接更換，就是減少維修開支。"},{"en":"Spending less on repairs can increase waste when usable products are discarded.","zh":"當可用產品被丟棄，減少維修開支會增加浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase concerns repair costs, not the original purchase price.","zh":"這個短語關乎維修成本，而不是原本購買價格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 159 - Designed to Last.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 160":[{"front":"a book review of","meaning":"對……的書評","examples":[{"en":"The article is a book review of Oliver Sacks’s Musicophilia.","zh":"這篇文章是對 Oliver Sacks 的《Musicophilia》的書評。"},{"en":"A book review of something is an article that describes and evaluates that book.","zh":"a book review of something 指描述並評價某本書的文章。"},{"en":"A student may write a book review of a novel for English class.","zh":"學生可能為英文課寫一篇對小說的書評。"},{"en":"A good review explains both what the book is about and whether it is worth reading.","zh":"好書評會解釋書的內容，也會說明它是否值得閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when the main purpose is to judge a book, not just summarise it.","zh":"當主要目的是評價一本書，而不只是概述它時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the latest work of","meaning":"……的最新作品","examples":[{"en":"Norman M. Weinberger reviews the latest work of Oliver Sacks on music.","zh":"Norman M. Weinberger 評論 Oliver Sacks 關於音樂的最新作品。"},{"en":"The latest work of someone means that person’s most recent book, article, film, or creation.","zh":"the latest work of someone 指某人最近期的書、文章、電影或創作。"},{"en":"A newspaper may interview a novelist about the latest work of her career.","zh":"報章可能訪問小說家，談論她職業生涯中的最新作品。"},{"en":"Readers often compare an author’s latest work with earlier books.","zh":"讀者常把作者的最新作品與早期書籍比較。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing a new publication by a known creator.","zh":"介紹知名創作者的新出版作品時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"endlessly fascinating subjects","meaning":"令人着迷不已的題材","examples":[{"en":"Music and the brain are both endlessly fascinating subjects.","zh":"音樂和大腦都是令人着迷不已的題材。"},{"en":"Endlessly fascinating subjects are topics that remain interesting no matter how much people study them.","zh":"endlessly fascinating subjects 指無論人們研究多少仍然有趣的題目。"},{"en":"Space, dreams, and human memory are endlessly fascinating subjects for many students.","zh":"太空、夢和人類記憶對許多學生來說都是令人着迷不已的題材。"},{"en":"A subject becomes endlessly fascinating when each answer leads to more questions.","zh":"當每個答案都引出更多問題，一個題材就會變得令人着迷不已。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests deep, lasting interest rather than short-term curiosity.","zh":"這個短語暗示深層而持久的興趣，而不是短暫好奇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a neuroscientist specialising in","meaning":"專門研究……的神經科學家","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer is a neuroscientist specialising in auditory learning and memory.","zh":"這位評論者是一名專門研究聽覺學習與記憶的神經科學家。"},{"en":"A neuroscientist specialising in something is a brain scientist whose main research area is that topic.","zh":"neuroscientist specialising in something 指主要研究某題目的大腦科學家。"},{"en":"A neuroscientist specialising in sleep may study how rest affects memory.","zh":"專門研究睡眠的神經科學家可能研究休息如何影響記憶。"},{"en":"Specialisation helps researchers develop deeper knowledge of one area.","zh":"專門化幫助研究者在某一領域建立更深入知識。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both the person’s profession and their expert focus.","zh":"這個短語同時指出某人的職業和專業焦點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"auditory learning and memory","meaning":"聽覺學習與記憶","examples":[{"en":"Weinberger specialises in auditory learning and memory.","zh":"Weinberger 專門研究聽覺學習與記憶。"},{"en":"Auditory learning and memory involve how people learn and remember sounds.","zh":"auditory learning and memory 涉及人們如何學習和記住聲音。"},{"en":"A music student uses auditory learning and memory when recognising a melody by ear.","zh":"音樂學生憑耳朵辨認旋律時，就在運用聽覺學習與記憶。"},{"en":"Strong auditory memory helps people remember voices, songs, and pronunciation.","zh":"強的聽覺記憶幫助人記住聲音、歌曲和發音。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to neuroscience and psychology, especially research about sound.","zh":"這個短語屬於神經科學和心理學，尤其是關於聲音的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"especially intriguing","meaning":"特別耐人尋味","examples":[{"en":"He finds the relationship between music and the brain especially intriguing.","zh":"他覺得音樂與大腦之間的關係特別耐人尋味。"},{"en":"Especially intriguing means particularly interesting because it raises questions or curiosity.","zh":"especially intriguing 指因引發問題或好奇而特別有趣。"},{"en":"A teacher may find a quiet student’s sudden improvement especially intriguing.","zh":"老師可能覺得安靜學生突然進步特別耐人尋味。"},{"en":"Something becomes intriguing when it is unusual but not yet fully explained.","zh":"當某事不尋常但尚未完全解釋，它就會令人耐人尋味。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than simply saying something is interesting.","zh":"這個短語比單純說某事有趣更強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have high expectations of","meaning":"對……抱有很高期望","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer had high expectations of Musicophilia.","zh":"評論者對《Musicophilia》抱有很高期望。"},{"en":"To have high expectations of something means to believe it will be very good.","zh":"have high expectations of something 指相信某事會非常出色。"},{"en":"Parents may have high expectations of a new school if its exam results are strong.","zh":"如果一間新學校考試成績很好，家長可能對它抱有很高期望。"},{"en":"High expectations can lead to disappointment if the final result is only ordinary.","zh":"如果最終結果只是普通，高期望可能導致失望。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears before a review or judgement.","zh":"這個短語常出現在評論或判斷之前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the latest offering from","meaning":"……的最新作品","examples":[{"en":"Musicophilia is the latest offering from Oliver Sacks.","zh":"《Musicophilia》是 Oliver Sacks 的最新作品。"},{"en":"The latest offering from someone means the newest work, product, or creation by that person.","zh":"latest offering from someone 指某人最新的作品、產品或創作。"},{"en":"A bakery’s latest offering may be a new cake for the summer season.","zh":"麵包店的最新出品可能是夏季新蛋糕。"},{"en":"Fans pay attention to the latest offering from a favourite writer or artist.","zh":"粉絲會留意喜愛作家或藝術家的最新作品。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds slightly promotional and is common in reviews.","zh":"這個短語略帶宣傳口吻，常見於評論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"neurologist","meaning":"神經科醫生","examples":[{"en":"Oliver Sacks was a neurologist who wrote extensively about unusual medical cases.","zh":"Oliver Sacks 是一位神經科醫生，曾大量書寫不尋常醫學個案。"},{"en":"A neurologist is a doctor who studies and treats disorders of the brain and nervous system.","zh":"neurologist 指研究並治療大腦和神經系統疾病的醫生。"},{"en":"A patient with seizures may be referred to a neurologist for further tests.","zh":"有癲癇發作的病人可能被轉介給神經科醫生作進一步檢查。"},{"en":"Neurologists help diagnose problems involving movement, memory, speech, or sensation.","zh":"神經科醫生幫助診斷涉及動作、記憶、說話或感覺的問題。"},{"en":"This word refers to a medical specialist, not a general scientist.","zh":"這個字指醫學專科醫生，而不是一般科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"prolific author","meaning":"多產作家","examples":[{"en":"Oliver Sacks was a neurologist and prolific author.","zh":"Oliver Sacks 是神經科醫生，也是多產作家。"},{"en":"A prolific author is a writer who produces many books or articles.","zh":"prolific author 指創作許多書籍或文章的作家。"},{"en":"A prolific children’s writer may publish a new story every year.","zh":"多產的兒童作家可能每年出版一個新故事。"},{"en":"Prolific authors often become well known because readers see their work repeatedly.","zh":"多產作家常因讀者反覆看到其作品而變得知名。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quantity of writing, not automatically quality.","zh":"這個短語描述寫作數量，不自動等於質素高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"confess to feeling","meaning":"承認感到……","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer confesses to feeling slightly guilty about his criticism.","zh":"評論者承認對自己的批評感到有點內疚。"},{"en":"To confess to feeling something means to admit honestly that one has that feeling.","zh":"confess to feeling something 指誠實承認自己有某種感受。"},{"en":"A teacher may confess to feeling nervous before a difficult parents’ meeting.","zh":"老師可能承認在困難家長會前感到緊張。"},{"en":"People confess to feelings when they want to sound sincere or fair.","zh":"當人們想顯得真誠或公平時，可能會承認自己的感受。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces an emotion the speaker may feel awkward about.","zh":"這個短語常引出說話者可能覺得尷尬的情緒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"feel guilty about","meaning":"對……感到內疚","examples":[{"en":"He felt guilty about giving the book a partly unfavourable review.","zh":"他對給這本書部分負面的評論感到內疚。"},{"en":"To feel guilty about something means to feel bad because one thinks one may have done wrong.","zh":"feel guilty about something 指因覺得自己可能做錯而感到不好受。"},{"en":"A student may feel guilty about forgetting a friend’s birthday.","zh":"學生可能因忘記朋友生日而感到內疚。"},{"en":"Guilt can appear when criticism seems harsh toward someone we respect.","zh":"當批評對我們尊重的人似乎太嚴厲時，內疚感可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an uncomfortable moral feeling.","zh":"這個短語描述一種不舒服的道德感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"mixed reactions","meaning":"褒貶不一的反應","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer had mixed reactions to the book.","zh":"評論者對這本書有褒貶不一的反應。"},{"en":"Mixed reactions are feelings or opinions that include both positive and negative parts.","zh":"mixed reactions 指同時包含正面和負面部分的感受或意見。"},{"en":"Students may have mixed reactions to online lessons because they are convenient but lonely.","zh":"學生可能對網課有褒貶不一的反應，因為它方便但令人孤單。"},{"en":"A book can impress readers in some chapters and disappoint them in others.","zh":"一本書可以在某些章節令人欣賞，在另一些章節令人失望。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone cannot simply praise or criticise something.","zh":"當某人不能單純讚揚或批評某事時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the best part of","meaning":"……中最出色的部分","examples":[{"en":"Sacks himself is the best part of Musicophilia.","zh":"Sacks 本人是《Musicophilia》中最出色的部分。"},{"en":"The best part of something is its strongest, most enjoyable, or most valuable element.","zh":"the best part of something 指某事中最強、最令人享受或最有價值的元素。"},{"en":"The best part of the school trip may be the conversation on the bus.","zh":"學校旅行中最出色的部分可能是巴士上的談話。"},{"en":"A review often identifies the best part before discussing weaknesses.","zh":"書評常先指出最出色部分，再討論弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights what stands out most positively.","zh":"這個短語突出最正面突出的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"richly document","meaning":"詳細記錄","examples":[{"en":"Sacks richly documents his own life in the book.","zh":"Sacks 在書中詳細記錄自己的生活。"},{"en":"To richly document something means to record it with many details and examples.","zh":"richly document something 指以許多細節和例子記錄某事。"},{"en":"A family album can richly document a child’s early years.","zh":"家庭相簿可以詳細記錄孩子的早年生活。"},{"en":"Rich documentation helps readers feel that events are vivid and real.","zh":"詳細記錄幫助讀者覺得事件生動而真實。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests detailed recording, not a brief mention.","zh":"這個短語暗示細緻記錄，而不是簡短提及。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"highly personal experiences","meaning":"非常個人的經歷","examples":[{"en":"The author reveals highly personal experiences from his life.","zh":"作者透露了自己生活中非常個人的經歷。"},{"en":"Highly personal experiences are private events or feelings closely connected to someone’s life.","zh":"highly personal experiences 指與某人生活密切相關的私人事件或感受。"},{"en":"A speaker may share highly personal experiences when discussing illness or grief.","zh":"演講者談論疾病或悲傷時，可能分享非常個人的經歷。"},{"en":"Such experiences can make writing warmer and more human.","zh":"這類經歷可以令寫作更溫暖、更有人情味。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests emotional honesty and privacy.","zh":"這個短語暗示情感上的誠實和私密性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on the cover of","meaning":"在……的封面上","examples":[{"en":"A photograph of Sacks appears on the cover of the book.","zh":"Sacks 的照片出現在書的封面上。"},{"en":"On the cover of something means printed or shown on the outside front part.","zh":"on the cover of something 指印在或展示在外部正面。"},{"en":"A famous athlete may appear on the cover of a sports magazine.","zh":"著名運動員可能出現在體育雜誌封面上。"},{"en":"Covers create first impressions before readers open the book.","zh":"封面在讀者打開書前已建立第一印象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where an image, title, or name appears.","zh":"這個短語描述圖像、標題或名字出現的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"wearing headphones","meaning":"戴着耳筒","examples":[{"en":"The photograph shows Sacks wearing headphones.","zh":"照片顯示 Sacks 戴着耳筒。"},{"en":"Wearing headphones means having headphones on one’s ears or head.","zh":"wearing headphones 指耳朵或頭上戴着耳筒。"},{"en":"A student wearing headphones may be listening to a language exercise.","zh":"戴着耳筒的學生可能正在聽語言練習。"},{"en":"Headphones can help people focus on sound without outside noise.","zh":"耳筒可以幫助人專注於聲音，不受外界噪音干擾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what someone has on while listening.","zh":"這個短語描述某人在聆聽時戴着甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"eyes closed","meaning":"閉着眼睛","examples":[{"en":"Sacks is pictured with his eyes closed as he listens to music.","zh":"Sacks 被拍到閉着眼睛聆聽音樂。"},{"en":"Eyes closed means someone’s eyes are shut.","zh":"eyes closed 指某人的眼睛合上。"},{"en":"A singer may practise with eyes closed to focus on pitch.","zh":"歌手可能閉着眼睛練習，以專注音準。"},{"en":"People often close their eyes when they want to listen more deeply.","zh":"人們想更深入聆聽時，常會閉上眼睛。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest concentration, rest, or emotional absorption.","zh":"這個短語可以暗示專注、休息或情感投入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"clearly enchanted","meaning":"明顯陶醉","examples":[{"en":"Sacks looks clearly enchanted by the performance.","zh":"Sacks 看起來明顯陶醉於演奏之中。"},{"en":"Clearly enchanted means obviously delighted, absorbed, or charmed by something.","zh":"clearly enchanted 指明顯感到愉快、投入或被某事吸引。"},{"en":"A child may look clearly enchanted while watching a magic show.","zh":"孩子觀看魔術表演時，可能看起來明顯陶醉。"},{"en":"Music can enchant listeners when it captures their full attention.","zh":"當音樂完全吸引聽眾注意力，它可以令人陶醉。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests visible enjoyment and fascination.","zh":"這個短語暗示可見的享受和着迷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"listen to someone perform","meaning":"聆聽某人演奏","examples":[{"en":"Sacks listens to Alfred Brendel perform Beethoven’s Pathétique Sonata.","zh":"Sacks 聆聽 Alfred Brendel 演奏貝多芬《悲愴奏鳴曲》。"},{"en":"To listen to someone perform means to hear that person play, sing, act, or present live or recorded work.","zh":"listen to someone perform 指聽某人演奏、唱歌、表演或呈現現場或錄製作品。"},{"en":"Students may listen to a classmate perform a poem in assembly.","zh":"學生可能在早會聆聽同學朗誦詩。"},{"en":"Listening to someone perform can reveal skill, emotion, and interpretation.","zh":"聆聽某人表演可以看出技巧、情感和詮釋。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the audience’s act of hearing a performance.","zh":"這個短語集中於觀眾聆聽表演的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Beethoven’s Pathétique Sonata","meaning":"貝多芬《悲愴奏鳴曲》","examples":[{"en":"The cover shows Sacks listening to Beethoven’s Pathétique Sonata.","zh":"封面顯示 Sacks 正在聆聽貝多芬《悲愴奏鳴曲》。"},{"en":"Beethoven’s Pathétique Sonata is a famous piano sonata by Ludwig van Beethoven.","zh":"Beethoven’s Pathétique Sonata 是路德維希・貝多芬著名的鋼琴奏鳴曲。"},{"en":"A piano student may study Beethoven’s Pathétique Sonata to learn dramatic expression.","zh":"鋼琴學生可能學習貝多芬《悲愴奏鳴曲》來掌握戲劇性表達。"},{"en":"Famous classical pieces often carry emotional and historical associations.","zh":"著名古典樂曲常帶有情感和歷史聯想。"},{"en":"This title identifies the specific music being heard.","zh":"這個標題指出正在被聆聽的具體音樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make a positive impression","meaning":"留下正面印象","examples":[{"en":"The cover photograph makes a positive impression.","zh":"封面照片留下正面印象。"},{"en":"To make a positive impression means to create a good first feeling or opinion.","zh":"make a positive impression 指創造良好的第一感覺或看法。"},{"en":"A clean classroom can make a positive impression on visiting parents.","zh":"乾淨課室可以給到訪家長留下正面印象。"},{"en":"First impressions matter because they shape what people expect next.","zh":"第一印象很重要，因為它塑造人們接下來的期望。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when appearance or behaviour creates approval.","zh":"當外表或行為令人認同時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be borne out by","meaning":"得到……證實","examples":[{"en":"The positive impression is borne out by the contents of the book.","zh":"這種正面印象得到書中內容證實。"},{"en":"To be borne out by something means to be supported or confirmed by it.","zh":"be borne out by something 指得到某事支持或證實。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may be borne out by excellent exam results.","zh":"學生的信心可能得到優秀考試成績證實。"},{"en":"If later evidence matches a first impression, that impression is borne out.","zh":"如果後來證據符合第一印象，該印象就得到證實。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is proved correct afterwards.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事之後被證明正確。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the contents of the book","meaning":"書中內容","examples":[{"en":"The contents of the book confirm the impression created by its cover.","zh":"書中內容證實了封面所形成的印象。"},{"en":"The contents of the book are the ideas, chapters, cases, and information inside it.","zh":"contents of the book 指書內的想法、章節、個案和資訊。"},{"en":"A reader may check the contents of a book before deciding whether to buy it.","zh":"讀者可能先查看書中內容，再決定是否購買。"},{"en":"Good contents can strengthen a good cover, while weak contents can disappoint readers.","zh":"好內容可以加強好封面，而薄弱內容可以令讀者失望。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to what the book actually contains.","zh":"這個短語指書實際包含的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"throughout the book","meaning":"貫穿全書","examples":[{"en":"Sacks’s voice throughout the book is calm and learned.","zh":"Sacks 貫穿全書的寫作聲音沉着而有學識。"},{"en":"Throughout the book means from the beginning to the end of the book.","zh":"throughout the book 指從書的開頭到結尾。"},{"en":"A mystery novel may keep readers tense throughout the book.","zh":"懸疑小說可能貫穿全書都令讀者緊張。"},{"en":"Repeated style or tone throughout a book helps create unity.","zh":"貫穿全書重複出現的風格或語氣有助建立統一感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something present across the whole text.","zh":"這個短語描述在整本書中都存在的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"steady and erudite","meaning":"沉穩而博學","examples":[{"en":"Sacks’s writing voice is steady and erudite.","zh":"Sacks 的寫作聲音沉穩而博學。"},{"en":"Steady and erudite means calm, controlled, and deeply knowledgeable.","zh":"steady and erudite 指冷靜、有控制力，而且知識深厚。"},{"en":"A teacher’s steady and erudite explanation can make a difficult topic feel manageable.","zh":"老師沉穩而博學的解釋可以令困難題目變得可處理。"},{"en":"Readers trust a writer more when expertise is shown without panic or exaggeration.","zh":"當專業知識在沒有慌張或誇張下呈現，讀者會更信任作者。"},{"en":"This phrase praises both emotional control and learning.","zh":"這個短語同時讚揚情緒控制和學識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"never pontifical","meaning":"從不以說教口吻自居","examples":[{"en":"Sacks sounds knowledgeable but never pontifical.","zh":"Sacks 聽起來知識豐富，但從不以說教口吻自居。"},{"en":"Never pontifical means never sounding self-important, preachy, or superior.","zh":"never pontifical 指從不聽起來自以為重要、說教或高人一等。"},{"en":"A good doctor explains clearly but is never pontifical with patients.","zh":"好醫生會清楚解釋，但不會對病人以說教口吻自居。"},{"en":"Experts become easier to trust when they teach without talking down to people.","zh":"當專家教導而不居高臨下，人們會更容易信任他們。"},{"en":"This phrase praises knowledge without arrogance.","zh":"這個短語讚揚有知識而不傲慢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pontifical","meaning":"自以為是且說教式的","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer praises Sacks for being erudite without sounding pontifical.","zh":"評論者讚揚 Sacks 博學而不顯得自以為是且說教式。"},{"en":"Pontifical means speaking in a self-important, moralising, or overly authoritative way.","zh":"pontifical 指說話自以為重要、道德說教或過分權威。"},{"en":"A manager sounds pontifical if he lectures staff without listening to them.","zh":"如果經理只訓話而不聆聽員工，他就聽起來很說教。"},{"en":"Pontifical language can annoy readers because it feels superior.","zh":"說教式語言可能令讀者反感，因為它感覺高人一等。"},{"en":"This word is usually negative when describing tone.","zh":"這個字描述語氣時通常帶負面意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"neither…nor…","meaning":"既不……也不……","examples":[{"en":"Sacks is neither self-conscious nor self-promoting.","zh":"Sacks 既不局促不自然，也不自我宣傳。"},{"en":"Neither…nor… is used to say that two things are both not true.","zh":"neither…nor… 用來表示兩件事都不是真的。"},{"en":"The new rule is neither fair nor practical.","zh":"這條新規則既不公平，也不實際。"},{"en":"This structure helps reject two descriptions at the same time.","zh":"這個結構幫助同時否定兩種描述。"},{"en":"It is useful when making a balanced negative statement.","zh":"作出平衡的否定陳述時，這個句式很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"self-conscious","meaning":"局促不自然的；過分在意自己的","examples":[{"en":"Sacks does not sound self-conscious when describing his experiences.","zh":"Sacks 描述自己的經歷時，聽起來並不局促不自然。"},{"en":"Self-conscious means awkwardly aware of oneself and worried about how one appears.","zh":"self-conscious 指尷尬地意識到自己，並擔心自己的形象。"},{"en":"A shy student may feel self-conscious when speaking in front of the class.","zh":"害羞學生在全班面前說話時，可能感到局促不自然。"},{"en":"Self-conscious writing can feel stiff because the writer worries too much about image.","zh":"過分在意自己的寫作可能顯得僵硬，因為作者太擔心形象。"},{"en":"This word describes discomfort about being watched or judged.","zh":"這個字描述因被觀看或評價而感到不自在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"self-promoting","meaning":"自我宣傳的","examples":[{"en":"The book is personal without being self-promoting.","zh":"這本書很個人化，但並不自我宣傳。"},{"en":"Self-promoting means trying too hard to praise oneself or advertise one’s own success.","zh":"self-promoting 指過分努力讚揚自己或宣傳自己的成功。"},{"en":"A job applicant can mention achievements without sounding self-promoting.","zh":"求職者可以提到成就，而不顯得自我宣傳。"},{"en":"Writing becomes self-promoting when the writer cares more about image than insight.","zh":"當作者更關心形象而不是見解，寫作就會變得自我宣傳。"},{"en":"This word is usually negative when someone seems to advertise themselves.","zh":"當某人似乎在宣傳自己時，這個字通常帶負面意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the preface","meaning":"前言","examples":[{"en":"The preface explains the aims and approach of the book.","zh":"前言解釋了這本書的目標和方法。"},{"en":"The preface is an introductory section at the beginning of a book.","zh":"preface 指書開頭的介紹部分。"},{"en":"Students may read the preface to understand why an author wrote the book.","zh":"學生可能閱讀前言，以理解作者為何寫這本書。"},{"en":"A good preface prepares readers for the book’s method and purpose.","zh":"好前言會讓讀者準備好理解書的方法和目的。"},{"en":"This word refers to introductory material before the main chapters.","zh":"這個字指正文章節之前的介紹材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"give a good idea of","meaning":"令人清楚了解","examples":[{"en":"The preface gives a good idea of what the book will deliver.","zh":"前言令人清楚了解這本書將提供的內容。"},{"en":"To give a good idea of something means to help people understand it clearly in advance.","zh":"give a good idea of something 指幫助人事先清楚理解某事。"},{"en":"A course outline gives students a good idea of what they will study.","zh":"課程大綱讓學生清楚了解將會學甚麼。"},{"en":"Clear previews reduce confusion because readers know what to expect.","zh":"清楚預覽能減少困惑，因為讀者知道應期待甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when something provides a useful preview.","zh":"當某物提供有用預覽時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"what the book will deliver","meaning":"該書將提供的內容","examples":[{"en":"The preface prepares readers for what the book will deliver.","zh":"前言讓讀者準備好了解該書將提供的內容。"},{"en":"What the book will deliver means the content, value, or experience the book is expected to provide.","zh":"what the book will deliver 指該書預期提供的內容、價值或閱讀體驗。"},{"en":"A back-cover summary may show what the book will deliver to busy readers.","zh":"封底簡介可能向忙碌讀者顯示該書將提供的內容。"},{"en":"Readers feel disappointed when a book promises more than it delivers.","zh":"當一本書承諾多於實際提供的內容，讀者會失望。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what readers can expect to receive from a book.","zh":"這個短語集中於讀者可以期待從書中得到甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"convey the insights","meaning":"傳達見解","examples":[{"en":"Sacks wants to convey the insights produced by recent research.","zh":"Sacks 想傳達近期研究產生的見解。"},{"en":"To convey the insights means to communicate important understandings clearly.","zh":"convey the insights 指清楚傳達重要理解。"},{"en":"A teacher uses examples to convey insights from a difficult article.","zh":"老師用例子來傳達一篇困難文章中的見解。"},{"en":"Insights matter only if readers can understand and apply them.","zh":"見解只有在讀者能理解和應用時才有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when knowledge is passed from expert work to an audience.","zh":"當知識從專家工作傳遞給讀者時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be gleaned from","meaning":"從……收集得來","examples":[{"en":"The insights were gleaned from a rapidly growing body of research.","zh":"這些見解是從迅速增長的研究成果中收集得來的。"},{"en":"To be gleaned from something means to be collected carefully from a source.","zh":"be gleaned from something 指從某來源仔細收集得來。"},{"en":"Useful advice can be gleaned from old exam reports.","zh":"有用建議可以從舊考試報告中收集得來。"},{"en":"Gleaning information takes time because the reader must select what matters.","zh":"收集資訊需要時間，因為讀者必須選出重要內容。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful extraction rather than quick copying.","zh":"這個短語暗示仔細提取，而不是快速複製。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a growing body of work","meaning":"越來越多的研究成果","examples":[{"en":"Sacks draws on a rapidly growing body of work about the brain.","zh":"Sacks 引用越來越多關於大腦的研究成果。"},{"en":"A growing body of work means an increasing amount of research or writing on a topic.","zh":"growing body of work 指關於某題目的研究或著作數量不斷增加。"},{"en":"There is a growing body of work on how sleep affects learning.","zh":"關於睡眠如何影響學習的研究成果越來越多。"},{"en":"As research grows, writers can connect more studies and form stronger explanations.","zh":"隨着研究增加，作者可以連結更多研究並形成更有力解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic discussion.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"neural underpinnings","meaning":"神經基礎","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses the neural underpinnings of musical perception.","zh":"這本書討論音樂感知的神經基礎。"},{"en":"Neural underpinnings are the brain processes or structures that support an ability.","zh":"neural underpinnings 指支撐某種能力的大腦過程或結構。"},{"en":"Scientists study the neural underpinnings of reading to understand dyslexia.","zh":"科學家研究閱讀的神經基礎，以理解讀寫障礙。"},{"en":"Understanding neural underpinnings helps explain why a skill can be damaged or improved.","zh":"理解神經基礎有助解釋為何某技能會受損或改善。"},{"en":"This phrase links behaviour with the brain mechanisms behind it.","zh":"這個短語把行為與背後的大腦機制連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"musical perception and imagery","meaning":"音樂感知與意象","examples":[{"en":"Researchers study the neural basis of musical perception and imagery.","zh":"研究者研究音樂感知與意象的神經基礎。"},{"en":"Musical perception and imagery involve hearing music and imagining music in the mind.","zh":"musical perception and imagery 涉及聽到音樂，以及在腦中想像音樂。"},{"en":"A pianist uses musical imagery when silently hearing a piece before playing it.","zh":"鋼琴家在演奏前心中默默聽見樂曲時，就是使用音樂意象。"},{"en":"Studying these abilities helps explain how the brain handles sound and imagination.","zh":"研究這些能力有助解釋大腦如何處理聲音和想像。"},{"en":"This phrase connects real listening with inner musical experience.","zh":"這個短語把真實聆聽與內在音樂經驗連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"complex and bizarre disorders","meaning":"複雜而奇異的障礙","examples":[{"en":"The book examines complex and sometimes bizarre musical disorders.","zh":"這本書研究複雜而有時奇異的音樂障礙。"},{"en":"Complex and bizarre disorders are conditions that are difficult to explain and very unusual.","zh":"complex and bizarre disorders 指難以解釋且非常不尋常的病症。"},{"en":"A doctor may study a bizarre disorder when a patient hears music that is not there.","zh":"當病人聽到不存在的音樂時，醫生可能研究這種奇異障礙。"},{"en":"Such disorders reveal how many separate processes support ordinary abilities.","zh":"這類障礙揭示普通能力背後有許多獨立過程。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses both difficulty and strangeness.","zh":"這個短語同時強調困難和奇特。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be prone to","meaning":"容易出現……","examples":[{"en":"Musical perception can be prone to unusual neurological disorders.","zh":"音樂感知容易出現不尋常的神經障礙。"},{"en":"To be prone to something means to be likely or easily affected by it.","zh":"be prone to something 指容易或很可能受某事影響。"},{"en":"A tired student may be prone to careless mistakes.","zh":"疲倦學生容易犯粗心錯誤。"},{"en":"People are prone to problems when a system is delicate or overloaded.","zh":"當系統脆弱或負荷過重，人們就容易出現問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes vulnerability or tendency.","zh":"這個短語描述脆弱性或傾向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stress the importance of","meaning":"強調……的重要性","examples":[{"en":"Sacks stresses the importance of careful observation.","zh":"Sacks 強調細心觀察的重要性。"},{"en":"To stress the importance of something means to emphasise strongly that it matters.","zh":"stress the importance of something 指強烈強調某事很重要。"},{"en":"A doctor may stress the importance of taking medicine on time.","zh":"醫生可能強調按時服藥的重要性。"},{"en":"People stress important actions when ignoring them could cause harm.","zh":"當忽視某行動可能造成傷害，人們會強調其重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces strong advice or emphasis.","zh":"這個短語引出強烈建議或重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the art of observation","meaning":"觀察的藝術","examples":[{"en":"Sacks values the simple art of observation.","zh":"Sacks 重視簡單的觀察藝術。"},{"en":"The art of observation is the skill of watching carefully and noticing meaningful details.","zh":"art of observation 指仔細觀看並注意有意義細節的技能。"},{"en":"A good teacher uses the art of observation to notice when students are confused.","zh":"好老師運用觀察的藝術，注意學生何時感到困惑。"},{"en":"Careful observation can reveal problems that machines or forms may miss.","zh":"細心觀察可以揭示機器或表格可能錯過的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase treats observing as a skilled human practice.","zh":"這個短語把觀察視為有技巧的人類實踐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the richness of","meaning":"……的豐富性","examples":[{"en":"He also emphasises the richness of the human context.","zh":"他也強調人的處境的豐富性。"},{"en":"The richness of something means its depth, variety, and meaningful detail.","zh":"richness of something 指某事的深度、多樣性和有意義細節。"},{"en":"A family story shows the richness of ordinary life through small memories.","zh":"家庭故事透過小記憶展示日常生活的豐富性。"},{"en":"Richness appears when a situation has many emotional and social layers.","zh":"當一個情況有許多情感和社會層次時，就會呈現豐富性。"},{"en":"This phrase praises depth rather than simple size.","zh":"這個短語讚揚深度，而不只是規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the human context","meaning":"人文背景；人的處境","examples":[{"en":"Medical cases should be understood within their human context.","zh":"醫學個案應放在其人的處境中理解。"},{"en":"The human context is the personal, emotional, social, and daily-life background of a situation.","zh":"human context 指一個情況中的個人、情感、社會和日常生活背景。"},{"en":"A teacher understands poor homework better after learning the student’s family context.","zh":"老師了解學生家庭背景後，會更理解功課差的原因。"},{"en":"Without human context, a medical case may become only a set of symptoms.","zh":"沒有人文背景，醫學個案可能只變成一組症狀。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that patients are people, not just data.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者，病人是人，不只是數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"combine A with B","meaning":"把A與B結合","examples":[{"en":"Sacks wants to combine observation and description with modern technology.","zh":"Sacks 想把觀察與描述同現代科技結合。"},{"en":"To combine A with B means to use two things together.","zh":"combine A with B 指把兩樣東西一起使用。"},{"en":"A teacher can combine grammar drills with games to make lessons clearer.","zh":"老師可以把文法操練與遊戲結合，使課堂更清楚。"},{"en":"Combining old and new methods can keep the strengths of both.","zh":"結合舊方法和新方法可以保留兩者的優點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when two approaches support each other.","zh":"當兩種方法能互相支持時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"observation and description","meaning":"觀察與描述","examples":[{"en":"The book combines observation and description with scientific research.","zh":"這本書把觀察與描述同科學研究結合。"},{"en":"Observation and description mean carefully noticing something and explaining what is seen.","zh":"observation and description 指仔細注意某事，並解釋所見內容。"},{"en":"In science class, students practise observation and description when recording plant growth.","zh":"在科學課中，學生記錄植物生長時，就是練習觀察與描述。"},{"en":"Good description turns careful observation into useful knowledge.","zh":"好描述會把細心觀察轉化為有用知識。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses seeing clearly before explaining deeply.","zh":"這個短語強調先看清楚，再深入解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the latest in technology","meaning":"最新科技","examples":[{"en":"Sacks recognises the value of the latest in technology.","zh":"Sacks 承認最新科技的價值。"},{"en":"The latest in technology means the newest tools, machines, or methods available.","zh":"latest in technology 指現有最新的工具、機器或方法。"},{"en":"Hospitals often use the latest in technology to scan the brain more precisely.","zh":"醫院常使用最新科技更精確地掃描大腦。"},{"en":"New technology can reveal details that older methods miss.","zh":"新科技可以揭示舊方法錯過的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing modern technical advances.","zh":"討論現代技術進步時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"enter into someone’s experience","meaning":"代入並理解某人的經歷","examples":[{"en":"Sacks tries to imaginatively enter into the experience of his patients.","zh":"Sacks 嘗試以想像代入並理解病人的經歷。"},{"en":"To enter into someone’s experience means to understand what life feels like from that person’s point of view.","zh":"enter into someone’s experience 指從某人的角度理解生活感受。"},{"en":"A good counsellor tries to enter into a teenager’s experience before giving advice.","zh":"好輔導員給建議前，會嘗試代入青少年的經歷。"},{"en":"This effort builds empathy because the listener sees more than symptoms or behaviour.","zh":"這種努力建立同理心，因為聆聽者看到的不只是症狀或行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep imaginative understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述深入而具想像力的理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"patients and subjects","meaning":"病人與研究對象","examples":[{"en":"The book describes the experiences of Sacks’s patients and research subjects.","zh":"這本書描述 Sacks 的病人與研究對象的經歷。"},{"en":"Patients and subjects are people receiving medical care or participating in research.","zh":"patients and subjects 指接受醫療照顧或參與研究的人。"},{"en":"Doctors must protect the dignity of patients and subjects when writing case reports.","zh":"醫生撰寫個案報告時，必須保護病人與研究對象的尊嚴。"},{"en":"Their stories help readers understand how conditions affect real lives.","zh":"他們的故事幫助讀者理解疾病如何影響真實生活。"},{"en":"This phrase includes both clinical patients and research participants.","zh":"這個短語包括臨床病人和研究參與者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"practise neurology","meaning":"從事神經科工作","examples":[{"en":"Sacks had been practising neurology for forty years.","zh":"Sacks 已從事神經科工作四十年。"},{"en":"To practise neurology means to work as a doctor in the field of brain and nerve disorders.","zh":"practise neurology 指以醫生身份從事大腦和神經疾病領域的工作。"},{"en":"A doctor may practise neurology in a hospital clinic.","zh":"醫生可能在醫院診所從事神經科工作。"},{"en":"Years of practice help doctors recognise unusual symptoms more accurately.","zh":"多年實踐幫助醫生更準確辨認不尋常症狀。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to professional medical work, not casual study.","zh":"這個短語指專業醫療工作，而不是隨意研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be torn between","meaning":"在……之間左右為難","examples":[{"en":"Sacks is torn between traditional observation and high-tech methods.","zh":"Sacks 在傳統觀察與高科技方法之間左右為難。"},{"en":"To be torn between two things means to find it difficult to choose between them.","zh":"be torn between two things 指難以在兩者之間選擇。"},{"en":"A student may be torn between studying medicine and becoming a musician.","zh":"學生可能在讀醫和成為音樂家之間左右為難。"},{"en":"People feel torn when both choices have real value.","zh":"當兩個選擇都有真正價值，人就會感到左右為難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inner conflict or divided loyalty.","zh":"這個短語描述內心衝突或忠誠分裂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the old-fashioned path of","meaning":"……的傳統路線","examples":[{"en":"His heart lies with the old-fashioned path of clinical observation.","zh":"他內心真正傾向臨床觀察的傳統路線。"},{"en":"The old-fashioned path of something means the traditional way of doing it.","zh":"old-fashioned path of something 指做某事的傳統方式。"},{"en":"Some teachers still prefer the old-fashioned path of handwritten notes.","zh":"有些老師仍偏好手寫筆記的傳統路線。"},{"en":"Traditional methods may survive because they preserve human judgement.","zh":"傳統方法可能因保留人的判斷而延續。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound affectionate rather than simply negative.","zh":"這個短語可以帶親切感，而不只是負面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"newfangled","meaning":"新式的；新潮的","examples":[{"en":"Sacks remains cautious about newfangled technological methods.","zh":"Sacks 對新式科技方法仍保持謹慎。"},{"en":"Newfangled means new, modern, and sometimes viewed with suspicion.","zh":"newfangled 指新、現代，而且有時被懷疑的。"},{"en":"An older worker may distrust a newfangled app until it proves useful.","zh":"年長員工可能不信任新式應用程式，直到它證明有用。"},{"en":"People call something newfangled when it feels unfamiliar or unnecessarily modern.","zh":"當某物感覺陌生或不必要地現代，人們可能稱它為 newfangled。"},{"en":"This word often carries a mildly sceptical tone.","zh":"這個字常帶輕微懷疑語氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a high-tech approach","meaning":"高科技方法","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer contrasts observation with a high-tech approach.","zh":"評論者把觀察與高科技方法作對比。"},{"en":"A high-tech approach uses advanced machines, digital tools, or modern technology.","zh":"high-tech approach 指使用先進機器、數碼工具或現代科技的方法。"},{"en":"A hospital may use a high-tech approach to diagnose brain disease.","zh":"醫院可能使用高科技方法診斷腦部疾病。"},{"en":"High-tech methods can be powerful, but they may miss human details.","zh":"高科技方法可以很強大，但可能錯過人的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts modern technology with older, simpler methods.","zh":"這個短語把現代科技與較舊、較簡單的方法作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take heed of","meaning":"重視；留意","examples":[{"en":"Sacks knows that he must take heed of technological developments.","zh":"Sacks 知道自己必須重視科技發展。"},{"en":"To take heed of something means to pay careful attention to it.","zh":"take heed of something 指仔細留意某事。"},{"en":"Drivers should take heed of weather warnings before travelling.","zh":"司機出行前應重視天氣警告。"},{"en":"Ignoring important changes can leave professionals behind.","zh":"忽視重要變化可能令專業人士落後。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests serious attention, not casual noticing.","zh":"這個短語暗示認真注意，而不是隨便留意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take heed of the latter","meaning":"重視後者","examples":[{"en":"He knows that he must take heed of the latter approach.","zh":"他知道自己必須重視後者的方法。"},{"en":"Take heed of the latter means pay attention to the second of two things mentioned.","zh":"take heed of the latter 指留意前面提到兩件事中的第二件。"},{"en":"A teacher may prefer paper books but still take heed of the latter option, online learning.","zh":"老師可能偏好紙本書，但仍重視後者，也就是網上學習。"},{"en":"The latter approach may matter even if someone personally prefers the former one.","zh":"即使某人個人偏好前者，後者的方法仍可能重要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to the second item in a comparison.","zh":"這個短語指回比較中的第二項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"his heart lies with","meaning":"內心真正傾向……","examples":[{"en":"Although Sacks respects technology, his heart lies with observation.","zh":"雖然 Sacks 尊重科技，但他內心真正傾向觀察。"},{"en":"If someone’s heart lies with something, they truly prefer or feel emotionally loyal to it.","zh":"if someone’s heart lies with something 指某人真正偏好或在情感上忠於某事。"},{"en":"A lawyer may earn money in business, but her heart lies with human-rights work.","zh":"律師可能在商業中賺錢，但內心真正傾向人權工作。"},{"en":"People may respect one option while feeling more deeply attached to another.","zh":"人們可能尊重一個選項，同時對另一個選項有更深依附。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inner preference rather than official opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述內心偏好，而不是官方意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the former","meaning":"前者","examples":[{"en":"His heart lies with the former, more traditional approach.","zh":"他內心真正傾向前者，也就是較傳統的方法。"},{"en":"The former means the first of two things just mentioned.","zh":"the former 指剛才提到兩者中的第一者。"},{"en":"If a student can choose between history and biology and prefers the former, they prefer history.","zh":"如果學生可在歷史和生物之間選擇，並偏好前者，就是偏好歷史。"},{"en":"This word avoids repeating the first option again.","zh":"這個字避免再次重複第一個選項。"},{"en":"It is useful in formal comparisons, but the reference must be clear.","zh":"它適合用於正式比較，但指代必須清楚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"consist mainly of","meaning":"主要由……組成","examples":[{"en":"The book consists mainly of detailed descriptions of cases.","zh":"這本書主要由個案的詳細描述組成。"},{"en":"To consist mainly of something means to be mostly made up of that thing.","zh":"consist mainly of something 指大部分由某物構成。"},{"en":"A lunchbox may consist mainly of rice, vegetables, and chicken.","zh":"飯盒可能主要由飯、蔬菜和雞肉組成。"},{"en":"If a course consists mainly of lectures, students may get little practice.","zh":"如果課程主要由講座組成，學生可能很少練習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main contents or structure of something.","zh":"這個短語描述某物的主要內容或結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"detailed descriptions of","meaning":"對……的詳細描述","examples":[{"en":"Musicophilia contains detailed descriptions of neurological cases.","zh":"《Musicophilia》包含對神經科個案的詳細描述。"},{"en":"Detailed descriptions of something give many clear facts, examples, and observations about it.","zh":"detailed descriptions of something 指提供關於某事的大量清楚事實、例子和觀察。"},{"en":"A police report may include detailed descriptions of what witnesses saw.","zh":"警方報告可能包括對證人所見內容的詳細描述。"},{"en":"Detailed descriptions help readers picture a case more accurately.","zh":"詳細描述幫助讀者更準確想像個案。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts full explanation with brief summary.","zh":"這個短語把完整解釋與簡短概述作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cases involving patients","meaning":"涉及病人的個案","examples":[{"en":"Most chapters describe cases involving Sacks’s patients.","zh":"大多數章節描述涉及 Sacks 病人的個案。"},{"en":"Cases involving patients are medical examples in which real patients are studied or described.","zh":"cases involving patients 指研究或描述真實病人的醫學例子。"},{"en":"Doctors use cases involving patients to teach students about unusual symptoms.","zh":"醫生用涉及病人的個案教學生認識不尋常症狀。"},{"en":"Real patient cases make medical ideas more concrete and human.","zh":"真實病人個案令醫學概念更具體、更有人情味。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to clinical stories, not imaginary examples.","zh":"這個短語指臨床故事，而不是想像例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in his practice","meaning":"在其診療工作中","examples":[{"en":"Sacks had encountered most of the patients in his medical practice.","zh":"Sacks 在其診療工作中遇到大多數病人。"},{"en":"In his practice means during his professional work as a doctor.","zh":"in his practice 指在他作為醫生的專業工作期間。"},{"en":"A dentist may notice common brushing mistakes in her practice.","zh":"牙醫可能在其診療工作中注意到常見刷牙錯誤。"},{"en":"Doctors learn from repeated real cases in daily clinical work.","zh":"醫生從日常臨床工作中反覆出現的真實個案學習。"},{"en":"This phrase connects knowledge with professional experience.","zh":"這個短語把知識與專業經驗連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"brief discussions of","meaning":"對……的簡短討論","examples":[{"en":"The book also includes brief discussions of scientific reports.","zh":"這本書也包括對科學報告的簡短討論。"},{"en":"Brief discussions of something are short explanations or comments about it.","zh":"brief discussions of something 指對某事的短解釋或評論。"},{"en":"A lesson may include brief discussions of news stories before the main activity.","zh":"課堂可能在主要活動前簡短討論新聞故事。"},{"en":"Brief discussions give context without taking over the whole text.","zh":"簡短討論提供背景，但不會佔據整篇文本。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests limited but useful attention.","zh":"這個短語暗示有限但有用的關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"contemporary neuroscientific reports","meaning":"當代神經科學報告","examples":[{"en":"Sacks refers to contemporary neuroscientific reports throughout the book.","zh":"Sacks 貫穿全書提到當代神經科學報告。"},{"en":"Contemporary neuroscientific reports are recent research papers or findings about the brain and nervous system.","zh":"contemporary neuroscientific reports 指近期關於大腦和神經系統的研究論文或發現。"},{"en":"A student may read contemporary reports to understand current brain research.","zh":"學生可能閱讀當代報告，以理解目前的大腦研究。"},{"en":"Using contemporary research helps connect old clinical observations with modern science.","zh":"使用當代研究有助把舊臨床觀察與現代科學連起來。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to current neuroscience literature.","zh":"這個短語指當前神經科學文獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be sprinkled liberally throughout","meaning":"大量穿插於……之中","examples":[{"en":"Scientific discussions are sprinkled liberally throughout the text.","zh":"科學討論大量穿插於全文之中。"},{"en":"To be sprinkled liberally throughout something means to appear often in many parts of it.","zh":"be sprinkled liberally throughout something 指頻繁出現在某物的許多部分。"},{"en":"Humorous comments may be sprinkled liberally throughout a teacher’s lesson.","zh":"老師課堂中可能大量穿插幽默評論。"},{"en":"Frequent small additions can shape the feeling of a whole text.","zh":"頻繁的小加入可以塑造整篇文本的感覺。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests many scattered examples, not one single section.","zh":"這個短語暗示許多分散例子，而不是單一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"throughout the text","meaning":"遍佈全文","examples":[{"en":"References to current research appear throughout the text.","zh":"對現時研究的引用遍佈全文。"},{"en":"Throughout the text means across the whole written piece.","zh":"throughout the text 指遍及整篇書面文本。"},{"en":"Key vocabulary appears throughout the text, so students meet it repeatedly.","zh":"關鍵詞彙遍佈全文，所以學生會反覆遇到它。"},{"en":"When an idea appears throughout a text, it becomes a major theme.","zh":"當一個想法遍佈全文，它就成為主要主題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something spread from beginning to end.","zh":"這個短語描述某物從頭到尾分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"haunted by music","meaning":"被音樂縈繞；受音樂困擾","examples":[{"en":"The first part of the book is entitled Haunted by Music.","zh":"這本書第一部分題為「被音樂縈繞」。"},{"en":"Haunted by music means troubled, possessed, or constantly occupied by music in the mind.","zh":"haunted by music 指心中被音樂困擾、佔據或不斷縈繞。"},{"en":"A person may feel haunted by a song that repeats in their head all day.","zh":"一個人可能整天被腦中重複的歌曲縈繞。"},{"en":"Music can feel haunting when it will not leave someone’s thoughts.","zh":"當音樂無法離開某人的思緒，就可能令人感到被縈繞。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests both attraction and disturbance.","zh":"這個短語同時暗示吸引和困擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the strange case of","meaning":"……的奇特個案","examples":[{"en":"The section begins with the strange case of Tony Cicoria.","zh":"這部分以 Tony Cicoria 的奇特個案開始。"},{"en":"The strange case of someone means an unusual example involving that person.","zh":"strange case of someone 指涉及某人的不尋常例子。"},{"en":"A doctor may discuss the strange case of a patient who suddenly loses speech.","zh":"醫生可能討論一名突然失語病人的奇特個案。"},{"en":"Strange cases attract attention because they challenge normal expectations.","zh":"奇特個案吸引注意，因為它們挑戰正常預期。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an unusual real-life story or medical example.","zh":"這個短語引出不尋常的真實故事或醫學例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"nonmusical","meaning":"沒有音樂背景的","examples":[{"en":"Tony Cicoria had previously considered himself nonmusical.","zh":"Tony Cicoria 先前認為自己沒有音樂背景。"},{"en":"Nonmusical means not interested in, skilled at, or connected with music.","zh":"nonmusical 指對音樂沒有興趣、技巧或關聯。"},{"en":"A nonmusical student may still enjoy listening to songs casually.","zh":"沒有音樂背景的學生仍可能隨意享受聽歌。"},{"en":"Calling oneself nonmusical suggests music has not been a strong part of one’s identity.","zh":"稱自己 nonmusical 暗示音樂不是自己身份中的重要部分。"},{"en":"This word describes a lack of musical background or ability.","zh":"這個字描述缺乏音樂背景或能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a middle-aged surgeon","meaning":"中年外科醫生","examples":[{"en":"Cicoria was a middle-aged surgeon when the unusual experience occurred.","zh":"當這次不尋常經歷發生時，Cicoria 是一名中年外科醫生。"},{"en":"A middle-aged surgeon is a doctor in midlife who performs operations.","zh":"middle-aged surgeon 指處於中年、負責做手術的醫生。"},{"en":"A middle-aged surgeon may have many years of hospital experience.","zh":"中年外科醫生可能已有多年醫院經驗。"},{"en":"The detail matters because Cicoria was not a young music student.","zh":"這個細節重要，因為 Cicoria 不是年輕音樂學生。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both age range and profession.","zh":"這個短語同時指出年齡階段和職業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be consumed by","meaning":"被……完全佔據","examples":[{"en":"He became consumed by a sudden love of music.","zh":"他被突然出現的音樂熱愛完全佔據。"},{"en":"To be consumed by something means to be completely occupied or controlled by it.","zh":"be consumed by something 指被某事完全佔據或支配。"},{"en":"A student may be consumed by anxiety before an important exam.","zh":"學生可能在重要考試前被焦慮完全佔據。"},{"en":"Strong emotions or interests can take over a person’s thoughts and routines.","zh":"強烈情感或興趣可以佔據一個人的思想和日常。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests intensity that is difficult to ignore.","zh":"這個短語暗示難以忽視的強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a love of music","meaning":"對音樂的熱愛","examples":[{"en":"Cicoria developed an intense love of music after the accident.","zh":"Cicoria 在意外後產生了對音樂的強烈熱愛。"},{"en":"A love of music is a strong enjoyment of or emotional attachment to music.","zh":"love of music 指對音樂強烈享受或情感依附。"},{"en":"A child may develop a love of music after joining a school choir.","zh":"孩子加入學校合唱團後，可能培養出對音樂的熱愛。"},{"en":"This love can change how people spend their time and attention.","zh":"這種熱愛可以改變人們如何花時間和注意力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep liking, not casual interest only.","zh":"這個短語描述深厚喜愛，而不只是隨意興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be hit by lightning","meaning":"被閃電擊中","examples":[{"en":"Cicoria’s musical transformation began after he was hit by lightning.","zh":"Cicoria 的音樂轉變在他被閃電擊中後開始。"},{"en":"To be hit by lightning means to be struck by an electrical discharge from a storm.","zh":"be hit by lightning 指被暴風雨中的放電擊中。"},{"en":"A person hit by lightning needs urgent medical attention.","zh":"被閃電擊中的人需要緊急醫療照顧。"},{"en":"Such an event can cause injury, shock, or rare neurological changes.","zh":"這類事件可以造成受傷、休克或罕見神經變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sudden and dangerous natural accident.","zh":"這個短語描述突然且危險的自然意外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"crave listening to","meaning":"渴望聆聽……","examples":[{"en":"He suddenly began to crave listening to piano music.","zh":"他突然開始渴望聆聽鋼琴音樂。"},{"en":"To crave listening to something means to feel a strong desire to hear it.","zh":"crave listening to something 指強烈想聽某物。"},{"en":"A tired worker may crave listening to quiet music after a stressful day.","zh":"疲倦員工在壓力大的一天後，可能渴望聆聽安靜音樂。"},{"en":"A craving is stronger than ordinary preference because it feels hard to resist.","zh":"渴望比普通偏好更強，因為它感覺難以抗拒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an intense desire for sound or music.","zh":"這個短語描述對聲音或音樂的強烈慾望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"never care for","meaning":"從不喜歡","examples":[{"en":"He had never cared for piano music before the accident.","zh":"意外前，他從不喜歡鋼琴音樂。"},{"en":"To never care for something means to have never liked or been interested in it.","zh":"never care for something 指從未喜歡或對某事感興趣。"},{"en":"A child may never care for vegetables until learning a new recipe.","zh":"孩子可能從不喜歡蔬菜，直到學會新食譜。"},{"en":"If someone suddenly loves what they never cared for, the change seems striking.","zh":"如果某人突然愛上自己從不喜歡的東西，這種變化就很突出。"},{"en":"This phrase is softer than saying “hated”.","zh":"這個短語比說 “hated” 更柔和。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"過去","examples":[{"en":"In the past, Cicoria had shown little interest in music.","zh":"過去，Cicoria 對音樂興趣很少。"},{"en":"In the past means during an earlier time, before now or before a later event.","zh":"in the past 指在較早時候，在現在或後來事件之前。"},{"en":"In the past, students used paper dictionaries more often than phone apps.","zh":"過去，學生比現在更常使用紙本字典，而不是手機應用程式。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare an earlier situation with a present change.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較早前情況與現在變化。"},{"en":"It is often used when explaining development over time.","zh":"解釋隨時間發展時常使用它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"compose music","meaning":"作曲","examples":[{"en":"Cicoria began to play the piano and compose music.","zh":"Cicoria 開始彈鋼琴並作曲。"},{"en":"To compose music means to create original music.","zh":"compose music 指創作原創音樂。"},{"en":"A student may compose music for a school drama performance.","zh":"學生可能為學校戲劇表演作曲。"},{"en":"Composing music requires arranging notes, rhythm, and emotion into a piece.","zh":"作曲需要把音符、節奏和情感組織成作品。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to creating music, not just playing music written by others.","zh":"這個短語指創作音樂，而不只是演奏別人寫的音樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"arise spontaneously","meaning":"自發出現","examples":[{"en":"Musical ideas arose spontaneously in his mind.","zh":"音樂想法在他腦中自發出現。"},{"en":"To arise spontaneously means to appear naturally without deliberate planning.","zh":"arise spontaneously 指在沒有刻意計劃下自然出現。"},{"en":"A solution may arise spontaneously while someone is walking home.","zh":"一個解決方法可能在某人步行回家時自發出現。"},{"en":"Spontaneous ideas can feel surprising because they were not forced.","zh":"自發想法可能令人驚訝，因為它們不是被強迫產生的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sudden natural emergence.","zh":"這個短語描述突然自然出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a torrent of notes","meaning":"大量湧現的音符","examples":[{"en":"The music appeared in his mind as a torrent of notes.","zh":"音樂以大量湧現的音符形式出現在他腦中。"},{"en":"A torrent of notes means a large, rapid flow of musical notes.","zh":"torrent of notes 指大量、快速流出的音符。"},{"en":"A pianist improvising excitedly may produce a torrent of notes.","zh":"鋼琴家興奮即興演奏時，可能彈出大量湧現的音符。"},{"en":"The image suggests music arriving too quickly to control easily.","zh":"這個意象暗示音樂來得太快，難以輕易控制。"},{"en":"This phrase uses water imagery to describe intense musical flow.","zh":"這個短語用水流意象描述強烈音樂流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a near-death experience","meaning":"瀕死經驗","examples":[{"en":"Cicoria had a near-death experience when the lightning struck him.","zh":"Cicoria 被閃電擊中時有瀕死經驗。"},{"en":"A near-death experience is an event in which someone comes very close to dying.","zh":"near-death experience 指某人非常接近死亡的事件。"},{"en":"A car crash survivor may describe a near-death experience afterwards.","zh":"車禍生還者之後可能描述瀕死經驗。"},{"en":"Such experiences can change how people think about life and priorities.","zh":"這類經驗可以改變人們對生命和優先次序的看法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious event, not a minor scare.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重事件，而不是小驚嚇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the direct result of","meaning":"……的直接結果","examples":[{"en":"His musicality may have been the direct result of a neurological change.","zh":"他的音樂才能可能是神經變化的直接結果。"},{"en":"The direct result of something is an effect caused clearly and immediately by it.","zh":"direct result of something 指由某事清楚而直接造成的結果。"},{"en":"A broken window may be the direct result of a football hitting it.","zh":"破窗可能是足球擊中它的直接結果。"},{"en":"If one event directly causes another, the link is easier to explain.","zh":"如果一件事直接造成另一件事，兩者關係較容易解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a clear cause-and-effect relationship.","zh":"這個短語指出清楚的因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"auditory regions","meaning":"聽覺區域","examples":[{"en":"The researchers considered possible changes in the brain’s auditory regions.","zh":"研究者考慮大腦聽覺區域可能出現的變化。"},{"en":"Auditory regions are parts of the brain involved in processing sound.","zh":"auditory regions 指大腦中參與處理聲音的部分。"},{"en":"Scientists may study auditory regions when a patient hears sounds incorrectly.","zh":"當病人錯誤聽到聲音時，科學家可能研究聽覺區域。"},{"en":"Damage to these regions can affect hearing, music, or speech perception.","zh":"這些區域受損可能影響聽覺、音樂或語言感知。"},{"en":"This phrase connects sound processing with brain location.","zh":"這個短語把聲音處理與大腦位置連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cerebral cortex","meaning":"大腦皮層","examples":[{"en":"The auditory regions form part of the cerebral cortex.","zh":"聽覺區域構成大腦皮層的一部分。"},{"en":"The cerebral cortex is the outer layer of the brain involved in many complex functions.","zh":"cerebral cortex 指參與許多複雜功能的大腦外層。"},{"en":"Doctors may study the cerebral cortex when investigating speech or memory problems.","zh":"醫生研究說話或記憶問題時，可能檢視大腦皮層。"},{"en":"Damage to different cortical areas can affect different abilities.","zh":"不同皮層區域受損可以影響不同能力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an important part of the brain.","zh":"這個短語指大腦的重要部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"electroencephalography","meaning":"腦電圖檢查","examples":[{"en":"Electroencephalography was used to examine Cicoria’s brain activity.","zh":"腦電圖檢查被用來檢查 Cicoria 的大腦活動。"},{"en":"Electroencephalography is a test that records electrical activity in the brain.","zh":"electroencephalography 是記錄大腦電活動的測試。"},{"en":"A hospital may use electroencephalography to investigate seizures.","zh":"醫院可能使用腦電圖檢查來調查癲癇發作。"},{"en":"The test helps doctors see patterns in brain waves.","zh":"這項測試幫助醫生看到腦電波模式。"},{"en":"This word is often shortened to EEG.","zh":"這個字常縮寫為 EEG。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"EEG results","meaning":"腦電圖結果","examples":[{"en":"Cicoria’s EEG results appeared normal after the accident.","zh":"事故後，Cicoria 的腦電圖結果看似正常。"},{"en":"EEG results are the findings from a test that records brain-wave activity.","zh":"EEG results 指記錄腦電波活動測試所得的結果。"},{"en":"A doctor may compare EEG results before and after treatment.","zh":"醫生可能比較治療前後的腦電圖結果。"},{"en":"Normal EEG results do not always explain every neurological symptom.","zh":"正常腦電圖結果不一定能解釋每種神經症狀。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in medical discussions of brain activity.","zh":"這個短語常見於關於大腦活動的醫學討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"brain waves","meaning":"腦電波","examples":[{"en":"The test showed his brain waves to be normal.","zh":"測試顯示他的腦電波正常。"},{"en":"Brain waves are patterns of electrical activity produced by the brain.","zh":"brain waves 指大腦產生的電活動模式。"},{"en":"Sleep studies record brain waves to understand different sleep stages.","zh":"睡眠研究會記錄腦電波，以理解不同睡眠階段。"},{"en":"Changes in brain waves may help doctors detect seizures or other problems.","zh":"腦電波變化可能幫助醫生發現癲癇或其他問題。"},{"en":"This phrase makes brain activity easier to describe.","zh":"這個短語令大腦活動較容易描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"trauma","meaning":"創傷","examples":[{"en":"The EEG was performed shortly after his physical trauma.","zh":"腦電圖在他身體創傷後不久進行。"},{"en":"Trauma means serious injury or emotional shock caused by a disturbing event.","zh":"trauma 指由令人不安事件造成的嚴重傷害或情緒震盪。"},{"en":"A cyclist may suffer trauma after a serious road accident.","zh":"單車手在嚴重交通意外後可能受創。"},{"en":"Physical trauma can affect the body and sometimes the brain.","zh":"身體創傷可以影響身體，有時也影響大腦。"},{"en":"This word is used for serious harm, not small everyday stress.","zh":"這個字用於嚴重傷害，而不是日常小壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"subsequent conversion to","meaning":"隨後轉向……","examples":[{"en":"The test followed his subsequent conversion to music.","zh":"這項測試是在他隨後轉向音樂後進行的。"},{"en":"Subsequent conversion to something means a later strong change toward a new interest, belief, or way of life.","zh":"subsequent conversion to something 指後來強烈轉向一種新興趣、信念或生活方式。"},{"en":"A student’s subsequent conversion to reading may begin after one inspiring novel.","zh":"學生隨後轉向閱讀，可能始於一本啟發他的小說。"},{"en":"Conversion suggests a major change, not a small preference.","zh":"conversion 暗示重大改變，而不是小偏好。"},{"en":"This phrase links a later transformation with what came before.","zh":"這個短語把後來轉變與先前事件連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"more sensitive tests","meaning":"更靈敏的測試","examples":[{"en":"More sensitive tests are now available to examine his condition.","zh":"現在已有更靈敏的測試可檢查他的狀況。"},{"en":"More sensitive tests can detect smaller or subtler changes than older tests.","zh":"more sensitive tests 能比舊測試檢測更小或更細微的變化。"},{"en":"A modern scan may be a more sensitive test for early disease.","zh":"現代掃描可能是檢測早期疾病的更靈敏測試。"},{"en":"Sensitive tests matter when standard results look normal but symptoms remain.","zh":"當標準結果看似正常但症狀仍存在時，靈敏測試很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improved ability to detect hidden problems.","zh":"這個短語描述發現隱藏問題的能力提升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"decline to undergo","meaning":"拒絕接受","examples":[{"en":"Cicoria has declined to undergo further neurological tests.","zh":"Cicoria 已拒絕接受進一步神經科測試。"},{"en":"To decline to undergo a test means to politely or formally refuse to have it.","zh":"decline to undergo a test 指禮貌或正式地拒絕接受測試。"},{"en":"A patient may decline to undergo surgery if the risks feel too high.","zh":"如果風險感覺太高，病人可能拒絕接受手術。"},{"en":"Refusing tests can limit what doctors are able to discover.","zh":"拒絕測試會限制醫生能發現的內容。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in medical contexts.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於醫療語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"delve into","meaning":"深入探究","examples":[{"en":"He does not want to delve into the causes of his musicality.","zh":"他不想深入探究自己音樂才能的成因。"},{"en":"To delve into something means to investigate it deeply and carefully.","zh":"delve into something 指深入而仔細地調查某事。"},{"en":"A journalist may delve into why a school policy failed.","zh":"記者可能深入探究一項學校政策失敗的原因。"},{"en":"Deep investigation can reveal causes that a quick look would miss.","zh":"深入調查可以揭示快速查看會錯過的成因。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests serious exploration beneath the surface.","zh":"這個短語暗示深入表面以下的認真探索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the causes of","meaning":"……的成因","examples":[{"en":"The researchers remain interested in the causes of his transformation.","zh":"研究者仍對他轉變的成因感興趣。"},{"en":"The causes of something are the reasons or factors that make it happen.","zh":"causes of something 指令某事發生的原因或因素。"},{"en":"Doctors try to identify the causes of repeated headaches.","zh":"醫生嘗試找出反覆頭痛的成因。"},{"en":"Understanding causes helps people choose better treatments or solutions.","zh":"理解成因有助人選擇更好治療或解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on why something happened.","zh":"這個短語集中於某事為何發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"musicality","meaning":"音樂才能；音樂感","examples":[{"en":"Cicoria does not want scientists to investigate his unexpected musicality.","zh":"Cicoria 不想科學家研究他意外出現的音樂才能。"},{"en":"Musicality is a person’s natural sense of music, rhythm, expression, or musical ability.","zh":"musicality 指一個人對音樂、節奏、表達或音樂能力的自然感覺。"},{"en":"A child may show musicality by clapping accurately to a rhythm.","zh":"孩子準確按節奏拍手時，可能顯示音樂感。"},{"en":"Musicality can appear in singing, playing, listening, or composing.","zh":"音樂感可以出現在唱歌、演奏、聆聽或作曲中。"},{"en":"This word describes musical ability or sensitivity, not just liking songs.","zh":"這個字描述音樂能力或敏感度，而不只是喜歡歌曲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"What a shame!","meaning":"真可惜！","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer responds to Cicoria’s refusal by saying, “What a shame!”","zh":"評論者對 Cicoria 的拒絕回應說：「真可惜！」"},{"en":"What a shame! means that something is disappointing or unfortunate.","zh":"What a shame! 指某事令人失望或可惜。"},{"en":"If a concert is cancelled because of rain, someone may say, “What a shame!”","zh":"如果音樂會因下雨取消，有人可能說：「真可惜！」"},{"en":"People use this phrase when a good opportunity is lost.","zh":"當好機會失去時，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It expresses regret without sounding very formal.","zh":"它表達遺憾，但語氣不很正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a range of musicality","meaning":"各種音樂能力","examples":[{"en":"The second part of the book explores a range of musical abilities and disorders.","zh":"這本書第二部分探討各種音樂能力和障礙。"},{"en":"A range of musicality means different levels or forms of musical ability.","zh":"range of musicality 指不同水平或形式的音樂能力。"},{"en":"A class may contain a range of musicality, from beginners to trained pianists.","zh":"一個班可能有各種音樂能力，從初學者到受訓鋼琴手都有。"},{"en":"Studying a range helps researchers understand both normal and unusual cases.","zh":"研究一系列能力有助研究者理解正常和不尋常個案。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests variety rather than one single ability.","zh":"這個短語暗示多樣性，而不是單一能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cover a wider variety of","meaning":"涵蓋更廣泛的……","examples":[{"en":"Part II covers a wider variety of topics.","zh":"第二部分涵蓋更廣泛的題目。"},{"en":"To cover a wider variety of something means to include more different types of it.","zh":"cover a wider variety of something 指包括更多不同類型的某物。"},{"en":"A revised course may cover a wider variety of writing tasks.","zh":"修訂課程可能涵蓋更廣泛的寫作任務。"},{"en":"Wider coverage can make a book more useful to different readers.","zh":"較廣泛的涵蓋範圍可以令一本書對不同讀者更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broader scope.","zh":"這個短語描述更廣闊的範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"little or nothing that is new","meaning":"幾乎沒有新意","examples":[{"en":"Some chapters offer little or nothing that is new.","zh":"有些章節幾乎沒有新意。"},{"en":"Little or nothing that is new means very little fresh information or no new information at all.","zh":"little or nothing that is new 指很少新資訊，甚至完全沒有新資訊。"},{"en":"A lecture may offer little that is new if it repeats last week’s lesson.","zh":"如果講座重複上星期的課，可能幾乎沒有新意。"},{"en":"Readers may feel disappointed when a chapter does not add fresh insight.","zh":"當章節沒有加入新見解，讀者可能感到失望。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises material as familiar or unoriginal.","zh":"這個短語批評內容熟悉或缺乏原創性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"merely note that","meaning":"只是指出","examples":[{"en":"One short chapter merely notes that blind people often hear better.","zh":"其中一個短章只是指出失明人士通常聽覺較好。"},{"en":"To merely note that means to simply mention something without much explanation.","zh":"merely note that 指只是提到某事，而沒有太多解釋。"},{"en":"A report may merely note that attendance fell, without explaining why.","zh":"報告可能只是指出出席率下降，卻沒有解釋原因。"},{"en":"Readers may want more analysis when a writer only notes a fact.","zh":"當作者只指出事實時，讀者可能想要更多分析。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the treatment is too brief.","zh":"這個短語暗示處理得太簡短。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the blind","meaning":"失明人士","examples":[{"en":"The chapter discusses the hearing abilities of the blind.","zh":"這一章討論失明人士的聽覺能力。"},{"en":"The blind means people who cannot see or have very serious sight loss.","zh":"the blind 指看不見或視力嚴重受損的人。"},{"en":"Services for the blind may include guide dogs, Braille signs, and audio books.","zh":"為失明人士提供的服務可能包括導盲犬、點字標示和有聲書。"},{"en":"Some blind people develop strong listening skills because they rely heavily on sound.","zh":"有些失明人士因高度依賴聲音而發展出強聽覺能力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a group of people and should be used respectfully.","zh":"這個短語指一群人，應尊重地使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the sighted","meaning":"視力正常的人","examples":[{"en":"The blind may have better hearing than the sighted.","zh":"失明人士的聽覺可能比視力正常的人更好。"},{"en":"The sighted means people who can see.","zh":"the sighted 指能看見的人。"},{"en":"Public signs are often designed for the sighted first, which can exclude blind users.","zh":"公共標示常先為視力正常的人設計，這可能排除失明使用者。"},{"en":"Comparing the blind and the sighted can reveal how the brain adapts to sensory loss.","zh":"比較失明人士與視力正常的人，可以揭示大腦如何適應感官喪失。"},{"en":"This phrase is usually used in contrast with blind people.","zh":"這個短語通常與失明人士作對比使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"present the strangest cases","meaning":"呈現最奇特的個案","examples":[{"en":"The most engaging chapters present the strangest cases.","zh":"最吸引人的章節呈現最奇特的個案。"},{"en":"To present the strangest cases means to show the most unusual examples clearly to readers.","zh":"present the strangest cases 指清楚向讀者展示最不尋常的例子。"},{"en":"A science teacher may present strange cases to make a difficult topic memorable.","zh":"科學老師可能呈現奇特個案，使困難題目更容易記住。"},{"en":"Strange cases attract attention because they break normal patterns.","zh":"奇特個案吸引注意，因為它們打破正常模式。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that unusual stories make the writing more interesting.","zh":"這個短語暗示不尋常故事令寫作更有趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"amusia","meaning":"失音樂症","examples":[{"en":"Amusia prevents a person from hearing sounds as music.","zh":"失音樂症使人無法把聲音感知為音樂。"},{"en":"Amusia is a condition in which a person cannot properly perceive music.","zh":"amusia 是一種令人無法正常感知音樂的狀況。"},{"en":"A person with amusia may hear a song as ordinary noise.","zh":"患有失音樂症的人可能把歌曲聽成普通噪音。"},{"en":"This condition can make singing, recognising tunes, or enjoying music difficult.","zh":"這種狀況可以令人難以唱歌、辨認旋律或享受音樂。"},{"en":"This word names a specific musical perception disorder.","zh":"這個字指一種特定音樂感知障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"an inability to","meaning":"無法……","examples":[{"en":"Amusia is an inability to perceive sounds as music.","zh":"失音樂症是無法把聲音感知為音樂。"},{"en":"An inability to do something means a lack of ability to do it.","zh":"inability to do something 指缺乏做某事的能力。"},{"en":"An inability to concentrate can make homework take much longer.","zh":"無法集中可以令功課花更長時間。"},{"en":"Inability may come from illness, injury, lack of training, or temporary stress.","zh":"無法做某事可能來自疾病、受傷、缺乏訓練或暫時壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a missing or weakened capacity.","zh":"這個短語描述缺失或削弱的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hear sounds as music","meaning":"把聲音感知為音樂","examples":[{"en":"People with amusia cannot hear sounds as music.","zh":"患有失音樂症的人不能把聲音感知為音樂。"},{"en":"To hear sounds as music means to perceive sound patterns as melody, rhythm, or musical structure.","zh":"hear sounds as music 指把聲音模式感知為旋律、節奏或音樂結構。"},{"en":"A child may first hear sounds as music when they recognise a repeated tune.","zh":"孩子辨認出重複旋律時，可能第一次把聲音感知為音樂。"},{"en":"If the brain cannot organise sound musically, music may seem like random noise.","zh":"如果大腦不能以音樂方式組織聲音，音樂可能像隨機噪音。"},{"en":"This phrase describes musical perception, not ordinary hearing alone.","zh":"這個短語描述音樂感知，而不只是普通聽覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"dysharmonia","meaning":"和聲感知障礙","examples":[{"en":"Dysharmonia specifically affects the perception of harmony.","zh":"和聲感知障礙特別影響對和聲的感知。"},{"en":"Dysharmonia is a disorder that affects a person’s ability to perceive harmony in music.","zh":"dysharmonia 是影響人感知音樂中和聲能力的障礙。"},{"en":"A musician with dysharmonia may still follow a tune but struggle with chords.","zh":"患有和聲感知障礙的音樂人可能仍能跟上旋律，但難以感知和弦。"},{"en":"The condition shows that musical abilities can be separated in the brain.","zh":"這種狀況顯示音樂能力可以在大腦中分離。"},{"en":"This word refers to a very specific musical impairment.","zh":"這個字指非常特定的音樂功能損害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a highly specific impairment","meaning":"高度特定的功能損害","examples":[{"en":"Dysharmonia is a highly specific impairment of musical perception.","zh":"和聲感知障礙是音樂感知中高度特定的功能損害。"},{"en":"A highly specific impairment affects one narrow ability rather than many abilities.","zh":"highly specific impairment 指影響一種很狹窄能力，而不是很多能力。"},{"en":"A patient may have a specific impairment in reading numbers but not words.","zh":"病人可能有閱讀數字但不是文字的特定功能損害。"},{"en":"Specific impairments help researchers identify separate mental processes.","zh":"特定功能損害幫助研究者識別分開的心理過程。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses precision in what is damaged.","zh":"這個短語強調受損內容的精確性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the ability to hear harmony","meaning":"感知和聲的能力","examples":[{"en":"The disorder affects the ability to hear harmony.","zh":"這種障礙影響感知和聲的能力。"},{"en":"The ability to hear harmony means being able to perceive how different notes sound together.","zh":"ability to hear harmony 指能感知不同音符一起響起時的效果。"},{"en":"Choir singers need the ability to hear harmony when singing in parts.","zh":"合唱團歌手分聲部唱歌時，需要感知和聲的能力。"},{"en":"Losing this ability may make chords sound confusing or unpleasant.","zh":"失去這種能力可能令和弦聽起來混亂或不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one part of musical understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述音樂理解的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"understand melody","meaning":"理解旋律","examples":[{"en":"Some patients can still understand melody despite losing their sense of harmony.","zh":"有些病人即使失去和聲感，仍能理解旋律。"},{"en":"To understand melody means to recognise and follow the main tune of music.","zh":"understand melody 指辨認並跟隨音樂的主旋律。"},{"en":"A child may understand a melody well enough to hum it after one listening.","zh":"孩子聽一次後能哼出旋律，可能表示他理解旋律。"},{"en":"Melody can remain clear even when harmony becomes difficult to perceive.","zh":"即使和聲變得難以感知，旋律仍可能保持清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to grasping the tune, not the lyrics.","zh":"這個短語指掌握曲調，而不是歌詞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be left intact","meaning":"保持完整；未受損","examples":[{"en":"The patient’s ability to understand melody may be left intact.","zh":"病人理解旋律的能力可能保持完整。"},{"en":"To be left intact means to remain undamaged or unchanged.","zh":"be left intact 指保持未受損或未改變。"},{"en":"After a fall, a phone screen may be cracked but the camera left intact.","zh":"手機跌落後，螢幕可能裂了，但相機仍保持完整。"},{"en":"In brain disorders, one ability may be damaged while another is left intact.","zh":"在腦部障礙中，一種能力可能受損，而另一種能力保持完整。"},{"en":"This phrase helps contrast damaged and preserved functions.","zh":"這個短語幫助對比受損和保留的功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"specific dissociations","meaning":"特定功能分離","examples":[{"en":"The cases reveal specific dissociations among musical abilities.","zh":"這些個案揭示音樂能力之間的特定功能分離。"},{"en":"Specific dissociations are clear separations between abilities that can be damaged independently.","zh":"specific dissociations 指能力之間清楚分開，並可獨立受損。"},{"en":"A patient may lose speech but keep singing, showing a dissociation.","zh":"病人可能失去說話能力但保留唱歌能力，顯示功能分離。"},{"en":"Dissociations help scientists see that the brain does not process everything as one unit.","zh":"功能分離幫助科學家看見大腦不是把所有東西作為一個單位處理。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in neuroscience and psychology.","zh":"這個短語常見於神經科學和心理學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be found throughout","meaning":"在……各處都可見","examples":[{"en":"Such dissociations are found throughout the cases in the book.","zh":"這類功能分離在書中各個個案中都可見。"},{"en":"To be found throughout something means to appear repeatedly in many parts of it.","zh":"be found throughout something 指在某物許多部分反覆出現。"},{"en":"Similar grammar mistakes may be found throughout a student’s essay.","zh":"相似文法錯誤可能在學生文章各處都可見。"},{"en":"Repeated patterns across many cases make an observation more important.","zh":"當模式在許多個案中反覆出現，觀察就更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is widespread within a text or group.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事在文本或群體內廣泛存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"recount a case","meaning":"敘述個案","examples":[{"en":"Sacks recounts many unusual cases involving music and the brain.","zh":"Sacks 敘述許多涉及音樂和大腦的不尋常個案。"},{"en":"To recount a case means to tell or describe a specific example in detail.","zh":"recount a case 指詳細講述或描述一個具體例子。"},{"en":"A doctor may recount a case to teach students how a rare illness appeared.","zh":"醫生可能敘述個案，教學生罕見疾病如何出現。"},{"en":"Recounting cases can make abstract medical ideas easier to understand.","zh":"敘述個案可以令抽象醫學概念較容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than simply saying “tell a story”.","zh":"這個短語比 simply saying “tell a story” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"to Sacks’s credit","meaning":"值得肯定的是","examples":[{"en":"To Sacks’s credit, the book gives serious attention to music therapy.","zh":"值得肯定的是，這本書認真關注音樂治療。"},{"en":"To someone’s credit means that something should be praised about that person.","zh":"to someone’s credit 指某人某方面值得讚揚。"},{"en":"To the teacher’s credit, she admitted the instructions were unclear.","zh":"值得老師肯定的是，她承認指示不清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a positive point, often after criticism.","zh":"這個短語常在批評後引出正面之處。"},{"en":"It gives fair recognition for something done well.","zh":"它公平肯定做得好的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"bring readers into","meaning":"帶讀者進入……","examples":[{"en":"Part III brings readers into the realm of music therapy.","zh":"第三部分帶讀者進入音樂治療的領域。"},{"en":"To bring readers into a subject means to introduce them to it clearly and engagingly.","zh":"bring readers into a subject 指清楚而吸引地介紹讀者認識某題目。"},{"en":"A good opening chapter brings readers into the world of the story.","zh":"好的開首章節會帶讀者進入故事世界。"},{"en":"Writers bring readers into difficult topics by using examples and human stories.","zh":"作者透過例子和人的故事，帶讀者進入困難題目。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests guiding readers into unfamiliar territory.","zh":"這個短語暗示引導讀者進入陌生領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the underappreciated realm of","meaning":"被低估的……領域","examples":[{"en":"The book explores the underappreciated realm of music therapy.","zh":"這本書探索被低估的音樂治療領域。"},{"en":"The underappreciated realm of something is an area that deserves more attention than it receives.","zh":"underappreciated realm of something 指某個值得更多關注但未獲足夠重視的領域。"},{"en":"The underappreciated realm of school counselling often helps students quietly.","zh":"被低估的學校輔導領域常默默幫助學生。"},{"en":"Underappreciated fields may be important even if few people notice them.","zh":"被低估的領域即使很少人注意，也可能很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase praises a field while suggesting it has been overlooked.","zh":"這個短語一方面讚揚某領域，一方面暗示它被忽視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"music therapy","meaning":"音樂治療","examples":[{"en":"Music therapy can help patients with speech and movement disorders.","zh":"音樂治療可以幫助有語言和運動障礙的病人。"},{"en":"Music therapy uses music to support physical, emotional, cognitive, or communication needs.","zh":"music therapy 使用音樂來支援身體、情緒、認知或溝通需要。"},{"en":"A therapist may use songs to help a patient practise speaking after a stroke.","zh":"治療師可能用歌曲幫助中風後病人練習說話。"},{"en":"Music can support treatment because rhythm and melody engage the brain and body.","zh":"音樂可以支援治療，因為節奏和旋律會調動大腦和身體。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a clinical use of music, not casual entertainment.","zh":"這個短語指音樂的臨床用途，而不是普通娛樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"melodic intonation therapy","meaning":"旋律語調治療","examples":[{"en":"Melodic intonation therapy uses musical patterns to support speech.","zh":"旋律語調治療使用音樂模式來支援說話。"},{"en":"Melodic intonation therapy is a treatment that uses melody and rhythm to help people speak.","zh":"melodic intonation therapy 是使用旋律和節奏幫助人說話的療法。"},{"en":"A patient may sing simple phrases before gradually saying them normally.","zh":"病人可能先唱出簡單短語，再逐步正常說出。"},{"en":"Musical patterns can help speech because singing may use partly different brain pathways.","zh":"音樂模式可以幫助說話，因為唱歌可能使用部分不同的大腦路徑。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific speech therapy method.","zh":"這個短語指一種特定言語治療方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"expressive aphasic patients","meaning":"表達性失語症患者","examples":[{"en":"The therapy is used with expressive aphasic patients.","zh":"這種療法用於表達性失語症患者。"},{"en":"Expressive aphasic patients are people who have difficulty producing spoken language, often after brain injury.","zh":"expressive aphasic patients 指難以產生口語的人，通常是在腦傷後出現。"},{"en":"A patient may understand a question but struggle to express an answer verbally.","zh":"病人可能理解問題，但難以用說話表達答案。"},{"en":"Therapy aims to rebuild communication, not intelligence.","zh":"治療目標是重建溝通，而不是重建智力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to patients with a specific speech-production problem.","zh":"這個短語指有特定語言表達問題的病人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"express thoughts verbally","meaning":"以說話表達思想","examples":[{"en":"Expressive aphasic patients cannot easily express their thoughts verbally.","zh":"表達性失語症患者不能輕易以說話表達思想。"},{"en":"To express thoughts verbally means to communicate ideas through spoken words.","zh":"express thoughts verbally 指透過口語詞句傳達想法。"},{"en":"A nervous student may understand an answer but struggle to express it verbally.","zh":"緊張學生可能理解答案，但難以用說話表達。"},{"en":"Speech disorders can block verbal expression even when thoughts are clear.","zh":"語言障礙可以阻礙口語表達，即使思想清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on speaking ideas aloud.","zh":"這個短語集中於把想法說出來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"following a stroke","meaning":"中風後","examples":[{"en":"Some patients lose the ability to speak following a stroke.","zh":"有些病人在中風後失去說話能力。"},{"en":"Following a stroke means after a stroke has occurred.","zh":"following a stroke 指中風發生之後。"},{"en":"A person may need speech therapy following a stroke.","zh":"一個人在中風後可能需要言語治療。"},{"en":"Stroke can damage brain areas involved in movement, language, or memory.","zh":"中風可以損害涉及動作、語言或記憶的大腦區域。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the medical event that came before the symptom.","zh":"這個短語指出症狀之前發生的醫療事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cerebral incident","meaning":"腦部事件；腦部事故","examples":[{"en":"A stroke is one example of a cerebral incident.","zh":"中風是腦部事件的一個例子。"},{"en":"A cerebral incident is an event that affects the brain, often suddenly.","zh":"cerebral incident 指影響大腦的事件，通常突然發生。"},{"en":"A doctor may investigate a cerebral incident if a patient suddenly cannot speak.","zh":"如果病人突然不能說話，醫生可能調查腦部事件。"},{"en":"Brain incidents can lead to changes in movement, language, memory, or awareness.","zh":"腦部事件可以導致動作、語言、記憶或意識變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and medical.","zh":"這個短語較正式，屬醫學用語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"become capable of","meaning":"變得能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The therapy may help patients become capable of fluent speech again.","zh":"這種療法可能幫助病人再次變得能夠流利說話。"},{"en":"To become capable of doing something means to gain the ability to do it.","zh":"become capable of doing something 指取得做某事的能力。"},{"en":"After months of practice, a beginner may become capable of holding a simple conversation.","zh":"經過數月練習後，初學者可能變得能夠進行簡單對話。"},{"en":"Treatment is successful when patients regain abilities they had lost.","zh":"當病人重新獲得失去的能力，治療就是成功的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes development from inability to ability.","zh":"這個短語描述從不能到能夠的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"fluent speech","meaning":"流利說話","examples":[{"en":"Melodic intonation therapy may help patients regain fluent speech.","zh":"旋律語調治療可能幫助病人恢復流利說話。"},{"en":"Fluent speech is smooth, natural speech without many pauses or blocks.","zh":"fluent speech 指順暢、自然、沒有太多停頓或阻塞的說話。"},{"en":"A language learner may develop fluent speech through regular practice with real people.","zh":"語言學習者可以透過定期與真人練習培養流利說話。"},{"en":"Losing fluent speech can make communication slow and frustrating.","zh":"失去流利說話能力會令溝通緩慢而令人沮喪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the quality of spoken language.","zh":"這個短語描述口語語言的質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"demonstrate the power of","meaning":"展示……的力量","examples":[{"en":"Sacks demonstrates the power of music to affect movement.","zh":"Sacks 展示音樂影響動作的力量。"},{"en":"To demonstrate the power of something means to show clearly how strong or effective it is.","zh":"demonstrate the power of something 指清楚顯示某物有多強或多有效。"},{"en":"A teacher may demonstrate the power of examples by explaining a hard idea simply.","zh":"老師可以透過簡單解釋困難概念，展示例子的力量。"},{"en":"Real cases can demonstrate power more convincingly than general claims.","zh":"真實個案比一般聲稱更能有說服力地展示力量。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces evidence that something has a strong effect.","zh":"這個短語引出某物有強烈效果的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"near-miraculous power","meaning":"近乎奇蹟的力量","examples":[{"en":"Music can have a near-miraculous power over some patients.","zh":"音樂對某些病人可以有近乎奇蹟的力量。"},{"en":"Near-miraculous power means an effect so impressive that it almost seems like a miracle.","zh":"near-miraculous power 指效果令人印象深刻，幾乎像奇蹟。"},{"en":"A therapy may feel near-miraculous if a patient suddenly walks more smoothly.","zh":"如果病人突然走得更順暢，療法可能感覺有近乎奇蹟的力量。"},{"en":"Such power surprises people because ordinary explanation seems insufficient.","zh":"這種力量令人驚訝，因為普通解釋似乎不足。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses amazement without claiming a real miracle.","zh":"這個短語表達驚嘆，但不聲稱真正有奇蹟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"animate Parkinson’s patients","meaning":"令柏金遜症患者活動起來","examples":[{"en":"Music can animate Parkinson’s patients who have difficulty moving.","zh":"音樂可以令行動困難的柏金遜症患者活動起來。"},{"en":"To animate Parkinson’s patients means to help them move, respond, or become physically lively.","zh":"animate Parkinson’s patients 指幫助柏金遜症患者移動、回應或變得身體活躍。"},{"en":"Rhythmic music may animate a patient who was sitting stiffly moments before.","zh":"有節奏的音樂可能令剛才僵坐的病人活動起來。"},{"en":"Movement can improve when music provides timing and emotional energy.","zh":"當音樂提供節奏和情感能量，動作可能改善。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests music can bring motion back to people who seem frozen.","zh":"這個短語暗示音樂可以把動作帶回看似僵住的人身上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Parkinson’s patients","meaning":"柏金遜症患者","examples":[{"en":"Some Parkinson’s patients respond strongly to music.","zh":"有些柏金遜症患者對音樂反應強烈。"},{"en":"Parkinson’s patients are people with Parkinson’s disease, a condition that affects movement.","zh":"Parkinson’s patients 指患有柏金遜症的人，這是一種影響動作的疾病。"},{"en":"Parkinson’s patients may have shaking, stiffness, or difficulty starting movement.","zh":"柏金遜症患者可能有震顫、僵硬或難以開始動作。"},{"en":"Music may help some patients move with better rhythm.","zh":"音樂可能幫助部分病人以更好節奏移動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people living with a neurological disorder.","zh":"這個短語指患有神經系統疾病的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"severe movement disorders","meaning":"嚴重運動障礙","examples":[{"en":"Music may help people with severe movement disorders.","zh":"音樂可能幫助有嚴重運動障礙的人。"},{"en":"Severe movement disorders are serious conditions that make movement difficult or abnormal.","zh":"severe movement disorders 指令動作困難或異常的嚴重病症。"},{"en":"A patient with a severe movement disorder may struggle to walk across a room.","zh":"有嚴重運動障礙的病人可能難以走過一間房。"},{"en":"Movement disorders affect independence because daily actions become harder.","zh":"運動障礙會影響獨立生活，因為日常動作變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious problems with bodily movement.","zh":"這個短語描述身體動作上的嚴重問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be frozen into odd postures","meaning":"僵在奇怪姿勢中","examples":[{"en":"Some patients are frozen into odd postures until music begins.","zh":"有些病人在音樂開始前僵在奇怪姿勢中。"},{"en":"To be frozen into odd postures means to be stuck in unusual body positions and unable to move easily.","zh":"be frozen into odd postures 指卡在不尋常身體姿勢中，難以移動。"},{"en":"A patient may stand frozen in a doorway before a rhythm helps them step forward.","zh":"病人可能僵在門口，直到節奏幫助他向前踏步。"},{"en":"Frozen posture can make simple actions frightening or impossible.","zh":"僵住姿勢可以令簡單動作變得可怕或不可能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical immobility, not feeling cold.","zh":"這個短語描述身體不能動，而不是感到寒冷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"achieve this effect","meaning":"產生這種效果","examples":[{"en":"Scientists cannot yet explain how music achieves this effect.","zh":"科學家尚未能解釋音樂如何產生這種效果。"},{"en":"To achieve this effect means to produce this particular result.","zh":"achieve this effect 指產生這個特定結果。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask how a story achieves its emotional effect on readers.","zh":"老師可能問一個故事如何對讀者產生情感效果。"},{"en":"Understanding an effect helps people use it more safely and effectively.","zh":"理解效果有助人更安全和有效地使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with a specific outcome.","zh":"這個短語把原因與具體結果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be unfamiliar with","meaning":"不熟悉……","examples":[{"en":"Some readers may be unfamiliar with neuroscience.","zh":"有些讀者可能不熟悉神經科學。"},{"en":"To be unfamiliar with something means not to know much about it.","zh":"be unfamiliar with something 指對某事知道不多。"},{"en":"New students may be unfamiliar with the school library system.","zh":"新生可能不熟悉學校圖書館系統。"},{"en":"Writers need to explain terms when readers are unfamiliar with the topic.","zh":"當讀者不熟悉題目時，作者需要解釋術語。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited knowledge or experience.","zh":"這個短語描述有限知識或經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"neuroscience and music behaviour","meaning":"神經科學與音樂行為","examples":[{"en":"The book introduces general readers to neuroscience and music behaviour.","zh":"這本書向一般讀者介紹神經科學與音樂行為。"},{"en":"Neuroscience and music behaviour refers to the study of how the brain relates to musical actions and experiences.","zh":"neuroscience and music behaviour 指研究大腦如何與音樂行動和經驗相關。"},{"en":"A course on this topic may examine listening, singing, memory, and emotion.","zh":"關於這題目的課程可能研究聆聽、唱歌、記憶和情緒。"},{"en":"Understanding music behaviour helps explain why music affects speech and movement.","zh":"理解音樂行為有助解釋音樂為何影響說話和動作。"},{"en":"This phrase connects brain science with how people respond to music.","zh":"這個短語把腦科學與人們如何回應音樂連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"something of a revelation","meaning":"頗令人耳目一新的事物","examples":[{"en":"Musicophilia may be something of a revelation to new readers.","zh":"《Musicophilia》對新讀者來說可能頗令人耳目一新。"},{"en":"Something of a revelation is a surprising discovery that changes how someone sees a subject.","zh":"something of a revelation 指令人驚訝的發現，改變某人看待題目的方式。"},{"en":"A museum visit can be something of a revelation for a child who dislikes history.","zh":"對不喜歡歷史的孩子來說，博物館參觀可能頗令人耳目一新。"},{"en":"A book feels revelatory when it opens a world the reader had not noticed.","zh":"當一本書打開讀者未曾注意的世界，它就令人有啟發感。"},{"en":"This phrase means quite eye-opening, but not necessarily completely shocking.","zh":"這個短語意思是頗開眼界，但不一定完全震驚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"satisfy those seeking","meaning":"滿足尋求……的人","examples":[{"en":"The book may not satisfy those seeking detailed scientific explanations.","zh":"這本書可能不能滿足尋求詳細科學解釋的人。"},{"en":"To satisfy those seeking something means to meet the needs of people looking for it.","zh":"satisfy those seeking something 指滿足正在尋找某物的人的需要。"},{"en":"A short course may not satisfy those seeking advanced exam practice.","zh":"短課程可能不能滿足尋求高階考試練習的人。"},{"en":"Readers feel unsatisfied when a book gives stories but not enough explanation.","zh":"當一本書提供故事但解釋不足，讀者會感到不滿足。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the audience whose expectations may or may not be met.","zh":"這個短語指出哪些讀者的期望可能被滿足或未被滿足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"causes and implications","meaning":"成因與含義","examples":[{"en":"Some readers want to understand the causes and implications of the cases.","zh":"有些讀者想理解這些個案的成因與含義。"},{"en":"Causes and implications are the reasons something happens and the wider meanings or effects it has.","zh":"causes and implications 指某事發生的原因，以及它更廣泛的意義或影響。"},{"en":"A teacher may discuss the causes and implications of poor attendance.","zh":"老師可能討論出席率差的成因與含義。"},{"en":"Understanding causes explains the past, while implications show why the issue matters.","zh":"理解成因解釋過去，而理解含義顯示問題為何重要。"},{"en":"This phrase asks both “why did it happen?” and “what does it mean?”","zh":"這個短語同時問「為何發生？」和「這代表甚麼？」"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the phenomena described","meaning":"所描述的現象","examples":[{"en":"The book does not fully explain the phenomena described.","zh":"這本書沒有完全解釋所描述的現象。"},{"en":"The phenomena described are the unusual events, behaviours, or conditions mentioned in the text.","zh":"phenomena described 指文本中提到的不尋常事件、行為或狀況。"},{"en":"A science article should explain the phenomena described, not just list them.","zh":"科學文章應解釋所描述的現象，而不只是列出它們。"},{"en":"Readers may feel curious when strange phenomena are described but not fully explained.","zh":"當奇怪現象被描述但未被完全解釋時，讀者可能感到好奇。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to the things the writer has presented.","zh":"這個短語指回作者已呈現的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"for one thing","meaning":"其中一點是","examples":[{"en":"For one thing, Sacks is more comfortable discussing patients than experiments.","zh":"其中一點是，Sacks 討論病人比討論實驗更自在。"},{"en":"For one thing introduces one reason among several possible reasons.","zh":"for one thing 用來引出多個可能理由中的其中一個。"},{"en":"I prefer the library; for one thing, it is quieter than the café.","zh":"我較喜歡圖書館；其中一點是，它比咖啡店安靜。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise an explanation without listing every reason at once.","zh":"這個短語有助組織解釋，而不用一次列出所有理由。"},{"en":"It often signals that more reasons may follow.","zh":"它常暗示之後可能還有更多理由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be more at ease doing","meaning":"做……時更自在","examples":[{"en":"Sacks appears to be more at ease discussing patients.","zh":"Sacks 討論病人時似乎更自在。"},{"en":"To be more at ease doing something means to feel more comfortable and natural while doing it.","zh":"be more at ease doing something 指做某事時感到更舒服和自然。"},{"en":"A shy student may be more at ease speaking in a small group.","zh":"害羞學生在小組中說話時可能更自在。"},{"en":"People perform better when they are at ease with the task.","zh":"當人們對任務感到自在，表現會更好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes comfort and confidence in an activity.","zh":"這個短語描述在活動中的舒適和信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"discussing patients than experiments","meaning":"討論病人多於實驗","examples":[{"en":"Sacks seems more comfortable discussing patients than experiments.","zh":"Sacks 似乎較喜歡討論病人，而不是實驗。"},{"en":"Discussing patients than experiments contrasts human case discussion with technical research discussion.","zh":"discussing patients than experiments 對比人的個案討論與技術研究討論。"},{"en":"A doctor-writer may prefer discussing patients because stories feel more personal.","zh":"醫生作家可能偏好討論病人，因為故事更有人情味。"},{"en":"Focusing on patients can make a book warm, but may leave experiments underexplained.","zh":"集中於病人可以令書更溫暖，但可能使實驗解釋不足。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the reviewer’s view of Sacks’s preference.","zh":"這個短語突出評論者對 Sacks 偏好的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"tend to be","meaning":"往往會","examples":[{"en":"Sacks tends to be insufficiently critical of some research.","zh":"Sacks 對某些研究往往不夠批判。"},{"en":"Tend to be means usually or often have a certain quality.","zh":"tend to be 指通常或經常具有某種特質。"},{"en":"New students tend to be quiet during the first week.","zh":"新生在第一週往往會比較安靜。"},{"en":"A tendency is not always true, but it describes a common pattern.","zh":"趨勢不一定每次都正確，但描述常見模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when making a careful generalisation.","zh":"作出謹慎概括時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"rather uncritical","meaning":"相當缺乏批判性","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer finds Sacks rather uncritical when assessing scientific claims.","zh":"評論者認為 Sacks 評估科學主張時相當缺乏批判性。"},{"en":"Rather uncritical means not questioning something enough.","zh":"rather uncritical 指沒有足夠質疑某事。"},{"en":"A student is rather uncritical if they believe every website without checking sources.","zh":"如果學生不查來源就相信每個網站，他就相當缺乏批判性。"},{"en":"Being uncritical can make weak evidence seem stronger than it is.","zh":"缺乏批判性可能令薄弱證據看似比實際更強。"},{"en":"This phrase is a polite but clear criticism.","zh":"這個短語是禮貌但清楚的批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"accept scientific findings","meaning":"接受科學發現","examples":[{"en":"Sacks sometimes appears too willing to accept scientific findings.","zh":"Sacks 有時似乎太願意接受科學發現。"},{"en":"To accept scientific findings means to believe or treat research results as valid.","zh":"accept scientific findings 指相信或把研究結果視為有效。"},{"en":"Doctors usually accept scientific findings only after studies are carefully checked.","zh":"醫生通常在研究被仔細檢查後才接受科學發現。"},{"en":"Accepting findings too quickly may hide weaknesses in method or evidence.","zh":"太快接受研究結果可能隱藏方法或證據中的弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase is about trusting research conclusions.","zh":"這個短語關於信任研究結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"scientific findings and theories","meaning":"科學發現與理論","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer wanted a more critical treatment of scientific findings and theories.","zh":"評論者希望對科學發現與理論有更具批判性的處理。"},{"en":"Scientific findings and theories are research results and explanations built from them.","zh":"scientific findings and theories 指研究結果以及由結果建立的解釋。"},{"en":"A textbook should distinguish between findings and theories when teaching science.","zh":"教科書教授科學時應區分發現與理論。"},{"en":"Theories help organise findings, but both may need testing and criticism.","zh":"理論幫助組織發現，但兩者都可能需要測試和批判。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both evidence and interpretation.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋證據和詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"music-brain oddities","meaning":"音樂與大腦相關的異常現象","examples":[{"en":"The causes of music-brain oddities remain unclear.","zh":"音樂與大腦相關異常現象的成因仍不清楚。"},{"en":"Music-brain oddities are unusual conditions linking music with brain function.","zh":"music-brain oddities 指把音樂與大腦功能連起來的不尋常狀況。"},{"en":"A person suddenly hearing music after an injury would be a music-brain oddity.","zh":"一個人在受傷後突然聽到音樂，就是音樂與大腦相關的異常現象。"},{"en":"Such oddities are difficult to explain because music uses many brain systems.","zh":"這類異常難以解釋，因為音樂使用許多大腦系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and refers to strange neurological music cases.","zh":"這個短語較口語，指奇怪的神經音樂個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"remain poorly understood","meaning":"仍未被充分理解","examples":[{"en":"Many music-related neurological problems remain poorly understood.","zh":"許多與音樂相關的神經問題仍未被充分理解。"},{"en":"To remain poorly understood means still not be explained clearly or completely.","zh":"remain poorly understood 指仍未被清楚或完整解釋。"},{"en":"Some rare diseases remain poorly understood because few patients have them.","zh":"有些罕見疾病因病人很少而仍未被充分理解。"},{"en":"When a problem is poorly understood, diagnosis and treatment are harder.","zh":"當問題未被充分理解，診斷和治療會更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses continuing uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語強調持續的不確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"could have done more to","meaning":"本可以做更多去……","examples":[{"en":"Sacks could have done more to explain the wider implications of his cases.","zh":"Sacks 本可以做更多去解釋其個案的更廣泛含義。"},{"en":"Could have done more to means had the chance or ability to do more, but did not.","zh":"could have done more to 指本有機會或能力做更多，但沒有做到。"},{"en":"A school could have done more to support students after the exam failure.","zh":"學校在考試失敗後本可以做更多去支援學生。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses criticism of missed effort or incomplete action.","zh":"這個短語表達對錯失努力或行動不完整的批評。"},{"en":"It is softer than saying someone completely failed.","zh":"它比說某人完全失敗更柔和。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"draw out the implications","meaning":"帶出含義；闡明啟示","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer wanted Sacks to draw out the implications of his observations.","zh":"評論者希望 Sacks 帶出其觀察的含義。"},{"en":"To draw out the implications means to explain the wider meaning or consequences of something.","zh":"draw out the implications 指解釋某事更廣泛的意義或後果。"},{"en":"A teacher may draw out the implications of a historical event for today’s society.","zh":"老師可能帶出歷史事件對今日社會的啟示。"},{"en":"Observations become more useful when their larger meaning is explained.","zh":"當較大意義被解釋，觀察會變得更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase asks the writer to go beyond description.","zh":"這個短語要求作者超越描述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"careful observations","meaning":"細緻觀察","examples":[{"en":"The book contains many careful observations of patients.","zh":"這本書包含許多對病人的細緻觀察。"},{"en":"Careful observations are detailed and thoughtful notices of what happens.","zh":"careful observations 指對發生之事作出詳細而有思考的注意。"},{"en":"A nurse makes careful observations when checking breathing, mood, and movement.","zh":"護士檢查呼吸、情緒和動作時，就是作細緻觀察。"},{"en":"Careful observations can reveal changes before test results do.","zh":"細緻觀察可以在測試結果前揭示變化。"},{"en":"This phrase praises attentive watching and recording.","zh":"這個短語讚揚專注觀看和記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"successful treatments","meaning":"成功療法","examples":[{"en":"Some of the treatments described in the book have been successful.","zh":"書中描述的一些療法是成功的。"},{"en":"Successful treatments are medical or therapeutic methods that improve a patient’s condition.","zh":"successful treatments 指能改善病人狀況的醫療或治療方法。"},{"en":"Speech therapy can be a successful treatment for some communication problems.","zh":"言語治療可以是某些溝通問題的成功療法。"},{"en":"A treatment is judged successful when symptoms improve or daily life becomes easier.","zh":"當症狀改善或日常生活變得較容易，療法就被判斷為成功。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to positive treatment outcomes.","zh":"這個短語指正面的治療結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"specific dissociations among","meaning":"……之間的特定功能分離","examples":[{"en":"The cases reveal specific dissociations among components of music comprehension.","zh":"這些個案揭示音樂理解組成部分之間的特定功能分離。"},{"en":"Specific dissociations among abilities are clear separations between abilities that can fail independently.","zh":"specific dissociations among abilities 指能力之間清楚分開，並可獨立失效。"},{"en":"A patient may lose reading ability while keeping speaking ability, showing a dissociation.","zh":"病人可能失去閱讀能力但保留說話能力，顯示功能分離。"},{"en":"Such separations help researchers map different mental processes.","zh":"這類分離幫助研究者繪製不同心理過程。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a complex ability has separable parts.","zh":"這個短語顯示複雜能力有可分開的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"components of music comprehension","meaning":"音樂理解的組成部分","examples":[{"en":"Harmony and melody are separate components of music comprehension.","zh":"和聲和旋律是音樂理解中分開的組成部分。"},{"en":"Components of music comprehension are the different abilities involved in understanding music.","zh":"components of music comprehension 指理解音樂所涉及的不同能力。"},{"en":"Rhythm, melody, harmony, and timbre can all be components of musical understanding.","zh":"節奏、旋律、和聲和音色都可以是音樂理解的組成部分。"},{"en":"If one component is damaged, the rest may still work.","zh":"如果其中一個組成部分受損，其他部分可能仍能運作。"},{"en":"This phrase breaks music understanding into smaller parts.","zh":"這個短語把音樂理解拆成較小部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"loss of the ability to","meaning":"失去……的能力","examples":[{"en":"Some patients experience loss of the ability to perceive harmony.","zh":"有些病人失去感知和聲的能力。"},{"en":"Loss of the ability to do something means no longer being able to do it.","zh":"loss of the ability to do something 指不再能夠做某事。"},{"en":"A stroke may cause loss of the ability to speak clearly.","zh":"中風可能導致失去清楚說話的能力。"},{"en":"Losing an ability can affect daily life even if other abilities remain.","zh":"即使其他能力仍在，失去一種能力也可能影響日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious reduction in function.","zh":"這個短語描述功能的嚴重下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"perceive harmony but not melody","meaning":"能感知旋律但不能感知和聲","examples":[{"en":"A patient may lose the ability to perceive harmony but not melody.","zh":"病人可能失去感知和聲的能力，但沒有失去感知旋律的能力。"},{"en":"To perceive harmony but not melody means to recognise combined notes but not the main tune, or the reverse depending on the case.","zh":"perceive harmony but not melody 指能辨認合在一起的音符但不能辨認主旋律，或按個案相反。"},{"en":"A patient might enjoy a tune but fail to notice whether chords sound right.","zh":"病人可能喜歡一段旋律，卻無法注意和弦是否正確。"},{"en":"Such cases show that harmony and melody can be processed separately.","zh":"這類個案顯示和聲和旋律可以被分開處理。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a selective musical difficulty.","zh":"這個短語突出選擇性的音樂困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"indicate that","meaning":"顯示","examples":[{"en":"The dissociations indicate that music is not processed in one single centre.","zh":"這些功能分離顯示音樂不是在單一中樞處理的。"},{"en":"To indicate that means to show or suggest that something is true.","zh":"indicate that 指顯示或暗示某事為真。"},{"en":"Dark clouds indicate that rain may be coming.","zh":"烏雲顯示可能快要下雨。"},{"en":"Evidence indicates a conclusion when it points clearly in that direction.","zh":"當證據清楚指向某方向，它就顯示某結論。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what a sign or result suggests.","zh":"這個短語引出某個跡象或結果所暗示的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a single music centre","meaning":"單一音樂中樞","examples":[{"en":"The evidence suggests that there is no single music centre in the brain.","zh":"證據顯示大腦中沒有單一音樂中樞。"},{"en":"A single music centre would be one brain area responsible for all music processing.","zh":"single music centre 指一個負責所有音樂處理的大腦區域。"},{"en":"People may wrongly imagine that one small part of the brain handles all music.","zh":"人們可能錯誤想像大腦中某一小部分處理所有音樂。"},{"en":"Separate musical impairments suggest music uses several brain systems.","zh":"分開的音樂功能損害顯示音樂使用多個大腦系統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simplified idea that the reviewer questions.","zh":"這個短語描述評論者質疑的簡化想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"brain localisation","meaning":"大腦功能定位","examples":[{"en":"Many readers believe strongly in the brain localisation of mental functions.","zh":"許多讀者強烈相信心智能力的大腦功能定位。"},{"en":"Brain localisation is the idea that particular mental functions are linked to particular brain areas.","zh":"brain localisation 指特定心智能力與特定大腦區域相關的想法。"},{"en":"Doctors use brain localisation when connecting speech loss to damage in certain regions.","zh":"醫生把語言喪失與某些區域受損連起來時，就使用大腦功能定位。"},{"en":"Localisation can be useful, but complex abilities may involve networks rather than one spot.","zh":"功能定位可以有用，但複雜能力可能涉及網絡，而不是單一位置。"},{"en":"This phrase concerns where functions are located in the brain.","zh":"這個短語關於功能在大腦中的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"mental functions","meaning":"心智能力","examples":[{"en":"Different mental functions may be distributed across several brain regions.","zh":"不同心智能力可能分布於多個大腦區域。"},{"en":"Mental functions are abilities of the mind, such as memory, attention, language, and perception.","zh":"mental functions 指心智的能力，例如記憶、注意力、語言和感知。"},{"en":"Studying mental functions helps teachers understand learning difficulties.","zh":"研究心智能力有助老師理解學習困難。"},{"en":"Some mental functions depend on cooperation among several brain systems.","zh":"有些心智能力依賴多個大腦系統合作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to what the mind can do.","zh":"這個短語指心智能做到的事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a missed educational opportunity","meaning":"錯失的教育機會","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer considers this omission a missed educational opportunity.","zh":"評論者認為這個遺漏是錯失的教育機會。"},{"en":"A missed educational opportunity is a chance to teach or explain something useful that was not taken.","zh":"missed educational opportunity 指沒有把握到教導或解釋有用內容的機會。"},{"en":"A teacher misses an educational opportunity if students ask a good question and it is ignored.","zh":"如果學生提出好問題但被忽視，老師就錯失教育機會。"},{"en":"Missing such chances can leave readers with less understanding than they could have gained.","zh":"錯失這類機會可以令讀者得到的理解少於本可得到的。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises an unexplained point that could have helped learning.","zh":"這個短語批評一個本可幫助學習但未被解釋的點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"another conclusion one could draw","meaning":"另一個可得出的結論是","examples":[{"en":"Another conclusion one could draw concerns the limits of drug treatment.","zh":"另一個可得出的結論關於藥物治療的限制。"},{"en":"Another conclusion one could draw means another reasonable idea that can be taken from the evidence.","zh":"another conclusion one could draw 指可從證據中得出的另一個合理想法。"},{"en":"After exam results improve, another conclusion one could draw is that feedback helped.","zh":"考試成績改善後，另一個可得出的結論是回饋有幫助。"},{"en":"The same evidence can support more than one lesson or implication.","zh":"同一證據可以支持不止一個教訓或含義。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an additional interpretation.","zh":"這個短語引出額外詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no cures for","meaning":"沒有治療……的方法","examples":[{"en":"There appear to be no reliable cures for some music-related disorders.","zh":"有些與音樂相關的障礙似乎沒有可靠治療方法。"},{"en":"No cures for something means no treatments that can fully remove the condition.","zh":"no cures for something 指沒有能完全消除該狀況的療法。"},{"en":"Some chronic illnesses have no complete cures, only ways to manage symptoms.","zh":"有些慢性病沒有完整治療方法，只有管理症狀的方法。"},{"en":"When there is no cure, care may focus on comfort and function.","zh":"當沒有治癒方法，照顧可能集中於舒適和功能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the limits of treatment.","zh":"這個短語描述治療的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"neurological problems involving music","meaning":"涉及音樂的神經系統問題","examples":[{"en":"The book describes neurological problems involving music.","zh":"這本書描述涉及音樂的神經系統問題。"},{"en":"Neurological problems involving music are brain or nerve disorders that affect musical perception, memory, or response.","zh":"neurological problems involving music 指影響音樂感知、記憶或反應的大腦或神經障礙。"},{"en":"A patient may have a neurological problem involving music if songs trigger seizures.","zh":"如果歌曲引發癲癇，病人可能有涉及音樂的神經系統問題。"},{"en":"These problems reveal how music depends on the nervous system.","zh":"這些問題揭示音樂如何依賴神經系統。"},{"en":"This phrase links musical experience with medical brain conditions.","zh":"這個短語把音樂經驗與醫學腦部狀況連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"alleviate a symptom","meaning":"紓緩症狀","examples":[{"en":"A drug may alleviate a symptom in one patient.","zh":"一種藥物可能在一名病人身上紓緩症狀。"},{"en":"To alleviate a symptom means to make that symptom less severe.","zh":"alleviate a symptom 指令該症狀較不嚴重。"},{"en":"Pain medicine can alleviate a headache without curing the cause.","zh":"止痛藥可以紓緩頭痛，但未必治療成因。"},{"en":"Alleviating symptoms can improve daily life even when a disease remains.","zh":"即使疾病仍在，紓緩症狀也可以改善日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase means reduce discomfort, not necessarily cure.","zh":"這個短語意思是減少不適，不一定是治癒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"aggravate a symptom","meaning":"加重症狀","examples":[{"en":"The same drug may aggravate a symptom in another patient.","zh":"同一種藥物可能在另一名病人身上加重症狀。"},{"en":"To aggravate a symptom means to make it worse.","zh":"aggravate a symptom 指令症狀惡化。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can aggravate anxiety before an exam.","zh":"睡眠不足可以加重考試前的焦慮。"},{"en":"A treatment that helps one person may worsen symptoms in another.","zh":"幫助一個人的治療可能令另一個人的症狀惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase is the opposite of alleviate a symptom.","zh":"這個短語與 alleviate a symptom 相反。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in another patient","meaning":"在另一名病人身上","examples":[{"en":"A treatment that helps one patient may harm another patient.","zh":"幫助一名病人的治療可能傷害另一名病人。"},{"en":"In another patient means in a different person receiving treatment.","zh":"in another patient 指在另一個接受治療的人身上。"},{"en":"A medicine may reduce pain in one patient but cause dizziness in another patient.","zh":"藥物可能在一名病人身上減痛，但在另一名病人身上引起頭暈。"},{"en":"Individual reactions matter because bodies and brains differ.","zh":"個人反應很重要，因為身體和大腦不同。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights variation between people.","zh":"這個短語突出人與人之間的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"positive and negative effects","meaning":"正面及負面影響","examples":[{"en":"A medication may have both positive and negative effects.","zh":"藥物可能同時有正面及負面影響。"},{"en":"Positive and negative effects are helpful and harmful results of the same action or treatment.","zh":"positive and negative effects 指同一行動或治療帶來的有益和有害結果。"},{"en":"A phone can have positive effects on learning but negative effects on sleep.","zh":"手機可以對學習有正面影響，但對睡眠有負面影響。"},{"en":"Decisions become harder when one choice brings both benefits and costs.","zh":"當一個選擇同時帶來好處和代價，決定會更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase supports balanced evaluation.","zh":"這個短語支持平衡評估。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in the same patient","meaning":"在同一名病人身上","examples":[{"en":"A drug can produce contrasting effects in the same patient.","zh":"藥物可以在同一名病人身上產生相反效果。"},{"en":"In the same patient means within one person, not across different people.","zh":"in the same patient 指在同一個人身上，而不是不同人之間。"},{"en":"A medicine may improve sleep but reduce appetite in the same patient.","zh":"藥物可能在同一名病人身上改善睡眠，但降低食慾。"},{"en":"Mixed effects in one patient make treatment decisions more complicated.","zh":"同一病人身上的混合效果令治療決定更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights internal complexity within a single case.","zh":"這個短語突出單一個案內部的複雜性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"almost exclusively","meaning":"幾乎全都是","examples":[{"en":"The treatments mentioned are almost exclusively antiepileptic medications.","zh":"提到的治療幾乎全都是抗癲癇藥物。"},{"en":"Almost exclusively means nearly all, with very few exceptions.","zh":"almost exclusively 指幾乎全部，例外很少。"},{"en":"A café that sells almost exclusively coffee offers very few other drinks.","zh":"幾乎只賣咖啡的咖啡店提供很少其他飲品。"},{"en":"If examples come almost exclusively from one category, the discussion may feel narrow.","zh":"如果例子幾乎全來自一個類別，討論可能顯得狹窄。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises strong concentration in one area.","zh":"這個短語強調高度集中於某一範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"antiepileptic medications","meaning":"抗癲癇藥物","examples":[{"en":"Most of the drugs described are antiepileptic medications.","zh":"大多數被描述的藥物都是抗癲癇藥物。"},{"en":"Antiepileptic medications are drugs used to prevent or reduce seizures.","zh":"antiepileptic medications 指用來預防或減少癲癇發作的藥物。"},{"en":"A doctor may prescribe antiepileptic medication after repeated seizures.","zh":"病人反覆癲癇發作後，醫生可能處方抗癲癇藥物。"},{"en":"These drugs affect brain activity, so their effects may vary between patients.","zh":"這些藥物影響大腦活動，因此效果可能因病人而異。"},{"en":"This phrase names a medical drug category.","zh":"這個短語指一類醫學藥物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"damp down","meaning":"減弱；抑制","examples":[{"en":"These medications damp down the general excitability of the brain.","zh":"這些藥物會抑制大腦整體興奮性。"},{"en":"To damp down something means to reduce or calm it.","zh":"damp down something 指減少或平息某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may damp down a noisy class by speaking quietly and setting clear tasks.","zh":"老師可能透過輕聲說話和設定清楚任務來平息嘈吵班級。"},{"en":"Medication can damp down overactive brain activity, but it may affect other functions too.","zh":"藥物可以抑制過度活躍的大腦活動，但也可能影響其他功能。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests lowering intensity.","zh":"這個短語暗示降低強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the excitability of the brain","meaning":"大腦興奮性","examples":[{"en":"Antiepileptic drugs reduce the excitability of the brain.","zh":"抗癲癇藥物降低大腦興奮性。"},{"en":"The excitability of the brain is how easily brain cells become active or overstimulated.","zh":"excitability of the brain 指大腦細胞有多容易變得活躍或過度受刺激。"},{"en":"Doctors may try to lower brain excitability in patients with seizures.","zh":"醫生可能嘗試降低癲癇病人的大腦興奮性。"},{"en":"If excitability is too high, abnormal electrical activity may spread.","zh":"如果興奮性太高，異常電活動可能擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in neurological explanations of brain activity.","zh":"這個短語用於大腦活動的神經科解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in general","meaning":"整體而言","examples":[{"en":"The medication affects the brain in general rather than one precise area.","zh":"這種藥物整體而言影響大腦，而不是某一精確區域。"},{"en":"In general means overall or in most cases, not in every detail.","zh":"in general 指整體來說或在大多數情況下，而不是每個細節。"},{"en":"In general, students learn better when they sleep enough.","zh":"整體而言，學生睡眠足夠時學得更好。"},{"en":"A treatment that affects the body in general may have broad side effects.","zh":"整體影響身體的治療可能有廣泛副作用。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a broad statement rather than a precise one.","zh":"這個短語給出廣泛陳述，而不是精確陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"effectiveness varies widely","meaning":"成效差異很大","examples":[{"en":"The effectiveness of these treatments varies widely among patients.","zh":"這些治療在病人之間成效差異很大。"},{"en":"Effectiveness varies widely means something works very differently in different cases.","zh":"effectiveness varies widely 指某事在不同個案中效果非常不同。"},{"en":"The effectiveness of a study method varies widely among students.","zh":"一種學習方法在學生之間的成效可能差異很大。"},{"en":"Wide variation makes it difficult to predict who will benefit.","zh":"差異很大令預測誰會受益變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that one result does not apply to everyone.","zh":"這個短語提醒一個結果不適用於所有人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in many of the cases described","meaning":"在所描述的許多個案中","examples":[{"en":"In many of the cases described, the patients had normal EEG results.","zh":"在所描述的許多個案中，病人的腦電圖結果正常。"},{"en":"In many of the cases described means in many of the examples discussed in the text.","zh":"in many of the cases described 指在文本中討論的許多例子中。"},{"en":"In many of the cases described in a report, families needed housing support.","zh":"在報告所描述的許多個案中，家庭需要住屋支援。"},{"en":"Repeated patterns across cases can support a reviewer’s criticism.","zh":"跨個案反覆出現的模式可以支持評論者的批評。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to examples already presented.","zh":"這個短語指已呈現的例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be reported to have","meaning":"據報具有……","examples":[{"en":"Several patients were reported to have normal brain-wave results.","zh":"據報幾名病人的腦電波結果正常。"},{"en":"To be reported to have something means that a source says someone had it.","zh":"be reported to have something 指某來源說某人有某事物。"},{"en":"The patient was reported to have improved after three weeks of therapy.","zh":"據報病人在三星期治療後有所改善。"},{"en":"This phrase gives information while showing it comes from a report.","zh":"這個短語提供資訊，同時顯示資訊來自報告。"},{"en":"It is useful when the writer did not personally observe the fact.","zh":"當作者沒有親自觀察事實時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"normal EEG results","meaning":"正常腦電圖結果","examples":[{"en":"Some patients had music-related symptoms despite normal EEG results.","zh":"有些病人即使有正常腦電圖結果，仍有音樂相關症狀。"},{"en":"Normal EEG results mean the brain-wave test did not show clear abnormal activity.","zh":"normal EEG results 指腦電波測試沒有顯示明顯異常活動。"},{"en":"A patient may still have symptoms even when standard test results look normal.","zh":"即使標準測試結果看似正常，病人仍可能有症狀。"},{"en":"Normal results can be reassuring, but they may not explain every problem.","zh":"正常結果可以令人放心，但未必能解釋每個問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the outcome of a standard brain-wave test.","zh":"這個短語描述標準腦電波測試的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"recognise the existence of","meaning":"承認……的存在","examples":[{"en":"Sacks recognises the existence of newer diagnostic technologies.","zh":"Sacks 承認較新診斷科技的存在。"},{"en":"To recognise the existence of something means to acknowledge that it exists.","zh":"recognise the existence of something 指承認某物存在。"},{"en":"A school may recognise the existence of bullying before it can solve the problem.","zh":"學校必須先承認欺凌存在，才可解決問題。"},{"en":"Acknowledging something exists is not the same as using it fully.","zh":"承認某物存在不等於充分使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when someone admits a factor matters.","zh":"當某人承認某因素重要時，常使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"far more sensitive ways to","meaning":"靈敏得多的……方法","examples":[{"en":"There are far more sensitive ways to analyse brain waves.","zh":"現在有靈敏得多的方法分析腦電波。"},{"en":"Far more sensitive ways to do something are methods that detect much finer details.","zh":"far more sensitive ways to do something 指能偵測細微得多細節的方法。"},{"en":"Modern cameras offer far more sensitive ways to examine tiny cracks in buildings.","zh":"現代相機提供靈敏得多的方法檢查建築物細小裂縫。"},{"en":"More sensitive methods can reveal problems older tools miss.","zh":"更靈敏方法可以揭示舊工具錯過的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase compares improved precision with older methods.","zh":"這個短語把改進後的精確度與舊方法作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"analyse brain waves","meaning":"分析腦電波","examples":[{"en":"New technologies can analyse brain waves more precisely.","zh":"新科技可以更精確地分析腦電波。"},{"en":"To analyse brain waves means to examine patterns of electrical activity in the brain.","zh":"analyse brain waves 指檢查大腦電活動模式。"},{"en":"Doctors analyse brain waves when investigating seizures or unusual episodes.","zh":"醫生調查癲癇或不尋常發作時，會分析腦電波。"},{"en":"Better analysis may reveal subtle problems hidden in standard results.","zh":"更好的分析可能揭示標準結果中隱藏的細微問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a technical medical process.","zh":"這個短語描述一個技術性醫療過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the standard neurological EEG test","meaning":"標準神經科腦電圖測試","examples":[{"en":"The standard neurological EEG test may fail to detect subtle abnormalities.","zh":"標準神經科腦電圖測試可能未能偵測細微異常。"},{"en":"The standard neurological EEG test is the usual brain-wave test used in neurology.","zh":"standard neurological EEG test 指神經科中常用的一般腦電波測試。"},{"en":"A clinic may use a standard EEG test before ordering more advanced scans.","zh":"診所可能先使用標準腦電圖測試，再安排更先進掃描。"},{"en":"Standard tests are useful, but they may miss very subtle changes.","zh":"標準測試有用，但可能錯過非常細微的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts ordinary testing with newer, more sensitive methods.","zh":"這個短語把普通測試與較新、更靈敏方法作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"call for their use","meaning":"呼籲使用它們","examples":[{"en":"Sacks does not strongly call for the use of newer tests.","zh":"Sacks 沒有強烈呼籲使用較新的測試。"},{"en":"To call for their use means to publicly or clearly recommend that they should be used.","zh":"call for their use 指公開或清楚建議應使用它們。"},{"en":"A report may call for the use of safer buses after repeated accidents.","zh":"在反覆意外後，報告可能呼籲使用更安全巴士。"},{"en":"Calling for a method shows stronger support than merely mentioning it.","zh":"呼籲使用某方法比只是提及它顯示更強支持。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when someone urges action.","zh":"當某人敦促行動時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"exhibit compassion for","meaning":"對……表現出同情","examples":[{"en":"Sacks exhibits great compassion for his patients.","zh":"Sacks 對他的病人表現出極大同情。"},{"en":"To exhibit compassion for someone means to show care and sympathy for their suffering.","zh":"exhibit compassion for someone 指對某人的痛苦表現關心和同情。"},{"en":"A nurse exhibits compassion when listening patiently to a frightened patient.","zh":"護士耐心聆聽受驚病人時，就是表現出同情。"},{"en":"Compassion helps people feel seen as human, not just as problems.","zh":"同情幫助人感到自己被視為人，而不只是問題。"},{"en":"This phrase praises visible kindness and concern.","zh":"這個短語讚揚可見的善意和關懷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the greatest compassion","meaning":"極大的同情心","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer acknowledges Sacks’s great compassion for patients.","zh":"評論者承認 Sacks 對病人有極大的同情心。"},{"en":"The greatest compassion means very deep sympathy and care.","zh":"greatest compassion 指非常深的同情和關懷。"},{"en":"A doctor shows great compassion when explaining bad news gently.","zh":"醫生溫柔解釋壞消息時，就表現出極大同情心。"},{"en":"Compassion matters because patients often feel afraid and vulnerable.","zh":"同情心很重要，因為病人常感到害怕和脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises strong emotional concern for others.","zh":"這個短語強調對他人的強烈情感關懷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"convey no sense of urgency","meaning":"沒有傳達出迫切感","examples":[{"en":"Sacks conveys no sense of urgency about improving diagnosis.","zh":"Sacks 對改善診斷沒有傳達出迫切感。"},{"en":"To convey no sense of urgency means to make something seem not very immediate or pressing.","zh":"convey no sense of urgency 指令某事看起來不太即時或迫切。"},{"en":"A warning email conveys no urgency if it uses vague and calm language.","zh":"如果警告電郵使用含糊而平靜的語言，就沒有傳達迫切感。"},{"en":"Without urgency, readers may not feel that action is needed soon.","zh":"沒有迫切感，讀者可能不覺得需要很快行動。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises a lack of pressure or immediacy.","zh":"這個短語批評缺乏壓力或即時感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the pursuit of","meaning":"對……的追求","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer wants more urgency in the pursuit of better treatments.","zh":"評論者希望在追求更好治療方面有更多迫切感。"},{"en":"The pursuit of something is the active effort to achieve or find it.","zh":"pursuit of something 指積極努力達成或尋找某事。"},{"en":"Students may work hard in the pursuit of a scholarship.","zh":"學生可能努力追求獎學金。"},{"en":"Pursuit requires time, energy, and continued attention.","zh":"追求需要時間、精力和持續關注。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a serious search or goal.","zh":"這個短語暗示認真的尋找或目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"new avenues","meaning":"新途徑；新方向","examples":[{"en":"Researchers should investigate new avenues in diagnosis and treatment.","zh":"研究者應探索診斷和治療的新途徑。"},{"en":"New avenues are new possible ways of studying, solving, or developing something.","zh":"new avenues 指研究、解決或發展某事的新可能方法。"},{"en":"A school may explore new avenues for helping students who fear speaking.","zh":"學校可能探索幫助害怕說話學生的新方向。"},{"en":"New avenues become important when old methods do not fully solve the problem.","zh":"當舊方法未能完全解決問題，新途徑就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests fresh directions for future work.","zh":"這個短語暗示未來工作的全新方向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"diagnosis and treatment","meaning":"診斷與治療","examples":[{"en":"New technology could improve the diagnosis and treatment of these disorders.","zh":"新科技可以改善這些障礙的診斷與治療。"},{"en":"Diagnosis and treatment mean identifying a condition and then managing or curing it.","zh":"diagnosis and treatment 指識別病症，然後管理或治療它。"},{"en":"A hospital improves diagnosis and treatment when tests are faster and doctors communicate clearly.","zh":"當測試更快且醫生溝通清楚，醫院就改善診斷與治療。"},{"en":"Better diagnosis can lead to more suitable treatment.","zh":"更好的診斷可以帶來更合適的治療。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both finding the problem and helping the patient.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋找出問題和幫助病人兩方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"this absence echoes","meaning":"這種缺失呼應了……","examples":[{"en":"This absence of urgency echoes a concern expressed in the preface.","zh":"這種迫切感的缺失呼應了前言中表達的擔憂。"},{"en":"This absence echoes something means this lack repeats or reflects an earlier idea.","zh":"this absence echoes something 指這種缺乏重複或反映早前的想法。"},{"en":"A student’s silence may echo the worry raised by her parents.","zh":"學生的沉默可能呼應她父母提出的擔憂。"},{"en":"Echoes connect one part of a text with another.","zh":"呼應把文本的一部分與另一部分連起來。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an idea appears again in a related form.","zh":"這個短語顯示某想法以相關形式再次出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"express fear that","meaning":"表達對……的擔憂","examples":[{"en":"Sacks expresses fear that careful observation may disappear.","zh":"Sacks 表達對細心觀察可能消失的擔憂。"},{"en":"To express fear that means to say one is worried that something may happen.","zh":"express fear that 指說出自己擔心某事可能發生。"},{"en":"Parents may express fear that children spend too much time online.","zh":"家長可能表達對孩子花太多時間上網的擔憂。"},{"en":"Expressing fear often introduces a warning about the future.","zh":"表達擔憂常引出對未來的警告。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when concern is stated directly.","zh":"當憂慮被直接說出時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be lost","meaning":"消失；失傳","examples":[{"en":"He worries that the art of observation may be lost.","zh":"他擔心觀察的藝術可能會消失。"},{"en":"To be lost means to disappear, be forgotten, or no longer be practised.","zh":"be lost 指消失、被遺忘或不再被實踐。"},{"en":"A local dialect may be lost if children stop speaking it.","zh":"如果孩子停止使用本地方言，該方言可能失傳。"},{"en":"Skills can be lost when new technology replaces old training completely.","zh":"當新科技完全取代舊訓練，技能可能失傳。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disappearance or loss of continuity.","zh":"這個短語描述消失或延續中斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"rely too much on","meaning":"過分依賴","examples":[{"en":"Doctors should not rely too much on new technologies.","zh":"醫生不應過分依賴新科技。"},{"en":"To rely too much on something means to depend on it excessively.","zh":"rely too much on something 指過度依靠某物。"},{"en":"Students may rely too much on translation apps and stop learning vocabulary deeply.","zh":"學生可能過分依賴翻譯應用程式，而停止深入學習詞彙。"},{"en":"Overdependence can weaken human judgement and practical skill.","zh":"過度依賴可以削弱人的判斷和實用技能。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against using one tool as the whole solution.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要把一種工具當成全部解決方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"call for both approaches","meaning":"呼籲同時採用兩種方法","examples":[{"en":"Sacks ultimately calls for both observation and technology.","zh":"Sacks 最終呼籲同時採用觀察和科技。"},{"en":"To call for both approaches means to recommend using two methods together.","zh":"call for both approaches 指建議把兩種方法一起使用。"},{"en":"A school may call for both discipline and emotional support.","zh":"學校可能呼籲同時採用紀律和情感支援。"},{"en":"Combining approaches can solve problems that one method cannot handle alone.","zh":"結合方法可以解決單一方法不能獨自處理的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase supports balance rather than choosing only one side.","zh":"這個短語支持平衡，而不是只選一方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the neurological community","meaning":"神經學界","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer hopes that the neurological community will respond.","zh":"評論者希望神經學界會回應。"},{"en":"The neurological community is the group of doctors and researchers who study the nervous system.","zh":"neurological community 指研究神經系統的醫生和研究者群體。"},{"en":"The neurological community may debate new findings about memory loss.","zh":"神經學界可能辯論關於記憶喪失的新發現。"},{"en":"A response from this community can shape future diagnosis and treatment.","zh":"這個群體的回應可以塑造未來診斷和治療。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a professional field as a group of people.","zh":"這個短語把一個專業領域視為一群人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"we can only hope that","meaning":"我們只能希望","examples":[{"en":"We can only hope that researchers will pursue both approaches.","zh":"我們只能希望研究者會追求兩種方法。"},{"en":"We can only hope that means the speaker strongly wishes something will happen but cannot control it.","zh":"we can only hope that 指說話者強烈希望某事發生，但不能控制它。"},{"en":"We can only hope that the new teacher will understand the class’s needs.","zh":"我們只能希望新老師會理解班上的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses desire mixed with uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語表達願望，同時帶有不確定。"},{"en":"It is often used near the end of an argument or review.","zh":"它常用於論點或評論接近結尾時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生為每條題目選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option marked by the right letter.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選出由正確字母標示的答案選項。"},{"en":"In reading exams, students should check whether the question asks for a letter or a word.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生應檢查題目要求填字母還是單字。"},{"en":"Copying the wrong letter can cost marks even when the thinking is correct.","zh":"即使思路正確，抄錯字母也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in multiple-choice instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於多項選擇題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"mixed feelings about","meaning":"對……感受複雜","examples":[{"en":"The question asks why the writer has mixed feelings about the book.","zh":"題目問為何作者對這本書感受複雜。"},{"en":"Mixed feelings about something are both positive and negative feelings toward it.","zh":"mixed feelings about something 指對某事同時有正面和負面感受。"},{"en":"A student may have mixed feelings about moving schools because it is exciting but frightening.","zh":"學生可能對轉校感受複雜，因為既興奮又害怕。"},{"en":"Mixed feelings appear when something has strengths and weaknesses at the same time.","zh":"當某事同時有優點和弱點，複雜感受就會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a reaction is not simple.","zh":"當反應不簡單時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"a sense of guilt","meaning":"內疚感","examples":[{"en":"A sense of guilt alone did not cause the reviewer’s mixed reaction.","zh":"單是內疚感並沒有造成評論者的複雜反應。"},{"en":"A sense of guilt is a feeling that one may have done something wrong.","zh":"sense of guilt 指覺得自己可能做錯事的感覺。"},{"en":"A student may feel a sense of guilt after copying homework.","zh":"學生抄功課後可能有內疚感。"},{"en":"Guilt can make criticism feel uncomfortable even when criticism is fair.","zh":"即使批評公平，內疚感也可能令批評令人不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an inner moral discomfort.","zh":"這個短語描述內心的道德不安。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"expect something to be better than it was","meaning":"期望……比實際更好","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer expected the book to be better than it was.","zh":"評論者期望這本書比實際更好。"},{"en":"To expect something to be better than it was means to believe it would be stronger than the final result.","zh":"expect something to be better than it was 指相信某物會比最終結果更出色。"},{"en":"A student may expect a film to be better than it was after hearing many good reviews.","zh":"學生聽到許多好評後，可能期望電影比實際更好。"},{"en":"High expectations can make an average result feel disappointing.","zh":"高期望可以令普通結果感覺令人失望。"},{"en":"This phrase explains disappointment caused by a gap between hope and reality.","zh":"這個短語解釋希望與現實之間落差造成的失望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"fail to include","meaning":"未能包括","examples":[{"en":"One option incorrectly suggests that Sacks failed to include personal stories.","zh":"其中一個選項錯誤地暗示 Sacks 未能包括個人故事。"},{"en":"To fail to include something means not to put it in when it was expected or needed.","zh":"fail to include something 指在預期或需要時沒有加入某物。"},{"en":"A student may lose marks if they fail to include evidence in an essay.","zh":"如果學生未能在作文中包括證據，可能失分。"},{"en":"Missing important material can weaken an argument or report.","zh":"缺少重要材料可以削弱論點或報告。"},{"en":"This phrase points to an omission.","zh":"這個短語指出遺漏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"personal stories","meaning":"個人故事","examples":[{"en":"The book contains many of Sacks’s personal stories.","zh":"這本書包含許多 Sacks 的個人故事。"},{"en":"Personal stories are true or autobiographical accounts from someone’s own life.","zh":"personal stories 指來自某人自己生活的真實或自傳式敘述。"},{"en":"A teacher may use personal stories to make a lesson warmer and clearer.","zh":"老師可能使用個人故事令課堂更溫暖和清楚。"},{"en":"Personal stories help readers connect facts with human experience.","zh":"個人故事幫助讀者把事實與人的經驗連起來。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to life experiences, not fictional plots.","zh":"這個短語指人生經歷，而不是虛構情節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"the tone of voice","meaning":"語氣；寫作聲音","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to the tone of voice used throughout the book.","zh":"題目提到全書使用的語氣。"},{"en":"Tone of voice means the attitude or feeling expressed through writing or speech.","zh":"tone of voice 指透過寫作或說話表達出的態度或感覺。"},{"en":"A polite tone of voice can make criticism easier to accept.","zh":"禮貌語氣可以令批評較容易被接受。"},{"en":"Tone affects readers because it shapes how they feel about the writer.","zh":"語氣會影響讀者，因為它塑造他們對作者的感覺。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe spoken sound or written style.","zh":"這個短語可以描述說話聲音或寫作風格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"autobiographical description","meaning":"自傳式描述","examples":[{"en":"The book contains rich autobiographical description.","zh":"這本書包含豐富的自傳式描述。"},{"en":"Autobiographical description is writing that describes events or experiences from the author’s own life.","zh":"autobiographical description 指描述作者自己生活事件或經歷的寫作。"},{"en":"A memoir often contains autobiographical description of childhood and family.","zh":"回憶錄常包含關於童年和家庭的自傳式描述。"},{"en":"Such description can make a book feel personal and honest.","zh":"這類描述可以令書感覺個人化和真誠。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to self-life writing inside a wider text.","zh":"這個短語指較大文本中的自我人生書寫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"reconcile A with B","meaning":"調和A與B","examples":[{"en":"Sacks tries to reconcile traditional observation with new technologies.","zh":"Sacks 嘗試調和傳統觀察與新科技。"},{"en":"To reconcile A with B means to make two different ideas or methods work together.","zh":"reconcile A with B 指令兩種不同想法或方法能一起運作。"},{"en":"A school may try to reconcile strict rules with student freedom.","zh":"學校可能嘗試調和嚴格規則與學生自由。"},{"en":"Reconciliation is needed when two approaches seem to pull in different directions.","zh":"當兩種方法似乎朝不同方向拉扯，就需要調和。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finding balance between two things.","zh":"這個短語描述在兩者之間尋找平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"traditional observation","meaning":"傳統觀察方法","examples":[{"en":"Sacks remains strongly attached to traditional observation.","zh":"Sacks 仍強烈依戀傳統觀察方法。"},{"en":"Traditional observation means careful human watching and description without relying mainly on machines.","zh":"traditional observation 指主要不依賴機器，而透過人仔細觀看和描述。"},{"en":"A doctor uses traditional observation when noticing how a patient walks into the room.","zh":"醫生注意病人如何走進房間時，就是使用傳統觀察方法。"},{"en":"Observation can reveal mood, movement, and behaviour that tests may not capture.","zh":"觀察可以揭示測試未必捕捉到的情緒、動作和行為。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts clinical human judgement with high-tech testing.","zh":"這個短語把臨床人的判斷與高科技測試作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"new technologies","meaning":"新科技","examples":[{"en":"The preface considers how new technologies can complement observation.","zh":"前言考慮新科技如何補充觀察。"},{"en":"New technologies are recently developed tools, machines, or methods.","zh":"new technologies 指最近發展出的工具、機器或方法。"},{"en":"Hospitals use new technologies to scan organs more clearly.","zh":"醫院使用新科技更清楚掃描器官。"},{"en":"New technologies can improve diagnosis, but they still need human interpretation.","zh":"新科技可以改善診斷，但仍需要人的詮釋。"},{"en":"This phrase often refers to modern tools that change professional practice.","zh":"這個短語常指改變專業實踐的現代工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"a detailed description of","meaning":"對……的詳細描述","examples":[{"en":"One option refers to a detailed description of musical disorders.","zh":"其中一個選項提到對音樂障礙的詳細描述。"},{"en":"A detailed description of something gives clear, specific information about it.","zh":"detailed description of something 指提供關於某事的清楚具體資訊。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask for a detailed description of a science experiment.","zh":"老師可能要求學生對科學實驗作詳細描述。"},{"en":"Details help readers understand what happened and why it matters.","zh":"細節幫助讀者理解發生了甚麼及其重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests more than a brief summary.","zh":"這個短語暗示不只是簡短概述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"various musical disorders","meaning":"各種音樂障礙","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses various musical disorders through individual cases.","zh":"這本書透過個別個案討論各種音樂障礙。"},{"en":"Various musical disorders are different conditions that affect musical perception, memory, or response.","zh":"various musical disorders 指影響音樂感知、記憶或反應的不同狀況。"},{"en":"One disorder may affect melody, while another affects rhythm.","zh":"一種障礙可能影響旋律，另一種則影響節奏。"},{"en":"Studying different disorders helps researchers see separate parts of musical ability.","zh":"研究不同障礙有助研究者看見音樂能力的不同部分。"},{"en":"This phrase shows variety within music-related neurological problems.","zh":"這個短語顯示音樂相關神經問題內部的多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"explain how people understand music","meaning":"解釋人們如何理解音樂","examples":[{"en":"The book examines how the brain perceives and understands music.","zh":"這本書研究大腦如何感知和理解音樂。"},{"en":"To explain how people understand music means to describe how listeners recognise rhythm, melody, harmony, and emotion.","zh":"explain how people understand music 指描述聽眾如何辨認節奏、旋律、和聲和情感。"},{"en":"A music teacher may explain how people understand music by comparing tune and beat.","zh":"音樂老師可能透過比較曲調和節拍，解釋人們如何理解音樂。"},{"en":"Understanding music involves hearing, memory, feeling, and prediction.","zh":"理解音樂涉及聽覺、記憶、感受和預測。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the mental process behind musical experience.","zh":"這個短語集中於音樂經驗背後的心理過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"abandon simple observation","meaning":"摒棄簡單觀察","examples":[{"en":"Sacks does not argue that doctors should abandon simple observation.","zh":"Sacks 沒有主張醫生應摒棄簡單觀察。"},{"en":"To abandon simple observation means to stop using careful direct watching as a method.","zh":"abandon simple observation 指停止使用仔細直接觀看作為方法。"},{"en":"A teacher should not abandon observation just because test scores are available.","zh":"老師不應只因有測驗分數就摒棄觀察。"},{"en":"Simple observation remains useful because behaviour often gives important clues.","zh":"簡單觀察仍然有用，因為行為常提供重要線索。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving up a basic human method.","zh":"這個短語描述放棄一種基本人類方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"what is disappointing about","meaning":"……令人失望之處","examples":[{"en":"The question asks what is disappointing about Cicoria’s case.","zh":"題目問 Cicoria 個案令人失望之處。"},{"en":"What is disappointing about something means the part that causes regret or dissatisfaction.","zh":"what is disappointing about something 指某事中造成遺憾或不滿的部分。"},{"en":"What is disappointing about the trip is that the museum was closed.","zh":"這次旅行令人失望之處是博物館關門。"},{"en":"A case becomes disappointing when a useful chance to learn is missed.","zh":"當有用的學習機會被錯過，個案就令人失望。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for the negative point in an otherwise interesting situation.","zh":"這個短語詢問一個本來有趣情況中的負面之處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"refuse to undergo further tests","meaning":"拒絕接受進一步測試","examples":[{"en":"Cicoria refuses to undergo further neurological tests.","zh":"Cicoria 拒絕接受進一步神經科測試。"},{"en":"To refuse to undergo further tests means to say no to more medical examinations.","zh":"refuse to undergo further tests 指拒絕更多醫學檢查。"},{"en":"A patient may refuse further tests if they fear stress, cost, or bad news.","zh":"如果病人害怕壓力、費用或壞消息，可能拒絕進一步測試。"},{"en":"Refusal can prevent doctors from finding a clearer explanation.","zh":"拒絕測試可能阻止醫生找到更清楚解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a patient’s decision not to continue testing.","zh":"這個短語描述病人決定不繼續測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"determine the cause of","meaning":"確定……的成因","examples":[{"en":"Researchers cannot determine the cause of his sudden musicality without further testing.","zh":"沒有進一步測試，研究者不能確定他突然出現音樂才能的成因。"},{"en":"To determine the cause of something means to identify why it happened.","zh":"determine the cause of something 指找出某事發生的原因。"},{"en":"Doctors run tests to determine the cause of repeated dizziness.","zh":"醫生進行測試，以確定反覆頭暈的成因。"},{"en":"Without evidence, the cause may remain uncertain.","zh":"沒有證據，成因可能仍不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when people seek a clear explanation.","zh":"當人們尋找清楚解釋時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"sudden musicality","meaning":"突然出現的音樂才能","examples":[{"en":"Cicoria developed sudden musicality after being struck by lightning.","zh":"Cicoria 被閃電擊中後突然出現音樂才能。"},{"en":"Sudden musicality is an unexpected and rapid appearance of musical ability or interest.","zh":"sudden musicality 指音樂能力或興趣意外而快速出現。"},{"en":"A child may show sudden musicality after discovering the piano at school.","zh":"孩子在學校接觸鋼琴後，可能突然展現音樂才能。"},{"en":"Sudden change seems remarkable when there was little musical interest before.","zh":"如果之前很少音樂興趣，突然改變就顯得不尋常。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights both speed and surprise.","zh":"這個短語同時突出速度和驚訝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"be struck by lightning","meaning":"被閃電擊中","examples":[{"en":"Cicoria nearly died after being struck by lightning.","zh":"Cicoria 被閃電擊中後幾乎死亡。"},{"en":"To be struck by lightning means to be hit by an electrical discharge during a storm.","zh":"be struck by lightning 指在暴風雨中被放電擊中。"},{"en":"People should stay away from open fields if lightning may strike.","zh":"如果可能有閃電，人們應遠離空曠田野。"},{"en":"Being struck by lightning can cause burns, heart problems, or neurological injury.","zh":"被閃電擊中可以造成燒傷、心臟問題或神經損傷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rare but dangerous event.","zh":"這個短語描述罕見但危險的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"reveal anything","meaning":"顯示任何異常","examples":[{"en":"His earlier brain scans did not reveal anything abnormal.","zh":"他早前的大腦掃描沒有顯示任何異常。"},{"en":"To reveal anything means to show or uncover any useful information.","zh":"reveal anything 指顯示或揭示任何有用資訊。"},{"en":"A blood test may not reveal anything if the illness is mild.","zh":"如果疾病輕微，驗血可能不會顯示任何問題。"},{"en":"Normal tests can be frustrating when symptoms still continue.","zh":"當症狀仍持續而測試正常，會令人沮喪。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when an examination gives no clear answer.","zh":"當檢查沒有給出清楚答案時，常使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"agree with the views of","meaning":"符合……的看法","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the writer’s views.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否符合作者的看法。"},{"en":"To agree with the views of someone means to match that person’s opinion.","zh":"agree with the views of someone 指與某人的觀點相符。"},{"en":"In a reading test, an answer agrees with the writer only if the text supports it.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，只有文本支持某答案，它才符合作者看法。"},{"en":"Students should not use their own opinion when judging the writer’s view.","zh":"學生判斷作者觀點時不應使用自己的意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in Yes, No, Not Given questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 Yes, No, Not Given 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與……的看法相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the views expressed in the passage.","zh":"一項陳述可能與文章中表達的看法相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what that person thinks.","zh":"contradict the views of someone 指說出與某人想法相反的意思。"},{"en":"A claim contradicts the writer if the writer clearly argues against it.","zh":"如果作者清楚反對某說法，該說法就與作者觀點矛盾。"},{"en":"Contradiction must be based on textual evidence, not guessing.","zh":"矛盾必須基於文本證據，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a clear conflict with an opinion.","zh":"這個短語指出與觀點的清楚衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Students write NOT GIVEN when it is impossible to determine the writer’s view.","zh":"當無法判斷作者觀點時，學生寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資料作決定。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions a patient’s age, it is impossible to say how old they are.","zh":"如果篇章從未提到病人年齡，就無法判斷他幾歲。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students should not guess beyond the text.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生不應超出文本猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase explains uncertainty caused by missing evidence.","zh":"這個短語解釋因缺乏證據造成的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"a highly reputable writer","meaning":"聲譽很高的作家","examples":[{"en":"Oliver Sacks was a highly reputable medical writer.","zh":"Oliver Sacks 是一位聲譽很高的醫學作家。"},{"en":"A highly reputable writer is a writer widely respected for quality, knowledge, or reliability.","zh":"highly reputable writer 指因質素、知識或可靠性而廣受尊重的作家。"},{"en":"Students may trust a highly reputable writer more than an unknown blogger.","zh":"學生可能比起不知名博客，更信任聲譽很高的作家。"},{"en":"Reputation can raise expectations before a reader opens the book.","zh":"聲譽可以在讀者打開書前提高期望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong public or professional respect.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈的公眾或專業尊重。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"anything less than favourable","meaning":"並非完全正面的……","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer feels uneasy about giving Sacks anything less than a favourable review.","zh":"評論者對給 Sacks 並非完全正面的評論感到不自在。"},{"en":"Anything less than favourable means not fully positive or approving.","zh":"anything less than favourable 指並非完全正面或認同。"},{"en":"A teacher may hesitate to write anything less than favourable about a hardworking student.","zh":"老師可能不太願意對努力學生寫出並非完全正面的評語。"},{"en":"Respect for someone can make criticism feel uncomfortable.","zh":"對某人的尊重可以令批評變得不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase often softens the idea of negative judgement.","zh":"這個短語常柔化負面判斷的意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"a completely favourable review","meaning":"完全正面的評論","examples":[{"en":"The book did not receive a completely favourable review.","zh":"這本書沒有得到完全正面的評論。"},{"en":"A completely favourable review is a review that is entirely positive.","zh":"completely favourable review 指完全正面的評論。"},{"en":"A film may get a favourable review for acting but criticism for its ending.","zh":"一部電影可能因演技得到正面評價，但因結局受到批評。"},{"en":"When a review is not completely favourable, it contains both praise and criticism.","zh":"當評論不是完全正面，它就同時包含讚揚和批評。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fully approving evaluation.","zh":"這個短語描述完全認同的評價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"a good treatment for","meaning":"是……的良好療法","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not claim that Beethoven’s sonata is a good treatment for disorders.","zh":"文章沒有聲稱貝多芬奏鳴曲是治療障礙的良好療法。"},{"en":"A good treatment for something is a method that helps improve or manage that condition.","zh":"good treatment for something 指有助改善或管理某狀況的方法。"},{"en":"Rest and fluids can be a good treatment for a mild cold.","zh":"休息和補充水分可以是輕微感冒的良好療法。"},{"en":"A treatment should be judged by evidence, not by how pleasant it sounds.","zh":"療法應根據證據判斷，而不是根據它聽起來是否愉快。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a condition with a helpful method.","zh":"這個短語把狀況與有幫助的方法連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"be of little importance","meaning":"不太重要","examples":[{"en":"The statement suggests that technology is of little importance to Sacks.","zh":"該陳述暗示科技對 Sacks 不太重要。"},{"en":"To be of little importance means to matter very little.","zh":"be of little importance 指重要性很低。"},{"en":"A student’s handwriting may be of little importance in an online exam.","zh":"在網上考試中，學生筆跡可能不太重要。"},{"en":"Something can be useful without being central to someone’s main approach.","zh":"某物可以有用，但不一定是某人主要方法的核心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes low importance, not total uselessness.","zh":"這個短語描述重要性低，而不是完全無用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Sacks values technology, although he favours observation compared with high-tech methods.","zh":"Sacks 重視科技，雖然與高科技方法相比，他更偏好觀察。"},{"en":"Compared with means looked at in relation to another thing.","zh":"compared with 指與另一事物放在一起看。"},{"en":"Compared with last year, this class is more confident in speaking.","zh":"與去年相比，這班學生說話更有信心。"},{"en":"Comparisons help show relative strengths and weaknesses.","zh":"比較有助顯示相對優點和弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when judging one thing beside another.","zh":"當把一件事與另一件事並列評價時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"be undervalued","meaning":"被低估","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer describes music therapy as undervalued.","zh":"評論者把音樂治療描述為被低估。"},{"en":"To be undervalued means to be given less respect, attention, or importance than deserved.","zh":"be undervalued 指得到的尊重、關注或重要性低於應得程度。"},{"en":"School librarians are sometimes undervalued despite helping students read.","zh":"學校圖書館主任雖然幫助學生閱讀，有時仍被低估。"},{"en":"An undervalued method may still be very effective in practice.","zh":"被低估的方法在實踐中仍可能非常有效。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something deserves more recognition.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事值得更多認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"show little scepticism","meaning":"表現出很少懷疑精神","examples":[{"en":"Sacks showed little scepticism towards some scientific findings.","zh":"Sacks 對某些科學發現表現出很少懷疑精神。"},{"en":"To show little scepticism means to question something very little.","zh":"show little scepticism 指對某事很少提出質疑。"},{"en":"A student shows little scepticism if they trust every online article.","zh":"如果學生相信每篇網上文章，就是表現出很少懷疑精神。"},{"en":"Little scepticism can make weak evidence seem more reliable than it is.","zh":"懷疑精神不足可以令薄弱證據顯得比實際更可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises a lack of critical questioning.","zh":"這個短語批評缺乏批判性質疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"draw on theories and findings","meaning":"引用理論與研究結果","examples":[{"en":"Sacks draws on scientific theories and findings throughout the book.","zh":"Sacks 貫穿全書引用科學理論與研究結果。"},{"en":"To draw on theories and findings means to use them as support or background.","zh":"draw on theories and findings 指使用理論和研究結果作支持或背景。"},{"en":"A student essay may draw on research findings to support its argument.","zh":"學生作文可能引用研究結果來支持論點。"},{"en":"Using theories helps writers connect cases with wider explanations.","zh":"使用理論幫助作者把個案與更廣泛解釋連起來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using existing knowledge in writing.","zh":"這個短語描述在寫作中使用現有知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"phenomena presented in the book","meaning":"書中所呈現的現象","examples":[{"en":"The theories are used to describe the phenomena presented in the book.","zh":"這些理論被用來描述書中所呈現的現象。"},{"en":"Phenomena presented in the book are the events, behaviours, or conditions the book describes.","zh":"phenomena presented in the book 指書中描述的事件、行為或狀況。"},{"en":"A science textbook may explain the phenomena presented in diagrams and case studies.","zh":"科學教科書可能解釋圖表和個案研究中呈現的現象。"},{"en":"Theories help readers understand why the described phenomena may occur.","zh":"理論幫助讀者理解所描述現象為何可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to the book’s examples and cases.","zh":"這個短語指回書中的例子和個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"be eager to","meaning":"渴望去……","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not suggest that Sacks is eager to adopt new testing methods.","zh":"文章沒有暗示 Sacks 渴望採用新測試方法。"},{"en":"To be eager to do something means to want to do it strongly and willingly.","zh":"be eager to do something 指強烈而樂意地想做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be eager to join the drama club after watching a performance.","zh":"學生看完表演後，可能渴望加入戲劇學會。"},{"en":"Eagerness shows positive desire, not reluctant acceptance.","zh":"渴望顯示正面意願，而不是勉強接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong willingness.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈願意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":23},{"front":"new testing methods","meaning":"新測試方法","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer believes that newer testing methods deserve greater attention.","zh":"評論者認為新測試方法值得更多關注。"},{"en":"New testing methods are recently developed ways to examine or measure a condition.","zh":"new testing methods 指最近發展出來、用於檢查或量度某狀況的方法。"},{"en":"Hospitals may use new testing methods when standard tests do not explain symptoms.","zh":"當標準測試無法解釋症狀，醫院可能使用新測試方法。"},{"en":"New methods can reveal details that older tests miss.","zh":"新方法可以揭示舊測試錯過的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in medical or scientific discussion.","zh":"這個短語常用於醫學或科學討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"complete each sentence","meaning":"完成每句句子","examples":[{"en":"Students complete each sentence with the correct ending.","zh":"學生用正確句末選項完成每句句子。"},{"en":"To complete each sentence means to add the missing ending so the sentence makes sense.","zh":"complete each sentence 指加入缺失句尾，使句子意思完整。"},{"en":"In a reading exercise, students must choose an ending that matches the passage.","zh":"在閱讀練習中，學生必須選擇符合篇章的句尾。"},{"en":"The correct answer must fit both grammar and meaning.","zh":"正確答案必須同時符合文法和意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"the correct ending","meaning":"正確句末選項","examples":[{"en":"Each sentence must be matched with the correct ending.","zh":"每句句子都必須與正確句末選項配對。"},{"en":"The correct ending is the option that completes a sentence accurately.","zh":"correct ending 指能準確完成句子的選項。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole sentence before choosing the correct ending.","zh":"學生應先讀完整句，再選擇正確句末選項。"},{"en":"A wrong ending may sound grammatical but contradict the passage.","zh":"錯誤句尾可能聽起來合文法，但與文章矛盾。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the final part of a sentence-completion answer.","zh":"這個短語指句子完成題答案的最後部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"dissociations between harmony and melody","meaning":"和聲與旋律之間的功能分離","examples":[{"en":"The dissociations between harmony and melody suggest separate brain processes.","zh":"和聲與旋律之間的功能分離暗示分開的大腦過程。"},{"en":"Dissociations between harmony and melody are cases where one musical ability is affected but the other remains.","zh":"dissociations between harmony and melody 指一種音樂能力受影響而另一種仍保留的個案。"},{"en":"A patient may recognise tunes but fail to judge whether chords sound right.","zh":"病人可能辨認旋律，但無法判斷和弦是否正確。"},{"en":"Such dissociations show that music understanding has separable parts.","zh":"這類功能分離顯示音樂理解有可分開的部分。"},{"en":"This phrase links musical symptoms with brain organisation.","zh":"這個短語把音樂症狀與大腦組織連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"the treatment of musical disorders","meaning":"音樂障礙的治療","examples":[{"en":"The treatment of musical disorders can produce inconsistent outcomes.","zh":"音樂障礙的治療可以產生不一致結果。"},{"en":"The treatment of musical disorders means medical or therapeutic attempts to improve music-related conditions.","zh":"treatment of musical disorders 指改善音樂相關狀況的醫療或治療嘗試。"},{"en":"A therapist may use music exercises as part of treatment.","zh":"治療師可能使用音樂練習作為治療一部分。"},{"en":"Outcomes differ because patients and disorders are not all the same.","zh":"結果不同，是因為病人和障礙並不全都一樣。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on helping people with music-related neurological problems.","zh":"這個短語集中於幫助有音樂相關神經問題的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"varied results","meaning":"不同的結果","examples":[{"en":"The evidence indicates that medication can have varied results.","zh":"證據顯示藥物可以有不同的結果。"},{"en":"Varied results are outcomes that differ from case to case.","zh":"varied results 指因個案不同而不同的結果。"},{"en":"A study method may produce varied results among students with different habits.","zh":"一種學習方法可能在習慣不同的學生中產生不同結果。"},{"en":"Varied results make it harder to recommend one solution for everyone.","zh":"結果各異會令人更難向所有人推薦同一方案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inconsistent or diverse outcomes.","zh":"這個短語描述不一致或多樣的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"EEG scans of Sacks’s patients","meaning":"Sacks病人的腦電圖掃描","examples":[{"en":"The EEG scans of Sacks’s patients often appeared normal.","zh":"Sacks 病人的腦電圖掃描常看似正常。"},{"en":"EEG scans of patients are brain-wave tests carried out on those patients.","zh":"EEG scans of patients 指對那些病人進行的腦電波測試。"},{"en":"A doctor may compare EEG scans before and after a seizure.","zh":"醫生可能比較癲癇發作前後的腦電圖掃描。"},{"en":"Normal scans can be puzzling when symptoms are still present.","zh":"當症狀仍存在，正常掃描可能令人困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to medical test results from Sacks’s cases.","zh":"這個短語指 Sacks 個案中的醫學測試結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"show no music-brain disorders","meaning":"顯示沒有音樂與大腦相關障礙","examples":[{"en":"Standard EEG scans may show no music-brain disorders despite clear symptoms.","zh":"即使有清楚症狀，標準腦電圖掃描也可能顯示沒有音樂與大腦相關障礙。"},{"en":"To show no music-brain disorders means not to reveal abnormal brain activity related to musical symptoms.","zh":"show no music-brain disorders 指沒有揭示與音樂症狀相關的異常大腦活動。"},{"en":"A test may show no problem even when a patient still feels unwell.","zh":"即使病人仍覺得不適，測試可能顯示沒有問題。"},{"en":"This can happen when the test is not sensitive enough for the condition.","zh":"當測試對該狀況不夠靈敏時，這種情況可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a limit of standard testing.","zh":"這個短語突出標準測試的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"unravel the mysteries","meaning":"解開謎團","examples":[{"en":"Further research may help the neurological community unravel the mysteries.","zh":"進一步研究可能幫助神經學界解開謎團。"},{"en":"To unravel the mysteries means to explain confusing or unknown things step by step.","zh":"unravel the mysteries 指逐步解釋令人困惑或未知的事情。"},{"en":"Detectives unravel mysteries by collecting clues and testing explanations.","zh":"偵探透過收集線索和測試解釋來解開謎團。"},{"en":"Scientific mysteries become clearer when better evidence is gathered.","zh":"當更好證據被收集，科學謎團會變得更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests solving something complex.","zh":"這個短語暗示解決複雜問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"be key to","meaning":"是……的關鍵","examples":[{"en":"Sensitive testing may be key to understanding music-brain disorders.","zh":"靈敏測試可能是理解音樂與大腦相關障礙的關鍵。"},{"en":"To be key to something means to be very important for achieving or understanding it.","zh":"be key to something 指對達成或理解某事非常重要。"},{"en":"Regular practice is key to improving pronunciation.","zh":"定期練習是改善發音的關鍵。"},{"en":"A key factor can unlock progress when other methods are not enough.","zh":"當其他方法不足時，關鍵因素可以打開進展。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies something essential or highly important.","zh":"這個短語指出必要或非常重要的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":24},{"front":"be used in isolation","meaning":"被單獨使用","examples":[{"en":"New technologies should not be used in isolation from clinical observation.","zh":"新科技不應與臨床觀察分離而被單獨使用。"},{"en":"To be used in isolation means to be used alone, without support from other methods.","zh":"be used in isolation 指單獨使用，而沒有其他方法支持。"},{"en":"A grammar app should not be used in isolation from real speaking practice.","zh":"文法應用程式不應與真實說話練習分離而單獨使用。"},{"en":"Using one method alone can create blind spots.","zh":"單獨使用一種方法可能造成盲點。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that tools work better when combined with other approaches.","zh":"這個短語提醒工具與其他方法結合時效果更好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"a misconception","meaning":"錯誤觀念","examples":[{"en":"The evidence challenges a common misconception about brain organisation.","zh":"證據挑戰關於大腦組織的常見錯誤觀念。"},{"en":"A misconception is a wrong idea that many people believe.","zh":"misconception 指許多人相信的錯誤想法。"},{"en":"It is a misconception that quiet students are always lazy or uninterested.","zh":"認為安靜學生總是懶惰或沒興趣，是錯誤觀念。"},{"en":"Misconceptions persist when simple explanations sound attractive.","zh":"當簡單解釋聽起來吸引，錯誤觀念會持續。"},{"en":"This word is useful when correcting a false belief.","zh":"糾正錯誤信念時，這個字很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":25},{"front":"a single functional centre","meaning":"單一功能中樞","examples":[{"en":"It is a misconception to believe that music has a single functional centre in the brain.","zh":"相信音樂在大腦中有單一功能中樞是一種錯誤觀念。"},{"en":"A single functional centre is one brain area thought to perform a whole function by itself.","zh":"single functional centre 指被認為能獨自完成整個功能的一個大腦區域。"},{"en":"People may wrongly imagine that memory has one single centre in the brain.","zh":"人們可能錯誤想像記憶在大腦中有單一中樞。"},{"en":"Complex abilities often depend on several connected brain regions.","zh":"複雜能力常依賴多個相連的大腦區域。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an oversimplified view of brain organisation.","zh":"這個短語描述對大腦組織的過度簡化看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 160 - Book review on Musicophilia.pdf","sourcePage":25}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 161":[{"front":"What Are Dreams?","meaning":"夢究竟是甚麼？","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines what dreams are and what functions they may serve.","zh":"文章探討夢究竟是甚麼，以及夢可能有甚麼功能。"},{"en":"“What are dreams?” asks what dreams consist of and why they may happen during sleep.","zh":"“What are dreams?” 是在問夢由甚麼構成，以及為何它們可能在睡眠中出現。"},{"en":"A student may ask “What are dreams?” after waking from a strange story-like experience at night.","zh":"學生晚上醒來後記得一段奇怪、像故事般的經驗，可能會問「夢究竟是甚麼？」"},{"en":"If scientists understand what dreams are, they may better understand memory, emotion, and sleep.","zh":"如果科學家了解夢是甚麼，他們可能更理解記憶、情緒和睡眠。"},{"en":"This question is not only about dream images, but also about the possible purpose of dreaming.","zh":"這個問題不只關於夢中的影像，也關於造夢可能有甚麼目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"thousands of years ago","meaning":"數千年前","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of years ago, dreams were interpreted very differently.","zh":"數千年前，人們對夢的解讀非常不同。"},{"en":"Thousands of years ago means a very long time in the ancient past.","zh":"Thousands of years ago 指遠古過去的很長時間以前。"},{"en":"Thousands of years ago, people explained illness, weather, and dreams through religion or myth.","zh":"數千年前，人們透過宗教或神話解釋疾病、天氣和夢。"},{"en":"If a belief began thousands of years ago, it may have changed many times before reaching us today.","zh":"如果一種信念始於數千年前，它傳到今天前可能已改變很多次。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a broad ancient time period, not an exact date.","zh":"這個片語提供一個概括的古代時期，而不是精確日期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be seen as messages from","meaning":"被視為來自……的訊息","examples":[{"en":"Dreams were once seen as messages from the gods.","zh":"夢曾被視為來自神明的訊息。"},{"en":"To be seen as messages from someone means to be understood as communication sent by that person or power.","zh":"To be seen as messages from someone 指被理解為由某人或某種力量傳來的溝通。"},{"en":"In some ancient cultures, unusual events were seen as messages from spirits or ancestors.","zh":"在一些古代文化中，異常事件被視為來自靈魂或祖先的訊息。"},{"en":"If people see dreams as divine messages, they may take them seriously and act on them.","zh":"如果人們把夢視為神聖訊息，他們可能會認真對待並根據夢行事。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how people interpret something as meaningful communication.","zh":"這個片語顯示人們如何把某事解讀為有意義的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the gods","meaning":"神明","examples":[{"en":"Ancient people sometimes believed that the gods communicated through dreams.","zh":"古人有時相信神明透過夢與人溝通。"},{"en":"The gods are divine beings worshipped in religious traditions.","zh":"The gods 是宗教傳統中被崇拜的神聖存在。"},{"en":"In Greek myths, the gods could reward, punish, warn, or guide human beings.","zh":"在希臘神話中，神明可以獎賞、懲罰、警告或引導人類。"},{"en":"If people believed the gods sent dreams, dream interpretation became spiritually important.","zh":"如果人們相信神明傳送夢境，解夢就變得有宗教重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to supernatural beings, not ordinary rulers.","zh":"這個片語指超自然神聖存在，而不是普通統治者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be considered prophetic","meaning":"被視為能預示未來","examples":[{"en":"Dreams are still considered prophetic in some cultures.","zh":"在一些文化中，夢仍被視為能預示未來。"},{"en":"To be considered prophetic means to be believed to predict future events.","zh":"To be considered prophetic 指被相信能預測未來事件。"},{"en":"A dream about danger may be considered prophetic if something similar happens later.","zh":"如果之後發生相似事情，一個關於危險的夢可能被視為能預示未來。"},{"en":"If people think dreams are prophetic, they may use them when making important decisions.","zh":"如果人們認為夢能預示未來，他們可能在作重要決定時參考夢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a belief in future prediction, not scientific certainty.","zh":"這個片語描述對預測未來的信念，而不是科學確定性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ancient Greece","meaning":"古希臘","examples":[{"en":"Dreams played a role in healing practices in ancient Greece.","zh":"夢在古希臘的治療做法中扮演角色。"},{"en":"Ancient Greece means the civilisation of Greek-speaking societies in the ancient world.","zh":"Ancient Greece 指古代世界中說希臘語社會的文明。"},{"en":"Ancient Greece is remembered for philosophy, theatre, medicine, temples, and myths.","zh":"古希臘以哲學、戲劇、醫學、神廟和神話著稱。"},{"en":"If a custom came from ancient Greece, it may show how early Europeans understood health or religion.","zh":"如果一種習俗來自古希臘，它可能顯示早期歐洲人如何理解健康或宗教。"},{"en":"This phrase places an idea in an old Greek historical setting.","zh":"這個片語把某想法放在古希臘歷史背景中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sleep at the temples of","meaning":"睡在……的神廟","examples":[{"en":"Sick people slept at the temples of Asclepius.","zh":"病人睡在阿斯克勒庇俄斯的神廟。"},{"en":"To sleep at the temples of a god means to stay overnight in a sacred place connected with that god.","zh":"To sleep at the temples of a god 指在與某神明相關的神聖場所過夜。"},{"en":"Ancient patients might sleep at a temple because they hoped for guidance or healing.","zh":"古代病人可能睡在神廟，因為他們希望得到指引或治療。"},{"en":"If people believed a temple was holy, sleeping there could become part of a healing ritual.","zh":"如果人們相信神廟是神聖的，在那裡睡覺就可能成為治療儀式的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a religious practice linked with illness and dreams.","zh":"這個片語描述與疾病和夢相關的宗教做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the god of medicine","meaning":"醫藥之神","examples":[{"en":"Asclepius was worshipped as the god of medicine.","zh":"阿斯克勒庇俄斯被崇拜為醫藥之神。"},{"en":"The god of medicine is a divine figure believed to have power over healing and health.","zh":"The god of medicine 是被相信掌管治療和健康的神明。"},{"en":"In a myth-based society, sick people might pray to the god of medicine for recovery.","zh":"在以神話為基礎的社會中，病人可能向醫藥之神祈求康復。"},{"en":"If a god is linked with medicine, temples to that god may become places of healing.","zh":"如果某神明與醫藥有關，供奉該神的神廟可能成為治療場所。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a god by the area of life he controls.","zh":"這個片語透過某神明掌管的生活範疇來識別他。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in order to receive","meaning":"為了得到……","examples":[{"en":"Patients slept in the temple in order to receive healing dreams.","zh":"病人睡在神廟中，為了得到具有治療作用的夢。"},{"en":"In order to receive something means for the purpose of getting it.","zh":"In order to receive something 指為了取得某物。"},{"en":"A student may join a workshop in order to receive feedback on writing.","zh":"學生可能參加工作坊，為了得到寫作回饋。"},{"en":"If people sleep in a temple in order to receive dreams, the dream is the hoped-for result.","zh":"如果人們睡在神廟中是為了得到夢境，那個夢就是期望的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links an action with its intended benefit.","zh":"這個片語清楚連接行動與預期好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"healing dreams","meaning":"具有治療作用的夢","examples":[{"en":"Ancient Greeks believed that healing dreams could restore health.","zh":"古希臘人相信具有治療作用的夢可以恢復健康。"},{"en":"Healing dreams are dreams believed to help a sick person recover or understand how to recover.","zh":"Healing dreams 是被相信能幫助病人康復或理解如何康復的夢。"},{"en":"A patient might hope for a healing dream that shows which treatment to follow.","zh":"病人可能希望得到一個具有治療作用的夢，顯示應採取哪種治療。"},{"en":"If people believe dreams can heal, they may treat sleep as part of medicine.","zh":"如果人們相信夢可以治病，他們可能把睡眠視為醫學的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dreams linked with recovery, not ordinary night-time images.","zh":"這個片語描述與康復有關的夢，而不是普通夜間影像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"modern dream science","meaning":"現代夢境科學","examples":[{"en":"Modern dream science began to develop in the late nineteenth century.","zh":"現代夢境科學在19世紀末開始發展。"},{"en":"Modern dream science is the scientific study of dreams using psychology, biology, and sleep research.","zh":"Modern dream science 是使用心理學、生物學和睡眠研究來科學研究夢。"},{"en":"Researchers in modern dream science may study brain activity while people sleep.","zh":"現代夢境科學的研究人員可能研究人睡覺時的大腦活動。"},{"en":"If dream science uses experiments and brain scans, it moves beyond myth and guesswork.","zh":"如果夢境科學使用實驗和腦掃描，它就超越神話和猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to scientific investigation of dreams, not traditional dream interpretation.","zh":"這個片語指對夢的科學研究，而不是傳統解夢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at the end of the 19th century","meaning":"在19世紀末","examples":[{"en":"Freud developed his theories at the end of the nineteenth century.","zh":"佛洛伊德在19世紀末發展他的理論。"},{"en":"At the end of the 19th century means during the final years of the 1800s.","zh":"At the end of the 19th century 指1800年代的最後幾年。"},{"en":"Many scientific and medical ideas changed at the end of the 19th century.","zh":"許多科學和醫學想法在19世紀末改變。"},{"en":"If a theory appeared at the end of the 19th century, it came before modern brain-scanning technology.","zh":"如果一個理論在19世紀末出現，它早於現代腦掃描技術。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a historical time near the late 1800s.","zh":"這個片語提供接近1800年代後期的歷史時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"theorise that","meaning":"提出理論認為","examples":[{"en":"Freud theorised that dreams expressed unconscious desires.","zh":"佛洛伊德提出理論認為夢表達潛意識慾望。"},{"en":"To theorise that something is true means to suggest an explanation based on ideas or evidence.","zh":"To theorise that something is true 指根據想法或證據提出解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may theorise that students are tired because they study too late.","zh":"老師可能提出理論認為學生疲倦是因為溫習太晚。"},{"en":"If scientists theorise about dreams, they are trying to explain a hidden mental process.","zh":"如果科學家對夢提出理論，他們是在嘗試解釋隱藏的心理過程。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a proposed explanation, not necessarily a proven fact.","zh":"這個片語引出一個提出的解釋，而不一定是已證實事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the expression of","meaning":"……的表現","examples":[{"en":"He regarded dreams as the expression of hidden desires.","zh":"他把夢視為隱藏慾望的表現。"},{"en":"The expression of something is the way a feeling, idea, or wish is shown.","zh":"The expression of something 是感受、想法或願望被顯示出來的方式。"},{"en":"Crying can be the expression of sadness, pain, or relief.","zh":"哭泣可以是悲傷、痛苦或鬆一口氣的表現。"},{"en":"If dreams are the expression of hidden wishes, they may reveal feelings people do not admit when awake.","zh":"如果夢是隱藏願望的表現，它們可能揭示人清醒時不承認的感受。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an inner state with an outward form.","zh":"這個片語把內在狀態與外在形式連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"unconscious desires","meaning":"潛意識慾望","examples":[{"en":"Freud believed that dreams revealed unconscious desires.","zh":"佛洛伊德相信夢揭示潛意識慾望。"},{"en":"Unconscious desires are wishes or drives that exist in the mind without full awareness.","zh":"Unconscious desires 是存在於心中但沒有完全意識到的願望或驅力。"},{"en":"A person may not realise that their fear of failure is linked to an unconscious desire for approval.","zh":"一個人可能沒有意識到自己對失敗的恐懼與渴望被認可的潛意識慾望有關。"},{"en":"If dreams express unconscious desires, analysing them may help uncover hidden feelings.","zh":"如果夢表達潛意識慾望，分析夢可能幫助揭示隱藏感受。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to wishes below conscious awareness.","zh":"這個片語指低於意識察覺的願望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stem from childhood","meaning":"源自童年","examples":[{"en":"Some emotional difficulties may stem from childhood experiences.","zh":"一些情緒困難可能源自童年經歷。"},{"en":"To stem from childhood means to originate in events, relationships, or feelings from early life.","zh":"To stem from childhood 指源於早年生活中的事件、關係或感受。"},{"en":"A fear of speaking in class may stem from childhood embarrassment.","zh":"害怕在課堂上說話可能源自童年時的尷尬經驗。"},{"en":"If an adult problem stems from childhood, therapy may explore early memories.","zh":"如果成人問題源自童年，治療可能探索早期記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase points to childhood as the source of a later issue.","zh":"這個片語指出童年是後來問題的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hidden emotions","meaning":"隱藏的情緒","examples":[{"en":"Psychoanalysis attempts to uncover hidden emotions.","zh":"精神分析嘗試揭示隱藏的情緒。"},{"en":"Hidden emotions are feelings that a person has but does not clearly recognise or express.","zh":"Hidden emotions 是一個人擁有但沒有清楚認出或表達的感受。"},{"en":"A student may show anger, but the hidden emotion may be fear of failing.","zh":"學生可能表現出憤怒，但隱藏的情緒可能是害怕失敗。"},{"en":"If hidden emotions are ignored, they may appear later as stress, dreams, or conflict.","zh":"如果隱藏的情緒被忽視，它們可能之後以壓力、夢或衝突形式出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes feelings beneath the surface.","zh":"這個片語描述表面之下的感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"through analysis","meaning":"透過分析","examples":[{"en":"Freud believed that hidden feelings could be explored through analysis.","zh":"佛洛伊德相信隱藏感受可以透過分析被探索。"},{"en":"Through analysis means by carefully studying and interpreting details.","zh":"Through analysis 指透過仔細研究和解讀細節。"},{"en":"A teacher can understand a student’s writing problems through analysis of repeated mistakes.","zh":"老師可以透過分析反覆錯誤，了解學生的寫作問題。"},{"en":"If therapists examine dreams through analysis, they look for patterns and meanings.","zh":"如果治療師透過分析檢視夢，他們會尋找模式和意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using careful examination as the method.","zh":"這個片語描述使用仔細檢視作為方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cure mental illness","meaning":"治療精神疾病","examples":[{"en":"He hoped that dream analysis could help cure mental illness.","zh":"他希望夢境分析可以幫助治療精神疾病。"},{"en":"To cure mental illness means to remove or successfully treat a serious problem affecting the mind.","zh":"To cure mental illness 指消除或成功治療影響心理的嚴重問題。"},{"en":"Counselling, medication, and support may help people manage or recover from mental illness.","zh":"輔導、藥物和支援可能幫助人管理或從精神疾病中康復。"},{"en":"If a treatment cures an illness, symptoms should reduce or disappear in a lasting way.","zh":"如果一種治療能治癒疾病，症狀應持久減少或消失。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than “help”; it suggests full recovery or effective treatment.","zh":"這個片語比 “help” 更強，暗示完全康復或有效治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Freudian model","meaning":"佛洛伊德理論模式","examples":[{"en":"The Freudian model influenced psychology for many decades.","zh":"佛洛伊德理論模式影響心理學數十年。"},{"en":"The Freudian model is Freud’s way of explaining the mind through unconscious desires, childhood experiences, and analysis.","zh":"Freudian model 是佛洛伊德透過潛意識慾望、童年經驗和分析來解釋心智的方法。"},{"en":"A therapist using a Freudian model may ask about dreams and early family memories.","zh":"使用佛洛伊德理論模式的治療師，可能會詢問夢境和早期家庭記憶。"},{"en":"If a model becomes influential, later psychologists may accept, revise, or reject it.","zh":"如果一個模式變得有影響力，後來的心理學家可能接受、修訂或拒絕它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to Freud’s theoretical framework.","zh":"這個片語指佛洛伊德的理論框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"psychoanalysis","meaning":"精神分析","examples":[{"en":"Psychoanalysis explores unconscious thoughts and emotional conflicts.","zh":"精神分析探索潛意識思想和情緒衝突。"},{"en":"Psychoanalysis is a form of therapy and theory that examines hidden thoughts, desires, dreams, and childhood experiences.","zh":"Psychoanalysis 是一種治療和理論，研究隱藏思想、慾望、夢和童年經驗。"},{"en":"In psychoanalysis, a patient may talk freely while the therapist listens for deeper patterns.","zh":"在精神分析中，病人可能自由談話，而治療師聆聽更深層模式。"},{"en":"If unconscious conflicts affect behaviour, psychoanalysis tries to bring them into awareness.","zh":"如果潛意識衝突影響行為，精神分析嘗試把它們帶入意識。"},{"en":"This word refers to Freud’s tradition of exploring the hidden mind.","zh":"這個詞指佛洛伊德傳統中對隱藏心智的探索。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"dominate until","meaning":"一直主導至……","examples":[{"en":"The Freudian model dominated until the 1970s.","zh":"佛洛伊德理論模式一直主導至1970年代。"},{"en":"To dominate until a time means to remain the main influence up to that point.","zh":"To dominate until a time 指一直到某時間點仍保持主要影響力。"},{"en":"A traditional teaching method may dominate until new technology changes classroom practice.","zh":"傳統教學方法可能一直主導至新科技改變課堂做法。"},{"en":"If one theory dominates for decades, students may learn it before alternative explanations.","zh":"如果一個理論主導數十年，學生可能先學到它，再學其他解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase shows long-lasting control or influence before a change.","zh":"這個片語顯示改變前長期的控制或影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"research into","meaning":"對……的研究","examples":[{"en":"New research into brain chemistry challenged earlier psychological theories.","zh":"對大腦化學作用的新研究挑戰了早期心理學理論。"},{"en":"Research into something means careful study of that topic.","zh":"Research into something 指對某主題的仔細研究。"},{"en":"Research into student sleep can help schools design better timetables.","zh":"對學生睡眠的研究可以幫助學校設計更好時間表。"},{"en":"If research into the brain produces new evidence, old ideas about dreams may change.","zh":"如果對大腦的研究產生新證據，關於夢的舊想法可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the subject being studied.","zh":"這個片語引出被研究的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"chemistry of the brain","meaning":"大腦化學作用","examples":[{"en":"Scientists began to study the chemistry of the brain.","zh":"科學家開始研究大腦化學作用。"},{"en":"The chemistry of the brain means the chemicals and chemical processes that affect brain function.","zh":"Chemistry of the brain 指影響大腦功能的化學物質和化學過程。"},{"en":"Brain chemistry can influence mood, sleep, attention, and memory.","zh":"大腦化學作用可以影響情緒、睡眠、注意力和記憶。"},{"en":"If brain chemistry changes, a person may feel anxious, depressed, or unusually energetic.","zh":"如果大腦化學作用改變，一個人可能感到焦慮、抑鬱或異常精力充沛。"},{"en":"This phrase explains mental life partly through biological processes.","zh":"這個片語透過生物過程部分解釋心理生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"emotional problems","meaning":"情緒問題","examples":[{"en":"Emotional problems may have several different causes.","zh":"情緒問題可能有幾種不同原因。"},{"en":"Emotional problems are difficulties with feelings, mood, stress, fear, anger, or sadness.","zh":"Emotional problems 是與感受、心情、壓力、恐懼、憤怒或悲傷有關的困難。"},{"en":"A student may have emotional problems after bullying, family conflict, or exam pressure.","zh":"學生在受欺凌、家庭衝突或考試壓力後，可能出現情緒問題。"},{"en":"If emotional problems are not addressed, they may affect sleep, study, and relationships.","zh":"如果情緒問題沒有得到處理，它們可能影響睡眠、學習和人際關係。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental and feeling-based difficulties, not ordinary bad moods only.","zh":"這個片語描述心理和情感上的困難，而不只是普通壞心情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"biological or chemical roots","meaning":"生物或化學根源","examples":[{"en":"Some emotional disorders have biological or chemical roots.","zh":"一些情緒障礙有生物或化學根源。"},{"en":"Biological or chemical roots are causes connected with the body, brain, genes, hormones, or brain chemicals.","zh":"Biological or chemical roots 是與身體、大腦、基因、荷爾蒙或大腦化學物質有關的原因。"},{"en":"A person’s depression may have chemical roots if medication helps correct brain imbalance.","zh":"如果藥物幫助糾正大腦失衡，一個人的抑鬱可能有化學根源。"},{"en":"If a problem has biological roots, blaming only childhood may be too simple.","zh":"如果問題有生物根源，只責怪童年可能過於簡單。"},{"en":"This phrase points to physical causes behind mental or emotional problems.","zh":"這個片語指出心理或情緒問題背後的身體原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"environmental causes","meaning":"環境因素","examples":[{"en":"Emotional problems may have environmental causes as well.","zh":"情緒問題也可能有環境因素。"},{"en":"Environmental causes are outside factors in a person’s surroundings that contribute to a problem.","zh":"Environmental causes 是一個人周圍環境中促成問題的外在因素。"},{"en":"Noise, poverty, family stress, and unsafe housing can be environmental causes of poor sleep.","zh":"噪音、貧窮、家庭壓力和不安全住屋都可以是睡眠差的環境因素。"},{"en":"If a child grows up under constant pressure, the environment may affect emotional health.","zh":"如果孩子在持續壓力下長大，環境可能影響情緒健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes causes outside the body or brain chemistry.","zh":"這個片語描述身體或大腦化學作用以外的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"以及；也有……","examples":[{"en":"Mental illness may have biological causes as well as environmental ones.","zh":"精神疾病可能有生物原因，以及環境原因。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to, so it adds another item or cause.","zh":"As well as 指「除此之外也有」，所以它加入另一項或另一個原因。"},{"en":"Good language learning needs listening practice as well as grammar study.","zh":"良好語言學習需要聆聽練習，也需要文法學習。"},{"en":"If an illness has chemical causes as well as life-stress causes, treatment may need several approaches.","zh":"如果一種疾病有化學原因，也有生活壓力原因，治療可能需要幾種方法。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two things are both included.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩件事都被包括。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in other words","meaning":"換句話說","examples":[{"en":"In other words, emotional illness cannot always be blamed on childhood.","zh":"換句話說，情緒疾病不能總是歸咎於童年。"},{"en":"In other words introduces the same idea again in a clearer or simpler way.","zh":"In other words 用更清楚或更簡單的方式再次表達同一想法。"},{"en":"The bus is cheaper and faster; in other words, it is the better choice for this trip.","zh":"巴士更便宜也更快；換句話說，它是這次旅程更好的選擇。"},{"en":"If a writer says “in other words”, they are helping readers understand the point more directly.","zh":"如果作者說 “in other words”，他是在幫助讀者更直接理解重點。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for restating a conclusion.","zh":"這個片語適合用來重新表達結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"not just because of","meaning":"不只是因為……","examples":[{"en":"People may become ill not just because of past experiences.","zh":"人們可能生病，不只是因為過去經歷。"},{"en":"Not just because of means not only caused by one reason, but also by other reasons.","zh":"Not just because of 指不只由一個原因造成，也由其他原因造成。"},{"en":"A student may fail a test not just because of laziness, but because of poor sleep and unclear teaching.","zh":"學生考試不合格不只是因為懶惰，也可能因睡眠差和教學不清。"},{"en":"If depression happens not just because of childhood, biology and environment must also be considered.","zh":"如果抑鬱不只是因為童年，生物和環境也必須被考慮。"},{"en":"This phrase prevents an explanation from becoming too narrow.","zh":"這個片語避免解釋變得過於狹窄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"chemical imbalance","meaning":"化學物質失衡","examples":[{"en":"Some mental illnesses may involve a chemical imbalance.","zh":"一些精神疾病可能涉及化學物質失衡。"},{"en":"A chemical imbalance is an unhealthy difference in the level or activity of chemicals in the brain or body.","zh":"Chemical imbalance 是大腦或身體中化學物質水平或活動的不健康差異。"},{"en":"Doctors may consider chemical imbalance when a patient’s mood changes severely without an obvious event.","zh":"當病人心情在沒有明顯事件下嚴重改變，醫生可能考慮化學物質失衡。"},{"en":"If medication corrects a chemical imbalance, symptoms may become easier to manage.","zh":"如果藥物糾正化學物質失衡，症狀可能變得較容易管理。"},{"en":"This phrase links mental illness with biology, not weakness of character.","zh":"這個片語把精神疾病與生物學連接，而不是與性格軟弱連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be cured with medication","meaning":"以藥物治療","examples":[{"en":"Certain disorders may be treated or controlled with medication.","zh":"某些疾病可以用藥物治療或控制。"},{"en":"To be cured with medication means to be successfully treated by drugs prescribed for the condition.","zh":"To be cured with medication 指透過為該病處方的藥物成功治療。"},{"en":"Some infections can be cured with medication when antibiotics are used correctly.","zh":"一些感染如果正確使用抗生素，可以用藥物治癒。"},{"en":"If symptoms have a chemical cause, medication may reduce them more effectively than talking alone.","zh":"如果症狀有化學原因，藥物可能比單靠談話更有效減少症狀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes drug treatment, though not every illness can be fully cured this way.","zh":"這個片語描述藥物治療，但並非每種疾病都能如此完全治癒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the most important event in","meaning":"……中最重要的事件","examples":[{"en":"The discovery of REM sleep was a major event in dream science.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠的發現是夢境科學中的重大事件。"},{"en":"The most important event in a field is the event that changes understanding more than others.","zh":"The most important event in a field 是比其他事件更大程度改變理解的事件。"},{"en":"The invention of the microscope was one of the most important events in biology.","zh":"顯微鏡的發明是生物學中最重要的事件之一。"},{"en":"If an event allows scientists to measure sleep directly, it can transform dream research.","zh":"如果一個事件讓科學家能直接量度睡眠，它可以改變夢境研究。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a turning point in a subject.","zh":"這個片語突顯某學科中的轉捩點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the discovery of","meaning":"……的發現","examples":[{"en":"The discovery of REM sleep transformed the study of dreams.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠的發現改變了夢的研究。"},{"en":"The discovery of something means the act of finding or identifying it for the first time.","zh":"The discovery of something 指首次發現或識別某事物的行動。"},{"en":"The discovery of bacteria changed how doctors understood disease.","zh":"細菌的發現改變了醫生對疾病的理解。"},{"en":"If researchers make a discovery, old explanations may need to be revised.","zh":"如果研究人員有新發現，舊解釋可能需要修訂。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces something newly found or recognised.","zh":"這個片語引出新被發現或認識的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a phase of sleep","meaning":"睡眠階段","examples":[{"en":"REM is a distinctive phase of sleep.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠是一個獨特的睡眠階段。"},{"en":"A phase of sleep is a stage or period within the sleep cycle.","zh":"A phase of sleep 是睡眠週期中的一個階段或時期。"},{"en":"Deep sleep is a phase of sleep when the body rests and repairs itself.","zh":"深層睡眠是一個身體休息和修復自身的睡眠階段。"},{"en":"If scientists identify different sleep phases, they can study what happens in each one.","zh":"如果科學家識別不同睡眠階段，他們可以研究每個階段發生甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one part of the sleeping process.","zh":"這個片語描述睡眠過程中的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be characterised by","meaning":"以……為特徵","examples":[{"en":"REM sleep is characterised by intense brain activity.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠以強烈的大腦活動為特徵。"},{"en":"To be characterised by something means to have it as a main feature.","zh":"To be characterised by something 指以某事作為主要特徵。"},{"en":"A good classroom is characterised by clear rules, active students, and respectful discussion.","zh":"好課室以清晰規則、活躍學生和尊重討論為特徵。"},{"en":"If a sleep stage is characterised by rapid eye movement, that feature helps identify it.","zh":"如果一個睡眠階段以快速眼動為特徵，該特徵就幫助識別它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the defining qualities of something.","zh":"這個片語描述某事物的定義性特質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"intense brain activity","meaning":"強烈的大腦活動","examples":[{"en":"REM sleep involves intense brain activity.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠涉及強烈的大腦活動。"},{"en":"Intense brain activity means the brain is working strongly and actively.","zh":"Intense brain activity 指大腦強烈而活躍地運作。"},{"en":"Solving a difficult maths problem may involve intense brain activity.","zh":"解一道困難數學題可能涉及強烈的大腦活動。"},{"en":"If brain activity is intense during sleep, the brain is not simply switched off.","zh":"如果睡眠期間大腦活動強烈，大腦就不是單純關機。"},{"en":"This phrase describes high mental or neurological activity.","zh":"這個片語描述高度心理或神經活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rapid eye movement","meaning":"快速眼動","examples":[{"en":"REM stands for rapid eye movement.","zh":"REM 代表快速眼動。"},{"en":"Rapid eye movement is the quick movement of the eyes during a particular stage of sleep.","zh":"Rapid eye movement 是眼睛在某一睡眠階段中快速移動。"},{"en":"Scientists may observe rapid eye movement to identify when a sleeper is in REM sleep.","zh":"科學家可能觀察快速眼動，以識別睡眠者是否處於快速眼動睡眠。"},{"en":"If rapid eye movement appears, researchers may expect vivid dreaming to be more likely.","zh":"如果出現快速眼動，研究人員可能預期鮮明夢境較可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is the full form behind the abbreviation REM.","zh":"這個片語是縮寫 REM 的完整形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be awakened in the midst of","meaning":"在……期間被喚醒","examples":[{"en":"Participants were awakened in the midst of REM sleep.","zh":"參加者在快速眼動睡眠期間被喚醒。"},{"en":"To be awakened in the midst of something means to be woken up while it is still happening.","zh":"To be awakened in the midst of something 指在某事仍在發生時被叫醒。"},{"en":"A child may be awakened in the midst of a storm by loud thunder.","zh":"孩子可能在暴風雨期間被響亮雷聲吵醒。"},{"en":"If sleepers are awakened during REM, they may remember dreams more clearly.","zh":"如果睡眠者在快速眼動睡眠期間被喚醒，他們可能更清楚記得夢。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises interruption during an ongoing process.","zh":"這個片語強調在持續過程中被打斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"vivid dreams","meaning":"鮮明的夢境","examples":[{"en":"People awakened during REM often reported vivid dreams.","zh":"在快速眼動睡眠期間被喚醒的人常報告鮮明的夢境。"},{"en":"Vivid dreams are dreams that feel clear, detailed, colourful, or emotionally strong.","zh":"Vivid dreams 是感覺清晰、細緻、色彩鮮明或情緒強烈的夢。"},{"en":"A vivid dream may feel so real that a person remembers it all morning.","zh":"鮮明的夢境可能真實得令人整個早上都記得。"},{"en":"If a dream is vivid, the sleeper may describe places, people, and feelings in detail.","zh":"如果夢很鮮明，睡眠者可能詳細描述地方、人物和感受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dreams that are easy to picture and remember.","zh":"這個片語描述容易想像和記住的夢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lead researchers to conclude that","meaning":"令研究人員得出……的結論","examples":[{"en":"The reports led researchers to conclude that REM was linked to dreaming.","zh":"這些報告令研究人員得出快速眼動睡眠與造夢有關的結論。"},{"en":"To lead researchers to conclude that means to provide evidence that makes researchers reach a judgment.","zh":"To lead researchers to conclude that 指提供證據，使研究人員作出判斷。"},{"en":"Repeated test results may lead teachers to conclude that students need more practice.","zh":"反覆測驗結果可能令老師得出學生需要更多練習的結論。"},{"en":"If many sleepers report dreams after REM, researchers may connect REM with dreaming.","zh":"如果許多睡眠者在快速眼動睡眠後報告有夢，研究人員可能把快速眼動睡眠與造夢連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how evidence produces a scientific conclusion.","zh":"這個片語顯示證據如何產生科學結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"most dreaming took place during","meaning":"大部分造夢發生在……期間","examples":[{"en":"Researchers initially believed that most dreaming took place during REM sleep.","zh":"研究人員最初相信大部分造夢發生在快速眼動睡眠期間。"},{"en":"Most dreaming took place during a period means the majority of dreams happened in that stage or time.","zh":"Most dreaming took place during a period 指大多數夢在該階段或時間發生。"},{"en":"If most revision takes place during weekends, weekday study may be limited.","zh":"如果大部分溫習發生在週末，平日學習可能有限。"},{"en":"If most dreaming happens in REM sleep, scientists will focus on that sleep stage.","zh":"如果大部分造夢發生在快速眼動睡眠期間，科學家就會集中研究該睡眠階段。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an activity with the main time it occurs.","zh":"這個片語把活動與其主要發生時間連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"electroencephalograph","meaning":"腦電圖儀","examples":[{"en":"An electroencephalograph records electrical activity in the brain.","zh":"腦電圖儀記錄大腦中的電活動。"},{"en":"An electroencephalograph is a machine that measures the brain’s electrical signals.","zh":"Electroencephalograph 是量度大腦電訊號的機器。"},{"en":"Doctors may use an electroencephalograph when they need to study sleep or seizures.","zh":"醫生需要研究睡眠或癲癇發作時，可能使用腦電圖儀。"},{"en":"If the machine records unusual patterns, researchers can compare different stages of sleep.","zh":"如果機器記錄到異常模式，研究人員可以比較不同睡眠階段。"},{"en":"This word refers to equipment for measuring brain activity.","zh":"這個詞指量度大腦活動的設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"EEG","meaning":"腦電圖","examples":[{"en":"Researchers used EEG equipment to examine sleeping brains.","zh":"研究人員使用腦電圖設備檢查睡眠中的大腦。"},{"en":"EEG is a method of recording electrical activity in the brain, often through sensors on the head.","zh":"EEG 是記錄大腦電活動的方法，通常透過頭部感應器進行。"},{"en":"A sleep laboratory may use EEG to identify when a person enters REM sleep.","zh":"睡眠實驗室可能使用腦電圖識別一個人何時進入快速眼動睡眠。"},{"en":"If EEG patterns change, scientists can tell that the brain has entered a different state.","zh":"如果腦電圖模式改變，科學家就能知道大腦進入不同狀態。"},{"en":"This abbreviation is commonly used in sleep and brain research.","zh":"這個縮寫常用於睡眠和大腦研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"resemble that of","meaning":"與……的情況相似","examples":[{"en":"Brain activity during REM resembles that of the waking brain.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠期間的大腦活動與清醒大腦的情況相似。"},{"en":"To resemble that of something means to be similar to the pattern or condition of that thing.","zh":"To resemble that of something 指與某事物的模式或狀態相似。"},{"en":"A child’s handwriting may resemble that of an older sibling.","zh":"孩子的字跡可能與哥哥或姐姐的字跡相似。"},{"en":"If a sleeping brain resembles a waking brain, sleep is more active than it looks.","zh":"如果睡眠中的大腦與清醒大腦相似，睡眠就比表面看來更活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase compares one state with another.","zh":"這個片語把一種狀態與另一種狀態比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the waking brain","meaning":"清醒時的大腦","examples":[{"en":"The REM brain can be almost as active as the waking brain.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠中的大腦可以幾乎像清醒時的大腦一樣活躍。"},{"en":"The waking brain is the brain when a person is awake and conscious.","zh":"The waking brain 是人在清醒和有意識時的大腦。"},{"en":"The waking brain helps people talk, plan, notice danger, and solve problems.","zh":"清醒時的大腦幫助人說話、計劃、察覺危險和解決問題。"},{"en":"If the sleeping brain is as active as the waking brain, dreams may involve complex mental work.","zh":"如果睡眠中的大腦像清醒時的大腦一樣活躍，夢可能涉及複雜心理工作。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the awake brain with the sleeping brain.","zh":"這個片語把清醒大腦與睡眠大腦作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a lot more was going on","meaning":"當時發生的事情比想像中更多","examples":[{"en":"The findings showed that a lot more was going on during sleep than expected.","zh":"這些發現顯示，睡眠期間發生的事情比預期多得多。"},{"en":"A lot more was going on means much more activity or complexity was happening than people realised.","zh":"A lot more was going on 指發生的活動或複雜情況比人們意識到的多很多。"},{"en":"A quiet classroom may look calm, but a lot more is going on if students are thinking hard.","zh":"安靜課室可能看起來平靜，但如果學生正在努力思考，實際上發生的事情比表面更多。"},{"en":"If brain scans show strong activity during sleep, sleep is not simply rest.","zh":"如果腦掃描顯示睡眠期間有強烈活動，睡眠就不只是休息。"},{"en":"This phrase reveals hidden activity behind an apparently quiet situation.","zh":"這個片語揭示表面安靜情況背後的隱藏活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"anyone had suspected","meaning":"任何人先前所猜想的","examples":[{"en":"Night-time brain activity was greater than anyone had suspected.","zh":"夜間大腦活動比任何人先前所猜想的更大。"},{"en":"Anyone had suspected means any person had previously guessed, believed, or expected.","zh":"Anyone had suspected 指任何人先前猜測、相信或預期的情況。"},{"en":"The repair cost was higher than anyone had suspected before the mechanic opened the engine.","zh":"在機械師打開引擎前，維修費比任何人先前所猜想的更高。"},{"en":"If sleep is more active than anyone suspected, old ideas about rest may be wrong.","zh":"如果睡眠比任何人先前所猜想的更活躍，關於休息的舊想法可能是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase shows surprise because reality exceeds earlier expectations.","zh":"這個片語顯示現實超出早前預期，因此令人驚訝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"do not know for sure","meaning":"仍未能確定","examples":[{"en":"Scientists still do not know for sure why people dream.","zh":"科學家仍未能確定人為何會造夢。"},{"en":"To not know for sure means to lack complete certainty.","zh":"To not know for sure 指缺乏完全確定性。"},{"en":"A doctor may not know for sure what caused a headache until test results arrive.","zh":"在檢查結果到來前，醫生可能仍未能確定頭痛原因。"},{"en":"If scientists do not know for sure, they may suggest theories rather than final answers.","zh":"如果科學家仍未能確定，他們可能提出理論，而不是最終答案。"},{"en":"This phrase shows uncertainty in a careful and honest way.","zh":"這個片語以謹慎而誠實的方式顯示不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have lots of theories","meaning":"有很多理論","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have lots of theories but no final answer.","zh":"研究人員有很多理論，但沒有最終答案。"},{"en":"To have lots of theories means to have many possible explanations.","zh":"To have lots of theories 指有許多可能解釋。"},{"en":"Students may have lots of theories about why a classmate is absent, but only the teacher knows the reason.","zh":"學生可能對同學為何缺席有很多理論，但只有老師知道原因。"},{"en":"If evidence is incomplete, researchers may keep several theories open.","zh":"如果證據不完整，研究人員可能保留幾種理論。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that there are many ideas, but not necessarily proof.","zh":"這個片語顯示有許多想法，但不一定有證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"on one side are","meaning":"一方是……","examples":[{"en":"On one side are scientists who regard dreams as random activity.","zh":"一方是把夢視為隨機活動的科學家。"},{"en":"On one side are introduces one group or position in a debate.","zh":"On one side are 用來引出辯論中的一個群體或立場。"},{"en":"On one side are parents who want more homework; on the other are students who need more rest.","zh":"一方是想要更多功課的家長；另一方是需要更多休息的學生。"},{"en":"If a writer says “on one side are”, a contrasting view will often follow.","zh":"如果作者說 “on one side are”，之後通常會有相反觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise opposing opinions.","zh":"這個片語幫助組織對立意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"essentially random","meaning":"基本上是隨機的","examples":[{"en":"Hobson believed that dreams were essentially random.","zh":"Hobson相信夢基本上是隨機的。"},{"en":"Essentially random means basically without clear order, purpose, or planned meaning.","zh":"Essentially random 指基本上沒有清晰次序、目的或預定意義。"},{"en":"A teacher may say guesses are essentially random if students answer without reading the passage.","zh":"如果學生沒有閱讀文章就作答，老師可能說那些答案基本上是隨機猜測。"},{"en":"If dreams are essentially random, they may not need deep symbolic interpretation.","zh":"如果夢基本上是隨機的，它們可能不需要深層象徵解讀。"},{"en":"This phrase means “mainly random”, even if some patterns still appear.","zh":"這個片語意思是「主要是隨機」，即使仍可能有一些模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"colleague","meaning":"同事；研究拍檔","examples":[{"en":"Hobson developed the theory with his colleague Robert McCarley.","zh":"Hobson與他的同事Robert McCarley共同發展該理論。"},{"en":"A colleague is someone you work with, especially in the same organisation or field.","zh":"Colleague 是與你一起工作的人，尤其在同一機構或領域中。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask a colleague to review a worksheet before using it in class.","zh":"老師可能請同事在課堂使用前檢查工作紙。"},{"en":"If researchers work with colleagues, they can share ideas, data, and criticism.","zh":"如果研究人員與同事合作，他們可以分享想法、數據和批評。"},{"en":"This word refers to a work partner, not necessarily a close friend.","zh":"這個詞指工作拍檔，而不一定是親密朋友。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"activation-synthesis hypothesis","meaning":"活化合成假說","examples":[{"en":"The activation-synthesis hypothesis explains dreams as the brain’s response to random signals.","zh":"活化合成假說把夢解釋為大腦對隨機訊號的反應。"},{"en":"The activation-synthesis hypothesis is a theory that dreams are created when the brain tries to make sense of random nerve activity.","zh":"Activation-synthesis hypothesis 是一個理論，認為夢是大腦嘗試理解隨機神經活動時產生的。"},{"en":"Under this theory, a strange dream may come from the brain building a story from scattered signals.","zh":"根據這個理論，奇怪的夢可能來自大腦把零散訊號組成故事。"},{"en":"If the theory is right, dreams may not begin as hidden messages but as random brain activity.","zh":"如果該理論正確，夢可能不是從隱藏訊息開始，而是從隨機大腦活動開始。"},{"en":"This phrase names a scientific explanation of how dreams form.","zh":"這個片語命名一個解釋夢如何形成的科學理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"describe how dreams are formed","meaning":"描述夢境如何形成","examples":[{"en":"The hypothesis describes how dreams are formed during REM sleep.","zh":"該假說描述夢境如何在快速眼動睡眠中形成。"},{"en":"To describe how dreams are formed means to explain the process by which dreams come into existence.","zh":"To describe how dreams are formed 指解釋夢產生的過程。"},{"en":"A science lesson may describe how rain is formed from water vapour.","zh":"科學課可能描述雨如何由水蒸氣形成。"},{"en":"If a theory describes dream formation, it should explain brain signals, images, and memory.","zh":"如果一個理論描述夢境形成，它應解釋大腦訊號、影像和記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on process, not just meaning.","zh":"這個片語著重過程，而不只是意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"nerve signals","meaning":"神經訊號","examples":[{"en":"Nerve signals are sent through the brain during REM sleep.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠期間，神經訊號在大腦中傳送。"},{"en":"Nerve signals are messages carried by nerve cells through electrical or chemical activity.","zh":"Nerve signals 是神經細胞透過電活動或化學活動傳送的訊息。"},{"en":"When you touch something hot, nerve signals quickly tell the brain to pull your hand away.","zh":"當你碰到熱的東西，神經訊號會迅速告訴大腦把手縮回。"},{"en":"If random nerve signals activate images, the brain may create dream scenes from them.","zh":"如果隨機神經訊號啟動影像，大腦可能從中創造夢境場景。"},{"en":"This phrase describes communication inside the nervous system.","zh":"這個片語描述神經系統內部的溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be sent out from","meaning":"從……發出","examples":[{"en":"The signals are sent out from a small region at the base of the brain.","zh":"這些訊號從大腦底部的一個小區域發出。"},{"en":"To be sent out from somewhere means to begin there and move outward to other places.","zh":"To be sent out from somewhere 指從某處開始並向其他地方傳送。"},{"en":"School notices may be sent out from the office to all parents by email.","zh":"學校通告可能從校務處透過電郵發送給所有家長。"},{"en":"If nerve signals are sent out from one brain region, they may activate other areas.","zh":"如果神經訊號從一個腦區發出，它們可能啟動其他區域。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the starting point of movement or communication.","zh":"這個片語顯示移動或溝通的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at the base of the brain","meaning":"在大腦底部","examples":[{"en":"The pons is located at the base of the brain.","zh":"腦橋位於大腦底部。"},{"en":"At the base of the brain means in the lower part of the brain near where it connects to the spinal cord.","zh":"At the base of the brain 指在大腦下方、接近連接脊髓的位置。"},{"en":"Doctors study structures at the base of the brain because they control important body functions.","zh":"醫生研究大腦底部的結構，因為它們控制重要身體功能。"},{"en":"If a signal begins at the base of the brain, it may affect basic sleep and body processes.","zh":"如果訊號始於大腦底部，它可能影響基本睡眠和身體過程。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the physical location of a brain structure.","zh":"這個片語提供大腦結構的身體位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the pons","meaning":"腦橋","examples":[{"en":"The pons sends signals that may activate dream imagery.","zh":"腦橋發出可能啟動夢境意象的訊號。"},{"en":"The pons is a part of the brainstem involved in sleep, breathing, and communication between brain areas.","zh":"Pons 是腦幹的一部分，涉及睡眠、呼吸和腦區之間的溝通。"},{"en":"Scientists may study the pons when examining REM sleep.","zh":"科學家研究快速眼動睡眠時，可能研究腦橋。"},{"en":"If the pons sends signals during sleep, those signals may help trigger dream activity.","zh":"如果腦橋在睡眠期間發出訊號，那些訊號可能幫助觸發夢境活動。"},{"en":"This word names a specific brain structure, not a general brain area.","zh":"這個詞命名一個特定大腦結構，而不是一般腦區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"activate images","meaning":"啟動影像","examples":[{"en":"The nerve signals activate images that appear in dreams.","zh":"神經訊號啟動出現在夢中的影像。"},{"en":"To activate images means to trigger visual scenes or pictures in the mind.","zh":"To activate images 指觸發腦中的視覺場景或圖像。"},{"en":"A smell from childhood can activate images of an old home or family meal.","zh":"童年氣味可以啟動舊家或家庭飯局的影像。"},{"en":"If brain signals activate images during sleep, the mind may build a dream from them.","zh":"如果大腦訊號在睡眠中啟動影像，心智可能從中建立夢境。"},{"en":"This phrase links brain activity with mental pictures.","zh":"這個片語把大腦活動與心理圖像連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put a crimp in","meaning":"妨礙；限制……發展","examples":[{"en":"The theory put a crimp in dream research for a time.","zh":"這個理論一度妨礙了夢境研究的發展。"},{"en":"To put a crimp in something means to slow, limit, or interfere with it.","zh":"To put a crimp in something 指減慢、限制或干擾某事。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can put a crimp in a school sports day.","zh":"大雨可以妨礙學校運動日。"},{"en":"If dreams are thought meaningless, that belief may reduce interest in studying them.","zh":"如果夢被認為毫無意義，這種信念可能降低研究它們的興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something making progress more difficult.","zh":"這個片語描述某事令進展更困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"meaningless nocturnal firings","meaning":"毫無意義的夜間神經放電","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists viewed dreams as meaningless nocturnal firings.","zh":"一些科學家把夢視為毫無意義的夜間神經放電。"},{"en":"Meaningless nocturnal firings are night-time nerve activities believed to have no deeper meaning.","zh":"Meaningless nocturnal firings 是被認為沒有更深意義的夜間神經活動。"},{"en":"Under this view, a strange dream is like the brain producing random sparks during sleep.","zh":"在這個觀點下，奇怪的夢就像大腦在睡眠中產生隨機火花。"},{"en":"If dreams are only meaningless firings, interpreting their symbols may seem unnecessary.","zh":"如果夢只是毫無意義的神經放電，解讀其象徵可能顯得沒有必要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strongly biological and anti-symbolic view of dreams.","zh":"這個片語描述一種強烈生物學且反象徵的夢境觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"what is the point of doing?","meaning":"做……有甚麼意義？","examples":[{"en":"If dreams are meaningless, what is the point of studying them?","zh":"如果夢毫無意義，研究它們有甚麼意義？"},{"en":"What is the point of doing something means why it is worth doing or what useful purpose it has.","zh":"What is the point of doing something 指做某事為何值得，或它有甚麼有用目的。"},{"en":"A student may ask, “What is the point of memorising this?” if the teacher never explains its use.","zh":"如果老師從不解釋用途，學生可能問：「背這個有甚麼意義？」"},{"en":"If an activity has no clear benefit, people may question why they should spend time on it.","zh":"如果一項活動沒有清楚好處，人們可能質疑為何應花時間做它。"},{"en":"This phrase challenges the purpose or value of an action.","zh":"這個片語質疑一個行動的目的或價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"spend about a quarter of","meaning":"花大約四分之一……","examples":[{"en":"Adults spend about a quarter of their sleep time in REM.","zh":"成年人把睡眠時間的大約四分之一花在快速眼動睡眠中。"},{"en":"To spend about a quarter of something means to use roughly one fourth of it.","zh":"To spend about a quarter of something 指使用大約四分之一。"},{"en":"A student may spend about a quarter of revision time checking old mistakes.","zh":"學生可能把大約四分之一溫習時間用於檢查舊錯誤。"},{"en":"If adults spend a large part of sleep in REM, that stage is biologically important to study.","zh":"如果成年人睡眠中有很大部分是快速眼動睡眠，該階段就值得從生物學上研究。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate proportion.","zh":"這個片語提供近似比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sleep time","meaning":"睡眠時間","examples":[{"en":"A significant part of adult sleep time is spent in REM.","zh":"成年人睡眠時間中相當大的一部分用於快速眼動睡眠。"},{"en":"Sleep time is the period during which a person is asleep.","zh":"Sleep time 是一個人睡着的時間。"},{"en":"A student’s sleep time may be too short if they use their phone late at night.","zh":"如果學生深夜使用手機，睡眠時間可能太短。"},{"en":"If sleep time is reduced, memory, mood, and attention may suffer the next day.","zh":"如果睡眠時間減少，第二天記憶、情緒和注意力可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the amount of time spent sleeping.","zh":"這個片語描述用於睡覺的時間量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"much of it dreaming","meaning":"當中很多時間在造夢","examples":[{"en":"Adults spend much of their REM sleep dreaming.","zh":"成年人的快速眼動睡眠中，當中很多時間在造夢。"},{"en":"Much of it dreaming means a large part of that time is spent having dreams.","zh":"Much of it dreaming 指那段時間中的很大部分都在造夢。"},{"en":"A person may spend much of a long train ride reading if the journey is quiet.","zh":"如果旅程安靜，一個人可能把漫長火車旅程中的很多時間用於閱讀。"},{"en":"If much of REM sleep involves dreaming, REM becomes central to dream research.","zh":"如果快速眼動睡眠中很多時間涉及造夢，快速眼動睡眠就成為夢境研究的核心。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what occupies a large part of a period.","zh":"這個片語顯示某段時間主要被甚麼佔用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be essentially paralysed","meaning":"基本上處於癱瘓狀態","examples":[{"en":"During REM sleep, the body is essentially paralysed.","zh":"在快速眼動睡眠期間，身體基本上處於癱瘓狀態。"},{"en":"To be essentially paralysed means to be almost unable to move, even if not permanently injured.","zh":"To be essentially paralysed 指幾乎不能移動，即使不是永久受傷。"},{"en":"A person may feel essentially paralysed by fear and unable to speak in an emergency.","zh":"一個人在緊急情況中可能因恐懼基本上動彈不得，無法說話。"},{"en":"If the body is paralysed during REM, people are less likely to act out their dreams.","zh":"如果身體在快速眼動睡眠中癱瘓，人就較不可能把夢中的動作做出來。"},{"en":"This phrase means movement is mostly blocked.","zh":"這個片語指動作大多被阻止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the brain is buzzing","meaning":"大腦活動非常活躍","examples":[{"en":"Although the body is still, the brain is buzzing with activity.","zh":"雖然身體靜止，大腦活動卻非常活躍。"},{"en":"The brain is buzzing means the brain is highly active and full of signals or mental activity.","zh":"The brain is buzzing 指大腦高度活躍，充滿訊號或心理活動。"},{"en":"Before an exam, a student’s brain may be buzzing with facts, worries, and plans.","zh":"考試前，學生的大腦可能充滿事實、擔憂和計劃，活動非常活躍。"},{"en":"If the brain is buzzing during sleep, sleep can include intense internal activity.","zh":"如果大腦在睡眠中非常活躍，睡眠可以包含強烈內在活動。"},{"en":"This phrase uses an image of busy movement to describe mental activity.","zh":"這個片語用忙碌活動的意象描述心理活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"PET technology","meaning":"正電子掃描技術","examples":[{"en":"PET technology allows researchers to observe activity in the brain.","zh":"正電子掃描技術讓研究人員觀察大腦活動。"},{"en":"PET technology is a brain-imaging method that shows activity by tracking changes in the body.","zh":"PET technology 是一種腦部影像方法，透過追蹤身體變化顯示活動。"},{"en":"Doctors may use PET technology to study how different brain areas work.","zh":"醫生可能使用正電子掃描技術研究不同腦區如何運作。"},{"en":"If PET technology shows active regions during sleep, scientists can compare dream states with waking states.","zh":"如果正電子掃描技術顯示睡眠期間的活躍區域，科學家可以比較夢境狀態與清醒狀態。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to advanced scanning equipment used in medical research.","zh":"這個片語指醫學研究中使用的先進掃描設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fMRI technology","meaning":"功能性磁力共振成像技術","examples":[{"en":"Scientists use fMRI technology to watch the dreaming brain.","zh":"科學家使用功能性磁力共振成像技術觀察造夢時的大腦。"},{"en":"fMRI technology is a scanning method that shows which brain areas are active by measuring blood-flow changes.","zh":"fMRI technology 是一種掃描方法，透過量度血流變化顯示哪些腦區活躍。"},{"en":"Researchers may use fMRI technology while participants look at pictures or listen to sounds.","zh":"研究人員可能在參加者看圖片或聽聲音時使用功能性磁力共振成像技術。"},{"en":"If fMRI shows one area becomes active, scientists may link that area with a mental task.","zh":"如果功能性磁力共振成像顯示某區域變得活躍，科學家可能把該區與某心理任務連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a tool for studying brain activity in real time.","zh":"這個片語指即時研究大腦活動的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the dreaming brain","meaning":"造夢時的大腦","examples":[{"en":"Brain imaging reveals which regions are active in the dreaming brain.","zh":"腦部影像揭示造夢時的大腦中哪些區域活躍。"},{"en":"The dreaming brain is the brain while a person is dreaming.","zh":"The dreaming brain 是人在造夢時的大腦。"},{"en":"Scientists study the dreaming brain to see which areas handle emotion, memory, and imagery.","zh":"科學家研究造夢時的大腦，以查看哪些區域處理情緒、記憶和影像。"},{"en":"If the dreaming brain shows strong emotion areas, dreams may help process feelings.","zh":"如果造夢時的大腦顯示情緒區域強烈活躍，夢可能幫助處理感受。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on brain activity during dreams.","zh":"這個片語著重夢境期間的大腦活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"one of the most active areas","meaning":"最活躍的區域之一","examples":[{"en":"The limbic system is one of the most active areas during REM sleep.","zh":"邊緣系統是快速眼動睡眠期間最活躍的區域之一。"},{"en":"One of the most active areas means one region that shows especially high activity compared with others.","zh":"One of the most active areas 指與其他區域相比，活動特別高的其中一個區域。"},{"en":"During a difficult listening test, language areas may be among the most active areas of the brain.","zh":"在困難聆聽測驗期間，語言區域可能是大腦最活躍的區域之一。"},{"en":"If an emotion centre is highly active during dreams, emotions may shape dream content.","zh":"如果情緒中心在夢中高度活躍，情緒可能塑造夢境內容。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a region that is especially busy.","zh":"這個片語指出特別忙碌的區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"limbic system","meaning":"邊緣系統","examples":[{"en":"The limbic system plays a major role in emotion.","zh":"邊緣系統在情緒中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"The limbic system is a group of brain structures involved in emotion, memory, and motivation.","zh":"Limbic system 是一組涉及情緒、記憶和動機的大腦結構。"},{"en":"Fear, pleasure, and emotional memories can involve the limbic system.","zh":"恐懼、快樂和情緒記憶都可能涉及邊緣系統。"},{"en":"If the limbic system is active during dreams, dream emotions may feel strong.","zh":"如果邊緣系統在夢中活躍，夢中的情緒可能感覺強烈。"},{"en":"This phrase names an emotional and memory-related brain system.","zh":"這個片語命名與情緒和記憶有關的大腦系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"control our emotions","meaning":"控制我們的情緒","examples":[{"en":"The limbic system helps control our emotions.","zh":"邊緣系統幫助控制我們的情緒。"},{"en":"To control our emotions means to manage feelings such as fear, anger, sadness, and pleasure.","zh":"To control our emotions 指管理恐懼、憤怒、悲傷和快樂等感受。"},{"en":"Deep breathing can help students control their emotions before a presentation.","zh":"深呼吸可以幫助學生在演講前控制情緒。"},{"en":"If a brain system controls emotions, activity there may affect how dreams feel.","zh":"如果某個大腦系統控制情緒，那裡的活動可能影響夢的感覺。"},{"en":"This phrase describes managing emotional reactions.","zh":"這個片語描述管理情緒反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"much less active","meaning":"活躍程度低得多","examples":[{"en":"The prefrontal cortex is much less active during REM sleep.","zh":"前額葉皮層在快速眼動睡眠期間活躍程度低得多。"},{"en":"Much less active means working far less strongly than before or than another area.","zh":"Much less active 指比以前或比另一區域運作弱得多。"},{"en":"A classroom is much less active after lunch if students are tired.","zh":"如果學生疲倦，午飯後課室活躍程度可能低得多。"},{"en":"If the reasoning part of the brain is less active, dreams may become less logical.","zh":"如果大腦中負責推理的部分活躍程度較低，夢可能變得較不合邏輯。"},{"en":"This phrase compares levels of activity.","zh":"這個片語比較活動水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"prefrontal cortex","meaning":"前額葉皮層","examples":[{"en":"The prefrontal cortex is involved in reasoning and logical thought.","zh":"前額葉皮層涉及推理和邏輯思考。"},{"en":"The prefrontal cortex is the front part of the brain linked with planning, judgment, and self-control.","zh":"Prefrontal cortex 是大腦前部，與計劃、判斷和自我控制有關。"},{"en":"A student uses the prefrontal cortex when checking whether an answer makes sense.","zh":"學生檢查答案是否合理時，會使用前額葉皮層。"},{"en":"If this area is less active during dreams, strange events may seem acceptable.","zh":"如果這個區域在夢中較不活躍，奇怪事件可能看似可以接受。"},{"en":"This phrase names a brain area important for rational control.","zh":"這個片語命名對理性控制重要的腦區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be associated with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The prefrontal cortex is associated with logical thinking.","zh":"前額葉皮層與邏輯思考有關。"},{"en":"To be associated with something means to be connected with it.","zh":"To be associated with something 指與某事有連繫。"},{"en":"Regular reading is often associated with stronger vocabulary.","zh":"定期閱讀常與較強詞彙量有關。"},{"en":"If a brain region is associated with reasoning, reduced activity there may affect logic.","zh":"如果某腦區與推理有關，那裡活動減少可能影響邏輯。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a link, not always a direct cause.","zh":"這個片語顯示關聯，而不一定是直接原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"logical thinking","meaning":"邏輯思考","examples":[{"en":"Reduced logical thinking may explain the unusual structure of dreams.","zh":"邏輯思考減少可能解釋夢的奇怪結構。"},{"en":"Logical thinking is reasoning in a clear, ordered, and sensible way.","zh":"Logical thinking 是以清晰、有序和合理的方式推理。"},{"en":"Students use logical thinking when they compare evidence before choosing an answer.","zh":"學生在選答案前比較證據時，就是使用邏輯思考。"},{"en":"If logical thinking is weaker during dreams, impossible events may feel normal.","zh":"如果夢中邏輯思考較弱，不可能事件可能感覺正常。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised reasoning, not emotional reaction.","zh":"這個片語描述有組織的推理，而不是情緒反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"explain why","meaning":"解釋為何……","examples":[{"en":"Reduced activity in the prefrontal cortex may explain why dreams seem illogical.","zh":"前額葉皮層活動減少可能解釋為何夢看起來不合邏輯。"},{"en":"To explain why something happens means to give the reason for it.","zh":"To explain why something happens 指給出某事發生的原因。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain why a grammar answer is wrong by pointing to the verb tense.","zh":"老師可能透過指出動詞時態，解釋為何一個文法答案錯誤。"},{"en":"If brain activity changes during sleep, it may explain why dreams feel different from waking thought.","zh":"如果睡眠期間大腦活動改變，這可能解釋為何夢感覺不同於清醒思想。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with a puzzling result.","zh":"這個片語把原因與令人困惑的結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lack a coherent storyline","meaning":"缺乏連貫情節","examples":[{"en":"Dreams often lack a coherent storyline.","zh":"夢常缺乏連貫情節。"},{"en":"To lack a coherent storyline means to have no clear, logical sequence of events.","zh":"To lack a coherent storyline 指沒有清晰、合邏輯的事件次序。"},{"en":"A student’s essay may lack a coherent storyline if each paragraph jumps to a new topic.","zh":"如果學生作文每段都跳到新題目，它可能缺乏連貫情節。"},{"en":"If the reasoning part of the brain is less active, dream events may not connect properly.","zh":"如果大腦中負責推理的部分較不活躍，夢境事件可能無法恰當連接。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a story that feels broken or illogical.","zh":"這個片語描述感覺破碎或不合邏輯的故事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"non-REM sleep","meaning":"非快速眼動睡眠","examples":[{"en":"Some dreaming also occurs during non-REM sleep.","zh":"一些造夢也發生在非快速眼動睡眠期間。"},{"en":"Non-REM sleep is sleep that is not rapid-eye-movement sleep and includes several other sleep stages.","zh":"Non-REM sleep 是不是快速眼動睡眠的睡眠，並包括其他幾個睡眠階段。"},{"en":"People may still have thoughts or simple dreams during non-REM sleep.","zh":"人們在非快速眼動睡眠期間仍可能有想法或簡單夢境。"},{"en":"If dreaming occurs outside REM, dreams cannot be explained by REM alone.","zh":"如果造夢在快速眼動睡眠以外也發生，夢就不能只用快速眼動睡眠解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts other sleep stages with REM sleep.","zh":"這個片語把其他睡眠階段與快速眼動睡眠作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"generally less vivid","meaning":"一般較不鮮明","examples":[{"en":"Dreams during non-REM sleep are generally less vivid.","zh":"非快速眼動睡眠期間的夢一般較不鮮明。"},{"en":"Generally less vivid means usually not as clear, detailed, or intense.","zh":"Generally less vivid 指通常沒有那麼清晰、細緻或強烈。"},{"en":"A memory from last year may be generally less vivid than a memory from yesterday.","zh":"去年的記憶一般比昨天的記憶較不鮮明。"},{"en":"If non-REM dreams are less vivid, people may remember fewer details after waking.","zh":"如果非快速眼動睡眠中的夢較不鮮明，人醒來後可能記得較少細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a usual pattern, not every single case.","zh":"這個片語描述一般模式，而不是每一個個案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"anterior cingulate cortex","meaning":"前扣帶皮層","examples":[{"en":"The anterior cingulate cortex detects conflicts and discrepancies.","zh":"前扣帶皮層察覺衝突和不一致之處。"},{"en":"The anterior cingulate cortex is a brain region involved in attention, conflict monitoring, and emotional regulation.","zh":"Anterior cingulate cortex 是涉及注意力、衝突監察和情緒調節的大腦區域。"},{"en":"A person may use systems like the anterior cingulate cortex when noticing that two ideas do not fit together.","zh":"當一個人注意到兩個想法不吻合時，可能使用像前扣帶皮層這類系統。"},{"en":"If this area helps detect conflict, it may matter when dreams involve personal problems.","zh":"如果這個區域幫助察覺衝突，當夢涉及個人問題時，它可能很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific brain region linked with monitoring and emotion.","zh":"這個片語命名與監察和情緒相關的特定腦區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"detect discrepancies","meaning":"察覺不一致之處","examples":[{"en":"This brain region helps detect discrepancies.","zh":"這個大腦區域幫助察覺不一致之處。"},{"en":"To detect discrepancies means to notice differences, conflicts, or things that do not match.","zh":"To detect discrepancies 指注意到差異、衝突或不吻合的地方。"},{"en":"A teacher can detect discrepancies between a student’s answer and the passage.","zh":"老師可以察覺學生答案與文章之間的不一致之處。"},{"en":"If the brain detects a conflict between behaviour and values, it may create emotional tension.","zh":"如果大腦察覺行為與價值觀之間有衝突，它可能產生情緒張力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes noticing inconsistency.","zh":"這個片語描述注意到不一致。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"thorny problems","meaning":"棘手問題","examples":[{"en":"People sometimes solve thorny problems in their dreams.","zh":"人們有時在夢中解決棘手問題。"},{"en":"Thorny problems are difficult problems with many complications.","zh":"Thorny problems 是有許多複雜情況的困難問題。"},{"en":"A family argument about money can become a thorny problem if everyone has different needs.","zh":"如果每個人都有不同需要，關於金錢的家庭爭執可能變成棘手問題。"},{"en":"If a problem is thorny, a simple answer may not solve it.","zh":"如果問題棘手，簡單答案可能不能解決它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes problems that are hard to handle neatly.","zh":"這個片語描述難以妥善處理的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"figure out","meaning":"想出；解決","examples":[{"en":"Some people figure out difficult problems while dreaming.","zh":"有些人在造夢時想出困難問題的解法。"},{"en":"To figure out something means to understand it or find a solution to it.","zh":"To figure out something 指理解某事或找到其解決方法。"},{"en":"A student may figure out a maths problem after drawing a diagram.","zh":"學生畫圖後可能解決一道數學題。"},{"en":"If the mind keeps working during sleep, it may figure out a problem in a new way.","zh":"如果大腦在睡眠中繼續工作，它可能以新方式想出問題答案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes solving or understanding something after effort.","zh":"這個片語描述經過努力後解決或理解某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"survey the internal milieu","meaning":"檢視內在心理環境","examples":[{"en":"The brain may survey the internal milieu during dreams.","zh":"大腦可能在夢中檢視內在心理環境。"},{"en":"To survey the internal milieu means to examine one’s inner mental and emotional state.","zh":"To survey the internal milieu 指檢查一個人的內在心理和情緒狀態。"},{"en":"A person may survey their inner feelings after a serious argument with a friend.","zh":"一個人在與朋友嚴重爭吵後，可能檢視自己的內在感受。"},{"en":"If dreams survey inner concerns, they may bring hidden worries into story form.","zh":"如果夢檢視內在關注，它們可能把隱藏憂慮變成故事形式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the mind checking its own emotional landscape.","zh":"這個片語描述心智檢查自己的情緒地景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"internal milieu","meaning":"內在心理環境","examples":[{"en":"Dreams may reflect a person’s internal milieu.","zh":"夢可能反映一個人的內在心理環境。"},{"en":"Internal milieu means a person’s inner mental environment, including emotions, worries, memories, and conflicts.","zh":"Internal milieu 指一個人的內在心理環境，包括情緒、憂慮、記憶和衝突。"},{"en":"A student’s internal milieu before exams may include pressure, hope, fear, and ambition.","zh":"學生考試前的內在心理環境可能包含壓力、希望、恐懼和抱負。"},{"en":"If the internal milieu is troubled, dreams may contain anxiety or unresolved problems.","zh":"如果內在心理環境不安，夢可能包含焦慮或未解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the inner psychological world, not the physical surroundings.","zh":"這個片語指內在心理世界，而不是外在物理環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"try to figure out","meaning":"嘗試弄清楚","examples":[{"en":"The dreaming brain may try to figure out what actions to take.","zh":"造夢時的大腦可能嘗試弄清楚應採取甚麼行動。"},{"en":"To try to figure out something means to attempt to understand it or decide what to do.","zh":"To try to figure out something 指嘗試理解某事或決定應怎樣做。"},{"en":"A student may try to figure out which revision method works best before an exam.","zh":"學生可能在考試前嘗試弄清楚哪種溫習方法最有效。"},{"en":"If the brain reviews problems in dreams, it may be trying to decide how to respond.","zh":"如果大腦在夢中回顧問題，它可能正在嘗試決定如何回應。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active problem-solving, even if the answer is not yet clear.","zh":"這個片語暗示主動解難，即使答案尚未清楚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"what it should be doing","meaning":"它應該做甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The brain may assess what it should be doing.","zh":"大腦可能評估它應該做甚麼。"},{"en":"What it should be doing means the right action or response that something ought to take.","zh":"What it should be doing 指某事物應該採取的正確行動或反應。"},{"en":"A student under pressure may wonder what they should be doing first: revising, sleeping, or asking for help.","zh":"受壓學生可能會想自己應該先做甚麼：溫習、睡覺，還是求助。"},{"en":"If dreams test possible actions, the brain may be exploring what it should do next.","zh":"如果夢測試可能行動，大腦可能正在探索接下來應該做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on choosing an appropriate action.","zh":"這個片語著重選擇合適行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"conflict with who we are","meaning":"與真正的自己產生衝突","examples":[{"en":"Dreams may reveal whether our actions conflict with who we are.","zh":"夢可能揭示我們的行動是否與真正的自己產生衝突。"},{"en":"To conflict with who we are means to go against our values, identity, or sense of self.","zh":"To conflict with who we are 指違背我們的價值觀、身份或自我感。"},{"en":"A student who values honesty may feel uneasy if cheating conflicts with who they are.","zh":"重視誠實的學生，如果作弊與真正的自己產生衝突，可能會感到不安。"},{"en":"If daily behaviour conflicts with identity, dreams may express guilt, confusion, or tension.","zh":"如果日常行為與身份產生衝突，夢可能表達內疚、混亂或張力。"},{"en":"This phrase connects action with personal values.","zh":"這個片語把行動與個人價值連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"vital mental functions","meaning":"重要的心理功能","examples":[{"en":"Dreaming may appear to serve vital mental functions.","zh":"造夢看起來可能發揮重要的心理功能。"},{"en":"Vital mental functions are important jobs of the mind, such as processing emotions, memories, or problems.","zh":"Vital mental functions 是心智的重要工作，例如處理情緒、記憶或問題。"},{"en":"Sleep may support vital mental functions by helping students remember what they learned.","zh":"睡眠可能透過幫助學生記住所學內容，支持重要心理功能。"},{"en":"If dreaming helps emotional balance, it may serve an important mental function.","zh":"如果造夢幫助情緒平衡，它可能發揮重要心理功能。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that dreaming may do something necessary for the mind.","zh":"這個片語暗示造夢可能為心智做某些必要事情。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"no one has yet been able to say that","meaning":"尚未有人能證明……","examples":[{"en":"No one has yet been able to prove that dreaming is essential.","zh":"尚未有人能證明造夢是必要的。"},{"en":"No one has yet been able to say that means nobody has so far shown or stated it with certainty.","zh":"No one has yet been able to say that 指到目前為止仍沒有人能確定地顯示或說明某事。"},{"en":"No one has yet been able to prove that one study method works best for every student.","zh":"尚未有人能證明一種學習方法對每個學生都最好。"},{"en":"If evidence is still missing, scientists must avoid making a final claim.","zh":"如果證據仍然不足，科學家必須避免作出最終主張。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses careful uncertainty.","zh":"這個片語表達謹慎的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be essential to life","meaning":"對生命不可或缺","examples":[{"en":"Dreaming has not been proven to be essential to life.","zh":"造夢尚未被證明對生命不可或缺。"},{"en":"To be essential to life means to be necessary for survival or normal living.","zh":"To be essential to life 指對生存或正常生活是必要的。"},{"en":"Clean water is essential to life because people cannot survive without it.","zh":"清潔食水對生命不可或缺，因為人沒有它就不能生存。"},{"en":"If dreaming is not essential to life, people may survive even with little or no dreaming.","zh":"如果造夢對生命並非不可或缺，人可能即使很少或沒有造夢仍能生存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something absolutely necessary, not just useful.","zh":"這個片語描述絕對必要的東西，而不只是有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"even sanity","meaning":"甚至對精神正常也不可或缺","examples":[{"en":"Scientists cannot prove that dreams are essential even to sanity.","zh":"科學家不能證明夢甚至對精神正常也不可或缺。"},{"en":"Even sanity means even a person’s mental health or ability to think normally.","zh":"Even sanity 指甚至一個人的精神健康或正常思考能力。"},{"en":"People may need sleep for health, but it is harder to prove that dreams are necessary even for sanity.","zh":"人可能需要睡眠來保持健康，但更難證明夢甚至對精神正常是必要的。"},{"en":"If someone loses dreams yet remains mentally stable, dreams may not be essential to sanity.","zh":"如果某人失去夢卻仍精神穩定，夢可能不是精神正常所必需。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that even a very important mental condition is not proven to depend on dreams.","zh":"這個片語強調即使是非常重要的心理狀態，也未被證明依賴夢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"MAO inhibitors","meaning":"單胺氧化酶抑制劑","examples":[{"en":"MAO inhibitors are an older class of antidepressants.","zh":"單胺氧化酶抑制劑是較舊式的一類抗抑鬱藥。"},{"en":"MAO inhibitors are medicines that affect brain chemicals and are used to treat some forms of depression.","zh":"MAO inhibitors 是影響大腦化學物質並用於治療某些抑鬱症的藥物。"},{"en":"A doctor may prescribe MAO inhibitors only when carefully considering diet and drug interactions.","zh":"醫生可能只有在仔細考慮飲食和藥物相互作用後，才處方單胺氧化酶抑制劑。"},{"en":"If MAO inhibitors reduce REM sleep, they help scientists study whether REM dreaming is necessary.","zh":"如果單胺氧化酶抑制劑減少快速眼動睡眠，它們有助科學家研究快速眼動造夢是否必要。"},{"en":"This phrase names a type of antidepressant medication.","zh":"這個片語命名一類抗抑鬱藥物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an older class of antidepressants","meaning":"較舊式的一類抗抑鬱藥","examples":[{"en":"MAO inhibitors belong to an older class of antidepressants.","zh":"單胺氧化酶抑制劑屬於較舊式的一類抗抑鬱藥。"},{"en":"An older class of antidepressants is a group of depression medicines developed earlier than newer drugs.","zh":"An older class of antidepressants 是比新式藥物更早發展出來的一組抑鬱症藥物。"},{"en":"Doctors may use an older class of antidepressants when newer medicines are not suitable.","zh":"當新式藥物不合適時，醫生可能使用較舊式的一類抗抑鬱藥。"},{"en":"If a drug belongs to an older class, it may have different benefits and side effects.","zh":"如果藥物屬於較舊式類別，它可能有不同好處和副作用。"},{"en":"This phrase compares older medication types with more recent ones.","zh":"這個片語把較舊藥物類型與較新藥物作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"block REM sleep","meaning":"阻止快速眼動睡眠","examples":[{"en":"Some medications almost completely block REM sleep.","zh":"一些藥物幾乎完全阻止快速眼動睡眠。"},{"en":"To block REM sleep means to prevent or greatly reduce that stage of sleep.","zh":"To block REM sleep 指阻止或大幅減少該睡眠階段。"},{"en":"A medicine may block REM sleep if it changes brain chemicals involved in sleep cycles.","zh":"如果藥物改變涉及睡眠週期的大腦化學物質，它可能阻止快速眼動睡眠。"},{"en":"If REM sleep is blocked, scientists can observe whether people still function normally.","zh":"如果快速眼動睡眠被阻止，科學家可以觀察人是否仍能正常運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stopping or limiting a sleep stage.","zh":"這個片語描述停止或限制某睡眠階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"without detectable effects","meaning":"沒有可察覺的影響","examples":[{"en":"REM sleep can be reduced without detectable harmful effects.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠可以被減少，而沒有可察覺的有害影響。"},{"en":"Without detectable effects means without effects that can be noticed, measured, or clearly identified.","zh":"Without detectable effects 指沒有可被注意、量度或清楚識別的影響。"},{"en":"A small change in classroom lighting may happen without detectable effects on exam results.","zh":"課室燈光的小改變可能對考試成績沒有可察覺的影響。"},{"en":"If a person loses REM sleep without detectable effects, the loss may not obviously damage daily life.","zh":"如果一個人失去快速眼動睡眠而沒有可察覺的影響，這種失去可能沒有明顯損害日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean no effects exist; it means none have been clearly observed.","zh":"這個片語不代表完全沒有影響；它表示沒有被清楚觀察到的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"REM rebound","meaning":"快速眼動睡眠反彈","examples":[{"en":"People may experience a REM rebound after stopping certain drugs.","zh":"人們停止某些藥物後，可能經歷快速眼動睡眠反彈。"},{"en":"REM rebound is an increase in REM sleep after it has been reduced or suppressed.","zh":"REM rebound 是快速眼動睡眠被減少或抑制後出現的增加。"},{"en":"A sleeper may have more intense dreams during REM rebound after missing dream sleep for several nights.","zh":"睡眠者在幾晚缺少夢睡眠後，可能在快速眼動睡眠反彈期間有更強烈的夢。"},{"en":"If the brain increases REM after restriction, it may be trying to recover lost REM time.","zh":"如果大腦在限制後增加快速眼動睡眠，它可能正在嘗試追回失去的快速眼動睡眠時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a bounce-back effect in sleep patterns.","zh":"這個片語描述睡眠模式中的反彈效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stop the medication","meaning":"停止服藥","examples":[{"en":"Extra REM sleep may occur after patients stop the medication.","zh":"病人停止服藥後，可能出現額外快速眼動睡眠。"},{"en":"To stop the medication means to stop taking a prescribed drug.","zh":"To stop the medication 指停止服用處方藥。"},{"en":"A patient should ask a doctor before stopping medication suddenly.","zh":"病人在突然停止服藥前，應先詢問醫生。"},{"en":"If stopping medication changes sleep, the drug was probably affecting sleep chemistry.","zh":"如果停止服藥改變睡眠，該藥物很可能正在影響睡眠化學作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ending a course of drug treatment.","zh":"這個片語描述結束一段藥物治療。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors","meaning":"選擇性血清素再攝取抑制劑","examples":[{"en":"Selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors can reduce dreaming.","zh":"選擇性血清素再攝取抑制劑可以減少造夢。"},{"en":"Selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors are antidepressants that affect serotonin levels in the brain.","zh":"Selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors 是影響大腦血清素水平的抗抑鬱藥。"},{"en":"Doctors may prescribe selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors for depression or anxiety.","zh":"醫生可能為抑鬱或焦慮處方選擇性血清素再攝取抑制劑。"},{"en":"If these drugs reduce dreaming, they can provide evidence about the link between brain chemistry and dreams.","zh":"如果這些藥物減少造夢，它們可以提供關於大腦化學作用與夢之間關係的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase names a common class of antidepressant medicine.","zh":"這個片語命名一類常見抗抑鬱藥物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"SSRIs","meaning":"選擇性血清素再攝取抑制劑","examples":[{"en":"SSRIs are commonly prescribed antidepressants.","zh":"SSRIs 是常被處方的抗抑鬱藥。"},{"en":"SSRIs are selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors, a type of medicine used to treat depression and anxiety.","zh":"SSRIs 是選擇性血清素再攝取抑制劑，一種用於治療抑鬱和焦慮的藥物。"},{"en":"A doctor may explain possible side effects before giving a patient SSRIs.","zh":"醫生可能在給病人 SSRIs 前解釋可能副作用。"},{"en":"If SSRIs change dreaming, researchers may study how serotonin affects sleep.","zh":"如果 SSRIs 改變造夢，研究人員可能研究血清素如何影響睡眠。"},{"en":"This abbreviation is often used in medicine and psychology.","zh":"這個縮寫常用於醫學和心理學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"reduce dreaming by","meaning":"將造夢減少……","examples":[{"en":"Some antidepressants reduce dreaming by a third to a half.","zh":"一些抗抑鬱藥將造夢減少三分之一至一半。"},{"en":"To reduce dreaming by an amount means to make dreaming occur less by that proportion.","zh":"To reduce dreaming by an amount 指按該比例令造夢減少。"},{"en":"A medicine that reduces headaches by half leaves patients with far fewer painful days.","zh":"能把頭痛減少一半的藥物，會令病人疼痛日子大大減少。"},{"en":"If dreaming is reduced by a large amount without obvious harm, its necessity becomes harder to prove.","zh":"如果造夢大幅減少而沒有明顯傷害，它的必要性就更難證明。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the size of a decrease.","zh":"這個片語顯示減少幅度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"permanently lose the ability to","meaning":"永久失去……的能力","examples":[{"en":"A person may permanently lose the ability to dream.","zh":"一個人可能永久失去造夢的能力。"},{"en":"To permanently lose the ability to do something means to become unable to do it forever or for an extremely long time.","zh":"To permanently lose the ability to do something 指永遠或極長時間不能做某事。"},{"en":"A serious injury may cause someone to permanently lose the ability to move one hand.","zh":"嚴重受傷可能令某人永久失去移動一隻手的能力。"},{"en":"If a patient permanently loses dreaming but lives normally, dreams may not be essential to daily functioning.","zh":"如果病人永久失去造夢能力但生活正常，夢可能不是日常運作所必需。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lasting loss of an ability.","zh":"這個片語描述能力的持久喪失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be disabling","meaning":"令人喪失正常生活能力","examples":[{"en":"The inability to dream does not necessarily have to be disabling.","zh":"無法造夢不一定會令人喪失正常生活能力。"},{"en":"To be disabling means to seriously limit a person’s normal activities or independence.","zh":"To be disabling 指嚴重限制一個人的正常活動或獨立生活。"},{"en":"Severe anxiety can be disabling if it stops someone from leaving home or working.","zh":"如果嚴重焦慮令某人無法出門或工作，它就可能令人喪失正常生活能力。"},{"en":"If losing dreams is not disabling, the person may still think, work, and live normally.","zh":"如果失去夢並不令人喪失正常生活能力，該人可能仍能正常思考、工作和生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a condition that prevents normal functioning.","zh":"這個片語描述阻礙正常運作的狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"observe a patient","meaning":"觀察一名病人","examples":[{"en":"The researcher had been observing a patient for many years.","zh":"研究人員多年來一直觀察一名病人。"},{"en":"To observe a patient means to watch, monitor, and record their condition over time.","zh":"To observe a patient 指隨時間觀察、監察並記錄病人的狀況。"},{"en":"A doctor may observe a patient after surgery to check whether recovery is normal.","zh":"醫生可能在手術後觀察病人，以檢查康復是否正常。"},{"en":"If researchers observe someone for many years, they can notice long-term effects.","zh":"如果研究人員多年觀察某人，他們可以注意到長期影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful medical or scientific monitoring.","zh":"這個片語描述仔細的醫學或科學監察。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a fragment of shrapnel","meaning":"一塊彈片","examples":[{"en":"The patient was injured by a fragment of shrapnel.","zh":"這名病人被一塊彈片所傷。"},{"en":"A fragment of shrapnel is a small sharp piece of metal from an explosive weapon.","zh":"A fragment of shrapnel 是爆炸武器產生的一小塊尖銳金屬。"},{"en":"A soldier may be injured by shrapnel even if the explosion happens several metres away.","zh":"即使爆炸發生在幾米外，士兵也可能被彈片所傷。"},{"en":"If shrapnel enters the body, it can damage tissue, organs, or the brain.","zh":"如果彈片進入身體，它可以損害組織、器官或大腦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a dangerous piece of metal from an explosion.","zh":"這個片語描述爆炸產生的危險金屬碎片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"penetrate the brain","meaning":"刺入大腦","examples":[{"en":"The shrapnel penetrated his brain.","zh":"彈片刺入了他的大腦。"},{"en":"To penetrate the brain means to enter the brain by force from outside.","zh":"To penetrate the brain 指從外部以力量進入大腦。"},{"en":"A serious head injury may occur if a sharp object penetrates the skull and brain.","zh":"如果尖銳物體刺穿頭骨並刺入大腦，可能造成嚴重頭部損傷。"},{"en":"If metal penetrates the brain, it can damage the areas controlling sleep, movement, or memory.","zh":"如果金屬刺入大腦，它可能損害控制睡眠、動作或記憶的區域。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a severe physical injury.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重身體傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, the patient experienced no REM sleep.","zh":"因此，該病人沒有快速眼動睡眠。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what happened before.","zh":"As a result 指因為之前發生的事情。"},{"en":"The bus broke down; as a result, many students arrived late.","zh":"巴士壞了；因此，許多學生遲到。"},{"en":"If a brain injury damages sleep areas, REM sleep may disappear as a result.","zh":"如果腦傷損害睡眠區域，快速眼動睡眠可能因此消失。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with its consequence.","zh":"這個片語連接原因與結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"remember any dreams","meaning":"記得任何夢境","examples":[{"en":"The patient did not remember any dreams.","zh":"該病人不記得任何夢境。"},{"en":"To remember any dreams means to recall dream experiences after waking.","zh":"To remember any dreams 指醒來後回想起夢的經驗。"},{"en":"Some people wake up knowing they dreamed but cannot remember any details.","zh":"有些人醒來知道自己造過夢，但記不起任何細節。"},{"en":"If a person never remembers dreams, researchers may ask whether they dream at all.","zh":"如果一個人從不記得夢，研究人員可能會問他是否真的造夢。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on dream recall, not necessarily dream occurrence.","zh":"這個片語著重夢境回憶，而不一定是夢是否發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"probably the most normal person","meaning":"大概是最正常的人","examples":[{"en":"Lavie described the patient as an exceptionally normal person.","zh":"Lavie把該病人描述為異常正常的人。"},{"en":"Probably the most normal person means someone who appears extremely ordinary and mentally healthy despite unusual circumstances.","zh":"Probably the most normal person 指即使處於異常情況，仍看起來極普通且心理健康的人。"},{"en":"A patient with a rare condition may still live like a normal person, working and enjoying hobbies.","zh":"患有罕見狀況的病人仍可能像正常人一樣生活、工作和享受興趣。"},{"en":"If someone without REM sleep seems normal, researchers must question whether dreaming is necessary.","zh":"如果沒有快速眼動睡眠的人看起來正常，研究人員就必須質疑造夢是否必要。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses normal functioning in a surprising case.","zh":"這個片語強調在令人驚訝的個案中仍能正常運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"one of the most successful","meaning":"最成功的人之一","examples":[{"en":"The patient was also one of the most successful people Lavie knew.","zh":"該病人也是Lavie認識的人中最成功的人之一。"},{"en":"One of the most successful means among the people who have achieved the greatest results.","zh":"One of the most successful 指在取得最大成果的人當中。"},{"en":"A student can be one of the most successful in class because of steady effort, not natural talent alone.","zh":"學生可以因持續努力，而不只是天賦，成為班中最成功的人之一。"},{"en":"If a person without dreams is highly successful, dream loss may not prevent achievement.","zh":"如果沒有夢的人非常成功，失去夢可能不會阻止成就。"},{"en":"This phrase places someone near the top in success.","zh":"這個片語把某人放在成功程度接近頂尖的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"versatile artist","meaning":"多才多藝的藝術工作者","examples":[{"en":"The patient was a lawyer, painter and newspaper editor.","zh":"這名病人是一名律師、畫家和報章編輯。"},{"en":"A versatile artist is someone with many creative abilities or skills in different fields.","zh":"Versatile artist 是在不同範疇有多種創意能力或技能的人。"},{"en":"A versatile artist may paint, write, design, and perform music.","zh":"多才多藝的藝術工作者可能繪畫、寫作、設計和演奏音樂。"},{"en":"If someone succeeds in several areas, their creativity may not depend on dream recall.","zh":"如果某人在幾個範疇都成功，他的創意可能不依賴夢境回憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a person with wide-ranging talents.","zh":"這個片語描述有廣泛才能的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"editor of a puzzle column","meaning":"智力遊戲專欄編輯","examples":[{"en":"He worked as the editor of a puzzle column.","zh":"他擔任智力遊戲專欄編輯。"},{"en":"An editor of a puzzle column is a person who prepares, checks, or manages puzzles in a newspaper or magazine.","zh":"Editor of a puzzle column 是為報紙或雜誌準備、檢查或管理智力遊戲的人。"},{"en":"A puzzle-column editor may choose crosswords, number games, and logic questions for readers.","zh":"智力遊戲專欄編輯可能為讀者選擇填字遊戲、數字遊戲和邏輯題。"},{"en":"If someone edits puzzles, they need clear thinking, accuracy, and creativity.","zh":"如果某人編輯智力遊戲，他需要清晰思考、準確和創意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific newspaper role.","zh":"這個片語描述一個特定報章職位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"popular newspaper","meaning":"受歡迎的報章","examples":[{"en":"The column appeared in a popular Israeli newspaper.","zh":"該專欄刊登於一份受歡迎的以色列報章。"},{"en":"A popular newspaper is a newspaper read by many people.","zh":"Popular newspaper 是由許多人閱讀的報章。"},{"en":"A popular newspaper may use clear language and everyday topics to reach a wide audience.","zh":"受歡迎的報章可能使用清晰語言和日常題目，以接觸廣泛讀者。"},{"en":"If a column appears in a popular newspaper, many readers may see it regularly.","zh":"如果專欄刊登於受歡迎的報章，許多讀者可能定期看到它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a newspaper with a large readership.","zh":"這個片語描述讀者眾多的報章。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the mystery of REM sleep","meaning":"快速眼動睡眠之謎","examples":[{"en":"The mystery of REM sleep is that it appears almost everywhere in certain animals.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠之謎在於它幾乎出現在某些動物中各處。"},{"en":"The mystery of REM sleep is the unanswered question of why this sleep stage is so common.","zh":"The mystery of REM sleep 是為何這個睡眠階段如此普遍但仍未解開的問題。"},{"en":"A scientist may call something a mystery when evidence exists but the explanation remains unclear.","zh":"當有證據但解釋仍不清楚時，科學家可能稱某事為謎。"},{"en":"If REM sleep is common yet not clearly essential, researchers need a better explanation for it.","zh":"如果快速眼動睡眠很常見但又不明顯必要，研究人員就需要更好解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights an unresolved scientific puzzle.","zh":"這個片語突顯一個未解決的科學謎題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"even though","meaning":"儘管……","examples":[{"en":"REM sleep is widespread even though it may not be essential.","zh":"儘管快速眼動睡眠可能不是必要的，它仍然很普遍。"},{"en":"Even though means despite the fact that.","zh":"Even though 指儘管某事實如此。"},{"en":"A student may keep studying even though the test is difficult.","zh":"儘管測驗困難，學生可能仍繼續溫習。"},{"en":"If REM sleep is common even though it may not be essential, its function remains puzzling.","zh":"如果快速眼動睡眠儘管可能不是必要仍然常見，其功能就仍令人困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces contrast between two facts.","zh":"這個片語引出兩個事實之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be ubiquitous","meaning":"無處不在；普遍存在","examples":[{"en":"REM sleep is ubiquitous among mammals and birds.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠在哺乳類動物和鳥類中普遍存在。"},{"en":"To be ubiquitous means to be found almost everywhere within a group or place.","zh":"To be ubiquitous 指在某群體或地方幾乎到處都能找到。"},{"en":"Smartphones are ubiquitous in many cities because nearly everyone carries one.","zh":"智能手機在許多城市中無處不在，因為幾乎每個人都攜帶一部。"},{"en":"If REM sleep is ubiquitous in mammals and birds, it may serve a widespread biological role.","zh":"如果快速眼動睡眠在哺乳類動物和鳥類中普遍存在，它可能有廣泛生物作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something extremely common.","zh":"這個片語描述某事極其常見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at least in","meaning":"至少在……之中","examples":[{"en":"REM sleep is common, at least in mammals and birds.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠很常見，至少在哺乳類動物和鳥類之中。"},{"en":"At least in means the statement is true for that group, even if not for all groups.","zh":"At least in 指某說法對該群體為真，即使不一定對所有群體為真。"},{"en":"Online learning is common, at least in large universities.","zh":"網上學習很常見，至少在大型大學中如此。"},{"en":"If REM sleep is found at least in mammals and birds, scientists should be careful before claiming it exists in all animals.","zh":"如果快速眼動睡眠至少在哺乳類動物和鳥類中被發現，科學家在聲稱它存在於所有動物時應謹慎。"},{"en":"This phrase limits a claim to a known area.","zh":"這個片語把主張限制在已知範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"that does not mean","meaning":"這並不代表……","examples":[{"en":"The presence of REM sleep does not mean that all animals dream.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠的存在並不代表所有動物都會造夢。"},{"en":"That does not mean introduces a warning that one fact should not be overinterpreted.","zh":"That does not mean 用來提醒人不要過度解讀一個事實。"},{"en":"A student is quiet in class; that does not mean they understand everything.","zh":"學生在課堂上安靜；這並不代表他明白所有東西。"},{"en":"If an animal has REM sleep, that alone does not prove it has human-like dreams.","zh":"如果一種動物有快速眼動睡眠，單憑這一點並不能證明它有人類般的夢。"},{"en":"This phrase prevents a false conclusion.","zh":"這個片語防止錯誤結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"physiological reasons","meaning":"生理原因","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers believe REM evolved for physiological reasons.","zh":"一些研究人員相信快速眼動睡眠因生理原因而演化。"},{"en":"Physiological reasons are causes related to how the body functions.","zh":"Physiological reasons 是與身體如何運作有關的原因。"},{"en":"Shivering happens for physiological reasons because it helps the body stay warm.","zh":"發抖有生理原因，因為它幫助身體保暖。"},{"en":"If REM sleep helps body temperature or brain repair, its reason may be physiological rather than psychological.","zh":"如果快速眼動睡眠幫助體溫或大腦修復，其原因可能是生理而非心理。"},{"en":"This phrase explains something through body processes.","zh":"這個片語透過身體過程解釋某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be unique about","meaning":"……的獨特之處","examples":[{"en":"Temperature regulation is one thing that is unique about mammals and birds.","zh":"體溫調節是哺乳類動物和鳥類的獨特之處之一。"},{"en":"To be unique about something means to be a special feature that distinguishes it from others.","zh":"To be unique about something 指作為把某物與其他事物區分開的特殊特徵。"},{"en":"One thing unique about humans is our complex use of language.","zh":"人類的獨特之處之一是我們複雜的語言使用。"},{"en":"If warm-blooded animals share a unique feature, that feature may explain a shared sleep pattern.","zh":"如果溫血動物共享一項獨特特徵，該特徵可能解釋共同睡眠模式。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what makes a group special.","zh":"這個片語指出令某群體特別的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"regulate body temperature","meaning":"調節體溫","examples":[{"en":"Mammals and birds regulate body temperature internally.","zh":"哺乳類動物和鳥類從體內調節體溫。"},{"en":"To regulate body temperature means to keep the body at a stable and suitable temperature.","zh":"To regulate body temperature 指令身體保持穩定而合適的溫度。"},{"en":"Sweating helps humans regulate body temperature on hot days.","zh":"出汗幫助人在炎熱日子調節體溫。"},{"en":"If animals can regulate body temperature, they can remain active in changing weather.","zh":"如果動物能調節體溫，它們可以在天氣變化中保持活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the body’s control of heat.","zh":"這個片語描述身體對熱量的控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"no good evidence","meaning":"沒有充分證據","examples":[{"en":"There is no good evidence that cold-blooded animals experience REM sleep.","zh":"沒有充分證據顯示冷血動物經歷快速眼動睡眠。"},{"en":"No good evidence means there is not enough reliable proof to support a claim.","zh":"No good evidence 指沒有足夠可靠證據支持某主張。"},{"en":"There is no good evidence that one night of cramming works better than regular study.","zh":"沒有充分證據顯示通宵死背比定期溫習更有效。"},{"en":"If no good evidence exists, scientists should avoid stating the claim as fact.","zh":"如果沒有充分證據，科學家應避免把該主張說成事實。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a claim is not well supported.","zh":"這個片語顯示某主張缺乏良好支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cold-blooded animal","meaning":"冷血動物","examples":[{"en":"No cold-blooded animal has been clearly shown to have REM sleep.","zh":"尚未有冷血動物被清楚證明有快速眼動睡眠。"},{"en":"A cold-blooded animal is an animal whose body temperature depends mainly on the environment.","zh":"Cold-blooded animal 是體溫主要取決於環境的動物。"},{"en":"Lizards and many fish are cold-blooded animals.","zh":"蜥蜴和許多魚類都是冷血動物。"},{"en":"If the environment is cold, a cold-blooded animal may become slower and less active.","zh":"如果環境寒冷，冷血動物可能變得較慢和較不活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts reptiles, fish, and amphibians with warm-blooded mammals and birds.","zh":"這個片語把爬行類、魚類和兩棲類與溫血哺乳類和鳥類作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"heat up the brain","meaning":"令大腦升溫","examples":[{"en":"REM sleep may heat up the brain.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠可能令大腦升溫。"},{"en":"To heat up the brain means to raise the brain’s temperature or activity level.","zh":"To heat up the brain 指提高大腦溫度或活動水平。"},{"en":"Physical exercise can heat up the body, while mental effort can make the brain highly active.","zh":"身體運動可以令身體升溫，而心理努力可以令大腦高度活躍。"},{"en":"If REM sleep warms the brain, it may help maintain healthy brain function.","zh":"如果快速眼動睡眠令大腦變暖，它可能幫助維持健康大腦功能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible physiological effect of sleep.","zh":"這個片語描述睡眠的一種可能生理作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cool it off","meaning":"令大腦降溫","examples":[{"en":"Non-REM sleep may cool the brain off.","zh":"非快速眼動睡眠可能令大腦降溫。"},{"en":"To cool it off means to lower its temperature or reduce its activity.","zh":"To cool it off 指降低其溫度或減少其活動。"},{"en":"After exercise, sitting in the shade can help cool the body off.","zh":"運動後坐在陰涼處可以幫助身體降溫。"},{"en":"If non-REM sleep cools the brain, alternating sleep stages may help balance brain temperature.","zh":"如果非快速眼動睡眠令大腦降溫，交替睡眠階段可能幫助平衡大腦溫度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing heat or activity.","zh":"這個片語描述降低熱度或活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"changing sleep cycles","meaning":"不斷轉換的睡眠週期","examples":[{"en":"Changing sleep cycles may help maintain the brain.","zh":"不斷轉換的睡眠週期可能幫助維持大腦。"},{"en":"Changing sleep cycles are shifts between different stages of sleep during the night.","zh":"Changing sleep cycles 是夜間不同睡眠階段之間的轉換。"},{"en":"A sleeper may move through light sleep, deep sleep, and REM sleep several times.","zh":"睡眠者可能多次經歷淺層睡眠、深層睡眠和快速眼動睡眠。"},{"en":"If sleep cycles change regularly, the brain may get different kinds of rest and activity.","zh":"如果睡眠週期定期轉換，大腦可能獲得不同種類的休息和活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the natural alternation of sleep stages.","zh":"這個片語描述睡眠階段的自然交替。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"allow the brain to repair itself","meaning":"讓大腦自行修復","examples":[{"en":"Alternating sleep stages may allow the brain to repair itself.","zh":"交替睡眠階段可能讓大腦自行修復。"},{"en":"To allow the brain to repair itself means to create conditions for the brain to recover and restore normal function.","zh":"To allow the brain to repair itself 指創造條件，讓大腦恢復並重建正常功能。"},{"en":"Good sleep may allow the brain to recover after a stressful day of study.","zh":"良好睡眠可能讓大腦在壓力大的學習日後恢復。"},{"en":"If sleep stages support repair, poor sleep may leave the brain less refreshed.","zh":"如果睡眠階段支持修復，睡眠差可能令大腦較不清爽。"},{"en":"This phrase connects sleep with biological recovery.","zh":"這個片語把睡眠與生物修復連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"fill a basic physiological function","meaning":"發揮基本生理功能","examples":[{"en":"REM sleep may fill a basic physiological function.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠可能發揮基本生理功能。"},{"en":"To fill a basic physiological function means to perform a simple but important job for the body.","zh":"To fill a basic physiological function 指為身體執行簡單但重要的工作。"},{"en":"Sweating fills a basic physiological function by helping control body temperature.","zh":"出汗透過幫助控制體溫來發揮基本生理功能。"},{"en":"If REM sleep helps maintain the brain, its function may be physical rather than psychological.","zh":"如果快速眼動睡眠幫助維持大腦，它的功能可能是身體上的，而不是心理上的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an essential body-related role.","zh":"這個片語描述與身體有關的基本作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"epiphenomenon","meaning":"附帶現象","examples":[{"en":"Dreams may be an epiphenomenon rather than the main purpose of REM.","zh":"夢可能是附帶現象，而不是快速眼動睡眠的主要目的。"},{"en":"An epiphenomenon is a side effect that appears with a process but is not its main cause or purpose.","zh":"Epiphenomenon 是伴隨某過程出現，但不是其主要原因或目的的副作用。"},{"en":"Steam above a kettle is an epiphenomenon of boiling water, not the reason the water boils.","zh":"水壺上的蒸氣是水沸騰的附帶現象，而不是水沸騰的原因。"},{"en":"If dreams are an epiphenomenon, REM sleep may exist for another biological reason.","zh":"如果夢是附帶現象，快速眼動睡眠可能因另一個生物原因而存在。"},{"en":"This word describes something secondary, not central.","zh":"這個詞描述次要而非核心的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"extraneous by-product","meaning":"非必要的副產品","examples":[{"en":"Dreams may be merely an extraneous by-product of REM sleep.","zh":"夢可能只是快速眼動睡眠的非必要副產品。"},{"en":"An extraneous by-product is an unnecessary side result of a process.","zh":"Extraneous by-product 是某過程產生的不必要附帶結果。"},{"en":"Noise from a machine may be an extraneous by-product of its operation.","zh":"機器運作時的噪音可能是其運作的非必要副產品。"},{"en":"If dreams are only a by-product, the real function of REM may lie elsewhere.","zh":"如果夢只是副產品，快速眼動睡眠的真正功能可能在別處。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something is produced incidentally, not intentionally or essentially.","zh":"這個片語暗示某事是偶然產生，而不是有意或必要產生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"foam on beer","meaning":"啤酒上的泡沫","examples":[{"en":"Siegel compared dreams to foam on beer.","zh":"Siegel把夢比作啤酒上的泡沫。"},{"en":"Foam on beer is the layer of bubbles on top of beer, used here as an image of something extra.","zh":"Foam on beer 是啤酒表面的氣泡層，在這裡用作額外東西的意象。"},{"en":"A chef may say decoration is like foam on beer if it looks nice but is not the main food.","zh":"如果裝飾好看但不是主菜，廚師可能說它像啤酒上的泡沫。"},{"en":"If dreams are like foam on beer, they may accompany REM sleep without being its purpose.","zh":"如果夢像啤酒上的泡沫，它們可能伴隨快速眼動睡眠，但不是其目的。"},{"en":"This phrase is a metaphor for a visible but secondary by-product.","zh":"這個片語是可見但次要副產品的比喻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"whatever the function of","meaning":"不論……的功能是甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Whatever the function of dreams, they may still be useful in therapy.","zh":"不論夢的功能是甚麼，它們在治療中仍可能有用。"},{"en":"Whatever the function of something means no matter what its true purpose is.","zh":"Whatever the function of something 指不管某事真正目的為何。"},{"en":"Whatever the function of homework, it should help students learn rather than simply keep them busy.","zh":"不論功課的功能是甚麼，它都應幫助學生學習，而不是只令他們忙碌。"},{"en":"If scientists disagree about why dreams exist, therapists may still use them practically.","zh":"如果科學家不同意夢為何存在，治療師仍可能實際運用它們。"},{"en":"This phrase allows a discussion to continue despite uncertainty.","zh":"這個片語讓討論在不確定下仍能繼續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"play a role in therapy","meaning":"在治療中發揮作用","examples":[{"en":"Dreams can play a role in therapy during the day.","zh":"夢可以在日間治療中發揮作用。"},{"en":"To play a role in therapy means to be used as part of treatment or counselling.","zh":"To play a role in therapy 指被用作治療或輔導的一部分。"},{"en":"Drawing may play a role in therapy for children who struggle to explain feelings in words.","zh":"對難以用文字解釋感受的兒童來說，繪畫可能在治療中發揮作用。"},{"en":"If dreams reveal hidden worries, discussing them may help treatment.","zh":"如果夢揭示隱藏憂慮，討論它們可能有助治療。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something contributing to a therapeutic process.","zh":"這個片語描述某事對治療過程作出貢獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"during the day","meaning":"在日間","examples":[{"en":"Dreams experienced at night may be discussed during the day.","zh":"夜間經歷的夢可能在日間被討論。"},{"en":"During the day means in the daytime, after morning and before night.","zh":"During the day 指白天，即早上之後、夜晚之前。"},{"en":"A person may write down a dream during the day before the memory fades.","zh":"一個人可能在日間寫下夢，以免記憶消退。"},{"en":"If night dreams are discussed during the day, they can become material for reflection.","zh":"如果夜間的夢在日間被討論，它們可以成為反思材料。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts daytime activity with night-time sleep.","zh":"這個片語把白天活動與夜間睡眠作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the use of dreams in therapy","meaning":"在治療中運用夢境","examples":[{"en":"Clara Hill has studied the use of dreams in therapy.","zh":"Clara Hill研究過在治療中運用夢境。"},{"en":"The use of dreams in therapy means discussing or analysing dreams as part of counselling or psychological treatment.","zh":"The use of dreams in therapy 指把討論或分析夢境作為輔導或心理治療的一部分。"},{"en":"A therapist may ask a patient how a dream made them feel, rather than simply what happened in it.","zh":"治療師可能問病人一個夢令他有甚麼感覺，而不只是夢中發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"If dream discussion helps patients see hidden concerns, it can support therapy.","zh":"如果夢境討論幫助病人看見隱藏關注，它可以支持治療。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dreams as a therapeutic tool.","zh":"這個片語描述把夢作為治療工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a backdoor into","meaning":"進入……的間接途徑","examples":[{"en":"Dreams may provide a backdoor into a patient’s thinking.","zh":"夢可能提供進入病人思想的間接途徑。"},{"en":"A backdoor into something is an indirect way to reach or understand it.","zh":"A backdoor into something 是到達或理解某事的間接方法。"},{"en":"A child’s drawing may provide a backdoor into feelings they cannot yet explain.","zh":"孩子的畫可能提供進入他們尚未能解釋的感受的間接途徑。"},{"en":"If patients find direct questions difficult, dreams may offer another route into their thoughts.","zh":"如果病人覺得直接問題困難，夢可能提供另一條進入其思想的路徑。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an indirect but useful access point.","zh":"這個片語暗示一個間接但有用的入口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"reveal things about","meaning":"揭示關於……的事情","examples":[{"en":"Dreams may reveal things about a person that were previously hidden.","zh":"夢可能揭示關於一個人以前隱藏的事情。"},{"en":"To reveal things about someone means to show information about their feelings, thoughts, or character.","zh":"To reveal things about someone 指顯示關於某人感受、思想或性格的資料。"},{"en":"A student’s choice of story may reveal things about what they value.","zh":"學生選擇的故事可能揭示關於他重視甚麼的事情。"},{"en":"If dreams reveal hidden fears, therapists may better understand the patient.","zh":"如果夢揭示隱藏恐懼，治療師可能更理解病人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bringing unknown information into view.","zh":"這個片語描述把未知資料呈現出來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"not know something was there","meaning":"不知道某事物原來存在","examples":[{"en":"Dreams may uncover feelings that patients did not know were there.","zh":"夢可能揭示病人不知道原來存在的感受。"},{"en":"To not know something was there means to be unaware that a feeling, memory, or problem existed.","zh":"To not know something was there 指不知道某種感受、記憶或問題存在。"},{"en":"A student may not know anxiety is there until they freeze during a presentation.","zh":"學生可能直到演講時僵住，才知道焦慮原來存在。"},{"en":"If a dream shows fear or anger, the person may realise the emotion was already inside them.","zh":"如果夢顯示恐懼或憤怒，當事人可能意識到該情緒本來已在內心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes discovering something hidden in oneself.","zh":"這個片語描述發現自己內在隱藏的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"train therapists to","meaning":"訓練治療師去……","examples":[{"en":"Hill trains therapists to work with patients’ dreams.","zh":"Hill訓練治療師去運用病人的夢境。"},{"en":"To train therapists to do something means to teach counsellors or mental-health professionals how to use a method.","zh":"To train therapists to do something 指教導輔導員或心理健康專業人士如何使用某種方法。"},{"en":"A clinic may train therapists to help children talk about grief safely.","zh":"診所可能訓練治療師去幫助兒童安全地談論悲傷。"},{"en":"If therapists are trained to discuss dreams, they may use them more carefully and respectfully.","zh":"如果治療師受訓去討論夢境，他們可能更謹慎和尊重地使用夢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes professional preparation for a treatment skill.","zh":"這個片語描述為治療技能作專業準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"work with patients’ dreams","meaning":"運用病人的夢境","examples":[{"en":"Some therapists work with patients’ dreams during counselling.","zh":"一些治療師在輔導中運用病人的夢境。"},{"en":"To work with patients’ dreams means to discuss, explore, and use dreams as part of therapy.","zh":"To work with patients’ dreams 指把夢境作為治療的一部分來討論、探索和運用。"},{"en":"A therapist may ask what a dream scene reminds the patient of in daily life.","zh":"治療師可能問病人夢中場景令他想起日常生活中的甚麼。"},{"en":"If dreams contain repeated fears, working with them may help the patient understand those fears.","zh":"如果夢包含反覆恐懼，運用這些夢可能幫助病人理解恐懼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using dream material in treatment.","zh":"這個片語描述在治療中使用夢境材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in essence","meaning":"本質上","examples":[{"en":"In essence, these therapists continue part of Freud’s approach.","zh":"本質上，這些治療師延續了佛洛伊德方法的一部分。"},{"en":"In essence means basically or in the most important sense.","zh":"In essence 指基本上，或從最重要意義上來說。"},{"en":"In essence, a good example sentence should teach the meaning, not just contain the word.","zh":"本質上，好的例句應教出意思，而不只是包含該詞。"},{"en":"If two methods look different but share the same main idea, they may be similar in essence.","zh":"如果兩種方法看起來不同但共享同一主要想法，它們本質上可能相似。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the core point.","zh":"這個片語給出核心重點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"heirs to Freud","meaning":"佛洛伊德的繼承者","examples":[{"en":"Modern dream therapists may be considered heirs to Freud.","zh":"現代夢境治療師可被視為佛洛伊德的繼承者。"},{"en":"Heirs to Freud are people who continue, inherit, or develop Freud’s ideas.","zh":"Heirs to Freud 是延續、繼承或發展佛洛伊德思想的人。"},{"en":"A modern teacher who uses an old educator’s methods may be called an heir to that tradition.","zh":"使用舊教育家方法的現代老師，可被稱為該傳統的繼承者。"},{"en":"If therapists still analyse hidden meanings in dreams, they may be seen as following Freud’s legacy.","zh":"如果治療師仍分析夢中的隱藏意義，他們可能被視為延續佛洛伊德的遺產。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intellectual inheritance, not family inheritance.","zh":"這個片語描述思想上的繼承，而不是家庭繼承。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"dream imagery","meaning":"夢境意象","examples":[{"en":"Therapists use dream imagery to explore emotional conflicts.","zh":"治療師使用夢境意象來探索情緒衝突。"},{"en":"Dream imagery means the pictures, scenes, symbols, or visual details that appear in dreams.","zh":"Dream imagery 指出現在夢中的圖像、場景、象徵或視覺細節。"},{"en":"A dream of being lost in a school may create imagery of corridors, locked doors, and empty rooms.","zh":"迷失在學校中的夢可能創造走廊、鎖上的門和空房間等意象。"},{"en":"If dream imagery repeats, it may point to a worry the person has not fully faced.","zh":"如果夢境意象反覆出現，它可能指向當事人尚未完全面對的憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the visual content of dreams.","zh":"這個片語指夢的視覺內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"uncover hidden emotions","meaning":"揭示隱藏情緒","examples":[{"en":"Dream analysis may uncover hidden emotions and feelings.","zh":"夢境分析可能揭示隱藏情緒和感受。"},{"en":"To uncover hidden emotions means to reveal feelings that were not clearly recognised before.","zh":"To uncover hidden emotions 指揭示以前沒有清楚意識到的感受。"},{"en":"Talking about a dream may uncover sadness that a patient has been avoiding.","zh":"談論一個夢可能揭示病人一直逃避的悲傷。"},{"en":"If hidden emotions are uncovered, therapy can address the real source of distress.","zh":"如果隱藏情緒被揭示，治療就可以處理痛苦的真正來源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bringing buried feelings into awareness.","zh":"這個片語描述把埋藏感受帶入意識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"provide clues to","meaning":"為……提供線索","examples":[{"en":"Dreams may provide clues to serious psychological conditions.","zh":"夢可能為嚴重心理狀況提供線索。"},{"en":"To provide clues to something means to give signs that help people understand or investigate it.","zh":"To provide clues to something 指提供有助人理解或調查某事的跡象。"},{"en":"A student’s repeated mistakes can provide clues to what grammar they have not understood.","zh":"學生反覆犯錯可以為他不明白哪個文法提供線索。"},{"en":"If dream patterns change suddenly, they may give therapists clues about mental health.","zh":"如果夢境模式突然改變，它們可能為治療師提供關於心理健康的線索。"},{"en":"This phrase describes indirect evidence, not full proof.","zh":"這個片語描述間接證據，而不是完整證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the nature of","meaning":"……的本質","examples":[{"en":"Dream patterns may reveal the nature of certain mental illnesses.","zh":"夢境模式可能揭示某些精神疾病的本質。"},{"en":"The nature of something means its basic character, qualities, or true form.","zh":"The nature of something 指某事物的基本性質、特點或真實形式。"},{"en":"A teacher may study the nature of students’ mistakes before planning a lesson.","zh":"老師可能先研究學生錯誤的本質，再計劃課堂。"},{"en":"If dreams reveal the nature of an illness, they may show what kind of problem it is.","zh":"如果夢揭示疾病的本質，它們可能顯示那是甚麼類型的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase asks what something is really like.","zh":"這個片語詢問某事實際上是甚麼樣子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"serious mental illnesses","meaning":"嚴重精神疾病","examples":[{"en":"Dreams may differ in people with serious mental illnesses.","zh":"患有嚴重精神疾病的人，其夢可能有所不同。"},{"en":"Serious mental illnesses are severe conditions that significantly affect thinking, mood, behaviour, or daily life.","zh":"Serious mental illnesses 是嚴重影響思考、心情、行為或日常生活的疾病。"},{"en":"A person with a serious mental illness may need long-term medical and social support.","zh":"患有嚴重精神疾病的人可能需要長期醫療和社會支援。"},{"en":"If dreams change in serious illness, researchers may study them as signs of mental functioning.","zh":"如果夢在嚴重疾病中改變，研究人員可能把它們作為心理運作的跡象來研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes severe psychological conditions, not ordinary stress.","zh":"這個片語描述嚴重心理狀況，而不是普通壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"schizophrenics","meaning":"思覺失調症患者","examples":[{"en":"Schizophrenics may experience dreams of poorer quality.","zh":"思覺失調症患者可能經歷質素較差的夢。"},{"en":"Schizophrenics are people with schizophrenia, a serious mental illness affecting thought, perception, and behaviour.","zh":"Schizophrenics 是患有思覺失調症的人；這是一種影響思想、感知和行為的嚴重精神疾病。"},{"en":"A person with schizophrenia may need medication, therapy, and community support.","zh":"思覺失調症患者可能需要藥物、治療和社區支援。"},{"en":"If schizophrenic patients report unusual dreams, researchers may compare them with dreams of healthy sleepers.","zh":"如果思覺失調症患者報告異常夢境，研究人員可能把它們與健康睡眠者的夢作比較。"},{"en":"This word refers to people with a specific psychiatric condition.","zh":"這個詞指患有特定精神疾病的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"poor-quality dreams","meaning":"質素較差的夢","examples":[{"en":"Some patients report poor-quality dreams with limited social content.","zh":"一些病人報告質素較差且社交內容有限的夢。"},{"en":"Poor-quality dreams are dreams that may be less vivid, less detailed, or less socially rich.","zh":"Poor-quality dreams 是可能較不鮮明、較少細節或社交內容較不豐富的夢。"},{"en":"A poor-quality dream may contain objects and scenes but few people or emotions.","zh":"質素較差的夢可能包含物件和場景，但少有人物或情緒。"},{"en":"If dreams have limited content, they may reveal something about the dreamer’s mental state.","zh":"如果夢內容有限，它們可能揭示夢者心理狀態的某些方面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dreams judged as less developed or less rich.","zh":"這個片語描述被判斷為較不完整或較不豐富的夢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"objects rather than people","meaning":"物件而不是人物","examples":[{"en":"Their dreams may focus on objects rather than people.","zh":"他們的夢可能集中於物件而不是人物。"},{"en":"Objects rather than people means things are emphasised instead of human characters.","zh":"Objects rather than people 指重點放在物件，而不是人類角色。"},{"en":"A lonely child’s drawing may show buildings and toys rather than people.","zh":"孤獨孩子的畫可能展示建築物和玩具，而不是人物。"},{"en":"If dreams focus on objects rather than people, they may contain less social interaction.","zh":"如果夢集中於物件而不是人物，它們可能包含較少社交互動。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly contrasts things with human beings.","zh":"這個片語清楚對比事物與人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"understand human behaviour","meaning":"理解人類行為","examples":[{"en":"Dream research may help us understand human behaviour.","zh":"夢境研究可能幫助我們理解人類行為。"},{"en":"To understand human behaviour means to know why people think, feel, choose, and act as they do.","zh":"To understand human behaviour 指明白人為何如此思考、感受、選擇和行動。"},{"en":"Teachers try to understand student behaviour before deciding how to respond.","zh":"老師在決定如何回應前，會嘗試理解學生行為。"},{"en":"If dreams reveal hidden emotion, they may help explain waking behaviour.","zh":"如果夢揭示隱藏情緒，它們可能幫助解釋清醒時的行為。"},{"en":"This phrase connects psychological evidence with real-life actions.","zh":"這個片語把心理證據與現實行動連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a big piece of it","meaning":"當中的重要一環","examples":[{"en":"Dreaming may represent a big piece of human psychology.","zh":"造夢可能代表人類心理學當中的重要一環。"},{"en":"A big piece of it means an important part of a larger subject or problem.","zh":"A big piece of it 指較大主題或問題中的重要部分。"},{"en":"Sleep is a big piece of student health because it affects memory, mood, and energy.","zh":"睡眠是學生健康的重要一環，因為它影響記憶、情緒和精力。"},{"en":"If dreaming is a big piece of psychology, ignoring it would leave our understanding incomplete.","zh":"如果造夢是心理學的重要一環，忽視它會令我們的理解不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important component, not the whole thing.","zh":"這個片語描述重要組成部分，而不是全部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"our own storytelling time","meaning":"我們自己講故事的時間","examples":[{"en":"Cartwright describes dreaming as our own storytelling time.","zh":"Cartwright把造夢描述為我們自己講故事的時間。"},{"en":"Our own storytelling time means a private period when the mind creates stories from feelings, memories, and concerns.","zh":"Our own storytelling time 指心智從感受、記憶和關注中創造故事的私人時間。"},{"en":"A child may use bedtime as storytelling time to make sense of the day.","zh":"孩子可能把睡前時間用作講故事的時間，以理解一天的經歷。"},{"en":"If dreams are storytelling time, they may organise emotional experiences into scenes and plots.","zh":"如果夢是講故事的時間，它們可能把情緒經驗組織成場景和情節。"},{"en":"This phrase presents dreaming as personal narrative-making.","zh":"這個片語把造夢呈現為個人的敘事創造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"help us know who we are","meaning":"幫助我們了解自己","examples":[{"en":"Dreams may help us understand who we are.","zh":"夢可能幫助我們了解自己是誰。"},{"en":"To help us know who we are means to help us recognise our values, fears, hopes, and identity.","zh":"To help us know who we are 指幫助我們認出自己的價值觀、恐懼、希望和身份。"},{"en":"A difficult choice may help a student know who they are and what they truly care about.","zh":"困難選擇可能幫助學生了解自己是誰，以及真正重視甚麼。"},{"en":"If dreams reveal repeated concerns, they may show what matters deeply to us.","zh":"如果夢揭示反覆關注，它們可能顯示我們內心深處重視甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase connects dreams with self-understanding.","zh":"這個片語把夢與自我理解連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"where we are going","meaning":"我們正走向何方","examples":[{"en":"Dreams may reflect where we believe our lives are going.","zh":"夢可能反映我們相信自己人生正走向何方。"},{"en":"Where we are going means the direction our life, plans, or future seems to be taking.","zh":"Where we are going 指我們的生活、計劃或未來似乎正在走向的方向。"},{"en":"A student choosing subjects may wonder where they are going in study and career.","zh":"選科的學生可能思考自己在學業和職業上正走向何方。"},{"en":"If dreams show anxiety about change, they may reflect uncertainty about the future.","zh":"如果夢顯示對改變的焦慮，它們可能反映對未來方向的不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to life direction, not physical travel only.","zh":"這個片語指人生方向，而不只是實際旅行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"how we are going to get there","meaning":"我們將如何達成目標","examples":[{"en":"Dreams may help us imagine how to achieve our goals.","zh":"夢可能幫助我們想像如何達成目標。"},{"en":"How we are going to get there means the way or steps by which we reach a future goal.","zh":"How we are going to get there 指我們達到未來目標的方法或步驟。"},{"en":"A student who wants to study abroad must plan how they are going to get there.","zh":"想出國讀書的學生必須計劃自己將如何達成目標。"},{"en":"If dreams explore possible choices, they may help us think about paths forward.","zh":"如果夢探索可能選擇，它們可能幫助我們思考前進路徑。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on method and progress toward a goal.","zh":"這個片語著重方法和朝目標前進的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"study depression in","meaning":"研究……的抑鬱情況","examples":[{"en":"Cartwright studied depression in divorced men and women.","zh":"Cartwright研究離婚男女的抑鬱情況。"},{"en":"To study depression in a group means to research how depression appears or changes among those people.","zh":"To study depression in a group 指研究抑鬱在該群體中如何出現或變化。"},{"en":"Psychologists may study depression in teenagers after major exams.","zh":"心理學家可能研究青少年在大型考試後的抑鬱情況。"},{"en":"If researchers study depression in divorced adults, they may learn how people recover from emotional loss.","zh":"如果研究人員研究離婚成人的抑鬱情況，他們可能了解人如何從情感失落中恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the group being researched.","zh":"這個片語指出被研究的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"divorced men and women","meaning":"離婚男女","examples":[{"en":"The research involved divorced men and women.","zh":"這項研究涉及離婚男女。"},{"en":"Divorced men and women are adults whose marriages have legally ended.","zh":"Divorced men and women 是婚姻已依法結束的成年人。"},{"en":"Divorced men and women may experience sadness, stress, financial change, or relief after separation.","zh":"離婚男女在分開後可能經歷悲傷、壓力、財政變化或釋然。"},{"en":"If researchers study this group, they can examine how people cope after a major life change.","zh":"如果研究人員研究這個群體，他們可以考察人們如何應對重大人生變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people by marital status.","zh":"這個片語以婚姻狀況描述人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"vivid dreams with strong storylines","meaning":"情節鮮明而連貫的夢","examples":[{"en":"Good dreamers experience vivid dreams with strong storylines.","zh":"善於造夢的人會經歷情節鮮明而連貫的夢。"},{"en":"Vivid dreams with strong storylines are clear, memorable dreams with organised events like a story.","zh":"Vivid dreams with strong storylines 是清晰、令人記得，並有像故事般有組織事件的夢。"},{"en":"A person may wake from such a dream and describe the beginning, conflict, and ending.","zh":"一個人可能從這類夢醒來後，描述開頭、衝突和結局。"},{"en":"If dreams have strong storylines, they may help organise confusing emotions.","zh":"如果夢有連貫情節，它們可能幫助整理混亂情緒。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts rich, structured dreams with vague dream fragments.","zh":"這個片語把豐富、有結構的夢與模糊夢片段作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be less likely to remain depressed","meaning":"較少可能持續抑鬱","examples":[{"en":"Good dreamers were less likely to remain depressed.","zh":"善於造夢的人較少可能持續抑鬱。"},{"en":"To be less likely to remain depressed means to have a lower chance of staying depressed over time.","zh":"To be less likely to remain depressed 指隨時間持續抑鬱的機會較低。"},{"en":"A person with strong social support may be less likely to remain depressed after a crisis.","zh":"有強大社交支援的人，在危機後可能較少持續抑鬱。"},{"en":"If dreaming helps process painful emotions, people may recover from depression more easily.","zh":"如果造夢幫助處理痛苦情緒，人們可能更容易從抑鬱中恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase links a lower risk with emotional recovery.","zh":"這個片語把較低風險與情緒康復連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"diffuse strong emotions","meaning":"紓緩強烈情緒","examples":[{"en":"Dreaming may help diffuse strong emotions.","zh":"造夢可能幫助紓緩強烈情緒。"},{"en":"To diffuse strong emotions means to reduce their intensity so they feel less overwhelming.","zh":"To diffuse strong emotions 指降低情緒強度，使其不那麼壓倒人。"},{"en":"Talking to a trusted friend can diffuse anger after an argument.","zh":"與可信朋友談話可以在爭吵後紓緩憤怒。"},{"en":"If dreams replay difficult feelings safely, they may help the mind calm down.","zh":"如果夢安全地重播困難感受，它們可能幫助心智平靜下來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes softening powerful feelings.","zh":"這個片語描述減弱強烈感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"mental-health activity","meaning":"有助精神健康的活動","examples":[{"en":"Cartwright describes dreaming as a mental-health activity.","zh":"Cartwright把造夢描述為有助精神健康的活動。"},{"en":"A mental-health activity is something that supports emotional balance, coping, or psychological well-being.","zh":"Mental-health activity 是支持情緒平衡、應對能力或心理福祉的活動。"},{"en":"Journalling can be a mental-health activity if it helps people understand their feelings.","zh":"如果寫日記幫助人理解感受，它可以是有助精神健康的活動。"},{"en":"If dreaming helps people process grief, it may support mental health.","zh":"如果造夢幫助人處理悲傷，它可能支持精神健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an activity that may protect or improve the mind.","zh":"這個片語描述可能保護或改善心智的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"which paragraph contains","meaning":"哪一段包含……","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which paragraph contains each piece of information.","zh":"學生識別哪一段包含每項資料。"},{"en":"Which paragraph contains means which section of the passage includes the required idea or detail.","zh":"Which paragraph contains 指文章哪一部分包括所需想法或細節。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students must find which paragraph contains a scientist’s opinion.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生必須找出哪一段包含某科學家的意見。"},{"en":"If two paragraphs mention sleep, students should choose the one that contains the exact information.","zh":"如果兩段都提到睡眠，學生應選擇包含準確資料的那一段。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in paragraph-matching tasks.","zh":"這個片語常見於段落配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reference to","meaning":"提及……","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for a reference to a versatile artist.","zh":"題目要求找出提及一位多才多藝藝術家的地方。"},{"en":"A reference to something is a mention of it in speech or writing.","zh":"Reference to something 是在說話或寫作中提到某事。"},{"en":"A passage may include a reference to a famous scientist without giving much detail.","zh":"文章可能提及一位著名科學家，但沒有提供太多細節。"},{"en":"If students find a reference to an artist, they should check what the text says about that person.","zh":"如果學生找到提及藝術家的地方，他們應檢查文本怎樣描述該人物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mention, not necessarily a long explanation.","zh":"這個片語描述提到某事，而不一定是長篇解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"versatile artist","meaning":"多才多藝的藝術家","examples":[{"en":"The patient was versatile enough to work as a lawyer, painter and editor.","zh":"該病人多才多藝，足以擔任律師、畫家和編輯。"},{"en":"A versatile artist is a creative person who can work skilfully in several different areas.","zh":"Versatile artist 是能在幾個不同範疇熟練工作的創意人士。"},{"en":"A versatile artist may paint portraits, design posters, write poems, and teach children.","zh":"多才多藝的藝術家可能畫肖像、設計海報、寫詩和教孩子。"},{"en":"If someone has many talents, one injury or limitation may not define their whole ability.","zh":"如果某人有許多才能，一次受傷或限制可能不會定義他的全部能力。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights flexibility and wide creative skill.","zh":"這個片語突顯靈活性和廣泛創意技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"discussion of whether","meaning":"對是否……的討論","examples":[{"en":"The passage includes a discussion of whether animals dream.","zh":"文章包括對動物是否造夢的討論。"},{"en":"A discussion of whether something is true examines both the possibility and the uncertainty.","zh":"Discussion of whether something is true 會檢視某事的可能性和不確定性。"},{"en":"A class may have a discussion of whether homework should be optional.","zh":"班上可能進行對功課是否應自選的討論。"},{"en":"If evidence is unclear, a discussion of whether something happens should avoid simple yes-or-no claims.","zh":"如果證據不清楚，對某事是否發生的討論應避免簡單的是或否主張。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a debated question.","zh":"這個片語引出有爭議的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"mammals and birds","meaning":"哺乳類動物和鳥類","examples":[{"en":"REM sleep is widespread among mammals and birds.","zh":"快速眼動睡眠在哺乳類動物和鳥類中很普遍。"},{"en":"Mammals and birds are two groups of warm-blooded animals.","zh":"Mammals and birds 是兩類溫血動物。"},{"en":"Humans, dogs, and whales are mammals, while sparrows and eagles are birds.","zh":"人類、狗和鯨魚是哺乳類動物，而麻雀和鷹是鳥類。"},{"en":"If REM sleep appears in mammals and birds, it may be linked with warm-blooded biology.","zh":"如果快速眼動睡眠出現在哺乳類動物和鳥類中，它可能與溫血生物學有關。"},{"en":"This phrase groups animals that regulate body temperature internally.","zh":"這個片語把能從體內調節體溫的動物歸為一組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be associated with therapeutic benefits","meaning":"與治療效益有關","examples":[{"en":"Dream exploration may be associated with therapeutic benefits.","zh":"探索夢境可能與治療效益有關。"},{"en":"To be associated with therapeutic benefits means to be linked with helpful effects in treatment.","zh":"To be associated with therapeutic benefits 指與治療中的有幫助效果有關。"},{"en":"Talking about painful memories may be associated with therapeutic benefits when guided by a trained counsellor.","zh":"在受訓輔導員引導下談論痛苦記憶，可能與治療效益有關。"},{"en":"If dream discussion helps patients understand emotions, it may support treatment.","zh":"如果夢境討論幫助病人理解情緒，它可能支持治療。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a connection with healing or counselling value.","zh":"這個片語顯示與治療或輔導價值有關。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"therapeutic benefits","meaning":"治療效益","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers believe dreams offer therapeutic benefits.","zh":"一些研究人員相信夢提供治療效益。"},{"en":"Therapeutic benefits are helpful effects that support treatment, healing, or emotional recovery.","zh":"Therapeutic benefits 是支持治療、康復或情緒恢復的有幫助效果。"},{"en":"Exercise may have therapeutic benefits for people with mild anxiety.","zh":"運動可能對輕度焦慮人士有治療效益。"},{"en":"If discussing dreams reduces distress, the discussion may provide therapeutic benefits.","zh":"如果討論夢境減少痛苦，該討論可能提供治療效益。"},{"en":"This phrase describes health-related advantages, especially in treatment.","zh":"這個片語描述與健康有關的好處，尤其在治療中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"well-being","meaning":"身心健康","examples":[{"en":"Dreaming may contribute to emotional well-being.","zh":"造夢可能有助情緒上的身心健康。"},{"en":"Well-being means a person’s overall physical, mental, and emotional health.","zh":"Well-being 指一個人的整體身體、心理和情緒健康。"},{"en":"Enough sleep, supportive friends, and safe housing can improve well-being.","zh":"足夠睡眠、支持性的朋友和安全住屋可以改善身心健康。"},{"en":"If dreams help regulate emotions, they may support a person’s well-being.","zh":"如果夢幫助調節情緒，它們可能支持一個人的身心健康。"},{"en":"This word describes more than happiness; it includes general health and balance.","zh":"這個詞描述的不只是快樂，也包括整體健康和平衡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"advanced scientific technology","meaning":"先進科學技術","examples":[{"en":"Researchers use advanced scientific technology to examine REM sleep.","zh":"研究人員使用先進科學技術檢查快速眼動睡眠。"},{"en":"Advanced scientific technology means modern, complex tools used to study difficult scientific questions.","zh":"Advanced scientific technology 指用來研究困難科學問題的現代複雜工具。"},{"en":"Hospitals use advanced scientific technology to scan the brain and diagnose disease.","zh":"醫院使用先進科學技術掃描大腦和診斷疾病。"},{"en":"If dream research uses advanced technology, scientists can observe processes once hidden from view.","zh":"如果夢境研究使用先進技術，科學家可以觀察曾經看不見的過程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes powerful modern research equipment.","zh":"這個片語描述強大的現代研究設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"investigate the REM stage","meaning":"研究快速眼動睡眠階段","examples":[{"en":"Brain-imaging equipment can investigate the REM stage.","zh":"腦部影像設備可以研究快速眼動睡眠階段。"},{"en":"To investigate the REM stage means to study what happens during rapid-eye-movement sleep.","zh":"To investigate the REM stage 指研究快速眼動睡眠期間發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Researchers may investigate the REM stage by recording eye movement, brain activity, and dream reports.","zh":"研究人員可能透過記錄眼動、大腦活動和夢境報告來研究快速眼動睡眠階段。"},{"en":"If scientists study this stage carefully, they may understand why vivid dreams often occur then.","zh":"如果科學家仔細研究這階段，他們可能理解為何鮮明夢境常在此時出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes scientific study of a specific sleep phase.","zh":"這個片語描述對特定睡眠階段的科學研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"raise a question about","meaning":"對……提出疑問","examples":[{"en":"The random-dream theory raised a question about the value of research.","zh":"隨機夢理論對研究價值提出疑問。"},{"en":"To raise a question about something means to make people doubt it or think more carefully about it.","zh":"To raise a question about something 指令人懷疑某事或更仔細思考某事。"},{"en":"A failed exam result may raise a question about whether the teaching method is working.","zh":"考試成績不理想可能對教學方法是否有效提出疑問。"},{"en":"If dreams are random, scientists may ask whether studying their meaning is useful.","zh":"如果夢是隨機的，科學家可能問研究其意義是否有用。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces doubt or debate.","zh":"這個片語引出懷疑或辯論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"usefulness of research","meaning":"研究的用途；價值","examples":[{"en":"Scientists questioned the usefulness of research into meaningless dreams.","zh":"科學家質疑對毫無意義的夢進行研究的用途。"},{"en":"The usefulness of research means the practical or intellectual value that a study may have.","zh":"Usefulness of research 指一項研究可能具有的實際或知識價值。"},{"en":"A school may question the usefulness of a survey if no one uses the results.","zh":"如果沒有人使用結果，學校可能質疑一項調查的用途。"},{"en":"If a topic appears meaningless, people may doubt whether research on it is worth funding.","zh":"如果某主題看似毫無意義，人們可能懷疑研究它是否值得資助。"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether research produces valuable understanding or benefits.","zh":"這個片語詢問研究是否產生有價值的理解或好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be regarded as","meaning":"被視為……","examples":[{"en":"Ancient people regarded dreams as divine messages.","zh":"古人把夢視為神聖訊息。"},{"en":"To be regarded as something means to be considered or understood in that way.","zh":"To be regarded as something 指被認為或理解為某種事物。"},{"en":"A quiet library may be regarded as a safe place for students to study.","zh":"安靜圖書館可能被視為學生學習的安全地方。"},{"en":"If dreams are regarded as messages, people may try to interpret them carefully.","zh":"如果夢被視為訊息，人們可能嘗試仔細解讀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how people view or classify something.","zh":"這個片語描述人們如何看待或分類某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a means of communicating with","meaning":"與……溝通的方法","examples":[{"en":"Dreams were regarded as a means of communicating with the gods.","zh":"夢被視為與神明溝通的方法。"},{"en":"A means of communicating with someone is a method used to exchange messages with them.","zh":"A means of communicating with someone 是與某人交換訊息的方法。"},{"en":"Email is a means of communicating with teachers outside class.","zh":"電郵是在課外與老師溝通的方法。"},{"en":"If dreams are seen as communication with gods, they become religiously important.","zh":"如果夢被視為與神明溝通，它們就具有宗教重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a channel for sending or receiving messages.","zh":"這個片語描述傳送或接收訊息的渠道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"predict the future","meaning":"預測未來","examples":[{"en":"Some cultures believe that dreams can predict the future.","zh":"一些文化相信夢可以預測未來。"},{"en":"To predict the future means to say what will happen before it happens.","zh":"To predict the future 指在事情發生前說出將會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Weather reports try to predict future rain, storms, and temperature changes.","zh":"天氣報告嘗試預測未來的降雨、暴風和氣溫變化。"},{"en":"If people believe a dream predicts the future, they may change their behaviour after waking.","zh":"如果人們相信一個夢預測未來，他們醒來後可能改變行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes forecasting events before they occur.","zh":"這個片語描述在事件發生前作出預測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"superstitious and unreliable","meaning":"迷信而不可靠","examples":[{"en":"The option describes dreams as superstitious and unreliable.","zh":"該選項把夢描述為迷信而不可靠。"},{"en":"Superstitious and unreliable means based on irrational belief and not dependable as evidence.","zh":"Superstitious and unreliable 指基於非理性信念，且不能作為可靠證據。"},{"en":"Choosing medicine by lucky numbers would be superstitious and unreliable.","zh":"用幸運數字選藥會是迷信而不可靠的做法。"},{"en":"If dream predictions often fail, people may call them unreliable.","zh":"如果夢的預言經常落空，人們可能稱它們不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises a belief as unscientific and untrustworthy.","zh":"這個片語批評某信念不科學且不可信。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"medical relief","meaning":"醫療上的紓緩","examples":[{"en":"Ancient people sometimes sought medical relief through dream rituals.","zh":"古人有時透過夢境儀式尋求醫療上的紓緩。"},{"en":"Medical relief means help that reduces illness, pain, or physical suffering.","zh":"Medical relief 指減少疾病、疼痛或身體痛苦的幫助。"},{"en":"A patient with a fever may seek medical relief from a doctor or clinic.","zh":"發燒病人可能向醫生或診所尋求醫療上的紓緩。"},{"en":"If people believed a god could heal them through dreams, sleeping in a temple seemed useful.","zh":"如果人們相信神明能透過夢治療他們，睡在神廟中就看似有用。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on easing sickness or pain.","zh":"這個片語著重緩解疾病或痛楚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"mental illness","meaning":"精神疾病","examples":[{"en":"Freud believed dream analysis could help treat mental illness.","zh":"佛洛伊德相信夢境分析可以幫助治療精神疾病。"},{"en":"Mental illness is a health condition that affects mood, thinking, behaviour, or daily functioning.","zh":"Mental illness 是影響心情、思考、行為或日常運作的健康狀況。"},{"en":"Depression, anxiety disorders, and schizophrenia are examples of mental illness.","zh":"抑鬱症、焦慮症和思覺失調症都是精神疾病例子。"},{"en":"If mental illness is untreated, it may affect sleep, relationships, school, or work.","zh":"如果精神疾病未被治療，它可能影響睡眠、人際關係、學業或工作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to real health conditions, not personal weakness.","zh":"這個片語指真實健康狀況，而不是個人軟弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"fall asleep in a temple","meaning":"在神廟中入睡","examples":[{"en":"Sick people would fall asleep in a temple hoping for a healing dream.","zh":"病人會在神廟中入睡，希望得到具有治療作用的夢。"},{"en":"To fall asleep in a temple means to begin sleeping inside a sacred building.","zh":"To fall asleep in a temple 指在神聖建築物內開始睡覺。"},{"en":"A traveller may fall asleep in a quiet hall after a long and tiring journey.","zh":"旅客在漫長疲累旅程後，可能在安靜大堂中入睡。"},{"en":"If ancient patients fell asleep in a temple, they may have hoped the god would send guidance.","zh":"如果古代病人在神廟中入睡，他們可能希望神明傳來指引。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sleep as part of a religious healing practice.","zh":"這個片語描述睡眠作為宗教治療做法的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"control reasoning","meaning":"控制推理","examples":[{"en":"The prefrontal cortex helps control reasoning.","zh":"前額葉皮層幫助控制推理。"},{"en":"To control reasoning means to guide logical thought, judgment, and decision-making.","zh":"To control reasoning 指引導邏輯思考、判斷和決策。"},{"en":"A student controls reasoning when they check evidence instead of guessing quickly.","zh":"學生檢查證據而不是快速猜測時，就是在控制推理。"},{"en":"If the brain area that controls reasoning is less active, dreams may become strange or illogical.","zh":"如果控制推理的腦區較不活躍，夢可能變得奇怪或不合邏輯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental regulation of logic.","zh":"這個片語描述對邏輯的心理調節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"brain temperature rises","meaning":"大腦溫度上升","examples":[{"en":"One theory suggests that brain temperature rises during REM sleep.","zh":"一個理論提出，大腦溫度在快速眼動睡眠期間上升。"},{"en":"Brain temperature rises means the brain becomes warmer.","zh":"Brain temperature rises 指大腦變得較暖。"},{"en":"Body temperature may rise during exercise because muscles use more energy.","zh":"運動期間身體溫度可能上升，因為肌肉使用更多能量。"},{"en":"If brain temperature rises during REM, the sleep stage may help maintain brain physiology.","zh":"如果大腦溫度在快速眼動睡眠期間上升，該睡眠階段可能幫助維持大腦生理狀態。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a measurable physical change in the brain.","zh":"這個片語描述大腦中可量度的身體變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"warm-blooded","meaning":"溫血的","examples":[{"en":"Mammals and birds are warm-blooded animals.","zh":"哺乳類動物和鳥類是溫血動物。"},{"en":"Warm-blooded means able to keep body temperature relatively stable from inside the body.","zh":"Warm-blooded 指能從體內把體溫保持相對穩定。"},{"en":"Humans are warm-blooded, so the body works to stay near a safe temperature.","zh":"人類是溫血的，所以身體會努力保持在安全溫度附近。"},{"en":"If animals are warm-blooded, they may need sleep processes that help regulate temperature.","zh":"如果動物是溫血的，它們可能需要幫助調節體溫的睡眠過程。"},{"en":"This word contrasts mammals and birds with cold-blooded animals.","zh":"這個詞把哺乳類和鳥類與冷血動物作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be more likely to experience","meaning":"較有可能經歷……","examples":[{"en":"Mammals are more likely than cold-blooded animals to experience REM sleep.","zh":"哺乳類動物比冷血動物較有可能經歷快速眼動睡眠。"},{"en":"To be more likely to experience something means to have a higher chance of going through it.","zh":"To be more likely to experience something 指經歷某事的機會較高。"},{"en":"Students who sleep late are more likely to experience tiredness in morning lessons.","zh":"晚睡的學生較有可能在早上課堂經歷疲倦。"},{"en":"If mammals are more likely to experience REM sleep, body temperature control may be part of the reason.","zh":"如果哺乳類動物較有可能經歷快速眼動睡眠，體溫控制可能是原因之一。"},{"en":"This phrase compares probability between groups.","zh":"這個片語比較不同群體之間的可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be concluded from","meaning":"可從……得出結論","examples":[{"en":"A conclusion can be drawn from the evidence about animals and REM.","zh":"可從關於動物和快速眼動睡眠的證據中得出結論。"},{"en":"To be concluded from evidence means to be decided or inferred based on that evidence.","zh":"To be concluded from evidence 指根據證據作出判斷或推論。"},{"en":"A teacher may conclude from test results that students need more vocabulary practice.","zh":"老師可能從測驗結果得出結論，認為學生需要更多詞彙練習。"},{"en":"If REM appears mainly in warm-blooded animals, scientists may infer a link with temperature control.","zh":"如果快速眼動睡眠主要出現在溫血動物中，科學家可能推論它與體溫控制有關。"},{"en":"This phrase connects evidence with a reasoned conclusion.","zh":"這個片語把證據與合理結論連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"match each statement with","meaning":"將每項陳述與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match each statement with the correct researcher.","zh":"學生將每項陳述與正確研究人員配對。"},{"en":"To match each statement with someone means to connect each sentence to the person who expressed that idea.","zh":"To match each statement with someone 指把每個句子連接到表達該想法的人。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may match each statement with Freud, Hobson, or another researcher.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能把每項陳述與佛洛伊德、Hobson或另一位研究人員配對。"},{"en":"If two researchers discuss dreams differently, careful matching prevents confusion.","zh":"如果兩位研究人員對夢有不同討論，仔細配對可以避免混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common matching task.","zh":"這個片語描述常見配對任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"merely a trivial by-product","meaning":"只是一種無關重要的副產品","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists regard dreams as merely a trivial by-product.","zh":"一些科學家把夢視為只是一種無關重要的副產品。"},{"en":"Merely a trivial by-product means only a small, unimportant side result of another process.","zh":"Merely a trivial by-product 指只是另一個過程的小而不重要的附帶結果。"},{"en":"A little steam may be merely a trivial by-product of boiling water.","zh":"少量蒸氣可能只是水沸騰的一種無關重要的副產品。"},{"en":"If dreams are only a trivial by-product, researchers may doubt whether they have deep meaning.","zh":"如果夢只是一種無關重要的副產品，研究人員可能懷疑它們是否有深層意義。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly reduces the importance of something.","zh":"這個片語強烈降低某事的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"accompany REM sleep","meaning":"伴隨快速眼動睡眠","examples":[{"en":"Dreams may accompany REM sleep without serving a major function.","zh":"夢可能伴隨快速眼動睡眠，而不發揮主要功能。"},{"en":"To accompany REM sleep means to happen together with REM sleep.","zh":"To accompany REM sleep 指與快速眼動睡眠一起發生。"},{"en":"Music may accompany a film scene without being the main event.","zh":"音樂可能伴隨電影場景，但不是主要事件。"},{"en":"If dreams accompany REM sleep, they may appear alongside it rather than cause it.","zh":"如果夢伴隨快速眼動睡眠，它們可能是與它一同出現，而不是造成它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows two things occurring together.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩件事同時發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"benefit treatment","meaning":"有助治療","examples":[{"en":"Exploring patients’ dreams may benefit treatment.","zh":"探索病人的夢可能有助治療。"},{"en":"To benefit treatment means to improve or support the process of helping a patient recover.","zh":"To benefit treatment 指改善或支持幫助病人康復的過程。"},{"en":"Clear communication between doctor and patient can benefit treatment.","zh":"醫生與病人之間清晰溝通可以有助治療。"},{"en":"If dream discussion reveals hidden worries, therapy may become more effective.","zh":"如果夢境討論揭示隱藏憂慮，治療可能變得更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something making treatment more helpful.","zh":"這個片語描述某事令治療更有幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"reveal unconscious thoughts","meaning":"揭示潛意識思想","examples":[{"en":"Dream analysis may reveal unconscious thoughts.","zh":"夢境分析可能揭示潛意識思想。"},{"en":"To reveal unconscious thoughts means to show ideas or feelings that exist below conscious awareness.","zh":"To reveal unconscious thoughts 指顯示存在於意識察覺之下的想法或感受。"},{"en":"A person’s repeated dreams may reveal worries they have not admitted openly.","zh":"一個人反覆出現的夢可能揭示他尚未公開承認的憂慮。"},{"en":"If unconscious thoughts are revealed, therapy can discuss them directly.","zh":"如果潛意識思想被揭示，治療就可以直接討論它們。"},{"en":"This phrase connects dream interpretation with hidden mental content.","zh":"這個片語把夢境解讀與隱藏心理內容連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"cope with difficulties","meaning":"應付困難","examples":[{"en":"Dreaming may help people cope with difficulties experienced during the day.","zh":"造夢可能幫助人應付日間經歷的困難。"},{"en":"To cope with difficulties means to manage problems, stress, or painful situations.","zh":"To cope with difficulties 指處理問題、壓力或痛苦情況。"},{"en":"A student may cope with exam pressure by planning revision and talking to a teacher.","zh":"學生可能透過計劃溫習和與老師談話來應付考試壓力。"},{"en":"If dreams process strong emotions, they may help people handle daily problems.","zh":"如果夢處理強烈情緒，它們可能幫助人應付日常問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes managing hardship rather than removing it immediately.","zh":"這個片語描述管理困難，而不是立即消除困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"encounter during the day","meaning":"在日間遇到","examples":[{"en":"People may process problems they encounter during the day while dreaming.","zh":"人們可能在造夢時處理日間遇到的問題。"},{"en":"To encounter something during the day means to meet, experience, or face it while awake.","zh":"To encounter something during the day 指在清醒時遇到、經歷或面對某事。"},{"en":"A worker may encounter a difficult customer during the day and think about it later.","zh":"員工可能在日間遇到難纏顧客，之後一直想起。"},{"en":"If a problem is emotionally strong, the mind may return to it in dreams at night.","zh":"如果問題情緒上很強烈，心智可能在夜間夢中回到它。"},{"en":"This phrase links waking experiences with later mental processing.","zh":"這個片語把清醒經歷與之後的心理處理連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"decode dreams","meaning":"解讀夢境","examples":[{"en":"Freud believed therapists could decode dreams.","zh":"佛洛伊德相信治療師可以解讀夢境。"},{"en":"To decode dreams means to interpret their symbols, images, and hidden meanings.","zh":"To decode dreams 指解釋夢中的象徵、影像和隱藏意義。"},{"en":"A therapist may try to decode a repeated dream about being lost.","zh":"治療師可能嘗試解讀一個關於迷路的反覆夢。"},{"en":"If dreams contain disguised emotions, decoding them may reveal what the patient fears or wants.","zh":"如果夢包含被偽裝的情緒，解讀它們可能揭示病人恐懼或想要甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase treats dreams like messages that need interpretation.","zh":"這個片語把夢視為需要解釋的訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"originate in childhood","meaning":"源自童年","examples":[{"en":"Some unconscious desires may originate in childhood.","zh":"一些潛意識慾望可能源自童年。"},{"en":"To originate in childhood means to begin or develop from early life experiences.","zh":"To originate in childhood 指從早年生活經歷開始或發展出來。"},{"en":"A fear of dogs may originate in childhood after a frightening bite.","zh":"對狗的恐懼可能源自童年時一次嚇人的咬傷。"},{"en":"If a feeling originates in childhood, adult behaviour may be shaped by early memories.","zh":"如果一種感受源自童年，成人行為可能受早期記憶塑造。"},{"en":"This phrase points to childhood as the starting point.","zh":"這個片語指出童年是起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"regulate strong emotions","meaning":"調節強烈情緒","examples":[{"en":"Dreaming may help regulate strong emotions.","zh":"造夢可能幫助調節強烈情緒。"},{"en":"To regulate strong emotions means to manage powerful feelings so they become less overwhelming.","zh":"To regulate strong emotions 指管理強烈感受，使其不那麼壓倒人。"},{"en":"A child may regulate strong emotions by breathing slowly and naming the feeling.","zh":"孩子可能透過慢慢呼吸和說出感受名稱來調節強烈情緒。"},{"en":"If dreams help process fear or grief, they may support emotional balance.","zh":"如果夢幫助處理恐懼或悲傷，它們可能支持情緒平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlling intense feelings in a healthier way.","zh":"這個片語描述以較健康方式控制強烈感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"occur randomly","meaning":"隨機出現","examples":[{"en":"Hobson believed that dreams seemed to occur randomly.","zh":"Hobson相信夢似乎隨機出現。"},{"en":"To occur randomly means to happen without clear order, plan, or purpose.","zh":"To occur randomly 指沒有清晰次序、計劃或目的地發生。"},{"en":"If students guess answers without reading, their correct answers may occur randomly.","zh":"如果學生不閱讀就猜答案，他們答對可能只是隨機出現。"},{"en":"If dreams occur randomly, they may not follow hidden messages or personal meaning.","zh":"如果夢隨機出現，它們可能不跟隨隱藏訊息或個人意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes events that seem accidental.","zh":"這個片語描述看似偶然的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"have limited research significance","meaning":"研究價值有限","examples":[{"en":"Random dreams might appear to have limited research significance.","zh":"隨機夢可能看起來研究價值有限。"},{"en":"To have limited research significance means to seem not very useful or important for scientific study.","zh":"To have limited research significance 指看起來對科學研究不太有用或不太重要。"},{"en":"A survey with only three answers may have limited research significance.","zh":"只有三個答案的調查可能研究價值有限。"},{"en":"If dreams are meaningless random signals, some scientists may think they are not worth studying deeply.","zh":"如果夢是毫無意義的隨機訊號，一些科學家可能認為它們不值得深入研究。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weak value for research.","zh":"這個片語描述較弱的研究價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 161 - What Are Dreams?.pdf","sourcePage":21}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 162":[{"front":"reed-bed water treatment","meaning":"蘆葦水床污水處理","examples":[{"en":"Reed-bed water treatment uses plants and microorganisms to purify wastewater.","zh":"蘆葦水床污水處理利用植物和微生物來淨化污水。"},{"en":"Reed-bed water treatment is a natural system that cleans wastewater as it passes through planted beds.","zh":"蘆葦水床污水處理是一種天然系統，讓污水流經種有植物的床層時被淨化。"},{"en":"A small village may use reed-bed water treatment when a large treatment plant is too expensive.","zh":"當大型污水處理廠太昂貴，小村莊可能使用蘆葦水床污水處理。"},{"en":"The reeds provide roots where microorganisms can break down waste and remove pollutants.","zh":"蘆葦提供根部環境，讓微生物分解廢物並清除污染物。"},{"en":"This method is useful when communities want simple, low-energy wastewater treatment.","zh":"當社區想要簡單、低耗能的污水處理方式，這種方法很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in recent years","meaning":"近年來","examples":[{"en":"In recent years, scientists have studied the role of plant roots in water purification.","zh":"近年來，科學家研究植物根部在淨水中的作用。"},{"en":"In recent years means during the last few years, not long ago in the past.","zh":"in recent years 指在過去幾年間，即不久以前至現在。"},{"en":"In recent years, many schools have used more online learning tools.","zh":"近年來，許多學校使用更多網上學習工具。"},{"en":"New problems or discoveries often receive more attention in recent years.","zh":"新問題或新發現往往在近年來受到更多關注。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a modern trend or recent development.","zh":"這個短語引入現代趨勢或近期發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"it has been shown that","meaning":"研究顯示","examples":[{"en":"It has been shown that plant roots play an important part in purifying water.","zh":"研究顯示，植物根部在淨化水方面擔當重要角色。"},{"en":"It has been shown that means research or evidence has demonstrated something.","zh":"it has been shown that 指研究或證據已經證明某事。"},{"en":"It has been shown that sleep helps students remember new vocabulary.","zh":"研究顯示，睡眠有助學生記住新詞彙。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when they want to sound evidence-based rather than personal.","zh":"作者想令說法聽起來有證據支持，而不是個人意見時，會用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a finding, not just an opinion.","zh":"這個短語引入研究發現，而不只是看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"more accurately","meaning":"更準確地說","examples":[{"en":"Plants, or more accurately their roots, help remove pollutants from water.","zh":"植物，或更準確地說是它們的根部，有助清除水中的污染物。"},{"en":"More accurately means to say something in a more exact or precise way.","zh":"more accurately 指以更精確或更準確的方式說某事。"},{"en":"The student lives in Kowloon, or more accurately, in Sham Shui Po.","zh":"這名學生住在九龍，更準確地說，是住在深水埗。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects or sharpens an earlier statement so the meaning is clearer.","zh":"這個短語修正或細化前面的說法，使意思更清楚。"},{"en":"It is useful when the first description is true but not specific enough.","zh":"當第一個描述是對的但不夠具體時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"play a crucial part in","meaning":"在……中擔當關鍵角色","examples":[{"en":"Plant roots play a crucial part in natural water treatment.","zh":"植物根部在天然水處理中擔當關鍵角色。"},{"en":"To play a crucial part in something means to be extremely important in making it happen.","zh":"play a crucial part in something 指在促成某事方面極其重要。"},{"en":"Teachers play a crucial part in helping weaker students build confidence.","zh":"老師在幫助較弱學生建立信心方面擔當關鍵角色。"},{"en":"If one crucial part is missing, the whole system may work less effectively.","zh":"如果缺少一個關鍵部分，整個系統可能運作得較差。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is not minor but central.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事不是次要，而是核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"purify dirty water","meaning":"淨化污水","examples":[{"en":"Wetlands can purify dirty water before it reaches rivers.","zh":"濕地可以在污水流入河流前淨化污水。"},{"en":"To purify dirty water means to remove harmful substances so the water becomes cleaner.","zh":"purify dirty water 指清除有害物質，使水變得較乾淨。"},{"en":"A simple filter can help purify dirty water during a camping trip.","zh":"露營時，簡單濾水器可以幫助淨化污水。"},{"en":"If dirty water is not purified, it may harm people, animals, and rivers.","zh":"如果污水沒有被淨化，可能傷害人類、動物和河流。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of making polluted water safer or cleaner.","zh":"這個短語描述令受污染的水更安全或更乾淨的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"enter seas and rivers","meaning":"流入海洋和河流","examples":[{"en":"Wastewater should be treated before it enters seas and rivers.","zh":"污水應在流入海洋和河流前接受處理。"},{"en":"To enter seas and rivers means to flow into natural bodies of water.","zh":"enter seas and rivers 指流入天然水體。"},{"en":"Rainwater from streets may enter rivers after passing through roadside drains.","zh":"街道雨水可能經過路邊排水渠後流入河流。"},{"en":"If polluted water enters seas and rivers, it can damage fish and coastal habitats.","zh":"如果受污染的水流入海洋和河流，可能破壞魚類和沿岸棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase explains where untreated water may end up.","zh":"這個短語解釋未處理的水可能最終流向哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"15th-century Britain","meaning":"15世紀的英國","examples":[{"en":"Wetlands were used for water purification in 15th-century Britain.","zh":"在 15 世紀的英國，濕地被用於淨水。"},{"en":"15th-century Britain means Britain during the years from 1401 to 1500.","zh":"15th-century Britain 指 1401 年至 1500 年期間的英國。"},{"en":"A history lesson on 15th-century Britain may discuss farming, towns, and early sanitation.","zh":"關於 15 世紀英國的歷史課可能討論農業、城鎮和早期衞生。"},{"en":"Referring to this period shows that wetland purification has a long history.","zh":"提及這個時期顯示濕地淨水有悠久歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event in a specific historical century.","zh":"這個短語把事件放在特定歷史世紀中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be purified by passing through","meaning":"透過流經……而被淨化","examples":[{"en":"Dirty water was purified by passing through wetlands.","zh":"污水透過流經濕地而被淨化。"},{"en":"To be purified by passing through something means to become cleaner while moving through it.","zh":"be purified by passing through something 指在穿過某物時變得更乾淨。"},{"en":"Rainwater can be purified by passing through layers of sand and gravel.","zh":"雨水可以透過流經沙和碎石層而被淨化。"},{"en":"As water passes through natural materials, some pollutants may be trapped or broken down.","zh":"當水流經天然材料，一些污染物可能被截留或分解。"},{"en":"This phrase explains cleaning through movement across or inside a material.","zh":"這個短語解釋水透過流經或穿過材料而被清潔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"wetlands","meaning":"濕地","examples":[{"en":"Wetlands naturally remove pollutants from wastewater.","zh":"濕地自然地清除污水中的污染物。"},{"en":"Wetlands are areas of land where water covers the soil or keeps it very wet.","zh":"wetlands 指水覆蓋土壤或令土壤長期潮濕的土地區域。"},{"en":"A nature reserve may protect wetlands because they support birds, fish, and plants.","zh":"自然保護區可能保護濕地，因為它們支持鳥類、魚類和植物。"},{"en":"Wetlands can slow water flow, trap pollutants, and provide habitats.","zh":"濕地可以減慢水流、截留污染物並提供棲息地。"},{"en":"This word refers to water-rich natural areas such as marshes and swamps.","zh":"這個詞指沼澤、濕原等富水天然地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"natural way of water purification","meaning":"天然淨水方式","examples":[{"en":"Wetlands provide a natural way of water purification.","zh":"濕地提供一種天然淨水方式。"},{"en":"A natural way of water purification uses natural materials or living organisms to clean water.","zh":"natural way of water purification 指利用天然材料或生物來清潔水。"},{"en":"A pond with plants can be a natural way of water purification if roots and microbes filter waste.","zh":"如果植物根部和微生物能過濾廢物，有植物的池塘可以是一種天然淨水方式。"},{"en":"Natural purification can reduce the need for heavy machines and chemicals.","zh":"天然淨水可以減少對大型機械和化學品的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cleaning water by working with nature.","zh":"這個短語描述順應自然來清潔水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"prove effective","meaning":"證實有效","examples":[{"en":"Natural wetland treatment has proved effective in many regions.","zh":"天然濕地處理在許多地區已證實有效。"},{"en":"To prove effective means to show through use or evidence that something works well.","zh":"prove effective 指透過使用或證據顯示某事運作良好。"},{"en":"A new homework method proves effective if students make fewer mistakes after using it.","zh":"如果學生使用新功課方法後錯誤減少，該方法就證實有效。"},{"en":"A treatment system proves effective when it consistently produces cleaner water.","zh":"當處理系統持續產生較乾淨的水，就證實有效。"},{"en":"This phrase means the method has been shown to work, not merely promised to work.","zh":"這個短語表示方法已被顯示有效，而不只是聲稱有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"nowadays","meaning":"現今","examples":[{"en":"Nowadays, constructed wetlands are commonly used in rural areas.","zh":"現今，人工濕地常用於鄉郊地區。"},{"en":"Nowadays means at the present time, especially compared with the past.","zh":"nowadays 指現時，尤其是與過去相比。"},{"en":"Nowadays, many students submit homework online instead of on paper.","zh":"現今，許多學生在網上提交功課，而不是用紙本。"},{"en":"This word introduces a modern situation or current habit.","zh":"這個詞引入現代情況或當前習慣。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing old and present practices.","zh":"當比較過去和現在的做法時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"subsurface-flow wetlands","meaning":"地下流人工濕地","examples":[{"en":"Subsurface-flow wetlands treat wastewater beneath the surface.","zh":"地下流人工濕地在表面以下處理污水。"},{"en":"Subsurface-flow wetlands are wetland systems where water moves below the surface of the bed.","zh":"subsurface-flow wetlands 指水在床層表面以下流動的濕地系統。"},{"en":"A village may choose subsurface-flow wetlands because they leave no open wastewater on top.","zh":"村莊可能選擇地下流人工濕地，因為表面沒有開放污水。"},{"en":"Keeping water below the surface can reduce smells and mosquito problems.","zh":"讓水在表面以下流動可以減少氣味和蚊患問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a hidden-flow wetland treatment system.","zh":"這個短語描述一種隱藏水流的濕地處理系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"common alternative to","meaning":"……的常見替代方案","examples":[{"en":"Reed beds are a common alternative to conventional treatment systems.","zh":"蘆葦床是傳統處理系統的常見替代方案。"},{"en":"A common alternative to something is another choice that people often use instead.","zh":"common alternative to something 指人們常用來取代某事物的另一選擇。"},{"en":"Buses are a common alternative to private cars in busy city centres.","zh":"在繁忙市中心，巴士是私家車的常見替代方案。"},{"en":"People choose alternatives when the usual method is too costly, unsuitable, or inconvenient.","zh":"當通常方法太昂貴、不合適或不方便，人們會選擇替代方案。"},{"en":"This phrase shows contrast between the standard option and another practical choice.","zh":"這個短語顯示標準選項與另一實用選擇之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"wastewater treatment","meaning":"污水處理","examples":[{"en":"Constructed wetlands can provide effective wastewater treatment.","zh":"人工濕地可以提供有效污水處理。"},{"en":"Wastewater treatment is the process of cleaning used water before it returns to the environment.","zh":"wastewater treatment 指在用過的水回到環境前把它清潔的過程。"},{"en":"A town needs wastewater treatment so sewage does not flow directly into rivers.","zh":"城鎮需要污水處理，令污水不會直接流入河流。"},{"en":"Good wastewater treatment protects public health, fish, and drinking-water sources.","zh":"良好污水處理保護公共健康、魚類和飲用水源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to making dirty used water safer.","zh":"這個短語指令骯髒用水變得更安全。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rural areas","meaning":"鄉郊地區","examples":[{"en":"Reed-bed systems are particularly suitable for rural areas.","zh":"蘆葦床系統尤其適合鄉郊地區。"},{"en":"Rural areas are countryside places with villages, farms, and lower population density.","zh":"rural areas 指有村莊、農場且人口密度較低的鄉村地方。"},{"en":"A rural area may not have enough money or people to support a large treatment plant.","zh":"鄉郊地區可能沒有足夠資金或人口支持大型處理廠。"},{"en":"Simple natural systems can suit rural areas because land is often more available.","zh":"簡單天然系統可能適合鄉郊地區，因為土地通常較充足。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts countryside regions with towns and cities.","zh":"這個短語把鄉村地區與城鎮和城市作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"over the last decade","meaning":"在過去十年間","examples":[{"en":"Over the last decade, the use of reed-bed systems has increased significantly.","zh":"在過去十年間，蘆葦床系統的使用顯著增加。"},{"en":"Over the last decade means during the past ten years.","zh":"over the last decade 指在過去十年期間。"},{"en":"Over the last decade, many families have started using mobile payment.","zh":"在過去十年間，許多家庭開始使用流動支付。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for describing gradual change across several years.","zh":"這個短語適合描述跨越數年的逐漸變化。"},{"en":"It shows a trend, not a single sudden event.","zh":"它顯示一種趨勢，而不是單一突發事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"significant growth in","meaning":"……的顯著增長","examples":[{"en":"There has been significant growth in the number of wetland systems.","zh":"濕地系統的數量出現顯著增長。"},{"en":"Significant growth in something means a large and noticeable increase.","zh":"significant growth in something 指大幅而明顯的增加。"},{"en":"A school may see significant growth in student numbers after improving its results.","zh":"學校改善成績後，學生人數可能出現顯著增長。"},{"en":"Significant growth can create new opportunities but also new management problems.","zh":"顯著增長可以帶來新機會，但也帶來新管理問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increase that is important enough to mention.","zh":"這個短語描述值得提及的重要增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"systems in use","meaning":"正在使用的系統","examples":[{"en":"The number and size of the systems in use have increased.","zh":"正在使用的系統在數量和規模上都有增加。"},{"en":"Systems in use are systems that are currently operating or being used.","zh":"systems in use 指目前正在運作或被使用的系統。"},{"en":"A school may review all computers in use before buying new ones.","zh":"學校購買新電腦前，可能檢查所有正在使用的電腦。"},{"en":"If more systems are in use, maintenance and monitoring may become more important.","zh":"如果更多系統正在使用，維修和監察可能變得更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to real operating systems, not just planned designs.","zh":"這個短語指真正在運作的系統，而不只是計劃中的設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"conventional mechanism","meaning":"傳統處理機制","examples":[{"en":"The conventional mechanism used in large cities may be unsuitable for villages.","zh":"大城市使用的傳統處理機制可能不適合村莊。"},{"en":"A conventional mechanism is the usual or traditional system used to do something.","zh":"conventional mechanism 指用來做某事的通常或傳統系統。"},{"en":"A conventional heating system may work well in a city flat but not in a remote cabin.","zh":"傳統供暖系統可能適合城市單位，但不適合偏遠小屋。"},{"en":"Conventional mechanisms can fail when local conditions are very different.","zh":"當本地條件很不一樣，傳統機制可能失效。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the standard method, not necessarily the best method everywhere.","zh":"這個短語指標準方法，但不一定是各地最佳方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"large volumes of water","meaning":"大量的水","examples":[{"en":"Urban treatment plants process large volumes of water.","zh":"城市處理廠處理大量的水。"},{"en":"Large volumes of water means very great amounts of water.","zh":"large volumes of water 指非常大量的水。"},{"en":"A swimming pool needs large volumes of water to fill it properly.","zh":"游泳池需要大量的水才能完全注滿。"},{"en":"Treating large volumes of water requires equipment, energy, and careful control.","zh":"處理大量的水需要設備、能源和仔細控制。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the scale of water being handled.","zh":"這個短語強調正在處理的水量規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be inappropriate in","meaning":"不適合用於……","examples":[{"en":"Large conventional plants may be inappropriate in rural areas.","zh":"大型傳統處理廠可能不適合用於鄉郊地區。"},{"en":"To be inappropriate in a place means to be unsuitable for that setting or situation.","zh":"be inappropriate in a place 指不適合某環境或情況。"},{"en":"Loud music is inappropriate in a hospital ward because patients need rest.","zh":"大聲音樂不適合用於醫院病房，因為病人需要休息。"},{"en":"A method may be inappropriate when it is too expensive, too large, or too complex.","zh":"當一種方法太昂貴、太大型或太複雜，它可能不適合。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a solution does not fit the context.","zh":"這個短語顯示解決方法不符合語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"common reed","meaning":"普通蘆葦","examples":[{"en":"The common reed transfers oxygen to its root system.","zh":"普通蘆葦把氧氣傳送到其根系。"},{"en":"The common reed is a tall wetland plant often used in natural wastewater treatment.","zh":"common reed 指常用於天然污水處理的高大濕地植物。"},{"en":"A pond may contain common reed along its edges where the soil stays wet.","zh":"池塘邊緣泥土潮濕的地方可能有普通蘆葦。"},{"en":"Its roots create a useful zone where microorganisms can live and clean water.","zh":"它的根部形成有用區域，讓微生物生存並清潔水。"},{"en":"This phrase names the plant that often forms the main part of a reed bed.","zh":"這個短語命名常構成蘆葦床主要部分的植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have the ability to","meaning":"有能力去……","examples":[{"en":"The common reed has the ability to transfer oxygen through its tissues.","zh":"普通蘆葦有能力透過其組織傳送氧氣。"},{"en":"To have the ability to do something means to be capable of doing it.","zh":"have the ability to do something 指有能力做某事。"},{"en":"Some students have the ability to explain difficult ideas in simple words.","zh":"有些學生有能力用簡單語言解釋困難概念。"},{"en":"A plant’s special ability can make it useful in environmental treatment.","zh":"植物的特殊能力可以令它在環境處理中有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what someone or something can do.","zh":"這個短語描述某人或某物能做甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"transfer oxygen","meaning":"傳送氧氣","examples":[{"en":"Reeds transfer oxygen from their leaves to their roots.","zh":"蘆葦把氧氣從葉傳送到根部。"},{"en":"To transfer oxygen means to move oxygen from one place to another.","zh":"transfer oxygen 指把氧氣從一處移到另一處。"},{"en":"Blood transfers oxygen from the lungs to the rest of the body.","zh":"血液把氧氣從肺部傳送到身體其他部分。"},{"en":"When reeds transfer oxygen to their roots, they create better conditions for helpful microbes.","zh":"當蘆葦把氧氣傳送到根部，它們為有益微生物創造更好條件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes oxygen being carried through a system.","zh":"這個短語描述氧氣在系統中被運送。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"down through","meaning":"向下穿過……","examples":[{"en":"Oxygen moves down through the stem and rhizomes.","zh":"氧氣向下穿過莖和根莖。"},{"en":"Down through means moving downward inside or across something.","zh":"down through 指在某物內部或穿過某物向下移動。"},{"en":"Rainwater may move down through soil before reaching groundwater.","zh":"雨水可能向下穿過土壤，然後到達地下水。"},{"en":"Movement down through layers can filter water or carry substances deeper.","zh":"向下穿過層層物質可以過濾水或把物質帶到更深處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direction and pathway at the same time.","zh":"這個短語同時描述方向和路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stem and rhizomes","meaning":"莖和根莖","examples":[{"en":"The reed’s stem and rhizomes carry oxygen towards the roots.","zh":"蘆葦的莖和根莖把氧氣帶向根部。"},{"en":"Stem and rhizomes are plant parts that support growth and help move materials through the plant.","zh":"stem and rhizomes 指支持植物生長並幫助物質在植物內移動的部分。"},{"en":"In a garden, the stem holds leaves up, while rhizomes may spread underground.","zh":"在花園中，莖支撐葉子，而根莖可能在地下伸展。"},{"en":"These plant parts help reeds survive in wet soil and support wastewater treatment.","zh":"這些植物部分幫助蘆葦在濕土中生存，並支持污水處理。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to above-ground and underground plant structures.","zh":"這個短語指地上和地下的植物結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"root system","meaning":"根系","examples":[{"en":"A large population of microorganisms develops in the root system.","zh":"大量微生物在根系中生長。"},{"en":"A root system is the network of roots that anchors a plant and absorbs water and nutrients.","zh":"root system 指固定植物並吸收水和養分的根部網絡。"},{"en":"A healthy tree needs a strong root system to survive storms and dry weather.","zh":"健康樹木需要強大根系來抵禦風暴和乾旱天氣。"},{"en":"In reed beds, the root system provides a living space for microorganisms.","zh":"在蘆葦床中，根系為微生物提供生活空間。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to all the roots working together below the plant.","zh":"這個短語指植物下方所有根部共同運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as a result of","meaning":"由於……","examples":[{"en":"As a result of oxygen transfer, microorganisms grow around the roots.","zh":"由於氧氣傳送，微生物在根部周圍生長。"},{"en":"As a result of means because of something that happened before.","zh":"as a result of 指因為之前發生的某事。"},{"en":"As a result of heavy rain, the football match was cancelled.","zh":"由於大雨，足球比賽被取消。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with its consequence.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining why a change happened.","zh":"當解釋變化為何發生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a large population of","meaning":"大量的……","examples":[{"en":"A large population of microorganisms develops within the reed bed.","zh":"大量微生物在蘆葦床內生長。"},{"en":"A large population of something means a great number of living organisms in one place.","zh":"large population of something 指在一個地方有大量生物。"},{"en":"A pond with too much food waste may develop a large population of insects.","zh":"如果池塘有太多食物廢物，可能滋生大量昆蟲。"},{"en":"A large population of helpful microbes can make wastewater treatment more effective.","zh":"大量有益微生物可以令污水處理更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for many living things, not for objects.","zh":"這個短語用於很多生物，而不是物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"microorganisms","meaning":"微生物","examples":[{"en":"Microorganisms digest waste and remove pollutants from the water.","zh":"微生物分解廢物並清除水中的污染物。"},{"en":"Microorganisms are tiny living things, such as bacteria and fungi, that are too small to see clearly without a microscope.","zh":"microorganisms 指細菌和真菌等微小生物，沒有顯微鏡難以清楚看見。"},{"en":"Yogurt contains microorganisms that help change milk into a thicker food.","zh":"乳酪含有微生物，幫助把牛奶變成較濃稠的食物。"},{"en":"In wastewater systems, microorganisms break down waste into less harmful substances.","zh":"在污水系統中，微生物把廢物分解成較無害的物質。"},{"en":"This word refers to very small organisms that can be useful or harmful.","zh":"這個詞指非常細小、可以有益或有害的生物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"aerobic conditions","meaning":"好氧環境","examples":[{"en":"Some microorganisms live in aerobic conditions where oxygen is present.","zh":"有些微生物生活在有氧氣存在的好氧環境中。"},{"en":"Aerobic conditions are conditions where oxygen is available.","zh":"aerobic conditions 指有氧氣可用的環境。"},{"en":"Compost breaks down faster in aerobic conditions when air can enter the pile.","zh":"當空氣能進入堆肥堆，堆肥在好氧環境中分解得更快。"},{"en":"Some bacteria need aerobic conditions to digest organic waste efficiently.","zh":"有些細菌需要好氧環境，才能有效分解有機廢物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an oxygen-rich environment.","zh":"這個短語描述富含氧氣的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"anoxic conditions","meaning":"缺氧環境","examples":[{"en":"Anoxic conditions contain very little free oxygen.","zh":"缺氧環境含有極少游離氧氣。"},{"en":"Anoxic conditions are environments where oxygen is almost absent but not always completely absent.","zh":"anoxic conditions 指氧氣幾乎不存在但未必完全沒有的環境。"},{"en":"Fish may struggle in a pond with anoxic conditions because there is too little oxygen.","zh":"魚在缺氧池塘中可能難以生存，因為氧氣太少。"},{"en":"Different microorganisms become active when oxygen levels are very low.","zh":"當氧氣水平很低，不同微生物會變得活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a low-oxygen environment.","zh":"這個短語描述低氧環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"anaerobic conditions","meaning":"厭氧環境","examples":[{"en":"Other microorganisms develop under anaerobic conditions.","zh":"其他微生物在厭氧環境下生長。"},{"en":"Anaerobic conditions are conditions with no oxygen available.","zh":"anaerobic conditions 指沒有氧氣可用的環境。"},{"en":"Food waste in a sealed bin may break down under anaerobic conditions and produce bad smells.","zh":"密封垃圾桶中的廚餘可能在厭氧環境下分解並產生臭味。"},{"en":"Some microorganisms can digest waste without oxygen, but the process may be slower or smellier.","zh":"有些微生物可以在沒有氧氣下分解廢物，但過程可能較慢或較臭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a no-oxygen environment.","zh":"這個短語描述無氧環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"move slowly through","meaning":"緩慢流經……","examples":[{"en":"Wastewater moves slowly through the mass of reed roots.","zh":"污水緩慢流經大量蘆葦根。"},{"en":"To move slowly through something means to pass through it at a low speed.","zh":"move slowly through something 指以低速度穿過某物。"},{"en":"Rainwater moves slowly through soil before reaching a well.","zh":"雨水在到達水井前緩慢流經土壤。"},{"en":"Slow movement gives roots, sand, and microorganisms more time to clean the water.","zh":"緩慢流動給根部、沙和微生物更多時間淨化水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual movement through a material or system.","zh":"這個短語描述水或物質逐漸穿過材料或系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mass of reed roots","meaning":"大量蘆葦根","examples":[{"en":"The mass of reed roots slows the movement of wastewater.","zh":"大量蘆葦根減慢污水流動。"},{"en":"A mass of reed roots is a thick group or network of reed roots growing together.","zh":"mass of reed roots 指許多蘆葦根密集生長在一起的根部網絡。"},{"en":"A garden plant with a dense root mass can hold soil firmly in place.","zh":"有濃密根團的園藝植物可以牢牢固定泥土。"},{"en":"In treatment beds, a thick root mass slows water and creates space for microbes.","zh":"在處理床中，濃密根團會減慢水流，並為微生物創造空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes many roots forming one dense structure.","zh":"這個短語描述大量根部形成一個密集結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be successfully treated","meaning":"得到有效處理","examples":[{"en":"Wastewater can be successfully treated as it passes through the roots.","zh":"污水在流經根部時可以得到有效處理。"},{"en":"To be successfully treated means to be processed in a way that achieves the intended improvement.","zh":"be successfully treated 指經過處理後達到預期改善。"},{"en":"A patient is successfully treated when the medicine reduces the illness safely.","zh":"當藥物安全地減輕病情，病人就是得到有效治療。"},{"en":"Wastewater is successfully treated when pollutants are reduced to safer levels.","zh":"當污染物被降低至較安全水平，污水就是得到有效處理。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the treatment works as intended.","zh":"這個短語顯示處理按預期奏效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"within the root zones","meaning":"在根區內","examples":[{"en":"Several natural processes occur within the root zones.","zh":"多種天然過程在根區內發生。"},{"en":"Within the root zones means inside the areas around plant roots.","zh":"within the root zones 指在植物根部周圍的區域內。"},{"en":"Nutrients collect within the root zones where plants absorb water from the soil.","zh":"養分聚集在根區內，植物在那裡從土壤吸水。"},{"en":"In reed beds, the root zones are active places where microbes and plant roots interact.","zh":"在蘆葦床中，根區是微生物和植物根部互相作用的活躍地方。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the treatment area around roots.","zh":"這個短語指出根部周圍的處理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"biological processes","meaning":"生物過程","examples":[{"en":"Biological processes help break down organic waste.","zh":"生物過程有助分解有機廢物。"},{"en":"Biological processes are changes or actions carried out by living organisms.","zh":"biological processes 指由生物進行的變化或行動。"},{"en":"Digestion is a biological process because the body breaks food down for energy.","zh":"消化是生物過程，因為身體把食物分解成能量。"},{"en":"In reed beds, bacteria use biological processes to digest pollutants.","zh":"在蘆葦床中，細菌利用生物過程分解污染物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to cleaning or change caused by living things.","zh":"這個短語指由生物造成的清潔或變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"physical and chemical processes","meaning":"物理及化學過程","examples":[{"en":"Physical and chemical processes also remove pollutants.","zh":"物理及化學過程也會清除污染物。"},{"en":"Physical and chemical processes are non-living actions such as filtering, settling, reacting, or binding substances.","zh":"physical and chemical processes 指非生物作用，例如過濾、沉降、反應或結合物質。"},{"en":"A water filter uses physical processes when it traps dirt in tiny holes.","zh":"濾水器把污垢困在小孔中時，就是使用物理過程。"},{"en":"Chemical processes can change pollutants into less harmful forms.","zh":"化學過程可以把污染物轉變成較無害形式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cleaning mechanisms that do not depend only on living organisms.","zh":"這個短語描述不只依賴生物的清潔機制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"interact with one another","meaning":"互相作用","examples":[{"en":"Different purification processes interact with one another.","zh":"不同淨化過程互相作用。"},{"en":"To interact with one another means to affect each other through contact or connection.","zh":"interact with one another 指透過接觸或連繫互相影響。"},{"en":"In a group project, students interact with one another when they share ideas and correct mistakes.","zh":"在小組項目中，學生分享想法並改正錯誤時，就是互相作用。"},{"en":"When processes interact, the final result may be stronger than one process alone.","zh":"當多個過程互相作用，最終效果可能比單一過程更強。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that several parts work together.","zh":"這個短語顯示幾個部分共同運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"degrade pollutants","meaning":"分解污染物","examples":[{"en":"Microorganisms degrade pollutants in wastewater.","zh":"微生物分解污水中的污染物。"},{"en":"To degrade pollutants means to break harmful substances down into simpler or less harmful materials.","zh":"degrade pollutants 指把有害物質分解成較簡單或較無害的物質。"},{"en":"Some bacteria can degrade oil after a small spill in soil.","zh":"小規模漏油後，有些細菌可以分解土壤中的油污。"},{"en":"If pollutants are degraded, the water becomes safer for rivers and wildlife.","zh":"如果污染物被分解，水對河流和野生生物會較安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes chemical or biological breakdown of pollution.","zh":"這個短語描述污染物的化學或生物分解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"remove pollutants","meaning":"清除污染物","examples":[{"en":"Reed beds can remove a wide range of pollutants.","zh":"蘆葦床可以清除多種污染物。"},{"en":"To remove pollutants means to take harmful substances out of air, water, or soil.","zh":"remove pollutants 指從空氣、水或土壤中去除有害物質。"},{"en":"A water filter removes pollutants before the water is used for cooking.","zh":"濾水器在水用於煮食前清除污染物。"},{"en":"Removing pollutants protects people and ecosystems from harmful chemicals or waste.","zh":"清除污染物可以保護人類和生態系統免受有害化學品或廢物傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on taking contamination away from a system.","zh":"這個短語著重把污染從系統中移走。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a good range of","meaning":"多種……","examples":[{"en":"The system removes a good range of harmful substances.","zh":"該系統清除多種有害物質。"},{"en":"A good range of something means many different types, enough to be useful.","zh":"good range of something 指許多不同種類，足以有實用價值。"},{"en":"A library with a good range of books can serve children, adults, and researchers.","zh":"有多種書籍的圖書館可以服務兒童、成人和研究者。"},{"en":"A treatment system is more useful if it removes a good range of pollutants.","zh":"如果處理系統能清除多種污染物，就更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests variety and practical coverage.","zh":"這個短語表示多樣性和實際覆蓋範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"household wastewater","meaning":"家居污水","examples":[{"en":"Household wastewater can consume oxygen in rivers.","zh":"家居污水可以消耗河流中的氧氣。"},{"en":"Household wastewater is used water from homes, such as water from sinks, showers, toilets, and washing machines.","zh":"household wastewater 指來自家居的用過的水，例如洗手盆、淋浴、廁所和洗衣機的水。"},{"en":"A family produces household wastewater every day when cooking, bathing, and cleaning.","zh":"家庭每天煮食、洗澡和清潔時都會產生家居污水。"},{"en":"If household wastewater enters rivers untreated, it can reduce oxygen and harm fish.","zh":"如果家居污水未經處理流入河流，可以降低氧氣並傷害魚類。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to dirty water from ordinary homes.","zh":"這個短語指來自普通家庭的污水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"farms and factories","meaning":"農場和工廠","examples":[{"en":"Wastewater from farms and factories may contain harmful pollutants.","zh":"來自農場和工廠的污水可能含有有害污染物。"},{"en":"Farms and factories are places where food is produced, animals are raised, or goods are manufactured.","zh":"farms and factories 指生產食物、飼養動物或製造貨品的地方。"},{"en":"Wastewater from farms and factories may include fertilisers, chemicals, oils, or organic waste.","zh":"來自農場和工廠的污水可能包括肥料、化學品、油或有機廢物。"},{"en":"If this wastewater is not controlled, nearby rivers may become polluted.","zh":"如果這些污水不受控制，附近河流可能被污染。"},{"en":"This phrase points to agricultural and industrial sources of waste.","zh":"這個短語指出農業和工業廢物來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"consume oxygen","meaning":"消耗氧氣","examples":[{"en":"Organic waste consumes oxygen as it decomposes in water.","zh":"有機廢物在水中分解時會消耗氧氣。"},{"en":"To consume oxygen means to use up oxygen.","zh":"consume oxygen 指使用掉氧氣。"},{"en":"Burning a candle consumes oxygen in a closed room.","zh":"在密閉房間中燃燒蠟燭會消耗氧氣。"},{"en":"When too much waste consumes oxygen in a river, fish may not have enough to survive.","zh":"當太多廢物在河流中消耗氧氣，魚類可能沒有足夠氧氣生存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes oxygen being used until less is available.","zh":"這個短語描述氧氣被用掉，令可用氧氣減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lead to the death of","meaning":"導致……死亡","examples":[{"en":"A serious lack of oxygen can lead to the death of aquatic creatures.","zh":"嚴重缺氧可以導致水生生物死亡。"},{"en":"To lead to the death of something means to cause it to die.","zh":"lead to the death of something 指造成某生物死亡。"},{"en":"Extreme heat can lead to the death of small plants if they are not watered.","zh":"如果沒有澆水，極端高溫可以導致小植物死亡。"},{"en":"Pollution can lead to the death of fish when oxygen levels fall too low.","zh":"當氧氣水平太低，污染可以導致魚類死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a serious harmful result.","zh":"這個短語解釋嚴重有害結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"aquatic creatures","meaning":"水生生物","examples":[{"en":"Low oxygen levels can harm fish and other aquatic creatures.","zh":"低氧水平可以傷害魚類和其他水生生物。"},{"en":"Aquatic creatures are animals that live in water.","zh":"aquatic creatures 指生活在水中的動物。"},{"en":"Frogs, fish, crabs, and water insects are aquatic creatures.","zh":"青蛙、魚、蟹和水生昆蟲都是水生生物。"},{"en":"Aquatic creatures need clean water and enough oxygen to survive.","zh":"水生生物需要乾淨的水和足夠氧氣才能生存。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to living animals in rivers, lakes, ponds, and seas.","zh":"這個短語指生活在河流、湖泊、池塘和海洋中的動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"aquatic plants","meaning":"水生植物","examples":[{"en":"Several aquatic plants play an important role in water purification.","zh":"幾種水生植物在淨水中擔當重要角色。"},{"en":"Aquatic plants are plants that grow in or near water.","zh":"aquatic plants 指生長在水中或水邊的植物。"},{"en":"Water lilies and reeds are aquatic plants often found in ponds and wetlands.","zh":"睡蓮和蘆葦是常見於池塘和濕地的水生植物。"},{"en":"Aquatic plants can absorb nutrients and release oxygen into the water.","zh":"水生植物可以吸收養分並把氧氣釋放到水中。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to plants adapted to wet environments.","zh":"這個短語指適應潮濕環境的植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not only…but…as well","meaning":"不但……而且也……","examples":[{"en":"Aquatic plants not only release oxygen but absorb nutrients as well.","zh":"水生植物不但釋放氧氣，而且也吸收養分。"},{"en":"Not only…but…as well is used to show that two things are both true.","zh":"not only…but…as well 用來顯示兩件事都是真的。"},{"en":"A good teacher not only explains grammar but gives useful examples as well.","zh":"好老師不但解釋文法，而且也提供有用例子。"},{"en":"This structure adds a second point and makes the sentence more emphatic.","zh":"這個結構加入第二個重點，使句子更強調。"},{"en":"It is useful when one thing has more than one benefit.","zh":"當一件事有多於一個好處時，這個結構很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"absorb carbon dioxide","meaning":"吸收二氧化碳","examples":[{"en":"Aquatic plants absorb carbon dioxide from the water.","zh":"水生植物從水中吸收二氧化碳。"},{"en":"To absorb carbon dioxide means to take in carbon dioxide from air or water.","zh":"absorb carbon dioxide 指從空氣或水中吸收二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Trees absorb carbon dioxide from the air as they grow.","zh":"樹木在生長時從空氣中吸收二氧化碳。"},{"en":"When plants absorb carbon dioxide, they can use it during photosynthesis.","zh":"當植物吸收二氧化碳，它們可以在光合作用中使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes plants taking in a gas they need.","zh":"這個短語描述植物吸收所需氣體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"release oxygen into","meaning":"把氧氣釋放到……","examples":[{"en":"Plants release oxygen into the water and improve conditions for fish.","zh":"植物把氧氣釋放到水中，改善魚類的生存條件。"},{"en":"To release oxygen into something means to give oxygen out into that place.","zh":"release oxygen into something 指把氧氣釋放到某地方。"},{"en":"Houseplants release oxygen into the air during photosynthesis.","zh":"室內植物在光合作用期間把氧氣釋放到空氣中。"},{"en":"Oxygen released into water can help fish and microorganisms survive.","zh":"釋放到水中的氧氣可以幫助魚類和微生物生存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes oxygen moving out from a plant into its surroundings.","zh":"這個短語描述氧氣從植物進入周圍環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"improve the environment for","meaning":"改善……的生存環境","examples":[{"en":"Higher oxygen levels improve the environment for fish.","zh":"較高氧氣水平改善魚類的生存環境。"},{"en":"To improve the environment for something means to make conditions better for it to live or work.","zh":"improve the environment for something 指令某物生活或工作的條件更好。"},{"en":"Quiet study rooms improve the environment for students who need concentration.","zh":"安靜自修室改善需要集中精神的學生的學習環境。"},{"en":"Cleaner water improves the environment for aquatic life by reducing stress and disease.","zh":"較乾淨的水透過減少壓力和疾病，改善水生生物的生存環境。"},{"en":"This phrase links better conditions with healthier results.","zh":"這個短語把較好條件與較健康結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"absorb nutrients from","meaning":"從……吸收養分","examples":[{"en":"Reeds absorb excess nutrients from wastewater.","zh":"蘆葦從污水中吸收過量養分。"},{"en":"To absorb nutrients from something means to take in useful substances from it.","zh":"absorb nutrients from something 指從某物中吸收有用物質。"},{"en":"Plant roots absorb nutrients from soil after rain dissolves minerals.","zh":"雨水溶解礦物質後，植物根部從泥土吸收養分。"},{"en":"Removing excess nutrients from wastewater can reduce algae growth in rivers.","zh":"從污水中清除過量養分可以減少河流中的藻類生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes plants taking in substances needed for growth.","zh":"這個短語描述植物吸收生長所需物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"differ in their preferences for","meaning":"對……的偏好有所不同","examples":[{"en":"Britain and the United States differ in their preferences for water-purifying plants.","zh":"英國和美國對淨水植物的偏好有所不同。"},{"en":"To differ in their preferences for something means to prefer different choices.","zh":"differ in their preferences for something 指不同群體偏好不同選擇。"},{"en":"Students may differ in their preferences for online lessons or face-to-face classes.","zh":"學生可能對網課或面授課的偏好有所不同。"},{"en":"Preferences can differ because of climate, cost, tradition, or local experience.","zh":"偏好可能因氣候、成本、傳統或本地經驗而不同。"},{"en":"This phrase compares what different groups like or choose.","zh":"這個短語比較不同群體喜歡或選擇甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bulrushes","meaning":"蒲草","examples":[{"en":"Bulrushes are excellent water-purifying plants.","zh":"蒲草是出色的淨水植物。"},{"en":"Bulrushes are tall wetland plants that grow near water and can help clean it.","zh":"bulrushes 指生長在水邊、能幫助淨水的高大濕地植物。"},{"en":"A pond edge may have bulrushes growing in shallow water.","zh":"池塘邊緣的淺水中可能長有蒲草。"},{"en":"Bulrushes can absorb nutrients and provide surfaces where microorganisms live.","zh":"蒲草可以吸收養分，並提供微生物生活的表面。"},{"en":"This word names a type of plant often associated with wetlands.","zh":"這個詞命名一種常與濕地相關的植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"rushes","meaning":"燈心草","examples":[{"en":"Rushes can remove nutrients, oil and bacteria from water.","zh":"燈心草可以清除水中的養分、油和細菌。"},{"en":"Rushes are grass-like wetland plants that often grow in damp places.","zh":"rushes 指像草的濕地植物，常生長在潮濕地方。"},{"en":"A wet field may contain rushes if the soil stays waterlogged.","zh":"如果土壤長期積水，濕田可能長有燈心草。"},{"en":"Rushes help water treatment by taking up nutrients and supporting microorganisms.","zh":"燈心草透過吸收養分和支持微生物來幫助水處理。"},{"en":"This word refers to simple-looking plants that can be useful in wetlands.","zh":"這個詞指外形簡單但在濕地中有用的植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"water purifiers","meaning":"淨水植物","examples":[{"en":"Bulrushes and rushes are effective natural water purifiers.","zh":"蒲草和燈心草是有效的天然淨水植物。"},{"en":"Water purifiers are things that remove dirt, pollutants, or harmful organisms from water.","zh":"water purifiers 指能清除水中污垢、污染物或有害生物的東西。"},{"en":"A home filter can act as a water purifier for drinking water.","zh":"家用濾水器可以作為飲用水的淨水器。"},{"en":"Natural water purifiers such as plants can reduce pollution without heavy machinery.","zh":"植物等天然淨水物可以不用大型機械而減少污染。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to anything that helps make water cleaner.","zh":"這個短語指任何有助令水更乾淨的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"remove excess nutrients","meaning":"清除過量養分","examples":[{"en":"Aquatic plants remove excess nutrients from polluted water.","zh":"水生植物從受污染的水中清除過量養分。"},{"en":"To remove excess nutrients means to take away too much nitrogen, phosphorus, or other growth substances.","zh":"remove excess nutrients 指去除過多氮、磷或其他促進生長的物質。"},{"en":"A pond may need plants to remove excess nutrients after fertiliser runs into it.","zh":"肥料流入池塘後，池塘可能需要植物來清除過量養分。"},{"en":"If excess nutrients remain, algae may grow too quickly and damage water quality.","zh":"如果過量養分仍然存在，藻類可能過快生長並破壞水質。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing nutrient pollution.","zh":"這個短語描述減少養分污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as well as","meaning":"以及","examples":[{"en":"Reed beds remove oil and nutrients as well as harmful bacteria.","zh":"蘆葦床清除油和養分，以及有害細菌。"},{"en":"As well as means in addition to another thing.","zh":"as well as 指除了另一事物之外，也包括某事。"},{"en":"A good school library offers quiet space as well as books.","zh":"好學校圖書館提供書籍，以及安靜空間。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another item to show a wider range of effects or features.","zh":"這個短語加入另一項目，顯示更廣泛效果或特色。"},{"en":"It is useful when one system does more than one job.","zh":"當一個系統做多於一項工作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Escherichia coli","meaning":"大腸桿菌","examples":[{"en":"Escherichia coli can be removed by suitable wetland plants.","zh":"合適濕地植物可以清除大腸桿菌。"},{"en":"Escherichia coli is a type of bacterium often found in the intestines of humans and animals.","zh":"Escherichia coli 是一種常見於人類和動物腸道中的細菌。"},{"en":"Water tests may look for Escherichia coli to check whether sewage contamination is present.","zh":"水質測試可能檢測大腸桿菌，以查看是否有污水污染。"},{"en":"High levels of this bacterium can warn that water may be unsafe.","zh":"這種細菌水平高，可以警告水可能不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is the scientific name often shortened to E. coli.","zh":"這個短語是常縮寫為 E. coli 的科學名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Salmonella","meaning":"沙門氏菌","examples":[{"en":"Some reed-bed systems can help remove Salmonella from wastewater.","zh":"有些蘆葦床系統可以幫助從污水中清除沙門氏菌。"},{"en":"Salmonella is a type of bacterium that can cause food poisoning and illness.","zh":"Salmonella 是一種可以造成食物中毒和疾病的細菌。"},{"en":"Food safety officers may test chicken or eggs for Salmonella.","zh":"食物安全人員可能檢測雞肉或雞蛋是否有沙門氏菌。"},{"en":"Removing Salmonella from wastewater helps reduce health risks.","zh":"從污水中清除沙門氏菌有助降低健康風險。"},{"en":"This word names a harmful bacterium that treatment systems may target.","zh":"這個詞命名一種處理系統可能針對的有害細菌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"grow freely","meaning":"自由生長；大量生長","examples":[{"en":"Algae grow freely during the warmer summer months.","zh":"藻類在較暖的夏季月份大量生長。"},{"en":"To grow freely means to grow easily and without much control or restriction.","zh":"grow freely 指容易地、幾乎不受控制或限制地生長。"},{"en":"Weeds may grow freely in an empty garden after weeks of rain.","zh":"連續下雨幾星期後，雜草可能在空花園中大量生長。"},{"en":"If nutrients are high and temperatures are warm, algae can grow freely and cover water surfaces.","zh":"如果養分高且溫度暖，藻類可以大量生長並覆蓋水面。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest uncontrolled growth.","zh":"這個短語可以暗示不受控制的生長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"die off","meaning":"大量枯死","examples":[{"en":"Many algae die off when winter arrives.","zh":"冬天來臨時，許多藻類大量枯死。"},{"en":"To die off means to die in large numbers over a period of time.","zh":"die off 指在一段時間內大量死亡。"},{"en":"Flowers may die off after several nights of frost.","zh":"連續幾晚結霜後，花可能大量枯死。"},{"en":"When algae die off, their dead material can sink and pollute the bottom of the water.","zh":"當藻類大量枯死，它們的死體物質可能下沉並污染水底。"},{"en":"This phrase describes group decline, not one single organism dying.","zh":"這個短語描述群體衰亡，而不是單一生物死亡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"foul the bottom of","meaning":"污染……的底部","examples":[{"en":"Dead algae can foul the bottom of a pool.","zh":"死藻可以污染池底。"},{"en":"To foul the bottom of something means to make its lower surface dirty, smelly, or polluted.","zh":"foul the bottom of something 指令某物底部變髒、發臭或受污染。"},{"en":"Food waste can foul the bottom of a rubbish bin if it is left for days.","zh":"如果廚餘放置多日，可以污染垃圾桶底部。"},{"en":"Dead plant matter can foul the bottom of water bodies as it rots.","zh":"死植物物質腐爛時，可以污染水體底部。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pollution or dirt collecting at the bottom.","zh":"這個短語描述污染或污垢在底部積聚。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"artificial reed beds","meaning":"人工蘆葦床","examples":[{"en":"Artificial reed beds can purify wastewater in different ways.","zh":"人工蘆葦床可以用不同方式淨化污水。"},{"en":"Artificial reed beds are human-made reed systems designed to treat wastewater.","zh":"artificial reed beds 指人造的蘆葦系統，用來處理污水。"},{"en":"A small hotel may build artificial reed beds to clean water from bathrooms and kitchens.","zh":"小型酒店可能建造人工蘆葦床，以清潔浴室和廚房排出的水。"},{"en":"Because they are designed, artificial reed beds can be shaped for different treatment needs.","zh":"因為它們是設計出來的，人工蘆葦床可以按不同處理需要塑造。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts constructed systems with natural wetlands.","zh":"這個短語把人工系統與天然濕地作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"horizontal and downflow systems","meaning":"水平流及下流式系統","examples":[{"en":"Reed beds may use horizontal or downflow systems.","zh":"蘆葦床可能使用水平流或下流式系統。"},{"en":"Horizontal and downflow systems are two designs where water moves sideways or downward through the bed.","zh":"horizontal and downflow systems 指水在床層中水平或向下流動的兩種設計。"},{"en":"A treatment engineer may choose a horizontal system for light pollution and a downflow system for stronger waste.","zh":"處理工程師可能為輕度污染選擇水平系統，為較高濃度污水選擇下流式系統。"},{"en":"Different flow directions affect speed, oxygen, land use, and cleaning power.","zh":"不同流向會影響速度、氧氣、土地使用和淨化能力。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two ways wastewater can move through reed beds.","zh":"這個短語比較污水穿過蘆葦床的兩種方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"perform best when","meaning":"在……時效果最佳","examples":[{"en":"The reeds perform best when dense root hairs have developed.","zh":"當濃密根毛已經長成，蘆葦效果最佳。"},{"en":"To perform best when something happens means to work most effectively under that condition.","zh":"perform best when something happens 指在某條件下運作最有效。"},{"en":"Students perform best when they sleep enough and understand the task clearly.","zh":"當學生睡眠足夠並清楚理解任務，他們表現最佳。"},{"en":"Reed beds work better after roots grow enough to support microorganisms.","zh":"當根部充分生長以支持微生物，蘆葦床運作更好。"},{"en":"This phrase links strong performance with the right condition.","zh":"這個短語把良好表現與合適條件連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dense layer of root hairs","meaning":"濃密的根毛層","examples":[{"en":"A dense layer of root hairs improves water treatment.","zh":"濃密的根毛層改善水處理。"},{"en":"A dense layer of root hairs is a thick covering of tiny root structures around plant roots.","zh":"dense layer of root hairs 指植物根部周圍由微小根部結構形成的厚層。"},{"en":"A plant with many root hairs can absorb water and nutrients more effectively.","zh":"有許多根毛的植物可以更有效吸收水和養分。"},{"en":"In reed beds, dense root hairs create more surface area for treatment processes.","zh":"在蘆葦床中，濃密根毛創造更多表面面積供處理過程發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a thick root surface that helps cleaning.","zh":"這個短語描述有助淨化的厚根部表面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fully develop","meaning":"完全生長","examples":[{"en":"The reed roots take about three years to fully develop.","zh":"蘆葦根大約需要三年才完全生長。"},{"en":"To fully develop means to grow or form completely.","zh":"fully develop 指完全成長或形成。"},{"en":"A child’s reading confidence may take years to fully develop.","zh":"孩子的閱讀信心可能需要多年才完全發展。"},{"en":"Treatment beds may not work at their best until roots fully develop.","zh":"在根部完全生長前，處理床可能未能發揮最佳效果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching a mature or complete stage.","zh":"這個短語描述達到成熟或完整階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"vary widely among","meaning":"在……之間差異很大","examples":[{"en":"The type of wetland used varies widely among European countries.","zh":"所使用的濕地類型在歐洲國家之間差異很大。"},{"en":"To vary widely among places means to be very different from one place to another.","zh":"vary widely among places 指不同地方之間有很大差異。"},{"en":"School lunch prices vary widely among different districts.","zh":"不同地區之間的學校午餐價格差異很大。"},{"en":"Designs vary widely because countries have different climates, budgets, and rules.","zh":"設計差異很大，因為各國有不同氣候、預算和規定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large differences across groups or places.","zh":"這個短語描述群體或地方之間的大差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"depend on","meaning":"取決於","examples":[{"en":"The wetland design depends on each country’s development priorities.","zh":"濕地設計取決於每個國家的發展優先事項。"},{"en":"To depend on something means to be decided or affected by it.","zh":"depend on something 指由某事決定或受其影響。"},{"en":"A student’s revision plan depends on how much time they have before the exam.","zh":"學生的溫習計劃取決於考試前還有多少時間。"},{"en":"If conditions change, the best choice may depend on new costs or needs.","zh":"如果條件改變，最佳選擇可能取決於新的成本或需要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one thing is controlled by another factor.","zh":"這個短語顯示一件事受另一因素控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"development priorities","meaning":"發展優先事項","examples":[{"en":"Different countries have different development priorities.","zh":"不同國家有不同發展優先事項。"},{"en":"Development priorities are the goals or needs a government or community chooses to focus on first.","zh":"development priorities 指政府或社區選擇首先集中處理的目標或需要。"},{"en":"A city may set housing and transport as its development priorities.","zh":"城市可能把房屋和交通列為發展優先事項。"},{"en":"Priorities affect which projects receive money, land, and attention.","zh":"優先事項影響哪些項目獲得資金、土地和關注。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why places may choose different designs or policies.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何不同地方會選擇不同設計或政策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"horizontal-flow wetlands","meaning":"水平流人工濕地","examples":[{"en":"Horizontal-flow wetlands move wastewater across a long reed bed.","zh":"水平流人工濕地讓污水流經長形蘆葦床。"},{"en":"Horizontal-flow wetlands are systems where water travels sideways through the treatment bed.","zh":"horizontal-flow wetlands 指水在處理床中橫向流動的系統。"},{"en":"A farm may use a horizontal-flow wetland when the wastewater is only lightly polluted.","zh":"當污水只是輕微受污染，農場可能使用水平流人工濕地。"},{"en":"Horizontal movement gives water time to pass through roots, gravel, and microorganisms.","zh":"水平流動讓水有時間穿過根部、碎石和微生物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a wetland design based on sideways flow.","zh":"這個短語描述一種以橫向水流為基礎的濕地設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"vertical-flow wetlands","meaning":"垂直流人工濕地","examples":[{"en":"Vertical-flow wetlands direct wastewater down through several layers.","zh":"垂直流人工濕地引導污水向下穿過多層。"},{"en":"Vertical-flow wetlands are systems where wastewater moves downward through planted treatment layers.","zh":"vertical-flow wetlands 指污水向下穿過種有植物的處理層的系統。"},{"en":"A small factory may use a vertical-flow wetland if the wastewater is stronger.","zh":"如果污水濃度較高，小型工廠可能使用垂直流人工濕地。"},{"en":"Downward flow can improve contact with oxygen, gravel, roots, and microorganisms.","zh":"向下流動可以改善污水與氧氣、碎石、根部和微生物的接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a wetland design based on water moving down.","zh":"這個短語描述一種以水向下流動為基礎的濕地設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sludge treatment","meaning":"污泥處理","examples":[{"en":"Constructed wetlands have also been used successfully for sludge treatment.","zh":"人工濕地也已成功用於污泥處理。"},{"en":"Sludge treatment is the processing of thick waste material left after wastewater treatment.","zh":"sludge treatment 指處理污水處理後留下的濃稠廢物。"},{"en":"A sewage plant needs sludge treatment so thick waste does not pile up untreated.","zh":"污水處理廠需要污泥處理，避免濃稠廢物未經處理地堆積。"},{"en":"Treating sludge reduces smells, pollution, and health risks.","zh":"處理污泥可以減少臭味、污染和健康風險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to dealing with the solid or semi-solid part of waste.","zh":"這個短語指處理廢物中的固體或半固體部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"specialised designs","meaning":"專門設計","examples":[{"en":"Specialised designs can treat agricultural and industrial wastewater.","zh":"專門設計可以處理農業和工業污水。"},{"en":"Specialised designs are designs made for a particular purpose or problem.","zh":"specialised designs 指為特定目的或問題而設計的方案。"},{"en":"A wheelchair ramp is a specialised design that helps people enter buildings safely.","zh":"輪椅斜道是幫助人安全進入建築物的專門設計。"},{"en":"Wastewater from farms and factories may need specialised designs because pollutants differ.","zh":"農場和工廠的污水可能需要專門設計，因為污染物不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes designs created for specific needs.","zh":"這個短語描述為特定需要而創造的設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"allow the retention of","meaning":"讓……得以保留","examples":[{"en":"Some wetland designs allow the retention of useful microorganisms.","zh":"有些濕地設計讓有用微生物得以保留。"},{"en":"To allow the retention of something means to make it possible to keep it in place.","zh":"allow the retention of something 指使某物能夠被保留在原位。"},{"en":"A good classroom routine allows the retention of useful study habits.","zh":"良好課室常規可以讓有用學習習慣得以保留。"},{"en":"Keeping microorganisms in the bed helps the system continue digesting waste.","zh":"把微生物留在床層中，有助系統繼續分解廢物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preventing useful things from being lost.","zh":"這個短語描述防止有用事物流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"microbiological organisms","meaning":"微生物","examples":[{"en":"Microbiological organisms help digest waste in constructed wetlands.","zh":"微生物幫助在人工濕地中分解廢物。"},{"en":"Microbiological organisms are tiny living organisms, especially bacteria, fungi, and similar microbes.","zh":"microbiological organisms 指微小生物，尤其是細菌、真菌和類似微生物。"},{"en":"Compost contains microbiological organisms that break down food scraps.","zh":"堆肥含有分解食物殘渣的微生物。"},{"en":"These organisms are important because they carry out much of the cleaning work.","zh":"這些生物很重要，因為它們執行大部分清潔工作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to living microscopic helpers in a treatment system.","zh":"這個短語指處理系統中的顯微活體幫手。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"constructed wetlands","meaning":"人工濕地","examples":[{"en":"Constructed wetlands imitate natural water-purification processes.","zh":"人工濕地模仿天然淨水過程。"},{"en":"Constructed wetlands are human-made wetlands designed to treat wastewater.","zh":"constructed wetlands 指人造、用來處理污水的濕地。"},{"en":"A school campus could use constructed wetlands to clean runoff before it reaches a pond.","zh":"學校校園可以使用人工濕地，在雨水徑流到達池塘前把它清潔。"},{"en":"These systems copy nature by using plants, gravel, water flow, and microorganisms.","zh":"這些系統透過使用植物、碎石、水流和微生物來模仿自然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes engineered wetlands built for environmental treatment.","zh":"這個短語描述為環境處理而建造的工程濕地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"agricultural wastewater","meaning":"農業污水","examples":[{"en":"Some reed beds are designed to treat agricultural wastewater.","zh":"有些蘆葦床被設計用來處理農業污水。"},{"en":"Agricultural wastewater is dirty water from farms, crops, animals, fertilisers, or farm buildings.","zh":"agricultural wastewater 指來自農場、作物、動物、肥料或農場建築的污水。"},{"en":"A dairy farm may produce agricultural wastewater when washing floors and equipment.","zh":"奶牛場清洗地面和設備時可能產生農業污水。"},{"en":"If untreated, agricultural wastewater can carry nutrients and bacteria into rivers.","zh":"如果未經處理，農業污水可以把養分和細菌帶入河流。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to wastewater from farming activities.","zh":"這個短語指來自農業活動的污水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"industrial wastewater","meaning":"工業污水","examples":[{"en":"Specialised wetlands can treat certain kinds of industrial wastewater.","zh":"專門濕地可以處理某些種類的工業污水。"},{"en":"Industrial wastewater is used water from factories, workshops, or production processes.","zh":"industrial wastewater 指來自工廠、工場或生產過程的用過的水。"},{"en":"A food factory may produce industrial wastewater when cleaning machines.","zh":"食品工廠清洗機器時可能產生工業污水。"},{"en":"Industrial wastewater may contain chemicals, oils, metals, or high levels of organic waste.","zh":"工業污水可能含有化學品、油、金屬或高含量有機廢物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to wastewater from industrial activity.","zh":"這個短語指來自工業活動的污水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"control diffuse pollution","meaning":"控制分散性污染","examples":[{"en":"Constructed wetlands can help control diffuse pollution.","zh":"人工濕地可以幫助控制分散性污染。"},{"en":"To control diffuse pollution means to reduce pollution that comes from many scattered sources.","zh":"control diffuse pollution 指減少來自許多分散來源的污染。"},{"en":"Farms can create diffuse pollution when rain washes fertiliser from several fields into streams.","zh":"雨水把多塊田的肥料沖入溪流時，農場可以造成分散性污染。"},{"en":"Wetlands help control this pollution by slowing runoff and trapping pollutants.","zh":"濕地透過減慢徑流和截留污染物來幫助控制這種污染。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to managing pollution that does not come from one clear pipe.","zh":"這個短語指管理不是來自單一明確管道的污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"slightly polluted","meaning":"輕微受污染","examples":[{"en":"A horizontal system may be used when the water is only slightly polluted.","zh":"當水只是輕微受污染時，可以使用水平系統。"},{"en":"Slightly polluted means containing a small amount of pollution.","zh":"slightly polluted 指含有少量污染。"},{"en":"A stream may be slightly polluted after light runoff from a garden.","zh":"花園少量徑流流入後，溪流可能輕微受污染。"},{"en":"Slightly polluted water may need treatment, but it is easier to clean than heavily polluted water.","zh":"輕微受污染的水可能需要處理，但比嚴重污染的水較容易清潔。"},{"en":"This phrase describes low-level contamination.","zh":"這個短語描述低程度污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"free-water surface flow","meaning":"自由水面流","examples":[{"en":"In a free-water surface-flow wetland, water moves above the bed.","zh":"在自由水面流濕地中，水在床層上方流動。"},{"en":"Free-water surface flow means water flows openly above the soil, sand, or gravel surface.","zh":"free-water surface flow 指水在土壤、沙或碎石表面上方開放流動。"},{"en":"A shallow pond with reeds may use free-water surface flow if water is visible on top.","zh":"如果水在表面可見，有蘆葦的淺池可能使用自由水面流。"},{"en":"Open surface water can support wildlife, but it may also allow smells or mosquitoes.","zh":"開放表面水可以支持野生生物，但也可能產生氣味或蚊患。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a wetland system with visible water flow.","zh":"這個短語描述有可見水流的濕地系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"subsurface water flow","meaning":"地下水流","examples":[{"en":"In a subsurface water-flow wetland, effluent passes through the bed.","zh":"在地下水流濕地中，排放水穿過床層。"},{"en":"Subsurface water flow means water moves below the visible surface.","zh":"subsurface water flow 指水在可見表面以下流動。"},{"en":"A garden drainage system may use subsurface water flow so water does not stand on the path.","zh":"花園排水系統可能使用地下水流，使水不會積在路面上。"},{"en":"Hidden flow can reduce odours because wastewater is not exposed on the surface.","zh":"隱藏水流可以減少臭味，因為污水沒有暴露在表面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes water moving through material beneath the top layer.","zh":"這個短語描述水在頂層下方穿過材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in the former","meaning":"在前者中","examples":[{"en":"In the former system, the water flows above the sand and gravel.","zh":"在前者中，水在沙和碎石上方流動。"},{"en":"In the former means in the first of two things just mentioned.","zh":"in the former 指在剛提到的兩者中的第一個。"},{"en":"There are two classes, online and face-to-face; in the former, students study at home.","zh":"有兩種課堂，網課和面授課；在前者中，學生在家學習。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers follow comparisons between two options.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者跟上兩個選項之間的比較。"},{"en":"It refers back to the first item, not the second.","zh":"它指回第一項，而不是第二項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"effluent","meaning":"經處理的污水；排放水","examples":[{"en":"The effluent flows slowly through the reed bed.","zh":"排放水緩慢流經蘆葦床。"},{"en":"Effluent is wastewater or liquid waste flowing out from a treatment process, factory, or sewage system.","zh":"effluent 指從處理過程、工廠或污水系統流出的污水或液態廢物。"},{"en":"A factory must test its effluent before releasing it into a river.","zh":"工廠在把排放水排入河流前，必須先測試它。"},{"en":"If effluent contains pollutants, it needs further treatment before discharge.","zh":"如果排放水含有污染物，就需要進一步處理才可排放。"},{"en":"This word refers to outflowing wastewater.","zh":"這個詞指流出的污水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"flow freely above","meaning":"在……上方自由流動","examples":[{"en":"In one system, the effluent flows freely above the filter bed.","zh":"在一種系統中，排放水在過濾床上方自由流動。"},{"en":"To flow freely above something means to move openly over its top without being hidden inside it.","zh":"flow freely above something 指在某物頂部開放地流動，而不是藏在其內部。"},{"en":"Rainwater may flow freely above a paved playground during heavy rain.","zh":"大雨期間，雨水可能在鋪面操場上方自由流動。"},{"en":"Open flow can be easier to see but may create smell or mosquito problems.","zh":"開放水流較容易看見，但可能造成氣味或蚊患問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible movement over a surface.","zh":"這個短語描述水在表面上方可見地流動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sand-and-gravel bed","meaning":"沙石床","examples":[{"en":"The reeds are planted in a sand-and-gravel bed.","zh":"蘆葦種植在沙石床中。"},{"en":"A sand-and-gravel bed is a layer or area made of sand and small stones.","zh":"sand-and-gravel bed 指由沙和小石組成的層或區域。"},{"en":"A garden path may use a sand-and-gravel bed to help rainwater drain away.","zh":"花園小徑可能使用沙石床，幫助雨水排走。"},{"en":"In reed beds, sand and gravel support plants and help filter wastewater.","zh":"在蘆葦床中，沙和碎石支撐植物並幫助過濾污水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the material base in which reeds grow.","zh":"這個短語描述蘆葦生長的材料基底。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the latter","meaning":"在後者中","examples":[{"en":"In the latter system, the effluent passes through the filter material.","zh":"在後者中，排放水穿過過濾材料。"},{"en":"In the latter means in the second of two things just mentioned.","zh":"in the latter 指在剛提到的兩者中的第二個。"},{"en":"There are two options, cycling and walking; in the latter, no bicycle is needed.","zh":"有兩個選項，踏單車和步行；在後者中，不需要單車。"},{"en":"This phrase helps avoid repeating the full name of the second option.","zh":"這個短語有助避免重複第二個選項的完整名稱。"},{"en":"It refers back to the second item, not the first.","zh":"它指回第二項，而不是第一項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pass through","meaning":"穿過","examples":[{"en":"Wastewater passes through layers of sand and gravel.","zh":"污水穿過沙和碎石層。"},{"en":"To pass through something means to move from one side or part of it to another.","zh":"pass through something 指從某物的一邊或一部分移到另一邊或另一部分。"},{"en":"Air passes through a window screen when the window is open.","zh":"窗戶打開時，空氣穿過窗紗。"},{"en":"As water passes through filtering materials, particles and pollutants may be trapped.","zh":"當水穿過過濾材料，微粒和污染物可能被截留。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement inside or across a barrier or layer.","zh":"這個短語描述在屏障或層內部或穿越其中的移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"plant stems and leaves","meaning":"植物莖和葉","examples":[{"en":"Effluent is treated by plant stems, leaves and rhizomes.","zh":"排放水由植物莖、葉和根莖處理。"},{"en":"Plant stems and leaves are the parts of plants that support growth and exchange gases with the environment.","zh":"plant stems and leaves 指支持植物生長並與環境交換氣體的植物部分。"},{"en":"In a garden, plant stems hold leaves up so they can receive sunlight.","zh":"在花園中，植物莖支撐葉子，讓葉子接受陽光。"},{"en":"Stems, leaves, and rhizomes can help create conditions for water purification.","zh":"莖、葉和根莖可以幫助創造淨水條件。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies visible plant parts involved in treatment.","zh":"這個短語指出參與處理的可見植物部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"densely planted","meaning":"種植得十分密集","examples":[{"en":"Free-water wetlands are usually densely planted.","zh":"自由水面濕地通常種植得十分密集。"},{"en":"Densely planted means filled with many plants growing close together.","zh":"densely planted 指有許多植物緊密生長在一起。"},{"en":"A densely planted garden path may feel cooler because leaves provide shade.","zh":"種植得十分密集的花園小徑可能較涼快，因為葉子提供遮蔭。"},{"en":"Dense planting can help trap pollutants, but it may also reduce oxygen movement.","zh":"密集種植可以幫助截留污染物，但也可能減少氧氣流動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a high concentration of plants in one area.","zh":"這個短語描述某區域有高密度植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"water depth","meaning":"水深","examples":[{"en":"The water depth is typically less than 0.4 metres.","zh":"水深通常少於 0.4 米。"},{"en":"Water depth is the distance from the water surface to the bottom.","zh":"water depth 指水面到底部的距離。"},{"en":"Children’s pools usually have shallow water depth for safety.","zh":"兒童泳池通常水深較淺，以保障安全。"},{"en":"Water depth affects plants, oxygen, temperature, and how easily people can maintain the system.","zh":"水深影響植物、氧氣、溫度，以及人們維修系統的難易度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how deep the water is.","zh":"這個短語描述水有多深。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"less than 0.4 metres","meaning":"少於0.4米","examples":[{"en":"These wetlands normally have water depths of less than 0.4 metres.","zh":"這些濕地通常水深少於 0.4 米。"},{"en":"Less than 0.4 metres means under forty centimetres deep or long.","zh":"less than 0.4 metres 指深度或長度少於四十厘米。"},{"en":"A low step may be less than 0.4 metres high, so most adults can step over it easily.","zh":"低矮台階可能少於 0.4 米高，所以大多數成年人可以輕易跨過。"},{"en":"Shallow water can affect which plants grow and how oxygen enters the system.","zh":"淺水可以影響哪些植物生長，以及氧氣如何進入系統。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a maximum measurement below a stated amount.","zh":"這個短語給出低於某數值的最大量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dense planting","meaning":"密集種植","examples":[{"en":"Dense planting can restrict oxygen entering the water.","zh":"密集種植可以限制氧氣進入水中。"},{"en":"Dense planting means growing many plants close together in one area.","zh":"dense planting 指在一個區域內讓許多植物緊密生長。"},{"en":"Dense planting in a garden can reduce weeds by covering open soil.","zh":"花園中的密集種植可以覆蓋裸露土壤，從而減少雜草。"},{"en":"In water treatment, dense planting may trap material but also slow oxygen diffusion.","zh":"在水處理中，密集種植可能截留物質，但也會減慢氧氣擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a planting pattern with little empty space.","zh":"這個短語描述空隙很少的種植模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"limit the diffusion of oxygen","meaning":"限制氧氣擴散","examples":[{"en":"Dense vegetation may limit the diffusion of oxygen into the water.","zh":"密集植被可能限制氧氣擴散到水中。"},{"en":"To limit the diffusion of oxygen means to reduce how easily oxygen spreads through a substance or space.","zh":"limit the diffusion of oxygen 指減少氧氣在物質或空間中擴散的容易程度。"},{"en":"A sealed classroom limits the diffusion of fresh air if windows stay closed.","zh":"如果窗戶一直關閉，密封課室會限制新鮮空氣擴散。"},{"en":"If oxygen diffusion is limited, some organisms may not get enough oxygen.","zh":"如果氧氣擴散受限制，有些生物可能得不到足夠氧氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slowing or reducing the spread of oxygen.","zh":"這個短語描述減慢或減少氧氣擴散。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"work particularly well for","meaning":"對……特別有效","examples":[{"en":"Horizontal systems work particularly well for lightly polluted effluent.","zh":"水平系統對輕度污染排放水特別有效。"},{"en":"To work particularly well for something means to be especially effective for that purpose or condition.","zh":"work particularly well for something 指對某目的或情況尤其有效。"},{"en":"Flashcards work particularly well for memorising vocabulary before a test.","zh":"單字卡對考試前記憶詞彙特別有效。"},{"en":"A method may work well for one problem but poorly for another.","zh":"一種方法可能對一個問題有效，但對另一問題效果差。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the situation where a method is most suitable.","zh":"這個短語指出方法最適合的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"low-strength effluent","meaning":"低濃度污水","examples":[{"en":"Low-strength effluent contains relatively low levels of pollution.","zh":"低濃度污水含有相對較低水平的污染物。"},{"en":"Low-strength effluent is wastewater that has a lower concentration of pollutants.","zh":"low-strength effluent 指污染物濃度較低的污水或排放水。"},{"en":"Water from a lightly used washroom may be low-strength effluent compared with sewage from toilets.","zh":"與廁所污水相比，使用量較少的洗手間排水可能是低濃度污水。"},{"en":"Low-strength effluent is usually easier to treat than heavily polluted liquid waste.","zh":"低濃度污水通常比嚴重污染的液態廢物較容易處理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wastewater that is not very strong or concentrated.","zh":"這個短語描述濃度不高的污水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"undergo pretreatment","meaning":"接受預先處理","examples":[{"en":"Some effluent undergoes pretreatment before entering the reed bed.","zh":"有些排放水在進入蘆葦床前接受預先處理。"},{"en":"To undergo pretreatment means to receive an earlier treatment before the main process begins.","zh":"undergo pretreatment 指在主要過程開始前接受較早階段的處理。"},{"en":"Vegetables may undergo pretreatment by being washed before cooking.","zh":"蔬菜在烹煮前可能透過清洗接受預先處理。"},{"en":"Pretreatment can remove large solids and make later treatment easier.","zh":"預先處理可以清除大型固體，令後續處理更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparation before the main treatment stage.","zh":"這個短語描述主要處理階段前的準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"some form of pretreatment","meaning":"某種形式的預先處理","examples":[{"en":"The system performs well after some form of pretreatment.","zh":"該系統在某種形式的預先處理後效果良好。"},{"en":"Some form of pretreatment means at least one earlier treatment step before the main process.","zh":"some form of pretreatment 指主要過程前至少有一個早期處理步驟。"},{"en":"A stain on clothes may need some form of pretreatment before normal washing.","zh":"衣物上的污漬在正常清洗前可能需要某種形式的預先處理。"},{"en":"Pretreatment can prevent the main system from being overloaded.","zh":"預先處理可以防止主要系統負荷過重。"},{"en":"This phrase is general because the exact first step may vary.","zh":"這個短語較概括，因為確切第一步可能不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"play an invaluable role in","meaning":"在……中發揮不可估量的作用","examples":[{"en":"Reed beds play an invaluable role in final-stage water treatment.","zh":"蘆葦床在最後階段水處理中發揮不可估量的作用。"},{"en":"To play an invaluable role in something means to be extremely useful and important in it.","zh":"play an invaluable role in something 指在某事中極其有用和重要。"},{"en":"Nurses play an invaluable role in helping patients recover after surgery.","zh":"護士在幫助手術後病人康復方面發揮不可估量的作用。"},{"en":"If a role is invaluable, the system would be much weaker without it.","zh":"如果某角色不可估量，沒有它系統會弱很多。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly praises the importance of something.","zh":"這個短語強烈讚揚某事的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tertiary treatment","meaning":"三級污水處理","examples":[{"en":"Reed beds may be used during tertiary treatment.","zh":"蘆葦床可能用於三級污水處理期間。"},{"en":"Tertiary treatment is the advanced final stage of wastewater treatment after earlier cleaning steps.","zh":"tertiary treatment 指在早期清潔步驟後進行的進階最後階段污水處理。"},{"en":"A treatment plant may use tertiary treatment to remove remaining nutrients or bacteria.","zh":"處理廠可能使用三級處理來清除殘餘養分或細菌。"},{"en":"This stage improves water quality before discharge or reuse.","zh":"這個階段在排放或重用前改善水質。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a later, more polishing stage of treatment.","zh":"這個短語指較後期、更深度淨化的處理階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"polishing of effluent","meaning":"污水深度淨化","examples":[{"en":"The polishing of effluent removes remaining pollutants.","zh":"污水深度淨化清除殘餘污染物。"},{"en":"Polishing of effluent is the final cleaning step that improves already-treated wastewater.","zh":"polishing of effluent 指改善已處理污水的最後清潔步驟。"},{"en":"A school report may be polished after the main writing is finished.","zh":"學校報告完成主要寫作後，可能再作潤飾。"},{"en":"In wastewater treatment, polishing removes small remaining problems after earlier treatment.","zh":"在污水處理中，深度淨化會在早期處理後清除小量殘餘問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes final-stage improvement rather than the first cleaning step.","zh":"這個短語描述最後階段改善，而不是第一步清潔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"long reed bed","meaning":"長形蘆葦床","examples":[{"en":"A horizontal system uses a long reed bed.","zh":"水平系統使用長形蘆葦床。"},{"en":"A long reed bed is an extended planted bed that gives wastewater more distance to travel.","zh":"long reed bed 指延伸較長的種植床，讓污水有更長距離流動。"},{"en":"A farm may need a long reed bed if water must flow slowly for proper cleaning.","zh":"如果水需要緩慢流動才能妥善淨化，農場可能需要長形蘆葦床。"},{"en":"The longer the bed, the more land it may require.","zh":"床層越長，可能需要越多土地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical length of the treatment area.","zh":"這個短語描述處理區域的實體長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"flow horizontally through","meaning":"水平流經……","examples":[{"en":"The liquid flows horizontally through the roots.","zh":"液體水平流經根部。"},{"en":"To flow horizontally through something means to move sideways through it.","zh":"flow horizontally through something 指橫向穿過某物。"},{"en":"Air may flow horizontally through a classroom when windows on both sides are open.","zh":"當課室兩邊窗戶打開，空氣可能水平流經課室。"},{"en":"Horizontal flow gives water time to contact roots and filtering materials.","zh":"水平流動讓水有時間接觸根部和過濾材料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sideways movement through a system.","zh":"這個短語描述在系統中橫向移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"about 100 metres long","meaning":"約100米長","examples":[{"en":"A horizontal reed bed may be about 100 metres long.","zh":"水平蘆葦床可能約 100 米長。"},{"en":"About 100 metres long means roughly one hundred metres in length.","zh":"about 100 metres long 指長度大約一百米。"},{"en":"A running track straight section may be about 100 metres long.","zh":"跑道直路部分可能約 100 米長。"},{"en":"Saying “about” shows the measurement is approximate, not exact.","zh":"說 about 顯示量度是約數，不是精確數字。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a practical sense of size.","zh":"這個短語給出實際大小感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the downside of","meaning":"……的缺點","examples":[{"en":"The downside of horizontal reed beds is their large land requirement.","zh":"水平蘆葦床的缺點是需要大量土地。"},{"en":"The downside of something is its disadvantage or negative side.","zh":"downside of something 指某事的缺點或負面一面。"},{"en":"The downside of online shopping is that you cannot try items before buying them.","zh":"網上購物的缺點是購買前不能試用商品。"},{"en":"A method may work well but still have a downside that limits its use.","zh":"一種方法可能有效，但仍有缺點限制其使用。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a drawback.","zh":"這個短語引入不利之處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"use up land space","meaning":"佔用土地空間","examples":[{"en":"Horizontal systems use up a great deal of land space.","zh":"水平系統佔用大量土地空間。"},{"en":"To use up land space means to occupy land so it is no longer available for other uses.","zh":"use up land space 指佔用土地，使它不能再用於其他用途。"},{"en":"A large car park can use up land space that might otherwise become a playground.","zh":"大型停車場可以佔用原本可作操場的土地空間。"},{"en":"Systems that use up too much land may be unsuitable in crowded areas.","zh":"佔用太多土地的系統可能不適合擠迫地區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes consuming limited physical space.","zh":"這個短語描述消耗有限實體空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take a long time to","meaning":"需要很長時間才……","examples":[{"en":"Horizontal beds can take a long time to produce clean water.","zh":"水平床可能需要很長時間才產生潔淨水。"},{"en":"To take a long time to do something means to need much time before it is finished.","zh":"take a long time to do something 指需要大量時間才完成某事。"},{"en":"Learning pronunciation can take a long time to master.","zh":"學習發音可能需要很長時間才掌握。"},{"en":"Slow systems may still be useful if they are cheap, simple, and reliable.","zh":"緩慢系統如果便宜、簡單且可靠，仍可能有用。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights time as a limitation.","zh":"這個短語突出時間是一項限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"produce clean water","meaning":"產生潔淨食水","examples":[{"en":"The reed bed gradually produces cleaner water.","zh":"蘆葦床逐漸產生較乾淨的水。"},{"en":"To produce clean water means to create or output water that has fewer pollutants.","zh":"produce clean water 指產生或輸出污染物較少的水。"},{"en":"A household filter can produce clean water for drinking and cooking.","zh":"家用濾水器可以產生供飲用和煮食的潔淨水。"},{"en":"Treatment systems produce clean water by removing waste, solids, and harmful organisms.","zh":"處理系統透過清除廢物、固體和有害生物來產生潔淨水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the desired result of water treatment.","zh":"這個短語描述水處理的理想結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"vertical-flow reed bed","meaning":"垂直流蘆葦床","examples":[{"en":"A vertical-flow reed bed directs wastewater downwards.","zh":"垂直流蘆葦床引導污水向下流動。"},{"en":"A vertical-flow reed bed is a reed-bed system where wastewater moves down through layers.","zh":"vertical-flow reed bed 指污水向下穿過多層的蘆葦床系統。"},{"en":"A rural workshop may use a vertical-flow reed bed if space is limited.","zh":"如果空間有限，鄉郊工場可能使用垂直流蘆葦床。"},{"en":"Downward flow can treat stronger wastewater in a smaller area.","zh":"向下流動可以在較小面積中處理較高濃度污水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a compact reed-bed design based on downward movement.","zh":"這個短語描述一種以向下流動為基礎的緊湊蘆葦床設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sealed trench","meaning":"密封溝槽","examples":[{"en":"The reeds grow inside a sealed trench.","zh":"蘆葦生長在密封溝槽內。"},{"en":"A sealed trench is a long narrow hole lined or closed so liquid cannot leak out freely.","zh":"sealed trench 指經襯墊或封閉的長窄坑道，使液體不能隨意滲漏。"},{"en":"Builders may use a sealed trench to guide drainage water safely.","zh":"建築工人可能使用密封溝槽來安全引導排水。"},{"en":"Sealing the trench helps control where wastewater goes.","zh":"密封溝槽有助控制污水流向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a contained channel used in treatment design.","zh":"這個短語描述處理設計中的受控渠道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"gravel-filled trench","meaning":"填滿碎石的溝槽","examples":[{"en":"A vertical reed bed is a gravel-filled trench.","zh":"垂直蘆葦床是填滿碎石的溝槽。"},{"en":"A gravel-filled trench is a narrow channel filled with small stones.","zh":"gravel-filled trench 指填滿小石的窄渠道。"},{"en":"A garden drain may use a gravel-filled trench to help water move away.","zh":"花園排水可能使用填滿碎石的溝槽來幫助水排走。"},{"en":"Gravel creates spaces where water can pass and microorganisms can live.","zh":"碎石創造空隙，讓水通過並讓微生物生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both the shape and material of the treatment bed.","zh":"這個短語同時描述處理床的形狀和材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be planted in a bed","meaning":"種植在……床層中","examples":[{"en":"The reeds are planted in a bed about 60 centimetres deep.","zh":"蘆葦種植在約 60 厘米深的床層中。"},{"en":"To be planted in a bed means to be grown in a prepared layer or area of soil, sand, or gravel.","zh":"be planted in a bed 指在準備好的土壤、沙或碎石層中種植。"},{"en":"Flowers may be planted in a raised bed outside a classroom.","zh":"花可以種植在課室外的高架花床中。"},{"en":"The depth and material of the bed affect how roots grow and water drains.","zh":"床層的深度和材料會影響根部如何生長和排水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where plants are placed for growth.","zh":"這個短語描述植物被放在哪裡生長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"apply wastewater to","meaning":"把污水注入……","examples":[{"en":"Wastewater is applied to the top of the reed bed.","zh":"污水被注入蘆葦床頂部。"},{"en":"To apply wastewater to something means to put or spread wastewater onto it for treatment.","zh":"apply wastewater to something 指把污水放到或分布到某物上進行處理。"},{"en":"A treatment worker may apply wastewater to a filter bed in measured amounts.","zh":"處理工人可能按量把污水注入過濾床。"},{"en":"Controlled application prevents the system from flooding or becoming overloaded.","zh":"受控注入可以防止系統水浸或負荷過重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first step of feeding wastewater into a treatment bed.","zh":"這個短語描述把污水送入處理床的第一步。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rhizome zone","meaning":"根莖區","examples":[{"en":"The wastewater first flows through the rhizome zone.","zh":"污水首先流經根莖區。"},{"en":"The rhizome zone is the layer where plant rhizomes grow and help treatment begin.","zh":"rhizome zone 指植物根莖生長並幫助處理開始的層。"},{"en":"In a reed bed, the rhizome zone sits near the upper plant-root area.","zh":"在蘆葦床中，根莖區位於較上層的植物根部區域附近。"},{"en":"This zone helps spread wastewater and supports organisms that break down waste.","zh":"這個區域幫助分散污水，並支持分解廢物的生物。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies one treatment layer around underground plant stems.","zh":"這個短語指出地下植物莖周圍的一個處理層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sludge as a substrate","meaning":"以污泥作為基質","examples":[{"en":"The rhizome zone uses sludge as a substrate.","zh":"根莖區以污泥作為基質。"},{"en":"Sludge as a substrate means sludge is used as the material or base where organisms live or processes occur.","zh":"sludge as a substrate 指污泥被用作生物生活或過程發生的材料或基底。"},{"en":"In composting, food waste can act as a substrate for microbes.","zh":"在堆肥中，食物廢物可以作為微生物的基質。"},{"en":"A suitable substrate gives microorganisms something to live on and break down.","zh":"合適基質給微生物生活和分解的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sludge serving as a working base in the treatment layer.","zh":"這個短語描述污泥在處理層中作為工作基底。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"root zone","meaning":"根區","examples":[{"en":"The water then passes through the root zone.","zh":"然後水穿過根區。"},{"en":"The root zone is the area around plant roots where water, nutrients, and microorganisms interact.","zh":"root zone 指植物根部周圍水、養分和微生物互相作用的區域。"},{"en":"Gardeners water the root zone because that is where plants take in water.","zh":"園丁澆灌根區，因為植物在那裡吸水。"},{"en":"In reed beds, the root zone is important because much treatment happens there.","zh":"在蘆葦床中，根區很重要，因為許多處理過程在那裡發生。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the active area around roots.","zh":"這個短語指根部周圍的活躍區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sand as a substrate","meaning":"以沙作為基質","examples":[{"en":"The root zone contains sand as a substrate.","zh":"根區含有以沙作為基質的部分。"},{"en":"Sand as a substrate means sand is used as the base material that supports roots and microbes.","zh":"sand as a substrate 指使用沙作為支撐根部和微生物的基底材料。"},{"en":"Aquarium plants may grow in sand as a substrate at the bottom of a tank.","zh":"水族箱植物可能在缸底以沙作為基質生長。"},{"en":"Sand allows water to pass through while also filtering particles.","zh":"沙讓水通過，同時過濾微粒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sand serving as a treatment and support material.","zh":"這個短語描述沙作為處理和支撐材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"layer of gravel","meaning":"碎石層","examples":[{"en":"A layer of gravel provides drainage beneath the sand.","zh":"碎石層在沙下方提供排水。"},{"en":"A layer of gravel is a spread of small stones placed over an area.","zh":"layer of gravel 指鋪在某區域上的一層小石。"},{"en":"A plant pot may have a layer of gravel at the bottom to help water drain.","zh":"花盆底部可能有碎石層，以幫助排水。"},{"en":"Gravel layers create spaces that let water move through more easily.","zh":"碎石層創造空隙，使水更容易流過。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a drainage-supporting layer of small stones.","zh":"這個短語描述支持排水的小石層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"for drainage","meaning":"用作排水","examples":[{"en":"The lowest gravel layer is used for drainage.","zh":"最底的碎石層用作排水。"},{"en":"For drainage means for carrying water away or preventing water from collecting.","zh":"for drainage 指用來把水排走或防止積水。"},{"en":"Builders may slope a roof for drainage so rainwater does not stay on top.","zh":"建築工人可能把屋頂做成斜面用作排水，使雨水不會停留在上面。"},{"en":"Good drainage prevents standing water, smells, and damage.","zh":"良好排水可以防止積水、臭味和損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose of a layer, pipe, or slope.","zh":"這個短語解釋某層、管道或斜坡的用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"underdrainage system","meaning":"地下排水系統","examples":[{"en":"The treated water is collected in an underdrainage system.","zh":"經處理的水被收集在地下排水系統中。"},{"en":"An underdrainage system is a drainage system placed beneath a treatment bed or ground surface.","zh":"underdrainage system 指放在處理床或地表下方的排水系統。"},{"en":"A sports field may have an underdrainage system to remove rainwater after storms.","zh":"運動場可能有地下排水系統，以在暴雨後排走雨水。"},{"en":"Underdrainage collects treated water and directs it to an outlet.","zh":"地下排水系統收集處理後的水，並把它導向出口。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to hidden drainage below the surface.","zh":"這個短語指表面以下的隱藏排水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"large stones","meaning":"大石","examples":[{"en":"The underdrainage system contains large stones.","zh":"地下排水系統含有大石。"},{"en":"Large stones are bigger pieces of rock used to create space and support drainage.","zh":"large stones 指用來創造空隙並支持排水的較大岩石塊。"},{"en":"A garden drain may use large stones so water can move through gaps easily.","zh":"花園排水可能使用大石，讓水容易穿過空隙。"},{"en":"Large stones prevent fine material from blocking the bottom drainage layer too quickly.","zh":"大石可防止細小材料太快堵塞底部排水層。"},{"en":"This phrase describes coarse material used in drainage structures.","zh":"這個短語描述用於排水結構的粗粒材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"flow onto the surface","meaning":"流到……表面","examples":[{"en":"The effluent first flows onto the surface of the bed.","zh":"排放水首先流到床層表面。"},{"en":"To flow onto the surface means to move onto the top layer of something.","zh":"flow onto the surface 指流到某物的頂層或表面。"},{"en":"Rainwater may flow onto the surface of a road before entering drains.","zh":"雨水可能先流到道路表面，再進入排水渠。"},{"en":"Once wastewater flows onto the surface, it can begin moving down through treatment layers.","zh":"一旦污水流到表面，就可以開始向下穿過處理層。"},{"en":"This phrase describes water reaching the top of a system.","zh":"這個短語描述水到達系統頂部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"percolate slowly through","meaning":"緩慢滲過……","examples":[{"en":"The liquid percolates slowly through the different layers.","zh":"液體緩慢滲過不同層。"},{"en":"To percolate slowly through something means to filter or seep gradually through small spaces.","zh":"percolate slowly through something 指逐漸穿過細小空隙或滲過某物。"},{"en":"Coffee percolates slowly through ground beans before collecting in a pot.","zh":"咖啡緩慢滲過咖啡粉後流入壺中。"},{"en":"Slow percolation gives treatment layers time to trap and break down pollutants.","zh":"緩慢滲流給處理層時間截留和分解污染物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes liquid moving gradually through porous material.","zh":"這個短語描述液體逐漸穿過多孔材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"different layers","meaning":"不同層","examples":[{"en":"The reed bed contains several different treatment layers.","zh":"蘆葦床含有幾個不同處理層。"},{"en":"Different layers are separate levels or bands of material arranged one above another.","zh":"different layers 指一層一層分開排列的材料或水平。"},{"en":"A sandwich has different layers such as bread, vegetables, cheese, and meat.","zh":"三文治有不同層，例如麵包、蔬菜、芝士和肉。"},{"en":"In a treatment bed, different layers can perform different cleaning functions.","zh":"在處理床中，不同層可以執行不同清潔功能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a structure built from several levels.","zh":"這個短語描述由多個層級構成的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"outlet pipe","meaning":"出水管","examples":[{"en":"The treated liquid eventually enters an outlet pipe.","zh":"經處理的液體最終進入出水管。"},{"en":"An outlet pipe is a pipe that carries liquid out of a system.","zh":"outlet pipe 指把液體從系統中帶出去的管道。"},{"en":"A sink has an outlet pipe that carries used water away.","zh":"洗手盆有出水管，把用過的水排走。"},{"en":"In a reed bed, the outlet pipe collects treated water after it passes through the layers.","zh":"在蘆葦床中，出水管在水穿過各層後收集處理後的水。"},{"en":"This phrase names the exit pipe for water or liquid waste.","zh":"這個短語命名水或液態廢物的出口管道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"通往；導致","examples":[{"en":"The outlet pipe leads to a horizontal-flow bed.","zh":"出水管通往水平流床。"},{"en":"To lead to somewhere means to go or connect to that place.","zh":"lead to somewhere 指通向或連接到某地方。"},{"en":"A school corridor may lead to the library.","zh":"學校走廊可能通往圖書館。"},{"en":"Pipes and paths lead to places by guiding movement in a set direction.","zh":"管道和道路透過引導移動方向而通往某地。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe physical connection or a result.","zh":"這個短語可以描述實體連接或結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be cleaned by","meaning":"由……淨化","examples":[{"en":"The wastewater is cleaned by millions of microorganisms.","zh":"污水由數以百萬計的微生物淨化。"},{"en":"To be cleaned by something means to be made cleaner through that agent or process.","zh":"be cleaned by something 指透過某媒介或過程變得更乾淨。"},{"en":"Clothes are cleaned by detergent, water, and movement in a washing machine.","zh":"衣物由洗衣劑、水和洗衣機中的轉動清潔。"},{"en":"Wastewater can be cleaned by plants, bacteria, sand, and gravel working together.","zh":"污水可以由植物、細菌、沙和碎石共同淨化。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what performs the cleaning action.","zh":"這個短語指出執行清潔動作的是甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"millions of bacteria","meaning":"數以百萬計的細菌","examples":[{"en":"Millions of bacteria help digest the waste.","zh":"數以百萬計的細菌幫助分解廢物。"},{"en":"Millions of bacteria means a very large number of tiny bacterial organisms.","zh":"millions of bacteria 指數量非常多的微小細菌生物。"},{"en":"A healthy compost bin may contain millions of bacteria breaking down food scraps.","zh":"健康的堆肥箱可能含有數以百萬計的細菌分解廚餘。"},{"en":"Large numbers of bacteria can speed up waste digestion in treatment systems.","zh":"大量細菌可以加快處理系統中的廢物分解。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the huge number of microscopic organisms involved.","zh":"這個短語強調參與其中的微生物數量巨大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"algae and fungi","meaning":"藻類和真菌","examples":[{"en":"Algae and fungi also contribute to the treatment process.","zh":"藻類和真菌也促成處理過程。"},{"en":"Algae and fungi are living organisms that can grow in moist environments and take part in decomposition or nutrient cycling.","zh":"algae and fungi 指能在潮濕環境中生長，並參與分解或養分循環的生物。"},{"en":"Fungi break down fallen leaves in a garden, while algae may grow in ponds.","zh":"真菌在花園中分解落葉，而藻類可能在池塘中生長。"},{"en":"In treatment systems, algae and fungi can support cleaning alongside bacteria.","zh":"在處理系統中，藻類和真菌可以與細菌一起支持淨化。"},{"en":"This phrase names two types of organisms involved in natural processes.","zh":"這個短語命名參與自然過程的兩類生物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"digest waste","meaning":"分解廢物","examples":[{"en":"Microorganisms digest waste as the water passes through the bed.","zh":"當水流經床層時，微生物分解廢物。"},{"en":"To digest waste means to break waste down into simpler substances.","zh":"digest waste 指把廢物分解成較簡單物質。"},{"en":"Bacteria in compost digest waste from fruit peels and vegetable scraps.","zh":"堆肥中的細菌分解果皮和菜屑等廢物。"},{"en":"When microorganisms digest waste, pollution levels can fall.","zh":"當微生物分解廢物，污染水平可以下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes biological breakdown of unwanted material.","zh":"這個短語描述不需要物質的生物分解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"including sewage","meaning":"包括污水","examples":[{"en":"The organisms can digest many kinds of waste, including sewage.","zh":"這些生物可以分解多種廢物，包括污水。"},{"en":"Including sewage means sewage is one example among the kinds of waste mentioned.","zh":"including sewage 指污水是所提到多種廢物中的一個例子。"},{"en":"A town must treat many waste streams, including sewage from homes.","zh":"城鎮必須處理多種廢物流，包括家居污水。"},{"en":"Adding “including” shows the list is not limited to that one item.","zh":"加上 including 顯示列表不只限於那一項。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces sewage as part of a wider group.","zh":"這個短語把污水作為較大群組的一部分引入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"standing water","meaning":"積水","examples":[{"en":"A vertical-flow system does not leave standing water on the surface.","zh":"垂直流系統不會在表面留下積水。"},{"en":"Standing water is water that stays still in one place instead of flowing away.","zh":"standing water 指停留在一處而沒有流走的水。"},{"en":"Mosquitoes may breed in standing water left in buckets after rain.","zh":"雨後留在水桶中的積水可能滋生蚊子。"},{"en":"Removing standing water can reduce smells and insects.","zh":"清除積水可以減少臭味和昆蟲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes still water that may create problems.","zh":"這個短語描述可能造成問題的靜止水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"unpleasant smells","meaning":"難聞氣味","examples":[{"en":"The absence of standing water helps prevent unpleasant smells.","zh":"沒有積水有助防止難聞氣味。"},{"en":"Unpleasant smells are bad or offensive odours.","zh":"unpleasant smells 指不好聞或令人反感的氣味。"},{"en":"Food waste can create unpleasant smells if it is left in a bin for too long.","zh":"如果廚餘在垃圾桶中放太久，可能產生難聞氣味。"},{"en":"In wastewater treatment, smells often appear when waste decomposes poorly.","zh":"在污水處理中，當廢物分解不良，氣味常會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes odours people want to avoid.","zh":"這個短語描述人們想避免的氣味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"much more effective than","meaning":"比……有效得多","examples":[{"en":"Vertical-flow systems are much more effective than horizontal ones in several respects.","zh":"垂直流系統在幾方面比水平系統有效得多。"},{"en":"Much more effective than means far better at achieving a result.","zh":"much more effective than 指在達成結果方面好得多。"},{"en":"Daily practice is much more effective than last-minute revision for language learning.","zh":"對語言學習而言，每日練習比臨急抱佛腳有效得多。"},{"en":"A system may be much more effective if it treats stronger waste in less space.","zh":"如果一個系統能在較少空間處理較高濃度廢水，它可能有效得多。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a strong comparison between two methods.","zh":"這個短語對兩種方法作強烈比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"reduce biochemical oxygen demand","meaning":"降低生化需氧量","examples":[{"en":"Reed beds can reduce biochemical oxygen demand in wastewater.","zh":"蘆葦床可以降低污水中的生化需氧量。"},{"en":"To reduce biochemical oxygen demand means to lower the amount of oxygen needed to break down organic waste.","zh":"reduce biochemical oxygen demand 指降低分解有機廢物所需的氧氣量。"},{"en":"A treatment plant reduces biochemical oxygen demand before releasing water into a river.","zh":"處理廠在把水排入河流前降低生化需氧量。"},{"en":"Lower demand means the treated water will take less oxygen from natural waters.","zh":"需氧量較低表示處理後的水會從天然水域消耗較少氧氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important goal in wastewater treatment.","zh":"這個短語描述污水處理中的重要目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"biochemical oxygen demand","meaning":"生化需氧量","examples":[{"en":"Biochemical oxygen demand measures the oxygen needed to break down waste.","zh":"生化需氧量量度分解廢物所需的氧氣。"},{"en":"Biochemical oxygen demand is a measure of how much oxygen microorganisms need to decompose organic matter in water.","zh":"biochemical oxygen demand 指微生物分解水中有機物所需氧氣量的量度。"},{"en":"A river with high biochemical oxygen demand may not have enough oxygen for fish.","zh":"生化需氧量高的河流可能沒有足夠氧氣供魚類生存。"},{"en":"Wastewater treatment aims to reduce this demand before discharge.","zh":"污水處理旨在排放前降低這項需氧量。"},{"en":"This phrase is often shortened to BOD in environmental science.","zh":"這個短語在環境科學中常縮寫為 BOD。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"suspended solids","meaning":"懸浮固體","examples":[{"en":"Vertical-flow beds reduce the level of suspended solids.","zh":"垂直流床降低懸浮固體水平。"},{"en":"Suspended solids are tiny particles floating or hanging in water rather than dissolving.","zh":"suspended solids 指漂浮或懸在水中而沒有溶解的微小顆粒。"},{"en":"Muddy water has suspended solids that make it look cloudy.","zh":"泥濁的水有懸浮固體，所以看起來混濁。"},{"en":"Removing suspended solids makes water clearer and reduces pollution load.","zh":"清除懸浮固體可以令水更清澈並降低污染負荷。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to solid particles carried in liquid.","zh":"這個短語指液體中攜帶的固體顆粒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reduce ammonia levels","meaning":"降低氨水平","examples":[{"en":"Vertical systems can also reduce ammonia levels.","zh":"垂直系統也可以降低氨水平。"},{"en":"To reduce ammonia levels means to lower the amount of ammonia in water or waste.","zh":"reduce ammonia levels 指降低水或廢物中的氨含量。"},{"en":"A fish tank filter helps reduce ammonia levels so fish remain healthy.","zh":"魚缸濾水器有助降低氨水平，使魚保持健康。"},{"en":"High ammonia levels can be toxic, so reducing them improves water quality.","zh":"高氨水平可以有毒，所以降低它能改善水質。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lowering a harmful nitrogen compound.","zh":"這個短語描述降低一種有害含氮化合物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"eliminate smells","meaning":"消除氣味","examples":[{"en":"Vertical-flow treatment helps eliminate unpleasant smells.","zh":"垂直流處理有助消除難聞氣味。"},{"en":"To eliminate smells means to remove bad odours completely or almost completely.","zh":"eliminate smells 指完全或幾乎完全去除臭味。"},{"en":"Cleaning a fridge can eliminate smells from old food.","zh":"清潔雪櫃可以消除舊食物的氣味。"},{"en":"Treatment systems eliminate smells by preventing waste from rotting on the surface.","zh":"處理系統透過防止廢物在表面腐爛來消除氣味。"},{"en":"This phrase describes getting rid of unwanted odours.","zh":"這個短語描述去除不想要的氣味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"considerably smaller than","meaning":"比……小得多","examples":[{"en":"Vertical reed beds are considerably smaller than horizontal beds.","zh":"垂直蘆葦床比水平床小得多。"},{"en":"Considerably smaller than means much smaller in size.","zh":"considerably smaller than 指尺寸小得多。"},{"en":"A laptop is considerably smaller than a desktop computer and easier to carry.","zh":"手提電腦比桌上電腦小得多，也較易攜帶。"},{"en":"Smaller systems can be useful where land is expensive or limited.","zh":"在土地昂貴或有限的地方，較小系統很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a strong size comparison.","zh":"這個短語作出強烈尺寸比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be capable of handling","meaning":"能夠處理……","examples":[{"en":"Vertical-flow systems are capable of handling heavily polluted water.","zh":"垂直流系統能夠處理嚴重污染的水。"},{"en":"To be capable of handling something means to be able to deal with it successfully.","zh":"be capable of handling something 指能夠成功處理某事。"},{"en":"A strong computer is capable of handling large video files.","zh":"強大的電腦能夠處理大型影片檔案。"},{"en":"A treatment system must be capable of handling the pollution level it receives.","zh":"處理系統必須能夠處理所接收的污染水平。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ability to manage a difficult task or load.","zh":"這個短語描述處理困難任務或負荷的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"stronger effluent","meaning":"較高濃度污水","examples":[{"en":"Vertical reed beds can treat stronger effluent.","zh":"垂直蘆葦床可以處理較高濃度污水。"},{"en":"Stronger effluent is wastewater with a higher concentration of pollutants.","zh":"stronger effluent 指污染物濃度較高的污水或排放水。"},{"en":"Water from a food-processing factory may be stronger effluent than water from a hand basin.","zh":"食品加工廠的水可能比洗手盆排水屬於較高濃度污水。"},{"en":"Stronger effluent needs more powerful treatment because it contains more waste.","zh":"較高濃度污水需要更強處理，因為它含有更多廢物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wastewater that is harder to clean.","zh":"這個短語描述較難清潔的污水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"heavily polluted matter","meaning":"嚴重污染物質","examples":[{"en":"The system can process heavily polluted matter.","zh":"該系統可以處理嚴重污染物質。"},{"en":"Heavily polluted matter is material containing a high level of harmful substances.","zh":"heavily polluted matter 指含有高水平有害物質的材料。"},{"en":"Mud near a factory drain may become heavily polluted matter if chemicals collect there.","zh":"如果化學品在工廠排水口附近積聚，那裡的泥可能變成嚴重污染物質。"},{"en":"Heavily polluted matter needs careful treatment before it can be safely released or reused.","zh":"嚴重污染物質在安全排放或重用前需要仔細處理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes waste with serious contamination.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重受污染的廢物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"longer service life","meaning":"較長使用壽命","examples":[{"en":"Vertical-flow systems usually have a longer service life.","zh":"垂直流系統通常有較長使用壽命。"},{"en":"Longer service life means something can be used effectively for a longer period before replacement.","zh":"longer service life 指某物在需要更換前可有效使用較長時間。"},{"en":"A high-quality school chair has a longer service life if it does not break easily.","zh":"如果高質素學校椅子不容易壞，就有較長使用壽命。"},{"en":"Longer service life can reduce replacement costs and waste.","zh":"較長使用壽命可以降低更換成本和廢物量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes durability over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間保持耐用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"work more efficiently","meaning":"運作得更有效率","examples":[{"en":"A vertical system works more efficiently than a horizontal one.","zh":"垂直系統比水平系統運作得更有效率。"},{"en":"To work more efficiently means to produce a better result using less time, space, energy, or effort.","zh":"work more efficiently 指用較少時間、空間、能源或努力產生更好結果。"},{"en":"A student works more efficiently when they revise with a clear checklist.","zh":"學生使用清楚清單溫習時，會運作得更有效率。"},{"en":"Efficient systems save resources while still doing the job well.","zh":"高效率系統節省資源，同時仍能做好工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes better performance with less waste.","zh":"這個短語描述以較少浪費達到更好表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"require more management","meaning":"需要更多管理","examples":[{"en":"The more efficient system also requires more management.","zh":"較高效的系統也需要更多管理。"},{"en":"To require more management means to need more planning, checking, and control.","zh":"require more management 指需要更多規劃、檢查和控制。"},{"en":"A large school trip requires more management than a short walk to a nearby park.","zh":"大型學校旅行比步行到附近公園需要更多管理。"},{"en":"More complex systems often work better but need closer supervision.","zh":"較複雜系統通常效果更好，但需要更密切監督。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a trade-off between efficiency and effort.","zh":"這個短語顯示效率與工作量之間的取捨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be operated for a few days","meaning":"連續運作數天","examples":[{"en":"Each reed bed may be operated for a few days at a time.","zh":"每個蘆葦床可一次連續運作數天。"},{"en":"To be operated for a few days means to be used or run continuously for several days.","zh":"be operated for a few days 指被連續使用或運行幾天。"},{"en":"A classroom air purifier may be operated for a few days during heavy pollution.","zh":"在嚴重空氣污染期間，課室空氣淨化機可能連續運作數天。"},{"en":"Operating a bed for only a period allows it to rest afterwards.","zh":"只讓床層運作一段時間，使它之後可以休養。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited-time use of a system.","zh":"這個短語描述系統有限時間的使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"then be rested","meaning":"然後停用休養","examples":[{"en":"After operating for several days, the bed is rested.","zh":"運作數天後，床層會停用休養。"},{"en":"To then be rested means to be stopped from use afterwards so it can recover.","zh":"then be rested 指之後停止使用，使其恢復。"},{"en":"An athlete may train hard for two days and then be rested before a competition.","zh":"運動員可能訓練兩天後，在比賽前停下休息。"},{"en":"Resting a reed bed helps maintain treatment performance over time.","zh":"讓蘆葦床休養有助長期維持處理表現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a pause after use.","zh":"這個短語描述使用後的暫停。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"several beds","meaning":"多個蘆葦床","examples":[{"en":"Several beds are needed to maintain continuous treatment.","zh":"需要多個蘆葦床來維持連續處理。"},{"en":"Several beds means more than two treatment beds or planted areas.","zh":"several beds 指多於兩個處理床或種植區。"},{"en":"A clinic may need several treatment rooms so patients can be seen continuously.","zh":"診所可能需要多個治療室，讓病人可以持續被診治。"},{"en":"When one bed rests, another bed can operate, so treatment does not stop.","zh":"當一個床層休養，另一個床層可以運作，因此處理不會停止。"},{"en":"This phrase describes multiple units working together.","zh":"這個短語描述多個單元共同運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"distribution system","meaning":"分配系統","examples":[{"en":"A distribution system directs wastewater to different beds.","zh":"分配系統把污水引導到不同床層。"},{"en":"A distribution system is a set of pipes, channels, or controls that sends material to different places.","zh":"distribution system 指把物質送到不同地方的一套管道、渠道或控制裝置。"},{"en":"A school lunch distribution system sends meals to different classrooms.","zh":"學校午餐分配系統把膳食送到不同課室。"},{"en":"In reed-bed treatment, distribution helps balance the load across several beds.","zh":"在蘆葦床處理中，分配有助在多個床層之間平衡負荷。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the system that shares flow among parts.","zh":"這個短語指在各部分之間分配流量的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"advantages over","meaning":"相對於……的優點","examples":[{"en":"Natural purification has several advantages over conventional treatment.","zh":"天然淨化相對於傳統處理有幾個優點。"},{"en":"Advantages over something are benefits compared with another option.","zh":"advantages over something 指與另一選項相比的好處。"},{"en":"Cycling has advantages over driving in crowded streets because it is cheaper and easier to park.","zh":"在擠迫街道上，踏單車相對於駕車有優點，因為較便宜且較易泊車。"},{"en":"A method may have advantages over another if it costs less or causes less harm.","zh":"如果一種方法成本較低或傷害較少，它相對於另一方法可能有優點。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a comparison of benefits.","zh":"這個短語引入好處比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"require less expenditure","meaning":"所需開支較少","examples":[{"en":"Natural systems require less expenditure than mechanical systems.","zh":"天然系統比機械系統所需開支較少。"},{"en":"To require less expenditure means to need less money to build, run, or maintain.","zh":"require less expenditure 指建造、運作或維修所需金錢較少。"},{"en":"A shared school bus may require less expenditure than each family driving separately.","zh":"共用校巴可能比每個家庭分別駕車所需開支較少。"},{"en":"Lower expenditure can make a system easier for small communities to afford.","zh":"較低開支可以令小社區較容易負擔系統。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on financial cost.","zh":"這個短語著重財務成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"installation and operation","meaning":"安裝和運作","examples":[{"en":"Installation and operation costs are relatively low.","zh":"安裝和運作成本相對較低。"},{"en":"Installation and operation means setting up a system and then running it.","zh":"installation and operation 指建立系統，然後使其運行。"},{"en":"A school considers installation and operation before buying new air conditioners.","zh":"學校購買新冷氣機前會考慮安裝和運作。"},{"en":"A system may be cheap to install but expensive to operate, so both costs matter.","zh":"系統可能安裝便宜但運作昂貴，所以兩種成本都重要。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both starting and continuing costs.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋開始和持續成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"maintenance costs","meaning":"維修保養費用","examples":[{"en":"Reed beds can reduce long-term maintenance costs.","zh":"蘆葦床可以減少長期維修保養費用。"},{"en":"Maintenance costs are the money needed to keep something working properly.","zh":"maintenance costs 指保持某物正常運作所需的金錢。"},{"en":"An old lift may have high maintenance costs because it breaks down often.","zh":"舊升降機可能因經常故障而有高維修保養費用。"},{"en":"Lower maintenance costs make a system easier to manage over many years.","zh":"較低維修保養費用令系統多年來更容易管理。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to repair and upkeep expenses.","zh":"這個短語指維修和保養開支。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"improve the surrounding landscape","meaning":"改善周圍景觀","examples":[{"en":"A reed bed can improve the surrounding landscape.","zh":"蘆葦床可以改善周圍景觀。"},{"en":"To improve the surrounding landscape means to make the nearby area look better or more natural.","zh":"improve the surrounding landscape 指令附近地區看起來更美觀或更自然。"},{"en":"Planting trees can improve the surrounding landscape of a school playground.","zh":"種樹可以改善學校操場的周圍景觀。"},{"en":"A treatment system that looks natural can make an area more attractive.","zh":"看起來自然的處理系統可以令地區更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase connects environmental function with appearance.","zh":"這個短語把環境功能與外觀連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"natural habitats","meaning":"自然棲息地","examples":[{"en":"Reed beds provide natural habitats for many organisms.","zh":"蘆葦床為許多生物提供自然棲息地。"},{"en":"Natural habitats are places where plants and animals normally live and find food, shelter, and breeding space.","zh":"natural habitats 指植物和動物正常生活、覓食、藏身和繁殖的地方。"},{"en":"A pond can be a natural habitat for frogs, insects, and water plants.","zh":"池塘可以是青蛙、昆蟲和水生植物的自然棲息地。"},{"en":"Protecting habitats helps wildlife survive and reproduce.","zh":"保護棲息地有助野生生物生存和繁殖。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to living spaces created by nature or nature-like conditions.","zh":"這個短語指由自然或類自然條件形成的生活空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"floodplains","meaning":"河漫灘；洪泛平原","examples":[{"en":"Natural reed beds are often found in floodplains.","zh":"天然蘆葦床常見於河漫灘。"},{"en":"Floodplains are low flat areas beside rivers that can become covered with water during floods.","zh":"floodplains 指河流旁邊低平、在洪水時可能被水覆蓋的地區。"},{"en":"Farmers may use floodplains because the soil can be rich after river flooding.","zh":"農民可能使用洪泛平原，因為河水氾濫後土壤可以很肥沃。"},{"en":"Floodplains store excess water and can reduce flood pressure downstream.","zh":"洪泛平原儲存多餘水量，並能減少下游洪水壓力。"},{"en":"This word refers to land naturally connected with river flooding.","zh":"這個詞指與河流氾濫自然相連的土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"waterlogged depressions","meaning":"積水低窪地","examples":[{"en":"Reeds can grow in waterlogged depressions.","zh":"蘆葦可以生長在積水低窪地。"},{"en":"Waterlogged depressions are low areas where water collects and keeps the ground very wet.","zh":"waterlogged depressions 指水聚集並使地面非常潮濕的低窪地區。"},{"en":"After heavy rain, a school field may have waterlogged depressions where puddles remain.","zh":"大雨後，學校操場可能有水窪停留的積水低窪地。"},{"en":"Wet low areas can support reeds because their roots tolerate saturated soil.","zh":"潮濕低地可以支持蘆葦，因為其根部能忍受飽水土壤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes low, wet places in the landscape.","zh":"這個短語描述地貌中的低濕地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"estuaries","meaning":"河口","examples":[{"en":"Reed beds are also naturally found in estuaries.","zh":"蘆葦床也自然見於河口。"},{"en":"Estuaries are areas where rivers meet the sea and fresh water mixes with salt water.","zh":"estuaries 指河流入海、淡水與鹹水混合的地區。"},{"en":"Birds often feed in estuaries because fish and small animals are abundant there.","zh":"鳥類常在河口覓食，因為那裡有豐富魚類和小動物。"},{"en":"Estuaries are important habitats but can be damaged by pollution and development.","zh":"河口是重要棲息地，但可能受污染和發展破壞。"},{"en":"This word refers to river-mouth environments.","zh":"這個詞指河流入海口環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"biologically proven","meaning":"經生物學驗證的","examples":[{"en":"Reed-bed treatment is a biologically proven method.","zh":"蘆葦床處理是經生物學驗證的方法。"},{"en":"Biologically proven means shown to work through biological evidence or natural living processes.","zh":"biologically proven 指透過生物證據或自然生命過程顯示有效。"},{"en":"Composting is biologically proven because microorganisms clearly break down organic waste.","zh":"堆肥是經生物學驗證的，因為微生物清楚分解有機廢物。"},{"en":"A biologically proven treatment is more trustworthy when repeated results show it works.","zh":"當重複結果顯示有效，經生物學驗證的處理方法更可信。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests support from biological science.","zh":"這個短語表示得到生物科學支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"environmentally friendly","meaning":"環保的","examples":[{"en":"Natural reed beds provide an environmentally friendly treatment method.","zh":"天然蘆葦床提供一種環保的處理方法。"},{"en":"Environmentally friendly means causing little harm to the natural environment.","zh":"environmentally friendly 指對自然環境造成較少傷害。"},{"en":"A shop is more environmentally friendly when it reduces plastic bags and saves electricity.","zh":"商店減少膠袋並節省電力時，就更環保。"},{"en":"Environmentally friendly systems usually reduce pollution, waste, or energy use.","zh":"環保系統通常減少污染、廢物或能源使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choices designed to protect nature.","zh":"這個短語描述旨在保護自然的選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"visually unobtrusive","meaning":"外觀不礙眼的","examples":[{"en":"A reed bed is visually unobtrusive in a rural landscape.","zh":"蘆葦床在鄉村景觀中外觀不礙眼。"},{"en":"Visually unobtrusive means not easily noticed in a negative way and not spoiling the view.","zh":"visually unobtrusive 指不會以負面方式惹人注意，也不破壞景觀。"},{"en":"A small wooden sign can be visually unobtrusive in a historic village.","zh":"小木牌在歷史村落中可以是外觀不礙眼的。"},{"en":"Treatment systems that blend in are more acceptable to nearby residents.","zh":"能融入環境的處理系統較容易被附近居民接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that does not look ugly or intrusive.","zh":"這個短語描述看起來不醜陋、不突兀的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have the extra virtue of","meaning":"還有……的額外優點","examples":[{"en":"Reed beds have the extra virtue of blending into the landscape.","zh":"蘆葦床還有融入景觀的額外優點。"},{"en":"To have the extra virtue of something means to have an additional good quality.","zh":"have the extra virtue of something 指還有一項額外好處。"},{"en":"Walking to school has the extra virtue of giving children daily exercise.","zh":"步行上學還有讓孩子每日運動的額外優點。"},{"en":"A system may be chosen because it works well and has extra environmental or visual benefits.","zh":"一個系統可能因為有效，且有額外環境或視覺好處而被選用。"},{"en":"This phrase adds one more advantage to an already useful thing.","zh":"這個短語為本已有用的事物加入另一個優點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"mechanical treatment systems","meaning":"機械污水處理系統","examples":[{"en":"Natural systems may perform better than mechanical treatment systems.","zh":"天然系統可能比機械污水處理系統表現更好。"},{"en":"Mechanical treatment systems are systems that use machines and equipment to treat wastewater.","zh":"mechanical treatment systems 指使用機器和設備處理污水的系統。"},{"en":"A city sewage plant often relies on mechanical treatment systems with pumps and tanks.","zh":"城市污水處理廠通常依賴有泵和池的機械處理系統。"},{"en":"Mechanical systems can treat large flows but may cost more to build and maintain.","zh":"機械系統可以處理大量水流，但建造和維修成本可能較高。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts machine-based treatment with natural treatment.","zh":"這個短語把機械式處理與天然處理作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"over the medium to long term","meaning":"中長期而言","examples":[{"en":"Over the medium to long term, reed beds can be highly economical.","zh":"中長期而言，蘆葦床可以非常經濟。"},{"en":"Over the medium to long term means across several years or a longer future period.","zh":"over the medium to long term 指跨越數年或更長未來時期。"},{"en":"Over the medium to long term, daily reading can greatly improve vocabulary.","zh":"中長期而言，每日閱讀可以大大改善詞彙量。"},{"en":"Some systems cost money at first but save more later.","zh":"有些系統起初要花錢，但之後節省更多。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on results beyond the immediate short term.","zh":"這個短語著重超越即時短期的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in most cases","meaning":"在大多數情況下","examples":[{"en":"In most cases, natural systems cost less to install.","zh":"在大多數情況下，天然系統安裝成本較低。"},{"en":"In most cases means usually, though not always.","zh":"in most cases 指通常如此，但並非永遠如此。"},{"en":"In most cases, students improve when they practise a little every day.","zh":"在大多數情況下，學生每天練習一點就會進步。"},{"en":"This phrase allows for exceptions while describing the general situation.","zh":"這個短語在描述一般情況時容許例外。"},{"en":"It is useful when a statement is broadly true but not universal.","zh":"當一項說法大致正確但不是普遍絕對時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"cost-effective to install","meaning":"安裝成本效益較高","examples":[{"en":"Reed-bed systems are often more cost-effective to install.","zh":"蘆葦床系統通常安裝成本效益較高。"},{"en":"Cost-effective to install means giving good value for the money spent on setting something up.","zh":"cost-effective to install 指安裝某物所花的錢能帶來良好價值。"},{"en":"LED lights can be cost-effective to install if they reduce electricity bills for years.","zh":"如果 LED 燈能多年減少電費，它們就可能安裝成本效益較高。"},{"en":"A system is cost-effective when the benefits justify the installation cost.","zh":"當好處足以合理化安裝成本，系統就是具成本效益。"},{"en":"This phrase evaluates financial value at the setup stage.","zh":"這個短語評估設置階段的財務價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"environmentally sound","meaning":"對環境無害的","examples":[{"en":"Reed-bed treatment is naturally environmentally sound.","zh":"蘆葦床處理天然上是對環境無害的。"},{"en":"Environmentally sound means safe and sensible from an environmental point of view.","zh":"environmentally sound 指從環境角度看安全而合理。"},{"en":"A recycling plan is environmentally sound if it reduces waste without creating new pollution.","zh":"如果回收計劃減少廢物而不造成新污染，它就是對環境無害的。"},{"en":"Environmentally sound choices protect resources and avoid unnecessary harm.","zh":"對環境無害的選擇會保護資源並避免不必要傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than simply saying something looks green.","zh":"這個短語比單純說某物看起來環保更強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"protect groundwater","meaning":"保護地下水","examples":[{"en":"Natural treatment systems help protect groundwater.","zh":"天然處理系統有助保護地下水。"},{"en":"To protect groundwater means to prevent underground water from being polluted or overused.","zh":"protect groundwater 指防止地下水被污染或過度使用。"},{"en":"Farmers protect groundwater by using fertiliser carefully near wells.","zh":"農民在水井附近謹慎使用肥料，就是保護地下水。"},{"en":"If groundwater is polluted, it can be difficult and expensive to clean.","zh":"如果地下水被污染，清理可能困難且昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes safeguarding hidden freshwater resources.","zh":"這個短語描述保護隱藏淡水資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"dams and creeks","meaning":"水壩和溪流","examples":[{"en":"Reed beds can protect dams and creeks from polluted runoff.","zh":"蘆葦床可以保護水壩和溪流免受受污染徑流影響。"},{"en":"Dams and creeks are water bodies or waterways that can store or carry water.","zh":"dams and creeks 指能儲存或輸送水的水體或水道。"},{"en":"A farm may have small creeks flowing into a dam used for animals.","zh":"農場可能有小溪流流入供牲畜使用的水壩。"},{"en":"Polluted runoff can damage dams and creeks by carrying waste, soil, and chemicals into them.","zh":"受污染徑流可以把廢物、泥土和化學品帶入水壩和溪流，從而造成破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to important local water resources.","zh":"這個短語指重要的本地水資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與文章資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether the statements agree with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與文章資料一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the information means to match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information 指符合文章所說內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says reed beds use microorganisms, a statement saying the same thing agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說蘆葦床使用微生物，而陳述說同一件事，就是與資料一致。"},{"en":"Students should choose TRUE only when the text clearly supports the statement.","zh":"只有當文本清楚支持陳述時，學生才應選 TRUE。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE, FALSE and NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE、FALSE 和 NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文章資料相反","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料相反。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說法與文章內容相反。"},{"en":"If the passage says water flows downward but the statement says it flows upward, it contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說水向下流，但陳述說水向上流，就是與資料相反。"},{"en":"Students should choose FALSE only when the text clearly disagrees with the statement.","zh":"只有當文本清楚不支持陳述時，學生才應選 FALSE。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct conflict with the source text.","zh":"這個短語描述與來源文本直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Students write “NOT GIVEN” when the passage provides no relevant information.","zh":"當文章沒有提供相關資料時，學生寫 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the text does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文本沒有說明該陳述是真還是假。"},{"en":"If a passage explains reed beds but never mentions cost in Japan, there is no information on that point.","zh":"如果文章解釋蘆葦床但從未提到日本成本，該點就是文中沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when the text gives no evidence.","zh":"當文本沒有證據時，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase explains when NOT GIVEN is the correct answer.","zh":"這個短語解釋何時 NOT GIVEN 是正確答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"conventional method","meaning":"傳統方法","examples":[{"en":"The statement describes reed-bed treatment as a conventional method.","zh":"該陳述把蘆葦床處理描述為傳統方法。"},{"en":"A conventional method is the usual or traditional way of doing something.","zh":"conventional method 指做某事的通常或傳統方式。"},{"en":"Taking notes by hand is still a conventional method in many classrooms.","zh":"在許多課室中，手寫筆記仍是傳統方法。"},{"en":"A method can be conventional in one place but alternative in another.","zh":"一種方法在某地可以是傳統方法，但在另一地可以是替代方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a standard approach, not a new or unusual one.","zh":"這個短語描述標準做法，而不是新奇做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"urban areas","meaning":"市區","examples":[{"en":"Large conventional treatment systems are usually found in urban areas.","zh":"大型傳統處理系統通常見於市區。"},{"en":"Urban areas are towns and cities where many people live close together.","zh":"urban areas 指許多人密集居住的城鎮和城市。"},{"en":"Urban areas often need large sewage systems because many homes produce wastewater.","zh":"市區通常需要大型污水系統，因為許多家庭都產生污水。"},{"en":"Crowded urban areas usually have less spare land for large natural systems.","zh":"擠迫市區通常沒有太多空地可作大型天然系統。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts city regions with rural areas.","zh":"這個短語把城市地區與鄉郊地區作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"break down pollutants","meaning":"分解污染物","examples":[{"en":"Processes around reed roots help break down pollutants.","zh":"蘆葦根周圍的過程有助分解污染物。"},{"en":"To break down pollutants means to change harmful substances into simpler or less harmful forms.","zh":"break down pollutants 指把有害物質轉變成較簡單或較無害形式。"},{"en":"Sunlight can help break down some pollutants on outdoor surfaces.","zh":"陽光可以幫助分解戶外表面上的某些污染物。"},{"en":"If pollutants are broken down, they are less likely to harm water life.","zh":"如果污染物被分解，它們較不可能傷害水生生命。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing pollution through decomposition or reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述透過分解或反應減少污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"difficult bacterium to eliminate","meaning":"難以清除的細菌","examples":[{"en":"Some bacteria may be more difficult to eliminate than others.","zh":"有些細菌可能比其他細菌更難清除。"},{"en":"A difficult bacterium to eliminate is a bacterium that is hard to remove or kill.","zh":"difficult bacterium to eliminate 指難以去除或殺死的細菌。"},{"en":"Hospitals must be careful with bacteria that are difficult to eliminate from surfaces.","zh":"醫院必須小心處理難以從表面清除的細菌。"},{"en":"If a bacterium survives ordinary treatment, stronger or longer treatment may be needed.","zh":"如果細菌在普通處理後仍存活，就可能需要更強或更長時間的處理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a microbe that resists removal.","zh":"這個短語描述抗拒清除的微生物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete the diagram","meaning":"完成圖表","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the diagram using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成圖表。"},{"en":"To complete the diagram means to fill missing labels or information in a picture or chart.","zh":"complete the diagram 指填入圖片或圖表中缺失的標籤或資料。"},{"en":"In a science test, students may complete the diagram of a plant root system.","zh":"在科學測驗中，學生可能要完成植物根系圖。"},{"en":"Students should copy words carefully because diagram labels are often short and exact.","zh":"學生應仔細抄寫字詞，因為圖表標籤通常簡短而精確。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction for visual information.","zh":"這個短語是視覺資料題中的常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個詞","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than three words.","zh":"每個答案應包含不多於三個詞。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must be one, two, or three words only.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案只能是一個、兩個或三個詞。"},{"en":"If the answer limit is no more than three words, “layer of gravel” is allowed.","zh":"如果答案限制是不多於三個詞，“layer of gravel” 是可以的。"},{"en":"Writing four words can lose marks even if the meaning is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫四個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict word-limit rule.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格字數限制規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"vertical-flow reed bed","meaning":"垂直流蘆葦床","examples":[{"en":"The diagram shows the layers of a vertical-flow reed bed.","zh":"圖表顯示垂直流蘆葦床的各層。"},{"en":"A vertical-flow reed bed is a treatment bed where wastewater travels downward through layers.","zh":"vertical-flow reed bed 指污水向下穿過各層的處理床。"},{"en":"A diagram of a vertical-flow reed bed may show sludge, sand, gravel, and an outlet pipe.","zh":"垂直流蘆葦床圖可能顯示污泥、沙、碎石和出水管。"},{"en":"Understanding the layers helps students see how the water is cleaned step by step.","zh":"理解各層有助學生看見水如何一步步被淨化。"},{"en":"This phrase names the system shown in the diagram.","zh":"這個短語命名圖表所示的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"substrate","meaning":"基質","examples":[{"en":"Sand or sludge can serve as a substrate in the treatment bed.","zh":"沙或污泥可以在處理床中作為基質。"},{"en":"A substrate is the material or surface on which organisms grow or processes take place.","zh":"substrate 指生物生長或過程發生的材料或表面。"},{"en":"Soil is a substrate for garden plants because roots grow in it.","zh":"土壤是園藝植物的基質，因為根部在其中生長。"},{"en":"In reed beds, the substrate supports roots and microorganisms.","zh":"在蘆葦床中，基質支撐根部和微生物。"},{"en":"This word refers to the base material used in a biological system.","zh":"這個詞指生物系統中使用的基底材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"drainage layer","meaning":"排水層","examples":[{"en":"A gravel drainage layer lies beneath the root zone.","zh":"碎石排水層位於根區下方。"},{"en":"A drainage layer is a layer of material that helps water flow away.","zh":"drainage layer 指幫助水流走的一層材料。"},{"en":"A plant pot may need a drainage layer so roots do not sit in water.","zh":"花盆可能需要排水層，使根部不會浸在水中。"},{"en":"Good drainage layers prevent water from collecting and causing smells or root damage.","zh":"良好排水層防止水積聚並造成臭味或根部損害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a layer designed to carry water downward or outward.","zh":"這個短語描述設計用來把水向下或向外帶走的層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"match the advantages and disadvantages","meaning":"配對優點和缺點","examples":[{"en":"Students match the advantages and disadvantages with the two systems.","zh":"學生把優點和缺點與兩個系統配對。"},{"en":"To match the advantages and disadvantages means to connect each benefit or drawback to the correct system.","zh":"match the advantages and disadvantages 指把每項好處或壞處連接到正確系統。"},{"en":"In a reading exercise, students may match the advantages of cycling and driving with the right transport type.","zh":"在閱讀練習中，學生可能把踏單車和駕車的優點配對到正確交通方式。"},{"en":"This task requires students to understand comparison, not just copy words.","zh":"這類題目要求學生理解比較，而不只是抄字。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an exam activity based on sorting pros and cons.","zh":"這個短語描述根據利弊分類的考試活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"downflow system","meaning":"下流式系統","examples":[{"en":"A downflow system directs wastewater vertically through the bed.","zh":"下流式系統引導污水垂直穿過床層。"},{"en":"A downflow system is a system where liquid moves downward through treatment layers.","zh":"downflow system 指液體向下穿過處理層的系統。"},{"en":"A coffee machine uses a simple downflow process when water moves through ground coffee.","zh":"咖啡機在水流經咖啡粉時使用簡單下流過程。"},{"en":"Downward movement can help wastewater contact several treatment materials in order.","zh":"向下流動可以幫助污水依次接觸多種處理材料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a system based on downward flow.","zh":"這個短語描述以向下水流為基礎的系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"require several beds","meaning":"需要多個床層","examples":[{"en":"A vertical-flow treatment system may require several beds.","zh":"垂直流處理系統可能需要多個床層。"},{"en":"To require several beds means to need more than one treatment bed to operate properly.","zh":"require several beds 指需要多於一個處理床才能正常運作。"},{"en":"A hospital may require several rooms so cleaning can continue while one room is being used.","zh":"醫院可能需要多個房間，讓一間使用時其他房間可以繼續清潔或服務。"},{"en":"Several beds allow one bed to rest while others continue treating wastewater.","zh":"多個床層讓一個床層休養時，其他床層繼續處理污水。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that multiple units are needed for continuous operation.","zh":"這個短語顯示連續運作需要多個單元。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be easier to construct","meaning":"較容易建造","examples":[{"en":"A simple horizontal bed may be easier to construct.","zh":"簡單的水平床可能較容易建造。"},{"en":"To be easier to construct means to be simpler to build.","zh":"be easier to construct 指建造起來較簡單。"},{"en":"A wooden shelf is easier to construct than a full kitchen cabinet.","zh":"木架比完整廚櫃較容易建造。"},{"en":"Simpler construction can reduce labour, time, and cost.","zh":"較簡單建造可以減少勞力、時間和成本。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how difficult building something is.","zh":"這個短語比較建造某物的難度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be built on a gradient","meaning":"建於斜坡上","examples":[{"en":"A horizontal system may be built on a gradient to help the water flow.","zh":"水平系統可能建於斜坡上，以幫助水流動。"},{"en":"To be built on a gradient means to be built on a slight slope.","zh":"be built on a gradient 指建在輕微斜坡上。"},{"en":"A driveway may be built on a gradient so rainwater drains toward the street.","zh":"私家車道可能建於斜坡上，使雨水流向街道。"},{"en":"A gradient helps water move naturally without needing as much pumping.","zh":"斜坡幫助水自然移動，減少抽水需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using slope to guide movement.","zh":"這個短語描述利用坡度引導移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"need little attention","meaning":"無需太多照料","examples":[{"en":"A passive treatment system may need relatively little attention.","zh":"被動處理系統可能無需太多照料。"},{"en":"To need little attention means to require only a small amount of checking or management.","zh":"need little attention 指只需要少量檢查或管理。"},{"en":"A hardy houseplant needs little attention if it survives with weekly watering.","zh":"如果耐種室內植物每週澆水即可存活，它就無需太多照料。"},{"en":"Systems that need little attention are useful where skilled staff are limited.","zh":"在熟練員工有限的地方，無需太多照料的系統很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes low maintenance or low supervision needs.","zh":"這個短語描述低維修或低監督需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"produce less sludge","meaning":"產生較少污泥","examples":[{"en":"Some natural systems may produce less sludge than mechanical plants.","zh":"有些天然系統可能比機械處理廠產生較少污泥。"},{"en":"To produce less sludge means to create a smaller amount of thick waste material.","zh":"produce less sludge 指產生較少濃稠廢物。"},{"en":"A cleaner food process may produce less sludge in its wastewater tank.","zh":"較清潔的食品加工過程可能在污水池中產生較少污泥。"},{"en":"Less sludge means less material needs to be removed, transported, or treated later.","zh":"較少污泥表示之後需要移除、運輸或處理的材料較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing the solid waste left after treatment.","zh":"這個短語描述減少處理後留下的固體廢物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"not operate continuously","meaning":"不會持續運作","examples":[{"en":"An individual vertical bed does not operate continuously.","zh":"單一垂直床不會持續運作。"},{"en":"To not operate continuously means to work for periods, then stop or rest.","zh":"not operate continuously 指運作一段時間後停止或休養。"},{"en":"A classroom projector may not operate continuously because it is turned off between lessons.","zh":"課室投影機不會持續運作，因為課與課之間會關掉。"},{"en":"A system may stop regularly so it can recover or avoid overload.","zh":"系統可能定期停止，以便恢復或避免負荷過重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes interrupted rather than nonstop operation.","zh":"這個短語描述間歇運作，而不是不停運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"need a deeper bed","meaning":"需要較深的床層","examples":[{"en":"Vertical-flow systems generally need a deeper bed.","zh":"垂直流系統通常需要較深的床層。"},{"en":"To need a deeper bed means to require a treatment layer with greater depth.","zh":"need a deeper bed 指需要深度更大的處理層。"},{"en":"A plant with long roots may need a deeper pot to grow well.","zh":"有長根的植物可能需要較深花盆才能生長良好。"},{"en":"A deeper bed allows wastewater to pass through more treatment layers.","zh":"較深床層讓污水穿過更多處理層。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a design requirement involving depth.","zh":"這個短語描述涉及深度的設計要求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"deal with heavily polluted water","meaning":"處理污染較嚴重的水","examples":[{"en":"Vertical systems can deal with more heavily polluted water.","zh":"垂直系統可以處理污染較嚴重的水。"},{"en":"To deal with heavily polluted water means to treat water that contains high levels of pollutants.","zh":"deal with heavily polluted water 指處理含高水平污染物的水。"},{"en":"A factory may need a stronger system to deal with heavily polluted water from production.","zh":"工廠可能需要更強系統來處理生產中產生的嚴重污染水。"},{"en":"If a system cannot deal with strong pollution, dirty water may remain unsafe.","zh":"如果系統不能處理高濃度污染，污水可能仍不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the ability to handle difficult wastewater.","zh":"這個短語描述處理困難污水的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be less effective","meaning":"效果較差","examples":[{"en":"The horizontal system is less effective for strong effluent.","zh":"水平系統對高濃度污水效果較差。"},{"en":"To be less effective means to work less well or produce a weaker result.","zh":"be less effective 指運作較差或產生較弱結果。"},{"en":"Last-minute revision is less effective than daily practice for learning vocabulary.","zh":"對學習詞彙而言，臨急抱佛腳比每日練習效果較差。"},{"en":"A system may be less effective when conditions are too difficult for its design.","zh":"當條件對設計而言太困難，系統可能效果較差。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weaker performance compared with another method or condition.","zh":"這個短語描述與另一方法或情況相比表現較弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"choose two correct letters","meaning":"選出兩個正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose two correct letters for the final questions.","zh":"學生為最後問題選出兩個正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose two correct letters means to select exactly two answer options marked by letters.","zh":"choose two correct letters 指正好選出兩個以字母標示的答案選項。"},{"en":"If a question asks for two letters, writing three answers may be marked wrong.","zh":"如果題目要求兩個字母，寫三個答案可能被扣分。"},{"en":"Students should check the number required before transferring answers.","zh":"學生轉寫答案前應檢查所需數量。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a precise multiple-answer exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語給出精確的多答案考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"natural water-purification system","meaning":"天然淨水系統","examples":[{"en":"The natural water-purification system offers environmental and financial benefits.","zh":"天然淨水系統提供環境和財務好處。"},{"en":"A natural water-purification system cleans water by using natural processes such as plants, soil, and microorganisms.","zh":"natural water-purification system 指利用植物、土壤和微生物等自然過程清潔水的系統。"},{"en":"A village pond with reeds may act as a natural water-purification system for runoff.","zh":"有蘆葦的村莊池塘可以作為雨水徑流的天然淨水系統。"},{"en":"Such systems can reduce pollution while costing less to run.","zh":"這類系統可以減少污染，同時運作成本較低。"},{"en":"This phrase describes water cleaning that works with nature rather than heavy machinery.","zh":"這個短語描述順應自然而不是依賴大型機械的淨水方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"use microorganisms","meaning":"利用微生物","examples":[{"en":"Reed beds use microorganisms to digest waste.","zh":"蘆葦床利用微生物分解廢物。"},{"en":"To use microorganisms means to rely on tiny living organisms to carry out a task.","zh":"use microorganisms 指依靠微小生物執行某項工作。"},{"en":"Compost bins use microorganisms to turn food scraps into soil-like material.","zh":"堆肥箱利用微生物把食物殘渣變成像泥土的材料。"},{"en":"Using microorganisms can make waste treatment more natural and less machine-dependent.","zh":"利用微生物可以令廢物處理更天然，較少依賴機械。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using microscopic life as a working tool.","zh":"這個短語描述把顯微生命作為工作工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"low operating costs","meaning":"低運作成本","examples":[{"en":"Natural treatment systems usually have low operating costs.","zh":"天然處理系統通常有低運作成本。"},{"en":"Low operating costs are the small ongoing expenses needed to run a system.","zh":"low operating costs 指運行系統所需的持續開支較少。"},{"en":"A bicycle has low operating costs because it needs no fuel and little maintenance.","zh":"單車運作成本低，因為不需要燃料且維修少。"},{"en":"Low operating costs help small communities keep a system running for years.","zh":"低運作成本幫助小社區多年維持系統運作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to regular running costs after installation.","zh":"這個短語指安裝後的日常運行成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"help prevent flooding","meaning":"幫助防止水浸","examples":[{"en":"Wetlands can sometimes help prevent flooding by holding excess water.","zh":"濕地有時可以透過儲存多餘水量幫助防止水浸。"},{"en":"To help prevent flooding means to reduce the chance or severity of land being covered by water.","zh":"help prevent flooding 指降低土地被水淹浸的機會或嚴重程度。"},{"en":"A park with ponds can help prevent flooding by storing rainwater during storms.","zh":"有池塘的公園可以在風暴期間儲存雨水，幫助防止水浸。"},{"en":"Wetlands slow water down, so less water rushes into rivers at once.","zh":"濕地減慢水流，因此較少水一次過湧入河流。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing flood risk, not guaranteeing that floods never happen.","zh":"這個短語描述減低水災風險，而不是保證永不水浸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"visually attractive","meaning":"外觀吸引","examples":[{"en":"Reed beds can be visually attractive and improve the landscape.","zh":"蘆葦床可以外觀吸引並改善景觀。"},{"en":"Visually attractive means pleasant or appealing to look at.","zh":"visually attractive 指看起來 pleasant、有吸引力。"},{"en":"A school garden can be visually attractive if it has flowers, paths, and seating.","zh":"如果學校花園有花、小徑和座位，就可以外觀吸引。"},{"en":"Attractive treatment systems may face less public opposition because they look natural.","zh":"外觀吸引的處理系統可能較少受到公眾反對，因為看起來自然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes appearance, not technical performance.","zh":"這個短語描述外觀，而不是技術表現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"function in all climates","meaning":"能在所有氣候下運作","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether the system can function in all climates.","zh":"該陳述問系統是否能在所有氣候下運作。"},{"en":"To function in all climates means to work properly in every type of weather and temperature condition.","zh":"function in all climates 指在每種天氣和溫度條件下都能正常運作。"},{"en":"A school air-conditioning system may not function in all climates if it was designed only for mild weather.","zh":"如果學校冷氣系統只為溫和天氣設計，就未必能在所有氣候下運作。"},{"en":"A treatment system may perform differently in hot, cold, dry, or wet climates.","zh":"處理系統在炎熱、寒冷、乾燥或潮濕氣候中的表現可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether a system is universally suitable, not just locally effective.","zh":"這個短語詢問系統是否普遍適用，而不只是本地有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 162 - Water Treatment  - Reed Bed.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 163":[{"front":"teleworking","meaning":"遙距工作","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking allows employees to work away from a conventional office.","zh":"遙距工作讓員工可以在傳統辦公室以外工作。"},{"en":"Teleworking means doing one’s job from home or another place instead of a normal office.","zh":"teleworking 指在家或其他地方工作，而不是在普通辦公室工作。"},{"en":"A parent may use teleworking to finish reports at home while still taking children to school.","zh":"家長可能透過遙距工作在家完成報告，同時仍能送孩子上學。"},{"en":"Teleworking can reduce commuting time, but it may also make teamwork harder.","zh":"遙距工作可以減少通勤時間，但也可能令團隊合作更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on where work is done, not whether the job is full-time or part-time.","zh":"這個短語重點是工作地點，而不是該工作是全職還是兼職。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"work remotely","meaning":"遙距工作","examples":[{"en":"Many employees now work remotely from home.","zh":"許多員工現在在家遙距工作。"},{"en":"To work remotely means to do one’s job away from the usual workplace, often using the internet.","zh":"work remotely 指在通常工作地點以外工作，通常使用互聯網。"},{"en":"A designer can work remotely from a café if she has a laptop and a stable connection.","zh":"如果設計師有手提電腦和穩定網絡，她可以在咖啡店遙距工作。"},{"en":"If people work remotely, companies may need better online communication systems.","zh":"如果人們遙距工作，公司可能需要更好的網上溝通系統。"},{"en":"The phrase describes distance from the office, not working alone without contact.","zh":"這個短語描述離開辦公室工作，而不是完全沒有聯絡地獨自工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be said to have","meaning":"據稱具有……","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking is said to have many social and environmental benefits.","zh":"據稱，遙距工作具有許多社會和環境好處。"},{"en":"Be said to have means people claim or report that something has a particular quality or effect.","zh":"be said to have 指人們聲稱或報告某物具有某種特質或效果。"},{"en":"This new study method is said to have helped many students remember vocabulary faster.","zh":"據稱，這種新學習方法幫助許多學生更快記住詞彙。"},{"en":"When something is said to have benefits, the writer may later examine whether the claim is true.","zh":"當某事據稱有好處，作者之後可能檢視該說法是否真確。"},{"en":"The phrase reports a claim without always proving it immediately.","zh":"這個短語報告一種說法，但不一定立即證明它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"benefits for organisations","meaning":"對機構的好處","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking may provide significant benefits for organisations.","zh":"遙距工作可能為機構帶來重大好處。"},{"en":"Benefits for organisations are advantages that help companies, schools, charities, or public bodies operate better.","zh":"benefits for organisations 指幫助公司、學校、慈善機構或公共機構運作得更好的優點。"},{"en":"Flexible working can bring benefits for organisations by reducing office costs and improving staff retention.","zh":"彈性工作可以透過減少辦公室成本和改善員工留任率，為機構帶來好處。"},{"en":"If employees are more productive at home, the organisation may save money and finish work faster.","zh":"如果員工在家生產力更高，機構可能節省金錢並更快完成工作。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on institutional advantages, not only personal comfort.","zh":"這個短語重點是機構層面的優勢，而不只是個人舒適。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"provoke mixed reactions","meaning":"引起不同反應","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking provokes mixed reactions among employees and managers.","zh":"遙距工作在員工和管理者之間引起不同反應。"},{"en":"To provoke mixed reactions means to cause different people to respond in different ways.","zh":"provoke mixed reactions 指令不同人有不同回應。"},{"en":"A new school uniform rule may provoke mixed reactions from students, parents, and teachers.","zh":"新校服規定可能在學生、家長和老師之間引起不同反應。"},{"en":"Teleworking can please employees who want flexibility but worry managers who value direct supervision.","zh":"遙距工作可以令想要彈性的員工高興，但令重視直接監督的管理者擔心。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a change is not welcomed or rejected by everyone in the same way.","zh":"這個短語顯示某改變不是被所有人以同一方式歡迎或拒絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"acolytes","meaning":"忠實支持者","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking has enthusiastic acolytes who strongly support it.","zh":"遙距工作有熱情的忠實支持者，他們強烈支持它。"},{"en":"Acolytes are loyal followers or strong supporters of an idea, person, or movement.","zh":"acolytes 指某想法、人物或運動的忠誠追隨者或強烈支持者。"},{"en":"A new teaching method may attract acolytes who praise it at every staff meeting.","zh":"新教學方法可能吸引忠實支持者，他們在每次教職員會議都稱讚它。"},{"en":"Enthusiastic acolytes can help spread an idea, but they may also ignore its weaknesses.","zh":"熱情支持者可以幫助傳播想法，但也可能忽視其弱點。"},{"en":"The word is often used slightly critically for devoted supporters.","zh":"這個詞常略帶批評意味，用於形容非常投入的支持者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"experience something first-hand","meaning":"親身經歷某事","examples":[{"en":"Some employees experience the advantages and drawbacks of teleworking first-hand.","zh":"有些員工親身經歷遙距工作的優點和缺點。"},{"en":"To experience something first-hand means to know it directly through personal experience.","zh":"experience something first-hand 指透過個人經驗直接了解某事。"},{"en":"A student who joins an exchange programme experiences cultural differences first-hand.","zh":"參加交流計劃的學生會親身經歷文化差異。"},{"en":"First-hand experience often makes a person’s opinion more practical and less theoretical.","zh":"親身經驗通常令人的看法更實際、更少理論化。"},{"en":"The phrase means learning by living through something, not only reading about it.","zh":"這個短語指透過親身經歷學習，而不只是閱讀相關資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"whether you like it or not","meaning":"不論你喜歡與否","examples":[{"en":"Whether you like it or not, work is becoming less dependent on location.","zh":"不論你喜歡與否，工作正變得較少依賴地點。"},{"en":"Whether you like it or not means something is true or will happen even if you dislike it.","zh":"whether you like it or not 指即使你不喜歡，某事仍然是真實或會發生。"},{"en":"Whether you like it or not, students need to check grammar carefully before submitting essays.","zh":"不論你喜歡與否，學生提交作文前都需要仔細檢查文法。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when a change cannot easily be avoided.","zh":"這個短語用於某個改變不容易避免的情況。"},{"en":"It can sound direct, so it is often used to stress reality.","zh":"它聽起來可以較直接，所以常用來強調現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"it is true to say that","meaning":"可以說","examples":[{"en":"It is true to say that modern work is no longer tied to one location.","zh":"可以說，現代工作不再綁定於單一地點。"},{"en":"It is true to say that means it is accurate or reasonable to make this statement.","zh":"it is true to say that 指作出這個陳述是準確或合理的。"},{"en":"It is true to say that regular practice matters more than last-minute revision.","zh":"可以說，定期練習比臨急抱佛腳更重要。"},{"en":"Writers use the phrase to present a general claim carefully rather than aggressively.","zh":"作者使用這個短語，以較謹慎而非強硬的方式提出一般說法。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a statement the writer believes is supported by evidence.","zh":"這個短語引入作者認為有證據支持的陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be dependent on geography","meaning":"受地理位置限制","examples":[{"en":"Many forms of work are no longer dependent on geography.","zh":"許多工作形式不再受地理位置限制。"},{"en":"To be dependent on geography means to be limited by where people live or where an office is located.","zh":"be dependent on geography 指受人們居住地或辦公室所在地限制。"},{"en":"Online tutoring is less dependent on geography because students can learn from teachers in another city.","zh":"網上補習較少受地理位置限制，因為學生可以向另一個城市的老師學習。"},{"en":"If a job is not tied to location, employers can hire from a wider area.","zh":"如果工作不受地點限制，僱主可以從更廣地區聘請人才。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how physical place affects opportunity.","zh":"這個短語描述實體地點如何影響機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"open up opportunities","meaning":"開拓機會","examples":[{"en":"Remote technology opens up opportunities for new ways of working.","zh":"遙距科技為新的工作方式開拓機會。"},{"en":"To open up opportunities means to create new chances that were not available before.","zh":"open up opportunities 指創造以前沒有的新機會。"},{"en":"Online courses open up opportunities for students who cannot travel to a city school.","zh":"網上課程為不能到城市學校上課的學生開拓機會。"},{"en":"When technology reduces distance, people can access jobs, lessons, and services more easily.","zh":"當科技減少距離限制，人們可以更容易接觸工作、課程和服務。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests removing limits and creating possibilities.","zh":"這個短語暗示移除限制並創造可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a range of opportunities","meaning":"一系列機會","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking creates a range of opportunities for employers and staff.","zh":"遙距工作為僱主和員工創造一系列機會。"},{"en":"A range of opportunities means several different chances or possibilities.","zh":"a range of opportunities 指幾種不同機會或可能性。"},{"en":"A school careers fair gives students a range of opportunities to meet employers and ask questions.","zh":"學校職業展為學生提供一系列機會，讓他們見僱主和提問。"},{"en":"Teleworking may create opportunities to save office space, hire distant workers, and improve flexibility.","zh":"遙距工作可能創造節省辦公空間、聘請遠方員工和改善彈性的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses variety, not just one single chance.","zh":"這個短語強調多樣性，而不是單一機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"work in new ways","meaning":"以新方式工作","examples":[{"en":"Digital technology allows people to work in new ways.","zh":"數碼科技讓人們以新方式工作。"},{"en":"To work in new ways means to use different methods, places, schedules, or tools for doing a job.","zh":"work in new ways 指使用不同方法、地點、時間安排或工具來完成工作。"},{"en":"Teachers work in new ways when they use online quizzes and video feedback.","zh":"老師使用網上測驗和影片回饋時，就是以新方式工作。"},{"en":"New ways of working can improve flexibility but may require new rules and habits.","zh":"新工作方式可以改善彈性，但也可能需要新規則和習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on changed work methods, not merely using new equipment.","zh":"這個短語重點是工作方法改變，而不只是使用新設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"working environments","meaning":"工作環境","examples":[{"en":"Teleworkers can choose from a variety of working environments.","zh":"遙距工作者可以從多種工作環境中選擇。"},{"en":"Working environments are the places and conditions in which people do their jobs.","zh":"working environments 指人們工作的地點和條件。"},{"en":"A quiet home office, a shared workspace, and a company office are different working environments.","zh":"安靜家庭辦公室、共享工作空間和公司辦公室都是不同工作環境。"},{"en":"A good working environment can improve concentration, comfort, and productivity.","zh":"良好工作環境可以改善專注力、舒適度和生產力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to both physical setting and work conditions.","zh":"這個短語同時指實體環境和工作條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"surveys show that","meaning":"調查顯示","examples":[{"en":"Surveys show that teleworking can increase productivity.","zh":"調查顯示遙距工作可以提高生產力。"},{"en":"Surveys show that means questionnaire results or collected responses provide evidence for a claim.","zh":"surveys show that 指問卷結果或收集到的回應為某說法提供證據。"},{"en":"Surveys show that many students prefer short feedback videos to long written comments.","zh":"調查顯示許多學生比起長篇書面評語，更喜歡短回饋影片。"},{"en":"Survey evidence can reveal broad patterns in how people think or behave.","zh":"調查證據可以揭示人們想法或行為上的廣泛模式。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces evidence from people’s reported experiences or opinions.","zh":"這個短語引入來自人們回報經驗或意見的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"productivity increase","meaning":"生產力提升","examples":[{"en":"The productivity increase was not mainly caused by longer working hours.","zh":"生產力提升並非主要由較長工時造成。"},{"en":"A productivity increase is a rise in the amount or quality of work produced in a given time.","zh":"productivity increase 指在特定時間內完成的工作數量或質素上升。"},{"en":"A student may see a productivity increase after turning off her phone during study time.","zh":"學生在溫習時關掉電話後，可能出現生產力提升。"},{"en":"Productivity can increase because people face fewer interruptions, not just because they work longer.","zh":"生產力可以因干擾減少而提升，而不只是因為工作時間較長。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on more effective output.","zh":"這個短語重點是更有效產出。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"primarily because of","meaning":"主要由於……","examples":[{"en":"The improvement was not primarily because of employees working longer.","zh":"改善並非主要由於員工工作時間更長。"},{"en":"Primarily because of means mainly as a result of one factor.","zh":"primarily because of 指主要因某一因素而造成。"},{"en":"A student improved primarily because of daily practice, not because of luck.","zh":"學生進步主要由於每天練習，而不是運氣。"},{"en":"The phrase helps identify the main cause while allowing other smaller causes.","zh":"這個短語幫助指出主要原因，同時容許仍有較小原因。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining why something happened.","zh":"它適合用於解釋某事為何發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"longer working hours","meaning":"較長工時","examples":[{"en":"Some teleworkers report longer working hours.","zh":"有些遙距工作者表示工時較長。"},{"en":"Longer working hours means spending more time working than before or than expected.","zh":"longer working hours 指比以前或比預期花更多時間工作。"},{"en":"A teacher may have longer working hours during exam season because there are more papers to mark.","zh":"老師在考試季可能因為要批改更多試卷而工時較長。"},{"en":"Longer hours can increase output, but they may also cause tiredness and stress.","zh":"較長工時可以增加產出，但也可能造成疲倦和壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes time spent working, not necessarily better work.","zh":"這個短語描述工作時間，不一定代表工作更好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as is sometimes suggested","meaning":"正如有時所說","examples":[{"en":"Higher productivity is not simply the result of longer hours, as is sometimes suggested.","zh":"生產力較高並不單純是較長工時的結果，正如有時所說那樣。"},{"en":"As is sometimes suggested means as some people occasionally claim or imply.","zh":"as is sometimes suggested 指正如有些人偶爾聲稱或暗示。"},{"en":"Good grades are not only about natural talent, as is sometimes suggested.","zh":"好成績不只是關於天賦，正如有時所說那樣。"},{"en":"The phrase lets the writer refer to a common idea while questioning it.","zh":"這個短語讓作者提到一個常見想法，同時質疑它。"},{"en":"It often introduces a correction to an oversimplified claim.","zh":"它常用來修正過分簡化的說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"although prevalent","meaning":"雖然很普遍","examples":[{"en":"Although prevalent, working longer is not the most important factor.","zh":"雖然工作時間較長很普遍，但它不是最重要因素。"},{"en":"Although prevalent means although something is common or widespread.","zh":"although prevalent 指雖然某事常見或廣泛存在。"},{"en":"Although prevalent, online revision videos are not always enough without practice.","zh":"雖然網上溫習影片很普遍，但沒有練習時不一定足夠。"},{"en":"A common behaviour may still be less important than another hidden factor.","zh":"常見行為仍可能不及另一個隱藏因素重要。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts frequency with importance.","zh":"這個短語對比普遍程度與重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"influencing factors","meaning":"影響因素","examples":[{"en":"Longer hours are only one of several influencing factors.","zh":"較長工時只是幾個影響因素之一。"},{"en":"Influencing factors are things that affect a result or decision.","zh":"influencing factors 指會影響結果或決定的事物。"},{"en":"Sleep, practice, and confidence are influencing factors in exam performance.","zh":"睡眠、練習和信心都是考試表現的影響因素。"},{"en":"If many factors influence productivity, managers should not blame or praise one cause only.","zh":"如果許多因素影響生產力，管理者不應只歸因於單一原因。"},{"en":"The phrase points to causes that shape an outcome.","zh":"這個短語指出塑造結果的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"closely matched control group","meaning":"條件非常相近的對照組","examples":[{"en":"The researchers compared teleworkers with a closely matched control group.","zh":"研究人員把遙距工作者與條件非常相近的對照組比較。"},{"en":"A closely matched control group is a comparison group made very similar to the study group except for the factor being tested.","zh":"closely matched control group 指除正在測試的因素外，與研究組非常相似的比較組。"},{"en":"A school study may compare students in two classes with similar ages, marks, and backgrounds.","zh":"學校研究可能比較兩班年齡、分數和背景相近的學生。"},{"en":"Matching groups closely helps researchers judge whether the tested factor really matters.","zh":"令組別條件相近有助研究人員判斷被測試因素是否真正重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a careful research design for fair comparison.","zh":"這個短語描述用於公平比較的仔細研究設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"non-teleworkers","meaning":"非遙距工作者","examples":[{"en":"The control group consisted of non-teleworkers.","zh":"對照組由非遙距工作者組成。"},{"en":"Non-teleworkers are employees who do not work remotely and usually work at the normal workplace.","zh":"non-teleworkers 指不遙距工作、通常在正常工作地點工作的員工。"},{"en":"In a company survey, non-teleworkers may include receptionists, factory staff, and office-based managers.","zh":"在公司調查中，非遙距工作者可能包括接待員、工廠員工和駐辦公室經理。"},{"en":"Comparing teleworkers with non-teleworkers can show whether remote work changes productivity or absence.","zh":"比較遙距工作者與非遙距工作者，可以顯示遙距工作是否改變生產力或缺勤。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the group not using teleworking.","zh":"這個短語指出沒有使用遙距工作的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"not only…but also…","meaning":"不但……而且……","examples":[{"en":"Teleworkers showed not only higher productivity but also lower absenteeism.","zh":"遙距工作者不但生產力較高，而且缺勤較少。"},{"en":"Not only…but also… connects two points and emphasises that both are true.","zh":"not only…but also… 連接兩個重點，並強調兩者都成立。"},{"en":"Good sleep helps students not only remember more but also feel calmer in exams.","zh":"良好睡眠不但幫助學生記得更多，而且令他們在考試中更冷靜。"},{"en":"The structure is useful when one result is already positive and another result strengthens it.","zh":"當一個結果已經正面，而另一個結果進一步加強它時，這個句式很有用。"},{"en":"It presents a double benefit or double effect.","zh":"它呈現雙重好處或雙重效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"absenteeism","meaning":"缺勤","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking may help reduce employee absenteeism.","zh":"遙距工作可能有助減少員工缺勤。"},{"en":"Absenteeism is the habit or rate of employees being absent from work.","zh":"absenteeism 指員工缺席工作的習慣或比率。"},{"en":"A school may track student absenteeism to see whether illness or stress is causing missed lessons.","zh":"學校可能追蹤學生缺勤，以了解疾病或壓力是否導致缺課。"},{"en":"If employees can work from home when mildly ill or blocked by transport problems, absenteeism may fall.","zh":"如果員工輕微生病或受交通問題阻礙時仍可在家工作，缺勤可能下降。"},{"en":"The word refers to absence from work or school, not simply taking approved holidays.","zh":"這個詞指工作或上學缺席，而不只是獲批准假期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"error rates","meaning":"錯誤率","examples":[{"en":"The teleworkers also had lower error rates.","zh":"遙距工作者的錯誤率也較低。"},{"en":"Error rates are the frequency or percentage of mistakes in work, tests, or processes.","zh":"error rates 指工作、測驗或流程中錯誤出現的頻率或百分比。"},{"en":"A student’s error rate in spelling may fall after regular correction practice.","zh":"學生定期改正練習後，串字錯誤率可能下降。"},{"en":"Lower error rates can improve quality and reduce the time spent fixing mistakes.","zh":"較低錯誤率可以改善質素並減少修正錯誤所花時間。"},{"en":"The phrase measures how often mistakes happen.","zh":"這個短語量度錯誤發生得有多頻密。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"add to the knowledge base","meaning":"擴充知識基礎","examples":[{"en":"The SUSTEL research added to the economic knowledge base on teleworking.","zh":"SUSTEL 研究擴充了關於遙距工作的經濟知識基礎。"},{"en":"To add to the knowledge base means to increase what is known about a subject.","zh":"add to the knowledge base 指增加人們對某主題已知的內容。"},{"en":"A small classroom study can add to the knowledge base on how students learn vocabulary.","zh":"小型課室研究可以擴充關於學生如何學習詞彙的知識基礎。"},{"en":"New findings help future researchers, employers, and policymakers make better decisions.","zh":"新發現幫助未來研究人員、僱主和政策制定者作出更好決定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes contributing useful information to an existing field.","zh":"這個短語描述為現有領域貢獻有用資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"economic impact","meaning":"經濟影響","examples":[{"en":"The research examined the economic impact of teleworking.","zh":"該研究檢視遙距工作的經濟影響。"},{"en":"Economic impact means the effect something has on costs, income, productivity, jobs, or business activity.","zh":"economic impact 指某事對成本、收入、生產力、職位或商業活動的影響。"},{"en":"A new train line may have an economic impact by helping shops attract more customers.","zh":"新鐵路線可能透過幫助商店吸引更多顧客而產生經濟影響。"},{"en":"Teleworking can affect office rent, employee travel costs, and company productivity.","zh":"遙距工作可以影響辦公室租金、員工交通成本和公司生產力。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on money and economic activity.","zh":"這個短語重點是金錢和經濟活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"space utilisation","meaning":"空間運用","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking can improve an organisation’s space utilisation.","zh":"遙距工作可以改善機構的空間運用。"},{"en":"Space utilisation is how efficiently rooms, desks, buildings, or land are used.","zh":"space utilisation 指房間、桌位、建築物或土地被使用得有多有效率。"},{"en":"A school improves space utilisation when it uses an empty classroom for after-school tutoring.","zh":"學校把空置課室用於課後補習，就是改善空間運用。"},{"en":"If fewer employees need desks every day, a company can use office space more efficiently.","zh":"如果每天需要辦公桌的員工較少，公司就能更有效使用辦公空間。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on making better use of physical space.","zh":"這個短語重點是更好使用實體空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the case of","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"In the case of absenteeism, teleworking produced clear benefits.","zh":"就缺勤而言，遙距工作帶來明顯好處。"},{"en":"In the case of means when considering this particular example, topic, or situation.","zh":"in the case of 指在考慮這個特定例子、題目或情況時。"},{"en":"In the case of listening exams, students must practise speed as well as vocabulary.","zh":"就聆聽考試而言，學生必須練習速度，也要練習詞彙。"},{"en":"The phrase helps narrow a general discussion to one specific area.","zh":"這個短語幫助把一般討論收窄至一個具體範疇。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing several separate effects.","zh":"它適合用於比較幾種不同影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"those surveyed","meaning":"受訪者","examples":[{"en":"Over 60 per cent of those surveyed reported that they could work during disruptions.","zh":"超過百分之六十的受訪者表示，他們能在受阻期間工作。"},{"en":"Those surveyed are the people who answered questions in a survey.","zh":"those surveyed 指在調查中回答問題的人。"},{"en":"Those surveyed in a school questionnaire may include students, teachers, and parents.","zh":"學校問卷中的受訪者可能包括學生、老師和家長。"},{"en":"The opinions of those surveyed help researchers understand patterns in a group.","zh":"受訪者的意見幫助研究人員理解群體中的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase refers only to respondents, not necessarily everyone in society.","zh":"這個短語只指回應調查的人，不一定是社會上所有人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"enable someone to work","meaning":"讓某人能夠工作","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking enabled employees to work when they could not reach the office.","zh":"遙距工作讓員工在不能到達辦公室時仍能工作。"},{"en":"To enable someone to work means to make it possible for that person to do their job.","zh":"enable someone to work 指令某人能夠完成自己的工作。"},{"en":"A school laptop can enable a student to work from home during bad weather.","zh":"學校手提電腦可以讓學生在惡劣天氣中在家工作。"},{"en":"If technology enables people to work during disruptions, organisations lose fewer working hours.","zh":"如果科技讓人在受阻期間仍能工作，機構就會損失較少工作時間。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on making work possible despite obstacles.","zh":"這個短語重點是在有障礙下仍使工作成為可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be prevented from","meaning":"因……而無法","examples":[{"en":"Some employees were prevented from reaching their workplace by illness.","zh":"有些員工因病而無法到達工作場所。"},{"en":"To be prevented from doing something means to be stopped from doing it by a problem or barrier.","zh":"be prevented from doing something 指因問題或障礙而被阻止做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be prevented from attending class by a transport strike.","zh":"學生可能因交通罷工而無法上課。"},{"en":"When people are prevented from travelling, remote tools may allow them to continue working.","zh":"當人們無法出行，遙距工具可能讓他們繼續工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes being blocked, not simply choosing not to act.","zh":"這個短語描述受到阻礙，而不是單純選擇不行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reach a work location","meaning":"到達工作地點","examples":[{"en":"Illness or transport problems may prevent someone from reaching a work location.","zh":"疾病或交通問題可能阻止某人到達工作地點。"},{"en":"To reach a work location means to arrive at the place where one normally works.","zh":"reach a work location 指到達某人通常工作的地方。"},{"en":"A nurse may fail to reach her work location on time if roads are flooded.","zh":"如果道路水浸，護士可能無法準時到達工作地點。"},{"en":"If employees cannot reach the workplace, teleworking can reduce lost time.","zh":"如果員工不能到達工作場所，遙距工作可以減少損失時間。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to physical arrival at a workplace.","zh":"這個短語指實際到達工作場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"transport problems","meaning":"交通問題","examples":[{"en":"Transport problems can stop employees from travelling to the office.","zh":"交通問題可以阻止員工前往辦公室。"},{"en":"Transport problems are difficulties with buses, trains, roads, traffic, or other travel systems.","zh":"transport problems 指巴士、火車、道路、交通擠塞或其他出行系統的困難。"},{"en":"A train delay is a transport problem that can make students late for school.","zh":"火車延誤是交通問題，可能令學生上學遲到。"},{"en":"When transport problems are frequent, remote work or flexible hours may reduce stress.","zh":"當交通問題頻繁，遙距工作或彈性工時可能減少壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes travel-related obstacles.","zh":"這個短語描述與出行有關的障礙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in around half the cases","meaning":"在約一半個案中","examples":[{"en":"In around half the cases, organisations reported reduced space requirements.","zh":"在約一半個案中，機構表示空間需求減少。"},{"en":"In around half the cases means in approximately 50 per cent of the examples studied.","zh":"in around half the cases 指在所研究例子中約百分之五十的情況。"},{"en":"In around half the cases, students improved after receiving weekly feedback.","zh":"在約一半個案中，學生在收到每週回饋後進步。"},{"en":"The phrase reports a common pattern without saying it happened every time.","zh":"這個短語報告常見模式，但不是說每次都發生。"},{"en":"It is useful for describing survey or research results.","zh":"它適合用於描述調查或研究結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"respondents","meaning":"受訪者","examples":[{"en":"Many respondents identified substantial reductions in office space.","zh":"許多受訪者指出辦公空間大幅減少。"},{"en":"Respondents are people who answer questions in a survey, interview, or questionnaire.","zh":"respondents 指在調查、訪問或問卷中回答問題的人。"},{"en":"Survey respondents may be asked about travel habits, work stress, or family time.","zh":"調查受訪者可能被問及出行習慣、工作壓力或家庭時間。"},{"en":"Researchers analyse respondents’ answers to find patterns and differences.","zh":"研究人員分析受訪者答案，以找出模式和差異。"},{"en":"The word refers to people who respond to research questions.","zh":"這個詞指回應研究問題的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"identify substantial reductions","meaning":"指出大幅減少","examples":[{"en":"Respondents identified substantial reductions in space requirements.","zh":"受訪者指出空間需求大幅減少。"},{"en":"To identify substantial reductions means to notice and report large decreases.","zh":"identify substantial reductions 指注意到並報告大幅下降。"},{"en":"A school may identify substantial reductions in printing costs after moving forms online.","zh":"學校把表格轉到網上後，可能指出列印成本大幅減少。"},{"en":"Large reductions can change budgets, planning, and daily operations.","zh":"大幅減少可以改變預算、規劃和日常運作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recognising a significant fall in something.","zh":"這個短語描述辨認某事顯著下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"space requirements","meaning":"空間需求","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking can reduce an organisation’s space requirements.","zh":"遙距工作可以減少機構的空間需求。"},{"en":"Space requirements are the amount of physical space needed for work, storage, meetings, or operations.","zh":"space requirements 指工作、儲存、會議或運作所需的實體空間量。"},{"en":"A growing school may have higher space requirements if it accepts more students.","zh":"如果學校收更多學生，發展中的學校可能有更高空間需求。"},{"en":"If fewer staff need desks every day, office space requirements can fall.","zh":"如果每天需要辦公桌的員工較少，辦公室空間需求可以下降。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how much space is needed.","zh":"這個短語重點是需要多少空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"to the point where","meaning":"甚至到了……的程度","examples":[{"en":"One organisation reduced its office needs to the point where it closed its central office.","zh":"一個機構把辦公室需求減少，甚至到了關閉中央辦公室的程度。"},{"en":"To the point where means reaching such a degree that a particular result happens.","zh":"to the point where 指達到某種程度，以致某結果發生。"},{"en":"The noise grew to the point where students could no longer hear the teacher.","zh":"噪音變大，甚至到了學生再也聽不到老師說話的程度。"},{"en":"If office use falls enough, a company may no longer need a central office.","zh":"如果辦公室使用量下降足夠多，公司可能不再需要中央辦公室。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a change has become strong enough to cause a major consequence.","zh":"這個短語顯示某變化已強到造成重大後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"do away with","meaning":"廢除；取消","examples":[{"en":"One organisation completely did away with its central office.","zh":"一個機構完全取消了中央辦公室。"},{"en":"To do away with something means to remove, abolish, or stop using it.","zh":"do away with something 指移除、廢除或停止使用某物。"},{"en":"A school may do away with paper notices and send messages through an app instead.","zh":"學校可能取消紙本通告，改為透過應用程式發訊息。"},{"en":"If a company no longer needs a physical office, it may do away with that cost.","zh":"如果公司不再需要實體辦公室，它可能取消該項成本。"},{"en":"The phrase describes eliminating something that was previously used.","zh":"這個短語描述消除以前使用的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"central office","meaning":"中央辦公室","examples":[{"en":"Some companies no longer require a large central office.","zh":"一些公司不再需要大型中央辦公室。"},{"en":"A central office is the main workplace or headquarters where staff traditionally gather.","zh":"central office 指員工傳統上聚集的主要工作場所或總部。"},{"en":"A charity’s central office may handle finance, planning, and staff meetings.","zh":"慈善機構的中央辦公室可能處理財務、規劃和員工會議。"},{"en":"If many employees work remotely, the need for a central office may decrease.","zh":"如果許多員工遙距工作，對中央辦公室的需要可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the main office location, not every small branch.","zh":"這個短語指主要辦公地點，而不是每個小分部。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"regarding","meaning":"關於……","examples":[{"en":"Regarding weekend travel, home-based workers may behave differently from office workers.","zh":"關於週末出行，在家工作者的行為可能與辦公室員工不同。"},{"en":"Regarding means about or concerning a particular topic.","zh":"regarding 指關於或涉及某個特定題目。"},{"en":"Regarding homework, the teacher said students should submit it before Friday.","zh":"關於功課，老師說學生應在星期五前提交。"},{"en":"The word helps introduce the subject being discussed next.","zh":"這個詞幫助引入接下來要討論的主題。"},{"en":"It is common in formal writing and business communication.","zh":"它常見於正式寫作和商業溝通。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"non-commuting travel","meaning":"非通勤出行","examples":[{"en":"The study also examined non-commuting travel at weekends.","zh":"該研究也檢視週末的非通勤出行。"},{"en":"Non-commuting travel is travel that is not for going between home and work.","zh":"non-commuting travel 指不是往返家和工作地點的出行。"},{"en":"Shopping trips, visits to friends, and weekend leisure journeys are non-commuting travel.","zh":"購物、探訪朋友和週末休閒旅程都是非通勤出行。"},{"en":"If people work from home, their commuting may fall but other local travel may increase.","zh":"如果人們在家工作，他們的通勤可能減少，但其他本地出行可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase separates work travel from other types of travel.","zh":"這個短語把工作出行與其他出行類型分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"home-based workers","meaning":"在家工作者","examples":[{"en":"Home-based workers include many people who are not formal telecommuters.","zh":"在家工作者包括許多並非正式遙距辦公者的人。"},{"en":"Home-based workers are people who do some or all of their work from home.","zh":"home-based workers 指部分或全部工作在家完成的人。"},{"en":"A freelance designer and a remote call-centre employee can both be home-based workers.","zh":"自由身設計師和遙距客服中心員工都可以是在家工作者。"},{"en":"Home-based workers may use more local shops because they spend more time near home.","zh":"在家工作者可能使用更多本地商店，因為他們有更多時間留在家附近。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the worker’s base location, not the exact job type.","zh":"這個短語重點是工作者的基地位置，而不是確切工作類型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"substantial population","meaning":"相當龐大的人口群","examples":[{"en":"Home-based workers form a substantial population.","zh":"在家工作者形成一個相當龐大的人口群。"},{"en":"A substantial population is a large enough group to be important or noticeable.","zh":"substantial population 指大到重要或值得注意的群體。"},{"en":"International students form a substantial population in some university towns.","zh":"在一些大學城，國際學生形成相當龐大的人口群。"},{"en":"If a group is substantial, its behaviour can affect local shops, transport, and services.","zh":"如果某群體相當龐大，其行為可以影響本地商店、交通和服務。"},{"en":"The phrase means a sizeable group, not necessarily the majority.","zh":"這個短語指數量可觀的群體，不一定是大多數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"spend more time doing","meaning":"花更多時間做……","examples":[{"en":"Home-based workers spend more time shopping away from home.","zh":"在家工作者花更多時間在外購物。"},{"en":"To spend more time doing something means to use a greater amount of time on that activity.","zh":"spend more time doing something 指把更多時間用於某活動。"},{"en":"Students who want better pronunciation may spend more time listening to natural speech.","zh":"想改善發音的學生可能花更多時間聽自然語音。"},{"en":"If people spend more time in local shops, neighbourhood businesses may benefit.","zh":"如果人們花更多時間在本地商店，社區企業可能受益。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change in how time is used.","zh":"這個短語描述時間使用方式的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"traditional workers","meaning":"傳統工作模式的員工","examples":[{"en":"The study compared home-based workers with traditional workers.","zh":"該研究把在家工作者與傳統工作模式的員工作比較。"},{"en":"Traditional workers are employees who work in the usual office or workplace rather than mainly from home.","zh":"traditional workers 指在普通辦公室或工作場所工作，而不是主要在家工作的人。"},{"en":"A traditional worker may commute to the same office every weekday.","zh":"傳統工作模式的員工可能每個工作日通勤到同一辦公室。"},{"en":"Comparing traditional workers with home-based workers can show how work location affects daily habits.","zh":"比較傳統員工與在家工作者，可以顯示工作地點如何影響日常習慣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes conventional work arrangements.","zh":"這個短語描述傳統工作安排。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"half-time telecommuting","meaning":"一半時間遙距辦公","examples":[{"en":"Half-time telecommuting could greatly reduce carbon emissions.","zh":"一半時間遙距辦公可以大幅減少碳排放。"},{"en":"Half-time telecommuting means working remotely for about half of one’s working time.","zh":"half-time telecommuting 指大約一半工作時間遙距工作。"},{"en":"An employee may work from home on Mondays and Fridays as part of half-time telecommuting.","zh":"員工可能星期一和星期五在家工作，作為一半時間遙距辦公的一部分。"},{"en":"If millions of people commute only half as often, fuel use and emissions may fall.","zh":"如果數百萬人通勤次數減半，燃料使用和排放可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a partial remote-work arrangement, not full-time home working.","zh":"這個短語描述部分遙距工作安排，而不是全職在家工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reduce carbon emissions","meaning":"減少碳排放","examples":[{"en":"Telecommuting could reduce carbon emissions substantially.","zh":"遙距辦公可以大幅減少碳排放。"},{"en":"To reduce carbon emissions means to lower the amount of carbon dioxide released into the air.","zh":"reduce carbon emissions 指降低釋放到空氣中的二氧化碳量。"},{"en":"Taking the bus instead of driving alone can reduce carbon emissions.","zh":"乘巴士而不是獨自駕車可以減少碳排放。"},{"en":"If fewer employees commute by car, transport-related emissions may decrease.","zh":"如果較少員工開車通勤，與交通相關的排放可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used in environmental discussions about climate change.","zh":"這個短語常用於關於氣候變化的環境討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"metric tons a year","meaning":"每年……公噸","examples":[{"en":"The estimated saving exceeds 51 million metric tons a year.","zh":"估計節省量超過每年5100萬公噸。"},{"en":"Metric tons a year measures an amount saved, used, or produced each year in tonnes.","zh":"metric tons a year 以公噸量度每年節省、使用或生產的數量。"},{"en":"A recycling programme may save several thousand metric tons of waste a year.","zh":"回收計劃可能每年節省數千公噸垃圾。"},{"en":"Annual figures help compare long-term environmental effects across policies.","zh":"年度數字幫助比較不同政策的長期環境影響。"},{"en":"The phrase gives both a unit and a time period.","zh":"這個短語同時提供單位和時間段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the equivalent of","meaning":"相當於","examples":[{"en":"The reduction would be the equivalent of removing millions of commuters from the road.","zh":"這項減幅相當於把數百萬通勤者從道路上移除。"},{"en":"The equivalent of means equal in value, effect, amount, or meaning to something else.","zh":"the equivalent of 指在價值、效果、數量或意思上等同於另一事物。"},{"en":"Walking 10,000 steps may be the equivalent of several kilometres of movement.","zh":"走一萬步可能相當於行走幾公里。"},{"en":"Comparisons using equivalents help readers understand large numbers more easily.","zh":"使用等值比較可以幫助讀者更容易理解大數字。"},{"en":"The phrase explains an unfamiliar amount by comparing it with a familiar effect.","zh":"這個短語透過與熟悉效果比較，解釋陌生數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take commuters off the road","meaning":"減少道路上的通勤者","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking can effectively take commuters off the road.","zh":"遙距工作可以有效減少道路上的通勤者。"},{"en":"To take commuters off the road means to reduce the number of people travelling by road to work.","zh":"take commuters off the road 指減少經道路上班的人數。"},{"en":"A company shuttle bus can take commuters off the road if workers stop driving separate cars.","zh":"如果員工不再各自駕車，公司穿梭巴士可以減少道路上的通勤者。"},{"en":"Fewer commuters on roads can reduce traffic, fuel use, and air pollution.","zh":"道路上的通勤者減少，可以減少交通擠塞、燃料使用和空氣污染。"},{"en":"The phrase is usually about reducing road traffic, not physically removing people.","zh":"這個短語通常指減少道路交通，而不是字面移走人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"additional carbon-footprint savings","meaning":"額外的碳足跡減幅","examples":[{"en":"Additional carbon-footprint savings can come from lower office energy use.","zh":"額外的碳足跡減幅可以來自較低的辦公室能源使用。"},{"en":"Additional carbon-footprint savings are further reductions in the environmental impact caused by a person or organisation.","zh":"additional carbon-footprint savings 指個人或機構造成的環境影響進一步減少。"},{"en":"A family may gain additional carbon-footprint savings by using less heating after improving insulation.","zh":"家庭改善隔熱後少用暖氣，可能獲得額外碳足跡減幅。"},{"en":"If offices use less electricity, teleworking can save emissions beyond commuting alone.","zh":"如果辦公室用電較少，遙距工作節省的排放就不只來自通勤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to extra environmental savings.","zh":"這個短語指額外環境節省。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"carbon footprint","meaning":"碳足跡","examples":[{"en":"Reduced travel can lower an employee’s carbon footprint.","zh":"減少出行可以降低員工的碳足跡。"},{"en":"A carbon footprint is the total greenhouse-gas impact caused by a person, product, activity, or organisation.","zh":"carbon footprint 指個人、產品、活動或機構造成的總溫室氣體影響。"},{"en":"A student can reduce her carbon footprint by walking to school and wasting less food.","zh":"學生可以透過步行上學和減少浪費食物來降低碳足跡。"},{"en":"Lower carbon footprints help reduce pressure on the climate.","zh":"較低碳足跡有助減少對氣候的壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase measures environmental impact, not the physical size of a footmark.","zh":"這個短語量度環境影響，而不是腳印的實體大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reduced office energy use","meaning":"減少辦公室能源使用","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking may result in reduced office energy use.","zh":"遙距工作可能導致辦公室能源使用減少。"},{"en":"Reduced office energy use means less electricity, heating, cooling, or lighting is needed in offices.","zh":"reduced office energy use 指辦公室需要較少電力、暖氣、冷氣或照明。"},{"en":"A company may have reduced office energy use if fewer floors are open each day.","zh":"如果每天開放較少樓層，公司可能減少辦公室能源使用。"},{"en":"Lower office energy use can cut costs and reduce emissions.","zh":"較低辦公室能源使用可以減少成本和排放。"},{"en":"The phrase describes energy savings in workplace buildings.","zh":"這個短語描述工作場所建築中的能源節省。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"roadway repairs","meaning":"道路維修","examples":[{"en":"Less commuting may reduce the need for roadway repairs.","zh":"較少通勤可能減少對道路維修的需要。"},{"en":"Roadway repairs are maintenance work done to fix damaged roads, surfaces, or lanes.","zh":"roadway repairs 指修復受損道路、路面或行車線的保養工作。"},{"en":"A city may schedule roadway repairs after heavy rain creates potholes.","zh":"大雨造成路洞後，城市可能安排道路維修。"},{"en":"If fewer vehicles use the roads, wear and tear may fall and repairs may be needed less often.","zh":"如果較少車輛使用道路，磨損可能下降，維修可能較少需要。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to fixing roads, not repairing vehicles.","zh":"這個短語指修理道路，而不是修理車輛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"urban heating","meaning":"城市熱效應","examples":[{"en":"Lower office use may also reduce urban heating.","zh":"較低辦公室使用也可能減少城市熱效應。"},{"en":"Urban heating is the warming effect created in cities by buildings, roads, vehicles, and energy use.","zh":"urban heating 指建築物、道路、車輛和能源使用在城市中造成的升溫效應。"},{"en":"A city centre may feel hotter than nearby countryside because of urban heating.","zh":"市中心可能因城市熱效應而比附近鄉郊感覺更熱。"},{"en":"If offices use less energy and fewer cars enter the city, heat released into urban areas may decrease.","zh":"如果辦公室用較少能源、較少汽車進入城市，釋放到市區的熱量可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to city-level heat, not heating one room.","zh":"這個短語指城市層面的熱，而不是加熱一個房間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"office construction","meaning":"辦公室建設","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking could reduce demand for new office construction.","zh":"遙距工作可能減少對新辦公室建設的需求。"},{"en":"Office construction is the building of new workplaces, office towers, or business premises.","zh":"office construction 指建造新工作場所、辦公大樓或商業處所。"},{"en":"A city may see less office construction if companies keep more staff working from home.","zh":"如果公司讓更多員工在家工作，城市可能出現較少辦公室建設。"},{"en":"Reduced office construction can save materials, energy, and land.","zh":"減少辦公室建設可以節省物料、能源和土地。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to building offices, not ordinary office work.","zh":"這個短語指建造辦公室，而不是普通辦公工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"business travel","meaning":"公幹","examples":[{"en":"Online meetings can reduce business travel.","zh":"網上會議可以減少公幹。"},{"en":"Business travel is travel done for work purposes, such as meetings, conferences, or client visits.","zh":"business travel 指為工作目的而出行，例如開會、出席會議或拜訪客戶。"},{"en":"A manager may take business travel to visit a branch office in another city.","zh":"經理可能因公幹前往另一城市探訪分公司。"},{"en":"If video calls replace some trips, companies can save money and reduce emissions.","zh":"如果視像通話取代部分旅程，公司可以節省金錢並減少排放。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to work-related travel, not holidays.","zh":"這個短語指與工作有關的出行，而不是假期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"paper usage","meaning":"紙張使用量","examples":[{"en":"Electronic documents can significantly reduce paper usage.","zh":"電子文件可以顯著減少紙張使用量。"},{"en":"Paper usage is the amount of paper used for printing, forms, notes, and records.","zh":"paper usage 指列印、表格、筆記和記錄所使用的紙張數量。"},{"en":"A school can reduce paper usage by letting students submit homework online.","zh":"學校可以透過讓學生網上交功課來減少紙張使用量。"},{"en":"Less paper usage can lower costs and reduce waste.","zh":"較少紙張使用量可以降低成本並減少浪費。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on paper consumption.","zh":"這個短語重點是紙張消耗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"electronic documents","meaning":"電子文件","examples":[{"en":"Electronic documents are increasingly replacing printed paperwork.","zh":"電子文件正越來越多地取代印刷文件。"},{"en":"Electronic documents are files stored and shared digitally rather than printed on paper.","zh":"electronic documents 指以數碼方式儲存和分享，而不是印在紙上的文件。"},{"en":"A teacher may send electronic documents to students before a lesson.","zh":"老師可能在上課前向學生發送電子文件。"},{"en":"Using electronic documents can reduce printing, storage space, and paper waste.","zh":"使用電子文件可以減少列印、儲存空間和紙張浪費。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to digital files such as PDFs, forms, or shared documents.","zh":"這個短語指 PDF、表格或共享文件等數碼檔案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"replace paper","meaning":"取代紙張","examples":[{"en":"Digital records can replace paper in many office processes.","zh":"數碼記錄可以在許多辦公流程中取代紙張。"},{"en":"To replace paper means to use digital tools or other methods instead of printed documents.","zh":"replace paper 指使用數碼工具或其他方法代替印刷文件。"},{"en":"A clinic may replace paper forms with online patient records.","zh":"診所可能用網上病人記錄取代紙本表格。"},{"en":"Replacing paper can save storage space and make documents easier to search.","zh":"取代紙張可以節省儲存空間，並令文件更容易搜尋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing from physical documents to non-paper systems.","zh":"這個短語描述由實體文件轉向非紙本系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"energy utilisation","meaning":"能源使用","examples":[{"en":"Energy utilisation will continue to grow as industries expand.","zh":"隨着產業擴展，能源使用將繼續增長。"},{"en":"Energy utilisation is the use of electricity, fuel, gas, or other forms of energy.","zh":"energy utilisation 指電力、燃料、氣體或其他能源形式的使用。"},{"en":"A factory’s energy utilisation may rise when it adds more machines.","zh":"工廠增加更多機器時，能源使用可能上升。"},{"en":"Higher energy use can increase costs and environmental impact if efficiency does not improve.","zh":"如果效率沒有提高，較高能源使用可以增加成本和環境影響。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how much energy is used.","zh":"這個短語重點是使用多少能源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"continue to grow","meaning":"持續增長","examples":[{"en":"Energy demand will continue to grow as economies develop.","zh":"隨着經濟發展，能源需求將持續增長。"},{"en":"To continue to grow means to keep increasing over time.","zh":"continue to grow 指隨時間繼續增加。"},{"en":"A student’s vocabulary will continue to grow if she reads and reviews words every day.","zh":"如果學生每天閱讀和複習詞語，她的詞彙量會持續增長。"},{"en":"When industries expand, demand for energy, workers, and materials may keep rising.","zh":"當產業擴張，對能源、工人和物料的需求可能持續上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ongoing increase rather than a single rise.","zh":"這個短語描述持續增加，而不是一次性上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"expand an industry","meaning":"擴展產業","examples":[{"en":"Countries often use more energy as they expand their industries.","zh":"國家在擴展產業時，通常使用更多能源。"},{"en":"To expand an industry means to increase the size, output, number of businesses, or range of activities in that sector.","zh":"expand an industry 指增加某行業的規模、產量、企業數量或活動範圍。"},{"en":"A city may expand its tourism industry by building hotels and training guides.","zh":"城市可能透過建酒店和培訓導遊來擴展旅遊業。"},{"en":"Industrial expansion usually increases demand for energy, transport, and workers.","zh":"產業擴展通常增加對能源、交通和工人的需求。"},{"en":"The phrase describes economic growth within a specific field.","zh":"這個短語描述特定領域中的經濟增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"improve one’s standard of living","meaning":"提高生活水平","examples":[{"en":"Energy use often rises as societies improve their standard of living.","zh":"當社會提高生活水平時，能源使用通常上升。"},{"en":"To improve one’s standard of living means to make daily life more comfortable, healthy, or secure.","zh":"improve one’s standard of living 指令日常生活更舒適、健康或安全。"},{"en":"A family may improve its standard of living by getting safer housing and reliable electricity.","zh":"家庭可能透過獲得更安全住屋和可靠電力來提高生活水平。"},{"en":"Higher living standards often increase demand for transport, heating, cooling, and appliances.","zh":"較高生活水平通常增加對交通、暖氣、冷氣和電器的需求。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on quality of life and material conditions.","zh":"這個短語重點是生活質素和物質條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"efficient use of energy","meaning":"有效使用能源","examples":[{"en":"The efficient use of energy remains extremely important.","zh":"有效使用能源仍然極為重要。"},{"en":"Efficient use of energy means using less energy to achieve the same result or avoiding waste.","zh":"efficient use of energy 指用較少能源達到同樣結果，或避免浪費。"},{"en":"Turning off unused lights is a simple example of efficient energy use at school.","zh":"關掉不用的燈，是學校有效使用能源的簡單例子。"},{"en":"If energy is used efficiently, costs and emissions can both fall.","zh":"如果能源被有效使用，成本和排放都可以下降。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on doing more with less energy.","zh":"這個短語重點是用較少能源做更多事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be of prime importance","meaning":"極為重要","examples":[{"en":"Energy efficiency will always be of prime importance.","zh":"能源效率永遠極為重要。"},{"en":"To be of prime importance means to be extremely important or among the most important things.","zh":"be of prime importance 指極其重要或屬於最重要事項之一。"},{"en":"Safety is of prime importance when students use chemicals in a laboratory.","zh":"學生在實驗室使用化學品時，安全極為重要。"},{"en":"When resources are limited, using them efficiently becomes especially important.","zh":"當資源有限，有效率地使用它們就變得特別重要。"},{"en":"The phrase gives very strong emphasis to importance.","zh":"這個短語非常強調重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"instead of","meaning":"而非；代替","examples":[{"en":"Employees can telecommute instead of travelling to an office.","zh":"員工可以遙距辦公，而非前往辦公室。"},{"en":"Instead of means in place of or rather than something else.","zh":"instead of 指取代或而不是另一事物。"},{"en":"A student may review mistakes instead of simply rereading notes before an exam.","zh":"學生考試前可能檢討錯誤，而不是只重讀筆記。"},{"en":"Choosing one action instead of another can change time, cost, and results.","zh":"選擇一個行動代替另一個，可以改變時間、成本和結果。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly shows contrast between two options.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示兩個選項之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"conventional methods","meaning":"傳統方式","examples":[{"en":"Telecommuting can replace more conventional methods of travelling to work.","zh":"遙距辦公可以取代較傳統的上班出行方式。"},{"en":"Conventional methods are the usual, traditional, or widely accepted ways of doing something.","zh":"conventional methods 指做某事的通常、傳統或廣泛接受的方法。"},{"en":"Writing notes by hand is a conventional method of studying vocabulary.","zh":"手寫筆記是學習詞彙的傳統方式。"},{"en":"New technology may replace conventional methods when it is cheaper or more convenient.","zh":"當新科技更便宜或更方便時，它可能取代傳統方式。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts familiar old methods with newer alternatives.","zh":"這個短語把熟悉舊方法與較新替代方案作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"great potential to","meaning":"有很大潛力去……","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking has great potential to save energy.","zh":"遙距工作有很大潛力節省能源。"},{"en":"Great potential to do something means a strong possibility of producing a good result.","zh":"great potential to do something 指有很大可能產生好結果。"},{"en":"Online tutoring has great potential to help students in remote areas.","zh":"網上補習有很大潛力幫助偏遠地區學生。"},{"en":"Potential becomes real only if the system is planned and used well.","zh":"潛力只有在系統被良好規劃和使用時才會變成現實。"},{"en":"The phrase describes promise, not guaranteed success.","zh":"這個短語描述前景，而不是保證成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"conserve energy","meaning":"節約能源","examples":[{"en":"Telecommuting can help conserve energy and fuel.","zh":"遙距辦公可以幫助節約能源和燃料。"},{"en":"To conserve energy means to save energy and avoid unnecessary use.","zh":"conserve energy 指節省能源並避免不必要使用。"},{"en":"A family can conserve energy by using fans before turning on air conditioning.","zh":"家庭可以先使用風扇再開冷氣，以節約能源。"},{"en":"Conserving energy can reduce bills and lower environmental impact.","zh":"節約能源可以減少帳單並降低環境影響。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on careful use rather than complete non-use.","zh":"這個短語重點是謹慎使用，而不是完全不用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"major areas","meaning":"主要範疇","examples":[{"en":"The passage identifies three major areas where resources can be saved.","zh":"文章指出三個可以節省資源的主要範疇。"},{"en":"Major areas are important categories or parts of a topic.","zh":"major areas 指某主題中的重要類別或部分。"},{"en":"In writing improvement, grammar, structure, and examples are three major areas.","zh":"在改善寫作方面，文法、結構和例子是三個主要範疇。"},{"en":"Dividing a problem into major areas helps people plan solutions more clearly.","zh":"把問題分成主要範疇，有助人們更清楚規劃解決方法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to broad important sections, not small details.","zh":"這個短語指廣泛而重要的部分，而不是小細節。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"vehicle-related materials","meaning":"與車輛有關的物料","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking can reduce the use of vehicle-related materials and resources.","zh":"遙距工作可以減少與車輛有關的物料和資源使用。"},{"en":"Vehicle-related materials are materials used to make, maintain, or operate vehicles.","zh":"vehicle-related materials 指用於製造、保養或操作車輛的物料。"},{"en":"Rubber tyres, metal parts, engine oil, and batteries are vehicle-related materials.","zh":"橡膠輪胎、金屬零件、機油和電池都是與車輛有關的物料。"},{"en":"If fewer vehicles are needed or used, demand for these materials may fall.","zh":"如果需要或使用的車輛較少，對這些物料的需求可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase connects transport habits with material use.","zh":"這個短語把交通習慣與物料使用連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"highway-related materials","meaning":"與公路有關的物料","examples":[{"en":"Less commuting reduces demand for highway-related materials.","zh":"較少通勤會減少對與公路有關的物料的需求。"},{"en":"Highway-related materials are materials used to build, expand, repair, or maintain roads.","zh":"highway-related materials 指用於建造、擴建、修理或保養道路的物料。"},{"en":"Asphalt, concrete, road signs, and barriers are highway-related materials.","zh":"瀝青、混凝土、路牌和護欄都是與公路有關的物料。"},{"en":"If traffic falls, roads may wear out more slowly and need fewer materials for repair.","zh":"如果交通量下降，道路可能磨損得較慢，維修所需物料較少。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to resources connected with road infrastructure.","zh":"這個短語指與道路基建相關的資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"work-related materials","meaning":"與工作有關的物料","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking can also conserve work-related materials and resources.","zh":"遙距工作也可以節約與工作有關的物料和資源。"},{"en":"Work-related materials are items used for doing office or job tasks.","zh":"work-related materials 指用於辦公或工作任務的物品。"},{"en":"Paper, printer ink, folders, pens, and office furniture can be work-related materials.","zh":"紙張、打印墨水、文件夾、筆和辦公家具都可以是與工作有關的物料。"},{"en":"If documents become electronic, paper and printing materials may be used less.","zh":"如果文件變成電子化，紙張和列印物料可能使用較少。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to resources connected with daily work activities.","zh":"這個短語指與日常工作活動相關的資源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a tremendous amount of","meaning":"大量的……","examples":[{"en":"A tremendous amount of energy is used to produce transport equipment.","zh":"生產運輸設備需要大量能源。"},{"en":"A tremendous amount of something means a very large quantity of it.","zh":"a tremendous amount of something 指非常大量的某物。"},{"en":"A school festival can require a tremendous amount of planning if many classes take part.","zh":"如果許多班級參與，學校節日可能需要大量規劃。"},{"en":"When production needs a huge amount of energy, reducing demand can save many resources.","zh":"當生產需要大量能源，減少需求可以節省許多資源。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly emphasises large quantity.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調數量龐大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be required to produce","meaning":"生產……需要","examples":[{"en":"Large amounts of energy are required to produce vehicles.","zh":"生產車輛需要大量能源。"},{"en":"Be required to produce something means be needed in order to make it.","zh":"be required to produce something 指製造某物所必需。"},{"en":"Clean water and electricity are required to produce many medicines safely.","zh":"安全生產許多藥物需要乾淨水和電力。"},{"en":"If less transport equipment is produced, less energy may be required.","zh":"如果生產較少運輸設備，所需能源可能較少。"},{"en":"The phrase connects production with necessary resources.","zh":"這個短語把生產與必要資源連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"transportation equipment","meaning":"運輸設備","examples":[{"en":"Transportation equipment includes cars, buses, trains and aircraft.","zh":"運輸設備包括汽車、巴士、火車和飛機。"},{"en":"Transportation equipment is machinery or vehicles used to move people or goods.","zh":"transportation equipment 指用來運送人或貨物的機械或車輛。"},{"en":"A delivery company depends on transportation equipment such as vans and lorries.","zh":"送貨公司依賴客貨車和貨車等運輸設備。"},{"en":"Producing and maintaining transport equipment uses energy and raw materials.","zh":"生產和保養運輸設備會使用能源和原材料。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the tools and vehicles used for transport.","zh":"這個短語指用於運輸的工具和車輛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"automobiles","meaning":"汽車","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturing automobiles requires considerable energy and resources.","zh":"製造汽車需要相當多能源和資源。"},{"en":"Automobiles are cars or motor vehicles used mainly for road travel.","zh":"automobiles 指主要用於道路出行的汽車或機動車輛。"},{"en":"Many families depend on automobiles when public transport is limited.","zh":"當公共交通有限，許多家庭依賴汽車。"},{"en":"If fewer people commute by car, demand for automobiles and fuel may decrease.","zh":"如果較少人開車通勤，對汽車和燃料的需求可能下降。"},{"en":"The word is formal and means cars.","zh":"這個詞較正式，意思是 cars。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"jet aircraft","meaning":"噴射客機","examples":[{"en":"Jet aircraft require substantial resources to manufacture and operate.","zh":"噴射客機需要大量資源來製造和操作。"},{"en":"Jet aircraft are aeroplanes powered by jet engines.","zh":"jet aircraft 指由噴射引擎推動的飛機。"},{"en":"Airlines use jet aircraft to carry passengers across countries and oceans.","zh":"航空公司使用噴射客機把乘客運送到不同國家和橫越海洋。"},{"en":"Manufacturing and flying jet aircraft requires fuel, metals, maintenance, and skilled labour.","zh":"製造和飛行噴射客機需要燃料、金屬、維修和熟練勞工。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to aircraft used for fast air transport.","zh":"這個短語指用於快速航空運輸的飛機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"promote telecommuting","meaning":"推廣遙距辦公","examples":[{"en":"Governments and employers may promote telecommuting to reduce travel.","zh":"政府和僱主可能推廣遙距辦公以減少出行。"},{"en":"To promote telecommuting means to encourage or support remote working arrangements.","zh":"promote telecommuting 指鼓勵或支持遙距工作安排。"},{"en":"A company may promote telecommuting by giving staff secure laptops and clear online meeting rules.","zh":"公司可能透過提供安全手提電腦和清晰網上會議規則來推廣遙距辦公。"},{"en":"If telecommuting is promoted well, traffic and office costs may decrease.","zh":"如果遙距辦公推廣得好，交通和辦公室成本可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes actively encouraging remote work.","zh":"這個短語描述主動鼓勵遙距工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"less use of equipment","meaning":"較少使用設備","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking could lead to less use of transport equipment.","zh":"遙距工作可能導致較少使用運輸設備。"},{"en":"Less use of equipment means the equipment is operated or needed less often.","zh":"less use of equipment 指設備被操作或需要的頻率較低。"},{"en":"A school may see less use of printers after students submit assignments online.","zh":"學生網上提交功課後，學校可能較少使用打印機。"},{"en":"If transport equipment is used less, fuel, maintenance, and replacement costs may fall.","zh":"如果運輸設備使用較少，燃料、保養和更換成本可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reduced dependence on physical tools or machines.","zh":"這個短語描述對實體工具或機器的依賴減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be required for production","meaning":"生產……所需","examples":[{"en":"Less energy would be required for vehicle production.","zh":"車輛生產所需能源會較少。"},{"en":"Be required for production means be needed to make goods or equipment.","zh":"be required for production 指製造貨品或設備所需要。"},{"en":"Clean rooms are required for production of sensitive electronic parts.","zh":"生產敏感電子零件需要潔淨室。"},{"en":"If fewer products are made, fewer materials and less energy may be required for production.","zh":"如果製造較少產品，生產所需物料和能源可能較少。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies what manufacturing depends on.","zh":"這個短語指出製造依賴甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"maintenance and repair","meaning":"保養和維修","examples":[{"en":"Vehicles consume energy during production, maintenance and repair.","zh":"車輛在生產、保養和維修期間消耗能源。"},{"en":"Maintenance and repair are the regular care and fixing needed to keep equipment working.","zh":"maintenance and repair 指保持設備運作所需的定期照顧和修理。"},{"en":"A school computer room needs maintenance and repair when keyboards break or software fails.","zh":"當鍵盤損壞或軟件故障，學校電腦室需要保養和維修。"},{"en":"Regular maintenance can prevent expensive repairs later.","zh":"定期保養可以防止日後昂貴維修。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both routine care and fixing problems.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋日常照顧和修理問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fuel resources","meaning":"燃料資源","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking can reduce the consumption of fuel resources.","zh":"遙距工作可以減少燃料資源消耗。"},{"en":"Fuel resources are energy sources such as petrol, diesel, gas, or other fuels.","zh":"fuel resources 指汽油、柴油、氣體或其他燃料等能源來源。"},{"en":"A bus company uses fuel resources every day to operate its vehicles.","zh":"巴士公司每天使用燃料資源來操作車輛。"},{"en":"If commuting decreases, less petrol and diesel may be consumed.","zh":"如果通勤減少，汽油和柴油消耗可能較少。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to fuels used for transport, heating, or power.","zh":"這個短語指用於交通、供暖或供電的燃料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"gases needed to operate","meaning":"操作……所需的氣體燃料","examples":[{"en":"Fewer gases would be needed to operate transport equipment.","zh":"操作運輸設備所需的氣體燃料會較少。"},{"en":"Gases needed to operate equipment are fuel gases used to make machines run.","zh":"gases needed to operate equipment 指令機器運作所用的燃料氣體。"},{"en":"A factory may need gas to operate heating systems and some machinery.","zh":"工廠可能需要氣體燃料來操作供暖系統和某些機械。"},{"en":"If machines are used less often, the fuel gases needed to operate them may also decrease.","zh":"如果機器使用頻率較低，操作它們所需的氣體燃料也可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase links equipment use with fuel demand.","zh":"這個短語把設備使用與燃料需求連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"operate equipment","meaning":"操作設備","examples":[{"en":"Fuel is needed to operate most conventional transport equipment.","zh":"大多數傳統運輸設備需要燃料來操作。"},{"en":"To operate equipment means to run, control, or use machines or tools.","zh":"operate equipment 指運行、控制或使用機器或工具。"},{"en":"A technician must know how to operate equipment safely in a school laboratory.","zh":"技術員必須知道如何在學校實驗室安全操作設備。"},{"en":"Operating heavy equipment usually requires training because mistakes can be dangerous.","zh":"操作重型設備通常需要培訓，因為錯誤可能危險。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on using machinery, not owning it.","zh":"這個短語重點是使用機械，而不是擁有它。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"build and maintain highways","meaning":"興建和保養公路","examples":[{"en":"Considerable energy is needed to build and maintain highways.","zh":"興建和保養公路需要相當多能源。"},{"en":"To build and maintain highways means to construct roads and keep them safe and usable.","zh":"build and maintain highways 指建造道路並保持其安全和可使用。"},{"en":"A government may build and maintain highways so goods can move between cities.","zh":"政府可能興建和保養公路，讓貨物能在城市之間運送。"},{"en":"More traffic can increase the need to repair road surfaces and expand lanes.","zh":"更多交通可以增加修補路面和擴闊行車線的需要。"},{"en":"The phrase includes both creating roads and looking after them.","zh":"這個短語包括創造道路和照顧道路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a great deal of energy","meaning":"大量能源","examples":[{"en":"Highway construction requires a great deal of energy.","zh":"公路建設需要大量能源。"},{"en":"A great deal of energy means a large amount of energy.","zh":"a great deal of energy 指大量能源。"},{"en":"A large hospital uses a great deal of energy for lights, machines, heating, and cooling.","zh":"大型醫院為照明、機器、暖氣和冷氣使用大量能源。"},{"en":"Activities requiring a lot of energy usually have higher costs and environmental impacts.","zh":"需要大量能源的活動通常成本和環境影響較高。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly emphasises energy quantity.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調能源數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"construction equipment","meaning":"建築設備","examples":[{"en":"Energy is required to operate construction equipment.","zh":"操作建築設備需要能源。"},{"en":"Construction equipment is machinery used for building, digging, lifting, or road work.","zh":"construction equipment 指用於建造、挖掘、吊運或道路工程的機械。"},{"en":"Cranes, bulldozers, and concrete mixers are examples of construction equipment.","zh":"起重機、推土機和混凝土攪拌車都是建築設備例子。"},{"en":"Heavy construction equipment uses fuel and needs regular maintenance.","zh":"重型建築設備使用燃料，也需要定期保養。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to machines used on building sites.","zh":"這個短語指建築工地使用的機器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"manufacture and transport materials","meaning":"生產和運送物料","examples":[{"en":"Companies use energy to manufacture and transport construction materials.","zh":"公司使用能源來生產和運送建築物料。"},{"en":"To manufacture and transport materials means to make materials and move them to where they are needed.","zh":"manufacture and transport materials 指製造物料並把它們運到需要的地方。"},{"en":"A furniture company must manufacture wood panels and transport them to shops.","zh":"家具公司必須生產木板，並把它們運送到商店。"},{"en":"Both production and transport use energy, so reducing demand can save resources twice.","zh":"生產和運送都使用能源，所以減少需求可以在兩方面節省資源。"},{"en":"The phrase covers making goods and delivering them.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋製造貨品和運送貨品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"an increase in the percentage of","meaning":"……比例的上升","examples":[{"en":"An increase in the percentage of telecommuters could reduce traffic.","zh":"遙距辦公者比例上升可以減少交通。"},{"en":"An increase in the percentage of a group means that group forms a larger share of the total.","zh":"an increase in the percentage of a group 指該群體在總數中所佔比例變大。"},{"en":"An increase in the percentage of students cycling to school can reduce congestion at the gate.","zh":"騎單車上學學生比例上升，可以減少校門口擠塞。"},{"en":"If the share of telecommuters rises, fewer people may commute during rush hour.","zh":"如果遙距辦公者比例上升，繁忙時間通勤人數可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on proportion, not only absolute number.","zh":"這個短語重點是比例，而不只是絕對數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"decrease the need for","meaning":"減少對……的需要","examples":[{"en":"More teleworking would decrease the need for expanded highways.","zh":"更多遙距工作會減少對擴建公路的需要。"},{"en":"To decrease the need for something means to make it less necessary.","zh":"decrease the need for something 指令某事變得較不必要。"},{"en":"Online forms can decrease the need for paper storage in a school office.","zh":"網上表格可以減少學校辦公室對紙本儲存的需要。"},{"en":"If traffic falls, governments may not need to widen roads as urgently.","zh":"如果交通量下降，政府可能不再那麼迫切需要擴闊道路。"},{"en":"The phrase links a change with reduced demand.","zh":"這個短語把某變化與需求下降連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"expanded highways","meaning":"擴建公路","examples":[{"en":"Lower commuter traffic could reduce demand for expanded highways.","zh":"較低通勤交通量可以減少對擴建公路的需求。"},{"en":"Expanded highways are roads that have been widened or extended to carry more traffic.","zh":"expanded highways 指被加闊或延長，以承載更多交通的道路。"},{"en":"A city may build expanded highways when existing roads become too crowded.","zh":"當現有道路太擠塞，城市可能建造擴建公路。"},{"en":"If fewer people commute, road expansion may be less necessary.","zh":"如果較少人通勤，道路擴建可能較不必要。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to larger road capacity.","zh":"這個短語指更大的道路容量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"associated road maintenance","meaning":"相關道路保養","examples":[{"en":"Reduced traffic may also lower associated road-maintenance costs.","zh":"交通減少也可能降低相關道路保養成本。"},{"en":"Associated road maintenance is the repair and upkeep connected with road use.","zh":"associated road maintenance 指與道路使用相關的維修和保養。"},{"en":"A town with heavy lorry traffic may face high associated road-maintenance costs.","zh":"有大量貨車交通的小鎮可能面對高昂相關道路保養成本。"},{"en":"When road use falls, surfaces may wear out more slowly and maintenance costs may decrease.","zh":"當道路使用下降，路面可能磨損較慢，保養成本可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase links road upkeep with the activity that causes it.","zh":"這個短語把道路保養與造成它的活動連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be related to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The first two categories are related to travelling to work.","zh":"前兩個類別與上班出行有關。"},{"en":"To be related to something means to have a connection with it.","zh":"be related to something 指與某事有聯繫。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be related to late-night phone use.","zh":"學生疲倦可能與深夜使用手機有關。"},{"en":"If two resource categories are related to commuting, reducing commuting may affect both.","zh":"如果兩個資源類別都與通勤有關，減少通勤可能同時影響兩者。"},{"en":"The phrase shows connection, not always direct cause.","zh":"這個短語顯示關聯，不一定是直接因果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"socially","meaning":"從社會層面來看","examples":[{"en":"Socially, many respondents reported a better quality of life.","zh":"從社會層面來看，許多受訪者表示生活質素更好。"},{"en":"Socially means from the point of view of people’s lives, relationships, and communities.","zh":"socially 指從人們生活、關係和社區的角度看。"},{"en":"Socially, a school club can help shy students make friends.","zh":"從社會層面來看，學校學會可以幫助害羞學生交朋友。"},{"en":"A policy may save money economically but create problems socially if people feel isolated.","zh":"一項政策在經濟上可能省錢，但如果令人感到孤立，在社會層面可能造成問題。"},{"en":"The word introduces the social side of an issue.","zh":"這個詞引入議題的社會面向。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"survey respondents","meaning":"調查受訪者","examples":[{"en":"Most survey respondents believed teleworking improved their lives.","zh":"大多數調查受訪者相信遙距工作改善了他們的生活。"},{"en":"Survey respondents are people who answer a survey’s questions.","zh":"survey respondents 指回答調查問題的人。"},{"en":"Survey respondents in a workplace study may describe stress, productivity, and job satisfaction.","zh":"職場研究中的調查受訪者可能描述壓力、生產力和工作滿意度。"},{"en":"Their answers help researchers understand how a policy affects real people.","zh":"他們的答案幫助研究人員理解政策如何影響真人。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the people providing survey data.","zh":"這個短語指提供調查數據的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"better quality of life","meaning":"更佳生活質素","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking gave many respondents a better quality of life.","zh":"遙距工作令許多受訪者有更佳生活質素。"},{"en":"Better quality of life means daily life becomes healthier, easier, happier, or more balanced.","zh":"better quality of life 指日常生活變得更健康、更容易、更快樂或更平衡。"},{"en":"A shorter commute can give a worker a better quality of life by leaving more time for family.","zh":"較短通勤可以為員工帶來更佳生活質素，因為有更多時間陪家人。"},{"en":"If people have more control over their time, stress may fall and life may feel better.","zh":"如果人們對時間有更大控制，壓力可能下降，生活可能感覺更好。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to overall well-being, not only income.","zh":"這個短語指整體幸福感，而不只是收入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"work-life balance","meaning":"工作與生活平衡","examples":[{"en":"Flexible working can improve work-life balance.","zh":"彈性工作可以改善工作與生活平衡。"},{"en":"Work-life balance is the ability to manage job responsibilities and personal life without one destroying the other.","zh":"work-life balance 指能夠管理工作責任和個人生活，而不讓其中一方摧毀另一方。"},{"en":"A parent has better work-life balance if she can finish work and still attend her child’s school event.","zh":"如果家長能完成工作又參加孩子的學校活動，她就有較好的工作與生活平衡。"},{"en":"Poor balance can lead to stress, tiredness, and family conflict.","zh":"平衡差可以導致壓力、疲倦和家庭衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the relationship between work and personal time.","zh":"這個短語重點是工作與私人時間之間的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"report health benefits","meaning":"表示有健康益處","examples":[{"en":"Many teleworkers reported health benefits.","zh":"許多遙距工作者表示有健康益處。"},{"en":"To report health benefits means to say that one has experienced improvements in health or well-being.","zh":"report health benefits 指說自己經歷了健康或身心狀態改善。"},{"en":"Students may report health benefits after a school introduces longer lunch breaks and less homework.","zh":"學校引入較長午飯時間和較少功課後，學生可能表示有健康益處。"},{"en":"If people sleep more and commute less, they may feel less tired and stressed.","zh":"如果人們睡得更多、通勤較少，他們可能感到較少疲倦和壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes people stating positive health effects.","zh":"這個短語描述人們表示有正面健康效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a significant number","meaning":"相當數目的……","examples":[{"en":"A significant number of respondents used more local services.","zh":"相當數目的受訪者使用更多本區服務。"},{"en":"A significant number means a large enough number to be important or worth noticing.","zh":"a significant number 指大到重要或值得注意的數量。"},{"en":"A significant number of students may need extra help if many fail the same test.","zh":"如果許多學生同一測驗不合格，相當數目的學生可能需要額外幫助。"},{"en":"When many people change behaviour, local businesses and services can be affected.","zh":"當許多人改變行為，本地企業和服務可能受到影響。"},{"en":"The phrase does not give an exact number but signals importance.","zh":"這個短語沒有給出精確數字，但表示重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"use local services","meaning":"使用本區服務","examples":[{"en":"Home-based employees may use local services more frequently.","zh":"在家工作的員工可能更頻繁使用本區服務。"},{"en":"To use local services means to buy from or visit services in one’s nearby community.","zh":"use local services 指購買或使用附近社區的服務。"},{"en":"A worker at home may use local cafés, pharmacies, gyms, and post offices during breaks.","zh":"在家工作的員工可能在休息時間使用本地咖啡店、藥房、健身室和郵局。"},{"en":"More use of local services can support neighbourhood businesses.","zh":"更多使用本區服務可以支持社區企業。"},{"en":"The phrase connects daily habits with community economies.","zh":"這個短語把日常習慣與社區經濟連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"become involved in","meaning":"更積極參與……","examples":[{"en":"Teleworkers may become more involved in their local communities.","zh":"遙距工作者可能更積極參與本地社區。"},{"en":"To become involved in something means to take part in it more actively.","zh":"become involved in something 指更主動參與某事。"},{"en":"A parent may become involved in school activities after working closer to home.","zh":"家長在離家較近工作後，可能更積極參與學校活動。"},{"en":"If people spend more time in their neighbourhood, they may join local groups or events.","zh":"如果人們在社區中花更多時間，他們可能加入本地團體或活動。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests participation, not just living nearby.","zh":"這個短語暗示參與，而不只是住在附近。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"local communities","meaning":"本地社區","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking can strengthen involvement in local communities.","zh":"遙距工作可以加強人們對本地社區的參與。"},{"en":"Local communities are groups of people living in the same neighbourhood or area.","zh":"local communities 指生活在同一鄰里或地區的人群。"},{"en":"Local communities may share schools, shops, parks, clinics, and public spaces.","zh":"本地社區可能共享學校、商店、公園、診所和公共空間。"},{"en":"When people spend more time locally, they may build stronger community ties.","zh":"當人們在本區花更多時間，他們可能建立更強社區連繫。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to nearby social life, not the whole country.","zh":"這個短語指附近社會生活，而不是整個國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"loss of teamwork","meaning":"團隊合作減少","examples":[{"en":"The loss of teamwork is a possible disadvantage of teleworking.","zh":"團隊合作減少是遙距工作的可能缺點。"},{"en":"Loss of teamwork means a reduction in cooperation, shared effort, and group spirit.","zh":"loss of teamwork 指合作、共同努力和團隊精神下降。"},{"en":"A class project may suffer a loss of teamwork if students never meet or discuss their roles.","zh":"如果學生從不見面或討論角色，班級項目可能出現團隊合作減少。"},{"en":"If remote workers communicate poorly, projects may become slower and less creative.","zh":"如果遙距工作者溝通差，項目可能變慢且創意下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes weakened cooperation.","zh":"這個短語描述合作變弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"team spirit","meaning":"團隊精神","examples":[{"en":"Employers may need to protect team spirit among remote workers.","zh":"僱主可能需要保護遙距工作者之間的團隊精神。"},{"en":"Team spirit is the feeling of cooperation, shared purpose, and support within a group.","zh":"team spirit 指群體中的合作感、共同目標和支持感。"},{"en":"A sports team with strong team spirit encourages weaker players instead of blaming them.","zh":"有強團隊精神的運動隊會鼓勵較弱隊員，而不是責怪他們。"},{"en":"If people work apart for too long, team spirit may weaken unless communication is planned.","zh":"如果人們分開工作太久，除非有計劃地溝通，團隊精神可能削弱。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to group morale and unity.","zh":"這個短語指團體士氣和凝聚力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"teleworking populations","meaning":"遙距工作群體","examples":[{"en":"The company studied teamwork within teleworking populations.","zh":"該公司研究遙距工作群體中的團隊合作。"},{"en":"Teleworking populations are groups of employees or workers who work remotely.","zh":"teleworking populations 指遙距工作的員工或工作者群體。"},{"en":"A large firm may compare communication patterns in office staff and teleworking populations.","zh":"大公司可能比較辦公室員工和遙距工作群體的溝通模式。"},{"en":"Studying remote-worker groups helps managers understand isolation, productivity, and teamwork.","zh":"研究遙距工作者群體幫助管理者理解孤立感、生產力和團隊合作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a group of teleworkers, not a national population.","zh":"這個短語指遙距工作者群體，而不是國家人口。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tackle a problem through","meaning":"透過……處理問題","examples":[{"en":"Oracle tackled communication problems through redesigned offices.","zh":"Oracle 透過重新設計辦公室處理溝通問題。"},{"en":"To tackle a problem through something means to deal with the problem by using that method.","zh":"tackle a problem through something 指使用某方法處理問題。"},{"en":"A school may tackle lateness through earlier bus arrangements and clearer attendance rules.","zh":"學校可能透過較早巴士安排和更清楚出席規則來處理遲到問題。"},{"en":"Choosing the right method can make a difficult problem easier to manage.","zh":"選擇合適方法可以令困難問題較容易處理。"},{"en":"The phrase links a problem with the approach used to solve it.","zh":"這個短語把問題與用來解決它的方法連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"functional offices","meaning":"多功能趣味辦公室","examples":[{"en":"Oracle developed “FUNctional” offices to encourage interaction.","zh":"Oracle 發展「FUNctional」辦公室以鼓勵互動。"},{"en":"Functional offices are offices designed to support work needs effectively; here the spelling also suggests fun.","zh":"functional offices 指被設計來有效支援工作需要的辦公室；此處串法也暗示 fun。"},{"en":"A functional office may include quiet rooms, meeting areas, and shared spaces for informal discussion.","zh":"多功能辦公室可能包括安靜房間、會議區和非正式討論共享空間。"},{"en":"If an office is designed well, it can make teamwork easier when remote staff visit.","zh":"如果辦公室設計良好，遙距員工回來時可以更容易合作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical office design, with a playful meaning in this context.","zh":"這個短語指實用辦公室設計，在此語境也帶玩味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be designed to","meaning":"被設計用來……","examples":[{"en":"The offices were designed to increase communication.","zh":"這些辦公室被設計用來增加溝通。"},{"en":"Be designed to means be planned or created for a particular purpose.","zh":"be designed to 指為某特定目的而規劃或創造。"},{"en":"A school timetable may be designed to give students breaks between difficult lessons.","zh":"學校時間表可能被設計用來讓學生在困難課堂之間休息。"},{"en":"If a space is designed to encourage conversation, people may meet and share ideas more often.","zh":"如果空間被設計用來鼓勵對話，人們可能更常見面和分享想法。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the purpose behind a design.","zh":"這個短語解釋設計背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"increase communication and interaction","meaning":"增加溝通和互動","examples":[{"en":"The new office design aimed to increase communication and interaction.","zh":"新辦公室設計旨在增加溝通和互動。"},{"en":"To increase communication and interaction means to make people talk, share ideas, and work together more often.","zh":"increase communication and interaction 指令人更常交談、分享想法和合作。"},{"en":"A teacher may arrange desks in groups to increase communication and interaction among students.","zh":"老師可能把桌子排成小組，以增加學生之間的溝通和互動。"},{"en":"More interaction can reduce isolation and strengthen teamwork.","zh":"更多互動可以減少孤立感並加強團隊合作。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on improving contact between people.","zh":"這個短語重點是改善人與人之間的接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"when people are at the office","meaning":"當人們在辦公室時","examples":[{"en":"The space encourages interaction when employees are at the office.","zh":"當員工在辦公室時，該空間鼓勵互動。"},{"en":"When people are at the office means during the time they are physically present in the workplace.","zh":"when people are at the office 指在人們實際身處工作場所的時間。"},{"en":"Team meetings may be scheduled when people are at the office rather than working from home.","zh":"團隊會議可能安排在大家在辦公室時，而不是在家工作時。"},{"en":"If remote workers visit the office only sometimes, those visits should be used for collaboration.","zh":"如果遙距工作者只偶爾回辦公室，那些日子應用於合作。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts office presence with remote work.","zh":"這個短語把在辦公室出現與遙距工作作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be focused around","meaning":"圍繞……設計","examples":[{"en":"The offices are focused around a central café.","zh":"這些辦公室圍繞中央咖啡區設計。"},{"en":"Be focused around something means be organised with that thing as the centre or main feature.","zh":"be focused around something 指以某物為中心或主要特色來組織。"},{"en":"A school festival may be focused around student performances in the main hall.","zh":"學校節日可能圍繞禮堂中的學生表演來安排。"},{"en":"If an office is focused around a café, people may meet informally and exchange ideas.","zh":"如果辦公室圍繞咖啡區設計，人們可能非正式見面並交換想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the central organising point of a place or plan.","zh":"這個短語描述某地方或計劃的中心組織點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"central café","meaning":"中央咖啡區","examples":[{"en":"The office includes a central café for informal meetings.","zh":"辦公室包括一個用於非正式會面的中央咖啡區。"},{"en":"A central café is a shared café area placed at the centre of a workplace or building.","zh":"central café 指設於工作場所或建築物中心的共享咖啡區。"},{"en":"A company may use a central café to encourage staff from different departments to meet.","zh":"公司可能使用中央咖啡區，鼓勵不同部門員工見面。"},{"en":"Informal spaces can create conversations that do not happen in formal meeting rooms.","zh":"非正式空間可以創造正式會議室中不會發生的對話。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a social meeting point inside an office.","zh":"這個短語指辦公室內的社交會面點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stimulate ideas","meaning":"激發意念","examples":[{"en":"Informal meeting spaces can stimulate ideas.","zh":"非正式會面空間可以激發意念。"},{"en":"To stimulate ideas means to encourage people to think creatively or produce new thoughts.","zh":"stimulate ideas 指鼓勵人創意思考或產生新想法。"},{"en":"A teacher may stimulate ideas by showing students an unusual picture before writing.","zh":"老師可能在寫作前展示一張不尋常圖片來激發學生意念。"},{"en":"Casual conversation can lead to new solutions because people speak more freely.","zh":"隨意對話可以帶來新解決方法，因為人們說話更自由。"},{"en":"The phrase describes encouraging fresh thinking.","zh":"這個短語描述鼓勵新思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"face-to-face contact","meaning":"面對面接觸","examples":[{"en":"Shared offices encourage face-to-face contact.","zh":"共享辦公室鼓勵面對面接觸。"},{"en":"Face-to-face contact is direct contact between people who are physically in the same place.","zh":"face-to-face contact 指身處同一地方的人之間的直接接觸。"},{"en":"A teacher may prefer face-to-face contact when giving sensitive feedback to a student.","zh":"老師給學生敏感回饋時，可能較喜歡面對面接觸。"},{"en":"Direct contact can build trust and reduce misunderstandings that online messages create.","zh":"直接接觸可以建立信任，並減少網上訊息造成的誤會。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts in-person communication with remote communication.","zh":"這個短語把親身溝通與遙距溝通作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"paradoxical","meaning":"看似矛盾的","examples":[{"en":"Longer working hours combined with a better life may seem paradoxical.","zh":"較長工時同時帶來更好生活，可能看似矛盾。"},{"en":"Paradoxical means seeming contradictory because two things appear unlikely to be true together.","zh":"paradoxical 指看似自相矛盾，因為兩件事似乎不可能同時成立。"},{"en":"It may seem paradoxical that a strict routine can make a student feel freer.","zh":"嚴格規律反而令學生感覺更自由，這可能看似矛盾。"},{"en":"A situation can look contradictory until the hidden explanation becomes clear.","zh":"情況可能看似矛盾，直到隱藏解釋變得清楚。"},{"en":"The word describes something that sounds opposite to common expectation.","zh":"這個詞描述聽起來與一般預期相反的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"report both…and…","meaning":"同時表示……和……","examples":[{"en":"Many teleworkers report both longer hours and a better quality of life.","zh":"許多遙距工作者同時表示工時較長和生活質素更好。"},{"en":"Report both…and… means state that two things are true at the same time.","zh":"report both…and… 指表示兩件事同時成立。"},{"en":"Some students report both more homework and better exam confidence after a new course.","zh":"一些學生在新課程後同時表示功課更多和考試信心更高。"},{"en":"When two results seem to conflict, the writer may need to explain how both can happen.","zh":"當兩個結果看似衝突，作者可能需要解釋兩者如何同時發生。"},{"en":"The phrase presents two reported outcomes together.","zh":"這個短語把兩個被報告的結果一起呈現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be associated with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Long working hours are usually associated with increased stress.","zh":"長工時通常與壓力增加有關。"},{"en":"To be associated with something means to be connected with it in people’s experience or research.","zh":"be associated with something 指在經驗或研究中與某事有聯繫。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is often associated with weaker concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足常與課堂專注力較弱有關。"},{"en":"If two things are associated, one may occur with the other, but that does not always prove direct cause.","zh":"如果兩件事有關，一件可能伴隨另一件出現，但不一定證明直接因果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes connection or relationship.","zh":"這個短語描述聯繫或關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"increased stress","meaning":"壓力增加","examples":[{"en":"Longer hours often result in increased stress.","zh":"較長工時通常導致壓力增加。"},{"en":"Increased stress means a higher level of mental or physical pressure.","zh":"increased stress 指心理或身體壓力水平上升。"},{"en":"A student may feel increased stress when several deadlines fall in the same week.","zh":"當幾個限期落在同一星期，學生可能感到壓力增加。"},{"en":"Too much stress can affect sleep, patience, health, and work quality.","zh":"太多壓力可以影響睡眠、耐性、健康和工作質素。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stress becoming stronger or more frequent.","zh":"這個短語描述壓力變得更強或更頻繁。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"domestic tension","meaning":"家庭關係緊張","examples":[{"en":"Excessive working hours can create domestic tension.","zh":"過長工時可以造成家庭關係緊張。"},{"en":"Domestic tension is stress or conflict inside the home or family.","zh":"domestic tension 指家庭或家居內部的壓力或衝突。"},{"en":"A parent working late every night may create domestic tension if family duties are ignored.","zh":"如果家長每晚工作到很晚而忽視家庭責任，可能造成家庭關係緊張。"},{"en":"When work takes over home life, arguments and resentment may increase.","zh":"當工作佔據家庭生活，爭吵和怨氣可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to household conflict, not international affairs.","zh":"這個短語指家庭衝突，而不是國際事務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"reduce quality of life","meaning":"降低生活質素","examples":[{"en":"Stress and tension can reduce quality of life.","zh":"壓力和緊張可以降低生活質素。"},{"en":"To reduce quality of life means to make daily life less healthy, comfortable, happy, or satisfying.","zh":"reduce quality of life 指令日常生活較不健康、舒適、快樂或滿足。"},{"en":"Long travel times can reduce quality of life by leaving little time for rest or family.","zh":"長途出行可以因休息或家庭時間很少而降低生活質素。"},{"en":"If stress continues for months, people may sleep worse and enjoy life less.","zh":"如果壓力持續數月，人們可能睡得更差，也較少享受生活。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a decline in overall well-being.","zh":"這個短語描述整體幸福感下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"one possible explanation","meaning":"一個可能的解釋","examples":[{"en":"One possible explanation is that teleworkers save commuting time.","zh":"一個可能的解釋是遙距工作者節省了通勤時間。"},{"en":"One possible explanation is one reason that may help account for a situation.","zh":"one possible explanation 指可以幫助解釋某情況的一個原因。"},{"en":"One possible explanation for low marks is that students misunderstood the instructions.","zh":"低分的一個可能解釋是學生誤解了指示。"},{"en":"The phrase is careful because it does not claim to be the only answer.","zh":"這個短語很謹慎，因為它沒有聲稱是唯一答案。"},{"en":"It introduces a likely cause while leaving room for other causes.","zh":"它引入一個可能原因，同時保留其他原因空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for many individuals","meaning":"對很多人而言","examples":[{"en":"For many individuals, extra working time is less than the time saved.","zh":"對很多人而言，額外工作時間少於節省下來的時間。"},{"en":"For many individuals means for many separate people, not necessarily everyone.","zh":"for many individuals 指對許多個別人士而言，但不一定是所有人。"},{"en":"For many individuals, online banking is more convenient than visiting a branch.","zh":"對很多人而言，網上銀行比親身到分行更方便。"},{"en":"The phrase recognises that people’s experiences may differ.","zh":"這個短語承認人們的經驗可能不同。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing survey results without overgeneralising.","zh":"它適合用於討論調查結果而不過度概括。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"time saved in commuting","meaning":"通勤所節省的時間","examples":[{"en":"The time saved in commuting may exceed the extra time spent working.","zh":"通勤所節省的時間可能超過額外工作時間。"},{"en":"Time saved in commuting is the time people no longer spend travelling to and from work.","zh":"time saved in commuting 指人們不再花在往返工作地點上的時間。"},{"en":"A worker who stops taking a one-hour train each way saves two hours of commuting time daily.","zh":"如果員工不再每程坐一小時火車，每天就節省兩小時通勤時間。"},{"en":"Saved commuting time can be used for rest, family, exercise, or extra work.","zh":"節省下來的通勤時間可以用於休息、家庭、運動或額外工作。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the time gained by not travelling to the workplace.","zh":"這個短語重點是不前往工作場所而得到的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have more time available for","meaning":"有更多時間可用於……","examples":[{"en":"Teleworkers may have more time available for family activities.","zh":"遙距工作者可能有更多時間可用於家庭活動。"},{"en":"To have more time available for something means to have extra time that can be used for it.","zh":"have more time available for something 指有額外時間可以用於某事。"},{"en":"A student who finishes homework early has more time available for reading.","zh":"早早完成功課的學生有更多時間可用於閱讀。"},{"en":"If commuting disappears, people may use the extra time for childcare or exercise.","zh":"如果通勤消失，人們可能把額外時間用於照顧孩子或運動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes usable time becoming greater.","zh":"這個短語描述可用時間增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"family and other activities","meaning":"家庭及其他活動","examples":[{"en":"Saved commuting time can be used for family and other activities.","zh":"節省下來的通勤時間可以用於家庭及其他活動。"},{"en":"Family and other activities are non-work activities such as childcare, meals, hobbies, exercise, and community events.","zh":"family and other activities 指照顧孩子、吃飯、嗜好、運動和社區活動等非工作活動。"},{"en":"A parent may use extra time for family dinner, homework help, or a short walk.","zh":"家長可能把額外時間用於家庭晚餐、幫孩子做功課或短途散步。"},{"en":"More time for non-work activities can improve work-life balance.","zh":"更多非工作活動時間可以改善工作與生活平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts personal life with work duties.","zh":"這個短語把個人生活與工作責任作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"stress associated with","meaning":"與……相關的壓力","examples":[{"en":"The stress associated with commuting can be considerable.","zh":"與通勤相關的壓力可以相當大。"},{"en":"Stress associated with something is pressure or anxiety connected with that situation.","zh":"stress associated with something 指與某情況有關的壓力或焦慮。"},{"en":"The stress associated with exams may come from deadlines, fear, and family expectations.","zh":"與考試相關的壓力可能來自限期、恐懼和家庭期望。"},{"en":"If commuting is crowded and unpredictable, it can add stress before work even starts.","zh":"如果通勤擁擠又難預測，工作開始前已可能增加壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source linked to stress.","zh":"這個短語指出與壓力相關的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"commute long distances","meaning":"長途通勤","examples":[{"en":"Employees who commute long distances often experience high stress.","zh":"長途通勤的員工通常承受高壓力。"},{"en":"To commute long distances means to travel far between home and work regularly.","zh":"commute long distances 指定期在家和工作地點之間遠距離出行。"},{"en":"A teacher may commute long distances if she lives in one city but teaches in another.","zh":"如果老師住在一個城市但在另一城市教書，她可能長途通勤。"},{"en":"Long commutes can reduce sleep, family time, and patience.","zh":"長途通勤可以減少睡眠、家庭時間和耐性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes regular work travel over a large distance.","zh":"這個短語描述遠距離的定期上班出行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"arise from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"The extra stress may arise from additional working time.","zh":"額外壓力可能源自額外工作時間。"},{"en":"To arise from something means to be caused by or come from it.","zh":"arise from something 指由某事造成或來自某事。"},{"en":"Misunderstandings may arise from unclear instructions.","zh":"誤會可能源自不清楚的指示。"},{"en":"If extra work time replaces rest time, tiredness and stress may result.","zh":"如果額外工作時間取代休息時間，疲倦和壓力可能出現。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the source of a problem or situation.","zh":"這個短語解釋問題或情況的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"most significantly","meaning":"最重要的是","examples":[{"en":"Most significantly, teleworking gives employees greater control over their time.","zh":"最重要的是，遙距工作讓員工對時間有更大控制。"},{"en":"Most significantly means most importantly or most meaningfully.","zh":"most significantly 指最重要或最有意義的是。"},{"en":"A study plan helps students organise work; most significantly, it reduces panic before exams.","zh":"學習計劃幫助學生組織工作；最重要的是，它減少考試前恐慌。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the point the writer considers most important.","zh":"這個短語引入作者認為最重要的重點。"},{"en":"It guides readers to focus on the key effect.","zh":"它引導讀者集中於關鍵效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in effect","meaning":"實際上","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking can, in effect, create additional usable time.","zh":"遙距工作實際上可以創造額外可用時間。"},{"en":"In effect means in practice or as a real result, even if not formally stated that way.","zh":"in effect 指實際上或作為真實結果，即使不是正式如此說。"},{"en":"Shorter school days with the same learning may, in effect, give students more rest time.","zh":"如果較短上課日仍有同樣學習量，實際上可能給學生更多休息時間。"},{"en":"If saved commuting time can be used freely, it is almost like creating extra time.","zh":"如果節省下來的通勤時間可以自由使用，它幾乎等於創造額外時間。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the practical meaning of a situation.","zh":"這個短語解釋某情況的實際意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"create time","meaning":"騰出時間","examples":[{"en":"Flexible working can effectively create time for other activities.","zh":"彈性工作可以有效騰出時間做其他活動。"},{"en":"To create time means to free up time by organising tasks or removing wasted time.","zh":"create time 指透過安排任務或移除浪費時間，騰出可用時間。"},{"en":"A student can create time for exercise by planning homework earlier in the week.","zh":"學生可以透過在星期初提早安排功課，騰出時間運動。"},{"en":"If commuting is removed, the saved minutes can become time for family or rest.","zh":"如果通勤被移除，節省下來的分鐘可以變成家庭或休息時間。"},{"en":"The phrase is metaphorical because time is not made, but made available.","zh":"這個短語是比喻，因為時間不是被製造，而是被騰出來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"opportunities for multitasking","meaning":"同時處理多項工作的機會","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking creates more opportunities for multitasking.","zh":"遙距工作創造更多同時處理多項工作的機會。"},{"en":"Opportunities for multitasking are chances to handle more than one task in the same period.","zh":"opportunities for multitasking 指在同一段時間處理多於一項任務的機會。"},{"en":"A parent working from home may start laundry during a lunch break and answer emails afterwards.","zh":"在家工作的家長可能在午休時開始洗衣，之後回覆電郵。"},{"en":"Multitasking can save time, but it can also reduce focus if overdone.","zh":"同時處理多項工作可以節省時間，但過度時也可能降低專注力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to chances to combine tasks, not always doing everything well.","zh":"這個短語指結合任務的機會，不一定代表每件事都做得好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"greater control of activities","meaning":"對活動有更大控制","examples":[{"en":"Remote workers may gain greater control of their daily activities.","zh":"遙距工作者可能對日常活動有更大控制。"},{"en":"Greater control of activities means more ability to decide when and how tasks are done.","zh":"greater control of activities 指更能決定何時及如何完成任務。"},{"en":"A student has greater control of study activities when she chooses her own revision timetable.","zh":"當學生自行選擇溫習時間表，她就對學習活動有更大控制。"},{"en":"More control can reduce stress because people can match tasks to their energy and needs.","zh":"更多控制可以減少壓力，因為人們可以把任務配合自己的精力和需要。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on increased choice and flexibility.","zh":"這個短語重點是選擇和彈性增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"survey respondent","meaning":"調查受訪者","examples":[{"en":"One survey respondent explained how teleworking freed up weekends.","zh":"一位調查受訪者解釋遙距工作如何令週末更空閒。"},{"en":"A survey respondent is one person who answers questions in a survey.","zh":"survey respondent 指在調查中回答問題的一個人。"},{"en":"A survey respondent may write a short comment explaining why online lessons help or hurt learning.","zh":"調查受訪者可能寫短評，解釋網上課堂為何幫助或損害學習。"},{"en":"Individual comments can make survey statistics easier to understand.","zh":"個別評論可以令調查統計更容易理解。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a single person giving survey information.","zh":"這個短語指提供調查資訊的一名人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the amount of time","meaning":"時間的總量","examples":[{"en":"The amount of time had not changed, but it was used differently.","zh":"時間的總量沒有改變，但使用方式不同了。"},{"en":"The amount of time means how much time is available or spent.","zh":"amount of time 指可用或花費的時間有多少。"},{"en":"A student may have the same amount of time each evening but use it better with a timetable.","zh":"學生每晚可能有相同時間，但透過時間表使用得更好。"},{"en":"Changing how time is used can improve life even if total hours remain the same.","zh":"即使總小時數不變，改變時間使用方式也可以改善生活。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on quantity of time.","zh":"這個短語重點是時間數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make the weekends freer","meaning":"令週末有更多空閒時間","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking can make the weekends freer.","zh":"遙距工作可以令週末有更多空閒時間。"},{"en":"To make the weekends freer means to leave more free time on Saturdays and Sundays.","zh":"make the weekends freer 指令星期六和星期日有更多自由時間。"},{"en":"A worker who finishes household chores during weekday breaks may make the weekends freer.","zh":"在工作日休息時間完成家務的員工，可能令週末有更多空閒時間。"},{"en":"Freer weekends can improve rest, family time, and leisure.","zh":"較空閒的週末可以改善休息、家庭時間和休閒。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reducing weekend pressure by moving tasks elsewhere.","zh":"這個短語描述透過把任務移到其他時間來減少週末壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"domestic activities","meaning":"家務活動","examples":[{"en":"Domestic activities can sometimes be completed during breaks.","zh":"家務活動有時可以在休息期間完成。"},{"en":"Domestic activities are household tasks such as cooking, cleaning, laundry, and childcare.","zh":"domestic activities 指煮食、清潔、洗衣和照顧孩子等家庭任務。"},{"en":"A person working from home may do small domestic activities between meetings.","zh":"在家工作的人可能在會議之間做小型家務活動。"},{"en":"Completing small chores during the day can free up time later.","zh":"白天完成小家務可以釋放之後的時間。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to home duties, not business activities.","zh":"這個短語指家中責任，而不是商業活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be fitted in","meaning":"被安排在……進行","examples":[{"en":"Household tasks can be fitted in during lunchtime.","zh":"家務可以被安排在午膳時間進行。"},{"en":"To be fitted in means to be arranged within a busy schedule.","zh":"be fitted in 指被安排進繁忙時間表之中。"},{"en":"A student may fit in ten minutes of vocabulary review before dinner.","zh":"學生可能在晚飯前安排十分鐘詞彙複習。"},{"en":"When small tasks are fitted into gaps, the evening may feel less crowded.","zh":"當小任務被安排在空檔中，晚上可能感覺沒那麼擠迫。"},{"en":"The phrase describes placing an activity into available time.","zh":"這個短語描述把活動放入可用時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"during lunchtimes","meaning":"在午膳時間","examples":[{"en":"Some domestic activities can be completed during lunchtimes.","zh":"一些家務活動可以在午膳時間完成。"},{"en":"During lunchtimes means in the period when people usually stop work or study to eat lunch.","zh":"during lunchtimes 指在人們通常停止工作或學習吃午飯的時段。"},{"en":"A student may visit the library during lunchtime if she has a project deadline.","zh":"如果學生有項目限期，她可能在午膳時間去圖書館。"},{"en":"Short midday breaks can be used for simple tasks if they do not remove needed rest.","zh":"中午短休息可以用於簡單任務，只要不剝奪必要休息。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a specific part of the day.","zh":"這個短語指出一天中的特定時段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"early morning","meaning":"清早","examples":[{"en":"Teleworkers may complete household tasks in the early morning.","zh":"遙距工作者可能在清早完成家務。"},{"en":"Early morning means the first part of the morning, soon after waking or before normal work begins.","zh":"early morning 指早上最初的時段，通常在醒來後不久或正常工作開始前。"},{"en":"A student may revise vocabulary in the early morning when the house is quiet.","zh":"學生可能在清早家中安靜時複習詞彙。"},{"en":"Using early morning time can make the rest of the day feel more organised.","zh":"使用清早時間可以令一天餘下部分感覺更有組織。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a time near the start of the day.","zh":"這個短語指一天開始附近的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"office cubicle","meaning":"辦公室間隔工作位","examples":[{"en":"Employees working in an office cubicle have access to technical help.","zh":"在辦公室間隔工作位工作的員工可以獲得技術協助。"},{"en":"An office cubicle is a small divided workspace inside a larger office.","zh":"office cubicle 指大型辦公室內以間隔分開的小型工作空間。"},{"en":"A call-centre worker may sit in an office cubicle with a computer, phone, and headset.","zh":"客服中心員工可能坐在有電腦、電話和耳機的辦公室間隔工作位。"},{"en":"Cubicles provide personal workspaces, but they may feel small or isolating.","zh":"間隔工作位提供個人工作空間，但可能感覺細小或令人孤立。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a partitioned office work area.","zh":"這個短語指有隔板分隔的辦公工作區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"something goes wrong with","meaning":"……出了問題","examples":[{"en":"Employees need support when something goes wrong with their equipment.","zh":"當設備出了問題時，員工需要支援。"},{"en":"Something goes wrong with a machine or system when it stops working properly.","zh":"something goes wrong with a machine or system 指機器或系統停止正常運作。"},{"en":"If something goes wrong with a student’s laptop before an online exam, she needs quick help.","zh":"如果學生手提電腦在網上考試前出了問題，她需要快速協助。"},{"en":"Technical problems can delay work if no support is available.","zh":"如果沒有支援，技術問題可以延誤工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes malfunction or unexpected trouble.","zh":"這個短語描述故障或意外麻煩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hardware or software","meaning":"硬件或軟件","examples":[{"en":"Technical staff support both hardware and software.","zh":"技術支援職員同時支援硬件和軟件。"},{"en":"Hardware or software refers to the physical parts of a computer system and the programs that run on it.","zh":"hardware or software 指電腦系統的實體部分和在其上運行的程式。"},{"en":"A broken keyboard is a hardware problem, while a frozen app is a software problem.","zh":"壞掉的鍵盤是硬件問題，而凍結的應用程式是軟件問題。"},{"en":"Remote workers may need help with both devices and digital systems.","zh":"遙距工作者可能需要設備和數碼系統兩方面的協助。"},{"en":"The phrase covers the main physical and digital parts of technology.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋科技的主要實體和數碼部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have the option of","meaning":"可以選擇……","examples":[{"en":"Office workers have the option of calling technical support.","zh":"辦公室員工可以選擇致電技術支援。"},{"en":"To have the option of doing something means to be able to choose that action.","zh":"have the option of doing something 指能夠選擇採取某行動。"},{"en":"Students may have the option of submitting homework online or on paper.","zh":"學生可能可以選擇網上或紙本提交功課。"},{"en":"Having options can reduce stress because people are not trapped in one solution.","zh":"有選擇可以減少壓力，因為人們不會被困於單一解決方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an available choice.","zh":"這個短語描述可用選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"call in","meaning":"召來……協助","examples":[{"en":"Employees can call in an IT specialist when a computer fails.","zh":"當電腦故障時，員工可以召來資訊科技專員協助。"},{"en":"To call in someone means to ask a specialist or helper to come and deal with a problem.","zh":"call in someone 指請專家或幫手前來處理問題。"},{"en":"A school may call in a plumber when a classroom sink leaks.","zh":"課室洗手盆漏水時，學校可能召來水喉匠協助。"},{"en":"Calling in an expert can solve problems faster than trying without the right skills.","zh":"召來專家可以比沒有相關技能地自行嘗試更快解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bringing someone in for help.","zh":"這個短語描述請某人前來幫忙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"IT specialist","meaning":"資訊科技專員","examples":[{"en":"An IT specialist can repair office computers and software.","zh":"資訊科技專員可以修理辦公室電腦和軟件。"},{"en":"An IT specialist is a person trained to manage, repair, or support computer systems and networks.","zh":"IT specialist 指受訓管理、修理或支援電腦系統和網絡的人。"},{"en":"A school may ask an IT specialist to fix the Wi-Fi before online lessons begin.","zh":"學校可能請資訊科技專員在網課開始前修好 Wi-Fi。"},{"en":"Without IT support, technical problems can stop employees from working efficiently.","zh":"沒有資訊科技支援，技術問題可以阻止員工有效工作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a technology support expert.","zh":"這個短語指科技支援專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be supported by","meaning":"得到……支援","examples":[{"en":"Office equipment is usually supported by technical staff.","zh":"辦公室設備通常得到技術支援職員支援。"},{"en":"To be supported by someone means to receive help, maintenance, or assistance from them.","zh":"be supported by someone 指獲得某人的幫助、保養或協助。"},{"en":"New students may be supported by older classmates during their first week.","zh":"新生第一週可能得到高年級同學支援。"},{"en":"If equipment is supported by experts, workers do not have to solve every problem alone.","zh":"如果設備得到專家支援，員工就不用獨自解決每個問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes having help available.","zh":"這個短語描述有協助可用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"technical staff","meaning":"技術支援職員","examples":[{"en":"Technical staff maintain the organisation’s equipment.","zh":"技術支援職員保養機構設備。"},{"en":"Technical staff are employees who look after equipment, systems, repairs, and technical support.","zh":"technical staff 指照顧設備、系統、維修和技術支援的員工。"},{"en":"A school’s technical staff may set up projectors, repair computers, and manage networks.","zh":"學校技術支援職員可能設置投影機、修理電腦和管理網絡。"},{"en":"Good technical staff help prevent small equipment problems from stopping work.","zh":"良好技術支援職員幫助防止小設備問題中斷工作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people with practical technology or equipment skills.","zh":"這個短語指具備實用科技或設備技能的人員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"regular updates","meaning":"定期更新","examples":[{"en":"Computers and software require regular updates.","zh":"電腦和軟件需要定期更新。"},{"en":"Regular updates are repeated improvements or security changes installed over time.","zh":"regular updates 指隨時間重複安裝的改善或安全變更。"},{"en":"A phone needs regular updates to fix bugs and protect personal information.","zh":"手機需要定期更新，以修正錯誤並保護個人資料。"},{"en":"Without updates, software may become unsafe, slow, or incompatible with new systems.","zh":"沒有更新，軟件可能變得不安全、緩慢或與新系統不兼容。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to ongoing technical maintenance.","zh":"這個短語指持續技術保養。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"office tools","meaning":"辦公工具","examples":[{"en":"Employees depend on various office tools and communication systems.","zh":"員工依賴各種辦公工具和溝通系統。"},{"en":"Office tools are the equipment, software, and systems people use to complete work tasks.","zh":"office tools 指人們用來完成工作任務的設備、軟件和系統。"},{"en":"Email, calendars, printers, spreadsheets, and video-call platforms are office tools.","zh":"電郵、日曆、打印機、試算表和視像會議平台都是辦公工具。"},{"en":"If office tools fail, even simple work may be delayed.","zh":"如果辦公工具故障，即使簡單工作也可能延誤。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both physical and digital work tools.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋實體和數碼工作工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"various and sundry","meaning":"各式各樣的","examples":[{"en":"Home workers must maintain various and sundry pieces of equipment.","zh":"在家工作者必須保養各式各樣的設備。"},{"en":"Various and sundry means many different kinds of things, often small or mixed.","zh":"various and sundry 指許多不同種類的東西，通常細小或混雜。"},{"en":"A teacher’s bag may contain various and sundry items such as markers, keys, notes, and cables.","zh":"老師的袋裏可能有各式各樣的物品，例如白板筆、鑰匙、筆記和電線。"},{"en":"Managing many small tools can become tiring when there is no office support.","zh":"當沒有辦公室支援，管理許多小工具可能變得疲累。"},{"en":"The phrase is slightly old-fashioned and emphasises variety.","zh":"這個短語略為舊式，強調種類繁多。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"landline phones","meaning":"固網電話","examples":[{"en":"Some offices still use landline phones.","zh":"一些辦公室仍使用固網電話。"},{"en":"Landline phones are telephones connected by physical telephone lines rather than mobile networks.","zh":"landline phones 指透過實體電話線而不是流動網絡連接的電話。"},{"en":"A school office may use landline phones for calls to parents and public services.","zh":"學校辦公室可能使用固網電話致電家長和公共服務。"},{"en":"Landlines can be reliable, but they are less flexible than mobile phones.","zh":"固網電話可以可靠，但比手提電話缺乏彈性。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to fixed phones, not smartphones.","zh":"這個短語指固定電話，而不是智能電話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"internet connections","meaning":"互聯網連線","examples":[{"en":"Reliable internet connections are essential for teleworking.","zh":"可靠互聯網連線對遙距工作至關重要。"},{"en":"Internet connections are links that allow computers or devices to access the internet.","zh":"internet connections 指讓電腦或裝置接入互聯網的連接。"},{"en":"A student needs a stable internet connection to attend an online lesson without interruptions.","zh":"學生需要穩定互聯網連線，才能不中斷地上網課。"},{"en":"Poor connections can delay meetings, stop file uploads, and reduce productivity.","zh":"連線差可以延誤會議、阻止文件上載並降低生產力。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to network access and reliability.","zh":"這個短語指網絡接入和可靠度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be up to someone","meaning":"由某人負責","examples":[{"en":"When you work from home, equipment maintenance is often up to you.","zh":"當你在家工作時，設備保養通常由你負責。"},{"en":"Be up to someone means be that person’s responsibility or decision.","zh":"be up to someone 指某事由某人負責或決定。"},{"en":"If a student studies independently, planning revision is up to her.","zh":"如果學生自學，溫習計劃就由她負責。"},{"en":"When support is not nearby, the worker may have to solve more problems alone.","zh":"當支援不在附近，工作者可能要獨自解決更多問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes responsibility being placed on a person.","zh":"這個短語描述責任落在某人身上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"work from home","meaning":"在家工作","examples":[{"en":"Employees who work from home may need to solve their own technical problems.","zh":"在家工作的員工可能需要解決自己的技術問題。"},{"en":"To work from home means to do one’s job at home instead of travelling to a workplace.","zh":"work from home 指在家完成工作，而不是前往工作場所。"},{"en":"A customer-service employee can work from home if calls are handled through a secure online system.","zh":"如果電話透過安全網上系統處理，客服員工可以在家工作。"},{"en":"Working from home can save travel time but may require self-discipline and good equipment.","zh":"在家工作可以節省交通時間，但可能需要自律和良好設備。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the location of work.","zh":"這個短語描述工作地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"encounter technical problems","meaning":"遇到技術問題","examples":[{"en":"Teleworkers will occasionally encounter technical problems.","zh":"遙距工作者偶爾會遇到技術問題。"},{"en":"To encounter technical problems means to experience difficulties with equipment, software, or systems.","zh":"encounter technical problems 指遇到設備、軟件或系統方面的困難。"},{"en":"A student may encounter technical problems when a video lesson suddenly freezes.","zh":"當視像課堂突然凍結，學生可能遇到技術問題。"},{"en":"Technical problems can interrupt work and create stress if support is slow.","zh":"如果支援緩慢，技術問題可以中斷工作並造成壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes running into technology-related trouble.","zh":"這個短語描述遇上與科技有關的麻煩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"get the support one needs","meaning":"獲得所需支援","examples":[{"en":"Remote workers may struggle to get the support they need.","zh":"遙距工作者可能難以獲得所需支援。"},{"en":"To get the support one needs means to receive the help required to solve a problem or continue working.","zh":"get the support one needs 指得到解決問題或繼續工作所需的幫助。"},{"en":"A student with weak Wi-Fi may need quick support before an online exam starts.","zh":"Wi-Fi 差的學生可能在網上考試開始前需要快速支援。"},{"en":"Without enough support, small technical problems can become serious delays.","zh":"沒有足夠支援，小技術問題可以變成嚴重延誤。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on receiving necessary help.","zh":"這個短語重點是得到必要幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hard drive","meaning":"硬碟","examples":[{"en":"A failed hard drive can prevent a teleworker from working.","zh":"故障硬碟可以阻止遙距工作者工作。"},{"en":"A hard drive is a computer storage device that holds files, programs, and data.","zh":"hard drive 指儲存文件、程式和數據的電腦儲存裝置。"},{"en":"A student may lose essays if a hard drive breaks and there is no backup.","zh":"如果硬碟損壞而沒有備份，學生可能失去作文。"},{"en":"If a hard drive fails, work may stop until data is recovered or the device is replaced.","zh":"如果硬碟故障，工作可能停止，直到數據恢復或裝置更換。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to computer storage hardware.","zh":"這個短語指電腦儲存硬件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"crash","meaning":"當機；突然故障","examples":[{"en":"A computer hard drive can crash without warning.","zh":"電腦硬碟可能毫無預警地突然故障。"},{"en":"To crash means to suddenly stop working, especially for a computer system or device.","zh":"crash 指突然停止運作，尤其是電腦系統或裝置。"},{"en":"A student may panic if her laptop crashes while she is writing an essay.","zh":"如果手提電腦在學生寫作文時當機，她可能會恐慌。"},{"en":"Regular backups reduce the damage when a computer crashes.","zh":"定期備份可以減少電腦當機時造成的損害。"},{"en":"The word describes sudden technical failure.","zh":"這個詞描述突然技術故障。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have the funds to","meaning":"有資金去……","examples":[{"en":"Some home workers may not have the funds to replace damaged equipment.","zh":"有些在家工作者可能沒有資金更換損壞設備。"},{"en":"To have the funds to do something means to have enough money to pay for it.","zh":"have the funds to do something 指有足夠金錢支付某事。"},{"en":"A student may not have the funds to buy a new laptop immediately.","zh":"學生可能沒有資金立即購買新手提電腦。"},{"en":"If workers must pay for their own equipment, lack of funds can stop them from working properly.","zh":"如果工作者必須自行支付設備費用，缺乏資金可以阻止他們正常工作。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on financial ability.","zh":"這個短語重點是財政能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"replace equipment","meaning":"更換設備","examples":[{"en":"A teleworker may need to replace faulty equipment personally.","zh":"遙距工作者可能需要親自更換故障設備。"},{"en":"To replace equipment means to remove broken or old equipment and get a working substitute.","zh":"replace equipment 指移除壞掉或舊設備，並取得可運作替代品。"},{"en":"A school may replace equipment when old projectors stop connecting to new laptops.","zh":"當舊投影機無法連接新手提電腦，學校可能更換設備。"},{"en":"Replacing equipment can be expensive, especially if the worker pays alone.","zh":"更換設備可能很昂貴，尤其是工作者獨自支付時。"},{"en":"The phrase describes getting a new item to take the place of the old one.","zh":"這個短語描述取得新物品來取代舊物品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to complete the summary using words from the list.","zh":"考生需要使用列表中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill missing words in a shortened version of the passage.","zh":"complete the summary 指填補文章簡短版本中的缺漏字詞。"},{"en":"A student should read the whole summary before choosing words from the list.","zh":"學生應先讀完整個摘要，再從列表中選字。"},{"en":"Summary completion tests meaning, grammar, and exact word choice.","zh":"摘要填空測試意思、文法和準確用字。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"list of words","meaning":"詞語列表","examples":[{"en":"The question provides a list of words for completing the summary.","zh":"題目提供一個詞語列表，用於完成摘要。"},{"en":"A list of words is a set of word choices given for a task.","zh":"list of words 指任務中提供的一組詞語選項。"},{"en":"In a vocabulary exercise, students may choose answers from a list of words below the passage.","zh":"在詞彙練習中，學生可能從文章下方的詞語列表中選答案。"},{"en":"A word list limits possible answers and helps students focus on meaning and grammar.","zh":"詞語列表限制可能答案，幫助學生集中於意思和文法。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to provided answer options.","zh":"這個短語指所提供的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"write the correct letter","meaning":"寫上正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should write the correct letter in each box.","zh":"考生應在每個方格中寫上正確字母。"},{"en":"To write the correct letter means to put the letter of the chosen answer option in the answer space.","zh":"write the correct letter 指把所選答案選項的字母寫在答案位置。"},{"en":"If the correct option is C, students should write C clearly rather than copying the whole word.","zh":"如果正確選項是 C，學生應清楚寫 C，而不是抄整個詞。"},{"en":"Writing the wrong letter loses the mark even if the student understood the passage.","zh":"即使學生理解文章，寫錯字母也會失分。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard instruction for matching or multiple-choice tasks.","zh":"這個短語是配對題或選擇題的標準指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"on your answer sheet","meaning":"在答題紙上","examples":[{"en":"Answers should be written on your answer sheet.","zh":"答案應寫在答題紙上。"},{"en":"On your answer sheet means in the official place where exam answers must be recorded.","zh":"on your answer sheet 指在必須記錄考試答案的正式位置上。"},{"en":"A student may lose marks if she writes answers in the question booklet but not on the answer sheet.","zh":"如果學生把答案寫在試題冊而不是答題紙上，可能會失分。"},{"en":"Answer sheets help examiners mark responses clearly and consistently.","zh":"答題紙幫助考官清楚而一致地評分。"},{"en":"The phrase tells candidates where final answers must go.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生最終答案必須寫在哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"benefits for society and companies","meaning":"對社會和公司的好處","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking is said to have benefits for society and companies.","zh":"據稱，遙距工作對社會和公司都有好處。"},{"en":"Benefits for society and companies are advantages that help both the public and organisations.","zh":"benefits for society and companies 指同時幫助公眾和機構的優點。"},{"en":"Reducing traffic can benefit society through cleaner air and help companies through lower office costs.","zh":"減少交通可以透過更潔淨空氣令社會受益，也可以透過較低辦公成本令公司受益。"},{"en":"If a work practice helps communities and employers, it may be easier to support politically.","zh":"如果一種工作做法幫助社區和僱主，它可能較容易獲得政策支持。"},{"en":"The phrase looks at wider public effects and business effects together.","zh":"這個短語同時看更廣泛公共效果和商業效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"spend more time shopping","meaning":"花更多時間購物","examples":[{"en":"Home-based workers may spend more time shopping at weekends.","zh":"在家工作者可能在週末花更多時間購物。"},{"en":"To spend more time shopping means to use a greater amount of time buying goods or visiting shops.","zh":"spend more time shopping 指用更多時間買東西或逛商店。"},{"en":"A person working near home may spend more time shopping in local stores during breaks.","zh":"在家附近工作的人可能在休息期間花更多時間在本地商店購物。"},{"en":"More shopping time can support neighbourhood businesses but may also increase non-commuting travel.","zh":"更多購物時間可以支持社區商店，但也可能增加非通勤出行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how people use their time outside work.","zh":"這個短語描述人們在工作以外如何使用時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"benefit the environment","meaning":"對環境有益","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking can benefit the environment by reducing travel.","zh":"遙距工作可以透過減少出行對環境有益。"},{"en":"To benefit the environment means to help protect nature or reduce pollution and resource use.","zh":"benefit the environment 指幫助保護自然或減少污染和資源使用。"},{"en":"Recycling food containers can benefit the environment by reducing waste.","zh":"回收食物容器可以透過減少浪費而對環境有益。"},{"en":"If fewer people drive to work, air pollution and carbon emissions may decrease.","zh":"如果較少人開車上班，空氣污染和碳排放可能下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a positive environmental effect.","zh":"這個短語描述正面環境效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"decreased road repairs","meaning":"減少道路維修","examples":[{"en":"Lower traffic levels may result in decreased road repairs.","zh":"較低交通量可能導致道路維修減少。"},{"en":"Decreased road repairs means fewer repairs are needed for roads because there is less damage or wear.","zh":"decreased road repairs 指由於損壞或磨損較少，道路需要較少維修。"},{"en":"A quiet private road may need decreased road repairs compared with a busy truck route.","zh":"與繁忙貨車路線相比，安靜私人道路可能需要較少道路維修。"},{"en":"If commuting traffic falls, road surfaces may last longer before repair is needed.","zh":"如果通勤交通下降，路面可能在需要維修前維持更久。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a reduction in road-maintenance work.","zh":"這個短語描述道路保養工作減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"send documents electronically","meaning":"以電子方式傳送文件","examples":[{"en":"Office staff can send documents electronically instead of printing them.","zh":"辦公室員工可以以電子方式傳送文件，而不是列印它們。"},{"en":"To send documents electronically means to share files by email, online platforms, or digital systems.","zh":"send documents electronically 指透過電郵、網上平台或數碼系統分享文件。"},{"en":"A teacher may send worksheets electronically so students can open them on tablets.","zh":"老師可能以電子方式傳送工作紙，讓學生在平板電腦上開啟。"},{"en":"Sending documents digitally can save paper, postage, and storage space.","zh":"數碼傳送文件可以節省紙張、郵費和儲存空間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes digital delivery rather than physical printing or mailing.","zh":"這個短語描述數碼傳送，而不是實體列印或郵寄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"public and private transport","meaning":"公共及私人交通工具","examples":[{"en":"Transportation equipment includes public and private transport.","zh":"運輸設備包括公共及私人交通工具。"},{"en":"Public and private transport means travel systems used by the public, such as buses, and personal vehicles, such as cars.","zh":"public and private transport 指公共使用的交通系統，例如巴士，以及個人車輛，例如私家車。"},{"en":"Students may use public transport to school, while some parents rely on private transport.","zh":"學生可能乘搭公共交通上學，而一些家長依賴私人交通工具。"},{"en":"Reducing work travel can affect both buses and private cars.","zh":"減少工作出行可以影響巴士和私家車。"},{"en":"The phrase covers shared transport and personally owned transport.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋共享交通和個人擁有的交通工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"with the rise of","meaning":"隨着……興起","examples":[{"en":"With the rise of telecommuting, demand for transport may fall.","zh":"隨着遙距辦公興起，對交通的需求可能下降。"},{"en":"With the rise of something means as that thing becomes more common or important.","zh":"with the rise of something 指隨着某事變得更常見或更重要。"},{"en":"With the rise of online learning, more students need reliable internet at home.","zh":"隨着網上學習興起，更多學生需要家中有可靠互聯網。"},{"en":"When a new practice grows, it can change older habits and industries.","zh":"當新做法增長，它可以改變舊習慣和行業。"},{"en":"The phrase links an increasing trend with its effects.","zh":"這個短語把上升趨勢與其影響連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"conserve resources","meaning":"節約資源","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking can conserve fuel, materials and other resources.","zh":"遙距工作可以節約燃料、物料和其他資源。"},{"en":"To conserve resources means to save resources and avoid using them wastefully.","zh":"conserve resources 指節省資源並避免浪費使用。"},{"en":"A school can conserve resources by reusing books and reducing unnecessary printing.","zh":"學校可以透過重用書本和減少不必要列印來節約資源。"},{"en":"Resource conservation can lower costs and reduce environmental damage.","zh":"節約資源可以降低成本並減少環境破壞。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on careful use of limited materials or energy.","zh":"這個短語重點是謹慎使用有限物料或能源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"construction and maintenance","meaning":"建設和保養","examples":[{"en":"Energy is used in the construction and maintenance of highways.","zh":"能源用於公路的建設和保養。"},{"en":"Construction and maintenance means building something and keeping it in good condition afterwards.","zh":"construction and maintenance 指建造某物，並在之後保持其良好狀態。"},{"en":"A school building needs both construction and maintenance: first it is built, then it is repaired and cleaned.","zh":"校舍需要建設和保養：先被建造，之後被維修和清潔。"},{"en":"Roads require energy not only when built but also when repaired over many years.","zh":"道路不只在建造時需要能源，多年維修時也需要能源。"},{"en":"The phrase combines creation with ongoing care.","zh":"這個短語結合創建和持續照顧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"complete each sentence with","meaning":"用……完成每句句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete each sentence with the correct ending.","zh":"考生用正確句尾完成每句句子。"},{"en":"To complete each sentence with something means to finish every sentence using the suitable option.","zh":"complete each sentence with something 指用合適選項完成每個句子。"},{"en":"Students may complete each sentence with a verb from the box in a grammar exercise.","zh":"在文法練習中，學生可能用方框中的動詞完成每句句子。"},{"en":"The ending must fit both meaning and grammar.","zh":"句尾必須在意思和文法上都配合。"},{"en":"The phrase is an instruction for sentence-completion tasks.","zh":"這個短語是句子完成題的指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the correct ending","meaning":"正確句尾","examples":[{"en":"Each statement must be matched with the correct ending.","zh":"每項陳述必須與正確句尾配對。"},{"en":"The correct ending is the option that completes a sentence accurately and logically.","zh":"correct ending 指準確並合邏輯地完成句子的選項。"},{"en":"In a reading test, the correct ending must match the passage, not just sound natural.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，正確句尾必須符合文章，而不只是聽起來自然。"},{"en":"A wrong ending may use familiar words but change the meaning.","zh":"錯誤句尾可能使用熟悉詞語，但改變意思。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the right completion option.","zh":"這個短語指正確的完成選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be connected with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"More working time is often connected with stress and tension.","zh":"更多工作時間通常與壓力和緊張有關。"},{"en":"To be connected with something means to have a relationship or association with it.","zh":"be connected with something 指與某事有關係或聯繫。"},{"en":"Poor concentration may be connected with lack of sleep.","zh":"專注力差可能與睡眠不足有關。"},{"en":"When two things are connected, one may influence the other or appear with it.","zh":"當兩件事有關，一件可能影響另一件或與它一起出現。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a link, not always a direct cause.","zh":"這個短語顯示關聯，不一定是直接原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stress and tension","meaning":"壓力和緊張","examples":[{"en":"Longer working hours can cause stress and tension.","zh":"較長工時可以造成壓力和緊張。"},{"en":"Stress and tension are mental pressure and emotional strain caused by demands or conflict.","zh":"stress and tension 指由要求或衝突造成的心理壓力和情緒拉扯。"},{"en":"A student may feel stress and tension when exams and family problems happen together.","zh":"當考試和家庭問題同時出現，學生可能感到壓力和緊張。"},{"en":"If stress and tension continue, sleep, mood, and relationships may suffer.","zh":"如果壓力和緊張持續，睡眠、心情和關係可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes pressure that can affect both mind and body.","zh":"這個短語描述會影響身心的壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"office concept","meaning":"辦公室概念","examples":[{"en":"Oracle’s office concept aims to improve communication.","zh":"Oracle 的辦公室概念旨在改善溝通。"},{"en":"An office concept is the main design idea or approach behind a workplace.","zh":"office concept 指工作場所背後的主要設計想法或方式。"},{"en":"A company may use an open-office concept to encourage quick conversations between teams.","zh":"公司可能使用開放式辦公室概念，以鼓勵團隊之間快速對話。"},{"en":"The office concept affects how people meet, focus, relax, and share information.","zh":"辦公室概念影響人們如何見面、專注、放鬆和分享資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the thinking behind office design.","zh":"這個短語指辦公室設計背後的思路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"aim to improve","meaning":"旨在改善……","examples":[{"en":"The office design aims to improve contact between colleagues.","zh":"辦公室設計旨在改善同事之間的接觸。"},{"en":"To aim to improve something means to have the goal of making it better.","zh":"aim to improve something 指以令某事變得更好為目標。"},{"en":"A reading programme may aim to improve students’ confidence and accuracy.","zh":"閱讀計劃可能旨在改善學生信心和準確度。"},{"en":"If a design aims to improve communication, it should create more chances for people to meet.","zh":"如果設計旨在改善溝通，它應創造更多讓人見面的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase states the intended purpose of an action or plan.","zh":"這個短語說明行動或計劃的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"communication with colleagues","meaning":"與同事的溝通","examples":[{"en":"Remote work may reduce communication with colleagues.","zh":"遙距工作可能減少與同事的溝通。"},{"en":"Communication with colleagues means sharing information, ideas, questions, and feedback with people you work with.","zh":"communication with colleagues 指與共事的人分享資訊、想法、問題和回饋。"},{"en":"A teacher needs communication with colleagues when planning exams across several classes.","zh":"老師在幾個班級之間規劃考試時，需要與同事溝通。"},{"en":"If communication weakens, mistakes may increase and teamwork may suffer.","zh":"如果溝通減弱，錯誤可能增加，團隊合作也可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on work-related interaction between co-workers.","zh":"這個短語重點是同事之間與工作有關的互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be maintained by","meaning":"由……保養","examples":[{"en":"Office computers are normally maintained by technical support staff.","zh":"辦公室電腦通常由技術支援職員保養。"},{"en":"To be maintained by someone means to be kept working properly through that person’s regular care.","zh":"be maintained by someone 指透過某人的定期照顧而保持正常運作。"},{"en":"School air conditioners may be maintained by outside technicians every summer.","zh":"學校冷氣機可能每年夏天由外判技術員保養。"},{"en":"When equipment is maintained well, breakdowns become less frequent.","zh":"當設備保養良好，故障會較少發生。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who is responsible for upkeep.","zh":"這個短語指出誰負責維護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"technical support staff","meaning":"技術支援職員","examples":[{"en":"Technical support staff maintain workplace equipment.","zh":"技術支援職員保養工作場所設備。"},{"en":"Technical support staff are workers who help with computers, software, networks, and other equipment.","zh":"technical support staff 指協助處理電腦、軟件、網絡和其他設備的員工。"},{"en":"A college’s technical support staff may help students reset passwords before online exams.","zh":"學院技術支援職員可能在網上考試前幫學生重設密碼。"},{"en":"Quick technical support can prevent small faults from becoming long work stoppages.","zh":"快速技術支援可以防止小故障變成長時間停工。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to staff who solve practical technology problems.","zh":"這個短語指解決實際科技問題的員工。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"equipment does not work","meaning":"設備無法運作","examples":[{"en":"Home workers face problems when their equipment does not work.","zh":"當設備無法運作時，在家工作者會面對問題。"},{"en":"Equipment does not work means a device, machine, or system fails to function properly.","zh":"equipment does not work 指裝置、機器或系統無法正常運作。"},{"en":"If a student’s printer does not work, she may need to submit the assignment online.","zh":"如果學生的打印機無法運作，她可能需要網上提交作業。"},{"en":"Broken equipment can stop work when there is no quick replacement or repair.","zh":"當沒有快速替代品或維修，壞掉設備可以令工作停止。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical failure of tools or machines.","zh":"這個短語描述工具或機器的實際故障。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"author’s attitude towards","meaning":"作者對……的態度","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the author’s attitude towards teleworking.","zh":"題目詢問作者對遙距工作的態度。"},{"en":"An author’s attitude towards something is how the writer feels or thinks about it.","zh":"author’s attitude towards something 指作者對某事的感受或看法。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may judge the author’s attitude towards technology as cautious but positive.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能判斷作者對科技的態度是謹慎但正面。"},{"en":"Word choice, examples, and conclusions can reveal the writer’s attitude.","zh":"用字、例子和結論可以揭示作者態度。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for the writer’s viewpoint, not the reader’s opinion.","zh":"這個短語詢問作者觀點，而不是讀者意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be surprised by","meaning":"對……感到驚訝","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that the author is surprised by teleworking’s rapid growth.","zh":"該選項暗示作者對遙距工作的快速增長感到驚訝。"},{"en":"To be surprised by something means to feel that it is unexpected or unusual.","zh":"be surprised by something 指覺得某事出乎意料或不尋常。"},{"en":"A teacher may be surprised by a quiet student’s excellent speech.","zh":"老師可能對安靜學生的精彩演講感到驚訝。"},{"en":"Surprise often appears when reality is different from what someone expected.","zh":"當現實不同於某人預期，驚訝常會出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an emotional reaction to unexpected information.","zh":"這個短語描述對意外資訊的情緒反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rapid growth","meaning":"快速增長","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking has experienced rapid growth in many industries.","zh":"遙距工作在許多行業中經歷快速增長。"},{"en":"Rapid growth means fast increase over a short period.","zh":"rapid growth 指在短時間內快速增加。"},{"en":"A new app may experience rapid growth if many students recommend it to friends.","zh":"如果許多學生向朋友推薦，新應用程式可能經歷快速增長。"},{"en":"Rapid growth can create opportunities but also pressure on systems and managers.","zh":"快速增長可以創造機會，但也會對系統和管理者造成壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes speed of expansion.","zh":"這個短語描述擴展速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be unconcerned about","meaning":"對……不感到擔憂","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that the author is unconcerned about future developments.","zh":"該選項暗示作者對未來發展不感到擔憂。"},{"en":"To be unconcerned about something means not to be worried or interested in it.","zh":"be unconcerned about something 指對某事不擔心或不關心。"},{"en":"A student who is unconcerned about deadlines may start homework too late.","zh":"對限期不感到擔憂的學生，可能太遲才開始做功課。"},{"en":"If managers are unconcerned about remote-work problems, small issues may become serious.","zh":"如果管理者不擔心遙距工作問題，小問題可能變得嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lack of worry or attention.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏擔憂或注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"future development","meaning":"未來發展","examples":[{"en":"The future development of teleworking depends partly on technology.","zh":"遙距工作的未來發展部分取決於科技。"},{"en":"Future development means how something will grow, change, or improve later.","zh":"future development 指某事日後如何增長、改變或改善。"},{"en":"The future development of online education may depend on better platforms and teacher training.","zh":"網上教育的未來發展可能取決於更好平台和教師培訓。"},{"en":"If technology improves, remote work may become easier and more common.","zh":"如果科技改善，遙距工作可能變得更容易和更普遍。"},{"en":"The phrase looks ahead to later change.","zh":"這個短語展望之後的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"generally positive and encouraging","meaning":"整體正面而令人鼓舞","examples":[{"en":"The passage presents teleworking as generally positive and encouraging.","zh":"文章把遙距工作呈現為整體正面而令人鼓舞。"},{"en":"Generally positive and encouraging means mostly favourable and giving reasons for hope.","zh":"generally positive and encouraging 指大體上贊同，並給人希望理由。"},{"en":"A teacher’s feedback can be generally positive and encouraging while still pointing out mistakes.","zh":"老師的回饋可以整體正面而令人鼓舞，同時仍指出錯誤。"},{"en":"If a report highlights benefits but admits some problems, its attitude may still be generally positive.","zh":"如果報告突出好處但承認一些問題，其態度仍可能整體正面。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an overall supportive tone.","zh":"這個短語描述整體支持性的語氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be worried about","meaning":"擔心……","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that the author is worried about economic problems.","zh":"該選項暗示作者擔心經濟問題。"},{"en":"To be worried about something means to feel anxious or concerned about it.","zh":"be worried about something 指對某事感到焦慮或關注。"},{"en":"A parent may be worried about a child’s long commute to school.","zh":"家長可能擔心孩子上學通勤時間太長。"},{"en":"Worry can lead people to ask for more information or prepare solutions.","zh":"擔心可以令人尋求更多資訊或準備解決方法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes concern about a possible problem.","zh":"這個短語描述對可能問題的憂慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"economic problems","meaning":"經濟問題","examples":[{"en":"Teleworking may create some economic and organisational challenges.","zh":"遙距工作可能造成一些經濟和組織方面的挑戰。"},{"en":"Economic problems are difficulties involving money, costs, jobs, income, productivity, or business activity.","zh":"economic problems 指涉及金錢、成本、職位、收入、生產力或商業活動的困難。"},{"en":"A small shop faces economic problems if rent rises while customers spend less.","zh":"如果租金上升而顧客消費減少，小店就會面對經濟問題。"},{"en":"Economic problems can force organisations to change budgets, staffing, and working methods.","zh":"經濟問題可以迫使機構改變預算、人手和工作方式。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on financial and business-related difficulties.","zh":"這個短語重點是財務和商業相關困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 163 - Tele-working.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 164":[{"front":"the impact of environment on","meaning":"環境對……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines the impact of environment on children’s development.","zh":"文章探討環境對兒童發展的影響。"},{"en":"The impact of environment on someone means the way surroundings, people, and experiences affect that person.","zh":"impact of environment on someone 指周圍環境、人和經歷如何影響某人。"},{"en":"A noisy home can have an impact on a child’s ability to concentrate on homework.","zh":"嘈雜的家庭環境可以影響孩子專心做功課的能力。"},{"en":"A safe school environment can support confidence, friendship, and learning.","zh":"安全的學校環境可以支持信心、友誼和學習。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how outside conditions shape development.","zh":"討論外在條件如何塑造成長時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"determine how a child develops","meaning":"決定兒童如何成長","examples":[{"en":"Many genetic and environmental factors determine how a child develops.","zh":"許多遺傳和環境因素決定兒童如何成長。"},{"en":"To determine how a child develops means to influence the way a child grows physically, mentally, socially, or emotionally.","zh":"determine how a child develops 指影響兒童在身體、心理、社交或情緒上如何成長。"},{"en":"Good sleep, patient teaching, and family support can help determine how a child develops.","zh":"良好睡眠、耐心教導和家庭支援可以幫助決定兒童如何成長。"},{"en":"If a child grows up with little stimulation, their language and confidence may develop differently.","zh":"如果兒童在缺乏刺激的環境中長大，他的語言和信心可能以不同方式發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining causes of child development.","zh":"解釋兒童發展成因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in reality","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In reality, it is impossible to identify every influence on a child.","zh":"事實上，要找出對兒童的每一項影響是不可能的。"},{"en":"In reality means in the actual situation, not just in theory or imagination.","zh":"in reality 指在真實情況中，而不只是理論或想像中。"},{"en":"A timetable may look simple on paper; in reality, students may need breaks between lessons.","zh":"時間表在紙上可能看似簡單；事實上，學生可能需要課與課之間的休息。"},{"en":"In reality, child development is affected by many factors at the same time.","zh":"事實上，兒童發展同時受到許多因素影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when correcting an oversimplified idea.","zh":"糾正過度簡化的想法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"account for","meaning":"解釋；說明","examples":[{"en":"No single theory can account for every influence on development.","zh":"沒有單一理論能解釋發展中的每一項影響。"},{"en":"To account for something means to explain it or show why it happens.","zh":"account for something 指解釋某事或說明它為何發生。"},{"en":"A teacher may not be able to account for a student’s sudden improvement without knowing about extra practice at home.","zh":"如果老師不知道學生在家額外練習，就可能無法解釋他突然進步的原因。"},{"en":"A simple explanation may fail to account for a complex problem.","zh":"簡單解釋可能無法說明一個複雜問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing whether an explanation is complete.","zh":"討論某個解釋是否完整時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"each and every influence","meaning":"每一項影響","examples":[{"en":"It would be impossible to examine each and every influence on a child.","zh":"要檢視對兒童的每一項影響是不可能的。"},{"en":"Each and every influence means all influences without exception.","zh":"each and every influence 指所有影響，沒有例外。"},{"en":"A doctor cannot examine each and every influence on a patient’s stress in one short appointment.","zh":"醫生不可能在一次短短診症中檢視病人壓力的每一項影響。"},{"en":"When a topic is very complex, studying every single influence may be unrealistic.","zh":"當主題非常複雜時，研究每一項影響可能並不現實。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises completeness.","zh":"這個短語強調完全和無遺漏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ultimately determine","meaning":"最終決定","examples":[{"en":"Many different factors ultimately determine who a child becomes.","zh":"許多不同因素最終決定兒童會成為怎樣的人。"},{"en":"Ultimately determine means finally decide or strongly shape the final result.","zh":"ultimately determine 指最終決定或強烈塑造最後結果。"},{"en":"A student’s habits, support, and choices may ultimately determine their exam progress.","zh":"學生的習慣、支援和選擇可能最終決定他的考試進步。"},{"en":"Early experiences may not show their full effect until much later.","zh":"早期經歷的完整影響可能到很久之後才顯現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing long-term outcomes.","zh":"討論長期結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"apparent influences","meaning":"明顯的影響因素","examples":[{"en":"Researchers can examine some of the most apparent influences on children.","zh":"研究人員可以檢視一些對兒童最明顯的影響因素。"},{"en":"Apparent influences are influences that are easy to notice or seem clear.","zh":"apparent influences 指容易注意到或看似清楚的影響因素。"},{"en":"A child’s school, friends, and home routines are apparent influences on daily behaviour.","zh":"兒童的學校、朋友和家庭日常規律都是對日常行為的明顯影響。"},{"en":"Apparent influences may be important, but hidden influences can matter too.","zh":"明顯影響因素可能重要，但隱藏因素也可能重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when separating visible factors from less obvious ones.","zh":"區分可見因素和不太明顯因素時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"genetic influences","meaning":"遺傳影響","examples":[{"en":"Genetic influences account for a substantial part of child development.","zh":"遺傳影響解釋兒童發展中相當大的一部分。"},{"en":"Genetic influences are effects that come from genes inherited from parents.","zh":"genetic influences 指來自父母遺傳基因的影響。"},{"en":"A child’s height may be partly shaped by genetic influences.","zh":"兒童的身高可能部分由遺傳影響塑造。"},{"en":"Genetic influences can affect development, but they usually work together with environment.","zh":"遺傳影響可以影響發展，但通常會與環境共同作用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in the nature-versus-nurture discussion.","zh":"在先天與後天討論中，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"parenting","meaning":"教養方式","examples":[{"en":"Parenting is one of the factors that may shape a child’s development.","zh":"教養方式是可能塑造兒童發展的因素之一。"},{"en":"Parenting means the way parents care for, guide, teach, and discipline their children.","zh":"parenting 指父母照顧、引導、教導和管教子女的方式。"},{"en":"Patient parenting can help a child feel safe enough to ask questions.","zh":"有耐性的教養方式可以幫助孩子感到安全，敢於提問。"},{"en":"Harsh or inconsistent parenting may affect confidence and behaviour.","zh":"嚴厲或不一致的教養方式可能影響信心和行為。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing family influence.","zh":"討論家庭影響時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lifetime experiences","meaning":"一生的經歷","examples":[{"en":"A person’s personality is shaped partly by their lifetime experiences.","zh":"一個人的性格部分由其一生經歷塑造。"},{"en":"Lifetime experiences are all the important things a person goes through during life.","zh":"lifetime experiences 指一個人在一生中經歷的重要事情。"},{"en":"Moving schools, making friends, working, and facing failure can all be lifetime experiences.","zh":"轉校、交朋友、工作和面對失敗都可以是一生經歷的一部分。"},{"en":"These experiences can change how people think, react, and relate to others.","zh":"這些經歷可以改變人們如何思考、反應和與他人相處。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how life shapes personality.","zh":"解釋人生如何塑造性格時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"family relationships","meaning":"家庭關係","examples":[{"en":"Family relationships can contribute to a child’s growth.","zh":"家庭關係可以有助兒童成長。"},{"en":"Family relationships are the connections between parents, children, siblings, and relatives.","zh":"family relationships 指父母、子女、兄弟姊妹和親人之間的連繫。"},{"en":"Warm family relationships can help children feel secure and supported.","zh":"溫暖的家庭關係可以幫助兒童感到安全和受支持。"},{"en":"Conflict in family relationships may affect a child’s mood and behaviour.","zh":"家庭關係中的衝突可能影響兒童情緒和行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing emotional and social development.","zh":"討論情緒和社交發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"contribute to","meaning":"促成；有助於","examples":[{"en":"Genetics and experience both contribute to a child’s growth.","zh":"遺傳和經驗都促成兒童成長。"},{"en":"To contribute to something means to help cause it or add to it.","zh":"contribute to something 指幫助造成某事或為其添加影響。"},{"en":"Regular reading can contribute to better vocabulary.","zh":"定期閱讀可以有助於更好的詞彙量。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can contribute to low concentration the next day.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致翌日專注力低。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when several factors work together to create a result.","zh":"當幾個因素共同造成結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a child’s growth","meaning":"兒童的成長","examples":[{"en":"Many social and biological factors contribute to a child’s growth.","zh":"許多社會和生物因素都有助兒童的成長。"},{"en":"A child’s growth includes physical, mental, emotional, and social development.","zh":"child’s growth 包括身體、心理、情緒和社交發展。"},{"en":"Good food and regular sleep support a child’s physical growth.","zh":"良好食物和定期睡眠支持兒童身體成長。"},{"en":"Encouragement and friendship can support a child’s emotional growth.","zh":"鼓勵和友誼可以支持兒童情緒成長。"},{"en":"This phrase is broader than height or body size alone.","zh":"這個短語比單純身高或體型更廣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"think of something as","meaning":"把某事視為……","examples":[{"en":"We can think of these influences as building blocks.","zh":"我們可以把這些影響視為基本組成部分。"},{"en":"To think of something as something means to understand or imagine it in that way.","zh":"think of something as something 指以某種方式理解或想像某事。"},{"en":"Students can think of grammar as a toolkit rather than a list of punishments.","zh":"學生可以把文法視為工具箱，而不是懲罰清單。"},{"en":"Thinking of influences as building blocks helps us see how they combine.","zh":"把影響視為基本組成部分，幫助我們看見它們如何組合。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when using a comparison to explain an idea.","zh":"使用比較來解釋想法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"building blocks","meaning":"基本組成部分","examples":[{"en":"Genetic and environmental influences act as building blocks of development.","zh":"遺傳和環境影響充當發展的基本組成部分。"},{"en":"Building blocks are basic parts that combine to create something larger.","zh":"building blocks 指組合成較大事物的基本部分。"},{"en":"Vocabulary and grammar are building blocks of strong writing.","zh":"詞彙和文法是強大寫作的基本組成部分。"},{"en":"If one building block is weak, the final structure may be less stable.","zh":"如果其中一個基本部分薄弱，最終結構可能較不穩固。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how complex things are formed from simpler parts.","zh":"解釋複雜事物如何由簡單部分形成時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tend to have","meaning":"往往具有","examples":[{"en":"Most people tend to have the same basic developmental components.","zh":"大多數人往往具有相同的基本發展組成元素。"},{"en":"Tend to have means usually have, though not always.","zh":"tend to have 指通常具有，但不一定永遠如此。"},{"en":"Young children tend to have short attention spans during long lessons.","zh":"幼童在長課堂中往往注意力較短。"},{"en":"People tend to have better habits when routines are simple and consistent.","zh":"當日常規律簡單而一致，人們往往有更好習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a general pattern, not an absolute rule.","zh":"描述一般模式而非絕對規則時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"basic components","meaning":"基本組成元素","examples":[{"en":"The same basic components can produce very different personalities.","zh":"相同的基本組成元素可以產生非常不同的性格。"},{"en":"Basic components are the main simple parts from which something is made.","zh":"basic components 指構成某物的主要簡單部分。"},{"en":"Flour, water, salt, and yeast are basic components of bread.","zh":"麵粉、水、鹽和酵母是麵包的基本組成元素。"},{"en":"The same components can create different results depending on how they are combined.","zh":"相同元素可以因組合方式不同而產生不同結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when breaking a complex idea into parts.","zh":"把複雜想法拆成部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be put together","meaning":"被組合起來","examples":[{"en":"The components can be put together in countless ways.","zh":"這些組成元素可以用無數種方式被組合起來。"},{"en":"Be put together means be combined or arranged to form something.","zh":"be put together 指被結合或排列以形成某物。"},{"en":"A lesson can be put together from videos, examples, games, and discussion.","zh":"一堂課可以由影片、例子、遊戲和討論組合起來。"},{"en":"The same materials can produce different outcomes when they are put together differently.","zh":"相同材料以不同方式組合時，可以產生不同結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing combination or construction.","zh":"描述組合或建構時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an infinite number of ways","meaning":"無數種方式","examples":[{"en":"Biological and social factors can combine in an infinite number of ways.","zh":"生物和社會因素可以以無數種方式結合。"},{"en":"An infinite number of ways means so many possible ways that they cannot be counted.","zh":"infinite number of ways 指可能方式多到無法計算。"},{"en":"Students can express the same idea in an infinite number of ways.","zh":"學生可以用無數種方式表達同一想法。"},{"en":"When many factors interact, the number of possible outcomes becomes extremely large.","zh":"當許多因素互動，可能結果的數量就變得極大。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing huge variety.","zh":"強調巨大多樣性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"overall personality","meaning":"整體性格","examples":[{"en":"Both nature and nurture help shape a person’s overall personality.","zh":"先天和後天都幫助塑造一個人的整體性格。"},{"en":"Overall personality means a person’s general pattern of character, behaviour, emotions, and attitudes.","zh":"overall personality 指一個人在性格、行為、情緒和態度上的整體模式。"},{"en":"A child’s overall personality may include confidence, patience, curiosity, and kindness.","zh":"兒童的整體性格可能包括信心、耐性、好奇心和善良。"},{"en":"Personality develops through both inherited tendencies and life experiences.","zh":"性格透過遺傳傾向和人生經歷共同發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the whole person rather than one single trait.","zh":"討論整個人而非單一特質時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be shaped by","meaning":"由……塑造","examples":[{"en":"Personality is shaped by both genetic inheritance and experience.","zh":"性格由遺傳特質和經驗共同塑造。"},{"en":"To be shaped by something means to be influenced and formed by it.","zh":"be shaped by something 指被某物影響並形成。"},{"en":"A student’s study habits may be shaped by teachers, parents, and exam pressure.","zh":"學生的學習習慣可能由老師、家長和考試壓力塑造。"},{"en":"Childhood experiences can shape how people handle stress later in life.","zh":"童年經歷可以塑造人們日後如何處理壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining long-term influence.","zh":"解釋長期影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"genetic inheritance","meaning":"遺傳特質","examples":[{"en":"Some aspects of personality may reflect genetic inheritance.","zh":"性格的某些方面可能反映遺傳特質。"},{"en":"Genetic inheritance means traits or tendencies passed from parents to children through genes.","zh":"genetic inheritance 指透過基因由父母傳給子女的特徵或傾向。"},{"en":"Eye colour is a simple example of genetic inheritance.","zh":"眼睛顏色是遺傳特質的一個簡單例子。"},{"en":"Some inherited tendencies may appear more strongly in certain environments.","zh":"某些遺傳傾向可能在特定環境中更強地表現出來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing biological influence.","zh":"討論生物影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be a result of","meaning":"是……的結果","examples":[{"en":"Many behaviours are a result of both biology and experience.","zh":"許多行為都是生物因素和經驗共同作用的結果。"},{"en":"To be a result of something means to be caused or produced by it.","zh":"be a result of something 指由某事造成或產生。"},{"en":"A child’s fear of dogs may be a result of one frightening experience.","zh":"孩子怕狗可能是一次驚嚇經歷的結果。"},{"en":"Good exam performance can be a result of practice, sleep, and clear teaching.","zh":"好的考試表現可以是練習、睡眠和清楚教學的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining causes.","zh":"解釋原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"puzzle philosophers","meaning":"令哲學家困惑","examples":[{"en":"The nature–nurture question has puzzled philosophers for centuries.","zh":"先天與後天問題令哲學家困惑了幾個世紀。"},{"en":"To puzzle philosophers means to make thinkers confused or deeply curious about a difficult question.","zh":"puzzle philosophers 指令思想家對困難問題感到困惑或深深好奇。"},{"en":"Questions about free will and responsibility have puzzled philosophers for a long time.","zh":"關於自由意志和責任的問題長期令哲學家困惑。"},{"en":"A problem puzzles people when there is no simple answer.","zh":"當問題沒有簡單答案時，就會令人困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an issue has caused long debate.","zh":"當議題引起長期爭論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"for hundreds of years","meaning":"數百年來","examples":[{"en":"The debate has continued for hundreds of years.","zh":"這場爭論已持續數百年。"},{"en":"For hundreds of years means for several centuries.","zh":"for hundreds of years 指好幾個世紀以來。"},{"en":"People have used markets for hundreds of years to buy and sell food.","zh":"人們數百年來使用市場買賣食物。"},{"en":"A question discussed for hundreds of years is usually complex and difficult to settle.","zh":"被討論數百年的問題通常複雜且難以定論。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing a long historical period.","zh":"強調長久歷史時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be referred to as","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"The issue is frequently referred to as the nature versus nurture debate.","zh":"這個議題經常被稱為先天與後天之爭。"},{"en":"To be referred to as something means to be called or named that.","zh":"be referred to as something 指被稱作或命名為某事。"},{"en":"Hong Kong is often referred to as a major financial centre.","zh":"香港常被稱為重要金融中心。"},{"en":"Giving an issue a name helps people discuss it more clearly.","zh":"為議題命名有助人們更清楚討論它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing a term.","zh":"引入術語時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"nature versus nurture debate","meaning":"先天與後天之爭","examples":[{"en":"The nature versus nurture debate concerns biology and environment.","zh":"先天與後天之爭涉及生物因素和環境。"},{"en":"The nature versus nurture debate asks whether genes or life experiences matter more in development.","zh":"nature versus nurture debate 問的是基因還是生活經歷對發展更重要。"},{"en":"Teachers may discuss this debate when explaining why siblings can be so different.","zh":"老師解釋兄弟姊妹為何可以很不同時，可能討論這場爭論。"},{"en":"Modern research usually shows that nature and nurture interact rather than work separately.","zh":"現代研究通常顯示先天與後天會互動，而不是分開作用。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to discussions of human development.","zh":"這個短語是人類發展討論的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"account for","meaning":"佔；解釋……的比例","examples":[{"en":"Genetic influences may account for 40 to 50 percent of child development.","zh":"遺傳影響可能佔兒童發展的百分之四十至五十。"},{"en":"Account for can mean make up a certain share or proportion of something.","zh":"account for 可以指佔某事的一定比例。"},{"en":"Rent may account for half of a family’s monthly spending.","zh":"租金可能佔家庭每月開支的一半。"},{"en":"If one factor accounts for a large percentage, it is important but may not explain everything.","zh":"如果一個因素佔很大比例，它很重要，但未必解釋一切。"},{"en":"This use of account for is common in statistics and research writing.","zh":"account for 的這種用法常見於統計和研究寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"apply to all siblings","meaning":"適用於所有兄弟姊妹","examples":[{"en":"Some genetic influences may apply to all siblings in a family.","zh":"某些遺傳影響可能適用於家庭中的所有兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"Apply to all siblings means affect every brother and sister in the same family.","zh":"apply to all siblings 指影響同一家庭中的每個兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"A family rule about bedtime may apply to all siblings, not just the youngest child.","zh":"關於睡覺時間的家庭規則可能適用於所有兄弟姊妹，而不只是最年幼的孩子。"},{"en":"Shared influences can make siblings more similar because they experience the same condition.","zh":"共享影響可以令兄弟姊妹更相似，因為他們經歷相同條件。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing shared and non-shared influences.","zh":"比較共享與非共享影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"genetic background","meaning":"遺傳背景","examples":[{"en":"Nature refers to a person’s genetic background.","zh":"先天指一個人的遺傳背景。"},{"en":"Genetic background means the inherited biological information a person receives from parents.","zh":"genetic background 指一個人從父母遺傳而來的生物資訊。"},{"en":"A doctor may ask about family history to understand a patient’s genetic background.","zh":"醫生可能詢問家族病史，以了解病人的遺傳背景。"},{"en":"Genetic background can affect height, health risks, and some behavioural tendencies.","zh":"遺傳背景可以影響身高、健康風險和某些行為傾向。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing inherited factors.","zh":"討論遺傳因素時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"most researchers agree that","meaning":"大多數研究人員同意","examples":[{"en":"Most researchers agree that development involves nature and nurture.","zh":"大多數研究人員同意發展涉及先天與後天。"},{"en":"Most researchers agree that means the majority of experts accept a point as likely or well supported.","zh":"most researchers agree that 指大部分專家接受某觀點可能正確或有充分支持。"},{"en":"Most researchers agree that sleep affects learning and memory.","zh":"大多數研究人員同意睡眠會影響學習和記憶。"},{"en":"When many researchers agree, the claim is stronger than one person’s opinion.","zh":"當許多研究人員同意時，該說法比個人意見更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when presenting a broad expert view.","zh":"呈現廣泛專家觀點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"complex interaction","meaning":"複雜的相互作用","examples":[{"en":"Child development involves a complex interaction of genes and environment.","zh":"兒童發展涉及基因和環境的複雜相互作用。"},{"en":"A complex interaction means several factors affect each other in complicated ways.","zh":"complex interaction 指幾個因素以複雜方式互相影響。"},{"en":"A student’s performance may result from a complex interaction of sleep, teaching, confidence, and home support.","zh":"學生表現可能來自睡眠、教學、信心和家庭支援的複雜相互作用。"},{"en":"When factors interact, changing one factor may change the effect of another.","zh":"當因素互動時，改變一個因素可能改變另一個因素的效果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when simple cause-and-effect is not enough.","zh":"當簡單因果不足以解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"aspects of development","meaning":"發展的不同方面","examples":[{"en":"Some aspects of development are strongly influenced by biology.","zh":"發展的某些方面深受生物因素影響。"},{"en":"Aspects of development are different parts of how a child grows and changes.","zh":"aspects of development 指兒童成長和變化的不同部分。"},{"en":"Language, height, emotional control, and social skills are aspects of development.","zh":"語言、身高、情緒控制和社交技能都是發展的不同方面。"},{"en":"Different aspects of development may be affected by different causes.","zh":"發展的不同方面可能受到不同原因影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when development is divided into separate areas.","zh":"當發展被分成不同範疇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be strongly influenced by","meaning":"深受……影響","examples":[{"en":"The timing of puberty is strongly influenced by heredity.","zh":"青春期開始的時間深受遺傳影響。"},{"en":"To be strongly influenced by something means to be greatly affected by it.","zh":"be strongly influenced by something 指受到某物很大影響。"},{"en":"A child’s accent may be strongly influenced by the people around them.","zh":"兒童的口音可能深受身邊人影響。"},{"en":"Strong influence does not mean other factors have no effect at all.","zh":"強烈影響不代表其他因素完全沒有作用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one factor plays a major role.","zh":"當某因素扮演主要角色時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"play a role","meaning":"發揮作用","examples":[{"en":"Environmental influences also play a role in development.","zh":"環境影響也在發展中發揮作用。"},{"en":"To play a role means to have some effect or importance in a situation.","zh":"play a role 指在某情況中有影響或重要性。"},{"en":"Parents, teachers, and friends all play a role in a child’s confidence.","zh":"父母、老師和朋友都在兒童信心中發揮作用。"},{"en":"Even a small factor can play a role when combined with many others.","zh":"即使是小因素，與許多其他因素結合時也可以發揮作用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when adding another contributing factor.","zh":"加入另一個影響因素時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"timing of puberty","meaning":"青春期開始的時間","examples":[{"en":"The timing of puberty is largely influenced by heredity.","zh":"青春期開始的時間主要受遺傳影響。"},{"en":"Timing of puberty means when a young person begins the physical changes of adolescence.","zh":"timing of puberty 指年輕人何時開始青春期的身體變化。"},{"en":"Doctors may discuss the timing of puberty if a child develops much earlier or later than classmates.","zh":"如果孩子比同學早很多或遲很多發育，醫生可能討論青春期開始時間。"},{"en":"Genes can influence puberty timing, but health and nutrition may also matter.","zh":"基因可以影響青春期時間，但健康和營養也可能重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing biological development.","zh":"討論生物發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"largely the result of","meaning":"主要是……的結果","examples":[{"en":"Puberty timing is largely the result of heredity.","zh":"青春期開始時間主要是遺傳的結果。"},{"en":"Largely the result of means mostly caused by something, though not necessarily only by it.","zh":"largely the result of 指主要由某事造成，但不一定只由它造成。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be largely the result of daily practice.","zh":"學生進步可能主要是每日練習的結果。"},{"en":"If something is largely the result of one factor, other factors may still have smaller effects.","zh":"如果某事主要是一個因素的結果，其他因素仍可能有較小影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying the main cause.","zh":"指出主要原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"heredity","meaning":"遺傳","examples":[{"en":"Heredity can influence physical development.","zh":"遺傳可以影響身體發展。"},{"en":"Heredity is the passing of traits from parents to children through genes.","zh":"heredity 指透過基因把特徵由父母傳給子女。"},{"en":"Hair colour, eye colour, and some health risks can be affected by heredity.","zh":"髮色、眼睛顏色和某些健康風險都可以受遺傳影響。"},{"en":"Heredity can set tendencies, but environment can influence how they appear.","zh":"遺傳可以設定傾向，但環境可以影響它們如何表現。"},{"en":"This word is central to biological explanations of development.","zh":"這個詞是發展的生物解釋中的核心詞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have an effect","meaning":"產生影響","examples":[{"en":"Environmental factors such as nutrition can also have an effect.","zh":"營養等環境因素也可以產生影響。"},{"en":"To have an effect means to influence something or cause a change.","zh":"have an effect 指影響某事或造成改變。"},{"en":"A kind teacher can have an effect on a shy student’s confidence.","zh":"仁慈的老師可以對害羞學生的信心產生影響。"},{"en":"Small habits may have a large effect if repeated for years.","zh":"小習慣如果持續多年，可能產生很大影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing influence.","zh":"討論影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"from the earliest moments of life","meaning":"從生命最初階段開始","examples":[{"en":"Nature and nurture interact from the earliest moments of life.","zh":"先天與後天從生命最初階段開始互動。"},{"en":"From the earliest moments of life means from the very beginning of a person’s existence.","zh":"from the earliest moments of life 指從一個人生命存在的最早開始。"},{"en":"Babies begin learning sounds from the earliest moments of life.","zh":"嬰兒從生命最初階段開始學習聲音。"},{"en":"Early care can matter because development begins before a child can speak.","zh":"早期照顧可能很重要，因為發展在孩子會說話前已開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing that influence starts very early.","zh":"強調影響很早開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"interaction of heredity and environment","meaning":"遺傳與環境的相互作用","examples":[{"en":"The interaction of heredity and environment shapes development.","zh":"遺傳與環境的相互作用塑造發展。"},{"en":"The interaction of heredity and environment means the way genes and surroundings work together.","zh":"interaction of heredity and environment 指基因和周圍環境如何共同作用。"},{"en":"A child may inherit musical ability, but lessons and practice affect how far it develops.","zh":"孩子可能遺傳音樂能力，但課堂和練習會影響它發展到甚麼程度。"},{"en":"Genes may create potential, while environment can support or limit that potential.","zh":"基因可能創造潛能，而環境可以支持或限制這種潛能。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining nature and nurture together.","zh":"一起解釋先天與後天時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"work to shape","meaning":"共同塑造","examples":[{"en":"Genes and experience work together to shape a child’s future.","zh":"基因和經驗共同塑造兒童的未來。"},{"en":"Work to shape means help form, influence, or direct how something develops.","zh":"work to shape 指幫助形成、影響或引導某事如何發展。"},{"en":"Good teachers and daily reading work together to shape stronger writing habits.","zh":"好老師和每日閱讀共同塑造更強的寫作習慣。"},{"en":"Several influences can work together and create an effect none would create alone.","zh":"幾個影響因素可以共同作用，創造單一因素不會造成的效果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when different factors jointly affect a result.","zh":"當不同因素共同影響結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"genetic instructions","meaning":"遺傳指令","examples":[{"en":"A child inherits genetic instructions from their parents.","zh":"兒童從父母遺傳得到遺傳指令。"},{"en":"Genetic instructions are information in genes that guides how the body develops and functions.","zh":"genetic instructions 指基因中的資訊，指導身體如何發展和運作。"},{"en":"A recipe gives instructions for making food; genes give biological instructions for growth.","zh":"食譜給予製作食物的指令；基因則給予成長的生物指令。"},{"en":"Genetic instructions can influence traits, but the environment affects how some instructions are expressed.","zh":"遺傳指令可以影響特徵，但環境會影響某些指令如何表現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when genes are compared to a plan or code.","zh":"把基因比作計劃或編碼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"inherit from","meaning":"從……遺傳","examples":[{"en":"Children inherit genetic material from their parents.","zh":"兒童從父母遺傳基因材料。"},{"en":"To inherit from someone means to receive something from them, often through family or genetics.","zh":"inherit from someone 指從某人獲得某物，通常透過家庭或遺傳。"},{"en":"A child may inherit eye colour from one parent and hair texture from the other.","zh":"孩子可能從一位父母遺傳眼睛顏色，從另一位父母遺傳髮質。"},{"en":"People can inherit property, habits, names, or biological traits.","zh":"人可以繼承財產、習慣、姓名或生物特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is passed down.","zh":"當某物被傳下來時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"set out a road map for","meaning":"為……訂立發展藍圖","examples":[{"en":"Genes may set out a road map for development.","zh":"基因可能為發展訂立藍圖。"},{"en":"To set out a road map for something means to provide a basic plan or direction for it.","zh":"set out a road map for something 指為某事提供基本計劃或方向。"},{"en":"A school improvement plan can set out a road map for better teaching.","zh":"學校改善計劃可以為更好教學訂立發展藍圖。"},{"en":"Genes may guide development, but the environment can affect the route taken.","zh":"基因可能指導發展，但環境可以影響實際路線。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a guiding plan.","zh":"描述指導性計劃時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"road map for development","meaning":"發展藍圖","examples":[{"en":"Genetic instructions provide a road map for development.","zh":"遺傳指令提供發展藍圖。"},{"en":"A road map for development is a guiding plan that shows how growth may proceed.","zh":"road map for development 指顯示成長可能如何進行的指導計劃。"},{"en":"A teacher may create a road map for development for a student’s writing skills.","zh":"老師可能為學生寫作能力制定發展藍圖。"},{"en":"A road map gives direction, but real progress may change with conditions.","zh":"藍圖提供方向，但真正進展可能隨條件改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a plan for growth.","zh":"描述成長計劃時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"impact how","meaning":"影響……如何","examples":[{"en":"The environment can impact how genetic directions are expressed.","zh":"環境可以影響遺傳方向如何被表現出來。"},{"en":"Impact how means affect the way something happens or appears.","zh":"impact how 指影響某事發生或呈現的方式。"},{"en":"A teacher’s feedback can impact how confidently a student writes.","zh":"老師的回饋可以影響學生寫作時有多自信。"},{"en":"Nutrition and stress can affect how some biological tendencies appear.","zh":"營養和壓力可以影響某些生物傾向如何表現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the influence is on the manner, not just the result.","zh":"當影響的是方式而不只是結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be expressed","meaning":"被表現出來","examples":[{"en":"Genetic tendencies may be expressed differently in different environments.","zh":"遺傳傾向可能在不同環境中以不同方式被表現出來。"},{"en":"Be expressed means be shown, revealed, or made visible.","zh":"be expressed 指被展示、顯露或變得可見。"},{"en":"A child’s confidence may be expressed through speaking more in class.","zh":"兒童的信心可能透過在課堂上更常發言而表現出來。"},{"en":"A tendency may exist quietly until the right environment allows it to appear.","zh":"一種傾向可能安靜存在，直到合適環境讓它出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when hidden qualities become visible.","zh":"當隱藏特質變得可見時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be shaped or silenced","meaning":"被塑造或抑制","examples":[{"en":"Environmental conditions can cause genetic tendencies to be shaped or silenced.","zh":"環境條件可以令遺傳傾向被塑造或抑制。"},{"en":"Be shaped or silenced means be developed in a certain way or prevented from appearing.","zh":"be shaped or silenced 指被以某種方式發展，或被阻止表現出來。"},{"en":"A child’s curiosity can be shaped by good questions or silenced by constant criticism.","zh":"兒童的好奇心可以由好問題塑造，也可以被不斷批評抑制。"},{"en":"Supportive surroundings may strengthen a tendency, while harsh surroundings may suppress it.","zh":"支持性環境可能強化某種傾向，而嚴苛環境可能抑制它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an influence can either develop or block a trait.","zh":"當影響可以發展或阻礙特質時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"occur at certain moments","meaning":"在特定時刻發生","examples":[{"en":"The interaction does not occur only at certain moments.","zh":"這種相互作用並不只在特定時刻發生。"},{"en":"Occur at certain moments means happen at specific points in time.","zh":"occur at certain moments 指在特定時間點發生。"},{"en":"A child’s fear may occur at certain moments, such as before exams or medical appointments.","zh":"兒童的恐懼可能在特定時刻出現，例如考試或看醫生前。"},{"en":"Some influences happen at one moment, but development often continues over time.","zh":"有些影響在某一刻發生，但發展通常會持續一段時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing timing.","zh":"討論時間點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"periods of time","meaning":"一段段時期","examples":[{"en":"Development continues across different periods of time.","zh":"發展會跨越不同時期持續進行。"},{"en":"Periods of time are lengths of time, such as days, years, or life stages.","zh":"periods of time 指時間長度，例如數天、數年或人生階段。"},{"en":"A teacher may compare students’ progress across different periods of time.","zh":"老師可能比較學生在不同時期的進步。"},{"en":"Some changes are visible after weeks, while others appear over years.","zh":"有些變化幾星期後可見，另一些則需多年才出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing development over time.","zh":"討論隨時間發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"persistent and lifelong","meaning":"持續一生的","examples":[{"en":"The interaction between nature and nurture is persistent and lifelong.","zh":"先天與後天之間的相互作用是持續一生的。"},{"en":"Persistent and lifelong means continuing for a long time and throughout life.","zh":"persistent and lifelong 指長期持續並貫穿一生。"},{"en":"Reading habits can have persistent and lifelong effects on learning.","zh":"閱讀習慣可以對學習產生持續一生的影響。"},{"en":"Development does not stop in childhood because genes and experience continue to interact.","zh":"發展不會在童年停止，因為基因和經驗會繼續互動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an influence continues rather than disappears quickly.","zh":"當影響會持續而不是很快消失時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"shared environment","meaning":"共享環境","examples":[{"en":"A shared environment includes influences experienced by siblings together.","zh":"共享環境包括兄弟姊妹共同經歷的影響。"},{"en":"Shared environment means the surroundings or experiences that brothers and sisters have in common.","zh":"shared environment 指兄弟姊妹共同擁有的環境或經歷。"},{"en":"Siblings may share the same home, parents, school district, and family routines.","zh":"兄弟姊妹可能共享同一個家、父母、學區和家庭規律。"},{"en":"Shared environments can make children in one family more similar.","zh":"共享環境可以令同一家庭中的兒童更相似。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing what siblings experience together.","zh":"討論兄弟姊妹共同經歷甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"common environment","meaning":"共同環境","examples":[{"en":"Shared environment is also called common environment.","zh":"共享環境也稱為共同環境。"},{"en":"Common environment means the environment shared by members of the same family or group.","zh":"common environment 指同一家庭或群體成員共同擁有的環境。"},{"en":"Children in the same classroom have a common environment during school hours.","zh":"同一課室中的兒童在上課時間有共同環境。"},{"en":"A common environment can shape similar habits, language, and expectations.","zh":"共同環境可以塑造相似習慣、語言和期望。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful as another term for shared environment.","zh":"這個短語可作 shared environment 的另一說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"指的是","examples":[{"en":"The term refers to influences that make siblings more alike.","zh":"這個術語指的是令兄弟姊妹更相似的影響。"},{"en":"To refer to something means to mean, describe, or point to it.","zh":"refer to something 指意思是、描述或指向某事。"},{"en":"In grammar, the word “they” can refer to a group of people.","zh":"在文法中，they 這個詞可以指一群人。"},{"en":"Clear definitions help students know exactly what a term refers to.","zh":"清楚定義幫助學生知道術語確切指的是甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining terminology.","zh":"解釋術語時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"environmental influences","meaning":"環境影響","examples":[{"en":"Environmental influences can affect children in different ways.","zh":"環境影響可以以不同方式影響兒童。"},{"en":"Environmental influences are effects from surroundings, experiences, people, and social conditions.","zh":"environmental influences 指來自周圍環境、經歷、人和社會條件的影響。"},{"en":"A child’s neighbourhood, teachers, friends, and diet can all be environmental influences.","zh":"兒童的社區、老師、朋友和飲食都可以是環境影響。"},{"en":"The same environmental influence may affect two children differently.","zh":"同一環境影響可能以不同方式影響兩名兒童。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing non-genetic causes.","zh":"討論非遺傳原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have the effect of","meaning":"產生……的作用","examples":[{"en":"Shared experiences may have the effect of making siblings more similar.","zh":"共同經歷可能產生令兄弟姊妹更相似的作用。"},{"en":"To have the effect of doing something means to produce that result.","zh":"have the effect of doing something 指產生某個結果。"},{"en":"A strict homework routine may have the effect of improving study habits.","zh":"嚴格功課規律可能產生改善學習習慣的作用。"},{"en":"A shared family rule can make siblings behave more similarly at home.","zh":"共同家庭規則可以令兄弟姊妹在家中行為更相似。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a result caused by an action or condition.","zh":"描述由行動或條件造成的結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make siblings more similar","meaning":"令兄弟姊妹更相似","examples":[{"en":"A shared environment may make siblings more similar to one another.","zh":"共享環境可能令兄弟姊妹彼此更相似。"},{"en":"To make siblings more similar means to cause brothers and sisters to become more alike.","zh":"make siblings more similar 指令兄弟姊妹變得更相像。"},{"en":"Growing up with the same bedtime routine may make siblings more similar in sleep habits.","zh":"在相同睡覺規律下長大，可能令兄弟姊妹在睡眠習慣上更相似。"},{"en":"Shared schools and family rules can create similar expectations and behaviour.","zh":"共同學校和家庭規則可以創造相似期望和行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining shared environmental effects.","zh":"解釋共享環境效應時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"shared family experiences","meaning":"共同家庭經歷","examples":[{"en":"Shared family experiences form part of the common environment.","zh":"共同家庭經歷構成共同環境的一部分。"},{"en":"Shared family experiences are events and routines that family members go through together.","zh":"shared family experiences 指家庭成員一起經歷的事件和日常規律。"},{"en":"Family meals, holidays, arguments, and moving house can be shared family experiences.","zh":"家庭飯局、假期、爭執和搬屋都可以是共同家庭經歷。"},{"en":"Such experiences can create common memories and similar expectations among siblings.","zh":"這些經歷可以在兄弟姊妹之間創造共同記憶和相似期望。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing what children in one family share.","zh":"討論同一家庭兒童共享甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"shared peer groups","meaning":"共同朋輩群組","examples":[{"en":"Siblings may sometimes belong to shared peer groups.","zh":"兄弟姊妹有時可能屬於共同朋輩群組。"},{"en":"Shared peer groups are groups of friends or classmates that siblings have in common.","zh":"shared peer groups 指兄弟姊妹共同擁有的朋友或同學群體。"},{"en":"Two brothers may join the same football team and share the same group of friends.","zh":"兩兄弟可能加入同一支足球隊，並有同一群朋友。"},{"en":"Shared peer groups can make siblings adopt similar language, interests, or behaviour.","zh":"共同朋輩群組可以令兄弟姊妹採用相似語言、興趣或行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when friends are part of a shared environment.","zh":"當朋友屬於共享環境的一部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the same school and community","meaning":"相同的學校和社區","examples":[{"en":"Siblings may share the same school and community.","zh":"兄弟姊妹可能共享相同的學校和社區。"},{"en":"The same school and community means the children attend the same school and live in the same local area.","zh":"same school and community 指兒童就讀同一學校並生活在同一本地區域。"},{"en":"Two sisters may meet the same teachers and neighbours because they grow up in the same community.","zh":"兩姊妹可能因在同一社區長大而遇到相同老師和鄰居。"},{"en":"Shared places can create shared habits, values, and social expectations.","zh":"共同地方可以創造共同習慣、價值觀和社會期望。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing common surroundings.","zh":"描述共同周圍環境時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"strong evidence for","meaning":"支持……的有力證據","examples":[{"en":"There has not been strong evidence for many shared environmental effects.","zh":"對許多共享環境效應，並沒有有力證據支持。"},{"en":"Strong evidence for something means reliable proof or support showing that it is likely true.","zh":"strong evidence for something 指可靠證明或支持，顯示某事很可能是真的。"},{"en":"A doctor needs strong evidence for a treatment before recommending it widely.","zh":"醫生在廣泛建議一種療法前，需要有力證據支持。"},{"en":"Without strong evidence, researchers must be careful about making firm claims.","zh":"沒有有力證據時，研究人員必須小心作出肯定說法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in academic and scientific writing.","zh":"這個短語適用於學術和科學寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"environmental effects","meaning":"環境效應","examples":[{"en":"Some environmental effects are more evident during childhood.","zh":"某些環境效應在童年期間更明顯。"},{"en":"Environmental effects are changes or influences caused by surroundings and experiences.","zh":"environmental effects 指由周圍環境和經歷造成的變化或影響。"},{"en":"A noisy classroom can have environmental effects on students’ concentration.","zh":"嘈雜課室可以對學生專注力產生環境效應。"},{"en":"Environmental effects may change as children grow older and choose different surroundings.","zh":"隨着兒童長大並選擇不同環境，環境效應可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing how environment affects outcomes.","zh":"描述環境如何影響結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be measured in adults","meaning":"在成年人身上量度","examples":[{"en":"Many behaviours have been measured in adults.","zh":"許多行為已在成年人身上量度。"},{"en":"Be measured in adults means be studied or recorded in grown-up people.","zh":"be measured in adults 指在成年人身上被研究或記錄。"},{"en":"Researchers may measure stress levels in adults before and after a workplace change.","zh":"研究人員可能在工作場所改變前後量度成年人壓力水平。"},{"en":"Results measured in adults may not always apply directly to children.","zh":"在成年人身上量度的結果未必能直接適用於兒童。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying the age group in a study.","zh":"指出研究年齡組別時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be evident in","meaning":"在……中明顯可見","examples":[{"en":"Shared environmental effects are evident in children and adolescents.","zh":"共享環境效應在兒童和青少年中明顯可見。"},{"en":"Be evident in means be clearly seen or noticeable in a particular group or situation.","zh":"be evident in 指在某群體或情況中清楚可見或可注意到。"},{"en":"A student’s nervousness may be evident in their shaking voice.","zh":"學生的緊張可能在顫抖的聲音中明顯可見。"},{"en":"If an effect is evident in children, researchers can observe it more clearly at that age.","zh":"如果某效應在兒童中明顯可見，研究人員就能在該年齡更清楚觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing visible signs.","zh":"描述可見跡象時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"children and adolescents","meaning":"兒童和青少年","examples":[{"en":"Shared environmental effects are stronger in children and adolescents.","zh":"共享環境效應在兒童和青少年身上較強。"},{"en":"Children and adolescents means young people from childhood through the teenage years.","zh":"children and adolescents 指從童年到青少年階段的年輕人。"},{"en":"Schools must consider the emotional needs of children and adolescents.","zh":"學校必須考慮兒童和青少年的情緒需要。"},{"en":"Influences may be stronger at these ages because young people are still developing rapidly.","zh":"這些年齡的影響可能較強，因為年輕人仍在快速發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in education, psychology, and health.","zh":"這個短語適用於教育、心理學和健康。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"decrease across the life span","meaning":"隨一生逐漸減弱","examples":[{"en":"Shared environmental effects generally decrease across the life span.","zh":"共享環境效應通常隨一生逐漸減弱。"},{"en":"Decrease across the life span means become weaker as a person moves through life.","zh":"decrease across the life span 指隨着一個人走過人生階段而變弱。"},{"en":"Parental control may decrease across the life span as children become adults.","zh":"隨着孩子成為成年人，父母控制可能隨一生逐漸減弱。"},{"en":"Some shared family influences fade when siblings choose different schools, jobs, and friends.","zh":"當兄弟姊妹選擇不同學校、工作和朋友，一些共同家庭影響會淡化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an effect changes with age.","zh":"當效應隨年齡改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"new developments in","meaning":"……方面的新發展","examples":[{"en":"New developments in behavioural genetics have improved research methods.","zh":"行為遺傳學方面的新發展改善了研究方法。"},{"en":"New developments in something are recent changes, discoveries, or improvements in that field.","zh":"new developments in something 指某領域近期的變化、發現或改善。"},{"en":"New developments in teaching technology allow students to practise speaking online.","zh":"教學科技方面的新發展讓學生能在網上練習口語。"},{"en":"New research tools can make old questions easier to study.","zh":"新研究工具可以令舊問題更容易研究。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing progress in a field.","zh":"討論某領域進展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"behavior genetic methods","meaning":"行為遺傳學研究方法","examples":[{"en":"Behavior genetic methods help researchers study family similarities.","zh":"行為遺傳學研究方法幫助研究人員研究家庭相似性。"},{"en":"Behavior genetic methods are research tools used to study how genes and environment affect behaviour.","zh":"behavior genetic methods 指用來研究基因和環境如何影響行為的研究工具。"},{"en":"Twin studies are one type of behaviour genetic method.","zh":"雙生子研究是一種行為遺傳學方法。"},{"en":"These methods help researchers separate inherited influences from environmental ones.","zh":"這些方法幫助研究人員分開遺傳影響和環境影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is technical and common in psychology research.","zh":"這個短語較技術性，常見於心理學研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make it possible to","meaning":"令……成為可能","examples":[{"en":"New techniques make it possible to identify important environments.","zh":"新技術令識別重要環境成為可能。"},{"en":"Make it possible to means allow something to happen or become achievable.","zh":"make it possible to 指讓某事能夠發生或變得可達成。"},{"en":"Online dictionaries make it possible to check pronunciation quickly.","zh":"網上字典令快速查發音成為可能。"},{"en":"Better research designs make it possible to study hidden influences more carefully.","zh":"更好的研究設計令更仔細研究隱藏影響成為可能。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining what a tool or change enables.","zh":"解釋工具或改變能帶來甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"specify shared environments","meaning":"確定重要的共享環境","examples":[{"en":"Researchers can now specify shared environments of importance.","zh":"研究人員現在可以確定重要的共享環境。"},{"en":"To specify shared environments means to identify exactly which common surroundings or experiences matter.","zh":"specify shared environments 指準確指出哪些共同環境或經歷重要。"},{"en":"A school study may specify classroom noise as a shared environment affecting all pupils.","zh":"學校研究可能把課室噪音確定為影響所有學生的共享環境。"},{"en":"Naming the exact shared environment helps researchers move beyond vague explanations.","zh":"指出確切共享環境有助研究人員超越模糊解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research becomes more precise.","zh":"當研究變得更精準時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"of importance","meaning":"重要的","examples":[{"en":"Researchers aim to identify environmental factors of importance.","zh":"研究人員旨在識別重要的環境因素。"},{"en":"Of importance means important or worth attention.","zh":"of importance 指重要或值得注意。"},{"en":"A teacher may list grammar points of importance before an exam.","zh":"老師可能在考試前列出重要文法點。"},{"en":"Identifying factors of importance helps people focus on what really matters.","zh":"識別重要因素幫助人們專注真正要緊的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and common in academic writing.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常見於學術寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tease apart","meaning":"區分；拆解分析","examples":[{"en":"Researchers try to tease apart genetic and environmental influences.","zh":"研究人員嘗試區分遺傳和環境影響。"},{"en":"To tease apart two things means to separate them carefully when they are mixed together.","zh":"tease apart two things 指在兩者混在一起時仔細分開它們。"},{"en":"A teacher may tease apart grammar mistakes and vocabulary mistakes in a student’s essay.","zh":"老師可能在學生文章中區分文法錯誤和詞彙錯誤。"},{"en":"When causes overlap, researchers need careful methods to separate them.","zh":"當原因互相重疊，研究人員需要仔細方法來分開它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when complex factors are difficult to distinguish.","zh":"當複雜因素難以辨別時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"familial sources","meaning":"家庭來源","examples":[{"en":"Familial sources arise from experiences within the family.","zh":"家庭來源來自家庭內部的經歷。"},{"en":"Familial sources are causes or influences that come from the family setting.","zh":"familial sources 指來自家庭環境的原因或影響。"},{"en":"Parents’ routines, sibling relationships, and family income can be familial sources of influence.","zh":"父母規律、兄弟姊妹關係和家庭收入都可以是影響的家庭來源。"},{"en":"Familial sources may affect all siblings or only some siblings in different ways.","zh":"家庭來源可能影響所有兄弟姊妹，也可能以不同方式只影響部分人。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when tracing influence back to the family.","zh":"把影響追溯到家庭時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"nonfamilial sources","meaning":"非家庭來源","examples":[{"en":"Nonfamilial sources include influences outside the family.","zh":"非家庭來源包括家庭以外的影響。"},{"en":"Nonfamilial sources are causes or influences that come from outside family life.","zh":"nonfamilial sources 指來自家庭生活以外的原因或影響。"},{"en":"Friends, teachers, neighbourhoods, and online communities can be nonfamilial sources of influence.","zh":"朋友、老師、社區和網上社群都可以是非家庭影響來源。"},{"en":"These sources can make siblings different even if they share the same home.","zh":"即使兄弟姊妹共享同一家庭，這些來源也可以令他們不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining influences beyond family.","zh":"解釋家庭以外的影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rate of influence","meaning":"影響比例","examples":[{"en":"The rate of influence of the shared environment is relatively low.","zh":"共享環境的影響比例相對較低。"},{"en":"Rate of influence means the amount or proportion of effect a factor has.","zh":"rate of influence 指某因素具有的影響量或比例。"},{"en":"A study may compare the rate of influence of sleep, diet, and exercise on exam performance.","zh":"研究可能比較睡眠、飲食和運動對考試表現的影響比例。"},{"en":"A low rate of influence suggests the factor explains only a small part of the difference.","zh":"低影響比例暗示該因素只能解釋差異中的小部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when influence is measured quantitatively.","zh":"當影響以數量方式量度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"non-shared environment","meaning":"非共享環境","examples":[{"en":"The non-shared environment affects siblings differently.","zh":"非共享環境以不同方式影響兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"Non-shared environment means experiences that are not the same for each child in a family.","zh":"non-shared environment 指同一家庭中每個孩子並不相同的經歷。"},{"en":"One sibling may have a strict teacher, while another has a supportive teacher.","zh":"一個兄弟姊妹可能遇到嚴厲老師，另一個則遇到支持性老師。"},{"en":"Non-shared environments can help explain why siblings grow up differently.","zh":"非共享環境可以幫助解釋兄弟姊妹為何成長得不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in behavioural genetics.","zh":"這個短語在行為遺傳學中很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lie hidden within","meaning":"隱藏於……之中","examples":[{"en":"The importance of the non-shared environment lay hidden within earlier studies.","zh":"非共享環境的重要性隱藏於早期研究之中。"},{"en":"Lie hidden within means exist inside something but not be noticed immediately.","zh":"lie hidden within 指存在於某物之中，但沒有立即被注意到。"},{"en":"A common writing mistake may lie hidden within a student’s fluent essay.","zh":"常見寫作錯誤可能隱藏於學生流暢的文章之中。"},{"en":"Important findings can remain unnoticed until researchers look at the data differently.","zh":"重要發現可能一直未被注意，直到研究人員以不同方式看數據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something is present but not obvious.","zh":"當某物存在但不明顯時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"quantitative genetic studies","meaning":"數量遺傳學研究","examples":[{"en":"Quantitative genetic studies compare genetic and environmental effects.","zh":"數量遺傳學研究比較遺傳和環境效應。"},{"en":"Quantitative genetic studies use numbers and statistical methods to study genetic influence.","zh":"quantitative genetic studies 指使用數字和統計方法研究遺傳影響的研究。"},{"en":"Researchers may use quantitative genetic studies to compare similarities between twins.","zh":"研究人員可能使用數量遺傳學研究來比較雙生子的相似性。"},{"en":"These studies can estimate how much variation is linked to genes or environment.","zh":"這些研究可以估算有多少變異與基因或環境有關。"},{"en":"This phrase is technical and common in psychology and genetics.","zh":"這個短語較技術性，常見於心理學和遺傳學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"nearly a century ago","meaning":"接近一個世紀前","examples":[{"en":"Quantitative genetic research began nearly a century ago.","zh":"數量遺傳學研究在接近一個世紀前開始。"},{"en":"Nearly a century ago means almost one hundred years ago.","zh":"nearly a century ago 指差不多一百年前。"},{"en":"Nearly a century ago, many schools used very different teaching methods from today.","zh":"接近一個世紀前，許多學校使用與今天非常不同的教學方法。"},{"en":"A research tradition that began nearly a century ago has a long history of development.","zh":"接近一個世紀前開始的研究傳統有長久發展歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving historical timing.","zh":"提供歷史時間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"quantitative genetic methods","meaning":"數量遺傳學方法","examples":[{"en":"Researchers use quantitative genetic methods to study resemblance.","zh":"研究人員使用數量遺傳學方法研究相似性。"},{"en":"Quantitative genetic methods are statistical tools used to estimate genetic and environmental contributions.","zh":"quantitative genetic methods 指用來估算遺傳和環境貢獻的統計工具。"},{"en":"Twin data can be analysed with quantitative genetic methods.","zh":"雙生子數據可以用數量遺傳學方法分析。"},{"en":"These methods help researchers move from general guesses to measured estimates.","zh":"這些方法幫助研究人員由一般猜測走向量化估算。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in technical discussions of heredity and environment.","zh":"在遺傳和環境的技術討論中，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"twin and adoption methods","meaning":"雙生子和領養研究方法","examples":[{"en":"Twin and adoption methods help separate nature from nurture.","zh":"雙生子和領養研究方法幫助分開先天與後天。"},{"en":"Twin and adoption methods are research designs comparing twins or adopted children to study genes and environment.","zh":"twin and adoption methods 指比較雙生子或領養兒童，以研究基因和環境的研究設計。"},{"en":"Adoption studies can compare children with biological and adoptive relatives.","zh":"領養研究可以比較兒童與親生親屬和養育親屬。"},{"en":"These methods help researchers see whether similarity comes more from genes or shared upbringing.","zh":"這些方法幫助研究人員看相似性更多來自基因還是共同教養。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in behavioural genetics.","zh":"這個短語適用於行為遺傳學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"explain family resemblance","meaning":"解釋家庭成員間的相似性","examples":[{"en":"Researchers use genetic methods to explain family resemblance.","zh":"研究人員使用遺傳方法解釋家庭成員間的相似性。"},{"en":"To explain family resemblance means to show why relatives are similar in appearance, behaviour, or traits.","zh":"explain family resemblance 指說明親屬在外貌、行為或特質上為何相似。"},{"en":"A child and parent may share facial features, and genetics can explain part of that resemblance.","zh":"孩子和父母可能有相似臉部特徵，遺傳可以解釋其中一部分相似性。"},{"en":"Family resemblance can come from genes, shared environment, or both.","zh":"家庭相似性可以來自基因、共享環境或兩者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when studying why relatives are alike.","zh":"研究親屬為何相似時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"complex phenotypes","meaning":"複雜表型","examples":[{"en":"Complex phenotypes are influenced by multiple genetic and environmental factors.","zh":"複雜表型受多個遺傳和環境因素影響。"},{"en":"Complex phenotypes are observable traits shaped by many causes, not just one gene.","zh":"complex phenotypes 指由許多原因塑造、而非單一基因決定的可觀察特徵。"},{"en":"Intelligence, personality, height, and mental health can be complex phenotypes.","zh":"智力、性格、身高和心理健康都可以是複雜表型。"},{"en":"Because many factors are involved, complex phenotypes are difficult to explain completely.","zh":"由於涉及許多因素，複雜表型很難被完整解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is technical and useful in genetics.","zh":"這個短語較技術性，適用於遺傳學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"it has emerged that","meaning":"研究顯示","examples":[{"en":"It has emerged that family resemblance is largely genetic.","zh":"研究顯示，家庭成員間的相似性主要是遺傳性的。"},{"en":"It has emerged that means research or evidence has gradually shown something to be true.","zh":"it has emerged that 指研究或證據逐漸顯示某事為真。"},{"en":"It has emerged that students learn vocabulary better when they meet words in context.","zh":"研究顯示，學生在語境中接觸詞彙時學得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the conclusion became clear over time.","zh":"這個短語暗示結論隨時間逐漸清楚。"},{"en":"It is useful when reporting research findings.","zh":"報告研究發現時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the origins of","meaning":"……的起源","examples":[{"en":"Researchers investigate the origins of family resemblance.","zh":"研究人員調查家庭相似性的起源。"},{"en":"The origins of something are the causes, beginnings, or sources of it.","zh":"origins of something 指某事的原因、開始或來源。"},{"en":"Historians investigate the origins of a festival to understand why people celebrate it.","zh":"歷史學家調查節日的起源，以理解人們為何慶祝。"},{"en":"Knowing the origins of a trait helps researchers judge whether genes or environment matter more.","zh":"了解一種特質的起源，有助研究人員判斷基因還是環境更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when asking where something comes from.","zh":"詢問某事從何而來時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"run in families","meaning":"在家族中遺傳","examples":[{"en":"Many characteristics run in families primarily for genetic reasons.","zh":"許多特徵主要因遺傳原因在家族中出現。"},{"en":"To run in families means to appear often among members of the same family.","zh":"run in families 指某特徵經常出現在同一家族成員中。"},{"en":"Musical ability may run in families, especially when both genes and practice are involved.","zh":"音樂能力可能在家族中出現，尤其當基因和練習都涉及時。"},{"en":"If a health condition runs in families, doctors may ask about family medical history.","zh":"如果某健康狀況在家族中遺傳，醫生可能詢問家族病史。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when traits appear repeatedly among relatives.","zh":"當特質反覆出現在親屬之間時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"primarily for genetic reasons","meaning":"主要出於遺傳原因","examples":[{"en":"Many family similarities occur primarily for genetic reasons.","zh":"許多家庭相似性主要出於遺傳原因。"},{"en":"Primarily for genetic reasons means mainly because of inherited genes.","zh":"primarily for genetic reasons 指主要因遺傳基因而發生。"},{"en":"Two siblings may look alike primarily for genetic reasons.","zh":"兩名兄弟姊妹可能主要出於遺傳原因而長得相似。"},{"en":"Saying primarily does not mean environment has no role at all.","zh":"說 primarily 不代表環境完全沒有作用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying the main biological cause.","zh":"指出主要生物原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"best available evidence","meaning":"現有最可靠的證據","examples":[{"en":"The best available evidence comes from quantitative genetic research.","zh":"現有最可靠的證據來自數量遺傳學研究。"},{"en":"Best available evidence means the strongest and most reliable evidence currently known.","zh":"best available evidence 指目前已知最強、最可靠的證據。"},{"en":"Doctors use the best available evidence when choosing treatments for patients.","zh":"醫生為病人選擇治療方法時，會使用現有最可靠的證據。"},{"en":"Evidence may improve over time, so the best available evidence can change.","zh":"證據可能隨時間改善，所以現有最可靠證據也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research is not perfect but still informative.","zh":"當研究不完美但仍有參考價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"explain all of the variance","meaning":"解釋所有變異","examples":[{"en":"Genetic influence cannot explain all of the variance in complex traits.","zh":"遺傳影響不能解釋複雜特徵中的所有變異。"},{"en":"To explain all of the variance means to account for all the differences found between people or results.","zh":"explain all of the variance 指解釋人與人或結果之間的所有差異。"},{"en":"Study time cannot explain all of the variance in exam scores because sleep and teaching also matter.","zh":"學習時間不能解釋考試分數中的所有變異，因為睡眠和教學也重要。"},{"en":"If a factor cannot explain all variance, researchers must look for other causes.","zh":"如果一個因素不能解釋所有變異，研究人員就必須尋找其他原因。"},{"en":"This phrase is technical and common in statistics.","zh":"這個短語較技術性，常見於統計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"remaining variance","meaning":"剩餘變異","examples":[{"en":"The remaining variance is attributed to environmental influence.","zh":"剩餘變異被歸因於環境影響。"},{"en":"Remaining variance means the differences still unexplained after one factor has been considered.","zh":"remaining variance 指考慮某一因素後仍未被解釋的差異。"},{"en":"After accounting for study hours, the remaining variance in test scores may involve sleep, stress, and teaching quality.","zh":"在解釋學習時數後，考試分數的剩餘變異可能涉及睡眠、壓力和教學質素。"},{"en":"Remaining variance reminds researchers that one explanation is rarely complete.","zh":"剩餘變異提醒研究人員，單一解釋很少完整。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in statistical and research writing.","zh":"這個短語適用於統計和研究寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be ascribed to","meaning":"歸因於","examples":[{"en":"The unexplained variance must be ascribed to environmental influences.","zh":"未解釋的變異必須歸因於環境影響。"},{"en":"To be ascribed to something means to be attributed to it as the cause or source.","zh":"be ascribed to something 指被歸因於某事，視其為原因或來源。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be ascribed to lack of sleep rather than laziness.","zh":"學生疲倦可能歸因於睡眠不足，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"If genetic factors do not explain a difference, researchers may ascribe it to environment.","zh":"如果遺傳因素不能解釋差異，研究人員可能把它歸因於環境。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and useful in academic explanation.","zh":"這個短語較正式，適用於學術解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"affect only some siblings","meaning":"只影響部分兄弟姊妹","examples":[{"en":"Non-shared influences may affect only some siblings in a family.","zh":"非共享影響可能只影響家庭中的部分兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"Affect only some siblings means influence one or a few brothers or sisters, but not all of them.","zh":"affect only some siblings 指影響一個或幾個兄弟姊妹，但不是全部。"},{"en":"One child’s serious illness may affect only some siblings if others are too young to remember it.","zh":"一名孩子的嚴重疾病可能只影響部分兄弟姊妹，如果其他人年紀太小而不記得。"},{"en":"Different teachers and friends can affect siblings in different ways.","zh":"不同老師和朋友可以以不同方式影響兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why siblings develop differently.","zh":"解釋兄弟姊妹為何發展不同時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"total influence on children","meaning":"對兒童的整體影響","examples":[{"en":"Non-shared environments account for a large part of the total influence on children.","zh":"非共享環境佔對兒童整體影響的很大部分。"},{"en":"Total influence on children means the whole combined effect of all factors affecting children.","zh":"total influence on children 指所有影響兒童因素加起來的整體效果。"},{"en":"Family, school, friends, health, and media all form part of the total influence on children.","zh":"家庭、學校、朋友、健康和媒體都是對兒童整體影響的一部分。"},{"en":"Looking at total influence prevents researchers from focusing too narrowly on one cause.","zh":"查看整體影響可以避免研究人員過度狹窄地聚焦單一原因。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing overall effects.","zh":"討論整體效果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take many decades for","meaning":"花了數十年才……","examples":[{"en":"It took many decades for the meaning of the findings to emerge.","zh":"這些發現的含意花了數十年才浮現。"},{"en":"Take many decades for something means require many tens of years before it happens or becomes clear.","zh":"take many decades for something 指某事需要數十年才發生或變清楚。"},{"en":"It may take many decades for a city to recover fully from poor planning.","zh":"一個城市可能要花數十年才從糟糕規劃中完全恢復。"},{"en":"Some research findings are not understood immediately because their implications are hidden.","zh":"有些研究發現不會立即被理解，因為其含意是隱藏的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when understanding develops very slowly.","zh":"當理解非常緩慢地發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"full meaning","meaning":"完整含意","examples":[{"en":"The full meaning of the research was not understood immediately.","zh":"研究的完整含意並沒有立即被理解。"},{"en":"Full meaning means the complete importance, implication, or message of something.","zh":"full meaning 指某事完整的重要性、含意或訊息。"},{"en":"A student may not understand the full meaning of a poem after one reading.","zh":"學生讀一次詩後，可能未理解其完整含意。"},{"en":"The full meaning of a discovery may become clear only when later studies confirm it.","zh":"一項發現的完整含意可能只有在後來研究確認後才變清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something has deeper significance.","zh":"當某事有更深層意義時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"grow up in the same family","meaning":"在同一家庭長大","examples":[{"en":"Siblings may grow up in the same family but develop differently.","zh":"兄弟姊妹可能在同一家庭長大，但發展得不同。"},{"en":"Grow up in the same family means spend childhood in the same household or family setting.","zh":"grow up in the same family 指在同一家庭或家庭環境中度過童年。"},{"en":"Two sisters may grow up in the same family but have different friends and teachers.","zh":"兩姊妹可能在同一家庭長大，但有不同朋友和老師。"},{"en":"Shared family life does not guarantee identical personalities.","zh":"共享家庭生活不保證性格完全相同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing siblings.","zh":"比較兄弟姊妹時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"it must be the case that","meaning":"必然是……","examples":[{"en":"It must be the case that some environmental effects are not shared.","zh":"必然是有些環境效應並非共享的。"},{"en":"It must be the case that means the evidence strongly suggests this must be true.","zh":"it must be the case that 指證據強烈顯示某事必定為真。"},{"en":"If two students studied the same notes but one had private tutoring, it must be the case that they had different support.","zh":"如果兩名學生溫習同一份筆記，但其中一人有私人補習，那必然是他們得到不同支援。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to draw a necessary conclusion from evidence.","zh":"這個短語用來從證據推出必要結論。"},{"en":"It is useful in logical reasoning.","zh":"它適用於邏輯推理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"salient environmental effects","meaning":"顯著的環境效應","examples":[{"en":"Salient environmental effects may operate differently for each child.","zh":"顯著的環境效應可能對每名兒童以不同方式發揮作用。"},{"en":"Salient environmental effects are environmental influences that are especially noticeable or important.","zh":"salient environmental effects 指特別明顯或重要的環境影響。"},{"en":"A serious illness in the family may be a salient environmental effect for one child.","zh":"家庭中的嚴重疾病可能對一名兒童成為顯著環境效應。"},{"en":"Salient effects can shape development more strongly than ordinary daily events.","zh":"顯著效應可以比普通日常事件更強烈地塑造發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying the most important environmental influences.","zh":"找出最重要環境影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"implication","meaning":"含意；推論","examples":[{"en":"The findings had an important implication for environmental research.","zh":"這些發現對環境研究有重要含意。"},{"en":"An implication is a meaning, result, or conclusion suggested by something.","zh":"implication 指某事暗示的意思、結果或結論。"},{"en":"If students improve after feedback, the implication is that feedback matters.","zh":"如果學生在回饋後進步，其含意就是回饋很重要。"},{"en":"Research findings may have implications for schools, families, and policy.","zh":"研究發現可能對學校、家庭和政策有含意。"},{"en":"This word is useful when a result suggests a wider lesson.","zh":"當結果暗示更廣泛教訓時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lie fallow","meaning":"長期未被發展；被擱置","examples":[{"en":"The idea of non-shared environments lay fallow for many years.","zh":"非共享環境這個想法多年來被擱置未發展。"},{"en":"Lie fallow means remain unused, undeveloped, or inactive for a period of time.","zh":"lie fallow 指在一段時間內未被使用、未被發展或不活躍。"},{"en":"A good business idea may lie fallow until someone has enough money to develop it.","zh":"好的商業想法可能一直被擱置，直到有人有足夠資金發展它。"},{"en":"Research ideas can lie fallow when scholars focus on other questions.","zh":"當學者聚焦其他問題，研究想法可能長期未被發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is metaphorical and originally comes from unused farmland.","zh":"這個短語是比喻，原本來自閒置農地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"firmly on","meaning":"牢牢集中於……","examples":[{"en":"The field’s attention was firmly on the nature–nurture debate.","zh":"該領域的注意力牢牢集中於先天與後天之爭。"},{"en":"Firmly on means strongly focused on something.","zh":"firmly on 指強烈聚焦於某事。"},{"en":"During exam season, students’ attention is firmly on revision.","zh":"考試季節，學生的注意力牢牢集中於溫習。"},{"en":"When attention is firmly on one issue, other important questions may be ignored.","zh":"當注意力牢牢集中於一個議題，其他重要問題可能被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing strong focus.","zh":"描述強烈聚焦時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be implicitly taken to mean","meaning":"被暗中理解為","examples":[{"en":"Nurture was implicitly taken to mean the shared family environment.","zh":"後天被暗中理解為共享家庭環境。"},{"en":"Be implicitly taken to mean something means be understood in that way without being stated directly.","zh":"be implicitly taken to mean something 指未被直接說明，但被理解為某意思。"},{"en":"In some schools, success is implicitly taken to mean high exam marks.","zh":"在一些學校，成功被暗中理解為高考試分數。"},{"en":"Hidden assumptions can limit how people think about a topic.","zh":"隱藏假設可以限制人們如何思考一個主題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing unstated meanings.","zh":"討論未明言的意思時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"theories of socialization","meaning":"社會化理論","examples":[{"en":"Theories of socialization often focused on family-wide influences.","zh":"社會化理論常聚焦整個家庭層面的影響。"},{"en":"Theories of socialization explain how people learn behaviours, values, and roles from society.","zh":"theories of socialization 指解釋人們如何從社會學習行為、價值觀和角色的理論。"},{"en":"A theory of socialization may examine how children learn manners from parents and teachers.","zh":"社會化理論可能檢視兒童如何從父母和老師學習禮貌。"},{"en":"These theories help explain how children become members of a community.","zh":"這些理論幫助解釋兒童如何成為社區成員。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in sociology and developmental psychology.","zh":"這個短語適用於社會學和發展心理學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"from Freud onwards","meaning":"自弗洛伊德以來","examples":[{"en":"From Freud onwards, many theories emphasised family experiences.","zh":"自弗洛伊德以來，許多理論強調家庭經驗。"},{"en":"From Freud onwards means starting with Freud and continuing after him.","zh":"from Freud onwards 指從弗洛伊德開始並在之後延續。"},{"en":"From the 1990s onwards, many students began using computers for schoolwork.","zh":"自1990年代以來，許多學生開始使用電腦做功課。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a historical starting point and what followed it.","zh":"這個短語標示歷史起點以及其後發展。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing intellectual history.","zh":"描述思想史時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be doled out","meaning":"被分配","examples":[{"en":"Environmental influences were assumed to be doled out by family.","zh":"環境影響被假定由家庭分配。"},{"en":"Be doled out means be distributed or given out, often in portions.","zh":"be doled out 指被分發或派發，通常是一份一份地給。"},{"en":"A teacher may dole out worksheets to each group before an activity.","zh":"老師可能在活動前向每組派發工作紙。"},{"en":"Earlier theories imagined environmental influence as if families handed it out equally.","zh":"早期理論把環境影響想像成由家庭平均分配出去。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound slightly mechanical or critical.","zh":"這個短語可以帶有稍微機械或批判的語氣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on a family-by-family basis","meaning":"以逐個家庭為單位","examples":[{"en":"Earlier theories treated environments on a family-by-family basis.","zh":"早期理論以逐個家庭為單位看待環境。"},{"en":"On a family-by-family basis means considering each family as a whole unit.","zh":"on a family-by-family basis 指把每個家庭作為一個整體單位來考慮。"},{"en":"A school may contact parents on a family-by-family basis when planning support.","zh":"學校規劃支援時，可能以逐個家庭為單位聯絡家長。"},{"en":"This approach may miss differences between children within the same family.","zh":"這種方法可能錯過同一家庭內不同兒童之間的差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the unit of analysis is the family.","zh":"當分析單位是家庭時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"In contrast, non-shared environments differ for each child.","zh":"相比之下，非共享環境對每名兒童都不同。"},{"en":"In contrast means by comparison with something different or opposite.","zh":"in contrast 指與不同或相反事物相比。"},{"en":"One student enjoys group work; in contrast, another learns better alone.","zh":"一名學生喜歡小組活動；相比之下，另一名學生獨自學習更好。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers see a clear difference between two ideas.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者看見兩個想法之間的清楚差異。"},{"en":"It is useful when moving from one side of a comparison to the other.","zh":"從比較的一方轉到另一方時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on a child-by-child basis","meaning":"以每名兒童為單位","examples":[{"en":"Non-shared influences operate on a child-by-child basis.","zh":"非共享影響以每名兒童為單位發揮作用。"},{"en":"On a child-by-child basis means considering each child separately.","zh":"on a child-by-child basis 指分開考慮每一名兒童。"},{"en":"A teacher may give feedback on a child-by-child basis because each student makes different mistakes.","zh":"老師可能以每名兒童為單位給回饋，因為每名學生犯不同錯誤。"},{"en":"This approach recognises that siblings can experience the same family differently.","zh":"這種方法承認兄弟姊妹可以以不同方式經歷同一家庭。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the focus is individual children rather than the whole family.","zh":"當焦點是個別兒童而非整個家庭時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be shorthand for","meaning":"是……的簡稱","examples":[{"en":"Non-shared environment is shorthand for a component of variance.","zh":"非共享環境是表型變異某個組成部分的簡稱。"},{"en":"Be shorthand for something means be a short way of referring to a more complex idea.","zh":"be shorthand for something 指以簡短方式指代較複雜想法。"},{"en":"“Screen time” is shorthand for many activities, including games, videos, and social media.","zh":"screen time 是許多活動的簡稱，包括遊戲、影片和社交媒體。"},{"en":"A shorthand term is useful, but students still need to understand the full meaning.","zh":"簡稱很有用，但學生仍需要理解完整意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a simple label represents a technical idea.","zh":"當簡單標籤代表技術概念時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"component of phenotypic variance","meaning":"表型變異的組成部分","examples":[{"en":"The term refers to a component of phenotypic variance.","zh":"這個術語指表型變異的一個組成部分。"},{"en":"A component of phenotypic variance is one part of the observed differences between individuals.","zh":"component of phenotypic variance 指個體之間可觀察差異中的一部分。"},{"en":"In test scores, one component of variance may be teaching quality, while another may be study time.","zh":"在測驗分數中，變異的一個組成部分可能是教學質素，另一個可能是學習時間。"},{"en":"This phrase helps researchers divide complex differences into parts.","zh":"這個短語幫助研究人員把複雜差異分成不同部分。"},{"en":"It is technical and belongs to genetics and statistics.","zh":"它較技術性，屬於遺傳學和統計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"refer to effects rather than events","meaning":"指影響而非事件","examples":[{"en":"The phrase refers to effects rather than specific events.","zh":"這個短語指影響，而不是具體事件。"},{"en":"Refer to effects rather than events means the term describes results, not the actual experiences that caused them.","zh":"refer to effects rather than events 指該術語描述結果，而不是造成結果的實際經歷。"},{"en":"A child’s low confidence is an effect, while being laughed at in class may be an event.","zh":"孩子的低自信是一種影響，而在課堂被取笑可能是一個事件。"},{"en":"Researchers must be careful not to confuse measured effects with real-life incidents.","zh":"研究人員必須小心，不要把被量度的效應與真實生活事件混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when clarifying technical terminology.","zh":"澄清技術術語時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in recent years","meaning":"近年","examples":[{"en":"Research in recent years has focused more on peer influence.","zh":"近年的研究更多聚焦朋輩影響。"},{"en":"In recent years means during the last few years or the recent period.","zh":"in recent years 指在最近幾年或近期一段時間內。"},{"en":"In recent years, many schools have used more online learning tools.","zh":"近年，許多學校使用更多網上學習工具。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a newer trend or change.","zh":"這個短語表示較新的趨勢或變化。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing recent research with older ideas.","zh":"比較近期研究與舊想法時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"peer influence","meaning":"朋輩影響","examples":[{"en":"Peer influence may override the influence of parents.","zh":"朋輩影響可能凌駕父母影響。"},{"en":"Peer influence means the effect that friends or people of the same age have on someone.","zh":"peer influence 指朋友或同齡人對某人的影響。"},{"en":"Teenagers may dress differently because of peer influence.","zh":"青少年可能因朋輩影響而改變衣着。"},{"en":"Peer influence can encourage good habits, but it can also increase risky behaviour.","zh":"朋輩影響可以鼓勵好習慣，也可以增加冒險行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing adolescent behaviour.","zh":"討論青少年行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be overridden by","meaning":"被……凌駕；抵銷","examples":[{"en":"Parental influence can sometimes be overridden by peers.","zh":"父母影響有時會被朋輩凌駕。"},{"en":"To be overridden by something means to be weakened, replaced, or dominated by a stronger influence.","zh":"be overridden by something 指被較強影響削弱、取代或支配。"},{"en":"A student’s plan to study may be overridden by the desire to join friends online.","zh":"學生本想溫習，但這個計劃可能被想和朋友上網的慾望抵銷。"},{"en":"When peer influence is strong, parents’ advice may have less effect.","zh":"當朋輩影響很強，父母建議可能較少發揮作用。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one force cancels or dominates another.","zh":"當一種力量抵銷或支配另一種力量時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"variations in knowledge","meaning":"知識上的差異","examples":[{"en":"Research has found increasing variations in children’s knowledge.","zh":"研究發現兒童知識上的差異正在增加。"},{"en":"Variations in knowledge are differences in what people know or understand.","zh":"variations in knowledge 指人們所知道或理解內容上的差異。"},{"en":"In one class, there may be variations in knowledge because some students read more at home.","zh":"同一班中可能有知識差異，因為有些學生在家讀得更多。"},{"en":"Different friends, media, and cultures can create differences in children’s knowledge.","zh":"不同朋友、媒體和文化可以造成兒童知識上的差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing what different children have learned.","zh":"比較不同兒童學到甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"acquire from other cultures","meaning":"從其他文化中獲取","examples":[{"en":"Children acquire knowledge from other cultures.","zh":"兒童從其他文化中獲取知識。"},{"en":"To acquire from other cultures means to gain knowledge, habits, or ideas from cultures different from one’s own.","zh":"acquire from other cultures 指從不同於自己文化的地方獲得知識、習慣或想法。"},{"en":"Students may acquire new greetings from other cultures through travel or films.","zh":"學生可能透過旅遊或電影從其他文化中學到新的打招呼方式。"},{"en":"Contact with other cultures can broaden what children know beyond their family background.","zh":"接觸其他文化可以擴闊兒童在家庭背景以外的知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing cultural learning.","zh":"討論文化學習時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a number of","meaning":"多個；若干","examples":[{"en":"A number of interests may conflict within a family.","zh":"家庭內可能有多個利益互相衝突。"},{"en":"A number of means several or more than one.","zh":"a number of 指幾個或多於一個。"},{"en":"A number of students asked for extra speaking practice before the exam.","zh":"若干學生在考試前要求額外口語練習。"},{"en":"When a number of factors are involved, the situation becomes harder to explain simply.","zh":"當涉及多個因素，情況就更難用簡單方式解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for introducing several examples or causes.","zh":"引入幾個例子或原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"conflicting interests","meaning":"互相衝突的利益","examples":[{"en":"Parents and children may have conflicting interests.","zh":"父母和子女可能有互相衝突的利益。"},{"en":"Conflicting interests are needs or goals that clash with one another.","zh":"conflicting interests 指彼此衝突的需要或目標。"},{"en":"A teenager may want freedom, while parents want safety, creating conflicting interests.","zh":"青少年可能想要自由，而父母想要安全，於是產生互相衝突的利益。"},{"en":"Conflicting interests can lead to argument if people do not negotiate.","zh":"如果人們不協商，互相衝突的利益可以導致爭執。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when different people want different things.","zh":"當不同人想要不同東西時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"between fathers and mothers","meaning":"父母之間","examples":[{"en":"Some interests conflict between fathers and mothers.","zh":"有些利益在父母之間發生衝突。"},{"en":"Between fathers and mothers means involving both parents and the differences between them.","zh":"between fathers and mothers 指涉及父母雙方以及兩者之間的差異。"},{"en":"Decisions about school choice may create disagreement between fathers and mothers.","zh":"關於選校的決定可能在父母之間造成分歧。"},{"en":"Children may experience different rules if parents disagree with each other.","zh":"如果父母彼此不同意，兒童可能經歷不同規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing the roles or views of two parents.","zh":"比較父母雙方角色或看法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"potential genetic factors","meaning":"潛在遺傳因素","examples":[{"en":"Siblings share some potential genetic factors.","zh":"兄弟姊妹共享一些潛在遺傳因素。"},{"en":"Potential genetic factors are inherited influences that may affect a trait or behaviour.","zh":"potential genetic factors 指可能影響某特徵或行為的遺傳影響。"},{"en":"A family history of allergies may be a potential genetic factor for a child’s health.","zh":"家族過敏史可能是影響兒童健康的潛在遺傳因素。"},{"en":"Potential factors may not always appear, especially if the environment changes their expression.","zh":"潛在因素不一定總會出現，尤其當環境改變其表現時。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when genes may play a role but are not the whole answer.","zh":"當基因可能有作用但不是完整答案時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"differentiate siblings","meaning":"令兄弟姊妹有所不同","examples":[{"en":"Both genes and experience can differentiate siblings.","zh":"基因和經驗都可以令兄弟姊妹有所不同。"},{"en":"To differentiate siblings means to make brothers and sisters different from one another.","zh":"differentiate siblings 指令兄弟姊妹彼此不同。"},{"en":"Different schools can differentiate siblings even if they live in the same home.","zh":"即使住在同一個家，不同學校也可以令兄弟姊妹有所不同。"},{"en":"Genes, friends, teachers, and life events can all create differences between siblings.","zh":"基因、朋友、老師和人生事件都可以造成兄弟姊妹之間的差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why family members are not identical.","zh":"解釋家庭成員為何不完全相同時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"very difficult","meaning":"非常困難","examples":[{"en":"Separating these influences is very difficult.","zh":"分開這些影響非常困難。"},{"en":"Very difficult means hard to do, understand, or solve.","zh":"very difficult 指難以做到、理解或解決。"},{"en":"It is very difficult to learn pronunciation well without hearing enough examples.","zh":"如果沒有聽到足夠例子，要學好發音非常困難。"},{"en":"A task becomes very difficult when many factors are mixed together.","zh":"當許多因素混在一起，任務就變得非常困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing a high level of challenge.","zh":"強調高度挑戰時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"random measurement error","meaning":"隨機測量誤差","examples":[{"en":"Non-shared environmental estimates include random measurement error.","zh":"非共享環境估算包括隨機測量誤差。"},{"en":"Random measurement error means accidental inaccuracy that occurs when data are measured.","zh":"random measurement error 指量度數據時出現的偶然不準確。"},{"en":"A scale may create random measurement error if it gives slightly different readings each time.","zh":"如果磅每次給出略有不同的讀數，就可能造成隨機測量誤差。"},{"en":"Random error can make research results less precise.","zh":"隨機誤差可以令研究結果較不精準。"},{"en":"This phrase is technical and common in research methods.","zh":"這個短語較技術性，常見於研究方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not be systematic","meaning":"並非有系統","examples":[{"en":"Some non-shared influences may not be systematic.","zh":"某些非共享影響可能並非有系統。"},{"en":"Not be systematic means not follow a clear, regular, or predictable pattern.","zh":"not be systematic 指不跟隨清楚、規律或可預測的模式。"},{"en":"A student’s mistakes may not be systematic if they happen randomly in different areas.","zh":"如果學生錯誤隨機出現在不同地方，就可能並非有系統。"},{"en":"If influences are not systematic, researchers may struggle to identify a stable cause.","zh":"如果影響並非有系統，研究人員可能難以找出穩定原因。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when patterns are unclear.","zh":"當模式不清楚時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"operate idiosyncratically","meaning":"以個別而獨特的方式發揮作用","examples":[{"en":"Environmental influences may operate idiosyncratically.","zh":"環境影響可能以個別而獨特的方式發揮作用。"},{"en":"To operate idiosyncratically means to work in a highly individual, unusual, or person-specific way.","zh":"operate idiosyncratically 指以高度個人化、不尋常或因人而異的方式運作。"},{"en":"The same teacher’s strictness may motivate one student but frighten another.","zh":"同一位老師的嚴格可能激勵一名學生，卻嚇怕另一名學生。"},{"en":"If influences operate idiosyncratically, general rules may not explain every child.","zh":"如果影響以個別方式運作，一般規則可能無法解釋每個孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and useful when effects differ from person to person.","zh":"這個短語較正式，適合描述效果因人而異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cannot be ascertained","meaning":"無法確定","examples":[{"en":"Some environmental mechanisms cannot easily be ascertained.","zh":"某些環境機制無法輕易確定。"},{"en":"Cannot be ascertained means cannot be found out or determined with certainty.","zh":"cannot be ascertained 指無法確切查明或判斷。"},{"en":"The cause of a student’s sudden silence cannot be ascertained without more information.","zh":"沒有更多資料，學生突然沉默的原因無法確定。"},{"en":"If a mechanism cannot be ascertained, researchers must avoid overconfident conclusions.","zh":"如果機制無法確定，研究人員必須避免過度肯定的結論。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and useful in cautious writing.","zh":"這個短語較正式，適用於謹慎寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"whether or not","meaning":"是否","examples":[{"en":"Researchers ask whether or not these mechanisms can be identified.","zh":"研究人員詢問這些機制是否能被識別。"},{"en":"Whether or not means if something is true or not true.","zh":"whether or not 指某事是否為真。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask whether or not extra homework actually improves results.","zh":"老師可能詢問額外功課是否真的改善成績。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a question with two possible answers.","zh":"這個短語引入有兩種可能答案的問題。"},{"en":"It is useful when an issue remains uncertain.","zh":"當議題仍不確定時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"quasi-experimental designs","meaning":"準實驗設計","examples":[{"en":"Quasi-experimental designs can help researchers study environmental mechanisms.","zh":"準實驗設計可以幫助研究人員研究環境機制。"},{"en":"Quasi-experimental designs are research designs that compare groups without full random assignment.","zh":"quasi-experimental designs 指比較不同群體但沒有完全隨機分配的研究設計。"},{"en":"A school may compare two existing classes after one receives a new reading programme.","zh":"學校可能在其中一班接受新閱讀計劃後，比較兩個現有班級。"},{"en":"These designs can study real-world settings when true experiments are difficult.","zh":"當真正實驗難以進行時，這些設計可以研究真實世界環境。"},{"en":"This phrase is technical and common in research methods.","zh":"這個短語較技術性，常見於研究方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"behavioral genetic designs","meaning":"行為遺傳學研究設計","examples":[{"en":"Behavioral genetic designs compare genetic and non-genetic factors.","zh":"行為遺傳學研究設計比較遺傳和非遺傳因素。"},{"en":"Behavioral genetic designs are research plans used to study how genes and environment influence behaviour.","zh":"behavioral genetic designs 指用來研究基因和環境如何影響行為的研究計劃。"},{"en":"Twin studies and adoption studies are examples of behavioural genetic designs.","zh":"雙生子研究和領養研究都是行為遺傳學研究設計的例子。"},{"en":"These designs help researchers separate inherited similarity from environmental similarity.","zh":"這些設計幫助研究人員分開遺傳相似性和環境相似性。"},{"en":"This phrase is technical and useful in psychology research.","zh":"這個短語較技術性，適用於心理學研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"identify systematic mechanisms","meaning":"找出有系統的機制","examples":[{"en":"Researchers hope to identify systematic environmental mechanisms.","zh":"研究人員希望找出有系統的環境機制。"},{"en":"To identify systematic mechanisms means to find clear, regular processes that explain an effect.","zh":"identify systematic mechanisms 指找出清楚而有規律、能解釋某效應的過程。"},{"en":"A school may identify systematic mechanisms behind lateness, such as bus delays and timetable design.","zh":"學校可能找出遲到背後的有系統機制，例如巴士延誤和時間表設計。"},{"en":"Finding mechanisms helps researchers move from description to explanation.","zh":"找出機制幫助研究人員由描述走向解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when studying how an effect happens.","zh":"研究某效應如何發生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cross-sectionally","meaning":"以橫斷面方式","examples":[{"en":"The mechanisms may be studied cross-sectionally.","zh":"這些機制可以以橫斷面方式研究。"},{"en":"Cross-sectionally means by comparing different people or groups at one point in time.","zh":"cross-sectionally 指在同一時間點比較不同人或群體。"},{"en":"A school may study reading ability cross-sectionally by testing students from several year groups in the same week.","zh":"學校可能在同一星期測試幾個年級的學生，以橫斷面方式研究閱讀能力。"},{"en":"Cross-sectional research is quicker than following the same people for many years.","zh":"橫斷面研究比多年追蹤同一批人更快。"},{"en":"This word is technical and common in research design.","zh":"這個詞較技術性，常見於研究設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"longitudinally","meaning":"以縱向方式","examples":[{"en":"Researchers also examine development longitudinally.","zh":"研究人員也以縱向方式檢視發展。"},{"en":"Longitudinally means by studying the same people or cases over a period of time.","zh":"longitudinally 指在一段時間內研究同一批人或個案。"},{"en":"A teacher may track students longitudinally from Form 1 to Form 6.","zh":"老師可能從中一到中六縱向追蹤學生。"},{"en":"Longitudinal research can show how change happens, not just how groups differ at one moment.","zh":"縱向研究可以顯示變化如何發生，而不只是某一刻群體有何不同。"},{"en":"This word is technical and useful in developmental research.","zh":"這個詞較技術性，適用於發展研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the impetus for","meaning":"……的推動力","examples":[{"en":"This unanswered question was the impetus for the current study.","zh":"這個未解答問題是當前研究的推動力。"},{"en":"The impetus for something is the force, reason, or motivation that starts it.","zh":"impetus for something 指啟動某事的力量、原因或動機。"},{"en":"A rise in student stress may be the impetus for a new school counselling programme.","zh":"學生壓力上升可能成為新學校輔導計劃的推動力。"},{"en":"Unanswered questions often push researchers to begin new studies.","zh":"未解答問題常推動研究人員開始新研究。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why an action began.","zh":"解釋行動為何開始時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"current study","meaning":"當前研究","examples":[{"en":"The current study examines non-shared environmental mechanisms.","zh":"當前研究檢視非共享環境機制。"},{"en":"Current study means the study being discussed now.","zh":"current study 指正在討論的這項研究。"},{"en":"The current study may use interviews, test scores, and family data.","zh":"當前研究可能使用訪談、測驗分數和家庭數據。"},{"en":"Referring to the current study helps readers distinguish it from earlier research.","zh":"提到當前研究有助讀者把它與早期研究區分開來。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic writing.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"complete the table below","meaning":"完成下表","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the table below with words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的詞語完成下表。"},{"en":"Complete the table below means fill in missing information in the table that follows.","zh":"complete the table below 指填寫下方表格中缺少的資料。"},{"en":"Students should complete the table below by finding exact words in the reading passage.","zh":"學生應透過在閱讀篇章中尋找準確詞語來完成下表。"},{"en":"This task tests whether students can locate and summarise specific information.","zh":"這項任務測試學生能否定位並概括特定資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in IELTS-style reading instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 IELTS 類閱讀指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"no more than three words","meaning":"不多於三個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than three words.","zh":"每個答案應包含不多於三個字。"},{"en":"No more than three words means the answer must use one, two, or three words only.","zh":"no more than three words 指答案只能使用一個、兩個或三個英文詞。"},{"en":"If the answer is “shared family experiences,” it has three words and follows the rule.","zh":"如果答案是 shared family experiences，它有三個詞，符合規則。"},{"en":"Writing four words can lose marks even if the meaning is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫四個詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"This instruction is important in completion questions.","zh":"這項指示在填空題中很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"type of impact","meaning":"影響類型","examples":[{"en":"The table compares different types of impact on children.","zh":"表格比較對兒童的不同影響類型。"},{"en":"Type of impact means a category or kind of influence.","zh":"type of impact 指影響的類別或種類。"},{"en":"A report may compare the type of impact caused by school, family, and friends.","zh":"報告可能比較學校、家庭和朋友造成的影響類型。"},{"en":"Grouping impacts by type helps students organise information clearly.","zh":"按類型整理影響有助學生清楚組織資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when classifying effects.","zh":"分類效應時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"applicability to siblings","meaning":"對兄弟姊妹的適用情況","examples":[{"en":"The table shows the applicability of each influence to siblings.","zh":"表格顯示每種影響對兄弟姊妹的適用情況。"},{"en":"Applicability to siblings means whether and how an influence applies to brothers and sisters.","zh":"applicability to siblings 指某影響是否以及如何適用於兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"A family rule has broad applicability to siblings if it affects all children in the home.","zh":"如果家庭規則影響家中所有孩子，它對兄弟姊妹就有廣泛適用性。"},{"en":"Some influences apply to all siblings, while others affect only one child.","zh":"有些影響適用於所有兄弟姊妹，另一些則只影響一名兒童。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing shared and non-shared effects.","zh":"比較共享和非共享效應時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"including all siblings","meaning":"包括所有兄弟姊妹","examples":[{"en":"Some influences apply to all siblings in a family.","zh":"有些影響適用於家庭中的所有兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"Including all siblings means involving every brother and sister in the family.","zh":"including all siblings 指涉及家庭中的每一個兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"A family holiday including all siblings can become a shared memory.","zh":"包括所有兄弟姊妹的家庭旅行可以成為共同記憶。"},{"en":"Experiences including all siblings may create similarities among them.","zh":"包括所有兄弟姊妹的經歷可能在他們之間創造相似性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an influence is shared by the whole sibling group.","zh":"當影響由整個兄弟姊妹群體共享時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"including some siblings","meaning":"包括部分兄弟姊妹","examples":[{"en":"Non-shared influences may apply to only some siblings.","zh":"非共享影響可能只適用於部分兄弟姊妹。"},{"en":"Including some siblings means involving only part of the sibling group, not everyone.","zh":"including some siblings 指只涉及兄弟姊妹中的一部分，而不是所有人。"},{"en":"A private music lesson may affect one child, including some siblings but not all.","zh":"私人音樂課可能影響一名孩子，即只包括部分兄弟姊妹而非全部。"},{"en":"Experiences that include only some siblings can create differences inside the same family.","zh":"只包括部分兄弟姊妹的經歷可以在同一家庭內造成差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining non-shared influence.","zh":"解釋非共享影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"complete the following summary","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the following summary with words from the passage.","zh":"考生使用文章中的詞語完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"Complete the following summary means fill in missing words in the short summary that comes next.","zh":"complete the following summary 指填寫接下來短摘要中的缺漏詞語。"},{"en":"Students should complete the following summary by matching ideas to the passage.","zh":"學生應透過把摘要意思與文章配對來完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"Summary completion tests both reading comprehension and accurate wording.","zh":"摘要填空同時測試閱讀理解和準確用詞。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"indicate that","meaning":"顯示","examples":[{"en":"Recent research indicated that peers may outweigh parental influence.","zh":"近期研究顯示，朋輩可能比父母影響更大。"},{"en":"Indicate that means show, suggest, or point to a conclusion.","zh":"indicate that 指顯示、暗示或指出某結論。"},{"en":"Falling test scores may indicate that students need more practice.","zh":"測驗分數下降可能顯示學生需要更多練習。"},{"en":"Research can indicate a pattern without proving every detail completely.","zh":"研究可以顯示一種模式，但未必完全證明每個細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence suggests something.","zh":"當證據暗示某事時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"frequently be overridden","meaning":"經常被凌駕","examples":[{"en":"The influence of parents can frequently be overridden by peers.","zh":"父母的影響可能經常被朋輩凌駕。"},{"en":"Frequently be overridden means often be weakened or replaced by a stronger influence.","zh":"frequently be overridden 指經常被較強影響削弱或取代。"},{"en":"A student’s plan to sleep early can frequently be overridden by late-night messages from friends.","zh":"學生早睡的計劃可能經常被朋友深夜訊息打亂。"},{"en":"If peer pressure is strong, parental advice may often lose force.","zh":"如果朋輩壓力很強，父母建議可能常常失去力量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one influence often dominates another.","zh":"當一種影響常支配另一種影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"peer pressure","meaning":"朋輩壓力","examples":[{"en":"Peer pressure may shape children’s behaviour and choices.","zh":"朋輩壓力可能塑造兒童行為和選擇。"},{"en":"Peer pressure is the influence people feel from friends or people of the same age to behave in a certain way.","zh":"peer pressure 指人們受到朋友或同齡人影響，而覺得要以某種方式行事。"},{"en":"A teenager may buy fashionable shoes because of peer pressure.","zh":"青少年可能因朋輩壓力而購買流行鞋款。"},{"en":"Peer pressure can lead to risky choices, but it can also encourage positive habits.","zh":"朋輩壓力可以導致冒險選擇，但也可以鼓勵正面習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing social influence among young people.","zh":"討論年輕人之間的社會影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"competing interests","meaning":"互相競爭的利益","examples":[{"en":"The study found competing interests among family members.","zh":"研究發現家庭成員之間有互相競爭的利益。"},{"en":"Competing interests are different goals or needs that conflict with each other.","zh":"competing interests 指彼此衝突的不同目標或需要。"},{"en":"Parents may want a child to study, while the child wants more free time.","zh":"父母可能希望孩子溫習，而孩子想要更多自由時間。"},{"en":"Competing interests can create tension unless people negotiate clearly.","zh":"如果人們不清楚協商，互相競爭的利益可以造成緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when different people want different outcomes.","zh":"當不同人想要不同結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"between parents themselves","meaning":"甚至在父母彼此之間","examples":[{"en":"Interests may conflict even between parents themselves.","zh":"利益甚至可能在父母彼此之間發生衝突。"},{"en":"Between parents themselves means among the parents, not just between parents and children.","zh":"between parents themselves 指在父母之間，而不只是父母與子女之間。"},{"en":"One parent may prefer strict rules, while the other prefers more freedom.","zh":"一位父母可能偏好嚴格規則，另一位則偏好更多自由。"},{"en":"Disagreement between parents themselves can create mixed messages for children.","zh":"父母彼此之間的分歧可以給孩子造成混亂訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when conflict exists inside the parenting side.","zh":"當衝突存在於父母一方內部時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"agree with the claims of","meaning":"與作者的主張一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether statements agree with the claims of the writer.","zh":"考生判斷陳述是否與作者的主張一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the claims of someone means match the views or arguments that person makes.","zh":"agree with the claims of someone 指符合某人的觀點或論點。"},{"en":"A statement agrees with the writer’s claim only if the text clearly supports it.","zh":"只有文本清楚支持某陳述時，它才與作者主張一致。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when judging the writer’s claims.","zh":"判斷作者主張時，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in YES, NO, NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 YES, NO, NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"contradict the views of","meaning":"與作者觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the views of the writer.","zh":"一個陳述可能與作者觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the views of someone means to say the opposite of what that person argues or believes.","zh":"contradict the views of someone 指說出與某人論點或信念相反的內容。"},{"en":"If a writer says environment matters and a statement says it has no effect, the statement contradicts the writer.","zh":"如果作者說環境重要，而陳述說環境沒有影響，該陳述就與作者相矛盾。"},{"en":"A contradiction must be based on the text, not on personal opinion.","zh":"矛盾必須基於文本，而不是個人意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in reading-comprehension tasks.","zh":"這個短語適用於閱讀理解題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"It may be impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"可能無法判斷作者怎樣想。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to give a definite answer.","zh":"impossible to say 指沒有足夠資料給出確定答案。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions a student’s age, it is impossible to say whether they are twelve or fifteen.","zh":"如果文章從未提到學生年齡，就無法判斷他是十二歲還是十五歲。"},{"en":"In reading tests, impossible to say often leads to a NOT GIVEN answer.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，無法判斷通常會導向 NOT GIVEN 答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence is missing.","zh":"當證據缺失時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"environmental impact","meaning":"環境影響","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether family size increases environmental impact.","zh":"這個陳述問家庭大小是否增加環境影響。"},{"en":"Environmental impact means the effect something has on surroundings, development, or the natural world.","zh":"environmental impact 指某事對周圍環境、發展或自然界造成的影響。"},{"en":"A factory’s environmental impact may include air pollution and water use.","zh":"工廠的環境影響可能包括空氣污染和用水。"},{"en":"In child development, environmental impact can mean the effect of home, school, and peers.","zh":"在兒童發展中，環境影響可以指家庭、學校和朋輩的效果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful because environment can refer to social or natural surroundings.","zh":"這個短語很有用，因為 environment 可以指社會或自然環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the greater…the greater…","meaning":"越……，就越……","examples":[{"en":"The statement suggests that the more children there are, the greater the impact.","zh":"這個陳述暗示孩子越多，影響就越大。"},{"en":"The greater…the greater… means when one thing increases, another also increases.","zh":"the greater…the greater… 指一件事增加時，另一件事也增加。"},{"en":"The greater the practice time, the greater the chance of improvement.","zh":"練習時間越多，進步機會就越大。"},{"en":"This structure shows a direct relationship between two changes.","zh":"這個結構顯示兩種變化之間的直接關係。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining comparison, cause, and result.","zh":"解釋比較、原因和結果時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"methods based on twin studies","meaning":"以雙生子研究為基礎的方法","examples":[{"en":"Methods based on twin studies compare genetic similarities.","zh":"以雙生子研究為基礎的方法比較遺傳相似性。"},{"en":"Methods based on twin studies are research approaches that use twins to study genes and environment.","zh":"methods based on twin studies 指使用雙生子來研究基因和環境的研究方法。"},{"en":"Researchers may compare identical and non-identical twins to estimate genetic influence.","zh":"研究人員可能比較同卵和異卵雙生子，以估算遺傳影響。"},{"en":"Twin-based methods help separate shared upbringing from inherited similarity.","zh":"雙生子方法幫助分開共同成長環境和遺傳相似性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in behavioural genetics.","zh":"這個短語適用於行為遺傳學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"encounter unexpected differences","meaning":"遇到出乎意料的差異","examples":[{"en":"Twin studies may encounter unexpected differences between siblings.","zh":"雙生子研究可能遇到兄弟姊妹之間出乎意料的差異。"},{"en":"To encounter unexpected differences means to find differences that were not predicted.","zh":"encounter unexpected differences 指發現原本沒有預測到的差異。"},{"en":"A teacher may encounter unexpected differences between two students who had the same lessons.","zh":"老師可能在接受相同課堂的兩名學生之間遇到出乎意料的差異。"},{"en":"Unexpected differences can push researchers to look for new explanations.","zh":"出乎意料的差異可以推動研究人員尋找新解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence challenges assumptions.","zh":"當證據挑戰假設時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be explained purely by","meaning":"純粹由……解釋","examples":[{"en":"Not all sibling differences can be explained purely by genetics.","zh":"並非所有兄弟姊妹差異都能純粹由遺傳解釋。"},{"en":"Be explained purely by means be completely accounted for by one cause alone.","zh":"be explained purely by 指完全由單一原因解釋。"},{"en":"A student’s success cannot be explained purely by intelligence because effort and support also matter.","zh":"學生成功不能純粹由智力解釋，因為努力和支援也重要。"},{"en":"If one factor cannot explain the whole result, researchers must consider other influences.","zh":"如果一個因素不能解釋整個結果，研究人員必須考慮其他影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when rejecting a single-cause explanation.","zh":"拒絕單一原因解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"children of the same age","meaning":"同齡兒童","examples":[{"en":"Children may be strongly influenced by others of the same age.","zh":"兒童可能深受同齡兒童影響。"},{"en":"Children of the same age are children who are at about the same stage of life.","zh":"children of the same age 指年齡相若、處於相近人生階段的兒童。"},{"en":"A ten-year-old may copy the clothes, slang, or games of children of the same age.","zh":"十歲孩子可能模仿同齡兒童的衣着、俚語或遊戲。"},{"en":"Same-age peers can affect behaviour because children want to belong.","zh":"同齡朋輩可以影響行為，因為兒童想有歸屬感。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing peer influence.","zh":"討論朋輩影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"language spoken by","meaning":"由……所說的語言","examples":[{"en":"The statement compares language spoken by peers and parents.","zh":"這個陳述比較由朋輩和父母所說的語言。"},{"en":"Language spoken by someone means the language that person or group uses in daily communication.","zh":"language spoken by someone 指某人或某群體在日常溝通中使用的語言。"},{"en":"A child may use the language spoken by classmates more often than the language spoken at home.","zh":"兒童可能更常使用同學所說的語言，而不是家中所說的語言。"},{"en":"Language use can show which social group has stronger influence.","zh":"語言使用可以顯示哪個社交群體有更強影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing communication and identity.","zh":"討論溝通和身份時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be generally accepted among","meaning":"在……之間獲普遍接受","examples":[{"en":"The theory may not yet be generally accepted among researchers.","zh":"這個理論可能尚未在研究人員之間獲普遍接受。"},{"en":"Be generally accepted among a group means be widely agreed with by people in that group.","zh":"be generally accepted among a group 指在某群體中被廣泛同意。"},{"en":"A teaching method may become generally accepted among teachers after many successful trials.","zh":"一種教學方法在多次成功試驗後，可能在老師之間獲普遍接受。"},{"en":"If an idea is not generally accepted, experts may still be debating it.","zh":"如果一個想法尚未被普遍接受，專家可能仍在爭論。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the level of agreement in a field.","zh":"描述某領域的認同程度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"researchers in the field","meaning":"該領域的研究人員","examples":[{"en":"Researchers in the field continue to debate non-shared influences.","zh":"該領域的研究人員繼續爭論非共享影響。"},{"en":"Researchers in the field are experts working in a particular area of study.","zh":"researchers in the field 指在某個研究範疇工作的專家。"},{"en":"Researchers in the field of education may study how homework affects learning.","zh":"教育領域的研究人員可能研究功課如何影響學習。"},{"en":"When researchers in a field disagree, more evidence is usually needed.","zh":"當某領域研究人員意見不同，通常需要更多證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when referring to specialists.","zh":"指代專家時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"according to the passage","meaning":"根據文章","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which statement is true according to the passage.","zh":"題目問根據文章哪個陳述正確。"},{"en":"According to the passage means based only on information given in the reading text.","zh":"according to the passage 指只根據閱讀文章提供的資料。"},{"en":"According to the passage, students should choose the answer supported by the text, not by outside knowledge.","zh":"根據文章，學生應選擇文本支持的答案，而不是外部知識支持的答案。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that evidence must come from the passage.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者證據必須來自文章。"},{"en":"It is common in reading-comprehension questions.","zh":"它常見於閱讀理解題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"current studies of","meaning":"關於……的現行研究","examples":[{"en":"Current studies of non-shared environments use several research designs.","zh":"關於非共享環境的現行研究使用幾種研究設計。"},{"en":"Current studies of something are recent or ongoing research projects about that topic.","zh":"current studies of something 指關於某主題的近期或正在進行的研究項目。"},{"en":"Current studies of online learning examine attention, motivation, and exam results.","zh":"關於網上學習的現行研究檢視注意力、動機和考試結果。"},{"en":"Current studies may use better methods than older research.","zh":"現行研究可能使用比舊研究更好的方法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the latest research focus.","zh":"討論最新研究焦點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be somewhat biased","meaning":"有點偏頗","examples":[{"en":"Some research methods may be somewhat biased.","zh":"某些研究方法可能有點偏頗。"},{"en":"Be somewhat biased means be partly unfair or influenced in one direction.","zh":"be somewhat biased 指部分不公平或受到某一方向影響。"},{"en":"A survey may be somewhat biased if only confident students answer it.","zh":"如果只有有自信的學生回答問卷，調查可能有點偏頗。"},{"en":"Biased methods can make results less reliable.","zh":"偏頗方法可以令結果較不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when criticism is cautious rather than extreme.","zh":"當批評是謹慎而非極端時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not be sufficiently substantiated","meaning":"尚未獲充分證實","examples":[{"en":"Some claims have not yet been sufficiently substantiated.","zh":"某些說法尚未獲充分證實。"},{"en":"Not be sufficiently substantiated means not be supported by enough evidence.","zh":"not be sufficiently substantiated 指沒有足夠證據支持。"},{"en":"A rumour about a school policy should not be believed if it is not sufficiently substantiated.","zh":"如果關於學校政策的傳聞尚未獲充分證實，就不應輕信。"},{"en":"Researchers need strong data before a claim can be treated as reliable.","zh":"在某說法被視為可靠之前，研究人員需要強有力數據。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and useful in cautious academic writing.","zh":"這個短語較正式，適合謹慎學術寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"highly systematic","meaning":"高度有系統的","examples":[{"en":"Non-shared influences may not operate in a highly systematic way.","zh":"非共享影響可能不以高度有系統的方式運作。"},{"en":"Highly systematic means very organised, regular, and predictable.","zh":"highly systematic 指非常有組織、有規律和可預測。"},{"en":"A school timetable is highly systematic if lessons follow the same pattern every week.","zh":"如果課堂每週跟隨相同模式，學校時間表就是高度有系統的。"},{"en":"If an influence is not highly systematic, it may affect each child differently.","zh":"如果某影響並非高度有系統，它可能以不同方式影響每名兒童。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing whether patterns are regular.","zh":"討論模式是否規律時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be applied in practice","meaning":"應用於實際情況","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether the findings can be applied in practice.","zh":"題目問這些發現是否能應用於實際情況。"},{"en":"To be applied in practice means to be used in real situations, not just discussed in theory.","zh":"be applied in practice 指被用於真實情況，而不只是停留在理論討論。"},{"en":"A teaching theory is useful only if it can be applied in practice in real classrooms.","zh":"教學理論只有能應用於真實課室時才有用。"},{"en":"Research findings about children should lead to better support if they are applied well.","zh":"如果能好好應用，關於兒童的研究發現應帶來更好支援。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when connecting research with real-world action.","zh":"把研究與現實行動連接起來時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 164 - The Impact of Environment to Children.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 165":[{"front":"the return of monkey life","meaning":"猴群生態的回歸","examples":[{"en":"The regeneration of forests has encouraged the return of monkey life.","zh":"森林再生促成了猴群生態的回歸。"},{"en":"The return of monkey life means monkeys begin living in an area again after they had disappeared or declined.","zh":"the return of monkey life 指猴子在曾經消失或減少的地區重新生活。"},{"en":"A village may notice the return of bird life after trees are planted around the river.","zh":"村莊在河邊重新種樹後，可能注意到鳥類生態的回歸。"},{"en":"If forests recover, animals may find food and shelter again, leading to the return of wildlife.","zh":"如果森林恢復，動物可能再次找到食物和庇護，從而令野生動物回歸。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ecological recovery, not simply one animal passing through.","zh":"這個片語描述生態恢復，而不只是某隻動物經過。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"grow anew","meaning":"重新生長","examples":[{"en":"Rainforest trees are growing anew on former farmland.","zh":"雨林樹木正在舊農地上重新生長。"},{"en":"Grow anew means begin to grow again after being damaged, cut down, or absent.","zh":"grow anew 指在受損、被砍伐或消失後再次開始生長。"},{"en":"Grass may grow anew in a playground after rain and proper care.","zh":"操場上的草在下雨和適當護理後可能重新生長。"},{"en":"If farmland is abandoned, trees and shrubs may grow anew over several years.","zh":"如果農地被棄置，樹木和灌木可能在數年間重新生長。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests recovery and a new start.","zh":"這個片語暗示恢復和新的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Central American farmland","meaning":"中美洲農地","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are studying regenerating forests on Central American farmland.","zh":"科學家正在研究中美洲農地上的再生森林。"},{"en":"Central American farmland means agricultural land in Central America.","zh":"Central American farmland 指位於中美洲的農業土地。"},{"en":"Central American farmland may be used for cattle, coffee, cacao, or food crops.","zh":"中美洲農地可能用於牧牛、咖啡、可可或糧食作物。"},{"en":"If farming stops on some land, forest may slowly return and become useful for wildlife.","zh":"如果某些土地停止耕作，森林可能慢慢回復，並對野生動物有用。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the geographical and agricultural setting of the research.","zh":"這個片語給出研究的地理和農業背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"find ways for...to benefit one another","meaning":"找出令……互惠互利的方法","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are finding ways for monkeys and agriculture to benefit one another.","zh":"研究人員正在找出令猴子和農業互惠互利的方法。"},{"en":"Find ways for two things to benefit one another means discover methods that help both sides.","zh":"find ways for two things to benefit one another 指找出能幫助雙方的方法。"},{"en":"A school may find ways for older and younger students to benefit one another through mentoring.","zh":"學校可能透過導師計劃，找出令高低年級學生互惠互利的方法。"},{"en":"If farmers protect trees and monkeys spread seeds, farming and wildlife can both gain advantages.","zh":"如果農民保護樹木，而猴子傳播種子，農業和野生動物都可以受益。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on mutual benefit rather than conflict.","zh":"這個片語集中於互惠，而不是衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"remote working cattle ranch","meaning":"偏遠而仍在營運的牧牛場","examples":[{"en":"Hacienda La Pacifica is a remote working cattle ranch.","zh":"Hacienda La Pacifica 是一個偏遠而仍在營運的牧牛場。"},{"en":"A remote working cattle ranch is an isolated farm that is still actively raising cattle.","zh":"remote working cattle ranch 指偏僻而仍積極飼養牛隻的農場。"},{"en":"A remote working cattle ranch may have few nearby houses but many fields, fences, and animals.","zh":"偏遠而仍在營運的牧牛場附近可能很少房屋，但有許多田地、圍欄和牲畜。"},{"en":"Because such ranches cover large areas, they can sometimes include patches of forest.","zh":"由於這類牧場佔地廣，有時可以包括森林小片區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both location and function.","zh":"這個片語同時描述位置和功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for decades","meaning":"數十年來","examples":[{"en":"The ranch has supported a community of howler monkeys for decades.","zh":"這個牧場數十年來一直支持一個吼猴群落。"},{"en":"For decades means for many periods of ten years.","zh":"for decades 指經過許多個十年。"},{"en":"A family shop may serve the same neighbourhood for decades.","zh":"家族小店可能數十年來服務同一社區。"},{"en":"If monkeys survive in one place for decades, the habitat must provide enough food and shelter.","zh":"如果猴子能在同一地方生存數十年，該棲息地必須提供足夠食物和庇護。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a long period of time.","zh":"這個片語強調很長一段時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be home to","meaning":"是……的棲息地","examples":[{"en":"Hacienda La Pacifica is home to a community of mantled howler monkeys.","zh":"Hacienda La Pacifica 是一個披毛吼猴群落的棲息地。"},{"en":"Be home to means be the place where people, animals, or plants live.","zh":"be home to 指是人、動物或植物生活的地方。"},{"en":"A wetland may be home to many birds, insects, and fish.","zh":"濕地可能是許多鳥類、昆蟲和魚類的棲息地。"},{"en":"If a ranch is home to monkeys, it provides food, trees, and space for them.","zh":"如果牧場是猴子的棲息地，它就為牠們提供食物、樹木和空間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a place as a habitat.","zh":"這個片語把地方描述為棲息地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a community of","meaning":"一個……群落","examples":[{"en":"A community of howler monkeys has lived on the ranch for many years.","zh":"一個吼猴群落多年來一直生活在這個牧場。"},{"en":"A community of animals means a group living together or sharing the same area.","zh":"a community of animals 指一群共同生活或共享同一地區的動物。"},{"en":"A community of cats may gather near a market where people feed them.","zh":"一個貓群落可能聚集在有人餵食的街市附近。"},{"en":"If a community of monkeys survives, the group must be able to feed, breed, and move safely.","zh":"如果一個猴群能生存，牠們必須能覓食、繁殖和安全移動。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests more than one animal; it describes a living group.","zh":"這個片語不只指一隻動物，而是描述一個活生生的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mantled howler monkeys","meaning":"披毛吼猴","examples":[{"en":"Mantled howler monkeys have survived in the fragmented landscape.","zh":"披毛吼猴在破碎化的景觀中生存下來。"},{"en":"Mantled howler monkeys are a type of howler monkey found in Central and South America.","zh":"mantled howler monkeys 指一種分布於中美洲和南美洲的吼猴。"},{"en":"Visitors may hear mantled howler monkeys before they see them because their calls are very loud.","zh":"遊客可能先聽到披毛吼猴，然後才看到牠們，因為牠們叫聲很大。"},{"en":"If forest becomes fragmented, adaptable monkeys like howlers may survive better than species needing continuous forest.","zh":"如果森林變得破碎化，像吼猴這種適應力強的猴子，可能比需要連續森林的物種更能生存。"},{"en":"The phrase names the particular monkey species discussed.","zh":"這個片語指出文章討論的特定猴種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"native primates","meaning":"本土靈長類動物","examples":[{"en":"Several native primates once lived in the area.","zh":"幾種本土靈長類動物曾經生活在該地區。"},{"en":"Native primates are primate species that naturally belong to a particular region.","zh":"native primates 指自然屬於某一地區的靈長類物種。"},{"en":"A national park may protect native primates by preserving fruit trees and nesting areas.","zh":"國家公園可能透過保護果樹和棲息區來保護本土靈長類動物。"},{"en":"If native primates disappear, the local ecosystem loses animals that once helped spread seeds.","zh":"如果本土靈長類動物消失，當地生態系統就失去曾幫助傳播種子的動物。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to local monkeys or related animals, not introduced species.","zh":"這個片語指本地猴類或相關動物，而不是外來物種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"white-faced capuchin monkeys","meaning":"白面卷尾猴","examples":[{"en":"White-faced capuchin monkeys disappeared from the ranch area.","zh":"白面卷尾猴從牧場地區消失了。"},{"en":"White-faced capuchin monkeys are small Central American monkeys with pale faces and dark bodies.","zh":"white-faced capuchin monkeys 指面部較淺、身體較深色的中美洲小型猴類。"},{"en":"Tourists may recognise white-faced capuchin monkeys because they are active and curious.","zh":"遊客可能認得白面卷尾猴，因為牠們活躍又好奇。"},{"en":"If forest patches become too small, capuchins may leave or fail to survive there.","zh":"如果森林小片區太細，卷尾猴可能離開或無法在那裡生存。"},{"en":"The phrase names one of the monkey species affected by habitat change.","zh":"這個片語指出受棲息地改變影響的其中一種猴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"spider monkeys","meaning":"蜘蛛猴","examples":[{"en":"Spider monkeys need large areas of continuous forest.","zh":"蜘蛛猴需要大片連綿不斷的森林。"},{"en":"Spider monkeys are long-limbed monkeys that often move through trees using their arms and tails.","zh":"spider monkeys 指四肢修長，常用手臂和尾巴在樹間移動的猴類。"},{"en":"A zoo sign may explain that spider monkeys need climbing space and social groups.","zh":"動物園標示可能解釋蜘蛛猴需要攀爬空間和社群。"},{"en":"If forests are cut into small patches, spider monkeys may struggle because they need wide connected habitat.","zh":"如果森林被切成小片，蜘蛛猴可能難以生存，因為牠們需要廣闊相連的棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase names a monkey species that is less tolerant of fragmented forest.","zh":"這個片語指出一種較不能忍受破碎森林的猴類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"once common in","meaning":"曾經常見於……","examples":[{"en":"All three monkey species were once common in the region.","zh":"三種猴類都曾經常見於該地區。"},{"en":"Once common in means used to be frequently found in a place but may not be common now.","zh":"once common in 指過去常在某地出現，但現在可能不再常見。"},{"en":"Fireflies were once common in some villages before light pollution increased.","zh":"螢火蟲在光污染增加前，曾經常見於一些村莊。"},{"en":"If an animal was once common but is now rare, the environment has probably changed.","zh":"如果某動物過去常見但現在罕見，環境很可能已經改變。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the past with the present.","zh":"這個片語比較過去和現在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"vanish after","meaning":"在……之後消失","examples":[{"en":"Two monkey species vanished after the highway was built.","zh":"兩種猴類在公路建成後消失。"},{"en":"Vanish after means disappear following a particular event or change.","zh":"vanish after 指在某事件或變化之後消失。"},{"en":"Small shops may vanish after a large shopping mall opens nearby.","zh":"大型商場在附近開業後，小店可能消失。"},{"en":"If animals vanish after construction, the project may have damaged their habitat or movement routes.","zh":"如果動物在建設工程後消失，該項目可能破壞了牠們的棲息地或移動路線。"},{"en":"The phrase links disappearance with a later cause or trigger.","zh":"這個片語把消失與後來的原因或觸發因素連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be built nearby","meaning":"在附近建成","examples":[{"en":"The Pan-American Highway was built nearby in the 1950s.","zh":"泛美公路在二十世紀五十年代於附近建成。"},{"en":"Be built nearby means be constructed close to the place being discussed.","zh":"be built nearby 指在正在討論的地方附近建造完成。"},{"en":"A new hospital may be built nearby so residents can reach care more quickly.","zh":"新醫院可能在附近建成，令居民能更快得到醫療服務。"},{"en":"If a major road is built nearby, noise, traffic, and habitat changes may follow.","zh":"如果主要道路在附近建成，噪音、交通和棲息地變化可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes location in relation to another place.","zh":"這個片語描述相對於另一地方的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"surrounding land","meaning":"周邊土地","examples":[{"en":"Most of the surrounding land was cleared for cattle-raising.","zh":"大部分周邊土地被清理以用作牧牛業。"},{"en":"Surrounding land means the land around a particular place.","zh":"surrounding land 指某一地點周圍的土地。"},{"en":"The surrounding land near a school may include roads, shops, parks, and housing estates.","zh":"學校附近的周邊土地可能包括道路、商店、公園和屋苑。"},{"en":"If surrounding land is cleared, animals may be trapped in smaller habitat patches.","zh":"如果周邊土地被清理，動物可能被困在更小的棲息地片區中。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the area around the main site.","zh":"這個片語集中於主要地點周圍的區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be cleared for","meaning":"被清理以用作……","examples":[{"en":"Large areas of forest were cleared for cattle-raising.","zh":"大片森林被清理以用作牧牛業。"},{"en":"Be cleared for means trees or vegetation are removed so the land can be used for a purpose.","zh":"be cleared for 指樹木或植被被移除，以便土地用於某目的。"},{"en":"A field may be cleared for a new school building.","zh":"一塊田地可能被清理以用作新校舍。"},{"en":"If forest is cleared for farming, wildlife may lose food, shelter, and movement routes.","zh":"如果森林被清理作農業用途，野生動物可能失去食物、庇護和移動路線。"},{"en":"The phrase describes land-use change after removal of vegetation.","zh":"這個片語描述植被移除後的土地用途改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cattle-raising","meaning":"牧牛業","examples":[{"en":"Forest was removed to make room for cattle-raising.","zh":"森林被移除，以騰出空間作牧牛業。"},{"en":"Cattle-raising means keeping and breeding cows or bulls for meat, milk, or farming income.","zh":"cattle-raising 指飼養和繁殖牛隻，以獲得肉、奶或農業收入。"},{"en":"A family may depend on cattle-raising if it sells milk to nearby towns.","zh":"如果一家人把牛奶賣到附近城鎮，可能依賴牧牛業維生。"},{"en":"If cattle-raising expands into forest areas, wildlife habitat may shrink.","zh":"如果牧牛業擴展到森林地區，野生動物棲息地可能縮小。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to livestock farming involving cattle.","zh":"這個片語指涉及牛隻的畜牧業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"enlightened ranch owner","meaning":"思想開明的牧場主人","examples":[{"en":"An enlightened ranch owner preserved strips of native trees.","zh":"一位思想開明的牧場主人保留了一排排本土樹木。"},{"en":"An enlightened ranch owner is a forward-thinking landowner who makes sensible choices beyond short-term profit.","zh":"enlightened ranch owner 指有遠見、作出超越短期利潤的理性選擇的土地擁有人。"},{"en":"An enlightened shop owner may reduce plastic use before the law requires it.","zh":"思想開明的店主可能在法律要求前已減少使用塑膠。"},{"en":"If a ranch owner preserves trees, the decision may help both cattle and wildlife.","zh":"如果牧場主人保留樹木，這個決定可能同時幫助牛隻和野生動物。"},{"en":"The phrase praises wise and progressive judgement.","zh":"這個片語讚賞明智而進步的判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"choose to leave","meaning":"選擇保留……","examples":[{"en":"The owner chose to leave some native trees standing.","zh":"牧場主人選擇保留一些本土樹木。"},{"en":"Choose to leave means deliberately decide not to remove something.","zh":"choose to leave 指刻意決定不移除某物。"},{"en":"A family may choose to leave an old tree in the garden because it gives shade.","zh":"一個家庭可能選擇保留花園中的老樹，因為它提供樹蔭。"},{"en":"If farmers choose to leave trees, animals may keep using them as food and travel routes.","zh":"如果農民選擇保留樹木，動物可能繼續把它們用作食物和移動路線。"},{"en":"The phrase shows active preservation, not forgetfulness.","zh":"這個片語顯示主動保育，而不是忘記處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"strips of native trees","meaning":"一排排本土樹木","examples":[{"en":"The ranch owner preserved strips of native trees.","zh":"牧場主人保留了一排排本土樹木。"},{"en":"Strips of native trees are long narrow lines of local tree species left or planted across land.","zh":"strips of native trees 指橫跨土地而被保留或種植的狹長本地樹種帶。"},{"en":"A farm may keep strips of native trees between fields to reduce wind and protect soil.","zh":"農場可能在田地之間保留一排排本土樹木，以減少風力並保護土壤。"},{"en":"If strips of trees remain, monkeys and birds can move through open farmland more safely.","zh":"如果樹帶仍然存在，猴子和鳥類可以更安全地穿越開闊農地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes narrow bands of local vegetation.","zh":"這個片語描述狹長的本地植被帶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"use something as windbreaks","meaning":"把……用作防風林","examples":[{"en":"The owner used the trees as windbreaks.","zh":"牧場主人把樹木用作防風林。"},{"en":"Use something as windbreaks means use it to block or reduce strong wind.","zh":"use something as windbreaks 指用某物阻擋或減弱強風。"},{"en":"Farmers may use rows of trees as windbreaks to protect young crops.","zh":"農民可能把一排排樹木用作防風林，以保護幼苗。"},{"en":"If trees reduce dry winds, crops lose less moisture and animals suffer less stress.","zh":"如果樹木減弱乾風，作物失水較少，動物承受的壓力也較少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a practical agricultural use of trees.","zh":"這個片語描述樹木在農業上的實際用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"protect...from...","meaning":"保護……免受……影響","examples":[{"en":"The windbreaks protected cattle and crops from dry-season winds.","zh":"防風林保護牛隻和作物免受旱季強風影響。"},{"en":"Protect A from B means keep A safe from harm caused by B.","zh":"protect A from B 指保護 A 免受 B 造成的傷害。"},{"en":"Sunscreen protects skin from strong sunlight.","zh":"防曬霜保護皮膚免受強烈陽光傷害。"},{"en":"If trees protect crops from wind, farmers may get better growth and less damage.","zh":"如果樹木保護作物免受強風影響，農民可能得到更好生長和較少損害。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly shows danger and defence.","zh":"這個片語清楚顯示危險和防禦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"food crops","meaning":"糧食作物","examples":[{"en":"The trees protected both the cattle and their food crops.","zh":"樹木同時保護牛隻和牠們的糧食作物。"},{"en":"Food crops are plants grown for people or animals to eat.","zh":"food crops 指為人或動物食用而種植的植物。"},{"en":"Rice, corn, beans, and vegetables are common food crops in many communities.","zh":"米、粟米、豆類和蔬菜是許多社區常見的糧食作物。"},{"en":"If dry winds damage food crops, farmers may lose income and families may face higher food prices.","zh":"如果旱風吹壞糧食作物，農民可能失去收入，家庭也可能面對更高食物價格。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to crops grown for nutrition, not decoration.","zh":"這個片語指為營養而種植的作物，而不是裝飾植物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"dry-season winds","meaning":"旱季強風","examples":[{"en":"Windbreaks reduced the effects of dry-season winds.","zh":"防風林減少了旱季強風的影響。"},{"en":"Dry-season winds are strong winds that occur during the dry part of the year.","zh":"dry-season winds 指一年中乾旱季節出現的強風。"},{"en":"Farmers may plant trees to reduce dry-season winds that remove moisture from soil.","zh":"農民可能種樹，以減少帶走土壤水分的旱季強風。"},{"en":"If dry-season winds are severe, young plants may dry out or break.","zh":"如果旱季強風嚴重，幼苗可能乾枯或折斷。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a seasonal climate pressure.","zh":"這個片語描述一種季節性氣候壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in the process","meaning":"在過程中","examples":[{"en":"In the process, the farmer created a valuable research site.","zh":"在過程中，這位農民創造了一個有價值的研究地點。"},{"en":"In the process means while doing one thing, another result also happens.","zh":"in the process 指做某事時，另一個結果也同時發生。"},{"en":"A student may organise their notes and, in the process, discover gaps in their understanding.","zh":"學生整理筆記時，可能在過程中發現自己理解上的空隙。"},{"en":"If a farmer preserves trees for wind protection, they may also create wildlife habitat in the process.","zh":"如果農民為防風而保留樹木，也可能在過程中創造野生動物棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an additional result.","zh":"這個片語引出額外結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"unwittingly founded","meaning":"無意中建立","examples":[{"en":"The farmer unwittingly founded a unique natural laboratory.","zh":"這位農民無意中建立了一個獨特的天然實驗場。"},{"en":"Unwittingly founded means created or established something without realising it at the time.","zh":"unwittingly founded 指在當時沒有意識到的情況下創造或建立某事物。"},{"en":"A teacher who starts a small reading club may unwittingly found a school-wide tradition.","zh":"老師開辦一個小型閱讀會，可能無意中建立全校傳統。"},{"en":"If someone’s practical decision later becomes valuable for research, they may have founded something by accident.","zh":"如果某人的實際決定後來對研究有價值，他可能是偶然建立了某事。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights an unintended but important result.","zh":"這個片語突出非本意但重要的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"unique laboratory for","meaning":"研究……的獨特實驗場","examples":[{"en":"The ranch became a unique laboratory for the study of monkeys.","zh":"這個牧場成為研究猴子的獨特實驗場。"},{"en":"A unique laboratory for something is a special place where that subject can be studied unusually well.","zh":"unique laboratory for something 指一個能特別有效地研究某主題的特殊地方。"},{"en":"A busy railway station can be a unique laboratory for studying how people move through crowds.","zh":"繁忙火車站可以成為研究人群流動的獨特實驗場。"},{"en":"If monkeys live beside farmland, the ranch becomes useful for studying wildlife in altered landscapes.","zh":"如果猴子生活在農地旁邊，牧場就成為研究受改造景觀中野生動物的有用地方。"},{"en":"The phrase does not always mean an indoor science lab.","zh":"這個片語不一定指室內科學實驗室。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the study of monkeys","meaning":"對猴子的研究","examples":[{"en":"The preserved trees created opportunities for the study of monkeys.","zh":"被保留的樹木為對猴子的研究創造了機會。"},{"en":"The study of monkeys means scientific observation and research into monkey behaviour, diet, movement, and survival.","zh":"the study of monkeys 指對猴子行為、飲食、移動和生存的科學觀察和研究。"},{"en":"A student interested in the study of monkeys may learn biology, ecology, and animal behaviour.","zh":"對猴子研究感興趣的學生可能學習生物學、生態學和動物行為。"},{"en":"If monkeys live near farms, researchers can study how they adapt to human activity.","zh":"如果猴子生活在農場附近，研究人員可以研究牠們如何適應人類活動。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to scientific research, not casual watching.","zh":"這個片語指科學研究，而不是隨便觀看。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"primatologist","meaning":"靈長類動物學家","examples":[{"en":"Ken Glander is a primatologist from Duke University.","zh":"Ken Glander 是來自杜克大學的靈長類動物學家。"},{"en":"A primatologist is a scientist who studies primates such as monkeys, apes, and lemurs.","zh":"primatologist 指研究猴子、猿和狐猴等靈長類動物的科學家。"},{"en":"A primatologist may spend months in a forest recording what monkeys eat and how they move.","zh":"靈長類動物學家可能在森林中花數月記錄猴子吃甚麼和如何移動。"},{"en":"If a primatologist studies forest regeneration, they may connect animal behaviour with plant recovery.","zh":"如果靈長類動物學家研究森林再生，就可能把動物行為與植物恢復連接起來。"},{"en":"The word names a specialist in primate research.","zh":"這個詞指靈長類研究專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in an effort to understand","meaning":"為了了解……","examples":[{"en":"Glander is studying the monkeys in an effort to understand forest regeneration.","zh":"Glander 正在研究猴子，為了了解森林再生。"},{"en":"In an effort to understand means with the purpose of learning or explaining something.","zh":"in an effort to understand 指以學習或解釋某事為目的。"},{"en":"Doctors may collect patient histories in an effort to understand why symptoms keep returning.","zh":"醫生可能收集病歷，為了了解症狀為何反覆出現。"},{"en":"If scientists observe monkeys carefully, they may understand how animals help forests recover.","zh":"如果科學家仔細觀察猴子，就可能了解動物如何幫助森林恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the purpose behind an action.","zh":"這個片語解釋行動背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the relationship between","meaning":"……之間的關係","examples":[{"en":"The research examines the relationship between howlers and regenerating forests.","zh":"該研究檢視吼猴與再生森林之間的關係。"},{"en":"The relationship between two things is the way they are connected or affect each other.","zh":"the relationship between two things 指兩者如何連接或互相影響。"},{"en":"Teachers may study the relationship between sleep and exam performance.","zh":"老師可能研究睡眠與考試表現之間的關係。"},{"en":"If monkeys eat fruit and spread seeds, they may influence how forests grow back.","zh":"如果猴子吃水果並傳播種子，牠們可能影響森林如何重新生長。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on connection and interaction.","zh":"這個片語集中於連繫和互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"regenerating forests","meaning":"再生中的森林","examples":[{"en":"Howler monkeys can thrive in regenerating forests.","zh":"吼猴能在再生中的森林茁壯生存。"},{"en":"Regenerating forests are forests that are growing back after being cut, burnt, or damaged.","zh":"regenerating forests 指被砍伐、焚燒或破壞後正在重新生長的森林。"},{"en":"A hillside can become a regenerating forest if farming stops and trees return naturally.","zh":"如果耕作停止而樹木自然回歸，山坡可以變成再生中的森林。"},{"en":"If regenerating forests provide young leaves and fruit, some animals can quickly move back in.","zh":"如果再生森林提供嫩葉和果實，一些動物可以很快遷回。"},{"en":"The phrase describes forests in recovery.","zh":"這個片語描述正在恢復的森林。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at the edges of","meaning":"在……邊緣","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys live in woodland at the edges of grazing lands.","zh":"猴子生活在牧草地邊緣的林地中。"},{"en":"At the edges of means near the outer boundary of an area.","zh":"at the edges of 指在某區域外圍邊界附近。"},{"en":"Children may play at the edges of a park where the grass meets the pavement.","zh":"孩子可能在公園邊緣、草地與行人路交界處玩耍。"},{"en":"If woodland grows at the edges of farmland, animals can use it as a border habitat.","zh":"如果林地在農地邊緣生長，動物可以把它用作邊界棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes position near a boundary.","zh":"這個片語描述靠近邊界的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"grazing lands","meaning":"牧草地","examples":[{"en":"Regenerating trees grow beside cattle-grazing lands.","zh":"再生樹木生長在牛隻牧草地旁邊。"},{"en":"Grazing lands are areas where animals such as cattle feed on grass.","zh":"grazing lands 指牛等動物吃草的土地。"},{"en":"Farmers may move cows between grazing lands so the grass can recover.","zh":"農民可能把牛在不同牧草地之間移動，讓草地恢復。"},{"en":"If trees grow near grazing lands, they can provide shade, food, and wildlife corridors.","zh":"如果樹木在牧草地附近生長，就能提供樹蔭、食物和野生動物通道。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to land used for feeding livestock.","zh":"這個片語指用來餵養牲畜的土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"disturbed woodlands","meaning":"受干擾的林地","examples":[{"en":"Disturbed woodlands are increasingly important to tropical wildlife.","zh":"受干擾的林地對熱帶野生動物日益重要。"},{"en":"Disturbed woodlands are forest areas changed by human activity, fire, farming, or other disruption.","zh":"disturbed woodlands 指被人類活動、火災、耕作或其他干擾改變的森林地區。"},{"en":"A woodland beside a road may be disturbed but still support birds and insects.","zh":"道路旁邊的林地可能受干擾，但仍支持鳥類和昆蟲。"},{"en":"If original forests disappear, disturbed woodlands may become the only remaining habitat.","zh":"如果原始森林消失，受干擾林地可能成為僅存棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase does not mean useless forest; it means altered forest.","zh":"這個片語不是指無用森林，而是指被改變的森林。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"increasingly important","meaning":"日益重要","examples":[{"en":"The study of disturbed forests is increasingly important.","zh":"對受干擾森林的研究日益重要。"},{"en":"Increasingly important means becoming more important over time.","zh":"increasingly important 指隨時間變得越來越重要。"},{"en":"Digital skills are increasingly important because many services now operate online.","zh":"數碼技能日益重要，因為許多服務現在在線上運作。"},{"en":"If natural forests are disappearing, studying damaged or recovering forests becomes more urgent.","zh":"如果天然森林正在消失，研究受損或恢復中的森林就變得更迫切。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a rising level of importance.","zh":"這個片語顯示重要性上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"throughout much of","meaning":"遍及……大部分地區","examples":[{"en":"Disturbed forests are common throughout much of the New World Tropics.","zh":"受干擾森林常見於新世界熱帶地區的大部分地方。"},{"en":"Throughout much of means across a large part of an area.","zh":"throughout much of 指遍及某區域的大部分地方。"},{"en":"Public buses operate throughout much of the city, but not every village is covered.","zh":"公共巴士遍及城市大部分地區，但不是每條村都有覆蓋。"},{"en":"If disturbed forests occur throughout much of a region, conservation must include them.","zh":"如果受干擾森林遍及某地區大部分地方，保育就必須包括它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes wide but not complete coverage.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛但不完全的覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the New World Tropics","meaning":"新世界熱帶地區","examples":[{"en":"Many original forests have disappeared across the New World Tropics.","zh":"許多原始森林已在新世界熱帶地區消失。"},{"en":"The New World Tropics refers to tropical regions of the Americas.","zh":"the New World Tropics 指美洲的熱帶地區。"},{"en":"Scientists studying the New World Tropics may work in rainforests, dry forests, and plantations.","zh":"研究新世界熱帶地區的科學家可能在雨林、乾旱森林和種植園工作。"},{"en":"If habitats across the New World Tropics are altered, many species must adapt or decline.","zh":"如果新世界熱帶地區的棲息地被改變，許多物種必須適應或減少。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a broad geographical region.","zh":"這個片語給出一個廣闊地理區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the only forests left","meaning":"僅存的森林","examples":[{"en":"In many regions, disturbed woodlands are the only forests left.","zh":"在許多地區，受干擾林地是僅存的森林。"},{"en":"The only forests left means the last remaining forest areas after most forest has disappeared.","zh":"the only forests left 指大部分森林消失後最後剩下的森林地區。"},{"en":"In a city district, a few old parks may be the only green spaces left.","zh":"在城市區域中，幾個舊公園可能是僅存的綠地。"},{"en":"If disturbed woodlands are the only forests left, they become crucial for wildlife survival.","zh":"如果受干擾林地是僅存的森林，它們對野生動物生存就變得關鍵。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses scarcity and remaining value.","zh":"這個片語強調稀少和剩餘價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tropical dry forests","meaning":"熱帶乾旱森林","examples":[{"en":"Tropical dry forests once covered most of Central America.","zh":"熱帶乾旱森林曾覆蓋中美洲大部分地區。"},{"en":"Tropical dry forests are warm forests that have a clear dry season and less constant rainfall than rainforests.","zh":"tropical dry forests 指有明顯旱季、降雨不如雨林持續的溫暖森林。"},{"en":"Some tropical dry forests lose many leaves during the dry season to save water.","zh":"有些熱帶乾旱森林在旱季會落下許多葉子以節省水分。"},{"en":"If tropical dry forests are cleared, species adapted to seasonal drought lose habitat.","zh":"如果熱帶乾旱森林被清除，適應季節性乾旱的物種就會失去棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a specific type of tropical ecosystem.","zh":"這個片語描述特定類型的熱帶生態系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cover most of","meaning":"覆蓋……大部分","examples":[{"en":"Tropical dry forests once covered most of the region.","zh":"熱帶乾旱森林曾覆蓋該地區大部分地方。"},{"en":"Cover most of means extend over the largest part of an area.","zh":"cover most of 指延伸覆蓋某區域的最大部分。"},{"en":"Snow may cover most of a playground after a heavy storm.","zh":"大風雪後，雪可能覆蓋操場大部分地方。"},{"en":"If forests cover most of a region, wildlife can move more freely across it.","zh":"如果森林覆蓋某地區大部分地方，野生動物就能更自由地移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes wide physical coverage.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛的實體覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"remain undisturbed","meaning":"保持未受干擾","examples":[{"en":"By the 1980s, very little dry forest remained undisturbed.","zh":"到二十世紀八十年代，只有很少乾旱森林保持未受干擾。"},{"en":"Remain undisturbed means continue without being damaged, cleared, or heavily changed.","zh":"remain undisturbed 指繼續未被破壞、清除或嚴重改變。"},{"en":"A quiet study room remains undisturbed if nobody enters or makes noise.","zh":"如果沒有人進入或製造噪音，安靜自修室就保持未受干擾。"},{"en":"If only a little forest remains undisturbed, most habitat has already been altered.","zh":"如果只有少量森林保持未受干擾，大部分棲息地已被改變。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses protection from disruption.","zh":"這個片語強調免受干擾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"less than two per cent","meaning":"少於百分之二","examples":[{"en":"Less than two per cent of the original forest remained undisturbed.","zh":"少於百分之二的原始森林保持未受干擾。"},{"en":"Less than two per cent means a very small amount, below 2 out of every 100.","zh":"less than two per cent 指非常少，低於每一百之中的二。"},{"en":"If less than two per cent of students choose a subject, the school may struggle to run the class.","zh":"如果少於百分之二的學生選某科，學校可能難以開班。"},{"en":"If less than two per cent of forest remains, the loss is extremely severe.","zh":"如果少於百分之二的森林仍然存在，損失就極其嚴重。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a precise sign of scarcity.","zh":"這個片語給出稀少程度的精確標記。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be protected","meaning":"受到保護","examples":[{"en":"Less than one per cent of the forest was protected.","zh":"少於百分之一的森林受到保護。"},{"en":"Be protected means be legally, physically, or actively kept safe from damage.","zh":"be protected 指在法律上、實際上或透過行動被保護免受損害。"},{"en":"A historic building may be protected so developers cannot demolish it.","zh":"歷史建築可能受到保護，因此發展商不能拆卸它。"},{"en":"If forest is protected, logging, farming, or hunting may be restricted.","zh":"如果森林受到保護，伐木、耕作或狩獵可能受限制。"},{"en":"The phrase implies active measures to prevent harm.","zh":"這個片語暗示有主動措施防止傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"persist at","meaning":"在……繼續生存","examples":[{"en":"Howlers persist at La Pacifica because they can eat leaves.","zh":"吼猴能在 La Pacifica 繼續生存，因為牠們能吃樹葉。"},{"en":"Persist at a place means continue to survive or remain there despite difficulty.","zh":"persist at a place 指即使有困難仍繼續在某地生存或留下。"},{"en":"Small shops may persist in an old market because local residents still support them.","zh":"小店可能在舊街市中繼續生存，因為本地居民仍支持它們。"},{"en":"If howlers can eat leaves when fruit is scarce, they can persist where other monkeys disappear.","zh":"如果吼猴在水果稀少時能吃樹葉，就能在其他猴子消失的地方繼續生存。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests survival under pressure.","zh":"這個片語暗示在壓力下生存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"leaf-eaters","meaning":"食葉動物","examples":[{"en":"Howler monkeys are highly adaptable leaf-eaters.","zh":"吼猴是適應力很強的食葉動物。"},{"en":"Leaf-eaters are animals that feed mainly or partly on leaves.","zh":"leaf-eaters 指主要或部分以樹葉為食的動物。"},{"en":"Caterpillars are common leaf-eaters in many gardens.","zh":"毛蟲是許多花園中常見的食葉動物。"},{"en":"If an animal can live as a leaf-eater, it may survive when fruit is limited.","zh":"如果動物能以食葉方式生存，在水果有限時可能仍能活下來。"},{"en":"The phrase describes diet and feeding strategy.","zh":"這個片語描述飲食和覓食策略。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"when it is available","meaning":"在有供應時","examples":[{"en":"Howlers eat fruit when it is available.","zh":"吼猴在有水果供應時會吃水果。"},{"en":"When it is available means when something can be found or obtained.","zh":"when it is available 指當某物能被找到或取得時。"},{"en":"Students use the library room when it is available after lessons.","zh":"學生在課後圖書館房間有空時使用它。"},{"en":"If fruit is seasonal, monkeys eat it when it is available and use other foods when it is not.","zh":"如果水果有季節性，猴子在有供應時吃水果，沒有時則吃其他食物。"},{"en":"The phrase shows dependence on supply.","zh":"這個片語顯示取決於供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"unlike","meaning":"與……不同","examples":[{"en":"Unlike spider monkeys, howlers do not require extensive fruiting forests.","zh":"與蜘蛛猴不同，吼猴不需要大片結果實的森林。"},{"en":"Unlike means different from someone or something else.","zh":"unlike 指與某人或某物不同。"},{"en":"Unlike younger children, older students may study independently for longer periods.","zh":"與年幼孩子不同，年長學生可能能較長時間獨立學習。"},{"en":"If howlers do not need large fruiting forests, they can survive in smaller or disturbed areas.","zh":"如果吼猴不需要大片結果實的森林，牠們就能在較小或受干擾地區生存。"},{"en":"The word introduces a clear contrast.","zh":"這個詞引出清楚對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"depend on","meaning":"依賴……","examples":[{"en":"Spider monkeys depend on large areas of fruiting trees.","zh":"蜘蛛猴依賴大片結果實的樹木。"},{"en":"Depend on means need something in order to live, work, or succeed.","zh":"depend on 指需要某物才能生活、運作或成功。"},{"en":"Many students depend on public transport to get to school on time.","zh":"許多學生依賴公共交通準時上學。"},{"en":"If an animal depends on one habitat type, habitat loss can be especially dangerous.","zh":"如果動物依賴某一種棲息地，棲息地喪失可能特別危險。"},{"en":"The phrase shows reliance.","zh":"這個片語顯示依靠關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"large areas of fruiting trees","meaning":"大片結果實的樹木","examples":[{"en":"Some primates need large areas of fruiting trees.","zh":"有些靈長類動物需要大片結果實的樹木。"},{"en":"Large areas of fruiting trees are wide spaces containing many trees that produce fruit.","zh":"large areas of fruiting trees 指有許多結果實樹木的廣闊空間。"},{"en":"A fruit bat colony may need large areas of fruiting trees to find enough food.","zh":"果蝠群落可能需要大片結果實的樹木才能找到足夠食物。"},{"en":"If fruiting trees are scattered too widely, animals may spend more energy travelling.","zh":"如果結果實的樹木分布太零散，動物可能花更多能量移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both food supply and habitat size.","zh":"這個片語同時描述食物供應和棲息地大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be particularly interested in","meaning":"對……特別感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Glander is particularly interested in the monkeys’ tolerance of toxins.","zh":"Glander 對猴子忍受毒素的能力特別感興趣。"},{"en":"Be particularly interested in means be especially keen to study or know about something.","zh":"be particularly interested in 指特別想研究或了解某事。"},{"en":"A doctor may be particularly interested in a patient’s sleep habits if tiredness is the main problem.","zh":"如果疲倦是主要問題，醫生可能對病人的睡眠習慣特別感興趣。"},{"en":"If one feature explains survival, researchers may pay special attention to it.","zh":"如果某一特徵能解釋生存，研究人員可能特別關注它。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a focused interest.","zh":"這個片語顯示集中的興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ability to thrive on","meaning":"靠……茁壯生存的能力","examples":[{"en":"Howlers have the ability to thrive on toxic leaves.","zh":"吼猴有靠有毒樹葉茁壯生存的能力。"},{"en":"Ability to thrive on something means the capacity to live well by using it as food or support.","zh":"ability to thrive on something 指利用某物作食物或支持而生活良好的能力。"},{"en":"Some students have the ability to thrive on structured routines and clear deadlines.","zh":"有些學生有靠結構清晰的常規和明確截止日期而表現良好的能力。"},{"en":"If howlers thrive on leaves that other animals avoid, they gain a survival advantage.","zh":"如果吼猴能靠其他動物避開的樹葉茁壯生存，牠們就獲得生存優勢。"},{"en":"The phrase means doing well, not merely surviving.","zh":"這個片語指生活得好，而不只是勉強生存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"leaves loaded with toxins","meaning":"含有大量毒素的樹葉","examples":[{"en":"Howlers can eat leaves loaded with toxins.","zh":"吼猴可以吃含有大量毒素的樹葉。"},{"en":"Leaves loaded with toxins are leaves containing a large amount of poisonous chemicals.","zh":"leaves loaded with toxins 指含有大量有毒化學物的葉子。"},{"en":"Some garden plants have leaves loaded with toxins, so children should not eat unknown leaves.","zh":"有些園藝植物有含毒素的葉子，所以孩子不應吃未知葉子。"},{"en":"If monkeys can digest toxic leaves, they can use a food source others cannot.","zh":"如果猴子能消化有毒樹葉，就能使用其他動物不能用的食物來源。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the leaves are chemically difficult or dangerous to eat.","zh":"這個片語強調葉子在化學上難吃或危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"poisonous substances","meaning":"有毒物質","examples":[{"en":"Plants produce poisonous substances as a form of defence.","zh":"植物產生有毒物質作為一種防禦。"},{"en":"Poisonous substances are materials or chemicals that can harm or kill living things.","zh":"poisonous substances 指能傷害或殺死生物的材料或化學物。"},{"en":"Cleaning products may contain poisonous substances and should be kept away from children.","zh":"清潔用品可能含有有毒物質，應遠離兒童存放。"},{"en":"If plants contain poisonous substances, animals may avoid eating them.","zh":"如果植物含有有毒物質，動物可能避免吃它們。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to harmful chemicals or materials.","zh":"這個片語指有害化學物或材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be designed to protect","meaning":"旨在保護……","examples":[{"en":"Plant toxins are designed to protect the plants from animals.","zh":"植物毒素旨在保護植物免受動物侵害。"},{"en":"Be designed to protect means have the purpose of keeping something safe from harm.","zh":"be designed to protect 指目的在於保護某物免受傷害。"},{"en":"A bicycle helmet is designed to protect the head during accidents.","zh":"單車頭盔旨在意外時保護頭部。"},{"en":"If toxins make leaves unpleasant or dangerous, they protect plants from being eaten.","zh":"如果毒素令葉子難吃或危險，它們就保護植物免被吃掉。"},{"en":"The phrase explains protective purpose or function.","zh":"這個片語解釋保護目的或功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"long-term exposure to","meaning":"長期接觸……","examples":[{"en":"Long-term exposure to a toxin may increase an animal’s tolerance.","zh":"長期接觸某種毒素可能提高動物的耐受力。"},{"en":"Long-term exposure to something means contact with it over a long period.","zh":"long-term exposure to something 指長時間與某物接觸。"},{"en":"Long-term exposure to loud noise can damage hearing.","zh":"長期接觸巨大噪音可能損害聽力。"},{"en":"If animals repeatedly eat small amounts of a toxin, their bodies may adapt over time.","zh":"如果動物反覆吃少量毒素，牠們的身體可能隨時間適應。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on repeated or prolonged contact.","zh":"這個片語集中於反覆或長時間接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a specific plant toxin","meaning":"某種特定植物毒素","examples":[{"en":"Leaf-eaters may adapt to a specific plant toxin.","zh":"食葉動物可能適應某種特定植物毒素。"},{"en":"A specific plant toxin is one particular poisonous chemical produced by plants.","zh":"a specific plant toxin 指植物產生的某一種特定有毒化學物。"},{"en":"A scientist may test whether an insect can tolerate a specific plant toxin in one crop.","zh":"科學家可能測試昆蟲是否能忍受某種作物中的特定植物毒素。"},{"en":"If an animal adapts to one toxin, it may still be vulnerable to a different toxin.","zh":"如果動物適應一種毒素，仍可能容易受另一種毒素影響。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses one exact chemical defence.","zh":"這個片語強調一種確切的化學防禦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"increase someone’s ability to","meaning":"提升某人……的能力","examples":[{"en":"Exposure can increase a monkey’s ability to neutralize toxins.","zh":"接觸毒素可以提升猴子中和毒素的能力。"},{"en":"Increase someone’s ability to means make someone better able to do something.","zh":"increase someone’s ability to 指令某人更有能力做某事。"},{"en":"Daily speaking practice can increase a student’s ability to answer questions naturally.","zh":"每日口語練習可以提升學生自然回答問題的能力。"},{"en":"If repeated exposure helps the body adapt, the animal may handle toxins more effectively.","zh":"如果反覆接觸幫助身體適應，動物可能更有效處理毒素。"},{"en":"The phrase links practice or experience with improved ability.","zh":"這個片語把練習或經驗與能力提升連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"neutralize poisonous substances","meaning":"中和有毒物質","examples":[{"en":"Howlers can neutralize poisonous substances in leaves.","zh":"吼猴可以中和樹葉中的有毒物質。"},{"en":"Neutralize poisonous substances means make harmful chemicals less dangerous or harmless.","zh":"neutralize poisonous substances 指令有害化學物變得較不危險或無害。"},{"en":"Medicine may help neutralize stomach acid when a person has serious heartburn.","zh":"當人嚴重胃酸倒流時，藥物可能幫助中和胃酸。"},{"en":"If monkeys neutralize plant toxins, they can safely absorb nutrients from difficult leaves.","zh":"如果猴子中和植物毒素，就能安全吸收難消化葉子的營養。"},{"en":"The phrase describes reducing harmful chemical effects.","zh":"這個片語描述減低有害化學作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"absorb leaf nutrients","meaning":"吸收樹葉中的營養","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys neutralize toxins and absorb leaf nutrients.","zh":"猴子中和毒素並吸收樹葉中的營養。"},{"en":"Absorb leaf nutrients means take useful food substances from leaves into the body.","zh":"absorb leaf nutrients 指把葉子中有用的食物物質吸收到身體內。"},{"en":"Plants absorb nutrients from soil, while animals absorb nutrients from food.","zh":"植物從泥土吸收養分，而動物從食物吸收營養。"},{"en":"If toxins are neutralised first, monkeys can absorb more useful material from the leaves.","zh":"如果毒素先被中和，猴子就能從葉子中吸收更多有用物質。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on getting nourishment from leaves.","zh":"這個片語集中於從樹葉獲得營養。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"generations of howlers","meaning":"多代吼猴","examples":[{"en":"Glander has observed several generations of howlers.","zh":"Glander 已觀察多代吼猴。"},{"en":"Generations of howlers means successive groups of howler monkeys born over time.","zh":"generations of howlers 指隨時間出生的一代又一代吼猴。"},{"en":"A teacher may teach several generations of students during a long career.","zh":"老師在漫長職業生涯中可能教過多代學生。"},{"en":"If scientists observe several generations, they can see long-term changes in behaviour and survival.","zh":"如果科學家觀察多代，就能看見行為和生存上的長期變化。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses continuity over time.","zh":"這個片語強調時間上的延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"keep their systems primed","meaning":"令身體系統保持良好狀態","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys keep their digestive systems primed by sampling different plants.","zh":"猴子透過試食不同植物，令其消化系統保持良好狀態。"},{"en":"Keep their systems primed means keep the body ready to respond effectively.","zh":"keep their systems primed 指令身體保持準備好有效反應的狀態。"},{"en":"Athletes keep their bodies primed by warming up before training.","zh":"運動員訓練前熱身，以令身體保持準備狀態。"},{"en":"If monkeys regularly sample different plants, their digestion may stay prepared for varied toxins.","zh":"如果猴子定期試食不同植物，其消化系統可能保持準備好應對不同毒素。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests maintaining readiness.","zh":"這個片語暗示維持準備狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sample a variety of plants","meaning":"試食多種植物","examples":[{"en":"Howlers sample a variety of plants before selecting their main foods.","zh":"吼猴在選擇主要食物前會試食多種植物。"},{"en":"Sample a variety of plants means try small amounts of many different plants.","zh":"sample a variety of plants 指少量嘗試許多不同植物。"},{"en":"A shopper may sample a variety of teas before choosing one to buy.","zh":"購物者可能先試飲多種茶，再選擇購買哪一款。"},{"en":"If monkeys sample many plants, they can learn which ones are nutritious and safe.","zh":"如果猴子試食許多植物，就能知道哪些有營養又安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes testing options before making a choice.","zh":"這個片語描述在選擇前測試不同選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"focus on a small number of","meaning":"集中於少量……","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys focus on a small number of nutritious food items.","zh":"猴子集中於少量營養豐富的食物。"},{"en":"Focus on a small number of means concentrate on only a few things instead of many.","zh":"focus on a small number of 指集中於少數事物，而不是許多事物。"},{"en":"A student may focus on a small number of weak grammar areas before an exam.","zh":"學生考試前可能集中於少量薄弱文法範疇。"},{"en":"If monkeys identify the best foods, they can spend less energy eating poor-quality leaves.","zh":"如果猴子識別出最佳食物，就能少花能量吃低質葉子。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests selective attention.","zh":"這個片語暗示有選擇性的注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"nutritious food items","meaning":"營養豐富的食物","examples":[{"en":"Howlers identify and select the most nutritious food items.","zh":"吼猴識別並選擇最營養豐富的食物。"},{"en":"Nutritious food items are foods that provide useful energy, protein, vitamins, or minerals.","zh":"nutritious food items 指提供有用能量、蛋白質、維他命或礦物質的食物。"},{"en":"Parents may pack nutritious food items such as fruit, eggs, and whole-grain bread for lunch.","zh":"家長可能為午餐準備水果、雞蛋和全麥麵包等營養豐富的食物。"},{"en":"If animals choose nutritious food, they can grow, reproduce, and stay healthy more easily.","zh":"如果動物選擇營養豐富的食物，就較容易成長、繁殖和保持健康。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to food quality, not just quantity.","zh":"這個片語指食物質素，而不只是數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"more howler-friendly than","meaning":"比……更適合吼猴","examples":[{"en":"Leaves in young forests are more howler-friendly than those in ancient forests.","zh":"年輕森林中的樹葉比古老森林中的樹葉更適合吼猴。"},{"en":"More howler-friendly than means more suitable or helpful for howler monkeys than something else.","zh":"more howler-friendly than 指比另一事物更適合或更有利於吼猴。"},{"en":"A quiet park is more child-friendly than a busy road because children can play safely.","zh":"安靜公園比繁忙道路更適合孩子，因為孩子可以安全玩耍。"},{"en":"If young leaves contain fewer toxins, they may be easier for howlers to eat.","zh":"如果嫩葉含毒素較少，對吼猴來說可能較容易食用。"},{"en":"The phrase compares how suitable two environments are for one species.","zh":"這個片語比較兩種環境對某一物種的適合程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"centuries-old trees","meaning":"已有數百年歷史的樹木","examples":[{"en":"Centuries-old trees often produce higher levels of toxins.","zh":"已有數百年歷史的樹木常產生較高水平的毒素。"},{"en":"Centuries-old trees are trees that have lived for hundreds of years.","zh":"centuries-old trees 指已生長數百年的樹木。"},{"en":"A park may protect centuries-old trees because they are part of local history.","zh":"公園可能保護已有數百年歷史的樹木，因為它們是本地歷史的一部分。"},{"en":"If old trees invest more in chemical defence, their leaves may be harder for animals to eat.","zh":"如果老樹投入更多能量於化學防禦，其葉子對動物來說可能較難吃。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses great age.","zh":"這個片語強調極高樹齡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"survive farther south","meaning":"在更南面的地區存活","examples":[{"en":"Old trees survive farther south in mature forests.","zh":"老樹在更南面的成熟森林中存活。"},{"en":"Survive farther south means continue living in areas located more to the south.","zh":"survive farther south 指在位置更偏南的地區繼續生存。"},{"en":"Some plants survive farther north only when winters become warmer.","zh":"有些植物只有在冬天變暖時，才能在更北面的地區存活。"},{"en":"If old trees survive farther south, their distribution may reflect climate and forest maturity.","zh":"如果老樹在更南面的地區存活，其分布可能反映氣候和森林成熟度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes survival in a particular geographical direction.","zh":"這個片語描述在特定地理方向上的生存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put most of their limited energy into","meaning":"把大部分有限能量投放於……","examples":[{"en":"Young trees put most of their limited energy into growth.","zh":"年輕樹木把大部分有限能量投放於生長。"},{"en":"Put most of their limited energy into means use most available resources for one main purpose.","zh":"put most of their limited energy into 指把大多數可用資源用於一個主要目的。"},{"en":"A student before exams may put most of their limited energy into revision rather than social events.","zh":"考試前的學生可能把大部分有限精力投放於溫習，而不是社交活動。"},{"en":"If young trees spend energy growing, they may produce fewer chemical defences.","zh":"如果年輕樹木把能量用於生長，就可能產生較少化學防禦。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a trade-off in resource use.","zh":"這個片語顯示資源使用上的取捨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"produce lower levels of toxin","meaning":"產生較低水平的毒素","examples":[{"en":"Younger trees produce lower levels of toxin.","zh":"較年輕的樹木產生較低水平的毒素。"},{"en":"Produce lower levels of toxin means make smaller amounts of poisonous chemicals.","zh":"produce lower levels of toxin 指製造較少量的有毒化學物。"},{"en":"Some vegetables produce lower levels of bitter chemicals when they grow quickly.","zh":"有些蔬菜快速生長時，可能產生較低水平的苦味化學物。"},{"en":"If young leaves contain fewer toxins, leaf-eating animals may prefer them.","zh":"如果嫩葉含毒素較少，食葉動物可能較喜歡它們。"},{"en":"The phrase compares chemical defence levels.","zh":"這個片語比較化學防禦水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"well-established old-growth trees","meaning":"生長穩固的老林樹木","examples":[{"en":"Well-established old-growth trees invest more energy in chemical defence.","zh":"生長穩固的老林樹木把更多能量投放於化學防禦。"},{"en":"Well-established old-growth trees are mature trees that have grown for a long time in stable forest.","zh":"well-established old-growth trees 指在穩定森林中生長很久的成熟樹木。"},{"en":"A well-established old tree may have deep roots and a large crown.","zh":"生長穩固的老樹可能有深根和巨大樹冠。"},{"en":"If older trees grow slowly, they may protect themselves by producing stronger toxins.","zh":"如果老樹生長緩慢，可能透過產生更強毒素來保護自己。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mature, stable forest trees.","zh":"這個片語描述成熟而穩定的森林樹木。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the value of maturing forests","meaning":"逐漸成熟的森林的價值","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are studying the value of maturing forests to primates.","zh":"研究人員正在研究逐漸成熟的森林對靈長類動物的價值。"},{"en":"The value of maturing forests means the importance of forests that are gradually becoming older and more developed.","zh":"the value of maturing forests 指逐漸變老和更發展成熟的森林的重要性。"},{"en":"A city may study the value of maturing trees because older trees give more shade.","zh":"城市可能研究逐漸成熟樹木的價值，因為較老樹木提供更多樹蔭。"},{"en":"If maturing forests provide food and movement routes, they become valuable to monkeys.","zh":"如果逐漸成熟的森林提供食物和移動路線，它們對猴子就變得有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase asks why recovering forests matter.","zh":"這個片語詢問恢復中的森林為何重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a subject of study","meaning":"研究課題","examples":[{"en":"Forest recovery is a subject of study at Santa Rosa National Park.","zh":"森林恢復是 Santa Rosa 國家公園的一個研究課題。"},{"en":"A subject of study is a topic that researchers examine carefully.","zh":"a subject of study 指研究人員仔細檢視的主題。"},{"en":"Student stress has become a subject of study in many schools.","zh":"學生壓力已成為許多學校的研究課題。"},{"en":"If forest recovery is studied, scientists can learn which animals return first and why.","zh":"如果森林恢復受到研究，科學家可以了解哪些動物最先回來以及原因。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a research topic.","zh":"這個片語指出研究主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at one time","meaning":"曾經；一度","examples":[{"en":"Large areas of the park had at one time been burnt.","zh":"公園大片地區曾經被焚燒。"},{"en":"At one time means in the past, during an earlier period.","zh":"at one time 指在過去某一時期。"},{"en":"At one time, many students used paper dictionaries instead of phone apps.","zh":"曾經許多學生使用紙本字典，而不是手機應用程式。"},{"en":"If land was burnt at one time but is now forested, the area has changed greatly.","zh":"如果土地曾經被焚燒，但現在已有森林，該地區已大大改變。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a former situation.","zh":"這個片語指過去的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be burnt to make space for","meaning":"被焚燒以騰出空間作……","examples":[{"en":"Forests were burnt to make space for ranching and farming.","zh":"森林被焚燒以騰出空間作牧場和農業。"},{"en":"Be burnt to make space for means be destroyed by fire so land can be used for another purpose.","zh":"be burnt to make space for 指被火燒毀，以便土地用於另一目的。"},{"en":"Grassland may be burnt to make space for new buildings, though this can damage wildlife.","zh":"草地可能被焚燒以騰出空間興建新建築，雖然這會傷害野生動物。"},{"en":"If forests are burnt for agriculture, habitat loss can happen very quickly.","zh":"如果森林被焚燒作農業用途，棲息地流失可能非常迅速。"},{"en":"The phrase describes destructive land conversion.","zh":"這個片語描述破壞性的土地轉換。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cattle ranching","meaning":"牧牛業","examples":[{"en":"Large areas were converted for cattle ranching.","zh":"大片地區被改造成牧牛業用地。"},{"en":"Cattle ranching means raising cattle on large areas of land.","zh":"cattle ranching 指在大片土地上飼養牛隻。"},{"en":"Cattle ranching may require grassland, fences, water sources, and workers.","zh":"牧牛業可能需要草地、圍欄、水源和工人。"},{"en":"If cattle ranching expands into forest, trees may be removed for pasture.","zh":"如果牧牛業擴展到森林，樹木可能被移除作牧草地。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a large-scale livestock activity.","zh":"這個片語指大型畜牧活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"coffee farming","meaning":"咖啡種植業","examples":[{"en":"Some forest was destroyed for coffee farming.","zh":"一些森林因咖啡種植業而被破壞。"},{"en":"Coffee farming is the growing of coffee plants for harvest and sale.","zh":"coffee farming 指種植咖啡樹以收成和出售。"},{"en":"Coffee farming may provide income for rural families in mountainous regions.","zh":"咖啡種植業可能為山區農村家庭提供收入。"},{"en":"If coffee farming expands without planning, forests may be cleared for plantations.","zh":"如果咖啡種植業在沒有規劃下擴張，森林可能被清理作種植園。"},{"en":"The phrase names an agricultural activity based on coffee crops.","zh":"這個片語指出以咖啡作物為基礎的農業活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"thereby devastating","meaning":"因而嚴重破壞","examples":[{"en":"The burning destroyed trees, thereby devastating monkey habitat.","zh":"焚燒摧毀樹木，因而嚴重破壞猴子棲息地。"},{"en":"Thereby devastating means causing severe damage as a result of the previous action.","zh":"thereby devastating 指因前一個行動而造成嚴重破壞。"},{"en":"A factory may pollute a river, thereby devastating fish populations downstream.","zh":"工廠可能污染河流，因而嚴重破壞下游魚類種群。"},{"en":"If trees are destroyed, monkeys lose food and shelter, so their habitat is devastated.","zh":"如果樹木被摧毀，猴子失去食物和庇護，其棲息地就被嚴重破壞。"},{"en":"The phrase links an action with a serious consequence.","zh":"這個片語把行動與嚴重後果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"local monkey habitat","meaning":"本地猴子棲息地","examples":[{"en":"Forest clearance devastated local monkey habitat.","zh":"森林清理嚴重破壞了本地猴子棲息地。"},{"en":"Local monkey habitat means the nearby natural area where monkeys live, feed, rest, and move.","zh":"local monkey habitat 指附近猴子生活、覓食、休息和移動的自然區域。"},{"en":"A forest strip beside a farm can be local monkey habitat if monkeys use it daily.","zh":"如果猴子每天使用農場旁的森林帶，它就可以是本地猴子棲息地。"},{"en":"If habitat is cleared, monkeys may have fewer trees for food and travel.","zh":"如果棲息地被清除，猴子用作食物和移動的樹木就會減少。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a place with the needs of local monkeys.","zh":"這個片語把地方與本地猴子的需要連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"protect the area by designating it","meaning":"透過把……指定為……加以保護","examples":[{"en":"The government protected the area by designating it a national park.","zh":"政府透過把該地區指定為國家公園加以保護。"},{"en":"Protect the area by designating it means officially give land a protected status.","zh":"protect the area by designating it 指正式給予土地受保護地位。"},{"en":"A council may protect a wetland by designating it a conservation zone.","zh":"市議會可能透過把濕地指定為保育區加以保護。"},{"en":"If an area becomes a national park, harmful activities may be restricted.","zh":"如果某地區成為國家公園，有害活動可能受到限制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes legal protection through official naming.","zh":"這個片語描述透過官方命名進行法律保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"designate something a national park","meaning":"把……指定為國家公園","examples":[{"en":"The government designated Santa Rosa a national park.","zh":"政府把 Santa Rosa 指定為國家公園。"},{"en":"Designate something a national park means officially declare it a protected park of national importance.","zh":"designate something a national park 指正式宣布某地為具有國家重要性的受保護公園。"},{"en":"A country may designate a mountain area a national park to protect rare animals.","zh":"國家可能把山區指定為國家公園，以保護稀有動物。"},{"en":"If land is designated a national park, farming, hunting, and building may be controlled.","zh":"如果土地被指定為國家公園，耕作、狩獵和建築可能受管制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an official conservation decision.","zh":"這個片語描述官方保育決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"indigenous trees","meaning":"本土樹木","examples":[{"en":"Indigenous trees began to return after the land was protected.","zh":"土地受到保護後，本土樹木開始回歸。"},{"en":"Indigenous trees are tree species that naturally belong to a region.","zh":"indigenous trees 指自然屬於某地區的樹種。"},{"en":"A city may plant indigenous trees because they suit local soil and climate.","zh":"城市可能種植本土樹木，因為它們適合本地土壤和氣候。"},{"en":"If indigenous trees return, native insects, birds, and monkeys may also benefit.","zh":"如果本土樹木回歸，本地昆蟲、鳥類和猴子也可能受惠。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts native species with imported ones.","zh":"這個片語把本地物種與外來物種作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be absent for decades","meaning":"消失了數十年","examples":[{"en":"Some native tree species had been absent for decades.","zh":"一些本土樹種已消失了數十年。"},{"en":"Be absent for decades means not be present for many tens of years.","zh":"be absent for decades 指在許多個十年間沒有出現。"},{"en":"A traditional festival may be absent for decades before local people revive it.","zh":"傳統節日可能消失數十年後被本地人復興。"},{"en":"If a tree species has been absent for decades, its return shows strong ecological recovery.","zh":"如果某樹種消失了數十年，其回歸顯示強烈生態恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a long disappearance.","zh":"這個片語強調長期消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"invade abandoned pastures","meaning":"進佔被棄置的牧草地","examples":[{"en":"Native trees began to invade the abandoned pastures.","zh":"本土樹木開始進佔被棄置的牧草地。"},{"en":"Invade abandoned pastures means spread naturally into unused grazing fields.","zh":"invade abandoned pastures 指自然擴散到不再使用的放牧草地。"},{"en":"Weeds may invade an abandoned garden when nobody cuts or clears it.","zh":"如果沒有人修剪或清理，雜草可能進佔被棄置的花園。"},{"en":"If trees invade pasture, open grassland can gradually become young forest.","zh":"如果樹木進佔牧草地，開闊草地可以逐漸變成年輕森林。"},{"en":"The phrase describes plants moving into unused land.","zh":"這個片語描述植物進入未使用土地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"abandoned pastures","meaning":"被棄置的牧草地","examples":[{"en":"Indigenous trees regenerated across abandoned pastures.","zh":"本土樹木在被棄置的牧草地上再生。"},{"en":"Abandoned pastures are grazing lands no longer used for livestock.","zh":"abandoned pastures 指不再用於牲畜放牧的草地。"},{"en":"An abandoned pasture may first grow weeds, then shrubs, and later young trees.","zh":"被棄置的牧草地可能先長雜草，再長灌木，之後長出年輕樹木。"},{"en":"If pastures are abandoned, nature may slowly reclaim the land.","zh":"如果牧草地被棄置，大自然可能慢慢重新佔據土地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes former farmland left unused.","zh":"這個片語描述被閒置的舊農地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reborn forests","meaning":"重生的森林","examples":[{"en":"Capuchins were the first monkeys to use the reborn forests.","zh":"卷尾猴是最先使用重生森林的猴子。"},{"en":"Reborn forests are forests that have grown back after being destroyed or cleared.","zh":"reborn forests 指被摧毀或清除後重新長回來的森林。"},{"en":"A burned hillside may become a reborn forest after years of protection and rainfall.","zh":"被燒過的山坡在多年保護和雨水後，可能變成重生森林。"},{"en":"If reborn forests provide food, animals may return step by step.","zh":"如果重生森林提供食物，動物可能一步步回來。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests ecological renewal.","zh":"這個片語暗示生態更新。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be followed by","meaning":"隨後有……","examples":[{"en":"The capuchins were followed by howler monkeys.","zh":"卷尾猴之後，隨後有吼猴回來。"},{"en":"Be followed by means happen or arrive after something else.","zh":"be followed by 指某事之後發生或到來另一事。"},{"en":"A school announcement may be followed by questions from students.","zh":"學校公告之後，可能隨後有學生提問。"},{"en":"If one species returns first and another follows later, recovery is happening in stages.","zh":"如果一個物種先回來，另一個物種之後跟隨，恢復就是分階段發生。"},{"en":"The phrase shows sequence.","zh":"這個片語顯示次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"continuous forest","meaning":"連綿不斷的森林","examples":[{"en":"Spider monkeys need large areas of continuous forest.","zh":"蜘蛛猴需要大片連綿不斷的森林。"},{"en":"Continuous forest is forest that remains connected without large gaps of roads, farms, or open land.","zh":"continuous forest 指沒有道路、農田或開闊地大片切斷而保持相連的森林。"},{"en":"Some birds need continuous forest because they avoid crossing open fields.","zh":"有些鳥類需要連綿不斷的森林，因為牠們避免穿越開闊田地。"},{"en":"If forest is broken into patches, animals needing continuous forest may decline.","zh":"如果森林被切割成小片，需要連續森林的動物可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses connected habitat.","zh":"這個片語強調相連的棲息地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"following protection of","meaning":"在……受到保護後","examples":[{"en":"Monkey populations increased following protection of the area.","zh":"在該地區受到保護後，猴子種群增加。"},{"en":"Following protection of means after an area has been protected.","zh":"following protection of 指在某地區受到保護之後。"},{"en":"Bird numbers may rise following protection of a wetland from development.","zh":"在濕地受到保護免受發展後，鳥類數量可能上升。"},{"en":"If hunting and clearing stop after protection, animal populations may recover.","zh":"如果保護後狩獵和清理停止，動物種群可能恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase connects conservation action with later results.","zh":"這個片語把保育行動與後來結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"population doubled","meaning":"種群數量增加一倍","examples":[{"en":"The capuchin population doubled within 28 years.","zh":"卷尾猴種群在28年內增加一倍。"},{"en":"Population doubled means the number of individuals became twice as large.","zh":"population doubled 指個體數量變成原來的兩倍。"},{"en":"A school’s student population doubled after a new housing estate opened nearby.","zh":"新屋苑在附近落成後，學校學生人數增加一倍。"},{"en":"If a monkey population doubles, survival and reproduction have improved.","zh":"如果猴子種群增加一倍，生存和繁殖情況已改善。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a clear measure of growth.","zh":"這個片語給出清楚的增長量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"increase sevenfold","meaning":"增加至七倍","examples":[{"en":"The number of howlers increased sevenfold.","zh":"吼猴數量增加至七倍。"},{"en":"Increase sevenfold means become seven times larger than before.","zh":"increase sevenfold 指變成原來的七倍。"},{"en":"A small club’s membership may increase sevenfold if a famous teacher promotes it.","zh":"如果著名老師宣傳，小型學會會員人數可能增加至七倍。"},{"en":"If a population increases sevenfold, the growth is much stronger than simply doubling.","zh":"如果種群增加至七倍，增長就遠大於只是翻倍。"},{"en":"The phrase describes very large multiplication.","zh":"這個片語描述非常大的倍數增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the same traits that","meaning":"同樣令……的特徵","examples":[{"en":"The same traits that help howlers survive also explain their rapid population growth.","zh":"同樣令吼猴生存下來的特徵，也解釋了牠們快速的種群增長。"},{"en":"The same traits that means the very same characteristics which cause one result also cause another.","zh":"the same traits that 指造成一個結果的同一批特徵，也造成另一結果。"},{"en":"The same habits that help a student revise early also reduce exam stress.","zh":"同樣幫助學生提早溫習的習慣，也能減少考試壓力。"},{"en":"If flexible feeding helps survival, it may also help reproduction and population growth.","zh":"如果靈活覓食有助生存，也可能有助繁殖和種群增長。"},{"en":"The phrase links one set of qualities to multiple effects.","zh":"這個片語把同一組特質與多個效果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"explain a population boom","meaning":"解釋種群激增","examples":[{"en":"Flexible feeding habits help explain the howlers’ population boom.","zh":"靈活的覓食習慣有助解釋吼猴的種群激增。"},{"en":"Explain a population boom means give the reason why a population grows very quickly.","zh":"explain a population boom 指給出種群快速增長的原因。"},{"en":"Cheaper housing may help explain a population boom in a small town.","zh":"較便宜住屋可能有助解釋小鎮人口激增。"},{"en":"If animals reproduce early and find food easily, their numbers may rise rapidly.","zh":"如果動物早熟繁殖並容易找到食物，數量可能迅速上升。"},{"en":"The phrase connects causes with sudden population growth.","zh":"這個片語把原因與突然的種群增長連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reproduction is faster than","meaning":"繁殖速度比……快","examples":[{"en":"Howler reproduction is faster than that of other local monkeys.","zh":"吼猴的繁殖速度比其他本地猴類快。"},{"en":"Reproduction is faster than means babies are produced earlier or more often than in another group.","zh":"reproduction is faster than 指比另一群體更早或更頻密地產生後代。"},{"en":"Some insects’ reproduction is faster than that of mammals because they lay many eggs quickly.","zh":"有些昆蟲的繁殖速度比哺乳類動物快，因為牠們很快產下許多卵。"},{"en":"If howlers reproduce faster, their population can recover more quickly after protection.","zh":"如果吼猴繁殖較快，在受到保護後其種群能更快恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase compares reproductive speed.","zh":"這個片語比較繁殖速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"native monkey species","meaning":"本土猴類物種","examples":[{"en":"Howlers reproduce faster than other native monkey species.","zh":"吼猴比其他本土猴類物種繁殖得更快。"},{"en":"Native monkey species are monkey species that naturally live in a particular region.","zh":"native monkey species 指自然生活在某地區的猴類物種。"},{"en":"A forest reserve may protect several native monkey species at the same time.","zh":"森林保護區可能同時保護幾種本土猴類物種。"},{"en":"If one native species adapts better than others, its population may recover faster.","zh":"如果某一種本土物種比其他物種更能適應，其種群可能更快恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to local monkey types, not animals introduced by people.","zh":"這個片語指本地猴類，而不是人類引入的動物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"give birth for the first time","meaning":"首次生育","examples":[{"en":"Howlers give birth for the first time at about three and a half years old.","zh":"吼猴約三歲半時首次生育。"},{"en":"Give birth for the first time means produce a baby for the first time in life.","zh":"give birth for the first time 指一生中第一次產下幼兒或幼崽。"},{"en":"A female animal that gives birth for the first time may need protection and food.","zh":"首次生育的雌性動物可能需要保護和食物。"},{"en":"If howlers first reproduce at a young age, their population can grow faster.","zh":"如果吼猴較年輕時首次繁殖，其種群可以增長得更快。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the beginning of reproduction.","zh":"這個片語標示繁殖的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Howlers reproduce earlier compared with capuchins and spider monkeys.","zh":"與卷尾猴和蜘蛛猴相比，吼猴較早繁殖。"},{"en":"Compared with means when measured or judged against something else.","zh":"compared with 指與另一事物衡量或判斷時。"},{"en":"Compared with walking, cycling can save time on a short trip.","zh":"與步行相比，短途踩單車可以節省時間。"},{"en":"If one species reproduces earlier compared with another, it may recover faster after disturbance.","zh":"如果某物種與另一物種相比繁殖較早，就可能在受干擾後更快恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces comparison.","zh":"這個片語引入比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"eight or more","meaning":"八歲或以上","examples":[{"en":"Spider monkeys may not reproduce until they are eight or more years old.","zh":"蜘蛛猴可能直到八歲或以上才繁殖。"},{"en":"Eight or more means at least eight, and possibly a higher number.","zh":"eight or more 指至少八，並可能更多。"},{"en":"A child may need eight or more hours of sleep to feel rested.","zh":"孩子可能需要八小時或以上睡眠才感到休息足夠。"},{"en":"If an animal waits eight or more years before reproducing, population recovery is slow.","zh":"如果動物要等八年或以上才繁殖，種群恢復就很慢。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a minimum number.","zh":"這個片語給出最低數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"once every four years","meaning":"每四年一次","examples":[{"en":"A female spider monkey may have a baby once every four years.","zh":"雌性蜘蛛猴可能每四年產下一隻幼猴。"},{"en":"Once every four years means one time in each four-year period.","zh":"once every four years 指每四年期間一次。"},{"en":"Some international sports events happen once every four years.","zh":"有些國際體育賽事每四年舉行一次。"},{"en":"If a monkey gives birth only once every four years, its population grows slowly.","zh":"如果猴子每四年才生育一次，其種群增長就很慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a low frequency.","zh":"這個片語描述低頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"well-fed howlers","meaning":"營養充足的吼猴","examples":[{"en":"Well-fed howlers can reproduce relatively frequently.","zh":"營養充足的吼猴可以相對頻繁地繁殖。"},{"en":"Well-fed howlers are howler monkeys that have enough nutritious food.","zh":"well-fed howlers 指有足夠營養食物的吼猴。"},{"en":"Well-fed children usually have more energy for school and play.","zh":"營養充足的孩子通常有更多精力上學和玩耍。"},{"en":"If howlers are well-fed, females may be healthy enough to produce infants more often.","zh":"如果吼猴營養充足，雌猴可能健康到能更頻繁地產下幼猴。"},{"en":"The phrase links good nutrition with biological success.","zh":"這個片語把良好營養與生物成功連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"produce an infant","meaning":"誕下一隻幼猴","examples":[{"en":"A healthy female howler can produce an infant every two years.","zh":"健康的雌性吼猴可以每兩年誕下一隻幼猴。"},{"en":"Produce an infant means give birth to a baby animal.","zh":"produce an infant 指生下一隻幼年動物。"},{"en":"A zoo may record when a female primate produces an infant to monitor the population.","zh":"動物園可能記錄雌性靈長類何時誕下幼崽，以監察種群。"},{"en":"If females produce infants regularly, the population can increase quickly.","zh":"如果雌性定期誕下幼崽，種群就能迅速增加。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and biological.","zh":"這個片語較正式，屬生物學用語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"adaptable feeders","meaning":"適應力強的覓食動物","examples":[{"en":"Howlers are adaptable feeders that can survive on different plants.","zh":"吼猴是適應力強的覓食動物，能靠不同植物生存。"},{"en":"Adaptable feeders are animals able to eat several types of food depending on what is available.","zh":"adaptable feeders 指能根據可取得食物而吃幾種食物的動物。"},{"en":"Urban birds are adaptable feeders when they eat seeds, insects, and human leftovers.","zh":"城市鳥類吃種子、昆蟲和人類剩食時，就是適應力強的覓食動物。"},{"en":"If animals are adaptable feeders, they are less vulnerable when one food source disappears.","zh":"如果動物是適應力強的覓食者，當某一食物來源消失時就較不脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes feeding flexibility.","zh":"這個片語描述覓食上的靈活性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"comparatively small home range","meaning":"相對細小的活動範圍","examples":[{"en":"Howlers need only a comparatively small home range.","zh":"吼猴只需要相對細小的活動範圍。"},{"en":"A comparatively small home range is a relatively limited area where an animal lives and searches for food.","zh":"comparatively small home range 指動物生活和覓食的相對有限區域。"},{"en":"A cat in a quiet neighbourhood may have a comparatively small home range if food is nearby.","zh":"如果附近有食物，安靜社區中的貓可能有相對細小的活動範圍。"},{"en":"If howlers need little space, more groups can survive in fragmented landscapes.","zh":"如果吼猴需要的空間很少，更多群體就能在破碎景觀中生存。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the space needs of one animal with another.","zh":"這個片語比較一種動物與另一種動物的空間需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"Spider monkeys, on the other hand, require much more space.","zh":"另一方面，蜘蛛猴需要更多空間。"},{"en":"On the other hand introduces a contrasting point.","zh":"on the other hand 引出相反或對比的觀點。"},{"en":"Online lessons are convenient; on the other hand, some students miss face-to-face support.","zh":"網上課堂很方便；另一方面，有些學生想念面對面支援。"},{"en":"If howlers need little space but spider monkeys need much more, their survival chances differ.","zh":"如果吼猴需要少量空間而蜘蛛猴需要更多空間，牠們的生存機會就不同。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show contrast between two ideas.","zh":"這個片語幫助顯示兩個想法之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"occupy a huge home range","meaning":"佔用很大的活動範圍","examples":[{"en":"Spider monkeys occupy a huge home range.","zh":"蜘蛛猴佔用很大的活動範圍。"},{"en":"Occupy a huge home range means live and travel across a very large area.","zh":"occupy a huge home range 指在非常大的區域內生活和移動。"},{"en":"A large predator may occupy a huge home range because it needs many hunting grounds.","zh":"大型捕食者可能佔用很大的活動範圍，因為牠需要許多狩獵地。"},{"en":"If an animal occupies a huge home range, roads and farms can easily interrupt its movement.","zh":"如果動物佔用很大活動範圍，道路和農田就很容易打斷其移動。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses large space requirements.","zh":"這個片語強調大型空間需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"also crucial is the fact that","meaning":"同樣關鍵的是……這個事實","examples":[{"en":"Also crucial is the fact that howler food contains water.","zh":"同樣關鍵的是吼猴食物含有水分這個事實。"},{"en":"Also crucial is the fact that means another very important point is that.","zh":"also crucial is the fact that 指另一個非常重要的點是。"},{"en":"Also crucial is the fact that students need sleep, not only study time, before exams.","zh":"同樣關鍵的是，考試前學生需要睡眠，而不只是溫習時間。"},{"en":"If leaves contain water, howlers can survive where open water is scarce.","zh":"如果樹葉含有水分，吼猴就能在露天水源稀少的地方生存。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an additional key reason.","zh":"這個片語引出另一個關鍵原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hold plenty of water","meaning":"含有大量水分","examples":[{"en":"The leaves eaten by howlers hold plenty of water.","zh":"吼猴吃的樹葉含有大量水分。"},{"en":"Hold plenty of water means contain a large amount of water.","zh":"hold plenty of water 指含有大量水。"},{"en":"Cucumbers hold plenty of water, which is why they taste fresh and juicy.","zh":"青瓜含有大量水分，所以吃起來清爽多汁。"},{"en":"If leaves hold water, animals eating them may not need to drink as often.","zh":"如果葉子含水，吃葉子的動物可能不需要經常喝水。"},{"en":"The phrase describes water content.","zh":"這個片語描述含水量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"survive away from","meaning":"遠離……仍能生存","examples":[{"en":"Howlers can survive away from streams and water holes.","zh":"吼猴能遠離溪流和水坑仍然生存。"},{"en":"Survive away from means continue living without being close to something usually needed.","zh":"survive away from 指不靠近通常需要的某物也能繼續生活。"},{"en":"Some plants can survive away from rivers because their roots reach deep underground water.","zh":"有些植物能遠離河流生存，因為其根部可到達地下深層水源。"},{"en":"If monkeys get water from leaves, they can live farther from open water sources.","zh":"如果猴子從葉子取得水分，就能住得離露天水源更遠。"},{"en":"The phrase shows independence from a usual resource.","zh":"這個片語顯示對通常資源的獨立性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"open streams and water holes","meaning":"露天溪流和水坑","examples":[{"en":"Some monkey species depend on open streams and water holes.","zh":"有些猴類物種依賴露天溪流和水坑。"},{"en":"Open streams and water holes are visible natural water sources where animals can drink.","zh":"open streams and water holes 指動物可飲用的可見天然水源。"},{"en":"During drought, wild animals may gather around open streams and water holes.","zh":"乾旱期間，野生動物可能聚集在露天溪流和水坑附近。"},{"en":"If these water sources dry up, species that depend on them may suffer.","zh":"如果這些水源乾涸，依賴它們的物種可能受苦。"},{"en":"The phrase describes accessible outdoor water sources.","zh":"這個片語描述可接觸的戶外水源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"give someone an advantage over","meaning":"令某人比……有優勢","examples":[{"en":"This ability gives howlers an advantage over other monkeys.","zh":"這種能力令吼猴比其他猴子有優勢。"},{"en":"Give someone an advantage over means make someone better able to succeed than another person or group.","zh":"give someone an advantage over 指令某人比另一人或群體更有能力成功。"},{"en":"Good English skills can give a student an advantage over others in an interview.","zh":"良好英語能力可以令學生在面試中比其他人有優勢。"},{"en":"If howlers need less open water, drought affects them less than other monkeys.","zh":"如果吼猴較少需要露天水源，乾旱對牠們的影響就比其他猴子少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a comparative benefit.","zh":"這個片語描述比較上的好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"suffer during","meaning":"在……期間受影響","examples":[{"en":"Other monkey species have suffered during the drought.","zh":"其他猴類物種在乾旱期間受到影響。"},{"en":"Suffer during means experience harm, difficulty, or loss in a particular period.","zh":"suffer during 指在某段時期經歷傷害、困難或損失。"},{"en":"Small shops may suffer during roadworks because customers cannot reach them easily.","zh":"道路工程期間，小店可能受影響，因為顧客不容易到達。"},{"en":"If drought reduces fruit and water, animals that depend on them may suffer.","zh":"如果乾旱減少水果和水源，依賴它們的動物可能受苦。"},{"en":"The phrase connects hardship with a time or event.","zh":"這個片語把困難與某段時間或事件連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"long, ongoing drought","meaning":"長期持續的乾旱","examples":[{"en":"The region has experienced a long, ongoing drought.","zh":"該地區經歷了長期持續的乾旱。"},{"en":"A long, ongoing drought is a dry period that lasts for a long time and has not ended yet.","zh":"long, ongoing drought 指持續很久而且尚未結束的乾旱期。"},{"en":"Farmers may lose crops during a long, ongoing drought because soil stays dry for months.","zh":"在長期持續的乾旱期間，農民可能因泥土數月乾燥而失去作物。"},{"en":"If drought continues, animals may struggle to find water and fresh leaves.","zh":"如果乾旱持續，動物可能難以找到水和新鮮葉子。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both duration and continuation.","zh":"這個片語同時強調時間長和仍在持續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ecologist","meaning":"生態學家","examples":[{"en":"Alejandro Estrada is an ecologist working in Mexico.","zh":"Alejandro Estrada 是一位在墨西哥工作的生態學家。"},{"en":"An ecologist is a scientist who studies relationships between living things and their environment.","zh":"ecologist 指研究生物與環境之間關係的科學家。"},{"en":"An ecologist may study how pollution affects fish in a river.","zh":"生態學家可能研究污染如何影響河流中的魚。"},{"en":"If an ecologist studies monkeys on farms, they examine how animals and human land use interact.","zh":"如果生態學家研究農場上的猴子，他們會檢視動物和人類土地使用如何互動。"},{"en":"The word names a specialist in ecosystems.","zh":"這個詞指生態系統專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"study the ecology of","meaning":"研究……的生態","examples":[{"en":"Estrada has been studying the ecology of plantation-dwelling howlers.","zh":"Estrada 一直研究生活在種植園中的吼猴的生態。"},{"en":"Study the ecology of means examine how living things interact with food, habitat, climate, and other species.","zh":"study the ecology of 指檢視生物如何與食物、棲息地、氣候和其他物種互動。"},{"en":"Scientists may study the ecology of bees by observing flowers, weather, and nesting sites.","zh":"科學家可能透過觀察花朵、天氣和築巢地點來研究蜜蜂的生態。"},{"en":"If researchers study plantation howlers, they learn how monkeys survive in human-altered land.","zh":"如果研究人員研究種植園吼猴，就能了解猴子如何在人類改造土地中生存。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on organisms in their environment.","zh":"這個片語集中於生物與其環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"thrive in a habitat","meaning":"在某棲息地繁衍生息","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys thrive in a habitat altered by humans.","zh":"這些猴子在人類改造過的棲息地繁衍生息。"},{"en":"Thrive in a habitat means live, feed, reproduce, and do well in that environment.","zh":"thrive in a habitat 指在該環境中生活、覓食、繁殖並發展良好。"},{"en":"Some birds thrive in city habitats because buildings provide nesting places.","zh":"有些鳥類在城市棲息地繁衍生息，因為建築物提供築巢位置。"},{"en":"If animals thrive in altered habitats, they may be more adaptable than expected.","zh":"如果動物在被改造棲息地繁衍生息，牠們可能比預期更適應。"},{"en":"The phrase means successful living, not just survival.","zh":"這個片語指成功生活，而不只是生存。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be totally altered by humans","meaning":"被人類徹底改變","examples":[{"en":"The cacao plantation has been totally altered by humans.","zh":"這個可可種植園已被人類徹底改變。"},{"en":"Be totally altered by humans means be completely changed by human activity.","zh":"be totally altered by humans 指被人類活動完全改變。"},{"en":"A river may be totally altered by humans if it is straightened, dammed, and polluted.","zh":"如果河流被拉直、築壩和污染，就可能被人類徹底改變。"},{"en":"If a habitat is totally altered but still supports wildlife, conservation opportunities may remain.","zh":"如果棲息地被徹底改變但仍支持野生動物，保育機會可能仍存在。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses complete human transformation.","zh":"這個片語強調完整的人類改造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cacao plantation","meaning":"可可種植園","examples":[{"en":"The howlers live successfully in a cacao plantation.","zh":"吼猴成功生活在可可種植園中。"},{"en":"A cacao plantation is a farm where cacao trees are grown for cocoa beans.","zh":"cacao plantation 指種植可可樹以取得可可豆的農場。"},{"en":"Workers on a cacao plantation may harvest pods that are later used to make chocolate.","zh":"可可種植園的工人可能收割日後用來製作朱古力的豆莢。"},{"en":"If shade trees grow above cacao, monkeys may find leaves and fruit there.","zh":"如果遮蔭樹在可可上方生長，猴子可能在那裡找到葉子和果實。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an agricultural habitat.","zh":"這個片語描述農業棲息地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"need shade to grow","meaning":"需要遮蔭才能生長","examples":[{"en":"Cacao plants need shade to grow well.","zh":"可可植物需要遮蔭才能良好生長。"},{"en":"Need shade to grow means require protection from direct sunlight in order to develop properly.","zh":"need shade to grow 指需要避免直接陽光照射，才能正常發展。"},{"en":"Some houseplants need shade to grow because strong sun burns their leaves.","zh":"有些室內植物需要遮蔭才能生長，因為強烈陽光會灼傷葉子。"},{"en":"If cacao needs shade, farmers may keep tall trees above the crop.","zh":"如果可可需要遮蔭，農民可能在作物上方保留高樹。"},{"en":"The phrase links plant growth with light conditions.","zh":"這個片語把植物生長與光照條件連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"form a protective canopy over","meaning":"在……上方形成保護性樹冠","examples":[{"en":"Tall trees form a protective canopy over the cacao crop.","zh":"高樹在可可作物上方形成保護性樹冠。"},{"en":"Form a protective canopy over means create a layer of branches and leaves above something to shelter it.","zh":"form a protective canopy over 指在某物上方形成枝葉層以提供庇護。"},{"en":"Trees along a street can form a protective canopy over pedestrians on hot days.","zh":"街道兩旁的樹木可以在炎熱日子為行人形成保護性樹冠。"},{"en":"If shade trees cover cacao, they protect the crop from too much sun and heat.","zh":"如果遮蔭樹覆蓋可可，就能保護作物免受過多陽光和熱力影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes natural overhead protection.","zh":"這個片語描述天然的上方保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"move in","meaning":"遷入","examples":[{"en":"The howlers moved in after nearby forests were cut.","zh":"附近森林被砍伐後，吼猴遷入。"},{"en":"Move in means begin living in a new place.","zh":"move in 指開始在新地方生活。"},{"en":"A family may move in after a flat has been repaired and cleaned.","zh":"單位維修和清潔後，一個家庭可能遷入。"},{"en":"If forests are cut, animals may move into plantations that still contain trees.","zh":"如果森林被砍伐，動物可能遷入仍有樹木的種植園。"},{"en":"The phrase describes relocation into a place.","zh":"這個片語描述遷到某地居住。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"nearby forests were cut","meaning":"附近森林被砍伐","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys arrived after nearby forests were cut down.","zh":"附近森林被砍伐後，猴子來到了這裡。"},{"en":"Nearby forests were cut means forests close to the area were removed by people.","zh":"nearby forests were cut 指靠近該地區的森林被人類移除。"},{"en":"If nearby trees are cut for construction, birds may move into gardens and parks.","zh":"如果附近樹木因建設被砍伐，鳥類可能遷入花園和公園。"},{"en":"When forests are cut, animals lose habitat and may search for new places to live.","zh":"當森林被砍伐，動物失去棲息地，可能尋找新生活地點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes local deforestation.","zh":"這個片語描述本地森林砍伐。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"strange habitat","meaning":"特殊的棲息地","examples":[{"en":"The mixed plantation provides a strange but productive habitat.","zh":"這種混合種植園提供了一個特殊但有生產力的棲息地。"},{"en":"A strange habitat is an unusual living environment that may not look natural at first.","zh":"strange habitat 指一種不尋常、起初可能看起來不自然的生活環境。"},{"en":"City rooftops can be a strange habitat for plants, birds, and insects.","zh":"城市天台可以是植物、鳥類和昆蟲的特殊棲息地。"},{"en":"If a plantation still has shade trees, it may support wildlife despite being artificial.","zh":"如果種植園仍有遮蔭樹，即使它是人工環境，也可能支持野生動物。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests an unexpected place where life can succeed.","zh":"這個片語暗示生命能成功生存的意想不到地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"support about as many...as...","meaning":"容納的……數量約與……相同","examples":[{"en":"The plantation supports about as many monkeys as a wild forest of the same size.","zh":"這個種植園容納的猴子數量約與同等大小的野生森林相同。"},{"en":"Support about as many A as B means provide enough resources for roughly the same number as another place.","zh":"support about as many A as B 指提供資源，讓數量大約與另一地方相同。"},{"en":"A small online class may support about as many students as a physical classroom if the system works well.","zh":"如果系統運作良好，小型網上課堂可容納的學生數量約與實體課室相同。"},{"en":"If a plantation supports as many monkeys as forest, it has surprising habitat value.","zh":"如果種植園容納的猴子數量與森林相同，它就有令人意外的棲息地價值。"},{"en":"The phrase compares capacity.","zh":"這個片語比較承載能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"same-sized patch of wild forest","meaning":"同等大小的一片野生森林","examples":[{"en":"The plantation supports as many monkeys as a same-sized patch of wild forest.","zh":"這個種植園容納的猴子數量與同等大小的一片野生森林一樣多。"},{"en":"A same-sized patch of wild forest is an area of natural forest equal in size to another area being compared.","zh":"same-sized patch of wild forest 指與被比較地區面積相同的一片天然森林。"},{"en":"Scientists may compare a farm with a same-sized patch of forest to test wildlife value.","zh":"科學家可能把農場與同等大小的一片森林比較，以測試野生動物價值。"},{"en":"If two habitats are the same size, differences in animal numbers may reflect habitat quality.","zh":"如果兩個棲息地面積相同，動物數量差異可能反映棲息地質素。"},{"en":"The phrase controls comparison by keeping area equal.","zh":"這個片語透過保持面積相同來控制比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"shade trees","meaning":"遮蔭樹","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys eat leaves and fruit from the shade trees.","zh":"猴子吃遮蔭樹上的葉子和水果。"},{"en":"Shade trees are trees grown or kept to provide shade for crops, animals, or people.","zh":"shade trees 指為作物、動物或人提供遮蔭而種植或保留的樹木。"},{"en":"A school playground may have shade trees so children can rest out of the sun.","zh":"學校操場可能有遮蔭樹，讓孩子避開陽光休息。"},{"en":"If cacao farms keep shade trees, monkeys may use them for food and movement.","zh":"如果可可農場保留遮蔭樹，猴子可能把它們用作食物和移動路線。"},{"en":"The phrase describes trees with a protective shading function.","zh":"這個片語描述具有遮蔭保護功能的樹。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"leave something alone","meaning":"不碰；不破壞……","examples":[{"en":"The howlers leave the valuable cacao pods alone.","zh":"吼猴不碰有價值的可可豆莢。"},{"en":"Leave something alone means not touch, damage, use, or interfere with it.","zh":"leave something alone 指不觸碰、不破壞、不使用或不干擾某物。"},{"en":"A child should leave hot pans alone in the kitchen.","zh":"孩子在廚房中應該不碰熱鍋。"},{"en":"If monkeys leave cacao pods alone, farmers are less likely to see them as pests.","zh":"如果猴子不破壞可可豆莢，農民就較不會把牠們視為害獸。"},{"en":"The phrase means deliberately not disturbing something.","zh":"這個片語指刻意不打擾某物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"valuable cacao pods","meaning":"有價值的可可豆莢","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys do not damage the valuable cacao pods.","zh":"猴子不會破壞有價值的可可豆莢。"},{"en":"Valuable cacao pods are the important fruit of cacao trees that contain beans used to make cocoa and chocolate.","zh":"valuable cacao pods 指可可樹上重要的果實，內含用來製作可可和朱古力的豆。"},{"en":"Farmers protect valuable cacao pods because damaged pods reduce income.","zh":"農民保護有價值的可可豆莢，因為受損豆莢會減少收入。"},{"en":"If monkeys avoid the pods, they can live in plantations without harming the main crop.","zh":"如果猴子避開豆莢，就能在種植園生活而不傷害主要作物。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the economically important part of the plant.","zh":"這個片語指出植物中具經濟價值的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"underappreciated benefits","meaning":"被低估的好處","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys bring underappreciated benefits to the plantation.","zh":"猴子為種植園帶來被低估的好處。"},{"en":"Underappreciated benefits are useful effects that people do not notice or value enough.","zh":"underappreciated benefits 指人們沒有充分注意或重視的有用效果。"},{"en":"A quiet student may bring underappreciated benefits to a group by organising notes carefully.","zh":"安靜學生可能透過仔細整理筆記，為小組帶來被低估的好處。"},{"en":"If monkeys spread seeds and fertilise soil, farmers may benefit without realising it.","zh":"如果猴子傳播種子並為土壤施肥，農民可能在不知不覺中受益。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights hidden value.","zh":"這個片語突出隱藏價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"bring benefits to","meaning":"為……帶來好處","examples":[{"en":"Howler monkeys bring several benefits to cacao farms.","zh":"吼猴為可可農場帶來幾項好處。"},{"en":"Bring benefits to means provide advantages or helpful results for someone or something.","zh":"bring benefits to 指為某人或某物提供優勢或有用結果。"},{"en":"Better lighting can bring benefits to a classroom by helping students read more comfortably.","zh":"更好的照明可以為課室帶來好處，幫助學生更舒服地閱讀。"},{"en":"If monkeys improve soil and spread seeds, they bring practical benefits to farms.","zh":"如果猴子改善土壤並傳播種子，就為農場帶來實際好處。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on positive effects.","zh":"這個片語集中於正面效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"disperse the seeds of","meaning":"傳播……的種子","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys disperse the seeds of fig and shade trees.","zh":"猴子傳播無花果樹和遮蔭樹的種子。"},{"en":"Disperse the seeds of means spread seeds away from the parent plant.","zh":"disperse the seeds of 指把種子從母株附近傳播出去。"},{"en":"Birds disperse the seeds of berries when they eat the fruit and fly elsewhere.","zh":"鳥類吃漿果後飛到別處，就會傳播漿果植物的種子。"},{"en":"If monkeys disperse seeds, new trees can grow in different parts of the farm or forest.","zh":"如果猴子傳播種子，新樹就能在農場或森林不同地方生長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an important ecological service.","zh":"這個片語描述重要的生態服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fertilize the soil","meaning":"為土壤施肥","examples":[{"en":"The monkeys help fertilize the soil.","zh":"猴子幫助為土壤施肥。"},{"en":"Fertilize the soil means add nutrients that help plants grow better.","zh":"fertilize the soil 指增加養分，使植物生長得更好。"},{"en":"Gardeners fertilize the soil with compost before planting vegetables.","zh":"園丁在種菜前用堆肥為土壤施肥。"},{"en":"If monkeys leave droppings on the ground, nutrients may return to the soil.","zh":"如果猴子在地上留下糞便，養分可能回到土壤中。"},{"en":"The phrase connects animal activity with plant growth.","zh":"這個片語把動物活動與植物生長連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"forage for fruit","meaning":"覓食水果","examples":[{"en":"Spider monkeys also forage for fruit in the plantation.","zh":"蜘蛛猴也在種植園中覓食水果。"},{"en":"Forage for fruit means search for fruit to eat.","zh":"forage for fruit 指尋找水果來吃。"},{"en":"Children may forage for berries in a garden only if adults know they are safe.","zh":"孩子只有在成人知道漿果安全時，才可以在花園中覓食漿果。"},{"en":"If animals forage in plantations, farms may function partly as feeding habitat.","zh":"如果動物在種植園覓食，農場可能部分作為覓食棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes searching for food in a natural or semi-natural setting.","zh":"這個片語描述在自然或半自然環境中尋找食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in the long term","meaning":"長遠而言","examples":[{"en":"Spider monkeys still need nearby forest in the long term.","zh":"長遠而言，蜘蛛猴仍需要附近森林。"},{"en":"In the long term means over a long period, not just immediately.","zh":"in the long term 指長時間來看，而不只是眼前。"},{"en":"Saving money is difficult now, but in the long term it can reduce stress.","zh":"儲錢現在很難，但長遠而言可以減少壓力。"},{"en":"If monkeys use plantations today but need forests later, conservation must plan beyond short-term survival.","zh":"如果猴子今天使用種植園，但日後仍需要森林，保育就必須超越短期生存來規劃。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on future lasting needs or effects.","zh":"這個片語集中於未來持久需要或影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"see the advantages of","meaning":"看見……的好處","examples":[{"en":"Estrada hopes farmers will see the advantages of living alongside monkeys.","zh":"Estrada 希望農民會看見與猴子共存的好處。"},{"en":"See the advantages of means understand the benefits of something.","zh":"see the advantages of 指理解某事的好處。"},{"en":"Parents may see the advantages of reading aloud when children become more confident with words.","zh":"當孩子對文字更有信心時，家長可能看見朗讀的好處。"},{"en":"If farmers see benefits from monkeys, they may be more willing to protect them.","zh":"如果農民看見猴子的好處，就可能更願意保護牠們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes recognising positive value.","zh":"這個片語描述認識到正面價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"associate with wild monkeys","meaning":"與野生猴子共存","examples":[{"en":"Farmers may benefit from associating with wild monkeys.","zh":"農民可能因與野生猴子共存而受益。"},{"en":"Associate with wild monkeys means live, work, or interact in areas where wild monkeys are present.","zh":"associate with wild monkeys 指在有野生猴子的地區生活、工作或互動。"},{"en":"A tour guide may associate with wild animals by leading visitors through protected habitats carefully.","zh":"導遊可能透過小心帶領遊客穿越受保護棲息地，與野生動物接觸。"},{"en":"If farmers associate peacefully with monkeys, ecotourism and ecological services may become possible.","zh":"如果農民和平地與猴子共存，生態旅遊和生態服務可能變得可行。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests coexistence and contact.","zh":"這個片語暗示共存和接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"potential ecotourism projects","meaning":"具潛力的生態旅遊項目","examples":[{"en":"Wild monkeys could support potential ecotourism projects.","zh":"野生猴子可以支持具潛力的生態旅遊項目。"},{"en":"Potential ecotourism projects are possible tourism activities based on nature and conservation.","zh":"potential ecotourism projects 指以自然和保育為基礎的可能旅遊活動。"},{"en":"A village with rare birds may develop potential ecotourism projects such as guided walks.","zh":"擁有稀有鳥類的村莊可能發展導賞步行等具潛力的生態旅遊項目。"},{"en":"If visitors pay to see monkeys responsibly, farmers may earn income while protecting habitat.","zh":"如果遊客負責任地付費觀看猴子，農民可能一邊保護棲息地，一邊獲得收入。"},{"en":"The phrase describes possible nature-based business opportunities.","zh":"這個片語描述可能的自然旅遊商機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be viewed as a conflict between","meaning":"被視為……之間的衝突","examples":[{"en":"Conservation is often viewed as a conflict between farming and nature.","zh":"保育常被視為農業與自然之間的衝突。"},{"en":"Be viewed as a conflict between means be seen as a situation where two things oppose each other.","zh":"be viewed as a conflict between 指被看成兩件事互相對立的情況。"},{"en":"Homework may be viewed as a conflict between study and rest if students are overloaded.","zh":"如果學生功課過多，功課可能被視為學習與休息之間的衝突。"},{"en":"If farming and conservation are seen as enemies, people may miss chances for cooperation.","zh":"如果農業和保育被視為敵人，人們可能錯過合作機會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common but possibly limited viewpoint.","zh":"這個片語描述常見但可能有限的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"farming practices","meaning":"農業做法","examples":[{"en":"Some farming practices can be adapted to support wildlife.","zh":"有些農業做法可以被調整以支持野生動物。"},{"en":"Farming practices are the methods farmers use to grow crops or raise animals.","zh":"farming practices 指農民用來種植作物或飼養動物的方法。"},{"en":"Farming practices include watering, planting, fertilising, grazing, and harvesting.","zh":"農業做法包括灌溉、種植、施肥、放牧和收成。"},{"en":"If farmers keep shade trees or reduce chemicals, farming practices can become more wildlife-friendly.","zh":"如果農民保留遮蔭樹或減少化學品，農業做法可以變得更適合野生動物。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical agricultural methods.","zh":"這個片語指實際農業方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"preserve nature","meaning":"保護大自然","examples":[{"en":"Conservation policies aim to preserve nature.","zh":"保育政策旨在保護大自然。"},{"en":"Preserve nature means protect natural places, species, and ecological processes from damage.","zh":"preserve nature 指保護自然地方、物種和生態過程免受破壞。"},{"en":"A community can preserve nature by cleaning rivers and planting native trees.","zh":"社區可以透過清潔河流和種植本土樹木來保護大自然。"},{"en":"If nature is preserved, wildlife has a better chance of surviving alongside people.","zh":"如果大自然受到保護，野生動物就更有機會與人類共存。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on protection and long-term care.","zh":"這個片語集中於保護和長期照料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"move away from that vision","meaning":"擺脫那種看法","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are moving away from the idea that farming and conservation must conflict.","zh":"研究人員正在擺脫農業和保育必然衝突的看法。"},{"en":"Move away from that vision means stop accepting an old way of seeing a situation.","zh":"move away from that vision 指不再接受舊有的看待情況方式。"},{"en":"Schools may move away from the vision that learning means memorising facts only.","zh":"學校可能擺脫學習只是背誦事實的看法。"},{"en":"If research shows farms can help wildlife, people may abandon the old conflict model.","zh":"如果研究顯示農場可以幫助野生動物，人們可能放棄舊有衝突模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shift in thinking.","zh":"這個片語描述思維上的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"consider ways in which","meaning":"考慮……的方法","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are considering ways in which farms can support primates.","zh":"科學家正在考慮農場可以支持靈長類動物的方法。"},{"en":"Consider ways in which means think carefully about possible methods by which something can happen.","zh":"consider ways in which 指仔細思考某事可以發生的可能方法。"},{"en":"Teachers may consider ways in which homework can support learning without causing stress.","zh":"老師可能考慮功課如何支持學習而不造成壓力的方法。"},{"en":"If farms can keep useful trees, they may support animals as well as crops.","zh":"如果農場能保留有用樹木，就可能同時支持動物和作物。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces practical possibilities.","zh":"這個片語引出實際可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"commercial activities","meaning":"商業活動","examples":[{"en":"Commercial activities can sometimes contribute to conservation.","zh":"商業活動有時可以有助於保育。"},{"en":"Commercial activities are actions done to earn money, such as farming, tourism, or selling products.","zh":"commercial activities 指為賺錢而進行的活動，例如農業、旅遊或出售產品。"},{"en":"A market stall, a farm, and a tour company all carry out commercial activities.","zh":"市集攤檔、農場和旅行公司都進行商業活動。"},{"en":"If commercial activities reward habitat protection, businesses may help conservation rather than harm it.","zh":"如果商業活動獎勵棲息地保護，企業就可能幫助而非傷害保育。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to money-making activities.","zh":"這個片語指賺取收入的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"become a tool for","meaning":"成為……的工具","examples":[{"en":"Agriculture may become a tool for primate conservation.","zh":"農業可能成為靈長類動物保育的工具。"},{"en":"Become a tool for means start to be used as a practical way to achieve a goal.","zh":"become a tool for 指開始被用作達成某目標的實際方法。"},{"en":"Storytelling can become a tool for teaching history when facts feel too distant.","zh":"當史實感覺遙遠時，說故事可以成為教授歷史的工具。"},{"en":"If farms provide food and tree cover, agriculture can help protect animals.","zh":"如果農場提供食物和樹木覆蓋，農業就可以幫助保護動物。"},{"en":"The phrase shows something being used purposefully.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事被有目的地使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"conservation of primates","meaning":"靈長類動物保育","examples":[{"en":"The project explores new approaches to the conservation of primates.","zh":"該項目探索靈長類動物保育的新方法。"},{"en":"Conservation of primates means protecting monkeys, apes, lemurs, and their habitats.","zh":"conservation of primates 指保護猴子、猿、狐猴及其棲息地。"},{"en":"Conservation of primates may involve forest protection, community education, and careful tourism.","zh":"靈長類動物保育可能涉及森林保護、社區教育和謹慎旅遊。"},{"en":"If farms can support primates, conservation does not need to happen only inside parks.","zh":"如果農場能支持靈長類動物，保育就不需要只在公園內發生。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to protecting a whole group of related animals.","zh":"這個片語指保護一整個相關動物群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"human-modified landscapes","meaning":"經人類改造的景觀","examples":[{"en":"Some primates can survive in human-modified landscapes.","zh":"有些靈長類動物能在經人類改造的景觀中生存。"},{"en":"Human-modified landscapes are areas changed by people through farming, roads, buildings, or plantations.","zh":"human-modified landscapes 指被人類透過農業、道路、建築或種植園改變的地區。"},{"en":"City parks, orchards, and roadside forests are examples of human-modified landscapes.","zh":"城市公園、果園和路邊森林都是經人類改造的景觀例子。"},{"en":"If animals survive in human-modified landscapes, conservation can include farms and villages.","zh":"如果動物能在經人類改造的景觀中生存，保育就可以包括農場和村莊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes nature shaped by human activity.","zh":"這個片語描述被人類活動塑造的自然。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"contain the following information","meaning":"包含以下資料","examples":[{"en":"Candidates identify which paragraph contains the following information.","zh":"考生識別哪一段包含以下資料。"},{"en":"Contain the following information means include the details listed in the question.","zh":"contain the following information 指包括題目列出的細節。"},{"en":"A school notice may contain the following information: date, place, fee, and contact person.","zh":"學校通告可能包含以下資料：日期、地點、費用和聯絡人。"},{"en":"If a paragraph contains the information, students should match it with the correct letter.","zh":"如果某段包含該資料，學生應把它與正確字母配對。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in reading-location tasks.","zh":"這個片語常見於閱讀定位題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"use any letter more than once","meaning":"同一字母可使用多於一次","examples":[{"en":"The same paragraph letter may be used more than once.","zh":"同一段落字母可使用多於一次。"},{"en":"Use any letter more than once means one answer option can be used for several questions.","zh":"use any letter more than once 指同一答案選項可用於幾條題目。"},{"en":"In a matching exercise, students may use the same paragraph letter twice if two facts appear there.","zh":"在配對練習中，如果兩項資料出現在同一段，學生可以同一段落字母用兩次。"},{"en":"If students wrongly assume each letter is used once only, they may lose marks.","zh":"如果學生錯誤以為每個字母只能用一次，可能會失分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an important exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語給出重要考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"provide better feeding opportunities","meaning":"提供較好的覓食機會","examples":[{"en":"Younger forests provide howlers with better feeding opportunities.","zh":"較年輕的森林為吼猴提供較好的覓食機會。"},{"en":"Provide better feeding opportunities means offer more suitable chances to find and eat food.","zh":"provide better feeding opportunities 指提供更合適的尋找和進食食物的機會。"},{"en":"A school can provide better learning opportunities by keeping the library open after class.","zh":"學校課後開放圖書館，可以提供較好的學習機會。"},{"en":"If young forests have low-toxin leaves, howlers can feed more easily there.","zh":"如果年輕森林有低毒素葉子，吼猴就能更容易在那裡覓食。"},{"en":"The phrase connects environment with access to food.","zh":"這個片語把環境與取得食物連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a reference to","meaning":"提及……","examples":[{"en":"The question includes a reference to changing attitudes towards wildlife.","zh":"題目包括提及對野生動物態度轉變的內容。"},{"en":"A reference to something is a mention of that thing.","zh":"a reference to something 指提到某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to find a reference to pollution in the passage.","zh":"老師可能要求學生在文章中找出提及污染的地方。"},{"en":"If a question asks for a reference, students should locate where the idea is mentioned.","zh":"如果題目要求找出提及某事的地方，學生應定位該想法在哪裡出現。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful for reading questions about specific information.","zh":"這個片語適用於關於特定資料的閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"changing attitudes towards wildlife","meaning":"對野生動物態度的轉變","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes changing farmers’ attitudes towards wildlife.","zh":"文章描述農民對野生動物態度的轉變。"},{"en":"Changing attitudes towards wildlife means people begin to think differently about wild animals.","zh":"changing attitudes towards wildlife 指人們開始以不同方式看待野生動物。"},{"en":"A community may change its attitude towards bats after learning that they control insects.","zh":"社區在得知蝙蝠能控制昆蟲後，可能改變對蝙蝠的態度。"},{"en":"If farmers see monkeys as useful rather than harmful, they may protect them.","zh":"如果農民把猴子視為有用而非有害，就可能保護牠們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shift in human perception.","zh":"這個片語描述人類看法上的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"means by which","meaning":"……所採用的方法","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about the means by which howlers select food.","zh":"題目詢問吼猴選擇食物所採用的方法。"},{"en":"Means by which means the method or process used to do something.","zh":"means by which 指用來做某事的方法或過程。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask about the means by which students remember new vocabulary.","zh":"老師可能詢問學生記住新詞彙所採用的方法。"},{"en":"If howlers sample plants before choosing food, sampling is the means by which they select their diet.","zh":"如果吼猴先試食植物再選食物，試食就是牠們選擇飲食的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase asks about method.","zh":"這個片語詢問方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"select the best available diet","meaning":"選擇現有最佳飲食","examples":[{"en":"Howlers sample plants to select the best available diet.","zh":"吼猴試食植物，以選擇現有最佳飲食。"},{"en":"Select the best available diet means choose the most suitable food options that can be found.","zh":"select the best available diet 指從可找到的食物中選擇最合適的飲食。"},{"en":"A student in a canteen may select the best available lunch by choosing fruit, rice, and vegetables.","zh":"學生在飯堂可能透過選水果、米飯和蔬菜來選擇現有最佳午餐。"},{"en":"If food sources change, animals must choose the best diet from what remains.","zh":"如果食物來源改變，動物必須從剩下的食物中選擇最佳飲食。"},{"en":"The phrase combines choice with limited availability.","zh":"這個片語結合選擇和有限供應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"figures relating to","meaning":"與……有關的數字","examples":[{"en":"The passage provides figures relating to forest loss.","zh":"文章提供與森林流失有關的數字。"},{"en":"Figures relating to something are numbers or statistics about that topic.","zh":"figures relating to something 指關於某主題的數字或統計資料。"},{"en":"A school report may include figures relating to attendance and exam results.","zh":"學校報告可能包括與出席率和考試成績有關的數字。"},{"en":"If figures show large forest loss, the problem becomes clearer and harder to ignore.","zh":"如果數字顯示森林大量流失，問題就更清楚，也更難忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces numerical evidence.","zh":"這個片語引出數字證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reduction of natural wildlife habitat","meaning":"天然野生動物棲息地的減少","examples":[{"en":"The figures show the reduction of natural wildlife habitat.","zh":"這些數字顯示天然野生動物棲息地的減少。"},{"en":"Reduction of natural wildlife habitat means a decrease in the area where wild animals can live naturally.","zh":"reduction of natural wildlife habitat 指野生動物能自然生活的地區面積減少。"},{"en":"Road building can cause reduction of wildlife habitat when forests are divided into small patches.","zh":"道路建設把森林分割成小片時，可能造成野生動物棲息地減少。"},{"en":"If habitat is reduced, animals may have less food, shelter, and breeding space.","zh":"如果棲息地減少，動物可能有更少食物、庇護和繁殖空間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes habitat loss.","zh":"這個片語描述棲息地喪失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"over a period of time","meaning":"在一段時間內","examples":[{"en":"The habitat declined substantially over a period of time.","zh":"棲息地在一段時間內大幅減少。"},{"en":"Over a period of time means during a length of time, not all at once.","zh":"over a period of time 指在一段時間之中，而不是一次過發生。"},{"en":"A student’s English can improve over a period of time through daily reading.","zh":"學生可以透過每日閱讀，在一段時間內改善英語。"},{"en":"If forest declines over time, each year’s loss may seem small but the final damage can be large.","zh":"如果森林隨時間減少，每年的損失可能看似小，但最終破壞可能很大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual change.","zh":"這個片語描述逐漸變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"complete the summary below","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete the summary below with words from the passage.","zh":"考生用文章中的字詞完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"Complete the summary below means fill in missing words in the short text that follows.","zh":"complete the summary below 指填入後面短文中的缺失字詞。"},{"en":"In a reading exercise, students complete the summary below by locating key ideas in the passage.","zh":"在閱讀練習中，學生透過定位文章中的關鍵想法來完成以下摘要。"},{"en":"If students understand the main ideas, they can choose words that fit both meaning and grammar.","zh":"如果學生理解主旨，就能選出意思和文法都合適的字。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"one word only","meaning":"只可填一個詞","examples":[{"en":"Each answer must contain one word only.","zh":"每個答案只可填一個詞。"},{"en":"One word only means the answer must be exactly one word, not two or more.","zh":"one word only 指答案必須正好是一個詞，而不是兩個或更多。"},{"en":"If the instruction says one word only, “water” is acceptable but “fresh water” is not.","zh":"如果指示說只可填一個詞，“water” 可以接受，但 “fresh water” 不可以。"},{"en":"Ignoring this instruction can make a correct idea lose marks.","zh":"忽視這個指示可能令正確想法失分。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict word-limit rule.","zh":"這個片語給出嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have an advantage over","meaning":"比……有優勢","examples":[{"en":"Howlers have an advantage over other Central American monkeys.","zh":"吼猴比其他中美洲猴子有優勢。"},{"en":"Have an advantage over means be in a better position than another person, group, or species.","zh":"have an advantage over 指比另一人、群體或物種處於更有利位置。"},{"en":"Students who revise early have an advantage over those who start the night before.","zh":"提早溫習的學生比考試前一晚才開始的學生有優勢。"},{"en":"If howlers can eat leaves and tolerate drought, they may survive better than other monkeys.","zh":"如果吼猴能吃樹葉並忍受乾旱，牠們可能比其他猴子更能生存。"},{"en":"The phrase describes comparative strength.","zh":"這個片語描述比較上的強項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rapid rate of reproduction","meaning":"快速的繁殖率","examples":[{"en":"Howlers have a more rapid rate of reproduction.","zh":"吼猴有更快速的繁殖率。"},{"en":"Rapid rate of reproduction means producing offspring quickly or frequently.","zh":"rapid rate of reproduction 指快速或頻繁地產生後代。"},{"en":"Insects often have a rapid rate of reproduction because many eggs hatch in a short time.","zh":"昆蟲通常有快速的繁殖率，因為許多卵在短時間內孵化。"},{"en":"If a species reproduces quickly, its population can recover faster after decline.","zh":"如果某物種繁殖得快，其種群在下降後可以更快恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to how fast a population can grow through births.","zh":"這個片語指種群透過出生而增長的速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"local monkey species","meaning":"本地猴類物種","examples":[{"en":"Howlers differ from the other local monkey species.","zh":"吼猴與其他本地猴類物種不同。"},{"en":"Local monkey species are the monkey types naturally found in the area being discussed.","zh":"local monkey species 指自然存在於所討論地區的猴類種類。"},{"en":"A wildlife guide may compare local monkey species by diet, size, and behaviour.","zh":"野生動物導遊可能按飲食、大小和行為比較本地猴類物種。"},{"en":"If one local species adapts better to farms, its numbers may grow while others decline.","zh":"如果某一本地物種更適應農場，其數量可能上升，而其他物種下降。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on monkeys native to a particular region.","zh":"這個片語集中於某地區本土猴類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"survive without eating fruit","meaning":"不吃水果也能生存","examples":[{"en":"Howlers can survive for periods without eating fruit.","zh":"吼猴可以有一段時間不吃水果也能生存。"},{"en":"Survive without eating fruit means continue living even when fruit is not part of the diet.","zh":"survive without eating fruit 指即使飲食中沒有水果仍能繼續生活。"},{"en":"A person can survive without dessert, but not without enough basic food and water.","zh":"人可以沒有甜品也能生存，但不能沒有足夠基本食物和水。"},{"en":"If fruit is scarce, howlers can rely on leaves instead.","zh":"如果水果稀少，吼猴可以改為依賴樹葉。"},{"en":"The phrase shows dietary flexibility.","zh":"這個片語顯示飲食靈活性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"relatively small habitat area","meaning":"相對細小的棲息地範圍","examples":[{"en":"Howlers can live inside a relatively small habitat area.","zh":"吼猴可以生活在相對細小的棲息地範圍內。"},{"en":"A relatively small habitat area is a living space that is smaller than what similar animals may need.","zh":"relatively small habitat area 指比相似動物所需空間較小的生活區域。"},{"en":"Some insects can survive in a relatively small garden if food plants are available.","zh":"如果有食用植物，一些昆蟲可以在相對細小的花園中生存。"},{"en":"If howlers need only a small area, fragmented forests can still support them.","zh":"如果吼猴只需要小範圍，破碎森林仍能支持牠們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limited space that is still usable.","zh":"這個片語描述有限但仍可使用的空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"flexible diet","meaning":"靈活的飲食","examples":[{"en":"The howlers’ flexible diet helps them survive environmental change.","zh":"吼猴靈活的飲食幫助牠們在環境變化中生存。"},{"en":"A flexible diet means the ability to eat different kinds of food when conditions change.","zh":"flexible diet 指在情況改變時能吃不同種類食物的能力。"},{"en":"A student with a flexible diet can still eat well when the canteen runs out of one dish.","zh":"飯堂某道菜賣完時，有靈活飲食的學生仍可以吃得好。"},{"en":"If animals can switch from fruit to leaves, they are less affected by seasonal food shortages.","zh":"如果動物能從水果轉吃樹葉，就較少受季節性食物短缺影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adaptability in food choice.","zh":"這個片語描述食物選擇上的適應力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tolerate high levels of","meaning":"忍受高水平的……","examples":[{"en":"Howlers can tolerate high levels of plant toxins.","zh":"吼猴能忍受高水平的植物毒素。"},{"en":"Tolerate high levels of means endure a large amount of something difficult or harmful.","zh":"tolerate high levels of 指承受大量困難或有害的東西。"},{"en":"Some people cannot tolerate high levels of noise when they study.","zh":"有些人在溫習時不能忍受高水平噪音。"},{"en":"If monkeys tolerate plant toxins, they can eat leaves that other species avoid.","zh":"如果猴子能忍受植物毒素，就能吃其他物種避開的葉子。"},{"en":"The phrase describes resistance to a strong pressure or substance.","zh":"這個片語描述對強大壓力或物質的抵抗力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"survive periods of drought","meaning":"熬過乾旱時期","examples":[{"en":"Howlers survive periods of drought better than other monkeys.","zh":"吼猴比其他猴子更能熬過乾旱時期。"},{"en":"Survive periods of drought means continue living through times when there is little rain or water.","zh":"survive periods of drought 指在雨水或水源很少的時期繼續生存。"},{"en":"Some plants survive periods of drought by storing water in thick stems.","zh":"有些植物透過在粗莖中儲水來熬過乾旱時期。"},{"en":"If howlers get water from leaves, drought may affect them less severely.","zh":"如果吼猴從樹葉取得水分，乾旱對牠們的影響可能較輕。"},{"en":"The phrase describes endurance during dry conditions.","zh":"這個片語描述在乾燥條件下的忍耐力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"look at the following features","meaning":"查看以下特徵","examples":[{"en":"Candidates look at the following features and locations.","zh":"考生查看以下特徵和地點。"},{"en":"Look at the following features means examine the listed characteristics carefully.","zh":"look at the following features 指仔細檢視列出的特徵。"},{"en":"In a science worksheet, students may look at the following features of insects: wings, legs, and antennae.","zh":"在科學工作紙中，學生可能查看昆蟲的以下特徵：翅膀、腳和觸角。"},{"en":"If students identify each feature correctly, they can match it with the right location.","zh":"如果學生正確識別每項特徵，就能把它與正確地點配對。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a list for comparison.","zh":"這個片語引出用於比較的列表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"list of locations","meaning":"地點列表","examples":[{"en":"The task provides a list of three locations.","zh":"任務提供三個地點的列表。"},{"en":"A list of locations is a set of place names used as answer choices.","zh":"list of locations 指一組作為答案選項的地名。"},{"en":"A geography quiz may give a list of locations and ask students to match rivers to them.","zh":"地理小測可能給出地點列表，要求學生把河流與它們配對。"},{"en":"If a feature appears in one location, students should choose that place from the list.","zh":"如果某特徵出現在某一地點，學生應從列表中選出該地方。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to location options in a matching task.","zh":"這個片語指配對題中的地點選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"match each feature with","meaning":"把每項特徵與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Candidates match each feature with the correct location.","zh":"考生把每項特徵與正確地點配對。"},{"en":"Match each feature with means connect every listed characteristic to the right answer option.","zh":"match each feature with 指把每個列出的特徵連接到正確答案選項。"},{"en":"Students may match each animal feature with the correct species in a biology test.","zh":"學生可能在生物測驗中把每項動物特徵與正確物種配對。"},{"en":"If one feature belongs to a plantation and another to a national park, the answers must differ.","zh":"如果一項特徵屬於種植園，另一項屬於國家公園，答案就必須不同。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a matching task.","zh":"這個片語描述配對任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"see the return of","meaning":"見證……重新出現","examples":[{"en":"The park has seen the return of native tree species.","zh":"公園見證了本土樹種重新出現。"},{"en":"See the return of means experience or witness something coming back.","zh":"see the return of 指經歷或見證某事物回來。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood may see the return of small shops after rent becomes more affordable.","zh":"租金變得較可負擔後，社區可能見證小店重新出現。"},{"en":"If trees return after protection, the ecosystem is beginning to recover.","zh":"如果樹木在保護後回歸，生態系統就開始恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a place experiencing recovery.","zh":"這個片語描述某地經歷恢復。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"native tree species","meaning":"本土樹木品種","examples":[{"en":"Several native tree species returned after protection began.","zh":"保護開始後，幾種本土樹木品種回歸。"},{"en":"Native tree species are tree types that naturally belong to a local area.","zh":"native tree species 指自然屬於本地地區的樹木種類。"},{"en":"A park may plant native tree species because they support local insects and birds.","zh":"公園可能種植本土樹木品種，因為它們支持本地昆蟲和鳥類。"},{"en":"If native trees return, the food web may gradually become healthier.","zh":"如果本土樹木回歸，食物網可能逐漸變得更健康。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to local tree types.","zh":"這個片語指本地樹木種類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"support only one species","meaning":"只容納一個物種","examples":[{"en":"One location supports only one native monkey species.","zh":"其中一個地點只容納一種本土猴類物種。"},{"en":"Support only one species means provide habitat for just one type of animal or plant.","zh":"support only one species 指只為一種動物或植物提供棲息地。"},{"en":"A small pond may support only one fish species if the water is shallow and seasonal.","zh":"如果水塘很淺且有季節性，小池塘可能只容納一種魚。"},{"en":"If a site supports only one monkey species, its habitat may be too limited for others.","zh":"如果某地只支持一種猴類，其棲息地可能對其他猴類太有限。"},{"en":"The phrase describes restricted biodiversity.","zh":"這個片語描述受限制的生物多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"help the agriculture of","meaning":"促進……的農業","examples":[{"en":"The monkey population helps the agriculture of the area.","zh":"猴子種群促進該地區的農業。"},{"en":"Help the agriculture of an area means support farming through useful effects such as seed dispersal or soil fertilisation.","zh":"help the agriculture of an area 指透過傳播種子、為土壤施肥等有用效果支持農業。"},{"en":"Bees help the agriculture of a region by pollinating fruit trees and vegetables.","zh":"蜜蜂透過為果樹和蔬菜授粉，促進一個地區的農業。"},{"en":"If monkeys spread shade-tree seeds, they can indirectly support plantation crops.","zh":"如果猴子傳播遮蔭樹種子，就能間接支持種植園作物。"},{"en":"The phrase connects wildlife with farming benefits.","zh":"這個片語把野生動物與農業好處連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be home to populations of","meaning":"是多個……種群的棲息地","examples":[{"en":"Santa Rosa is home to populations of all three monkey species.","zh":"Santa Rosa 是三種猴類種群的棲息地。"},{"en":"Be home to populations of means provide habitat for groups of a particular species or several species.","zh":"be home to populations of 指為某一種或幾種物種的群體提供棲息地。"},{"en":"A wetland may be home to populations of frogs, birds, and insects.","zh":"濕地可能是青蛙、鳥類和昆蟲多個種群的棲息地。"},{"en":"If a park supports populations of all local monkeys, it has high conservation value.","zh":"如果公園支持所有本地猴類種群，它就有高保育價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a place supporting living groups.","zh":"這個片語描述某地支持活生生的群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"all three local monkey species","meaning":"三種本地猴類物種","examples":[{"en":"The national park supports all three local monkey species.","zh":"國家公園支持三種本地猴類物種。"},{"en":"All three local monkey species means every one of the three monkey types naturally found in the area.","zh":"all three local monkey species 指自然存在於該地區的三種猴類全部。"},{"en":"A reserve that protects all local bird species is more valuable than one protecting only a few.","zh":"保護所有本地鳥類的保護區，比只保護少數物種的地區更有價值。"},{"en":"If all three monkey species return, forest recovery is more complete.","zh":"如果三種猴類都回歸，森林恢復就更完整。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses full inclusion of the local monkey groups.","zh":"這個片語強調完整包括本地猴類群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be altered by the construction of","meaning":"因興建……而被改變","examples":[{"en":"The landscape was altered by the construction of a major highway.","zh":"該景觀因興建一條主要公路而被改變。"},{"en":"Be altered by the construction of means be changed because something was built.","zh":"be altered by the construction of 指因某物被建成而改變。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood may be altered by the construction of a new railway station.","zh":"社區可能因興建新火車站而被改變。"},{"en":"If a highway is built through forest, animal movement and habitat shape may change.","zh":"如果公路穿過森林興建，動物移動和棲息地形態可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase links physical change to a building project.","zh":"這個片語把實體改變與建設項目連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"transport link","meaning":"交通幹線","examples":[{"en":"The Pan-American Highway is an important transport link.","zh":"泛美公路是一條重要交通幹線。"},{"en":"A transport link is a road, railway, bridge, or route that connects places and allows movement.","zh":"transport link 指連接地方並容許移動的道路、鐵路、橋樑或路線。"},{"en":"A new bridge can become a major transport link between two towns.","zh":"新橋可以成為連接兩個城鎮的主要交通幹線。"},{"en":"If a transport link cuts through habitat, it can help people travel but harm wildlife movement.","zh":"如果交通幹線穿過棲息地，它可以幫助人類出行，但傷害野生動物移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes infrastructure that connects areas.","zh":"這個片語描述連接不同地區的基建。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 165 - The return of monkey life.pdf","sourcePage":14}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 166":[{"front":"Alfred Nobel: The Man Behind the Nobel Prize","meaning":"Alfred Nobel：諾貝爾獎背後的人物","examples":[{"en":"Alfred Nobel used his fortune to establish the Nobel Prize.","zh":"Alfred Nobel 用他的財產成立諾貝爾獎。"},{"en":"The man behind the Nobel Prize was Alfred Nobel, whose money and will made the prizes possible.","zh":"諾貝爾獎背後的人物是 Alfred Nobel；他的金錢和遺囑令獎項成為可能。"},{"en":"A history lesson about Nobel may explain how one inventor’s wealth became an international award system.","zh":"關於 Nobel 的歷史課可能解釋一位發明家的財富如何變成國際獎項制度。"},{"en":"If a person leaves money for a public purpose, their influence can continue after death.","zh":"如果一個人把金錢留作公共用途，他的影響可以在死後延續。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the person whose life and decisions created the Nobel Prize.","zh":"這個短語集中於其人生和決定創立諾貝爾獎的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"since 1901","meaning":"自1901年以來","examples":[{"en":"Since 1901, the Nobel Prize has honoured outstanding achievements.","zh":"自1901年以來，諾貝爾獎表揚傑出成就。"},{"en":"Since 1901 means from the year 1901 until the present or a later stated time.","zh":"「since 1901」意思是從1901年直到現在或後來某個指定時間。"},{"en":"Since 1901, many schools, museums, and prizes have changed with the modern world.","zh":"自1901年以來，許多學校、博物館和獎項都隨現代世界改變。"},{"en":"If an award has existed since 1901, it has a long history and strong tradition.","zh":"如果一個獎項自1901年以來存在，它就有悠久歷史和強大傳統。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the starting point of a continuing period.","zh":"這個短語提供一段持續時期的起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Nobel Prize","meaning":"諾貝爾獎","examples":[{"en":"The Nobel Prize recognises major contributions to science, literature and peace.","zh":"諾貝爾獎表揚對科學、文學和和平的重大貢獻。"},{"en":"The Nobel Prize is an international award given for outstanding work in several important fields.","zh":"「Nobel Prize」是頒給在幾個重要範疇有傑出工作的人的國際獎項。"},{"en":"Students may learn about the Nobel Prize when studying famous scientists, writers, or peace activists.","zh":"學生研究著名科學家、作家或和平倡議者時，可能會學到諾貝爾獎。"},{"en":"If someone wins a Nobel Prize, their work is usually seen as highly influential.","zh":"如果有人獲得諾貝爾獎，其工作通常被視為很有影響力。"},{"en":"The phrase names one of the world’s best-known award systems.","zh":"這個短語指出世界上最著名的獎項制度之一。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"honour someone for","meaning":"因……而表揚某人","examples":[{"en":"The prize honours people for outstanding achievements.","zh":"該獎項因傑出成就而表揚人們。"},{"en":"To honour someone for something means to publicly recognise and praise them because of it.","zh":"「honour someone for」某事，意思是因為該事而公開認可和讚揚某人。"},{"en":"A school may honour a student for years of volunteer service.","zh":"學校可能因學生多年義工服務而表揚他。"},{"en":"If a community honours someone for brave action, others may be inspired to help too.","zh":"如果社區因勇敢行為而表揚某人，其他人也可能受到鼓舞去幫助。"},{"en":"The phrase connects public praise with the reason for that praise.","zh":"這個短語把公開讚揚與讚揚原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"from all corners of the globe","meaning":"來自世界各地","examples":[{"en":"Prize winners have come from all corners of the globe.","zh":"得獎者來自世界各地。"},{"en":"From all corners of the globe means from many different countries and regions around the world.","zh":"「from all corners of the globe」意思是來自世界上許多不同國家和地區。"},{"en":"A university may attract students from all corners of the globe.","zh":"一所大學可能吸引來自世界各地的學生。"},{"en":"If an award welcomes people from many places, it becomes truly international.","zh":"如果一個獎項歡迎來自許多地方的人，它就真正具有國際性。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses worldwide range and diversity.","zh":"這個短語強調全球範圍和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"outstanding achievements","meaning":"傑出成就","examples":[{"en":"The Nobel Prize recognises outstanding achievements in several fields.","zh":"諾貝爾獎表揚幾個範疇中的傑出成就。"},{"en":"Outstanding achievements are excellent accomplishments that are much better than ordinary results.","zh":"「outstanding achievements」是遠高於普通成果的優秀成就。"},{"en":"A student may receive a scholarship for outstanding achievements in science and service.","zh":"學生可能因科學和服務方面的傑出成就而獲得獎學金。"},{"en":"If someone’s achievements change a field, they may be recognised internationally.","zh":"如果某人的成就改變一個領域，他可能受到國際認可。"},{"en":"The phrase describes work that is exceptional and worthy of praise.","zh":"這個短語描述卓越並值得讚揚的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"efforts to promote peace","meaning":"促進和平的努力","examples":[{"en":"The Peace Prize honours efforts to promote peace.","zh":"和平獎表揚促進和平的努力。"},{"en":"Efforts to promote peace are actions taken to reduce conflict and encourage cooperation.","zh":"「efforts to promote peace」是為減少衝突和鼓勵合作而採取的行動。"},{"en":"A school may recognise students’ efforts to promote peace by resolving class disputes calmly.","zh":"學校可能表揚學生透過冷靜解決班內爭執來促進和平的努力。"},{"en":"If leaders promote peace successfully, communities may suffer less violence.","zh":"如果領袖成功促進和平，社區可能承受較少暴力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes work aimed at making relationships or societies more peaceful.","zh":"這個短語描述旨在令關係或社會更和平的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lay the foundations for","meaning":"為……奠定基礎","examples":[{"en":"Alfred Nobel’s will laid the foundations for the international prizes.","zh":"Alfred Nobel 的遺囑為國際獎項奠定基礎。"},{"en":"To lay the foundations for something means to create the basic conditions that make it possible later.","zh":"「lay the foundations for」某事，意思是創造令它日後成為可能的基本條件。"},{"en":"Good reading habits can lay the foundations for strong writing skills.","zh":"良好閱讀習慣可以為強大寫作能力奠定基礎。"},{"en":"If a law creates funding and rules for a project, it may lay the foundations for future success.","zh":"如果法律為項目建立資金和規則，它可能為未來成功奠定基礎。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an early action that supports later development.","zh":"這個短語描述支撐後來發展的早期行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"write one’s last will","meaning":"寫下遺囑","examples":[{"en":"Nobel wrote his last will in 1895.","zh":"Nobel 於1895年寫下遺囑。"},{"en":"To write one’s last will means to prepare a legal document saying what should happen to one’s property after death.","zh":"「write one’s last will」意思是準備法律文件，說明死後財產應如何處理。"},{"en":"An elderly person may write a last will to make sure their family understands their wishes.","zh":"長者可能寫下遺囑，以確保家人明白其意願。"},{"en":"If someone writes a clear will, disputes after death may be reduced.","zh":"如果有人寫下清楚遺囑，死後爭議可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a final legal statement about one’s estate.","zh":"這個短語描述就個人遺產作出最終法律聲明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"leave much of one’s wealth to","meaning":"將大部分財產留給……","examples":[{"en":"He left much of his wealth to the establishment of the prizes.","zh":"他將大部分財產留給獎項的成立。"},{"en":"To leave much of one’s wealth to something means to give a large part of one’s money or property to it after death.","zh":"「leave much of one’s wealth to」某事，意思是死後把大部分金錢或財產給予該事。"},{"en":"A donor may leave much of her wealth to a hospital in her will.","zh":"捐贈者可能在遺囑中將大部分財產留給醫院。"},{"en":"If someone leaves wealth to education, future students may benefit for many years.","zh":"如果有人把財產留給教育，未來學生可能多年受惠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using an inheritance to support a chosen purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述用遺產支持自己選定的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the establishment of","meaning":"……的成立","examples":[{"en":"His fortune supported the establishment of the Nobel Prize.","zh":"他的財產支持諾貝爾獎的成立。"},{"en":"The establishment of something is the act of creating or setting it up formally.","zh":"「the establishment of」某物，是正式創立或設立它的行動。"},{"en":"The establishment of a new school requires money, staff, buildings, and official approval.","zh":"新學校的成立需要金錢、員工、建築物和官方批准。"},{"en":"If an organisation is established properly, it can continue working after its founder dies.","zh":"如果機構妥善成立，它可以在創辦人去世後繼續運作。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the formal beginning of something.","zh":"這個短語集中於某事物的正式開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"engineer and inventor","meaning":"工程師兼發明家","examples":[{"en":"Immanuel Nobel was an engineer and inventor.","zh":"Immanuel Nobel 是工程師兼發明家。"},{"en":"An engineer and inventor is someone who designs practical systems and creates new devices or methods.","zh":"「engineer and inventor」是設計實用系統並創造新裝置或方法的人。"},{"en":"A person who builds safer bridges and invents new tools can be both an engineer and inventor.","zh":"一個建造更安全橋樑並發明新工具的人，可以既是工程師也是發明家。"},{"en":"If an inventor also understands engineering, their ideas may become practical products.","zh":"如果發明家也懂工程，他的想法可能變成實用產品。"},{"en":"The phrase combines technical problem-solving with creativity.","zh":"這個短語結合技術解難和創意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"build bridges and buildings","meaning":"興建橋樑和建築物","examples":[{"en":"Nobel’s father built bridges and buildings in Stockholm.","zh":"Nobel 的父親在斯德哥爾摩興建橋樑和建築物。"},{"en":"To build bridges and buildings means to construct structures used for transport, work, housing, or public life.","zh":"「build bridges and buildings」意思是建造用於交通、工作、住房或公共生活的結構。"},{"en":"A construction company may build bridges and buildings for a growing city.","zh":"建築公司可能為發展中的城市興建橋樑和建築物。"},{"en":"If engineers build safe bridges, people and goods can move more easily.","zh":"如果工程師興建安全橋樑，人和貨物就能更容易移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical construction work.","zh":"這個短語描述實際建築工程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in connection with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"He experimented with explosives in connection with his construction work.","zh":"他試驗爆炸物，與其建築工程有關。"},{"en":"In connection with means related to or because of a particular matter.","zh":"「in connection with」意思是與某事有關或因某事而發生。"},{"en":"A school may contact parents in connection with a sports day arrangement.","zh":"學校可能就運動會安排與家長聯絡。"},{"en":"If experiments are done in connection with construction, they are meant to solve building problems.","zh":"如果試驗與建築有關，它們就是為了解決建造問題。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a relationship between two things.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩件事之間的關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"construction work","meaning":"建築工程","examples":[{"en":"Explosives could make difficult construction work more efficient.","zh":"爆炸物可以令困難的建築工程更有效率。"},{"en":"Construction work is the practical work of building or repairing structures.","zh":"「construction work」是建造或修理結構的實際工作。"},{"en":"Road construction work may cause noise, dust, and traffic delays near a school.","zh":"學校附近的道路建築工程可能造成噪音、塵土和交通延誤。"},{"en":"If construction work involves rock, controlled blasting may save time.","zh":"如果建築工程涉及岩石，受控爆破可能節省時間。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the physical process of building.","zh":"這個短語指實際建造過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"experiment with","meaning":"試驗；研究……","examples":[{"en":"Immanuel Nobel experimented with different techniques for blasting rock.","zh":"Immanuel Nobel 試驗不同爆破岩石技術。"},{"en":"To experiment with something means to test it to see how it works.","zh":"「experiment with」某物，意思是測試它以了解其運作方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may experiment with games to make grammar lessons more active.","zh":"老師可能試驗用遊戲令文法課更活躍。"},{"en":"If engineers experiment with a new method, they can discover both benefits and risks.","zh":"如果工程師試驗新方法，他們可以發現好處和風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes trying something in a controlled or exploratory way.","zh":"這個短語描述以受控制或探索方式嘗試某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"blasting rock","meaning":"爆破岩石","examples":[{"en":"Controlled explosions are useful for blasting rock during construction.","zh":"受控爆炸在建築工程中對爆破岩石有用。"},{"en":"Blasting rock means breaking rock apart with explosives.","zh":"「blasting rock」意思是用爆炸物把岩石炸開。"},{"en":"Workers may use blasting rock methods before building a tunnel through a mountain.","zh":"工人在山中建隧道前，可能使用爆破岩石的方法。"},{"en":"If rock is too hard to dig by hand, blasting can make construction faster.","zh":"如果岩石太硬，不能用人手挖掘，爆破可以令工程更快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a forceful engineering method.","zh":"這個短語描述一種強力工程方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"industrial and business ventures","meaning":"工業及商業項目","examples":[{"en":"Immanuel Nobel succeeded in his industrial and business ventures.","zh":"Immanuel Nobel 在工業及商業項目中取得成功。"},{"en":"Industrial and business ventures are projects or companies connected with manufacturing, trade, or investment.","zh":"「industrial and business ventures」是與製造、貿易或投資有關的項目或公司。"},{"en":"A family may risk savings on a new business venture, such as opening a factory.","zh":"家庭可能把積蓄投放在新商業項目上，例如開設工廠。"},{"en":"If business ventures succeed, they can create wealth and jobs.","zh":"如果商業項目成功，它們可以創造財富和職位。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical commercial projects, often with risk.","zh":"這個短語描述實際商業項目，通常帶有風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be successful in","meaning":"在……方面取得成功","examples":[{"en":"He was successful in several business ventures.","zh":"他在幾個商業項目方面取得成功。"},{"en":"To be successful in something means to achieve good results in that area.","zh":"「be successful in」某事，意思是在該範疇取得好結果。"},{"en":"A student may be successful in public speaking after regular practice.","zh":"學生定期練習後，可能在公開演說方面取得成功。"},{"en":"If a business is successful, it may allow the owner to support the family better.","zh":"如果生意成功，東主可能更好地支持家庭。"},{"en":"The phrase connects success with a specific activity or field.","zh":"這個短語把成功與特定活動或範疇連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"bring one’s family to","meaning":"把家人帶到……","examples":[{"en":"His business success enabled him to bring his family to St. Petersburg.","zh":"他的商業成功使他能把家人帶到聖彼得堡。"},{"en":"To bring one’s family to a place means to move or take family members there.","zh":"「bring one’s family to」某地，意思是把家人搬到或帶到那裡。"},{"en":"A parent may bring the family to a new city after finding a stable job.","zh":"父母找到穩定工作後，可能把家人帶到新城市。"},{"en":"If a business becomes successful abroad, the owner may be able to reunite the family there.","zh":"如果海外生意成功，東主可能能夠讓家人在那裡團聚。"},{"en":"The phrase describes relocating family members because circumstances have changed.","zh":"這個短語描述因情況改變而遷移家人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be given a first-class education","meaning":"接受一流教育","examples":[{"en":"His sons were given a first-class education by private teachers.","zh":"他的兒子們由私人教師教授，接受一流教育。"},{"en":"To be given a first-class education means to receive excellent teaching and learning opportunities.","zh":"「be given a first-class education」意思是接受優秀教學和學習機會。"},{"en":"A child given a first-class education may learn languages, science, music, and critical thinking.","zh":"接受一流教育的孩子可能學習語言、科學、音樂和批判思考。"},{"en":"If students receive excellent education early, they may develop wider interests and skills.","zh":"如果學生早期接受優秀教育，他們可能發展更廣泛的興趣和技能。"},{"en":"The phrase describes very high-quality schooling or training.","zh":"這個短語描述非常高質素的教育或培訓。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"private teachers","meaning":"私人教師","examples":[{"en":"Private teachers taught Nobel science, languages and literature.","zh":"私人教師教授 Nobel 科學、語言和文學。"},{"en":"Private teachers are tutors hired to teach a student outside ordinary school classes.","zh":"「private teachers」是在普通學校課堂以外受聘教導學生的導師。"},{"en":"A family may hire private teachers if a child needs special preparation for exams.","zh":"如果孩子需要特殊考試準備，家庭可能聘請私人教師。"},{"en":"If private teachers provide individual attention, students may progress quickly.","zh":"如果私人教師提供個別關注，學生可能進步很快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes personalised teaching outside a normal classroom.","zh":"這個短語描述普通課室以外的個人化教學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"natural sciences","meaning":"自然科學","examples":[{"en":"His education included natural sciences, languages and literature.","zh":"他的教育包括自然科學、語言和文學。"},{"en":"Natural sciences are subjects that study the physical world, such as chemistry, physics, and biology.","zh":"「natural sciences」是研究物理世界的科目，例如化學、物理和生物。"},{"en":"Students study natural sciences when they learn how plants grow or how electricity works.","zh":"學生學習植物如何生長或電如何運作時，就是在學自然科學。"},{"en":"If someone has strong training in natural sciences, they may understand experiments more deeply.","zh":"如果某人在自然科學方面受過良好訓練，他可能更深入理解實驗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes scientific subjects about nature and matter.","zh":"這個短語描述關於自然和物質的科學科目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"by the age of 17","meaning":"到十七歲時","examples":[{"en":"By the age of 17, Nobel was fluent in five languages.","zh":"到十七歲時，Nobel 已能流利使用五種語言。"},{"en":"By the age of 17 means before or at the time someone reached seventeen years old.","zh":"「by the age of 17」意思是在某人十七歲之前或達到十七歲時。"},{"en":"By the age of 17, some students have already decided what subject they want to study.","zh":"到十七歲時，有些學生已決定想讀甚麼科目。"},{"en":"If a person masters several languages by 17, they probably had strong education and practice.","zh":"如果一個人在十七歲時掌握幾種語言，他很可能有良好教育和練習。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a deadline based on age.","zh":"這個短語提供以年齡為基準的期限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be fluent in","meaning":"能流利使用……","examples":[{"en":"Alfred Nobel was fluent in Swedish, Russian, French, English and German.","zh":"Alfred Nobel 能流利使用瑞典語、俄語、法語、英語和德語。"},{"en":"To be fluent in a language means to speak or use it smoothly and confidently.","zh":"「be fluent in」某語言，意思是能流暢而自信地說或使用它。"},{"en":"A student fluent in English can join discussions without translating every sentence in their head.","zh":"能流利使用英語的學生可以參與討論，而不用在腦中翻譯每句。"},{"en":"If someone is fluent in several languages, they can communicate across cultures more easily.","zh":"如果有人能流利使用幾種語言，他可以更容易跨文化溝通。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong practical language ability.","zh":"這個短語描述強大的實際語言能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"primary interests","meaning":"主要興趣","examples":[{"en":"His primary interests included literature, chemistry and physics.","zh":"他的主要興趣包括文學、化學和物理。"},{"en":"Primary interests are the subjects or activities a person cares about most.","zh":"「primary interests」是某人最關心的科目或活動。"},{"en":"A student’s primary interests may be music, biology, and computer programming.","zh":"學生的主要興趣可能是音樂、生物和電腦程式編寫。"},{"en":"If someone’s primary interests are broad, their career may combine several fields.","zh":"如果某人的主要興趣很廣泛，他的職業可能結合幾個領域。"},{"en":"The phrase describes main personal interests, not minor hobbies.","zh":"這個短語描述主要個人興趣，而不是小興趣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"English literature and poetry","meaning":"英國文學與詩歌","examples":[{"en":"Nobel developed a strong interest in English literature and poetry.","zh":"Nobel 對英國文學與詩歌產生濃厚興趣。"},{"en":"English literature and poetry refers to novels, plays, poems, and other creative writing in English.","zh":"「English literature and poetry」指英文小說、戲劇、詩和其他創意寫作。"},{"en":"A student may study English literature and poetry to understand language, emotion, and culture.","zh":"學生可能學習英國文學與詩歌，以理解語言、情感和文化。"},{"en":"If someone loves poetry, they may value imagination as well as scientific thinking.","zh":"如果有人喜愛詩歌，他可能重視想像力，也重視科學思考。"},{"en":"The phrase names a literary field that interested Nobel deeply.","zh":"這個短語指出 Nobel 深感興趣的文學範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"join an enterprise","meaning":"加入企業","examples":[{"en":"His father wanted his sons to join the family enterprise as engineers.","zh":"他的父親希望兒子們以工程師身份加入家族企業。"},{"en":"To join an enterprise means to become part of a business or organised commercial activity.","zh":"「join an enterprise」意思是加入一項生意或有組織的商業活動。"},{"en":"A graduate may join a family enterprise instead of working for a large company.","zh":"畢業生可能加入家族企業，而不是為大型公司工作。"},{"en":"If children join a family business, they may be expected to continue the parents’ work.","zh":"如果孩子加入家族生意，他們可能被期望延續父母的工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes entering a business organisation.","zh":"這個短語描述進入商業組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"dislike someone’s interest in","meaning":"不喜歡某人對……的興趣","examples":[{"en":"Immanuel Nobel disliked Alfred’s interest in poetry.","zh":"Immanuel Nobel 不喜歡 Alfred 對詩歌的興趣。"},{"en":"To dislike someone’s interest in something means to disapprove of or feel unhappy about what they enjoy.","zh":"「dislike someone’s interest in」某事，意思是不認同或不喜歡對方喜愛的東西。"},{"en":"A parent may dislike a child’s interest in video games if it affects homework.","zh":"如果電子遊戲影響功課，父母可能不喜歡孩子對它的興趣。"},{"en":"If a family wants practical careers, they may dislike artistic interests.","zh":"如果家庭希望孩子從事實用職業，他們可能不喜歡藝術興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes negative feelings toward another person’s passion.","zh":"這個短語描述對另一個人熱愛之事的負面感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rather introverted","meaning":"相當內向","examples":[{"en":"Alfred’s father found him rather introverted.","zh":"Alfred 的父親覺得他相當內向。"},{"en":"Rather introverted means quite quiet, inward-looking, and less eager to socialise.","zh":"「rather introverted」意思是頗安靜、較內省、不太熱衷社交。"},{"en":"A rather introverted student may prefer reading alone to joining a large party.","zh":"相當內向的學生可能較喜歡獨自閱讀，而不是參加大型派對。"},{"en":"If someone is introverted, they may think deeply but avoid crowded social events.","zh":"如果某人內向，他可能深入思考，但避免擁擠社交活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes personality gently, not as an insult.","zh":"這個短語溫和地描述性格，而不是侮辱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"widen someone’s horizons","meaning":"擴闊某人的眼界","examples":[{"en":"His father sent him abroad to widen his horizons.","zh":"他的父親把他送往外國，以擴闊他的眼界。"},{"en":"To widen someone’s horizons means to help them experience new places, ideas, and ways of thinking.","zh":"「widen someone’s horizons」意思是幫助某人經歷新地方、新想法和新思維方式。"},{"en":"Studying overseas can widen a student’s horizons by exposing them to new cultures.","zh":"海外留學可以讓學生接觸新文化，從而擴闊眼界。"},{"en":"If people travel and learn from others, they may see more possibilities for their future.","zh":"如果人們旅行並向他人學習，他們可能看見更多未來可能性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes expanding knowledge and perspective.","zh":"這個短語描述擴展知識和視野。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"send someone abroad","meaning":"把某人送往外國","examples":[{"en":"Alfred was sent abroad for further technical training.","zh":"Alfred 被送往外國接受進一步技術培訓。"},{"en":"To send someone abroad means to arrange for them to go to another country.","zh":"「send someone abroad」意思是安排某人前往另一個國家。"},{"en":"A company may send an employee abroad for specialist training.","zh":"公司可能把員工送往外國接受專門培訓。"},{"en":"If students are sent abroad, they may learn new skills and become more independent.","zh":"如果學生被送往外國，他們可能學到新技能並變得更獨立。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sending a person overseas for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述為某目的把人送到海外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"further training in","meaning":"……方面的進一步培訓","examples":[{"en":"He received further training in chemical engineering.","zh":"他接受了化學工程方面的進一步培訓。"},{"en":"Further training in something means additional learning after basic education.","zh":"「further training in」某範疇，意思是在基本教育後接受額外學習。"},{"en":"A nurse may receive further training in emergency care.","zh":"護士可能接受急救護理方面的進一步培訓。"},{"en":"If a worker gets further training, they can handle more difficult tasks.","zh":"如果員工接受進一步培訓，他們可以處理更困難任務。"},{"en":"The phrase describes extra education in a specific field.","zh":"這個短語描述特定領域的額外教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"chemical engineering","meaning":"化學工程","examples":[{"en":"Nobel studied chemical engineering in several countries.","zh":"Nobel 在幾個國家學習化學工程。"},{"en":"Chemical engineering is the field that uses chemistry to design industrial processes and materials.","zh":"「chemical engineering」是利用化學來設計工業過程和材料的領域。"},{"en":"A chemical engineering student may learn how to produce fuels, plastics, or medicines safely.","zh":"化學工程學生可能學習如何安全生產燃料、塑膠或藥物。"},{"en":"If chemical engineering is applied well, laboratory ideas can become factory products.","zh":"如果化學工程應用得好，實驗室想法可以變成工廠產品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a practical science-based engineering field.","zh":"這個短語描述一個實用的科學工程領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"during a two-year period","meaning":"在兩年期間","examples":[{"en":"During a two-year period, Nobel travelled through Europe and America.","zh":"在兩年期間，Nobel 遊歷歐洲和美國。"},{"en":"During a two-year period means over the course of two years.","zh":"「during a two-year period」意思是在兩年時間內。"},{"en":"During a two-year period, a student may prepare for exams, apply to university, and learn new skills.","zh":"在兩年期間，學生可能備考、申請大學並學習新技能。"},{"en":"If someone travels widely during two years, they can gain broad experience quickly.","zh":"如果有人在兩年內廣泛旅行，他可以快速獲得豐富經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the length of time in which events happened.","zh":"這個短語提供事件發生的時間長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"private laboratory","meaning":"私人實驗室","examples":[{"en":"In Paris, Nobel worked in the private laboratory of a famous chemist.","zh":"在巴黎，Nobel 在一位著名化學家的私人實驗室工作。"},{"en":"A private laboratory is a research space owned or used by an individual or non-public organisation.","zh":"「private laboratory」是由個人或非公共組織擁有或使用的研究空間。"},{"en":"A company may test new products in a private laboratory before selling them.","zh":"公司可能在私人實驗室測試新產品，然後才出售。"},{"en":"If a scientist works in a well-equipped private laboratory, experiments may progress faster.","zh":"如果科學家在設備完善的私人實驗室工作，實驗可能推進得更快。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a specialised research place outside ordinary classrooms.","zh":"這個短語描述普通課室以外的專門研究場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"famous chemist","meaning":"著名化學家","examples":[{"en":"Professor T. J. Pelouze was a famous chemist in Paris.","zh":"T. J. Pelouze 教授是巴黎一位著名化學家。"},{"en":"A famous chemist is a scientist widely known for work in chemistry.","zh":"「famous chemist」是因化學工作而廣為人知的科學家。"},{"en":"Students may read about a famous chemist who discovered a useful medicine or material.","zh":"學生可能讀到發現有用藥物或材料的著名化學家。"},{"en":"If a young researcher works with a famous chemist, they may gain valuable training.","zh":"如果年輕研究者與著名化學家共事，他可能獲得寶貴訓練。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a well-known expert in chemistry.","zh":"這個短語指出化學領域中的知名專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"come into contact with","meaning":"接觸到……","examples":[{"en":"Nobel came into contact with Ascanio Sobrero and his invention.","zh":"Nobel 接觸到 Ascanio Sobrero 和他的發明。"},{"en":"To come into contact with someone or something means to meet, encounter, or be exposed to them.","zh":"「come into contact with」某人或某物，意思是遇見、接觸或接觸到他們。"},{"en":"A student may come into contact with new ideas during an exchange programme.","zh":"學生可能在交流計劃中接觸到新想法。"},{"en":"If a scientist comes into contact with a new invention, it may influence their later work.","zh":"如果科學家接觸到新發明，它可能影響其後來工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes exposure that can lead to learning or change.","zh":"這個短語描述可能帶來學習或改變的接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"nitroglycerine","meaning":"硝酸甘油","examples":[{"en":"Nitroglycerine is a powerful but highly unstable explosive liquid.","zh":"硝酸甘油是一種威力強大但高度不穩定的爆炸性液體。"},{"en":"Nitroglycerine is a chemical liquid that can explode with great force but is difficult to handle safely.","zh":"「nitroglycerine」是一種能以巨大力量爆炸，但難以安全處理的化學液體。"},{"en":"In a chemistry lesson, nitroglycerine may be discussed as an example of a dangerous explosive.","zh":"在化學課中，硝酸甘油可能被作為危險爆炸物的例子來討論。"},{"en":"If nitroglycerine is exposed to heat or pressure, it may explode unpredictably.","zh":"如果硝酸甘油接觸熱力或壓力，它可能以難以預測的方式爆炸。"},{"en":"The word names the substance Nobel tried to make safer and more practical.","zh":"這個詞指出 Nobel 試圖令其更安全和更實用的物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"highly explosive liquid","meaning":"高爆炸性的液體","examples":[{"en":"Nitroglycerine was a highly explosive liquid.","zh":"硝酸甘油是一種高爆炸性的液體。"},{"en":"A highly explosive liquid is a liquid that can explode very powerfully and easily.","zh":"「highly explosive liquid」是能非常猛烈且容易爆炸的液體。"},{"en":"A laboratory must store highly explosive liquids under strict safety rules.","zh":"實驗室必須在嚴格安全規則下存放高爆炸性液體。"},{"en":"If such a liquid is shaken, heated, or pressured, it may cause serious accidents.","zh":"如果這類液體被搖晃、加熱或施壓，它可能造成嚴重意外。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a substance that is dangerous because of its explosive power.","zh":"這個短語描述因爆炸威力而危險的物質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be considered too dangerous to","meaning":"被認為太危險而不能……","examples":[{"en":"Nitroglycerine was considered too dangerous to use practically.","zh":"硝酸甘油被認為太危險而不能實際使用。"},{"en":"To be considered too dangerous to do something means people judge it unsafe for that use.","zh":"「be considered too dangerous to」做某事，意思是人們判斷它對該用途不安全。"},{"en":"A broken playground slide may be considered too dangerous to use until it is repaired.","zh":"損壞的遊樂場滑梯在維修前可能被認為太危險而不能使用。"},{"en":"If a material explodes unpredictably, workers may refuse to use it on building sites.","zh":"如果材料會難以預測地爆炸，工人可能拒絕在建築地盤使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why a useful idea may not yet be practical.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何有用想法可能尚未實用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be of practical use","meaning":"具實際用途","examples":[{"en":"The substance needed to be made safer before it could be of practical use.","zh":"該物質必須變得更安全，才可以具實際用途。"},{"en":"To be of practical use means to be useful in real situations, not only in theory.","zh":"「be of practical use」意思是在真實情況中有用，而不只是理論上有用。"},{"en":"A classroom idea is of practical use only if teachers can apply it with real students.","zh":"課堂想法只有在老師能用於真實學生時，才具實際用途。"},{"en":"If an invention is too dangerous, it cannot be of practical use until the safety problem is solved.","zh":"如果發明太危險，它在安全問題解決前不能具實際用途。"},{"en":"The phrase describes usefulness in everyday or professional practice.","zh":"這個短語描述在日常或專業實踐中的有用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"explosive power","meaning":"爆炸威力","examples":[{"en":"Nitroglycerine’s explosive power greatly exceeded that of gunpowder.","zh":"硝酸甘油的爆炸威力遠遠超過火藥。"},{"en":"Explosive power is the force or energy released when something explodes.","zh":"「explosive power」是某物爆炸時釋放出的力量或能量。"},{"en":"Fireworks have explosive power, so they must be handled carefully.","zh":"煙花有爆炸威力，因此必須小心處理。"},{"en":"If a substance has great explosive power, it can break rock but also cause danger.","zh":"如果物質有巨大爆炸威力，它可以破碎岩石，但也造成危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the strength of an explosion.","zh":"這個短語描述爆炸的強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"greatly exceed that of","meaning":"遠遠超過……的","examples":[{"en":"The explosive power of nitroglycerine greatly exceeded that of gunpowder.","zh":"硝酸甘油的爆炸威力遠遠超過火藥的威力。"},{"en":"To greatly exceed that of something means to be much greater than the amount or quality of that thing.","zh":"「greatly exceed that of」某物，意思是遠遠高於該物的數量或質素。"},{"en":"The storage space of a new phone may greatly exceed that of an older model.","zh":"新電話的儲存空間可能遠遠超過舊型號。"},{"en":"If one material’s power greatly exceeds another’s, it may be more useful but also more dangerous.","zh":"如果一種材料的威力遠遠超過另一種，它可能更有用，但也更危險。"},{"en":"The phrase is used for strong comparison.","zh":"這個短語用於強烈比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"gunpowder","meaning":"火藥","examples":[{"en":"Nitroglycerine was more powerful than gunpowder.","zh":"硝酸甘油比火藥威力更強。"},{"en":"Gunpowder is an explosive powder traditionally used in guns, fireworks, and blasting.","zh":"「gunpowder」是傳統上用於槍械、煙花和爆破的爆炸性粉末。"},{"en":"A history class may discuss how gunpowder changed warfare and construction.","zh":"歷史課可能討論火藥如何改變戰爭和建築工程。"},{"en":"If a new explosive is stronger than gunpowder, it can do heavier work with less material.","zh":"如果新爆炸物比火藥更強，它可以用較少材料完成更重工作。"},{"en":"The word names an older explosive used as a comparison with nitroglycerine.","zh":"這個詞指出一種較舊爆炸物，用來與硝酸甘油比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in an unpredictable manner","meaning":"以難以預測的方式","examples":[{"en":"The liquid could explode in an unpredictable manner.","zh":"該液體可能以難以預測的方式爆炸。"},{"en":"In an unpredictable manner means in a way that cannot be easily expected or controlled.","zh":"「in an unpredictable manner」意思是以不容易預計或控制的方式。"},{"en":"A damaged lift may stop in an unpredictable manner, so people avoid using it.","zh":"損壞的升降機可能以難以預測的方式停下，因此人們避免使用。"},{"en":"If a chemical reacts unpredictably, workers cannot handle it safely.","zh":"如果化學物質反應難以預測，工人就不能安全處理它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes behaviour that is uncertain and risky.","zh":"這個短語描述不確定且有風險的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be subjected to","meaning":"受到……","examples":[{"en":"Nitroglycerine could explode if subjected to heat or pressure.","zh":"硝酸甘油如果受到熱力或壓力，可能會爆炸。"},{"en":"To be subjected to something means to be exposed to it or made to experience it.","zh":"「be subjected to」某事，意思是暴露於它或被迫經歷它。"},{"en":"A phone subjected to water may stop working.","zh":"電話如果受到水浸，可能停止運作。"},{"en":"If an unstable substance is subjected to pressure, it may react dangerously.","zh":"如果不穩定物質受到壓力，它可能危險地反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes exposure to a condition, often an unpleasant or risky one.","zh":"這個短語描述接觸某種條件，通常是不愉快或有風險的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"heat and pressure","meaning":"熱力與壓力","examples":[{"en":"The explosive was highly sensitive to heat and pressure.","zh":"該爆炸物對熱力與壓力高度敏感。"},{"en":"Heat and pressure are two physical conditions involving high temperature and force.","zh":"「heat and pressure」是涉及高溫和力量的兩種物理條件。"},{"en":"Some foods change texture under heat and pressure in a pressure cooker.","zh":"有些食物在壓力煲中的熱力與壓力下會改變質感。"},{"en":"If an explosive reacts to heat and pressure, storage and transport become dangerous.","zh":"如果爆炸物會對熱力與壓力反應，儲存和運輸就變得危險。"},{"en":"The phrase names conditions that can trigger a chemical reaction.","zh":"這個短語指出可觸發化學反應的條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"put something to practical use","meaning":"將……付諸實際應用","examples":[{"en":"Nobel wanted to put nitroglycerine to practical use in construction.","zh":"Nobel 想將硝酸甘油付諸建築工程中的實際應用。"},{"en":"To put something to practical use means to use an idea or material in real work.","zh":"「put something to practical use」意思是在真實工作中使用某想法或材料。"},{"en":"A student puts grammar to practical use when writing a clear email.","zh":"學生寫出清楚電郵時，就是把文法付諸實際應用。"},{"en":"If a discovery remains only in a laboratory, it has not yet been put to practical use.","zh":"如果發現只停留在實驗室，它就尚未被付諸實際應用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes turning knowledge into real application.","zh":"這個短語描述把知識轉化為真實應用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"safety problems","meaning":"安全問題","examples":[{"en":"Nobel realised that the safety problems had to be solved.","zh":"Nobel 意識到安全問題必須解決。"},{"en":"Safety problems are dangers or risks that may hurt people or damage property.","zh":"「safety problems」是可能傷害人或破壞財物的危險或風險。"},{"en":"A school laboratory has safety problems if chemicals are stored carelessly.","zh":"如果化學品儲存不慎，學校實驗室就有安全問題。"},{"en":"If safety problems are not solved, useful technology may remain unusable.","zh":"如果安全問題沒有解決，有用科技可能仍不能使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes issues that must be fixed before something can be safe.","zh":"這個短語描述某物安全使用前必須修正的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"develop a method for","meaning":"研發……的方法","examples":[{"en":"He sought to develop a method for controlled detonation.","zh":"他試圖研發受控引爆的方法。"},{"en":"To develop a method for something means to create a planned way to do it.","zh":"「develop a method for」某事，意思是創造一套有計劃的方法去完成它。"},{"en":"A teacher may develop a method for helping students remember new vocabulary.","zh":"老師可能研發幫助學生記住新詞彙的方法。"},{"en":"If scientists develop a reliable method, a dangerous process can become safer.","zh":"如果科學家研發出可靠方法，危險過程可以變得更安全。"},{"en":"The phrase describes designing a practical procedure.","zh":"這個短語描述設計實用程序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"controlled detonation","meaning":"受控引爆","examples":[{"en":"A safe explosive requires a reliable method of controlled detonation.","zh":"安全爆炸物需要可靠的受控引爆方法。"},{"en":"Controlled detonation means causing an explosive to explode at the chosen time and place.","zh":"「controlled detonation」意思是在選定時間和地點令爆炸物爆炸。"},{"en":"Engineers use controlled detonation when they need to remove rock without causing wider damage.","zh":"工程師需要移除岩石而不造成更廣泛破壞時，會使用受控引爆。"},{"en":"If detonation is controlled, workers can plan the blast and keep people away.","zh":"如果引爆受控制，工人可以計劃爆破並讓人遠離。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts safe planned explosion with unpredictable explosion.","zh":"這個短語把安全有計劃的爆炸與不可預測爆炸作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"after his return to","meaning":"返回……之後","examples":[{"en":"After his return to Sweden, Nobel continued his experiments.","zh":"返回瑞典之後，Nobel 繼續他的實驗。"},{"en":"After his return to a place means after he came back there.","zh":"「after his return to」某地，意思是他回到那裡之後。"},{"en":"After her return to school, a student may need time to catch up on missed lessons.","zh":"學生返回學校後，可能需要時間追回錯過的課。"},{"en":"If someone continues work after returning home, the earlier trip may have shaped the project.","zh":"如果有人回家後繼續工作，早前旅程可能已塑造該項目。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the time after someone comes back.","zh":"這個短語提供某人回來後的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"concentrate on developing","meaning":"專注研發……","examples":[{"en":"Nobel concentrated on developing nitroglycerine as a usable explosive.","zh":"Nobel 專注研發硝酸甘油，使其成為可用爆炸物。"},{"en":"To concentrate on developing something means to focus attention and effort on improving it.","zh":"「concentrate on developing」某物，意思是集中注意力和努力去改良它。"},{"en":"A student may concentrate on developing speaking skills before an oral exam.","zh":"學生可能在口試前專注發展說話技巧。"},{"en":"If a scientist concentrates on one problem, progress may become faster and deeper.","zh":"如果科學家專注於一個問題，進展可能更快更深入。"},{"en":"The phrase describes focused effort toward improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述集中努力以求改進。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"several explosions","meaning":"多宗爆炸","examples":[{"en":"Several explosions occurred during the early experiments.","zh":"早期實驗期間發生了多宗爆炸。"},{"en":"Several explosions means more than two explosive incidents happened.","zh":"「several explosions」意思是發生了兩次以上爆炸事件。"},{"en":"A factory must close for inspection if several explosions happen in a short time.","zh":"如果工廠短時間內發生多宗爆炸，它必須關閉接受檢查。"},{"en":"If early tests cause repeated explosions, the material is clearly dangerous to handle.","zh":"如果早期測試造成反覆爆炸，該材料顯然很難安全處理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated explosive accidents or events.","zh":"這個短語描述重複發生的爆炸事故或事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"including one in which","meaning":"包括一宗……的事故","examples":[{"en":"One accident, including one in which his brother died, had serious consequences.","zh":"其中一宗事故，包括一宗他弟弟喪生的事故，造成嚴重後果。"},{"en":"Including one in which means giving a specific example where something happened.","zh":"「including one in which」意思是提出一個發生某事的具體例子。"},{"en":"The school had several accidents, including one in which a student broke an arm.","zh":"學校發生了幾宗意外，包括一宗學生手臂骨折的事故。"},{"en":"If one accident involves a death, authorities are likely to act more strictly.","zh":"如果一宗事故涉及死亡，當局很可能採取更嚴格行動。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a serious example within a larger group.","zh":"這個短語在較大群組中引入一個嚴重例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"convince the authorities that","meaning":"令當局相信","examples":[{"en":"The fatal explosion convinced the authorities that production was dangerous.","zh":"致命爆炸令當局相信生產是危險的。"},{"en":"To convince the authorities that something is true means to make officials believe it.","zh":"「convince the authorities that」某事為真，意思是令官方相信它。"},{"en":"Repeated complaints may convince the authorities that a road crossing is unsafe.","zh":"反覆投訴可能令當局相信某個過路處不安全。"},{"en":"If evidence convinces officials of danger, they may ban or restrict the activity.","zh":"如果證據令官員相信有危險，他們可能禁止或限制該活動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes persuading people in power through evidence or events.","zh":"這個短語描述透過證據或事件說服掌權者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"exceedingly dangerous","meaning":"極度危險","examples":[{"en":"The authorities considered nitroglycerine production exceedingly dangerous.","zh":"當局認為硝酸甘油生產極度危險。"},{"en":"Exceedingly dangerous means extremely unsafe and likely to cause serious harm.","zh":"「exceedingly dangerous」意思是極不安全，並很可能造成嚴重傷害。"},{"en":"Driving without brakes would be exceedingly dangerous on a busy road.","zh":"在繁忙道路上駕駛沒有煞車的車會極度危險。"},{"en":"If a process is exceedingly dangerous, officials may forbid it in crowded areas.","zh":"如果某過程極度危險，官員可能禁止它在擠迫地區進行。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly emphasises high risk.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調高風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"forbid further experimentation","meaning":"禁止進一步試驗","examples":[{"en":"The authorities forbade further experimentation within Stockholm.","zh":"當局禁止在斯德哥爾摩市內進一步試驗。"},{"en":"To forbid further experimentation means to officially stop people from doing more tests.","zh":"「forbid further experimentation」意思是正式阻止人們繼續做更多測試。"},{"en":"A school may forbid further experiments if students ignore safety rules in the lab.","zh":"如果學生在實驗室無視安全規則，學校可能禁止進一步實驗。"},{"en":"If tests cause serious accidents, officials may stop them until safer methods exist.","zh":"如果測試造成嚴重事故，官員可能在有更安全方法前停止它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an official ban on continuing experiments.","zh":"這個短語描述對繼續實驗的官方禁令。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"within the city limits","meaning":"在市界範圍內","examples":[{"en":"Explosive experiments were forbidden within the Stockholm city limits.","zh":"爆炸物實驗被禁止在斯德哥爾摩市界範圍內進行。"},{"en":"Within the city limits means inside the official boundary of a city.","zh":"「within the city limits」意思是在城市的正式邊界內。"},{"en":"Fireworks may be banned within the city limits to protect residents.","zh":"為保護居民，煙花可能在市界範圍內被禁止。"},{"en":"If dangerous experiments are moved outside city limits, fewer people may be at risk.","zh":"如果危險實驗移到市界外，較少人可能受風險影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a location inside a city’s legal boundary.","zh":"這個短語描述城市法律邊界內的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"move one’s experimentation to","meaning":"將試驗移到……","examples":[{"en":"Nobel moved his experimentation to a barge on a lake.","zh":"Nobel 將試驗移到湖上的一艘駁船。"},{"en":"To move one’s experimentation to a place means to shift the location where tests are carried out.","zh":"「move one’s experimentation to」某地，意思是轉移進行測試的位置。"},{"en":"A science club may move experiments outdoors if they produce strong smells.","zh":"如果實驗產生強烈氣味，科學學會可能把實驗移到戶外。"},{"en":"If city testing is banned, researchers may move experiments to a safer isolated site.","zh":"如果城市測試被禁止，研究人員可能把實驗移到較安全的偏僻地點。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing the place of research activity.","zh":"這個短語描述改變研究活動的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a barge anchored on","meaning":"停泊在……的駁船","examples":[{"en":"His laboratory was moved to a barge anchored on Lake Malaren.","zh":"他的實驗室被移到停泊在馬拉倫湖上的駁船。"},{"en":"A barge anchored on a lake is a flat boat fixed in place on the water.","zh":"「a barge anchored on」湖，是固定在水上的平底船。"},{"en":"Workers may use a barge anchored on a river as a temporary construction platform.","zh":"工人可能使用停泊在河上的駁船作臨時施工平台。"},{"en":"If dangerous experiments are done on an anchored barge, they are farther from city buildings.","zh":"如果危險實驗在停泊的駁船上進行，它們就離城市建築物較遠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a floating but fixed work location.","zh":"這個短語描述浮在水上但固定的工作地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not be discouraged","meaning":"沒有氣餒","examples":[{"en":"Alfred was not discouraged by the accidents or official restrictions.","zh":"Alfred 沒有因事故或官方限制而氣餒。"},{"en":"To not be discouraged means to continue trying despite difficulties or setbacks.","zh":"「not be discouraged」意思是儘管遇到困難或挫折仍繼續嘗試。"},{"en":"A student was not discouraged by one failed test and kept practising.","zh":"學生沒有因一次測驗不合格而氣餒，並繼續練習。"},{"en":"If inventors are not discouraged by early failure, they may eventually solve the problem.","zh":"如果發明家不因早期失敗而氣餒，他們最終可能解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes persistence after disappointment.","zh":"這個短語描述失望後仍然堅持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"start mass production","meaning":"開始大量生產","examples":[{"en":"Nobel was able to start mass production of nitroglycerine.","zh":"Nobel 能夠開始大量生產硝酸甘油。"},{"en":"To start mass production means to begin making a product in large quantities.","zh":"「start mass production」意思是開始大量製造某產品。"},{"en":"A company may start mass production after a prototype has passed safety tests.","zh":"原型通過安全測試後，公司可能開始大量生產。"},{"en":"If mass production begins, the product can reach more customers and industries.","zh":"如果大量生產開始，產品可以接觸更多顧客和行業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes moving from experiment to large-scale manufacturing.","zh":"這個短語描述從實驗走向大規模製造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mass production","meaning":"大量生產","examples":[{"en":"The invention eventually made mass production possible.","zh":"該發明最終使大量生產成為可能。"},{"en":"Mass production is the process of making large numbers of the same product.","zh":"「mass production」是大量製造相同產品的過程。"},{"en":"Factories use mass production to make phones, clothes, and household items quickly.","zh":"工廠使用大量生產快速製造電話、衣物和家居用品。"},{"en":"If mass production lowers costs, more people can buy the product.","zh":"如果大量生產降低成本，更多人就能購買該產品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes large-scale repeated manufacturing.","zh":"這個短語描述大規模重複製造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"handling of","meaning":"……的處理","examples":[{"en":"Nobel wanted to make the handling of nitroglycerine safer.","zh":"Nobel 想令硝酸甘油的處理更安全。"},{"en":"The handling of something means the way it is carried, used, stored, or managed.","zh":"「handling of」某物，意思是搬運、使用、儲存或管理它的方式。"},{"en":"The handling of hot food in a kitchen requires gloves and care.","zh":"廚房中處理熱食需要手套和小心。"},{"en":"If the handling of a dangerous chemical improves, accidents may decrease.","zh":"如果危險化學品的處理改善，事故可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on safe practical treatment of an object or substance.","zh":"這個短語集中於對物件或物質的安全實際處理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"experiment with additives","meaning":"試驗不同添加劑","examples":[{"en":"He experimented with different additives to stabilise the liquid.","zh":"他試驗不同添加劑來穩定該液體。"},{"en":"To experiment with additives means to test extra substances added to change a material’s properties.","zh":"「experiment with additives」意思是測試加入的額外物質，以改變材料特性。"},{"en":"A food scientist may experiment with additives to keep bread soft for longer.","zh":"食品科學家可能試驗添加劑，以令麵包更長時間保持柔軟。"},{"en":"If the right additive is found, a dangerous liquid may become easier to handle.","zh":"如果找到合適添加劑，危險液體可能變得更容易處理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes testing added materials for a practical effect.","zh":"這個短語描述為實際效果而測試加入材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mix something with","meaning":"將……與……混合","examples":[{"en":"Nobel mixed nitroglycerine with kieselguhr.","zh":"Nobel 將硝酸甘油與矽藻土混合。"},{"en":"To mix something with another substance means to combine them together.","zh":"「mix something with」另一物質，意思是把兩者結合在一起。"},{"en":"A cook may mix flour with water to make dough.","zh":"廚師可能將麵粉與水混合來製作麵糰。"},{"en":"If a liquid explosive is mixed with an absorbent material, it may become more stable.","zh":"如果液體爆炸物與吸收性材料混合，它可能變得更穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase describes combining materials to change the result.","zh":"這個短語描述結合材料以改變結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"kieselguhr","meaning":"矽藻土","examples":[{"en":"Kieselguhr absorbed nitroglycerine and helped form a stable paste.","zh":"矽藻土吸收硝酸甘油，並幫助形成穩定糊狀物。"},{"en":"Kieselguhr is a porous earth-like material that can absorb liquid.","zh":"「kieselguhr」是一種多孔、類似泥土並能吸收液體的材料。"},{"en":"A laboratory might use an absorbent material to soak up a spill safely.","zh":"實驗室可能使用吸收性材料安全吸收濺出的液體。"},{"en":"If kieselguhr absorbs nitroglycerine, the explosive becomes easier to shape and handle.","zh":"如果矽藻土吸收硝酸甘油，爆炸物會變得更容易塑形和處理。"},{"en":"The word names the material that helped Nobel make dynamite safer.","zh":"這個詞指出幫助 Nobel 令炸藥更安全的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"turn the liquid into a paste","meaning":"將液體變成糊狀物","examples":[{"en":"Mixing it with kieselguhr turned the liquid into a paste.","zh":"將它與矽藻土混合，把該液體變成糊狀物。"},{"en":"To turn the liquid into a paste means to change it from a flowing liquid into a thick, soft substance.","zh":"「turn the liquid into a paste」意思是把流動液體變成濃稠柔軟的物質。"},{"en":"A cook can turn cooked beans into a paste by crushing them.","zh":"廚師可以透過壓碎熟豆，把它們變成糊狀物。"},{"en":"If an explosive liquid becomes a paste, it may be easier to shape safely.","zh":"如果爆炸性液體變成糊狀物，它可能更容易安全塑形。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change in physical form.","zh":"這個短語描述物理形態的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be shaped into rods","meaning":"可被製成棒狀","examples":[{"en":"The paste could be shaped into rods.","zh":"該糊狀物可被製成棒狀。"},{"en":"To be shaped into rods means to be formed into long straight pieces.","zh":"「be shaped into rods」意思是被製成長而直的條狀物。"},{"en":"Clay can be shaped into rods before children use it for a craft project.","zh":"黏土可以先被製成棒狀，然後孩子用它做手工。"},{"en":"If explosive paste is shaped into rods, workers can insert it into narrow holes.","zh":"如果爆炸糊狀物被製成棒狀，工人就能把它插入狹窄孔洞。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a material into a useful physical form.","zh":"這個短語描述把材料製成有用的物理形態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"suitable for insertion into","meaning":"適合插入……","examples":[{"en":"The rods were suitable for insertion into drilling holes.","zh":"這些棒狀物適合插入鑽孔。"},{"en":"Suitable for insertion into something means the shape or size fits well enough to be put inside it.","zh":"「suitable for insertion into」某物，意思是形狀或大小適合放入其中。"},{"en":"A key must be suitable for insertion into the lock before it can open the door.","zh":"鑰匙必須適合插入鎖中，才能開門。"},{"en":"If rods fit into drilling holes, controlled blasting becomes easier to arrange.","zh":"如果棒狀物能放入鑽孔，受控爆破就更容易安排。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical fitness for being placed inside something.","zh":"這個短語描述適合被放入某物內的物理配合。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"drilling holes","meaning":"鑽孔","examples":[{"en":"Workers placed dynamite rods into drilling holes.","zh":"工人把炸藥棒放入鑽孔中。"},{"en":"Drilling holes are holes made by a drill, often in rock, wood, metal, or concrete.","zh":"「drilling holes」是由鑽機在岩石、木材、金屬或混凝土中鑽出的孔。"},{"en":"A worker may make drilling holes before fixing shelves to a wall.","zh":"工人固定層架到牆上前，可能先鑽孔。"},{"en":"If holes are drilled into rock, explosives can be placed inside for controlled blasting.","zh":"如果在岩石中鑽孔，爆炸物可以放入其中作受控爆破。"},{"en":"The phrase names prepared holes used in construction or repair.","zh":"這個短語指出建築或維修中預先鑽出的孔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"patent a material","meaning":"為材料取得專利","examples":[{"en":"Nobel patented the new explosive material in 1867.","zh":"Nobel 於1867年為這種新爆炸材料取得專利。"},{"en":"To patent a material means to obtain legal protection for an invention involving that material.","zh":"「patent a material」意思是為涉及該材料的發明取得法律保護。"},{"en":"A company may patent a new medical material before selling it worldwide.","zh":"公司可能在全球銷售新醫療材料前為它取得專利。"},{"en":"If an inventor patents a material, others cannot freely copy and sell it.","zh":"如果發明家為材料取得專利，其他人就不能隨意複製和出售它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes protecting an invention through law.","zh":"這個短語描述透過法律保護發明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"under the name","meaning":"以……的名稱","examples":[{"en":"He patented the substance under the name dynamite.","zh":"他以「dynamite」的名稱為該物質取得專利。"},{"en":"Under the name means using a particular official or public name.","zh":"「under the name」意思是使用某個正式或公開名稱。"},{"en":"A writer may publish stories under the name of a pen name.","zh":"作家可能以筆名出版故事。"},{"en":"If a product is sold under a memorable name, customers may recognise it more easily.","zh":"如果產品以易記名稱出售，顧客可能更容易認出它。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the name used for something.","zh":"這個短語引入某物所使用的名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dynamite","meaning":"炸藥","examples":[{"en":"Dynamite made controlled blasting safer and more practical.","zh":"炸藥令受控爆破更安全、更實用。"},{"en":"Dynamite is an explosive invented by Nobel by making nitroglycerine easier to handle.","zh":"「dynamite」是 Nobel 發明的爆炸物，透過令硝酸甘油更易處理而成。"},{"en":"Engineers once used dynamite to break rock for tunnels, roads, and canals.","zh":"工程師曾使用炸藥破碎岩石，以建造隧道、道路和運河。"},{"en":"If dynamite can be detonated reliably, construction work becomes faster and safer than using unstable liquid.","zh":"如果炸藥能可靠引爆，建築工程會比使用不穩定液體更快、更安全。"},{"en":"The word names Nobel’s famous explosive invention.","zh":"這個詞指出 Nobel 著名的爆炸物發明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"detonate dynamite rods","meaning":"引爆炸藥棒","examples":[{"en":"A detonator was required to detonate the dynamite rods.","zh":"引爆炸藥棒需要雷管。"},{"en":"To detonate dynamite rods means to cause the sticks of dynamite to explode.","zh":"「detonate dynamite rods」意思是使炸藥棒爆炸。"},{"en":"Only trained workers should detonate explosives on a construction site.","zh":"只有受訓工人才應在建築地盤引爆爆炸物。"},{"en":"If dynamite rods are detonated at the right time, rock can be broken in a controlled way.","zh":"如果炸藥棒在正確時間被引爆，岩石可以以受控方式被破碎。"},{"en":"The phrase describes setting off shaped explosive material.","zh":"這個短語描述引爆成形爆炸材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"detonator","meaning":"雷管；引爆器","examples":[{"en":"Nobel invented a detonator for setting off dynamite.","zh":"Nobel 發明了用來引爆炸藥的雷管。"},{"en":"A detonator is a device used to start an explosion.","zh":"「detonator」是用來引發爆炸的裝置。"},{"en":"In controlled blasting, a detonator must work reliably so the timing is safe.","zh":"在受控爆破中，雷管必須可靠運作，時間安排才安全。"},{"en":"If a detonator fails, the explosive may remain dangerous and unstable.","zh":"如果雷管失效，爆炸物可能仍然危險且不穩定。"},{"en":"The word names the device that triggers an explosive charge.","zh":"這個詞指出觸發爆炸裝藥的裝置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"blasting cap","meaning":"雷管","examples":[{"en":"A blasting cap initiates the explosion of dynamite.","zh":"雷管啟動炸藥的爆炸。"},{"en":"A blasting cap is a small explosive device used to set off a larger explosive.","zh":"「blasting cap」是用來引爆較大爆炸物的小型爆炸裝置。"},{"en":"Construction workers handle blasting caps under strict safety procedures.","zh":"建築工人在嚴格安全程序下處理雷管。"},{"en":"If a blasting cap is ignited, it can trigger the main explosive charge.","zh":"如果雷管被點燃，它可以觸發主要爆炸裝藥。"},{"en":"The phrase names a small but important part of controlled blasting.","zh":"這個短語指出受控爆破中細小但重要的部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be ignited by","meaning":"由……點燃","examples":[{"en":"The blasting cap could be ignited by lighting a fuse.","zh":"雷管可以由點燃導火線來引燃。"},{"en":"To be ignited by something means to be set on fire or activated by it.","zh":"「be ignited by」某物，意思是由它點着或啟動。"},{"en":"A candle is ignited by a match.","zh":"蠟燭由火柴點燃。"},{"en":"If a fuse ignites a blasting cap, the cap can start the explosive reaction.","zh":"如果導火線點燃雷管，雷管可以開始爆炸反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes what causes burning or detonation to begin.","zh":"這個短語描述甚麼引起燃燒或引爆開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"light a fuse","meaning":"點燃導火線","examples":[{"en":"A worker could detonate the explosive by lighting a fuse.","zh":"工人可以透過點燃導火線引爆爆炸物。"},{"en":"To light a fuse means to set fire to the cord or material that leads to an explosion or firework.","zh":"「light a fuse」意思是點燃連接爆炸物或煙花的線或材料。"},{"en":"Fireworks should only be used by adults who know how to light a fuse safely.","zh":"煙花只應由懂得安全點燃導火線的成年人使用。"},{"en":"If a fuse is lit, people must move away before the explosive goes off.","zh":"如果導火線被點燃，人們必須在爆炸物爆炸前離開。"},{"en":"The phrase describes starting a delayed ignition process.","zh":"這個短語描述開始延遲引燃過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pneumatic drill","meaning":"風動鑽；氣動鑽","examples":[{"en":"The pneumatic drill came into general use at around the same time.","zh":"風動鑽大約在同一時期開始普及使用。"},{"en":"A pneumatic drill is a powerful drilling tool operated by compressed air.","zh":"「pneumatic drill」是由壓縮空氣驅動的強力鑽孔工具。"},{"en":"Road workers may use a pneumatic drill to break hard concrete.","zh":"道路工人可能使用風動鑽破碎硬混凝土。"},{"en":"If workers use pneumatic drills with explosives, tunnels can be made more efficiently.","zh":"如果工人把風動鑽與爆炸物一起使用，隧道可以更有效率地建成。"},{"en":"The phrase names a tool that helped modern construction.","zh":"這個短語指出幫助現代建築的工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"come into general use","meaning":"開始普及使用","examples":[{"en":"The pneumatic drill soon came into general use.","zh":"風動鑽很快開始普及使用。"},{"en":"To come into general use means to become widely used by many people or industries.","zh":"「come into general use」意思是被許多人或行業廣泛使用。"},{"en":"Online payment came into general use when shops and customers found it convenient.","zh":"當商店和顧客覺得網上付款方便，它就開始普及使用。"},{"en":"If a tool saves time and money, it may quickly come into general use.","zh":"如果工具節省時間和金錢，它可能很快開始普及。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a change from limited use to common use.","zh":"這個短語描述由有限使用轉為普遍使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"drastically reduce the cost of","meaning":"大幅降低……的成本","examples":[{"en":"These inventions drastically reduced the cost of construction work.","zh":"這些發明大幅降低了建築工程成本。"},{"en":"To drastically reduce the cost of something means to make it much cheaper.","zh":"「drastically reduce the cost of」某事，意思是令其成本大幅下降。"},{"en":"Shared textbooks can drastically reduce the cost of learning materials for families.","zh":"共用課本可以大幅降低家庭的學習材料成本。"},{"en":"If technology cuts labour time, the total cost of a project may fall sharply.","zh":"如果科技減少勞動時間，項目總成本可能急劇下降。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a large decrease in expense.","zh":"這個短語描述開支大幅減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"drill tunnels","meaning":"鑽挖隧道","examples":[{"en":"Dynamite and pneumatic drills made it cheaper to drill tunnels.","zh":"炸藥和風動鑽令鑽挖隧道更便宜。"},{"en":"To drill tunnels means to cut or bore long passages through rock or earth.","zh":"「drill tunnels」意思是在岩石或泥土中鑽挖長通道。"},{"en":"Engineers drill tunnels for trains, roads, water pipes, and underground cables.","zh":"工程師為火車、道路、水管和地下電纜鑽挖隧道。"},{"en":"If tunnel drilling becomes cheaper, transport and infrastructure can expand faster.","zh":"如果隧道鑽挖變得更便宜，交通和基建可以更快擴展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making underground passages by machinery and engineering methods.","zh":"這個短語描述透過機械和工程方法製造地下通道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"build canals","meaning":"興建運河","examples":[{"en":"The inventions reduced the cost of building canals.","zh":"這些發明降低了興建運河的成本。"},{"en":"To build canals means to construct artificial waterways for boats, irrigation, or transport.","zh":"「build canals」意思是建造供船隻、灌溉或運輸使用的人工水道。"},{"en":"A government may build canals to move water to dry farming areas.","zh":"政府可能興建運河，把水輸送到乾旱農區。"},{"en":"If canal construction becomes cheaper, trade and farming may improve.","zh":"如果運河建設變得更便宜，貿易和農業可能改善。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating man-made water routes.","zh":"這個短語描述創造人工水路。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the market for","meaning":"……的市場","examples":[{"en":"The market for dynamite and detonating caps grew rapidly.","zh":"炸藥和雷管的市場迅速增長。"},{"en":"The market for something means demand from buyers who want that product or service.","zh":"「the market for」某物，意思是想購買該產品或服務的買家需求。"},{"en":"The market for online lessons grew when students needed flexible study options.","zh":"當學生需要彈性學習選項，網上課程市場增長。"},{"en":"If a product saves money in construction, the market for it can expand quickly.","zh":"如果產品能在建築中省錢，其市場可以快速擴大。"},{"en":"The phrase describes commercial demand.","zh":"這個短語描述商業需求。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"grow very rapidly","meaning":"增長得非常迅速","examples":[{"en":"Demand for Nobel’s inventions grew very rapidly.","zh":"對 Nobel 發明的需求增長得非常迅速。"},{"en":"To grow very rapidly means to increase quickly in size, number, or demand.","zh":"「grow very rapidly」意思是在規模、數量或需求上快速增加。"},{"en":"A new tutoring centre may grow very rapidly if many parents recommend it.","zh":"如果許多家長推薦，新補習中心可能增長得非常迅速。"},{"en":"If a product solves an urgent problem, demand can rise in a short time.","zh":"如果產品解決緊急問題，需求可以在短時間內上升。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses fast growth.","zh":"這個短語強調快速增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prove oneself to be","meaning":"證明自己是……","examples":[{"en":"Nobel proved himself to be a skilful entrepreneur.","zh":"Nobel 證明自己是一位精明能幹的企業家。"},{"en":"To prove oneself to be something means to show through actions that one has that quality or ability.","zh":"「prove oneself to be」某種人，意思是透過行動顯示自己具有該特質或能力。"},{"en":"A student may prove herself to be a strong leader by organising a difficult event calmly.","zh":"學生可能透過冷靜組織困難活動，證明自己是強大的領袖。"},{"en":"If an inventor builds successful businesses, he proves he can do more than invent.","zh":"如果發明家建立成功生意，他證明自己不只是會發明。"},{"en":"The phrase describes demonstrating ability through results.","zh":"這個短語描述透過結果展示能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"skilful entrepreneur","meaning":"精明能幹的企業家","examples":[{"en":"Nobel was a skilful entrepreneur as well as an inventor.","zh":"Nobel 既是發明家，也是一位精明能幹的企業家。"},{"en":"A skilful entrepreneur is a businessperson who can identify opportunities and build successful ventures.","zh":"「skilful entrepreneur」是能識別機會並建立成功企業的商人。"},{"en":"A skilful entrepreneur may turn a small idea into a useful product and a profitable company.","zh":"精明企業家可能把小想法變成有用產品和有利可圖的公司。"},{"en":"If an inventor is also entrepreneurial, the invention may reach the market faster.","zh":"如果發明家也具企業家精神，發明可能更快進入市場。"},{"en":"The phrase describes business ability, not only scientific talent.","zh":"這個短語描述商業能力，而不只是科學才華。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"over the years","meaning":"多年來","examples":[{"en":"Over the years, Nobel founded factories in many countries.","zh":"多年來，Nobel 在許多國家創辦工廠。"},{"en":"Over the years means during a long period of time.","zh":"「over the years」意思是在很長一段時間內。"},{"en":"Over the years, a teacher may develop better explanations for difficult grammar points.","zh":"多年來，老師可能為困難文法點發展出更好的解釋。"},{"en":"If a business expands over the years, it may move from one city to many countries.","zh":"如果生意多年來擴展，它可能由一個城市走向許多國家。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual development across time.","zh":"這個短語描述跨時間的逐步發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"found factories and laboratories","meaning":"創辦工廠和實驗室","examples":[{"en":"Nobel founded factories and laboratories around the world.","zh":"Nobel 在世界各地創辦工廠和實驗室。"},{"en":"To found factories and laboratories means to establish places for manufacturing and research.","zh":"「found factories and laboratories」意思是建立製造和研究場所。"},{"en":"A technology company may found laboratories to test new materials before building factories.","zh":"科技公司可能先創辦實驗室測試新材料，再建立工廠。"},{"en":"If a business has both factories and labs, it can produce goods and improve them.","zh":"如果企業同時有工廠和實驗室，它可以生產貨品並改良它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating a network for production and innovation.","zh":"這個短語描述建立生產和創新網絡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in more than 20 countries","meaning":"在二十多個國家","examples":[{"en":"His businesses operated in more than 20 countries.","zh":"他的業務在二十多個國家營運。"},{"en":"In more than 20 countries means across at least twenty-one nations.","zh":"「in more than 20 countries」意思是在至少二十一個國家。"},{"en":"A large charity may work in more than 20 countries after many years of growth.","zh":"大型慈善機構多年發展後，可能在二十多個國家工作。"},{"en":"If a company operates in many countries, it must manage languages, laws, and markets.","zh":"如果公司在許多國家營運，它必須管理語言、法律和市場。"},{"en":"The phrase shows wide international reach.","zh":"這個短語顯示廣泛國際覆蓋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"live much of one’s life in","meaning":"一生大部分時間居於……","examples":[{"en":"Nobel lived much of his life in Paris.","zh":"Nobel 一生大部分時間居於巴黎。"},{"en":"To live much of one’s life in a place means to spend a large part of one’s lifetime there.","zh":"「live much of one’s life in」某地，意思是把人生大部分時間花在那裡生活。"},{"en":"A writer may live much of her life in a small town and use it as a setting in novels.","zh":"作家可能一生大部分時間住在小鎮，並把它用作小說背景。"},{"en":"If someone lives abroad for many years, that place may shape their friendships and work.","zh":"如果某人在海外生活多年，那個地方可能塑造其友誼和工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes where a person spent a major part of life.","zh":"這個短語描述某人一生主要居住地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be constantly travelling","meaning":"經常四處奔波","examples":[{"en":"Despite living in Paris, he was constantly travelling.","zh":"儘管居於巴黎，他仍經常四處奔波。"},{"en":"To be constantly travelling means to travel very often, with little time staying in one place.","zh":"「be constantly travelling」意思是經常旅行，很少長時間停留在一地。"},{"en":"A regional manager may be constantly travelling between offices.","zh":"區域經理可能經常在各辦公室之間奔波。"},{"en":"If someone travels constantly for work, private life may become difficult to maintain.","zh":"如果某人因工作經常四處奔波，私生活可能難以維持。"},{"en":"The phrase describes frequent movement from place to place.","zh":"這個短語描述頻繁從一地移到另一地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"engage in business activities","meaning":"從事商業活動","examples":[{"en":"Nobel travelled frequently to engage in business activities.","zh":"Nobel 經常旅行以從事商業活動。"},{"en":"To engage in business activities means to take part in commercial work such as meetings, sales, production, or investment.","zh":"「engage in business activities」意思是參與會議、銷售、生產或投資等商業工作。"},{"en":"A shop owner may engage in business activities by negotiating with suppliers.","zh":"店主可能透過與供應商談判來從事商業活動。"},{"en":"If someone travels to engage in business, work demands may reduce their personal time.","zh":"如果有人為從事商業活動而旅行，工作需求可能減少其私人時間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active involvement in business.","zh":"這個短語描述積極參與商業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"work intensively","meaning":"密集地工作","examples":[{"en":"He worked intensively in his various laboratories.","zh":"他在多所實驗室密集地工作。"},{"en":"To work intensively means to work with great focus, effort, and energy.","zh":"「work intensively」意思是高度專注、努力而投入地工作。"},{"en":"Students may work intensively before final exams, revising for many hours each day.","zh":"學生可能在期末考試前密集地溫習，每天溫習很多小時。"},{"en":"If a scientist works intensively, progress may be fast but exhaustion can build up.","zh":"如果科學家密集地工作，進展可能很快，但疲憊也會累積。"},{"en":"The phrase describes concentrated and demanding work.","zh":"這個短語描述集中而吃力的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"various laboratories","meaning":"多所實驗室","examples":[{"en":"Nobel carried out research in various laboratories.","zh":"Nobel 在多所實驗室進行研究。"},{"en":"Various laboratories means several different research spaces or labs.","zh":"「various laboratories」意思是幾個不同研究空間或實驗室。"},{"en":"A medical researcher may test samples in various laboratories before confirming results.","zh":"醫學研究員可能在多所實驗室測試樣本，然後確認結果。"},{"en":"If experiments are carried out in different labs, the researcher can compare equipment and conditions.","zh":"如果實驗在不同實驗室進行，研究員可以比較設備和條件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes more than one place of scientific work.","zh":"這個短語描述不止一個科學工作場所。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"focus on the development of","meaning":"專注於……的發展","examples":[{"en":"He focused on the development of explosives technology.","zh":"他專注於爆炸物技術的發展。"},{"en":"To focus on the development of something means to concentrate on improving or advancing it.","zh":"「focus on the development of」某事，意思是集中於改良或推進它。"},{"en":"A school may focus on the development of students’ writing skills for a whole term.","zh":"學校可能整個學期專注於學生寫作能力的發展。"},{"en":"If researchers focus on one technology, they may make deeper progress in that area.","zh":"如果研究人員專注於一項技術，他們可能在該領域取得更深入進展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes concentrated attention on progress.","zh":"這個短語描述對進步的集中注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"explosives technology","meaning":"爆炸物技術","examples":[{"en":"Nobel made major advances in explosives technology.","zh":"Nobel 在爆炸物技術方面取得重大進展。"},{"en":"Explosives technology is the science and engineering of making, controlling, and using explosive materials.","zh":"「explosives technology」是製造、控制和使用爆炸材料的科學與工程。"},{"en":"Mining and tunnelling depend on safe explosives technology when rock must be broken.","zh":"採礦和挖隧道需要破碎岩石時，依賴安全的爆炸物技術。"},{"en":"If explosives technology becomes safer, construction can be faster with fewer accidents.","zh":"如果爆炸物技術變得更安全，建築可以更快且事故更少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a technical field involving powerful and risky materials.","zh":"這個短語描述涉及強大而有風險材料的技術領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"chemical inventions","meaning":"化學發明","examples":[{"en":"His work also included several chemical inventions.","zh":"他的工作也包括幾項化學發明。"},{"en":"Chemical inventions are new products, materials, or processes created through chemistry.","zh":"「chemical inventions」是透過化學創造的新產品、材料或過程。"},{"en":"A new waterproof coating can be a chemical invention if it is made by a new formula.","zh":"如果新防水塗層由新配方製成，它可以是一項化學發明。"},{"en":"If chemical inventions solve practical problems, they may become valuable industries.","zh":"如果化學發明解決實際問題，它們可能成為有價值的產業。"},{"en":"The phrase describes inventions based on chemical knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述基於化學知識的發明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"synthetic rubber","meaning":"合成橡膠","examples":[{"en":"Nobel experimented with materials such as synthetic rubber.","zh":"Nobel 試驗合成橡膠等材料。"},{"en":"Synthetic rubber is rubber-like material made artificially rather than taken directly from natural rubber trees.","zh":"「synthetic rubber」是人工製造、類似橡膠而不是直接取自天然橡膠樹的材料。"},{"en":"Car tyres and machine parts may use synthetic rubber because it can be designed for strength.","zh":"汽車輪胎和機械零件可能使用合成橡膠，因為它可按強度設計。"},{"en":"If natural rubber is scarce, synthetic rubber can become an important substitute.","zh":"如果天然橡膠短缺，合成橡膠可以成為重要替代品。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a man-made material with rubber-like properties.","zh":"這個短語描述具有橡膠特性的人造材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"artificial silk","meaning":"人造絲","examples":[{"en":"Artificial silk was among the materials that interested Nobel.","zh":"人造絲是 Nobel 感興趣的材料之一。"},{"en":"Artificial silk is a man-made fibre designed to look or feel like natural silk.","zh":"「artificial silk」是設計成看起來或摸起來像天然絲綢的人造纖維。"},{"en":"Clothing factories may use artificial silk to make shiny fabric at lower cost.","zh":"服裝廠可能使用人造絲，以較低成本製作有光澤布料。"},{"en":"If artificial silk is cheaper than natural silk, more people can buy silk-like clothing.","zh":"如果人造絲比天然絲綢便宜，更多人就能購買類似絲綢的衣物。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a manufactured substitute for silk.","zh":"這個短語描述絲綢的人造替代品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"by the time of one’s death","meaning":"到某人去世時","examples":[{"en":"By the time of his death, Nobel held hundreds of patents.","zh":"到 Nobel 去世時，他擁有數百項專利。"},{"en":"By the time of one’s death means before or at the point when that person died.","zh":"「by the time of one’s death」意思是在某人去世之前或去世時。"},{"en":"By the time of her death, the teacher had influenced thousands of students.","zh":"到那位老師去世時，她已影響數以千計學生。"},{"en":"If someone has achieved much by the time of death, their legacy may be remembered for generations.","zh":"如果有人到去世時已取得許多成就，他的遺產可能被幾代人記住。"},{"en":"The phrase looks back at a whole life up to its end.","zh":"這個短語回顧一生直到終結。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hold 355 patents","meaning":"擁有355項專利","examples":[{"en":"Nobel held 355 patents by the time he died.","zh":"Nobel 去世時擁有355項專利。"},{"en":"To hold 355 patents means to legally own rights to 355 inventions or technical ideas.","zh":"「hold 355 patents」意思是合法擁有355項發明或技術想法的權利。"},{"en":"A modern company may hold many patents for phone designs, software, and materials.","zh":"現代公司可能擁有許多電話設計、軟件和材料專利。"},{"en":"If an inventor holds many patents, it shows long-term creativity and technical work.","zh":"如果發明家擁有許多專利，這顯示長期創意和技術工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes legal ownership of many inventions.","zh":"這個短語描述對許多發明的法律擁有權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"intensive work and travel","meaning":"密集工作與奔波","examples":[{"en":"Intensive work and travel left Nobel little time for private life.","zh":"密集工作與奔波令 Nobel 幾乎沒有時間過私生活。"},{"en":"Intensive work and travel means demanding labour combined with frequent movement between places.","zh":"「intensive work and travel」意思是高強度工作加上頻繁往返不同地方。"},{"en":"A consultant’s intensive work and travel may leave little time for family meals.","zh":"顧問的密集工作與奔波可能令他幾乎沒有時間與家人吃飯。"},{"en":"If someone works hard and travels constantly, rest and relationships may suffer.","zh":"如果有人努力工作又經常旅行，休息和人際關係可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a busy lifestyle with heavy pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述壓力很大的忙碌生活方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"leave little time for","meaning":"幾乎沒有時間做……","examples":[{"en":"His demanding career left little time for private life.","zh":"他要求很高的事業令他幾乎沒有時間過私生活。"},{"en":"To leave little time for something means to make it difficult to spend much time on it.","zh":"「leave little time for」某事，意思是令某人難以花很多時間在該事上。"},{"en":"Long commuting can leave little time for exercise after work.","zh":"長時間通勤可能令下班後幾乎沒有時間做運動。"},{"en":"If a job leaves little time for rest, health and relationships may suffer.","zh":"如果工作令人幾乎沒有時間休息，健康和人際關係可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how one demand reduces time for another part of life.","zh":"這個短語描述一種需求如何減少生活中另一部分的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"private life","meaning":"私生活","examples":[{"en":"Nobel’s private life received less attention than his scientific work.","zh":"Nobel 的私生活比他的科學工作受到較少關注。"},{"en":"Private life means a person’s personal relationships, home life, and activities outside public work.","zh":"「private life」指一個人的個人關係、家庭生活和公開工作以外的活動。"},{"en":"A famous actor may protect his private life by avoiding unnecessary interviews.","zh":"著名演員可能透過避免不必要訪問來保護私生活。"},{"en":"If work fills every day, private life can become limited or lonely.","zh":"如果工作佔滿每天，私生活可能變得有限或孤獨。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts personal life with public career.","zh":"這個短語把個人生活與公開事業作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"feel like an old man","meaning":"覺得自己像個老人","examples":[{"en":"At 43, Nobel already felt like an old man.","zh":"43歲時，Nobel 已覺得自己像個老人。"},{"en":"To feel like an old man means to feel tired, worn out, or older than one’s actual age.","zh":"「feel like an old man」意思是感到疲累、耗盡，或比實際年齡老。"},{"en":"After a week of poor sleep, a student may say he feels like an old man.","zh":"一星期睡眠不足後，學生可能說自己像個老人。"},{"en":"If work and travel are exhausting, even a middle-aged person may feel old.","zh":"如果工作和奔波令人疲憊，即使中年人也可能感覺老了。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a feeling of physical or emotional tiredness.","zh":"這個短語描述身體或情緒上的疲憊感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"advertise in a newspaper","meaning":"在報章刊登廣告","examples":[{"en":"Nobel advertised in a newspaper for a secretary.","zh":"Nobel 在報章刊登廣告招聘秘書。"},{"en":"To advertise in a newspaper means to place a notice in a printed paper to find, sell, or announce something.","zh":"「advertise in a newspaper」意思是在印刷報章上刊登通知，以尋找、出售或宣布某事。"},{"en":"A small shop may advertise in a local newspaper for part-time workers.","zh":"小店可能在本地報章刊登廣告招聘兼職員工。"},{"en":"If someone needs staff before online platforms exist, newspaper adverts can reach many readers.","zh":"如果有人在網上平台出現前需要員工，報章廣告可以接觸許多讀者。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a traditional way of public announcement.","zh":"這個短語描述傳統公開公告方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"highly educated","meaning":"受過高等教育的","examples":[{"en":"He described himself as a wealthy, highly educated gentleman.","zh":"他形容自己是一位富有、受過高等教育的紳士。"},{"en":"Highly educated means having received a great deal of formal learning or advanced education.","zh":"「highly educated」意思是接受了大量正式學習或高等教育。"},{"en":"A highly educated applicant may speak several languages and understand specialist subjects.","zh":"受過高等教育的申請人可能會說幾種語言並理解專門科目。"},{"en":"If someone is highly educated, they may have more choices in professional work.","zh":"如果有人受過高等教育，他在專業工作中可能有更多選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase describes educational background, not necessarily wisdom or kindness.","zh":"這個短語描述教育背景，而不一定是智慧或善良。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a lady of mature age","meaning":"成熟女士","examples":[{"en":"The advertisement sought a lady of mature age.","zh":"該廣告尋找一位成熟女士。"},{"en":"A lady of mature age means an adult woman who is no longer very young and is expected to be responsible.","zh":"「a lady of mature age」意思是不再非常年輕、並被期望負責任的成年女性。"},{"en":"In an old-fashioned advert, an employer might ask for a lady of mature age to manage a household.","zh":"在舊式廣告中，僱主可能要求成熟女士管理家務。"},{"en":"If a job requires discretion and experience, the employer may prefer an older applicant.","zh":"如果工作需要謹慎和經驗，僱主可能較喜歡年長申請人。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds formal and old-fashioned today.","zh":"這個短語在今天聽起來正式而老派。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be versed in languages","meaning":"精通多種語言","examples":[{"en":"The successful applicant needed to be versed in languages.","zh":"成功申請人需要精通多種語言。"},{"en":"To be versed in languages means to have good knowledge or skill in several languages.","zh":"「be versed in languages」意思是對幾種語言有良好知識或能力。"},{"en":"A hotel receptionist should be versed in languages if many foreign guests arrive.","zh":"如果有很多外國客人到訪，酒店接待員應精通多種語言。"},{"en":"If a secretary is versed in languages, they can handle letters from different countries.","zh":"如果秘書精通多種語言，他可以處理來自不同國家的信件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong language knowledge, especially for work.","zh":"這個短語描述強大的語言知識，尤其用於工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"supervisor of the household","meaning":"家務主管","examples":[{"en":"Nobel wanted a secretary who could also act as supervisor of the household.","zh":"Nobel 想要一位也能擔任家務主管的秘書。"},{"en":"A supervisor of the household is a person who manages domestic arrangements and staff.","zh":"「supervisor of the household」是管理家庭安排和家中員工的人。"},{"en":"In a large home, a supervisor of the household may organise meals, cleaning, visitors, and accounts.","zh":"在大宅中，家務主管可能安排膳食、清潔、訪客和帳目。"},{"en":"If the household is busy, a supervisor can help daily life run smoothly.","zh":"如果家庭事務繁忙，主管可以幫助日常生活順利運作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a management role inside a home.","zh":"這個短語描述家庭內部的管理角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the most qualified applicant","meaning":"最符合資格的申請人","examples":[{"en":"Bertha Kinsky was the most qualified applicant.","zh":"Bertha Kinsky 是最符合資格的申請人。"},{"en":"The most qualified applicant is the person whose skills, education, and experience best match the job.","zh":"「the most qualified applicant」是技能、教育和經驗最符合工作的申請人。"},{"en":"A school may choose the most qualified applicant after checking training, references, and interviews.","zh":"學校可能在檢查培訓、推薦和面試後選出最符合資格的申請人。"},{"en":"If someone is clearly the most qualified, they are more likely to be hired.","zh":"如果某人明顯最符合資格，他更可能被聘用。"},{"en":"The phrase compares applicants and identifies the strongest one.","zh":"這個短語比較申請人並指出最強的一位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"turn out to be","meaning":"結果是","examples":[{"en":"The successful applicant turned out to be an Austrian countess.","zh":"成功申請人結果是一位奧地利女伯爵。"},{"en":"To turn out to be something means to be discovered later as that thing.","zh":"「turn out to be」某物，意思是後來被發現原來是該物或該身份。"},{"en":"The quiet student turned out to be the best speaker in the class.","zh":"那位安靜學生結果是班中最好的演講者。"},{"en":"If someone turns out to be more experienced than expected, the result may surprise others.","zh":"如果某人結果比預期更有經驗，這結果可能令其他人驚訝。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a later discovery about identity or reality.","zh":"這個短語描述後來對身份或現實的發現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Austrian countess","meaning":"奧地利女伯爵","examples":[{"en":"Bertha Kinsky was an Austrian countess.","zh":"Bertha Kinsky 是一位奧地利女伯爵。"},{"en":"An Austrian countess is a woman of noble rank connected with Austria.","zh":"「Austrian countess」是與奧地利有關、具有貴族爵位的女性。"},{"en":"In a history book, an Austrian countess may appear in stories about European aristocracy.","zh":"在歷史書中，奧地利女伯爵可能出現在歐洲貴族故事中。"},{"en":"If a countess becomes a peace activist, her social position may help her message spread.","zh":"如果女伯爵成為和平倡議者，其社會地位可能幫助她的信息傳播。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies Bertha’s nationality and noble title.","zh":"這個短語指出 Bertha 的國籍和貴族頭銜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"after working a very short time","meaning":"工作了很短時間後","examples":[{"en":"After working a very short time for Nobel, she returned to Austria.","zh":"為 Nobel 工作了很短時間後，她返回奧地利。"},{"en":"After working a very short time means after spending only a brief period in the job.","zh":"「after working a very short time」意思是在該工作中只待了很短時間後。"},{"en":"A new assistant may leave after working a very short time if the role is not suitable.","zh":"如果工作角色不適合，新助理可能工作了很短時間後離開。"},{"en":"If someone works briefly but remains in contact, the relationship may still become important.","zh":"如果有人工作時間很短但仍保持聯絡，關係仍可能變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the job period was short.","zh":"這個短語強調工作時間短。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in spite of this","meaning":"儘管如此","examples":[{"en":"In spite of this, Nobel and Bertha remained close friends.","zh":"儘管如此，Nobel 和 Bertha 仍保持親密朋友關係。"},{"en":"In spite of this means although the situation just mentioned might suggest the opposite.","zh":"「in spite of this」意思是雖然剛提到的情況可能暗示相反結果。"},{"en":"The project was difficult; in spite of this, the students finished it on time.","zh":"項目很困難；儘管如此，學生仍準時完成。"},{"en":"If someone leaves a job quickly but friendships continue, the earlier separation did not end the relationship.","zh":"如果有人很快離職但友誼持續，早前分離並沒有結束關係。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces contrast with an expected result.","zh":"這個短語引出與預期結果相反的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"remain friends","meaning":"保持朋友關係","examples":[{"en":"They remained friends for several decades.","zh":"他們保持朋友關係數十年。"},{"en":"To remain friends means to continue having a friendly relationship over time.","zh":"「remain friends」意思是隨時間繼續維持友好關係。"},{"en":"Two classmates may remain friends even after going to different universities.","zh":"兩位同學即使入讀不同大學，仍可能保持朋友關係。"},{"en":"If people keep writing and supporting each other, friendship can last for many years.","zh":"如果人們持續通信並互相支持，友誼可以維持多年。"},{"en":"The phrase describes friendship that continues despite distance or change.","zh":"這個短語描述即使距離或情況改變仍持續的友誼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"write letters to each other","meaning":"互相通信","examples":[{"en":"Nobel and Bertha continued to write letters to each other.","zh":"Nobel 和 Bertha 繼續互相通信。"},{"en":"To write letters to each other means to communicate by sending written messages back and forth.","zh":"「write letters to each other」意思是透過來回寄送書面訊息溝通。"},{"en":"Before email, friends abroad often wrote letters to each other to stay close.","zh":"電郵出現前，海外朋友常互相通信以保持親近。"},{"en":"If two people exchange letters for years, their ideas may influence one another.","zh":"如果兩人多年交換信件，他們的想法可能互相影響。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ongoing written communication between people.","zh":"這個短語描述人與人之間持續的書面交流。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"become increasingly critical of","meaning":"越來越批評……","examples":[{"en":"Bertha became increasingly critical of the arms race.","zh":"Bertha 越來越批評軍備競賽。"},{"en":"To become increasingly critical of something means to grow more openly disapproving of it over time.","zh":"「become increasingly critical of」某事，意思是隨時間越來越公開不認同它。"},{"en":"Parents may become increasingly critical of a school policy if problems continue.","zh":"如果問題持續，家長可能越來越批評學校政策。"},{"en":"If a person sees more harm from a system, their criticism may become stronger.","zh":"如果一個人看到某制度造成更多傷害，其批評可能變得更強。"},{"en":"The phrase describes criticism that grows gradually.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸增強的批評。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"arms race","meaning":"軍備競賽","examples":[{"en":"Bertha von Suttner strongly opposed the international arms race.","zh":"Bertha von Suttner 強烈反對國際軍備競賽。"},{"en":"An arms race is a competition between countries to build more and stronger weapons.","zh":"「arms race」是國家之間製造更多、更強武器的競爭。"},{"en":"In history lessons, students may study how an arms race can increase fear between nations.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生可能學習軍備競賽如何增加國家之間的恐懼。"},{"en":"If countries keep adding weapons, mistrust may grow and peace becomes harder.","zh":"如果國家不斷增加武器，不信任可能增長，和平變得更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dangerous military competition.","zh":"這個短語描述危險的軍事競爭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Lay Down Your Arms","meaning":"《放下武器》","examples":[{"en":"Lay Down Your Arms became an influential anti-war book.","zh":"《放下武器》成為一本有影響力的反戰書籍。"},{"en":"Lay Down Your Arms is the title of a book arguing against war and militarism.","zh":"「Lay Down Your Arms」是一本反對戰爭和軍國主義的書名。"},{"en":"A literature class may discuss Lay Down Your Arms as a text about peace activism.","zh":"文學課可能討論《放下武器》作為和平倡議文本。"},{"en":"If a book changes public opinion about war, it can influence political debate.","zh":"如果一本書改變公眾對戰爭的看法，它可以影響政治辯論。"},{"en":"The phrase names Bertha von Suttner’s important anti-war work.","zh":"這個短語指出 Bertha von Suttner 的重要反戰作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"prominent figure","meaning":"重要人物","examples":[{"en":"Bertha became a prominent figure in the peace movement.","zh":"Bertha 成為和平運動中的重要人物。"},{"en":"A prominent figure is a well-known and important person in a field or movement.","zh":"「prominent figure」是某領域或運動中知名且重要的人。"},{"en":"A doctor may become a prominent figure in public health after leading successful campaigns.","zh":"醫生領導成功公共健康運動後，可能成為公共健康界的重要人物。"},{"en":"If someone writes influential books and speaks publicly, they may become prominent.","zh":"如果有人寫有影響力的書並公開發言，他可能變得重要而知名。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a person with visibility and importance.","zh":"這個短語描述具能見度和重要性的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"peace movement","meaning":"和平運動","examples":[{"en":"Her writing helped strengthen the European peace movement.","zh":"她的寫作幫助加強歐洲和平運動。"},{"en":"The peace movement is organised activity that works to prevent war and promote peaceful solutions.","zh":"「peace movement」是致力防止戰爭和推動和平解決方法的有組織活動。"},{"en":"Students may join a peace movement by taking part in discussions, campaigns, or charity events.","zh":"學生可能透過參與討論、活動或慈善事件加入和平運動。"},{"en":"If more writers and activists support peace, the movement can gain influence.","zh":"如果更多作家和倡議者支持和平，運動可以獲得影響力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes collective action for peace.","zh":"這個短語描述為和平而集體行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"no doubt","meaning":"毫無疑問","examples":[{"en":"No doubt Bertha’s ideas influenced Nobel’s final will.","zh":"毫無疑問，Bertha 的思想影響了 Nobel 的最後遺囑。"},{"en":"No doubt means almost certainly or with very little uncertainty.","zh":"「no doubt」意思是幾乎肯定或幾乎沒有不確定。"},{"en":"No doubt regular practice helped the student improve so quickly.","zh":"毫無疑問，定期練習幫助那名學生快速進步。"},{"en":"If two people exchange ideas for decades, one may no doubt influence the other.","zh":"如果兩人數十年交換思想，一方毫無疑問可能影響另一方。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses strong confidence.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"influence someone when","meaning":"在某人……時影響他","examples":[{"en":"Her peace activism influenced Nobel when he wrote his will.","zh":"她的和平倡議在 Nobel 寫遺囑時影響了他。"},{"en":"To influence someone when they do something means to affect their thinking or decision at that time.","zh":"「influence someone when」他做某事，意思是在那時影響他的想法或決定。"},{"en":"A teacher’s advice may influence a student when choosing university subjects.","zh":"老師的建議可能在學生選擇大學科目時影響他。"},{"en":"If a friend’s ideas shape an important decision, their influence can last for years.","zh":"如果朋友的想法塑造一個重要決定，其影響可以持續多年。"},{"en":"The phrase connects influence with a specific moment of choice.","zh":"這個短語把影響與特定抉擇時刻連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"final will","meaning":"最後遺囑","examples":[{"en":"Nobel’s final will established prizes in several fields.","zh":"Nobel 的最後遺囑設立了幾個範疇的獎項。"},{"en":"A final will is the last legal document stating how a person’s property should be used after death.","zh":"「final will」是說明一個人死後財產應如何使用的最後法律文件。"},{"en":"A person may change earlier wills before writing a final will.","zh":"一個人在寫最後遺囑前，可能修改早前遺囑。"},{"en":"If a final will leaves money to charity, public benefits may continue long after death.","zh":"如果最後遺囑把金錢留給慈善，公共利益可以在死後很久繼續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a final legal statement of wishes.","zh":"這個短語描述最後的法律意願聲明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"include a prize for","meaning":"包括頒給……的獎項","examples":[{"en":"The will included a prize for people who promoted peace.","zh":"遺囑包括頒給促進和平人士的獎項。"},{"en":"To include a prize for someone or something means to contain an award meant for that person, group, or achievement.","zh":"「include a prize for」某人或某事，意思是包含給予該人、群體或成就的獎項。"},{"en":"A school ceremony may include a prize for students who serve the community.","zh":"學校頒獎禮可能包括頒給服務社區學生的獎項。"},{"en":"If an award system includes peace, it values social contribution as well as scientific achievement.","zh":"如果獎項制度包括和平，它就重視社會貢獻以及科學成就。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adding a specific award category.","zh":"這個短語描述加入特定獎項類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"several years after","meaning":"……數年後","examples":[{"en":"Several years after Nobel’s death, Bertha received the Peace Prize.","zh":"Nobel 去世數年後，Bertha 獲得和平獎。"},{"en":"Several years after means a number of years later.","zh":"「several years after」意思是幾年之後。"},{"en":"Several years after leaving school, a student may return as a teacher.","zh":"離校數年後，學生可能以老師身份回來。"},{"en":"If recognition comes several years after an event, the earlier influence may still be remembered.","zh":"如果認可在事件數年後才來，早前影響仍可能被記住。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a later time in relation to an earlier event.","zh":"這個短語提供相對於早前事件的較後時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Norwegian Storting","meaning":"挪威國會","examples":[{"en":"The Norwegian Storting decided who would receive the Peace Prize.","zh":"挪威國會決定誰會獲得和平獎。"},{"en":"The Norwegian Storting is the parliament of Norway.","zh":"「Norwegian Storting」是挪威的國會。"},{"en":"A civics lesson may mention the Norwegian Storting when explaining how the Peace Prize is awarded.","zh":"公民教育課解釋和平獎如何頒發時，可能提到挪威國會。"},{"en":"If a national parliament is involved in choosing a prize, the process has official authority.","zh":"如果國家議會參與選擇獎項，過程就具有官方權威。"},{"en":"The phrase names the institution connected with the Nobel Peace Prize decision.","zh":"這個短語指出與諾貝爾和平獎決定相關的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"award a prize to","meaning":"將獎項頒給……","examples":[{"en":"The Nobel Peace Prize was awarded to Bertha von Suttner in 1905.","zh":"諾貝爾和平獎於1905年頒給 Bertha von Suttner。"},{"en":"To award a prize to someone means to officially give them a prize.","zh":"「award a prize to」某人，意思是正式把獎項頒給他。"},{"en":"A school may award a prize to a student for excellent improvement.","zh":"學校可能因學生進步優秀而將獎項頒給他。"},{"en":"If a prize is awarded to an activist, their cause may receive more public attention.","zh":"如果獎項頒給倡議者，其理念可能得到更多公眾關注。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formal recognition through an award.","zh":"這個短語描述透過獎項作正式認可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"die in","meaning":"在……去世","examples":[{"en":"Alfred Nobel died in San Remo, Italy.","zh":"Alfred Nobel 在意大利聖雷莫去世。"},{"en":"To die in a place means to pass away there.","zh":"「die in」某地，意思是在那裡去世。"},{"en":"A famous writer may die in a city far from the place where they were born.","zh":"著名作家可能在遠離出生地的城市去世。"},{"en":"If someone dies abroad, their estate and will may involve several countries.","zh":"如果有人在海外去世，其遺產和遺囑可能涉及幾個國家。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the location of a person’s death.","zh":"這個短語提供某人去世的地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"when the will was opened","meaning":"當遺囑被公開時","examples":[{"en":"When Nobel’s will was opened, its contents caused surprise.","zh":"當 Nobel 的遺囑被公開時，其內容令人驚訝。"},{"en":"When the will was opened means when the legal document was read or made known after death.","zh":"「when the will was opened」意思是死後法律文件被宣讀或公開時。"},{"en":"A family may learn unexpected decisions when a relative’s will is opened.","zh":"當親人的遺囑被公開時，家庭可能得知意外決定。"},{"en":"If a will leaves money to public prizes, relatives may be surprised or upset.","zh":"如果遺囑把金錢留給公共獎項，親屬可能驚訝或不滿。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the moment when a will’s contents become known.","zh":"這個短語描述遺囑內容被知悉的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"come as a surprise","meaning":"令人感到意外","examples":[{"en":"It came as a surprise that most of his fortune would fund prizes.","zh":"他大部分財產將用作資助獎項，這令人感到意外。"},{"en":"To come as a surprise means to be unexpected.","zh":"「come as a surprise」意思是出乎意料。"},{"en":"It came as a surprise when the quiet student won the speaking competition.","zh":"安靜學生贏得演講比賽時，這令人感到意外。"},{"en":"If someone’s decision is very different from family expectations, it may surprise everyone.","zh":"如果某人的決定與家庭期望非常不同，它可能令所有人驚訝。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an unexpected result or piece of news.","zh":"這個短語描述意外的結果或消息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"one’s fortune","meaning":"某人的財產","examples":[{"en":"Nobel’s fortune was used to finance the prizes.","zh":"Nobel 的財產被用來資助獎項。"},{"en":"One’s fortune means a large amount of money or wealth belonging to a person.","zh":"「one’s fortune」意思是屬於某人的大量金錢或財富。"},{"en":"A successful business owner may use part of her fortune to build a school.","zh":"成功企業主可能用部分財產興建學校。"},{"en":"If a fortune is left to public causes, it can support work for many years.","zh":"如果財產被留給公共事業，它可以多年支持相關工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes personal wealth, especially a large amount.","zh":"這個短語描述個人財富，尤其是大量財富。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be used for","meaning":"被用於……","examples":[{"en":"His wealth was to be used for prizes in five fields.","zh":"他的財富將被用於五個範疇的獎項。"},{"en":"To be used for something means to serve a particular purpose.","zh":"「be used for」某事，意思是服務於特定目的。"},{"en":"A classroom fund may be used for books, displays, and learning games.","zh":"課室基金可能被用於書本、展示和學習遊戲。"},{"en":"If money is used for education, it may benefit students rather than one family only.","zh":"如果金錢被用於教育，它可能惠及學生，而不只是某個家庭。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the purpose of a resource.","zh":"這個短語解釋資源的用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"physiology or medicine","meaning":"生理學或醫學","examples":[{"en":"One Nobel Prize recognises achievements in physiology or medicine.","zh":"其中一項諾貝爾獎表揚生理學或醫學成就。"},{"en":"Physiology or medicine refers to the study of how living bodies work and how disease can be treated.","zh":"「physiology or medicine」指研究生命體如何運作，以及疾病如何治療。"},{"en":"A student interested in physiology or medicine may study the heart, lungs, cells, and illnesses.","zh":"對生理學或醫學感興趣的學生可能研究心臟、肺、細胞和疾病。"},{"en":"If research improves treatment for disease, it may be recognised in this field.","zh":"如果研究改善疾病治療，它可能在此領域獲得認可。"},{"en":"The phrase names one major Nobel Prize category.","zh":"這個短語指出一個主要諾貝爾獎類別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"executors of a will","meaning":"遺囑執行人","examples":[{"en":"Two young engineers served as the executors of Nobel’s will.","zh":"兩位年輕工程師擔任 Nobel 遺囑的執行人。"},{"en":"Executors of a will are people legally responsible for carrying out the instructions in a will.","zh":"「executors of a will」是法律上負責執行遺囑指示的人。"},{"en":"A family may choose a trusted lawyer as executor of a will.","zh":"家庭可能選擇可信任律師作為遺囑執行人。"},{"en":"If executors manage the estate carefully, the deceased person’s wishes can be fulfilled.","zh":"如果執行人仔細管理遺產，逝者意願就能實現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a legal responsibility after someone’s death.","zh":"這個短語描述某人去世後的法律責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"set about doing something","meaning":"着手做某事","examples":[{"en":"The executors set about forming the Nobel Foundation.","zh":"遺囑執行人着手成立諾貝爾基金會。"},{"en":"To set about doing something means to begin doing it with intention and effort.","zh":"「set about doing something」意思是有意識並努力地開始做某事。"},{"en":"After exams, a student may set about organising old notes and books.","zh":"考試後，學生可能着手整理舊筆記和書本。"},{"en":"If executors set about forming an organisation, they start turning the will into reality.","zh":"如果執行人着手成立機構，他們就開始把遺囑變成現實。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the active beginning of a task.","zh":"這個短語描述主動開始一項任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Nobel Foundation","meaning":"諾貝爾基金會","examples":[{"en":"The Nobel Foundation manages the financial basis of the prizes.","zh":"諾貝爾基金會管理獎項的財務基礎。"},{"en":"The Nobel Foundation is the organisation created to manage Nobel’s assets and support the prizes.","zh":"「Nobel Foundation」是為管理 Nobel 資產並支持獎項而成立的組織。"},{"en":"A foundation may manage donations so that prizes or scholarships can continue each year.","zh":"基金會可能管理捐款，使獎項或獎學金每年延續。"},{"en":"If an award has a strong foundation behind it, it can operate reliably over time.","zh":"如果獎項背後有強大的基金會，它可以長期可靠運作。"},{"en":"The phrase names the organisation that supports the Nobel Prize system.","zh":"這個短語指出支持諾貝爾獎制度的組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"form an organisation","meaning":"成立機構","examples":[{"en":"The executors formed an organisation to manage Nobel’s assets.","zh":"遺囑執行人成立機構來管理 Nobel 的資產。"},{"en":"To form an organisation means to create a structured group for a particular purpose.","zh":"「form an organisation」意思是為特定目的創立有結構的團體。"},{"en":"Parents may form an organisation to support children with special learning needs.","zh":"家長可能成立機構，支援有特殊學習需要的孩子。"},{"en":"If a task is too large for individuals, forming an organisation can make work more systematic.","zh":"如果任務對個人來說太大，成立機構可以令工作更有系統。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creating a formal group.","zh":"這個短語描述創立正式團體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"take care of","meaning":"管理；處理","examples":[{"en":"The foundation was created to take care of the financial assets.","zh":"該基金會被創立來管理金融資產。"},{"en":"To take care of something means to manage, protect, or deal with it responsibly.","zh":"「take care of」某物，意思是負責任地管理、保護或處理它。"},{"en":"A class monitor may take care of the classroom keys.","zh":"班長可能負責保管課室鎖匙。"},{"en":"If an organisation takes care of money properly, the funds can last longer.","zh":"如果機構妥善管理金錢，資金可以維持更久。"},{"en":"The phrase describes responsible management.","zh":"這個短語描述負責任的管理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"financial assets","meaning":"金融資產","examples":[{"en":"Nobel left substantial financial assets for the prizes.","zh":"Nobel 留下大量金融資產供獎項使用。"},{"en":"Financial assets are money, investments, or property with monetary value.","zh":"「financial assets」是具有金錢價值的金錢、投資或財產。"},{"en":"A foundation may hold financial assets such as stocks, bonds, and bank deposits.","zh":"基金會可能持有股票、債券和銀行存款等金融資產。"},{"en":"If financial assets are well managed, they can support scholarships for many years.","zh":"如果金融資產管理得好，它們可以多年支持獎學金。"},{"en":"The phrase describes wealth that can be used or invested.","zh":"這個短語描述可使用或投資的財富。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be left for a purpose","meaning":"為某目的而留下","examples":[{"en":"The assets were left for the purpose of funding international prizes.","zh":"這些資產為資助國際獎項的目的而留下。"},{"en":"To be left for a purpose means to be given or reserved for a specific use after someone’s death.","zh":"「be left for a purpose」意思是某物在某人死後被給予或保留作特定用途。"},{"en":"A grandparent may leave money for the purpose of paying grandchildren’s school fees.","zh":"祖父母可能留下金錢，用於支付孫兒女學費。"},{"en":"If money is left for a clear purpose, executors must use it according to that intention.","zh":"如果金錢為明確目的而留下，執行人必須按該意願使用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes inheritance tied to a particular goal.","zh":"這個短語描述與特定目標相連的遺產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"coordinate the work of","meaning":"協調……的工作","examples":[{"en":"The foundation coordinates the work of the Prize-Awarding Institutions.","zh":"基金會協調頒獎機構的工作。"},{"en":"To coordinate the work of groups means to organise their activities so they work together smoothly.","zh":"「coordinate the work of」不同群體，意思是組織其活動，使他們順暢合作。"},{"en":"A school office coordinates the work of teachers, parents, and students during exams.","zh":"考試期間，學校辦公室協調老師、家長和學生的工作。"},{"en":"If several institutions are involved, coordination prevents confusion and repeated work.","zh":"如果幾個機構參與，協調可防止混亂和重複工作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organising different people or bodies toward one system.","zh":"這個短語描述組織不同人士或機構以配合同一系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Prize-Awarding Institutions","meaning":"頒獎機構","examples":[{"en":"Several Prize-Awarding Institutions select the Nobel laureates.","zh":"幾個頒獎機構選出諾貝爾獎得主。"},{"en":"Prize-Awarding Institutions are organisations responsible for choosing and giving prizes.","zh":"「Prize-Awarding Institutions」是負責選出並頒發獎項的組織。"},{"en":"A university committee can act like a prize-awarding institution when it selects scholarship winners.","zh":"大學委員會選擇獎學金得主時，可以像頒獎機構一樣運作。"},{"en":"If institutions choose winners independently, the award process may gain credibility.","zh":"如果機構獨立選出得主，頒獎過程可能更有公信力。"},{"en":"The phrase names the bodies that decide who receives the Nobel Prizes.","zh":"這個短語指出決定誰獲得諾貝爾獎的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not without difficulties","meaning":"並非沒有困難","examples":[{"en":"The establishment of the foundation was not without difficulties.","zh":"基金會的成立並非沒有困難。"},{"en":"Not without difficulties means there were some problems or obstacles.","zh":"「not without difficulties」意思是存在一些問題或障礙。"},{"en":"Starting a new school club is not without difficulties because members, rooms, and funds are needed.","zh":"成立新學校社團並非沒有困難，因為需要成員、房間和資金。"},{"en":"If relatives contest a will, carrying out its instructions becomes harder.","zh":"如果親屬對遺囑提出爭議，執行其指示會變得更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase politely says that a process was difficult.","zh":"這個短語委婉地表示過程有困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"contest a will","meaning":"對遺囑提出爭議","examples":[{"en":"Some of Nobel’s relatives contested his will.","zh":"Nobel 的一些親屬對他的遺囑提出爭議。"},{"en":"To contest a will means to challenge its legality or fairness.","zh":"「contest a will」意思是挑戰遺囑的合法性或公平性。"},{"en":"Family members may contest a will if they believe the instructions are unclear or unfair.","zh":"如果家庭成員認為指示不清楚或不公平，他們可能對遺囑提出爭議。"},{"en":"If a will is contested, the distribution of money may be delayed.","zh":"如果遺囑受爭議，金錢分配可能被延遲。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a legal dispute over a deceased person’s wishes.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞逝者意願的法律爭議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be questioned by authorities","meaning":"受到當局質疑","examples":[{"en":"The will was questioned by authorities in several countries.","zh":"該遺囑受到幾個國家當局質疑。"},{"en":"To be questioned by authorities means to be examined or challenged by official bodies.","zh":"「be questioned by authorities」意思是被官方機構審視或質疑。"},{"en":"A building plan may be questioned by authorities if safety rules are unclear.","zh":"如果安全規則不清楚，建築計劃可能受到當局質疑。"},{"en":"If a legal document affects several countries, officials may examine it carefully.","zh":"如果法律文件影響幾個國家，官員可能仔細審查它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes official doubt or investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述官方疑問或調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"one’s greatness lay in","meaning":"某人的偉大之處在於","examples":[{"en":"Nobel’s greatness lay in his ability to combine different talents.","zh":"Nobel 的偉大之處在於他能結合不同才能。"},{"en":"One’s greatness lay in something means the main reason for that person’s greatness was found there.","zh":"「one’s greatness lay in」某事，意思是某人偉大的主要原因在於那裡。"},{"en":"A teacher’s greatness may lie in making weak students feel capable.","zh":"老師的偉大之處可能在於令能力較弱學生覺得自己做得到。"},{"en":"If someone combines science, business, and social concern, their greatness may come from that range.","zh":"如果有人結合科學、商業和社會關懷，其偉大之處可能來自這種廣度。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the source of someone’s importance.","zh":"這個短語指出某人重要性的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ability to combine A with B","meaning":"將 A 與 B 結合的能力","examples":[{"en":"Nobel combined a scientist’s mind with an industrialist’s dynamism.","zh":"Nobel 將科學家的頭腦與工業家的魄力結合起來。"},{"en":"The ability to combine A with B means being able to bring two different strengths together.","zh":"「ability to combine A with B」意思是能把兩種不同優點結合起來。"},{"en":"A good teacher combines strict standards with kindness.","zh":"好老師把嚴格標準與仁慈結合起來。"},{"en":"If a leader combines vision with practical planning, ideas are more likely to succeed.","zh":"如果領袖把遠見與實際規劃結合，想法更可能成功。"},{"en":"The phrase describes joining different qualities effectively.","zh":"這個短語描述有效結合不同特質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"penetrating mind","meaning":"敏銳深刻的頭腦","examples":[{"en":"Nobel possessed the penetrating mind of a scientist.","zh":"Nobel 擁有科學家敏銳深刻的頭腦。"},{"en":"A penetrating mind is an ability to understand difficult ideas deeply and clearly.","zh":"「penetrating mind」是深入而清楚理解困難想法的能力。"},{"en":"A student with a penetrating mind may notice the hidden assumption in an argument.","zh":"具有敏銳頭腦的學生可能注意到論點中的隱藏假設。"},{"en":"If someone thinks deeply, they can see causes that others miss.","zh":"如果某人思考深入，他可以看見其他人忽略的原因。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sharp and deep intelligence.","zh":"這個短語描述敏銳而深刻的智慧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"scientist and inventor","meaning":"科學家兼發明家","examples":[{"en":"Nobel combined the skills of a scientist and inventor.","zh":"Nobel 結合了科學家兼發明家的能力。"},{"en":"A scientist and inventor is someone who studies how things work and creates new practical solutions.","zh":"「scientist and inventor」是研究事物如何運作並創造新實用方案的人。"},{"en":"A scientist and inventor may test materials in a lab and then design a useful product.","zh":"科學家兼發明家可能在實驗室測試材料，然後設計有用產品。"},{"en":"If scientific knowledge becomes an invention, society may gain new tools or technologies.","zh":"如果科學知識變成發明，社會可能獲得新工具或技術。"},{"en":"The phrase combines research ability with creative application.","zh":"這個短語結合研究能力與創意應用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"forward-looking dynamism","meaning":"前瞻性的魄力","examples":[{"en":"He also possessed the forward-looking dynamism of an industrialist.","zh":"他也擁有工業家的前瞻性魄力。"},{"en":"Forward-looking dynamism means energetic action guided by future possibilities.","zh":"「forward-looking dynamism」意思是由未來可能性引導的積極行動力。"},{"en":"A school leader with forward-looking dynamism may introduce new courses before students demand them.","zh":"具有前瞻性魄力的校長可能在學生要求前引入新課程。"},{"en":"If a businessperson thinks ahead and acts boldly, their company may grow quickly.","zh":"如果商人有前瞻思維並大膽行動，其公司可能快速增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active ambition directed toward the future.","zh":"這個短語描述面向未來的積極抱負。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"industrialist","meaning":"工業家","examples":[{"en":"Nobel was a successful industrialist as well as a chemist.","zh":"Nobel 既是化學家，也是一位成功工業家。"},{"en":"An industrialist is a person who owns or manages large businesses in manufacturing or industry.","zh":"「industrialist」是擁有或管理大型製造或工業企業的人。"},{"en":"An industrialist may build factories, hire workers, and sell products internationally.","zh":"工業家可能建工廠、聘請工人並向國際銷售產品。"},{"en":"If an industrialist invests in new technology, an entire industry may change.","zh":"如果工業家投資新科技，整個行業可能改變。"},{"en":"The word describes a major business figure in industry.","zh":"這個詞描述工業界的重要商業人物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"social and peace-related issues","meaning":"社會及和平相關議題","examples":[{"en":"Nobel took a strong interest in social and peace-related issues.","zh":"Nobel 對社會及和平相關議題有濃厚興趣。"},{"en":"Social and peace-related issues are matters concerning society, conflict, justice, and peaceful relations.","zh":"「social and peace-related issues」是關於社會、衝突、公義和和平關係的事情。"},{"en":"A student group may discuss social and peace-related issues such as poverty, war, and refugees.","zh":"學生小組可能討論貧窮、戰爭和難民等社會及和平相關議題。"},{"en":"If an industrialist cares about peace, their interests go beyond business profit.","zh":"如果工業家關心和平，其興趣就超越商業利潤。"},{"en":"The phrase describes public concerns about society and peace.","zh":"這個短語描述關於社會與和平的公共關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hold radical views","meaning":"持有激進觀點","examples":[{"en":"He held views that were considered radical in his era.","zh":"他持有在其時代被視為激進的觀點。"},{"en":"To hold radical views means to have opinions that strongly challenge accepted ideas.","zh":"「hold radical views」意思是持有強烈挑戰既有想法的意見。"},{"en":"A student may hold radical views about school reform if they want a completely new system.","zh":"如果學生想要完全新的制度，他可能對學校改革持有激進觀點。"},{"en":"If ideas are far ahead of their time, people may call them radical.","zh":"如果想法遠超時代，人們可能稱它們為激進。"},{"en":"The phrase describes opinions seen as bold or extreme by others.","zh":"這個短語描述被他人視為大膽或極端的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in one’s era","meaning":"在某人的時代","examples":[{"en":"Nobel’s social ideas were unusual in his era.","zh":"Nobel 的社會思想在他的時代很不尋常。"},{"en":"In one’s era means during the period in which that person lived or was active.","zh":"「in one’s era」意思是在某人生活或活躍的時期。"},{"en":"A scientist may be misunderstood in his era but admired later.","zh":"科學家可能在其時代不被理解，但後來受人敬佩。"},{"en":"If an idea is unusual in its era, society may need time to accept it.","zh":"如果想法在其時代不尋常，社會可能需要時間接受它。"},{"en":"The phrase places a person or idea in historical context.","zh":"這個短語把人物或想法放進歷史背景中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"dramatic works","meaning":"戲劇作品","examples":[{"en":"Nobel wrote poetry and dramatic works.","zh":"Nobel 寫詩和戲劇作品。"},{"en":"Dramatic works are plays or other writings intended for performance or dramatic expression.","zh":"「dramatic works」是劇本或其他用於表演或戲劇表達的文字。"},{"en":"A literature class may study dramatic works to understand dialogue and conflict.","zh":"文學課可能研究戲劇作品，以理解對白和衝突。"},{"en":"If a scientist writes dramatic works, it shows interests beyond technical research.","zh":"如果科學家寫戲劇作品，這顯示其興趣超越技術研究。"},{"en":"The phrase describes creative writing connected with drama.","zh":"這個短語描述與戲劇相關的創意寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"an extension of","meaning":"……的延伸","examples":[{"en":"The Nobel Prizes became an extension of his personal interests.","zh":"諾貝爾獎成為他個人興趣的延伸。"},{"en":"An extension of something is a continuation or outward expression of it.","zh":"「an extension of」某事，是它的延續或外在表達。"},{"en":"A school magazine can be an extension of students’ interest in writing.","zh":"學校雜誌可以是學生寫作興趣的延伸。"},{"en":"If prizes reflect a person’s interests, they continue that person’s values after death.","zh":"如果獎項反映一個人的興趣，它們就在死後延續其價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something growing out of an earlier idea or passion.","zh":"這個短語描述某物從早前想法或熱情中延伸出來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fulfilment of","meaning":"……的實現","examples":[{"en":"The prizes represented the fulfilment of Nobel’s lifetime interests.","zh":"這些獎項代表 Nobel 畢生興趣的實現。"},{"en":"The fulfilment of something is the achievement or realisation of a wish, plan, or interest.","zh":"「fulfilment of」某事，是願望、計劃或興趣的達成或實現。"},{"en":"Publishing a first book may be the fulfilment of a student’s childhood dream.","zh":"出版第一本書可能是學生童年夢想的實現。"},{"en":"If a person’s money creates lasting prizes, their lifelong interests become real institutions.","zh":"如果一個人的金錢創造持久獎項，其畢生興趣就變成真實機構。"},{"en":"The phrase describes bringing an important aim into reality.","zh":"這個短語描述把重要目標變成現實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lifetime interests","meaning":"畢生興趣","examples":[{"en":"Science, literature and peace were among Nobel’s lifetime interests.","zh":"科學、文學和和平都是 Nobel 的畢生興趣之一。"},{"en":"Lifetime interests are subjects or activities that remain important to a person throughout life.","zh":"「lifetime interests」是在人一生中持續重要的科目或活動。"},{"en":"A teacher’s lifetime interests may include language, children’s development, and public service.","zh":"老師的畢生興趣可能包括語言、兒童發展和公共服務。"},{"en":"If a person supports their lifetime interests in a will, their values may continue after death.","zh":"如果一個人在遺囑中支持其畢生興趣，其價值觀可能在死後延續。"},{"en":"The phrase describes lasting personal concerns.","zh":"這個短語描述持久的個人關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"符合文中資料","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否符合文章。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the text says.","zh":"「agree with the information given」意思是符合文本所說。"},{"en":"In a reading test, a statement agrees with the text only if the passage clearly supports it.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，只有文章清楚支持某陳述，它才符合文本。"},{"en":"If students rely on outside knowledge instead of the passage, they may choose the wrong answer.","zh":"如果學生依賴外部知識而不是文章，他們可能選錯答案。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds learners to judge answers by textual evidence.","zh":"這個短語提醒學習者以文本證據判斷答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文中資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict the information in the passage.","zh":"陳述可能與文章資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"「contradict the information」意思是說出與文章所說相反的內容。"},{"en":"If the passage says Nobel was successful, calling him unsuccessful contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說 Nobel 成功，稱他不成功就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"When a statement contradicts the text, the correct exam answer is usually FALSE or NO.","zh":"當陳述與文本矛盾，考試答案通常是 FALSE 或 NO。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a clear conflict with the source.","zh":"這個短語描述與來源的清楚衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"This response is used when the passage provides no relevant information.","zh":"當文章沒有提供相關資料時，使用這個回答。"},{"en":"No information on this means the text does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"「no information on this」意思是文本沒有說該陳述是真是假。"},{"en":"If a passage never mentions someone’s favourite food, there is no information on this.","zh":"如果文章從未提及某人最喜歡的食物，文中就沒有相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from general knowledge when the passage gives no evidence.","zh":"當文章沒有證據時，學生不應憑常識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase is essential for NOT GIVEN questions.","zh":"這個短語對 NOT GIVEN 題很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be first awarded","meaning":"首次頒發","examples":[{"en":"The Nobel Prizes were first awarded after Nobel’s death.","zh":"諾貝爾獎在 Nobel 去世後首次頒發。"},{"en":"To be first awarded means to be given for the first time.","zh":"「be first awarded」意思是首次被頒發。"},{"en":"A school prize may be first awarded in the year a new scholarship is created.","zh":"新獎學金設立的那一年，學校獎項可能首次頒發。"},{"en":"If an award is first given after its founder dies, the founder never sees the ceremony.","zh":"如果獎項在創辦人死後才首次頒發，創辦人就看不到頒獎禮。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the first official presentation of a prize.","zh":"這個短語標示獎項首次正式頒授。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"want someone to have a better education","meaning":"希望某人接受更好的教育","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Nobel’s father wanted him to receive a better education.","zh":"該陳述問 Nobel 的父親是否希望他接受更好的教育。"},{"en":"To want someone to have a better education means to hope they receive higher-quality learning.","zh":"「want someone to have a better education」意思是希望某人接受更高質素的學習。"},{"en":"Parents may want their children to have a better education than they had themselves.","zh":"父母可能希望孩子接受比自己更好的教育。"},{"en":"If a father sends his child abroad for training, education may be one of his goals.","zh":"如果父親把孩子送往外國受訓，教育可能是其目標之一。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a wish for improved learning opportunities.","zh":"這個短語描述對更好學習機會的願望。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"unsuccessful businessman","meaning":"不成功的商人","examples":[{"en":"Nobel was not an unsuccessful businessman.","zh":"Nobel 並不是不成功的商人。"},{"en":"An unsuccessful businessman is someone whose business efforts fail or do not produce good results.","zh":"「unsuccessful businessman」是商業努力失敗或沒有好成果的人。"},{"en":"A shop owner may be an unsuccessful businessman if the shop loses money every month.","zh":"如果店舖每月虧損，店主可能是不成功的商人。"},{"en":"If a person builds companies in many countries, they are unlikely to be described as unsuccessful.","zh":"如果一個人在許多國家建立公司，他不太可能被稱為不成功。"},{"en":"The phrase describes failure in business.","zh":"這個短語描述商業上的失敗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be selected by","meaning":"由……挑選","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether Bertha was selected by Nobel for the Peace Prize.","zh":"該陳述問 Bertha 是否由 Nobel 挑選獲和平獎。"},{"en":"To be selected by someone means to be chosen by that person or body.","zh":"「be selected by」某人，意思是由該人或機構選出。"},{"en":"A student may be selected by teachers to represent the school in a debate.","zh":"學生可能由老師挑選代表學校參加辯論。"},{"en":"If a prize winner is selected by a committee, one individual may not control the choice.","zh":"如果得獎者由委員會選出，單一個人未必控制選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies who makes the selection.","zh":"這個短語指出誰作出選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the first Peace Prize","meaning":"首屆和平獎","examples":[{"en":"The first Peace Prize was awarded before Bertha received hers.","zh":"首屆和平獎在 Bertha 獲獎之前已頒發。"},{"en":"The first Peace Prize means the earliest award given in the Nobel Peace Prize category.","zh":"「the first Peace Prize」指諾貝爾和平獎類別中最早頒發的獎項。"},{"en":"A history quiz may ask who received the first Peace Prize.","zh":"歷史測驗可能問誰獲得首屆和平獎。"},{"en":"If someone received a later Peace Prize, they were not necessarily the first winner.","zh":"如果某人獲得較後的和平獎，他不一定是首位得主。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the beginning of the Peace Prize tradition.","zh":"這個短語標示和平獎傳統的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be established after someone’s death","meaning":"在某人去世後成立","examples":[{"en":"The Nobel Foundation was established after Nobel’s death.","zh":"諾貝爾基金會在 Nobel 去世後成立。"},{"en":"To be established after someone’s death means to be formally created after that person has died.","zh":"「be established after someone’s death」意思是在某人去世後正式創立。"},{"en":"A charity may be established after a teacher’s death to continue her work.","zh":"慈善機構可能在老師去世後成立，以延續她的工作。"},{"en":"If an organisation is created after death, executors may have to carry out the plan.","zh":"如果機構在死後創立，執行人可能必須執行該計劃。"},{"en":"The phrase connects formal creation with a person’s passing.","zh":"這個短語把正式成立與某人離世連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"social involvement","meaning":"社會參與","examples":[{"en":"Nobel’s social involvement was unusual for an industrialist of his era.","zh":"Nobel 的社會參與對他那個時代的工業家而言並不尋常。"},{"en":"Social involvement means active interest or participation in issues affecting society.","zh":"「social involvement」意思是積極關心或參與影響社會的議題。"},{"en":"A business owner shows social involvement by supporting education, health, or peace projects.","zh":"企業主透過支持教育、健康或和平項目展現社會參與。"},{"en":"If wealthy people take social issues seriously, they may use their resources beyond private gain.","zh":"如果富裕人士認真看待社會議題，他們可能把資源用於私人利益以外。"},{"en":"The phrase describes engagement with public concerns.","zh":"這個短語描述對公共關注的參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be uncommon in","meaning":"在……中並不常見","examples":[{"en":"His radical social views were uncommon in the nineteenth century.","zh":"他的激進社會觀點在十九世紀並不常見。"},{"en":"To be uncommon in a period or place means to be unusual there.","zh":"「be uncommon in」某時期或地方，意思是在那裡不尋常。"},{"en":"Online learning was uncommon in many schools before it became necessary.","zh":"網上學習在變得必要之前，在許多學校並不常見。"},{"en":"If an idea is uncommon in its time, people may not understand it immediately.","zh":"如果想法在其時代並不常見，人們可能不會立即理解它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that is not widely found or accepted.","zh":"這個短語描述不普遍或不被廣泛接受的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"complete the notes","meaning":"完成筆記","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the notes using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的詞語完成筆記。"},{"en":"Complete the notes means fill in missing information in short organised points.","zh":"「complete the notes」意思是填寫簡短有組織重點中的缺失資料。"},{"en":"In a reading exam, students complete notes by finding exact words in the text.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生透過在文本中找準確字詞完成筆記。"},{"en":"If notes are incomplete, students must scan for names, dates, causes, and results.","zh":"如果筆記不完整，學生必須掃讀姓名、日期、原因和結果。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction for note-completion tasks.","zh":"這個短語是筆記填充題的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"no more than two words","meaning":"不多於兩個詞","examples":[{"en":"Each answer must contain no more than two words.","zh":"每個答案必須包含不多於兩個詞。"},{"en":"No more than two words means one or two words only, not three or more.","zh":"「no more than two words」意思是只可一個或兩個詞，不可三個或更多。"},{"en":"If the answer is “private teachers”, it fits a two-word limit.","zh":"如果答案是 “private teachers”，它符合兩詞限制。"},{"en":"If students write extra words, the answer may be marked wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"如果學生寫多了詞，即使意思正確，答案也可能被判錯。"},{"en":"The phrase sets a strict word limit in an exam.","zh":"這個短語在考試中設定嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"accumulate a great fortune","meaning":"累積巨額財富","examples":[{"en":"Nobel’s father accumulated a great fortune through business.","zh":"Nobel 的父親透過生意累積巨額財富。"},{"en":"To accumulate a great fortune means to gradually build up a large amount of wealth.","zh":"「accumulate a great fortune」意思是逐漸建立大量財富。"},{"en":"A business owner may accumulate a fortune after many years of successful trade.","zh":"企業主可能經過多年成功貿易後累積財富。"},{"en":"If wealth is accumulated through industry, it can later be invested in education or charity.","zh":"如果財富透過工業累積，它之後可以投資於教育或慈善。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the gradual growth of substantial wealth.","zh":"這個短語描述大量財富的逐步增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be determined to","meaning":"決心去……","examples":[{"en":"Immanuel Nobel was determined to give his sons an excellent education.","zh":"Immanuel Nobel 決心給兒子們優秀教育。"},{"en":"To be determined to do something means to have a strong decision and not give up easily.","zh":"「be determined to」做某事，意思是有強烈決心並不輕易放棄。"},{"en":"A student may be determined to improve pronunciation before a speaking exam.","zh":"學生可能決心在口試前改善發音。"},{"en":"If parents are determined to educate their children well, they may make major sacrifices.","zh":"如果父母決心好好教育孩子，他們可能作出重大犧牲。"},{"en":"The phrase describes firm intention and persistence.","zh":"這個短語描述堅定意圖和毅力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the best education","meaning":"最優質的教育","examples":[{"en":"Private teachers provided Nobel with the best education available.","zh":"私人教師為 Nobel 提供當時可得的最優質教育。"},{"en":"The best education means the highest-quality learning opportunities that can be obtained.","zh":"「the best education」意思是能獲得的最高質素學習機會。"},{"en":"Parents may move to another district to give their child the best education they can afford.","zh":"父母可能搬到另一區，以給孩子他們負擔得起的最優質教育。"},{"en":"If a child receives excellent education, their talents may develop more fully.","zh":"如果孩子接受優秀教育，其才能可能更充分發展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes education judged to be especially strong.","zh":"這個短語描述被判斷為特別優秀的教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be trained in","meaning":"接受……方面的培訓","examples":[{"en":"Nobel was sent abroad to be trained in chemical engineering.","zh":"Nobel 被送往外國接受化學工程方面的培訓。"},{"en":"To be trained in something means to receive instruction and practice in that skill or field.","zh":"「be trained in」某事，意思是接受該技能或領域的教學和練習。"},{"en":"New nurses are trained in patient care before working independently.","zh":"新護士在獨立工作前接受病人護理方面的培訓。"},{"en":"If workers are properly trained in safety, accidents may decrease.","zh":"如果工人接受適當安全培訓，事故可能減少。"},{"en":"The phrase describes learning a practical or professional skill.","zh":"這個短語描述學習實用或專業技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"during one’s studies","meaning":"在某人求學期間","examples":[{"en":"During his studies in Paris, Nobel worked in a private laboratory.","zh":"在巴黎求學期間，Nobel 在私人實驗室工作。"},{"en":"During one’s studies means while someone is receiving education or training.","zh":"「during one’s studies」意思是在某人接受教育或培訓期間。"},{"en":"During her studies, a university student may take part in research projects.","zh":"大學生求學期間可能參與研究項目。"},{"en":"If students gain work experience during their studies, they may understand the field better.","zh":"如果學生在求學期間獲得工作經驗，他們可能更理解該領域。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to events happening while someone is learning.","zh":"這個短語指某人學習期間發生的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a more powerful explosive than","meaning":"比……威力更強的爆炸物","examples":[{"en":"Nitroglycerine was a more powerful explosive than gunpowder.","zh":"硝酸甘油是比火藥威力更強的爆炸物。"},{"en":"A more powerful explosive than another one releases greater destructive force when it explodes.","zh":"「a more powerful explosive than」另一種，是爆炸時釋放更大破壞力的爆炸物。"},{"en":"Engineers must handle a more powerful explosive with stricter safety controls.","zh":"工程師必須以更嚴格安全控制處理威力更強的爆炸物。"},{"en":"If an explosive is more powerful, it can do more work but may create greater danger.","zh":"如果爆炸物威力更強，它可以完成更多工作，但也可能造成更大危險。"},{"en":"The phrase compares the strength of explosive materials.","zh":"這個短語比較爆炸材料的強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"experiments be banned","meaning":"試驗被禁止","examples":[{"en":"Experiments with nitroglycerine were banned within Stockholm.","zh":"硝酸甘油實驗在斯德哥爾摩市內被禁止。"},{"en":"If experiments are banned, people are officially not allowed to continue testing.","zh":"如果 experiments are banned，意思是人們被正式禁止繼續測試。"},{"en":"A school may ban experiments involving fire if students have not learned safety rules.","zh":"如果學生未學安全規則，學校可能禁止涉及火的實驗。"},{"en":"If accidents occur repeatedly, authorities may ban further experiments in crowded areas.","zh":"如果事故反覆發生，當局可能禁止在擠迫地區進一步實驗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes official prohibition of testing.","zh":"這個短語描述對測試的官方禁止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"move experiments to a lake","meaning":"將試驗移至湖上","examples":[{"en":"Nobel moved his experiments to a barge on a lake.","zh":"Nobel 將實驗移至湖上的駁船。"},{"en":"To move experiments to a lake means to shift testing from land or city areas to a water-based location.","zh":"「move experiments to a lake」意思是把測試由陸地或城市地區轉移到水上地點。"},{"en":"Scientists may move noisy experiments away from homes to reduce danger or disturbance.","zh":"科學家可能把嘈吵實驗移離住宅，以減少危險或滋擾。"},{"en":"If dangerous tests are moved to a lake, fewer buildings and people may be nearby.","zh":"如果危險測試移至湖上，附近可能有較少建築物和人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes relocating experiments for safety or space.","zh":"這個短語描述為安全或空間而搬遷實驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"make something easier to use","meaning":"令……更容易使用","examples":[{"en":"Dynamite made nitroglycerine safer and easier to use.","zh":"炸藥令硝酸甘油更安全、更容易使用。"},{"en":"To make something easier to use means to make it simpler, safer, or more practical to handle.","zh":"「make something easier to use」意思是令某物更簡單、更安全或更實用地處理。"},{"en":"A clear instruction sheet can make a new machine easier to use.","zh":"清楚說明書可以令新機器更容易使用。"},{"en":"If a dangerous liquid becomes a stable paste, workers can use it more safely.","zh":"如果危險液體變成穩定糊狀物，工人可以更安全地使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improving practical usability.","zh":"這個短語描述改善實際可用性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"along with","meaning":"連同；以及","examples":[{"en":"Nobel invented dynamite along with a detonator.","zh":"Nobel 發明炸藥，連同雷管。"},{"en":"Along with means together with or in addition to.","zh":"「along with」意思是連同或以及。"},{"en":"A student should bring a pencil along with an eraser to an exam.","zh":"學生應帶鉛筆以及橡皮擦去考試。"},{"en":"If an invention needs a second device to work safely, both may become important together.","zh":"如果一項發明需要第二個裝置才能安全運作，兩者可能一起變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase adds another related item.","zh":"這個短語加入另一個相關項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"dramatically lower the cost","meaning":"大幅降低成本","examples":[{"en":"The new inventions dramatically lowered the cost of construction work.","zh":"這些新發明大幅降低了建築工程成本。"},{"en":"To dramatically lower the cost means to reduce the price or expense by a large amount.","zh":"「dramatically lower the cost」意思是大幅減少價格或開支。"},{"en":"Online textbooks can dramatically lower the cost of study materials for students.","zh":"網上課本可以大幅降低學生學習材料成本。"},{"en":"If a tool makes work faster, it can lower labour costs and total project costs.","zh":"如果工具令工作更快，它可以降低勞工成本和項目總成本。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a very large cost reduction.","zh":"這個短語描述非常大的成本下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 166 - Alfred Nobel - The man behind the Nobel Prize.pdf","sourcePage":14}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 167":[{"front":"The Flavour Industry","meaning":"食品香味產業","examples":[{"en":"The flavour industry creates many of the tastes and aromas found in processed foods.","zh":"食品香味產業創造加工食品中許多味道和香氣。"},{"en":"The flavour industry is the business of designing, producing and selling flavours for food and drinks.","zh":"食品香味產業是為食品和飲品設計、生產和銷售香味的行業。"},{"en":"A snack company may hire the flavour industry to make crisps taste like barbecue or cheese.","zh":"零食公司可能聘請食品香味產業，使薯片有燒烤味或芝士味。"},{"en":"If processed food loses taste during manufacturing, the flavour industry can help restore it.","zh":"如果加工食品在製造過程中失去味道，食品香味產業可以幫助恢復味道。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a specialised food business, not simply ordinary cooking.","zh":"這個短語指專門的食品行業，而不只是普通烹飪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"read through","meaning":"仔細閱讀","examples":[{"en":"Consumers should read through the nutritional information on packaged food.","zh":"消費者應仔細閱讀包裝食品上的營養資料。"},{"en":"To read through something means to read it carefully from beginning to end.","zh":"“Read through” 某內容指由頭到尾仔細閱讀。"},{"en":"A student should read through the instructions before starting an exam paper.","zh":"學生開始做試卷前，應仔細閱讀指示。"},{"en":"If consumers read through food labels, they may notice sugar, sodium and flavouring ingredients.","zh":"如果消費者仔細閱讀食品標籤，可能會注意到糖、鈉和香味成分。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests careful reading, not just a quick look.","zh":"這個短語暗示仔細閱讀，而不是快速瞄一眼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"nutritional information","meaning":"營養資料","examples":[{"en":"Nutritional information helps consumers understand what a food product contains.","zh":"營養資料幫助消費者了解食品含有甚麼。"},{"en":"Nutritional information is the label information about calories, fat, sugar, salt, vitamins and other nutrients.","zh":"營養資料是關於卡路里、脂肪、糖、鹽、維他命和其他營養素的標籤資料。"},{"en":"Parents may check nutritional information before buying breakfast cereal for children.","zh":"家長為孩子購買早餐穀物前，可能查看營養資料。"},{"en":"If nutritional information shows high sugar, consumers may choose a healthier option.","zh":"如果營養資料顯示糖分高，消費者可能選擇較健康選項。"},{"en":"The phrase helps people judge food by content, not just taste or packaging.","zh":"這個短語幫助人根據成分判斷食品，而不只是看味道或包裝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"kitchen pantry","meaning":"廚房食品儲藏櫃","examples":[{"en":"Packaged foods are often stored in a kitchen pantry.","zh":"包裝食品常存放在廚房食品儲藏櫃中。"},{"en":"A kitchen pantry is a cupboard, shelf or small storage area where food is kept at home.","zh":"廚房食品儲藏櫃是在家中存放食物的櫃、架或小儲藏空間。"},{"en":"A family may keep rice, pasta, canned soup and snacks in the kitchen pantry.","zh":"家庭可能把米、意粉、罐頭湯和零食放在廚房食品儲藏櫃中。"},{"en":"If a pantry is full of packaged food, many labels may contain added flavourings.","zh":"如果食品儲藏櫃滿是包裝食品，許多標籤可能含有添加香味劑。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a home food-storage place.","zh":"這個短語指家中的食物儲存地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be likely to find","meaning":"很可能會發現","examples":[{"en":"You are likely to find flavouring ingredients on many food labels.","zh":"你很可能會在許多食品標籤上發現香味成分。"},{"en":"To be likely to find something means there is a good chance you will see or discover it.","zh":"“Be likely to find” 某物指你很有機會看見或發現它。"},{"en":"In a busy supermarket, you are likely to find several brands of instant noodles.","zh":"在繁忙超市中，你很可能會發現幾個品牌的即食麵。"},{"en":"If a product is highly processed, you are likely to find a long ingredients list.","zh":"如果產品高度加工，你很可能會發現很長的成分表。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses probability, not complete certainty.","zh":"這個短語表達可能性，而不是完全肯定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"innocuous-looking ingredient","meaning":"看似無害的成分","examples":[{"en":"Natural flavour may appear to be an innocuous-looking ingredient.","zh":"天然香味劑可能看起來是看似無害的成分。"},{"en":"An innocuous-looking ingredient is an ingredient that seems harmless or unimportant at first sight.","zh":"看似無害的成分，是初看似乎無害或不重要的成分。"},{"en":"A small amount of colouring on a label may look like an innocuous-looking ingredient to busy shoppers.","zh":"對忙碌購物者來說，標籤上一點色素可能看似無害。"},{"en":"If consumers do not understand an ingredient, its harmless appearance may hide a complex process.","zh":"如果消費者不了解某成分，其無害外觀可能掩蓋複雜加工過程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something that looks safe, though it may deserve closer attention.","zh":"這個短語描述看起來安全、但可能值得細看之物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"recur on a number of products","meaning":"重複出現於多種產品上","examples":[{"en":"The phrase “natural flavour” recurs on a number of food products.","zh":"“Natural flavour” 這個短語重複出現於多種食品上。"},{"en":"To recur on a number of products means to appear again and again on several different items.","zh":"“Recur on a number of products” 指在幾種不同產品上反覆出現。"},{"en":"The same warning may recur on a number of cleaning products in a supermarket.","zh":"同一警告可能重複出現於超市多種清潔產品上。"},{"en":"If one ingredient recurs on many labels, consumers may start wondering what it really means.","zh":"如果一種成分在許多標籤上重複出現，消費者可能開始想知道它真正意思。"},{"en":"The phrase describes repeated appearance across products.","zh":"這個短語描述在多種產品上的重複出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"natural flavour","meaning":"天然香味劑","examples":[{"en":"Natural flavour is added to many processed foods and drinks.","zh":"天然香味劑被加入許多加工食品和飲品中。"},{"en":"Natural flavour is a flavouring ingredient derived from natural sources but often processed industrially.","zh":"天然香味劑是源自天然來源、但常經工業加工的香味成分。"},{"en":"A fruit drink may contain natural flavour to make it taste more like fresh oranges.","zh":"水果飲品可能含有天然香味劑，使它味道更像新鮮橙。"},{"en":"If processing removes a food’s original taste, natural flavour may be added back in.","zh":"如果加工去除了食品原有味道，天然香味劑可能被重新加入。"},{"en":"The phrase can sound simple, but the production behind it may be complex.","zh":"這個短語聽起來簡單，但背後生產過程可能很複雜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the story of what…is","meaning":"關於……究竟是甚麼的來龍去脈","examples":[{"en":"The story of what natural flavour is turns out to be surprisingly complex.","zh":"關於天然香味劑究竟是甚麼的來龍去脈，結果出人意料地複雜。"},{"en":"The story of what something is means the full explanation of its nature, origin and meaning.","zh":"“The story of what…is” 指完整解釋某事物的本質、來源和意思。"},{"en":"The story of what a school rule is may include past accidents, parent concerns and teacher decisions.","zh":"關於一條校規究竟是甚麼的來龍去脈，可能包括過去意外、家長關注和老師決定。"},{"en":"If the story of an ingredient is complex, the label alone may not explain enough.","zh":"如果一種成分的來龍去脈很複雜，單靠標籤可能解釋不足。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for the deeper background behind a simple name.","zh":"這個短語追問簡單名稱背後的深層背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"how it got into your food","meaning":"它如何加入食物之中","examples":[{"en":"Few consumers know how flavouring gets into their food.","zh":"很少消費者知道香味劑如何加入他們的食物之中。"},{"en":"How it got into your food means the process by which an ingredient was added to what you eat.","zh":"“How it got into your food” 指某成分被加入你所吃食物的過程。"},{"en":"A child may ask how colouring got into a sweet after seeing a bright blue candy.","zh":"孩子看見鮮藍色糖果後，可能問色素如何加入糖果之中。"},{"en":"If people know how additives get into food, they can make more informed choices.","zh":"如果人們知道添加劑如何進入食物，就能作出更明智選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the hidden route from factory to plate.","zh":"這個短語強調由工廠到餐桌的隱藏路徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"where it came from","meaning":"它來自哪裏","examples":[{"en":"The label does not necessarily reveal where the flavour came from.","zh":"標籤不一定揭示香味來自哪裏。"},{"en":"Where it came from means the original source or origin of something.","zh":"“Where it came from” 指某事物的原本來源或起源。"},{"en":"A shopper may ask where a vegetable came from before deciding whether to buy it.","zh":"購物者可能先問蔬菜來自哪裏，再決定是否購買。"},{"en":"If a flavour’s source is unclear, consumers may not know whether it came from fruit, spice or another material.","zh":"如果香味來源不清楚，消費者可能不知道它來自水果、香料還是其他材料。"},{"en":"The phrase asks about origin, not just present use.","zh":"這個短語詢問來源，而不只是目前用途。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the result of","meaning":"……的結果","examples":[{"en":"The final taste is the result of several complex industrial processes.","zh":"最終味道是幾個複雜工業過程的結果。"},{"en":"The result of something is what happens because of it.","zh":"某事的結果，是因它而發生的事情。"},{"en":"A student’s high score may be the result of regular practice and careful feedback.","zh":"學生高分可能是定期練習和仔細回饋的結果。"},{"en":"If a flavour is the result of many processes, it did not simply come straight from fresh food.","zh":"如果香味是許多過程的結果，它就不是直接來自新鮮食物。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an outcome with its causes.","zh":"這個短語把結果與原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"more complex than you might imagine","meaning":"比你想像中更複雜","examples":[{"en":"The production of natural flavour is more complex than you might imagine.","zh":"天然香味劑的生產比你想像中更複雜。"},{"en":"More complex than you might imagine means involving more steps, details or difficulty than expected.","zh":"“More complex than you might imagine” 指包含比預期更多步驟、細節或困難。"},{"en":"Organising a school trip is more complex than you might imagine because safety, transport and parents must all be considered.","zh":"組織學校旅行比你想像中更複雜，因為安全、交通和家長都必須考慮。"},{"en":"If a simple label hides many factory processes, the product is more complex than it appears.","zh":"如果簡單標籤隱藏許多工廠過程，產品就比表面更複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase corrects an overly simple first impression.","zh":"這個短語糾正過於簡單的第一印象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"health watchdogs","meaning":"健康監察組織","examples":[{"en":"Health watchdogs began examining dietary cholesterol more closely.","zh":"健康監察組織開始更仔細檢視膳食膽固醇。"},{"en":"Health watchdogs are organisations or groups that monitor health risks and warn the public.","zh":"健康監察組織是監察健康風險並警告公眾的機構或團體。"},{"en":"A health watchdog may test popular drinks and report if they contain too much sugar.","zh":"健康監察組織可能測試流行飲品，並報告它們是否含糖過多。"},{"en":"If health watchdogs raise concerns, food companies may change ingredients or labels.","zh":"如果健康監察組織提出關注，食品公司可能改變成分或標籤。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests public-health supervision and pressure.","zh":"這個短語暗示公共健康監督和壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"nutritionists","meaning":"營養學家","examples":[{"en":"Nutritionists study how food affects human health.","zh":"營養學家研究食物如何影響人類健康。"},{"en":"Nutritionists are experts who study diet, nutrients and their effects on the body.","zh":"營養學家是研究飲食、營養素及其對身體影響的專家。"},{"en":"A nutritionist may advise a patient to reduce sugary drinks and eat more vegetables.","zh":"營養學家可能建議病人減少含糖飲品並多吃蔬菜。"},{"en":"If nutritionists warn about an ingredient, consumers may become more careful.","zh":"如果營養學家警告某成分，消費者可能變得更小心。"},{"en":"The word refers to food-and-health specialists.","zh":"這個詞指食物與健康方面的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"turn one’s attention to","meaning":"將注意力轉向……","examples":[{"en":"Researchers began turning their attention to cholesterol in the 1980s.","zh":"研究人員在1980年代開始將注意力轉向膽固醇。"},{"en":"To turn one’s attention to something means to start focusing on it.","zh":"“Turn one’s attention to” 某事指開始集中關注它。"},{"en":"After solving the timetable problem, the head teacher turned her attention to student attendance.","zh":"解決時間表問題後，校長將注意力轉向學生出席率。"},{"en":"If scientists turn their attention to a nutrient, more studies and public discussion may follow.","zh":"如果科學家將注意力轉向某營養素，可能會有更多研究和公眾討論。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a shift in focus.","zh":"這個短語顯示焦點轉移。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cholesterol","meaning":"膽固醇","examples":[{"en":"Cholesterol is found mainly in animal-sourced foods.","zh":"膽固醇主要存在於動物來源食品中。"},{"en":"Cholesterol is a waxy substance in the body and in some foods, especially animal products.","zh":"膽固醇是身體和某些食物中的蠟狀物質，尤其存在於動物產品。"},{"en":"A doctor may ask a patient to check cholesterol levels after a blood test.","zh":"醫生可能在驗血後要求病人檢查膽固醇水平。"},{"en":"If a diet contains too much unhealthy fat, cholesterol concerns may increase.","zh":"如果飲食含有太多不健康脂肪，膽固醇方面的擔憂可能增加。"},{"en":"The word is often used in discussions of heart health and diet.","zh":"這個詞常用於心臟健康和飲食討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"waxy steroid metabolite","meaning":"蠟狀類固醇代謝物","examples":[{"en":"Cholesterol is a waxy steroid metabolite found in the body.","zh":"膽固醇是人體中發現的一種蠟狀類固醇代謝物。"},{"en":"A waxy steroid metabolite is a fat-like chemical substance produced or used in body processes.","zh":"蠟狀類固醇代謝物是身體過程中產生或使用的類脂肪化學物質。"},{"en":"In science lessons, students may learn that some body chemicals feel oily or waxy rather than watery.","zh":"在科學課中，學生可能學到某些身體化學物質感覺像油或蠟，而不是水。"},{"en":"If a substance is a metabolite, it is connected with chemical changes inside living cells.","zh":"如果某物是代謝物，它就與活細胞內的化學變化有關。"},{"en":"The phrase is technical and describes cholesterol’s chemical nature.","zh":"這個短語較技術性，描述膽固醇的化學性質。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"mainly consume from","meaning":"主要從……攝取","examples":[{"en":"People mainly consume dietary cholesterol from animal-sourced products.","zh":"人們主要從動物來源產品攝取膳食膽固醇。"},{"en":"To mainly consume something from a source means to get most of it from that source.","zh":"“Mainly consume something from” 某來源指大部分從該來源取得某物。"},{"en":"Many students mainly consume caffeine from coffee or energy drinks.","zh":"許多學生主要從咖啡或能量飲品攝取咖啡因。"},{"en":"If people mainly consume cholesterol from animal products, changing those foods can affect intake.","zh":"如果人們主要從動物產品攝取膽固醇，改變這些食物就能影響攝取量。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the primary source of consumption.","zh":"這個短語指出攝取的主要來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"animal-sourced products","meaning":"動物來源產品","examples":[{"en":"Cheese, egg yolks and meat are animal-sourced products.","zh":"芝士、蛋黃和肉類是動物來源產品。"},{"en":"Animal-sourced products are foods or materials that come from animals.","zh":"動物來源產品是來自動物的食物或材料。"},{"en":"Milk, chicken, fish and butter are common animal-sourced products in many diets.","zh":"牛奶、雞肉、魚和牛油是許多飲食中常見的動物來源產品。"},{"en":"If a person avoids animal-sourced products, they may follow a vegan diet.","zh":"如果一個人避免動物來源產品，他可能遵循純素飲食。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts animal-based items with plant-based ones.","zh":"這個短語把動物性項目與植物性項目作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"egg yolks","meaning":"蛋黃","examples":[{"en":"Egg yolks contain significant amounts of cholesterol.","zh":"蛋黃含有相當多膽固醇。"},{"en":"Egg yolks are the yellow central parts of eggs.","zh":"蛋黃是雞蛋中央的黃色部分。"},{"en":"Bakers may use egg yolks to make cakes richer and custards thicker.","zh":"烘焙師可能使用蛋黃，使蛋糕更香濃，吉士更濃稠。"},{"en":"Because egg yolks contain fat and cholesterol, some people limit how often they eat them.","zh":"因為蛋黃含脂肪和膽固醇，有些人限制食用頻率。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to one specific part of an egg, not the whole egg.","zh":"這個短語指雞蛋中的特定部分，而不是整隻蛋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"poultry","meaning":"家禽肉","examples":[{"en":"Poultry is one of the animal-sourced foods mentioned in the passage.","zh":"家禽肉是文章提到的動物來源食品之一。"},{"en":"Poultry means meat from birds such as chickens, ducks and turkeys.","zh":"家禽肉指來自雞、鴨和火雞等鳥類的肉。"},{"en":"A supermarket may sell poultry beside beef, pork and fish.","zh":"超市可能把家禽肉放在牛肉、豬肉和魚旁邊出售。"},{"en":"If people reduce red meat, they may choose poultry as an alternative source of protein.","zh":"如果人們減少紅肉，可能選擇家禽肉作為替代蛋白質來源。"},{"en":"The word refers to bird meat used as food.","zh":"這個詞指用作食物的鳥類肉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"blame something for contributing to","meaning":"指責……導致","examples":[{"en":"Nutritionists blamed cholesterol for contributing to several health problems.","zh":"營養學家指責膽固醇導致幾種健康問題。"},{"en":"To blame something for contributing to a problem means to say it is one cause of that problem.","zh":"“Blame something for contributing to” 某問題指說它是該問題的原因之一。"},{"en":"Parents may blame late-night phone use for contributing to poor sleep.","zh":"家長可能指責深夜使用手機導致睡眠差。"},{"en":"If researchers blame an ingredient for health problems, companies may face pressure to change recipes.","zh":"如果研究人員指責某成分導致健康問題，公司可能面對改變配方的壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase links criticism with a partial cause.","zh":"這個短語把批評與部分原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"growing rates of","meaning":"日益上升的……比率","examples":[{"en":"Researchers were concerned about the growing rates of obesity and diabetes.","zh":"研究人員關注肥胖症和糖尿病日益上升的比率。"},{"en":"Growing rates of something mean that the number or percentage is increasing.","zh":"日益上升的某事比率指數量或百分比正在增加。"},{"en":"Schools may worry about growing rates of student stress before public exams.","zh":"學校可能擔心公開考試前學生壓力日益上升的比率。"},{"en":"If growing rates of disease appear, health experts may investigate diet and lifestyle.","zh":"如果疾病比率日益上升，健康專家可能調查飲食和生活方式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a rising trend.","zh":"這個短語描述上升趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"obesity","meaning":"肥胖症","examples":[{"en":"Obesity is associated with numerous long-term health risks.","zh":"肥胖症與許多長期健康風險有關。"},{"en":"Obesity is a medical condition in which a person has too much body fat in a way that may harm health.","zh":"肥胖症是一種醫學狀況，指一個人體內脂肪過多，可能傷害健康。"},{"en":"A doctor may discuss obesity with a patient by looking at weight, diet, activity and other health signs.","zh":"醫生可能透過檢視體重、飲食、活動和其他健康指標，與病人討論肥胖症。"},{"en":"Obesity can increase the risk of diabetes, heart disease and joint problems.","zh":"肥胖症可以增加糖尿病、心臟病和關節問題風險。"},{"en":"The word refers to a health condition, not simply appearance.","zh":"這個詞指健康狀況，而不只是外貌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"heart disease","meaning":"心臟病","examples":[{"en":"Diet is one of several factors associated with heart disease.","zh":"飲食是與心臟病相關的幾個因素之一。"},{"en":"Heart disease refers to medical problems that affect the heart and blood vessels.","zh":"心臟病指影響心臟和血管的醫學問題。"},{"en":"A doctor may advise exercise and balanced eating to reduce the risk of heart disease.","zh":"醫生可能建議運動和均衡飲食，以減低心臟病風險。"},{"en":"If a diet is high in unhealthy fat and salt, heart disease risk may increase.","zh":"如果飲食中不健康脂肪和鹽分高，心臟病風險可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used in health and nutrition discussions.","zh":"這個短語常用於健康和營養討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"diabetes","meaning":"糖尿病","examples":[{"en":"Diabetes has become increasingly common in many societies.","zh":"糖尿病在許多社會中變得越來越常見。"},{"en":"Diabetes is a condition in which the body cannot control blood sugar properly.","zh":"糖尿病是一種身體無法正常控制血糖的疾病。"},{"en":"A person with diabetes may need to monitor food, exercise and medicine carefully.","zh":"糖尿病患者可能需要仔細監察食物、運動和藥物。"},{"en":"If diabetes is not managed, it can damage nerves, kidneys and eyesight.","zh":"如果糖尿病沒有管理好，可能損害神經、腎臟和視力。"},{"en":"The word refers to a serious long-term health condition.","zh":"這個詞指嚴重的長期健康問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Western societies","meaning":"西方社會","examples":[{"en":"Processed foods form a large part of the diet in many Western societies.","zh":"在許多西方社會中，加工食品構成飲食的一大部分。"},{"en":"Western societies are societies in regions such as Europe, North America and countries shaped by similar cultural traditions.","zh":"西方社會是指歐洲、北美等地區，以及受相似文化傳統影響的國家。"},{"en":"In many Western societies, busy workers often rely on packaged meals and takeaway food.","zh":"在許多西方社會，忙碌工人常依賴包裝餐和外賣食品。"},{"en":"If processed food becomes common in Western societies, diet-related health concerns may rise.","zh":"如果加工食品在西方社會變得常見，與飲食有關的健康關注可能上升。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a broad cultural and geographical group, not one single country.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛文化和地理群體，而不是單一國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"public awareness of","meaning":"公眾對……的認識","examples":[{"en":"Public awareness of the health effects of diet gradually increased.","zh":"公眾對飲食健康影響的認識逐漸提高。"},{"en":"Public awareness of something means how much ordinary people know and care about it.","zh":"公眾對某事的認識，指普通人對它知道和關心的程度。"},{"en":"Public awareness of recycling rose after schools and shops began campaigns.","zh":"學校和商店開始宣傳後，公眾對回收的認識提高。"},{"en":"If public awareness of nutrition grows, companies may change labels and ingredients.","zh":"如果公眾對營養的認識提高，公司可能改變標籤和成分。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on what the general public understands.","zh":"這個短語強調一般公眾理解甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as awareness grew","meaning":"隨着認知提高","examples":[{"en":"As public awareness grew, food companies changed some of their practices.","zh":"隨着公眾認知提高，食品公司改變了部分做法。"},{"en":"As awareness grew means while people gradually became more informed about an issue.","zh":"“As awareness grew” 指當人們逐漸更了解某議題時。"},{"en":"As awareness of cyberbullying grew, schools introduced clearer online-behaviour rules.","zh":"隨着對網絡欺凌的認知提高，學校引入更清晰的網上行為規則。"},{"en":"If awareness of health risks grows, consumers may demand safer products.","zh":"如果對健康風險的認知提高，消費者可能要求更安全產品。"},{"en":"The phrase links increased understanding with later action.","zh":"這個短語把理解增加與後續行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stop cooking something in","meaning":"停止使用……烹調某物","examples":[{"en":"McDonald’s stopped cooking its French fries in beef tallow.","zh":"麥當勞停止使用牛脂烹調炸薯條。"},{"en":"To stop cooking something in an ingredient means to no longer use that ingredient as the cooking medium.","zh":"“Stop cooking something in” 某成分指不再使用該成分作烹調媒介。"},{"en":"A family may stop cooking vegetables in butter and use olive oil instead.","zh":"家庭可能停止使用牛油煮蔬菜，改用橄欖油。"},{"en":"If a restaurant stops cooking food in animal fat, the flavour and nutritional content may change.","zh":"如果餐廳停止使用動物脂肪烹調食物，味道和營養含量可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing the fat, oil or liquid used for cooking.","zh":"這個短語描述改變烹調所用的脂肪、油或液體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"French fries","meaning":"炸薯條","examples":[{"en":"The flavour of McDonald’s French fries changed when the cooking oil changed.","zh":"當烹調油改變，麥當勞炸薯條的味道也改變。"},{"en":"French fries are thin pieces of potato fried in oil and often served with salt.","zh":"炸薯條是切成細條並在油中炸熟、常加鹽食用的薯仔。"},{"en":"Many children order French fries with burgers or chicken meals.","zh":"許多孩子點漢堡或雞餐時會配炸薯條。"},{"en":"If French fries are cooked in different oil, their smell, texture and taste can change.","zh":"如果炸薯條用不同油烹調，其氣味、質感和味道都可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a common fried potato food.","zh":"這個短語指常見的油炸薯仔食品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cottonseed oil","meaning":"棉籽油","examples":[{"en":"Cottonseed oil was once mixed with beef tallow for frying.","zh":"棉籽油曾與牛脂混合用來油炸。"},{"en":"Cottonseed oil is a vegetable oil made from the seeds of cotton plants.","zh":"棉籽油是由棉花植物種子製成的植物油。"},{"en":"A food factory may use cottonseed oil because it can handle high cooking temperatures.","zh":"食品工廠可能使用棉籽油，因為它能承受高烹調溫度。"},{"en":"If cottonseed oil is mixed with another fat, the final flavour may change.","zh":"如果棉籽油與另一種脂肪混合，最終味道可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a plant-based cooking oil.","zh":"這個短語指一種植物性食用油。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"beef tallow","meaning":"牛脂","examples":[{"en":"Beef tallow gave the fries a distinctive taste and aroma.","zh":"牛脂賦予炸薯條獨特味道和香氣。"},{"en":"Beef tallow is rendered fat from cattle, used in cooking or food production.","zh":"牛脂是由牛提煉出的脂肪，用於烹調或食品生產。"},{"en":"Some old recipes use beef tallow because it gives fried food a rich flavour.","zh":"一些舊食譜使用牛脂，因為它令油炸食品味道濃郁。"},{"en":"If beef tallow is removed from a recipe, the food may lose part of its original aroma.","zh":"如果牛脂從配方中移除，食物可能失去部分原有香氣。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to animal fat, not vegetable oil.","zh":"這個短語指動物脂肪，而不是植物油。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"restaurant chain","meaning":"連鎖餐廳","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant chain changed to vegetable oil in 1990.","zh":"這間連鎖餐廳在1990年改用植物油。"},{"en":"A restaurant chain is a group of restaurants with the same brand and similar menu in many locations.","zh":"連鎖餐廳是在許多地點使用同一品牌和相似餐牌的一組餐廳。"},{"en":"A restaurant chain may sell the same burger in different cities or countries.","zh":"連鎖餐廳可能在不同城市或國家出售同一款漢堡。"},{"en":"If a restaurant chain changes one ingredient, millions of meals may be affected.","zh":"如果連鎖餐廳改變一種成分，數以百萬計餐點都可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a business with repeated restaurant outlets.","zh":"這個短語指擁有重複餐廳分店的企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"use vegetable oil instead","meaning":"改用植物油","examples":[{"en":"The company began using vegetable oil instead of animal fat.","zh":"該公司開始改用植物油，而不是動物脂肪。"},{"en":"To use vegetable oil instead means to replace another fat or oil with oil from plants.","zh":"“Use vegetable oil instead” 指用植物來源油取代另一種脂肪或油。"},{"en":"A family may use vegetable oil instead of butter when cooking for someone who avoids dairy.","zh":"家庭為避免奶類的人煮食時，可能改用植物油而不是牛油。"},{"en":"If a company uses vegetable oil instead of beef fat, cholesterol content may fall but flavour may change.","zh":"如果公司改用植物油而不是牛脂，膽固醇含量可能下降，但味道可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly shows replacement.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示替代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"substantially lower","meaning":"大幅降低","examples":[{"en":"The change substantially lowered the cholesterol content of the fries.","zh":"這項改變大幅降低了炸薯條的膽固醇含量。"},{"en":"To substantially lower something means to reduce it by a large or meaningful amount.","zh":"“Substantially lower” 某事指以大幅或有意義的程度減少它。"},{"en":"Turning off unused lights can substantially lower a school’s electricity bill over a year.","zh":"關掉不用的燈，一年下來可以大幅降低學校電費。"},{"en":"If an ingredient change substantially lowers cholesterol, it may answer some health concerns.","zh":"如果成分改變大幅降低膽固醇，就可能回應部分健康關注。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a significant reduction, not a tiny one.","zh":"這個短語暗示顯著減少，而不是微小下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cholesterol content","meaning":"膽固醇含量","examples":[{"en":"The new cooking oil reduced the cholesterol content of the product.","zh":"新烹調油降低了產品的膽固醇含量。"},{"en":"Cholesterol content is the amount of cholesterol contained in a food.","zh":"膽固醇含量是食品中所含膽固醇的份量。"},{"en":"A person with heart concerns may compare the cholesterol content of different meals.","zh":"有心臟健康關注的人可能比較不同餐點的膽固醇含量。"},{"en":"If cholesterol content is lowered, the product may seem healthier to consumers.","zh":"如果膽固醇含量降低，產品對消費者來說可能顯得較健康。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a measurable nutritional amount.","zh":"這個短語指可量度的營養份量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"create a new dilemma","meaning":"造成新的兩難局面","examples":[{"en":"Reducing cholesterol created a new dilemma concerning flavour.","zh":"減少膽固醇造成了關於味道的新兩難局面。"},{"en":"To create a new dilemma means to solve one problem but produce a difficult choice or new problem.","zh":"“Create a new dilemma” 指解決一個問題，卻產生困難選擇或新問題。"},{"en":"A school may create a new dilemma if it bans phones but students need them for online homework.","zh":"如果學校禁止手機，但學生又需要手機做網上功課，就可能造成新兩難局面。"},{"en":"If healthier oil removes flavour, a company must choose between nutrition and taste.","zh":"如果較健康的油去除了味道，公司就必須在營養與味道之間選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a problem with two competing needs.","zh":"這個短語描述兩種需要互相競爭的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"give something a rich aroma","meaning":"賦予……濃郁香氣","examples":[{"en":"The old oil mixture gave the fries a rich aroma.","zh":"舊油混合物賦予炸薯條濃郁香氣。"},{"en":"To give something a rich aroma means to make it smell strong, deep and pleasant.","zh":"“Give something a rich aroma” 指令某物聞起來強烈、深厚而令人愉快。"},{"en":"Garlic and butter can give bread a rich aroma when it is baked.","zh":"烤麵包時，蒜和牛油可以賦予麵包濃郁香氣。"},{"en":"If an ingredient gives food a rich aroma, removing it may make the food seem less satisfying.","zh":"如果某成分賦予食物濃郁香氣，移除它可能令食物感覺沒那麼滿足。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on smell, not only taste.","zh":"這個短語強調氣味，而不只是味道。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mouthfeel","meaning":"入口質感","examples":[{"en":"Fat strongly influences the mouthfeel of fried food.","zh":"脂肪強烈影響油炸食品的入口質感。"},{"en":"Mouthfeel is the way food feels in the mouth, such as creamy, crispy, smooth or oily.","zh":"入口質感是食物在口中感覺如何，例如香滑、酥脆、順滑或油潤。"},{"en":"A yoghurt may taste good but have poor mouthfeel if it feels watery and thin.","zh":"乳酪可能味道不錯，但如果感覺水汪汪又稀薄，入口質感就差。"},{"en":"If fat is reduced, the mouthfeel of a food may become lighter or less rich.","zh":"如果脂肪減少，食物入口質感可能變得較輕或不夠濃厚。"},{"en":"The word describes texture as experienced while eating.","zh":"這個詞描述進食時感受到的質地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"food critic","meaning":"美食評論家","examples":[{"en":"James Beard was a well-known American food critic.","zh":"James Beard 是一位著名美國美食評論家。"},{"en":"A food critic is a person who reviews food, restaurants and cooking professionally.","zh":"美食評論家是專業評論食物、餐廳和烹飪的人。"},{"en":"A food critic may write about whether a new restaurant’s dishes are creative and balanced.","zh":"美食評論家可能撰文評論新餐廳菜式是否有創意和平衡。"},{"en":"If a food critic praises a meal, more customers may become curious about it.","zh":"如果美食評論家稱讚一餐，更多顧客可能對它感到好奇。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to someone who judges food as part of their work.","zh":"這個短語指以評論食物為工作的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"admit that","meaning":"承認","examples":[{"en":"The critic admitted that he enjoyed the fries’ rich mouthfeel.","zh":"這位評論家承認他喜歡炸薯條濃厚的入口質感。"},{"en":"To admit that something is true means to say it honestly, especially when it may be surprising or inconvenient.","zh":"“Admit that” 某事為真指誠實說出它，尤其當它可能令人意外或不方便時。"},{"en":"A student may admit that they did not prepare enough for the test.","zh":"學生可能承認自己沒有充分準備測驗。"},{"en":"If a critic admits liking an unhealthy food, the statement may feel more honest and human.","zh":"如果評論家承認喜歡不健康食品，該說法可能感覺更真誠和有人性。"},{"en":"The phrase often introduces a frank confession or acknowledgement.","zh":"這個短語常引出坦白承認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"bland in comparison","meaning":"相比之下味道較淡","examples":[{"en":"Pure vegetable oil tasted bland in comparison with the old mixture.","zh":"純植物油與舊混合物相比味道較淡。"},{"en":"Bland in comparison means much less strong, interesting or flavourful than something else.","zh":"“Bland in comparison” 指與另一物相比，味道、趣味或效果弱得多。"},{"en":"A plain soup may taste bland in comparison with one cooked with herbs and stock.","zh":"清湯與加入香草和高湯煮成的湯相比，可能味道較淡。"},{"en":"If a healthier recipe tastes bland in comparison, customers may reject the change.","zh":"如果較健康配方相比之下味道較淡，顧客可能拒絕改變。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a contrast in taste or impact.","zh":"這個短語製造味道或效果上的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"current ingredients list","meaning":"現時的成分表","examples":[{"en":"The current ingredients list reveals how the flavour was restored.","zh":"現時的成分表揭示味道如何被恢復。"},{"en":"The current ingredients list is the present label showing what a product contains.","zh":"現時的成分表是目前標籤上顯示產品含有甚麼的列表。"},{"en":"A shopper may check the current ingredients list to see whether a recipe has changed.","zh":"購物者可能查看現時成分表，看配方是否改變。"},{"en":"If the ingredients list includes natural flavour, it may explain how taste was added back.","zh":"如果成分表包括天然香味劑，就可能解釋味道如何被重新加入。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to today’s official list of product ingredients.","zh":"這個短語指今日官方列出的產品成分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"overcome a predicament","meaning":"克服困境","examples":[{"en":"The company used natural flavour to overcome the predicament.","zh":"該公司使用天然香味劑克服困境。"},{"en":"To overcome a predicament means to find a way out of a difficult or awkward problem.","zh":"“Overcome a predicament” 指找到方法擺脫困難或尷尬問題。"},{"en":"A teacher may overcome a predicament by moving an outdoor lesson indoors when it rains.","zh":"下雨時，老師可能把戶外課移到室內，以克服困境。"},{"en":"If a company loses flavour after changing oil, adding flavouring may solve the problem.","zh":"如果公司換油後失去味道，加入香味劑可能解決問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dealing successfully with a tricky situation.","zh":"這個短語描述成功處理棘手情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"aside from","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"Aside from preservatives, the fries contain three principal ingredients.","zh":"除了防腐劑之外，炸薯條含有三種主要成分。"},{"en":"Aside from means except for or in addition to something being set apart.","zh":"“Aside from” 指除了某事之外，或把某事先放在一旁。"},{"en":"Aside from homework, students also need time to rest and exercise.","zh":"除了功課之外，學生也需要時間休息和運動。"},{"en":"If a label says aside from preservatives, it separates them from the main ingredients being discussed.","zh":"如果標籤說除了防腐劑之外，就是把它們與正在討論的主要成分分開。"},{"en":"The phrase helps exclude or set aside one part before focusing on another.","zh":"這個短語幫助先排除或放下一部分，再集中另一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"preservatives","meaning":"防腐劑","examples":[{"en":"Preservatives help packaged foods remain safe for longer.","zh":"防腐劑幫助包裝食品更長時間保持安全。"},{"en":"Preservatives are substances added to food to slow spoilage and extend shelf life.","zh":"防腐劑是加入食品中以減慢變壞並延長保存期的物質。"},{"en":"Jam, canned soup and packaged bread may contain preservatives.","zh":"果醬、罐頭湯和包裝麵包可能含有防腐劑。"},{"en":"If preservatives are not used, some foods may spoil faster or become unsafe.","zh":"如果不使用防腐劑，一些食品可能更快變壞或變得不安全。"},{"en":"The word refers to ingredients that help food last longer.","zh":"這個詞指幫助食物保存更久的成分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"essentially","meaning":"基本上；實質上","examples":[{"en":"The product essentially contains potato, oil and flavouring.","zh":"該產品基本上含有薯仔、油和香味劑。"},{"en":"Essentially means basically or in its most important form.","zh":"“Essentially” 指基本上或以最重要形式來說。"},{"en":"A simple sandwich is essentially bread with filling between the slices.","zh":"簡單三文治基本上是在兩片麵包之間加入餡料。"},{"en":"If a long label essentially reduces to three main ingredients, the basic structure is easier to understand.","zh":"如果長標籤實質上可歸納為三種主要成分，基本結構就較容易理解。"},{"en":"The word simplifies a complicated description.","zh":"這個詞把複雜描述簡化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"main ingredients","meaning":"主要成分","examples":[{"en":"The main ingredients are potato, soybean oil and natural flavour.","zh":"主要成分是薯仔、大豆油和天然香味劑。"},{"en":"Main ingredients are the most important or largest ingredients in a product or recipe.","zh":"主要成分是產品或食譜中最重要或份量最大的成分。"},{"en":"The main ingredients of a salad may be lettuce, tomatoes and dressing.","zh":"沙律的主要成分可能是生菜、番茄和醬汁。"},{"en":"If consumers know the main ingredients, they can understand what the food is mostly made of.","zh":"如果消費者知道主要成分，就能理解食物主要由甚麼製成。"},{"en":"The phrase separates central components from minor additives.","zh":"這個短語把核心成分與少量添加劑分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"soybean oil","meaning":"大豆油","examples":[{"en":"Soybean oil is commonly used in processed and fried foods.","zh":"大豆油常用於加工食品和油炸食品。"},{"en":"Soybean oil is vegetable oil made from soybeans.","zh":"大豆油是由大豆製成的植物油。"},{"en":"A food factory may use soybean oil for frying snacks or making sauces.","zh":"食品工廠可能使用大豆油油炸零食或製作醬汁。"},{"en":"If soybean oil replaces animal fat, cholesterol may be reduced but flavour may need adjustment.","zh":"如果大豆油取代動物脂肪，膽固醇可能降低，但味道可能需要調整。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a common plant-based oil.","zh":"這個短語指常見植物油。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mysterious component","meaning":"神秘成分","examples":[{"en":"Natural flavour is the most mysterious component on the ingredients list.","zh":"天然香味劑是成分表上最神秘的成分。"},{"en":"A mysterious component is a part of something whose nature or purpose is not immediately clear.","zh":"神秘成分是某物中本質或用途不會立即清楚的一部分。"},{"en":"A student may find a mysterious component inside a toy and wonder what it does.","zh":"學生可能在玩具內發現神秘零件，並好奇它有甚麼作用。"},{"en":"If an ingredient is mysterious, consumers may need more explanation than the label provides.","zh":"如果一種成分神秘，消費者可能需要比標籤更多的解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests uncertainty about one part of a larger whole.","zh":"這個短語暗示對整體中某一部分的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"enter our diet through","meaning":"透過……進入我們的飲食","examples":[{"en":"Natural flavour entered our diet through the rise of processed foods.","zh":"天然香味劑透過加工食品的興起進入我們的飲食。"},{"en":"To enter our diet through something means to become part of what we eat because of that route or change.","zh":"“Enter our diet through” 某事指因某途徑或變化而成為我們所吃東西的一部分。"},{"en":"More sugar entered children’s diets through sweetened drinks and packaged snacks.","zh":"更多糖分透過加糖飲品和包裝零食進入兒童飲食。"},{"en":"If processed food spreads, certain additives can enter everyday diets without people noticing.","zh":"如果加工食品擴散，某些添加劑可能在人們不察覺下進入日常飲食。"},{"en":"The phrase explains how a substance becomes common in food habits.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物如何在飲食習慣中變得常見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the rise of processed foods","meaning":"加工食品的興起","examples":[{"en":"The rise of processed foods increased demand for manufactured flavours.","zh":"加工食品的興起增加了對製造香味的需求。"},{"en":"The rise of processed foods means the growing popularity and availability of industrially prepared food.","zh":"加工食品的興起指工業製備食品越來越受歡迎和容易取得。"},{"en":"The rise of processed foods can be seen in supermarkets full of packaged meals and snacks.","zh":"超市充滿包裝餐和零食，顯示加工食品的興起。"},{"en":"If processed foods rise, companies need flavours that survive factories, transport and storage.","zh":"如果加工食品興起，公司就需要能承受工廠、運輸和儲存的香味。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a major change in modern eating habits.","zh":"這個短語描述現代飲食習慣的重大改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"processed foods","meaning":"加工食品","examples":[{"en":"Processed foods often contain added flavourings, colours and preservatives.","zh":"加工食品常含有添加香味劑、色素和防腐劑。"},{"en":"Processed foods are foods changed from their original state by industrial or mechanical methods.","zh":"加工食品是透過工業或機械方法從原本狀態改變而成的食品。"},{"en":"Instant noodles, canned soup and packaged biscuits are common processed foods.","zh":"即食麵、罐頭湯和包裝餅乾是常見加工食品。"},{"en":"If foods are heavily processed, original taste and texture may need to be rebuilt.","zh":"如果食品高度加工，原有味道和質感可能需要被重建。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts factory-prepared food with fresh, minimally changed food.","zh":"這個短語把工廠製備食品與新鮮、少加工食品作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"make up more than","meaning":"佔超過……","examples":[{"en":"Processed foods make up more than 90 per cent of the American diet.","zh":"加工食品佔美國飲食超過90%。"},{"en":"To make up more than a percentage means to form a larger share than that amount.","zh":"“Make up more than” 某百分比指構成比該數量更大的比例。"},{"en":"Homework may make up more than 30 per cent of a student’s final grade.","zh":"功課可能佔學生最終成績超過30%。"},{"en":"If processed foods make up most of a diet, their ingredients become a major health issue.","zh":"如果加工食品佔飲食大部分，其成分就成為重大健康議題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes proportion or share.","zh":"這個短語描述比例或份額。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the proportion is growing","meaning":"所佔比例正在增加","examples":[{"en":"Processed foods already dominate the diet, and the proportion is growing.","zh":"加工食品已主導飲食，而且所佔比例正在增加。"},{"en":"The proportion is growing means the share or percentage is increasing.","zh":"“The proportion is growing” 指份額或百分比正在上升。"},{"en":"In many classes, the proportion of students using tablets for notes is growing.","zh":"在許多班級中，使用平板記筆記的學生比例正在增加。"},{"en":"If the proportion of processed food grows, people may consume more additives without intending to.","zh":"如果加工食品比例增加，人們可能在無意間攝取更多添加劑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an increasing share of a whole.","zh":"這個短語描述整體中不斷增加的份額。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"represent a burgeoning industry","meaning":"構成迅速發展的產業","examples":[{"en":"Processed food represents a burgeoning industry in several developing countries.","zh":"加工食品在幾個發展中國家構成迅速發展的產業。"},{"en":"To represent a burgeoning industry means to be part of a business area that is growing quickly.","zh":"“Represent a burgeoning industry” 指屬於一個快速增長的商業領域。"},{"en":"Online tutoring represents a burgeoning industry where many families seek extra support.","zh":"網上補習構成迅速發展的產業，許多家庭在其中尋求額外支援。"},{"en":"If demand rises fast, a small market can become a burgeoning industry.","zh":"如果需求快速上升，小市場可以變成迅速發展的產業。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a product area with rapid business growth.","zh":"這個短語把產品領域與快速商業增長連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"burgeoning industry","meaning":"迅速發展的產業","examples":[{"en":"Packaged food has become a burgeoning industry in Asia.","zh":"包裝食品在亞洲已成為迅速發展的產業。"},{"en":"A burgeoning industry is an industry that is growing rapidly and attracting more business activity.","zh":"迅速發展的產業是快速增長並吸引更多商業活動的行業。"},{"en":"Elderly care may become a burgeoning industry as the population ages.","zh":"隨着人口老化，長者護理可能成為迅速發展的產業。"},{"en":"If an industry is burgeoning, companies may invest heavily before the market becomes crowded.","zh":"如果一個產業迅速發展，公司可能在市場變得擁擠前大量投資。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests fast expansion and new opportunities.","zh":"這個短語暗示快速擴張和新機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"developing countries","meaning":"發展中國家","examples":[{"en":"Demand for processed food is increasing in many developing countries.","zh":"許多發展中國家對加工食品的需求正在增加。"},{"en":"Developing countries are countries whose economies, industries and public services are still growing and changing.","zh":"發展中國家是經濟、工業和公共服務仍在增長和變化中的國家。"},{"en":"In developing countries, supermarkets and packaged foods may spread quickly as incomes rise.","zh":"在發展中國家，隨着收入上升，超市和包裝食品可能快速擴散。"},{"en":"If processed foods become popular in developing countries, eating habits can change rapidly.","zh":"如果加工食品在發展中國家流行，飲食習慣可以迅速改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to countries still undergoing economic development.","zh":"這個短語指仍在經濟發展中的國家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be boxed, bagged, canned or packaged","meaning":"被裝盒、入袋、罐裝或包裝","examples":[{"en":"Processed foods may be boxed, bagged, canned or otherwise packaged.","zh":"加工食品可能被裝盒、入袋、罐裝或以其他方式包裝。"},{"en":"To be boxed, bagged, canned or packaged means to be placed in containers for storage and sale.","zh":"“Be boxed, bagged, canned or packaged” 指被放進容器中以便儲存和銷售。"},{"en":"Rice may be bagged, soup may be canned and biscuits may be boxed.","zh":"米可以入袋，湯可以罐裝，餅乾可以裝盒。"},{"en":"If food is packaged, it can be transported and stored more easily.","zh":"如果食物被包裝，就能更容易運輸和儲存。"},{"en":"The phrase lists common ways processed food is prepared for shops.","zh":"這個短語列出加工食品為商店準備的常見方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ingredients label","meaning":"成分標籤","examples":[{"en":"Processed products usually have an ingredients label.","zh":"加工產品通常有成分標籤。"},{"en":"An ingredients label is the part of a package that lists what the product contains.","zh":"成分標籤是包裝上列出產品含有甚麼的部分。"},{"en":"A shopper may read the ingredients label to check for peanuts or dairy.","zh":"購物者可能閱讀成分標籤，以檢查是否含花生或奶類。"},{"en":"If an ingredients label is long, the food may contain many additives or processed components.","zh":"如果成分標籤很長，食品可能含有許多添加劑或加工成分。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the label that tells consumers what is inside.","zh":"這個短語指告訴消費者內裏含有甚麼的標籤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"processing involves","meaning":"加工過程涉及","examples":[{"en":"Food processing sometimes involves adding salt, sugar or preservatives.","zh":"食品加工有時涉及添加鹽、糖或防腐劑。"},{"en":"Processing involves something means that thing is part of the process.","zh":"“Processing involves” 某事指該事是過程的一部分。"},{"en":"Making bread involves mixing, kneading, waiting and baking.","zh":"製作麵包涉及混合、搓揉、等待和烘焙。"},{"en":"If processing involves additives, the final food may differ greatly from the original ingredient.","zh":"如果加工過程涉及添加劑，最終食品可能與原材料非常不同。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what steps or actions are included.","zh":"這個短語解釋包括哪些步驟或行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"add sodium or sugar","meaning":"添加鈉或糖","examples":[{"en":"Manufacturers may add sodium or sugar to improve flavour or preservation.","zh":"製造商可能添加鈉或糖，以改善味道或保存效果。"},{"en":"To add sodium or sugar means to put salt-related substances or sweeteners into food.","zh":"“Add sodium or sugar” 指把含鹽相關物質或甜味劑加入食品。"},{"en":"A soup factory may add sodium so the soup tastes stronger and lasts longer.","zh":"湯品工廠可能添加鈉，使湯味道更濃並保存更久。"},{"en":"If companies add too much sodium or sugar, health concerns may increase.","zh":"如果公司添加過多鈉或糖，健康關注可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase points to common additions in processed food.","zh":"這個短語指出加工食品中的常見添加物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be coloured","meaning":"被加入色素","examples":[{"en":"Some processed foods are coloured to make them look more attractive.","zh":"一些加工食品被加入色素，以令它們看起來更吸引。"},{"en":"To be coloured means to have colour added or changed artificially or deliberately.","zh":"“Be coloured” 指被人工或有意地加入或改變顏色。"},{"en":"Sweets may be coloured brightly so children notice them on the shelf.","zh":"糖果可能被加入鮮艷色素，使孩子在貨架上注意到它們。"},{"en":"If food is coloured, it may look fresher or fruitier than it really is.","zh":"如果食物被加入色素，它可能看起來比實際更新鮮或更有水果味。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing appearance through colour.","zh":"這個短語描述透過顏色改變外觀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be bleached","meaning":"被漂白","examples":[{"en":"Certain food ingredients are bleached during industrial processing.","zh":"某些食品成分在工業加工過程中被漂白。"},{"en":"To be bleached means to be made lighter or whiter by chemical treatment.","zh":"“Be bleached” 指透過化學處理變得更淺色或更白。"},{"en":"Flour may be bleached to give it a cleaner white appearance.","zh":"麵粉可能被漂白，使其外觀更潔白。"},{"en":"If an ingredient is bleached, its colour changes even if its basic role stays the same.","zh":"如果成分被漂白，即使基本用途不變，其顏色也改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an industrial colour-lightening process.","zh":"這個短語描述工業上的淡化顏色過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be stabilised","meaning":"被加入穩定處理","examples":[{"en":"Processed foods may be stabilised to maintain a consistent texture.","zh":"加工食品可能被加入穩定處理，以保持一致質感。"},{"en":"To be stabilised means to be treated so a product stays steady and does not change easily.","zh":"“Be stabilised” 指被處理到產品保持穩定、不容易改變。"},{"en":"A sauce may be stabilised so it remains smooth on the supermarket shelf.","zh":"醬汁可能被加入穩定處理，使它在超市貨架上保持順滑。"},{"en":"If food is stabilised, it may look and feel the same for longer.","zh":"如果食物被穩定處理，它可能更長時間看起來和吃起來一樣。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making a product more consistent and reliable.","zh":"這個短語描述令產品更一致和可靠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be emulsified","meaning":"被乳化","examples":[{"en":"Some food products are emulsified to prevent their ingredients from separating.","zh":"一些食品被乳化，以防止成分分離。"},{"en":"To be emulsified means to be mixed so oil and water-based parts stay together.","zh":"“Be emulsified” 指被混合到油性和水性部分能保持結合。"},{"en":"Mayonnaise is emulsified so the oil, egg and vinegar form a smooth sauce.","zh":"蛋黃醬被乳化，使油、蛋和醋形成順滑醬汁。"},{"en":"If a dressing is not emulsified, it may separate into layers.","zh":"如果沙律醬沒有被乳化，可能分成幾層。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a process that keeps mixed ingredients united.","zh":"這個短語描述保持混合成分結合的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be dehydrated","meaning":"被脫水","examples":[{"en":"Food can be dehydrated to extend its storage life.","zh":"食物可以被脫水，以延長保存期。"},{"en":"To be dehydrated means to have water removed.","zh":"“Be dehydrated” 指水分被移除。"},{"en":"Fruit may be dehydrated to make dried mango or raisins.","zh":"水果可能被脫水，製成芒果乾或提子乾。"},{"en":"If food is dehydrated, bacteria may grow more slowly because there is less moisture.","zh":"如果食物被脫水，因為水分較少，細菌可能生長較慢。"},{"en":"The phrase describes removing water for preservation.","zh":"這個短語描述為保存而去除水分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be odour-concealed","meaning":"被掩蓋氣味","examples":[{"en":"Unpleasant smells may be odour-concealed during food processing.","zh":"食品加工期間，難聞氣味可能被掩蓋。"},{"en":"To be odour-concealed means to have an unpleasant smell hidden or masked.","zh":"“Be odour-concealed” 指難聞氣味被遮蓋或掩飾。"},{"en":"A rubbish bin may be odour-concealed with a scented cover, though the waste remains inside.","zh":"垃圾桶可能用香味蓋掩蓋氣味，雖然垃圾仍在內。"},{"en":"If a processed ingredient smells bad, manufacturers may conceal the odour before selling the product.","zh":"如果加工成分氣味難聞，製造商可能在出售產品前掩蓋氣味。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on hiding smell rather than removing the source.","zh":"這個短語強調掩蓋氣味，而不是移除來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be sweetened","meaning":"被加甜","examples":[{"en":"Many packaged foods are sweetened to appeal to consumers.","zh":"許多包裝食品被加甜，以吸引消費者。"},{"en":"To be sweetened means to have sugar or another sweetener added.","zh":"“Be sweetened” 指被加入糖或另一種甜味劑。"},{"en":"Plain yoghurt may be sweetened with fruit syrup to make it more attractive to children.","zh":"原味乳酪可能用水果糖漿加甜，使它對孩子更吸引。"},{"en":"If a food is heavily sweetened, it may taste pleasant but contain more sugar than expected.","zh":"如果食物被大量加甜，它可能味道愉快，但含糖量比預期高。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adding sweetness deliberately.","zh":"這個短語描述有意加入甜味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sap the original flavour from","meaning":"令……失去原有味道","examples":[{"en":"Heavy processing can sap the original flavour from a product.","zh":"大量加工可以令產品失去原有味道。"},{"en":"To sap the original flavour from something means to remove or weaken its natural taste.","zh":"“Sap the original flavour from” 某物指移除或削弱其天然味道。"},{"en":"Overboiling vegetables can sap the original flavour from them and leave them watery.","zh":"過度烚煮蔬菜會令它們失去原有味道，並變得水汪汪。"},{"en":"If industrial processing saps flavour from food, manufacturers may add flavouring later.","zh":"如果工業加工令食物失去味道，製造商可能之後加入香味劑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes loss of natural taste.","zh":"這個短語描述天然味道流失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be added back in","meaning":"被重新加入","examples":[{"en":"Flavour must often be added back in after processing.","zh":"加工後，味道往往必須被重新加入。"},{"en":"To be added back in means to be put into something again after it was removed or lost.","zh":"“Be added back in” 指某物被移除或流失後再次放入。"},{"en":"If soup tastes weak after extra water is added, salt may be added back in.","zh":"如果加水後湯味變淡，鹽可能被重新加入。"},{"en":"When processing removes aroma, flavourings can be added back in to restore taste.","zh":"當加工去除香氣，香味劑可以被重新加入以恢復味道。"},{"en":"The phrase describes restoring something that disappeared earlier.","zh":"這個短語描述恢復早前消失的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bring to mind","meaning":"令人聯想到","examples":[{"en":"The words “natural flavour” may bring to mind traditional ingredients.","zh":"“Natural flavour” 這些字可能令人聯想到傳統食材。"},{"en":"To bring something to mind means to make someone think of it.","zh":"“Bring something to mind” 指令人想起某事。"},{"en":"The smell of fresh bread may bring to mind breakfast at home.","zh":"新鮮麵包的氣味可能令人聯想到家中的早餐。"},{"en":"If a label uses the word “natural,” it may bring to mind farms, herbs and fresh fruit.","zh":"如果標籤使用 “natural” 一詞，可能令人聯想到農場、香草和新鮮水果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes mental association.","zh":"這個短語描述心理聯想。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fresh barley","meaning":"新鮮大麥","examples":[{"en":"Consumers may imagine fresh barley when they read the word “natural.”","zh":"消費者讀到 “natural” 一詞時，可能想像新鮮大麥。"},{"en":"Fresh barley is newly harvested or unprocessed barley, a grain used in food and drink.","zh":"新鮮大麥是剛收割或未加工的大麥，一種用於食品和飲品的穀物。"},{"en":"A traditional market may sell fresh barley for soups, drinks or grain dishes.","zh":"傳統市場可能出售新鮮大麥，用於湯、飲品或穀物菜式。"},{"en":"If a label makes people imagine fresh barley, it creates a natural and wholesome image.","zh":"如果標籤令人想像新鮮大麥，它就創造自然和健康的形象。"},{"en":"The phrase gives an example of the simple ingredients consumers may picture.","zh":"這個短語給出消費者可能想像的簡單食材例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hand-ground spices","meaning":"手磨香料","examples":[{"en":"The label may bring to mind hand-ground spices from a traditional market.","zh":"標籤可能令人聯想到來自傳統市場的手磨香料。"},{"en":"Hand-ground spices are spices crushed or ground manually rather than by industrial machines.","zh":"手磨香料是以人手磨碎或研磨，而不是用工業機器處理的香料。"},{"en":"A grandmother may use hand-ground spices to make curry taste fresher and more personal.","zh":"祖母可能使用手磨香料，使咖喱味道更新鮮和更有個人味道。"},{"en":"If people imagine hand-ground spices, they may think of tradition, freshness and care.","zh":"如果人們想像手磨香料，可能會想到傳統、新鮮和用心。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts small-scale preparation with factory production.","zh":"這個短語把小規模製備與工廠生產作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dried herbs","meaning":"乾香草","examples":[{"en":"Dried herbs are commonly associated with natural cooking.","zh":"乾香草常與天然烹調聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Dried herbs are leaves or plant parts preserved by removing moisture.","zh":"乾香草是透過去除水分保存的葉子或植物部分。"},{"en":"A cook may add dried herbs to soup when fresh herbs are not available.","zh":"當沒有新鮮香草時，廚師可能把乾香草加入湯中。"},{"en":"If herbs are dried, they last longer but may taste different from fresh ones.","zh":"如果香草被乾燥處理，它們保存更久，但味道可能與新鮮香草不同。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to plant seasonings used in cooking.","zh":"這個短語指烹調中使用的植物調味料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bustling street market","meaning":"熙來攘往的街市","examples":[{"en":"The description may evoke a bustling street market full of spices.","zh":"這段描述可能令人想起充滿香料、熙來攘往的街市。"},{"en":"A bustling street market is a busy outdoor market full of people, noise and activity.","zh":"熙來攘往的街市是人多、嘈雜而活動頻繁的戶外市場。"},{"en":"Tourists may visit a bustling street market to buy fruit, snacks and local food.","zh":"遊客可能到熙來攘往的街市購買水果、小食和本地食物。"},{"en":"If a food label evokes such a market, consumers may imagine freshness and tradition.","zh":"如果食品標籤令人想起這種街市，消費者可能想像新鮮和傳統。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a lively everyday scene.","zh":"這個短語營造生動的日常場景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"natural sources","meaning":"天然來源","examples":[{"en":"Many supposedly natural sources are processed in industrial facilities.","zh":"許多所謂天然來源在工業設施中被加工。"},{"en":"Natural sources are materials that come from plants, animals or other parts of nature.","zh":"天然來源是來自植物、動物或自然界其他部分的材料。"},{"en":"Lemon peel, vanilla beans and herbs can be natural sources of flavour.","zh":"檸檬皮、雲呢拿豆和香草可以是香味的天然來源。"},{"en":"If natural sources are processed heavily, the final ingredient may feel less simple than expected.","zh":"如果天然來源被大量加工，最終成分可能比預期不那麼簡單。"},{"en":"The phrase describes origin, not necessarily the whole production method.","zh":"這個短語描述來源，而不一定描述整個生產方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, many natural flavours are developed in factories and laboratories.","zh":"事實上，許多天然香味劑是在工廠和實驗室中研發的。"},{"en":"In fact is used to introduce the real situation, often correcting or strengthening a previous idea.","zh":"“In fact” 用來引出真實情況，常用於糾正或加強前面想法。"},{"en":"The restaurant looks small; in fact, it serves hundreds of customers each day.","zh":"這間餐廳看起來很小；事實上，它每天服務數百名顧客。"},{"en":"If “natural” sounds simple, in fact the production may involve advanced chemistry.","zh":"如果 “natural” 聽起來簡單，事實上生產可能涉及先進化學。"},{"en":"The phrase often reveals a surprising truth.","zh":"這個短語常揭示令人意外的真相。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be engineered to culinary perfection","meaning":"被精心調製至完美食用效果","examples":[{"en":"Flavours are engineered to culinary perfection in specialised factories.","zh":"香味在專門工廠中被精心調製至完美食用效果。"},{"en":"To be engineered to culinary perfection means to be carefully designed to taste extremely good.","zh":"“Be engineered to culinary perfection” 指被仔細設計到味道極佳。"},{"en":"A snack flavour may be engineered so each bite tastes salty, smoky and slightly sweet.","zh":"零食香味可能被精心調製，使每一口都有鹹味、煙熏味和微甜味。"},{"en":"If flavours are engineered this way, the result may feel natural even though it was carefully manufactured.","zh":"如果香味如此被調製，結果即使經精心製造，也可能感覺自然。"},{"en":"The phrase shows deliberate scientific design for food pleasure.","zh":"這個短語顯示為食品享受而進行的有意科學設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"factories and plants","meaning":"工廠和生產設施","examples":[{"en":"Flavour companies operate factories and production plants near New York.","zh":"香味公司在紐約附近經營工廠和生產設施。"},{"en":"Factories and plants are industrial buildings where goods or ingredients are made.","zh":"工廠和生產設施是製造貨品或成分的工業建築。"},{"en":"A city may have factories and plants that produce drinks, snacks or packaging.","zh":"城市可能有生產飲品、零食或包裝的工廠和生產設施。"},{"en":"If flavours come from factories and plants, the process is industrial rather than home-style cooking.","zh":"如果香味來自工廠和生產設施，過程就是工業化，而不是家庭式烹調。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to places of large-scale production.","zh":"這個短語指大規模生產的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"off the New Jersey Turnpike","meaning":"位於新澤西州收費公路附近","examples":[{"en":"Several flavour companies operate near the New Jersey Turnpike.","zh":"幾間香味公司在新澤西州收費公路附近營運。"},{"en":"Off the New Jersey Turnpike means located near or accessible from that major road in New Jersey.","zh":"“Off the New Jersey Turnpike” 指位於新澤西州該主要道路附近或可由該道路到達。"},{"en":"A hotel off a highway may be convenient for drivers who need a quick overnight stop.","zh":"位於高速公路附近的酒店對需要快速過夜的司機可能很方便。"},{"en":"If factories are located off a major road, trucks can move ingredients and products easily.","zh":"如果工廠位於主要道路附近，貨車就能容易運送原料和產品。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a practical location near a transport route.","zh":"這個短語給出靠近交通路線的實際位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"firms such as","meaning":"……等公司","examples":[{"en":"Firms such as International Flavors & Fragrances manufacture food flavourings.","zh":"International Flavors & Fragrances 等公司製造食品香味劑。"},{"en":"Firms such as means companies like the example being named.","zh":"“Firms such as” 指像所提例子那樣的公司。"},{"en":"Firms such as large delivery platforms can change how small restaurants reach customers.","zh":"大型外賣平台等公司可以改變小餐廳接觸顧客的方式。"},{"en":"If a writer says “firms such as,” the named company is an example, not the only one.","zh":"如果作者說 “firms such as”，所提公司是例子，而不是唯一公司。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces examples of businesses.","zh":"這個短語引出商業公司例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"isolate and manufacture","meaning":"分離並製造","examples":[{"en":"Specialist firms isolate and manufacture tastes and aromas.","zh":"專門公司分離並製造味道和香氣。"},{"en":"To isolate and manufacture something means to separate it from a source and then produce it industrially.","zh":"“Isolate and manufacture” 某物指從來源中分離它，然後以工業方式生產。"},{"en":"A laboratory may isolate a useful compound from a plant and manufacture it for medicine.","zh":"實驗室可能從植物中分離有用化合物，並製造成藥物。"},{"en":"If companies isolate an aroma, they can reproduce it for many food products.","zh":"如果公司分離出一種香氣，就能為許多食品複製它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both scientific separation and industrial production.","zh":"這個短語同時描述科學分離和工業生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be incorporated into","meaning":"被加入……之中","examples":[{"en":"Manufactured flavours are incorporated into many foods and drinks.","zh":"製造出來的香味被加入許多食品和飲品之中。"},{"en":"To be incorporated into something means to be added and made part of it.","zh":"“Be incorporated into” 某物指被加入並成為其中一部分。"},{"en":"New safety rules may be incorporated into a school handbook.","zh":"新安全規則可能被加入學校手冊中。"},{"en":"If flavour chemicals are incorporated into a drink, they become part of the final taste.","zh":"如果香味化學物被加入飲品中，它們就成為最終味道的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adding something into a larger whole.","zh":"這個短語描述把某物加入較大整體之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a summery burst of","meaning":"一股充滿夏日氣息的……","examples":[{"en":"The drink has a summery burst of fresh orange flavour.","zh":"這款飲品有一股充滿夏日氣息的新鮮橙味。"},{"en":"A summery burst of something is a sudden strong taste or feeling that reminds people of summer.","zh":"“A summery burst of” 某物指突然強烈出現、令人聯想到夏天的味道或感覺。"},{"en":"A cold lemon drink can give a summery burst of freshness on a hot day.","zh":"在炎熱日子，一杯凍檸檬飲品可以帶來一股充滿夏日氣息的清新感。"},{"en":"If a product has a summery burst of fruit flavour, consumers may imagine sunshine and holidays.","zh":"如果產品有一股夏日水果味，消費者可能想像陽光和假期。"},{"en":"The phrase is vivid and marketing-friendly.","zh":"這個短語生動，而且帶有市場推廣感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"naturally squeezed orange juice","meaning":"天然鮮榨橙汁","examples":[{"en":"The flavour is designed to resemble naturally squeezed orange juice.","zh":"這種香味被設計成類似天然鮮榨橙汁。"},{"en":"Naturally squeezed orange juice is juice pressed from oranges without being artificially flavoured.","zh":"天然鮮榨橙汁是由橙壓榨出來、沒有人工調味的果汁。"},{"en":"A café may advertise naturally squeezed orange juice to suggest freshness.","zh":"咖啡店可能宣傳天然鮮榨橙汁，以暗示新鮮。"},{"en":"If a drink only resembles naturally squeezed juice, the taste may be created by flavouring rather than fresh fruit.","zh":"如果飲品只是類似天然鮮榨果汁，其味道可能由香味劑而不是新鮮水果創造。"},{"en":"The phrase creates an image of freshness and simplicity.","zh":"這個短語創造新鮮和簡單的形象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"wood-smoked aroma","meaning":"木煙熏香氣","examples":[{"en":"Barbecue sauces may contain a manufactured wood-smoked aroma.","zh":"燒烤醬可能含有人造木煙熏香氣。"},{"en":"A wood-smoked aroma is the smell of food exposed to smoke from burning wood.","zh":"木煙熏香氣是食物接觸燃燒木材煙霧後產生的氣味。"},{"en":"Grilled meat can have a wood-smoked aroma when cooked over charcoal or wood.","zh":"肉類在木炭或木材上烤時，可以有木煙熏香氣。"},{"en":"If sauce contains a manufactured smoke aroma, it may taste grilled even without a barbecue.","zh":"如果醬汁含有人造煙熏香氣，即使沒有燒烤，也可能吃起來像烤過。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a smoky smell associated with outdoor cooking.","zh":"這個短語描述與戶外烹調相關的煙熏氣味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"barbecue sauces","meaning":"燒烤醬","examples":[{"en":"Barbecue sauces often rely on added smoke flavour.","zh":"燒烤醬常依賴添加煙熏味。"},{"en":"Barbecue sauces are thick sauces used to flavour grilled or roasted food.","zh":"燒烤醬是用來為烤製或燒烤食物調味的濃稠醬汁。"},{"en":"A family may brush barbecue sauce on chicken before putting it on the grill.","zh":"家庭可能在把雞肉放上烤架前刷上燒烤醬。"},{"en":"If barbecue sauce contains smoke flavour, it can suggest outdoor cooking even in packaged food.","zh":"如果燒烤醬含有煙熏味，它可以令包裝食品也帶有戶外烹調感。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to sauces associated with grilled food.","zh":"這個短語指與燒烤食物相關的醬汁。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"creamy and buttery taste","meaning":"香濃幼滑的牛油味","examples":[{"en":"Flavour manufacturers can reproduce a creamy and buttery taste.","zh":"香味製造商可以重現香濃幼滑的牛油味。"},{"en":"A creamy and buttery taste is a rich, smooth flavour like cream or butter.","zh":"香濃幼滑的牛油味，是像忌廉或牛油一樣濃郁順滑的味道。"},{"en":"Popcorn may have a creamy and buttery taste even when little real butter is used.","zh":"爆谷即使只用了很少真正牛油，也可能有香濃幼滑的牛油味。"},{"en":"If a product lacks dairy fat, flavouring may help create a creamy and buttery taste.","zh":"如果產品缺少奶類脂肪，香味劑可能幫助創造香濃幼滑的牛油味。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both flavour and texture impression.","zh":"這個短語同時描述味道和質感印象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"dairy products","meaning":"奶類製品","examples":[{"en":"Many dairy products contain added flavour compounds.","zh":"許多奶類製品含有添加香味化合物。"},{"en":"Dairy products are foods made from milk, such as yoghurt, cheese, cream and butter.","zh":"奶類製品是由牛奶製成的食品，例如乳酪、芝士、忌廉和牛油。"},{"en":"A supermarket may keep dairy products in a refrigerated section.","zh":"超市可能把奶類製品放在冷藏區。"},{"en":"If dairy products are flavoured, they may taste like strawberry, vanilla or chocolate.","zh":"如果奶類製品被調味，可能有士多啤梨、雲呢拿或朱古力味。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to milk-based foods.","zh":"這個短語指以奶為基礎的食品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sun-drenched meadows","meaning":"陽光普照的草原","examples":[{"en":"The flavours do not necessarily come from sun-drenched meadows.","zh":"這些香味不一定來自陽光普照的草原。"},{"en":"Sun-drenched meadows are grassy fields filled with bright sunlight.","zh":"陽光普照的草原是充滿明亮陽光的草地。"},{"en":"Food adverts may show sun-drenched meadows to make dairy products seem natural and fresh.","zh":"食品廣告可能展示陽光普照的草原，使奶類製品看似天然新鮮。"},{"en":"If flavour is made in a laboratory, the image of sun-drenched meadows may be misleading.","zh":"如果香味在實驗室製成，陽光普照草原的形象可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a romantic image of nature.","zh":"這個短語創造浪漫化的自然形象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"backyard grills","meaning":"後院烤架","examples":[{"en":"Smoke flavour may be produced in a laboratory rather than on backyard grills.","zh":"煙熏味可能在實驗室製造，而不是在後院烤架上產生。"},{"en":"Backyard grills are outdoor cooking devices used at home for grilling food.","zh":"後院烤架是在家中戶外用來烤食物的烹調設備。"},{"en":"Families may cook burgers and sausages on backyard grills during summer gatherings.","zh":"家庭可能在夏日聚會中用後院烤架烤漢堡和香腸。"},{"en":"If smoke flavour comes from a lab, the taste may imitate food cooked on backyard grills.","zh":"如果煙熏味來自實驗室，其味道可能模仿在後院烤架上烤出的食物。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests casual home barbecue cooking.","zh":"這個短語暗示輕鬆的家庭燒烤。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be formed in laboratories","meaning":"在實驗室製成","examples":[{"en":"Many commercial flavours are formed in laboratories and test tubes.","zh":"許多商業香味在實驗室和試管中製成。"},{"en":"To be formed in laboratories means to be created or developed through scientific work in labs.","zh":"“Be formed in laboratories” 指透過實驗室科學工作創造或研發。"},{"en":"Some medicines are formed in laboratories before being tested and produced widely.","zh":"一些藥物在廣泛測試和生產前，先在實驗室製成。"},{"en":"If flavours are formed in laboratories, their taste may be designed with great precision.","zh":"如果香味在實驗室製成，其味道可能被非常精準地設計。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts scientific creation with traditional cooking.","zh":"這個短語把科學創造與傳統烹調作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"test tubes","meaning":"試管","examples":[{"en":"Scientists analyse and combine flavour chemicals in test tubes.","zh":"科學家在試管中分析並混合香味化學物。"},{"en":"Test tubes are small glass or plastic tubes used in laboratories for experiments.","zh":"試管是實驗室中用於實驗的小玻璃或塑膠管。"},{"en":"Students may use test tubes in science class to mix safe liquids and observe reactions.","zh":"學生可能在科學課使用試管混合安全液體並觀察反應。"},{"en":"If flavour chemicals are tested in test tubes, food taste can begin as laboratory chemistry.","zh":"如果香味化學物在試管中測試，食品味道可以始於實驗室化學。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to basic laboratory equipment.","zh":"這個短語指基本實驗室設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"industry giants","meaning":"行業巨企","examples":[{"en":"Large flavour companies have become industry giants.","zh":"大型香味公司已成為行業巨企。"},{"en":"Industry giants are very large and powerful companies in a particular business field.","zh":"行業巨企是在某商業領域中非常大型且有力量的公司。"},{"en":"Technology industry giants can influence how people communicate, shop and work.","zh":"科技行業巨企可以影響人們溝通、購物和工作的方式。"},{"en":"If a flavour company becomes an industry giant, it may supply ingredients to many global brands.","zh":"如果香味公司成為行業巨企，它可能向許多全球品牌供應成分。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests size, influence and market power.","zh":"這個短語暗示規模、影響力和市場力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"scientists dubbed flavourists","meaning":"被稱為香味調配師的科學家","examples":[{"en":"The scientists who design commercial flavours are dubbed flavourists.","zh":"設計商業香味的科學家被稱為香味調配師。"},{"en":"Scientists dubbed flavourists are scientists given the specialist title of flavourists.","zh":"被稱為香味調配師的科學家，是獲得香味調配師這個專門稱號的科學家。"},{"en":"A laboratory worker may be dubbed an expert if they develop rare skills over many years.","zh":"如果實驗室工作者多年來培養稀有技能，可能被稱為專家。"},{"en":"If scientists are dubbed flavourists, their job combines chemistry with taste and smell design.","zh":"如果科學家被稱為香味調配師，他們的工作就結合化學與味覺、嗅覺設計。"},{"en":"The phrase explains a special professional name.","zh":"這個短語解釋一個特殊職業名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"flavourists","meaning":"香味調配師","examples":[{"en":"Flavourists combine chemistry with a highly trained sense of smell.","zh":"香味調配師把化學與高度受訓的嗅覺結合起來。"},{"en":"Flavourists are specialists who design and adjust flavours for food and drink products.","zh":"香味調配師是為食品和飲品設計及調整香味的專家。"},{"en":"A flavourist may spend months creating a strawberry flavour for yoghurt.","zh":"香味調配師可能花數月時間為乳酪創造士多啤梨味。"},{"en":"If a flavourist changes one chemical slightly, the final taste may become fresher or more artificial.","zh":"如果香味調配師稍微改變一種化學物，最終味道可能變得更新鮮或更人工。"},{"en":"The word refers to professionals who create commercial taste and aroma.","zh":"這個詞指創造商業味道和香氣的專業人士。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"potent chemicals","meaning":"效力強的化學物質","examples":[{"en":"Small amounts of potent chemicals can create powerful aromas.","zh":"少量效力強的化學物質可以創造強烈香氣。"},{"en":"Potent chemicals are chemicals that have a strong effect even in tiny amounts.","zh":"效力強的化學物質是即使份量很少也有強烈效果的化學物。"},{"en":"A tiny drop of a potent cleaning chemical may give a whole room a strong smell.","zh":"一小滴效力強的清潔化學物可能令整個房間有強烈氣味。"},{"en":"If flavour chemicals are potent, manufacturers need only very small quantities.","zh":"如果香味化學物效力強，製造商只需要極少量。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong chemical effect, not necessarily danger.","zh":"這個短語描述強化學效果，不一定表示危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"olfactory senses","meaning":"嗅覺","examples":[{"en":"Flavour chemicals stimulate the olfactory senses.","zh":"香味化學物刺激嗅覺。"},{"en":"Olfactory senses are the senses related to smell.","zh":"嗅覺是與氣味相關的感官。"},{"en":"The smell of fresh coffee can wake up the olfactory senses in the morning.","zh":"早上新鮮咖啡的氣味可以喚醒嗅覺。"},{"en":"If aroma chemicals stimulate the olfactory senses strongly, food may seem more flavourful.","zh":"如果香氣化學物強烈刺激嗅覺，食物可能顯得更有味道。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to smell perception, not taste alone.","zh":"這個短語指氣味感知，而不只是味覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"send something into overdrive","meaning":"令……極度活躍","examples":[{"en":"Strong aroma chemicals can send the olfactory senses into overdrive.","zh":"強烈香氣化學物可以令嗅覺極度活躍。"},{"en":"To send something into overdrive means to make it work extremely hard or become highly active.","zh":"“Send something into overdrive” 指令某事物非常努力運作或變得高度活躍。"},{"en":"A sudden deadline can send a whole office into overdrive.","zh":"突如其來的限期可以令整個辦公室極度活躍起來。"},{"en":"If a smell sends the nose into overdrive, the aroma may feel intense and hard to ignore.","zh":"如果一種氣味令鼻子極度活躍，該香氣可能感覺強烈且難以忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a system becoming unusually active.","zh":"這個短語描述系統變得異常活躍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a mix of techniques","meaning":"多種技術的結合","examples":[{"en":"Flavourists use a mix of scientific and sensory techniques.","zh":"香味調配師使用科學和感官多種技術的結合。"},{"en":"A mix of techniques means several different methods used together.","zh":"多種技術的結合指幾種不同方法一起使用。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a mix of techniques, such as examples, questions and short quizzes.","zh":"老師可能使用多種技術的結合，例如例子、提問和小測。"},{"en":"If one method is not enough, a mix of techniques can give a fuller result.","zh":"如果單一方法不足，多種技術結合可以帶來更完整結果。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests combining approaches rather than relying on one tool.","zh":"這個短語暗示結合方法，而不是依賴單一工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be refined over many years","meaning":"經多年改良","examples":[{"en":"The techniques have been refined over many years.","zh":"這些技術經多年改良。"},{"en":"To be refined over many years means to be improved slowly through long practice and experience.","zh":"“Be refined over many years” 指透過長時間練習和經驗慢慢改善。"},{"en":"A family recipe may be refined over many years as each generation adjusts it.","zh":"家庭食譜可能隨着每一代調整而經多年改良。"},{"en":"If a technique is refined over decades, small errors are removed and results become more reliable.","zh":"如果技術經數十年改良，小錯誤會被移除，結果變得更可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual improvement over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間逐漸改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dense, intricate chemistry","meaning":"深奧複雜的化學","examples":[{"en":"Flavour creation involves dense, intricate chemistry.","zh":"香味創造涉及深奧複雜的化學。"},{"en":"Dense, intricate chemistry means complex scientific work with many closely connected chemical details.","zh":"深奧複雜的化學，指有許多緊密相連化學細節的複雜科學工作。"},{"en":"Developing a new medicine can involve dense, intricate chemistry that non-scientists find hard to follow.","zh":"研發新藥可能涉及深奧複雜的化學，非科學家難以跟上。"},{"en":"If flavour creation involves such chemistry, a simple taste may have a complicated chemical structure.","zh":"如果香味創造涉及這種化學，一種簡單味道也可能有複雜化學結構。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses technical complexity.","zh":"這個短語強調技術複雜性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"spectrometers","meaning":"光譜儀","examples":[{"en":"Spectrometers help scientists identify chemical components.","zh":"光譜儀幫助科學家識別化學成分。"},{"en":"Spectrometers are scientific instruments used to measure and analyse substances through their spectra.","zh":"光譜儀是透過光譜量度和分析物質的科學儀器。"},{"en":"A laboratory may use spectrometers to find what chemicals are present in a sample.","zh":"實驗室可能使用光譜儀找出樣本中有甚麼化學物。"},{"en":"If flavour scientists use spectrometers, they can understand the chemical basis of an aroma.","zh":"如果香味科學家使用光譜儀，就能理解香氣的化學基礎。"},{"en":"The word refers to advanced measuring equipment.","zh":"這個詞指先進量度設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"gas chromatographs","meaning":"氣相色譜儀","examples":[{"en":"Gas chromatographs separate and analyse volatile compounds.","zh":"氣相色譜儀分離並分析揮發性化合物。"},{"en":"Gas chromatographs are laboratory instruments that separate chemicals in a gas or vapour mixture.","zh":"氣相色譜儀是分離氣體或蒸氣混合物中化學物的實驗室儀器。"},{"en":"Scientists may use gas chromatographs to analyse the smell of coffee, fruit or smoke.","zh":"科學家可能使用氣相色譜儀分析咖啡、水果或煙味。"},{"en":"If a flavour contains many volatile compounds, a gas chromatograph can help identify them.","zh":"如果香味含有許多揮發性化合物，氣相色譜儀可以幫助識別它們。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to specialist equipment for chemical separation.","zh":"這個短語指用於化學分離的專門設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"headspace-vapour analysers","meaning":"頂空蒸氣分析儀","examples":[{"en":"Headspace-vapour analysers examine aromas released above a sample.","zh":"頂空蒸氣分析儀檢查樣本上方釋放出的香氣。"},{"en":"Headspace-vapour analysers are instruments that study the gases above a food or liquid sample.","zh":"頂空蒸氣分析儀是研究食品或液體樣本上方氣體的儀器。"},{"en":"A lab may use a headspace-vapour analyser to examine the aroma coming from orange juice.","zh":"實驗室可能使用頂空蒸氣分析儀檢查橙汁散發的香氣。"},{"en":"If aromas rise from a sample, this equipment can help identify the chemicals in that vapour.","zh":"如果香氣從樣本中升起，這種設備可以幫助識別蒸氣中的化學物。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to specialised aroma-analysis technology.","zh":"這個短語指專門的香氣分析科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"break down the components of","meaning":"分析……的組成部分","examples":[{"en":"Laboratory equipment can break down the components of a flavour.","zh":"實驗室設備可以分析一種香味的組成部分。"},{"en":"To break down the components of something means to separate and identify its parts.","zh":"“Break down the components of” 某物指分離並識別其各部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may break down the components of an essay into introduction, body paragraphs and conclusion.","zh":"老師可能把文章組成部分分析為引言、主體段和結論。"},{"en":"If scientists break down a flavour, they can see which chemicals create each note.","zh":"如果科學家分析一種香味，就能看見哪些化學物創造每種氣味層次。"},{"en":"The phrase describes detailed analysis into parts.","zh":"這個短語描述把整體分成部分作詳細分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"minute amounts","meaning":"微量","examples":[{"en":"Modern instruments can detect chemicals in extremely minute amounts.","zh":"現代儀器能偵測極微量的化學物。"},{"en":"Minute amounts are extremely small quantities.","zh":"微量是極小的份量。"},{"en":"A strong perfume may be noticed even in minute amounts.","zh":"強烈香水即使是微量也可能被察覺。"},{"en":"If a machine detects minute amounts of a chemical, it can analyse very subtle flavours.","zh":"如果機器能偵測微量化學物，它就能分析非常細微的香味。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses tiny quantity.","zh":"這個短語強調極小份量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"one part per billion","meaning":"十億分之一","examples":[{"en":"Some flavour compounds can be detected at one part per billion.","zh":"一些香味化合物可以在十億分之一的濃度下被偵測到。"},{"en":"One part per billion means one unit of a substance in one billion units of a mixture.","zh":"十億分之一指混合物十億個單位中有一個單位的某物質。"},{"en":"Scientists may measure pollution at one part per billion when even tiny traces matter.","zh":"當即使微小痕量也重要時，科學家可能以十億分之一量度污染。"},{"en":"If a flavour compound is noticeable at this level, it is extremely powerful.","zh":"如果香味化合物在這個水平仍可察覺，它就極其強烈。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an extraordinarily tiny concentration.","zh":"這個短語描述極其微小的濃度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not to be outdone","meaning":"不甘示弱","examples":[{"en":"Not to be outdone, the human nose can detect even smaller quantities.","zh":"人類鼻子不甘示弱，能偵測更少量的物質。"},{"en":"Not to be outdone means not wanting to seem less impressive than someone or something else.","zh":"“Not to be outdone” 指不想顯得比別人或其他事物遜色。"},{"en":"One student brought a colourful poster; not to be outdone, another built a full model.","zh":"一名學生帶來彩色海報；另一名不甘示弱，製作了一個完整模型。"},{"en":"If machines are sensitive, the phrase shows the human nose can be even more impressive.","zh":"如果機器很靈敏，這個短語顯示人類鼻子可以更令人驚訝。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a competing or matching achievement.","zh":"這個短語引出競爭或相匹配的成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"isolate aromas","meaning":"分辨香氣","examples":[{"en":"The human nose can isolate aromas at extremely low concentrations.","zh":"人類鼻子能在極低濃度下分辨香氣。"},{"en":"To isolate aromas means to distinguish one smell from others.","zh":"“Isolate aromas” 指把一種氣味與其他氣味區分出來。"},{"en":"A chef may isolate the aroma of basil in a sauce even when garlic and tomato are also present.","zh":"即使醬汁中也有蒜和番茄，廚師仍可能分辨出羅勒香氣。"},{"en":"If the nose can isolate aromas, it can identify subtle smells that machines may miss.","zh":"如果鼻子能分辨香氣，就能識別機器可能錯過的細微氣味。"},{"en":"The phrase describes separating one scent mentally from a mixture.","zh":"這個短語描述在混合氣味中把一種氣味分離出來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"three parts per trillion","meaning":"萬億分之三","examples":[{"en":"The nose may detect aromas at concentrations as low as three parts per trillion.","zh":"鼻子可能在低至萬億分之三的濃度下偵測香氣。"},{"en":"Three parts per trillion means three units of a substance in one trillion units of a mixture.","zh":"萬億分之三指混合物一萬億個單位中有三個單位的某物質。"},{"en":"Such a tiny concentration is like finding a few drops in an enormous swimming pool.","zh":"這樣微小的濃度就像在巨大泳池中找幾滴液體。"},{"en":"If the nose can detect aromas at this level, human smell is extremely sensitive.","zh":"如果鼻子能在這個水平偵測香氣，人類嗅覺就極其靈敏。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an almost unimaginably small amount.","zh":"這個短語描述幾乎難以想像的小份量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as much an art as a science","meaning":"既是藝術，也是科學","examples":[{"en":"Flavour creation is as much an art as a science.","zh":"香味創造既是藝術，也是科學。"},{"en":"As much an art as a science means it needs creativity and judgement as well as technical knowledge.","zh":"“As much an art as a science” 指它既需要創意和判斷，也需要技術知識。"},{"en":"Teaching is as much an art as a science because teachers need both methods and sensitivity.","zh":"教學既是藝術，也是科學，因為老師既需要方法，也需要敏感度。"},{"en":"If flavour creation needs a trained nose, it cannot rely on machines alone.","zh":"如果香味創造需要受訓嗅覺，它就不能只依靠機器。"},{"en":"The phrase balances creative skill with scientific precision.","zh":"這個短語平衡創意技巧和科學精確度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"require a trained nose","meaning":"需要受過訓練的嗅覺","examples":[{"en":"Professional flavour creation requires a trained nose.","zh":"專業香味創造需要受過訓練的嗅覺。"},{"en":"To require a trained nose means to need someone whose sense of smell has been carefully developed.","zh":"“Require a trained nose” 指需要嗅覺經仔細培養的人。"},{"en":"A tea buyer may require a trained nose to judge freshness and aroma.","zh":"茶葉買手可能需要受過訓練的嗅覺，以判斷新鮮度和香氣。"},{"en":"If a job requires a trained nose, practice and experience are as important as equipment.","zh":"如果工作需要受訓嗅覺，練習和經驗就與設備同樣重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes expert smell judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述專業嗅覺判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a delicate sense of balance","meaning":"細膩的平衡感","examples":[{"en":"A flavourist needs a delicate sense of balance when combining aromas.","zh":"香味調配師在結合香氣時需要細膩的平衡感。"},{"en":"A delicate sense of balance is the ability to judge small differences and avoid too much or too little.","zh":"細膩的平衡感是判斷細微差異並避免過多或過少的能力。"},{"en":"A cook needs a delicate sense of balance when adding salt, sourness and sweetness to soup.","zh":"廚師在湯中加入鹽味、酸味和甜味時，需要細膩的平衡感。"},{"en":"If one aroma is too strong, the whole flavour may lose balance.","zh":"如果一種香氣太強，整體香味可能失去平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful judgement in mixing elements.","zh":"這個短語描述混合元素時的仔細判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"poetic sense","meaning":"富詩意的感受力","examples":[{"en":"Successful flavourists often describe aromas with a poetic sense of detail.","zh":"成功的香味調配師常以富詩意的細節感描述香氣。"},{"en":"A poetic sense is an imaginative and sensitive way of noticing and describing experience.","zh":"富詩意的感受力，是以富想像力和敏感方式注意並描述經驗。"},{"en":"A writer with a poetic sense may describe rain as silver threads on the window.","zh":"有詩意感受力的作家可能把雨描述為窗上的銀線。"},{"en":"If flavourists use poetic detail, they can communicate subtle smells more vividly.","zh":"如果香味調配師使用富詩意的細節，就能更生動地傳達細微氣味。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests creativity beyond technical measurement.","zh":"這個短語暗示超越技術量度的創意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be wary of","meaning":"對……保持警惕","examples":[{"en":"Consumers may be wary of the industrialisation of natural flavour.","zh":"消費者可能對天然香味劑的工業化保持警惕。"},{"en":"To be wary of something means to be careful or suspicious about it.","zh":"“Be wary of” 某事指對它小心或有所懷疑。"},{"en":"Parents may be wary of online adverts that promise instant exam success.","zh":"家長可能對承諾即時考試成功的網上廣告保持警惕。"},{"en":"If consumers are wary of flavour production, they may read labels more carefully.","zh":"如果消費者對香味生產保持警惕，可能更仔細閱讀標籤。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests caution, not complete rejection.","zh":"這個短語暗示謹慎，而不是完全拒絕。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"industrialisation of","meaning":"……的工業化","examples":[{"en":"The industrialisation of flavour production has transformed processed food.","zh":"香味生產的工業化改變了加工食品。"},{"en":"Industrialisation of something means turning it into a large-scale, machine-based or factory-based process.","zh":"某事的工業化指把它變成大規模、機器或工廠主導的過程。"},{"en":"The industrialisation of farming changed how food was grown, stored and transported.","zh":"農業工業化改變了食物種植、儲存和運輸方式。"},{"en":"If flavour production becomes industrialised, tastes can be reproduced consistently for millions of products.","zh":"如果香味生產工業化，味道就能為數以百萬計產品一致地複製。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a shift from small-scale craft to large-scale production.","zh":"這個短語描述由小規模工藝轉向大規模生產。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on its own","meaning":"單獨而言","examples":[{"en":"Natural flavour on its own is not considered a major health risk.","zh":"天然香味劑單獨而言不被視為重大健康風險。"},{"en":"On its own means by itself, without considering other things around it.","zh":"“On its own” 指單獨來看，不考慮周圍其他事物。"},{"en":"Sugar on its own may not explain a person’s health; total diet and exercise also matter.","zh":"糖單獨而言未必能解釋一個人的健康；整體飲食和運動也重要。"},{"en":"If natural flavour is considered on its own, it may seem less worrying than sugar, fat and sodium.","zh":"如果單獨考慮天然香味劑，它可能比糖、脂肪和鈉較不令人擔心。"},{"en":"The phrase separates one factor from the wider situation.","zh":"這個短語把一個因素與更大情況分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"present a clear reason for alarm","meaning":"構成明確的警號","examples":[{"en":"The flavour industry may not present a clear reason for alarm by itself.","zh":"香味產業本身可能不構成明確的警號。"},{"en":"To present a clear reason for alarm means to give obvious cause for serious concern.","zh":"“Present a clear reason for alarm” 指提供明顯而嚴重的擔憂原因。"},{"en":"A small spelling mistake does not present a clear reason for alarm, but repeated missing homework might.","zh":"一個小串字錯誤不構成明確警號，但反覆欠交功課可能構成。"},{"en":"If an ingredient is not directly harmful, it may not by itself justify panic.","zh":"如果成分不是直接有害，它本身未必足以令人恐慌。"},{"en":"The phrase describes whether something should seriously worry people.","zh":"這個短語描述某事是否應令人大為擔心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"widely agree that","meaning":"廣泛同意","examples":[{"en":"Nutritionists widely agree that sugar, fat and sodium are major concerns.","zh":"營養學家廣泛同意糖、脂肪和鈉是主要關注。"},{"en":"To widely agree that something is true means many experts or people share the same view.","zh":"“Widely agree that” 某事為真指許多專家或人士有相同看法。"},{"en":"Teachers widely agree that regular reading helps students improve vocabulary.","zh":"老師普遍同意定期閱讀能幫助學生改善詞彙。"},{"en":"If nutritionists widely agree on a risk, the concern is not just one person’s opinion.","zh":"如果營養學家廣泛同意某風險，該關注就不只是個人意見。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests broad consensus.","zh":"這個短語暗示廣泛共識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the real assault on health","meaning":"對健康的真正傷害","examples":[{"en":"The real assault on health comes from excessive sugar, fat and sodium.","zh":"對健康的真正傷害來自過量糖、脂肪和鈉。"},{"en":"The real assault on health means the main thing that seriously harms health.","zh":"對健康的真正傷害指嚴重損害健康的主要事物。"},{"en":"For many students, the real assault on concentration may be lack of sleep, not difficult textbooks.","zh":"對許多學生來說，對專注力的真正傷害可能是睡眠不足，而不是困難教科書。"},{"en":"If sugar, fat and sodium are the real assault, flavouring may be a helper rather than the main enemy.","zh":"如果糖、脂肪和鈉是真正傷害，香味劑可能是幫手，而不是主要敵人。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly identifies the major source of harm.","zh":"這個短語強烈指出主要傷害來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the last few decades","meaning":"在過去數十年間","examples":[{"en":"Processed-food consumption has risen sharply in the last few decades.","zh":"加工食品消費在過去數十年間急劇上升。"},{"en":"In the last few decades means during the most recent several periods of ten years.","zh":"“In the last few decades” 指在最近幾個十年期間。"},{"en":"In the last few decades, mobile phones have changed communication around the world.","zh":"在過去數十年間，手機改變了世界各地的溝通方式。"},{"en":"If processed-food consumption rises over decades, health effects may become visible slowly.","zh":"如果加工食品消費在數十年間上升，健康影響可能慢慢變得明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a recent long-term time frame.","zh":"這個短語給出近期長期時間框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stem from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"Many dietary health problems stem from excessive consumption of processed food.","zh":"許多與飲食有關的健康問題源自過量食用加工食品。"},{"en":"To stem from something means to originate from it or be caused by it.","zh":"“Stem from” 某事指源於它或由它造成。"},{"en":"A student’s stress may stem from poor time management rather than lack of ability.","zh":"學生壓力可能源自時間管理差，而不是能力不足。"},{"en":"If health problems stem from diet, changing food habits may reduce risk.","zh":"如果健康問題源自飲食，改變飲食習慣可能降低風險。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the source of a problem.","zh":"這個短語指向問題來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"an unholy trinity of","meaning":"三大禍首","examples":[{"en":"The writer describes sugar, fat and sodium as an unholy trinity.","zh":"作者把糖、脂肪和鈉描述為三大禍首。"},{"en":"An unholy trinity of things is a group of three harmful or troubling things acting together.","zh":"“An unholy trinity of” 某些事物指三種有害或令人困擾的事物一起作用。"},{"en":"For students, lack of sleep, poor planning and phone distraction can become an unholy trinity before exams.","zh":"對學生來說，睡眠不足、規劃差和手機干擾可以在考試前成為三大禍首。"},{"en":"If sugar, fat and sodium appear together in processed food, they can create serious health concerns.","zh":"如果糖、脂肪和鈉一起出現在加工食品中，可能造成嚴重健康關注。"},{"en":"The phrase is strongly negative and memorable.","zh":"這個短語非常負面且令人容易記住。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sugar, fat and sodium","meaning":"糖、脂肪和鈉","examples":[{"en":"Sugar, fat and sodium are common in heavily processed food.","zh":"糖、脂肪和鈉常見於高度加工食品中。"},{"en":"Sugar, fat and sodium are three ingredients often linked to taste, preservation and health concerns.","zh":"糖、脂肪和鈉是三種常與味道、保存和健康關注相關的成分。"},{"en":"A snack may taste good because it contains a lot of sugar, fat and sodium.","zh":"零食可能因含有大量糖、脂肪和鈉而味道好。"},{"en":"If a diet contains too much sugar, fat and sodium, health risks may increase over time.","zh":"如果飲食含有過多糖、脂肪和鈉，健康風險可能隨時間增加。"},{"en":"The phrase names three major dietary concerns in processed food.","zh":"這個短語指出加工食品中的三大飲食關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"health risk","meaning":"健康風險","examples":[{"en":"Natural flavour alone is not regarded as a significant health risk.","zh":"天然香味劑本身不被視為重大健康風險。"},{"en":"A health risk is something that may harm health or increase the chance of illness.","zh":"健康風險是可能傷害健康或增加患病機會的事物。"},{"en":"Smoking is a health risk because it can damage the lungs and heart.","zh":"吸煙是健康風險，因為它會損害肺部和心臟。"},{"en":"If an ingredient is a small health risk on its own, the whole diet may still matter more.","zh":"如果一種成分本身健康風險小，整體飲食可能仍然更重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes possible danger to physical well-being.","zh":"這個短語描述對身體健康的可能危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"play a role in","meaning":"在……中發揮作用","examples":[{"en":"Flavouring plays a role in making processed foods more appealing.","zh":"香味劑在令加工食品更吸引方面發揮作用。"},{"en":"To play a role in something means to contribute to it or be one factor in it.","zh":"“Play a role in” 某事指對它有貢獻或是其中一個因素。"},{"en":"Sleep plays a role in memory because the brain uses rest to organise information.","zh":"睡眠在記憶中發揮作用，因為大腦利用休息整理資料。"},{"en":"If flavouring plays a role in food appeal, it helps people enjoy products more.","zh":"如果香味劑在食品吸引力中發揮作用，它就幫助人們更享受產品。"},{"en":"The phrase shows partial contribution, not necessarily the only cause.","zh":"這個短語顯示部分貢獻，而不一定是唯一原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"taste fresh and nutritious","meaning":"吃起來新鮮而有營養","examples":[{"en":"Added flavours can make processed foods taste fresh and nutritious.","zh":"添加香味可以令加工食品吃起來新鮮而有營養。"},{"en":"To taste fresh and nutritious means to seem natural, lively and healthy when eaten.","zh":"“Taste fresh and nutritious” 指食用時感覺天然、有活力和健康。"},{"en":"A packaged fruit drink may taste fresh and nutritious even if it contains little real fruit.","zh":"包裝水果飲品即使含很少真正水果，也可能吃起來新鮮而有營養。"},{"en":"If flavouring creates a fresh taste, consumers may think the product is healthier than it is.","zh":"如果香味劑創造新鮮味道，消費者可能以為產品比實際更健康。"},{"en":"The phrase describes perceived taste, not guaranteed nutrition.","zh":"這個短語描述感受到的味道，而不是保證營養。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"even when they are not","meaning":"即使實際上並非如此","examples":[{"en":"Some foods taste wholesome even when they are not particularly healthy.","zh":"一些食品吃起來健康，即使實際上並非特別健康。"},{"en":"Even when they are not means although the reality is different from how they appear.","zh":"“Even when they are not” 指雖然實際情況與表象不同。"},{"en":"A drink may look natural even when it is not made mainly from fruit.","zh":"飲品可能看起來天然，即使實際上並非主要由水果製成。"},{"en":"If food tastes healthy even when it is not, consumers may eat more of it.","zh":"如果食品吃起來健康，即使實際上並非如此，消費者可能吃得更多。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a contrast between appearance and truth.","zh":"這個短語製造表象與真相之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be considered the culprit","meaning":"被視為罪魁禍首","examples":[{"en":"The flavour industry should not be considered the main culprit.","zh":"食品香味產業不應被視為主要罪魁禍首。"},{"en":"To be considered the culprit means to be regarded as the main person or thing responsible for a problem.","zh":"“Be considered the culprit” 指被視為對問題負主要責任的人或事物。"},{"en":"A teacher should not be considered the culprit if poor results come from lack of sleep and no revision.","zh":"如果成績差源自睡眠不足和沒有溫習，老師不應被視為罪魁禍首。"},{"en":"If sugar, fat and sodium cause the greatest harm, flavouring may not be the main culprit.","zh":"如果糖、脂肪和鈉造成最大傷害，香味劑可能不是主要罪魁禍首。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies blame or responsibility.","zh":"這個短語指出責任或歸咎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"willing accomplice","meaning":"自願幫兇","examples":[{"en":"The writer describes natural flavour as a willing accomplice to unhealthy food.","zh":"作者把天然香味劑描述為不健康食品的自願幫兇。"},{"en":"A willing accomplice is someone or something that knowingly helps a harmful action happen.","zh":"自願幫兇是明知而幫助有害行動發生的人或事物。"},{"en":"In a class prank, a student who opens the door for others may be a willing accomplice.","zh":"在班級惡作劇中，替其他人開門的學生可能是自願幫兇。"},{"en":"If flavouring makes unhealthy food easier to enjoy, it can help the problem without being the main cause.","zh":"如果香味劑令不健康食品更容易令人享受，它就能幫助問題，即使不是主要原因。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests helpful participation in something negative.","zh":"這個短語暗示在負面事情中提供幫助。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"which paragraph contains","meaning":"哪一段包含……","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which paragraph contains each piece of information.","zh":"學生識別哪一段包含每項資料。"},{"en":"Which paragraph contains means which section of the passage includes the stated detail.","zh":"“Which paragraph contains” 指文章哪一部分包括所述細節。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students scan names, dates and key phrases to find which paragraph contains an answer.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生掃讀姓名、日期和關鍵短語，以找出哪一段包含答案。"},{"en":"If one paragraph contains several details, students may use the same letter more than once.","zh":"如果一段包含幾項細節，學生可能不止一次使用同一字母。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in paragraph-matching tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於段落配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the following information","meaning":"以下資料","examples":[{"en":"The task asks students to locate the following information.","zh":"題目要求學生找出以下資料的位置。"},{"en":"The following information means the details listed after the instruction.","zh":"以下資料指指示後列出的細節。"},{"en":"Students should read the following information carefully before searching the passage.","zh":"學生搜尋文章前，應仔細閱讀以下資料。"},{"en":"If the following information uses paraphrases, students must look for meaning rather than exact words.","zh":"如果以下資料使用改寫，學生必須尋找意思，而不只是完全相同的字。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the items that come next.","zh":"這個短語指接下來列出的項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"use any letter more than once","meaning":"可重複使用任何字母","examples":[{"en":"The same paragraph letter may be used more than once.","zh":"同一段落字母可以被使用超過一次。"},{"en":"Use any letter more than once means an answer option can be repeated.","zh":"“Use any letter more than once” 指答案選項可以重複使用。"},{"en":"In a matching task, students may use B twice if paragraph B contains two answers.","zh":"在配對題中，如果 B 段包含兩個答案，學生可以使用 B 兩次。"},{"en":"If this instruction is given, students should not force every answer to have a different letter.","zh":"如果給出這個指示，學生不應強行讓每個答案都有不同字母。"},{"en":"The phrase changes how students handle matching questions.","zh":"這個短語改變學生處理配對題的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"examples of companies","meaning":"公司例子","examples":[{"en":"The passage gives examples of companies that manufacture natural flavours.","zh":"文章給出製造天然香味劑的公司例子。"},{"en":"Examples of companies are specific company names used to illustrate a point.","zh":"公司例子是用來說明某觀點的具體公司名稱。"},{"en":"A business textbook may give examples of companies that changed their branding successfully.","zh":"商業教科書可能給出成功改變品牌形象的公司例子。"},{"en":"If a passage includes company examples, readers can see that the industry is real and specific.","zh":"如果文章包括公司例子，讀者就能看見該行業是真實且具體的。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to concrete business cases.","zh":"這個短語指具體商業案例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"create natural flavours","meaning":"製造天然香味劑","examples":[{"en":"Specialist companies create natural flavours for processed products.","zh":"專門公司為加工產品製造天然香味劑。"},{"en":"To create natural flavours means to design flavourings from natural sources for use in food or drink.","zh":"“Create natural flavours” 指從天然來源設計用於食品或飲品的香味劑。"},{"en":"A flavour company may create natural flavours that make yoghurt taste like mango or vanilla.","zh":"香味公司可能製造天然香味劑，使乳酪有芒果味或雲呢拿味。"},{"en":"If companies create natural flavours well, processed products can taste fresher than they are.","zh":"如果公司製造天然香味劑的技術好，加工產品可以吃起來比實際更新鮮。"},{"en":"The phrase describes professional flavour design.","zh":"這個短語描述專業香味設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an instance of","meaning":"……的一個例子","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for an instance of a company responding to public concern.","zh":"題目要求找出一個公司回應公眾關注的例子。"},{"en":"An instance of something is one example or case of it.","zh":"某事的一個例子，是它的一個案例或情況。"},{"en":"A refund after a complaint is an instance of a shop taking customer service seriously.","zh":"投訴後退款，是商店認真對待顧客服務的一個例子。"},{"en":"If a passage asks for an instance, students should find one specific example.","zh":"如果文章要求找出一個例子，學生應尋找一個具體例子。"},{"en":"The phrase means a particular example, not a general idea.","zh":"這個短語意思是特定例子，而不是一般概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"multinational franchise","meaning":"跨國特許經營連鎖企業","examples":[{"en":"A multinational franchise changed its cooking oil after public criticism.","zh":"一間跨國特許經營連鎖企業在公眾批評後改變烹調油。"},{"en":"A multinational franchise is a branded business operating through outlets in many countries.","zh":"跨國特許經營連鎖企業是透過多國分店營運的品牌企業。"},{"en":"A fast-food chain with restaurants in dozens of countries is a multinational franchise.","zh":"在數十個國家有餐廳的快餐連鎖店就是跨國特許經營連鎖企業。"},{"en":"If a multinational franchise changes an ingredient, the decision can affect customers worldwide.","zh":"如果跨國特許經營連鎖企業改變一種成分，該決定可以影響全球顧客。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an international chain business.","zh":"這個短語描述國際連鎖企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"respond to public pressure","meaning":"回應公眾壓力","examples":[{"en":"Large food companies sometimes respond to public pressure by changing ingredients.","zh":"大型食品公司有時透過改變成分來回應公眾壓力。"},{"en":"To respond to public pressure means to act because many people are criticising or demanding change.","zh":"“Respond to public pressure” 指因許多人批評或要求改變而採取行動。"},{"en":"A school may respond to public pressure by improving lunch quality after parents complain.","zh":"家長投訴後，學校可能透過改善午餐質素回應公眾壓力。"},{"en":"If customers worry about health, companies may respond by reducing salt, sugar or fat.","zh":"如果顧客擔心健康，公司可能透過減少鹽、糖或脂肪作回應。"},{"en":"The phrase connects public opinion with organisational action.","zh":"這個短語把公眾意見與組織行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a statement on","meaning":"關於……的陳述","examples":[{"en":"The passage contains a statement on the health effects of flavourings.","zh":"文章包含一項關於香味劑健康影響的陳述。"},{"en":"A statement on something is a written or spoken comment about that topic.","zh":"關於某事的陳述，是就該題目作出的書面或口頭評論。"},{"en":"A school may issue a statement on exam arrangements before bad weather arrives.","zh":"學校可能在惡劣天氣到來前發布關於考試安排的陳述。"},{"en":"If a passage includes a statement on health effects, students should look for a clear claim or judgement.","zh":"如果文章包括關於健康影響的陳述，學生應尋找清楚主張或判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase points to an expressed view about a topic.","zh":"這個短語指對某題目表達出的看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"health effects","meaning":"對健康的影響","examples":[{"en":"Consumers often ask about the health effects of food additives.","zh":"消費者常詢問食品添加劑對健康的影響。"},{"en":"Health effects are the ways something influences the body or well-being.","zh":"對健康的影響，是某事物影響身體或健康狀況的方式。"},{"en":"Doctors study the health effects of sleep, exercise and diet.","zh":"醫生研究睡眠、運動和飲食對健康的影響。"},{"en":"If an additive has negative health effects, regulators may restrict its use.","zh":"如果添加劑有負面健康影響，監管機構可能限制其使用。"},{"en":"The phrase can refer to good or bad effects on health.","zh":"這個短語可以指對健康的好或壞影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a solution turns into a problem","meaning":"解決方法反而造成問題","examples":[{"en":"The change to vegetable oil shows how a solution can turn into a problem.","zh":"改用植物油顯示解決方法如何反而造成問題。"},{"en":"A solution turns into a problem when something meant to fix one issue creates another issue.","zh":"當原本用來解決一個問題的做法造成另一個問題，解決方法就反而造成問題。"},{"en":"Moving lessons online solved travel problems but became a problem for students without stable internet.","zh":"網上上課解決了交通問題，但對沒有穩定網絡的學生來說卻成為問題。"},{"en":"If removing beef fat lowers cholesterol but weakens flavour, the solution creates a new difficulty.","zh":"如果移除牛脂降低膽固醇但削弱味道，解決方法就造成新困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unintended consequences.","zh":"這個短語描述意料之外的後果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"encounter a term","meaning":"遇到某個用語","examples":[{"en":"Consumers may encounter the term “natural flavour” on food packaging.","zh":"消費者可能在食品包裝上遇到 “natural flavour” 這個用語。"},{"en":"To encounter a term means to see or come across a word or phrase.","zh":"“Encounter a term” 指看見或碰到某個詞語或短語。"},{"en":"Students may encounter the term “sustainability” in science, geography and business lessons.","zh":"學生可能在科學、地理和商業課中遇到 “sustainability” 這個用語。"},{"en":"If consumers encounter a term often but do not understand it, confusion can grow.","zh":"如果消費者常遇到某個用語但不了解它，困惑可能增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes meeting language in reading or daily life.","zh":"這個短語描述在閱讀或日常生活中遇到語言。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a place in the home","meaning":"家中的某個地方","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to a place in the home where packaged food is stored.","zh":"題目指家中某個存放包裝食品的地方。"},{"en":"A place in the home means a specific area or room inside a house or flat.","zh":"家中的某個地方指屋或單位內的特定區域或房間。"},{"en":"A kitchen cupboard is a place in the home where families keep dry food.","zh":"廚櫃是家中存放乾糧的地方。"},{"en":"If the question asks for a home location, students should look for words like pantry, kitchen or cupboard.","zh":"如果題目問家庭位置，學生應尋找 pantry、kitchen 或 cupboard 這類詞。"},{"en":"The phrase points to a domestic setting.","zh":"這個短語指家庭環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"transformation of food","meaning":"食物的轉變過程","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes the transformation of food during processing.","zh":"文章描述食品加工期間食物的轉變過程。"},{"en":"Transformation of food means the way food changes in form, taste, colour, texture or storage life.","zh":"食物的轉變過程指食物在形態、味道、顏色、質感或保存期上的改變。"},{"en":"Turning fresh milk into cheese is one kind of food transformation.","zh":"把新鮮牛奶變成芝士是一種食物轉變。"},{"en":"If processing transforms food too much, flavour may need to be added back in.","zh":"如果加工令食物轉變過多，味道可能需要被重新加入。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how food becomes different from its original state.","zh":"這個短語強調食物如何變得不同於原本狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"processed grocery items","meaning":"加工雜貨食品","examples":[{"en":"Processed grocery items may undergo numerous chemical and physical treatments.","zh":"加工雜貨食品可能經歷許多化學和物理處理。"},{"en":"Processed grocery items are packaged supermarket foods that have been changed from their original form.","zh":"加工雜貨食品是超市中已從原本形態改變的包裝食品。"},{"en":"Breakfast cereal, canned soup and frozen meals are processed grocery items.","zh":"早餐穀物、罐頭湯和冷凍餐都是加工雜貨食品。"},{"en":"If grocery items are processed heavily, labels may list many additives and stabilisers.","zh":"如果雜貨食品高度加工，標籤可能列出許多添加劑和穩定劑。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to everyday supermarket products that have been industrially prepared.","zh":"這個短語指經工業製備的日常超市產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a comparison of A and B","meaning":"A 與 B 的比較","examples":[{"en":"The passage makes a comparison of human and technological detection abilities.","zh":"文章對人類和科技檢測能力作出比較。"},{"en":"A comparison of A and B means looking at two things together to see similarities or differences.","zh":"A 與 B 的比較指把兩件事放在一起看，以找出相似或差異。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask for a comparison of city life and village life.","zh":"老師可能要求學生比較城市生活與鄉村生活。"},{"en":"If a passage compares machines and the human nose, students should notice which is stronger in each way.","zh":"如果文章比較機器和人類鼻子，學生應注意各自在哪方面較強。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful for questions about contrast.","zh":"這個短語適用於關於對比的題目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"technological abilities","meaning":"科技能力","examples":[{"en":"Modern instruments have remarkable technological abilities.","zh":"現代儀器有驚人的科技能力。"},{"en":"Technological abilities are what machines, tools or systems can do through technology.","zh":"科技能力是機器、工具或系統透過科技能做到的事情。"},{"en":"Smartphones have technological abilities such as translation, navigation and video calling.","zh":"智能手機有翻譯、導航和視像通話等科技能力。"},{"en":"If instruments have strong technological abilities, they can detect chemicals humans cannot easily measure.","zh":"如果儀器科技能力強，就能偵測人類難以量度的化學物。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on machine-based capability.","zh":"這個短語強調以機器為基礎的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"flavour detection","meaning":"味道與香氣檢測","examples":[{"en":"Both machines and the human nose are used in flavour detection.","zh":"機器和人類鼻子都用於味道與香氣檢測。"},{"en":"Flavour detection is the process of identifying tastes and aromas.","zh":"味道與香氣檢測是識別味道和香氣的過程。"},{"en":"A food company may use flavour detection to check whether every batch tastes the same.","zh":"食品公司可能使用味道與香氣檢測，檢查每批產品味道是否一致。"},{"en":"If flavour detection is precise, tiny changes in smell can be noticed before products reach shops.","zh":"如果檢測精準，產品到達商店前就能注意到微小氣味變化。"},{"en":"The phrase combines sensory judgement and scientific analysis.","zh":"這個短語結合感官判斷和科學分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"diet-related health conditions","meaning":"與飲食有關的健康問題","examples":[{"en":"Obesity and diabetes are diet-related health conditions.","zh":"肥胖症和糖尿病是與飲食有關的健康問題。"},{"en":"Diet-related health conditions are illnesses or health problems linked to what people eat.","zh":"與飲食有關的健康問題，是與人們所吃食物相關的疾病或健康問題。"},{"en":"High blood pressure may be a diet-related health condition when salt intake is very high.","zh":"當鹽分攝取非常高時，高血壓可能是與飲食有關的健康問題。"},{"en":"If processed food consumption rises, diet-related health conditions may become more common.","zh":"如果加工食品消費增加，與飲食有關的健康問題可能更常見。"},{"en":"The phrase connects eating habits with health outcomes.","zh":"這個短語把飲食習慣與健康結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"符合文中資料","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the passage.","zh":"學生判斷每項陳述是否符合文章資料。"},{"en":"To agree with the information given means to match what the text says.","zh":"“Agree with the information given” 指與文本所說內容相符。"},{"en":"If the passage says natural flavour is not the main health risk, a similar statement agrees with the information given.","zh":"如果文章說天然香味劑不是主要健康風險，相同意思的陳述就符合文中資料。"},{"en":"Students should choose TRUE only when the whole statement matches the passage.","zh":"只有整項陳述與文章相符時，學生才應選 TRUE。"},{"en":"The phrase is used in reading-comprehension tasks.","zh":"這個短語用於閱讀理解題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與文中資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement may contradict information provided by the writer.","zh":"陳述可能與作者提供的資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"“Contradict the information” 指說出與文章內容相反的意思。"},{"en":"If the text says vegetable oil was used later, a statement saying it was used first contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文本說植物油是後來使用的，而陳述說它最先使用，就是與文中資料矛盾。"},{"en":"One changed detail can make a statement contradict the passage.","zh":"一個被改變的細節可以令陳述與文章矛盾。"},{"en":"The phrase helps students identify FALSE answers.","zh":"這個短語幫助學生識別 FALSE 答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"文中沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"This response is used when the passage provides no relevant information.","zh":"當文章沒有提供相關資料時，使用這個回應。"},{"en":"No information on this means the text does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"文中沒有相關資料指文本沒有說明該陳述是真還是假。"},{"en":"If a passage mentions a company but not its profit, there is no information on that profit.","zh":"如果文章提到一間公司但沒有提及其利潤，關於利潤就沒有資料。"},{"en":"Students should not guess from general knowledge when there is no information in the passage.","zh":"當文章沒有資料時，學生不應根據常識猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase signals a NOT GIVEN answer.","zh":"這個短語表示 NOT GIVEN 答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have a strong flavour","meaning":"味道濃烈","examples":[{"en":"Pure vegetable oils may not have a strong flavour on their own.","zh":"純植物油本身味道可能不濃烈。"},{"en":"To have a strong flavour means to taste powerful, clear or noticeable.","zh":"“Have a strong flavour” 指味道強烈、清楚或明顯。"},{"en":"Garlic soup has a strong flavour that can stay in the mouth for a long time.","zh":"蒜湯味道濃烈，可以在口中停留很久。"},{"en":"If an oil does not have a strong flavour, food cooked in it may taste bland.","zh":"如果油味道不濃烈，用它煮的食物可能味道較淡。"},{"en":"The phrase describes intensity of taste.","zh":"這個短語描述味道強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be lower in cholesterol than","meaning":"膽固醇含量低於……","examples":[{"en":"The statement compares whether one cooking oil is lower in cholesterol than another.","zh":"該陳述比較一種烹調油的膽固醇含量是否低於另一種。"},{"en":"To be lower in cholesterol than something means to contain less cholesterol than it.","zh":"“Be lower in cholesterol than” 某物指膽固醇含量比它少。"},{"en":"A plant-based spread may be lower in cholesterol than butter.","zh":"植物性抹醬的膽固醇含量可能低於牛油。"},{"en":"If a new cooking oil is lower in cholesterol, companies may promote it as healthier.","zh":"如果新烹調油膽固醇較低，公司可能宣傳它較健康。"},{"en":"The phrase makes a nutritional comparison.","zh":"這個短語作出營養比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"become more popular","meaning":"變得更受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Processed foods are becoming more popular in some Asian countries.","zh":"加工食品在一些亞洲國家變得更受歡迎。"},{"en":"To become more popular means to be liked, bought or used by more people.","zh":"“Become more popular” 指被更多人喜歡、購買或使用。"},{"en":"Cycling may become more popular if a city builds safe bike lanes.","zh":"如果城市建造安全單車徑，踩單車可能變得更受歡迎。"},{"en":"If processed foods become more popular, supermarkets may sell more packaged meals and snacks.","zh":"如果加工食品變得更受歡迎，超市可能出售更多包裝餐和零食。"},{"en":"The phrase describes rising public acceptance or use.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾接受度或使用量上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"food processing","meaning":"食品加工","examples":[{"en":"Food processing can involve preservation, colouring, drying and flavouring.","zh":"食品加工可以涉及保存、着色、乾燥和調味。"},{"en":"Food processing is the changing of food from its original state for storage, safety, convenience or taste.","zh":"食品加工是為儲存、安全、方便或味道而改變食物原本狀態。"},{"en":"Freezing vegetables, canning soup and drying fruit are forms of food processing.","zh":"冷凍蔬菜、罐裝湯和水果乾都是食品加工形式。"},{"en":"If food processing is heavy, the final product may contain many added ingredients.","zh":"如果食品加工程度高，最終產品可能含有許多添加成分。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the methods used to prepare food before sale or storage.","zh":"這個短語指銷售或儲存前處理食物的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"involve the use of","meaning":"涉及使用……","examples":[{"en":"Not all food processing necessarily involves the use of natural flavours.","zh":"並非所有食品加工都必然涉及使用天然香味劑。"},{"en":"To involve the use of something means to include that thing as part of the process.","zh":"“Involve the use of” 某物指把該物包括為過程的一部分。"},{"en":"Cleaning a classroom may involve the use of disinfectant, gloves and rubbish bags.","zh":"清潔課室可能涉及使用消毒劑、手套和垃圾袋。"},{"en":"If processing does not involve flavourings, taste may come only from the original ingredients.","zh":"如果加工不涉及使用香味劑，味道可能只來自原本成分。"},{"en":"The phrase explains whether a tool or ingredient is included.","zh":"這個短語解釋是否包括某工具或成分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for the final question.","zh":"學生為最後一題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option marked by the right letter.","zh":"“Choose the correct letter” 指選出由正確字母標示的答案選項。"},{"en":"Students should read all options before choosing the correct letter in a multiple-choice question.","zh":"在選擇題中，學生應先閱讀所有選項，再選出正確字母。"},{"en":"If two answers look similar, the passage evidence should decide which letter is correct.","zh":"如果兩個答案看似相似，文章證據應決定哪個字母正確。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"conclude that","meaning":"得出結論認為","examples":[{"en":"The writer concludes that flavourings help make processed food appealing.","zh":"作者得出結論認為香味劑幫助令加工食品吸引。"},{"en":"To conclude that something is true means to reach that final judgement after considering evidence.","zh":"“Conclude that” 某事為真指考慮證據後達到該最終判斷。"},{"en":"After reading the survey, the teacher concluded that students needed more vocabulary practice.","zh":"閱讀調查後，老師得出結論認為學生需要更多詞彙練習。"},{"en":"If the writer concludes something, it is usually the final meaning they want readers to take away.","zh":"如果作者得出某結論，通常就是希望讀者帶走的最終意思。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a reasoned final view.","zh":"這個短語引出有理據的最終看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"major cause of","meaning":"……的主要成因","examples":[{"en":"Natural flavour is not described as the major cause of dietary disease.","zh":"天然香味劑並沒有被描述為飲食疾病的主要成因。"},{"en":"A major cause of something is one of the most important reasons it happens.","zh":"某事的主要成因，是導致它發生的最重要原因之一。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can be a major cause of poor concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以是課堂專注力差的主要成因。"},{"en":"If sugar and fat are the major causes, flavouring may be a secondary concern.","zh":"如果糖和脂肪是主要成因，香味劑可能是次要關注。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a main reason, not a minor factor.","zh":"這個短語指出主要原因，而不是小因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"dietary health problems","meaning":"與飲食有關的健康問題","examples":[{"en":"Excessive sugar, fat and sodium contribute to dietary health problems.","zh":"過量糖、脂肪和鈉會造成與飲食有關的健康問題。"},{"en":"Dietary health problems are health issues linked to what people eat and drink.","zh":"與飲食有關的健康問題，是與人們所吃和所喝東西相關的健康問題。"},{"en":"Tooth decay, obesity and diabetes can be dietary health problems when eating habits are poor.","zh":"當飲食習慣差時，蛀牙、肥胖症和糖尿病都可以是與飲食有關的健康問題。"},{"en":"If processed foods dominate a diet, dietary health problems may become more common.","zh":"如果加工食品主導飲食，與飲食有關的健康問題可能更常見。"},{"en":"The phrase connects nutrition with illness or poor health.","zh":"這個短語把營養與疾病或健康欠佳連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"unhealthy but not as bad as","meaning":"不健康，但沒有……那麼差","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that flavourings are unhealthy but not as bad as other ingredients.","zh":"該選項暗示香味劑不健康，但沒有其他成分那麼差。"},{"en":"Unhealthy but not as bad as means harmful to some degree, but less harmful than something else.","zh":"“Unhealthy but not as bad as” 指某程度上有害，但比另一事物傷害較少。"},{"en":"A sweetened yoghurt may be unhealthy but not as bad as a large sugary soft drink.","zh":"加糖乳酪可能不健康，但沒有一大杯含糖汽水那麼差。"},{"en":"If one ingredient is unhealthy but not the worst problem, the writer may treat it as a secondary concern.","zh":"如果一種成分不健康但不是最嚴重問題，作者可能把它視為次要關注。"},{"en":"The phrase makes a comparison of harm.","zh":"這個短語比較傷害程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"health benefits","meaning":"健康益處","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not claim that natural flavours provide health benefits.","zh":"文章沒有聲稱天然香味劑提供健康益處。"},{"en":"Health benefits are positive effects that improve or protect health.","zh":"健康益處是改善或保護健康的正面效果。"},{"en":"Regular walking can provide health benefits such as better mood and stronger heart function.","zh":"定期步行可以提供健康益處，例如更好心情和更強心臟功能。"},{"en":"If a product claims health benefits, consumers should look for evidence.","zh":"如果產品聲稱有健康益處，消費者應尋找證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes helpful effects on health.","zh":"這個短語描述對健康有幫助的效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cancel out","meaning":"抵銷","examples":[{"en":"One harmful ingredient may cancel out the benefit of another ingredient.","zh":"一種有害成分可能抵銷另一種成分的益處。"},{"en":"To cancel out something means to reduce or remove its effect by an opposite effect.","zh":"“Cancel out” 某效果指透過相反效果減弱或消除它。"},{"en":"A good night’s sleep may be cancelled out by skipping breakfast and drinking too much coffee.","zh":"一晚好睡眠可能被不吃早餐和喝太多咖啡抵銷。"},{"en":"If a food contains vitamins but also a lot of sugar, the sugar may reduce its health value.","zh":"如果食物含維他命但也含大量糖，其糖分可能降低健康價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one effect neutralising another.","zh":"這個短語描述一種效果中和另一種效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"unhealthy foods","meaning":"不健康的食物","examples":[{"en":"Flavouring can make unhealthy foods taste fresher and more attractive.","zh":"香味劑可以令不健康的食物吃起來更新鮮、更吸引。"},{"en":"Unhealthy foods are foods that may harm health when eaten often or in large amounts.","zh":"不健康的食物是經常或大量食用時可能傷害健康的食物。"},{"en":"Many fried snacks and sugary drinks are unhealthy foods if they replace balanced meals.","zh":"如果油炸零食和含糖飲品取代均衡膳食，它們就是不健康的食物。"},{"en":"If unhealthy foods taste fresh, consumers may underestimate how processed they are.","zh":"如果不健康的食物吃起來新鮮，消費者可能低估其加工程度。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to food with poor nutritional value or health risks.","zh":"這個短語指營養價值差或有健康風險的食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make something taste better","meaning":"令……味道更好","examples":[{"en":"Natural flavour helps make processed foods taste better.","zh":"天然香味劑幫助令加工食品味道更好。"},{"en":"To make something taste better means to improve its flavour so people enjoy eating or drinking it more.","zh":"“Make something taste better” 指改善味道，使人更享受吃或喝它。"},{"en":"A little lemon juice can make soup taste better if it feels too heavy.","zh":"如果湯感覺太膩，一點檸檬汁可以令它味道更好。"},{"en":"If flavouring makes processed food taste better, people may buy it more often.","zh":"如果香味劑令加工食品味道更好，人們可能更常購買。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improving taste, not necessarily improving health.","zh":"這個短語描述改善味道，而不一定改善健康。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 167 - The Flavour Industry.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 168":[{"front":"growing up in New Zealand","meaning":"在新西蘭成長","examples":[{"en":"The study follows thousands of children growing up in New Zealand.","zh":"這項研究追蹤數千名在新西蘭成長的兒童。"},{"en":"Growing up in New Zealand means spending one’s childhood and early development in New Zealand.","zh":"growing up in New Zealand 指在新西蘭度過童年和早期發展階段。"},{"en":"A child growing up in New Zealand may experience local schools, languages, food, and family customs.","zh":"在新西蘭成長的孩子可能經歷當地學校、語言、食物和家庭習俗。"},{"en":"If researchers follow children growing up in New Zealand, they can understand how the country shapes their lives.","zh":"如果研究人員追蹤在新西蘭成長的兒童，就能了解這個國家如何塑造他們的生活。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on where childhood takes place.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於童年在哪裡發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"it has long been known that","meaning":"人們早已知道","examples":[{"en":"It has long been known that early childhood has a major influence on health.","zh":"人們早已知道幼兒期對健康有重大影響。"},{"en":"It has long been known that means people have understood this fact for a long time.","zh":"it has long been known that 指人們很久以前已明白這個事實。"},{"en":"It has long been known that sleep affects students’ concentration and memory.","zh":"人們早已知道睡眠會影響學生的專注力和記憶。"},{"en":"If something has long been known, new research may focus on explaining exactly how it works.","zh":"如果某事早已為人所知，新研究可能集中解釋它究竟如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an established idea.","zh":"這個片語引入已確立的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the first one thousand days of life","meaning":"人生最初一千日","examples":[{"en":"The first one thousand days of life are critical to a child’s development.","zh":"人生最初一千日對兒童發展至關重要。"},{"en":"The first one thousand days of life means the early period from pregnancy through about the first two years after birth.","zh":"the first one thousand days of life 指由懷孕至出生後約兩年的早期階段。"},{"en":"During the first one thousand days of life, babies need nutrition, care, sleep, and safe surroundings.","zh":"在人生最初一千日，嬰兒需要營養、照顧、睡眠和安全環境。"},{"en":"If this early period is unhealthy or unstable, later development may be affected.","zh":"如果這個早期階段不健康或不穩定，日後發展可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a very important early-life window.","zh":"這個片語突出生命早期一個非常重要的窗口期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be critical in ensuring","meaning":"對確保……至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Early nutrition is critical in ensuring a child’s healthy future.","zh":"早期營養對確保孩子健康的未來至關重要。"},{"en":"To be critical in ensuring something means to be extremely important in making sure it happens.","zh":"be critical in ensuring something 指對確保某事發生極為重要。"},{"en":"Regular practice is critical in ensuring steady progress in language learning.","zh":"定期練習對確保語言學習穩定進步至關重要。"},{"en":"If early care is poor, it may be harder to ensure good health later.","zh":"如果早期照顧不足，日後可能較難確保良好健康。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor plays a key role in achieving a result.","zh":"這個片語顯示某因素在達成結果中扮演關鍵角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a healthy future","meaning":"健康的未來","examples":[{"en":"The study investigates factors that contribute to a healthy future.","zh":"這項研究調查有助健康未來的因素。"},{"en":"A healthy future means later life with good physical, mental, and social well-being.","zh":"a healthy future 指日後有良好的身體、心理和社交福祉。"},{"en":"A child needs food, safety, learning, and family support to build a healthy future.","zh":"孩子需要食物、安全、學習和家庭支援來建立健康的未來。"},{"en":"If early problems are ignored, a healthy future may become harder to achieve.","zh":"如果早期問題被忽視，健康的未來可能較難實現。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to long-term well-being, not only the absence of illness.","zh":"這個片語指長遠福祉，而不只是沒有疾病。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"precisely what happens","meaning":"究竟發生甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Researchers want to understand precisely what happens during early childhood.","zh":"研究人員想了解幼兒期究竟發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Precisely what happens means exactly what takes place, without vague guessing.","zh":"precisely what happens 指確切發生甚麼，而不是含糊猜測。"},{"en":"A doctor may ask precisely what happens before a patient feels dizzy.","zh":"醫生可能詢問病人頭暈前究竟發生甚麼。"},{"en":"If researchers know precisely what happens in early life, they can design better support.","zh":"如果研究人員知道早期生活究竟發生甚麼，就能設計更好的支援。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses exact understanding.","zh":"這個片語強調精確理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"during this period","meaning":"在這段期間","examples":[{"en":"Children undergo rapid development during this period.","zh":"兒童在這段期間經歷快速發展。"},{"en":"During this period means within the time being discussed.","zh":"during this period 指在正在討論的這段時間內。"},{"en":"During this period, students should avoid distractions and focus on revision.","zh":"在這段期間，學生應避免分心並專注溫習。"},{"en":"If children receive strong support during this period, later learning may become easier.","zh":"如果孩子在這段期間得到強大支援，日後學習可能更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a specific time frame.","zh":"這個片語指出特定時間範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"individual","meaning":"個人","examples":[{"en":"The researchers collected detailed information about each individual.","zh":"研究人員收集關於每個個人的詳細資料。"},{"en":"An individual is one person considered separately from a group.","zh":"individual 是被單獨看待的一個人，而不是整個群體。"},{"en":"A teacher may adjust feedback for each individual because students have different needs.","zh":"老師可能為每個個人調整回饋，因為學生有不同需要。"},{"en":"If researchers study individuals carefully, they can see differences hidden by averages.","zh":"如果研究人員仔細研究個人，就能看到平均數隱藏的差異。"},{"en":"This word focuses on one person rather than the whole group.","zh":"這個詞聚焦於一個人，而不是整個群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be less well documented","meaning":"記錄得較少","examples":[{"en":"The experiences of very young children have been less well documented.","zh":"非常年幼兒童的經歷記錄得較少。"},{"en":"To be less well documented means to have fewer records, studies, or written details.","zh":"be less well documented 指相關記錄、研究或書面細節較少。"},{"en":"A small village’s history may be less well documented than a capital city’s history.","zh":"小村莊的歷史可能比首都城市的歷史記錄得較少。"},{"en":"If children’s early experiences are not well documented, policymakers may lack reliable evidence.","zh":"如果兒童早期經歷記錄不足，政策制定者可能缺乏可靠證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shortage of recorded information.","zh":"這個片語描述記錄資料不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"allocate resources appropriately","meaning":"適當分配資源","examples":[{"en":"Governments need reliable evidence to allocate resources appropriately.","zh":"政府需要可靠證據來適當分配資源。"},{"en":"To allocate resources appropriately means to distribute money, staff, time, or services where they are most needed.","zh":"allocate resources appropriately 指把金錢、人手、時間或服務分配到最需要的地方。"},{"en":"A school may allocate resources appropriately by giving extra tutors to students who need support.","zh":"學校可以把額外導師安排給需要支援的學生，以適當分配資源。"},{"en":"If resources are allocated poorly, some families may receive help too late.","zh":"如果資源分配不當，一些家庭可能太遲才得到幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on fair and effective distribution.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於公平而有效的分配。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"public health policy","meaning":"公共衞生政策","examples":[{"en":"The findings may influence future public health policy.","zh":"這些研究發現可能影響未來公共衞生政策。"},{"en":"Public health policy is government planning and action designed to protect people’s health.","zh":"public health policy 是政府為保護人民健康而制定的規劃和行動。"},{"en":"Vaccination programmes, nutrition advice, and smoking rules are part of public health policy.","zh":"疫苗接種計劃、營養建議和吸煙規例都是公共衞生政策的一部分。"},{"en":"If research shows a serious health risk, public health policy may change.","zh":"如果研究顯示嚴重健康風險，公共衞生政策可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to health decisions made for the whole community.","zh":"這個片語指為整個社區作出的健康決策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"education policy","meaning":"教育政策","examples":[{"en":"Education policy should be based on reliable evidence.","zh":"教育政策應建基於可靠證據。"},{"en":"Education policy is the set of rules, plans, and decisions that shape schools and learning.","zh":"education policy 是塑造學校和學習的規則、計劃和決定。"},{"en":"Class size, curriculum, homework rules, and teacher training can all be affected by education policy.","zh":"班級大小、課程、功課規則和教師培訓都可能受教育政策影響。"},{"en":"If evidence shows children need early language support, education policy may fund preschool programmes.","zh":"如果證據顯示兒童需要早期語言支援，教育政策可能資助學前課程。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to official decisions about learning systems.","zh":"這個片語指關於學習制度的官方決策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be based upon","meaning":"建基於……","examples":[{"en":"Public policy needs to be based upon quantifiable data.","zh":"公共政策需要建基於可量化數據。"},{"en":"To be based upon something means to use it as the foundation or main support.","zh":"be based upon something 指以某事作為基礎或主要支持。"},{"en":"A teacher’s advice should be based upon a student’s actual work, not guesses.","zh":"老師的建議應建基於學生的實際作品，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"If policy is based upon weak evidence, it may fail to solve the real problem.","zh":"如果政策建基於薄弱證據，它可能無法解決真正問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the foundation of an idea, decision, or plan.","zh":"這個片語顯示想法、決定或計劃的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"quantifiable data","meaning":"可量化數據","examples":[{"en":"The study provides quantifiable data about child development.","zh":"這項研究提供關於兒童發展的可量化數據。"},{"en":"Quantifiable data is information that can be counted, measured, or expressed in numbers.","zh":"quantifiable data 是可以被計算、量度或用數字表達的資料。"},{"en":"Test scores, income levels, birth weights, and attendance rates are quantifiable data.","zh":"測驗分數、收入水平、出生體重和出席率都是可量化數據。"},{"en":"If researchers have quantifiable data, they can compare groups more accurately.","zh":"如果研究人員有可量化數據，就能更準確比較群體。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to measurable evidence.","zh":"這個片語指可量度的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Ministry of Social Development","meaning":"社會發展部","examples":[{"en":"The New Zealand Ministry of Social Development began the study.","zh":"新西蘭社會發展部開展了這項研究。"},{"en":"The Ministry of Social Development is a government department concerned with people’s welfare and social support.","zh":"Ministry of Social Development 是關注人民福祉和社會支援的政府部門。"},{"en":"A ministry may fund research to understand families, children, and poverty better.","zh":"部門可能資助研究，以更好了解家庭、兒童和貧窮。"},{"en":"If a government department starts a long study, the results may shape future services.","zh":"如果政府部門開展長期研究，結果可能塑造未來服務。"},{"en":"This phrase names the public body behind the project.","zh":"這個片語指出項目背後的公共機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"begin a longitudinal study","meaning":"開展縱向研究","examples":[{"en":"The ministry began a longitudinal study of children’s early lives.","zh":"該部門開展了一項關於兒童早期生活的縱向研究。"},{"en":"To begin a longitudinal study means to start research that follows the same people over time.","zh":"begin a longitudinal study 指開始一項長期追蹤同一批人的研究。"},{"en":"A university may begin a longitudinal study to track students from Form 1 to graduation.","zh":"大學可能開展縱向研究，追蹤學生由中一到畢業。"},{"en":"If researchers start early, they can see how childhood experiences affect later outcomes.","zh":"如果研究人員早期開始，就能看到童年經歷如何影響日後結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the start of long-term research.","zh":"這個片語描述長期研究的開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"longitudinal study","meaning":"縱向研究","examples":[{"en":"A longitudinal study follows the same participants over a long period.","zh":"縱向研究會在長時間內追蹤同一批參加者。"},{"en":"A longitudinal study is research that observes the same people, group, or cases repeatedly over time.","zh":"longitudinal study 是隨時間反覆觀察同一批人、群體或個案的研究。"},{"en":"A health researcher may use a longitudinal study to see how diet affects people after many years.","zh":"健康研究人員可能使用縱向研究，了解飲食多年後如何影響人。"},{"en":"If the same children are followed, researchers can connect early experiences with later development.","zh":"如果同一批兒童被追蹤，研究人員就能把早期經歷與日後發展連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts long-term tracking with a one-time survey.","zh":"這個片語把長期追蹤與一次性調查作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"early days","meaning":"早期階段","examples":[{"en":"The study examines the early days of thousands of children’s lives.","zh":"這項研究檢視數千名兒童生命的早期階段。"},{"en":"Early days means the beginning period of a life, project, or process.","zh":"early days 指人生、項目或過程的開始時期。"},{"en":"In the early days of a new job, workers may need extra guidance.","zh":"在新工作的早期階段，員工可能需要額外指導。"},{"en":"If problems appear in the early days, support can be provided before they grow serious.","zh":"如果問題在早期階段出現，就可以在它們變嚴重前提供支援。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the starting stage.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於開始階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"with a view to doing something","meaning":"目的是；期望能夠","examples":[{"en":"The researchers began the project with a view to extending it for two decades.","zh":"研究人員開展這個項目，目的是把它延長至二十年。"},{"en":"With a view to doing something means with the aim or intention of doing it later.","zh":"with a view to doing something 指以日後做某事為目的或意圖。"},{"en":"A student may save money with a view to studying overseas.","zh":"學生可能儲錢，目的是到海外升學。"},{"en":"If a project starts with a long-term aim, researchers must plan for future follow-up.","zh":"如果項目一開始有長期目的，研究人員就必須規劃日後跟進。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose behind an action.","zh":"這個片語解釋行動背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"extend something for","meaning":"將……延長","examples":[{"en":"The team hoped to extend the study for two decades.","zh":"團隊希望將這項研究延長二十年。"},{"en":"To extend something for a period means to make it continue for that length of time.","zh":"extend something for a period 指令某事持續某段時間。"},{"en":"A school may extend a reading programme for another year if students benefit from it.","zh":"如果學生受益，學校可能將閱讀計劃延長一年。"},{"en":"If a study is extended, researchers can collect more long-term evidence.","zh":"如果研究被延長，研究人員可以收集更多長期證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lengthening the duration of an activity.","zh":"這個片語描述延長活動的持續時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"two decades","meaning":"二十年","examples":[{"en":"The children may be followed for approximately two decades.","zh":"這些兒童可能被追蹤約二十年。"},{"en":"Two decades means twenty years.","zh":"two decades 指二十年。"},{"en":"A teacher who has taught for two decades has seen many changes in students and schools.","zh":"任教二十年的老師見過學生和學校許多變化。"},{"en":"If a study lasts two decades, it can show how childhood affects adulthood.","zh":"如果研究持續二十年，它可以顯示童年如何影響成年。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a long time span.","zh":"這個片語表示一段很長的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be recruited","meaning":"獲招募","examples":[{"en":"A total of 6,846 babies were recruited for the study.","zh":"共有6,846名嬰兒獲招募參與這項研究。"},{"en":"To be recruited means to be invited or selected to take part in a study, job, or organisation.","zh":"be recruited 指被邀請或選中參與研究、工作或組織。"},{"en":"Volunteers may be recruited for a community clean-up project.","zh":"義工可能獲招募參與社區清潔項目。"},{"en":"If enough participants are recruited, the study can produce more reliable results.","zh":"如果招募到足夠參加者，研究就能產生更可靠結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bringing people into a project.","zh":"這個片語描述把人納入某項目。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"densely populated area","meaning":"人口稠密地區","examples":[{"en":"The babies came from a densely populated area of New Zealand.","zh":"這些嬰兒來自新西蘭一個人口稠密地區。"},{"en":"A densely populated area is a place where many people live close together.","zh":"densely populated area 是許多人密集居住的地方。"},{"en":"A city centre is usually more densely populated than a mountain village.","zh":"市中心通常比山村更人口稠密。"},{"en":"If an area is densely populated, schools and clinics may face higher demand.","zh":"如果一個地區人口稠密，學校和診所可能面對更高需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place with a high number of people in limited space.","zh":"這個片語描述有限空間中人口很多的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"it is hoped that","meaning":"人們希望","examples":[{"en":"It is hoped that the participants will remain in the study until adulthood.","zh":"人們希望參加者會留在研究中直到成年。"},{"en":"It is hoped that means people hope or expect something will happen.","zh":"it is hoped that 指人們希望或期望某事會發生。"},{"en":"It is hoped that the new library will encourage more students to read.","zh":"人們希望新圖書館會鼓勵更多學生閱讀。"},{"en":"If participants stay in a study, researchers can collect stronger long-term evidence.","zh":"如果參加者留在研究中，研究人員就能收集更有力的長期證據。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a desired future result.","zh":"這個片語引入期望中的未來結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be followed until","meaning":"被持續追蹤至","examples":[{"en":"The children may be followed until they reach the age of 21.","zh":"這些兒童可能被持續追蹤至21歲。"},{"en":"To be followed until a time means to be observed or tracked up to that point.","zh":"be followed until a time 指被觀察或追蹤至某個時間點。"},{"en":"Patients may be followed until their symptoms disappear.","zh":"病人可能被持續跟進至症狀消失。"},{"en":"If children are followed until adulthood, researchers can see long-term outcomes.","zh":"如果兒童被追蹤至成年，研究人員可以看到長期結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continued observation up to a limit.","zh":"這個片語描述持續觀察至某個界限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reach the age of","meaning":"到達……歲","examples":[{"en":"The researchers hope to follow the children until they reach the age of 21.","zh":"研究人員希望追蹤這些兒童直到他們到達21歲。"},{"en":"To reach the age of a number means to become that many years old.","zh":"reach the age of a number 指年齡達到某個歲數。"},{"en":"When students reach the age of eighteen, they may make more legal decisions for themselves.","zh":"當學生到達十八歲，他們可能可以為自己作出更多法律決定。"},{"en":"If participants reach the age of 21 during the study, researchers can compare childhood and early adulthood.","zh":"如果參加者在研究中到達21歲，研究人員可以比較童年和成年早期。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a specific age milestone.","zh":"這個片語給出特定年齡里程碑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"collectively known as","meaning":"統稱為","examples":[{"en":"The first four reports are collectively known as Growing Up in New Zealand.","zh":"首四份報告統稱為 Growing Up in New Zealand。"},{"en":"Collectively known as means called by one shared name as a group.","zh":"collectively known as 指一組事物共同以同一名稱稱呼。"},{"en":"Several small islands may be collectively known as one island chain.","zh":"幾個小島可能統稱為一個群島。"},{"en":"If reports are collectively known by one title, readers can recognise them as part of the same project.","zh":"如果幾份報告以同一標題統稱，讀者就能認出它們屬於同一項目。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a shared name for several items.","zh":"這個片語為幾個項目給出共同名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be published","meaning":"被出版","examples":[{"en":"Four reports had been published by 2014.","zh":"到2014年，已有四份報告被出版。"},{"en":"To be published means to be made available to the public in print or online.","zh":"be published 指以印刷或網上形式向公眾發布。"},{"en":"A student’s poem may be published in the school magazine.","zh":"學生的詩可能被刊登在校刊上。"},{"en":"If research is published, other people can read, question, and use it.","zh":"如果研究被出版，其他人就能閱讀、質疑和使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information being officially released.","zh":"這個片語描述資訊被正式發布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"show something to be","meaning":"顯示……是","examples":[{"en":"The reports show New Zealand to be a complex and changing country.","zh":"這些報告顯示新西蘭是一個複雜而不斷轉變的國家。"},{"en":"To show something to be a certain way means to provide evidence that it has that quality.","zh":"show something to be a certain way 指提供證據顯示某物具有某種特質。"},{"en":"Exam results may show a student to be stronger in reading than writing.","zh":"考試結果可能顯示學生閱讀比寫作更強。"},{"en":"If data shows a country to be changing, policy must respond to new realities.","zh":"如果數據顯示一個國家正在轉變，政策就必須回應新現實。"},{"en":"This phrase links evidence with a conclusion about what something is like.","zh":"這個片語把證據與對某事本質的結論連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"complex, changing country","meaning":"複雜而不斷轉變的國家","examples":[{"en":"The reports portray New Zealand as a complex, changing country.","zh":"這些報告把新西蘭描繪成一個複雜而不斷轉變的國家。"},{"en":"A complex, changing country is a nation with many different groups, needs, and social changes.","zh":"complex, changing country 是有許多不同群體、需要和社會變化的國家。"},{"en":"A complex, changing country may have families from many cultures and languages.","zh":"複雜而不斷轉變的國家可能有來自許多文化和語言的家庭。"},{"en":"If a country changes quickly, old policies may no longer fit its population.","zh":"如果一個國家快速轉變，舊政策可能不再適合其人口。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a society that cannot be understood in a simple way.","zh":"這個片語描述不能用簡單方式理解的社會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"participants and their families","meaning":"參加者及其家人","examples":[{"en":"The participants and their families differ from earlier generations.","zh":"參加者及其家人與前幾代人不同。"},{"en":"Participants and their families means the people taking part in the study and the relatives they live with or depend on.","zh":"participants and their families 指參與研究的人，以及與他們同住或被他們依靠的親人。"},{"en":"A school study may collect information from students and their families to understand home support.","zh":"學校研究可能從學生及其家人收集資料，以了解家庭支援。"},{"en":"If families change across generations, children’s experiences may also change.","zh":"如果家庭跨代改變，兒童經歷也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase includes both the study subjects and their family background.","zh":"這個片語包括研究對象及其家庭背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be markedly different from","meaning":"與……有明顯分別","examples":[{"en":"Today’s families are markedly different from those in previous studies.","zh":"今日的家庭與以往研究中的家庭有明顯分別。"},{"en":"To be markedly different from something means to be clearly and noticeably different.","zh":"be markedly different from something 指與某事物清楚而明顯地不同。"},{"en":"Online learning is markedly different from traditional classroom learning.","zh":"網上學習與傳統課室學習有明顯分別。"},{"en":"If families are markedly different from earlier generations, old assumptions may be unreliable.","zh":"如果家庭與前幾代人有明顯分別，舊假設可能不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a strong and visible difference.","zh":"這個片語強調強烈而可見的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"previous generations","meaning":"前幾代人","examples":[{"en":"The participants differ considerably from previous generations.","zh":"參加者與前幾代人有相當大差異。"},{"en":"Previous generations are people who lived or grew up earlier than the current group.","zh":"previous generations 是比當前群體更早生活或成長的人。"},{"en":"Previous generations often used letters and landline phones before smartphones became common.","zh":"在智能手機普及前，前幾代人常使用書信和固定電話。"},{"en":"If children today differ from previous generations, schools may need new approaches.","zh":"如果今日兒童與前幾代人不同，學校可能需要新方法。"},{"en":"This phrase compares today’s people with those before them.","zh":"這個片語把今日的人與之前的人作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the majority were identified as","meaning":"大多數被界定為","examples":[{"en":"The majority of the babies were identified as European New Zealanders.","zh":"大多數嬰兒被界定為歐裔新西蘭人。"},{"en":"The majority were identified as means most of the group were classified or described in that way.","zh":"the majority were identified as 指該群體大多數被分類或描述為某一類。"},{"en":"In a school survey, the majority of students may be identified as living nearby.","zh":"在學校調查中，大多數學生可能被界定為住在附近。"},{"en":"If most participants are identified as one group, researchers still need to examine minority groups carefully.","zh":"如果大多數參加者被界定為某一群體，研究人員仍需要仔細研究少數群體。"},{"en":"This phrase reports how a group is categorised.","zh":"這個片語報告某群體如何被分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"European New Zealanders","meaning":"歐裔新西蘭人","examples":[{"en":"European New Zealanders formed the largest ethnic group in the cohort.","zh":"歐裔新西蘭人構成該研究群組中最大的族裔群體。"},{"en":"European New Zealanders are New Zealanders whose ethnic background is mainly European.","zh":"European New Zealanders 是族裔背景主要為歐洲的新西蘭人。"},{"en":"A census may record European New Zealanders alongside Maori, Pacific, Asian, and other groups.","zh":"人口普查可能把歐裔新西蘭人與毛利人、太平洋島裔、亞裔和其他群體並列記錄。"},{"en":"If European New Zealanders form the largest group, their experiences may strongly affect overall results.","zh":"如果歐裔新西蘭人構成最大群體，他們的經歷可能強烈影響整體結果。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an ethnic category in New Zealand.","zh":"這個片語指新西蘭的一個族裔分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"one quarter","meaning":"四分之一","examples":[{"en":"Approximately one quarter of the babies were Maori.","zh":"約四分之一的嬰兒是毛利人。"},{"en":"One quarter means one out of four equal parts, or 25 percent.","zh":"one quarter 指四個相等部分中的一部分，即百分之二十五。"},{"en":"If a class has 40 students, one quarter is 10 students.","zh":"如果一班有40名學生，四分之一就是10名學生。"},{"en":"If one quarter of a cohort belongs to one group, that group is large enough to study meaningfully.","zh":"如果一個研究群組有四分之一屬於某群體，該群體就大到值得仔細研究。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a simple fraction.","zh":"這個片語表示簡單分數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Maori","meaning":"毛利人","examples":[{"en":"Maori are the indigenous people of New Zealand.","zh":"毛利人是新西蘭的原住民。"},{"en":"Maori refers to New Zealand’s indigenous people and their culture, language, and communities.","zh":"Maori 指新西蘭原住民及其文化、語言和社群。"},{"en":"Schools in New Zealand may teach Maori language, songs, and history.","zh":"新西蘭學校可能教授毛利語、歌曲和歷史。"},{"en":"If a study includes Maori children, researchers should consider cultural identity and family background.","zh":"如果研究包括毛利兒童，研究人員應考慮文化身份和家庭背景。"},{"en":"This word names an important indigenous group in New Zealand.","zh":"這個詞指出新西蘭一個重要原住民群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"indigenous New Zealanders","meaning":"新西蘭原住民","examples":[{"en":"The Maori are indigenous New Zealanders.","zh":"毛利人是新西蘭原住民。"},{"en":"Indigenous New Zealanders are the original peoples of New Zealand before later settlement.","zh":"indigenous New Zealanders 是後來定居者到來前新西蘭的原有民族。"},{"en":"Indigenous New Zealanders have cultural traditions, languages, and histories connected to the land.","zh":"新西蘭原住民擁有與土地相連的文化傳統、語言和歷史。"},{"en":"If policy affects children, it should consider the rights and experiences of indigenous communities.","zh":"如果政策影響兒童，就應考慮原住民社群的權利和經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the first peoples of New Zealand.","zh":"這個片語指出新西蘭的最早民族。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Pacific peoples","meaning":"太平洋島裔人士","examples":[{"en":"Many participants were of Pacific ethnic backgrounds.","zh":"許多參加者有太平洋島裔族裔背景。"},{"en":"Pacific peoples are people with ethnic origins in Pacific Island communities.","zh":"Pacific peoples 是族裔源自太平洋島嶼社群的人。"},{"en":"Pacific peoples in New Zealand may have family links to Samoa, Tonga, Fiji, or other islands.","zh":"新西蘭的太平洋島裔人士可能與薩摩亞、湯加、斐濟或其他島嶼有家庭連繫。"},{"en":"If a study includes Pacific peoples, researchers should consider language, migration, and family networks.","zh":"如果研究包括太平洋島裔人士，研究人員應考慮語言、移民和家庭網絡。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to diverse Pacific Island communities.","zh":"這個片語指多元的太平洋島嶼社群。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"originate in","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"Pacific participants originated in islands across the Pacific.","zh":"太平洋島裔參加者源自太平洋各島嶼。"},{"en":"To originate in a place means to come from that place originally.","zh":"originate in a place 指最初來自某地方。"},{"en":"A family recipe may originate in a small village before spreading to cities.","zh":"一道家庭食譜可能源自小村莊，後來傳到城市。"},{"en":"If a community originates in several islands, its culture may include many languages and traditions.","zh":"如果一個社群源自幾個島嶼，其文化可能包括多種語言和傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where something or someone comes from.","zh":"這個片語描述某事或某人來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"one in six","meaning":"每六人中有一人","examples":[{"en":"Approximately one in six of the children were Asian.","zh":"約每六名兒童中有一名是亞裔。"},{"en":"One in six means one person or item out of every six.","zh":"one in six 指每六人或每六件事物中有一個。"},{"en":"If one in six students takes the bus, transport planning must consider them.","zh":"如果每六名學生中有一人乘巴士，交通規劃就必須考慮他們。"},{"en":"If one in six children belongs to a group, that group represents a significant minority.","zh":"如果每六名兒童中有一人屬於某群體，該群體就是重要少數。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a proportion in everyday language.","zh":"這個片語以日常語言表示比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have more than one ethnicity","meaning":"擁有多於一種族裔身分","examples":[{"en":"Almost half of the children had more than one ethnicity.","zh":"幾乎一半兒童擁有多於一種族裔身分。"},{"en":"To have more than one ethnicity means to identify with or come from more than one ethnic background.","zh":"have more than one ethnicity 指認同或來自多於一種族裔背景。"},{"en":"A child may have more than one ethnicity if their parents come from different cultural groups.","zh":"如果孩子父母來自不同文化群體，孩子可能擁有多於一種族裔身分。"},{"en":"If many children have mixed ethnic backgrounds, simple categories may not describe them well.","zh":"如果許多孩子有混合族裔背景，簡單分類可能不能很好描述他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes multiple ethnic identities.","zh":"這個片語描述多重族裔身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"descriptive report","meaning":"描述性報告","examples":[{"en":"The first three publications are descriptive reports.","zh":"首三份出版物是描述性報告。"},{"en":"A descriptive report mainly presents what was found, observed, or recorded.","zh":"descriptive report 主要呈現被發現、觀察或記錄到的內容。"},{"en":"A school may write a descriptive report showing students’ attendance, results, and home languages.","zh":"學校可能撰寫描述性報告，展示學生出席率、成績和家庭語言。"},{"en":"If a report is descriptive, it may not yet explain deep causes.","zh":"如果報告是描述性的，它可能尚未解釋深層原因。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a report that focuses on describing facts and patterns.","zh":"這個片語描述聚焦於描述事實和模式的報告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"portray the cohort","meaning":"描繪研究群組","examples":[{"en":"The reports portray the cohort at several stages of development.","zh":"這些報告描繪研究群組在幾個發展階段的情況。"},{"en":"To portray the cohort means to describe or present the study group in detail.","zh":"portray the cohort 指詳細描述或呈現研究群組。"},{"en":"A teacher may portray a class by describing students’ strengths, needs, and learning habits.","zh":"老師可能透過描述學生的強項、需要和學習習慣來描繪一班學生。"},{"en":"If reports portray a cohort over time, readers can see how the group changes.","zh":"如果報告隨時間描繪研究群組，讀者可以看到該群體如何改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes presenting a detailed picture of a research group.","zh":"這個片語描述呈現研究群組的詳細圖像。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cohort","meaning":"研究群組","examples":[{"en":"The cohort consists of thousands of children born during the same period.","zh":"這個研究群組由同一時期出生的數千名兒童組成。"},{"en":"A cohort is a group of people who share a common feature, such as birth period or study membership.","zh":"cohort 是共享某共同特徵的一群人，例如出生時期或研究成員身份。"},{"en":"A university may study a cohort of students who entered in the same year.","zh":"大學可能研究同一年入學的一個學生群組。"},{"en":"If a cohort is followed over time, researchers can compare development within the same group.","zh":"如果一個研究群組被長期追蹤，研究人員可以比較同一群體內的發展。"},{"en":"This word is common in long-term studies.","zh":"這個詞常見於長期研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"before birth","meaning":"出生前","examples":[{"en":"The first report describes the children and families before birth.","zh":"第一份報告描述出生前的兒童和家庭。"},{"en":"Before birth means during pregnancy, before a baby is born.","zh":"before birth 指嬰兒出生之前，即懷孕期間。"},{"en":"Doctors may give parents advice before birth about nutrition, sleep, and feeding plans.","zh":"醫生可能在出生前給父母關於營養、睡眠和餵哺計劃的建議。"},{"en":"If family circumstances are recorded before birth, researchers can compare them with later child outcomes.","zh":"如果家庭情況在出生前已被記錄，研究人員可以把它們與日後兒童結果比較。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the prenatal period.","zh":"這個片語指產前時期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at nine months","meaning":"在九個月大時","examples":[{"en":"The second report follows the babies at nine months of age.","zh":"第二份報告追蹤九個月大的嬰兒。"},{"en":"At nine months means when the babies are nine months old.","zh":"at nine months 指嬰兒九個月大時。"},{"en":"At nine months, many babies can sit, crawl, or respond to familiar voices.","zh":"在九個月大時，許多嬰兒可以坐、爬或回應熟悉聲音。"},{"en":"If researchers study babies at nine months, they can record early health and family routines.","zh":"如果研究人員研究九個月大的嬰兒，就能記錄早期健康和家庭習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a specific age in infancy.","zh":"這個片語給出嬰兒期中的特定年齡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"at two years of age","meaning":"在兩歲時","examples":[{"en":"The third report examines the children at two years of age.","zh":"第三份報告檢視兩歲兒童。"},{"en":"At two years of age means when the children are two years old.","zh":"at two years of age 指孩子兩歲時。"},{"en":"At two years of age, many children begin to use more words and show independence.","zh":"在兩歲時，許多孩子開始使用更多詞語並表達獨立性。"},{"en":"If children are assessed at age two, researchers can observe early language and behaviour.","zh":"如果孩子在兩歲時接受評估，研究人員可以觀察早期語言和行為。"},{"en":"This phrase marks an early childhood milestone.","zh":"這個片語標示幼兒期的一個里程碑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"make history","meaning":"創下歷史；具有歷史意義","examples":[{"en":"The first report made history by interviewing both mothers and fathers.","zh":"第一份報告透過訪問母親和父親而創下歷史。"},{"en":"To make history means to do something important or new enough to be remembered.","zh":"make history 指做出重要或嶄新到值得被記住的事情。"},{"en":"A school may make history if its students win the city’s first robotics championship.","zh":"如果學生贏得全市首個機械人比賽冠軍，學校可能創下歷史。"},{"en":"If a report includes both parents for the first time, it may change how future studies are designed.","zh":"如果報告首次包括父母雙方，它可能改變未來研究的設計方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an achievement with special significance.","zh":"這個片語描述具有特殊意義的成就。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"contain interviews with","meaning":"載有與……的訪問","examples":[{"en":"The report contains interviews with the children’s mothers and fathers.","zh":"該報告載有與兒童母親和父親的訪問。"},{"en":"To contain interviews with people means to include recorded questions and answers from those people.","zh":"contain interviews with people 指包括與那些人的問答記錄。"},{"en":"A documentary may contain interviews with teachers, parents, and students.","zh":"紀錄片可能載有與老師、家長和學生的訪問。"},{"en":"If a report contains interviews with both parents, it gives a wider family perspective.","zh":"如果報告載有與父母雙方的訪問，它就提供更廣闊的家庭角度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one type of information included in a report.","zh":"這個片語描述報告中包含的一種資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"analytical report","meaning":"分析性報告","examples":[{"en":"The fourth publication is a more analytical report.","zh":"第四份出版物是一份較具分析性的報告。"},{"en":"An analytical report examines information in order to explain patterns, causes, or relationships.","zh":"analytical report 會檢視資料，以解釋模式、原因或關係。"},{"en":"A school may write an analytical report to explain why attendance fell.","zh":"學校可能撰寫分析性報告，解釋出席率為何下降。"},{"en":"If a report is analytical, it goes beyond describing facts and tries to interpret them.","zh":"如果報告是分析性的，它不只是描述事實，還嘗試詮釋事實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a report focused on explanation and analysis.","zh":"這個片語描述聚焦於解釋和分析的報告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"explore the definition of","meaning":"探討……的定義","examples":[{"en":"The fourth report explores the definition of childhood vulnerability.","zh":"第四份報告探討兒童脆弱處境的定義。"},{"en":"To explore the definition of something means to examine what it really means and how it should be understood.","zh":"explore the definition of something 指檢視某事真正意思和應如何理解。"},{"en":"A teacher may explore the definition of success before students write an essay about it.","zh":"老師可能在學生寫成功主題文章前，先探討成功的定義。"},{"en":"If a concept is hard to measure, researchers must first define it clearly.","zh":"如果某概念難以量度，研究人員必須先清楚定義它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful examination of meaning.","zh":"這個片語描述對意思的仔細檢視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"vulnerability","meaning":"脆弱處境；易受傷害狀況","examples":[{"en":"The study examines factors associated with vulnerability in children.","zh":"這項研究檢視與兒童脆弱處境有關的因素。"},{"en":"Vulnerability means being more likely to be harmed, disadvantaged, or placed at risk.","zh":"vulnerability 指較容易受到傷害、處於不利位置或面對風險。"},{"en":"A child in unsafe housing may experience vulnerability because daily life is unstable.","zh":"住在不安全住所中的孩子可能經歷脆弱處境，因為日常生活不穩定。"},{"en":"If several risks build up, vulnerability can affect health, learning, and behaviour.","zh":"如果幾種風險累積，脆弱處境可以影響健康、學習和行為。"},{"en":"This word describes a fragile or at-risk condition.","zh":"這個詞描述脆弱或有風險的狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"prospective parents","meaning":"準父母","examples":[{"en":"The first report describes the expectations of prospective parents.","zh":"第一份報告描述準父母的期望。"},{"en":"Prospective parents are people who are expecting or planning to become parents.","zh":"prospective parents 是正在期待或計劃成為父母的人。"},{"en":"Prospective parents may attend classes about childbirth and infant care.","zh":"準父母可能參加關於分娩和嬰兒照顧的課程。"},{"en":"If prospective parents lack support, pregnancy and early childcare may become more stressful.","zh":"如果準父母缺乏支援，懷孕和早期育兒可能變得更有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to future or soon-to-be parents.","zh":"這個片語指未來或即將成為父母的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"hopes, dreams, and realities","meaning":"希望、夢想與現實","examples":[{"en":"The report examines parents’ hopes, dreams, and realities.","zh":"該報告檢視父母的希望、夢想與現實。"},{"en":"Hopes, dreams, and realities means people’s wishes, ideals, and actual life conditions.","zh":"hopes, dreams, and realities 指人們的願望、理想和實際生活情況。"},{"en":"A student’s hopes, dreams, and realities may differ when choosing a university.","zh":"學生選大學時，其希望、夢想與現實可能不同。"},{"en":"If parents’ dreams are high but income is low, family life may involve difficult choices.","zh":"如果父母夢想很高但收入低，家庭生活可能涉及艱難選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts aspiration with real circumstances.","zh":"這個片語把抱負與真實環境作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"average age of parents","meaning":"父母的平均年齡","examples":[{"en":"The average age of parents having a child was around 30.","zh":"生育孩子的父母平均年齡約為30歲。"},{"en":"The average age of parents means the typical age calculated across a group of mothers and fathers.","zh":"average age of parents 指在一組母親和父親中計算出的典型年齡。"},{"en":"A survey may compare the average age of parents in cities and rural areas.","zh":"調查可能比較城市和鄉郊地區父母的平均年齡。"},{"en":"If the average age rises, families may have different income, work, and housing situations.","zh":"如果平均年齡上升，家庭可能有不同收入、工作和住屋情況。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a general age pattern in a group.","zh":"這個片語給出群體中的一般年齡模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"legally binding relationship","meaning":"具法律約束力的關係","examples":[{"en":"Around two-thirds of the parents were in legally binding relationships.","zh":"約三分之二父母處於具法律約束力的關係中。"},{"en":"A legally binding relationship is a relationship recognised by law, such as marriage or a formal civil partnership.","zh":"legally binding relationship 是受法律承認的關係，例如婚姻或正式民事伴侶關係。"},{"en":"A legally binding agreement gives people rights and duties they cannot simply ignore.","zh":"具法律約束力的協議給予人們不能隨便忽視的權利和責任。"},{"en":"If parents are in a legally binding relationship, family responsibilities may be formally recognised.","zh":"如果父母處於具法律約束力的關係中，家庭責任可能被正式承認。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on legal status, not only emotional closeness.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於法律地位，而不只是情感親密。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"one-third of the children","meaning":"三分之一的兒童","examples":[{"en":"One-third of the children had at least one parent born overseas.","zh":"三分之一的兒童至少有一名父母在海外出生。"},{"en":"One-third of the children means one out of every three children in the group.","zh":"one-third of the children 指該群體中每三名兒童有一名。"},{"en":"If one-third of the children speak another language at home, schools may need language support.","zh":"如果三分之一的兒童在家說另一種語言，學校可能需要語言支援。"},{"en":"When one-third of a group shares a feature, that feature is important for planning.","zh":"當一個群體有三分之一共享某特徵，該特徵對規劃很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a proportion of children.","zh":"這個片語表示兒童中的一個比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"grow up in","meaning":"在……長大","examples":[{"en":"Some of the parents did not grow up in New Zealand.","zh":"一些父母並非在新西蘭長大。"},{"en":"To grow up in a place means to spend childhood there.","zh":"grow up in a place 指在某地度過童年。"},{"en":"A child who grows up in a coastal town may learn to swim early.","zh":"在海邊小鎮長大的孩子可能很早學會游泳。"},{"en":"If parents grow up in another country, they may bring different languages and customs into family life.","zh":"如果父母在另一個國家長大，他們可能把不同語言和習俗帶入家庭生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the place where childhood happens.","zh":"這個片語描述童年發生的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a significant difference from","meaning":"與……有重大分別","examples":[{"en":"This represented a significant difference from earlier studies.","zh":"這與早期研究相比有重大分別。"},{"en":"A significant difference from something means a meaningful and noticeable difference compared with it.","zh":"significant difference from something 指與某事相比有具意義且明顯的差異。"},{"en":"A school’s new exam results may show a significant difference from last year’s results.","zh":"學校新考試成績可能與去年成績有重大分別。"},{"en":"If current families differ significantly from earlier studies, old findings may need updating.","zh":"如果現今家庭與早期研究有重大分別，舊研究發現可能需要更新。"},{"en":"This phrase marks an important comparison.","zh":"這個片語標示重要比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a vast majority of","meaning":"絕大多數","examples":[{"en":"In earlier studies, a vast majority of parents were native-born New Zealanders.","zh":"在早期研究中，絕大多數父母都是新西蘭本地出生人士。"},{"en":"A vast majority of means almost all, or a very large proportion of a group.","zh":"a vast majority of 指幾乎全部，或一個群體中非常大的比例。"},{"en":"A vast majority of students may prefer shorter quizzes to one long final test.","zh":"絕大多數學生可能較喜歡短測，而不是一次長期末試。"},{"en":"If a vast majority share one background, minority experiences may be less visible.","zh":"如果絕大多數人共享同一背景，少數群體經驗可能較不顯眼。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a very large majority.","zh":"這個片語強調非常大的多數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"born and bred","meaning":"土生土長的","examples":[{"en":"Most parents in previous studies were New Zealanders born and bred.","zh":"以往研究中的大多數父母都是土生土長的新西蘭人。"},{"en":"Born and bred means born and raised in a particular place.","zh":"born and bred 指在某地出生並長大。"},{"en":"A teacher born and bred in a small town may know many local families.","zh":"土生土長於小鎮的老師可能認識許多本地家庭。"},{"en":"If many parents are born and bred locally, their childhood experiences may be more similar.","zh":"如果許多父母都是本地土生土長，他們的童年經歷可能較相似。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises both birthplace and upbringing.","zh":"這個片語同時強調出生地和成長背景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"planned birth","meaning":"計劃中的生育","examples":[{"en":"Around 60% of the births in the cohort were planned.","zh":"該研究群組中約60%的出生是計劃中的生育。"},{"en":"A planned birth means the pregnancy or child’s arrival was intended by the parents.","zh":"planned birth 指懷孕或孩子到來是父母有意計劃的。"},{"en":"Some couples plan a birth after they have stable work and housing.","zh":"一些伴侶可能在工作和住屋穩定後計劃生育。"},{"en":"If a birth is planned, parents may prepare finances, childcare, and leave more easily.","zh":"如果生育是計劃中的，父母可能較容易準備財務、託兒和假期。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts intended births with unplanned ones.","zh":"這個片語把有意計劃的生育與意外懷孕作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hope to have","meaning":"希望擁有","examples":[{"en":"Most families hoped to have two or three children.","zh":"大多數家庭希望擁有兩至三名孩子。"},{"en":"To hope to have something means to wish or plan to have it in the future.","zh":"hope to have something 指希望或計劃日後擁有某物。"},{"en":"A young couple may hope to have a larger home before their second child is born.","zh":"年輕夫婦可能希望在第二個孩子出生前擁有較大的住所。"},{"en":"If families hope to have more children, income and childcare become important considerations.","zh":"如果家庭希望擁有更多孩子，收入和託兒就成為重要考慮。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a desired future family plan.","zh":"這個片語表達期望中的未來家庭計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"during pregnancy","meaning":"懷孕期間","examples":[{"en":"Some women changed their behaviour during pregnancy.","zh":"一些女性在懷孕期間改變自己的行為。"},{"en":"During pregnancy means in the period when a woman is carrying a baby before birth.","zh":"during pregnancy 指女性在分娩前懷有胎兒的期間。"},{"en":"During pregnancy, doctors may advise women about diet, exercise, and medical check-ups.","zh":"懷孕期間，醫生可能就飲食、運動和身體檢查給予建議。"},{"en":"If habits change during pregnancy, the baby’s early health may be affected.","zh":"如果習慣在懷孕期間改變，嬰兒早期健康可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the time before childbirth.","zh":"這個片語指分娩前的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"with regard to","meaning":"關於；在……方面","examples":[{"en":"The study collected information with regard to smoking, alcohol, and exercise.","zh":"這項研究收集關於吸煙、飲酒和運動方面的資料。"},{"en":"With regard to means about or concerning a particular subject.","zh":"with regard to 指關於某個特定主題。"},{"en":"A school may ask parents questions with regard to transport and meal arrangements.","zh":"學校可能向家長詢問關於交通和膳食安排的問題。"},{"en":"If researchers collect data with regard to health habits, they can examine possible risks.","zh":"如果研究人員收集關於健康習慣的數據，就能檢視可能風險。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the topic being discussed or measured.","zh":"這個片語引入正在討論或量度的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"change one’s behaviour","meaning":"改變自己的行為","examples":[{"en":"Some mothers changed their behaviour after becoming pregnant.","zh":"一些母親懷孕後改變自己的行為。"},{"en":"To change one’s behaviour means to act differently from before.","zh":"change one’s behaviour 指行動方式與以前不同。"},{"en":"A student may change their behaviour by sleeping earlier before exams.","zh":"學生可能在考試前早睡，以改變自己的行為。"},{"en":"If mothers reduce smoking or alcohol during pregnancy, they may protect the baby’s health.","zh":"如果母親在懷孕期間減少吸煙或飲酒，可能保護嬰兒健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift in habits or actions.","zh":"這個片語描述習慣或行動的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"public health campaign","meaning":"公共衞生宣傳活動","examples":[{"en":"The findings may be useful for future public health campaigns.","zh":"這些研究發現可能對未來公共衞生宣傳活動有用。"},{"en":"A public health campaign is an organised effort to improve people’s health through messages, services, or advice.","zh":"public health campaign 是透過訊息、服務或建議改善人民健康的有組織行動。"},{"en":"A campaign may encourage parents to breastfeed, vaccinate babies, or stop smoking.","zh":"宣傳活動可能鼓勵父母母乳餵哺、為嬰兒接種疫苗或戒煙。"},{"en":"If a campaign uses clear evidence, it may reach the families most in need.","zh":"如果宣傳活動使用清楚證據，它可能接觸到最有需要的家庭。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to health promotion for the public.","zh":"這個片語指面向公眾的健康推廣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"caesarean section","meaning":"剖腹生產","examples":[{"en":"Nearly a quarter of the babies were delivered by caesarean section.","zh":"接近四分之一嬰兒透過剖腹生產出生。"},{"en":"A caesarean section is an operation in which a baby is delivered through a cut in the mother’s abdomen and uterus.","zh":"caesarean section 是透過切開母親腹部和子宮取出嬰兒的手術。"},{"en":"Doctors may perform a caesarean section if natural birth would be risky.","zh":"如果自然分娩有風險，醫生可能進行剖腹生產。"},{"en":"If the caesarean rate is high, health researchers may examine medical and social reasons.","zh":"如果剖腹生產率很高，健康研究人員可能檢視醫療和社會原因。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a surgical method of childbirth.","zh":"這個片語指一種外科分娩方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be delivered by","meaning":"透過……出生","examples":[{"en":"Some babies were delivered by caesarean section.","zh":"一些嬰兒透過剖腹生產出生。"},{"en":"To be delivered by a method means to be born through that method.","zh":"be delivered by a method 指透過某種方法出生。"},{"en":"Some babies are delivered by natural birth, while others are delivered by surgery.","zh":"一些嬰兒自然分娩出生，另一些則透過手術出生。"},{"en":"If a baby is delivered by caesarean section, the mother usually needs time to recover from surgery.","zh":"如果嬰兒透過剖腹生產出生，母親通常需要時間從手術中恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the method of childbirth.","zh":"這個片語描述分娩方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"World Health Organisation","meaning":"世界衞生組織","examples":[{"en":"The World Health Organisation recommends exclusive breastfeeding for six months.","zh":"世界衞生組織建議全母乳餵哺六個月。"},{"en":"The World Health Organisation is an international body that gives health guidance to countries.","zh":"World Health Organisation 是向各國提供健康指引的國際機構。"},{"en":"Governments may refer to World Health Organisation advice during disease outbreaks.","zh":"疾病爆發期間，政府可能參考世界衞生組織建議。"},{"en":"If the organisation recommends a practice, health authorities may include it in public guidelines.","zh":"如果該組織建議某做法，衞生當局可能把它納入公共指引。"},{"en":"This phrase names a global health authority.","zh":"這個片語指出全球健康權威機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"recommend that","meaning":"建議","examples":[{"en":"Health guidelines recommend that babies be breastfed exclusively.","zh":"健康指引建議嬰兒應全母乳餵哺。"},{"en":"Recommend that means advise or suggest that something should be done.","zh":"recommend that 指建議某事應該被做。"},{"en":"Teachers may recommend that students read the question twice before answering.","zh":"老師可能建議學生回答前先讀兩次題目。"},{"en":"If experts recommend that families follow a habit, they usually base it on evidence.","zh":"如果專家建議家庭跟從某習慣，通常是以證據為基礎。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces advice or guidance.","zh":"這個片語引入建議或指引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"breastfeed exclusively","meaning":"全母乳餵哺","examples":[{"en":"Health authorities recommend that mothers breastfeed exclusively for six months.","zh":"衞生當局建議母親全母乳餵哺六個月。"},{"en":"To breastfeed exclusively means to feed a baby only breast milk, without other food or drink.","zh":"breastfeed exclusively 指只用母乳餵哺嬰兒，不給其他食物或飲品。"},{"en":"A mother may need workplace and family support to breastfeed exclusively after returning home.","zh":"母親回家後可能需要工作場所和家庭支援，才能全母乳餵哺。"},{"en":"If exclusive breastfeeding is difficult, parents may seek advice from nurses or doctors.","zh":"如果全母乳餵哺有困難，父母可能向護士或醫生尋求建議。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific infant feeding practice.","zh":"這個片語描述一種特定嬰兒餵哺方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"median duration","meaning":"中位持續時間","examples":[{"en":"The median duration of exclusive breastfeeding was four months.","zh":"全母乳餵哺的中位持續時間為四個月。"},{"en":"Median duration means the middle length of time when all cases are arranged from shortest to longest.","zh":"median duration 指把所有個案由最短至最長排列後，中間那個持續時間。"},{"en":"If the median duration of a hospital stay is three days, half of patients stayed less and half stayed more.","zh":"如果住院中位持續時間是三天，即一半病人住得較短，一半住得較長。"},{"en":"Median duration can describe a typical pattern without being distorted by extreme cases.","zh":"中位持續時間可以描述典型模式，而不太受極端個案扭曲。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for statistical time measurement.","zh":"這個片語用於統計上的時間量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"exclusive breastfeeding","meaning":"全母乳餵哺","examples":[{"en":"Exclusive breastfeeding means that the baby receives no other food or drink.","zh":"全母乳餵哺指嬰兒不接受其他食物或飲品。"},{"en":"Exclusive breastfeeding is feeding a baby only breast milk for a period of time.","zh":"exclusive breastfeeding 是在一段時間內只用母乳餵哺嬰兒。"},{"en":"Nurses may teach new mothers how to manage exclusive breastfeeding safely.","zh":"護士可能教新手母親如何安全處理全母乳餵哺。"},{"en":"If exclusive breastfeeding lasts longer, researchers may examine health outcomes for babies and mothers.","zh":"如果全母乳餵哺持續較久，研究人員可能檢視嬰兒和母親的健康結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes breast-milk-only feeding.","zh":"這個片語描述只餵母乳的餵哺方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"return to full-time work","meaning":"重返全職工作","examples":[{"en":"Almost one-third of the mothers had returned to full-time work.","zh":"接近三分之一母親已重返全職工作。"},{"en":"To return to full-time work means to go back to working normal full working hours after a break.","zh":"return to full-time work 指休息或休假後回到正常全職工時。"},{"en":"A parent may return to full-time work after maternity leave ends.","zh":"家長可能在產假結束後重返全職工作。"},{"en":"If a mother returns to full-time work, childcare arrangements may become necessary.","zh":"如果母親重返全職工作，託兒安排可能變得必要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes going back to a full work schedule.","zh":"這個片語描述回到全職工作時間表。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"solid food","meaning":"固體食物","examples":[{"en":"By nine months, all the babies were eating solid food.","zh":"到九個月大時，所有嬰兒都在吃固體食物。"},{"en":"Solid food is food that is not liquid, such as soft fruit, rice, vegetables, or mashed meat.","zh":"solid food 是非液體食物，例如軟水果、米飯、蔬菜或肉泥。"},{"en":"Parents often introduce solid food gradually while babies still drink milk.","zh":"父母常在嬰兒仍喝奶時逐步引入固體食物。"},{"en":"If a baby starts solid food too early or too late, parents may need medical advice.","zh":"如果嬰兒太早或太遲開始吃固體食物，父母可能需要醫療建議。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the stage when babies begin eating food with texture.","zh":"這個片語指嬰兒開始吃有質感食物的階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"live in accommodation","meaning":"居住在住所中","examples":[{"en":"More than half of the babies lived in accommodation owned by their families.","zh":"超過一半嬰兒居住在由家人擁有的住所中。"},{"en":"To live in accommodation means to live in a house, flat, room, or other place of residence.","zh":"live in accommodation 指居住在房屋、單位、房間或其他居所中。"},{"en":"Students may live in accommodation near school if they come from another city.","zh":"如果學生來自另一個城市，可能居住在學校附近的住所中。"},{"en":"If families own their accommodation, they may have more housing stability.","zh":"如果家庭擁有自己的住所，可能有較高住屋穩定性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where people live.","zh":"這個片語描述人們住在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"experience a drop in income","meaning":"經歷收入下降","examples":[{"en":"Almost all the parents experienced a drop in income.","zh":"幾乎所有父母都經歷收入下降。"},{"en":"To experience a drop in income means to receive less money than before.","zh":"experience a drop in income 指收入比以前減少。"},{"en":"A family may experience a drop in income if one parent stops working to care for a baby.","zh":"如果父母其中一方停止工作照顧嬰兒，家庭可能經歷收入下降。"},{"en":"If income falls sharply, families may cut spending on transport, food, or childcare.","zh":"如果收入大幅下降，家庭可能削減交通、食物或託兒開支。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a financial decrease.","zh":"這個片語描述財政上的減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a steep drop","meaning":"大幅下降","examples":[{"en":"Some families experienced a steep drop in income.","zh":"一些家庭經歷收入大幅下降。"},{"en":"A steep drop is a large and sudden decrease.","zh":"steep drop 是巨大而突然的下降。"},{"en":"A shop may see a steep drop in sales after a nearby road closes.","zh":"附近道路關閉後，店舖銷售可能大幅下降。"},{"en":"If a family has a steep drop in income, paying rent and bills may become difficult.","zh":"如果家庭收入大幅下降，支付租金和帳單可能變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the fall is serious, not small.","zh":"這個片語強調下降嚴重，而不是輕微。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"mostly due to","meaning":"主要由於","examples":[{"en":"The income reduction was mostly due to mothers not working.","zh":"收入減少主要由於母親沒有工作。"},{"en":"Mostly due to means mainly caused by something.","zh":"mostly due to 指主要由某事造成。"},{"en":"The delay was mostly due to heavy traffic, not poor planning.","zh":"延誤主要由於交通擠塞，而不是計劃差。"},{"en":"If a family’s income falls mostly due to one parent leaving work, childcare support may help.","zh":"如果家庭收入下降主要由於一名家長離開工作，託兒支援可能有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main cause.","zh":"這個片語指出主要原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be immunised","meaning":"接受免疫接種","examples":[{"en":"More than 90% of the babies were immunised.","zh":"超過90%的嬰兒接受免疫接種。"},{"en":"To be immunised means to receive vaccines that help protect against disease.","zh":"be immunised 指接種疫苗以幫助預防疾病。"},{"en":"Children may be immunised before starting kindergarten.","zh":"兒童可能在入讀幼稚園前接受免疫接種。"},{"en":"If many babies are immunised, serious disease can spread less easily.","zh":"如果許多嬰兒接受免疫接種，嚴重疾病就較不容易傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase describes receiving medical protection through vaccination.","zh":"這個片語描述透過疫苗接種獲得醫療保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be in very good health","meaning":"健康狀況非常好","examples":[{"en":"Almost all the babies were in very good health.","zh":"幾乎所有嬰兒健康狀況非常好。"},{"en":"To be in very good health means to be physically well, with few or no serious health problems.","zh":"be in very good health 指身體狀況良好，幾乎沒有或沒有嚴重健康問題。"},{"en":"A child in very good health can usually eat, sleep, play, and grow normally.","zh":"健康狀況非常好的孩子通常能正常吃、睡、玩和成長。"},{"en":"If most babies are in very good health, the cohort begins from a strong health position.","zh":"如果大多數嬰兒健康狀況非常好，該研究群組就從良好健康基礎開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a positive health condition.","zh":"這個片語描述正面的健康狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"post-natal depression","meaning":"產後抑鬱","examples":[{"en":"Eleven per cent of the mothers experienced post-natal depression.","zh":"百分之十一的母親經歷產後抑鬱。"},{"en":"Post-natal depression is depression that can affect a mother after giving birth.","zh":"post-natal depression 是母親分娩後可能出現的抑鬱。"},{"en":"A mother with post-natal depression may feel exhausted, hopeless, anxious, or unable to enjoy daily life.","zh":"有產後抑鬱的母親可能感到疲憊、絕望、焦慮或無法享受日常生活。"},{"en":"If post-natal depression is recognised early, families and doctors can provide support.","zh":"如果產後抑鬱及早被識別，家庭和醫生就能提供支援。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a mental health condition after childbirth.","zh":"這個片語指分娩後的精神健康狀況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"alarming statistic","meaning":"令人憂慮的統計數字","examples":[{"en":"The rate of post-natal depression may be considered an alarming statistic.","zh":"產後抑鬱率可能被視為令人憂慮的統計數字。"},{"en":"An alarming statistic is a number that causes worry because it suggests a serious problem.","zh":"alarming statistic 是令人擔心的數字，因為它暗示嚴重問題。"},{"en":"A high number of students skipping breakfast could be an alarming statistic for a school nurse.","zh":"大量學生不吃早餐，對校護來說可能是令人憂慮的統計數字。"},{"en":"If a statistic is alarming, it may lead to public campaigns or extra services.","zh":"如果統計數字令人憂慮，它可能引發公共宣傳或額外服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a worrying piece of numerical evidence.","zh":"這個片語描述令人擔心的數字證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"mental health campaign","meaning":"精神健康宣傳活動","examples":[{"en":"The findings may support future mental health campaigns.","zh":"這些研究發現可能支持未來精神健康宣傳活動。"},{"en":"A mental health campaign is an organised effort to raise awareness and improve support for emotional well-being.","zh":"mental health campaign 是提高認知並改善情緒福祉支援的有組織行動。"},{"en":"A school mental health campaign may teach students how to ask for help when they feel anxious.","zh":"學校精神健康宣傳活動可能教學生感到焦慮時如何求助。"},{"en":"If research identifies a common problem, campaigns can target the people most affected.","zh":"如果研究識別出常見問題，宣傳活動可以針對最受影響的人。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to public action about psychological well-being.","zh":"這個片語指關於心理福祉的公共行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be put in childcare","meaning":"被安排接受託兒服務","examples":[{"en":"Many babies were put in childcare while their mothers worked or studied.","zh":"許多嬰兒在母親工作或學習時被安排接受託兒服務。"},{"en":"To be put in childcare means to be placed under the care of another person or service while parents are unavailable.","zh":"be put in childcare 指父母無法照顧時，由其他人或服務照顧孩子。"},{"en":"A baby may be put in childcare when both parents work during the day.","zh":"如果父母雙方白天工作，嬰兒可能被安排接受託兒服務。"},{"en":"If children are put in childcare, the quality of the provider can affect daily routines and development.","zh":"如果兒童被安排接受託兒服務，服務提供者的質素可影響日常習慣和發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arranging care outside direct parental care.","zh":"這個片語描述安排父母直接照顧以外的照顧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"childcare provider","meaning":"託兒服務提供者","examples":[{"en":"The type of childcare provider varied according to ethnicity.","zh":"託兒服務提供者的類型因族裔而異。"},{"en":"A childcare provider is a person, family member, centre, or service that looks after children.","zh":"childcare provider 是照顧兒童的人、家庭成員、中心或服務。"},{"en":"Grandparents, daycare centres, and babysitters can all be childcare providers.","zh":"祖父母、日間託兒中心和保姆都可以是託兒服務提供者。"},{"en":"If childcare providers differ across groups, family culture and work patterns may partly explain it.","zh":"如果託兒服務提供者因群體而異，家庭文化和工作模式可能部分解釋這現象。"},{"en":"This phrase names whoever provides care for children.","zh":"這個片語指出提供兒童照顧的人或服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"vary by ethnicity","meaning":"因族裔而異","examples":[{"en":"Childcare arrangements varied by ethnicity.","zh":"託兒安排因族裔而異。"},{"en":"To vary by ethnicity means to differ among ethnic groups.","zh":"vary by ethnicity 指在不同族裔群體之間有所不同。"},{"en":"Food customs, languages, and family roles may vary by ethnicity in a multicultural school.","zh":"在多元文化學校中，飲食習俗、語言和家庭角色可能因族裔而異。"},{"en":"If childcare varies by ethnicity, services should not assume all families use the same arrangements.","zh":"如果託兒安排因族裔而異，服務不應假設所有家庭都使用相同安排。"},{"en":"This phrase describes differences linked to ethnic background.","zh":"這個片語描述與族裔背景相關的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be looked after by","meaning":"由……照顧","examples":[{"en":"Maori and Pacific children were more likely to be looked after by grandparents.","zh":"毛利和太平洋島裔兒童較可能由祖父母照顧。"},{"en":"To be looked after by someone means to be cared for or supervised by that person.","zh":"be looked after by someone 指由某人照顧或看管。"},{"en":"A child may be looked after by an aunt when parents work late.","zh":"父母工作至很晚時，孩子可能由姨姨照顧。"},{"en":"If children are looked after by grandparents, family bonds may become stronger.","zh":"如果孩子由祖父母照顧，家庭連繫可能變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes who provides care.","zh":"這個片語描述誰提供照顧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tend to be sent to","meaning":"往往被送往","examples":[{"en":"European New Zealand children tended to be sent to daycare.","zh":"歐裔新西蘭兒童往往被送往日間託兒服務。"},{"en":"To tend to be sent to a place means to be usually or commonly placed there.","zh":"tend to be sent to a place 指通常或常被安排到某地方。"},{"en":"Younger children may tend to be sent to smaller classes if they need extra attention.","zh":"如果年幼兒童需要更多關注，可能往往被送往較小班級。"},{"en":"If one group tends to use daycare more, researchers may examine work schedules and family support.","zh":"如果某群體較常使用日間託兒，研究人員可能檢視工作時間表和家庭支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common pattern rather than an absolute rule.","zh":"這個片語描述常見模式，而不是絕對規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"daycare","meaning":"日間託兒服務","examples":[{"en":"Many European New Zealand children attended daycare.","zh":"許多歐裔新西蘭兒童接受日間託兒服務。"},{"en":"Daycare is a service where young children are cared for during the day while parents work or study.","zh":"daycare 是父母工作或學習時，白天照顧幼兒的服務。"},{"en":"A daycare centre may provide meals, play, naps, and early learning activities.","zh":"日間託兒中心可能提供膳食、遊戲、午睡和早期學習活動。"},{"en":"If daycare is expensive or unavailable, parents may struggle to return to work.","zh":"如果日間託兒服務昂貴或不足，父母可能難以重返工作。"},{"en":"This word refers to daytime childcare outside the home.","zh":"這個詞指家外的日間兒童照顧服務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"provide more insights into","meaning":"讓人更深入了解","examples":[{"en":"The third report provides more insights into children’s development.","zh":"第三份報告讓人更深入了解兒童發展。"},{"en":"To provide more insights into something means to help people understand it more deeply.","zh":"provide more insights into something 指幫助人更深入理解某事。"},{"en":"Student interviews can provide more insights into why homework is not completed.","zh":"學生訪問可以讓人更深入了解為何功課未完成。"},{"en":"If reports include observations and parent interviews, they can reveal more than numbers alone.","zh":"如果報告包括觀察和家長訪問，它們能揭示比單靠數字更多的內容。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving deeper understanding.","zh":"這個片語描述提供更深理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"children’s development","meaning":"兒童發展","examples":[{"en":"The report examines several aspects of children’s development.","zh":"該報告檢視兒童發展的幾個方面。"},{"en":"Children’s development means how children grow physically, emotionally, socially, cognitively, and behaviourally.","zh":"children’s development 指兒童在身體、情緒、社交、認知和行為上的成長。"},{"en":"Teachers observe children’s development through speech, play, movement, and problem-solving.","zh":"老師透過說話、遊戲、動作和解難觀察兒童發展。"},{"en":"If development is delayed, early support can help children catch up.","zh":"如果發展延遲，早期支援可以幫助兒童追上。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the many ways children grow and change.","zh":"這個片語指兒童成長和轉變的多個方面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"physically and emotionally","meaning":"在身體及情緒方面","examples":[{"en":"The children were assessed physically and emotionally.","zh":"這些兒童在身體及情緒方面接受評估。"},{"en":"Physically and emotionally means in terms of the body and feelings.","zh":"physically and emotionally 指從身體和感受兩方面來看。"},{"en":"After a long exam season, students may feel tired physically and emotionally.","zh":"漫長考試季後，學生可能在身體及情緒方面都感到疲倦。"},{"en":"If children are healthy physically but stressed emotionally, support should address both areas.","zh":"如果兒童身體健康但情緒受壓，支援應同時處理兩方面。"},{"en":"This phrase combines body health with emotional well-being.","zh":"這個片語結合身體健康和情緒福祉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"behaviourally and cognitively","meaning":"在行為及認知方面","examples":[{"en":"The report also examined the children behaviourally and cognitively.","zh":"該報告也在行為及認知方面檢視兒童。"},{"en":"Behaviourally and cognitively means in terms of actions and thinking abilities.","zh":"behaviourally and cognitively 指從行動和思考能力方面來看。"},{"en":"Teachers may assess children behaviourally and cognitively by watching how they play and solve problems.","zh":"老師可能透過觀察孩子如何玩耍和解難，在行為及認知方面評估他們。"},{"en":"If a child struggles behaviourally and cognitively, both classroom habits and learning skills may need support.","zh":"如果孩子在行為及認知方面都有困難，課堂習慣和學習技能可能都需要支援。"},{"en":"This phrase combines behaviour with mental development.","zh":"這個片語結合行為和心智發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"home environment","meaning":"家庭環境","examples":[{"en":"The study documented major changes in the children’s home environments.","zh":"這項研究記錄了兒童家庭環境的重大變化。"},{"en":"A home environment is the living situation, people, routines, and conditions inside a child’s home.","zh":"home environment 是孩子家中的居住情況、人物、日常習慣和條件。"},{"en":"A calm home environment can help a child sleep, read, and feel secure.","zh":"平靜的家庭環境可以幫助孩子睡眠、閱讀和感到安全。"},{"en":"If the home environment changes often, children may need extra emotional support.","zh":"如果家庭環境經常改變，兒童可能需要額外情緒支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the surroundings in which family life happens.","zh":"這個片語描述家庭生活發生的周圍環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be documented","meaning":"被記錄","examples":[{"en":"Changes in family circumstances were carefully documented.","zh":"家庭情況的變化被仔細記錄。"},{"en":"To be documented means to be recorded in detail through notes, data, photos, or reports.","zh":"be documented 指透過筆記、數據、照片或報告詳細記錄。"},{"en":"A school incident should be documented so staff can follow up properly.","zh":"學校事件應被記錄，以便職員妥善跟進。"},{"en":"If changes are documented over time, researchers can identify patterns.","zh":"如果變化隨時間被記錄，研究人員就能識別模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information being officially recorded.","zh":"這個片語描述資訊被正式記下。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"socio-economic circumstances","meaning":"社會經濟狀況","examples":[{"en":"The report examined changes in socio-economic circumstances.","zh":"該報告檢視社會經濟狀況的變化。"},{"en":"Socio-economic circumstances are conditions related to money, work, education, housing, and social position.","zh":"socio-economic circumstances 是與金錢、工作、教育、住屋和社會地位相關的條件。"},{"en":"A child’s socio-economic circumstances may affect access to books, healthcare, and safe housing.","zh":"孩子的社會經濟狀況可能影響接觸書本、醫療和安全住屋的機會。"},{"en":"If family income falls, socio-economic circumstances can change quickly.","zh":"如果家庭收入下降，社會經濟狀況可以迅速改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the social and financial conditions of life.","zh":"這個片語描述生活中的社會和財政條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"childcare arrangements","meaning":"託兒安排","examples":[{"en":"Many families changed their childcare arrangements.","zh":"許多家庭改變了託兒安排。"},{"en":"Childcare arrangements are plans for who looks after a child, where, and when.","zh":"childcare arrangements 是關於誰、在哪裡和何時照顧孩子的安排。"},{"en":"A family may use grandparents on weekdays and daycare on busy workdays.","zh":"家庭可能平日由祖父母照顧，繁忙工作日使用日間託兒服務。"},{"en":"If a parent returns to work, childcare arrangements may need to change.","zh":"如果家長重返工作，託兒安排可能需要改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical plans for child care.","zh":"這個片語描述兒童照顧的實際計劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"direct observations","meaning":"直接觀察","examples":[{"en":"Researchers collected information through direct observations of the children.","zh":"研究人員透過直接觀察兒童收集資料。"},{"en":"Direct observations are information gathered by watching people or events oneself.","zh":"direct observations 是透過親自觀看人物或事件而收集的資料。"},{"en":"A teacher may use direct observations to see how a child plays with classmates.","zh":"老師可能使用直接觀察來了解孩子如何與同學玩耍。"},{"en":"If researchers observe children directly, they do not rely only on parents’ reports.","zh":"如果研究人員直接觀察兒童，就不只依賴家長報告。"},{"en":"This phrase describes first-hand watching as evidence.","zh":"這個片語描述以第一手觀看作為證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"parental interviews","meaning":"家長訪問","examples":[{"en":"The study also used parental interviews.","zh":"這項研究也使用家長訪問。"},{"en":"Parental interviews are conversations with parents used to collect information.","zh":"parental interviews 是用來收集資料的家長訪談。"},{"en":"A school may use parental interviews to understand a child’s routines and needs at home.","zh":"學校可能使用家長訪問，以了解孩子在家的日常習慣和需要。"},{"en":"If parental interviews are combined with direct observation, researchers get a fuller picture.","zh":"如果家長訪問與直接觀察結合，研究人員就能得到更完整圖像。"},{"en":"This phrase describes parents as information sources.","zh":"這個片語描述家長作為資訊來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a high proportion of","meaning":"高比例的……","examples":[{"en":"A high proportion of the two-year-olds were in very good health.","zh":"高比例的兩歲兒童健康狀況非常好。"},{"en":"A high proportion of means a large share or percentage of a group.","zh":"a high proportion of 指一個群體中很大的比例或百分比。"},{"en":"A high proportion of students may use the library during exam season.","zh":"考試季期間，高比例的學生可能使用圖書館。"},{"en":"If a high proportion of children are healthy, the overall health picture looks positive.","zh":"如果高比例兒童健康，整體健康情況看起來正面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large part of a group.","zh":"這個片語描述群體中的很大部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"know one’s gender","meaning":"知道自己的性別","examples":[{"en":"Two-thirds of the children knew their gender.","zh":"三分之二兒童知道自己的性別。"},{"en":"To know one’s gender means to understand whether one is identified as a boy, girl, or another gender category.","zh":"know one’s gender 指明白自己被識別為男孩、女孩或其他性別類別。"},{"en":"A two-year-old may point to themselves and say whether they are a boy or girl.","zh":"兩歲兒童可能指着自己說自己是男孩或女孩。"},{"en":"If children know their gender early, it may show developing self-awareness.","zh":"如果兒童早期知道自己的性別，這可能顯示自我意識正在發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a child’s awareness of identity.","zh":"這個片語描述孩子對身份的認知。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"use one’s own name","meaning":"使用自己的名字","examples":[{"en":"Many children could use their own name by the age of two.","zh":"許多兒童到兩歲時能使用自己的名字。"},{"en":"To use one’s own name means to say or recognise one’s name when referring to oneself.","zh":"use one’s own name 指在提到自己時能說出或認出自己的名字。"},{"en":"A toddler may say their own name when asking for a toy.","zh":"幼兒想要玩具時可能說出自己的名字。"},{"en":"If children use their own name, it may show early language and self-awareness.","zh":"如果兒童能使用自己的名字，可能顯示早期語言和自我意識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple developmental sign.","zh":"這個片語描述簡單的發展跡象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"express independence","meaning":"表達獨立性","examples":[{"en":"Many two-year-olds expressed independence in some way.","zh":"許多兩歲兒童以某種方式表達獨立性。"},{"en":"To express independence means to show a wish to do things by oneself.","zh":"express independence 指顯示想自己做事的意願。"},{"en":"A child may express independence by insisting on putting on their own shoes.","zh":"孩子可能堅持自己穿鞋來表達獨立性。"},{"en":"If children express independence, parents may need to balance safety with freedom.","zh":"如果兒童表達獨立性，父母可能需要平衡安全與自由。"},{"en":"This phrase describes early self-directed behaviour.","zh":"這個片語描述早期自主行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in some way","meaning":"以某種方式","examples":[{"en":"Most children demonstrated independence in some way.","zh":"大多數兒童以某種方式展示獨立性。"},{"en":"In some way means in one form or manner, even if the exact form differs.","zh":"in some way 指以某種形式或方式，即使具體形式不同。"},{"en":"Every student can contribute in some way, such as asking questions or helping organise notes.","zh":"每名學生都可以以某種方式作出貢獻，例如提問或幫忙整理筆記。"},{"en":"If children show independence in different ways, researchers should look beyond one behaviour.","zh":"如果兒童以不同方式展示獨立性，研究人員不應只看一種行為。"},{"en":"This phrase allows for variation.","zh":"這個片語容許不同變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the most common first word","meaning":"最常見的第一個詞語","examples":[{"en":"A variation of “Mum” was the most common first word.","zh":"“Mum” 的變體是最常見的第一個詞語。"},{"en":"The most common first word is the word most often spoken first by children in a group.","zh":"most common first word 是某群兒童最常首先說出的詞語。"},{"en":"In many families, a baby’s first word may be a form of “mum” or “dad”.","zh":"在許多家庭中，嬰兒的第一個詞可能是「媽媽」或「爸爸」的某種形式。"},{"en":"If one word is the most common first word, it may reflect who cares for children most often.","zh":"如果某詞是最常見的第一個詞語，它可能反映誰最常照顧孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an early language pattern.","zh":"這個片語描述早期語言模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a variation on","meaning":"……的變體","examples":[{"en":"The most common first word was a variation on “Mum”.","zh":"最常見的第一個詞語是 “Mum” 的變體。"},{"en":"A variation on something is a slightly different form of the same basic word, idea, or pattern.","zh":"variation on something 是同一基本詞語、想法或模式的稍微不同形式。"},{"en":"“Mama”, “Mummy”, and “Mum” are variations on the same family word.","zh":"“Mama”、“Mummy” 和 “Mum” 都是同一家庭稱呼的變體。"},{"en":"If children use different versions of a word, researchers may group them as variations.","zh":"如果兒童使用同一詞的不同版本，研究人員可能把它們歸為變體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a related but not identical form.","zh":"這個片語描述相關但不完全相同的形式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"favourite first food","meaning":"最喜愛的早期食物","examples":[{"en":"A banana was the most commonly named favourite first food.","zh":"香蕉是最常被提名的最喜愛早期食物。"},{"en":"Favourite first food means an early solid food that a baby or family especially liked.","zh":"favourite first food 指嬰兒或家庭特別喜歡的早期固體食物。"},{"en":"A parent may remember apple puree as a baby’s favourite first food.","zh":"家長可能記得蘋果蓉是嬰兒最喜愛的早期食物。"},{"en":"If many families name bananas, the food may be easy to prepare, soft, and sweet.","zh":"如果許多家庭提到香蕉，這種食物可能容易準備、柔軟且甜。"},{"en":"This phrase connects early feeding with preference.","zh":"這個片語把早期餵食與偏好連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bilingual or multilingual","meaning":"雙語或多語的","examples":[{"en":"Many of the children were bilingual or multilingual.","zh":"許多兒童是雙語或多語的。"},{"en":"Bilingual or multilingual means able to use two languages or more than two languages.","zh":"bilingual or multilingual 指能使用兩種語言或多於兩種語言。"},{"en":"A bilingual child may speak one language at home and another at school.","zh":"雙語孩子可能在家說一種語言，在學校說另一種語言。"},{"en":"If children are multilingual, schools may need to support several home languages.","zh":"如果兒童是多語的，學校可能需要支援幾種家庭語言。"},{"en":"This phrase describes language ability across two or more languages.","zh":"這個片語描述跨兩種或更多語言的能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"constitute a large minority","meaning":"構成一個大型少數群體","examples":[{"en":"Bilingual children constituted a large minority of the cohort.","zh":"雙語兒童構成該研究群組中的一個大型少數群體。"},{"en":"To constitute a large minority means to form a sizeable but not majority part of a group.","zh":"constitute a large minority 指組成一個相當大但未過半的群體部分。"},{"en":"Students who take the bus may constitute a large minority in a suburban school.","zh":"在郊區學校中，乘巴士上學的學生可能構成一個大型少數群體。"},{"en":"If a group is a large minority, services should not treat it as unimportant.","zh":"如果某群體是大型少數，服務不應把它視為不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an important minority share.","zh":"這個片語描述重要的少數比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"digital exposure","meaning":"接觸電子媒體的程度","examples":[{"en":"Digital exposure was already high among two-year-olds.","zh":"兩歲兒童接觸電子媒體的程度已經很高。"},{"en":"Digital exposure means contact with screens, computers, tablets, phones, television, or digital media.","zh":"digital exposure 指接觸螢幕、電腦、平板、手機、電視或數碼媒體。"},{"en":"A child’s digital exposure may include cartoons, video calls, and simple learning apps.","zh":"孩子的電子媒體接觸可能包括卡通、視像通話和簡單學習應用程式。"},{"en":"If digital exposure is high very early, researchers may study its effect on language and attention.","zh":"如果電子媒體接觸在很早期已很高，研究人員可能研究它對語言和注意力的影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how much young children encounter digital technology.","zh":"這個片語描述幼兒接觸數碼科技的程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"one in seven","meaning":"每七人中有一人","examples":[{"en":"One in seven two-year-olds had used a laptop or children’s computer.","zh":"每七名兩歲兒童中有一名曾使用手提電腦或兒童電腦。"},{"en":"One in seven means one person or item out of every seven.","zh":"one in seven 指每七人或每七件事物中有一個。"},{"en":"If one in seven students forgets lunch, the school may consider emergency snacks.","zh":"如果每七名學生中有一人忘記帶午餐，學校可能考慮備用小食。"},{"en":"If one in seven toddlers has used a computer, digital contact has begun early for many families.","zh":"如果每七名幼兒中有一人曾用電腦，許多家庭的數碼接觸已很早開始。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a proportion in a simple way.","zh":"這個片語以簡單方式表示比例。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"electronic devices","meaning":"電子裝置","examples":[{"en":"Many young children had already used electronic devices.","zh":"許多年幼兒童已經使用過電子裝置。"},{"en":"Electronic devices are tools such as phones, tablets, laptops, televisions, or children’s computers.","zh":"electronic devices 是手機、平板、手提電腦、電視或兒童電腦等工具。"},{"en":"Parents may limit electronic devices during meals so children can talk with family.","zh":"父母可能在用餐時限制電子裝置，讓孩子與家人說話。"},{"en":"If children use electronic devices often, their screen habits may develop early.","zh":"如果兒童經常使用電子裝置，他們的螢幕習慣可能很早形成。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to digital tools used for information, play, or communication.","zh":"這個片語指用於資訊、遊戲或溝通的數碼工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"watch something daily","meaning":"每日觀看……","examples":[{"en":"Eighty per cent of the children watched television or DVDs daily.","zh":"百分之八十兒童每日觀看電視或 DVD。"},{"en":"To watch something daily means to watch it every day.","zh":"watch something daily 指每天觀看某物。"},{"en":"A child may watch cartoons daily after dinner.","zh":"孩子可能晚飯後每日觀看卡通。"},{"en":"If children watch screens daily, parents may need to balance screen time with reading and play.","zh":"如果兒童每日觀看螢幕，父母可能需要平衡螢幕時間、閱讀和玩耍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated everyday viewing habit.","zh":"這個片語描述重複的每日觀看習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"by contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"By contrast, fewer children had books read to them every day.","zh":"相比之下，較少兒童每日有人讀書給他們聽。"},{"en":"By contrast introduces a clear difference from the previous point.","zh":"by contrast 引入與前一點清楚不同的情況。"},{"en":"Many students watch videos daily; by contrast, fewer read books every night.","zh":"許多學生每天看影片；相比之下，較少學生每晚閱讀書本。"},{"en":"If two habits differ sharply, a contrast helps readers notice the gap.","zh":"如果兩種習慣差異很大，對比能幫助讀者注意到差距。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for comparing two patterns.","zh":"這個片語適合比較兩種模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have books read to them","meaning":"有人讀書給他們聽","examples":[{"en":"Two-thirds of the children had books read to them each day.","zh":"三分之二兒童每日有人讀書給他們聽。"},{"en":"To have books read to them means someone reads books aloud for them.","zh":"have books read to them 指有人為他們朗讀書本。"},{"en":"A parent may read picture books to a toddler before bedtime.","zh":"家長可能在睡前讀圖畫書給幼兒聽。"},{"en":"If children have books read to them often, they may hear more vocabulary and story patterns.","zh":"如果兒童經常有人讀書給他們聽，他們可能聽到更多詞彙和故事模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shared reading, not independent reading.","zh":"這個片語描述共讀，而不是獨立閱讀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"evaluate risk factors","meaning":"評估風險因素","examples":[{"en":"The fourth report evaluates twelve environmental risk factors.","zh":"第四份報告評估十二個環境風險因素。"},{"en":"To evaluate risk factors means to examine conditions that may increase the chance of harm or poor outcomes.","zh":"evaluate risk factors 指檢視可能增加傷害或不良結果機會的條件。"},{"en":"A doctor may evaluate risk factors such as family history, diet, and exercise.","zh":"醫生可能評估家族病史、飲食和運動等風險因素。"},{"en":"If researchers evaluate risks carefully, they can identify children who may need extra support.","zh":"如果研究人員仔細評估風險，就能識別可能需要額外支援的兒童。"},{"en":"This phrase describes judging possible sources of danger.","zh":"這個片語描述判斷可能的危險來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"environmental risk factor","meaning":"環境風險因素","examples":[{"en":"Living in cramped housing is an environmental risk factor.","zh":"居住在擠迫住所是一個環境風險因素。"},{"en":"An environmental risk factor is a condition in a person’s surroundings that may harm development or health.","zh":"environmental risk factor 是人周圍環境中可能傷害發展或健康的條件。"},{"en":"Noise, unsafe housing, and pollution can be environmental risk factors for children.","zh":"噪音、不安全住屋和污染都可以是兒童的環境風險因素。"},{"en":"If several environmental risk factors are present, a child’s development may be more vulnerable.","zh":"如果幾個環境風險因素同時存在，孩子發展可能更脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes risk from the living environment.","zh":"這個片語描述來自生活環境的風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"increase the likelihood of","meaning":"增加……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"Certain conditions increase the likelihood of poor developmental outcomes.","zh":"某些條件會增加不良發展結果的可能性。"},{"en":"To increase the likelihood of something means to make it more likely to happen.","zh":"increase the likelihood of something 指令某事更有可能發生。"},{"en":"Missing lessons can increase the likelihood of weak exam performance.","zh":"缺課可以增加考試表現較弱的可能性。"},{"en":"If families face poverty and cramped housing, the likelihood of developmental problems may rise.","zh":"如果家庭面對貧窮和擠迫住屋，發展問題的可能性可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes raising the chance of a result.","zh":"這個片語描述提高某結果的機會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"poor developmental outcomes","meaning":"不良發展結果","examples":[{"en":"The study identifies factors linked to poor developmental outcomes.","zh":"這項研究識別與不良發展結果有關的因素。"},{"en":"Poor developmental outcomes are negative results in a child’s growth, learning, behaviour, or health.","zh":"poor developmental outcomes 是兒童成長、學習、行為或健康方面的負面結果。"},{"en":"Delayed speech and serious behavioural problems can be poor developmental outcomes.","zh":"語言發展延遲和嚴重行為問題都可以是不良發展結果。"},{"en":"If risk factors are addressed early, poor developmental outcomes may be reduced.","zh":"如果風險因素及早處理，不良發展結果可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unfavourable results in child development.","zh":"這個片語描述兒童發展中的不利結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"draw on experiences in","meaning":"借鑑……的經驗","examples":[{"en":"The report draws on experiences in Western Europe.","zh":"該報告借鑑西歐的經驗。"},{"en":"To draw on experiences in a place means to use lessons or knowledge gained from that place.","zh":"draw on experiences in a place 指使用從某地獲得的教訓或知識。"},{"en":"A school may draw on experiences in Finland when improving reading lessons.","zh":"學校改善閱讀課時，可能借鑑芬蘭的經驗。"},{"en":"If researchers draw on another region’s work, they can test whether ideas fit their own context.","zh":"如果研究人員借鑑另一地區的工作，就能測試那些想法是否適合本地情境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using existing experience as a resource.","zh":"這個片語描述把既有經驗作為資源使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Western Europe","meaning":"西歐","examples":[{"en":"The risk factors were originally collated in Western Europe.","zh":"這些風險因素最初在西歐被整理彙編。"},{"en":"Western Europe refers to the western part of Europe, including countries such as France, Germany, the Netherlands, and the United Kingdom.","zh":"Western Europe 指歐洲西部，包括法國、德國、荷蘭和英國等國家。"},{"en":"Social policies in Western Europe are often compared with those in other developed regions.","zh":"西歐的社會政策常與其他已發展地區比較。"},{"en":"If criteria come from Western Europe, researchers must check whether they suit New Zealand families.","zh":"如果準則來自西歐，研究人員必須檢查它們是否適合新西蘭家庭。"},{"en":"This phrase names a broad European region.","zh":"這個片語指出一個廣泛的歐洲地區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"specific factors","meaning":"特定因素","examples":[{"en":"The researchers applied several specific factors to the New Zealand population.","zh":"研究人員把幾個特定因素應用於新西蘭人口。"},{"en":"Specific factors are particular causes, conditions, or details being examined.","zh":"specific factors 是正在被檢視的特定原因、條件或細節。"},{"en":"A doctor may consider specific factors such as age, diet, and family history.","zh":"醫生可能考慮年齡、飲食和家族病史等特定因素。"},{"en":"If specific factors are measured clearly, researchers can compare risk more accurately.","zh":"如果特定因素被清楚量度，研究人員就能更準確比較風險。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on exact factors rather than general ideas.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於確切因素，而不是一般想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be collated","meaning":"被整理彙編","examples":[{"en":"The risk factors had previously been collated in Europe.","zh":"這些風險因素先前已在歐洲被整理彙編。"},{"en":"To be collated means to be gathered, organised, and arranged together.","zh":"be collated 指被收集、整理並放在一起。"},{"en":"A teacher may collate students’ survey answers before writing a class report.","zh":"老師撰寫班級報告前，可能整理學生問卷答案。"},{"en":"If data is collated carefully, patterns become easier to see.","zh":"如果數據被仔細整理彙編，模式就更容易看見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collecting and organising information.","zh":"這個片語描述收集並組織資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be used in a New Zealand context","meaning":"在新西蘭情境中使用","examples":[{"en":"The factors were used in a New Zealand context for the first time.","zh":"這些因素首次在新西蘭情境中使用。"},{"en":"To be used in a New Zealand context means to be applied to New Zealand’s society, families, and conditions.","zh":"be used in a New Zealand context 指被應用於新西蘭的社會、家庭和條件中。"},{"en":"A teaching method from another country may need adjustment before being used in a New Zealand context.","zh":"來自另一國家的教學方法在新西蘭情境中使用前，可能需要調整。"},{"en":"If imported criteria are used locally, researchers must check cultural and social fit.","zh":"如果外來準則在本地使用，研究人員必須檢查文化和社會是否適合。"},{"en":"This phrase describes applying an idea within New Zealand’s real situation.","zh":"這個片語描述把想法應用於新西蘭真實情況中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be born to an adolescent mother","meaning":"由青少年母親所生","examples":[{"en":"Being born to an adolescent mother may increase a child’s vulnerability.","zh":"由青少年母親所生可能增加兒童的脆弱處境。"},{"en":"To be born to an adolescent mother means to have a mother who is still a teenager or very young.","zh":"be born to an adolescent mother 指母親仍是青少年或非常年輕時出生。"},{"en":"A baby born to an adolescent mother may need extra family and health-service support.","zh":"由青少年母親所生的嬰兒可能需要額外家庭和醫療服務支援。"},{"en":"If a mother is very young, income, education, and childcare pressures may be greater.","zh":"如果母親非常年輕，收入、教育和託兒壓力可能更大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one possible early-life risk factor.","zh":"這個片語描述一個可能的早期生活風險因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"income-tested benefits","meaning":"入息審查福利","examples":[{"en":"Some children had parents receiving income-tested benefits.","zh":"一些兒童的父母正在領取入息審查福利。"},{"en":"Income-tested benefits are welfare payments given only when a person or family’s income is below a certain level.","zh":"income-tested benefits 是只有在人或家庭收入低於某水平時才提供的福利金。"},{"en":"A family may receive income-tested benefits if a parent loses work and income falls.","zh":"如果家長失業並且收入下降，家庭可能領取入息審查福利。"},{"en":"If many families rely on such benefits, researchers may examine poverty and child development together.","zh":"如果許多家庭依賴這類福利，研究人員可能一併檢視貧窮和兒童發展。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to government support based on income.","zh":"這個片語指以收入為基礎的政府支援。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cramped conditions","meaning":"擠迫的居住環境","examples":[{"en":"Living in cramped conditions may affect children’s development.","zh":"居住在擠迫環境中可能影響兒童發展。"},{"en":"Cramped conditions are living conditions with too little space for the number of people present.","zh":"cramped conditions 是居住空間相對人數太少的情況。"},{"en":"A family of six sharing one small room may live in cramped conditions.","zh":"六人家庭共用一間小房，可能生活在擠迫環境中。"},{"en":"If children live in cramped conditions, sleep, study, and play may become difficult.","zh":"如果兒童生活在擠迫環境中，睡眠、學習和玩耍可能變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes overcrowded living space.","zh":"這個片語描述過度擁擠的生活空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in addition to","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"In addition to descriptive reports, future research will study changing vulnerability.","zh":"除了描述性報告之外，未來研究將研究變化中的脆弱處境。"},{"en":"In addition to means besides or as well as something already mentioned.","zh":"in addition to 指除了已提及的某事之外，也包括另一事。"},{"en":"In addition to homework, students should read examples to improve writing.","zh":"除了功課之外，學生也應閱讀例子來改善寫作。"},{"en":"If research includes analysis in addition to description, it can explain patterns more deeply.","zh":"如果研究除了描述之外還包括分析，就能更深入解釋模式。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another item or idea.","zh":"這個片語加入另一個項目或想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"聚焦於","examples":[{"en":"Future reports will focus on children who move in and out of vulnerability.","zh":"未來報告將聚焦於進出脆弱處境的兒童。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give it special attention.","zh":"focus on something 指特別注意某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may focus on grammar errors that students repeat most often.","zh":"老師可能聚焦於學生最常重複的文法錯誤。"},{"en":"If researchers focus on changing risk, they can see which children recover and which remain vulnerable.","zh":"如果研究人員聚焦於變化中的風險，就能看到哪些兒童恢復，哪些仍脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main subject of attention.","zh":"這個片語描述注意力的主要對象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"move in and out of vulnerability","meaning":"進出脆弱處境","examples":[{"en":"Some children move in and out of vulnerable circumstances.","zh":"一些兒童會進出脆弱處境。"},{"en":"To move in and out of vulnerability means to enter and leave risky or disadvantaged situations over time.","zh":"move in and out of vulnerability 指隨時間進入和離開有風險或處於不利的情況。"},{"en":"A family may move in and out of vulnerability if work is unstable and income changes often.","zh":"如果工作不穩定、收入經常改變，家庭可能進出脆弱處境。"},{"en":"If children move in and out of risk, one-time data may not show their full experience.","zh":"如果兒童進出風險狀態，一次性數據可能不能顯示完整經歷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing rather than fixed vulnerability.","zh":"這個片語描述變化中的、而非固定的脆弱處境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"transition","meaning":"轉變；過渡","examples":[{"en":"The researchers want to understand how these transitions affect later life.","zh":"研究人員想了解這些轉變如何影響日後生活。"},{"en":"A transition is a change from one state, stage, or situation to another.","zh":"transition 是從一種狀態、階段或情況轉到另一種的變化。"},{"en":"Moving from kindergarten to primary school is an important transition for young children.","zh":"從幼稚園升上小學是幼兒的重要過渡。"},{"en":"If transitions happen too often, children may feel unstable or stressed.","zh":"如果轉變太頻繁，兒童可能感到不穩定或受壓。"},{"en":"This word describes a process of change.","zh":"這個詞描述變化過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"affect later life","meaning":"影響日後生活","examples":[{"en":"Early changes in vulnerability may affect a child’s later life.","zh":"脆弱處境的早期變化可能影響孩子日後生活。"},{"en":"To affect later life means to influence what happens in the future as a person grows older.","zh":"affect later life 指影響一個人長大後未來發生的事情。"},{"en":"Childhood reading habits may affect later life by shaping confidence and learning skills.","zh":"童年閱讀習慣可能透過塑造信心和學習技能來影響日後生活。"},{"en":"If early hardship affects later life, support should begin before problems become permanent.","zh":"如果早期困難會影響日後生活，支援就應在問題變永久前開始。"},{"en":"This phrase connects early experiences with future outcomes.","zh":"這個片語把早期經歷與未來結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"to date","meaning":"到目前為止","examples":[{"en":"To date, the longitudinal study has been highly successful.","zh":"到目前為止，這項縱向研究非常成功。"},{"en":"To date means up to the present time or up to the time being discussed.","zh":"to date 指直到現在或直到正在討論的時間為止。"},{"en":"To date, the school has received 300 applications for the summer course.","zh":"到目前為止，學校已收到300份暑期課程申請。"},{"en":"If a study has succeeded to date, it has performed well so far but still needs to continue.","zh":"如果研究到目前為止成功，它目前表現良好，但仍需要繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase marks progress up to now.","zh":"這個片語標示至今的進展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"highly successful","meaning":"非常成功","examples":[{"en":"The project has been highly successful in retaining participants.","zh":"這個項目在保留參加者方面非常成功。"},{"en":"Highly successful means very effective or achieving very good results.","zh":"highly successful 指非常有效或取得非常好結果。"},{"en":"A reading programme is highly successful if students read more and improve their scores.","zh":"如果閱讀計劃令學生讀得更多並提高分數，它就是非常成功。"},{"en":"If a long study keeps most participants, it becomes more valuable for future analysis.","zh":"如果長期研究能保留大多數參加者，它對未來分析就更有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong success, not just acceptable performance.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈成功，而不只是表現尚可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"dropout rate","meaning":"退出率","examples":[{"en":"The study has maintained a very small dropout rate.","zh":"這項研究維持了很低的退出率。"},{"en":"Dropout rate is the percentage of participants who leave a study, school, or programme before it ends.","zh":"dropout rate 是參加者在研究、學校或計劃完結前離開的百分比。"},{"en":"A course with a high dropout rate may be too expensive, difficult, or poorly supported.","zh":"退出率高的課程可能太昂貴、太困難或支援不足。"},{"en":"If a study has a low dropout rate, its long-term results are more reliable.","zh":"如果研究退出率低，其長期結果會較可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase measures how many people stop participating.","zh":"這個片語量度有多少人停止參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"among participants","meaning":"在參加者之中","examples":[{"en":"The dropout rate among participants has remained low.","zh":"參加者之中的退出率一直很低。"},{"en":"Among participants means within the group of people taking part.","zh":"among participants 指在參與的人群之中。"},{"en":"Among participants in a workshop, confidence may improve after several practice sessions.","zh":"在工作坊參加者之中，幾次練習後信心可能提升。"},{"en":"If dropout is low among participants, most people are still providing data.","zh":"如果參加者之中的退出率低，大多數人仍在提供數據。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the people involved in a study or activity.","zh":"這個片語聚焦於參與研究或活動的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"even those living abroad","meaning":"即使是居於海外的人","examples":[{"en":"Even participants living abroad have continued to provide information.","zh":"即使是居於海外的參加者也繼續提供資料。"},{"en":"Even those living abroad means including people who no longer live in the original country.","zh":"even those living abroad 指包括不再住在原本國家的人。"},{"en":"Even students living abroad can join an online class if the time zone works.","zh":"如果時區合適，即使是居於海外的學生也可以參加網上課堂。"},{"en":"If overseas participants still respond, the study can keep a wider and more complete sample.","zh":"如果海外參加者仍回應，研究就能保持更廣泛和完整的樣本。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that distance did not stop participation.","zh":"這個片語強調距離沒有阻止參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"predominantly in Australia","meaning":"主要在澳洲","examples":[{"en":"Most overseas participants were living predominantly in Australia.","zh":"大多數海外參加者主要居於澳洲。"},{"en":"Predominantly in Australia means mainly or mostly in Australia.","zh":"predominantly in Australia 指主要或大多在澳洲。"},{"en":"A company’s overseas customers may be predominantly in Australia if most orders come from there.","zh":"如果大多數訂單來自澳洲，一間公司的海外客戶可能主要在澳洲。"},{"en":"If overseas participants are mostly in one country, researchers may consider migration patterns.","zh":"如果海外參加者大多在同一國家，研究人員可能考慮移民模式。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main overseas location.","zh":"這個片語指出主要海外地點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"continue to provide information","meaning":"繼續提供資料","examples":[{"en":"Participants abroad continued to provide information to the study.","zh":"海外參加者繼續向研究提供資料。"},{"en":"To continue to provide information means to keep giving data or answers over time.","zh":"continue to provide information 指隨時間持續提供數據或答案。"},{"en":"Parents may continue to provide information through yearly surveys.","zh":"家長可能透過年度問卷繼續提供資料。"},{"en":"If participants keep responding, the study can track changes more accurately.","zh":"如果參加者持續回應，研究就能更準確追蹤變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing cooperation in research.","zh":"這個片語描述研究中的持續合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"paint a portrait of","meaning":"描繪……的面貌","examples":[{"en":"The study paints a detailed portrait of New Zealand society.","zh":"這項研究詳細描繪新西蘭社會的面貌。"},{"en":"To paint a portrait of something means to describe it clearly and fully, as if creating a picture with words or data.","zh":"paint a portrait of something 指清楚而全面地描述某事，就像用文字或數據畫出圖像。"},{"en":"A documentary can paint a portrait of a city through interviews, streets, and family stories.","zh":"紀錄片可以透過訪問、街道和家庭故事描繪一個城市的面貌。"},{"en":"If a study includes many details, it can show what society really looks like.","zh":"如果研究包含許多細節，它可以顯示社會真正面貌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating a rich description.","zh":"這個片語描述創造豐富描寫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"revealing portrait","meaning":"揭示性強的寫照","examples":[{"en":"The reports provide a revealing portrait of the country and its people.","zh":"這些報告提供了該國及其人民的揭示性寫照。"},{"en":"A revealing portrait is a description that shows important truths or hidden details.","zh":"revealing portrait 是展示重要真相或隱藏細節的描述。"},{"en":"A school survey can provide a revealing portrait of students’ stress and study habits.","zh":"學校調查可以提供學生壓力和學習習慣的揭示性寫照。"},{"en":"If a portrait is revealing, it helps readers see beyond surface impressions.","zh":"如果寫照揭示性強，它能幫助讀者看見表面印象以外的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a description that teaches us something important.","zh":"這個片語描述能讓我們學到重要事情的描寫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"inform public policy","meaning":"為公共政策提供參考","examples":[{"en":"Findings from the study may inform future public policy.","zh":"這項研究的發現可能為未來公共政策提供參考。"},{"en":"To inform public policy means to provide evidence or understanding that helps shape government decisions.","zh":"inform public policy 指提供證據或理解，以幫助塑造政府決策。"},{"en":"Research on traffic accidents can inform public policy on road safety.","zh":"關於交通意外的研究可以為道路安全公共政策提供參考。"},{"en":"If child-development data informs policy, services may be better targeted.","zh":"如果兒童發展數據為政策提供參考，服務可能更能針對需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research guiding official decisions.","zh":"這個片語描述研究引導官方決策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"form a cohort","meaning":"組成研究群組","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of babies formed the study cohort.","zh":"數千名嬰兒組成研究群組。"},{"en":"To form a cohort means to make up a group of participants with a shared feature.","zh":"form a cohort 指組成一個具有共同特徵的參加者群體。"},{"en":"Students entering university in the same year may form a cohort for research.","zh":"同年入讀大學的學生可能組成一個研究群組。"},{"en":"If babies born in the same period form a cohort, researchers can compare their development over time.","zh":"如果同一時期出生的嬰兒組成研究群組，研究人員可以隨時間比較他們的發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating or making up a study group.","zh":"這個片語描述建立或構成研究群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"probably end when","meaning":"可能在……時結束","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether the study will probably end when the children are ten.","zh":"該陳述問研究是否可能在兒童十歲時結束。"},{"en":"Probably end when means likely to finish at the time that something happens.","zh":"probably end when 指很可能在某事發生時完成。"},{"en":"A school project will probably end when students submit their final presentations.","zh":"學校專題可能在學生提交最終匯報時結束。"},{"en":"If a study is planned to continue to age 21, it will not probably end at age ten.","zh":"如果研究計劃持續到21歲，它就不大可能在十歲時結束。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an expected finishing point.","zh":"這個片語描述預期的結束點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"reach ten","meaning":"年滿十歲","examples":[{"en":"The project is intended to continue well beyond the time the children reach ten.","zh":"該項目打算在兒童年滿十歲後仍繼續很久。"},{"en":"To reach ten means to become ten years old.","zh":"reach ten 指變成十歲。"},{"en":"When children reach ten, they may become more independent in school and friendships.","zh":"當兒童年滿十歲，他們在學校和友誼中可能變得更獨立。"},{"en":"If research continues beyond age ten, it can examine adolescence as well as childhood.","zh":"如果研究在十歲後仍繼續，它可以檢視青春期以及童年。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a specific age point.","zh":"這個片語給出特定年齡點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"eventually","meaning":"最終","examples":[{"en":"The question asks how many reports may eventually be published.","zh":"題目問最終可能會出版多少份報告。"},{"en":"Eventually means in the end, after some time has passed.","zh":"eventually 指一段時間過後最終發生。"},{"en":"A student who practises speaking every week may eventually become confident.","zh":"每週練習說話的學生最終可能變得有信心。"},{"en":"If a long study continues, more reports may eventually be published.","zh":"如果長期研究繼續，最終可能會出版更多報告。"},{"en":"This word points to a later final result.","zh":"這個詞指向較後的最終結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be similar to","meaning":"與……相似","examples":[{"en":"The findings show that current families are not necessarily similar to earlier generations.","zh":"研究發現顯示現今家庭不一定與前幾代相似。"},{"en":"To be similar to something means to share features or qualities with it.","zh":"be similar to something 指與某物共享特徵或質素。"},{"en":"A new school timetable may be similar to last year’s, but with shorter lunch breaks.","zh":"新學校時間表可能與去年的相似，但午飯時間較短。"},{"en":"If today’s families are not similar to earlier ones, old research may not fully apply.","zh":"如果今日家庭與早期家庭不相似，舊研究可能不能完全適用。"},{"en":"This phrase compares likeness between two things.","zh":"這個片語比較兩者之間的相似性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"take part in","meaning":"參與","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of parents and children took part in the study.","zh":"數千名父母和兒童參與了這項研究。"},{"en":"To take part in something means to participate in it.","zh":"take part in something 指參與某事。"},{"en":"Students may take part in a reading competition to practise English.","zh":"學生可能參與閱讀比賽來練習英文。"},{"en":"If many families take part in a study, the findings can represent more experiences.","zh":"如果許多家庭參與研究，研究發現就能代表更多經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active participation.","zh":"這個片語描述主動參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a good place to raise children","meaning":"適合養育兒童的地方","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether parents consider New Zealand a good place to raise children.","zh":"該陳述問父母是否認為新西蘭是適合養育兒童的地方。"},{"en":"A good place to raise children is a place with safety, education, healthcare, family support, and opportunities.","zh":"good place to raise children 是有安全、教育、醫療、家庭支援和機會的地方。"},{"en":"Parents may see a neighbourhood with parks and good schools as a good place to raise children.","zh":"父母可能認為有公園和好學校的社區是適合養育兒童的地方。"},{"en":"If housing is expensive or services are weak, a place may become harder for families.","zh":"如果住屋昂貴或服務薄弱，一個地方對家庭而言可能變得較困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes whether an environment supports child upbringing.","zh":"這個片語描述某環境是否支持兒童成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"classify the following statements","meaning":"將以下陳述分類","examples":[{"en":"Candidates classify the following statements according to the relevant report.","zh":"考生根據相關報告將以下陳述分類。"},{"en":"To classify the following statements means to sort the listed statements into correct groups or categories.","zh":"classify the following statements 指把列出的陳述分到正確組別或類別。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students may classify statements as relating to Report 1, Report 2, or Report 3.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生可能把陳述分類為與報告一、報告二或報告三有關。"},{"en":"If students classify statements carefully, they must match meaning rather than only keywords.","zh":"如果學生仔細分類陳述，就必須配對意思，而不只是關鍵字。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個片語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"according to the report","meaning":"根據相關報告","examples":[{"en":"Each statement must be classified according to the report it describes.","zh":"每項陳述必須根據它所描述的報告分類。"},{"en":"According to the report means based on the information given in that report.","zh":"according to the report 指根據該報告中提供的資料。"},{"en":"According to the report, most babies were in very good health.","zh":"根據報告，大多數嬰兒健康狀況非常好。"},{"en":"If an answer must be according to the report, students should not use outside knowledge.","zh":"如果答案必須根據報告，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the source of evidence.","zh":"這個片語指出證據來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"relate to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The task asks which report each statement relates to.","zh":"任務問每項陳述與哪份報告有關。"},{"en":"To relate to something means to be connected with it or about it.","zh":"relate to something 指與某事連接或關於某事。"},{"en":"A question about breastfeeding relates to health and infant care.","zh":"關於母乳餵哺的問題與健康和嬰兒照顧有關。"},{"en":"If a statement relates to the fourth report, it should match the report’s focus on vulnerability.","zh":"如果陳述與第四份報告有關，它應符合該報告對脆弱處境的焦點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes connection to a topic.","zh":"這個片語描述與主題的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be unique because","meaning":"獨特之處在於","examples":[{"en":"The first report is unique because it includes interviews with both parents.","zh":"第一份報告獨特之處在於它包括與父母雙方的訪問。"},{"en":"To be unique because means to be special or different for a particular reason.","zh":"be unique because 指因某個特定原因而特別或不同。"},{"en":"A school project may be unique because students interview grandparents instead of using textbooks only.","zh":"學校專題可能因學生訪問祖父母而不是只用課本而獨特。"},{"en":"If a report includes both mothers and fathers for the first time, that feature makes it special.","zh":"如果報告首次包括母親和父親，這個特徵使它特別。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why something is unlike others.","zh":"這個片語解釋某事為何與其他不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"both parents","meaning":"父母雙方","examples":[{"en":"The report contains information from both parents.","zh":"該報告載有來自父母雙方的資料。"},{"en":"Both parents means the mother and the father, or both people acting as parents.","zh":"both parents 指母親和父親，或兩名擔任父母角色的人。"},{"en":"A teacher may speak with both parents to understand a child’s home situation better.","zh":"老師可能與父母雙方交談，以更好理解孩子的家庭情況。"},{"en":"If information comes from both parents, the family picture may be more balanced.","zh":"如果資料來自父母雙方，家庭圖像可能更平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the two parental figures together.","zh":"這個片語指兩名父母角色一起。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"look at how","meaning":"研究……如何","examples":[{"en":"The fourth report looks at how children might be at risk.","zh":"第四份報告研究兒童可能如何處於風險中。"},{"en":"To look at how something happens means to examine the way or process by which it happens.","zh":"look at how something happens 指檢視某事發生的方式或過程。"},{"en":"A teacher may look at how students plan essays before teaching writing structure.","zh":"老師可能先研究學生如何規劃文章，再教授寫作結構。"},{"en":"If researchers look at how risk develops, they can design more precise support.","zh":"如果研究人員研究風險如何形成，就能設計更精準的支援。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a process being examined.","zh":"這個片語引入正在被檢視的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be at risk","meaning":"處於風險中","examples":[{"en":"Some environmental conditions place children at risk.","zh":"一些環境條件使兒童處於風險中。"},{"en":"To be at risk means to be in a situation where harm or difficulty is more likely.","zh":"be at risk 指處於傷害或困難更可能發生的情況。"},{"en":"Children may be at risk if they live in unsafe housing or lack regular meals.","zh":"如果兒童住在不安全住所或缺乏定時膳食，可能處於風險中。"},{"en":"If a child is at risk, early support can reduce future problems.","zh":"如果孩子處於風險中，早期支援可以減少未來問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exposure to possible harm.","zh":"這個片語描述暴露於可能傷害之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lead to financial hardship","meaning":"導致經濟困難","examples":[{"en":"Having a child may lead to financial hardship for some families.","zh":"生育孩子可能導致一些家庭經濟困難。"},{"en":"To lead to financial hardship means to cause serious money difficulties.","zh":"lead to financial hardship 指造成嚴重金錢困難。"},{"en":"Losing a job after a baby is born can lead to financial hardship.","zh":"嬰兒出生後失業可能導致經濟困難。"},{"en":"If income falls while expenses rise, families may struggle to pay bills.","zh":"如果收入下降而開支上升，家庭可能難以支付帳單。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a life event with money pressure.","zh":"這個片語把人生事件與金錢壓力連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"financial hardship","meaning":"經濟困難","examples":[{"en":"A sharp fall in income can create financial hardship.","zh":"收入急跌可以造成經濟困難。"},{"en":"Financial hardship means serious difficulty paying for basic needs such as food, housing, bills, or childcare.","zh":"financial hardship 指難以支付食物、住屋、帳單或託兒等基本需要。"},{"en":"A family may experience financial hardship after medical bills or job loss.","zh":"家庭可能在醫療費或失業後經歷經濟困難。"},{"en":"If financial hardship continues, children’s nutrition, housing, and learning opportunities may be affected.","zh":"如果經濟困難持續，兒童營養、住屋和學習機會可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stressful money problems.","zh":"這個片語描述令人受壓的金錢問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"come from direct observations","meaning":"來自直接觀察","examples":[{"en":"Some of the information came from direct observations of children.","zh":"部分資料來自對兒童的直接觀察。"},{"en":"To come from direct observations means to be based on what researchers personally saw.","zh":"come from direct observations 指建基於研究人員親眼看到的內容。"},{"en":"A teacher’s notes about playground behaviour may come from direct observations.","zh":"老師關於操場行為的筆記可能來自直接觀察。"},{"en":"If information comes from direct observation, it may confirm or challenge what parents report.","zh":"如果資料來自直接觀察，它可能確認或挑戰家長報告。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies first-hand observation as the source.","zh":"這個片語指出第一手觀察作為來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"use electronic devices","meaning":"使用電子裝置","examples":[{"en":"Many two-year-olds had already used electronic devices.","zh":"許多兩歲兒童已經使用過電子裝置。"},{"en":"To use electronic devices means to operate tools such as tablets, phones, laptops, televisions, or children’s computers.","zh":"use electronic devices 指操作平板、手機、手提電腦、電視或兒童電腦等工具。"},{"en":"A toddler may use an electronic device to watch cartoons or talk to grandparents by video.","zh":"幼兒可能使用電子裝置觀看卡通或與祖父母視像通話。"},{"en":"If young children use devices often, adults may need clear rules about screen time.","zh":"如果年幼兒童經常使用裝置，成人可能需要清楚螢幕時間規則。"},{"en":"This phrase describes interacting with digital tools.","zh":"這個片語描述與數碼工具互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be modelled on","meaning":"以……為藍本","examples":[{"en":"The vulnerability criteria were modelled on those used in Western Europe.","zh":"脆弱處境準則以西歐使用的準則為藍本。"},{"en":"To be modelled on something means to be designed by following its example.","zh":"be modelled on something 指按照某事例子設計。"},{"en":"A school’s mentoring scheme may be modelled on a successful programme from another city.","zh":"學校的導師計劃可能以另一城市的成功計劃為藍本。"},{"en":"If criteria are modelled on another region’s work, they may need local adjustment.","zh":"如果準則以另一地區的工作為藍本，它們可能需要本地調整。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using an existing model as a guide.","zh":"這個片語描述使用既有模式作為指引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"negatively affect","meaning":"對……造成負面影響","examples":[{"en":"Several early-life risks may negatively affect a child’s development.","zh":"幾種早期生活風險可能對兒童發展造成負面影響。"},{"en":"To negatively affect something means to harm it or make it worse.","zh":"negatively affect something 指傷害某事或令它變差。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can negatively affect a student’s memory and mood.","zh":"睡眠不足可以對學生記憶和心情造成負面影響。"},{"en":"If housing is unsafe or overcrowded, it may negatively affect children’s health and learning.","zh":"如果住屋不安全或過度擠迫，可能對兒童健康和學習造成負面影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a harmful influence.","zh":"這個片語描述有害影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards 168 - Growing up in New Zealand.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 169":[{"front":"the fluoridation controversy","meaning":"食水加氟爭議","examples":[{"en":"The fluoridation controversy involves scientific evidence, public policy and individual rights.","zh":"食水加氟爭議涉及科學證據、公共政策和個人權利。"},{"en":"The fluoridation controversy is the debate over whether fluoride should be added to public water.","zh":"the fluoridation controversy 指是否應在公共食水中加入氟化物的爭議。"},{"en":"A community meeting may discuss the fluoridation controversy before changing water policy.","zh":"社區會議可能在改變食水政策前討論食水加氟爭議。"},{"en":"The controversy continues because people disagree about benefits, risks and personal choice.","zh":"這場爭議持續，是因為人們對好處、風險和個人選擇有分歧。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when science, health policy and values all become part of one debate.","zh":"當科學、健康政策和價值觀都成為同一場辯論的一部分時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"long-standing debate","meaning":"長期爭議","examples":[{"en":"The long-standing debate over water fluoridation remains unresolved.","zh":"關於食水加氟的長期爭議仍未解決。"},{"en":"A long-standing debate is an argument that has continued for many years.","zh":"long-standing debate 指持續多年的爭議。"},{"en":"Schools may have a long-standing debate over homework if parents and teachers disagree.","zh":"如果家長和老師意見不同，學校可能長期爭議是否應有功課。"},{"en":"Long-standing debates continue when evidence or values do not settle the issue.","zh":"當證據或價值觀未能解決問題，長期爭議就會持續。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that a disagreement is old and still active.","zh":"這個短語暗示分歧已存在很久，而且仍然活躍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"whether to fluoridate","meaning":"是否在食水中加氟","examples":[{"en":"Communities continue to debate whether to fluoridate their drinking water.","zh":"社區繼續爭論是否在食水中加氟。"},{"en":"Whether to fluoridate means whether fluoride should be added to water.","zh":"whether to fluoridate 指是否應在食水中加入氟化物。"},{"en":"A city council may vote on whether to fluoridate local water supplies.","zh":"市議會可能投票決定是否在本地食水供應中加氟。"},{"en":"People debate this question because it affects everyone who drinks the water.","zh":"人們爭論這個問題，因為它影響所有飲用該水的人。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a yes-or-no policy decision about adding fluoride.","zh":"這個短語引出關於加入氟化物的「是或否」政策決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"drinking water","meaning":"食水","examples":[{"en":"Fluoride may be added to public drinking water.","zh":"氟化物可能被加入公共食水中。"},{"en":"Drinking water is water that is safe or intended for people to drink.","zh":"drinking water 指安全或預定供人飲用的水。"},{"en":"Schools need clean drinking water so students can stay healthy during the day.","zh":"學校需要乾淨食水，讓學生在一天中保持健康。"},{"en":"If drinking water is polluted, a whole community may face health risks.","zh":"如果食水受污染，整個社區都可能面對健康風險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to water for human consumption, not water for washing or farming.","zh":"這個短語指供人飲用的水，而不是洗滌或農業用水。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fluoridation","meaning":"食水加氟","examples":[{"en":"Fluoridation is intended to reduce tooth decay in the community.","zh":"食水加氟旨在減少社區中的蛀牙。"},{"en":"Fluoridation means adding fluoride to water, usually to protect teeth.","zh":"fluoridation 指在水中加入氟化物，通常是為了保護牙齒。"},{"en":"A public-health department may recommend fluoridation after studying children’s dental health.","zh":"公共衛生部門研究兒童牙齒健康後，可能建議食水加氟。"},{"en":"Fluoridation is debated because it affects everyone using the water supply.","zh":"食水加氟具爭議，因為它影響所有使用該食水供應的人。"},{"en":"This word is mainly used in discussions of water policy and dental health.","zh":"這個字主要用於水務政策和牙齒健康討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the addition of fluorine to","meaning":"在……中加入氟","examples":[{"en":"Fluoridation involves the addition of fluorine compounds to public water supplies.","zh":"食水加氟涉及在公共食水供應中加入氟化合物。"},{"en":"The addition of fluorine to something means putting fluorine compounds into it.","zh":"the addition of fluorine to something 指把氟化合物加入某物之中。"},{"en":"The addition of vitamins to food may be used to improve public health.","zh":"在食物中加入維他命可能被用來改善公共健康。"},{"en":"Adding a substance to water requires careful control because many people consume it.","zh":"在水中加入物質需要小心控制，因為很多人會飲用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the act of putting fluorine-related chemicals into a supply.","zh":"這個短語描述把與氟有關的化學物質加入供應系統的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"public water supplies","meaning":"公共食水供應","examples":[{"en":"Some governments add fluoride to public water supplies.","zh":"有些政府在公共食水供應中加入氟化物。"},{"en":"Public water supplies are water systems provided for a whole community.","zh":"public water supplies 指提供給整個社區的食水系統。"},{"en":"A city must test public water supplies regularly to keep residents safe.","zh":"城市必須定期測試公共食水供應，以保障居民安全。"},{"en":"If something is added to public water supplies, many people receive it automatically.","zh":"如果某物被加入公共食水供應，很多人會自動攝取它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to shared water systems, not private bottles or wells.","zh":"這個短語指共享食水系統，而不是私人瓶裝水或水井。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"with the aim of reducing","meaning":"目的是減少……","examples":[{"en":"Fluoride is added with the aim of reducing tooth decay.","zh":"加入氟化物的目的是減少蛀牙。"},{"en":"With the aim of reducing something means with the purpose of making it less serious or less common.","zh":"with the aim of reducing something 指目的是令某事較不嚴重或較少發生。"},{"en":"A school may start a reading scheme with the aim of reducing learning gaps.","zh":"學校可能推行閱讀計劃，目的是減少學習差距。"},{"en":"Public policies are often introduced with the aim of reducing a social problem.","zh":"公共政策常被引入，目的是減少某個社會問題。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the intended purpose behind an action.","zh":"這個短語解釋行動背後的目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tooth decay","meaning":"蛀牙","examples":[{"en":"Fluoridation is promoted as a way to prevent tooth decay.","zh":"食水加氟被推廣為預防蛀牙的方法。"},{"en":"Tooth decay is damage to teeth caused by bacteria and acid.","zh":"tooth decay 指由細菌和酸造成的牙齒損壞。"},{"en":"Children may get tooth decay if they eat too much sugar and rarely brush their teeth.","zh":"如果孩子吃太多糖又很少刷牙，可能會蛀牙。"},{"en":"Tooth decay can lead to pain, infection and dental treatment.","zh":"蛀牙可以導致疼痛、感染和牙科治療。"},{"en":"This phrase means teeth becoming damaged, not simply becoming yellow.","zh":"這個短語指牙齒受損，而不只是變黃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be mixed with water","meaning":"與水混合","examples":[{"en":"Fluorine compounds form fluoride when they are mixed with water.","zh":"氟化合物與水混合時會形成氟化物。"},{"en":"To be mixed with water means to be combined with water.","zh":"be mixed with water 指與水結合。"},{"en":"Powdered medicine may be mixed with water before a child drinks it.","zh":"粉末藥物可能在兒童飲用前與水混合。"},{"en":"When chemicals are mixed with water, their concentration must be controlled.","zh":"當化學物質與水混合時，其濃度必須被控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple process of combining a substance with water.","zh":"這個短語描述把某物質與水結合的簡單過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"desired concentration","meaning":"理想濃度","examples":[{"en":"The desired concentration of fluoride is carefully controlled.","zh":"氟化物的理想濃度受到仔細控制。"},{"en":"Desired concentration means the target amount of a substance in a mixture.","zh":"desired concentration 指混合物中某物質的目標分量。"},{"en":"A nurse may check the desired concentration of disinfectant before cleaning equipment.","zh":"護士可能在清潔設備前檢查消毒劑的理想濃度。"},{"en":"If the concentration is too high, a useful substance may become harmful.","zh":"如果濃度太高，有用物質可能變得有害。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when the exact amount matters.","zh":"當準確分量很重要時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"approximately one part per million","meaning":"約百萬分之一","examples":[{"en":"The target level is approximately one part per million.","zh":"目標水平約為百萬分之一。"},{"en":"Approximately one part per million means about one unit in every million units.","zh":"approximately one part per million 指每一百萬個單位中約有一個單位。"},{"en":"Scientists use parts per million to describe very small concentrations.","zh":"科學家使用百萬分之一來描述非常低的濃度。"},{"en":"Small concentrations can still matter when many people are exposed every day.","zh":"當很多人每天接觸時，即使低濃度也可能重要。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a precise but very tiny measurement.","zh":"這個短語給出精確但非常微小的量度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"depend on","meaning":"取決於……","examples":[{"en":"The appropriate concentration may depend on the regional climate.","zh":"合適濃度可能取決於地區氣候。"},{"en":"Depend on means be affected or decided by something else.","zh":"depend on 指受某事影響或由某事決定。"},{"en":"The time needed for homework may depend on the difficulty of the task.","zh":"做功課所需時間可能取決於任務難度。"},{"en":"Water intake can depend on weather because people drink more when it is hot.","zh":"飲水量可能取決於天氣，因為天氣炎熱時人們喝更多水。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one thing changes according to another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一件事會根據另一件事而改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"regional temperature","meaning":"地區氣溫","examples":[{"en":"Regional temperature affects how much water people are likely to drink.","zh":"地區氣溫影響人們可能飲用多少水。"},{"en":"Regional temperature means the usual temperature in a particular area.","zh":"regional temperature 指某地區通常的氣溫。"},{"en":"A hot regional temperature may increase demand for air conditioning.","zh":"炎熱的地區氣溫可能增加對冷氣的需求。"},{"en":"If a region is hotter, people may drink more water and take in more fluoride.","zh":"如果某地區較熱，人們可能喝更多水並攝取更多氟化物。"},{"en":"This phrase connects local climate with human behaviour.","zh":"這個短語把本地氣候與人類行為連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hence","meaning":"因而；因此","examples":[{"en":"Hotter regions encourage greater water consumption and hence higher fluoride intake.","zh":"較炎熱地區會促使人們飲用更多水，因而攝取更多氟化物。"},{"en":"Hence means therefore or as a result.","zh":"hence 意思是因此或結果是。"},{"en":"The bus was delayed, and hence many students arrived late.","zh":"巴士延誤，因此許多學生遲到。"},{"en":"If people drink more fluoridated water, their fluoride intake may increase; hence climate matters.","zh":"如果人們飲用更多加氟食水，氟化物攝取量可能增加；因此氣候很重要。"},{"en":"This word is formal and shows cause and effect.","zh":"這個字較正式，用來表示因果關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be likely to drink","meaning":"可能會飲用","examples":[{"en":"People in warmer areas are likely to drink more water.","zh":"較暖地區的人可能會飲用更多水。"},{"en":"Be likely to drink means probably drink.","zh":"be likely to drink 指很可能會飲用。"},{"en":"Students are likely to drink more water after sports lessons.","zh":"學生在體育課後可能會飲用更多水。"},{"en":"Hot weather can make people more likely to drink frequently.","zh":"炎熱天氣可以令人更可能經常喝水。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a probable behaviour, not a certainty.","zh":"這個短語描述可能行為，而不是確定事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fluoridated water","meaning":"加氟食水","examples":[{"en":"Children who drink fluoridated water may experience less tooth decay.","zh":"飲用加氟食水的兒童可能較少蛀牙。"},{"en":"Fluoridated water is water that has fluoride added to it.","zh":"fluoridated water 指加入了氟化物的水。"},{"en":"A family may not notice fluoridated water because it looks like ordinary tap water.","zh":"家庭可能不會察覺加氟食水，因為它看起來像普通自來水。"},{"en":"Fluoridated water affects a whole community when it comes from public supplies.","zh":"當加氟食水來自公共供應時，它會影響整個社區。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to debates about dental health and public choice.","zh":"這個短語是牙齒健康和公共選擇辯論的核心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"average rate of tooth decay","meaning":"平均蛀牙率","examples":[{"en":"Some studies report a lower average rate of tooth decay among children.","zh":"有些研究報告兒童的平均蛀牙率較低。"},{"en":"The average rate of tooth decay is the usual level of tooth decay in a group.","zh":"average rate of tooth decay 指某群體中蛀牙的通常水平。"},{"en":"A dentist may compare the average rate of tooth decay between two schools.","zh":"牙醫可能比較兩間學校的平均蛀牙率。"},{"en":"A lower average rate suggests fewer dental problems across the group.","zh":"較低平均蛀牙率暗示整個群體牙齒問題較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a group pattern, not one person’s teeth.","zh":"這個短語描述群體模式，而不是某一個人的牙齒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"seem greatly reduced","meaning":"看來大幅降低","examples":[{"en":"The rate of tooth decay seems greatly reduced in some studies.","zh":"在一些研究中，蛀牙率看來大幅降低。"},{"en":"Seem greatly reduced means appear to have become much lower.","zh":"seem greatly reduced 指看起來已大幅下降。"},{"en":"After new safety rules, accidents may seem greatly reduced in school reports.","zh":"新安全規則實施後，學校報告中的意外可能看來大幅降低。"},{"en":"A result may seem reduced, but researchers still need to check the method.","zh":"結果可能看似下降，但研究者仍需檢查方法。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a strong decrease, while leaving room for interpretation.","zh":"這個短語暗示大幅減少，同時仍保留詮釋空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a typical figure claimed","meaning":"常被提出的典型數字","examples":[{"en":"A typical figure claimed is a reduction of around 50%.","zh":"常被提出的典型數字是約減少五成。"},{"en":"A typical figure claimed is a number often stated by supporters or reports.","zh":"typical figure claimed 指支持者或報告常提出的數字。"},{"en":"A company may give a typical figure claimed for energy savings in an advertisement.","zh":"公司可能在廣告中給出常被提出的節能數字。"},{"en":"Claimed figures should be checked because they may depend on method and context.","zh":"被聲稱的數字應被檢查，因為它們可能取決於方法和語境。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a commonly repeated numerical claim.","zh":"這個短語引出經常被重複的數字說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a 50% reduction","meaning":"減少五成","examples":[{"en":"Supporters often refer to a 50% reduction in tooth decay.","zh":"支持者常提到蛀牙減少五成。"},{"en":"A 50% reduction means something has been reduced by half.","zh":"a 50% reduction 指某事減少了一半。"},{"en":"A shop offering a 50% reduction sells an item at half its original price.","zh":"商店提供五成折扣時，商品以原價一半出售。"},{"en":"A 50% reduction sounds impressive, but the evidence behind it still matters.","zh":"減少五成聽起來很可觀，但背後證據仍然重要。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear numerical decrease.","zh":"這個短語給出清楚的數字減幅。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"an apparently enormous benefit","meaning":"看來非常巨大的好處","examples":[{"en":"Supporters describe the reduction as an apparently enormous benefit.","zh":"支持者把這個減幅描述為看來非常巨大的好處。"},{"en":"An apparently enormous benefit is a benefit that seems very large at first sight.","zh":"an apparently enormous benefit 指初看似乎非常巨大的好處。"},{"en":"Free public transport may appear to be an enormous benefit for low-income families.","zh":"免費公共交通對低收入家庭來說，可能看似非常巨大的好處。"},{"en":"A benefit can seem enormous, but costs and risks may still need examination.","zh":"好處可能看似巨大，但成本和風險仍可能需要檢視。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a large-looking advantage, not necessarily a final judgement.","zh":"這個短語表示看起來很大的優勢，但不一定是最終判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the major argument in favour of","meaning":"支持……的主要理據","examples":[{"en":"Reduced tooth decay is the major argument in favour of fluoridation.","zh":"減少蛀牙是支持食水加氟的主要理據。"},{"en":"The major argument in favour of something is the main reason supporting it.","zh":"the major argument in favour of something 指支持某事的主要理由。"},{"en":"Lower cost may be the major argument in favour of online meetings.","zh":"較低成本可能是支持網上會議的主要理據。"},{"en":"A policy becomes more persuasive when its major argument is easy to understand.","zh":"當政策的主要理據容易理解，它會更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the strongest supporting point.","zh":"這個短語指出最強的支持點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"grounds for opposition","meaning":"反對理由","examples":[{"en":"Critics have presented three main grounds for opposition.","zh":"批評者提出了三個主要反對理由。"},{"en":"Grounds for opposition are reasons for disagreeing with or resisting something.","zh":"grounds for opposition 指不同意或抗拒某事的理由。"},{"en":"Parents may have grounds for opposition if a school rule is unfair.","zh":"如果校規不公平，家長可能有反對理由。"},{"en":"Opposition becomes stronger when people can explain clear reasons for it.","zh":"當人們能清楚解釋理由，反對聲音會更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in debates or policy discussions.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於辯論或政策討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"opponents claim that","meaning":"反對者聲稱","examples":[{"en":"Opponents claim that the benefits of fluoridation are exaggerated.","zh":"反對者聲稱食水加氟的好處被誇大。"},{"en":"Opponents claim that means people against the idea say that something is true.","zh":"opponents claim that 指反對某想法的人聲稱某事是真實的。"},{"en":"Opponents claim that the new road will increase noise near homes.","zh":"反對者聲稱新道路會增加住宅附近噪音。"},{"en":"A claim may be challenged if evidence is weak or disputed.","zh":"如果證據薄弱或有爭議，聲稱可能受到挑戰。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the view of people who disagree with a proposal.","zh":"這個短語引出反對某建議者的觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"benefits are exaggerated","meaning":"好處被誇大","examples":[{"en":"Some critics believe that the claimed benefits are exaggerated.","zh":"有些批評者認為聲稱的好處被誇大。"},{"en":"Benefits are exaggerated means the good effects are described as larger than they really are.","zh":"benefits are exaggerated 指好處被描述得比實際更大。"},{"en":"An advertisement may exaggerate the benefits of a fitness app.","zh":"廣告可能誇大健身應用程式的好處。"},{"en":"If benefits are exaggerated, people may support a policy for the wrong reasons.","zh":"如果好處被誇大，人們可能因錯誤理由支持政策。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that positive claims may be overstated.","zh":"這個短語提醒正面說法可能被過度表述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"not firmly established","meaning":"尚未獲充分證實","examples":[{"en":"Opponents argue that the benefits are not firmly established.","zh":"反對者認為這些好處尚未獲充分證實。"},{"en":"Not firmly established means not clearly proven or accepted with strong evidence.","zh":"not firmly established 指尚未被清楚證明或以強證據接受。"},{"en":"A new teaching method may be promising but not firmly established yet.","zh":"一種新教學方法可能有前景，但尚未獲充分證實。"},{"en":"If evidence is not firmly established, people may ask for more research.","zh":"如果證據尚未充分確立，人們可能要求更多研究。"},{"en":"This phrase shows uncertainty about a claim.","zh":"這個短語顯示對某說法的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"health risks","meaning":"健康風險","examples":[{"en":"Critics have raised concerns about possible health risks.","zh":"批評者提出對潛在健康風險的憂慮。"},{"en":"Health risks are possible dangers to a person’s health.","zh":"health risks 指對人健康可能造成的危險。"},{"en":"Smoking creates serious health risks for the lungs and heart.","zh":"吸煙會對肺部和心臟造成嚴重健康風險。"},{"en":"Even small health risks can matter when a whole population is exposed.","zh":"當整個人口都接觸某物時，即使小健康風險也可能重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing possible harm to health.","zh":"這個短語用於討論對健康的可能傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"members of the population","meaning":"部分市民","examples":[{"en":"Some members of the population may be more sensitive to fluoride.","zh":"部分市民可能對氟化物較敏感。"},{"en":"Members of the population means people within a community or country.","zh":"members of the population 指一個社區或國家中的人。"},{"en":"Some members of the population may need extra healthcare support.","zh":"部分市民可能需要額外醫療支援。"},{"en":"A policy can affect different members of the population in different ways.","zh":"一項政策可以以不同方式影響不同市民。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and refers to people as part of a larger group.","zh":"這個短語較正式，把人視為較大群體的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"allergic reactions","meaning":"過敏反應","examples":[{"en":"Opponents have raised the possibility of allergic reactions.","zh":"反對者提出出現過敏反應的可能性。"},{"en":"Allergic reactions are harmful body responses to a substance.","zh":"allergic reactions 指身體對某物質產生的有害反應。"},{"en":"A child may have allergic reactions after eating peanuts.","zh":"孩子吃花生後可能出現過敏反應。"},{"en":"Allergic reactions can range from mild skin irritation to serious breathing problems.","zh":"過敏反應可以從輕微皮膚刺激到嚴重呼吸問題不等。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when the body reacts badly to something.","zh":"當身體對某物有不良反應時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"high levels of fluoride","meaning":"高水平的氟化物","examples":[{"en":"High levels of fluoride can damage the appearance of teeth.","zh":"高水平的氟化物可以損害牙齒外觀。"},{"en":"High levels of fluoride means a larger-than-normal amount of fluoride.","zh":"high levels of fluoride 指高於正常水平的氟化物分量。"},{"en":"High levels of salt in food can be unhealthy over time.","zh":"食物中高水平的鹽長遠可能不健康。"},{"en":"A substance may be helpful at low levels but harmful at high levels.","zh":"一種物質在低水平時可能有益，但在高水平時有害。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on amount and possible risk.","zh":"這個短語集中於分量和可能風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cause discolouration","meaning":"導致變色","examples":[{"en":"Excessive fluoride can cause discolouration of otherwise healthy teeth.","zh":"過量氟化物可以導致本來健康的牙齒變色。"},{"en":"To cause discolouration means to make something change to an unwanted colour.","zh":"cause discolouration 指令某物變成不想要的顏色。"},{"en":"Coffee may cause discolouration on white cups over time.","zh":"咖啡長時間可能導致白杯變色。"},{"en":"Tooth discolouration can affect appearance even if the tooth is not painful.","zh":"牙齒變色即使沒有疼痛，也可以影響外觀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visible colour change.","zh":"這個短語描述可見的顏色變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"otherwise healthy teeth","meaning":"本來健康的牙齒","examples":[{"en":"Fluorosis may affect the appearance of otherwise healthy teeth.","zh":"氟斑牙可能影響本來健康的牙齒外觀。"},{"en":"Otherwise healthy teeth are teeth that are healthy except for the problem being discussed.","zh":"otherwise healthy teeth 指除了正在討論的問題外本來健康的牙齒。"},{"en":"A child may have otherwise healthy teeth but still have white marks from fluorosis.","zh":"孩子的牙齒本來健康，但仍可能因氟斑牙有白色斑點。"},{"en":"A cosmetic problem can matter even when teeth are not decayed.","zh":"即使牙齒沒有蛀壞，外觀問題仍可能重要。"},{"en":"This phrase separates general health from one specific defect.","zh":"這個短語把整體健康與某個特定缺陷分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"proponents","meaning":"支持者","examples":[{"en":"Proponents argue that low fluoride concentrations are safe.","zh":"支持者認為低濃度氟化物是安全的。"},{"en":"Proponents are people who support an idea, plan or policy.","zh":"proponents 指支持某個想法、計劃或政策的人。"},{"en":"Proponents of school lunches say they help children eat more healthily.","zh":"學校午餐的支持者說它們幫助孩子吃得更健康。"},{"en":"Proponents often highlight benefits when defending a policy.","zh":"支持者在維護政策時常突出好處。"},{"en":"This word refers to supporters, not critics.","zh":"這個字指支持者，而不是批評者。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in such small concentrations","meaning":"在如此低的濃度下","examples":[{"en":"Supporters do not consider fluoride dangerous in such small concentrations.","zh":"支持者不認為氟化物在如此低的濃度下有危險。"},{"en":"In such small concentrations means at such low levels in a mixture.","zh":"in such small concentrations 指在混合物中處於如此低水平。"},{"en":"A medicine may be safe in small concentrations but harmful if taken in large amounts.","zh":"藥物在低濃度下可能安全，但大量服用則有害。"},{"en":"Concentration matters because the same substance can have different effects at different levels.","zh":"濃度很重要，因為同一物質在不同水平下可以有不同效果。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why supporters see the risk as low.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何支持者認為風險低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"whereas opponents disagree","meaning":"然而反對者並不同意","examples":[{"en":"Supporters consider the risk minor, whereas opponents disagree.","zh":"支持者認為風險輕微，然而反對者並不同意。"},{"en":"Whereas opponents disagree means but people against the idea do not accept that view.","zh":"whereas opponents disagree 指但反對該想法的人不接受這個看法。"},{"en":"The school says the rule is fair, whereas parents disagree.","zh":"學校說規則公平，然而家長並不同意。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly contrasts two opposing positions.","zh":"這個短語清楚對比兩個相反立場。"},{"en":"It is useful when both sides look at the same issue differently.","zh":"當雙方以不同方式看待同一問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"obtain more than","meaning":"攝取超過……","examples":[{"en":"People who drink more water may obtain more than the standard daily amount.","zh":"飲水較多的人可能攝取超過標準每日分量。"},{"en":"To obtain more than something means to receive or take in a greater amount than it.","zh":"obtain more than something 指得到或攝取比某數量更多的東西。"},{"en":"A student may obtain more than enough information from several library books.","zh":"學生可能從幾本圖書館書籍中取得超過足夠的資料。"},{"en":"People who consume more of a source may obtain more of the substance inside it.","zh":"人們攝取某來源越多，就可能攝取更多其中所含物質。"},{"en":"This phrase compares actual intake with a standard amount.","zh":"這個短語把實際攝取量與標準分量作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"standard daily intake","meaning":"標準每日攝取量","examples":[{"en":"Water consumption affects a person’s standard daily fluoride intake.","zh":"飲水量影響一個人的標準每日氟化物攝取量。"},{"en":"Standard daily intake is the usual recommended amount taken in each day.","zh":"standard daily intake 指每天通常建議攝取的分量。"},{"en":"Nutrition labels may show standard daily intake for vitamins and minerals.","zh":"營養標籤可能顯示維他命和礦物質的標準每日攝取量。"},{"en":"If people drink more water, their actual intake may exceed the standard amount.","zh":"如果人們飲用更多水，實際攝取量可能超過標準分量。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in health and nutrition discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於健康和營養討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"an infringement on individual rights","meaning":"對個人權利的侵犯","examples":[{"en":"Some people regard fluoridation as an infringement on individual rights.","zh":"有些人把食水加氟視為對個人權利的侵犯。"},{"en":"An infringement on individual rights is an action that limits personal freedom unfairly.","zh":"an infringement on individual rights 指不公平地限制個人自由的行為。"},{"en":"A rule that searches students’ bags without reason may be seen as an infringement on rights.","zh":"無理由搜查學生書包的規則可能被視為對權利的侵犯。"},{"en":"People object when they feel a policy removes personal choice.","zh":"當人們覺得政策剝奪個人選擇時，就會反對。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in legal, political and ethical debate.","zh":"這個短語用於法律、政治和倫理辯論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"individual rights","meaning":"個人權利","examples":[{"en":"The debate raises important questions about individual rights.","zh":"這場辯論提出了關於個人權利的重要問題。"},{"en":"Individual rights are freedoms and protections belonging to each person.","zh":"individual rights 指屬於每個人的自由和保障。"},{"en":"Privacy is an individual right that schools and employers should respect.","zh":"私隱是學校和僱主應尊重的個人權利。"},{"en":"Public health policies may create tension between safety and individual rights.","zh":"公共衛生政策可能在安全與個人權利之間造成張力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what each person should be free to choose or refuse.","zh":"這個短語集中於每個人應能自由選擇或拒絕甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"compulsory medication","meaning":"強制用藥","examples":[{"en":"Opponents describe fluoridation as compulsory medication of an entire community.","zh":"反對者把食水加氟描述為對整個社區強制用藥。"},{"en":"Compulsory medication means people receive a medical substance without individual choice.","zh":"compulsory medication 指人們在沒有個人選擇下接受醫療物質。"},{"en":"Some parents object to compulsory medication because they want to decide for their children.","zh":"有些家長反對強制用藥，因為他們想為孩子作決定。"},{"en":"A public measure feels compulsory when people cannot easily opt out.","zh":"當人們不能輕易退出，公共措施就會感覺像強制。"},{"en":"This phrase is used by critics who see fluoridation as forced treatment.","zh":"這個短語由把食水加氟視為強制治療的批評者使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"all members of a community","meaning":"社區所有成員","examples":[{"en":"Fluoridated water reaches all members of a community.","zh":"加氟食水會到達社區所有成員。"},{"en":"All members of a community means every person living in that community.","zh":"all members of a community 指住在該社區的每一個人。"},{"en":"A public warning should reach all members of a community during a storm.","zh":"風暴期間，公共警告應傳達給社區所有成員。"},{"en":"Community-wide policies matter because they affect children, adults and older people together.","zh":"全社區政策很重要，因為它同時影響兒童、成年人和長者。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that nobody in the group is excluded.","zh":"這個短語強調群體中沒有人被排除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have important implications","meaning":"有重要影響","examples":[{"en":"The fluoridation issue has important implications for public policy.","zh":"食水加氟問題對公共政策有重要影響。"},{"en":"To have important implications means to have serious effects or meanings for something else.","zh":"have important implications 指對另一件事有嚴重影響或意義。"},{"en":"A new exam system may have important implications for teachers and students.","zh":"新考試制度可能對老師和學生有重要影響。"},{"en":"If a policy affects personal choice, it has implications beyond simple health results.","zh":"如果政策影響個人選擇，它的影響就超越簡單健康結果。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an issue matters in a wider way.","zh":"這個短語顯示某議題有更廣泛的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"according to the experts","meaning":"根據專家所說","examples":[{"en":"According to the experts, fluoridation may be both beneficial and safe.","zh":"根據專家所說，食水加氟可能既有益又安全。"},{"en":"According to the experts means as specialists say or judge.","zh":"according to the experts 指根據專家的說法或判斷。"},{"en":"According to the experts, the old bridge needs urgent repair.","zh":"根據專家所說，舊橋需要緊急維修。"},{"en":"Expert opinion can guide decisions, but people may still debate values and risks.","zh":"專家意見可以指導決定，但人們仍可能辯論價值和風險。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the source of a claim.","zh":"這個短語指出某說法的來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"unquestionably beneficial","meaning":"毫無疑問有益的","examples":[{"en":"Some authorities present fluoridation as unquestionably beneficial.","zh":"有些權威機構把食水加氟呈現為毫無疑問有益的。"},{"en":"Unquestionably beneficial means clearly helpful and not needing doubt or debate.","zh":"unquestionably beneficial 指明顯有幫助，不需要懷疑或辯論。"},{"en":"Clean drinking water is unquestionably beneficial for public health.","zh":"清潔食水對公共健康毫無疑問有益。"},{"en":"Calling a policy unquestionably beneficial may silence people who still have concerns.","zh":"把政策稱為毫無疑問有益，可能使仍有疑慮的人被壓下去。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses very strong confidence in a benefit.","zh":"這個短語表達對好處非常強的信心。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"non-hazardous measure","meaning":"無害的措施","examples":[{"en":"Supporters regard fluoridation as a non-hazardous public-health measure.","zh":"支持者把食水加氟視為一項無害的公共衛生措施。"},{"en":"A non-hazardous measure is an action that is not considered dangerous.","zh":"non-hazardous measure 指被認為沒有危險的行動。"},{"en":"Washing hands is a non-hazardous measure that reduces infection risk.","zh":"洗手是減少感染風險的無害措施。"},{"en":"A measure may be accepted more easily if people believe it is safe.","zh":"如果人們相信措施安全，它可能較容易被接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an intervention seen as low-risk.","zh":"這個短語描述被視為低風險的干預措施。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the wisdom of doing something","meaning":"做某事是否明智","examples":[{"en":"The writer questions the wisdom of leaving a technical issue entirely to a public vote.","zh":"作者質疑把技術問題完全交由公眾投票決定是否明智。"},{"en":"The wisdom of doing something means whether doing it is sensible or wise.","zh":"the wisdom of doing something 指做某事是否合理或明智。"},{"en":"A parent may question the wisdom of giving a young child a smartphone.","zh":"家長可能質疑給年幼孩子智能手機是否明智。"},{"en":"People question wisdom when an action may create serious consequences.","zh":"當一項行動可能造成嚴重後果，人們會質疑其明智程度。"},{"en":"This phrase invites careful judgement, not just personal preference.","zh":"這個短語邀請謹慎判斷，而不只是個人喜好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"allow the public to vote on","meaning":"讓公眾就……投票","examples":[{"en":"Some communities allow the public to vote on fluoridation.","zh":"有些社區讓公眾就食水加氟投票。"},{"en":"To allow the public to vote on something means to let citizens decide it by voting.","zh":"allow the public to vote on something 指讓市民透過投票決定某事。"},{"en":"A town may allow the public to vote on a new library project.","zh":"城鎮可能讓公眾就新圖書館項目投票。"},{"en":"Public votes can give legitimacy, but voters may need clear information first.","zh":"公眾投票可以帶來合法性，但選民可能首先需要清楚資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase connects policy decisions with democratic participation.","zh":"這個短語把政策決定與民主參與連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"reject a measure","meaning":"否決一項措施","examples":[{"en":"Voters may choose to reject a public-health measure.","zh":"選民可能選擇否決一項公共衛生措施。"},{"en":"To reject a measure means to refuse or vote against a proposed action.","zh":"reject a measure 指拒絕或投票反對一項建議行動。"},{"en":"Residents may reject a parking plan if it removes too many spaces.","zh":"如果泊車計劃取消太多車位，居民可能否決它。"},{"en":"A measure may be rejected when people doubt its safety, cost or fairness.","zh":"當人們懷疑措施的安全、成本或公平性時，它可能被否決。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in policy and voting contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於政策和投票語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"must be questioned","meaning":"必須受到質疑","examples":[{"en":"The assumption that experts alone should decide policy must also be questioned.","zh":"專家單獨決定政策的假設也必須受到質疑。"},{"en":"Must be questioned means should not be accepted without careful examination.","zh":"must be questioned 指不應未經仔細檢視就接受。"},{"en":"A school rule must be questioned if it punishes students unfairly.","zh":"如果校規不公平懲罰學生，就必須受到質疑。"},{"en":"Questioning an assumption helps reveal hidden values or weak evidence.","zh":"質疑假設有助揭示隱藏價值觀或薄弱證據。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages critical thinking.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵批判思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"scientific aspects of","meaning":"……的科學層面","examples":[{"en":"Many studies focus mainly on the scientific aspects of the controversy.","zh":"許多研究主要集中於這場爭議的科學層面。"},{"en":"Scientific aspects of an issue are the parts related to evidence, experiments and data.","zh":"scientific aspects of an issue 指與證據、實驗和數據有關的部分。"},{"en":"A climate lesson may focus on the scientific aspects of rising temperatures.","zh":"氣候課可能集中於氣溫上升的科學層面。"},{"en":"Looking only at scientific aspects may miss social or ethical questions.","zh":"只看科學層面可能忽略社會或倫理問題。"},{"en":"This phrase separates science-related issues from other dimensions.","zh":"這個短語把科學相關問題與其他層面分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"assume that","meaning":"假設","examples":[{"en":"Earlier research often assumed that the science was unproblematic.","zh":"早期研究常假設科學方面沒有問題。"},{"en":"To assume that means to accept something as true without fully proving it.","zh":"assume that 指在未完全證明下接受某事為真。"},{"en":"A teacher should not assume that quiet students understand everything.","zh":"老師不應假設安靜學生明白一切。"},{"en":"Wrong assumptions can lead to weak conclusions.","zh":"錯誤假設可以導致薄弱結論。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a belief is taken as a starting point.","zh":"這個短語用於某個信念被視為出發點時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be unproblematic","meaning":"沒有問題的","examples":[{"en":"The scientific evidence should not automatically be treated as unproblematic.","zh":"科學證據不應自動被視為沒有問題。"},{"en":"To be unproblematic means to have no obvious difficulty, doubt or complication.","zh":"be unproblematic 指沒有明顯困難、疑問或複雜之處。"},{"en":"A school policy may look unproblematic until students explain how it affects them.","zh":"校規可能看似沒有問題，直到學生解釋它如何影響他們。"},{"en":"Evidence is not unproblematic if methods or interpretations are disputed.","zh":"如果方法或詮釋有爭議，證據就不是沒有問題的。"},{"en":"This phrase means “not causing problems”, but it is often used critically.","zh":"這個短語意思是「不造成問題」，但常帶批判意味。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"exclude something from","meaning":"把……排除在……之外","examples":[{"en":"Some studies excluded scientific knowledge from sociological examination.","zh":"有些研究把科學知識排除在社會學分析之外。"},{"en":"To exclude something from something else means to leave it out.","zh":"exclude something from something else 指把某物排除在另一範圍之外。"},{"en":"A teacher should not exclude weaker students from class discussion.","zh":"老師不應把較弱學生排除在課堂討論之外。"},{"en":"If research excludes social values, it may miss why people disagree.","zh":"如果研究排除社會價值觀，可能錯過人們分歧的原因。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is deliberately or effectively left outside.","zh":"這個短語顯示某物被有意或實際上放在外面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sociological examination","meaning":"社會學分析","examples":[{"en":"Scientific controversies can also be subjected to sociological examination.","zh":"科學爭議也可以接受社會學分析。"},{"en":"Sociological examination means studying something by looking at society, groups and values.","zh":"sociological examination 指從社會、群體和價值觀角度研究某事。"},{"en":"A sociological examination of education may ask how family income affects success.","zh":"對教育的社會學分析可能會問家庭收入如何影響成功。"},{"en":"This kind of examination can reveal power, trust and public disagreement.","zh":"這類分析可以揭示權力、信任和公眾分歧。"},{"en":"This phrase treats a topic as a social issue, not only a technical one.","zh":"這個短語把某主題視為社會議題，而不只是技術議題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the traditional view of science","meaning":"傳統科學觀","examples":[{"en":"The traditional view of science emphasises objectivity and formal methods.","zh":"傳統科學觀強調客觀性和正式方法。"},{"en":"The traditional view of science is the idea that science is mainly objective and rule-based.","zh":"traditional view of science 指科學主要是客觀和按規則運作的想法。"},{"en":"In school, students often first learn the traditional view of science through experiments.","zh":"在學校，學生常透過實驗最先學到傳統科學觀。"},{"en":"This view may overlook how people and institutions shape research.","zh":"這種觀點可能忽視人和制度如何塑造研究。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an older understanding of how science works.","zh":"這個短語引出對科學如何運作的較舊理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a special kind of knowledge","meaning":"一種特殊知識","examples":[{"en":"Science is often treated as a special kind of knowledge.","zh":"科學常被視為一種特殊知識。"},{"en":"A special kind of knowledge means knowledge seen as different from ordinary opinion.","zh":"a special kind of knowledge 指被視為不同於普通意見的知識。"},{"en":"Medical knowledge is often treated as special because it requires training and evidence.","zh":"醫學知識常被視為特殊，因為它需要訓練和證據。"},{"en":"Treating science as special can increase trust, but may also reduce public questioning.","zh":"把科學視為特殊可以增加信任，但也可能減少公眾質疑。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the status given to scientific knowledge.","zh":"這個短語突出科學知識被賦予的地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be established through","meaning":"透過……建立","examples":[{"en":"Scientific claims are expected to be established through reliable methods.","zh":"科學主張被期望透過可靠方法確立。"},{"en":"To be established through something means to be proven or built by using that process.","zh":"be established through something 指透過某過程被證明或建立。"},{"en":"A school rule should be established through discussion and clear evidence.","zh":"校規應透過討論和清楚證據建立。"},{"en":"Knowledge becomes stronger when it is established through careful testing.","zh":"當知識透過仔細測試建立，它會變得更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the method by which something gains support.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事取得支持的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"scientific methods","meaning":"科學方法","examples":[{"en":"Researchers use scientific methods to test hypotheses.","zh":"研究者使用科學方法測試假設。"},{"en":"Scientific methods are organised ways of collecting evidence and testing ideas.","zh":"scientific methods 指有組織地收集證據和測試想法的方法。"},{"en":"Students use scientific methods when they compare plant growth under different light levels.","zh":"學生比較植物在不同光線下的生長時，就是使用科學方法。"},{"en":"Good methods reduce guesswork and make results more reliable.","zh":"良好方法可以減少猜測，令結果更可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the procedures used in scientific inquiry.","zh":"這個短語指科學探究中使用的程序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be objectively applied","meaning":"被客觀地應用","examples":[{"en":"Scientific procedures are supposed to be objectively applied.","zh":"科學程序理應被客觀地應用。"},{"en":"To be objectively applied means to be used fairly without personal bias.","zh":"be objectively applied 指在沒有個人偏見下公平使用。"},{"en":"Exam rules should be objectively applied to every student.","zh":"考試規則應被客觀地應用於每個學生。"},{"en":"If methods are not objectively applied, results may favour one side unfairly.","zh":"如果方法沒有被客觀應用，結果可能不公平地偏向一方。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses fairness and neutrality in practice.","zh":"這個短語強調實踐中的公平和中立。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"scientific community","meaning":"科學界","examples":[{"en":"Members of the scientific community evaluate research findings.","zh":"科學界成員評估研究結果。"},{"en":"The scientific community is the group of scientists working in related fields.","zh":"scientific community 指在相關領域工作的科學家群體。"},{"en":"The scientific community may review a new study before accepting its results.","zh":"科學界可能在接受新研究結果前先審查它。"},{"en":"Debate within the scientific community can improve weak research.","zh":"科學界內的辯論可以改善薄弱研究。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to scientists as a professional group.","zh":"這個短語把科學家視為專業群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in recent years","meaning":"近年","examples":[{"en":"In recent years, sociologists have challenged traditional ideas about science.","zh":"近年，社會學家挑戰了關於科學的傳統觀念。"},{"en":"In recent years means during the last few years or modern period.","zh":"in recent years 指在過去幾年或近代時期。"},{"en":"In recent years, many schools have used more online learning tools.","zh":"近年，許多學校使用更多網上學習工具。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a change that has happened not long ago.","zh":"這個短語引出不久前發生的變化。"},{"en":"It helps compare newer developments with older views.","zh":"它幫助把較新的發展與較舊觀點作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a major challenge to","meaning":"對……的重大挑戰","examples":[{"en":"The sociology of science presents a major challenge to the traditional view.","zh":"科學社會學對傳統觀點提出重大挑戰。"},{"en":"A major challenge to something is a serious questioning of it.","zh":"a major challenge to something 指對某事的嚴重質疑。"},{"en":"Online shopping created a major challenge to small local shops.","zh":"網上購物對本地小店構成重大挑戰。"},{"en":"A challenge becomes major when it forces people to rethink old assumptions.","zh":"當挑戰迫使人重新思考舊假設，它就變得重大。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong pressure against an established idea.","zh":"這個短語顯示對既有想法的強大壓力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sociology of science","meaning":"科學社會學","examples":[{"en":"The sociology of science examines how social forces shape knowledge.","zh":"科學社會學研究社會力量如何塑造知識。"},{"en":"Sociology of science is the study of how science is affected by society and institutions.","zh":"sociology of science 指研究科學如何受社會和制度影響的學科。"},{"en":"A sociologist may study how funding affects research priorities.","zh":"社會學家可能研究資金如何影響研究優先次序。"},{"en":"This field asks how values, careers and communities influence scientific work.","zh":"這個領域會問價值觀、職業和社群如何影響科學工作。"},{"en":"This phrase treats science as a human activity as well as a method of inquiry.","zh":"這個短語把科學視為人類活動，也視為探究方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"scientific knowledge","meaning":"科學知識","examples":[{"en":"Scientific knowledge is produced and evaluated by human communities.","zh":"科學知識由人類社群生產和評估。"},{"en":"Scientific knowledge is knowledge developed through research, evidence and testing.","zh":"scientific knowledge 指透過研究、證據和測試發展出來的知識。"},{"en":"Doctors rely on scientific knowledge when choosing treatments for patients.","zh":"醫生為病人選擇治療時依靠科學知識。"},{"en":"Scientific knowledge can change when new evidence appears.","zh":"當新證據出現時，科學知識可以改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to knowledge accepted or debated within science.","zh":"這個短語指在科學內被接受或辯論的知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be socially negotiated","meaning":"經社會協商形成","examples":[{"en":"Scientific knowledge may be socially negotiated rather than purely objective.","zh":"科學知識可能是經社會協商形成，而非純粹客觀。"},{"en":"To be socially negotiated means to be shaped through discussion, agreement and disagreement among people.","zh":"be socially negotiated 指透過人與人之間的討論、同意和分歧被塑造。"},{"en":"School rules are socially negotiated when teachers, parents and students all influence them.","zh":"當老師、家長和學生都影響校規時，校規就是經社會協商形成。"},{"en":"Knowledge may be negotiated when evidence needs interpretation by a community.","zh":"當證據需要由社群詮釋時，知識可能經協商形成。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that social interaction can shape what is accepted.","zh":"這個短語顯示社會互動可以塑造被接受的內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be inevitably linked to","meaning":"無可避免地與……相連","examples":[{"en":"Scientific judgements may be inevitably linked to social values.","zh":"科學判斷可能無可避免地與社會價值觀相連。"},{"en":"Inevitably linked to something means unable to be separated from it.","zh":"inevitably linked to something 指無法與某事分開。"},{"en":"Housing policy is inevitably linked to income and family needs.","zh":"住房政策無可避免地與收入和家庭需要相連。"},{"en":"If decisions affect people, they are often linked to values as well as facts.","zh":"如果決定影響人，它們常與價值觀以及事實相連。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses an unavoidable connection.","zh":"這個短語強調不可避免的關聯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"relevant parties","meaning":"相關人士","examples":[{"en":"The values of all relevant parties may affect a scientific controversy.","zh":"所有相關人士的價值觀都可能影響科學爭議。"},{"en":"Relevant parties are the people or groups connected to an issue.","zh":"relevant parties 指與某議題有關的人或群體。"},{"en":"In a school dispute, relevant parties may include students, parents and teachers.","zh":"在學校爭議中，相關人士可能包括學生、家長和老師。"},{"en":"Decisions are fairer when all relevant parties have a chance to speak.","zh":"當所有相關人士都有機會發言，決定會更公平。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies everyone whose interests or views matter.","zh":"這個短語指出所有利益或觀點重要的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"scientists and non-scientists","meaning":"科學家及非科學界人士","examples":[{"en":"Both scientists and non-scientists participate in public debates about science.","zh":"科學家及非科學界人士都參與關於科學的公共辯論。"},{"en":"Scientists and non-scientists means experts and people outside professional science.","zh":"scientists and non-scientists 指專家和專業科學以外的人。"},{"en":"A hospital policy may be discussed by doctors, patients and ordinary residents.","zh":"醫院政策可能由醫生、病人和普通居民討論。"},{"en":"Public science debates involve non-scientists because policies affect their lives too.","zh":"公共科學辯論涉及非科學界人士，因為政策也影響他們的生活。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that science-related decisions are not only for experts.","zh":"這個短語強調與科學有關的決定不只是專家的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be exempt from","meaning":"不受……約束；獲豁免於……","examples":[{"en":"Scientific knowledge should not be exempt from social inquiry.","zh":"科學知識不應免於社會學探究。"},{"en":"To be exempt from something means to be free from a rule, duty or examination.","zh":"be exempt from something 指不受某規則、責任或審查約束。"},{"en":"A student may be exempt from PE because of a medical condition.","zh":"學生可能因醫療狀況獲豁免上體育課。"},{"en":"If science is not exempt from inquiry, its social influences can be examined.","zh":"如果科學不免於探究，其社會影響就可以被檢視。"},{"en":"This phrase means something is not subject to a normal requirement.","zh":"這個短語指某物不受一般要求限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"social inquiry","meaning":"社會學探究","examples":[{"en":"The sociology of science subjects scientific claims to social inquiry.","zh":"科學社會學把科學主張置於社會學探究之下。"},{"en":"Social inquiry means investigation into society, relationships and human values.","zh":"social inquiry 指對社會、關係和人類價值觀的研究。"},{"en":"A social inquiry into poverty may examine wages, housing and education.","zh":"對貧窮的社會學探究可能檢視工資、住屋和教育。"},{"en":"Social inquiry helps explain why people respond differently to the same evidence.","zh":"社會學探究有助解釋為何人們對同一證據有不同反應。"},{"en":"This phrase studies the human context around an issue.","zh":"這個短語研究議題周圍的人類語境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"develop as an orderly process","meaning":"以有序過程發展","examples":[{"en":"Scientific knowledge does not always develop as an orderly process.","zh":"科學知識不一定總是以有序過程發展。"},{"en":"To develop as an orderly process means to grow in a smooth, clear and step-by-step way.","zh":"develop as an orderly process 指以順暢、清楚和逐步的方式發展。"},{"en":"A project rarely develops as an orderly process if people keep changing the plan.","zh":"如果人們不斷改變計劃，項目很少會以有序過程發展。"},{"en":"Scientific change may be messy because evidence and interpretation shift over time.","zh":"科學變化可能混亂，因為證據和詮釋會隨時間轉變。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts smooth progress with fragmented change.","zh":"這個短語把順暢進展與零散變化作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be characterised by","meaning":"具有……的特點","examples":[{"en":"Kuhn argued that science is characterised by periodic revolutions.","zh":"Kuhn 認為科學具有週期性重大變革的特點。"},{"en":"To be characterised by something means to have it as a typical feature.","zh":"be characterised by something 指以某物作為典型特徵。"},{"en":"A good classroom is characterised by clear rules and active discussion.","zh":"好課室具有清楚規則和積極討論的特點。"},{"en":"A period of change may be characterised by uncertainty and debate.","zh":"變革時期可能具有不確定和辯論的特點。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main features of something.","zh":"這個短語指出某事物的主要特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"periodic revolutions","meaning":"週期性的重大變革","examples":[{"en":"Scientific development may involve periodic revolutions in thought.","zh":"科學發展可能涉及思想上的週期性重大變革。"},{"en":"Periodic revolutions are major changes that happen from time to time.","zh":"periodic revolutions 指不時發生的重大變化。"},{"en":"Technology industries may experience periodic revolutions when new tools change daily life.","zh":"當新工具改變日常生活，科技行業可能經歷週期性重大變革。"},{"en":"A revolution in thinking can replace old methods with new ones.","zh":"思維上的重大變革可以以新方法取代舊方法。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests repeated but not constant dramatic change.","zh":"這個短語暗示反覆但非持續不斷的劇烈變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"methods of study","meaning":"研究方法","examples":[{"en":"Scientific revolutions can change accepted methods of study.","zh":"科學革命可以改變被接受的研究方法。"},{"en":"Methods of study are the ways people investigate or learn about a subject.","zh":"methods of study 指人們研究或學習某主題的方法。"},{"en":"A student’s methods of study may include reading, testing and summarising notes.","zh":"學生的學習方法可能包括閱讀、測試和總結筆記。"},{"en":"Better methods can produce more reliable answers.","zh":"更好的方法可以產生更可靠的答案。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how research or learning is carried out.","zh":"這個短語集中於研究或學習如何進行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"assessment criteria","meaning":"評估準則","examples":[{"en":"Researchers may change their assessment criteria during a scientific revolution.","zh":"研究者可能在科學革命期間改變評估準則。"},{"en":"Assessment criteria are standards used to judge quality, success or truth.","zh":"assessment criteria 指用來判斷質素、成功或真實性的標準。"},{"en":"Teachers use assessment criteria to mark essays fairly.","zh":"老師使用評估準則公平批改作文。"},{"en":"If criteria change, the same evidence may be judged differently.","zh":"如果準則改變，同一證據可能被不同地評估。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how evaluation is done.","zh":"這個短語適合解釋評估如何進行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in a fragmented way","meaning":"以零散的方式","examples":[{"en":"Scientific change may occur in a fragmented rather than orderly way.","zh":"科學變化可能以零散而非有序的方式發生。"},{"en":"In a fragmented way means in separate, uneven or disconnected pieces.","zh":"in a fragmented way 指以分散、不均或不連貫的部分發生。"},{"en":"A group project may develop in a fragmented way if members do not communicate.","zh":"如果組員不溝通，小組項目可能以零散方式發展。"},{"en":"Fragmented change can make progress difficult to follow.","zh":"零散變化會令人難以跟進進展。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts messy development with smooth progress.","zh":"這個短語把混亂發展與順暢進步作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a shift from one way of thinking to another","meaning":"從一種思維方式轉向另一種","examples":[{"en":"A scientific revolution involves a shift from one way of thinking to another.","zh":"科學革命涉及從一種思維方式轉向另一種。"},{"en":"A shift from one way of thinking to another is a major change in viewpoint.","zh":"a shift from one way of thinking to another 指觀點上的重大改變。"},{"en":"A student may shift from memorising grammar to understanding patterns.","zh":"學生可能從死記文法轉向理解模式。"},{"en":"Such shifts happen when old explanations no longer work well.","zh":"當舊解釋不再有效，這類轉變就會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change in mindset, not just a change in details.","zh":"這個短語描述心態改變，而不只是細節改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not solely on the basis of","meaning":"並非純粹基於……","examples":[{"en":"Scientific change is not made solely on the basis of formal rules.","zh":"科學變化並非純粹基於正式規則而作出。"},{"en":"Not solely on the basis of means not only because of one factor.","zh":"not solely on the basis of 指並非只因一個因素。"},{"en":"A school should not choose students solely on the basis of exam scores.","zh":"學校不應純粹基於考試成績選學生。"},{"en":"Decisions may include evidence, values, experience and practical needs.","zh":"決定可能包括證據、價值觀、經驗和實際需要。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against explaining something by one factor alone.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要只用單一因素解釋某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"clear rules","meaning":"清晰規則","examples":[{"en":"Scientific decisions cannot always be reduced to clear rules.","zh":"科學決定不一定總能簡化為清晰規則。"},{"en":"Clear rules are simple, understandable standards for what should be done.","zh":"clear rules 指關於應做甚麼的簡單、易明標準。"},{"en":"A classroom needs clear rules about phones, homework and respect.","zh":"課室需要關於手機、功課和尊重的清晰規則。"},{"en":"Some situations are too complex to be solved by clear rules alone.","zh":"有些情況太複雜，不能單靠清晰規則解決。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rules that people can easily understand and follow.","zh":"這個短語描述人們容易理解和遵守的規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"formal scientific practice","meaning":"正式科學實踐","examples":[{"en":"Social influences may operate alongside formal scientific practice.","zh":"社會影響可能與正式科學實踐同時運作。"},{"en":"Formal scientific practice means organised scientific work using accepted methods and procedures.","zh":"formal scientific practice 指使用被接受方法和程序的有組織科學工作。"},{"en":"Laboratory records are part of formal scientific practice.","zh":"實驗室記錄是正式科學實踐的一部分。"},{"en":"Social values can influence research even when formal methods are used.","zh":"即使使用正式方法，社會價值觀仍可影響研究。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the official procedures of doing science.","zh":"這個短語指進行科學的官方程序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"include social factors","meaning":"包括社會因素","examples":[{"en":"The acceptance of a theory may include social factors.","zh":"一個理論被接受可能包括社會因素。"},{"en":"To include social factors means to involve influences such as values, institutions or group interests.","zh":"include social factors 指涉及價值觀、制度或群體利益等影響。"},{"en":"A school’s success may include social factors like family support and neighbourhood safety.","zh":"學校成功可能包括家庭支援和社區安全等社會因素。"},{"en":"If social factors matter, evidence alone may not explain a decision fully.","zh":"如果社會因素重要，單靠證據可能不能完全解釋決定。"},{"en":"This phrase adds human and community influences to an explanation.","zh":"這個短語把人和社群影響加入解釋中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"develop a full analysis of","meaning":"對……作出完整分析","examples":[{"en":"Kuhn did not develop a full analysis of those social factors.","zh":"Kuhn 沒有對那些社會因素作出完整分析。"},{"en":"To develop a full analysis of something means to examine it completely and systematically.","zh":"develop a full analysis of something 指完整而有系統地研究某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may develop a full analysis of why students failed a test.","zh":"老師可能完整分析學生測驗失敗的原因。"},{"en":"Without full analysis, important causes may remain hidden.","zh":"如果沒有完整分析，重要原因可能仍然被隱藏。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful and complete explanation.","zh":"這個短語暗示仔細而完整的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take a concept further","meaning":"進一步發展一個概念","examples":[{"en":"Collins took Kuhn’s concept further by examining experimental interpretation.","zh":"Collins 透過研究實驗詮釋，進一步發展 Kuhn 的概念。"},{"en":"To take a concept further means to develop an idea in more detail or apply it more widely.","zh":"take a concept further 指更詳細地發展一個想法，或更廣泛地應用它。"},{"en":"A student may take a class idea further by testing it in a project.","zh":"學生可能透過專題測試課堂概念，進一步發展該想法。"},{"en":"Ideas develop when later thinkers extend earlier work.","zh":"後來思想家延伸早期工作時，想法就會發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes building on someone else’s idea.","zh":"這個短語描述在他人想法上繼續建構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"assert that","meaning":"斷言","examples":[{"en":"Collins asserted that experimental results do not explain themselves.","zh":"Collins 斷言實驗結果不會自己解釋自己。"},{"en":"To assert that means to state something firmly as true.","zh":"assert that 指堅定地聲稱某事為真。"},{"en":"A manager may assert that safety must come before speed.","zh":"經理可能斷言安全必須先於速度。"},{"en":"Strong assertions still need evidence if others disagree.","zh":"如果他人不同意，強烈斷言仍需要證據。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a confident claim.","zh":"這個短語引出自信的主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the outcome of an experiment","meaning":"實驗結果","examples":[{"en":"The outcome of an experiment may require extensive interpretation.","zh":"實驗結果可能需要大量詮釋。"},{"en":"The outcome of an experiment is the result produced by the experiment.","zh":"outcome of an experiment 指實驗產生的結果。"},{"en":"Students record the outcome of an experiment after changing one variable.","zh":"學生改變一個變量後記錄實驗結果。"},{"en":"A result may not be meaningful until researchers interpret it carefully.","zh":"結果可能要到研究者仔細詮釋後才有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what the experiment produces.","zh":"這個短語集中於實驗產生了甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be immediately comprehended","meaning":"立即被理解","examples":[{"en":"The meaning of a result may not be immediately comprehended.","zh":"結果的意義可能不會立即被理解。"},{"en":"To be immediately comprehended means to be understood at once.","zh":"be immediately comprehended 指立刻被明白。"},{"en":"A difficult graph may not be immediately comprehended by students.","zh":"困難圖表可能不會立即被學生理解。"},{"en":"Complex results need discussion before people understand what they mean.","zh":"複雜結果需要討論，人們才理解其意思。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that understanding may take time.","zh":"這個短語顯示理解可能需要時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be open to interpretation","meaning":"可有不同詮釋","examples":[{"en":"Experimental evidence is often open to interpretation.","zh":"實驗證據常可有不同詮釋。"},{"en":"To be open to interpretation means it can be understood in more than one way.","zh":"be open to interpretation 指可以用多於一種方式理解。"},{"en":"A short message like “fine” may be open to interpretation.","zh":"像 “fine” 這樣的短訊可能可有不同詮釋。"},{"en":"Evidence becomes controversial when different groups interpret it differently.","zh":"當不同群體不同地詮釋證據，證據就會具爭議。"},{"en":"This phrase signals uncertainty or multiple possible meanings.","zh":"這個短語表示不確定或有多種可能意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"discussion between scientists","meaning":"科學家之間的討論","examples":[{"en":"Scientific meaning may emerge through discussion between scientists.","zh":"科學意義可能透過科學家之間的討論出現。"},{"en":"Discussion between scientists means scientists talking, debating and comparing interpretations.","zh":"discussion between scientists 指科學家交談、辯論和比較詮釋。"},{"en":"Researchers may discuss unclear results before publishing a paper.","zh":"研究者可能在發表論文前討論不清楚的結果。"},{"en":"Scientific meaning can become clearer when experts challenge one another’s ideas.","zh":"當專家互相挑戰想法，科學意義可以變得更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights science as a shared conversation.","zh":"這個短語突出科學是一種共同對話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"reinterpretation","meaning":"重新詮釋","examples":[{"en":"New evidence may lead to the reinterpretation of earlier results.","zh":"新證據可能導致對早期結果的重新詮釋。"},{"en":"Reinterpretation means understanding something again in a new way.","zh":"reinterpretation 指以新方式再次理解某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may encourage reinterpretation of a poem after students learn its history.","zh":"學生了解詩的歷史後，老師可能鼓勵他們重新詮釋詩。"},{"en":"New information can make old evidence look different.","zh":"新資訊可以令舊證據看起來不同。"},{"en":"This word describes a change in meaning, not a change in the original facts.","zh":"這個字描述意義上的改變，而不是原始事實的改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the light of","meaning":"按照；鑑於","examples":[{"en":"Researchers reinterpret findings in the light of later experiments.","zh":"研究者按照後來實驗重新詮釋研究結果。"},{"en":"In the light of means considering new information or evidence.","zh":"in the light of 指考慮到新資訊或證據。"},{"en":"A teacher may change a lesson plan in the light of students’ test results.","zh":"老師可能鑑於學生測驗結果改變教案。"},{"en":"New evidence can change how people understand earlier events.","zh":"新證據可以改變人們對早前事件的理解。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the reason for rethinking something.","zh":"這個短語引出重新思考某事的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"traditional distinctions between","meaning":"……之間的傳統區分","examples":[{"en":"The analysis challenges traditional distinctions between facts and theories.","zh":"該分析挑戰事實與理論之間的傳統區分。"},{"en":"Traditional distinctions between two things are old accepted ways of separating them.","zh":"traditional distinctions between two things 指把兩者分開的舊有公認方式。"},{"en":"The distinction between work and home has become less clear with remote work.","zh":"隨著遙距工作，工作與家庭之間的區分變得不那麼清楚。"},{"en":"Old categories may weaken when real situations become more complicated.","zh":"當真實情況變得更複雜，舊分類可能減弱。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how concepts are separated.","zh":"這個短語集中於概念如何被分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"facts and theories","meaning":"事實與理論","examples":[{"en":"It may be difficult to maintain a strict separation between facts and theories.","zh":"要在事實與理論之間保持嚴格分隔可能很困難。"},{"en":"Facts and theories are evidence-based observations and explanations of those observations.","zh":"facts and theories 指以證據為基礎的觀察，以及對那些觀察的解釋。"},{"en":"In science class, students learn facts and theories about gravity.","zh":"在科學課中，學生學習關於重力的事實與理論。"},{"en":"Theories help people organise facts into meaningful explanations.","zh":"理論幫助人把事實組織成有意義的解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing scientific knowledge.","zh":"這個短語常見於科學知識討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"scientific knowledge and values","meaning":"科學知識與價值觀","examples":[{"en":"The boundary between scientific knowledge and values may be unclear.","zh":"科學知識與價值觀之間的界線可能不清楚。"},{"en":"Scientific knowledge and values are evidence-based claims and beliefs about what matters.","zh":"scientific knowledge and values 指以證據為基礎的主張，以及關於甚麼重要的信念。"},{"en":"A health debate may involve scientific knowledge about risk and values about freedom.","zh":"健康辯論可能涉及關於風險的科學知識，以及關於自由的價值觀。"},{"en":"Values influence how people judge whether evidence is enough for action.","zh":"價值觀會影響人們判斷證據是否足以採取行動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that facts and priorities can interact.","zh":"這個短語顯示事實和優先考慮可以互相影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"no longer be justified","meaning":"不再站得住腳","examples":[{"en":"Traditional distinctions may no longer be justified.","zh":"傳統區分可能不再站得住腳。"},{"en":"No longer be justified means no longer have enough reason or support.","zh":"no longer be justified 指不再有足夠理由或支持。"},{"en":"A strict school rule may no longer be justified if circumstances have changed.","zh":"如果情況已改變，嚴格校規可能不再站得住腳。"},{"en":"When evidence weakens, an old belief may no longer be justified.","zh":"當證據變弱，舊信念可能不再合理。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a past reason may no longer work.","zh":"這個短語顯示過去的理由可能不再有效。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"social processes","meaning":"社會過程","examples":[{"en":"Social processes influence the production of knowledge.","zh":"社會過程影響知識的生產。"},{"en":"Social processes are patterns of interaction among people and groups.","zh":"social processes 指人與群體之間互動的模式。"},{"en":"Peer pressure in a classroom is a simple social process.","zh":"課室中的朋輩壓力是一種簡單社會過程。"},{"en":"Research can be influenced by social processes such as funding, debate and reputation.","zh":"研究可以受資金、辯論和聲譽等社會過程影響。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how human relationships shape outcomes.","zh":"這個短語解釋人際關係如何塑造結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be involved at all stages of","meaning":"參與……的所有階段","examples":[{"en":"Social processes are involved at all stages of scientific research.","zh":"社會過程參與科學研究的所有階段。"},{"en":"To be involved at all stages of something means to affect every part of the process.","zh":"be involved at all stages of something 指影響整個過程的每一部分。"},{"en":"Parents may be involved at all stages of a child’s school application.","zh":"家長可能參與孩子入學申請的所有階段。"},{"en":"If values appear at every stage, they cannot be treated as outside the process.","zh":"如果價值觀出現在每個階段，就不能把它們視為過程以外的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses continuous involvement from beginning to end.","zh":"這個短語強調從開始到結束的持續參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the creation of knowledge","meaning":"知識的創造","examples":[{"en":"Values may influence the creation of scientific knowledge.","zh":"價值觀可能影響科學知識的創造。"},{"en":"The creation of knowledge is the process of producing new understanding.","zh":"creation of knowledge 指產生新理解的過程。"},{"en":"Universities support the creation of knowledge through research and teaching.","zh":"大學透過研究和教學支持知識的創造。"},{"en":"Knowledge creation may depend on what questions researchers choose to ask.","zh":"知識創造可能取決於研究者選擇提出甚麼問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how knowledge is made, not only how it is used.","zh":"這個短語集中於知識如何被創造，而不只是如何被使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"evaluation and establishment","meaning":"評估與確立","examples":[{"en":"Research requires the evaluation and establishment of scientific claims.","zh":"研究需要對科學主張作出評估與確立。"},{"en":"Evaluation and establishment means judging claims and confirming them as accepted knowledge.","zh":"evaluation and establishment 指評估主張，並把它們確認為被接受的知識。"},{"en":"Teachers use evaluation before establishing whether students have understood a topic.","zh":"老師會先評估，再確定學生是否理解某主題。"},{"en":"A claim becomes stronger after careful evaluation and repeated support.","zh":"經過仔細評估和反覆支持後，主張會變得更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of testing and confirming ideas.","zh":"這個短語描述測試和確認想法的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"social values","meaning":"社會價值觀","examples":[{"en":"Social values may shape how evidence is assessed.","zh":"社會價值觀可能塑造證據如何被評估。"},{"en":"Social values are shared beliefs about what is important, fair or desirable.","zh":"social values 指關於甚麼重要、公平或值得追求的共同信念。"},{"en":"A society that values equality may judge school policy differently from one that values competition.","zh":"重視平等的社會，可能與重視競爭的社會不同地評價教育政策。"},{"en":"Social values influence what risks people accept or reject.","zh":"社會價值觀影響人們接受或拒絕哪些風險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to community beliefs, not only personal opinions.","zh":"這個短語指社群信念，而不只是個人意見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in the same way as","meaning":"正如……一樣","examples":[{"en":"In the same way as scientists overlooked values, sociologists overlooked scientific criticism.","zh":"正如科學家忽視價值觀一樣，社會學家也忽視了科學批評。"},{"en":"In the same way as means similarly to or just like.","zh":"in the same way as 指類似於或正如。"},{"en":"In the same way as students need feedback, teachers need support too.","zh":"正如學生需要回饋一樣，老師也需要支援。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two similar patterns or mistakes.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種相似模式或錯誤。"},{"en":"It helps show that two groups may behave alike.","zh":"它幫助顯示兩個群體可能有相似行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"overlook social values","meaning":"忽視社會價值觀","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers have overlooked the role of social values.","zh":"有些研究者忽視了社會價值觀的作用。"},{"en":"To overlook social values means to fail to notice how shared beliefs affect an issue.","zh":"overlook social values 指未能注意共同信念如何影響某議題。"},{"en":"A school policy may fail if it overlooks parents’ values about discipline.","zh":"如果校規忽視家長對紀律的價值觀，它可能失敗。"},{"en":"Overlooking values can make a debate seem purely technical when it is not.","zh":"忽視價值觀可能令辯論看似純技術性，但其實不是。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that important human concerns may be missed.","zh":"這個短語提醒重要的人類關注可能被錯過。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"downplay an important part of","meaning":"淡化……的重要部分","examples":[{"en":"Sociologists may have downplayed an important part of the debate.","zh":"社會學家可能淡化了這場辯論的重要部分。"},{"en":"To downplay an important part of something means to make it seem less important than it is.","zh":"downplay an important part of something 指令某重要部分看似不太重要。"},{"en":"A company may downplay complaints to protect its image.","zh":"公司可能淡化投訴，以保護形象。"},{"en":"If scientific criticism is downplayed, the debate becomes incomplete.","zh":"如果科學批評被淡化，辯論就會變得不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests underestimating or reducing the importance of something.","zh":"這個短語暗示低估或削弱某事的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"eminent scientists","meaning":"傑出科學家","examples":[{"en":"Several eminent scientists have questioned aspects of fluoridation.","zh":"幾位傑出科學家質疑了食水加氟的某些方面。"},{"en":"Eminent scientists are highly respected scientists with strong reputations.","zh":"eminent scientists 指非常受尊重、聲譽很高的科學家。"},{"en":"An eminent scientist may influence public discussion because people trust their expertise.","zh":"傑出科學家可能因專業知識受信任而影響公共討論。"},{"en":"When eminent scientists disagree, the public may realise the issue is complex.","zh":"當傑出科學家意見不同，公眾可能意識到議題很複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes scientists with recognised authority.","zh":"這個短語描述具有公認權威的科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"question aspects of","meaning":"質疑……的某些方面","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers have questioned aspects of the evidence for fluoridation.","zh":"有些研究者質疑支持食水加氟證據的某些方面。"},{"en":"To question aspects of something means to raise doubts about parts of it.","zh":"question aspects of something 指對其中一些部分提出疑問。"},{"en":"Parents may question aspects of a school plan without rejecting the whole plan.","zh":"家長可能質疑學校計劃的某些方面，而不是否定整個計劃。"},{"en":"Questioning one aspect can reveal weaknesses in a wider argument.","zh":"質疑某一方面可以揭示更大論點中的弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase allows partial criticism rather than total rejection.","zh":"這個短語容許部分批評，而不是完全否定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"analyse classic studies","meaning":"分析經典研究","examples":[{"en":"Sutton analysed classic North American fluoridation studies.","zh":"Sutton 分析了北美經典食水加氟研究。"},{"en":"To analyse classic studies means to examine important older research carefully.","zh":"analyse classic studies 指仔細檢視重要的舊研究。"},{"en":"A student may analyse classic experiments in psychology to understand research methods.","zh":"學生可能分析心理學經典實驗，以理解研究方法。"},{"en":"Reanalysing classic studies can reveal hidden weaknesses.","zh":"重新分析經典研究可以揭示隱藏弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase shows careful study of influential research.","zh":"這個短語顯示對有影響力研究的仔細研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the effect of fluoridation on","meaning":"食水加氟對……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The studies examined the effect of fluoridation on tooth decay.","zh":"這些研究檢視食水加氟對蛀牙的影響。"},{"en":"The effect of fluoridation on something means how fluoridation changes or influences it.","zh":"effect of fluoridation on something 指食水加氟如何改變或影響某事。"},{"en":"Researchers may study the effect of sleep on memory.","zh":"研究者可能研究睡眠對記憶的影響。"},{"en":"To judge a policy, people need to know its effect on real outcomes.","zh":"要評價政策，人們需要知道它對實際結果的影響。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause or policy with its result.","zh":"這個短語把原因或政策與結果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"significant methodological shortcomings","meaning":"重大的研究方法缺陷","examples":[{"en":"Sutton identified significant methodological shortcomings in the earlier studies.","zh":"Sutton 在早期研究中指出重大的研究方法缺陷。"},{"en":"Significant methodological shortcomings are serious weaknesses in how research was designed or conducted.","zh":"significant methodological shortcomings 指研究設計或進行方式中的嚴重弱點。"},{"en":"A survey has methodological shortcomings if it asks only a small, biased group.","zh":"如果調查只詢問小而有偏差的群體，就有研究方法缺陷。"},{"en":"Weak methods can make impressive results less reliable.","zh":"薄弱方法可以令看似出色的結果較不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises the research process, not only the conclusion.","zh":"這個短語批評研究過程，而不只是結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"research methodology","meaning":"研究方法","examples":[{"en":"Weak research methodology can undermine an otherwise influential study.","zh":"薄弱研究方法可以削弱一項本來有影響力的研究。"},{"en":"Research methodology means the methods used to design, collect and analyse research.","zh":"research methodology 指用來設計、收集和分析研究的方法。"},{"en":"Good research methodology explains who was studied and how data were collected.","zh":"良好研究方法會解釋研究對象是誰，以及數據如何收集。"},{"en":"Poor methodology can make results unreliable even if the topic is important.","zh":"即使主題重要，差劣方法也會令結果不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the practical structure of research.","zh":"這個短語指研究的實際結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cast doubt on","meaning":"令人懷疑……","examples":[{"en":"Sutton’s analysis cast doubt on the claimed benefits of fluoridation.","zh":"Sutton 的分析令人懷疑食水加氟聲稱的好處。"},{"en":"To cast doubt on something means to make people question whether it is true.","zh":"cast doubt on something 指令人質疑某事是否真確。"},{"en":"Missing records may cast doubt on a company’s financial report.","zh":"缺失記錄可能令人懷疑公司的財務報告。"},{"en":"Strong criticism can cast doubt on research if it reveals method problems.","zh":"如果強烈批評揭示方法問題，它可以令人懷疑研究。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that confidence in a claim has weakened.","zh":"這個短語顯示對某主張的信心減弱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the extent of reductions","meaning":"減幅","examples":[{"en":"The study questioned the extent of reductions in tooth decay.","zh":"該研究質疑蛀牙減幅。"},{"en":"The extent of reductions means how large the decreases really are.","zh":"extent of reductions 指減少的實際幅度有多大。"},{"en":"A teacher may examine the extent of improvement after a new reading programme.","zh":"老師可能檢視新閱讀計劃後的進步幅度。"},{"en":"A policy may work, but people may still debate how big its effect is.","zh":"一項政策可能有效，但人們仍可能爭論其效果有多大。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the size of a decrease.","zh":"這個短語集中於下降的大小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be cited in","meaning":"在……中被引用","examples":[{"en":"Sutton’s book was not cited in sociological analyses of the issue.","zh":"Sutton 的書沒有在關於該議題的社會學分析中被引用。"},{"en":"To be cited in a study means to be mentioned as a source or reference.","zh":"be cited in a study 指在研究中被作為來源或參考提及。"},{"en":"A useful article may be cited in many student essays.","zh":"一篇有用文章可能在許多學生作文中被引用。"},{"en":"If a book is not cited, its argument may receive little attention.","zh":"如果一本書沒有被引用，其論點可能很少受到關注。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic writing.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a single analysis","meaning":"任何一項分析","examples":[{"en":"The book was absent from every single sociological analysis examined.","zh":"該書在每一項被檢視的社會學分析中都沒有出現。"},{"en":"A single analysis means one individual piece of analysis.","zh":"a single analysis 指任何一項個別分析。"},{"en":"Not a single analysis mentioned the missing survey data.","zh":"沒有任何一項分析提到缺失的調查數據。"},{"en":"If every analysis ignores a source, an important perspective may disappear.","zh":"如果每項分析都忽略某來源，重要觀點可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that there were no exceptions.","zh":"這個短語強調沒有例外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"scientific uncertainty","meaning":"科學上的不確定性","examples":[{"en":"Differences in values become more visible in a situation of scientific uncertainty.","zh":"在科學上不確定的情況下，價值觀差異變得更明顯。"},{"en":"Scientific uncertainty exists when evidence does not give a clear final answer.","zh":"scientific uncertainty 指證據未能給出清楚最終答案的情況。"},{"en":"During a new disease outbreak, scientific uncertainty may make decisions harder.","zh":"新疾病爆發期間，科學上的不確定性可能令決策更困難。"},{"en":"When science is uncertain, values often influence what risks people accept.","zh":"當科學不確定時，價值觀常影響人們接受哪些風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doubt or incompleteness in scientific evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述科學證據中的疑問或不完整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"differences in values","meaning":"價值觀差異","examples":[{"en":"The two sides may disagree because of differences in values.","zh":"雙方可能因價值觀差異而不同意。"},{"en":"Differences in values are disagreements about what matters most.","zh":"differences in values 指對甚麼最重要有分歧。"},{"en":"Parents may disagree about school rules because of differences in values about freedom and discipline.","zh":"家長可能因對自由和紀律的價值觀差異而不同意校規。"},{"en":"Values affect whether people prioritise safety, choice, cost or equality.","zh":"價值觀影響人們是否優先考慮安全、選擇、成本或平等。"},{"en":"This phrase explains disagreement that is not simply about facts.","zh":"這個短語解釋不只是事實層面的分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be highlighted","meaning":"被凸顯","examples":[{"en":"Scientific uncertainty allows differences in values to be highlighted.","zh":"科學上的不確定性使價值觀差異被凸顯。"},{"en":"To be highlighted means to be made clear, noticeable or emphasised.","zh":"be highlighted 指被清楚顯示、變得明顯或被強調。"},{"en":"A teacher may highlight common grammar mistakes before an exam.","zh":"老師可能在考試前凸顯常見文法錯誤。"},{"en":"Uncertainty highlights values because people must decide what risk matters most.","zh":"不確定性凸顯價值觀，因為人們必須決定哪種風險最重要。"},{"en":"This phrase means something becomes easier to see.","zh":"這個短語表示某事變得更容易看見。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"evidence for the benefits","meaning":"證明好處的證據","examples":[{"en":"A supporter may regard the evidence for the benefits as substantial.","zh":"支持者可能認為證明好處的證據頗為充分。"},{"en":"Evidence for the benefits means proof or support showing that something is helpful.","zh":"evidence for the benefits 指顯示某事有幫助的證明或支持。"},{"en":"A school may look for evidence for the benefits of smaller classes.","zh":"學校可能尋找證明小班教學有好處的證據。"},{"en":"People are more likely to support a policy if the evidence for benefits seems strong.","zh":"如果證明好處的證據看似有力，人們較可能支持政策。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on proof of positive effects.","zh":"這個短語集中於正面效果的證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"quite substantial","meaning":"頗為充分","examples":[{"en":"The evidence supporting fluoridation may appear quite substantial.","zh":"支持食水加氟的證據可能看來頗為充分。"},{"en":"Quite substantial means fairly large, strong or important.","zh":"quite substantial 指相當大、強或重要。"},{"en":"A student may make quite substantial progress after practising daily for two months.","zh":"學生每天練習兩個月後，可能有頗為顯著的進步。"},{"en":"Substantial evidence can support action, but it may still be debated.","zh":"充分證據可以支持行動，但仍可能被辯論。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something is meaningful in size or strength.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事在規模或力度上有意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"evidence of harm","meaning":"證明有害的證據","examples":[{"en":"Supporters argue that the evidence of harm is limited.","zh":"支持者認為證明有害的證據有限。"},{"en":"Evidence of harm means proof or signs that something may cause damage.","zh":"evidence of harm 指某事可能造成傷害的證明或跡象。"},{"en":"Doctors look for evidence of harm before stopping a medicine.","zh":"醫生在停止一種藥物前會尋找有害證據。"},{"en":"If evidence of harm is weak, supporters may accept a policy as safe enough.","zh":"如果有害證據薄弱，支持者可能接受政策足夠安全。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on proof of negative effects.","zh":"這個短語集中於負面效果的證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"limited and dubious","meaning":"有限且可疑","examples":[{"en":"Some supporters describe the evidence of harm as limited and dubious.","zh":"有些支持者把有害證據描述為有限且可疑。"},{"en":"Limited and dubious means small in amount and doubtful in quality.","zh":"limited and dubious 指數量少且質素可疑。"},{"en":"A rumour based on one unclear photo may be limited and dubious evidence.","zh":"只基於一張模糊照片的傳聞，可能是有限且可疑的證據。"},{"en":"When evidence is limited and dubious, people may not treat it as decisive.","zh":"當證據有限且可疑，人們可能不會把它視為決定性。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly questions the strength of evidence.","zh":"這個短語強烈質疑證據力度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"likely benefits","meaning":"可能帶來的好處","examples":[{"en":"Policy decisions often compare likely benefits with possible dangers.","zh":"政策決定常比較可能帶來的好處與潛在危險。"},{"en":"Likely benefits are good results that are expected or probable.","zh":"likely benefits 指預期或可能出現的好結果。"},{"en":"A student may consider the likely benefits of joining a study group.","zh":"學生可能考慮加入學習小組可能帶來的好處。"},{"en":"A policy may be supported if likely benefits seem greater than risks.","zh":"如果可能好處看似大於風險，政策可能獲支持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes expected advantages, not guaranteed results.","zh":"這個短語描述預期優勢，而不是保證結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"outweigh the possible dangers","meaning":"利多於可能的害處","examples":[{"en":"A supporter may conclude that the benefits outweigh the possible dangers.","zh":"支持者可能總結認為好處利多於可能的害處。"},{"en":"To outweigh the possible dangers means to be more important than the possible risks.","zh":"outweigh the possible dangers 指比可能風險更重要。"},{"en":"A vaccine may be accepted if its benefits outweigh the possible dangers.","zh":"如果疫苗的好處大於可能危險，它可能被接受。"},{"en":"People compare benefits and dangers when deciding whether a policy is worth it.","zh":"人們在決定政策是否值得時，會比較好處和危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in risk-benefit judgement.","zh":"這個短語用於風險與好處判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"hence","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"The supporter believes the risks are small and hence favours fluoridation.","zh":"支持者相信風險很小，因此支持食水加氟。"},{"en":"Hence means therefore or for that reason.","zh":"hence 意思是因此或基於那個原因。"},{"en":"The road is flooded, and hence the bus route has changed.","zh":"道路水浸，因此巴士路線已改變。"},{"en":"If someone believes the benefits are large, they may hence support the policy.","zh":"如果某人相信好處很大，因此可能支持該政策。"},{"en":"This word connects a reason with a conclusion.","zh":"這個字把理由與結論連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the cheapest and easiest way","meaning":"最便宜而簡單的方法","examples":[{"en":"Fluoridation may be seen as the cheapest and easiest way to prevent tooth decay.","zh":"食水加氟可能被視為預防蛀牙最便宜而簡單的方法。"},{"en":"The cheapest and easiest way is the method that costs least and requires least effort.","zh":"cheapest and easiest way 指成本最低且最少費力的方法。"},{"en":"Sending a group message may be the cheapest and easiest way to contact parents.","zh":"發送群組訊息可能是聯絡家長最便宜而簡單的方法。"},{"en":"Cheap and easy methods are attractive when they reach many people.","zh":"當方法能接觸很多人，而且便宜容易，就會有吸引力。"},{"en":"This phrase compares practical convenience with other methods.","zh":"這個短語把實際便利性與其他方法作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make sure that","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Supporters want to make sure that every child receives protection.","zh":"支持者想確保每個孩子都得到保護。"},{"en":"To make sure that something happens means to ensure it happens.","zh":"make sure that something happens 指確保某事發生。"},{"en":"A teacher may check homework diaries to make sure that students know the deadline.","zh":"老師可能檢查功課冊，以確保學生知道截止日期。"},{"en":"Policies are often designed to make sure that help reaches everyone.","zh":"政策常被設計成確保幫助能到達每個人。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an effort to guarantee a result.","zh":"這個短語顯示努力保證某個結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reap the benefits","meaning":"享受到好處","examples":[{"en":"Community-wide measures allow more children to reap the benefits.","zh":"全社區措施讓更多孩子享受到好處。"},{"en":"To reap the benefits means to enjoy the good results of something.","zh":"reap the benefits 指享受某事帶來的好結果。"},{"en":"Students who revise early may reap the benefits during the exam.","zh":"早早溫習的學生可能在考試中享受到好處。"},{"en":"Public-health measures are valued when many people reap the benefits.","zh":"當很多人享受到好處，公共衛生措施就會被重視。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests receiving rewards after an action or policy.","zh":"這個短語暗示在行動或政策之後得到回報。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"though the evidence is substantial","meaning":"儘管證據充分","examples":[{"en":"Though the evidence is substantial, some uncertainty remains.","zh":"儘管證據充分，仍有一些不確定性。"},{"en":"Though the evidence is substantial means although there is a strong amount of evidence.","zh":"though the evidence is substantial 指雖然有相當強的證據。"},{"en":"Though the evidence is substantial, a court may still ask for further clarification.","zh":"儘管證據充分，法庭仍可能要求進一步澄清。"},{"en":"Strong evidence does not always remove every doubt.","zh":"強證據不一定消除所有疑問。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast between strength and uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語引出證據力度與不確定性之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"there is some doubt about","meaning":"對……仍有疑問","examples":[{"en":"Opponents argue that there is some doubt about the claimed benefits.","zh":"反對者認為對聲稱的好處仍有疑問。"},{"en":"There is some doubt about something means people are not fully sure it is true.","zh":"there is some doubt about something 指人們未完全確定某事為真。"},{"en":"There is some doubt about whether the new timetable will reduce delays.","zh":"人們對新時間表是否會減少延誤仍有疑問。"},{"en":"Doubt may remain when studies disagree or methods are questioned.","zh":"當研究互相矛盾或方法受到質疑，疑問可能仍然存在。"},{"en":"This phrase shows partial uncertainty, not complete rejection.","zh":"這個短語顯示部分不確定，而不是完全否定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be necessary for","meaning":"對……是必需的","examples":[{"en":"Fluoridation is not strictly necessary for maintaining healthy teeth.","zh":"食水加氟對維持牙齒健康並非絕對必需。"},{"en":"To be necessary for something means to be needed in order for it to happen.","zh":"be necessary for something 指為了達成某事而需要。"},{"en":"Sleep is necessary for concentration and memory.","zh":"睡眠對專注和記憶是必需的。"},{"en":"If something is not necessary, people may prefer voluntary alternatives.","zh":"如果某事不是必需，人們可能偏好自願替代方法。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a requirement with an outcome.","zh":"這個短語把需要條件與結果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"forego the benefits","meaning":"放棄這些好處","examples":[{"en":"Opponents may prefer to forego the benefits rather than accept a health risk.","zh":"反對者可能寧願放棄這些好處，也不願接受健康風險。"},{"en":"To forego the benefits means to give up the advantages.","zh":"forego the benefits 指放棄優勢或好處。"},{"en":"A family may forego the benefits of a cheaper flat if the area feels unsafe.","zh":"如果地區令人覺得不安全，家庭可能放棄較便宜單位的好處。"},{"en":"People may give up benefits when they think the risk is unacceptable.","zh":"當人們認為風險不可接受，就可能放棄好處。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a deliberate choice to sacrifice an advantage.","zh":"這個短語顯示有意犧牲優勢的選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a slight chance of harm","meaning":"輕微的受害可能性","examples":[{"en":"Some people oppose fluoridation because of a slight chance of harm.","zh":"有些人因輕微的受害可能性而反對食水加氟。"},{"en":"A slight chance of harm means a small possibility that damage may occur.","zh":"slight chance of harm 指可能造成傷害的小可能性。"},{"en":"Parents may avoid a playground if there is even a slight chance of injury.","zh":"即使只有輕微受傷可能，家長也可能避開某個遊樂場。"},{"en":"Small risks can matter when they affect many people.","zh":"當風險影響很多人，即使小風險也可能重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes low probability, not zero risk.","zh":"這個短語描述低機率，而不是零風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a small percentage of the population","meaning":"一小部分人口","examples":[{"en":"Critics claim that a small percentage of the population may be harmed.","zh":"批評者聲稱一小部分人口可能受到傷害。"},{"en":"A small percentage of the population means a small part of all people in a group.","zh":"small percentage of the population 指某群體中一小部分人。"},{"en":"A small percentage of students may need special exam arrangements.","zh":"一小部分學生可能需要特別考試安排。"},{"en":"Even a small percentage matters when the whole population is large.","zh":"當整體人口很大，即使一小部分也很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a minority within a larger group.","zh":"這個短語描述較大群體中的少數。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be harmed by","meaning":"受到……傷害","examples":[{"en":"Some individuals may be harmed by excessive fluoride exposure.","zh":"有些人可能因過量接觸氟化物而受到傷害。"},{"en":"To be harmed by something means to be damaged or hurt because of it.","zh":"be harmed by something 指因某事而受損或受傷。"},{"en":"Children may be harmed by second-hand smoke at home.","zh":"兒童可能在家中受到二手煙傷害。"},{"en":"People worry more when a policy may harm vulnerable groups.","zh":"當政策可能傷害弱勢群體，人們會更擔心。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the cause of harm.","zh":"這個短語指出傷害的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"oppose fluoridation of water supplies","meaning":"反對在公共食水中加氟","examples":[{"en":"Opponents may oppose fluoridation of public water supplies.","zh":"反對者可能反對在公共食水中加氟。"},{"en":"To oppose fluoridation of water supplies means to disagree with adding fluoride to public water.","zh":"oppose fluoridation of water supplies 指不同意在公共食水中加入氟化物。"},{"en":"Residents may oppose a water policy if they feel it removes personal choice.","zh":"如果居民覺得食水政策剝奪個人選擇，可能會反對。"},{"en":"Opposition may come from doubts about safety, evidence or rights.","zh":"反對可能來自對安全、證據或權利的疑慮。"},{"en":"This phrase states a clear position against water fluoridation.","zh":"這個短語表明反對食水加氟的清楚立場。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"favour the voluntary use of","meaning":"支持自願使用……","examples":[{"en":"Some critics favour the voluntary use of fluoride products.","zh":"有些批評者支持自願使用氟化物產品。"},{"en":"To favour the voluntary use of something means to support people choosing it freely.","zh":"favour the voluntary use of something 指支持人們自由選擇使用某物。"},{"en":"A school may favour voluntary tutoring rather than compulsory extra lessons.","zh":"學校可能支持自願補習，而不是強制額外課堂。"},{"en":"Voluntary use respects personal choice while still allowing access to a benefit.","zh":"自願使用尊重個人選擇，同時仍讓人取得好處。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts personal choice with compulsory measures.","zh":"這個短語把個人選擇與強制措施作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"fluoride tablets","meaning":"氟化物藥片","examples":[{"en":"People who want extra fluoride can choose to take fluoride tablets.","zh":"想額外攝取氟化物的人可以選擇服用氟化物藥片。"},{"en":"Fluoride tablets are tablets containing fluoride, usually used to support dental health.","zh":"fluoride tablets 指含有氟化物、通常用於支持牙齒健康的藥片。"},{"en":"Parents may ask a dentist before giving fluoride tablets to a child.","zh":"家長在給孩子服用氟化物藥片前，可能會詢問牙醫。"},{"en":"Tablets allow individuals to choose fluoride intake more directly than water fluoridation.","zh":"與食水加氟相比，藥片讓個人更直接選擇氟化物攝取。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a voluntary fluoride product.","zh":"這個短語指自願使用的氟化物產品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"consider the scientific evidence","meaning":"考慮科學證據","examples":[{"en":"Both sides consider the scientific evidence concerning fluoridation.","zh":"雙方都考慮關於食水加氟的科學證據。"},{"en":"To consider the scientific evidence means to examine research and data before judging.","zh":"consider the scientific evidence 指在作判斷前檢視研究和數據。"},{"en":"A school board may consider scientific evidence before changing lunch rules.","zh":"校董會可能在改變午餐規則前考慮科學證據。"},{"en":"People may consider the same evidence but reach different conclusions.","zh":"人們可能考慮同一證據，但得出不同結論。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses evidence-based discussion.","zh":"這個短語強調以證據為基礎的討論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"differ in their assessments of","meaning":"對……有不同評估","examples":[{"en":"The two sides differ in their assessments of the benefits and costs.","zh":"雙方對好處和代價有不同評估。"},{"en":"To differ in their assessments of something means to judge it differently.","zh":"differ in their assessments of something 指對某事作出不同判斷。"},{"en":"Teachers may differ in their assessments of a student’s writing style.","zh":"老師可能對學生寫作風格有不同評估。"},{"en":"People disagree when they weigh the same benefits and costs differently.","zh":"當人們不同地衡量同一組好處和代價，就會不同意。"},{"en":"This phrase explains disagreement in evaluation.","zh":"這個短語解釋評價上的分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"social benefits and costs","meaning":"社會效益與代價","examples":[{"en":"Public-health policies involve both social benefits and costs.","zh":"公共衛生政策涉及社會效益與代價。"},{"en":"Social benefits and costs are the positive and negative effects on society.","zh":"social benefits and costs 指對社會的正面和負面影響。"},{"en":"Free bus travel may bring social benefits but also public costs.","zh":"免費巴士乘車可能帶來社會效益，但也帶來公共成本。"},{"en":"Policy debate often asks whether benefits to many justify costs to some.","zh":"政策辯論常問，多數人的好處是否能合理化部分人的代價。"},{"en":"This phrase looks beyond individual effects to society as a whole.","zh":"這個短語不只看個人影響，也看整個社會。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rationality and irrationality","meaning":"理性與非理性","examples":[{"en":"The disagreement is not simply a conflict between rationality and irrationality.","zh":"這場分歧不只是理性與非理性的衝突。"},{"en":"Rationality and irrationality refer to reasonable thinking and unreasonable thinking.","zh":"rationality and irrationality 指合理思考與不合理思考。"},{"en":"A disagreement about careers may involve values, not just rationality and irrationality.","zh":"關於職業的分歧可能涉及價值觀，而不只是理性與非理性。"},{"en":"Calling one side irrational can hide legitimate concerns.","zh":"把一方稱為非理性可能隱藏其合理關注。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts reason with lack of reason.","zh":"這個短語把理性與缺乏理性作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a legitimate difference in values","meaning":"合理的價值觀差異","examples":[{"en":"The opposing positions reflect a legitimate difference in values.","zh":"對立立場反映合理的價值觀差異。"},{"en":"A legitimate difference in values is a reasonable disagreement about what matters most.","zh":"legitimate difference in values 指關於甚麼最重要的合理分歧。"},{"en":"Two parents may have a legitimate difference in values about strict discipline.","zh":"兩位家長可能在嚴格紀律方面有合理的價值觀差異。"},{"en":"Policy debates can be fair even when people value different things.","zh":"即使人們重視不同事物，政策辯論仍可以是合理的。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that disagreement can be reasonable, not foolish.","zh":"這個短語顯示分歧可以是合理的，而不是愚蠢的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"place a positive value on","meaning":"對……給予正面評價","examples":[{"en":"Supporters place a positive value on preventing tooth decay.","zh":"支持者對預防蛀牙給予正面評價。"},{"en":"To place a positive value on something means to consider it important and desirable.","zh":"place a positive value on something 指認為某事重要且值得追求。"},{"en":"A school may place a positive value on kindness as well as grades.","zh":"學校可能對善良以及成績給予正面評價。"},{"en":"People support policies when they strongly value the outcome those policies produce.","zh":"當人們強烈重視政策產生的結果時，就會支持該政策。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what someone treats as a benefit.","zh":"這個短語解釋某人把甚麼視為好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"place a negative value on","meaning":"對……給予負面評價","examples":[{"en":"Opponents place a negative value on possible health risks.","zh":"反對者對潛在健康風險給予負面評價。"},{"en":"To place a negative value on something means to treat it as harmful or undesirable.","zh":"place a negative value on something 指把某事視為有害或不值得追求。"},{"en":"Parents may place a negative value on too much screen time.","zh":"家長可能對過多螢幕時間給予負面評價。"},{"en":"People may reject a policy when they value its possible harms very negatively.","zh":"當人們非常負面地看待政策的可能傷害，就可能拒絕該政策。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what someone treats as a cost or danger.","zh":"這個短語解釋某人把甚麼視為代價或危險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"possible health risks","meaning":"潛在健康風險","examples":[{"en":"Even small possible health risks may influence public opinion.","zh":"即使小的潛在健康風險也可能影響公眾意見。"},{"en":"Possible health risks are harms to health that may happen but are not certain.","zh":"possible health risks 指可能發生但不確定的健康傷害。"},{"en":"A new medicine label may list possible health risks.","zh":"新藥標籤可能列出潛在健康風險。"},{"en":"People may react strongly to possible risks if exposure is compulsory.","zh":"如果接觸是強制的，人們可能對潛在風險有強烈反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uncertain but possible harm to health.","zh":"這個短語描述不確定但可能出現的健康傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"compulsory intake","meaning":"強制攝取","examples":[{"en":"Fluoridated water results in compulsory intake for most residents.","zh":"加氟食水導致大多數居民強制攝取氟化物。"},{"en":"Compulsory intake means people take in a substance without freely choosing each dose.","zh":"compulsory intake 指人們在沒有自由選擇每次分量下攝取某物質。"},{"en":"Compulsory school meals would mean students eat what the school provides.","zh":"強制學校午餐會意味學生吃學校提供的食物。"},{"en":"People object to compulsory intake when they want control over their own bodies.","zh":"當人們想控制自己身體時，可能反對強制攝取。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts forced or automatic intake with choice.","zh":"這個短語把強制或自動攝取與選擇作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"voluntary intake","meaning":"自願攝取","examples":[{"en":"Tablets allow individuals to choose voluntary fluoride intake.","zh":"藥片讓個人選擇自願攝取氟化物。"},{"en":"Voluntary intake means taking something by personal choice.","zh":"voluntary intake 指根據個人選擇攝取某物。"},{"en":"Vitamins are usually a form of voluntary intake because people choose whether to take them.","zh":"維他命通常是一種自願攝取，因為人們可選擇是否服用。"},{"en":"Voluntary intake respects choice but may not reach everyone equally.","zh":"自願攝取尊重選擇，但未必能平均到達每個人。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts individual choice with compulsory exposure.","zh":"這個短語把個人選擇與強制接觸作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"from a sociological point of view","meaning":"從社會學角度看","examples":[{"en":"From a sociological point of view, opposition is not necessarily irrational.","zh":"從社會學角度看，反對食水加氟不一定不理性。"},{"en":"From a sociological point of view means looking at an issue through society, groups and values.","zh":"from a sociological point of view 指從社會、群體和價值觀角度看議題。"},{"en":"From a sociological point of view, school failure may involve poverty and family stress.","zh":"從社會學角度看，學業失敗可能涉及貧窮和家庭壓力。"},{"en":"This viewpoint helps explain why people respond differently to the same evidence.","zh":"這種角度有助解釋為何人們對同一證據反應不同。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a social rather than purely technical analysis.","zh":"這個短語表示社會分析，而不是純技術分析。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"not necessarily irrational","meaning":"不一定不理性","examples":[{"en":"Opposition to fluoridation is not necessarily irrational.","zh":"反對食水加氟不一定不理性。"},{"en":"Not necessarily irrational means not automatically unreasonable.","zh":"not necessarily irrational 指不自動等於不合理。"},{"en":"A student’s fear of exams is not necessarily irrational if past failures were painful.","zh":"如果過去失敗很痛苦，學生害怕考試不一定不理性。"},{"en":"People may have reasonable values behind views others dislike.","zh":"人們在他人不喜歡的觀點背後可能有合理價值觀。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against dismissing disagreement too quickly.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要太快否定分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"claims to rationality","meaning":"自稱合乎理性的說法","examples":[{"en":"Claims to rationality may form part of a political strategy.","zh":"自稱合乎理性的說法可能構成政治策略的一部分。"},{"en":"Claims to rationality are statements that present a position as reasonable or scientific.","zh":"claims to rationality 指把某立場呈現為合理或科學的說法。"},{"en":"A company may use claims to rationality to make its price rise seem unavoidable.","zh":"公司可能使用自稱合乎理性的說法，使加價看似不可避免。"},{"en":"Such claims can persuade people by suggesting opponents are emotional or foolish.","zh":"這類說法可以透過暗示反對者情緒化或愚蠢來說服人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how “being rational” can be used rhetorically.","zh":"這個短語描述「理性」如何被修辭性地使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"scientific authority","meaning":"科學權威","examples":[{"en":"Experts may invoke scientific authority to support a policy.","zh":"專家可能引用科學權威來支持一項政策。"},{"en":"Scientific authority is the credibility or power given to science and experts.","zh":"scientific authority 指科學和專家被賦予的可信度或權力。"},{"en":"A government may use scientific authority when explaining a vaccine programme.","zh":"政府解釋疫苗計劃時，可能使用科學權威。"},{"en":"Authority can guide decisions, but it should not hide uncertainty.","zh":"權威可以指導決定，但不應隱藏不確定性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the influence of expert knowledge.","zh":"這個短語指專家知識的影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be better seen as","meaning":"較適宜被視為……","examples":[{"en":"Such claims may be better seen as part of a campaign strategy.","zh":"這類說法較適宜被視為宣傳策略的一部分。"},{"en":"Be better seen as means should more accurately be understood as.","zh":"be better seen as 指較準確地應被理解為。"},{"en":"A student’s silence may be better seen as shyness, not laziness.","zh":"學生沉默較適宜被視為害羞，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"Reframing something can change how people judge it.","zh":"重新界定某事可以改變人們如何判斷它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a more suitable interpretation.","zh":"這個短語引入更合適的詮釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a strategy to promote","meaning":"推廣……的策略","examples":[{"en":"Scientific authority may be used as a strategy to promote fluoridation.","zh":"科學權威可能被用作推廣食水加氟的策略。"},{"en":"A strategy to promote something is a planned method for encouraging support for it.","zh":"strategy to promote something 指鼓勵人支持某事的計劃方法。"},{"en":"Free trials can be a strategy to promote a new learning app.","zh":"免費試用可以是推廣新學習應用程式的策略。"},{"en":"Promotion strategies try to persuade people, not just inform them.","zh":"推廣策略試圖說服人，而不只是通知人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a method used to gain public acceptance.","zh":"這個短語描述用來取得公眾接受的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"incontrovertible statements of fact","meaning":"無可爭議的事實陳述","examples":[{"en":"Scientific claims should not always be treated as incontrovertible statements of fact.","zh":"科學主張不應總被視為無可爭議的事實陳述。"},{"en":"Incontrovertible statements of fact are claims that cannot reasonably be disputed.","zh":"incontrovertible statements of fact 指無法合理爭議的主張。"},{"en":"“Water boils at a certain temperature under standard pressure” may be treated as a factual statement.","zh":"「水在標準壓力下於某溫度沸騰」可被視為事實陳述。"},{"en":"Controversial evidence should not be presented as impossible to question.","zh":"具爭議的證據不應被呈現為不可能被質疑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes claims treated as completely settled.","zh":"這個短語描述被視為完全定案的主張。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be bound up in","meaning":"與……密不可分","examples":[{"en":"Social values are bound up in decisions about fluoridation.","zh":"社會價值觀與食水加氟決定密不可分。"},{"en":"To be bound up in something means to be closely connected with it.","zh":"be bound up in something 指與某事緊密相連。"},{"en":"Family choices are often bound up in money, time and emotion.","zh":"家庭選擇常與金錢、時間和情感密不可分。"},{"en":"Public-health decisions are bound up in evidence and values together.","zh":"公共衛生決定與證據和價值觀同時密不可分。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that two things cannot easily be separated.","zh":"這個短語強調兩件事不易分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"declarations by scientific experts","meaning":"科學專家的聲明","examples":[{"en":"Declarations by scientific experts should inform but not settle the debate.","zh":"科學專家的聲明應提供資訊，但不應結束辯論。"},{"en":"Declarations by scientific experts are formal statements made by specialists.","zh":"declarations by scientific experts 指專家作出的正式聲明。"},{"en":"A declaration by doctors may guide schools during a health emergency.","zh":"醫生的聲明可能在健康緊急情況中指導學校。"},{"en":"Expert declarations can help debate, but they may not answer ethical questions fully.","zh":"專家聲明可以幫助辯論，但未必完全回答倫理問題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to authoritative expert statements.","zh":"這個短語指具權威性的專家陳述。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be considered the final word","meaning":"被視為最終定論","examples":[{"en":"Expert opinion should not always be considered the final word on public policy.","zh":"專家意見不應總被視為公共政策的最終定論。"},{"en":"To be considered the final word means to be treated as the last and decisive answer.","zh":"be considered the final word 指被視為最後且決定性的答案。"},{"en":"A doctor’s advice matters, but a patient’s values may also matter in treatment decisions.","zh":"醫生建議很重要，但病人的價值觀也可能影響治療決定。"},{"en":"If expert opinion is the final word, public debate may be limited.","zh":"如果專家意見是最終定論，公共辯論可能受限制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes complete authority over a decision.","zh":"這個短語描述對決定的完全權威。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct letter for each multiple-choice question.","zh":"考生為每條多項選擇題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option marked by the right letter.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選出以正確字母標示的答案選項。"},{"en":"Students should check whether the answer asks for a letter or a word.","zh":"學生應檢查答案要求填字母還是單字。"},{"en":"Copying the wrong letter can lose marks even when the idea is correct.","zh":"即使想法正確，抄錯字母也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"optimum amount","meaning":"最適當分量","examples":[{"en":"The optimum amount of fluoride depends partly on local temperature.","zh":"最適當的氟化物分量部分取決於本地氣溫。"},{"en":"The optimum amount is the best or most suitable quantity.","zh":"optimum amount 指最佳或最合適的數量。"},{"en":"A doctor may recommend the optimum amount of exercise for a patient’s condition.","zh":"醫生可能根據病人情況建議最適當的運動量。"},{"en":"Too little may be ineffective, while too much may be harmful.","zh":"太少可能無效，太多可能有害。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the most suitable level.","zh":"這個短語集中於最合適水平。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be calculated partly according to","meaning":"部分按照……計算","examples":[{"en":"The fluoride concentration is calculated partly according to the regional climate.","zh":"氟化物濃度部分按照地區氣候計算。"},{"en":"To be calculated partly according to something means one factor helps decide the final number.","zh":"be calculated partly according to something 指某一因素幫助決定最終數字。"},{"en":"School fees may be calculated partly according to family income.","zh":"學費可能部分按照家庭收入計算。"},{"en":"If climate affects water intake, it may affect the fluoride level chosen.","zh":"如果氣候影響飲水量，它可能影響所選氟化物水平。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a calculation uses more than one factor.","zh":"這個短語顯示計算使用不止一個因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"how hot an area is","meaning":"某地區有多炎熱","examples":[{"en":"Water consumption may depend on how hot an area is.","zh":"飲水量可能取決於某地區有多炎熱。"},{"en":"How hot an area is means the temperature level of a place.","zh":"how hot an area is 指某地的氣溫水平。"},{"en":"How hot an area is affects clothing, electricity use and water needs.","zh":"某地區有多炎熱會影響衣著、用電量和用水需要。"},{"en":"People usually drink more water in hotter areas.","zh":"人們通常在較炎熱地區喝更多水。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about the heat of a region.","zh":"這個短語詢問某地區的炎熱程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"dental problems","meaning":"牙齒問題","examples":[{"en":"Fluoridation policies are intended to reduce dental problems.","zh":"食水加氟政策旨在減少牙齒問題。"},{"en":"Dental problems are health issues involving teeth or gums.","zh":"dental problems 指涉及牙齒或牙齦的健康問題。"},{"en":"A child with dental problems may need fillings or regular check-ups.","zh":"有牙齒問題的孩子可能需要補牙或定期檢查。"},{"en":"Poor brushing and high sugar intake can cause dental problems.","zh":"刷牙不足和高糖攝取可以造成牙齒問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is broader than tooth decay alone.","zh":"這個短語比單指蛀牙更廣泛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"personal freedom","meaning":"個人自由","examples":[{"en":"Compulsory public-health measures may restrict personal freedom.","zh":"強制公共衛生措施可能限制個人自由。"},{"en":"Personal freedom is the ability to make choices about one’s own life and body.","zh":"personal freedom 指對自己生活和身體作選擇的能力。"},{"en":"A student may feel personal freedom when choosing their own elective subjects.","zh":"學生選擇自己的選修科時，可能感到有個人自由。"},{"en":"Public rules can protect health while also limiting personal freedom.","zh":"公共規則可以保護健康，同時也限制個人自由。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in debates about state power and individual choice.","zh":"這個短語常出現在關於國家權力和個人選擇的辯論中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"excessive fluoride","meaning":"過量氟化物","examples":[{"en":"Excessive fluoride may cause dental discolouration.","zh":"過量氟化物可能導致牙齒變色。"},{"en":"Excessive fluoride means too much fluoride.","zh":"excessive fluoride 指太多氟化物。"},{"en":"Excessive salt in food can damage health over time.","zh":"食物中過量鹽分長遠可以損害健康。"},{"en":"A useful substance can become harmful when the amount is excessive.","zh":"當分量過多，有用物質也可能變得有害。"},{"en":"This phrase warns about overdose or too high a level.","zh":"這個短語提醒過量或水平過高的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be added by mistake","meaning":"被錯誤加入","examples":[{"en":"Strict controls reduce the risk of excessive fluoride being added by mistake.","zh":"嚴格控制可減少過量氟化物被錯誤加入的風險。"},{"en":"To be added by mistake means to be put in accidentally or at the wrong amount.","zh":"be added by mistake 指被意外加入或以錯誤分量加入。"},{"en":"Sugar may be added by mistake to a dish that should be salty.","zh":"糖可能被錯誤加入本應是鹹的菜式。"},{"en":"In public water systems, small mistakes can affect many people.","zh":"在公共食水系統中，小錯誤可以影響很多人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes accidental addition, not deliberate policy.","zh":"這個短語描述意外加入，而不是有意政策。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"mention someone in order to","meaning":"提及某人以……","examples":[{"en":"The writer mentions Kuhn in order to show that science has a social dimension.","zh":"作者提及 Kuhn，以顯示科學有社會層面。"},{"en":"To mention someone in order to do something means to refer to that person for a purpose.","zh":"mention someone in order to do something 指為某目的提及某人。"},{"en":"A teacher may mention a writer in order to explain a literary style.","zh":"老師可能提及某位作家，以解釋一種文學風格。"},{"en":"Writers mention experts to support, challenge or develop an argument.","zh":"作者提及專家，以支持、挑戰或發展論點。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a person is included in a text.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何某人物被包括在文本中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"contrast one view with another","meaning":"把一種觀點與另一種作比較","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether the writer contrasts Kuhn’s view with Collins’s.","zh":"題目問作者是否把 Kuhn 的觀點與 Collins 的觀點作比較。"},{"en":"To contrast one view with another means to show the differences between two opinions.","zh":"contrast one view with another 指顯示兩種意見之間的差異。"},{"en":"A student may contrast two historians’ views in an essay.","zh":"學生可能在作文中比較兩位歷史學家的觀點。"},{"en":"Contrasting views helps readers see what each thinker adds.","zh":"對比觀點幫助讀者看見每位思想家補充了甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when comparing ideas by difference.","zh":"這個短語用於透過差異比較想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the rational nature of","meaning":"……的理性本質","examples":[{"en":"The traditional model emphasises the rational nature of scientific inquiry.","zh":"傳統模式強調科學探究的理性本質。"},{"en":"The rational nature of something means its basis in reason and logical thinking.","zh":"rational nature of something 指某事以理性和邏輯思考為基礎。"},{"en":"Maths lessons often highlight the rational nature of problem-solving.","zh":"數學課常突出解難的理性本質。"},{"en":"A process seems rational when clear reasons guide each step.","zh":"當清楚理由指導每一步，過程看起來就是理性的。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on logic rather than emotion or habit.","zh":"這個短語集中於邏輯，而不是情緒或習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"scientific inquiry","meaning":"科學探究","examples":[{"en":"Scientific inquiry involves evidence, interpretation and debate.","zh":"科學探究涉及證據、詮釋和辯論。"},{"en":"Scientific inquiry is the process of asking questions and investigating them scientifically.","zh":"scientific inquiry 指提出問題並以科學方式研究它們的過程。"},{"en":"Students practise scientific inquiry when they test how light affects plant growth.","zh":"學生測試光線如何影響植物生長時，就是進行科學探究。"},{"en":"Inquiry becomes stronger when results are checked and discussed.","zh":"當結果被檢查和討論，探究會變得更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes science as active investigation.","zh":"這個短語把科學描述為主動研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"argue one’s case adequately","meaning":"充分論證自己的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The option questions whether Kuhn argued his case adequately.","zh":"該選項質疑 Kuhn 是否充分論證自己的觀點。"},{"en":"To argue one’s case adequately means to explain and support one’s position well enough.","zh":"argue one’s case adequately 指充分解釋並支持自己的立場。"},{"en":"A student argues their case adequately when they use examples and evidence.","zh":"學生使用例子和證據時，就是充分論證自己的觀點。"},{"en":"A weak argument fails if it does not answer likely objections.","zh":"如果論點沒有回答可能反對意見，就會失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase judges how well someone defends a viewpoint.","zh":"這個短語評價某人維護觀點的程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"non-scientific considerations","meaning":"非科學因素","examples":[{"en":"Social values are examples of non-scientific considerations.","zh":"社會價值觀是非科學因素的例子。"},{"en":"Non-scientific considerations are factors outside scientific evidence, such as ethics or politics.","zh":"non-scientific considerations 指科學證據以外的因素，例如倫理或政治。"},{"en":"A hospital policy may include non-scientific considerations like patient dignity.","zh":"醫院政策可能包括病人尊嚴等非科學因素。"},{"en":"Such considerations matter when decisions affect people’s lives.","zh":"當決定影響人的生活，這類因素就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean unimportant; it means not purely scientific.","zh":"這個短語不是指不重要，而是指不純粹屬於科學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"flaws in the way something was conducted","meaning":"……的進行方式存在缺陷","examples":[{"en":"Sutton found flaws in the way earlier studies were conducted.","zh":"Sutton 發現早期研究的進行方式存在缺陷。"},{"en":"Flaws in the way something was conducted are weaknesses in how it was carried out.","zh":"flaws in the way something was conducted 指某事進行方法中的弱點。"},{"en":"A survey has flaws if the questions lead people toward one answer.","zh":"如果調查問題引導人選某一答案，該調查就有缺陷。"},{"en":"Method flaws can make research conclusions less reliable.","zh":"方法缺陷可以令研究結論較不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises the process rather than only the result.","zh":"這個短語批評過程，而不只是結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"achieve unique results","meaning":"取得獨特結果","examples":[{"en":"The earlier studies did not necessarily achieve unique results.","zh":"早期研究不一定取得獨特結果。"},{"en":"To achieve unique results means to produce results that are clearly special or not repeated elsewhere.","zh":"achieve unique results 指產生清楚特別或其他地方沒有重複的結果。"},{"en":"A class project may not achieve unique results if many groups find the same answer.","zh":"如果許多小組找到同一答案，班級專題可能沒有取得獨特結果。"},{"en":"Results may seem important but still need comparison with other studies.","zh":"結果可能看似重要，但仍需要與其他研究比較。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether findings are distinct.","zh":"這個短語集中於研究結果是否獨特。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"long-term effects","meaning":"長遠影響","examples":[{"en":"Researchers continue to debate the long-term effects of fluoridation.","zh":"研究者繼續辯論食水加氟的長遠影響。"},{"en":"Long-term effects are results that appear or continue over a long period.","zh":"long-term effects 指長時間後出現或持續的結果。"},{"en":"Teachers may study the long-term effects of early reading support.","zh":"老師可能研究早期閱讀支援的長遠影響。"},{"en":"A policy can look successful at first but have different long-term effects.","zh":"一項政策初看可能成功，但有不同長遠影響。"},{"en":"This phrase asks what happens after many years, not immediately.","zh":"這個短語問多年後會發生甚麼，而不是立即結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"greater than previously believed","meaning":"比先前所認為的更大","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that the effect was greater than previously believed.","zh":"該選項暗示影響比先前所認為的更大。"},{"en":"Greater than previously believed means larger or stronger than people earlier thought.","zh":"greater than previously believed 指比人們早前認為的更大或更強。"},{"en":"The cost of repairs may be greater than previously believed after closer inspection.","zh":"經過更仔細檢查後，維修成本可能比先前所認為的更大。"},{"en":"New evidence can show that an effect was underestimated.","zh":"新證據可以顯示某影響曾被低估。"},{"en":"This phrase compares new understanding with an older belief.","zh":"這個短語把新理解與舊信念作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reveal one’s true motivations","meaning":"揭示真正動機","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether scientists should reveal their true motivations.","zh":"題目問科學家是否應揭示自己的真正動機。"},{"en":"To reveal one’s true motivations means to show the real reasons behind one’s actions.","zh":"reveal one’s true motivations 指顯示自己行動背後的真實原因。"},{"en":"A politician may be asked to reveal true motivations behind a policy change.","zh":"政治人物可能被要求揭示政策改變背後的真正動機。"},{"en":"Hidden motivations can affect how people judge a public claim.","zh":"隱藏動機可以影響人們如何判斷公共主張。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on honesty about underlying reasons.","zh":"這個短語集中於對深層原因的誠實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be responsible for deciding policy","meaning":"負責決定政策","examples":[{"en":"Scientists should not be solely responsible for deciding public policy.","zh":"科學家不應單獨負責決定公共政策。"},{"en":"To be responsible for deciding policy means to have the duty or authority to make policy choices.","zh":"be responsible for deciding policy 指有責任或權力作出政策選擇。"},{"en":"A school board may be responsible for deciding homework policy.","zh":"校董會可能負責決定功課政策。"},{"en":"Public policy often needs expert advice and public values together.","zh":"公共政策常需要專家建議和公眾價值觀共同參與。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who has decision-making power.","zh":"這個短語指出誰有決策權。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be concerned solely with","meaning":"只關注……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists are not necessarily concerned solely with objective truth.","zh":"科學家不一定只關注客觀真相。"},{"en":"To be concerned solely with something means to care only about that thing.","zh":"be concerned solely with something 指只關心某一件事。"},{"en":"A school should not be concerned solely with exam scores.","zh":"學校不應只關注考試分數。"},{"en":"People often consider values, careers and institutions as well as truth.","zh":"人們常考慮價值觀、職業和制度，而不只是真相。"},{"en":"This phrase limits concern to one factor only.","zh":"這個短語把關注限制在單一因素上。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reach an agreement on","meaning":"就……達成共識","examples":[{"en":"Experts may struggle to reach an agreement on a controversial issue.","zh":"專家可能難以就具爭議議題達成共識。"},{"en":"To reach an agreement on something means to arrive at a shared decision or view.","zh":"reach an agreement on something 指對某事達成共同決定或觀點。"},{"en":"Parents and teachers may reach an agreement on a student’s support plan.","zh":"家長和老師可能就學生支援計劃達成共識。"},{"en":"Agreement is harder when evidence is uncertain and values differ.","zh":"當證據不確定而價值觀不同，共識較難達成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of settling disagreement.","zh":"這個短語描述解決分歧的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"agree with the views of the writer","meaning":"與作者的觀點一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether each statement agrees with the writer’s views.","zh":"考生判斷每項陳述是否與作者的觀點一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the views of the writer means to match what the writer thinks.","zh":"agree with the views of the writer 指與作者所想相符。"},{"en":"In reading exams, students should answer from the text, not from personal opinion.","zh":"在閱讀考試中，學生應根據文本作答，而不是個人意見。"},{"en":"A statement agrees with the writer only if the writer clearly supports it.","zh":"只有當作者清楚支持某陳述時，它才與作者觀點一致。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in Yes, No, Not Given questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於 Yes, No, Not Given 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"contradict the writer’s views","meaning":"與作者的觀點相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A “No” response means that the statement contradicts the writer’s views.","zh":"“No” 回答表示該陳述與作者的觀點相矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the writer’s views means to say the opposite of what the writer thinks.","zh":"contradict the writer’s views 指說出與作者所想相反的意思。"},{"en":"A statement contradicts a text if the text clearly says the opposite.","zh":"如果文本清楚說出相反內容，陳述就與文本矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should look for direct evidence before choosing “No”.","zh":"學生在選 “No” 前應尋找直接證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear conflict with the writer’s opinion.","zh":"這個短語描述與作者意見的清楚衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"“Not Given” means that it is impossible to say what the writer thinks.","zh":"“Not Given” 表示無法判斷作者怎樣想。"},{"en":"Be impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide.","zh":"be impossible to say 指沒有足夠資料作決定。"},{"en":"If a passage does not mention a person’s age, it is impossible to say how old they are.","zh":"如果篇章沒有提到某人的年齡，就無法判斷他幾歲。"},{"en":"Students should avoid guessing when the text gives no evidence.","zh":"當文本沒有證據，學生應避免猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase explains uncertainty caused by missing information.","zh":"這個短語解釋因資料缺失造成的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"keep something separate from","meaning":"把……與……分開","examples":[{"en":"Scientific knowledge cannot always be kept separate from social values.","zh":"科學知識不一定總能與社會價值觀分開。"},{"en":"To keep something separate from something else means to prevent the two from mixing.","zh":"keep something separate from something else 指防止兩者混在一起。"},{"en":"Some people try to keep work separate from family life.","zh":"有些人嘗試把工作與家庭生活分開。"},{"en":"In public debates, facts and values may be difficult to separate.","zh":"在公共辯論中，事實和價值觀可能難以分開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an attempt to maintain a boundary.","zh":"這個短語描述維持界線的嘗試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"disregard doubts","meaning":"忽視疑慮","examples":[{"en":"Many sociologists disregarded the doubts raised by some scientists.","zh":"許多社會學家忽視了一些科學家提出的疑慮。"},{"en":"To disregard doubts means to ignore questions or concerns.","zh":"disregard doubts 指忽視問題或憂慮。"},{"en":"A manager may disregard doubts from staff and push ahead too quickly.","zh":"經理可能忽視員工疑慮，太快推進計劃。"},{"en":"Ignoring doubts can make an analysis incomplete.","zh":"忽視疑慮可以令分析不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that concerns were not given enough attention.","zh":"這個短語暗示疑慮沒有得到足夠關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"concerning fluoridation","meaning":"關於食水加氟","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists expressed doubts concerning fluoridation.","zh":"有些科學家表達了關於食水加氟的疑慮。"},{"en":"Concerning fluoridation means about or related to fluoridation.","zh":"concerning fluoridation 指關於或與食水加氟有關。"},{"en":"Parents may ask questions concerning a new school health policy.","zh":"家長可能提出關於新學校健康政策的問題。"},{"en":"Doubts concerning a policy can focus on evidence, safety or rights.","zh":"關於政策的疑慮可以集中於證據、安全或權利。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal way to say “about fluoridation”.","zh":"這個短語是 “about fluoridation” 的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"receive insufficient attention","meaning":"未獲充分關注","examples":[{"en":"Sutton’s methodological criticism received insufficient attention.","zh":"Sutton 對研究方法的批評未獲充分關注。"},{"en":"To receive insufficient attention means to be noticed or discussed less than it deserves.","zh":"receive insufficient attention 指受到的注意或討論少於應得程度。"},{"en":"Quiet students may receive insufficient attention in a noisy classroom.","zh":"在嘈吵課室中，安靜學生可能未獲充分關注。"},{"en":"Important criticism can be lost if researchers focus only on popular evidence.","zh":"如果研究者只集中於熱門證據，重要批評可能被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something has been under-discussed.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事討論不足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"outside North America","meaning":"在北美洲以外","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks about reactions outside North America.","zh":"該陳述問及北美洲以外的反應。"},{"en":"Outside North America means in places other than North America.","zh":"outside North America 指在北美洲以外的地方。"},{"en":"A film popular in the US may be less known outside North America.","zh":"在美國受歡迎的電影，在北美洲以外可能較少人知道。"},{"en":"Evidence from one region may not show reactions elsewhere.","zh":"來自一個地區的證據未必顯示其他地方的反應。"},{"en":"This phrase defines a geographical limit by exclusion.","zh":"這個短語透過排除某地區來界定地理範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"valid arguments on both sides","meaning":"雙方都有合理理據","examples":[{"en":"The writer recognises valid arguments on both sides of the debate.","zh":"作者承認這場辯論雙方都有合理理據。"},{"en":"Valid arguments on both sides are reasonable points made by each opposing group.","zh":"valid arguments on both sides 指對立雙方各自提出的合理觀點。"},{"en":"In a school uniform debate, there may be valid arguments on both sides.","zh":"在校服辯論中，雙方可能都有合理理據。"},{"en":"Recognising valid arguments does not mean treating all claims as equally strong.","zh":"承認合理理據不等於把所有說法都視為同等有力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a balanced view of disagreement.","zh":"這個短語顯示對分歧的平衡看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"complete each sentence","meaning":"完成每個句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates complete each sentence with the correct ending.","zh":"考生用正確句尾完成每個句子。"},{"en":"To complete each sentence means to add the missing part so the sentence is finished.","zh":"complete each sentence 指加入缺失部分，使句子完整。"},{"en":"Students complete each sentence by choosing the option that matches the passage.","zh":"學生透過選擇與篇章相符的選項完成每個句子。"},{"en":"The ending must fit both grammar and meaning.","zh":"句尾必須同時符合文法和意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading and grammar tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀和文法題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the correct ending","meaning":"正確句尾","examples":[{"en":"Each statement must be matched with the correct ending.","zh":"每項陳述都必須與正確句尾配對。"},{"en":"The correct ending is the phrase or clause that completes a sentence accurately.","zh":"correct ending 指準確完成句子的短語或從句。"},{"en":"A student should read the whole sentence before choosing the correct ending.","zh":"學生應先讀完整句，再選正確句尾。"},{"en":"A wrong ending may fit grammar but not match the passage meaning.","zh":"錯誤句尾可能合文法，但不符合篇章意思。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the final part of a sentence-completion answer.","zh":"這個短語集中於句子完成題答案的最後部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be established through objective methods","meaning":"透過客觀方法確立","examples":[{"en":"The traditional view holds that scientific knowledge is established through objective methods.","zh":"傳統觀點認為科學知識是透過客觀方法確立的。"},{"en":"To be established through objective methods means to be proven by fair, unbiased procedures.","zh":"be established through objective methods 指透過公平、無偏見的程序被證明。"},{"en":"A school survey is stronger if results are established through objective methods.","zh":"如果學校調查結果是透過客觀方法確立的，就更有力。"},{"en":"Objective methods reduce the influence of personal preference.","zh":"客觀方法減少個人偏好的影響。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses the traditional ideal of science.","zh":"這個短語表達科學的傳統理想。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be affected by the beliefs of","meaning":"受到……的信念影響","examples":[{"en":"A sociological view argues that knowledge is affected by the beliefs of those involved.","zh":"社會學觀點認為知識受到參與者的信念影響。"},{"en":"To be affected by the beliefs of people means to be influenced by what they think is true or important.","zh":"be affected by the beliefs of people 指受他們認為真實或重要的事情影響。"},{"en":"A classroom rule may be affected by teachers’ beliefs about discipline.","zh":"課室規則可能受到老師對紀律的信念影響。"},{"en":"Beliefs shape which questions people ask and which answers they trust.","zh":"信念塑造人們提出哪些問題，以及信任哪些答案。"},{"en":"This phrase connects ideas with the people who hold them.","zh":"這個短語把想法與持有想法的人連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"everyone concerned","meaning":"所有相關人士","examples":[{"en":"The values of everyone concerned may shape the debate.","zh":"所有相關人士的價值觀都可能塑造這場辯論。"},{"en":"Everyone concerned means all the people affected by or involved in an issue.","zh":"everyone concerned 指受某議題影響或參與其中的所有人。"},{"en":"Before changing a timetable, a school should listen to everyone concerned.","zh":"在改變時間表前，學校應聆聽所有相關人士。"},{"en":"Decisions are fairer when affected people are included.","zh":"當受影響的人被包括在內，決定會更公平。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses broad participation.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"not always be understood at first","meaning":"最初未必能被理解","examples":[{"en":"The results of scientific research are not always understood at first.","zh":"科學研究結果最初未必能被理解。"},{"en":"Not always be understood at first means may not be clear immediately.","zh":"not always be understood at first 指未必立即清楚。"},{"en":"A difficult poem may not be understood at first by students.","zh":"困難詩歌最初未必能被學生理解。"},{"en":"Some results need time, debate and further evidence before they make sense.","zh":"有些結果需要時間、辯論和更多證據才變得有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that understanding can develop gradually.","zh":"這個短語顯示理解可以逐步發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be able to choose whether","meaning":"能夠選擇是否……","examples":[{"en":"Opponents argue that people should be able to choose whether they receive fluoride.","zh":"反對者認為人們應能夠選擇是否攝取氟化物。"},{"en":"To be able to choose whether means to have the right or ability to decide yes or no.","zh":"be able to choose whether 指有權利或能力決定是否做某事。"},{"en":"Patients should be able to choose whether to join a treatment trial.","zh":"病人應能夠選擇是否參加治療試驗。"},{"en":"Choice matters more when a decision affects the body or health.","zh":"當決定影響身體或健康，選擇就更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises personal control.","zh":"這個短語強調個人控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"insufficient proof","meaning":"證據不足","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to insufficient proof for a cautious approach.","zh":"該選項提到證據不足，因此應採取審慎做法。"},{"en":"Insufficient proof means not enough evidence to be fully confident.","zh":"insufficient proof 指沒有足夠證據令人完全有信心。"},{"en":"A teacher should not accuse a student of cheating with insufficient proof.","zh":"老師不應在證據不足下指控學生作弊。"},{"en":"When proof is insufficient, people may choose a more careful policy.","zh":"當證據不足，人們可能選擇較謹慎的政策。"},{"en":"This phrase describes weak or incomplete evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述薄弱或不完整的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"support a cautious approach","meaning":"支持審慎做法","examples":[{"en":"Scientific uncertainty may support a cautious approach to public policy.","zh":"科學上的不確定性可能支持公共政策採取審慎做法。"},{"en":"To support a cautious approach means to justify acting carefully and avoiding unnecessary risk.","zh":"support a cautious approach 指合理化小心行事並避免不必要風險。"},{"en":"A doctor may support a cautious approach when a new treatment has limited evidence.","zh":"當新療法證據有限，醫生可能支持審慎做法。"},{"en":"Caution becomes reasonable when possible harm is serious or evidence is unclear.","zh":"當可能傷害嚴重或證據不清，審慎就變得合理。"},{"en":"This phrase connects uncertainty with careful decision-making.","zh":"這個短語把不確定性與謹慎決策連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"risks outweigh the benefits","meaning":"弊大於利","examples":[{"en":"An opponent may believe that the risks outweigh the benefits.","zh":"反對者可能相信風險弊大於利。"},{"en":"Risks outweigh the benefits means the possible harms are more important than the advantages.","zh":"risks outweigh the benefits 指可能傷害比好處更重要。"},{"en":"A family may cancel a trip if the safety risks outweigh the benefits.","zh":"如果安全風險大於好處，家庭可能取消旅行。"},{"en":"People reject policies when they judge the harms to be greater than the gains.","zh":"當人們判斷傷害大於收益，就會拒絕政策。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in cost-benefit or risk-benefit thinking.","zh":"這個短語用於成本效益或風險效益思考。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"not the only ones who benefit","meaning":"並非唯一受益者","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that children are not the only ones who benefit from fluoridation.","zh":"該選項暗示兒童並非食水加氟的唯一受益者。"},{"en":"Not the only ones who benefit means other people also receive advantages.","zh":"not the only ones who benefit 指其他人也得到好處。"},{"en":"Students are not the only ones who benefit from a quiet library; teachers do too.","zh":"學生並非安靜圖書館的唯一受益者；老師也受益。"},{"en":"A public-health measure may help several groups, not just its main target group.","zh":"公共衛生措施可能幫助多個群體，而不只是主要目標群體。"},{"en":"This phrase expands the group of beneficiaries.","zh":"這個短語擴大了受益者群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 169 - The fluoridation controversy.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 170":[{"front":"mind music","meaning":"腦海中的音樂","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines music that plays repeatedly inside the mind.","zh":"文章探討在腦海中反覆播放的音樂。"},{"en":"Mind music means music that appears in your thoughts even when no real music is playing.","zh":"Mind music 指即使沒有真實音樂播放，也會出現在思想中的音樂。"},{"en":"A student may hear mind music while walking to school after listening to a catchy song at breakfast.","zh":"學生早餐時聽過一首易記歌曲後，步行上學時可能聽到腦海中的音樂。"},{"en":"If the brain has little else to do, mind music may fill the quiet space.","zh":"如果大腦沒有其他事情要處理，腦海中的音樂可能填補安靜空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes music in the mind, not music heard through the ears.","zh":"這個片語描述腦中的音樂，而不是耳朵實際聽到的音樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"investigate earworms","meaning":"研究「洗腦歌」現象","examples":[{"en":"Scientists investigate earworms to understand memory and thought.","zh":"科學家研究「洗腦歌」現象，以理解記憶和思想。"},{"en":"To investigate earworms means to study why songs repeat in people’s minds without conscious choice.","zh":"To investigate earworms 指研究為何歌曲會在人們腦中不由自主地重複。"},{"en":"Psychologists may investigate earworms by asking people to record songs that get stuck in their heads.","zh":"心理學家可能要求人們記錄腦海中揮之不去的歌曲，以研究「洗腦歌」現象。"},{"en":"If researchers investigate earworms, they may learn how memory, mood, and attention interact.","zh":"如果研究人員研究「洗腦歌」現象，他們可能了解記憶、情緒和注意力如何互相作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes scientific study of a common mental experience.","zh":"這個片語描述對常見心理經驗的科學研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get something out of your head","meaning":"把……從腦海中揮去","examples":[{"en":"Some songs are difficult to get out of your head.","zh":"有些歌曲很難從腦海中揮去。"},{"en":"To get something out of your head means to stop thinking about it repeatedly.","zh":"To get something out of your head 指停止反覆想起某事。"},{"en":"A student may struggle to get a funny advertisement song out of their head during homework.","zh":"學生做功課時，可能很難把一首有趣廣告歌從腦海中揮去。"},{"en":"If a tune is very catchy, it may be harder to get out of your head.","zh":"如果旋律非常易記，它可能更難從腦海中揮去。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when a thought, worry, or song keeps returning.","zh":"這個片語常用於思想、擔憂或歌曲不斷回來的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have a song stuck in your head","meaning":"有一首歌在腦海中揮之不去","examples":[{"en":"Many people have experienced having a song stuck in their head.","zh":"許多人都經歷過有一首歌在腦海中揮之不去。"},{"en":"To have a song stuck in your head means a tune keeps repeating in your mind without your choice.","zh":"To have a song stuck in your head 指一段旋律不由自主地在腦中重複。"},{"en":"After hearing a pop song in a shop, you may have it stuck in your head all afternoon.","zh":"在商店聽過一首流行歌後，你可能整個下午都有那首歌在腦海中揮之不去。"},{"en":"If a chorus repeats many times, listeners may later have the song stuck in their heads.","zh":"如果副歌重複很多次，聽眾之後可能有那首歌在腦海中揮之不去。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an involuntary mental replay of music.","zh":"這個片語描述音樂在腦中不由自主地重播。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"play on an endless loop","meaning":"無限循環播放","examples":[{"en":"An earworm may seem to play on an endless loop.","zh":"洗腦旋律可能像是在無限循環播放。"},{"en":"To play on an endless loop means to repeat again and again with no clear stopping point.","zh":"To play on an endless loop 指一次又一次重複，沒有明確停止點。"},{"en":"A shop song can feel as if it plays on an endless loop when customers hear it every hour.","zh":"如果顧客每小時都聽到同一首店舖歌曲，它可能感覺像在無限循環播放。"},{"en":"If a musical phrase is short and catchy, the brain may loop it repeatedly.","zh":"如果一段旋律短而易記，大腦可能會反覆循環播放它。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests tiring repetition, not normal listening.","zh":"這個片語暗示令人疲累的重複，而不是正常聆聽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"involuntary musical images","meaning":"非自願音樂意象","examples":[{"en":"Scientists call earworms involuntary musical images.","zh":"科學家把洗腦旋律稱為非自願音樂意象。"},{"en":"Involuntary musical images are pieces of music that appear in the mind without deliberate effort.","zh":"Involuntary musical images 是沒有刻意努力下出現在腦中的音樂片段。"},{"en":"A person may experience involuntary musical images while brushing their teeth or waiting for a bus.","zh":"一個人在刷牙或等巴士時，可能經歷非自願音樂意象。"},{"en":"If the brain recalls a tune automatically, the music feels self-starting rather than chosen.","zh":"如果大腦自動回想起旋律，那段音樂感覺像自行開始，而不是被選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is the scientific name for music that repeats inside the mind.","zh":"這個片語是腦中反覆音樂的科學名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"earworms","meaning":"洗腦旋律；縈繞腦海的歌曲","examples":[{"en":"Earworms are tunes that repeat involuntarily in the mind.","zh":"洗腦旋律是不由自主地在腦海中重複的旋律。"},{"en":"Earworms are songs or musical fragments that get stuck in your head.","zh":"Earworms 是卡在腦海中的歌曲或音樂片段。"},{"en":"A simple advertising jingle can become an earworm after you hear it several times.","zh":"一段簡單廣告歌聽過幾次後，可能變成洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"Earworms may appear more often when people are tired, bored, or doing routine tasks.","zh":"當人們疲倦、沉悶或做例行工作時，洗腦旋律可能更常出現。"},{"en":"This word describes a mental music loop, not an actual insect.","zh":"這個詞描述腦中的音樂循環，而不是實際昆蟲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a wave of new research","meaning":"一股新的研究浪潮","examples":[{"en":"A wave of new research is examining why earworms occur.","zh":"一股新的研究浪潮正在探討洗腦旋律為何出現。"},{"en":"A wave of new research means many new studies appearing around the same time.","zh":"A wave of new research 指許多新研究在相近時間出現。"},{"en":"A wave of new research on sleep may help schools understand why students are tired.","zh":"一股關於睡眠的新研究浪潮，可能幫助學校理解學生為何疲倦。"},{"en":"When many scientists study the same question, knowledge can grow quickly.","zh":"當許多科學家研究同一問題，知識可以快速增長。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a sudden increase in academic attention.","zh":"這個片語暗示學術關注突然增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"shed light on","meaning":"闡明；令……更清楚","examples":[{"en":"New studies are shedding light on the causes of earworms.","zh":"新研究正在闡明洗腦旋律的成因。"},{"en":"To shed light on something means to make it clearer or easier to understand.","zh":"To shed light on something 指令某事更清楚或更容易理解。"},{"en":"A teacher’s example can shed light on a difficult grammar rule.","zh":"老師的例子可以闡明一條困難文法規則。"},{"en":"If research sheds light on memory, doctors and teachers may understand learning better.","zh":"如果研究闡明記憶，醫生和老師可能更理解學習。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when new information explains a confusing issue.","zh":"這個片語用於新資訊解釋令人困惑的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what can be learned from","meaning":"可以從……中了解甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are exploring what can be learned from earworms.","zh":"研究人員正在探索可以從洗腦旋律中了解甚麼。"},{"en":"What can be learned from something means the useful knowledge or lesson that it may provide.","zh":"What can be learned from something 指某事可提供的有用知識或教訓。"},{"en":"Teachers may ask what can be learned from students’ common mistakes.","zh":"老師可能會問可以從學生常犯錯誤中了解甚麼。"},{"en":"If earworms reveal how memory works, they can teach scientists about the mind.","zh":"如果洗腦旋律揭示記憶如何運作，它們可以讓科學家了解心智。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the value of studying an experience or problem.","zh":"這個片語著重研究某經驗或問題的價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"neuroscientists","meaning":"神經科學家","examples":[{"en":"Neuroscientists study how music affects the brain.","zh":"神經科學家研究音樂如何影響大腦。"},{"en":"Neuroscientists are scientists who study the brain, nerves, and nervous system.","zh":"Neuroscientists 是研究大腦、神經和神經系統的科學家。"},{"en":"Neuroscientists may use brain scans to see which areas become active during music.","zh":"神經科學家可能使用腦部掃描，查看聽音樂時哪些區域被啟動。"},{"en":"If neuroscientists understand attention better, they may help people with memory or learning problems.","zh":"如果神經科學家更理解注意力，他們可能幫助有記憶或學習問題的人。"},{"en":"This word refers to brain researchers, not general doctors.","zh":"這個詞指大腦研究人員，而不是一般醫生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cognitive psychologists","meaning":"認知心理學家","examples":[{"en":"Cognitive psychologists investigate memory and thought processes.","zh":"認知心理學家研究記憶和思考過程。"},{"en":"Cognitive psychologists study how people think, learn, remember, pay attention, and solve problems.","zh":"Cognitive psychologists 研究人如何思考、學習、記憶、集中注意和解決問題。"},{"en":"A cognitive psychologist may test how distractions affect exam revision.","zh":"認知心理學家可能測試干擾如何影響考試溫習。"},{"en":"If a song keeps returning to the mind, cognitive psychologists may ask which memory system is involved.","zh":"如果一首歌不斷回到腦中，認知心理學家可能會問涉及哪個記憶系統。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to psychologists who focus on mental processes.","zh":"這個片語指專注於心理過程的心理學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"explore the mysteries of","meaning":"探索……的奧秘","examples":[{"en":"Researchers use earworms to explore the mysteries of memory.","zh":"研究人員利用洗腦旋律探索記憶的奧秘。"},{"en":"To explore the mysteries of something means to study something that is still not fully understood.","zh":"To explore the mysteries of something 指研究仍未被完全理解的事物。"},{"en":"Scientists explore the mysteries of sleep by watching brain activity at night.","zh":"科學家透過觀察夜間腦活動，探索睡眠的奧秘。"},{"en":"If earworms behave strangely, they may help researchers explore hidden parts of memory.","zh":"如果洗腦旋律表現奇特，它們可能幫助研究人員探索記憶中隱藏部分。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful investigation into a difficult question.","zh":"這個片語暗示對困難問題作仔細研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"beyond our conscious control","meaning":"超出我們的意識控制","examples":[{"en":"Some mental processes occur beyond our conscious control.","zh":"一些心理過程發生在我們的意識控制之外。"},{"en":"Beyond our conscious control means outside what we can deliberately choose or manage.","zh":"Beyond our conscious control 指超出我們能刻意選擇或管理的範圍。"},{"en":"A nervous student may blush beyond their conscious control during a speech.","zh":"緊張學生演講時可能不由自主臉紅，超出其意識控制。"},{"en":"If a song appears without permission, it shows that not all thoughts are controlled consciously.","zh":"如果一首歌未經允許般出現，就顯示並非所有思想都受意識控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental or physical events that happen automatically.","zh":"這個片語描述自動發生的心理或身體事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have full control over","meaning":"完全控制……","examples":[{"en":"People do not have full control over every thought process.","zh":"人們不能完全控制每一個思考過程。"},{"en":"To have full control over something means to be able to completely direct or manage it.","zh":"To have full control over something 指能完全指揮或管理某事。"},{"en":"A driver has full control over a car only when the steering and brakes work properly.","zh":"只有當軚盤和煞車正常運作時，駕駛者才完全控制汽車。"},{"en":"If people had full control over thoughts, unwanted songs would disappear immediately.","zh":"如果人們能完全控制思想，不想要的歌曲就會立即消失。"},{"en":"This phrase shows complete power over an action, object, or mental process.","zh":"這個片語顯示對行動、物件或心理過程的完全控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"thought processes","meaning":"思考過程","examples":[{"en":"Earworms reveal something about involuntary thought processes.","zh":"洗腦旋律揭示了一些關於非自願思考過程的東西。"},{"en":"Thought processes are the ways the mind forms ideas, memories, decisions, and reactions.","zh":"Thought processes 是大腦形成想法、記憶、決定和反應的方式。"},{"en":"Teachers can understand students better by asking them to explain their thought processes.","zh":"老師可以要求學生解釋思考過程，從而更理解他們。"},{"en":"If thought processes happen automatically, people may not notice why an idea appears.","zh":"如果思考過程自動發生，人們可能不察覺一個想法為何出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how thinking works, not just what someone thinks.","zh":"這個片語描述思考如何運作，而不只是某人想甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be an illusion","meaning":"是一種錯覺","examples":[{"en":"The idea that we fully control our thoughts may be an illusion.","zh":"我們完全控制思想這個想法可能是一種錯覺。"},{"en":"To be an illusion means to seem true but not actually be true.","zh":"To be an illusion 指看起來是真的，但實際上並非如此。"},{"en":"A quiet classroom can be an illusion of understanding if students are silent but confused.","zh":"如果學生安靜但困惑，安靜課室可能是一種理解的錯覺。"},{"en":"If thoughts appear without choice, complete mental control may only be an illusion.","zh":"如果思想不經選擇而出現，完全心理控制可能只是一種錯覺。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that appearance may differ from reality.","zh":"這個片語提醒表象可能與現實不同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"found a master’s programme","meaning":"創辦碩士課程","examples":[{"en":"Lauren Stewart founded a master’s programme in music and the brain.","zh":"Lauren Stewart創辦了一個關於音樂與大腦的碩士課程。"},{"en":"To found a master’s programme means to create or establish a postgraduate course of study.","zh":"To found a master’s programme 指創立或設立一個研究生課程。"},{"en":"A university may found a master’s programme when a new field becomes important.","zh":"當新領域變得重要，大學可能創辦碩士課程。"},{"en":"If many students want to study music and neuroscience, a new programme may be created.","zh":"如果許多學生想研究音樂與神經科學，一個新課程可能被創立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes starting an academic programme, not simply teaching one class.","zh":"這個片語描述開設學術課程，而不只是教授一堂課。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"music, mind and brain","meaning":"音樂、心智與大腦","examples":[{"en":"The programme focuses on music, mind and brain.","zh":"該課程集中於音樂、心智與大腦。"},{"en":"Music, mind and brain refers to the study of how music connects with thought, emotion, memory, and brain activity.","zh":"Music, mind and brain 指研究音樂如何與思想、情緒、記憶和腦活動連接。"},{"en":"A course on music, mind and brain may examine why songs affect mood.","zh":"關於音樂、心智與大腦的課程可能探討歌曲為何影響情緒。"},{"en":"If researchers study these three areas together, they can link musical experience with mental and neurological processes.","zh":"如果研究人員把這三個範疇一起研究，就能把音樂經驗與心理和神經過程連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase names an interdisciplinary field, not just music theory.","zh":"這個片語命名一個跨學科領域，而不只是音樂理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"recent research has taken place","meaning":"近期研究已在……進行","examples":[{"en":"Recent research has taken place at Goldsmiths, University of London.","zh":"近期研究已在倫敦大學金匠學院進行。"},{"en":"Recent research has taken place means new studies have been carried out in a particular place or period.","zh":"Recent research has taken place 指新研究已在某地方或時期進行。"},{"en":"Recent research has taken place in schools to test how phone use affects attention.","zh":"近期研究已在學校進行，以測試手機使用如何影響注意力。"},{"en":"If research takes place in a university lab, scientists can control conditions more carefully.","zh":"如果研究在大學實驗室進行，科學家可以更仔細控制條件。"},{"en":"This phrase reports where or when studies have been conducted.","zh":"這個片語報告研究在哪裡或何時進行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be unable to observe","meaning":"無法觀察……","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have been unable to observe earworms directly in the brain.","zh":"研究人員一直無法直接在大腦中觀察洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"To be unable to observe something means not to be able to see, measure, or monitor it directly.","zh":"To be unable to observe something 指不能直接看見、量度或監察某事。"},{"en":"Teachers may be unable to observe students’ private study habits at home.","zh":"老師可能無法觀察學生在家中的私人溫習習慣。"},{"en":"If earworms occur unpredictably, scientists may be unable to observe them during brain scans.","zh":"如果洗腦旋律無法預測地出現，科學家可能無法在腦掃描期間觀察它們。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a limit in what researchers can directly measure.","zh":"這個片語顯示研究人員直接量度事物的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what happens in the brain","meaning":"大腦內發生甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Scientists want to know what happens in the brain during an earworm.","zh":"科學家想知道洗腦旋律出現時大腦內發生甚麼。"},{"en":"What happens in the brain means the activity, changes, or processes occurring inside the brain.","zh":"What happens in the brain 指大腦內正在發生的活動、變化或過程。"},{"en":"Doctors study what happens in the brain when people sleep, learn, or feel fear.","zh":"醫生研究人在睡覺、學習或感到恐懼時大腦內發生甚麼。"},{"en":"If scientists know what happens in the brain, they can better explain memory and attention.","zh":"如果科學家知道大腦內發生甚麼，就能更好解釋記憶和注意力。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about internal brain processes, not outward behaviour only.","zh":"這個片語詢問內部腦過程，而不只是外在行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"occur unpredictably","meaning":"無法預測地出現","examples":[{"en":"Earworms occur unpredictably and are difficult to monitor.","zh":"洗腦旋律無法預測地出現，因此難以監察。"},{"en":"To occur unpredictably means to happen without a clear pattern or warning.","zh":"To occur unpredictably 指在沒有清晰模式或預警下發生。"},{"en":"Headaches that occur unpredictably can make daily planning difficult.","zh":"如果頭痛無法預測地出現，日常安排會變得困難。"},{"en":"If earworms occur unpredictably, researchers cannot easily schedule experiments around them.","zh":"如果洗腦旋律無法預測地出現，研究人員就不容易圍繞它們安排實驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes events that are hard to foresee.","zh":"這個片語描述難以預見的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"much of what is known","meaning":"大部分已知資料","examples":[{"en":"Much of what is known about earworms comes from self-reports.","zh":"關於洗腦旋律的大部分已知資料來自自我報告。"},{"en":"Much of what is known means a large part of the available knowledge.","zh":"Much of what is known 指現有知識中的很大部分。"},{"en":"Much of what is known about students’ stress comes from surveys and interviews.","zh":"關於學生壓力的大部分已知資料來自調查和訪談。"},{"en":"If much of what is known depends on self-reports, researchers must consider memory and honesty.","zh":"如果大部分已知資料依賴自我報告，研究人員必須考慮記憶和誠實程度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main source of current knowledge.","zh":"這個片語描述目前知識的主要來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"come from surveys","meaning":"來自調查","examples":[{"en":"Much of the evidence comes from surveys and questionnaires.","zh":"大部分證據來自調查和問卷。"},{"en":"To come from surveys means to be collected through questions answered by many people.","zh":"To come from surveys 指透過許多人回答問題而收集得來。"},{"en":"Information about school lunches may come from surveys completed by students and parents.","zh":"關於學校午餐的資料可能來自學生和家長完成的調查。"},{"en":"If evidence comes from surveys, it can show patterns in people’s reported experiences.","zh":"如果證據來自調查，它可以顯示人們自述經驗中的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies surveys as the source of data.","zh":"這個片語指出調查是數據來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"questionnaires","meaning":"問卷","examples":[{"en":"Researchers use questionnaires to collect information about earworms.","zh":"研究人員使用問卷收集關於洗腦旋律的資料。"},{"en":"Questionnaires are sets of written or online questions used to collect people’s answers.","zh":"Questionnaires 是用來收集人們答案的一組書面或網上問題。"},{"en":"A school may use questionnaires to ask students how they feel about homework.","zh":"學校可能使用問卷詢問學生對功課的感受。"},{"en":"If many people answer the same questionnaire, researchers can compare their responses.","zh":"如果許多人回答同一份問卷，研究人員就可以比較他們的回應。"},{"en":"This word refers to a common tool for gathering self-reported data.","zh":"這個詞指收集自我報告數據的常見工具。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"diary studies","meaning":"日記研究","examples":[{"en":"Diary studies record people’s experiences over several days.","zh":"日記研究記錄人們在幾天內的經驗。"},{"en":"Diary studies are research methods in which participants write down experiences as they happen over time.","zh":"Diary studies 是要求參加者隨時間寫下正在發生經驗的研究方法。"},{"en":"A sleep diary study may ask students to record bedtime, mood, and tiredness each day.","zh":"睡眠日記研究可能要求學生每天記錄睡覺時間、心情和疲倦程度。"},{"en":"If people record earworms soon after they occur, the data may be more accurate.","zh":"如果人們在洗腦旋律出現後不久記錄下來，數據可能更準確。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research based on repeated personal records.","zh":"這個片語描述基於反覆個人記錄的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"laboratory experiments","meaning":"實驗室實驗","examples":[{"en":"Laboratory experiments allow researchers to test theories under controlled conditions.","zh":"實驗室實驗讓研究人員在受控條件下測試理論。"},{"en":"Laboratory experiments are studies carried out in a controlled research setting.","zh":"Laboratory experiments 是在受控研究環境中進行的研究。"},{"en":"A memory experiment may ask students to remember word lists in a quiet laboratory.","zh":"記憶實驗可能要求學生在安靜實驗室中記住詞表。"},{"en":"If conditions are controlled, researchers can compare results more fairly.","zh":"如果條件受控，研究人員可以更公平地比較結果。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to experiments designed to test ideas carefully.","zh":"這個片語指為仔細測試想法而設計的實驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be published in","meaning":"刊登於……","examples":[{"en":"A Goldsmiths study was published in the journal Memory and Cognition.","zh":"一項金匠學院研究刊登於《Memory and Cognition》期刊。"},{"en":"To be published in a journal means to appear in an academic magazine or research publication.","zh":"To be published in a journal 指出現在學術雜誌或研究刊物中。"},{"en":"A study on student sleep may be published in an education journal.","zh":"關於學生睡眠的研究可能刊登於教育期刊。"},{"en":"If research is published in a respected journal, other researchers can read and test it.","zh":"如果研究刊登於受尊重期刊，其他研究人員可以閱讀和測試它。"},{"en":"This phrase tells readers where a study formally appeared.","zh":"這個片語告訴讀者研究正式出現在哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"tend to match","meaning":"往往與……相符","examples":[{"en":"The music imagined in the mind tends to match real recordings closely.","zh":"腦海中想像的音樂往往與真實錄音十分相符。"},{"en":"To tend to match something means usually to be similar to it.","zh":"To tend to match something 指通常與某物相似。"},{"en":"A student’s memory of a song may tend to match the original rhythm even without music playing.","zh":"即使沒有音樂播放，學生對歌曲的記憶可能往往與原本節奏相符。"},{"en":"If imagined music matches recordings, the brain is storing details quite accurately.","zh":"如果想像音樂與錄音相符，大腦就是相當準確地儲存細節。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a common pattern, not a perfect rule.","zh":"這個片語暗示常見模式，而不是完美規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"actual recordings","meaning":"實際錄音","examples":[{"en":"Imagined music can closely resemble actual recordings.","zh":"想像中的音樂可以非常像實際錄音。"},{"en":"Actual recordings are real recorded versions of music, not music imagined in the mind.","zh":"Actual recordings 是音樂的真實錄製版本，而不是腦中想像的音樂。"},{"en":"A singer may compare a student’s humming with the actual recording of the song.","zh":"歌手可能把學生哼出的旋律與歌曲的實際錄音作比較。"},{"en":"If a person’s tapping matches the actual recording, their memory of tempo is accurate.","zh":"如果某人的打拍子與實際錄音相符，他對速度的記憶就是準確的。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts real audio with remembered or imagined music.","zh":"這個片語把真實音訊與記住或想像的音樂作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have volunteers do something","meaning":"要求參加者做某事","examples":[{"en":"The researchers had volunteers tap to the beat of their earworms.","zh":"研究人員要求參加者跟着洗腦旋律的節拍打拍子。"},{"en":"To have volunteers do something means to ask or instruct research participants to perform an action.","zh":"To have volunteers do something 指要求或指示研究參加者做某個動作。"},{"en":"A teacher may have students read aloud to check pronunciation.","zh":"老師可能要求學生大聲朗讀，以檢查發音。"},{"en":"If researchers have volunteers record their feelings daily, they can compare patterns over time.","zh":"如果研究人員要求參加者每天記錄感受，他們可以比較隨時間出現的模式。"},{"en":"This structure means arranging for people to do a task.","zh":"這個結構表示安排人們完成一項任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tap to the beat","meaning":"跟着節拍打拍子","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers tapped to the beat of the music they imagined.","zh":"參加者跟着他們想像的音樂節拍打拍子。"},{"en":"To tap to the beat means to move a finger, hand, or foot in time with music.","zh":"To tap to the beat 指用手指、手或腳跟着音樂節奏移動。"},{"en":"A child may tap to the beat on the desk while listening to a song.","zh":"小朋友聽歌時可能在桌上跟着節拍打拍子。"},{"en":"If someone taps steadily, researchers can estimate the tempo of the music in their mind.","zh":"如果某人穩定打拍子，研究人員可以估計他腦中音樂的速度。"},{"en":"This phrase connects body movement with musical rhythm.","zh":"這個片語把身體動作與音樂節奏連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"during a four-day period","meaning":"在四日期間","examples":[{"en":"The participants recorded their earworms during a four-day period.","zh":"參加者在四日期間記錄他們的洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"During a four-day period means over the course of four days.","zh":"During a four-day period 指在四天的過程中。"},{"en":"A student may record sleep hours during a four-day period before changing study habits.","zh":"學生可能在四日期間記錄睡眠時數，再改變學習習慣。"},{"en":"If data are collected over several days, researchers may see repeated patterns.","zh":"如果數據在幾天內收集，研究人員可能看見重複模式。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the length of time in which something happens.","zh":"這個片語說明某事發生的時間長度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"device attached to the wrist","meaning":"綁在手腕上的裝置","examples":[{"en":"A device attached to each volunteer’s wrist recorded movement.","zh":"綁在每位參加者手腕上的裝置記錄動作。"},{"en":"A device attached to the wrist is a small tool worn on the wrist to measure or record something.","zh":"Device attached to the wrist 是戴在手腕上，用來量度或記錄某事的小工具。"},{"en":"A fitness watch is a device attached to the wrist that can count steps.","zh":"健身手錶就是綁在手腕上的裝置，可以計算步數。"},{"en":"If wrist devices record movement, researchers can study tapping without watching every participant.","zh":"如果手腕裝置記錄動作，研究人員就不用一直觀察每位參加者也能研究打拍子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wearable recording equipment.","zh":"這個片語描述可穿戴記錄設備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"record their movements","meaning":"記錄他們的動作","examples":[{"en":"The wrist device recorded the volunteers’ movements.","zh":"手腕裝置記錄了參加者的動作。"},{"en":"To record their movements means to measure and save information about how people move.","zh":"To record their movements 指量度並保存關於人們如何移動的資料。"},{"en":"A sports app can record runners’ movements during training.","zh":"運動應用程式可以記錄跑步者訓練時的動作。"},{"en":"If researchers record hand movements, they can compare tapping speed with a song’s tempo.","zh":"如果研究人員記錄手部動作，他們可以把打拍速度與歌曲速度比較。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collecting movement data.","zh":"這個片語描述收集動作數據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tapping tempo","meaning":"打拍子的速度","examples":[{"en":"The tapping tempo was compared with the original recording.","zh":"打拍子的速度被拿來與原本錄音作比較。"},{"en":"Tapping tempo is the speed at which someone taps to match a rhythm.","zh":"Tapping tempo 是某人為配合節奏而打拍子的速度。"},{"en":"A music teacher may check a student’s tapping tempo before teaching a new song.","zh":"音樂老師可能在教新歌前檢查學生打拍子的速度。"},{"en":"If tapping tempo is close to the recording, the listener remembers the speed well.","zh":"如果打拍子的速度接近錄音，聽者就很好地記住了歌曲速度。"},{"en":"This phrase links physical tapping with musical speed.","zh":"這個片語把身體打拍與音樂速度連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"within ten per cent of","meaning":"與……相差不超過百分之十","examples":[{"en":"The imagined tempos were within ten per cent of the originals.","zh":"想像中的速度與原本速度相差不超過百分之十。"},{"en":"Within ten per cent of something means no more than ten per cent higher or lower than it.","zh":"Within ten per cent of something 指比某數值高或低不超過百分之十。"},{"en":"If a bill estimate is within ten per cent of the final price, it is fairly accurate.","zh":"如果帳單估算與最終價格相差不超過百分之十，它就相當準確。"},{"en":"When volunteers tap within ten per cent of a song’s tempo, their memory is close to the real version.","zh":"當參加者打拍速度與歌曲速度相差不超過百分之十，他們的記憶就接近真實版本。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a small margin of difference.","zh":"這個片語顯示差異幅度很小。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"original recordings","meaning":"原本錄音","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers’ tapping closely matched the original recordings.","zh":"參加者的打拍與原本錄音非常吻合。"},{"en":"Original recordings are the real versions of songs used as the standard for comparison.","zh":"Original recordings 是用作比較標準的歌曲真實版本。"},{"en":"A music student may compare their singing with the original recordings to check timing.","zh":"音樂學生可能把自己的歌唱與原本錄音比較，以檢查時間掌握。"},{"en":"If remembered music matches original recordings, the memory contains accurate musical details.","zh":"如果記憶中的音樂與原本錄音相符，那段記憶就包含準確音樂細節。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the actual recorded songs, not later memory or imitation.","zh":"這個片語指實際錄製的歌曲，而不是後來的記憶或模仿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"report hearing earworms often","meaning":"表示經常出現洗腦旋律","examples":[{"en":"Some people report hearing earworms often.","zh":"有些人表示經常出現洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"To report hearing earworms often means to say that repeated mental music happens frequently.","zh":"To report hearing earworms often 指說自己經常經歷腦中音樂反覆出現。"},{"en":"A student may report hearing earworms often during quiet revision periods.","zh":"學生可能表示在安靜溫習時經常出現洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"If many people report the same experience, researchers may look for shared causes.","zh":"如果許多人報告同一經驗，研究人員可能尋找共同原因。"},{"en":"This phrase describes self-reported frequency, not direct brain measurement.","zh":"這個片語描述自我報告的頻率，而不是直接腦部測量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"find them intrusive","meaning":"覺得它們造成滋擾","examples":[{"en":"Some people find earworms intrusive and distracting.","zh":"有些人覺得洗腦旋律造成滋擾並令人分心。"},{"en":"To find them intrusive means to feel that they enter your thoughts unwanted and disturb you.","zh":"To find them intrusive 指覺得它們不受歡迎地進入思想並造成干擾。"},{"en":"A student may find phone notifications intrusive while trying to read.","zh":"學生嘗試閱讀時，可能覺得手機通知造成滋擾。"},{"en":"If earworms interrupt concentration, people may experience them as annoying rather than enjoyable.","zh":"如果洗腦旋律打斷專注，人們可能覺得它們煩人，而不是有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something enters mental space without welcome.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事不受歡迎地進入心理空間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"slightly different brain structures","meaning":"略有不同的大腦結構","examples":[{"en":"Frequent earworm sufferers may have slightly different brain structures.","zh":"經常受洗腦旋律困擾的人可能有略有不同的大腦結構。"},{"en":"Slightly different brain structures means small differences in the size, shape, or tissue of brain areas.","zh":"Slightly different brain structures 指大腦區域的大小、形狀或組織有小差異。"},{"en":"Researchers may compare brain structures between people who learn music and those who do not.","zh":"研究人員可能比較學音樂和沒有學音樂的人之間的大腦結構。"},{"en":"If brain structures differ, scientists may ask whether the difference affects memory or emotion.","zh":"如果大腦結構不同，科學家可能會問這差異是否影響記憶或情緒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes small physical differences in the brain, not personality alone.","zh":"這個片語描述大腦中的細小身體差異，而不只是性格。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"gray matter","meaning":"灰質","examples":[{"en":"Some participants had more gray matter in particular brain regions.","zh":"一些參加者在特定大腦區域有更多灰質。"},{"en":"Gray matter is brain tissue that contains many nerve cell bodies and helps process information.","zh":"Gray matter 是含有許多神經細胞體並幫助處理資訊的腦組織。"},{"en":"Brain scans can measure gray matter in areas linked with memory and emotion.","zh":"腦掃描可以量度與記憶和情緒相關區域的灰質。"},{"en":"If one group has more gray matter in a region, scientists may study what that region does.","zh":"如果某群體在某區域有更多灰質，科學家可能研究該區域的功能。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a physical part of the brain.","zh":"這個片語指大腦的身體部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"areas associated with","meaning":"與……有關的區域","examples":[{"en":"The differences appeared in areas associated with processing emotions.","zh":"差異出現在與處理情緒有關的區域。"},{"en":"Areas associated with something are parts of the brain or body linked to that function.","zh":"Areas associated with something 是與某功能有關的大腦或身體部分。"},{"en":"Doctors may study brain areas associated with language after a patient has speech problems.","zh":"病人出現語言問題後，醫生可能研究與語言有關的大腦區域。"},{"en":"If earworm differences appear in emotion-related areas, mood may be part of the explanation.","zh":"如果洗腦旋律差異出現在與情緒有關的區域，情緒可能是解釋的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a connection between a location and a function.","zh":"這個片語顯示位置與功能之間的連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"process emotions","meaning":"處理情緒","examples":[{"en":"Certain brain regions help people process emotions.","zh":"某些大腦區域幫助人處理情緒。"},{"en":"To process emotions means to recognise, handle, and make sense of feelings.","zh":"To process emotions 指辨認、處理並理解感受。"},{"en":"A child may need time to process emotions after moving to a new school.","zh":"孩子轉到新學校後，可能需要時間處理情緒。"},{"en":"If music affects mood, the brain regions that process emotions may become involved.","zh":"如果音樂影響心情，處理情緒的大腦區域可能參與其中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental handling of feelings, not just having feelings.","zh":"這個片語描述心理上處理感受，而不只是有感受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"low cognitive load","meaning":"低認知負荷","examples":[{"en":"Earworms often occur during periods of low cognitive load.","zh":"洗腦旋律常在低認知負荷時期出現。"},{"en":"Low cognitive load means the mind is not using much attention, memory, or problem-solving effort.","zh":"Low cognitive load 指大腦沒有使用太多注意力、記憶或解難努力。"},{"en":"Folding clothes creates low cognitive load because the task is simple and repetitive.","zh":"摺衣服造成低認知負荷，因為任務簡單而重複。"},{"en":"When cognitive load is low, the brain may have space for music to appear.","zh":"當認知負荷低，大腦可能有空間讓音樂出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes easy mental conditions, not physical tiredness only.","zh":"這個片語描述容易的心理狀態，而不只是身體疲倦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"while doing chores","meaning":"做家務時","examples":[{"en":"People often experience earworms while doing chores.","zh":"人們常在做家務時經歷洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"While doing chores means during routine household tasks such as washing dishes, cleaning, or folding clothes.","zh":"While doing chores 指在洗碗、清潔或摺衣服等日常家務期間。"},{"en":"A person may hum a song while doing chores because the work does not require deep thought.","zh":"一個人做家務時可能哼歌，因為工作不需要深入思考。"},{"en":"If chores are repetitive, the mind may drift and an earworm may begin.","zh":"如果家務重複，大腦可能游離，洗腦旋律可能開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common everyday situation for automatic thoughts.","zh":"這個片語描述自動思想常出現的日常情境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"liken something to","meaning":"把……比作……","examples":[{"en":"Dr Stewart likens earworms to sonic screen savers.","zh":"Stewart博士把洗腦旋律比作聲音版屏幕保護程式。"},{"en":"To liken something to something else means to compare the two because they are similar in some way.","zh":"To liken something to something else 指因兩者在某方面相似而把它們作比較。"},{"en":"A teacher may liken memory to a filing cabinet to make the idea clearer.","zh":"老師可能把記憶比作文件櫃，以令概念更清楚。"},{"en":"If earworms are likened to screen savers, they are presented as something that fills an idle mind.","zh":"如果洗腦旋律被比作屏幕保護程式，它們就被呈現為填補閒置大腦的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a comparison that helps explain an idea.","zh":"這個片語引入有助解釋想法的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sonic screen savers","meaning":"聲音版屏幕保護程式","examples":[{"en":"Earworms may act like sonic screen savers for an idle mind.","zh":"洗腦旋律可能像閒置大腦的聲音版屏幕保護程式。"},{"en":"Sonic screen savers are imagined sound patterns that fill the mind when it has little else to do.","zh":"Sonic screen savers 是當大腦沒有其他事情可做時，填補思想的想像聲音模式。"},{"en":"A bored commuter may experience a song like a sonic screen saver while staring out of a window.","zh":"沉悶通勤者望出窗外時，可能經歷一首像聲音版屏幕保護程式的歌曲。"},{"en":"If the mind is idle, repeated music may keep it lightly occupied.","zh":"如果大腦閒置，重複音樂可能令它輕微保持有事可做。"},{"en":"This metaphor compares mental music to a screen saver on a computer.","zh":"這個比喻把心理音樂比作電腦屏幕保護程式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"keep the mind entertained","meaning":"令大腦保持有事可做","examples":[{"en":"Earworms may keep the mind entertained when it is unoccupied.","zh":"當大腦沒有事情佔用時，洗腦旋律可能令大腦保持有事可做。"},{"en":"To keep the mind entertained means to give the brain something interesting to process.","zh":"To keep the mind entertained 指給大腦一些有趣的東西去處理。"},{"en":"A puzzle can keep the mind entertained during a long train journey.","zh":"益智遊戲可以在漫長火車旅程中令大腦保持有事可做。"},{"en":"If a task is boring, an earworm may keep the mind entertained in the background.","zh":"如果任務沉悶，洗腦旋律可能在背景中令大腦保持有事可做。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests mental occupation rather than serious learning.","zh":"這個片語暗示心理上有事可做，而不是嚴肅學習。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"otherwise unoccupied","meaning":"在沒有其他事情佔用時","examples":[{"en":"The mind may generate music when it is otherwise unoccupied.","zh":"大腦在沒有其他事情佔用時，可能產生音樂。"},{"en":"Otherwise unoccupied means not busy with any other task or thought.","zh":"Otherwise unoccupied 指沒有忙於其他任務或想法。"},{"en":"A person waiting alone at a bus stop may be otherwise unoccupied.","zh":"一個人在巴士站獨自等候時，可能沒有其他事情佔用。"},{"en":"If the mind is otherwise unoccupied, it may fill the space with memories, worries, or music.","zh":"如果大腦沒有其他事情佔用，它可能用記憶、擔憂或音樂填補空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes spare mental capacity.","zh":"這個片語描述空出的心理容量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"test a theory","meaning":"驗證理論","examples":[{"en":"Stewart and her colleagues tested the theory in an experiment.","zh":"Stewart和她的同事在實驗中驗證該理論。"},{"en":"To test a theory means to check whether an explanation is supported by evidence.","zh":"To test a theory 指檢查某解釋是否得到證據支持。"},{"en":"A teacher may test a theory about revision by comparing two study methods.","zh":"老師可能透過比較兩種溫習方法來驗證關於溫習的理論。"},{"en":"If an experiment supports the theory, researchers may become more confident in it.","zh":"如果實驗支持該理論，研究人員可能對它更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes turning an idea into something that can be checked.","zh":"這個片語描述把想法變成可檢驗的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"give someone various tasks","meaning":"給某人不同任務","examples":[{"en":"The researchers gave volunteers various tasks after playing songs.","zh":"研究人員播放歌曲後，給參加者不同任務。"},{"en":"To give someone various tasks means to ask them to do several different activities.","zh":"To give someone various tasks 指要求某人做幾種不同活動。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students various tasks, such as reading, writing, and speaking practice.","zh":"老師可能給學生不同任務，例如閱讀、寫作和口語練習。"},{"en":"If volunteers do different tasks, researchers can compare which conditions produce earworms.","zh":"如果參加者做不同任務，研究人員可以比較哪些條件會產生洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"This phrase describes assigning different activities for study or practice.","zh":"這個片語描述為研究或練習分配不同活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sit idly","meaning":"閒坐着","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers who sat idly were more likely to hear earworms.","zh":"閒坐着的參加者更有可能聽到洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"To sit idly means to sit without doing anything active or demanding.","zh":"To sit idly 指坐着而沒有做任何主動或費力的事情。"},{"en":"A student who sits idly before class may start thinking about a song or a worry.","zh":"學生上課前閒坐着時，可能開始想起一首歌或一件擔心的事。"},{"en":"If people sit idly after hearing music, the tune may have space to return.","zh":"如果人們聽完音樂後閒坐着，旋律可能有空間回來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a passive state with little mental effort.","zh":"這個片語描述低心理努力的被動狀態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be most likely to","meaning":"最有可能……","examples":[{"en":"Idle participants were most likely to report hearing music internally.","zh":"閒置的參加者最有可能報告自己在內心聽到音樂。"},{"en":"To be most likely to do something means to have the highest chance of doing it.","zh":"To be most likely to do something 指做某事的機會最高。"},{"en":"Students who revise regularly are most likely to remember vocabulary in exams.","zh":"定期溫習的學生最有可能在考試中記得詞彙。"},{"en":"If idle people are most likely to hear earworms, boredom may be part of the cause.","zh":"如果閒置的人最有可能聽到洗腦旋律，沉悶可能是成因之一。"},{"en":"This phrase compares probability between groups or situations.","zh":"這個片語比較不同群體或情況的可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the more …, the less likely …","meaning":"越……，便越不可能……","examples":[{"en":"The more challenging the task, the less likely an earworm was to occur.","zh":"任務越具挑戰性，洗腦旋律便越不可能出現。"},{"en":"The more…, the less likely… means as one thing increases, the chance of another thing decreases.","zh":"The more…, the less likely… 指一件事增加時，另一件事發生的機會下降。"},{"en":"The more carefully students check answers, the less likely they are to make simple mistakes.","zh":"學生越仔細檢查答案，就越不可能犯簡單錯誤。"},{"en":"If a task demands more attention, the brain has less spare space for repeated music.","zh":"如果任務需要更多注意力，大腦就有較少空間播放重複音樂。"},{"en":"This structure clearly shows an opposite relationship between two things.","zh":"這個結構清楚顯示兩件事之間的相反關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"challenging activity","meaning":"具挑戰性的活動","examples":[{"en":"A challenging activity can reduce the occurrence of earworms.","zh":"具挑戰性的活動可以減少洗腦旋律出現。"},{"en":"A challenging activity is a task that requires attention, effort, and problem-solving.","zh":"Challenging activity 是需要注意力、努力和解難能力的任務。"},{"en":"Solving a difficult puzzle is a challenging activity because it keeps the mind busy.","zh":"解一道困難謎題是具挑戰性的活動，因為它令大腦保持忙碌。"},{"en":"If the mind is focused on a challenging activity, unwanted music may occur less often.","zh":"如果大腦專注於具挑戰性的活動，不想要的音樂可能較少出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an activity that uses mental effort.","zh":"這個片語描述使用心理努力的活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"match people’s moods","meaning":"配合人們的情緒","examples":[{"en":"The songs in people’s heads often match their moods.","zh":"人們腦海中的歌曲常配合他們的情緒。"},{"en":"To match people’s moods means to fit or reflect how people are feeling.","zh":"To match people’s moods 指符合或反映人們的感受。"},{"en":"A slow song may match someone’s mood when they feel tired or sad.","zh":"當某人疲倦或傷心時，慢歌可能配合他的情緒。"},{"en":"If a person feels energetic, a fast earworm may match that feeling.","zh":"如果一個人感到精力充沛，快節奏洗腦旋律可能配合那種感覺。"},{"en":"This phrase connects music choice with emotional state.","zh":"這個片語把音樂選擇與情緒狀態連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not random","meaning":"並非隨機","examples":[{"en":"The choice of earworm is often not random.","zh":"洗腦旋律的選擇通常並非隨機。"},{"en":"Not random means not happening by pure chance, but influenced by a pattern or cause.","zh":"Not random 指不是純粹偶然發生，而是受到模式或原因影響。"},{"en":"A student’s mistakes are not random if they always occur with past tense verbs.","zh":"如果學生的錯誤總是出現在過去式動詞上，那些錯誤就並非隨機。"},{"en":"If earworms match mood and recent listening, their appearance may follow clear influences.","zh":"如果洗腦旋律配合情緒和近期聆聽，它們的出現可能跟隨清楚影響。"},{"en":"This phrase tells us to look for reasons behind a pattern.","zh":"這個片語提醒我們尋找模式背後的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"energised and upbeat","meaning":"精神充沛而樂觀的","examples":[{"en":"An energised and upbeat person may experience a faster song.","zh":"精神充沛而樂觀的人可能經歷一首較快的歌曲。"},{"en":"Energised and upbeat means feeling lively, positive, and full of energy.","zh":"Energised and upbeat 指感到有活力、正面並充滿能量。"},{"en":"After exercise, a student may feel energised and upbeat before starting homework.","zh":"運動後，學生開始做功課前可能感到精神充沛而樂觀。"},{"en":"If someone feels energised and upbeat, their mind may choose a brighter, faster tune.","zh":"如果某人精神充沛而樂觀，他的大腦可能選擇更明亮、更快的旋律。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a positive and active mood.","zh":"這個片語描述正面而活躍的情緒。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be likely to be uptempo","meaning":"可能節奏明快","examples":[{"en":"An earworm is likely to be uptempo when the listener feels energetic.","zh":"當聽者感到有活力，洗腦旋律可能節奏明快。"},{"en":"To be likely to be uptempo means to probably have a fast, lively beat.","zh":"To be likely to be uptempo 指很可能有快速、活潑的節拍。"},{"en":"A workout song is likely to be uptempo because it helps people move quickly.","zh":"運動歌曲可能節奏明快，因為它幫助人快速移動。"},{"en":"If a person is in a cheerful mood, an uptempo tune may fit their energy.","zh":"如果一個人心情愉快，節奏明快的旋律可能符合他的能量。"},{"en":"This phrase connects probability with musical speed and mood.","zh":"這個片語把可能性與音樂速度和情緒連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fixate on","meaning":"執着於；反覆想着……","examples":[{"en":"The brain may fixate on songs heard recently.","zh":"大腦可能執着於最近聽過的歌曲。"},{"en":"To fixate on something means to keep focusing on it in a repeated or unusually strong way.","zh":"To fixate on something 指以重複或異常強烈的方式持續集中於某事。"},{"en":"A student may fixate on one small mistake after a presentation.","zh":"學生演講後可能反覆想着一個小錯誤。"},{"en":"If the brain fixates on a recent song, the tune may return again and again.","zh":"如果大腦執着於最近聽過的歌曲，旋律可能一次又一次回來。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests repeated attention that is hard to stop.","zh":"這個片語暗示難以停止的重複注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be exposed to","meaning":"接觸到……","examples":[{"en":"The brain often repeats music it has been exposed to recently.","zh":"大腦常重複最近接觸到的音樂。"},{"en":"To be exposed to something means to come into contact with it or experience it.","zh":"To be exposed to something 指接觸或經歷某事。"},{"en":"Children exposed to different accents may become better at understanding spoken English.","zh":"接觸到不同口音的兒童，可能更擅長理解英語口語。"},{"en":"If you are exposed to a song many times, you may remember it without trying.","zh":"如果你多次接觸到一首歌，你可能不費力也記住它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes contact that can influence memory or behaviour.","zh":"這個片語描述可以影響記憶或行為的接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"receive heavy radio play","meaning":"在電台頻繁播放","examples":[{"en":"Songs receiving heavy radio play often become earworms.","zh":"在電台頻繁播放的歌曲常變成洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"To receive heavy radio play means to be played very often on radio stations.","zh":"To receive heavy radio play 指在電台非常經常地被播放。"},{"en":"A summer pop song may receive heavy radio play if many listeners request it.","zh":"如果許多聽眾點播，一首夏日流行歌可能在電台頻繁播放。"},{"en":"If people hear a song repeatedly on the radio, it may become familiar and memorable.","zh":"如果人們反覆在電台聽到一首歌，它可能變得熟悉又容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes frequent public broadcasting of a song.","zh":"這個片語描述歌曲被頻繁公開廣播。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"top the earworm charts","meaning":"成為最常見的洗腦歌曲","examples":[{"en":"Frequently played songs often top the earworm charts.","zh":"經常播放的歌曲常成為最常見的洗腦歌曲。"},{"en":"To top the earworm charts means to be among the songs most often reported as stuck in people’s heads.","zh":"To top the earworm charts 指成為最常被報告在腦海中揮之不去的歌曲之一。"},{"en":"A catchy pop song may top the earworm charts after being used in many adverts.","zh":"一首易記流行歌如果被許多廣告使用，可能成為最常見的洗腦歌曲。"},{"en":"If a song has a strong chorus, more people may report it as an earworm.","zh":"如果歌曲有強烈副歌，更多人可能報告它是洗腦歌。"},{"en":"This phrase uses “charts” like music rankings, but for mental repetition.","zh":"這個片語像音樂排行榜一樣使用 “charts”，但指心理重複。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pay attention to","meaning":"留意……","examples":[{"en":"A song can return later even if you did not pay attention to it.","zh":"即使你沒有留意一首歌，它之後也可以回來。"},{"en":"To pay attention to something means to notice it carefully and focus on it.","zh":"To pay attention to something 指仔細注意並集中於某事。"},{"en":"A student may not pay attention to background music while studying in a café.","zh":"學生在咖啡店溫習時，可能沒有留意背景音樂。"},{"en":"If the brain records a song without attention, it may return later as an earworm.","zh":"如果大腦在沒有注意下記錄一首歌，它之後可能以洗腦旋律形式回來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active noticing, not just being near something.","zh":"這個片語描述主動注意，而不只是接近某事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"worm its way into","meaning":"悄悄鑽進……","examples":[{"en":"A tune can worm its way into the subconscious.","zh":"一段旋律可以悄悄鑽進潛意識。"},{"en":"To worm its way into something means to enter slowly, quietly, or without being noticed.","zh":"To worm its way into something 指慢慢、安靜或不被察覺地進入某處。"},{"en":"A catchy slogan can worm its way into a shopper’s mind after repeated adverts.","zh":"一句易記口號在廣告反覆播放後，可以悄悄鑽進購物者腦中。"},{"en":"If music plays in the background, it may enter memory without conscious attention.","zh":"如果音樂在背景播放，它可能在沒有意識注意下進入記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something sneaks into the mind gradually.","zh":"這個片語暗示某事逐漸偷偷進入腦海。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"subconscious","meaning":"潛意識","examples":[{"en":"Music may remain in the subconscious without conscious awareness.","zh":"音樂可能在沒有意識察覺下留在潛意識中。"},{"en":"The subconscious is the part of the mind that stores thoughts or memories outside conscious attention.","zh":"Subconscious 是儲存意識注意之外的思想或記憶的心智部分。"},{"en":"A smell from childhood may stay in the subconscious and later bring back memories.","zh":"童年時的氣味可能留在潛意識中，之後帶回記憶。"},{"en":"If a song enters the subconscious, it may return even when you do not remember hearing it.","zh":"如果一首歌進入潛意識，即使你不記得聽過它，它也可能回來。"},{"en":"This word refers to mental activity below conscious awareness.","zh":"這個詞指低於意識察覺的心理活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"unpublished study","meaning":"未出版的研究","examples":[{"en":"The passage refers to an unpublished study by Ira Hyman.","zh":"文章提到Ira Hyman的一項未出版研究。"},{"en":"An unpublished study is research that has not yet appeared formally in a journal or book.","zh":"Unpublished study 是尚未正式刊登於期刊或書籍的研究。"},{"en":"A university team may discuss an unpublished study at a conference before submitting it.","zh":"大學團隊可能在提交前，於會議上討論一項未出版研究。"},{"en":"If a study is unpublished, readers should treat its findings carefully until more details are available.","zh":"如果研究尚未出版，讀者應謹慎看待其發現，直到有更多細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research that exists but is not formally published.","zh":"這個片語描述已存在但未正式出版的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"listen to music while doing other tasks","meaning":"一邊做其他事情一邊聽音樂","examples":[{"en":"Some participants listened to music while doing other tasks.","zh":"一些參加者一邊做其他事情一邊聽音樂。"},{"en":"To listen to music while doing other tasks means to hear music in the background during another activity.","zh":"To listen to music while doing other tasks 指在做另一項活動時把音樂作為背景聽。"},{"en":"A student may listen to music while doing homework or tidying a room.","zh":"學生可能一邊做功課或整理房間，一邊聽音樂。"},{"en":"If attention is divided, the song may be stored without being fully noticed.","zh":"如果注意力被分散，歌曲可能在沒有被完全留意下被儲存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes multitasking with music.","zh":"這個片語描述伴隨音樂的多工活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be more likely to report","meaning":"更有可能表示……","examples":[{"en":"Multitasking participants were more likely to report later earworms.","zh":"多工參加者更有可能表示之後出現洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"To be more likely to report something means to have a higher chance of saying that it happened.","zh":"To be more likely to report something 指表示某事發生的機會較高。"},{"en":"Students who study late may be more likely to report tiredness the next morning.","zh":"晚睡溫習的學生第二朝更有可能表示疲倦。"},{"en":"If multitasking listeners report more earworms, divided attention may play a role.","zh":"如果多工聽眾更常報告洗腦旋律，分散注意力可能有作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a higher reported probability in one group.","zh":"這個片語描述某群體報告某事的可能性較高。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"return as earworms","meaning":"以洗腦旋律形式再次出現","examples":[{"en":"Songs heard in the background may return as earworms.","zh":"在背景中聽到的歌曲可能以洗腦旋律形式再次出現。"},{"en":"To return as earworms means to come back later as repeated music in the mind.","zh":"To return as earworms 指之後以腦中重複音樂的形式回來。"},{"en":"A song from a supermarket may return as an earworm hours after shopping.","zh":"超級市場歌曲可能在購物數小時後以洗腦旋律形式再次出現。"},{"en":"If background music is catchy, it may return later even when the listener is alone.","zh":"如果背景音樂易記，即使聽者獨處時，它也可能之後回來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes music reappearing mentally after earlier exposure.","zh":"這個片語描述音樂在早前接觸後於心理上再次出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"The results were compared with those of participants who only listened.","zh":"這些結果與只聽音樂的參加者結果相比。"},{"en":"Compared with means examined beside another person, group, or result to see differences.","zh":"Compared with 指把某人、群體或結果放在另一者旁邊檢視差異。"},{"en":"A student’s latest essay can be compared with an earlier one to measure progress.","zh":"學生最新作文可以與早前作文相比，以量度進步。"},{"en":"If multitasking listeners differ from focused listeners, comparison helps reveal the effect of attention.","zh":"如果多工聽眾與專注聽眾不同，比較有助揭示注意力的影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to show contrast between two sets of data or situations.","zh":"這個片語用於顯示兩組數據或情況之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fragments of a song","meaning":"歌曲片段","examples":[{"en":"Some earworms consist of only fragments of a song.","zh":"有些洗腦旋律只由歌曲片段組成。"},{"en":"Fragments of a song are short pieces of music rather than the whole song.","zh":"Fragments of a song 是音樂的短小部分，而不是整首歌曲。"},{"en":"A person may remember only one line of a chorus as a song fragment.","zh":"一個人可能只記得副歌中的一句作為歌曲片段。"},{"en":"If the brain cannot recall the next part, a fragment may repeat again and again.","zh":"如果大腦不能回想下一部分，歌曲片段可能一次又一次重複。"},{"en":"This phrase describes incomplete musical pieces.","zh":"這個片語描述不完整的音樂片段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"repeat like a broken record","meaning":"像壞掉的唱片般重複","examples":[{"en":"A short musical fragment may repeat like a broken record.","zh":"一小段音樂片段可能像壞掉的唱片般重複。"},{"en":"To repeat like a broken record means to repeat the same thing again and again without moving forward.","zh":"To repeat like a broken record 指同一件事一次又一次重複，沒有繼續下去。"},{"en":"A child asking the same question every minute may sound like a broken record.","zh":"每分鐘問同一問題的孩子，可能聽起來像壞掉的唱片。"},{"en":"If a song fragment repeats like a broken record, the listener may feel trapped by it.","zh":"如果歌曲片段像壞掉的唱片般重複，聽者可能感到被困住。"},{"en":"This phrase compares repetition to an old record that cannot continue properly.","zh":"這個片語把重複比作不能正常繼續的舊唱片。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hit a part of","meaning":"到達……部分","examples":[{"en":"The mind may hit a part of the song it cannot remember.","zh":"大腦可能到達歌曲中它不能記住的部分。"},{"en":"To hit a part of something means to reach that point in a sequence.","zh":"To hit a part of something 指到達一個序列中的某一點。"},{"en":"A student telling a story may hit a part they cannot explain clearly.","zh":"學生講故事時可能到達一個自己不能清楚解釋的部分。"},{"en":"If the mind hits a forgotten section of a song, it may go back to the beginning.","zh":"如果大腦到達歌曲中忘記了的部分，它可能回到開頭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching a point that creates a problem or pause.","zh":"這個片語描述到達會造成問題或停頓的一點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"loop back","meaning":"循環返回前面","examples":[{"en":"The tune loops back when the next section cannot be recalled.","zh":"當下一段無法被回想起來，旋律就循環返回前面。"},{"en":"To loop back means to return to an earlier point and repeat from there.","zh":"To loop back 指返回較早位置並從那裡重複。"},{"en":"A video may loop back to the start after it finishes playing.","zh":"影片播放完後可能循環返回開頭。"},{"en":"If the brain forgets the next line, the song may loop back to the part it knows.","zh":"如果大腦忘記下一句，歌曲可能循環返回它知道的部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes circular repetition.","zh":"這個片語描述循環式重複。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rather than moving on","meaning":"而不是繼續下去","examples":[{"en":"The mind repeats the fragment rather than moving on.","zh":"大腦重複該片段，而不是繼續下去。"},{"en":"Rather than moving on means instead of continuing to the next part.","zh":"Rather than moving on 指而不是繼續到下一部分。"},{"en":"A student may keep rereading one sentence rather than moving on to the next paragraph.","zh":"學生可能一直重讀同一句，而不是繼續讀下一段。"},{"en":"If the brain cannot recall the next musical phrase, it repeats the old one instead.","zh":"如果大腦不能回想下一句音樂短句，它就改為重複舊短句。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly contrasts repetition with progress.","zh":"這個片語清楚對比重複與推進。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"become more entrenched","meaning":"變得更根深蒂固","examples":[{"en":"Repeated fragments may make an earworm more entrenched.","zh":"重複的片段可能令洗腦旋律變得更根深蒂固。"},{"en":"To become more entrenched means to become more fixed, established, and difficult to remove.","zh":"To become more entrenched 指變得更固定、更牢固，並更難移除。"},{"en":"A bad study habit can become more entrenched if a student repeats it every night.","zh":"如果學生每晚重複壞溫習習慣，該習慣可能變得更根深蒂固。"},{"en":"If a song fragment repeats many times, it may become harder to stop thinking about it.","zh":"如果歌曲片段重複很多次，它可能變得更難停止想起。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something becoming deeply stuck.","zh":"這個片語描述某事變得深深卡住。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"according to a theory known as","meaning":"根據一個稱為……的理論","examples":[{"en":"According to a theory known as the Zeigarnik effect, unfinished tasks remain active in memory.","zh":"根據一個稱為蔡格尼克效應的理論，未完成任務會在記憶中保持活躍。"},{"en":"According to a theory known as introduces an explanation that has a specific name.","zh":"According to a theory known as 用來引入一個有特定名稱的解釋。"},{"en":"According to a theory known as spaced repetition, review works better when spread over time.","zh":"根據一個稱為間隔重複的理論，把溫習分散在不同時間會更有效。"},{"en":"If a writer names a theory, readers can connect the idea with a wider area of research.","zh":"如果作者命名一個理論，讀者就能把想法與更廣泛研究連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to introduce a recognised explanation.","zh":"這個片語用於引入公認的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Zeigarnik effect","meaning":"蔡格尼克效應","examples":[{"en":"The Zeigarnik effect concerns the mental impact of unfinished activities.","zh":"蔡格尼克效應關於未完成活動的心理影響。"},{"en":"The Zeigarnik effect is the idea that unfinished tasks may stay more active in memory than completed tasks.","zh":"Zeigarnik effect 是指未完成任務可能比已完成任務在記憶中更活躍的想法。"},{"en":"A student may keep thinking about an unfinished essay even after leaving school.","zh":"學生離開學校後，可能仍一直想起未完成的作文。"},{"en":"If a song stops before the chorus ends, the unfinished feeling may make it return mentally.","zh":"如果歌曲在副歌結束前停止，未完成感可能令它在腦中回來。"},{"en":"This phrase names a memory effect linked to incomplete actions.","zh":"這個片語命名與未完成行動有關的記憶效應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be named for","meaning":"以……命名","examples":[{"en":"The effect was named for the psychologist Bluma Zeigarnik.","zh":"這個效應以心理學家Bluma Zeigarnik命名。"},{"en":"To be named for someone means to be given a name because of that person.","zh":"To be named for someone 指因某人而被賦予某個名稱。"},{"en":"A school building may be named for a teacher who served the community for decades.","zh":"一棟校舍可能以服務社區數十年的老師命名。"},{"en":"If a discovery is named for a researcher, the name preserves their contribution.","zh":"如果一項發現以研究人員命名，該名稱就保存了其貢獻。"},{"en":"This phrase explains where a name comes from.","zh":"這個片語解釋名稱來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"unfinished thoughts","meaning":"未完成的想法","examples":[{"en":"Unfinished thoughts may remain more active in the mind.","zh":"未完成的想法可能在腦中保持更活躍。"},{"en":"Unfinished thoughts are ideas, worries, or tasks that feel incomplete.","zh":"Unfinished thoughts 是感覺尚未完成的想法、擔憂或任務。"},{"en":"A student may have unfinished thoughts about a difficult question after an exam.","zh":"考試後，學生可能對一道困難題目有未完成的想法。"},{"en":"If a thought is unfinished, the mind may return to it again and again.","zh":"如果一個想法未完成，大腦可能一次又一次回到它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental material that has not reached closure.","zh":"這個片語描述尚未得到結束感的心理內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"weigh on the mind","meaning":"沉重地佔據腦海","examples":[{"en":"Incomplete activities can weigh on the mind more heavily.","zh":"未完成活動可以更沉重地佔據腦海。"},{"en":"To weigh on the mind means to trouble someone’s thoughts and feel mentally heavy.","zh":"To weigh on the mind 指困擾某人的思想，令人感到心理沉重。"},{"en":"An unpaid bill may weigh on a parent’s mind during the day.","zh":"未付帳單可能整天沉重地佔據父母腦海。"},{"en":"If an unfinished task weighs on the mind, it may keep returning until it is completed.","zh":"如果未完成任務佔據腦海，它可能一直回來直到完成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a thought that feels burdensome.","zh":"這個片語描述感覺有負擔的想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"more heavily than","meaning":"比……更強烈","examples":[{"en":"Unfinished tasks may affect memory more heavily than completed ones.","zh":"未完成任務可能比已完成任務更強烈地影響記憶。"},{"en":"More heavily than means with stronger weight, pressure, or influence than something else.","zh":"More heavily than 指比另一事物有更大的重量、壓力或影響。"},{"en":"A serious deadline may weigh more heavily than a small classroom task.","zh":"重要截止日期可能比小型課堂任務更沉重地影響人。"},{"en":"If unfinished work affects memory more heavily, people may keep thinking about it.","zh":"如果未完成工作更強烈地影響記憶，人們可能一直想起它。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the strength of two effects.","zh":"這個片語比較兩種影響的強度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"expose students to","meaning":"讓學生接觸……","examples":[{"en":"Researchers exposed students to interrupted songs.","zh":"研究人員讓學生接觸被中斷的歌曲。"},{"en":"To expose students to something means to let them experience or come into contact with it.","zh":"To expose students to something 指讓學生經歷或接觸某事。"},{"en":"Teachers expose students to different accents so listening becomes easier.","zh":"老師讓學生接觸不同口音，使聆聽變得更容易。"},{"en":"If students are exposed to interrupted songs, researchers can test whether unfinished music returns later.","zh":"如果學生接觸被中斷的歌曲，研究人員可以測試未完成音樂是否之後回來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes controlled contact for learning or research.","zh":"這個片語描述為學習或研究而安排的受控接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"interrupted songs","meaning":"被中斷的歌曲","examples":[{"en":"Experiments have tested how people respond to interrupted songs.","zh":"實驗測試了人們如何回應被中斷的歌曲。"},{"en":"Interrupted songs are songs that stop before they finish or before the expected part arrives.","zh":"Interrupted songs 是在完成前或預期部分到來前停止的歌曲。"},{"en":"A song interrupted just before the chorus may feel unfinished and annoying.","zh":"一首剛到副歌前就被中斷的歌曲，可能令人感到未完成和煩躁。"},{"en":"If interrupted songs remain active in memory, they may become earworms later.","zh":"如果被中斷的歌曲在記憶中保持活躍，它們之後可能變成洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"This phrase describes music that is cut off too early.","zh":"這個片語描述太早被切斷的音樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"yield mixed results","meaning":"得出好壞參半的結果","examples":[{"en":"The experiments yielded mixed results.","zh":"這些實驗得出好壞參半的結果。"},{"en":"To yield mixed results means to produce findings that are not all clear or consistent.","zh":"To yield mixed results 指產生不完全清晰或一致的發現。"},{"en":"A new teaching method may yield mixed results if some students improve but others do not.","zh":"如果有些學生進步而另一些沒有，新教學方法可能得出好壞參半的結果。"},{"en":"If experiments yield mixed results, researchers need more tests before drawing firm conclusions.","zh":"如果實驗結果好壞參半，研究人員在得出確定結論前需要更多測試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence that is partly supportive and partly uncertain.","zh":"這個片語描述部分支持但部分不確定的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pinpoint a spot","meaning":"準確指出一個位置","examples":[{"en":"Scientists cannot pinpoint a single spot where earworms occur.","zh":"科學家無法準確指出洗腦旋律出現的單一位置。"},{"en":"To pinpoint a spot means to identify an exact location.","zh":"To pinpoint a spot 指識別一個準確位置。"},{"en":"A doctor may try to pinpoint the spot where a patient feels pain.","zh":"醫生可能嘗試準確指出病人感到疼痛的位置。"},{"en":"If many brain regions are involved, scientists cannot reduce earworms to one exact place.","zh":"如果許多腦區都參與其中，科學家就不能把洗腦旋律簡化為一個確切位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finding a precise location, not just a general area.","zh":"這個片語描述找出精確位置，而不只是大概區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"imaging studies","meaning":"腦部影像研究","examples":[{"en":"Imaging studies show which brain regions become active.","zh":"腦部影像研究顯示哪些大腦區域變得活躍。"},{"en":"Imaging studies are research studies that use scanning technology to look inside the body or brain.","zh":"Imaging studies 是使用掃描技術觀察身體或大腦內部的研究。"},{"en":"Doctors use imaging studies to examine injuries that cannot be seen from outside.","zh":"醫生使用影像研究檢查從外面看不到的傷患。"},{"en":"If imaging studies show brain activity during music, researchers can compare hearing and imagining music.","zh":"如果腦部影像研究顯示聽音樂時的大腦活動，研究人員可以比較聽音樂和想像音樂。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to studies using images from scans.","zh":"這個片語指使用掃描影像的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"deliberately imagine music","meaning":"刻意想像音樂","examples":[{"en":"Participants deliberately imagined music during brain scans.","zh":"參加者在腦掃描期間刻意想像音樂。"},{"en":"To deliberately imagine music means to intentionally create music in the mind.","zh":"To deliberately imagine music 指有意識地在腦中創造音樂。"},{"en":"A singer may deliberately imagine music before performing to remember the melody.","zh":"歌手演出前可能刻意想像音樂，以記住旋律。"},{"en":"If participants deliberately imagine music, researchers can study mental music at a chosen time.","zh":"如果參加者刻意想像音樂，研究人員就能在選定時間研究心理音樂。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts intentional imagining with involuntary earworms.","zh":"這個片語把有意想像與非自願洗腦旋律作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"actually listen to music","meaning":"實際聆聽音樂","examples":[{"en":"Imagining music and actually listening to it activate similar networks.","zh":"想像音樂和實際聆聽音樂會啟動相似網絡。"},{"en":"To actually listen to music means to hear real music through the ears, not only imagine it.","zh":"To actually listen to music 指透過耳朵聽到真實音樂，而不只是想像它。"},{"en":"A student may actually listen to music through headphones while travelling home.","zh":"學生回家途中可能透過耳機實際聆聽音樂。"},{"en":"If imagining music and hearing music activate similar areas, the brain treats them partly alike.","zh":"如果想像音樂和聽音樂啟動相似區域，大腦就部分地把它們相似處理。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts real listening with mental imagination.","zh":"這個片語把真實聆聽與心理想像作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"activate neurological networks","meaning":"啟動神經網絡","examples":[{"en":"Both imagined and real music activate neurological networks.","zh":"想像音樂和真實音樂都會啟動神經網絡。"},{"en":"To activate neurological networks means to make connected brain cells or brain areas become active.","zh":"To activate neurological networks 指令相連的腦細胞或腦區變得活躍。"},{"en":"Reading words aloud can activate neurological networks involved in language and sound.","zh":"大聲朗讀文字可以啟動涉及語言和聲音的神經網絡。"},{"en":"If music activates several networks, it may affect memory, movement, and emotion at once.","zh":"如果音樂啟動幾個網絡，它可能同時影響記憶、動作和情緒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes brain systems switching on during an activity.","zh":"這個片語描述大腦系統在活動中被啟動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"many of the same networks","meaning":"許多相同的神經網絡","examples":[{"en":"Imagining and hearing music involve many of the same networks.","zh":"想像和聽到音樂涉及許多相同的神經網絡。"},{"en":"Many of the same networks means a large number of identical or overlapping brain systems.","zh":"Many of the same networks 指大量相同或重疊的大腦系統。"},{"en":"Speaking and listening may use many of the same language networks.","zh":"說話和聆聽可能使用許多相同的語言網絡。"},{"en":"If imagining music uses many of the same networks as hearing it, mental music can feel vivid.","zh":"如果想像音樂使用許多與聽音樂相同的網絡，心理音樂就可以感覺生動。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights overlap between two processes.","zh":"這個片語突顯兩個過程之間的重疊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"first few notes","meaning":"開首幾個音符","examples":[{"en":"The first few notes of familiar music can trigger recognition.","zh":"熟悉音樂的開首幾個音符可以觸發辨認。"},{"en":"The first few notes are the opening sounds of a piece of music.","zh":"First few notes 是一段音樂開頭的聲音。"},{"en":"A listener may recognise a birthday song from the first few notes.","zh":"聽者可能從開首幾個音符認出生日歌。"},{"en":"If the first few notes are memorable, the brain may quickly predict the rest of the song.","zh":"如果開首幾個音符容易記住，大腦可能很快預測歌曲餘下部分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the very beginning of a melody.","zh":"這個片語指旋律的最開始部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"familiar music","meaning":"熟悉的音樂","examples":[{"en":"Familiar music activates particular regions of the brain.","zh":"熟悉的音樂會啟動大腦特定區域。"},{"en":"Familiar music is music that someone knows or has heard before.","zh":"Familiar music 是某人知道或以前聽過的音樂。"},{"en":"A childhood theme song may feel like familiar music after many years.","zh":"童年主題曲在多年後仍可能感覺像熟悉的音樂。"},{"en":"If music is familiar, the brain may recognise it quickly and expect what comes next.","zh":"如果音樂熟悉，大腦可能很快認出它並期待接下來的部分。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts known music with unfamiliar music.","zh":"這個片語把已知音樂與陌生音樂作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"right frontal portion","meaning":"右額葉部分","examples":[{"en":"The right frontal portion of the brain became active during familiar music.","zh":"熟悉音樂播放時，大腦右額葉部分變得活躍。"},{"en":"The right frontal portion is an area toward the front-right side of the brain.","zh":"Right frontal portion 是大腦前方右側的區域。"},{"en":"Brain scans may show activity in the right frontal portion during certain thinking tasks.","zh":"腦掃描可能顯示某些思考任務期間右額葉部分有活動。"},{"en":"If familiar music activates this area, it may be involved in recognition or expectation.","zh":"如果熟悉音樂啟動這個區域，它可能參與辨認或期待。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific brain region by location.","zh":"這個片語以位置命名特定腦區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"superior temporal portion","meaning":"顳上區","examples":[{"en":"The superior temporal portion also responded to familiar tunes.","zh":"顳上區也對熟悉旋律作出反應。"},{"en":"The superior temporal portion is an upper area of the temporal part of the brain, often linked with sound processing.","zh":"Superior temporal portion 是大腦顳葉上方區域，常與聲音處理有關。"},{"en":"Scientists may study the superior temporal portion when examining hearing and music.","zh":"科學家研究聽覺和音樂時，可能研究顳上區。"},{"en":"If this region responds to familiar tunes, it may help process remembered sound patterns.","zh":"如果這個區域對熟悉旋律有反應，它可能幫助處理記住的聲音模式。"},{"en":"This phrase names a brain area connected with auditory processing.","zh":"這個片語命名與聽覺處理有關的大腦區域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"become activated","meaning":"被啟動","examples":[{"en":"Several brain regions became activated when subjects heard familiar notes.","zh":"當受試者聽到熟悉音符時，幾個大腦區域被啟動。"},{"en":"To become activated means to start working or become active.","zh":"To become activated 指開始運作或變得活躍。"},{"en":"A phone screen becomes activated when someone taps it.","zh":"當有人輕觸手機螢幕，螢幕就被啟動。"},{"en":"If brain regions become activated during a task, researchers know they are involved in that process.","zh":"如果腦區在任務期間被啟動，研究人員就知道它們參與該過程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a system or area switching on.","zh":"這個片語描述系統或區域被開啟。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"supplementary motor area","meaning":"輔助運動區","examples":[{"en":"The supplementary motor area is involved in remembering sequences.","zh":"輔助運動區涉及記住次序。"},{"en":"The supplementary motor area is a brain region linked with planning movement and ordered sequences.","zh":"Supplementary motor area 是與規劃動作和有序次序有關的大腦區域。"},{"en":"A pianist may use brain systems like the supplementary motor area when remembering finger movements.","zh":"鋼琴家記住手指動作時，可能使用像輔助運動區這類大腦系統。"},{"en":"If music has a sequence, the brain may use this area to anticipate the next part.","zh":"如果音樂有次序，大腦可能使用這個區域來預測下一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase names a brain region involved in ordered action and memory.","zh":"這個片語命名涉及有序行動和記憶的腦區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be involved in","meaning":"涉及；參與……","examples":[{"en":"This brain region is involved in remembering sequences.","zh":"這個大腦區域涉及記住次序。"},{"en":"To be involved in something means to take part in it or have a role in it.","zh":"To be involved in something 指參與某事或在其中有作用。"},{"en":"Several teachers may be involved in planning a school concert.","zh":"幾位老師可能參與策劃學校音樂會。"},{"en":"If a brain region is involved in memory, damage to it may affect recall.","zh":"如果某腦區涉及記憶，該區受損可能影響回想。"},{"en":"This phrase shows participation or function.","zh":"這個片語顯示參與或功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"remember sequences","meaning":"記住次序","examples":[{"en":"The brain uses certain regions to remember musical sequences.","zh":"大腦使用某些區域來記住音樂次序。"},{"en":"To remember sequences means to recall items, sounds, movements, or events in the correct order.","zh":"To remember sequences 指以正確順序回想項目、聲音、動作或事件。"},{"en":"Students remember sequences when they learn the steps of a science experiment.","zh":"學生學習科學實驗步驟時，就是在記住次序。"},{"en":"If a person remembers a melody, they remember notes in order rather than separately.","zh":"如果一個人記住旋律，他是按次序記住音符，而不是分開記住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes memory for order.","zh":"這個片語描述對順序的記憶。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"unfamiliar music","meaning":"不熟悉的音樂","examples":[{"en":"Unfamiliar music produced a different pattern of brain activity.","zh":"不熟悉的音樂產生了不同的大腦活動模式。"},{"en":"Unfamiliar music is music that a person does not know or has not heard before.","zh":"Unfamiliar music 是某人不知道或以前未聽過的音樂。"},{"en":"A listener may need more attention when hearing unfamiliar music for the first time.","zh":"聽者第一次聽不熟悉的音樂時，可能需要更多注意力。"},{"en":"If music is unfamiliar, the brain cannot easily predict the next notes.","zh":"如果音樂不熟悉，大腦就不能輕易預測接下來的音符。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts new or unknown music with familiar music.","zh":"這個片語把新的或未知音樂與熟悉音樂作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be asked to recall","meaning":"被要求回想","examples":[{"en":"The subjects were asked to recall unfamiliar music.","zh":"受試者被要求回想不熟悉的音樂。"},{"en":"To be asked to recall something means to be requested to remember it.","zh":"To be asked to recall something 指被要求記起某事。"},{"en":"Students may be asked to recall key facts after reading a passage.","zh":"學生閱讀文章後，可能被要求回想關鍵事實。"},{"en":"If people are asked to recall unfamiliar music, the task may require effort and attention.","zh":"如果人們被要求回想不熟悉的音樂，該任務可能需要努力和注意力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a memory task set by someone else.","zh":"這個片語描述由他人設定的記憶任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"left frontal portions","meaning":"左額葉部分","examples":[{"en":"Unfamiliar music activated the left frontal portions of the brain.","zh":"不熟悉的音樂啟動了大腦左額葉部分。"},{"en":"Left frontal portions are areas toward the front-left side of the brain.","zh":"Left frontal portions 是大腦前方左側的區域。"},{"en":"Brain scans may show left frontal portions becoming active during difficult recall tasks.","zh":"腦掃描可能顯示困難回想任務期間左額葉部分變得活躍。"},{"en":"If unfamiliar music activates these areas, the brain may be working harder to reconstruct it.","zh":"如果不熟悉的音樂啟動這些區域，大腦可能正在更努力重建它。"},{"en":"This phrase names brain regions by their position.","zh":"這個片語以位置命名腦區。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"one factor that makes","meaning":"令……發生的其中一個因素","examples":[{"en":"One factor that makes songs memorable may be repetition.","zh":"令歌曲容易記住的其中一個因素可能是重複。"},{"en":"One factor that makes something happen means one cause or influence among several.","zh":"One factor that makes something happen 指幾個原因或影響中的其中一個。"},{"en":"One factor that makes students confident is repeated practice with clear feedback.","zh":"令學生有信心的其中一個因素，是有清晰回饋的反覆練習。"},{"en":"If repetition makes songs memorable, producers may repeat hooks many times.","zh":"如果重複令歌曲容易記住，製作人可能多次重複記憶點。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces one explanation without claiming it is the only one.","zh":"這個片語引出其中一個解釋，而不是聲稱它是唯一原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"repetition","meaning":"重複","examples":[{"en":"Repetition increases familiarity and anticipation.","zh":"重複增加熟悉感和期待感。"},{"en":"Repetition means doing, hearing, or seeing the same thing again and again.","zh":"Repetition 指一次又一次做、聽或看同一件事。"},{"en":"Students learn spelling through repetition when they write difficult words several times.","zh":"學生多次書寫困難字詞，就是透過重複學習拼字。"},{"en":"If a chorus repeats often, listeners may remember it more easily.","zh":"如果副歌經常重複，聽者可能更容易記住它。"},{"en":"This word describes repeated exposure or action.","zh":"這個詞描述反覆接觸或行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lead to familiarity","meaning":"令……變得熟悉","examples":[{"en":"Repetition leads to familiarity.","zh":"重複會令事物變得熟悉。"},{"en":"To lead to familiarity means to make something feel known because it has been experienced many times.","zh":"To lead to familiarity 指因多次經歷某事而令它感覺已知。"},{"en":"Repeated reading can lead to familiarity with common exam phrases.","zh":"反覆閱讀可以令學生熟悉常見考試片語。"},{"en":"If a song is played every morning, familiarity grows naturally.","zh":"如果一首歌每天早上播放，熟悉感自然增加。"},{"en":"This phrase connects repeated exposure with recognition.","zh":"這個片語把反覆接觸與辨認連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lead to anticipation","meaning":"產生期待","examples":[{"en":"Familiarity can lead to anticipation of what comes next.","zh":"熟悉感可以令人期待接下來會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"To lead to anticipation means to make someone expect what will happen next.","zh":"To lead to anticipation 指令人預期接下來會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"After reading many mystery stories, students may anticipate the detective’s final explanation.","zh":"讀過許多懸疑故事後，學生可能期待偵探最後的解釋。"},{"en":"If a melody is familiar, listeners may expect the next phrase before it arrives.","zh":"如果旋律熟悉，聽者可能在下一句到來前已期待它。"},{"en":"This phrase connects familiarity with expectation.","zh":"這個片語把熟悉感與期待連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be satisfied by","meaning":"由……得到滿足","examples":[{"en":"Anticipation is satisfied by hearing the expected phrase.","zh":"期待感由聽到預期的樂句得到滿足。"},{"en":"To be satisfied by something means to be fulfilled because what was expected or needed happens.","zh":"To be satisfied by something 指因預期或需要發生而得到滿足。"},{"en":"A student’s curiosity may be satisfied by a clear answer from the teacher.","zh":"學生的好奇心可能由老師清楚答案得到滿足。"},{"en":"If listeners expect a chorus and then hear it, their musical anticipation is satisfied.","zh":"如果聽者期待副歌並接着聽到它，他們的音樂期待就得到滿足。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a need or expectation being met.","zh":"這個片語描述需要或期待被滿足。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hit factory","meaning":"流行金曲製作工場","examples":[{"en":"The book examines how successful pop songs are manufactured.","zh":"這本書探討成功流行歌曲如何被製作出來。"},{"en":"A hit factory is a system, team, or industry that repeatedly produces popular songs.","zh":"Hit factory 是反覆製作流行歌曲的系統、團隊或行業。"},{"en":"A record company may act like a hit factory if it hires writers to create catchy choruses.","zh":"如果唱片公司聘請作曲人創作易記副歌，它可能像流行金曲製作工場。"},{"en":"If songs are designed for quick popularity, they may use repeated hooks and simple rhythms.","zh":"如果歌曲被設計成快速流行，它們可能使用重複記憶點和簡單節奏。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that pop hits can be produced deliberately, almost like products.","zh":"這個片語暗示流行金曲可以像產品般被刻意製造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"pump songs full of","meaning":"在歌曲中加入大量……","examples":[{"en":"Producers pump pop songs full of memorable hooks.","zh":"製作人在流行歌中加入大量易記記憶點。"},{"en":"To pump songs full of something means to put a large amount of that feature into songs.","zh":"To pump songs full of something 指在歌曲中加入大量某種特徵。"},{"en":"A producer may pump a dance track full of strong beats to keep people moving.","zh":"製作人可能在舞曲中加入大量強勁節拍，令人繼續跳動。"},{"en":"If songs are full of hooks, listeners may remember them after only one hearing.","zh":"如果歌曲充滿記憶點，聽者可能只聽一次就記住。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests deliberate addition of many attention-catching elements.","zh":"這個片語暗示刻意加入許多吸引注意的元素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"aural hooks","meaning":"聲音記憶點","examples":[{"en":"Pop producers use aural hooks to make songs memorable.","zh":"流行音樂製作人使用聲音記憶點令歌曲容易記住。"},{"en":"Aural hooks are catchy sound patterns that catch the ear and stay in memory.","zh":"Aural hooks 是吸引耳朵並留在記憶中的易記聲音模式。"},{"en":"A short repeated chorus can be an aural hook in a pop song.","zh":"短小重複副歌可以是流行歌中的聲音記憶點。"},{"en":"If an aural hook is strong, listeners may hum it later without meaning to.","zh":"如果聲音記憶點很強，聽者之後可能無意中哼出它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sound-based memory points in music.","zh":"這個片語描述音樂中以聲音為基礎的記憶點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"punchy melodic phrases","meaning":"強而有力的旋律短句","examples":[{"en":"Aural hooks are punchy melodic phrases that attract attention.","zh":"聲音記憶點是吸引注意的強而有力的旋律短句。"},{"en":"Punchy melodic phrases are short, strong, and memorable musical lines.","zh":"Punchy melodic phrases 是短小、有力並容易記住的音樂句子。"},{"en":"A phone ringtone often uses punchy melodic phrases so people recognise it quickly.","zh":"電話鈴聲常使用強而有力的旋律短句，讓人很快認出。"},{"en":"If a melody is punchy, it may stand out from the rest of the song.","zh":"如果旋律有力，它可能從歌曲其他部分中突出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes compact musical lines with impact.","zh":"這個片語描述精簡而有衝擊力的音樂句。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be designed to target","meaning":"被設計來針對……","examples":[{"en":"Musical hooks are designed to target the brain.","zh":"音樂記憶點被設計來針對大腦。"},{"en":"To be designed to target something means to be created with the aim of affecting that thing directly.","zh":"To be designed to target something 指被創造出來，目的在於直接影響某物。"},{"en":"A revision app may be designed to target weak vocabulary areas.","zh":"溫習應用程式可能被設計來針對薄弱詞彙範疇。"},{"en":"If a song hook targets memory, it may repeat sounds that the brain easily stores.","zh":"如果歌曲記憶點針對記憶，它可能重複大腦容易儲存的聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase shows deliberate design for a specific effect.","zh":"這個片語顯示為特定效果而刻意設計。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"leave someone wanting more","meaning":"令某人意猶未盡","examples":[{"en":"A strong hook can leave the listener wanting more.","zh":"強烈記憶點可以令聽者意猶未盡。"},{"en":"To leave someone wanting more means to make them interested enough to want the experience to continue.","zh":"To leave someone wanting more 指令人感興趣到想讓經驗繼續。"},{"en":"A short exciting chapter can leave students wanting more of the story.","zh":"一個短而刺激的章節可以令學生對故事意猶未盡。"},{"en":"If a musical phrase stops at the right moment, listeners may want to hear it again.","zh":"如果音樂短句在恰當時刻停止，聽者可能想再聽一次。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating desire for continuation or repetition.","zh":"這個片語描述令人想繼續或重複的效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"compare the melodic structure of","meaning":"比較……的旋律結構","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are comparing the melodic structure of two song groups.","zh":"研究人員正在比較兩組歌曲的旋律結構。"},{"en":"To compare the melodic structure of songs means to examine how their notes, patterns, and phrases are organised.","zh":"To compare the melodic structure of songs 指檢視歌曲的音符、模式和樂句如何組織。"},{"en":"A music teacher may compare the melodic structure of two folk songs.","zh":"音樂老師可能比較兩首民歌的旋律結構。"},{"en":"If earworm songs share structures, researchers may identify what makes them memorable.","zh":"如果洗腦歌曲有共同結構，研究人員可能找出它們令人難忘的原因。"},{"en":"This phrase describes technical comparison of melodies.","zh":"這個片語描述對旋律的技術性比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"often-mentioned songs","meaning":"經常被提及的歌曲","examples":[{"en":"The researchers selected often-mentioned earworm songs.","zh":"研究人員選取經常被提及的洗腦歌曲。"},{"en":"Often-mentioned songs are songs that many people name or report repeatedly.","zh":"Often-mentioned songs 是許多人反覆說出或報告的歌曲。"},{"en":"A teacher may collect often-mentioned errors to plan a grammar lesson.","zh":"老師可能收集經常被提及的錯誤來計劃文法課。"},{"en":"If a song is often mentioned as an earworm, it may have features that make it memorable.","zh":"如果一首歌經常被提及為洗腦歌，它可能有令人難忘的特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes songs that appear frequently in people’s reports.","zh":"這個片語描述經常出現在人們報告中的歌曲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"similarly popular songs","meaning":"受歡迎程度相若的歌曲","examples":[{"en":"The comparison group contained similarly popular songs.","zh":"比較組包含受歡迎程度相若的歌曲。"},{"en":"Similarly popular songs are songs with about the same level of public popularity.","zh":"Similarly popular songs 是公眾受歡迎程度大約相同的歌曲。"},{"en":"A researcher may compare two similarly popular films to study why one is remembered more.","zh":"研究人員可能比較兩部受歡迎程度相若的電影，以研究為何其中一部更令人記得。"},{"en":"If songs are similarly popular, differences in earworm effect may not be due only to fame.","zh":"如果歌曲受歡迎程度相若，洗腦效果差異可能不只是由名氣造成。"},{"en":"This phrase controls comparison by keeping popularity roughly equal.","zh":"這個片語透過保持受歡迎程度大致相等來控制比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be cited as","meaning":"被提及為……","examples":[{"en":"Some popular songs were not cited as earworms.","zh":"一些受歡迎歌曲沒有被提及為洗腦歌。"},{"en":"To be cited as something means to be mentioned or named as that thing.","zh":"To be cited as something 指被提及或命名為某事。"},{"en":"A book may be cited as an example of clear writing in a class.","zh":"一本書可能在課堂上被提及為清晰寫作的例子。"},{"en":"If a song is popular but not cited as an earworm, popularity alone may not explain earworms.","zh":"如果一首歌受歡迎但沒有被提及為洗腦歌，受歡迎程度本身可能不能解釋洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being used as a reported example.","zh":"這個片語描述被用作報告例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"assess the difference","meaning":"評估差異","examples":[{"en":"The study aims to assess the difference between the song groups.","zh":"這項研究旨在評估兩組歌曲之間的差異。"},{"en":"To assess the difference means to examine and judge how two things are not the same.","zh":"To assess the difference 指檢視並判斷兩件事有何不同。"},{"en":"A teacher may assess the difference between two essays by looking at structure and vocabulary.","zh":"老師可能透過查看結構和詞彙，評估兩篇作文的差異。"},{"en":"If researchers assess differences carefully, they can avoid guessing from impressions.","zh":"如果研究人員仔細評估差異，就可以避免憑印象猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful comparison and evaluation.","zh":"這個片語描述仔細比較和評價。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"earworm potential","meaning":"成為洗腦歌的潛力","examples":[{"en":"Some songs appear to have greater earworm potential.","zh":"有些歌曲似乎有更大成為洗腦歌的潛力。"},{"en":"Earworm potential means the likelihood that a song will get stuck in people’s heads.","zh":"Earworm potential 指一首歌卡在人們腦海中的可能性。"},{"en":"A ringtone with a simple repeated melody may have strong earworm potential.","zh":"有簡單重複旋律的鈴聲，可能有很強成為洗腦歌的潛力。"},{"en":"If a song has high earworm potential, listeners may remember it after hearing it only briefly.","zh":"如果一首歌有高洗腦潛力，聽者可能只短暫聽過也記住它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how likely music is to become mentally repetitive.","zh":"這個片語描述音樂變成心理重複的可能性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"share certain features","meaning":"具有某些共同特徵","examples":[{"en":"Songs with earworm potential share certain musical features.","zh":"有洗腦潛力的歌曲具有某些共同音樂特徵。"},{"en":"To share certain features means to have some qualities in common.","zh":"To share certain features 指有一些共同質素。"},{"en":"Successful school posters may share certain features, such as clear colours and short messages.","zh":"成功的學校海報可能具有某些共同特徵，例如清晰顏色和簡短訊息。"},{"en":"If earworm songs share features, those features may help explain why they stick.","zh":"如果洗腦歌曲有共同特徵，這些特徵可能幫助解釋它們為何揮之不去。"},{"en":"This phrase points to similarities within a group.","zh":"這個片語指出一個群體內的相似之處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"repeating pattern","meaning":"重複模式","examples":[{"en":"Many earworms contain a repeating pattern in pitch.","zh":"許多洗腦旋律在音高中包含重複模式。"},{"en":"A repeating pattern is a sound, shape, or action that happens again and again in a regular way.","zh":"Repeating pattern 是以規律方式一次又一次出現的聲音、形狀或動作。"},{"en":"A child may notice a repeating pattern of claps in a playground game.","zh":"孩子可能注意到操場遊戲中的拍手重複模式。"},{"en":"If a song has a repeating pattern, the brain may predict and remember it more easily.","zh":"如果歌曲有重複模式，大腦可能更容易預測和記住它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regular repetition that helps recognition.","zh":"這個片語描述有助辨認的規律重複。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ups and downs in pitch","meaning":"音高的升降","examples":[{"en":"Earworm melodies often contain regular ups and downs in pitch.","zh":"洗腦旋律常包含規律的音高升降。"},{"en":"Ups and downs in pitch are movements from higher notes to lower notes and back again.","zh":"Ups and downs in pitch 是音符從較高到較低，再回來的移動。"},{"en":"A simple children’s song may use clear ups and downs in pitch so children can sing it easily.","zh":"簡單兒歌可能使用清晰音高升降，讓兒童容易唱出。"},{"en":"If pitch rises and falls in a pattern, the melody may become easier to remember.","zh":"如果音高以某模式上升和下降，旋律可能更容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the shape of a tune.","zh":"這個片語描述旋律的形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"irregular musical interval","meaning":"不規則音程","examples":[{"en":"An irregular musical interval may make a tune memorable.","zh":"不規則音程可能令旋律容易記住。"},{"en":"An irregular musical interval is an unusual jump between two notes.","zh":"Irregular musical interval 是兩個音符之間不尋常的跳動。"},{"en":"A song may catch attention if one note suddenly jumps higher than expected.","zh":"如果一首歌中某個音突然跳得比預期高，它可能吸引注意。"},{"en":"If an interval surprises the listener, the melody may stand out in memory.","zh":"如果音程令聽者驚訝，旋律可能在記憶中突出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unexpected distance between notes.","zh":"這個片語描述音符之間出乎意料的距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"test results in reverse","meaning":"反向驗證研究結果","examples":[{"en":"The researchers plan to test their results in reverse.","zh":"研究人員計劃反向驗證他們的結果。"},{"en":"To test results in reverse means to check findings by starting from the predicted features and seeing if they produce the expected effect.","zh":"To test results in reverse 指從預測特徵開始，檢查它們是否產生預期效果。"},{"en":"If a teacher thinks short quizzes improve memory, they may test the idea in reverse by adding quizzes to a new class.","zh":"如果老師認為短測驗改善記憶，他們可能透過在新班加入測驗來反向驗證想法。"},{"en":"If predicted earworm songs actually get stuck, the earlier findings become stronger.","zh":"如果預測為洗腦歌的歌曲真的揮之不去，早前發現就更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes checking a conclusion from the opposite direction.","zh":"這個片語描述從相反方向檢查結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"play ringtones","meaning":"播放電話鈴聲","examples":[{"en":"The researchers will play song ringtones to volunteers.","zh":"研究人員會向參加者播放歌曲電話鈴聲。"},{"en":"To play ringtones means to let people hear short phone-like versions of songs.","zh":"To play ringtones 指讓人聽到像手機鈴聲般的歌曲短版本。"},{"en":"A phone shop may play ringtones so customers can choose one they like.","zh":"手機店可能播放電話鈴聲，讓顧客選擇喜歡的一個。"},{"en":"If ringtones are played several times, researchers can test which ones remain in memory.","zh":"如果鈴聲被播放幾次，研究人員可以測試哪些留在記憶中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using short musical sounds as test material.","zh":"這個片語描述使用短音樂聲作為測試材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"earworm and non-earworm varieties","meaning":"洗腦歌與非洗腦歌類型","examples":[{"en":"The test will compare earworm and non-earworm varieties of songs.","zh":"測試會比較洗腦歌與非洗腦歌類型的歌曲。"},{"en":"Earworm and non-earworm varieties are song types that are likely or unlikely to get stuck in the mind.","zh":"Earworm and non-earworm varieties 是很可能或不太可能卡在腦中的歌曲類型。"},{"en":"A researcher may compare catchy ringtone versions with less catchy ones.","zh":"研究人員可能比較易記鈴聲版本與較不易記的版本。"},{"en":"If one variety gets stuck more often, its musical features may explain the difference.","zh":"如果某類型更常揮之不去，其音樂特徵可能解釋差異。"},{"en":"This phrase separates songs by their tendency to repeat mentally.","zh":"這個片語按歌曲在腦中重複的傾向來區分它們。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"several times a day","meaning":"每日數次","examples":[{"en":"The ringtones will be played several times a day.","zh":"這些鈴聲會每日播放數次。"},{"en":"Several times a day means more than once during the same day.","zh":"Several times a day 指在同一天內多於一次。"},{"en":"A language learner may review vocabulary several times a day for better memory.","zh":"語言學習者可能每日數次溫習詞彙，以改善記憶。"},{"en":"If a ringtone is heard several times a day, it may become familiar very quickly.","zh":"如果鈴聲每日被聽到數次，它可能很快變得熟悉。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated frequency within one day.","zh":"這個片語描述一天內的重複頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"see which ones get stuck","meaning":"看哪些歌曲會揮之不去","examples":[{"en":"The experiment will see which songs get stuck in people’s heads.","zh":"實驗會看哪些歌曲會在人們腦海中揮之不去。"},{"en":"To see which ones get stuck means to find out which songs keep repeating in the mind.","zh":"To see which ones get stuck 指找出哪些歌曲會在腦中不斷重複。"},{"en":"A teacher may test different memory tricks to see which ones help students most.","zh":"老師可能測試不同記憶技巧，看哪些最幫助學生。"},{"en":"If certain ringtones get stuck more often, they may have stronger earworm features.","zh":"如果某些鈴聲更常揮之不去，它們可能有更強洗腦特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes testing which items remain in memory.","zh":"這個片語描述測試哪些項目會留在記憶中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"work together to","meaning":"合作去……","examples":[{"en":"Stewart and Halpern are working together to recruit participants.","zh":"Stewart和Halpern正在合作招募參加者。"},{"en":"To work together to do something means to cooperate in order to achieve a shared goal.","zh":"To work together to do something 指合作以達成共同目標。"},{"en":"Two teachers may work together to design a new reading course.","zh":"兩位老師可能合作設計新的閱讀課程。"},{"en":"If researchers work together, they can combine skills and collect more reliable data.","zh":"如果研究人員合作，他們可以結合技能並收集更可靠數據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cooperation for a purpose.","zh":"這個片語描述為某目的而合作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"recruit survey participants","meaning":"招募調查參加者","examples":[{"en":"The researchers are recruiting survey participants for a new study.","zh":"研究人員正在為一項新研究招募調查參加者。"},{"en":"To recruit survey participants means to find people willing to answer research questions.","zh":"To recruit survey participants 指尋找願意回答研究問題的人。"},{"en":"A university may recruit survey participants by sending emails to students.","zh":"大學可能透過向學生發電郵招募調查參加者。"},{"en":"If researchers recruit enough participants, the study may show clearer patterns.","zh":"如果研究人員招募足夠參加者，研究可能顯示更清晰模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes finding people to take part in survey research.","zh":"這個片語描述尋找人參與調查研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"different stages of life","meaning":"不同人生階段","examples":[{"en":"The study examines people at different stages of life.","zh":"這項研究考察不同人生階段的人。"},{"en":"Different stages of life are different age periods, such as childhood, youth, adulthood, and old age.","zh":"Different stages of life 是不同年齡時期，例如童年、青年、成年和老年。"},{"en":"People at different stages of life may have different sleep needs and music habits.","zh":"處於不同人生階段的人可能有不同睡眠需要和音樂習慣。"},{"en":"If age affects earworms, researchers should compare young, middle-aged, and older people.","zh":"如果年齡影響洗腦旋律，研究人員應比較年輕、中年和較年長人士。"},{"en":"This phrase describes life periods rather than social status.","zh":"這個片語描述人生時期，而不是社會地位。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"experience something differently","meaning":"對……有不同體驗","examples":[{"en":"People of different ages may experience earworms differently.","zh":"不同年齡的人可能對洗腦旋律有不同體驗。"},{"en":"To experience something differently means to feel, understand, or be affected by it in another way.","zh":"To experience something differently 指以不同方式感受、理解或受某事影響。"},{"en":"Children and adults may experience the same film differently because they notice different details.","zh":"兒童和成人可能因注意到不同細節，而對同一部電影有不同體驗。"},{"en":"If older people listen to music less often, they may experience fewer earworms.","zh":"如果較年長人士較少聽音樂，他們可能較少經歷洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights differences in personal experience.","zh":"這個片語突顯個人經驗的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"argue that","meaning":"主張；認為","examples":[{"en":"One could argue that older people know more songs.","zh":"有人可能主張較年長人士知道更多歌曲。"},{"en":"To argue that something is true means to give reasons for believing it.","zh":"To argue that something is true 指給出理由支持某事為真。"},{"en":"A student may argue that homework should be shorter but more focused.","zh":"學生可能主張功課應較短但更集中。"},{"en":"If someone argues that older people know more music, they may expect them to get more earworms.","zh":"如果有人認為較年長人士知道更多音樂，他們可能預期他們有更多洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a reasoned opinion, not necessarily a quarrel.","zh":"這個片語引出有理由支持的意見，而不一定是爭吵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"might get them more often","meaning":"可能更經常出現它們","examples":[{"en":"Older people might get earworms more often because they know more music.","zh":"較年長人士可能因知道更多音樂而更經常出現洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"Might get them more often means may experience them more frequently.","zh":"Might get them more often 指可能更頻繁地經歷它們。"},{"en":"Students who hear songs all day might get earworms more often than those who rarely listen to music.","zh":"整天聽歌的學生，可能比很少聽音樂的人更經常出現洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"If someone knows many tunes, there are more songs available for the mind to repeat.","zh":"如果某人知道許多旋律，大腦可重複的歌曲就更多。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a possible increase in frequency.","zh":"這個片語表達頻率可能增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"responses so far","meaning":"目前所得的回應","examples":[{"en":"The few responses so far suggest a different pattern.","zh":"目前所得的少數回應顯示另一種模式。"},{"en":"Responses so far are the answers or data collected up to the present point.","zh":"Responses so far 是到目前為止收集到的答案或數據。"},{"en":"The responses so far from students may show that the homework is too long.","zh":"目前從學生所得的回應可能顯示功課太長。"},{"en":"If early responses differ from expectations, researchers may adjust their questions.","zh":"如果早期回應與預期不同，研究人員可能調整問題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to partial evidence collected before a study is complete.","zh":"這個片語指研究完成前已收集的部分證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"indicate that","meaning":"顯示","examples":[{"en":"The early responses indicate that older people may experience fewer earworms.","zh":"早期回應顯示較年長人士可能經歷較少洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"To indicate that something is true means to show or suggest it.","zh":"To indicate that something is true 指顯示或暗示某事為真。"},{"en":"A student’s repeated spelling mistakes may indicate that they need more phonics practice.","zh":"學生反覆拼字錯誤可能顯示他需要更多自然拼讀練習。"},{"en":"If survey answers indicate a pattern, researchers may design a larger study to confirm it.","zh":"如果調查答案顯示某模式，研究人員可能設計更大型研究來確認。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces evidence that points toward a conclusion.","zh":"這個片語引出指向結論的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"less often","meaning":"較少出現","examples":[{"en":"Older participants appear to report earworms less often.","zh":"較年長參加者似乎較少報告洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"Less often means not as frequently.","zh":"Less often 指沒有那麼頻繁。"},{"en":"A student who sleeps well may feel tired less often during class.","zh":"睡得好的學生在課堂上可能較少感到疲倦。"},{"en":"If older people play music less often, earworms may also occur less often.","zh":"如果較年長人士較少播放音樂，洗腦旋律也可能較少出現。"},{"en":"This phrase compares frequency.","zh":"這個片語比較頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"play music as often as","meaning":"與……一樣經常播放音樂","examples":[{"en":"Older people may not play music as often as younger people do.","zh":"較年長人士可能不像年輕人一樣經常播放音樂。"},{"en":"To play music as often as someone else means to listen to or turn on music with the same frequency.","zh":"To play music as often as someone else 指以相同頻率聽音樂或打開音樂。"},{"en":"A busy parent may not play music as often as a teenager with headphones.","zh":"忙碌父母可能不像戴耳機的青少年一樣經常播放音樂。"},{"en":"If people play music less often, they may have fewer recent songs for the brain to repeat.","zh":"如果人們較少播放音樂，大腦可重複的近期歌曲可能較少。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how frequently different people listen to music.","zh":"這個片語比較不同人聽音樂的頻率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"contain the following information","meaning":"包含以下資料","examples":[{"en":"Students identify which paragraph contains the following information.","zh":"學生識別哪一段包含以下資料。"},{"en":"To contain the following information means to include the details listed after the instruction.","zh":"To contain the following information 指包含指示後列出的細節。"},{"en":"In a reading test, a paragraph may contain the following information even if it uses different words.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，即使用不同字眼，某段仍可能包含以下資料。"},{"en":"If students search only for exact keywords, they may miss the paragraph that contains the idea.","zh":"如果學生只搜尋完全相同的關鍵字，可能錯過包含該意思的段落。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in paragraph-matching tasks.","zh":"這個片語常見於段落配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"description of the characteristics","meaning":"對特徵的描述","examples":[{"en":"The question asks for a description of the characteristics of earworm songs.","zh":"題目要求對洗腦歌曲特徵的描述。"},{"en":"A description of the characteristics means an explanation of the main features of something.","zh":"Description of the characteristics 指解釋某事物的主要特徵。"},{"en":"A science report may include a description of the characteristics of healthy soil.","zh":"科學報告可能包括對健康土壤特徵的描述。"},{"en":"If students know the characteristics, they can distinguish one type of song from another.","zh":"如果學生知道特徵，他們就能區分一類歌曲和另一類歌曲。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on identifying important features.","zh":"這個片語著重識別重要特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"common to","meaning":"……所共有的","examples":[{"en":"The songs share several features common to memorable melodies.","zh":"這些歌曲具有幾個令人難忘旋律所共有的特徵。"},{"en":"Common to something means found in or shared by that group.","zh":"Common to something 指在該群體中找到或由該群體共享。"},{"en":"Clear instructions and regular practice are common to successful language courses.","zh":"清晰指示和定期練習是成功語言課程所共有的特徵。"},{"en":"If a pattern is common to many earworms, it may help explain why they are memorable.","zh":"如果某模式是許多洗腦旋律所共有的，它可能幫助解釋它們為何容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shared features within a category.","zh":"這個片語描述某類別中的共同特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"become earworms","meaning":"變成洗腦歌","examples":[{"en":"Some popular songs are more likely to become earworms.","zh":"一些受歡迎歌曲更有可能變成洗腦歌。"},{"en":"To become earworms means to turn into songs that repeat involuntarily in people’s minds.","zh":"To become earworms 指變成在人們腦中不由自主重複的歌曲。"},{"en":"A song from a short video may become an earworm after students hear it many times.","zh":"短片中的歌曲被學生聽很多次後，可能變成洗腦歌。"},{"en":"If a tune has a strong hook and frequent exposure, it may become an earworm.","zh":"如果旋律有強烈記憶點並且經常被聽到，它可能變成洗腦歌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a song changing from ordinary music into mental repetition.","zh":"這個片語描述歌曲由普通音樂變成心理重複。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"justification for research","meaning":"進行研究的理據","examples":[{"en":"The passage provides a justification for research into earworms.","zh":"文章提供了研究洗腦旋律的理據。"},{"en":"A justification for research is a reason that explains why a study is worth doing.","zh":"Justification for research 是解釋某項研究為何值得進行的理由。"},{"en":"Rising student stress may be a justification for research into sleep and homework.","zh":"學生壓力上升可能是研究睡眠和功課的理據。"},{"en":"If earworms reveal hidden thought processes, they justify scientific attention.","zh":"如果洗腦旋律揭示隱藏思考過程，它們就能證明科學關注有理。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose and value of research.","zh":"這個片語解釋研究的目的和價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"reaction to known and unknown songs","meaning":"對熟悉和陌生歌曲的反應","examples":[{"en":"The brain shows different reactions to known and unknown songs.","zh":"大腦對熟悉和陌生歌曲顯示不同反應。"},{"en":"Reaction to known and unknown songs means how the brain responds differently to familiar and unfamiliar music.","zh":"Reaction to known and unknown songs 指大腦如何不同地回應熟悉和不熟悉的音樂。"},{"en":"A child may smile at a known song but listen carefully to an unknown one.","zh":"孩子可能對熟悉歌曲微笑，但仔細聽陌生歌曲。"},{"en":"If known songs activate memory areas faster, familiarity changes the listening experience.","zh":"如果熟悉歌曲更快啟動記憶區域，熟悉感就改變聆聽經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase compares responses to music people know and do not know.","zh":"這個片語比較人們對已知和未知音樂的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"proposed research","meaning":"擬議中的研究","examples":[{"en":"The final paragraph describes proposed research into age differences.","zh":"最後一段描述了關於年齡差異的擬議研究。"},{"en":"Proposed research is research that researchers plan or suggest but have not yet fully completed.","zh":"Proposed research 是研究人員計劃或建議但尚未完全完成的研究。"},{"en":"A university may announce proposed research on how students use online dictionaries.","zh":"大學可能公布一項關於學生如何使用網上字典的擬議研究。"},{"en":"If proposed research receives enough participants, it can later produce stronger evidence.","zh":"如果擬議研究獲得足夠參加者，它之後可以產生更有力證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a planned study.","zh":"這個片語描述計劃中的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"frequency with which","meaning":"……發生的頻率","examples":[{"en":"The study examines the frequency with which earworms occur.","zh":"這項研究考察洗腦旋律發生的頻率。"},{"en":"The frequency with which something happens means how often it happens.","zh":"Frequency with which something happens 指某事發生得有多經常。"},{"en":"A teacher may record the frequency with which students miss homework.","zh":"老師可能記錄學生欠交功課的頻率。"},{"en":"If earworms occur daily for one person but monthly for another, their frequencies differ.","zh":"如果洗腦旋律對一個人每日出現，但對另一人每月出現，它們的頻率就不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal way to discuss how often something occurs.","zh":"這個片語是討論某事多久發生一次的正式說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"different age groups","meaning":"不同年齡組別","examples":[{"en":"Researchers are comparing earworms across different age groups.","zh":"研究人員正在比較不同年齡組別中的洗腦旋律。"},{"en":"Different age groups are groups of people separated by age, such as teenagers, adults, and older people.","zh":"Different age groups 是按年齡分開的人群，例如青少年、成年人和長者。"},{"en":"A health survey may compare exercise habits across different age groups.","zh":"健康調查可能比較不同年齡組別的運動習慣。"},{"en":"If one age group reports fewer earworms, researchers may ask what causes the difference.","zh":"如果某年齡組別較少報告洗腦旋律，研究人員可能會問原因是甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes comparison by age.","zh":"這個片語描述按年齡作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"complete the summary below","meaning":"完成以下摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary below means to fill in missing words in a short version of the passage.","zh":"To complete the summary below 指在文章簡短版本中填入缺失字詞。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should read the whole summary before choosing answers.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先閱讀整個摘要，再選擇答案。"},{"en":"If the blank needs a noun, students must choose a word that fits the grammar.","zh":"如果空格需要名詞，學生必須選擇符合文法的字。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common exam instruction for gap-filling tasks.","zh":"這個片語是填空題中常見的考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"one word only","meaning":"只可填一個字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer must contain one word only.","zh":"每個答案只可填一個字。"},{"en":"One word only means the answer must be exactly one word, not two or more.","zh":"One word only 指答案必須剛好一個字，不能兩個或更多。"},{"en":"If the answer is “brain regions”, it would break a one-word-only rule.","zh":"如果答案是 “brain regions”，就違反只填一字的規則。"},{"en":"When students see this instruction, they should copy only the single necessary word.","zh":"當學生看見這個指示，應只抄寫單一必要字。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a strict word limit in exam answers.","zh":"這個片語為考試答案設定嚴格字數限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"conclude that","meaning":"得出結論認為","examples":[{"en":"The researchers concluded that imagined music resembles recordings.","zh":"研究人員得出結論認為想像音樂類似錄音。"},{"en":"To conclude that something is true means to decide it after considering evidence.","zh":"To conclude that something is true 指考慮證據後判定某事為真。"},{"en":"A teacher may conclude that students need more practice after checking several essays.","zh":"老師檢查幾篇作文後，可能得出結論認為學生需要更多練習。"},{"en":"If data show similar tapping speeds, researchers may conclude that mental music is accurate.","zh":"如果數據顯示相似打拍速度，研究人員可能得出結論認為心理音樂是準確的。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a result reached from evidence.","zh":"這個片語引出由證據得出的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be quite similar to","meaning":"與……相當相似","examples":[{"en":"The music in our minds can be quite similar to real recordings.","zh":"我們腦中的音樂可以與真實錄音相當相似。"},{"en":"To be quite similar to something means to be fairly close to it in form, sound, or quality.","zh":"To be quite similar to something 指在形式、聲音或質素上相當接近某物。"},{"en":"A student’s spoken answer may be quite similar to the model answer but not identical.","zh":"學生的口語答案可能與範文相當相似，但不完全一樣。"},{"en":"If imagined music is similar to recordings, memory keeps more detail than expected.","zh":"如果想像音樂與錄音相似，記憶就保留了比預期更多的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong resemblance without saying two things are exactly the same.","zh":"這個片語顯示高度相似，但不是說兩者完全相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"record the rhythm","meaning":"記錄節奏","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers recorded the rhythm by tapping to the beat.","zh":"參加者透過跟着節拍打拍子記錄節奏。"},{"en":"To record the rhythm means to capture or measure the pattern of beats in music.","zh":"To record the rhythm 指捕捉或量度音樂中的節拍模式。"},{"en":"A music student may record the rhythm of a song by clapping it into an app.","zh":"音樂學生可能透過向應用程式拍手來記錄一首歌的節奏。"},{"en":"If rhythm is recorded, researchers can compare imagined music with real music.","zh":"如果節奏被記錄，研究人員可以比較想像音樂與真實音樂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes saving information about musical timing.","zh":"這個片語描述保存關於音樂時間安排的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"use a monitor","meaning":"使用監測器","examples":[{"en":"The researchers used a monitor to record movement.","zh":"研究人員使用監測器記錄動作。"},{"en":"To use a monitor means to use a device that measures and records information.","zh":"To use a monitor 指使用量度和記錄資訊的裝置。"},{"en":"Doctors may use a heart monitor to check a patient’s heartbeat.","zh":"醫生可能使用心跳監測器檢查病人心跳。"},{"en":"If researchers use a monitor, they can collect data more accurately than by guessing.","zh":"如果研究人員使用監測器，他們可以比靠猜測更準確地收集數據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using equipment to track changes or activity.","zh":"這個片語描述使用設備追蹤變化或活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"further research has demonstrated that","meaning":"進一步研究顯示","examples":[{"en":"Further research has demonstrated that frequent earworms are linked to brain differences.","zh":"進一步研究顯示經常出現洗腦旋律與大腦差異有關。"},{"en":"Further research has demonstrated that means later or additional studies have shown something with evidence.","zh":"Further research has demonstrated that 指後來或額外研究以證據顯示某事。"},{"en":"Further research has demonstrated that sleep affects memory more than many students expect.","zh":"進一步研究顯示睡眠對記憶的影響比許多學生預期更大。"},{"en":"If further research confirms an early finding, the argument becomes more reliable.","zh":"如果進一步研究確認早期發現，論點就變得更可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces support from later studies.","zh":"這個片語引入來自後續研究的支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"deal with something differently","meaning":"以不同方式處理……","examples":[{"en":"Some brains may deal with emotions differently.","zh":"一些大腦可能以不同方式處理情緒。"},{"en":"To deal with something differently means to handle or process it in another way.","zh":"To deal with something differently 指以另一種方式處理或加工某事。"},{"en":"Two students may deal with exam stress differently: one talks to friends, while another goes quiet.","zh":"兩名學生可能以不同方式處理考試壓力：一人與朋友傾談，另一人變得沉默。"},{"en":"If the brain deals with emotion differently, music may affect people in different ways.","zh":"如果大腦以不同方式處理情緒，音樂可能以不同方式影響人。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights variation in response or processing.","zh":"這個片語突顯反應或處理方式的差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be entertained by","meaning":"被……娛樂","examples":[{"en":"The brain may be entertained by earworms when unoccupied.","zh":"大腦在沒有事情佔用時，可能被洗腦旋律娛樂。"},{"en":"To be entertained by something means to be kept interested or amused by it.","zh":"To be entertained by something 指被某事保持興趣或逗樂。"},{"en":"Children may be entertained by a simple song during a long journey.","zh":"孩子在長途旅程中可能被一首簡單歌曲娛樂。"},{"en":"If the mind has no demanding task, repeated music may keep it lightly entertained.","zh":"如果大腦沒有費力任務，重複音樂可能令它輕微保持有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something providing interest, not necessarily deep pleasure.","zh":"這個片語描述某事提供興趣，而不一定是深層快樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be focused on a task","meaning":"專注於一項任務","examples":[{"en":"Earworms occur less often when the mind is focused on a task.","zh":"當大腦專注於一項任務時，洗腦旋律較少出現。"},{"en":"To be focused on a task means to give attention to one activity.","zh":"To be focused on a task 指把注意力放在一項活動上。"},{"en":"A student focused on solving maths problems may not notice background noise.","zh":"專注於解數學題的學生可能不會留意背景噪音。"},{"en":"If attention is fully used by a task, there may be less room for mental music.","zh":"如果注意力被任務充分使用，心理音樂可出現的空間可能較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes concentrated attention.","zh":"這個片語描述集中的注意力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reduction in the occurrence of","meaning":"……出現次數的減少","examples":[{"en":"Researchers observed a reduction in the occurrence of earworms.","zh":"研究人員觀察到洗腦旋律出現次數的減少。"},{"en":"A reduction in the occurrence of something means it happens less often.","zh":"Reduction in the occurrence of something 指某事發生得較少。"},{"en":"A school may see a reduction in the occurrence of lateness after changing bus arrangements.","zh":"學校改變校巴安排後，可能看見遲到出現次數的減少。"},{"en":"If harder tasks reduce earworms, mental effort may block repeated songs.","zh":"如果較困難任務減少洗腦旋律，心理努力可能阻止重複歌曲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decrease in frequency.","zh":"這個片語描述頻率下降。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be directly related to","meaning":"與……有直接關係","examples":[{"en":"The reduction was directly related to task difficulty.","zh":"這種減少與任務難度有直接關係。"},{"en":"To be directly related to something means to have a clear and close connection with it.","zh":"To be directly related to something 指與某事有清楚而密切的關係。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be directly related to regular practice.","zh":"學生的進步可能與定期練習有直接關係。"},{"en":"If earworms decrease as tasks become harder, the reduction is related to difficulty.","zh":"如果任務越難，洗腦旋律越少，減少就與難度有關。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a close connection between two factors.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩個因素之間的密切連繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reflect their moods","meaning":"反映他們的情緒","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers’ chosen songs reflected their moods.","zh":"參加者選擇的歌曲反映他們的情緒。"},{"en":"To reflect their moods means to show or match how they were feeling.","zh":"To reflect their moods 指顯示或配合他們的感受。"},{"en":"A tired student may choose quiet music that reflects their mood.","zh":"疲倦學生可能選擇安靜音樂，反映他的情緒。"},{"en":"If people feel cheerful, the songs in their heads may be brighter and faster.","zh":"如果人們感到愉快，腦中的歌曲可能更明亮、更快。"},{"en":"This phrase connects outer choices or mental music with inner feelings.","zh":"這個片語把外在選擇或心理音樂與內在感受連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choice of music","meaning":"音樂選擇","examples":[{"en":"The choice of music was not entirely accidental.","zh":"音樂選擇並非完全偶然。"},{"en":"Choice of music means the particular song or type of music selected or recalled.","zh":"Choice of music 指被選擇或回想起的特定歌曲或音樂類型。"},{"en":"A café’s choice of music can affect whether customers feel relaxed or rushed.","zh":"咖啡店的音樂選擇可以影響顧客感到放鬆還是匆忙。"},{"en":"If mood influences the choice of music, sad people may recall slower songs.","zh":"如果情緒影響音樂選擇，傷心的人可能回想起較慢的歌曲。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to what music is chosen and why.","zh":"這個片語指選擇甚麼音樂及其原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"look at the following statements","meaning":"閱讀以下陳述","examples":[{"en":"Students look at the following statements and match them with researchers.","zh":"學生閱讀以下陳述，並把它們與研究人員配對。"},{"en":"Look at the following statements means read the list of sentences given below the instruction.","zh":"Look at the following statements 指閱讀指示下方列出的句子。"},{"en":"In a matching task, students should look at the following statements before scanning for names.","zh":"在配對題中，學生應先閱讀以下陳述，再掃描姓名。"},{"en":"If students understand each statement’s meaning, they are less likely to match by keywords only.","zh":"如果學生理解每項陳述的意思，他們就較不可能只靠關鍵字配對。"},{"en":"This phrase is a reading-test instruction.","zh":"這個片語是閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"list of researchers","meaning":"研究人員名單","examples":[{"en":"The question provides a list of researchers.","zh":"題目提供一份研究人員名單。"},{"en":"A list of researchers is a set of names of people who conducted or discussed studies.","zh":"List of researchers 是進行或討論研究的人名集合。"},{"en":"A reading exercise may give a list of researchers before asking students to match findings.","zh":"閱讀練習可能在要求學生配對發現前，提供研究人員名單。"},{"en":"If several researchers are mentioned, a list helps students organise who said what.","zh":"如果文章提到幾位研究人員，名單幫助學生整理誰說了甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the names used as answer options.","zh":"這個片語指用作答案選項的姓名。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"match each statement with","meaning":"將每項陳述與……配對","examples":[{"en":"Students match each statement with the correct researcher.","zh":"學生將每項陳述與正確研究人員配對。"},{"en":"To match each statement with something means to connect every sentence to the right person, idea, or category.","zh":"To match each statement with something 指把每個句子連接到正確人物、想法或類別。"},{"en":"Students may match each statement with the paragraph that contains the same meaning.","zh":"學生可能將每項陳述與包含相同意思的段落配對。"},{"en":"If two researchers sound similar, students must read carefully before matching.","zh":"如果兩位研究人員說法相似，學生配對前必須仔細閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common exam matching task.","zh":"這個片語描述常見考試配對題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"may use any letter more than once","meaning":"每個字母可使用多於一次","examples":[{"en":"Students may use any letter more than once.","zh":"學生每個字母可使用多於一次。"},{"en":"May use any letter more than once means the same answer option can be chosen repeatedly.","zh":"May use any letter more than once 指同一答案選項可以重複選用。"},{"en":"In a matching task, one researcher may match two or three statements.","zh":"在配對題中，一位研究人員可能配對兩三項陳述。"},{"en":"If students assume each letter is used only once, they may choose wrong answers.","zh":"如果學生假設每個字母只可用一次，他們可能選錯答案。"},{"en":"This phrase tells students that repeated answers are allowed.","zh":"這個片語告訴學生重複答案是允許的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"intentionally memorable","meaning":"刻意令人容易記住的","examples":[{"en":"Some musicians create songs that are intentionally memorable.","zh":"有些音樂人創作刻意令人容易記住的歌曲。"},{"en":"Intentionally memorable means deliberately designed to be easy to remember.","zh":"Intentionally memorable 指被刻意設計成容易記住。"},{"en":"A school slogan may be intentionally memorable so students can repeat it easily.","zh":"學校口號可能被刻意設計得容易記住，讓學生容易重複。"},{"en":"If a song uses a strong hook, the writer may be trying to make it stick.","zh":"如果歌曲使用強烈記憶點，作曲人可能正在嘗試令它揮之不去。"},{"en":"This phrase describes memorability created on purpose, not by accident.","zh":"這個片語描述有意製造的易記性，而不是偶然。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"regulate how they think","meaning":"控制自己的思考方式","examples":[{"en":"People cannot completely regulate how they think.","zh":"人們不能完全控制自己的思考方式。"},{"en":"To regulate how they think means to control or manage their thought processes.","zh":"To regulate how they think 指控制或管理自己的思考過程。"},{"en":"A student may try to regulate how they think before an exam by breathing slowly.","zh":"學生可能在考試前透過慢慢呼吸來控制自己的思考方式。"},{"en":"If unwanted songs appear automatically, people cannot fully regulate every thought.","zh":"如果不想要的歌曲自動出現，人們就不能完全控制每個想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes control over mental habits and attention.","zh":"這個片語描述對心理習慣和注意力的控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"without knowing that","meaning":"在不知道……的情況下","examples":[{"en":"People may remember songs without knowing that they heard them.","zh":"人們可能在不知道自己聽過歌曲的情況下記住它們。"},{"en":"Without knowing that means without being aware of the fact that something happened.","zh":"Without knowing that 指沒有察覺某事曾經發生。"},{"en":"A child may learn a phrase from television without knowing that they heard it many times.","zh":"孩子可能在不知道自己聽過很多次的情況下，從電視學會一句話。"},{"en":"If music plays in the background, listeners may store it without noticing.","zh":"如果音樂在背景播放，聽者可能在沒有注意下儲存它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unconscious or unnoticed experience.","zh":"這個片語描述無意識或未被察覺的經驗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"similar effect on the brain","meaning":"對大腦產生相似影響","examples":[{"en":"Imagining music has a similar effect on the brain to hearing it.","zh":"想像音樂對大腦產生與聽音樂相似的影響。"},{"en":"A similar effect on the brain means producing nearly the same pattern of brain activity.","zh":"Similar effect on the brain 指產生幾乎相同的大腦活動模式。"},{"en":"Seeing a food photo may have a similar effect on the brain to smelling the food.","zh":"看食物照片可能對大腦產生與聞到食物相似的影響。"},{"en":"If imagined music affects the brain like real music, mental sound can be powerful.","zh":"如果想像音樂像真實音樂一樣影響大腦，心理聲音就可以很有力量。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the brain’s response to two experiences.","zh":"這個片語比較大腦對兩種經驗的反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"more persistent","meaning":"更持久；更難消退","examples":[{"en":"An earworm may become more persistent when a fragment repeats.","zh":"當片段重複時，洗腦旋律可能變得更持久。"},{"en":"More persistent means continuing for longer and becoming harder to stop.","zh":"More persistent 指持續更久並變得更難停止。"},{"en":"A cough may become more persistent if someone does not rest properly.","zh":"如果某人沒有好好休息，咳嗽可能變得更持久。"},{"en":"If a song fragment repeats many times, it may stay in the mind longer.","zh":"如果歌曲片段重複很多次，它可能在腦中停留更久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that keeps going despite attempts to stop it.","zh":"這個片語描述即使嘗試停止仍持續的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"short section of a song","meaning":"一小段歌曲","examples":[{"en":"Some earworms consist of a short section of a song.","zh":"有些洗腦旋律由一小段歌曲組成。"},{"en":"A short section of a song is a small part, such as one line, a chorus, or a few notes.","zh":"Short section of a song 是歌曲中的小部分，例如一句歌詞、副歌或幾個音符。"},{"en":"A listener may remember only the short section that appears in an advertisement.","zh":"聽者可能只記得廣告中出現的一小段歌曲。"},{"en":"If the short section is catchy, it may repeat without the rest of the song.","zh":"如果那一小段歌曲易記，它可能在沒有整首歌的情況下重複。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an incomplete but memorable musical part.","zh":"這個片語描述不完整但容易記住的音樂部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"constantly replayed","meaning":"不斷重播","examples":[{"en":"A short musical fragment may be constantly replayed in the mind.","zh":"一小段音樂片段可能在腦海中不斷重播。"},{"en":"Constantly replayed means repeated again and again with little or no break.","zh":"Constantly replayed 指幾乎沒有停頓地一次又一次重複。"},{"en":"A student may constantly replay a teacher’s warning before an important exam.","zh":"重要考試前，學生可能不斷重播老師的提醒。"},{"en":"If a tune is constantly replayed, it can become annoying even if the song is enjoyable.","zh":"如果旋律不斷重播，即使歌曲本身好聽，也可能變得煩人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated mental playback.","zh":"這個片語描述反覆的心理播放。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 170 - Mind Music.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 171":[{"front":"the importance of law","meaning":"法律的重要性","examples":[{"en":"The passage examines the importance of law in modern society.","zh":"文章探討法律在現代社會中的重要性。"},{"en":"The importance of law means the way law helps organise behaviour, rights, duties and public order.","zh":"the importance of law 指法律如何幫助組織行為、權利、責任和公共秩序。"},{"en":"Students can see the importance of law when school rules protect everyone’s safety and fairness.","zh":"當校規保障每個人的安全和公平時，學生可以看見法律的重要性。"},{"en":"Without law, people may not know what is allowed, forbidden or protected.","zh":"沒有法律，人們可能不知道甚麼被容許、禁止或保護。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that law affects daily life, not only courts and judges.","zh":"這個短語顯示法律影響日常生活，而不只是法庭和法官。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"influence virtually all of us","meaning":"幾乎影響我們所有人","examples":[{"en":"The law influences virtually all of us almost all the time.","zh":"法律幾乎一直影響我們所有人。"},{"en":"To influence virtually all of us means to affect nearly everyone in some way.","zh":"influence virtually all of us 指以某種方式影響幾乎每一個人。"},{"en":"Traffic rules influence virtually all of us because we walk, drive, cycle or use buses.","zh":"交通規則幾乎影響我們所有人，因為我們會步行、駕車、踩單車或乘巴士。"},{"en":"If a rule affects housing, food, work and travel, it influences almost everyone’s life.","zh":"如果一條規則影響住屋、食物、工作和交通，它就幾乎影響所有人的生活。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the effect is very widespread.","zh":"這個短語強調影響非常廣泛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"govern almost all aspects of","meaning":"規管……的幾乎所有方面","examples":[{"en":"The law governs almost all aspects of our behaviour.","zh":"法律規管我們行為的幾乎所有方面。"},{"en":"To govern almost all aspects of something means to control or regulate nearly every part of it.","zh":"govern almost all aspects of 某事，指控制或規管它的幾乎每一部分。"},{"en":"School rules govern almost all aspects of classroom behaviour, from speaking to submitting homework.","zh":"校規規管課室行為的幾乎所有方面，由發言到交功課。"},{"en":"When rules cover many actions, people must think about them in everyday decisions.","zh":"當規則涵蓋許多行動，人們在日常決定中就必須考慮它們。"},{"en":"The phrase describes wide control, not control of only one small area.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛控制，而不是只控制一個小範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"aspects of our behaviour","meaning":"我們行為的各個方面","examples":[{"en":"Many aspects of our behaviour are regulated by law.","zh":"我們行為的許多方面都受法律規管。"},{"en":"Aspects of our behaviour are different parts of how we act, speak, work and interact.","zh":"aspects of our behaviour 是我們如何行動、說話、工作和互動的不同部分。"},{"en":"Paying for goods, driving safely and respecting contracts are all aspects of behaviour affected by rules.","zh":"付款買東西、安全駕駛和尊重合約，都是受規則影響的行為方面。"},{"en":"Laws can guide behaviour by setting duties and consequences.","zh":"法律可以透過訂立責任和後果來引導行為。"},{"en":"The phrase breaks human conduct into different areas.","zh":"這個短語把人類行為分成不同範疇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"even after death","meaning":"甚至在死後","examples":[{"en":"The law can affect what happens to a person even after death.","zh":"法律甚至可以影響一個人在死後會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Even after death means after a person has died, not only while they are alive.","zh":"even after death 指在人死後，而不只是在人生前。"},{"en":"A will can decide how a person’s property is shared even after death.","zh":"遺囑可以決定一個人死後財產如何分配。"},{"en":"Legal rules about inheritance can affect families long after someone dies.","zh":"關於繼承的法律規則可以在人死後長時間影響家庭。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that law can continue to matter beyond a person’s lifetime.","zh":"這個短語顯示法律可以在一個人的生命結束後仍然重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"from the embryo onwards","meaning":"從胚胎階段開始","examples":[{"en":"The law affects human beings from the embryo onwards.","zh":"法律從胚胎階段開始影響人類。"},{"en":"From the embryo onwards means starting from the earliest stage of human development and continuing after that.","zh":"from the embryo onwards 指由人類發展最早階段開始，並在之後持續。"},{"en":"Medical rules may apply from the embryo onwards when clinics handle fertility treatment.","zh":"當診所處理生育治療時，醫療規則可能從胚胎階段開始適用。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that legal protection or regulation can begin very early.","zh":"這個短語顯示法律保護或規管可以很早開始。"},{"en":"It describes a starting point and everything that follows.","zh":"它描述一個起點以及之後的一切。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the air we breathe","meaning":"我們呼吸的空氣","examples":[{"en":"Environmental law regulates the quality of the air we breathe.","zh":"環境法規管我們呼吸的空氣質素。"},{"en":"The air we breathe means the air people take into their lungs every day.","zh":"the air we breathe 指人們每天吸入肺部的空氣。"},{"en":"Clean-air rules help protect the air we breathe from smoke, traffic fumes and factory pollution.","zh":"清潔空氣規則幫助保護我們呼吸的空氣，免受煙霧、汽車廢氣和工廠污染影響。"},{"en":"If the air we breathe is polluted, people may suffer asthma, coughing or other health problems.","zh":"如果我們呼吸的空氣受污染，人們可能患上哮喘、咳嗽或其他健康問題。"},{"en":"The phrase connects law with something basic and daily.","zh":"這個短語把法律與基本日常事物連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the food and drink we consume","meaning":"我們食用的食物和飲品","examples":[{"en":"The law regulates the food and drink we consume.","zh":"法律規管我們食用的食物和飲品。"},{"en":"The food and drink we consume means what we eat and drink in daily life.","zh":"the food and drink we consume 指我們日常吃和喝的東西。"},{"en":"Food-safety rules protect the food and drink we consume from harmful bacteria or false labels.","zh":"食物安全規則保護我們食用的食物和飲品，避免有害細菌或虛假標籤。"},{"en":"If regulation is weak, unsafe food may reach schools, shops and homes.","zh":"如果規管薄弱，不安全食物可能進入學校、商店和家庭。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that law affects ordinary meals, not only serious disputes.","zh":"這個短語顯示法律影響普通膳食，而不只是嚴重爭議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"family relationships","meaning":"家庭關係","examples":[{"en":"Family law governs many aspects of family relationships.","zh":"家庭法規管家庭關係的許多方面。"},{"en":"Family relationships are the connections and duties between parents, children, spouses and relatives.","zh":"family relationships 是父母、子女、配偶和親人之間的連繫與責任。"},{"en":"Divorce, childcare and inheritance can all affect family relationships.","zh":"離婚、照顧孩子和繼承都可以影響家庭關係。"},{"en":"When family relationships break down, legal rules may help decide responsibilities fairly.","zh":"當家庭關係破裂，法律規則可能幫助公平決定責任。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to personal ties that can also have legal effects.","zh":"這個短語指個人關係，也可以帶有法律影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"apply at the bottom of the ocean","meaning":"適用於海底","examples":[{"en":"Some legal rules apply even at the bottom of the ocean.","zh":"有些法律規則甚至適用於海底。"},{"en":"To apply at the bottom of the ocean means to remain legally relevant even in deep-sea areas.","zh":"apply at the bottom of the ocean 指即使在深海地區仍具有法律相關性。"},{"en":"Rules about seabed mining may apply at the bottom of the ocean.","zh":"關於海床採礦的規則可能適用於海底。"},{"en":"If companies take resources from the seabed, law may decide who has permission.","zh":"如果公司從海床取得資源，法律可能決定誰有許可。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that law can reach places far from ordinary life.","zh":"這個短語顯示法律可以到達遠離普通生活的地方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"apply in space","meaning":"適用於太空","examples":[{"en":"International law can also apply in space.","zh":"國際法也可以適用於太空。"},{"en":"To apply in space means to govern actions beyond Earth, such as satellites or space missions.","zh":"apply in space 指規管地球以外的行動，例如衛星或太空任務。"},{"en":"Rules may apply in space when countries launch satellites that could hit other objects.","zh":"當國家發射可能撞到其他物件的衛星，規則可能適用於太空。"},{"en":"Without legal rules, space activity could create conflict or dangerous debris.","zh":"沒有法律規則，太空活動可能造成衝突或危險碎片。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that law is not limited to land and sea.","zh":"這個短語顯示法律不限於陸地和海洋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"examine a label","meaning":"查看標籤","examples":[{"en":"Consumers often examine a label before buying a food product.","zh":"消費者在購買食品前常查看標籤。"},{"en":"To examine a label means to look carefully at the printed information on a product.","zh":"examine a label 指仔細查看產品上的印刷資料。"},{"en":"A parent may examine a label to check whether a snack contains peanuts.","zh":"家長可能查看標籤，以確認零食是否含花生。"},{"en":"Labels help consumers avoid ingredients, allergens or false claims.","zh":"標籤幫助消費者避免某些成分、致敏原或虛假聲稱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful checking before buying or using something.","zh":"這個短語描述購買或使用前仔細查核。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a food product","meaning":"食品","examples":[{"en":"Food products must comply with labelling regulations.","zh":"食品必須符合標籤規例。"},{"en":"A food product is any item made, packaged or sold for people to eat or drink.","zh":"a food product 是任何製造、包裝或出售給人食用或飲用的物品。"},{"en":"Bread, yoghurt and bottled juice are all food products.","zh":"麵包、乳酪和樽裝果汁都是食品。"},{"en":"If a food product has unclear ingredients, consumers may not be able to make safe choices.","zh":"如果食品成分不清楚，消費者可能無法作出安全選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to food as something sold and regulated.","zh":"這個短語指作為商品和受規管物品的食物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"engage in work as","meaning":"以……身分工作","examples":[{"en":"A person may engage in work as either an employee or an employer.","zh":"一個人可以以僱員或僱主身分工作。"},{"en":"To engage in work as something means to take part in work in that role.","zh":"engage in work as 某身份，指以該角色參與工作。"},{"en":"A student may engage in weekend work as a shop assistant.","zh":"學生可能以店務助理身分做周末工作。"},{"en":"The role a person works in affects their rights, duties and legal responsibilities.","zh":"一個人的工作角色會影響其權利、責任和法律義務。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the capacity or position in which someone works.","zh":"這個短語重點在某人工作的身份或位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"employee or employer","meaning":"僱員或僱主","examples":[{"en":"Employment law affects both the employee and the employer.","zh":"僱傭法影響僱員和僱主雙方。"},{"en":"An employee is a worker, while an employer is the person or organisation that hires workers.","zh":"employee 是受僱工作的人，而 employer 是聘請員工的人或機構。"},{"en":"A restaurant server is an employee, and the restaurant owner may be the employer.","zh":"餐廳侍應是僱員，而餐廳老闆可能是僱主。"},{"en":"Employment rules protect workers and also tell employers what they must provide.","zh":"僱傭規則保護員工，也告訴僱主必須提供甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase shows both sides of a work relationship.","zh":"這個短語顯示工作關係中的雙方。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"travel on the roads","meaning":"在道路上行駛","examples":[{"en":"Traffic laws apply whenever people travel on the roads.","zh":"每當人們在道路上行駛，交通法都適用。"},{"en":"To travel on the roads means to move along public roads by walking, cycling, driving or riding in vehicles.","zh":"travel on the roads 指透過步行、踩單車、駕車或乘車在公共道路上移動。"},{"en":"A family travelling on the roads must follow seat-belt and speed-limit rules.","zh":"一家人在道路上行駛時，必須遵守安全帶和限速規則。"},{"en":"Road rules reduce accidents by making everyone’s behaviour more predictable.","zh":"道路規則透過令每個人的行為更可預測來減少意外。"},{"en":"The phrase connects daily transport with legal duties.","zh":"這個短語把日常交通與法律責任連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stay in a hotel","meaning":"入住酒店","examples":[{"en":"Various legal duties arise when guests stay in a hotel.","zh":"當住客入住酒店，各種法律責任會產生。"},{"en":"To stay in a hotel means to rent a room there for a short period.","zh":"stay in a hotel 指短期租用酒店房間。"},{"en":"A traveller who stays in a hotel may have rights to safety, privacy and fair service.","zh":"入住酒店的旅客可能享有安全、私隱和公平服務的權利。"},{"en":"Hotels must follow rules on fire safety, hygiene and customer records.","zh":"酒店必須遵守消防安全、衞生和顧客記錄規則。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that ordinary travel can involve legal responsibilities.","zh":"這個短語顯示普通旅行也可以涉及法律責任。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"borrow a library book","meaning":"借閱圖書館書籍","examples":[{"en":"Even borrowing a library book involves rules and responsibilities.","zh":"即使借閱圖書館書籍也涉及規則和責任。"},{"en":"To borrow a library book means to take a book from a library for a limited time and return it later.","zh":"borrow a library book 指從圖書館借走一本書一段有限時間，之後歸還。"},{"en":"A student who borrows a library book must return it by the due date.","zh":"借閱圖書館書籍的學生必須在到期日前歸還。"},{"en":"If borrowers damage or lose books, the library may charge a fee.","zh":"如果借閱者損壞或遺失書籍，圖書館可能收費。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that even simple public services have rules.","zh":"這個短語顯示即使簡單公共服務也有規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"create a company","meaning":"成立公司","examples":[{"en":"Lawyers may help clients create a commercial company.","zh":"律師可能幫助客戶成立商業公司。"},{"en":"To create a company means to legally form a business organisation.","zh":"create a company 指在法律上成立一個商業組織。"},{"en":"Friends opening a café may need to create a company before signing contracts.","zh":"朋友開咖啡店前，可能需要先成立公司再簽合約。"},{"en":"Proper company formation helps decide ownership, tax duties and legal responsibility.","zh":"正式成立公司有助決定擁有權、稅務責任和法律責任。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to legal creation, not just having a business idea.","zh":"這個短語指法律上的成立，而不只是有商業想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"dissolve a company","meaning":"解散公司","examples":[{"en":"Legal procedures must be followed to dissolve a commercial company.","zh":"解散商業公司必須遵循法律程序。"},{"en":"To dissolve a company means to legally close it down so it no longer exists as a company.","zh":"dissolve a company 指在法律上關閉公司，使它不再作為公司存在。"},{"en":"A small business may dissolve a company after all debts are paid and trading stops.","zh":"小企業在還清所有債務並停止營業後，可能解散公司。"},{"en":"If the process is done incorrectly, owners may still face legal or financial problems.","zh":"如果程序處理不當，擁有人仍可能面對法律或財務問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formal closure of a business.","zh":"這個短語描述正式結束一間企業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a commercial company","meaning":"商業公司","examples":[{"en":"Company law regulates the creation and operation of a commercial company.","zh":"公司法規管商業公司的成立和運作。"},{"en":"A commercial company is a business organisation formed to trade, provide services or make profit.","zh":"a commercial company 是為交易、提供服務或賺取利潤而成立的商業組織。"},{"en":"A delivery firm, bookshop or software business can be a commercial company.","zh":"送貨公司、書店或軟件企業都可以是商業公司。"},{"en":"Commercial companies need rules because they deal with money, contracts, workers and customers.","zh":"商業公司需要規則，因為它們處理金錢、合約、員工和顧客。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a business entity rather than a charity or informal group.","zh":"這個短語指商業實體，而不是慈善機構或非正式團體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"engage the services of","meaning":"聘用……的服務","examples":[{"en":"A business may engage the services of a lawyer or consultant.","zh":"企業可能聘用律師或顧問的服務。"},{"en":"To engage the services of someone means to formally hire them to do professional work.","zh":"engage the services of 某人，指正式聘請他們做專業工作。"},{"en":"A family may engage the services of an architect before renovating a flat.","zh":"家庭裝修單位前，可能聘用建築師的服務。"},{"en":"Professionals are engaged when a task requires special knowledge or legal responsibility.","zh":"當任務需要專門知識或法律責任，就會聘用專業人士。"},{"en":"The phrase is more formal than “hire.”","zh":"這個短語比 “hire” 更正式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"anything from…to…","meaning":"由……以至……的任何事情","examples":[{"en":"Legal issues can involve anything from repairing a sink to planning a city.","zh":"法律問題可以涉及由維修洗手盆水管以至規劃城市的任何事情。"},{"en":"Anything from A to B means a very wide range, starting with one example and ending with another.","zh":"anything from A to B 指非常廣泛的範圍，由一個例子到另一個例子。"},{"en":"A school event may need help with anything from printing posters to managing crowds.","zh":"學校活動可能需要處理由印海報以至管理人群的任何事情。"},{"en":"This structure shows that many different types of matters are included.","zh":"這個結構顯示包括許多不同類型的事項。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights range and variety.","zh":"這個短語突出範圍和多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"plumbing a sink","meaning":"安裝或維修洗手盆水管","examples":[{"en":"Even plumbing a sink may involve contractual or safety rules.","zh":"即使安裝或維修洗手盆水管，也可能涉及合約或安全規則。"},{"en":"Plumbing a sink means installing or repairing the pipes that carry water to and from a sink.","zh":"plumbing a sink 指安裝或維修把水帶到洗手盆和排走的水管。"},{"en":"A homeowner may call a plumber when water leaks under the kitchen sink.","zh":"當廚房洗手盆下方漏水，屋主可能找水喉工。"},{"en":"Poor plumbing can cause flooding, mould and damage to nearby flats.","zh":"水管工程差可以造成水浸、發霉和鄰近單位損壞。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that even practical home repairs may involve rules.","zh":"這個短語顯示即使實際家居維修也可能涉及規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"planning a city","meaning":"規劃城市","examples":[{"en":"Planning a city requires knowledge of many areas of law.","zh":"規劃城市需要了解許多法律範疇。"},{"en":"Planning a city means designing how land, roads, housing, public services and buildings should develop.","zh":"planning a city 指設計土地、道路、住屋、公共服務和建築應如何發展。"},{"en":"City planners must decide where schools, parks, homes and transport links should go.","zh":"城市規劃者必須決定學校、公園、住宅和交通連接應設在哪裏。"},{"en":"Poor city planning can create traffic, pollution and unfair access to services.","zh":"差劣城市規劃可以造成交通、污染和服務取得不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase describes large-scale public organisation.","zh":"這個短語描述大規模公共組織。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be in the world of law","meaning":"身處法律世界之中","examples":[{"en":"When we enter into contracts, we are already in the world of law.","zh":"當我們訂立合約時，我們已經身處法律世界之中。"},{"en":"To be in the world of law means to be dealing with legal rules, rights or duties.","zh":"be in the world of law 指正在處理法律規則、權利或責任。"},{"en":"A student renting a flat enters the world of law when she signs a tenancy agreement.","zh":"學生簽署租約時，就進入法律世界。"},{"en":"People may enter this world without noticing because everyday agreements can be legal.","zh":"人們可能不知不覺進入這個世界，因為日常協議也可以具有法律性。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that law begins in ordinary actions, not only court cases.","zh":"這個短語顯示法律從普通行動開始，而不只是法庭案件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be widely recognised as","meaning":"被廣泛視為……","examples":[{"en":"Law is widely recognised as a standard for judging behaviour.","zh":"法律被廣泛視為判斷行為的標準。"},{"en":"To be widely recognised as something means many people accept that description as true.","zh":"be widely recognised as 某事，指許多人接受該描述為真。"},{"en":"A university may be widely recognised as a strong medical school.","zh":"一所大學可能被廣泛視為強大的醫學院。"},{"en":"Wide recognition gives an idea authority because many people accept it.","zh":"廣泛認可令一個想法具有權威，因為許多人接受它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad acceptance.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the standard by which","meaning":"用來判斷……的標準","examples":[{"en":"Law has become the standard by which behaviour is judged.","zh":"法律已成為用來判斷行為的標準。"},{"en":"The standard by which something is judged is the rule or measure used to assess it.","zh":"the standard by which 某事 is judged，是用來評估它的規則或尺度。"},{"en":"Exam rubrics are the standard by which essays are marked.","zh":"考試評分準則是用來評改文章的標準。"},{"en":"When a standard is clear, people can compare behaviour more fairly.","zh":"當標準清楚，人們可以更公平地比較行為。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the measure used for judgement.","zh":"這個短語指出判斷所用的尺度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"judge behaviour","meaning":"判斷行為","examples":[{"en":"Modern societies increasingly use law to judge behaviour.","zh":"現代社會越來越使用法律來判斷行為。"},{"en":"To judge behaviour means to decide whether actions are right, wrong, acceptable or punishable.","zh":"judge behaviour 指判定行動是對、錯、可接受還是應受懲罰。"},{"en":"A teacher may judge behaviour by asking whether students followed classroom rules.","zh":"老師可能透過學生是否遵守課室規則來判斷行為。"},{"en":"Legal judgement can affect punishment, compensation or public reputation.","zh":"法律判斷可以影響懲罰、賠償或公眾聲譽。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on evaluating actions.","zh":"這個短語重點在評估行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a telling development","meaning":"很能說明問題的發展","examples":[{"en":"The growing influence of law is a telling development in recent history.","zh":"法律影響力增長是近代歷史中很能說明問題的發展。"},{"en":"A telling development is a change that clearly reveals something important.","zh":"a telling development 是清楚揭示重要事情的變化。"},{"en":"More schools hiring counsellors is a telling development about student stress.","zh":"越來越多學校聘請輔導員，很能說明學生壓力問題。"},{"en":"When a change is telling, it points to a larger social pattern.","zh":"當一項發展很能說明問題，它指向更大的社會模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a development with strong meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述具有強烈意義的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in recent history","meaning":"在近代歷史中","examples":[{"en":"The role of law has expanded considerably in recent history.","zh":"法律角色在近代歷史中大幅擴展。"},{"en":"In recent history means during the relatively modern period, not ancient times.","zh":"in recent history 指在相對現代的時期，而不是古代。"},{"en":"In recent history, mobile phones have changed how students learn and communicate.","zh":"在近代歷史中，手機改變了學生學習和溝通的方式。"},{"en":"The phrase places a change within a modern historical timeframe.","zh":"這個短語把變化放在現代歷史時間框架內。"},{"en":"It usually refers to events close enough to still shape the present.","zh":"它通常指仍足以塑造現在的事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the idea of law","meaning":"法律觀念","examples":[{"en":"The idea of law has spread throughout social life.","zh":"法律觀念已擴散至整個社會生活。"},{"en":"The idea of law means the belief that rules, rights and duties should guide society.","zh":"the idea of law 指規則、權利和責任應指導社會這種信念。"},{"en":"When children learn fairness through classroom rules, they begin to understand the idea of law.","zh":"當孩子透過課室規則學習公平，他們開始理解法律觀念。"},{"en":"This idea spreads when people use legal language to discuss everyday problems.","zh":"當人們用法律語言討論日常問題，這種觀念就會擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to law as a social concept, not one single rule.","zh":"這個短語指作為社會概念的法律，而不是單一規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"permeate all parts of","meaning":"滲透……的各個部分","examples":[{"en":"Legal standards have permeated all parts of social life.","zh":"法律標準已滲透社會生活的各個部分。"},{"en":"To permeate all parts of something means to spread through nearly every area of it.","zh":"permeate all parts of 某事，指擴散至它幾乎每個範疇。"},{"en":"Digital technology has permeated all parts of school life, from homework to attendance records.","zh":"數碼科技已滲透學校生活各部分，由功課到點名記錄。"},{"en":"When an idea permeates society, people meet it in many ordinary situations.","zh":"當一個想法滲透社會，人們會在許多普通情況中遇到它。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests deep and widespread influence.","zh":"這個短語暗示深而廣的影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"social life","meaning":"社會生活","examples":[{"en":"Law increasingly influences every area of social life.","zh":"法律越來越影響社會生活的每個範疇。"},{"en":"Social life means the way people live together, interact and form relationships in society.","zh":"social life 指人們在社會中共同生活、互動和建立關係的方式。"},{"en":"Public transport, shopping, work and family events are all parts of social life.","zh":"公共交通、購物、工作和家庭活動都是社會生活的一部分。"},{"en":"Rules shape social life by deciding what behaviour is acceptable in shared spaces.","zh":"規則透過決定共享空間中哪些行為可接受來塑造社會生活。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to everyday life among people.","zh":"這個短語指人與人之間的日常生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a universal standard","meaning":"普遍標準","examples":[{"en":"Legality is increasingly treated as a universal standard.","zh":"合法性越來越被視為普遍標準。"},{"en":"A universal standard is a measure that is meant to apply broadly to everyone or every case.","zh":"universal standard 是旨在廣泛適用於所有人或所有情況的尺度。"},{"en":"Safety rules in a school should be a universal standard for all students, not only some classes.","zh":"學校安全規則應是所有學生的普遍標準，而不只是某些班級。"},{"en":"Universal standards can create fairness because people know the same rule applies to all.","zh":"普遍標準可以創造公平，因為人們知道同一規則適用於所有人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a standard used across many situations.","zh":"這個短語描述用於許多情況的標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be socially tolerated","meaning":"為社會所容許","examples":[{"en":"People often ask whether conduct should be socially tolerated.","zh":"人們常問某種行為是否應為社會所容許。"},{"en":"To be socially tolerated means to be allowed or accepted by society even if some people dislike it.","zh":"be socially tolerated 指即使有人不喜歡，仍被社會容許或接受。"},{"en":"Loud phone calls on buses may be socially tolerated in some places but not in others.","zh":"在某些地方，巴士上大聲講電話可能為社會所容許，但在另一些地方則不是。"},{"en":"If behaviour is no longer tolerated, people may demand new rules.","zh":"如果某行為不再被容忍，人們可能要求新規則。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on social acceptance, not only legal permission.","zh":"這個短語重點在社會接受，而不只是法律許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"progressively become","meaning":"逐漸成為","examples":[{"en":"Legality is progressively becoming the main test of acceptability.","zh":"合法性正逐漸成為可接受性的主要測試。"},{"en":"To progressively become something means to gradually turn into it over time.","zh":"progressively become 某事，指隨時間逐步變成它。"},{"en":"Online learning progressively became normal as more schools used digital platforms.","zh":"隨着更多學校使用數碼平台，網上學習逐漸成為正常做法。"},{"en":"Gradual change can be hard to notice until it becomes widespread.","zh":"漸變在變得廣泛之前可能難以察覺。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow development, not sudden change.","zh":"這個短語描述緩慢發展，而不是突然改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"whether it is legal","meaning":"是否合法","examples":[{"en":"People increasingly judge conduct according to whether it is legal.","zh":"人們越來越根據某行為是否合法來判斷它。"},{"en":"Whether it is legal means whether something is allowed by law.","zh":"whether it is legal 指某事是否受法律容許。"},{"en":"Before sharing customer data, a company must ask whether it is legal.","zh":"公司分享顧客資料前，必須問這是否合法。"},{"en":"If an action is illegal, it may bring fines, court action or reputational damage.","zh":"如果行動違法，可能帶來罰款、法律行動或聲譽損害。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on legal permission.","zh":"這個短語重點在法律許可。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Conduct is now judged by legality rather than by tradition alone.","zh":"現在行為是按合法性判斷，而不是只按傳統判斷。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of, and it shows a clear contrast between two ideas.","zh":"rather than 指而不是，並顯示兩個想法之間的清楚對比。"},{"en":"A school should solve bullying through clear action rather than empty warnings.","zh":"學校應透過清楚行動處理欺凌，而不是空洞警告。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show which basis or choice is being rejected.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示哪個基礎或選擇被排除。"},{"en":"It is useful when separating the real standard from another possible standard.","zh":"它適合用來分開真正標準和另一可能標準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be considered acceptable","meaning":"被認為可以接受","examples":[{"en":"Some conduct was traditionally considered acceptable despite lacking legal support.","zh":"有些行為傳統上被認為可以接受，即使缺乏法律支持。"},{"en":"To be considered acceptable means to be regarded as suitable, normal or allowed.","zh":"be considered acceptable 指被視為合適、正常或可容許。"},{"en":"In some homes, using phones at dinner is not considered acceptable.","zh":"在一些家庭中，晚飯時用手機不被認為可以接受。"},{"en":"What is considered acceptable can change as society’s values change.","zh":"隨着社會價值改變，被認為可接受的事也會改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes social judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述社會判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in earlier times","meaning":"在較早時期","examples":[{"en":"In earlier times, most people had little access to written law.","zh":"在較早時期，大多數人很少接觸到成文法律。"},{"en":"In earlier times means in the past, especially before modern conditions developed.","zh":"in earlier times 指在過去，尤其是在現代條件發展之前。"},{"en":"In earlier times, students often relied on libraries rather than online search engines.","zh":"在較早時期，學生常依靠圖書館，而不是網上搜尋器。"},{"en":"The phrase helps compare past and present situations.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較過去和現在的情況。"},{"en":"It usually introduces a historical contrast.","zh":"它通常引出歷史對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"by contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"By contrast, many people today can read and understand basic legal information.","zh":"相比之下，今天許多人能閱讀並理解基本法律資訊。"},{"en":"By contrast introduces an opposite or very different situation.","zh":"by contrast 引出相反或非常不同的情況。"},{"en":"Some students learn well by listening; by contrast, others need diagrams and practice.","zh":"有些學生靠聆聽學得好；相比之下，另一些需要圖表和練習。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers compare two clear differences.","zh":"這個短語幫助寫作者比較兩個清楚差異。"},{"en":"It signals that the next point should be understood against the previous one.","zh":"它表示下一點應與前一點對照理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a vast number of people","meaning":"大量人士","examples":[{"en":"A vast number of people can now access legal information.","zh":"現在大量人士可以取得法律資訊。"},{"en":"A vast number of people means a very large number of people.","zh":"a vast number of people 指非常多人。"},{"en":"A vast number of people use smartphones to read news, pay bills and communicate.","zh":"大量人士使用智能手機看新聞、付款和溝通。"},{"en":"When many people can access information, public discussion can become broader.","zh":"當許多人能取得資訊，公共討論可以變得更廣泛。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses large scale.","zh":"這個短語強調規模大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take an interest in","meaning":"對……產生興趣","examples":[{"en":"More members of the public can take an interest in law.","zh":"更多公眾成員可以對法律產生興趣。"},{"en":"To take an interest in something means to become curious about it or want to learn more.","zh":"take an interest in 某事，指對它產生好奇或想了解更多。"},{"en":"A child may take an interest in science after visiting a space museum.","zh":"孩子參觀太空博物館後，可能對科學產生興趣。"},{"en":"Public interest can grow when an issue affects people’s daily lives.","zh":"當議題影響人們日常生活，公眾興趣可以增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active curiosity.","zh":"這個短語描述主動好奇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the general population","meaning":"普羅大眾","examples":[{"en":"The general population can increasingly influence legal development.","zh":"普羅大眾越來越能影響法律發展。"},{"en":"The general population means ordinary people in society, not only experts or officials.","zh":"the general population 指社會中的普通人，而不只是專家或官員。"},{"en":"Public-health messages must be clear enough for the general population to understand.","zh":"公共衞生訊息必須清楚到普羅大眾能理解。"},{"en":"When ordinary people understand an issue, they can join public debate more confidently.","zh":"當普通人理解議題，他們可以更有信心參與公共討論。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to people as a whole community.","zh":"這個短語指作為整個社群的人們。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"help shape the law","meaning":"協助塑造法律","examples":[{"en":"Citizens can help shape the law through public debate and voting.","zh":"公民可以透過公共辯論和投票協助塑造法律。"},{"en":"To help shape the law means to influence how laws are made, changed or understood.","zh":"help shape the law 指影響法律如何制定、修改或理解。"},{"en":"Parents may help shape school rules by joining consultation meetings.","zh":"家長可以透過參加諮詢會協助塑造校規。"},{"en":"Public pressure can lead lawmakers to revise unfair rules.","zh":"公眾壓力可以促使立法者修訂不公平規則。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that ordinary people can influence legal development.","zh":"這個短語顯示普通人可以影響法律發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a versatile instrument","meaning":"多用途的工具","examples":[{"en":"Law is a versatile instrument that can serve very different purposes.","zh":"法律是一種多用途的工具，可以服務非常不同的目的。"},{"en":"A versatile instrument is a tool that can be used in many different ways.","zh":"versatile instrument 是可以用於許多不同方式的工具。"},{"en":"A smartphone is a versatile instrument because it can call, record, pay and navigate.","zh":"智能手機是多用途工具，因為它可以打電話、錄音、付款和導航。"},{"en":"Law can protect people, regulate business or, if misused, support unfair control.","zh":"法律可以保護人、規管企業，若被誤用，也可以支持不公平控制。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights flexibility of use.","zh":"這個短語突出用途上的靈活性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be used equally well for","meaning":"同樣可被用於……","examples":[{"en":"Law can be used equally well for beneficial or harmful purposes.","zh":"法律同樣可被用於有益或有害的目的。"},{"en":"To be used equally well for different purposes means to work effectively for very different aims.","zh":"be used equally well for 不同目的，指能有效服務非常不同的目標。"},{"en":"Social media can be used equally well for education or spreading rumours.","zh":"社交媒體同樣可被用於教育或散播謠言。"},{"en":"A powerful tool is not automatically good; its effect depends on how people use it.","zh":"強大工具不會自動是好的；其效果取決於人們如何使用它。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that the same thing can serve opposite goals.","zh":"這個短語強調同一事物可以服務相反目標。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the improvement of humanity","meaning":"改善人類福祉","examples":[{"en":"Fair laws can contribute to the improvement of humanity.","zh":"公平法律可以有助改善人類福祉。"},{"en":"The improvement of humanity means making human life fairer, safer, kinder or more dignified.","zh":"the improvement of humanity 指令人的生活更公平、安全、仁慈或有尊嚴。"},{"en":"Laws against child labour can support the improvement of humanity by protecting children.","zh":"禁止童工的法律可以透過保護兒童來支持改善人類福祉。"},{"en":"When laws reduce suffering, society becomes more humane.","zh":"當法律減少痛苦，社會會變得更人道。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on bettering human welfare.","zh":"這個短語重點在改善人類福祉。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the degradation of humanity","meaning":"令人類尊嚴受損","examples":[{"en":"Unjust laws can contribute to the degradation of humanity.","zh":"不公義法律可以令人類尊嚴受損。"},{"en":"The degradation of humanity means reducing human dignity, freedom or moral worth.","zh":"the degradation of humanity 指降低人的尊嚴、自由或道德價值。"},{"en":"Discriminatory rules can lead to the degradation of humanity by treating some people as less valuable.","zh":"歧視性規則可以透過把某些人視為較低價值而令人類尊嚴受損。"},{"en":"When law is used unfairly, it can damage society instead of improving it.","zh":"當法律被不公平使用，它可以損害社會，而不是改善社會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes harm to human dignity.","zh":"這個短語描述對人類尊嚴的傷害。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"put something in a significant position","meaning":"令……處於重要地位","examples":[{"en":"Its influence puts law in a very significant position.","zh":"法律的影響力令它處於非常重要的地位。"},{"en":"To put something in a significant position means to make it important or powerful in a situation.","zh":"put something in a significant position 指令某物在某情況中變得重要或有力。"},{"en":"Online learning put teachers’ digital skills in a significant position during school closures.","zh":"停課期間，網上學習令老師的數碼技能處於重要地位。"},{"en":"When something affects many decisions, it gains social importance.","zh":"當某事影響許多決定，它就取得社會重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making something central or influential.","zh":"這個短語描述令某事變得核心或有影響力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a rapidly developing world","meaning":"急速發展的世界","examples":[{"en":"Legal knowledge is essential in a rapidly developing world.","zh":"在急速發展的世界中，法律知識是必不可少的。"},{"en":"A rapidly developing world is a world where technology, business and society change quickly.","zh":"a rapidly developing world 是科技、商業和社會快速改變的世界。"},{"en":"Students need digital skills in a rapidly developing world because jobs keep changing.","zh":"在急速發展的世界中，學生需要數碼技能，因為工作不斷改變。"},{"en":"Fast development creates new problems that old rules may not cover clearly.","zh":"快速發展會產生舊規則未必清楚涵蓋的新問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes modern life as quick-changing and complex.","zh":"這個短語描述現代生活快速變化且複雜。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"all sorts of","meaning":"各式各樣的","examples":[{"en":"Modern society depends on all sorts of specialised skills.","zh":"現代社會依賴各式各樣的專門技能。"},{"en":"All sorts of means many different kinds of.","zh":"all sorts of 指許多不同種類的。"},{"en":"A school fair needs all sorts of help, from cooking to crowd control.","zh":"學校嘉年華需要各式各樣的幫助，由煮食到人群管理。"},{"en":"When a task is complex, all sorts of people may need to work together.","zh":"當任務複雜，各式各樣的人可能需要合作。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses variety.","zh":"這個短語強調多樣性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"valuable skills and knowledge","meaning":"寶貴的技能與知識","examples":[{"en":"Technical and legal knowledge are both valuable skills and knowledge.","zh":"技術和法律知識都是寶貴的技能與知識。"},{"en":"Valuable skills and knowledge are abilities and information that help people solve important problems.","zh":"valuable skills and knowledge 是幫助人解決重要問題的能力和資訊。"},{"en":"First-aid training is valuable knowledge because it can help someone in an emergency.","zh":"急救訓練是寶貴知識，因為它可以在緊急情況中幫到人。"},{"en":"Valuable skills can improve work, protect people and open opportunities.","zh":"寶貴技能可以改善工作、保護人並開拓機會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical ability that matters.","zh":"這個短語描述重要的實用能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"communications technology","meaning":"通訊科技","examples":[{"en":"Modern organisations rely heavily on communications technology.","zh":"現代機構非常依賴通訊科技。"},{"en":"Communications technology means tools and systems used to send, receive and share information.","zh":"communications technology 指用來傳送、接收和分享資訊的工具和系統。"},{"en":"Email, video calls and messaging apps are forms of communications technology.","zh":"電郵、視像通話和通訊應用程式都是通訊科技。"},{"en":"If communications technology fails, offices, schools and hospitals may struggle to coordinate work.","zh":"如果通訊科技失靈，辦公室、學校和醫院可能難以協調工作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to technology that connects people.","zh":"這個短語指連接人們的科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be relied upon by","meaning":"為……所依賴","examples":[{"en":"IT specialists are relied upon by the rest of society.","zh":"資訊科技專家為社會其他人所依賴。"},{"en":"To be relied upon by someone means to be depended on for help, skill or support.","zh":"be relied upon by 某人，指被依靠以提供幫助、技能或支援。"},{"en":"Nurses are relied upon by patients who need daily care and medicine.","zh":"需要日常照顧和藥物的病人依賴護士。"},{"en":"If a service is heavily relied upon, its failure can affect many people.","zh":"如果某服務被高度依賴，其失靈可以影響許多人。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dependence on someone or something.","zh":"這個短語描述對某人或某物的依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an IT help desk","meaning":"資訊科技支援台","examples":[{"en":"Many organisations maintain an IT help desk for technical support.","zh":"許多機構設有資訊科技支援台以提供技術支援。"},{"en":"An IT help desk is a service that helps people solve computer, software or network problems.","zh":"an IT help desk 是幫助人解決電腦、軟件或網絡問題的服務。"},{"en":"A student may contact the IT help desk if her school login stops working.","zh":"如果學校登入帳戶不能使用，學生可能聯絡資訊科技支援台。"},{"en":"Without an IT help desk, small technical problems can delay work for many staff.","zh":"沒有資訊科技支援台，小技術問題可以延誤許多員工的工作。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a support point for technology issues.","zh":"這個短語指處理科技問題的支援點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"local and central government","meaning":"地方及中央政府","examples":[{"en":"IT specialists work in both local and central government offices.","zh":"資訊科技專家在地方和中央政府辦公室工作。"},{"en":"Local and central government means government at community or regional level and at national level.","zh":"local and central government 指社區或地區層面的政府，以及國家層面的政府。"},{"en":"Local government may manage rubbish collection, while central government makes national policy.","zh":"地方政府可能管理垃圾收集，而中央政府制定全國政策。"},{"en":"Both levels need skilled staff to run public services.","zh":"兩個層面都需要熟練員工來運作公共服務。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts smaller-area government with national government.","zh":"這個短語對比較小地區政府與國家政府。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"without their knowledge","meaning":"沒有他們的知識","examples":[{"en":"Without their knowledge, many modern systems would stop functioning.","zh":"沒有他們的知識，許多現代系統會停止運作。"},{"en":"Without their knowledge means if their expertise or understanding were not available.","zh":"without their knowledge 指如果沒有他們的專業知識或理解。"},{"en":"Without nurses’ knowledge, hospitals could not give safe daily care.","zh":"沒有護士的知識，醫院不能提供安全的日常護理。"},{"en":"Specialist knowledge keeps complex systems running smoothly.","zh":"專門知識令複雜系統順利運作。"},{"en":"The phrase shows dependence on people’s expertise.","zh":"這個短語顯示對人們專業能力的依賴。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"commercial and social life","meaning":"商業與社會生活","examples":[{"en":"Technology supports many parts of commercial and social life.","zh":"科技支援商業與社會生活的許多部分。"},{"en":"Commercial and social life means business activity and ordinary interaction between people.","zh":"commercial and social life 指商業活動以及人與人之間的普通互動。"},{"en":"Online payment affects commercial life, while messaging apps affect social life.","zh":"網上付款影響商業生活，而通訊應用程式影響社會生活。"},{"en":"If technology fails, both buying goods and staying in touch can become difficult.","zh":"如果科技失靈，購買貨品和保持聯絡都可能變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase combines economic activity with community life.","zh":"這個短語結合經濟活動和社區生活。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"seize up","meaning":"停頓；無法運作","examples":[{"en":"Without technical support, many services would seize up within minutes.","zh":"沒有技術支援，許多服務會在幾分鐘內停頓。"},{"en":"To seize up means to stop working or moving properly.","zh":"seize up 指停止正常工作或移動。"},{"en":"A printer may seize up when paper jams inside it.","zh":"當紙張卡在打印機內，打印機可能無法運作。"},{"en":"If a payment system seizes up, shops may be unable to serve customers.","zh":"如果付款系統停頓，商店可能無法服務顧客。"},{"en":"The phrase describes sudden or serious failure to function.","zh":"這個短語描述突然或嚴重的功能失靈。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"legal understanding","meaning":"法律知識；對法律的理解","examples":[{"en":"Legal understanding is vital in a society governed by complex rules.","zh":"在由複雜規則管理的社會中，法律知識至關重要。"},{"en":"Legal understanding means knowing how laws, rights and duties work in practical situations.","zh":"legal understanding 指知道法律、權利和責任在實際情況中如何運作。"},{"en":"A tenant needs legal understanding before signing a long rental contract.","zh":"租客在簽長期租約前需要法律知識。"},{"en":"Without legal understanding, people may lose rights or break rules without realising it.","zh":"沒有法律理解，人們可能失去權利或在不知情下違規。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical knowledge of law.","zh":"這個短語指對法律的實用知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"just as vital","meaning":"同樣重要","examples":[{"en":"Legal knowledge is just as vital as technical expertise.","zh":"法律知識與技術專長同樣重要。"},{"en":"Just as vital means equally important and necessary.","zh":"just as vital 指同樣重要和必要。"},{"en":"In a hospital, clear communication is just as vital as medical equipment.","zh":"在醫院中，清楚溝通與醫療設備同樣重要。"},{"en":"If two skills are just as vital, society should not value one and ignore the other.","zh":"如果兩種技能同樣重要，社會不應重視一種而忽視另一種。"},{"en":"The phrase makes a strong comparison of importance.","zh":"這個短語對重要性作強烈比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"universally needed","meaning":"普遍需要的","examples":[{"en":"Some degree of legal understanding is universally needed.","zh":"某程度的法律理解是普遍需要的。"},{"en":"Universally needed means needed by almost everyone, not only a special group.","zh":"universally needed 指幾乎每個人都需要，而不只是某個特殊群體。"},{"en":"Basic digital skills are universally needed when schools and workplaces use online systems.","zh":"當學校和職場使用網上系統，基本數碼技能就是普遍需要的。"},{"en":"If something is universally needed, education should make it accessible to many people.","zh":"如果某事被普遍需要，教育就應令許多人能取得它。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses very broad necessity.","zh":"這個短語強調非常廣泛的必要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"put it like this","meaning":"這樣表達","examples":[{"en":"The comedian Jerry Seinfeld put it like this when describing lawyers.","zh":"喜劇演員 Jerry Seinfeld 在描述律師時這樣表達。"},{"en":"To put it like this means to explain an idea in this particular way.","zh":"put it like this 指用這種特定方式解釋一個想法。"},{"en":"A teacher might put it like this: grammar is a map, not a prison.","zh":"老師可能這樣表達：文法是一張地圖，不是一座監獄。"},{"en":"People use this phrase before giving a simple or memorable explanation.","zh":"人們在給出簡單或令人記得的解釋前會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a way of expressing an idea.","zh":"這個短語引出表達想法的方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"throw the dice","meaning":"擲骰子","examples":[{"en":"Seinfeld compares everyday life to throwing the dice in a game.","zh":"Seinfeld 把日常生活比作遊戲中擲骰子。"},{"en":"To throw the dice means to roll dice in a game, often before moving or taking a chance.","zh":"throw the dice 指在遊戲中擲骰子，通常是在移動或冒險前。"},{"en":"Children throw the dice before moving their pieces in a board game.","zh":"孩子在棋盤遊戲中移動棋子前會擲骰子。"},{"en":"The image suggests that life involves choices, rules and uncertain outcomes.","zh":"這個意象暗示人生涉及選擇、規則和不確定結果。"},{"en":"The phrase can imply chance or risk.","zh":"這個短語可以暗示機會或風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"play the game","meaning":"參與遊戲；按規則行事","examples":[{"en":"People participate in society without always understanding the rules of the game.","zh":"人們參與社會時，並不總是理解遊戲規則。"},{"en":"To play the game means to take part in an activity that has rules or expectations.","zh":"play the game 指參與一項有規則或期望的活動。"},{"en":"A new employee must learn how to play the game at work, such as meeting deadlines and reporting problems.","zh":"新員工必須學會在工作中按規則行事，例如準時完成任務和報告問題。"},{"en":"If people do not know the rules, they may make mistakes without intending to.","zh":"如果人們不知道規則，他們可能在無意中犯錯。"},{"en":"The phrase compares social life to a rule-based game.","zh":"這個短語把社會生活比作有規則的遊戲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"move pieces around the board","meaning":"在棋盤上移動棋子","examples":[{"en":"We make decisions as though we were moving pieces around a board.","zh":"我們作決定時，就好像在棋盤上移動棋子。"},{"en":"To move pieces around the board means to move game pieces according to rules in a board game.","zh":"move pieces around the board 指在棋盤遊戲中按照規則移動棋子。"},{"en":"In chess, players move pieces around the board to attack, defend and plan ahead.","zh":"在國際象棋中，玩家在棋盤上移動棋子以進攻、防守和預先計劃。"},{"en":"The comparison suggests that social decisions also depend on rules and consequences.","zh":"這個比喻暗示社會決定也取決於規則和後果。"},{"en":"The phrase creates an image of life as a structured game.","zh":"這個短語創造人生如有結構遊戲的意象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"if there is a problem","meaning":"如果出現問題","examples":[{"en":"If there is a legal problem, people often consult a lawyer.","zh":"如果出現法律問題，人們常諮詢律師。"},{"en":"If there is a problem introduces the situation in which help or action is needed.","zh":"if there is a problem 引出需要幫助或行動的情況。"},{"en":"If there is a problem with a bill, a customer should contact the company quickly.","zh":"如果帳單出現問題，顧客應盡快聯絡公司。"},{"en":"Problems often require specialist advice when ordinary knowledge is not enough.","zh":"當普通知識不足，問題常需要專家建議。"},{"en":"The phrase sets up a condition and likely response.","zh":"這個短語設定條件和可能反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"read the rules","meaning":"閱讀規則","examples":[{"en":"The lawyer is compared with someone who has read the rules of the game.","zh":"律師被比作讀過遊戲規則的人。"},{"en":"To read the rules means to know or study the instructions that control an activity.","zh":"read the rules 指知道或研究控制某活動的指示。"},{"en":"Before playing a new board game, students should read the rules carefully.","zh":"玩新棋盤遊戲前，學生應仔細閱讀規則。"},{"en":"People who understand the rules can avoid mistakes and advise others.","zh":"理解規則的人可以避免錯誤並建議他人。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests knowledge of how a system works.","zh":"這個短語暗示了解系統如何運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make sense of","meaning":"理解","examples":[{"en":"A lawyer helps clients make sense of complex legal rules.","zh":"律師幫助客戶理解複雜法律規則。"},{"en":"To make sense of something means to understand it clearly after it seemed confusing.","zh":"make sense of 某事，指在它原本令人困惑後清楚理解它。"},{"en":"A teacher helps students make sense of a difficult poem by explaining the images.","zh":"老師透過解釋意象，幫助學生理解困難詩歌。"},{"en":"When rules are complex, explanation can turn confusion into practical understanding.","zh":"當規則複雜，解釋可以把困惑轉化為實用理解。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the process of making something understandable.","zh":"這個短語描述令某事變得可理解的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the number of laws","meaning":"法律的數量","examples":[{"en":"The number of laws has never been greater.","zh":"法律的數量從未如此之多。"},{"en":"The number of laws means how many legal rules or statutes exist.","zh":"the number of laws 指存在多少法律規則或法令。"},{"en":"A small business may struggle when the number of laws about tax, safety and employment increases.","zh":"當關於稅務、安全和僱傭的法律數量增加，小企業可能感到吃力。"},{"en":"More laws can provide protection, but they can also make the system harder to understand.","zh":"更多法律可以提供保護，但也可以令制度更難理解。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on quantity.","zh":"這個短語重點在數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Acts of Parliament","meaning":"國會法令","examples":[{"en":"Dozens of new Acts of Parliament may be passed each year.","zh":"每年可能通過數十項新的國會法令。"},{"en":"Acts of Parliament are laws formally passed by Parliament.","zh":"Acts of Parliament 是由國會正式通過的法律。"},{"en":"An Act of Parliament may create new rules about schools, transport or healthcare.","zh":"一項國會法令可能制定關於學校、交通或醫療的新規則。"},{"en":"Once an Act is passed, people and organisations may have new legal duties.","zh":"一旦法令通過，個人和機構可能有新的法律責任。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to formal legislation.","zh":"這個短語指正式立法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be produced every year","meaning":"每年制定","examples":[{"en":"Many new laws are produced every year.","zh":"許多新法律每年制定。"},{"en":"To be produced every year means to be created or issued annually.","zh":"be produced every year 指每年被創造或發布。"},{"en":"A school may produce a new handbook every year to update rules for students.","zh":"學校可能每年製作新手冊，以更新學生規則。"},{"en":"When many rules are produced yearly, people need ways to keep up.","zh":"當許多規則每年制定，人們需要方法跟上。"},{"en":"The phrase describes regular yearly creation.","zh":"這個短語描述每年定期產生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"thereby delivering","meaning":"從而帶來","examples":[{"en":"New Acts are passed, thereby delivering thousands of additional rules.","zh":"新法令被通過，從而帶來數以千計的額外規則。"},{"en":"Thereby delivering means producing a result through the action just mentioned.","zh":"thereby delivering 指透過剛提到的行動產生某結果。"},{"en":"The school added online forms, thereby reducing paper use.","zh":"學校加入網上表格，從而減少紙張使用。"},{"en":"This phrase links an action directly to its consequence.","zh":"這個短語把一個行動直接連繫到其後果。"},{"en":"It is formal and often used in writing.","zh":"它較正式，常用於寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"legislative output","meaning":"立法產量","examples":[{"en":"The legislative output of Parliament has increased substantially.","zh":"國會的立法產量已大幅增加。"},{"en":"Legislative output means the amount of law produced by a law-making body.","zh":"legislative output 指立法機構制定的法律數量。"},{"en":"A busy council may have high legislative output if it passes many local rules.","zh":"如果通過許多地方規則，繁忙議會可能有高立法產量。"},{"en":"High output can show active government, but it may also create complexity.","zh":"高產量可以顯示政府活躍，但也可能造成複雜性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the quantity of new laws or regulations produced.","zh":"這個短語描述新法律或規例產生的數量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"more than double","meaning":"增加超過一倍","examples":[{"en":"The annual volume of legislation has more than doubled.","zh":"每年立法量已增加超過一倍。"},{"en":"To more than double means to increase to more than twice the original amount.","zh":"more than double 指增加到超過原本數量的兩倍。"},{"en":"If a class grows from 20 students to 45, its size has more than doubled.","zh":"如果一班由20名學生增至45名，班級人數就增加超過一倍。"},{"en":"A sharp increase can create pressure on teachers, workers or legal professionals.","zh":"急劇增加可以為老師、員工或法律專業人士造成壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes very large growth.","zh":"這個短語描述非常大的增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in recent times","meaning":"近年","examples":[{"en":"Parliamentary output has risen sharply in recent times.","zh":"近年國會產量急劇上升。"},{"en":"In recent times means in the modern or relatively recent past.","zh":"in recent times 指在現代或相對近期的過去。"},{"en":"In recent times, online meetings have become normal in many workplaces.","zh":"近年，網上會議在許多職場變得正常。"},{"en":"The phrase helps show that a change is not ancient but fairly current.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示某變化不是古老的，而是相當近期的。"},{"en":"It often introduces a modern trend.","zh":"它常引出現代趨勢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the legislature","meaning":"立法機關","examples":[{"en":"The legislature is responsible for passing new laws.","zh":"立法機關負責通過新法律。"},{"en":"The legislature is the part of government that makes or passes laws.","zh":"the legislature 是政府中制定或通過法律的部分。"},{"en":"Parliament, congress or a local council can act as a legislature.","zh":"國會、議會或地方議會都可以作為立法機關。"},{"en":"When the legislature passes a rule, citizens and organisations may need to follow it.","zh":"當立法機關通過規則，公民和機構可能需要遵守。"},{"en":"The word names the law-making body.","zh":"這個字指出制定法律的機構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pass an Act","meaning":"通過法令","examples":[{"en":"The legislature may pass an Act of Parliament after extensive debate.","zh":"立法機關可能在廣泛辯論後通過國會法令。"},{"en":"To pass an Act means to formally approve a law through the law-making process.","zh":"pass an Act 指透過立法程序正式批准法律。"},{"en":"A parliament may pass an Act to improve workplace safety.","zh":"國會可能通過法令以改善工作場所安全。"},{"en":"Once an Act is passed, it can create rights, duties or penalties.","zh":"一旦法令通過，它可以創造權利、責任或懲罰。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formal law-making.","zh":"這個短語描述正式立法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"legally binding","meaning":"具法律約束力的","examples":[{"en":"Statutory instruments create legally binding obligations.","zh":"法定文書創造具法律約束力的義務。"},{"en":"Legally binding means enforceable by law, so people must obey it.","zh":"legally binding 指可由法律執行，所以人們必須遵守。"},{"en":"A signed rental contract is legally binding if it meets legal requirements.","zh":"如果符合法律要求，已簽署租約就是具法律約束力的。"},{"en":"If an agreement is legally binding, ignoring it may lead to penalties or court action.","zh":"如果協議具法律約束力，忽視它可能導致懲罰或法律行動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes real legal force.","zh":"這個短語描述真正法律效力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"statutory instruments","meaning":"法定文書；附屬法例","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of statutory instruments supplement Acts of Parliament.","zh":"數以千計的法定文書補充國會法令。"},{"en":"Statutory instruments are detailed legal rules made under powers given by an Act of Parliament.","zh":"statutory instruments 是根據國會法令授權制定的詳細法律規則。"},{"en":"A main law may allow ministers to create statutory instruments about technical details.","zh":"主要法律可能容許部長制定關於技術細節的法定文書。"},{"en":"These instruments can add many practical rules to a legal system.","zh":"這些文書可以為法律制度加入許多實際規則。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to secondary or delegated legislation.","zh":"這個短語指次級或授權立法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in a system with so much law","meaning":"在法律如此繁多的制度中","examples":[{"en":"Lawyers play an essential role in a system with so much law.","zh":"在法律如此繁多的制度中，律師扮演必要角色。"},{"en":"In a system with so much law means in a society where there are many legal rules to understand.","zh":"in a system with so much law 指在有許多法律規則需要理解的社會中。"},{"en":"Small businesses may need advice in a system with so much law about tax and employment.","zh":"在關於稅務和僱傭的法律如此繁多的制度中，小企業可能需要建議。"},{"en":"More rules can make expert help more necessary.","zh":"更多規則可以令專家協助更有必要。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why legal professionals become important.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何法律專業人士變得重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"do a great deal to","meaning":"為……作出很大貢獻","examples":[{"en":"Lawyers do a great deal to protect the rights of citizens.","zh":"律師為保護公民權利作出很大貢獻。"},{"en":"To do a great deal to do something means to contribute a lot toward that result.","zh":"do a great deal to do something 指為達到某結果作出很多貢獻。"},{"en":"Good public transport can do a great deal to reduce traffic in a city.","zh":"良好公共交通可以為減少城市交通作出很大貢獻。"},{"en":"A strong support system can do a great deal to help students stay in school.","zh":"強大支援系統可以大大幫助學生留在學校。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a large positive contribution.","zh":"這個短語顯示很大的正面貢獻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"vindicate the rights of","meaning":"維護……的權利","examples":[{"en":"Lawyers help vindicate the rights of citizens and organisations.","zh":"律師幫助維護公民和組織的權利。"},{"en":"To vindicate the rights of someone means to defend, prove or enforce those rights.","zh":"vindicate the rights of 某人，指捍衛、證明或執行那些權利。"},{"en":"A lawyer may vindicate a tenant’s rights when a landlord keeps a deposit unfairly.","zh":"當業主不公平扣起按金，律師可以維護租客權利。"},{"en":"Rights matter only if people can actually enforce them.","zh":"權利只有在人們能實際執行時才有意義。"},{"en":"The phrase describes turning rights into real protection.","zh":"這個短語描述把權利變成真正保護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"citizens and organisations","meaning":"公民與組織","examples":[{"en":"Legal rights belong to both citizens and organisations.","zh":"法律權利屬於公民與組織。"},{"en":"Citizens and organisations means individual members of society and groups such as companies, charities or schools.","zh":"citizens and organisations 指社會中的個人，以及公司、慈善機構或學校等團體。"},{"en":"A citizen may sue for unfair treatment, while an organisation may defend its contract rights.","zh":"公民可以因不公平對待而起訴，而組織可以維護其合約權利。"},{"en":"Law protects both people and institutions because both take part in social life.","zh":"法律保護人和機構，因為兩者都參與社會生活。"},{"en":"The phrase covers individuals and formal groups.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋個人和正式團體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"develop the law","meaning":"推動法律發展","examples":[{"en":"Lawyers help develop the law through arguments presented in court.","zh":"律師透過在法庭提出論據幫助推動法律發展。"},{"en":"To develop the law means to help legal rules grow, change or become clearer.","zh":"develop the law 指幫助法律規則成長、改變或變得更清晰。"},{"en":"A court case about online privacy may develop the law for new technology.","zh":"關於網上私隱的法庭案件可能為新科技推動法律發展。"},{"en":"Law develops when new problems require old rules to be reinterpreted.","zh":"當新問題需要重新解讀舊規則，法律就會發展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes legal growth over time.","zh":"這個短語描述法律隨時間成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"legal arguments","meaning":"法律論據","examples":[{"en":"Judges consider legal arguments made by lawyers.","zh":"法官考慮律師提出的法律論據。"},{"en":"Legal arguments are reasoned claims about how the law should be understood or applied.","zh":"legal arguments 是關於法律應如何理解或適用的有理據主張。"},{"en":"A lawyer may make legal arguments about why a contract should be enforced.","zh":"律師可能提出法律論據，說明為何合約應被執行。"},{"en":"Strong legal arguments use rules, facts and previous cases.","zh":"強法律論據會使用規則、事實和先例。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to structured reasoning in law.","zh":"這個短語指法律中的結構化推理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be adopted by judges","meaning":"被法官採納","examples":[{"en":"Some arguments are adopted by judges and become part of the law.","zh":"有些論據被法官採納，並成為法律的一部分。"},{"en":"To be adopted by judges means to be accepted and used by judges in their decisions.","zh":"be adopted by judges 指被法官在裁決中接受和使用。"},{"en":"A new interpretation may be adopted by judges if it explains the law more fairly.","zh":"如果新解釋能更公平地說明法律，它可能被法官採納。"},{"en":"Once adopted, an argument can influence later cases.","zh":"一旦被採納，某論據可以影響之後案件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes judicial acceptance.","zh":"這個短語描述司法接受。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"become law","meaning":"成為法律","examples":[{"en":"A judicial principle may eventually become law.","zh":"一項司法原則最終可能成為法律。"},{"en":"To become law means to gain legal force or be accepted as part of the legal system.","zh":"become law 指取得法律效力或被接受為法律制度的一部分。"},{"en":"A rule about data protection may become law after Parliament passes it.","zh":"關於資料保障的規則在國會通過後可能成為法律。"},{"en":"When an idea becomes law, people may have to obey it.","zh":"當一個想法成為法律，人們可能必須遵守它。"},{"en":"The phrase describes movement from idea or proposal to legal rule.","zh":"這個短語描述由想法或建議變成法律規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"law courts","meaning":"法庭","examples":[{"en":"Law courts interpret, apply and sometimes develop legal principles.","zh":"法庭解釋、適用並有時發展法律原則。"},{"en":"Law courts are official places where judges hear cases and make legal decisions.","zh":"law courts 是法官審理案件和作出法律決定的官方地方。"},{"en":"A person may go to a law court to settle a contract dispute.","zh":"一個人可能到法庭解決合約爭議。"},{"en":"Courts help society resolve conflict through rules rather than force.","zh":"法庭幫助社會透過規則而不是武力解決衝突。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the judicial part of the legal system.","zh":"這個短語指法律制度中的司法部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"produce new law","meaning":"制定新法律原則","examples":[{"en":"Courts can produce new law through important judgments.","zh":"法庭可以透過重要判決制定新法律原則。"},{"en":"To produce new law means to create new legal principles or rules.","zh":"produce new law 指創造新的法律原則或規則。"},{"en":"A privacy case may produce new law about how companies use personal data.","zh":"一宗私隱案件可能制定關於公司如何使用個人資料的新法律。"},{"en":"New law may be needed when technology creates problems older rules did not imagine.","zh":"當科技造成舊規則未曾想像的問題，可能需要新法律。"},{"en":"The phrase describes law being created through decisions or legislation.","zh":"這個短語描述透過裁決或立法創造法律。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"revise old law","meaning":"修訂舊有法律","examples":[{"en":"Courts may revise old law when circumstances change.","zh":"當情況改變，法庭可能修訂舊有法律。"},{"en":"To revise old law means to update, correct or reinterpret existing legal rules.","zh":"revise old law 指更新、修正或重新解讀現有法律規則。"},{"en":"A court may revise old rules about communication when disputes involve emails and messages.","zh":"當爭議涉及電郵和訊息，法庭可能修訂關於溝通的舊規則。"},{"en":"Revision helps law remain useful when society changes.","zh":"修訂幫助法律在社會改變時仍然有用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes adapting existing law rather than creating everything from nothing.","zh":"這個短語描述調整現有法律，而不是從零開始創造一切。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"having heard the arguments of","meaning":"在聽取……的論據後","examples":[{"en":"Judges reach decisions having heard the arguments of lawyers.","zh":"法官在聽取律師的論據後作出裁決。"},{"en":"Having heard the arguments of someone means after listening to that person’s reasons.","zh":"having heard the arguments of 某人，指在聽取該人的理由之後。"},{"en":"A principal may decide a school dispute having heard the arguments of both students.","zh":"校長可能在聽取兩名學生的論據後決定學校爭議。"},{"en":"Listening to arguments first helps decision-makers act more fairly.","zh":"先聽取論據幫助決策者更公平行事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a decision made after hearing different sides.","zh":"這個短語描述在聽取不同方面後作出的決定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"despite their important role","meaning":"儘管他們角色重要","examples":[{"en":"Despite their important role, lawyers are not universally admired.","zh":"儘管律師角色重要，他們並非普遍受人敬重。"},{"en":"Despite their important role means although they do something significant.","zh":"despite their important role 指雖然他們做着重要事情。"},{"en":"Despite their important role in schools, cleaners are sometimes overlooked.","zh":"儘管清潔工在學校角色重要，他們有時被忽視。"},{"en":"Important work does not always lead to public praise.","zh":"重要工作不一定帶來公眾讚賞。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces contrast between value and reputation.","zh":"這個短語引出價值與聲譽之間的對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"develop the rules","meaning":"制定和發展規則","examples":[{"en":"Lawyers contribute to developing the rules that govern society.","zh":"律師有份制定和發展規管社會的規則。"},{"en":"To develop the rules means to help create, refine or improve the rules over time.","zh":"develop the rules 指隨時間幫助創造、完善或改善規則。"},{"en":"Teachers develop classroom rules after seeing what helps students learn safely.","zh":"老師在看到甚麼能幫助學生安全學習後，會發展課室規則。"},{"en":"Rules develop when people discover gaps, unfairness or new situations.","zh":"當人們發現漏洞、不公平或新情況，規則就會發展。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improvement and growth of rules.","zh":"這個短語描述規則的改善和成長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not universally admired","meaning":"並非普遍受人敬重","examples":[{"en":"Lawyers are respected by some people but are not universally admired.","zh":"律師受一些人尊重，但並非普遍受人敬重。"},{"en":"Not universally admired means not liked or respected by everyone.","zh":"not universally admired 指並非受到所有人喜歡或尊敬。"},{"en":"A strict headteacher may improve a school but still not be universally admired.","zh":"嚴格校長可能改善學校，但仍並非普遍受人敬重。"},{"en":"Public opinion can be mixed when a profession is powerful or misunderstood.","zh":"當某專業有權力或被誤解，公眾意見可能有分歧。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limited or divided admiration.","zh":"這個短語描述有限或分裂的敬佩。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"anti-lawyer jokes","meaning":"嘲諷律師的笑話","examples":[{"en":"Anti-lawyer jokes have existed for centuries.","zh":"嘲諷律師的笑話已存在數百年。"},{"en":"Anti-lawyer jokes are jokes that mock lawyers or present them negatively.","zh":"anti-lawyer jokes 是嘲弄律師或負面呈現律師的笑話。"},{"en":"People may tell anti-lawyer jokes when they think lawyers are expensive or argumentative.","zh":"當人們認為律師昂貴或好爭辯，可能講嘲諷律師的笑話。"},{"en":"Such jokes can reflect public suspicion of a profession.","zh":"這類笑話可以反映公眾對某專業的懷疑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes humour based on criticism of lawyers.","zh":"這個短語描述以批評律師為基礎的幽默。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have a long history","meaning":"歷史悠久","examples":[{"en":"Negative attitudes towards lawyers have a long history.","zh":"對律師的負面態度歷史悠久。"},{"en":"To have a long history means to have existed for a long time.","zh":"have a long history 指已存在很長時間。"},{"en":"Complaints about crowded housing have a long history in many large cities.","zh":"對擠迫住屋的投訴在許多大城市中歷史悠久。"},{"en":"If an attitude has a long history, it may be deeply rooted in culture.","zh":"如果一種態度歷史悠久，它可能深深植根於文化。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a present issue with the past.","zh":"這個短語把當前問題與過去連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"go back to","meaning":"可追溯至","examples":[{"en":"Anti-lawyer jokes go back to the ancient Greeks.","zh":"嘲諷律師的笑話可追溯至古希臘人。"},{"en":"To go back to a time means to have origins in that period.","zh":"go back to 某時期，指起源於該時期。"},{"en":"Some local festivals go back to farming traditions from centuries ago.","zh":"有些本地節日可追溯至數百年前的農耕傳統。"},{"en":"When something goes back far in history, it may be difficult to explain with one modern cause.","zh":"當某事歷史久遠，就可能難以用一個現代原因解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes historical origin.","zh":"這個短語描述歷史起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the ancient Greeks","meaning":"古希臘人","examples":[{"en":"Even the ancient Greeks told jokes about lawyers.","zh":"即使古希臘人也講關於律師的笑話。"},{"en":"The ancient Greeks were people of ancient Greece, whose culture influenced philosophy, politics and law.","zh":"the ancient Greeks 是古希臘的人，其文化影響哲學、政治和法律。"},{"en":"Students often study the ancient Greeks when learning about democracy and theatre.","zh":"學生學民主和戲劇時，常會研究古希臘人。"},{"en":"Mentioning the ancient Greeks shows that an idea or joke is very old.","zh":"提到古希臘人顯示某想法或笑話非常古老。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a historical civilisation.","zh":"這個短語指一個歷史文明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"more recently","meaning":"較近期","examples":[{"en":"More recently, a schoolchild made a joke about his father’s profession.","zh":"較近期，一名學童拿父親的職業開玩笑。"},{"en":"More recently means at a time closer to the present than the earlier example.","zh":"more recently 指比前一個例子更接近現在的時間。"},{"en":"In the past students used paper dictionaries; more recently, they often use phone apps.","zh":"過去學生使用紙本字典；較近期，他們常用手機應用程式。"},{"en":"The phrase helps move a discussion from older history to a newer example.","zh":"這個短語幫助討論由較古老歷史轉向較新例子。"},{"en":"It signals a time contrast.","zh":"它表示時間對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a famous Hollywood actor","meaning":"著名荷里活演員","examples":[{"en":"The story concerns the son of a famous Hollywood actor.","zh":"這個故事關於一位著名荷里活演員的兒子。"},{"en":"A famous Hollywood actor is a well-known film performer associated with the American film industry.","zh":"a famous Hollywood actor 是與美國電影業相關的知名電影演員。"},{"en":"A famous Hollywood actor may be recognised by people who have never met him.","zh":"著名荷里活演員可能被從未見過他的人認出。"},{"en":"Celebrity status can make even a small family story attract attention.","zh":"名人地位可以令一個小家庭故事也吸引注意。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies public fame and film profession.","zh":"這個短語指出公眾名氣和電影職業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"what someone does for a living","meaning":"某人以甚麼維生","examples":[{"en":"The child was asked what his father did for a living.","zh":"那孩子被問到他父親以甚麼維生。"},{"en":"What someone does for a living means what job they do to earn money.","zh":"what someone does for a living 指某人做甚麼工作來賺錢。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students what their parents do for a living during a career lesson.","zh":"老師可能在職業課中問學生父母以甚麼維生。"},{"en":"A person’s work can shape daily routine, income and social identity.","zh":"一個人的工作可以塑造日常生活、收入和社會身份。"},{"en":"The phrase is a natural way to ask about occupation.","zh":"這個短語是詢問職業的自然說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reply that","meaning":"回答說","examples":[{"en":"The child replied that his father sometimes played a lawyer.","zh":"那孩子回答說，他父親有時飾演律師。"},{"en":"To reply that something is true means to answer by giving that statement.","zh":"reply that 某事為真，指以該陳述作答。"},{"en":"A student may reply that she was absent because she was ill.","zh":"學生可能回答說她缺席是因為生病。"},{"en":"Replies give information and can also reveal attitude or humour.","zh":"回答提供資訊，也可以透露態度或幽默。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the content of an answer.","zh":"這個短語引出答案內容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a movie actor","meaning":"電影演員","examples":[{"en":"The boy described his father as a movie actor.","zh":"那男孩把父親描述為電影演員。"},{"en":"A movie actor is someone who performs roles in films.","zh":"movie actor 是在電影中飾演角色的人。"},{"en":"A movie actor may play a doctor in one film and a teacher in another.","zh":"電影演員可能在一部電影中演醫生，在另一部中演老師。"},{"en":"Acting roles can differ from the actor’s real personality or job knowledge.","zh":"演出角色可以與演員真實性格或職業知識不同。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a person’s film profession.","zh":"這個短語描述某人的電影職業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"play the good guy","meaning":"飾演好人","examples":[{"en":"An actor may play the good guy in one film and a villain in another.","zh":"演員可能在一部電影中飾演好人，在另一部中飾演反派。"},{"en":"To play the good guy means to act as the hero or morally positive character.","zh":"play the good guy 指飾演英雄或道德上正面的角色。"},{"en":"A child may enjoy films where a brave police officer plays the good guy.","zh":"孩子可能喜歡勇敢警察飾演好人的電影。"},{"en":"Actors can play good or bad characters without being like them in real life.","zh":"演員可以飾演好人或壞人，而現實中不一定像那些角色。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a role in a story.","zh":"這個短語指故事中的角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for balance","meaning":"為了持平","examples":[{"en":"For balance, the writer also mentions several admired lawyers.","zh":"為了持平，作者也提到幾位受敬重的律師。"},{"en":"For balance means to make an account fairer by including another side.","zh":"for balance 指透過加入另一面令描述更公平。"},{"en":"A teacher may discuss the disadvantages of exams and, for balance, also mention their benefits.","zh":"老師可能討論考試缺點，為了持平，也提到其好處。"},{"en":"Balanced writing helps readers avoid one-sided judgement.","zh":"平衡寫作幫助讀者避免單方面判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a correcting or balancing point.","zh":"這個短語引出修正或平衡觀點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"it is worth remembering that","meaning":"值得記住的是","examples":[{"en":"It is worth remembering that many lawyers have served society courageously.","zh":"值得記住的是，許多律師曾勇敢地服務社會。"},{"en":"It is worth remembering that means this point is important and should not be forgotten.","zh":"it is worth remembering that 指這一點重要，不應被忘記。"},{"en":"It is worth remembering that quiet students may understand more than they say.","zh":"值得記住的是，安靜學生可能比他們說出來的理解更多。"},{"en":"The phrase helps add a reminder that corrects a simple or negative view.","zh":"這個短語幫助加入提醒，以修正簡單或負面看法。"},{"en":"It introduces an important balancing thought.","zh":"它引出重要的平衡想法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"heroic and revered","meaning":"英勇且備受尊敬的","examples":[{"en":"Some lawyers have become heroic and revered public figures.","zh":"有些律師已成為英勇且備受尊敬的公眾人物。"},{"en":"Heroic and revered means admired for courage, service or moral strength.","zh":"heroic and revered 指因勇氣、服務或道德力量而受敬佩。"},{"en":"A nurse who saves patients during a disaster may become heroic and revered in the community.","zh":"在災難中拯救病人的護士，可能在社區中變得英勇且備受尊敬。"},{"en":"People become revered when their actions show sacrifice and principle.","zh":"當人的行動顯示犧牲和原則，他們會備受尊敬。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep public respect.","zh":"這個短語描述深厚公眾敬意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Roman philosopher and politician","meaning":"羅馬哲學家兼政治家","examples":[{"en":"Cicero was a Roman philosopher and politician.","zh":"西塞羅是羅馬哲學家兼政治家。"},{"en":"A Roman philosopher and politician was someone in ancient Rome involved in ideas and public government.","zh":"Roman philosopher and politician 是古羅馬中參與思想和公共治理的人。"},{"en":"A person can be both a thinker and a political leader if they write ideas and take public office.","zh":"如果一個人寫思想作品並擔任公職，他可以既是思想家也是政治領袖。"},{"en":"Such figures can influence law, public speech and political values.","zh":"這類人物可以影響法律、公共演說和政治價值。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies both intellectual and political roles.","zh":"這個短語同時指出思想和政治角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"campaigner for independence","meaning":"爭取獨立的運動人士","examples":[{"en":"Mahatma Gandhi was a leading campaigner for Indian independence.","zh":"甘地是爭取印度獨立的主要運動人士。"},{"en":"A campaigner for independence is someone who works to make a country or group politically free.","zh":"campaigner for independence 是致力令國家或群體在政治上自由的人。"},{"en":"A student campaigner may organise talks and petitions for a public cause.","zh":"學生運動人士可能為公共議題組織講座和請願。"},{"en":"Campaigners try to change public opinion, laws or political power.","zh":"運動人士嘗試改變公眾意見、法律或政治權力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes active work for freedom from outside control.","zh":"這個短語描述積極爭取脫離外來控制的自由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"characterise someone as","meaning":"把某人形容為","examples":[{"en":"Some comments characterise lawyers as selfish professionals.","zh":"有些評論把律師形容為自私的專業人士。"},{"en":"To characterise someone as something means to describe them as having that quality.","zh":"characterise someone as 某類人，指把他們描述為具有該特質。"},{"en":"A newspaper may characterise a mayor as decisive after quick action during a crisis.","zh":"報章可能在市長危機中迅速行動後，把他形容為果斷。"},{"en":"How people are characterised can shape public opinion about them.","zh":"人們被如何描述，可以塑造公眾對他們的看法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes labelling or portraying someone.","zh":"這個短語描述為某人貼標籤或塑造形象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"put personal reward above truth","meaning":"把個人利益置於真相之上","examples":[{"en":"Critics accuse some lawyers of putting personal reward above truth.","zh":"批評者指控一些律師把個人利益置於真相之上。"},{"en":"To put personal reward above truth means to care more about money or benefit than honesty.","zh":"put personal reward above truth 指比起誠實更重視金錢或利益。"},{"en":"A salesperson puts personal reward above truth if he lies to earn a commission.","zh":"如果銷售員為賺佣金而說謊，就是把個人利益置於真相之上。"},{"en":"When reward becomes more important than truth, trust is damaged.","zh":"當利益比真相更重要，信任就會受損。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises selfish and dishonest priorities.","zh":"這個短語批評自私和不誠實的優先次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"gain financially from","meaning":"從……中獲取金錢利益","examples":[{"en":"Some people claim that lawyers gain financially from others’ misfortune.","zh":"有些人聲稱律師從他人的不幸中獲取金錢利益。"},{"en":"To gain financially from something means to make money because of it.","zh":"gain financially from 某事，指因它而賺錢。"},{"en":"A repair company may gain financially from storms because more roofs need fixing.","zh":"維修公司可能從風暴中獲取金錢利益，因為更多屋頂需要修理。"},{"en":"Gaining financially from trouble can seem unfair if the service feels exploitative.","zh":"如果服務感覺像剝削，從困境中獲利可能顯得不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on money earned from a situation.","zh":"這個短語重點在從某情況中賺到的錢。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"misfortune","meaning":"不幸；厄運","examples":[{"en":"Lawyers are sometimes unfairly associated with other people’s misfortune.","zh":"律師有時被不公平地與他人的不幸聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Misfortune means bad luck, suffering or an unfortunate event.","zh":"misfortune 指壞運氣、痛苦或不幸事件。"},{"en":"Losing a job, having an accident or facing illness can all be forms of misfortune.","zh":"失業、遇上意外或患病都可以是不幸。"},{"en":"People may need professional help when misfortune creates legal or financial problems.","zh":"當不幸造成法律或財務問題，人們可能需要專業協助。"},{"en":"The word describes hardship rather than deliberate wrongdoing.","zh":"這個字描述困境，而不是故意犯錯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"undoubtedly","meaning":"毫無疑問","examples":[{"en":"There are undoubtedly some lawyers who behave unethically.","zh":"毫無疑問，有些律師行為不合道德。"},{"en":"Undoubtedly means certainly or without serious doubt.","zh":"undoubtedly 指肯定地或沒有嚴重疑問地。"},{"en":"There are undoubtedly students who learn better with pictures than with long explanations.","zh":"毫無疑問，有些學生用圖片比用長解釋學得更好。"},{"en":"The word signals strong confidence in a statement.","zh":"這個字表示對陳述有強烈信心。"},{"en":"It is often used before admitting a point fairly.","zh":"它常用於公平承認某一點之前。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fit that description","meaning":"符合那種描述","examples":[{"en":"A small number of professionals may fit that description.","zh":"少數專業人士可能符合那種描述。"},{"en":"To fit that description means to match the qualities or behaviour just described.","zh":"fit that description 指符合剛描述的特質或行為。"},{"en":"If someone is always late and careless, they may fit the description of an unreliable worker.","zh":"如果某人總是遲到又粗心，他可能符合不可靠員工的描述。"},{"en":"A description should not be applied to everyone if only a few people match it.","zh":"如果只有少數人符合描述，就不應把描述套用到所有人身上。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a person with a stated label.","zh":"這個短語把某人與一個既定標籤連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"just as there are","meaning":"正如也有……","examples":[{"en":"There are dishonest lawyers, just as there are dishonest people in other professions.","zh":"有不誠實的律師，正如其他專業中也有不誠實的人。"},{"en":"Just as there are means in the same way that such examples exist elsewhere.","zh":"just as there are 指正如其他地方也存在這類例子。"},{"en":"There are careless drivers, just as there are careful drivers on the same road.","zh":"有粗心司機，正如同一條路上也有謹慎司機。"},{"en":"The phrase helps make a comparison fairer by showing the problem is not unique.","zh":"這個短語透過顯示問題並非某群體獨有，令比較更公平。"},{"en":"It is used to avoid unfairly blaming one group only.","zh":"它用來避免不公平地只責怪一個群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in that category","meaning":"屬於那一類","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists and journalists may also fall into that category.","zh":"有些科學家和記者也可能屬於那一類。"},{"en":"In that category means belonging to the group or type just described.","zh":"in that category 指屬於剛描述的群體或類型。"},{"en":"If a student often helps others without being asked, she belongs in the category of helpful classmates.","zh":"如果學生常主動幫助他人，她就屬於樂於助人同學那一類。"},{"en":"Categories help organise examples, but they should be used carefully.","zh":"分類幫助組織例子，但應小心使用。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to classification.","zh":"這個短語指分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in general","meaning":"一般而言","examples":[{"en":"In general, it is unfair to condemn an entire profession.","zh":"一般而言，譴責整個專業是不公平的。"},{"en":"In general means usually or as a broad rule, though exceptions may exist.","zh":"in general 指通常或作為大體規則，雖然可能有例外。"},{"en":"In general, students improve faster when they receive clear feedback.","zh":"一般而言，學生收到清楚回饋時進步較快。"},{"en":"The phrase allows a writer to make a broad point without claiming it is always true.","zh":"這個短語讓寫作者提出廣泛觀點，而不聲稱永遠如此。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing patterns rather than every single case.","zh":"當討論模式而不是每個個案時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"no more just to say that…than…","meaning":"說……並不比說……更公平","examples":[{"en":"It is no more just to condemn lawyers than to condemn nurses for dealing with illness.","zh":"譴責律師並不比因護士處理疾病而譴責護士更公平。"},{"en":"No more just to say that A than B means A is not fair for the same reason B is not fair.","zh":"no more just to say that A than B 指 A 並不公平，原因與 B 不公平相同。"},{"en":"It is no more fair to blame teachers for exams than to blame doctors for illness.","zh":"責怪老師有考試，並不比責怪醫生有疾病更公平。"},{"en":"This structure compares two accusations and shows both are unfair.","zh":"這個結構比較兩個指控，並顯示兩者都不公平。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful for rejecting an unfair argument by analogy.","zh":"這個短語適合用類比反駁不公平論點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make a living from","meaning":"靠……維生","examples":[{"en":"Professionals make a living from providing specialised services.","zh":"專業人士靠提供專門服務維生。"},{"en":"To make a living from something means to earn money by doing it.","zh":"make a living from 某事，指靠做該事賺取收入。"},{"en":"A tutor makes a living from teaching students after school.","zh":"導師靠課後教學生維生。"},{"en":"People may earn money from solving problems without causing those problems.","zh":"人們可以靠解決問題賺錢，而不代表他們造成那些問題。"},{"en":"The phrase describes earning income through work.","zh":"這個短語描述透過工作賺取收入。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make the same accusation","meaning":"作出同樣指控","examples":[{"en":"It would be unfair to make the same accusation against nurses.","zh":"對護士作出同樣指控是不公平的。"},{"en":"To make the same accusation means to blame another person or group in the same way.","zh":"make the same accusation 指以相同方式責怪另一人或群體。"},{"en":"If we accuse drivers of causing traffic, we might make the same accusation against bus passengers unfairly.","zh":"如果我們指控司機造成交通，也可能不公平地對巴士乘客作出同樣指控。"},{"en":"Repeating an unfair accusation does not make it more reasonable.","zh":"重複不公平指控不會令它更合理。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to applying the same blame elsewhere.","zh":"這個短語指把同一責備套用到別處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in respect of","meaning":"關於；就……而言","examples":[{"en":"The same argument could be made in respect of many professions.","zh":"就許多專業而言，同樣論點也可以成立。"},{"en":"In respect of means regarding or concerning something.","zh":"in respect of 指關於或就某事而言。"},{"en":"A school may set different rules in respect of homework and attendance.","zh":"學校可能就功課和出席率訂立不同規則。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and often appears in law or official writing.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常見於法律或官方寫作。"},{"en":"It helps specify the topic being discussed.","zh":"它幫助指出正在討論的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"IT consultants","meaning":"資訊科技顧問","examples":[{"en":"IT consultants earn money by solving clients’ technical problems.","zh":"資訊科技顧問靠解決客戶技術問題賺錢。"},{"en":"IT consultants are specialists who advise people or organisations about computer and technology systems.","zh":"IT consultants 是為個人或機構提供電腦和科技系統建議的專家。"},{"en":"A small business may hire IT consultants to set up secure email and data backup.","zh":"小企業可能聘請資訊科技顧問設立安全電郵和資料備份。"},{"en":"When systems fail, consultants can help reduce delays and losses.","zh":"當系統故障，顧問可以幫助減少延誤和損失。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to technology advisers.","zh":"這個短語指科技顧問。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be involved in","meaning":"參與","examples":[{"en":"Many lawyers are involved in public law work.","zh":"許多律師參與公法工作。"},{"en":"To be involved in something means to take part in it or have a role in it.","zh":"be involved in 某事，指參與其中或在其中有角色。"},{"en":"Parents may be involved in school events by helping with food or supervision.","zh":"家長可以透過幫忙食物或監督來參與學校活動。"},{"en":"Being involved often brings responsibility and influence.","zh":"參與通常帶來責任和影響力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes participation.","zh":"這個短語描述參與。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"public law work","meaning":"公法工作","examples":[{"en":"Public law work often concerns the relationship between citizens and the state.","zh":"公法工作常涉及公民與國家之間的關係。"},{"en":"Public law work is legal work about government power, public bodies and citizens’ rights.","zh":"public law work 是關於政府權力、公共機構和公民權利的法律工作。"},{"en":"A lawyer doing public law work may challenge an unfair decision by a government department.","zh":"從事公法工作的律師可能挑戰政府部門的不公平決定。"},{"en":"This work can protect people when public authorities act wrongly.","zh":"當公共機關行事不當，這項工作可以保護人們。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to law involving the public sector and individual rights.","zh":"這個短語指涉及公共部門和個人權利的法律。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"civil liberties","meaning":"公民自由","examples":[{"en":"Some lawyers specialise in protecting civil liberties.","zh":"有些律師專門保護公民自由。"},{"en":"Civil liberties are basic freedoms such as free speech, privacy and freedom from unfair detention.","zh":"civil liberties 是言論自由、私隱和免受不公平拘留等基本自由。"},{"en":"A journalist may rely on civil liberties when reporting on public problems.","zh":"記者報道公共問題時，可能依靠公民自由。"},{"en":"If civil liberties are weak, citizens may be afraid to speak or protest.","zh":"如果公民自由薄弱，公民可能害怕發言或抗議。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to freedoms that protect individuals from excessive power.","zh":"這個短語指保護個人免受過度權力影響的自由。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"housing issues","meaning":"房屋問題","examples":[{"en":"Legal aid lawyers often deal with housing issues.","zh":"法律援助律師常處理房屋問題。"},{"en":"Housing issues are problems related to homes, rent, safety, eviction or living conditions.","zh":"housing issues 是與住所、租金、安全、迫遷或居住條件有關的問題。"},{"en":"A tenant facing a leaking ceiling and ignored complaints may have housing issues.","zh":"面對天花漏水且投訴被忽視的租客，可能有房屋問題。"},{"en":"Housing problems can affect health, school performance and family stability.","zh":"房屋問題可以影響健康、學業表現和家庭穩定。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to legal or social problems about where people live.","zh":"這個短語指關於人們居住地方的法律或社會問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be lavishly remunerated","meaning":"獲得優厚報酬","examples":[{"en":"Public-interest legal work is rarely lavishly remunerated.","zh":"公益法律工作很少獲得優厚報酬。"},{"en":"To be lavishly remunerated means to be paid very generously.","zh":"be lavishly remunerated 指獲得非常豐厚的報酬。"},{"en":"A charity worker may do important work but not be lavishly remunerated.","zh":"慈善工作者可能做重要工作，但不會獲得優厚報酬。"},{"en":"Some valuable jobs are poorly paid because they serve public needs rather than rich clients.","zh":"有些有價值的工作薪酬低，因為它們服務公共需要而不是富裕客戶。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on high payment.","zh":"這個短語重點在高報酬。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the quality of the service","meaning":"服務質素","examples":[{"en":"The quality of the service depends on the lawyer’s skill and commitment.","zh":"服務質素取決於律師的技能和投入。"},{"en":"The quality of the service means how good, reliable and useful the service is.","zh":"the quality of the service 指服務有多好、可靠和有用。"},{"en":"In a restaurant, the quality of the service includes speed, politeness and accuracy.","zh":"在餐廳中，服務質素包括速度、禮貌和準確度。"},{"en":"Good service quality can build trust, while poor quality creates complaints.","zh":"良好服務質素可以建立信任，而差劣質素會造成投訴。"},{"en":"The phrase evaluates how well a service is provided.","zh":"這個短語評估服務提供得有多好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rely on","meaning":"依賴","examples":[{"en":"The service provided by these lawyers relies on professional dedication.","zh":"這些律師提供的服務依賴專業投入。"},{"en":"To rely on something means to depend on it in order to work or succeed.","zh":"rely on 某事，指依靠它才能運作或成功。"},{"en":"A school relies on teachers arriving prepared for every lesson.","zh":"學校依賴老師每堂課都有準備。"},{"en":"If a system relies on one person too much, it may fail when that person is absent.","zh":"如果一個系統太依賴一個人，當那人缺席時就可能失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dependence.","zh":"這個短語描述依靠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"considerable professional dedication","meaning":"相當大的專業投入","examples":[{"en":"Public law work often requires considerable professional dedication.","zh":"公法工作常需要相當大的專業投入。"},{"en":"Considerable professional dedication means a high level of commitment to one’s work and professional values.","zh":"considerable professional dedication 指對工作和專業價值有高度投入。"},{"en":"A social worker shows professional dedication by helping families even when cases are difficult.","zh":"社工即使個案困難仍幫助家庭，就是展現專業投入。"},{"en":"Demanding public-interest work may require time, patience and moral commitment.","zh":"要求高的公益工作可能需要時間、耐性和道德承擔。"},{"en":"The phrase describes serious commitment, not casual effort.","zh":"這個短語描述認真投入，而不是隨便努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have nothing to do with","meaning":"與……毫無關係","examples":[{"en":"Much legal work has nothing to do with conflict or misfortune.","zh":"許多法律工作與衝突或不幸毫無關係。"},{"en":"To have nothing to do with something means to be unrelated to it.","zh":"have nothing to do with 某事，指與它無關。"},{"en":"A student’s poor handwriting may have nothing to do with intelligence.","zh":"學生字體差可能與智力毫無關係。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate a false connection from the real situation.","zh":"這個短語幫助把錯誤連繫與真實情況分開。"},{"en":"It is useful when correcting a mistaken assumption.","zh":"它適合用來修正錯誤假設。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be primarily concerned with","meaning":"主要涉及","examples":[{"en":"Many lawyers are primarily concerned with preparing legal paperwork.","zh":"許多律師主要涉及準備法律文件。"},{"en":"To be primarily concerned with something means to focus mainly on it.","zh":"be primarily concerned with 某事，指主要集中於它。"},{"en":"A school nurse is primarily concerned with student health and safety.","zh":"學校護士主要關注學生健康和安全。"},{"en":"The main focus of a job may be different from what outsiders imagine.","zh":"一份工作的主要焦點可能與外人想像不同。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the chief area of attention.","zh":"這個短語指出主要關注範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"draft documents","meaning":"草擬文件","examples":[{"en":"A large amount of legal work involves drafting documents.","zh":"大量法律工作涉及草擬文件。"},{"en":"To draft documents means to write formal papers, usually before they are finalised.","zh":"draft documents 指撰寫正式文件，通常是在定稿之前。"},{"en":"A lawyer may draft documents for a business sale or rental agreement.","zh":"律師可能為企業出售或租約草擬文件。"},{"en":"Careful drafting prevents confusion because rights and duties are written clearly.","zh":"仔細草擬可以避免混亂，因為權利和責任被清楚寫下。"},{"en":"The phrase describes formal document preparation.","zh":"這個短語描述正式文件準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a source of social disaffection","meaning":"社會不滿的來源","examples":[{"en":"Limited legal understanding is a source of social disaffection.","zh":"有限的法律理解是社會不滿的來源。"},{"en":"A source of social disaffection is something that causes people to feel alienated, dissatisfied or distrustful of society.","zh":"a source of social disaffection 是令人們對社會感到疏離、不滿或不信任的事物。"},{"en":"Unclear school rules can become a source of student disaffection if punishments seem unfair.","zh":"如果懲罰看似不公平，不清楚校規可以成為學生不滿的來源。"},{"en":"When people do not understand a system, they may feel excluded or angry.","zh":"當人們不了解一個制度，他們可能感到被排除或憤怒。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a cause of public dissatisfaction.","zh":"這個短語指出公眾不滿的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"public understanding of","meaning":"公眾對……的理解","examples":[{"en":"Public understanding of how law works is often limited.","zh":"公眾對法律如何運作的理解通常有限。"},{"en":"Public understanding of something means what ordinary people know or believe about it.","zh":"public understanding of 某事，指普通人對它知道或相信的內容。"},{"en":"Public understanding of mental health has improved as schools discuss it more openly.","zh":"隨着學校更公開討論心理健康，公眾對心理健康的理解已有改善。"},{"en":"Better public understanding can reduce fear, rumours and unfair judgement.","zh":"更好的公眾理解可以減少恐懼、謠言和不公平判斷。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on what society generally understands.","zh":"這個短語重點在社會一般理解甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"how law works","meaning":"法律如何運作","examples":[{"en":"Many people have only a vague idea of how law works.","zh":"許多人對法律如何運作只有模糊概念。"},{"en":"How law works means how legal rules are made, interpreted, enforced and changed.","zh":"how law works 指法律規則如何制定、解釋、執行和修改。"},{"en":"Students learn how law works when they study courts, rights and Parliament.","zh":"學生學習法庭、權利和國會時，就在了解法律如何運作。"},{"en":"If people understand how law works, they can use their rights more effectively.","zh":"如果人們理解法律如何運作，就能更有效使用自己的權利。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the operation of the legal system.","zh":"這個短語指法律制度的運作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"how it could be changed","meaning":"法律可如何修改","examples":[{"en":"Citizens may not know how the law could be changed.","zh":"公民可能不知道法律可如何修改。"},{"en":"How it could be changed means the ways a rule or system might be altered.","zh":"how it could be changed 指一條規則或制度可能如何被改變。"},{"en":"Students may complain about a school rule without knowing how it could be changed.","zh":"學生可能投訴校規，卻不知道它可如何修改。"},{"en":"Understanding change processes helps people move from anger to action.","zh":"理解修改程序幫助人由憤怒走向行動。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on possible routes to reform.","zh":"這個短語重點在改革的可能途徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"greater clarity about","meaning":"對……有更清晰的了解","examples":[{"en":"Greater clarity about legal processes could improve public confidence.","zh":"對法律程序有更清晰的了解，可以改善公眾信心。"},{"en":"Greater clarity about something means a clearer understanding of it.","zh":"greater clarity about 某事，指對它有更清楚理解。"},{"en":"Greater clarity about exam marking can reduce student anxiety.","zh":"對考試評分有更清晰了解，可以減少學生焦慮。"},{"en":"When processes are clearer, people are less likely to feel cheated or confused.","zh":"當程序更清楚，人們較少感到被欺騙或困惑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes improved understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述理解改善。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as a result of","meaning":"由於；作為……的結果","examples":[{"en":"Public understanding may improve as a result of better communication.","zh":"由於更好的溝通，公眾理解可能改善。"},{"en":"As a result of means because of something that caused a particular outcome.","zh":"as a result of 指因為某事而產生某結果。"},{"en":"Students may feel calmer as a result of clear exam instructions.","zh":"由於清楚考試指示，學生可能感到較平靜。"},{"en":"The phrase links a cause with its effect.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful for explaining why a change happened.","zh":"它適合用來解釋變化為何發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"public relations","meaning":"公共關係","examples":[{"en":"Better public relations could improve attitudes towards the legal profession.","zh":"更好的公共關係可以改善人們對法律專業的態度。"},{"en":"Public relations means communication used to shape how the public sees an organisation or profession.","zh":"public relations 指用來塑造公眾如何看待機構或專業的溝通。"},{"en":"A hospital uses public relations when it explains new services clearly to patients.","zh":"醫院向病人清楚解釋新服務時，就是在做公共關係。"},{"en":"Poor communication can damage trust even when the work itself is important.","zh":"即使工作本身重要，差劣溝通也可以損害信任。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to managing public understanding and reputation.","zh":"這個短語指管理公眾理解和聲譽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reduce public dissatisfaction","meaning":"減少公眾不滿","examples":[{"en":"Clearer explanations could reduce public dissatisfaction with the law.","zh":"更清楚的解釋可以減少公眾對法律的不滿。"},{"en":"To reduce public dissatisfaction means to lower the level of unhappiness or complaint among the public.","zh":"reduce public dissatisfaction 指降低公眾的不快或投訴程度。"},{"en":"A city can reduce public dissatisfaction by explaining roadworks before they begin.","zh":"城市可以在道路工程開始前作解釋，以減少公眾不滿。"},{"en":"People are less frustrated when they understand why a decision was made.","zh":"當人們理解某決定為何作出，他們較少沮喪。"},{"en":"The phrase describes making the public less unhappy.","zh":"這個短語描述令公眾較少不滿。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"aspects of public dissatisfaction","meaning":"公眾不滿的各個方面","examples":[{"en":"Better communication could address many aspects of public dissatisfaction.","zh":"更好的溝通可以處理公眾不滿的許多方面。"},{"en":"Aspects of public dissatisfaction are different parts or causes of public unhappiness.","zh":"aspects of public dissatisfaction 是公眾不快的不同部分或原因。"},{"en":"Long waiting times and unclear letters can both be aspects of dissatisfaction with public services.","zh":"漫長等候時間和不清楚信件都可以是對公共服務不滿的方面。"},{"en":"Solving only one cause may not remove all dissatisfaction.","zh":"只解決一個原因未必能消除所有不滿。"},{"en":"The phrase breaks public unhappiness into separate issues.","zh":"這個短語把公眾不滿分成不同問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct heading for each paragraph.","zh":"學生為每段選出正確標題。"},{"en":"To choose the correct heading means to select the title that best summarises a paragraph.","zh":"choose the correct heading 指選出最能概括段落的標題。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should identify the main idea before choosing a heading.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應先辨認主旨，再選標題。"},{"en":"A wrong heading may focus on a detail rather than the paragraph’s main point.","zh":"錯誤標題可能集中於細節，而不是段落主旨。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"from the list of headings","meaning":"從標題列表中","examples":[{"en":"Each paragraph must be matched with a heading from the list.","zh":"每段必須與標題列表中的一個標題配對。"},{"en":"From the list of headings means using only the heading options provided.","zh":"from the list of headings 指只使用所提供的標題選項。"},{"en":"Students should not invent their own title if the task says choose from the list.","zh":"如果題目說從列表中選擇，學生不應自創標題。"},{"en":"The list may contain extra headings that do not match any paragraph.","zh":"列表可能包含不配對任何段落的額外標題。"},{"en":"The phrase tells candidates where the answer choices are.","zh":"這個短語告訴考生答案選項在哪裏。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"areas of professional expertise","meaning":"不同的專業範疇","examples":[{"en":"Modern society relies on different areas of professional expertise.","zh":"現代社會依賴不同的專業範疇。"},{"en":"Areas of professional expertise are specialised fields of knowledge and skill.","zh":"areas of professional expertise 是專門知識和技能的領域。"},{"en":"Medicine, engineering, law and IT are all areas of professional expertise.","zh":"醫學、工程、法律和資訊科技都是不同專業範疇。"},{"en":"Complex societies need many experts because one person cannot master every field.","zh":"複雜社會需要許多專家，因為一個人不能精通每個領域。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to different specialised domains.","zh":"這個短語指不同專門領域。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"professional expertise","meaning":"專業知識","examples":[{"en":"Both technical and legal work require professional expertise.","zh":"技術和法律工作都需要專業知識。"},{"en":"Professional expertise is specialised knowledge and skill gained through training and experience.","zh":"professional expertise 是透過訓練和經驗取得的專門知識和技能。"},{"en":"A dentist needs professional expertise to diagnose pain and treat teeth safely.","zh":"牙醫需要專業知識來診斷疼痛並安全治療牙齒。"},{"en":"Without professional expertise, difficult tasks may be done badly or dangerously.","zh":"沒有專業知識，困難任務可能做得差或有危險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes trusted skill in a profession.","zh":"這個短語描述某專業中的可信技能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reasons why it is unfair to criticise","meaning":"批評……並不公平的原因","examples":[{"en":"The final paragraph gives reasons why it is unfair to criticise all lawyers.","zh":"最後一段給出批評所有律師並不公平的原因。"},{"en":"Reasons why it is unfair to criticise someone are explanations showing that blame is unreasonable.","zh":"reasons why it is unfair to criticise 某人，是顯示責備不合理的解釋。"},{"en":"It may be unfair to criticise all students for noise if only two students were talking.","zh":"如果只有兩名學生在說話，批評所有學生吵鬧可能並不公平。"},{"en":"Fair criticism should target real behaviour, not an entire group unfairly.","zh":"公平批評應針對真實行為，而不是不公平地針對整個群體。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a defence against overgeneralisation.","zh":"這個短語引出反對過度概括的辯護。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the disadvantages of","meaning":"……的缺點","examples":[{"en":"One heading refers to the disadvantages of the legal system.","zh":"一個標題提到法律制度的缺點。"},{"en":"The disadvantages of something are its weaknesses, problems or negative effects.","zh":"the disadvantages of 某事，是它的弱點、問題或負面影響。"},{"en":"The disadvantages of online learning may include poor concentration and weak social contact.","zh":"網上學習的缺點可能包括專注力差和社交接觸弱。"},{"en":"Understanding disadvantages helps people improve a system rather than praise it blindly.","zh":"理解缺點幫助人改善制度，而不是盲目讚美。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a critical view.","zh":"這個短語引出批判性看法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"apply throughout our lives","meaning":"貫穿我們一生","examples":[{"en":"The law applies throughout our lives, from before birth until after death.","zh":"法律貫穿我們一生，由出生前直到死後。"},{"en":"To apply throughout our lives means to be relevant at every stage of life.","zh":"apply throughout our lives 指在人生每個階段都相關。"},{"en":"Health, education, work, marriage and inheritance laws apply throughout people’s lives.","zh":"健康、教育、工作、婚姻和繼承法律貫穿人們一生。"},{"en":"Because rules follow people from childhood to old age, basic legal understanding matters.","zh":"因為規則由童年到老年都跟隨人們，基本法律理解很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses lifelong relevance.","zh":"這個短語強調終身相關性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"affect historical events","meaning":"影響歷史事件","examples":[{"en":"Legal ideas have affected many important historical events.","zh":"法律觀念影響了許多重要歷史事件。"},{"en":"To affect historical events means to influence what happened in the past.","zh":"affect historical events 指影響過去發生的事情。"},{"en":"Ideas about rights affected historical events such as campaigns for voting and equality.","zh":"關於權利的想法影響了爭取投票和平等的歷史事件。"},{"en":"Laws can shape history by changing who has power and protection.","zh":"法律可以透過改變誰有權力和保護來塑造歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase connects legal thought with major past changes.","zh":"這個短語把法律思想與重大過去變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"negative regard for","meaning":"對……的負面看法","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the public’s negative regard for lawyers.","zh":"文章討論公眾對律師的負面看法。"},{"en":"Negative regard for someone means an unfavourable opinion or lack of respect toward them.","zh":"negative regard for 某人，指對他們有不利看法或缺乏尊重。"},{"en":"A company may face negative regard from customers after repeated poor service.","zh":"公司在反覆提供差劣服務後，可能面對顧客的負面看法。"},{"en":"Negative regard can grow when people feel a group is selfish or unhelpful.","zh":"當人們覺得某群體自私或無幫助，負面看法可以增加。"},{"en":"The phrase describes public disapproval.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾不認同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"increasing ability to influence","meaning":"日益增強的影響能力","examples":[{"en":"Citizens have an increasing ability to influence the law.","zh":"公民有日益增強的影響法律能力。"},{"en":"Increasing ability to influence means growing power to affect decisions or outcomes.","zh":"increasing ability to influence 指影響決定或結果的能力正在增長。"},{"en":"Students have an increasing ability to influence school rules when councils listen to them.","zh":"當學生會聆聽學生意見，學生就有日益增強的能力影響校規。"},{"en":"More access to information can give people stronger influence in public debate.","zh":"更多資訊取得可以給人們在公共辯論中更強影響力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes growing power, not complete control.","zh":"這個短語描述權力增長，而不是完全控制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"growth in the number of","meaning":"……數量的增長","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes growth in the number of laws.","zh":"文章描述法律數量的增長。"},{"en":"Growth in the number of something means an increase in how many there are.","zh":"growth in the number of 某事，指其數量增加。"},{"en":"Growth in the number of students may require more classrooms and teachers.","zh":"學生數量的增長可能需要更多課室和老師。"},{"en":"When numbers grow, systems often need extra support to handle the increase.","zh":"當數量增長，制度通常需要額外支援來處理增加。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on rising quantity.","zh":"這個短語重點在數量上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"choose two letters","meaning":"選出兩個字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose two letters from the available answer options.","zh":"學生從可用答案選項中選出兩個字母。"},{"en":"Choose two letters means select exactly two answer choices, usually from options A, B, C and so on.","zh":"choose two letters 指準確選出兩個答案選項，通常從 A、B、C 等中選。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students must choose two letters only, not three.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生只能選出兩個字母，而不是三個。"},{"en":"Choosing too many options can make an answer wrong even if one choice is correct.","zh":"選太多選項可能令答案錯，即使其中一個選項正確。"},{"en":"The phrase is a strict exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是嚴格考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the following statements","meaning":"以下陳述","examples":[{"en":"Students decide which of the following statements reflect the passage.","zh":"學生判斷以下陳述哪些反映文章內容。"},{"en":"The following statements means the sentences listed after the instruction.","zh":"the following statements 指指示後列出的句子。"},{"en":"Students should read the following statements before searching for evidence in the text.","zh":"學生應先閱讀以下陳述，再在文本中尋找證據。"},{"en":"Each statement may contain key words that point to a paragraph.","zh":"每句陳述可能包含指向某段落的關鍵字。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a set of sentences to judge or match.","zh":"這個短語引出一組要判斷或配對的句子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"legal skills","meaning":"法律技能","examples":[{"en":"The writer argues that legal skills are essential in today’s world.","zh":"作者認為法律技能在現今世界必不可少。"},{"en":"Legal skills are abilities used to understand, apply, explain or argue about law.","zh":"legal skills 是用來理解、應用、解釋或辯論法律的能力。"},{"en":"Reading a contract carefully is a basic legal skill useful in daily life.","zh":"仔細閱讀合約是一項日常生活中有用的基本法律技能。"},{"en":"Legal skills help people protect rights and avoid serious mistakes.","zh":"法律技能幫助人保護權利並避免嚴重錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical abilities connected with law.","zh":"這個短語指與法律相關的實用能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in today’s world","meaning":"在現今世界","examples":[{"en":"Both technological and legal knowledge are essential in today’s world.","zh":"在現今世界，科技和法律知識都必不可少。"},{"en":"In today’s world means in modern society and current daily life.","zh":"in today’s world 指在現代社會和當前日常生活中。"},{"en":"In today’s world, students need to understand both online safety and communication skills.","zh":"在現今世界，學生需要理解網上安全和溝通技能。"},{"en":"The phrase often introduces a modern need or challenge.","zh":"這個短語常引出現代需要或挑戰。"},{"en":"It contrasts present conditions with the past.","zh":"它把現在條件與過去作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"legal training","meaning":"法律訓練","examples":[{"en":"Legal training equips people to understand and apply complex rules.","zh":"法律訓練裝備人們理解和應用複雜規則。"},{"en":"Legal training is education or practice that teaches people how law works.","zh":"legal training 是教人法律如何運作的教育或實踐。"},{"en":"A trainee lawyer receives legal training by studying cases and drafting documents.","zh":"見習律師透過研究案例和草擬文件接受法律訓練。"},{"en":"Good training helps people interpret rules accurately rather than guess.","zh":"良好訓練幫助人準確解讀規則，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to preparation for legal work or legal understanding.","zh":"這個短語指為法律工作或法律理解作準備。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"commercial law","meaning":"商業法","examples":[{"en":"Commercial law governs transactions between businesses.","zh":"商業法規管企業之間的交易。"},{"en":"Commercial law is the area of law dealing with business, trade, contracts and companies.","zh":"commercial law 是處理商業、貿易、合約和公司的法律範疇。"},{"en":"A shop owner may need commercial law advice before signing a supply agreement.","zh":"店主在簽供貨協議前，可能需要商業法建議。"},{"en":"Clear commercial rules help businesses trade with less risk and confusion.","zh":"清楚商業規則幫助企業以較少風險和混亂交易。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to law for business activity.","zh":"這個短語指商業活動相關法律。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be in demand","meaning":"需求很高","examples":[{"en":"Professionals with specialised legal knowledge may be in demand.","zh":"具專門法律知識的專業人士可能需求很高。"},{"en":"To be in demand means to be wanted or needed by many people or organisations.","zh":"be in demand 指被許多人或機構想要或需要。"},{"en":"Nurses may be in demand when hospitals do not have enough trained staff.","zh":"當醫院沒有足夠受訓員工，護士可能需求很高。"},{"en":"When a skill becomes important, people who have it may find more job opportunities.","zh":"當一項技能變得重要，擁有該技能的人可能找到更多工作機會。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong need in a market or society.","zh":"這個短語描述市場或社會中的強烈需要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be as important as","meaning":"與……同樣重要","examples":[{"en":"Knowledge of the law is as important as computer skills.","zh":"法律知識與電腦技能同樣重要。"},{"en":"To be as important as something means to have equal value or necessity.","zh":"be as important as 某事，指具有相同價值或必要性。"},{"en":"Clear communication is as important as strong exam knowledge in an interview.","zh":"在面試中，清楚溝通與強考試知識同樣重要。"},{"en":"If two skills are equally important, ignoring either one can create problems.","zh":"如果兩種技能同樣重要，忽視任何一種都可以造成問題。"},{"en":"The phrase makes a comparison of equal importance.","zh":"這個短語作出同等重要性的比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"computer skills","meaning":"電腦技能","examples":[{"en":"Modern organisations depend heavily on computer skills.","zh":"現代機構非常依賴電腦技能。"},{"en":"Computer skills are abilities needed to use computers, software and digital systems effectively.","zh":"computer skills 是有效使用電腦、軟件和數碼系統所需的能力。"},{"en":"A receptionist needs computer skills to manage bookings and send emails.","zh":"接待員需要電腦技能來管理預約和發送電郵。"},{"en":"Weak computer skills can slow down work and create mistakes.","zh":"電腦技能薄弱可以拖慢工作並造成錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to practical digital ability.","zh":"這個短語指實用數碼能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"function effectively","meaning":"有效運作","examples":[{"en":"Society could not function effectively without legal experts.","zh":"沒有法律專家，社會不能有效運作。"},{"en":"To function effectively means to work properly and produce useful results.","zh":"function effectively 指正常工作並產生有用結果。"},{"en":"A school cannot function effectively if teachers, cleaners and office staff are all absent.","zh":"如果老師、清潔工和校務處員工都缺席，學校不能有效運作。"},{"en":"Effective functioning requires clear roles, rules and support.","zh":"有效運作需要清楚角色、規則和支援。"},{"en":"The phrase describes working well, not merely existing.","zh":"這個短語描述運作良好，而不只是存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"legal experts","meaning":"法律專家","examples":[{"en":"Legal experts help individuals and organisations interpret the law.","zh":"法律專家幫助個人和組織解讀法律。"},{"en":"Legal experts are people with specialised knowledge of law, such as lawyers or judges.","zh":"legal experts 是有法律專門知識的人，例如律師或法官。"},{"en":"A company may ask legal experts to review a contract before signing it.","zh":"公司可能請法律專家在簽署前審視合約。"},{"en":"Experts help prevent mistakes when rules are difficult or consequences are serious.","zh":"當規則困難或後果嚴重，專家幫助防止錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to specialists in law.","zh":"這個短語指法律方面的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"teach students about","meaning":"教導學生有關……","examples":[{"en":"One option suggests that schools should teach students about the law.","zh":"一個選項建議學校應教導學生有關法律。"},{"en":"To teach students about something means to help them understand that topic through lessons or activities.","zh":"teach students about 某事，指透過課堂或活動幫助學生理解該主題。"},{"en":"Schools teach students about online safety so they know how to protect personal data.","zh":"學校教導學生有關網上安全，讓他們知道如何保護個人資料。"},{"en":"Teaching students about law can help them understand rights and responsibilities.","zh":"教導學生有關法律，可以幫助他們理解權利和責任。"},{"en":"The phrase describes education on a particular subject.","zh":"這個短語描述特定主題的教育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words taken from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill in missing words in a shortened version of the text.","zh":"complete the summary 指在文本的簡短版本中填入缺失字詞。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should check grammar before choosing each word.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生選每個字前應檢查文法。"},{"en":"Summary completion tests both understanding and accurate word choice.","zh":"摘要填空同時測試理解和準確選詞。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"one word only","meaning":"只限一個字詞","examples":[{"en":"Each answer must contain one word only.","zh":"每個答案只限一個字詞。"},{"en":"One word only means the answer must be exactly one word, not two or more.","zh":"one word only 指答案必須剛好是一個詞，而不是兩個或更多。"},{"en":"If the answer is “lawyers,” students should not write “many lawyers.”","zh":"如果答案是 “lawyers”，學生不應寫 “many lawyers”。"},{"en":"Writing extra words can make an answer wrong even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫額外字詞也可能令答案錯。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a strict answer-length rule.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格答案長度規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lawyers as professionals","meaning":"作為專業人士的律師","examples":[{"en":"The summary considers public attitudes towards lawyers as professionals.","zh":"摘要考慮公眾對作為專業人士的律師的態度。"},{"en":"Lawyers as professionals means lawyers viewed as members of a trained occupation with duties and standards.","zh":"lawyers as professionals 指把律師視為有訓練、有責任和標準的職業成員。"},{"en":"People may judge lawyers as professionals by their honesty, skill and service quality.","zh":"人們可能按誠實、技能和服務質素評價作為專業人士的律師。"},{"en":"A profession’s reputation depends on both public perception and actual conduct.","zh":"一個專業的聲譽取決於公眾看法和實際行為。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on lawyers in their professional role.","zh":"這個短語重點在律師的專業角色。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be of little interest to","meaning":"對……不太重要","examples":[{"en":"Critics claim that truth is of little interest to some lawyers.","zh":"批評者聲稱真相對一些律師不太重要。"},{"en":"To be of little interest to someone means to matter very little to that person.","zh":"be of little interest to 某人，指對該人而言幾乎不重要。"},{"en":"A long lecture may be of little interest to children if it has no stories or examples.","zh":"如果長篇講課沒有故事或例子，對孩子可能不太重要。"},{"en":"If truth is of little interest to a professional, trust in that profession suffers.","zh":"如果真相對專業人士不太重要，對該專業的信任會受損。"},{"en":"The phrase describes low importance or concern.","zh":"這個短語描述重要性或關注度低。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be concerned with making money","meaning":"只關心賺錢","examples":[{"en":"Some lawyers are accused of being more concerned with making money.","zh":"有些律師被指更關心賺錢。"},{"en":"To be concerned with making money means to focus mainly on earning income or profit.","zh":"be concerned with making money 指主要集中於賺取收入或利潤。"},{"en":"A tutor concerned only with making money may ignore whether students truly improve.","zh":"只關心賺錢的導師可能忽視學生是否真正進步。"},{"en":"When money becomes the main concern, service quality and ethics may suffer.","zh":"當金錢成為主要關注，服務質素和道德可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises financial focus when it overrides other values.","zh":"這個短語批評金錢焦點凌駕其他價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"may well be the case","meaning":"很可能確是如此","examples":[{"en":"This may well be the case with a small number of individuals.","zh":"對少數個人而言，這很可能確是如此。"},{"en":"May well be the case means something is quite possible or likely true.","zh":"may well be the case 指某事很可能或相當可能是真的。"},{"en":"Some students study better at night; this may well be the case for people who feel more awake then.","zh":"有些學生晚上學得更好；對那時較清醒的人而言，這很可能確是如此。"},{"en":"The phrase admits a point without saying it applies to everyone.","zh":"這個短語承認某一點，但不表示它適用於所有人。"},{"en":"It is useful for balanced argument.","zh":"它適合用於平衡論證。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in the same way that","meaning":"正如……一樣","examples":[{"en":"Some lawyers may be greedy in the same way that some other professionals are.","zh":"有些律師可能貪婪，正如其他一些專業人士一樣。"},{"en":"In the same way that means by a similar pattern or for a similar reason.","zh":"in the same way that 指以相似模式或基於相似原因。"},{"en":"Some students dislike maths in the same way that others dislike writing: they lack confidence.","zh":"有些學生不喜歡數學，正如另一些不喜歡寫作一樣：他們缺乏信心。"},{"en":"The phrase helps compare two situations fairly.","zh":"這個短語幫助公平比較兩種情況。"},{"en":"It shows similarity without saying the situations are identical.","zh":"它顯示相似性，但不是說兩種情況完全相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be driven by financial greed","meaning":"受金錢貪念驅使","examples":[{"en":"Professionals in any field may be driven by financial greed.","zh":"任何領域的專業人士都可能受金錢貪念驅使。"},{"en":"To be driven by financial greed means to be motivated mainly by wanting more money.","zh":"be driven by financial greed 指主要受想賺更多錢的慾望推動。"},{"en":"A company driven by financial greed may cut safety costs to increase profit.","zh":"受金錢貪念驅使的公司可能削減安全成本以增加利潤。"},{"en":"Greed can lead people to ignore fairness, truth or public duty.","zh":"貪念可以令人忽視公平、真相或公共責任。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly criticises a selfish motive.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評自私動機。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"criticise someone because","meaning":"因……而批評某人","examples":[{"en":"It is unfair to criticise lawyers because they deal with people’s problems.","zh":"因律師處理人們的問題而批評他們是不公平的。"},{"en":"To criticise someone because of something means to blame them for that reason.","zh":"criticise someone because of 某事，指因該原因責備某人。"},{"en":"It is unfair to criticise doctors because patients are ill; doctors are trying to help.","zh":"因病人生病而批評醫生是不公平的；醫生是在嘗試幫助。"},{"en":"Criticism should focus on wrongdoing, not on the fact that someone handles difficult cases.","zh":"批評應集中於錯誤行為，而不是某人處理困難個案這一事實。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a reason for blame.","zh":"這個短語引出責備的原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be similar to","meaning":"與……相似","examples":[{"en":"Condemning lawyers for solving problems would be similar to attacking nurses.","zh":"因律師解決問題而譴責他們，會與攻擊護士相似。"},{"en":"To be similar to something means to share important features with it.","zh":"be similar to 某事，指與它有重要相同特徵。"},{"en":"Forgetting homework is similar to missing a deadline at work because both show poor organisation.","zh":"忘記功課與工作中錯過期限相似，因為兩者都顯示組織能力差。"},{"en":"Comparisons help people see whether an argument is fair or unfair.","zh":"比較幫助人看見論點是否公平。"},{"en":"The phrase describes likeness, not exact sameness.","zh":"這個短語描述相似，而不是完全相同。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"for the same reason","meaning":"基於同一原因","examples":[{"en":"It would be unfair to criticise IT staff for the same reason.","zh":"基於同一原因，批評資訊科技員工也會不公平。"},{"en":"For the same reason means because of the same logic or cause just mentioned.","zh":"for the same reason 指基於剛提到的相同邏輯或原因。"},{"en":"If we should not blame doctors for illness, we should not blame nurses for the same reason.","zh":"如果我們不應因疾病而責怪醫生，基於同一原因，我們也不應責怪護士。"},{"en":"The phrase links two examples under one shared argument.","zh":"這個短語把兩個例子連到同一共同論點下。"},{"en":"It helps avoid repeating the full explanation.","zh":"它幫助避免重複完整解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"focus on questions relating to","meaning":"專注於與……有關的問題","examples":[{"en":"Many public lawyers focus on questions relating to housing and civil liberties.","zh":"許多公法律師專注於與房屋和公民自由有關的問題。"},{"en":"To focus on questions relating to something means to concentrate on issues connected with that topic.","zh":"focus on questions relating to 某事，指集中處理與該主題有關的議題。"},{"en":"A school counsellor may focus on questions relating to stress, friendship and family pressure.","zh":"學校輔導員可能專注於與壓力、友誼和家庭壓力有關的問題。"},{"en":"Focus helps professionals use their knowledge where it is most needed.","zh":"專注幫助專業人士把知識用在最需要的地方。"},{"en":"The phrase describes specialised attention to connected issues.","zh":"這個短語描述對相關問題的專門注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"require someone to have","meaning":"要求某人具備","examples":[{"en":"Demanding legal work requires lawyers to have considerable dedication.","zh":"要求高的法律工作要求律師具備相當大的投入。"},{"en":"To require someone to have something means to need that person to possess it.","zh":"require someone to have 某物，指需要該人具備它。"},{"en":"Teaching young children requires teachers to have patience and clear communication.","zh":"教年幼孩子要求老師具備耐性和清楚溝通能力。"},{"en":"Difficult jobs often require people to have both skill and commitment.","zh":"困難工作常要求人們具備技能和承擔。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a necessary quality or condition.","zh":"這個短語描述必要品質或條件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a lot of someone’s time","meaning":"某人大量時間","examples":[{"en":"A lot of a lawyer’s time may be spent preparing documents.","zh":"律師大量時間可能花在準備文件上。"},{"en":"A lot of someone’s time means a large part of that person’s available hours.","zh":"a lot of someone’s time 指某人可用時間中的很大部分。"},{"en":"A student may spend a lot of her time revising before final exams.","zh":"學生在期末考前可能花大量時間溫習。"},{"en":"If one task takes a lot of time, there may be less time for other duties.","zh":"如果一項任務佔用大量時間，其他職責的時間可能較少。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on time cost.","zh":"這個短語重點在時間成本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be spent writing","meaning":"被用於撰寫","examples":[{"en":"Much of a lawyer’s time is spent writing legal documents.","zh":"律師很多時間被用於撰寫法律文件。"},{"en":"To be spent writing means time is used for writing rather than other activities.","zh":"be spent writing 指時間被用於寫作，而不是其他活動。"},{"en":"A student’s Sunday may be spent writing an essay due on Monday.","zh":"學生的星期日可能被用於撰寫星期一到期的文章。"},{"en":"When professional work is spent writing, accuracy and wording become very important.","zh":"當專業工作時間被用於撰寫，準確性和措辭就變得非常重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how time is used.","zh":"這個短語描述時間如何被使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"deal with people’s misfortunes","meaning":"處理人們的不幸","examples":[{"en":"Many legal tasks do not involve dealing with people’s misfortunes.","zh":"許多法律任務並不涉及處理人們的不幸。"},{"en":"To deal with people’s misfortunes means to handle problems caused by their bad luck, suffering or difficult events.","zh":"deal with people’s misfortunes 指處理由壞運氣、痛苦或困難事件造成的問題。"},{"en":"A lawyer may deal with people’s misfortunes when helping after an accident or unfair dismissal.","zh":"律師在意外或不公平解僱後提供幫助時，可能處理人們的不幸。"},{"en":"However, legal work can also involve peaceful tasks like drafting contracts and creating companies.","zh":"然而，法律工作也可以涉及和平任務，例如草擬合約和成立公司。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on helping with hardship, not causing it.","zh":"這個短語重點在幫助處理困境，而不是造成困境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 171 - The importance of law.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 172":[{"front":"Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much?","meaning":"為甚麼我們經常觸碰陌生人？","examples":[{"en":"The article asks why people so often touch strangers when greeting them.","zh":"文章問為甚麼人們在打招呼時如此經常觸碰陌生人。"},{"en":"“Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much?” asks why physical contact is so common in greetings.","zh":"“Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much?” 問的是為甚麼身體接觸在問候中如此常見。"},{"en":"At a business event, people may touch strangers by shaking hands before they even know each other.","zh":"在商業活動中，人們甚至未認識對方前，可能已透過握手觸碰陌生人。"},{"en":"Such contact can build trust quickly, but it can also spread germs.","zh":"這類接觸可以快速建立信任，但也可能傳播細菌。"},{"en":"This title invites readers to question a habit that often feels normal.","zh":"這個標題邀請讀者質疑一個常被視為正常的習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"offer clues","meaning":"提供線索","examples":[{"en":"The history of the handshake offers clues about physical greetings.","zh":"握手的歷史為身體問候提供線索。"},{"en":"To offer clues means to provide hints that help people understand something.","zh":"offer clues 指提供有助人理解某事的提示。"},{"en":"A student’s spelling mistakes may offer clues about which sounds they find confusing.","zh":"學生的串字錯誤可能提供線索，顯示他們覺得哪些音混淆。"},{"en":"Old customs can offer clues about what people valued in the past.","zh":"舊習俗可以提供線索，讓我們了解過去人們重視甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase means the information does not give the full answer, but helps us work it out.","zh":"這個短語表示資料沒有給出完整答案，但幫助我們推斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for thousands of years","meaning":"數千年來","examples":[{"en":"The handshake has been used for different purposes for thousands of years.","zh":"數千年來，握手一直被用於不同目的。"},{"en":"For thousands of years means for a very long period across many generations.","zh":"for thousands of years 指跨越許多世代的非常長時間。"},{"en":"People have told stories to teach children lessons for thousands of years.","zh":"數千年來，人們一直透過故事教孩子道理。"},{"en":"A custom that lasts for thousands of years becomes deeply familiar to many societies.","zh":"一項延續數千年的習俗會變得在許多社會中非常熟悉。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long historical continuity.","zh":"這個短語強調長久的歷史延續。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"convey a great deal","meaning":"傳達很多意思","examples":[{"en":"A handshake, kiss or hug can convey a great deal.","zh":"握手、親吻或擁抱可以傳達很多意思。"},{"en":"To convey a great deal means to communicate many meanings or feelings.","zh":"convey a great deal 指傳達許多意思或感受。"},{"en":"A teacher’s calm smile can convey a great deal to a nervous student before an exam.","zh":"考試前，老師平靜的微笑可以向緊張學生傳達很多意思。"},{"en":"Body language can convey a great deal even when people say very little.","zh":"即使人們說得很少，身體語言也可以傳達很多意思。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one small action can carry many messages.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個小動作可以承載許多訊息。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"signal friendship","meaning":"表示友誼","examples":[{"en":"A physical greeting can signal friendship.","zh":"身體問候可以表示友誼。"},{"en":"To signal friendship means to show that you are friendly and not hostile.","zh":"signal friendship 指顯示自己友善而不是有敵意。"},{"en":"A new classmate may signal friendship by smiling and offering to sit together.","zh":"新同學可能透過微笑並邀請一起坐來表示友誼。"},{"en":"Friendly signals can make social situations feel safer and less awkward.","zh":"友善訊號可以令社交場合感覺更安全、不那麼尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an action that communicates goodwill.","zh":"這個短語描述傳達善意的行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"finalise a business transaction","meaning":"落實商業交易","examples":[{"en":"A handshake has traditionally been used to finalise a business transaction.","zh":"握手傳統上被用來落實商業交易。"},{"en":"To finalise a business transaction means to complete a business deal or agreement.","zh":"finalise a business transaction 指完成一項商業交易或協議。"},{"en":"After both sides agree on the price, they may sign a contract to finalise the transaction.","zh":"雙方同意價格後，可能簽合約來落實交易。"},{"en":"Finalising a transaction makes the agreement official and harder to change.","zh":"落實交易會令協議正式化，並較難改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a business arrangement reaches its final confirmed stage.","zh":"這個短語用於商業安排到達最終確認階段時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"indicate religious devotion","meaning":"表示宗教虔誠","examples":[{"en":"A kiss may indicate religious devotion.","zh":"親吻可能表示宗教虔誠。"},{"en":"To indicate religious devotion means to show deep respect, faith, or commitment to a religion.","zh":"indicate religious devotion 指顯示對宗教的深切尊重、信仰或投入。"},{"en":"A worshipper may light a candle to indicate religious devotion.","zh":"信徒可能點蠟燭來表示宗教虔誠。"},{"en":"Religious actions can express belief even without spoken words.","zh":"宗教行動即使沒有言語，也可以表達信念。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an outward sign of inner faith.","zh":"這個短語描述內在信仰的外在象徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"transmit disease","meaning":"傳播疾病","examples":[{"en":"Touching strangers can transmit disease.","zh":"觸碰陌生人可以傳播疾病。"},{"en":"To transmit disease means to pass an illness from one person to another.","zh":"transmit disease 指把疾病由一個人傳給另一個人。"},{"en":"Dirty hands can transmit disease if people touch food without washing them.","zh":"如果人們未洗手就觸碰食物，骯髒雙手可以傳播疾病。"},{"en":"Physical greetings may spread illness when many people touch the same hands or faces.","zh":"當很多人觸碰同一雙手或臉，身體問候可能傳播疾病。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why hygiene matters in social contact.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何衛生在社交接觸中很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"less beneficial consequences","meaning":"較不利的後果","examples":[{"en":"Physical contact can have less beneficial consequences.","zh":"身體接觸可能有較不利的後果。"},{"en":"Less beneficial consequences are results that are not helpful and may even be harmful.","zh":"less beneficial consequences 指沒有幫助、甚至可能有害的結果。"},{"en":"A school rule may have less beneficial consequences if it makes students afraid to ask questions.","zh":"如果學校規則令學生害怕提問，它可能帶來較不利的後果。"},{"en":"A greeting may build trust, but it can also have less beneficial consequences if it spreads germs.","zh":"問候可以建立信任，但如果傳播細菌，也可能有較不利的後果。"},{"en":"This phrase politely points to negative results.","zh":"這個短語以較委婉方式指出負面結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the spread of disease","meaning":"疾病傳播","examples":[{"en":"Close physical contact may contribute to the spread of disease.","zh":"密切身體接觸可能促成疾病傳播。"},{"en":"The spread of disease is the movement of illness from person to person or place to place.","zh":"spread of disease 指疾病在人與人或地方與地方之間移動。"},{"en":"Schools try to reduce the spread of disease by asking sick students to stay home.","zh":"學校要求患病學生留在家中，以減少疾病傳播。"},{"en":"Crowded places can increase the spread of disease because people share air and surfaces.","zh":"擠迫地方可以增加疾病傳播，因為人們共享空氣和表面。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to how an illness moves through a group.","zh":"這個短語指疾病如何在群體中擴散。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fears about…mount","meaning":"對……的憂慮加劇","examples":[{"en":"Fears about COVID-19 mounted around the world.","zh":"世界各地對 COVID-19 的憂慮加劇。"},{"en":"When fears about something mount, people become increasingly worried about it.","zh":"fears about something mount 指人們對某事越來越擔心。"},{"en":"Fears about exam results may mount as the announcement day gets closer.","zh":"隨着公布日臨近，學生對考試結果的憂慮可能加劇。"},{"en":"News reports and rising case numbers can cause public fears to mount quickly.","zh":"新聞報道和個案數字上升可以令公眾憂慮迅速加劇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes worry growing stronger over time.","zh":"這個短語描述憂慮隨時間變得更強。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"warn citizens to","meaning":"警告市民不要……","examples":[{"en":"France warned its citizens to pause cheek kissing.","zh":"法國警告市民暫停貼面吻。"},{"en":"To warn citizens to do something means to officially tell the public to take care or change behaviour.","zh":"warn citizens to do something 指官方告訴公眾要小心或改變行為。"},{"en":"The government may warn citizens to stay indoors during a typhoon.","zh":"政府可能警告市民在颱風期間留在室內。"},{"en":"Warnings help people avoid danger before a situation becomes worse.","zh":"警告幫助人們在情況惡化前避開危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for public safety advice.","zh":"這個短語常用於公共安全建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pause a custom","meaning":"暫停一項習俗","examples":[{"en":"Public-health concerns may cause people to pause a traditional custom.","zh":"公共衞生憂慮可能令人暫停一項傳統習俗。"},{"en":"To pause a custom means to stop doing a habit or tradition temporarily.","zh":"pause a custom 指暫時停止一個習慣或傳統。"},{"en":"A school may pause a prize-giving ceremony during a serious flu outbreak.","zh":"學校可能在嚴重流感爆發期間暫停頒獎典禮。"},{"en":"People pause customs when continuing them may create risk.","zh":"當繼續某習俗可能帶來風險，人們就會暫停它。"},{"en":"This phrase means temporary suspension, not permanent abandonment.","zh":"這個短語指暫時停止，而不是永久放棄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"famous cheek kisses","meaning":"著名的貼面吻","examples":[{"en":"France is well known for its famous cheek kisses.","zh":"法國以其著名的貼面吻聞名。"},{"en":"Famous cheek kisses are well-known greetings where people lightly kiss or touch cheeks.","zh":"famous cheek kisses 指人們輕吻或貼近面頰的著名問候方式。"},{"en":"Visitors to some European countries may see friends greeting each other with cheek kisses.","zh":"到訪一些歐洲國家的遊客可能看到朋友以貼面吻互相問候。"},{"en":"A famous greeting custom can become part of a country’s cultural image.","zh":"著名問候習俗可以成為一個國家文化形象的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to cheek kissing as a recognised social practice.","zh":"這個短語指貼面吻作為公認社交做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"across the world","meaning":"在世界各地","examples":[{"en":"Greetings changed across the world during the pandemic.","zh":"疫情期間，世界各地的問候方式都有所改變。"},{"en":"Across the world means in many countries or regions worldwide.","zh":"across the world 指在全球許多國家或地區。"},{"en":"Online learning became common across the world when schools closed.","zh":"當學校停課，網上學習在世界各地變得常見。"},{"en":"A health crisis can change habits across the world because people face similar risks.","zh":"健康危機可以改變世界各地的習慣，因為人們面對相似風險。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises wide global reach.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛全球範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"seal a business deal","meaning":"敲定商業交易","examples":[{"en":"Business deals are often sealed with a handshake.","zh":"商業交易常以握手敲定。"},{"en":"To seal a business deal means to confirm or finalise an agreement.","zh":"seal a business deal 指確認或落實一項協議。"},{"en":"After months of negotiation, two companies may seal a business deal by signing a contract.","zh":"經過數月談判後，兩家公司可能透過簽合約敲定商業交易。"},{"en":"Sealing a deal gives both sides confidence that the agreement will go ahead.","zh":"敲定交易令雙方有信心協議會繼續進行。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a business agreement becomes definite.","zh":"這個短語用於商業協議變得確定時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"elbow bump","meaning":"碰手肘問候","examples":[{"en":"Some people replaced handshakes with an elbow bump.","zh":"有些人用碰手肘問候取代握手。"},{"en":"An elbow bump is a greeting where two people lightly touch elbows instead of hands.","zh":"elbow bump 指兩人輕碰手肘而不是雙手的問候方式。"},{"en":"During a flu outbreak, classmates may use an elbow bump to greet each other safely.","zh":"流感爆發期間，同學可能用碰手肘問候來較安全地打招呼。"},{"en":"Elbow bumps reduce hand contact and may lower the chance of spreading germs.","zh":"碰手肘問候減少手部接觸，可能降低傳播細菌的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a contact greeting often used when handshakes feel risky.","zh":"這個短語指當握手感覺有風險時常用的接觸式問候。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"histories stretching back","meaning":"歷史可追溯至……","examples":[{"en":"Both greetings have histories stretching back thousands of years.","zh":"兩種問候方式的歷史都可追溯至數千年前。"},{"en":"Histories stretching back means origins or records that go far into the past.","zh":"histories stretching back 指起源或記錄延伸到很久以前。"},{"en":"Some local festivals have histories stretching back many generations.","zh":"有些本地節日的歷史可追溯至許多世代之前。"},{"en":"A custom with a long history may be hard to change quickly.","zh":"歷史悠久的習俗可能難以迅速改變。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses how old and deeply rooted something is.","zh":"這個短語強調某事物多古老、多根深蒂固。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be deeply entrenched","meaning":"根深蒂固","examples":[{"en":"Traditional greetings are often deeply entrenched in a culture.","zh":"傳統問候方式常在文化中根深蒂固。"},{"en":"To be deeply entrenched means to be strongly established and difficult to change.","zh":"be deeply entrenched 指非常牢固地建立，難以改變。"},{"en":"In some schools, exam-focused teaching is deeply entrenched because parents expect high scores.","zh":"在一些學校，應試教學因家長期望高分而根深蒂固。"},{"en":"Deeply entrenched habits continue because people repeat them without questioning them.","zh":"根深蒂固的習慣會延續，因為人們不加質疑地重複它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes customs or beliefs that are firmly fixed.","zh":"這個短語描述牢牢固定的習俗或信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be easily halted","meaning":"輕易停止","examples":[{"en":"Long-established customs are unlikely to be easily halted.","zh":"長久建立的習俗不太可能被輕易停止。"},{"en":"To be easily halted means to be stopped quickly and without much difficulty.","zh":"be easily halted 指迅速且不太困難地被停止。"},{"en":"A daily school routine is not easily halted if teachers and students depend on it.","zh":"如果老師和學生都依賴某個每日學校常規，它就不容易被輕易停止。"},{"en":"Customs are harder to halt when they are connected to identity and politeness.","zh":"當習俗與身份和禮貌相關，就更難停止。"},{"en":"This phrase usually suggests that stopping something will be difficult.","zh":"這個短語通常表示停止某事會很困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a popular theory","meaning":"一種流行理論","examples":[{"en":"A popular theory explains the handshake as a gesture of peace.","zh":"一種流行理論把握手解釋為和平姿態。"},{"en":"A popular theory is an explanation that many people know or accept.","zh":"popular theory 指許多人知道或接受的解釋。"},{"en":"A popular theory about sleep says that phones before bed make rest worse.","zh":"一種關於睡眠的流行理論認為睡前用手機會令休息變差。"},{"en":"A theory can be popular even if evidence for it is incomplete.","zh":"即使證據不完整，一個理論仍可以很流行。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a widely repeated explanation.","zh":"這個短語引入被廣泛重複的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the handshake’s origin","meaning":"握手的起源","examples":[{"en":"The exact origin of the handshake remains uncertain.","zh":"握手的確切起源仍不確定。"},{"en":"The handshake’s origin is the historical beginning of the custom of shaking hands.","zh":"handshake’s origin 指握手這項習俗的歷史開端。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to research the origin of a festival before celebrating it.","zh":"老師可能要求學生在慶祝節日前研究其起源。"},{"en":"When a custom is very old, its origin may be difficult to prove.","zh":"當習俗非常古老，其起源可能難以證明。"},{"en":"This phrase asks where and why the practice first began.","zh":"這個短語詢問這種做法最初在哪裡和為何開始。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"begin as a gesture of peace","meaning":"起初是表示和平的動作","examples":[{"en":"The handshake may have begun as a gesture of peace.","zh":"握手可能起初是表示和平的動作。"},{"en":"To begin as a gesture of peace means to start as an action showing no desire to fight.","zh":"begin as a gesture of peace 指最初是一個顯示不想打鬥的行動。"},{"en":"Two neighbours may offer a handshake as a gesture of peace after an argument.","zh":"兩名鄰居爭執後，可能伸手握手作為和平姿態。"},{"en":"Peaceful gestures reduce tension because they show friendly intentions.","zh":"和平姿態能降低緊張，因為它們顯示友好意圖。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a possible original meaning of a custom.","zh":"這個短語解釋一項習俗可能的原始意思。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"grasp hands","meaning":"握住對方的手","examples":[{"en":"People may have grasped hands to show that they carried no weapon.","zh":"人們可能握住對方的手，以顯示自己沒有攜帶武器。"},{"en":"To grasp hands means to hold another person’s hand firmly.","zh":"grasp hands 指牢牢握住另一個人的手。"},{"en":"A parent may grasp a child’s hand before crossing a busy road.","zh":"家長在過繁忙馬路前可能握住孩子的手。"},{"en":"Grasping hands can show support, agreement, or trust depending on the situation.","zh":"握手可以根據情境表示支持、同意或信任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct hand-to-hand contact.","zh":"這個短語描述直接的手與手接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prove that","meaning":"證明","examples":[{"en":"Grasping hands supposedly proved that neither person was armed.","zh":"據說握住對方的手證明雙方都沒有武器。"},{"en":"To prove that something is true means to show it clearly with evidence.","zh":"prove that something is true 指用證據清楚顯示某事為真。"},{"en":"A receipt can prove that a customer paid for an item.","zh":"收據可以證明顧客已付款購買物品。"},{"en":"Without evidence, a claim may sound possible but remain unproven.","zh":"沒有證據，說法可能聽起來合理，但仍未被證明。"},{"en":"This phrase connects evidence with certainty.","zh":"這個短語把證據與確定性連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hold a weapon","meaning":"手持武器","examples":[{"en":"An open hand showed that a person was not holding a weapon.","zh":"張開的手顯示一個人沒有手持武器。"},{"en":"To hold a weapon means to carry or grip something used for fighting or attack.","zh":"hold a weapon 指拿着或握着用於打鬥或攻擊的東西。"},{"en":"Security guards may ask people to raise their hands to show they are not holding a weapon.","zh":"保安人員可能要求人舉起雙手，以顯示他們沒有手持武器。"},{"en":"Showing empty hands can reduce fear because others see no immediate danger.","zh":"展示空手可以減少恐懼，因為別人看不到即時危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical possession of a weapon.","zh":"這個短語描述實際持有武器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ensure that","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Shaking hands was thought to ensure that no weapon was hidden.","zh":"人們曾認為握手可以確保沒有武器被藏起來。"},{"en":"To ensure that something happens means to make certain or make it more likely.","zh":"ensure that something happens 指確保某事發生或令它更有可能。"},{"en":"A teacher checks attendance to ensure that every student is safe.","zh":"老師點名是為了確保每位學生安全。"},{"en":"Careful planning can ensure that a school trip runs smoothly.","zh":"仔細規劃可以確保學校旅行順利進行。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when an action aims to guarantee a result.","zh":"這個短語用於某行動旨在保證某結果時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have something hiding up one’s sleeve","meaning":"袖中沒有藏着東西","examples":[{"en":"The gesture supposedly showed that a person had nothing hiding up their sleeve.","zh":"據說這個動作顯示一個人袖中沒有藏着東西。"},{"en":"To have something hiding up one’s sleeve means to have something secretly kept or planned.","zh":"have something hiding up one’s sleeve 指暗中藏有或計劃着某事。"},{"en":"A magician may appear to have a card hiding up his sleeve.","zh":"魔術師可能看似袖中藏着一張牌。"},{"en":"In ordinary speech, the phrase can mean someone has a secret plan or trick.","zh":"在日常說話中，這個短語可以指某人有秘密計劃或花招。"},{"en":"In the handshake theory, it refers literally to hidden weapons or objects.","zh":"在握手理論中，它字面上指藏着武器或物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reliable evidence","meaning":"可靠證據","examples":[{"en":"There is no reliable evidence proving this theory.","zh":"沒有可靠證據證明這個理論。"},{"en":"Reliable evidence is information that can be trusted because it is accurate and well supported.","zh":"reliable evidence 指準確且有充分支持、可以信任的資料。"},{"en":"A doctor needs reliable evidence before recommending a new treatment.","zh":"醫生在建議新療法前需要可靠證據。"},{"en":"If evidence is weak or unclear, a theory should not be treated as fact.","zh":"如果證據薄弱或不清楚，理論就不應被當作事實。"},{"en":"This phrase separates trustworthy proof from guesses or rumours.","zh":"這個短語把可信證明與猜測或傳聞分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"prove an assumption","meaning":"證明一項假設","examples":[{"en":"Historians have not been able to prove this assumption.","zh":"歷史學家一直未能證明這項假設。"},{"en":"To prove an assumption means to show that a belief or idea is true with evidence.","zh":"prove an assumption 指用證據顯示某信念或想法為真。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to prove an assumption by finding facts in the passage.","zh":"老師可能要求學生透過在文章中找事實來證明一項假設。"},{"en":"If no evidence supports an assumption, it remains only a possibility.","zh":"如果沒有證據支持假設，它仍只是可能性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing theories that sound reasonable but are uncertain.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論聽起來合理但不確定的理論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"throughout the ancient world","meaning":"遍及古代世界","examples":[{"en":"Images of handshakes appeared throughout the ancient world.","zh":"握手圖像遍及古代世界。"},{"en":"Throughout the ancient world means in many places across ancient societies.","zh":"throughout the ancient world 指在古代社會中的許多地方。"},{"en":"Trade routes existed throughout the ancient world, connecting cities and cultures.","zh":"貿易路線遍及古代世界，連接城市和文化。"},{"en":"If a symbol appears widely, it may have been understood by many different peoples.","zh":"如果一個象徵廣泛出現，它可能被許多不同民族理解。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses wide distribution in ancient times.","zh":"這個短語強調在古代時期分佈廣泛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"appear on","meaning":"出現在……上","examples":[{"en":"The handshake appears on ancient vases and gravestones.","zh":"握手出現在古代花瓶和墓碑上。"},{"en":"To appear on something means to be shown, written, printed, or displayed on its surface.","zh":"appear on something 指被顯示、寫上、印上或展示在某物表面。"},{"en":"A school logo may appear on uniforms, letters, and sports bags.","zh":"學校標誌可能出現在校服、信件和運動袋上。"},{"en":"Images that appear on objects can reveal what people considered important.","zh":"出現在物件上的圖像可以揭示人們認為甚麼重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where a sign, image, or word is found.","zh":"這個短語描述標誌、圖像或文字在哪裡被找到。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"gravestones","meaning":"墓碑","examples":[{"en":"Handshakes were sometimes shown on ancient gravestones.","zh":"握手有時出現在古代墓碑上。"},{"en":"Gravestones are stones placed at graves, often with names, dates, or images.","zh":"gravestones 指放在墳墓上的石碑，通常有姓名、日期或圖像。"},{"en":"A family may visit a gravestone to remember a relative who has died.","zh":"家庭可能探訪墓碑，以紀念去世親人。"},{"en":"Images on gravestones can show beliefs about death, family, or the afterlife.","zh":"墓碑上的圖像可以顯示關於死亡、家庭或來世的信念。"},{"en":"This word refers to memorial stones for the dead.","zh":"這個詞指紀念死者的石碑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"stone slabs","meaning":"石板","examples":[{"en":"Scenes of handshakes were carved on stone slabs.","zh":"握手場面被雕刻在石板上。"},{"en":"Stone slabs are flat pieces of stone used for building, writing, carving, or decoration.","zh":"stone slabs 指用於建築、書寫、雕刻或裝飾的平石塊。"},{"en":"A museum may display stone slabs with ancient writing on them.","zh":"博物館可能展示刻有古文字的石板。"},{"en":"Carved slabs can preserve images for centuries because stone lasts a long time.","zh":"雕刻石板可以保存圖像數百年，因為石頭很耐久。"},{"en":"This phrase describes flat stone surfaces used for records or art.","zh":"這個短語描述用於記錄或藝術的平坦石面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"scenes of weddings","meaning":"婚禮場面","examples":[{"en":"Ancient art includes scenes of weddings and agreements.","zh":"古代藝術包括婚禮和協議場面。"},{"en":"Scenes of weddings are pictures or descriptions showing marriage ceremonies.","zh":"scenes of weddings 指展示婚姻儀式的圖像或描述。"},{"en":"A family photo album may include scenes of weddings, birthdays, and graduations.","zh":"家庭相簿可能包括婚禮、生日和畢業典禮場面。"},{"en":"Wedding scenes reveal clothing, rituals, and social values of a time.","zh":"婚禮場面揭示某時代的服飾、儀式和社會價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual or written moments from wedding events.","zh":"這個短語描述婚禮事件中的視覺或文字片段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"gods making deals","meaning":"神明達成協議","examples":[{"en":"Some ancient images show gods making deals.","zh":"有些古代圖像顯示神明達成協議。"},{"en":"Gods making deals means divine figures are shown reaching agreements or promises.","zh":"gods making deals 指神聖人物被描繪為達成協議或承諾。"},{"en":"In a myth, gods may make deals with humans in exchange for loyalty or gifts.","zh":"在神話中，神明可能與人類達成協議，以換取忠誠或禮物。"},{"en":"Images of gods making deals can show that agreements were considered sacred or powerful.","zh":"神明達成協議的圖像可以顯示協議被視為神聖或有力量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a religious or mythological scene of agreement.","zh":"這個短語描述宗教或神話中的協議場面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"depart for war","meaning":"出征","examples":[{"en":"Young warriors were shown departing for war.","zh":"年輕戰士被描繪為出征。"},{"en":"To depart for war means to leave home or one’s community to go to battle.","zh":"depart for war 指離開家或社群去參戰。"},{"en":"A soldier may depart for war after saying goodbye to family.","zh":"士兵可能在與家人道別後出征。"},{"en":"Such scenes often show courage, fear, duty, and uncertainty.","zh":"這類場面常顯示勇氣、恐懼、責任和不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes leaving for military conflict.","zh":"這個短語描述前往軍事衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"arrival in the afterlife","meaning":"到達來世","examples":[{"en":"Some images represented the dead person’s arrival in the afterlife.","zh":"有些圖像代表死者到達來世。"},{"en":"Arrival in the afterlife means entering a life or world believed to exist after death.","zh":"arrival in the afterlife 指進入被相信存在於死亡之後的生命或世界。"},{"en":"Ancient cultures often created art showing a person’s journey to the afterlife.","zh":"古代文化常創作藝術，展示人前往來世的旅程。"},{"en":"Such images reveal beliefs about death, memory, and spiritual hope.","zh":"這類圖像揭示關於死亡、記憶和精神希望的信念。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to religious ideas about what happens after death.","zh":"這個短語指關於死後會發生甚麼的宗教觀念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"literary canon","meaning":"經典文學作品","examples":[{"en":"The handshake also appears in the Western literary canon.","zh":"握手也出現在西方經典文學作品中。"},{"en":"A literary canon is a group of important works widely studied and respected in a culture.","zh":"literary canon 指某文化中被廣泛研究和尊重的重要作品群。"},{"en":"Shakespeare’s plays are often treated as part of the English literary canon.","zh":"莎士比亞戲劇常被視為英語經典文學作品的一部分。"},{"en":"When a gesture appears in the canon, it suggests the gesture has long cultural importance.","zh":"當某姿態出現在經典作品中，表示它長期具有文化重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to recognised classic literature.","zh":"這個短語指公認的經典文學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"stretch back to","meaning":"可追溯至……","examples":[{"en":"Literary references to the gesture stretch back to the Iliad.","zh":"對這個姿態的文學提及可追溯至《伊利亞特》。"},{"en":"To stretch back to a time means to go back as far as that time in history.","zh":"stretch back to a time 指歷史上可追溯到某個時期。"},{"en":"A school tradition may stretch back to the year the school was founded.","zh":"學校傳統可能可追溯至學校創立那一年。"},{"en":"If a custom stretches back thousands of years, it has deep historical roots.","zh":"如果一項習俗可追溯至數千年前，它就有深厚歷史根源。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how far into the past something reaches.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事延伸到多遠的過去。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"catch-all utility","meaning":"廣泛而通用的用途","examples":[{"en":"The handshake has a catch-all utility in many social situations.","zh":"握手在許多社交情況中有廣泛而通用的用途。"},{"en":"Catch-all utility means a broad usefulness across many different situations.","zh":"catch-all utility 指在許多不同情況中的廣泛用途。"},{"en":"A smartphone has catch-all utility because people use it for calls, maps, payments, and photos.","zh":"智能手機有廣泛而通用的用途，因為人們用它打電話、看地圖、付款和拍照。"},{"en":"A gesture with catch-all utility can be used in business, friendship, and ceremony.","zh":"有廣泛用途的姿態可以用於商業、友誼和儀式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something useful in many contexts, not just one.","zh":"這個短語描述某事物在多種情境中有用，而不只限一種。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"friendship, romance and business alike","meaning":"同樣用於友誼、愛情和商業","examples":[{"en":"The handshake has been used in friendship, romance and business alike.","zh":"握手同樣用於友誼、愛情和商業。"},{"en":"Friendship, romance and business alike means all three areas use the gesture in similar ways.","zh":"friendship, romance and business alike 指這三個範疇都以相似方式使用該姿態。"},{"en":"A smile can matter in friendship, romance and business alike because it shows warmth.","zh":"微笑同樣可用於友誼、愛情和商業，因為它顯示溫暖。"},{"en":"When a custom works in many areas, its meaning can become flexible.","zh":"當一項習俗在許多範疇都可使用，其意思可以變得靈活。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the same action crosses different parts of life.","zh":"這個短語顯示同一行動跨越生活中不同部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make interpretation difficult","meaning":"令詮釋變得困難","examples":[{"en":"Its many uses make interpretation difficult.","zh":"它的多種用途令詮釋變得困難。"},{"en":"To make interpretation difficult means to make meaning hard to understand clearly.","zh":"make interpretation difficult 指令意思難以清楚理解。"},{"en":"A text message with no punctuation can make interpretation difficult.","zh":"沒有標點的短訊可以令詮釋變得困難。"},{"en":"If one gesture has many possible meanings, people may not know how to read it.","zh":"如果一個姿態有許多可能意思，人們可能不知道如何解讀。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why context is important.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何語境很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a complex and ambiguous motif","meaning":"複雜而含義不明確的主題","examples":[{"en":"The handshake is a complex and ambiguous motif in art.","zh":"握手是藝術中一個複雜而含義不明確的主題。"},{"en":"A complex and ambiguous motif is a repeated image or theme with several possible meanings.","zh":"complex and ambiguous motif 指有幾種可能意思的重複圖像或主題。"},{"en":"A broken clock in a film can be a complex and ambiguous motif if it suggests memory, loss, or time pressure.","zh":"電影中的破鐘如果暗示記憶、失去或時間壓力，就可以是複雜而含義不明確的主題。"},{"en":"Ambiguous motifs require careful interpretation because they are not limited to one meaning.","zh":"含義不明確的主題需要仔細詮釋，因為它不只限於一個意思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a symbol that is rich but not simple.","zh":"這個短語描述豐富但不簡單的象徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"art historian","meaning":"藝術史學家","examples":[{"en":"Glenys Davies is an art historian who studied classical images.","zh":"Glenys Davies 是研究古典圖像的藝術史學家。"},{"en":"An art historian is a person who studies the history, meaning, and context of artworks.","zh":"art historian 指研究藝術品的歷史、意義和語境的人。"},{"en":"An art historian may examine a painting to understand the clothing, symbols, and beliefs it shows.","zh":"藝術史學家可能研究一幅畫，以理解其中展示的服飾、象徵和信念。"},{"en":"Art historians help us see that images can carry social and historical meanings.","zh":"藝術史學家幫助我們看見圖像可以承載社會和歷史意義。"},{"en":"This phrase names an expert in the study of art history.","zh":"這個短語命名研究藝術史的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"classical art","meaning":"古典藝術","examples":[{"en":"The handshake appears frequently in classical art.","zh":"握手經常出現在古典藝術中。"},{"en":"Classical art refers to art from ancient Greek and Roman traditions or art inspired by them.","zh":"classical art 指古希臘和古羅馬傳統中的藝術，或受其啟發的藝術。"},{"en":"A museum may display classical art showing gods, athletes, soldiers, and family scenes.","zh":"博物館可能展示描繪神明、運動員、士兵和家庭場景的古典藝術。"},{"en":"Classical art helps historians understand ancient social customs and beliefs.","zh":"古典藝術幫助歷史學家理解古代社會習俗和信念。"},{"en":"This phrase usually points to ancient or classically inspired artistic work.","zh":"這個短語通常指古代或受古典啟發的藝術作品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be propelled by","meaning":"由……推動","examples":[{"en":"The handshake’s popularity in America may have been propelled by the Quakers.","zh":"握手在美國的流行可能由貴格會教徒推動。"},{"en":"To be propelled by something means to be pushed forward or made more successful by it.","zh":"be propelled by something 指被某事推動前進或促成成功。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may be propelled by a teacher’s encouragement.","zh":"學生的信心可能由老師的鼓勵推動。"},{"en":"A custom can spread faster when an influential group supports it.","zh":"當有影響力的群體支持一項習俗，它可以更快傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a force that helps something grow or move forward.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助某事成長或前進的力量。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"18th-century Quakers","meaning":"18世紀貴格會教徒","examples":[{"en":"Eighteenth-century Quakers helped popularise handshaking in America.","zh":"18 世紀貴格會教徒幫助握手在美國流行起來。"},{"en":"Eighteenth-century Quakers were members of the Quaker religious community living in the 1700s.","zh":"18th-century Quakers 指生活在 18 世紀的貴格會宗教社群成員。"},{"en":"A history class may study 18th-century Quakers to understand religious ideas about equality.","zh":"歷史課可能研究 18 世紀貴格會教徒，以理解關於平等的宗教思想。"},{"en":"Their social practices influenced how some Americans greeted one another.","zh":"他們的社交做法影響了一些美國人如何互相問候。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific religious group in a specific historical period.","zh":"這個短語指出特定歷史時期中的特定宗教群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in an effort to","meaning":"為了……","examples":[{"en":"Quakers used handshakes in an effort to reject social hierarchy.","zh":"貴格會教徒使用握手，是為了拒絕社會階級制度。"},{"en":"In an effort to do something means in order to try to achieve that aim.","zh":"in an effort to do something 指為了嘗試達成某目的。"},{"en":"A school may reduce homework in an effort to improve students’ sleep.","zh":"學校可能減少功課，為了改善學生睡眠。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the purpose behind an action.","zh":"這個短語顯示行動背後的目的。"},{"en":"It suggests an attempt, not always guaranteed success.","zh":"它表示嘗試，不一定保證成功。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"eschew hierarchy","meaning":"避免階級制度","examples":[{"en":"Quakers tried to eschew hierarchy and social rank.","zh":"貴格會教徒嘗試避免階級制度和社會等級。"},{"en":"To eschew hierarchy means to deliberately avoid systems where some people are treated as higher than others.","zh":"eschew hierarchy 指有意避免某些人被視為高於其他人的制度。"},{"en":"A teacher may eschew hierarchy by inviting students to share ideas openly.","zh":"老師可能透過邀請學生公開分享想法來避免階級感。"},{"en":"Avoiding hierarchy can make a group feel more equal and less formal.","zh":"避免階級制度可以令群體感覺更平等、較不拘謹。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal and means refusing ranked social differences.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是拒絕社會等級差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"social rank","meaning":"社會階級","examples":[{"en":"The bow often reflected differences in social rank.","zh":"鞠躬常反映社會階級差異。"},{"en":"Social rank is a person’s position or status within a social system.","zh":"social rank 指一個人在社會制度中的位置或地位。"},{"en":"In some old societies, clothing showed social rank clearly.","zh":"在一些舊社會中，衣着清楚顯示社會階級。"},{"en":"Greetings may change when people want to reduce visible differences in social rank.","zh":"當人們想減少可見的社會階級差異，問候方式可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to status levels among people.","zh":"這個短語指人與人之間的地位等級。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"democratic form of greeting","meaning":"較平等的問候方式","examples":[{"en":"The handshake was considered a more democratic form of greeting.","zh":"握手被視為較平等的問候方式。"},{"en":"A democratic form of greeting treats people as equal rather than ranking them by status.","zh":"democratic form of greeting 指把人視為平等，而不是按地位排序的問候方式。"},{"en":"A school principal who shakes hands with every student uses a more equal greeting style.","zh":"校長與每位學生握手，就是使用較平等的問候方式。"},{"en":"Such greetings can reduce distance between people of different positions.","zh":"這類問候可以減少不同位置人士之間的距離。"},{"en":"This phrase links greeting customs with equality.","zh":"這個短語把問候習俗與平等連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"then-common custom","meaning":"當時常見的習俗","examples":[{"en":"Bowing and hat doffing were then-common customs.","zh":"鞠躬和脫帽致意是當時常見的習俗。"},{"en":"A then-common custom is a practice that was common at that time in the past.","zh":"then-common custom 指在過去某個時期常見的做法。"},{"en":"Writing letters by hand was a then-common custom before email became popular.","zh":"在電郵流行前，手寫信是當時常見的習俗。"},{"en":"Customs that are common in one period may disappear in another.","zh":"某時期常見的習俗可能在另一時期消失。"},{"en":"This phrase places a habit in its historical context.","zh":"這個短語把習慣放在其歷史語境中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bow and curtsy","meaning":"鞠躬和屈膝禮","examples":[{"en":"The handshake replaced the bow and curtsy among some groups.","zh":"在一些群體中，握手取代了鞠躬和屈膝禮。"},{"en":"A bow and curtsy are formal greetings where people bend the body to show respect.","zh":"bow and curtsy 指人們彎身以表示尊重的正式問候方式。"},{"en":"In old court ceremonies, men might bow and women might curtsy.","zh":"在舊式宮廷儀式中，男性可能鞠躬，女性可能行屈膝禮。"},{"en":"These gestures can show politeness but may also reflect social hierarchy.","zh":"這些姿態可以表示禮貌，但也可能反映社會階級。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to traditional formal body greetings.","zh":"這個短語指傳統正式身體問候。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hat doffing","meaning":"脫帽致意","examples":[{"en":"Hat doffing was once a conventional greeting.","zh":"脫帽致意曾是一種傳統問候。"},{"en":"Hat doffing means lifting or removing a hat briefly to show respect.","zh":"hat doffing 指短暫抬起或脫下帽子以表示尊重。"},{"en":"In old films, a man may greet a woman by doffing his hat.","zh":"在舊電影中，男人可能透過脫帽向女性問好。"},{"en":"Hat doffing signals politeness but also reflects a time when hats were common.","zh":"脫帽致意表示禮貌，但也反映帽子常見的年代。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an old-fashioned greeting gesture.","zh":"這個短語描述舊式問候姿態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in their place","meaning":"取而代之","examples":[{"en":"In their place, Quakers adopted the handshake.","zh":"取而代之，貴格會教徒採用了握手。"},{"en":"In their place means instead of the things just mentioned.","zh":"in their place 指取代剛剛提到的事物。"},{"en":"The school removed long lectures; in their place, teachers used short discussions.","zh":"學校取消長時間講課；取而代之，老師使用短討論。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one practice has replaced another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一種做法取代另一種做法。"},{"en":"It helps writers explain a change from old customs to new ones.","zh":"它幫助作者解釋由舊習俗到新習俗的轉變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"extend a greeting to everyone","meaning":"向所有人作出問候","examples":[{"en":"The handshake was extended to everyone regardless of status.","zh":"握手不論身份地位都被用來向所有人作出問候。"},{"en":"To extend a greeting to everyone means to offer the same greeting to all people.","zh":"extend a greeting to everyone 指向所有人提供同一種問候。"},{"en":"A teacher extends a greeting to everyone by saying good morning to the whole class.","zh":"老師向全班說早安，就是向所有人作出問候。"},{"en":"Equal greetings can make people feel included rather than ranked.","zh":"平等問候可以令人感到被包括，而不是被分等級。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a greeting broad and inclusive.","zh":"這個短語描述使問候變得廣泛而包容。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"regardless of station","meaning":"不論社會地位","examples":[{"en":"Quakers shook hands with everyone regardless of station.","zh":"貴格會教徒不論社會地位與所有人握手。"},{"en":"Regardless of station means no matter what social position or status a person has.","zh":"regardless of station 指無論一個人有甚麼社會位置或身份。"},{"en":"A good public hospital treats patients regardless of station or income.","zh":"良好公立醫院不論社會地位或收入都會治療病人。"},{"en":"Ignoring station can make social interaction feel more equal.","zh":"不理會地位可以令社交互動感覺更平等。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses equality across social rank.","zh":"這個短語強調跨社會階級的平等。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lasting power","meaning":"長久延續的力量","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have proposed an explanation for the handshake’s lasting power.","zh":"科學家提出了握手長久延續力量的一種解釋。"},{"en":"Lasting power is the ability of something to continue or remain influential for a long time.","zh":"lasting power 指某事物長時間延續或保持影響力的能力。"},{"en":"A simple children’s song has lasting power if families keep singing it for generations.","zh":"如果家庭世代繼續唱一首簡單童謠，它就有長久延續的力量。"},{"en":"Customs have lasting power when they serve social, emotional, or practical needs.","zh":"當習俗滿足社交、情感或實際需要，就會有長久延續的力量。"},{"en":"This phrase asks why something does not easily disappear.","zh":"這個短語詢問某事為何不容易消失。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"film hundreds of strangers","meaning":"拍攝數百名陌生人","examples":[{"en":"Researchers filmed hundreds of strangers shaking hands.","zh":"研究人員拍攝數百名陌生人握手。"},{"en":"To film hundreds of strangers means to record many unknown people on video.","zh":"film hundreds of strangers 指用影片記錄許多不認識的人。"},{"en":"Researchers may film shoppers in a mall to study how people move through crowded spaces.","zh":"研究人員可能拍攝商場購物者，以研究人們如何穿過擠迫空間。"},{"en":"Filming behaviour lets scientists observe actions people may not notice themselves.","zh":"拍攝行為讓科學家觀察人們自己可能沒有注意到的動作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes collecting visual research data from many unfamiliar people.","zh":"這個短語描述從許多陌生人身上收集影像研究資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"nearly a quarter of","meaning":"接近四分之一","examples":[{"en":"Nearly a quarter of the participants sniffed their hands afterwards.","zh":"接近四分之一的參加者之後嗅自己的手。"},{"en":"Nearly a quarter of a group means almost 25 percent of that group.","zh":"nearly a quarter of a group 指某群體中接近百分之二十五。"},{"en":"Nearly a quarter of the class arrived early for extra revision.","zh":"接近四分之一的班級學生提早到校作額外溫習。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate proportion, not an exact number.","zh":"這個短語給出大約比例，而不是精確數字。"},{"en":"It means close to one in four people.","zh":"它的意思是接近每四人中一人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"participants","meaning":"參加者","examples":[{"en":"The participants were observed after shaking hands.","zh":"參加者在握手後被觀察。"},{"en":"Participants are people who take part in a study, event, activity, or experiment.","zh":"participants 指參與研究、事件、活動或實驗的人。"},{"en":"Participants in a school survey answer questions about their study habits.","zh":"學校調查的參加者會回答關於學習習慣的問題。"},{"en":"Researchers observe participants to understand behaviour and collect data.","zh":"研究人員觀察參加者，以理解行為並收集數據。"},{"en":"This word refers to people involved in an organised activity.","zh":"這個詞指參與有組織活動的人。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sniff one’s hands","meaning":"嗅自己的手","examples":[{"en":"Some participants sniffed their hands after the greeting.","zh":"有些參加者在問候後嗅自己的手。"},{"en":"To sniff one’s hands means to smell one’s hands by breathing in through the nose.","zh":"sniff one’s hands 指透過鼻子吸氣來聞自己的手。"},{"en":"A child may sniff their hands after touching flowers to smell the scent.","zh":"孩子摸過花後，可能嗅自己的手來聞香味。"},{"en":"People may sniff their hands without noticing it, especially after touching something unusual.","zh":"人們可能在沒有察覺下嗅自己的手，尤其是觸碰不尋常東西後。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small smelling action.","zh":"這個短語描述一個小型嗅聞動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"theorise that","meaning":"提出理論認為","examples":[{"en":"The researchers theorised that handshakes transmit chemical information.","zh":"研究人員提出理論認為握手會傳遞化學資訊。"},{"en":"To theorise that means to suggest an explanation based on evidence or reasoning.","zh":"theorise that 指根據證據或推理提出解釋。"},{"en":"Scientists may theorise that students remember better when learning is linked to emotion.","zh":"科學家可能提出理論認為，當學習與情感相連，學生記得更好。"},{"en":"A theory may need more testing before it becomes widely accepted.","zh":"一個理論在被廣泛接受前可能需要更多測試。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a possible explanation, not a proven fact.","zh":"這個短語引入可能解釋，而不是已證實事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"unconsciously use","meaning":"在不自覺下使用","examples":[{"en":"People may unconsciously use handshakes to gather information.","zh":"人們可能在不自覺下使用握手來收集資訊。"},{"en":"To unconsciously use something means to use it without being aware that you are doing so.","zh":"unconsciously use something 指在沒有意識到的情況下使用某物。"},{"en":"A student may unconsciously use gestures when explaining a difficult idea.","zh":"學生解釋困難概念時，可能在不自覺下使用手勢。"},{"en":"Unconscious habits can reveal how people think or feel without deliberate planning.","zh":"不自覺習慣可以揭示人們如何思考或感受，而不是刻意計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes behaviour that happens below conscious awareness.","zh":"這個短語描述在意識以下發生的行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"detect chemical signals","meaning":"察覺化學訊號","examples":[{"en":"A handshake may help people detect chemical signals.","zh":"握手可能幫助人察覺化學訊號。"},{"en":"To detect chemical signals means to notice information carried by smell or chemicals.","zh":"detect chemical signals 指注意到由氣味或化學物質承載的資訊。"},{"en":"A dog can detect chemical signals in a person’s scent.","zh":"狗可以從人的氣味中察覺化學訊號。"},{"en":"If humans detect chemical signals through touch or smell, greetings may carry hidden information.","zh":"如果人類透過觸碰或氣味察覺化學訊號，問候可能帶有隱藏資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sensing chemical information, often without words.","zh":"這個短語描述感知化學資訊，通常不用言語。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a means of communication","meaning":"溝通方式","examples":[{"en":"Smell may act as a means of communication.","zh":"氣味可能作為一種溝通方式。"},{"en":"A means of communication is a way of sending or receiving information.","zh":"means of communication 指傳送或接收資訊的方法。"},{"en":"Text messages are a common means of communication between classmates.","zh":"短訊是同學之間常見的溝通方式。"},{"en":"Communication does not always require speech; gestures and smells can also carry information.","zh":"溝通不一定需要說話；手勢和氣味也可以承載資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the method used to share meaning.","zh":"這個短語指出分享意思所用的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"just as other animals do","meaning":"正如其他動物一樣","examples":[{"en":"Humans may gather chemical information just as other animals do.","zh":"人類可能正如其他動物一樣收集化學資訊。"},{"en":"Just as other animals do means in the same way that animals do it.","zh":"just as other animals do 指以其他動物做某事的相同方式。"},{"en":"Babies learn by watching faces, just as other young animals learn by observing adults.","zh":"嬰兒透過觀察臉孔學習，正如其他幼小動物透過觀察成年個體學習一樣。"},{"en":"This phrase compares human behaviour with animal behaviour.","zh":"這個短語把人類行為與動物行為作比較。"},{"en":"It suggests that a human habit may have a biological basis.","zh":"它暗示人類習慣可能有生物基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"kiss-as-greeting","meaning":"作為問候的親吻","examples":[{"en":"The kiss-as-greeting has a similarly long history.","zh":"作為問候的親吻同樣有悠久歷史。"},{"en":"A kiss-as-greeting is a kiss used to say hello, welcome someone, or show respect.","zh":"kiss-as-greeting 指用來打招呼、歡迎某人或表示尊重的親吻。"},{"en":"In some families, a kiss-as-greeting is normal when relatives meet.","zh":"在一些家庭中，親戚見面時以親吻問候是正常的。"},{"en":"This kind of kiss can show warmth, but it may also create hygiene concerns.","zh":"這種親吻可以表示溫暖，但也可能造成衞生憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase distinguishes greeting kisses from romantic kisses.","zh":"這個短語把問候之吻與浪漫親吻區分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"similarly rich history","meaning":"同樣悠久而豐富的歷史","examples":[{"en":"Cheek kissing has a similarly rich history.","zh":"貼面吻有同樣悠久而豐富的歷史。"},{"en":"A similarly rich history means a history that is equally long, varied, and meaningful.","zh":"similarly rich history 指同樣長久、多樣且有意義的歷史。"},{"en":"Tea drinking and coffee drinking both have rich histories in different cultures.","zh":"飲茶和飲咖啡在不同文化中都有豐富歷史。"},{"en":"A rich history makes a custom harder to understand from one modern example alone.","zh":"豐富歷史令一項習俗難以只從一個現代例子理解。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the depth of two historical traditions.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種歷史傳統的深度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be incorporated into","meaning":"被納入……","examples":[{"en":"The kiss was incorporated into early Christian practices.","zh":"親吻被納入早期基督教做法中。"},{"en":"To be incorporated into something means to be included as part of it.","zh":"be incorporated into something 指被包括成為某事物的一部分。"},{"en":"A school may incorporate drama into English lessons to make speaking more natural.","zh":"學校可能把戲劇納入英文課，令說話更自然。"},{"en":"When a custom is incorporated into a religion, it gains a new meaning and role.","zh":"當習俗被納入宗教，它會獲得新的意義和角色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding something into a larger system.","zh":"這個短語描述把某事物加入較大系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"early Christianity","meaning":"早期基督教","examples":[{"en":"Kissing was used in ceremonies in early Christianity.","zh":"親吻在早期基督教儀式中被使用。"},{"en":"Early Christianity means the first period of Christian belief and practice after Christianity began.","zh":"early Christianity 指基督教開始後最初階段的信仰和做法。"},{"en":"A history class may study early Christianity to understand how religious customs developed.","zh":"歷史課可能研究早期基督教，以理解宗教習俗如何發展。"},{"en":"Practices from early Christianity sometimes continued in later church traditions.","zh":"早期基督教的做法有時延續到後來教會傳統中。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the early historical stage of Christianity.","zh":"這個短語指基督教的早期歷史階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"religious ceremonies","meaning":"宗教儀式","examples":[{"en":"Early Christians used kisses in religious ceremonies.","zh":"早期基督徒在宗教儀式中使用親吻。"},{"en":"Religious ceremonies are formal acts of worship or faith carried out by a religious community.","zh":"religious ceremonies 指由宗教社群進行的正式崇拜或信仰活動。"},{"en":"Weddings, prayers, baptisms, and funerals can be religious ceremonies.","zh":"婚禮、祈禱、洗禮和喪禮都可以是宗教儀式。"},{"en":"Ceremonies use repeated actions to express shared belief and belonging.","zh":"儀式使用重複動作來表達共同信仰和歸屬。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal spiritual events.","zh":"這個短語指正式精神或宗教活動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"instruct followers to","meaning":"指示信徒去……","examples":[{"en":"St. Paul instructed followers to greet one another with a holy kiss.","zh":"聖保羅指示信徒以聖潔之吻互相問候。"},{"en":"To instruct followers to do something means to tell believers or supporters to act in a certain way.","zh":"instruct followers to do something 指告訴信徒或支持者以某種方式行動。"},{"en":"A coach may instruct team members to shake hands after a match.","zh":"教練可能指示隊員在比賽後握手。"},{"en":"Instructions from a respected leader can shape group behaviour.","zh":"受尊敬領袖的指示可以塑造群體行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving guidance to people who follow a belief or leader.","zh":"這個短語描述向追隨某信念或領袖的人給予指引。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"salute one another","meaning":"互相致意","examples":[{"en":"Early Christians were instructed to salute one another with a kiss.","zh":"早期基督徒被指示以親吻互相致意。"},{"en":"To salute one another means to greet each other respectfully.","zh":"salute one another 指互相以尊重方式問候。"},{"en":"Students may salute one another with a smile before beginning a group activity.","zh":"學生可能在小組活動開始前以微笑互相致意。"},{"en":"A salute can be formal, religious, military, or simply polite depending on context.","zh":"致意可以是正式、宗教、軍事或純粹禮貌，視乎語境。"},{"en":"This phrase means mutual greeting with respect.","zh":"這個短語表示彼此尊重地問候。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a holy kiss","meaning":"聖潔之吻","examples":[{"en":"The holy kiss symbolised religious fellowship.","zh":"聖潔之吻象徵宗教團契。"},{"en":"A holy kiss is a kiss used as a sacred sign of greeting, unity, or faith.","zh":"holy kiss 指作為神聖問候、合一或信仰標誌的親吻。"},{"en":"In a religious community, a holy kiss may show that members belong to the same faith.","zh":"在宗教社群中，聖潔之吻可能顯示成員屬於同一信仰。"},{"en":"Because it is “holy”, the kiss is not mainly romantic or casual.","zh":"因為它是「聖潔的」，這個吻主要不是浪漫或隨意的。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a religious gesture of connection.","zh":"這個短語指宗教上的連繫姿態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in search of","meaning":"尋找……","examples":[{"en":"The book explores customs in search of the perfect greeting.","zh":"這本書探索習俗，以尋找完美問候方式。"},{"en":"In search of something means trying to find it.","zh":"in search of something 指嘗試尋找某物。"},{"en":"A student may read several books in search of a clear explanation.","zh":"學生可能閱讀幾本書，以尋找清楚解釋。"},{"en":"People search when they feel the answer is not obvious or complete.","zh":"當人們覺得答案不明顯或不完整，就會尋找。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an active attempt to find something better.","zh":"這個短語描述主動嘗試找到更好的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the Middle Ages","meaning":"在中世紀","examples":[{"en":"Kissing had legal and social functions in the Middle Ages.","zh":"在中世紀，親吻有法律和社會功能。"},{"en":"In the Middle Ages means during the medieval period of European history.","zh":"in the Middle Ages 指在歐洲歷史的中世紀時期。"},{"en":"In the Middle Ages, many agreements were made without modern written contracts.","zh":"在中世紀，許多協議並沒有現代書面合約。"},{"en":"Customs from the Middle Ages can help explain why later traditions developed.","zh":"中世紀的習俗可以幫助解釋後來傳統為何發展。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event in a historical period.","zh":"這個短語把事件放在歷史時期中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a sign of fidelity","meaning":"忠誠的象徵","examples":[{"en":"A kiss could serve as a sign of fidelity.","zh":"親吻可以作為忠誠的象徵。"},{"en":"A sign of fidelity is an action or symbol showing loyalty and faithfulness.","zh":"sign of fidelity 指顯示忠誠和信守承諾的行動或象徵。"},{"en":"A wedding ring can be a sign of fidelity in marriage.","zh":"結婚戒指可以是婚姻中忠誠的象徵。"},{"en":"Signs of fidelity reassure others that a promise or relationship is serious.","zh":"忠誠象徵令別人放心，知道承諾或關係是認真的。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an outward symbol of loyalty.","zh":"這個短語指忠誠的外在象徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"seal an agreement","meaning":"確立協議","examples":[{"en":"A kiss was sometimes used to seal an agreement.","zh":"親吻有時被用來確立協議。"},{"en":"To seal an agreement means to confirm it and make it feel final.","zh":"seal an agreement 指確認協議並令它感覺成為定案。"},{"en":"Two business partners may seal an agreement by signing papers.","zh":"兩名商業夥伴可能透過簽文件確立協議。"},{"en":"Sealing an agreement shows that both sides accept the terms.","zh":"確立協議顯示雙方接受條款。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a deal or promise becomes settled.","zh":"這個短語用於交易或承諾變得確定時。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"property transfer","meaning":"物業轉讓","examples":[{"en":"Kisses could accompany agreements such as property transfers.","zh":"親吻可以伴隨物業轉讓等協議。"},{"en":"Property transfer is the legal passing of land, buildings, or possessions from one person to another.","zh":"property transfer 指土地、建築物或財產由一人合法轉到另一人名下。"},{"en":"A family may need a lawyer for a property transfer after buying a flat.","zh":"家庭買樓後可能需要律師處理物業轉讓。"},{"en":"Property transfers require clear records because ownership is changing.","zh":"物業轉讓需要清楚記錄，因為擁有權正在改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the movement of ownership, not physical movement of a building.","zh":"這個短語指擁有權轉移，而不是建築物實際移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a swift kiss on the cheek","meaning":"快速親吻面頰","examples":[{"en":"A swift kiss on the cheek is a common greeting in many countries.","zh":"快速親吻面頰是許多國家的常見問候。"},{"en":"A swift kiss on the cheek is a quick, light kiss used to greet someone.","zh":"swift kiss on the cheek 指用來問候某人的快速輕吻面頰。"},{"en":"A grandmother may give a child a swift kiss on the cheek before school.","zh":"祖母可能在孩子上學前快速親吻他的面頰。"},{"en":"A quick cheek kiss can show warmth without being long or formal.","zh":"快速貼面吻可以表示溫暖，而不會太久或太正式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a brief social kiss, not a romantic scene.","zh":"這個短語描述短暫社交親吻，而不是浪漫場面。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be known in French as","meaning":"法文稱為……","examples":[{"en":"The cheek kiss is known in French as “la bise”.","zh":"貼面吻在法文中稱為 “la bise”。"},{"en":"To be known in French as something means to have that name in the French language.","zh":"be known in French as something 指在法語中有某個名稱。"},{"en":"The English Channel is known in French as “La Manche”.","zh":"英倫海峽法文稱為 “La Manche”。"},{"en":"Giving the French name can help readers understand the custom in its own culture.","zh":"提供法文名稱可以幫助讀者從其文化中理解該習俗。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a term from French.","zh":"這個短語引入一個法語詞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"standard greeting","meaning":"標準問候方式","examples":[{"en":"La bise is a standard greeting in much of the world.","zh":"La bise 是世界許多地方的標準問候方式。"},{"en":"A standard greeting is a normal and expected way to say hello.","zh":"standard greeting 指正常且被預期的打招呼方式。"},{"en":"In many offices, a handshake is a standard greeting when meeting a client.","zh":"在許多辦公室，與客戶見面時握手是標準問候方式。"},{"en":"Standard greetings reduce awkwardness because people know what to do.","zh":"標準問候方式減少尷尬，因為人們知道該做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the usual social behaviour in a place or group.","zh":"這個短語描述某地或某群體中的慣常社交行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"originate with","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"The word may have originated with the Romans.","zh":"這個詞可能源自羅馬人。"},{"en":"To originate with someone or a group means to begin with them.","zh":"originate with someone or a group 指由某人或某群體開始。"},{"en":"A school tradition may originate with one teacher who started it years ago.","zh":"學校傳統可能源自多年前開始它的一位老師。"},{"en":"When a word originates with an ancient culture, its meaning may change over time.","zh":"當一個詞源自古代文化，其意思可能隨時間改變。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a possible source or beginning.","zh":"這個短語指出可能來源或開端。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have a different term for","meaning":"對每種……有不同名稱","examples":[{"en":"The Romans had a different term for each type of kiss.","zh":"羅馬人對每種親吻有不同名稱。"},{"en":"To have a different term for something means to use a separate word or name for it.","zh":"have a different term for something 指為某事物使用獨立詞語或名稱。"},{"en":"English has different terms for a house, a flat, and a dormitory.","zh":"英語對 house、flat 和 dormitory 有不同名稱。"},{"en":"Different terms can show that a culture notices important distinctions.","zh":"不同名稱可以顯示一種文化注意到重要區分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing vocabulary categories.","zh":"這個短語適合用於比較詞彙分類。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"polite version","meaning":"禮貌形式","examples":[{"en":"The Romans called the polite version of a kiss “basium”.","zh":"羅馬人把親吻的禮貌形式稱為 “basium”。"},{"en":"A polite version is the socially acceptable or respectful form of something.","zh":"polite version 指某事物在社交上可接受或尊重人的形式。"},{"en":"“Could you please help me?” is a polite version of “Help me now.”","zh":"“Could you please help me?” 是 “Help me now.” 的禮貌形式。"},{"en":"A polite version softens behaviour so it fits social expectations.","zh":"禮貌形式會軟化行為，使其符合社交期望。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts acceptable manners with rougher or more intimate forms.","zh":"這個短語把可接受禮儀與較粗魯或較親密形式作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"two kisses are common","meaning":"通常親吻兩次","examples":[{"en":"In Paris, two kisses are common.","zh":"在巴黎，通常親吻兩次。"},{"en":"Two kisses are common means people usually give two cheek kisses in that place.","zh":"two kisses are common 指在某地人們通常給兩次貼面吻。"},{"en":"In some families, two kisses are common when relatives meet at a holiday dinner.","zh":"在一些家庭中，親戚在節日晚餐見面時通常親吻兩次。"},{"en":"Greeting numbers can vary by region, so visitors may feel unsure at first.","zh":"問候次數可以因地區而異，所以遊客起初可能不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a normal local custom.","zh":"這個短語描述正常本地習俗。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"expect three","meaning":"預期有三次","examples":[{"en":"In Provence, visitors may expect three cheek kisses.","zh":"在普羅旺斯，遊客可能預期有三次貼面吻。"},{"en":"To expect three means to be prepared for three of something.","zh":"expect three 指準備好會有三次某事物。"},{"en":"If a teacher says there will be three questions, students expect three tasks on the test.","zh":"如果老師說會有三題，學生就預期測驗有三項任務。"},{"en":"Visitors need to know local greeting rules so they are not surprised.","zh":"遊客需要了解本地問候規則，才不會感到驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what people should be ready for.","zh":"這個短語描述人們應準備面對甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be the norm","meaning":"是慣常做法","examples":[{"en":"Four kisses are the norm in the Loire Valley.","zh":"在羅亞爾河谷，四次親吻是慣常做法。"},{"en":"To be the norm means to be the usual or accepted practice.","zh":"be the norm 指是通常或被接受的做法。"},{"en":"In some schools, wearing uniforms is the norm.","zh":"在一些學校，穿校服是慣常做法。"},{"en":"When something is the norm, people may find alternatives unusual.","zh":"當某事是慣常做法，人們可能覺得其他做法不尋常。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what is normal in a group or place.","zh":"這個短語描述某群體或地方中的正常做法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be customary","meaning":"是習俗","examples":[{"en":"Three cheek kisses are customary in parts of Egypt.","zh":"在埃及部分地區，三次貼面吻是習俗。"},{"en":"To be customary means to be usual because of tradition or local practice.","zh":"be customary 指因傳統或本地做法而成為慣常。"},{"en":"It is customary to remove shoes before entering some homes.","zh":"進入一些家庭前脫鞋是習俗。"},{"en":"Customs can differ between regions, so polite behaviour in one place may not fit another.","zh":"習俗可以因地區而異，所以一地的禮貌行為未必適合另一地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what people traditionally do.","zh":"這個短語描述人們傳統上會做的事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"during the plague","meaning":"在瘟疫期間","examples":[{"en":"Cheek kissing may have stopped during the plague.","zh":"貼面吻可能在瘟疫期間停止。"},{"en":"During the plague means in the period when a serious infectious disease was spreading.","zh":"during the plague 指在嚴重傳染病傳播的時期。"},{"en":"During the plague, people often avoided crowds and close contact.","zh":"在瘟疫期間，人們常避開人群和密切接觸。"},{"en":"Disease outbreaks can interrupt customs that involve touch.","zh":"疾病爆發可以中斷涉及觸碰的習俗。"},{"en":"This phrase places a change within a time of epidemic danger.","zh":"這個短語把改變放在疫症危險時期中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be revived","meaning":"恢復","examples":[{"en":"The custom was revived centuries later.","zh":"這項習俗在數世紀後恢復。"},{"en":"To be revived means to be brought back after disappearing or becoming less common.","zh":"be revived 指在消失或變得較不常見後被重新帶回來。"},{"en":"A school tradition may be revived when former students ask for it to return.","zh":"當舊生要求恢復某活動，學校傳統可能被恢復。"},{"en":"Customs are revived when people decide they still have meaning.","zh":"當人們認為習俗仍有意義，它們就會被恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bringing an old practice back to life.","zh":"這個短語描述把舊做法重新帶回生活中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"after the French Revolution","meaning":"法國大革命後","examples":[{"en":"La bise may have returned after the French Revolution.","zh":"La bise 可能在法國大革命後回歸。"},{"en":"After the French Revolution means in the period following the major political revolution in France.","zh":"after the French Revolution 指法國重大政治革命之後的時期。"},{"en":"After a revolution, social customs may change because ideas about status and equality change.","zh":"革命後，社交習俗可能改變，因為人們對地位和平等的想法改變。"},{"en":"Historical events can make old customs disappear or return with new meanings.","zh":"歷史事件可以令舊習俗消失，或以新意思回歸。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a historical turning point.","zh":"這個短語給出歷史轉捩點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be temporarily paused","meaning":"暫時停止","examples":[{"en":"Cheek kissing was temporarily paused during a public-health scare.","zh":"在公共衞生恐慌期間，貼面吻被暫時停止。"},{"en":"To be temporarily paused means to be stopped for a short period, not forever.","zh":"be temporarily paused 指短時間停止，而不是永久停止。"},{"en":"A school sports day may be temporarily paused when heavy rain begins.","zh":"當大雨開始，學校運動會可能被暫時停止。"},{"en":"Temporary pauses allow people to reduce risk while keeping the option to restart later.","zh":"暫時停止讓人減低風險，同時保留之後重新開始的可能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a short-term stop.","zh":"這個短語描述短期停止。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"swine flu","meaning":"豬流感","examples":[{"en":"Swine flu caused concern about physical greetings in 2009.","zh":"豬流感在 2009 年引起對身體問候的憂慮。"},{"en":"Swine flu is a type of influenza that became a public-health concern.","zh":"swine flu 指一種曾成為公共衞生憂慮的流感。"},{"en":"During a swine flu outbreak, schools may remind students to wash hands often.","zh":"豬流感爆發期間，學校可能提醒學生經常洗手。"},{"en":"Disease outbreaks can change greeting habits because people avoid close contact.","zh":"疾病爆發可以改變問候習慣，因為人們避免密切接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific flu-related health concern.","zh":"這個短語命名一種與流感相關的特定健康憂慮。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"become a concern","meaning":"成為憂慮","examples":[{"en":"Swine flu became a public-health concern.","zh":"豬流感成為公共衞生憂慮。"},{"en":"To become a concern means to start worrying people or requiring attention.","zh":"become a concern 指開始令人擔心或需要關注。"},{"en":"Noise becomes a concern when students cannot concentrate in class.","zh":"當學生無法在課堂集中，噪音就成為憂慮。"},{"en":"A problem becomes a concern when it begins to affect safety, health, or daily life.","zh":"當問題開始影響安全、健康或日常生活，它就成為憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something turning into an issue people must address.","zh":"這個短語描述某事變成人們必須處理的問題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"advise against","meaning":"建議不要……","examples":[{"en":"The French Health Minister advised against cheek kissing.","zh":"法國衞生部長建議不要貼面吻。"},{"en":"To advise against something means to recommend not doing it.","zh":"advise against something 指建議不要做某事。"},{"en":"A doctor may advise against heavy exercise when a patient has a fever.","zh":"醫生可能建議病人發燒時不要做劇烈運動。"},{"en":"People advise against risky behaviour when the possible harm is greater than the benefit.","zh":"當可能傷害大於好處，人們會建議不要做高風險行為。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a warning in the form of advice.","zh":"這個短語以建議形式作出警告。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"coronavirus cases increased","meaning":"冠狀病毒個案增加","examples":[{"en":"The advice was issued as coronavirus cases increased.","zh":"這項建議是在冠狀病毒個案增加時發出的。"},{"en":"Coronavirus cases increased means more people were being confirmed with coronavirus infection.","zh":"coronavirus cases increased 指更多人被確診感染冠狀病毒。"},{"en":"When flu cases increase at school, teachers may ask students to wear masks.","zh":"當學校流感個案增加，老師可能要求學生戴口罩。"},{"en":"Rising case numbers can lead officials to change public-health advice.","zh":"個案數字上升可以令官員改變公共衞生建議。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a growing number of infections.","zh":"這個短語描述感染人數增加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reduction in social contacts","meaning":"減少社交接觸","examples":[{"en":"Officials advised a reduction in social contacts of a physical nature.","zh":"官員建議減少涉及身體接觸的社交接觸。"},{"en":"A reduction in social contacts means fewer meetings or interactions with other people.","zh":"reduction in social contacts 指減少與他人見面或互動。"},{"en":"During an outbreak, a school may ask students to reduce social contact outside class.","zh":"疫症爆發期間，學校可能要求學生減少課外社交接觸。"},{"en":"Reducing contact can slow disease spread when infections pass between people.","zh":"當感染在人與人之間傳播，減少接觸可以減慢疾病擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limiting interaction for safety.","zh":"這個短語描述為安全而限制互動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"of a physical nature","meaning":"涉及身體接觸的","examples":[{"en":"People were advised to reduce contact of a physical nature.","zh":"人們被建議減少涉及身體接觸的接觸。"},{"en":"Of a physical nature means involving touch or the body.","zh":"of a physical nature 指涉及觸碰或身體。"},{"en":"Sports such as rugby involve contact of a physical nature.","zh":"欖球等運動涉及身體接觸。"},{"en":"Physical contact becomes a concern when diseases can spread through touch or closeness.","zh":"當疾病可以透過觸碰或靠近傳播，身體接觸就成為憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase distinguishes body contact from conversation or online communication.","zh":"這個短語把身體接觸與談話或網上溝通區分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"include the practice of","meaning":"包括……的做法","examples":[{"en":"The warning included the practice of la bise.","zh":"警告包括 la bise 這種做法。"},{"en":"To include the practice of something means to mention or cover that custom as part of a wider warning or rule.","zh":"include the practice of something 指在更廣泛警告或規則中提到或涵蓋該習俗。"},{"en":"A school hygiene notice may include the practice of sharing water bottles.","zh":"學校衞生通告可能包括共用水樽的做法。"},{"en":"Including a specific practice helps people know exactly what behaviour to change.","zh":"包括具體做法可以幫助人們清楚知道要改變甚麼行為。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies one example within a broader category.","zh":"這個短語指出較大類別中的一個例子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"behavioural scientist","meaning":"行為科學家","examples":[{"en":"Val Curtis was a behavioural scientist who studied hygiene and contact.","zh":"Val Curtis 是研究衞生和接觸的行為科學家。"},{"en":"A behavioural scientist studies how and why people act in certain ways.","zh":"behavioural scientist 指研究人們如何及為何以某些方式行動的專家。"},{"en":"A behavioural scientist may study why people forget to wash their hands.","zh":"行為科學家可能研究人們為何忘記洗手。"},{"en":"Understanding behaviour helps create better health campaigns and social policies.","zh":"理解行為有助制定更好的健康宣傳和社會政策。"},{"en":"This phrase names an expert in human behaviour.","zh":"這個短語命名研究人類行為的專家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"one possible reason for","meaning":"……的一個可能原因","examples":[{"en":"Trust may be one possible reason for physical greetings.","zh":"信任可能是身體問候的一個可能原因。"},{"en":"One possible reason for something is one explanation that may be true.","zh":"one possible reason for something 指一個可能成立的解釋。"},{"en":"One possible reason for a student’s silence is that they are nervous, not uninterested.","zh":"學生沉默的一個可能原因是緊張，而不是沒有興趣。"},{"en":"Saying “possible” shows that other explanations may also exist.","zh":"說 “possible” 顯示也可能有其他解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a cautious explanation.","zh":"這個短語引入謹慎的解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"signify that","meaning":"表示","examples":[{"en":"A handshake may signify that the other person is trusted.","zh":"握手可能表示對方受到信任。"},{"en":"To signify that means to show, mean, or represent something.","zh":"signify that 指顯示、意味或代表某事。"},{"en":"A green light signifies that cars may move forward.","zh":"綠燈表示汽車可以向前行。"},{"en":"Gestures can signify feelings without words.","zh":"手勢可以不用言語表示感受。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a sign with its meaning.","zh":"這個短語把符號與其意思連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be trusted enough to","meaning":"受到足夠信任去……","examples":[{"en":"The other person may be trusted enough to share close physical contact.","zh":"對方可能受到足夠信任，能分享密切身體接觸。"},{"en":"To be trusted enough to do something means others feel safe allowing that action.","zh":"be trusted enough to do something 指別人感到安全，因此容許某行動。"},{"en":"A babysitter must be trusted enough to look after a child alone.","zh":"保母必須受到足夠信任，才能獨自照顧孩子。"},{"en":"Trust allows people to accept closeness, help, or responsibility.","zh":"信任令人接受親近、幫助或責任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a level of trust that permits an action.","zh":"這個短語描述足以容許某行動的信任程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"share germs","meaning":"互相傳播細菌","examples":[{"en":"Physical greetings can symbolically show a willingness to share germs.","zh":"身體問候可以象徵性地顯示願意互相傳播細菌。"},{"en":"To share germs means to pass bacteria or viruses between people through contact or closeness.","zh":"share germs 指透過接觸或靠近在人與人之間傳播細菌或病毒。"},{"en":"Children may share germs when they drink from the same bottle.","zh":"孩子共用同一個水樽時，可能互相傳播細菌。"},{"en":"Sharing germs can happen even when people are being friendly.","zh":"即使人們表現友好，也可能互相傳播細菌。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the health risk hidden inside close social contact.","zh":"這個短語解釋密切社交接觸中隱藏的健康風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"because of this","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"Because of this, greeting customs change during health crises.","zh":"因此，問候習俗在健康危機期間會改變。"},{"en":"Because of this means for the reason just mentioned.","zh":"because of this 指因為剛提到的原因。"},{"en":"The classroom was too noisy; because of this, the teacher moved the group activity outside.","zh":"課室太嘈；因此，老師把小組活動移到室外。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with a result.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"},{"en":"It helps readers follow the logic from one sentence to the next.","zh":"它幫助讀者跟上句子之間的邏輯。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"go in and out of style","meaning":"時興時不時興","examples":[{"en":"Physical greetings can go in and out of style.","zh":"身體問候可以時興時不時興。"},{"en":"To go in and out of style means to become popular, then unpopular, then possibly popular again.","zh":"go in and out of style 指變得流行，之後不流行，然後可能再次流行。"},{"en":"Certain school bag designs go in and out of style among teenagers.","zh":"某些書包款式在青少年之間會時興時不時興。"},{"en":"Customs may fall out of style during disease outbreaks and return when fear decreases.","zh":"習俗可能在疾病爆發期間不再時興，並在恐懼減少後回歸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing popularity over time.","zh":"這個短語描述流行程度隨時間改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"depending on","meaning":"視乎……","examples":[{"en":"The practice changes depending on public-health concerns.","zh":"這種做法視乎公共衞生憂慮而改變。"},{"en":"Depending on something means being affected or decided by that factor.","zh":"depending on something 指受某因素影響或由其決定。"},{"en":"Students may choose different revision methods depending on the exam format.","zh":"學生可能視乎考試形式選擇不同溫習方法。"},{"en":"When conditions change, behaviour may change depending on the new risks.","zh":"當條件改變，行為可能視乎新風險而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the result is not fixed.","zh":"這個短語顯示結果並非固定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"public-health concerns","meaning":"公共衞生憂慮","examples":[{"en":"Public-health concerns can alter social customs.","zh":"公共衞生憂慮可以改變社交習俗。"},{"en":"Public-health concerns are worries about the health and safety of a whole community.","zh":"public-health concerns 指對整個社群健康和安全的憂慮。"},{"en":"Public-health concerns may lead schools to cancel assemblies during an outbreak.","zh":"公共衞生憂慮可能令學校在疫情期間取消集會。"},{"en":"When public health is at risk, ordinary social behaviour may need to change.","zh":"當公共健康有風險，普通社交行為可能需要改變。"},{"en":"This phrase links health risks with public action.","zh":"這個短語把健康風險與公共行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lament the loss of","meaning":"慨嘆……的消失","examples":[{"en":"Leila Given lamented the loss of older greeting customs.","zh":"Leila Given 慨嘆舊式問候習俗的消失。"},{"en":"To lament the loss of something means to express sadness that it has disappeared.","zh":"lament the loss of something 指表達對某事消失的悲傷。"},{"en":"Older residents may lament the loss of small local shops after a mall opens.","zh":"商場開幕後，年長居民可能慨嘆小型本地商店的消失。"},{"en":"People lament a loss when they feel something valuable has been replaced or forgotten.","zh":"當人們覺得有價值的東西被取代或遺忘，就會慨嘆其消失。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses regret and sadness about change.","zh":"這個短語表達對改變的遺憾和傷感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the last generation’s customs","meaning":"上一代的習俗","examples":[{"en":"She described the last generation’s customs of greeting.","zh":"她描述了上一代的問候習俗。"},{"en":"The last generation’s customs are habits and traditions practised by people before the current generation.","zh":"last generation’s customs 指當代之前那一代人實踐的習慣和傳統。"},{"en":"A grandparent may explain the last generation’s customs of writing letters and visiting neighbours.","zh":"祖父母可能解釋上一代寫信和探訪鄰居的習俗。"},{"en":"Customs can change quickly when technology, health concerns, or social values change.","zh":"當科技、健康憂慮或社會價值改變，習俗可以快速轉變。"},{"en":"This phrase compares older habits with present-day behaviour.","zh":"這個短語把舊習慣與現代行為作比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"finger-tipping","meaning":"指尖相碰的問候方式","examples":[{"en":"Finger-tipping involved touching only the fingertips.","zh":"指尖相碰的問候方式只涉及觸碰指尖。"},{"en":"Finger-tipping is a greeting where people lightly touch fingertips instead of fully shaking hands.","zh":"finger-tipping 指人們輕觸指尖，而不是完整握手的問候方式。"},{"en":"A cautious person may prefer finger-tipping when they want to avoid full hand contact.","zh":"謹慎的人若想避免完整手部接觸，可能偏好指尖相碰。"},{"en":"Because it involves less contact, finger-tipping may spread fewer germs than a full handshake.","zh":"因為接觸較少，指尖相碰可能比完整握手傳播較少細菌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lighter, more limited form of touch greeting.","zh":"這個短語描述較輕、較有限的觸碰式問候。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"high handshake","meaning":"高舉式握手","examples":[{"en":"The high handshake was an older form of greeting.","zh":"高舉式握手是一種較舊的問候方式。"},{"en":"A high handshake is a greeting where the hands are raised higher than in an ordinary handshake.","zh":"high handshake 指雙手比普通握手舉得更高的問候方式。"},{"en":"Old photographs may show people using a high handshake in formal social settings.","zh":"舊照片可能顯示人們在正式社交場合使用高舉式握手。"},{"en":"Unusual greeting forms can disappear when one simpler custom becomes dominant.","zh":"當一種較簡單習俗變得主導，不尋常問候形式可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an older variation of handshaking.","zh":"這個短語指握手的一種舊式變體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in favour of","meaning":"被……取代","examples":[{"en":"Older customs disappeared in favour of the ordinary handshake.","zh":"舊習俗消失，被普通握手取代。"},{"en":"In favour of something means choosing or supporting it instead of another option.","zh":"in favour of something 指選擇或支持某事，而不是另一選項。"},{"en":"A school may stop printed notices in favour of email messages.","zh":"學校可能停止紙本通告，改用電郵訊息。"},{"en":"When one practice is chosen in favour of another, the older one may become rare.","zh":"當一種做法被選中而取代另一種，舊做法可能變得少見。"},{"en":"This phrase shows replacement or preference.","zh":"這個短語顯示取代或偏好。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"agents of bacterial transfer","meaning":"傳播細菌的媒介","examples":[{"en":"Hands can act as agents of bacterial transfer.","zh":"雙手可以作為傳播細菌的媒介。"},{"en":"Agents of bacterial transfer are things that help bacteria move from one person or surface to another.","zh":"agents of bacterial transfer 指幫助細菌從一個人或表面移到另一個人或表面的東西。"},{"en":"Door handles can act as agents of bacterial transfer when many people touch them.","zh":"當很多人觸碰門柄，門柄可以成為傳播細菌的媒介。"},{"en":"If hands are not washed, they can carry bacteria to food, faces, and other people.","zh":"如果沒有洗手，雙手可以把細菌帶到食物、臉和其他人身上。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how germs travel through contact.","zh":"這個短語解釋細菌如何透過接觸傳播。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cite early studies","meaning":"引用早期研究","examples":[{"en":"The nurse cited early studies on the spread of germs.","zh":"這名護士引用了關於細菌傳播的早期研究。"},{"en":"To cite early studies means to mention older research as evidence.","zh":"cite early studies 指提及較早研究作為證據。"},{"en":"A student may cite early studies when writing a report about sleep and memory.","zh":"學生寫關於睡眠和記憶的報告時，可能引用早期研究。"},{"en":"Citing studies makes an argument stronger because it shows support from research.","zh":"引用研究令論點更有力，因為它顯示有研究支持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using previous research to back up a claim.","zh":"這個短語描述用以往研究支持一項說法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"easily spread germs","meaning":"容易傳播細菌","examples":[{"en":"A handshake can easily spread germs.","zh":"握手可以容易傳播細菌。"},{"en":"To easily spread germs means to pass bacteria or viruses to others with little difficulty.","zh":"easily spread germs 指很容易把細菌或病毒傳給別人。"},{"en":"Children can easily spread germs when they share snacks without washing hands.","zh":"孩子未洗手就分享零食時，可以容易傳播細菌。"},{"en":"Germs spread more easily when many people touch the same surfaces.","zh":"當很多人觸碰同一表面，細菌更容易傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a simple action can create a health risk.","zh":"這個短語提醒一個簡單行動可以造成健康風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in conclusion","meaning":"總括而言","examples":[{"en":"In conclusion, she recommended a contact-free greeting.","zh":"總括而言，她建議使用非接觸式問候。"},{"en":"In conclusion means finally, after considering the main points.","zh":"in conclusion 指最後，在考慮主要重點之後。"},{"en":"In conclusion, a student may summarise the strongest reason in an essay.","zh":"總括而言，學生可能在文章中總結最強理由。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the writer or speaker is ending an argument.","zh":"這個短語表示作者或說話者正在結束論點。"},{"en":"It helps readers recognise the final judgement or recommendation.","zh":"它幫助讀者辨認最終判斷或建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"adopt a custom","meaning":"採用一項習俗","examples":[{"en":"She recommended that Americans adopt a different greeting custom.","zh":"她建議美國人採用另一種問候習俗。"},{"en":"To adopt a custom means to start using a habit or tradition.","zh":"adopt a custom 指開始使用某個習慣或傳統。"},{"en":"A school may adopt a custom of greeting visitors at the door.","zh":"學校可能採用在門口迎接訪客的習俗。"},{"en":"Customs are adopted when people believe they are useful, polite, or meaningful.","zh":"當人們相信習俗有用、禮貌或有意義，就會採用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking up a practice as one’s own.","zh":"這個短語描述把一種做法納為己用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"shake one’s own hands together","meaning":"雙手互握作揖","examples":[{"en":"The Chinese custom involved shaking one’s own hands together.","zh":"這項中國習俗涉及雙手互握作揖。"},{"en":"To shake one’s own hands together means to clasp or move one’s own hands as a greeting instead of touching another person.","zh":"shake one’s own hands together 指用自己的雙手互握或移動作問候，而不是觸碰他人。"},{"en":"During a health scare, people may shake their own hands together to greet others without contact.","zh":"在健康恐慌期間，人們可能雙手互握作揖，以無接觸方式問候他人。"},{"en":"This greeting keeps politeness while avoiding direct physical touch.","zh":"這種問候保留禮貌，同時避免直接身體接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a self-contained gesture rather than a handshake with another person.","zh":"這個短語描述自我完成的姿態，而不是與他人握手。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"at least","meaning":"至少","examples":[{"en":"At least this greeting would keep each person’s bacteria to themselves.","zh":"至少這種問候會讓每個人的細菌留在自己身上。"},{"en":"At least means no less than this, or used to show one small positive point.","zh":"at least 指不少於這個程度，或用來指出一個小好處。"},{"en":"The bus is late, but at least the station has seats and shelter.","zh":"巴士遲到，但至少車站有座位和遮蔽。"},{"en":"This phrase can soften a bad situation by pointing out one benefit.","zh":"這個短語可以透過指出一個好處來緩和壞情況。"},{"en":"It often means “if nothing else, this good thing is true”.","zh":"它常表示「即使沒有其他好處，至少這件好事是真的」。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stay at home","meaning":"留在自己身上","examples":[{"en":"She joked that people’s bacteria would then stay at home.","zh":"她開玩笑說，人們的細菌之後會留在自己身上。"},{"en":"Stay at home means remain with oneself or in one’s own place, rather than going elsewhere.","zh":"stay at home 指留在自己那裡或自己的地方，而不是去別處。"},{"en":"During illness, students should stay at home so they do not infect classmates.","zh":"生病期間，學生應留在家中，以免感染同學。"},{"en":"In the joke, bacteria “stay at home” because they are not passed to another person.","zh":"在這個笑話中，細菌「留在自己身上」，因為它們沒有傳給別人。"},{"en":"This phrase is used literally for people and humorously here for germs.","zh":"這個短語可字面用於人，在這裡則幽默地用於細菌。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"agree with the information","meaning":"與資料相符","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether each statement agrees with the text.","zh":"學生判斷每個陳述是否與文本資料相符。"},{"en":"To agree with the information means to match what the passage says.","zh":"agree with the information 指符合文章所說內容。"},{"en":"If a passage says handshakes spread germs, a similar statement agrees with the information.","zh":"如果文章說握手會傳播細菌，相似的陳述就與資料相符。"},{"en":"Students should choose TRUE only when the text clearly supports the statement.","zh":"只有當文本清楚支持陳述時，學生才應選 TRUE。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in TRUE, FALSE and NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於 TRUE、FALSE 和 NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A false statement contradicts the information in the passage.","zh":"錯誤陳述與文章資料矛盾。"},{"en":"To contradict the information means to say the opposite of what the passage says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說法與文章內容相反。"},{"en":"If the text says nearly a quarter, a statement saying exactly half contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文本說接近四分之一，而陳述說正好一半，就是與資料矛盾。"},{"en":"Students should choose FALSE only when there is clear disagreement with the text.","zh":"只有在與文本明確不一致時，學生才應選 FALSE。"},{"en":"This phrase describes direct conflict with the source.","zh":"這個短語描述與來源直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"there is no information on this","meaning":"沒有相關資料","examples":[{"en":"Choose “NOT GIVEN” when the passage gives no information on the statement.","zh":"當文章沒有關於該陳述的資料時，選 “NOT GIVEN”。"},{"en":"There is no information on this means the text does not say whether the statement is true or false.","zh":"there is no information on this 指文本沒有說明該陳述是真還是假。"},{"en":"If a passage discusses handshakes but not children’s greetings, there is no information on children’s greetings.","zh":"如果文章討論握手，但沒有提到兒童問候，就沒有兒童問候的相關資料。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when the passage gives no evidence.","zh":"當文章沒有證據時，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"This phrase explains when NOT GIVEN is the correct answer.","zh":"這個短語解釋何時 NOT GIVEN 是正確答案。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"an indicator of hospitality","meaning":"好客的表示","examples":[{"en":"A physical greeting can sometimes be interpreted as an indicator of hospitality.","zh":"身體問候有時可被理解為好客的表示。"},{"en":"An indicator of hospitality is a sign that someone is welcoming and friendly to guests.","zh":"indicator of hospitality 指顯示某人歡迎並友善對待客人的象徵。"},{"en":"Offering tea to visitors can be an indicator of hospitality in many homes.","zh":"在許多家庭中，向訪客奉茶可以是好客的表示。"},{"en":"Warm greetings make guests feel accepted and comfortable.","zh":"熱情問候令客人感到被接納和舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that shows a welcoming attitude.","zh":"這個短語描述顯示歡迎態度的事物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"start as a sign of peace","meaning":"起初是和平的象徵","examples":[{"en":"A popular theory suggests that handshaking started as a sign of peace.","zh":"一種流行理論認為握手起初是和平的象徵。"},{"en":"To start as a sign of peace means to begin as a way of showing friendly intentions.","zh":"start as a sign of peace 指最初作為顯示友好意圖的方式。"},{"en":"Two classmates may shake hands after an argument as a sign of peace.","zh":"兩名同學爭執後可能握手，作為和平的象徵。"},{"en":"A peaceful sign can reduce fear because it shows no wish to fight.","zh":"和平象徵可以減少恐懼，因為它顯示沒有打鬥意圖。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a possible first purpose of a gesture.","zh":"這個短語解釋一個姿態可能的最初目的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"roll up one’s sleeves","meaning":"捲起衣袖","examples":[{"en":"The passage does not say that people rolled up their sleeves.","zh":"文章沒有說人們捲起衣袖。"},{"en":"To roll up one’s sleeves means to fold sleeves upward so the lower arms are uncovered.","zh":"roll up one’s sleeves 指把衣袖向上摺起，露出前臂。"},{"en":"A cook may roll up their sleeves before washing dishes.","zh":"廚師洗碗前可能捲起衣袖。"},{"en":"In reading questions, students must check whether such details are actually stated.","zh":"在閱讀題中，學生必須檢查這類細節是否真的有提及。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal, though it may also suggest preparing to work hard.","zh":"這個短語可以是字面意思，也可以表示準備努力工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in different situations","meaning":"在不同情況下","examples":[{"en":"The meaning of a handshake varies in different situations.","zh":"握手的意思在不同情況下會有所不同。"},{"en":"In different situations means depending on the context or circumstances.","zh":"in different situations 指視乎語境或情況而定。"},{"en":"A smile can mean politeness, nervousness, or happiness in different situations.","zh":"微笑在不同情況下可以表示禮貌、緊張或快樂。"},{"en":"Context changes meaning because the same action can serve different purposes.","zh":"語境會改變意思，因為同一行動可以有不同目的。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds students not to interpret a gesture too simply.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生不要過度簡單地解讀姿態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be difficult to predict","meaning":"難以預測","examples":[{"en":"A gesture with many meanings can be difficult to predict or interpret.","zh":"有多種意思的姿態可能難以預測或詮釋。"},{"en":"To be difficult to predict means to be hard to know in advance.","zh":"be difficult to predict 指難以事先知道。"},{"en":"A student’s result may be difficult to predict if their practice scores go up and down.","zh":"如果學生練習分數忽高忽低，成績可能難以預測。"},{"en":"When a sign has several meanings, people may not know what it will communicate.","zh":"當一個符號有幾種意思，人們可能不知道它會傳達甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uncertainty about what will happen or what something means.","zh":"這個短語描述對將會發生甚麼或某事意思的不確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"become prevalent","meaning":"變得普及","examples":[{"en":"Handshakes became prevalent in America partly through Quaker influence.","zh":"握手在美國變得普及，部分是受貴格會影響。"},{"en":"To become prevalent means to become common or widespread.","zh":"become prevalent 指變得常見或廣泛。"},{"en":"Online payments became prevalent when shops and customers found them convenient.","zh":"當商店和顧客都覺得方便，網上付款變得普及。"},{"en":"A behaviour becomes prevalent when many people copy it and treat it as normal.","zh":"當許多人模仿某行為並把它視為正常，它就會變得普及。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practice spreading widely.","zh":"這個短語描述一種做法廣泛傳播。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"represent equality","meaning":"代表平等","examples":[{"en":"The handshake represented equality more clearly than formal bows.","zh":"握手比正式鞠躬更清楚代表平等。"},{"en":"To represent equality means to symbolise equal status between people.","zh":"represent equality 指象徵人與人之間的平等地位。"},{"en":"A round table can represent equality because no one sits at the head.","zh":"圓桌可以代表平等，因為沒有人坐在主位。"},{"en":"Equal symbols reduce social distance and make people feel respected.","zh":"平等象徵會減少社交距離，令人感到受尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an action or object carrying the idea of fairness.","zh":"這個短語描述承載公平概念的行動或物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"exactly 25 per cent","meaning":"正好25%","examples":[{"en":"The research reported nearly, rather than exactly, 25 per cent.","zh":"研究報告的是接近，而不是正好 25%。"},{"en":"Exactly 25 per cent means precisely one quarter, with no approximation.","zh":"exactly 25 per cent 指精確地四分之一，並非約數。"},{"en":"If exactly 25 per cent of a class is absent, 5 out of 20 students are missing.","zh":"如果一班正好 25% 缺席，即 20 名學生中有 5 人缺席。"},{"en":"In reading tasks, “nearly” and “exactly” are not the same.","zh":"在閱讀題中，“nearly” 和 “exactly” 並不相同。"},{"en":"This phrase warns students to notice precise numerical wording.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生注意精確數字措辭。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"smell one’s hands","meaning":"嗅自己的手","examples":[{"en":"Some participants smelled their hands after a handshake.","zh":"有些參加者在握手後嗅自己的手。"},{"en":"To smell one’s hands means to bring the hands near the nose and notice their scent.","zh":"smell one’s hands 指把手靠近鼻子並留意其氣味。"},{"en":"A cook may smell their hands after cutting garlic.","zh":"廚師切完蒜後可能嗅自己的手。"},{"en":"People may smell their hands to check whether a scent has been left there.","zh":"人們可能嗅自己的手，以檢查是否留下氣味。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple act of checking smell.","zh":"這個短語描述檢查氣味的簡單動作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"spot poisonous chemicals","meaning":"察覺有毒化學物","examples":[{"en":"The researchers did not claim that people were trying to spot poisonous chemicals.","zh":"研究人員沒有聲稱人們試圖察覺有毒化學物。"},{"en":"To spot poisonous chemicals means to notice or identify harmful chemical substances.","zh":"spot poisonous chemicals 指注意到或識別有害化學物質。"},{"en":"A lab worker may use special tests to spot poisonous chemicals in water.","zh":"實驗室工作人員可能使用特別測試來察覺水中的有毒化學物。"},{"en":"Without equipment, ordinary people usually cannot identify dangerous chemicals accurately.","zh":"沒有設備時，普通人通常不能準確識別危險化學物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes detecting harmful substances, not simply smelling a hand.","zh":"這個短語描述偵測有害物質，而不只是嗅手。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words from the passage.","zh":"學生使用文章中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill in missing words so the summary makes sense.","zh":"complete the summary 指填入缺失字詞，使摘要意思完整。"},{"en":"A student should read the whole summary before choosing answers.","zh":"學生在選答案前應閱讀整段摘要。"},{"en":"Grammar and meaning both help decide which word fits each gap.","zh":"文法和意思都幫助判斷哪個詞適合每個空格。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common instruction in reading exams.","zh":"這個短語是閱讀考試中的常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"no more than three words and/or a number","meaning":"不超過三個字及／或一個數字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer may contain no more than three words and/or a number.","zh":"每個答案可包含不超過三個字及／或一個數字。"},{"en":"No more than three words and/or a number means the answer must not exceed three words, though one number may be included.","zh":"no more than three words and/or a number 指答案不得超過三個詞，並可包括一個數字。"},{"en":"“two cheek kisses” fits the limit because it has three words and a number idea.","zh":"“two cheek kisses” 符合限制，因為它有三個詞並包含數字概念。"},{"en":"Writing extra words can lose marks even when the meaning is right.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫多餘字詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a strict answer-length rule.","zh":"這個短語給出嚴格答案長度規則。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the history of cheek kissing","meaning":"貼面吻的歷史","examples":[{"en":"The summary describes the history of cheek kissing.","zh":"摘要描述貼面吻的歷史。"},{"en":"The history of cheek kissing means how cheek kissing began, changed, disappeared, or returned over time.","zh":"history of cheek kissing 指貼面吻如何開始、改變、消失或隨時間回歸。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to trace the history of a custom from ancient times to today.","zh":"老師可能要求學生追溯一項習俗由古代至今天的歷史。"},{"en":"Studying history shows that greetings can change with religion, law, health, and culture.","zh":"研究歷史顯示問候方式可以隨宗教、法律、健康和文化而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the development of cheek kissing across time.","zh":"這個短語著重貼面吻跨時間的發展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"show fidelity","meaning":"表示忠誠","examples":[{"en":"In the Middle Ages, a kiss could show fidelity.","zh":"在中世紀，親吻可以表示忠誠。"},{"en":"To show fidelity means to show loyalty, faithfulness, or commitment.","zh":"show fidelity 指顯示忠誠、信守或承諾。"},{"en":"A promise to stay with a friend during trouble can show fidelity.","zh":"承諾在朋友困難時陪伴他，可以表示忠誠。"},{"en":"Symbols of fidelity reassure others that a relationship or agreement is serious.","zh":"忠誠象徵令別人相信關係或協議是認真的。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in relationships, religion, and promises.","zh":"這個短語常用於關係、宗教和承諾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"exchange kisses","meaning":"互相親吻","examples":[{"en":"People in Paris commonly exchange two cheek kisses.","zh":"巴黎人通常互相親吻面頰兩次。"},{"en":"To exchange kisses means two people kiss each other as part of a greeting or custom.","zh":"exchange kisses 指兩人作為問候或習俗互相親吻。"},{"en":"Relatives may exchange kisses when they meet at a family dinner.","zh":"親戚在家庭晚餐見面時可能互相親吻。"},{"en":"Exchanging kisses can show warmth, but it may be avoided during illness outbreaks.","zh":"互相親吻可以表示溫暖，但在疾病爆發期間可能被避免。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mutual kissing, not one-sided action.","zh":"這個短語描述互相親吻，而不是單方面行動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"remain suspended for","meaning":"持續暫停……","examples":[{"en":"The custom may have remained suspended for several centuries.","zh":"這項習俗可能持續暫停了幾個世紀。"},{"en":"To remain suspended for a period means to stay stopped or inactive during that time.","zh":"remain suspended for a period 指在某段時間內保持停止或不活動。"},{"en":"A school club may remain suspended for a year if no teacher can supervise it.","zh":"如果沒有老師能監督，學校學會可能暫停一年。"},{"en":"A suspended custom can return later if people decide to revive it.","zh":"暫停的習俗如果人們決定恢復，之後可以回歸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a long temporary stop.","zh":"這個短語描述長時間暫停。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"because of swine flu","meaning":"因為豬流感","examples":[{"en":"Cheek kissing was paused because of swine flu concerns.","zh":"由於對豬流感的憂慮，貼面吻被暫停。"},{"en":"Because of swine flu means due to worries or problems caused by swine flu.","zh":"because of swine flu 指由豬流感造成的憂慮或問題所致。"},{"en":"A school may cancel a trip because of flu cases among students.","zh":"學校可能因為學生中有流感個案而取消旅行。"},{"en":"Health concerns can stop social customs because people want to reduce infection risk.","zh":"健康憂慮可以停止社交習俗，因為人們想減少感染風險。"},{"en":"This phrase gives swine flu as the cause.","zh":"這個短語指出豬流感是原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"write answers to","meaning":"寫出……的答案","examples":[{"en":"Students write short answers to the final questions.","zh":"學生寫出最後問題的簡短答案。"},{"en":"To write answers to questions means to record responses to those questions.","zh":"write answers to questions 指把對問題的回答寫下來。"},{"en":"In a reading test, students should write answers to questions using only the passage.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，學生應只使用文章來寫出問題答案。"},{"en":"Writing clear answers prevents lost marks from spelling or grammar confusion.","zh":"寫出清楚答案可以避免因串字或文法混亂而失分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the act of responding in written form.","zh":"這個短語描述以書面形式作答。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"advise people to avoid","meaning":"建議人們避免……","examples":[{"en":"The minister advised people to avoid physical greetings.","zh":"部長建議人們避免身體問候。"},{"en":"To advise people to avoid something means to recommend that they not do it.","zh":"advise people to avoid something 指建議人們不要做某事。"},{"en":"A doctor may advise people to avoid crowded places during a serious outbreak.","zh":"醫生可能建議人們在嚴重疫情期間避免擠迫地方。"},{"en":"Advice to avoid contact is meant to reduce risk, not insult others.","zh":"建議避免接觸是為了減少風險，而不是冒犯他人。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a cautious recommendation.","zh":"這個短語給出謹慎建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"prevent the spread of","meaning":"防止……傳播","examples":[{"en":"Reducing physical contact may help prevent the spread of infection.","zh":"減少身體接觸可能有助防止感染傳播。"},{"en":"To prevent the spread of something means to stop it from moving to more people or places.","zh":"prevent the spread of something 指阻止某事傳到更多人或地方。"},{"en":"Washing hands can help prevent the spread of germs in a classroom.","zh":"洗手可以幫助防止課室中細菌傳播。"},{"en":"If people stay home when sick, they reduce the chance of spreading illness.","zh":"如果人們生病時留在家中，就會減少傳播疾病的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in public-health advice.","zh":"這個短語常用於公共衞生建議。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be transferred through","meaning":"可透過……傳播","examples":[{"en":"Bacteria can be transferred through a handshake.","zh":"細菌可透過握手傳播。"},{"en":"To be transferred through something means to be passed from one person, place, or surface to another by that method.","zh":"be transferred through something 指透過某方法從一個人、地方或表面傳到另一個。"},{"en":"Ink can be transferred through touch if a student holds a wet pen.","zh":"如果學生拿着未乾的筆，墨水可以透過觸碰轉移。"},{"en":"Germs are transferred through contact when people touch contaminated hands or objects.","zh":"當人們觸碰受污染的手或物件，細菌會透過接觸傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the route by which something moves.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事物移動的途徑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 172 - Why Do We Touch Strangers So Much? A History Of The Handshake Offers Clues.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 173":[{"front":"mite harvestman","meaning":"蟎盲蛛","examples":[{"en":"Few people have heard of the mite harvestman.","zh":"很少人聽說過蟎盲蛛。"},{"en":"A mite harvestman is a tiny arachnid related to daddy longlegs.","zh":"蟎盲蛛是一種細小的蛛形綱動物，與長腳蛛有親緣關係。"},{"en":"A biology student might need a microscope or a trained guide to identify a mite harvestman.","zh":"生物學生可能需要顯微鏡或受過訓練的嚮導，才能辨認蟎盲蛛。"},{"en":"Because the mite harvestman is so small and well hidden, it is difficult for ordinary people to notice.","zh":"因為蟎盲蛛非常細小又善於隱藏，普通人很難注意到牠。"},{"en":"The phrase names a rare, tiny animal, not a mite or an ordinary spider.","zh":"這個短語命名一種稀有細小動物，不是蟎，也不是普通蜘蛛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hear of","meaning":"聽說過……","examples":[{"en":"Few people have heard of this unusual arachnid.","zh":"很少人聽說過這種不尋常的蛛形綱動物。"},{"en":"To hear of something means to know that it exists because someone mentioned it or you read about it.","zh":"hear of something 指因有人提及或自己讀過而知道某事物存在。"},{"en":"A student may hear of a new scholarship from a teacher before seeing the official notice.","zh":"學生可能在看到正式通知前，先從老師口中聽說過新獎學金。"},{"en":"If few people have heard of an animal, it is probably not widely known to the public.","zh":"如果很少人聽說過某種動物，它很可能不為大眾熟知。"},{"en":"The phrase is about awareness, not hearing a sound directly.","zh":"這個短語關於知道某事，而不是直接聽到聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fewer still","meaning":"更少人會……","examples":[{"en":"Few people know the animal, and fewer still would recognise it nearby.","zh":"很少人認識這種動物，而更少人會在附近認出牠。"},{"en":"Fewer still means an even smaller number of people or things than the number just mentioned.","zh":"fewer still 指比剛才提到的數量更少的人或事物。"},{"en":"Many students have heard of the exam, but fewer still know its exact format.","zh":"許多學生聽說過這個考試，但更少人知道其確切格式。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises that the second group is smaller and rarer.","zh":"這個短語強調第二個群體更小、更少見。"},{"en":"It is useful when moving from uncommon to even more uncommon.","zh":"它適合用於由少見轉向更少見的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"recognise at close range","meaning":"近距離辨認","examples":[{"en":"Even trained observers may fail to recognise it at close range.","zh":"即使受過訓練的觀察者，也可能無法近距離辨認牠。"},{"en":"To recognise something at close range means to identify it even when it is very near.","zh":"recognise something at close range 指即使某物很近，也能辨認出它。"},{"en":"A student may recognise a bird at close range if she has studied its colours and shape.","zh":"如果學生學過鳥的顏色和形狀，她可能能近距離辨認某種鳥。"},{"en":"If an animal still cannot be recognised nearby, it must be very well camouflaged or very small.","zh":"如果動物在附近仍不能被辨認，它一定非常善於偽裝或非常細小。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses difficulty in identification, not distance from the object.","zh":"這個短語強調辨認困難，而不是物件距離遠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"arachnid","meaning":"蛛形綱動物","examples":[{"en":"The mite harvestman is a tiny arachnid.","zh":"蟎盲蛛是一種細小的蛛形綱動物。"},{"en":"An arachnid is an animal group that includes spiders, scorpions, ticks, and harvestmen.","zh":"arachnid 指包括蜘蛛、蠍子、蜱和盲蛛在內的一類動物。"},{"en":"A biology teacher may explain that an arachnid is not an insect because it has different body features.","zh":"生物老師可能解釋蛛形綱動物不是昆蟲，因為牠們有不同身體特徵。"},{"en":"Knowing that an animal is an arachnid helps students place it in the right scientific group.","zh":"知道某動物是蛛形綱動物，有助學生把它放入正確科學分類。"},{"en":"The word refers to a class of joint-legged animals, not only spiders.","zh":"這個詞指一類節肢動物，而不只是蜘蛛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a relative of","meaning":"……的近親","examples":[{"en":"The mite harvestman is a relative of the daddy longlegs.","zh":"蟎盲蛛是長腳蛛的近親。"},{"en":"A relative of an animal is another animal that belongs to a related biological group.","zh":"a relative of an animal 指屬於相關生物群的另一種動物。"},{"en":"A wolf is a relative of the domestic dog because they share evolutionary ancestry.","zh":"狼是家犬的近親，因為牠們有共同演化祖先。"},{"en":"Knowing that two animals are relatives helps scientists compare their body structures and history.","zh":"知道兩種動物是近親，有助科學家比較牠們的身體結構和歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase shows biological connection, not family relationship in the human sense.","zh":"這個短語表示生物學上的聯繫，而不是人類意義上的親屬關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"daddy longlegs","meaning":"長腳蛛；盲蛛","examples":[{"en":"The daddy longlegs is more familiar than the mite harvestman.","zh":"長腳蛛比蟎盲蛛更為人熟悉。"},{"en":"Daddy longlegs is a common name for certain long-legged arachnids.","zh":"daddy longlegs 是某些長腳蛛形綱動物的常見名稱。"},{"en":"A child may notice a daddy longlegs walking across a garden wall because its legs are so long.","zh":"孩子可能因牠的腳很長，而注意到一隻長腳蛛走過花園牆。"},{"en":"Compared with daddy longlegs, mite harvestmen are much harder to spot.","zh":"與長腳蛛相比，蟎盲蛛難發現得多。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and refers to a familiar long-legged creature.","zh":"這個短語較口語，指一種熟悉的長腳生物。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"stubby rather than long","meaning":"短粗而非修長","examples":[{"en":"Its legs are stubby rather than long.","zh":"牠的腳短粗而非修長。"},{"en":"Stubby rather than long means short and thick instead of long and thin.","zh":"stubby rather than long 指短而粗，而不是長而幼。"},{"en":"A pencil becomes stubby rather than long after being sharpened many times.","zh":"鉛筆被削很多次後，會變得短粗而不是修長。"},{"en":"This contrast helps readers imagine the animal as compact, not like a typical long-legged harvestman.","zh":"這個對比幫助讀者想像這種動物很短小結實，而不是典型長腳盲蛛。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly compares two opposite shapes.","zh":"這個短語清楚比較兩種相反形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as big as","meaning":"與……一樣大","examples":[{"en":"Its body is only as big as a sesame seed.","zh":"牠的身體只有芝麻一樣大。"},{"en":"As big as means the same size as something else.","zh":"as big as 指與另一物件大小相同。"},{"en":"A small tablet may be as big as a coin, so it is easy to carry.","zh":"小藥片可能與硬幣一樣大，所以容易攜帶。"},{"en":"Comparing size with a familiar object helps readers imagine something tiny.","zh":"用熟悉物件比較大小，有助讀者想像某物多細小。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to make size easy to understand.","zh":"這個短語用來令大小容易理解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sesame seed","meaning":"芝麻","examples":[{"en":"The animal’s body is about the size of a sesame seed.","zh":"這種動物的身體大約像一粒芝麻般大小。"},{"en":"A sesame seed is a very small seed often used on bread, snacks, or Asian food.","zh":"sesame seed 指常用於麵包、小食或亞洲食物上的非常細小種子。"},{"en":"A teacher may compare a tiny insect to a sesame seed so students can imagine its size.","zh":"老師可能把細小昆蟲比作芝麻，讓學生想像其大小。"},{"en":"If an animal is only the size of a sesame seed, it can easily disappear among soil or leaves.","zh":"如果動物只有芝麻大小，它很容易在泥土或葉子中消失。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a familiar image for something extremely small.","zh":"這個短語用熟悉圖像表達極細小的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dark, humid forests","meaning":"陰暗潮濕的森林","examples":[{"en":"Scientists search for the animals in dark, humid forests.","zh":"科學家在陰暗潮濕的森林中尋找這些動物。"},{"en":"Dark, humid forests are forests with little light and a lot of moisture in the air.","zh":"dark, humid forests 指光線少、空氣中水分很多的森林。"},{"en":"After rain, a forest floor may become dark and humid, making it suitable for small hidden animals.","zh":"下雨後，森林地面可能變得陰暗潮濕，適合細小隱蔽動物生活。"},{"en":"Such conditions help tiny creatures avoid drying out and stay concealed.","zh":"這種環境幫助細小生物避免乾燥並保持隱藏。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a damp, shaded habitat.","zh":"這個短語描述潮濕而陰暗的棲息地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sift through","meaning":"仔細翻查；篩查","examples":[{"en":"Researchers sift through leaf litter to find the animals.","zh":"研究人員仔細翻查落葉層，以找到這些動物。"},{"en":"To sift through something means to search carefully through many small pieces or details.","zh":"sift through something 指在許多細小物件或細節中仔細搜尋。"},{"en":"A student may sift through old notes to find one useful example for an essay.","zh":"學生可能仔細翻查舊筆記，為作文找一個有用例子。"},{"en":"When an animal is tiny and hidden, researchers must sift through material slowly and patiently.","zh":"當動物細小又隱蔽，研究人員必須慢慢而耐心地篩查材料。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests careful searching, not a quick look.","zh":"這個短語暗示仔細搜尋，而不是快速看一眼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"leaf litter","meaning":"落葉層","examples":[{"en":"Mite harvestmen hide among the leaf litter.","zh":"蟎盲蛛藏在落葉層之中。"},{"en":"Leaf litter is the layer of dead leaves and small plant material on the forest floor.","zh":"leaf litter 指森林地面上一層枯葉和小植物材料。"},{"en":"A child walking in autumn may hear dry leaf litter crackle underfoot.","zh":"孩子在秋天走路時，可能聽到乾落葉層在腳下沙沙作響。"},{"en":"Leaf litter can protect tiny animals by hiding them from predators and sunlight.","zh":"落葉層可以把細小動物藏起來，使牠們避開捕食者和陽光。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to fallen plant material, not rubbish made by people.","zh":"這個短語指掉落的植物材料，而不是人類製造的垃圾。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"respond by becoming motionless","meaning":"以靜止不動作出反應","examples":[{"en":"The animals respond to danger by becoming motionless.","zh":"這些動物以靜止不動來回應危險。"},{"en":"To respond by becoming motionless means to react by staying completely still.","zh":"respond by becoming motionless 指透過完全不動來作出反應。"},{"en":"A frightened child may freeze in place when a large dog suddenly runs toward him.","zh":"當一隻大狗突然跑向孩子時，受驚孩子可能僵在原地。"},{"en":"Remaining motionless can help a small animal avoid being noticed by a predator.","zh":"保持靜止可以幫助細小動物避免被捕食者注意。"},{"en":"The phrase describes stillness as a defensive reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述把靜止作為防禦反應。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"impossible to pick out","meaning":"幾乎無法辨認出來","examples":[{"en":"Their appearance makes them almost impossible to pick out.","zh":"牠們的外貌令牠們幾乎無法被辨認出來。"},{"en":"Impossible to pick out means extremely difficult to notice or identify among surrounding things.","zh":"impossible to pick out 指在周圍事物中極難注意到或辨認出來。"},{"en":"A brown button may be impossible to pick out if it falls onto a dark wooden floor.","zh":"如果棕色鈕扣掉在深色木地板上，可能幾乎無法辨認出來。"},{"en":"Camouflage can make an animal blend into its surroundings so well that observers miss it.","zh":"偽裝可以令動物與環境融為一體，使觀察者看不見牠。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses visual difficulty in finding something.","zh":"這個短語強調尋找某物時的視覺困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"trained eye","meaning":"受過訓練的眼睛；專業眼光","examples":[{"en":"Even a trained eye may fail to notice the animal.","zh":"即使受過訓練的眼睛也可能留意不到這種動物。"},{"en":"A trained eye is the ability of an experienced person to notice details that others miss.","zh":"trained eye 指有經驗的人能注意到別人看漏的細節。"},{"en":"A trained eye can spot grammar mistakes that a beginner overlooks.","zh":"專業眼光可以發現初學者忽略的文法錯誤。"},{"en":"If even a trained eye misses something, it must be very well hidden or subtle.","zh":"如果即使專業眼光也看漏某物，它一定非常隱蔽或微妙。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to expert observation, not literally a different kind of eye.","zh":"這個短語指專家觀察力，而不是字面上不同的眼睛。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"grains of dirt","meaning":"泥土顆粒","examples":[{"en":"The animals look like tiny grains of dirt.","zh":"這些動物看起來像細小泥土顆粒。"},{"en":"Grains of dirt are very small pieces of soil or dust.","zh":"grains of dirt 指非常細小的泥土或塵埃顆粒。"},{"en":"A tiny seed on the floor may look like a grain of dirt until someone looks closely.","zh":"地上的小種子在細看前可能像一粒泥土。"},{"en":"If an animal resembles dirt, predators and researchers may both overlook it.","zh":"如果動物像泥土，捕食者和研究人員都可能忽略牠。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a concrete image of something small and easily missed.","zh":"這個短語用具體圖像表達細小而容易看漏的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"invertebrate biologist","meaning":"無脊椎動物生物學家","examples":[{"en":"Gonzalo Giribet is an invertebrate biologist.","zh":"Gonzalo Giribet 是無脊椎動物生物學家。"},{"en":"An invertebrate biologist is a scientist who studies animals without backbones.","zh":"invertebrate biologist 指研究沒有脊骨動物的科學家。"},{"en":"An invertebrate biologist may study insects, worms, spiders, or tiny sea creatures.","zh":"無脊椎動物生物學家可能研究昆蟲、蠕蟲、蜘蛛或細小海洋生物。"},{"en":"Because many invertebrates are small, researchers often need careful collecting methods.","zh":"因為許多無脊椎動物很細小，研究人員通常需要仔細採集方法。"},{"en":"The phrase names a scientist who studies a huge group of animals.","zh":"這個短語命名研究龐大動物群的科學家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"spend years doing something","meaning":"花多年時間做某事","examples":[{"en":"The researchers spent six years searching for mite harvestmen.","zh":"研究人員花了六年時間尋找蟎盲蛛。"},{"en":"To spend years doing something means to use many years on one activity or goal.","zh":"spend years doing something 指用許多年在同一活動或目標上。"},{"en":"A writer may spend years researching a historical novel before writing the first chapter.","zh":"作家可能花多年時間研究歷史小說，才開始寫第一章。"},{"en":"Long projects often require patience because useful results do not appear quickly.","zh":"長期項目通常需要耐性，因為有用結果不會很快出現。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the amount of time and effort involved.","zh":"這個短語強調所涉及的時間和努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on five continents","meaning":"在五大洲","examples":[{"en":"The team searched for the animals on five continents.","zh":"團隊在五大洲尋找這些動物。"},{"en":"On five continents means in five of the world’s major land areas.","zh":"on five continents 指在世界主要陸地區域中的五個大洲。"},{"en":"A company may sell the same product on five continents if it has a global market.","zh":"如果公司有全球市場，它可能在五大洲銷售同一產品。"},{"en":"Searching on several continents suggests the research was wide-ranging and international.","zh":"在幾個大洲搜尋，顯示研究範圍廣泛且具國際性。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises geographical scale.","zh":"這個短語強調地理規模。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"extraordinary story to tell","meaning":"有非凡的故事可揭示","examples":[{"en":"The animals have an extraordinary geological story to tell.","zh":"這些動物有一個非凡的地質故事可揭示。"},{"en":"An extraordinary story to tell means something contains surprising information worth explaining.","zh":"extraordinary story to tell 指某事物包含值得解釋的驚人資訊。"},{"en":"An old family photo may have an extraordinary story to tell about migration and survival.","zh":"一張舊家庭照片可能有關於移民和生存的非凡故事可揭示。"},{"en":"If an animal’s distribution reveals ancient continental movement, its story becomes scientifically important.","zh":"如果動物分布揭示古代大陸移動，其故事就變得有科學重要性。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests hidden meaning behind something ordinary-looking.","zh":"這個短語暗示普通外表背後有隱藏意義。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"carry a record of","meaning":"保存……的記錄","examples":[{"en":"The species carry a record of ancient geological history.","zh":"這些物種保存古代地質歷史的記錄。"},{"en":"To carry a record of something means to preserve evidence or traces of it.","zh":"carry a record of something 指保存某事的證據或痕跡。"},{"en":"Tree rings carry a record of past droughts and good growing years.","zh":"樹木年輪保存過去乾旱和良好生長年份的記錄。"},{"en":"If a species stays in one area for millions of years, its DNA may record ancient events.","zh":"如果物種在某地停留數百萬年，其 DNA 可能記錄古代事件。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence being stored inside something.","zh":"這個短語描述證據被保存在某物之內。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hundreds of millions of years","meaning":"數億年","examples":[{"en":"Their history extends over hundreds of millions of years.","zh":"牠們的歷史延續了數億年。"},{"en":"Hundreds of millions of years means an extremely long period measured in several hundred million years.","zh":"hundreds of millions of years 指以數億年計的極長時間。"},{"en":"Fossils can show changes that happened over hundreds of millions of years.","zh":"化石可以顯示數億年間發生的變化。"},{"en":"Such a long timescale allows continents to move, collide, and separate.","zh":"如此漫長的時間尺度容許大陸移動、碰撞和分裂。"},{"en":"The phrase is used for deep geological time, not human history.","zh":"這個短語用於深層地質時間，而不是人類歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"geological history","meaning":"地質歷史","examples":[{"en":"The animals preserve evidence of geological history.","zh":"這些動物保存地質歷史的證據。"},{"en":"Geological history is the history of Earth’s rocks, landmasses, oceans, and physical changes.","zh":"geological history 指地球岩石、大陸塊、海洋和物理變化的歷史。"},{"en":"A mountain range can reveal geological history through its folded rocks.","zh":"山脈可以透過摺曲岩層揭示地質歷史。"},{"en":"Species distribution may reflect geological history if animals moved with ancient continents.","zh":"如果動物隨古代大陸移動，物種分布可能反映地質歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase connects living things with Earth’s physical past.","zh":"這個短語把生物與地球物理過去連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"chronicle the journeys of","meaning":"記錄……的變遷歷程","examples":[{"en":"Their distribution chronicles the journeys of the continents.","zh":"牠們的分布記錄了大陸的變遷歷程。"},{"en":"To chronicle the journeys of something means to record or reveal how it moved over time.","zh":"chronicle the journeys of something 指記錄或揭示某物如何隨時間移動。"},{"en":"Old ship logs chronicle the journeys of traders across the ocean.","zh":"舊船日誌記錄商人橫越海洋的旅程。"},{"en":"If related species live on separated continents, their locations can reveal continental movement.","zh":"如果相關物種生活在分離的大洲上，牠們的位置可以揭示大陸移動。"},{"en":"The phrase treats scientific evidence like a historical record.","zh":"這個短語把科學證據視為歷史記錄。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"landmasses","meaning":"大陸塊","examples":[{"en":"The Earth’s landmasses have repeatedly moved and separated.","zh":"地球的大陸塊曾反覆移動和分離。"},{"en":"Landmasses are large continuous areas of land, such as continents or major continental blocks.","zh":"landmasses 指大片連續陸地，例如大洲或主要大陸板塊。"},{"en":"Australia and Africa are examples of major landmasses.","zh":"澳洲和非洲都是主要大陸塊的例子。"},{"en":"When landmasses separate, populations of animals and plants may become isolated.","zh":"當大陸塊分離，動植物種群可能變得孤立。"},{"en":"The word focuses on large pieces of land, not small islands or fields.","zh":"這個詞重點是大片陸地，而不是小島或田地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"collide and break apart","meaning":"碰撞並分裂","examples":[{"en":"Continents have collided and broken apart several times.","zh":"大陸曾多次碰撞並分裂。"},{"en":"To collide and break apart means to crash together and later separate into pieces.","zh":"collide and break apart 指撞在一起，之後分離成不同部分。"},{"en":"Two pieces of ice may collide and break apart in a fast river.","zh":"兩塊冰可能在急流中碰撞並分裂。"},{"en":"When continents collide and break apart, they can carry species to new positions.","zh":"當大陸碰撞並分裂，它們可以把物種帶到新位置。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both joining and later separation.","zh":"這個短語同時描述結合和之後分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"carry animals and plants with them","meaning":"把動植物一同帶走","examples":[{"en":"Moving continents carried animals and plants with them.","zh":"移動的大陸把動植物一同帶走。"},{"en":"To carry animals and plants with them means to move living things along as landmasses shift.","zh":"carry animals and plants with them 指當大陸塊移動時，把生物一同移動。"},{"en":"If a floating log carries insects with it, the insects move without flying or swimming far.","zh":"如果漂浮木頭把昆蟲一同帶走，昆蟲不用飛或游很遠也能移動。"},{"en":"Continental movement can explain why related species appear on distant lands.","zh":"大陸移動可以解釋為何相關物種出現在相距遙遠的土地上。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that species may move passively with their habitat.","zh":"這個短語顯示物種可能隨棲息地被動移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"provide clues to","meaning":"為……提供線索","examples":[{"en":"These species provide clues to the continents’ former positions.","zh":"這些物種為大陸過去的位置提供線索。"},{"en":"To provide clues to something means to give evidence that helps explain or discover it.","zh":"provide clues to something 指提供有助解釋或發現某事的證據。"},{"en":"A student’s repeated mistakes provide clues to which grammar rule she does not understand.","zh":"學生反覆出錯可以提供線索，顯示她不明白哪條文法規則。"},{"en":"Species distribution can provide clues to where continents were joined in the past.","zh":"物種分布可以提供線索，顯示大陸過去在哪裡相連。"},{"en":"The phrase describes indirect evidence that helps solve a problem.","zh":"這個短語描述有助解決問題的間接證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"continents’ paths","meaning":"大陸的移動路徑","examples":[{"en":"Biologists use species to reconstruct the continents’ paths.","zh":"生物學家利用物種重建大陸的移動路徑。"},{"en":"Continents’ paths are the routes or movements continents have taken over geological time.","zh":"continents’ paths 指大陸在地質時間中走過的路線或移動。"},{"en":"A map animation can show the paths of continents as they drift apart.","zh":"地圖動畫可以顯示大陸漂離時的移動路徑。"},{"en":"If living species match ancient land connections, they help reveal those paths.","zh":"如果現存物種符合古代陸地連接，它們可以幫助揭示那些路徑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long-term movement of landmasses.","zh":"這個短語描述大陸塊的長期移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"notion of continental drift","meaning":"大陸漂移的概念","examples":[{"en":"The notion of continental drift developed partly from biological evidence.","zh":"大陸漂移的概念部分源自生物證據。"},{"en":"The notion of continental drift is the idea that continents move slowly over time.","zh":"notion of continental drift 指大陸會隨時間慢慢移動的想法。"},{"en":"Similar fossils on distant continents helped scientists consider this notion seriously.","zh":"遠隔大陸上相似化石幫助科學家認真考慮這個概念。"},{"en":"If continents drift, species that once lived together can end up far apart.","zh":"如果大陸漂移，曾經生活在一起的物種可能最終相隔很遠。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the concept before or during its scientific development.","zh":"這個短語指該科學想法形成前或形成中的概念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"continental drift","meaning":"大陸漂移","examples":[{"en":"Continental drift changed the distribution of many species.","zh":"大陸漂移改變了許多物種的分布。"},{"en":"Continental drift is the slow movement of continents across Earth’s surface over geological time.","zh":"continental drift 指大陸在地質時間中於地球表面慢慢移動。"},{"en":"A science teacher may use puzzle-like maps to explain continental drift.","zh":"科學老師可能用拼圖般的地圖解釋大陸漂移。"},{"en":"As continents move apart, related species can become separated by oceans.","zh":"隨着大陸分離，相關物種可能被海洋隔開。"},{"en":"The phrase explains large-scale land movement and its biological effects.","zh":"這個短語解釋大規模陸地移動及其生物影響。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"originally come from","meaning":"最初源自……","examples":[{"en":"The theory originally came from clues found in fossils.","zh":"該理論最初源自化石中的線索。"},{"en":"To originally come from something means to have that thing as the first source or origin.","zh":"originally come from something 指以某事作為最初來源或起源。"},{"en":"A school rule may originally come from a safety problem that happened years ago.","zh":"學校規則可能最初源自多年前發生的一次安全問題。"},{"en":"Knowing where an idea originally came from helps explain why it was taken seriously.","zh":"知道一個想法最初源自何處，有助解釋為何它受到重視。"},{"en":"The phrase points to the starting source of an idea.","zh":"這個短語指出一個想法的起始來源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be struck by the fact that","meaning":"對……這個事實印象深刻","examples":[{"en":"Wegener was struck by the fact that similar fossils appeared on both sides of the Atlantic.","zh":"Wegener 對相似化石出現在大西洋兩邊這個事實印象深刻。"},{"en":"To be struck by the fact that means to be strongly impressed or surprised by a particular fact.","zh":"be struck by the fact that 指對某個事實感到強烈印象或驚訝。"},{"en":"A teacher may be struck by the fact that many students made the same unusual mistake.","zh":"老師可能對許多學生犯同一個不尋常錯誤這個事實印象深刻。"},{"en":"A striking fact can lead someone to ask a new research question.","zh":"令人印象深刻的事實可以引導人提出新的研究問題。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a fact caught someone’s attention strongly.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事實強烈吸引了某人的注意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fossils of similar species","meaning":"相似物種的化石","examples":[{"en":"Fossils of similar species were found on different continents.","zh":"相似物種的化石在不同大洲被發現。"},{"en":"Fossils of similar species are preserved remains of related ancient organisms.","zh":"fossils of similar species 指相關古代生物保存下來的遺骸或痕跡。"},{"en":"A museum may display fossils of similar species to show how animals changed over time.","zh":"博物館可能展示相似物種的化石，以顯示動物如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"Finding similar fossils far apart can suggest that the land was once connected.","zh":"在遠隔地方找到相似化石，可能暗示土地曾經相連。"},{"en":"The phrase links fossil evidence with evolutionary and geological history.","zh":"這個短語把化石證據與演化及地質歷史連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on either side of","meaning":"在……兩邊","examples":[{"en":"Similar fossils appeared on either side of the Atlantic.","zh":"相似化石出現在大西洋兩邊。"},{"en":"On either side of something means on both sides of it.","zh":"on either side of something 指在某物的兩邊。"},{"en":"Shops on either side of a narrow street may share the same customers.","zh":"狹窄街道兩邊的商店可能共享同一批顧客。"},{"en":"If similar evidence appears on either side of an ocean, scientists may wonder whether the lands were once joined.","zh":"如果相似證據出現在海洋兩邊，科學家可能會思考陸地是否曾經相連。"},{"en":"The phrase describes two positions separated by something between them.","zh":"這個短語描述被中間某物隔開的兩個位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the Atlantic","meaning":"大西洋","examples":[{"en":"The Atlantic separated populations of similar ancient species.","zh":"大西洋分隔了相似古代物種的種群。"},{"en":"The Atlantic is the ocean between the Americas and Europe and Africa.","zh":"the Atlantic 指位於美洲與歐洲、非洲之間的海洋。"},{"en":"A flight from London to New York crosses the Atlantic.","zh":"從倫敦飛往紐約的航班會橫越大西洋。"},{"en":"If similar species are found on both sides of the Atlantic, their history may be very old.","zh":"如果相似物種出現在大西洋兩邊，牠們的歷史可能非常古老。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a major ocean barrier.","zh":"這個短語指主要海洋屏障。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"too big for someone to","meaning":"太大，以致某人無法……","examples":[{"en":"The ocean was too big for the animals to cross unaided.","zh":"海洋太大，以致這些動物無法獨自橫越。"},{"en":"Too big for someone to do something means the size or difficulty is beyond their ability.","zh":"too big for someone to do something 指大小或難度超出某人的能力。"},{"en":"The box was too heavy for one student to carry alone.","zh":"箱子太重，以致一名學生無法獨自搬動。"},{"en":"If an ocean is too large for an animal to cross, another explanation is needed for its distribution.","zh":"如果海洋大得令動物無法橫越，就需要另一個解釋牠的分布。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why an action was not possible.","zh":"這個短語解釋某行動為何不可能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"travel across on their own","meaning":"自行橫越","examples":[{"en":"The species could not have travelled across the ocean on their own.","zh":"這些物種不可能自行橫越海洋。"},{"en":"To travel across on their own means to move from one side to the other without help.","zh":"travel across on their own 指在沒有幫助下從一邊移動到另一邊。"},{"en":"A child may be too young to travel across the city on her own.","zh":"孩子可能太年幼，不能自行橫越城市。"},{"en":"If animals cannot travel across an ocean alone, their presence on both sides may suggest old land connections.","zh":"如果動物不能獨自橫越海洋，牠們在兩邊出現可能暗示古老陸地連接。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses independent movement without outside support.","zh":"這個短語強調沒有外部支援的獨立移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"speculate correctly","meaning":"作出正確推測","examples":[{"en":"Wegener speculated correctly that the continents had once been joined.","zh":"Wegener 正確推測大陸曾經連接在一起。"},{"en":"To speculate correctly means to make a reasoned guess that later turns out to be true.","zh":"speculate correctly 指作出有根據的猜測，而之後證明為真。"},{"en":"A teacher may speculate correctly that students are confused because the instructions are unclear.","zh":"老師可能正確推測學生困惑是因為指示不清。"},{"en":"Correct speculation can become important when later evidence supports it.","zh":"當之後證據支持，正確推測可以變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an educated guess that proves accurate.","zh":"這個短語描述後來證明準確的有根據猜測。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"as it turned out","meaning":"結果證明","examples":[{"en":"As it turned out, Wegener’s main idea was correct.","zh":"結果證明，Wegener 的主要想法是正確的。"},{"en":"As it turned out means the final result showed something different or confirmed something later.","zh":"as it turned out 指最終結果顯示某事不同，或後來確認某事。"},{"en":"I thought the test would be easy; as it turned out, the final question was very difficult.","zh":"我以為測驗會很容易；結果證明，最後一題非常困難。"},{"en":"The phrase often introduces what was discovered after more information became available.","zh":"這個短語常引入更多資料出現後的發現。"},{"en":"It helps contrast earlier uncertainty with later knowledge.","zh":"它幫助對比早前不確定與後來知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be welded together","meaning":"連接在一起","examples":[{"en":"The continents had originally been welded together.","zh":"大陸原本曾連接在一起。"},{"en":"To be welded together means to be joined tightly into one connected piece.","zh":"be welded together 指被牢固連接成一個相連整體。"},{"en":"Two metal bars can be welded together to make a stronger frame.","zh":"兩條金屬棒可以被焊接在一起，形成更堅固框架。"},{"en":"If continents were once welded together, species could spread across them without crossing oceans.","zh":"如果大陸曾經連接在一起，物種就能不用橫越海洋而擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase is metaphorical here and means firmly connected.","zh":"這裏的短語是比喻，意思是牢固相連。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"single landmass","meaning":"單一大陸塊","examples":[{"en":"Pangea was a single enormous landmass.","zh":"盤古大陸是一個巨大的單一大陸塊。"},{"en":"A single landmass is one continuous area of land rather than separate continents.","zh":"single landmass 指一片連續陸地，而不是分開的大洲。"},{"en":"A large island is a single landmass surrounded by water.","zh":"大島是一塊被水包圍的單一陸地。"},{"en":"If the continents once formed a single landmass, animals could move across regions now separated by oceans.","zh":"如果大洲曾形成單一大陸塊，動物就能穿越如今被海洋分隔的地區。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one connected piece of land.","zh":"這個短語描述一塊相連陸地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Pangea","meaning":"盤古大陸","examples":[{"en":"Pangea later broke apart into separate continents.","zh":"盤古大陸後來分裂成不同大洲。"},{"en":"Pangea was the ancient supercontinent that once joined most of Earth’s land together.","zh":"Pangea 指古代超大陸，曾把地球大部分陸地連在一起。"},{"en":"A geography teacher may use Pangea to explain why coastlines and fossils seem to match.","zh":"地理老師可能用盤古大陸解釋為何海岸線和化石似乎互相吻合。"},{"en":"When Pangea broke apart, species were carried into different regions.","zh":"當盤古大陸分裂，物種被帶到不同地區。"},{"en":"The word names a major ancient landmass in Earth’s history.","zh":"這個詞命名地球歷史中的主要古代大陸塊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"plate tectonics","meaning":"板塊構造","examples":[{"en":"Continental drift is scientifically known as plate tectonics.","zh":"大陸漂移在科學上稱為板塊構造。"},{"en":"Plate tectonics is the scientific theory that Earth’s outer shell is divided into moving plates.","zh":"plate tectonics 指地球外殼分成移動板塊的科學理論。"},{"en":"Earthquakes and volcanoes often occur where tectonic plates meet.","zh":"地震和火山常發生在板塊交界處。"},{"en":"Plate tectonics explains how continents move, collide, and separate over time.","zh":"板塊構造解釋大陸如何隨時間移動、碰撞和分離。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the scientific framework behind continental drift.","zh":"這個短語提供大陸漂移背後的科學框架。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be scientifically known as","meaning":"在科學上稱為……","examples":[{"en":"Continental drift is scientifically known as plate tectonics.","zh":"大陸漂移在科學上稱為板塊構造。"},{"en":"To be scientifically known as something means to have that formal name in science.","zh":"be scientifically known as something 指在科學中有某個正式名稱。"},{"en":"What people call “shooting stars” are scientifically known as meteors.","zh":"人們稱為「流星」的東西，在科學上稱為 meteors。"},{"en":"Scientific names make communication clearer among researchers.","zh":"科學名稱令研究人員之間的溝通更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase links a common idea with its formal scientific term.","zh":"這個短語把常見概念與正式科學術語連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"move species around the world","meaning":"令物種分布至世界各地","examples":[{"en":"Plate tectonics helped move species around the world.","zh":"板塊構造幫助令物種分布至世界各地。"},{"en":"To move species around the world means to change where species live on a global scale.","zh":"move species around the world 指在全球層面改變物種生活地點。"},{"en":"Human trade can move species around the world when insects travel inside cargo.","zh":"人類貿易可以在昆蟲藏於貨物中時，把物種帶到世界各地。"},{"en":"Continental movement can move species without the animals actively travelling long distances.","zh":"大陸移動可以在動物沒有主動長途移動下改變牠們的分布。"},{"en":"The phrase describes large-scale changes in species distribution.","zh":"這個短語描述物種分布的大規模變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"armadillos and their relatives","meaning":"犰狳及其近親","examples":[{"en":"Armadillos and their relatives occur in both Africa and South America.","zh":"犰狳及其近親出現在非洲和南美洲。"},{"en":"Armadillos and their relatives are animals in related groups that share evolutionary ancestry.","zh":"armadillos and their relatives 指有共同演化祖先的相關動物群。"},{"en":"A zoo guide may compare armadillos and their relatives to explain animal families.","zh":"動物園導賞員可能比較犰狳及其近親，以解釋動物家族。"},{"en":"Their distribution can help scientists understand past continental connections.","zh":"牠們的分布可以幫助科學家理解過去的大陸連接。"},{"en":"The phrase groups one familiar animal with related species.","zh":"這個短語把一種熟悉動物與相關物種歸為一組。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ancestors evolved","meaning":"祖先演化","examples":[{"en":"Their ancestors evolved when the continents were still joined.","zh":"牠們的祖先在大陸仍連接時演化。"},{"en":"Ancestors evolved means earlier forms of a species developed over time.","zh":"ancestors evolved 指某物種較早期形態隨時間發展。"},{"en":"Humans’ ancestors evolved long before modern cities and written language existed.","zh":"人類祖先早在現代城市和文字語言出現前已演化。"},{"en":"If ancestors evolved before continents separated, descendants may now live far apart.","zh":"如果祖先在大陸分離前已演化，後代現在可能相距很遠。"},{"en":"The phrase connects evolutionary development with past time.","zh":"這個短語把演化發展與過去時間連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be joined","meaning":"連接在一起","examples":[{"en":"Africa and South America were once joined.","zh":"非洲和南美洲曾經連接在一起。"},{"en":"To be joined means to be connected together as one piece or system.","zh":"be joined 指連接成一個整體或系統。"},{"en":"Two classrooms may be joined by opening a folding wall between them.","zh":"兩間課室可能透過打開中間摺牆而連接在一起。"},{"en":"If continents were once joined, animals could move between them without crossing an ocean.","zh":"如果大陸曾經連接，動物就能不用橫越海洋而在兩地之間移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes physical connection.","zh":"這個短語描述實體連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"spread north","meaning":"向北擴散","examples":[{"en":"Armadillos spread north after the American continents connected.","zh":"在美洲大陸連接後，犰狳向北擴散。"},{"en":"To spread north means to move or expand into areas further north.","zh":"spread north 指移動或擴展到更北的地區。"},{"en":"A plant species may spread north if warmer weather allows it to survive there.","zh":"如果天氣變暖令植物能在北方存活，該植物可能向北擴散。"},{"en":"When land connections form, animals may expand their range in new directions.","zh":"當陸地連接形成，動物可能向新方向擴展分布範圍。"},{"en":"The phrase describes directional expansion.","zh":"這個短語描述有方向性的擴展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"biogeographers","meaning":"生物地理學家","examples":[{"en":"Biogeographers study the geographic distribution of living things.","zh":"生物地理學家研究生物的地理分布。"},{"en":"Biogeographers are scientists who study where organisms live and why they are found there.","zh":"biogeographers 指研究生物生活在哪裡以及為何出現在那裡的科學家。"},{"en":"A biogeographer may ask why one frog species lives on one island but not another.","zh":"生物地理學家可能問為何某種青蛙生活在一個島上，而不在另一個島上。"},{"en":"Their work connects biology, geography, evolution, and geology.","zh":"他們的工作連接生物學、地理學、演化和地質學。"},{"en":"The word names researchers who study life across space.","zh":"這個詞命名研究生命空間分布的研究人員。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"compare related species","meaning":"比較相關物種","examples":[{"en":"Scientists compare related species to study continental movement.","zh":"科學家比較相關物種來研究大陸移動。"},{"en":"To compare related species means to examine similarities and differences among species with shared ancestry.","zh":"compare related species 指檢視有共同祖先物種之間的相似和差異。"},{"en":"A biology class may compare related species of birds by looking at their beaks and songs.","zh":"生物課可能透過觀察鳥喙和鳴聲比較相關鳥類。"},{"en":"Similarities between distant species can reveal when their ancestors separated.","zh":"遠隔物種之間的相似性可以揭示其祖先何時分離。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a method for studying evolution and geography.","zh":"這個短語描述研究演化和地理的方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"recognise cases where","meaning":"辨認……的情況","examples":[{"en":"Researchers must recognise cases where species spread independently.","zh":"研究人員必須辨認物種獨立擴散的情況。"},{"en":"To recognise cases where something happens means to identify examples of that situation.","zh":"recognise cases where something happens 指辨認某情況的例子。"},{"en":"A teacher must recognise cases where students guess correctly without understanding the rule.","zh":"老師必須辨認學生只是猜對而不是理解規則的情況。"},{"en":"If scientists mistake independent spread for continental drift, their conclusions may be wrong.","zh":"如果科學家把獨立擴散誤認為大陸漂移，結論可能錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses careful identification of different explanations.","zh":"這個短語強調仔細辨認不同解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"spread for other reasons","meaning":"因其他原因擴散","examples":[{"en":"Some species spread for reasons unrelated to continental drift.","zh":"有些物種因與大陸漂移無關的其他原因擴散。"},{"en":"To spread for other reasons means to expand because of causes different from the main explanation.","zh":"spread for other reasons 指因不同於主要解釋的原因而擴展。"},{"en":"A rumour may spread for other reasons, such as fear or curiosity, not because it is true.","zh":"謠言可能因恐懼或好奇等其他原因擴散，而不是因為它真實。"},{"en":"Some animals spread because they fly, float, or are carried by humans.","zh":"有些動物因會飛、漂浮或被人類帶走而擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that one pattern may have more than one possible cause.","zh":"這個短語提醒一種模式可能有不止一個原因。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cross great stretches of water","meaning":"橫越大片水域","examples":[{"en":"Some animals can cross great stretches of water.","zh":"有些動物能橫越大片水域。"},{"en":"To cross great stretches of water means to travel across large areas of sea, lake, or ocean.","zh":"cross great stretches of water 指穿越大片海、湖或海洋。"},{"en":"Birds may cross great stretches of water during migration.","zh":"鳥類遷徙期間可能橫越大片水域。"},{"en":"Animals that can cross water easily may not preserve clear evidence of ancient land connections.","zh":"能輕易橫越水域的動物，未必保存清晰的古代陸地連接證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes long-distance movement over water.","zh":"這個短語描述跨水域長距離移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be home to","meaning":"是……的棲息地","examples":[{"en":"Hawaii was once home to a giant flightless goose.","zh":"夏威夷曾是巨型不會飛的鵝的棲息地。"},{"en":"To be home to a species means to be a place where that species lives or once lived.","zh":"be home to a species 指某地是或曾是某物種生活的地方。"},{"en":"A city park may be home to bats, frogs, and many kinds of birds.","zh":"城市公園可能是蝙蝠、青蛙和多種鳥類的棲息地。"},{"en":"If a habitat is home to rare animals, protecting it becomes important.","zh":"如果棲息地是稀有動物的家，保護它就變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a place as a habitat.","zh":"這個短語把某地描述為棲息地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"giant flightless goose","meaning":"巨型不會飛的鵝","examples":[{"en":"Hawaii once had a giant flightless goose.","zh":"夏威夷曾有一種巨型不會飛的鵝。"},{"en":"A giant flightless goose is a large goose-like bird that cannot fly.","zh":"giant flightless goose 指一種大型、像鵝但不能飛的鳥。"},{"en":"Island birds sometimes become flightless when there are few predators and little need to escape.","zh":"當島上捕食者很少且不太需要逃走，島嶼鳥類有時會變得不會飛。"},{"en":"Flightless birds can be vulnerable if new predators or humans arrive.","zh":"如果新捕食者或人類到達，不會飛的鳥可能很脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both large size and loss of flying ability.","zh":"這個短語同時描述巨大體型和失去飛行能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"become extinct","meaning":"滅絕","examples":[{"en":"The Hawaiian goose eventually became extinct.","zh":"夏威夷鵝最終滅絕。"},{"en":"To become extinct means to disappear completely, with no living members left.","zh":"become extinct 指完全消失，沒有任何存活成員。"},{"en":"A plant can become extinct if its habitat is destroyed and no seeds survive.","zh":"如果植物棲息地被破壞且沒有種子存活，它可能滅絕。"},{"en":"Island species may become extinct quickly when new predators arrive.","zh":"當新捕食者到達，島嶼物種可能迅速滅絕。"},{"en":"The phrase describes final loss, not temporary rarity.","zh":"這個短語描述最終消失，而不是暫時稀少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"DNA extracted from","meaning":"從……提取的DNA","examples":[{"en":"Scientists studied DNA extracted from the bird’s bones.","zh":"科學家研究從鳥骨中提取的 DNA。"},{"en":"DNA extracted from something is genetic material taken out of a sample for study.","zh":"DNA extracted from something 指從樣本中取出的遺傳物質，用於研究。"},{"en":"A forensic scientist may study DNA extracted from a hair found at a crime scene.","zh":"法證科學家可能研究從犯罪現場頭髮中提取的 DNA。"},{"en":"DNA from bones can reveal relationships between extinct and living species.","zh":"來自骨骼的 DNA 可以揭示滅絕物種與現存物種之間的關係。"},{"en":"The phrase describes taking genetic evidence from a physical source.","zh":"這個短語描述從實體來源取得遺傳證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"evolve from","meaning":"由……演化而來","examples":[{"en":"The Hawaiian bird evolved from the Canada goose.","zh":"夏威夷鳥由加拿大雁演化而來。"},{"en":"To evolve from something means to develop over time from an earlier form or ancestor.","zh":"evolve from something 指隨時間由較早形態或祖先發展而來。"},{"en":"Modern domestic dogs evolved from wolf-like ancestors.","zh":"現代家犬由類似狼的祖先演化而來。"},{"en":"If an island bird evolved from a flying ancestor, its body may change after many generations.","zh":"如果島嶼鳥類由會飛祖先演化而來，牠的身體可能經許多世代後改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evolutionary origin.","zh":"這個短語描述演化起源。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"colonise Hawaii","meaning":"在夏威夷建立種群","examples":[{"en":"The ancestor of the bird colonised Hawaii.","zh":"這種鳥的祖先在夏威夷建立種群。"},{"en":"To colonise Hawaii means to arrive in Hawaii and establish a living population there.","zh":"colonise Hawaii 指到達夏威夷並在那裏建立可生存種群。"},{"en":"A plant can colonise a new island if its seeds arrive and grow successfully.","zh":"如果植物種子到達新島並成功生長，它就能在該島建立種群。"},{"en":"Once a species colonises an island, isolation may lead it to evolve in unusual ways.","zh":"一旦物種在島上建立種群，隔離可能令它以不尋常方式演化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes biological settlement, not political colonisation here.","zh":"這裏的短語描述生物定居，而不是政治殖民。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"branch off from","meaning":"從……分化出來","examples":[{"en":"The island population branched off from the original species.","zh":"島嶼種群從原本物種分化出來。"},{"en":"To branch off from something means to separate from it and develop in a different direction.","zh":"branch off from something 指從某事物分離，並向不同方向發展。"},{"en":"A small study group may branch off from a larger class to focus on speaking practice.","zh":"小型學習小組可能從大班分出來，集中練習口語。"},{"en":"When a population is isolated, it can branch off and become a new species over time.","zh":"當種群被隔離，它可以隨時間分化並成為新物種。"},{"en":"The phrase uses the image of a branch growing away from a trunk.","zh":"這個短語使用樹枝從樹幹長出的意象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lose the ability to fly","meaning":"失去飛行能力","examples":[{"en":"The goose eventually lost the ability to fly.","zh":"這種鵝最終失去飛行能力。"},{"en":"To lose the ability to fly means to change so that flight is no longer possible.","zh":"lose the ability to fly 指身體改變後不再能飛行。"},{"en":"Some island birds lose the ability to fly when walking becomes enough for survival.","zh":"有些島嶼鳥類在步行已足以生存時會失去飛行能力。"},{"en":"If a bird loses flight, it may become more vulnerable to predators.","zh":"如果鳥類失去飛行能力，它可能更容易受捕食者威脅。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a major evolutionary change in movement.","zh":"這個短語描述移動方式上的重大演化改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"half a million years ago","meaning":"五十萬年前","examples":[{"en":"This evolutionary change occurred about half a million years ago.","zh":"這次演化變化大約發生在五十萬年前。"},{"en":"Half a million years ago means about 500,000 years before the present.","zh":"half a million years ago 指距今約五十萬年。"},{"en":"A fossil dated to half a million years ago comes from a time far before recorded history.","zh":"被定年為五十萬年前的化石，來自有文字歷史以前很久的時期。"},{"en":"Such a timescale is long enough for major evolutionary changes to occur.","zh":"這樣的時間尺度足以讓重大演化變化發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep time, not recent history.","zh":"這個短語描述深遠時間，而不是近代歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"geologists estimate that","meaning":"地質學家估計","examples":[{"en":"Geologists estimate that Hawaii emerged from the Pacific around that time.","zh":"地質學家估計夏威夷大約在那個時期從太平洋形成。"},{"en":"Geologists estimate that means Earth scientists calculate or judge something based on evidence.","zh":"geologists estimate that 指地球科學家根據證據計算或判斷某事。"},{"en":"Geologists estimate that a volcano last erupted thousands of years ago by studying rocks.","zh":"地質學家可能透過研究岩石，估計火山上一次噴發在數千年前。"},{"en":"Geological estimates help connect the age of landforms with the evolution of species.","zh":"地質估算幫助把地貌年齡與物種演化連起來。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an evidence-based scientific approximation.","zh":"這個短語引入有證據支持的科學近似判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"emerge from the Pacific","meaning":"從太平洋形成","examples":[{"en":"The Hawaiian islands emerged from the Pacific Ocean.","zh":"夏威夷群島從太平洋形成。"},{"en":"To emerge from the Pacific means to rise or form out of the Pacific Ocean.","zh":"emerge from the Pacific 指從太平洋中升起或形成。"},{"en":"A volcanic island may emerge from the sea after repeated eruptions build up land.","zh":"火山島可能在反覆噴發堆積陸地後從海中形成。"},{"en":"When new islands emerge, animals and plants must arrive later to colonise them.","zh":"當新島形成，動植物必須之後到達才能建立種群。"},{"en":"The phrase describes land formation from the ocean.","zh":"這個短語描述陸地從海洋中形成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"jump around the planet","meaning":"在全球各地快速擴散","examples":[{"en":"Highly mobile species can jump around the planet.","zh":"高度流動的物種可以在全球各地快速擴散。"},{"en":"To jump around the planet means to spread quickly to many distant parts of the world.","zh":"jump around the planet 指迅速擴散到世界許多遙遠地區。"},{"en":"A weed may jump around the planet if its seeds travel in ships and cargo.","zh":"如果雜草種子隨船隻和貨物移動，它可能在全球各地快速擴散。"},{"en":"Species that spread quickly can make their ancient origins harder to trace.","zh":"擴散迅速的物種會令其古代起源更難追溯。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and suggests rapid global movement.","zh":"這個短語較口語，暗示快速全球移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"histories blur","meaning":"歷史脈絡變得模糊","examples":[{"en":"The histories of widely dispersing species become difficult to trace.","zh":"廣泛擴散物種的歷史脈絡變得難以追溯。"},{"en":"Histories blur means the past becomes unclear and hard to reconstruct.","zh":"histories blur 指過去變得不清楚，難以重建。"},{"en":"A family’s migration history may blur if records are lost and stories change over generations.","zh":"如果記錄遺失而故事經幾代改變，家庭遷徙歷史可能變得模糊。"},{"en":"When species move too often, their locations no longer clearly reflect ancient geography.","zh":"當物種移動太頻繁，其位置就不再清楚反映古代地理。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence becoming confused or unclear.","zh":"這個短語描述證據變得混亂或不清晰。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"difficult to say much about","meaning":"很難對……作出太多判斷","examples":[{"en":"It is difficult to say much about where cockroaches first evolved.","zh":"很難對蟑螂最初在哪裏演化作出太多判斷。"},{"en":"Difficult to say much about something means there is not enough clear evidence to explain it fully.","zh":"difficult to say much about something 指沒有足夠清楚證據去完整解釋某事。"},{"en":"If a student has written only one short paragraph, it is difficult to say much about her writing level.","zh":"如果學生只寫了一段短文，很難對她的寫作水平作出太多判斷。"},{"en":"When evidence is mixed or missing, researchers must be cautious.","zh":"當證據混雜或缺失，研究人員必須謹慎。"},{"en":"The phrase signals limited knowledge.","zh":"這個短語表示知識有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"move quickly from continent to continent","meaning":"迅速在各大洲之間遷移","examples":[{"en":"Cockroaches can move quickly from continent to continent.","zh":"蟑螂能迅速在各大洲之間遷移。"},{"en":"To move quickly from continent to continent means to spread rapidly between major land areas.","zh":"move quickly from continent to continent 指在主要陸地區域之間快速擴散。"},{"en":"A pest species may move quickly from continent to continent through international shipping.","zh":"害蟲物種可能透過國際航運迅速在各大洲之間遷移。"},{"en":"Rapid movement makes it difficult to tell whether distribution reflects ancient history or recent travel.","zh":"快速移動令人難以判斷分布反映古代歷史還是近期旅行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes fast long-distance spread.","zh":"這個短語描述快速長距離擴散。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"process known as dispersal","meaning":"稱為擴散的過程","examples":[{"en":"This process is known as dispersal.","zh":"這個過程稱為擴散。"},{"en":"A process known as dispersal is the movement of organisms from one area to another.","zh":"process known as dispersal 指生物由一個地區移動到另一地區的過程。"},{"en":"Seeds carried by wind are part of a process known as dispersal.","zh":"種子被風吹走，是稱為擴散的過程的一部分。"},{"en":"Dispersal can help species colonise new places, but it can also blur their historical patterns.","zh":"擴散可以幫助物種建立新種群，但也可能模糊其歷史模式。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the scientific name for a movement process.","zh":"這個短語引入某種移動過程的科學名稱。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"dispersal","meaning":"物種擴散","examples":[{"en":"Dispersal can obscure the geographic history of a species.","zh":"擴散可以模糊物種的地理歷史。"},{"en":"Dispersal is the spread of organisms from their original location to new places.","zh":"dispersal 指生物從原本位置擴散到新地方。"},{"en":"Birds help plant dispersal when they eat fruit and drop seeds elsewhere.","zh":"鳥吃水果後在別處排出種子，可以幫助植物擴散。"},{"en":"If dispersal happens often, species distribution may not reveal ancient continental movement clearly.","zh":"如果擴散經常發生，物種分布未必能清楚揭示古代大陸移動。"},{"en":"The word describes movement and spread across space.","zh":"這個詞描述在空間中的移動和擴展。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"limit many studies","meaning":"限制許多研究","examples":[{"en":"Rapid dispersal limits many biogeographical studies.","zh":"快速擴散限制了許多生物地理學研究。"},{"en":"To limit many studies means to make many investigations less complete or less reliable.","zh":"limit many studies 指令許多研究變得不完整或不夠可靠。"},{"en":"Missing student records can limit many studies of school performance.","zh":"學生記錄缺失可以限制許多關於學校表現的研究。"},{"en":"If species move too freely, researchers cannot easily use their locations as geological evidence.","zh":"如果物種移動太自由，研究人員就難以把其位置用作地質證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a factor that restricts research usefulness.","zh":"這個短語描述限制研究用途的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tend to concentrate on","meaning":"往往集中於……","examples":[{"en":"Many studies tend to concentrate on particular regions.","zh":"許多研究往往集中於特定地區。"},{"en":"To tend to concentrate on something means to usually focus attention on it.","zh":"tend to concentrate on something 指通常把注意力集中於某事。"},{"en":"A student may tend to concentrate on vocabulary and forget grammar when preparing for an exam.","zh":"學生準備考試時，可能往往集中於詞彙而忘記文法。"},{"en":"If research concentrates on only one region, global patterns may be missed.","zh":"如果研究只集中於一個地區，全球模式可能被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a common focus or habit.","zh":"這個短語描述常見焦點或習慣。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"particular parts of the world","meaning":"世界特定地區","examples":[{"en":"Earlier research focused on particular parts of the world.","zh":"早期研究集中於世界特定地區。"},{"en":"Particular parts of the world are specific regions or areas rather than the whole planet.","zh":"particular parts of the world 指特定地區或區域，而不是整個地球。"},{"en":"A travel guide may focus on particular parts of the world, such as Southeast Asia or Europe.","zh":"旅遊指南可能集中於世界特定地區，例如東南亞或歐洲。"},{"en":"Studying only selected regions can make conclusions too narrow.","zh":"只研究選定地區可能令結論過於狹窄。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts regional focus with global coverage.","zh":"這個短語把地區焦點與全球涵蓋作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"system for studying","meaning":"用來研究……的系統","examples":[{"en":"Giribet wanted a new system for studying global biogeography.","zh":"Giribet 想要一個用來研究全球生物地理學的新系統。"},{"en":"A system for studying something is an organised method or model used to investigate it.","zh":"system for studying something 指用來調查某事的有組織方法或模型。"},{"en":"A teacher may create a system for studying vocabulary by grouping words by topic and use.","zh":"老師可能透過按主題和用法分類詞語，建立用來研究詞彙的系統。"},{"en":"A good research system helps scientists compare evidence consistently.","zh":"良好研究系統幫助科學家一致地比較證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a structured way of doing research.","zh":"這個短語指有結構的研究方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"on a global scale","meaning":"在全球層面","examples":[{"en":"The researchers wanted to study biogeography on a global scale.","zh":"研究人員想在全球層面研究生物地理學。"},{"en":"On a global scale means across the whole world rather than in one region only.","zh":"on a global scale 指在全世界範圍內，而不是只在某一地區。"},{"en":"Climate change affects agriculture on a global scale.","zh":"氣候變化在全球層面影響農業。"},{"en":"Studying species globally can reveal patterns that regional studies miss.","zh":"全球研究物種可以揭示地區研究看不到的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses worldwide scope.","zh":"這個短語強調世界範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"realise that","meaning":"意識到","examples":[{"en":"Giribet realised that mite harvestmen might provide the ideal system.","zh":"Giribet 意識到蟎盲蛛可能提供理想系統。"},{"en":"To realise that means to become aware of or understand a fact.","zh":"realise that 指意識到或理解某個事實。"},{"en":"A student may realise that her mistakes come from weak planning, not weak English.","zh":"學生可能意識到她的錯誤來自計劃不足，而不是英文差。"},{"en":"Realising a key fact can change the direction of research or study.","zh":"意識到關鍵事實可以改變研究或學習方向。"},{"en":"The phrase marks a moment of understanding.","zh":"這個短語標示理解的時刻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"5,000 or so species","meaning":"約五千個物種","examples":[{"en":"There are about 5,000 or so species of mite harvestmen.","zh":"蟎盲蛛大約有五千個左右的物種。"},{"en":"5,000 or so species means approximately 5,000 species, not an exact number.","zh":"5,000 or so species 指約五千個物種，而不是精確數字。"},{"en":"A library may have 5,000 or so books if the exact count changes each year.","zh":"如果確切數量每年改變，圖書館可能有約五千本書。"},{"en":"Approximate numbers are useful when the total is large or still being updated.","zh":"當總數龐大或仍在更新，近似數字很有用。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a rough estimate.","zh":"這個短語提供粗略估算。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"on every continent except","meaning":"除……外每個大洲都有","examples":[{"en":"The animals occur on every continent except Antarctica.","zh":"除南極洲外，每個大洲都有這些動物。"},{"en":"On every continent except one means found across all continents apart from the named exception.","zh":"on every continent except one 指除了所說的例外大洲外，所有大洲都有。"},{"en":"A popular sport may be played on every continent except Antarctica.","zh":"一項受歡迎運動可能除南極洲外每個大洲都有進行。"},{"en":"A species found almost everywhere can still have clear limits if one continent lacks it.","zh":"幾乎到處都有的物種，如果某一大洲沒有，也仍有清楚限制。"},{"en":"The phrase describes very wide distribution with one exclusion.","zh":"這個短語描述非常廣泛但有一個例外的分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"unlike creatures such as","meaning":"與……之類的生物不同","examples":[{"en":"Unlike creatures such as cockroaches, mite harvestmen disperse poorly.","zh":"與蟑螂之類的生物不同，蟎盲蛛不善於擴散。"},{"en":"Unlike creatures such as something means different from those example creatures.","zh":"unlike creatures such as something 指不同於那些作為例子的生物。"},{"en":"Unlike pets such as dogs, fish do not need daily walks.","zh":"與狗之類的寵物不同，魚不需要每天散步。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces contrast by comparing one group with a familiar example.","zh":"這個短語透過與熟悉例子比較來引入對比。"},{"en":"It helps explain a feature by saying what it is not like.","zh":"它透過說明某物不像甚麼來解釋其特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cannot disperse well","meaning":"不善於擴散","examples":[{"en":"Mite harvestmen cannot disperse well over long distances.","zh":"蟎盲蛛不善於長距離擴散。"},{"en":"Cannot disperse well means unable to spread or move successfully to faraway places.","zh":"cannot disperse well 指不能成功擴散或移動到遙遠地方。"},{"en":"A plant with heavy seeds may not disperse well because the seeds fall near the parent plant.","zh":"種子很重的植物可能不善於擴散，因為種子落在母株附近。"},{"en":"Poor dispersal keeps species close to their original habitats.","zh":"擴散能力差會令物種留近原本棲息地。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why a species may preserve clear geographic patterns.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何物種可能保存清晰地理模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"typical species","meaning":"典型物種","examples":[{"en":"A typical species has a very limited geographic range.","zh":"典型物種的地理分布範圍非常有限。"},{"en":"A typical species is a normal or representative example of a group.","zh":"typical species 指某群體中正常或具代表性的例子。"},{"en":"A typical school day may include lessons, lunch, homework, and activities.","zh":"典型上課日可能包括課堂、午餐、功課和活動。"},{"en":"Describing a typical species helps readers understand the usual pattern, not the rare exception.","zh":"描述典型物種幫助讀者理解通常模式，而不是罕見例外。"},{"en":"The phrase points to what is common for the group.","zh":"這個短語指出該群體中常見的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a range of less than","meaning":"分布範圍少於……","examples":[{"en":"Most species have a range of less than fifty miles.","zh":"大多數物種的分布範圍少於五十英里。"},{"en":"A range of less than a distance means a distribution area smaller than that distance.","zh":"a range of less than a distance 指分布區域小於某距離。"},{"en":"A small shop may deliver within a range of less than five kilometres.","zh":"小店可能只在少於五公里範圍內送貨。"},{"en":"A limited range can show that a species does not travel far from its habitat.","zh":"有限分布範圍可以顯示物種不會離棲息地很遠。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a maximum area or distance.","zh":"這個短語描述最大範圍或距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"young islands","meaning":"年代較新的島嶼","examples":[{"en":"Mite harvestmen are absent from geologically young islands.","zh":"蟎盲蛛不出現在地質年代較新的島嶼上。"},{"en":"Young islands are islands that formed relatively recently in geological time.","zh":"young islands 指在地質時間中相對近期形成的島嶼。"},{"en":"A volcanic island may be young if it rose from the sea only a few hundred thousand years ago.","zh":"如果火山島只在幾十萬年前從海中升起，它可能是年代較新的島嶼。"},{"en":"Species with poor dispersal may be absent from young islands because they formed after ancient land connections disappeared.","zh":"擴散能力差的物種可能不出現在年輕島嶼上，因為它們在古代陸地連接消失後才形成。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to geological age, not the age of people living there.","zh":"這個短語指地質年齡，而不是島上居民的年齡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"emerge long after","meaning":"在……很久之後形成","examples":[{"en":"Hawaii emerged long after Pangea had broken apart.","zh":"夏威夷在盤古大陸分裂很久之後才形成。"},{"en":"To emerge long after something means to form or appear much later than that earlier event.","zh":"emerge long after something 指在較早事件很久之後才形成或出現。"},{"en":"A new town may emerge long after the old railway line has closed.","zh":"新市鎮可能在舊鐵路關閉很久之後才形成。"},{"en":"If an island forms long after a species’ ancient dispersal, that species may never reach it naturally.","zh":"如果島嶼在某物種古代擴散之後很久才形成，該物種可能永遠不能自然到達。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a large time gap.","zh":"這個短語強調巨大的時間差距。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"break-up of Pangea","meaning":"盤古大陸的分裂","examples":[{"en":"The break-up of Pangea separated many ancient species.","zh":"盤古大陸的分裂分隔了許多古代物種。"},{"en":"The break-up of Pangea was the process in which the supercontinent split into separate landmasses.","zh":"break-up of Pangea 指超大陸分裂成不同陸塊的過程。"},{"en":"A geography lesson may use maps to show the break-up of Pangea over millions of years.","zh":"地理課可能用地圖展示盤古大陸如何在數百萬年間分裂。"},{"en":"When Pangea broke apart, related species could be carried to different continents.","zh":"當盤古大陸分裂，相關物種可能被帶到不同大洲。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a major event in Earth’s geological history.","zh":"這個短語描述地球地質歷史中的重大事件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"former student of","meaning":"……以前的學生","examples":[{"en":"Sarah Boyer was a former student of Dr Giribet.","zh":"Sarah Boyer 曾是 Giribet 博士以前的學生。"},{"en":"A former student of someone is a person who studied under that teacher or researcher in the past.","zh":"former student of someone 指過去跟隨某位老師或研究人員學習的人。"},{"en":"A former student of a music teacher may later become a professional performer.","zh":"音樂老師以前的學生日後可能成為專業表演者。"},{"en":"Former students often continue a teacher’s research methods or ideas in new projects.","zh":"以前的學生常在新項目中延續老師的研究方法或想法。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an educational relationship from the past.","zh":"這個短語描述過去的教育關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be distributed all over the world","meaning":"分布於世界各地","examples":[{"en":"The group is distributed all over the world.","zh":"這個類群分布於世界各地。"},{"en":"To be distributed all over the world means to be found in many regions globally.","zh":"be distributed all over the world 指在全球許多地區都能找到。"},{"en":"English learning apps are distributed all over the world through online stores.","zh":"英語學習應用程式透過網上商店分布於世界各地。"},{"en":"Wide distribution can make a group useful for comparing global patterns.","zh":"廣泛分布可以令某群體適合用來比較全球模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes worldwide presence.","zh":"這個短語描述全球存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not disperse very far","meaning":"不會擴散到很遠","examples":[{"en":"The animals do not disperse very far from their original habitats.","zh":"這些動物不會從原本棲息地擴散到很遠。"},{"en":"Not disperse very far means not move or spread far from where they began.","zh":"not disperse very far 指不會離開起點很遠地移動或擴散。"},{"en":"A plant with seeds that fall straight down may not disperse very far from the parent plant.","zh":"種子直接掉落的植物可能不會從母株擴散到很遠。"},{"en":"Limited dispersal helps preserve local genetic patterns.","zh":"有限擴散有助保存本地遺傳模式。"},{"en":"The phrase explains why a species may stay geographically restricted.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何物種可能受地理限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lack in mobility","meaning":"缺乏移動能力","examples":[{"en":"Mite harvestmen lack mobility.","zh":"蟎盲蛛缺乏移動能力。"},{"en":"To lack mobility means to have little ability to move far or easily.","zh":"lack mobility 指缺乏遠距離或輕易移動的能力。"},{"en":"An elderly person may lack mobility after an injury and need help with stairs.","zh":"長者受傷後可能缺乏移動能力，需要別人幫忙上樓梯。"},{"en":"If an animal lacks mobility, its spread depends more on long-term land movement than daily travel.","zh":"如果動物缺乏移動能力，其分布更依賴長期陸地移動，而不是日常旅行。"},{"en":"The phrase describes limited movement ability.","zh":"這個短語描述移動能力有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make up for something in","meaning":"以……彌補……的不足","examples":[{"en":"What the animals lack in mobility, they make up for in age.","zh":"這些動物在移動能力上的不足，以年代久遠來彌補。"},{"en":"To make up for something in another quality means to compensate for one weakness with another strength.","zh":"make up for something in another quality 指用另一個優點彌補某弱點。"},{"en":"A small school may lack space but make up for it in close teacher support.","zh":"小學校可能空間不足，但以緊密教師支援作彌補。"},{"en":"Mite harvestmen do not move far, but their ancient age makes them valuable to researchers.","zh":"蟎盲蛛不會移動很遠，但其古老年代令牠們對研究人員有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a trade-off between weakness and strength.","zh":"這個短語突出弱點與優點之間的取捨。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"among the first land animals","meaning":"最早期陸生動物之一","examples":[{"en":"Their ancestors were among the first land animals.","zh":"牠們的祖先是最早期陸生動物之一。"},{"en":"Among the first land animals means part of the earliest groups of animals to live on land.","zh":"among the first land animals 指屬於最早在陸地生活的動物群之一。"},{"en":"Early arthropods were among the first land animals because they could survive outside water.","zh":"早期節肢動物是最早期陸生動物之一，因為牠們能在水外生存。"},{"en":"Being ancient makes a species group useful for studying deep evolutionary history.","zh":"古老物種群對研究深層演化歷史很有用。"},{"en":"The phrase places an organism very early in land-animal history.","zh":"這個短語把生物放在陸生動物歷史非常早期的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"400-million-year-old rocks","meaning":"有四億年歷史的岩石","examples":[{"en":"Related fossils have been found in 400-million-year-old rocks.","zh":"相關化石已在有四億年歷史的岩石中被發現。"},{"en":"400-million-year-old rocks are rocks that formed about four hundred million years ago.","zh":"400-million-year-old rocks 指約四億年前形成的岩石。"},{"en":"Fossils in very old rocks can show what ancient life looked like.","zh":"非常古老岩石中的化石可以顯示古代生命的樣貌。"},{"en":"Finding related fossils in ancient rocks proves the animal group has a very long history.","zh":"在古老岩石中找到相關化石，證明該動物群有非常悠久歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the geological age of the rock evidence.","zh":"這個短語提供岩石證據的地質年齡。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"evolve long before","meaning":"早在……之前已演化","examples":[{"en":"Mite harvestmen evolved long before Pangea broke apart.","zh":"蟎盲蛛早在盤古大陸分裂之前已演化。"},{"en":"To evolve long before something means to develop much earlier than that later event.","zh":"evolve long before something 指在某較後事件很久之前已發展出來。"},{"en":"Some fish groups evolved long before humans appeared.","zh":"有些魚類群早在人類出現之前已演化。"},{"en":"If a species evolved before continental break-up, its distribution may reflect ancient land movements.","zh":"如果物種在大陸分裂前已演化，其分布可能反映古代陸地移動。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that one event happened far earlier than another.","zh":"這個短語強調一件事比另一件事早很多發生。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be carried along by","meaning":"隨着……被帶動","examples":[{"en":"The animals were carried along by continental drift.","zh":"這些動物隨着大陸漂移被帶動。"},{"en":"To be carried along by something means to be moved by a larger force or process.","zh":"be carried along by something 指被較大的力量或過程帶着移動。"},{"en":"Leaves may be carried along by a river after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後，葉子可能隨河水被帶走。"},{"en":"Tiny animals with poor mobility may be moved by continents rather than by their own travel.","zh":"移動能力差的細小動物可能由大陸移動帶動，而不是靠自己旅行。"},{"en":"The phrase shows passive movement caused by something bigger.","zh":"這個短語顯示由更大事物造成的被動移動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ever since","meaning":"從那時起一直","examples":[{"en":"They have travelled with the continents ever since.","zh":"從那時起，牠們一直隨大陸旅行。"},{"en":"Ever since means continuously from that time until now or a later point.","zh":"ever since 指從那個時間起一直到現在或後來某時間點。"},{"en":"She failed one spelling test and has practised every week ever since.","zh":"她一次串字測驗不合格後，從那時起每星期都練習。"},{"en":"The phrase links a past event with a long continuing result.","zh":"這個短語把過去事件與長期持續結果連起來。"},{"en":"It shows that something did not just happen once.","zh":"它顯示某事不是只發生一次。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"manage to get around the world","meaning":"得以分布至世界各地","examples":[{"en":"The animals managed to get around the world through continental movement.","zh":"這些動物透過大陸移動得以分布至世界各地。"},{"en":"To manage to get around the world means to succeed in becoming distributed globally.","zh":"manage to get around the world 指成功變得全球分布。"},{"en":"A small local song may manage to get around the world if it spreads online.","zh":"一首本地小歌如果在網上傳開，可能得以傳遍世界。"},{"en":"For mite harvestmen, global distribution happened through ancient land movement, not active travel.","zh":"對蟎盲蛛而言，全球分布是透過古代陸地移動，而不是主動旅行。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests achieving wide spread despite difficulty.","zh":"這個短語暗示儘管困難仍成功廣泛分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"only because","meaning":"只是因為","examples":[{"en":"They spread globally only because they are extremely ancient.","zh":"牠們全球擴散只是因為牠們極其古老。"},{"en":"Only because means for this reason alone or mainly this reason.","zh":"only because 指只因為這個原因，或主要因為這個原因。"},{"en":"A student may pass only because she revised the exact topic the night before.","zh":"學生可能只是因為前一晚溫習到相同題目才合格。"},{"en":"The phrase limits the explanation to one key cause.","zh":"這個短語把解釋限制在一個關鍵原因上。"},{"en":"It often corrects a possible misunderstanding about why something happened.","zh":"它常用來糾正對某事發生原因的誤解。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"gather thousands of specimens","meaning":"收集數千個標本","examples":[{"en":"The researchers gathered thousands of mite harvestmen.","zh":"研究人員收集了數千個蟎盲蛛標本。"},{"en":"To gather thousands of specimens means to collect many individual samples for study.","zh":"gather thousands of specimens 指收集許多個體樣本作研究。"},{"en":"A biology class may gather leaf specimens to compare shape, colour, and size.","zh":"生物課可能收集葉子標本，以比較形狀、顏色和大小。"},{"en":"Large sample collections help scientists see patterns that one or two examples cannot show.","zh":"大量樣本收藏幫助科學家看見一兩個例子無法顯示的模式。"},{"en":"The phrase describes scientific collecting on a large scale.","zh":"這個短語描述大規模科學採集。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"extract DNA","meaning":"提取DNA","examples":[{"en":"The scientists extracted DNA from the specimens.","zh":"科學家從標本中提取 DNA。"},{"en":"To extract DNA means to remove genetic material from cells or tissue for analysis.","zh":"extract DNA 指從細胞或組織中取出遺傳物質作分析。"},{"en":"A medical lab may extract DNA from a blood sample to test for a genetic condition.","zh":"醫學實驗室可能從血液樣本中提取 DNA，以檢測遺傳疾病。"},{"en":"Extracted DNA can reveal relationships between species that look very similar.","zh":"提取出的 DNA 可以揭示外表非常相似物種之間的關係。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a laboratory process for studying genes.","zh":"這個短語描述研究基因的實驗室過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"variations in the genes","meaning":"基因差異","examples":[{"en":"Variations in the genes revealed evolutionary relationships.","zh":"基因差異揭示了演化關係。"},{"en":"Variations in the genes are differences in DNA sequences between individuals or species.","zh":"variations in the genes 指個體或物種之間 DNA 序列的差別。"},{"en":"Genetic variations can help doctors understand why patients respond differently to medicine.","zh":"基因差異可以幫助醫生理解為何病人對藥物反應不同。"},{"en":"In evolutionary studies, gene differences can show which species are more closely related.","zh":"在演化研究中，基因差異可以顯示哪些物種親緣關係較近。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to meaningful differences in genetic material.","zh":"這個短語指遺傳物質中的有意義差別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"build an evolutionary tree","meaning":"建立演化樹","examples":[{"en":"The scientists used genetic evidence to build an evolutionary tree.","zh":"科學家使用遺傳證據建立演化樹。"},{"en":"To build an evolutionary tree means to create a diagram showing how species are related over time.","zh":"build an evolutionary tree 指建立一個圖表，顯示物種如何隨時間相關。"},{"en":"A biology teacher may build a simple evolutionary tree to show how mammals share ancestors.","zh":"生物老師可能建立簡單演化樹，顯示哺乳動物如何共享祖先。"},{"en":"Genetic evidence helps place branches in the tree more accurately.","zh":"遺傳證據幫助更準確地放置樹上的分支。"},{"en":"The phrase describes organising evolutionary relationships visually.","zh":"這個短語描述以視覺方式整理演化關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"evolutionary tree","meaning":"演化樹","examples":[{"en":"An evolutionary tree shows how species are related.","zh":"演化樹顯示物種如何有親緣關係。"},{"en":"An evolutionary tree is a branching diagram that represents shared ancestry and species divergence.","zh":"evolutionary tree 指用分支圖表示共同祖先和物種分化。"},{"en":"Students can use an evolutionary tree to see that humans and chimpanzees share a common ancestor.","zh":"學生可以使用演化樹看見人類和黑猩猩有共同祖先。"},{"en":"Branches that split recently usually show closer relationships than branches that split long ago.","zh":"最近分開的分支通常顯示比很久以前分開的分支更近的關係。"},{"en":"The phrase is a visual model of evolution.","zh":"這個短語是演化的視覺模型。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"calculate how quickly","meaning":"計算……的速度","examples":[{"en":"The researchers calculated how quickly the DNA mutated.","zh":"研究人員計算 DNA 發生突變的速度。"},{"en":"To calculate how quickly something happens means to work out its rate using evidence or numbers.","zh":"calculate how quickly something happens 指用證據或數字計算某事發生的速率。"},{"en":"A teacher may calculate how quickly a student’s reading speed improves each month.","zh":"老師可能計算學生每月閱讀速度進步得多快。"},{"en":"In genetics, mutation rates help estimate when species lineages separated.","zh":"在遺傳學中，突變速率幫助估計物種譜系何時分離。"},{"en":"The phrase describes measuring speed or rate.","zh":"這個短語描述量度速度或速率。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"DNA mutate","meaning":"DNA發生突變","examples":[{"en":"DNA mutates gradually over long periods.","zh":"DNA 會在漫長時期中逐漸發生突變。"},{"en":"When DNA mutates, its genetic sequence changes.","zh":"當 DNA mutates，遺傳序列會發生改變。"},{"en":"A small DNA mutation may have no visible effect, while another may affect a trait.","zh":"小型 DNA 突變可能沒有可見影響，而另一種可能影響某特徵。"},{"en":"Over millions of years, mutations can help scientists estimate evolutionary timing.","zh":"經過數百萬年，突變可以幫助科學家估計演化時間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes genetic change, not intentional change by an organism.","zh":"這個短語描述遺傳變化，而不是生物有意作出改變。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"estimate when","meaning":"估計……的時間","examples":[{"en":"Genetic changes helped the team estimate when lineages separated.","zh":"遺傳變化幫助團隊估計譜系何時分離。"},{"en":"To estimate when something happened means to make an evidence-based judgment about its time.","zh":"estimate when something happened 指根據證據判斷某事發生的時間。"},{"en":"A historian may estimate when an old house was built by studying its materials.","zh":"歷史學家可能透過研究材料估計舊屋何時建成。"},{"en":"Genetic differences can act like a clock for estimating evolutionary splits.","zh":"遺傳差異可以像時鐘一樣，用來估計演化分裂時間。"},{"en":"The phrase describes approximate timing, not exact certainty.","zh":"這個短語描述近似時間，而不是絕對確定。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lineages branch off","meaning":"譜系分化","examples":[{"en":"Different lineages branched off at different times.","zh":"不同譜系在不同時間分化。"},{"en":"When lineages branch off, groups of organisms separate from a common ancestor and develop differently.","zh":"lineages branch off 指生物群從共同祖先分離並以不同方式發展。"},{"en":"Two family lines may branch off when siblings move to different countries and start separate families.","zh":"當兄弟姊妹移居不同國家並建立各自家庭，兩條家族線可能分開。"},{"en":"In evolution, branching off can eventually produce distinct species.","zh":"在演化中，譜系分化最終可以產生不同物種。"},{"en":"The phrase uses a tree image to describe separation over time.","zh":"這個短語用樹的意象描述隨時間分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"compare A to B","meaning":"把A與B比較","examples":[{"en":"The scientists compared the animals’ evolution to continental movement.","zh":"科學家把這些動物的演化與大陸移動比較。"},{"en":"To compare A to B means to examine A and B together to find similarities, differences, or connections.","zh":"compare A to B 指一起檢視 A 和 B，以找出相似、差異或關聯。"},{"en":"A teacher may compare a student’s first essay to the final version to show improvement.","zh":"老師可能把學生第一篇作文與最終版本比較，以顯示進步。"},{"en":"Comparing genetic history to geological movement can reveal whether the two patterns match.","zh":"把遺傳歷史與地質移動比較，可以揭示兩種模式是否吻合。"},{"en":"The phrase describes studying two things side by side.","zh":"這個短語描述並排研究兩件事。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"movements of the continents","meaning":"大陸的移動","examples":[{"en":"The species’ history reflects the movements of the continents.","zh":"物種歷史反映大陸的移動。"},{"en":"Movements of the continents are the long-term shifts of landmasses across Earth’s surface.","zh":"movements of the continents 指大陸塊在地球表面上的長期移動。"},{"en":"Maps can show movements of the continents from Pangea to their present positions.","zh":"地圖可以顯示大陸從盤古大陸到現今位置的移動。"},{"en":"If species history matches those movements, biology can support geological conclusions.","zh":"如果物種歷史與這些移動吻合，生物學可以支持地質結論。"},{"en":"The phrase describes geological motion over millions of years.","zh":"這個短語描述數百萬年間的地質運動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"patterns are remarkably clear","meaning":"規律非常清晰","examples":[{"en":"The genetic and geological patterns are remarkably clear.","zh":"遺傳和地質規律非常清晰。"},{"en":"Patterns are remarkably clear means the connections or repeated features are very easy to see.","zh":"patterns are remarkably clear 指關聯或重複特徵非常容易看見。"},{"en":"A teacher may say the error pattern is remarkably clear if every student misses the same grammar point.","zh":"如果每個學生都錯同一個文法點，老師可能說錯誤模式非常清晰。"},{"en":"Clear patterns help researchers make stronger arguments.","zh":"清晰模式幫助研究人員提出更有力論點。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises unusually strong evidence.","zh":"這個短語強調異常有力的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"trace something back to","meaning":"把……追溯至","examples":[{"en":"The researchers traced the species back to ancestors on Pangea.","zh":"研究人員把這些物種追溯至盤古大陸上的祖先。"},{"en":"To trace something back to a source means to follow evidence to its origin.","zh":"trace something back to a source 指沿着證據找出其起源。"},{"en":"A teacher may trace a student’s repeated spelling error back to a pronunciation problem.","zh":"老師可能把學生反覆串錯字追溯至發音問題。"},{"en":"Tracing a species back to ancient ancestors helps explain its current distribution.","zh":"把物種追溯至古代祖先，有助解釋其現今分布。"},{"en":"The phrase describes finding where something began.","zh":"這個短語描述找出某事起點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lineage","meaning":"譜系","examples":[{"en":"One lineage includes species from several distant continents.","zh":"一個譜系包括來自幾個遙遠大洲的物種。"},{"en":"A lineage is a line of descent from a common ancestor.","zh":"lineage 指由共同祖先延續下來的一條世系。"},{"en":"A family tree shows different lineages within one extended family.","zh":"家譜顯示一個大家庭中的不同譜系。"},{"en":"In evolution, a lineage can split into several species over time.","zh":"在演化中，一條譜系可以隨時間分裂成幾個物種。"},{"en":"The word refers to ancestry and descent.","zh":"這個詞指祖先關係和傳承。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be separated by","meaning":"相隔……","examples":[{"en":"The populations are now separated by thousands of miles of ocean.","zh":"這些種群現在相隔數千英里的海洋。"},{"en":"To be separated by something means to have that thing between two places or groups.","zh":"be separated by something 指兩個地方或群體之間隔着某物。"},{"en":"Two schools may be separated by a busy road, making travel between them difficult.","zh":"兩所學校可能相隔一條繁忙馬路，令往來困難。"},{"en":"If populations are separated by ocean, they may evolve independently.","zh":"如果種群相隔海洋，它們可能獨立演化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a barrier or distance between things.","zh":"這個短語描述事物之間的屏障或距離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"thousands of miles of ocean","meaning":"數千英里的海洋","examples":[{"en":"The related species are separated by thousands of miles of ocean.","zh":"相關物種相隔數千英里的海洋。"},{"en":"Thousands of miles of ocean means an enormous sea distance between places.","zh":"thousands of miles of ocean 指地方之間有極大的海洋距離。"},{"en":"Families living on opposite sides of the Pacific are separated by thousands of miles of ocean.","zh":"住在太平洋兩邊的家庭相隔數千英里的海洋。"},{"en":"Such a distance makes ordinary animal travel very unlikely.","zh":"這樣的距離令普通動物移動非常不可能。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises how far apart the locations are.","zh":"這個短語強調地點相隔多遠。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sites were in Gondwana","meaning":"地點曾位於岡瓦納大陸","examples":[{"en":"The distant sites were once part of Gondwana.","zh":"這些遙遠地點曾經是岡瓦納大陸的一部分。"},{"en":"Sites were in Gondwana means those places belonged to the ancient southern landmass called Gondwana.","zh":"sites were in Gondwana 指那些地方曾屬於名為岡瓦納的古代南方大陸塊。"},{"en":"A rock found in South America and another in Africa may both come from regions that were in Gondwana.","zh":"南美洲一塊岩石和非洲另一塊岩石，可能都來自曾位於岡瓦納大陸的地區。"},{"en":"If distant sites were once joined, related species there may share ancient origins.","zh":"如果遙遠地點曾經相連，那裏的相關物種可能有古老共同起源。"},{"en":"The phrase links modern locations with an ancient continent.","zh":"這個短語把現代地點與古代大陸連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Gondwana","meaning":"岡瓦納大陸","examples":[{"en":"Gondwana formed a major region of Pangea.","zh":"岡瓦納大陸形成盤古大陸的一個主要區域。"},{"en":"Gondwana was an ancient southern supercontinent that included land now found in places such as Africa, South America, Antarctica, Australia, and India.","zh":"Gondwana 是古代南方超大陸，包括今日非洲、南美洲、南極洲、澳洲和印度等地。"},{"en":"A geology class may study Gondwana to understand why fossils match across southern continents.","zh":"地質課可能研究岡瓦納大陸，以理解為何南方大陸之間化石相符。"},{"en":"When Gondwana broke apart, related species were carried to separated lands.","zh":"當岡瓦納大陸分裂，相關物種被帶到分離的陸地。"},{"en":"The word names a major ancient landmass.","zh":"這個詞命名一個主要古代大陸塊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"preserve smaller patterns","meaning":"保存較小規模的模式","examples":[{"en":"The animals preserve smaller patterns of continental drift as well.","zh":"這些動物也保存了較小規模的大陸漂移模式。"},{"en":"To preserve smaller patterns means to keep evidence of more detailed or local historical patterns.","zh":"preserve smaller patterns 指保留更詳細或本地歷史模式的證據。"},{"en":"Old street names may preserve smaller patterns of a city’s past neighbourhoods.","zh":"舊街名可能保存城市昔日社區的較小規模模式。"},{"en":"Even local genetic differences can reveal small-scale geological events.","zh":"即使本地遺傳差異也可以揭示小規模地質事件。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests evidence exists at both large and detailed scales.","zh":"這個短語暗示證據同時存在於大尺度和細節尺度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"analyse the DNA of","meaning":"分析……的DNA","examples":[{"en":"The scientists analysed the DNA of a Florida species.","zh":"科學家分析了一個佛羅里達物種的 DNA。"},{"en":"To analyse the DNA of something means to study its genetic material carefully.","zh":"analyse the DNA of something 指仔細研究其遺傳物質。"},{"en":"Doctors may analyse the DNA of a patient to check for inherited disease risk.","zh":"醫生可能分析病人的 DNA，以檢查遺傳疾病風險。"},{"en":"DNA analysis can reveal relationships that appearance alone cannot show.","zh":"DNA 分析可以揭示單靠外表無法顯示的關係。"},{"en":"The phrase describes close scientific examination of genetic information.","zh":"這個短語描述對遺傳資訊的仔細科學檢視。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be surprised to find that","meaning":"驚訝地發現","examples":[{"en":"They were surprised to find that the species lacked close American relatives.","zh":"他們驚訝地發現該物種缺乏近親的美洲親戚。"},{"en":"To be surprised to find that means to discover something unexpected.","zh":"be surprised to find that 指發現出乎意料的事情。"},{"en":"A teacher may be surprised to find that quiet students wrote the most creative stories.","zh":"老師可能驚訝地發現安靜學生寫出最有創意的故事。"},{"en":"Unexpected findings often lead researchers to check other evidence.","zh":"意外發現常引導研究人員檢查其他證據。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a result that went against expectation.","zh":"這個短語引入違反預期的結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be related to","meaning":"與……有親緣關係","examples":[{"en":"The Florida species was not closely related to other North American species.","zh":"佛羅里達物種與其他北美物種沒有密切親緣關係。"},{"en":"To be related to another species means to share evolutionary ancestry with it.","zh":"be related to another species 指與另一物種有共同演化祖先。"},{"en":"Lions are related to domestic cats, though they look and behave very differently.","zh":"獅子與家貓有親緣關係，雖然牠們外表和行為很不同。"},{"en":"If a species is not closely related to nearby species, its history may be unusual.","zh":"如果某物種與附近物種關係不近，其歷史可能不尋常。"},{"en":"The phrase describes biological relationship, not friendship or location.","zh":"這個短語描述生物關係，而不是友誼或位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"closest relatives","meaning":"關係最密切的近親","examples":[{"en":"Its closest relatives live in West Africa.","zh":"牠關係最密切的近親生活在西非。"},{"en":"Closest relatives are the species or organisms most closely connected by ancestry.","zh":"closest relatives 指在祖先關係上最接近的物種或生物。"},{"en":"A dog’s closest wild relatives include wolves.","zh":"狗最接近的野生近親包括狼。"},{"en":"If an animal’s closest relatives live far away, scientists may look for an ancient geographic explanation.","zh":"如果動物最接近的近親生活在遙遠地方，科學家可能尋找古代地理解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the nearest evolutionary connections.","zh":"這個短語指出最近的演化聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"investigate the geological history of","meaning":"研究……的地質歷史","examples":[{"en":"Dr Boyer investigated the geological history of Florida.","zh":"Boyer 博士研究佛羅里達的地質歷史。"},{"en":"To investigate the geological history of a place means to study how its land formed and moved over time.","zh":"investigate the geological history of a place 指研究某地的陸地如何形成和移動。"},{"en":"A scientist may investigate the geological history of a mountain by studying its rocks.","zh":"科學家可能透過研究岩石來研究山脈的地質歷史。"},{"en":"Geological history can explain why today’s species relationships look surprising.","zh":"地質歷史可以解釋為何今日物種關係看起來令人驚訝。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research into a place’s physical past.","zh":"這個短語描述對某地物理過去的研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"recent research","meaning":"近期研究","examples":[{"en":"Recent research helped explain the unexpected genetic pattern.","zh":"近期研究幫助解釋這個意外遺傳模式。"},{"en":"Recent research means studies or findings produced not long ago.","zh":"recent research 指不久前完成的研究或發現。"},{"en":"Recent research on sleep has changed how some schools think about early start times.","zh":"近期關於睡眠的研究改變了一些學校對早上上課時間的看法。"},{"en":"New findings can explain puzzles that older evidence could not solve.","zh":"新發現可以解釋舊證據無法解決的謎題。"},{"en":"The phrase points to updated scientific information.","zh":"這個短語指較新的科學資訊。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"explain the mystery","meaning":"解開謎團","examples":[{"en":"Geological evidence helped explain the mystery.","zh":"地質證據幫助解開這個謎團。"},{"en":"To explain the mystery means to make a puzzling situation understandable.","zh":"explain the mystery 指令令人困惑的情況變得可理解。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain the mystery of low test scores by showing that students missed one key topic.","zh":"老師可能指出學生錯過一個關鍵題目，從而解開低分之謎。"},{"en":"Evidence can turn a surprising result into a logical story.","zh":"證據可以把驚人結果變成合邏輯故事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes solving confusion with an explanation.","zh":"這個短語描述用解釋解決困惑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"start out welded to","meaning":"最初與……連接","examples":[{"en":"Florida started out welded to West Africa.","zh":"佛羅里達最初與西非連接。"},{"en":"To start out welded to something means to begin as part of a landmass firmly connected to it.","zh":"start out welded to something 指一開始作為與某地牢固相連的大陸塊一部分。"},{"en":"Two school buildings may start out connected before later renovation separates them.","zh":"兩座校舍可能最初相連，之後翻新才分開。"},{"en":"If Florida began attached to Africa, its species may share African connections.","zh":"如果佛羅里達最初連着非洲，其物種可能有非洲關聯。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an original physical connection.","zh":"這個短語描述最初的實體連接。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"near Senegal","meaning":"鄰近塞內加爾","examples":[{"en":"Florida was once attached to West Africa near Senegal.","zh":"佛羅里達曾經連接在鄰近塞內加爾的西非地區。"},{"en":"Near Senegal means close to the area of Senegal in West Africa.","zh":"near Senegal 指靠近西非塞內加爾一帶。"},{"en":"A shipping route near Senegal may pass along the west coast of Africa.","zh":"鄰近塞內加爾的航線可能沿非洲西岸經過。"},{"en":"Naming a nearby modern country helps readers imagine the ancient position more clearly.","zh":"命名附近現代國家有助讀者更清楚想像古代位置。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a geographical reference point.","zh":"這個短語提供地理參照點。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"collide with","meaning":"與……碰撞","examples":[{"en":"North America later collided with this landmass.","zh":"北美洲後來與這塊大陸碰撞。"},{"en":"To collide with something means to crash into it or come into forceful contact with it.","zh":"collide with something 指撞上某物或與它發生強力接觸。"},{"en":"Two bicycles may collide with each other if riders turn without looking.","zh":"如果騎車者轉彎前不看路，兩部單車可能互相碰撞。"},{"en":"When landmasses collide, they can join, fold rocks, or change continental shapes.","zh":"當大陸塊碰撞，它們可以連接、摺曲岩石或改變大陸形狀。"},{"en":"The phrase describes strong physical contact.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈實體接觸。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as Pangea was forming","meaning":"在盤古大陸形成期間","examples":[{"en":"The collision occurred as Pangea was forming.","zh":"這次碰撞發生在盤古大陸形成期間。"},{"en":"As Pangea was forming means during the period when the supercontinent was coming together.","zh":"as Pangea was forming 指在超大陸正逐漸組合形成的時期。"},{"en":"A school may make timetable changes as a new campus is forming.","zh":"學校可能在新校區形成期間更改時間表。"},{"en":"Events during the formation of Pangea affected where land pieces and species later ended up.","zh":"盤古大陸形成期間的事件影響了陸地碎片和物種後來的位置。"},{"en":"The phrase places an event within a larger process.","zh":"這個短語把事件放在較大過程之中。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rip away from","meaning":"從……分裂開來","examples":[{"en":"North America later ripped away from West Africa.","zh":"北美洲後來從西非分裂開來。"},{"en":"To rip away from something means to separate forcefully from it.","zh":"rip away from something 指以強力方式從某物分離。"},{"en":"A poster may rip away from a wall if the wind pulls it hard.","zh":"如果風猛烈拉扯，海報可能從牆上撕離。"},{"en":"When continents rip away from each other, oceans can open between them.","zh":"當大陸彼此分裂開來，海洋可能在中間形成。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests dramatic separation.","zh":"這個短語暗示劇烈分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take Florida with it","meaning":"把佛羅里達一同帶走","examples":[{"en":"North America took Florida with it when the continents separated.","zh":"當大陸分離時，北美洲把佛羅里達一同帶走。"},{"en":"To take Florida with it means that Florida moved along together with North America.","zh":"take Florida with it 指佛羅里達與北美洲一起移動。"},{"en":"A bus leaving the station takes all its passengers with it.","zh":"巴士離開車站時，會把所有乘客一同帶走。"},{"en":"If a land fragment moves with a larger continent, species on it move too.","zh":"如果陸地碎片隨較大大陸移動，上面的物種也會一同移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one part being carried along by a larger piece.","zh":"這個短語描述一部分被較大部分帶着走。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"come along for the ride","meaning":"順勢一同被帶走","examples":[{"en":"The ancestors of Florida’s harvestmen came along for the ride.","zh":"佛羅里達盲蛛的祖先順勢一同被帶走。"},{"en":"To come along for the ride means to be carried along with something else, often without choosing the movement.","zh":"come along for the ride 指隨某事物一起被帶走，通常不是自己選擇移動。"},{"en":"A child may come along for the ride when parents drive to the supermarket.","zh":"父母駕車去超市時，孩子可能順道一同前往。"},{"en":"The harvestmen did not travel actively; they moved because the land beneath them moved.","zh":"這些盲蛛不是主動旅行；牠們移動是因腳下土地移動。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and suggests passive travel with a larger movement.","zh":"這個短語較口語，暗示隨較大移動被動同行。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"dozens or even hundreds of","meaning":"數十甚至數百個……","examples":[{"en":"Giribet hopes to study dozens or even hundreds of species.","zh":"Giribet 希望研究數十甚至數百個物種。"},{"en":"Dozens or even hundreds of something means many items, possibly from around twenty-four to several hundred.","zh":"dozens or even hundreds of something 指許多項目，可能由約二十四個到數百個。"},{"en":"A teacher may read dozens or even hundreds of essays during exam season.","zh":"老師在考試季可能批改數十甚至數百篇作文。"},{"en":"Studying many species gives researchers stronger evidence than studying one or two.","zh":"研究許多物種比研究一兩個能提供更強證據。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a large and possibly expanding number.","zh":"這個短語強調數量龐大且可能擴大。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"find clues about","meaning":"找出關於……的線索","examples":[{"en":"The research may find new clues about plate tectonics.","zh":"這項研究可能找出關於板塊構造的新線索。"},{"en":"To find clues about something means to discover pieces of evidence that help explain it.","zh":"find clues about something 指發現有助解釋某事的證據片段。"},{"en":"A teacher may find clues about a student’s anxiety by reading repeated comments in her journal.","zh":"老師可能透過閱讀學生日記中反覆出現的留言，找出關於她焦慮的線索。"},{"en":"Small clues can lead to larger explanations when researchers connect them carefully.","zh":"當研究人員仔細連繫小線索，它們可以導向更大解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase describes discovering helpful evidence.","zh":"這個短語描述發現有用證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a single animal","meaning":"單一動物","examples":[{"en":"A single animal cannot reveal every geological pattern.","zh":"單一動物不能揭示每一種地質模式。"},{"en":"A single animal means one animal species or one individual animal, depending on context.","zh":"a single animal 按語境可指一個動物物種或一隻個體動物。"},{"en":"A doctor cannot judge a whole illness pattern from a single patient.","zh":"醫生不能只從單一病人判斷整個疾病模式。"},{"en":"One species may provide clues, but many species give a fuller picture.","zh":"一個物種可能提供線索，但許多物種能給出更完整圖像。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the limits of one example.","zh":"這個短語強調單一例子的限制。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"choose the correct letter","meaning":"選出正確字母","examples":[{"en":"Students choose the correct letter for each question.","zh":"學生為每題選出正確字母。"},{"en":"To choose the correct letter means to select the answer option marked by the right letter.","zh":"choose the correct letter 指選擇以正確字母標示的答案選項。"},{"en":"If option B matches the passage, students should write B clearly.","zh":"如果選項 B 符合文章，學生應清楚寫上 B。"},{"en":"Choosing the correct letter requires understanding meaning, not just recognising words.","zh":"選出正確字母需要理解意思，而不只是認出字詞。"},{"en":"The phrase is a standard multiple-choice instruction.","zh":"這個短語是標準選擇題指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"difficult to find","meaning":"難以找到","examples":[{"en":"Mite harvestmen are difficult to find in forest litter.","zh":"蟎盲蛛在森林落葉層中難以找到。"},{"en":"Difficult to find means not easy to see, locate, or discover.","zh":"difficult to find 指不容易看見、定位或發現。"},{"en":"A small black earring is difficult to find if it falls under a sofa.","zh":"如果黑色小耳環掉到梳化底，它會很難找到。"},{"en":"Tiny size, camouflage, and hiding behaviour can make an animal difficult to find.","zh":"細小體型、偽裝和隱藏行為可以令動物難以找到。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the challenge of locating something.","zh":"這個短語重點是尋找某物的困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"with the naked eye","meaning":"用肉眼","examples":[{"en":"Very small animals can still sometimes be seen with the naked eye.","zh":"非常細小的動物有時仍能用肉眼看見。"},{"en":"With the naked eye means without using a microscope, telescope, or other instrument.","zh":"with the naked eye 指不使用顯微鏡、望遠鏡或其他儀器。"},{"en":"Some planets can be seen with the naked eye on a clear night.","zh":"在晴朗夜晚，有些行星可以用肉眼看見。"},{"en":"If an animal cannot be seen with the naked eye, scientists need magnification or special tools.","zh":"如果動物不能用肉眼看見，科學家就需要放大工具或特殊工具。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ordinary human vision without equipment.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有設備下的普通人類視力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be confused with","meaning":"與……混淆","examples":[{"en":"The animal should not be confused with the daddy longlegs.","zh":"這種動物不應與長腳蛛混淆。"},{"en":"To be confused with something means to be mistaken for something similar.","zh":"be confused with something 指被誤認為相似的另一事物。"},{"en":"Learners often confuse “affect” with “effect” because the words look similar.","zh":"學習者常把 affect 與 effect 混淆，因為兩字外形相似。"},{"en":"Clear features help prevent one species from being confused with another.","zh":"清楚特徵有助防止一個物種與另一個混淆。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against mixing up two different things.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要把兩件不同事物搞亂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"distinguish from the surroundings","meaning":"與周圍環境區分","examples":[{"en":"The animals are difficult to distinguish from their surroundings.","zh":"這些動物很難與周圍環境區分。"},{"en":"To distinguish something from the surroundings means to see it as separate from what is around it.","zh":"distinguish something from the surroundings 指把某物看成與周圍事物分開。"},{"en":"A white phone is hard to distinguish from white bedsheets if it lies face down.","zh":"如果白色手機反轉放在白色床單上，就很難與周圍環境區分。"},{"en":"Camouflage works by making an animal look like its background.","zh":"偽裝的作用是令動物看似背景的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on visual separation from the environment.","zh":"這個短語重點是與環境作視覺分離。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"exist in large numbers","meaning":"大量存在","examples":[{"en":"The question asks whether they exist in large numbers in one place.","zh":"題目問牠們是否在同一地方大量存在。"},{"en":"To exist in large numbers means to be present in a high quantity.","zh":"exist in large numbers 指以很高數量存在。"},{"en":"Ants may exist in large numbers near food waste in a park.","zh":"螞蟻可能在公園食物垃圾附近大量存在。"},{"en":"If a species exists in large numbers, it may be easier to observe and study.","zh":"如果物種大量存在，它可能較容易被觀察和研究。"},{"en":"The phrase describes abundance, not wide distribution alone.","zh":"這個短語描述豐富數量，而不只是廣泛分布。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be of interest to","meaning":"令……感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Mite harvestmen are of interest to researchers studying geology.","zh":"蟎盲蛛令研究地質的研究人員感興趣。"},{"en":"To be of interest to someone means to be important, useful, or worth studying for that person.","zh":"be of interest to someone 指對某人而言重要、有用或值得研究。"},{"en":"Old school records may be of interest to historians studying education.","zh":"舊學校記錄可能令研究教育的歷史學家感興趣。"},{"en":"A tiny animal can be of interest if it provides evidence about a much larger question.","zh":"如果細小動物能提供關於更大問題的證據，它也可以有研究價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes research value or relevance.","zh":"這個短語描述研究價值或相關性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be studied far less than","meaning":"研究程度遠低於……","examples":[{"en":"The statement compares how much different species have been studied.","zh":"該陳述比較不同物種被研究的程度。"},{"en":"To be studied far less than something means to receive much less research attention than it.","zh":"be studied far less than something 指研究關注大幅少於另一事物。"},{"en":"Local dialects may be studied far less than standard languages.","zh":"本地方言的研究程度可能遠低於標準語言。"},{"en":"If a species is studied less, scientists may know very little about its behaviour or history.","zh":"如果某物種研究較少，科學家可能對其行為或歷史所知甚少。"},{"en":"The phrase compares research attention.","zh":"這個短語比較研究關注程度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"effects of climate on","meaning":"氣候對……的影響","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to the effects of climate on evolution.","zh":"選項提到氣候對演化的影響。"},{"en":"The effects of climate on something are the ways temperature, rain, and environmental conditions influence it.","zh":"effects of climate on something 指溫度、雨量和環境條件影響某事的方式。"},{"en":"The effects of climate on farming include changes in crop growth and water supply.","zh":"氣候對農業的影響包括作物生長和供水變化。"},{"en":"If climate changes, species may adapt, move, or die out over time.","zh":"如果氣候改變，物種可能隨時間適應、遷移或滅絕。"},{"en":"The phrase connects environmental conditions with a result.","zh":"這個短語把環境條件與結果連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unusual relationship with","meaning":"與……有不尋常的關係","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests an unusual relationship with other organisms.","zh":"該選項暗示與其他生物有不尋常的關係。"},{"en":"An unusual relationship with something is a connection that is not normal or expected.","zh":"unusual relationship with something 指不正常或不符合預期的聯繫。"},{"en":"A plant may have an unusual relationship with ants if the ants protect it from insects.","zh":"如果螞蟻保護植物免受昆蟲侵害，該植物可能與螞蟻有不尋常關係。"},{"en":"Unusual relationships can interest scientists because they may reveal hidden ecological processes.","zh":"不尋常關係會令科學家感興趣，因為它們可能揭示隱藏生態過程。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a surprising connection.","zh":"這個短語描述令人驚訝的聯繫。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"provide evidence relating to","meaning":"提供與……有關的證據","examples":[{"en":"The animals provide evidence relating to geological history.","zh":"這些動物提供與地質歷史有關的證據。"},{"en":"To provide evidence relating to something means to give information that supports or helps explain that topic.","zh":"provide evidence relating to something 指提供支持或幫助解釋該題目的資料。"},{"en":"Attendance records may provide evidence relating to why exam results fell.","zh":"出席紀錄可能提供與考試成績下降原因有關的證據。"},{"en":"Species distribution can provide evidence relating to ancient continental positions.","zh":"物種分布可以提供與古代大陸位置有關的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence connected to a larger question.","zh":"這個短語描述與較大問題相關的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"field outside entomology","meaning":"昆蟲學以外的領域","examples":[{"en":"The research contributes to a field outside entomology.","zh":"這項研究對昆蟲學以外的領域有貢獻。"},{"en":"A field outside entomology is an area of study other than insect science.","zh":"field outside entomology 指昆蟲科學以外的研究領域。"},{"en":"A study of bees may contribute to agriculture, a field outside entomology.","zh":"關於蜜蜂的研究可能對農業這個昆蟲學以外的領域有貢獻。"},{"en":"Research on small animals can help geology if their distribution records continental movement.","zh":"如果細小動物的分布記錄大陸移動，牠們的研究可以幫助地質學。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a study has value beyond its original subject.","zh":"這個短語顯示研究價值超越原本主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"factor contributing to","meaning":"促成……的因素","examples":[{"en":"The question asks about a factor contributing to Wegener’s theory.","zh":"題目問促成 Wegener 理論的一個因素。"},{"en":"A factor contributing to something is one cause or influence that helps produce it.","zh":"factor contributing to something 指有助造成某事的一個原因或影響。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can be a factor contributing to poor concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以是導致課堂專注力差的因素。"},{"en":"Similar fossils were one factor contributing to the idea of continental drift.","zh":"相似化石是促成大陸漂移概念的一個因素。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies one part of a larger explanation.","zh":"這個短語指出較大解釋中的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"present-day continents","meaning":"現今的大洲","examples":[{"en":"The present-day continents were once part of a single landmass.","zh":"現今的大洲曾經是單一大陸塊的一部分。"},{"en":"Present-day continents are the continents as they exist now.","zh":"present-day continents 指現時存在的大洲。"},{"en":"A map of present-day continents shows Africa, Asia, Europe, North America, South America, Australia, and Antarctica.","zh":"現今大洲地圖顯示非洲、亞洲、歐洲、北美洲、南美洲、澳洲和南極洲。"},{"en":"Comparing ancient landmasses with present-day continents helps explain how Earth’s surface changed.","zh":"比較古代陸塊與現今大洲，有助解釋地球表面如何改變。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts modern geography with ancient geography.","zh":"這個短語把現代地理與古代地理作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"changes in sea level","meaning":"海平面變化","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to changes in sea level.","zh":"選項提到海平面變化。"},{"en":"Changes in sea level are rises or falls in the height of the ocean surface.","zh":"changes in sea level 指海洋表面高度上升或下降。"},{"en":"Coastal towns may flood more often because of changes in sea level.","zh":"沿海城鎮可能因海平面變化而更常水浸。"},{"en":"Sea-level change can connect or separate land areas over long periods.","zh":"海平面變化可以在長時間中連接或分隔陸地。"},{"en":"The phrase describes ocean-height change, not ordinary waves.","zh":"這個短語描述海洋高度變化，而不是普通海浪。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"distance that species could travel","meaning":"物種能夠移動的距離","examples":[{"en":"Wegener considered the distance that species could travel.","zh":"Wegener 考慮了物種能夠移動的距離。"},{"en":"The distance that species could travel means how far organisms are able to move by themselves.","zh":"distance that species could travel 指生物能靠自己移動多遠。"},{"en":"A bird can travel a much greater distance than a tiny soil animal.","zh":"鳥類能移動的距離遠大於細小土壤動物。"},{"en":"If a species cannot travel far, its presence on distant continents needs another explanation.","zh":"如果物種不能移動很遠，它出現在遙遠大洲就需要另一種解釋。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on movement ability and geographic separation.","zh":"這個短語重點是移動能力和地理分隔。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"absence of certain fossils","meaning":"缺少某些化石","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to the absence of certain fossils.","zh":"選項提到缺少某些化石。"},{"en":"Absence of certain fossils means particular fossils are missing from a place where they might be expected.","zh":"absence of certain fossils 指某些化石在預期可能出現的地方缺失。"},{"en":"The absence of student records can make it hard to prove who attended a class.","zh":"缺少學生記錄可能令人難以證明誰上過課。"},{"en":"Missing fossils can be evidence, but only if researchers know where they should have appeared.","zh":"缺失的化石可以是證據，但前提是研究人員知道它們本應在哪裡出現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the significance of something not being found.","zh":"這個短語描述某物未被找到的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"living conditions","meaning":"生存環境","examples":[{"en":"The option compares living conditions on opposite sides of the Atlantic.","zh":"選項比較大西洋兩邊的生存環境。"},{"en":"Living conditions are the environmental or social conditions in which people, animals, or plants live.","zh":"living conditions 指人、動物或植物生活其中的環境或社會條件。"},{"en":"Good living conditions for students include safe housing, enough sleep, and a quiet study space.","zh":"學生的良好生活條件包括安全住屋、足夠睡眠和安靜學習空間。"},{"en":"If two regions have similar living conditions, similar species may survive in both places.","zh":"如果兩個地區有相似生存環境，相似物種可能能在兩地存活。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the situation that supports life.","zh":"這個短語描述支持生命的情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"point illustrated by","meaning":"由……說明的論點","examples":[{"en":"The reference to armadillos illustrates continental connection and separation.","zh":"提到犰狳說明了大陸連接和分離這個論點。"},{"en":"A point illustrated by something is an idea explained through an example.","zh":"point illustrated by something 指透過例子說明的想法。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a late bus as a point illustrated by poor transport planning.","zh":"老師可能用遲到巴士來說明交通規劃差這個論點。"},{"en":"Examples make abstract ideas clearer by showing them in a concrete case.","zh":"例子透過具體個案令抽象想法更清楚。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an example with the idea it supports.","zh":"這個短語把例子與它支持的想法連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"regions separate and connect","meaning":"地區分裂及連接","examples":[{"en":"Continental regions can separate and later become connected.","zh":"大陸地區可以分裂，之後又連接起來。"},{"en":"Regions separate and connect means areas of land can split apart and later join or link again.","zh":"regions separate and connect 指陸地區域可以分開，之後再連接或相通。"},{"en":"Two school departments may separate for different projects and connect again for a joint event.","zh":"兩個學校部門可能因不同項目而分開，之後為聯合活動再次連接。"},{"en":"When land regions separate and reconnect, animal distributions can change dramatically.","zh":"當陸地地區分裂又重新連接，動物分布可以大幅改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes changing relationships between areas.","zh":"這個短語描述區域之間關係的變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"travel longer distances","meaning":"移動更長距離","examples":[{"en":"Some animals can travel longer distances than others.","zh":"有些動物能比其他動物移動更長距離。"},{"en":"To travel longer distances means to move farther than another animal, person, or group.","zh":"travel longer distances 指比另一動物、人或群體移動得更遠。"},{"en":"A cyclist can travel longer distances than someone walking at the same speed for one hour.","zh":"在同一小時內，騎單車的人能比步行者移動更長距離。"},{"en":"Species that travel farther can colonise islands or cross barriers more easily.","zh":"能移動更遠的物種較容易在島嶼建立種群或穿越屏障。"},{"en":"The phrase compares movement range.","zh":"這個短語比較移動範圍。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"tend to spread","meaning":"往往向……擴散","examples":[{"en":"Some species tend to spread in a particular direction.","zh":"有些物種往往向特定方向擴散。"},{"en":"To tend to spread means to usually expand or move outward in a certain way.","zh":"tend to spread 指通常以某種方式向外擴展或移動。"},{"en":"A rumour may tend to spread faster in a small school where everyone talks.","zh":"在人人交談的小學校中，謠言往往擴散得更快。"},{"en":"If a species tends to spread north, climate or land connection may be involved.","zh":"如果物種往往向北擴散，氣候或陸地連接可能有關。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a usual pattern of expansion.","zh":"這個短語描述擴展的通常模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be stated in","meaning":"在……中被提及","examples":[{"en":"The question asks which idea is stated in the paragraph.","zh":"題目問哪個想法在該段中被提及。"},{"en":"To be stated in a text means to be directly said or clearly expressed there.","zh":"be stated in a text 指在文本中被直接說出或清楚表達。"},{"en":"If a rule is stated in the notice, students should not say it is only implied.","zh":"如果規則在通告中被提及，學生不應說它只是暗示。"},{"en":"In reading tests, stated information is easier to prove than guessed information.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，明確提及的資料比猜測資料更容易證明。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on what the text actually says.","zh":"這個短語重點是文本實際說了甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"habitat that supports","meaning":"能供……生存的棲息地","examples":[{"en":"An island habitat may support unusual bird species.","zh":"島嶼棲息地可能能供不尋常鳥類生存。"},{"en":"A habitat that supports a species provides the food, shelter, space, and conditions it needs to survive.","zh":"habitat that supports a species 指提供食物、遮蔽、空間和條件，使某物種能存活的棲息地。"},{"en":"A pond with clean water and plants can support frogs and dragonflies.","zh":"有乾淨水和植物的池塘可以支持青蛙和蜻蜓。"},{"en":"If a habitat supports unusual species, it may be important for conservation.","zh":"如果棲息地支持不尋常物種，它可能對保育很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an environment that allows life to continue.","zh":"這個短語描述能讓生命延續的環境。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be more likely to become extinct","meaning":"較有可能滅絕","examples":[{"en":"Some isolated species may be more likely to become extinct.","zh":"一些孤立物種可能較有可能滅絕。"},{"en":"To be more likely to become extinct means to have a higher risk of disappearing completely.","zh":"be more likely to become extinct 指完全消失的風險較高。"},{"en":"A rare plant in one small valley is more likely to become extinct if a fire destroys that valley.","zh":"如果一種稀有植物只在一個小山谷中生長，而火災摧毀該山谷，它就較有可能滅絕。"},{"en":"Small isolated populations have fewer chances to recover from disease or habitat loss.","zh":"細小孤立種群較少機會從疾病或棲息地喪失中恢復。"},{"en":"The phrase compares extinction risk.","zh":"這個短語比較滅絕風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"become flightless","meaning":"變得不會飛","examples":[{"en":"The goose became flightless after reaching Hawaii.","zh":"這種鵝到達夏威夷後變得不會飛。"},{"en":"To become flightless means to lose the ability to fly over evolutionary time.","zh":"become flightless 指在演化時間中失去飛行能力。"},{"en":"Island birds may become flightless if they no longer need to escape many predators.","zh":"如果島嶼鳥類不再需要逃避許多捕食者，牠們可能變得不會飛。"},{"en":"Becoming flightless can save energy, but it can also make a bird vulnerable.","zh":"變得不會飛可以節省能量，但也可以令鳥類變得脆弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an evolutionary change in movement ability.","zh":"這個短語描述移動能力上的演化變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"evidence of limited value","meaning":"價值有限的證據","examples":[{"en":"Cockroach evidence is of limited value for this research.","zh":"蟑螂證據對這項研究價值有限。"},{"en":"Evidence of limited value is evidence that is useful only a little or not enough to answer the question fully.","zh":"evidence of limited value 指只有少量用途或不足以完整回答問題的證據。"},{"en":"A single blurry photo is evidence of limited value if no one can identify the animal clearly.","zh":"如果沒有人能清楚辨認動物，一張模糊照片就是價值有限的證據。"},{"en":"If a species spreads too easily, its current location may not tell much about ancient continents.","zh":"如果物種太容易擴散，其現今位置未必能說明很多古代大陸情況。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence with weak usefulness.","zh":"這個短語描述用途較弱的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"spread too quickly","meaning":"擴散得太快","examples":[{"en":"Cockroaches spread too quickly to preserve clear geographic patterns.","zh":"蟑螂擴散得太快，無法保存清晰地理模式。"},{"en":"To spread too quickly means to move or expand so fast that earlier patterns become unclear.","zh":"spread too quickly 指移動或擴展得太快，以致早期模式變得不清楚。"},{"en":"A rumour may spread too quickly for teachers to find its original source.","zh":"謠言可能擴散得太快，以致老師難以找出原本來源。"},{"en":"Species that spread quickly may hide evidence of where they first evolved.","zh":"擴散迅速的物種可能掩蓋牠們最初在哪裡演化的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that rapid movement can reduce historical clarity.","zh":"這個短語顯示快速移動可以降低歷史清晰度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"reproduce too rapidly","meaning":"繁殖得太快","examples":[{"en":"The option suggests that cockroaches reproduce too rapidly.","zh":"選項暗示蟑螂繁殖得太快。"},{"en":"To reproduce too rapidly means to produce offspring very quickly and in large numbers.","zh":"reproduce too rapidly 指非常快速並大量產生後代。"},{"en":"Mosquitoes may reproduce too rapidly after heavy rain if standing water remains.","zh":"大雨後如果積水留下，蚊子可能繁殖得太快。"},{"en":"Rapid reproduction can help a species spread, but it does not always explain ancient distribution.","zh":"快速繁殖可以幫助物種擴散，但不一定解釋古代分布。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on fast population growth.","zh":"這個短語重點是快速人口增長。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"evolve into many species","meaning":"演化成許多物種","examples":[{"en":"Some animals evolve into many different species.","zh":"有些動物演化成許多不同物種。"},{"en":"To evolve into many species means one ancestral group gradually divides into several distinct species.","zh":"evolve into many species 指一個祖先群體逐漸分化成幾個不同物種。"},{"en":"Island finches may evolve into many species if different islands favour different beak shapes.","zh":"如果不同島嶼偏向不同鳥喙形狀，島嶼雀鳥可能演化成許多物種。"},{"en":"Environmental differences can push separate populations along different evolutionary paths.","zh":"環境差異可以推動分離種群走向不同演化路徑。"},{"en":"The phrase describes diversification over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間多樣化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"agree with the claims of","meaning":"與作者的說法一致","examples":[{"en":"Students decide whether statements agree with the writer’s claims.","zh":"學生判斷陳述是否與作者的說法一致。"},{"en":"To agree with the claims of someone means to match what that person says or argues.","zh":"agree with the claims of someone 指與某人所說或主張相符。"},{"en":"In a reading test, a statement agrees with the writer only if the passage clearly supports it.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，只有文章清楚支持時，陳述才與作者說法一致。"},{"en":"Students should not rely on outside knowledge when checking the writer’s claims.","zh":"學生檢查作者說法時不應依賴外部知識。"},{"en":"The phrase is used to test whether a statement fits the text.","zh":"這個短語用來測試陳述是否符合文本。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contradict the claims of","meaning":"與作者的說法相反","examples":[{"en":"A “No” answer contradicts the writer’s claims.","zh":"“No” 答案表示與作者的說法相反。"},{"en":"To contradict the claims of someone means to say the opposite of what that person argues.","zh":"contradict the claims of someone 指說出與某人主張相反的意思。"},{"en":"If a writer says an animal disperses poorly, a statement saying it spreads easily would contradict the claim.","zh":"如果作者說某動物不善於擴散，而陳述說牠容易擴散，就是與該說法相反。"},{"en":"In exams, contradiction must be based on clear meaning in the passage.","zh":"在考試中，矛盾必須基於文章中的清楚意思。"},{"en":"The phrase describes direct opposition to a stated view.","zh":"這個短語描述與明確觀點直接相反。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"impossible to say","meaning":"無法判斷","examples":[{"en":"Students choose “Not Given” when it is impossible to determine the writer’s view.","zh":"當無法判斷作者觀點時，學生選擇 “Not Given”。"},{"en":"Impossible to say means there is not enough information to decide confidently.","zh":"impossible to say 指資料不足，不能有信心作出判斷。"},{"en":"If a passage mentions a species’ DNA but not its colour, it is impossible to say what colour it is from that text.","zh":"如果文章提到物種 DNA 但沒有提到顏色，就無法從該文本判斷牠是甚麼顏色。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students should not invent evidence when the writer gives none.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，當作者沒有提供證據，學生不應自創證據。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the answer cannot be supported.","zh":"這個短語表示答案不能被支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"colonisation of Hawaii","meaning":"鵝在夏威夷建立種群","examples":[{"en":"The colonisation of Hawaii by geese involved dispersal rather than continental drift.","zh":"鵝在夏威夷建立種群涉及擴散，而不是大陸漂移。"},{"en":"Colonisation of Hawaii means a species arrived in Hawaii and established a population there.","zh":"colonisation of Hawaii 指某物種到達夏威夷並在那裏建立種群。"},{"en":"A plant’s colonisation of a new island can begin when seeds arrive by wind or birds.","zh":"植物在新島建立種群，可能由種子透過風或鳥類到達開始。"},{"en":"If geese reached Hawaii by flying or dispersal, the event does not prove continental drift.","zh":"如果鵝透過飛行或擴散到達夏威夷，該事件就不能證明大陸漂移。"},{"en":"The phrase describes biological settlement on the islands.","zh":"這個短語描述在群島上的生物定居。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"provide evidence of","meaning":"提供……的證據","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether the event provides evidence of continental drift.","zh":"該陳述問該事件是否提供大陸漂移的證據。"},{"en":"To provide evidence of something means to give facts or signs that support its existence or truth.","zh":"provide evidence of something 指提供支持某事存在或真實的事實或跡象。"},{"en":"A student’s improved essays provide evidence of better grammar control.","zh":"學生作文進步提供了文法控制改善的證據。"},{"en":"Similar species on separated continents can provide evidence of ancient land connections.","zh":"分離大洲上的相似物種可以提供古代陸地連接的證據。"},{"en":"The phrase describes support for a claim.","zh":"這個短語描述對某聲稱的支持。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reason why","meaning":"……的原因","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains the reason why mite harvestmen are absent from Hawaii.","zh":"文章解釋蟎盲蛛不出現在夏威夷的原因。"},{"en":"Reason why means the cause or explanation for something.","zh":"reason why 指某事的原因或解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask the reason why a student missed three lessons in one week.","zh":"老師可能詢問學生一星期缺席三堂課的原因。"},{"en":"Explaining the reason why helps readers understand the logic behind a fact.","zh":"解釋原因有助讀者理解某事實背後的邏輯。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces cause or explanation.","zh":"這個短語引入原因或解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"evolve more quickly than","meaning":"演化得比……快","examples":[{"en":"The statement compares how quickly the DNA of different species evolved.","zh":"該陳述比較不同物種 DNA 演化得有多快。"},{"en":"To evolve more quickly than another species means to change genetically or biologically at a faster rate.","zh":"evolve more quickly than another species 指以更快速度在遺傳或生物上改變。"},{"en":"Bacteria can evolve more quickly than large mammals because they reproduce rapidly.","zh":"細菌可能比大型哺乳動物演化得更快，因為牠們繁殖迅速。"},{"en":"Faster evolution may make comparisons harder if mutation rates differ greatly.","zh":"如果突變速率差異很大，較快演化可能令比較更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase compares evolutionary speed.","zh":"這個短語比較演化速度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"theory concerning","meaning":"關於……的理論","examples":[{"en":"The question refers to Dr Boyer’s theory concerning Florida’s origins.","zh":"題目提到 Boyer 博士關於佛羅里達起源的理論。"},{"en":"A theory concerning something is an explanation or idea about that topic.","zh":"theory concerning something 指關於某題目的解釋或想法。"},{"en":"A historian may propose a theory concerning why an old town was abandoned.","zh":"歷史學家可能提出關於舊城鎮為何被放棄的理論。"},{"en":"A theory about Florida’s origins can help explain why its species relate to Africa.","zh":"關於佛羅里達起源的理論可以幫助解釋其物種為何與非洲有關。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces the subject of a theory.","zh":"這個短語引入某理論的主題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be widely accepted","meaning":"被廣泛接受","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether the theory is widely accepted.","zh":"該陳述問該理論是否被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"To be widely accepted means to be believed or supported by many people in a field.","zh":"be widely accepted 指在某領域中被許多人相信或支持。"},{"en":"A teaching method may be widely accepted if many schools use it successfully.","zh":"如果許多學校成功使用某教學方法，它可能被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"A theory needs strong evidence before it becomes widely accepted.","zh":"理論需要強有力證據，才會被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"The phrase describes broad approval or agreement.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛認可或同意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"complete the summary","meaning":"完成摘要","examples":[{"en":"Students complete the summary using words from the list.","zh":"學生使用列表中的字詞完成摘要。"},{"en":"To complete the summary means to fill missing words in a shortened version of the passage.","zh":"complete the summary 指填補文章簡短版本中的缺漏字詞。"},{"en":"A student should read the whole summary before choosing words from the list.","zh":"學生應先讀完整個摘要，再從列表中選字。"},{"en":"Summary completion tests whether learners understand both meaning and grammar.","zh":"摘要填空測試學習者是否理解意思和文法。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common reading-exam instruction.","zh":"這個短語是常見閱讀考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"age and evolution","meaning":"年代及演化","examples":[{"en":"The summary describes the age and evolution of mite harvestmen.","zh":"摘要描述蟎盲蛛的年代及演化。"},{"en":"Age and evolution refers to how old a group is and how it has changed over time.","zh":"age and evolution 指某群體有多古老，以及它如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"A museum display may explain the age and evolution of dinosaurs using fossils and timelines.","zh":"博物館展示可能用化石和時間線解釋恐龍的年代及演化。"},{"en":"Knowing a species’ age can help scientists understand why its distribution is important.","zh":"知道物種年代可以幫助科學家理解其分布為何重要。"},{"en":"The phrase combines time depth with biological change.","zh":"這個短語結合時間深度與生物變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"first creatures to live on land","meaning":"最早在陸地生活的生物","examples":[{"en":"Their ancestors were among the first creatures to live on land.","zh":"牠們的祖先是最早在陸地生活的生物之一。"},{"en":"The first creatures to live on land were early animals that moved from water-based life to land habitats.","zh":"first creatures to live on land 指從水中生活轉向陸地棲息地的早期動物。"},{"en":"A science lesson may explain how early creatures needed body features that stopped them drying out on land.","zh":"科學課可能解釋早期生物需要能防止在陸地上乾死的身體特徵。"},{"en":"Being among the first land creatures means a group has an extremely ancient history.","zh":"屬於最早期陸生生物，代表該群體有極其古老的歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a major stage in the history of life.","zh":"這個短語指生命歷史中的重大階段。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"study differences in DNA","meaning":"研究DNA差異","examples":[{"en":"The researchers study differences in the animals’ DNA.","zh":"研究人員研究這些動物的 DNA 差異。"},{"en":"To study differences in DNA means to compare genetic sequences to find variation.","zh":"study differences in DNA 指比較遺傳序列以找出變異。"},{"en":"Doctors study differences in DNA to understand why some diseases run in families.","zh":"醫生研究 DNA 差異，以理解為何某些疾病會在家族中出現。"},{"en":"DNA differences can show how closely related two species are.","zh":"DNA 差異可以顯示兩個物種親緣關係有多近。"},{"en":"The phrase describes genetic comparison.","zh":"這個短語描述遺傳比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"trace the development of","meaning":"追溯……的發展","examples":[{"en":"Genetic evidence helps trace the development of different lineages.","zh":"遺傳證據幫助追溯不同譜系的發展。"},{"en":"To trace the development of something means to follow how it changed or grew over time.","zh":"trace the development of something 指跟隨某事如何隨時間改變或成長。"},{"en":"A teacher may trace the development of a student’s writing by comparing essays from September to June.","zh":"老師可能透過比較九月至六月的作文，追溯學生寫作發展。"},{"en":"Tracing development helps researchers see where branches split and how patterns formed.","zh":"追溯發展幫助研究人員看見分支在哪裏分裂，以及模式如何形成。"},{"en":"The phrase describes following a history step by step.","zh":"這個短語描述一步步追蹤歷史。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"branches of a species","meaning":"物種的分支","examples":[{"en":"An evolutionary tree contains several branches of a species group.","zh":"演化樹包含一個物種群的幾個分支。"},{"en":"Branches of a species are separate evolutionary lines that come from a common ancestor.","zh":"branches of a species 指來自共同祖先的不同演化線。"},{"en":"A family tree has branches when children and grandchildren form different family lines.","zh":"當子女和孫輩形成不同家族線，家譜就有分支。"},{"en":"In biology, branches show how groups split and develop in different directions.","zh":"在生物學中，分支顯示群體如何分裂並向不同方向發展。"},{"en":"The phrase uses a tree image to explain evolutionary relationships.","zh":"這個短語用樹的意象解釋演化關係。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reflect changes in","meaning":"反映……的變化","examples":[{"en":"The animals’ evolution reflects changes in continental locations.","zh":"這些動物的演化反映大陸位置的變化。"},{"en":"To reflect changes in something means to show or mirror those changes.","zh":"reflect changes in something 指顯示或映照某事的變化。"},{"en":"A student’s improved grades may reflect changes in study habits.","zh":"學生成績進步可能反映學習習慣的變化。"},{"en":"If animal lineages match shifting continents, their evolution reflects geological change.","zh":"如果動物譜系與移動大陸吻合，其演化就反映地質變化。"},{"en":"The phrase describes one pattern showing another pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述一種模式顯示另一種模式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"location of continents","meaning":"大陸的位置","examples":[{"en":"Their distribution reflects changes in the location of continents.","zh":"牠們的分布反映大陸位置的變化。"},{"en":"Location of continents means where the continents are or were positioned on Earth.","zh":"location of continents 指大陸現在或過去在地球上的位置。"},{"en":"Ancient maps of continental location look very different from modern maps.","zh":"古代大陸位置地圖與現代地圖看起來很不同。"},{"en":"When continental locations change, animals living on those lands move with them.","zh":"當大陸位置改變，生活在那些陸地上的動物會隨之移動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the position of landmasses.","zh":"這個短語描述大陸塊的位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"far apart","meaning":"相距很遠","examples":[{"en":"Related species now live in places that are far apart.","zh":"相關物種現在生活在相距很遠的地方。"},{"en":"Far apart means separated by a large distance.","zh":"far apart 指相隔很大距離。"},{"en":"Two friends may live far apart after one moves to another country.","zh":"如果一位朋友搬到另一個國家，兩個朋友可能相距很遠。"},{"en":"If related species live far apart, scientists may look for ancient connections between those places.","zh":"如果相關物種生活在相距很遠的地方，科學家可能尋找那些地方之間的古代連接。"},{"en":"The phrase describes distance, not emotional disagreement.","zh":"這個短語描述距離，而不是情感分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"used to form","meaning":"過去曾構成……","examples":[{"en":"These distant regions used to form part of Gondwana.","zh":"這些遙遠地區過去曾構成岡瓦納大陸的一部分。"},{"en":"Used to form part of something means once belonged to or made up part of it.","zh":"used to form part of something 指過去曾屬於或構成某物的一部分。"},{"en":"This classroom used to form part of the old library before the school was renovated.","zh":"這間課室在學校翻新前曾是舊圖書館的一部分。"},{"en":"If distant lands used to form one region, related species there may share ancient origins.","zh":"如果遙遠陸地過去曾構成同一地區，那裏的相關物種可能有古老共同起源。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a present place with its past structure.","zh":"這個短語把現今地方與其過去結構連起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"huge landmass","meaning":"巨大陸塊","examples":[{"en":"Gondwana was part of a huge landmass called Pangea.","zh":"岡瓦納大陸是名為盤古大陸的巨大陸塊的一部分。"},{"en":"A huge landmass is an extremely large continuous area of land.","zh":"huge landmass 指極其龐大的連續陸地區域。"},{"en":"Asia is a huge landmass compared with a small island.","zh":"與小島相比，亞洲是一塊巨大陸塊。"},{"en":"A huge landmass can allow species to spread widely before later separation occurs.","zh":"巨大陸塊可以讓物種在之後分離前廣泛擴散。"},{"en":"The phrase describes very large connected land.","zh":"這個短語描述非常大型的相連陸地。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 173 - The value of research into mite harvestmen.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 174":[{"front":"ecological importance","meaning":"生態重要性","examples":[{"en":"The passage explains the ecological importance of bees.","zh":"文章解釋蜜蜂的生態重要性。"},{"en":"Ecological importance means the value something has in keeping natural systems healthy and balanced.","zh":"ecological importance 指某物在維持自然系統健康和平衡方面的價值。"},{"en":"Trees have ecological importance because they provide shade, oxygen, and homes for animals.","zh":"樹木有生態重要性，因為它們提供樹蔭、氧氣和動物棲息地。"},{"en":"If bees disappear, their ecological importance becomes clear because many plants cannot reproduce normally.","zh":"如果蜜蜂消失，牠們的生態重要性就會變得明顯，因為許多植物不能正常繁殖。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why a species matters to the environment.","zh":"解釋某物種為何對環境重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"early Cretaceous period","meaning":"白堊紀早期","examples":[{"en":"Bees began to evolve sometime in the early Cretaceous period.","zh":"蜜蜂在白堊紀早期某個時候開始演化。"},{"en":"The early Cretaceous period was an ancient period in Earth’s history when many plants and animals were evolving.","zh":"early Cretaceous period 指地球歷史上一個古老時期，當時許多植物和動物正在演化。"},{"en":"A science teacher may mention the early Cretaceous period when explaining the history of flowering plants.","zh":"科學老師解釋開花植物歷史時，可能提到白堊紀早期。"},{"en":"Placing bees in the early Cretaceous period shows that their relationship with plants is very ancient.","zh":"把蜜蜂放在白堊紀早期，顯示牠們與植物的關係非常古老。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing evolution and geological time.","zh":"討論演化和地質年代時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the Earth’s history","meaning":"地球歷史","examples":[{"en":"The change occurred during an early period of the Earth’s history.","zh":"這種轉變發生在地球歷史早期的一個時期。"},{"en":"The Earth’s history means the long record of changes in the planet, from its formation to the present.","zh":"Earth’s history 指地球由形成至今的漫長變化記錄。"},{"en":"Fossils help students understand important events in the Earth’s history.","zh":"化石幫助學生理解地球歷史中的重要事件。"},{"en":"Studying the Earth’s history shows how living things changed as environments changed.","zh":"研究地球歷史顯示生物如何隨環境改變而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when placing natural events in a long time frame.","zh":"把自然事件放入長時間框架時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hunting wasps","meaning":"捕獵黃蜂","examples":[{"en":"Certain hunting wasps gradually developed into bees.","zh":"某些捕獵黃蜂逐漸發展成蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Hunting wasps are wasps that catch other insects for food.","zh":"hunting wasps 指捕捉其他昆蟲作食物的黃蜂。"},{"en":"A nature documentary may show hunting wasps carrying prey back to their nests.","zh":"自然紀錄片可能展示捕獵黃蜂把獵物帶回巢中。"},{"en":"When some hunting wasps began using pollen instead of insects, they started moving toward bee-like behaviour.","zh":"當某些捕獵黃蜂開始使用花粉而不是昆蟲，牠們就開始走向類似蜜蜂的行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the ancestors of bees.","zh":"描述蜜蜂祖先時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"of a certain type","meaning":"某一類的","examples":[{"en":"Hunting wasps of a certain type began to adopt a different diet.","zh":"某一類的捕獵黃蜂開始採用不同飲食。"},{"en":"Of a certain type means belonging to a particular kind or category.","zh":"of a certain type 指屬於某一特定種類或類別。"},{"en":"Students of a certain type enjoy open-ended questions more than fixed-answer drills.","zh":"某一類學生比起固定答案操練，更喜歡開放式問題。"},{"en":"When only insects of a certain type change behaviour, the change may not apply to all insects.","zh":"當只有某一類昆蟲改變行為，這種改變未必適用於所有昆蟲。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when narrowing a general group to a specific subgroup.","zh":"把一般群體收窄到特定小組時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"become bees by","meaning":"透過……變成蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"Some hunting wasps became bees by adopting a vegetarian diet.","zh":"一些捕獵黃蜂透過採用素食飲食變成蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Become bees by means changed into bees through a particular action or process.","zh":"become bees by 指透過某個行動或過程逐漸變成蜜蜂。"},{"en":"A small club can become successful by offering activities that students truly enjoy.","zh":"小型學會可以透過提供學生真正喜歡的活動而變得成功。"},{"en":"In evolution, small behavioural changes can gradually produce major differences over time.","zh":"在演化中，小小行為改變可以隨時間產生重大差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the method or process behind a change.","zh":"解釋改變背後的方法或過程時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"adopt a vegetarian diet","meaning":"採用素食飲食","examples":[{"en":"The ancestral wasps adopted a vegetarian diet based on pollen.","zh":"祖先黃蜂採用了以花粉為基礎的素食飲食。"},{"en":"To adopt a vegetarian diet means to start eating plant-based food instead of animal-based food.","zh":"adopt a vegetarian diet 指開始吃植物性食物，而不是動物性食物。"},{"en":"A person may adopt a vegetarian diet for health, religion, or environmental reasons.","zh":"一個人可能因健康、宗教或環境原因採用素食飲食。"},{"en":"When the ancestral wasps adopted pollen as food, their relationship with flowers changed.","zh":"當祖先黃蜂採用花粉作食物，牠們與花的關係就改變了。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a shift in eating habits.","zh":"描述飲食習慣轉變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rely more and more on","meaning":"越來越依賴……","examples":[{"en":"The insects began to rely more and more on plant pollen.","zh":"這些昆蟲開始越來越依賴植物花粉。"},{"en":"To rely more and more on something means to depend on it increasingly over time.","zh":"rely more and more on something 指隨時間越來越依靠某物。"},{"en":"Students may rely more and more on online dictionaries when reading difficult articles.","zh":"學生閱讀困難文章時，可能越來越依賴網上字典。"},{"en":"As insects used pollen more often, flowers became more important to their survival.","zh":"隨着昆蟲更常使用花粉，花對牠們的生存變得更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when dependence gradually increases.","zh":"描述依賴逐漸增加時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pollen of plants","meaning":"植物花粉","examples":[{"en":"Bees obtain protein from the pollen of plants.","zh":"蜜蜂從植物花粉中取得蛋白質。"},{"en":"The pollen of plants is the fine powder produced by flowers and used in plant reproduction.","zh":"pollen of plants 指花朵產生、用於植物繁殖的細粉。"},{"en":"People with allergies may sneeze when pollen of plants spreads through the air.","zh":"當植物花粉在空氣中飄散，有過敏的人可能打噴嚏。"},{"en":"For bees, plant pollen is not just dust; it is an important food source.","zh":"對蜜蜂來說，植物花粉不只是粉末，而是重要食物來源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing flowers, bees, and reproduction.","zh":"討論花、蜜蜂和繁殖時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a source of protein","meaning":"蛋白質來源","examples":[{"en":"Pollen became a major source of protein for early bees.","zh":"花粉成為早期蜜蜂的主要蛋白質來源。"},{"en":"A source of protein is food that provides protein for growth, repair, and energy.","zh":"source of protein 指提供蛋白質以供生長、修復和能量使用的食物。"},{"en":"Eggs, beans, fish, and tofu can be sources of protein in a human diet.","zh":"雞蛋、豆類、魚和豆腐都可以是人類飲食中的蛋白質來源。"},{"en":"When bees collect pollen, they are collecting a source of protein for themselves and their young.","zh":"當蜜蜂採集花粉，牠們是在為自己和幼蟲收集蛋白質來源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the nutritional value of food.","zh":"解釋食物營養價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"offspring","meaning":"後代","examples":[{"en":"The bees gathered pollen for themselves and their offspring.","zh":"蜜蜂為自己和後代採集花粉。"},{"en":"Offspring means the young or children of a person, animal, or plant.","zh":"offspring 指人、動物或植物的幼體或子代。"},{"en":"Birds feed their offspring until the young birds can fly and find food.","zh":"鳥會餵養後代，直到幼鳥能飛行和覓食。"},{"en":"Animals often change their behaviour when they need to protect or feed their offspring.","zh":"當動物需要保護或餵養後代，牠們常會改變行為。"},{"en":"This word is common in biology and animal behaviour.","zh":"這個詞常見於生物學和動物行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as an alternative to","meaning":"作為……的替代品","examples":[{"en":"They used pollen as an alternative to eating insects.","zh":"牠們用花粉作為吃昆蟲的替代品。"},{"en":"As an alternative to something means instead of that option.","zh":"as an alternative to something 指作為某選項的替代。"},{"en":"A student may use flashcards as an alternative to rereading the same notes.","zh":"學生可以使用單詞卡作為反覆重讀同一份筆記的替代方法。"},{"en":"When pollen became an alternative food, bees no longer had to depend only on hunted insects.","zh":"當花粉成為替代食物，蜜蜂就不再只依賴捕獵昆蟲。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing two possible choices.","zh":"比較兩個可能選擇時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in so doing","meaning":"在這樣做的過程中","examples":[{"en":"In so doing, the insects accidentally carried pollen between plants.","zh":"在這樣做的過程中，這些昆蟲意外地在植物之間攜帶花粉。"},{"en":"In so doing means while doing that action, or as a result of doing it.","zh":"in so doing 指在做那件事時，或因做那件事而。"},{"en":"A teacher may correct one essay carefully; in so doing, she notices a common class mistake.","zh":"老師仔細批改一篇文章；在這樣做的過程中，她注意到全班常見錯誤。"},{"en":"The insects were seeking food, but in so doing they helped plants reproduce.","zh":"這些昆蟲是在尋找食物，但在這樣做的過程中幫助植物繁殖。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one action creates an extra result.","zh":"當一個行動產生額外結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"accidentally transport","meaning":"意外運送","examples":[{"en":"The early bees accidentally transported pollen on their bodies.","zh":"早期蜜蜂意外地把花粉運送在身體上。"},{"en":"To accidentally transport something means to carry it from one place to another without intending to.","zh":"accidentally transport something 指無意中把某物從一地帶到另一地。"},{"en":"A traveller may accidentally transport seeds on muddy shoes after walking through a field.","zh":"旅客穿過田地後，可能在沾泥鞋子上意外運送種子。"},{"en":"Bees did not plan to help plants, but they accidentally transported pollen while feeding.","zh":"蜜蜂並沒有計劃幫助植物，但牠們取食時意外運送花粉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when movement happens unintentionally.","zh":"描述非故意移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on their bodies","meaning":"在牠們的身體上","examples":[{"en":"The bees carried pollen on their bodies to other flowers.","zh":"蜜蜂把花粉帶在牠們的身體上，到其他花朵去。"},{"en":"On their bodies means attached to or located on the outside of their physical bodies.","zh":"on their bodies 指附着於或位於牠們身體外部。"},{"en":"Dogs may carry dust on their bodies after running through a dry field.","zh":"狗在乾田中奔跑後，身體上可能帶着灰塵。"},{"en":"Pollen on bees’ bodies can rub off when they land on another flower.","zh":"蜜蜂身體上的花粉在牠們降落到另一朵花時，可以被擦落。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing where something is carried.","zh":"描述某物被帶在哪裏時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"plants of the same species","meaning":"同一品種的植物","examples":[{"en":"The pollen was transported to other plants of the same species.","zh":"花粉被運送到同一品種的其他植物。"},{"en":"Plants of the same species are plants that belong to the same biological kind and can usually reproduce with one another.","zh":"plants of the same species 指屬於同一生物種類、通常可以彼此繁殖的植物。"},{"en":"Apple trees of the same species may share pollen through insects.","zh":"同一品種的蘋果樹可能透過昆蟲互相傳遞花粉。"},{"en":"Pollination works best when pollen reaches a compatible plant of the same species.","zh":"當花粉到達兼容的同一品種植物時，授粉效果最好。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing plant reproduction.","zh":"討論植物繁殖時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"bring about pollination","meaning":"促成授粉","examples":[{"en":"The accidental movement of pollen helped bring about pollination.","zh":"花粉的意外移動有助促成授粉。"},{"en":"To bring about pollination means to cause or make pollination happen.","zh":"bring about pollination 指造成或令授粉發生。"},{"en":"A gardener may plant flowers that attract bees to bring about pollination in a vegetable garden.","zh":"園丁可能種植吸引蜜蜂的花，以在菜園中促成授粉。"},{"en":"Without insects moving pollen, pollination may not occur in many flowering plants.","zh":"沒有昆蟲移動花粉，許多開花植物可能不會授粉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how a process is caused.","zh":"解釋一個過程如何被促成時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the stage was set for","meaning":"為……創造條件","examples":[{"en":"The stage was set for closer adaptation between bees and plants.","zh":"這為蜜蜂和植物之間更緊密的適應創造條件。"},{"en":"The stage was set for something means the necessary conditions were ready for it to happen.","zh":"the stage was set for something 指某事發生所需條件已經準備好。"},{"en":"Once students understand basic grammar, the stage is set for more advanced writing.","zh":"一旦學生理解基本文法，就為更高階寫作創造條件。"},{"en":"When bees began carrying pollen, the conditions were ready for a deeper plant–bee relationship.","zh":"當蜜蜂開始攜帶花粉，就為更深層的植物與蜜蜂關係創造了條件。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how one development prepares for another.","zh":"解釋一個發展如何為另一個發展鋪路時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a succession of","meaning":"一連串的……","examples":[{"en":"A succession of mutual adaptations followed over time.","zh":"隨時間出現一連串相互適應。"},{"en":"A succession of something means a series of things happening one after another.","zh":"succession of something 指一系列事情一件接一件發生。"},{"en":"A student may improve through a succession of small corrections and better drafts.","zh":"學生可能透過一連串小修正和更好的草稿而進步。"},{"en":"One adaptation can lead to another, creating a long chain of changes.","zh":"一種適應可以導致另一種適應，形成一長串變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing repeated developments over time.","zh":"描述隨時間重複出現的發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ever-closer mutual adaptations","meaning":"日益緊密的相互適應","examples":[{"en":"Bees and flowers developed ever-closer mutual adaptations.","zh":"蜜蜂和花發展出日益緊密的相互適應。"},{"en":"Ever-closer mutual adaptations are changes in two living things that make them increasingly suited to each other.","zh":"ever-closer mutual adaptations 指兩種生物的變化令它們越來越適合彼此。"},{"en":"A plant may develop a flower shape that fits the body of a particular pollinator.","zh":"植物可能發展出適合某種授粉者身體的花形。"},{"en":"When both sides change in response to each other, their relationship can become more specialised.","zh":"當雙方因應彼此而改變，牠們的關係可以變得更專門化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing co-evolution.","zh":"討論共同演化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"flowering plants","meaning":"開花植物","examples":[{"en":"Flowering plants evolved features that attracted bees.","zh":"開花植物演化出吸引蜜蜂的特徵。"},{"en":"Flowering plants are plants that produce flowers as part of reproduction.","zh":"flowering plants 指以開花作為繁殖一部分的植物。"},{"en":"Apple trees, roses, sunflowers, and orchids are flowering plants.","zh":"蘋果樹、玫瑰、向日葵和蘭花都是開花植物。"},{"en":"Flowers can attract insects with colour, scent, pollen, and nectar.","zh":"花可以透過顏色、氣味、花粉和花蜜吸引昆蟲。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing plant reproduction and pollination.","zh":"討論植物繁殖和授粉時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in particular","meaning":"尤其是","examples":[{"en":"In particular, flowers began offering richer rewards to bees.","zh":"尤其是，花開始向蜜蜂提供更豐富的回報。"},{"en":"In particular means especially or more specifically.","zh":"in particular 指尤其是，或更具體地說。"},{"en":"Students often struggle with grammar; in particular, they find articles difficult.","zh":"學生常在文法上遇到困難；尤其是，他們覺得冠詞很難。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows a general point to one important example.","zh":"這個短語把一般觀點收窄到一個重要例子。"},{"en":"It is useful when highlighting a specific detail.","zh":"突出具體細節時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reward bees for","meaning":"因……而回饋蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"Flowers reward bees for helping with their reproduction.","zh":"花因蜜蜂幫助其繁殖而回饋蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To reward bees for something means to give bees food or benefits in return for what they do.","zh":"reward bees for something 指因蜜蜂做了某事而給牠們食物或好處作回報。"},{"en":"A teacher may reward students for careful reading by praising their accurate answers.","zh":"老師可能因學生仔細閱讀而稱讚其準確答案，以作回報。"},{"en":"Flowers provide nectar and pollen, and bees help transfer pollen between plants.","zh":"花提供花蜜和花粉，而蜜蜂幫助植物之間轉移花粉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining exchange or mutual benefit.","zh":"解釋交換或互惠時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"unwitting role","meaning":"無意中擔當的角色","examples":[{"en":"Bees perform an unwitting role in plant reproduction.","zh":"蜜蜂在植物繁殖中無意中擔當一個角色。"},{"en":"An unwitting role is a role someone or something plays without knowing or intending it.","zh":"unwitting role 指某人或某物在不知道或無意之下擔當的角色。"},{"en":"A child may play an unwitting role in spreading a new word at school by repeating it to friends.","zh":"孩子把一個新詞重複給朋友聽，可能無意中在學校傳播這個詞。"},{"en":"Bees seek food, but they unwittingly help plants reproduce while doing so.","zh":"蜜蜂尋找食物，但在這樣做時無意中幫助植物繁殖。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an important effect is accidental.","zh":"當重要效果是偶然產生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"plant reproduction","meaning":"植物繁殖","examples":[{"en":"Pollination is essential to the reproduction of many plants.","zh":"授粉對許多植物的繁殖至關重要。"},{"en":"Plant reproduction is the process by which plants produce new plants.","zh":"plant reproduction 指植物產生新植物的過程。"},{"en":"Seeds, flowers, pollen, and fruit can all be involved in plant reproduction.","zh":"種子、花、花粉和果實都可以涉及植物繁殖。"},{"en":"If pollination fails, plant reproduction may also fail for many species.","zh":"如果授粉失敗，許多物種的植物繁殖也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in biology and ecology.","zh":"這個短語適用於生物學和生態學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"provide richer sources of","meaning":"提供更豐富的……來源","examples":[{"en":"Flowers began to provide richer sources of pollen.","zh":"花開始提供更豐富的花粉來源。"},{"en":"To provide richer sources of something means to offer more abundant or more valuable supplies of it.","zh":"provide richer sources of something 指提供更充足或更有價值的某物供應。"},{"en":"A school library can provide richer sources of reading material than a small classroom shelf.","zh":"學校圖書館可以比小小課室書架提供更豐富的閱讀材料來源。"},{"en":"When flowers offered better pollen rewards, bees had more reason to visit them.","zh":"當花提供更好的花粉回報，蜜蜂就有更多理由造訪。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing improved supply or reward.","zh":"描述供應或回報改善時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"another source of nutrition","meaning":"另一種營養來源","examples":[{"en":"Nectar gave bees another source of nutrition.","zh":"花蜜給蜜蜂另一種營養來源。"},{"en":"Another source of nutrition means an additional food supply that provides energy or nutrients.","zh":"another source of nutrition 指提供能量或營養的額外食物來源。"},{"en":"Milk can be another source of nutrition for children who do not eat much solid food.","zh":"對不太吃固體食物的孩子來說，牛奶可以是另一種營養來源。"},{"en":"When bees gained nectar as well as pollen, their diet became richer.","zh":"當蜜蜂除了花粉還獲得花蜜，牠們的飲食變得更豐富。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing food and energy sources.","zh":"討論食物和能量來源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"nectar","meaning":"花蜜","examples":[{"en":"Bees collect nectar from flowers as an energy-rich food.","zh":"蜜蜂從花朵採集花蜜，作為富含能量的食物。"},{"en":"Nectar is a sweet liquid produced by flowers that attracts pollinators.","zh":"nectar 指花產生、用來吸引授粉者的甜液體。"},{"en":"A child may see bees drinking nectar from flowers in a garden.","zh":"孩子可能在花園看到蜜蜂從花朵吸食花蜜。"},{"en":"Nectar gives bees energy, while bees help flowers move pollen.","zh":"花蜜給蜜蜂能量，而蜜蜂幫助花朵轉移花粉。"},{"en":"This word is important in discussions of bees and pollination.","zh":"這個詞在討論蜜蜂和授粉時很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"consist of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"About 15 per cent of the human diet consists of bee-pollinated crops.","zh":"人類飲食約百分之十五由蜜蜂授粉的農作物組成。"},{"en":"Consist of means be made up of particular parts or materials.","zh":"consist of 指由特定部分或材料組成。"},{"en":"A healthy lunch may consist of rice, vegetables, protein, and fruit.","zh":"健康午餐可能由米飯、蔬菜、蛋白質和水果組成。"},{"en":"If part of our diet consists of bee-pollinated crops, bees affect what we eat.","zh":"如果我們部分飲食由蜜蜂授粉作物組成，蜜蜂就影響我們吃甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing components of a whole.","zh":"描述整體的組成部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"crops pollinated by bees","meaning":"由蜜蜂授粉的農作物","examples":[{"en":"Many important crops are pollinated by bees.","zh":"許多重要農作物由蜜蜂授粉。"},{"en":"Crops pollinated by bees are food plants that depend on bees to move pollen and help them produce fruit or seeds.","zh":"crops pollinated by bees 指依靠蜜蜂移動花粉、幫助結果或結籽的食用植物。"},{"en":"Apples, almonds, and some berries are examples of crops that may rely on bee pollination.","zh":"蘋果、杏仁和某些莓果都是可能依賴蜜蜂授粉的農作物例子。"},{"en":"If bee numbers fall, crops pollinated by bees may produce less food.","zh":"如果蜜蜂數量下降，由蜜蜂授粉的農作物可能產量減少。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the link between insects and agriculture.","zh":"解釋昆蟲與農業之間的連繫時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"animal products","meaning":"動物產品","examples":[{"en":"Many animal products also depend indirectly on bee activity.","zh":"許多動物產品也間接依賴蜜蜂活動。"},{"en":"Animal products are foods or materials that come from animals, such as milk, meat, eggs, or wool.","zh":"animal products 指來自動物的食物或材料，例如牛奶、肉、蛋或羊毛。"},{"en":"A supermarket sells animal products such as cheese, yoghurt, chicken, and eggs.","zh":"超級市場售賣芝士、乳酪、雞肉和雞蛋等動物產品。"},{"en":"If livestock eat crops pollinated by bees, animal products can depend indirectly on bees.","zh":"如果牲畜吃由蜜蜂授粉的作物，動物產品就可以間接依賴蜜蜂。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing food chains and agriculture.","zh":"討論食物鏈和農業時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ultimately derive from","meaning":"最終源自……","examples":[{"en":"Some foods ultimately derive from bee-pollinated forage crops.","zh":"有些食物最終源自由蜜蜂授粉的飼料作物。"},{"en":"Ultimately derive from means finally come from a particular original source.","zh":"ultimately derive from 指最終來自某個原始來源。"},{"en":"Many plastic products ultimately derive from oil.","zh":"許多塑膠產品最終源自石油。"},{"en":"Milk may seem unrelated to bees, but it can ultimately derive from animals eating bee-pollinated feed crops.","zh":"牛奶看似與蜜蜂無關，但它可能最終源自動物食用蜜蜂授粉的飼料作物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when tracing something back to its deeper source.","zh":"追溯某物更深來源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"bee-pollinated forage crops","meaning":"由蜜蜂授粉的飼料作物","examples":[{"en":"Livestock consume bee-pollinated forage crops.","zh":"牲畜食用由蜜蜂授粉的飼料作物。"},{"en":"Bee-pollinated forage crops are animal-feed plants that rely on bees for pollination.","zh":"bee-pollinated forage crops 指依靠蜜蜂授粉的動物飼料植物。"},{"en":"Cattle may eat forage crops that first needed insects to help them reproduce.","zh":"牛可能吃一些先需要昆蟲幫助繁殖的飼料作物。"},{"en":"When bees pollinate forage crops, they indirectly support animals raised for food.","zh":"當蜜蜂為飼料作物授粉，牠們就間接支援供人食用的動物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining indirect links between bees and human diets.","zh":"解釋蜜蜂與人類飲食之間的間接連繫時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"account for","meaning":"佔……","examples":[{"en":"Animal products account for another 15 per cent of our diet.","zh":"動物產品佔我們飲食中另外百分之十五。"},{"en":"Account for means make up a particular part or percentage of a total.","zh":"account for 指構成整體中的某一部分或百分比。"},{"en":"Transport costs may account for a large part of a family’s monthly budget.","zh":"交通費可能佔家庭每月預算的一大部分。"},{"en":"If animal products account for a large share of the diet, their production matters greatly.","zh":"如果動物產品佔飲食中很大比例，其生產就非常重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining proportions.","zh":"解釋比例時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"it follows that","meaning":"由此可見","examples":[{"en":"It follows that about one-third of our food depends on bees.","zh":"由此可見，我們約三分之一的食物依賴蜜蜂。"},{"en":"It follows that means this conclusion naturally comes from the facts just given.","zh":"it follows that 指這個結論自然來自剛才給出的事實。"},{"en":"If a student never attends class and never studies, it follows that their progress will be slow.","zh":"如果學生從不上課也不溫習，由此可見，他的進步會很慢。"},{"en":"After adding direct and indirect food sources, it follows that bees affect a large part of our diet.","zh":"加上直接和間接食物來源後，由此可見蜜蜂影響我們飲食的大部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when drawing a logical conclusion.","zh":"推出邏輯結論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"around one-third of","meaning":"約三分之一的……","examples":[{"en":"Around one-third of human food is linked to bee pollination.","zh":"約三分之一的人類食物與蜜蜂授粉有關。"},{"en":"Around one-third of something means about one part out of three equal parts.","zh":"around one-third of something 指約三等份中的一份。"},{"en":"Around one-third of a class may choose science as their favourite subject.","zh":"約三分之一的班級學生可能選擇科學作為最喜歡的科目。"},{"en":"Saying around one-third shows an approximate but meaningful proportion.","zh":"說 around one-third 顯示一個大約但有意義的比例。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving estimated quantities.","zh":"提供估算數量時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"directly or indirectly","meaning":"直接或間接地","examples":[{"en":"Our food supply is directly or indirectly dependent on bees.","zh":"我們的食物供應直接或間接依賴蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Directly or indirectly means either in an immediate way or through another step in between.","zh":"directly or indirectly 指以直接方式，或透過中間步驟發生。"},{"en":"A teacher can help students directly through lessons and indirectly by encouraging confidence.","zh":"老師可以透過課堂直接幫助學生，也可以透過鼓勵信心間接幫助。"},{"en":"Bees support food directly by pollinating crops and indirectly by supporting animal feed.","zh":"蜜蜂透過為作物授粉直接支援食物，也透過支援動物飼料間接支援食物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when influence happens in more than one way.","zh":"當影響以多於一種方式發生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be dependent on","meaning":"依賴……","examples":[{"en":"Many crops are dependent on pollinating insects.","zh":"許多農作物依賴授粉昆蟲。"},{"en":"To be dependent on something means to need it in order to survive, function, or succeed.","zh":"be dependent on something 指需要某物才能生存、運作或成功。"},{"en":"A child may be dependent on adults for food, transport, and safety.","zh":"孩子可能依賴成人提供食物、交通和安全。"},{"en":"If a crop is dependent on insects, poor pollination can reduce its yield.","zh":"如果農作物依賴昆蟲，授粉不足可以降低產量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining reliance.","zh":"解釋依賴關係時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pollinating services","meaning":"授粉服務","examples":[{"en":"Bees provide essential pollinating services to agriculture.","zh":"蜜蜂為農業提供必不可少的授粉服務。"},{"en":"Pollinating services are the natural work of moving pollen so plants can produce seeds or fruit.","zh":"pollinating services 指移動花粉、使植物能結籽或結果的自然工作。"},{"en":"Farmers benefit from pollinating services when bees visit fruit trees in spring.","zh":"春天蜜蜂造訪果樹時，農民就受益於授粉服務。"},{"en":"Without these services, many crops would produce less food.","zh":"沒有這些服務，許多農作物產量會較低。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the economic value of natural processes.","zh":"描述自然過程的經濟價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on a global basis","meaning":"在全球層面","examples":[{"en":"On a global basis, bee pollination has enormous economic value.","zh":"在全球層面，蜜蜂授粉有巨大經濟價值。"},{"en":"On a global basis means when considered across the whole world.","zh":"on a global basis 指從整個世界範圍來看。"},{"en":"On a global basis, clean water shortages affect millions of people.","zh":"在全球層面，清潔食水短缺影響數以百萬計的人。"},{"en":"Looking globally shows that bee pollination is not just a local farming issue.","zh":"從全球角度看，蜜蜂授粉不只是本地農業問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing worldwide importance.","zh":"討論全球重要性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"annual value","meaning":"每年價值","examples":[{"en":"The annual value of bee-dependent crops is extremely high.","zh":"依賴蜜蜂的作物每年價值極高。"},{"en":"Annual value means the amount of money something is worth in one year.","zh":"annual value 指某物在一年中的金錢價值。"},{"en":"A company may calculate the annual value of its online sales.","zh":"公司可能計算網上銷售的每年價值。"},{"en":"Estimating annual value helps people understand economic importance.","zh":"估算每年價值幫助人們理解經濟重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing money and yearly production.","zh":"討論金錢和年度生產時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"agricultural crops","meaning":"農作物","examples":[{"en":"Many agricultural crops require insect pollination.","zh":"許多農作物需要昆蟲授粉。"},{"en":"Agricultural crops are plants grown by farmers for food, animal feed, fibre, or other uses.","zh":"agricultural crops 指農民種植作食物、動物飼料、纖維或其他用途的植物。"},{"en":"Rice, wheat, apples, beans, and cotton are agricultural crops.","zh":"稻米、小麥、蘋果、豆類和棉花都是農作物。"},{"en":"When agricultural crops depend on insects, farming depends partly on healthy ecosystems.","zh":"當農作物依賴昆蟲，農業就部分依賴健康生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing farming and food production.","zh":"討論農業和糧食生產時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be estimated at","meaning":"估計為……","examples":[{"en":"The value of the crops is estimated at £1,000 million.","zh":"這些作物的價值估計為十億英鎊。"},{"en":"To be estimated at means to be judged approximately to have a certain value, size, or amount.","zh":"be estimated at 指被大約判斷為某個價值、大小或數量。"},{"en":"The cost of repairing the school roof was estimated at two million dollars.","zh":"維修學校屋頂的成本估計為二百萬美元。"},{"en":"Estimates help people discuss value even when the exact figure is difficult to know.","zh":"即使精確數字難以知道，估算也幫助人們討論價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving approximate figures.","zh":"提供大約數字時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"much of this pollination","meaning":"大部分這類授粉","examples":[{"en":"Much of this pollination is carried out by honey bees.","zh":"大部分這類授粉由蜜蜂完成。"},{"en":"Much of this pollination means a large part of the pollen-transfer work just mentioned.","zh":"much of this pollination 指剛才提到的花粉轉移工作中的大部分。"},{"en":"Much of the cleaning in a school may be done after students leave.","zh":"學校大部分清潔工作可能在學生離開後完成。"},{"en":"If much of pollination depends on honey bees, their health becomes economically important.","zh":"如果大部分授粉依賴蜜蜂，牠們的健康就變得有經濟重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when referring back to a large portion of a previous idea.","zh":"指回前文某想法的大部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be due to","meaning":"歸功於……","examples":[{"en":"Much of the world’s crop pollination is due to honey bees.","zh":"世界上大部分作物授粉歸功於蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Be due to means be caused by or result from something.","zh":"be due to 指由某事造成或源自某事。"},{"en":"The delay was due to heavy traffic near the station.","zh":"延誤是由於車站附近交通擠塞。"},{"en":"If crop pollination is due to bees, losing bees can reduce food production.","zh":"如果作物授粉歸功於蜜蜂，失去蜜蜂就可能減少糧食生產。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining causes.","zh":"解釋原因時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"honey bees","meaning":"蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"Honey bees provide economically valuable pollinating services.","zh":"蜜蜂提供具有經濟價值的授粉服務。"},{"en":"Honey bees are bees that live in colonies and produce honey while also pollinating plants.","zh":"honey bees 指群居並製造蜂蜜，同時為植物授粉的蜜蜂。"},{"en":"A beekeeper may keep honey bees near orchards to support fruit production.","zh":"養蜂人可能把蜜蜂養在果園附近，以支援水果生產。"},{"en":"Honey bees are valuable not only for honey but also for the crops they help produce.","zh":"蜜蜂的價值不只在蜂蜜，也在牠們幫助生產的農作物。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in agriculture, ecology, and food production.","zh":"這個短語在農業、生態和糧食生產中很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in monetary terms","meaning":"以金錢計算","examples":[{"en":"In monetary terms, pollination is more valuable than honey production.","zh":"以金錢計算，授粉比蜂蜜生產更有價值。"},{"en":"In monetary terms means when measured by money or economic value.","zh":"in monetary terms 指以金錢或經濟價值衡量。"},{"en":"In monetary terms, free public parks may seem cheap, but their health benefits are huge.","zh":"以金錢計算，免費公共公園可能看似便宜，但其健康好處很大。"},{"en":"Looking in monetary terms can show that an invisible service has real economic value.","zh":"以金錢計算可以顯示看不見的服務有真實經濟價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when turning benefits into financial value.","zh":"把好處轉化為財務價值時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"exceed the value of","meaning":"超過……的價值","examples":[{"en":"The value of pollination exceeds the value of the annual honey crop.","zh":"授粉的價值超過每年蜂蜜產量的價值。"},{"en":"To exceed the value of something means to be worth more than it.","zh":"exceed the value of something 指價值高於某物。"},{"en":"The value of good staff training may exceed the value of a new computer system.","zh":"良好員工培訓的價值可能超過新電腦系統的價值。"},{"en":"Bee pollination can be worth far more than the honey people collect.","zh":"蜜蜂授粉的價值可以遠高於人們收集的蜂蜜。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing economic importance.","zh":"比較經濟重要性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"annual honey crop","meaning":"每年蜂蜜產量","examples":[{"en":"The annual honey crop is worth much less than pollination services.","zh":"每年蜂蜜產量的價值遠低於授粉服務。"},{"en":"The annual honey crop is the amount of honey produced in one year.","zh":"annual honey crop 指一年內生產的蜂蜜數量。"},{"en":"A beekeeper may compare this year’s annual honey crop with last year’s.","zh":"養蜂人可能把今年的蜂蜜年產量與去年比較。"},{"en":"Even if the honey crop is valuable, pollination may bring greater economic benefits.","zh":"即使蜂蜜產量有價值，授粉可能帶來更大經濟好處。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing yearly honey production.","zh":"討論年度蜂蜜生產時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"by a factor of fifty","meaning":"達五十倍","examples":[{"en":"The value of pollination exceeds that of honey by a factor of fifty.","zh":"授粉的價值比蜂蜜高達五十倍。"},{"en":"By a factor of fifty means fifty times as much.","zh":"by a factor of fifty 指是五十倍。"},{"en":"A factory that makes 500 items instead of 10 has increased production by a factor of fifty.","zh":"工廠由生產10件物品增加到500件，就是增加了五十倍。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a very large difference, not a small increase.","zh":"這個短語顯示非常大的差異，而不是小幅增加。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing quantities or values.","zh":"比較數量或價值時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"apparently harmonious relationship","meaning":"表面和諧的關係","examples":[{"en":"The apparently harmonious relationship between bees and flowers involves competition.","zh":"蜜蜂與花之間表面和諧的關係涉及競爭。"},{"en":"An apparently harmonious relationship seems peaceful and cooperative on the surface.","zh":"apparently harmonious relationship 指表面上看似和平合作的關係。"},{"en":"Two departments may have an apparently harmonious relationship while quietly competing for budget.","zh":"兩個部門可能表面關係和諧，但暗中競爭預算。"},{"en":"In nature, cooperation can hide conflict when both sides seek their own benefits.","zh":"在自然界中，當雙方都追求自身利益時，合作可以隱藏衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when appearance and reality are different.","zh":"當表象與現實不同時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"conceal a conflict of interests","meaning":"隱藏利益衝突","examples":[{"en":"The relationship conceals a conflict of interests.","zh":"這種關係隱藏利益衝突。"},{"en":"To conceal a conflict of interests means to hide a situation where different sides want different benefits.","zh":"conceal a conflict of interests 指隱藏不同方面想得到不同利益的情況。"},{"en":"A friendly business partnership may conceal a conflict of interests if both partners want control.","zh":"友好的商業夥伴關係可能隱藏利益衝突，如果雙方都想掌控。"},{"en":"Bees want maximum food, while flowers want efficient pollination with minimum cost.","zh":"蜜蜂想取得最多食物，而花想以最低成本有效授粉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when hidden tension exists behind cooperation.","zh":"當合作背後有隱藏緊張關係時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"vice versa","meaning":"反之亦然","examples":[{"en":"Flowers need bees, and vice versa.","zh":"花需要蜜蜂，反之亦然。"},{"en":"Vice versa means the opposite is also true.","zh":"vice versa 指相反方向也同樣成立。"},{"en":"Teachers need students to participate, and vice versa: students need teachers to guide them.","zh":"老師需要學生參與，反之亦然：學生需要老師指導。"},{"en":"Saying vice versa avoids repeating the same idea in reverse.","zh":"使用 vice versa 可以避免重複相反方向的同一想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when two sides depend on each other.","zh":"當雙方互相依賴時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"it pays someone to","meaning":"對某人有利的是……","examples":[{"en":"It pays each partner to reduce costs and increase benefits.","zh":"對每一方有利的是降低成本並增加收益。"},{"en":"It pays someone to do something means it is useful or advantageous for that person to do it.","zh":"it pays someone to do something 指做某事對某人有用或有利。"},{"en":"It pays students to review mistakes before the next test.","zh":"對學生有利的是在下次測驗前檢討錯誤。"},{"en":"For bees and flowers, it pays to gain benefits while wasting as little energy as possible.","zh":"對蜜蜂和花來說，有利的是獲得好處，同時盡量少浪費能量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining practical advantage.","zh":"解釋實際利益時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"minimise costs","meaning":"將成本減至最低","examples":[{"en":"Both flowers and bees attempt to minimise their costs.","zh":"花和蜜蜂都試圖將成本減至最低。"},{"en":"To minimise costs means to reduce the energy, money, time, or effort needed as much as possible.","zh":"minimise costs 指盡量減少所需的能量、金錢、時間或努力。"},{"en":"A family may minimise travel costs by taking the bus instead of a taxi.","zh":"家庭可能透過乘巴士而不是的士來將交通成本減至最低。"},{"en":"Bees minimise costs by choosing flowers that give enough food for the energy spent.","zh":"蜜蜂透過選擇能提供足夠食物、值得消耗能量的花來降低成本。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing efficiency.","zh":"討論效率時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"maximise profits","meaning":"將收益增至最高","examples":[{"en":"Each side tries to maximise its biological profits.","zh":"每一方都試圖將自己的生物收益增至最高。"},{"en":"To maximise profits means to gain as much benefit as possible.","zh":"maximise profits 指盡可能獲得最大利益。"},{"en":"A small shop may maximise profits by reducing waste and selling popular products.","zh":"小店可能透過減少浪費和銷售受歡迎產品來將收益增至最高。"},{"en":"In nature, biological profit may mean more food, better reproduction, or higher survival chances.","zh":"在自然界中，生物收益可以指更多食物、更好繁殖或更高生存機會。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when economic language is used as a metaphor.","zh":"當經濟語言被用作比喻時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"an extreme case of","meaning":"……的極端例子","examples":[{"en":"This may sound like an extreme case of attributing human traits to animals.","zh":"這聽起來可能像是將人類特質賦予動物的極端例子。"},{"en":"An extreme case of something is a very strong or unusual example of it.","zh":"extreme case of something 指某事非常強烈或不尋常的例子。"},{"en":"A student rewriting an entire essay for one spelling error would be an extreme case of perfectionism.","zh":"學生因一個拼寫錯誤而重寫整篇文章，就是完美主義的極端例子。"},{"en":"Calling bees “consumers” may sound extreme, but it helps explain their choices.","zh":"把蜜蜂稱為「消費者」可能聽起來極端，但有助解釋牠們的選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing something unusually strong.","zh":"描述某事異常強烈時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"attribute human qualities to","meaning":"將人類特質賦予……","examples":[{"en":"The writer attributes human qualities to bees as a metaphor.","zh":"作者以比喻方式將人類特質賦予蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To attribute human qualities to something means to describe a non-human thing as if it thinks or acts like a person.","zh":"attribute human qualities to something 指把非人類事物描述得好像會像人一樣思考或行動。"},{"en":"A child may attribute human qualities to a toy bear by saying it feels lonely.","zh":"孩子說玩具熊感到孤單，就是將人類特質賦予玩具。"},{"en":"Writers sometimes do this to make animal behaviour easier for readers to understand.","zh":"作者有時這樣做，是為了令讀者更容易理解動物行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing personification or metaphor.","zh":"討論擬人化或比喻時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"non-human species","meaning":"非人類物種","examples":[{"en":"Economic language is applied metaphorically to non-human species.","zh":"經濟語言被比喻地應用於非人類物種。"},{"en":"Non-human species are living species that are not human beings.","zh":"non-human species 指不是人類的生物物種。"},{"en":"Dolphins, bees, trees, and fungi are all non-human species.","zh":"海豚、蜜蜂、樹木和真菌都是非人類物種。"},{"en":"Using human language for non-human species can be helpful if readers remember it is a metaphor.","zh":"對非人類物種使用人類語言可以有幫助，只要讀者記得那是比喻。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in biology and environmental writing.","zh":"這個短語適用於生物和環境寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"double-entry bookkeeping","meaning":"複式簿記","examples":[{"en":"The writer uses double-entry bookkeeping as an economic metaphor.","zh":"作者使用複式簿記作為經濟比喻。"},{"en":"Double-entry bookkeeping is an accounting method that records money coming in and going out in two linked entries.","zh":"double-entry bookkeeping 指一種會計方法，以兩個相連項目記錄收入和支出。"},{"en":"A business uses double-entry bookkeeping to track income, expenses, assets, and debts.","zh":"企業使用複式簿記追蹤收入、開支、資產和債務。"},{"en":"The metaphor suggests that bees and flowers both have costs and benefits to balance.","zh":"這個比喻暗示蜜蜂和花都有需要平衡的成本與收益。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when economic ideas are used to explain ecology.","zh":"當經濟概念被用來解釋生態時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"use something as a metaphor","meaning":"將某物用作比喻","examples":[{"en":"The marketplace is used as a metaphor for ecological competition.","zh":"市場被用作生態競爭的比喻。"},{"en":"To use something as a metaphor means to use one idea to explain another idea through comparison.","zh":"use something as a metaphor 指透過比較，用一個想法解釋另一個想法。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a traffic jam as a metaphor for information overload.","zh":"老師可能把交通擠塞用作資訊過載的比喻。"},{"en":"Metaphors help students understand abstract ideas through familiar images.","zh":"比喻幫助學生透過熟悉圖像理解抽象想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining figurative language.","zh":"解釋修辭語言時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"give insights into","meaning":"使人深入了解……","examples":[{"en":"Economic metaphors give insights into plant–pollinator relationships.","zh":"經濟比喻使人深入了解植物與授粉者之間的關係。"},{"en":"To give insights into something means to help people understand it more deeply.","zh":"give insights into something 指幫助人更深入理解某事。"},{"en":"Student diaries can give teachers insights into why homework is often late.","zh":"學生日記可以讓老師深入了解為何功課常常遲交。"},{"en":"Seeing bees as consumers gives insight into why they choose some flowers over others.","zh":"把蜜蜂視為消費者，可以讓人理解牠們為何選擇某些花而非其他花。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something reveals hidden meaning.","zh":"當某物揭示隱藏意思時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"what is really going on","meaning":"真正發生的事情","examples":[{"en":"The metaphor helps explain what is really going on between bees and flowers.","zh":"這個比喻幫助解釋蜜蜂與花之間真正發生的事情。"},{"en":"What is really going on means the true situation beneath the surface.","zh":"what is really going on 指表面之下的真實情況。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask what is really going on when a student suddenly stops doing homework.","zh":"當學生突然停止做功課，老師可能會問真正發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"The surface may look cooperative, but the deeper reality may involve competition.","zh":"表面可能看似合作，但更深層現實可能涉及競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when appearance may be misleading.","zh":"當表象可能誤導人時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the real world","meaning":"在現實世界中","examples":[{"en":"In the real world, bees and flowers compete for benefits.","zh":"在現實世界中，蜜蜂和花會為利益競爭。"},{"en":"In the real world means in actual life, not just in theory or appearance.","zh":"in the real world 指在真實生活中，而不只是理論或表面上。"},{"en":"In the real world, a business plan must work with limited money and time.","zh":"在現實世界中，商業計劃必須在金錢和時間有限下運作。"},{"en":"Ecological relationships may look simple in theory but involve costs and competition in reality.","zh":"生態關係在理論上可能看似簡單，但現實中涉及成本和競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting theory with actual situations.","zh":"對比理論和實際情況時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"operate in a competitive marketplace","meaning":"在競爭激烈的市場中運作","examples":[{"en":"Both flowers and bees operate in a competitive marketplace.","zh":"花和蜜蜂都在競爭激烈的市場中運作。"},{"en":"To operate in a competitive marketplace means to act in an environment where different sides compete for advantage.","zh":"operate in a competitive marketplace 指在不同方面爭取優勢的環境中行動。"},{"en":"Small shops operate in a competitive marketplace when many stores sell similar products nearby.","zh":"當附近許多商店售賣相似產品，小店就在競爭激烈的市場中運作。"},{"en":"Flowers compete for pollinators, while bees compare food rewards from different flowers.","zh":"花競爭授粉者，而蜜蜂比較不同花朵提供的食物回報。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when using business language to explain competition.","zh":"使用商業語言解釋競爭時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"form a community of","meaning":"組成……的群體","examples":[{"en":"The flowers form a community of competing retailers.","zh":"這些花組成一個互相競爭的零售商群體。"},{"en":"To form a community of something means to make up a group whose members share a space or role.","zh":"form a community of something 指組成一個成員共享空間或角色的群體。"},{"en":"Small shops on one street may form a community of local businesses.","zh":"一條街上的小店可能組成本地商戶群體。"},{"en":"Flowers in one area form a community because they compete for the same visiting bees.","zh":"同一區域的花組成一個群體，因為它們爭奪同一批到訪蜜蜂。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing a group with related members.","zh":"描述有相關成員的群體時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"seek to attract","meaning":"試圖吸引……","examples":[{"en":"Each flower seeks to attract suitable pollinators.","zh":"每朵花都試圖吸引合適的授粉者。"},{"en":"To seek to attract someone or something means to try to make them come, notice, or choose it.","zh":"seek to attract someone or something 指嘗試令某人或某物前來、注意或選擇它。"},{"en":"A school may seek to attract students by offering strong music and sports programmes.","zh":"學校可能透過提供強大的音樂和體育課程來吸引學生。"},{"en":"Flowers use colour, scent, nectar, and pollen to attract bees.","zh":"花利用顏色、氣味、花蜜和花粉來吸引蜜蜂。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing effort to gain attention.","zh":"描述努力獲得注意時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"discriminating consumers","meaning":"有選擇能力的消費者","examples":[{"en":"The bees behave like discriminating consumers.","zh":"蜜蜂表現得像有選擇能力的消費者。"},{"en":"Discriminating consumers are buyers who choose carefully instead of accepting anything offered.","zh":"discriminating consumers 指會仔細選擇、而不是接受任何供應的買家。"},{"en":"Discriminating consumers may compare price, quality, and service before choosing a restaurant.","zh":"有選擇能力的消費者可能在選餐廳前比較價格、質素和服務。"},{"en":"Bees act like careful consumers when they choose flowers with better rewards.","zh":"當蜜蜂選擇回報較好的花時，牠們表現得像仔細的消費者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing selective behaviour.","zh":"描述選擇性行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"juggle the costs and benefits","meaning":"權衡成本與收益","examples":[{"en":"Flowers must juggle the costs and benefits of attracting bees.","zh":"花必須權衡吸引蜜蜂的成本與收益。"},{"en":"To juggle the costs and benefits means to balance what is spent against what is gained.","zh":"juggle the costs and benefits 指平衡付出的東西與得到的東西。"},{"en":"A family may juggle the costs and benefits of buying a car instead of using public transport.","zh":"家庭可能權衡買車與使用公共交通的成本與收益。"},{"en":"Flowers must spend energy making nectar, but they gain pollination if bees visit.","zh":"花必須花能量製造花蜜，但如果蜜蜂到訪，就能獲得授粉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when decisions involve trade-offs.","zh":"當決定涉及取捨時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"invest in advertising","meaning":"投資於宣傳","examples":[{"en":"Plants invest in advertising through colour and scent.","zh":"植物透過顏色和氣味投資於宣傳。"},{"en":"To invest in advertising means to spend resources to attract attention.","zh":"invest in advertising 指投入資源來吸引注意。"},{"en":"A small café may invest in advertising by designing a bright sign and posting online.","zh":"小咖啡店可能透過設計鮮明招牌和在網上發文來投資於宣傳。"},{"en":"Flowers invest energy in colour and scent so bees can notice them.","zh":"花把能量投放在顏色和氣味上，讓蜜蜂注意到它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when using business language to describe attraction.","zh":"用商業語言描述吸引力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"by colour and scent","meaning":"透過顏色和氣味","examples":[{"en":"Flowers attract pollinators by colour and scent.","zh":"花透過顏色和氣味吸引授粉者。"},{"en":"By colour and scent means through visual appearance and smell.","zh":"by colour and scent 指透過視覺外觀和氣味。"},{"en":"A bakery may attract customers by colour and scent when fresh bread is displayed near the door.","zh":"麵包店把新鮮麵包放在門口附近時，可能透過顏色和氣味吸引顧客。"},{"en":"Bright colours and strong scents help flowers stand out to insects.","zh":"鮮明顏色和強烈氣味幫助花在昆蟲眼中突出。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how attraction works.","zh":"解釋吸引力如何運作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"provide rewards","meaning":"提供回報","examples":[{"en":"Flowers provide rewards in the form of nectar and pollen.","zh":"花以花蜜和花粉的形式提供回報。"},{"en":"To provide rewards means to offer something valuable in return for an action.","zh":"provide rewards 指提供有價值的東西來回應某個行動。"},{"en":"A teacher may provide rewards such as praise or stickers for careful work.","zh":"老師可能為仔細完成的功課提供稱讚或貼紙等回報。"},{"en":"Flowers provide food rewards so bees have a reason to visit them.","zh":"花提供食物回報，使蜜蜂有理由造訪。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining exchange and motivation.","zh":"解釋交換和動機時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"depend on cross-pollination","meaning":"依賴異花授粉","examples":[{"en":"Many plant species depend on cross-pollination.","zh":"許多植物品種依賴異花授粉。"},{"en":"To depend on cross-pollination means to need pollen to move between different plants of the same species.","zh":"depend on cross-pollination 指需要花粉在同一品種的不同植物之間移動。"},{"en":"Some fruit trees depend on cross-pollination and produce more fruit when another tree is nearby.","zh":"有些果樹依賴異花授粉，附近有另一棵樹時會結更多果。"},{"en":"If bees do not carry pollen between plants, species that need cross-pollination may reproduce poorly.","zh":"如果蜜蜂不在植物之間攜帶花粉，需要異花授粉的物種可能繁殖不佳。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing plant reproduction.","zh":"討論植物繁殖時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cross-pollination","meaning":"異花授粉","examples":[{"en":"Cross-pollination requires pollen to move between different plants.","zh":"異花授粉需要花粉在不同植物之間移動。"},{"en":"Cross-pollination is the transfer of pollen from one plant to another plant of the same species.","zh":"cross-pollination 指花粉從一株植物轉移到同一品種的另一株植物。"},{"en":"Bees can help cross-pollination when they visit several apple trees in one trip.","zh":"當蜜蜂在一次飛行中造訪幾棵蘋果樹，就可以幫助異花授粉。"},{"en":"Cross-pollination can increase genetic variety in plants.","zh":"異花授粉可以增加植物的基因多樣性。"},{"en":"This word is important in biology, farming, and ecology.","zh":"這個詞在生物、農業和生態中很重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be on a knife-edge","meaning":"處於危險而微妙的平衡","examples":[{"en":"A plant dependent on bees is on a biological knife-edge.","zh":"依賴蜜蜂的植物處於生物上的危險而微妙平衡。"},{"en":"To be on a knife-edge means to be in a very delicate and risky balance.","zh":"be on a knife-edge 指處於非常脆弱且有風險的平衡。"},{"en":"A small business may be on a knife-edge if one bad month could close it.","zh":"如果一個月生意差就可能倒閉，小企業就處於危險而微妙的平衡。"},{"en":"If a flower gives too little nectar, bees may ignore it; if it gives too much, bees may not visit another flower.","zh":"如果花蜜太少，蜜蜂可能忽略它；如果太多，蜜蜂可能不再造訪另一朵花。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a situation can easily fail.","zh":"當情況很容易失敗時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"provide sufficient nectar","meaning":"提供足夠花蜜","examples":[{"en":"A flower must provide sufficient nectar to attract a bee.","zh":"花必須提供足夠花蜜來吸引蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To provide sufficient nectar means to offer enough sweet liquid to interest a pollinator.","zh":"provide sufficient nectar 指提供足夠甜液體，以引起授粉者興趣。"},{"en":"A café must provide sufficient seating if it wants customers to stay.","zh":"如果咖啡店想顧客留下，就必須提供足夠座位。"},{"en":"If a flower provides too little nectar, bees may spend energy elsewhere.","zh":"如果花提供太少花蜜，蜜蜂可能把能量花在其他地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining minimum requirements.","zh":"解釋最低要求時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"attract the interest of","meaning":"引起……的興趣","examples":[{"en":"The reward must attract the interest of a passing bee.","zh":"這種回報必須引起路過蜜蜂的興趣。"},{"en":"To attract the interest of someone means to make them notice and want to learn more or take action.","zh":"attract the interest of someone 指令某人注意並想了解更多或採取行動。"},{"en":"A colourful poster can attract the interest of students walking past the library.","zh":"色彩鮮明的海報可以引起經過圖書館的學生興趣。"},{"en":"Flowers must attract bees before pollination can happen.","zh":"花必須先吸引蜜蜂，授粉才可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing how attention is gained.","zh":"描述如何獲得注意時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"satisfy all of one’s needs","meaning":"滿足某人的全部需要","examples":[{"en":"One flower should not satisfy all of a bee’s needs.","zh":"一朵花不應滿足蜜蜂的全部需要。"},{"en":"To satisfy all of one’s needs means to provide everything someone needs completely.","zh":"satisfy all of one’s needs 指完全提供某人所需的一切。"},{"en":"One lesson cannot satisfy all of a student’s needs in reading, writing, speaking, and grammar.","zh":"一堂課不能滿足學生在閱讀、寫作、說話和文法上的全部需要。"},{"en":"If one flower satisfied all a bee’s needs, the bee might stop visiting other flowers.","zh":"如果一朵花滿足蜜蜂全部需要，蜜蜂可能停止造訪其他花。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when complete satisfaction would stop further action.","zh":"當完全滿足會阻止後續行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in one visit","meaning":"在一次造訪中","examples":[{"en":"A bee should not obtain all the food it needs in one visit.","zh":"蜜蜂不應在一次造訪中取得全部所需食物。"},{"en":"In one visit means during a single trip to a place.","zh":"in one visit 指在一次前往某地的過程中。"},{"en":"A patient may not receive all treatment in one visit to the clinic.","zh":"病人未必在一次診所就診中完成所有治療。"},{"en":"If a bee gets enough food in one visit, it may not carry pollen to another flower.","zh":"如果蜜蜂在一次造訪中得到足夠食物，它可能不會把花粉帶到另一朵花。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing one occasion or trip.","zh":"討論一次場合或行程時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"satiated bee","meaning":"已吃飽的蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"A satiated bee may return directly to its nest.","zh":"已吃飽的蜜蜂可能直接返回蜂巢。"},{"en":"A satiated bee is a bee that has eaten enough and no longer needs more food at that moment.","zh":"satiated bee 指已吃夠、當下不再需要更多食物的蜜蜂。"},{"en":"A satiated child at a buffet may stop walking around for more food.","zh":"在自助餐中已吃飽的孩子可能不再四處拿食物。"},{"en":"If a bee is satiated too quickly, it may not help the flower with cross-pollination.","zh":"如果蜜蜂太快吃飽，它可能不會幫助花進行異花授粉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining how fullness changes behaviour.","zh":"解釋飽足如何改變行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"return to its nest","meaning":"返回蜂巢","examples":[{"en":"A fully fed bee may return to its nest instead of visiting another flower.","zh":"吃飽的蜜蜂可能返回蜂巢，而不是造訪另一朵花。"},{"en":"To return to its nest means to go back to the place where the insect or animal lives.","zh":"return to its nest 指回到昆蟲或動物居住的地方。"},{"en":"A bird may return to its nest after finding food for its chicks.","zh":"鳥找到食物餵幼鳥後，可能返回巢中。"},{"en":"If a bee returns to its nest too soon, pollen may not reach another flower.","zh":"如果蜜蜂太早返回蜂巢，花粉可能無法到達另一朵花。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing animal movement back home.","zh":"描述動物返回住所時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"The bee must visit another flower rather than return immediately to the nest.","zh":"蜜蜂必須造訪另一朵花，而不是立即返回蜂巢。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of.","zh":"rather than 指而不是。"},{"en":"A student should check the passage rather than guess the answer.","zh":"學生應查看文章，而不是猜答案。"},{"en":"Flowers benefit when a bee travels to another flower rather than stopping after one visit.","zh":"當蜜蜂前往另一朵花，而不是一次造訪後就停止，花就受益。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when making a clear contrast between two actions.","zh":"在兩個行動之間作清楚對比時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be out to get","meaning":"一心想取得……","examples":[{"en":"The bee is out to get the maximum possible reward.","zh":"蜜蜂一心想取得最大可能回報。"},{"en":"To be out to get something means to be determined to obtain it.","zh":"be out to get something 指決心取得某物。"},{"en":"A shopper during a sale may be out to get the best discount.","zh":"打折期間，購物者可能一心想取得最佳折扣。"},{"en":"Bees choose flowers in a way that helps them get as much food as possible.","zh":"蜜蜂選擇花朵的方式，有助牠們取得盡可能多的食物。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and describes strong self-interest.","zh":"這個短語較口語，描述強烈自身利益。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"maximum amount of","meaning":"最大量的……","examples":[{"en":"A bee seeks the maximum amount of nectar and pollen.","zh":"蜜蜂尋求最大量的花蜜和花粉。"},{"en":"The maximum amount of something is the greatest quantity possible.","zh":"maximum amount of something 指某物可能達到的最大數量。"},{"en":"A student may try to learn the maximum amount of vocabulary before an exam.","zh":"學生可能試圖在考試前學最多詞彙。"},{"en":"Bees gain more energy when they collect the maximum possible reward for each trip.","zh":"蜜蜂每次出行收集最大可能回報時，就能得到更多能量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the highest possible quantity.","zh":"描述最高可能數量時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"assess the quality and quantity","meaning":"評估質素和數量","examples":[{"en":"The bee must assess the quality and quantity of each reward.","zh":"蜜蜂必須評估每種回報的質素和數量。"},{"en":"To assess the quality and quantity means to judge how good something is and how much of it there is.","zh":"assess the quality and quantity 指判斷某物有多好以及有多少。"},{"en":"A shopper may assess the quality and quantity of fruit before buying a box.","zh":"購物者買一盒水果前，可能評估其質素和數量。"},{"en":"Bees benefit when they choose flowers with enough food and good nutritional value.","zh":"當蜜蜂選擇有足夠食物和良好營養價值的花時，就會受益。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when both amount and value matter.","zh":"當數量和價值都重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be on offer","meaning":"可供選擇；正在提供","examples":[{"en":"The bee evaluates the food rewards that are on offer.","zh":"蜜蜂評估正在提供的食物回報。"},{"en":"Be on offer means be available for someone to choose or receive.","zh":"be on offer 指可供某人選擇或獲得。"},{"en":"Students may compare the clubs on offer before choosing an after-school activity.","zh":"學生選擇課後活動前，可能比較可供選擇的學會。"},{"en":"Bees visit flowers and judge which rewards are available to them.","zh":"蜜蜂造訪花朵，判斷哪些回報可供牠們取得。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing available choices.","zh":"討論可用選項時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"energy costs","meaning":"能量成本","examples":[{"en":"Foraging involves significant energy costs for the bee.","zh":"覓食對蜜蜂來說涉及顯著能量成本。"},{"en":"Energy costs are the amount of energy needed to perform an action.","zh":"energy costs 指完成某行動所需的能量。"},{"en":"Walking up ten flights of stairs has higher energy costs than taking the lift.","zh":"走十層樓梯比乘升降機有更高能量成本。"},{"en":"If a bee spends too much energy flying, the food reward may not be worth the trip.","zh":"如果蜜蜂飛行花費太多能量，食物回報可能不值得這趟行程。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing effort and efficiency.","zh":"討論努力和效率時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make a calorific profit","meaning":"獲得熱量上的淨收益","examples":[{"en":"The bee must make a calorific profit on each trip.","zh":"蜜蜂每趟出行都必須獲得熱量上的淨收益。"},{"en":"To make a calorific profit means to gain more food energy than the energy spent.","zh":"make a calorific profit 指獲得的食物能量多於消耗的能量。"},{"en":"A runner eating after training gains energy, but only bees are described here as making a calorific profit.","zh":"跑步者訓練後進食會補充能量，但文中是把蜜蜂描述為獲得熱量淨收益。"},{"en":"If a bee burns more energy than it collects, the trip is not profitable in energy terms.","zh":"如果蜜蜂消耗的能量多於收集到的能量，這趟行程在能量上就不划算。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when food energy is treated like economic profit.","zh":"當食物能量被當作經濟收益來看時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"foraging trip","meaning":"覓食旅程","examples":[{"en":"A successful foraging trip provides more energy than it consumes.","zh":"成功的覓食旅程提供的能量多於它所消耗的能量。"},{"en":"A foraging trip is a journey made by an animal to search for food.","zh":"foraging trip 指動物外出尋找食物的旅程。"},{"en":"A squirrel may make a foraging trip across a park to find nuts.","zh":"松鼠可能穿過公園進行覓食旅程，尋找堅果。"},{"en":"For bees, a good foraging trip brings back enough nectar or pollen to justify the flight.","zh":"對蜜蜂來說，好的覓食旅程會帶回足夠花蜜或花粉，使飛行值得。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing animal feeding behaviour.","zh":"討論動物覓食行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not all that it seems","meaning":"並非表面看來那樣","examples":[{"en":"The apparent harmony is not all that it seems.","zh":"表面的和諧並非表面看來那樣。"},{"en":"Not all that it seems means the situation is more complicated than it appears.","zh":"not all that it seems 指情況比表面顯示的更複雜。"},{"en":"A quiet classroom is not all that it seems if students are confused but afraid to ask questions.","zh":"安靜課室並非表面看來那樣，如果學生其實困惑但不敢提問。"},{"en":"Bees and flowers may look cooperative, but each side is also pursuing its own benefit.","zh":"蜜蜂和花看似合作，但雙方也在追求自身利益。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when surface appearance hides a deeper reality.","zh":"當表象隱藏更深現實時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"an equilibrium based on","meaning":"基於……的平衡狀態","examples":[{"en":"The relationship is an equilibrium based on compromise.","zh":"這種關係是一種基於妥協的平衡狀態。"},{"en":"An equilibrium based on something is a balanced state created by that factor.","zh":"equilibrium based on something 指由某因素造成的平衡狀態。"},{"en":"A family budget may reach an equilibrium based on compromise between saving and spending.","zh":"家庭預算可能在儲蓄與開支之間達成基於妥協的平衡。"},{"en":"The bee–flower relationship stays balanced because each side gives up something and gains something.","zh":"蜜蜂與花的關係保持平衡，因為雙方都有所讓步，也有所獲得。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining a stable but delicate balance.","zh":"解釋穩定但微妙的平衡時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"compromises between","meaning":"……之間的妥協","examples":[{"en":"The ecological balance depends on compromises between competing interests.","zh":"生態平衡取決於互相競爭的利益之間的妥協。"},{"en":"Compromises between things are agreements or balances where each side gives up something.","zh":"compromises between things 指各方都有所讓步而形成的協議或平衡。"},{"en":"A school timetable requires compromises between exam subjects, PE, music, and rest time.","zh":"學校時間表需要在考試科目、體育、音樂和休息時間之間作出妥協。"},{"en":"Flowers must offer enough reward for bees, but not so much that bees stop moving between flowers.","zh":"花必須提供足夠回報給蜜蜂，但不能多到令蜜蜂停止在花之間移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when two needs cannot both be fully satisfied.","zh":"當兩種需要不能同時完全滿足時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"competing interests","meaning":"互相競爭的利益","examples":[{"en":"Bees and flowers have different but competing interests.","zh":"蜜蜂和花有不同但互相競爭的利益。"},{"en":"Competing interests are goals or benefits that conflict because each side wants something different.","zh":"competing interests 指各方想要不同東西，因而互相衝突的目標或利益。"},{"en":"Parents and teenagers may have competing interests when one wants safety and the other wants freedom.","zh":"當家長想要安全，而青少年想要自由時，雙方可能有互相競爭的利益。"},{"en":"Bees want maximum food, while flowers want pollen moved efficiently.","zh":"蜜蜂想要最多食物，而花想要花粉被有效移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining hidden conflict.","zh":"解釋隱藏衝突時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"protagonists","meaning":"主角；主要參與者","examples":[{"en":"The bees and flowers are the main protagonists in this ecological interaction.","zh":"蜜蜂和花是這種生態互動中的主要參與者。"},{"en":"Protagonists are the main characters or main participants in a story, event, or situation.","zh":"protagonists 指故事、事件或情況中的主角或主要參與者。"},{"en":"In a school debate, the two team leaders may become the main protagonists.","zh":"在學校辯論中，兩位隊長可能成為主要參與者。"},{"en":"Calling bees and flowers protagonists makes the ecological relationship feel like a drama with active players.","zh":"把蜜蜂和花稱為主角，令生態關係感覺像一場有主動角色的戲劇。"},{"en":"This word is useful in literature and in vivid explanations of real events.","zh":"這個詞適用於文學，也適用於對真實事件的生動解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sound remarkably like","meaning":"聽起來非常像……","examples":[{"en":"This ecological theory sounds remarkably like Adam Smith’s economic ideas.","zh":"這個生態理論聽起來非常像 Adam Smith 的經濟思想。"},{"en":"Sound remarkably like means seem very similar to something when described.","zh":"sound remarkably like 指描述起來與某事非常相似。"},{"en":"A student’s study plan may sound remarkably like an athlete’s training schedule.","zh":"學生的學習計劃可能聽起來非常像運動員的訓練時間表。"},{"en":"The bee–flower theory sounds like economics because both involve competition and benefit.","zh":"蜜蜂與花的理論聽起來像經濟學，因為兩者都涉及競爭和利益。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when drawing a surprising comparison.","zh":"作出令人意外的比較時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"eighteenth-century economist","meaning":"18世紀經濟學家","examples":[{"en":"Adam Smith was an influential eighteenth-century economist.","zh":"Adam Smith 是一位有影響力的18世紀經濟學家。"},{"en":"An eighteenth-century economist is a person who studied economics during the 1700s.","zh":"eighteenth-century economist 指在1700年代研究經濟學的人。"},{"en":"A history teacher may discuss an eighteenth-century economist when explaining early ideas about markets.","zh":"歷史老師解釋早期市場思想時，可能討論18世紀經濟學家。"},{"en":"Mentioning Smith connects ecological competition with old economic theory.","zh":"提到 Smith 把生態競爭與舊經濟理論連接起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving historical background.","zh":"提供歷史背景時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"postulate that","meaning":"假定；提出……","examples":[{"en":"Smith postulated that competition could produce social balance.","zh":"Smith 提出競爭可以產生社會平衡。"},{"en":"To postulate that means to suggest or assume an idea as a basis for discussion or theory.","zh":"postulate that 指提出或假設某想法，作為討論或理論基礎。"},{"en":"A scientist may postulate that sleep improves memory before testing it in an experiment.","zh":"科學家可能先假定睡眠改善記憶，再用實驗測試。"},{"en":"Smith’s idea helps the writer compare economic competition with ecological balance.","zh":"Smith 的想法幫助作者把經濟競爭與生態平衡作比較。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and common in academic explanation.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常見於學術解釋。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"human society","meaning":"人類社會","examples":[{"en":"Smith applied his economic theory to human society.","zh":"Smith 把他的經濟理論應用於人類社會。"},{"en":"Human society means organised groups of people living together with shared rules, work, and relationships.","zh":"human society 指人們以共同規則、工作和關係組織起來生活的群體。"},{"en":"Schools, markets, families, and governments are parts of human society.","zh":"學校、市場、家庭和政府都是人類社會的一部分。"},{"en":"Economic theories often try to explain how people act within society.","zh":"經濟理論常試圖解釋人們在社會中如何行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing social systems.","zh":"討論社會系統時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"competitive interactions","meaning":"競爭互動","examples":[{"en":"Competitive interactions may eventually create a form of balance.","zh":"競爭互動可能最終創造某種平衡。"},{"en":"Competitive interactions are situations where different individuals or groups affect one another while trying to gain advantage.","zh":"competitive interactions 指不同個體或群體在爭取優勢時互相影響的情況。"},{"en":"Two shops on the same street have competitive interactions when they lower prices to attract customers.","zh":"同一條街上的兩間店為吸引顧客而減價時，就有競爭互動。"},{"en":"In nature, competition can push species into a workable balance over time.","zh":"在自然界中，競爭可以隨時間把物種推向可運作的平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing rivalry and mutual influence.","zh":"討論競爭和互相影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"economic units","meaning":"經濟單位","examples":[{"en":"Smith described individuals and groups as economic units.","zh":"Smith 把個人和群體描述為經濟單位。"},{"en":"Economic units are people, households, companies, or groups viewed as decision-makers in an economy.","zh":"economic units 指在經濟中被視為決策者的人、家庭、公司或群體。"},{"en":"A family can be seen as an economic unit when it earns, spends, and saves money.","zh":"當家庭賺錢、花錢和儲蓄時，可以被視為經濟單位。"},{"en":"In the metaphor, flowers and bees behave like economic units because they weigh costs and rewards.","zh":"在這個比喻中，花和蜜蜂像經濟單位一樣行動，因為牠們權衡成本和回報。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when economic thinking is applied to behaviour.","zh":"當經濟思維被應用於行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"eventually result in","meaning":"最終導致……","examples":[{"en":"Competition may eventually result in a balanced society.","zh":"競爭可能最終導致一個平衡的社會。"},{"en":"Eventually result in means finally lead to a particular outcome after some time.","zh":"eventually result in 指經過一段時間後最終帶來某結果。"},{"en":"Regular practice may eventually result in better pronunciation.","zh":"定期練習可能最終帶來更好的發音。"},{"en":"In Smith’s theory, many self-interested actions can eventually create a larger balance.","zh":"在 Smith 的理論中，許多自利行動最終可以創造更大的平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a result develops gradually.","zh":"當結果逐漸形成時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"balanced society","meaning":"平衡的社會","examples":[{"en":"Smith believed competition could produce a balanced society.","zh":"Smith 相信競爭可以產生平衡的社會。"},{"en":"A balanced society is a society in which different needs, interests, and groups are kept in workable order.","zh":"balanced society 指不同需要、利益和群體能維持可運作秩序的社會。"},{"en":"A balanced society needs jobs, education, safety, freedom, and fairness.","zh":"平衡的社會需要工作、教育、安全、自由和公平。"},{"en":"If one group gains too much at others’ expense, society may lose balance.","zh":"如果一個群體過度受益而犧牲其他群體，社會可能失去平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing social order.","zh":"討論社會秩序時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"one might predict that","meaning":"人們可能會預測","examples":[{"en":"One might predict that economists would study pollination relationships.","zh":"人們可能會預測經濟學家會研究授粉關係。"},{"en":"One might predict that means someone could reasonably expect something to happen.","zh":"one might predict that 指人們可以合理預期某事發生。"},{"en":"One might predict that students who read daily will improve faster.","zh":"人們可能會預測每天閱讀的學生會進步得更快。"},{"en":"If bee–flower relationships resemble markets, it is reasonable to expect economists to be interested.","zh":"如果蜜蜂與花的關係像市場，預期經濟學家感興趣就是合理的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when making a careful expectation.","zh":"作出謹慎預期時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"find something of interest","meaning":"覺得某事有趣","examples":[{"en":"Economists may find bee–plant relationships of considerable interest.","zh":"經濟學家可能覺得蜜蜂與植物關係相當有趣。"},{"en":"To find something of interest means to consider it interesting, useful, or worth studying.","zh":"find something of interest 指認為某事有趣、有用或值得研究。"},{"en":"A teacher may find students’ reading habits of interest when planning lessons.","zh":"老師規劃課堂時，可能覺得學生閱讀習慣有研究價值。"},{"en":"Economists may be interested because the bee–plant relationship involves costs, rewards, and choices.","zh":"經濟學家可能感興趣，因為蜜蜂與植物關係涉及成本、回報和選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why a topic attracts attention.","zh":"解釋為何某主題吸引注意時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"this is the case","meaning":"情況確實如此","examples":[{"en":"This is the case in a long-term Israeli research project.","zh":"在一項長期以色列研究項目中，情況確實如此。"},{"en":"This is the case means this situation is true or actually happens.","zh":"this is the case 指這種情況是真的或確實發生。"},{"en":"Some students learn better through examples; this is the case in many language classes.","zh":"有些學生透過例子學得更好；在許多語言課中情況確實如此。"},{"en":"The writer says economists would be interested, and then shows this is true in a real project.","zh":"作者說經濟學家會感興趣，然後展示這在真實項目中確實如此。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when confirming a previous point.","zh":"確認前一點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"collaborate with","meaning":"與……合作","examples":[{"en":"Economists are collaborating with botanists and entomologists.","zh":"經濟學家正與植物學家和昆蟲學家合作。"},{"en":"To collaborate with someone means to work together with them on a shared task.","zh":"collaborate with someone 指與某人為共同任務一起工作。"},{"en":"A science teacher may collaborate with an English teacher to design a reading lesson about ecology.","zh":"科學老師可能與英文老師合作，設計一堂關於生態的閱讀課。"},{"en":"Different experts can solve complex problems better when they collaborate.","zh":"不同專家合作時，可以更好地解決複雜問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing teamwork across fields.","zh":"描述跨領域團隊合作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"botanists","meaning":"植物學家","examples":[{"en":"Botanists study plants and their ecological relationships.","zh":"植物學家研究植物及其生態關係。"},{"en":"Botanists are scientists who study plants.","zh":"botanists 指研究植物的科學家。"},{"en":"Botanists may examine flowers, roots, seeds, forests, and plant diseases.","zh":"植物學家可能研究花、根、種子、森林和植物疾病。"},{"en":"Their knowledge helps explain how plants reproduce and interact with pollinators.","zh":"他們的知識幫助解釋植物如何繁殖並與授粉者互動。"},{"en":"This word is common in biology and ecology.","zh":"這個詞常見於生物和生態學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"entomologists","meaning":"昆蟲學家","examples":[{"en":"Entomologists specialise in the scientific study of insects.","zh":"昆蟲學家專門從事昆蟲的科學研究。"},{"en":"Entomologists are scientists who study insects such as bees, ants, beetles, and butterflies.","zh":"entomologists 指研究蜜蜂、螞蟻、甲蟲和蝴蝶等昆蟲的科學家。"},{"en":"An entomologist may study how mosquitoes spread disease.","zh":"昆蟲學家可能研究蚊子如何傳播疾病。"},{"en":"Entomologists help us understand pollination because many pollinators are insects.","zh":"昆蟲學家幫助我們理解授粉，因為許多授粉者都是昆蟲。"},{"en":"This word is useful in biology, agriculture, and conservation.","zh":"這個詞適用於生物、農業和保育。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"long-term study","meaning":"長期研究","examples":[{"en":"The researchers are conducting a long-term study of pollination.","zh":"研究人員正進行授粉的長期研究。"},{"en":"A long-term study is research carried out over a long period.","zh":"long-term study 指長時間進行的研究。"},{"en":"A school may run a long-term study to see how reading habits change over five years.","zh":"學校可能進行長期研究，以了解閱讀習慣如何在五年間改變。"},{"en":"Long-term studies can reveal patterns that short observations miss.","zh":"長期研究可以揭示短期觀察錯過的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research takes time to produce reliable results.","zh":"當研究需要時間產生可靠結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pollination biology","meaning":"授粉生物學","examples":[{"en":"The project examines the pollination biology of native plants.","zh":"該項目研究本地植物的授粉生物學。"},{"en":"Pollination biology is the study of how pollination works in living organisms and ecosystems.","zh":"pollination biology 指研究授粉如何在生物和生態系統中運作的學科。"},{"en":"A university course in pollination biology may study flowers, insects, pollen, and reproduction.","zh":"授粉生物學大學課程可能研究花、昆蟲、花粉和繁殖。"},{"en":"Understanding pollination biology helps conservationists protect plants and pollinators together.","zh":"理解授粉生物學幫助保育人士同時保護植物和授粉者。"},{"en":"This phrase is technical and belongs to ecology and botany.","zh":"這個短語較技術性，屬於生態學和植物學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"native flora","meaning":"本地植物群","examples":[{"en":"The scientists are studying the native flora of Israel.","zh":"科學家正在研究以色列的本地植物群。"},{"en":"Native flora means the plant life that naturally belongs to a particular region.","zh":"native flora 指自然屬於某一地區的植物生命。"},{"en":"A country park may protect native flora such as local trees, grasses, and wildflowers.","zh":"郊野公園可能保護本地樹木、草和野花等本地植物群。"},{"en":"Studying native flora helps scientists understand local ecosystems.","zh":"研究本地植物群幫助科學家理解本地生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing plants in a specific place.","zh":"討論某特定地方的植物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in an attempt to","meaning":"試圖……","examples":[{"en":"The researchers are working together in an attempt to understand ecological dynamics.","zh":"研究人員正在合作，試圖理解生態動態。"},{"en":"In an attempt to means trying to do something, often because it is difficult or important.","zh":"in an attempt to 指試圖做某事，通常因為它困難或重要。"},{"en":"A school may change its timetable in an attempt to reduce student stress.","zh":"學校可能改變時間表，試圖減少學生壓力。"},{"en":"Scientists combine different skills in an attempt to answer complex ecological questions.","zh":"科學家結合不同技能，試圖回答複雜生態問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining purpose.","zh":"解釋目的時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"understand the dynamics of","meaning":"了解……的動態","examples":[{"en":"They hope to understand the dynamics of bee–plant relationships.","zh":"他們希望了解蜜蜂與植物關係的動態。"},{"en":"To understand the dynamics of something means to understand how its parts interact and change over time.","zh":"understand the dynamics of something 指理解其各部分如何互動並隨時間變化。"},{"en":"A teacher may try to understand the dynamics of a noisy class before changing rules.","zh":"老師在改變規則前，可能試圖了解嘈吵班級的互動動態。"},{"en":"Bee–plant dynamics include attraction, reward, competition, and pollination.","zh":"蜜蜂與植物的動態包括吸引、回報、競爭和授粉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when relationships are active and changing.","zh":"當關係是活躍而會變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"communities of bees and plants","meaning":"蜜蜂與植物群落","examples":[{"en":"The study examines entire communities of bees and plants.","zh":"該研究檢視整個蜜蜂與植物群落。"},{"en":"Communities of bees and plants are groups of interacting bee species and plant species in one area.","zh":"communities of bees and plants 指同一地區中互相作用的蜜蜂品種和植物品種群體。"},{"en":"A meadow may contain communities of bees and plants that depend on each other.","zh":"草地可能包含互相依賴的蜜蜂與植物群落。"},{"en":"Studying communities shows relationships that would be missed if only one species were examined.","zh":"研究群落可以顯示只研究單一物種時會錯過的關係。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when ecology is studied as a network.","zh":"當生態被作為網絡研究時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"more than passing academic interest","meaning":"不只具有短暫的學術價值","examples":[{"en":"The research is of more than passing academic interest.","zh":"這項研究不只具有短暫的學術價值。"},{"en":"More than passing academic interest means not merely briefly interesting to scholars, but practically important too.","zh":"more than passing academic interest 指不只是對學者有短暫興趣，而是也有實際重要性。"},{"en":"A study of school lunches may be of more than passing academic interest if it affects child health policy.","zh":"如果學校午餐研究影響兒童健康政策，它就不只具有短暫學術價值。"},{"en":"Pollination research matters because it can guide conservation and food production decisions.","zh":"授粉研究很重要，因為它可以指導保育和糧食生產決策。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when research has real-world importance.","zh":"當研究有現實世界重要性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"it is important that","meaning":"……是重要的","examples":[{"en":"It is important that authorities understand pollinator relationships.","zh":"當局了解授粉者關係是重要的。"},{"en":"It is important that means something matters and should be taken seriously.","zh":"it is important that 指某事重要並應被認真對待。"},{"en":"It is important that students read the question before writing an answer.","zh":"學生在寫答案前閱讀題目是重要的。"},{"en":"Authorities need ecological understanding before they can protect species effectively.","zh":"當局需要生態理解，才可以有效保護物種。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing necessity.","zh":"強調必要性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"authorities","meaning":"當局","examples":[{"en":"Authorities need ecological evidence when developing conservation policies.","zh":"當局制定保育政策時需要生態證據。"},{"en":"Authorities are official organisations or people with power to make decisions.","zh":"authorities 指有權作決定的官方組織或人士。"},{"en":"City authorities may close a road if it becomes unsafe after heavy rain.","zh":"如果道路在大雨後變得不安全，市政當局可能封路。"},{"en":"When authorities make conservation decisions, their choices can affect whole ecosystems.","zh":"當局作出保育決策時，其選擇可以影響整個生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing government or official responsibility.","zh":"討論政府或官方責任時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"dynamic relationships","meaning":"動態關係","examples":[{"en":"Conservationists must understand the dynamic relationships between plants and pollinators.","zh":"保育人士必須理解植物和授粉者之間的動態關係。"},{"en":"Dynamic relationships are relationships that change through interaction over time.","zh":"dynamic relationships 指透過互動隨時間改變的關係。"},{"en":"A teacher and class have a dynamic relationship because both sides affect each other’s behaviour.","zh":"老師和班級之間有動態關係，因為雙方都影響彼此行為。"},{"en":"Plant–pollinator relationships change when climate, habitat, or species numbers change.","zh":"當氣候、棲息地或物種數量改變，植物與授粉者關係也會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when relationships are active rather than fixed.","zh":"當關係是活躍而非固定時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pollinators","meaning":"授粉者","examples":[{"en":"Bees are among the world’s most important pollinators.","zh":"蜜蜂是世界上最重要的授粉者之一。"},{"en":"Pollinators are animals that move pollen from one flower to another, helping plants reproduce.","zh":"pollinators 指把花粉從一朵花移到另一朵花、幫助植物繁殖的動物。"},{"en":"Bees, butterflies, birds, and bats can act as pollinators.","zh":"蜜蜂、蝴蝶、鳥類和蝙蝠都可以擔當授粉者。"},{"en":"Without pollinators, many flowering plants would produce fewer seeds or fruits.","zh":"沒有授粉者，許多開花植物會產生較少種子或果實。"},{"en":"This word is central to ecology and agriculture.","zh":"這個詞是生態和農業的核心詞彙。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"especially true when","meaning":"在……時尤其如此","examples":[{"en":"This is especially true when authorities devise conservation policies.","zh":"當局制定保育政策時，這一點尤其如此。"},{"en":"Especially true when means particularly correct or important in a certain situation.","zh":"especially true when 指在某情況下特別正確或重要。"},{"en":"Clear instructions are useful in every lesson, but this is especially true when students are doing an exam task.","zh":"清楚指示在每堂課都有用，但當學生做考試題時尤其如此。"},{"en":"Understanding pollinators is especially important when conservation decisions may affect many species.","zh":"當保育決策可能影響許多物種，理解授粉者尤其重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when highlighting a situation where a point matters most.","zh":"突出某觀點在哪種情況下最重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"devise conservation policies","meaning":"制定保育政策","examples":[{"en":"Authorities need sound evidence to devise conservation policies.","zh":"當局需要可靠證據來制定保育政策。"},{"en":"To devise conservation policies means to design plans or rules for protecting nature.","zh":"devise conservation policies 指設計保護自然的計劃或規則。"},{"en":"A government may devise conservation policies to protect wetlands from development.","zh":"政府可能制定保育政策，保護濕地免受發展破壞。"},{"en":"Good policies need evidence about species, habitats, and human activities.","zh":"好政策需要關於物種、棲息地和人類活動的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing environmental planning.","zh":"討論環境規劃時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a good example comes from","meaning":"一個好例子來自……","examples":[{"en":"A good example comes from the tropical forests of South America.","zh":"一個好例子來自南美洲的熱帶森林。"},{"en":"A good example comes from means a clear case can be found in a particular place or situation.","zh":"a good example comes from 指一個清楚例子可在某地方或情況中找到。"},{"en":"A good example comes from schools that let students learn outdoors once a week.","zh":"一個好例子來自每週讓學生戶外學習一次的學校。"},{"en":"Specific examples make a general argument easier to understand.","zh":"具體例子令一般論點更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing evidence.","zh":"引入證據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tropical South America","meaning":"南美洲熱帶地區","examples":[{"en":"The example concerns rainforests in tropical South America.","zh":"這個例子涉及南美洲熱帶地區的雨林。"},{"en":"Tropical South America refers to the warm, humid regions of South America near the tropics.","zh":"tropical South America 指南美洲接近熱帶、溫暖潮濕的地區。"},{"en":"Tropical South America includes areas with dense rainforests and rich biodiversity.","zh":"南美洲熱帶地區包括擁有茂密雨林和豐富生物多樣性的地方。"},{"en":"Because the forests are species-rich, pollination relationships there can be especially complex.","zh":"因為森林物種豐富，那裏的授粉關係可能特別複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving geographical and ecological context.","zh":"提供地理和生態背景時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rainforests","meaning":"熱帶雨林","examples":[{"en":"Rainforests contain a very high diversity of plant species.","zh":"熱帶雨林含有非常高度多樣化的植物品種。"},{"en":"Rainforests are dense forests in wet tropical areas with many kinds of plants and animals.","zh":"rainforests 指位於潮濕熱帶地區、擁有許多植物和動物種類的茂密森林。"},{"en":"Students may learn about rainforests when studying climate, biodiversity, and conservation.","zh":"學生學習氣候、生物多樣性和保育時，可能學到熱帶雨林。"},{"en":"When rainforests are cut down, many species lose habitat at once.","zh":"當熱帶雨林被砍伐，許多物種會同時失去棲息地。"},{"en":"This word is useful in ecology and environmental studies.","zh":"這個詞適用於生態和環境研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"high diversity of","meaning":"高度多樣化的……","examples":[{"en":"There is a high diversity of tree species in tropical forests.","zh":"熱帶森林中有高度多樣化的樹木品種。"},{"en":"A high diversity of something means many different types are present.","zh":"high diversity of something 指存在許多不同種類。"},{"en":"A city with a high diversity of restaurants offers many kinds of food.","zh":"有高度多樣化餐廳的城市提供許多種類的食物。"},{"en":"High diversity in forests can make ecological relationships more complex.","zh":"森林中的高度多樣性可以令生態關係更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing variety in a system.","zh":"描述系統中的多樣性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tree species","meaning":"樹木品種","examples":[{"en":"An acre of rainforest may contain more than 120 tree species.","zh":"一英畝熱帶雨林可能含有超過120種樹木品種。"},{"en":"Tree species are different biological kinds of trees.","zh":"tree species 指不同生物種類的樹木。"},{"en":"Pine, oak, mango, and banyan are different tree species.","zh":"松樹、橡樹、芒果樹和榕樹都是不同樹木品種。"},{"en":"A forest with many tree species may need many different pollinators and seed dispersers.","zh":"擁有許多樹木品種的森林，可能需要許多不同授粉者和種子散播者。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing biodiversity.","zh":"討論生物多樣性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"per acre","meaning":"每英畝","examples":[{"en":"There may be over 120 tree species per acre.","zh":"每英畝可能有超過120種樹木品種。"},{"en":"Per acre means for each acre of land.","zh":"per acre 指每一英畝土地。"},{"en":"A farm may produce several tonnes of vegetables per acre each year.","zh":"農場每英畝每年可能生產數噸蔬菜。"},{"en":"Measuring species per acre helps scientists compare how dense biodiversity is.","zh":"以每英畝計算物種，有助科學家比較生物多樣性的密度。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing land-based quantities.","zh":"描述與土地相關的數量時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in a given acre","meaning":"在某一英畝範圍內","examples":[{"en":"In a given acre, only one or two trees may belong to one species.","zh":"在某一英畝範圍內，可能只有一兩棵樹屬於同一品種。"},{"en":"In a given acre means within one particular acre being considered.","zh":"in a given acre 指在正在考慮的某一特定英畝範圍內。"},{"en":"In a given classroom, only a few students may choose the same elective subject.","zh":"在某一課室內，可能只有少數學生選同一選修科。"},{"en":"If only one or two trees of a species exist in a given acre, pollination may require long-distance movement.","zh":"如果某一英畝內某品種只有一兩棵樹，授粉可能需要長距離移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when focusing on one specific measured area.","zh":"聚焦某一特定測量區域時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"individuals of a species","meaning":"某一品種的個體","examples":[{"en":"There may be very few individuals of any one tree species.","zh":"任何一種樹木品種的個體可能非常少。"},{"en":"Individuals of a species are single organisms that belong to the same species.","zh":"individuals of a species 指屬於同一物種的單個生物。"},{"en":"In a pond, there may be many individuals of one frog species.","zh":"在池塘中，可能有許多屬於同一青蛙物種的個體。"},{"en":"If individuals of a species are far apart, pollination or mating becomes harder.","zh":"如果某一物種的個體距離很遠，授粉或交配就更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in biology and ecology.","zh":"這個短語適用於生物和生態學。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"large, fast-flying bees","meaning":"體型大、飛行迅速的蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"The trees are pollinated by large, fast-flying bees.","zh":"這些樹由體型大、飛行迅速的蜜蜂授粉。"},{"en":"Large, fast-flying bees are bees big and strong enough to travel quickly over long distances.","zh":"large, fast-flying bees 指體型較大、力量足以快速長距離飛行的蜜蜂。"},{"en":"A large, fast-flying insect can move between scattered flowers more easily than a slow one.","zh":"體型大、飛行迅速的昆蟲比慢速昆蟲更容易在分散花朵之間移動。"},{"en":"These bees are important because rainforest trees of the same species may be far apart.","zh":"這些蜜蜂很重要，因為雨林中同一品種的樹可能距離很遠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing pollinators suited to long-distance work.","zh":"描述適合長距離工作的授粉者時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"there is evidence that","meaning":"有證據顯示","examples":[{"en":"There is evidence that bees learn the location of scattered trees.","zh":"有證據顯示蜜蜂會學習分散樹木的位置。"},{"en":"There is evidence that means information or observations support the idea that something is true.","zh":"there is evidence that 指有資料或觀察支持某事為真。"},{"en":"There is evidence that students remember vocabulary better when they review it several times.","zh":"有證據顯示學生多次複習詞彙時記得更好。"},{"en":"Evidence makes a claim stronger than a simple guess.","zh":"證據令說法比單純猜測更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in academic and scientific writing.","zh":"這個短語適用於學術和科學寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"learn the distribution of","meaning":"掌握……的分布","examples":[{"en":"The bees learn the distribution of trees across the forest.","zh":"蜜蜂掌握森林中樹木的分布。"},{"en":"To learn the distribution of something means to understand where things are spread out in an area.","zh":"learn the distribution of something 指了解某些東西在一個區域中如何分散。"},{"en":"A delivery driver learns the distribution of shops in a district after working there for months.","zh":"送貨司機在一個區工作數月後，會掌握該區商店的分布。"},{"en":"Bees that know where scattered trees are can forage more efficiently.","zh":"知道分散樹木位置的蜜蜂可以更有效率地覓食。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when location patterns matter.","zh":"當位置模式重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"scattered trees","meaning":"分散各處的樹木","examples":[{"en":"The bees travel between widely scattered trees.","zh":"蜜蜂在分散各處的樹木之間飛行。"},{"en":"Scattered trees are trees spread out far from one another rather than growing close together.","zh":"scattered trees 指彼此距離較遠、不是密集生長的樹木。"},{"en":"In a city park, scattered trees may stand across several lawns.","zh":"在城市公園中，分散各處的樹木可能分布在幾片草地上。"},{"en":"When trees are scattered, pollinators may need to fly long distances between them.","zh":"當樹木分散，授粉者可能需要在它們之間長距離飛行。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing uneven distribution.","zh":"描述不均勻分布時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"forage regularly","meaning":"定期覓食","examples":[{"en":"The bees forage regularly along familiar routes.","zh":"蜜蜂沿着熟悉路線定期覓食。"},{"en":"To forage regularly means to search for food repeatedly and often.","zh":"forage regularly 指經常反覆尋找食物。"},{"en":"Birds may forage regularly near a school canteen because crumbs are often dropped there.","zh":"鳥類可能在學校飯堂附近定期覓食，因為那裏常有食物碎屑。"},{"en":"Regular foraging routes help bees save time and energy.","zh":"固定覓食路線幫助蜜蜂節省時間和能量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing repeated feeding behaviour.","zh":"描述反覆覓食行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"along the same routes","meaning":"沿着相同路線","examples":[{"en":"Certain bees repeatedly travel along the same routes.","zh":"某些蜜蜂反覆沿着相同路線飛行。"},{"en":"Along the same routes means following the same paths again and again.","zh":"along the same routes 指一次又一次跟隨相同路徑。"},{"en":"A student may walk along the same route to school every morning.","zh":"學生可能每天早上沿着相同路線步行上學。"},{"en":"Bees that use the same routes can remember where good food sources are located.","zh":"使用相同路線的蜜蜂可以記住良好食物來源的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing repeated movement patterns.","zh":"描述重複移動模式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"trap-lining","meaning":"定線巡迴覓食","examples":[{"en":"Repeatedly visiting flowers along fixed routes is called trap-lining.","zh":"沿固定路線反覆造訪花朵被稱為定線巡迴覓食。"},{"en":"Trap-lining is a foraging pattern in which an animal visits food sources in a regular sequence.","zh":"trap-lining 指動物按固定順序造訪食物來源的覓食模式。"},{"en":"A delivery worker following the same list of stops each day behaves a little like trap-lining.","zh":"每天按同一清單送貨的送貨員，行為有點像定線巡迴覓食。"},{"en":"Trap-lining helps bees collect food efficiently from scattered trees.","zh":"定線巡迴覓食幫助蜜蜂有效率地從分散樹木收集食物。"},{"en":"This word is useful when describing organised animal foraging routes.","zh":"描述有組織的動物覓食路線時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"forage for up to","meaning":"覓食距離可達……","examples":[{"en":"The bees may forage for up to 23 kilometres from their nests.","zh":"這些蜜蜂離巢覓食距離可達23公里。"},{"en":"Forage for up to a distance means search for food as far as that maximum distance.","zh":"forage for up to a distance 指尋找食物的距離最遠可到某範圍。"},{"en":"A delivery driver may travel for up to 30 kilometres from the warehouse each day.","zh":"送貨司機每天可能從倉庫出發行駛最多30公里。"},{"en":"Long foraging distances allow bees to connect trees that are far apart.","zh":"長距離覓食讓蜜蜂能連接相距很遠的樹木。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving a maximum range.","zh":"提供最大範圍時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"long-distance pollinators","meaning":"長距離授粉者","examples":[{"en":"These bees act as long-distance pollinators.","zh":"這些蜜蜂擔當長距離授粉者。"},{"en":"Long-distance pollinators are animals that move pollen across large distances between plants.","zh":"long-distance pollinators 指在植物之間長距離移動花粉的動物。"},{"en":"In a scattered forest, long-distance pollinators can connect trees that grow far apart.","zh":"在分散森林中，長距離授粉者可以連接相距很遠的樹木。"},{"en":"Without long-distance pollinators, isolated plants may fail to reproduce effectively.","zh":"沒有長距離授粉者，孤立植物可能無法有效繁殖。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in conservation and forest ecology.","zh":"這個短語適用於保育和森林生態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"issue of current concern","meaning":"當前關注的問題","examples":[{"en":"Forest fragmentation is an issue of current concern.","zh":"森林破碎化是當前關注的問題。"},{"en":"An issue of current concern is a problem people are worried about now.","zh":"issue of current concern 指人們現在擔心的問題。"},{"en":"Student mental health is an issue of current concern in many schools.","zh":"學生心理健康是許多學校當前關注的問題。"},{"en":"A current concern often needs research, policy, and public attention.","zh":"當前關注的問題通常需要研究、政策和公眾注意。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing a modern problem.","zh":"引入現代問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tropical forest conservation","meaning":"熱帶森林保育","examples":[{"en":"Bee flight range is important to tropical forest conservation.","zh":"蜜蜂飛行範圍對熱帶森林保育很重要。"},{"en":"Tropical forest conservation means protecting tropical forests and the species that live in them.","zh":"tropical forest conservation 指保護熱帶森林及其中生存的物種。"},{"en":"Tropical forest conservation may involve preventing illegal logging and creating protected reserves.","zh":"熱帶森林保育可能涉及防止非法伐木和建立保護區。"},{"en":"If pollinators cannot travel between forest areas, conservation plans may fail.","zh":"如果授粉者不能在森林區域之間移動，保育計劃可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing rainforest protection.","zh":"討論熱帶雨林保護時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"estimate the minimum sustainable size","meaning":"估算最低可持續面積","examples":[{"en":"Conservationists must estimate the minimum sustainable size of reserves.","zh":"保育人士必須估算保護區的最低可持續面積。"},{"en":"To estimate the minimum sustainable size means to calculate roughly the smallest area that can survive or function long term.","zh":"estimate the minimum sustainable size 指大約計算能長期生存或運作的最小面積。"},{"en":"City planners may estimate the minimum sustainable size of a park needed for a neighbourhood.","zh":"城市規劃者可能估算一個社區所需公園的最低可持續面積。"},{"en":"If a reserve is too small, it may not support enough plants, pollinators, and genetic exchange.","zh":"如果保護區太小，可能無法支持足夠植物、授粉者和基因交流。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when planning protected areas.","zh":"規劃保護區時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"forest reserve","meaning":"森林保護區","examples":[{"en":"A forest reserve must be large enough to support reproduction.","zh":"森林保護區必須足夠大，以支持繁殖。"},{"en":"A forest reserve is an area of forest protected from heavy development or destruction.","zh":"forest reserve 指受保護、避免嚴重發展或破壞的森林區域。"},{"en":"Families may visit a forest reserve to see trees, birds, insects, and streams.","zh":"家庭可能到森林保護區觀賞樹木、鳥類、昆蟲和溪流。"},{"en":"A reserve needs enough space for animals, plants, and pollinators to survive.","zh":"保護區需要足夠空間讓動物、植物和授粉者生存。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in conservation and land-use planning.","zh":"這個短語適用於保育和土地使用規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"islands of forest","meaning":"森林孤島","examples":[{"en":"Large-scale felling can leave isolated islands of forest.","zh":"大規模砍伐可以留下孤立的森林孤島。"},{"en":"Islands of forest are small forest areas left separate from a larger forest after clearing or development.","zh":"islands of forest 指清除或發展後與大型森林分離的小片森林區域。"},{"en":"A road project may divide woodland into islands of forest surrounded by buildings.","zh":"道路工程可能把林地分割成被建築物包圍的森林孤島。"},{"en":"Forest islands can isolate plants and animals, making reproduction and movement harder.","zh":"森林孤島可以隔離植物和動物，使繁殖和移動更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing habitat fragmentation.","zh":"討論棲息地破碎化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"large-scale felling","meaning":"大規模砍伐","examples":[{"en":"Large-scale felling causes severe forest fragmentation.","zh":"大規模砍伐造成嚴重森林破碎化。"},{"en":"Large-scale felling means cutting down trees over a large area.","zh":"large-scale felling 指在大範圍內砍伐樹木。"},{"en":"Large-scale felling near a village can remove shade, wildlife habitat, and flood protection.","zh":"村莊附近的大規模砍伐可以移除樹蔭、野生動物棲息地和防洪保護。"},{"en":"When many trees are cut at once, forests may break into isolated patches.","zh":"當大量樹木一次被砍伐，森林可能破碎成孤立斑塊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing deforestation.","zh":"討論森林砍伐時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"take place","meaning":"發生；進行","examples":[{"en":"Large-scale felling is taking place in many tropical regions.","zh":"大規模砍伐正在許多熱帶地區發生。"},{"en":"Take place means happen or occur.","zh":"take place 指發生或進行。"},{"en":"The school sports day will take place on Friday morning.","zh":"學校運動會將在星期五早上舉行。"},{"en":"When felling takes place across large areas, ecosystems can change quickly.","zh":"當砍伐在大範圍內發生，生態系統可以迅速改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing events or processes.","zh":"描述事件或過程時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"much discussion on","meaning":"有很多關於……的討論","examples":[{"en":"There is much discussion on seed dispersal distances.","zh":"有很多關於種子散播距離的討論。"},{"en":"Much discussion on something means many people talk, write, or argue about that topic.","zh":"much discussion on something 指許多人談論、書寫或爭論某主題。"},{"en":"There is much discussion on whether students should use phones at school.","zh":"有很多關於學生是否應在學校使用手機的討論。"},{"en":"A topic attracts much discussion when it affects important decisions.","zh":"當一個主題影響重要決策，它就會引起大量討論。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing that an issue is widely debated.","zh":"顯示議題被廣泛討論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"seed dispersal","meaning":"種子散播","examples":[{"en":"Seed dispersal is only one part of tree reproduction.","zh":"種子散播只是樹木繁殖的一部分。"},{"en":"Seed dispersal is the movement of seeds away from the parent plant.","zh":"seed dispersal 指種子離開母株並移動到其他地方。"},{"en":"Birds can help seed dispersal when they eat fruit and later drop seeds elsewhere.","zh":"鳥類吃果實後在其他地方排出種子，就可以幫助種子散播。"},{"en":"Seed dispersal helps plants spread, but pollination is also needed before seeds can form.","zh":"種子散播幫助植物擴散，但種子形成前也需要授粉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in plant biology and forest ecology.","zh":"這個短語適用於植物生物學和森林生態。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"one half of the equation","meaning":"問題的一半","examples":[{"en":"Seed dispersal is only one half of the equation.","zh":"種子散播只是問題的一半。"},{"en":"One half of the equation means only one of two important parts of a problem.","zh":"one half of the equation 指一個問題中兩個重要部分之一。"},{"en":"Practising speaking is one half of the equation; getting feedback is the other half.","zh":"練習說話是問題的一半；得到回饋是另一半。"},{"en":"For tree reproduction, moving seeds matters, but moving pollen matters too.","zh":"對樹木繁殖來說，移動種子重要，但移動花粉也重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a solution needs two connected parts.","zh":"當解決方案需要兩個相連部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"so far as…is concerned","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"Pollination is essential so far as tree reproduction is concerned.","zh":"就樹木繁殖而言，授粉是必不可少的。"},{"en":"So far as something is concerned means regarding that particular topic.","zh":"so far as something is concerned 指就某個特定主題而言。"},{"en":"So far as exam writing is concerned, clear structure is more important than fancy vocabulary.","zh":"就考試寫作而言，清楚結構比華麗詞彙更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase limits the statement to one area of discussion.","zh":"這個短語把說法限制在某一討論範圍內。"},{"en":"It is useful when focusing on a specific issue.","zh":"聚焦特定議題時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"reproduction of trees","meaning":"樹木繁殖","examples":[{"en":"Pollination and seed dispersal both affect the reproduction of trees.","zh":"授粉和種子散播都影響樹木繁殖。"},{"en":"The reproduction of trees is the process by which trees produce new trees.","zh":"reproduction of trees 指樹木產生新樹的過程。"},{"en":"Flowers, pollen, fruits, seeds, wind, animals, and insects can all be involved in tree reproduction.","zh":"花、花粉、果實、種子、風、動物和昆蟲都可以涉及樹木繁殖。"},{"en":"If pollination fails, the reproduction of trees may be reduced even if seeds can travel far.","zh":"如果授粉失敗，即使種子能遠距離移動，樹木繁殖仍可能減少。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing forest survival.","zh":"討論森林延續時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"must be addressed","meaning":"必須處理","examples":[{"en":"Another important question must be addressed.","zh":"另一個重要問題必須處理。"},{"en":"Must be addressed means must be dealt with or considered seriously.","zh":"must be addressed 指必須被處理或認真考慮。"},{"en":"If students keep arriving late, the transport problem must be addressed.","zh":"如果學生一直遲到，交通問題就必須處理。"},{"en":"A problem that is not addressed may continue to damage the final decision.","zh":"未被處理的問題可能繼續損害最終決策。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying necessary action.","zh":"指出必要行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in order to calculate","meaning":"為了計算……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists need more information in order to calculate suitable reserve distances.","zh":"科學家需要更多資料，以計算合適的保護區距離。"},{"en":"In order to calculate means for the purpose of working out a number or measurement.","zh":"in order to calculate 指為了計算某個數字或量度。"},{"en":"A family checks ticket prices in order to calculate the total cost of a trip.","zh":"家庭查看票價，以計算旅行總成本。"},{"en":"Scientists need data on bee flight ranges before they can calculate reserve spacing.","zh":"科學家需要蜜蜂飛行範圍的數據，才可以計算保護區間距。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why information is needed.","zh":"解釋為何需要資料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"proposed forest reserves","meaning":"建議中的森林保護區","examples":[{"en":"Researchers assess whether proposed forest reserves are sufficiently connected.","zh":"研究人員評估建議中的森林保護區是否有足夠連接。"},{"en":"Proposed forest reserves are protected forest areas that have been suggested but may not yet be fully established.","zh":"proposed forest reserves 指已被提出但可能尚未完全建立的受保護森林區。"},{"en":"A government may hold public meetings about proposed forest reserves before making a final decision.","zh":"政府在作最終決定前，可能就建議中的森林保護區舉行公眾會議。"},{"en":"Proposed reserves must be checked to see whether they can actually support wildlife.","zh":"建議中的保護區必須被檢查，以判斷它們是否真的能支持野生動物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in conservation planning.","zh":"這個短語適用於保育規劃。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be close enough to","meaning":"與……距離足夠接近","examples":[{"en":"A forest reserve must be close enough to another large forest.","zh":"森林保護區必須與另一大片森林距離足夠接近。"},{"en":"Be close enough to something means be near enough for a purpose to be achieved.","zh":"be close enough to something 指距離夠近，以便達到某目的。"},{"en":"A student’s home may be close enough to school for walking to be practical.","zh":"學生家可能離學校足夠近，可以實際步行上學。"},{"en":"If reserves are close enough, pollinators may travel between them.","zh":"如果保護區距離足夠接近，授粉者可能在它們之間移動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when distance affects success.","zh":"當距離影響成敗時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"large tract of forest","meaning":"大片森林","examples":[{"en":"Pollinators may need access to a large tract of forest.","zh":"授粉者可能需要進入大片森林。"},{"en":"A large tract of forest is a wide continuous area of forest land.","zh":"large tract of forest 指一大片連續森林土地。"},{"en":"Wildlife often survives better in a large tract of forest than in tiny isolated patches.","zh":"野生動物在大片森林中通常比在細小孤立斑塊中更容易生存。"},{"en":"Large forest areas can support more plants, animals, and pollination routes.","zh":"大片森林可以支持更多植物、動物和授粉路線。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing habitat size.","zh":"討論棲息地大小時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"flight range","meaning":"飛行範圍","examples":[{"en":"Scientists need to understand the flight range of pollinating bees.","zh":"科學家需要了解授粉蜜蜂的飛行範圍。"},{"en":"Flight range is the distance an animal or aircraft can fly from one point.","zh":"flight range 指動物或飛行器從某點出發能飛行的距離。"},{"en":"A drone’s flight range determines how far it can travel before the battery runs out.","zh":"無人機的飛行範圍決定它在電池耗盡前能飛多遠。"},{"en":"A bee’s flight range affects whether it can connect separated forest areas.","zh":"蜜蜂的飛行範圍影響牠是否能連接分離的森林區域。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when distance and movement matter.","zh":"當距離和移動很重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"long-distance foragers","meaning":"長距離覓食者","examples":[{"en":"Long-distance foragers may travel many kilometres from their nests.","zh":"長距離覓食者可能離巢數公里覓食。"},{"en":"Long-distance foragers are animals that search for food far from where they live.","zh":"long-distance foragers 指遠離住所尋找食物的動物。"},{"en":"Some seabirds are long-distance foragers because they fly far out to sea for fish.","zh":"有些海鳥是長距離覓食者，因為牠們飛到遠海捕魚。"},{"en":"Long-distance foragers can connect widely separated food sources or plant populations.","zh":"長距離覓食者可以連接相距很遠的食物來源或植物種群。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in ecology and animal behaviour.","zh":"這個短語適用於生態和動物行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"before this question can be answered","meaning":"在能回答這個問題之前","examples":[{"en":"More research is needed before this question can be answered.","zh":"在能回答這個問題之前，需要更多研究。"},{"en":"Before this question can be answered means before people have enough evidence to give a reliable answer.","zh":"before this question can be answered 指在人們有足夠證據給出可靠答案之前。"},{"en":"A doctor may need test results before a patient’s question can be answered.","zh":"醫生可能需要測試結果，才能回答病人的問題。"},{"en":"Scientists need more data on bee movement before they can judge reserve distances confidently.","zh":"科學家需要更多蜜蜂移動數據，才可以有信心判斷保護區距離。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence is still incomplete.","zh":"當證據仍不完整時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be vital to our survival","meaning":"對我們的生存至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Bees are vital to our survival.","zh":"蜜蜂對我們的生存至關重要。"},{"en":"To be vital to our survival means to be extremely important for humans to continue living.","zh":"be vital to our survival 指對人類繼續生存極其重要。"},{"en":"Clean water is vital to our survival because the body cannot function without it.","zh":"清潔食水對我們的生存至關重要，因為身體沒有水不能運作。"},{"en":"Bees support food production and natural vegetation, so their loss would affect human life deeply.","zh":"蜜蜂支持糧食生產和天然植被，所以失去牠們會深深影響人類生活。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing life-and-death importance.","zh":"強調生死攸關的重要性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"visual impact","meaning":"視覺效果","examples":[{"en":"Vegetation contributes greatly to the visual impact of human environments.","zh":"植被大大影響人類生活環境的視覺效果。"},{"en":"Visual impact means the effect something has on how a place looks.","zh":"visual impact 指某物對一個地方外觀造成的影響。"},{"en":"Street trees can improve the visual impact of a busy road.","zh":"街道樹木可以改善繁忙道路的視覺效果。"},{"en":"When plants disappear, a town may look harsher, hotter, and less welcoming.","zh":"當植物消失，城鎮可能看起來更嚴酷、更炎熱和較不友善。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing appearance and design.","zh":"討論外觀和設計時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"human environments","meaning":"人類生活環境","examples":[{"en":"Plants improve the appearance and ecology of human environments.","zh":"植物改善人類生活環境的外觀和生態。"},{"en":"Human environments are places shaped or used by people, such as cities, farms, parks, and homes.","zh":"human environments 指由人類塑造或使用的地方，例如城市、農場、公園和家居。"},{"en":"Schools and housing estates are human environments where greenery can improve daily life.","zh":"學校和屋苑都是人類生活環境，綠化可以改善日常生活。"},{"en":"Plants in human environments can reduce heat, improve air, and make places more pleasant.","zh":"人類生活環境中的植物可以減少熱力、改善空氣，並令地方更舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing nature around people.","zh":"討論人類周圍的自然時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"derive from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"Much of the beauty of our surroundings derives from vegetation.","zh":"我們周圍環境的許多美感源自植被。"},{"en":"Derive from means come from or originate in something.","zh":"derive from 指來自或起源於某物。"},{"en":"Many English words derive from Latin or French.","zh":"許多英文詞源自拉丁語或法語。"},{"en":"If beauty derives from vegetation, losing plants also reduces the quality of human surroundings.","zh":"如果美感源自植被，失去植物也會降低人類周圍環境的質素。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when tracing the source of something.","zh":"追溯某事來源時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"vegetation","meaning":"植被","examples":[{"en":"Most natural vegetation depends on animal pollination.","zh":"大多數天然植被依賴動物授粉。"},{"en":"Vegetation means plants growing in an area, especially collectively.","zh":"vegetation 指某區域中生長的植物，尤其是作為整體來看。"},{"en":"A hillside covered in grass, bushes, and trees has thick vegetation.","zh":"覆蓋着草、灌木和樹木的山坡有茂密植被。"},{"en":"Vegetation provides beauty, shade, oxygen, habitat, and food for many species.","zh":"植被提供美感、樹蔭、氧氣、棲息地和許多物種的食物。"},{"en":"This word is useful in ecology, geography, and environmental writing.","zh":"這個詞適用於生態、地理和環境寫作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"natural vegetation","meaning":"天然植被","examples":[{"en":"Bees pollinate both crops and natural vegetation.","zh":"蜜蜂為農作物和天然植被授粉。"},{"en":"Natural vegetation is plant life that grows without being planted or managed mainly by humans.","zh":"natural vegetation 指不是主要由人類種植或管理而自然生長的植物。"},{"en":"Forests, wild grasses, and native shrubs can be natural vegetation.","zh":"森林、野草和本地灌木都可以是天然植被。"},{"en":"If pollinators decline, natural vegetation may reproduce less successfully.","zh":"如果授粉者減少，天然植被可能繁殖得較不成功。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting wild plants with farm crops.","zh":"對比野生植物和農作物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"occupy key positions","meaning":"佔據關鍵位置","examples":[{"en":"Bees occupy key positions in ecological networks.","zh":"蜜蜂在生態網絡中佔據關鍵位置。"},{"en":"To occupy key positions means to hold important roles in a system.","zh":"occupy key positions 指在系統中擁有重要角色。"},{"en":"Nurses occupy key positions in hospitals because they connect patients, doctors, and care routines.","zh":"護士在醫院中佔據關鍵位置，因為他們連接病人、醫生和護理流程。"},{"en":"Bees occupy key positions because they link plants, crops, animals, and human food supplies.","zh":"蜜蜂佔據關鍵位置，因為牠們連接植物、農作物、動物和人類食物供應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing central roles.","zh":"描述核心角色時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"web of relationships","meaning":"關係網絡","examples":[{"en":"Species survive within a complex web of relationships.","zh":"物種在複雜的關係網絡中生存。"},{"en":"A web of relationships is a network of connections between many people, organisms, or things.","zh":"web of relationships 指許多人、生物或事物之間的連接網絡。"},{"en":"In a school, students, teachers, parents, and rules form a web of relationships.","zh":"在學校中，學生、老師、家長和規則形成關係網絡。"},{"en":"In nature, changing one species can affect many others in the web.","zh":"在自然界中，改變一個物種可以影響網絡中的許多其他物種。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining interconnected systems.","zh":"解釋互相連繫的系統時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"sustain the living architecture","meaning":"維持生命體系","examples":[{"en":"Pollinators help sustain the living architecture of the planet.","zh":"授粉者幫助維持地球的生命體系。"},{"en":"To sustain the living architecture means to support the living structure that keeps ecosystems functioning.","zh":"sustain the living architecture 指支撐使生態系統運作的生命結構。"},{"en":"Teachers and families sustain the living architecture of a school community by supporting students daily.","zh":"老師和家庭透過每天支援學生，維持學校社群的生命體系。"},{"en":"Pollinators keep plants reproducing, and plants support food webs, soil, climate, and habitats.","zh":"授粉者讓植物繁殖，而植物支撐食物網、土壤、氣候和棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase is metaphorical and describes ecological support.","zh":"這個短語是比喻性，描述生態支撐作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"living architecture of our planet","meaning":"地球的生命結構","examples":[{"en":"Plants and pollinators form part of the living architecture of our planet.","zh":"植物和授粉者構成地球生命結構的一部分。"},{"en":"The living architecture of our planet means the connected structure of life that supports Earth’s ecosystems.","zh":"living architecture of our planet 指支撐地球生態系統的相連生命結構。"},{"en":"Forests, oceans, insects, soil organisms, and plants all belong to this living architecture.","zh":"森林、海洋、昆蟲、土壤生物和植物都屬於這種生命結構。"},{"en":"If key species disappear, the structure of living systems can weaken.","zh":"如果關鍵物種消失，生命系統的結構可能削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing Earth’s life as an interconnected structure.","zh":"把地球生命描述為互相連接的結構時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to choose the correct heading for each paragraph.","zh":"考生需要為每段選出正確標題。"},{"en":"To choose the correct heading means to select the title that best summarises a paragraph.","zh":"choose the correct heading 指選出最能概括段落的標題。"},{"en":"In IELTS reading, students choose headings by identifying the main idea, not one small detail.","zh":"在 IELTS 閱讀中，學生透過找出主旨來選標題，而不是看一個小細節。"},{"en":"Choosing the wrong heading often happens when students match only repeated words.","zh":"當學生只配對重複字眼時，常會選錯標題。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading-test instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀測驗指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The question provides a list of headings for the passage.","zh":"題目提供文章的標題列表。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a set of possible paragraph titles to choose from.","zh":"list of headings 指一組可供選擇的段落標題。"},{"en":"Students may read the list of headings before skimming each paragraph.","zh":"學生可能先閱讀標題列表，再略讀每段。"},{"en":"A heading list helps test whether students understand paragraph main ideas.","zh":"標題列表有助測試學生是否理解段落主旨。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in matching-headings questions.","zh":"這個短語常見於配對標題題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"parallels between","meaning":"……之間的相似之處","examples":[{"en":"The passage draws parallels between bee activity and human economics.","zh":"文章指出蜜蜂活動與人類經濟之間的相似之處。"},{"en":"Parallels between two things are similarities that make them comparable.","zh":"parallels between two things 指令兩者可以比較的相似之處。"},{"en":"A teacher may draw parallels between sports training and exam preparation.","zh":"老師可能指出運動訓練與考試準備之間的相似之處。"},{"en":"Seeing parallels between bees and markets helps readers understand ecological competition.","zh":"看見蜜蜂與市場之間的相似之處，幫助讀者理解生態競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing two different fields.","zh":"比較兩個不同領域時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"human activities","meaning":"人類活動","examples":[{"en":"Economic metaphors connect bee behaviour with human activities.","zh":"經濟比喻把蜜蜂行為與人類活動連接起來。"},{"en":"Human activities are things people do, such as farming, trading, building, travelling, or studying.","zh":"human activities 指人類所做的事情，例如耕作、交易、建造、旅行或學習。"},{"en":"Shopping, working, driving, and using electricity are everyday human activities.","zh":"購物、工作、駕車和用電都是日常人類活動。"},{"en":"Human activities can affect ecosystems through farming, logging, pollution, and conservation.","zh":"人類活動可以透過農業、伐木、污染和保育影響生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when linking people’s behaviour with environmental change.","zh":"把人類行為與環境變化連接起來時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"evolutionary turning point","meaning":"進化轉捩點","examples":[{"en":"The move from hunting to pollen feeding was an evolutionary turning point.","zh":"從捕獵轉向以花粉為食是一個進化轉捩點。"},{"en":"An evolutionary turning point is a major change that shifts the future development of a species.","zh":"evolutionary turning point 指改變物種未來發展方向的重大變化。"},{"en":"The ability to walk upright was an evolutionary turning point in human history.","zh":"直立行走能力是人類歷史中的進化轉捩點。"},{"en":"Once wasps began feeding on pollen, a new relationship with flowering plants could develop.","zh":"一旦黃蜂開始以花粉為食，牠們就能與開花植物發展出新關係。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a change redirects evolution.","zh":"當某變化改變演化方向時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lack of total co-operation","meaning":"缺乏完全合作","examples":[{"en":"The bee–plant relationship involves a lack of total co-operation.","zh":"蜜蜂與植物關係涉及缺乏完全合作。"},{"en":"Lack of total co-operation means the two sides do not fully work together because each has its own interests.","zh":"lack of total co-operation 指雙方沒有完全合作，因為各自有自身利益。"},{"en":"A group project may suffer from a lack of total co-operation if every student wants the easiest task.","zh":"如果每個學生都想做最容易任務，小組項目可能出現缺乏完全合作。"},{"en":"Bees and flowers cooperate partly, but both still try to maximise their own benefits.","zh":"蜜蜂和花部分合作，但雙方仍試圖將自身利益最大化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when cooperation is mixed with conflict.","zh":"當合作中混合衝突時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"preservation of","meaning":"……的保育","examples":[{"en":"Pollinator research may support the preservation of individual plant species.","zh":"授粉者研究可能支持個別植物品種的保育。"},{"en":"Preservation of something means protecting it so it continues to exist.","zh":"preservation of something 指保護某物，使它繼續存在。"},{"en":"Museums work for the preservation of old photographs, tools, and documents.","zh":"博物館致力於保存舊照片、工具和文件。"},{"en":"If pollinators disappear, the preservation of some plants becomes harder.","zh":"如果授粉者消失，某些植物的保育會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing conservation and protection.","zh":"討論保育和保護時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"individual plant species","meaning":"個別植物品種","examples":[{"en":"Some individual plant species depend on specialised pollinators.","zh":"某些個別植物品種依賴專門授粉者。"},{"en":"Individual plant species are particular kinds of plants considered separately.","zh":"individual plant species 指被分開考慮的特定植物種類。"},{"en":"A rare orchid is an individual plant species that may need special protection.","zh":"罕見蘭花是一種可能需要特別保護的個別植物品種。"},{"en":"If one plant species depends on one pollinator, losing that pollinator can threaten the plant.","zh":"如果一個植物品種依賴一種授粉者，失去該授粉者就可能威脅植物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when focusing on one species rather than whole forests.","zh":"聚焦單一物種而不是整片森林時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"commercial value","meaning":"商業價值","examples":[{"en":"The commercial value of bees greatly exceeds the value of honey.","zh":"蜜蜂的商業價值遠超蜂蜜的價值。"},{"en":"Commercial value is the amount of money or economic benefit something can produce.","zh":"commercial value 指某物能產生的金錢價值或經濟利益。"},{"en":"A busy train station has commercial value because many shops can serve passengers there.","zh":"繁忙火車站有商業價值，因為許多商店可以服務乘客。"},{"en":"Bees have commercial value because their pollination supports valuable crops.","zh":"蜜蜂有商業價值，因為牠們的授粉支援有價值的農作物。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing economic importance.","zh":"討論經濟重要性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"structure of flowering plants","meaning":"開花植物的結構","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to the structure of flowering plants.","zh":"這個選項提到開花植物的結構。"},{"en":"The structure of flowering plants means the parts and arrangement of plants that produce flowers.","zh":"structure of flowering plants 指開花植物的部分及其排列方式。"},{"en":"A biology diagram may show the structure of flowering plants, including petals, stamens, and ovaries.","zh":"生物圖表可能展示開花植物的結構，包括花瓣、雄蕊和子房。"},{"en":"Plant structure affects how pollinators reach nectar and pollen.","zh":"植物結構影響授粉者如何到達花蜜和花粉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing plant anatomy.","zh":"討論植物解剖時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"pursuit of self-interest","meaning":"追求自身利益","examples":[{"en":"Both flowers and bees are engaged in the pursuit of self-interest.","zh":"花和蜜蜂都在追求自身利益。"},{"en":"Pursuit of self-interest means trying to gain one’s own advantage or benefit.","zh":"pursuit of self-interest 指試圖取得自身優勢或利益。"},{"en":"A shopper comparing prices is acting in pursuit of self-interest.","zh":"購物者比較價格，就是在追求自身利益。"},{"en":"Bees seek food, while flowers seek pollination, so both sides pursue their own benefit.","zh":"蜜蜂尋求食物，而花尋求授粉，所以雙方都追求自己的利益。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining competition and motivation.","zh":"解釋競爭和動機時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"need for further research","meaning":"需要進一步研究","examples":[{"en":"The passage emphasises the need for further research into pollinators.","zh":"文章強調需要進一步研究授粉者。"},{"en":"Need for further research means more study is required before people can fully understand or decide something.","zh":"need for further research 指在人們能完全理解或作決定前，需要更多研究。"},{"en":"Doctors may state a need for further research before recommending a new treatment widely.","zh":"醫生可能在廣泛建議新療法前，指出需要進一步研究。"},{"en":"More research on bee flight range can help design better forest reserves.","zh":"對蜜蜂飛行範圍作更多研究，可以幫助設計更好的森林保護區。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when evidence is not yet complete.","zh":"當證據尚未完整時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"complete the sentences below","meaning":"完成以下句子","examples":[{"en":"Candidates need to complete the sentences below using words from the passage.","zh":"考生需要使用文章中的詞語完成以下句子。"},{"en":"Complete the sentences below means fill in missing words in the sentences that follow the instruction.","zh":"complete the sentences below 指填寫指示後句子中的缺漏詞語。"},{"en":"Students should complete the sentences below by checking the exact wording in the text.","zh":"學生應透過檢查文本中的準確用詞來完成以下句子。"},{"en":"This task tests understanding and careful word choice.","zh":"這項任務測試理解和仔細選詞。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reading exam instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於閱讀考試指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"no more than two words and/or a number","meaning":"不多於兩個字及／或一個數字","examples":[{"en":"Each answer should contain no more than two words and/or a number.","zh":"每個答案應包含不多於兩個字及／或一個數字。"},{"en":"No more than two words and/or a number means the answer must be very short and follow that limit.","zh":"no more than two words and/or a number 指答案必須很短並符合該限制。"},{"en":"If the answer is “23 kilometres,” it follows the limit because it has a number and one word.","zh":"如果答案是 23 kilometres，它符合限制，因為有一個數字和一個詞。"},{"en":"Writing too many words can lose marks even if the idea is correct.","zh":"即使意思正確，寫太多詞也可能失分。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in IELTS-style completion tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於 IELTS 類填空題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"feed on","meaning":"以……為食","examples":[{"en":"Hunting wasps used to feed on other insects.","zh":"捕獵黃蜂以前以其他昆蟲為食。"},{"en":"To feed on something means to eat it as food.","zh":"feed on something 指把某物作為食物來吃。"},{"en":"Cows feed on grass, while many birds feed on seeds or insects.","zh":"牛以草為食，而許多鳥以種子或昆蟲為食。"},{"en":"When ancestral wasps stopped feeding mainly on insects, their diet began to change.","zh":"當祖先黃蜂不再主要以昆蟲為食，牠們的飲食開始改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing what animals eat.","zh":"描述動物吃甚麼時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"The ancestral wasps ate insects rather than vegetation.","zh":"祖先黃蜂吃昆蟲，而不是植物。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of.","zh":"rather than 指而不是。"},{"en":"A student may revise with examples rather than memorising rules alone.","zh":"學生可能用例子溫習，而不是只背規則。"},{"en":"The contrast shows that early wasps were hunters, not plant feeders.","zh":"這個對比顯示早期黃蜂是捕獵者，而不是以植物為食。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when separating two alternatives.","zh":"區分兩個選項時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"additional food","meaning":"額外食物","examples":[{"en":"Flowers provided nectar as an additional food for bees.","zh":"花提供花蜜作為蜜蜂的額外食物。"},{"en":"Additional food means extra food beyond what is already available.","zh":"additional food 指原本已有食物以外的額外食物。"},{"en":"A school may provide fruit as additional food for children who stay late for activities.","zh":"學校可能為留下參加活動的兒童提供水果作為額外食物。"},{"en":"Nectar gave bees another energy source besides pollen.","zh":"花蜜給蜜蜂花粉以外的另一種能量來源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing an extra supply of nutrition.","zh":"描述額外營養供應時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in the form of","meaning":"以……的形式","examples":[{"en":"Flowers offered extra nutrition in the form of nectar.","zh":"花以花蜜的形式提供額外營養。"},{"en":"In the form of means appearing or being provided as a particular type of thing.","zh":"in the form of 指以某種特定形式出現或被提供。"},{"en":"A teacher may give feedback in the form of written comments.","zh":"老師可能以書面評語的形式給予回饋。"},{"en":"Flowers provide rewards in the form of nectar and pollen, not money or praise.","zh":"花以花蜜和花粉的形式提供回報，而不是金錢或稱讚。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the shape or type of something.","zh":"描述某物的形式或種類時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"food production","meaning":"糧食生產","examples":[{"en":"A large proportion of human food production relies on bees.","zh":"人類糧食生產中很大比例依賴蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Food production is the process of growing, raising, harvesting, and preparing food.","zh":"food production 指種植、飼養、收成和準備食物的過程。"},{"en":"Farms, fisheries, factories, and markets all play roles in food production.","zh":"農場、漁業、工廠和市場都在糧食生產中扮演角色。"},{"en":"If pollination declines, food production can become less reliable.","zh":"如果授粉下降，糧食生產可能變得較不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing agriculture and human survival.","zh":"討論農業和人類生存時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"rely on the activity of","meaning":"依賴……的活動","examples":[{"en":"Many crops rely on the activity of pollinating insects.","zh":"許多農作物依賴授粉昆蟲的活動。"},{"en":"To rely on the activity of something means to depend on what it does.","zh":"rely on the activity of something 指依靠某物所做的事情。"},{"en":"A shop may rely on the activity of delivery drivers to send goods to customers.","zh":"商店可能依賴送貨司機的活動，把貨物送到顧客手上。"},{"en":"Crops rely on insects because the insects move pollen between flowers.","zh":"農作物依賴昆蟲，因為昆蟲在花朵之間移動花粉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when one process depends on another agent’s actions.","zh":"當一個過程依賴另一個行動者的活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"take place effectively","meaning":"有效進行","examples":[{"en":"Pollination can take place effectively only if bees visit several flowers.","zh":"只有蜜蜂造訪幾朵花，授粉才能有效進行。"},{"en":"To take place effectively means to happen successfully and produce the intended result.","zh":"take place effectively 指成功發生並產生預期結果。"},{"en":"A group discussion can take place effectively only if everyone listens and takes turns.","zh":"只有每個人聆聽並輪流發言，小組討論才能有效進行。"},{"en":"Pollination is more effective when pollen is moved between different flowers of the same species.","zh":"當花粉在同一品種的不同花之間移動，授粉會更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when conditions affect success.","zh":"當條件影響成敗時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"travel from one flower to another","meaning":"從一朵花飛到另一朵花","examples":[{"en":"Bees must travel from one flower to another during pollination.","zh":"授粉期間，蜜蜂必須從一朵花飛到另一朵花。"},{"en":"To travel from one flower to another means to move between flowers instead of staying in one place.","zh":"travel from one flower to another 指在花之間移動，而不是停留在一處。"},{"en":"A child may move from one activity station to another during a school fair.","zh":"孩子在學校嘉年華中可能從一個活動站移到另一個活動站。"},{"en":"Bees moving between flowers allow pollen to be transferred.","zh":"蜜蜂在花之間移動，使花粉能被轉移。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the movement needed for pollination.","zh":"解釋授粉所需移動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"go back to the nest","meaning":"返回蜂巢","examples":[{"en":"A bee may go back to the nest after collecting enough food.","zh":"蜜蜂收集足夠食物後可能返回蜂巢。"},{"en":"To go back to the nest means to return to the bee’s home or colony.","zh":"go back to the nest 指返回蜜蜂的家或群體。"},{"en":"A bird may go back to the nest after collecting twigs or food.","zh":"鳥收集樹枝或食物後，可能返回巢中。"},{"en":"If a bee goes back too early, it may not pollinate another flower.","zh":"如果蜜蜂太早返回蜂巢，它可能不會為另一朵花授粉。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing an animal returning home.","zh":"描述動物回家時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"balance something against something","meaning":"將……與……權衡","examples":[{"en":"Bees balance the energy costs of a trip against its rewards.","zh":"蜜蜂將一趟旅程的能量成本與其回報權衡。"},{"en":"To balance something against something means to compare two sides before deciding whether it is worth it.","zh":"balance something against something 指在作決定前比較兩方面是否值得。"},{"en":"A student may balance the cost of extra lessons against the improvement they may bring.","zh":"學生可能將補習費用與可能帶來的進步權衡。"},{"en":"Bees must decide whether the food reward is worth the energy spent flying.","zh":"蜜蜂必須判斷食物回報是否值得飛行所花的能量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing cost-benefit thinking.","zh":"描述成本效益思維時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"calorific rewards","meaning":"熱量回報","examples":[{"en":"Nectar and pollen provide calorific rewards to bees.","zh":"花蜜和花粉為蜜蜂提供熱量回報。"},{"en":"Calorific rewards are food benefits that provide energy in the form of calories.","zh":"calorific rewards 指以卡路里形式提供能量的食物好處。"},{"en":"A snack after sports gives a child a calorific reward for the energy used.","zh":"運動後的零食給孩子補充消耗能量的熱量回報。"},{"en":"Bees need calorific rewards because flying and foraging consume energy.","zh":"蜜蜂需要熱量回報，因為飛行和覓食會消耗能量。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing food energy as a benefit.","zh":"把食物能量作為好處討論時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"practise an activity known as","meaning":"進行一種稱為……的活動","examples":[{"en":"The bees practise an activity known as trap-lining.","zh":"蜜蜂進行一種稱為定線巡迴覓食的活動。"},{"en":"To practise an activity known as something means to regularly do an activity with that name.","zh":"practise an activity known as something 指定期進行一種有該名稱的活動。"},{"en":"Some students practise an activity known as shadowing to improve pronunciation.","zh":"有些學生進行一種稱為 shadowing 的活動來改善發音。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a technical term after describing the behaviour.","zh":"這個短語在描述行為後引入技術術語。"},{"en":"This structure is useful when naming a process for learners.","zh":"為學習者命名一個過程時，這個結構很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"best title for","meaning":"……的最佳標題","examples":[{"en":"The question asks candidates to select the best title for the passage.","zh":"題目要求考生選出文章的最佳標題。"},{"en":"The best title for something is the title that most accurately summarises its main idea.","zh":"best title for something 指最準確概括其主旨的標題。"},{"en":"Students choose the best title for an article after identifying the overall message.","zh":"學生找出整體訊息後，為文章選出最佳標題。"},{"en":"A title that focuses on only one detail may not be the best title for the whole passage.","zh":"只聚焦一個細節的標題，未必是整篇文章的最佳標題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in main-idea reading questions.","zh":"這個短語適用於主旨閱讀題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"evolutionary history","meaning":"進化歷史","examples":[{"en":"The passage refers briefly to the evolutionary history of bees.","zh":"文章簡短提到蜜蜂的進化歷史。"},{"en":"Evolutionary history is the record of how a species or group changed over time.","zh":"evolutionary history 指某物種或群體隨時間如何改變的記錄。"},{"en":"Fossils and DNA can help scientists reconstruct the evolutionary history of animals.","zh":"化石和 DNA 可以幫助科學家重構動物的進化歷史。"},{"en":"The evolutionary history of bees includes their shift from hunting insects to feeding on pollen.","zh":"蜜蜂的進化歷史包括牠們從捕獵昆蟲轉向以花粉為食。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing origins and long-term biological change.","zh":"討論起源和長期生物變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"social behaviour","meaning":"社會行為","examples":[{"en":"The option focuses on the social behaviour of bees.","zh":"這個選項聚焦蜜蜂的社會行為。"},{"en":"Social behaviour means how animals or people interact with others in a group.","zh":"social behaviour 指動物或人在群體中如何與其他成員互動。"},{"en":"Ants show social behaviour when they work together to find food.","zh":"螞蟻一起尋找食物時，就展現社會行為。"},{"en":"Bee social behaviour may include cooperation inside the hive, but this passage focuses more on pollination and ecology.","zh":"蜜蜂社會行為可能包括蜂巢內合作，但這篇文章更聚焦授粉和生態。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing group interaction.","zh":"討論群體互動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"geographical distribution","meaning":"地理分布","examples":[{"en":"The option refers to the geographical distribution of bees.","zh":"這個選項提到蜜蜂的地理分布。"},{"en":"Geographical distribution means where a species, object, or activity is found across places or regions.","zh":"geographical distribution 指某物種、物件或活動在不同地方或地區中的分布。"},{"en":"A map can show the geographical distribution of different languages in a country.","zh":"地圖可以顯示一個國家不同語言的地理分布。"},{"en":"Knowing the geographical distribution of pollinators helps conservationists protect the right habitats.","zh":"了解授粉者的地理分布，有助保育人士保護合適棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when location patterns are important.","zh":"當地點模式重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 174 - The Ecological Importance of Bees.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"ielts/reading/passage-3/Practice 175":[{"front":"uncover the secret of","meaning":"揭開……的秘密","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have tried to uncover the secret of Stradivarius quality.","zh":"科學家一直嘗試揭開史特拉第瓦里小提琴音質的秘密。"},{"en":"To uncover the secret of something means to discover the hidden reason why it is special, successful, or mysterious.","zh":"uncover the secret of something 指發現某事物特殊、成功或神秘背後的隱藏原因。"},{"en":"A teacher may try to uncover the secret of why one class learns vocabulary faster than another.","zh":"老師可能嘗試揭開為何某班比另一班更快學會詞彙的秘密。"},{"en":"If researchers uncover the secret of an old technique, modern makers may be able to copy it.","zh":"如果研究人員揭開舊技術的秘密，現代製作者可能能夠模仿它。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that the answer is hidden and needs careful investigation.","zh":"這個片語暗示答案是隱藏的，需要仔細調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"long-dead craftsmen","meaning":"已故多年的工匠","examples":[{"en":"The violins were made by long-dead Italian craftsmen.","zh":"這些小提琴由已故多年的意大利工匠製作。"},{"en":"Long-dead craftsmen are skilled makers who died a very long time ago.","zh":"long-dead craftsmen 指已去世很久的熟練製作者。"},{"en":"Museums often display furniture made by long-dead craftsmen whose names are no longer known.","zh":"博物館常展示由已故多年的工匠製作、但姓名已不詳的家具。"},{"en":"If long-dead craftsmen left no clear records, modern researchers must study their objects directly.","zh":"如果已故多年的工匠沒有留下清楚記錄，現代研究人員就必須直接研究其作品。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a sense of historical distance and lost knowledge.","zh":"這個片語帶出歷史距離和失落知識的感覺。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Italian craftsmen","meaning":"意大利工匠","examples":[{"en":"Italian craftsmen in Cremona produced many famous violins.","zh":"克雷莫納的意大利工匠製作了許多著名小提琴。"},{"en":"Italian craftsmen are skilled makers from Italy who create objects by hand or with traditional methods.","zh":"Italian craftsmen 指來自意大利、以手工或傳統方法製作物件的熟練工匠。"},{"en":"Italian craftsmen may be known for furniture, shoes, musical instruments, or decorative objects.","zh":"意大利工匠可能以家具、鞋履、樂器或裝飾物聞名。"},{"en":"If Italian craftsmen develop a strong tradition, later generations may continue to study their methods.","zh":"如果意大利工匠發展出強大傳統，後代可能繼續研究他們的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses nationality and skilled manual work.","zh":"這個片語強調國籍和熟練手工。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the Cremona region","meaning":"克雷莫納地區","examples":[{"en":"Many highly valued violins came from the Cremona region.","zh":"許多價值極高的小提琴來自克雷莫納地區。"},{"en":"The Cremona region refers to the area around Cremona in Italy, famous for historic violin making.","zh":"the Cremona region 指意大利克雷莫納一帶，以歷史悠久的小提琴製作聞名。"},{"en":"A music student may learn that the Cremona region produced instruments now kept in major collections.","zh":"音樂學生可能學到克雷莫納地區製作了如今收藏於重要館藏中的樂器。"},{"en":"If an instrument comes from a famous region, its history may affect how people value it.","zh":"如果樂器來自著名地區，其歷史可能影響人們如何評價它。"},{"en":"The phrase connects place with craftsmanship and reputation.","zh":"這個片語把地方與工藝和聲譽連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"beautiful works of art","meaning":"精美的藝術品","examples":[{"en":"Stradivarius violins are regarded as beautiful works of art.","zh":"史特拉第瓦里小提琴被視為精美的藝術品。"},{"en":"Beautiful works of art are objects or creations admired for their beauty, skill, and artistic value.","zh":"beautiful works of art 指因美感、技巧和藝術價值而受欣賞的物件或創作。"},{"en":"A handmade vase can be a beautiful work of art if its shape and decoration move viewers.","zh":"如果手工花瓶的形狀和裝飾打動觀者，它可以是精美的藝術品。"},{"en":"If a musical instrument is admired visually as well as musically, it may be treated as art.","zh":"如果樂器在視覺和音樂上都受欣賞，它可能被視為藝術品。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests value beyond practical function.","zh":"這個片語暗示價值超越實用功能。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be coveted by","meaning":"受到……渴求","examples":[{"en":"The finest violins are coveted by collectors and players.","zh":"最優質的小提琴受到收藏家和演奏者渴求。"},{"en":"Be coveted by means be strongly desired by a particular group of people.","zh":"be coveted by 指被某一群人強烈渴望擁有。"},{"en":"A rare first edition may be coveted by book collectors.","zh":"罕見的初版書可能受到藏書家渴求。"},{"en":"If an object is rare and famous, it may be coveted even by people who cannot afford it.","zh":"如果物件稀有又著名，即使買不起的人也可能渴求它。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests strong desire, often for something valuable or hard to obtain.","zh":"這個片語暗示強烈渴望，通常用於有價值或難以取得的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"collectors as well as players","meaning":"收藏家及演奏者","examples":[{"en":"The instruments are valued by collectors as well as players.","zh":"這些樂器受到收藏家及演奏者重視。"},{"en":"Collectors as well as players means both people who collect instruments and people who perform with them.","zh":"collectors as well as players 指收藏樂器的人和用樂器演奏的人兩者。"},{"en":"Vintage guitars may interest collectors as well as players because they have both history and sound quality.","zh":"復古結他可能吸引收藏家及演奏者，因為它既有歷史，也有音質。"},{"en":"If both collectors and performers want an instrument, its price may rise sharply.","zh":"如果收藏家和演奏者都想要一件樂器，其價格可能急升。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that two different groups value the same object.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩個不同群體重視同一物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"particularly outstanding","meaning":"特別出色的","examples":[{"en":"Particularly outstanding violins have sold for enormous sums.","zh":"特別出色的小提琴曾以巨額價格售出。"},{"en":"Particularly outstanding means especially excellent compared with others of the same kind.","zh":"particularly outstanding 指在同類之中特別優秀。"},{"en":"A particularly outstanding student essay may combine clear structure, strong examples, and accurate language.","zh":"特別出色的學生文章可能結合清晰結構、有力例子和準確語言。"},{"en":"If an instrument is particularly outstanding, buyers may pay far more than usual.","zh":"如果樂器特別出色，買家可能支付遠高於平常的價格。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights exceptional quality.","zh":"這個片語突出非凡質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"reputedly","meaning":"據說","examples":[{"en":"Some Stradivarius violins have reputedly sold for over a million pounds.","zh":"據說有些史特拉第瓦里小提琴曾以超過一百萬英鎊售出。"},{"en":"Reputedly means according to what people say, though it may not be fully confirmed.","zh":"reputedly 指據人們所說，雖然未必完全證實。"},{"en":"The old restaurant is reputedly the best place in town for handmade noodles.","zh":"據說那間老餐廳是城中吃手工麵最好的地方。"},{"en":"If a violin reputedly sold for a huge sum, the writer is reporting a claim rather than proving it directly.","zh":"如果據說某小提琴以巨額售出，作者是在報告說法，而不是直接證明。"},{"en":"The word is useful when information is widely said but uncertain.","zh":"這個詞適合用於廣泛流傳但不確定的資料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"change hands for","meaning":"以……價格轉手","examples":[{"en":"Rare violins have changed hands for more than a million pounds.","zh":"稀有小提琴曾以超過一百萬英鎊的價格轉手。"},{"en":"Change hands for a price means be sold from one owner to another for that amount of money.","zh":"change hands for a price 指以某金額由一位擁有人售予另一位擁有人。"},{"en":"A small flat in the city may change hands for millions because land is scarce.","zh":"城市中的小單位可能因土地稀少而以數百萬價格轉手。"},{"en":"If an object changes hands for a high price, the market believes it is valuable.","zh":"如果物件以高價轉手，市場相信它有價值。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used for expensive sales.","zh":"這個片語常用於昂貴交易。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"In contrast, most fine modern violins cost much less.","zh":"相比之下，大多數優質現代小提琴便宜得多。"},{"en":"In contrast introduces a clear difference from what was just mentioned.","zh":"in contrast 引出與剛提到內容的清楚差異。"},{"en":"Some luxury watches cost thousands; in contrast, a simple school watch may cost very little.","zh":"有些名貴手錶價值數千元；相比之下，普通學生手錶可能很便宜。"},{"en":"If old violins sell for millions while modern ones cost less, the price gap becomes obvious.","zh":"如果古老小提琴售價數百萬，而現代小提琴便宜得多，價格差距就很明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase helps readers compare two different situations.","zh":"這個片語幫助讀者比較兩種不同情況。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fine modern instruments","meaning":"優質現代樂器","examples":[{"en":"Fine modern instruments typically cost about £10,000.","zh":"優質現代樂器通常約售一萬英鎊。"},{"en":"Fine modern instruments are high-quality musical instruments made in recent times.","zh":"fine modern instruments 指近代製作的高質素樂器。"},{"en":"A music school may buy fine modern instruments because they are reliable and less risky than historic ones.","zh":"音樂學校可能購買優質現代樂器，因為它們可靠，而且比歷史名琴風險較低。"},{"en":"If modern instruments are well made, they can serve serious performers even without famous old labels.","zh":"如果現代樂器製作精良，即使沒有著名古老標籤，也能服務專業演奏者。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts recent high-quality instruments with antique ones.","zh":"這個片語把近代高質素樂器與古董樂器作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"factory-made violins","meaning":"工廠製造的小提琴","examples":[{"en":"Factory-made violins for beginners can be relatively inexpensive.","zh":"初學者用的工廠製造小提琴可以相對便宜。"},{"en":"Factory-made violins are violins produced in larger numbers using standardised industrial methods.","zh":"factory-made violins 指使用標準化工業方法大量生產的小提琴。"},{"en":"A beginner may rent a factory-made violin before buying a handmade one.","zh":"初學者可能先租用工廠製造的小提琴，再購買手工小提琴。"},{"en":"If a violin is factory-made, it may be cheaper but less individually adjusted.","zh":"如果小提琴是工廠製造，可能較便宜，但個別調校較少。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts mass production with hand craftsmanship.","zh":"這個片語把大量生產與手工工藝作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reflect large differences in","meaning":"反映……的巨大差異","examples":[{"en":"Researchers ask whether the prices reflect large differences in quality.","zh":"研究人員詢問這些價格是否反映質素上的巨大差異。"},{"en":"Reflect large differences in means show or represent big differences in something.","zh":"reflect large differences in 指顯示或代表某方面的巨大差異。"},{"en":"House prices may reflect large differences in location, size, and transport access.","zh":"樓價可能反映地點、大小和交通便利度上的巨大差異。"},{"en":"If prices do not reflect real quality differences, reputation may be affecting the market.","zh":"如果價格沒有反映真實質素差異，聲譽可能正在影響市場。"},{"en":"The phrase connects visible results with possible underlying differences.","zh":"這個片語把可見結果與可能的內在差異連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"vigorous debate","meaning":"激烈辯論","examples":[{"en":"The subject has caused vigorous debate for more than a century.","zh":"這個主題在超過一個世紀以來引起激烈辯論。"},{"en":"Vigorous debate is strong, active discussion with firm opinions on different sides.","zh":"vigorous debate 指不同立場帶着堅定意見進行強烈而活躍的討論。"},{"en":"School uniform rules can cause vigorous debate among parents, students, and teachers.","zh":"校服規則可以在家長、學生和老師之間引起激烈辯論。"},{"en":"If evidence is uncertain but people care deeply, debate may become vigorous.","zh":"如果證據不確定，但人們非常關心，辯論可能變得激烈。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests energetic disagreement, not a quiet conversation.","zh":"這個片語暗示有力分歧，而不是安靜談話。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"remain highly contentious","meaning":"仍然極具爭議","examples":[{"en":"The question of violin quality remains highly contentious.","zh":"小提琴質素的問題仍然極具爭議。"},{"en":"Remain highly contentious means continue to cause strong disagreement.","zh":"remain highly contentious 指繼續引起強烈分歧。"},{"en":"Whether exams should be the main measure of ability remains highly contentious in education.","zh":"考試是否應是衡量能力的主要方法，在教育中仍然極具爭議。"},{"en":"If experts disagree for many years, the issue remains contentious rather than settled.","zh":"如果專家多年來意見不一，該議題就是仍具爭議，而非已解決。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that a debate is still unresolved.","zh":"這個片語顯示辯論仍未有定論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"provoke strongly held views","meaning":"引起強烈堅持的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The issue provokes strongly held views among musicians and scientists.","zh":"這個議題在音樂家和科學家之間引起強烈堅持的觀點。"},{"en":"Provoke strongly held views means cause people to express opinions they believe firmly.","zh":"provoke strongly held views 指令人表達自己堅定相信的意見。"},{"en":"Homework policies can provoke strongly held views because families experience them daily.","zh":"功課政策可以引起強烈堅持的觀點，因為家庭每天都經歷它。"},{"en":"If a topic touches money, tradition, and professional pride, it may provoke strong views.","zh":"如果主題涉及金錢、傳統和專業自豪感，就可能引起強烈觀點。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests opinions are not casual or weak.","zh":"這個片語暗示意見不是隨便或薄弱的。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"divergent views","meaning":"分歧的觀點","examples":[{"en":"Violin makers and scientists hold divergent views on the subject.","zh":"小提琴製作者和科學家對這個主題持有分歧觀點。"},{"en":"Divergent views are opinions that differ from one another, often in important ways.","zh":"divergent views 指彼此不同、而且往往在重要方面不同的意見。"},{"en":"Parents and teachers may hold divergent views about how much homework is useful.","zh":"家長和老師可能對多少功課有用持有分歧觀點。"},{"en":"If evidence can be interpreted differently, experts may develop divergent views.","zh":"如果證據可以有不同詮釋，專家可能形成分歧觀點。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on disagreement between perspectives.","zh":"這個片語集中於不同角度之間的分歧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"musicians, violin makers and scientists alike","meaning":"音樂家、小提琴製作者和科學家全都","examples":[{"en":"The debate interests musicians, violin makers and scientists alike.","zh":"這場辯論令音樂家、小提琴製作者和科學家全都感興趣。"},{"en":"Musicians, violin makers and scientists alike means all three groups are interested or involved in the same issue.","zh":"musicians, violin makers and scientists alike 指三個群體全都對同一議題感興趣或參與其中。"},{"en":"A public health problem may concern doctors, teachers and parents alike.","zh":"公共健康問題可能令醫生、老師和家長全都關心。"},{"en":"If a violin debate affects performance, craft and measurement, all three groups naturally care.","zh":"如果小提琴辯論影響演奏、工藝和測量，三個群體自然都關心。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses that several different groups share the same concern.","zh":"這個片語強調幾個不同群體有共同關注。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a distinctive voice of its own","meaning":"自己獨特的聲音","examples":[{"en":"Every violin has a distinctive voice of its own.","zh":"每把小提琴都有自己獨特的聲音。"},{"en":"A distinctive voice of its own means a unique sound or character that makes something recognisable.","zh":"a distinctive voice of its own 指令某物容易被認出的獨特聲音或個性。"},{"en":"A good writer has a distinctive voice of their own when readers can recognise their style.","zh":"如果讀者能認出某作家的風格，那位好作家就有自己獨特的聲音。"},{"en":"If every violin sounds slightly different, performers may choose one that fits their musical personality.","zh":"如果每把小提琴聲音都略有不同，演奏者可能選擇符合自己音樂個性的那一把。"},{"en":"The phrase treats sound as if it were an individual identity.","zh":"這個片語把聲音視為個別身份。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"immediately recognise the difference between","meaning":"立即辨別……之間的分別","examples":[{"en":"A trained listener can immediately recognise the difference between two singers.","zh":"受過訓練的聽眾能立即辨別兩位歌手之間的分別。"},{"en":"Immediately recognise the difference between means notice the distinction at once without needing much time.","zh":"immediately recognise the difference between 指不用很多時間就立刻注意到差異。"},{"en":"A teacher can immediately recognise the difference between careful homework and rushed homework.","zh":"老師能立即辨別認真功課和趕工功課之間的分別。"},{"en":"If someone has trained hearing, small changes in sound may be obvious to them.","zh":"如果某人聽力受過訓練，細微聲音變化對他們可能很明顯。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests quick and confident recognition.","zh":"這個片語暗示快速而有信心的辨認。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"operatic aria","meaning":"歌劇詠唱調","examples":[{"en":"Two singers may perform the same operatic aria very differently.","zh":"兩位歌手可能以非常不同方式演唱同一首歌劇詠唱調。"},{"en":"An operatic aria is a solo song in an opera, usually sung with strong emotion and technique.","zh":"operatic aria 指歌劇中的獨唱歌曲，通常帶強烈情感和技巧。"},{"en":"A music student may study an operatic aria to practise breath control and expression.","zh":"音樂學生可能練習歌劇詠唱調，以訓練呼吸控制和表達。"},{"en":"If two singers perform the same aria, listeners can compare tone, power and interpretation.","zh":"如果兩位歌手演唱同一詠唱調，聽眾可以比較音色、力量和詮釋。"},{"en":"The phrase belongs to classical vocal music.","zh":"這個片語屬於古典聲樂。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"skilled violinist","meaning":"技巧純熟的小提琴手","examples":[{"en":"A skilled violinist can distinguish subtle differences in sound.","zh":"技巧純熟的小提琴手能分辨聲音中的細微差異。"},{"en":"A skilled violinist is a violin player with strong technique, training, and musical judgement.","zh":"skilled violinist 指具有高超技巧、訓練和音樂判斷力的小提琴演奏者。"},{"en":"A skilled violinist may notice when a string is slightly out of tune.","zh":"技巧純熟的小提琴手可能注意到琴弦有一點點走音。"},{"en":"If a violinist is highly skilled, they can adjust pressure, speed and angle while playing.","zh":"如果小提琴手技巧很高，演奏時就能調整力度、速度和角度。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights expertise in performance.","zh":"這個片語突出演奏專業。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"distinguish between","meaning":"區分……","examples":[{"en":"A violinist can distinguish between different qualities of tone.","zh":"小提琴手能區分不同音色質素。"},{"en":"Distinguish between means recognise the difference between two or more things.","zh":"distinguish between 指辨認兩個或更多事物之間的差異。"},{"en":"Students must distinguish between fact and opinion when reading news articles.","zh":"學生閱讀新聞文章時，必須區分事實和意見。"},{"en":"If two sounds are very similar, it takes training to distinguish between them.","zh":"如果兩種聲音非常相似，就需要訓練才能區分它們。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on careful comparison.","zh":"這個片語集中於仔細比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sound produced by","meaning":"由……產生的聲音","examples":[{"en":"Experts compare the sound produced by different violins.","zh":"專家比較由不同小提琴產生的聲音。"},{"en":"Sound produced by means the sound created or generated by a particular instrument, person, or object.","zh":"sound produced by 指由某件樂器、某人或某物創造或發出的聲音。"},{"en":"A science teacher may compare the sound produced by metal, wood, and glass.","zh":"科學老師可能比較由金屬、木材和玻璃產生的聲音。"},{"en":"If the same player uses two violins, differences in sound may come from the instruments themselves.","zh":"如果同一演奏者使用兩把小提琴，聲音差異可能來自樂器本身。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a sound with its source.","zh":"這個片語把聲音與其來源連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"individual notes","meaning":"個別音符","examples":[{"en":"Individual notes may sound slightly different each time they are played.","zh":"個別音符每次演奏時可能聽起來略有不同。"},{"en":"Individual notes are single musical sounds rather than whole phrases or melodies.","zh":"individual notes 指單一音樂聲音，而不是整句樂句或旋律。"},{"en":"A piano teacher may ask students to practise individual notes before playing the full song.","zh":"鋼琴老師可能要求學生先練習個別音符，再彈整首歌。"},{"en":"If individual notes vary, the listener’s impression of the whole instrument may also change.","zh":"如果個別音符有所變化，聽眾對整件樂器的印象也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on one sound at a time.","zh":"這個片語集中於一次一個聲音。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"perceived tone","meaning":"感知音色","examples":[{"en":"The perceived tone depends on the overall design of the violin.","zh":"感知音色取決於小提琴的整體設計。"},{"en":"Perceived tone means the quality of sound as heard and judged by the listener.","zh":"perceived tone 指由聽眾聽到並判斷的聲音質素。"},{"en":"A singer’s perceived tone may change depending on the room, microphone and listener position.","zh":"歌手的感知音色可能因房間、咪高峰和聽眾位置而改變。"},{"en":"If two listeners perceive tone differently, measurement alone may not settle the debate.","zh":"如果兩位聽眾對音色感知不同，單靠測量未必能解決爭論。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses human hearing and judgement.","zh":"這個片語強調人類聽覺和判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be related to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"A violin’s tone may be related to its overall construction.","zh":"小提琴的音色可能與其整體構造有關。"},{"en":"Be related to means have a connection with something.","zh":"be related to 指與某事有連繫。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be related to lack of sleep rather than laziness.","zh":"學生疲倦可能與睡眠不足有關，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"If sound quality is related to construction, changing the design may change the tone.","zh":"如果音質與構造有關，改變設計可能改變音色。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests connection, not always direct proof.","zh":"這個片語暗示連繫，不一定是直接證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"overall design","meaning":"整體設計","examples":[{"en":"The overall design of the instrument influences its sound.","zh":"樂器的整體設計影響其聲音。"},{"en":"Overall design means the complete arrangement of all parts, not just one small feature.","zh":"overall design 指所有部分的完整安排，而不只是單一小特徵。"},{"en":"The overall design of a classroom affects how easily students can see, hear, and move.","zh":"課室的整體設計影響學生有多容易看見、聽見和移動。"},{"en":"If a violin’s overall design changes, many sound qualities may change together.","zh":"如果小提琴的整體設計改變，許多聲音特質可能一起改變。"},{"en":"The phrase encourages looking at the whole system.","zh":"這個片語鼓勵看整個系統。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"The perceived tone may depend on overall design rather than individual resonances.","zh":"感知音色可能取決於整體設計，而不是個別共振。"},{"en":"Rather than shows contrast and means not the second thing, but the first thing instead.","zh":"rather than 表示對比，意思是不是第二件事，而是第一件事。"},{"en":"A student may need better sleep rather than more coffee before an exam.","zh":"學生考試前可能需要更好睡眠，而不是更多咖啡。"},{"en":"If tone depends on design rather than one measurement, scientists must study the whole instrument.","zh":"如果音色取決於設計而不是一項測量，科學家就必須研究整件樂器。"},{"en":"The phrase helps separate the real explanation from a less likely one.","zh":"這個片語幫助把真正解釋與較不可能的解釋分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"particular resonances","meaning":"特定共振","examples":[{"en":"Particular resonances do not fully explain the instrument’s tone.","zh":"特定共振不能完全解釋該樂器的音色。"},{"en":"Particular resonances are specific frequencies at which an object naturally vibrates strongly.","zh":"particular resonances 指物件自然強烈震動的特定頻率。"},{"en":"A glass may have a particular resonance that makes it ring when tapped.","zh":"玻璃杯可能有一個特定共振，被敲擊時會響起來。"},{"en":"If only a few resonances are measured, they may not capture the whole sound character.","zh":"如果只量度少數共振，可能無法捕捉整體聲音性格。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to specific vibration behaviours.","zh":"這個片語指特定震動行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"various attempts have been made to","meaning":"人們曾多次嘗試……","examples":[{"en":"Various attempts have been made to analyse the sound of fine violins.","zh":"人們曾多次嘗試分析優質小提琴的聲音。"},{"en":"Various attempts have been made to means people have tried several different ways to do something.","zh":"various attempts have been made to 指人們以幾種不同方式嘗試做某事。"},{"en":"Various attempts have been made to reduce homework stress, including shorter tasks and clearer deadlines.","zh":"人們曾多次嘗試減少功課壓力，包括縮短任務和更清楚截止日期。"},{"en":"If a problem is difficult, researchers may make many attempts before finding a reliable method.","zh":"如果問題困難，研究人員可能需要多次嘗試才找到可靠方法。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests repeated effort from different angles.","zh":"這個片語暗示從不同角度反覆努力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"analyse global properties","meaning":"分析整體特性","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have tried to analyse the global properties of violin sound.","zh":"研究人員曾嘗試分析小提琴聲音的整體特性。"},{"en":"Analyse global properties means study the overall characteristics of a system rather than isolated details.","zh":"analyse global properties 指研究一個系統的整體特徵，而不是孤立細節。"},{"en":"Doctors may analyse global patterns in sleep, diet and mood rather than one symptom alone.","zh":"醫生可能分析睡眠、飲食和心情的整體模式，而不是單一症狀。"},{"en":"If violin sound depends on many interacting parts, global analysis may be more useful.","zh":"如果小提琴聲音取決於許多互動部分，整體分析可能更有用。"},{"en":"The phrase encourages whole-system investigation.","zh":"這個片語鼓勵整體系統調查。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"global properties","meaning":"整體特性","examples":[{"en":"Global properties may be more important than individual frequencies.","zh":"整體特性可能比個別頻率更重要。"},{"en":"Global properties are the overall features of a whole object or system.","zh":"global properties 指整個物件或系統的整體特徵。"},{"en":"A school’s global properties include atmosphere, teaching style, rules and relationships.","zh":"學校的整體特性包括氣氛、教學風格、規則和關係。"},{"en":"If global properties matter most, one small measurement cannot explain the whole result.","zh":"如果整體特性最重要，一項小測量不能解釋整體結果。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts the whole with separate parts.","zh":"這個片語把整體與分開部分作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"extremely difficult to distinguish","meaning":"極難分辨","examples":[{"en":"It is extremely difficult to distinguish a Stradivarius from a modern copy by measurements alone.","zh":"單靠測量極難分辨史特拉第瓦里小提琴和現代仿製品。"},{"en":"Extremely difficult to distinguish means very hard to tell two things apart.","zh":"extremely difficult to distinguish 指非常難把兩件事物分辨開來。"},{"en":"It can be extremely difficult to distinguish two identical-looking phone models without checking their settings.","zh":"如果不檢查設定，兩款外觀相同的手機型號可能極難分辨。"},{"en":"If differences are subtle, even careful measurements may not separate the objects clearly.","zh":"如果差異細微，即使仔細測量也未必能清楚區分物件。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses serious difficulty in identification.","zh":"這個片語強調辨認上的嚴重困難。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fine Stradivarius instrument","meaning":"優質的史特拉第瓦里小提琴","examples":[{"en":"A fine Stradivarius instrument may be difficult to identify scientifically.","zh":"優質的史特拉第瓦里小提琴可能難以用科學方法識別。"},{"en":"A fine Stradivarius instrument is a high-quality violin or related instrument made by Stradivarius.","zh":"fine Stradivarius instrument 指由 Stradivarius 製作的高質素小提琴或相關樂器。"},{"en":"A museum may protect a fine Stradivarius instrument with strict temperature and security controls.","zh":"博物館可能用嚴格溫度和保安控制保護優質的史特拉第瓦里樂器。"},{"en":"If an instrument is historically famous, people may expect science to find clear proof of its quality.","zh":"如果樂器有著名歷史，人們可能期待科學找到其質素的清楚證據。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a prized historic instrument.","zh":"這個片語指珍貴的歷史樂器。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"indifferent modern copy","meaning":"平庸的現代仿製品","examples":[{"en":"Some listeners cannot distinguish a fine violin from an indifferent modern copy.","zh":"有些聽眾不能把優質小提琴和平庸的現代仿製品分辨出來。"},{"en":"An indifferent modern copy is a modern imitation that is ordinary or not especially good.","zh":"indifferent modern copy 指現代製作、但普通或不特別出色的仿製品。"},{"en":"A cheap copy of a designer bag may look acceptable from far away but feel indifferent up close.","zh":"平價仿製名牌袋遠看可能可以接受，但近看感覺平庸。"},{"en":"If listeners cannot tell a great violin from an ordinary copy, judging quality becomes complicated.","zh":"如果聽眾不能分辨名琴和平庸仿製品，判斷質素就變得複雜。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts famous excellence with ordinary imitation.","zh":"這個片語把著名卓越與普通仿製作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on the basis of","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists cannot judge quality on the basis of measured response alone.","zh":"科學家不能單靠量度所得的反應來判斷質素。"},{"en":"On the basis of means using something as the reason, evidence, or foundation for a judgement.","zh":"on the basis of 指以某事作為判斷的原因、證據或基礎。"},{"en":"A teacher should not judge a student’s ability on the basis of one bad quiz.","zh":"老師不應根據一次差劣小測來判斷學生能力。"},{"en":"If a decision is based on limited evidence, the conclusion may be unreliable.","zh":"如果決定基於有限證據，結論可能不可靠。"},{"en":"The phrase explains what a judgement depends on.","zh":"這個片語解釋判斷取決於甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"measured response alone","meaning":"單靠量度所得的反應","examples":[{"en":"The measured response alone may not reveal the quality of a violin.","zh":"單靠量度所得的反應可能無法揭示小提琴的質素。"},{"en":"Measured response alone means only the data recorded by instruments, without human listening or wider context.","zh":"measured response alone 指只有儀器記錄的數據，而沒有人的聆聽或更廣背景。"},{"en":"A fitness watch’s measured response alone may not show how tired a person feels.","zh":"健身手錶單靠量度所得的反應，未必顯示一個人有多疲倦。"},{"en":"If sound quality includes human judgement, measurements alone may miss important qualities.","zh":"如果音質包含人的判斷，單靠測量可能錯過重要特質。"},{"en":"The phrase warns against relying only on numbers.","zh":"這個片語提醒人不要只依賴數字。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"supreme detection device","meaning":"極出色的探測工具","examples":[{"en":"The human ear is a supreme detection device.","zh":"人耳是一種極出色的探測工具。"},{"en":"A supreme detection device is an extremely effective tool for noticing small differences.","zh":"supreme detection device 指極有效察覺細微差異的工具。"},{"en":"A trained teacher’s eye can be a supreme detection device for spotting small writing mistakes.","zh":"受訓老師的眼睛可以是極出色的探測工具，用來發現小寫作錯誤。"},{"en":"If the ear detects subtle sound differences better than machines, human judgement remains important.","zh":"如果耳朵比機器更能察覺細微聲音差異，人類判斷仍然重要。"},{"en":"The phrase praises exceptional sensitivity.","zh":"這個片語讚賞非凡敏感度。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have yet to be developed","meaning":"尚未研發出來","examples":[{"en":"A system matching the human brain has yet to be developed.","zh":"能比得上人腦的系統尚未研發出來。"},{"en":"Have yet to be developed means has not been created or perfected so far.","zh":"have yet to be developed 指到目前為止尚未被創造或完善。"},{"en":"A simple cure for every type of cancer has yet to be developed.","zh":"能治療所有癌症的簡單療法尚未研發出來。"},{"en":"If a tool has yet to be developed, researchers still need better methods and evidence.","zh":"如果工具尚未研發出來，研究人員仍需要更好方法和證據。"},{"en":"The phrase points to something that remains unfinished.","zh":"這個片語指出某事仍未完成。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"match the brain’s ability to","meaning":"比得上大腦……的能力","examples":[{"en":"Machines cannot yet match the brain’s ability to assess complex sounds.","zh":"機器尚未能比得上大腦評估複雜聲音的能力。"},{"en":"Match the brain’s ability to means equal the brain’s skill in doing something.","zh":"match the brain’s ability to 指與大腦做某事的能力相等。"},{"en":"Translation software may not fully match the brain’s ability to understand humour and context.","zh":"翻譯軟件未必完全比得上大腦理解幽默和語境的能力。"},{"en":"If machines cannot match human listening, expert musicians remain important in testing violins.","zh":"如果機器不能比得上人類聆聽，專家音樂家在測試小提琴時仍然重要。"},{"en":"The phrase compares machine performance with human mental skill.","zh":"這個片語比較機器表現與人類心智能力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sophisticated ability","meaning":"精密複雜的能力","examples":[{"en":"The brain has a sophisticated ability to interpret sound.","zh":"大腦有精密複雜的能力去詮釋聲音。"},{"en":"Sophisticated ability means a highly developed and complex skill.","zh":"sophisticated ability 指高度發展且複雜的技能。"},{"en":"Experienced doctors have a sophisticated ability to notice patterns in symptoms.","zh":"經驗豐富的醫生有精密複雜的能力去注意症狀模式。"},{"en":"If a task requires many subtle judgements, a sophisticated ability is needed.","zh":"如果任務需要許多細微判斷，就需要精密複雜的能力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes advanced skill, not simple talent.","zh":"這個片語描述高階技能，而不是簡單天賦。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"assess complex sounds","meaning":"評估複雜聲音","examples":[{"en":"The human brain can assess complex sounds with great sensitivity.","zh":"人腦能以高度敏感度評估複雜聲音。"},{"en":"Assess complex sounds means judge detailed sound qualities involving many tones, layers, or changes.","zh":"assess complex sounds 指判斷包含許多音調、層次或變化的細緻聲音質素。"},{"en":"A sound engineer must assess complex sounds when mixing music for a concert.","zh":"音響工程師為演唱會混音時，必須評估複雜聲音。"},{"en":"If a violin produces many interacting vibrations, the listener must assess complex sound patterns.","zh":"如果小提琴產生許多互相作用的震動，聽眾就必須評估複雜聲音模式。"},{"en":"The phrase is about careful judgement of complicated audio information.","zh":"這個片語關於對複雜聲音資訊作仔細判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"skilled violin makers","meaning":"技巧純熟的小提琴製作者","examples":[{"en":"Skilled violin makers adjust an instrument during construction.","zh":"技巧純熟的小提琴製作者會在製作期間調整樂器。"},{"en":"Skilled violin makers are craftspeople with the training to build, shape and refine violins.","zh":"skilled violin makers 指受過訓練、能建造、塑形和精修小提琴的工匠。"},{"en":"A skilled violin maker may listen, carve, adjust and test many times before finishing an instrument.","zh":"技巧純熟的小提琴製作者可能在完成樂器前反覆聆聽、雕製、調整和測試。"},{"en":"If the maker is skilled, small changes in wood or shape can be used to improve tone.","zh":"如果製作者技巧純熟，木材或形狀上的微小改變可以用來改善音色。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights expert craftsmanship.","zh":"這個片語突出專家工藝。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"optimise the tone","meaning":"優化音色","examples":[{"en":"Makers use several techniques to optimise the tone of a violin.","zh":"製作者使用幾種技術來優化小提琴的音色。"},{"en":"Optimise the tone means adjust something so its sound quality becomes as good as possible.","zh":"optimise the tone 指調整某物，使其聲音質素盡可能變好。"},{"en":"A singer may optimise their tone by controlling breathing and mouth shape.","zh":"歌手可能透過控制呼吸和口形來優化音色。"},{"en":"If a maker changes thickness carefully, they may improve how the violin vibrates.","zh":"如果製作者仔細改變厚度，就可能改善小提琴的震動方式。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests careful improvement toward the best result.","zh":"這個片語暗示朝最佳結果作細心改進。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"construction process","meaning":"製作過程","examples":[{"en":"The tone is adjusted throughout the construction process.","zh":"音色在整個製作過程中被調整。"},{"en":"Construction process means the series of steps involved in building or making something.","zh":"construction process 指建造或製作某物所涉及的一連串步驟。"},{"en":"During a school model-building project, students check the construction process from planning to finishing.","zh":"在學校模型製作項目中，學生檢查從計劃到完成的製作過程。"},{"en":"If tone is adjusted during construction, the final sound depends on many small decisions.","zh":"如果音色在製作期間調整，最終聲音就取決於許多小決定。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on making, not only the finished product.","zh":"這個片語集中於製作，而不只是成品。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"select wood of the highest possible quality","meaning":"選用最高品質的木材","examples":[{"en":"Violin makers select wood of the highest possible quality.","zh":"小提琴製作者選用最高品質的木材。"},{"en":"Select wood of the highest possible quality means choose the best available wood for the task.","zh":"select wood of the highest possible quality 指為工作選擇可取得的最佳木材。"},{"en":"A carpenter building a fine table may select wood of the highest possible quality to avoid cracks.","zh":"木匠製作優質桌子時，可能選用最高品質的木材以避免裂紋。"},{"en":"If the wood is poor, even skilled work may not produce a rich sound.","zh":"如果木材差，即使工藝高超也未必能產生豐富聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase shows careful material choice before making begins.","zh":"這個片語顯示製作開始前對材料的仔細選擇。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"front and back plates","meaning":"前後面板","examples":[{"en":"The front and back plates affect the instrument’s sound.","zh":"前後面板影響樂器的聲音。"},{"en":"Front and back plates are the wooden panels on the front and back of a violin’s body.","zh":"front and back plates 指小提琴琴身前方和後方的木製面板。"},{"en":"A repairer may inspect the front and back plates for cracks before adjusting a violin.","zh":"修理師在調整小提琴前，可能檢查前後面板有沒有裂紋。"},{"en":"If these plates vibrate differently, the sound of the instrument can change.","zh":"如果這些面板震動方式不同，樂器聲音可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase names important structural parts of a violin.","zh":"這個片語指出小提琴的重要結構部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"test by tapping","meaning":"透過敲擊測試","examples":[{"en":"Makers test the wood by tapping it with a hammer.","zh":"製作者用鎚敲擊木材來測試它。"},{"en":"Test by tapping means check a material’s sound or quality by striking it lightly.","zh":"test by tapping 指輕敲材料，透過聲音檢查其質素。"},{"en":"A shopper may test a watermelon by tapping it and listening to the sound.","zh":"購物者可能透過敲擊西瓜並聽聲音來測試它。"},{"en":"If wood rings clearly when tapped, a maker may judge it suitable for an instrument.","zh":"如果木材被敲擊時清脆作響，製作者可能判斷它適合做樂器。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a simple practical test using sound.","zh":"這個片語描述使用聲音的簡單實用測試。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"judge how well it rings","meaning":"判斷其共鳴效果","examples":[{"en":"They judge the wood by how well it rings.","zh":"他們根據木材共鳴效果來判斷它。"},{"en":"Judge how well it rings means assess the wood by listening to how clearly and strongly it vibrates after being tapped.","zh":"judge how well it rings 指透過聆聽木材被敲後震動得多清晰和強烈來評估它。"},{"en":"A music teacher may judge a bell by how well it rings after a gentle strike.","zh":"音樂老師可能輕敲鐘後，根據其共鳴效果來判斷它。"},{"en":"If wood rings well, it may vibrate freely and produce a lively tone.","zh":"如果木材共鳴良好，它可能能自由震動並產生活潑音色。"},{"en":"The phrase connects listening with material quality.","zh":"這個片語把聆聽與材料質素連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"skilfully carve","meaning":"熟練地雕製","examples":[{"en":"The makers skilfully carve the plates from solid wood.","zh":"製作者熟練地從實木雕製面板。"},{"en":"Skilfully carve means cut and shape material with careful control and high ability.","zh":"skilfully carve 指以仔細控制和高超能力切割並塑造材料。"},{"en":"A chef may skilfully carve fruit into flowers for a banquet display.","zh":"廚師可能熟練地把水果雕成花，用於宴會展示。"},{"en":"If violin plates are carved skilfully, their shape and thickness can support better sound.","zh":"如果小提琴面板被熟練地雕製，其形狀和厚度可以支持更好聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights controlled hand skill.","zh":"這個片語突出受控的手工技巧。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"carve something out of","meaning":"從……雕製某物","examples":[{"en":"The plates are carved out of carefully selected wood.","zh":"面板是從精心選擇的木材雕製而成。"},{"en":"Carve something out of means create a shaped object by cutting material away from a larger piece.","zh":"carve something out of 指從較大材料中切去部分，製成有形物件。"},{"en":"A child may carve a small boat out of soft wood during a craft lesson.","zh":"孩子可能在手工課中從軟木雕出一艘小船。"},{"en":"If a maker carves plates out of solid wood, mistakes may be difficult to undo.","zh":"如果製作者從實木雕製面板，錯誤可能很難補救。"},{"en":"The phrase describes shaping by removing material.","zh":"這個片語描述透過移除材料來塑形。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"solid wood","meaning":"實木","examples":[{"en":"The violin plates are carved from solid wood.","zh":"小提琴面板由實木雕製而成。"},{"en":"Solid wood is real wood cut from a tree, not thin layers or artificial board.","zh":"solid wood 指從樹木切出的真木材，而不是薄木層或人造板。"},{"en":"A solid wood desk is usually heavier and more durable than a cheap fibreboard desk.","zh":"實木書桌通常比便宜纖維板書桌更重、更耐用。"},{"en":"If a violin is made from solid wood, the natural grain and vibration of the wood matter.","zh":"如果小提琴由實木製成，木材的天然紋理和震動就很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses real, whole wood material.","zh":"這個片語強調真實、完整的木材材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take great care to","meaning":"非常小心地去……","examples":[{"en":"Makers take great care to achieve the correct shape.","zh":"製作者非常小心地去達到正確形狀。"},{"en":"Take great care to means do something very carefully to avoid mistakes.","zh":"take great care to 指非常小心地做某事，以避免錯誤。"},{"en":"A nurse takes great care to give the correct medicine to the correct patient.","zh":"護士非常小心地把正確藥物給正確病人。"},{"en":"If makers take great care with shape, they reduce the risk of poor sound.","zh":"如果製作者非常小心處理形狀，就能降低聲音欠佳的風險。"},{"en":"The phrase shows careful attention and responsibility.","zh":"這個片語顯示細心和責任感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the right degree of","meaning":"適當程度的……","examples":[{"en":"The plates need the right degree of arching.","zh":"面板需要適當程度的弧度。"},{"en":"The right degree of something means the suitable amount or level of it.","zh":"the right degree of something 指某事物合適的數量或水平。"},{"en":"A good essay needs the right degree of detail, not too little and not too much.","zh":"好文章需要適當程度的細節，不能太少，也不能太多。"},{"en":"If the arching is too high or too flat, the violin’s sound may be affected.","zh":"如果弧度太高或太平，小提琴聲音可能受影響。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses balance and precision.","zh":"這個片語強調平衡和精準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"arching","meaning":"弧度","examples":[{"en":"The arching of the plates affects the violin’s tone.","zh":"面板的弧度影響小提琴音色。"},{"en":"Arching means the curved shape of a surface, especially when it rises like an arch.","zh":"arching 指表面的彎曲形狀，尤其像拱形般隆起。"},{"en":"The arching of a bridge helps spread weight safely to both sides.","zh":"橋的弧度有助把重量安全分散到兩邊。"},{"en":"If a violin plate has different arching, it may vibrate differently.","zh":"如果小提琴面板有不同弧度，它可能以不同方式震動。"},{"en":"The word describes shape that can affect structure and sound.","zh":"這個詞描述能影響結構和聲音的形狀。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"variations in thickness","meaning":"厚度差異","examples":[{"en":"Small variations in thickness influence the instrument’s response.","zh":"細小的厚度差異會影響樂器的反應。"},{"en":"Variations in thickness are differences in how thick or thin parts of a material are.","zh":"variations in thickness 指材料各部分厚薄上的差異。"},{"en":"A phone case with variations in thickness may protect corners better than the centre.","zh":"有厚度差異的手機殼，可能比中心更能保護角位。"},{"en":"If wood is thicker in one area, it may vibrate differently from a thinner area.","zh":"如果木材某處較厚，它的震動方式可能不同於較薄位置。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights small physical differences.","zh":"這個片語突出細小的物理差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"optimise the thickness","meaning":"調整至最佳厚度","examples":[{"en":"Traditional makers optimise the thickness by testing the plates.","zh":"傳統製作者透過測試面板，把厚度調整至最佳。"},{"en":"Optimise the thickness means adjust thickness until it works as well as possible.","zh":"optimise the thickness 指調整厚度，直到其效果盡可能好。"},{"en":"A designer may optimise the thickness of a laptop so it is light but not fragile.","zh":"設計師可能把手提電腦厚度調整至最佳，使其輕巧但不脆弱。"},{"en":"If violin plates are too thick or too thin, sound quality may suffer.","zh":"如果小提琴面板太厚或太薄，音質可能受損。"},{"en":"The phrase shows careful adjustment toward the best balance.","zh":"這個片語顯示朝最佳平衡作仔細調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"test the feel of","meaning":"測試……的手感","examples":[{"en":"Makers test the feel of the plates when they are flexed.","zh":"製作者在面板被彎曲時測試其手感。"},{"en":"Test the feel of means judge something by touching, bending, holding, or handling it.","zh":"test the feel of 指透過觸摸、彎曲、握持或操作來判斷某物。"},{"en":"A shopper may test the feel of a jacket before deciding whether the cloth is comfortable.","zh":"購物者可能先測試外套的手感，再決定布料是否舒服。"},{"en":"If violin makers test the feel of wood, their hands help judge stiffness and response.","zh":"如果小提琴製作者測試木材手感，他們的雙手有助判斷硬度和反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes practical judgement through touch.","zh":"這個片語描述透過觸感作實用判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be flexed","meaning":"被彎曲","examples":[{"en":"The plates are flexed to test their stiffness.","zh":"面板被彎曲以測試其硬度。"},{"en":"Be flexed means be bent slightly to see how flexible or stiff something is.","zh":"be flexed 指被稍微彎曲，以查看某物有多柔韌或堅硬。"},{"en":"A shoe sole may be flexed in a shop to check whether it is comfortable for walking.","zh":"鞋底可能在店中被彎曲，以檢查走路是否舒服。"},{"en":"If a wooden plate is flexed, the maker can feel how resistant it is to bending.","zh":"如果木板被彎曲，製作者就能感受到它抗彎程度。"},{"en":"The phrase describes controlled bending for testing.","zh":"這個片語描述為測試而進行的受控彎曲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tap at different positions","meaning":"敲擊不同位置","examples":[{"en":"The makers tap the plates at different positions.","zh":"製作者敲擊面板的不同位置。"},{"en":"Tap at different positions means strike various places lightly to compare their sound or response.","zh":"tap at different positions 指輕敲不同地方，以比較其聲音或反應。"},{"en":"A mechanic may tap at different positions on a wall to find a hollow space.","zh":"技工可能敲擊牆上不同位置，以尋找空心位置。"},{"en":"If each position sounds different, the maker can learn where the wood is too thick or too thin.","zh":"如果每個位置聲音不同，製作者就能知道木材哪裡太厚或太薄。"},{"en":"The phrase describes testing several points, not just one.","zh":"這個片語描述測試多個位置，而不只是單一位置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"with the knuckles","meaning":"用指關節","examples":[{"en":"Traditional makers tap the wood with their knuckles.","zh":"傳統製作者用指關節敲擊木材。"},{"en":"With the knuckles means using the finger joints to tap or knock on something.","zh":"with the knuckles 指用手指關節敲打某物。"},{"en":"A visitor may knock on a door with the knuckles instead of using a bell.","zh":"訪客可能用指關節敲門，而不是按門鐘。"},{"en":"If makers tap wood with their knuckles, they can hear and feel its response directly.","zh":"如果製作者用指關節敲木材，就能直接聽到並感受其反應。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a simple hand-based testing method.","zh":"這個片語描述簡單的手工測試方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"emerge","meaning":"出現；興起","examples":[{"en":"A group of scientifically minded violin makers has emerged.","zh":"一群具有科學思維的小提琴製作者已經興起。"},{"en":"Emerge means appear, develop, or become known.","zh":"emerge 指出現、發展或變得為人所知。"},{"en":"A new group of student leaders may emerge after a school event.","zh":"學校活動後，可能出現一群新的學生領袖。"},{"en":"If new technology becomes useful, new methods and new experts may emerge.","zh":"如果新科技變得有用，新的方法和專家可能興起。"},{"en":"The word suggests something becoming visible or important over time.","zh":"這個詞暗示某事物隨時間變得可見或重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"overtly scientific approach","meaning":"明確採用科學的方式","examples":[{"en":"Some makers take a more overtly scientific approach.","zh":"有些製作者採用更明確的科學方式。"},{"en":"An overtly scientific approach is a clearly science-based method using measurement, testing, and evidence.","zh":"overtly scientific approach 指清楚以科學為基礎、使用量度、測試和證據的方法。"},{"en":"A school may take an overtly scientific approach to improving sleep by collecting data on student routines.","zh":"學校可能透過收集學生作息數據，明確採用科學方式改善睡眠。"},{"en":"If violin makers use controlled tests, their work becomes more openly scientific.","zh":"如果小提琴製作者使用受控測試，其工作就變得更公開科學化。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts visible scientific method with informal tradition.","zh":"這個片語把可見的科學方法與非正式傳統作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"violin making","meaning":"小提琴製作","examples":[{"en":"Scientific measurements are increasingly used in violin making.","zh":"科學測量越來越多地用於小提琴製作。"},{"en":"Violin making is the craft of designing, carving, assembling, and adjusting violins.","zh":"violin making 指設計、雕製、組裝和調整小提琴的工藝。"},{"en":"A student interested in violin making must learn woodwork, acoustics, varnishing, and patience.","zh":"對小提琴製作感興趣的學生必須學習木工、聲學、上漆和耐性。"},{"en":"If violin making combines tradition and science, makers may improve both craft and consistency.","zh":"如果小提琴製作結合傳統和科學，製作者可能改善工藝和一致性。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the whole process of creating violins.","zh":"這個片語指創造小提琴的整個過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"common practice","meaning":"常見做法","examples":[{"en":"Controlled measurement has become a common practice among some makers.","zh":"受控量度已成為一些製作者之間的常見做法。"},{"en":"Common practice means something that people in a group often do.","zh":"common practice 指某群體中人們經常做的事。"},{"en":"It is common practice for teachers to check attendance at the beginning of class.","zh":"老師在課堂開始時點名是常見做法。"},{"en":"If a method becomes common practice, it is no longer unusual or experimental.","zh":"如果某方法成為常見做法，它就不再罕見或實驗性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a widely used habit or procedure.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛使用的習慣或程序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"adopt a practice","meaning":"採用一種做法","examples":[{"en":"Some makers have adopted controlled testing methods.","zh":"有些製作者已採用受控測試方法。"},{"en":"Adopt a practice means start using a method regularly.","zh":"adopt a practice 指開始定期使用某種方法。"},{"en":"A school may adopt a practice of giving short quizzes every Friday.","zh":"學校可能採用每星期五小測的做法。"},{"en":"If makers adopt scientific testing, their workshop routines may change.","zh":"如果製作者採用科學測試，其工作室常規可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a method becoming part of normal work.","zh":"這個片語顯示某方法成為正常工作的一部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"replace something by","meaning":"以……取代……","examples":[{"en":"They replace traditional tapping by controlled measurements.","zh":"他們以受控量度取代傳統敲擊。"},{"en":"Replace something by means stop using one method and use another instead.","zh":"replace something by 指停止使用一種方法，改用另一種。"},{"en":"A school may replace paper notices by email to save time and printing costs.","zh":"學校可能以電郵取代紙本通告，以節省時間和印刷成本。"},{"en":"If makers replace tapping with measurements, judgement becomes more data-based.","zh":"如果製作者以測量取代敲擊，判斷就變得更以數據為本。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly shows substitution.","zh":"這個片語清楚顯示替代。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"controlled measurements","meaning":"受控量度","examples":[{"en":"Controlled measurements are used during the carving process.","zh":"受控量度用於雕製過程中。"},{"en":"Controlled measurements are carefully planned measurements taken under set conditions.","zh":"controlled measurements 指在既定條件下仔細規劃和取得的測量。"},{"en":"A doctor uses controlled measurements of blood pressure by asking the patient to sit still first.","zh":"醫生會先要求病人坐定，再進行受控血壓量度。"},{"en":"If measurements are controlled, results are more reliable and easier to compare.","zh":"如果測量受控，結果就更可靠，也更容易比較。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts systematic testing with rough guessing.","zh":"這個片語把系統測試與粗略猜測作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"carving process","meaning":"雕製過程","examples":[{"en":"The plates are tested repeatedly during the carving process.","zh":"面板在雕製過程中被反覆測試。"},{"en":"The carving process is the series of steps in cutting and shaping material into the desired form.","zh":"carving process 指把材料切削和塑造成所需形狀的一連串步驟。"},{"en":"During the carving process, a sculptor may stop often to check the shape from different angles.","zh":"在雕製過程中，雕塑家可能經常停下來從不同角度檢查形狀。"},{"en":"If violin plates are tested while being carved, makers can adjust them before finishing.","zh":"如果小提琴面板在雕製時被測試，製作者就能在完成前調整它們。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on work while the object is still being shaped.","zh":"這個片語集中於物件仍在塑形時的工作。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"thinned plates","meaning":"削薄了的面板","examples":[{"en":"The thinned plates are tested for their resonant behaviour.","zh":"削薄了的面板會被測試其共振行為。"},{"en":"Thinned plates are wooden plates that have been made thinner by carving or scraping.","zh":"thinned plates 指透過雕削或刮削變薄了的木製面板。"},{"en":"A craft worker may handle thinned wood carefully because it can break more easily.","zh":"工匠可能小心處理削薄了的木材，因為它較容易斷裂。"},{"en":"If plates are thinned, their vibration and stiffness may change.","zh":"如果面板被削薄，其震動和硬度可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to material after some thickness has been removed.","zh":"這個片語指部分厚度已被移除後的材料。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be sprinkled with","meaning":"被撒上……","examples":[{"en":"The plates are sprinkled with flakes of glitter.","zh":"面板被撒上閃粉碎片。"},{"en":"Be sprinkled with means be lightly covered with small pieces or drops of something.","zh":"be sprinkled with 指被少量小片或小滴輕輕覆蓋。"},{"en":"A cake may be sprinkled with sugar before it is served.","zh":"蛋糕上桌前可能被撒上糖。"},{"en":"If a plate is sprinkled with glitter, the movement of the glitter can reveal vibration patterns.","zh":"如果面板被撒上閃粉，閃粉的移動可以顯示震動圖案。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a light, even scattering.","zh":"這個片語暗示輕而均勻地散落。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"flakes of glitter","meaning":"閃粉碎片","examples":[{"en":"Flakes of glitter reveal the vibration patterns of the plates.","zh":"閃粉碎片顯示面板的震動圖案。"},{"en":"Flakes of glitter are tiny shiny pieces used to show movement or create sparkle.","zh":"flakes of glitter 指用來顯示移動或製造閃亮效果的細小閃亮碎片。"},{"en":"In a craft lesson, students may use flakes of glitter to decorate cards.","zh":"在手工課中，學生可能使用閃粉碎片裝飾卡片。"},{"en":"If glitter moves into lines on a vibrating plate, it shows where the wood is moving less.","zh":"如果閃粉在震動面板上移動成線，就顯示木材哪些位置移動較少。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to small visible particles.","zh":"這個片語指細小可見粒子。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be suspended horizontally","meaning":"被水平懸掛","examples":[{"en":"The plates are suspended horizontally above a loudspeaker.","zh":"面板被水平懸掛在揚聲器上方。"},{"en":"Be suspended horizontally means be held in the air in a flat, level position.","zh":"be suspended horizontally 指以平坦、水平的位置被支撐在空中。"},{"en":"A lamp may be suspended horizontally over a dining table.","zh":"燈具可能被水平懸掛在餐桌上方。"},{"en":"If a violin plate is suspended horizontally, it can vibrate freely during testing.","zh":"如果小提琴面板被水平懸掛，它在測試時就能自由震動。"},{"en":"The phrase describes both position and support.","zh":"這個片語同時描述位置和支撐方式。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"above a loudspeaker","meaning":"在揚聲器上方","examples":[{"en":"The violin plate is positioned above a loudspeaker.","zh":"小提琴面板被放置在揚聲器上方。"},{"en":"Above a loudspeaker means placed higher than a speaker that produces sound.","zh":"above a loudspeaker 指被放在產生聲音的揚聲器之上。"},{"en":"A science teacher may place paper above a loudspeaker to show how sound makes it move.","zh":"科學老師可能把紙放在揚聲器上方，以展示聲音如何令它移動。"},{"en":"If the loudspeaker vibrates the plate from below, patterns can appear on its surface.","zh":"如果揚聲器從下方使面板震動，其表面可以出現圖案。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the setup of an acoustic experiment.","zh":"這個片語描述聲學實驗的設置。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"excite a resonance","meaning":"激發共振","examples":[{"en":"The loudspeaker excites a resonance in the wooden plate.","zh":"揚聲器在木板中激發共振。"},{"en":"Excite a resonance means cause an object to vibrate strongly at one of its natural frequencies.","zh":"excite a resonance 指使物件在其自然頻率之一上強烈震動。"},{"en":"A singer may excite a resonance in a glass if the note matches the glass’s natural vibration.","zh":"如果歌手的音符配合玻璃杯的自然震動，就可能激發玻璃杯共振。"},{"en":"If the speaker excites a resonance, the plate’s movement becomes easier to observe.","zh":"如果揚聲器激發共振，面板的移動就更容易被觀察。"},{"en":"The phrase describes triggering a natural vibration.","zh":"這個片語描述觸發自然震動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"form a pattern","meaning":"形成圖案","examples":[{"en":"The glitter forms a pattern when the plate vibrates.","zh":"當面板震動時，閃粉形成圖案。"},{"en":"Form a pattern means arrange into a visible shape or repeated design.","zh":"form a pattern 指排列成可見形狀或重複設計。"},{"en":"Students may form a pattern with coloured blocks to learn symmetry.","zh":"學生可能用彩色積木形成圖案來學習對稱。"},{"en":"If glitter forms lines on a vibrating plate, the pattern reveals how the plate moves.","zh":"如果閃粉在震動面板上形成線條，該圖案就顯示面板如何移動。"},{"en":"The phrase shows visible order appearing from movement or arrangement.","zh":"這個片語顯示可見秩序由移動或安排中出現。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"interactively tune","meaning":"以互動方式調校","examples":[{"en":"Makers interactively tune the resonances during carving.","zh":"製作者在雕製期間以互動方式調校共振。"},{"en":"Interactively tune means adjust something step by step while checking its response after each change.","zh":"interactively tune 指每次改變後檢查反應，再一步步調整。"},{"en":"A music teacher may interactively tune a student’s performance by listening and giving immediate feedback.","zh":"音樂老師可能透過聆聽和即時回饋，以互動方式調校學生表演。"},{"en":"If makers carve, test and adjust repeatedly, the tuning process becomes interactive.","zh":"如果製作者反覆雕削、測試和調整，調校過程就變得互動。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights adjustment through feedback.","zh":"這個片語突出透過回饋作調整。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"free plate resonances","meaning":"自由面板共振","examples":[{"en":"The makers measure the first few free plate resonances.","zh":"製作者量度最初幾個自由面板共振。"},{"en":"Free plate resonances are the natural vibrations of a violin plate before it is attached to the instrument.","zh":"free plate resonances 指小提琴面板在裝到樂器上之前的自然震動。"},{"en":"A loose wooden board may vibrate differently before it is fixed into a frame.","zh":"一塊鬆散木板在固定到框架前，可能有不同震動方式。"},{"en":"If makers measure free plate resonances, they can study the plate before final assembly.","zh":"如果製作者量度自由面板共振，就能在最後組裝前研究面板。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to vibration behaviour of separate plates.","zh":"這個片語指分離面板的震動行為。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"specified patterns","meaning":"指定圖案","examples":[{"en":"The resonances are adjusted to specified patterns.","zh":"共振被調整至指定圖案。"},{"en":"Specified patterns are particular patterns that have been chosen or required beforehand.","zh":"specified patterns 指事先選定或要求的特定圖案。"},{"en":"Students may arrange tiles into specified patterns during a design lesson.","zh":"學生可能在設計課中把瓷磚排列成指定圖案。"},{"en":"If makers aim for specified vibration patterns, their work follows a clear target.","zh":"如果製作者以指定震動圖案為目標，其工作就有清楚標準。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests planned standards rather than random results.","zh":"這個片語暗示計劃好的標準，而不是隨機結果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"very few examples of","meaning":"極少……的例子","examples":[{"en":"There are very few examples of such measurements on historic violins.","zh":"對歷史小提琴進行這類測量的例子極少。"},{"en":"Very few examples of means only a small number of cases exist.","zh":"very few examples of 指只有很少數案例存在。"},{"en":"There are very few examples of perfect exam essays written without planning.","zh":"完全沒有計劃卻寫得完美的考試文章例子極少。"},{"en":"If very few examples exist, researchers must be cautious about general conclusions.","zh":"如果例子極少，研究人員就必須謹慎作一般結論。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses limited evidence.","zh":"這個片語強調證據有限。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"really fine Italian instruments","meaning":"真正優質的意大利樂器","examples":[{"en":"Owners rarely permit tests on really fine Italian instruments.","zh":"擁有人很少容許對真正優質的意大利樂器進行測試。"},{"en":"Really fine Italian instruments are exceptionally good historic instruments made in Italy.","zh":"really fine Italian instruments 指在意大利製作、質素極高的歷史樂器。"},{"en":"A collector may keep a really fine Italian instrument in a climate-controlled room.","zh":"收藏家可能把真正優質的意大利樂器存放在恆溫恆濕房間中。"},{"en":"If an instrument is extremely valuable, owners may refuse risky scientific tests.","zh":"如果樂器極有價值，擁有人可能拒絕有風險的科學測試。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses high quality, origin and value.","zh":"這個片語強調高質素、來源和價值。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be reluctant to allow","meaning":"不願容許……","examples":[{"en":"Owners are reluctant to allow valuable violins to be dismantled.","zh":"擁有人不願容許珍貴小提琴被拆開。"},{"en":"Be reluctant to allow means be unwilling or hesitant to permit something.","zh":"be reluctant to allow 指不願意或猶豫是否准許某事。"},{"en":"Parents may be reluctant to allow young children to travel alone at night.","zh":"家長可能不願容許年幼孩子夜晚獨自出行。"},{"en":"If a test might damage a valuable object, owners will naturally hesitate.","zh":"如果測試可能損壞珍貴物件，擁有人自然會猶豫。"},{"en":"The phrase shows caution and unwillingness.","zh":"這個片語顯示謹慎和不願意。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be taken apart","meaning":"被拆開","examples":[{"en":"Historic violins cannot easily be taken apart for testing.","zh":"歷史小提琴不能輕易被拆開作測試。"},{"en":"Be taken apart means be separated into pieces or components.","zh":"be taken apart 指被分拆成不同部分或組件。"},{"en":"A phone may be taken apart by a repair technician to replace the battery.","zh":"手機可能由維修技術員拆開以更換電池。"},{"en":"If an old violin is taken apart, there is a risk of damage or loss of value.","zh":"如果古老小提琴被拆開，就有損壞或貶值風險。"},{"en":"The phrase describes dismantling an object.","zh":"這個片語描述拆解物件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for the sake of science","meaning":"為了科學研究","examples":[{"en":"Owners will not risk valuable instruments for the sake of science.","zh":"擁有人不會為了科學研究而冒險損害珍貴樂器。"},{"en":"For the sake of science means in order to help scientific knowledge or research.","zh":"for the sake of science 指為了幫助科學知識或研究。"},{"en":"Volunteers may join a medical study for the sake of science and future patients.","zh":"義工可能為了科學和未來病人參加醫學研究。"},{"en":"If a test risks damaging a priceless violin, owners may decide science is not worth the risk.","zh":"如果測試有損壞無價小提琴的風險，擁有人可能認為科學不值得這種風險。"},{"en":"The phrase explains a purpose, often with sacrifice or risk.","zh":"這個片語解釋目的，常帶犧牲或風險。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tests that have been performed","meaning":"已進行的測試","examples":[{"en":"The few tests that have been performed produced interesting results.","zh":"少數已進行的測試產生了有趣結果。"},{"en":"Tests that have been performed are experiments or examinations that have actually been carried out.","zh":"tests that have been performed 指實際已經進行的實驗或檢查。"},{"en":"The tests that have been performed on the new teaching method are still too few to prove success.","zh":"對新教學方法已進行的測試仍太少，未能證明成功。"},{"en":"If only a few tests have been done, their results are useful but limited.","zh":"如果只完成少數測試，其結果有用但有限。"},{"en":"The phrase distinguishes real evidence from proposed testing.","zh":"這個片語把真實證據與建議中的測試分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tune the resonant modes","meaning":"調校共振模式","examples":[{"en":"The early makers may have tuned the resonant modes of the plates.","zh":"早期製作者可能調校了面板的共振模式。"},{"en":"Tune the resonant modes means adjust the natural vibration patterns to desired pitches or relationships.","zh":"tune the resonant modes 指把自然震動模式調整到所需音高或關係。"},{"en":"A drum maker may tune the skin so it vibrates at the sound they want.","zh":"鼓製作者可能調校鼓面，使其震動出想要的聲音。"},{"en":"If violin makers tuned resonant modes, they were controlling how the plates responded to sound.","zh":"如果小提琴製作者調校共振模式，他們就是在控制面板如何回應聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase connects craft adjustment with acoustics.","zh":"這個片語把工藝調整與聲學連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"resonant modes","meaning":"共振模式","examples":[{"en":"The resonant modes could be recognised by tapping the wood.","zh":"共振模式可以透過敲擊木材被辨認出來。"},{"en":"Resonant modes are the natural vibration patterns of an object.","zh":"resonant modes 指物件的自然震動模式。"},{"en":"A metal ruler hanging over a desk has different resonant modes when it is flicked at different lengths.","zh":"懸在書桌邊的金屬尺，在不同長度被彈動時會有不同共振模式。"},{"en":"If a maker can hear resonant modes, they can adjust wood by ear.","zh":"如果製作者能聽出共振模式，就能憑耳朵調整木材。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to how an object vibrates naturally.","zh":"這個片語指物件如何自然震動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"individual plates","meaning":"個別面板","examples":[{"en":"The individual plates may have been tuned separately.","zh":"個別面板可能已被分開調校。"},{"en":"Individual plates are separate front or back wooden panels before they are assembled into the violin.","zh":"individual plates 指在組裝成小提琴之前分開的前面板或後面板。"},{"en":"A craft worker may test individual parts before putting together the final object.","zh":"工匠可能在組裝最終物件前測試個別部件。"},{"en":"If individual plates are tuned separately, each part is adjusted before joining the whole instrument.","zh":"如果個別面板被分開調校，每個部分就在加入整件樂器前被調整。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on separate components.","zh":"這個片語集中於分開的組件。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"exact musical intervals","meaning":"精確的音程","examples":[{"en":"The resonances may have been tuned to exact musical intervals.","zh":"共振可能已被調校至精確的音程。"},{"en":"Exact musical intervals are precise pitch distances between notes.","zh":"exact musical intervals 指音符之間精準的音高距離。"},{"en":"Music students learn exact intervals when practising scales and harmony.","zh":"音樂學生練習音階和和聲時會學習精確音程。"},{"en":"If resonances match exact musical intervals, the design reflects careful numerical thinking.","zh":"如果共振配合精確音程，設計就反映仔細的數字思維。"},{"en":"The phrase connects sound with mathematical precision.","zh":"這個片語把聲音與數學精準連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be consistent with","meaning":"與……一致","examples":[{"en":"This technique would be consistent with Renaissance ideas of perfection.","zh":"這種技術會與文藝復興時期關於完美的理念一致。"},{"en":"Be consistent with means agree with or fit well with something else.","zh":"be consistent with 指與另一事物相符或配合良好。"},{"en":"A student’s explanation is consistent with the evidence if it matches the facts in the passage.","zh":"如果學生的解釋符合文章事實，就是與證據一致。"},{"en":"If exact ratios were valued in the Renaissance, tuning by intervals would fit that worldview.","zh":"如果文藝復興時期重視精確比例，按音程調校就會符合那種世界觀。"},{"en":"The phrase shows compatibility, not necessarily proof.","zh":"這個片語顯示相容性，不一定是證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"prevailing Renaissance view","meaning":"文藝復興時期盛行的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The method reflected the prevailing Renaissance view of perfection.","zh":"這種方法反映了文藝復興時期盛行的完美觀。"},{"en":"Prevailing Renaissance view means the widely accepted belief during the Renaissance period.","zh":"prevailing Renaissance view 指文藝復興時期廣泛接受的信念。"},{"en":"In some periods, the prevailing view in education was that strict discipline produced good students.","zh":"在某些時期，教育界盛行的觀點是嚴格紀律能培養好學生。"},{"en":"If a craft method follows the prevailing view of its age, it reflects the values of that time.","zh":"如果工藝方法遵循其時代的盛行觀點，它就反映當時價值。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a technique with historical thinking.","zh":"這個片語把技術與歷史思想連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be measured in terms of","meaning":"以……來衡量","examples":[{"en":"Perfection was measured in terms of numbers and exact ratios.","zh":"完美以數字和精確比例來衡量。"},{"en":"Be measured in terms of means be judged according to a particular standard or factor.","zh":"be measured in terms of 指根據某特定標準或因素來判斷。"},{"en":"School success should not be measured only in terms of exam scores.","zh":"學校成功不應只以考試分數來衡量。"},{"en":"If perfection is measured through ratios, makers may aim for mathematical balance.","zh":"如果完美透過比例來衡量，製作者可能追求數學上的平衡。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the basis of judgement.","zh":"這個片語解釋判斷的基礎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"exact ratios","meaning":"精確比例","examples":[{"en":"Renaissance thinkers valued numbers and exact ratios.","zh":"文藝復興思想家重視數字和精確比例。"},{"en":"Exact ratios are precise relationships between quantities or measurements.","zh":"exact ratios 指數量或測量之間精確的關係。"},{"en":"A recipe may require exact ratios of flour, water and yeast to make good bread.","zh":"食譜可能需要麵粉、水和酵母的精確比例才能做出好麵包。"},{"en":"If violin design uses exact ratios, small measurement changes may affect the whole form.","zh":"如果小提琴設計使用精確比例，小小測量變化可能影響整體形態。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests mathematical precision.","zh":"這個片語暗示數學精準。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"historical data","meaning":"歷史數據","examples":[{"en":"There are no historical data to support the theory.","zh":"沒有歷史數據支持這個理論。"},{"en":"Historical data are records, documents, measurements, or evidence from the past.","zh":"historical data 指來自過去的記錄、文件、測量或證據。"},{"en":"Researchers use historical data such as letters, invoices and workshop notes to study old crafts.","zh":"研究人員使用信件、發票和工作室筆記等歷史數據研究舊工藝。"},{"en":"If no historical data exist, a theory may sound possible but remain unproven.","zh":"如果沒有歷史數據，理論可能聽起來可行，但仍未被證明。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on evidence from history.","zh":"這個片語集中於來自歷史的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"support this case","meaning":"支持這一論點","examples":[{"en":"No surviving records clearly support this case.","zh":"沒有留存記錄清楚支持這一論點。"},{"en":"Support this case means provide evidence for this argument or theory.","zh":"support this case 指為這個論點或理論提供證據。"},{"en":"A student needs examples from the passage to support their case in an essay.","zh":"學生需要文章例子來支持自己文章中的論點。"},{"en":"If no records support the case, readers should treat the claim cautiously.","zh":"如果沒有記錄支持這一論點，讀者就應謹慎看待該主張。"},{"en":"The phrase connects evidence with an argument.","zh":"這個片語把證據與論點連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"affect sound quality","meaning":"影響音質","examples":[{"en":"Several physical factors affect sound quality.","zh":"幾個物理因素影響音質。"},{"en":"Affect sound quality means influence how good, clear, rich or pleasant a sound is.","zh":"affect sound quality 指影響聲音有多好、清晰、豐富或悅耳。"},{"en":"Room size and microphone position can affect sound quality in an online lesson.","zh":"房間大小和咪高峰位置可以影響網上課堂的音質。"},{"en":"If wood, varnish and design affect sound quality, one factor alone cannot explain everything.","zh":"如果木材、清漆和設計都影響音質，單一因素就不能解釋一切。"},{"en":"The phrase links causes with what listeners hear.","zh":"這個片語把原因與聽眾聽到的效果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"presence of moisture","meaning":"水分的存在","examples":[{"en":"The presence of moisture can reduce the vibrancy of wood.","zh":"水分的存在可以降低木材鮮明有活力的音色。"},{"en":"Presence of moisture means water or dampness is present in a material or place.","zh":"presence of moisture 指材料或地方中有水分或潮氣。"},{"en":"The presence of moisture in a wall can lead to mould in a flat.","zh":"牆壁中水分的存在可以導致單位出現霉菌。"},{"en":"If wood contains too much moisture, it may vibrate less freely.","zh":"如果木材含有太多水分，可能較不能自由震動。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies water as a factor in a situation.","zh":"這個片語指出水分是情況中的因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"achieve the quality of","meaning":"達到……的品質","examples":[{"en":"Low internal damping helps achieve the quality of vibrancy.","zh":"低內部阻尼有助達到鮮明有活力的品質。"},{"en":"Achieve the quality of means successfully produce or reach a particular desirable feature.","zh":"achieve the quality of 指成功產生或達到某種理想特質。"},{"en":"A speaker may achieve the quality of clarity by using short sentences and clear examples.","zh":"講者可以透過使用短句和清楚例子達到清晰的品質。"},{"en":"If wood vibrates freely, it may help achieve a lively sound.","zh":"如果木材能自由震動，就可能幫助達到活潑聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a method with a desired quality.","zh":"這個片語把方法與理想品質連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"vibrancy","meaning":"鮮明有活力的音色","examples":[{"en":"High-quality wood can give a violin greater vibrancy.","zh":"高質素木材可以給小提琴更鮮明有活力的音色。"},{"en":"Vibrancy is a lively, rich and energetic quality in sound, colour or life.","zh":"vibrancy 指聲音、顏色或生活中的活潑、豐富和有能量的特質。"},{"en":"A market has vibrancy when it is full of voices, colours and movement.","zh":"當市場充滿聲音、色彩和動感時，它就有活力。"},{"en":"If a violin has vibrancy, its sound may feel alive rather than dull.","zh":"如果小提琴有 vibrancy，其聲音可能感覺有生命力，而不是沉悶。"},{"en":"The word suggests energy and freshness.","zh":"這個詞暗示能量和新鮮感。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"high-quality wood","meaning":"高質素木材","examples":[{"en":"Fine violins require high-quality wood.","zh":"優質小提琴需要高質素木材。"},{"en":"High-quality wood is strong, carefully chosen wood with good texture, dryness and vibration qualities.","zh":"high-quality wood 指堅固、經仔細選擇，並有良好紋理、乾燥度和震動特質的木材。"},{"en":"A carpenter may choose high-quality wood for a table meant to last for decades.","zh":"木匠可能為一張希望使用數十年的桌子選擇高質素木材。"},{"en":"If wood quality is poor, the finished object may crack, warp or sound weak.","zh":"如果木材質素差，成品可能裂開、變形或聲音薄弱。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses the importance of good material.","zh":"這個片語強調好材料的重要性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"low internal damping","meaning":"低內部阻尼","examples":[{"en":"Wood with low internal damping vibrates more freely.","zh":"具有低內部阻尼的木材震動得更自由。"},{"en":"Low internal damping means the material loses little vibration energy inside itself.","zh":"low internal damping 指材料內部流失的震動能量很少。"},{"en":"A bell with low damping keeps ringing longer after it is struck.","zh":"低阻尼的鐘被敲擊後會響得更久。"},{"en":"If violin wood has low internal damping, its sound may be more lively and sustained.","zh":"如果小提琴木材有低內部阻尼，其聲音可能更有活力並更持久。"},{"en":"The phrase describes efficient vibration.","zh":"這個片語描述高效震動。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"growth rings","meaning":"年輪","examples":[{"en":"Researchers measured the growth rings in Stradivarius wood.","zh":"研究人員量度史特拉第瓦里木材中的年輪。"},{"en":"Growth rings are the circular lines in wood that show how a tree grew year by year.","zh":"growth rings 指木材中顯示樹木逐年生長情況的圓形線紋。"},{"en":"Students can count growth rings on a tree stump to estimate the tree’s age.","zh":"學生可以數樹樁上的年輪來估計樹齡。"},{"en":"If growth rings are narrow or regular, they may tell researchers about the wood’s history.","zh":"如果年輪狹窄或規律，它們可能告訴研究人員木材的歷史。"},{"en":"The phrase connects tree growth with visible wood patterns.","zh":"這個片語把樹木生長與可見木紋連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"planks of wood","meaning":"木板","examples":[{"en":"The Italian makers sometimes used recently seasoned planks of wood.","zh":"意大利製作者有時使用最近乾燥處理過的木板。"},{"en":"Planks of wood are long, flat pieces of cut timber.","zh":"planks of wood 指切割好的長而平的木材。"},{"en":"A carpenter may store planks of wood in a dry room before making furniture.","zh":"木匠可能在製作家具前把木板存放在乾燥房間。"},{"en":"If planks are not properly dried, they may change shape after the instrument is made.","zh":"如果木板沒有適當乾燥，製成樂器後可能變形。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to prepared pieces of timber.","zh":"這個片語指已準備好的木材。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be seasoned for","meaning":"經過……年乾燥處理","examples":[{"en":"Some wood had been seasoned for only five years.","zh":"有些木材只經過五年乾燥處理。"},{"en":"Be seasoned for means be dried and aged for a certain period before use.","zh":"be seasoned for 指木材在使用前經過某段時間乾燥和陳放。"},{"en":"Timber for fine furniture may be seasoned for years so it becomes stable.","zh":"優質家具用木材可能經過多年乾燥處理，令它變得穩定。"},{"en":"If wood is not seasoned long enough, moisture may still affect its performance.","zh":"如果木材乾燥處理時間不夠，水分仍可能影響其表現。"},{"en":"The phrase describes preparation of wood over time.","zh":"這個片語描述木材隨時間準備的過程。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"intrinsic internal damping","meaning":"固有內部阻尼","examples":[{"en":"The wood’s intrinsic internal damping decreases over time.","zh":"木材的固有內部阻尼會隨時間下降。"},{"en":"Intrinsic internal damping is the natural tendency of wood itself to absorb vibration energy internally.","zh":"intrinsic internal damping 指木材本身在內部吸收震動能量的自然傾向。"},{"en":"A material’s intrinsic properties belong to the material itself, not to outside conditions.","zh":"材料的固有特性屬於材料本身，而不是外部條件。"},{"en":"If intrinsic damping decreases, old wood may vibrate more freely than before.","zh":"如果固有阻尼下降，古老木材可能比以前震動得更自由。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to a built-in physical property.","zh":"這個片語指內在的物理特性。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"decrease with time","meaning":"隨時間下降","examples":[{"en":"The internal damping of old wood may decrease with time.","zh":"舊木材的內部阻尼可能隨時間下降。"},{"en":"Decrease with time means become less as time passes.","zh":"decrease with time 指隨着時間過去而變少。"},{"en":"A new shoe’s stiffness may decrease with time as it is worn.","zh":"新鞋的硬度可能隨穿着時間而下降。"},{"en":"If damping decreases with time, older instruments may gradually become more resonant.","zh":"如果阻尼隨時間下降，較古老的樂器可能逐漸變得更有共鳴。"},{"en":"The phrase describes gradual reduction.","zh":"這個片語描述逐漸減少。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"contribute to","meaning":"促成；有助於","examples":[{"en":"The age of the wood may contribute to improved sound quality.","zh":"木材的年齡可能有助於改善音質。"},{"en":"Contribute to means help cause or add to a result.","zh":"contribute to 指幫助造成或增加某結果。"},{"en":"Regular sleep can contribute to better memory and concentration.","zh":"定期睡眠可以有助於更好的記憶和專注。"},{"en":"If old wood vibrates more freely, it may contribute to a richer violin tone.","zh":"如果舊木材震動更自由，它可能促成更豐富的小提琴音色。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests one factor among several causes.","zh":"這個片語暗示眾多原因中的一個因素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"improved quality","meaning":"改善了的品質","examples":[{"en":"Older wood may contribute to the improved quality of historic instruments.","zh":"較古老的木材可能有助於歷史樂器改善了的品質。"},{"en":"Improved quality means better standard, performance, or value than before.","zh":"improved quality 指比以前更好的標準、表現或價值。"},{"en":"A student’s improved quality of writing may come from clearer planning and more examples.","zh":"學生寫作質素改善，可能來自更清晰計劃和更多例子。"},{"en":"If wood changes over time, the instrument’s sound quality may improve gradually.","zh":"如果木材隨時間改變，樂器音質可能逐漸改善。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a positive change in standard.","zh":"這個片語描述標準上的正面變化。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"automatically contribute to","meaning":"自然而然有助於……","examples":[{"en":"Aging wood may automatically contribute to a richer tone.","zh":"木材老化可能自然而然有助於更豐富的音色。"},{"en":"Automatically contribute to means help produce a result without needing deliberate extra action.","zh":"automatically contribute to 指不需要額外刻意行動也有助於產生某結果。"},{"en":"Clear classroom routines can automatically contribute to better behaviour because students know what to do.","zh":"清晰課堂常規可以自然而然有助於更好行為，因為學生知道該做甚麼。"},{"en":"If wood naturally changes as it ages, time itself may help the sound.","zh":"如果木材隨老化自然改變，時間本身可能幫助聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a built-in or natural effect.","zh":"這個片語暗示內在或自然效果。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"older instruments","meaning":"較古老的樂器","examples":[{"en":"Older instruments may benefit from changes in the wood.","zh":"較古老的樂器可能受惠於木材中的變化。"},{"en":"Older instruments are musical instruments made many years or centuries ago.","zh":"older instruments 指多年前或數百年前製作的樂器。"},{"en":"A musician may borrow older instruments for special concerts because of their history and sound.","zh":"音樂家可能因歷史和聲音而借用較古老的樂器作特別演出。"},{"en":"If the material improves with age, older instruments may gain qualities newer ones lack.","zh":"如果材料隨年齡改善，較古老的樂器可能獲得新樂器缺乏的特質。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts historic instruments with modern ones.","zh":"這個片語把歷史樂器與現代樂器作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"explain why","meaning":"解釋為何","examples":[{"en":"The aging of wood may explain why modern violins improve over time.","zh":"木材老化可能解釋為何現代小提琴會隨時間改善。"},{"en":"Explain why means give the reason for something.","zh":"explain why 指給出某事的原因。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain why a grammar answer is wrong by showing the sentence structure.","zh":"老師可能透過展示句子結構，解釋為何某文法答案錯誤。"},{"en":"If wood changes with age, it may explain why a violin sounds better after years of playing.","zh":"如果木材隨年齡改變，這可能解釋為何小提琴在演奏多年後聲音更好。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces cause or reasoning.","zh":"這個片語引出原因或推理。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"appear to improve","meaning":"看來有所改善","examples":[{"en":"A modern instrument may appear to improve in its first few years.","zh":"現代樂器在最初幾年看來可能有所改善。"},{"en":"Appear to improve means seem to become better, though the cause may not be fully certain.","zh":"appear to improve 指看似變好，雖然原因未必完全確定。"},{"en":"A student may appear to improve after changing teachers, but extra practice may also be the reason.","zh":"學生換老師後看來有所改善，但額外練習也可能是原因。"},{"en":"If listeners hear a better tone over time, the instrument may appear to improve.","zh":"如果聽眾隨時間聽到更好音色，樂器可能看來有所改善。"},{"en":"The phrase is cautious because it reports appearance, not absolute proof.","zh":"這個片語較謹慎，因為它報告外觀，而不是絕對證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in its first few years","meaning":"在最初幾年","examples":[{"en":"A violin’s tone may develop in its first few years.","zh":"小提琴的音色可能在最初幾年發展。"},{"en":"In its first few years means during the early years after something is made or begins.","zh":"in its first few years 指某物製成或開始後的早期幾年。"},{"en":"A new school may change many rules in its first few years.","zh":"新學校可能在最初幾年改變許多規則。"},{"en":"If a violin changes in its first few years, players may notice the sound becoming warmer.","zh":"如果小提琴在最初幾年改變，演奏者可能注意到聲音變得更溫暖。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on the early stage of development.","zh":"這個片語集中於發展初期。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"account for","meaning":"解釋；造成","examples":[{"en":"The nature of the varnish may partly account for sound quality.","zh":"清漆的性質可能部分解釋音質。"},{"en":"Account for means explain or be the reason for something.","zh":"account for 指解釋某事或成為某事原因。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep may account for a student’s poor concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足可能解釋學生在課堂上專注力差。"},{"en":"If varnish affects vibration, it may account for part of a violin’s tone.","zh":"如果清漆影響震動，它可能解釋小提琴音色的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase links a cause with an observed result.","zh":"這個片語把原因與觀察到的結果連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"nature of the varnish","meaning":"清漆的性質","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have examined the nature of the varnish used on old violins.","zh":"研究人員檢視了用於古老小提琴上的清漆性質。"},{"en":"Nature of the varnish means the composition, qualities and behaviour of the protective coating.","zh":"nature of the varnish 指保護塗層的成分、特質和表現。"},{"en":"A furniture restorer may study the nature of the varnish before cleaning an old table.","zh":"家具修復師在清潔舊桌子前，可能研究清漆的性質。"},{"en":"If the varnish is hard, soft, thick or thin, it may affect how the wood vibrates.","zh":"如果清漆硬、軟、厚或薄，都可能影響木材如何震動。"},{"en":"The phrase asks what the varnish is like and how it works.","zh":"這個片語詢問清漆是甚麼樣，以及如何作用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"protect the instrument","meaning":"保護樂器","examples":[{"en":"Varnish is used to protect the instrument.","zh":"清漆用來保護樂器。"},{"en":"Protect the instrument means keep the musical instrument safe from damage, wear, moisture or dirt.","zh":"protect the instrument 指使樂器免受損壞、磨損、水分或污垢影響。"},{"en":"A violin case helps protect the instrument when a student carries it to school.","zh":"學生把小提琴帶到學校時，琴盒有助保護樂器。"},{"en":"If varnish protects wood from moisture, it may help preserve the violin for many years.","zh":"如果清漆保護木材免受水分影響，就可能幫助小提琴保存多年。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on preventing damage.","zh":"這個片語集中於防止損壞。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"for well over a century","meaning":"遠超過一個世紀","examples":[{"en":"The varnish theory has remained popular for well over a century.","zh":"清漆理論遠超過一個世紀以來一直流行。"},{"en":"For well over a century means for much more than one hundred years.","zh":"for well over a century 指遠遠超過一百年的時間。"},{"en":"Some schools have served the same neighbourhood for well over a century.","zh":"有些學校服務同一社區已遠超過一個世紀。"},{"en":"If a theory survives for well over a century, many people must have found it attractive.","zh":"如果一個理論存在遠超過一個世紀，必定有很多人覺得它有吸引力。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses a very long duration.","zh":"這個片語強調非常長的時間。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"popular theories about","meaning":"關於……的流行理論","examples":[{"en":"Several popular theories concern the Stradivarius secret.","zh":"有幾種關於史特拉第瓦里秘密的流行理論。"},{"en":"Popular theories about something are explanations that many people know, discuss, or believe.","zh":"popular theories about something 指許多人知道、討論或相信的解釋。"},{"en":"There are popular theories about why some students remember words faster than others.","zh":"關於為何有些學生記字較快，有一些流行理論。"},{"en":"If a theory is popular, it is not automatically proven by evidence.","zh":"如果一個理論流行，它不會自動等於有證據證明。"},{"en":"The phrase separates common belief from confirmed fact.","zh":"這個片語把普遍信念與已證實事實分開。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"some sort of magic composition","meaning":"某種神奇成分","examples":[{"en":"Some people believed the varnish had some sort of magic composition.","zh":"有些人相信清漆有某種神奇成分。"},{"en":"Some sort of magic composition means a mysterious special mixture thought to have extraordinary effects.","zh":"some sort of magic composition 指被認為有非凡效果的神秘特殊混合物。"},{"en":"A customer may believe a skincare product has some sort of magic formula if the advertising is exaggerated.","zh":"如果廣告誇張，顧客可能相信護膚產品有某種神奇配方。"},{"en":"If people cannot explain success, they may imagine a secret magical ingredient.","zh":"如果人們不能解釋成功，可能會想像有一種秘密神奇成分。"},{"en":"The phrase is slightly sceptical and suggests mystery rather than proof.","zh":"這個片語帶輕微懷疑語氣，暗示神秘而非證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"historical research","meaning":"歷史研究","examples":[{"en":"Historical research has challenged the secret-varnish theory.","zh":"歷史研究挑戰了秘密清漆理論。"},{"en":"Historical research is the study of past records, objects, documents and contexts.","zh":"historical research 指研究過去的記錄、物件、文件和背景。"},{"en":"Historical research may use letters, trade records and workshop notes to test old claims.","zh":"歷史研究可能使用信件、交易記錄和工作室筆記來檢驗舊主張。"},{"en":"If historical research finds ordinary varnish recipes, the secret theory becomes weaker.","zh":"如果歷史研究找到普通清漆配方，秘密理論就變弱。"},{"en":"The phrase describes evidence-based study of the past.","zh":"這個片語描述以證據為本的過去研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be similar to","meaning":"與……相似","examples":[{"en":"The old varnish was very similar to varnish used today.","zh":"舊清漆與今日使用的清漆非常相似。"},{"en":"Be similar to means be like something else in important ways.","zh":"be similar to 指在重要方面與另一事物相像。"},{"en":"This year’s exam format is similar to last year’s, so old papers are useful practice.","zh":"今年的考試形式與去年相似，所以舊試卷是有用練習。"},{"en":"If old varnish is similar to modern varnish, it may not contain a special secret ingredient.","zh":"如果舊清漆與現代清漆相似，它可能沒有特殊秘密成分。"},{"en":"The phrase compares shared features.","zh":"這個片語比較共同特徵。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"apart from the possibility that","meaning":"除了……這種可能性之外","examples":[{"en":"Apart from minor contamination, the varnish was probably ordinary.","zh":"除了輕微污染這種可能性之外，清漆大概很普通。"},{"en":"Apart from the possibility that means except for the chance that something may also be true.","zh":"apart from the possibility that 指除了某事也可能成立這個機會之外。"},{"en":"Apart from the possibility that the bus is delayed, we should arrive on time.","zh":"除了巴士可能延誤這種可能性之外，我們應該會準時到達。"},{"en":"If the only exception is minor contamination, the main conclusion remains that the varnish was ordinary.","zh":"如果唯一例外是輕微污染，主要結論仍是清漆普通。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces a limited exception.","zh":"這個片語引出有限例外。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be contaminated with","meaning":"被……污染","examples":[{"en":"The varnish may have been contaminated with workshop debris.","zh":"清漆可能被工作室碎屑污染。"},{"en":"Be contaminated with means be made impure or dirty by unwanted material.","zh":"be contaminated with 指被不想要的材料弄髒或變得不純。"},{"en":"Drinking water can be contaminated with bacteria if pipes are damaged.","zh":"如果水管受損，食水可能被細菌污染。"},{"en":"If varnish is contaminated with dust or insect parts, analysis may find unexpected substances.","zh":"如果清漆被灰塵或昆蟲部分污染，分析可能發現意外物質。"},{"en":"The phrase describes unwanted mixing or pollution.","zh":"這個片語描述不想要的混入或污染。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"passing insects","meaning":"飛過的昆蟲","examples":[{"en":"The varnish might have contained the wings of passing insects.","zh":"清漆可能含有飛過昆蟲的翅膀。"},{"en":"Passing insects are insects that happened to fly through or near a place.","zh":"passing insects 指剛好飛過或靠近某地方的昆蟲。"},{"en":"A wet painting left outside may catch dust, leaves, or passing insects.","zh":"留在戶外的濕畫作可能黏上灰塵、葉子或飛過的昆蟲。"},{"en":"If insects flew through a workshop, tiny parts could accidentally enter wet varnish.","zh":"如果昆蟲飛過工作室，細小部分可能意外進入濕清漆。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests accidental contact, not deliberate addition.","zh":"這個片語暗示意外接觸，而不是刻意添加。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"workshop floor","meaning":"工作室地面","examples":[{"en":"Debris from the workshop floor may have entered the varnish.","zh":"來自工作室地面的碎屑可能進入清漆。"},{"en":"Workshop floor means the floor of a place where practical making or repair work is done.","zh":"workshop floor 指進行實際製作或維修工作的地方的地面。"},{"en":"A carpenter sweeps the workshop floor to remove sawdust and sharp scraps.","zh":"木匠清掃工作室地面，以清除木屑和尖銳碎片。"},{"en":"If varnish is mixed near the workshop floor, dust and debris may fall into it.","zh":"如果清漆在工作室地面附近混合，灰塵和碎屑可能掉進去。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a concrete setting for craft work.","zh":"這個片語提供工藝工作的具體場景。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"convincing evidence","meaning":"令人信服的證據","examples":[{"en":"There is no convincing evidence for a secret formula.","zh":"沒有令人信服的證據支持有秘方。"},{"en":"Convincing evidence is strong proof that makes a claim believable.","zh":"convincing evidence 指令某主張可信的有力證據。"},{"en":"A teacher needs convincing evidence before deciding that a student copied homework.","zh":"老師在判斷學生抄功課前，需要令人信服的證據。"},{"en":"If evidence is weak or uncertain, it cannot convincingly support a theory.","zh":"如果證據薄弱或不確定，就不能有力支持理論。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses proof strong enough to persuade reasonable people.","zh":"這個片語強調足以說服理性人士的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"support the idea of","meaning":"支持……的說法","examples":[{"en":"The research does not support the idea of a magical varnish.","zh":"研究不支持神奇清漆的說法。"},{"en":"Support the idea of means provide evidence that makes an idea more believable.","zh":"support the idea of 指提供令某想法更可信的證據。"},{"en":"Good exam results may support the idea of using short daily revision.","zh":"好考試成績可能支持每日短時間溫習的說法。"},{"en":"If tests find ordinary materials, they do not support the idea of a secret mixture.","zh":"如果測試發現普通材料，就不支持有秘密混合物的說法。"},{"en":"The phrase connects evidence with a belief or explanation.","zh":"這個片語把證據與信念或解釋連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"secret formula","meaning":"秘方","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have found no evidence of a secret formula.","zh":"科學家沒有找到秘方的證據。"},{"en":"A secret formula is a special hidden recipe or mixture believed to create a unique result.","zh":"secret formula 指被認為能創造獨特結果的特殊隱藏配方或混合物。"},{"en":"A restaurant may claim to have a secret formula for its famous sauce.","zh":"餐廳可能聲稱自己的著名醬汁有秘方。"},{"en":"If no special ingredient is found, the success may come from skill rather than a formula.","zh":"如果沒有發現特殊成分，成功可能來自技巧，而不是配方。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests mystery, exclusivity and hidden knowledge.","zh":"這個片語暗示神秘、專屬和隱藏知識。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"claim that","meaning":"聲稱","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers claim that the timber was soaked in water.","zh":"有些研究人員聲稱木材曾被浸在水中。"},{"en":"Claim that means state something as true, often when others may question it.","zh":"claim that 指把某事說成真實，通常是在別人可能質疑時。"},{"en":"A company may claim that its product improves memory, but customers should check the evidence.","zh":"公司可能聲稱其產品改善記憶，但顧客應檢查證據。"},{"en":"If researchers claim something unusual, they need strong data to support it.","zh":"如果研究人員聲稱不尋常的事，就需要強力數據支持。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an assertion, not necessarily a proven fact.","zh":"這個片語引出主張，不一定是已證實事實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"soak the timber in water","meaning":"把木材浸在水中","examples":[{"en":"The makers may have soaked the timber in water before seasoning it.","zh":"製作者可能在乾燥處理前把木材浸在水中。"},{"en":"Soak the timber in water means leave wood in water for a period of time.","zh":"soak the timber in water 指把木材放在水中一段時間。"},{"en":"A craft worker may soak bamboo in water before bending it into shape.","zh":"工匠可能在彎曲竹材前先把竹浸在水中。"},{"en":"If timber is soaked, some substances may wash out before drying.","zh":"如果木材被浸泡，一些物質可能在乾燥前被洗出。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a preparation method for wood.","zh":"這個片語描述木材準備方法。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"leach out","meaning":"溶出；濾除","examples":[{"en":"Water may have been used to leach out harmful chemicals.","zh":"水可能被用來濾除有害化學物質。"},{"en":"Leach out means remove a substance gradually by washing or dissolving it away.","zh":"leach out 指透過沖洗或溶解，逐漸移除某種物質。"},{"en":"Rain can leach nutrients out of soil if the ground is left uncovered.","zh":"如果土地裸露，雨水可以把泥土中的養分濾走。"},{"en":"If soaking leaches out unwanted chemicals, the wood’s properties may change.","zh":"如果浸泡濾除不想要的化學物，木材性質可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes slow removal through liquid.","zh":"這個片語描述透過液體慢慢移除。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"supposedly harmful chemicals","meaning":"據稱有害的化學物質","examples":[{"en":"The soaking process was intended to remove supposedly harmful chemicals.","zh":"浸泡過程旨在移除據稱有害的化學物質。"},{"en":"Supposedly harmful chemicals are chemicals believed or claimed to be harmful, though the claim may be uncertain.","zh":"supposedly harmful chemicals 指被相信或聲稱有害，但該說法未必確定的化學物。"},{"en":"A product label may warn about supposedly harmful chemicals, but consumers should check reliable evidence.","zh":"產品標籤可能警告據稱有害的化學物質，但消費者應查看可靠證據。"},{"en":"If chemicals are only supposedly harmful, the theory depends on whether the harm can be proved.","zh":"如果化學物只是據稱有害，該理論就取決於能否證明傷害。"},{"en":"The phrase shows caution about a claim.","zh":"這個片語顯示對主張的謹慎。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"before it was seasoned","meaning":"在木材乾燥處理之前","examples":[{"en":"The timber may have been soaked before it was seasoned.","zh":"木材可能在乾燥處理之前被浸泡。"},{"en":"Before it was seasoned means before the wood was dried and aged for use.","zh":"before it was seasoned 指木材被乾燥和陳放以供使用之前。"},{"en":"Some bamboo may be soaked before it is dried and shaped into furniture.","zh":"有些竹材可能在乾燥並製成家具前先被浸泡。"},{"en":"If wood is soaked before seasoning, water treatment comes before drying in the preparation process.","zh":"如果木材在乾燥處理前被浸泡，水處理就是在準備過程中先於乾燥。"},{"en":"The phrase gives the order of two preparation steps.","zh":"這個片語給出兩個準備步驟的次序。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"recently sunken","meaning":"最近沉沒的","examples":[{"en":"Some theories involve recently sunken Venetian ships.","zh":"有些理論涉及最近沉沒的威尼斯船隻。"},{"en":"Recently sunken means having gone below the water not long before the time being discussed.","zh":"recently sunken 指在所討論時間不久前沉入水中。"},{"en":"Divers may explore a recently sunken boat to check whether anyone is trapped.","zh":"潛水員可能探索最近沉沒的小船，以檢查是否有人被困。"},{"en":"If ship wood was recently sunken, it might still be available for reuse.","zh":"如果船木最近沉沒，它可能仍可被取出再用。"},{"en":"The phrase describes something newly underwater.","zh":"這個片語描述剛沉入水中的東西。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Venetian war galleys","meaning":"威尼斯戰船","examples":[{"en":"The wood may have come from Venetian war galleys.","zh":"木材可能來自威尼斯戰船。"},{"en":"Venetian war galleys were fighting ships associated with Venice.","zh":"Venetian war galleys 指與威尼斯有關的戰鬥船隻。"},{"en":"A history class may study Venetian war galleys when learning about Mediterranean naval power.","zh":"歷史課學習地中海海軍力量時，可能研究威尼斯戰船。"},{"en":"If violin wood came from old ships, its history would be dramatic but needs evidence.","zh":"如果小提琴木材來自舊船，其歷史會很戲劇化，但需要證據。"},{"en":"The phrase combines place, history and military ships.","zh":"這個片語結合地方、歷史和軍事船隻。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"masts and oars","meaning":"桅杆和船槳","examples":[{"en":"The theory concerns wood taken from ship masts and oars.","zh":"該理論涉及取自船隻桅杆和船槳的木材。"},{"en":"Masts and oars are ship parts: masts hold sails, and oars are used for rowing.","zh":"masts and oars 是船的部分：桅杆支撐帆，船槳用來划船。"},{"en":"A museum model of an old ship may show tall masts and long oars.","zh":"舊船博物館模型可能展示高桅杆和長船槳。"},{"en":"If masts and oars were made from strong timber, that wood might later be reused.","zh":"如果桅杆和船槳由堅固木材製成，那些木材之後可能被再利用。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies specific wooden parts of ships.","zh":"這個片語指出船上的特定木製部分。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be used to make","meaning":"被用來製造……","examples":[{"en":"Timber from old ships may have been used to make violins.","zh":"舊船木材可能曾被用來製造小提琴。"},{"en":"Be used to make means serve as material for creating something.","zh":"be used to make 指作為製作某物的材料。"},{"en":"Recycled paper can be used to make notebooks for students.","zh":"再造紙可以被用來製造學生筆記本。"},{"en":"If old ship timber was used to make violins, the wood’s previous history may matter.","zh":"如果舊船木材被用來製造小提琴，木材過往歷史可能重要。"},{"en":"The phrase connects material with finished product.","zh":"這個片語把材料與成品連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"support this view","meaning":"支持這個觀點","examples":[{"en":"The scientific evidence does not convincingly support this view.","zh":"科學證據未能令人信服地支持這個觀點。"},{"en":"Support this view means provide evidence that makes this opinion or theory believable.","zh":"support this view 指提供證據令這個意見或理論可信。"},{"en":"A student should quote the passage to support their view in a reading answer.","zh":"學生應引用文章來支持閱讀答案中的觀點。"},{"en":"If the evidence is weak, it cannot strongly support the theory.","zh":"如果證據薄弱，就不能強力支持理論。"},{"en":"The phrase connects proof with opinion.","zh":"這個片語把證據與意見連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in conclusion","meaning":"總括而言","examples":[{"en":"In conclusion, science has not proved the superiority of Cremonese violins.","zh":"總括而言，科學尚未證明克雷莫納小提琴的優越性。"},{"en":"In conclusion introduces the final judgement after discussing evidence.","zh":"in conclusion 引出討論證據後的最終判斷。"},{"en":"In conclusion, the school should reduce homework but keep meaningful practice.","zh":"總括而言，學校應減少功課，但保留有意義的練習。"},{"en":"If a writer says “in conclusion”, they are summing up the main result of the argument.","zh":"如果作者說 in conclusion，就是在總結論證的主要結果。"},{"en":"The phrase signals the end of reasoning.","zh":"這個片語標示推理結束。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"provide convincing evidence","meaning":"提供令人信服的證據","examples":[{"en":"Science has not provided convincing evidence of intrinsic superiority.","zh":"科學尚未提供令人信服的證據證明固有優越性。"},{"en":"Provide convincing evidence means give strong proof that can persuade people.","zh":"provide convincing evidence 指提供能說服人的強力證據。"},{"en":"A student must provide convincing evidence before claiming that one method works best.","zh":"學生在聲稱某方法最好前，必須提供令人信服的證據。"},{"en":"If measurements do not clearly separate old and new violins, the evidence is not convincing.","zh":"如果測量不能清楚區分新舊小提琴，證據就不令人信服。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses proof, not belief.","zh":"這個片語強調證據，而不是信念。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"set something apart from","meaning":"令……有別於……","examples":[{"en":"Measurements do not clearly set Cremonese instruments apart from modern violins.","zh":"測量不能清楚令克雷莫納樂器有別於現代小提琴。"},{"en":"Set something apart from means make it clearly different from others.","zh":"set something apart from 指令某物明顯不同於其他事物。"},{"en":"Excellent customer service can set a small shop apart from large chains.","zh":"卓越顧客服務可以令小店有別於大型連鎖店。"},{"en":"If measurements cannot set old violins apart, their superiority is hard to prove scientifically.","zh":"如果測量不能令古老小提琴有別於現代小提琴，其優越性就難以用科學證明。"},{"en":"The phrase describes clear distinction.","zh":"這個片語描述清楚區別。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Cremonese instruments","meaning":"克雷莫納製造的樂器","examples":[{"en":"Cremonese instruments remain highly valued by musicians and collectors.","zh":"克雷莫納製造的樂器仍受到音樂家和收藏家高度重視。"},{"en":"Cremonese instruments are musical instruments made in Cremona, especially historic violins.","zh":"Cremonese instruments 指在克雷莫納製造的樂器，尤其是歷史名琴。"},{"en":"A collector may pay a high price for Cremonese instruments because of their history and reputation.","zh":"收藏家可能因歷史和聲譽而為克雷莫納製造的樂器支付高價。"},{"en":"If Cremonese instruments are famous, their name alone may influence expectations.","zh":"如果克雷莫納樂器很有名，名稱本身可能影響期望。"},{"en":"The phrase links instruments with a respected place of origin.","zh":"這個片語把樂器與受尊重的產地連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"finest violins","meaning":"最優質的小提琴","examples":[{"en":"Modern craftsmen can produce some of the finest violins available.","zh":"現代工匠能製作出一些現有最優質的小提琴。"},{"en":"Finest violins are violins of the highest quality in sound, craftsmanship, and playability.","zh":"finest violins 指在音色、工藝和演奏性方面最高質素的小提琴。"},{"en":"A music college may lend its finest violins only to advanced students.","zh":"音樂學院可能只把最優質的小提琴借給高階學生。"},{"en":"If modern makers can produce the finest violins, old instruments are not the only excellent choice.","zh":"如果現代製作者能製作最優質的小提琴，古老樂器就不是唯一優秀選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the top level of quality.","zh":"這個片語標示最高質素。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"skilled craftsmen today","meaning":"現今技巧純熟的工匠","examples":[{"en":"Skilled craftsmen today can make instruments of exceptional quality.","zh":"現今技巧純熟的工匠能製作出質素卓越的樂器。"},{"en":"Skilled craftsmen today are modern makers with strong practical ability and specialist training.","zh":"skilled craftsmen today 指具有強大實用能力和專門訓練的現代製作者。"},{"en":"Skilled craftsmen today may combine traditional handwork with modern tools.","zh":"現今技巧純熟的工匠可能結合傳統手工和現代工具。"},{"en":"If today’s craftsmen are highly skilled, modern instruments can compete with historic ones.","zh":"如果今日工匠技巧很高，現代樂器就能與歷史樂器競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase reminds us that excellent craft still exists now.","zh":"這個片語提醒我們優秀工藝如今仍存在。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"leading soloists","meaning":"頂尖獨奏家","examples":[{"en":"Some leading soloists occasionally perform on modern violins.","zh":"有些頂尖獨奏家偶爾使用現代小提琴演奏。"},{"en":"Leading soloists are top individual performers who play major parts alone or with an orchestra.","zh":"leading soloists 指單獨或與樂團合作演奏主要部分的頂尖個人演奏者。"},{"en":"A leading soloist may perform a concerto in front of a large audience.","zh":"頂尖獨奏家可能在大量觀眾面前演奏協奏曲。"},{"en":"If leading soloists choose modern instruments, those instruments gain credibility.","zh":"如果頂尖獨奏家選擇現代樂器，這些樂器就獲得可信度。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to musicians at a high professional level.","zh":"這個片語指高專業水平的音樂家。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"occasionally play on","meaning":"偶爾使用……演奏","examples":[{"en":"Some soloists occasionally play on modern instruments.","zh":"有些獨奏家偶爾使用現代樂器演奏。"},{"en":"Occasionally play on means use an instrument from time to time, but not regularly.","zh":"occasionally play on 指有時使用某樂器演奏，但不是經常。"},{"en":"A pianist may occasionally play on an electronic keyboard when a real piano is unavailable.","zh":"當沒有真鋼琴可用時，鋼琴家可能偶爾使用電子琴演奏。"},{"en":"If famous soloists occasionally use modern violins, they do not reject them completely.","zh":"如果著名獨奏家偶爾使用現代小提琴，他們就不是完全拒絕它們。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests limited but real use.","zh":"這個片語暗示有限但真實的使用。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"foremost soloists","meaning":"最頂尖的獨奏家","examples":[{"en":"The foremost soloists often continue to prefer historic instruments.","zh":"最頂尖的獨奏家常繼續偏好歷史樂器。"},{"en":"Foremost soloists are the most important or highly respected solo performers.","zh":"foremost soloists 指最重要或最受尊重的獨奏表演者。"},{"en":"The foremost soloists may be invited to perform with world-famous orchestras.","zh":"最頂尖的獨奏家可能獲邀與世界著名樂團演出。"},{"en":"If foremost soloists prefer old instruments, public belief in those instruments remains strong.","zh":"如果最頂尖獨奏家偏好古老樂器，公眾對那些樂器的信念仍會強烈。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the very top of the profession.","zh":"這個片語標示行業最高層次。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"not surprisingly","meaning":"不足為奇","examples":[{"en":"Not surprisingly, violin dealers defend the reputation of old instruments.","zh":"小提琴經銷商維護古老樂器的聲譽，這不足為奇。"},{"en":"Not surprisingly means the result is expected and easy to understand.","zh":"not surprisingly 指結果是預期之中且容易理解。"},{"en":"Not surprisingly, students who revise regularly usually feel calmer before exams.","zh":"經常溫習的學生考試前通常較冷靜，這不足為奇。"},{"en":"If dealers earn money from old violins, it is not surprising that they defend their value.","zh":"如果經銷商靠古老小提琴賺錢，他們維護其價值並不令人意外。"},{"en":"The phrase introduces an expected conclusion.","zh":"這個片語引出預期結論。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"vested interest in","meaning":"在……中有既得利益","examples":[{"en":"Violin dealers have a vested interest in maintaining high prices.","zh":"小提琴經銷商在維持高價中有既得利益。"},{"en":"A vested interest in something is a personal financial or practical benefit from a particular outcome.","zh":"vested interest in something 指從某結果中得到個人財務或實際好處。"},{"en":"A shop owner has a vested interest in attracting more customers to the street.","zh":"店主在吸引更多顧客到街上有既得利益。"},{"en":"If dealers profit from high prices, their opinions may not be completely neutral.","zh":"如果經銷商從高價中獲利，他們的意見可能不完全中立。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that self-interest may influence judgement.","zh":"這個片語提醒自利可能影響判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"maintain the legend of","meaning":"維持……的傳說","examples":[{"en":"Dealers help maintain the legend of Cremonese superiority.","zh":"經銷商幫助維持克雷莫納優越性的傳說。"},{"en":"Maintain the legend of means keep a famous belief or story alive.","zh":"maintain the legend of 指使一個著名信念或故事繼續存在。"},{"en":"A school may maintain the legend of an excellent old teacher by telling stories about them.","zh":"學校可能透過講述一位優秀老教師的故事，維持其傳說。"},{"en":"If dealers repeat stories of old violin superiority, buyers may continue to believe them.","zh":"如果經銷商重複古老小提琴優越性的故事，買家可能繼續相信。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests preserving reputation, whether fully proven or not.","zh":"這個片語暗示保存聲譽，不論是否完全證實。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"Cremonese legend","meaning":"克雷莫納小提琴的傳奇","examples":[{"en":"The Cremonese legend remains powerful among musicians.","zh":"克雷莫納小提琴的傳奇在音樂家之間仍然強大。"},{"en":"The Cremonese legend is the belief that instruments from Cremona have special unmatched quality.","zh":"Cremonese legend 指相信克雷莫納樂器具有特殊而無可比擬質素的信念。"},{"en":"A music student may hear the Cremonese legend before ever playing an old Italian violin.","zh":"音樂學生可能在真正演奏古老意大利小提琴前，已聽過克雷莫納傳奇。"},{"en":"If a legend is strong, it can shape expectations before evidence is considered.","zh":"如果傳奇很強，它可以在證據被考慮前塑造期望。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to reputation built around place, history and sound.","zh":"這個片語指圍繞地方、歷史和聲音建立的聲譽。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"intrinsic superiority","meaning":"固有優越性","examples":[{"en":"Some musicians believe in the intrinsic superiority of old Italian violins.","zh":"有些音樂家相信古老意大利小提琴具有固有優越性。"},{"en":"Intrinsic superiority means built-in or natural excellence that belongs to something itself.","zh":"intrinsic superiority 指某物本身內在或天然具有的卓越。"},{"en":"A school should not assume intrinsic superiority in expensive textbooks without checking learning results.","zh":"學校不應在沒有檢查學習結果下，假定昂貴教科書有固有優越性。"},{"en":"If old violins have intrinsic superiority, their advantage should exist beyond reputation or price.","zh":"如果古老小提琴有固有優越性，其優勢應超越聲譽或價格而存在。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to inner quality, not external image.","zh":"這個片語指內在質素，而不是外在形象。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"remain utterly unconvinced","meaning":"仍然完全不信服","examples":[{"en":"Many leading musicians remain utterly unconvinced by the scientific findings.","zh":"許多頂尖音樂家仍然完全不信服科學發現。"},{"en":"Remain utterly unconvinced means continue to be completely not persuaded.","zh":"remain utterly unconvinced 指繼續完全沒有被說服。"},{"en":"A parent may remain utterly unconvinced by a child’s excuse if the story keeps changing.","zh":"如果孩子的藉口一直改變，家長可能仍然完全不信服。"},{"en":"If musicians trust their ears more than measurements, they may reject scientific conclusions.","zh":"如果音樂家更信任自己的耳朵多於測量，他們可能拒絕科學結論。"},{"en":"The phrase shows strong continuing doubt.","zh":"這個片語顯示強烈而持續的懷疑。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reading passage has nine paragraphs","meaning":"閱讀文章共有九段","examples":[{"en":"The reading passage has nine paragraphs labelled A to I.","zh":"閱讀文章共有九段，標記為 A 至 I。"},{"en":"Reading passage has nine paragraphs means the text is divided into nine labelled sections.","zh":"reading passage has nine paragraphs 指文本被分成九個有標記的部分。"},{"en":"In an exam, students should note paragraph labels before answering matching-heading questions.","zh":"在考試中，學生回答配對標題題前應留意段落標記。"},{"en":"If a passage has many paragraphs, skimming the main idea of each one becomes important.","zh":"如果文章有很多段，略讀每段主旨就變得重要。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the structure of a reading text.","zh":"這個片語描述閱讀文本的結構。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"choose the correct heading","meaning":"選出正確標題","examples":[{"en":"Candidates choose the correct heading for each paragraph.","zh":"考生為每段選出正確標題。"},{"en":"Choose the correct heading means select the title that best matches the main idea of a paragraph.","zh":"choose the correct heading 指選出最符合段落主旨的標題。"},{"en":"Students should read the whole paragraph before choosing the heading, not only the first sentence.","zh":"學生選標題前應讀完整段，而不只是第一句。"},{"en":"If a heading is too narrow, it may match a detail but miss the main idea.","zh":"如果標題太狹窄，可能符合細節但錯過主旨。"},{"en":"The phrase is a common instruction in reading exams.","zh":"這個片語是閱讀考試常見指示。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"list of headings","meaning":"標題列表","examples":[{"en":"The task provides a list of possible headings.","zh":"任務提供一個可能標題列表。"},{"en":"A list of headings is a set of title options for students to match with paragraphs.","zh":"list of headings 指一組讓學生與段落配對的標題選項。"},{"en":"Students may cross out used headings if the exam allows each one only once.","zh":"如果考試規定每個標題只能用一次，學生可以刪去已用標題。"},{"en":"If two headings look similar, the paragraph’s overall focus decides the answer.","zh":"如果兩個標題看似相似，段落整體重點決定答案。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to answer choices in a heading-matching task.","zh":"這個片語指配對標題題中的答案選項。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"analysis of protective coatings","meaning":"對保護塗層的分析","examples":[{"en":"One heading concerns an analysis of protective coatings.","zh":"其中一個標題涉及對保護塗層的分析。"},{"en":"Analysis of protective coatings means careful study of materials applied to protect a surface.","zh":"analysis of protective coatings 指仔細研究用於保護表面的材料。"},{"en":"A museum may conduct an analysis of protective coatings before restoring an old painting.","zh":"博物館在修復舊畫前，可能對保護塗層進行分析。"},{"en":"If coatings affect both protection and appearance, analysing them helps explain the object’s condition.","zh":"如果塗層同時影響保護和外觀，分析它們有助解釋物件狀態。"},{"en":"The phrase connects scientific study with surface treatment.","zh":"這個片語把科學研究與表面處理連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"protective coatings","meaning":"保護塗層","examples":[{"en":"Varnish and other protective coatings can affect an instrument.","zh":"清漆和其他保護塗層可以影響樂器。"},{"en":"Protective coatings are layers applied to a surface to protect it from damage, moisture or wear.","zh":"protective coatings 指塗在表面、用來防止損壞、水分或磨損的層。"},{"en":"A phone screen protector is a protective coating or layer that reduces scratches.","zh":"手機螢幕保護貼是一種保護塗層或保護層，可減少刮痕。"},{"en":"If a coating is too thick, it may protect the surface but change how the material behaves.","zh":"如果塗層太厚，可能保護表面，但改變材料表現。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on protective surface layers.","zh":"這個片語集中於保護性表層。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"apply technology to","meaning":"把科技應用於……","examples":[{"en":"Some makers apply technology to violin production.","zh":"有些製作者把科技應用於小提琴製作。"},{"en":"Apply technology to means use modern tools, machines, or scientific methods in a particular activity.","zh":"apply technology to 指在某活動中使用現代工具、機器或科學方法。"},{"en":"Schools apply technology to teaching when they use learning platforms and digital quizzes.","zh":"學校使用學習平台和數碼小測時，就是把科技應用於教學。"},{"en":"If makers apply technology to old crafts, they may gain more control and consistency.","zh":"如果製作者把科技應用於舊工藝，可能得到更高控制度和一致性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes using technology for a practical purpose.","zh":"這個片語描述為實際目的使用科技。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"violin production","meaning":"小提琴製作","examples":[{"en":"Modern technology has influenced violin production.","zh":"現代科技已影響小提琴製作。"},{"en":"Violin production means the process of making violins, from materials to finished instruments.","zh":"violin production 指從材料到成品製作小提琴的過程。"},{"en":"A workshop may improve violin production by recording measurements for each instrument.","zh":"工作室可能透過記錄每件樂器的測量數據來改善小提琴製作。"},{"en":"If production methods change, the sound and consistency of violins may also change.","zh":"如果製作方法改變，小提琴的聲音和一致性也可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase covers both craft and manufacturing.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋工藝和製造。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a key factor","meaning":"關鍵因素","examples":[{"en":"Some theories treat the location of production as a key factor.","zh":"有些理論把製作地點視為關鍵因素。"},{"en":"A key factor is an important cause or element that strongly affects a result.","zh":"a key factor 指強烈影響結果的重要原因或元素。"},{"en":"Sleep is a key factor in exam performance because tired students concentrate less well.","zh":"睡眠是考試表現的關鍵因素，因為疲倦學生較難集中。"},{"en":"If location affects wood supply, training and tradition, it may be a key factor in instrument quality.","zh":"如果地點影響木材供應、訓練和傳統，它可能是樂器質素的關鍵因素。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights something especially important.","zh":"這個片語突出某事特別重要。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"controversial range of prices","meaning":"具爭議的價格差距","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes a controversial range of violin prices.","zh":"文章描述小提琴具爭議的價格差距。"},{"en":"A controversial range of prices is a large price difference that people argue about.","zh":"controversial range of prices 指引起人們爭論的大幅價格差異。"},{"en":"A city may have a controversial range of rents when tiny flats cost almost as much as large homes elsewhere.","zh":"如果城市中小單位租金幾乎等同其他地方的大屋，租金差距可能具爭議。"},{"en":"If old violins cost millions while modern ones cost far less, people debate whether the gap is justified.","zh":"如果古老小提琴價值數百萬，而現代琴便宜得多，人們會爭論差距是否合理。"},{"en":"The phrase links price differences with disagreement.","zh":"這個片語把價格差異與分歧連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"techniques of mass production","meaning":"大量生產技術","examples":[{"en":"Factory-made instruments rely on techniques of mass production.","zh":"工廠製造的樂器依賴大量生產技術。"},{"en":"Techniques of mass production are methods used to make many identical or similar products quickly.","zh":"techniques of mass production 指用來快速製造大量相同或相似產品的方法。"},{"en":"Fast-food chains use techniques of mass production to prepare meals consistently.","zh":"快餐連鎖店使用大量生產技術，以穩定地準備餐點。"},{"en":"If violins are mass-produced, they may be affordable but less individually refined.","zh":"如果小提琴大量生產，可能價格可負擔，但個別精修較少。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts industrial efficiency with individual craftsmanship.","zh":"這個片語把工業效率與個人工藝作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"advantages of older wood","meaning":"古老木材的優點","examples":[{"en":"The passage considers the possible advantages of older wood.","zh":"文章考慮古老木材的可能優點。"},{"en":"Advantages of older wood are benefits that wood may gain as it ages.","zh":"advantages of older wood 指木材隨年齡可能獲得的好處。"},{"en":"Older wood in furniture may be valued because it is stable, dry and visually rich.","zh":"家具中的古老木材可能因穩定、乾燥和紋理豐富而受重視。"},{"en":"If wood damping decreases over time, age may improve vibration and sound.","zh":"如果木材阻尼隨時間下降，年齡可能改善震動和聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on possible benefits of age.","zh":"這個片語集中於年齡可能帶來的好處。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"re-evaluation of","meaning":"重新評估……","examples":[{"en":"New evidence may lead to a re-evaluation of earlier theories.","zh":"新證據可能導致對早期理論的重新評估。"},{"en":"Re-evaluation of something means judging it again in light of new evidence or new thinking.","zh":"re-evaluation of something 指根據新證據或新思維重新判斷某事。"},{"en":"A student may need a re-evaluation of their study plan after several disappointing tests.","zh":"學生在幾次測驗失望後，可能需要重新評估學習計劃。"},{"en":"If scientific tests challenge an old story, researchers must reassess that story.","zh":"如果科學測試挑戰舊故事，研究人員就必須重新評估該故事。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a fresh judgement of an earlier idea.","zh":"這個片語描述對早期想法的新判斷。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"documentary evidence","meaning":"文獻證據","examples":[{"en":"Documentary evidence can support or weaken a historical theory.","zh":"文獻證據可以支持或削弱歷史理論。"},{"en":"Documentary evidence is proof from written records, documents, letters, contracts or archives.","zh":"documentary evidence 指來自書面記錄、文件、信件、合約或檔案的證據。"},{"en":"A historian may use documentary evidence from old receipts to learn what materials craftsmen bought.","zh":"歷史學家可能使用舊收據中的文獻證據，了解工匠購買了甚麼材料。"},{"en":"If no documents mention a secret formula, the theory becomes harder to prove.","zh":"如果沒有文件提到秘方，該理論就更難證明。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to evidence preserved in documents.","zh":"這個片語指保存在文件中的證據。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"mathematical basis","meaning":"數學基礎","examples":[{"en":"Exact ratios may have formed the mathematical basis of earlier design.","zh":"精確比例可能構成早期設計的數學基礎。"},{"en":"Mathematical basis means the numerical principles or calculations behind a design or idea.","zh":"mathematical basis 指設計或想法背後的數字原理或計算。"},{"en":"The mathematical basis of a bridge helps engineers decide its shape and strength.","zh":"橋樑的數學基礎幫助工程師決定其形狀和強度。"},{"en":"If violin design used exact ratios, its beauty may have been linked to numbers.","zh":"如果小提琴設計使用精確比例，其美感可能與數字有關。"},{"en":"The phrase connects design with mathematics.","zh":"這個片語把設計與數學連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"earlier design","meaning":"早期設計","examples":[{"en":"Renaissance ideas may have influenced earlier violin design.","zh":"文藝復興思想可能影響了早期小提琴設計。"},{"en":"Earlier design means design from an older period before later changes appeared.","zh":"earlier design 指後來變化出現前較早時期的設計。"},{"en":"A teacher may compare earlier design of mobile phones with today’s smartphones.","zh":"老師可能比較早期手機設計與今日智能手機。"},{"en":"If earlier violin design followed old ideas of proportion, history can help explain craft choices.","zh":"如果早期小提琴設計遵循舊比例觀念，歷史就能幫助解釋工藝選擇。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts older design with later development.","zh":"這個片語把舊設計與後來發展作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"manual woodworking techniques","meaning":"手工木工技術","examples":[{"en":"Traditional violin makers rely on manual woodworking techniques.","zh":"傳統小提琴製作者依賴手工木工技術。"},{"en":"Manual woodworking techniques are hand-based methods for cutting, shaping, smoothing and joining wood.","zh":"manual woodworking techniques 指以手工為主的木材切割、塑形、打磨和接合方法。"},{"en":"A carpenter uses manual woodworking techniques when shaping a table leg by hand.","zh":"木匠用手塑造桌腳時，就是使用手工木工技術。"},{"en":"If makers rely on hand techniques, skill and touch become especially important.","zh":"如果製作者依賴手工技術，技巧和觸感就特別重要。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts handcraft with machine production.","zh":"這個片語把手工與機器生產作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"preferences of top musicians","meaning":"頂尖音樂家的偏好","examples":[{"en":"The final paragraph discusses the preferences of top musicians.","zh":"最後一段討論頂尖音樂家的偏好。"},{"en":"Preferences of top musicians are the choices or favourites of highly respected performers.","zh":"preferences of top musicians 指非常受尊重的演奏者的選擇或喜好。"},{"en":"A violin shop may pay attention to the preferences of top musicians when recommending instruments.","zh":"小提琴店推薦樂器時，可能留意頂尖音樂家的偏好。"},{"en":"If top musicians prefer old violins, public opinion may continue to favour them.","zh":"如果頂尖音樂家偏好古老小提琴，公眾意見可能繼續偏向它們。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on what expert performers choose.","zh":"這個片語集中於專家演奏者選擇甚麼。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"saturated wood","meaning":"浸透水分的木材","examples":[{"en":"Some researchers have proposed the use of saturated wood.","zh":"有些研究人員提出使用浸透水分的木材。"},{"en":"Saturated wood is wood that has absorbed a large amount of water or liquid.","zh":"saturated wood 指吸收了大量水分或液體的木材。"},{"en":"Wood left in a flooded room may become saturated and difficult to dry.","zh":"留在水浸房間中的木材可能變得浸透水分，難以乾燥。"},{"en":"If saturated wood is later dried, its chemical or physical properties may change.","zh":"如果浸透水分的木材後來被乾燥，其化學或物理性質可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase describes wood filled with moisture.","zh":"這個片語描述充滿水分的木材。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"challenge for scientists","meaning":"科學家面對的挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Measuring complex violin sound remains a challenge for scientists.","zh":"量度複雜的小提琴聲音仍是科學家面對的挑戰。"},{"en":"A challenge for scientists is a problem that is difficult to study, measure or explain scientifically.","zh":"challenge for scientists 指科學上難以研究、量度或解釋的問題。"},{"en":"Predicting exactly how students learn from different teaching styles is a challenge for researchers.","zh":"準確預測學生如何從不同教學風格中學習，是研究人員面對的挑戰。"},{"en":"If human hearing notices qualities machines miss, violin sound becomes hard to measure scientifically.","zh":"如果人類聽覺注意到機器錯過的特質，小提琴聲音就很難以科學量度。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies a difficult scientific task.","zh":"這個片語指出困難的科學任務。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"agree with the information given","meaning":"與所提供資料一致","examples":[{"en":"Candidates decide whether each statement agrees with the information given.","zh":"考生判斷每個陳述是否與所提供資料一致。"},{"en":"Agree with the information given means match what the passage actually says.","zh":"agree with the information given 指與文章實際所說內容相符。"},{"en":"In reading tests, students should choose TRUE only when the statement agrees with the text.","zh":"在閱讀測驗中，只有當陳述與文本一致時，學生才應選 TRUE。"},{"en":"If a statement adds information not found in the passage, it may not agree with the given information.","zh":"如果陳述加入文章中沒有的資料，它可能不與所提供資料一致。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN tasks.","zh":"這個片語常見於 TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN 題。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"contradict the information","meaning":"與資料相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"A statement is false if it contradicts the passage.","zh":"如果陳述與文章相矛盾，該陳述就是錯誤。"},{"en":"Contradict the information means say the opposite of what the text says.","zh":"contradict the information 指說出與文本內容相反的東西。"},{"en":"If a passage says the shop opens at nine, a statement saying it opens at ten contradicts the information.","zh":"如果文章說商店九點開門，而陳述說十點開門，就與資料相矛盾。"},{"en":"When a statement contradicts the text clearly, students should mark it FALSE.","zh":"當陳述明確與文本矛盾時，學生應標記為 FALSE。"},{"en":"The phrase shows direct conflict with the source.","zh":"這個片語顯示與來源直接衝突。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no information on this","meaning":"沒有這方面的資料","examples":[{"en":"Candidates write NOT GIVEN if the passage provides no information on the claim.","zh":"如果文章沒有提供關於該主張的資料，考生寫 NOT GIVEN。"},{"en":"No information on this means the text does not say enough to decide whether the claim is true or false.","zh":"no information on this 指文本沒有說足夠內容來判斷該主張是真是假。"},{"en":"If a passage describes violin prices but not the maker’s childhood, there is no information on that childhood.","zh":"如果文章描述小提琴價格，但沒有描述製作者童年，就沒有這方面的資料。"},{"en":"Students should not use outside knowledge when the passage gives no information.","zh":"當文章沒有提供資料時，學生不應使用外部知識。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the answer cannot be proved from the text.","zh":"這個片語表示答案不能從文本證明。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"quality of a particular note","meaning":"某個音符的音質","examples":[{"en":"The quality of a particular note may vary between performances.","zh":"某個音符的音質可能在不同演奏之間有所不同。"},{"en":"Quality of a particular note means the sound character of one specific musical note.","zh":"quality of a particular note 指某一特定音符的聲音特質。"},{"en":"A piano teacher may ask a student to improve the quality of a particular note that sounds harsh.","zh":"鋼琴老師可能要求學生改善某個聽起來刺耳的音符音質。"},{"en":"If pressure or speed changes, the same note may sound warmer, brighter or weaker.","zh":"如果力度或速度改變，同一音符可能聽起來更溫暖、更明亮或更薄弱。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on one note’s sound, not the whole piece.","zh":"這個片語集中於一個音符的聲音，而不是整首樂曲。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"played on the same violin","meaning":"在同一把小提琴上演奏","examples":[{"en":"A note played on the same violin may sound different each time.","zh":"在同一把小提琴上演奏的音符，每次可能聽起來不同。"},{"en":"Played on the same violin means performed using one identical violin, not different instruments.","zh":"played on the same violin 指使用同一把小提琴演奏，而不是不同樂器。"},{"en":"The same melody played on the same violin can still change if the player uses different pressure.","zh":"同一旋律在同一把小提琴上演奏，如果演奏者使用不同力度，仍可能改變。"},{"en":"If sound varies even on the same instrument, performance technique matters.","zh":"如果即使在同一樂器上聲音仍有變化，演奏技巧就很重要。"},{"en":"The phrase controls the comparison by keeping the instrument constant.","zh":"這個片語透過保持樂器不變來控制比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"vary each time","meaning":"每次都有所不同","examples":[{"en":"The sound of an individual note may vary each time it is played.","zh":"個別音符的聲音每次演奏時都可能有所不同。"},{"en":"Vary each time means change slightly on every occasion.","zh":"vary each time 指每一次都略有改變。"},{"en":"A student’s speaking speed may vary each time they present, depending on confidence and topic.","zh":"學生每次演講時語速都可能因信心和題目而有所不同。"},{"en":"If a violin note varies each time, measuring one performance cannot describe every performance.","zh":"如果小提琴音符每次都有所不同，量度一次演奏不能描述所有演奏。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses repeated small differences.","zh":"這個片語強調反覆出現的小差異。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"analyse complex sound","meaning":"分析複雜聲音","examples":[{"en":"Scientific systems cannot yet analyse complex sound as effectively as the brain.","zh":"科學系統尚未能像大腦一樣有效分析複雜聲音。"},{"en":"Analyse complex sound means examine detailed sound patterns with many frequencies, tones and changes.","zh":"analyse complex sound 指檢視包含許多頻率、音色和變化的細緻聲音模式。"},{"en":"Sound engineers analyse complex sound when balancing voices, instruments and background noise.","zh":"音響工程師平衡人聲、樂器和背景噪音時，會分析複雜聲音。"},{"en":"If a sound contains many interacting parts, analysis becomes difficult.","zh":"如果聲音包含許多互相作用的部分，分析就變得困難。"},{"en":"The phrase describes careful study of complicated audio.","zh":"這個片語描述對複雜音訊的仔細研究。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"more accurately than humans","meaning":"比人類更準確","examples":[{"en":"The statement compares scientific instruments with human hearing.","zh":"該陳述把科學儀器與人類聽覺作比較。"},{"en":"More accurately than humans means with fewer mistakes or finer precision than people can achieve.","zh":"more accurately than humans 指比人類做到更少錯誤或更高精準度。"},{"en":"A calculator can add long numbers more accurately than humans doing the calculation by hand.","zh":"計算機加長數字時，可以比人手計算更準確。"},{"en":"If machines measured violin quality more accurately than humans, expert listening would be less important.","zh":"如果機器能比人類更準確地量度小提琴質素，專家聆聽就較不重要。"},{"en":"The phrase makes a comparison of precision.","zh":"這個片語作出精準度比較。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"handmade violins","meaning":"手工製作的小提琴","examples":[{"en":"Handmade violins may differ in design and sound.","zh":"手工製作的小提琴可能在設計和聲音上有所不同。"},{"en":"Handmade violins are violins made mainly by skilled people rather than mass-produced entirely by machines.","zh":"handmade violins 指主要由熟練工匠製作，而不是完全由機器大量生產的小提琴。"},{"en":"A handmade violin may take months to finish because each part is shaped and adjusted carefully.","zh":"手工製作的小提琴可能需要數月完成，因為每個部分都要仔細塑形和調整。"},{"en":"If violins are handmade, small differences between makers can affect the final instrument.","zh":"如果小提琴是手工製作，製作者之間的細小差異可能影響最終樂器。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts individual craft with factory production.","zh":"這個片語把個人工藝與工廠生產作對比。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"vary according to","meaning":"根據……而有所不同","examples":[{"en":"The statement suggests that violin quality varies according to the craftsman’s ability.","zh":"該陳述暗示小提琴質素根據工匠能力而有所不同。"},{"en":"Vary according to means change depending on a particular factor.","zh":"vary according to 指因某特定因素而改變。"},{"en":"Bus travel time may vary according to traffic, weather and roadworks.","zh":"巴士行程時間可能根據交通、天氣和道路工程而有所不同。"},{"en":"If quality varies according to skill, better makers usually produce better results.","zh":"如果質素根據技巧而變化，較好的製作者通常產生較好結果。"},{"en":"The phrase links difference with a cause.","zh":"這個片語把差異與原因連接起來。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"musical ability","meaning":"音樂能力","examples":[{"en":"A craftsman’s musical ability is not the same as woodworking skill.","zh":"工匠的音樂能力不等於木工技巧。"},{"en":"Musical ability is skill in understanding, performing, hearing or creating music.","zh":"musical ability 指理解、演奏、聆聽或創作音樂的能力。"},{"en":"A child with strong musical ability may remember melodies quickly and sing in tune.","zh":"音樂能力強的孩子可能很快記住旋律並唱準音。"},{"en":"If a violin maker has musical ability, they may judge tone more sensitively.","zh":"如果小提琴製作者有音樂能力，可能更敏感地判斷音色。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to music skill, not general intelligence.","zh":"這個片語指音樂方面的能力，而不是一般智力。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"gain in popularity","meaning":"日益普及","examples":[{"en":"Modern violins may gradually gain in popularity.","zh":"現代小提琴可能逐漸日益普及。"},{"en":"Gain in popularity means become more liked, accepted or commonly used.","zh":"gain in popularity 指變得更受喜愛、更被接受或更常使用。"},{"en":"Online lessons gained in popularity when students and teachers became more comfortable with video calls.","zh":"當學生和老師更習慣視像通話後，網上課堂日益普及。"},{"en":"If leading musicians start using modern violins, they may gain in popularity among younger players.","zh":"如果頂尖音樂家開始使用現代小提琴，它們可能在年輕演奏者之間日益普及。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a rise in public acceptance.","zh":"這個片語描述公眾接受度上升。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"amongst top violinists","meaning":"在頂尖小提琴手之間","examples":[{"en":"The statement asks whether modern instruments are becoming popular amongst top violinists.","zh":"該陳述問現代樂器是否正在頂尖小提琴手之間變得流行。"},{"en":"Amongst top violinists means within the group of the best or most respected violin players.","zh":"amongst top violinists 指在最好或最受尊重的小提琴演奏者群體之中。"},{"en":"A new bow design may become popular amongst top violinists if it improves control.","zh":"如果新弓設計改善控制，它可能在頂尖小提琴手之間變得流行。"},{"en":"If modern instruments gain support amongst top violinists, public attitudes may change.","zh":"如果現代樂器在頂尖小提琴手之間獲得支持，公眾態度可能改變。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the expert group being discussed.","zh":"這個片語指出正在討論的專家群體。"}],"source":"Passage 3 Flash Cards - 175 - Science and the Stradivarius - Uncovering the secret of quality.pdf","sourcePage":19}]};
